id;nome;nazione;citta;indirizzo;latitudine;longitudine;prezzoMedio;delivery;booking;tipoCucina;descrizione;servizi;recensioniIDs
1;Steirereck im Stadtpark;Austria;Vienna;Am Heumarkt 2a, Vienna, 1030, Austria;48.2043967;16.3815669;45;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;The architecture is the first thing you notice! Located in the Stadtpark, the building has a futuristic feel. The interior is bright and airy, featuring clean lines and elegant modern design, you can look into the kitchen through the pass. The clever division of the space into different wings creates a calm and relaxed atmosphere. The exceptional politeness and utmost professionalism of the service team ensure that you feel welcome and comfortable from the moment you arrive. Special mention goes to Birgit Reitbauer, an exemplary hostess, and sommelier René Antrag, for his superb wine recommendations – the perfect complement to Heinz Reitbauer and Michael Bauböck's distinctive, creative and often surprising cuisine. At lunchtime and in the evening, a six- or seven-course set menu is proposed, with an additional fantastic à la carte selection available in the evening. You can also compose your own four-or five-course set menu at lunchtime. The restaurant's bread and cheese trolley is renowned far beyond the city limits – the staff will enthusiastically talk you through the options.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2;Amador;Austria;Vienna;Grinzinger Straße 86, Vienna, 1190, Austria;48.2539745;16.3586534;28;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;A culinary highlight for the city and for Austria. This restaurant's location on the outskirts of the city in the Hajszan Neumann wine estate is something special in itself. Here, a wonderful brick vaulted ceiling and stylish interior design make for a distinctive look. Juan Amador's cuisine more than lives up to the setting: the finest ingredients are used to create a modern and sophisticated set menu comprising dishes that are finely balanced and consistently harmonious. The creative mastermind of this operation is supported by a highly motivated and pleasingly cordial team. Impressive wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4;Per Se;USA;New York;10 Columbus Circle, New York, 10019, USA;40.7680545;-73.9825882;90;true;true;Contemporary, French;An experience at Thomas Keller’s Per Se is one to be savored, recounted and remembered. Despite stellar views and a clever design allowing each table a view, your attention won’t stray from the plate. Such is the appeal of the place.There are two menus, one of which is vegetarian and may highlight a playful twist on borscht, with red beet agnolotti and crème fraîche. Both menus end in a grand dessert finale, like seasonal confections as well as such classics as a cappuccino semifreddo served with brioche donuts. They do offer supplements using lavish ingredients, but unless you’re richer than Croesus, you needn’t consider them. Just put yourself in the chef's hands and relish a meal that is balanced, varied and as seasonal as it gets.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
5;Le Bernardin;USA;New York;155 W. 51st St., New York, 10019, USA;40.76177;-73.98223;31;false;true;Seafood;Maguy Le Coze and Eric Ripert’s icon has been entertaining the city’s movers and shakers for close to 30 years and its popularity remains undimmed. Seafood restaurants have no hiding place when it comes to cooking fish or crustaceans and this kitchen always hits its marks—whether that’s lusciously sweet, seared langoustine in a truffled broth or golden-brown fluke with a bouillabaisse enriched with sea urchin. While seafood remains Ripert's passion, his vegetarian tasting menu makes waves with dishes like the Himalayan morel, spring pea and fava bean casserole or the warm artichoke panaché with vegetable risotto and Périgord black truffle vinaigrette. Finish with purple sweet potato baba au whisky cloaked with caramelized pecan whipped cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6;Eleven Madison Park;USA;New York;11 Madison Ave., New York, 10010, USA;40.7415543;-73.9872414;49;false;true;Vegan, Innovative;Chef Daniel Humm presides over this temple of modern elegance with a zealous dedication to masterful precision. Nothing is out of place and everything is custom made, from the staff’s suits to the handblown water vases.The plant-based menu is a bold vision of luxury dining and elevates the concept to unparalleled heights. The freshly baked, delicately crisped vegan roll presented with faux butter is a magical creation. A quenelle of tonburi, mimicking caviar, plated with horseradish cream and accompanied by a radish tostada with a swipe of pumpkin seed butter is simply stunning. Toothsome braised seitan, wrapped in spinach and dressed with morels, is amplified with luscious sauce work.Desserts, perhaps a frozen cherry blossom and rose confection dressed with strawberries, are equally accomplished.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7;Masa;USA;New York;10 Columbus Circle, New York, 10019, USA;40.76819;-73.98234;19;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;There is nothing like an omakase in the care of Chef Masa Takayama. The commotion of Columbus Circle gives way to the calm, collected ceremony of a room anchored by a strikingly smooth hinoki counter. Everything is in place, as chefs and servers work with a kind of harmony that recalls ballet. Every decision, every move, is in the service of his distinctive style, which many have copied but none have mastered. Fragrant white and black truffles, pearly beads of Osetra caviar, and vibrant garnishes make for brilliant touches that straddle the line between luxury and excess. Few have both the imagination and the know-how to make foie gras nigiri, and few serve abalone so meltingly tender. It is a captivating experience that is singularly memorable.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
8;The Inn at Little Washington;USA;Washington;309 Middle St., Washington, 22747, USA;38.7134767;-78.1595348;52;true;false;American, French;Chef Patrick O’Connell has long been the steward of this idyllic restaurant just outside Washington. In a town whose very existence seems tied to his success, dinner here recalls another era. The dining room is embellished to the very last inch, with fringe and fabric all over, patterned carpets, and lush wallpaper. The menu is divided between classics and vegetables, most of which are sourced locally and from the team’s own garden. Dinner always begins with pimento cheese packed into a crisp chip and ends with a playful pear dessert. In between, courses like lobster with caviar beurre blanc show the kitchen at its very best. And all throughout, roaming bread and cheese carts are a reminder of a luxury that’s less and less common.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
9;Smyth;USA;Chicago;177 N. Ada St., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8850485;-87.6606324;17;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;The very chic Smyth with its lounge styling and open kitchen is helmed by Chefs John Shields and Karen Urie-Shields. Their cooking is bold and often pushes boundaries, all the while impressing. Sheer creativity is applied to seasonal produce, some of which comes from their garden. A quail egg, gently smoked and topped with caviar, is given a twist with barley caramel. Resting inside its shell, plump Maine uni, amplified with a divine peach gel and wasabi cream, is both stunning and memorable. The chef's creativity is on full display in an utterly unique Dungeness crab dish, while wagyu sided by a truffle-flavored doughnut with marrow glaze is yet another hit. Savory sweets, like new potato ice cream, a corn macaron with peppery nasturtium, or the dark chocolate tartlet studded with kombu, raise the bar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11;Sorn;Thailand;Bangkok;56 Soi Sukhumvit 26, Khlong Tan, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7231336;100.5684937;61;false;true;Southern Thai;Immerse yourself in the food culture of Southern Thailand, with the exquisite cooking of self-taught Chef-Owner Supaksorn Jongsiri. Blending tradition with modernity, refinement with evolution, his perfectly paced menu offers an array of exhilarating flavours, all of which are in perfect harmony. Whether Tapi River prawns, Phuket lobster or Andaman squid, the ingredients will be truly stunning. The whole experience will more than make up for the very thorough process involved in securing a table.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
12;Azurmendi;Spain;Larrabetzu;Legina Auzoa, Larrabetzu, 48195, Spain;43.26065;-2.81454;78;false;true;Creative;A flagship of Vizcaya’s fine-dining scene and a leading light in sustainability, Azurmendi is a shining example of how to work with the environment around us. To do this, it has adapted its architecture and produce, and integrated new technologies in its quest to become a responsible restaurant business that aims to cook for a better future. Chef Eneko Atxa nurtures a sapling of the Tree of Gernika at the entrance of the restaurant in a manifestation of his desire to preserve the area's indigenous flora and fauna, to safeguard the values of Basque culture, and to offer guests a creative and informative culinary experience that is dedicated to the conservation of endemic species. His single tasting menu (Adarrak) includes an informative tour of the premises, such as the picnic served in a wicker basket in front of a vertical garden, snacks in a space decorated with recycled organic materials, and maritime-inspired appetisers in the corridor of the kitchen so you can watch its chefs hard at work. The superb wine list includes many limited production labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13;Aponiente;Spain;El Puerto de Santa María;Francisco Cossi Ochoa, El Puerto de Santa María, 11500, Spain;36.6033273;-6.2164435;49;false;false;Creative, Innovative;Ángel León, whose restaurant is housed in a tide mill dating back two centuries, is known as “the chef of the sea” and any mention of him means a journey of continual gastronomic discovery. As he says himself, at Aponiente “the aim is to raise awareness, open people's minds and introduce them to new concepts that are impossible to find anywhere else”. Totally committed to sustainability, this is a chef who seeks to surprise diners with new techniques and ingredients (such as seafood sausages, plankton, bioluminescence, cooking with seawater etc), always honing a philosophy which revolves around recycling, making the most of what the natural estuaries have to offer and championing the salvaging of discarded fish. His contemporary cuisine, based around resources from both the Mediterranean and the Atlantic, provides further surprises on the dessert menu, on which dishes somehow manage to combine the maritime world with sweeter textures (his “20 leagues under the sea”, a seaweed millefeuille presented inside a book by Jules Verne, is a particular delight).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14;DiverXO;Spain;Madrid;Padre Damián 23, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.4582913;-3.6856715;29;true;false;Creative;With dishes such as “Galician lobster waking up on the beaches of Goa”, “drunken crabs partying in Jerez”, and the “Minutejo del Agus” mini pork sandwich (a homage to snacks he enjoyed as a child with his father), Dabiz Muñoz’s fun, hedonistic and often irreverent cuisine breaks the mould of cutting-edge gastronomic cuisine by entering his highly personal and dream-like world. As a result, he ensures a rollercoaster of emotions that constantly challenge the palate. In this striking setting, the single “Flying Pigs Cuisine” tasting menu invites his guests on a spectacular journey across the world’s different cuisines, including Asian fusion, but with the predominant use of Spanish ingredients to help create more recognisable flavours. Highlighting themes such as invasive species and the Pyrenean ecosystem, the chef works without limits, combining local ingredients with exotic condiments. You’ll need to book well in advance to secure a table!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15;Noor;Spain;Córdoba;Pablo Ruiz Picasso 8, Córdoba, 14014, Spain;37.8899393;-4.7585272;71;false;false;Creative;Meaning “light” in Arabic, Noor is so much more than a fine-dining restaurant. Behind every detail there is a multi-faceted team that contributes its knowledge to bring to the fore the essence of the cultured and magical city of Córdoba, which has been a beacon of light since the reign of Caliph Abd al-Rahman III. In the restaurant's bright interior, with its open kitchen and incredible interior design, chef Paco Morales (ably supported by second in command Paola Gualandi) revives the spirit of Andalusian cuisine using modern ideas and techniques. Every season, the restaurant explores a different historical period, currently the “Golden Age”, as part of which three menus (Mudéjar, Morisco and Al-Yazira) reinterpret the splendour of the 16C and 17C. Standout dishes here include the durum wheat with smoked butter and chicken and calamari broth (a reinterpretation of the Abbasiya recipe) and the locally grown oranges with orange blossom, fried almonds and extra virgin olive oil for dessert.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16;Cenador de Amós;Spain;Villaverde de Pontones;Plaza del Sol, Villaverde de Pontones, 39793, Spain;43.4124884;-3.6988243;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Discover the secrets hidden in the Casa-Palacio Mazarrasa (1756), a mecca for foodies that certainly makes an impression and continues to evolve! The culinary experience begins with welcome drinks and appetisers in the glass-paned pavilion or on the terrace, and culminates in elegant dining spaces with a rustic yet modern feel. Always sporting his trademark cap, chef Jesús Sánchez runs the restaurant with the invaluable support of wife Marián Martínez, who is charge of the front of house. He remains consistently loyal to local ingredients, seasonality and to a firm commitment to sustainability via his surprise “La Gran Experiencia” menu, a heartfelt tribute to his natural surroundings, his Cantabrian identity and its history, and all the painstaking research that has gone into every bite. As an example, the sourdough bread baked on the premises always receives fulsome praise. We highly recommend taking a stroll through the small vegetable garden in the grounds and admiring the photos on display which highlight another of the chef’s great passions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
17;Quique Dacosta;Spain;Dénia;Rascassa 1, Dénia, 03700, Spain;38.8537884;0.0852209;30;true;true;Creative;This restaurant reflects the personality of the eponymous chef, who was awarded the Gold Medal for Merit in the Fine Arts in 2020."Can a flavour be beautiful?" was the subject of a debate between artists in the documentary Cocinar Belleza ("Cooking Beauty"). Here, it has been thrust to the fore in an aesthetically enchanting tasting menu of the same name. Based on the iconic signature dishes of the house, it also includes other lesser-known creations, which, in the hands of this chef, are the source of unexpected details and harmonies of flavour. His philosophy is to champion nature and showcase the produce of the Mediterranean, always maintaining a clear commitment to the circular economy and even delivering the odd deliberately provocative dish as food for thought.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
18;Atrio;Spain;Cáceres;Plaza San Mateo 1, Cáceres, 10003, Spain;39.4730183;-6.3713456;88;true;false;Creative;A temple of Spanish gastronomy that should be on the bucket list of every food-lover. Atrio exudes elegance, enthusiasm and sincerity, matched by impeccable service to enhance the dining experience to the full. For guests keen to stay over, the superb guestrooms available at the hotel-restaurant are complemented by the eleven highly luxurious suites at the Casa Palacio Paredes Saavedra, barely 30 metres away. Cáceres-born chef Toño Pérez is at the helm, conjuring up creative cuisine of the highest technical level on a single yet extensive tasting menu that the kitchen adapts in line with your preferences. On it, we find the full flavours of Iberian pork (his famous “happy pig”) and the Extremadura region, paying full respect to the DNA of local traditions by showcasing the myriad nuances of his native land (as a result, you’ll find multiple pork-inspired options ranging from pork fat, ham and dewlap to loin, rind and jus). Make sure you take time to visit Atrio’s spectacular wine cellar, featuring highly renowned labels and historic vintages.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
20;El Celler de Can Roca;Spain;Girona;Can Sunyer 48, Girona, 17007, Spain;41.9932026;2.807927;59;false;true;Creative;The Roca brothers like to say that their success is down to the balance struck in a metaphorical "three-player game", with Joan in charge of the savoury dishes, Josep as the sommelier and Jordi on dessert duty.But little matter how they go about winning diners over, their ultimate goal is to create a feast for the eyes, the palate and all of the senses. This is an exceptionally high-calibre restaurant that celebrates contrasts, memories, journeys... It is also characterised by a penchant for working with local produce, a focus on sustainability and the aim to "raise awareness" of the challenges posed by climate change. The spectacular appetisers are a tribute to the evolution of this establishment and its emblematic dishes!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
21;Reua Thai;Netherlands;Nuth;Dorpstraat 45b, Nuth, 6361EK, Netherlands;50.9191536;5.8838304;85;true;true;Thai;Reua Thai has a rather rough-hewn feel, with wooden ornaments adding to the unique character of the space. Pattama Simons is an aficionado of authentic Thai cuisine but adds a touch of finesse. She often works with produce from her own garden or local suppliers and takes the time to create depth in her cooking. For example, she infuses beef stock with cinnamon, lemongrass, peanut and coriander to achieve a vibrant and subtly spicy flavour profile. This broth serves as a rich foundation to elevate chopped beef, rice noodles and daikon. With a choice of options for each course, the set menu is recommended to fully appreciate this aromatic cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
22;Restobar Vista;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Holland Amerikakade 104, Rotterdam, 3072 MC, Netherlands;51.9069713;4.4883515;97;false;true;Modern French;Dine against the stunning backdrop of the Rotterdam skyline and the Nieuwe Maas River at Restobar Vista. On the ground floor of the De Rotterdam building, the tastefully modern restaurant is done out in muted colours. The team assembled by Henrie van der Heijden, head chef at Vista in Willemstad, creates distinctly French dishes, with the occasional nod to the Mediterranean. Think succulent roasted tournedos on a bed of caramelised onion, accompanied by a rich Madeira sauce and potato rösti. The chefs eschew complexity and delight diners with their unpretentious dishes. The extensive menu and fantastic value for money will bring a smile to your face.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
23;Alma Bistro;Netherlands;Breda;Ginnekenstraat 88, Breda, 4811 JJ, Netherlands;51.5838108;4.7771145;86;true;true;Modern French;Located in an imposing building in the centre of Breda, this bistro exudes elegance and charm. The kitchen on the upper floor catches your eye as soon as you enter. Chef Wouter van Laarhoven and sommelier Malou Hagenaars, the duo behind Alma in Oisterwijk, have assembled a team who handle the finest ingredients with sensibility. Their cuisine is distinctive and ambitious. Highlights of the menu include steak tartare or whole turbot. Scallops are paired with a foie gras cream, crushed hazelnuts and a rice wine and vinegar sauce infused with yuzu. Be sure to explore the tempting wine list!;;[]
25;Akelaŕe;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Paseo del Padre Orcolaga 56, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20008, Spain;43.3027805;-2.0731493;28;true;false;Creative, Traditional Cuisine;With his impressive CV and distinctive moustache, chef Pedro Subijana is an icon of the restaurant scene and as such commands the utmost respect. As one of the founding fathers of the New Basque Cuisine movement, he believes in constant evolution, and even if the focus here is squarely on creativity and technique his approach is rooted in tradition. Located inside the spectacular hotel of the same name on Mt Igueldo, Akelaré has already celebrated its golden jubilee, and continues to impress with its interior design, views of the Bay of Biscay and meticulous cuisine. Its versatile tasting options (Aranori and Bekarki), which enable guests to mix and match dishes between the two menus, are based on well-established house specialities and innovative new recipes, all of which demonstrate an impressive gastronomic flair. One of its latest innovations is a new plated version of its famous Gin & Tonic, which now comes in the form of a Gin & Tonic tartlet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
26;Martín Berasategui;Spain;Lasarte - Oria;Loidi 4, Lasarte - Oria, 20160, Spain;43.2669352;-2.0157211;89;true;true;Creative;As a subtle tribute to his father, Martín Berasategui has based the logo of his restaurant on his own handwritten signature, but he could well have his name up in gold lettering! This humble and jovial chef considers himself to be merely a “conveyor of happiness” who owes his success to the passion and effort that he always puts into his work, the unwavering support of his wife (Oneka Arregui) and, as he says himself, his incredible team. In this elegant space with no shortage of relaxing views of the surrounding countryside, diners can experience a hedonistic approach to cuisine that is highly original and creative. The fixed priced à la carte and the tasting menu both combine the restaurant's signature dishes (caramelised millefeuille with smoked eel, foie gras, spring onion and green apple) with entirely new creations (suckling lamb chop, liquid fritter, spicy carrots and shallot stuffed with Iberian pork). All the dishes also specify the year in which they were created.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
28;ABaC;Spain;Barcelona;Avenida del Tibidabo 1, Barcelona, 08022, Spain;41.4103822;2.1367664;75;true;false;Creative;Tradition, cutting-edge, flavour, attitude and passion, along with a consistent approach, define to perfection the cooking of Jordi Cruz. In his elegant restaurant boasting views of a tranquil garden dotted with some amazing works of contemporary art, he offers diners a unique gastronomic experience that constantly evolves in line with ingredients from the changing seasons. These are always combined with his technical ability as he revisits Mediterranean flavours with a nod to influences from elsewhere around the globe. The experience here, which begins with appetisers in the kitchen, is centred around a single tasting menu featuring new recipes alongside the restaurant’s renowned signature dishes. One of his extraordinary dishes is his tribute to Le Petit Prince, writer Antoine de Saint-Exupéry’s iconic fable, which features a half sphere of Crema Catalana with nitro/lio creamy popcorn, burnt caramel ice-cream and rice water.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
30;Arzak;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Avenida Alcalde José Elosegi 273, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20015, Spain;43.3214016;-1.9490932;78;false;false;Creative, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is a real institution in San Sebastián as it has been Michelin starred since 1974. Hospitality, history and modernity converge in this century-old family mansion in Alto de Miracruz, a culinary mecca run by the tandem of Juan Mari Arzak and his daughter Elena (the latter taking over the reins in magnificent fashion) who have succeeded in perfectly combining the most surprising innovations with expertise rooted in Basque tradition. The creativity, presentation and intense flavours of their dishes are the result of experiments conducted in the Laboratorio Arzak in the same building, where they work, with utmost respect, with a “flavour workbench” of more than 1 000 ingredients of the very best quality. Guests can choose between an extensive tasting menu with a wine-pairing option, and the set menu-style à la carte, with a choice of dishes that varies with the seasons. The roast duck with cacao, dehydrated orange and carob Turkish delight completely bowled us over!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
31;Cocina Hermanos Torres;Spain;Barcelona;Taquígraf Serra 20, Barcelona, 08029, Spain;41.3865273;2.1400168;93;true;true;Creative;Once over the threshold, a fascinating experience awaits at Cocina Hermanos Torres – one that transports guests to a world where time has stood still thanks to the magical setting and highly delicate Mediterranean cuisine that takes us away from our everyday lives. The Torres twins (Sergio and Javier) dreamt of incorporating their culinary microcosmos into the heart of the dining room, transforming the culinary experience into a true spectacle, hence the three cooking stations that dominate the centre of the room, around which tables are arranged beneath romantic “clouds” of light. The cuisine here is centred on a superb menu that invites guests on a gourmet journey extolling the very best seasonal and local ingredients, using them in such a way to extract maximum impact and flavour with a minimum of intervention. This includes standout dishes such as the cured squid with poultry consommé and caviar – a spectacular “sea and mountains” combination. The magnificent wine cellar here is overseen by no fewer than five sommeliers! If you wish to book a table for one you’ll need to contact the restaurant ahead of time.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
32;Ultraviolet by Paul Pairet;China Mainland;Shanghai;'somewhere in Shanghai' - meet at Mr & Mrs Bund restaurant - 6F, Bund 18, 18 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.240358;121.48509;98;false;false;Innovative;This multi-sensory experience at a secret location that combines innovative and surprising dishes with lights, sounds and scents will give you quite an adrenaline rush. After the success of Mr & Mrs Bund, chef Paul Pairet created this clever concept where 10 lucky diners are taken on an interactive culinary journey beyond their wildest dreams. Be dazzled by the creative mix of tastes, unconventional presentations and enthusiastic service, all enhanced by imagination.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
33;Taian Table;China Mainland;Shanghai;101-102, Building No. 1, Garden Office, No.161, Lane 465, Zhenning Road, Changning, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.221807;121.474049;21;false;true;Innovative;A fixture on the city's dining scene since 2016, this brainchild of chef Stefan Stiller is familiar to all local foodies. With counter seats enclosing an island where the chefs cook, all guests get to feel the vibrant vibe up close. The 10- or 12-course set menu changes every few weeks. Deftly crafted original creations showcase layers of tastes and textures, melding German traditions with uniquely Asian flavours such as kimchi and curry.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
35;Le Calandre;Italy;Rubano;via Liguria 1, località Sarmeola, Rubano, 35030, Italy;45.4215425;11.8096633;50;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;Situated away from the main road and the main shopping centre, the fabulous Le Calandre is run by the Alajmo family. The soft lighting (even during the day) perfectly complements the decor in the minimalist-style dining room designed by brothers Massimiliano and Raffaele (as is most of the tableware used in the restaurant). The cuisine is presented on three tasting menus (Classico, Max and Raf), with the option of reducing the number of courses and choosing dishes from different menus, almost à la carte style. With its combination of familiar flavours and imaginative twists, Max’s cuisine celebrates the restaurant’s signature dishes such as the “passi d’oro” 2.0 risotto and the famous cuttlefish cappuccino in black ink, as well as creative dishes inspired by the passing seasons. The restaurant also has its own delicatessen for anyone keen to purchase a gourmet souvenir.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
36;Enrico Bartolini al Mudec;Italy;Milan;via Tortona 56, Milan, 20144, Italy;45.4516;9.161865;65;true;true;Creative;Having received three stars for this restaurant (his flagship address in Milan), Enrico Bartolini has no intention of resting on his laurels. Assisted by resident chef Davide Boglioli, he continues to create new yet approachable dishes full of intense flavours and a variety of influences, so simply sit back and enjoy the perfectly balanced results. There are two tasting menus served here: “Mudec Experience” and the “Best of”, the latter showcasing the chef’s classic favourites. Dishes can be chosen à la carte style from both menus. If you’d like to taste cold spaghetti, leave room for one of the five dishes served on the “creative cheeses” menu that features interesting and unusual combinations. Situated on the third floor of Milan’s Museo delle Culture (Mudec), the restaurant has an elegant and contemporary lounge-style vibe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[6]
37;Uliassi;Italy;Senigallia;banchina di Levante 6, Senigallia, 60019, Italy;43.7194609;13.2206503;25;false;false;Creative, Seafood;The Adriatic Riviera, a perfect picture-postcard summer holiday destination, is the setting for this fine restaurant run by chef Mauro Uliassi. Hidden among the private beach clubs that crowd Senigallia’s seafront, this three-Michelin-star restaurant comes as a surprise, surrounded as it is by beach parasols and the sound of the sea lapping on the shore. The strength and originality of Uliassi’s cuisine lies in his ability to make good use of local ingredients, taking inspiration from the culinary traditions that have been so familiar and successful along this coastline over the past few decades and giving them a personal, creative twist. Fish and seafood obviously take pride of place, although there’s also room on the menu for meat, inspired by the Marche’s traditional game dishes – the delicious skewered pigeon is cooked to perfection! The colourful dining experience here is enhanced by the owner’s warm welcome, with Mauro’s sister Catia and his son Filippo working alongside the chef. It’s also worth mentioning that the restaurant has a keen focus on the environment, hence its banning of the use of plastic and doing its utmost to persuade its fish suppliers not to use polystyrene to transport their fish.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
38;Enoteca Pinchiorri;Italy;Florence;via Ghibellina 87, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.770066;11.2621974;50;true;true;Italian Contemporary;The cuisine at Pinchiorri is striking for its opulent and grandiose style which impresses without becoming overly fussy or excessive, so that the main focus in every dish is the flavour of its ingredients. The magnificent feast of courses resembles a firework display, with each course more impressive than the last in a growing crescendo of delights. It’s worth coming here simply to experience the service, an impeccable waltz directed by Alessandro Tomberli, one of the best maître-d’s in Italy. Annie Féolde, one of the restaurant’s icons, left the reins to the highly talented chef Riccardo Monco, who continues to nurture and satisfy the Italian appetite for fine cuisine. Credit must also go to Giorgio Pinchiorri, who has developed a wine list that is renowned across the globe.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
39;Atelier Moessmer Norbert Niederkofler;Italy;Brunico;via Walther Von der Vogelweide 17, Brunico, 39031, Italy;46.7927709;11.949283;58;false;false;Creative, Alpine;Situated in a vast historic park near the centre of Brunico, this restaurant occupies a villa that was once part of the Moessmer textile factory – to illustrate the fact, an interesting fabric book dating from the early 20C is displayed on a large central table in the dining room. Here, the chef’s “Cook the Mountain” philosophy takes centre stage with a focus on top-quality produce sourced from the surrounding mountains, and a seasonal approach which ensures that flavours and ingredients are always at their best. Dinner starts with delicious appetisers served in the small lounge, perhaps accompanied by an aperitif. Having enjoyed this delicious prelude, you then move to the dining room or to the counter with its stools facing the kitchen. Wherever you choose to sit, you continue with the chef’s single tasting menu – a series of superb dishes that confirm this chef from the Ahrntal valley as one of the masters of contemporary Italian cuisine.;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
40;Villa Crespi;Italy;Orta San Giulio;via Fava 18, Orta San Giulio, 28016, Italy;45.7964778;8.4159486;85;true;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Just a stone’s throw from the enchanting village of Orta San Giulio with its picture-postcard views of the lake and San Giulio island, this three-Michelin-star restaurant boasts a stunning location in a late-19C Moorish-style villa. Impressive both inside and out, this aristocratic residence was once the home of the Crespi family. Today, the villa’s leading light is Antonino Cannavacciuolo, who is now at the helm of a number of Michelin-starred restaurants, of which the Villa Crespi, the most famous and celebrated of them all, is the flagship. Although this chef originally from Vico Equense in Campania takes inspiration from all over Italy and further afield, it is the passion, colour and intense flavours of his native region that shine through in all his dishes. The two tasting menus, as well as the concise à la carte, showcase elegant dishes full of goodness where the focus is on fish and seafood (although meat also features). This is Mediterranean cuisine in all its glory, with a contemporary style that is never forced – typical of Cannavacciuolo at his very best.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
41;Quattro Passi;Italy;Marina del Cantone;via Vespucci 13/n, Marina del Cantone, 80061, Italy;40.5857091;14.3537561;80;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;This restaurant’s 40-year history began with present owner-chef Fabrizio Mellino’s grandfather, who ran a small business selling eggs from his own hens. From this, he decided to branch out and open a pizzeria “four steps from the sea” (hence the name Quattro Passi), which over the years his son Antonio and now his grandson Fabrizio have transformed into a temple to Mediterranean cuisine. Flavours, strong technique and quality ingredients combine to create an exciting feast for the tastebuds which finishes with a selection of small chocolate eggs with unusual flavours such as roquefort, rocket, chilli pepper and lemon. A host of different influences (the sea, the Sannio region, France, Japan) and ingredients (San Marzano tomatoes, Amalfi lemons) come together in Fabrizio’s cuisine, resulting in dishes that are simple, delicious and full of flavour. It’s not an easy journey to Marina del Cantone, but once here you’ll be warmly welcomed by Raffaele and his team, after which you can sit back and enjoy a truly memorable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
42;La Pergola;Italy;Rome;via Cadlolo 101, Rome, 00136, Italy;41.9187946;12.4461151;17;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Following complete refurbishment, the new Pergola pays tribute to the colours and materials of Rome, from the Travertine marble to the red colour scheme. The terrace has also had a face-lift, but fortunately the view hasn’t changed – however many times you come here, you find that your memory never quite does justice to the magnificent and expansive views of the capital. Below Monte Mario hill, the whole of Rome, encircled by hills, is spread out before you, appearing silent and enchanted, almost as if it were dozing. Although he’s been at the helm here since 1994, Heinz Beck’s enthusiasm remains undiminished, as he continues to update his dishes, explore new avenues and create imaginative cuisine with a strong Italian and Mediterranean flavour. In addition to the spectacular wine list, there’s also a remarkable choice of water and coffee.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
43;Reale;Italy;Castel di Sangro;contrada Santa Liberata, località Casadonna, Castel di Sangro, 67031, Italy;41.7800349;14.094554;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Housed in a 16C monastery amid gardens and vineyards in the foothills surrounding Castel di Sangro, this restaurant boasts a simple, minimalist style which is echoed in its cuisine, created by one of the most easily identified and recognisable chefs in Italy. For years, Niko Romito has been renowned for his minimalist-style dishes which are prepared from just a few ingredients, featuring sauces with an Italian rather than classically French flavour, and this remarkable chef continues to research and evolve. He focuses on ingredients and recipes from his native Abruzzo, paying particular attention to vegetables and creating dishes that are striking for their intense flavours. As ever, his dishes are apparently simple yet often the result of complex preparation that leaves his guests full of spellbound admiration.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
45;Osteria Francescana;Italy;Modena;via Stella 22, Modena, 41121, Italy;44.6448099;10.9215518;96;true;false;Creative;Situated in Via Stella, this restaurant eschews an overly ornate decor in favour of a simpler, more contemporary and elegant style which is enhanced by striking works of art (Massimo Bottura is a passionate art enthusiast). This understated style is echoed in the cuisine, where grandiose gestures are replaced by a balanced approach which pays careful attention to every detail. The menu has a broad reach, including specialities from Modena and Emilia (ingredients such as Parmesan cheese, balsamic vinegar and tagliatelle and tortellini pasta), as well as classic international dishes, which the chef reinterprets with a light and playful touch, reminding us that food should not be a boring ritual but instead an enjoyable experience influenced by memory and culture. The impressive wine list includes lesser-known labels from small-scale producers with interesting stories, as well as top-quality options from established wineries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
46;Dal Pescatore;Italy;Runate;località Runate 15, Runate, 46013, Italy;45.1712728;10.3565788;34;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Having held three Michelin stars since 1996 (an Italian record), this restaurant is situated in the village of Runate which lies between Cremona and Mantova and has just a few dozen inhabitants. Now close to celebrating half a century in business, Dal Pescatore is run by an extraordinary couple who have transformed what was an old family inn into a temple of elegance and hospitality. Antonio Santini oversees the front of house, while his wife Nadia is at the helm in the kitchen, aided by sons Giovanni and Alberto. In a setting boasting an elegant mix of old and new, where space, light and colours combine to create an enchanting ambience, enjoy memorable dishes that have evolved over the decades, improving year after year without ever succumbing to modern trends so that the focus is always on flavour and the joy of good food. Dal Pescatore boasts a fairy-tale setting, occupying a delightful country house in the Parco dell’Oglio.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
47;Piazza Duomo;Italy;Alba;vicolo dell'Arco 1, angolo piazza Risorgimento 4, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.7005555;8.0359341;80;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;A distinctive red door marks the entrance to this temple of Italian cuisine. Once inside, make your way to the first floor, where you’re greeted by pink walls and a fresco by Francesco Clemente, as well as the restaurant’s friendly front-of-house staff. Here, the individual cuisine of chef Enrico Crippa takes centre stage on three tasting menus, with a fourth shorter menu available at lunchtime. One of the menus is inspired by the vegetable gardens and the seasons, another by the region, while the third takes guests on a culinary journey through Italy and further afield. What is obvious in every single, delicious bite is the chef’s passion for plants, with vegetables, flowers, wild and cultivated herbs harvested daily all featuring in memorable, beautifully presented dishes. The iconic appetisers featuring countless delicious ingredients are a feast for the eyes and the tastebuds alike and were particularly enjoyed by our inspectors. It hardly needs mentioning that this region is passionate about wine, so it’s not entirely surprising that the restaurant offers three different wine lists: Solopiemonte pays superb homage to the region, while Tuttoilresto (divided into two options, white and red) is a celebration of French wines. The efficient and enthusiastic serving staff succeed in taking good care of guests without being excessively formal, so that three hours (roughly the amount of time you need to allow for your meal) pass almost without noticing. The chef adds the finishing touch by bidding a discreet and friendly farewell at the end of the meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
48;Schloss Schauenstein;Switzerland;Fürstenau;Schlossgass 77, Fürstenau, 7414, Switzerland;46.7211969;9.4462648;75;true;true;Creative, Country cooking;Could there be a more fascinating backdrop for Andreas Caminada's culinary magic than a magnificent manor house that harmoniously combines history and modern design? In all its creativity and finesse, the cuisine draws almost exclusively on what the Graubünden region has to offer – some ingredients are produced on site. The standards, style and sense of individuality also extend to the guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
49;Restaurant de l'Hôtel de Ville;Switzerland;Crissier;Rue d'Yverdon 1, Crissier, 1023, Switzerland;46.5539842;6.5767178;60;false;false;Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine;Only a 15-minute drive from Lausanne, this restaurant, known simply as "Crissier" by its regulars, has a long and illustrious history. Since Frédy Girardet was first awarded three stars back in 1975, the Restaurant de l'Hôtel de Ville has successively showcased the talents of a stunning cast of great chefs, including the likes of Philippe Rochat, Benoît Violier… and now Franck Giovannini. At the head of an impressive kitchen team, he crafts high-flying dishes. The extensive à la carte lineup is truly decadent and consummately backed by a slick front-of-house team, on hand to satisfy the customer’s every whim. Among the many signature recipes, we recommend the Bresse poultry and the strawberry and lime soufflé – both of which are for two. Beautifully balanced and skilfully crafted dishes, flanked by painstakingly curated wines and served in stylish dining rooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
50;Sven Wassmer Memories;Switzerland;Bad Ragaz;Bernhard-Simon-Strasse 2, Bad Ragaz, 7310, Switzerland;47.0002941;9.5037741;78;false;false;Creative, Farm to table;Unique cuisine that has no need for showy gimmicks. The top-notch ingredients reflect a close affinity with Switzerland. Bold and full of contrasts, honest and accessible – this is the kind of food you wish you came across more often! The same goes for the restaurant as a whole: a chic and casually elegant setting, and perfectly coordinated, professional service provided by a relaxed and charming front-of-house team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
51;Cheval Blanc by Peter Knogl;Switzerland;Basel;Blumenrain 8, Basel, 4001, Switzerland;47.5604261;7.5875706;51;true;false;Classic French;In a stylish high-ceilinged room, diners sit at tables set with top-drawer tableware to enjoy classic cuisine that impresses with its sense of finesse and perfect craftsmanship. The well-defined flavours and fantastic contrasts also incorporate the odd Asian influence. Top-quality produce is of course the order of the day. The well-organised and professional service team also provides expert wine recommendations.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
52;Kanda;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Toranomon Hills Residential Tower, 1-1-1 Atago, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0002, Japan;35.6658;139.748;34;false;false;Japanese;Good cuisine, says Hiroyuki Kanda, should convey beauty, craftsmanship and feeling. This kappo-style restaurant, where guests sit close around the kitchen, is inspired by the Japanese hospitality of the tea ceremony. Delving deep into the essence of Japanese cuisine, Kanda showcases the culture through creativity filled with surprises. The interior was crafted with the assistance of contemporary artist Hiroshi Sugimoto. The beauty of the classics resonates with a refined modern sensibility.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
53;Azabu Kadowaki;Japan;Tokyo;2-7-2 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.655993;139.733551;36;false;false;Japanese;The essence of the free-flowing creativity exhibited here lies in the joy of people. Inspired by his belief that the customer is the teacher, Toshiya Kadowaki has always focused on how make others happy. One example is his truffle rice: by incorporating mushrooms not traditionally used in Japanese cuisine, he created a dish that became synonymous with the restaurant. Kadowaki says that food has the power to make people happy. By blending Western ingredients with Japanese techniques, he develops specialities that transcend borders.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
54;Kohaku;Japan;Tokyo;3-5-5 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.700825;139.740832;61;true;false;Japanese;Japanese cuisine that bubbles with creativity and refuses to be bound by genre. Tsukuri are paired not with soy sauce but on jellied bonito stock and bitter orange. Western ingredients such as caviar and truffles intensify impact. Not wanting to be trapped by the past, Chef Koji Koizumi changes his offerings year by year, driving constantly forward in pursuit of the new. With delicate creations of subtly layered flavours, he captures the sensibility of the age.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
55;SÉZANNE;Japan;Tokyo;7F, Four Seasons Hotel Tokyo at Marunouchi, 1-11-1 Marunouchi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-6277, Japan;35.678083;139.767155;66;false;false;French, Contemporary;Prix fixe menus trace the steps of Daniel Calvert’s culinary journey. His experiences in each city—London, New York, Paris, Hong Kong—interweaves and elevates the culinary cultures of their respective countries. A borderless sensibility joins French ingredients such as foie gras and vin jaune with Japanese influences such as soy sauce and sake lees. ‘The key to success is consistency’, says Calvert, who fine-tunes his craft with each dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
56;Harutaka;Japan;Tokyo;6F, 8-3-1 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669269;139.759203;67;false;true;Sushi;Sometimes our connections intervene to change our lives. Harutaka Takahashi’s mischievous youth in Asahikawa took a turn for the better when, through a tempura master who was a close friend of his potter uncle, he landed a job at Sukiyabashi Jiro. Like Ravel’s Bolero, sushi here is presented with a particular rhythm, building toward a crescendo of sweetness, sourness and temperature in harmony. Destiny is in the taste and texture of every piece of sushi at Harutaka.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
57;L'OSIER;Japan;Tokyo;7-5-5 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669667;139.761203;21;true;true;French, French Contemporary;‘L’Osier’ means ‘The Willow’. The name comes from the willow trees that once symbolised Ginza and is a nod to the shop’s founding location. When the doors open, guests are greeted by a glass artwork depicting a willow tree. Half a century has passed since the restaurant opened, but it has never stopped innovating. Chef Olivier Chaignon cultivates relationships with producers around the country, creating French cuisine at the cutting edge of the era.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
58;Kagurazaka Ishikawa;Japan;Tokyo;5-37 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.701212;139.739466;34;true;false;Japanese;Attended by a coterie of apprentices, Hideki Ishikawa never forgets the mindset of constant study. He visits producing regions, returning with the most outstanding foods. Each dish contains no more than two main ingredients. With unobtrusive technique, Ishikawa expresses the quality of his fare with flavours of elegant simplicity, pursuing the true character of Japanese cuisine. In so doing, he reminds us of the bounty of nature and respect for ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
59;RyuGin;Japan;Tokyo;7F, Tokyo Midtown Hibiya, 1-1-2 Yurakucho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0006, Japan;35.673583;139.759193;31;false;false;Japanese;What better location to showcase the wonders of Japan than steps from the Imperial Palace? With the Japanese flag emblazoned on his shirt, Seiji Yamamoto expresses his respect for spirituality and Japanese ingredients. The chef notes that ryori, the word for cuisine, consists of two characters meaning ‘discernment’ and ‘measurement.’ Yamamoto innovates from a scientific perspective, based on clear theoretical grounds. The restaurant’s name derives from a proverb: Ryu ginzureba kumo okoru: ’When the dragon sings, clouds form.’ The ‘Dragon of Hibiya’ is leading a Japanese culinary movement for a new age.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
60;L'Effervescence;Japan;Tokyo;2-26-4 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.660299;139.719454;49;false;true;French, Contemporary;Shinobu Namae’s vision is the connection between nature and people. In search of knowledge about ingredients, he visits producers, plunges into the ocean, and hikes through the hills and fields. The list of producers on his menus tells the story of his cuisine. ‘Artisanal Vegetables’ serves up the fragrances and minerals of the good earth on a single platter. ‘Forest to Ocean’, a seafood dish, expresses the cycles of nature. Knowledge gained and ideas conceived in his travels resonate in the creations on the plate.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
61;Joël Robuchon;Japan;Tokyo;Yebisu Garden Place, 1-13-1 Mita, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0062, Japan;35.641903;139.714528;51;true;true;French, Contemporary;Le Caviar Imperial tops the list in a procession of dishes, each a work of art on a plate. Breads and desserts roll by on a trolley for your selection. Joël Robuchon’s eponymous restaurant is a crystallisation of the great chef’s gastronomy. Carrying the torch for the Joël Robuchon esprit is Chef Kenichiro Sekiya, recipient of the prestigious Meilleurs Ouvriers de France (MOF) title. Sekiya is shaping the future of Japan’s culinary landscape, devising new recipes based on the teachings of his famous mentor.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
62;Quintessence;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Garden City Shinagawa Gotenyama, 6-7-29 Kitashinagawa, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 141-0001, Japan;35.624038;139.732977;23;false;false;French, Contemporary;Chef Shuzo Kishida is ever mindful of three key elements: ingredients, flame, seasoning. He is always trying to evolve on these fronts. His drive to create new recipes each season derives from constant fine-tuning of sensibility and accumulated experience. Goat’s-milk bavarois has been a speciality since the day Kishida opened his restaurant. Putting the spotlight on the future of French cuisine, Kishida also takes pride in turning out the next generation of chefs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
64;Xin Rong Ji (Xinyuan South Road);China Mainland;Beijing;1F, East Tower, Genesis Beijing, 8 Xinyuan South Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.94638;116.450148;23;true;false;Taizhou;This flagship of the chain has an elegant but relaxed dining space done out in modern Chinese style. The menu is essentially the same as at other branches, focusing on Taizhou cooking and fish from the East China Sea. But the 28-day-old baby Peking duck, which you have to pre-order, is available exclusively at this location. Try also the duck stew with fish maw and taro – the taro is so starchy and tender that it melts in your mouth.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
65;Chao Shang Chao (Chaoyang);China Mainland;Beijing;L406B, 4F, CP Center, 20 Jinhe East Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.910992;116.461892;60;true;false;Chao Zhou;Upon arrival at this upmarket restaurant, diners step into a hallway lined with steeply priced dried fish maws. With years of experience in Hong Kong and Shanghai, Chef Cheung has revamped the menu with his new takes on Chaozhou classics – dishes such as braised eel wrapped in lotus leaf with dried tangerine peel and plum sauce show precision and finesse. Besides the vast wine list, the tea menu also brims with options that will tickle your fancy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
66;De Librije;Netherlands;Zwolle;Spinhuisplein 1, Zwolle, 8011 ZZ, Netherlands;52.5153644;6.0980183;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;De Librije is a culinary institution that has held three MICHELIN stars since 2004. Chef Jonnie and hostess Thérèse Boer are an inspiring power couple who are driving Dutch gastronomy forward. Sustainable regional produce, a focus on vegetables, inventive techniques, the use of fermentation for freshness and acidity. These terms are commonplace today, and that is partly thanks to chef Boer. He incorporates them into his very personal take on cuisine, which abounds with expressive flavours and memorable dishes. Pike-perch from the IJsselmeer, for example, is cooked until perfectly succulent, glazed with apple syrup that is not overly sweet, and topped with zolderspek (cured "attic bacon") that has been smoked in-house. A few well-thought-out vegetable garnishes and a beurre blanc made with Riesling round off this ode to the Dutch terroir. Diners tuck into their food in the extraordinary setting: the glass-covered courtyard of a former prison. Every detail hits the right note. From the tour of the kitchen with Jonnie to the private dining experience that completely immerses guests in the world of De Librije. Exemplary service from an attentive but discreet front-of-house team led by Thérèse, a consummate professional who knows how to perfectly complement the flavours on your plate with her wine pairings. In a word: sublime!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
68;JL Studio;Taiwan;Taichung;2F, 689, Section 4, Yifeng Road, Nantun District, Taichung, 408, Taiwan;24.1504863;120.6285199;45;false;true;Singaporean, Contemporary;JL stands for Jimmy Lim, a Singaporean chef who honed his skills in world-famous kitchens. His single evening set menu, Experience, pays tribute to his roots with original creations that strike a fine balance of flavours. The dishes are complex, sophisticated and understated with an element of surprise. Singaporean staples like satay and chilli crab are re-imagined in ingenious forms and textures that playfully subvert expectations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
69;Le Palais;Taiwan;Taipei;17F, Palais de Chine Hotel, 3, Section 1, Chengde Road, Datong District, Taipei, 103, Taiwan;25.0491625;121.5168892;23;true;true;Cantonese;After the departure of the Macanese chef, the kitchen is now helmed by the Hongkonger well-versed in Cantonese cooking. Rest assured that signature dishes like crispy Cantonese-style roast duck, Peking duck and white gourd stuffed with shrimp and crabmeat still taste as good as ever. Pre-order these items to avoid missing out. For dim sum, try Chinese spinach and salted egg dumplings with a colourful filling enrobed in a translucent skin.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
70;Addison;USA;San Diego;5200 Grand Del Mar Way, San Diego, 92130, USA;32.9412972;-117.1988908;88;true;true;Contemporary, Californian;Chef William Bradley has helmed the stoves at Addison since 2006, transforming this Southern Californian oasis into a world-class dining destination. Global inspiration and Californian sentimentality are at the heart of his approach, and no dish captures this better than sesame-seasoned Koshihikari rice finished with applewood-smoked sabayon and crowned with Regiis Ova reserve caviar. From chicken liver churros to a riff on chips and dip, dishes are playful yet polished. Opening bites, such as Kumamoto oysters with pickled green strawberry or Iberian ham folded over a gloriously golden potato, display finely tuned flavors. Shellfish-studded chawanmushi exemplifies masterful control over technique, flavors and textures. Meals conclude with a selection of stunning small bites.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
72;The French Laundry;USA;Yountville;6640 Washington St., Yountville, 94599, USA;38.40443;-122.36474;47;false;false;Contemporary, French;Thomas Keller’s legendary destination still doesn’t miss a beat. In fact this may be known as the greatest cooking space in America, as every aspect is carefully determined—from the counter height to the flowing lines of the ceiling. Chef Keller continues to pair classic French techniques with wildly fresh ingredients in a setting that is a perfect storm of restaurant greatness—we should all be so lucky to score a reservation here.Dinner may bring signature oysters with white sturgeon caviar in a warm sabayon studded with tapioca pearls, or Pacific shima aji tartare composed with puffed grains and a vibrant tomato and jalapeño "chiffon". Wolf Ranch quail is then presented with white asparagus and dark cherries, while "Coffee and Donuts" is a perfect finish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
73;Quince;USA;San Francisco;470 Pacific Ave., San Francisco, 94133, USA;37.7975054;-122.4032607;58;false;true;Contemporary, Californian;To mark its 20th anniversary, Chef Michael and Lindsay Tusk have given their restaurant a luxe refresh that has reinvigorated the early 1900's Jackson Square setting. The commitment to seasonality and locality is striking, with much of the produce sourced from their partner farm. Dinner here celebrates the season with an array of elegant presentations. A small bowlful of gently cooked first-of-the-season peas are served in a silky broth brimming with flavor from guanciale and Tomales Bay clam. Pasta has always been a highlight here, and the agnolotti filled with white asparagus is no exception. Local lamb cooked in the fireplace is arranged with a springtime melange of fava beans, green garlic, and edible blossoms, and accompanied by freshly baked bread tinted by vegetable ash.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
74;SingleThread;USA;Healdsburg;131 North St., Healdsburg, 95448, USA;38.6122599;-122.8697229;30;false;false;Contemporary, Californian;Here, in the bucolic loveliness at the heart of Sonoma Wine Country, sense of place combines exquisitely with the deeply personal vision of owners Chef Kyle Connaughton and head farmer Katina Connaughton. The nearby 24-acre farm provides much of the bounty prepared in the kitchen, and the couple’s time in Japan informs the restaurant’s ethos and the kaiseki-influenced cuisine. The menu begins memorably with a botanical landscape interspersed with impeccable first bites that introduce the central themes of the meal: impeccable ingredients, precise knife technique, artistic presentation and pure, harmonious flavors. The expert use of the donabe (Japanese clay pot) is also a trademark and transforms seafood and vegetables alike into true delicacies.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
75;Benu;USA;San Francisco;22 Hawthorne St., San Francisco, 94105, USA;37.7853763;-122.3990601;73;true;true;Asian, Contemporary;Benu is an oasis in the center of the city. Patience seems to define this kitchen in its relentless pursuit of excellence, whether that may be perfecting technique or waiting for just the right moment to serve an ingredient at its peak. Meals begin with a series of highly technical small bites. While these delicacies alone may rival some of the country's most ambitious tasting menus, there's more. Faux-shark's fin and xiao long bao are a delightful classic, but Chef Corey Lee continues to reimagine and redefine his nightly offerings. Dishes like barbecued quail with house-made XO sauce and an elevated take on traditional Korean beef barbecue convey a distinct personality and reflect a singular marriage between contemporary Asian influences.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
76;Zén;;Singapore;41 Bukit Pasoh Road, 089855, Singapore;1.2796271;103.84042;18;true;true;European Contemporary;The celebrity chef of Frantzén fame opened his third Asian venture in this shophouse (c 1926). Diners are offered an aperitif and amuse-bouche on the first floor, before the eight-course neo-Nordic, seafood-heavy tasting menu with Japanese influences unfolds on the second floor. Fermented food is the leitmotif recurring in Swedish and Japanese diets, and this kitchen uses it occasionally to great effect. The friendly, thoughtful service is also a plus.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
77;Odette;;Singapore;National Gallery, #01-04, 1 St. Andrew's Road (entrance via Supreme Court wing's foyer), 178957, Singapore;1.2896459;103.8516;18;false;false;French Contemporary;Where better to find a priceless jewel of the Singapore dining scene than in The National Gallery? Chef Julien Royer and his highly accomplished kitchen make wonderful use of luxury ingredients of unimpeachable quality. Creative combinations, impeccable techniques and exquisite plating result in dishes that are as elegant as they are memorable. The understated and graceful room, overseen by a highly polished service team, provides the perfect backdrop.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
78;Les Amis;;Singapore;Shaw Centre, #01-16, 1 Scotts Road, 228208, Singapore;1.30626;103.83204;87;true;true;French;Haute cuisine is increasingly about the chef embracing creative freedom and dictating the whole experience. At the longstanding, singularly sophisticated and world-renowned Les Amis, the choice is yours. The prix-fixe menus present a wide range of modern French classics with occasional Asian twists, in which simple ingredient combinations and seasoning highlight the natural flavours. Consider booking the chef's table for an intimate experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
79;Hiša Franko;Slovenia;Kobarid;Staro selo 1, Kobarid, 5222, Slovenia;46.2472961;13.5382362;84;true;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Situated in the lush Soča valley with magnificent mountains as a backdrop, “Franko’s house” boasts a beautiful, welcoming, simple yet elegant ambience from the moment you enter the small room near the entrance where guests can enjoy an aperitif before their meal. Very few cuisines reflect the personality of the chef like that of Ana Roš Stojan. Her strong, determined, extrovert and contagiously friendly character is perfectly mirrored on a long tasting menu, on which dishes have intensive and decisive flavours with no half measures. Each course is a true discovery, in which local and Slovenian ingredients and traditions are skilfully combined with influences from elsewhere in the world with grace, good taste and the chef’s own inimitable style. Following on from the “50 shades of Life” menu (dedicated to the chef’s age), this year’s menu is entitled “50 shades of Red”, a colour which symbolises all the hard work at Hiša Franko, from the red of passion to the cuisine and the service of the brilliant and well-trained young staff. The wine-pairing choices are excellent, with three different options: one based on more classic wines, another which allows guests to explore natural wines and highly individual labels, and a third non-alcoholic option featuring home-made drinks. Among the house specialities which are nearly always present on the menu, don’t miss the corn beignet with fermented cottage cheese and smoked trout roe, and the hay-baked potatoes with fenugreek and roasted yeast-infused sour cream – the latter is a very simple dish that offers an interesting take on a childhood favourite. Should you decide to spend the night here, the copious and highly colourful breakfast is equally recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
80;Frantzén;Sweden;Stockholm;Klara Norra Kyrkogata 26, Stockholm, 111 22, Sweden;59.3341673;18.0597575;90;false;false;Modern Cuisine;World-renowned Chef Björn Frantzén provides a truly immersive experience that you won't forget in a hurry at his uber-stylish restaurant. Ring the bell to enter, before enjoying an aperitif in the top-floor lounge while the day's ingredients are explained, then head to the dining room with its beautiful counter seating to witness the exceptionally talented chefs at work as they craft creative, perfectly executed dishes. The service works like clockwork to enhance the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
81;noma;Denmark;Copenhagen;Refshalevej 96, Copenhagen, 1432 K, Denmark;55.6833118;12.6106175;78;true;false;Creative;This elegant yet relaxed waterside restaurant offers a unique experience, from the greenhouses at the entrance to the ingredients on the plate. The test kitchen is one of the most advanced in the world and offers a tasting menu of creative, complex dishes with vivid natural flavours. Professional, informal service puts guests at ease. Book well in advance.;Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
82;Jordnær;Denmark;Gentofte;Gentoftegade 29, Gentofte, 2800, Denmark;55.7481416;12.5412347;87;true;true;Creative;Chef-Owner Eric Kragh Vildgaard is the driving force behind this remarkable dining experience, demonstrating enormous technical skill across his procession of bold and creative dishes, all founded on seafood and vegetable produce of the utmost quality. The cooking varies between the wisely restrained (the pure, precise hamachi, ponzu and wasabi) and the hyper-detailed (the stunningly plated, multi-layered chawanmushi). Tina oversees the charming service in this stylish and sophisticated oasis, which is expertly run at every turn.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
83;Geranium;Denmark;Copenhagen;Per Henrik Lings Allé, Parken National Stadium, Copenhagen, 2100 Ø, Denmark;55.7040847;12.5725289;75;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Located on the 8th floor of the National Football Stadium, this luxurious restaurant boasts panoramic park views and provides a truly singular dining experience. The surprise, meat-free tasting menu comprises many beautifully presented dishes, each one as highly creative and impeccably precise as the last. First-rate ingredients and exceptional technique combine to create layers of flavour in every mouthful, and the poised, disarmingly hospitable service team are equally impressive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
84;RE-NAA;Norway;Stavanger;Nordbøgata 8, Stavanger, 4006, Norway;58.9739705;5.7308447;28;true;false;Creative, Seafood;The kitchen quite literally takes centre stage at this impeccable restaurant, sitting in the middle of the stylish room and providing a stage for the chefs to prepare intricate, superbly crafted dishes. Top-notch local fish and shellfish underpins the cooking, with supreme skill evident in the refined balance between the delicate seafood flavours and some stronger components – the grilled scallop with sea buckthorn and pumpkin sauce is a perfect example. The menu has around 20 servings and every aspect unfolds masterfully thanks to the exceptional kitchen and service teams.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
85;Maaemo;Norway;Oslo;Dronning Eufemias gate 23, Oslo, 0194, Norway;59.9075293;10.7586363;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Time seems to stand still when you dine at this truly exceptional restaurant, such is its overwhelming quality. The unique dining experience begins with a drink in the cosy lounge before moving into a dramatic, high-ceilinged dining room with a theatrically lit open kitchen. A surprise seasonal tasting menu comprises a succession of expertly crafted, consistently memorable dishes that deliver sublime flavours and textures in superbly conceived combinations.;Air conditioning;[]
88;HAJIME;Japan;Osaka;1-9-11 Edobori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0002, Japan;34.688612;135.496084;37;false;false;Innovative;An artwork resembling a planet dominates the dining room. Look closely and the ‘planet’ contains overlapping images of cuisine, which gather together to form a picture of the Earth. ‘Dialogue with the Earth’ is, indeed, the theme of this restaurant. The experience of growing up amid the beauty of nature shaped the bold world view of Hajime Yoneda. The digitised recipes and detailed cuisine attest to his experience as a system engineer. Cuisine that draws inspiration from all Creation is imbued with love and respect for nature.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
89;Kikunoi Honten;Japan;Kyoto;459 Shimokawaracho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0825, Japan;35.001535;135.782079;47;true;false;Japanese;Kikunoi is spreading the word worldwide about the allure of Japanese cuisine. Yoshihiro Murata sets his sights on innovation while evangelising Kyoto’s graceful ryotei culture. Occasionally Western ingredients get added to the mix, infusing a contemporary sensibility. Change accumulates in layers here, as a result of shifting personnel: Chef Murata invites trainees from overseas to pass on to them the true nature of Japanese cuisine and Japanese traditions of service. Fixing his gaze on the future of Japanese cooking, Murata cultivates the next generation of chefs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Shoes must be removed;[]
90;Isshisoden Nakamura;Japan;Kyoto;136 Matsushitacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8093, Japan;35.010397;135.765083;40;true;false;Japanese;‘Isshisoden’ means ‘transmission of mysteries or secret techniques of a craft to successive generations of descendants’. Motokazu Nakamura trained his spirit at Tenryuji Temple to make himself feel worthy of being entrusted with them. From his priestly teacher the chef learned the phrase ‘Aji sunawachi kokoro nari’: delicious taste is the creation of a sincere heart. The flavours of white miso zoni and tilefish baked in sake are truths that cannot be expressed in words.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
92;Gion Sasaki;Japan;Kyoto;566-27 Komatsucho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0811, Japan;34.998881;135.775049;23;true;false;Japanese;The ‘Sasaki Theatre’ keeps on pressing forward. Taking the spotlight are the next generation of chefs, a blur of motion in the spacious kitchen that is their stage. A charcoal brazier is fixed at centre stage, in tribute to the primordial flame. To educate his young players, Hiroshi Sasaki solicits menu ideas from his apprentices. The cuisine that emerges from this exchange of ideas may well debut in future productions. The troupe works as one to depict the future of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
93;Kashiwaya Osaka Senriyama;Japan;Osaka;2-5-18 Senriyamanishi, Suita, Osaka, 565-0851, Japan;34.770287;135.501289;26;true;false;Japanese;Kashiwaya was the name of a ryokan inn once run by an ancestor of Chef Hideaki Matsuo. A devotee of Japanese culture and familiar with the tea ceremony, Matsuo inherited the restaurant as a family business. The menu pays homage to ancient seasonal festivals and events while adding creative touches with a view to the future. Although he runs the restaurant as a ryotei, Matsuo was an early adopter of the practice of pairing beverages with dishes. He is in constant search for the Japanese cuisine of the future.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Shoes must be removed;[]
94;ES:SENZ;Germany;Grassau;Mietenkamer Straße 65, Grassau, 83224, Germany;47.7856302;12.4656176;21;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Here in the restaurant of Das Achental hotel, Edip Sigl impresses diners with his distinctive culinary style. His dishes are modern, sophisticated and packed with flavour and intense contrasts. However, they always remain wonderfully balanced. For example, the fantastic Mieral pigeon is given a nice barbecued note with a roasted finish and served with a harmonious onion and beetroot filling in a crispy baked tart and slices of intense-flavoured Périgord truffle. Diners choose from two set menus comprising six or eight courses dubbed "Chiemgau pur" and "Chiemgau goes around the world". As the names suggest, the first is dedicated entirely to premium produce from the Chiemgau region, while the second combines local and international ingredients. Be it Balfego tuna, brown trout or lamb, the quality of the produce is outstanding! The sophistication of the cuisine is matched by the courteous waitstaff, who also provide sound wine recommendations. Tip: Ask for a table by the large window front in the chic dining space for a view of the garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
95;Waldhotel Sonnora;Germany;Dreis;Auf'm Eichelfeld 1, Dreis, 54518, Germany;49.9377323;6.8109342;41;true;false;Classic French;This legendary fine dining establishment has an exemplary pair of hosts in husband-and-wife team Magdalena and Clemens Rambichler. In the kitchen, the chef cultivates the house specialities, such as "Kleine Torte" of beef tenderloin tartare with N25 caviar, but also showcases his own style. Top-notch ingredients are precisely prepared, down to the last detail, without the importance of flavour ever being lost from sight. This starts with the amuse-bouches (a veritable explosion of flavours!), followed, for example, by the excellent firm-fleshed, charcoal-grilled turbot from the Vendeé – which has a wonderful smoky aroma – harmoniously combined with terrific fresh black morels, fine white asparagus and a very elegant PX sherry note in the classic beurre noisette. The set menu features two intriguing wine pairings. You can also dine à la carte. Magdalena Rambichler is always on hand, cordial and extremely competent as she heads up the service team. The decor is stylish, elegant and discreetly modern. The inviting individually designed guestrooms are equally fabulous.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
96;The Table Kevin Fehling;Germany;Hamburg;Shanghaiallee 15, Hamburg, 20457, Germany;53.5426398;10.0028597;27;false;false;Creative, International;In his set menu (dubbed "Das Tor zur Welt" – "Gateway to the World"), Kevin Fehling makes use of a wide variety of ingredients – Asian, Middle Eastern and South American – and also likes to combine these, crossover style, with classic French-based cuisine. An array of wonderfully complementary flavours turn creations such as "The Sea – poached oyster, hamachi, sea urchin & horseradish" or "Ballotine of quail, aubergine, kumquat, argan oil cream & saffron broth" into characteristic dishes that shine in terms of the quality of the produce, precision, and depth of flavour. In the stylish, relaxed atmosphere at the long and winding table after which the restaurant is named, you can see the action unfold in the kitchen – everything runs like a well-oiled machine or an orchestra! Restaurant manager David Eitel, part of the charming, attentive service team, who interact with guests in a laid-back manner, should also be mentioned.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
97;Aqua;Germany;Wolfsburg;Parkstraße 1, Wolfsburg, 38440, Germany;52.4328494;10.7899785;50;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The Ritz-Carlton is located in the heart of Volkswagen's fascinating Autostadt, and here – somewhat hidden away at the end of a corridor on the ground floor – is a truly worthwhile destination for any gourmet: Aqua. The design is elegant and sleek, and the service is professional yet pleasingly informal and charming – there's no need to be intimidated by three-star cuisine here! The dishes are impressively innovative, occasionally surprising and feature remarkably bold combinations. Named "New Discovery" and "My Solidarity", the set menus feature exciting dishes such as Saibling char and its caviar with yellow carrot, shiso and miso, or pigeon à l'étouffée, bean and preserved lemon. The hallmark of Sven Elverfeld's style is clear – he has a knack for presenting complex dishes with apparent ease. To sum up: This place is all about eating, experiencing and enjoying!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
99;Restaurant Bareiss;Germany;Baiersbronn;Hermine-Bareiss-Weg 1, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5205845;8.3269876;56;false;false;Classic French;Claus-Peter Lumpp is truly a master of his trade! Since March 1992, the native Swabian has been head chef at the Bareiss fine dining restaurant and is, so to speak, part of the furniture. His cuisine is still classically French in style, but he also incorporates modern elements. He combines, for example, top fresh and tender roasted langostino with pumpkin in the form of jelly, fine slices and puree as well as a crustacean sauce with tremendous strength and flavour expression, refined with a bit of ginger. The wonderful cheese trolley deserves a mention, and the trolley of sweets and chocolates is equally enticing. Then there is the refined atmosphere, which is in no small part down to the excellent service provided under the tutelage of Thomas Brandt, a maître d' of the old school. Sommelier Teoman Mezda provides excellent wine recommendations. It's a bonus that you can also enjoy this at lunchtime!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
100;Rutz;Germany;Berlin;Chausseestraße 8, Berlin, 10115, Germany;52.5283507;13.3860867;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Let yourself be taken on a "journey" courtesy of Marco Müller's "Inspiration" tasting menu, over the course of which he applies his own clear culinary style to skilfully build a narrative arc. The pleasant team will explain the ideas behind the dishes in a relaxed and informal way and are happy to answer questions. The menu features terrific ingredients such as Wagyu beef from Germany, the distinctive flavour of which is in a class of its own, and squid (an invasive species from the North Sea). From rabbit tartare or dry-aged carp, some of the dishes here are sure to surprise even experienced foodies at times – in an absolutely positive way! It is remarkable how the best products are showcased here while retaining their authenticity - everything looks so effortless and yet is full of complexity. In summer, the best place to sit is on the small but inviting terrace. If you are in Berlin, don't miss the opportunity to try this cuisine!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
101;Victor's Fine Dining by christian bau;Germany;Perl;Schlossstraße 27, Perl, 66706, Germany;49.5351732;6.3872109;23;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Few chefs could bring together the flavours of French and Japanese cuisine more distinctively than Christian Bau. Elements of both styles can be found in his "Paris-Tokyo" set menu, a fine example being his mackerel with caviar, buttermilk, yuzu kosho and chives, served on an elaborate Japanese waffle. His meticulous craftsmanship is second to none, as is the exceptional quality of the produce. He skilfully incorporates fresh ideas while remaining true to his own unique style. His dishes are perfectly balanced and full of finesse, but most of all they are truly original. There is also a range of "specials" with which to supplement the set menu. Charming and professional service. You can spend an elegant stay at Victor's Residenz-Hotel Schloss Berg.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
104;La Table du Castellet;France;Le Castellet;3001 route des Hauts-du-Camp, au Circuit Paul Ricard, Le Castellet, 83330, France;43.2499288;5.7838874;23;false;false;Creative;The walls of this well-known luxury resort is a haven of Provençal bliss from the grounds overlooking the Var hinterland and the sea on the horizon to the ponds, lavender beds and superb cuisine rich in the scents and flavours of the South of France. Former sous-chef to Christophe Bacquié, Fabien Ferré is going from strength to strength and his artistic sensitivity for Mediterranean produce calls to mind Matisse, who was captivated by the light of Provence. Ferré crafts a high-flying veggie and seafood score, starring dishes such as shrimp carabineros with Meyer lemon and coral roe sauce, or squid in marjoram. His refined and virtuoso cuisine elevates the natural flavour of the ingredients, bolstered by memorable full-bodied sauces, a case in point being the aloe vera-scented vinaigrette that accompanies the mackerel fillet. It is arguably worth the trip here just for the cheese cellar, without forgetting the terrific selection of wines and a heavenly terrace for an aperitif and coffee.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
105;Plénitude - Cheval Blanc Paris;France;Paris;8 quai du Louvre, Paris, 75001, France;48.8588148;2.3421588;59;true;true;Creative;The revamped Samaritaine department store is home to the luxurious Cheval Blanc Hotel, within whose walls lies this restaurant, the haunt of low-profile chef, Arnaud Donckele, who has three stars to his name at La Vague d'Or in St Tropez. Wholly committed, he pops in and out of the kitchen to share his passion with diners. His new spin on classical cuisine takes you on a voyage between Normandy, his place of birth, and the Mediterranean, his home of adoption and the Paris region… It is impossible not to be bowled over by his work, from its delicacy and generosity to the exceptional quality of the ingredients. This virtuoso sauce maker, who can be compared with a perfume “nose” or an oenologist, lavishes phenomenal care and attention over his jus, dressings and sauces which should be tasted first to better appreciate the complex aromatic universe of each dish. When it comes to the sweet course, he can count on Maxime Frédéric, previously of the George V, to take the desserts to a whole new dimension. The absolute pinnacle of fine dining.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
106;Le Petit Nice;France;Marseille;Anse de Maldormé, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2802565;5.3520484;56;true;false;Seafood;Le Petit Nice is inextricably linked to the city of Marseille and to Gérald Passedat's personality. The heir to a family of artists, the chef was practically born in this restaurant just a stone’s throw from the Mediterranean “that carries and inspires (me)”. The Mediterranean Sea, its fish and shellfish are the backbone of his culinary identity, whose fascinating facets come to the fore in his “Ma Bouille Abaisse”, a signature dish among signature dishes. As you begin to eat, you will appreciate the subtle progression of intense flavours of this bouillabaisse that is both familiar yet complex. After kicking off with a superb rosette of raw fish in a clear stock, the feast continues with other fish escorted by a more distinctive saffron stock, to end with a grand finale of whole cooked fish in a big-boned soupe de roche. Depending on the season, over 65 types of fish are used in the kitchen fished by small boats with long lines in respect of the marine ecosystem, which is only fitting given the establishment’s fantastic seafront location.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
107;Mirazur;France;Menton;30 avenue Aristide-Briand, Menton, 06500, France;43.7859304;7.5280514;56;true;false;Creative;Argentine chef Mauro Colagreco has taken up residence on the Italian border, between the mountains and the sea, in a restaurant boasting mesmerising views of the Mediterranean. His culinary creations now reflect the lunar calendar, with ingredients being gathered and dishes being concocted in accordance with the phases of the moon – an ancient practice revived by followers of biodynamic agriculture. He harvests his plants at peak ripeness to create daily alternating set menus based on realms of nature such as "flowers", "fruit", "leaves" and "roots". This exacting philosophy allows the chef to get the very best from his vast vegetable gardens, as well as from his hand-picked supply of fish, shellfish and meat. Delivered by a talented kitchen team, his cuisine is in no danger of falling into routine. As technically flawless as the dishes may be, they remain thoroughly accessible, prioritising flavours that are combined in perfect harmony.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
109;Pic;France;Valence;285 avenue Victor-Hugo, Valence, 26000, France;44.9176875;4.8855601;78;false;true;Creative;The first thing to mention about Maison Pic (in the Drôme département of southeast France) is its special atmosphere. An artfully lit room designed to cast light on the dishes, floral creations, a thick carpet that muffles the steps of a front-of-house team dressed in classic attire. Here, they serve food the old-fashioned way, on a porcelain plate under a cloche. The lofty culinary obsessions of a chef who has been dubbed "the tightrope walker of flavours" – adulation of Japan, original presentations – make themselves felt in the dishes. Anne-Sophie Pic now serves a single set menu with ten "ports of call". A member of the highly exclusive club of female three-starred chefs, she is now director of the foundation "Donnons du goût à l'enfance". Beyond her boundless talent, she is an iconic figure.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
110;Pierre Gagnaire;France;Paris;6 rue Balzac, Paris, 75008, France;48.8732506;2.3003862;27;false;false;Creative;In an interior dominated by a masterful charcoal work, an "urban cave painting" depicting a bestiary by the artist Adel Abdessemed, Pierre Gagnaire continues to finetune France’s culinary scene with his adventurous, wholehearted and excessive signature cuisine. This fan of jazz and contemporary art never rests on his laurels. Gagnaire's restaurant, which has had three stars since 1996, reflects his character: modern, understated and subtly sophisticated, all of which is in perfect harmony with the service. The poetic dishes are constantly reinvented, like small "satellite" portions sent into orbit by the chef, making it impossible to cite a single emblematic dish, or even a main characteristic – other than sheer excellence!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
111;Flocons de Sel;France;Megève;1775 route du Leutaz, Le Leutaz, Megève, 74120, France;45.8302404;6.5969625;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;(Temporarily closed, reopening planned for second half of 2025) Emmanuel Renaut fell in love with Haute Savoie as a child, long before achieving his Meilleur Ouvrier de France title, and his predilection for Alpine produce is deeply ingrained (pike, char and whitefish from Lake Geneva, mushrooms and wild herbs, mountain cheeses). At times he has fun subverting the regional cooking that is expected of him – a case in point being his superb langoustines marinated in citron, caviar with zesty grapefruit and gentian roots. Plants are also given an increasingly important role in his cuisine. An enchanting high-altitude chalet at the summit of fine dining.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
112;Alléno Paris au Pavillon Ledoyen;France;Paris;8 avenue Dutuit, Paris, 75008, France;48.8660932;2.3164993;69;true;true;Creative;This prestigious Parisian institution housed in an elegant building set in the Jardins des Champs-Élysées has huge windows looking out onto the most beautiful avenue in the world. It is the very epitome of the great French restaurant: the luxurious setting, the culture of beautifully dressed tables, the seamlessly orchestrated service – it all makes for a unique backdrop, fit to showcase gastronomy in all its glory. Chef Yannick Alléno has achieved a real tour de force by stamping his hallmark on the menu from the outset. His cuisine is dazzling and technical, and his jus and sauces (what the chef calls "the verb of French cuisine"), enhanced by skilful extractions, deserve a special mention. This is what happens when the avant-garde puts itself at the service of the great French culinary tradition.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
114;Le Pré Catelan;France;Paris;Route de Suresnes - bois de Boulogne, Paris, 75016, France;48.8639374;2.2507182;85;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;How time flies! Frédéric Anton has been the chef of the Pré Catalan, the legendary Napoleon III lodge nestled in the Bois de Boulogne and refurbished by Pierre-Yves Rochon courtesy of designer furniture and a palette of green, white and silver tones, for over 25 years. Born in Nancy, this celebrity chef and Meilleur Ouvrier de France learned the ropes under Joël Robuchon. His tasting menu, which stars top-drawer produce (scallops, langoustine, salmon, caviar) is a masterclass of high-flying understatement and razor-sharp precision. His culinary score, which rises to a crescendo of pure perfection, bears witness to the chef’s experience and vision of fine dining. Not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
115;Le Cinq;France;Paris;Four Seasons Hotel George V, 31 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.8687604;2.3008612;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Unadulterated style and opulence - lofty columns, ornate mouldings and bouquets of fresh flowers, all bathed in soft light pouring in from the interior garden... It is here, in one of the most prestigious luxury hotels of Paris, that chef Christian Le Squer works his magic year after year, earning our greatest respect. His timeless cuisine, ever at the service of outstanding produce, unveils his virtuoso technique and phenomenal delicacy, illustrated by a foaming vin jaune-flavoured butter sauce served with lobster or the delicate cream of cauliflower that flanks sea urchin roe. This lad from Morbihan never ceases to pay tribute to his native Brittany in the heart of Paris, celebrating the region with ingredients like soured milk served with caviar and seabass or salted butter with lobster. On the dessert side, pastry wizard Michael Bartocetti composes a high-flying score inspired by nature, forgoing sugar in favour of fruit and honey. Finally, the service under the auspices of Eric Beaumard (also an outstanding sommelier) is a model of empathy and style that is close to perfection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
118;Épicure;France;Paris;Le Bristol, 112 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75008, France;48.8717223;2.3145978;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The Bristol is the quintessence of luxury from its lavish suites and spa to its manicured formal garden, rooftop pool and the dining area appointed with Louis XVI furnishings, mirrors, and tall French windows opening onto a lush green patio. Chef Arnaud Faye has brilliantly taken over the helm of the hotel’s fine dining venue with a light, delicate repertory that errs towards minimalist. Purity depicts each crisp legible flavour, further enhanced by generous helpings. The ingredients are of course irreproachable and the technique flawless, while the sauces feature a subtle blend of suave yet gutsy, without forgetting the art-directed plating or even the bread, which is made on the premises from heirloom varieties of wheat.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
119;Arpège;France;Paris;84 rue de Varenne, Paris, 75007, France;48.8557538;2.3170127;77;true;true;Creative;"The best cookbook ever written was by Mother Nature herself," according to Alain Passard. His name is associated with vegetables – and, for those in the know, a certain beetroot in a salt crust. He called it before anyone else with his 100% vegetable-based menu, initially considered radical. Nowadays, his green philosophy is de rigueur at every restaurant. Despite his success, the chef who fetes fruit and flowers never feels more at home than when in one of his three kitchen gardens in the west of France, where his twin vocations of cook and gardener meet. He heads there for inspiration, exploring the culinary possibilities of vegetables in a bid to elevate this ordinary ingredient so often relegated to the status of a side dish. A bucolic fresco references this environment in the restaurant's dining room.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
120;Le Louis XV - Alain Ducasse à l'Hôtel de Paris;France;Monaco;Place du Casino, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7391839;7.4271047;38;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;It is difficult to present the Louis XV without mentioning Alain Ducasse. You need a raft of superlatives to describe his impact. This native of Orthez (in southwest France) with an enduring love for the Mediterranean is a brilliant chef and businessman. Now a citizen of Monaco, he also heads up an empire of over 30 establishments with a presence on every continent. He was just 33 years old when he was awarded three stars at the Louis XV after reaching an astonishing standard. His famous vegetable-based "Jardins de Provence" set menu, which launched here in Monaco on 27 May 1987, has been one of the touchstones of French gastronomy for the last 30 years. Here, Alain Ducasse's signature style is brought to life by his loyal right-hand man, Emmanuel Pilon, in cuisine that masterfully celebrates the essence of the ingredients and the Mediterranean.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
121;Restaurant Marcon;France;Saint-Bonnet-le-Froid;Larsiallas, 18 chemin de Brard, Saint-Bonnet-le-Froid, 43290, France;45.1386734;4.4342679;38;false;true;Creative;The Marcons are a family team: Régis Marcon Senior, a self-proclaimed Auvergnat-Italian, an exceptional cook, an entrepreneur and a culinary authority, works with his sons, Jacques and Paul. Jacques is confidently moving to the forefront, while Paul has recently joined the team. Here, one thing is clear: the market and the seasons dictate the menu. There is something for everyone: meat from the plateau, Le Puy green lentils, asparagus, broad beans, snails and, above all, mushrooms – the family's speciality, which they pick in autumn. This is food with strong roots – think sautéed early girolles and baby garden carrots glazed in wild lovage, or a gently fried fillet of arctic char and fennel confit in a butter of elderflower. Without forgetting, the cheeseboard, laden with Salers, Fourme and Saint-Nectaire - quite irresistible!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
122;Kei;France;Paris;5 rue du Coq-Héron, Paris, 75001, France;48.8643947;2.3422847;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Kei for Kei Kobayashi, a chef born in Nagano, Japan, who trained with the likes of Gilles Goujon and Alain Ducasse. His father was a cook in a traditional kaiseki restaurant (where high-flying meals are served in small courses – akin to Western haute cuisine), but it was while watching a documentary on French cuisine that he found his vocation. Today, his work verges on perfection: a virtuoso blend of flavours and exquisite plating, he allows high-quality ingredients to shout their name simply and stunningly. For example, binchotan smoked royal langoustine sweet pepper seasoning or Vendée pigeon lacquered in red miso. Each dish is flawlessly crafted and supremely legible. The desserts also attain head-spinning heights of culinary excellence.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
123;Les Prés d'Eugénie - Michel Guérard;France;Eugénie-les-Bains;Place de l'Impératrice, Eugénie-les-Bains, 40320, France;43.696604;-0.3797229;78;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Some chefs owe their reputation as much to their cuisine as to their human qualities: Michel Guérard, who died in August 2024, was one of them. Considered one of the founding fathers of "la nouvelle cuisine", admired by his peers the world over, he always put the same passion and dedication into his work, leaving his kitchen teams and family an incomparable gastronomic heritage. At Les Prés d'Eugénie, you get the full experience: the enchanting setting of a gorgeous mansion set in the verdant grounds, a front-of-house team with laser-like attention to the smallest of details… and, above all, cooking that is exceptional in every way. The dishes reflect the DNA of Chef Guérard: a showcasing of naturalist cuisine, of course, an omnipresent lightness of touch, and the ability to marry the most diverse flavours with great precision, like a conductor guiding an orchestra. The restaurant is located in the wood-panelled apartments of the Empress, which are steeped in the history of the building.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
126;La Vague d'Or - Cheval Blanc St-Tropez;France;Saint-Tropez;Plage de la Bouillabaisse, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2665849;6.6261535;94;false;false;Creative;Picture a luxury hotel set amidst pine trees in the picturesque Gulf of Saint Tropez - an idyllic scene for knockout food. Dedicated and demanding, chef Arnaud Donckele pays a vibrant tribute to this sun-drenched landscape. He starts with a painstaking study of the local fish in a bid to devise recipes that reveal the full scope of each species’ nuances, textures and tastes in a range of compositions that are infinitely varied. Each ingredient is of course flawlessly crafted, but the chef’s strong suit is undeniably sauces, referred to as “ephemeral” or “velvety”, and which are both big boned and delicate. In fact, their names already read like a guide to the Mediterranean underworld: sabayon of a reduction of scarlet prawns flavoured with star anise and marigold, “creamy little blue fish from the sea” flavoured with tomatoes and riquette, stock of abalone and shellfish in lemon flavoured olive oil… His turf recipes are equally high flying and embody a constant quest for the perfect tomato, pepper or courgette to underscore pigeon, lamb or sweetbread. An exceptional experience every time!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
129;Georges Blanc;France;Vonnas;Place du Marché, Vonnas, 01540, France;46.2201083;4.9894987;69;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This Bourg-en-Bresse native whose ancestors used to make lemonade and sell coal has come a long way! That said, Georges Blanc's grandmother was once named best cook in the world by food writer Curnonsky. Nowadays the chef is at the head of a small empire in Vonnas. Out of a 100m2 house, he has built an estate of several hectares: the illuminated village gardens and houses are a magical sight at night. But the show also takes place at your table, where the Bresse province is represented by its emblematic poularde AOP, and deep-flavoured sauces and skilful cooking techniques come into their own. Georges Blanc is the oldest Michelin-starred establishment in the world, having received its first star in 1929. It will also delight fans of fine wines, with a wine list to make Bacchus blush.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
130;Le 1947 à Cheval Blanc;France;Courchevel;Cheval Blanc, Le Jardin Alpin, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4094877;6.6338696;87;false;true;Creative;Yannick Alléno has trodden a remarkable path! At one great restaurant after another, the chef from the Paris region has always been adept at channelling his passion into fulfilling his ambition. Within the Hôtel Cheval Blanc, he regales a few lucky diners (just five tables) with a striking repertoire of contemporary cuisine, in which creativity and audacity are entirely guided by the quest for flavours. The Savoie region is shown in its best light through his use of superb ingredients, each of these edible treasures being prepared with the greatest care. This chef's true passion are his sauces, which are truly unforgettable – they are the fruit of a long-term labour of love revolving around extraction and fermentation, as well as consummate technical skill: a master class in haute cuisine.;Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
131;La Marine;France;L'Herbaudière;3 rue Marie-Lemonnier, L'Herbaudière, 85330, France;47.0237104;-2.2999341;89;false;false;Creative, Seafood;Alexandre Couillon rises at dawn to go to Noirmoutier fish auction, which sells the best Atlantic fish, before stopping by his own vegetable garden, just a few minutes from the restaurant. The tasting menu, which religiously keeps pace with the seasons and availability, exalts and celebrates fine ingredients, allowing them to shout their name with a simplicity that only the world’s top chefs can attain. Knowing what and where to strip back and pare down to release the flavours and tantalise the eater’s imagination is a fine art. The quality of the fish, seafood and vegetables is exceptional. Alexandre’s other talents include cooking over a fire, harvesting coastal plants, fruit coulis and vegetable pickles, broth and gutsy jus, without forgetting cooking fish to absolute perfection! Memories shine bright of both the mackerel cooked over hot embers and accompanied by confit beetroot or an incredible lettuce grilled over a flame, blueberries in elderflower vinegar and the dessert of buckwheat, caramel mousse, confit citrus fruits and sea lettuce (seaweed) sorbet. The interior has been revamped in natural materials and soft colours, while the grocery shop, Le Petit Couillon, sells produce from the artisans and farmer partners.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
133;Le Clos des Sens;France;Annecy;13 rue Jean-Mermoz - à Annecy-le-Vieux, Annecy, 74940, France;45.9176317;6.1445765;19;true;true;Creative;This spruce establishment in the upper reaches of Annecy is home to Franck Derouet and his associate Thomas Lorival. Together they craft a culinary repertory whose veggie and lake-focused slant is clearly founded on a locavore philosophy as everything comes from their own garden or within a 100km radius. Each dish is sprinkled with seasonal fruit, vegetables, flowers and herbs, adding a poetic and modern art flourish. Their work with fish from the lake involves in-depth reflection about texture and cooking methods, resulting in dishes like raw fera (lake fish) enhanced by a powerful garum, fermented over several weeks, or aged pike grilled like red meat. In a bid to respect the seasons, the chef may introduce the odd carnivorous note into his menu, particularly during the angling close season. As well as a wine list exclusively from local wineries, the establishment offers “food and jus” pairings of vegetable stocks, broths and herbal teas with different dishes that explore new tasting and aromatic horizons, while celebrating the manifest camaraderie and common ethos that motivate the kitchen and front of house teams. A genuine banquet for the senses.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
135;Caprice;;Hong Kong;6F, Four Seasons Hotel, 8 Finance Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2866489;114.1566097;39;false;false;French Contemporary;One of Hong Kong's most glamorous and elegant restaurants, Caprice also boasts impressive harbour views and always delivers an amazing experience. The harmonious, high-calibre French cuisine features premium ingredients, demonstrates superb techniques and shows a mastery of flavours. Only prix-fixe menus are served: four or five courses at lunch, and two seven-course options at dinner. Check out the stunning wine list and dazzling selection of cheeses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
136;8 1/2 Otto e Mezzo - Bombana;;Hong Kong;Shop 202, 2F, Alexandra House, 18 Chater Road, Central, Hong Kong;22.2814635;114.15867;77;false;false;Italian;Owner-chef Umberto Bombana’s restaurant oozes Italian charm and passion on every level and is named after the Fellini film – one of his favourites. The Italian classics are made with the best ingredients and the cooking showcases their true flavours. Don’t miss the house-made pasta and ask about the seasonal offerings. The buonissimo food, along with personable and professional service, makes for an unforgettable experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
137;Jade Dragon;;Macau;2F, The Shops at the Boulevard, City of Dreams, Estrada do Istmo, Cotai, Macau;22.149137;113.56715;57;false;false;Cantonese;This lavish room is a destination in itself – Chinese art, ebony, crystal, jade, gold and silver are all used to great effect but they don’t outshine the food. The head chef has a passion for recipes deeply rooted in Cantonese traditions, but jazzed up with modern techniques and exotic ingredients from around the world. Besides the double-boiled tonic soups with herbal medicine, seasonal offerings such as roasted prime rib with chilli are also a delight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
138;Forum;;Hong Kong;1F, Sino Plaza, 255-257 Gloucester Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong;22.2813972;114.1821905;33;false;false;Cantonese;Co-founder and chef of this upmarket spot, the late Yeung Koon-yat – aka the "abalone king" – created the iconic Ah Yat braised abalone decades ago. To this day, it remains the speciality that attracts food-loving crowds from near and far. As well as the tender and flavourful abalone, classics such as pan-seared leopard coral grouper fillet and baked stuffed crab shell are nicely made. The extensive wine list showcases boutique wineries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
140;L'Atelier de Joël Robuchon;;Hong Kong;Shop 401, 4F, Landmark Atrium, 15 Queen's Road Central, Hong Kong;22.281199;114.15816;85;true;false;French Contemporary;With his "ateliers" around the world, Joël Robuchon is now a brand synonymous with modern French fine dining. The emblematic red and black colour scheme and long counter with an intimate view of the kitchen are as much of a signature as the cooking, which embodies refinement, astuteness and finesse. From the bread basket to the petit fours, the focus is always on top-notch globally sourced produce and solid classic skills.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
141;T'ang Court;;Hong Kong;1-2F, The Langham Hotel, 8 Peking Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.296572;114.1698;56;true;true;Cantonese;It’s easy to see why this restaurant remains so popular after opening its doors 30-plus years ago. Comfort and luxury are factors, thanks to the plush fabrics, beautifully dressed tables and Chinese art. But the ability and experience of the head chef and his kitchen play an even bigger part. Their soups made with top notch ingredients win the hearts of countless connoisseurs. Other specialities include Peking duck, and baked stuffed crab shell.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
142;Sushi Shikon;;Hong Kong;7F, The Landmark Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 15 Queen's Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.2806103;114.1577893;98;true;true;Sushi;Hailing from Tokyo, the head chef Kakinuma is a master in ageing raw fish for deeper and fuller flavours. Some are aged together with pickled fish entrails that add exceptional umami. He takes meticulous care to keep flavours of each piece pristine without interfering with the next. Apart from sushi, Shimane abalone steamed in sake is also a highlight. The elegant interior design and artisan dinnerware befit the sophisticated food.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
143;Zilte;Belgium;Antwerpen;Hanzestedenplaats 5, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.228828;4.4047543;91;false;false;Creative;Zilte strives to offer a global emotional experience, starting with the view of the city skyline from the top floor of the Museum aan de Stroom. The understated designer interior is elegant and cosy, offset by the chef’s old record player which adds a nostalgic jazzy note. Everything is spot on from the gracious welcome and the wine waiter’s savvy tips to the sweet treats served with coffee. Viki Geunes has stripped his restaurant of everything but the essentials, starting with outstanding quality ingredients as he harnesses his creative flair to make each dish a masterpiece of excellence. For example, Geunes may add a tempura of sea urchin, thinly sliced hearts of palm, cream of celery and an unusual mandarin-flavoured miso to immaculately cooked langoustine. He may then also craft a second dish with the same ingredients, surprising us with a whole new repertory of textures. This fastidiously meticulous chef delicately plays with each texture and flavour, conjuring up food that is complex and gutsy, yet free of fussy frills. Now add sauces to die for and exotic side dishes with a surprising, yet mild spicy note and the portrait of Viki Geunes’ consummate skill and talent is complete.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
144;Boury;Belgium;Roeselare;Rumbeeksesteenweg 300, Roeselare, 8800, Belgium;50.9374466;3.1403981;61;true;false;Creative French;The brick villa of Tim Boury and Inge Waeles sets the scene for a splendid example of modern gastronomy from the attentive service and felicitous wine-food pairings by sommelier Mathieu Vanneste to the fashionably stylish interior and the gorgeous patio and bar. Every detail has clearly been meticulously masterminded, but with an eye on maintaining a casual vibe, proving that perfection is not necessarily starched and stuffy. Chef Boury’s painstaking recipes mingle classicism with creative peps and he cannot be equalled for his ability to enhance exceptional ingredients. His cuisine attains a pinnacle of high-flying virtuosity, whether by the complexity of flavours and textures or by a prodigious sauce that hits the spot every time. To give you an example, we sampled a partridge dish, the memory of which lingers with us still. The succulent breast was first served on a bed of creamy Jerusalem artichoke risotto, buttery cèpe mushrooms and a stunning sauce made from partridge gravy with a hint of liquorice. The second dish featured a crusty pastry case of confit partridge thighs, sweet onions and fresh almonds, all of which coated in white Alba truffle shavings. A unique fine dining experience from start to finish, depicted by striking flavours, raw ingredients, velvety and crunchy textures and divine seasonings, all of which underpinned by wholesome Flemish earthiness. Tim Boury is definitely at the apex of international haute cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
145;L'Enclume;United Kingdom;Cartmel;Cavendish Street, Cartmel, LA11 6QA, United Kingdom;54.2017708;-2.9538681;42;false;false;Creative British;Exceptional produce is the bedrock of everything they do at L’Enclume. Simon Rogan's 'Our Farm' provides ingredients that are picked daily and fashioned into a menu infused with Simon’s special brand of culinary alchemy. Every element is prepared with one eye on sustainability and another on maximum flavour, like the Orkney scallop dusted with a powder of its own roe. Everything is improved by the proud, enthusiastic service team and your visit can be enhanced in a number of ways: by a seat at the 'Aulis' chef's table, by a summertime tour round the farm or by a stay in one of the bedrooms spread about the village.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
146;Hélène Darroze at The Connaught;United Kingdom;London;Carlos Place, Mayfair, London, W1K 2AL, United Kingdom;51.510188;-0.1492905;75;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A wood-panelled dining room within the historic Connaught Hotel might suggest an overly formal environment for Hélène Darroze’s London restaurant, but the knowledgeable and sunny service team ensure the atmosphere is as bright and comfortable as the room itself. A set menu allows the talented kitchen to provide a balanced experience focused on the best seasonal produce, while some of the accompanying flavours are informed by Hélène’s international travels, like Isle of Mull lobster with tandoori spices. For dessert, the signature 'Baba' with a choice of Armagnacs from Hélène's brother Marc is a must.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
147;Alain Ducasse at The Dorchester;United Kingdom;London;Park Lane, Mayfair, London, W1K 1QA, United Kingdom;51.5073381;-0.152575;22;true;false;French;Executive Chef Jean-Philippe Blondet is bringing his own spin to the classical Francophone cooking of world-renowned chef Alain Ducasse. There's a newfound adventurousness to some of the dishes, like the regular injection of citrus, but what remains is the supreme technical skill and exceptional quality of the produce – some of which, like lobster and turbot, is from the luxury end of the scale. Some Ducasse signatures still shine through, like the peerless rum baba for dessert – if it isn't on the menu, be sure to ask for it.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
148;Fat Duck;United Kingdom;Bray;High Street, Bray, SL6 2AQ, United Kingdom;51.5078582;-0.7017529;56;true;true;Creative;For three decades, Heston Blumenthal has been blazing his own idiosyncratic trail at this iconic restaurant, where emotions and memories play a vital role in the enjoyment of the cooking. The dishes bear all the Heston hallmarks: innovative, playful and multi-sensory – epitomised by dishes like 'Off to the Land of Nod', a nostalgic dessert involving Horlicks, an eye mask and edible 'pillows'. Crucially, for all its originality, the cooking also showcases harmonious and utterly delicious flavours and textures. Charming, interactive service heightens the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
149;Sketch, The Lecture Room and Library;United Kingdom;London;9 Conduit Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 2XG, United Kingdom;51.5126775;-0.1415369;81;true;false;Modern French;There are few more joyously colourful and lavishly decorated restaurants than Mourad Mazouz and Pierre Gagnaire’s 18th-century house of fun. Everything comes with a sense of theatre, from the unfailingly attentive service to Gagnaire’s signature multi-dish cooking. Here, a skilfully roasted langoustine tail in liquorice beurre noisette is not enough, it must be contrasted by an array of complex accompanying dishes crafted with mind-blowing detail. Each element is always exceptionally cooked and the original combinations are brilliantly conceived.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
151;The Ledbury;United Kingdom;London;127 Ledbury Road, Notting Hill, London, W11 2AQ, United Kingdom;51.516681;-0.2000731;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;As one of the capital's finest restaurants, among The Ledbury's great strengths has always been Brett Graham's close relationship with his suppliers. In some cases that supplier is himself, with deer raised on their own small estate and the restaurant housing its own mushroom cabinet. These stunning ingredients are amplified by the chefs with beautifully balanced and harmonious combinations, like wild turbot paired with rich smoked eel, salty N25 caviar and the slight acidity of nashi pear. The service team are refreshingly approachable and have an impressive knack for putting everyone at ease.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
153;Waterside Inn;United Kingdom;Bray;Ferry Road, Bray, SL6 2AT, United Kingdom;51.5091092;-0.6994376;79;false;false;Classic French;Set in a picture perfect spot on a bank of the Thames, this long-standing bastion of culinary excellence continues to go from strength to strength. Luxury is at every turn, from the finest crockery to indulgent ingredients, and this, combined with the effortless service, creates a truly memorable dining experience. The menu lists newer creations alongside the French classics, with the kitchen’s exceptional craft on display throughout – be it in a sublime lobster jus or a textbook 'quenelle de brochet à la Lyonnaise'.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
154;Landhaus Bacher;Austria;Mautern an der Donau;Südtiroler Platz 2, Mautern an der Donau, 3512, Austria;48.393172;15.5794174;94;false;true;Classic Cuisine;A remarkable symbiosis of tradition and modernity has been created here. Thomas Dorfer's cuisine sees classic, elegant elements perfectly allied with Asian and Mediterranean influences, which, far from following fashionable trends, instead highlight special details, such as the fantastic BBQ sturgeon coated in sweet soy sauce, which harmonises beautifully with oven-cooked peppers, pata negra oil, grilled watermelon, fresh almonds and almond purée. There are four set menus to choose from, plus an appealing lunch set menu – but all dishes can be ordered individually. Senior chef Lisl Wagner-Bacher's classics, such as the baked egg with caviar, still feature on the menu. There is also an impressive selection of wines. The highly attentive service provided by a team led by restaurant manager and sommelier Susanne Dorfer-Bacher is top-notch too. Opt to dine inside in an elegant "country house" atmosphere, or in the gorgeous garden.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
155;Döllerer;Austria;Golling an der Salzach;Markt 56, Golling an der Salzach, 5440, Austria;47.5972979;13.1677057;76;true;true;Innovative, Alpine;There is something unique about Andreas Döllerer's cuisine. For some 20 years, his Alpine style has been his passion. In what he dubs his "Alpine Cuisine", he uses only excellent ingredients from the region. Building on classical foundations, he skilfully works in contrasts and textures to cook up innovative dishes such as "Gletscherrübe 23": dried, rehydrated and baked beetroot with a beetroot and black elder marinade and beetroot ice cream, served with soufflé-style Semmelkren (horseradish sauce) and a subtly spicy horseradish velouté, accompanied by tender Romanesco lettuce with a delicate elderflower vinaigrette. Excellent wine recommendations from Master Sommelier Alexander Koblinger – the vaulted wine cellar is home to over 3 700 different labels. Dishes are served in the elegant restaurant or on the beautiful terrace, which overlooks the "edible garden", where herbs, vegetables and fruit are grown for the kitchen. In this historical building in the heart of Golling, there are pretty, cosy guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
156;Ois;Austria;Neufelden;Unternberg 6, Neufelden, 4120, Austria;48.4814599;14.0023486;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Austrian;The Mühltalhof is a marvellous combination of traditional and modern. Not only do they have appealing guestrooms but also, most importantly, great food! Boasting a modern interior design characterised by chic black furnishings and fittings, Ois has just five tables. A 12-course set menu is prepared in kitchens that can be glimpsed through the open sliding door. Owner and chef Philip Rachinger has a style of his own, which is characterised by intense and skilfully combined flavours, not least in ‘Lake trout BBQ, chanterelles, yolk and lettuce’. The excellent service team includes a fantastic sommelier: charming, relaxed and professional Daniel Schicker recommends very interesting wine pairings. Alternatively, the second restaurant serves a four-course carte-blanche menu.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
157;Taubenkobel;Austria;Schützen am Gebirge;Hauptstraße 31, Schützen am Gebirge, 7081, Austria;47.8515574;16.6264336;57;true;true;French Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;A truly idyllic spot nestled in the sleepy little village of Schützen. This family business was run by Walter Eselböck for many years, and now his daughter Barbara and her husband, Alain Weissgerber, have taken over the reins. With a deft hand, the chef-patron creates dishes that seamlessly merge regional flavours, international inspirations and classic French techniques. A prime example is the super-fresh carabinero, grilled to perfection and served in its shell with a delicately spiced brunoise of local peppers and a nutty, aromatic beurre blanc made from brown butter. The impressive wine list features a wide range of labels from Austria and France. Always on hand, warm-hearted and obliging, Barbara Eselböck proves herself to be a natural-born hostess. With its charmingly elegant restaurant and wonderful sheltered terrace, as well as tastefully decorated guestrooms and a private swimming pond in the garden, there are plenty of delightful areas in which to unwind. There is also a small grocery shop on site.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
158;Obauer;Austria;Werfen;Markt 46, Werfen, 5450, Austria;47.4755112;13.1902449;89;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This lovely establishment dating back to the 15C is located in the heart of Werfen, known for its distinctive castle complex. It has been run by the Obauer family for decades and now brothers Karl and Rudolf are in charge. Their classic cuisine draws on modern influences and uses select ingredients, e.g. for dishes such as tur­bot and tip­sy char, toma­toes, peas, wild rasp­ber­ries. Choose between the two set menus or dine à la carte. At lunchtime, there is a moderately priced set menu, including tempting classics such as Wiener schnitzel with Pinzgau veal. Berthold Obauer represents the next generation to lead the friendly and attentive service team, Sommelière Magdalena Gleiss recommends the right wines with charm and profound expertise. The decor is modern and elegant in style, incorporating the historical architecture of the building. There is also a gorgeous terrace to the rear of the property. Overnight guests can look forward to comfortable guestrooms and a delicious breakfast.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
159;SENNS.Restaurant;Austria;Salzburg;Söllheimerstrasse 16, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8361594;13.063525;87;false;false;Creative;Gusswerk – once a bell foundry – is an impressive location for a restaurant. Details of the old industrial architecture have been skilfully combined with chic, stylish modern furnishings. The centrepiece is the open kitchen, where Andreas Senn and chef Christian Geisler cook up a creative set menu, the finesse of which is really memorable! Great care is taken to incorporate the five flavour elements into the dishes. The service is top-notch, very good wine recommendations.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
160;Silvio Nickol Gourmet Restaurant;Austria;Vienna;Coburgbastei 4, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2058003;16.3770073;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Silvio Nickol has a style all of his own that you won't forget in a hurry! In the exclusive Palais Coburg, he serves up extremely imaginative cuisine featuring highly sophisticated combinations based on excellent seasonal produce. For instance, the exceptional red mullet harmonises beautifully with sweet and spicy semi-dried tomato and an exquisite rich bisque sauce. Two set menus are available, one with seven courses, the other with nine. The professional front-of-house team will expertly talk you through the menu and competently guide you through the truly impressive wine list. The elegant interior has a striking vaulted ceiling and eye-catching decorative crystal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
161;Stüva;Austria;Ischgl;Dorfstr. 73, Ischgl, 6561, Austria;47.00948;10.28901;95;true;false;Creative French, Modern Cuisine;This fine dining restaurant in Hotel Yscla (Yscla is the Rhaeto-Romanic name for Ischgl) features a stylish blend of slick modern design and lovely wood finishings. Benjamin Parth's cuisine echoes this sleekness. With just a few components on the plate, he succeeds in creating wonderfully expressive dishes in terms of flavour. In his four- to seven-course set menu, for example, he combines perfectly fried, succulent red mullet, fine sea shell tartare and a tremendously vibrant bouillabaisse, eschewing any unnecessary frills. Only the finest ingredients are used, and his craftsmanship is second to none. Sarah Parth is the experienced front-of-house manager, and her wine recommendations are testament to her in-depth knowledge as a sommelier. Dining here is a real treat!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
162;Restaurant 141 by Joachim Jaud;Austria;Mieming;Obermieming 141, Mieming, 6414, Austria;47.3076251;10.9869243;95;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Part of the renowned Alpenresort Schwarz, this chic, modern restaurant is housed in the old main building, which dates back to 1694. Joachim Jaud, who hails from nearby Telfs, completed his training here. After honing his skills at top-flight establishments, he returned to become head chef in April 2024. He and his small team serve up a creative seasonal set menu comprising five or seven courses. His dishes, skilfully pared down to the essentials, attest to a subtle touch and are full of expression. He is a chef who uses only top-notch ingredients, some sourced locally. There is a fine selection of wines, including numerous organic options and some rare gems. The waitstaff are very friendly, attentive and adept. In case you were wondering, the "141" in the restaurant's name simply refers to the address of the resort. Alongside the wonderful food, there is an extensive range of amenities for spa-goers, holidaymakers and golfers.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
163;Doubek;Austria;Vienna;Kochgasse 13, Vienna, 1080, Austria;48.2131761;16.3494422;47;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Partners Stefan Doubek and Nora Pein offer a one-of-a-kind dining experience, which begins with an uncommonly courtly welcome from the doorman. And things get more interesting: in the open kitchen, food is cooked using four fire sources, including a wood-fired oven and a barbecue. Absolute precision and attention to detail goes into harnessing the flames to prepare fish and seafood, as well as dry-aged duck cooked whole. The result is a set menu that is brimming over with personality and sophisticated combinations of premium ingredients – subtle Japanese accents are also harmoniously integrated. The meal concludes with a delightful sweet finale featuring an array of little treats, elegantly presented at your table. If you prefer to be surprised, do not break the wax seal of the menu you are given. One thing is for sure: the 16 or so intriguing courses delivered to your table will make your time here fly by. In some cases, the chefs themselves come out to talk you through their dishes, which are served on hand-made crockery. Your charming, friendly and competent hostess presides over the minimalist, stylish dining area, bringing a tangible sense of enthusiasm to her recommendations for wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
164;Ikarus;Austria;Salzburg;Wilhelm-Spazier-Straße 7a, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7935688;13.0078642;95;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;An unusual concept, the architecturally impressive Hangar-7 is both a Red Bull exhibition space and a fine dining restaurant. Diners are given a choice of three set menus featuring a winning combination of international and domestic dishes: the guest chef menu, the "Ikarus menu" and a vegetarian alternative – all available in six or eight courses. The decor is stylish and elegant and the attentive front-of-house team includes a highly accomplished sommelier who is on hand to provide astute wine recommendations. Tip for motorists: you can park directly opposite.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
165;Mraz & Sohn;Austria;Vienna;Wallensteinstraße 59, Vienna, 1200, Austria;48.2313246;16.3762794;23;true;true;Creative;This establishment run by Markus Mraz and his sons Lukas and Manuel is a real institution on Vienna's gourmet scene. They serve a surprise set menu comprising a whole series of small courses. They like to concentrate on one main ingredient, which forms the basis of the menu. This approach results in dishes such as their Korean-style chanterelle goulash: a true taste explosion of roasted notes, mild spiciness and full-bodied mushroom flavour. The place has a chic, modern feel and the atmosphere is totally relaxed – they don't stand on ceremony or formality here. In one of the three rooms there is a clear view of the open kitchen. Charming service comes courtesy of attentive and very well-trained staff, not least the sommelier, who maintains a terrific wine cellar and guarantees perfectly balanced wine pairings teeming with interesting ideas.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
166;Griggeler Stuba;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Oberlech 568, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2174694;10.1386433;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;The cosy restaurant proposes regional cuisine enhanced by judicious use of a variety of herbs. A preponderance of wood and appealing little details create a harmonious decor that is infused with Alpine charm.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
167;Kräuterreich by Vitus Winkler;Austria;Sankt Veit im Pongau;Kirchweg 2, Sankt Veit im Pongau, 5621, Austria;47.32784;13.15309;19;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;"Avant-garde Alpine" would be a good label for Vitus Winkler's cuisine, which is creative, firmly rooted in the local region and always very flavourful despite its complexity. The owner expresses his strong connection to his homeland and his love for nature and the mountains in his surprise menu, featuring plenty of herbs, berries, roots etc, as seen in dishes like the Pinzgau Angus beef with parsley root, black currant and larch. An intriguing touch: The menu is structured as a hike through the different altitude zones – from the village, through fields, river & lake, forest & meadow, up to the tree line, and to the alpine pasture, culminating at the summit. This fine dining restaurant is housed in Hotel Sonnhof, which dates back to 1928 – both are run by Vitus and Eva-Maria Winkler, who represent the fourth generation of their family to be at the helm. You can sit in the modern Alpine-style conservatory, in the cosy wood-panelled dining room or at the chef's table. The service is friendly and attentive. Affording mountain views, the terrace is also delightful.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
169;Schwarzer Adler;Austria;Hall in Tirol;Eugenstr. 3, Hall in Tirol, 6060, Austria;47.2811406;11.5082452;65;true;false;European Contemporary;Chef Johannes Nuding needs no introduction, having previously conjured up three-star cuisine at London's Sketch – The Lecture Room & Library. His clearly structured dishes showcase his talent for harmoniously combining ingredients, spices, textures and flavours. A shining example is his wonderfully tender char from the Passeier Valley (fantastic quality!) elegantly prepared with a hint of green curry, served with a rich, perfectly reduced beurre blanc and a sweet-and-sour marmalade of orange and grapefruit, as well as bitter salad leaves for a slightly tart finish. Given the quality of the six-course set menu (with an optional extra course), it's hard to believe they have a kitchen staff of just three! The lady of the house presides over the dining room with warmth and finesse. Located in a charming little street in the old town, this restaurant boasts a refined atmosphere, with modern and elegant furnishings laid out beneath a beautiful old wooden ceiling. The small bar area with a vaulted ceiling is also inviting, as is the walk-in wine cellar.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
171;Konstantin Filippou;Austria;Vienna;Dominikanerbastei 17, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2107279;16.3797942;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Konstantin Filippou presents an extensive tasting menu in which fish and seafood are given top billing, meat is largely dispensed with or plays more of a supporting role. The ingredients for the very modern and contrasting small plates that make up his menu come mainly from Brittany or Scandinavia – for example, the outstanding langostino from Norway, which he serves with cabbage, grapefruit and the wild seaweed cochayuyo. As a native Styrian with Greek roots, the chef-patron discreetly incorporates influences from both his home province and Greek heritage. The minimalist interior is done out in a palette dominated by black and grey. The waitstaff are attentive and competent, including when it comes to recommending just the right wine – you will also find one or two international treasures on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
172;Delta;Greece;Athens;364 Syggrou Avenue, Athens, 17674, Greece;37.9388218;23.6920295;95;false;false;Creative, Greek;Delta is located inside the Stavros Niarchos Foundation Cultural Centre (SNFCC), an avant-garde complex that also houses the National Library of Greece and the Greek National Opera. This restaurant, on the fifth floor of the building, comes as a pleasant surprise thanks to the design of its dining spaces as well as other details such as the exclusively designed bronze bar, the dreamlike trees suspended from the ceiling, and the impressive sea views. Here, chefs George Papazacharias and Thanos Feskos, both of whom have been trained in some of Europe’s best restaurants, showcase their creative cuisine, which places sustainability at the heart of everything, hence the continual focus on the provenance of ingredients (from their own kitchen garden, locally sourced, responsible fishing etc). The striking cuisine here is focused on a single 12-course tasting menu called Omnivore, which can be savoured alongside an extensive selection of Greek and international wines plus a choice of champagnes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
175;César;USA;New York;333 Hudson St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7271776;-74.0076088;46;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;César Ramirez is one of the few chefs who, night after night, has the difficult task of meeting his own singular standards of high-wire precision. His new downtown restaurant brings a sleek, minimal look to a century-old address. As might be expected, world-class seafood plays a large role in his tasting menu which features such delights as a morsel of blackthroat seaperch from Chiba, crudo of fluke from Jeju Island, and langoustine from Norway dressed with caviar and smoked trout. A masterful hand with sauces and a sense for harmonious, exacting combinations demonstrate both creativity and maturity. An eager service team oversees the spacious room where counter and table seating alike offer a prime vantage point for watching this kinetic kitchen.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
176;odo;USA;New York;17 W. 20th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7407048;-73.9929904;41;true;true;Japanese, Contemporary;A serene atmosphere awaits in-the-know diners at this secluded counter, closed off from the cocktail bar in front to foster a mood of intimacy. The service, like the ambience, is warm but unobtrusive, allowing focus to fall on the singular kaiseki menu on offer. Under the assured hand of namesake Chef Hiroki Odo, the cuisine skillfully blends tradition and creative personal touches for a meal that is anything but stuffy. Flavors are both vibrant and precise, with a depth and purity that attests to superbly sourced ingredients and careful preparation. From a savory broth with impeccably cooked tilefish, lifted with locally grown yuzu, to springy house-made soba noodles with indulgently rich salmon roe, this is cooking that will linger in the memory.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
179;Chef's Table at Brooklyn Fare;USA;New York;431 W. 37th St., New York, 10018, USA;40.7560823;-73.9964997;100;false;false;Contemporary;This famed address hidden in the back corner of a Hell’s Kitchen grocery store has entered a new era under Chefs Max Natmessnig and Marco Prins. The room is a box of luxury and sparkles as bright as ever under the spotlights, with most guests seated at a glossy walnut counter that wraps around a brigade of cooks who have nowhere to hide. The team works quickly, sending out a volley of delicate tarts and bites that showcase skill and refinement. Highlights have included sea scallop in a lush brown butter sauce, turbot with firefly squid and herb-oil swirled buttermilk, and buri tartare with smoky creme fraiche and finger lime. All the while, an excellent service team keeps close watch from all corners of the room.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
180;Sushi Noz;USA;New York;181 E. 78th St., New York, 10075, USA;40.77384;-73.958275;32;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;There is a certain energy that courses through this sacred space, where every detail recreates an intimate Japanese refuge. Some of the tools alone are marvels, and Chef Nozomu Abe is a meticulous and engaging craftsman. When booking, keep an eye out for his dates and time slots.  Commence with cooked dishes like pearly sea perch with fresh ponzu dipping sauce and slender pieces of meltingly tender ice fish. Miso soup is the perfect backdrop for silky-soft eel “noodles” with salted egg yolk cream and crispy tofu pieces, while sushi is jewel-like. True to Japanese hospitality, kimono-dressed staff and the chef himself see guests off with a spirit of gratitude.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
181;Atomix;USA;New York;104 E. 30th St., New York, 10016, USA;40.7443058;-73.9826751;84;false;true;Korean, Contemporary;Chef Junghyun Park and his wife Ellia are global ambassadors for contemporary Korean cooking, but all roads lead back to their Murray Hill brownstone. Sporting dark finishes and soothing earth tones, the room unfolds into a chic bar and subterranean dining counter that is as warm and as inviting as the servers. This is one of the city’s most coveted reservations – and for good reason. Raw marinated blue crab – ganjang gejang – arrives reimagined as a tart with golden queen rice. Fluke from Jeju Island comes paired with abalone and watermelon. Filefish and veal tartare sings with a bold liver sauce. The menu is ever-evolving, but the team's commitment to Korean traditions prepared with finesse and flair is steadfast.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
182;Saga;USA;New York;70 Pine St., New York, 10005, USA;40.706144;-74.0078519;21;false;true;Contemporary;In a landmark skyscraper that towers over the city, Saga is a jewel in every sense of the word. An aperitif from the terrace is a striking start before settling into one of several intimate rooms fit with peach and emerald velvet, green marble tables, and carved stone accents. An aura of class and comfort takes hold in preparation for a cuisine that is inspired and delightful. The team is currently presenting a roster of signatures. The likes of egg soufflé with caviar and bonito foam as well as black bass and scallop with carrot-ginger curry lead to a dry-aged duck tagine served with msemmen—griddled flatbread—and all the trimmings. Dessert displays particular strength for its sharp focus, say an arrangement of treats with sweet potato and birch as a theme.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
184;Aquavit;USA;New York;65 E. 55th St., New York, 10022, USA;40.76078;-73.97214;16;true;false;Scandinavian, Contemporary;No detail goes unnoticed at this contemporary Swedish beauty, sporting a sleek bar and open kitchen with Chef Emma Bengtsson at the helm. Enjoy the eponymous infused spirit along with bites from one of two dinner tasting menus. Expect glazed earthenware, slate platters and wooden boxes cradling the likes of a medallion of North Sea cod, torched ever so slightly, and accompanied by a light-textured mussel foam and petite wedges of roasted red endive. Lean and tender duck breast sided by a petite block of compressed leg meat is dressed tableside with a beet sauce enriched with duck jus. The meal may end with a composition of green apple and fennel featuring rye cake, apple ice, bitter caramel and whipped, smoked crème fraîche.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
185;Aska;USA;Brooklyn;47 S. 5th St., Brooklyn, 11249, USA;40.7123772;-73.9667551;24;true;false;Scandinavian, Contemporary;Eating here is serious business, but happily the place isn’t blighted by a monastic atmosphere—a contented buzz fills the room, helped along by the chefs who deliver the dishes themselves.Chef Fredrik Berselius and his ace team delight diners with their highly accomplished Nordic cuisine. Local products are woven into the seasonal tasting, and items like prawn shells and venison bones are transformed into luscious sauces that enhance each plating. Creme royale with claw of lobster, trout roe and essence of elderflower is a dish to dream about, while venison from New York is perfectly minimalist with morel mushroom, wild leek and a delicate jus.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
186;Atera;USA;New York;77 Worth St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7168498;-74.0055912;19;false;true;Contemporary;Counter dining can sometimes be a cramped affair, but fortunately, this one is spacious enough to leave plenty of elbow room, allowing guests to enjoy the immersive experience in comfort. The kitchen, led by Danish chef Ronny Emborg, runs with a quiet tranquility that forms a sharp contrast to the boisterous playlist, which helps keep the room from feeling stuffy. The menu comprises numerous beguiling courses with global accents, featuring subtle flavors and deftly weaving together both delicacy and richness. A dish of minute, briny shigoku oysters strikes an intriguing balance between vegetal and fruit notes when matched with kiwi and cucumber, while a perfectly cooked morsel of halibut is bolstered with an impeccable buttery shrimp bisque.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
187;Jean-Georges;USA;New York;1 Central Park West, New York, 10023, USA;40.76907;-73.98155;22;true;false;Contemporary, French Contemporary;Chef Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s culinary empire stretches far and wide, but Central Park will always be his home. Chef de Cuisine Joseph Rhee and this team sustain a legacy defined by a mastery of French techniques and a respect for global flavors. The signature egg toast with caviar is an assured start before launching into an ever-evolving menu rich with precision and elegance. Efforts like tomatillo-lemon verbena jus, black truffle with za’atar, and sunflower seed ajo blanco demonstrate originality and boldness in spades. Those opting for the vegetarian menu will enjoy the season's best produce, like heirloom tomatoes composed with crunchy vegetable mignonette and spiced dressing.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
188;Gabriel Kreuther;USA;New York;41 W. 42nd St., New York, 10036, USA;40.75397;-73.982025;89;true;false;Contemporary, Alsatian;Distinctively housed at the base of the Grace building, this modern dining room happens to be perfect for celebrating special occasions. Dishes reflect global sensibilities with a strong creative edge, as in the Montauk red shrimp tartare crowned with a cayenne tuile, surrounded by a creamy jalapeño coulis. Foie gras arrives in myriad guises, perhaps as a seared lobe as rich as custard, surrounded by roasted quince, chestnuts and vanilla gastrique. Old-school luxuries extend right through to the cheese trolley. The cocktail list is dedicated to the history of Bryant Park across the street, while as an homage to the eponymous chef’s Alsatian heritage, the wine selection prominently features rieslings, pinot blancs and gewürztraminers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
189;minibar;USA;Washington;855 E St. NW, Washington, 20004, USA;38.896294;-77.02386;51;true;false;Contemporary;A single door, with a host to match, marks the entrance to this culinary oasis that goes far beyond its tiny name. The lounge is ideal for a glass of champagne, after which guests can settle at the counter built around the chefs' stainless-steel workspace.The team is passionate, skilled, and full of technical expertise, creating a menu that gets off to a stimulating start, perhaps a watermelon "margarita" which is in fact a wedge of compressed watermelon infused with mezcal, garnished with lime and salt. Whimsy is a driving force here, and it is delightfully rendered in items like the cauliflower and caviar. The meal hits its crescendo with the likes of a perfectly cooked squab breast sauced with huckleberry gastrique. The fun is carried through to the very end, with the crowd-pleasing fried ice cream donut.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
190;Jônt;USA;Washington;1904 14th St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.9158847;-77.0321498;89;true;true;Contemporary;Chef Ryan Ratino's ambitious counter is an experience like nothing else in the city. Sitting just above Bresca, the room is a constant hive of activity with sharp-suited servers gliding about and laser-focused chefs working in perfect tandem. From the cutlery to the cooking, expect beauty and boldness. Top-rate seafood and meat from Japan and beautiful sauces form the core of this menu. Think delicate tarts with wagyu tartare, grilled sawara with beet and pomegranate sauce, and a particularly striking king crab rice cooked in a donabe. Dessert is its own counter that ends with a treasure box of mignardises. All throughout, a high-energy playlist matches a high-performing team who want nothing more than for guests to enjoy themselves.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
191;Oriole;USA;Chicago;661 W. Walnut St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8862095;-87.6453022;18;false;true;Contemporary, American Contemporary;Guests enter this former warehouse through a converted freight elevator, a testament to Oriole’s unique brand of elegance, further exemplified by the striking ceiling collage above the spotless open kitchen. Chef Noah Sandoval and team execute a thoughtful tasting menu that blends French and Japanese elements. Begin with an aperitif and small bites in the impressive bar area, with the likes of a maitake mushroom and ricotta tartlet. Move to the dining room with a luscious canapé of foie gras mousse, then the meal begins in earnest. A composition of lightly cooked beets with sake lees, sea buckthorn, and puffed wild rice shows a delicate balance of flavors and textures, while a dish of skate wing and Dungeness crab with a toasted kombu butter is pure indulgence.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
193;TURK FATİH TUTAK;Türkiye;Istanbul;Bomonti, Cumhuriyet Hacıahmet Silahşör Caddesi, Yeniyol Sokak No:2, Şişli, Istanbul, 34440, Türkiye;41.058398;28.977656;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;Fatih Tutak expresses his love for his Turkish terroir here, showcasing ingredients from the region and produce from local traders on a daily basis. This is a chef who cooks with respect for tradition and what nature has to offer. Familiar flavours are given a new dimension, and centuries-old practices are tailored to the current zeitgeist. Part of his originality lies in his nuanced use of delicate acidity and smoky flavours. Think grilled lamb with a sumptuous fermented vegetable jus or confit mackerel with the tang of kaffir lime. He combines his dry-aged tomato tartare with Oscietra caviar, fermented tomato, creamy cheese and a wonderful fig jus. The exuberance of bold flavours is this chef's trademark. Be sure to peruse the fantastic wine list with its abundance of Turkish labels – we were bowled over by the Blanc de Noir Karasi 2021. Hors d'oeuvres are served in the lounge, which boasts magnificent city views. Then you move to the intimate main dining space, where you can watch the chefs in action. For dessert, you are invited into the open kitchen of this chic establishment. This is an adventure from start to finish, guided by the inspiring work of Fatih Tutak.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
194;Gaa;Thailand;Bangkok;46/1 Sukhumvit 53, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.72725;100.57828;22;false;true;Indian, Contemporary;Gaa's setting reflects Chef Garima Arora's culinary style: blending tradition with modern techniques. Garima personally serves a tasting menu inspired by her Indian heritage, featuring inventive street food reinterpretations. Her assured and skilful cooking showcases precisely balanced spicing, remarkable flavour combinations, and delightful texture and temperature contrasts.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
195;Baan Tepa;Thailand;Bangkok;561 Ramkhamhaeng Road, Hua Mak, Bang Kapi, Bangkok, 10240, Thailand;13.7608267;100.6263514;63;true;false;Thai contemporary;Chef Chudaree 'Tam' Debhakam brings the farm-to-table concept to life with her detailed, contemporary Thai tasting menu. Seasonal and sustainable ingredients, some sourced from her own backyard, highlight a culinary journey through Thailand. The dishes present bold flavours and delicate spices, crafted by a charming team within an elegant villa setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
196;Sühring;Thailand;Bangkok;10 Soi Yen Akat 3, Chong Nonsi, Yan Nawa, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7108084;100.5457264;34;true;false;German, Contemporary;At Sühring, twin chefs Matthias and Thomas present a modern German tasting menu influenced by family recipes, childhood memories, and travels. Each dish showcases expertly prepared seasonal ingredients using traditional German techniques such as fermenting, pickling, and curing. The restaurant, located in a restored 1970s villa, offers an exceptional dining experience, especially when seated at the kitchen counter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
197;Chef's Table;Thailand;Bangkok;61F, Tower Club at Lebua, 1055 Silom Road, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7215006;100.5171696;23;false;false;French Contemporary;Start with champagne or a cocktail in the Pink Bar before taking your seat in this visually stunning restaurant housed inside the Lebua at State Tower hotel. Originally from the Loire Valley, chef Vincent Thierry spearheads the detailed and sophisticated modern French cooking. Dishes deliver well-judged, balanced flavours with the help of contemporary techniques and a global outlook. Top quality ingredients are to the fore and sauces are a highlight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
198;Côte by Mauro Colagreco;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, Capella Bangkok, 300/2 Charoenkrung Road, Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.713092;100.510847;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Côte brings the essence of Riviera-inspired cuisine to Bangkok, embracing Mediterranean, French and Italian influences. The dishes are skilfully crafted and presented using modern techniques by Italian chef Davide Garavaglia, who worked at Colagreco's principal restaurant for years. The culinary team revels in surprising guests at each course, curating seasonal menus based on the finest produce available that day.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
199;R-Haan;Thailand;Bangkok;131 Soi Sukhumvit 53, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.731805;100.57972;81;false;true;Thai;R-Haan aims to reflect the way in which food has influenced Thai people and culture. Relax in the lounge with a cocktail before entering the main dining room for cuisine that encapsulates the beauty of Thailand and its provinces. The traditional Thai menu brings the essence of the country to your plate. A refined Thai welcome takes the form of an amuse-bouche, then come the mains, served the traditional way, family style, followed by iconic local desserts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
200;Mezzaluna;Thailand;Bangkok;65F, Tower Club at Lebua, 1055 Silom Road, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7221259;100.516932;90;true;true;French Contemporary;Perched on the 65th floor of the Lebua Hotel, Mezzaluna offers sky-high and breathtaking views. Toast to the high life at Sky Bar before settling in for a gastronomic journey. The accomplished chef and his team deliver European delights with Japanese precision in a seven-course set menu, along with some surprises. The flavours are balanced and sophisticated, and the food is creative and technically precise. A wine list of substantial proportions and prices accompanies.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
201;Bardal;Spain;Ronda;José Aparicio 1, Ronda, 29400, Spain;36.74161;-5.16655;54;false;false;Creative;Some people call Ronda the “city of dreams”. But without drifting off into reverie, we are indeed talking about one of the most beautiful towns in Andalucia, where Bardal, not far from the impressive bridge over El Tajo de Ronda, is now a flagship of the local restaurant scene. Here, chef Benito Gómez, a Catalan by birth who has made the region his home, cooks up creative cuisine, steering clear of gimmickry and labels, while the recognisable flavours in his cooking have a connection to local tradition and are transformed into a subtle interplay of contrasts and textures. Diners are given a choice of two tasting menus with different numbers of courses (Bardal and Gran Menú Bardal). Both come with wine-pairing options and a trolley with a large selection of cheeses prior to dessert. One section of the menu we especially liked was the trilogy of grilled heart of lettuce with a beef emulsion, Bágoa peas with Payoyo cheese, and chicken skin and shrimp.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
202;El Portal de Echaurren;Spain;Ezcaray;Padre José García 19, Ezcaray, 26280, Spain;42.3257846;-3.0144146;84;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Francis Paniego exudes honesty, sincerity, passion and a love for his profession and his family legacy, which sees him and his brother Chefe (maître d' and sommelier) as the fifth generation in charge of this restaurant that has been in business for over a century. Here, you will discover a reinterpretation of the chef’s roots but from a more creative perspective, to which he brings his exceptional technical skill to bear on the ingredients he uses, such as offal (the “tendon” gnocchi were delicious), that elevates the palate to new heights. These dishes, served in the guise of a tasting menu, are presented alongside a selection of appetisers and starters (served in the Salón de la Galería or at El Portal’s bar) that showcase the pillars upon which this restaurant (such as his sorely missed mother Marisa Sánchez) are based. The experience continues in the dining room with constant nods to the local area, its people and to the flavours of La Rioja. Many of the finishing touches to dishes are added in front of guests.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
203;El Rincón de Juan Carlos;Spain;Adeje;Avenida Virgen de Guadalupe 21, La Caleta, Adeje, 38679, Spain;28.1018325;-16.7535126;44;false;true;Creative;If you’re on the lookout for an authentic gourmet experience and you’re not familiar with the elaborate cooking of the Padrón brothers (Juan Carlos and Jonathan) at the Royal Hideaway Corales Beach resort, it’s high time to book a table here! Located on the fifth floor of this innovatively designed hotel, the restaurant delights guests with the ocean and sunset views from several of its tables and the high level of service and cuisine, with many of its dishes eliciting a strong emotional response. In keeping with its philosophy, the focus here is on traditional Canary Island recipes (albeit from a creative perspective) and a high level of refinement in its presentation. There’s just a single yet extensive tasting menu along with several wine-pairing options (we were particularly impressed and surprised by dishes such as the onion soup and “flan roto”, the clam and mussel combination, the magical “sweet tree” that is served along with the petits fours, as well as one of the restaurant’s signature dishes, the superb “turrón” of Canary Island morcilla with almond praline.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
204;Amelia by Paulo Airaudo;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Zubieta 26, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20007, Spain;43.3168594;-1.9859469;24;false;false;Creative, Italian and Japanese;In terms of technical excellence and personality, this restaurant is constantly striving to be different, to challenge the palate of its guests and be the benchmark eatery on La Concha bay. Housed in the Villa Favorita hotel, this restaurant is presided over by chef Paulo Airaudo, who hails from Córdoba (Argentina). Here, he conjures up creative cuisine that stands out for its excellent fish and seafood, combining the essence of Basque culinary tradition with subtle Spanish, Italian and Asian influences in dishes that are expressive, intense and beautifully balanced. The decorative backdrop strikes an aesthetic balance between the classic and the modern, with three large tables and a bar where you can eat while watching the chefs at work – the latter also serve the dishes themselves. The single tasting menu with wine-pairing options (including champagne) and wines by the glass, is based around premium ingredients from around the world. As a result, a strong international feel is evident in everything that happens here, from the dishes on the menu to the service and the clientele.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
205;El Poblet;Spain;Valencia;Correos 8-1º, Valencia, 46002, Spain;39.469784;-0.3745175;57;true;false;Creative;This restaurant was founded by culinary maestro Quique Dacosta as a tribute to his own life story, while the name El Poblet was the original name of his famous restaurant in Dénia, which now bears his own name. Chef Luis Valls’ cuisine, which is focused on recipes and ingredients from the surrounding area, especially his beloved Albufera, is also centred around a fusion of innovation and modern Valencian cuisine that is deeply rooted in tradition and teeming with personality. This is showcased via exquisite textures, bold flavours, top-quality local ingredients and even a reinvented take on charcuterie that will definitely leave an impression. Choose between several menus (a short version available midweek, one vegetarian (pre-booking required) and two tasting-style menus: Ciutat Vella and Territori. The wine cellar also features some great labels as well as an incredible selection of malt whiskies. The restaurant has also carried out research on citrus fruits including citrons, kumquats, and pear lemons.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
206;Retiro da Costiña;Spain;Santa Comba;Avenida de Santiago 12, Santa Comba, 15840, Spain;43.0334653;-8.8038837;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that will be a pleasant surprise for guests, both in terms of its passion for hospitality, its use of the very best ingredients, and its small town location. Ably supported by his family, Manuel García strives for culinary excellence through his impressive “Costiña 85 aniversario” tasting menu (a nod to the history of the business which was founded by his grandparents in 1939). This “gastro-sensory” experience, which provides an insight into traditional Galician flavours and ingredients (sea bass, spider crab, locally reared chicken etc) from a creative perspective, evolves in stages in the Champagne “corner” on the ground floor followed by the bakery, the spectacular bodega, and the pleasant dining room on the first floor, before ending in the impressive lounge with its sofas and fireplace for a post-dinner coffee, delicious petits-fours and an extensive choice of spirits. In addition, the delightful design-inspired villas close to the restaurant are modelled on a typical Celtic “castro” settlement in the heart of nature. If you are staying here, don’t miss the stunning breakfast.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
207;Ricard Camarena;Spain;Valencia;Avenida Burjassot 54, Valencia, 46009, Spain;39.48512;-0.3852003;56;true;true;Creative;This magnificent place is part of the refurbished Bombas Gens factory, which also houses an arts and culture centre. Here, there is a large foyer with a contemporary feel, a private bar where hors d'oeuvres are served, and the modern dining room at the back, with an open-plan kitchen where you can enjoy a final aperitif.Along with seven other chefs, Ricard Camarena was distinguished/commended with the Cocinero del Año award (Madrid Fusión, 2021) for his "green activism". His is a coherent signature cuisine solidly grounded in homegrown vegetables and a painstaking process of research. His set menus convey a clear commitment to sustainability, as he uses every last leaf of the vegetables to make his sauces or even the occasional beverage.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
208;Deessa;Spain;Madrid;Plaza de la Lealtad 5, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4158561;-3.6928119;29;false;true;Creative;Deessa is a restaurant like no other and is the gourmet standard-bearer of the Mandarin Oriental Ritz in Madrid. The incomparable dining room, exquisitely laid out in the Alfonso XIII salon overlooking the garden, is the perfect setting in which to savour the intrinsic beauty of the great Quique Dacosta’s exquisite culinary vision. This celebrated chef keeps a watchful eye on everything here, closely following the cuisine created by resident head chef Domenico Vildacci. Their elegant dishes exploring the flavours of the Mediterranean and the Extremadura region are showcased on two tasting menus: one entitled “Histórico Quique Dacosta”, featuring the chef’s signature dishes from his three-Michelin-starred restaurant in Dénia, and “Contemporáneo QDRITZ”. A reduced version of both menus, enticingly called “Esencia”, is also available at lunchtime midweek.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
209;Bo.TiC;Spain;Corçà;Avenida Costa brava 6, Corçà, 17121, Spain;41.9877609;3.0160537;28;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant is remarkable both in terms of its location in an old carriage factory and its ongoing quest to delight diners with its flavoursome cuisine and enthusiasm. Beyond the attractive garden are two minimalist-style dining areas, one overlooking the kitchen (including a “chef’s table”) the other, which is cosier, laid out within the stone walls of what used to be the carpentry workshop. Here, chef Albert Sastregener offers two set menus (Degustación and Del Chef) plus a concise à la carte featuring dishes from the former. These abound with imaginative and technically sophisticated creations that are respectful of Catalan tradition without excluding international influences. As an example, one of his local “zero-km” growers (Hidenori Futami) supplies him with vegetables and shoots native to Japan. We particularly enjoyed Bo.TiC’s highly original, delicate and beautifully presented snacks on its menus, which are separated into different sections (Bar, Season, Roasts and Bakery).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
210;Coque;Spain;Madrid;Marqués de Riscal 11, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.430643;-3.690676;45;true;true;Creative;The Sandoval brothers (Mario in the kitchen, Diego front of house, and Rafael in his role as sommelier) are considered three of the biggest stars in Spain’s hospitality industry. This magnificent restaurant, occupying around 1 100m² of space, offers various sensory experiences that take place in stages with stops in the colourful English-style bar, the small room dedicated to Macallan whiskies, the spectacular wine cellar (including a “sacristy” where they pour sherries using a traditional “venencia”), the kitchen (for a final appetiser), and then on to the dining room. Aware of the need for a greater understanding of ingredients, chef Mario Sandoval offers guests his “Chamberí” menu (there’s also a vegan-vegetarian option) showcasing creative cooking that champions the best seasonal products to the full (shrimp from Motril, wild Galician clams, Toro Bravo beef etc). You can also find out more about the research that he carries out in his “agrolab” at the Jaral de la Mira farm-estate.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
211;Paco Roncero;Spain;Madrid;Alcalá 15, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4176733;-3.7002477;96;true;false;Creative;In this elegant avant-garde space on the top floor of a 19C building, this restaurant is run by Paco Roncero, a chef who is constantly on the move and constantly pursuing new goals, which includes reinventing his cuisine from one year to the next.In this splendid setting, you can look forward to a comprehensive and highly interactive dining experience that is centred on two highly interesting menus: “Esencia” (only lunchtime on Thursdays and Fridays) and “Afirmación”. The chef, who has an unwavering enthusiasm for olive oil, demonstrates his full creativity and imagination in his starters (his signature Filipino of foie gras with white chocolate and cardamom is a prime example), before moving on to delicious, traditionally inspired mains in which seasonal ingredients are to the fore, before surprising guests with desserts that combine sweet and savoury flavours (such as the highly original beetroot with black garlic). The spectacular terrace is an added bonus!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
213;Smoked Room;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana 57, Madrid, 28046, Spain;40.4385556;-3.691358;19;false;false;Contemporary;This place is somewhat reminiscent of a speakeasy, and a meal here is quite the experience. They play ingeniously with smoky flavours and aromas without ever overwhelming the palate. Located in the Hyatt Regency Hesperia Madrid, Smoked Room has its own entrance and, positioning itself as an exclusive alternative, shares its space with the restaurant Leña Madrid. The aesthetically pleasing dining area has an intimate feel and features a Japanese-style bar facing the kitchen as well as just two tables. Sophisticated cuisine is showcased here in a single tasting menu ("Todo es humo" – or "Everything is smoke"), which is based on lightly smoked and charcoal-grilled dishes and always features exquisite combinations of the finest seasonal produce, matured fish and meats, seaweed etc. Reservations are taken from the 15th of each month.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
215;Voro;Spain;Canyamel;Urbanización Atalaya de Canyamel, Canyamel, 07589, Spain;39.6690394;3.4395565;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in a separate building belonging to the Cap Vermell Grand Hotel, this restaurant sets the tone with its name (from the Latin “to devour”) and a keen desire to explore global cuisine. In its attractive dining spaces crowned by high ceilings, discover the culinary philosophy of chef Álvaro Salazar, a man whose efforts revolve around a single idea: to create cuisine without constraints, with a commitment to the environment and to his Mediterranean roots. Choose between two modern and creative tasting menus (“Voro” and “Devoro”) that stand out for their attention to detail and meticulous presentation and the fact that each dish tells a story, with each referencing the chef's professional achievements, his native Linares (Jaén), the island of Mallorca, the Mediterranean Sea – the list goes on. The menus mix seasonal dishes with some of Voro’s iconic signature classics and are separated into sections that follow the sun’s journey through the day (Dawn, Zenith and Sunset).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
216;Pepe Vieira;Spain;Raxó;Camiño da Serpe, Raxó, 36992, Spain;42.40942;-8.75447;40;true;false;Creative;It is a miracle to find a restaurant of this standard in the middle of the countryside, but Pepe Vieira bucks this trend! In this spectacular restaurant surrounded by woods, gardens and pleasant terraces, chef Xosé T. Cannas takes a bold approach to everything, exploring new recipes and ingredients from elsewhere which he combines with superb local ingredients (particularly from the sea) on tasting menus (Romasanta, O Señor de Andrade and A Santa Elección) that take guests on a journey back to the roots of Galician cuisine which is described here as the “la última cociña do mundo”! Sustainability is the backbone of the experience, which begins with aperitifs in the garden before exploring the building’s different spaces and then moving to the dining room, which opens out onto nature via huge picture windows. The splendid wine list is based around the theme of the Camino de Santiago. Guests have the additional option of 14 individual cube-style bedrooms with an unexpected cutting-edge design that enables guests to experience their natural surroundings to the full.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
217;Enoteca Paco Pérez;Spain;Barcelona;Marina 19, Barcelona, 08005, Spain;41.3867832;2.1969283;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the luxurious Hotel Arts and overseen by award-winning chef Paco Pérez, this restaurant serves highly nuanced Mediterranean cuisine that is enriched with international influences and the occasional nod to Asian fusion cooking. The governing principles in the kitchen are underpinned by an utmost respect for seasonal ingredients and a clear goal to elevate traditional dining concepts such as “sea and mountains”. To highlight this, the chef particularly enjoys cooking with sea cucumbers from the Mar d'Amunt and produce from vegetable gardens close to it, hence their special hint of salinity. If we were to attempt to find a concept or premise to help us define this restaurant we would have to focus on its bright interior, its meticulous design dominated by different white tones and, above all, its obsession with local ingredients to help tell a story. One standout dish that we particularly enjoyed was the “The sea remembering Gaudí” (two different varieties of shrimp, tuna belly, scallops, and poached egg yolk).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
220;Alevante;Spain;Chiclana de la Frontera;Amílcar Barca, Chiclana de la Frontera, 11130, Spain;36.346905;-6.1641536;76;true;true;Creative;The luxury Gran Meliá Sancti Petri hotel’s gourmet restaurant boasts a bright, elegant and minimalist design – the only thing adorning the walls of the dining room are the silhouettes of shoals of fish and curtains made from traditional hemp rope. Given that this is the offshoot of the extraordinary Aponiente restaurant in El Puerto de Santa María, guests can savour (via the Gran Menú Alevante), many of the dishes that have led to acclaimed chef’s Ángel León’s reputation as “El Chef del Mar”. The experience (overseen by chef Cristian Rodríguez) begins with enticing appetisers accompanied by wines from the Cádiz area in the bar at the entrance and continues in the dining room, where the best maritime fish and seafood (sea urchins, shrimp, mackerel, dogfish etc) take centre stage. The menu, which includes extraordinary dishes such as deep-fried pepper in a chilled soup, and the moray eel mochi, comes with the “Alevante Crew” book, as the common thread here is a journey by boat to discover the ingredients used.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
221;L'Escaleta;Spain;Cocentaina;Pujada Estació del Nord 205, Cocentaina, 03824, Spain;38.7570756;-0.4451945;71;true;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;In this attractive villa on the slopes of Montcabrer (the “magic mountain”), diners get a real sense of the evolution of a family restaurant that has been in business for over 40 years. Here, the culinary memories that shape this restaurant are drawn upon to convey concepts, emotions and stories through its dishes. Eschewing unnecessary frills, chef Kiko Moya complements his à la carte with two tasting menus (Sabor and Saboer) which celebrate the terroir by using the best local and seasonal produce and by drawing on tradition – but this does not mean his cuisine is in any way lacking in creativity. Famous for its “arroces al cuadrado”, a rice speciality served in a rectangular iron tray and then finished in the oven, the painstakingly curated menu is complemented by an excellent wine list. Dishes we particularly enjoyed included the freshwater rice with blue crab and eel, along with the delicious home-made Potrota dessert with baked pear – the latter a rural-rustic recipe that has been superbly brought up to date.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
222;BonAmb;Spain;Xàbia;Carretera de Benitachell 100, Xàbia, 03730, Spain;38.7701412;0.148496;91;false;true;Creative;A unique restaurant, where each season finds inspiration in a different theme. Occupying a restored country house in beautifully landscaped surroundings, the setting is as appealing as the menu. The latter comes courtesy of Alberto Ferruz, who also runs the Michelin-starred Casa Pepa in Ondara. This is a chef who always turns to the Mediterranean and Alicante's Marina Alta for his magnificent fish and seafood, which take centre stage alongside produce from his bountiful vegetable gardens, and herbs from the Montgó mountains. Here, three creative tasting menus (“Encesa”, “Pesquera” and “Fustal”) perpetuate the memory of the “Encesers” – farmers who, in ancient times, would risk their lives by fishing along the cliffs at dusk – using a light source to attract fish (a technique called “Encesa”). These menus are offered as part of the restaurant’s “Fustes” season, the latter a reference to the personalised wooden object that these men would leave at a crossroads as proof that they were safe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
223;DSTAgE;Spain;Madrid;Regueros 8, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4246847;-3.6962925;92;false;false;Creative;The most striking thing about this restaurant housed in an industrial loft in the Salesas district of the city is how it embodies Vitoria-born chef Diego Guerrero's determination to be free to create, to surprise and to break down the barriers around our personal comfort zones. The high-ceilinged interior has a relaxed feel with its exposed brick walls, retro design features, internal patio and an open-view kitchen that maximises the connection between the chefs and their customers. There’s also an annexe (DSPOT Studio & Events) dedicated to creativity, research and event planning. Thanks to his different approach, the chef showcases the evolution of cuisine, through set menus (Dtaste, Dstage and Denjoy) that offer a fun culinary journey around the world, fusing all kinds of ingredients and creating incredible trompe l’oeil effects. For the complete dining experience, choose the wine pairing option.;Air conditioning;[]
224;Skina;Spain;Marbella;Cánovas del Castillo 9, Marbella, 29601, Spain;36.5116735;-4.9012506;71;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Real gems are often hidden in unusual and rather obscure places, but rarely in such a tiny venue as this! Tucked away in one the narrow streets of Marbella's old town, this restaurant has only four tables. Marcos Granda, its famous owner and sommelier, justifies the small size of the place perfectly, saying, "What Skina has to offer is huge."The young chef from Toledo, Mario Cachinero, proposes creative and sincere cuisine that strives to put a new spin on traditional Andalusian recipes and that he describes as being "all about harmonies and contrasts". However, to achieve this, the raw ingredients (wild Galician fish caught by traditional methods, premium oils from Jaén produced in mountain olive groves, select cuts of meat etc) are meticulously and skilfully put to work in order to bring out even more of their flavour.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
225;Venta Moncalvillo;Spain;Daroca de Rioja;Carretera de Medrano 6, Daroca de Rioja, 26373, Spain;42.3715602;-2.5805894;88;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Ignacio Echapresto’s personal story shows that everything is possible in life, as one day he decided to change professions, swapping his blacksmith’s workshop for a restaurant kitchen. Here, in this tiny hamlet with a population of just 50 inhabitants, the chef and his brother Carlos (who is in charge of the restaurant and the wine cellar) have restructured the cuisine with much more of an emphasis on sustainability and the restaurant’s own kitchen garden - as a result, the experience begins with a stroll through the latter, as well as a selection of snacks, before heading to the dining room. Dine in comfortable outbuildings that overlook attractive verdant surroundings, where you can choose between two tasting menus (Vegetal and Moncalvillo) that change with the seasons and are based around what is picked daily, a process they call “the luxury of immediacy”, and dishes that combine just two or three ingredients (artichokes, broad beans, pumpkin, quince, cod, venison etc). The splendid wine cellar also includes gourmet mead produced on the property.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
226;Cabaña Buenavista;Spain;El Palmar;Calle Buenavista s/n - Urbanización Buenavista, El Palmar, 30120, Spain;37.92464;-1.163767;85;false;false;Creative;A culinary experience in every sense! From the moment you enter, you are guided through a surprising sequence of flavours and sensations, starting with appetisers (served in the delightful garden and on the glass-fronted terrace overlooking the lake) and then at the bar in the dining room, where the chef adds the finishing touches to starters in front of you. You then continue to the spectacular modern dining room with its surprising setting in a large thatched hut. Here, you savour main dishes that are in perfect harmony with Murcia’s culinary traditions such as the Chato Murciano pork with the traditional “olla fresca” (accompanied by a pork jowl sandwich). Chef Pablo González’s creative cuisine is showcased on a concise à la carte and two tasting menus (Olivo and Experience) that constantly reference regional recipes and stand out for their presentation, with several dishes completed at your table. All the music you’ll hear in the background here, both classical and modern, is by artists from the province of Murcia.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
227;Les Cols;Spain;Olot;Carretera de la Canya, Olot, 17800, Spain;42.1946503;2.5009;28;false;true;Creative;Ably assisted by her three daughters (Clara, Martina and Carlota) and her husband Manuel Puigvert, chef Fina Puigdevall builds her creativity around seasonality, sustainability (the family has its own vegetable garden which can be visited at the Casa Horitzó R&D centre in the Vall de Bianya) and the use of produce from the volcanic region of La Garrotxa – they are also staunch advocates of the “food that hasn't travelled” concept. Today, the old family farm is a building with a remarkably cutting-edge interior design that revolves around a relationship between its dining spaces and nature. This is especially noticeable in the events pavilion, which is visually ethereal and where hens roam freely! It offers an impressive single tasting menu: Horizonte, Naturaleza Viva & Mística (Horizon, Living and Mystical Nature) that starts with eye-catching aperitifs and appetisers in the garden (in fine weather) and includes unusual dishes such as “onion royale” and, in season, delicious grilled peas with black sausage (butifarra), bacon, snails and mint.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
228;Mugaritz;Spain;Errenteria;Aldura Aldea 20 - Otzazulueta Baserria, Errenteria, 20100, Spain;43.2722067;-1.9171152;57;true;true;Innovative;Mugaritz is much more than a restaurant, offering food-enthusiasts a very different dining experience. Here, absolutely everything is questioned, hence the focus on both individual and general tastes to the extent that, in the words of the chef, “the experience is as much playful as it is gastronomic”. The intentions of Andoni Luis Aduriz, who likes nothing more than breaking the rules, can be seen in a small glossary placed on your table, detailing terms defined by the chef, his staff and even his customers in a cooperative endeavour to add meaning to the dining experience. Dishes, many of which are eaten directly with the hands, do not follow a classic order and constantly aim to transcend borders, both in terms of flavour and the flow of the single tasting menu. One particularly outstanding dish is called “De frente: la piel que habito (“Front on: the skin I inhabit”) – a conceptual creation in which a false skin of cider gelatine is added to a face, accompanied by pieces of fried bread with a pepper emulsion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
229;Iván Cerdeño;Spain;Toledo;Cigarral del Ángel, Toledo, 45004, Spain;39.8619154;-4.0462052;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At the historic Cigarral del Ángel (a “cigarral” is a typical Toledo-style country house), set in lush gardens on the banks of the Tagus, guests can savour the unusual cuisine of chef Iván Cerdeño, who creates dishes based on memories from the past and seasonality. In them, he showcases the finest ingredients from La Mancha, the distinctive flavours of game from the Montes de Toledo, and colourful produce from local vegetable gardens. He also takes inspiration from the different cultures that have left their legacy here, as well as from the distant seas around the Iberian Peninsula. Pickles, sauces, escabeches and marinades all feature strongly, as part of cuisine that combines the culinary roots of La Mancha with a contemporary slant. This is evidenced on four menus: the midweek Mediodía option and three tasting menus (Monte y Ribera, Toledo Olvidado (Forgotten Toledo) and Memorias de un Cigarral) that usually start with “atisbos” – small traditional appetisers with a modern touch. We thoroughly enjoyed the wild boar with pickle (a mouth-watering roast rib with spicy Mexican-influenced nuances and flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
230;Culler de Pau;Spain;O Grove;Reboredo 73, O Grove, 36980, Spain;42.4752854;-8.8957637;72;true;false;Creative;O Grove is a peninsula with stunning coves of fine white sand that overlooks the entrance to the Arousa estuary dotted with shellfish beds. This is the setting for Culler de Pau, in a valley full of cornfields and small orchards, where chef Javier Olleros has his family home and where he runs this business with his wife Amaranta Rodríguez, with an ethos that is underpinned by concerns about issues such as obesity, the climate crisis and the fast food culture. In the minimalist-style dining room, adorned with stunning works of sculpture that showcase the inner light that shines within us, discover “zero-mile” cooking on three menus (Ronsel, Marexada and Descuberta) that reflect a commitment to the environment and to the Atlantic. Culler de Pau has its own vegetable garden, hence its desire for guests to share in the immediate pleasure of tasting herbs and other produce that has just been harvested and which form the basis of its aromatic soups. One signature dish that you must try is the egg with San Simón cheese and “migas”.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
231;M.B;Spain;Guía de Isora;Maria Zambrano 2, Carretera TF 47, Guía de Isora, 38687, Spain;28.171041;-16.799017;80;true;false;Creative;In keeping with the Ritz-Carlton Abama, a spectacular resort boasting attractive gardens, palm trees and a whole host of leisure options and one that fully deserves its myriad plaudits, the M.B restaurant exudes the same essence of luxury and exclusivity that is reserved for the chosen few. It features a room used for welcome drinks and after-dinner coffee (including innovatively presented petits-fours) and cocktails, a contemporary-style main dining room with a predominantly white decor, and two glass-fronted galleries that are used as terraces in the summer months. On his meticulously prepared à la carte and two tasting menus, chef Erlantz Gorostiza faithfully recreates the amazing dishes devised by culinary maestro Martín Berasategui (including many of the latter’s iconic dishes and the year in which they were created), through dishes bursting with passion, technique and flavour that are based around the island’s best ingredients. We were particularly impressed by the “soldier shrimp” from El Hierro over an almond kernel with green gazpacho and shiso sorbet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
232;LÚ Cocina y Alma;Spain;Jerez de la Frontera;Zaragoza 2, Jerez de la Frontera, 11402, Spain;36.6876345;-6.1357554;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Juanlu Fernández, a fan of slow cooking over a wood fire, defines his style as “rearguard avant-garde”, an expression that highlights his personal, somewhat crazy interpretation of cooking which is based around classic French cuisine but which also showcases the best Andalucian ingredients. In his attractive restaurant, designed by Mexican architect Jean Porsche, he aims to personalise the experience by involving guests in the creative process (the kitchen is visible from the dining room) through two tasting menus that define his cuisine to perfection: “Duxende”, which is described as the restaurant’s soul, and “El Festín”, a journey across the senses, enabling guests to discover the region’s history and recipes. As a result, seemingly humble dishes (such as the Atlantic sea bass stew “a la roteña” and the cuttlefish “a la cochambrosa”) are transformed by stellar technique and premium ingredients. The wines and sherries of Jerez take centre stage in the wine pairing options, as well as featuring prominently on the cocktail list.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
233;Bao Li Xuan;China Mainland;Shanghai;3F, Chamber of Commerce Shanghai, Lane 108, North Shanxi Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.242798;121.482315;76;true;true;Cantonese;The Bvlgari Hotel's Chinese restaurant is nestled in an adjacent century-old building, complete with six private rooms inspired by Bvlgari jewellery. Solid skills and precision mark dishes such as soy-marinated chicken with silky flesh and a hint of Chinese rose wine aromas. Hand-crafted dim sum are the main event – the flaky, airy puff pastry is particularly well done. Try the whole abalone or char siu pork pastry for a full-flavoured bite.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
234;Canton 8 (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;63 Runan Street, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.204708;121.47799;16;false;false;Cantonese;This is the place to go for quality dim sum and classic Cantonese fare at affordable prices. Under the experienced Chef Mak from Hong Kong, the menu has been slightly revamped. Rest assured that quintessential all-time favourites such as double-boiled soups, stir-fries and seafood dishes are still served. The signature char siu pork entices with its appetising colour, springy texture and robust flavours. Save room for the exquisite desserts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
236;The House of Rong;China Mainland;Shanghai;170 Nanyang Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.22789;121.45071;60;false;true;Taizhou;A historical mansion once belonging to architect IM Pei's family is now home to the Shanghai flagship of this upmarket dining group. Adorned by Pei's original drawings and traditional architectural motifs in the Suzhou style, the space befits the class of the brand. The seafood-focused menu can be customised to your party's liking, delivering an array of flavours with top-notch ingredients mostly from Taizhou, such as wild-caught yellow croaker.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
237;Fu He Hui;China Mainland;Shanghai;1037 Yuyuan Road, Changning, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2205002;121.4250678;100;false;false;Vegetarian;Exuding Zen-inspired serenity, the rooms reflect a philosophy that veganism isn’t just about the food, but is a way of life. Only set menus are served and they change every season to make use of the best local ingredients. Masterfully crafted and plated courses include some authentically recreated recipes from the past. Tea is also closely related to Zen so do order from the extensive tea menu to complement the dishes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
238;8 ½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana;China Mainland;Shanghai;6-7F, Associate Mission Building, 169 Yuanmingyuan Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.244394;121.48346;47;false;true;Italian;The third restaurant under the aegis of chef Umberto Bombana comes with a glitzy cocktail bar and a balcony with jaw-dropping views. But the glass-clad wine cellar with amazing selections – both by the glass and by the bottle – also catches the eye. The kitchen excels at well-judged Italian classics, complemented by a seafood-heavy tasting menu that showcases the ocean's finest flavours alongside handmade pasta and bread that are simply unmissable.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
239;Imperial Treasure Fine Chinese Cuisine;China Mainland;Shanghai;L402-403, 4F, Yi Feng Galleria, 99 East Beijing Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2425862;121.4844198;56;true;true;Cantonese;This restaurant from the Singaporean group is furnished in a black colour scheme and generously decorated with crystals, which befits the well-crafted dim sum, barbecued meat and seafood it serves. Specialities like scrambled ‘osmanthus’ egg with crabmeat, roasted chicken stuffed with glutinous rice, and diced chicken with tofu and salted fish in claypot all exhibit finesse and refinement. Double-boiled soups are also highly sought-after.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
240;Ji Pin Court;China Mainland;Shanghai;3F, 55 South Wulumuqi Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.206108;121.448654;50;true;false;Cantonese;This oasis in the bustling city centre serves traditional Cantonese cooking, and its chef is particular about every detail. The signature fried chicken with sand ginger in claypot smells and tastes divine, and every piece of meat and condiment is diced in uniform sizes. Tea-smoked pigeon seduces with juicy flesh and smoky depth from pu erh tea leaves. Ask the sommelier to pair your food with wine from their well-curated selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
241;102 House;China Mainland;Shanghai;5F, The House of Roosevelt, Bund 27, 27 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2423721;121.4854918;83;true;false;Cantonese;The story of 102 House started in a residential home in Foshan, Guangdong. The kitchen is helmed by a chef with around 20 years of experience. For diners to experience the quintessence of traditional Cantonese banquets, various set menus are offered. Items change seasonally, but his signature sweet and sour pork is always available, featuring the cut between loin and belly for the perfect texture, alongside house-made fruit vinegar.;Air conditioning;[]
243;Arnolfo;Italy;Colle di Val d'Elsa;viale della Rimembranza 24, Colle di Val d'Elsa, 53034, Italy;43.4221;11.1165;70;false;true;Creative, Country cooking;With sharp lines created by the use of iron and glass, this modern building is especially designed to allow guests to admire the views from wherever they’re sitting. To the rear of the dining room, the large open-view kitchen framed by a superb yellow Siena marble wall is home to chef Gaetano Trovato (Mentor Chef Award 2024) and his team. Although there are three tasting menus available, one of which is vegetarian, any of the courses can also be chosen à la carte style. We could say so much about Arnolfo’s cuisine, but we’ll limit ourselves to mentioning the bread (which has been central to this chef’s work from the very beginning), duck, Chianina beef, Valdarno chicken and the ice-cream which always features among the desserts. Our inspector particularly enjoyed the delightful amuse-bouche with which guests are welcomed, the caponata with Taggiasca olives and basil, and the mullet served with white asparagus, peas and mint. The wine list is impressive, both for its quality and for the extensive selection of wines not only from Italy and France but also from other countries around the world – 7,000 different labels in total.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
244;Duomo;Italy;Ragusa;via Cap. Bocchieri 31, Ragusa, 97100, Italy;36.9267762;14.7408182;65;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;Chef Ciccio Sultano provides an intimate portrait of Sicily at this restaurant situated just a stone’s throw from the Duomo di San Giorgio in the heart of Ibla, one of the most charming historic centres in Sicily. Drawing on his deep knowledge of the region, he creates some of the island’s most spectacular cuisine, which is served in comfortable, intimate dining rooms. There are two tasting menus, from which dishes can also be chosen à la carte. We highly recommend the pasta with sea urchin, chard and hazelnuts.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
245;Harry's Piccolo;Italy;Trieste;piazza Unità d'Italia 2, Trieste, 34121, Italy;45.6497242;13.7675069;74;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Thanks to its hushed ambience, Harry’s Piccolo is an ideal choice for a romantic dinner or a business meal, with fine cuisine prepared by chefs Matteo Metullio and Davide De Pra (Passion Dessert Award 2024). Despite their youth, these two chefs demonstrate plenty of ability and creativity, serving dishes that showcase local meat, fish and seafood, and seasonal vegetables, as well as hints of the Orient, in this elegant setting. Memorable dishes include the tagliatelle with mussel water, saffron, sea urchins and wild fennel, and desserts such as the sesame ice cream with pepper cream and a touch of dashi. The wine list focuses particularly on the region, while also featuring some top-quality labels from outside Italy including a good selection of sparkling wines such as the renowned Krug champagne. Added bonuses are the friendly service, and an outdoor space for an aperitif or after-dinner drink with views of one of Italy’s most beautiful squares.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
246;Torre del Saracino;Italy;Vico Equense;via Torretta 9, Vico Equense, 80069, Italy;40.6606947;14.419559;61;false;true;Creative;From the coast road you take a series of hairpin bends down to Marina di Equa, the beach at Vico, where you will see this old fortified tower standing just a few metres from the sea. In the tower itself, with music playing in the background, guests can savour an aperitif accompanied by an extraordinary selection of imaginative antipasti that offer an introduction to the excellent cuisine that awaits. From here, you move into one of two dining elegant dining rooms decorated in vintage 1970s style which look out at Vesuvius and the Bay of Naples – the setting for a meal that will linger long in the memory. Gennaro Esposito is one of the best chefs in Campania, creating beautifully presented dishes of meat and fish (often in the same dish) that are not only delicious but also full of the colour and vitality of his region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
247;St. George by Heinz Beck;Italy;Taormina;viale San Pancrazio 46, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.8554565;15.2900353;78;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;One of the most desirable and exclusive locations in Taormina, the St. George is situated in the Hashbee Hotel, an early-20C villa on the edge of Taormina’s historic centre which has retained all the charm of a private house with its elegant lounge and breathtaking terrace adorned with palm trees that frame the Straits of Messina. The cuisine comes courtesy of a partnership between Heinz Beck and resident chef Salvatore Iuliano. The three-starred Michelin chef’s instinctive elegance and gastronomic intuition combine with Calabrian-born Salvatore’s passionate and colourful take on Mediterranean cuisine. Together, the cuisine and setting guarantee an unforgettable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
248;Agli Amici;Italy;Godia;via Liguria 252, Godia, 33100, Italy;46.1021988;13.2661162;60;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Serving signature cuisine, Agli Amici is one of the leading restaurants in Friuli-Venezia Giulia, a border region of diverse cultural influences that is teeming with top-quality ingredients. Many of these are showcased on the two tasting menus (one of which is vegetarian), from which guests can also choose individual dishes à la carte. Owner-chef Emanuele Scarello makes full use of the array of ingredients from the region’s pastureland, mountains and vegetable gardens, which he transforms into culinary works of art. His interesting use of Godia potatoes involves a modern reinterpretation of a local butter and sage dish using roots, apple and fermented turnips. Front of house, Michela is responsible for a young, close-knit and professional team of staff.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
249;La Rei Natura by Michelangelo Mammoliti;Italy;Serralunga d'Alba;via Roddino 21, Serralunga d'Alba, 12050, Italy;44.5942745;8.0002065;24;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;At this restaurant, the young yet already experienced Piedmontese chef (who also has Calabrian origins) offers three tasting menus. Dishes are also available à la carte style on two of these – “ Emozioni” (which features creative dishes inspired by childhood memories and flavours) and “Voyage” (ingredients, recipes and influences from the chef’s experience working around the world, including a delicious mango and coconut dessert). The third, Mad100% Natura, is a blind tasting menu on which the chef demonstrates his love and passion for his ingredients with real creativity. Most of his vegetables are sourced from local biodynamic gardens and greenhouses. On our last visit, we particularly enjoyed the courgettes “alla beccafico”, spaghetti with tomato sauce in honour of Nonna Tita, and the vegetable pizza served as a dessert. The high quality of the cuisine is equalled by the impressive selection of wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
250;Caino;Italy;Montemerano;via della Chiesa 4, Montemerano, 58014, Italy;42.6220221;11.4906283;86;true;true;Tuscan, Contemporary;Standing in the centre of a charming Tuscan village, Caino is at the epicentre of the cuisine of the Maremma, where Valeria Piccini is its proudest ambassador. This skilful chef sources the best ingredients from the region and then extracts every ounce of flavour from them, as demonstrated by the cacio cheese ravioli in beetroot cream and the pici pasta “alla amatriciana”. If you’re a fan of fish and seafood, try the stew which is made using delicately flavoured fish and a cream sauce, and served with blanched seasonal vegetables and traditional Tuscan crostino. Front of house, Valeria is ably assisted by son Andrea, who oversees the well-stocked wine cellar featuring a selection of different Brunello and Barolo vintages, as well as Bordeaux-style Tuscan labels, all at excellent prices. And if you’re in company, make sure you share a good Vin Santo Occhio di Pernice from 1988 or 1989. In summer, the bistro-style Il Giardino di Caino opens on the terrace, serving simpler dishes inspired by old family traditions.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
251;Seta by Antonio Guida;Italy;Milan;via Andegari 9, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4694121;9.1910082;92;false;false;International, Contemporary;Situated within the Mandarin Oriental hotel, a popular choice for international travellers, this restaurant serves cuisine that reflects the cosmopolitan flavours of Milan. Three tasting menus are available: the first showcases chef Antonio Guida’s classic specialities, the second has a seasonal focus, and the third chooses one particular ingredient as its theme. In spring, different species of oily fish take centre stage including anchovies, spatula fish and bonito served with whelks, kidneys and samphire, all of which are truly delicious! The extensive wine selection features a choice of wines by the glass as well as some excellent magnum options, including a few fine vintages.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[7]
252;La Madia;Italy;Licata;corso Filippo Re Capriata 22, Licata, 92027, Italy;37.1070131;13.9338055;18;true;true;Creative, Sicilian;Park in one of the streets near this restaurant and prepare yourself for a delightful journey through Sicily and its culinary traditions! Chef Pino Cuttaia, who is demonstrably in love with his native island, highlights his ingredients in a simple and unfussy way. He uses contemporary techniques, such as in the extremely light mozzarella and tomato dish served at the beginning of the meal, as well as more traditional methods evident in the black Nebrodi suckling pig served with a tomato-based “sugo della Domenica” (Sunday gravy). The two small dining rooms with a modern and minimalist feel offer an attractive setting for this enjoyable culinary experience. Wine-enthusiasts will appreciate the interesting selection of labels (including large bottles popular with connoisseurs). We recommend the 2019 Baglio Cristo di Campobello Adènzia, a red wine with earthy notes and delightful finesse.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
253;Madonnina del Pescatore;Italy;Marzocca;via Lungomare Italia 11, Marzocca, 60019, Italy;43.6806944;13.2821211;31;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;It’s now forty years since the Madonnina opened in 1984, yet chef Moreno Cedroni has not lost the creative touch that has resulted in him becoming one of the most influential chefs of his generation. Year after year, eating at La Madonnina remains a novelty: the menu succeeds like no other in reflecting past traditions and future culinary trends, especially in its fish and seafood dishes, and new dishes are added regularly, often having been researched in the laboratory next to the restaurant using specialised food technology. There are two tasting menus available: “Ricordi d'infanzia & Mariella 1984-2024” featuring chef Cedroni’s great classic dishes, and “Luca e Moreno... Il Viaggio di Marco Polo” which includes dishes with an Asian and Middle Eastern influence. The chef’s wife Mariella oversees the excellent service front of house, while this wonderful couple’s commitment to their cuisine is also demonstrated by their vegetable garden situated almost right on the beach, which provides vegetables infused with the salty sea air – a brilliant idea that represents their strong connection to the land. The wine list features a popular selection of French sparkling wines.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
254;Campo del Drago;Italy;Montalcino;Località Castiglion del Bosco, Montalcino, 53024, Italy;43.08386;11.422479;27;true;false;Contemporary, Tuscan;A certain amount of patience is required to get to this restaurant accessed via a dusty yet attractive dirt track that wends its way through typical Tuscan landscapes. On arrival, you’ll find an enchanting village of medieval origin with a tower and an old, frescoed church, where the Rosewood Castiglion del Bosco (awarded 3 Michelin keys) offers excellent service, splendid guestrooms and one of the best restaurants in the region. Here, chef Matteo Temperini serves some of the most interesting and creative dishes in Tuscany, many of which are prepared using vegetables from the hotel’s own kitchen garden, all showcased on three tasting menus and an à la carte from which a minimum of three courses must be chosen. Dishes are served in an elegant, contemporary-style dining room with a panoramic terrace, while the wine list features over 700 labels with a focus on the region – plenty of Brunellos, plus a particularly noteworthy 2016 Sasso al Sole, also available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
255;Castel fine dining;Italy;Tirol;vicolo dei Castagni 18, Tirol, 39019, Italy;46.6862223;11.1568653;17;false;true;Creative, International;180° views of the Val Venosta provide the theatrical setting for chef Gerhard Wieser’s precise, technical cuisine at this restaurant, where the tasting menu changes with the seasons and focuses on the region, with the exception of a few ingredients such as the Sicilian scampi which offer an exquisite alternative to the meat dishes on offer here. Highlights include the local, organic suckling pig ravioli served with parmesan foam and three types of pepper (Szechuan, South Tyrolean and Indian) which add an original flavour to the dish. Talented sommelier Ivana is on hand to help with wine choices, paying careful attention to guests’ individual preferences, while praise is also due to Florian and his staff for their excellent service.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
256;Villa Feltrinelli;Italy;Gargnano;via Rimembranza 38/40, Gargnano, 25084, Italy;45.693253;10.669477;57;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;Villa Feltrinelli was the lakeside holiday home of the Milanese family of the same name, who chose this beautiful location on Lake Garda for its scenery of rugged mountains and its relaxing ambience. Today, over a century later, this beautiful setting is home to a luxury hotel and restaurant. Sip an aperitif on the lakeside, then move to the beautiful terrace or elegant dining room to enjoy Stefano Baiocco’s surprise tasting menu which features freshwater fish, seafood and the finest cuts of Italian meat, all expertly prepared and skilfully flavoured with different aromatic herbs. In short, this restaurant has it all – timeless appeal, striking architecture and breathtaking beauty.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
257;Il Pagliaccio;Italy;Rome;via dei Banchi Vecchi 129/a, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.89793;12.4673729;77;true;false;Creative, Innovative;From its location in the heart of Rome, this restaurant takes guests on a culinary journey across the globe, with a focus on Asia and Japan in particular. Anthony Genovese blends influences from his experiences and travels to astonishing effect on two tasting menus – one dedicated to recipes that have become his signature dishes over the years, the other featuring new creations, all served in a quiet, elegant setting where excellent service is the order of the day. When the restaurant is open at lunchtime (on Saturdays), there’s also a shorter tasting menu, while if you want a longer and more private experience, you can book the Parallelsmenu served in a small room for a maximum of six guests.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
258;Locanda Sant'Uffizio Enrico Bartolini;Italy;Cioccaro;strada Sant'Uffizio 1, Cioccaro, 14030, Italy;45.0271679;8.2778294;82;true;true;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Nestled amid the picturesque hills of the Monferrato region, this restaurant overseen by multi-Michelin-starred Enrico Bartolini sees Gabriele Boffa at the helm in the kitchen, a chef who is young in years but already a real connoisseur of Piedmontese cuisine. With experience in some of the world’s best restaurants behind him, Boffa has accumulated expert knowledge and remarkable technical skills. His cuisine ranges from classic regional dishes interpreted in their purest form – such as his extraordinary agnolotti del plin – to more creative options, which demonstrate a connection with the region, whether in their ingredients or recipes. The setting here is that of an old monastery converted into a smart hotel, with meals served either in an elegant dining room or in the old limonaia (where lemon trees were once stored). The dishes on offer will linger long in the memory, from the generous amuses-bouches to the delicious bread and incredible focaccia, the top-quality meat and much more besides!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
259;Santa Elisabetta;Italy;Florence;piazza Santa Elisabetta 3, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7717322;11.2558883;68;false;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Thought to date back to Byzantine times, the Torre della Pagliazza has had many uses over the centuries, including housing a women’s prison in the 12C. Today it is home to one of the most interesting gourmet restaurants in Florence, where chef Rocco De Santis creates imaginative Mediterranean cuisine which is precise and full of flavour, with influences from his native Campania and an emphasis on fish and seafood. At lunchtime, a tasting menu of just three courses (“Carte Blanche”) is also available. As there are just a few tables here, guests are advised to book well in advance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
260;San Domenico;Italy;Imola;via Sacchi 1, Imola, 40026, Italy;44.3557172;11.7124431;55;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Although the kitchens have been recently updated with the latest equipment and a chef's table (“Saletta 22”) which allows guests to admire the chefs at work, San Domenico has retained its timeless charm – from the almost English-style ambience of its dining rooms to the outdoor tables overlooking an attractive square with public gardens in the historic centre. This setting provides the perfect backdrop for Massimiliano Mascia’s cuisine, which includes a selection of local and Italian dishes, all prepared simply, without excessive frills and with a focus on flavour and guest satisfaction that avoids modern trends. The extensive wine list offers an array of excellent labels, including a section dedicated exclusively to rare bottles produced before 1985!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
261;La Peca;Italy;Lonigo;via Alberto Giovanelli 2, Lonigo, 36045, Italy;45.3848934;11.3990641;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Overlooking attractive rolling hills, La Peca has long been a bastion of top-quality cuisine full of strong and decisive flavours, which aims to satisfy the palate without resorting to unnecessary frills. The extensive selection includes tasting menus and an à la carte, making it impossible to list all the dishes we found memorable. However, special mention should go to the Laguna Veneta seafood antipasto, as well as the extraordinary risotto with guinea fowl, leeks and Garganega grape must, and the classic wholewheat bigoli pasta with anchovies, featuring the creative addition of red onion ice-cream, marinated anchovies and anchovy crostini. The main dishes include the excellent mallard duck, as well as fish such as barbecued eel with radicchio, apple and horseradish. The restaurant has always been strong on desserts, serving memorable options such as a reinterpreted cassata, Mont Blanc and an extraordinary choice of ice-creams and sorbets. The impressive wine cellar features around 2 000 different labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
262;daní maison;Italy;Ischia;via Montetignuso 4, Ischia, 80077, Italy;40.7302578;13.9487527;39;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;This aptly named restaurant (At Nino’s house) is situated in chef Nino Di Costanzo’s own house in a residential district amid the hills of Ischia. Once over the threshold, you make your way through a garden planted with a variety of Mediterranean maquis shrubs and flowers, where aperitifs and post-dinner drinks are served in the evening. There are just a few tables in the dining room, which is crowned by a typical vaulted ceiling and where guests wishing to watch the chef at work can take a seat right in front of the kitchen. The dishes here are extremely elaborate, technical and sophisticated, perfect for anyone who loves concept-based cuisine with occasionally surprising results, including in presentation. If you’re coming here by car, take care on the last stretch of road which is particularly narrow.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
263;Terra The Magic Place;Italy;Sarentino;località Prati 21, Sarentino, 39058, Italy;46.6521107;11.3221975;26;false;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;At the end of the long uphill road through the woods, there is Terra, a magical place in a fairy-tale landscape, where you can enjoy a romantic and refined atmosphere combining the tradition of wood with modern elements, such as the wine cellar suspended over the room. The patron Heinrich Schneider has become a great chef starting out from being self taught. Study and application, together with a great love for and attachment to the mountains, did the rest. The gastronomic experience is offered through a single organized tasting menu in which, with a good pace, you can enjoy little masterpieces of aesthetics and taste. The locally sourced beef is splendid: a double tasting based on braised meat with a glaze of garbanzo beans, stellaria and liquid gnocchi, potatoes and charcoal-grilled tenderloin with a glaze of spices, pimpernel oil and scorzonera. For the wines, you need only trust in the completeness of the list (alcohol-free wines too) and the enthusiastic expertise of Gisela, the chef's sister. Being in a rather isolated position, you may like to take advantage of the exclusive private resort that completes a truly unique experience.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
264;Enoteca La Torre;Italy;Rome;lungotevere delle Armi 22/23, Rome, 00195, Italy;41.916491;12.4693268;16;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;Situated within the aristocratic Hotel Villa Laetitia with its fine architecture dating from 1911, this restaurant occupies a magnificent dining room adorned with stucco and columns, with splendid windows overlooking the exclusive garden – the perfect setting for a special occasion. Chef Domenico Stile has not forgotten his native Campania, which features in many of his dishes (from the Tarallo crackers to the baba dessert), alongside more creative influences from Italy and further afield.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
265;Taverna Estia;Italy;Brusciano;via Guido De Ruggiero 108, Brusciano, 80031, Italy;40.9083323;14.4232938;64;false;true;Contemporary, Creative;An aromatic herb garden greets visitors to this restaurant, followed by jasmine-covered alcoves that provide the perfect setting for a romantic dinner in fine weather or, if you prefer to eat indoors, an elegant dining room with a wine cellar and open-view kitchen. The restaurant is run by brothers Mario and Francesco Sposito (the former front of house, the latter in the kitchen), who together keep alive the soul of the restaurant that they inherited from their parents. They have also improved the quality so that the restaurant’s reputation now extends well beyond the region. Choose from different tasting menus (from which dishes can be chosen à la carte if you prefer) featuring remarkable and exciting dishes influenced by the flavours of Campania. More than a thousand wines, including an impressive choice of French labels, complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
266;Krèsios;Italy;Telese;via San Giovanni 59, Telese, 82037, Italy;41.2045624;14.5000207;41;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;This old country house is the setting for some of the region’s most innovative cuisine. There’s no choice here, just one long surprise tasting menu with many courses that takes guests on a fast-paced and exciting culinary voyage. Although some of the dishes are inspired by Campanian traditions, the menu features flavours from around the world, recreating often little-known Italian and international recipes with a personalised twist. Chef Giuseppe Iannotti always succeeds in surprising his guests, thanks to his ingredients, cooking techniques and stunning presentations. A selection of wines from small-scale producers completes the picture – after all, Krèsios is simply another name for Bacchus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
267;Il Piccolo Principe;Italy;Viareggio;piazza Giacomo Puccini 1, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.8809756;10.2355866;60;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;Situated on the ground floor of the iconic Grand Hotel Principe di Piemonte, one of Versilia’s finest hotels, this gourmet restaurant boasts an elegant, contemporary-style dining room which has recently been extended into an exclusive wing adorned with works of art and bespoke designer furniture. Giuseppe Mancino is the name behind the success of this restaurant, a talented chef from Campania who delights his guests with his beautifully presented, “photogenic” cuisine. His dishes are creative and enticing, delicious and at the same time elegant – he manages to find the perfect balance between the fragrant flavours of Mediterranean cuisine and the precision of French technique. His dishes are showcased on three tasting menus, one of which is vegetarian, from which courses can be chosen individually à la carte style. The wine list is also excellent, proudly highlighting labels from Tuscany while at the same time including a selection of French options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
268;Verso Capitaneo;Italy;Milan;piazza del Duomo 21, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4648103;9.189585;92;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;The two Capitaneo brothers, united by their passion for cuisine yet with very different characters, have opened this restaurant in Piazza Duomo following years of experience working in Michelin-starred restaurants. In this informal ambience, guests have the option of dining either at black glass tables or at large benches arranged around the kitchen, from where they can observe the entertaining sight of the chef at work in the kitchen. The cuisine focuses on extremely fresh, top-quality ingredients showcased using unfussy techniques that put flavour centre stage. Exciting dishes include the blue lobster with yellow courgettes and the house “welcome” snack – an intriguing rose of beetroot petals and caviar, the latter one of the restaurant’s most featured posts on Instagram.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
269;Antica Osteria Cera;Italy;Lughetto;via Marghera 24, Lughetto, 30010, Italy;45.3881476;12.1302222;43;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;One of Italy’s most famous addresses for fish and seafood, this restaurant offers an extensive menu featuring classic house favourites alongside a growing list of more modern options. In this elegant, modern and minimalist-style setting (despite the name, don’t expect a trattoria-style ambience here!) enjoy raw fish dishes and grilled options alongside more traditional, often Venetian, specialities such as the Venetian-style spider crab, and classic Italian dishes such as the warm steamed fish salad and the fritto misto (mixed fried fish). In all dishes, the excellent quality of the ingredients shines through. There’s also an excellent wine list, with a particular focus on white wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
270;Antica Corona Reale;Italy;Cervere;via Fossano 13, Cervere, 12040, Italy;44.63505;7.788635;75;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Situated between the Langhe and Monviso, this long-established restaurant celebrated its 200th anniversary a few years ago. Run by the Vivalda family for five generations, the restaurant started out as a dairy farm before gaining a well-earned reputation for its cuisine. Owner-chef Gian Piero Vivalda (Passion Dessert Award 2024) creates top-quality menus featuring expertly prepared, colourful and aromatic dishes. Popular with food-lovers from Italy and abroad, Cervere is also a point of reference for many local businesses who supply the restaurant with capon, guinea fowl, veal, Carmagnola peppers, porcini mushrooms and much more besides. The menu offers an array of enticing flavours, with modern dishes featuring alongside classic favourites, including a delicate raviolo of bagna càuda served with legendary bouillabaisse, which has made a reappearance on the menu after guests’ insistent requests. In summer, dine alfresco in the shade of a beautiful pergola among colourful flowers and a small fountain. Two small private rooms are available for intimate dinners, one of which is in the wine cellar surrounded by legendary bottles of wine. There’s also a small shop selling cakes and biscuits.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
271;Glam Enrico Bartolini;Italy;Venice;calle Tron, sestiere Santa Croce 1961, Venice, 30135, Italy;45.4413057;12.3298209;55;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;The discreet, partially hidden entrance to Palazzo Venart opens into what is a rarity in Venice – a small but charming garden with beautiful furniture in what is a genuine orangery. A second garden overlooks the Grand Canal and offers tables where, in summer, guests can enjoy a coffee or liqueur after their meal. Nestled between these two gardens, a magnificent hotel is home to the restaurant itself, where Michelin-starred chef Enrico Bartolini and the highly talented resident chef Donato Ascani offer guests a fine-dining experience. There are two tasting menus: “Arte, orti e laguna” which features dishes that pay tribute to Venice and its culinary traditions, and “I Classici del Glam”, showcasing iconic dishes from the chef’s long career. Every course is prepared with the chef’s natural instinct for care and passion and is full of intense and harmonious flavours. The option of arriving here by boat makes this restaurant even more exclusive.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
273;Miramonti l'Altro;Italy;Concesio;via Crosette 34, località Costorio, Concesio, 25062, Italy;45.6135819;10.2043986;98;false;false;Italian Contemporary, French;A French-Italian couple is at the helm in this attractive classic-style villa on the outskirts of Brescia, where a few tables have been laid out in the bay windows overlooking the garden. The friendly, experienced wife oversees the front of house, while her Breton husband is in the kitchen, where he recreates memories of his childhood in France through his use of French ingredients and culinary techniques. The menu also features more obviously Italian and Mediterranean dishes, all of which showcase the delicious, generous flavours that are the hallmark of the cuisine here. There is also an unforgettable cheese trolley with an excellent selection of cheeses in which Italy has the upper hand!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
274;Acquolina;Italy;Rome;via del Vantaggio 14, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9086474;12.4753719;79;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;This modern, softly lit restaurant is situated in The First Roma hotel near Piazza del Popolo. With few decorations to distract the gaze and discreet, professional service, all the attention here is concentrated on Daniele Lippi’s cuisine. The chef creates two tasting menus – the first, shorter option focuses on fish dishes, while the second longer menu also includes a few meat options. Whichever you choose, you’ll enjoy creative cuisine which is also hearty, generous and full of substance, with a strong emphasis on aromatic herbs and a few barbecued dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
275;D'O;Italy;Cornaredo;piazza della Chiesa 14, loc. San Pietro all'Olmo, Cornaredo, 20007, Italy;45.48711;9.01175;82;false;true;Creative, Italian Contemporary;Two of the three dining rooms at this restaurant overlook a charming square with an elm tree and 17C church. After two decades of hard, painstaking work on his own, combined with years of experience elsewhere (including early spells with top chefs such as Marchesi and Ducasse), chef Davide Oldani has by now developed his own precise, recognisable style and is an established personality in the world of Italian cuisine. His creative dishes are rooted in Italian traditions and showcase superlative technique, beautiful presentation and convincing flavours. Year after year, this chef fine-tunes his “pop” cuisine with a real focus on detail, as demonstrated by the workshop he has created for his flour and yeast products. Our inspector particularly praised the warm and cold Grana Padano served with caramelised onions – an exciting interpretation of an iconic dish!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
276;L'Olivo;Italy;Anacapri;via Capodimonte 14, Anacapri, 80071, Italy;40.5559154;14.2220085;97;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;This two-Michelin-starred restaurant is situated far from the crowded alleyways of Capri, in the greener and more residential Anacapri, where its backdrop is the semi-hidden Capri Palace, one of the island’s most luxurious hotels. Here, a large, elegant drawing room is the setting for Italian cuisine with a particular focus on Campania, with dishes which are occasionally reinterpreted with a modern twist and always brightly coloured and full of flavour. A real pleasure for the palate, with primi that are truly exploding with flavour (such as the eliche pasta with rock fish and the risotto with a Neapolitan ragu), chef Andrea Migliaccio’s cuisine is accompanied by impeccable and professional service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
277;Magnolia;Italy;Longiano;via Pelliciano 35, loc. Montilgallo, Longiano, 47020, Italy;44.0731058;12.3498464;88;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Situated in the elegant Relais Villa Margherita, an 18C villa converted into a stylish residence with just six guestrooms, verdant grounds and a swimming pool, Magnolia occupies a contemporary, veranda-style dining room with large picture windows boasting sweeping views of the Romagna hills as far as the mountainous “peak” of San Marino. Here, skilful chef Alberto Faccani serves a clever combination of the classic favourites that have marked his career, alongside other more unusual dishes that demonstrate a tireless search for experimentation. His contemporary style is elegant and balanced, as demonstrated by the delicate coconut milk sauce that provides the final flourish to his cuttlefish with caviar and peas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
278;Piazzetta Milù;Italy;Castellammare di Stabia;corso Alcide De Gasperi 23, Castellammare di Stabia, 80053, Italy;40.7018717;14.4829218;35;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Champagne enthusiasts will be in their element here, thanks to a wine list (presented on a tablet) that features almost 5 000 labels. Emanuele oversees the wine selection with great enthusiasm, introducing guests to his world of small-scale wineries with a real ability to find something to suit every palate. Your dining experience begins in the wine cellar, where the first part of your meal is served in an enchanting setting surrounded by some of the world’s best wines. The whole family is involved in running this restaurant, which started out as a pizzeria and has since become one of the region’s best addresses thanks to the passion and dedication of the latest generation. Chef Maicol creates dishes from Campania as well as exotic fare from much further afield, ably assisted by his brothers Valerio and Emanuele front of house.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
279;Villa Elena;Italy;Bergamo;via San Vigilio 56, Bergamo, 24129, Italy;45.7105439;9.648062;43;false;false;Creative;Situated near the Città Alta in a delightful setting surrounded by hills, Villa Elena is one of the most sumptuous villas in the countryside around Bergamo. Housed in a 16C building with a medieval tower and a terrace-cum-garden, the restaurant boasts a stunning interior decor of stucco, marble, mirrors and frescoes. This luxurious ambience is more than equalled by the fine cuisine created by Marco Galtarossa in partnership with Enrico Bartolini (the Italian chef with the largest number of Michelin stars). The occasionally elaborate dishes are sometimes divided into several courses, and combined with a clever use of aromatic herbs, all of which makes this the perfect choice for a memorable meal and special occasion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
280;George Restaurant;Italy;Naples;corso Vittorio Emanuele 135, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8372677;14.2300686;87;false;true;Contemporary;This roof-garden restaurant in one of Naples’ most luxurious hotels (Grand Hotel Parker’s) boasts an open-view kitchen facing a breathtaking panorama that takes in Vesuvius, the Bay of Naples and the city itself, which extends below the hotel in an evocative display of sparkling lights. It’s a challenge for the cuisine to compete with so much beauty but young chef Domenico Candela is more than equal to the task. His cuisine showcases the culinary specialities of the city and further afield with extraordinary skill, combining superb produce and recipes from Campania with techniques learnt in France to produce truly remarkable reinterpretations of regional dishes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
281;Colonnade;Switzerland;Lucerne;Haldenstrasse 10, Lucerne, 6002, Switzerland;47.0552386;8.3197697;30;true;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;Dating back to 1906, the Mandarin Oriental, situated on the lakeshore, is certainly a stylish setting in which to dine. This restaurant exudes the charm of yesteryear with contemporary elegance. With wonderful Art Nouveau light fittings hanging from the high ceiling, striking marble columns and an almost floor-to-ceiling glazed wine cabinet, the interior is a sight to behold. Chef Gilad Peled and his enthusiastic team showcase their modern take on French cuisine – take, for example, the sweetbreads with peas, asparagus, morels and wild garlic. There are two tasting menus, which can comprise three, five or eight courses (with an optional additional cheese course), one of which is vegetarian. There is an excellent selection of wines from around the globe, and head sommelier Moritz Dresing provides the most astute recommendations. A nice touch: The tasting menu includes a brief visit to the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
282;Magdalena;Switzerland;Schwyz;Rickenbachstrasse 127, Schwyz, 6432, Switzerland;47.0169188;8.6659803;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The motto here is "raw, rough, regional." Chef Dominik Hartmann (whose CV includes a stint with Andreas Caminada) and his team win diners over with modern, seasonal cuisine that is aromatic and brimming with robust flavours. They certainly don't do things by halves here! Ingredients are sourced as locally as possible with a preference for working with small producers. There is a 100% vegetarian surprise menu comprising five to seven courses – five or six at lunchtime (Sat-Sun). The home-made bread is extremely morish! Great selection of Swiss wines. The sleek, upscale interior has floor-to-ceiling windows that afford an impressive view of the valley!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
284;La Table du Valrose;Switzerland;Rougemont;Place de la Gare 2, Rougemont, 1659, Switzerland;46.4886078;7.2085597;84;true;true;Modern French, Farm to table;At an altitude of some 1 000m, in the triangle formed by the cantons of Fribourg, Bern and Waad, this restaurant takes you to new heights of culinary enjoyment and refinement. Surrounded by a magnificent mountain landscape, the chic decor is an artful blend of Alpine wood, contemporary furnishings and designer lamps. Chef Benoît Carcenat creates modern and seasonal French cuisine that embraces both tradition and innovation. The menu features produce from the Pays d'Enhaut, Saanenland and Intyamon regions – a host of ingredients that have benefitted from the mountain air! List of 700 different wines for you to choose from. Modern guestrooms, exceptional service and a delicious breakfast round off this delightful experience.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
285;L'Atelier Robuchon;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai Wilson 37, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2121299;6.152408;80;true;true;French Contemporary;On the shores of Lake Geneva, luxury hotel The Woodward boasts a fine dining restaurant that is the epitome of elegance. In a space done out in warm dark wood and vivid reds, diners take their seats at high tables or at the counter affording interesting views into the open kitchen. Opt for the tasting menu (there is also a vegetarian set menu) or choose from the à la carte dishes. Service courtesy of a charming and highly attentive team!;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
287;The Japanese Restaurant;Switzerland;Andermatt;Gotthardstrasse 4, Andermatt, 6490, Switzerland;46.6363781;8.5947275;81;false;true;Japanese Contemporary, Fusion;In the sleek and stylish restaurant of luxury hotel The Chedi, at nearly 1 500m above sea level, Fabio Toffolon and his twin brother Dominik Sato are at the helm. Working with first-rate ingredients, they serve up an intriguing blend of Japanese cuisine and classic European influences – combining, for example, a classic beurre blanc with Asian flavours and premium-quality king crab. The highlight is the omakase menu, which has four to six courses. The focal point in the restaurant is the open kitchen – take some time to watch the chefs at work!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
288;La Brezza;Switzerland;Ascona;via Albarelle 16, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1507302;8.7728734;76;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Chef Marco Campanella serves highly personalised cuisine at this restaurant, where he pays careful attention to simple ingredients and combinations influenced by his many travels around the world, with an added touch of Mediterranean flavour thanks to his Italian origins. The two menus remain unchanged, namely “Moving Mountains” (vegan) and “Ispirazione” (with fish and meat), and guests are able to choose between six and eight courses. The wine list will more than satisfy connoisseurs, who will also enjoy the recommendations offered by the talented sommelier. In summer the terrace offers a delightful setting with exceptional views of Lake Maggiore.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
290;Da Vittorio - St. Moritz;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Johannes Badrutt 11, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4998838;9.8468053;45;true;true;Italian;If you happen to be in St Moritz in the winter season, then take advantage of the opportunity to dine at the stylish yet cosy restaurant of the Carlton Hotel, in its serene location overlooking the lake. During the winter months, a fantastic kitchen team serves up precise and light Italian cuisine that steers clear of fuss and frills. The focus lies squarely on the produce that goes into the dishes. Some of the brilliantly prepared specialties from the parent restaurant in Brusaporto, Lombardy, make an appearance, including, of course, the signature pasta dish, paccheri alla Vittorio, but also many fish dishes, such as crudo d'Amare, raw fish and shellfish. Plus, an excellent front-of-house team: confident, charming and classy!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
291;Einstein Gourmet;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Berneggstrasse 2, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4215599;9.375374;99;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;On the fifth floor of the renowned Hotel Einstein, chefs Sebastian Zier and Richard Schmidtkonz present an international set menu, showcasing exceptional precision and culinary artistry. Over four to six courses, diners are treated to meticulously crafted compositions of impeccably sourced, top-notch ingredients. A prime example is the exquisite French duck breast – bursting with flavour and finesse, cooked to a perfect rosy hue, it offers a delightful contrast of tenderness and texture, complemented by harmonious roast aromas. If you would like a vegetarian alternative, it's best to mention it when you book. In the stylish dining space, the exceptional front-of-house team will attend to you with charm and a laid-back demeanour. When it comes to wine, you are in good hands with sommelier Loris Lenzo, who engages with diners in a relaxed yet professional manner. With 3 000 labels stored in an impressive vaulted wine cellar made of white Bordeaux limestone, he presents the big names as well as the odd hidden gem from Switzerland.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
292;IGNIV by Andreas Caminada;Switzerland;Bad Ragaz;Bernhard-Simon-Strasse 2, Bad Ragaz, 7310, Switzerland;47.0003991;9.5022986;55;true;true;Creative;This stylish restaurant in a historical vaulted room inside the Grand Resort Bad Ragaz showcases a concept that was devised by none other than celebrated chef Andreas Caminada: an elaborate, creative "fine dining sharing experience". In keeping with the name (igniv is a Romansh word meaning "nest"), the focus is on the well-being of guests and the pleasure of communal dining. First-rate ingredients are used to create a very special set menu, each course of which is made up of several small dishes – all designed for sharing. Shored up by a competent sommelier, the charming service team is second to none. The outstanding wine list features top-notch wines, often regional, that are available by the glass. Last but not least, the impressive Candy Store awaits you.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
293;The Counter;Switzerland;Zurich;Bahnhofplatz 15, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3772343;8.5405447;42;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;After a successful stint at two-star restaurant 7132 Silver in Vals, Mitja Birlo has made the move to Zurich. Here, in an impressive building next to the main railway station – a prime city-centre location – he unleashes his cosmopolitan culinary concept. In a relaxed, modern and elegant interior, diners take their seats on comfortable bar chairs at the eponymous counter right next to the open kitchen to observe the creation of a surprise menu of numerous exciting delicacies, some larger, some smaller. One example is their sophisticated take on celeriac: it is served as a roasted slice, as an aromatic purée and as a tower of thinly sliced "celeriac pastrami", finished with a fantastic sauce that exudes the fruity, earthy tones of beetroot and the pleasingly mild spiciness of black pepper. In addition ot excellent wine pairings, there is a high-calibre alcohol-free alternative. The accomplished service team led by Florentina Birlo ensures that everything runs smoothly. Smaller groups can also reserve the Chef's Table.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
294;Mammertsberg;Switzerland;Freidorf;Bahnhofstrasse 28, Freidorf, 9306, Switzerland;47.4860199;9.3920453;62;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The exclusive boutique hotel is only one side of this beautiful old establishment with a fabulous view that reaches all the way to Lake Constance. Another is the restaurant run by the duo of MICHELIN-starred chefs, Andreas Caminada and Silvio Germann: here, the latter, as head chef, uses the best ingredients to cook up creative dishes – elaborate but not fussy, reduced yet with real depth of flavour. The whole service team is truly outstanding! The decor is an elegant blend of traditional and modern, and the terrace is wonderful.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
296;IGNIV Zürich by Andreas Caminada;Switzerland;Zurich;Marktgasse 17, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3719489;8.5437311;28;true;true;Sharing, Modern Cuisine;Andreas Caminada is the man behind this fabulous venture in the Marktgasse Hotel. In a high-ceilinged space with small glass-topped tables and striking blue curtains, diners are served a set menu designed for sharing. A superb selection of wines is available. Then there is the first-class service provided by the charming and accomplished front-of-house team. Our tip: Try an espresso from the house roastery in Fürstenau.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
297;Widder Restaurant;Switzerland;Zurich;Rennweg 7, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3722176;8.5398173;81;false;false;Modern French, Contemporary;In the chic fine dining restaurant of the luxurious Widder boutique hotel, chef Stefan Heilemann and his team skilfully bridge the gap between classic and modern cuisine, drawing on international influences. In their dishes, thoughtful preparation and precise technique meet elegance and well-balanced flavours. The chef's penchant for acidity shines through, for example, in his sherry vinegar escabeche sauce, which accompanies the perfectly cooked, slightly translucent red mullet fillet. Or take his rhubarb concoction, in which the tartness perfectly counters the sweetness of nut butter ice cream, the refreshing tang of yoghurt and the nuttiness of macadamia. Home-grown produce is also used. There are two tasting menus, one of which is vegetarian, each comprising four to six courses. You can also choose from the chef's classics on the "Supplements" menu. The highly adept waitstaff impress with their pleasingly relaxed approach. Tip: Book the Chef's Table! Widder Bar is one floor below.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
298;The Restaurant;Switzerland;Zurich;Kurhausstrasse 65, Zurich, 8000, Switzerland;47.3726725;8.5731534;65;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The Dolder Grand luxury hotel (a former "Kurhaus" or health resort, built in 1899) boasts a truly fantastic location above Zurich – even the driveway to the garage is impressive! If possible, book a window seat in the hotel's chic fine dining restaurant so you can savour the magnificent view of the city while you eat. The huge glass wine cabinet also draws the eye. Chef Heiko Nieder's elaborate and detail-oriented cooking is modern and creative but equally classical. This Schleswig-Holstein native always puts the (top-notch) produce centre stage and cooks up fantastically harmonious compositions. His vegetarian alternatives are no less impressive. Tip: the five-course "amuse-bouche menu", served at lunchtime, allows you to sample a good cross-section of the food.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
299;roots;Switzerland;Basel;Bachlettenstrasse 1, Basel, 4054, Switzerland;47.55043;7.581;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;It might come as a surprise to find such an outstanding fine dining restaurant in an event venue. The location of the Rhypark congress centre next to the Dreirosenbrücke, by the Rhine, is superb, the interior is chic and modern, and the terrace is wonderful. Then there is the creative cuisine of Pascal Steffen and his team, who serve a surprise menu comprising six, seven, nine or 10 courses, showcasing excellent produce, predominantly from the region – scan the barcode to reveal the ingredients. The food is primarily plant-based (eg the exceptional signature dish "roots garten"), but fish and meat also feature. The chefs take an appealingly pared-down approach, which in no way detracts from the depth of flavour and sophistication of their dishes! Harmonious pairings of fine wines or alcohol-free beverages are available by the glass. Delightfully attentive service courtesy of an adept front-of-house team.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
300;7132 Silver;Switzerland;Vals;Poststrasse 560, Vals, 7132, Switzerland;46.6226102;9.181299;16;true;true;Creative, Innovative;At this stylishly urban restaurant (housed in 7132 Hotel, a heritage building that is a magnet for design and architecture fans), Dutchman Marcel Koolen has taken charge of the kitchen. With the support of his international team and executive chef Matthias Schmidberger, he proposes highly creative cuisine with a strong vegetable component. For example, when he combines artichoke pieces cooked in salt dough with artichoke and potato crisps and pickled Vals vegetables and arranges them on a tomato, pepper and basil cream, the result is packed with incredible flavours. The chef is also a dab hand at preparing meat, fish and shellfish. The surprise menu, also available in a fully vegetarian form, can be accompanied by wine pairings or home-made alcohol-free pairings. As for the service, the team led by Franziska Wölfle is professional, charming and always on hand. The chefs, too, join in with serving and talk you through the dishes. The aperitif is taken in the kitchen, complete with a sneak peek behind the scenes.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
301;Pic Beau-Rivage Palace;Switzerland;Lausanne;Place du Port 17, Lausanne, 1006, Switzerland;46.5080909;6.6297747;49;false;true;Creative;After nearly a year's renovation, French chef Anne-Sophie Pic's luxurious restaurant now welcomes diners with its elegant, bright and modern leather livery overlooking the lake. This exquisite new atmosphere is a perfect match for the light, expressive and almost airy creations of chef Jordan Theurillat. Once past the entrance to the restaurant, there is a table-bar where excellent non-alcoholic cocktails and small plates to combine are prepared, using produce from the garden in particular. Dishes such as the famous ‘Lake Geneva féra impregnated with fig leaf from the garden and spruce, fresh almond cream with amazake’ or ‘venison chop marinated and smoked with juniper berry and imperator root, end-of-summer tomato confit with mace’ clearly express this refined and daring vision of cuisine, with a strong regional inspiration. In four set menus customers will find the same concern for demanding invention that has always linked the history of the Pic family to that of French gastronomy. Quality service.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
302;Taverne zum Schäfli;Switzerland;Wigoltingen;Oberdorfstrasse 8, Wigoltingen, 8556, Switzerland;47.5957416;9.0325819;90;false;false;Creative, Farm to table;A true culinary beacon in the region, this 300-year-old half-timbered house is wonderfully inviting from the outside. Chef-patron Christian Kuchler is a master of classic cuisine, but he also incorporates carefully balanced creative touches and Asian influences. All the dishes have one thing in common: the finest ingredients, which are showcased through precise technique, their natural flavours allowed to shine without relying on unnecessary flourishes. For example, the perfectly pan-seared hand-dived scallop with its lovely roasted notes harmonises beautifully with the creamy vin jaune foam, delicate little artichoke hearts, butter-soft mussels and lightly sautéed spinach. The set menu and à la carte dishes are equally enticing. The tastefully furnished and cosy lounges offer comfortable seating, as does the charming terrace. First-class service rounds off the experience perfectly – restaurant manager and sommelier Fabian Mennel provides expert wine recommendations. The list features some marvellous German Rieslings, regional gems and red wines from France and Italy with an impressive range of vintages.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
303;Ecco St. Moritz;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Maistra 3, Saint Moritz, 7512, Switzerland;46.4776485;9.8109132;63;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Ascona in summer, St Moritz in winter? This is how top chef Rolf Fliegauf and his team do it, changing locations according to the seasons. In the warm season they cook at Ecco on Lake Maggiore and as the snow settles on the ground they migrate to the Engadine valley, to the fine dining restaurant of the Giardino Mountain hotel. You can sense the energy and expertise of this Swabian-born chef – this is cuisine you can rely on! He wins over diners with the light and playful touch he brings to his modern dishes. Throughout the four to seven courses of the set menu, the focus is on the top-notch ingredients. Your highly committed and charming host, Jenifer Fliegauf, is the driving force behind the extremely friendly front-of-house team, ensuring her guests receive attentive and unflappable service.;Car park;[]
304;focus ATELIER;Switzerland;Vitznau;Seestrasse 18, Vitznau, 6354, Switzerland;47.0151885;8.4775489;98;false;true;Creative, International;This restaurant is as exclusive as everything else at the luxurious Park Hotel Vitznau. Patrick Mahler and his team offer a unique culinary experience in the form of an exciting six- or nine-course set menu. Full of contrasts, it blends classic, Japanese and Scandinavian elements. The signature dish is certainly worthy of its status: an exquisite combination of velvety duck liver ice cream, a spicy and delicately sweetened beef fillet tartare with an intensely flavoursome beetroot gel, dried beetroot cubes and egg yolk pearls. The quality of the ingredients is second to none, and the preparation is executed with the utmost precision. With over 35 000 bottles and comprehensive vintage collections, the wine cellar is a treasure trove for wine connoisseurs. The service is impeccable: seamless, professional, and the chefs personally present and explain each dish. The restaurant itself is upscale and chic, housed in an elegant and spacious glass cube overlooking the lake – the terrace is simply idyllic!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
306;Myojaku;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-2-34 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.659411;139.726652;77;false;true;Japanese;Hidetoshi Nakamura refuses to be bound by the conventions of Japanese cuisine. What’s important, he says, is not to cling to forms but to keep exploring, ever on the lookout for new ideas. One approach that embodies this mindset is vegetable mizuni, food prepared using only water and salt. Rather than lean on kombu and dried bonito flakes, Nakamura expresses the ingredients themselves, along with one of Japan’s treasures: water. Cuisine that captures the bounty of farm, mountain, ocean and river in its natural state is as clear and pure as water itself.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
307;PRISMA;Japan;Tokyo;6-4-6 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.661579;139.716582;51;true;true;Italian;Tomofumi Saito is a culinary artist who is always setting his sights on higher goals. Tagliolini with caviar and red wine sauce is his speciality. He prepares the caviar himself to ensure just the right degree of saltiness. The combinations of ingredients and sauces change over time, as he tinkers in search of the ideal, and thinks up his menu only after personally checking the quality of ingredients at the market. His wife, Noriko, writes up the menu daily, conveying the chef’s passion.;Air conditioning;[]
308;Seizan;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-17-29 Mita, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0073, Japan;35.647433;139.739938;81;false;false;Japanese;The name combines two of the four characters of Haruhiko Yamamoto’s name. The chef’s approach to cuisine and commitment to entertaining guests were both learned from his mentor in Gifu. He is also enthusiastic about guiding the next generation, as shown by the smiles and positive attitude of his young crew. Yamamoto may surprise with innovative dishes, but with wansashi—the pairing of sashimi and soup, considered the essence of Japanese cuisine—he stays true to tradition. Each item is the product of painstaking effort the customer never sees.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
309;Tempura Kondo;Japan;Tokyo;9F, 5-5-13 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671184;139.763104;54;false;false;Tempura;For half a century, this culinary artisan has spread the word of tempura around the world. By introducing vegetables, Tempura Kondo sought to establish tempura as a cuisine not only of Japan but of the world. Tempura, the chef explains, may technically be a fried food but its true nature is a steamed food. The flavour of each tempura piece is elicited by enrobing it in batter and using hot oil to draw out the moisture. The chef’s tempura of sweet potato, created to surpass the flavour of baked sweet potato, is typical of this.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
310;ASAHINA Gastronome;Japan;Tokyo;1-4 Nihombashikabutocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0026, Japan;35.68274;139.779323;26;true;true;French;Décor is chic in white and silver – like the cuisine, classic yet modern. Chef Satoru Asahina’s theme is ‘traditional heritage with modern innovation’. Classic recipes are read with a modern interpretation: for example, poulet en vessie – chicken wrapped in pig’s bladder. The name ‘Gastronome’ reflects Asahina’s desire that his restaurant become a gathering-place for gourmets. Elegant cuisine as beautiful as a painting.;Air conditioning;[]
311;Tempura Motoyoshi;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 2-8-11 Ebisunishi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0021, Japan;35.649532;139.707611;62;true;true;Tempura;The essence of tempura is removing moisture from seafood and vegetables using batter and oil. Kazuhito Motoyoshi opens a whole new world in tempura techniques with the use of liquid nitrogen. A scientific discovery: ‘molecular tempura’, as it were. The chef considers the coating of fine granules, frying temperature, richness or lightness of flavour and the temperature of each piece to bring out maximum deliciousness. The evolution of tempura stokes our curiosity and along with it continues to evolve. A ceaseless quest for the ultimate in flavour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
312;HOMMAGE;Japan;Tokyo;4-10-5 Asakusa, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0032, Japan;35.718485;139.79699;35;false;false;French, Contemporary;Modern French cuisine by Asakusa native Noboru Arai. The chef chose the name ‘Hommage’, meaning ‘respect’ or ‘tribute’, out of a conviction never to forget his gratitude to all who contributed to his success. The fare combines foodstuffs from various countries, pursuing originality with the emphasis on seasonal sensibility. Chickpea hummus comes from Arai’s experience in the south of France. Blancmange of kaminariokoshi (a sweet, rice-based cake) and financier made of ningyo-yaki mould are Arai’s hommage to Asakusa.;Air conditioning;[]
313;MAZ;Japan;Tokyo;3F, Tokyo Garden Terrace Kioicho, 1-3 Kioicho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 102-0094, Japan;35.679726;139.737003;79;true;true;Innovative;MAZ operates under the supervision of Virgilio Martínez Véliz, chef of Central Restaurante in Lima, Peru. Through gastronomy, MAZ interprets the abundant natural environment of Peru from the vertical perspective of altitude. Directing the kitchen here is Santiago Fernández Saim. The menu, organised into themes for each of Peru’s environments—the Pacific coast, the Amazon rainforest and the Andes—is an encounter between diverse ecosystems and the seasons of Japan.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
314;Florilège;Japan;Tokyo;2F,  Azabudai Hills Garden Plaza D, 5-10-7 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.661598;139.743562;55;false;false;French;After a debut in Minamiaoyama and an engagement in Gaiemmae, Florilège has taken a new stage in Azabudai. In his latest foray, Chef Hiroyasu Kawate enters the world of table d’hôte: guests are seated around a single large table to share the joy of good food and conversation. Another change is a switch to plant-based cuisine, with the accent on vegetables. With his eye on the future, Kawate is promoting the cause of sustainability.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
315;Ginza Fukuju;Japan;Tokyo;5F, 8-8-19 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.668529;139.761573;66;true;false;Japanese;Katsuhiro Onodera unearths exquisite flavours by combining the barest minimum of ingredients. The starting point for his creativity is his Tohoku hometown of Kesennuma, where he grew up surrounded by mountains on one side and ocean on the other. Turban shell and bamboo shoot soup, served in seashells, is a homegrown greeting to welcome the spring. Crab baked in the shell and hot pots are somehow hearty and delicate at the same time. The dishes engage all five senses, leaving lasting memories of what you ate.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
316;Kioicho Fukudaya;Japan;Tokyo;1-13 Kioicho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 102-0094, Japan;35.680327;139.735892;31;false;false;Japanese;The totality of this ryotei’s art—the cuisine, the ceremonial furnishings, the service—makes a deep impression. The original owner-chef learned the basics of cooking under the guidance of legendary epicure Kitaoji Rosanjin. The current chef, guardian of the traditions of the Fukuda family, displays his talents with creations that delight guests, squarely focused on respect for ingredients. He puts into practice Rosanjin’s famous dictum: ‘Eight or nine times out of ten, the quality of the ingredients selected determines the quality of a dish.’;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
317;ESqUISSE;Japan;Tokyo;9F, 5-4-6 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671688;139.763347;24;false;false;French, Contemporary;It is now over a decade since Lionel Beccat left his native France to take to a new stage in Japan. He travelled extensively in Japan, feeling the earth, breathing its natural world through his skin, to know its foodstuffs and culture intimately. Two cultures coexist inside his soul, stirring a new terroir in his imagination. The cuisine that inspiration creates is as subtle and beautiful as a work of art.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
318;Tempura Ginya;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 5-17-9 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.637444;139.723162;98;true;false;Tempura;Tempura is skilfully deep-fried using the convection of hot oil. The chef learned his craft by scrutinising each ingredient at the market and tinkering constantly with the oil in his pans. Thinly battered tempura pieces are fried quickly and lightly to prevent too much oil absorption. This unique method allows the chef to bring out their natural aroma and flavour. Sea urchin tempura and shiitake mushrooms stuffed with shrimp are legacies of the chef’s apprentice days, honed to a higher level.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
319;Den;Japan;Tokyo;2-3-18 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.67321;139.712697;29;true;true;Japanese;Den is a messenger of Japanese cuisine today, both in Japan and around the world. The goal is cooking that brings smiles to everyone’s faces, no matter where in the world they’re from. A salad called ‘Hatake no Yosu’ is the next evolution in takiawase, each vegetable cooked in a different way. A carrot medallion, carved like a smiley emoji, evokes a chuckle. Friendly service makes diners feel at home and food taste even better – no wonder the walls and pillars are festooned with autographs of appreciative visitors.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
320;Ginza Kojyu;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 5-4-8 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671381;139.763089;95;true;false;Japanese;Standing at a counter made from a 700-year-old cypress, Toru Okuda celebrates the vitality of nature through his cooking. The shop boasts water from Okuda’s native Shizuoka, fish from Suruga Bay and wasabi and tea from his home prefecture as well. His heartfelt respect and love for Japanese food led him to open a branch in Paris to spread the gospel of true Japanese cuisine. Opening a fish restaurant in a country without a culture of ikejime  was a bold move. By proclaiming food in which Japan can take pride before the world, Okuda is leading one of the world’s great cuisines into an exciting future.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
322;Sukiyabashi Jiro Roppongiten;Japan;Tokyo;3F, Roppongi Hills Residence B, 6-12-2 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.658713;139.729049;42;true;false;Sushi;Each piece of sushi is subtly modulated through the process of weighing, preparing and forming. The chef displays his finesse in seasoning sushi rice with rice vinegar, true to his conviction that sushi flavour is determined 60% by the rice and 40% by the toppings. The chef runs the kitchen with his sons, guiding them as mentor and disciples. His strict attitude reflects the spirit of a Showa-era craftsman. The chef learned to say “thank you” in numerous languages as a way to convey his gratitude to customers visiting from abroad.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
323;NARISAWA;Japan;Tokyo;2-6-15 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.671585;139.722147;83;false;false;Innovative;With a focus on ‘innovative satoyama cuisine’, this restaurant promotes the satoyama culture of Japan. The chef creates dishes inspired by the unique food culture connected to forests, rivers, lakes, and seas. ‘Bread of the Forest 2010’, made with wild yeast harvested from the Shirakami-Sanchi mountain range, is baked while showing off the leavening process. Innovation preserves the wisdom of predecessors who thrived in harmony with nature, passing these values to the next generation while breathing new life into them.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
324;Ginza Shinohara;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-8-17 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.673039;139.767805;53;false;false;Japanese;The vibrant and rustic menu is a miracle created by the chef’s journey. It intertwines the elegance of Japanese cuisine that reflects the changing seasons with the nostalgic flavours of country cooking. The appetisers echo ancient traditions, while boar and bear meat convey the satoyama culture. The Koka rice is cooked in a Shigaraki earthenware pot. What you get is the result of his childhood in Shiga and the skills he honed in the Kansai region.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
326;Kutan;Japan;Tokyo;2-5-5 Shintomi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0041, Japan;35.671572;139.774073;97;true;false;Japanese;Kotaro Nakashima’s twin obsessions are creativity and change. Fried items are served first, deftly paired with companionable beverages. Thin rolls of tuna are interspersed, putting his experience as a sushi chef to good use. Hot pots are filled with seasonal flavours such as pepper flowers and matsutake mushrooms, to the delight of guests. He pays close attention to temperature, aroma and texture, avoiding being a slave to convention. With a versatile and creative imagination, he is broadening the horizons of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
327;Akasaka Kikunoi;Japan;Tokyo;6-13-8 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.669635;139.734126;56;true;false;Japanese;Kikunoi’s pedigree is in ryotei culture, with its deep roots in Kyoto. Cobblestones hemmed in by bamboo and the harmonious ambience of sukiya-style architecture put the mind at rest. An attractive feature is the choice of tatami mat or counter seating, combining the charms of ryotei and kappo. The menu is identical to the Kyoto flagship, with ingredients and even water sourced from the ancient capital, ensuring consistency of flavour. Akasaka Kikunoi is devoted to its mission of spreading the message of Japanese cuisine to the world.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
328;Jingumae Higuchi;Japan;Tokyo;2-19-12 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.673471;139.710124;79;false;true;Japanese;While respecting tradition, the chef pursues originality. Years of accumulated experience and a constant drive for improvement foster creativity. The omakase set menu entertains with a dynamic interplay of hot and cold dishes and varying intensities of flavours. Soba is served after the rice, and several desserts are prepared so guests can choose their favourite. The variety of dishes reflects a heartfelt desire to ensure satisfaction.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
329;ZURRIOLA;Japan;Tokyo;4F, Kojun Bldg, 6-8-7 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670064;139.762822;74;false;false;Spanish, Contemporary;Zurriola is the name of a beach in San Sebastián. The chef will never forget his stay in Spain’s Basque Country, where every day was filled with passion. He applies the flame-manipulation skills learned there, such as using the plancha (steel grill) and the charcoal and glowing embers of the asado (barbecue). His culinary style he terms ‘modern Spanish’, is an update to traditional Spanish cooking. Ravioli of grapevine-smoked caviar shows off the Basque style.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
330;Sushi Kanesaka;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 8-10-3 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.667938;139.762691;76;true;true;Sushi;Shinji Kanesaka tells the story of Japanese culture in sushi. The elaborately designed sukiya-style interior design and dinnerware reflect this aesthetic. In crafting his nigiri, Kanesaka prizes seamless harmony among the sushi trinity of rice, topping and wasabi. His love for baseball in his student days taught him the importance of teamwork, and his command of his staff from behind the counter is reassuring. The chef has branches overseas as well, preaching the wonders of sushi to the world.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
331;King's Joy;China Mainland;Beijing;2 Wudaoying Hutong, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.946681;116.410004;95;true;false;Vegetarian;Adjacent to Yonghe Temple, this historical courtyard house-turned-restaurant has a muted decor inspired by Zen aesthetics. Since opening its doors over 10 years ago, its ethos has revolved around simple cooking methods such as steaming, slow-cooking and sautéing to accentuate the ingredients' natural flavours and therapeutic properties. Their three lacto-ovo vegetarian menus comprise over 10 courses, and all can be made vegan upon request.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
332;Jingji;China Mainland;Beijing;2F, The Ritz-Carlton Hotel, 83A Jianguo Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.910623;116.4856;85;false;true;Beijing Cuisine;Jingji is a portmanteau of ‘Beijing’ and ‘Yueji’, the official flower of the city. It specialises in royal cuisine that not only pays homage to the nation’s culinary traditions, but also captures the essence of regional recipes. The seasonally driven menu focuses mainly on seafood and vegetables – pre-order your favourite seafood. The must-try crabmeat and crab roe on crispy fish maw impresses by deep umami and contrasting textures.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
333;Shanghai Cuisine;China Mainland;Beijing;South side of Pacific Century Place, 2A Gongrentiyuchang North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.930881;116.453254;65;true;true;Shanghainese;This cosy, understated dining room is adorned in neutral greys with teal green accents. The Shanghainese head chef and the mostly Shanghainese kitchen team reinterpret the classics with modern twists. Check out the chef’s recommendations that feature rare seasonal ingredients. Deep-fried pork thigh with garlic and red fermented tofu boasts a crispy crust and irresistible aromas. Attentive, but unfawning service makes for a total experience.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
334;Lu Shang Lu;China Mainland;Beijing;2A01-2A03 / 2A05-2A13, 2F, Sunshine Financial Center, No.1 Tower, 33 Jinghui Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9106329;116.4570814;16;true;true;Shandong;Shandong cooking is the speciality here, especially Confucius cuisine, with sea cucumber and live seafood shipped daily from Jiaodong peninsula. The chef from Yantai knows the food from his home province inside out and is clearly proud to serve his specialities. Try his roast 45-day-old duck served with caviar, prawn crackers and Shandong pancakes, combining the characteristics of both Beijingese and Shandong cooking. The room is bright and airy, but also consider booking a room for more privacy.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
335;De Groene Lantaarn;Netherlands;Staphorst;Gemeenteweg 364, Staphorst, 7951 PG, Netherlands;52.6601173;6.2466765;55;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;A dynamic duo with bags of personality, hostess Cindy Borger and chef Jarno Eggen are making their mark on the Dutch culinary landscape. They have revamped the interior of their stately premises with a unique contemporary decor, incorporating the chef's own skateboards and colourful artwork. The rear terrace, overlooking the vegetable garden and the windmill, is simply idyllic. This is where the chef has the freedom to express his creative vision. The fact that he has the flour for his bread ground in that very mill is a detail that speaks volumes. Indeed, respect for the produce, which is often locally sourced, is at the heart of everything they do here. He has a knack for combining unexpected flavours and exotic seasonings, always striking the perfect balance. For instance, he transforms Wagyu beef into a marbled terrine, giving it a quick crust – the result is incredibly rich and butter-soft. To accompany this, he serves a green pepper sauce, perfectly balanced with the yuzu's citrus notes, which cuts through the richness of the dish – a testament to his expertise. Chef Jarno Eggen invites you on a thrilling culinary adventure, where traditional flavours meet innovative techniques.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
336;Flore;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Nieuwe Doelenstraat 2, Amsterdam, 1012 CP, Netherlands;52.3676602;4.8942749;18;true;true;Contemporary, Creative French;(Temporarily closed. Flore has opened a pop-up at Basecamp Amsterdam, Tom Schreursweg 40, 1067 MC Amsterdam) Flore is entirely focused on providing a mindful fine dining experience. Housed in De L'Europe hotel, this upscale restaurant is lent a unique feel by its modern interior design, which features natural materials. Bas van Kranen's original approach to nature, which characterises his cuisine, emphasises vegetables, local produce and sustainability. Biodynamic growers have become regular suppliers and dairy products have been banished from the kitchen. His search for solutions feeds his creativity, and has resulted in a very pure style of cooking. Game appears on the menu in the autumn and winter, but in spring and summer, the chef turns his attention to the North Sea. The plant-based set menu is a constant, all year round. The small dishes are full of surprises right up to the last bite – a prime example is his signature dish featuring seasonal fruits and vegetables, each prepared differently. The intricate dance of flavours and textures is complemented by a fig peel oil, its gentle sweetness binding everything together. A light, airy hazelnut and Dutch wasabi emulsion adds a moderate kick. Bas van Kranen explores the depths of his ingredients, creating dishes that evoke emotion. He clearly takes pride in working with Dutch produce and now has the confidence to cook just the way he wants to.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
337;De Bokkedoorns;Netherlands;Overveen;Zeeweg 53, Overveen, 2051 EB, Netherlands;52.39688;4.57934;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A veritable culinary institution, De Bokkedoorns was established in 1961 and has held on to its two Michelin stars for the past 30 years. Owner Pascal Beeren, who represents the third generation to run the restaurant, likes to personally give his diners a warm welcome. Modern luxury meets plush comfort in this inviting space, where stunning views of the surrounding natural beauty evoke a sense of serenity. Roy Eijkelkamp is also a stalwart of the restaurant, having worked here under the tutelage of Lucas Rive, who taught him the art of adding intensity and depth to sauces – remember to save some bread so you can mop up every last drop! This chef champions a minimalist cooking style, creating unfussy dishes by preparing the finest ingredients in time-honoured tradition. Think grilled lobster tail with green apple, razor clam mousse, deep-fried soft shell crab and an exquisite fennel broth-based sauce. Innovative flourishes keep his cuisine captivating, exemplified by a dessert featuring pancakes with a subtly sweetened sour cream ice cream, caviar and nut cakes. Complete with an expertly curated wine list, this is an extraordinary dining experience in every detail.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
338;Vinkeles;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Keizersgracht 384, Amsterdam, 1016 GB, Netherlands;52.3692878;4.8839959;18;true;true;Creative, Classic Cuisine;Jurgen van der Zalm has made the kitchen at Vinkeles his own. Having spent years here as a sous-chef, honing his classic culinary skills, he now charts his own course, without breaking with the house style: premium-quality ingredients and rich sauces are still the name of the game. For instance, he braises veal sweetbreads, coats them in miso breadcrumbs, glazes them with an XO sauce made from fermented mushrooms and adds a drizzle of sambai and a lemon foam. A burst of freshness is provided by accoutrements such as sweet-and-sour onion, giving a perfect finishing touch to this minimalist dish. And it would be remiss not to mention the incredibly intense sauce made from Anjou pigeon cooking juices, delicately infused with cocoa and cherries. Chef Van der Zalm is a master saucier who combines a playful approach to international influences, bold innovation and a respect for tradition in his highly personal creations. A unique experience awaits you in what was once the bakery of this 18C Roman Catholic almshouse, whose original wood and stone have been incorporated into a modern interior.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
339;Parkheuvel;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Heuvellaan 21, Rotterdam, 3016 GL, Netherlands;51.903823;4.4715943;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in Het Park and boasting a spectacular view of the Meuse River – best enjoyed from the terrace – this elegant pavilion is the ideal setting in which to indulge in a wonderful fine dining experience. Erik van Loo is a chef with a feel for classic finesse. This comes through, for example, in the lobster cream sauce, full bodied and rich, which takes his well-known combination of bream chicken and langoustine ravioli to the next level. At Parkheuvel, it is the sauces that really blow diners away. His son Juliën's input adds detail and diversity in the preparation of the dishes as he brings his youthful energy to the table. For instance, he combines foie gras with sweet-and-sour pickled beetroot, a Pinot Grigio and dark chocolate jelly, as well as apple and sesame garnishes for added playfulness. The sommelier's astute recommendations and amazing collection are definitely the icing on the cake. Parkheuvel's tradition of excellence in fine dining is being perpetuated with passion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
340;De Nieuwe Winkel;Netherlands;Nijmegen;Gebroeders Van Limburgplein 7, Nijmegen, 6511 BW, Netherlands;51.8473893;5.8595982;27;false;false;Organic, Vegan;Emile van der Staak's vision comes to life in this urban restaurant, where you can see the impressive team at work in the open kitchen. His botanical gastronomy showcases the "age of plants'' at this MICHELIN Green Star restaurant that is taking a stand against climate change. He is a visionary writing a story, with every chapter whetting your appetite. Emile van der Staak's source of inspiration is Food Forest Ketelbroek. This is where he makes discoveries, reflects and creates — and his is a creative spirit that seems to know no bounds. He has developed a precise technique of bringing the microseasons to life in his set menu, which changes three times a year. Take, for example, his dish based on SCOBY, the biofilm that develops on kombucha during the fermentation process. The chef slices the pellicle into thin strips, allowing its umami essence, akin to the taste of shrimp, to shine through. Pickled radish, ginger and a mushroom and onion sauce – spicy, sweet and subtly tangy – add an extra kick. Sichuan pickled pepper and a rich walnut milk elevate the whole dish. Talk about innovation! This is cuisine that takes familiar flavours to the next level. The heavenly "no-chocolate" dessert with roasted Alkmaar groats, and the almond-based "Brie" are mind-blowing. A groundbreaking experience.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
341;De Lindehof;Netherlands;Nuenen;Beekstraat 1, Nuenen, 5671 CS, Netherlands;51.4765594;5.5547065;44;true;false;Creative, Asian Influences;Soenil Bahadoer's success is a testament to the power of hard work and dedication. Coming from an Indo-Surinamese background, the chef has always had to go the extra mile to prove himself. This became motivation for him to impress everyone with his innovative and unique approach to cooking. In this atmospheric restaurant adorned with modern art, he shows what he is made of. Chef Bahadoer gives European dishes a twist by drawing on influences from Suriname, India and Indonesia. His creations are spicy and exceptionally captivating. The flavour profiles are occasionally complex but always balanced, and his seasoning is spot on. He imparts intense, spicy nuances to premium ingredients such as foie gras and pigeon. Think perfectly cooked langoustine glazed with Wagyu fat and dusted with a blend of paprika and tomato. The dish is finished with the crisp textures of green apple and a fiery kick of turmeric – sensational! Soenil Bahadoer had to fight his way to the top, but his ability to create extraordinary dining experiences every day proves he belongs there.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
342;Inter Scaldes;Netherlands;Kruiningen;Zandweg 2, Kruiningen, 4416 NA, Netherlands;51.4571608;4.0241076;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;To say that Sanne and Jeroen Achtien have breathed new life into this institution would be an understatement. The beautiful manor house has undergone an extensive makeover, resulting in a luxurious and trendy space with a lounge feel – the curved seats create a certain intimacy. The light, airy extension looks out onto the magnificent garden. After appetisers in the lounge, diners swing by the kitchen for a glimpse of the impressive team in action and an additional amuse-bouche.Drawing on his Frisian roots and experience gained in Switzerland, the chef showcases the finest produce available in the Zeeland area. His creative cooking grounded in expertise, occasionally complex, and highly exuberant. Perfectly poached fillets of North Sea sole are topped with a delicate potato cylinder filled with Zeeland mussels. The chef combines crunchy vegetables with the salty tang of razor clams, cockles, oyster and herbs. A dashi-infused mousseline adds vibrancy, and a sublime potato purée completes this generous homage to the Zeeland terroir. Tessa van de Wouw, a sommelier with a true passion for wine, adds the finishing flourish with her expert pairings.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
343;Restaurant 212;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Amstel 212, Amsterdam, 1017 AH, Netherlands;52.365853;4.900326;40;false;true;Creative;As soon as you step into this quintessential canal house in the centre of Amsterdam, Richard van Oostenbrugge and Thomas Groot draw you into their world. There is something theatrical about the sight of the chefs working meticulously in their open kitchen. There is an enchanting intimacy and luxurious comfort about Restaurant 212. Nothing is left to chance here, and that goes for the attentive service, too. Fun fact: On the ceiling, you can still see marks from the champagne being uncorked when this place was awarded its first MICHELIN star. With their inventiveness and classical know-how (those sauces!), both chefs put their own stamp on their creations. An ingredient will undergo the most surprising of transformations, and it all seems to happen with such ease – therein lies the chefs' originality. The venison cooked in hay, for instance, is elevated by a perfectly reduced, intensely flavoursome sauce with a glistening sheen. A padrón pepper in tempura and an ingenious association of plum and Meaux mustard provide fine spiciness and extra dimensions. The simplicity of this cuisine is what makes it so ingenious! Nothing is overdone, and nothing is lacking. The real stars of this show are the extraordinary produce and the talent of two friends.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
345;Tribeca;Netherlands;Heeze;Jan Deckersstraat 7, Heeze, 5591 HN, Netherlands;51.3793;5.577939;47;true;true;Creative;The talented Jan Sobecki puts his ambition into practice in chic, elegant Tribeca. The refinement of his cooking, the balance of his dishes and the many wonderful flavours in every mouthful, are impressive. The chef knows how to translate his ideas to the plate, and this makes Tribeca a top restaurant. Chapeau!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
346;De Lindenhof;Netherlands;Giethoorn;Beulakerweg 77, Giethoorn, 8355 AC, Netherlands;52.7465818;6.0797711;46;true;false;Creative, Classic French;De Lindenhof offers a unique experience that starts with the location: a splendid farmhouse with a thatched roof that exudes character and elegance. The English garden is magnificent – the scene could not be more idyllic! Out back is the chef's little sailing boat, in which he likes to cruise the canals (sometimes taking guests with him!). There are also luxurious guestrooms for a relaxing stay. But the main draws are the enthusiastic service provided by hostess Marjan and the ingredient-led cuisine of Martin Kruithof, a traditional chef who has moved with the times. When he incorporates international influences and creative ideas, he never goes overboard and tends to stick to classic flavours. The quality of the produce is impressively showcased, and his dishes are presented in such a way that you can see exactly what you're eating. For example, he cooks top-quality langoustine to a turn and elevates it with a sauce with a hint of caper, then, for a burst of freshness, he adds fragrant vegetables such as broad beans from his own garden and camomile flowers. This is a wonderfully simple take on refined cuisine! What a pleasure it is to be spoiled by Martin Kruithof.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
347;De Treeswijkhoeve;Netherlands;Waalre;Valkenswaardseweg 14, Waalre, 5582 VB, Netherlands;51.3780193;5.4693081;56;false;false;Creative;Dick Middelweerd's cuisine defies categorisation. He is a chef who embraces daring combinations and contrasts. His creativity is boundless, yet always grounded in a deep respect for tradition. Drawing on Asian influences, he seeks out umami notes and extra depth. Kick off your meal with crispy-seared calf sweetbreads with a coffee glaze, accompanied by a rich veal jus infused with Oloroso sherry and finished with an ethereal coffee foam and winter truffle. And why not finish with a miso crème brûlée with toasted rice ice cream and various textures of green apple with sake? It's all possible here. The chef harmonises local and global flavours, which the sommelier masterfully complements with his wine pairings. His exquisite selection of Australian wines is well worth exploring. The decor of this charming farmhouse strikes a perfect balance between contemporary elegance and rustic character. The front-of-house team is led by hostess Anne-Laura, whose effortless charm and sophistication make this dining experience all the more delightful.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
348;'t Nonnetje;Netherlands;Harderwijk;Vischmarkt 38, Harderwijk, 3841 BG, Netherlands;52.3509952;5.6202128;26;false;true;Creative, Modern French;Having been given free rein to do his own thing by owner Robert-Jan Nijland, chef Michel van der Kroft has come up with a unique culinary style that puts great emphasis on vegetables and incorporates Portuguese influences. He can carry off the classic Escoffier recipes just as well as any chef. Think perfectly cooked tournedos Rossini, or a sublime foie gras and smoked eel terrine with aged balsamic and textures of beetroot. He also delights diners with his creative vegetarian dishes and his ravioli with Queijo da Serra da Estrela sheep's cheese – a house specialty. With a generous and refined touch, Chef Van der Kroft puts a unique and generous spin on familiar flavours. When it's time for coffee, for instance, the chef delivers a warm pastel de nata and comes to the table with a pot of chocolate mousse and a wooden spoon. It's a heartwarming gesture that works so well in this inviting setting. 't Nonnetje combines intimacy, sleek design and exclusivity. This converted fisherman's cottage redefines cosy fine dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
349;Fred;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Boompjes 41, Rotterdam, 3011 XC, Netherlands;51.9162456;4.4894221;41;false;true;Creative French;Everything revolves around luxury and opulence at this restaurant. On the way to your table, for example, you step past the cheese store (the cheese trolley is excellent!), champagne is presented on a special cart. The vibrant decor is complemented by finishings made of the finest materials, as innovative design meets modern elegance. Chef Mustert's cuisine is equally tasteful. For example, he elevates langoustines of exceptional quality in a combination with various types of melon, subtle hints of celery and both a foamy butter sauce and curry oil. The results are pared down, intense and incredibly rich! Fred Mustert's creations are exciting and everything is precisely balanced. You will want to mop up every last drop of the sauces with your bread. With a sure hand, he gives classic flavour combinations an original twist. Chef Mustert delivers culinary perfection, curated in a very appealing menu. Less really is more with Fred!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
350;Ciel Bleu;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Ferdinand Bolstraat 333, Amsterdam, 1072 LH, Netherlands;52.3486359;4.8928264;58;false;true;Creative;Ciel Bleu immediately lives up to its name. Here, you dine on the top floor of the luxurious Okura Hotel with a spectacular view of the blue sky and the Amsterdam skyline as a backdrop. The modern elegance of the restaurant and the superlative presentation of the dishes are equally pleasing to the eye.Arjan Speelman's cuisine is technically accomplished, creative and laced with international influences and seasonings. This chef effortlessly combines a classic beurre blanc with exotic spices and ingredients from around the globe. Every detail is precise, every bite a surprise. A nice touch: with each course, a herb in its original form is brought to the table – this herb will be featured in the next dish.Dining at Ciel Bleu is intriguing. You will be served by one of the best front-of-house teams in the country, starring sommelier Noël Vanwittenbergh and maître d' Francesco Simonelli. The sky really is the limit here!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
351;Aan de Poel;Netherlands;Amstelveen;Handweg 1, Amstelveen, 1185 TS, Netherlands;52.2997964;4.8447563;18;true;false;Creative, Modern French;The view of De Poel Lake is simply breathtaking. The large windows and elegant interior design allow you to fully immerse yourself in the charm of this location. Stefan van Sprang's culinary creations are a perfect match for this gorgeous setting. The chef likes to add the finishing touches to his dishes tableside and present the day's lunchtime set menu – which makes for a more personal dining experience. (In the evening, there are à la carte options and a set menu.) This skilled craftsman deftly combines diverse influences and uses his creativity to put his own spin on classic recipes. To add aromatic nuances, he avails himself of the herb garden right behind the restaurant. For example, he showcases the intense flavours of Dutch lamb saddle and neck with a playful combination of tender and crispy textures, adding zest with a chimichurri and depth with a lamb jus. To provide further complexity, he incorporates a Mediterranean ratatouille and salty oyster leaf. The captivating blend of familiar flavours and original garnishes elevates the produce to new heights. This is a treat for both the palate and the eye, complemented by an exclusive wine list that the sommeliers will be happy to help you explore.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
353;FG - François Geurds;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Katshoek 37B, Rotterdam, 3032 AE, Netherlands;51.9265521;4.4795369;27;true;false;Creative;Striving for nothing less than perfection, François Geurds has created a trendy urban restaurant that is immediately captivating. With luxurious porcelain custom-made for specific dishes, and an impressive collection of knives and trolleys… At FG, they do not shy away from the spectacular. The private dining room even features an upside-down garden! Chef Geurds loves working with premium ingredients such as Wagyu A5 and lobster, but sometimes he also lets celeriac take centre stage. His dishes are thought-provoking and characterised by meticulous attention to detail and original ideas. His sauces are wonderfully complex. For example, he boldly combines fermented banana with seared avocado, salty caviar and a fantastic beurre blanc made with caviar's own fat. This is a technically adept chef who likes to test boundaries, always maintaining a sense of balance. His innovations are compelling. Cap off your meal with a rich coffee from the barista, and treat yourself to something from the impressive dessert trolley. At FG, nothing is left to chance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
354;Sushi Masaki Saito;Canada;Toronto;88 Avenue Rd., Toronto, M5R 2H2, Canada;43.6723401;-79.3958233;18;true;true;Japanese;Even if you lived next door, omakase with Chef Masaki Saito would still feel like a faraway adventure. The foyer's marble staircase, a 200-year-old hinoki counter and traditional Japanese paneling and woodwork set the stage as he slices, scores and sauces the greatest treasures of the sea. Only here will you find shirako boldly skewered and grilled over binchotan, and only here will you eat melting slabs of chutoro buried under a blizzard of white truffles. Fish comes exclusively from Japan, and for the nigiri, assistants are quick to bring him his prized rice from Niigata prefecture, warm and tinged with his special blend of vinegars, after every round. Laughter fills the air, thanks to Saito and his jovial team, and for a few blissful hours, the world outside melts away.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
355;Xin Rong Ji;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 501, 5F, Chinese Financial Center, 33 Jiaozi Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5833001;104.060602;58;false;false;Taizhou;On the eve of the upmarket restaurant chain's 30th anniversary, it opened its first Chengdu outpost in 2023. The large space is furnished in a lavish but understated manner, and has lovely views of the Twin Towers. You can find the brand's signature luxury seafood on the menu, but it's the Taizhou recipes jazzed with by local touches that truly shine. Try the sea anemone glass noodles with pickled chillies, or mapo tofu with cod milt.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
356;Yu Zhi Lan;China Mainland;Chengdu;24-1 Changfa Street, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.669182;104.055887;51;true;false;Sichuan;This low-key dining concept doesn’t need a sign. The owner-chef Lan Guijun is a local legend who took Sichuanese to the level of haute cuisine so gourmands will always find their way here. The rooms exude rustic charm, dotted by ceramic art and pottery made by the chef himself. Before you can taste his elegant, elaborate multi-course meal that brings out the ingredients’ natural flavours, you need to book a table with a deposit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
357;Molino de Urdániz;Taiwan;Taipei;GF, Hotel MVSA, 61, Section 1, Jianguo North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 10491, Taiwan;25.0507432;121.5372068;79;true;true;Spanish Contemporary;Spanish-themed paintings hang in the dining area, which boasts a stunning glazed wine cellar. The two chefs take diners on a poetic culinary journey to the Pyrenees of the Basque Country with a seafood-heavy tasting menu. Produce from Taiwan and Japan is woven into edible works of art that embody Spanish traditions, Asian influences and natural beauty. The clever use of colours and seasonal ingredients makes the experience a real delight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
358;RAW;Taiwan;Taipei;301, Lequn 3rd Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.0827948;121.5594375;34;false;false;Innovative;André Chiang’s dining concept in his hometown features a futuristic interior with gigantic organic wood forms that contrast with the faux industrial setting. Inspired by the chef’s journey around the world, the 10-course menu changes with the seasons, reinventing Taiwanese cuisine with sleek plating and a stimulating blend of flavours, textures and temperatures. It’s notoriously hard to get a table so stay tuned for when the online system opens for booking and act fast.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
359;logy;Taiwan;Taipei;6, Lane 109, Section 1, Anhe Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0356024;121.5532054;55;false;false;Asian Contemporary;logy, a sibling of the Florilège in Tokyo, is helmed by a Japanese chef hailing from Hokkaido. Using local produce and the freshest catch from his home prefecture, he melds Japanese and European techniques to create contemporary recipes, underscored by strong Asian influences. The omakase menu changes every two months, but a variation of the Japanese-Taiwanese fusion chawanmushi is a firm fixture. Plan far in advance and book online.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
360;Mudan;Taiwan;Taipei;17, Lane 52, Siwei Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.035223;121.54723;96;false;false;Tempura;When it comes to tempura, precision is the name of the game. With decades of experience in Japanese cooking, the head chef brings out the best in every ingredient with his keen sense for oil blend, oil temperature and batter consistency, sealing in the umami with an incredibly thin, crisp and light batter. The simple, cosy room is decorated with Japanese garden details. Reservations are mandatory, with only two sittings, at 12.30pm and 6.30pm.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
362;Sons & Daughters;USA;San Francisco;708 Bush St., San Francisco, 94108, USA;37.7902661;-122.4091443;41;false;false;Contemporary;Offering an abundance of poise, polish, and charm, this cozy Nob Hill jewel box remains quietly impressive. A cleanly minimalist new Nordic style is clearer than ever in an elegant tasting menu that deftly weaves together a variety of preserved fruits and vegetables, flawless seafood, and aged meats. Meals are off to an impressive start with the likes of a refreshing cured California trout dressed with a chilled fish bone broth drizzled with herbed oil. Rutabaga is transformed into thin, flat strands mimicking pasta and comes dressed with a creamy-textured smoked pork fat sauce. The applewood roasted quail features crisped-skin breast plated with a luscious jus and bouquet of Napa Valley greens, while the leg and thigh are glazed with fermented blueberry.;Air conditioning;[]
365;Vespertine;USA;Culver City;3599 Hayden Ave., Culver City, 90232, USA;34.024204;-118.38166;90;false;false;Contemporary;Chef Jordan Kahn's singular operation is tucked inside a strikingly futuristic edifice of red steel ("the Waffle"), a fitting spot for this highly creative restaurant where diners enjoy a tasting menu that is equally out of the ordinary. Each dish is visually stunning, with cuisine that is not only daringly inventive (at times downright whimsical), but also marshals finely honed technique and impeccably balanced flavors, as in an artful dish of scallop with passionfruit, ají amarillo, and petals of horseradish tuile, or an "obsidian mirror" of smoked mussel cream with salted plum. The meal ends as strong as it begins, with a mesmerizing dessert that features kaleidoscopic flavors.Together with their sister restaurants, Vespertine works to ensure all ingredients are used in their entirety.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
366;Providence;USA;Hollywood;5955 Melrose Ave., Hollywood, 90038, USA;34.083576;-118.3301829;15;false;false;Seafood;Purity and precision are the underpinnings of Chef Michael Cimarusti's California cooking, inspired by flavors from Asia and the Mediterranean. The tasting menu blends classic technique with a modern sensibility, and sources the freshest and most sustainable seafood, often wild-caught from American waters. At no point during the meal will you doubt its impeccable quality, especially while savoring dishes such as seared Alaskan halibut with green beans and geoduck in a bouillabaisse sauce, or the hiramasa sashimi, plated in the shape of a flower, and treated to a tableside pour of basil-infused fumet sauce. The soft-poached egg topped with Santa Barbara uni, breadcrumbs, and Champagne sauce is a Providence signature.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
367;Aubergine;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;Monte Verde at 7th Ave., Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93921, USA;36.55406;-121.924355;32;false;true;Contemporary, Californian;Easygoing luxury and refinement strike a harmonious note within L’Auberge Carmel, where every element seems designed to delight. Chef Justin Cogley balances classic technique with a sleek, modern aesthetic, and his cooking captures a sense of place that feels wholly his own. Products of spectacular quality are prepared skillfully and painstakingly presented with an artistic eye, as in a surprising "cabbage" taco filled with shallot jam, Madeira-braised treviso, Kaluga queen caviar and cabbage chips. The hits keep coming, like the rice roulade with Dungeness crab finished in a white dashi and butter sauce or the triple-seared dry-aged ribeye brushed in wagyu XO. Fabulously accommodating sommeliers are ever present to help navigate a wine list of real distinction.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
369;Acquerello;USA;San Francisco;1722 Sacramento St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.79167;-122.42131;35;false;false;Italian, Contemporary;With its signature A-frame ceiling and luxuriously warm furnishings, this dining room has been Chef Suzette Gresham’s home since 1989. The cooking remains top rate, promising finesse and bold flavors in equal measure. Handmade pastas combine classic technique with a touch of personal style, and mimicking the art on the walls, some dishes like carrot and ginger terrine or the must-order cheese plate arrive as visual masterpieces. Sweets are a notable strength, down to the very last few bites when one of the best mignardises carts in town rolls up stacked with chocolates, pâtes de fruits, and caramels rolls. Speaking of bests, friendly sommeliers are essential guides for navigating one of the deepest Italian wine and Champagne cellars in the country.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
372;Californios;USA;San Francisco;355 11th St., San Francisco, 94103, USA;37.7712406;-122.4131414;67;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Chef Val M. Cantú's Californios is a divine dining temple where a passionate focus on heritage is applied with masterful technique. The attractive space, with its dark walls, colorful artwork, and lively playlist, keeps things more festive than hallowed, and the patio area is especially pleasant. The foundational elements of Mexican cuisine are elevated here through the team's ingenuity and the utilization of the finest products. Familiar dishes are turned complex and deliciously unique. Lime cured cold-smoked hamachi is presented with a sweet lime aguachile with pickled buddha's hand and cold pressed cilantro, then beer- and mezcal-battered black cod in a sour cherry tamarind salsa makes a nice addition to a tortilla.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
374;Harbor House;USA;Elk;5600 CA-1, Elk, 95432, USA;39.1355655;-123.7190639;62;true;true;Californian, Creative;Veering off into the wilds of Mendocino County is certainly a most delightful detour—one that culminates in the dining room of the Harbor House Inn.Driven by impeccable technique and devotion to sustainability, the cooking is highly original. Chef Matthew Kammerer is devout when it comes to hyper-local and foraged ingredients, elevating not only delicacies like sea urchin, but also more humble items like seaweed harvested from the nearby coastline, or lace lichen plucked from overhanging trees. Compelling, Japanese-accented creations have included a sake-poached abalone paired with a luscious sauce made from its liver. Fantastic sourdough is flecked with sea lettuce, and kombu flavors a silky ice cream with coffee, lavender and honey—an ingenious union of sweet and savory tastes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
375;Trèsind Studio;;Dubai;St. Regis Gardens, The Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.114932;55.1391176;18;true;false;Indian;The surprise multi-course tasting menu is a masterpiece of originality, intrigue and precision, featuring flavours and tastes from all four compass points of India. While the chefs work away with quiet diligence and focus in the open kitchen, the service team provide detailed explanations of each elegant creation. A little theatre here and there with certain courses adds to an unforgettable experience. There’s something magical happening here – and with just 20 seats and a rooftop location – you’ll feel you’re in on the secret.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
376;STAY by Yannick Alléno;;Dubai;One&Only The Palm Hotel, West Crescent Road, The Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.0992961;55.1326916;15;false;false;French;This elegant, high-ceilinged restaurant is exclusively set at the end of the Palm in a colonial-style property, which is breathtakingly opulent in design, with magical tropical gardens and a private dock. Inside, it’s luxurious without being stuffy, and service follows suit, with a team that are attentive and professional yet relaxed and personable. The cuisine is innovative, creative and intriguing, combining French tradition with modern culinary advances to create à la carte dishes and exclusive menus. The combination of flavours is harmonious, and dishes are cohesive, creating an unforgettable experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
378;Row on 45;;Dubai;45th Floor, Tower 2, Grosvenor House Hotel, Al Emreef Street, Dubai Marina, Dubai;25.0861613;55.1435576;41;false;false;Creative;This gastronomic venture comes from acclaimed British chef, Jason Atherton. Its name combines the acronym for its “refinement of work” and its location on the 45th floor of The Grosvenor House. A penthouse-like setting with an open kitchen, this intimate culinary experience seats 22 guests and offers a 17-course tasting menu divided into three acts. The dishes feature fine Japanese ingredients prepared with French techniques, such as Hokkaido scallop and Saroma Wagyu A5. The full menu is sophisticated, refined and immaculately presented, delivering well-judged and complex flavours. If you’re going to opt for the four-seater chef’s table, be sure to book well in advance.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
379;Agli Amici Rovinj;Croatia;Rovinj;Šetalište Vijeća Europe 1-2, Rovinj, 52210, Croatia;45.0747789;13.6360524;78;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant occupies a beautiful building on the elegant seafront promenade of Rovinj’s modern marina and is a delightful place to eat thanks to its large terrace and stunning views of the azure sea and its verdant islands. At nightfall, the church of St Euphemia adds even more charm to the setting. Simone De Lucca is at the helm in the kitchen here, overseen by Emanuele Scarello from the Michelin-two-star Agli Amici in Udine. There are two tasting menus: Rovinj and Istria (the first dedicated to fish and seafood, the second to meat dishes), from which individual courses can be chosen à la carte style. One of the most interesting dishes is the grilled cuttlefish with sautéed risotto, which is garnished with a vegetable sauce and decorated with a mosaic of flowers from the Istrian coast and is perfectly balanced in flavour and colourful presentation. Award-winning sommelier Kristijan Harjač is on hand front of house with an excellent selection of Croatian wines (including by the glass), such as fragrant Istrian Malvasia, Dalmatian reds and sparkling wines from the Plešivica region.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
380;Meta;;Singapore;9 Mohamed Sultan Road, 238959, Singapore;1.2789446;103.8414145;26;false;false;Innovative;Chef Sun Kim hails from Korea's Busan, and his refined modern cooking combines Korean traditions and bold flavours with contemporary minimalist aesthetics. The dining room shares the same space as the kitchen, for a chef's table feel. The steamed Jeju abalone with gochujang seaweed risotto is a hit, with its contrasting textures – the tender mollusc, creamy rice and crunchy lily bulbs. The seafood-heavy single set menu will also appeal to meat lovers.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
381;Jaan by Kirk Westaway;;Singapore;Swissôtel The Stamford, Equinox Complex, Level 70, 2 Stamford Road, 178882, Singapore;1.293387;103.85314;61;true;true;British Contemporary;Embodying the quintessence of fine dining, this romantic restaurant has it all – food, service, ambiance and spectacular views. Chef Westaway makes good use of top-notch British produce and inspirations, such as scallops from Scotland and turbot from Cornwall, to turn out modern culinary creations that never fail to impress. Some British classics also got a makeover – “hen’s egg” is a refined take on the breakfast favourite dippy eggs with soldiers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
382;Saint Pierre;;Singapore;One Fullerton, #02-02B, 1 Fullerton Road, 049213, Singapore;1.2862377;103.854219;76;false;false;French Contemporary;The unobstructed views of the Marina Bay, smart décor and discreet service don’t outshine Chef Emmanuel’s modern French cuisine, underpinned by solid skills and characterised by Asian overtones. His unique ability to accentuate the natural flavours of premium produce is what keeps diners returning. The seafood heavy tasting menu showcases the breadth and depth of his repertoire. It’s closed on some public holidays, so call ahead to check.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
384;Cloudstreet;;Singapore;84 Amoy Street, 069903, Singapore;1.280977;103.8470099;35;true;false;Innovative;The enchanting Cloudstreet is named after the Tim Winton book, which is fitting as Australia is where Sri Lankan chef Rishi Naleendra learnt his trade and developed his considerable skills. Diners at his restaurant are taken on a thrilling culinary journey, courtesy of his impressive creativity and artistry. He has also gathered together a service team who clearly share his pride and passion. When it comes to dessert, diners move to a room upstairs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
386;Bottiglieria 1881;Poland;Krakow;ul. Bocheńska 5, Krakow, 31 061, Poland;50.0486603;19.9460552;69;true;false;Creative;Sophistication, depth and a wonderful purity of flavour can all be found in the cooking at this marble-floored restaurant. Choose from two tasting menus, the ‘Introduction’ or the ‘Full Experience’, both of which feature creative, well-balanced dishes. The best of the Polish larder is used throughout, while each finely crafted course is finished with an artistic flourish. Sit in the century old cellar for an intimate dining experience, or ask for a table opposite the open kitchen to see the talented team at work as they produce such stunning cooking.;Interesting wine list;[]
387;Milka;Slovenia;Kranjska Gora;Vršiška cesta 45, Kranjska Gora, 4280, Slovenia;46.4755987;13.7845892;98;false;true;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Situated near the Austrian and Italian borders, Milka boasts a superb location overlooking a crystal-clear lake surrounded by mountains. The restaurant offers a fine gastronomic synthesis of its region, skilfully interpreted and prepared by chef David Žefran, who makes full use of local ingredients. The surprise menu flows naturally and features ingredients that follow the seasons. The chefs themselves bring their dishes to the dining room, providing detailed and enthusiastic descriptions of each course. Although dishes are prepared with a modern touch, the character of the region shines through, especially in the choice of ingredients. Dishes include delicious salmon from the Danube accompanied by black radish and elderflower, a glazed brioche with fermented butter, and venison served with the perfect accompaniment of a dark beer sauce – every detail is carefully thought out. The wine list will delight connoisseurs: many of the wineries featured have a close relationship with the restaurant. Stylish guestrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
388;Taian Table;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, LN Garden Hotel, 368 Huanshi East Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.138026;113.280695;18;false;false;European Contemporary;If creative, refined dining with a modern twist is your thing, you should feel right at home in Taian Table. This kitchen team turns the best ingredients from around the world into sophisticated works of art in the display kitchen with their well-honed European techniques. There is only one 8-course degustation menu that changes bimonthly, but diners also have the option of ordering other seasonal and signature offerings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
390;Imperial Treasure Fine Chinese Cuisine;China Mainland;Guangzhou;L514B, 5F, IGC Mall, 222 Xingmin Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.118473;113.326514;58;false;true;Cantonese;As in other branches of this Singapore-based chain, the kitchen team never fails to deliver quality dishes thanks to inspired insights and honed skills. The must-try black pepper mud crab exudes an intoxicating aroma and seafood flavour, while double-boiled fish maw soup with shark bones warms the heart and soul. Their dim sum lunch is to die for – deftly crafted translucent rice noodle rolls and tofu skin rolls stuffed with shrimps and chives.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
393;AIRA;Sweden;Stockholm;Biskopsvägen 9, Stockholm, 115 21, Sweden;59.3207155;18.1237288;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Swedish;This strikingly designed restaurant sits near the beautiful Royal Djurgården. Its stage is the open kitchen, with the chefs often adding their finishing touches tableside. Beautifully composed dishes use top quality Nordic ingredients and deliver well-judged flavours and textures, featuring the likes of halibut with fermented melon, sesame and jalapeno. Service is top-notch and it’s worth opting for either a wine pairing or the creative non-alcoholic option featuring ingredients from their garden. Be sure arrive early for a drink on the waterside terrace too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
394;Kong Hans Kælder;Denmark;Copenhagen;Vingaardsstræde 6, Copenhagen, 1070, Denmark;55.6787423;12.5839958;91;false;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;This elegant restaurant is set in an intimate, historic and wonderfully atmospheric cellar, where a charming team attend to your every need. Cooking is rooted in French gastronomy, with its luxury ingredients and rich flavours, but the chef also stamps his own mark on the accomplished, imaginative dishes, with some subtle modernisation and lighter touches.;Interesting wine list;[]
395;Vollmers;Sweden;Malmo;Tegelgårdsgatan 5, Malmo, 211 33, Sweden;55.6046461;12.9966201;83;true;true;Contemporary;The young team provide cheerful service at this intimate restaurant on a cobbled street in the Old Town. The surprise menu comes with numerous extra courses, including some inspired by the owners’ childhood memories, and texture and acidity are used to good effect in the creative, sophisticated dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
397;Palace;Finland;Helsinki;Eteläranta 10, Helsinki, 00130, Finland;60.1653036;24.9523857;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Take in magical views over the harbour from the 10th floor of this modernist building, constructed in 1952 for the Olympic Games. Beautifully delicate modern dishes feature on a multi-course tasting menu packed with well-balanced flavours. These are presented both by the chefs and the top-notch serving team.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
398;Henne Kirkeby Kro;Denmark;Henne;Strandvejen 234, Henne, 6854, Denmark;55.7270112;8.2423144;54;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This traditional-looking 18C thatched inn has a contrastingly modern interior and comes complete with a bespoke chef's table as well as some sumptuously stylish bedrooms. A well-chosen wine list accompanies original, well-balanced and technically accomplished dishes. Lunch sees a lighter menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
399;Koan;Denmark;Copenhagen;Langeliniekaj 5, Copenhagen, 2100, Denmark;55.6954973;12.6001611;29;false;true;Creative;This elegant restaurant provides a hugely engaging experience from start to finish, with its technically accomplished and completely original cooking. The heritage of Korean-born chef-owner Kristian Baumann influences the flavours and techniques across the 17 course tasting menu. He leads the team in an open kitchen, delivering creative, refined dishes built around superb ingredients. Service is professional yet relaxed, and the whole event is perfectly choreographed.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
400;Aloë;Sweden;Stockholm;Svartlösavägen 52, Stockholm, 125 33, Sweden;59.2843177;17.9857179;92;true;true;Creative;Your evening starts with snacks in the lounge of this welcoming suburban restaurant, before you take a seat at either a table or the counter to enjoy the procession of memorable dishes. The surprise menu features the finest European ingredients cooked with global influences, showcasing intense flavours and some original combinations. Finish the evening with tea or coffee and an impressive array of mignardises that are a real event. The engaging and attentive service is pitched just right.This restaurant will be temporarily closed from the 9th February.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
401;Alchemist;Denmark;Copenhagen;Refshalevej 173C, Copenhagen, 1432 K, Denmark;55.6940951;12.6137461;30;true;true;Innovative;An immersive and perfectly choreographed experience, eating here is a highly theatrical affair at the pinnacle of destination dining. Dinner is divided into acts and set across several locations, including a balcony, a play area and a spectacular planetarium-like dome with images projected onto the ceiling. Dishes are technically complex and highly creative with dramatic contrasts. Chef-owner Rasmus Munk believes food is a great way to communicate with people, so accompanies his cooking with statements and ideas about the world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
402;a|o|c;Denmark;Copenhagen;Dronningens Tværgade 2, Copenhagen, 1302 K, Denmark;55.6831927;12.5889875;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This spacious, bright and simply decorated restaurant is set within the vaulted basement of a delightful 17C building close to Nyhavn harbour and is filled with huge, well-spaced tables. The set tasting menu uses ingredients of exceptional quality in confidently cooked, harmonious dishes which showcase finesse, depth and sublime, clearly defined flavours. It comes as little surprise that the wine list is excellent too.;Interesting wine list;[]
405;Oro;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida General San Martin 889, Rio de Janeiro, 22441-015, Brazil;-22.98601;-43.22471;41;false;false;Creative;One of those restaurants that every food-lover should get to know! The rapport formed between chef Felipe Bronze and sommelier Cecilia Aldaz works wonderfully well, with large doses of friendliness, in this charming and elegant restaurant one block from Leblon beach, where the cuisine is a fusion of Brazilian roots and cutting-edge technique. This is reflected in the Afetividade and Criatividade menus (with two and four main courses, respectively) which pay homage to the different regions of Brazil. The kitchen is situated upstairs, hence the almost constant and careful movement of trays up and down the stairs. What impressed us first and foremost was the creativity of the starters, including the superb oysters with jabuticaba, and the selection of appetisers to eat with your hands, some of which are crunchy, some Brazilian, and others inspired by Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
406;D.O.M.;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Barão de Capanema 549, São Paulo, 01411-011, Brazil;-23.5661451;-46.667572;99;true;true;Creative;For a unique dining experience, Alex Atala, Brazil’s most internationally renowned chef, demonstrates that, despite being involved in various projects, he always has something new to share. The tasting menu (there’s also a vegetarian option) is a journey across the flavours of the Amazon region, exploring river communities and almost-unknown ingredients (priprioca root, palmetto heart of palm, ants, açai, jambu, tucupi etc) sourced from small-scale local producers, as well as offering surprising textures and flavours that will delight the tastebuds – all of which are creatively prepared and based, occasionally, around European-inspired combinations. In this modern, elegant restaurant decorated with indigenous decorative objects, try dishes such as ant with pineapple and tucupi hollandaise, and “pirarucu with moqueca” (a traditional Amazonian fish soup). A place to open up your mind, so prepare yourself for surprises galore!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
407;Evvai;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Joaquim Antunes 108, São Paulo, 05415-000, Brazil;-23.5670869;-46.6790725;30;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Brazilian;It is not always a given to find a restaurant that is fully able to express a chef’s desire and passion for food, life, art and nature, but this is definitely the case at Evvai, where Luiz Filipe Souza has created a unique space where his true essence shines through both in the ambience and his cuisine. His innovative cooking, a fusion of Brazilian and Italian influences, results in dishes that are not only visually attractive, but teeming with skill, knowledge and balance. This is showcased on a single tasting menu, Oriundi (symbolising the interchange between cultures), featuring delicate appetisers that fly the flag of both Brazil and Italy. These are followed by the scallops sautéed in duck fat - an impressive, and surprisingly prepared dish that has been on the menu at Evvai since it first opened. Another recipe that stands out here is the highly complex Melipona honey dessert, prepared using a variety of different techniques.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
408;Tuju;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Frei Galvão, 135, São Paulo, 01454-060, Brazil;-23.5805339;-46.6855567;56;true;true;Creative;If a great dining experience appeals to you, the new Tuju has opened its doors in this elegant three-storey building that lives and breathes food just a few metres from the Museu da Casa Brasileira (MCB), in a quiet street in the Jardim Paulistano district. The experience begins at the entrance on the ground floor, which is also home to both the wine cellar and an internal garden. The restaurant itself is on the second floor with a large open kitchen surrounded by tables, while the third floor is the setting for a large bar with a view. Chef Ivan Ralston, well supported by a great team of cooks, is fully committed to gastronomy in a profound way, using his knowledge to combine seasonal Brazilian products and flavours (especially from São Paulo) with the most contemporary European techniques, and always with a focus on creativity and research. The weather conditions of each individual season determine the composition of his tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
409;Oteque;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Conde de Irajá 581, Rio de Janeiro, 22271-020, Brazil;-22.95747;-43.194424;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A temple of gastronomy in the city. Once you’ve passed over the threshold of the discreet façade you can leave the hustle and bustle of daily life behind you in this high-ceilinged restaurant where old and highly contemporary exist alongside each other. The main dining room has an industrial feel about it with its bare, open-brick walls and six large round tables plus a dining counter at one end in front of the open kitchen. Famous chef Alberto Landgraf, who is nowadays involved in several international projects, offers a single surprise tasting menu that varies according to the seasons with some dishes substituted daily in line with the availability of the best and freshest ingredients. His trademarks are simplicity and naturalness, qualities that are visible in his championing of Brazilian breeds and the transparency of every single flavour. A good example of this is the spectacular bluefin tuna with fish mayonnaise and Ossetra caviar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
410;Lasai;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Largo dos Leões 35, Humaitá, Rio de Janeiro, 22260-210, Brazil;-22.9532398;-43.1964089;82;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Innovative;Dining at this restaurant with just 10 seats is like attending a show, but with the best seats in the house! Although it starts out quietly, the kitchen comes to life as the chefs embark on the task in hand, with interesting interaction between chef Rafa Costa e Silva and his guests. The surprise tasting menu, modern in style, begins with a variety of appetisers, and includes outstanding vegetarian dishes (cooked to perfection and based around seasonal organic ingredients from his gardens in Itanhangá and Vale das Videiras), with the option of superb wine pairings. “Lasai” translates as “tranquil” in Basque – the restaurant takes its name from the time the chef spent refining his skills in the award-winning Mugaritz (in Errentería, in Spain’s Basque country). You’ll need to book ahead and be punctual, as the experience starts at the same time for every guest.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
411;Pujol;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Tennyson 133, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11550, Mexico;19.4324232;-99.1947841;26;true;true;Mexican, Modern Cuisine;Chef-owner Enrique Olvera’s seminal dining room has long stood as one of the country’s most famous addresses. This breezy, contemporary space is a constant hive of activity, thanks to servers dressed in sharp, black suits and a crowd eager to dine here. Some come for the taco omakase, but the culinary heart of this restaurant lies in the seasonal tasting menu. Tradition and invention go hand-in-hand in the likes of scallop ceviche with egg salad or grilled Baja coast rockfish with butternut squash puree and sherry foam. The savory progression culminates with mole madre, an effort like no other that celebrates Mexican history and cuisine in the most profound way. The wine list features an impressive number of regional vintners, some of whom bottle exclusively for the restaurant.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
415;NARA NIKON;Japan;Nara;3 Nabeyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8264, Japan;34.686899;135.829383;99;false;false;Japanese;Shojiro Shimizu is dedicated to showcasing Japanese cuisine to the world. Centuries-old cooking techniques are on full display here, including grilling over a charcoal brazier and cooking rice in a kamado (traditional stove). Appetisers are indispensable here, as they express a sense of season. The restaurant’s name refers to a Zen chant intoned by the Zen master Dogen Zenji (1200–1253). Shimizu’s serious attitude to cooking is encapsulated in the Zen proverb, ‘Do what must be done in this moment in what you must achieve in this moment’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
418;Koryu;Japan;Osaka;3-3-3 Uchiawajimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0038, Japan;34.686929;135.510132;63;true;true;Japanese;A willow tree bending to describe an arc is the symbol of the restaurant and the meaning of its name. In this modern sukiya-type interior, the arc bends toward a wickerwork ceiling. Koryu’s location on the river’s edge reminds you that Osaka is known as the ‘City of Water’. The aim of the house is to be true to its Naniwa (Osaka) roots. The sumptuously arranged “Naniwa” sashimi platter is a remarkable sight. Traditional vegetables also befit the Osaka cuisine. Like the willow tree, Koryu applies a supple creative spirit to a solid foundation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
419;Tenjimbashi Aoki;Japan;Osaka;7-12-14 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0041, Japan;34.71394;135.511084;37;false;true;Japanese;Scrupulous attention is paid to the ceremonial space, cuisine, serving vessels and sense of the seasons. The chef learned his guiding principles at a restaurant in Hozenji Alley. Entrusted with preparing the appetiser platters, he became schooled in the knowledge and aesthetics of Japanese cuisine. Aiming for artistic beauty in all aspects, he grows his own flowers to decorate the sukiya interior and collects seasonal serving vessels to delight guests. Technique, experience and sensibility all merge to create assortments of dishes that celebrate the seasons and their festivals.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
420;Gion Maruyama;Japan;Kyoto;570-171 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002587;135.776068;55;false;true;Japanese;Flowers are arranged, the ceremonial space is well appointed, serving vessels are carefully chosen. The tea ceremony spirit pervades Gion Maruyama’s graceful service. The Gion location is a ryotei but, in a modern touch, it also features counter seating. The chef has spent many years seeking out delicious flavours. He spells ‘oishii’ (good-tasting) the old-fashioned way, with the characters that mean ‘beautiful’ and ‘taste’, recalling the sensibilities of an older time. ‘Flavour, not seasoning’ is the chef’s credo. Devotion to Kyoto cuisine that reverberates in all senses.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
422;Sojiki Nakahigashi;Japan;Kyoto;32-3 Jodoji Ishibashicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8406, Japan;35.027601;135.792708;87;true;true;Japanese;Picking wild grasses and flowers, the chef harvests vegetables from the field. His ‘herbivorous cuisine’, conceived in respect and gratitude for food, uses everything and wastes nothing. Appetizer platters, served by his own hand, tell tales about the current season. The main dish is rice cooked in an old-style okudo stove and roasted dried sardines.Written by brush on the wooden tag at the entrance is the instruction is ‘Garnish rice cooked in the okudo stove with char-grilled snacks and wild grasses and flowers’. The chef’s intention when he opened his restaurant pervades his menu today.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
423;La Cime;Japan;Osaka;3-2-15 Kawaramachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0048, Japan;34.685818;135.503519;70;true;true;French, Contemporary;Yusuke Takada unravels the mysteries of the classics while pursuing the modern. Takada is the author of a new French cuisine, one imbued with the essence of Japan. Takada’s aim in using traditional ingredients such as kudzu vine, tofu skin, miso and wasabi is to proclaim the goodness of foodstuffs grown and raised in Japan. Cultural elements from Osaka and his native Amami Ōshima weave together into a story that is unique and fascinating.;Air conditioning;[]
425;Ryō-shō;Japan;Kyoto;570-166 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.00237;135.775871;77;false;false;Japanese;Mixing tradition with his own experiences and ideas, the chef gives run to his imagination. Emulating tea ceremony procedure, he starts you off with a steamed dish of mochi rice and seasonal fish. Borrowing from French techniques, the secret ingredient of the white-vinegar dressing is cheese, while sauce for meat dishes is prepared from grilled meat juices. Serving vessels run the gamut from antique to modern Japanese and Western pieces. The chef draws on a wealth of experience to create a unique interpretation of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
426;Wagokoro Izumi;Japan;Kyoto;634-3 Nioitenjincho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8414, Japan;35.000922;135.76047;29;false;false;Japanese;The name ‘Wagokoro’ was chosen as the chef aims for cuisine that calms the soul. Rather than pursue beautiful presentation for its own sake, the chef seeks a natural appearance that delights the hearts of diners.This commitment shines in grilled items such as rolled omelette and sweetfish, as well as in bowls of stewed items. Handmade thick-fried tofu and fish cake are the perfect companions to their broth. Flavours as only a chef who has toiled earnestly in the fields of Kyoto cooking can produce.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
427;Gion Matayoshi;Japan;Kyoto;570-123 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.003349;135.774545;72;false;false;Japanese;The chef travels to different regions, searching for quality ingredients and checking them with his own eyes. He spares no efforts in his cooking, crafting a menu in which his dedication to service shines. Broth for soups draws umami from makombu and dried bonito. Sashimi plates are presented one type of fish at a time, each accompanied by the perfect condiment. Sesame tofu is served lightly deep-fried or simmered in a small bowl. Tofu is enrobed in whole wheat flour from the chef’s hometown of Okinawa, infusing it with the flavours of the region.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
428;Yusokuryori Mankamero;Japan;Kyoto;387 Ebisucho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8118, Japan;35.022114;135.750507;20;false;false;Japanese;This longstanding ryotei conveys the elegance of Kyoto culture to a modern clientele. ‘Organic cuisine’ takes on a special meaning here, denoting a style of cooking that began in the imperial court during the Heian period (794–1185). Clad in traditional Heian-era hunting robes, the chef deftly works the ingredients with knives, never touching them with his hands, in accordance with ritual practice. The Kyoto kaiseki menu is modeled after chakaiseki, with items added to express the shifting seasons. The chef and his son tend to food preparation while the proprietress waits on customers in Kyoto dialect. A family tradition going back eleven generations keeps this restaurant thriving.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
430;Ogata;Japan;Kyoto;726 Shinkamanzacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8471, Japan;35.003191;135.755967;99;false;true;Japanese;Bold, elegant cuisine, stripped down and pure, sets off works by Rosanjin and other artists. Avoiding piling element upon element, Ogata finds creativity in deceptively unsophisticated appearances. Technique is guided by intuition gained from each ingredient or inspired by seasonal expressions. Seasonal aesthetics are manifested through the choice of ingredients, revealing the natural vitality of each.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
432;Gion Nishikawa;Japan;Kyoto;473 Shimokawaracho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0825, Japan;34.999797;135.778857;97;true;true;Japanese;The chef selects ingredients in a way that treasures interaction with food producers. Against a backdrop of kombu boxes, decorating his walls like hanging scrolls, he prepares his dishes in a spirit of gratitude. His principle is that true flavours are subtle. In wanmono, he aims for a light flavour that brings out the umami of the makombu. But cooking is not the only thing that bewitches diners at Gion Nishikawa. The sukiya design of the interior makes the mood of old Gion palpable, while the chef’s affable personality keeps the room ringing with conversation and laughter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
433;Shimmonzen Yonemura;Japan;Kyoto;255 Umemotocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0064, Japan;35.006215;135.776646;52;true;true;Innovative;Freewheeling cuisine by a chef with Japanese spirit and Western learning. Gratin of truffles and clams is reminiscent of scallop coquilles served at Western restaurants. Use of serving dishes irrespective of cuisine shows a blending of Western and Japanese styles. Lacquered wooden trays, however, change with each dish, professing a sensitivity to beauty that pervades every aspect of Shimmonzen Yonemura. Supported by a team of young workers, the cuisine of Chef Masayasu Yonemura evolves with each restaurant he opens, from Kiyacho to Yasaka to Shimmonzen.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
434;Kyokaiseki Kichisen;Japan;Kyoto;5 Shimogamo Morimotocho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-0805, Japan;35.035717;135.771236;58;true;false;Japanese;Next to Shimogamo Shrine, surrounded by the Tadasu-no-Mori forest, lies Kyokaiseki Kichisen. The chef, a devotee of Japanese cuisine and the performing arts, built a ryotei on this spot. Respectful of Kyoto traditions, menu items are accompanied by charming details. Lids of soup dishes are emblazoned with dew, expressing freshness. Tuna sashimi is arrayed like a sea of clouds, creating a fairytale-like scene. Serving dishes of Kyoyaki ceramics, garnished with fresh-cut flowers, beguile the eyes. A unique interpretation of Kyoto kaiseki, accompanied by the spirit of graceful service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
437;Shunsaiten Tsuchiya;Japan;Osaka;41-4 Toyotsucho, Suita, Osaka, 564-0051, Japan;34.760534;135.490966;34;false;false;Tempura, Japanese;The menu is tempura kaiseki and the tempura of Yukihiko Tsuchisaka is the product of training in Japanese cuisine. Steamed abalone is ripple-cut to add texture, then fried in thin batter and served with dipping sauce made from its liver. Oil-and-coating combinations and frying methods are products of extensive research. Tsuchisaka makes conversation as he serves customers, an attentive practice he learned at a counter kappo. His motto is ‘true devotion’, and his sincerity permeates both service and cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
438;Miyamaso;Japan;Kyoto;375 Hanase Harachicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 601-1102, Japan;35.233154;135.793011;44;false;true;Japanese;Dishes made from the wild grasses of Miyama crowd the dinner table. Bounty of the season, handpicked in the great outdoors, is carefully selected and lovingly conjured into cuisine. Flavours are restrained, not extravagant, yet rich for all that, weaving a tale of the shifting seasons. Here we find nature and humanity living in the same moment, bestowing gratitude and respect on each other. Cuisine that prizes the natural world as it is.;Air conditioning,Car park,Shoes must be removed,Valet parking;[]
439;Kikunoi Roan;Japan;Kyoto;118 Saitocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8012, Japan;35.003449;135.770647;65;true;false;Japanese;‘Food has no borders’, declares the creed of Kikunoi. Carrying on the spirit of his brother, who runs Kikunoi Roan’s parent restaurant, Yoshiharu Murata seeks out new flavours using Western ingredients such as truffles and olive oil. In Kyoto restaurants, inclusion of a tea room is considered de rigueur, so while Kikunoi Roan sports a new style of counter and kitchen, the upper floor is equipped with a tea room, called Roan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
440;KAHALA;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-9-2 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697522;135.499685;82;false;false;Innovative;KAHALA opened the year after the 1970 Osaka Expo. Owner-chef Yoshifumi Mori was one of the first to discover and popularise ingredients used by many of today’s chefs. His hobby is lacquerware, and serves cuisine with a philosophical bent, delicious flavours harbouring a personal attitude to life, on lacquerware he made himself. With his elite team, he creates a small but top-notch dining emporium. The cooks toiling silently in the kitchen at the back, the dishwashing crew and the service staff all deserve a round of applause.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
441;Kenninji Gion Maruyama;Japan;Kyoto;566-15 Komatsucho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0811, Japan;34.998809;135.774574;87;true;false;Japanese;Situated on the south side of Kennin-ji Temple, the restaurant looks out on Yasaka Pagoda. Pass through the elegant gate, have a seat in the waiting area, and relax in the courtyard cooled with sprinkled water. The proprietor welcomes guests with the four-fold etiquette of the wabi-cha school of tea ceremony: harmony, respect, purity and tranquillity. In cuisine, he prizes the five unseen senses, with care paid to light, sound, temperature, fragrance and taste. Even the water is steeped in history, tradition and the four seasons. Unseen yet deep and strong are the roots of Kyoto culture here.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
442;Numata;Japan;Osaka;7F, 1-10-2 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697954;135.497901;50;true;true;Tempura;Tempura informed by other Japanese culinary disciplines. Freshly pressed sesame oil is the cooking oil of choice to bring out the flavour in the carefully selected tempura pieces. The chef hails from Amakusa, Kumamoto Prefecture, so his seafood and vegetables arrive from Kumamoto too. Mutually complementing seafood and vegetables alternate throughout the meal. Putting flavour first, vegetables are peeled just before serving. Insistence on quality and meticulous preparation mark a true artisan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
444;Kodaiji Wakuden;Japan;Kyoto;512 Washiocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0072, Japan;35.001635;135.779734;77;true;false;Japanese;This ryotei began life as a restaurant and ryokan in Kyotango. With the rustic beauty of the Tango countryside and the refinement of Kyoto as its themes, Kodaiji Wakuden is opening a new era in ryotei culture. Crab, a speciality of the restaurant’s birthplace, is cooked in a sunken hearth, a hole strikingly carved in the middle of tatami seating. Also remarkable is the tradition of this establishment, the flagship of the Wakuden group of restaurants, of appointing carefully selected young chefs to run it, to invite the fresh breeze of new ideas, guided by a philosophy of constant innovation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed;[]
445;ION Harbour by Simon Rogan;Malta;Valletta;11 St. Barbara Bastion, Valletta, VLT 1961, Malta;35.8962481;14.5141768;17;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;You’ll find impeccable service, a great view and truly special cuisine at ION Harbour. The kitchen is led by chef Simon Rogan, who holds Three Michelin Stars for his Lake District restaurant, L’Enclume, in the UK. Resident chef Oli Marlow offers complex dishes, using produce grown, reared or caught from the Maltese islands wherever possible, following the chef’s farm-to-fork philosophy. The view over the Grand Harbour is stunning and provides an amazing backdrop for your meal, while the professional service adds to the experience. When it comes to the wine, ask for some Maltese producers and you will discover excellent choices such as the 2020 Chardonnay from the Ta’ Betta Wine Estate, which is an intense and opulent option.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
446;Lafleur;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Palmengartenstraße 11, Frankfurt on the Main, 60325, Germany;50.1214911;8.6565825;18;false;false;Modern French, Creative;Andreas Krolik has been synonymous with fantastic vegan cuisine for years. Here in the Palmenhaus, adjacent to the Palmengarten, the chef creatively combines top-notch ingredients by virtue of extremely precise craftsmanship. His style is modern, yet rooted in classic culinary tradition. For example, the happy marriage of John Dory and Norwegian scallops, with a nutty macadamia crunch, sweet and sour pointed cabbage, firm pumpkin and the exotic touch of a curry-lemongrass sauce, is delicious. In the evening, two set menus are served: "Grands Produits" with meat and fish, and "Ethical Vegan Cuisine" a testament to the chef's passion for plant-based cuisine. At lunchtime, there are two appealing set menus, dubbed "Casual" and "Casual Green", each with three or four courses. Service comes courtesy of a very friendly and well-trained front-of-house team led by restaurant manager Boris Häbel, and the decor is stylish and modern. The wine pairings for the set menus are first-rate. Incidentally, the restaurant's name is a nod to the famous Château Lafleur vineyard near Bordeaux.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
447;IKIGAI;Germany;Krün;Elmau 2, Krün, 82493, Germany;47.4620032;11.1869112;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Every ounce of luxury that the unique hideaway of Schloss Elmau offers in the hotel and spa finds its culinary match in this restaurant. Chef Christoph Rainer draws inspiration from his travels to Japan and other Asian countries, as is reflected in the renaming of the restaurant, from Luce d'Oro to IKIGAI (the Japanese word means "a reason for being"). A love for Japan can be discerned in appealing details such as the elegant tableware, which includes decorative Japanese kokeshi dolls, but first and foremost when it comes to the food. Christoph Rainer consistently incorporates Asian and Japanese elements into his creations, which feature top-notch ingredients. "Unstuffed organic goose liver, ceriboshi, sakura miso, black cherry" is a highlight. A terrific wine list plus a nice selection of sake for pairing with the food. The service team come across as friendly and competent. The refined interior with its pared-back design and warm wood sets a sophisticated tone.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
448;Lakeside;Germany;Hamburg;Fontenay 10, Hamburg, 20354, Germany;53.565225;9.9980345;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Step out of the lift on the seventh floor of the imposing The Fontenay hotel and you will find yourself in an airy, light-filled space that bowls diners over with its bold design in elegant white, as well as its frankly sensational views over the city and the Outer Alster. The modern cuisine conjured up by Julian Stowasser is complex but never overcomplicated, showcasing premium ingredients and meticulous craftsmanship. There is a seven-course set menu comprising dishes such as Breton lobster, pineapple, coriander and lemongrass broth or Challans duck breast, black salsify, mandarin and ginger. Michel Buder heads up a beautifully trained front-of-house team: relaxed yet professional, efficient and experienced – including astute wine recommendations from sommelier Stefanie Hehn. If you have an aperitif in the chic bar on the sixth floor before your meal, you reach the restaurant via a curved staircase.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
450;Ösch Noir;Germany;Donaueschingen;Golfplatz 1, Donaueschingen, 78166, Germany;47.9655184;8.5471151;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Your curiosity will be piqued before you even get to your table: you pass by the open kitchen and catch a glimpse into the pots and pans. In this stylish and elegant fine dining restaurant housed in luxury hotel Der Öschberghof, Manuel Ulrich skilfully incorporates a judicious touch of modernity into his classic French-based cuisine. Every detail is considered, and his dishes never fail to impress with their precise craftsmanship and depth of flavour. For example, the combination of perfectly tempered Gillardeau oysters, glazed black salsify with a satisfying bite, the subtle piquancy of nasturtium and a dollop of Imperial Oscietra Caviar, with its pleasing nutty and salty notes, makes for a delightful culinary voyage to the sea and is a real feel-good dish. There are two set menus available: "Noir" and the vegetarian "Vert". The well-coordinated and enthusiastic front-of-house team, led by sommelier Michael Häni, delivers exceptional service – and you can count on him for excellent recommendations and the occasional surprise. He draws from an impressive wine list. There are also two house-made non-alcoholic options to accompany the set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
451;Courtier;Germany;Weissenhaus;Parkallee 1, Weissenhaus, 23758, Germany;54.3025337;10.7656888;73;true;true;Creative, Classic Cuisine;This stately home estate dating back to 1896 makes for a wonderfully idyllic setting with its romantic grounds dotted with old trees, its pond and its tantalising glimpses of the Baltic Sea – the terrace is to die for, especially at sunset! Using excellent ingredients, chef Christian Scharrer creates an extremely flavoursome fusion of classic cuisine and modern accents. And as you might expect from a stately home, diners are seated in sumptuous surroundings boasting stylish details such as chandeliers, mouldings and huge wall paintings by the French artist Jacques Courtier, after whom this restaurant is named. Then there is the attentive and smooth service provided by your cordial hostess, Nathalie Scharrer, and her professional front-of-house team.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
452;AURA by Alexander Herrmann & Tobias Bätz;Germany;Wirsberg;Marktplatz 11, Wirsberg, 95339, Germany;50.1073707;11.6069241;57;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Alexander Herrmann is a MICHELIN-starred chef, a restaurateur, a cookbook author, and a famous face on account of his appearances on various TV cooking shows. Located in Wirsberg, his family-run Posthotel is steeped in tradition. He and head chef Tobias Bätz form a well-oiled machine in this chic, modern and elegant fine dining restaurant. Their set menu (either with meat or vegetarian) proposes a culinary adventure showcasing the finest Franconian ingredients, including some real rarities. These are creatively and occasionally very elaborately prepared to go into dishes such as pickled and fried forest mushrooms with forest mushroom broth, larch oil, cassis berries and spruce extract. Accompanied by Franconian wines. The set menu starts at 6pm. Friendly service is provided with aplomb – even the chefs get in on the act and talk you through the dishes. The small cards with information about the ingredients which have been prepared and preserved in Future Lab ANIMA are a nice touch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
453;Mühle;Germany;Schluchsee;Unterer Mühlenweg 13, Schluchsee, 79859, Germany;47.8213714;8.1905051;72;true;false;Modern French, Creative;Niclas Nussbaumer is the chef at the helm of this fine dining restaurant in the small boutique hotel of the same name, which boasts a pleasant location slightly off the beaten track. His style draws on the foundations of classic French cuisine, while incorporating modern, innovative elements. He skilfully showcases first-rate seasonal ingredients, which he is keen to source from the region, impressing with his ability to combine flavours and textures and create clever contrasts. Subtle Asian influences are thrown in here and there, as seen in the grilled monkfish with yuzu kosho and tomato. Another standout is the "Black Forest Cherry" – a delightful reimagining of the classic local dessert. If you wish, you can extend the set menu to include a cheese course. Harmonious beverage pairings. The friendly and pleasingly personalised service comes courtesy of a front-of-house team led by the charming Lea Rupp – the chefs also come out to talk diners through the dishes. Tip: Why not stay overnight in one of the tastefully done out guestrooms in this picture-perfect building dating back to 1603?;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
454;PUR;Germany;Berchtesgaden;Hintereck 1, Berchtesgaden, 83471, Germany;47.6340765;13.0468265;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;The picturesque location on the Obersalzberg affords a fantastic mountain panorama for diners to take in. But the fine dining restaurant of the luxurious Kempinski Hotel Berchtesgaden has plenty more to offer than the view. First, the chic interior with its elegantly pared-down and modern design draws on a colour palette of soothing dark tones. Then there are the culinary creations of Ulrich Heimann, who proposes a harmoniously balanced tasting menu comprising five or seven courses. His dishes are cleverly structured, never cluttered, and they showcase impressively high-quality ingredients. The sauces are the crowning glory – a shining example is the extremely flavoursome jus that elevates the Challens duck breast with celery, truffle and quince to new heights. Not only is the food excellent, but the service is very friendly and obliging. On warm summer days, you can make the most of the wonderful terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
455;Meierei Dirk Luther;Germany;Glücksburg;Uferstraße 1, Glücksburg, 24960, Germany;54.8225486;9.4999203;82;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Temporarily closed for renovation.An elegant setting of gorgeous wooden tables and floor-to-ceiling windows – some seats afford a particularly good view of Flensburg Fjord. Beautiful vistas aside, it is Dirk Luther's cuisine that will really impress. The Hamburg native does a fantastic job of bringing together classic and modern styles of cooking, and even the odd moment of sheer brilliance is in evidence here. It is also worth mentioning the exceptional quality of the ingredients – particularly when it comes to fish and shellfish. The cordial front-of-house team is agreeably relaxed and discreet, while remaining attentive and professional. Those wishing to stay longer and enjoy the fantastic location on the Baltic Sea will find stylish, high-quality guestrooms and a tasteful spa at Vitalhotel Alter Meierhof.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
456;Ophelia;Germany;Constance;Seestraße 25, Constance, 78464, Germany;47.6671426;9.1874594;60;true;true;Creative French, International;Elegance and sophistication permeate every inch of this establishment, from the inviting lounge – perfect for an aperitif, digestif or coffee – to the stylish, contemporary restaurant and the fabulous terrace overlooking Lake Constance. The Riva hotel's fine dining restaurant boasts a prime waterfront location, but it captures hearts first and foremost with its classic-inspired cuisine under the culinary direction of Dirk Hoberg. This spruce Jugendstil villa dating from 1909 provides the setting in which to sample a tasting menu composed of refined and meticulously crafted dishes, complete with sauces inspired by the classics of French cuisine – the Château Chalon sauce, for example, is exquisite! The chefs serve one or two courses themselves. The extensive wine list features a particularly good selection of regional labels and sparkling wines, and the sommelier's recommendations are spot on. Tip: Book the "Kitchen Table" right by the pass to the open kitchen. Up to four diners can sit here with a clear view of the chefs at work.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
458;etz;Germany;Nuremberg;Wiesentalstraße 40, Nuremberg, 90419, Germany;49.4575467;11.0536916;75;false;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Felix Schneider und sein Team nehmen Sie mit in ihren ganz eigenen Kosmos. Ihr bis ins Detail konsequent umgesetztes Nachhaltigkeits-Konzept spiegelt sich klar in ihrem außergewöhnlichen saisonalen Menü wider, das voller eigener Ideen und Sinnhaftigkeit steckt. Man sammelt, pflanzt, fermentiert..., alles ist selbst produziert, von Schinken über Butter bis hin zu Miso und Essig. Um 18 Uhr startet die kleine Tour durch die Versuchsküche, danach serviert man Ihnen während vier bis fünf kurzweiligen Stunden zahlreiche kreative Gänge - omnivor (Fisch/Fleisch) oder vegetarisch. Beste Produktqualität ist bei den aromatisch-süßen Ur-Tomaten ebenso offensichtlich wie bei der topfrischen, nach Ikejime-Art geschlachteten Goldforelle. Dazu eine dynamische Getränkebegleitung, Weine oder alkoholfreie Kreationen. Dank offener Küche ist es hier freundschaftlich und locker, alles ist eingespielt und professionell. Die Köche servieren mit und erklären die Gerichte. Hinweis: Das Restaurant liegt etwas versteckt in einem Hinterhof, Zugang über Kirschgartenstr. 6.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
459;Tim Raue;Germany;Berlin;Rudi-Dutschke-Straße 26, Berlin, 10969, Germany;52.5070342;13.3933841;36;true;true;Asian, German;European cuisine that draws on Asia for inspiration – Tim Raue pulls off this modern and refreshing feat in truly original fashion. This Berlin-born chef has a style that is all his own and certainly unique in Germany. He works with a highly skilled team to turn out his flavourful creations. Diners have a choice of set menus dubbed "Kolibri x Berlin" (a tribute to Berlin) and "Koi", with his signature dishes of "Wasabi Langoustine" and "Duck 'Marie-Anne'" or "Königsberger Klops Grandma Gerda" available in each. There is also a vegan set menu. The restaurant is also open for lunch on Saturdays, serving two lunch menus – one of which is vegan – each with a choice of four to seven courses. The appeal of this place lies in its daring to be different. The lively urban ambience in no way detracts from the high standard of the cuisine. Thanks to hostess Marie-Anne Wild and her charming front-of-house team, you will feel at home in this sleek and elegant restaurant. The selection on the fantastic, extensive wine list is fantastic, with a very good wine flight to accompany the menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
460;Lorenz Adlon Esszimmer;Germany;Berlin;Unter den Linden 77, Berlin, 10117, Germany;52.5159333;13.380011;77;true;true;Creative;As you enter the exclusive Hotel Adlon Kempinski, the lobby sets the tone for the refined feel of the restaurant on the first floor. With a little luck, you will get a table with a view of the Brandenburg Gate. The sophisticated, classically opulent interior meets its match in Reto Brändli's wonderfully refined and creative French cuisine. Consistently top-notch ingredients are used to create elaborate and exquisitely balanced compositions that showcase superb technical precision – the sauces are extraordinary with their flawless consistency and aromas! The service team led by Oliver Kraft and sommelier Hans-Martin Konrad is also outstanding: from the outset, diners are treated in an extremely courteous and professional manner. Judicious wine suggestions plucked from a comprehensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
461;CODA Dessert Dining;Germany;Berlin;Friedelstraße 47, Berlin, 12047, Germany;52.4900681;13.4274391;95;false;false;Creative, Innovative;Don't be fooled by the unassuming-looking exterior of this Neukölln eatery – a very special take on fine dining awaits you inside. The atmosphere in the dimly lit interior is lively and laid back. Dine either at the counter, with a view into the kitchen, or at one of the surrounding tables. If you're lucky, you'll be given a sneak peek into how one ingredient or another is prepared in the kitchen. Chef René Frank cooks in his own style, which is certainly unique: he and his team apply patisserie techniques to prepare innovative dishes such as "aubergine, pecan, apple balsamic vinegar, liquorice salt" or "parsley root, black garlic & pistachio". Desserts are by no means the only focus, and refined sugar is avoided completely. You are invited to embark on a culinary adventure in 15 servings. The service is relaxed and very friendly. In addition to the pairing drinks that accompany the tasting menu, there is also an optional wine flight available. The wine list showcases a well-curated selection of German Rieslings, as well as an appealing range of sparkling wines and choice of sake.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
462;Jante;Germany;Hanover;Marienstraße 116, Hanover, 30171, Germany;52.3701441;9.7607489;73;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Tony Hohlefeld and his kitchen team steer clear of showmanship and unnecessary frills in their bid to bring technical excellence and original ideas to the table. The dishes here are sophisticated but not overly elaborate, complex but appealingly light, full of contrasts and yet wonderfully balanced, as in the char with dock and sour asparagus, or the venison with beetroot and greengage. A set menu is proposed with the option to upgrade. When making a reservation, you can also state your preference for a vegetarian/vegan menu. The easy style of the food reflects the atmosphere in this semi-circular building with floor-to-ceiling windows. The sleek Scandinavian-style interior contributes to the overall experience, as does the excellent service provided by pleasingly laid-back maître d' and sommelier Mona Schrader – the charming front-of-house team positively radiates cordiality and professional competence.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
464;bianc;Germany;Hamburg;Am Sandtorkai 50, Hamburg, 20457, Germany;53.5430154;9.9943521;40;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;Native Italian Matteo Ferrantino brings the flavours of southern Europe to Hamburg. The chef previously ran the kitchen of the two-star Vila Joya restaurant in the Portuguese city of Albufeira alongside Dieter Koschina. Here at Bianc, he serves a modern, creative take on Mediterranean cuisine in the form of two set menus "Emotion" and "Garden" (vegetarian) made with top-notch ingredients. Each begins with an array of amuse-bouches and is rounded off with a series of equally delicate petits fours. And in between, for example, "Red prawn, onion, cantaloupe, pata negra" or "Azores squid, egg yolk, guanciale, Pecorino" – interesting combinations that do full justice to the menu name "Emotion"! Architect Julia Erdmann has designed a chic interior that captures the charm of an Italian piazza, plus a view into the kitchen. The hors d'oeuvre served by the kitchen pass is a nice idea that contributes to the unique atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
465;100/200 Kitchen;Germany;Hamburg;Brandshofer Deich 68, Hamburg, 20539, Germany;53.5374323;10.0285764;59;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;What an experience! Here on the third floor of an unassuming factory building, in a loft-style space with an industrial chic design, the open kitchen takes centre stage. Working at a fantastic Molteni stove, set to either 100°C or 200°C – hence the name – the chefs deliver a creative surprise menu that is aligned with the seasons. With a passion and style that is all his own, Thomas Imbusch brings out the seasonal flavours through fermentation and smoking, for example, and turns out honest dishes that remain close to nature. Respect for the produce is the ethos here, with the emphasis on sustainability and small-scale producers who they know personally. To be enjoyed with organic wines or alcohol-free beverages. The "Carte Blanche Tasting Menu" is available in a slimmed-down version at Der Stundentisch. Head to Die Empore to dine à la carte (no reservation necessary). NB: Booking is via an online ticket-purchasing system.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
466;FACIL;Germany;Berlin;Potsdamer Straße 3, Berlin, 10785, Germany;52.5090625;13.3737404;92;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;A real oasis of calm in the middle of Berlin! Up here on the fifth floor of The Mandala Hotel, diners can sit on the pleasant little terrace amid the chestnut trees and fountain. It belongs to this elegant, light and airy rooftop garden restaurant, where even inside you almost feel like you're outdoors thanks to the all-round floor-to-ceiling windows. Beautiful bamboo plants give a nod to Asia. As well as the great location, Facil also boasts incredible food courtesy of Michael Kempf (culinary director) and Joachim Gerner (chef de cuisine). Rooted in classical cooking, it also skilfully integrates Asian and Mediterranean influences. Creative dishes brimming with flavours and aromas. All this is rounded off by the smart, professional service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
467;Tohru in der Schreiberei;Germany;Munich;Burgstraße 5, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.137597;11.577475;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Japanese Contemporary;It is absolutely worth climbing the 23 steps leading to the top floor of Munich's oldest townhouse ! It was here, in 1552, that the city's history began to be recorded – today, a very different story is being told. Tohru Nakamura, a Munich native of German-Japanese descent, bridges the gap between classic French and European cuisine and the culinary traditions of Japan. The combination of ingredients and flavours from both cultures makes for a unique twist, particularly notable in the exceptional sauces and broths – for instance, the kefir broth with beetroot and blackcurrant wood is sensational, perfectly complementing the fantastic pairing of top-quality Ozaki Wagyu beef and aromatic smoked eel. The set menu is served on the upper floor, accessible via a rather steep staircase. The tasteful, high-end interior has been designed with an eye for detail. Always on hand to provide expert guidance and elucidate the chef's culinary concept, the waitstaff are attentive and professional. A nice touch: Diners are even greeted with a tour of the kitchen!;Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
468;Tantris;Germany;Munich;Johann-Fichte-Straße 7, Munich, 80805, Germany;48.1697565;11.588259;48;true;false;French Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;Tantris boasts an undeniably distinctive look, showcasing a bold orange and black colour scheme. A few modern touches have been added, such as a striking walk-in glass wine cabinet, complementing the restaurant's legendary style without compromising its iconic 1970s charm. The culinary artistry of Benjamin Chmura and his team shines through in their masterful balance of textures and flavours, often incorporating playful bursts of acidity. This is beautifully exemplified in dishes such as "Printemps" (green asparagus, almonds, anise) and "Petit Bateau" (brill, mussels, vadouvan). The anticipation mounts as you savour the wonderful selection of bread with French butter served beforehand. There is a set menu comprising six or eight courses in the evening and one with four or six courses at lunchtime. The charming waitstaff impress with their efficiency and knowledge. The wine list is a delight for connoisseurs – the recommendations made by the sommelier team are spot on! Tip: Rare gems from the hotel's wine cellar are also available by the glass to accompany the set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
469;L.A. Jordan;Germany;Deidesheim;Ketschauerhofstraße 1, Deidesheim, 67146, Germany;49.4077831;8.184894;21;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Hotel, restaurants, event location – the former Bassermann-Jordan winery operates as all of the above. Historical architecture and modern interiors go hand in hand, both in Ketschauer Hof hotel and in the fine dining restaurant tucked away in the peaceful courtyard, home to its magnificent terrace. Devising a wonderful set menu, Daniel Schimkowitsch steers clear of gimmickry, instead bringing out distinctly intense flavours in a creative, pleasingly pared-back way. Japanese influences make themselves felt in dishes such as the smooth marron crayfish "à la nage", the succulent and tender meat of which is lent just the right degree of spiciness by Japanese mustard and harmonised brilliantly with the fantastic fine Kyoto miso sauce. Excellent ingredients are at the core of the menu. The well-curated German and international wine list counts over 1 000 different labels, and the wine pairing for the set menu is interesting. The service is everything you would hope for: charming, professional and responsive. In the L.A. Jordan Lounge, choose from the long list of à la carte dishes on the board.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
470;Horváth;Germany;Berlin;Paul-Lincke-Ufer 44a, Berlin, 10999, Germany;52.4963922;13.420793;28;false;true;Creative;The location on the Landwehrkanal in lively Kreuzberg, among other restaurants and shops, is special and a draw in itself. Out front is a lovely terrace shielded from the street. Inside, the atmosphere is intimate and cosy . The combination of old wood panelling and chic, modern design, along with a striking mural by Jim Avignon, draws as much attention as the glass-fronted kitchen. Here, Sebastian Frank conjures up dishes rooted in the culinary traditions of his Austrian homeland with plenty of creativity and an emphasis on sustainability. He showcases excellent ingredients, which he prefers to source from Berlin and the surrounding Brandenburg region, in an unembellished, seemingly unspectacular manner, and it is perhaps precisely for this reason that his cuisine is so memorable. Vegetarian dishes take centre stage. Tip: The signature dishes "celery ripe and young" and "soup greens 'Seleskowitz'"can be added to the current set menu. Cards provide information on each course. Sebastian Frank also enjoys interacting with guests and explaining his creations. Interesting wine list dedicated to Eastern Europe and Austria.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
471;Votum;Germany;Hanover;Hannah-Arendt-Platz 1, Hanover, 30159, Germany;52.3700128;9.7338212;56;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Benjamin Gallein is no stranger to the region. His creative cuisine is one of the fine dining options available in the Leineschloss, which is the seat of Lower Saxony's state parliament. The restaurant is housed in the modern extension of this historic building situated on the Platz der Göttinger Sieben, close to the Leine River. The name Votum is a reference to the choices to be made within the set menu: diners decide on the order of the courses, on potential "upgrades", as well as the wine pairings (alcohol-free alternatives also available). The dishes are named e.g. "cauliflower, parsley, egg, breadcrumbs" or "mularde from Odefey & Töchter, fermented plum, trumpet mushroom, hay". The glass-walled dining area makes for an elegant setting, as does the beautiful terrace overlooking the river. Attentive and well-drilled service, with the chefs occasionally delivering the dishes themselves. Schorse and Casino Royale also belong to the hotel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
472;Coeur D'Artichaut;Germany;Münster;Alter Fischmarkt 11A, Münster, 48143, Germany;51.9638925;7.6294251;70;true;false;Modern French, Creative;Somewhat tucked away in a courtyard (where there is a fabulous terrace in summer) and just a stone's throw from the cathedral, this appealing "casual fine dining" restaurant awaits. Almost reminiscent of a stage in a theatre, the stylish dining area features a striking ceiling with densely packed pendant lights and an eye-catching open kitchen. Here, French-born Frédéric Morel draws on his Breton roots and incorporates influences from his adopted home in Northern Germany and adds a touch of modern creativity – his sauces and stocks are outstanding! When selecting his high-quality ingredients, he is mindful of the seasons and the region in which they are sourced. The "Morel's Tasting" set menu, which changes every month, is composed of six or eight courses. A four-course version is available on Sundays only (excluding public holidays and Sundays in December). The chefs personally serve and present the dishes. House-made alcohol-free pairings make for a sophisticated and creative alternative to wine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
473;Atelier;Germany;Munich;Promenadeplatz 2, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1402487;11.5735681;47;true;true;Creative French, Seasonal Cuisine;This remarkable restaurant in Hotel Bayerischer Hof is reminiscent of an artist's studio – chic grey dominates the colour scheme, and everything is tastefully done, down to the last detail. This understated luxury provides the backdrop, courtesy of Axel Vervoordt's interior design. The extremely personable and young yet experienced service team pull out all the stops and are always on hand. Using top-quality seasonal ingredients, chef Anton Gschwendtner and his team conjure up a pared-back take on French cuisine, drawing on Asian influences. Fantastic dishes include ikejime salmon trout with Maison Morisseau bouchot mussels, carrot, kimchi emulsion and umami vinaigrette, or tender pink-roasted saddle of venison from Gutshof Polting with cranberries, Brussels sprouts and beech mushrooms, as well as a wonderful combination of a vinegar venison jus and a lightly foamed cognac and miso sauce. A vegetarian set menu can be arranged with a day's notice. The extensive wine list is wonderful – the wines served by the glass complement the set menus beautifully. Alternatively, opt for the signature wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
474;ammolite - The Lighthouse Restaurant;Germany;Rust;Peter-Thumb-Straße 6, Rust, 77977, Germany;48.259724;7.7251226;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic French;This beacon of gastronomy at Europa-Park is part of Hotel Bell Rock and is indeedlocated in a lighthouse. Designed by hotel Claudio Carbone, the interior is timelessly chic and elegantly grand. Translucent organza curtains in shimmering gold and warm tones create an intimate atmosphere and promote a feeling of tranquillity. Seated on plush velvet-upholstered armchairs at exquisitely set tables, diners enjoy attentive and competent service provided by a well-coordinated team. Chef Peter Hagen-Wiest presents two eight-course set menus: "Around the World" and "Green Forest" (vegetarian). Both reflect his cosmopolitan outlook and, at the same time, his ties to the region. Rather unspectacular-sounding dishes such as "char, barley, bacon" or "Breton red mullet, foie gras, lemon" belie a complexity of flavors and a delicate balance rarely encountered. The quality of the ingredients is beyond question. Decent wine selection and interesting pairings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
477;Essigbrätlein;Germany;Nuremberg;Weinmarkt 3, Nuremberg, 90403, Germany;49.455062;11.0748188;73;false;false;Innovative, Farm to table;You have to ring the bell to enter this small restaurant in the middle of Nuremberg's old town. It is a lovely intimate setting, with its cosy and inviting atmosphere and extremely charming and attentive front-of-house team. Working together seamlessly, Andree Köthe and Yves Ollech have developed a cooking style that is truly one of a kind and defies categorisation. Their creativity knows no bounds, resulting in exquisite and intelligently crafted dishes in which vegetables take centre stage, showcasing local produce. Their unwavering dedication to sustainability, embodied by their "leaf to root" approach, sets a remarkable example. The entire team is committed to this concept and happy to answer any questions you may have. Wine pairings that perfectly match the set menu are available. The top-notch wine list is a treat for Riesling enthusiasts in particular. It's best to request the vegetarian lunch set menu when making your reservation.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
480;Vendôme;Germany;Bergisch Gladbach;Kadettenstraße, Bergisch Gladbach, 51429, Germany;50.9665691;7.1604778;39;true;false;Creative, Classic French;Joachim Wissler has been running the kitchen at the elegant fine dining restaurant of the luxurious Althoff Grandhotel Schloss Bensberg since 2000. Drawing on classic French techniques, this Swabian-born chef infuses his dishes with modern flair, resulting in creative, beautifully crafted plates with complex and harmonious flavours. Highlights of the menu include the "carabinero special" and Lechtal trout sagohachi, as well as Portuguese red mullet and Kyushu Wagyu beef. There is a choice of two set menus (one of which is vegetarian) composed of five or seven courses. First rate service comes courtesy of a competent front-of-house team who are always on hand and yet pleasantly unobtrusive. More delights are to be found on the wine list, with fans of German Riesling particularly well catered for.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
481;OPUS V;Germany;Mannheim;O5, 9-12, Mannheim, 68161, Germany;49.4858598;8.4699546;36;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Shopping and fine dining under one roof? Head to the top floor of the engelhorn Mode im Quadrat department store for precisely that. A team headed up by Dominik Paul cooks modern and creative cuisine. The dishes bowl over diners with flavours that range from bold and robust to low-key, subtle and highly elegant. Made using excellent ingredients, everything is nicely pared down and wonderfully balanced. Clever wine pairings – that accompany, for example, the "wagyu, sepia, sake", "salmon, oyster, kohlrabi" or "beef, mushroom, bone marrow" – also make an impression with a few surprises. In the evening, there is the six-course set menu, "Urban Nature", and the four-course set menu, "Chef's Choice". On Saturday lunchtime, the restaurant serves a three-course menu – this option is also available on Wednesday evenings. The sleek, contemporary interior with a Nordic feel is attractive, and there is an open kitchen. The highlight, of course, is the roof terrace with a view of the city! N.B. The restaurant also has its own entrance.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
482;Speisemeisterei;Germany;Stuttgart;Schloss Hohenheim 1B, Stuttgart, 70599, Germany;48.712699;9.2137792;88;false;false;Creative, Innovative;The Kavaliersbau (squire's lodge) of Hohenheim Castle, in a quiet location outside the city, is a haven for the discerning foodie. This is thanks in no small part to Stefan Gschwendtner, who puts his own stamp on bold, precisely crafted, very intelligently structured dishes. In the process, he elevates the ingredients to stardom, allowing their intrinsic flavours to take centre stage. Take, for example, the char from Birnbaum fish farm, which is wonderfully tender, almost raw, subtly tempered and lightly salted. The set menu comprises seven courses. On Mondays, Thursdays and Sundays, a shorter version with five courses can be ordered in advance. First-rate service comes courtesy of a friendly and highly adept front-of-house team armed with astute wine recommendations. Non-alcoholic pairings are also available to accompany the set menu. In summer, this elegant restaurant expands onto the delightful terrace.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
484;EssZimmer;Germany;Munich;Am Olympiapark 1, Munich, 80809, Germany;48.1766707;11.557409;90;false;false;Modern French, Creative;Located on the third floor of the architecturally spectacular BMW Welt building, this glass-walled restaurant seems to be floating above the exhibition. Upon exiting the lift, you pass through a cosy lounge area to get to this chic urban-style establishment. From the tables at the floor-to-ceiling windows, you can look out at the high-end cars. The culinary creations served up by top chef Bobby Bräuer and his team are no less captivating. Prepared in time-honoured tradition, the bisque made with expertly barbecued green crab, for example, is a delight: intense flavour, rich colour and subtle seasoning with an elegant wisp of saffron and a hint of lemongrass providing a touch of sharpness. This is accompanied by marinated slices and tartare of scallop and aromatic celeriac. The John Dory with porcini, muscat squash and pata negra is another impressive combination. The five- to eight-course set menu is also available in a vegetarian version. Elegantly dressed in black, the waitstaff are attentive and professional.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
486;sein;Germany;Karlsruhe;Scheffelstraße 57, Karlsruhe, 76135, Germany;49.0062467;8.3818104;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Thorsten Bender's creative cuisine certainly explains the popularity of this little restaurant nestled on a quiet residential street. The chef's distinctive style shines through in his technically accomplished, clearly structured dishes, into which he seamlessly incorporates Asian flavours. A shining example is the raw marinated Icelandic char, thinly sliced and artfully arranged in the shape of a rose, accompanied by slivers of daikon radish and pear, as well as a green bergamot and coriander sauce, creating a harmonious interplay of acidity and fruitiness. Here, top-notch ingredients take centre stage. The upscale interior has a chic, modern feel. Friendly service comes courtesy of Franziska Dufner's experienced team – the chefs are also on hand to serve their dishes. The evening set menu comprises five to eight courses. A vegetarian alternative is also available by prior arrangement. At lunchtime, there is a four-course set menu, expandable to five courses.;Air conditioning;[]
487;Gourmetrestaurant Dichter;Germany;Rottach-Egern;Aribostraße 19, Rottach-Egern, 83700, Germany;47.6941309;11.7538484;86;false;true;Creative French, Modern Cuisine;If you don't take the side entrance, you can reach this fine dining restaurant via the lobby of the luxurious Parkhotel Egerner Höfe, just beyond the elegant bar and decorative glass wine cabinets. The setting is upmarket, slick and modern, with three Japanese holly trees housed in eye-catching glass cubes. Floor-to-ceiling windows afford views onto the grounds and sculptures outside. Traditional French cuisine meets modern innovation in this kitchen, where dishes are expertly crafted with particular emphasis on regional produce. Fish from the lake and other local produce are skilfully showcased. The exquisitely flavoursome Tegernsee char, for example, which is harmoniously combined with cauliflower and mace, deserves a mention here. The set menu ranges from five to nine courses. Attentive and friendly service. Excellent wine recommendations, courtesy of the remarkable sommelier Tobias Blaha. Tip: Two kitchen-side seats can be booked for an exclusive seven-course set menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
488;AUGUST;Germany;Augsburg;Johannes-Haag-Straße 14, Augsburg, 86153, Germany;48.3710103;10.9126019;56;true;false;Creative;A place that lives, sleeps and breathes art! Not only is there the special cachet of the listed Haag Villa (1877), there is also Christian Grünwald's cooking, the likes of which you would be hard pressed to find anywhere else. We are in the company of an extremely creative chef who stands out for having his own distinctive signature. This he showcases in a seasonal set menu – the various appetisers are a fantastic introduction! He draws inspiration from nature and uses ingredients of excellent quality. For example, the "local venison, Butter von 4 Hölzern, spruce needle powder, roasted macaroni almond, sour cherry, parsley root" exudes a wonderful forest aroma. The food is served on illuminated "display window" tables, with decorative and edible items on show under their glass tops. The space is extremely stylish, the atmosphere is pleasingly relaxed, inviting and familiar – Christian Grünwald himself is also on hand to shed light on his creations. Practical tip: You will find parking on the villa's premises.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
489;Le Pavillon;Germany;Bad Peterstal;Dollenberg 3, Bad Peterstal, 77740, Germany;48.4574092;8.2507048;59;false;false;Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine;It is not only nature lovers who are drawn to the idyllic Black Forest landscape, thanks to the scenically located and family-run Dollenberg hotel. This resort is also home to a fantastic fine dining restaurant. Head chef Martin Herrmann celebrates the classics while remaining open to modern innovations. He cooks up an eight-course set menu, which you can also trim down to a shorter version. The appealingly pared-back dishes are prepared using high-quality ingredients, and the sauces are a real highlight - for example, the great classic vin jaune sauce to accompany beautifully cooked, firm turbot with artichoke. Then there is high-quality tableware and magnificent views through the floor-to-ceiling windows, as well as the relaxed yet stylish service and knowledgeable wine recommendations. Sommelier Christophe Meyer proposes wines from his own "CM Edition" range.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
490;Hirschen;Germany;Sulzburg;Hauptstraße 69, Sulzburg, 79295, Germany;47.8404612;7.7088806;74;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;What is it that draws legions of visitors from near and far to this tranquil village in Markgräflerland? Douce Steiner and Udo Weiler's hotel-restaurant is housed in a picture-perfect building that dates back over 500 years. It boasts a charming, elegant dining area and friendly, attentive service. Windows allow a glimpse into the kitchen, where the chefs create a five- to seven-course set menu that takes its cue from the seasons. In doing so, they draw on classic French influences and use regional produce wherever possible. Ultra-fresh langoustine royale, for example, is elevated by the subtle contrasts provided by a combination of red Kampot pepper, pink grapefruit, olive oil and basil. To round out the set menu, you have the option to include classic extras such as foie gras or frogs' legs. Tip: Leave some room for the wonderful selection of small treats to go with your espresso. The idyllic courtyard is a lovely spot in which to enjoy an aperitif or digestif. Should you wish to extend your stay, very tasteful guestrooms are available.;;[]
492;Alois - Dallmayr Fine Dining;Germany;Munich;Dienerstraße 14, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1383054;11.5771585;80;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Dallmayr is a name that has always been synonymous with good taste and excellent ingredients, and that is also true of Alois. Head through the bar to a staircase that leads you up to the first floor of the iconic delicatessen. This is a chic and elegant setting in which to savour Rosina Ostler's cuisine, which skilfully blends classic French and Nordic styles with her Bavarian roots. This gives the array of dishes on the menu a unique hallmark: cleverly devised, thoughtfully structured and at the same time delicate creations such as "lobster, pumpkin, lavender" or "duck, radicchio, whisky" will linger long in the memory of diners. The quality of the ingredients is second to none. At lunchtime, there is a pared-down version of the set menu. Seek out Julien Morlat for judicious recommendations from a wine list that leaves nothing to be desired, especially when it comes to Old World wines. The charming waitstaff is supported by the chefs, who talk diners through their dishes, making for a refreshingly relaxed atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
493;Sylvestre Wahid - Les Grandes Alpes;France;Courchevel;28 rue de l'Église, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4144213;6.6349308;95;true;true;Creative;In an exclusive setting comprising just four tables, Sylvestre Wahid serves only around 15 lucky guests per sitting. This tailor-made culinary interlude is built around the chef's signature dishes, which he reinterprets at this ski resort location according to his inspiration – think Roscoff crab or a lemon and seaweed dessert. In an open kitchen where he is assisted by his trusted team, the chef displays a marvellous sense of daring, masterfully pairing lobster and crab with ingredients typical of Pakistani cuisine – spices, chilli and lemon acar pickles, lentil dahl etc. Magnificent produce, premium ingredients, delicate sauces, expert seasonings, impeccable technical skill and, above all, a dash of emotion – the generous tasting menu showcases it all.;;[]
494;La Table des Amis;France;Bonnieux;Les Mas Les Eydins, 2420 chemin du Four, Bonnieux, 84480, France;43.8511871;5.3018513;94;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Christophe Bacquié greets diners like old friends in his gorgeous farmhouse set in peaceful countryside, surrounded by vineyards, olive groves and lavender fields. With his wife Alexandra and a closeknit, committed team, all of whom share his passion for Southern France and its produce and wines, Bacquié unfolds a single set menu with a strong Mediterranean identity. With flavour as his watchword, he crafts the finest ingredients simply and transparently and we were delighted to see some of his signature dishes, such as his modern aioli and his vision of iced Calisson, in pride of place on the menu. An authentic Provençal property and the guarantee of wholehearted hospitality.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
495;La Voile - La Réserve Ramatuelle;France;Ramatuelle;Chemin de la Quessine, Ramatuelle, 83350, France;43.1923476;6.6481676;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This exclusive luxury hotel, which blends seamlessly into its natural surroundings, is the HQ of talented Éric Canino, a chef influenced by his fruitful collaboration with Michel Guérard. Inspired by the master of healthy cuisine, Éric composes his own Provençal score, with fruit and vegetables, fish and seafood (plus some poultry), enhanced with aromatic herbs and olive oil. His culinary scope is phenomenal, ranging as it does from a modern use of citrus fruits to textbook perfect sauces and reductions that add character and depth to each dish. His red mullet poached in seawater (one of the chef’s favourite cooking methods), paired with crushed tomatoes and citrus fruits and escorted by a truly superlative reduction of fish heads, is emblematic of this virtuoso chef. Consummate pastry chef Julien Coulomb (stints at le Cinq and Plénitude with Maxime Frédéric) signs creations stamped with delicate subtlety, such as his strawberry and rhubarb delight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
496;Les Ambassadeurs by Christophe Cussac;France;Monaco;Hôtel Métropole Monte-Carlo, 4 avenue de la Madone, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7405056;7.4275615;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The Métropole Monte Carlo Hotel, an iconic Belle Epoque extravaganza (1886), has been entirely revamped by Jacques Garcia, including the luxurious restaurant that sports the graphic palette so dear to the interior designer (bronze, ivory, warm yellow and gold). At the helm, virtuoso chef Christophe Cussac (former disciple of Joël Robuchon who ran the two-star restaurant before it closed for works) brilliantly navigates between a pure-bred Gallic culinary line-up and more modern recipes, all of which with the Mediterranean as baseline. Examples of the chef’s consummate skill include two sweet juicy langoustine tails, green beans and a Maltaise sauce. His high-flying, meticulous cuisine, depicted by spot on seasoning, cooking and plating, gives rise to dishes that are the quintessence of harmony and balance. Special mention for the incredible bread and dessert trolleys.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
497;L'Abysse au Pavillon Ledoyen;France;Paris;8 avenue Dutuit, Paris, 75008, France;48.8662069;2.3164988;49;true;true;Japanese, Creative;A Japanese sushi master, outstanding quality ingredients (ikejime fish from the Atlantic) and the creative touch of Yannick Alléno… an enticing prospect. The pared-back restaurant room features work by contemporary artists – the installation made up of thousands of wooden chopsticks is by Japanese artist Tadashi Kawamata and the ceramic walls were designed by the American William Coggin. Add to this the tip-top service typical of a high-calibre establishment, a sumptuous wine list full of sought-after sakes and 12 seats at the pale wood counter, where you are right in the middle of the action. Sensational!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
500;La Scène;France;Paris;32 avenue Matignon, Paris, 75008, France;48.8720257;2.3143813;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Stéphanie Le Quellec has professed her aim to "deconsecrate haute cuisine" via her set menus comprising different numbers of courses or "acts". The dishes may appear simple but every last detail has been carefully considered so that the bold flavours come through loud and clear. Happily, some of her signature dishes are reprised here, such as caviar, French toast and Pompadour apple. Tuck in to pastry chef Pierre Chirac's top-notch desserts – he creates "cooked" desserts with distinct tasting notes, like his dual-origin Tahiti vanilla in a crème brûlée and Madagascar vanilla in an ice cream. There is a fine choice of wines by the glass served from magnums and even jeroboams. It all comes together thanks to a well-coordinated team, from the kitchen to the front-of-house staff, who provide attentive and friendly service. At lunchtime, a tempting menu based on seasonal ingredients is served in the bistro.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
501;La Table Lionel Giraud;France;Narbonne;Rond-point de la Liberté - 68 avenue du Général-Leclerc, Narbonne, 11100, France;43.1743172;2.9918502;86;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The place is named after Abbé St Crescent, who in the Middle Ages opened his doors to pilgrims on the Camino de Santiago. The arcades and bare stones may be a throwback to the distant past, but today the decor is ultra-modern, with finely crafted black and white polished concrete floors and sculptural one-piece seats. Lionel Giraud, son of a restaurant owner, is a strong advocate of locally sourced produce. An inventive chef, he honours ingredients from the most noble (Mediterranean red tuna) to the most modest (green beans) and everything in between, such as an authentic Corbières buffalo mozzarella. He is also a proponent of ikejime, the Japanese method of killing fish that maintains the quality of the meat and is argued to be more humane.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
503;Flaveur;France;Nice;25 rue Gubernatis, Nice, 06000, France;43.7014072;7.2718302;53;true;true;Creative;The Tourteaux brothers, Gaël and Mickaël, are inseparable. Not only did they attend the same hotel school in Nice (and sit exams in the same room) and both train at the Negresco during Alain Llorca's time there, but they also share the same motivation to run their own place, delivering good, honest, tasty fare. The result of this fraternal alliance is Flaveur, a project into which they ploughed all their energy to the point of receiving a Michelin star in 2011, and a second one in 2018.How might the "Tourteaux touch" be summed up? A certain kind of confidence, boldness and measured risk-taking. For example, when it comes to local ingredients and spices from afar, it's not either/or, it's both! A scorpion fish from Nice comes up against a fish broth enhanced with vadouvan, a heavily aromatic blend of Indian spices... They often go out on a limb, but the risk always pays off. Fine and masterful cuisine with character from start to finish. Bravo!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
504;L'Oiseau Blanc;France;Paris;19 avenue Kléber, Paris, 75116, France;48.8707602;2.2933134;38;true;true;Creative;This is the "contemporary French fine dining" restaurant at The Peninsula, a luxury hotel located near the Arc de Triomphe. It is named after the plane in which Nungesser and Coli attempted the first North Atlantic crossing in 1927, and a life-size replica of the plane is affixed to the top of the hotel, as if poised to take to the skies before your very eyes. A fine tribute to the two aviation pioneers, as well as to the sky over Paris! Perched above the rooftops and encased in glass, the restaurant feels like it is in flight over the capital, while the terrace offers a fantastic view of the Eiffel Tower and the Sacré Cœur. A perfect setting in which to sample the fine cuisine of chef David Bizet, which hits the nail on the head in all respects: cooking, jus and sauces, visuals. As for the desserts, pastry chef Anne Coruble treats our taste buds to the fruits of her talents. A great success.;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
505;Duende;France;Nîmes;Quai de la Fontaine, Nîmes, 30900, France;43.8388191;4.3527079;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Duende! Come and see how the arts of bullfighting and flamenco dancing have set fire to the imagination of Pierre Gagnaire. The fine dining establishment of the Hotel Imperator has its own separate entrance, in line with the chef’s independent spirit. Premium ingredients, proven technical expertise, spontaneity and originality. The master chef has entrusted the keys of his house to Nicolas Fontaine and Masaki Nagao, who seem to know their mentor and his rebellious spirit inside out. The tasting menu pays a subtle tribute to the finest produce from the Gard and the Mediterranean region (Baron des Cévennes pork, vegetables from small market gardeners, fish from the Mediterranean) in subtle, delicate dishes. The superb wine list of over 1,000 references demonstrates a clear penchant for regional vintages. Charming welcome paired with swish, highly professional and elegant service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
506;Restaurant Le Meurice Alain Ducasse;France;Paris;Le Meurice, 228 rue de Rivoli, Paris, 75001, France;48.86525;2.3278399;75;false;false;Creative;Take an iconic luxury hotel opposite the Jardin des Tuileries and an incredibly gifted chef, Alain Ducasse, then add a sprinkling of luxury à la Versailles (white ceiling adorned with gilding, crystal chandeliers) and – voilà! – you get Le Meurice. This place has not failed to catch the imagination of wealthy foreign patrons, who come to soak up that Parisian je-ne-sais-quoi. The Ducasse brand is cultivated by executive chef Amaury Bouhours: the tasting menus featuring dishes served in small portions are both a tribute to French tradition and a showcase of the chef's creativity. High-profile pastry chef Cédric Grolet creates desserts, images of which do the rounds on social networks.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
507;La Grenouillère;France;La Madelaine-sous-Montreuil;19 rue de la Grenouillère, La Madelaine-sous-Montreuil, 62170, France;50.4710226;1.7544175;71;false;false;Creative;(Temporarily closed) Few chefs show such a strong culinary personality as Alexandre Gauthier in La Madelaine-sous-Montreuil (near the northern tip of France). The story unfolds in a space with two tiered metal rooftops (designed by architect Patrick Bouchain) and views onto the verdant surroundings and the kitchens. This is the laboratory in which the chef cooks up "contemporary cuisine with French roots, liberated from its certainties and preconceptions". Like an alchemist, he teases out flavours in on-point dishes, each a vignette of creativity in which the ingredients sing the praises of the seasons. Artistic and experimental cuisine, to be savoured in this old Picardy farmhouse imbued with a luxury that remains close to nature.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
508;Lalique;France;Bommes;1707 route des Gourgues, Bommes, 33210, France;44.5493811;-0.3374123;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Château Lafaurie-Peyraguey is the ideal setting for a first-rate meal: the lavish dining area is adorned with (you guessed it!) a Lalique crystal chandelier, and the glass-paned extension commands a fine view of the vineyards. Chef Jérôme Schilling boasts a flawless CV (including Guy Lassausaie, Joël Robuchon, Thierry Marx and Meilleur Ouvrier de France 2023) and describes himself as a "cuisinier des vignes" ("cook of the vines"). His dishes inspired by the Sauternes terroir sport names such as "Interpretation of the 2011 vintage": langoustines, kalamensi and pollen, or "the grape seed": hake confit, bergamot and elderflower. The food is served in magnificent crystalware by Lalique and other fine china tableware, upping the table arts ante to a whole new level. A timeless place, where skilful, precise cuisine aims to exalt the distinctive flavour profile of Sauternes, which needless to say enjoys pride of place on the extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
509;La Côte d'Or;France;Saulieu;Le Relais Bernard Loiseau, 2 avenue Bernard-Loiseau, Saulieu, 21210, France;47.2797873;4.2321852;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This famous institution of the Morvan region, which has seen so many generations of chefs and lovers of fine food pass through its doors since the days of Alexandre Dumaine and then Bernard Loiseau, has embarked on a new chapter. After over 40 years of loyal service, Patrick Bertron has passed the baton to his right-hand man Louis-Philippe Vigilant. There is no doubt that the restaurant will retain the culinary signature of authenticity that sealed its reputation. As an alternative to the chef's new creations, nostalgic guests can travel back in time with some of Bernard Loiseau’s great classics, such as frog's legs with garlic purée and parsley juice, or pan-fried pike-perch in red wine sauce.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
510;Racine;France;Reims;6 place Godinot, Reims, 51100, France;49.2528607;4.03752;22;true;false;Creative;Here in the heart of Reims, there is definitely something interesting afoot. This small restaurant has a delightfully pared-back and contemporary interior with bay windows looking out onto a charming Japanese garden. The setting is in perfect harmony with the cuisine of Japanese chef Kazuyuki Tanaka. He crafts elegant and creative dishes that are rife with different flavours and influences, using aromatic herbs, vegetables, plants, condiments etc. Each one is a surprise, not only in terms of the exceptional quality of the ingredients (such as the langoustine or lobster) but also by their technical mastery and aesthetic appeal. An excellent wine list, including 250 champagnes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
512;La Fourchette des Ducs;France;Obernai;6 rue de la Gare, Obernai, 67210, France;48.4620365;7.488355;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Nicolas Stamm-Corby strikes the perfect balance between celebrating the classics and a touch of inventiveness that hits the spot every time. Whatever the season, he regales us with artfully presented dishes, in which premium produce takes the limelight. In winter, the ballotine of squab and foie gras, cabbage stuffed with "fil d'or" choucroute and pigeon jus with truffles sings a heartfelt ode to Alsace! Gifted young pastry chef Benjamin Mornay demonstrates his skills with a delicious baba au rhum, with crème chiboust, Tahitian vanilla ice-cream and a tasting of “ron diplomatico” that lingers with us still, as does the almost indecent trolley of miniature delights: fruit tarts, kougelhopf, cherry financiers and lavender honey madeleines…;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
514;Py-r;France;Toulouse;19 descente de la Halle-aux-Poissons, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.599313;1.4408583;26;true;false;Creative;Pierre Lambinon is nothing if not wholehearted! In this restaurant just a stone's throw from the Pont Neuf, he is making waves with his cooking. The meal begins with a festival of appetisers, bringing a foretaste of the flavours that will define the meal. The chef is at his most inspired when it comes to deftly preparing dishes based on herbs from the garden, fish and seafood and fine seasonal vegetables – intoxicating seafood aromas, grilled notes and the bitter overtones of vegetables. For example, line-caught hake from Saint-Jean-de-Luz and Pyrenean trout gravlax, broad beans and wild garlic in a big-boned pesto and citrus juice with concentrated honey. It's original, but he pulls it off! The vaulted, predominantly white interior is hung with eye-catching artwork by contemporary artists. The epitome of stylish!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
515;Marsan par Hélène Darroze;France;Paris;4 rue d'Assas, Paris, 75006, France;48.8499883;2.3279216;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The stylish interior, oozing understated glamour, provides the perfect foil to food embodied by the “special something” that depicts the cooking of Hélène Darroze, descended from a family of cooks. Namely, the ability to scour her homeland of southwest France for ingredients that nurture her culinary inspiration, paired with an unmistakable flair for artistic plating: terrine of Landes foie gras, blue lobster in tandoori spices (a signature dish), armagnac-flavoured baba. Her rigour, insatiable curiosity and game-changing mixture of talent and intuition hit the spot every time. A stellar success.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
516;Le Jules Verne;France;Paris;Tour Eiffel - 6 avenue Gustave-Eiffel, Paris, 75007, France;48.85756;2.29462;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Frédéric Anton presides over the fortunes of this emblematic restaurant on the second floor of the Eiffel Tower, accessible by a private lift. The magic of this location 125m up from ground level instantly bewitches diners, who are further captivated by the high-flying cuisine. Every day, Kévin Garcia's teams pull out all the stops to elevate blue-ribbon produce and deliver delicate, perfectly judged dishes boasting flavour combinations that are always on point. For example, a sublime soufflé of scallops with a Dieppoise sauce and Oscietra caviar, or grenobloise-style caramelised calf sweetbread, perfectly executed with no unnecessary frills. Germain Decreton's desserts are in keeping with the lofty standards. When booking, ask for one of the tables near the windows, as the view over Paris through the tower's iron fretwork is nothing short of spectacular. An impeccable welcome and very committed service.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
517;David Toutain;France;Paris;29 rue Surcouf, Paris, 75007, France;48.8602663;2.3097038;30;false;false;Creative;The grandson of farmers, Normandy-born David Toutain started out in the kitchen of Bernard Loiseau, before making a name for himself at a series of renowned establishments (including Arpège, Agapé Substance). In a modern, loft-style space, he has brought a showcase of culinary experimentation to a quiet street in a neighbourhood of government buildings. His technical prowess brings clarity to his dishes as he tirelessly taps into contemporary tastes (rather like his best friend, Alexandre Mazzia) to produce an ambitious cuisine d'auteur. He and his team now serve their creations in the form of "surprise" set menus comprising four to 10 courses. The desserts by pastry chef Émilie Gérardi deserve a special mention. The terrific wine list features a number of reasonably priced bottles.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
518;Le Puits Saint Jacques;France;Pujaudran;57 avenue Victor-Capoul, Pujaudran, 32600, France;43.5907291;1.149996;92;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Once a coaching stop on the Camino de Santiago, this characterful Gers house is the site of a handsome dining room that blends historic (beams, bricks and tiles) with modern (light fittings, furnishings, tableware) details. Chef William Candelon’s culinary score is a delicious patchwork of hearty country fare and contemporary sobriety, in a bid to showcase first-class ingredients: lamb sweetbread, morel mushrooms, truffles, guinea fowl, Challans duck.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
519;Auberge de l'Ill;France;Illhaeusern;2 rue de Collonges-au-Mont-d'Or, Illhaeusern, 68970, France;48.1844003;7.433043;56;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The Auberge de l'Ill is much more than just a restaurant. It embodies the Alsatian inn in all its glory – an inviting and friendly place, untouched by the passage of time, where every customer is welcomed like a member of the family… It is an institution in the region, but also renowned throughout France and beyond! Since it was established in 1882 (between Sélestat and Riquewihr), the restaurant has made a name for itself thanks to its matelote with riesling and dishes based on local game. Marc Haeberlin, grandson of the founders, now serves the classical repertoire (foie gras terrine served by the spoonful, frog’s leg mousseline, salmon soufflé) alongside more modern creations. The legend lives on.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
520;La Table d'Olivier Nasti;France;Kaysersberg;9-13 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Kaysersberg, 68240, France;48.1386233;7.265581;90;true;false;Creative;Ah, Kaysersberg! This small village on the Alsace wine route comes into view between two valleys – you can't miss the iconic red façade of Hotel Le Chambard, which houses La Table d'Olivier Nasti, Meilleur Ouvrier de France 2007. The chef's objective is to showcase the terroir and restore tradition in a series of creative, visually arresting, even playful dishes. To this end, no ingredients are off limits: game, morels from the Vosges, foie gras, truffles and even Arctic char. He has created a personal menu that takes the seasons into account and pays particular attention to sauces and decoctions. As for the wine, talented and enthusiastic sommelier Jean-Baptiste Klein is a mine of information. The Chambard's guestrooms are decorated in a chic, refined style, and let's not forget the gorgeous spa.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
521;JY'S;France;Colmar;3 allée du Champ-de-Mars, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0755636;7.3533263;21;true;false;Creative;Schillinger is a name that resonates particularly strongly in Alsace. First there was Jean, then there was his son Jean-Yves, who, after a period on the New York City restaurant scene (Destinée, Olica), returned home in 2002. Here in this restaurant bordering the Champ-de-Mars Park, he is full of bright ideas. His cuisine embraces one tradition after another with disconcerting ease – Alsace, the United States, Brittany and Japan. Confident in his strengths, he deploys a no-holds-barred approach – as in, for example, his Breton lobster cooked in a Cona coffee maker and served with the claw in a spring roll and fresh herb agnolotti, or a medley of green apple textures flanked by a seafood lemon and caviar sorbet..., not to mention the trolley laden with exquisite bite-sized desserts. A unique experience and exceptional flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
522;Serge Vieira;France;Chaudes-Aigues;Le Couffour, Chaudes-Aigues, 15110, France;44.8442761;3.0019613;27;false;true;Creative;Imagine a contemporary vessel built out of stone, iron and glass set in a medieval fortress with a 360° view of the countryside. Marie-Aude and Serge Vieira fell in love with the spot and quickly turned this out-of-the-ordinary venue into an establishment whose reputation extends far beyond the borders of Auvergne. Serge, whose talent and kindness were beloved of all, bequeathed his substantial culinary heritage to Marie-Aude and her teams, all of whom are committed to upholding Serge’s enthusiastic and sensitive approach to food while enhancing the outstanding produce of Auvergne. An example: slab of Aubrac beef, courgette cannelloni and marigold-flavoured mash, black garlic and an ivy-flavoured gravy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
523;Le Pressoir d'Argent - Gordon Ramsay;France;Bordeaux;InterContinental Bordeaux - Le Grand Hôtel, 2-5 place de la Comédie, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8424463;-0.5747973;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;British chef Gordon Ramsay (born in Scotland) is a true culinary talent who has already been awarded three Michelin stars in England. He signs off on Le Pressoir d'Argent's menu who breathes a touch of modernity into the classic cuisine. It all comes together to enhance that French art de vivre – the opulent and refined decor and ultra competent service, the celebration of the finest ingredients from the abundant Bordeaux and Aquitaine region (foie gras, truffles, caviar, fish)… and the solid silver Christofle lobster press that is moved from table to table. The competence of the three sommeliers is remarkable, as they advise you on the 1 000-bottle selection, two thirds of which are from Bordeaux, naturally!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
524;Château de Beaulieu - Christophe Dufossé;France;Busnes;1098 rue de Lillers, Busnes, 62350, France;50.581874;2.5070873;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Christophe Dufossé has been thriving in his homeland, as his cooking illustrates. This pretty château set in leafy grounds sports a contemporary conservatory extension. The chef champions organic, self-sufficient and sustainable surf and turf cooking centred on vegetables and produce from the region. Every dish is delicately and generously crafted – and flanked by big-boned, classically curated sauces. Standout dishes include his red mullet à l’unilateral (cooked on one side) with a punchy jus of fish bones, cucumber tagliatelle and an emulsion of fresh almonds or his stunningly unorthodox dessert which features green asparagus, an icy lemon balm foam, olive oil sponge biscuit, finely diced raw asparagus and kalamansi and a sorbet of lemon and lemon balm. Other highlights are the bread and sweets, particularly the lavish dessert trolley.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
525;Le Grand Restaurant - Jean-François Piège;France;Paris;7 rue d'Aguesseau, Paris, 75008, France;48.8701983;2.3193146;26;true;false;Creative;Welcome to Jean-François Piège's "laboratory of great cuisine", a tiny dining area beneath a sculptural ceiling made up of panes of glass that catch and reflect the light. The chef gives full expression to the scope and breadth of his experience and know-how, executing timeless signature cuisine that finds its source in the annals of French gastronomy (the chef is said to own one of the finest cookery libraries of Paris). There is no carte but a tasting menu that tours the regions of France and revolves around Piège’s "mijotés modernes". This consummate chef demonstrates his creative talent and ability to provoke culinary emotion and taste without falling foul of the temptation to flaunt his skill. He invariably surprises us with dishes that are the epitome of simplicity and flavour, such as his succulent veal sweetbread cooked on walnut shells, served with whelks and a spicy stock emulsified by spring lettuce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
527;Guy Savoy;France;Paris;11 quai de Conti, Paris, 75006, France;48.8566248;2.3391955;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the exceptional setting of the Hôtel de la Monnaie, Guy Savoy is continuing the story he began a few decades ago – back when, as a young boy, he would peek into the pans in the kitchen of his family's restaurant, La Buvette de l'Esplanade, in Bourgoin-Jallieu. Here, he has taken things to another level, with six dining rooms adorned with contemporary paintings and sculptures (many lent by François Pinault) and with old-fashioned windows overlooking the Seine. The splendour of the backdrop in no way distracts the chef from his mission, which is to pay tribute to French cuisine every day. It is a joy to rediscover his emblematic artichoke soup with truffle, to be relished with a brioche spread with truffle butter.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
529;Table - Bruno Verjus;France;Paris;3 rue de Prague, Paris, 75012, France;48.8486151;2.3759654;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Bruno Verjus's approach is to select the finest ingredients and cook them with humility and the utmost respect. This remarkable character was previously an entrepreneur, blogger and food critic. Behind the counter (where diners are seated on comfortable bar stools), he waxes lyrical about his suppliers and the desire to take a back seat to the artisans who produce what he then cooks – on that note, when it comes to either the recipes or the ingredients, the chef considers himself to be a "middle man". Everything is made to order, with garnishes and sauces designed with just one thing in mind: to elevate produce without distorting it. Let yourself be transported by the wide-ranging set menu (poetically named "Colour of the Day") and devised daily according to available ingredients: Utah Beach natural oysters, calf brain and sea anemone fritters, lobster from the Île d'Yeu, red mullet grilled skin on, "poularde gauloise rôtie en patience"... The premium ingredients are exceptional. Online booking only.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
530;Jean Sulpice;France;Talloires-Montmin;303 route du Port, Talloires-Montmin, 74290, France;45.8393308;6.210543;30;false;false;Creative;The Auberge du Père Bise is buzzier than ever under the impetus of Jean Sulpice and his wife, Magali! A keen sportsman, the chef serves delicate food that is healthy and light in a single set menu. Wild herbs, flowers and plants add contrast and colour to his creative and incisive dishes, which are a delicious roll call of fish from the lake. Served in beautiful ceramic tableware, this poetic experience unfolds in an elegant contemporary dining space whose lakeside terrace commands a view of the crystal-clear waters of Lake Annecy that borders on hypnotic. The front-of-house is professionally managed by Coline Humbert, who sets an elegant cheerful tone. An exceptional foil for a bold gastronomic experience that never fails to deliver.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
531;La Grand'Vigne - Les Sources de Caudalie;France;Martillac;Chemin de Smith-Haut-Lafitte, Martillac, 33650, France;44.7310086;-0.5571095;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Not far from Bordeaux, this property is a little paradise nestled in the vineyards of Château Smith Haut Lafitte, a Graves grand cru classé winery. Nicolas Masse is the chef behind La Grand'Vigne, the hotel's fine dining restaurant. Masse strives tirelessly towards a single goal, which is to showcase the bountiful produce of Aquitaine (from caviar to Pyrenean lamb), including its vegetable cornucopia and its wines, especially those of Pessac Léognan. As legible as it is pure, his high-flying cuisine is dedicated to revealing the distinctive flavour of painstakingly selected produce from southwest France. Nothing is too good, whether it be the front-of-house service or the wine suggestions. A truly mind-blowing experience!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
532;Le Pré - Xavier Beaudiment;France;Clermont-Ferrand;Route de la Baraque, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7886787;3.0519431;31;false;false;Creative;"The Auvergne I want to present to you is the one we harvest every morning in our mountains, meadows and forests." The proclamations of Xavier Beaudiment, who comes from the region, are no empty words. Le Pré is the epitome of simplicity – the chef's recipes use pork, eggs or peas, which may not be ingredients that make your mouth water, but he lovingly crafts them to draw out their flavour. Let yourself be swept along by this instinctive cuisine that is moulded into poetic-sounding set menus that pay homage to his terroir. His dishes also involve the 200 plants and wild herbs that grow in the shelter of the volcanoes. A superb wine list accompanies you on this culinary adventure.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
534;L'Auberge de Montmin;France;Talloires-Montmin;1983 route de Talloires, Col de la Forclaz, Talloires-Montmin, 74210, France;45.8072811;6.2486842;27;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Forclaz Pass (1 147m) is not just a paradise for paragliders, but also for fine food lovers, thanks to this restaurant, which has been refurbished and extended without losing its snug Alpine appeal. Chef Florian Favario adds an increasingly creative spin to cuisine based on the best of local produce (eg lamb and piglets, home-grown vegetables, seasonal fruit). He masterfully combines wildflowers, plants and herbs, such as thyme, sage, oregano, agastache, hyssop, mint flower etc. The resulting feast of extraordinary scents elevates dishes that are already at the apex of culinary technique and know-how. These detailed dishes, presented in walnut tableware designed by the chef himself, are brought out of the kitchen by a crack team led by an attentive Sandrine, the chef's wife. A drink before dinner on the terrace is the perfect opportunity to take in the view of the mountain pastures.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
536;La Merise;France;Laubach;7 rue d'Eschbach, Laubach, 67580, France;48.8800665;7.7224093;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This traditional Alsace house near Haguenau is a remarkable new construction built out of old materials so as to seamlessly blend in with its rural setting overlooking the hills and orchards. It is the haunt of Christelle and Cédric Deckert. Using high-quality ingredients, the chef concocts his own intriguing take on classical, yet never boring recipes, enhanced by subtle and skilfully prepared jus and sauces. The brilliant sommelier Joël Brendel is a treasure trove of insightful tips.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
538;Les Morainières;France;Jongieux;1400 route de Marétel, Jongieux, 73170, France;45.7449451;5.7982975;52;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Michaël Arnoult, who was sous-chef to Emmanuel Renaut, has transformed this place overlooking the hilly vineyards and the Rhone Valley into a veritable corner of paradise. His modus operandi: using fresh ingredients and respecting those who cultivated them. Choosing local producers, getting to know them and collaborating with them is a matter of priority. Game, green asparagus, suckling lamb, trout or Arctic char... you get a sense of his exacting standards in the dishes. If we had to pick a representative dish, it might be the superbly fresh crayfish tartar, enhanced by its subtle carcass jus, coriander flowers and sweet marigold: pure excellence! The refined interior reflects the chef's cuisine and looks out onto the valley. There are six comfortable guestrooms a few kilometres from the restaurant. More than ever, Les Morainières is worth the detour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
539;Cédric Burtin;France;Saint-Rémy;Chemin de Martorez, Saint-Rémy, 71100, France;46.7567708;4.8200267;30;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Welcome to this tranquil 19C watermill, by a millstream. It is flanked by a cottage garden, whose sole purpose is to supply the restaurant’s kitchen. After growing up in the Charolais countryside, chef Cédric Burtin did stints in Lyon restaurants operated by world-class chefs of the ilk of Paul Bocuse and Pierre Orsi. Today, his own restaurant enjoys a fine reputation in the region amongst the locals and a clientele from further afield. This subtle chef’s inventive hallmark and his flair for allowing fresh ingredients to shout their name, thanks to virtuoso technique and mouth-watering plating, are second to none.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
541;Le Sarkara;France;Courchevel;Le K2 Palace, 238 rue des Clarines, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4122032;6.638871;40;false;false;Creative;Gifted pastry chef Sébastien Vauxion takes you on a sweet-toothed escapade, the likes of which you won't have experienced before! His creations, based on fruit and vegetables (combined with dairy produce, chocolate and coffee), are genuinely mind blowing and infinitely tantalising. Take, for example, the potato flanked by Buddha’s hand and parsley, or celeriac with black truffle and mildly spicy citrus fruit pickles. And while the overall effect is undeniably sweet, rest assured, the coherence of each course is fully in keeping with traditional culinary codes thus ensuring that the palate remains fresh and eager for more. One leaves thrilled by the sheer originality and unabashed modernity of this culinary adventure.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
542;René et Maxime Meilleur;France;Saint-Martin-de-Belleville;Hameau de Saint-Marcel, Saint-Martin-de-Belleville, 73440, France;45.3690463;6.5133065;81;false;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Father René and son Maxime shine the spotlight on their mountain terroir as they lovingly craft each ingredient, while seeking inspired new ways of preparing regional delicacies. Cheese, fish from the lake as well as herbs and berries that René picks daily are at the core of their “intelligent”, legible cuisine. An entirely family affair, mum, daughter, daughter- and son-in-law all play a role too, waiting on tables or in the back office. Finally, should you wish to spend the night, book yourself into the chalet next-door and snuggle up in the exquisitely chic alpine-styled rooms and suites.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
543;Le Parc Les Crayères;France;Reims;64 boulevard Henry-Vasnier, Reims, 51100, France;49.2410909;4.0517461;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This mansion standing in superb grounds was once the property of Louise Pommery. In the hands of interior designer Pierre-Yves Rochon, the classical elegance of this small early-20C château has been elevated. Chef Christophe Moret, who has worked with some of the greatest chefs in the world (eg Alain Ducasse, Bruno Cirino, Jacques Maximin) immediately found the alchemy to suit this beautiful house down to the ground. Using top-notch ingredients, he creates refined, accessible dishes that are as generous as they are delicious – for instance, turbot cooked until golden, buckwheat, marine plants, seared squid and Oscietra-infused fermented milk. Rosalie Boucher's desserts are cleverly devised for lightness – just look at her strawberry-based creation. These gems feature on the various menus, but also – an increasingly rare pleasure – on the à la carte menu. The wine list features close to 900 champagnes. Superb guestrooms and suites.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
544;Le Skiff Club;France;Pyla-sur-Mer;Hôtel Ha(a)ïtza, 1 avenue Louis-Gaume, Pyla-sur-Mer, 33115, France;44.606014;-1.20669;71;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this 1930s Basque hotel nestled in a pine forest and redesigned by Philippe Starck, Le Skiff Club restaurant is a veritable haven with its cosy little dining area decorated in the style of a yacht club. Stéphane Carrade is a talented and skilled captain, cooking up delightful "progressive terroir" cuisine, in a superb celebration of the Aquitaine region of southwest France. This is a chef who combines generosity and finesse in dishes such as courgette flower stuffed with duxelles and spider crab, green crab soup with pain d'épice, and blue lobster grilled over wood from Bordeaux wine barriques, aubergine with chanterelles and bone marrow, Ha(a)ïtza sauce. Finally, Alexandre Blay's desserts keep all the promises this restaurant makes: his work with chocolate – cf. his confit of barbecued prunes and Biscarrosse black garlic with port, warm ganache and ice cream with hints of liquorice – combines finesse and originality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
545;Blue Bay Marcel Ravin;France;Monaco;40 avenue Princesse-Grace, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7488966;7.4379746;60;true;false;Creative;After moving from Martinique to Monaco and from Alsace to Belgium, Marcel Ravin, who exhibits a distinct culinary personality, signs off on creative cuisine that transports us to the West Indies. With flawless technical prowess (superb sauces), he recounts his personal history, including his happy youth spent in Martinique. He references the dishes cooked by his grandmother (calalou, blaff, "next day's bread"), which he reinterprets with panache, incorporating the fine ingredients of these parts: poultry and veal from Piedmont, fish from the Mediterranean, vegetables and aromatic herbs from the kitchen garden. An appealing cuisine bursting with West Indian flavours, nicely rounded off by the fruity and spicy creations of pastry chef Floriane Grand. Sit back and enjoy this culinary experience in the lavish setting of the Monte Carlo Bay Hotel and Resort, on the edge of the Larvotto Peninsula, with a superb terrace opening out onto the sea.;Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
546;Takao Takano;France;Lyon;33 rue Malesherbes, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7704797;4.842588;45;true;false;Creative;One cannot help but be impressed by the trajectory of Takao Takano's career. Originally from Yamanashi Prefecture, Japan, he quickly dropped his law studies to devote himself body and soul to his real passion: cooking. Since 2013, he has been plying his trade in this elegant, pared-back restaurant located in the 6th district of Lyon. It has been a hit with diners since day one thanks to original, deftly crafted dishes, which delight and surprise at the same time. They certainly fulfil the chef’s pledge to himself: "Keep it simple – keep it good". Let's linger for a moment over the quickly seared Breton langoustine, melt-in-the-mouth turnip greens and smoked eel or Bresse squab paired with green asparagus, guanciale and Vaucluse truffle... Intelligently devised recipes and deliciously balanced flavours: that's Takao Takano down to a T.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
547;La Table de Pavie;France;Saint-Emilion;5 place du Clocher, Saint-Emilion, 33330, France;44.8934495;-0.1566263;61;true;false;Creative;In the world-famous village of Saint Émilion, Yannick Alléno rigorously supervises the restaurant of this luxury hotel, a former convent whose nuns offered sanctuary to pilgrims and travellers. Alléno has recruited Sébastien Faramond and a trusted team, who turn out finely tuned dishes that lean towards the terroir of Southwest France, albeit with the sauces and reductions that are the trademark and signature of executive chef Alléno. The starter, almost but not quite vegetarian thanks to wafer-thin shavings of Gascony bacon, invites the diner to explore Aquitaine’s culinary cornucopia, while the dessert, a warm chocolate tart, Maury-flavoured sauce and an ice cream perfumed with Tahitian vanilla, signed Sébastien Nabaille, is wickedly tempting. Needless to say, the superb wines of Saint-Émilion will play a prominent role in your meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
548;Maison Ronan Kervarrec;France;Saint-Grégoire;1 impasse du Vieux-Bourg, Saint-Grégoire, 35760, France;48.1533015;-1.6805561;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A vibrant, indulgent homage to the Brittany he knows and loves! Thriving in his native region, Ronan Kervarrec eschews trends in a bid to tell his personal and professional story through food. The culinary tale he conjures up here features buckwheat, buttermilk, fish, shellfish, butter, seaweed, gavotte (a thin, crispy pancake), chouchen (a local form of mead) and sablé breton. In tribute to his father, who was a saucier at the George V, the chef expertly executes a range of jus and sauces, which vary from intense to subtly flavoured. Floor to ceiling windows give onto a terrace overlooking the pretty garden. Very professional welcome and service from the chef's wife and her team. Guestrooms for overnight stays and a small delicatessen where you can purchase gourmet souvenirs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
551;Relais de la Poste;France;Magescq;24 avenue de Maremne, Magescq, 40140, France;43.7787343;-1.2179647;85;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The Coussau family are champions of classicism. Chef, Jean, and his niece, Clémentine, conjure up heart-warming food that pays tribute to the splendid produce of les Landes: foie gras, poultry, Chalosse beef, salmon from the Adour River and fish from Capbreton. A closeknit network of local suppliers enable them to rustle up signature dishes that the regulars come here in droves to sample: scrambled eggs with black truffles, warm duck foie gras with raisins and sole with cèpes. In autumn, you may sample roast woodpigeon or hare à la royale, without forgetting a superbly airy and creamy Grand Marnier soufflé, filled with a refreshing sorbet of bloody orange. Fine French dining at its best in a knockout location between the Atlantic Ocean and pine forests.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
552;Mère Brazier;France;Lyon;12 rue Royale, Lyon, 69001, France;45.7714309;4.8372034;22;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Eugénie Brazier (1895-1977), an exceptional chef who inspired an entire branch of French cuisine, obtained three stars in two different establishments. It is in her Lyon restaurant, on rue Royale, that Mathieu Viannay gives his take on the Brazier "legend". In a magnificent hybrid decor, 1930s stained glass windows and mouldings are blended with Saarinen Tulip chairs (a bold design move!) and the chef pays a vibrant tribute to the iconic dishes once served on the premises (Bresse chicken with truffles, crispy pike bread, a stunning Grand Marnier soufflé), infusing them with his talent and novel ideas. Be sure to try the lunch menu, which represents the best value for money. When it comes to dessert, pastry chef Rodolphe Tronc, who has worked for Pierre Gagnaire among others, takes no prisoners with his remarkable technique and his eye for detail, especially when it comes to his delightfully old-fashioned Norwegian omelette.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
553;Christopher Coutanceau;France;La Rochelle;Plage de la Concurrence, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1553629;-1.1599181;91;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;On the Plage de la Concurrence, the sign on the front of the restaurant leaves you in no doubt as to what to expect: "Christopher Coutanceau, cook and fisherman". Fishing is a passion that has long been passed down through the family – his grandfather, then his father Richard, were devotees of seafood ingredients. Christopher takes it one step further: in addition to being an experienced fisherman, he is an advocate for sustainable fishing and a campaigner against waste. His cuisine is true to his convictions – a bouquet of marine scents, an ode to the ocean. Premium fish and seafood, such as turbot, sole and sea urchins, are prepared with the same tenderness and imagination as modest young mackerel and sardines, which the chef elevates with the same devotion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
555;Le Neuvième Art;France;Lyon;173 rue Cuvier, Lyon, 69006, France;45.767953;4.8564194;85;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;It was in the kitchens of Paul Bocuse and Régis Marcon, among others, that Christophe Roure learned the ropes. He holds three professional qualifications (in cookery, charcuterie and pastry-making, no less!) and was named Meilleur Ouvrier de France in 2007. Based in Lyon since 2014, he showcases his qualities as a chef day in, day out: subtle inventiveness, precision in his marriages of flavours, and of course an impeccable choice of ingredients. For example, his shellfish and miller mushroom ragoût is a marvel of balance and finesse, in which the lemongrass-scented hollandaise sauce teases out the seafood flavours and undergrowth notes of the mushroom. To be savoured with all of one's senses.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
556;William Frachot;France;Dijon;Hostellerie du Chapeau Rouge, 5 rue Michelet, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3212722;5.0356396;96;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This 19C former coaching inn bang in the heart of historic Dijon is the HQ of one of Burgundy’s most talented chefs. A local lad and son of restaurateurs, William Frachot, who is something of a globetrotter (England, Quebec), devises stripped-back dishes in his own image: serious and applied, juggling international flavours and regional produce. He adds just the right dose of inventiveness and energy, illustrated by his new take on eggs meurette and his steadfast commitment to freshwater fish (perch, black bass, pike, zander) depicted by brook trout, zander and river fish soup. Meals are served in a distinctive interior featuring light wood cladding, grape vine motifs and mustard yellow swivel Shark chairs - each design choice is a nod to Burgundy's heritage. Inspired and accomplished cuisine peppered with influences from near and far.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
557;Cyril Attrazic;France;Aumont-Aubrac;10 route du Languedoc, Aumont-Aubrac, 48130, France;44.7169426;3.2877885;31;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;To quote Cyril Attrazic: “I was in love with the Maison, even before I fell for cooking”. To explain, the Maison is the family hotel restaurant business founded by his grandmother in the heart of Aubrac, a high-altitude plateau that could be mistaken for the Mongolian Steppes. By virtue of farming traditions and the harsh climate, the restaurant doesn’t mess about with hospitality, albeit in a modern vein. The chef scrupulously applies the advice of his mentor, Michel Bras: only cook local ingredients (…) with an identity. He does just this, showcasing a giant cèpe picked in the next-door woods or the legendary Aubrac beef rich in the flavour of a thousand flowers, all of which is served in “his ecosystem”. It would be difficult to find anywhere better to taste and smell Lozère.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
558;Le Chabichou by Stéphane Buron;France;Courchevel;90 rue des Chenus, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.41616;6.629984;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Stéphane Buron, a well-established chef and Meilleur Ouvrier de France in 2004, faithfully perpetuates the heritage of this institution: premium ingredients prepared in time-honoured tradition, a repertoire full of finesse and welcome variations on the classics... fine work! Nowadays they serve a single set menu of five to nine courses that highlights the ingredients of the region, down to the trolley decked with fine mountain cheeses. As for the decor, the interior exudes a hushed elegance: carpeting, coffered ceiling, comfortable immaculate-white designer chairs, modern tables with smoked glass tops. On top of that, charming service and a great wine list.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
559;La Table de Franck Putelat;France;Carcassonne;80 chemin des Anglais, au Sud de la Cité, Carcassonne, 11000, France;43.2013363;2.3603104;68;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The fortified Cité Médiévale is part of the time-honoured heritage of Carcassonne and its region… and the same could almost be said of Franck Putelat. In his place at the foot of the ramparts of the medieval town, this native of the Jura, who has made the Aude département his home, cooks the produce from his large (one hectare) vegetable garden, in line with his culinary concept of "classic-fiction". This translates into a clever rendering of the old gourmet hits, which the chef revisits according to what inspires him on that day. Three examples that have become iconic are his parmentier with sea fig, cassoulet with pigeon supreme and pigeon leg sausage, and bouillabaisse with duck foie gras. Appetising visuals, flavour and finesse, to be savoured in a lively atmosphere, in the company of a very diverse clientele. Pastry chef Alexis Pocinho crafts a particularly balanced selection of sweets. There are seven rooms available for overnight guests.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
560;Christophe Hay - Fleur de Loire;France;Blois;26 quai Villebois-Mareuil, Blois, 41000, France;47.5823386;1.3378048;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Chef Christophe Hay is now installed in a grandiose 17C hospice on the banks of the Loire. The centuries-old stone edifice overlooks the river, from which the chef draws all his inspiration. Caroline Tissier, interior designer, was entrusted with recreating his universe in this splendid hotel, that also boasts a brasserie, a pastry shop and a spa. In a modern room decked in premium materials, the chef rolls out his creative fine dining skills and iconic dishes, which are remarkable not only for their lightness, but also flavour and texture. He is determined to highlight the best ingredients from the Loire Valley, fish (exclusively) from the Loire, caught by his “appointed” fisherman, veg from his own kitchen garden as well as from local market gardeners, meat from his Wagyu farm, Ossetra caviar from Sologne…;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
561;Le Coquillage;France;Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes;Lieu-dit Le Buot, Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes, 35350, France;48.6430654;-1.8711232;97;true;true;Seafood, Creative;Hugo Roellinger began his career as an officer in the Merchant Navy, before returning to dry land in France… and to cooking, a passion that he has nurtured since childhood. He trained with the crème de la crème of the chef world, patiently refining his art. Today his dishes are a testament to the forging of a true culinary personality. He is now at the helm of the family ship (a château magnificently perched over the Bay of Mont Saint Michel), where he demonstrates astounding conviction and a deep-rooted sense of modesty. In the dishes, home-grown aromatic herbs and vegetables as well as fish (and shellfish) caught in the Bay of Mont Saint Michel mingle with numerous spices from further afield, in the greatest Saint-Malo tradition. The emotion rises to a crescendo over the course of the meal, thanks to a bewitching interplay of flavours and masterful creativity.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
562;La Table de Yoann Conte;France;Veyrier-du-Lac;13 vieille route des Pensières, Veyrier-du-Lac, 74290, France;45.8889235;6.1721868;21;false;true;Creative;Breton chef Yoann Conte discovered the meaning of brotherhood and the importance of food on the high seas. He champions the art of mixing unpolished, straightforward dishes with the exclusive world of fine dining. An extreme hiker in his spare time, his lakeside garden benefits from his herbalist know-how. His cooking is in his likeness: physical, down-to-earth, adventurous and wryly humorous. Supported by a highly motivated team and often to be found doing the rounds in the dining room, he creates menus that combine his farming roots, globetrotting career and Breton heritage, culminating in the “Ultimate Synthesis” menu! The food and wine pairings, intelligently chosen by the chef and his sommelier, are emblematic of the establishment’s sustainable ethos. Eleven lovely guestrooms overlooking the lake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
564;Casadelmar;France;Porto-Vecchio;Route de Palombaggia, Porto-Vecchio, 20137, France;41.5948102;9.3099771;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Here in Porto Vecchio, everything revolves around the sea. The ancient Genoese city fought off the onslaught of barbarian invasions and is a symbol of pride for Corsicans. Another source of pride is this restaurant: a mecca for lovers of seafood. Don't be distracted by the enchanting view of the bay, nor by the location of this superb hotel – it is on the plate that the most remarkable things happen! Chef Fabio Bragagnolo's cooking is inspired by both Corsica and Italy, eg roast loin of Corsican pork (porcu nustrale) with rosemary, fermented plums and carrots, and hazelnuts from Cervione, an intoxicating dish that smacks of the local terroir. Meticulous from start to finish, the meal culminates in delicate low-sugar desserts, such as bitter orange and Grand Marnier soufflé, a symphony of orange flavours on the palate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
565;La Villa Archange;France;Le Cannet;Rue de l'Ouest, Le Cannet, 06110, France;43.5716556;7.014556;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A cosy little venue with old wooden floorboards and big comfy armchairs – the ideal setting to sample chef Bruno Oger's cuisine. Breton by birth, he has adopted the Mediterranean as his home, and now concocts inspired seafood dishes drawn from Brittany and the French Riviera… Abalone from the island of Groix seared with artichokes rubs shoulders with Brittany lobster, followed by a lemon dessert of citrus fruits, bloody orange sorbet and olive oil. A table d'hôte in the kitchen provides the opportunity to glean insights into the culinary process. Also the official chef of the Cannes Film Festival, Bruno Oger has cooked for many an A-lister: Uma Thurman, Robert De Niro and Audrey Tautou... Confirmation, if any were needed, of his credentials.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
567;Rùn;;Hong Kong;2F, The St. Regis Hotel, 1 Harbour Drive, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2801399;114.175716;31;true;true;Cantonese;Chef Hung has worked in many 5-star hotels and values food quality and shrewd techniques more than anything else. Seasonal ingredients from around the world are painstakingly prepared the traditional way and then plated with modern refinement. Wok-fried crab claw with dried shrimps, spring onion and layered bean curd sheet is exquisitely presented and loaded with umami. The wine and tea sommeliers, as well as the professional service team, make for a pleasant experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
568;The Eight;;Macau;2F, Grand Lisboa Hotel, Avenida de Lisboa, Macau, Macau;22.190475;113.54341;61;false;false;Cantonese;The lavish interior sports goldfish motifs and the number eight to wish diners good fortune. The menu is traditional Cantonese starring intelligently and crisply crafted quality ingredients. The head chef adds a new spin to familiar dishes with imported produce like Japanese chillies, carabineros from Argentina, and lobster from Australia – try the Cantonese-style sautéed lobster. The lunchtime menu offers over 40 kinds of dim sum.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
569;Amber;;Hong Kong;7F, The Landmark Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 15 Queen's Road Central, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2805311;114.1577065;89;true;true;French Contemporary;Dutch-born chef Richard Ekkebus's restaurant has undergone a radical revamp. The bright space is characterised by organic curves, luxury materials and a gold and beige colour palette. As opposed to the à la carte of the past, it now serves only prix-fixe menus, one of which is vegetarian, dairy- and gluten-free with reduced salt and sugar. Top-notch ingredients are sourced globally and crafted into light and delicate creations with a modern touch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
570;L'Envol;;Hong Kong;3F, The St. Regis Hotel, 1 Harbour Drive, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2799005;114.1761315;25;true;false;French Contemporary;Managed by Chef Olivier Elzer, L’Envol is elegantly furnished in marble and wood. Shrewdly prepared, artfully plated dishes coupled with thoughtful service capture the quintessence of French fine dining. Only set menus are offered and they change from time to time – and usually have a seafood focus, featuring courses like Hokkaido sea urchin box, or ‘la langoustine de Loctudy’. Many wine choices are not found elsewhere and can be ordered by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
571;Feng Wei Ju;;Macau;5F, StarWorld Hotel, Avenida da Amizade, Macau, Macau;22.189952;113.5479285;91;true;true;Hunanese, Sichuan;The opulent room is covered in gold and red, the festive colours for the Chinese. The menu offers Sichuan classics, such as sautéed chicken with peanuts and chilli, and Hunanese fare like steamed carp fish head with chilli. Hand-pulled noodles are also worth trying – watching the chefs pulling them in the display kitchen adds to the entertainment. Boiled mandarin fish fillets in chilli oil comes in portions generous enough for a few to share.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
572;Tin Lung Heen;;Hong Kong;102F, The Ritz-Carlton, International Commerce Centre, 1 Austin Road West, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3032802;114.1598747;43;false;true;Cantonese;Aptly named ‘sky dragon pavilion’ in Chinese, this grand restaurant perched on the 102nd floor of a skyscraper is furnished generously in red wood veneer. The vast windows flood the room with natural light and make it a good spot to see the sunset or the city’s nightscape. Among the signature dishes are honey-glazed Iberian pork char siu (pre-ordering needed), and double-boiled chicken soup with fish maw in coconut. Private rooms are also charming.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
573;Tate;;Hong Kong;210 Hollywood Road, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.2855757;114.1477192;85;true;false;Innovative;Owner-chef Vicky Lau tells edible stories with an 8-course tasting menu that treads the boundary between French and Chinese cooking in a feminine, sophisticated way. Each dish is an ode to an ingredient, such as Spanish sea perch, local three-yellow chicken or Australian Wagyu. Wine flights are predominantly French – but also consider sake. A shorter and substantially different 6-course menu is served at lunch on Fridays and Saturdays.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
574;Ying Jee Club;;Hong Kong;Shop G05, 107-108, GF & 1F, Nexxus Building, 41 Connaught Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.284338;114.156654;68;false;true;Cantonese;Rather than gimmicky promotions, the owner prefers to divert his energy and resources into finding quality ingredients and honing the chefs’ skills. The tasteful, modern room adorned with marble tables, velvet seats and metallic trim primes the diners for Cantonese classics re-created with finesse. Crispy salted chicken is silky and tender without being overly oily while stir-fried lobster with shallot and scallion boasts juicy meat in thin crisp crust.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
575;The Huaiyang Garden;;Macau;Shop 2206a & 2208, 2F, The Londoner, Estrada do Istmo, Cotai, Macau;22.1458883;113.5652198;40;false;false;Huaiyang;The room has a Jiangnan garden theme, with perforated screens imitating patterned windows commonly seen in Suzhou architecture. Helmed by the renowned culinary master Chef Zhou, the kitchen team excels in sophisticated Huaiyang fare incorporating fresh river fish shipped from the region twice a week, such as stir-fried shrimps with roe and tomalley, or Liangxi-style crispy eel. Dingsheng cake with date filling is a great way to end your meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
577;Alain Ducasse at Morpheus;;Macau;3F, Morpheus, City of Dreams, Estrada do Istmo, Cotai, Macau;22.1501736;113.5669767;80;false;true;French Contemporary;Water, glass and mood lighting are combined dramatically to create a unique space that is both stylish and intimate, as befits its striking host hotel. The 6-course signature menu can be broken down with a minimum of 3 courses. Every dish is the quintessence of flavour, balance and high-flying gourmet technique. Those familiar with other restaurants headed by renowned French chef Alain Ducasse around the world will recognise his inimitable hallmark.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
578;Bo Innovation;;Hong Kong;1F, H Code, 45 Pottinger Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2823708;114.154711;52;false;false;Innovative;In 2022, owner-chef Alvin Leung moved his highly acclaimed restaurant to this new spot. Just like the art that exudes local flavours, his playful creations are a nod to the Hong Kong food culture. The only tasting menu served at dinner is also inspired by Chinese elements and famous paintings like Andy Warhol’s Campbell’s Soup Cans. Pleasant surprises, bespoke serving vessels and theatrical presentation make for a fun-filled, immersive experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
579;Noi by Paulo Airaudo;;Hong Kong;5F, Four Seasons Hotel, 8 Finance Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.286618;114.1566761;28;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Chefs Airaudo and Troiano deliver a season-driven omakase menu that changes every two to three months. The 10+ courses prominently feature seafood shipped daily from Japan, as in the signature dish of Hokkaido red uni on egg custard. Blue lobster is painstakingly prepared and chargrilled to perfection. The food nods to Italian traditions, updated with a modern aesthetic and the latest techniques. Excellent wine pairings elevate the whole experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
580;Wing Lei;;Macau;GF, Wynn Hotel, Rua Cidade de Sintra, NAPE, Macau, Macau;22.188028;113.54578;67;false;true;Cantonese;Equally suited to power lunches and friendly get-togethers, this strikingly lavish restaurant dominated by a frosted crystal flying dragon offers far more than just a treat for the eye. Cantonese classics and dim sum crafted with top-notch ingredients are what keep diners coming back. Besides the main menu, ask about their seasonal dishes such as clay pot rice and Dongshan goat in winter. Thoughtful service adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
581;Lai Ching Heen;;Hong Kong;GF, Regent, 18 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.293337;114.17395;82;true;true;Cantonese;Remodelled and renamed Lai Ching Heen in 2022, the main dining room can now be accessed straight from the hotel lobby. In addition to the updated décor, expansive harbour views and Hong Kong’s skyline with its electric glow remain a joy to behold. Onto the menu, all-time favourites like stuffed crab shell with crabmeat, and crispy Lung Kong chicken are still offered. Don’t miss the dim sum lunch with exquisitely crafted bite-sized morsels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
583;Octavium;;Hong Kong;8F, One Chinachem Central, 22 Des Voeux Road Central,  Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2825493;114.1571177;52;false;true;Italian;The smart minimalist dining room dotted in Italian furniture provides the perfect foil for elegant Italian classics, whose flawless craftsmanship showcases the head chef’s Sicilian roots and premium Japanese produce. To experience his culinary vision in all its glory, go for the 6- or 8-course tasting menu that changes regularly to reflect the seasons. The house-made pasta, like red prawn spaghetti, is simply unmissable!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
584;The Yeatman;Portugal;Vila Nova de Gaia;Rua do Choupelo (Santa Marinha), Vila Nova de Gaia, 4400-088, Portugal;41.1336845;-8.6133869;76;true;false;Creative;Everyone knows that the city of Oporto has a timeless, almost magical charm, but not everyone is aware that one of the best places to experience this is on the opposite side of the River Douro in Vila Nova de Gaia.Here, chef Ricardo Costa conjures up his creative cuisine on a single tasting menu which starts with drinks and appetisers in the bar and kitchen and is based around two key pillars: traditional Portuguese cuisine (with a nod to the chef’s home town of Aveiro), and premium seasonal ingredients which are always treated with the greatest of delicacy. It also features several panoramic dining spaces: the main dining room with its large picture windows and, above all, the spectacular terrace, which overlooks the most beautiful parts of the city. The wine cellar is one of the best in Portugal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
586;Antiqvvm;Portugal;Porto;Rua de Entre Quintas 220, Porto, 4050-240, Portugal;41.14776;-8.62831;59;true;false;Creative;There are places in the world that, because of their location, exert a special power of attraction and this is definitely the case with Antiqvvm, situated in a leafy park in the centre of Porto, next to the Museu Romântico. This sensation is enhanced by its pleasant garden boasting idyllic views of the banks of the Douro!In its elegant dining rooms, tastefully embellished with classic and contemporary decorative detail, chef Vítor Matos has a fondness for creative seasonal cuisine that places huge emphasis on his ingredients, combining these in a way that aims to enhance the main component of each dish (we particularly enjoyed the blue lobster with Moqueca, and the Silken & Smooth Tofu Mount Fuji, with chilli, citrus fruit, mango and curry). In his own words, the chef, who finds inspiration from his surroundings, “is continually striving to promote the values of cuisine that is cultural, natural, evolving, social and artistic”. He offers just two tasting menus: Sensory Moments (the Imperial Anjou Pigeon was our favourite dish) and Organic (vegetarian).;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
587;Ocean;Portugal;Porches;Rua Anneliese Pohl, Porches, 8400-450, Portugal;37.1008268;-8.3792041;50;true;false;Creative;A very special restaurant with all the key ingredients to ensure an experience that will live long in the memory. The entrance, embellished with striking Murano glass, provides a sense of the theatrical before heading into the dining room, which is decorated in an elegant array of golden, white and blue tones. Its impressive windows, which open out towards the coast and infinite Atlantic vistas, are equally striking. Austrian-born chef Hans Neuner adds influences gained by his annual travels as well as those undertaken by the Portuguese during the “Age of Discoveries”. Via his cuisine, the chef takes us on a journey to the Asian continent with his “Expedition to Asia” menu, which combines Portuguese flavours with the spices, textures and freshness of Asian cuisine. Prime examples are the kimchi served with quail in its own jus, and the traditional soup with dumplings and tofu – both of which offer the perfect combination of flavour and texture. It’s well worth casting a keen eye over the wine list, which is truly exceptional.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
589;Belcanto;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Serpa Pinto 10A, Lisbon, 1200-026, Portugal;38.7104102;-9.1415741;83;false;false;Creative, Portuguese;Belcanto boasts a superb location in the Bairro Alto (Chiado) district popular with tourists, on a corner close to a former convent damaged by the large earthquake that devastated the city in 1755. In his culinary empire’s showcase gourmet restaurant, chef José Avillez offers a modern à la carte and a single tasting menu entitled Belcanto that takes guests on a journey of gastronomic discovery in a dining room divided into different spaces, alongside a chef’s table in the kitchen. Avillez explains that all his dishes are influenced by Lisbon’s different light, its maritime shoreline and its distinct districts: in the words of this celebrated chef, “cooking is our very own fado, and our own form of expression”. He recreates recipes that recall our childhood memories, such as the classic “grandmother’s rice pudding” (arroz-doce da nossa avó), which boasts a sublime delicacy and a truly special flavour. Interestingly, the napkin provided for dessert is in the shape of a sleeve, recalling the way the chef once wiped his mouth on his sleeve as a child!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
590;Casa de Chá da Boa Nova;Portugal;Leça da Palmeira;Avenida da Liberdade, Leça da Palmeira, 4450-705, Portugal;41.2027411;-8.7147233;36;true;true;Seafood;Rarely is the concept of “bringing the sea to your table” more apt or authentic than at this restaurant where the waves almost break in the dining room! In this unique and spectacular building (an officially listed national monument) standing on the rocks above the Praia da Boa Nova, chef Rui Paula presents cuisine inspired by a verse (“Hitherto unchartered waters”) by famous Portuguese poet Luís Vaz de Camões in his most celebrated work, The Lusiads. This is showcased on a concise, impressive and well-structured tasting menu entitled Cantos, which can be ordered with 6, 12 or 21 dishes. His cuisine, which is centred around the maritime world and which always makes full use of truly exceptional ingredients (Roja Prawn/Broccoli/Kaffir Lime, Squid "Chanel", John Dory/Razor clam/Quinoa), has a strong focus on presentation, texture and flavour, as well as contemporary techniques that extract the maximum from the extraordinary fish and seafood from the Atlantic. When time allows, the chef also enjoys mixing with his guests in the dining room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
591;Il Gallo d'Oro;Portugal;Funchal;Estrada Monumental 147, Funchal, 9004-532, Portugal;32.6382988;-16.9266478;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Madeira is often called “paradise on Earth” and the “pearl of the Atlantic”, apt descriptions which are enhanced by a meal at Il Gallo d’Oro, the island’s very own culinary Eden. Here, French chef Benoît Sinthon conjures up fresh, delicious and creative cuisine that showcases the full flavours of the Atlantic, both from the island and its surrounding waters (Atlantic Inspiration, From Our Sea, Mackerel by Benoît Sinthon, From Valley to Mountain etc), reviving old recipes and reinterpreting them through the use of contemporary techniques and ingredients that support his quest for sustainability (many of which are sourced from the PortoBay organic garden). Two tasting menus are available here: Terroir Experience (which champions ingredients from the island itself) and Il Gallo d’Oro Top Experience (that showcases ingredients from different regions around Europe).To make your experience even more special, why not book the chef’s table or dine on the terrace with its idyllic views?;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
592;Ma Langue Sourit;Luxembourg;Oetrange;1 rue Remich, Oetrange, 5331, Luxembourg;49.5978074;6.2493973;16;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Wholehearted and dedicated, Cyril Molard aims to ensure that the diner enjoys their meal as much as a child devouring an ice cream! Every detail has been endlessly pondered over and then fine-tuned in this cosy, trendy establishment. Creative side dishes set out to showcase the flavours of outstanding produce. The chef may add whoomph to a dish with subtle additions of tangy acidity. When he cooks asparagus, you can be certain it will be the best you have ever tasted. The fish is cooked to perfection and the succulent side dishes are paired with sauces that err towards the classical in a bid to shine the spotlight on the main ingredient. Examples include a succulent fish stock made with red wine that accompanies a pithiviers (puff pastry pie) filled with ultra-fresh scallops and aromatic truffles – a match made in heaven! Molard and his team occasionally pop out to the dining room to see how diners our enjoying their meal and to chat with them in a casual, good-natured vibe. Apparently sticking your tongue out is an insider code that means you’re enjoying the meal!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
593;L'Eau Vive;Belgium;Arbre;route de Floreffe 37, Arbre, 5170, Belgium;50.3636851;4.8469885;92;false;true;Modern French, Modern Cuisine;Imagine a romantic dinner on a lush green terrace with the soft murmur of running water in the background! The dining room and the chef’s table right in the kitchen of this former 17C mill are also steeped in character and popular. Everything revolves around the diner in this establishment which is the epitome of friendly. The talent of Pierre Résimont shines through in a lineup of familiar flavours to which he adds an inventive spin depicted by delicate craftsmanship and generosity. Examples include pie of pigeon breast and foie gras, immaculately baked to a golden crisp. Three different seasonings, among which miso and curry, underscore the depth and flavour of cauliflower. The powerful black truffle flavoured pigeon gravy is emblematic of his rich, generous cuisine. Rather than showy gimmicks, he prefers to regale diners quietly with food throbbing with flavour. Pierre is a consummate chef who knows how to pamper his guests. We recommend extending your stay in one of the establishment’s guestrooms.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
594;Hertog Jan at Botanic;Belgium;Antwerpen;Leopoldstraat 26, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2145635;4.4054987;26;false;false;Creative, Asian Influences;A meal by Gert De Mangeleer and sommelier Joachim Bouden is in a class of its own. First the swish Botanic Sanctuary Hotel, which immerses you in a world unlike any other. Concrete and muted shades of grey set the scene in the intimate restaurant which boasts a breathtaking architectural backdrop. In a bid to maintain the element of surprise, the establishment asks guests not to post photos on social media, so we won’t dwell on the amazing chef’s table where diners are invited to admire the chef at work first hand either. Suffice it to say that chef De Mangeleer’s love affair with Asia grows more pronounced over time. Knife-edged precision and boundless creativity remain the hallmark of this chef, who painstakingly pairs daring combinations of ingredients. For example, he may flank langoustine with passion fruit, vanilla oil, cocoa and an exquisite shellfish jus. The chef’s talent shines through in his flair for culinary sophistication and unorthodox ideas that enhance the taste and flavour of each ingredient, as he reinvents textbook techniques and jazzes up pedigree recipes with his inimitable stamp. A truly unforgettable experience, whose memory will linger long in our minds.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
595;La Villa Lorraine by Yves Mattagne;Belgium;Brussels;Avenue du Vivier d'Oie 75, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.7995831;4.3784982;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Villa Lorraine is the type of swish cosmopolitan establishment that would be quite at home in London or Paris. It features a variety of settings, including the Lounge Bar which offers a range of dishes to share in a casual vibe, many of which are Asian in inspiration, such as gyoza of lobster or a red tuna “filet américain”. It is a pleasure to watch the final touches being added to each plate on the elegant counter. A real tree catches the eye in the luxurious, urbane Restaurant, which oozes designer style. Seasoned chef, Yves Mattagne reveals his passion for noble produce like turbot and Anjou pigeon, combining his classical background with meticulous craftsmanship and a sprinkling of modern touches. For example, slow-cooked partridge presented and flambeed at the table, before being carved and plated in the kitchen. The result is an exquisite festival of wintry delights: tender, juicy meat, a meaty jus with lashings of butter, earthy girolle mushrooms, gutsy dried raisins and the final flourish of flambeed cognac. A significant proportion of the menu is prepared or finished at the table (the Sea Grill’s lobster press has found its way to the Villa), further adding to the fascinating experience, as do the attentive service and knockout wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
597;Bozar Restaurant;Belgium;Brussels;rue Baron Horta 3, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8442362;4.3598358;42;true;false;Modern French, Creative;Karen Torosyan is a genuine craftsman and an enthusiastic chef who, whilst respecting tradition, has developed his own culinary signature. In the company of his executive cheffe, Cassandre Ercolini, he raises ancestral culinary techniques to the rank of art. It is impossible not to be enthralled by his calm, high-precision gestures as he appropriates the mythical pâté en croûte and pithiviers recipe (by reservation only). This perfectionist seeks to communicate his emotions with each dish.His puff pastry creations are presented to the diner before going into the oven in this inclusive experience. Each bite is a moment of sheer bliss from the rich, crunchy pastry to the unctuous filling (for example, sweetbread, foie gras, Corrèze veal, cabbage and black trumpet mushrooms), further underscored by a harmonious jus. Searingly good food! Subtle interpretations that revive the classics of French and Belgian cuisine. Chef Torosyan aims for delicacy and reaches dizzying heights of intensity.Each dish is a masterpiece of artistry, with no detail left to chance, which is also the case of the interior. This magnificent restaurant is emblematic of Victor Horta’s Art nouveau architecture. Karen Torosyan has found his place at Bozar.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
598;Slagmolen;Belgium;Opglabbeek;Molenweg 177, Opglabbeek, 3660, Belgium;51.0431658;5.6159232;78;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, French;The charm of this authentic watermill, whose machinery is visible inside, is flanked by a modern “barn”, which sports immense windows overlooking the stunning natural countryside. In addition to a peaceful terrace, the establishment boasts four deluxe rooms to prolong the evening in style. A marriage of old and new also characterises the food. The styles of dad, Bert, and Giel, his son, have been merged and are gathering momentum. Family favourites such as lobster and a dame blanche dessert (with vanilla ice cream prepared on the spot) remain firm fixtures on the menu, complete with traditional techniques and lashings of generosity. However, the younger generation is adding a distinctive whiff of modernity to the plating and through subtle details that underscore and highlight contrasting flavours, whilst losing none of the establishment’s hallmark delicacy or generosity. Heaven for discerning foodies with healthy appetites.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
599;L'air du temps;Belgium;Liernu;rue de la Croix Monet 2, Liernu, 5310, Belgium;50.5927328;4.8329862;41;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;L'Air du Temps is a universe all of its own and the square farmstead tucked away in the Namur countryside is a picture of present-day elegance. The stripped-back edifice blends in perfectly with the surrounding landscape and Sang Hoon Degeimbre’s immense cottage garden, where he finds much of his inspiration. A champion of the natural world, his culinary repertory is rich in novelty and coloured by his Korean roots. Fermentation and acidity are a common theme of his intricate recipes, as is his habit of serving each course in several small plates. For example, he may underscore courgette with salty anchovy and dashi, further pairing it with kimchi and a subtle lacto-fermented sauce. Each mouthful reveals a fascinating creative quest driven by chef Degeimbre’s philosophy, as the water menu so aptly illustrates. In this restaurant, the zeitgeist is expressed in its purest form. For an entirely global experience, treat yourself to a night in one of the tastefully appointed elegant guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
600;Nuance;Belgium;Duffel;Kiliaanstraat 8, Duffel, 2570, Belgium;51.0957136;4.505835;43;true;true;Creative;Thierry Theys’ cuisine is the pinnacle of “nuanced”. Despite his youth, he has already made a name for himself on the Belgian gastronomic scene and owes his reputation to his highly individual recipes. Right from the very first bite, he unveils his high-flying precision and technical craftsmanship. Not afraid of challenges, each dish is rich in emotion. For example, he may prepare langoustine with a pop-corn crust, served with red beetroot, sumac and a beurre blanc. He adds a new dimension to a perfectly pink loin of hare served with a champagne beurre blanc. This chef knows how to nurture and draw out the distinctive character of outstanding ingredients, down to the tiniest detail. Suave, delicate food that suits our modern tastebuds. The mind-blowing experience is further enhanced by a fantastic selection of wines, available by the glass, a decadent range of sweet titbits served with coffee and super slick service. The stylish interior, a masterclass in good taste, provides the perfect foil to this exceptional establishment.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
601;Le Chalet de la Forêt;Belgium;Uccle;drêve de Lorraine 43, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7842411;4.3868414;70;false;true;Creative, Modern French;Pascal Devalkeneer’s chalet is magnificently set on the edge of the Sonian Forest and the chalet’s terrace makes the most of this fantastic natural environment. The restaurant overlooking the chef’s cottage garden oozes luxurious elegance to which you should add well-oiled, slick service and, above all, chef Devalkeneer’s personal stamp on each dish. His blend of classicism and creativity reveals surgical precision, as well as a quest for subtlety and generosity. He scours the countryside of Belgium and France for the best ingredients from Aveyron lamb to abalone from the Brittany coast and honey from his own beehives, with which he crafts an amazing floral dessert starter… He works with exceptional ingredients, flanking them with intriguing side dishes to create a felicitous festival of flavours. For example, he may delicately perfume seabass with bay leaf, adding green asparagus and black truffle, before adding the final definitive flourish, a vivacious dressing of confit shallots, a gutsy gravy and a last-minute hollandaise sauce. This high-flying craftsmanship unveils chef Devalkeneer’s talent, demonstrated by his deep-seated understanding of the role and impact of each ingredient which enables him to create combinations that intelligently enrich and exalt the original flavour. The sommelier is a fountain of insightful wine tips, with a preference for Burgundies. This chalet is a temple of superlative culinary art that never fails to surprise.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
602;Hof van Cleve - Floris Van Der Veken;Belgium;Kruishoutem;Riemegemstraat 1, Kruishoutem, 9770, Belgium;50.9039501;3.5098648;41;true;true;Creative;Floris Van Der Veken is following in the footsteps of his mentor, Peter Goossens. He has taken over this elegant welcoming farmstead and culinary landmark, whose codes he continues to uphold. As attentive as ever, Serge Sierens seamlessly supervises the front of house. A quick glance at the menus reveals the importance given to the ingredient. Corrèze lamb rules supreme in raviolis or in a medium rare saddle of lamb coated in a powerful meaty jus. This last-minute approach to dining demands painstaking attention, phenomenal knowhow and a scattering of international notes. The kitchen team attaches equal importance to a lowly leek or a noble turbot. Save room for afters, because the dessert trolley remains a highlight of this venerable establishment. It is also a pleasure to witness chef Van Der Veken’s quest for his own culinary identity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
603;La Table de Maxime;Belgium;Our;Our 23, Our, 6852, Belgium;49.959957;5.122613;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French;Welcome to Our, a characteristic Ardennes village nestling in peaceful countryside, that has become a beacon for discerning gourmets thanks to Maxime Collard. After a stint as deputy at Karmeliet, he has forged his own style in his homeland. An old farmstead has been restored and turned into an elegant modern restaurant, whose many windows and mirrors seem to invite the countryside indoors. Chef Collard invariably avoids showing off his extensive technical background, preferring to unveil the essence of a few premium ingredients, local whenever possible. Examples include tail of blue lobster, poached in the plate, paired with cherries, almond cream, Neufchâteau mozzarella, cherry jelly and an exquisite beurre blanc. Modern, highly aromatic cuisine, overflowing in subtle nuances and generosity, depicts the handiwork of this high-flying artisan. The à la carte pigeon is a whole pigeon, cooked on the bone. When you sit down to a meal at Maxime’s, your tastebuds are in for a moment of pure bliss!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
604;Ralf Berendsen;Belgium;Neerharen;Paalsteenlaan 90, Neerharen, 3620, Belgium;50.9152264;5.6676398;28;true;true;Creative, Modern French;The Butte aux Bois luxury hotel is exquisitely located in the grandiose countryside of Hoge Kempen National Park. From the tree-lined terrace to the dark parquet flooring and bright airy dining room, everything about this restaurant oozes character and class, bewitching the diner even before the first bite. Perfectionist chef Ralf Berendsen now takes centre stage. He spices up familiar flavours with delicate nuances and subtle international ingredients. His cooking is complex but never overly complicated or fussy. He may combine North Sea crab and foie gras in two dishes, in which the fresh crab meat is offset by briny seaweed notes, hot jalapeno, a subtle green apple vinaigrette and dashi underscored by almonds – to die for! We would queue to eat here just for Berendsen’s knockout sauces! Discerning foodies will be even more delighted to learn that Ralf was a baker-pastry chef in a former life, hence the irresistible bread and the wickedly tempting miniature dessert trolley.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
605;Bartholomeus;Belgium;Heist;Zeedijk 267, Heist, 8301, Belgium;51.341769;3.2436215;74;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Bart Desmidt, with his right-hand man Philip and the gracious Sandra, take you on a whirlwind tour of flavours in Bartholomeus, a swanky restaurant with Japanese overtones. Admire the cheerful chefs seamlessly working together in the theatrically visible kitchen. The seats (only 18) around the counter are reserved for amateurs of high-flying cuisine. There is a single set menu and Sandra can be relied upon for judicious wine-food pairings, delving into a splendid cellar which boasts a knock-out selection of wines by the glass. The cast of exceptional ingredients features stars such as wagyu beef, turbot, langoustine, all of which are crafted with awe-inspiring know-how. Creative, bang-on recipes designed to showcase the produce: oysters, wagyu and lemon explode in a festival of flavour or textbook-perfect fluffy soufflé of langoustines, subtly flanked by caviar. The chefs’ consummate technique and boundless creativity left us reeling – you won’t be disappointed by their carte blanche menu…;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
606;Sir Kwinten;Belgium;Sint-Kwintens-Lennik;Markt 9a, Sint-Kwintens-Lennik, 1750, Belgium;50.8056605;4.1554453;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Wine is central to Sir Kwinten, as you cannot fail but notice as soon as you cross the threshold of this imposing mansion. Flacons of wine are showcased in a display case and Gueuze beer bottles escort you on your way to the restroom. Yannick Dehandschutter is a consummate sommelier, who gets as much pleasure out of suggesting local beers and wine from the Dappeersveld estate as the production of a few daring winegrowers.Now make your way upstairs to the elegant dining room, where wine also takes centre stage, thanks to matches made in heaven courtesy of a classical lineup and unencumbered recipes crafted by chef Glenn Verhasselt. His sauces illustrate his immense knowhow and sensitivity by their fascinating subtlety. A textbook game sauce underscores the big-boned character of saddle of hare, while delicate blue lobster is enhanced with cannelloni stuffed with lobster meat and Flandrien Grand Cru cheese in an exquisite blend of generosity and delicacy. Whenever possible, the chef highlights ingredients from his native Pajottenland in a highly personal tribute.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
607;Castor;Belgium;Beveren-Leie;Kortrijkseweg 164, Beveren-Leie, 8791, Belgium;50.8720569;3.3430165;24;true;true;Modern French;Purity is the name of the game at Castor. The elegant yet austere cube on Kortrijkseweg is home to a modern interior of wood, glass and concrete. Stefanie embodies the restaurant’s classy front of house, while Maarten Bouckaert surprises the diner right from the appetisers, as he rolls out his superlative talent for combining flawless textbook technique (think velvety vichyssoise or crisp Anna potatoes) with a delicate neoteric spin. The sauces are to die for! Nothing leaves the chef’s kitchen that hasn’t been endlessly puzzled over and preened. Medium rare local lamb, served with confit of neck and rillettes, is enhanced by a perfectly balanced blend of ras el hanout, aubergine chermoula, anchovies and black garlic, while a creamy rosemary sauce adds a final flourish. The insightful tips of the eclectic sommelier ensure that there is a wine to suit all palates and all wallets. A young chef who cooks like a seasoned veteran but with the contagious enthusiasm of youth.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
608;La Paix;Belgium;Anderlecht;rue Ropsy-Chaudron 49, Anderlecht, 1070, Belgium;50.8437035;4.3281195;50;false;false;Asian Influences, Creative;La Paix, a culinary landmark of Brussels dating back to 1892, was originally where the local butchers came for a bite to eat at the end of their working day. Chef David Martin has traded in the traditional brasserie score for a neoteric menu that is as impressive as the interior is lavish. La Paix now blends Brussels’ heritage with Japanese minimalism, depicted by a shimmering flock of origami birds dangling from the ceiling and soft lighting, setting an almost reverential vibe as Martin and his team add the final touch to their creations on the “altar”. You can choose between three set menus, named after the chef’s father and the parents of Nathalie, the lady of the house. The menus blend purebred Gallicism and Japanese purity, with a highly creative personal twist, often embodied by Norwegian seafood. Chef Martin is on a permanent quest for perfection. The flavours are bold, often contrasted, such as a lemon stuffed with stracciatella, fresh tartare of langoustine, yuzu, caviar and a hint of miso. Or how about a disruptive crunchy moshi stuffed with earthy chicory, velvety tuna and a creamy layer of black miso and Jerusalem artichoke? David Martin is a larger-than-life chef who is determined to chart new culinary territories.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
609;d'Eugénie à Emilie;Belgium;Baudour;place de la Résistance 1, Baudour, 7331, Belgium;50.4833038;3.8379089;90;false;true;Classic French, Traditional Cuisine;Éric Fernez inherited his love of cooking from his grand-mother Eugénie, a passion he has passed on to his daughter, Émilie. Premium produce, generous classical cuisine and the added dimension that wine can bring to a dish are the foundations of this family’s values. Éric, a past master of old school cooking, who can rely entirely on his right-hand man, David Cataudela, crafts nostalgic food that spans the annals of French cookery. You can expect to sample classic produce such as pigeon, pig’s trotters and sole (prepared à la Fernand Point, no less!) courtesy of almost-forgotten recipes. The sauces are in a class of their own, illustrated by a fresh, fruity, tangy blackcurrant jus that enhances venison. The jaw-dropping range of timeless à la carte and seasonal set menus reveal the establishment’s desire to bend over backwards to suit its customers. This elegant restaurant is ideal for both special occasion decadence and everyday classical fare. The chef, who often pops out to greet diners and chat with them, enjoys getting first-hand feedback from his diners.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
610;Cuchara;Belgium;Lommel;Lepelstraat 3, Lommel, 3920, Belgium;51.2309534;5.3097212;22;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Music and nature enjoy guest-star roles at Cuchara. The former adds a relaxed lounge mood, while the latter, embodied by a mainly wood and leather interior, paints a distinctive trendy picture. A seven-metre-long tree sculpture hanging from the ceiling seems to float over the dining room! Mysterious, intimate, even quirky, Cuchara and Jan Tournier get a kick out of surprising diners. His punchy food is distinctive and individual and he manages to astound with just a few ingredients. Each bite sparks and triggers a whole range of unexpected nuances and emotions. Tournier will marinade his salmon for two days in Koji before masterfully cooking it at 41°C and pairing it with wasabi, trout roe, chives and shiso oil. However, that’s not all, because there is a final flourish of exquisite delicacy, consisting of a jus of consummate depth made up of colza, shrimp, squid ink and hollandaise sauce – to die for! Unique, expressive, fascinating cuisine that gives rise to a symphony of flavours that will knock the socks off your tastebuds!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
611;La Durée;Belgium;Izegem;Leenstraat 28, Izegem, 8870, Belgium;50.9119799;3.1957656;37;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Ah – if only time could stand still for a moment! This wish may cross your mind as you taste Anglelo Rosseel’s subtle fare. This sensitive chef harnesses his consummate technical prowess to craft distinctive and inventive recipes that intuitively blend the flavours of carefully selected ingredients. Chef Rosseel’s cuisine, which is divinely crafted, sensual and delicate, seeks to draw out the best of each primarily seasonal ingredient, often underpinned by exquisite sauces. His weakness for fresh Mediterranean flavours shines through in recipes such as an Italian lemon shell, filled with almond biscuits, crumble, chunks of sweet lemon confit, contrasting bitter fresh lemon juice granita, a drizzling of limoncello and a scoop of velvety lemon ice cream for the final flourish, all of which in a whirlwind of flavours that will send your tastebuds spinning into heaven. The wine list cleverly offsets the subtle culinary score. A majestic villa, dripping in natural details and modern elegance, provides the setting for this one-of-a-kind dining experience.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
612;The Jane;Belgium;Antwerpen;Paradeplein 1, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.2023273;4.4233593;87;true;true;Creative;The Jane is unique in Benelux. This designer-inspired culinary temple is quirkily housed in a large chapel, whose façade continues to bear a crucifix! A striking light fixture and stained-glass windows catch the eye in the theatrical interior, whose former altar provides a stage for the chefs to work their magic behind a glazed screen. Nick Bril takes you on a journey from Latin America and Asia to culinary paradise with dishes that reflect his personality. Each ingredient calls upon an incredible variety of combinations and techniques, yet the coherence between the delicate side dishes and the powerful main ingredient is consummate with gutsy sauces adding a final flourish. Examples include turbot smoked in Indian spices, curry and lovage, sprinkled with grey shrimp. Nothing leaves the kitchen that hasn’t been pondered and puzzled over in the flavoursome, occasionally complex culinary score. Upstairs, Untitled serves trendy nosh and a spot-on beverage menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
613;De Jonkman;Belgium;Sint-Kruis;Maalsesteenweg 438, Sint-Kruis, 8310, Belgium;51.207236;3.2777835;60;false;false;Creative;Filip Claeys is mad about fish. The grandson of a fisherman, he founded NorthSeaChefs, which endeavours to encourage consumers to eat lesser known and accidentally caught fish. Equally at home with red meat and top-drawer ingredients such as langoustine, he also wows diners with lowly dogfish, thanks to his inventive, original style. Delicate sauces showcase his classical training, whilst allowing his personality to shine through in dishes such as tartare of artichoke, underscored by hints of rhubarb and a white ajo cream with toasted almonds. Or how about oxtail flanked by tarragon cream, a sabayon of curd and confit of chard that add complexity, subtlety and depth to the whole dish? Each course is served in several plates so that the diner can better taste the individual qualities of each ingredient. The friendly, home-from-home vibe that reigns throughout the establishment adds a relaxed note to the chef’s high-flying craftsmanship. Let the sommelier guide you in choosing just the right wine for your meal. Heaven for foodies, this elegant restaurant sports a designer interior dotted with wooden fixtures and fittings.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
614;Kwonsooksoo;South Korea;Seoul;4F, 37 Apgujeong-ro 80-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06016, South Korea;37.52437;127.04355;30;false;false;Korean;Chef Kwon Woo-joong’s homage to tradition is evident in every facet of Kwonsooksoo, even in the name itself (sooksoo is an archaic term for professional cook). Inspired by time-honored methods of cooking, Kwon digs deep into his own roots. He tirelessly scours the country for rare finds that best represent each of the seasons and transforms even the most mundane ingredients into something special. What the diners get to experience is passion on a plate, coupled with a good dose of ingenuity.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
615;Mingles;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 19 Dosan-daero 67-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06016, South Korea;37.52535;127.04426;97;false;true;Korean, Korean Contemporary;Chef Kang Min-goo's keen eye for detail shines with warm minimalism takes center stage at Mingles, where the interior design highlights the understated elegance of Korean aesthetics. Complementing this ambiance are exquisite tableware and decor crafted by Korean artisans, further enhancing the refined charm of traditional Korean cuisine. From the beginning, Kang has marched to the beat of his own drum, breaking down barriers by marrying the old with the new, but always with a deep respect for tradition. His journey and evolution continues, with dishes like Abalone and Cabbage Seon and Fish Mandu showcasing the creativity of the chef and his talented team.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
616;La Yeon;South Korea;Seoul;23F Shilla Hotel, 249 Dongho-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04605, South Korea;37.555813;127.00517;47;false;false;Korean, Modern Cuisine;Time-honored traditions of Korean cuisine are given a contemporary touch at La Yeon. Located on the 23rd floor of The Shilla Hotel, this refined dining space offers stunning vistas over Namsan Park. It's the detail here that are noteworthy, from the fine tableware to the attentive service. Hansik and wine pairings elevate the dining experience to another level.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
617;Soigné;South Korea;Seoul;#201, 2F Sinsa square, 652 Gangnam-daero, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06027, South Korea;37.51933;127.01903;37;false;false;Innovative;Soigné, under the slogan “Contemporary Cuisine of Seoul,” is a culinary destination where Chef Lee Jun and his team present creative and refined dishes. While drawing inspiration from global cuisines, the restaurant stays rooted in the essence of Korean flavors and ingredients. At the heart of the restaurant is an open kitchen, offering guests a dynamic view of the cooking process. Soigné also features a main dining room, private rooms, and a bespoke dining space known as the Red Room, catering to diverse dining experiences.The menu is uniquely referred to as “Episodes” and is regularly refreshed. Each episode revolves around a distinct theme, creating a poetic dining journey with a sense of beginning, climax, and resolution. To enhance the experience, thoughtfully curated wine pairings accompany each episode, ensuring a harmonious and memorable meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
618;Kojima;South Korea;Seoul;6F Boon the Shop, 21 Apgujeong-ro 60-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06016, South Korea;37.52559;127.04193;71;true;true;Sushi;Chef Kim Woo-tae offers omakase crafted from seasonal Korean wild seafood and high-quality ingredients, emphasizing their fresh, natural flavors. The chef’s friendly and calm demeanor adds a distinct vibe to Kojima. The chef, who trained in the Edomae sushi philosophy, remains dedicated to improving his craft. The strength of Team Kojima lies in their ability to transform high-quality ingredients into an exquisite selection of tsumami and nigiri. They also recommend the best sake to pair with the food for a more vibrant dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
619;Mitou;South Korea;Seoul;24 Dosan-daero 70-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06064, South Korea;37.52206;127.04502;32;false;true;Japanese;At Mitou, the prowess and ingenuity of the chef duo Kwon Young-woon and Kim Bo-mi are showcased through authentic Japanese cuisine prepared with fresh seasonal ingredients. Indeed, their relentless struggle to incorporate seasonality into the menu starts with a careful selection of quality ingredients. In particular, chicken, eggs, rice and vegetables used at this establishment are sourced from Chef Kwon’s family farm. A culmination of such painstaking effort, the fare at Mitou genuinely reflects a sense of earnestness, modesty and dedication harbored by the two chefs as eternal students of culinary art. It thus comes as no surprise that customers eagerly anticipate Mitou’s new offerings every season.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
620;alla prima;South Korea;Seoul;13 Hakdong-ro 17-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06045, South Korea;37.51346;127.02602;22;true;true;Innovative;Chef Kim Jin-hyuk continues to attract discerning gourmets with his whimsically creative and modern offerings. His reverence for seasonal ingredients, his attention to balance, and his delicate yet assertive sauces come together like a symphony that pairs well with both wine and sake. The L-shaped counter with ample seating, the gleaming open kitchen, the spacious dining hall, and the private dining room each do their part to make the diners feel comfortable. Be sure to reserve ahead.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
622;Hand and Flowers;United Kingdom;Marlow;126 West Street, Marlow, SL7 2BP, United Kingdom;51.5696616;-0.7836567;87;false;true;Modern British;This flagship operation from Tom Kerridge – the king of British pub dining – provides exactly what you'd expect: classic dishes executed with such skill and precision that they soar to rarely seen heights. The menu is not overly long but it still proves hard to choose, as every dish sounds so appealing. The ingredients are exemplary, presentation is first-rate and the bold, natural flavours are given room to shine, resulting in memorable dishes like an outstanding banana soufflé. The beams add character to the room, while the friendly staff keep the atmosphere light and convivial.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
623;Gymkhana;United Kingdom;London;42 Albemarle Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 4JH, United Kingdom;51.5085431;-0.141547;88;false;true;Indian;The clubs of colonial India are the inspiration for this impeccably run restaurant. It's spread across two levels: the ground floor booths are perfect for lunch, while the vivid red basement has a more intimate feel. The extensive menus are predominantly Northern Indian in style, featuring superbly executed, traditionally based dishes. Balance, sophistication and depth are all present in the cooking, with options like tandoori masala lamb chops and kid goat methi keema standing out.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
624;Midsummer House;United Kingdom;Cambridge;Midsummer Common, Cambridge, CB4 1HA, United Kingdom;52.2120545;0.1284006;48;false;true;Creative;In an idyllic location overlooking Midsummer Common, inside an equally beautiful Victorian house, you'll find this stylish, long-standing restaurant. Over 20 years into its lifetime, the dishes are continually evolving thanks to a kitchen which is not afraid to push the boundaries. Every course is packed full of personality and originality, especially the stand-out desserts like delicious coconut parfait served in a mock-coconut shell made of Nyangbo chocolate. Luxury ingredients are generously used, flavours are measured and there’s an appealing range of different textures.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
625;The Glenturret Lalique;United Kingdom;Crieff;The Glenturret Distillery, The Hosh, Torreglen, Crieff, PH7 4HA, United Kingdom;56.3890265;-3.8527163;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This intimate restaurant mixes the luxury with the familiar, in both its décor and its dishes. The likes of tattie scones are served alongside Highland Wagyu and caviar, in a room that features both a rustic beamed ceiling and maple leaf Lalique chandeliers. Chef Mark Donald adeptly balances local and global influences in sophisticated, precisely crafted dishes with superb depth of flavour. Set inside The Glenturret Distillery, the restaurant boasts some truly unique aged malts, and they even offer a whisky tasting selection as well as a top-class wine list. Stay overnight to complete the experience.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
626;Ynyshir;United Kingdom;Machynlleth;Eglwysfach, Machynlleth, SY20 8TA, United Kingdom;52.5445284;-3.9439501;36;true;true;Creative;For a truly unique experience, head for rural Wales and this matt black, part-Georgian house with an immersive approach and a pumping soundtrack. Dinner starts early, which gives Chef-Owner Gareth Ward 5 hours to take diners on a playful culinary journey around the globe. He has a particular reverence for Japanese cuisine, with sashimi and A5 Wagyu beef likely to appear on the surprise menu of around 30 vibrant, exceptionally skilful servings. Regional sheepskins and handmade crockery show the team's pride in their Welsh locale, while you can extend your visit in one of the luxurious bedrooms.;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
628;Restaurant Andrew Fairlie;United Kingdom;Auchterarder;Auchterarder, PH3 1NF, United Kingdom;56.2832316;-3.7517344;59;true;true;Modern French;Hidden away in the depths of the world-famous Gleneagles Hotel, this intimate restaurant has a luxurious classical elegance, courtesy of dark wood walls, clever lighting and colourful food-themed art. The philosophy and spirit of the late Andrew Fairlie live on in refined cooking with a French heart and a Scottish soul. Techniques are rooted in the classics and superb quality produce guides the menu, with 95% of the vegetables coming from their walled Victorian garden. Service is formal but comes with plenty of personality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
629;Opheem;United Kingdom;Birmingham;48 Summer Row, Birmingham, B3 1JJ, United Kingdom;52.481614;-1.9079211;19;true;true;Indian;Locally born and bred chef-owner Aktar Islam has fashioned a wonderful dining experience at this ever-developing restaurant. A spacious bar and sitting room are cleverly used as a space in which to enjoy snacks and a drink before heading to the dining room and its open kitchen. The series of flavoursome, excellently spiced and carefully balanced dishes are creative, modern takes on Indian recipes. Well-chosen wines from the excellent sommelier are on-hand to accompany.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
632;Alex Dilling at Hotel Café Royal;United Kingdom;London;68 Regent Street, Soho, London, W1B 4DY, United Kingdom;51.5100201;-0.1359557;77;false;true;Modern French;In a discreet, intimate environment inside the grand Hotel Café Royal, the eponymous chef has the perfect canvas in which to showcase his impressive and accomplished cuisine. Alex's dishes are exquisite in appearance and, like a seasoned orchestra, everything on the plate adds its own note of flavour to produce something harmonious and exhilarating. Whether Cornish sardines, Scottish girolles or Kaluga caviar, the kitchen knows how to bring the best out of its exquisite ingredients.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
633;Chapter One by Mickael Viljanen;Ireland;Dublin City;18-19 Parnell Square North, Rotunda, Dublin City, D01 T3V8, Ireland;53.354379;-6.2639708;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Mickael Viljanen’s basement restaurant is a stylish, elegant spot decorated with eye-catching art. Superb service complements cooking that focuses on prime luxury ingredients – like Donegal lobster or Limousin sweetbreads – and sees classic French techniques combined with subtle modern touches. Mickael’s creativity and personality shine through in perfectly balanced, immaculately executed dishes with sublime natural flavours and beautiful presentation. The 'Irish Coffee' is made in the dining room and is, like everything else, an experience to remember.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
635;Liath;Ireland;Blackrock;Blackrock Market, 19a Main Street, Blackrock, A94 C8Y1, Ireland;53.3011683;-6.178472;38;false;true;Creative;There's a slightly magical feel to this stylish, cosy restaurant. With just a handful of tables, it makes for a personal dining experience, with Damien Grey and his small team offering a genuinely warm welcome and explaining the dishes personally. The surprise tasting menu showcases bold, original dishes centred around the five tastes – salty, savoury, sweet, bitter and sour – which come together in perfect harmony. First-class ingredients are present throughout, treated with precision and strong modern technique by the chefs. Excellent wine pairings further enhance the experience.;Air conditioning;[]
636;La Dame de Pic London;United Kingdom;London;10 Trinity Square, City of London, London, EC3N 4AJ, United Kingdom;51.5101629;-0.0779535;23;true;false;Modern French, French Contemporary;Anne-Sophie Pic’s London outpost is a charmingly run place situated in the impressive Beaux-Arts style Four Seasons Hotel. An airy, high-ceilinged room with attractive modern art is the stage for cooking rooted in classic French techniques where excellent quality ingredients combine in delicate combinations, with a range of spices judiciously used to add extra complexity and depth of flavour. Keep an eye out for Anne-Sophie's signature dishes, like the Les Berlingots pasta parcels or the striking 'White Millefeuille' for dessert.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
637;The Clove Club;United Kingdom;London;Shoreditch Town Hall, 380 Old Street, Shoreditch, London, EC1V 9LT, United Kingdom;51.5271054;-0.0793371;42;true;true;Creative;Go for the house martini as you enjoy an array of snacks like crispy buttermilk chicken and crab dumpling that precede the start of The Clove Club's multi-course set menu. The roll-call of prime British ingredients includes Orkney scallops, Wiltshire trout, Torbay prawns, Herdwick lamb and Middle White pork – all starring in seasonally pertinent dishes where their natural flavours are allowed to shine through. The historic surroundings of Shoreditch Town Hall provide the perfect backdrop, with the open-plan kitchen adding a little more theatre to proceedings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
638;Kitchen Table;United Kingdom;London;70 Charlotte Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 4QG, United Kingdom;51.5203616;-0.13647;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There's a lot of courses on James Knappett's creative surprise menu, but you'll be glad of it once you've tried such superb cooking. You’ll start in the lounge with drinks and accomplished canapés that set the tone for the evening, before being guided to your seat at the beautiful kitchen counter – where you can watch the chefs finish dishes close-up. Outstanding British produce is at the heart of the experience, with the seafood often proving a highlight, whether it's soft and smoky eel or fresh squid enhanced by a creamy lobster sauce.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
641;dede;Ireland;Baltimore;Customs House, Baltimore, P81  K291, Ireland;51.4835036;-9.3725309;57;false;false;Turkish, Creative;Chef Ahmet Dede’s warm, inviting restaurant in this West Cork coastal village is a masterful marriage between his Irish surroundings and his Turkish heritage. Superb local produce is the bedrock of the cooking, enhanced by skilful, judicious spicing which delivers multiple layers of authentic Turkish flavours while never overpowering the core ingredients – as with a refined take on street food 'îçli köfte'. The charismatic Ahmet and his mostly Turkish brigade deliver their dishes with pride, while co-owner Maria runs the service with a friendly charm.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
642;Patrick Guilbaud;Ireland;Dublin City;21 Upper Merrion Street, Dublin City, D02 KF79, Ireland;53.338452;-6.2529969;22;true;false;Modern French;This iconic restaurant has been thriving since 1981, thanks to both the eponymous chef and the exceptional team he has around him. It sits hidden away within a Georgian townhouse and oozes sumptuousness and sophistication thanks to features such as a gilt barrel ceiling and hand-crafted marquetry. The accomplished cooking isn’t to be upstaged, however: it is French at heart yet has a restrained modernity and showcases some bold yet superbly balanced flavours. The Irish ingredients are certainly luxurious and the baba flambé with your choice of rum provides an inviting, classical way to finish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
643;Ikoyi;United Kingdom;London;180 Strand, Strand, London, WC2R 1EA, United Kingdom;51.512381;-0.1154759;64;false;true;Creative;Top restaurants never stop developing – and that’s certainly the case with Ikoyi. Founder and chef Jeremy Chan’s surprise tasting menu uses high quality organic produce from the British Isles, married with the spices of West Africa, to create dishes that are as unique and creative as they are bold and beautiful to behold – and they now display even greater levels of depth and complexity. Dishes like aged turbot with egusi miso or suya with creamed peas are bound to enthral, while the theatrically presented smoked jollof rice will always be one of the highlights.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
644;Dinner by Heston Blumenthal;United Kingdom;London;66 Knightsbridge, Knightsbridge, London, SW1X 7LA, United Kingdom;51.5021106;-0.1599147;55;false;true;Traditional British;The menu may take inspiration from one of England's oldest recipe books, The Forme of Cury, but there is still something decidedly 'Heston' about the modern and creative dishes on show at this restaurant housed inside The Mandarin Oriental Hotel. You need only take one look at dishes like the signature illusory 'Meat Fruit' to see the eponymous chef's playful influence. Crucially, the flavours of the creations are sublime too, with the aforementioned dish providing a smooth, utterly delicious chicken liver parfait, regardless of its fun, fruity form.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
646;Moor Hall;United Kingdom;Aughton;Prescot Road, Aughton, L39 6RT, United Kingdom;53.5423365;-2.8919183;88;false;false;Modern British;Charming grounds lead up to this beautifully restored 16th-century country house, where your meal commences with an array of snacks – the last served in the kitchen by Head Chef Mark Birchall, who introduces some of the outstanding produce to come. Once you’re settled in the striking Scandic-style dining room, the main event begins: a procession of refined, stunningly detailed dishes. Mark’s understanding of flavour is impeccable, showcased in brilliant combinations like warm ripe tomatoes with tiny cubes of bone marrow. Among the accommodation options are garden rooms that reflect the natural surroundings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
647;Da Terra;United Kingdom;London;8 Patriot Square, Bethnal Green, London, E2 9NF, United Kingdom;51.530411;-0.05607;76;true;false;Creative;In contrast to the grandeur of its location inside the Town Hall Hotel, there's an understated, modern look to Da Terra. Chef Rafael Cagali hails from Brazil and his great grandfather was from Italy, and these influences, along with time spent working in Spain, come together in skilfully crafted, highly original cooking founded on Brazilian traditions. The strikingly presented dishes are bursting with colour, and the surprise menu builds beautifully as you move from course to course. Wine pairings are thoughtfully chosen, with admirable originality.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
649;Aramburu;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Vicente López 1661, Buenos Aires, C1018ABA, Argentina;-34.5916443;-58.3891732;75;false;true;Creative;Unusual snacks hanging from a tree, maritime-inspired light bites teeming with flavour and delicacy, delicious seasonal dishes such as courgette flower tempura and Patagonian prawns on volcanic rock, and exquisite Angus beef served with a nori taco are all part of the gastronomic experience at this restaurant located in the heart of the Recoleta district, with access via the pleasant Pasaje del Correo. This is one of those places that everyone is talking about thanks to its high levels of cuisine. Here, chef Gonzalo Aramburu, who can often be seen from the dining room working the stoves alongside his team, focuses on a single surprise tasting menu (around 18 courses) that aims to combine innovation, technique and aesthetics through the use of the best Argentinian ingredients. For dessert, coffee and a post-dinner cocktail, guests need to head up to the first floor, where a private room is also available. Haute cuisine with an Argentinian soul!;Air conditioning;[]
650;Jungsik;South Korea;Seoul;11 Seolleung-ro 158-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06014, South Korea;37.525584;127.041069;67;false;false;Contemporary;Touted as a pioneer of modern Korean fine dining, Chef Yim Jung-sik — with his Seoul and New York restaurants - is credited for introducing Korean cuisine to the world with an innovative flair that is entirely his own. What Yim does best is drawing inspiration from the familiar — gimbap, bibimbap, platter of nine delicacies and napa wraps with pork — and creating something unexpected yet surprisingly evocative and authentic. Whimsical desserts, a good wine list and attentive service — Jungsik has it all.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
651;Thaller - Restaurant;Austria;Sankt Veit am Vogau;Am Kirchplatz 4, Sankt Veit am Vogau, 8423, Austria;46.7466243;15.6256799;62;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This building opposite the magnificent Baroque parish church has been in the family since 1882, and Norbert Thaller has run the family business with his delightful wife Manuela since 2002. Sustainability has always been a priority for the couple, who are deeply connected to their homeland and nature. In his seven-course set menu, the chef-patron follows the rhythm of the seasons. Many of his fantastic ingredients come from his beautiful garden with its vegetable and herb patches, greenhouses and fish pond. His dishes are imaginative, sophisticated and modern, but also still down-to-earth. A vegetarian set menu can be pre-ordered. The well-curated wine list features an extensive selection of natural and organic wines. Tip: Try Manuela's own vermouth as an aperitif! The tasteful interior design marries old-world charm and contemporary style. There is also an inviting terrace overlooking the garden. The Gasthaus serves hearty home-style cooking at lunchtime.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
652;RAU nature-based cuisine;Austria;Großraming;Pechgraben 23, Großraming, 4463, Austria;47.9155479;14.5368954;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Chef-patron Klemens Gold is forging his own path at this small restaurant in a delightfully secluded location. His inspiration comes from his natural surroundings, which makes for a unique and exciting set menu. For his ‘10 seasons’ concept (ten different set menus per year) he uses the best the market has to offer, forages some items himself in the forest, grows vegetables and herbs in his own garden, ferments and pickles. One example of his absolutely unique brand of cuisine is a dish of crisp, firm, top-quality Bavarian prawns, marinated in home-grown ginger and tangy rapeseed oil, served with home-made, airy, crispy kroepoek made from Austrian rice and a broth brimming with umami flavours that has been made from roasted carcasses, ginger and home-made soy sauce. Drink tip: ‘Combuchont’ from his own tea cellar. In keeping with the "nature-based cuisine": clear design using natural materials and colours – large windows offer a view of the greenery outside.;Car park;[]
653;Paula;Austria;Sankt Wolfgang im Salzkammergut;Markt 88, Sankt Wolfgang im Salzkammergut, 5360, Austria;47.7381569;13.4479361;91;false;true;Creative;Sebastian Leutgeb and Miriam Grädler form the dedicated team behind this trendy yet cosy little restaurant housed in the Hotel and Wirtshaus Weisser Bär, right on the market square. The young chef successfully marries Austrian and French influences in his creative cuisine, which comes in the format of a five- or eight-course set menu, featuring dishes such as trout in a tomato sauce, or pigeon with cherry and macadamia. Meanwhile, Miriam Grädler is your friendly and competent maître d' and sommelier. The name of the restaurant is a tribute to the chef's grandmother, Paula. Tip: In the summer season, on Wednesdays and Saturdays, local musicians put on a small concert in the village. It is well worth experiencing – and you can also see and hear everything from the comfort of the restaurant.;Air conditioning;[]
654;Harald Irka am Pfarrhof - Fine Dine;Austria;Sankt Andrä im Sausal;Im Sausal 1, Sankt Andrä im Sausal, 8441, Austria;46.7896872;15.3748743;62;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;The setting could not be delightful! This historical rectory, whose foundations date back to the 13C, nestles in a tranquil spot overlooked by the parish church. Your dedicated hosts, Lisa Gasser and Harald Irka, run this culinary gem with their outstanding team led by sommelier Marina Kühlinger. The cuisine of the owner and his sous-chef Jan Gollinger artfully marries creativity with seasonal produce and classical foundations. Both regional and international ingredients are expertly prepared, exemplified in dishes such as ikejime salmon trout with watermelon, tomato and aromatic blossoms, as well as in timeless classics: pike quenelles with pumpkin, capellini and Nantua sauce – each displaying a masterful balance of refined lightness and robust flavours. The surprise menu, which can be booked online as a combination or individual ticket, comes in five or seven courses. A five-course lunch is served on Sundays. Tip: The tastefully renovated former stables boast fantastic guest rooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
656;Bootshaus;Austria;Traunkirchen;Klosterplatz 4, Traunkirchen, 4801, Austria;47.8458914;13.7898524;87;true;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;This place has a real ace up its sleeve – its superb lakeside location on the peninsula! The large windows of this stylish restaurant afford spectacular views, and the terrace is a real highlight. But the creative cuisine is also worthy of undivided attention. Lukas Nagl draws on an impressive wealth of ideas to add his own special touch to a particularly regional take on fine dining. This involves incorporating fermented flavours and Japanese influences, without using any ingredients from further afield. His affinity to the lakes in the Salzkammergut makes itself felt in his five- to seven-course set menu – take, for instance, the highly aromatic, tender and succulent crayfish sourced from the Traun, or the Arctic char, served beautifully translucent and infused with a delicate smoky flavour. Very attentive and friendly service. The restaurant is located inside Das Traunsee – Das Hotel zum See.;Great view,Terrace;[]
657;Hubert Wallner;Austria;Maria Wörth;Seeplatz Nr. 6, Maria Wörth, 9082, Austria;46.6228942;14.1180517;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Here the enjoyment begins with the magnificent location right by Wörthersee – on balmy summer evenings, you can experience many a beautiful sunset over the lake from the marvellous terrace! Inside, a plush, modern and elegant interior in a palette of light, warm colours awaits you. Service is organised in the classical way and the brigade is friendly and professional. The food is billed as "Austrian-Mediterranean" cuisine and Hubert Wallner and team are inspired by the Alpine region. There are two set menus comprising five to seven courses, plus a few excellent extras before, in between and after. À la carte options are also available. If you prefer something more exclusive, there is the option of booking the Chef's Table. The wine cellar contains over 3 000 wines. You can stay overnight in the adjoining Hermitage Vital Resort.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
658;Die Weinbank - Restaurant;Austria;Ehrenhausen;Hauptstraße 44, Ehrenhausen, 8461, Austria;46.724348;15.5856935;36;false;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;The names Fuchs and Zach are shorthand for a successful combination of creative cuisine and tailored wine recommendations. Gerhard Fuchs brings exceptional depth of flavour to his dishes, drawing on his wealth of culinary experience. Premium ingredients are prepared without any fuss, particularly exemplified by the "Dotterraviolo" – featuring wafer-thin pasta cooked al dente and filled with a wonderfully creamy egg yolk that is aromatic and bursts with colour. This has been a house classic and signature dish for years! There is no à la carte selection, just a surprise menu – available in a longer or shorter version. Christian Zach, a veritable "walking wine encyclopaedia", serves wines with utmost dedication and profound expertise, selecting from an impressive collection of over 35 000 bottles comprising more than 4 000 different labels. The decor is an attractive alliance of warm wood and sleek, modern lines – with wine bottles adding a decorative touch. There are very few tables, so be sure to book in advance!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
659;Lukas Kapeller;Austria;Steyr;Damberggasse 27, Steyr, 4400, Austria;48.0339875;14.4315961;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This place describes itself as "small, refined, modern", which goes both for the five tasteful guestrooms and the restaurant on the 2nd floor, where a smart modern interior meets with a distinct sense of intimacy. Guests soak up the cosy atmosphere with a personal touch, while in the open kitchen a seven-course set menu is prepared by a team headed up by owners Lukas Kapeller and Michael Schlöglhofer. Dishes such as king oyster mushrooms with celery, tarragon and nut butter or grilled pikeperch with peas, radishes and horseradish steer clear of unnecessary frills and put the focus on regional ingredients. In such a beautiful location on a small hill surrounded by greenery, it is hard to believe you're in the centre of Steyr.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
661;Geschwister Rauch - Restaurant;Austria;Bad Gleichenberg;Trautmannsdorf 6, Bad Gleichenberg, 8343, Austria;46.8732383;15.8830557;37;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;In the quiet village of Trautmannsdorf, overlooking Bad Gleichenberg, Richard Rauch and his sister Sonja have established themselves as pillars of the Austrian gastronomy scene. The chef-patron draws on local and international influences, showcasing his creativity with dishes such as sweet and sour stuffed peppers with octopus, physalis and cucumber, or Hütter free-range chicken (meat and egg) – served in the form of two tasting menus. The ingredients used are second to none, and the restaurant's own pig farm is a key supplier. There is also a shop on site, where you can purchase high-quality food items to take home. The terrace, shaded by grapevines, is a lovely spot in summer. The charming service team is on hand to cater to your every need, including when it comes to choosing the right wine. In addition to the fine dining restaurant, the siblings also open the Wirtshaus at lunchtime. Comfortable accommodation is available at the adjacent Villa Rosa (1913), where they also organise cookery classes.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
662;Geiger Alm;Austria;Altaussee;Lichtersberg 77, Altaussee, 8992, Austria;47.6605502;13.743594;32;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;This place is the epitome of cosy rusticity! Housed in a quaint old timber building, the restaurant has a delightful Alpine-style interior and serves flavoursome dishes that draw on regional culinary tradition and seasonal produce. It's clear that your hosts are passionate about what they do. In the kitchen, Dominik Utassy prepares a four- to eight-course set menu (vegetarian version available), using carefully selected ingredients. Eva-Maria Utassy expertly manages the service with unaffected charm, offering astute wine recommendations. Given the limited number of seats, you would be wise to book early. In summer, dine out on the terrace and take in the surrounding natural beauty.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
663;Mörwald „Toni M.“;Austria;Feuersbrunn;Kleine Zeile 15, Feuersbrunn, 3483, Austria;48.4393466;15.7862565;100;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Toni Mörwald, one of Austria's best-known chefs, who runs several restaurants and is also an award-winning cookery book author, is at the helm of this elegant restaurant in the small wine-growing village of Feuersbrunn. Using top-notch ingredients, his repertoire tends towards the classic, but that doesn't preclude the occasional Mediterranean or Asian influence. Dishes such as "Maibock fillet, celeriac, Cox, black morels, whey" demonstrate clarity and coherence, convincing with their finesse and flavour. The terrific wine list features great picks from Austria and a fantastic selection of champagnes and sparkling wines. There are tasteful guestrooms on site, at Villa Katharina and Hotel am Wagram.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
664;Kilian Stuba;Austria;Hirschegg;Oberseitestraße 6, Hirschegg, 6992, Austria;47.3486576;10.1719794;39;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;From the moment you arrive, service of the highest standard awaits you here in the fine dining restaurant of the A-ROSA Ifen Hotel Kleinwalsertal. Then there is the fabulously chic interior design… and the cuisine by Sascha Kemmerer, who trained under Ortwin Adam, recipient of a MICHELIN star in 1978 in the original Ifen Hotel. He wins diners over with the outstanding craftsmanship and harmonious flavours of his creative dishes. With a predilection for regional ingredients, he also looks beyond the borders of the Kleinwalsertal. The set menu echoes the changing seasons and comprises four to six courses, which you can also order individually. In addition, there is a short à la carte selection – including dishes for two. The chef likes to get involved, serving one or two courses himself. In summer, head for the terrace with its marvellous mountain views!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
665;Kirchenwirt;Austria;Leogang;Leogang 3, Leogang, 5771, Austria;47.4388503;12.7608766;93;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Dating back to 1326, this traditional inn located in the heart of Leogang has been run with enthusiasm by the same family for over 130 years. Barbara Kottke and her brother Hans-Jörg Unterrainer represent the sixth generation at the helm. In their cosy, rustic dining area – or, in summer, on the terrace with a view of the parish church – you can choose between a six-course tasting menu (also available in a pescetarian version) and à la carte dishes. Chef Stefan Birnbacher proposes, for example, a creation he calls "Alpine Waters": a mildly spiced, pickled brook trout served with a wafer-thin layer of lardo, and kohlrabi – pickled and in the form of a cream – along with a broth made with Leogang saffron and seasoned with hemp nut oil. His signature caviar dish ("Black Gold") is another tantalising option. There is also a hearty beef broth or Wiener schnitzel. The owner and his front-of-house team really know their way around the fantastic national and international wine list. Tip: gorgeous guestrooms in the hotel.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
667;Herzig;Austria;Vienna;Schanzstrasse 14, Vienna, 1150, Austria;48.2000916;16.3168775;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Sören Herzig's restaurant is located in the 15th district, on the ground floor of the historical Dorotheum-Fünfhaus (previously a pawnshop). In this listed building dating back to the 1920s, the dining space was once an auction hall and has a minimalist, industrial-style atmosphere that is reminiscent of a New York gallery – relaxed and distinctively stylish. Gorgeous hardwood flooring, comfortable designer chairs and artwork by the likes of Peter Jellitsch and Clemens Wolf underscore the tastefully chic interior. The spectacular rooftop terrace affords breathtaking views, making it an ideal spot for an aperitif or a nightcap. As for the food, the modern dishes are made from the best ingredients and without gimmickry, eg "Tristan lobster [tempura], pumpkin, pear, koji rice" "aubergine [barigoule], beluga lentil, almond, cinnamon blossom". The set menu comes in a large or smaller format and can also be made vegetarian by prior arrangement. The adept service and the sommelier's insightful wine recommendations are the icing on the cake.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
668;Pramerl & the Wolf;Austria;Vienna;Pramergasse 21, Vienna, 1090, Austria;48.2220879;16.3648326;21;false;true;Creative;This former pub in Vienna's ninth district is now a great casual fine dining restaurant. In a pleasantly informal atmosphere, the friendly and highly competent front-of-house team serve dishes that draw on modern inspiration and feature contrasts that work well. A sophisticated surprise menu with the focus squarely on the excellent ingredients is proposed. Tip: take the U4 underground line to get here.;Terrace;[]
669;Edvard;Austria;Vienna;Schottenring 24, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2162673;16.3681893;66;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The fine dining restaurant of the Anantara Palais Hansen Hotel has a tasteful interior channeling an elegant style. It serves a seasonally inspired menu injected with fresh pops of colour by chef Paul Gamauf. His dishes show his penchant for vegetables and herbs, plus subtle Mediterranean influences. Preserves also play a role. The combination of flavours and textures is successful, all the components are extremely well balanced and beautifully presented. You can choose a set menu comprising five, seven or nine courses. This is accompanied by a sophisticated wine list with a penchant for Austria, although other European productions are also represented. Incidentally, the name "Edvard" is a tribute to the original architect of the hotel, Baron Theophil Edvard von Hansen.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
670;The Glass Garden;Austria;Salzburg;Mönchsberg Park 26, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8039566;13.03569;25;true;true;Creative;Housed in a distinctive glass vault with an elegant interior and a magnificent view of the city, Schloss Mönchstein's fine dining restaurant is really impressive. Here, well-drilled waitstaff serve fabulous modern cuisine with a personal touch. Opt for one of two set menus with four or six courses, one of which is vegan. There are also some à la carte dishes, and ‘grosses pièces’ such as fish in a salt crust can be ordered in advance (at least 2 people). The wine list includes a decent selection of Austrian labels as well as some big names from France and Italy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
671;Rouge Noir;Austria;Weissensee;Neusach 1, Weissensee, 9762, Austria;46.7164248;13.3104989;32;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Experience a truly unique dining concept: a chef's table, limited to 10 diners, in a private room on the first floor of the Neusacherhof hotel. With its decorative display of cookbooks, the space almost feels like a small library, and the atmosphere is especially intimate. A large window affords spectacular lake views over Weissensee and the surrounding meadows and mountains. Chef duo Stefan Glantschnig and David Traun present a 12-course tasting menu featuring beautifully composed, creative dishes, such as Amur carp and parasol mushroom or langoustine and tomato. The menu draws on the region's produce and culinary traditions but also incorporates flavours from around the globe. As an alternative to wine, non-alcoholic pairings are available. Service with a personal touch comes courtesy of owner Stefan Glantschnig, who serves and explains the dishes himself. A charming detail: the evening begins with a portion of freshly prepared popcorn and champagne.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
672;Waldschänke;Austria;Grieskirchen;Kickendorf 15, Grieskirchen, 4710, Austria;48.2450595;13.8353432;29;false;false;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;A family business par excellence! While owner Heinz Grabmer and his motivated team take care of the service side of things, Elisabeth Grabmer and son Clemens form a well-oiled machine in the kitchen. They skilfully navigate between classic and modern cuisine, the highlight of their handiwork being the two set menus. These feature dishes such as wonderfully rare fillet of Almenland ox accompanied by well-seasoned king trumpet mushrooms and oyster mushrooms with beautiful roasted notes and an aromatic small spelt foam finished with a terrific jus boasting shine and depth. The à la carte menu is a little more traditional – for example, creamed veal or baked carp. Thanks to its location on the edge of the forest, the garden terrace is a lovely spot in summer - ‘bird concert’ included!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
674;Wörgötter - Fine Dining;Austria;Ligist;Marktplatz 40, Ligist, 8563, Austria;46.9937365;15.2069035;88;true;false;Creative, French;Located in the centre of Ligist, this restaurant run by the Wörgötter family has won diners over with its twin dining concepts: "Wirtshaus" ("Traditional Inn") and "Fine Dining". The latter proposes creative, modern cuisine that draws on international influences. At the helm in the kitchen, Florian Wörgötter represents the third generation of the family and is supported by his father Mathias. The reasonably priced surprise menu impresses with well thought-out combinations that create interesting contrasts and are packed with wonderful flavours: yellowfin tuna, beer radish, jalapeño, shiso, or pork greaves, gyoza, pointed cabbage, brown butter. Select a bottle from the nicely curated wine list, or opt for harmonious wine pairings by the glass to set off the menu perfectly. Guests take their seats in the elegantly decorated rooms or, in summer, out on the terrace in front of the building. The service is charming and efficient, with the chef's partner and mother also forming part of the team. The bar in the entrance area invites you to linger for a nightcap.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
676;Tanglberg;Austria;Vorchdorf;Pettenbacher straße 3, Vorchdorf, 4655, Austria;48.0033128;13.9235021;86;false;false;French;The wrought-iron sign of the centuries-old Tanglberg announces the "gallery and restaurant" that lie behind the listed façade, where both contemporary art and good food await you. Maximilian Schellerer presides in the kitchen, serving up a clear cuisine, reduced to the essentials and featuring modern elements. Two five-course set menus are offered. The chef uses high-quality produce, such as fabulously fresh hand-dived scallops from Norway, brought to you pan-fried to perfection and delicately seasoned, or first-rate rack of lamb, herb-crusted with a light and aromatic crumb coating. Service is provided by the dedicated hostess, owner Friederike Maria Staudinger, who clearly takes great pleasure in her front-of-house role. They also have a number of guestrooms.;Interesting wine list;[]
677;Esslokal;Austria;Hadersdorf am Kamp;Hauptplatz 16, Hadersdorf am Kamp, 3493, Austria;48.4591171;15.7208653;98;false;false;Contemporary;When you enter the restaurant, the first thing you see is the open kitchen. The laid-back atmosphere in the various rooms is fantastic. Unique details and modern art truly define the space. In summer, tables are laid out beneath the boughs of a walnut tree on the terrace in the beautiful garden. Chef-patron Roland Huber draws on Asian influences to serve up creative cuisine. Fantastic dishes such as sweetbreads and carabinero, cauliflower, lemon leaf, hazelnut and truffle are available à la carte or in the form of a three- to six-course menu. The wine list is impressive, and equally noteworthy is the attentive and highly knowledgeable front-of-house team, led with a personal touch by the lady of the house. Dining here is a joy from start to finish.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
678;Die Forelle;Austria;Weissensee;Techendorf 80, Weissensee, 9762, Austria;46.7174377;13.2894545;100;false;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Nothing could make more sense here in the picturesque Weissensee Nature Park than to align the kitchen philosophy with the natural surroundings – the name of the set menu "BERG.SEE.KÜCHE." ("MOUNTAIN.LAKE.FOOD.") doesn't give away too much. In six courses – plus extras – patron Hannes Müller brings his own signature to creations such as "rhubarb, mountain brook trout, carrot, yarrow, sunflower seeds" or "red cabbage, venison, celery, miso". Light, fresh dishes, flavoured with herbs from the immediate vicinity or fermented foods from the previous season. When it comes to the quality of the ingredients, the restaurant relies on personal links with producers, eg sourcing Krainer Steinschaf mutton from the family's own farm – Zöhrer-Bauernhof. The wine list is centred on Austria, but also includes natural and orange wines. Cordial hostess and sommelier Monika Müller's commitment is palpable. The view from the modern restaurant across the meadows to the lake is fantastic. Stylish and elegant accommodation is available in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
679;Les Deux Kitzbühel - Brasserie & Bar;Austria;Kitzbühel;Franz-Reisch-Straße 7, Kitzbühel, 6370, Austria;47.4456666;12.3893438;71;false;true;Modern French;Does the name "Les Deux" sound familiar? Following in the footsteps of his Munich "original", Fabrice Kieffer's sophisticated concept has now also made its way here. Chef Marc Fröhlich specialises in classics such as pâté en croûte and steak au poivre, as well as more modern dishes (eg braised beetroot, feta, frisée, pomegranate). Wolfgang Hirn, meanwhile, manages the service team, and does so with style, expertise and charm. The atmosphere is elegant yet lively, making for a certain bistro vibe. You can also simply enjoy a glass of champagne at the beautiful bar. There is a small terrace in front of the building.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
680;Beef Club;Austria;Fiss;Laurschweg 28, Fiss, 6533, Austria;47.0552532;10.6105543;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;A terrific modern concept that would also be right at home in Vienna or Munich! This restaurant is to be found in the exclusive Schlosshotel at an altitude of 1 436m. The sophisticated and upscale decor boasts elegant dark colours and the atmosphere is lively. Mathias Seidel and Nikolaus Platteter are your chefs. The "Beef Club Menu", available in four or six courses (plus amuse-bouches and petits fours), includes delicate creations such as "Tristan crayfish, wakame, radish, green apple" - a vegetarian set menu is also available. Plus there is an à la carte selection featuring beautifully grilled cuts straight out of the Big Green Egg. The Austrian and international wine list is first class – specialities include the Romanée-Conti and Ornellaia selection, as well as magnum and double magnum bottles. The wine pairings by the glass are also very good - alternatively, there is a non-alcoholic beverage accompaniment. Skilful service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
681;Moritz;Austria;Grafenstein;Oberwuchel 5, Grafenstein, 9131, Austria;46.6318956;14.449163;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A little off the beaten track but well worth the trip! Surrounded by meadows and fields, this restaurant surprises with its upscale and modern decor. The bright and airy dining space has the feel of a conservatory. In summer, the glass walls can be opened to the beautiful garden, creating a terrace feeling. Anja-Margaretha Moritz, your warm and attentive hostess, adds a personal touch that definitely contributes to the almost intimate atmosphere. As for the food, under the direction of Roman Pichler, excellent regional produce is meticulously prepared and presented in pleasingly pared-down dishes that are rich in contrasts and yet beautifully harmonious. A great combination of delicate acidity and sweetness, herbal notes and floral accents makes the beetroot, dill and mustard seeds, as well as fennel blossoms, marigold and oxalis an extremely flavourful creation. There is a surprise menu comprising five or seven courses, which, alternatively, can be ordered individually – but you can also take a peek at the menu beforehand if you wish.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
682;Lieperts;Austria;Leutschach an der Weinstraße;Arnfelser Straße 2, Leutschach an der Weinstraße, 8452, Austria;46.6675112;15.4676211;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This establishment is officially named Lieperts Café, Dinner, Rooms, which accurately reflects its offerings: You can come for a wonderful breakfast Fri-Sun, then later in the day, a selection of appealing snacks and drinks are available. Owner and eponym Manuel Liepert serves up fine dining cuisine Mon-Tue and Fri-Sat (reservations required). This comes in the form of a five- to seven-course surprise menu preluded by a number of delectable amuse-bouches. Dishes such as chicken, papaya, peanut and sweet potato or pan-seared pike-perch, beurre blanc, green strawberry and mushrooms showcase a contemporary approach with regional and international influences. Maître d' Lisa Kürbisch provides interesting recommendations from the wine impressive list dominated by labels from the region. There are four tastefully decorated, modern guestrooms.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
685;Verdi;Austria;Linz;Pachmayrstraße 137, Linz, 4040, Austria;48.3417578;14.2711746;55;true;false;International, Creative;Located on the edge of a forest in the countryside above Linz, this restaurant is a fine dining institution in the city, thanks to the unwavering commitment of owner Erich Lukas. His son Philipp has now joined him in the kitchen. Their modern and pleasingly accessible cuisine based on classical foundations is pared back to the essentials, with the odd Asian influence thrown in here and there. Take, for example, the piglet belly cooked until crispy on the outside and wonderfully tender on the inside, combined with the subtle acidity of a Calamansi gel and served in an intense broth flavoured with the hot and spicy notes of Karashi mustard and the appealing pungency of lemongrass – a dish that represents the scale of their ambition and is real pleasure to eat! The chic interior (some tables with view of Linz), fantastic terrace, judicious wine suggestions, and exceedingly charming and professional service team also play their part.;Car park,Terrace;[]
686;Artis;Austria;Graz;Schmiedgasse 20, Graz, 8010, Austria;47.0689865;15.4390449;24;true;false;Creative, International;This restaurant located in the pedestrian area makes for an inviting eatery with its stylish interior done out in a palette of dark colours. Its surprise menu comprises four, six or eight courses. The modern and creative dishes are prepared using excellent international ingredients – a shining example of the first-rate quality of the ingredients is the hand-dived Norwegian scallops, flavoured and seasoned with daikon radish, wasabi, buttermilk and horseradish. Tip: Make a reservation at the chef's table to be seated right in front of the open kitchen!;;[]
687;Esszimmer - Everybody's Darling;Austria;Vienna;Tuchlauben 22, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2109718;16.3717636;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;An intriguing, innovative concept combining Tagesbar ("daytime bar", serving great cocktails) and Esszimmer (meaning "dining room"). Hidden behind a curtain, and with only a handful of covers, the stylish restaurant has a pleasantly private feel. They serve a modern set menu (a vegetarian version is available if pre-ordered), in which chef Alexander Kumptner incorporates the occasional and subtle Italian or Asian accent into his own style – "vongole, 'nduja, orzo, basil" is a good example. The focus is on the high quality of the ingredients. The professional and charming service runs like clockwork.;Air conditioning;[]
688;TIAN;Austria;Vienna;Himmelpfortgasse 23, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.20523;16.3744339;19;true;false;Vegetarian, Creative;This beacon of vegetarian gourmet cuisine proposes a set menu with six or eight courses that can also be vegan. The depth of flavour in the dishes such as "chioggia, radish, juneberry" or "king oyster mushroom, pumpkin, elderflower" is down to the technical prowess of the chef duo Paul Ivić and Florian Burtscher, as well as the fantastic quality of the ingredients, which are seasonal and locally sourced. There's a great selection of organic wines – alternatively, opt for one of the non-alcoholic beverage accompaniments. The waitstaff are warm and professional, and they always go about their work with a smile. The stylish decor incorporates modern design into a historical setting.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
689;Atelier Fischer;Austria;Sankt Gilgen;Ischler Straße 16, Sankt Gilgen, 5340, Austria;47.7655713;13.3678748;38;false;false;Creative;It's a shame you can't enjoy Stefan Fischer's high-calibre cuisine all year round. The surprise menu consists of five to eight contemporary and innovative courses, with dishes such as smoked South Burgenland pigeon from southern Burgenland with umeboshi plum, spelt, consommé, shiitake mushroom, elderberry and rowanberry. Wine pairing recommendations come courtesy of the amiable and highly qualified sommelier. This tastefully designed restaurant occupies the first floor of a modern pavilion on the waterfront promenade – as one would expect, spots on the terrace are much in demand. The floor-to-ceiling windows ensure spectacular views from inside, too. The establishment also runs a café on the ground floor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
690;dahoam by Andreas Herbst;Austria;Leogang;Rain 100, Leogang, 5771, Austria;47.4383683;12.7207056;20;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Having worked with some big names in the industry, such as Johanna Maier, Andreas Döllerer and Mario Lohninger, Andreas Herbst has returned home (dahoam in the local dialect) with his wife Andrea to take over the reins of Hotel Riederalm from his parents. His connection to his homeland is reflected in his culinary philosophy, as he finds creative ways to marry traditional with modern. This involves a lot of fermenting, pickling, foraging and even making white chocolate from local grains. In this regard, this restaurant is breaking new ground in the region. His set menu ("Journey through Leogang", in small, medium or large formats) includes "artichoke, egg yolk & tarragon" or "Leogang saddle of venison, fermented red cabbage & chestnuts". An original idea: a map made of white bull leather shows their local producers. Chic decor – ask for a table near the window for the view.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
691;Interalpen - Chef's Table;Austria;Telfs;Dr.-Hans-Liebherr-Alpenstraße 1, Telfs, 6410, Austria;47.331274;11.1187317;25;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Are you looking for a special kind of dining experience? In the restaurant of the Interalpen-Hotel Tyrol, in a fabulous location on the Seefeld high plateau, the eponymous Chef's Table is just the ticket. Diners are seated in the kitchen, at two high tables. Here, in the thick of the action, you can watch Mario Döring and his team at work – the chefs themselves also present their dishes. Harmonious combinations of different ingredients and textures in the creative courses are evident in the seasonal set menu, not least in the desserts by patissier Michael Hollaus – for example, he successfully marries the fruitiness of poached vineyard peach with the subtle acidity of champagne foam and the crunchiness of a layered almond tart. Diners can also opt for the wine or non-alcoholic drink pairings. This special "Chef's Table" experience is available by reservation and in the evening only (Mon-Fri).;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
692;[aend];Austria;Vienna;Mollardgasse 76, Vienna, 1060, Austria;48.1896429;16.3410168;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The clean and minimalist design immediately catches the eye, as do the striking brick arches overhead. The clear view into the open kitchen showcases the skill and dedication of Fabian Günzel's team. The pared-down interior is reflected in the set menu, which comprises up to 15 modern and creative courses, made using top-quality produce. Superb wine recommendations.;Air conditioning;[]
693;Mesnerhaus;Austria;Mauterndorf;Markt 56, Mauterndorf, 5570, Austria;47.133416;13.6785494;45;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Set in the Salzburg mountains, in the UNESCO Biosphere Park, Mesnerhaus has been run by Maria and Josef Steffner since 2007. The modern interior design within the venerable walls of this building dating back to 1420se, incorporates the historical architecture beautifully. An extremely warm and welcoming hostess, Maria is responsible for the wine cellar, restaurant and hotel, which has six cosy rooms and a suite. With just as much dedication, Josef delivers expressive, creative cuisine made from regional and seasonal produce, served as a set menu or à la carte. The signature dish Lungau potato with sour cream, egg yolk and Grüll caviar is fabulous.;Car park;[]
694;Die Geniesserstube im Alpenhof;Austria;Tux;Hintertux 750, Tux, 6294, Austria;47.115608;11.6841259;76;false;false;Alpine, Classic Cuisine;The Alpenhof hotel has created a really inviting space for its diners. The Genießerstube may be a dining option for hotel guests, but having been expertly set apart, it feels like a small restaurant in its own right. Diners take their seats in a cosy, elegant wood-panelled room with just a few tables and enjoy the attentions of an experienced, attentive and well-organised front-of-house team – the chefs occasionally deliver the food themselves. In his three- to six-course set menu, head chef Maximilian Stock draws on excellent produce to create clearly structured and flavourful dishes, such as sliced cabbage with sauerkraut beurre blanc, chives and pomme soufflée. And be sure to sample one of the desserts! Before or after your meal, why not head to the bar?;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
695;Gründler's Gourmet Stüberl;Austria;Achenkirch;Seestraße 35, Achenkirch, 6215, Austria;47.5088961;11.7040198;61;true;false;Classic Cuisine;A family business run with great warmth and commitment, where everyone pitches in. A father-and-son team is in charge of the kitchen, serving up a contemporary take on classic dishes in a four- to six-course set menu. Dishes such as female duck breast with celeriac, pickled plum and crispy cannelloni are rooted in French culinary tradition and showcase in-season and regional ingredients. However, there are also internationally influenced dishes, such as Alpine prawn with razor clam, pumpkin, yuzu and samphire. Gourmet Stüberl is a separate space in the restaurant area of Kulinarik Hotel Alpin. The decor is inviting and upscale, the atmosphere pleasantly intimate and the waitstaff charming and adept – you might even be served by one of the chefs. The wine list features a decent selection of Austrian as well as international labels. Should you wish to extend your stay, there are lovely guestrooms.;Car park,Great view;[]
696;APRON;Austria;Vienna;Am Heumarkt 35, Vienna, 1030, Austria;48.199514;16.3767832;72;true;true;Creative, Austrian;This tastefully designed restaurant is housed in Hotel Am Konzerthaus Vienna - MGallery, not far from the Stadtpark and the historical centre of Vienna. In the impressive open kitchen, modern dishes are meticulously prepared using seasonal ingredients. The internationally inspired dishes are beautifully plated and presented in a set menu comprising five or seven courses. The combination of stylish contemporary interior design and impeccable, attentive service creates a welcoming and enjoyable atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
697;Berggericht;Austria;Kitzbühel;Hinterstadt 15, Kitzbühel, 6370, Austria;47.4460509;12.390866;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;You enter this first-floor restaurant with a stylish and sophisticated interior via a narrow little street. Their four- or six-course set menu (also vegetarian on reservation), which they have dubbed "Tyrolean Feast", draws on elements of classic cuisine, but also skilfully incorporates modern accents and influences from the chef's Tyrolean homeland. Good examples of this are the yellowfin mackerel with a coriander and kiwi sauce and the Tyrolean free-range chicken ballotine with a poultry farce filling. Service is provided by an experienced and friendly team, who are happy to recommend the wines that best accompany the set menu.;Interesting wine list;[]
698;Hubertusstube;Austria;Neustift im Stubaital;Scheibe 44, Neustift im Stubaital, 6167, Austria;47.1082718;11.2996497;22;false;true;Classic Cuisine;In a cosy, elegantly rustic interior featuring pale wood panelling and decorative elements, guests are served classic and regional cuisine by a professional front-of-house team.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
699;Guat'z Essen;Austria;Stumm;Obere März 36, Stumm, 6275, Austria;47.2972176;11.8866642;27;false;true;Vegetarian, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant may be rather inconspicuously located on the edge of a small village, but it is certainly worthy of your attention. "From Permaculture to Table" is the concept behind it. Peter Fankhauser is doing remarkable work here in two respects: first, he keeps a 1 000m² permaculture garden and is therefore himself able to supply the restaurant with fruit and vegetables. Only cereals and dairy produce are sourced elsewhere in the region. Secondly, these ingredients are transformed into elaborate dishes that are brimming with flavour and aroma, complexity and intensity. They serve a single vegetarian set menu, which comprises nine courses on Wednesdays and Thursdays, and 13 courses on Fridays and Saturdays. Service starts at the same time for all diners, with explanations provided about the sustainable philosophy.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
700;Paznaunerstube;Austria;Ischgl;Dorfstr. 95, Ischgl, 6561, Austria;47.00865;10.28622;44;false;false;Contemporary, Innovative;With Martin Sieberer as head chef since 1996, this restaurant in the luxurious Hotel Tofana Royal is something of an institution. His two sons Thomas and Michael now support him as chefs in the kitchen, and together they turn out innovative dishes made from outstanding ingredients. Take, for example, the butter-soft sous-vide-cooked prime rib of Paznaun Highland beef with an intense port reduction, which lends great depth of flavour, accompanied by Jerusalem artichoke preparations in various textures. We highly recommend the "Royalmenü", a six-, eight- or 10-course set menu! The distinguished atmosphere smacks of Alpine sophistication. The service is unparalleled, with a well-coordinated and professional team catering to guests' every desire.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
701;Sigwart's Tiroler Weinstuben;Austria;Brixlegg;Marktstr. 40, Brixlegg, 6230, Austria;47.4278286;11.8770721;25;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The first written record of this fabulous inn dates back to 1774. It has now been run by the Sigwart family for six generations. The dedication of the chef-patron and her team is evident in every detail, from the cosy wood-panelled interior featuring a lovely tiled stove and antique farmhouse cupboards, to the charming and adept service and, of course, the delicious food. The cuisine is classic with the occasional Asian twist. The dishes are impressively robust in terms of flavour and in no way lacking in sophistication. Seated at beautifully laid tables, diners tuck into classics such as a light lobster foam soup with pike dumplings. The wine list, while not overly extensive, offers a high-quality selection, with a particularly noteworthy collection of magnums and whiskies.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
702;Guth;Austria;Lauterach;Wälderstraße 10, Lauterach, 6923, Austria;47.4718721;9.7311434;34;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The chef-patron at this modern restaurant regales his diners with seasonal dishes drawing on regional tradition as well as more international fare. The large windows look out onto the garden, which in summer boasts an appealing two-part terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
703;Mangold;Austria;Lochau;Pfänderstraße 3, Lochau, 6911, Austria;47.53006;9.75236;98;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This friendly family-run restaurant serving contemporary regional cuisine proposes a range of very different dining spaces. Stube is cosy and rustic, Rossini is Mediterranean and the Wintergarten is light and airy. Plus there is the secluded inner courtyard.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
704;Alpin Gourmet Stube;Austria;Sankt Anton am Arlberg;Sankt Jakober Dorfstraße 35, Sankt Anton am Arlberg, 6580, Austria;47.1407338;10.2830469;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in the quiet St Jakob district, the Jehle-Kathrein family's establishment is warm and welcoming. That goes for both the hotel, Gletscherblick, and the tastefully decorated, elegant little Alpine-style fine dining restaurant. Choose between the set menu of the day and the fine dining set menu, in which chef Paul Markovics presents a variety of flavours and interesting contrasts. He also places a strong emphasis on the region when it comes to his choice of ingredients. For example, he combines perfectly medium-rare fried and finely seasoned Tyrolean venison loin (of excellent quality!) with the smoothness of an intensely flavourful porcini purée, the rich nutty taste of a creamy, airy pistachio hollandaise and the fruity notes of dried peach. Astute wine recommendations – the selection is pleasingly down-to-earth and affordable.;Car park;[]
705;MAYER's Restaurant;Austria;Zell am See;Hofmannsthalstraße 10, Zell am See, 5700, Austria;47.3426236;12.8048614;77;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Creative;The location of this restaurant is rather exceptional, housed as it is in beautiful parkland. The building adjoins Schloss Prielau, which was first mentioned in a document dating back to 1425. Anette and Andreas Mayer have been putting their heart and soul into this place for over 20 years. Well-versed in classic culinary tradition, the chef-patron puts a modern and creative spin on top-notch produce, such as organic Tauern veal, which he serves four ways – tender fillet, sweetbreads, osso buco ravioli and braised cheek – with earthy notes of sweet and delicate beetroot and a potato tarte Tatin. Opt for a set menu with fish and meat or a vegetarian/vegan version. In an original touch, your senses are stimulated with house-made aromatic essences at the beginning and end of the meal. In a chic setting, the competent service team is led by your charming hostess, and sommelier Reinhard Walcher is on hand with excellent wine recommendations. You can stay overnight in cosy, comfortable guestrooms and suites. Close by is Lake Zell, with its own private lido.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
706;Z'SOM;Austria;Vienna;Gußhausstraße 12, Vienna, 1040, Austria;48.1974893;16.3718516;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine, South American;The name "Z'SOM" (meaning "together") conjures up a sense of community and culinary delight in a sociable and relaxed atmosphere. Your friendly hosts Judith Lergetporer and Diego Briones really put their heart and soul into this place. While she presides over the restaurant floor, welcoming guests with warmth and charm, he is at work in the open kitchen, skilfully incorporating his Chilean roots and international experience into original, flavourful and sophisticated dishes. Think premium-quality wild prawns with Amarillo chilli, succulent pigeon à la royale or delicious lavender ice cream infused with coconut. The lady of the house talks diners through the wine pairings that go with the set menu with real enthusiasm.;;[]
707;Esszimmer;Austria;Salzburg;Müllner Hauptstraße 33, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8066955;13.0341933;72;false;false;Creative, Classic Cuisine;As far as Salzburg's foodies are concerned, the Kaiblinger family's elegant restaurant with its vibrant, colourful decor is as important a landmark as the Mönchsberg. Made using excellent produce, Andreas Kaiblinger's culinary creations are classical in their foundations and full of flavour. He sparingly incorporates Asian and Mediterranean seasonings and gives his dishes a certain individuality. He and his team work meticulously to create punchy cuisine. Your charming maître d', Andrea Kaiblinger, has some fascinating wine recommendations up her sleeve. Delightful rear courtyard terrace!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
708;Austria Stuben;Austria;Obergurgl;Kressbrunnenweg 3, Obergurgl, 6456, Austria;46.8713805;11.0288489;88;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;This stylish little restaurant in the Gourmet & Wine Hotel Austria set at an altitude of 1 930m only has space for a handful of diners per service. In the modern-Alpine interior, high-calibre design meets beautiful old floor-to-ceiling wood panelling. The kitchen follows its own philosophy: the cuisine is close to nature and regionally sourced yet open to international influences. Carinthian-born head chef Verena Stattmann proposes a fine dining set menu in the evening – this is where she gives free rein to her passion for cooking, which is reflected not least in the distinctiveness of her cuisine. The menu name "Paradoxon" is a nod to the deliberate contrast of non-classic combinations, such as Carinthian salmon with raw and marinated kohlrabi and a velvety citrus emulsion. The attentive and professional service team is overseen by co-owner and sommelier Maximilian Steiner, who has a roughly 1 200-strong selection of wines at his fingertips. In addition to various wine pairings, there are also interesting non-alcoholic drinks designed to accompany the set menu.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
709;Ötztaler Stube;Austria;Sölden;Auweg 3, Sölden, 6450, Austria;46.9668234;11.0087392;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant in the Hotel Das Central has bags of character! Gorgeous Swiss pine panelling and furnishings create a warm and cosy atmosphere and exude a sense of tradition. The kitchen team prepares a set menu comprising five or seven courses, with a vegetarian version also available on request. The dishes draw on modern influences to showcase regional culinary tradition, featuring locally sourced ingredients such as Längenfeld salmon trout or fallow deer from Sölden. The dedicated front-of-house team provides courteous service and wine recommendations from over 30 000 bottles stored in the cellar!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
711;Bruderherz Fine Dine;Austria;Fiss;Oberer Spelsweg 6, Fiss, 6533, Austria;47.0533247;10.6233813;67;true;false;Creative;Housed in Das Marent hotel, this stylish fine dining restaurant with its modern Alpine-inspired decor fully lives up to the name. Brothers Alexander and Christian Marent pour their heart and soul into providing their guests with a memorable dining experience. Crafted with meticulous care and high-quality ingredients, the dishes of chef Christian Marent showcase a creative fusion of regional and international flavours. The Tyrolean salmon trout with radish and saffron vinegar, and the rack of lamb with chorizo, black-eyed beans, sweetcorn and jalapeño are fine examples of this successful blend of influences. The wine list primarily features Austrian and Spanish choices. Friendly and adept service.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
712;Gannerhof;Austria;Innervillgraten;Gasse 93, Innervillgraten, 9932, Austria;46.8065609;12.3753849;81;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Innovative;It is well worth making the journey from Silian up to this place steeped in over 300 years of tradition – perched at an altitude of around 1 400m, it promises a wealth of picturesque views. Not only do the three Villgrater farmhouses and the ‘Genussgarten’ form a beautiful, authentic sight, but you can also feel the connection with nature, the region and the people. Lots of local wood, plenty of ornaments, and modern touches here and there create a rustic cosiness in the various dining areas. Carola and Josef Mühlmann run the hotel together and are also both to be found working in the kitchen. In their seven-course menu the combination of aromatic goat curds, lightly sautéed and mildly marinated trout heart, delicately spiced oil and crispy kale leaf chips, for example, provides plenty of flavourful expression and an innovative touch. On the wine list: Austria and South Tyrol. Tip: You can also buy the delicious bread baked by the chef using flour from the own mill.;Car park;[]
714;Tudor Hall;Greece;Athens;3A Vasileos Georgiou A, Athens, 10564, Greece;37.9762768;23.7349329;84;false;true;Contemporary;If the idea of having lunch or dinner on the elegant rooftop of a hotel, with piano music in the background and the eternal Acropolis as a backdrop sounds appealing, then Tudor Hall is definitely the place, especially for a romantic candlelit supper – but make sure you book a table in advance. Here, on the 7th floor of the King George Hotel, next to the central Syntagma Square, chef Asterios Koustoudis (who is also executive chef of the adjacent Hotel Grande Bretagne, home to the GB Roof Garden restaurant) showcases his contemporary take on Greek cuisine that is built around a concise à la carte and one tasting menu. The end result is a superb mix of slick service, sommelier recommendations and meticulous cuisine featuring delicious dishes that are surprisingly technical and pleasing on the eye. Make sure you try the superb cod.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
716;Patio;Greece;Athens;11 Litous, Vouliagmeni, Athens, 16671, Greece;37.8138388;23.7739344;75;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in Vouliagmeni (an upmarket beach area on the shores of the Saronic Gulf just half an hour from Athens), this restaurant occupying a delightful internal patio in The Margi luxury hotel will come as a pleasant surprise. Here, in a verdant setting away from the centre of Athens, it is much easier to showcase the restaurant’s “From Farm to Fork” philosophy and concept. Chef Panagiotis Giakalis’ cuisine is presented on two tasting menus that champion modern Greek cooking of a high technical level, with particular emphasis on flavours from Greece and from the wider Mediterranean, wherever possible using ingredients (eggs, vegetables, fruit, olive oil, wine etc) sourced from their own estate. The covered side porch, the olive trees planted in huge pots, and the romantic candlelit ambience at night are particularly impressive, plus the hotel also owns a farm that guests can visit and enjoy a meal in beautiful natural surroundings.;Terrace;[]
717;Hervé;Greece;Athens;170 Trion Ierarchon Street, Athens, 118 52, Greece;37.9668533;23.7094435;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Hervé’s three co-owners are heavily involved in the smooth running of this modern restaurant, situated a little way from the centre but well connected thanks to its location next to the Petralona metro stop. Herve Pronzato is the French-born executive chef who has lent his name to the business, ably assisted by Grigoris Kikis (a young Greek chef who is constantly seeking excellence in his cooking) and George Efthimopoulos (an expert in hospitality and the restaurant’s general manager). One of the special features of this young, informal eatery is the elegant French-style yet Japanese-inspired counter where guests can watch the chefs at work (the latter serve dishes personally and are happy to explain their preparation in detail). The cuisine is centred around a single tasting menu featuring fusion dishes influenced by French, Asian and Italian cooking. You’ll need to book ahead, and when you do you’ll receive a digital code that will let you through the front door!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
718;Hytra;Greece;Athens;1 Petrou Kokkali Street, Athens, 11521, Greece;37.9820541;23.7537128;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If you’re looking for a restaurant with plenty of innate charm, this could be the perfect option for you. Hytra is located inside the lush garden of Megaron Music hall, in a modern building that blends the fine aspects of contemporary design, the breathtaking view of Athens and the Athenian sky. Housing a balcony, a unique dining experience is offered under the stars and a warm, atmospheric inside dining area where guests can enjoy memorable dining experiences. The contemporary-style Greek cuisine on offer here, featuring fine textures and meticulous presentation, is based around Greek ingredients and herbs grown in the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, all of which are very clearly evident in its sauces, creams, seasonings, and even its cocktails. Choose between the à la carte and tree enticing tasting menus, one of which (Think Green) is vegetarian.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
719;CTC Urban Gastronomy;Greece;Athens;15 Plateon Street, Athens, 10435, Greece;37.9804964;23.7168694;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If a dining experience under the stars appeals to you, this highly-sought-after restaurant, particularly during the summer months, will definitely fit the bill thanks to its charming urban terrace dotted with verdant trees and shrubs. Nor will the interior disappoint, with an elegant dining room decorated in soft colours and boasting a sophisticated ambience and subdued lighting. Here, chef Alexandros Tsiotinis, ably supported by his team, champions modern Mediterranean cuisine that is characterised by dishes that are meticulously prepared and extremely creative. More often than not based around classic dishes, including some from abroad, these are showcased in options Such as sea bass ceviche, Pesto calamari and a reinterpreted version of Tarte tatin. The surprise 11-course tasting menu is gradually revealed by serving staff as if they are unveiling a secret. You can also choose some excellent wine pairings to accompany you on this gastronomic journey!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
720;Spondi;Greece;Athens;5 Pyrronos Street, Athens, 116 36, Greece;37.9653138;23.7431159;59;true;false;French;In this elegant restaurant close to a busy square behind the ancient Panathenaic Stadium, enjoy highly professional service, attractive vaulted dining rooms, and two Mediterranean-inspired terraces perfect for alfresco dining and a romantic candlelit supper. The cooking here is centred around elaborate and highly visual contemporary French cuisine that is showcased via an array of à la carte dishes as well as on an enticing “Discovery” tasting menu. Seasonal produce is very much to the fore here, although some ever-popular ingredients (crab, langoustine, lamb, chocolate etc) feature all year round. Particularly friendly and attentive service is a constant here!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
721;The Zillers;Greece;Athens;54 Mitropoleos, Athens, 10563, Greece;37.9757055;23.7294908;90;true;true;Contemporary, Greek;This restaurant occupies the former family home of the German architect Ernst Zillers, who came to Athens to design some of its public buildings, fell in love with the city and remained here for the rest of his life. The building, which is situated next to the Greek Orthodox cathedral and has now been converted into a hotel (Zillers Boutique Hotel), boasts a rooftop terrace and multi-purpose Roof Garden with fine view of the cathedral and the Acropolis. During the day it serves light meals and snacks, but in the evening chef Vasilis Roussos and his team spring into action here! He offers two tasting menus: Synecdoche and Synthesis, both with creative dishes of traditional Greek influence and touches of international flavour. One standout dish was the Prawn Valley, a refreshing combination of raw prawns with a delicate tomato sauce, bergamot and kumquat that will definitely leave a lasting memory. The wine list also features a variety of Greek options to pair with your meal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
723;Soil;Greece;Athens;5 Ferekidou Street, Athens, 116 35, Greece;37.9669545;23.7429946;53;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;There are few restaurants that are able to convey a connection between food, nature and a love for their country, but here chef Tasos Mantis manages to express his full passion for all three through his cooking. The experience starts with a presentation of some of the ingredients that will be used in your dishes, many are sourced from the garden overseen by the chef’s father. At Soil, the stars of the show are the vegetables, and above all the aromatic herbs, which are showcased on a single tasting menu that transmits originality, creativity and, first and foremost, quality. Located just a few steps from the Panathenaic stadium (the setting for the first Olympic Games of the modern era), occupies a house with a romantic patio shaded by orange and lemon trees. It also features a chef’s table, enabling guests to interact with the chef at close quarters as he prepares his dishes. An excellent selection of wines and a highly original non-alcoholic drinks pairing option adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
724;Fleur de Sel;Serbia;Novi Slankamen;Počenta bb, Novi Slankamen, 22323, Serbia;45.16454;20.19224;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;It’s well worth travelling the 60-odd kilometres from the centre of Belgrade to get to this fascinating property serving fine cuisine and excellent wines. The restaurant is situated within the Atelje Vina Šapat winery and is surrounded by 12 hectares of vines planted with Merlot, Franconia, Cabernet Sauvignon and Teroldego red grape varieties, as well as Chardonnay, Moscato and Sauvignon Blanc (for the white wines). The dining room is elegant, classic and contemporary in style, with large windows that allow guests to enjoy extensive views of the peaceful Danube, the vineyards and the verdant countryside all around. Here, the talented chef Nikola Stojaković serves cuisine that is inspired by Serbian traditions and local ingredients, adding his own personalised creativity influenced by his many years working abroad. Guests can choose à la carte-style or from three tasting menus – we particularly recommend the interesting “From the Danube to the Adriatic” menu which features a selection of fresh- and saltwater fish. If you’re looking for a culinary experience that takes you closer to the kitchen where you can watch the chefs at work, then opt for the chef’s table. Finally, the wine list boasts 500 diverse labels with a truly international focus, although our obvious recommendation is to try the wines produced by the winery itself, guided by the passion and expertise of sommelier Dušan Vranić.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
725;Langouste;Serbia;Belgrade;Kosančićev Venac 29, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8176948;20.450754;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated on the edge of the historic centre, this restaurant boasts large picture windows offering views of the Sava river and the more modern part of the city. At the helm in the kitchen, Marko Deric is a young and passionate chef who has returned to Belgrade after working in different restaurants around Europe. His cuisine focuses on Serbian recipes and ingredients which he reinterprets with imaginative and contemporary touches influenced by France and Italy. There are three tasting menus – two five-course options (one meat, the other fish) and the eight-course “Langouste” which includes the best of the other two menus. Some of the vegetables are sourced from a biodynamic kitchen garden on the outskirts of Belgrade.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
726;IDAM by Alain Ducasse;Qatar;Doha;5th Floor, Museum of Islamic Art, Corniche Promenade, Doha, Qatar;25.2957162;51.5393359;50;true;true;French Contemporary;Take the lift to the top floor of the extraordinarily beautiful Museum of Islamic Art and wonder at the glorious views over the Bay – then head to this equally stunning restaurant. Relax in the high-backed leather chairs and choose one of the seasonal tasting menus (there is a shorter one at lunch). This is all about refined and sophisticated contemporary French dishes, with many of them finished tableside by the charming staff who talk you through the preparations. Whether lamb or quail, asparagus or beetroot, each component is exquisite in every sense. Desserts, such as chocolate and orange ravioli, are equally memorable.;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
727;Jamavar;Qatar;Doha;Al Corniche Street, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.3185882;51.5363128;31;false;true;Indian;Part of a small international group, this Indian restaurant is named after the intricate 16th-century shawls of Kashmir and sits inside the Sheraton Grand Hotel. It’s a smart spot, with a mix of modern and traditional elements in its décor. The extensive menu covers all regions of India, from Old Delhi butter chicken to Kerala-style beef, and includes refined small plates and several dishes from the tandoor such as succulent lamb chops. Fine ingredients are used and bold flavours are delivered, with the spicing impressively well-judged.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
728;Pajta;Hungary;Őriszentpéter;Templomszer 7, Őriszentpéter, 9941, Hungary;46.8498752;16.4043202;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Pajta means ‘barn’, which is where it all began for Flóra and Ferenc – in the small barn beside this glass-fronted restaurant. The whole complex has a natural feel, from the beautiful meadow to the two-storey, nature-inspired forest lodges 1km down the road (they arrange transportation). Menus change with the seasons and perfectly reflect the area, championing produce from Őrség in historical Hungarian dishes. Fermenting and pickling are a feature, adding a welcome punch to the flavour-packed creations. Neighbouring Austria and Slovenia join Hungary for a tri-country wine pairing experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
729;Rumour;Hungary;Budapest;Petőfi Tér 3, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.4938437;19.0506611;15;true;true;Creative;After travelling the world, Chef Jenő returned home to open this unique restaurant. Located in the heart of the city, it comes with concrete walls hung with mirrors, and a 21-seater counter which wraps around the large open kitchen. Red leather stools and placemats provide colour, while a trendy soundtrack adds to the vibe. The set menu showcases elements from Jenő’s travels via a series of refined, creative, sometimes playful dishes that burst with flavour. These are matched by some serious wine pairings, with the Hungarian option offering some wonderfully unique, bespoke choices.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
730;Salt;Hungary;Budapest;Királyi Pál utca 4, Budapest, 1053, Hungary;47.4904;19.05914;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Within a boutique hotel sits this small, sophisticated restaurant, whose open kitchen forms an integral part of the stylishly lit room. Shelves are full of jars containing colourfully preserved foraged fruits, vegetables and herbs, and the butter, lardo and Mangalitsa ham are all produced in-house. The surprise set menu is made up of intricate, exquisitely constructed dishes – many of which are updated versions of classic Hungarian recipes – and tables all face the wood-clad ‘pass’, where the chefs assemble the dishes with skill and dexterity.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
731;Borkonyha Winekitchen;Hungary;Budapest;Sas utca 3, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.4993951;19.0524595;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;While it would be easy to do, to pass by this unassuming-looking restaurant near the Basilica would be a mistake. The kitchen here sources top-class ingredients, treats them with the utmost respect and allows them to shine. Subtle Hungarian influences run throughout dishes which are well-conceived, skilfully executed and have a notable intensity of flavour. There is an à la carte, but go for the tasting menu for the best experience. Wines are key here too: they offer 100 labels, including some of Hungary’s top producers, with many available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
732;42;Hungary;Esztergom;Széchenyi tér 23, Esztergom, 2500, Hungary;47.7931391;18.7415203;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A colourful townhouse with a striking glass cube extension plays host to this series of intimate dining rooms. Like the building itself, the philosophy they follow is one of constant evolution, perfectly summed up by the tasting menu’s name: ‘Heritage and Inspiration’. Assured, skilful cooking has a Hungarian heart and honest flavours, but the kitchen also likes to spark curiosity, so you’ll find dishes like Mangalitsa sausage and crunchy cabbage with a paprika, red pepper, sour cream and dill oil sauce. An impressive wine cellar adds to the experience, as do the luxuriously appointed suites.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
733;essência;Hungary;Budapest;Sas utca 17, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.5010955;19.0521322;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Portuguese;Portuguese Chef-Owner Tiago and his Hungarian wife Éva have created a warmly run and deliciously different restaurant in the heart of the city. A bright front room with arched windows leads past the open kitchen to a more intimate room where patches of blue and white tiling hint at Tiago’s heritage. At dinner, pick from 5 or 7 courses – some have choices, allowing you to lead with either Portuguese or Hungarian influences, or to combine them for the best of both worlds. The interesting, flavour-packed dishes are poised and elegant, and Tiago has a deft touch when it comes to seasoning.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
735;Costes;Hungary;Budapest;Ráday utca 4, Budapest, 1092, Hungary;47.4889155;19.0621952;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Elegance and sophistication lead the way at Costes, from the smart décor to the well-orchestrated service. Ask for a seat to the front of the main room for a feeling of space, then enjoy the eager anticipation as the sommelier presents an exceptional, mostly Hungarian wine selection. The modern 7 course tasting menu comprises memorable dishes which not only look stunning with their bright colours and artistic style, but are packed with vibrant, complementary flavours. Seasonality plays an important role here too, with the featured ingredients always informing you of what’s in season right now.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
736;Joo Ok;USA;New York;22 W. 32nd St., 16th Fl., New York, 10001, USA;40.747503;-73.9867244;37;false;false;Korean, Contemporary;This Seoul transplant has an unusual entrance—via freight elevator up 16 floors—but the elegant space is instantly inviting. Echoing a traditional Korean home, guests are welcomed with savory crackers and drinks before being escorted to the dining room, where a minimalist design is juxtaposed with views of the Manhattan skyline. Joo Ok delivers a Korean tasting menu that is rooted in tradition but presented through a modern lens. Dishes are stunning, as in the jat jeup chae - tender lobster and Korean pear tucked inside salted cucumber slices. Makgeolli bread topped with freshwater eel is a dramatic single bite, but their signature deul gi reum with diced geoduck, spotted shrimp, and a whole quail egg in house-pressed perilla seed oil is equally memorable.;Air conditioning;[]
737;Shota Omakase;USA;Brooklyn;50 S. 3rd St., Brooklyn, 11249, USA;40.7135237;-73.9659318;52;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Far from the subway stop on a quiet street in Williamsburg, find this welcoming omakase counter hidden away near Domino Park. Chef Cheng Lin sets the tone as a friendly, relaxed guide for the night’s proceedings. And whereas some chefs practically take vows of silence with regards to sourcing and technique, he is quick to share where in Japan the fish is from, why he uses Inochi-no Ichi rice, and what it took to find his special aged soys and vinegars. His intentionality delivers in the form of excellent, seasonal product and a fine-tuned parade of nigiri, for which the rice is refreshed repeatedly. Prepared dishes like binchotan-seared sawara with citrus sauce, shiso, and nori or even a restorative cup of dashi with mushrooms also show distinction.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
738;Bar Miller;USA;New York;620 E. 6th St., New York, 10009, USA;40.7240177;-73.9806355;49;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;From the team behind Rosella, this diminutive spot with a sprinkling of seats steers clear of the familiar minimalist design, favoring bold colors and eye-catching details (note the custom pottery displayed behind the counter).These confident chefs deliver an omakase that is a showpiece of sustainable sourcing, much of it local—even the rice is sourced from New York state. Their personality is evident in dishes such as daikon vichyssoise with wakame butter-braised greens and gently poached salmon. Dry-aged fluke topped with apple ice in a sweet soy sauce holds its own, while the duo of uni and the mellow, dry-aged mackerel with yuzu kosho are two standouts from the nigiri course. Desserts, like the amazake and the corn gelato with caviar, round out the singular experience.;Counter dining;[]
739;Torrisi;USA;New York;275 Mulberry St., New York, 10012, USA;40.724364;-73.9952778;25;true;false;Contemporary, Italian-American;There is perfection in the details at Torrisi, where waiters are crisply dressed in dinner jackets and tables are draped in pressed linens, but the buzzy warmth is as charming as the good looks. Nestled inside the landmark Puck Building, this highly imaginative restaurant expertly balances the creative and the familiar. Nothing feels copied or contrived, and while some of the dishes may seem familiar, they've all been revamped with panache. The team caters to excited diners who feast on items like the escarole and endive salad and chicken stracciatella soup with textbook chicken broth, fluffy egg and savory meatballs. It's the boule, baked, finished on the grill and filled with dreamy clams, that's pure aromatic bliss.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
740;Noz 17;USA;New York;458 W. 17th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7435866;-74.0058783;46;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;This downtown sibling of the impressive Upper East original is elegant and inviting.The seven-seat cypress counter is the focal point of the intimate dining room, where an abundance of wood and gently calibrated lighting produce a serene setting.Chef Junichi Matsuzaki is highly skilled and talented. The omakase shows off the chef's free-wheeling style with a procession that keeps the palate stimulated. Otsumami, sashimi and nigiri all show off an impressive display of top-notch product that has been expertly treated and handled. A slice of pearlescent white cuttlefish, intricately scored so it practically melts in the mouth, accompanied by a mouth-coating demitasse of snapper bone broth, are just two of the delights presented to diners.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
742;Rezdôra;USA;New York;27 E. 20th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7390046;-73.9890088;21;true;true;Italian, Regional Cuisine;If you’ve been lucky enough to sample the ethereal cuisine of Emilia-Romagna, you’re in for a treat at Chef Stefano Secchi's cherished osteria. Nestled into a well-designed space in the Flatiron District, this cheerful spot brings the Italian region’s signature cuisine stateside.Rotating specials and pastas top the charts, and the regional pasta tasting is a sleeper hit. It takes guts to serve a handful of penne with pomodoro sauce or two tortellini in chicken brodo, but when pasta is as refined as this, nobody is complaining. Starters like the feather-light gnocco fritto with mortadella and Prosciutto di Parma, bookended by an appealingly restrained dessert like parmesan cheesecake crowned by citrus gelée, all but guarantee a return visit.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
743;La Bastide by Andrea Calstier;USA;North Salem;721 Titicus Rd., North Salem, 10560, USA;41.3376917;-73.5630221;74;false;true;French;Head to this modern farmhouse in Westchester where a soothing design perfectly complements sweeping views of the pastoral landscape. Husband and wife duo Chef Andrea Calstier and General Manager Elena Oliver are at ease in their intimate dining room, a space fit with only a few tables and perfectly calibrated for the tasting to come. The menu draws on their upbringing in the south of France. A simple-sounding salad is so much more with grilled gem lettuce paired with poached celtuce, cured egg yolk, and an olive oil sabayon. Squab with rosemary and fig leaf is as accomplished as grilled black sea bass with artichokes and razor clams. Dessert is a particular strength, and the combination of chocolate with goat cheese is a thrilling finale.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
744;Shmoné;USA;New York;61 W. 8th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7332903;-73.9986028;67;false;true;Israeli, Middle Eastern;This small, sleek space punches way above its weight with dazzling neo-Levantine cuisine. Many kitchens boast about using fresh ingredients, but Shmoné takes that philosophy to another level, creating a new menu daily (though some items stick around). The cooking relies on the grill all the way through to dessert, where grilled figs atop Chantilly cream have made an appearance. Dishes aren't repeated but they're certainly memorable, as in thin slices of hamachi or flatiron Wagyu slid off a skewer tableside and boasting smoky tenderness. The flavors are impressively dialed in and make for a focused meal that is surprisingly approachable and humble.The interior has a celebratory ambience—snag a seat at the counter for views of the bar and open kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
746;Corima;USA;New York;3 Allen St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7146562;-73.9929074;88;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;On the edge of Chinatown, Chef Fidel Caballero is not holding anything back. Whether you sit at the kitchen counter for the ambitious tasting menu or order à la carte in the boisterous dining room, the cooking is a singularly original and bold celebration of Mexican cuisine. If anything, there must be an order of sourdough tortillas somewhere on the table. Made with Sonoran wheat and chicken fat, these delicate, perfectly griddled discs served with recado negro butter will lock in a return visit. Better yet, this won’t be the only course worth returning for. The likes of lobster nicuatole, black cod with salsa Veracruzana, and sweetbreads with bitter almond foam make for lasting impressions. From the bar, find Mexican spirits and natural wines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
747;Jua;USA;New York;36 E. 22nd St., New York, 10010, USA;40.740014;-73.9874479;60;true;true;Korean, Korean Contemporary;Several years in, and Chef Hoyoung Kim and his team continue to deliver their promise of a nicely poised, modern Korean prix-fix that is both familiar and substantial. Jook with smoked eel and sesame is as comforting as it is refined, while crispy seaweed cradling tuna tartare and rice capped with caviar is as luxurious of a start as one could hope for. Have you ever seen a banchan as minimalist and as impactful as this one? Probably not. Dinner typically ends with a glazed Korean-style donut and a silky-smooth orb of ice cream. All the while, this slim and sleek restaurant is right at home being in such close proximity to the Flatiron Building thanks to its soaring ceilings, sultry lighting and a packed dining room humming with energy.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
748;One White Street;USA;New York;1 White St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7193546;-74.006101;59;true;true;Contemporary;This 19th-century townhouse, once the downtown hangout for John Lennon and Yoko Ono, has been transformed into a destination of culinary excellence, thanks to Chef Austin Johnson. The lower level operates more like a wine bar with crowds aplenty, while the higher floors offer the same seasonal tasting menu, starring products sourced from their upstate farm. Bold and clever flavors come easily to this kitchen team, as seen in cheddar gougères garnished with caviar and lemon zest, followed by a melting square of braised lamb with black garlic purée and charred Chinese celery.Gorgeous marble, superb tile work and modern light fixtures decorate the intimate and attractive wood-clad space.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
749;bōm;USA;New York;17 W. 19th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7396183;-73.9924497;55;true;true;Korean, Contemporary;This modern counter tucked behind sister restaurant Oiji Mi showcases contemporary Korean fare with a focus on wagyu beef. The space itself is a stunner with soaring ceilings, sharply dressed servers, and a spacious marble counter that has built-in barbecue grills. These grills quietly work throughout the evening, searing off premium cuts such as tenderloin, short rib, and ribeye that are kept in a dry-aging chamber in full view of the dining room. But know that there is more at play here than just beef. The likes of uni, caviar, truffles, and crab make appearances, and the kitchen has no qualms about stacking such luxury on top of one another. Recent highlights include a croustade of baesuk, jujube, and tofu as well as bone broth with radish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
751;Tuome;USA;New York;536 E. 5th St., New York, 10009, USA;40.724194;-73.9828;15;false;false;Fusion, Asian Contemporary;Classically trained Chef Thomas Chen is the one to thank for the fabulous Tuome. It's an Asian-inspired menu, which is no surprise as the chef is a master of weaving together ingredients to delicious and surprising effect. The intimate space is outfitted with a backlit bar, bay windows, and comfortable purple seats. Service is fittingly unfussy yet deeply knowledgeable. Don’t miss the seared octopus served atop pork XO sauce or the lamb chops, served perfectly medium rare and finished with a shishito chimichurri, black pepper jus, and a dollop of onion soubise. Finally, deep-fried buns which arrive as Chinese “beignets” accompanied by vanilla ice cream laced with red bean paste, goat's milk caramel, and yuzu marmalade render dessert wholly unmissable.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
752;Dirt Candy;USA;New York;86 Allen St., New York, 10002, USA;40.71794;-73.99087;27;true;false;Vegetarian, Vegan;Chef Amanda Cohen was an advocate of vegetable- and plant-based cooking long before it was cool, and her Lower East Side flagship continues to flourish as a pioneer in ethical eating with refined technique. Now, it enters an exciting new chapter in its long history. A single tasting menu yields a breadth of dishes that never masquerade as meat. A simple-seeming salad is anything but, with a blend of fresh and pickled iceberg lettuce with roasted celtuce, crispy puffed rice, and labneh that hits every mark. Then, a single yeasted donut is filled with a tomato, topped with smoked feta, and finished with concassé cherry tomatoes for an inventive take on a single ingredient. Dessert, too, follows in the same imaginative vein, with savory onions making their way into sweet dishes. A meal of this caliber is a true experience, and guests are sure to leave feeling nourished.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
753;Casa Mono;USA;New York;52 Irving Pl., New York, 10003, USA;40.735895;-73.9873421;62;true;true;Spanish, Contemporary;There’s something reassuring about a kitchen that gets in whole beasts and does its own butchery—you just know it understands the essence of what good cooking is all about. Here at the small but perfectly formed Casa Mono, dishes are none of those one-bite wonders that blight so many places these days. Nor do they arrive in a stampede at your table. Instead, they are sent out in a sensible order, for the benefit of the diner rather than the convenience of the kitchen.The cuisine is nominally influenced by the Costa Brava, but its reach is far greater than that and the tapas are especially refined. Scrambled eggs with uni is a must, while confit goat will make you question why you don’t see more of it on other menus. This is food to cure what ails you.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
754;Kosaka;USA;New York;220 W. 13th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.738316;-74.00137;30;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Chef Yoshihiko Kousaka is in control of this beloved sushiya, which offers a stellar omakase in an elegant setting. The dining room flaunts a classic Japanese sensibility—outfitted with a counter for 12, a few tables, soft piano music, as well as an attentive staff that enhance the overall experience.Some counters like to keep everyone in sync, but Chef Kousaka is more flexible. It is certainly a rigorous balancing act, but he moves with confidence and skill. Fish is minimally embellished, relying instead on impeccable technique. Highlights include everything from red snapper and Japanese sea bass to wild winter yellowtail and firefly squid. Supplemental items such as fresh or seared uni or a crisp bowl of oshinko moriwase, are also available and can augment your meal. For hand rolls and dessert, visit sister spot, Maki Kosaka.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
755;Daniel;USA;New York;60 E. 65th St., New York, 10065, USA;40.7667521;-73.9675039;68;true;true;French;Daniel is a classic New York restaurant. For over thirty years, this fine dining room has been the spot for brokering deals and celebrating special occasions. With art from James Rosenquist complementing the coffered ceilings capped with signature Bernardaud porcelain chandeliers, it remains an iconic Upper East Side spot.Executive Chef Eddy Leroux's multicourse tasting menus showcase high-quality ingredients and classic French cuisine. Recent highlights have included the kataifi-crusted Alaskan wild salmon topped with roe and crispy skin, followed by a half-moon of macadamia mousseline with praline, cookie ruse, and a cherry brandy anglaise. As might be expected, the wine list features an impressive collection of French wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
756;Restaurant Yuu;USA;Brooklyn;55 Nassau Ave., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7233627;-73.9521628;37;true;true;French Contemporary, Japanese;At the start of service, the lights dim and servers pull back curtains to reveal the full kitchen team dressed in stark whites and standing at attention. This is just the beginning of a carefully choreographed performance by Chef Yuu Shimano, whose classic French training and Japanese heritage translates to beauty and boldness on the plate. The lengthy menu celebrates top-grade shellfish and proteins that waver between light and indulgent. Think smoked surf clam with celeriac or abalone risotto with nori powder. The signature duck and foie pastry is a treasure from another era, while a pre-dessert “mojito” is a sweet flash of modern-day brilliance. The warehouse-chic space is impressive in scale and carefully tended to by a quiet but attentive team.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
757;The Four Horsemen;USA;Brooklyn;295 Grand St., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.7129264;-73.9574999;84;false;true;American, Californian;Reservations are required or be ready to queue at this eternally cool Williamsburg wine bar part-owned by LCD Soundsystem frontman, James Murphy. Four Horseman's wine list is eclectic and laser-focused on varietals, and Chef Nick Curtola's succinct and seasonally changing menu rarely misses.Start with the veal sweetbread skewers with soy-cured egg yolk. Or the crisp chickpea crepe, woven with pieces of squash blossoms that lures you in with a layer of glistening lardon. Fried skate wing comes to you deep golden and impossibly crisp, and the Berkshire pork is tender with a hint of cider glaze. Let the sociable staff talk you into closing over a silky crème caramel topped with deeply toasted crispy bits of soba.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
758;L’Abeille;USA;New York;412 Greenwich St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7219387;-74.0099509;20;true;false;French, Contemporary;L’Abeille reflects the luxurious charms of TriBeCa from its corner perch in this prized zip code. The restaurant is a darling space designed to the hilt with velvet cushioned seats and booths, a striking marble bar and handsome tables set with Christofle cutlery. The young Chef Mitsunobu Nagae is a calm, collected presence in the open kitchen, and years spent working at Joël Robuchon restaurants worldwide are evident. A harmonious union of French cooking with Japanese sensibilities, Nagae’s food is immediately approachable. From grilled trout with Champagne caviar sauce and scallion oil to lychee mousse with strawberry and shiso, each course is a vision of refinement. Charming servers in fitted suits roam the floor, keeping close watch on every seat.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
759;Family Meal at Blue Hill;USA;New York;75 Washington Pl., New York, 10011, USA;40.7319711;-73.9996385;51;true;false;American;Knowing when to leave something alone, whether you’re a painter, singer or cook, requires confidence in your material and your own ability. Dan Barber’s New York City outpost displays its utter trust in the products at hand by not interfering with them too much but also by giving them space to let their natural flavors shine.This intimate, sophisticated space is as popular as ever and the team clearly shares the chef's passion and pride. There is just one menu, a fixed, seasonally inspired menu dominated by vegetables (sourced from the upstate Blue Hill at Stone Barns) with grains and some proteins woven throughout the meal. Served family-style, there is a relaxed elegance to dining here, where sustainability guides every move.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
760;Francie;USA;Brooklyn;134 Broadway, Brooklyn, 11249, USA;40.7103459;-73.9637588;65;true;false;Contemporary, Italian;Francie is headed by John Winterman and native New Yorker, Chef Chris Cipollone. Set within a striking, limestone-clad building in South Williamsburg, this haven features sleek ash wood and mosaic tile flooring, exposed red brick walls, and widely spaced tables.The open kitchen is a true-to-life stage for this team, who can be seen prepping, cooking, and putting the finishing touches on a series of Mediterranean-style plates. Pasta is a must, as in the conchiglie with a luscious clam sauce. Shelled clams, bits of bacon, and sesame breadcrumbs complete the delightful preparation. Lamb is a springtime treat when dressed with green garlic persillade and young onion soubise. Caramelized apple atop buttery cake with crème fraîche and green apple brunoise is a fine finale to the array of impressive cuisine offered here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
761;Crown Shy;USA;New York;70 Pine St., New York, 10005, USA;40.7067068;-74.0087206;46;true;true;Contemporary, American;Crown Shy occupies a stunning setting in the landmark Art Deco tower, 70 Pine Street. The striking lobby leads to a modern dining room with soaring ceilings, marble floors, and expansive windows. It’s an undeniable feast for the senses, the energy made all the more palpable thanks to a long bar and an upbeat playlist. The kitchen, meanwhile, moves like clockwork with an approachably creative style. Gruyère fritters are a classic, as are the pillowy ricotta gnocchi, sometimes finished with vin jaune or, if the season is right, shaved white truffles. Charred carrots with razor clams and coconut curry as well as beef carpaccio with bagna cauda and lavash impress as well. Entrees like the jang-glazed pork katsu are begging to be shared.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
762;Oxomoco;USA;Brooklyn;128 Greenpoint Ave., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7300224;-73.9555039;100;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Don’t let the casual ambience fool you: Oxomoco is a serious dining room capable of great things in its wood-fired oven. The room is lively and packed but always conducive to conversation.Tacos are the main draw, especially when piled with the likes of tender flank steak or soft-shell crab. However, this kitchen team doesn’t stick to merely one dish or area of Mexico. Instead, they reach widely across a myriad of regions, always balancing abundance with fresh and vibrant flavors. The menu thereby tempts and tantalizes with such large and small items as the tropical hamachi agua chile and tlayuda crafted from smoky corn on a shell. Other standouts include the brined, fried and smoked “giant chicken.";Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
763;Yoshino;USA;New York;342 Bowery, New York, 10012, USA;40.7262829;-73.9920393;52;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Revered Tokyo chef Tadashi “Edowan” Yoshida has taken NYC by storm, as his latest venture was received with pomp, glory and of course, sold-out seats. Named for the town in Nara Prefecture where his father hails, there is a precise quality to every facet of this space—as in the hinoki counter (sourced from a 300-year-old tree) and hand-made chairs to the knives crafted by a master from Saga Prefecture.This meticulous approach is seen again in the presentation of dishes. Meals bring an element of theater, so much so that diners will find themselves leaning forward to absorb every detail—envision the dramatic removal of a glass dome to reveal a perfect piece of smoked salmon. The main event though just might be the nigiri, tailed by bruléed tamago.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
765;Icca;USA;New York;20 Warren St., New York, 10007, USA;40.7141336;-74.0077126;42;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Chef counters are a treat, but a seat in front of Chef Kazushige Suzuki feels like a best-kept secret. The room has a presence of its own, notable in scale and hidden away in the back past a cocktail bar. Friendly as ever and seemingly never in a hurry, the chef sources fish entirely from Japan and keeps his nigiri traditional with little more adornment than a brushing of nikiri.Other dishes that bookend the meal flex far more creativity and panache. Hokkaido hairy crab with capellini and shiso or snow trout marinated in koji for seven days are uniquely satisfying, while beef sourced from Japan makes regular appearances. At the meal’s end, disbelief may turn into wonder as guests dive into apple sorbet boldly topped with Yamazaki 12 whisky.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
768;YingTao;USA;New York;805 9th Ave., New York, 10019, USA;40.7655966;-73.9875299;44;true;false;Contemporary, Chinese;Owner Bolun Yao's beloved grandmother serves as both the namesake and culinary inspiration for this stylish Hell's Kitchen hideaway, an unassumingly ambitious project that aims to reinterpret Chinese cuisine through the lens of Western fine dining. Chef Jakub Baster lends his experienced hand to the effort, composing elegant dishes that blend a wide array of Chinese flavors and ingredients with elements of French technique and a contemporary style. The results are simultaneously inventive and familiar. Flavors tend toward subtlety, with careful attention paid to textures, as in a silky soy milk custard matched with celery root, and savory, mildly spiced doubanjiang, or rich crab noodles with egg yolk and smoked tobiko. To finish, a reimagining of nian gao (sweet rice cake) is sure to delight.;Air conditioning;[]
769;The Musket Room;USA;New York;265 Elizabeth St., New York, 10012, USA;40.723915;-73.99375;36;false;true;Contemporary, American Contemporary;Sleek glass-framed doors are a noticeable reprieve from the bustling stretch upon which The Musket Room is set. Inside, the space is rustic and cozy—think Danish-style chairs, industrial lighting, and midcentury modern furniture.Service is easy yet informed and complements the nature of this food turned out by a team led by Chef Mary Attea. The lived-in vibe is bolstered by the menu's flexibility in offering an omnivore or vegan tasting menu or a range of à la carte items. The tasting menu may feature dishes such as seared skin-on mackerel plated with mentaiko aioli, sungold tomatoes, and a dashi broth or lamb loin wrapped in grape leaves and roasted, then composed with a pine nut and charred chile relish and eggplant puree.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
770;Sushi Ichimura;USA;New York;412 Greenwich St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7217842;-74.0100019;52;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Among real sushi enthusiasts, Chef Eiji Ichimura is a household name. His career in the city spans two decades, and his commitment to edomae-style omakase has shaped this city’s sushi sensibility. He now finds himself in Tribeca behind a 10-seat counter made from gorgeous cedar wood. In some ways, there are no surprises: He works meticulously and at his own pace, slicing fish flown in from Japan three times a week. His rice is defined and generally warm, and his uni and caviar sandwich as well as his double and triple-layer tuna nigiri are still signatures. There’s just one thing: the price is steep, but that doesn’t faze his regulars, of which there are many. But regular or not, he treats everyone like a guest of his home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
771;Oiji Mi;USA;New York;17 W. 19th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7396366;-73.9924121;16;false;true;Korean, Contemporary;Chef Brian Kim and his team serve up very impressive modern Korean cuisine in a sleek space attended to by a fleet of staff. There is a refinement and a more subtle approach to flavors on this five-course prix fixe menu. Standouts include striped jack hwe, finished with a luscious seaweed scallion vinaigrette. Chili lobster ramyun plates tender lobster meat tossed in a vibrant gochujang over springy noodles. Desserts like cheese-stuffed chapssal donuts are a surefire hit.The beverage program is creative and skillful, with eye-catching cocktails and a well-curated wine list sharing house favorites.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
772;Essential by Christophe;USA;New York;103 W. 77th St., New York, 10024, USA;40.7808334;-73.9766573;72;false;true;French Contemporary, Contemporary;Push past the heavy iron doors to this modern restaurant tucked at the base of a classic townhouse. Supple leather, brass touches and various shades of beige comprise the contemporary, elegant space, where a buzzy bar and a welcoming dining room await. Chef Christophe Bellanca's dishes echo a simple elegance, evidenced by plump white asparagus on a fragrant bergamot-flavored crème with a refreshing herb vinaigrette and paper-thin slices of watermelon radish. French technique is married with Asian flavors in a dish of three blue prawns with genmaicha tuille, and braised black sea bass with shiitake chutney, razor clams and a turmeric emulsion is memorable. For a light ending, the orange soufflé is bright and fragrant, especially when served with green cardamom ice cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
773;Gramercy Tavern;USA;New York;42 E. 20th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7387578;-73.988991;63;false;true;Contemporary, American;This fabled NY icon is high on most people's roll call. It's one of those places that manages the rare trick of being so confident in its abilities and can be all things to all diners. You’ll probably leave happy whether you’re here on a date, to impress the in-laws or seal a deal. The “Tavern” side is a prized spot for lunch, especially if you can sit at the bar. It doesn't take reservations so get here early. The “Dining Room” though is for those who like a little more pomp with their pappardelle and truly comes to life at night. Service is attentive throughout.Focused on impeccable products, the seasonal and creative American cuisine is a perfect match for the woody surrounds. It's also sure of its footing and unthreatening in its vocabulary.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
774;Clover Hill;USA;Brooklyn;20 Columbia Pl., Brooklyn, 11201, USA;40.6933811;-73.9985773;61;true;false;Contemporary, Latin American;Squirreled away on a quiet street in Brooklyn Heights, this intimate restaurant is a charming box of elegance and comfort. Under the leadership of Chef Sam Rogers, this tiny but mighty kitchen now enters a new chapter. He and his team are a focused bunch, working in perfect sync to deliver an abundance of courses that draw inspiration from Latin America. Little tarts stacked with poblano peppers and guanciale give way to a single boiled potato coated in a Huancaína-inspired sauce flecked with caviar. Find spice and smoke deployed across a range of local fish and American wagyu, with one highlight being a grilled, dry-aged sirloin paired with a stunning cabbage puree. Service matches the setting, quiet and calm in all the right ways.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
775;Meju;USA;Queens;5-28 49th Ave., Queens, 11101, USA;40.7436597;-73.9555175;18;false;false;Korean, Regional Cuisine;Hiding behind a banchan shop in Long Island City, this chef’s counter is as much a classroom as it is a restaurant. Chef Hooni Kim is a worthy guide as he builds a deeply personal menu around traditional Korean ingredients that he’s been wild fermenting and aging for the last decade. Dazzling versions of doenjang, gochujang, ganjang and ssamjang shine with silky tofu, fried pancakes, Miyazaki beef and Niman Ranch pork. He brings the room together and impresses with carefully calibrated dishes that appear strikingly minimalist. Details are impressive, and many of the service pieces are handmade from Korean clay. An unassuming bowl of rice with kimchi is an homage to his mentor. It is a poignant finale that looks rather ordinary but has long-lasting impact.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
776;Sushi Nakazawa;USA;New York;23 Commerce St., New York, 10014, USA;40.731716;-74.00451;15;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;For a truly memorable sushi adventure, head to this sleek and contemporary ten-seat counter to discover flavorful and fatty cuts of fish, available at a more palatable price point compared to many of the city’s other notable sushi counters. Chef Daisuke Nakazawa’s signature style combines supremely tender fish with perfectly seasoned rice, a spark of wasabi and judicious brush of nikiri for consistently excellent results.Enjoy a spectrum of sushi from Hokkaido cherry salmon and live Massachusetts sea scallop with citrus and salt. Then move on to outstanding uni, and finally, a handroll of fatty tuna chopped so finely that it almost seems emulsified.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
777;Semma;USA;New York;60 Greenwich Ave., New York, 10011, USA;40.7360595;-74.0006729;44;true;true;Indian, Regional Cuisine;Chef Vijay Kumar runs the show at Semma, where regional south Indian cuisine is on full display. This is authentic Indian cooking that doesn't pander to American expectations, and if some of the dishes are unfamiliar, lean on the staff who know their stuff and are eager to share. One bite in and you'll quickly learn that this cooking is all heart. Dishes are spicy, but the heat is used as elegantly as it is liberally. Start with the mulaikattiya thaniyam, the chef's childhood snack that bursts with flavor. The gunpowder dosa, a classic rice and lentil crepe filled with potato masala, is on every table for a reason. Attu kari sukka is falling-apart tender lamb in a dark brown curry redolent of warm spices.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
779;Kochi;USA;New York;652 Tenth Ave., New York, 10036, USA;40.7619767;-73.9935116;38;true;true;Korean, Contemporary;The idea that tasting menus are hours-long and showy is far from true here. The vibe is boisterous, and the crowds are delighted to be here. The open kitchen is the obvious centerpiece. From here, a young team blitzes out an array of impressive grilled bites meant to be eaten with your hands—Kochi is Korean for skewer, after all.Chef Sungchul Shim taps into his Korean roots and fine-dining pedigree to create a solid but playful menu. Start with sweet potato and sunchoke gratin paired with a clever doenjang béchamel, then salmon bibimbap, mingling pollock roe, candied anchovy and toasted nori with brown soy-butter rice, is a harmonious high point. A stick of rich and nutty black sesame ice cream is the last hurrah. Worth the splurge? Without a doubt.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
781;Nōksu;USA;New York;49 W. 32nd St., New York, 10001, USA;40.7483502;-73.9879966;19;true;false;Contemporary, Korean;Eating underground in the subway system may not sound appealing, but that hasn't stopped Chef Dae Kim. In the heart of Koreatown at Herald Square behind a code-locked door, find a black marble counter that stretches the length of the room. Every chef is armed with tweezers to manage and primp gorgeous dishes that are largely contemporary in their design. Seafood is a serious focus with the likes of crab, fluke, clams, and mackerel. The restaurant’s signature is obvious once you spot the squab dry aging in a fridge. Against the backdrop of 80s hits playing overhead, a chef holds the bird up and repeatedly ladles hot oil over it in the style of Peking duck. It’s a defining reminder that in New York City, anything can happen anywhere.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
783;Estela;USA;New York;47 E. Houston St., New York, 10012, USA;40.72471;-73.9948;82;true;false;Contemporary, American;This boisterous SoHo alcove is an ideal place to convene with friends over exquisite nibbles and quenching cocktails. The talented chef behind this operation, Ignacio Mattos, is unfaltering and impressively consistent in his creative renditions of such bold and iconic dishes as ricotta dumplings with mushrooms and Pecorino Sardo. The menu also offers an array of shareable plates that changes regularly, like the mound of warm crab cloaked by shaved celeriac. Dinner might kick off with perfect, sashimi-grade tuna pounded thin and dressed with a dollop of inky pil pil sauce or enticingly plated fried arroz negro scattered with tender squid and hazelnut-studded romesco.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
784;Tempura Matsui;USA;New York;222 E. 39th St., New York, 10016, USA;40.748191;-73.974663;20;true;false;Japanese, Tempura;Tempura Matsui skillfully demonstrates why tempura is a celebrated Japanese cuisine type in its own right. The prized seats are at the counter, especially if you want to see the master at work.The chef uses a mix of sesame and cottonseed oils and the batter is used sparingly. You’ll start with a seasonal soup including seared scallop with wheat cake, before having some beautifully arranged sashimi. Then, the main event begins in the traditional way with crispy shrimp legs. Dishes turned out of this kitchen usually vary according to the seasons, but could include the likes of wonderfully tender squid, succulent Hokkaido scallop, tender cauliflower, as well as snow crab wrapped in shiso leaf. Be sure to end with tencha, with its mellow and deeply flavorful broth.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
785;Jeju Noodle Bar;USA;New York;679 Greenwich St., New York, 10014, USA;40.732952;-74.00744;15;true;false;Korean;Settle in to your perch at one of the tables, or (preferably) at the engaging counter where you can watch each dish come together. If that doesn't have your taste buds tingling, the kitchen's concise number of unique items at a steal of a price will hit the spot. Persian cucumber kimchi with a spicy plum dressing, shiso and sesame seeds is a delight, while the aroma of pork bone broth that precedes the arrival of gochu ramyun brimming with curly noodles, bean sprouts and pickled cabbage is a veritable thesis on ace ingredients. Pyunche salad mingling sushi-grade amberjack is a simple yet delicious wonder. Not far behind is the surprising toro ssam bap, highlighting the eponymous fatty fish with scrambled egg, tobiko and toasted seaweed.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
787;Noda;USA;New York;37 W. 20th St., New York, 10001, USA;40.7404543;-73.9930802;93;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Chef Shigeyuki Tsunoda's iconic eight-seat half-moon shaped counter is fronted by the team's cocktail den, Shinji. Throughout this arena, the signature speak-easy vibe is a distinct element and the dark cozy space with exposed brick walls is a prized spot for some excellent sushi enhanced by an impressive beverage program with vintage champagne and a comprehensive sake collection showcasing rare bottles not found elsewhere. Chef Shigeyuki Tsunoda undertakes his duties with calm, unhurried efficiency and his omakase is rooted in tradition. Confident knife cuts, warmed rice and pristine fish are par for the course. The meal begins with small snacks before progressing into the pristine nigiri, where the standouts, among many, are sea eel and two kinds of uni.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
788;Shion 69 Leonard Street;USA;New York;69 Leonard St., New York, 10013, USA;40.71757;-74.00549;92;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;There are just eight seats and a distinctive Japanese charm at Chef Shion Uino's quiet sushi-ya, which features prized, beautiful seafood sourced primarily from Japan (including impressive amount directly from fishermen in his hometown of Amakusa). Never, at any point, does it look like the chef is cutting from a filet he’s already sliced. The product is whole and luscious every time, which is all the more reason why the nigiri sees little beyond a dot of wasabi or a dab of nikiri. Regulars, of which there are many, are treated to special pieces throughout the evening and will recognize some of his signature dishes, like hairy crab dressed with Japanese black vinegar, as well as his unrivaled tamago, which tastes as perfect as it looks.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
790;Jōji;USA;New York;1 Vanderbilt Ave., New York, 10017, USA;40.7532627;-73.9783451;15;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Hidden away in a corner of Grand Central, at the base of the ritzy One Vanderbilt building, Jōji presents a disarming oasis of calm and sophistication amidst the hustle and bustle. The meal begins with small plates that blend Japanese flavors with seasonal elements, as in a sashimi of buri with green apple, ginger, and yuzu zest, followed by nigiri featuring a blend of Koshihikari and Nanatsuboshi rice, carefully vinegared to showcase the flavor of the fish. The variety of excellent seafood, largely sourced from Toyosu Market, is impressive, and even devoted sybarites will leave satisfied. Expect an abundance of luxury ingredients (and commensurate pricing), like a lightly cooked langoustine layered with creamy petals of uni, or a delicate, silky chawanmushi topped with golden Osetra.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
791;Xiquet;USA;Washington;2404 Wisconsin Ave. NW, Washington, 20007, USA;38.9215871;-77.0723834;15;false;false;Spanish;Chef Danny Lledó's kitchen is equipped with a smoker and a wood-fired hearth to produce a menu that proudly extols Spanish cuisine with a focus on the delights of Valencia. Morsels like dill-cured bonito arranged with creamy, cool ajo blanco lead up to heartier compositions such as crisped-skin turbot with smoked trout roe-studded beurre blanc. The rice preparations steal the show, like the Alicante-style rice with rabbit and mushrooms cooked over the hearth. The meal is creative and intriguing, while showcasing first-rate products procured with an eye toward sustainability. The sparely elegant third-floor room hosts a mere handful of tables. After dinner, guests are invited to conclude the evening with coffee and mignardise in the lounge.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
792;Rooster & Owl;USA;Washington;2436 14th St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.9214669;-77.0321599;81;true;false;Contemporary, Fusion;A talented husband-and-wife duo is behind this appealingly contemporary, hipster hot spot. The setting is the perfect match for its modern, edgy cuisine, which meanders from the Middle East and Mediterranean all the way to Asia.There is unabashed creativity unleashed in such dishes as fried oyster mushrooms with mushroom powder serving as tempura batter. Barbecue carrots may then be given the North Carolina treatment, dabbed with vinegar, grilled to smoky perfection and served with savory cornbread ice cream. In closing, a seemingly simple brie custard is in fact ultra-inventive, thanks to a trickle of red cherry mostarda and honeycomb. Since you get to mix and match menu items, the bar follows suit and tailors wine options to guests' selections.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
793;Masseria;USA;Washington;1340 4th St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.909504;-76.99908;27;true;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;With its seamless blend of indoor and outdoor spaces, this is a shining beacon amid high-rises, restaurants, and stores galore. Donning that requisite brick walls and farmhouse vibe, the former warehouse feels glam yet spartan—with a stainless steel kitchen, chrome accents, and an impressive glass-encased wine cellar. Such a feel-good sense extends to the staff, who clearly like working here as much as diners enjoy lingering over meals.Chef/owner Nicholas Stefanelli's Puglian heritage comes through in the menu. His dishes hit all the right notes, balancing playful with serious elements, as in a cigar box filled with focaccia. You’ll want to save room though for the maccheroni with goat ragù. Even dessert strays from the pack—beet ice cream anyone?;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
794;Métier;USA;Washington;1015 7th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.903503;-77.0218;97;false;true;Contemporary, Modern French;Métier's spare and sleek dining space may be best described as one part living room and two parts art gallery, and a window to the kitchen gives a taste of what is to come. The space is elegant and the service echoes the sophistication with an attentive eye. Chef Eric Ziebold plies his "metier" in an ambitious tasting that pulls global flavors in inspired ways. A riff on cassoulet, for instance, unveils flageolet bean purée with a pork jowl croquette and Santa Barbara uni. The crowning flourish is a sorbet made from aji dulce peppers grown at the restaurant's garden in Virgnia. A satin-smooth, double fermented chocolate ganache with toasted fennel-crème anglaise is as stunning as it is ingenious.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
795;Elcielo Washington;USA;Washington;1280 4th St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.9090145;-76.9994792;34;true;false;Colombian, Contemporary;This concept from Chef Juan Manuel Barrientos can be found adjacent to Union Market's La Cosecha. Presentation is the cornerstone here, with an admirable level of showmanship, and dishes embody a love letter to the chef's native Colombia. This is deeply personal cooking, with the chef utilizing Colombian ingredients in dishes that share history and purpose. Two set menus are served throughout the restaurant's two dining rooms. From the snacks to the corn broth that makes you rethink this staple to the chocotherapy dessert, this dining experience is seamless.  The ingredients are Colombian, many of the dishes have history, purpose and definition. All the while, a warm staff enhances the experience.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
796;Reverie;USA;Washington;3201 Cherry Hill Ln. NW, Washington, 20007, USA;38.90346;-77.06323;61;true;true;Contemporary;Chef Johnny Spero and his team have risen from the ashes with a new look and an energized commitment. Enter through a stone garden to find a chic space dominated by the open kitchen where sustainably minded, East Coast-focused seafood takes center stage. The kitchen plays with expectations and delivers excitement at every turn. Even a tuna tostada is anything but ho-hum with its fresh approach. A memorable dish of diced surf clams with tomato granita bursts with umami and acidity, while sweet morsels of spider crab offer comfort with a buttery porridge of Carolina gold rice and an unctuous sauce of thickened egg yolk. The unexpected hits keep coming through dessert, where kelp cooked with vanilla syrup is finished over the grill for a smoky-sweet bite that brings the meal full circle.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
797;Causa;USA;Washington;920 Blagden Alley NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9069049;-77.024685;71;true;true;Peruvian, Latin American;Chef Carlos Delgado delivers a taste of his birthplace in a dual concept space in Blagden Alley. Nestled on the first floor, Causa seats around 20 for a tasting menu that takes diners on a journey of flavors inspired by the topography of Peru. It all begins in Lima with coastal seafood, then progresses into the Andes and the Amazon. Chicha morada kombucha, made from purple corn, is a perfect partner for the Peruvian classic and namesake dish, causa, with its mashed potatoes hit with aji amarillo paste, then topped with cucumber, avocado and tuna tartare. Next, the humble bomba rice is given a luxe glow-up courtesy of uni, caviar and a criolla sauce. Dessert definitely doesn't disappoint, as in the passion fruit and mint gelato scoops piped with macambo mousse.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
798;Bresca;USA;Washington;1906 14th St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.915782;-77.03195;28;false;false;Contemporary, American;It's set on busy 14th Street, but beautiful Bresca far from blends in with the crowd. Instead, it mixes the warmth of a neighborhood treasure with the talent of a special occasion spot. Inside, splashes of gold, a living wall crafted from moss and design elements teetering between whimsical and downright surreal, create a contemporary vibe. The cooking is casual yet ambitious, thanks to Chef Ryan Ratino’s cutting-edge credentials. Find a clear sense of artistry in the likes of a foie gras "negroni" topped with Campari gelée or the agreeably priced and perfect pappardelle with lamb ragù. Service is highly professional without a trace of pretense.Cocktails, like The Daulphine St. Punch, may be relished in lieu of dessert.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
799;Tail Up Goat;USA;Washington;1827 Adams Mill Rd. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.9232785;-77.0428198;70;false;false;Contemporary;When three forward-thinking restaurateurs combine their talents, the result is bound to be an easygoing haven, where the food, drinks, and hospitality mesh effortlessly. Fittingly, the mood here is buzzy, but don’t be fooled by the casual vibe, as this kitchen team is serious.Start with an assortment of snacks, including a crudité of radishes and wax beans with white miso dip, or a crisp tart shell filled with creamy eggplant and serrano pepper apricot relish. Mains offer a refined take on Americana classics, like steak and potatoes with a seared strip steak and a crunchy potato pavé with a dusting of green onion powder. To finish, consider the rather un-French version of baba au rhum, featuring apricot honey, toasted marshmallow, and vanilla gelato.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
800;Oyster Oyster;USA;Washington;1440 8th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.909302;-77.023015;53;true;false;Vegetarian, Contemporary;It is highly rare for a tasting menu to leave one feeling—well—energized, but so goes the imaginative cooking at this vegetable-focused gem where local farms are the very essence of this passionate operation. The imaginative compositions from Chef Rob Rubba and his team offer delicious insights into what is possible with vegetables. There is true creativity here, as in a pasta course which features agnolotti filled with a creamy eggplant and house-grown mushrooms, served brodo-style with a roasted corn broth and accompanied by a truffle tart. Even bread service is special—enriched with "garleeks" and accompanied by sunflower seed and marigold "butter." A baton of summer squash is elevated by a filling of pumpkin seed "ricotta.";Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
802;Imperfecto: The Chef's Table;USA;Washington;1124 23rd St. NW, Washington, 20037, USA;38.9039056;-77.0505927;61;true;true;Latin American;Boasting all the buzz of a hornet’s nest, this soaring box of glass and marble virtually reaches for the sky. Inside, it's decked out with brass accents, terra-cotta, and a tight counter positioned directly under Chef Enrique Limardo’s perch. The counter functions as a restaurant within a restaurant with room for just a handful of diners to enjoy an elaborate tasting menu that celebrates Latin flavors, ace ingredients, and exacting technique. The attention to detail is superb, and meals take on an intimate form. Dishes, perhaps aged grouper with BBQ lettuce and broccolini tabbouleh, or duck with Carolina rice, hum with flavor. Desserts are equally skillful, as in pickled peach with matcha sponge cake.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
803;Sushi Nakazawa;USA;Washington;1100 Pennsylvania Ave. NW, Washington, 20004, USA;38.8946236;-77.0270052;83;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;This second outpost of Chef Daisuke Nakazawa’s critically acclaimed sushi house is elegant and intimate with dark wood and gold accents. For the best seat, angle for one of the leather stools at the marble counter, where you can watch the itamae work their magic. The team works in a tidy fashion, their hands moving as adeptly as a surgeon along meticulously organized counters. Ingredients are sourced both locally and from abroad and each course is presented like a revelation—from Japanese sumi ika with shiso and pickled plum sauce to lightly torched kama toro with spicy daikon. It will take you a couple of hours to work your way through the luxurious 20-course omakase of the chef, who trained under the legendary Jiro Ono, but rest assured it is time well spent.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
804;Mita;USA;Washington;804 V St. NW, Washington, 20037, USA;38.9177028;-77.0230631;59;true;false;Vegetarian, Latin American;Latin American cuisine, only plant based. That's the premise behind this contemporary space set in the Shaw neighborhood. It's tasting menu only, but short and long formats ensure a fit. Chefs Tatiana Mora and Miguel Guerra share their creative spirit here, where influences span from Brazil and Bolivia to Colombia and dishes sport originality. A basket of arepas is a fun dish featuring a variety of textures and flavors with tasty sauces like guasacaca, cashew sour cream with chili oil, and butter made of chontaduro. Watermelon crudo with fermented carrot in a cucumber leche de tigre sauce is inventive and bold, while a slice of mushroom terrine wrapped in greens with layers of potato delivers on umami, bite after bite.;Air conditioning;[]
805;Albi;USA;Washington;1346 4th St. SE, Washington, 20003, USA;38.8741148;-77.0009665;82;false;false;Middle Eastern, Lebanese;This Navy Yard denizen is hip and lively. Arranged around a roaring hearth, the space features an inviting bar at one end and chef's counter at the other.Albi is a sterling example of open-fire cooking at its best. À la carte is one way to go, but guests may just do better with the hyper-seasonal prix-fixe. Regardless, Chef/owner Michael Rafidi's dishes are full of surprises as he weaves in the flavors of the eastern Mediterranean with a myriad of local ingredients. Favorites like baba ghanoush and kefta are handled with precision, but the tastiest dishes come from the wood-fired hearth, imbued with smoke and char. A dessert of brown butter knafeh with yogurt ice cream is a marvel, while the wine program flaunts a litany of Mediterranean and Middle Eastern labels.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
806;Gravitas;USA;Washington;1401 Okie St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.9146396;-76.9845997;25;false;true;Contemporary, American;Chef Matt Baker is luring diners to Ivy City with this gorgeous spot, which transforms local products into modern, deeply complex items. The décor pays homage to the place's industrial bones with exposed brick and stark walls, softened by greenery. Fine service and an open kitchen enhance the appeal.Set menus are available with three, four, and six courses to choose from, along with some supplements. Wonderful yellowfin sashimi comes with a complex soy vinaigrette while the tagliatelle with sweetbreads in a pork and pancetta ragu with brown butter cream and sun chokes is a standout. For dessert, it has to be his riff on a Butterfinger with salted caramel, peanut butter nougat, chocolate cremeux, salted caramel ice cream, and candied peanuts.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
807;Rose’s Luxury;USA;Washington;717 8th St. SE, Washington, 20003, USA;38.8806478;-76.9950588;76;false;false;Contemporary;This dining room is all about fun, with a laid-back décor including exposed bulbs strung above the counter facing into the open kitchen, lending a convivial mood that’s like dining in a friend's backyard. The family-style prix fixe menu has its own cheeky tone, starting with the "really, really, really good challah" (and it is), served with an artful ruffle of caraway honey butter. The cooking is equal parts approachable and ingenious, as in a signature salad of spiced pork paired with airy coconut cream and lychee, spiked with lime juice and a bevy of fresh herbs, or Korean rice cakes coated with a creamy, spicy gochujang alla vodka sauce. Desserts offer their own excitement, as in a sticky toffee pudding enhanced with earthy, complex mole negro, paired with a soothing horchata ice cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
808;Rania;USA;Washington;427 11th St. NW, Washington, 20004, USA;38.8956098;-77.0267996;80;false;false;Indian, Contemporary;This fine dining concept seems fit for a queen, and good thing too, since Rania translates to "queen" in Hindi and Sanskrit. They deliver something entirely enticing here with an inventive menu. There are plenty of contemporary touches along with a few surprises (think braised pork belly vindalooo). Dishes like shiso leaf chaat balance a playful spirit with elegant overtones, while ghee-roasted lamb folded inside a delicate lentil cheela has a spicy kick that is tempered with a buttermilk mousse. Finally, a slightly sweet, strained yogurt mousse with a hint of pistachio and cardamom is the perfect finale. Cocktails are designed to complement the rich, bold flavors.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
809;Little Pearl;USA;Washington;921 Pennsylvania Ave. SE, Washington, 20003, USA;38.8833557;-76.9936368;74;false;true;Contemporary;Just down the street from Rose’s Luxury and Pineapple and Pearls, this intimate boîte is yet another feather in the same restaurant group’s proverbial cap. Possessing all the charm of a carriage house, the dining room is closer to a sunroom encased in glass with expansive views of the green surroundings. The cooking is equally attractive: Seasonal fare prepared with panache and a touch of luxury. Think oysters with fried potatoes and seaweed remoulade or poached pears with bay leaf ice cream. The menu is a revolving door of ideas, except for the signature angel egg amuse. An eclectic wine list makes for a thoughtful pairing. In total, dinner here goes for less than other tasting menus in town, but with no less boldness, care, and creativity.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
811;Omakase at Barracks Row;USA;Washington;522 8th St. SE, Washington, 20003, USA;38.8818451;-76.9949278;78;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Chef Yi "Ricky" Wang, who trained under Chef Nakazawa before running a series of pop-ups, is now settled in at this counter, located up a set of metal stairs in an industrial-chic space. Take special note of the paintings that line that staircase—they're nods to a longstanding tradition of fishermen brushing their catch with ink and pressing it into rice paper—and you may be presented with a similar piece at your meal. Chef Wang's omakase features a few otsumami, perhaps poached sweet shrimp in a smoked Maine uni sauce, before progressing to nigiri. It's all impressive, from the Boston surf clam finished with kumquat kosho to the hay-smoked Spanish mackerel sourced from the Carolinas that's bold but balanced. Musk melon with strawberries imported from Japan is a satisfying finale.;Air conditioning;[]
812;The Dabney;USA;Washington;122 Blagden Alley NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9062921;-77.0245936;21;false;false;American, Contemporary;The Dabney exudes charming, contemporary farmhouse vibes with its exposed brick, light walls, and dark wood, and the look is completed by a slickly arranged open kitchen complete with a wood-fired hearth. Chef/owner Jeremiah Langhorne serves up the flavors of the Mid-Atlantic with a hint of a Southern accent and the tasting menu is a deeper, more committed expression of the team's talents. Begin with bite-sized snacks including their pie crust tart with pickled blueberries, granola crumble, and cheese fondue or their Madeira compressed melon. Then, hearth-roasted vegetables are served over a bed of farro salad with whipped ricotta, herbs from their rooftop garden, and finished with a pour of a basil sauce. American wagyu cap grilled over coals is accompanied by eggplant prepared three ways for a perfectly satisfying main dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
813;Kinship;USA;Washington;1015 7th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.903282;-77.0218;30;true;false;Contemporary, French Contemporary;Kinship is a prominent fixture thanks to Chef Eric Ziebold and wife/partner Célia Laurent’s inspired cuisine. They have earned a devoted following who gladly dress to dine here. In addition to Métier downstairs, the space comprises a fireplace-warmed lounge, lively bar, and minimalist-chic dining room.The à la carte is driven by the seasons, changing often to adapt to what's available. The food hums with flavor and balance, as in Catalan spiced confit squid with tempura tentacles, lemon shallot gremolata, and Romesco sauce, or perfectly rendered and lacquered duck. For desserts, any of them seal the deal, but the roasted Maui pineapple with coconut frangipane, lime all-spice cream, and pineapple sherbet is a fierce competitor.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
814;Cariño;USA;Chicago;4662 N. Broadway, Chicago, 60640, USA;41.9669579;-87.6585142;50;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;In a cozy corner of Uptown where the train rumbles overhead, Chef Norman Fenton mines his history and his travels to celebrate Mexican cuisine in a distinct, ambitious manner. He lists out ingredients like an auctioneer, and his pace is energetic. Quickly, the courses compound: A stunning huitlacoche ravioli with fried corn silk, then a queso truffle quesadilla, and at some point, a lamb tartare tostada seasoned in the style of al pastor. Indeed, this tasting menu features boldness and creativity in spades, starting with “chips and salsa” in the form of salsa verde jelly and a tortilla crumble. The best seats are at the counter, which offer an up-close view of this small team, all of whom work diligently and engage with guests freely.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
815;Indienne;USA;Chicago;217 W. Huron St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.89465;-87.634932;85;true;false;Indian, Contemporary;In a city where kitchens break molds and defy expectations, Chef Sujan Sarkar makes a splash of his own on this quiet strip of River North. Vegan, vegetarian, and non-vegetarian tasting menus deliver an original, modern vision of Indian cuisine. His food may look like pieces of art but taste like familiar favorites pulled from across his vibrant homeland. At times showcasing a hint of French sensibility, pani puris, chats and curries arrive deftly spiced and elegantly presented. The kitchen is quick, and the overall effect is impressive refinement. All the while, the expansive room balances smooth warehouse floors and exposed ceilings with thick wooden beams, white tablecloths and rose-pink booths.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
816;Elske;USA;Chicago;1350 W. Randolph Ave., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8843534;-87.6608602;82;false;false;Contemporary, American Contemporary;Year after year, Chefs David and Anna Posey hit their marks with this Danish oasis. A marvelous patio seamlessly flows into an airy dining room that fills up quickly — and for good reason. In choosing between the set tasting and the a la carte, there is no wrong answer. Both journeys capture the spirit of what makes this restaurant special by showing a respect for the seasons, delightful originality, and a stylish flair that never comes at the cost of flavor. Past highlights include lamb tartare on rye, duck liver tart with salted tamp, and yeasted chickpea pancakes with smoked trout. The signature dessert is a sunflower seed parfait with sour honey and licorice. Juice pairings and esoteric wines round out the evening.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
817;Esmé;USA;Chicago;2200 N. Clark St., Chicago, 60614, USA;41.92198;-87.63824;40;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;Together with his co-owner and wife, Katrina Bravo, Chef Jenner Tomaska lays bare lofty ambitions at this airy atelier. The minimalist, well-lit space evokes an art gallery, complete with a high concept tasting that's aimed at blurring the boundaries between art and dining. The show begins with intriguing bites served at standing tables just inside. The multicourse meal that follows features a variety of dishes, each offered on custom pieces made by local artists. Flavorful compositions showcase unexpected combinations, as in "tomahawk" style Dover sole in a vin jaune sauce with spiced compressed pear and seaweed. Goat cheese ice cream with yuzu marmalade and a cynar-cured egg yolk expertly balances sweet and savory.;;[]
818;Mako;USA;Chicago;731 W. Lake St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8857746;-87.6468966;24;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Veteran chef B.K. Park has spun out this inspiring shrine to omakase. With nothing but a lone plaque marking its entrance, this Japanese delight can be tough to spot. But once inside, the surrounding din of traffic fades and you’ll be transfixed by the team's dedication to sushi.Mako is a hot ticket, with just 22 seats from which to savor the smartly considered omakase. Throughout the evening, the chef and itamae showcase their style through unique adornments, like sudachi juice and sesame-pepper soy. Equally enticing are cooked items, like braised abalone or black cod with burnt scallion ponzu. Not to be outdone, chawanmushi stocked with mushroom and crab is the essence of elegance. Dessert is not an afterthought, as in sweet potato with whiskey caramel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
819;Galit;USA;Chicago;2429 N. Lincoln Ave., Chicago, 60614, USA;41.92607;-87.64959;79;true;true;Middle Eastern, Mediterranean Cuisine;Its exterior is unassuming, but one step inside the hot spot and you'll be smitten by its lively vibe, warm hospitality and seductive aromas. Chef Zach Engel brings his experience to bear on this personal brand of modern Middle Eastern cuisine. His prix-fixe allows diners to make their own selections from a range of options. A generous first course kicks things off: Creamy hummus with brisket and salatim (spreads and pickles) accompanied by just-cooked, flame-kissed pita. Even familiar favorites like crackling-crisp falafel with mango labneh offer surprising depth. The team’s impressive intentionality extends to its beverage program, as esoteric wines from Armenia, Lebanon, Palestine, and Israel tell their own stories and make for beautiful pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
820;Schwa;USA;Chicago;1466 N. Ashland Ave., Chicago, 60662, USA;41.9087844;-87.667733;90;false;false;Contemporary, Innovative;Schwa is like a punky teenager who refuses to grow up. Year after year, the restaurant sticks to its guns with no servers, rap music booming overhead, and wildly imaginative, over-the-top cooking. Its divisiveness and fiercely independent spirit are memorable. As for what might come out of this kitchen, it’s anybody’s guess. How about gumbo but serve it chilled, aerated, and with a blue crab chip dotted with hoja santa aioli? A flaky, buttery cinnamon tart shell could arrive filled with foie gras ice cream and apples. Medallions of quail might be dusted in jerk seasoning and plated with onion rings and candied guava. Ever had a milk bun dusted in powdered mustard? At the meal’s end, the chefs may offer you a shot of whiskey. Have at it.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle;[]
821;Atelier;USA;Chicago;4835 N. Western Ave., Chicago, 60625, USA;41.9695433;-87.6888121;97;true;false;American;This Lincoln Square boîte has always blended in with its humble surrounds, but enthusiasts know that it’s the inside that counts and where culinary excellence has long thrived. In full view of the dining room, Chef Christian Hunter and his team chart new waters, ever determined to make their own mark on this intimate space. Working quietly and seamlessly, the kitchen delivers a carefully calibrated tasting menu supported by nearby farms and packed with flavor and originality. Familiar dishes like marinated beets, pimento cheese and Caesar salad arrive remodeled and refined, astutely seasoned, and never a leaf or morsel out of place. Hope that the warm clam chowder with lamb bacon and chive oil is still available. It’s a total showstopper.;Air conditioning;[]
822;EL Ideas;USA;Chicago;2419 W. 14th St., Chicago, 60608, USA;41.862929;-87.686825;33;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;Channeling all the ease of an underground dinner party, Chef Phillip Foss invites guests into his literal home (he lives upstairs). There is but one seating, everyone is served at the same time, and people are encouraged to bring as much wine as they want. The warehouse space feels most like a test kitchen, and guests can wander about, explore the pantry, and practically stand next to the chefs as they cook and plate. The cuisine is creative, starting with a shrimp cocktail croquette with shrimp snow that must be licked off the plate. Maybe there’s a play on oysters Rockefeller or maybe there's a riff on banh mi and French dip. There is one signature that never changes: French fries with potato leek soup and nitro-poached vanilla ice cream.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle;[]
824;Kasama;USA;Chicago;1001 N. Winchester Ave., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.8995437;-87.6758818;74;false;false;Filipino, Contemporary;Drawing its name, fittingly, from the Tagalog word for “together,” Kasama unites the culinary talents (and fine dining pedigrees) of husband-and-wife team Tim Flores and Genie Kwon. Flores's background provides inspiration for this modern interpretation of Filipino cuisine, while Kwon’s pastry training elevates the sweet side of things. Homey traditional preparations are reimagined in elegant, inventive dishes, as in an “adobo” of mussels and wild mushrooms that strikes a perfect balance of tangy, sweet, and savory. Desserts, like a “mais con yelo” that features sweet corn semifreddo and milk granita, are every bit as satisfying. During the day, the space offers a less lofty experience, operating as a bakery with a selection of simpler dishes and top-notch pastries.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
825;Sepia;USA;Chicago;123 N. Jefferson St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8840951;-87.6426104;88;false;false;American, American Contemporary;Housed within a 19th-century print shop, this urbane dining room mixes original details with modern touches. Muted tones in the exposed brick walls and custom tile floors complement newer elements like floor-to-ceiling wine storage and dramatic chandeliers.Chef Andrew Zimmerman’s menu is a delicious amalgam of American cuisine with hints of Southeast Asian, Korean, and Mediterranean tastes. Gnocchi may seem commonplace, but this version is memorable thanks to the rich flavors of lamb sugo and ciabatta breadcrumbs. Chicken is downright exciting, served crisp-skinned with a buttery Albufera sauce, crumbly chestnuts, caramelized fennel, and sausage. Desserts keep the bar high, and may include a toffee-coconut cake with chocolate ganache and burnt caramel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
826;Boka;USA;Chicago;1729 N. Halsted St., Chicago, 60614, USA;41.9135974;-87.6482441;22;true;false;Contemporary, American;After more than a decade of excellence, Chef/owner Lee Wolen’s flagship shines as bright as ever. The relaxed dining room fitted with banquettes and mirrored light bulbs exudes elegance with a bit of romance and quirk. All the while, an appealing modern menu celebrates seasonal ingredients with bold preparations and exceptional clarity. To start, braised turnips sound sleepy but it’s a superb effort with coriander yogurt and puffed quinoa. Pasta is exceptional. Think ricotta ravioli with summer corn and smoked buttermilk or porcini gnudi packed with garlicky intensity. Dry-aged Rohan duck matched with roasted shallot and plum jam is a standout, but so too is the black truffle roasted chicken. The talented cocktail program is its own adventure.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
827;Next;USA;Chicago;953 W. Fulton Market, Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8866924;-87.6518812;17;false;true;Contemporary;Whether you come to experience the cuisine of ancient Rome or Hollywood, a meal here is pure dinner theater. These culinary themes are unique and thoughtful, leaving diners wondering what's "next."While an earlier Italia menu showcased complex ingredients and flawless flavors and textures (think cacio e pepe and guanciale-wrapped branzino), the most recent "Paris 1906" culinary theme showcased celebrated French chef Auguste Escoffier's classic cuisine. Highlights included carrè d’agneau avec sauce choron, a well-executed plate of lamb and crispy sweetbreads with a vibrant sauce choron. The theme ran through to dessert, with a bombe Ceylan, a half-sphere of ice cream, rum and coffee with a delicate chocolate shell, served with griottine cherries and sauce anglaise.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
828;Moody Tongue;USA;Chicago;2515 S. Wabash Ave., Chicago, 60616, USA;41.8469648;-87.6252282;62;false;false;Contemporary, American Contemporary;Moody Tongue is a unique showcase, whereby a creative menu bearing a panoply of inspiration and influence is brilliantly matched with a virtuosic array of house-crafted brews. Discreetly perched atop the working brewery, this is a contemporary if at times austere dining room. Unsurprisingly, the word "moody" befits the intimate yet masculine vibe.Beverages are an equal partner to the food, and the beer pairing is a must to fully engage in the experience. Indulge in such creations as black cod with makhani curry paired with an orange blossom Belgian blonde ale or lamb borek paired with a cassis lambic. Even dessert gets its brew, such as the devil's food and strawberry mousse cake accompanied by bourbon-barrel aged chocolate stout.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
829;Narımor;Türkiye;Izmir;Sıra Mahallesi, Eren Sokak, Urla, Izmir, 35320, Türkiye;38.3193131;26.7672542;70;true;true;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Atilla Heilbronn serves up a distinctive take on Turkish cuisine. Having grown up in Germany and worked at several top-flight establishments, he has now set up shop at this stylish boutique hotel. The glass-paned restaurant can only accommodate a handful of tables, which makes for an intimate atmosphere. Hostess Buse adds to the vibe with her attentive service. Chef Heilbronn's meticulously crafted dishes are visually stunning and showcase the finest local ingredients. His German training is evident in the exceptional bread he bakes, including a dark sourdough and a pretzel-style baguette. His intriguing culinary creations never fail to amaze, eg the sea bream with tart apricot, briny samphire and a creamy kefir dressing is full of nuance and expression. Don't miss the opportunity to pair your meal with a bottle from Hus Wines, which has some real gems in store. Through his efforts to source first-rate produce and his extensive research into Turkish culinary traditions, this chef has developed a truly original style of cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
830;Araka;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kapalı Bakkal Sokak No:8, Yeniköy/Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34464, Türkiye;41.1171693;29.0630471;39;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Here you’ll find it's easy to forget you're in the metropolis of Istanbul. You’re actually in the Yeniköy district, in the north of the city, just beyond the exclusive marina you pass on the way (taking the Bosphorus ferry over is a must). Behind its charming façade, this rural-style restaurant awaits with its cosy, romantic interior and a terrace to the rear where you feel cut off from the world. This enchanting spot perfectly suits Zeynep Pınar Taşdemir's highly individual style. Seasonal ingredients are showcased on the menu. The young chef likes to express her creativity with vegetables and herbs. Pumpkin puree is imbued with the potent freshness of za'atar and combined with pickled vegetables and warm olives in a spicy sauce. A robust dish that is full of character and pleasingly harmonious thanks to its subtle acidity. This chef is adept at balancing spicy, savoury flavours with tangy aromas. She creates exciting dishes that let the regional produce do the talking.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
831;Kitchen By Osman Sezener;Türkiye;Bodrum;Dirmil Mahallesi, Balyek Caddesi No:5A, Yalıkavak, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1151435;27.3116394;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;Osman Sezener and his team offer a unique and international take on Turkish cuisine. Produce from the region takes centre stage and it is always guaranteed to be fresh and flavourful. The dishes are not overly complicated, but they certainly pack a punch. The perfectly fried sea bass is as fresh as if it had just been caught. The accompanying sauce, prepared like a beurre blanc, is enriched with oyster sauce and an elegant herb-infused oil. Fortunately, you are given (delicious!) sourdough bread, so you can mop up every last drop. The herbs come from gardens surrounding the restaurant and hit the spot every time. For instance, a salsa verde of fresh herbs beautifully elevates the octopus cooked in the charcoal oven. Generosity and finesse go hand in hand here. The extremely appealing à la carte selection really leaves you spoilt for choice! The luxury hotel The Bodrum Edition provides the ideal setting in which to explore this creativity. There is a certain laid-back vibe here that is pleasingly contemporary, warm and welcoming. But it is the breathtaking view over the resort and the bay that steals the show!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
832;Arkestra;Türkiye;Istanbul;Etiler, Dilhayat Sokak No:28, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34337, Türkiye;41.0782231;29.0313777;70;false;true;Fusion;Cenk Debensason has travelled extensively over the years, and this has shaped his personality as a chef. In brief, he grew up in Istanbul, trained in France, and matured as a chef in the United States. You also get a sense of his journey in his dishes. His spicy twist on a vol-au-vent, featuring al dente green asparagus and a lively gribiche sauce, showcases his understanding of French cooking. The chef seamlessly blends classic techniques with Asian flavours, for example in his perfectly seared sea bass, which he elevates with the intense sweet and sour complexity of a Thai sauce. The versatility of this cuisine will keep you on your toes throughout the entire meal. The vintage feel of this stylish 1960s villa is a perfect match for Cenk Debensason's personality. Be sure to visit the Listening Room on the upper floor before or after your meal to enjoy a delicious drink and the chef's carefully curated playlist – sometimes DJs also play. Alternatively, explore Ritmo, an atmospheric space in the same building where you can choose from a small mezze menu. A visit to Arkestra is an experience you won't forget in a hurry.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
833;Vino Locale;Türkiye;Izmir;Kuşçular Mahallesi, 8037. Sokak No:3, Urla, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.2812922;26.7467516;39;false;true;Country cooking, French Contemporary;Ozan and Seray Kumbasar are a power couple who run their business with total dedication. Her love of regional wines is infectious, and she gladly provides astute recommendations. Her trolley of digestifs is a veritable treasure trove. The chef (her husband) shares the same love for their terroir. What he does not grow himself, he likes to source from local producers. Every six weeks, his set menu changes in response to the seasons, which are the inspiration behind his sensual, sophisticated cuisine. His incredible salad is a combination of crunchy asparagus, a velvety pea cream, soft local goat's cheese, crispy fried artichokes and a fragrant herb oil. Radish vinaigrette adds a tangy kick that ties it all together – a masterpiece! At Vino Locale, the produce is put on a pedestal, with subtle details here and there betraying the chef's love for Thailand and Italy. The latter is also evident in the restaurant's decor, which is reminiscent of a trattoria. The art on the walls, the vibrant atmosphere and the romantic terrace all contribute to the infectious charm of this place. Get ready for a memorable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
834;Neolokal;Türkiye;Istanbul;Arap Camii Mahallesi, Bankalar Caddesi No:11/1, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34420, Türkiye;41.0239621;28.973378;19;true;false;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Neolokal bridges the gap between old and new. Respect for Turkish culinary traditions provides the foundation on which this restaurant is able to constantly renew itself. Flavours from the past are the mainstays here and are metamorphosed by the use of contemporary ideas and techniques. Maksut Aşkar and his young team preserve their culinary heritage and guide it into the future with their exciting cuisine. This also involves an emphasis on sustainability, with a vegetarian menu, using carefully selected local produce (including fine Turkish wines!) and working with nearby suppliers. Chef Aşkar puts his stamp on authentic recipes with a quirky subtlety. Think succulent dumpling with minced beef and bulgur, pine nuts and nuts seasoned with mild spices. A creamy emulsion of yoghurt with paprika and a parsley oil round off this light, original dish beautifully. The restaurant's location, in the Salt Galata, makes your experience all the more memorable. The large windows and fabulous terrace afford superb views of Istanbul's rooftops and magnificent mosques. Neolokal is truly special.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
836;Nicole;Türkiye;Istanbul;Tomtom Kaptan Sokak No:18, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34433, Türkiye;41.0302119;28.9777509;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;This restaurant is named after Agnés Marthe Nicole, one of the Franciscan nuns and owners who lived here in the early 20C. A series of narrow lanes leads to the building, which, as you will see, has undergone major renovations. At the entrance, you are greeted by works of modern art. On the top floor, the elegance and luxury of the place is taken up a notch – and the view of the old town from here is fabulous. Exquisite dishes and the well-heeled clientele show that this fine dining restaurant is of the highest calibre. The chef revamps traditional recipes from all over Turkey, adding delicate nuances, and he is clearly proud of his terroir. Shoulder of lamb sourced in Balikesir, for example, is cooked until butter soft in a keskek stew, with a patiently reduced jus that is simply irresistible. A vibrant blend of herbs and yoghurt, along with subtly spiced cooked grains, gives the dish a lively twist. Here, creativity is deployed with respect and a sense of purpose. This celebration of Turkey's rich bounty is complemented by a wine list showcasing local gems that will even surprise connoisseurs.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
837;Mikla;Türkiye;Istanbul;Meşrutiyet Caddesi No:15, 18th floor (18. kat), Tepebaşı/Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34430, Türkiye;41.0311474;28.9742896;100;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Mikla's New Anatolian Kitchen combines respect for tradition with a sense of innovation. The restaurant is an ambassador for the producers they work with, as well as for the great diversity of produce that Turkey has to offer. The chefs use only the finest ingredients (and wines!), which take pride of place in original dishes that are stripped of unnecessary fuss. Everything here revolves around the depth of the flavours, which possess a distinctive Nordic purity.The dishes are not overly elaborate, but their complexity lies in their delicate harmonies. As an example, smoked duck breast is barbecued until medium-rare and then elevated with a symphony of nuances: red wine pepper jelly, roasted hazelnut, tangy cider syrup, a subtly sweet plum sauce with the perfect touch of umami and crisp samphire. The sense of balance is incredible! And those who avoid meat will be glad to know that Mikla always offers a vegan set menu. An adventure awaits you here and that also goes for the setting – the magnificent 360° view of Istanbul you get from the 18th floor of the Marmara Pera hotel really is the icing on the cake.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
838;Sankai by Nagaya;Türkiye;Istanbul;Bebek, Cevdet Paşa Caddesi No:34, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34342, Türkiye;41.0779114;29.0441298;38;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Yoshizumi Nagaya is a Japanese chef who is making waves in Düsseldorf. His mastery of Japanese tradition and technical precision is widely praised there. In Istanbul, he is living up to his reputation. He has set up shop in the cosy boutique hotel Bebek, in the lively neighbourhood of the same name. His stylish Sankai offers stunning views of the Bosporus and subtly marries Japanese authenticity with European influences. His veal cheeks are cooked for 48 hours at a very low temperature until almost candied and intensely flavoursome, then served with beans, a ponzu mayonnaise, powdered vinegar and sesame seeds. Of course, you can also get great sushi here: it is meticulously prepared by Hiroko Shibata using fish from local waters. She serves up the sushi perfectly lukewarm, just sticky enough and with a splash of soy sauce to give this melt-in-your-mouth delicacy that final kick. Whether you order the sushi set menu or opt for the signature set menu, this Japanese dining adventure is compelling. And if you need a lift to or from the restaurant, we have some good news: Sankai by Nagaya provides a free luxury shuttle service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
839;Casa Lavanda;Türkiye;Istanbul;Ulupelit Köyü, Seçilmiş Sokak No:2, Şile, Istanbul, 34980, Türkiye;41.0871196;29.5117319;95;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Casa Lavanda is a haven of tranquillity some 40km from Istanbul. The family-run business includes both a hotel and this restaurant, authentic to its core and adorned with artwork by the proprietress. Tables on the terrace overlooking the magnificent garden are in great demand. Chef Emre Şen has his kitchen garden there, where 80% of the vegetables he uses are grown. This says a lot about his respect for his ingredients. He also has a friendly relationship with local producers who supply him with other goods he loves to work with. This chef is very attached to his terroir and exploits its natural bounty with a sure touch. His cuisine is a celebration of his homeland, Turkish culinary traditions and memories of his time spent in Italy. He whips up al dente agnolotti stuffed with burrata and mascarpone just as effortlessly as he cooks Black Sea sea bass to succulent perfection, serving it with garden-fresh vegetables and a punchy vermouth and mustard seed sauce. This delightfully authentic dining experience is complemented by a wine list featuring over 300 labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
840;OD Urla;Türkiye;Izmir;Rüstem Mahallesi, Süt Pınarı Mevkii, 2018/9 Sokak No:28, Urla, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.344805;26.7622838;22;true;true;Creative French, Country cooking;A winding road takes you to the top of the hill, from where you get a first impression of Osman Sezener's world. Once you arrive at his family estate, you trade the view of olive trees and vines for his impressive vegetable garden. A visit to the garden is an absolute must, as is an overnight stay in one of the guestrooms. This trendy glasshouse restaurant is surrounded by breathtaking natural beauty, and the chefs' passion and energy is infectious. The restaurant grows about half of its ingredients independently and sources other produce from nearby suppliers. Chef Sezener works with a supply radius of about ten kilometres. The commitment to sustainability and local sourcing is as much part of this restaurant's identity as its focus on open-fire cooking. The chef cooks on a charcoal grill to bring out the natural flavours and textures of his ingredients. The cuisine is simple and unpretentious, sometimes even bordering on the rustic, but it is always full of flavour. Take the smooth mashed potatoes with caramelised onions, the perfectly grilled squid glazed with a braised onion jus, and a tuile of the remaining parts of the squid sprinkled with fresh herbs. This cuisine is personal. The way the robust, tender beef rib is balanced with textures of celeriac is testament to the chef's understanding of the ingredients and flavours that nature yields (there is both a vegetarian and non-vegetarian set menu).;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
841;Maçakızı;Türkiye;Bodrum;Göltürkbükü Mahallesi, Keleşharim Caddesi No:70, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1364927;27.380815;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Maçakızı does not give away its secrets easily. The drive that snakes along the narrow roads raises your expectations with each turn, until you arrive at this luxury hotel nestled on a hillside of stunning natural beauty. The mesmerising views of the bay and the elegant decor will captivate you the moment you enter. This is a truly special place, make no mistake. The new take on Aegean cuisine that chef Aret Sahakyan and his team bring to the table only reinforces that feeling. The classic roots of their dishes are evident in the hearty sauces, such as the fish fumet with added butter that gives the barbecued sea bream a delightful richness. The chefs enthusiastically build on that foundation, with a focus on freshness and thoughtfully prepared garnishes. Think pickled vegetable salsa and the umami of fermented goat's cheese with al dente squid and creamy hummus. Champagne lovers will be delighted by the impressive assortment. The wine list is also wide-ranging and includes the best of Turkish and well-known European wine regions. The mysteries of Maçakızı are absolutely worth discovering!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
842;Jiangnan Wok‧Rong;China Mainland;Fuzhou;2F, Shangri-La Hotel, 9 Xinquan South Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.080538;119.312599;23;false;false;Huaiyang;The interior sports a tasteful green colour scheme with plant motifs and fish scale tiles for a style poised between Jiangnan and Fuzhou. In the same vein, the menu features authentic Huaiyang classics alongside Fujian produce and Minnan twists. Braised yellow croaker ‘lion’s head’ meatball impresses with rich silky texture and deep umami. Consider pre-ordering the ginger eight-treasure duck. Each of the 12 private rooms is equipped with tea serving facilities.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
844;Fleurs Et Festin;China Mainland;Xiamen;16 Liaohua Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4595235;118.0859617;47;true;true;Chao Zhou;A three-storey historic building is home to this Chaoshan restaurant. The ground floor sports several tables, while private rooms on the upper floors require a minimum spend. The kitchen team of Chaoshan natives excels in authentic dishes made with fresh produce. Braised goose web in spiced marinade is flavoursome and gelatinous in texture and the local green lobster with taro-scented wax gourd hits the spot every time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
845;Hokklo;China Mainland;Xiamen;6F, Waldorf Astoria Hotel, 1 Lianhua North Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.490016;118.134493;69;true;true;Fujian;“Hokklo” means "hospitable" in Fujian, in keeping with the welcoming space furnished in elegant East-meets-West style. Hailing from the Minnan region, the head chef champions a refined modern take on traditional Fujian cooking. Signatures include steamed wine-scented yellow croaker, mud crab braised in aged wine with dried longans, and Hakka-style braised He Tian chicken claypot with salt and wine. Peruse the seasonal offerings and extensive wine list, too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
846;Yanyu (Jiahe Road);China Mainland;Xiamen;2F, Building A, Xinjing Center, 21 Jiahe Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4826004;118.1152554;18;true;true;Fujian;For 10-plus years, this flagship establishment has been packed with loyal patrons. The modern stylish interior showcases top-notch dried seafood which is used in the famous Fujian Buddha jumps over the wall dish, but you can also enjoy other first-rate dishes without breaking the bank. Try Minnan prawn noodles in orange coloured tomalley soup or made to order black mochi packed with black sesame aroma. The seasonal menu is also worth exploring.;Car park;[]
847;GOAT;Thailand;Bangkok;12 Soi Ekkamai 10 Lane 2, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7274366;100.5872356;72;true;true;Thai contemporary;With high ceilings and an interior adorned with Sino-Portuguese-inspired colours, GOAT plays with design just as it gives the food a unique twist. Elements of Thai, Chinese and Western cuisines are cleverly brought together in a Thai seasonal concept. It's a showcase of the chef's latest inspirations, using herbs grown onsite and ingredients sourced from all over Thailand. The team also crafts and ferments soft drinks that pair perfectly with each course.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
848;AKKEE;Thailand;Nonthaburi;42/99 Mu 7, Pak Kret Bypass Road, Bang Talat, Pak Kret, Nonthaburi, 11120, Thailand;13.8984893;100.5151325;50;true;false;Thai, Contemporary;This unassuming Thai gem delights with bold, regional dishes served in an immersive, dimly lit setting. Chef-owner Sittikorn's meticulous technique shines in his skilful updates of classic Thai recipes that change with the seasons. One notable feature is the traditional preparation in a no-frills kitchen, resulting in dishes with a rustic edge and distinct flavours. For the full experience, opt for the set menu, paired with selected Thai draft beers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
850;AVANT;Thailand;Bangkok;30F, Kimpton Maa-Lai Bangkok, 78 Soi Ton Son, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10300, Thailand;13.7376889;100.5434457;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The Singaporean chef is renowned for his culinary approach that combines traditional and modern techniques with meticulous attention to detail. His introduction to each course reveals his enduring passion for his craft. Seated at the L-shaped counter, diners can soak up the dynamic energy of the kitchen. The city view adds another dimension to this memorable culinary experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
851;IGNIV;Thailand;Bangkok;GF, The St. Regis, 159 Ratchadamri Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7401168;100.5401729;37;true;false;European Contemporary;Igniv means “nest” in Romansh, the mother tongue of chef-founder Andreas Caminada, and there is certainly a playful nest-like quality to this elegant restaurant in The St. Regis Bangkok hotel. The chef has worked alongside the celebrated founder for many years, all collaborating to craft detailed dishes that are executed with a Swiss clock-making precision. Their excellent tasting menu inspires sharing, with multiple dishes served simultaneously.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
852;PRU;Thailand;Phuket;60/1 Mu 6, Srisoonthorn Road, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;8.0384939;98.2765202;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This striking, solar-panelled restaurant by the sea embodies its 'Plant, Raise, Understand' ethos with a culinary journey showcasing seasonal, local foods. Chef Jimmy introduces diners to Thailand's unique produce, using rare ingredients in a menu that focuses on seafood, plants, and home-made preserves and fermented foods. The Japanese Kappo-style counter lends views into the open kitchen, against the backdrop of the ocean.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Valet parking;[]
853;Signature;Thailand;Bangkok;11F, VIE Hotel Bangkok - MGallery, 117/39-40 Phayathai Road, Thanon Phetchaburi, Ratchathewi, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand;13.7506653;100.5319902;35;true;false;French;Veteran Chef Thierry Drapeau expands on his ‘cuisine of the soil’ philosophy he first explored in his native Loire Valley. The art-deco dining room has floor-to-ceiling windows and velvet curtains that open to reveal his stage – an open kitchen. Here, he achieves classic French flavours using imported herbs and edible flowers that evoke their terroir. The Flower Bouquet set menus rotate with the seasons, are great value and matched by excellent service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
854;Potong;Thailand;Bangkok;422 Vanich 1 Road, Samphanthawong, Bangkok, 10100, Thailand;13.7391592;100.5084546;65;true;true;Innovative;Traditional and novel converge at this Thai-Chinese fine dining restaurant from chef Pichaya “Pam” Soontornyanakij. Set in a historical Sino-Portuguese building that used to be Pam's family’s Chinese pharmacy, Potong blends rustic and modern décor from ground floor bar to rooftop chill space. Her progressive tasting menu is infused with storytelling and hits its peak with aged duck breast. To make it even better, ask the sommelier for a wine pairing.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
855;Suan Thip;Thailand;Nonthaburi;17/9 Mu 7, Sukhaprachasan 2 Road, Bang Phut, Pak Kret, Nonthaburi, 11120, Thailand;13.9271923;100.5021955;67;false;false;Thai;The lush riverside gardens, pavilion and ponds feel a world away from the bustle of Bangkok’s streets. Suan Thip serves refined royal Thai cuisine in an idyllic setting for weddings. The delectable stir-fried crispy catfish with curry, dry curry paste and kaffir lime chiffonade strikes the perfect balance of textures, spices and a citrus aroma. The betal leaf wraps offer another pleasurable gift of flavours with pink lotus petals and a superb Miang Kum sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
856;Aulis;Thailand;Phang-Nga;Iniala Beach House, 40/14 Mu 6, Ban Natai, Khok Kloi, Takua Thung, Phang-Nga, 82140, Thailand;8.2878698;98.274228;95;true;false;Creative;Opened in December 2023, Simon Rogan's first Thailand venture, Aulis, is based on a 'chef's table' concept. The multi-course tasting menu presents native ingredients, many sourced from Thailand and local grower collaborations. Begin with an amuse-bouche over drinks in the lounge, then take a seat in front of the open kitchen to watch the chefs precisely plate farm-to-table fare imbued with Rogan's signature flair. The non-alcoholic pairing is also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
857;Maison Dunand;Thailand;Bangkok;55 Soi Sathon 10, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7231296;100.5274976;29;false;false;French Contemporary;Following his successful time as Head Chef of Le Normandie, Arnaud Dunand Sauthier’s next venture was opening his own place. Here he welcomes you into a home designed like the Alpine chalets of the Savoie region in France, where he grew up. The French contemporary tasting menu is inspired by his alpine origins, childhood trips to Brittany and his glittering international culinary journey. Expect too an excellent wine cellar with good representation for Alsace and Savoie.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
858;Resonance;Thailand;Bangkok;108, 4 Soi Sukhumvit 65, Phra Khanong Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.722243;100.5916526;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At this relaxed and friendly restaurant, chef Shunsuke Shimomura takes diners on a journey through his past, weaving dishes from his experience working around the world into his precise seasonal tasting menu. Open for dinner only, the restaurant fills the ground floor of a contemporary two-storey house, with minimalist, all-white décor that puts the focus on the cooking. To add another layer of subtlety to your meal, ask for the tea pairing a day or two in advance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
859;Haoma;Thailand;Bangkok;231/3 Soi Sukhumvit 31, Khlong Toei Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7435066;100.5676933;88;false;true;Indian;Chef Deepanker Khosla says of his Haoma team, "We grow what we cook, we cook what we love.” And what is that? Sustainable, seasonal, local ingredients sourced from farmers, breeders, fisherfolk and the restaurant’s own garden. They’re turned into delicious, beautifully plated neo-Indian dishes that form seasonal tasting menus (including a vegetarian one). It all happens in a Nordic-style dining room where even the decor includes unused plant parts.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
860;Le Normandie;Thailand;Bangkok;5F, Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 48 Soi Charoen Krung 40,  Charoen Krung Road, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7238479;100.51627;23;false;true;French Contemporary;Set in an elegant space adorned with handcrafted chandeliers and breathtaking river views, Le Normandie has been Bangkok's premier destination for haute cuisine for over 60 years. Now led by a renowned British chef who began his career in New York, the restaurant continues to impress. Innovative techniques and a modern interpretation of classic French dishes ensure the sophisticated dining experience lives on.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
861;Wana Yook;Thailand;Bangkok;5/15 Phaya Thai Road, Thanon Phaya Thai, Ratchathewi, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand;13.7631965;100.5376899;77;true;true;Thai contemporary;Inside a charming 100-year-old colonial house, Chef Chalee Kader creates an innovative seasonal tasting menu inspired by ‘Khao Kaeng’ or ‘rice topped with curry,’ and here, every course features rice from a different region of Thailand. The chef’s flavoursome contemporary dishes are served in the beautiful dining room, elegantly outfitted with wood furniture and silk cushions. To complete the experience, enjoy after-dinner drinks at the cosy ground-floor bar.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
862;INDDEE;Thailand;Bangkok;68/1 Soi Lang Suan, Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7376678;100.5421848;65;false;false;Indian, Contemporary;This restaurant, tucked away in a small Bangkok alley, offers modern, Indian-inspired gastronomy. Their set menu showcases diverse Indian regions, extensively using the charcoal grill. Skilful and detailed creations like hand-pulled chicken khurchan shine, and the seafood, influenced by the chef's Japanese background, is a highlight. The impeccable service team enhances the overall experience with attentive, professional, and knowledgeable service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
863;NAWA;Thailand;Bangkok;1F, Parklane, 18 Soi Sukhumvit 61, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7233058;100.5840057;78;false;true;Thai contemporary;The logo, fashioned from an N and a W in the shape of a needle flower, stands for Nawa – Thai for innovation. Chefs Joe and Saki Hoshino embrace this concept using modern techniques to produce central Thai cuisine with authentic yet bold flavours, and a seasonal tasting menu of finger food, small bites and modified versions of main courses. The low-lit dining room has a modern and elegant design.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
864;Aksorn;Thailand;Bangkok;5F, Central: The Original Store, 1266 Charoenkrung Road, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7244882;100.5162344;61;false;true;Thai;Inspired by old Thai cookbooks, David Thompson revisits the culinary lives of different chefs. See the action in the open kitchen from the dining area or opt for the outdoor terrace to take in the city and street. The highlight dish features smoked kingfish relish with wild ginger. Try the refreshing Watsana, a non-alcoholic drink that perfectly balances sour notes with the sweetness of watermelon.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
865;Coda;Thailand;Bangkok;130-132 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7360104;100.5460976;16;true;true;Thai contemporary;With 10 years of experience working in Australia, the chef seamlessly blends his international perspective with a deep love for his homeland as he crafts the menu. His culinary philosophy celebrates the essence of regional Thai cuisine while incorporating modern techniques to forge a fresh identity. In an elegant, modern space with high ceilings, enjoy the concise, expertly seasoned tasting menu, rife with delicate yet richly layered flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
866;Samrub Samrub Thai;Thailand;Bangkok;39/11 Soi Yommarat, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7268938;100.5373823;43;true;true;Thai;This white, 4-storey renovated house in Si Lom hosts an intimate dining experience. The menu changes bi-monthly as chef Prin Polsuk, well-known on the scene for his work at Nahm and Sala Rim Naam, is inspired by new discoveries and seasonal changes. Delving into rare cookbooks, he reproduces ancient Thai recipes that trace the ages, and crafts a complex amalgamation of aromas to serve a truly original tasting menu. Bookings are only through social media.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
867;Nahm;Thailand;Bangkok;GF, Como Metropolitan, 27 Sathon Tai Road, Thung Maha Mek, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7231647;100.5389536;66;true;false;Thai;Every dish displays Chef Pim’s creativity and attention to detail, with her passion for authentic Thai flavours shining through in both the set menus and à la carte dishes. For the full experience, order the Heritage set menu. It boasts a stream of delicious dishes from savoury canapés to flavourful mains and a luscious dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
868;Jay Fai;Thailand;Bangkok;327 Maha Chai Road, Samran Rat, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.752571;100.5046981;58;true;false;Street Food;Jay Fai has long been a street food icon, and for good reason — the begoggled chef’s signature crispy, golden-brown crab omelettes are simply unparalleled. If you’re looking for another reason to love the local legend, then also try her excellent stir-fried noodles with seafood and gravy. This is a deservedly popular spot and they don’t take bookings, so be sure to arrive early and be prepared to queue.;Cash only;[]
869;Saneh Jaan;Thailand;Bangkok;Sindhorn Tower, 130-132 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7356117;100.5457543;56;true;true;Thai;Thai cuisine evolves here while honouring tradition. The menu offers classics and vintage recipes, including those favoured by the royal family. Standouts include sweet and sour crispy rice noodles with river prawns and flavoursome massaman curry with slow-cooked Kamphaeng Saen beef. Begin in the bar with signature cocktails made using Thai liqueurs and herbs.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
870;80/20;Thailand;Bangkok;1052-1054 Charoen Krung 26 Road, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7311121;100.5154966;80;false;true;Thai contemporary;Named for the ratio of local ingredients to the chef's inspiration, 80/20 promises a dynamic seasonal tasting menu, featuring innovative delights from the first bite to the last. The concept extends to the design, using predominantly Thai materials in an industrial loft style. The chef employs traditional techniques to create contemporary interpretations of classic Thai dishes with Lao influences. Mains are paired with aromatic Yasothon jasmine rice cooked in coconut milk and pandan.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
871;Elements, Inspired by Ciel Bleu;Thailand;Bangkok;25F, The Okura Prestige, 57 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7428645;100.5476497;62;false;true;French Contemporary;Boasting impressive city views, ideal for a date and featuring a chic décor with an open kitchen, oversized light fittings, and charcoal walls. Working closely with Ciel Bleu in Amsterdam, and inspired by French fine dining with Japanese influences, they offer three tasting experiences: Ku-Ki, Chikyu and Mizu, as well as The Complete Experience. A menu highlight is the Akita Wagyu, showcasing succulent marbled Japanese beef grilled to perfection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
873;Blue by Alain Ducasse;Thailand;Bangkok;Unit L101, 1F, ICONLUXE ICONSIAM Shopping Centre, 299 Charoen Nakhon Road, Khlong Ton Sai, Khlong San, Bangkok, 10600, Thailand;13.7265916;100.5105619;70;true;false;French Contemporary;The moment it launched in 2019, Blue by Alain Ducasse became a prime destination for gastronomy lovers from Bangkok and beyond. The restaurant brings the renowned chef’s contemporary French fine dining to Icon Siam in an elegant room with panoramic views of the Chao Phraya River. Under its executive chef, Blue offers diners a chance to savour world-class dishes using top quality ingredients. Advanced reservations are essential.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
874;Chim by Siam Wisdom;Thailand;Bangkok;315 Soi Ongkharak 13, Thanon Nakhon Chai Si, Dusit, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7891795;100.5185611;20;true;false;Thai;Chef Thanintorn 'Noom' Chantharawan's passionate take on traditional Thai cuisine balances domestic with international and classic with contemporary in dishes that use first-rate ingredients from around Thailand. The "Thai food in 4 Regions” set, presents a dazzling array of flavours. The setting, a vintage wooden house decorated with abundant greenery, invites you to relax and savour your meal. Booking is a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
875;Sen Omakase;Spain;Madrid;Santa María Magdalena 14, Madrid, 28016, Spain;40.4622352;-3.6701712;42;true;false;Japanese;If you enjoy Japanese cuisine, this is one of those places that is a must given its focus on presentation and the innovative touch that they add to its dishes (over 35 different courses). Chef Steven Wu, who trained in restaurants in both Tokyo and Kyoto, offers guests his surprise Omakase menu which is the only option here. His Kaiseki-style cooking places full emphasis on the seasonality of ingredients and a respect for tradition, replicating the five types of time-honoured preparation and cooking methods to ensure the perfect harmony between visual and tasting sensations. The immersive experience here develops in four different spaces, each with its own personality: the reception area (the garden-style corridor, where the aim is to recreate the different seasons of the year), a splendid Japanese dining counter, the tea room (where an ancestral ceremony takes place), and the cocktail bar, with its Japanese pop music, where you have the option of rounding off your meal with a choice of whiskies and cocktails.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
876;Cañabota;Spain;Seville;Orfila 3, Seville, 41003, Spain;37.3935972;-5.9936533;53;true;true;Seafood;It is possible to achieve excellence from apparent simplicity and Cañabota is a perfect example of this.This centrally located restaurant next to the Capilla de San Andrés (a chapel also known as the Hermandad de los Panaderos or Brotherhood of Bread-makers), has a gastro-bar ambience, with a fishmonger’s-style counter at the entrance and an open kitchen that enables guests to admire the grilling process at close quarters. Fish and seafood from Andalucia’s Atlantic coast are the mainstays on an à la carte which combines traditional and cutting-edge cooking, and a tasting menu that features even more elaborate dishes. We recommended booking in advance and allow yourself to be guided in your choices as the menu changes daily in line with the best fish and seafood available at market.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
877;A Tafona;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Virxe da Cerca 7, Santiago de Compostela, 15703, Spain;42.880744;-8.5402512;73;false;false;Contemporary;There are personal goals in life that develop with knowledge, travel experience and lots of effort, and this is the perspective from which we should assess the career of Lucía Freitas, a chef with an acute awareness for food intolerances and who is indefatigable in her quest for a healthier style of cooking that uses as many vegetables from her own garden as possible. This welcoming restaurant, with an interior design that combines a contemporary aesthetic, open stonework and a large skylight, is the perfect setting in which to savour modern, regionally inspired cuisine that showcases Galicia’s rich bounty (fish and seafood, in particular) in dishes that are delicious, colourful and feature strong technique and a feminine touch. Choose between two interesting tasting menus: Sosiego and Algarabía. The walls here are embellished with a fine collection of photos dedicated to the women who work in the town’s wholesale food market.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
878;Almo de Juan Guillamón;Spain;Murcia;Madre de Dios 15, Murcia, 30004, Spain;37.9842525;-1.132081;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant (which until recently was called AlmaMater) with plenty of character which extols the virtue of Mediterranean cuisine without closing its eyes to influences from elsewhere and which pulls out all the stops to ensure an authentic gourmet experience. Behind its floor-to-ceiling windows, the impression is of a young and contemporary eatery on two floors with a focus on market-inspired cuisine, featuring classic food pairings with an unfettered global approach. Chef Juan Guillamón allows himself full licence to introduce flavours acquired on his travels: for six seasons he worked as a chef for the Ferrari motor racing team, and was the personal chef for the British ambassador in Spain. The well-balanced à la carte, offering dishes such as the carpaccio of aged beef with black aioli, cured egg yolk and tartare sauce, and “parpatana” of red tuna with a fennel purée and caponata, is complemented by a tasting menu that is only available if served to the whole table.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
879;Esperit Roca;Spain;Sant Julià de Ramis;Major, Entrada 1, Sant Julià de Ramis, 17481, Spain;42.0323124;2.8453888;47;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;An old military fortress provides the backdrop for this Roca brothers venture, occupying the imposing Castillo de Sant Julià de Ramis, barely 10km from Girona, which they have transformed into a leading food and cultural centre. In this setting, which also features a superb hotel, everything makes an impression, from the access through the CCR exhibition explaining the creative processes of El Celler de Can Roca (CCR), to the impressive dome in the wine cellar (housing over 80 000 bottles), academy-library and the distillery that now acts as the restaurant’s R&D space. In the dining room, where the predominant materials are cement and concrete, the aim is to bring the surrounding natural landscapes into the heart of the room via the large picture windows. In terms of cuisine, the à la carte favours classic El Celler recipes, albeit with a twist that adds the eatery’s own personality. This is complemented by two highly original menus: Espíritu Salado (6 dishes and 2 desserts) and Espíritu Dulce (2 dishes and 6 desserts).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
880;MAE Barcelona;Spain;Barcelona;Sant Elíes 22, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.4012598;2.1443599;44;true;false;Creative;This restaurant occupying the erstwhile Freixa Tradició features a designer-inspired interior and brings together the expertise and dreams of three friends (the name MAE is the Costa Rican Spanish word for “companion” or “colleague”): manager Mariella Rodríguez (from Costa Rica) and chefs Diego Mondragón (from Colombia) and Germán Espinosa (from Spain). The cuisine here is built around the concept of “syncretism” which can be described as the “combination of different theories, attitudes and opinions”. When applied to MAE’s cooking, this translates into a surprising fusion of ingredients from around the world showcased in dishes such as Galician clams or the legendary Tarta de Santiago paired with, for example, chilli peppers or tepache from Latin America. The à la carte is complemented by two impressive tasting menus (MAE and Gran MAE), featuring superb dishes such as “molluscs with dried cherry tomatoes, seaweed and yellow chilli peppers”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
881;Els Casals;Spain;Sagàs;Masía Els Casals, Sagàs, 08517, Spain;42.0325482;1.9605884;73;true;true;Catalan, Contemporary;The devotion to the local area is clearly evident here thanks to the focus on vegetables from Els Casals’ own farm, meat from animals reared in semi liberty, eggs from their own hens, a herd of Duroc breed pigs, and local wild mushrooms, truffles etc. Almost all of its ingredients are sourced from the family farm, as part of a philosophy to “close the circle”: ingredients are produced, cooked and then served on the premises.The restaurant, which occupies an 18C farmhouse, reflects the work of five farmer brothers, one of whom, Oriol Rovira, is the chef. His à la carte features seasonal dishes, including game, and his famous Pularda poultry dish. Els Casals is a fine example of sustainability, with a philosophy centred on zero-miles ingredients. It also offers a few well-appointed guestrooms for those keen to stay longer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
882;Versátil;Spain;Zarza de Granadilla;Lagar 6, Zarza de Granadilla, 10710, Spain;40.2372182;-6.0476206;49;true;false;Contemporary;If the prospect of a short country break appeals to you, this restaurant in the north of Cáceres province is the perfect destination. It is rare to find refined cuisine of this level in such a small rural village, so Versátil will definitely come as a pleasant surprise, hence our recommendation to book ahead. Fronting the project is Alejandro Hernández (alongside his brothers Jesús David and José Luis who are in charge of the dining room), who worked under the renowned Martín Berasategui, under whom he acquired the culinary skills that he now showcases in this eclectic yet welcoming space. Choose between an à la carte of updated traditional cuisine with a nod to seasonal Extremadura ingredients (carpaccio of Iberian pork “presa” with a vegetable vinaigrette, charcoal-grilled Extremadura veal tenderloin etc) and two tasting menu options (Experiencia and Versátil). A more informal menu is also available in the Bodega, which also doubles as an art gallery.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
884;Deliranto;Spain;Salou;Llevant 7, Salou, 43840, Spain;41.0767475;1.1326351;34;false;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The quest for new culinary experiences has become a trend and that is precisely what is on offer here, where Deliranto’s haute cuisine is connected with stories, operas and classic tales (The Fable of Orpheus, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz, Alice in Wonderland etc) that transport us to another world. The unique, occasionally surreal cuisine of chef Josep Moreno starts off in the Cook & Travel gastro-bar, continues with more appetisers in the renovated kitchen, and reaches its zenith at the dining table where guests are treated to menus (short and long versions are both available) featuring a veritable symphony of starters and main courses. In this modern, eclectic eatery with just a few tables, the dining experience is considered a major spectacle, so that each course is as dramatic as the last, giving the impression that you are in an intimate theatre waiting for the curtain to rise. The culinary themes here change twice a year.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
885;Simpar;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Rúa Do Vilar 47, Santiago de Compostela, 15705, Spain;42.8785045;-8.5446005;40;false;false;Contemporary;In this restaurant, fronting one of the city’s emblematic cobbled streets leading to its famous Praza das Praterías and cathedral, they are proud to say that Simpar’s daily menus are always built around ingredients sourced the same day from trusted suppliers, whose names they are also happy to share with guests. In the contemporary-style interior, featuring a spacious bar at the entrance, young local chef Áxel Smyth showcases his fresh and creative Galician-inspired cuisine with a touch of elegance on two menus (Conocer and Simpar), plus a limited à la carte featuring dishes taken from the former. Strong technique adds immensely to the dining experience, and every menu has the option of adding an extra dish (an updated version of the traditional tripe with chickpea stew) to it. One of his signature dishes is Galician-style fish of the day, which changes with the seasons and is accompanied by crushed potatoes and a three-textured “ajada” sauce.;;[]
886;Refectorio;Spain;Sardón de Duero;Carretera N 122, Sardón de Duero, 47340, Spain;41.6156187;-4.4106521;60;true;false;Creative;Alongside its unquestionably high levels of gastronomy, Refectorio enjoys a spectacular setting in a 12C monastery surrounded by nature, wine cellars and vineyards, and is renowned for its spectacular and pinpoint service, which includes an aperitif in “La Cueva” (home to the bodega’s private collection). Reus-born chef Marc Segarra offers guests a choice of menus (Terroir, Origin and Legacy) and a highly creative culinary experience with wine-pairing options that provide a perfect opportunity to taste some superb vintages. Seasonal produce from the farm here and ingredients sourced from small-scale local producers also add to the appeal (recommended dishes include the delicious “14C escabeche”). Another interesting feature is the use of lees (the natural sediment produced during the wine fermentation process) in both the monkfish with emulsion dish and the butter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
887;OSA;Spain;Madrid;Ribera del Manzanares 123, Madrid, 28008, Spain;40.4289589;-3.7327587;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Although located a little away from the heart of the city, this small chalet on the banks of the Manzanares has everything it needs to win over its guests, including an open kitchen at the entrance, small inter-connecting dining rooms, and a wine cellar and chillout lounge upstairs.Via dishes such as red mullet amasake, saltwater eel, pigeon dokuganryu, and homemade stuffed pig’s trotter, the well-balanced duo of chefs at the helm, Jorge Muñoz and Sara Peral, clearly demonstrate that their time working at leading restaurants such as Mugaritz has been well spent. Their cuisine is centred on a single tasting menu (choose between long and short options) which is complemented by what might first appear to be simple touches but which bring out the full flavours of its top-notch seasonal ingredients through smoking and maturing techniques, precise cooking methods and dishes featuring an explosion of flavours. The raw ingredients used in the dishes are also brought to your table, with explanations of their provenance and how they are cooked.;Air conditioning;[]
888;NM;Spain;Oviedo;Víctor Chávarri 2, Oviedo, 33001, Spain;43.3652147;-5.8424752;92;true;false;Creative;NM is situated inside the spectacular and unique El Vasco shopping mall, which has one floor entirely dedicated to food and dining. This attractive restaurant, whose designer dining space occupies an area called Nastura, features a bar counter that can also be used for dining, and a focus on dishes prepared with top-quality ingredients which reflect the roots and traditions of the Asturias region on every plate. Here, award-winning chef Nacho Manzano employs contemporary techniques that extract the maximum from the ingredients he works with. This is demonstrated on a seasonal tasting menu (choose between the shorter or longer options) that takes guests on a journey through the bountiful meadows, woods and mountains of Cantabria and the family’s market garden in Narbasu. Consistency is the core message, built around the flavours and aromas of this region. You’ll need to state your menu preference when making your booking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
889;Fraula;Spain;Valencia;Cirilo Amorós 84, Valencia, 46004, Spain;39.4694922;-0.366224;94;false;true;Contemporary;Fraula is located just a few metres from the Mercado de Colón, a market that is a listed national monument and one of the best examples of local Modernist architecture from the early 20C. This minimalist-contemporary restaurant is both visually impressive and welcoming, and takes its name from the Valencian world for “strawberry”. Roseta Félix and Daniel Malavía, the two chefs at the helm here, enjoy creating a bond with their guests, hence their alternating appearances in the dining room. They offer three contemporary-style menus (Cebera, available at lunchtime from Tuesday to Friday, and two tasting-style menus: Alfàbega and Fraula) all of which are based around seasonal ingredients, especially those sourced from local market gardens. The dining experience covers all bases here, starting with superb appetisers (such as the delicious escabeche mussel tartlet with fries) and always ending with an impressive dessert - we particularly enjoyed the “huitlacoche, popcorn and black garlic”!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
890;Prodigi;Spain;Barcelona;Girona 145, Barcelona, 08037, Spain;41.3984715;2.1662592;75;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The first thing to attract your attention at Prodigi is its name, created from the first syllable of three neighbouring streets (Provença, Diagonal and Girona). In this contemporary-style restaurant, the à la carte remains faithful to seasonal ingredients despite its concise nature and extols the virtues of traditional Catalan cuisine which it has successfully brought up to date. It is complemented by two menus (one only available at lunchtime midweek, and a second more extensive tasting-style option). Chef Jordi Tarré, who always creates highly elegant dishes full of nuances, surprised us with dishes such as the red curry with seasonal mushrooms, smoked baba ganoush, braised mini cobs and coriander sprouts, and the grilled sea bass with tender broad beans and a salsify “manjar blanco”. Whatever you choose, you won’t be disappointed!;Air conditioning;[]
891;Toki;Spain;Madrid;Sagasta 28, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.42788;-3.6972754;32;true;true;Japanese;Savour Japanese cuisine in this exclusive restaurant bearing the hallmark of famous sommelier Marcos Granda, where the full focus is on enjoying the experience without worrying about the time (“toki” in Japanese). In this intimate and exclusive setting centred around a single sushi bar that is designed to personalise the guest experience to the full (Toki only has six seats!), chef Tadayoshi Teddy Motoa guides us on a magnificent journey through the history and evolution of Japanese cooking. His tasting menu shows us how the preparation of nigiri has changed over time (especially in the preparation of rice). In so doing, he enters into a dialogue with guests through three recipes (one contemporary, one from the 18C, and the third from the 16C) that are the height of delicacy, as well as premium ingredients that will delight the tastebuds. The extensive sake list is an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
892;Ayalga;Spain;Ribadesella;Dionisio Ruisánchez 6, Ribadesella, 33560, Spain;43.4651241;-5.067508;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;There are few places in Ribadesella with as much personality as the Villa Rosario hotel – the iconic Spanish colonial-style property dating back to 1914 that overlooks Playa de Santa Marina and is home to this restaurant. Featuring a glass-fronted terrace with splendid views of the Cantabrian Sea, Ayalga’s kitchen is run by chef Israel Moreno, a team player who, instead of considering himself to be the captain of the ship, sees himself as part of the crew on every watch. Options here include a concise, contemporary-inspired à la carte and two interesting tasting menus (Sabores de la Tierrina and Experiencia Ayalga), all of which feature dishes with a rare harmony, highly skilled technical detail, and superb flavours from the best local ingredients (in addition to newly created dishes such as the sirloin of venison with a spicy pumpkin purée, you’ll also find Ayalga’s classic recipes such as the egg with a foie gras and parmentier velouté). International wines have a strong presence on the extensive wine list here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
893;Taller Arzuaga;Spain;Quintanilla de Onésimo;Carretera N-122, Quintanilla de Onésimo, 47350, Spain;41.6280676;-4.3237821;46;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Taller is located at the prestigious Arzuaga bodega, where the worlds of wine and gastronomy go hand in hand. It’s possible to enhance your experience via a variety of activities (tastings, wine sessions, visits to the Finca La Planta to view its deer reserve) and even a chance to meet famous designer Amaya Arzuaga who makes an appearance here as often as she can! Access to the restaurant is via an interactive and highly surprising corridor-tunnel which leads to a cutting-edge dining room with views of inside the bodega, Taller’s attractive external surroundings, and everything that goes on in the kitchen. The cooking here, which is showcased on an à la carte and two tasting menus (Reserva and Gran Reserva), is highly creative in style with subtle nods to game and a desire to extract maximum flavour from ingredients sourced from the estate’s organic garden, home to over 100 different species.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
894;Auga;Spain;Gijón;Claudio Alvargonzález, Gijón, 33201, Spain;43.5465083;-5.6665859;41;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is located on one of the breakwaters at the heart of Gijón’s marina in a delightful and unique waterfront setting. Guests will be pleasantly surprised by Auga’s bright, elegant feel, featuring a classic-cum-contemporary dining room with a predominance of wood, and a superb terrace overlooking the sea where you would like time to stand still! The cuisine here varies depending on market availability and is built around the creativity of Gonzalo Pañeda, a highly experienced chef who demonstrates consummate skill in his dishes along with a deep-seated respect for his ingredients and for the traditions of Asturias, which he has skilfully brought up to date. Dishes we particularly enjoyed include the delightfully creamy scallop, roe and seaweed, and for dessert the intensely flavoured goat’s cheese soup with hazelnuts and honey.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
896;Montia;Spain;San Lorenzo de El Escorial;Juan de Austria 7, San Lorenzo de El Escorial, 28200, Spain;40.5925602;-4.1474372;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;If you’re keen to eat in a unique setting and somewhere with its own philosophy, Montia (a restaurant where the surrounding mountain landscapes provide the cornerstone for its cuisine) could be the place. It boasts a rustic-contemporary ambience which could not be more welcoming, featuring attractive natural wood tables and an open-view kitchen between the two dining rooms (one by the entrance with a fireplace, the other overlooking a small garden). Chef Daniel Ochoa, who can constantly be seen serving and explaining dishes, sees himself as both a farmer and forager. This is clearly evident in what he calls his “wild cuisine” that evolves with the seasons and flies the flag for small-scale local producers and is showcased on two menus: Montia and Montia XL. Standout dishes include the “callos” (tripe), one of the best to be found anywhere around Madrid, and the “pepitoria” of milk cap mushrooms and sea urchins.;Air conditioning;[]
897;Epílogo;Spain;Tomelloso;Paseo Ramón Ugena 15, Tomelloso, 13700, Spain;39.1491269;-3.0270091;43;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Epílogo’s setting, above a complex of function rooms, and its attractive cuisine, creative in style and focusing on mini dishes (which it describes as “new La Mancha cooking”, come as a pleasant surprise here. Head chef Rubén Sánchez-Camacho showcases his contemporary, regionally inspired recipes on two menus: El Inicio and Historias del Guadiana. The latter stands out for its showcasing of the Guadiana river as a tool for cultural connection, by trying to create a menu featuring ingredients and dishes from each region through which the river passes, from Castilla-La Mancha to Andalucia, but without forgetting the Alentejo or Algarve regions of Portugal which it also straddles. Its interesting dishes span the traditional (such as the garlic soup fritter) and the more innovative (the mussel royale).When it comes to your wine choice, we recommend following the guidance of sommelier Ramón, the chef’s brother, who is happy to suggest some superb pairings for you.;Air conditioning;[]
899;iBAi by Paulo Airaudo;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Getaria 15, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20005, Spain;43.3182991;-1.9806425;46;false;true;Basque;This centrally located restaurant, which was a popular name in local cuisine under the baton of chef Alicio Garro, has reinvented itself and has had a new lease of life thanks to award-winning chef Paulo Airaudo, who brings with him his personal vision of classic recipes. The bar at the entrance is still here, serving tapas made on the spot, and is perfect for an informal glass of wine. Added to this is the small dining room in the basement, featuring six impressively sized tables, each of which comes with its own “cupboard”. The cuisine, which comes courtesy of two tasting menus to which you can add different appetisers and starters, has a clear market focus, with the aim of showcasing time-honoured Basque cuisine through dishes such as the spectacular grilled Carabinero prawns as well as the five hake cheek “kokotxas” (two battered, two grilled and one confit).;;[]
900;Massana;Spain;Girona;Bonastruc de Porta 10-12, Girona, 17001, Spain;41.98505;2.81958;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A family-run restaurant with plenty of history and a positive future ahead of it. After more than 30 years at the helm, chef Pere Massana and his wife Ana Roger have brought their children into the business, with one in charge of the dining room, the other bringing fresh impetus to Massana’s cuisine in the kitchen.Here, you’ll find an elegant setting and a combination of tradition and innovation that highlights a constant focus on locally sourced ingredients and the use of contemporary cooking techniques to maximise flavour. There’s also plenty of attention to detail, presentation and balance. Nor is the chef afraid to introduce surprise touches or look further afield for inspiration. He also enjoys reworking the restaurant’s signature dishes such as the superb Homenaje al Magret de Pato Massana, a grilled duck speciality that has been on the menu since 1986.;Air conditioning;[]
902;Origen;Spain;Carcaixent;Avenida Germanies 3, Carcaixent, 46740, Spain;39.1192;-0.45192;88;true;false;Contemporary;After a long career working in restaurants in Spain and around the world (Austria, UK, Singapore, Mexico etc), chef Àlex Vidal has returned to his roots to open his own restaurant, which is contemporary in feel and boasts a glass-fronted kitchen on one side of the bright dining room. On the menu, the goal is to showcase honest Valencian cooking, particularly from the Carcaixent area, and to provide a modern vision of traditional dishes and stews which are always prepared with organic and locally sourced ingredients. The supremely delicate broths and sauces warrant special attention thanks to their nuanced flavours and unquestionable technical mastery. Four tasting menus are available: Mercat (lunchtime only), Carcaixent, Origen and Ternils. One dish you won’t want to miss out on is the delicious “amparín” of leek, cuttlefish and peanuts, which pays homage to the area’s gastronomic heritage with its version of Carcaixent’s most emblematic tapa.;Air conditioning;[]
903;Ansils;Spain;Anciles;General Ferraz 6, Anciles, 22469, Spain;42.5909183;0.5097959;74;false;true;Contemporary;This restaurant, located in a village in the Benasque valley, has been in business since 1984 and is run by the third generation of the family – it is now overseen by the niece and nephew of founder Pilarín Ferrer with Iris Jordán at the helm in the kitchen and her brother Bruno in charge of the dining room and wine cellar. Under their guidance, the restaurant has had a change of direction with a focus on contemporary cuisine that seeks inspiration from tradition through the culinary influences from the valley and a more modern perspective. Game and vegetables from their own garden take centre stage here, as they are keen to showcase time-honoured ingredients and revitalise the cooking techniques of bygone days (salting, curing, escabeches etc) but with elegance, personality and a lightness of touch. Choose between two tasting menus: Monte Bajo and Alta Montaña (the first offering four courses, the second six) to which they add small bites entitled “picnic in the mountains” at the start of the meal, plus a dessert selection at the end.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
904;En la Parra;Spain;Salamanca;San Pablo 80, Salamanca, 37008, Spain;40.9606615;-5.6642767;22;false;false;Contemporary;Located opposite the monumental and iconic Plateresque façade of the church of the Convento de San Esteban, designed in the style of a stone altarpiece, En la Parra features two contemporary dining rooms, the main one of which enjoys views of the open kitchen to watch the creative culinary process unfold. Ably supported by her husband Alberto Rodríguez in the dining room and wine cellar, chef Rocío Parra remains faithful to her modern style of cooking rooted in local and traditional cuisine. This is showcased on two tasting menus, Pizarra (Slate) and Granito (Granite), the names of which highlight the predominant geological characteristics of Salamanca’s vineyards. Both menus share some of the same dishes and vary only in the number of dishes on offer (19 or 25). These include a delicious succession of Iberian pork-based tapas and appetisers (from the producer FISAN) as well as more contemporary dishes (especially the main courses) that showcase ingredients from the province.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
905;Casa Nova;Spain;Sant Martí Sarroca;Finca Cal Tòfol – Barri La Bleda, Sant Martí Sarroca, 08731, Spain;41.3555907;1.6415855;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;More than just a restaurant, Casa Nova is a mini-paradise on Earth! This charming old country property that was once a poultry farm is run by a couple with a total commitment to sustainability and no half measures. Upon arrival in the car park, guests are given a close-up tour with explanations that highlight their environmental concerns. Following this, in a delightful atmosphere combining the past and present, chef Andrés Torres offers two contemporary-style menus (Viña and Gran Vendimia) that are based around time-honoured dishes made by his mother as well as local ingredients (the restaurant has a large kitchen garden with chickens, bees, tuna drying sheds and coffee roasters, grows its own shitake mushrooms, and produces its own vinegars, wines etc). There’s also the occasional international influence resulting from the chef’s humanitarian trips abroad (as an example, Casa Nova also bakes bread in a wood-fired oven in the same way as the indigenous communities on the Peruvian altiplano). The wine cellar features an impressive selection of vintage labels that come as a pleasant surprise.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
906;Kamezí;Spain;Playa Blanca;Mónaco 2, Playa Blanca, 35580, Spain;28.8598924;-13.8655864;55;true;false;Creative;Part of the highly attractive Kamezí Boutique Villas complex, this iconic space boasts attractive views that bring added personality to the dining experience, which is enhanced by the gourmet boutique. The striking display counter showcases its top-quality ingredients (the staff are happy to provide details on their suppliers from Lanzarote and across the Canaries), including bread baked on the premises. The creative cuisine, based around local flavours and ingredients, is centred on a single tasting menu entitled Bernegal (a large primitive ceramic plate typical of the Canaries), featuring dishes such as squid with a lemon and chilli pepper pilpil, avocado, cauliflower and chocolate. The archipelago also takes centre-stage on the wine list and cheese trolley!;Air conditioning;[]
907;Suto;Spain;Barcelona;Violant de Hungría Reina de Aragón 134, Barcelona, 08028, Spain;41.379936;2.1334655;82;true;false;Japanese;An intimate Japanese-style restaurant close to Sants railway station, featuring a bar (there are also a few tables) where guests can eat while watching young chef Yoshikazu Suto at work. The ambience here is more that of a private house in which the staff are cooking for you rather than a restaurant. The Omakase menu on offer here (which combines hot and cold dishes and is served to all guests at the same time) features highly personalised Japanese-style recipes, followed by delicious nigiri that are truly unforgettable and prepared with the best-quality fish imaginable. Additional interest here is provided by the chef’s aunt, who has created the artisanal-style crockery, and the impressive machine used to make kakigori, a traditional Japanese ice cream. One dish that particularly impressed us was the mackerel escabeche, served in two small tacos with shichimi (a blend of seven Japanese spices) sprinkled on top.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
908;Monte;Spain;San Feliz;San Feliz, San Feliz, 33638, Spain;43.1685435;-5.8225128;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, whose main attributes are its typical authenticity and charm, will come as a pleasant surprise in this small Asturian village. Behind the attractive terrace at the entrance, popular with locals for a beer or aperitif, is a rustic-contemporary interior where everything has been designed to please guests. Chef Xune Andrade returned to his native area to showcase its natural bounty in his cooking, which is contemporary in style and based around two tasting menus (both with a wine- or cider-pairing option). His dishes are inspired by home cooking and show a heavy commitment to his local terroir. To back this up, and in line with his philosophy (“if you raise animals, sow crops or harvest produce, we want to work with you!), he has created a local network that sees him work with producers within a maximum 20km radius.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
909;Fishølogy;Spain;Barcelona;Diputació 73, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3809826;2.154461;54;true;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;One of Barcelona’s most original dining options, in a city full of restaurants that definitely leave their mark. Here, with chef Riccardo Radice in the kitchen and Giulia Gabriele running the dining room, the first thing that strikes you is the name, that also includes the Danish symbol “Ø” to indicate the number zero, and the suffix “Logy”, Greek in origin, in reference to a particular field of study, in this instance fish and seafood which are treated differently here (through salting, maturing, smoking etc) to create what they call “charcuterie of the sea”. The à la carte is complemented by two tasting menus that are named after different sea depths: Bentos (up to 200m below sea level, where light can still penetrate) and the so-called Abisal (the final frontier, in complete darkness, up to 6 000m in depth). The meticulously and aesthetically presented dishes here are prepared with Spanish ingredients, with the occasional nod to Italy and Asia.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
910;RavioXO;Spain;Madrid;Plaza de Manuel Gómez Moreno 5, Madrid, 28020, Spain;40.4479012;-3.69463;97;true;false;Creative, Dumplings;In the words of chef Dabiz Muñoz, RavioXO is “the luxury of eating time”, a perfect metaphor to express his informal, handcrafted cuisine, which is fully centred on the world of pasta, with all the dough, fillings and sauces made individually. In this extensive restaurant, located next to El Corte Inglés’ gourmet dining space on the Paseo de la Castellana, the stylish decor is inspired by Lázaro Rosa-Violán, providing the backdrop for chef Balo Ortiz, who follows the culinary guidelines set out by award-winning Madrid chef Dabiz Muñoz in every dish. The cuisine here, shared between the à la carte and a tasting menu, reflects fusion cuisine that covers almost all of Asia as a result of the chef’s travels and features sauces and exotic ingredients alike (yozu kosho, Korean tempura, spider crab from Singapore, umeboshi, Gochujang pasta etc) alongside those from closer to home. Standout dishes, which are designed for sharing, include dumplings, eggs with morcilla, and the legendary Hong Kong Madriz “cocido”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
911;Cobo Evolución;Spain;Burgos;Plaza de la Libertad 9, Burgos, 09004, Spain;42.3415093;-3.698853;65;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This gourmet outpost of chef Miguel Cobo shares some of its facilities with the Cobo Tradición restaurant, with both eateries part of the same modern, spacious and centrally located gastronomic space called Cobo Estratos. The famous Parque Arqueológico de Atapuerca, located a little more than 20km from Burgos, has provided the inspiration and leitmotiv for this celebrity chef on a single yet extensive tasting (Humanidad) menu with no little creativity. His cuisine takes the palate on an incredible journey through the different stages of human evolution and explores the relationship with our surroundings through culinary stops in Africa, Atapuerca, Altamira, the Neolithic period, ancient Rome etc. Interesting dishes include one that has been on the menu since the very beginning (natural oyster with olive hollandaise and cold escabeche with garum) and a truly delicious new dish called Sequences of Pigeon, featuring two different courses and incredible cooking techniques. After your meal, why not head upstairs to discover “Evolution” through art!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
913;ARREA!;Spain;Santa Cruz de Campezo;Subida al Frontón 46, Santa Cruz de Campezo, 01110, Spain;42.6692746;-2.3497835;36;false;false;Regional Cuisine;When you drive through small villages such as this one, what you least expect to find is a restaurant like ARREA!, where owner-chef Edorta Lamo takes guests on a fascinating cultural and gastronomic journey through the almost subsistence-like landscapes of the Montaña Alavesa region, albeit from a more contemporary perspective. Its three highly distinct dining spaces also come as a surprise, comprising the Taberna (the waiting area), the Kuadra (only offering the Mendialdea menu, featuring five market-inspired dishes and the traditional “putxero” stew), and the main dining room, with its homely rustic ambience, dedicated exclusively to the gastronomic menu. This magical menu comprises a fixed section entitled “ongietorri lunch” (pâtés, hams, preserves, rennet, tiny fried birds etc) which are explained individually, followed by what ARREA refers to as “passes” (you need to choose a minimum of three), based around different ways of preparing partridge, trout, ingredients from the orchard, pigeon, deer and wild boar. Different lichens, which are found in these mountain landscapes, also feature as an ingredient here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
914;Dama Juana;Spain;Jaén;Melchor Cobo Medina 7, Jaén, 23001, Spain;37.767224;-3.7854772;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;There are some local customs and skills that you pick up at home from your family and it is undoubtedly this link which connects chef Juan Aceituno and his grandmother Juana (La Chucha), the woman who passed on her passion for food to her grandson. Following a recent refurbishment that has brought greater levels of comfort, the restaurant now features a main dining room in a contemporary minimalist style, plus a semi-private annexe, from where it is possible to watch the kitchen team at work. The updated traditional cuisine here aims to narrate a journey through the chef’s own life experiences, exploring the landscapes of Jaén via his Alacena, Blancal and Umbría tasting menus, plus his special Gran Menú María. The latter, named after his daughter, is only available by pre-booking, is served by the chef himself in a private dining space, and is accompanied by its own wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
915;Kaleja;Spain;Malaga;Marquesa de Moya 9, Malaga, 29015, Spain;36.7211416;-4.417923;68;false;false;Contemporary;The name of this restaurant is particularly apt (Kaleja is the Sephardic word for “alley”) given its location in Málaga’s Jewish quarter, just a few steps from the city’s Picasso Museum. The first thing that will strike you as you walk through the door is the subtle aroma of smoke, a key feature that sets this restaurant apart. Here, chef Dani Carnero has gone for a modern take on dishes of old, working with the heat of his wood-fired grill to create what he calls “candle cooking” – a style of cuisine that revives tastes and flavours from his childhood, in many cases connected to traditional Andalucian recipes that have been brought back to life and are served on two tasting menus (Memoria and Gran Menú Memoria). One dish that particularly stood out was Kaleja’s take on gazpacho (in Málaga, where it is often made with onion, it is called “gazpacho de floja”), with trout roe and almonds.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
916;El Molino de Alcuneza;Spain;Sigüenza;Carretera GU 128, Sigüenza, 19250, Spain;41.1055995;-2.6044708;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is part of a delightful hotel situated some 6km from the medieval town of Sigüenza, where the owners have restored a 15C flour mill. Here, surrounded by stone, wood and myriad tasteful details, the brother and sister team of Samuel and Blanca Moreno create modern cuisine rooted in tradition which aims to highlight the splendid seasonal bounty of the mountains around Sigüenza, hence the focus on wild mushrooms, game and vegetables from the property’s own garden. In its attractive dining spaces, complemented by an enclosed glass-fronted terrace, guests can choose between several interesting tasting menus (Molienda, Clásicos and Esencia). The restaurant also boasts one of the best choices of homemade artisan bread in the whole of Spain, made with organic spelt and other varieties of cereals.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
917;Quimbaya;Spain;Madrid;Zurbano 63, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.436379;-3.6930752;40;true;false;Colombian;If you want to take your tastebuds on a culinary journey, Quimbaya provides the perfect opportunity, thanks to chef Edwin Rodríguez’s ability to recreate the flavours of his native Colombia, the birthplace of the movement known as Magic Realism. This restaurant, which takes its name from an indigenous native group famous for its gold craftsmanship, features a small bar displaying a superb array of Colombian spirits, and a minimalist dining room with an open-view kitchen where guests can partly interact with the chefs at work. The cuisine here is based around a single 10-course tasting menu called Memorias that, in the restaurant’s own words, takes you on “a journey back to our memories in order to remember flavours that feed the soul and revive stories of dishes that are a vivid expression of all things Colombian”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
918;Tabaiba;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Portugal 79, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35010, Spain;28.1353754;-15.4397592;83;true;true;Creative;Located just a few metres from Las Canteras beach and taking its name from a native flower, Tabaiba enjoys surprising its guests with what it describes as its “evolutionary Canary Island cuisine”. In this small contemporary space, chef Abraham Ortega (who, along with his team, is usually seen sporting his typical sombrero), offers guests his highly personal and entertaining cuisine that takes seemingly humble Canarian cooking to new heights thanks to his superb technique and seasonal ingredients sourced from each of the islands. He also adds touches of sentimentality, such as the tribute to his grandmother in the sequence entitled “Chickpeas-Egg Yolk-Pork Belly”. His cuisine is exclusively served on two tasting menus (Tabaiba and Experiencia), featuring elaborate dishes (we thoroughly enjoyed the “Vieja-Gazpachuelo-Vinegar”) whose aim is to pay dutiful homage to the very best local ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
920;Casa Marcelo;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Hortas 1, Santiago de Compostela, 15705, Spain;42.880834;-8.5466466;45;true;true;Fusion;Located just a few metres from the cathedral, Casa Marcelo is the reward for many pilgrims when they complete the legendary Camino de Santiago and is worthy recompense (some would even say it is a religious experience in itself!) for all their exertions. This cosmopolitan setting, in which the chefs interact with guests, features a large central table with a convivial ambience (a nod to the friendly spirit of the Galician people), a counter to one side, a kitchen that is part of the dining room and, to the rear, a pleasant terrace full of vegetation, where you’ll also find a bright and colourful glass-fronted dining room. All you need to do here is choose the number of dishes you wish to eat (four or eight) and allow chef Marcelo Tejedor to prepare a surprise tasting menu for you. His cuisine takes its inspiration from various sources, ranging from local to more international (China, Mexico, Peru etc) cuisine, to which he adds a personal touch. We recommend booking ahead as it is often full.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
921;Citrus del Tancat;Spain;Alcanar;CN-340 KM1059 - Sol de Riu, Alcanar, 43530, Spain;40.528796;0.5094532;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;If you happen to have at your disposal an estate with plenty of history, an attractive small hotel (Tancat de Codorniu) surrounded by landscaped grounds, over 2 000 fruit trees (mainly orange, hence the name Citrus) and a large organic vegetable garden, you have the cornerstones of a project that is steeped in the local region. Here, the gastronomic cuisine comes courtesy of young chef Aitor López, who flies the flag for Mediterranean cooking that is based around locally sourced ingredients from the Ràpita fish auction and the Ebro delta, with a constant nod to Catalan and Valencian recipes that result from the restaurant’s location straddling both regions. His delicate cooking, including dishes such as roasted onion with langoustine and fish suquet, is centred around three tasting menus: Lo Canar, Montsià, and Sol de Riu. At the entrance to the estate you’ll find a second restaurant called Els Jardins del Tancat offering more straightforward cuisine based around rice dishes and grilled fish.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
922;Abantal;Spain;Seville;Alcalde José de la Bandera 7, Seville, 41003, Spain;37.3878998;-5.9836581;88;false;true;Creative;This elegant restaurant, the name of which is the linguistic predecessor of the Spanish word for apron ("delantal"), is enthusiastically run by a chef who brings his full expertise, emotion and intrinsic personality to his cuisine.Head chef Julio Fernández oversees everything that goes on here with the clear objective of transferring traditional Andalucian flavours to a more cutting-edge culinary approach, while maintaining the authenticity of local ingredients and produce and their seasonality. In the renovated room, the decor of which is akin to that of a museum, choose between two tasting menus with different numbers of courses, but both offering a wine pairing option. For an even more intense dining experience, why not book the chef’s table in the kitchen?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
923;Sollo;Spain;Fuengirola;Avenida del Higuerón 48, Fuengirola, 29640, Spain;36.5809892;-4.5956774;62;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;In this stylish restaurant at the Reserva del Higuerón resort, you’ll find an open kitchen and superb views of the coast, which provide a delightful backdrop for innovative cuisine that is resolutely focused on aquaponic production as an alternative production system for the future, combining the rearing of freshwater fish in its R&D laboratory with the growing of vegetables in a symbiotic environment (90% of Sollo’s ingredients are home produced). Here, Diego Gallegos, the so-called “caviar chef”, creates a tasting menu (Caminho) with a sustainable focus, featuring modern, balanced dishes based around the Mediterranean and his own home-grown ingredients, along with an added South American touch (the chef is from Brazil and his mother from Peru) and a nod to organically produced Riofrío caviar. As part of his “Diego & Friends” project, the chef also organises an annual event that brings together renowned chefs to champion sustainable cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
924;Eirado;Spain;Pontevedra;Plaza da Leña 3, Pontevedra, 36002, Spain;42.4326366;-8.6434132;63;false;true;Contemporary;If you’re looking for a restaurant that exudes the true spirit of Pontevedra, then look no further, as Eirado occupies one of the most charming properties in the town’s old quarter. Its compact dining rooms are imbued with the warmth and beauty that come with the bare stone walls that typify the character of this particular restaurant. Chef Iñaki Bretal creates modern cooking with clearly evident Galician and maritime roots (he buys his fish and seafood daily from the auction in Ribeira), demonstrating high levels of technique and not being afraid to incorporate touches of fusion, taking flavours acquired on his travels (Mexico, Japan, Germany, Canada etc) and merging them with what he refers to as “the very best of the best ingredients”. In addition to a meticulous à la carte, he offers two interesting tasting menus (Currican and Palangre) that vary in their number of courses, as well as an extensive wine list, from which young sommelier Raquel Fernández (who is also in charge of the dining room) creates some surprising wine pairings.;;[]
925;Oba-;Spain;Casas-Ibáñez;Tomás Pérez Úbeda 6, Casas-Ibáñez, 02200, Spain;39.2873133;-1.4694894;100;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Oba- is much more than just a restaurant, given that chefs Javier Sanz and Juan Sahuquillo go far beyond the normal vision of a fine-dining experience through a philosophy that connects them fully with their surroundings. On their menus (Cuaderno Medio, Cuaderno Largo and Cuaderno Extra Largo), they invite guests on an incredible journey inspired by the roots of La Mancha’s cuisine, making full use of the premium meat and vegetables from the Cabriel valley and the La Manchuela area in truly unexpected ways. They do so by combining traditional and innovative techniques (they are especially keen on fermentation) and showcasing the region’s small-scale producers. Local breeds (Manchega Machorra sheep, Celtibérico goat), game, poultry, fish, crayfish and vegetables grown in the river valley all feature heavily on the menu here, with plenty of attention paid to service, including finishing touches to some dishes at the table to encourage interaction with guests. Two pairings are also available, one with wine, the other featuring a choice of naturally produced drinks.;Air conditioning;[]
926;Casa Gerardo;Spain;Prendes;Carretera AS 19 Km 9, Prendes, 33438, Spain;43.53658;-5.7872;80;true;true;Modern Cuisine;When the word “prestigious” is mentioned, thoughts immediately turn to restaurants such as this one, which first opened in 1882 and has been run by five generations of the same family and continues to showcase authentic Asturian cuisine. Chef Marcos Morán now holds the reins here, in tandem with his father Pedro, with whom he has achieved a perfect symbiosis that is reflected in the balance between innovation and tradition. Choose between the modern-influenced à la carte, which includes a section dedicated to time-honoured recipes, and appetising tasting menus (Clásicos, Degustación 1882 and Geles, each with a wine-pairing option) featuring mains such as the unmissable Fabada de Prendes bean stew, the delicious Pitu de Caleya (a local chicken stew), Asturian tripe etc, and the rice dessert, “crema de arroz con leche requemada”. Marcos Morán’s strong connection to this area has not stopped him expanding further afield, as he now also manages Spanish-inspired restaurants in London, Brussels and, more recently, Nha Trang in Vietnam.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
927;Ceibe;Spain;Ourense;San Miguel 8, Ourense, 32005, Spain;42.3377294;-7.8637958;35;false;true;Galician, Creative;If you’re searching for the essence of Galician cuisine, make sure you book a table at “Ceibe”, an adjective that describes someone “who is able to choose and manage the way they act and think”. The escabeches and pickled and marinaded dishes on offer here are the signature of this restaurant close to the cathedral, in which the striking and traditional stone walls combine with a minimalist look and a kitchen that is very much part of the dining room. Here, Lydia del Olmo and Xosé Magalhaes are keen to ensure that that guests are able to see everything that happens, as part of an interesting culinary journey across Galicia that includes flavoursome main dishes and desserts that Lydia has “borrowed” from her grandmother. The two tasting menus (Enxebre and Esmorga) have close ties with the local terroir and both start with a traditional “queimada” – a typical Galician drink.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
928;La Salita;Spain;Valencia;Pere III El Gran 11, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.4623668;-0.3696366;19;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;A superb example of how perseverance, effort and solid values in the face of fresh challenges helps you to grow professionally. This restaurant, occupying an impressive mansion in the city’s Ruzafa district that has been decorated with plenty of charm and personality, stands out for its different dining options. In addition to the main dining room upstairs, it also boasts a pretty garden, two attractive tables in front of the kitchen and a particularly pleasant terrace where guests can enjoy aperitifs, a meal or a relaxing post-dinner drink. Chef Begoña Rodrigo showcases her talents on several tasting menus (Sangoreneta, Llauro Sangoreneta, Novençà, El Llauro), several of which are vegetarian, and which demonstrate her characteristic feminine touch and elegance, in particular the way she elevates the cooking of vegetables to new heights. Don’t leave without tasting La Tiara, one of her signature dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
929;La Casa de Manolo Franco;Spain;Valdemorillo;La Fuente 6, Valdemorillo, 28210, Spain;40.5009997;-4.0679548;46;true;false;Contemporary;The eponymous owner-chef, who amazed everyone by leaving the world of Formula 1 racing (in which he worked as a journalist) to return to his roots and take over the former family bar, demonstrates ambition, excellent technique and a strong desire to surprise. In this attractive restaurant, with its playful mix of the rustic and modern, Manu Franco focuses on the flavours of the Sierra de Guadarrama mountains, locally sourced meat, aromatic plants (such as thyme and lavender) and vegetables, all of which are showcased on a menu (available Wednesday to Friday lunchtimes and for dinner on Fridays and Saturdays) that changes with the seasons (Pequeño Otoño in autumn, Pequeño Invierno in winter etc) and another more extensive (and contemporary focused) tasting menu with a choice of long and short formats: Cerrar los Ojos (Close Your Eyes) and Cerrar los Ojos XL (Close Your Eyes) XL). One dish that we enjoyed in particular was the delicious ‘fighting bull beef with rice and oak smoke”.;Air conditioning;[]
931;Garena;Spain;Dima;Barrio Iturriotz 11, Dima, 48141, Spain;43.1295799;-2.7659276;88;true;false;Contemporary;If you’re on the lookout for a unique dining experience, head to this delightful 17C “baserri” (traditional country house) surrounded by vineyards and boasting impressive views. It also features the unusual ancestral custom of burning laurel branches to ward off evil spirits before each sitting. Garena boasts a bar area and terrace, a main dining room on the first floor, and a private space (usually reserved for groups) on the floor above. Chef Julen Baz showcases modern Basque cuisine with a firm focus on tradition and locally sourced ingredients and a penchant for grilled dishes. The cooking here is centred around two menus: Gurea, and another more extensive offering called Garena, through which he explains the subsistence cooking specific to Basque farmhouses and a gastronomic journey across 500 years of history, albeit from a more contemporary culinary perspective. As part of the experience, learn about native cattle breeds from the Mugarrieta cattle farm, basic preserving methods, and enjoy chilled ciders that are the perfect pairing for the desserts here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
932;La Finca;Spain;Loja;Carretera Salinas-Villanueva de Tapia (A-333), Loja, 18300, Spain;37.1638978;-4.2922482;42;false;true;Contemporary;One of those culinary jewels that could easily be overlooked, given that is just one of the gourmet options on offer at the luxury Royal Hideaway La Bobadilla hotel, a delightful property styled on a typical Andalucian-style farm estate, in the heart of the countryside in the province of Granada. The experience here (based around two highly creative surprise tasting menus entitled Cercanía and Lindes), starts in the spectacular old chapel (note the surprising sight of one of the world’s largest organs with over 1 600 pipes) where you’ll enjoy mini-stew starters teeming with flavour. It then moves on to the restaurant’s rustic-elegant dining room to savour dishes inspired by the culinary traditions of Granada and Málaga. These have been brought right up to date through the technical mastery of young chef Fernando Arjona, who trained under Pablo González at Cabaña Buenavista in Murcia but who now demonstrates his own personality at La Finca. One dish that we particularly enjoyed and left its mark was the grouper with a “Rondeña” jus and fennel soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
933;Ca l'Enric;Spain;La Vall de Bianya;Carretera Camprodón N 260, La Vall de Bianya, 17813, Spain;42.2217505;2.4401289;35;true;true;Creative;The Juncà siblings (with Jordi and Isabel in the kitchen and Joan in the role of sommelier and front of house manager) subtly focus on the history of the property and its personality, while continuing to extol the virtues of the wooded landscapes of the Vall de Bianya and its native ingredients.The hostal that first stood here in the late 19C has given way to this superb gastronomic restaurant with a contemporary look and interesting contrasts between modern design and the materials that connect us with our surroundings (stone, wood, leather etc). The à la carte and set menus (Memories in Evolution and Discovering the Valley) open the door to creative cuisine that embraces traditional Catalan cuisine while at the same time showcasing seasonal native ingredients. The attractive wine cellar occupies what was once a rainwater tank!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
934;Hospedería El Batán;Spain;Tramacastilla;Carretera A 1512, Tramacastilla, 44112, Spain;40.42797;-1.5602059;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This unique restaurant, in the heart of the Sierra de Albarracín mountains, occupies what was once a wool factory, hence its name (“fulling mill” in English) and its location on the banks of the Guadalaviar. The charm of the building is evident, thanks to the preservation of its original structure, and its quiet natural setting with its plethora of waterfalls. In the elegant dining room, furnished in the rustic style of the region with seating for just 18 guests (adding to its exclusive feel) and relaxing views of the countryside from most of its tables, enjoy delicious dishes prepared by María José Meda, a self-taught cook who has stepped away from the typical cuisine usually found in this area. From the appetisers onwards, her consistent, contemporary cooking with a creative touch showcases the natural bounty of Teruel province and the woods around the property (her Tierra tasting menu focuses on truffles, trout, and ingredients sourced from local vegetable gardens and meadows etc). A number of attractive guestrooms, plus a simpler restaurant called Alba del Sur, are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
935;L'Antic Molí;Spain;Ulldecona;Carretera Ulldecona - La Sénia KM 10, Ulldecona, 43550, Spain;40.611132;0.3306029;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;If you’ve never tried galera shrimp, you can do so here, as L’Antic Molí has brought it back into fashion on its exclusive menu dedicated to this Mediterranean shellfish (February and March only).This now-modernised former flour mill is firmly committed to zero-mile ingredients as chef Vicent Guimerà is a strong advocate of the Slow Food movement and to only using ingredients of local provenance. In this setting, equidistant between the sea and the mountains, his gastronomic restaurant offers a tasting menu called Mans (“hands”) that champions local ingredients, the circular economy, sustainability and ecology. His other bistro-style dining space offers a daily set menu. Well worth a visit!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
936;Ugo Chan;Spain;Madrid;Félix Boix 6, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.4633289;-3.6881793;41;true;false;Fusion;A contemporary restaurant with an open-view kitchen, two counters and a Japanese ambience that is far from lacking in personality. Its meticulous, constantly evolving cuisine could be described by quoting the Greek philosopher Heracles: “No man ever steps in the same river twice”. In his restaurant, which shares the nickname given to him by his grandfather when he was a boy (“Hugochan”, or “little Hugo”), chef Hugo Muñoz conjures up Japanese cuisine (on an à la carte and a personalised Omakase menu) in which seasonal ingredients take centre stage, incorporating enjoyable influences from other cultures and with a nod to iconic Madrid dishes (such as the tripe gyozas “a la madrileña” and his version of “Soldaditos de Pavía”) and other legendary chefs (Martín Berasategui, Joël Robuchon etc). One dish that we particularly enjoyed was the highly memorable caviar lentil Japanese curry with smoked breast of wood pigeon and coconut.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
937;Zaranda;Spain;Palma;Bala Roja 1, Palma, 07001, Spain;39.5655872;2.655429;43;false;true;Creative;Fernando Pérez Arellano’s legendary Zaranda restaurant continues to delight the senses in the city’s old quarter, within the walls of the Es Princep luxury hotel, but with a separate entrance.It stands above the remains of a former tannery, a connection recognised in the names of some of its appetisers. The enticing tasting menus (Hipodermis, Dermis and Epidermis) include highly unusual appetisers and pickles. These either have an Arab influence or a connection with the history of the leather tanning basins which are partially visible to guests through the glass floor. Thanks to Zaranda’s combination of meticulous presentation, delicate textures, the very best ingredients from the island, and astute food and wine pairings, you won’t be disappointed!;Air conditioning;[]
938;Quatre Molins;Spain;Cornudella de Montsant;Comte de Rius 8, Cornudella de Montsant, 43360, Spain;41.2645582;0.904766;17;true;true;Creative;Given his unique nickname, it would be a surprise not to have heard of Rafel Muria, the so-called “honey chef”, for whom this natural product is much more than a fad, given that his family have been involved in beekeeping since 1810 through their company artMuria. In this simple restaurant, this chef who trained in renowned restaurants in Spain, France and Italy focuses on creative cuisine of a high level which he showcases via elaborate dishes involving the discreet use of honey to add balance and stability. He offers a choice of two tasting menus (Espectáculo and Gran Espectáculo), as well as three stand-alone dishes that are representative of his cuisine and can be ordered as an extra: his famous tuna roe royale with pear compote, crayfish ravioli with a foie gras sauce and black truffle, and, for dessert, the “Coulant” with vanilla ice-cream (a Michel Bras recipe dating back to 1981). The excellent wine list focuses on estates from the Montsant and Priorat areas.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
939;Chirón;Spain;Valdemoro;Alarcón 27, Valdemoro, 28341, Spain;40.191578;-3.6764858;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;We’re not just paying lip service when we say that Chirón is one of the best places to eat on the outskirts of Madrid, just 25km from the Spanish capital.Here, chef Iván Muñoz, working alongside his sommelier brother Raúl, showcases the cooking of the Madrid region from a more modern and creative perspective, while at the same time paying homage to its traditional roots. Choose between highly enticing set menus with a touch of influence from La Mancha, which take us on a journey along the banks of the Tajo, Jarama and Tajuña rivers. The chef’s enthusiasm for the area and its local produce does not in any way prevent him from reinterpreting ingredients from elsewhere, an attribute which saw him win the International Red Prawn Competition in Dénia in 2020.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
940;Casa Arcas;Spain;Villanova;Carretera A-139, Villanova, 22467, Spain;42.5517197;0.4648088;47;true;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, occupying a small rural hotel in the Benasque valley, not far from the downhill ski slopes of Aramón-Cerler, is nestled is a truly enchanting natural setting. The couple in charge, Ainhoa Lozano and David Beltrán (the latter known as Tauste), show consummate professionalism and enthusiasm gained through working with master chef Martín Berasategui. The dining room, with its open fireplace and fine views, is the perfect setting in which to savour intensely flavoured creative cuisine. The superb menus here, all of which offer really impressive value for money, take guests on a mouthwatering journey through the mountains: choose between a cheaper 5-course option (Paseo SL-5), exclusively available to guests staying here, and two more extensive 7- and 10- course options (Sendero PR-7 and Gran Recorrido GR-10). Every dish is delicious although we particularly loved the Carabinero prawns with fennel and the medallion of black monkfish with textured asparagus and sea urchin.;Car park,Great view;[]
941;Saddle;Spain;Madrid;Amador de los Ríos 6, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4274475;-3.6911998;58;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The name of this restaurant located opposite the Ministry for the Interior is an equestrian nod to the legendary Jockey, a famous name in the history of Madrid gastronomy, that once occupied the premises.In essence, and despite the more modern look, Saddle replicates the philosophy and excellence of luxury restaurants from days gone by, hence the impeccable service and levels of comfort which enhance superb contemporary cuisine that is built around classic recipes. The overall ambience is one of space, light and elegance, and includes several private rooms plus an inner garden. The classic-contemporary menu (with media ración options) is complemented by a tasting menu. The constant movement of trolleys (bread, butter, cheese, spirits etc) adds a further special touch!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
942;José Carlos García;Spain;Malaga;Plaza de la Capilla, Malaga, 29016, Spain;36.71685;-4.4130483;63;false;false;Creative, Andalusian;This restaurant, overlooking the luxury yachts in the Muelle Uno dock, stands out for its contemporary dining space that is both elegant and informal. Here, cutting-edge trends and industrial design combine with exquisite vertical gardens and a chillout zone in a space that still remains completely in tune with the style and bright feel of the Mediterranean. Chef José Carlos García, a native of this delightful city, does not offer an à la carte option, instead focusing exclusively on two extensive tasting menus (one features three more courses than the other) that are constantly evolving. Demonstrating impressive technical skill, they feature dishes that champion locally sourced ingredients (around 70%) and showcase time-honoured “malagueño” flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
943;A'Barra;Spain;Madrid;Del Pinar 15, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.438683;-3.687633;76;true;true;International;A restaurant in which the Joselito brand of hams and the top-quality La Catedral de Navarra tinned and canned vegetables take centre stage. To a backdrop of a profusion of fine wood, a spacious layout and cutting-edge design, guests can choose between the elegant dining room, spacious private rooms and the exclusive Sergio Manzano chef’s table. “Without ingredients, there’s no cooking”, so here the focus is on guests experimenting with multiple taste sensations on the tasting menu and à la carte (on which “media ración” options are also available). Signature dishes here include the Huevo de Mos, with strips of Joselito bellota ham and smoked eel, and the toasted leeks served with an emulsion, Caspian Pearl caviar and textured egg yolk. Let A'Barra’s superb sommelier Valerio Carrera guide you in your pairing from the extensive wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
945;Casas Colgadas Restaurante;Spain;Cuenca;Canónigos, Cuenca, 16001, Spain;40.077857;-2.1283593;86;true;false;Contemporary;The experience of eating in one of the city’s iconic “hanging houses” is one not to be missed and this is certainly the case in this restaurant next to the striking Museo de Arte Abstracto Español, where entry is controlled by a code that you are sent when making a booking. In its meticulous contemporary-style interior, which has nevertheless retained its delightfully attractive original wooden beams, guests can enjoy unique views of the Huécar river gorge while savouring the concise Volver or Cocinamos Cuenca tasting menus, the latter offerings courses such as trout, radish, sardines, cheese, wine, walnuts, hare, Judía de la Virgen white beans, the delicious pigeon, and beetroot. Chef Jesús Segura has developed his repertoire around locally sourced ingredients while revising culinary traditions from a thoroughly modern and highly personal perspective: “my passion is translating the ancestral legacy of our grandparents as well as their exhaustive knowledge about wild herbs from the area, so that this expertise is not lost”.;Air conditioning;[]
946;Nublo;Spain;Haro;Plaza de San Martín 5, Haro, 26200, Spain;42.5777859;-2.8465048;82;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Occupying a 16C aristocratic property, Nublo is much more than just a restaurant. In fact, it has brought the gastronomic spotlight back to a town famous as the location for the largest concentration of century-old wine cellars in the world! Following an extensive interior design makeover, the restaurant has opted not to hide the scars of age, instead retaining spaces and dining rooms with lots of personality, such as the internal patio where you can see the goddess Nublo (at night, her transparent image is transposed onto a large “holy veil”). Here, chef Miguel Caño, who once worked at the famous Mugaritz run by Andoni Luis Aduriz, showcases his cooking on a tasting menu (an “executive”-style menu is also available on weekdays except Friday evening) that starts with the following maxim: “create pure flavours, showcase wood-fired cuisine and embark on a culinary journey through La Rioja, with a nod to its culture, its native ingredients and its landscapes, in order to offer cutting-edge cooking based on tradition”. The end result is perfect, especially over a candlelit supper.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
947;Poemas by Hermanos Padrón;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;León y Castillo 227, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35005, Spain;28.1211968;-15.4272769;28;false;false;Creative;A dazzling dining experience both in terms of the elegant setting and the gastronomic cuisine on offer in the exclusive and historic Santa Catalina hotel, a Royal Hideaway Hotel, in the heart of Las Palmas de Gran Canaria. At the helm you’ll find chef Adrián García, from nearby Arucas, who has been superbly trained by the Padrón brothers (Juan Carlos and Jonathan) and who recreates the flavoursome cuisine of these award-winning chefs along with all of their renowned creativity. This dining space, which has its own separate entrance next to the hotel piano-bar (where a pianist provides the musical backdrop), boasts a refined and classical interior design with a profusion of wood that comes as a pleasant surprise. The Poemas tasting menu (on which we particularly enjoyed the impressively presented prawns with a prawn head toffee and shiitake mushrooms) is complemented by the more concise Clásicos menu, however both menus feature some of the Padrón brothers’ signature dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
948;La Era de los Nogales;Spain;Sardas;Baja 2, Sardas, 22613, Spain;42.5067596;-0.3377657;43;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in a tiny village in the Alto Gállego region of Huesca province where its glass marquee-style design amid typical stone buildings comes as something of a surprise with the stunning backdrop of the Aragonese Pyrenees and its magical sunsets as a bonus! Here, chef Toño Rodríguez conjures up contemporary yet traditionally based cuisine that impresses with its high quality and flavour and a focus on local, seasonal ingredients with a nod to the classic dishes of the region (the appetisers, which are eaten while standing, are a tribute to the three provinces of Aragón) as well as those from his childhood. Three tasting menus (E-volución, R-ecuerdos and A-mbición) take centre stage and are complemented by a restricted à la carte available for dinner during the summer months (June to September). An array of fun desserts (such as the Pan de Sayón with Ecostean olive oil and chocolate), provide the finishing touch!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
949;Kokotxa;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Kanpandegi 11, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20003, Spain;43.3236003;-1.9870824;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the old town, between the port and the Santa María del Coro basilica, this restaurant bears a name that pays homage to one of the finest dishes in Basque cuisine, prepared with the delicious barbels of either hake or cod. In this pleasant eatery, run by the duo of Daniel López in the kitchen and Estela Velasco front of house, you’ll enjoy contemporary cuisine inspired by strong Basque traditions and the use of the very best market ingredients which are meticulously and masterfully prepared. The chef here likes to introduce influences from other cultures (Japan, India, Turkey etc), but always with a subtle approach that adds personality and brings pleasure to the palate. His cuisine is based around two menus (De Mercado and Degustación), both served for the whole table, and which vary in the number of courses. The fish dish of the day is always spectacular, although we also loved one of his meat dishes – Bresse chicken with pak choi, hazelnuts and PX sherry.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
950;COME by Paco Méndez;Spain;Barcelona;Avenida del Mistral 54, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3760837;2.1540201;59;true;true;Mexican, Fusion;If you were once a regular visitor to the legendary Hoja Santa, you won’t want to miss out on a visit to COME by Paco Méndez, which now occupies the same premises (also home to the former Niño Viejo restaurant) and which, in a nod to the attachment Mexicans have with the Day of the Dead, could be described as a “reborn restaurant”. At the helm here is chef Paco Méndez, who has taken over the reins with his wife and head pastry chef Erinna to give the format a new twist in which he showcases “the coming together of Mexican culture and cooking, Mediterranean ingredients and the legacy of El Bulli”. The experience starts with welcome drinks and snacks as soon as you walk through the door before heading to the dining room and private dining space (show cooking is also an option here) where you can discover the flavours of this Central American country from a modern and creative perspective on the menu COME Festival, with a permanent focus on zero-mile ingredients. The extensive selection of typical Mexican drinks (micheladas, tequilas, mezcales etc) is a must here.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
951;Els Tinars;Spain;Llagostera;Carretera de Sant Feliu de Guíxols, Llagostera, 17240, Spain;41.8274496;2.9533814;32;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant has played an important role in the history of Costa Brava tourism. It occupies an old yet attractively restored farmhouse with a luxuriant garden-terrace for the summer months, an R&D space where new dishes are created, plus a bright, Mediterranean-inspired interior. Chef Marc Gascons and his sister Elena (front of house) are responsible for the entire experience here, which revolves around an extensive and up-to-date à la carte of traditional Catalan cuisine and the best local ingredients sourced from nearby producers and the superb fish auction in Palamós. Two interesting set menus (one short, seasonal option, plus a tasting menu) are also available. One of the most requested dishes here is the tartare of Palamós prawns, which comes with different garnishes depending on the season. Guests who drive here are given a code for the external car park, which now has charging points for electric vehicles.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
952;Ricardo Temiño;Spain;Burgos;San Juan 3, Burgos, 09003, Spain;42.3432013;-3.7002022;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;If you’re keen to explore the more personal side of chef Ricardo Temiño’s cooking, this offshoot of the La Fábrica restaurant, but with the same entrance, is a space with its own individual character where the aim is to explore the rich culinary culture of Burgos in more depth. The experience begins with appetisers in front of the reception area, where you’ll find the extensive wine cellar, before heading into the kitchen (accompanied by the chef) to see how they age lamb, before moving on to the modern dining room with its semi-open kitchen. Here, the more concept-based, market-inspired cooking is showcased on a single tasting menu called Camino, inspired by the chef and his family’s life journey (there are references to his honeymoon, his grandmother, the early days of the La Fábrica restaurant etc), as well to as the extensive research he has carried out into different aspects of the province’s history (wool, fish, El Cid, the Camino de Santiago etc). An address that is well worth getting to know!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
953;Muxgo;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;León y Castillo 227, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35005, Spain;28.1219882;-15.4279542;16;false;false;Creative;Muxgo is part of the luxury Santa Catalina Royal Hideaway hotel, where the cooking is an ode to sustainable and organic cuisine. In its bright dining room, decorated with watercolours by artist Ana Beltrán and a mural that reflects some of chef Borja Marrero’s favourite ingredients, the latter conjures up creative and contemporary dishes that are always based around ingredients rooted in the DNA of the Canary Islands and, first and foremost, those grown on his own farm (pine bark, millet, prickly pear, meal from his own cattle etc). Dining options are centred around three tasting menus (Los Orígenes, Lo más profundo de Tejeda, and an “executive” menu, the latter, entitled “Sin olvidar el territorio” is only served at lunchtime midweek) featuring dishes that as elegant as they are delicious, such as the superb Mogán shrimp macerated in toasted almond oil. For an even more authentic experience you can also visit the restaurant’s farm in Tejeda but you’ll need to book this well in advance.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
954;Código de Barra;Spain;Cadiz;San Francisco 7, Cadiz, 11004, Spain;36.5338733;-6.2954065;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This gastronomic oasis, located along a busy pedestrianised street in the historic quarter of Cádiz, will definitely leave its mark thanks to its contemporary take on some of the more hidden aspects of the city’s cuisine over its 3 000-year history. The decorative combination of stone, brick and whitewashed walls that also extends to the small tables by the kitchen induces a sense of calm that provides the perfect habitat for chef Léon Griffioen (originally from the Netherlands) and his wife Paqui Márquez (sommelier and front of house) to showcase their skills. The cuisine is centred around two exclusive tasting menus (Qadis and Gadeira) which provide an insight into the flavours of Cádiz’s cuisine from a contemporary perspective, revealing specific aspects of its history through the region’s very best ingredients. Examples include the elegant “Candié” eggnog with prawns, the tomato escabeche with red shrimp, the “navazo”-grown vegetables from kitchen gardens by the coast, the estuary sea bream, the corvina fish “en adobo” etc.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
955;Alquimia - Laboratorio;Spain;Valladolid;Antigua 6, Valladolid, 47002, Spain;41.6538741;-4.7224762;20;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;An interesting gourmet option in the centre of the city, located at the foot of the emblematic Santa María de La Antigua church, one of the indisputable icons of Valladolid architecture.The restaurant, preceded by a terrace that is almost always full of university students, features a contemporary yet informal gastro-bar (Crisol) where you can order the daily menu as well as fun dishes designed for sharing. The restaurant’s so-called gastronomic space, with its open-view kitchen and decorative details inspired by the molecular cuisine that has lent the restaurant the second half of its name, is the domain of Alvar Hinojal. His culinary skill shines forth on three bold and creative tasting menus (Noradrenalina, Serotonina and Dopamina) on which every mouthful is full of delicious surprises.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
956;Kaido Sushi Bar;Spain;Valencia;Chile 3, Valencia, 46021, Spain;39.470454;-0.3575637;37;false;false;Japanese;A contemporary Japanese restaurant which despite its compact size, has plenty of personality. It only has space for ten guests who have to arrive in unison, then sit together around the bar to appreciate the gastronomic experience to the full, including the explanations and studied movements of renowned sushi chef Yoshikazu Yanome.His philosophy is built around the Edomae Sushi tradition (established during the Edo period from 1603-1868) of preparing the (at the time abundant) fresh fish and seafood caught daily in the waters of Tokyo bay. The same idea permeates the cuisine here, which nowadays is based around the superb natural bounty of Valencia’s coastal waters, with a special focus on the red prawn. Nigiris feature heavily on the menu here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
957;Tohqa;Spain;El Puerto de Santa María;de los Moros 4, El Puerto de Santa María, 11500, Spain;36.593785;-6.22757;30;false;false;Contemporary;A property with lots of history (it was formally a convent, then a bar) which is now popular as a restaurant (it occupies the premises of the erstwhile El Arriete). The space has a new look and its own personality, featuring a rustic-contemporary ambience, including a particularly pleasant internal patio. Eduardo and Juan José Pérez, the two brothers who run Tohqa (Eduardo is in charge of the kitchen, while Juan is the sommelier and runs the dining room) are passionate about Andalucía’s grilled dishes (Eduardo calls himself the “fire chef”), with a permanent focus on locally sourced ingredients (eel, tuna, prawns, cuttlefish etc) although some produce comes from the family farm run by his father in El Saucejo (in the province of Seville). On his menus (Anafe and Tohqa), Eduardo uses words such as seed, fire, salt and path to explain the restaurant’s true essence, what it wants to represent, its surroundings, and the people who have helped it reflect the true meaning of this region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
958;Gaytán;Spain;Madrid;Príncipe de Vergara 205, Madrid, 28002, Spain;40.4493113;-3.6783632;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The dream of chef Javier Aranda which then became a reality, Gaytán is far from your usual type of restaurant.This space impresses as soon you walk through the door thanks to the designer-inspired interior featuring the original wood columns that flank the large open kitchen overlooking the dining room, so that guests feel as though they are part of the creative process. The cuisine, complemented by a small menu for business customers during the week, aims to showcase what they describe here as the joys of the seasons, something they succeed in doing via the Inaurem menu (which is the Latin word for jewel or precious object) and especially the more extensive Javier Aranda menu, the latter revealing to guests the techniques and stages involved in creating each dish.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
959;Fogony;Spain;Sort;Avenida Generalitat 45, Sort, 25560, Spain;42.4159399;1.1320159;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the small town of Sort, famous for having the lottery shop with the biggest online sales in Spain (La Bruixa d’Or), the reputation of this family-run, one-Michelin-star restaurant has nothing whatsoever to do with luck!Its name refers to the effect of the cold and wet wind that blows through the Catalan Pyrenees but which turns warm and dry when it reaches the Pallars Sobirà area. With his zero-miles approach, chef Zaraida Cotonat, who nowadays works hand in hand with his son, offers menus with a focus on creative cuisine that combines tradition, modernity and sustainability, and always uses ingredients of local provenance (chicken from Torre d’Erbull, trout from Tavascán, Bruneta veal from the Pyrenees, lamb from the Xisqueta breed of sheep).;Air conditioning;[]
960;Nintai;Spain;Marbella;Ramón Gómez de la Serna 18, Marbella, 29602, Spain;36.5097674;-4.8997997;78;true;false;Japanese;Another culinary project courtesy of renowned sommelier Marcos Granda, who returned from Japan at the end of 2019 astonished by its culture and the country’s respect for the finest ingredients – a revelation which led to the development of this new project. Nintai features a design based around pure lines, large windows, several private dining spaces and a large sushi bar with 12 seats, where guests can watch him work, create and improvise his “itamae” style of cooking (which literally translates as “in front of the chopping board”). Here, everything induces a feeling of serenity – the perfect state of mind in which to savour the single ENSō tasting menu (two courses we particularly enjoyed were the Mushimono, showcasing the skill of steaming, and Otsukuri, based around raw textures) where the ingredients used are dependent on the seasons and market availability. Other highlights include the large cuts of tuna that are sliced in front of guests. Given that this is a Japanese restaurant, the desserts come as something of a surprise, plus Nintai also offers one of the best sake menus in Spain.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
962;La Finca;Spain;Elche;Partida de Perleta 1-7, Elche, 03295, Spain;38.2558416;-0.6492128;91;false;false;Creative;Chef Susi Díaz continues to reinvent herself, with the constant support of her husband and her children, as she continues her quest for home-inspired cooking that is teeming with personality, elegance, technique and, above all, passion. At La Finca, a restaurant with lots of charm in a rural setting, where the decor is urban-contemporary in style, traditional Alicante recipes evolve continually, thanks to a chef who recreates the flavours from this region with an added innovative twist. Her cuisine is full of deeply rooted influences and memories, taking full advantage of local ingredients, especially fish and seafood, to create visual surprises for guests, while incorporating aromatic herbs and organic flowers from her kitchen garden as a final touch. Order from the à la carte, create your own menu, or opt for the Origen tasting menu which comes in two formats (L and XL). There is a strong commitment to organic ingredients here, hence its support for the #PorElClima (For the Climate) community.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
963;La Bicicleta;Spain;Hoznayo;La Plaza 12, Hoznayo, 39716, Spain;43.390118;-3.701983;44;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The name of this restaurant occupying a large 18C house is deliberate as it reflects the professional relationship that chef Eduardo Quintana once had with cycling. This is highlighted by the saying by Albert Einstein at the entrance (“Life is like riding a bicycle – to keep your balance, you need to keep moving”) which influences his general attitude to life. It boasts a pleasant patio-terrace, where guests can savour appetisers, plus an attractive rustic-retro decor inside. The cuisine is centred on two tasting menus (La Vuelta en Bicicleta and La Escapada) featuring modern dishes that reinterpret Basque and Cantabrian traditions with a large dose of creativity, the use of select ingredients from the family’s own vegetable garden, plus influences from further afield. For an even more comprehensive experience before you eat, why not visit the garden which is just 1km away (it’s not a bad idea to take another pair of shoes just in case!).;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
964;Chispa Bistró;Spain;Madrid;Barquillo 8, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4202857;-3.6956288;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with an industrial vibe in the heart of the city’s Chueca district, featuring an open-view kitchen impressively and enthusiastically run by Juan D'Onofrio, a young Argentinian-born chef who is very happy with his life in Madrid, especially as it is said that “this is the city where everyone, including chefs, find their rightful place”! The aim of the contemporary cuisine here is to showcase the full nuances of the Mediterranean, to which the chef adds interesting Argentinian influences, with a strong focus on fire and the grill, and the use of aged fish and meat in which every flavour is emphasised. Dishes that made a particularly strong impression included the highly original shrimp, banana and Palo Cortado sherry starter, and the pigeon served as three different dishes that make full use of every part of the bird. A small adjoining, and more intimate, annexe (La Trasera de Chispa Bistró) provides another dining option here.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
965;Árbore da Veira;Spain;A Coruña;Parque Monte San Pedro, A Coruña, 15011, Spain;43.377457;-8.433224;85;true;true;Creative;Located closed to the emblematic artillery batteries that once protected the estuary, this restaurant on top of Monte de San Pedro will delight guests with its panoramic setting, with tables in the dining room offering views of both the city and the expanse of the ocean. It boasts several rooms for private events, lots of light, large bare tables, innovative tableware, and surprising culinary combinations, including impeccable cream sauces. In his own words, the cuisine of chef Luis Veira, a proud native of the city, “focuses the five senses firmly on the Atlantic”. This is reflected in a constant play of flavours and ingredients (he particularly enjoys combining those from the sea and mountains) that he showcases in an updated take on traditional cuisine on his à la carte and three enticing tasting menus: Semente, Raíces and Árbore. A fun option that particularly attracted our attention was “the cherry that fell from the tree”, an attractive dish comprising basil, foie gras and cherry gelatine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
966;Ricardo Sanz Wellington;Spain;Madrid;Velázquez 6, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4219171;-3.6843864;50;true;false;Japanese;In this elegant restaurant, located inside the luxury Hotel Wellington and overseen by award-winning chef Ricardo Sanz, savour spectacular nigiri prepared with rice from the Ebro delta, carabinero prawn usuzukuri with a salsa made from its own coral, and tuna tataki with vitello tonnato, alongside signature dishes such as “huevos rotos”, in which the eggs are accompanied by fingers of Canary Island potatoes and bluefin tuna instead of the usual ham. The chef has developed a legendary reputation by being the first to move away from the hallowed turf of Spanish cuisine to introduce a concept that combined Japanese and Mediterranean cooking, in so doing opening the door to influences from elsewhere (Mexico, Korea etc) but where the very best Iberian ingredients still provide the backbone. Allow yourself to be guided in your pairings (wine, sake, tea or beer) by the sommelier, and whatever you do, don’t pass up the chance to savour the delicate mochis to round off your dining experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
967;Choco;Spain;Córdoba;Compositor Serrano Lucena 14, Córdoba, 14010, Spain;37.8850096;-4.7623009;57;false;false;Creative, Andalusian;A delightful restaurant featuring an elegantly minimalist dining space, but one which has not lost its inherent, time-honoured authenticity.Here, chef Kisko García decided to create a connection with the barrio in which grew up, hence his creative cuisine (showcased on two tasting menus - Barrio Antiguo and Kisko García) that brings into the limelight the delightful flavours and aromas of the Valle de Los Pedroches and Villanueva de Córdoba – the Andalucía that had such a positive influence on his childhood. Locally sourced seasonal ingredients (organic wherever possible), fine flavours, teamwork and a positive attitude are all part of a delightful experience, which starts at the entrance, continues with an aperitif in the kitchen, and ends at your table in the dining room. A wine pairing option is also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
968;Ikaro;Spain;Logrono;Avenida de Portugal 3, Logrono, 26001, Spain;42.4643127;-2.4482165;17;true;true;Creative;Behind Ikaro’s façade, you’ll find a strong work ethic, enthusiasm and creativity in equal measure, along with the beautiful story of a dream come true. Here, couple Carolina Sánchez (from Cuenca in Ecuador) and Iñaki Murua (from Laguardia in Spain) are two chefs who now combine their working and personal lives after meeting at the Basque Culinary Center. Their attractive yet humble cuisine will surprise guests with its high level of technique, combining their respective culinary worlds: the superb bounty of La Rioja is enhanced by the fruits and condiments of Ecuador, resulting in dishes with incredible flavour.An interesting anecdote here is that Carolina Sánchez, who has become very well known in her role as a judge in her home country’s MasterChef series, has the honour of being the only female Ecuadorian chef to be awarded a Michelin star!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
969;San-Hô;Spain;Adeje;Avenida Virgen de Guadalupe, 21, La Caleta, Adeje, 38679, Spain;28.1017164;-16.7536227;47;true;true;Fusion;One of the gourmet dining options at the luxury Royal Hideaway Corales Beach hotel, San-Hô showcases truly fascinating fusion cuisine with a creative and personal touch which elevates this style of cooking to another level. This is achieved by combining, in occasionally highly surprising ways, culinary influences from Japan, Peru and the Canary Islands.The talented chefs at the helm, Adrián Bosch and Eduardo Domínguez (winners of the Canary Islands’ best chef award in 2012 and 2016 respectively), demonstrate their skill on two enticing tasting menus (Esencia and San Hô), as well as a concise à la carte for those who prefer to order individual dishes. Seating is either at a large counter, where the chefs cook in front of guests, in a contemporary dining room with panoramic windows, or on the pleasant terrace overlooking the garden and the sea.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
971;Omakase by Walt;Spain;Eivissa;Canonge Joan Planells 8, Eivissa, 07800, Spain;38.9077409;1.4307563;73;true;true;Japanese;This restaurant, where all is not what it seems, will come as something of a surprise! What, from the outside, appears to be a simple household appliance shop (you won’t find any sign whatsoever at the entrance) obscures this tiny, discreetly lit restaurant in the purest Japanese style, where the sushi bar and the chef are the undoubted stars of the show. Walter Sidoravicius, originally from Venezuela but with Lithuanian and German roots, has worked and trained around the world, most notably in Tokyo and as an instructor at the Basque Culinary Center. His cuisine is focused on a single Omakase menu that is full of intrigue – guests leave all decision-making to the chef who prepares elaborate dishes in full view that are fully respectful of Japanese tradition (cold and raw options, nigiris served in two parts, dishes served in traditional bowls etc). Guests are asked to arrive at the same time in order to enjoy the culinary experience together.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
973;La Tasquería;Spain;Madrid;Modesto Lafuente 82, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4454892;-3.6956819;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Javi Estévez, who revolutionised Madrid’s culinary scene by elevating humble offal to the realms of haute-cuisine, has added to his career path with this new restaurant which, for many years was the setting for Los Galetos de Tijuca, a Brazilian eatery very popular for its small barbecued chicken (galetos). Now, following a complete overall, it offers guests enhanced space and comfort and a new direction while remaining faithful to an idea that is part of its DNA – in their own words: “we are specialists in cooking offal, but we do other things as well.” The dining experience here is based around three tasting menus (M, Memoria 2015/2023 and The Menu), the aim of which is to recapture the city’s “offal culture” while reinterpreting it with contemporary concepts and techniques. This concept sees the kitchen working with offal such as brain, trotters, tripe, combs, and the famous fried and confit head of suckling pig, one of its most popular dishes, and one that we all share on our social media feeds!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
974;La Prensa;Spain;Saragossa;José Nebra 3, Saragossa, 50007, Spain;41.633181;-0.8746479;25;true;true;Contemporary;What in the 1970s started life as a wine merchant’s gradually became a leading restaurant on the city’s food scene. Here, the duo of chef Marisa Barberán and her husband David Pérez (sommelier and front-of-house manager) have created to a space in which the philosophy is based around one clear concept: a love for a job well done.In the minimalist-style dining room embellished with designer detail, savour contemporary and creative cuisine centred around two tasting menus. The essence of La Prensa’s cuisine is based around an honest approach, the use of the best seasonal ingredients from the region, and a mastery of modern techniques which enables the chef to play with flavours, colours and textures and to create dishes that are highly expressive and innovative.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
975;Les Moles;Spain;Ulldecona;Carretera de La Sénia, Ulldecona, 43550, Spain;40.602104;0.427955;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This family-run business, occupying an old farm with rustic charm and contemporary decorative detail, is firmly steeped in its surroundings and their natural bounty, as well as the history of Ulldecona. This is also demonstrated by its name, which refers to the millstones carved out of the local quarry. Chef Jeroni Castell does everything possible to bring a sustainable approach to his dishes, which are based around the perfect balance that should exist between local provenance, technique and fun, showcasing those products that encapsulate the Terres de l’Ebre region’s coastal and mountain landscapes. Standout dishes here include the “armónica” of grilled Balfegó red tuna with cured egg yolk, and a purée of mashed potato and butter, and El Delta del Ebro, a steamed seafood dish with Ostras del Sol oysters, and a tasting of eel and mackerel. Choose between an array of set menu options (Ànimament, El Camino Recorrido, Tradición, Vegetarian), plus an à la carte from which you can also order half-plates (medias raciones). The tasting menus all begin their life in the restaurant’s creative R&D space.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
976;Koy Shunka;Spain;Barcelona;De Copons 7, Barcelona, 08002, Spain;41.3857791;2.1754154;62;true;false;Japanese;At this discreet Japanese restaurant, hidden behind a large door that you have to knock on to gain access and which almost seems to be a “secret” address given its scarce signage, the concept is based around much more than a working philosophy as the skill of the chef is viewed as a veritable art form here. In this resolutely contemporary space, you’ll find a somewhat surprising wood-fired oven in the centre of the dining room, large fish-maturing cabinets, an impressive U-shaped counter where you can watch the culinary action unfold, and more conventional tables for those who prefer a more intimate meal. The cuisine of chef Hideki Matsuhisa, which brings together Japanese techniques and Mediterranean ingredients, always focuses on well-conceived pairings and a hint of creativity and is based around tasting menus that vary solely in their number of courses. We can highly recommend the Kaki dish – an oyster served on a bed of chopped onion with a Wagyu beef jus. The finishing touches to many of the dishes are added in front of you!;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
977;Ola Martín Berasategui;Spain;Bilbao;De la Ribera 13, Bilbao, 48005, Spain;43.2579547;-2.9264612;48;true;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;Located alongside the river, inside of the Tayko hotel. The aesthetics here are almost as impressive as the cuisine, which sees it proudly vaunting its open brickwork and concrete beams to highlight the fact that it was the first building to be constructed using these materials in the city’s historic quarter. The restaurant exudes personality and is keen to immerse guests in a sensory journey via the story of chef Martín Berasategui, enabling them to discover his vision and his particular sense of culinary excellence through the hands of his disciple Raúl Cabrera (known to everyone as Pintxo). The latter faithfully reproduces his mentor’s dishes with great passion, and with a continual emphasis on cuisine that showcases their ingredients and flavours. These are highlighted in exquisite recipes such as the “kokotxas” and slices of cod with a red prawn Vizcaína sauce, and on two tasting menus: Ola and “Lo mejor de la cocina de Martín Berasategui” (The Best of Martín Berasategui’s Cuisine).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
978;Emporium;Spain;Castelló d'Empúries;Santa Clara 31, Castelló d'Empúries, 17486, Spain;42.2558205;3.0760903;50;true;true;Contemporary;Named after the archaeological ruins at Empúries, this restaurant has declared its strong commitment to the gastronomy of the Alt Empordà by extolling the virtues of the sea and mountains that define the region.Located within the walls of the hotel of the same name, this eatery run by the same family since 1965 now has twins Màrius and Joan Jordà (the fourth generation) at the helm in the kitchen. In the impeccable dining room, they serve updated traditional cuisine that is not shy of creativity and which accentuates the flavours of the Alt Empordà through its use of locally sourced ingredients (fruit and vegetables from Torroella de Montgrí, fish from Port de la Selva and Roses, etc). The cuisine here is centred on two meticulous tasting menus (one shorter option called Mar y Montaña and a longer version called Universo Local), both with a wine pairing option.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
979;Baluarte;Spain;Soria;Caballeros 14, Soria, 42002, Spain;41.7625609;-2.4656422;86;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Accessed via an imposing monumental entrance, this restaurant occupies an impressive location within an aristocratic building where it will surprise guests as soon as they walk through the door thanks to its designer interior. Self-taught chef Óscar García, who has forged a strong bond with the extensive pine forests of the Tierras Altas in Soria province since his childhood, showcases his talent, passion and total commitment to the flavours of traditional Castilian cuisine, which he cleverly reworks through contemporary techniques. His cuisine is centred around two tasting menus (Tradicional and De Altura) which enable guests to appreciate the full glory of seasonal local ingredients with a particular penchant for wild mushrooms (St George’s, Grey Night, cep etc) and black truffles. We can highly recommend the Iberian ham broth with stewed pig’s trotters and organic leeks, as well as the delicious cod tripe stew with wild mushrooms, the texture of which will make you seriously question whether you prefer these dishes or the more traditional versions of them.;Air conditioning;[]
980;Trigo;Spain;Valladolid;Tintes 8, Valladolid, 47002, Spain;41.6526058;-4.7244307;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;It has always been said that wheat (“trigo” in Spanish) is the gold of Castille, hence its historical importance to the region.The restaurant, located just a few steps from the cathedral, reflects the strong passion that chef Víctor Martín has for his cuisine. Alongside his wife Noemí Martínez, a renowned sommelier who runs the dining room, he focuses on creative and contemporary cooking with strong roots in tradition, and is based on his relationship with small suppliers and their superb local produce and ingredients (vegetables from Tudela de Duero, pigeon from Tierra de Campos, chestnuts from Cacabelos etc). Not forgetting traditional pork products from his native León and the occasional seasonal fish dish. Allow the kitchen to treat you to their flights of fancy, accompanied by a wine from the splendid cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
981;Unic;Spain;Sant Josep de sa Talaia;Les Begònies 18, Sant Josep de sa Talaia, 07817, Spain;38.8898956;1.4077202;61;true;false;Innovative;Part of the modern Migjorn Ibiza hotel (located in the area around the Playa d’en Bossa), Unic impresses guests with its setting inside two glass cubes as well as its stylish decor. Here, French chef David Grussaute offers two tasting menus (Unic and La Xanga, with sections entitled Prelude, From the Sea, Surf & Turf, From the Land, and A Moment of Sweetness) that always champion locally sourced ingredients which enable him to showcase the culinary essence of both the island and the Mediterranean in close collaboration with small-scale producers, breeders and the local fishing community. All his dishes feature marked, intense flavours and highly delicate sauces, although if we had to highlight one dish that will remain in the memory, it would be the “Pityuses, island of pines” dessert, which was as refreshing as it was unexpected, and akin to eating a Mediterranean forest!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
982;Ambivium;Spain;Peñafiel;Camino de Carraovejas, Peñafiel, 47300, Spain;41.5946148;-4.0875496;62;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The Pago de Carraovejas wine estate (Ribera del Duero), guarded over by the iconic Castillo de Peñafiel, has built its prestige around wines teeming with personality. The same philosophy applies to Ambivium, a dining space created to ensure the same harmony and end result. Featuring cutting-edge designer detail, splendid service and idyllic views of the vineyards from the bar, the restaurant conjures up exquisite dishes that you can enjoy while admiring this glorious setting. Chef Cristóbal Muñoz offers a tasting menu (Cellarium: Roots and future) on which everything revolves around food conservation methods, ranging from time-honoured techniques to the latest innovative trends, superbly complemented by the 4,000 or so labels in the extraordinary wine cellar! The meticulous presentation and visual impact of the desserts stand out, in particular the one simply called Miel (Honey) a homage to the bodega’s beehives, which we found especially impressive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
983;Oria;Spain;Barcelona;Passeig de Gràcia 75, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3938241;2.1624525;23;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Gastro-hotels are definitely on the rise thanks to their increasing popularity with international guests, and the strong emphasis on high-quality cuisine at the Monument hotel (which includes the three-Michelin-star Lasarte) is a perfect example of this. Incorporated into the hotel lobby, the Oria is a spacious, elegant and unique restaurant overseen by chef Martín Berasategui, hence the high standard of its updated take on traditional cuisine with its roots in the Mediterranean but with a nod to the Basque Country. Choose between three surprise tasting menus: Formula Oria (lunchtime midweek only), Tradición (a journey back to the origins of Martín Berasategui’s cuisine and the flavours of the Basque country), and Itsasmendi (“mountain and sea” in the Basque language), which showcases the wealth of the region’s bounty. Resident chef Xabi Goikoetxea enjoys chatting and sharing impressions with guests in the dining room.;Air conditioning;[]
984;Enigma;Spain;Barcelona;Sepúlveda 38, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3768726;2.1541799;74;true;true;Creative;This unique, daring and unusual restaurant has raised its game once again with its focus on technical excellence and, above all, a desire to amaze its guests. Behind the discreet façade is an interior where fantasy reigns supreme, combining originality with a radical design that will definitely raise the eyebrows, including ceilings that appear to be suspended mid-air and give the impression of being in a futuristic freezer room! Chef Albert Adrià is at the helm in the kitchen, where he concentrates on a single 25-course tasting menu which changes every month. On it, he unveils his full culinary mastery – the finishing touches to many of his visually inspired dishes are added in front of guests to enable them to fully appreciate the innumerable (and often magical) techniques that he employs. He always works with the very best seasonal ingredients and organises the culinary experience around 4 different options: Tasting, 7 Wine Regions, Mature Wines, and 7 Million Bubbles. Make sure you book well ahead.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
985;Hofmann;Spain;Barcelona;La Granada del Penedès 14-16, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.3971709;2.1530609;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This institution in the upper reaches of Barcelona, which has played host to a number of chefs who have gone on to win their own Michelin stars, reflects the love affair that its founder chef, Mey Hofmann, had with food, a legacy that she has passed down to her daughter Silvia and her expert teaching staff. In the restaurant itself, featuring staff from the school and a large picture window through which guests can watch activity unfold in the kitchen, an à la carte-style menu is available at lunchtime (along with a slightly more refined Gastronómico Mediodía menu). In the evening, these are replaced by two extensive tasting menus (Gastronómico Noche and Luxury). The focus here is on modern fusion cuisine with strong roots in tradition, which is continually brought up to date in terms of the pairing of ingredients, technique and presentation. The desserts here are always a delight!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
987;Es Tragón;Spain;Sant Antoni de Portmany;Carretera Cap Negret, Sant Antoni de Portmany, 07820, Spain;38.9967311;1.2867365;65;false;false;Creative;An oasis of tranquillity on this busy island, occupying a beautiful villa surrounded by pines trees and boasting a pleasant tree-shaded terrace. Here, chef Álvaro Sanz is keen to involve his whole team in his culinary process, giving a new twist to his cuisine. The latter is inspired by Mediterranean traditions and revolves around a collaborative approach to theme-based cooking featuring input from historians, biologists, producers etc. His extensive tasting menu, accompanied by different types of sourdough bread, reflects a journey through the history of Mediterranean civilisations that is a highly cerebral yet serene dining experience with a strong focus on sustainability (locally grown organic ingredients, composting, recycling, energy saving etc).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
988;Los Guayres;Spain;Mogán;Avenida de los Marrero 2, Mogán, 35138, Spain;27.8225974;-15.7595468;92;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Spanish;Having travelled through the arid landscapes of the Mogán valley, this elegant and exotic restaurant will provide welcome relief as well as a magical dining experience.In this setting in the Cordial Mogán Playa hotel, your path will cross with Alexis Álvarez, a chef trained in some of the country’s best restaurants. Here, this native of Gran Canaria reaffirms his culinary style through a fusion of traditional Canary Island cuisine and more contemporary influences. The focus of his interesting menus teeming with innovative detail is on international dishes and ingredients from the islands (gofio, goat etc) and the abundant waters of the Atlantic (grouper, red tuna, sea bream etc). We strongly recommend booking a table on the terrace – a typical Canary Island-style balcony overlooking the hotel gardens.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
989;El Ermitaño;Spain;Benavente;Arrabal Huerta de los Salados, Benavente, 49600, Spain;42.00712;-5.65799;22;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;El Ermitaño is accessed by a minor road flanked by market gardens and fields of corn, a setting which reaffirms the gastronomic, cultural and family legacy of this aristocratic country house which retains close links with its surroundings and boasts an adjoining hermitage dating back to 1775. The Pérez brothers (Pedro Mario and Óscar Manuel), who look for contentment in even the smallest of things and who, in their own words, “cook what we are”, remain loyal to their history, their heritage and to their different yet complementary personalities. Take your pick between the à la carte, featuring the restaurant’s signature dishes (don’t miss the cured meat “canutillos” with duck liver and quince) and the occasionally creative and seasonally inspired dish, and two tasting menus: one that guests create themselves by selecting four dishes from the à la carte, and a second special menu based around baby lamb, a favourite ingredient of the team here. The latter includes up to 12 courses (we particularly enjoyed the glazed sweetbreads with potatoes, mangetout, radish and vinegar) and requires advance booking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
990;Zarate;Spain;Bilbao;Licenciado Poza 65, Bilbao, 48013, Spain;43.262561;-2.9435024;82;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;The history of Zarate is that of a man passionate about fishing and the sea, to the point where his cooking is described as “tidal-inspired cuisine”. Chef Sergio Ortiz de Zarate started his career in Lekeitio (Vizcaya), where he began to make a name for himself thanks to his superb baked wild fish. His traditional cooking gained further recognition following his move to Bilbao and a widening of his repertoire that involved more modern dishes and a focus on locally sourced ingredients. The strong guiding principles of the restaurant, the façade of which it shares with the “Taberna Zarate” (the latter offering an array of delicious tapas), are based around his exceptional knowledge of fish – Cantabria’s finest raw ingredient that he sources daily from the ports of Lekeitio and Ondarroa. The à la carte is complemented by two tasting menus with differing numbers of courses (Menú 13 Pasos and Menú 17 Pasos), on which you can find options such as marinated sardines with “migas” breadcrumbs and grapes, the monkfish and duck “mi-cuit” with wakame and apple, and squid risotto without rice.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
991;Maruja Limón;Spain;Vigo;Montero Ríos 4, Vigo, 36201, Spain;42.2404552;-8.7238918;24;false;true;Contemporary;Self-taught chef Rafa Centeno is proof that someone without a background in the world of gastronomy can still be rewarded with a Michelin star. Before opening his restaurant in 2001, this former graduate in industrial relations had never cooked professionally but started to see cooking as a form of personal expression. Located just a few metres from Vigo’s maritime promenade and named after his mother-in-law, Maruja Limón offers guests a fun, liberating and informal dining experience that Centeno hopes will re-awaken their emotions and memories. Ably supported in the kitchen by chef Inés Abril, he conjures up two tasting menus for guests: Esencia Maruja and Maruja en Estado Puro (both with a wine-pairing option). Dishes that you are likely to find here include tartare of Galician veal with watercress, parmesan and black truffle, grilled cured hake, smoked eel with macadamia nuts, and beef rib, barbecued tree tomatoes, fermented cabbage and kale.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
992;Riff;Spain;Valencia;Conde de Altea 18, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.4657836;-0.3684603;90;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;German chef Bernd Knöller considers himself Valencian at heart and is at the helm of this restaurant where he constantly reinvents what he offers, which has led to a more contemporary and fun ambience that includes a kitchen that overlooks the dining room and is surrounded by a counter where you can watch dishes being prepared in front of you as you eat. Globe-trotting chef Bernd Knöller has moved onto an important stage in his career which sees him interacting with his natural surroundings. This has led to him making a name for himself on the local food scene through his occasionally anarchic and always liberated vision of creative Mediterranean cuisine, which is available via a fixed price à la carte and two menus – one available at lunchtime, the other a tasting option. On these, you can enjoy rice dishes that showcase his love for his adopted region, fish and seafood that he sources at the local fish market, and unique dishes such as sweetbreads and onion (the lightly textured beef sweetbreads are served with a sweet roasted onion jus and a petal of pickled onion).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
993;Les Magnòlies;Spain;Arbúcies;Paseo Mossèn Antoni Serres 7, Arbúcies, 17401, Spain;41.8189509;2.5084947;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The very high level of cuisine in this impeccable family-run eatery situated in the La Selva area (in the province of Girona) comes as a pleasant surprise. The restaurant, which owes its name to the three mature magnolia trees that surround this 19C building, has managed to bring itself up-to-date while maintaining the classic elegance that is part of its DNA. The focus of head chef Víctor Torres, who shares his time with the award-winning Quirat de la Ciudad Condal at the InterContinental Barcelona, is on modern, technical cuisine but without losing sight of traditional values, hence his strong commitment to local organic ingredients on an à la carte with half-plate options, and two tasting menus (“A Walk through Montseny” and “A Trip through Montseny”). The guiding principle here is one taken from the great Joan Miró: “A cook is transformed into an artist when he/she has things to say on the plate, in the same way as a painter on a canvas”.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
994;O'Pazo;Spain;Padrón;Pazos s/n, Padrón, 15917, Spain;42.7564294;-8.65202;35;true;true;Grills;If you’re unfamiliar with O’Pazo, one of Galicia’s most renowned restaurants for grilled cuisine, you’re long overdue a visit to dine in this unique space created by the Vidal brothers (with Óscar in the kitchen and Manuel in the dining room), where everything revolves around the wood-fired grill. This charming property located next to the main road boasts an elegant interior design featuring an abundance of dark wood, providing the backdrop for traditionally based cuisine that is mainly served as part of the Rescaldo tasting menu. Despite the apparently simple grilled approach to cooking, the end result is a gourmet experience of the highest level which showcases Atlantic fish and seafood, produce from the fields around Padrón and, above all, the native Rubia Gallega breed of cattle (don’t miss the superb steak, which is braised and filleted). The extensive wine cellar features some top-notch Spanish and international labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
995;Voramar;Spain;Portbou;Passeig de la Sardana 6, Portbou, 17497, Spain;42.4265274;3.1615535;48;true;true;Contemporary;Situated right on the seafront, where it enjoys good views of Portbou’s bay and beach, this family-run restaurant providing attentive service has been renovated to offer a clear gourmet focus. The cuisine, in the hands of young chefs Guillem Gavilan and Pau Jamas (the former is in charge of all things savoury, the latter desserts), showcases enthusiasm, technical expertise and creativity, with a leitmotif based around seasonal ingredients and popular dishes that combine meat and fish/seafood (a good example is the Cap i Pota veal with Mediterranean red tuna). Here, everything revolves around two unique tasting menus (Petit Voramar and Gran Voramar), each based around an updated take on traditional cuisine, and both starting with an appetiser/tapas section called Vora (in tribute to the name by which the restaurant is better known locally). Guests can also request a choice of artisanal bread (rustic, with olives, cereals, sandwich, black bread etc) accompanied by premium olive oils.;Air conditioning;[]
997;DINS Santi Taura;Spain;Palma;Plaza de Llorenç Villalonga 4, Palma, 07001, Spain;39.565643;2.6529955;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located amid the attractive surroundings of Palma’s cathedral, on the ground floor of the attractive El Llorenç Parc de la Mar boutique hotel.In the elegant, contemporary style dining room, chef Santi Taura demonstrates his passion for traditional Mallorcan cuisine, taking everyday recipes from the islands and bringing them up to date, using native ingredients and prioritising flavour over and above anything else. He presides over a single tasting menu called Origens (11 courses, although another three courses can also be added) which changes in line with the seasons and takes us on a journey across the island, so that we can discover its traditions and ingredients through his creativity. The chef also enjoys passing from one table to the next before the meal to chat with his guests.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
998;Ababol;Spain;Albacete;Calderón de la Barca 14, Albacete, 02002, Spain;38.9887598;-1.854235;33;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Albacete, which has been known as the New York of the La Mancha region since the time when the Spanish writer known as Azorín coined the term in one of his poems, boasts an enticing gourmet focus thanks to the Ababol restaurant, which is the Spanish word for a type of red poppy. In its contemporary dining room, overlooked by the open kitchen, chef Juan Monteagudo conjures up dishes which showcase the traditional roots of La Mancha, select ingredients (many from its local farms), and sublime sauces that you’ll want to mop up on your plate! The French technical detail on display is influenced by the chef’s father (the artist Philippe André Georges Monteagudo) and is accompanied by a meticulous approach to presentation. The à la carte (half-portions are available) is complemented by two tasting menus (Tierra and Ababol) and a third dedicated to game during the hunting season. Everything on the menu is delicious but one dish that stood out for us was the “cauliflower with Iberian pork fat”.;Air conditioning;[]
999;Clos Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Raimundo Fernández Villaverde 24, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4465794;-3.6999179;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Here, in the impressive Madrid outpost of sommelier and restaurateur Marcos Granda, the owner of the famous Skina restaurant in Marbella who has brought this different dining option to Madrid, the kitchen and the wine cellar take on equal prominence.This eatery, with its contemporary ambience, is the perfect setting in which to enjoy modern cuisine with a creative tint, based around the traditional flavours and the best ingredients from around Spain. Here, the gastronomic approach is epitomised by Clos Madrid’s mantra: great restaurants are those that make guests feel important. The name Clos is a French word for a high-quality wine estate surrounded by a wall.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1000;Desde 1911;Spain;Madrid;Vivero 3, Madrid, 28040, Spain;40.4485341;-3.7098877;97;true;false;Seafood;A restaurant that pays full homage to its ingredients, the sea and the lasting legacy of La Coruña’s fishing tradition. This spacious and somewhat surprising eatery, occupying a former industrial workshop once used to manufacture electrical coil pumps, features various event spaces plus an interior patio on which to enjoy a post-lunch or -dinner digestif or coffee. As you would expect, the cooking is centred around its impressive fish and seafood which is shown to guests at the same time as the menu. Choose between four options (each with a set main course that changes daily, plus a choice of between 3 and 6 starters). The latter will always include one raw, one marinated and one soup-style option. Make sure you save space for the superb cheese and dessert trolleys! An extensive international wine list completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1001;Sa Clastra;Spain;Es Capdellà;Carretera Es Capdellà, Km 1.7, Es Capdellà, 07196, Spain;39.5918479;2.4800457;62;false;true;Creative;Located within the walls of the Castell Son Claret, with its delightful gardens and an interior of rare beauty. Head chef Jordi Cantó serves creative cuisine with a nod to the traditional cooking of Mallorca, which is showcased on a concise à la carte and a superb tasting menu (short and long options are available). The latter is particularly recommended for its gastronomic journey across the island that from the outset is full of nuances and childhood memories (it also comes with an explication of typical dishes that are represented with great finesse and creativity). Leave your car in the car park at the entrance to enjoy a delightful stroll through the garden! The hotel’s romantic patio is perfect for alfresco dining in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1002;Santerra;Spain;Madrid;General Pardiñas 56, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4289405;-3.6782994;37;true;false;Contemporary;It is hard to find a better restaurant than this for La Mancha cuisine in the Spanish capital, where the self-styled “cocina de monte bajo” (which literally means “scrubland cuisine”) is shown due respect and transformed into a gourmet experience. Located in the heart of the city’s Salamanca district, it offers different dining options, ranging from tapas and “raciones” (the Iberian ham croquettes are an absolute must) at the bar to more gastronomic fare in the dining room in the semi-basement. Chef Miguel Carretero showcases his full personality here, bringing the flavours of La Mancha to the Spanish capital through seasonal dishes in which game is ever present (roast loin of venison, duck royale, stuffed quail “a lo Tío Lucas”, pigeon soup etc) and which is particularly well expressed in his escabeches. The “media ración”-style à la carte is the perfect option to create your own personalised meal, and is complemented by the impressive Monte Bajo tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
1003;Atempo;Spain;Barcelona;Còrsega 200, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3910001;2.1522177;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This spacious and contemporary restaurant will surprise guests as soon as they walk through the door as they are accompanied to two kitchens, for hot and cold food respectively, in which they can try a pleasant array of appetisers and small snacks before being ushered into the elegant dining room. The cuisine here, based around a single tasting menu designed by celebrity chef Jordi Cruz, showcases contemporary cooking and techniques that aim to highlight the depth of flavours, something they succeed in here thanks to top-quality ingredients and highly consistent combinations. The interplay between the kitchen and the service in the dining room is particularly impressive, with the finishing touches to many of Atempo’s dishes added in front of guests. One standout dish was the hare royale, with a black garlic emulsion and roast pumpkin and white garlic cream – a French-inspired recipe combining both flavour and solid technique.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1004;Tula;Spain;Xàbia;Avenida de la Llibertat 36, Xàbia, 03730, Spain;38.7707289;0.1925837;69;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;If everyone is talking up a restaurant, it must be doing something right! In this unpretentious eatery overlooking Arenal beach, couple Borja Susilla and Clara Puig offer guests enticing dishes with the essence of the Mediterranean in which their training in leading restaurants (they met while working with chef Quique Dacosta) is clearly evident. Choose between an array of market-inspired specials (fresh fish, in particular) that you won’t find on the menu as well as a seven-course tasting menu and many dishes designed for sharing. The latter can be ordered as half-plates so that everyone can create their own menu and taste lots of dishes. Make sure you order the shisho leaf taco with pancetta, smoked eel and misonnaise, the delicious pig’s ear, and the potato fritter with a seafood sauce and San Antonio cheese, the latter a successful tribute to this maritime-inspired recipe.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1005;Messina;Spain;Marbella;Avenida Severo Ochoa 12, Marbella, 29603, Spain;36.5084597;-4.8806499;62;false;true;Creative;Messina reflects the dream of chef Mauricio Giovanini, who has explored beyond his Argentinian roots to develop his unique, non-conformist culinary style, ably supported by his wife PÍa Ninci in her role as sommelier and front-of-house manager. Here, you’ll find a space that has been brought pleasantly up to date, with a kitchen that opens onto the dining room and even an exclusive “Chef’s Table” for four guests who can savour unique dishes not available to other diners. On his menus, Giovanini strives for harmony and clear individual flavours through a focus on cuisine inspired by both Europe and Latin America. The unique nature of this chef stems from his observation that flavour resides in the liquid essence of foods, hence his use of pure juices and their by-products (concentrates, creams etc) that are a key part of his culinary concept. Today, he continues in the same vein, although he now shows much more interest in natural thickening agents. He also has a multi-purpose R&D space called InsIDe Messina, that can also be booked by guests.;Air conditioning;[]
1006;Barro;Spain;Ávila;Carretera de Salamanca 4, Ávila, 05002, Spain;40.6577005;-4.709749;77;false;false;Creative;Local, ecologically minded ingredients, a focus on a zero-waste philosophy, artisanally produced crockery and support for local small-scale producers are all key here. In this restaurant, which occupies an impressively refurbished 200-year-old warehouse previously used to store flour, the team works according to a single mantra: “cooking the past from the present, but with an eye on the future”. Fronted by Ávila-born chef Carlos Casillas, the restaurant features a kitchen visible from the dining room and boasts superb views of the city’s walls from the opposite bank of the River Adaja. His cuisine, which views food as a “live ecosystem”, is showcased on a single, creatively inspired tasting menu called Volver that the chef uses to surprise guests and pay homage to his origins and to all the people (kitchen team, breeders, farmers, artisans etc) who contribute to Barro’s day-to-day existence. The constantly evolving dishes here follow a series of unusually named stages (Caresses, Abstraction, Balance, Chiaroscuro, Mistreatment, Fires etc).;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1007;La Costa;Spain;El Ejido;Bulevar 48, El Ejido, 04700, Spain;36.7709659;-2.8276459;86;false;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The western part of Almería province is famous for its huge greenhouses, a key feature behind its identity and its superb fruit and vegetables. Chef José Álvarez has successfully transformed this family restaurant combining tradition and modernity, basing his cuisine on strong flavours and a constant desire to surprise. The stars of the show here are fish and seafood from the locally named Alborán Sea, as well as local vegetables, usually sourced from small-scale producers. The chef demonstrates his commitment to the local area through his “Verde Mar y Tierra Azul” (Green Sea and Blue Earth) tasting menu, about which he says: “If we were to remove the sea of plastic from the Mediterranean coastline around El Ejido, we would discover that we live in one of the world’s greenest oases”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1008;Cancook;Spain;Saragossa;de León XIII 2-4, Saragossa, 50008, Spain;41.6471441;-0.8804518;73;false;false;Creative;The duo of Ramsés González (in the kitchen) and Diego Millán (sommelier and front-of-house manager) were looking to take their gastronomic project to the next level, which led them to move to a large and more centrally located space in the centre of Zaragoza.Their aim is to ensure that what they offer is an experience, hence the culinary journey that they refer to as La Fresquera. This process begins with showing their ingredients (a minimum of 90% of which are from Aragón) to guests, continues with appetisers in the Research & Development kitchen (home to a private chef’s table), and ends up in the dining room upstairs (which includes a counter by the kitchen where the finishing touches are added to dishes). Choose between three creative tasting menus (Gran Menú, Festival and Evolución) that showcase the cuisine of the Aragón region.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1009;Il Bocconcino by Royal Hideaway;Spain;Adeje;Avenida Virgen de Guadalupe 21, La Caleta, Adeje, 38679, Spain;28.1020231;-16.7539875;84;false;false;Italian Contemporary;If you’re looking for an Italian restaurant with a difference, this dining space in the Royal Hideaway Corales Suites hotel won’t disappoint thanks to its superb terrace (which we highly recommend for lunch or dinner in fine weather) and its re-creation of Italian recipes from a relatively modern and progressive perspective, with the added attraction of always using (with the exception of the irreplaceable Pecorino and Parmesan) local ingredients sourced from the island. Chef Niki Pavanelli, who is originally from Bologna and can often be seen passing from table to table to explain his dishes, complements the à la carte with two extensive menus (Identidad and Il Boccocino). Don’t miss his updated Carbonara 3.0, Il Tortellino, which rekindles memories of his grandmother (la nonna) or, last but not least, the La Scarpetta dessert, through which he invites guests to discover the time-honoured Italian technique of the same name (the expression is “fare la scarpetta”) which consists of completely mopping up your plate with bread as a symbol of appreciation.;Great view,Terrace;[]
1010;L'Aliança d'Anglès;Spain;Anglès;Jacint Verdaguer 3, Anglès, 17160, Spain;41.95616;2.6390996;43;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Catalan;More than just a restaurant, this eatery is a part of local history as it occupies a building dating back to 1919 that once belonged to a group of farmers and acted as a casino and a type of social club. In the hands of the Feliu family since the 1950s, it has taken on a new lease of life under the baton of Cristina Feliu and her partner, chef Àlex Carrera, who came here to set up his own restaurant after working for several years at El Celler de Can Roca in the province of Girona. To a delightful 19C-style backdrop featuring lots of vintage decorative details, savour cooking with a contemporary flair where locally sourced ingredients take centre stage, all of which are explained in detail with every course. Two tasting menus (Descubierta and Emoción) are the only dining options, both of which begin with what the restaurant refers to as “vermouth time”.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1011;Callizo;Spain;Ainsa;Plaza Mayor, Ainsa, 22330, Spain;42.4176644;0.1381766;54;false;true;Creative, Innovative;It is surprising to find a restaurant of this level in a small town but Callizo offers a perfect gastronomic experience that will delight the senses and provide an opportunity to discover the wonderful landscapes and flavours of the Sobrarbe area. The restaurant, housed in a large, centrally located stone property with a surprisingly modern decor, plays an integral role in the dining experience, which involves a staged journey through the house to discover the true culinary essence of this region, albeit with a nod to other parts of the world. The dishes served here on two tasting menus (Tierra and Piedras) are well prepared with delicate textures and distinct contrasts that fly the flag for what the restaurant refers to as “techno-emotional mountain cuisine” which showcases the small-scale local producers who supply the restaurant. One dish that we particularly enjoyed was the trout ceviche from the nearby Cinca river, which was featured in the Spanish series “21st Century Pyrenean Landscapes”.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
1012;Maca de Castro;Spain;Port d'Alcúdia;Juno s/n, Port d'Alcúdia, 07410, Spain;39.8343;3.11829;18;false;true;Creative;A restaurant that is continually on the up thanks to chef Macarena de Castro (Maca), who has become increasingly committed to sustainability and supports a policy of reafforestation. Located on the first floor of a villa-style building, the restaurant features a dining space with a modern, avant-garde ambience that it shares with the Jardín Bistró (on the ground floor, with a format that is a little easier on the pocket). The single surprise tasting menu is both creative and inspired by the Mediterranean, with a focus on the best seasonal ingredients that Mallorca has to offer, most of which are sourced from nearby auctions, small-scale producers on the island, or from the restaurant’s vegetable garden in Sa Pobla. One of the main signature dishes that is usually on the menu here is the skate with salt and a rock samphire hollandaise sauce. As soon as you walk through the door here, the chef’s love of her local area is clearly evident via a poetically inspired book in which a daily thought for the day is highlighted.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1013;Pablo;Spain;Leon;Avenida Los Cubos 8, Leon, 24007, Spain;42.6004864;-5.5665652;58;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A family-run restaurant that has cooking in its blood and has moved with the times without losing its traditional values.Located just a few metres from León’s cathedral, known as the Pulchra Leonina, this restaurant is full of contrasts, ranging from the masonry on the façade, which is in keeping with its historic surroundings, to its surprising minimalist interior design, which features an unusual wood-panelled ceiling. Alongside his wife Yolanda Rojo (the daughter of the founder), chef Juanjo Losada creates what could be described as cutting-edge Leonese cuisine, as part of which his creative and meticulous dishes are built around the best local, natural and seasonal ingredients. The only option here is a single tasting menu that changes throughout the year along with a wine pairing option. He is also very keen on flying the flag for the region’s small-scale local producers.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1014;Baeza & Rufete;Spain;Alacant;Avenida de Ansaldo 31, Alacant, 03540, Spain;38.368797;-0.433443;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that exudes a passion for cooking, plenty of experience and the unmistakeable talent of staff trained by Martín Berasategui. The first thing that chef Joaquín Baeza will casually tell you is that, in keeping with his mentor, he is here to bring joy to his guests! This small, unpretentious restaurant is run with great dedication by the chef alongside Esther Castillo, who works as front-of-house manager and sommelier. The modern Mediterranean cooking here, whose leitmotifs are the diversity and seasonality of Alicante’s produce, gives pride of place to aromatic herbs picked personally by the chef (lemon basil, thyme, mint, lemon verbena etc) as well as olive oils with plenty of personality (Elipse Gourmet, Capilla del Fraile, Diez+Oro etc). His painstakingly prepared menus (Short and Long) are complemented by a few additional suggestions in the form of half or full “raciones”. The intensity of flavours here is amazing!;Air conditioning;[]
1015;Lienzo;Spain;Valencia;Plaza de Tetuán 18, Valencia, 46003, Spain;39.4750292;-0.3697428;64;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Lienzo occupies an elegant building with a minimalist feel. The decor here fully respects the name of the restaurant (“canvas” in English) thanks to the whitewashed walls embellished with striking, colourful canvases by Valencian artists which change every three months.Murcia-born chef María José Martínez, ably supported by her husband Juanjo Soria in the dining room, creates modern Mediterranean cuisine with no little creativity that showcases and fully respects seasonal Valencian ingredients from its market gardens, mountains and coastal waters. These are presented to their best in delicately prepared and meticulously presented dishes, including sublime sauces and creams, all of which feature on several enticing set menus: one “executive” option (Trazos) and two tasting menus (Pinceladas and Lienzo).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1016;Solana;Spain;Ampuero;La Bien Aparecida 11, Ampuero, 39849, Spain;43.3263141;-3.4531514;60;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Solana is impressively situated just a few metres from the Santuario de la Bien Aparecida, the venerated patron saint of Cantabria. If you’re looking for a picture-postcard view of the Cantabrian mountains you won’t find a better location than this, where the views from your table transport guests to a world of green meadows in which cows can been seen grazing nearby. Chef Ignacio Solana, alongside his sister Inma (sommelier and front-of-house manager), showcases contemporary cuisine with strong traditional roots that is faithful to both the sea and the mountains but with a nod to tradition and a constant love affair with seasonal vegetables sourced from its own garden as well as from market-gardeners in the Bajo Asón area. The à la carte, featuring Solana’s signature dishes (such as its famous ham croquettes, cod fritters, delicious small squid (“maganos”) with onions, chicken stew etc) pays tribute to the chef’s mother, perpetuates her legacy, and is complemented by two enticing tasting menus (Breñas and Golmaje).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1017;Beat;Spain;Calp;Urbanización Marisol Park 1A, Calp, 03710, Spain;38.6474226;0.060922;57;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, French Contemporary;Beat reflects the "culinary pulse " of The Cook Book hotel right from the outset, quickening the heartbeat from the very first bite of your appetisers.This bright restaurant, with its dominant white decor, reflects the true essence of the Mediterranean, providing the backdrop for what promises to be a stunning dining experience, marked by faultless ingredients and a harmony that sees flavours working together to their mutual benefit. Valencia-born chef José Manuel Miguel, the only chef to have been awarded a Michelin star in both France and Spain, continues his quest for excellence, steering what he offers towards his menus (including one that is vegetarian) without neglecting an impressive à la carte. All feature contemporary dishes that combine the vitality of the Mediterranean with the finesse of French cooking. The French influence here is typified by authentic butter from Normandy!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1019;Hisop;Spain;Barcelona;Passatge de Marimon 9, Barcelona, 08021, Spain;41.3944279;2.1480369;90;false;true;Creative;Named after an aromatic Mediterranean plant, this Michelin-starred restaurant has been enjoying the fruits of its success for some time now, in part due to its competitive pricing.In the contemporary, minimalist-style dining room, chef Oriol Ivern serves fresh, creative dishes that offer a different take on Catalan culinary tradition, and are always based around locally sourced seasonal ingredients and impressive combinations. In keeping with the chef’s personality, the aim of his cuisine is to offer truly unique dishes that are both playful and full of surprising detail. Although not extensive, the enticing à la carte is complemented by an interesting tasting menu with a wine pairing option. A must here, and one that is requested time and time again, is the red mullet with a “mollusc” mayonnaise.;Air conditioning;[]
1020;Audrey's;Spain;Calp;Avenida Juan Carlos I 48, Calp, 03710, Spain;38.6501744;0.072623;72;true;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;(Temporarily closed for refurbishment) This bright, fresh and elegant gastronomic jewel, which takes its name from Audrey Hepburn, the legendary star of the film “Breakfast at Tiffany’s”, is the fiefdom of chef Rafa Soler. Here, he conjures up highly developed and creative cuisine both in terms of technique and presentation, but which retains a strong connection with the soil, the past and seasonal ingredients. In the words of the chef himself, “we have access here to the full expression of Valencia’s culinary bounty”. Through his tasting menus (Roots, Origin and Farm), the latter vegetarian, discover dishes that exude personality and the soul of the Mediterranean, transforming ingredients with a respect for seasonality and minimum fuss. Standout details include the homemade bread that accompanies the menus and which is baked according to a family recipe (they have a bread oven in the suburban town of Burjassot) and the extra-virgin olive oil that they bottle themselves and which is produced from thousand-year-old trees in Traiguera (Castellón province).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1022;El Corral del Indianu;Spain;Arriondas;Avenida de Europa 14, Arriondas, 33540, Spain;43.3902522;-5.1842735;43;true;true;Creative;This restaurant, occupying the oldest building in Arriondas, has a name that recalls those Asturians who left to find their fortune in the Americas at the end of the 19C, and then returned home wealthy and with a new social status.While the setting is special, with an interior dining room with a rustic-contemporary feel and a second glass-fronted room boasting attractive views of a delightful rear garden, the main attraction here is the culinary expertise of chef José Antonio Campoviejo. This chef’s great passion for cooking is showcased in his attention to detail, flavours and creativity, with a focus on traditional recipes from the abundant natural bounty of the Asturias region (oysters from the Eo estuary, Pitu de Caleya chickens, the region’s incredible cheeses, etc). The restaurant also has two reserved parking spaces by the front door for its guests.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1023;Can Bosch;Spain;Cambrils;Rambla Jaume I 19, Cambrils, 43850, Spain;41.0670276;1.0590381;40;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Can Bosch showcases the honest and unbreakable family values that have been the guiding principles for this restaurant since it first opened its doors in 1969. Here, the exclusive use of seasonal ingredients and top-quality local fish and seafood are paramount, the latter sourced from the fish auction in Cambrils. Its savoury rice dishes are equally renowned, prepared using the Carnaroli del “Molí de Rafelet” variety of rice from the Ebro delta. Father and son Joan and Arnau Bosch subtly combine their respective culinary personalities in cuisine where tradition and innovation go hand in hand and where full respect is shown to the ingredients at their disposal. There’s no greater sign of success than the continued support of its customers, which has seen this restaurant maintain its Michelin star since the 1985 edition! The à la carte, which is heavily focused on top-notch ingredients, features a section dedicated exclusively to lobster (by prior order only), and is complemented by two set menus (Tradición and Degustación).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1024;Orobianco;Spain;Calp;Colina del Sol 49 A, Calp, 03710, Spain;38.6665147;0.0451019;96;false;true;Italian Contemporary;At Orobianco, spectacular views of Calp and its impressive Peñón de Ifach rock are complemented by Italian-inspired cuisine full of culinary nuances under the tutelage of award-winning chef Paolo Casagrande that will undoubtedly leaving a lasting impression! Elegance is an obvious thread here and is clearly in evidence in dishes available on two set menus (Short and Long). The restaurant’s culinary essence is a fusion of Italian cooking and local ingredients that showcase Spain and the Mediterranean through dishes such as cuttlefish tagliatelle, watercress risotto with red prawns, and spaghettoni with a pil-pil sauce. Add to this perfect cooking techniques, clean flavours, astute pairings of ingredients that add a contemporary touch to classic foundations, plus an impressive choice of artisanal Italian bread.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
1025;Raíces-Carlos Maldonado;Spain;Talavera de la Reina;Ronda de Canillo 3, Talavera de la Reina, 45600, Spain;39.9565163;-4.8321518;57;true;false;Creative;Chef Carlos Maldonado knows no limits and it is this which characterises his cooking, which is firmly steeped in the flavours and ingredients of La Mancha but which is also open to influences from around the world, as witnessed by the twinning between his beloved Talavera de la Reina and Puebla (Mexico).The restaurant, which could almost pass unnoticed because of its discreet façade, boasts a classic-contemporary look in varying tones of white, plus an adjoining dining room offering tables with a little more intimacy. His tasting menus (Raíces and Hechos de Barro) feature daring, highly technical dishes which are impressive for their equal measure of freshness and boldness. The tableware has been designed by the restaurant and even has the fingerprints of the chef’s son (Carlitos) printed on one of the dessert dishes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1026;Yugo The Bunker;Spain;Madrid;San Blas 4, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.410625;-3.694612;50;false;true;Japanese;If you’re unfamiliar with the concept of Japan’s traditional pubs (izakayas), you’ll be pleasantly surprised by Yugo, which replicates the feel of this aspect of Japanese daily life.The impeccable setting, featuring spaces with two distinct ambiences plus a sushi bar with a profusion of wood and decorative masks and flags, provides the backdrop for cuisine prepared to the minutest detail by Julián Mármol, who skilfully combines Japanese and Mediterranean cuisine while respecting the subtlety of the Far East. Everything stems from his use of the finest ingredients, resulting in a succession of taste sensations. The room in the basement, available for the exclusive use of club members, is known as “The Bunker”, the design of which is based on a bunker from WW2 and is used by guests when the main dining room is full.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
1027;Via Veneto;Spain;Barcelona;Ganduxer 10, Barcelona, 08021, Spain;41.3924046;2.1389712;42;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Almost everyone in Barcelona is aware of the legendary culinary status of Via Veneto! Even after half a century of service and change, the Monje family has retained the true values of this restaurant that seems anchored in the past, but which has been able to move with the times without losing an ounce of its personality. To an elegant and genuine Belle Époque backdrop, young chef David Andrés maintains the culinary status quo here through cuisine that underpins its classical heritage, albeit with a focus on a more modern technical approach and a select array of ingredients. Delicious game dishes (hare royale, red partridge with stewed cabbage, loin of venison etc) are also on the menu in season. Guests can visit the superb wine cellar, 6m underground, which boasts an outstanding collection of Spanish and French wines. A favourite dish here is the pressed roast duck cooked in its own jus and served two ways (for a minimum of two guests) which has featured on the menu since 1967!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1028;Fusion19;Spain;Muro;Avenida de s'Albufera 23, Muro, 07458, Spain;39.805798;3.1170442;31;false;false;Fusion;Located on one of Muro’s busiest streets, just a stone’s throw from its long beach, Fusion19 reflects the passion of a young chef who, having travelled and working in leading restaurants elsewhere, returned to his native island to put into practice everything that he had learnt. In the modern dining room, with its glass-fronted wine cellar, open-view kitchen and a space in the style of a winter garden, discover fusion cuisine which is based around “ingredients, memories and influences”. Chef Javier Hoebeeck offers a single, extensive tasting menu where fusion takes centre stage, combining Mallorcan and Mediterranean cuisine with that of Asia and Latin America. The focus is on ingredients sourced from the island and over 150 “elaborations” split into 5 large stages and steps (Origin, Influences, Memory, Product and Closure) that offer a global adventure for the palate.;Air conditioning;[]
1029;Elkano;Spain;Getaria;Herrerieta 2, Getaria, 20808, Spain;43.3030043;-2.2049087;29;true;true;Seafood, Grills;There are some people who think that grilling over a wood fire is something akin to cooking in prehistoric times! In Getaria, this tradition does not quite go back this far, but historical documents exist that show that this type of cooking is part of its gastronomic heritage. To fully understand this restaurant, we must mention Aitor Arregi, as well as the first Elkano opened by his father, and, of course, what they refer to here as its “culinary landscape”. Elkano perpetuates the values of a restaurant that is indelibly linked to the sea and those in the fishing industry who work every day to supply it with the best catch. This is without doubt one of the culinary temples of wood-fired cooking in which there is little requirement to overwork textures or flavours. The control of the grilling process is total, as is the choice of ingredients and the method of cooking. Fish stands out here, such as the legendary turbot, but you’ll also find an impressive choice of meat dishes. The superb dining room service works like a Swiss watch!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1030;Aürt;Spain;Barcelona;Paseo del Taulat 262-264, Barcelona, 08019, Spain;41.4089295;2.217281;53;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the lobby of the Hilton Diagonal Mar Barcelona hotel, Aürt will definitely leave a lasting impression on its guests, in a dining space where the philosophy is summed up a single statement: “I prefer thoughtful simplicity to forced complexity”. Here, chef Artur Martínez is breaking the culinary mould with his perception of gastronomy which involves “cooking that is straightforward but not simple”, with a complete focus on local ingredients, individual connections with producers and the raison d’être of each dish explained personally by Aürt’s cooks on islands that double as tables. The experience, which starts with an appreciation of limited-production Becaruda olive oil from centuries-old trees, is centred around locally sourced ingredients, such as white alubia beans from Ganxet, prawns from Palamós, Ripollesa lamb, and pork from Gascon pigs reared in the Solsonès region. Dishes here reinterpret traditional concepts through the pairing of contemporary techniques with seasonal produce and ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
1031;El Retiro;Spain;Llanes;Carretera Pancar, Llanes, 33500, Spain;43.4123756;-4.7621095;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This traditional, family-run restaurant in the small town of Llanes has definitely moved with the times, given that the original “chingre” founded by chef Ricardo González Sotres’ grandparents now boasts a look that combines modernity, rusticity and authenticity - an aesthetic enhanced by its natural rock walls. The gastronomic focus is clear here: contemporary Asturian cooking with a focus on technique and creativity, a respect for local ingredients, plus a strong desire to please the palate. Choose between delicious dishes on the à la carte (the grilled pigeon is a particular highlight) and two mouthwatering tasting menus: one, the traditionally inspired Pancar, the second, the more gastronomically focused San Patricio, which takes its name from the local chapel in Pancar and the famous holm oak (over 300 years old) that stands at the entrance to it.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1032;El Serbal;Spain;Santander;Avenida de Manuel García Lago 1, Santander, 39005, Spain;43.4776869;-3.7881718;68;true;false;Modern Cuisine;If a dining experience with picture-postcard views of the sea appeals to you, head to Sardinero beach where, on the first floor of the building known as Cormorán, you’ll find El Serbal. You’ll fall for all its culinary charms thanks to its honest approach and its roots in Cantabrian cooking, which is showcased here by an updated take on traditional cuisine that meets one of its key tenets: “to ensure that guests are happy and will want to return”. The à la carte, which is well complemented by three menus (Gastronomic, Tasting and a special Dom Perignon Moët Chandon option), champions the Cantabrian Sea’s superb fish that it buys daily at auction, hence the recital of available options at your table (on our latest visit we particularly enjoyed the mackerel with parsnip and salmis) and a desire to give greater visibility to native ingredients, with a special focus on mouthwatering meat from the Tudanca breed of cattle. On the ground floor you’ll find a more informal bistro-style space called Querida Mar.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1033;Aleia;Spain;Barcelona;Paseo de Gràcia 132, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3979938;2.1580032;59;true;true;Creative;At Aleia, enjoy a fascinating experience that you’ll rarely find elsewhere, thanks to its combination of fine dining and architecture, and a location on the first floor of the famous Casa Fuster (nowadays the Hotel Casa Fuster), a jewel of Catalan Modernism designed in the early 20C by Lluís Domènech i Montaner. In its bright dining room, with large columns flanking its stunning windows and an extraordinary undulating ceiling that is reminiscent of the titanium panels adorning the Guggenheim Museum in Bilbao, savour a single tasting menu with a creative and contemporary vision and a wine-pairing option. Under the guidance of award-winning Paulo Airaudo (from the Amelia by Paulo Airaudo restaurant in Donostia-San Sebastián), Jerez-born chef Rafa de Bedoya showcases consistency and flavour with its foundation in locally sourced seasonal ingredients. We particularly enjoyed the incredible appetisers and the beef fillet with “patates pebrots”. An excellent choice of wines by the glass is also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1034;Quirat;Spain;Barcelona;Avenida de Rius I Taulet 1, Barcelona, 08004, Spain;41.3729244;2.154929;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The gourmet restaurant at the Intercontinental Barcelona is another example of a hotel keen to diversify its services for guests by transforming itself into a foodie destination in its own right. Quirat, which has its own independent entrance (as well as access via the lobby), represents, in its own words, “the purity and wealth of the elements that form the land”. Chef Víctor Torres, who is renowned for his cuisine at the Michelin-starred Les Magnòlies in Arbúcies, creates contemporary Catalan cuisine that always showcases locally sourced ingredients while at the same time fully respecting seasonality. Dishes here are full of depth and flavour, with simplicity only evident in their sauces and reductions. Highlights on the menu include oyster with macadamia “ajoblanco” and pickled grape, Puy lentils with grilled red prawn, and duck magret with coffee, salsify and Melanosporum truffle – dishes that Víctor Torres views as tiny jewels, hence the naming of his menus 18K and 24K. The hotel even has its own kitchen garden!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1035;Kiro Sushi;Spain;Logrono;Emilia Pardo Bazán 5, Logrono, 26009, Spain;42.4747461;-2.4505514;85;true;true;Japanese;Kiro translates as “homeward journey” and as such symbolises what this restaurant means to Félix Jiménez who, dressed in his spotless white kimono, demonstrates the full array of skills he acquired in Japan. There, under the tutelage of maestro Yoshikawa Takamasa, he discovered the Edomae technique of preparing sushi, its tradition, the mystical meaning of its rules, and the secrets of Koshihikari rice… to create the perfect nigiri you need to remain faithful to the time-honoured Shokunin philosophy. These new premises are already a place of culinary pilgrimage given that behind the front door (which is over 300 years old), the dining experience is a ritual reserved for just six guests who eat at the counter. Here, the senses are transported to a new state of consciousness in order to savour everything on the exclusive menu, which is based around sushi but with lots of different mini grilled and smoked fish dishes. No alcohol is served here, just water and tea.;Air conditioning;[]
1037;Casa Bernardi;Spain;Benissa;Partida Pedramala 60C, Benissa, 03720, Spain;38.6917839;0.0785022;27;true;false;Italian Contemporary;If you’re looking for a pleasant place to dine in the Marina Alta area, this restaurant will make you feel very special. Run by Ferdinando Bernardi, a chef with lots of talent originally from Rimini in Italy, Casa Bernardi defines itself as “a place where “italianità” (true Italian hospitality) is all around you”. Located next to the road in an elevated setting within a residential district, it specialises in contemporary Italian cuisine with a strong focus on meticulous preparation, including perfectly al dente pasta and delicious Mediterranean dishes (we particularly enjoyed the squid ink lasagne and the spaghetti carbonara) that always showcase ingredients sourced from the Alicante region and close links with local suppliers. Choose between a concise à la carte (lunchtime only) and three tasting menus: Terra (vegetarian), Pasta Lovers and A Modo Mio. The attractive sea-view terrace is an added bonus!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1038;Malena;Spain;Gimenells;Carretera de Sucs, Gimenells, 25112, Spain;41.6563324;0.3896166;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This family-run restaurant occupies an old farm on the outskirts of Gimenells, where it works alongside the Institute for Food Research and Technology to promote the region’s locally grown produce. Features here include an attractive glass-fronted wine cellar, open kitchen, contemporary dining room, plus a pleasant private space with an open fire. The chef, Xixo Castaño, creates traditionally based modern cuisine that is showcased on two menus (De la Pizarra and Q), plus an à la carte that features dishes from both. He likes to start proceedings with a tasting of olive oils on different home-made breads followed by his superb grilled dishes (one of his strong suits) – he has even designed a technology that enables ingredients to absorb the generous aromas from the embers through the use of steam.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1039;Slow & Low;Spain;Barcelona;Comte Borrell 119, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3805322;2.1584002;66;false;false;World Cuisine, Contemporary;A restaurant with a modern ambience in which the equal measures of technical skill, creativity and delicate touches shown in its dishes will surprise and excite guests. Located closed to the Modernist-style Sant Antoni market, Slow & Low has a concept based around its open kitchen, with two counters that enable guests to experience the creative process to the full. Its internationally inspired cuisine combines ingredients from around the world on three menus that differ only in the number of courses on offer (SLOW, SLOW&LOW and SLOW&LONG), which show clear Mexican influence as well as a nod to Spanish, Argentinian and even Thai cuisine. Fish and vegetarian recipes also feature prominently. One surprise aspect of the longer tasting menu is the presentation, including a small seafood box similar to that found at a fish auction and similarly displayed with ice and seaweed decoration. The table service is shared by the chefs and waiting staff, who explain each dish in detail.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1040;Silabario;Spain;Vigo;Príncipe 44, Vigo, 36202, Spain;42.2365448;-8.7220674;61;true;false;Contemporary;A restaurant that is well worth a visit thanks to its highly skilled cuisine and its unique sixth floor location, beneath an audacious avant-garde steel-framed dome featuring no fewer than 154 triangular panes of glass that crowns the headquarters of the Real Club Celta de Vigo. Here, locally born chef Alberto González, who for several years had a Michelin star at the Silabario restaurant he ran in Tui (Pontevedra), focuses on the new style of Galician cooking that respects tradition, albeit from a more contemporary viewpoint, building his dishes around the quality of their ingredients. His à la carte (which also includes “media ración” options) is complemented by his weekday Berbés “market” menu (one of the least expensive set menus you’ll find in any Michelin-starred restaurant in Europe) and three tasting menus: Tempo (which respects the natural cycle of nature), Raíces (an insight into traditional Galician recipes), and Solaina (which celebrates its sun-blessed setting, and uses exclusive ingredients such as seafood, lamprey and eel).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1041;Fierro;Spain;Valencia;Doctor Serrano 4, Valencia, 46006, Spain;39.4625709;-0.3726653;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;With a culinary tradition dating back over half a century, this restaurant located just a few metres from the Ruzafa market is renowned for its fresh take on day-to-day tastes that will come as a pleasant surprise. The attentive couple at the helm in the kitchen, Germán Carrizo and Carito Lourenço, are the first to acknowledge that their dreams have well and truly come true in this small restaurant which allows them to enjoy the freedom to combine what they learned when working within the Quique Dacosta group with the culinary roots of Carito’s native Argentina (although don’t be surprised to also find inspiration from Spain and Italy here). Their cuisine is focused on two tasting menus (Evocación and Emoción), both with different wine-pairing options, and a 100% vegetarian version (it’s best to request this when you make your booking), the central theme of which is the Mediterranean and their own personal objective: “the construction of the taste memory of the future”. Guests can also savour a few seasonal extras such as truffles, caviar, artisanal cheeses etc!;Air conditioning;[]
1043;Villa Retiro;Spain;Xerta;Dels Molins 2, Xerta, 43592, Spain;40.9116908;0.4898701;87;false;true;Creative, Traditional Cuisine;Embark on a magical journey full of flavour across the Baix Ebre (Lower Ebro) region. Located in a stunning yet undiscovered area, this restaurant occupies charming former stables (nowadays redecorated in a more contemporary style) in the Spanish colonial-style Villa Retiro resort, which occupies buildings dating back to 1890. Here, chef Fran López continues to find inspiration in the natural bounty of the Ebro delta. On his menus (Clásico, Homenaje, and Más que un Homenaje), he offers traditional and creative market-inspired cooking, finger food and snacks teeming with local flavour (featuring the delta’s famous rice and its poultry, fish, shellfish, seaweed, aromatic herbs etc). An added bonus is the explanation of each dish by the team in the dining room. In addition, all the starters (such as the oysters with “aged” tomatoes, celery gel and pickled celery) are served on an iron plate that represents a map of the region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
1044;As Garzas;Spain;Barizo;Porto Barizo 40, Barizo, 15113, Spain;43.3213756;-8.8719851;57;false;false;Galician;In a remote Atlantic location at the heart of the Costa da Morte, this restaurant is impeccably run by chef Fernando Agrasar, who works here alongside his wife (who runs the front of house), his eldest son (in charge of bread and desserts) and Eva Fares, head chef and the partner of one of their children. The gourmet cuisine on offer is showcased on a tasting menu built around seasonal ingredients which highlights in a contemporary way Galicia’s gastronomic bounty (we particularly enjoyed the red mullet with a seaweed pil-pil and teardrop peas from Coristanco), as well as an à la carte menu featuring time-honoured classics, daily fish specials, savoury rice options etc. Every table boasts a stunning vista, although we recommend that you book those closer to the picture windows in order to get an even better view of the cliffs and the swell of the ocean from this property that the chef romantically refers to as his refuge at the end of the world. Garzas also has a handful of attractive rooms for guests wishing to stay the night.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
1045;Cal Paradís;Spain;Vall d'Alba;Avenida Vilafranca 30, Vall d'Alba, 12194, Spain;40.1767144;-0.0339761;86;false;false;Contemporary;A wonderful example of an honest, highly dedicated chef who also trained as a teacher, and who has been rewarded with a Michelin star. Miguel Barrera, who grew up surrounded by pots and pans in the family restaurant (El Paraíso), fulfilled his parents dream by becoming a teacher but was unable to ignore his own instincts, hence his decision to train as a chef before returning home. Following a period working with his family to provide a sense of continuity, he took over the reins of the restaurant, gave it a new name and carried out changes across the board. Today, he wins over his customers with his contemporary cuisine full of flavour which remains faithful to his Castellón roots, his memories, and to zero-mile ingredients, in many cases grown in his own garden. Centred around three tasting menus (Tradición, Gastromercat and Miguel Barrera), his cuisine features dishes that never disappoint, such as the tomatoes “de penjar” with whole sardines and grilled garlic, and some delicious rice options.;Air conditioning;[]
1046;Moments;Spain;Barcelona;Passeig de Gràcia 38-40, Barcelona, 08007, Spain;41.3911693;2.1664829;28;false;true;Creative;The fine-dining restaurant at the Mandarin Oriental Barcelona hotel is run by Raül Balam, son of the legendary chef Carme Ruscalleda. In addition to his own undeniable individual talent, you’ll note several culinary traits he has inherited from his mother. Dominated by amber and gold tones, the modern dining space also features a window through which it’s possible to watch the team at work in the kitchen. The cuisine here showcases the underlying creativity of Catalan tradition, healthy Mediterranean produce, and the intrinsic distinctiveness of each flavour... all brought together in a special Els Moments menu that takes guests on a journey across the eleven themed menus served at the restaurant over its 15-year history and showcases epic signature dishes such as the tartlet of creamy caviar and quail eggs, the creamy rice with prawns “in the style of fishermen from Sant Pol”, and the vegetarian ceviche with corn textures.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1047;Marc Fosh;Spain;Palma;De la Missió 7, Palma, 07003, Spain;39.5735982;2.6513729;73;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Although tucked away along a narrow street in the historic quarter of the city, this restaurant (part of a 17C seminary that has been superbly converted into the Convent de la Missió hotel) comes as a delightful surprise. In its meticulous modern interior, featuring brightly lit spaces with a minimalist feel and a pleasant patio-terrace, discover the cuisine of Marc Fosh, the first British chef to be awarded a Michelin star on Spanish soil. His cooking brings together flavour, technique and creativity and highlights, through simply constructed yet sophisticated combinations, the seasonal Mediterranean ingredients that he fell in love with when he first came to the island (nowadays, most of these are sourced from the restaurant’s farm on the Finca Son Mir or through its collaboration with small-scale local producers). Choose between several excellent menus: one available for lunch midweek, and two tasting-style options – Marc and Aromas del Mediterráneo (available for dinner only).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1048;La Aquarela;Spain;Patalavaca;Barranco de la Verga, Patalavaca, 35129, Spain;27.7744701;-15.6930938;91;false;false;Creative;Despite its somewhat unusual location in an apartment complex along the Playa de Patalavaca in the southern part of Gran Canaria, La Aquarela has become one of the leading names on the island’s restaurant scene. To a welcoming and hushed backdrop of classic decor and romantic tables (those overlooking the swimming pool are perfect for enjoying the sunset), savour delicate, highly technical dishes with lots of flavour and a strong connection to the local area, but with their own personality, as demonstrated by the occasional Nordic touch (chef Germán Ortega spent several years working in Stockholm). Up to 85% of its ingredients are locally sourced and are showcased in modern Canary Island dishes on three menus: Experiencia (combining the sea and the land), Tierra (vegetarian) and Fish Lovers (with an obvious focus on fish and seafood from the Atlantic waters around the islands).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1049;La Boscana;Spain;Bellvís;Carretera Bell-lloc d'Urgell, Bellvís, 25142, Spain;41.66112;0.8093196;33;true;true;Creative;If you’re looking for a special restaurant, La Boscana offers a culinary experience enhanced by its natural setting, with glass-fronted buildings overlooking pretty gardens, leafy groves and an idyllic lake, making this one of the most romantic places to eat in Spain! In its elegant dining room, bathed in natural light and embellished with designer details, enjoy innovative cuisine from Joël Castanyé that has a strong emphasis on detail, both in terms of technique and presentation. Through his menus (usually one concise menu and a second, more extensive, seasonal option), the chef skilfully reworks the flavours of Lérida as he searches for the perfect symbiosis between his savoury dishes and the fruits that enhance them, the latter sourced from various fruit farms in the local area as well as from his own garden. His delicious pork and apple tartlet pays homage to two of Lérida’s most iconic ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1050;Raúl Resino;Spain;Benicarló;Alacant 2, Benicarló, 12580, Spain;40.4221851;0.4293978;92;true;true;Creative;Raúl Resino, who is known as the fisherman-chef, signals his philosophy in a single sentence: “I cook as I think, I don’t think how I’m going to cook”.His creative cooking showcases a constant desire to move forward, hence his nod to Japanese cuisine and, above all, a strong focus on fish, seafood, rice and ingredients from nearby market gardens. He is also a great advocate of locally sourced ingredients and often heads out to catch his own fish. His cuisine (a single tasting menu called “Rancho Marinero de Pescadores”) is centred around the biodiversity of Castellón’s Mediterranean shoreline and recipes that local fishermen traditionally prepare on their boats. His particular dream is for more humble and lesser-known fish that don’t always make it to auction to become better known to the general public.;Air conditioning;[]
1052;Mu•na;Spain;Ponferrada;Gil y Carrasco 25, Ponferrada, 24401, Spain;42.5434;-6.59309;88;true;false;Fusion, Japanese Contemporary;Occupying the Casa de Las Bombas, opposite the Castillo de los Templarios, Mu•na’s Arabic name (meaning “desire”) alludes to its desire to satisfy our appetite and our tastebuds. Here, owner-chef Samuel Naveira works with both passion and enthusiasm in this contemporary setting where the decorative ants embellishing the walls are somewhat unusual but are a metaphor for the hard work and effort of the entire team. His cuisine, which he showcases on a single, highly original tasting menu (A Journey to Japan) introduces us to cuisine that plays with a fusion from around the globe while extolling the virtues of the Bierzo region’s seasonal ingredients. The latter have always been the cornerstone of his culinary message, albeit from the perspective of Japanese techniques and recipes (wild boar and apple yakitori, “Berciano” ramen, “botillo” ningo-yaki, “Aquanaria sea bass on the island of Shikoku” etc). The chef is so proud of his Michelin star that he has had it tattooed on his wrist!;Wheelchair access;[]
1054;Etxebarri;Spain;Axpe;Plaza San Juan 1, Axpe, 48291, Spain;43.1143511;-2.5974397;62;true;true;Grills;Food-lovers flock to this temple of cuisine like pilgrims to a religious shrine in order to unearth the secrets of flame-grilled cooking that have been mastered by Etxebarri’s owner-chef Bittor Arginzoniz, the life and soul of this restaurant, who invested everything in his dream here.His particular vision for life and for work resulted in him restoring this 18C country house in his home village, Axpe-Atxondo, at the foot of Mt Anboto. His unique cuisine focuses on top-quality grilled dishes using different types of wood (holm oak, vine shoots, oak from old barrels etc), utensils he invented himself, and an unusual system of pulleys that enables him to control the cooking process. We strongly recommend booking a minimum of two months ahead because of the huge waiting list to eat here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1055;Alkimia;Spain;Barcelona;Ronda San Antoni 41 - Principal, Barcelona, 08011, Spain;41.3826841;2.1635878;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Alkimia has a somewhat surprising location inside the Moritz beer factory, which has been redesigned as a gourmet complex. Once you’ve rung the bell to get in, you’ll find two different spaces (the bistro-style Alkostat and the Alkimia restaurant itself, in front of the kitchen), both featuring attractive designer details, avant-garde references to the marine world, alongside reclaimed classical furnishings that recall the interiors of Barcelona’s former aristocratic mansions (for which the architectural company External Reference was awarded top place for best design at the prestigious 2017 SBID Awards). In the gastronomic dining room, chef Jordi Vilà conjures up fresh, contemporary cuisine which is deeply rooted in Catalan tradition and has a strong focus on fish. He offers just a single tasting menu (Alkimia), although during the hunting season guests can pre-order a second game-inspired menu (Salvaje).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1056;Yayo Daporta;Spain;Cambados;Hospital 7, Cambados, 36630, Spain;42.5128612;-8.8148041;94;true;false;Creative;For those keen to experience the flavours of the Atlantic to the full, it’s hard to find a better place than this. Here, chef Yayo Daporta describes his cuisine as “based on common sense and the best possible taste”. What is certain is that there’s much more than this to his cuisine, which reinterprets Galician cooking, bringing it up to date in a way that takes it to another level. The sea takes pride of place with mussels, cockles, barnacles, seaweed and simply cooked razor clams all featuring in this attractive restaurant occupying a stone building that was once a royal hospital dating back to the 18C. The chef’s menus (Degustación and Gran Menú Yayo Daporta) demonstrate his unwavering loyalty to his local surroundings, with a focus on ingredients from the coast around Cambados and his own kitchen gardens (one in his own restaurant, the other in his Pazo A Capitana property). Make sure you visit the wine cellar managed by his wife, Esther Daporta, which guests can explore to choose their own wines!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1057;Mina;Spain;Bilbao;Muelle Marzana, Bilbao, 48003, Spain;43.2550491;-2.9248606;35;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Bilbao is not an easy place in which to make a name for yourself when it comes to food, however it is here that chef Álvaro Garrido decided to set up shop in a discreet building along the estuary, opposite the Ribera market. The pleasantly surprising interior decor of this restaurant, which owes its name to a former mine entrance that once existed beneath the building, features an open kitchen and a fusion of stone and wood (the bar is a single piece of oak) that combine with cutting-edge designer detail. Ably supported by his wife Lara Martín, the chef conjures up innovative cuisine with a hint of fusion influence on a single tasting menu (choose between a shorter and longer version). The cuisine is overtly seasonal, championing ingredients sourced from local suppliers, something that is strongly visible in dishes such as the seasonal tuna with codium or the delicious cod tripe with a smoked salsa and oyster mushroom. Take a seat at the counter to watch the chefs hard at work.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1058;Angle;Spain;Barcelona;Aragó 214, Barcelona, 08011, Spain;41.3882671;2.1597015;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located inside the Hotel Cram, but with a separate entrance, Angle is overseen by celebrity chef Jordi Cruz. Here, guests can enjoy an aperitif and appetisers in the foyer before heading up to the dining room on the first floor, a contemporary space that exudes elegance and serenity with its striking floor lamps, wooden fixtures and fittings and heavy curtains. In the kitchen, the award-winning chef’s modern, creative blueprint is followed to the letter without any unnecessary fuss, but with great care and attention and a sense of freedom. Based around market-inspired ingredients, the cuisine is showcased on a tasting menu that features dishes from the three-starred ABaC alongside others conceived in-house. However, everything is in keeping with the restaurant's mission to create “haute cuisine for everyday consumption”. We strongly advise saving space for the dessert menu, with its vast array of textures and flavours.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1059;Ama;Spain;Tolosa;Martín José Iraola 4, Tolosa, 20400, Spain;43.1322758;-2.0776318;18;false;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;With its mantra of “what is local protects us”, this spacious, comfortable yet unpretentious restaurant with a glass-fronted kitchen focuses on contemporary cooking which works with just a few ingredients to bring out the essence of every individual flavour. The team here views gastronomy as an opportunity to adapt traditional home-style cooking to a modern audience without the need to over-complicate, so that we enjoy good food through the use of the best seasonal ingredients sourced from trusted local suppliers. Chefs Gorka and Javier showcase their skills on a tasting menu (which can be extended by adding two extra dishes) that changes week by week in line with the availability of local ingredients from Tolosa and its region. During the game season, guests can enjoy unique meats such as Sagardoz venison. Don’t leave without trying Ama’s exquisite cheesecake!;Air conditioning;[]
1061;VelascoAbellà;Spain;Madrid;Víctor Andrés Belaúnde 25, Madrid, 28016, Spain;40.4559644;-3.6797233;19;true;true;Farm to table;Chef Óscar Velasco, ably supported by second in command and dessert maestro Montse Abellà, is back! Here, the couple, who view this challenge as a ”lifelong project”, focus on cooking that is close to Óscar’s heart and always showcases contemporary market-inspired cuisine that champions seasonal ingredients yet with a little more freedom than in his previous projects, while at the same time demonstrating equal levels of technique and elegance. The à la carte, featuring dishes such as white prawns “al ajillo” with fried egg and potatoes (which finds its way on to the menu at the insistence of his son), is complemented by an impressive tasting menu, although there’s also the option of ordering half-plates. In addition to the bright dining room, a separate space called El Apartamento (with its own kitchen) is also available for private dining. On the menu, it was a pleasant surprise to find iconic dishes from his successful stint at the helm of the erstwhile Santceloni, such as the legendary smoked ricotta ravioli with Paris 1925 Oscietra caviar.;Counter dining;[]
1062;Dos Palillos;Spain;Barcelona;Elisabets 9, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3833692;2.1686733;65;false;false;Fusion;In this bustling restaurant, where the closeness of the tables is more reminiscent of Asian restaurants, discover a tapas concept that has been taken to another level, hence its view that “tapas are not just a way of eating, but a philosophy for life”. Located just a few steps from Barcelona’s Museu d’Art Contemporani, Dos Palillos has a simple sake bar by the entrance, where you can eat without booking ahead, and a second more gastronomic U-shaped counter around an open kitchen, enabling guests to observe the full preparation process. At this second more attractive and elegant space, you can savour a particularly interesting surprise tasting menu – a fun fusion between Asian cooking (predominantly from Japan) and Iberian ingredients (including superb Galician seafood). The type of dishes that you’ll find on the menu include Japanese pil-pil “cocochas”, cold chicken pho, and chicken korma curry with baby lamb and mango pickle. The menu here changes daily.;Air conditioning;[]
1063;Béns d'Avall;Spain;Sóller;Urbanización Costa de Deià, Sóller, 07100, Spain;39.7766578;2.6665427;68;false;false;Contemporary;It’s not an easy task to find a family-run restaurant where everything slots together perfectly, but the combination of a pleasant ambience, cuisine based around select ingredients, and truly magical views of the Mediterranean and its coastline from its unique clifftop setting do just that at this eatery that has now celebrated its golden wedding. The secret to its success? The family’s motto of always doing things well.br>Here, the skill and knowledge of two generations have come together through the father and son duo of Benet and Jaume Vicens who extol the virtues of Mallorcan cooking but with a more contemporary, delicate and original approach alongside impressive technique, which reaches its full expression on the tasting menu. Make sure you book a table on the terrace to enjoy the spectacular sunset!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1065;Terra;Spain;Fisterra;Paseo Da Ribeira 65, Fisterra, 15155, Spain;42.9048181;-9.2623603;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Part of the region near La Coruña known as the Coast of Death, Fisterra has reinvigorated its culinary options thanks to this restaurant occupying a former bar overlooking Da Ribeira beach. Having trained in award-winning restaurants such as Casa Marcial (La Salgar, in the Asturias region) and Mina (Bilbao), young chef Brais Pichel has returned home to take his turn at the helm of the family business, transforming it into a contemporary space with a highly consistent culinary approach in the kitchen. Just a single tasting menu is on offer here, one which is modern in approach, changes almost daily, and showcases the labours of local producers, with fish featuring prominently. The cuisine will definitely leave a lasting impression thanks to the delicious and subtle dishes with a constant focus on the local area. The miniscule wine list is also a welcome surprise, with its emphasis on single-varietal, unfiltered natural wines from small-scale local producers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1066;Erre de Roca;Spain;Miranda de Ebro;Ronda del Ferrocarril 37, Miranda de Ebro, 09200, Spain;42.6876564;-2.9469716;56;true;false;Contemporary;When chefs have clear ideas and work with complete dedication, restaurants such as these, where guests can enjoy cuisine to the full, are the end result. Deeply connected to his native Miranda de Ebro, chef Alberto Molinero (who has other restaurants here and in Madrid), aims to create cuisine that delivers impact on every level with strong techniques and plenty of flavour yet without neglecting aesthetics, thanks to dishes that are contemporary in style and meticulous in presentation. In this elegantly informal space with a completely open kitchen, he offers guests a choice of three menus: one “executive” Mercado option (available at lunchtime from Wednesday to Friday only), and two more extensive tastings menus (Erre de Roca and the seasonally inspired De Temporada). One dish that particularly fascinated us was his elegant version of Segovia-style roast suckling pig, to which he adds eel fillets from Miranda de Ebro that were a surprising yet perfect combination.;Air conditioning;[]
1067;Andra Mari;Spain;Galdakao;Barrio Elexalde 22, Galdakao, 48960, Spain;43.2343555;-2.8325069;31;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;This restaurant was established by the Asúa family in its own farmhouse. The initial idea behind it was to provide a place to rest and sustenance for pilgrims visiting the nearby 13C Andra Mari church, hence its name. This stunning building boasting superb views of the Ibaizábal river valley features a wine cellar in the basement which can be visited by guests, a bar area for a pre-dinner drink, and two dining rooms decorated in a rustic-regional style, both of which benefit from lovely views. The cuisine on its à la carte and tasting menus (Elexalde and Andra Mari) is firmly focused on the rural and maritime roots of Vizcaya and a modern reinterpretation of traditional Basque flavours, but always based around the very best seasonal ingredients and a continual connection with small-scale local producers. One of the classic dishes that we really enjoyed was the hake served with a salsa verde.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
1068;Arrels;Spain;Sagunt;Castillo 18, Sagunt, 46500, Spain;39.6786129;-0.2781263;71;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;If you were planning a trip to Sagunt to discover its impressive heritage (castle, Roman theatre, Jewish quarter etc), there’s no excuse for not doing so, given that the town is also home to a gastronomic restaurant that is well worth a visit.This delightful eatery, occupying the former stables of the 16C Palacio de los Duques de Gaeta, features imposing stone arches that provide the backdrop for contemporary cuisine with a strong Mediterranean influence. Chef Vicky Sevilla, a young cook with lots of determination (she opened the restaurant when she was just 25), showcases modern, personal cooking with a strong connection to the local area (in the Valencian language, Arrels translates as “roots”) which can be savoured on her exquisite tasting menus featuring delicate dishes with finely texted sauces.;Air conditioning;[]
1069;Ferpel Gastronómico;Spain;Ortiguera;Coaña, Ortiguera, 33716, Spain;43.5592015;-6.7450058;17;false;false;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;If you’re on the lookout for a restaurant that will provide plenty of interesting surprises, it’s well worth heading to Ferpel, where the simple approach to local ingredients results in strong individual flavours in every dish. Local chef Elio Fernández is fully committed to his rural surroundings and his family, the two pillars upon which his work is based, creating contemporary cooking with its roots in the soil of the Asturias region. The experience starts with appetisers in the pastry section, where bread is baked every morning, and continues in the kitchen, where you’re served by the owner-chef himself. And then it’s on to the dining room upstairs, with its stunning views, where you can savour dishes on his two menus (Clásico and A Figueira). Popular ingredients in the kitchen here include grey mullet, oysters from the Eo estuary, sea urchin, and traditionally produced sausages from the San Lorenzo company.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1070;Eneko;Spain;Larrabetzu;Legina Auzoa, Larrabetzu, 48195, Spain;43.26056;-2.8142767;57;false;true;Creative;This homage to chef Eneko Atxa’s origins has a surprising location above the Gorka Izagirre txacoli wine cellar, in the same premises previously occupied by the three-Michelin-star Azurmendi restaurant, which is nowadays just a few metres away. In the dining room, the layout breaks the traditional mould with its open-view kitchens, and provides the backdrop for innovative dishes that remain faithful to Basque tradition while at the same time demonstrating the chef’s philosophy: “The artisan’s hands sculpt emotions”. The single tasting menu on offer here (called Sutan, the Basque for “fire”), is contemporary in feel and demonstrates impeccable technical skill and a whole array of flavours in signature dishes such as the oxtail ravioli with vegetable broth, which showcases a marvellous array of textures. If you would like a more extensive experience, why not book a pre-meal visit of the wine cellar along with a comprehensive tasting?;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
1071;Teatro kitchen & bar;Spain;Barcelona;Avenida del Paralelo 164, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3751383;2.1567921;25;true;true;Contemporary;A highly original eatery that maintains the essence of the legendary Tickets, but with its own attractive personality. Both its name and its meticulous decor are a nod to the theatres located in the city’s Parallel district, a sensation enhanced by the menu, which is presented almost like the script of a play, and includes the cast of all the cooks and waiters. This provides the backdrop for fun, varied cuisine in the shape of numerous snacks, tapas, a few classic recipes, alongside more innovative dishes. Options here include the possibility of ordering from the à la carte, which is presented in “acts” and “scenes” as if you were attending a theatre performance (Start the Show, The Great Outcome, and The End), as well as two tasting menus: Surprise Show (as part of which the chef chooses dishes based on your individual preferences and tastes) and À la Carte Show (where guests choose the “scenes” they wish to eat). While you’re here, why not enjoy a drink or cocktail in the Backstage bar?;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1072;Andreu Genestra;Spain;Llucmajor;Camí de Sa Torre, Km 8,7, Llucmajor, 07609, Spain;39.4374288;2.8000239;31;false;true;Creative;Chef Andreu Genestra has begun a new, and much more serious, culinary adventure within the walls of the luxurious and aristocratic Hotel Zoëtry in the rural surroundings of the historic Sa Torre estate, which dates back to the 14C and features a windmill and even its own church. In this restaurant, accessed via a beautiful patio that leads to the hotel’s various dining venues, the aim is to create uncomplicated contemporary cooking in tune with its surroundings yet with plenty of creativity. Choose between three extensive menus (one of which is vegetarian) based around a “Mediterranean” concept, although there’s also the option of ordering two or three options à la carte from these menus, with sustainability clearly evident in every dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1073;Atalaya;Spain;Alcossebre;Camí l'Atall 1A, Alcossebre, 12579, Spain;40.2490542;0.2851265;55;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;Located on the ground floor of an apartment block close to the marina, this pleasantly renovated restaurant features a space adjoining the wine cellar for aperitifs and appetisers, three welcoming Mediterranean-style dining rooms, plus a modern open kitchen enabling the team here to interact with guests. Young chefs Alejandra and Emanuel met in the kitchens of award-winning chef Martín Berasategui’s three-Michelin-star eatery in Lasarte-Oria, one of the restaurants which taught them to perfect contemporary techniques and identify the values of haute-cuisine that they were keen to introduce when they set out to realise their own dream together. Here, you’ll find modern, creative cuisine with a strong emphasis on presentation, textures and a skilful combination of ingredients. Take your pick from the three set menus available: Llaüt (lunch midweek), Bergantín and Goleta. Make sure you try the unforgettable Vinaroz king prawns “al ajillo”!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1074;Caelis;Spain;Barcelona;Via Laietana 49, Barcelona, 08003, Spain;41.387015;2.1743763;69;true;true;Creative;The Ohla Barcelona hotel’s fine-dining restaurant boasts an unmistakable appearance, due to the “eyes” or “ocular globes” designed by artist Frederic Amat that adorn its neo-Classical façade. Here, French chef Romain Fornell has introduced his new culinary vision that reinterprets concepts and recipes through cooking that features French-influenced Mediterranean cuisine, seasonal ingredients, identifiable flavours and astute pairings, plus a desire to involve guests in their dining experience. In addition to the different-sized tables in the dining room, you’ll find an open kitchen with bright and shiny copper pans hanging from the ceiling, plus a U-shaped chef’s table for 14 diners. Choose between several interesting tasting menus (Earth & Sea, Celebration and Vegetarian) and two slightly less expensive options at lunchtime. One of Caelis’ signature dishes and a definite must here is the delicious “Surf & Turf” cannelloni with lobster and foie gras.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1075;Mesón Sabor Andaluz;Spain;Alcalá del Valle;La Huerta 3, Alcalá del Valle, 11693, Spain;36.9009424;-5.1687994;36;false;true;Contemporary;Enjoy a high level of cuisine in this restaurant in a small village in the Sierra de Grazalema. This renovated property with a rustic ambience, which has been in business for over 25 years, showcases cuisine that has grown in complexity through dishes that champion traditional cuisine while increasingly finding their inspiration and identity in the local soil. This owes much to its collaboration with small-scale organic food projects (Cultivo Desterrado in Sanlúcar de Barrameda, Extiercol in Cuevas del Becerro etc) that give major prominence to locally grown ingredients such as “Triguero” asparagus and pistachios. The cooking here is concentrated around two superb tasting menus (Celemín and Fanega) that can always be enhanced by dishes that resonate with the family’s culinary “heritage” such as the famous Antoñita’s oxtail stew and the stewed leg of goat with garlic.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1076;Can Jubany;Spain;Calldetenes;Carretera C 25, Calldetenes, 08506, Spain;41.929287;2.301967;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A standout name in Catalan cuisine, both for its setting in a delightful farmhouse and the talent of chef Nandu Jubany, a man with a passion for motorbikes to the point where he has even taken part in the Dakar rally. The entrance to Can Jubany enables guests to admire the adjoining vegetable garden which provides many of its ingredients as well as the kitchen, where the focus is on a balance between tradition and cutting-edge cuisine. The welcoming interior is a pleasant surprise, featuring several rooms with a rustic-contemporary feel, different spaces for a post-dinner drink, plus a chef’s table right by the kitchen. The focus here is on contemporary cooking with its roots in tradition, with dishes built around the finest Catalan ingredients on the à la carte and two menus full of surprises (“A stroll around Catalunya” and “The Great Can Jubany Feast”). Dishes you are likely to encounter include dry rice with sea cucumber and crayfish broth, roasted suckling pig with seasonal garden vegetables, and vanilla brioche rum baba with ice-cream. Everything is delicious, whatever you choose!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1077;Rincón de Diego;Spain;Cambrils;Drassanes 19, Cambrils, 43850, Spain;41.0667735;1.0631489;22;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re on the lookout for a high-quality restaurant close to the beach or marina, there’s no excuse not to eat here, given its location near Regueral beach, just a few steps from the Club Nàutic de Cambrils. The restaurant is split between two floors with a highly contemporary ambience, where guests can savour cuisine by the acclaimed duo of chef Diego Campos, one of the bastions behind the resurgence of local gastronomy, and his son Rubén, who brings a fresh approach including an Asian touch resulting from his travels in Thailand, Singapore, China and Japan. The à la carte here is supported by three menus (Del Cava, Gastronómico and Súmmum). It is pleasantly surprising to see how this updated take on traditional cuisine that includes fish and seafood from Cambrils and sublime local rice dishes (monkfish “suquet”, rice with Mediterranean red lobster etc) combines perfectly with more contemporary-style dishes such as red tuna tartare with dashi, guacamole, and wasabi ice-cream, and Thai sea bass with Jerusalem artichoke purée.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1078;Etxeko Ibiza;Spain;Es Canar;Avenida de Cala Nova, Es Canar, 07840, Spain;39.0066031;1.5808591;45;false;false;Creative;Savour the exquisite gastronomic cuisine of Martín Berasategui on the “Isla Blanca”, as Ibiza is affectionately known to locals.Located within the walls of the luxurious Hotel Bless Ibiza, the restaurant is run by chef Paco Budia, one of Berasategui’s disciples, who loyally follows the culinary doctrines of his San Sebastián mentor in dishes teeming with fine textures and demonstrating impeccable presentation. Martín Berasategui’s stunning cuisine showcases some added Canary Island-inspired touches thanks to the use of an array of locally sourced ingredients alongside others from the north of Spain, all of which feature on an extensive à la carte and one tasting menu (El Viaje de Martín). The name Etxeko (which translates as “homemade” in Basque), is a nod to this famous chef’s native region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1079;Cocinandos;Spain;Leon;Plaza de San Marcos 5, Leon, 24001, Spain;42.6019852;-5.5810161;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of the restaurant, which comes from the Spanish verb “cocinar” (to cook), says it all as Yolanda León and Juanjo Pérez met while working together in different kitchens before they decided to come together to pursue a shared dream. The unexpectedly modern interior of the historic Casa del Peregrino (1750), next to the monumental Parador-Hostal de San Marcos, provides the backdrop for cuisine with an identity that stems from transparency. The creatively inspired cuisine here is centred around two tasting menus (Cocinar León and Gran Menú Cocinandos) which tell a story, are based around the best local ingredients, and evolve weekly in line with the seasons, accompanied by the region’s best wines. To enhance your experience further, enjoy a coffee in the garden, overlooked on one side by the historic San Marcos church and on the other by the city’s concert hall. During the summer months, a “Menú Parrilla”, designed for sharing, is also available in this delightful space.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1080;Rodero;Spain;Pamplona;Emilio Arrieta 3, Pamplona, 31002, Spain;42.8160025;-1.6367286;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s no better way to describe this restaurant than the chef’s assertion that “Rodero is a family and we try to make guests happy through our work, doing things well and with kindness”. Koldo Rodero was practically brought up in a kitchen and as a result recognised his vocation from an early age. His dream, to ensure that flavour is the core principle in his own cooking, is now a reality thanks to his vision of contemporary Navarran cuisine which is highly creative, intelligent and technical, and showcases his superb ability. Alongside his sisters, both of whom are in charge of the dining rooms, he has managed to transform this family business just a few steps from the bullring, so that it moves with the times while retaining the full virtues and flavours of Navarra’s spectacular natural bounty. The à la carte, which features half-“ración” options depending on the number of diners at the table, is complemented by two enticing menus (Para Gustar and Para Degustar). We can highly recommend the fresh squid with “papada” and citrus consommé, and the wild turbot with citrus pil pil and seaweed.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1081;Alameda;Spain;Hondarribia;Minasoroeta 1, Hondarribia, 20280, Spain;43.3612194;-1.7925817;56;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If you’re on the lookout for a restaurant with a true soul and no little history, you’ll find it at Alameda, where the Txapartegi brothers have transformed this restaurant into a must for food-lovers and where they closely follow the wise words of their grandmother Julia: “the shorter the distance between the soil and the stove, the better”. Choose between two distinct and pleasantly renovated dining spaces: the “taberna” and the gastronomic restaurant itself, the latter boasting a classic, rustic decor but with added attractive and modern features. Gorka and Kepa are at the helm in the kitchen, while Mikel performs sommelier and front-of-house duties. On the à la carte and two appetising set menus (Hondarribia and Gartzinea) they highlight deep-rooted Basque cooking from a more contemporary standpoint, creating what they call “Bidasoa cooking”, which is indelibly linked to the Bidasoa-Txingudi area and its locally produced ingredients. We particularly enjoyed the marinated and smoked Bonito del Norte tuna with onions and citrus fruit.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1082;Europa;Spain;Pamplona;Espoz y Mina 11-1°, Pamplona, 31002, Spain;42.8161985;-1.6418103;77;true;true;Contemporary;The Europa restaurant stands in the heart of Pamplona, very close to the Plaza del Castillo and the legendary Calle Estafeta, a world-famous street due to its association with the San Fermín running of the bulls festival. The Idoate Vidaurre family in charge here is almost as well known as the restaurant itself, thanks to its team of siblings for whom the art of hospitality is much more than just a profession. In the kitchen, chef Pilar Idoate creates an updated take on traditional cuisine with strong roots in Basque cooking. This is enhanced by top-quality ingredients that showcase the province of Navarra and which she uses to create superb dishes teeming with the flavour and fine and delicate textures that only come with the finest cuisine. Choose between the extensive, traditionally inspired à la carte, with the choice of ordering half-portions and an impressive array of fish and meat, and two set menus (Eugenia and Degustación), both with a wine-pairing option. Whatever you decide, you will be able to appreciate the full splendour and values of this restaurant that has held an esteemed Michelin star since 1993.;Air conditioning;[]
1083;Peix & Brases;Spain;Dénia;Plaza de Benidorm 18, Dénia, 03700, Spain;38.8460357;0.1079727;62;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Many are of the opinion that without tradition there is no modernity and Peix & Brases is no exception. Working from this basic premise, it builds its philosophy around both, as well as a focus on top-notch ingredients. Located almost in front of the port, with the sound of seagulls as a backdrop, Peix & Brases has two distinct ambiences: the gastro-bar on the ground floor serving more informal fusion-style dishes that it calls Mediterrasian, and its gastronomic dining room on the first floor, with access to an attractive rooftop terrace. Here, the extensive à la carte of traditional Mediterranean cooking is heavily focused towards the open grill, along with savoury rice dishes and top-quality, fresh seasonal ingredients. This is complemented by two further menus with a more gastronomic feel (Esencia and Degustación) and a strong focus on presentation.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1084;Ancestral;Spain;Illescas;Víctor Hugo 2, Illescas, 45200, Spain;40.1286157;-3.844914;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The undoubted stars of the show at Ancestral are fire and smoke! To a backdrop of contemporary-industrial decor and stunning lighting, and with lots of success behind him in other restaurants despite his young age, chef Víctor Infantes showcases his strong passion for cooking. His two tasting menus (Origen and Silvestre) change in line with market availability and always champion the produce and flavours of La Mancha from a modern perspective, converting humble ingredients into haute-cuisine dishes (including some surprising smoke-infused touches) but without renouncing time-honoured ancestral cooking techniques (hence the restaurant’s name). Highlights on the menu include the traditional “escabeche”, the Las Pedroñeras garlic soup served in a clay pot, the textured D.O.P La Mancha onion, and the wild duck with smoked butter, which is finished on the grill with a duxelle of wild mushrooms and a spicy fig compote.;Air conditioning;[]
1085;Bagá;Spain;Jaén;Reja de la Capilla 3, Jaén, 23001, Spain;37.7668005;-3.7861942;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;By adhering to the motto Sentir Jaén (Feel Jaén), clearly visible in the diminutive kitchen, this culinary jewel continues to realise its dream, in so doing become a must for experienced foodies.Despite its compact size, this restaurant, which takes its name from the blossom of the olive tree, boasts impressive designer detail in its decor and reflects chef Pedro Sánchez’s passion for seasonal local ingredients. These are showcased on a single tasting menu that speaks volumes for the enormous talent of this chef, who continually champions the bounty of his native region. Signature dishes here include the pumpkin fritters (buñuelos de carrueco) and the exquisite Quisquillas de Motril (local shrimp) with a partridge escabeche – a surf and turf dish that will linger long in the memory. Booking ahead is recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1086;Divinum;Spain;Girona;Albereda 7, Girona, 17004, Spain;41.9822044;2.8240743;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In this modern and contemporary restaurant, the standout qualities are the constant attentive service provided by the owners and the extraordinary quality of ingredients used. The cooking here, which is modern but with an eye on the past, aims to offer as many options as possible, hence the possibility of half-portions for dishes on the à la carte and the choice of two tasting menus (Petit and Essencia). Standout dishes include the superb seasonal Maresme peas (which are mixed with a pil-pil broth, cod tripe and truffle shavings), the texture and aroma of which were a delight, and Divinum’s version of “escalivada”, a very typical dish that has been completely transformed and deconstructed and includes an original sweet touch. The excellent cheese trolley features over 20 different varieties.;Air conditioning;[]
1087;Solla;Spain;San Salvador de Poio;Avenida Sineiro 7, San Salvador de Poio, 36005, Spain;42.4334655;-8.6686035;74;true;true;Creative, Seafood;Anyone who has grown up in the kitchen of a family-run restaurant with its customary hustle and bustle becomes used to the passion and excitement that comes with it. Pepe Solla, who has hospitality coursing through his veins, is the perfect example of this, becoming part of the history of the restaurant and vice-versa. His love for cooking came from his father (who was awarded a Michelin star at Casa Solla in 1980), and he has run the family business to the highest standard while continuing to evolve, in particular thanks to his obsession with immense flavours, and a focus on creative cooking inspired by the culinary traditions of Galicia. His menus (Trasmallo and Piobardeira), which champion ingredients sourced from the local area and the sea, showcase simplicity while still seeking to develop new concepts. On Sundays in summer, he hosts combined food and music events in the garden – a fun and highly enjoyable experience that begins with brunch and ends with live music.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1089;Radis;Spain;Jaén;Tableron 10, Jaén, 23001, Spain;37.7680566;-3.7863389;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Radis is one of those places in which a young chef (Juanjo Mesa) with the restaurant business in his blood, experience working in leading restaurants behind him, and an undeniable desire to please, has set up a business with a view to revolutionising the city’s dining options. Mesa recently won the title of “Best Olive Oil Chef” at the “Jaén, Paraíso Interior” contest organised as part of the San Sebastián Gastronomika festival, and in this small, centrally located eatery with a contemporary bistro feel and open kitchen, he puts all his efforts into a surprise tasting menu (to which extra dishes can be added) inspired by tradition and his childhood memories. He has brought this cuisine fully up to date thanks to strong technique, a delicate touch and superbly crafted sauces and jus. The name of the restaurant stems from the French word for radish – the chef’s nickname happens to be El Rabanito (“radish” in Spanish)!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1090;Nerua Guggenheim Bilbao;Spain;Bilbao;Avenida de Abandoibarra 2, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2688108;-2.93308;35;true;false;Creative;If you find the idea of eating inside a museum tempting, there’s no better place than the Guggenheim Bilbao, where the unique design of the building reverberates throughout your experience here. Nerua, which takes its name from the Latin for the River Nervión, situated at the point where the river’s freshwater meets the saltwater of the Atlantic, recreates a similar fusion in its own philosophy thanks to chef Josean Alija’s quest to revive traditional Basque flavours from an innovative perspective. As a result, he enhances the menu with dishes that will dazzle guests with their depth and nuanced play with vegetables. Choose between a modern à la carte and one tasting menu (Muina) with a nod to seasonal cooking through dishes such as sea bass with a saffron jus and acidified wild mushrooms, and the spectacular Iberian pancetta with pickled vegetables. We can also recommend adding the wine pairing option to discover some particularly interesting labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1091;Lera;Spain;Castroverde de Campos;Conquistadores Zamoranos 6, Castroverde de Campos, 49110, Spain;41.967639;-5.3137839;24;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Local landscapes define regions as much as their natural bounty and here, in the heart of the Castilian Meseta, you’ll find one of the culinary temples for game in the whole of Spain. Under the baton of Luis Alberto Lera, the restaurant (which also features a few attractive guestrooms) has had a new lease of life, incorporating more contemporary techniques into traditional recipes while continuing to respect the latter. It also acts as a culinary reference for game and hunting in order to showcase the gastronomic traditions of this region. Choose between a concise à la carte and one tasting menu (short and long options are available) which include vegetables, stews, escabeches etc, but always with game as their leitmotiv. The Pichón Bravío de Tierra de Campos pigeon (reared by the family in their iconic dovecotes), is without doubt the signature dish here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1092;Donaire;Spain;Adeje;Fernando López Arvelo 1, Planta 4, Adeje, 38660, Spain;28.0916898;-16.7387881;92;true;false;Contemporary;This charming restaurant, the fine-dining option in the Hotel GF Victoria, stands out for its setting in a completely glass-fronted, semi-circular room with pleasant views of the Costa Adeje coastline and the Atlantic. The chef at the helm, Jesús Camacho, developed his culinary foundations in the world of pastry, a factor that is undeniably evident in his dishes which are all created and designed with painstaking care and precision. The à la carte, which is well supported by two tasting menus (Donaire and Victoria), showcases a creative, contemporary flair with strong Canary Island and French influence, a strong emphasis on presentation and the use of native ingredients from the islands. One dish that particularly impressed us with its delicacy was the beetroot with “macho” vinegar, Aquanaria sea bass and goat’s milk Chantilly.;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1093;Nova;Spain;Ourense;Valle Inclán 5, Ourense, 32004, Spain;42.33977;-7.8623301;75;false;true;Contemporary;In this centrally located restaurant, with a name that showcases its desire to create new and innovative experiences, the emphasis is on “deep-rooted cuisine” that showcases the origins of Galicia cooking and its terroir (artisanal Pan de Cea bread, Ceboleiro chorizo, the Mos breed of chicken etc) with the aim, first and foremost, of bringing what is local to a wider audience. In this impeccable, contemporary-minimalist setting with an open-view kitchen, chefs Julio Sotomayor and Daniel Guzmán (who as well as being business partners are also cousins!) remain faithful to their principles, creating three surprise tasting menus every day (Raíces, Nova and Cima) that change according to product seasonality and vary in the number of courses on offer (8, 10 or 13). We recommend being guided in your choice of wines as the cellar here is home to a plethora of interesting wines from small-scale local producers.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1094;El Bohío;Spain;Illescas;Avenida Castilla-La Mancha 81, Illescas, 45200, Spain;40.1267656;-3.8462246;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that has managed to adapt with the times to the delight of its guests. Despite the bright, renovated new look and cuisine that is more in keeping with contemporary trends, it still retains the informal character of the early roadside “mesón” first opened by grandmother Valentina and whose name recalls her Cuban roots. It is impossible to talk about El Bohío without mentioning celebrity chef Pepe Rodríguez, who champions the DNA of this area by highlighting the culinary legacy of La Mancha, while at the same time adapting its flavours and ingredients to the present day in line with one of his maxims: “the cuisine of old seen through the eyes of today”. His signature dishes here include lentils with Butifarra sausage, La Mancha-style gazpacho, and updated versions of “pringá del cocido”, with cabbage and broth. You can also add his famous tripe tapa to any of the menus (Traditional, Seasonal and Tasting).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1095;El Xato;Spain;la Nucía;Avenida l'Esglèsia 3, la Nucía, 03530, Spain;38.6172486;-0.123197;82;true;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;A family-run restaurant with over 100 years of history, dating back to the simple wine cellar that first opened in 1915. Over time it became a tapas bar and now, run by the fourth generation, it is the most prestigious restaurant in the Marina Baixa area, where the staff do everything possible to ensure that diners “arrive as guests but leave as friends”. Chef Cristina Figueira, who is ably supported by her husband Francisco Cano (in charge of the dining room and wine cellar), began her training in the kitchens of El Xato under the watchful eye of her mother-in-law, Esperanza Fuster. Here, she demonstrates an inexhaustible spirit which has resulted in her becoming one of the most outstanding cooks in the region thanks to her mastery of Alicante cuisine and her creative vision closely linked to the true essence of this area. This is demonstrated by dishes such as her superb grilled langoustine tartare. Choose between two gastronomic menus (Tentaciones and Centenario), both of which feature a wine pairing option that showcases Valencian wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1096;Vandelvira;Spain;Baeza;Plaza de San Francisco, Baeza, 23440, Spain;37.9941772;-3.4689799;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If you’re visiting Baeza’s marvellous historic quarter, a Renaissance jewel that has been declared a World Heritage Site, eating in this restaurant will add an extra-special touch to the experience. Vandelvira occupies part of a 16C monastery with comfortable dining rooms and beautiful covered cloisters where guests can nowadays enjoy a glass of manzanilla sherry. The focus of young owner-chef Juan Carlos García is on a single tasting menu of creative cuisine, with a preference for humble ingredients from his own vegetable garden or the region, whichhe transforms into haute-cuisine dishes that showcase finesse, flavour and an extraordinary level of presentation. One dish that particularly appealed to us was the squid and Iberian ham, accompanied by a concentrated Iberian ham dashi broth and a delicious squid tartare.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1097;Ajonegro;Spain;Logrono;Hermanos Moroy 1 - bajo 9, Logrono, 26001, Spain;42.4658541;-2.4461804;70;true;true;Fusion;A restaurant that will delight guests both for its gourmet cuisine and the love story that is behind it. The dreams and sense of excitement evident within its walls developed relatively recently when the two chefs at the helm met while working with celebrated chef Jordi Cruz at the three-Michelin-starred ABaC. Mariana Sánchez, originally from Cuernavaca (Mexico), and Gonzalo Baquedano, who hails from Logroño, showcase their skills on an à la carte and a tasting menu (in the evening, the latter is combined with another shorter menu option) that showcase the fusion between Mexican and La Rioja cuisine with an emphasis on seasonal ingredients. The elegant and consistent cooking here subtly plays with spicy flavours that are adapted to European palates through variations on classic Mexican tacos. Standout dishes include the Mexican red prawn cocktail, the crispy pork cheek tacos, the venison with pink Mexican mole, and the sweetcorn-inspired “pastel de Elote” cake.;Air conditioning;[]
1098;Casona del Judío;Spain;Santander;Repuente 20, Santander, 39012, Spain;43.4686232;-3.8292585;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine;If you would like to eat in a really special setting, book a table at Casona del Judío, as it’s not every day that you get the chance to enjoy a Michelin-starred experience in an authentic 19C colonial-style property. Here, chef Sergio Bastard impresses guests by shining the spotlight on local ingredients as well as algae and herbs from the Cantabrian coast. His single Festival tasting menu (with a wine-pairing option) enables all his guests to share the same experience through dishes influenced by the sea, with a fusion of textures and pinpoint presentation. Access is via the Casona, which features a room in which the chef creates and explains his snacks before guests take their seats. Once seated, they will discover innovative culinary creations such as Salmuria, an unusual anchovy brine that he stores in small bottles and uses in sauces, in particular, to provide enhanced flavour and to add a touch of saltiness to his dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1099;BACK;Spain;Marbella;Pablo Casals 8, Marbella, 29602, Spain;36.509052;-4.894597;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Andalusian;If you’re looking for a fine-dining experience which also comes with an element of fun, this pleasant and modern bistro-style eatery is able to meet both requirements in a perfectly balanced manner. The first thing to mention is that Úbeda-born chef David Olivas has always been a free spirit when it comes to creating dishes for his guests, a fact clearly evident in his creative-contemporary cooking that showcases his technical ability and personality through the use of the best locally sourced ingredients – the cornerstone of his cuisine is to bring time-honoured flavours into the present day. Options on the à la carte are divided into two sections: “Our Classics…” (featuring BACK’s classic dishes), and “What is changing...”. These are ably supported by an impressive tasting menu entitled Entorno. We particularly enjoyed the “roasted and rested” duck breast featuring two succulent escalopes that have been smoked over apple wood, and served with pickled beets, anchovies and pistachios.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1100;La Botica de Matapozuelos;Spain;Matapozuelos;Plaza Mayor 2, Matapozuelos, 47230, Spain;41.4143484;-4.7914841;89;false;false;Contemporary, Castilian;A family - run restaurant and carvery (asador) occupying a rural property that in the past served as a pharmacy. The dining rooms are rustic in design and complemented by a private room in what was once the chemist shop. The contemporary menu is hugely influenced by the traditional products of the area. Extensive tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1101;Tatau;Spain;Huesca;Azara, Huesca, 22002, Spain;42.1385333;-0.4085046;88;true;false;Creative, Traditional Cuisine;This gastro-bar with a difference will definitely take you by surprise! It is the project of a couple (Tonino and Arantxa) who have always focused on the personality of their cuisine without being afraid to incorporate influences from elsewhere. The name Tatau connects with the charisma of Tonino and his tattoos, a chef who says that the different stages in his life history have left a “mark” and are represented through his culinary creativity. The restaurant features a fun décor as well as a striking bar and high tables designed so that guests can savour his tapas and “raciones” as they observe the preparation process. His cooking is based around a single tasting menu entitled Du Jour, which is enhanced by daily suggestions and game-inspired dishes (another menu called Saison is also available during the game-hunting season). Here, time-honoured flavours are to the fore in local ingredients such as Verdeña olive oil from Loscertales, trout from El Grado, Latón de La Fueva pork etc.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1102;Lillas Pastia;Spain;Huesca;del Parque 3, Huesca, 22002, Spain;42.136332;-0.4101935;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Following its move to new premises just behind the historic Casino de Huesca, this legendary restaurant has had a new lease of life, although it has retained its culinary essence and its moniker as the “House of the Truffle”. In this meticulous, contemporary setting, you’ll find a striking bar at the entrance leading to a gastronomic dining room separated from the former by a large wine rack, a semi-open kitchen plus, on one of the walls, a large AI-created illustration of an opera singer (hence the name Lillas Pastia, who ran the tavern in the famous opera Carmen). Here, chef Carmelo Bosque creates an updated take on traditional cuisine that is based around seasonal market ingredients and showcased on an à la carte and the 10-course Lillas tasting menu. Standout dishes include the cod brandade cannelloni with saffron, and the delicious creamy rice with truffle.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1103;Txispa;Spain;Axpe;San Juan Auzoa 45, Axpe, 48291, Spain;43.1145985;-2.6024292;63;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;Occasionally, simplicity is the greatest of treasures! Here, the experiment of combining the time-honoured techniques of Japanese cuisine with the barbecue techniques of a typical Basque “asador” has really paid off. Japanese chef Tetsuro Maeda, who has renovated a century-old house in a small village so quiet it’s almost possible to hear the silence around you, has taken simplicity as his leitmotiv, basing his cooking around exceptional ingredients (many from his own vegetable garden) to create dishes that reveal new and surprising nuances. Recipes that appear on the single surprise menu (anchovies stuffed with daikon sprouts, Txuleta Parda Alpina madurada, bay laurel ice-cream etc) are based around the best possible seasonal ingredients and are constantly evolving. The experience begins with appetisers in the kitchen, where guests can admire the open grill, and reaches its climax in the attractive, rustic-cum-minimalist dining room with just six tables. You’ll need to pay in advance and they expect you to be punctual!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1104;Kabo;Spain;Pamplona;Avenida de Zaragoza 10, Pamplona, 31003, Spain;42.8118407;-1.6433174;18;false;false;Contemporary;This pleasant, contemporary-style restaurant, which takes its name from the Masai word for “butterfly”, has expanded its facilities and enhanced its comfort following a change of location to just a few metres from its original home. On its single, contemporary tasting menu, based around seasonal ingredients, a love for its land, and support for small-scale local producers, the focus is firmly anchored on the cuisine of the Navarra region. One dish that we found particularly delightful was the Transformación dessert, which seemingly undergoes a metamorphosis from a silkworm into a butterfly on the plate under the gaze of mesmerised guests! Make sure you book ahead to enjoy this theatrical performance to the full!;Air conditioning;[]
1105;Mont Bar;Spain;Barcelona;Diputació 220, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3862568;2.1618511;19;true;true;Creative;A restaurant with a gastro-bar ambience that is becoming a must for every visitor to Barcelona. In this delightful setting featuring elegant decorative detail you’ll find an array of traditional and contemporary dishes, all of which showcase high levels of technique, plus presentation that is so refined that it is hard not to take a photo! In keeping with the philosophy of the owners, who hail from the small village of Mont (in the Val d’Aran), the cuisine here is based around fresh, seasonal and locally sourced ingredients. The à la carte and tasting menu feature inventive snacks, innovative tapas, and small sharing plates, always accompanied by impeccable and attentive service. We particularly enjoyed the superb seasonal suggestions (morel mushrooms, Reixago cheese and pork cheek, peas with vanilla, clams and hazelnuts, etc) but there are also dishes available all year round that are a must, such as the spectacular Iberian sobrasada mochi with Mahón cheese!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1106;Lluerna;Spain;Santa Coloma de Gramenet;Avenida Pallaresa 104, Santa Coloma de Gramenet, 08921, Spain;41.4554734;2.2065622;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The best aspect of this kind of family-run restaurant is the unhurried and stress-free approach which is very much in keeping with the principles of the Slow Food movement. The focus of the married couple that run and own Lluerna, Víctor Quintillà (in the kitchen) and Mar Gómez (front of house), is on sustainable cuisine that champions locally sourced ingredients (chicken from the Penedés area, Duroc pigs, Xisqueta lambs, pigeon from the Tatjé family etc). These are showcased via a modern take on Catalan recipes that uses skilled techniques to enhance their delicate textures and maximise each and every flavour. In the kitchen, visible from both the dining room and the chef’s table, the team creates cuisine that is exclusively focused on several set menus served to the whole table: Degustació (lunchtime midweek only), Vegetal, Presentació and Lluerna. The provenance of ingredients (organic where possible) for each dish is usually explained to guests when served.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1107;CEBO;Spain;Madrid;San Jerónimo 34, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4162213;-3.6984633;22;false;true;Creative;Located inside the luxury Hotel Urban, CEBO has taken on a new lease of life under the duo of Javier Sanz and Juan Sahuquillo, two young chefs who have enjoyed considerable success at their restaurants in Casa-Ibáñez (Cañitas Maite Gastro and Oba-). In this intimate setting, where high levels of service are very much to the fore, they look to explore in even greater detail the natural flavour of every ingredient (sourced from their own vegetable garden and small-scale producers around the country) with a focus on simplicity and superb technique, as highlighted in sauces that are perfectly balanced, as well as highly aesthetic presentation. Their creatively inspired cuisine is centred on two tasting menus: Clásicos (which can be combined with the à la carte and is only available lunchtimes midweek) and the more extensive and gastronomic Temporada, available in the evening and at weekends. For a post-meal drink, why not head up to the rooftop terrace with its superb views of the city?;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
1108;Retama;Spain;Torrenueva;Camino  de Altamar, Torrenueva, 13740, Spain;38.670718;-3.3219559;40;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Retama (“broom” in English), takes its name from this bush with yellow blossom that is a very common sight on Spain’s Central Meseta and in the area around La Caminera, an exclusive and tranquil country hotel with a 9-hole golf course and even its own aerodrome. Its restrained yet charming backdrop of bare tables and Nordic-inspired decor is the perfect setting in which to discover the cooking of chef Miguel Ángel Expósito – a champion of local ingredients and produce and the culinary heritage of traditional La Mancha recipes. His cuisine revolves around three tasting menus (Tradición, Finca La Caminera and Retama) that showcase the restaurant’s solid ties with this region (wild rabbit à la royale, “sequence of partridge from our estate”, shank of wild boar, beetroot escabeche etc), reinterpreting dishes from a modern perspective that incorporates the latest culinary techniques. The views of the countryside from your table are an absolute delight!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1110;La Lobita;Spain;Navaleno;Avenida La Constitución 54, Navaleno, 42149, Spain;41.8367514;-3.0064064;55;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;The history of this restaurant, a culinary temple for mushroom-lovers, is also one that showcases a love for hospitality, given that chef Elena Lucas represents (with infinite modesty) the third generation of the family to have worked in the kitchen here. Its name is an affectionate tribute to her grandmother (Luciana Lobo) and enables guests to gain a better understanding of her highly personal and creative cuisine which explores time-honoured flavours and champions the local surroundings and their natural bounty. Alongside her husband and sommelier Diego Muñoz, Elena Lucas strives to form a culinary dialogue with her guests as if we were enjoying a stroll with her through her local woods and pine groves (this affinity with her natural surroundings is visible in her dishes, such as the thyme “cuajada” (curd) with fermented pine nut honey, as well as the crockery and decor. One of the restaurant’s secret tricks is to only scrape and brush wild mushrooms that they are going to use that day, which they then wash with water and dry in the open air.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1111;La Fonda Xesc;Spain;Gombrèn;Plaza Roser 1, Gombrèn, 17531, Spain;42.24774;2.0907118;37;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in a small village in the Gerona municipality of Ripollés, this restaurant boasts a surprising setting in Gombrèn’s most historic inn, a large house dating back to 1730 that now features two distinct parts: the old section, beneath robust stone arches, and the new – a much brighter space that looks out onto the surrounding mountain landscapes through its panoramic windows. Here, chef Francesc Rovira, a disciple of the late great Santi Santamaria, oversees creative-cum-contemporary cuisine that clearly identifies with the region and which is tremendously tasty, aromatic and enticing despite the use of modest culinary techniques. It also features an array of delicate details and a philosophy that involves working with the best locally sourced seasonal ingredients (meat, potatoes, wild mushrooms, sausages etc). His cuisine is based around three menus, the highlight of which is the one dedicated to his sister Dolors Rovira.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1113;Víctor Gutiérrez;Spain;Salamanca;Empedrada 4, Salamanca, 37007, Spain;40.9630387;-5.6703452;35;false;true;Creative, Fusion;In this location opposite the Palacio de Congresos y Exposiciones, chef Víctor Gutiérrez, the only chef in the Castilla y León region with two Michelin stars (one here, the other at Taller in Quintanilla de Onésimo), conjures up cuisine based around three strong principles: ingredients, technique and feeling.His tasting menus (Mestizo, Criollo and Raíces) reveal his full passion and an unquestionable splash of creativity as he combines the region’s superb ingredients with the flavours of his native Peru and the occasional Japanese influence. Because of his desire to work with local and organic ingredients, many of these (vegetables, aromatic herbs and edible flowers) are sourced from his supplier Manolo’s organic market garden in Pelabravo, 10km or so from Salamanca. He also offers a takeaway service of more informal dishes under the brand name Sudaka.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1114;Blossom;Spain;Malaga;Strachan 11, Malaga, 29015, Spain;36.7197468;-4.420422;25;false;true;Fusion;(Temporarily on the 6th floor of the Molina Lario Hotel) If you’re looking for a restaurant in the pedestrianised streets around the cathedral in the centre of the city, this restaurant could be the perfect option. The focus in this relatively small space with just a handful of tables (the majority of which are on the pedestrian street it fronts), is on an interesting approach to fusion cuisine which combines creativity and South American flourishes from Peru, Mexico and Argentina. These stem from Argentina-born chef Emi Schobert who searches for his inspiration “in the sea, the mountains and local ingredients” and who has represented his country in the prestigious Bocuse d’Or world cooking competition on two occasions. His cuisine, which always showcases a constant delicacy in its presentation, is centred around a single tasting menu entitled Gran Menú Blossom, on which his sweetbread biscuit, with chickpea and Jerusalem artichoke took us completely by surprise. Given the limited space here, booking ahead is absolutely essential.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1115;Pabú;Spain;Madrid;Panamá 4, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.4565722;-3.6890656;66;false;false;Creative;A restaurant that is definitely in vogue and one which continues to gain new fans – even the royal family celebrated a birthday here! Located close to the legendary Santiago Bernabéu football stadium, Pabú reflects the gourmet vision of Coco Montes, a Cordon Bleu chef who has worked in prestigious restaurants such as Arpège in Paris, under the baton of famous chef Alain Passard. His cooking is based around the purity of ingredients, hence his championing of micro-seasonal cuisine that changes daily in line with provisions from his suppliers and is highly focused on vegetables, with little protein, delicate textures and plenty of personality. It also highlights an extensive knowledge of classic French techniques and is centred around two surprise tasting menus (Pate and Bubú), although dishes on these can also be ordered individually à la carte style. The bread here is made with natural sourdough, while the selection of international cheeses is particularly impressive.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1116;Tresmacarrons;Spain;El Masnou;Avenida del Maresme 21, El Masnou, 08320, Spain;41.4827541;2.3327657;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of this family-run restaurant is an unmistakeable reference to Michelin’s stars which the French refer to colloquially as “macaroons”.Here, in a modern yet welcoming ambience, discover chef Miquel Aldana’s propensity for high-quality Catalan cuisine that is contemporary in style, adapted to seasonality and firmly connected to the surrounding El Maresme area of Barcelona province. Tresmacarrons’ culinary philosophy is based around the pleasure of a job well done and complete commitment, as demonstrated by its tasting menus (Greatest Hits and Mirando al Mar). If you like the tableware here, make sure you tell Núria Orra, the front of house manager, as she was involved in its design and production!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1117;Amazing Chinese Cuisine (Changning);China Mainland;Shanghai;B5 Villa, 1665 Hongqiao Road, Changning, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2024972;121.3886;75;false;true;Chao Zhou;High-end Chaozhou cuisine characterises the menu, with over 200 items ranging from the classics to the creative – many made with ingredients specially sourced from Chaoshan region. Some signature dishes, such as chilled crab Chaozhou-style and marinated raw mantis shrimps, have to be pre-ordered. Crispy sea cucumber that takes days to prepare is another highlight. With just five private rooms in this villa, getting a table can be a challenge.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1118;Phénix;China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, The PuLi, 1 Changde Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.223997;121.44368;93;false;false;French;The chef cleverly uses Chinese produce in modern French fare. Meat starters and novel creations abound in the à la carte menu. The six-course Découverte menu gives diners a sense of what Phénix has to offer, but to appreciate the chef's vision in all its glory, opt for the 12-course Expérience omakase-style menu. The pigeon is a tour de force – chargrilled breast stuffed with foie gras and confit legs are doused in plum sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1119;Canton Table;China Mainland;Shanghai;5F, Bund 3, 3 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.236093;121.486211;32;false;true;Cantonese;Remodelled in 2019, the room exudes old-Shanghai flair with bare cement bricks, terrazzo flooring and murals of women in qipao. The head chef honed his skills in some famous kitchens for over 20 years. His menu is short but sweet, covering the quintessence of Cantonese food – barbecue meats and dim sum among other seasonal offerings. Scrambled egg with shredded fried fish maw stands out with its interesting textures and rich aromas.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1120;Oriental Sense & Palate;China Mainland;Shanghai;57 Sinan Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.216671;121.464255;81;false;false;Chao Zhou;This multi-storey marvel in a historical mansion exudes understated luxury. Chef Fai creates culinary gems that entice with pretty plating and precise execution. Be sure to order the juicy, deep-fried 20-day-old pigeon with crispy skin. The sautéed dried shrimps with minced pork seduces with contrasting textures and deep, mildly spicy flavours. Seafood dishes including whelk are also popular.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1121;Obscura;China Mainland;Shanghai;Tangxiang Cultural Space, 538 Xikang Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.236348;121.442233;36;true;true;Innovative;The chiaroscuro ring logo connotes completeness and the complementary relationship of the enthusiastic chef duo, who travel around China regularly to keep their prix-fixe seasonal menu fresh and inspired. With sound Western techniques, they interpret traditionally Chinese memories with unique scents, tastes, textures and a touch of whimsy, eg Cantonese roast pork disguised as ice cream. Consider pairing the food with non-alcoholic drinks. Leave your preconceptions at the door and be wowed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
1122;Ming Court;China Mainland;Shanghai;Level B1, Cordis Hotel, 333 Shenhong Road, Minhang, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.19512;121.31633;41;true;true;Cantonese;Weary travellers will find this airy dining room near Hongqiao airport a veritable haven. As well as serving the same classics as its namesake sister branch in Hong Kong, the experienced Shanghainese chef also imbues Cantonese dim sum with unique Shanghainese touches. Honey-glazed chai siu pork, and tofu skin beggar’s purses are both pieces de resistance here. Don’t forget to save some room for baked-to-order puff pastry egg tarts.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1126;Cheng Long Hang (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;216 Jiujiang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.239067;121.48161;96;false;true;Shanghainese;A household name among hairy crab lovers, this restaurant runs its own farm to ensure quality and a stable supply. Their crabs have flavoursome flesh, with their shells brimming with creamy yellow roe. Try the array of hairy crab dishes on offer, including drunken crabs steeped in Shaoxing wine for a month. Each serving of steamed meringue on stuffed crab shell uses the meat and roe of three hairy crabs and is sinfully satisfying.;Air conditioning;[]
1127;Da Dong (Xuhui);China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 602, 6F, iapm, 999 Middle Huaihai Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.230507;121.437471;30;true;false;Chinese Contemporary;Most customers come for the signature roast duck, boasting wonderfully crispy skin and succulent meat, served with steamed buns. Try also their braised sea cucumber with scallion. On top of the main menu, a seasonal one is also available, alongside new items made according to the 24 solar terms in the Chinese calendar. Come in a group to sample the variety of dishes on offer but be prepared – it’s always jam-packed after 6pm.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1128;Lao Zheng Xing;China Mainland;Shanghai;556 Fuzhou Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.235098;121.475464;16;false;false;Shanghainese;Known locally and internationally since its inception in 1862, Lao Zheng Xing is reputedly the oldest Shanghainese restaurant in the city and was responsible for creating a number of classic dishes. It moved to its current location in 1997, which gave it considerably more space as it now occupies several floors. Come with friends to enjoy signature dishes like fried river shrimps, eight treasures in spicy sauce and braised sea cucumber.;Air conditioning;[]
1130;Sheng Yong Xing (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;5F, Bund 5, 20 Guangdong Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2363387;121.4861839;61;true;false;Beijing Cuisine;The Beijing brand famous for Peking duck chose this prestigious address on the Bund for their first Shanghai outpost. Diners are greeted by a wine cellar tunnel foreshadowing the range of drinks to go with the signature bird. Each of the 45-day-old ducks roasted over jujube wood comes with a QR code that allows diners to trace its source. The views of the Bund and romantic ambiance also make for a great dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
1131;Yong Yi Ting;China Mainland;Shanghai;LG Level, Mandarin Oriental Pudong, 111 South Pudong Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.245216;121.50343;23;false;true;Jiangzhe;After renovation, the restaurant reopened in an elegant space styled to evoke Jiangnan's water towns, divided into zones by perforated screens mimicking Suzhou's gardens and sheer curtains with ink strokes. Jiangzhe classics are given a refined, creative spin, with signatures such as Hangzhou-style minced fish ball with green peas (pre-order only). At lunch, try dim sum such as Qiandaohu rice flour dumplings and four-colour dumplings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1132;Jin Xuan;China Mainland;Shanghai;53F, The Ritz-Carlton Pudong, 8 Century Avenue, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2384407;121.4968159;32;false;false;Cantonese;Next to the iconic Oriental Pearl Tower, this elegant dining room is perched on an upper floor of a sky-scraping hotel, commanding panoramic views of the Huangpu River and Pudong skyline. The menu covers much ground in Cantonese cuisine, including rare imported ingredients from Australian black cod to New Zealand lobster. The dim sum platter features an assortment of three crowd pleasers. The well-curated wine list has excellent choices by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
1133;Il Ristorante - Niko Romito;China Mainland;Shanghai;47F, Bvlgari Hotel, Lane 108, North Shanxi Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.229977;121.48704;39;true;true;Italian;Stunning vistas of the Pudong skyline, crystal chandeliers and semi-circular leather booths impart style and a sense of grandeur. The menu here, as at the Dubai and Beijing outlets, comprises creations supervised by celebrity chef Niko Romito and underpinned by well-honed skills to reflect seasonality. Handmade pasta is the must-try – the lobster linguine bursts with seafood umami. Be sure to save room for the creamy gelato di ricotta di bufala.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1134;Yong Fu (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;12F, Cathay Building, Jin Jiang Hotel, 59 South Maoming Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2229271;121.4567685;87;true;false;Ningbo;Shanghainese are no strangers to Ningbo cuisine and they know what they like! This restaurant with bags of old Shanghai charm serves wild-caught seafood shipped daily from Ningbo then meticulously prepared to highlight its natural flavours. Portion sizes can be tailored to your party size, and the emphasis is on seasonal items, such as razor clams from Ninghai (available Mar-May). The yellow croaker roe aspic and handmade glutinous rice balls are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1135;Lu Style (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;Room 207, 2F, Uni Elite, Lane 838, South Huangpi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.213823;121.472565;79;true;false;Shandong;The head chef is a Shandong native, who started his career at the age of 18 as an army chef. The menu features the freshest catch from Bohai Sea – shipped in daily – and the chef fine-tunes his recipes according to the season. The "Jiaodong cold appetiser platter" includes four kinds of seafood with different seasonings. Live or dried sea cucumber is braised in a scallion sauce with corn smut, a mushroom believed to have health benefits.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1137;Moose (Pudong);China Mainland;Shanghai;9F, L+Mall, 899 South Pudong Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.230604;121.51517;46;true;true;Jiangzhe;Moose has three Shanghai branches, all run by the same team. This Pudong one is geared towards the general public, with a Huaiyang-centric menu featuring some painstakingly made delicacies. From Anhui province, the head chef champions the pagoda version of braised pork belly in brown sauce, which shows exquisite knife work. The sautéed river shrimps are a light but umami-loaded option. Ask servers about the seasonal menu and catch of the day.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1138;Yi Long Court;China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, The Peninsula Hotel, Bund 32, 32 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.243758;121.507579;91;false;true;Cantonese;This flagship restaurant of The Peninsula, though decorated in the style of 1930s Shanghai, serves an unmistakably Cantonese menu with an abundance of excellent choices. The kitchen masters authentic Cantonese flavours underpinned by culinary traditions and classical skills. The Cantonese barbecue never disappoints, and there is a dim sum lunch set for solo diners. The deep-fried pork dumplings entice with a blistered crust and pork-mushroom filling.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1139;YongFoo Élite;China Mainland;Shanghai;200 Yongfu Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.211227;121.43842;81;true;false;Shanghainese;This building dating from 1930 was the British Consulate before its three-year makeover. Its heritage is matched by a menu of traditional Shanghainese dishes, including many ancient recipes rarely found elsewhere. The braised pork belly with pu'er tea exudes earthy depth and dark soy notes, and the decadent hairy crab roe and crabmeat options are loaded with flavours. The well-curated wine list is also worth checking out.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
1140;Narisawa;China Mainland;Shanghai;L7-05, 1000Trees, 600 Moganshan Road, Putuo, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2511252;121.4420253;96;false;false;Innovative;Featuring sustainable satoyama cuisine that connects diners with nature, this outpost of its Tokyo namesake serves a seasonal set menu built on Japanese traditions finessed by Western techniques. Having worked with chef-owner Narisawa for 10+ years, the head chef uses mostly Chinese ingredients in his cooking. The iconic "Bread of the Forest" is fermented and baked tableside in a stone pot and infused with seasonal produce such as white tea or kumquat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
1142;Seventh Son;China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop E2-03, 2F, Tower 1, Jing An Kerry Centre, 1515 West Nanjing Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.226083;121.4455729;53;true;false;Cantonese;The Hong Kong based chain opened this comfortable, traditionally decorated branch in 2014 and it’s been attracting a loyal fan base ever since. It delivers a traditional Cantonese menu, with the technical skills of the chef evident in dishes that range from dried seafood and soups to roast meats and stir-fries. At lunch they offer over 30 varieties of dim sum. Sautéed ‘osmanthus’ egg with crabmeat and shredded shrimp is the must-try speciality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1145;Yue Hai Tang;China Mainland;Shanghai;Vi Park, 161 Haowen Road, Minhang, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.1618626;121.3508843;86;false;false;Cantonese;Yue Hai Tang is the brainchild of an experienced chef who has worked in some of the most prestigious kitchens of Shanghai. His team, which has been with him for a long time, rustles up a wickedly enticing Cantonese barbecue. Besides the main menu, you will also see seasonal offerings and a selection of painstakingly crafted dishes, such as lobster and crab meat in pastry. The wine list boasts over 500 choices. Booking and pre-ordering dishes is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1146;Tou Zao;China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 211, East Wing, Shanghai Centre, 1376 West Nanjing Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2286321;121.4473688;66;true;true;Cantonese;Unlike the typical bustling Chinese joint, Tou Zao offers the serenity and intimate service of a sushiya. But the single prix-fixe menu, featuring hot entrées and dim sum, is unmistakably Cantonese. The sautéed lobster with scallion trio has addictive aromas and springy flesh. Spring rolls and Cantonese puff pastries are made tableside, baked à la minute and served piping hot. Deft control of heat and remarkable wok hei are the hallmarks of the food here.;;[]
1147;Wu You Xian;China Mainland;Shanghai;Room 1-103, 7 South Maoming Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2254163;121.456094;98;true;false;Dim Sum;Having relocated to larger premises in the city centre, this shop famous for crab xiaolongbao still always attracts queues. They serve over 20 varieties – crabmeat, roe, tomalley or combinations thereof – with plump fillings enrobed in translucent skin, each with a different dip. The buns with premium seafood such as abalone and sea cucumber are also popular. First-timers can go for the assorted option with several varieties in one steamer.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
1148;Lei Garden (Xuhui);China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 401, 4F, iapm, 999 Middle Huaihai Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.218122;121.454124;55;true;false;Cantonese;The chain may be spreading rapidly in Asia but quality control is strictly imposed to ensure all dim sum, roast meats and double-boiled soups achieve the same high standard as at the parent restaurant. This branch in a popular mall boasts hip décor and is always full. ‘Crossing-the-bridge’ geoduck is blanched at your table in a hot seafood stock that took six hours to make. Claypot rice with preserved meat is made à la minute.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1149;Lei Garden (Pudong);China Mainland;Shanghai;L3-17 & 18, IFC Mall, 8 Century Avenue, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2390697;121.4979215;84;true;false;Cantonese;Reservations are a must, as this branch of the chain is always packed with diners craving good quality Cantonese cuisine. At lunchtime, customers come in droves for the expertly crafted dim sum and soups. The dinner menu offers premium dishes such as seafood and abalone. Those wishing to avoid making too much of a dent in their wallets can opt for seasonal stir-fries, casseroles or the set menus for sharing.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1151;Yong Fu (Hongkou);China Mainland;Shanghai;56F, East Tower, Raffles City The Bund, 1089 Dongdaming Road, Hongkou, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2548014;121.5039397;43;true;false;Ningbo;The swanky room overlooking the Pudong skyline and Huangpu River boasts marble walls and exquisite chandeliers. Half of the menu features Ningbo classics, while the other half presents novelty dishes made with ingredients from all over China. Live seafood is shipped daily from Zhejiang Province in the small hours to ensure freshness. Try stir-fried white crabmeat, sautéed cattail with shrimp roe, and sticky rice balls with black sesame filling.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
1152;Sole;China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 109, Shanghai Centre, 1376 West Nanjing Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2280406;121.4468481;98;false;false;Cantonese;Sole opened its doors in 2023 with an all-Cantonese kitchen team. The head chef's glorious career spans 20-plus years and he excels at Cantonese classics – dim sum, Cantonese barbecue, seafood, double-boiled soups and stir-fries. The long menu also offers painstakingly made items such as deep-fried egg custard with chicken testicle. The scallop dumpling with crab roe stands out for its translucent skin, perfect pleats and rich buttery filling.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1153;Meet the Bund (Zhongshan Dong Er Road);China Mainland;Shanghai;S301, 3F, South Mall, The Bund Finance Center, 600 Zhongshan Dong Er Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.228818;121.493593;56;true;false;Fujian;Brass ceiling panels and chandeliers lend a touch of nostalgic elegance to the otherwise modern room. For an experience authentic, Fujianese is the mainstay of the menu, with all of the kitchen team hailing from the province. Try the umami-laden duck essence made the traditional way: a whole duck is steamed for hours and the juices collected with no water added. Check out the tea menu, which has a wealth of nice choices from Fujian.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1154;Ling Long;China Mainland;Shanghai;105, 1F, Waldorf Astoria Hotel, 2 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.241756;121.488143;43;true;true;Innovative;The dimly lit space in a century-old building on the Bund feels mysterious and theatrical. The vibe is matched by a season-driven menu divided into acts, like a play. Neo-Chinese creations are finessed by European techniques, and presented in whimsical and ceremonious ways. For a fine dining take on the classic beef in oyster sauce, beef from Shandong is marinated then deep-fried and grilled. Creative wine pairing options add to the fun.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1155;Fu 1039;China Mainland;Shanghai;1039 Yuyuan Road, Changning, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2203677;121.4250187;65;false;false;Shanghainese;The dining room in a heritage mansion circa 1920s is furnished in a retro style with a terrace and several private rooms. Unlike its two sisters, the original Fu focuses on home-style Shanghainese cooking, including some multi-step labour-intensive recipes. River fish is one of its strong suits, especially river eels prepared in a myriad of ways. Try also oil-blanched river shrimps that are bouncy in texture and loaded with umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1157;Zhou She (Minhang);China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 116, Hongqiao Lihpao Plaza, No.16-101, Lane 318, Suhong Road, Minhang, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.1971351;121.30628;71;true;false;Shanghainese;In Hongqiao district, near a train station and airport, this restaurant is a popular choice among travellers. The head chef is a Shanghai native, who respects traditions, while exploring other Chinese regional flavours. His menu is heavily based on Shanghainese cuisine, with occasional Cantonese and Huaiyang dishes. Try his marinated pigeon with green Sichuan peppercorns and silky meat, and the umami-rich sautéed shredded fish with chive sprouts.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1159;Beta;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot 3 & 4, GF, Cormar Suites, 10 Jalan Perak, Kuala Lumpur, 50450, Malaysia;3.1545381;101.7090051;63;false;false;Malaysian, Contemporary;Beta offers discerning foodies an exciting way to taste Malaysia’s rich culinary heritage with a touch of finesse. The chef reimagines favourites from around the country, often jazzed up with modern techniques and soigné plating. Head to the lounge first for a round of cocktails and appetisers, before sampling the main courses in the theatrically appointed dining room with open kitchen. Fine cocktail-food pairings to complement the intelligent dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
1160;Au Jardin;Malaysia;George Town;The Warehouse@Hin Bus Depot, 125 Jalan Timah, George Town, 10150, Malaysia;5.412;100.327;80;false;true;European Contemporary;Inside a bus depot-turned art space sits this distressed building clad in corrugated metal panels. However, the interior is miles apart from the exterior, boasting a modern and sleek look. The menu changes monthly and showcases sophisticated European fare with subtle local twists. Every item served has been well thought out – the homemade sourdough with tomato butter is always a highlight. Even the palate cleanser surprises in pleasant ways.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1161;Chim By Chef Noom;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;L2-03, TSLAW Tower, 39 Jalan Kamuning, Imbi, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1444067;101.7195484;50;false;false;Thai contemporary;Tucked inside an office building, this upmarket restaurant serves Thai dishes rooted in tradition but with creative twists and stylish plating. Chef Noom, who also owns Chim by Siam Wisdom, in Bangkok, devises two multicourse tasting menus that change every season. Quality ingredients from Japan are used in conjunction with local spices, fruit and vegetables. The Lost Recipe is a 200-year-old variation of tom yum with nicely balanced flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1162;Auntie Gaik Lean's Old School Eatery;Malaysia;George Town;1 Lebuh Bishop, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4180516;100.3423801;18;false;false;Peranakan;Memorabilia in show windows and a 60s soundtrack exude the charm of a bygone era. Chef Gaik Lean has been guarding her secret recipes for decades and she makes no compromises in terms of food quality. Many items are made from scratch, including her heavenly pie tee and gulai tumis that uses over eight ingredients in the curry paste, such as fresh saffron. Also try nasi ulam, an old-time recipe.;Air conditioning;[]
1163;DC. by Darren Chin;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;44 Persiaran Zaaba, Taman Tun Dr Ismail, Kuala Lumpur, 60000, Malaysia;3.141698;101.627274;97;false;true;French Contemporary;Divided into bars and dining rooms, the three-story restaurant also sports a Louis XIII-themed private room. Diners can choose from 4- to 7-course menus, plus one for vegetarians. Dishes range from modern classics, such as sole meunière and freshly made pasta, to novel creations with Japanese accents, all of which underscored by solid skills and quality international produce. Don’t miss the cheese trolley with 20 choices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1165;la Barbecue;USA;Austin;2401 E. Cesar Chavez St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.254782;-97.71734;42;true;false;Barbecue;Founded by the late LeAnn Mueller and now run by her wife, Ali Clem, la Barbecue's massive, custom-built pit in the backyard is the rarified workshop in which meaty miracles are realized. Inside, it's a simple space enlivened with bright colors and a disarming playlist with Tammy Wynette and Dolly Parton. During peak hours, you can expect a substantial wait, but your patience will be rewarded with a first taste of the brisket as you reach the counter. You will marvel at the sublimely succulent, flavorful beef, but don't overlook the array of equally tempting offerings like house-made sausages, and pork or beef ribs. The team likes to keep things spicy, as in the chipotle cole slaw or fresh kimchi. Don't miss the mac and cheese.;;[]
1167;Mixtli;USA;San Antonio;812 S. Alamo St., Ste. 103, San Antonio, 78205, USA;29.4156664;-98.4888715;25;true;false;Mexican;This trailblazing restaurant is from the visionary minds of Chefs Diego Galicia and Rico Torres. The acclaimed duo has fine dining chops but it's a shared reverence for Mexican cuisine that is the real driving force behind this endeavor. Tasting menus shift often, focusing on a different part of Mexico and may offer up cutting-edge interpretations of Oaxacan specialties or a meal focused on the cuisine of "Tierra Caliente." Not content to restrain their explorations to the regional diversity of Mexican cuisine, the menus also draw from the culinary past or even pre-Columbian times. Expect cooking that is both cerebral and delicious, with meticulously prepared, artfully plated dishes that tell a story while thrilling your palate.;Air conditioning;[]
1168;Le Jardinier Houston;USA;Houston;5500 Main St., Houston, 77004, USA;29.7265256;-95.389877;39;true;false;French, Contemporary;With locations in Manhattan and Miami, Chef Alain Verzeroli's also shares his verdant, stylish cooking with Houston. The location couldn’t be more apt: The Museum of Fine Arts matches his colorful dishes that are both beautiful and satisfying. Accomplished sauces, seasonal vegetables, and thoughtful cocktails tell a story in line with the restaurant’s name and design. Highlights include thin strands of zucchini spaghetti with yellow pepper coulis and Comté foam, as well as plump Maine diver scallops with carrot jus reduction and sugar snap peas. Desserts, like the yuzu mousse with raspberry compote and pistachio sable, are beautiful to behold. The entire evening is smooth sailing thanks to a highly professional and personable team.;Air conditioning;[]
1172;Musaafer;USA;Houston;5115 Westheimer Rd., Ste. C-3500, Houston, 77056, USA;29.7405722;-95.4639608;87;true;true;Indian, Contemporary;Dinner in a shopping mall doesn’t sound promising, unless you’re headed to Musaafer. The sheer scale of this grand hall, with its arches, towering windows, labyrinth-like layout, and elaborate patterns, feels like a palace of its own. The setting is as thrilling as the cooking. A large, deep-fried orb of onion xuixo arrives dusted in no fewer than 24 spices, filled with potato and onion, and served with tamarind and mint chutney. Plucky prawns are cooked in an elegant sauce of coriander, coconut milk, and curry leaves. Dal, a familiar favorite, is cooked for 72 hours with tomato, butter, and smoked chili. The attention to detail and careful spicing is evident at every turn, and the final result is one of both high style and utterly gratifying substance.;Air conditioning;[]
1173;March;USA;Houston;1624 Westheimer Rd., Houston, 77006, USA;29.7432132;-95.4004288;97;true;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;This ambitious atelier sets its sights on a culinary exploration of the Mediterranean, studiously delving into individual regions one by one, from the Maghreb in Northwest Africa to Murcia and Andalusia in Southern Spain, to Greece, with a tasting menu and beverage program inspired by each cuisine in turn. But if all that sounds a bit precious, rest assured that the experience itself is utterly disarming, with a winning sense of hospitality that makes for a meal that is both engaging and luxe. Guests start with finely tuned cocktails and first bites in the stylish lounge area before being whisked into the striking main dining room for more substantial fare. From beginning to end, gorgeously plated dishes show refinement and creativity, so sit back and enjoy the show.;Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
1174;Barley Swine;USA;Austin;6555 Burnet Rd., Ste. 400, Austin, 78757, USA;30.3415073;-97.7387028;20;false;false;Contemporary, American;The room is decidedly casual, and diners are welcome to come as they are, but there's no mistaking the passion of this kitchen. Chef/owner Bryce Gilmore makes deft use of local ingredients with a distinctly Southwestern palette of flavors that draws from Mexican and Southern traditions, while maintaining a contemporary, global sophistication. The tasting menu is carefully attuned to the seasons, and refinement is balanced with a sense of whimsy. A tiny everything bagel with a creamy smoked radish spread and cucumber infused with dill hot sauce might come as a first bite, and a flawlessly seared Muscovy duck breast might be matched with a buttery puree of popped corn and an earthy/sweet nixtamalized peach.From dishes bought at Goodwill and growing produce onsite to collecting rainwater for their garden, they're also committed to sustainability.;Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1175;BCN Taste & Tradition;USA;Houston;4210 Roseland St., Houston, 77006, USA;29.7348796;-95.3899265;82;true;false;Spanish, Contemporary;Tucked away off Richmond Avenue this restaurant, housed in a 1920s white stucco bungalow and managed by some of the most personable staff in the city, cooks with both flair and familiarity. Seafood is a highlight, as in brilliantly tender slivers of sea cucumber set on lobster rice, or thinly sliced octopus paired with potato purée and a striking smoked paprika. Chef Luis Roger knows his way around land, too, and his Iberian suckling pig arrives with a crackling crust, meltingly tender meat and a rich red wine sauce. The beverage selection is intriguing, featuring an all-Spanish wine list and a section dedicated to gin and tonics. Owner Ignacio Torras's private art collection (including Pablo Picasso's owl jugs) is yet another charming touch.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
1176;Olamaie;USA;Austin;1610 San Antonio St., Austin, 78701, USA;30.2795575;-97.743647;40;false;false;American, Southern;With its white clapboard and black shutters, Olamaie, named for the chef's grandmother, mother, and daughter, is a charming spot north of downtown Austin. Consider a cocktail, as their list is interesting and includes a daily punch and fun drinks like the Spaghetti Western martini with Texas olive-oil-washed gin, vodka, cherry tomato-infused dry vermouth, and basil eau de vie.Expect Southern cuisine that's been given a contemporary polish, and don't dare miss out on the buttermilk biscuit, served warm and accompanied by whipped honey butter sprinkled with sea salt. The chicken pressé is a novel take on chicken and dumplings and rounds out a bill of fare that also includes blackened dayboat fish, gumbo, and red rice with Gulf shrimp.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1177;Tatemó;USA;Houston;4740 Dacoma St., Houston, 77092, USA;29.8068644;-95.4605072;42;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;The famous idiom about not judging a book by its cover couldn’t be more applicable than to this tortilleria-turned-tasting menu. In an empty strip mall with little around except for a brewery and a doughnut shop, Chef Emmanuel Chavez delivers a beautifully pitched and portioned experience that celebrates heirloom corn from across Mexico. His riffs on ceviche, quesadillas, and gorditas are elegant to behold and even more satisfying to eat thanks, in part, to vibrant salsas and other creative sauce work. The most original and striking effort might be the black-as-night mole negro, which comes blanketed under a tortilla made from nixtamalized plantains. If you want wine, you’ll have to bring your own as the restaurant doesn’t have a liquor license.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
1178;LeRoy and Lewis Barbecue;USA;Austin;5621 Emerald Forest Dr., Austin, 78745, USA;30.2105038;-97.7872512;29;true;false;Barbecue, American;What started as a food truck in 2017 can now be enjoyed in a spacious brick and mortar location in Garrison Park. The moniker refers to the duo of married couples who run this enticing operation where the spacious setting gives off midcentury vibes with its glazed brick exterior and peak-roofed dining area.The excellent barbecue menu isn't built around brisket, although that beloved item is available as a daily special at the end of the week. In fact, several specials keep things interesting throughout the week, such as spice-crusted, melt-in-your mouth beef cheeks or the daily sausage which may be studded with Hatch green chiles and mozzarella cheese. The banana pudding tiramisu is a clever hybrid with coffee-soaked 'Nilla wafers.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1179;O Me O Il Mare;Italy;Gragnano;Via Roma 45/47, Gragnano, 80054, Italy;40.6916293;14.5157334;35;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Known around the world as the town of pasta, Gragnano is still home to small-scale pasta-makers renowned for their top-quality pasta. To reinforce this fact, this restaurant is housed in a building (dating back to 1695) once used as pasta factory. Now boasting a modern, spacious dining room with a vaulted ceiling and open-view kitchen, the restaurant serves three tasting menus, all with strong links to the region but also featuring more creative touches. The region also takes pride of place on the wine list – it’s worth asking the talented and experienced sommelier for her recommendations.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1180;La Buca;Italy;Cesenatico;corso Garibaldi 45, Cesenatico, 47042, Italy;44.200314;12.396823;42;true;true;Seafood, Contemporary;Choose a table on the outdoor summer terrace (right over the water!) at this restaurant in order to best appreciate its location overlooking the picturesque canal port and its period houses. The indoor dining room is also attractive, with its open-view kitchen and modern and elegant feel, while the menu focuses almost exclusively on fish, often served with vegetables, some of which are organic. Enjoy a wide selection of raw antipasti to start (some simple in their preparation, while others are more elaborate), then choose from an array of beautifully presented, modern dishes, such as stuffed mullet with pickled plums and lemon salad, perhaps accompanied by one of the many champagnes included on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1181;La Trattoria Enrico Bartolini;Italy;Castiglione della Pescaia;Località Badiola, Castiglione della Pescaia, 58043, Italy;42.78823;10.97122;69;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Grills;After a majestic picture-postcard approach via a long avenue lined with cypress trees and maritime pines, passing vineyards and Maremma cattle along the way, you finally arrive at this restaurant which serves trattoria-style cuisine full of intense, familiar and reassuring flavours. The decor here is elegant with the occasional rustic touch, while the service is of the highest level yet pleasantly friendly and informal. Welcome to Bartolini’s Maremma restaurant! Here, resident chef Bruno De Moura Cossio offers a choice of dishes with one common denominator, namely charcoal grilling. All the dishes served here have been grilled in some way, so that they have a distinctive barbecued flavour. However, although the chef’s Brazilian origins are obvious in many different ways, the ingredients are resolutely local, some even from the restaurant’s own farm. The friendly service makes guests feel completely at home, while the excellent wine selection is an added attraction – those produced on the estate itself are highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1182;LoRo;Italy;Trescore Balneario;via Bruse 2, Trescore Balneario, 24069, Italy;45.6938611;9.8324198;84;false;true;Creative;The cuisine served at LoRo is imaginative both in its presentation and its ingredients, which are combined in light, original and healthy (in the best sense of the word) dishes. The focus here is on fish and seafood, especially in the antipasti and primi courses, while all the dishes are listed with imaginative names on the menu. Chef Pierantonio Rocchetti reinterprets classic Italian favourites with flair and imagination, serving generous portions that do not skimp on flavour and taking guests on a delicious culinary journey that culminates in his excellent desserts. The restaurant’s “Sala Lab” is home to a large designer-style table that can be transformed to accommodate different numbers of guests, allowing the chef to prepare his dishes directly at the table in an ambience which is friendly and convivial while still maintaining an elegant feel.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1183;Serrae Villa Fiesole;Italy;Fiesole;Via Fra' Giovanni da Fiesole detto l'Angelico 35, Fiesole, 50014, Italy;43.80197;11.2980133;89;true;true;Italian Contemporary;The view of Florence is just one of the many reasons to come to Serrae, which also boasts an attractive renovated decor, a fine location in a Medici villa and, last but certainly not least, superb local cuisine which is imaginative and full of flavour. Bufala tortellini with smoked eel and lovage, and pigeon with liver “olives” are among the highlights.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1184;Casin del Gamba;Italy;Altissimo;via Roccolo Pizzati 1, Altissimo, 36070, Italy;45.6178;11.2615;47;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;The journey to get here – a winding road through woods and hills – may be challenging at times but the warm welcome offered by the whole family Dal Lago at this delightful restaurant makes you feel completely at home and more than compensates for the effort. Owner-chef Antonio shares the honours and duties of his role with long-established sous-chef Biolo. Together, they prepare cuisine that is perfectly balanced between classic flavours and modern trends, using local ingredients that respect the passing seasons. Game features on the menu in winter, while dishes are often seasoned with wild aromatic herbs (for example, the local snails served with thyme and onion bread). For her part, Signora Daria determinedly takes on two roles: she not only prepares the desserts, but also skilfully supervises front of house, ably assisted by son Luca who is happy to advise guests on their choice of wine. The well-structured wine list also includes a good number of organic wines.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1185;Palais Royal Restaurant;Italy;Venice;Calle Larga 22 Marzo 2032, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.4329;12.33462;43;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant is an Italian offshoot of the award-winning Palais Royal in Paris. To the delight of gourmet food-lovers, Greek chef Philip Chronopoulos now also serves his delicious gastronomic creations in Venice, in this restaurant in the Nolinski hotel housed in the former Palazzo della Borsa. The elliptical dining room, with a muffled ambience thanks to its beautiful carpet, has a charm of its own, which lightly harks back to the 1950s. Here, guests have a choice of two tasting menus which showcase cuisine with a Mediterranean flavour, French techniques, numerous Greek influences (including the opening course which reinterprets classic recipes), and Italian ingredients. Top-quality options such as lobster and caviar are prepared with precision and served with real skill – it comes as no surprise to learn that Philip previously worked with renowned chefs such as Joël Robuchon and Alain Passard. An excellent new address for the Venetian Lagoon!;Air conditioning;[]
1187;Ancòra;Italy;Cesenatico;viale Trento 31, Cesenatico, 47042, Italy;44.1955658;12.4042192;26;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;A new adventure for skilful chef Agostino Iacobucci (his original restaurant of the same name is in Castel Maggiore), housed within a villa that food-enthusiasts will remember as the former home of the two-Michelin-star Magnolia. In this elegant and welcoming setting, resident chef Marco Garattoni demonstrates the precise culinary techniques acquired during his many years working in top-quality restaurants. His dishes are contemporary, always colourful, beautifully presented, pleasing and attractive, even mouthwatering at times, and mostly based on fish, with the addition of a few vegetarian and meat options. Don’t miss one of this Neapolitan chef’s most famous signature dishes, namely his “babà a tre lievitazioni”, which is light, delicious and perfect in every way!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
1189;Abbruzzino;Italy;Catanzaro;via Fiume Savuto, località Santo Janni, Catanzaro, 88100, Italy;38.8901852;16.6236902;63;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;Having opened new premises in Lamezia Terme (Abbruzzino Oltre), this restaurant has retained young chef Antonio Fazio (who practically grew up here) at the helm at this address, where he continues to offer dishes that perfectly combine creativity with Calabrian traditions. This remains an excellent choice for anyone in search of regional cuisine reinterpreted with a contemporary twist. Front of house, the service overseen by the chef’s parents Antonio and Rosa is both friendly and professional. The impressive wine list is also influenced by the family’s love for the region, with one section completely dedicated to local labels, and another that focuses on wines from elsewhere in Italy and further afield. We particularly enjoyed the many delicious appetisers, as well as the rice with peas, pecorino and oysters, and the house signature dessert (bread, oil and sugar), which always features on the menu. Choose from two surprise tasting menus and a small à la carte.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1190;San Giorgio;Italy;Genoa;viale Brigate Bisagno 69r, Genoa, 16129, Italy;44.4016634;8.945731;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Ligurian;Situated in the city albeit not right in the centre, San Giorgio is a typical Genovese restaurant – elegant and classic in style, with excellent cuisine served by the Scala family who have been in charge for decades. Young chef Samuele Di Mauro is at the helm, having started here as an apprentice and worked his way to the position of sous-chef and then head chef in 2022. Despite a focus on modern presentation and techniques, as demonstrated in dishes such as the raw bluefin tuna seasoned with an intense verbena mousse and served with caper cream and a “caviar” of dried and fried tuna, his cuisine is Mediterranean in style, with its roots in Ligurian aromas and flavours. The wine list is as impressive as the cuisine, with an entire section dedicated to French and Italian sparkling wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1191;Dalla Gioconda;Italy;Gabicce Monte;via dell'Orizzonte 2, Gabicce Monte, 61011, Italy;43.963886;12.7725315;61;true;true;Country cooking, Creative;Between the blue sky and the Adriatic Sea, at the highest point of Gabicce Monte, Dalla Gioconda is the gourmet rebirth of a renowned dancing venue in the town. The design is warm, conceived and created with sustainability in mind. Thanks to a long experience at the Osteria Francescana of Massimo Bottura, the talented chef Davide Di Fabio creates precise and beautiful dishes, cooked with the best ingredients of the territory and of their own garden. The cellar hides real gems, and the summer terrace offers moments of sheer beauty.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1192;Cannavacciuolo Le Cattedrali Asti;Italy;Asti;frazione Valleandona 1/b, Asti, 14100, Italy;44.9078373;8.1173043;61;true;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in the hills outside Asti, this modern inn with guestrooms is nestled in around 18 hectares of woodland and meadows. The interior decor here is contemporary and minimalist, while the cuisine is overseen by the famous three-Michelin-star chef Antonino Cannavacciuolo, with resident chef Gianluca Renzi, who has already proved his worth at other top-quality restaurants, at the helm in the kitchen. Originally from Rome and having trained professionally in various locations, this chef creates cuisine that combines personal imaginative touches with regional influences, including traditional flavours from the Piedmont. The superb wine list features more than 2 000 labels, including an impressive selection of Barolo and Barbaresco wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1193;Pascucci al Porticciolo;Italy;Fiumicino;viale Traiano 85, angolo via Fiumara 2, Fiumicino, 00054, Italy;41.770165;12.2271443;73;true;true;Seafood;A focus on the sea underpins the whole philosophy of this restaurant, which is perhaps not surprising at a coastal location such as Fiumicino! Here, chef Pascucci celebrates the sea to the full on his “Come è profondo il mare” menu which showcases beautifully presented dishes accompanied by a wine list that celebrates local producers from the Lazio coast. The chef selects top-quality local ingredients which he prepares with an almost Oriental precision – we particularly recommend the raw gurnard with ceviche, Kaluga-Amur caviar and courgettes. Vanessa oversees the dedicated front-of-house team, who provide warm and attentive service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1194;Zur Rose;Italy;San Michele;via Josef Innerhofer 2, San Michele, 39057, Italy;46.455093;11.258857;63;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The long-established Zur Rose is a gourmet restaurant that has certainly made its mark along the romantic Tyrolean Wine Route. Here, chef Herbert Hintner serves his own version of creative, contemporary cuisine (ably assisted for the past five years by his son Daniel) which has a strong regional identity influenced by the Alto Adige, in an elegant building dating back to 1300 – the restaurant has been known as “La Rosa” since 1585. Ingredients and dishes change depending on the time of year, with two menus each season, one regional, the other vegetarian. Riding the crest of a wave for decades, Hintner’s cuisine never falters and continues to offer an unmissable gourmet experience.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1195;Votavota;Italy;Marina di Ragusa;lungomare Andrea Doria 48, Marina di Ragusa, 97010, Italy;36.7826492;14.5571721;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;The perfect choice for those who love the sea, courtesy of the splendid views of the Mediterranean through the picture windows in the dining room. Guests can observe the two chefs at work in the open-view kitchen, where they prepare top-quality and surprisingly creative dishes, with an obvious focus on fish and seafood. We particularly recommend the smoked spaghetti with butter and anchovies – a creamy dish full of intense flavours, which is seemingly simple yet demonstrates real culinary expertise and makes the journey here well worthwhile! The wine list includes an excellent selection of Sicilian labels, from Etna to the offshore islands – the sommelier will be happy to help with recommendations. Why not start your meal with the superb 700 di Cusumano, a top-quality Chardonnay and Pinot Nero blend?;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
1196;La Ciau del Tornavento;Italy;Treiso;piazza Leopoldo Baracco 7, Treiso, 12050, Italy;44.68925;8.08667;19;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Country cooking;Situated amid the Barbaresco hills just a few kilometres from Alba, this restaurant boasts views of the surrounding countryside, as well as an extraordinary wine cellar (which can be visited on request) and a quality of cuisine of the highest level. The menu offers an extensive choice of meat and fish dishes, from classic favourites to new creations, in a joint celebration of the past and present.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1197;Johannesstube;Italy;Nova Levante;via San Valentino 3, Nova Levante, 39056, Italy;46.4296498;11.5334034;83;true;true;Alpine, Modern Cuisine;The strictly regional ingredients used at this restaurant are sourced from local farmers and producers, with just a few exceptions such as sugar, truffles, salt, rice etc. Chef Theodor Falser is a purist where the region’s plentiful produce is concerned, although he does admit to a weakness for cooking and fermentation methods from further afield. He considers himself fortunate to have been born in these mountains and this good fortune is shared by those who are lucky enough to dine in this historic Stube-style restaurant built using vintage wood, which is the jewel in the Engel hotel’s crown. There’s also an excellent wine list with a focus on the Alto Adige.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1198;Al Sorriso;Italy;Soriso;via Roma 18, Soriso, 28010, Italy;45.7406906;8.4116747;49;false;true;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Fans of Piedmontese cuisine will be in their element in this restaurant situated in the attractive Novara hills thanks to enthusiastic chef Luisa Marelli and her husband Angelo Valazza. The latter is constantly on the lookout for excellent local ingredients, while his wife (a literature graduate and self-taught chef who is passionate about cooking) creates dishes which have become classics, are influenced by tradition and prepared with seasonal ingredients such as aromatic herbs, game, mushrooms and truffles. The wine list is particularly extensive.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1199;Il Papavero;Italy;Eboli;corso Garibaldi 112/113, Eboli, 84025, Italy;40.6190612;15.0539834;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Campanian;Papavero is the Italian for poppy, a plant which grows tall and has strong roots, making it an apt symbol for this restaurant housed in a palazzo in the town centre. In a few classic-style rooms, the chef offers a menu that focuses on fish and seafood, although ingredients from the surrounding countryside also feature. Simple, solid recipes made with just a few ingredients, exactly as described on the menu, and a passionate dedication to the Mediterranean result in attractive cuisine which also offers good value for money. In fine weather, meals are served outdoors under the jasmine in a romantic garden. A restaurant that appeals to the heart as well as the palate.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1200;Locanda San Lorenzo;Italy;Puos d'Alpago;via IV Novembre 79, Puos d'Alpago, 32016, Italy;46.1395908;12.363875;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The Dal Farra family opened this inn way back in 1900, when the current owner-chef Renzo’s grandparents established a simple osteria-style restaurant to provide meals for workers at the nearby mill. In the 1950s, Renzo’s parents took over at the helm, with a Michelin star awarded to the restaurant in 1997. Passion and consistency are the characteristics that have drawn guests to this restaurant for over a century: the cuisine makes full use of regional ingredients in dishes that have occasionally been reinterpreted with a modern twist. Some guests may prefer the modern dining room, although regulars may well choose the more rustic-style room, where two of the tables are laid out right in front of the fireplace. There’s a good selection of wine, plus a few simple guestrooms on the upper floors.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1201;Zash;Italy;Archi;SP 2 I/II 60, Archi, 95018, Italy;37.7079174;15.1998992;72;true;false;Creative;Once through the entrance gate, make your way through an orchard planted with citrus trees to get to this restaurant occupying a charming, carefully restored 19C “palmento” (a building once used for fermenting wine) that has retained its magical and romantic atmosphere. Here, Giuseppe Raciti’s top-quality cuisine is showcased on themed tasting menus from which dishes can also be chosen à la carte. The chef’s recipes are full of references to the island, as well as personal influences which he describes as “ricordi, viaggi, esperienze” (memories, travels, experiences). Elegant guestrooms dotted around the property add to the appeal of this truly idyllic property.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1202;Del Cambio;Italy;Turin;piazza Carignano 2, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0695181;7.6848806;29;true;true;Contemporary;Del Cambio, Turin’s historic restaurant par excellence, is Piedmont’s crowning jewel, with few equals in the whole of Europe. Here, the meticulously restored Risorgimento room, with origins that back to the 18C, features a decor and furnishings that are almost entirely from the 19C. The creaking parquet flooring, also original, accompanies your entry into this historic setting: Cavour had his own window table here to watch over the Palazzo Carignano, the first parliament of the newly united Italy. Another room (Pistoletto), simpler and more informal in feel, can be found behind its more historic sibling. Although Matteo Baronetto’s cuisine takes inspiration from the past with some regionally inspired dishes, he also creates more imaginative and original fare. In addition to wines by the glass, the extraordinary wine list will delight wine-buffs, especially with its choice of Barolo and Barbaresco labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1204;Primo Restaurant;Italy;Lecce;via 47° Reggimento Fanteria 7, Lecce, 73100, Italy;40.3526;18.177374;19;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;With just a few tables in a small room crowned by a typical vaulted ceiling in Lecce stone, this candle-lit restaurant is home to young chef Solaika Marrocco, who was born in 1995 in nearby Gallipoli. Here, she creates modern, highly personalised dishes which are not only a feast for the eyes but also for the palate. Despite her young age, this chef produces refined, elegantly simple cuisine which is never dull, and which often showcases ingredients from Puglia and the Salento. She also happily uses old traditional recipes to inspire her, creating her own bold, original and decidedly contemporary interpretations of traditional regional dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1205;Bluh Furore;Italy;Furore;via Dell'Amore 2, Furore, 84010, Italy;40.6152174;14.5423636;40;false;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The former Furore Inn hotel has reopened with a new contemporary Mediterranean look and a new name (the Furore Grand Hotel ), along with a new gourmet restaurant, the Bluh Furore. Boasting a white colour scheme, minimalist decor and attractive sea views, the restaurant is headed by executive chef Vincenzo Russo under the banner of famous three-Michelin-starred Enrico Bartolini, who is behind some of its legendary signature dishes, such as the half-fried prawn. The menu focuses on modern dishes that feature recipes and ingredients from Campania. A vegetarian tasting menu completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1206;Castello di Fighine;Italy;San Casciano dei Bagni;borgo di Fighine, San Casciano dei Bagni, 53040, Italy;42.88651;11.915653;18;true;true;Contemporary;A dirt track leads to this magical setting – an 11C castle perched among the Tuscan hills which is now privately owned and has been restored and renovated over the past 15 years. Situated in the hamlet surrounding the castle, the restaurant boasts a beautiful terrace shaded by wisteria where meals are served in fine weather. In the kitchen, the successful partnership between new resident chef Francesco Nunziata and three-starred Michelin chef Heinz Beck is immediately obvious. Two apartments are available in Casa Parretti for anyone wishing to prolong their stay here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1207;Il Luogo Aimo e Nadia;Italy;Milan;via Montecuccoli 6, Milan, 20147, Italy;45.458435;9.130776;39;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant has been part of the Milanese culinary scene for over 60 years and continues to attract food-lovers in search of top-quality cuisine today. It serves two tasting menus that showcase Italian cuisine in modern dishes, some inspired by the origins of the two chefs, Alessandro Negrini and Fabio Pisani (the former from Lombardy, the latter from Puglia). Make sure you allow plenty of time to peruse the extensive wine list which is displayed on a tablet and includes some hard-to-find labels. The service is courteous and attentive throughout.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1208;Dolada;Italy;Pieve d'Alpago;via Dolada 21, località Plois alt. 870, Pieve d'Alpago, 32010, Italy;46.1736379;12.3601001;19;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;An idyllic picture-postcard setting in a panoramic location overlooking Santa Croce lake, surrounded by villages and mountain peaks. This is matched by an elegant interior with a mix of antique and modern furnishings, and a succession of stylish small dining rooms and lounges, including an open fireplace where many of the ingredients are cooked. For over a century, this restaurant has told the story of the De Pra family and their love for the mountains which is clearly evident in the cuisine served here. Chef Riccardo has strengthened this connection by intensifying his search for local ingredients (game, mushrooms, freshwater fish etc) and cultivating his own kitchen garden and vineyard. The fragrant ingredients are prepared simply yet with technical expertise, with flavour always the primary focus – an infallible recipe for resounding success!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1209;Achilli al Parlamento;Italy;Rome;via dei Prefetti 15, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9024619;12.4769426;98;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Situated just a stone’s throw from the Parliament building, this elegant restaurant’s origins as a wine bar are visible in the many wine bottles that line the walls of the dining room. Various tasting menus feature creative dishes with the occasional influence from Campania in top-quality cuisine that is rooted in traditional flavours. There’s a huge choice of wines by the glass, while bottles can be chosen directly from the wine boutique. In the room nearest the entrance, you’ll find the bistro which serves simpler fare and is also open at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1210;La Magnolia;Italy;Forte dei Marmi;viale Morin 46, Forte dei Marmi, 55042, Italy;43.9497169;10.1774953;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed within the Lord Byron hotel, one of Forte del Marmi’s best hotels, this restaurant serves technically skilful and sophisticated cuisine which is striking and beautifully presented. The menu features meat and fish dishes with local and international influences, as well as a strong flavour of Campania, the chef’s native region. The excellent bread deserves a particular mention.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
1211;Andreina;Italy;Loreto;via Zona Industriale Brodolini, 2, Loreto, 60025, Italy;43.4404449;13.6208829;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Meats and Grills;Sixty years after this restaurant was opened by his grandmother Andreina, Errico Recanati continues to add his own distinctive mark to the family business. Following the complete renovation of the farmhouse interior, the dining rooms are even more elegant and welcoming than before. Here, the excellent staff offer attentive and discreet service, while the cuisine, rooted in local traditions, focuses especially on game and grilled dishes. The only features that have survived in the dining room are the grill and the fireplace! Recanati’s distinctive style makes full use of fire, charcoal embers and the afore-mentioned grill and spit: he is a real expert in the latter, enabling delightful grilled flavours and aromas to make their way into most of his dishes, which he often personalises by adding fruit and vegetables from his own garden. All of this contributes to what the chef himself describes as his “neo-rural” style of cuisine, which is beautifully illuminated by new lamps arranged on the tables with the precision of a stage set.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1213;Angelo Sabatelli;Italy;Putignano;via Santa Chiara 1, Putignano, 70017, Italy;40.8500527;17.1227135;61;false;true;Country cooking, Asian Influences;A talented and brilliant chef is at the helm in this restaurant in the town’s historic centre, where elegant, contemporary-style dining rooms provide the backdrop for technical cuisine that showcases local produce with the occasional added Asian flavour. A visit to the large, well-stocked wine cellar is highly recommended (there’s an excellent selection of sparkling wines and champagnes), where a couple of beautiful tables are used for tasting and private dinners.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1214;Il Pievano;Italy;Gaiole in Chianti;Località Spaltenna 13, Gaiole in Chianti, 53013, Italy;43.4654463;11.4293865;58;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Occupying the charming, romantic setting of a thousand-year-old monastery, this restaurant serves meals either in its Sala dei Papi dining room or at tables arranged in a delightful inner courtyard. Either way, you’re in the capable hands of young chef Stelios Sakalis who originally hails from Greece. He offers three tasting menus (one is a surprise menu) on which Tuscan and Greek traditions are reinterpreted with a contemporary look and flavour. We particularly enjoyed the many delicious starters, as well as the acorn-flour buttons with red prawns (saganaki) and the excellent pastry desserts. Make sure you try the Cantina del Castello wines which are made from the restaurant’s own grapes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1215;La Locanda del Borgo;Italy;Telese;località Monte Pugliano 1, Telese, 82037, Italy;41.2259613;14.5341855;70;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;Chef Luciano Villani creates menus that focus on simplicity, organic produce from the Sannio region and an uncompromising philosophy. The restaurant is situated within the Hotel Acquapetra Resort&Spa, once an old farmhouse transformed into a luxurious hamlet, where antique furnishings and modern cutting-edge facilities combine to ensure a delightful stay in elegant surroundings. The gourmet restaurant adds to its appeal, featuring cuisine that is delicious and always recognisably regional, albeit with the occasional influence from elsewhere. There are two tasting menus: Aqua (fish dishes only) and Petra (dedicated to meat dishes). Aperitifs and drinks are served in the charming bar next to the restaurant.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1216;Tre Olivi;Italy;Paestum;via Poseidonia 41, Paestum, 84047, Italy;40.42511;14.98659;41;true;true;Creative, Campanian;Oliver Glowig, German by birth but Italian by adoption, has returned to Campania where he’s now at the helm in the gourmet restaurant at the Savoy Beach Hotel. Here, his cuisine is showcased on two tasting menus (with dishes also available à la carte style) with many of his zero-mile ingredients sourced from the property’s own kitchen garden. He makes every effort to bring out the best of the Cilento’s abundant produce and typical Mediterranean recipes in his dishes which are contemporary in flavour and appearance. The restaurant’s only structural change is the new private room, which boasts its own kitchen, which can be used to host private events. The front of house also has new staff, whose skills ensure that guests are looked after with careful attention. When it comes to choosing wine, sommelier Roberto is on hand with his expert recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1217;Osteria Arbustico;Italy;Paestum;via Francesco Gregorio 40, Paestum, 84047, Italy;40.451699;14.9758186;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Campanian;Housed within the Royal Paestum hotel, this elegant, contemporary restaurant boasts an attractively simple and minimalist ambience in which owner-chef Cristian Torsiello’s cuisine takes centre stage. This 40-year-old chef (originally from Valva, a district of Salerno where the Osteria was first opened) showcases creative ideas and techniques in his search for perfect combinations. His deceptively simple dishes always allow the flavour of his locally sourced ingredients to shine through – his iconic spaghetti with saffron is a perfect example. For this dish, he prepares dried Gragnono pasta in the same way as a risotto, using a broth made with one-third beef stock, one-third parmesan cheese and one-third onions. He then blends this with sour butter and Abruzzo saffron to create a dish that is truly delicious and seemingly simple, despite its complex preparation. The wine list continues to evolve, boasting some 600 labels and including a few rare regional wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1218;San Martino;Italy;Scorzè;piazza Cappelletto 1, località Rio San Martino, Scorzè, 30037, Italy;45.5892243;12.110501;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A smart, elegant restaurant with a bright, minimalist decor in which large tables are well spaced out to create an exclusive feel. The chef’s wife brings a touch of friendly informality to the restaurant, along with an impressive knowledge of the excellent wine list, which offers a wide array of sparkling wines and champagnes. The cuisine here is modern and personalised, with a slight emphasis on fish, although meat dishes also feature.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1219;Il Buco;Italy;Sorrento;II rampa Marina Piccola 5, Sorrento, 80067, Italy;40.6272425;14.3750106;24;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the centre of Sorrento, this restaurant boasts a historic dining room housed in the 16C cellars of an old monastery, as well as a more contemporary-style room with an open-view wine cellar that displays an impressive selection of more than 1 600 different bottles. Wherever you choose to sit, you’ll enjoy cuisine influenced by the culinary traditions of Campania, albeit with a few imaginative touches. Chef Giuseppe Aversa’s first courses deserve a particular mention, especially the linguine with lemon-marinated scorpion fish, bottarga and dried tomatoes, and the gnocchi on a Neapolitan ragù with basil pesto and salted ricotta cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1220;Terrazza Bosquet;Italy;Sorrento;piazza Tasso 34, Sorrento, 80067, Italy;40.6284812;14.3758036;26;false;true;Creative;In the heart of Sorrento, a delightful garden leads like a long corridor up to the entrance of the Excelsior Vittoria, one of the most iconic hotels on the Sorrentine peninsula, where this gourmet restaurant sets out its tables on a panoramic terrace as soon as the weather allows (otherwise, guests eat indoors). Here, chef Antonino Montefusco prepares various tasting menus (including a vegetarian option) with dishes inspired by recipes and ingredients from Campania, all reinterpreted with an elegant, aesthetic touch. There’s an extensive wine list, including an excellent choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1221;Vespasia;Italy;Norcia;via Cesare Battisti 10, Norcia, 06046, Italy;42.7925634;13.0920268;30;false;false;Umbrian, Creative;Situated in the historic centre of Noto which is slowly returning to life after the earthquake, this restaurant is part of the smart Palazzo Seneca hotel. You pass through a succession of small rooms to get to the elegant Sala del Vespasia, where a female Japanese chef now showcases the best of Umbrian gastronomic delights after many years working in Campania and renowned restaurants elsewhere in Italy. Olive oil, cured hams, lentils, Cannara onions, crayfish and river fish, lamb from the Sibillini mountains and, of course, the excellent local black truffle are used in her creative and occasional complex dishes. Our description would not be complete without mentioning the excellent service and warm, friendly welcome offered by the Bianconi, a long-established family in Norcia’s hotel and restaurant sector.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1222;Atelier;Italy;Domodossola;piazza Matteotti 36, Domodossola, 28845, Italy;46.1149939;8.2957587;30;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;The long-established Atelier is not only one of the leading restaurants in Domodossola, it is also the first ever in the Val d’Ossola to be awarded a Michelin star, adding to the tourist appeal of the town. Here, owner-chef Giorgio Bartolucci, flanked by his enterprising sister Elisabetta, has succeeded in skilfully and enthusiastically breathing new life into this restaurant which was founded by his parents, while his wife Katia oversees the impeccable service front of house with professionalism and a friendly smile. The bespoke open-view kitchen (made by local craftsmen and almost as big as the dining room) is definitely intended to be a distinctive feature which the energetic chef hopes will create a real connection between guests and his team. Flavour, variety and presentation are the keystones of the cuisine at Atelier, where the dishes are exciting, inspirational and occasionally feature intriguing reinterpretations of traditional local recipes.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1223;Locanda Don Serafino;Italy;Ragusa;via Avv. Ottaviano 13, Ragusa, 97100, Italy;36.9245977;14.7407767;81;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;Situated on the ring road which runs around Ibla, one of the most charming and picturesque historic districts in Sicily, this restaurant is as delightful as its surroundings. Despite being partly built into the rock, the dining room here is elegant rather than rustic and the service highly attentive, making this the perfect choice for a romantic, gourmet dinner. Vincenzo Candiano is an extraordinary chef who continues to experiment with new dishes, combining classic favourites with other more innovative recipes (still with a Sicilian influence) on his menu. There’s also a renowned wine list with some superb vertical tasting options, plus one guestroom on the premises and others within walking distance in the charming hotel of the same name.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1224;Locanda Mammì;Italy;Agnone;contrada Castelnuovo 86, Agnone, 86081, Italy;41.8299804;14.3839118;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated amid beautiful countryside with views of the tranquil hills and rustic farmhouses that surround it, this restaurant is home to young and talented chef Stefania Di Pasquo who creates dishes using regional ingredients to which she adds her own personalised and modern touch. The wine list, which also includes a few champagnes, is skilfully overseen by the chef’s husband, sommelier Thomas Torsiello, while the dining room with its warm, romantic ambience, open fireplace and copper items on display, is in complete harmony with its surroundings. Guestrooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1225;Tilia;Italy;Toblach;via Dolomiti 31/b, Toblach, 39034, Italy;46.7236326;12.2241114;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This glass and steel cube in the middle of the garden of the former Grand Hotel in Dobbiaco has been home to the Tilia restaurant since 2010 and is now more intimate than ever, with just five tables and seating for 12 diners (booking is highly recommended). Chef Chris Oberhammer’s menu is enticing, featuring just under 20 dishes with a modern yet regional flavour. Many of the ingredients (such as the flour and some of the meat) are sourced from the “Klaude” farm which is run by one of the chef’s childhood friends with whom he works very closely, while other more exotic fare comes from further afield, adding luxury ingredients such as caviar, truffles (in season) and prawns to the mix. Anita Mancini oversees the front of house with skill and professionalism, as well as taking care of the wine list which includes a selection of international labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1226;La Sala dei Grappoli;Italy;Montalcino;Castello di Poggio alle Mura, Montalcino, 53024, Italy;42.980553;11.399909;98;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A beautiful drive through typical picture-postcard Tuscan scenery of vineyards, cypress and olive trees takes you to the imposing medieval Castello Banfi, which stands proudly in front of this restaurant. La Sala dei Grappoli takes its name from the vines depicted in frescoes on the walls of its dining room, although in fine weather you’ll want to take advantage of the outdoor terrace where the beautiful views combine with impeccable service and superb cuisine to offer an unforgettable experience. Originally from Puglia, chef Domenico Francone includes Puglian specialities on the menu, such as his taralli and exquisite panzerotti. Despite this, the chef has completely embraced Tuscan cuisine (often from the Maremma) which he interprets with real creativity, adding a personal touch to some of the region’s classic dishes. The wine list includes Castello Banfi’s fine Brunello wines, with recommendations provided by the excellent sommelier.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1227;Guidoristorante;Italy;Serralunga d'Alba;via Alba 15, Serralunga d'Alba, 12050, Italy;44.6414;7.98265;47;false;false;Piedmontese, Contemporary;Lidia and Guido Alciati opened their restaurant in 1961 and Italian cuisine has not been the same since – their hard work signalled the beginning of real change which revolutionised cooking in Italy. They were among the first to understand the importance of regional ingredients, sourcing excellent produce which Lidia then showcased in her superb dishes, while Guido was responsible for the attentive service and excellent wine list. Their teachings live on in the sumptuous dining rooms in Villa Fontanafredda, where their children continue the culinary traditions established by their parents. Ugo’s sensitive skills in the kitchen and Piero’s experience front of house contribute to the success of this restaurant, where the best food and wine from the region in served in deceptively simple dishes that have few equals. One of the highlights is the plin (stuffed agnolotti pasta closed with a “pinch” by Lidia), which has drawn visitors here from all around the world and which is as delicious as ever – the pasta is stuffed with meat and vegetables and served with a velvety meat sauce. A modern fireplace adds a contemporary feel to the austere, old-fashioned elegance in one of the dining rooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1228;Prezioso;Italy;Merano;via Fragsburg 3, Merano, 39012, Italy;46.642062;11.1910522;92;false;true;Alpine, Creative;Once you leave Merano, you follow a road through the woods for about 5km to reach Castel Fragsburg, a small, fairytale-like residence with an elegant feel and guestrooms decorated in the traditional style of the southern Tyrol. At the gourmet Prezioso restaurant, in fine weather lucky diners can choose to sit on one of the most spectacular terraces in Italy, perched high above the valley. In the kitchen, chef Egon Heiss demonstrates his culinary talent on a single tasting menu of creative dishes which are made mostly from local mountain ingredients, sourced from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden and other producers from the nearby mountain valleys. The menu nearly always features char and trout, as well as wild game and top-quality meat – the Val di Funes lamb served in two courses (the first as a pink fillet served with its own jus and confit tomatoes, the second a mouthwatering shoulder of lamb with aromatic herbs served with parsley polenta) is truly delicious.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1229;Borgo San Jacopo;Italy;Florence;borgo San Jacopo 62 r, Florence, 50125, Italy;43.7680838;11.251472;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Housed within the Hotel Lungarno, one of the most charming hotels in the city, this restaurant boasts the same elegant and exclusive style as the hotel. Chef Claudio Mengoni is at the helm here, having gained experience working in various Michelin-starred restaurants before returning home to Florence about three years ago. Here, he transforms carefully chosen Italian ingredients into refined fish, meat and vegetable dishes which respect the seasons and are beautifully presented. Sommelier Salvatore Biscotti is responsible for the excellent wine selection, which includes around a thousand different labels featuring renowned estates and small producers alike. It’s well worth booking one of the few romantic tables overlooking the Arno.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1230;Il Tiglio;Italy;Montemonaco;via Isola San Biagio 34, Montemonaco, 63088, Italy;42.9182376;13.316814;56;true;true;Contemporary, Cuisine from the Marches;It's quite a journey to reach the slopes at the foot of the Sibillini mountains where chef Enrico Mazzaroni’s restaurant is situated, but the effort to get here is more than compensated by the exquisite cuisine on the menu! Although the chef’s great passion is for regional ingredients such as mushrooms, trout, venison and potatoes (much of which is produced at his own agriturismo), his approach is decidedly creative and his recipes highly original. Balanced flavours are to the fore in dishes such as trout and veal with mushrooms thanks to the chef’s technical expertise, while over the years his presentation has become even more photogenic. A successful mix of experience and youth ensures excellent service, which adds to the enjoyable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1231;Due Camini;Italy;Savelletri;Strada Comunale Egnazia, Savelletri, 72015, Italy;40.8760649;17.396077;46;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;This is the most romantic restaurant in the Borgo Egnazia resort, where the soft candlelight creates a hushed, magical atmosphere that makes it perfect for a special occasion, dinner with a loved one, or simply a gourmet meal. Enjoy excellent service as you embark on a gastronomic journey that introduces you to specialities from chef Domingo Schingaro’s Puglia, dishes inspired by the region, and recipes influenced by the wider Mediterranean (depending on the menu). Many of the ingredients are sourced from the hotel’s own kitchen garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1232;Veritas;Italy;Naples;corso Vittorio Emanuele 141, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8372277;14.2311901;40;true;false;Campanian, Contemporary;Situated near the Vomero district, this welcoming restaurant offers attentive service and has an excellent sommelier who will be happy to guide you in your choice of wine, including recommendations from exciting small wineries in Campania. The cuisine is showcased on three tasting menus: Essenziale, Autentico and Libero, the last of which is the most typical of chef Caputi’s cuisine, with its focus on local flavours and decidedly contrasting combinations. We particularly enjoyed the spaghetti with clams, pine nuts and lemons – a pleasingly bold play on sweet and sour flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1233;Shalai;Italy;Linguaglossa;via Guglielmo Marconi 25, Linguaglossa, 95015, Italy;37.8433039;15.1419716;60;true;false;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the historic centre of Linguaglossa, one of the most picturesque villages around Etna, this restaurant is part of the highly recommended hotel of the same name which occupies a delightful 19C palazzo. The Pennisi family are at the helm, alongside chef Giovanni Santoro, a partnership which has resulted in a long-standing Michelin star here on the slopes of Mt Etna. Santoro creates extraordinarily varied cuisine, which is not surprising given that Linguaglossa is situated in a mountainous region with rich volcanic soil that produces a whole host of unrivalled ingredients, with the added advantage of being just a few kilometres from the sea. Superb wine list, including magnums, vertical wines and top-quality labels from Etna.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1234;Il Fagiano;Italy;Fasano del Garda;corso Zanardelli 190, Fasano del Garda, 25083, Italy;45.622704;10.570339;42;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;In the sumptuous setting of the Grand Hotel Fasano, this restaurant decorated with a profusion of wood has just a few tables, where guests can choose between tasting menus (including a vegetarian option) and an à la carte selection. Although influences from chef Maurizio Bufi’s native Puglia and the Lake Garda region can be detected in the cuisine, other Italian regions (and indeed other countries) also make an appearance in the creative dishes, which are inspired by whatever ingredients are in season.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1235;Il Cantinone e Sport Hotel Alpina;Italy;Madesimo;via A. De Giacomi 39, Madesimo, 23024, Italy;46.44052;9.35916;24;false;true;Contemporary;A family restaurant run with pride and enthusiasm, Il Cantinone delights guests with its array of local gastronomic delicacies sourced from the surrounding mountains and nearby lake, including ingredients such as buckwheat, trout, whitefish and eel, along with polenta, mushrooms and game. The menu also occasionally features more exotic influences acquired by chef Stefano Masanti during his time spent travelling the world before he returned to his beloved mountains.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1236;Maeba Restaurant;Italy;Ariano Irpino;contrada Serra 29, Ariano Irpino, 83031, Italy;41.1211871;15.0655007;40;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This charming restaurant is built on the site of an old 18C olive oil mill (part of which is still used as a convivial wine cellar) in a secluded and tranquil location. The rest of the building is modern, elegant and colourful, while the delightful outdoor space boasts a garden overlooking the surrounding hills and olive trees. Since early 2024, a former sous-chef here has returned to take over at the helm in the kitchen, where he creates dishes that mirror the modern simplicity of the setting. He offers a carefully prepared blind tasting menu (booking ahead is mandatory and you choose your number of courses when you book) that focuses on local ingredients and makes ample use of vegetables.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1237;L'Argine a Vencò;Italy;Dolegna del Collio;Località Vencò 15, Dolegna del Collio, 34070, Italy;46.0025426;13.4631925;25;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;This perfectly restored old mill is home to a chef who creates original cuisine that demonstrates her connection with her region and showcases ingredients grown in the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, especially the aromatic herbs that are a characteristic feature of many of the dishes served here. Antonia Klugmann’s house stands in attractive unspoilt scenery near the Slovenian border and in the middle of two major wine-producing areas, namely the Colli Orientali del Friuli and the better-known Collio, both of which are well represented on the extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1238;Romano;Italy;Viareggio;via Mazzini 120, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.8722767;10.2482771;46;false;true;Seafood;Opened in 1966, Romano is a real culinary institution in the Versilia region, serving cuisine made from top-quality ingredients, with a particular focus on local fish. Although its philosophy has not changed over the years, current chef Nicola Gronchi should be applauded for adding a hint of contemporary flavour and technical expertise to the cuisine, while still retaining everything that this restaurant does best, namely serving fish of the highest quality (there are also a few meat dishes), including the occasional typical Versilian recipe.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1239;Capriccio;Italy;Manerba del Garda;piazza San Bernardo 6, località Montinelle, Manerba del Garda, 25080, Italy;45.55285;10.56121;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;This restaurant standing on the shores of Lake Garda has been famous ever since it opened in the mid-1960s, thanks to its female owner’s passion for fish and seafood from the Mediterranean. Today, Giuliana continues to showcase fresh fish in her classic-style recipes and demonstrates real skill in bringing out the full flavour of her ingredients on a menu which also includes a few meat specialities. Among her memorable historic dishes are the aubergine parmigiana (on the menu since 1965) and the red berry soup marinated in cooked wine must and served with ice-cream and Italian-style meringue. Daughter Francesca offers guests a friendly welcome front of house, assisting them with their choice of dishes and also providing wine pairing recommendations. The interesting wine list will delight lovers of champagne and German Riesling. In summer, take a seat in the large, comfortable outdoor dining space with the restaurant’s bucolic garden in front of you and the lake in the background.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1240;Il Cappero;Italy;Isola Vulcano;via Vulcanello, Isola Vulcano, 98055, Italy;38.4308153;14.9570928;94;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The change of chef at this restaurant is echoed by the excellent level of cuisine on offer here. Young Onofrio Pagnotto, who was already sous-chef at the resort’s Tenerumi restaurant and who is supported by the hotel’s executive chef Davide Guidara, offers two tasting menus (one shorter than the other). Both menus showcase local ingredients prepared with technical expertise to create contemporary, Mediterranean dishes that are full of flavour. Onofrio is not afraid to use the occasional French sauce, as well as his beloved fermentations in his dishes. As a final flourish, the desserts come courtesy of Gianluca Colucci, the pastry chef shared with Tenerumi. After enjoying a first, delicious dessert in the dining room, guests move to the “pasticceria” corner where pastry chefs “improvise” a final dessert in line with guests’ preferences. Last but not least, the restaurant boasts a superb setting within the Therasia Resort perched on the Vulcanello promontory above the sea, with breathtaking views of the Aeolian islands often enhanced by blazing sunsets.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1241;La Tana Gourmet;Italy;Asiago;via Kaberlaba 19, Asiago, 36012, Italy;45.85289;11.49528;19;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Once a mountain refuge, the red house that overlooks this plateau is now home to one of the most interesting and avant-garde gourmet restaurants in Italy. Founder Alessandro Dal Degan, who offers a long surprise tasting menu (a culinary voyage, as he calls it), will take you on a journey through his beloved mountains, the Adriatic and beyond. Entrust yourself to his care in a spirit of curiosity and openness and prepare to explore new horizons. Dishes often include combinations that will sound unusual to you, but instead of picking these apart and thinking about the individual components, try to savour their complex, contrasting and yet harmonious flavours. As a result, this new and extraordinary experience will introduce you to some remarkable and occasionally unforgettable dishes. In addition to the musical backdrop (which provides the perfect soundtrack to the cuisine), special mention should be made of the wine pairings that come courtesy of business partner Enrico Maglio, who oversees the carefully researched and surprising wine list. The partnership with various local suppliers, which helps to showcase the region’s produce, is also highly commendable.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1242;Sissi;Italy;Merano;via Galilei 44, Merano, 39012, Italy;46.6738587;11.1608085;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated just outside the pedestrianised area of beautiful Merano, the main dining room of this restaurant has a welcoming feel and is decorated in attractive Art-Nouveau style. Here, owner-chef Andrea Fenoglio divides his time between the kitchen and front of house so that he can take time to chat with guests. His cuisine has solid classic foundations, with a good choice of dishes on the à la carte, plus a surprise tasting menu (Settepiatti ) which changes every year (as does the ceramic tableware on which it is served!). The cuisine is comforting and full of generous flavours, to which Fenoglio adds a light modern touch with his carefully chosen accompaniments and presentation. Whatever dish you choose, you can be sure of finding the perfect wine pairing for your meal on the skilfully constructed wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1244;21.9;Italy;Piobesi d'Alba;Località Carretta 4, Piobesi d'Alba, 12040, Italy;44.7326422;7.9903827;19;true;true;Country cooking, Creative;Run by chef Flavio Costa, Ligurian by birth and Piedmontese by adoption, this restaurant is named after the date his twin daughters were born. Housed on an estate that was producing wine as early as the 15C, the restaurant boasts stunning views of the surrounding hills and vineyards. Here, Flavio creates imaginative cuisine that harmoniously combines ingredients from Piedmont (meat) and Liguria (fish), as well as more contemporary combinations. We particularly enjoyed the pigeon, turnip greens and sweetcorn, as well as the chocolate, sweet beetroot and coconut dessert. In season, there’s also a menu featuring game dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1245;Il Patio;Italy;Pollone;via Oremo 14, Pollone, 13814, Italy;45.5820817;8.004503;100;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;A charming restaurant occupying an old stable, with a shaded terrace where guests can dine alfresco overlooking the garden. One of the most popular restaurants in the region, Il Patio owes its success first and foremost to its cuisine, closely followed by its impeccable and highly professional service. Owner-chef Sergio Vineis is at the helm in the kitchen, ably assisted by his son Simone, producing dishes which showcase local produce with a dash of creativity. Carefully chosen and extensive wine selection, including a few unpredictable choices.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1246;Zappatori;Italy;Pinerolo;corso Torino 34, Pinerolo, 10064, Italy;44.8847909;7.3320196;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Leaving Pinerolo’s arcades behind you, a small courtyard leads into this historic trattoria housed in a 20C building which current chef Christian Milone has transformed into an elegant restaurant, retaining some of the building’s old features and combining them with a more modern decor. This is the setting for traditional Piedmontese cuisine reinterpreted with a creative twist, served on smart and elegant tableware. There’s also a chef’s table for those who enjoying watching the chef at work, while the delightful winter garden is home to a small, more intimate dining room.;Air conditioning;[]
1247;Antica Osteria Nonna Rosa;Italy;Vico Equense;via Laudano 1, loc. Pietrapiana, Vico Equense, 80069, Italy;40.66156;14.43397;69;true;false;Campanian, Creative;The dining room at this restaurant has the warm ambience of an old country house, where two small niches with their own tables are perfect for a more private and romantic dinner. The decor includes dove-coloured walls, an array of lamps and even a typical nativity scene in which the chef and his mother (“Nonna Rosa”) make an appearance. The cuisine is original and creative with its roots in local traditions, and is prepared using ingredients from Campania and the restaurant’s own kitchen garden. Some years ago, owner-chef Giuseppe Guida purchased a large garden where he now grows all the vegetables used in his dishes. The restaurant describes its cuisine as “An exciting discovery of flavours from bygone days, with imaginative touches that are fully respectful of local traditions.”.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1248;La Trota;Italy;Rivodutri;via Santa Susanna 33, località Piedicolle, Rivodutri, 02010, Italy;42.4982957;12.8486278;69;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;Before entering this restaurant, stop for a moment to admire the crystal-clear waters of the Santa Susanna canal which runs opposite the building. La Trota has revolutionised and raised the standard of cooking freshwater fish, elevating it to the level of other produce traditionally considered to be more refined. At this restaurant, the Serva brothers, ably assisted by their respective children, showcase ingredients such as trout, tench, freshwater crayfish, pike and catfish, which are sourced from the clean waters nearby and which feature on the menu alongside a few meat dishes. They also make good use of wild herbs – guests are given an extract of these to take home, which they can use to make a warm herbal tea or a cool drink. There’s also an excellent choice of wine to accompany your meal, plus a surprising selection of cognacs and liqueurs. In fine weather, guests have the option of dining on the small wooden bridge spanning the canal. The restaurant celebrates its 60th anniversary in 2023.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1249;Joia;Italy;Milan;via Panfilo Castaldi 18, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4772538;9.2016981;71;true;true;Vegetarian, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant in one of Milan’s historic districts is home to the chef who first introduced the concept of natural, vegetarian cuisine to the world of Italian fine dining. Pietro Leemann is the man (and great philosopher) behind this “vegetarian restaurant” where the menu is 80% vegan and gluten free. This chef’s imaginative and dream-like dishes bear witness to the philosophical and spiritual transformation he has undergone over many years, with recipes that showcase the essence of their ingredients in colour, flavour, texture and presentation. The restaurant is minimalist and elegant in style, while its Joia Academyaims to introduce participants to all aspects of the chef’s philosophy.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1250;Acquerello;Italy;Fagnano Olona;via Patrioti 5, Fagnano Olona, 21054, Italy;45.6691814;8.8709213;65;true;false;Creative;The word “modern” sums up the cuisine here, although more than one word is needed to do justice to this restaurant. Housed in an old courtyard typical of Lombardy, Acquerello focuses on flavour rather than colour, with dishes created by a chef who enjoys being in the kitchen away from the spotlight. Although the restaurant offers an à la carte, our inspectors recommend the tasting menu with its fine balance of delicate flavours and original combinations that offer a hint of Eastern influence and pleasing contrasts in cooking methods and temperatures. The wine selection reflects the owner’s tastes: a slight emphasis on sparkling wines from the other side of the Alps, but also something for everyone.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1251;Aroma;Italy;Rome;via Labicana 125, Rome, 00184, Italy;41.8903751;12.4948543;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The open-view kitchen is the first thing guests see when they arrive at this delightful restaurant boasting views of Ancient Rome from the Colosseum to the dome of St Peter’s – a truly memorable sight!The name pays tribute to both the city and the aromas imbued in the Mediterranean cuisine served here. Local specialities also feature on the menu, often with a touch of creativity added by chef Giuseppe Di Iorio.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1252;Saporium Firenze;Italy;Florence;lungarno Benvenuto Cellini 63r, Florence, 50125, Italy;43.7646;11.2659859;26;true;false;Creative;A delightful small restaurant situated in a building on the Lungarno, close to the beautiful ascent on foot up to Piazzale Michelangelo. Vaulted ceilings and brick walls help to give the dining room a traditional atmosphere, which is enhanced by plants and elegant furniture. Young, talented chef Ariel Hagen delights guests with his highly personalised cuisine, using seasonal produce (such as fresh tagliolini pasta with elderflower) and fermented ingredients from his own workshop. The wine list is of the same high quality as the cuisine, featuring some excellent labels alongside an impressive choice of wines by the glass. In the evening, the Saporium Lounge serves tapas, wine and a selection of cocktails.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1253;Dolomieu;Italy;Madonna di Campiglio;via Castelletto Inferiore 10, Madonna di Campiglio, 38086, Italy;46.223693;10.8257548;88;true;false;Contemporary;Dolomieu is an intimate Stube-style restaurant furnished in oak which features just six tables, so booking well in advance is recommended. This is the most traditional part of the DV Chalet hotel, which otherwise boasts a modern and trendy Alpine-style decor. The tasting menu focuses on ingredients from the surrounding valleys, while the à la carte features interesting and tempting dishes such as ravioli with goat’s curd, raw Sicilian prawns and black truffle finished with a delicate chicken broth. Different wines are offered by the glass, all chosen by a maître-sommelier who is equally fond of wines from outside Italy.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1254;Re Maurì;Italy;Salerno;via Benedetto Croce, Salerno, 84121, Italy;40.6720876;14.734819;95;true;true;Creative;Situated in the Lloyd’s Baia hotel between Salerno and Vietri, in an elevated location overlooking the port, this restaurant offers splendid views of the bay from the floor-to-ceiling windows in the dining room which become even more stunning from the terrace where meals are served in fine weather. Specialities from Campania feature on the menu alongside dishes with a more international influence and ingredients from outside the region. Make sure you leave space for dessert: the cook worked as a pastry chef before coming here and the care he takes with his desserts is truly remarkable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1256;Contraste;Italy;Milan;via Giuseppe Meda 2, Milan, 20136, Italy;45.446095;9.17929;39;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Innovative;Following recent refurbishment, this restaurant in a period building that conjures up an image of old Milan has a bright and colourful feel thanks to its shades of blue, red and green. The courtyard, a small, tranquil space that adds an unexpected touch of greenery to this urban setting, is perfect for a cigar or aperitif. Once inside chef Matias Perdomo’s home, you have a choice between the “Riflesso” menu (traditional dishes yet prepared using modern techniques) and the “Riflessioni” menu (bolder and more innovative options featuring unusual combinations). Contraste’s philosophy lies in the chef’s ability to bring his ingredients to life, using imaginative combinations that delight and appeal to the palate. Overseen with professionalism by an excellent team that will offer recommendations for the best pairings (either wine or non-alcoholic options), the wine list includes a selection of labels from around the world, with a particular focus on France.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1257;Sarri;Italy;Imperia;lungomare C. Colombo 108, Borgo Prino, Imperia, 18100, Italy;43.87008;8.0059;83;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;This attractive restaurant boasts a beautiful location in the charming Borgo Prino, a row of houses facing the sea and painted in the pastel shades typical of the region. Liguria’s legendary mild climate means that meals can often be enjoyed outdoors, but if that’s not an option there’s also a charming dining room in an old warehouse decorated in impeccable contemporary style. The faultless, elegant service here is overseen with skill and charm by the chef’s wife, Alessandra. We’ve left the real reason for our enthusiasm until last: owner-chef Andrea Sarri delights guests with his superb cuisine, which features top-quality fish and seafood from the Ligurian Sea, as well as seasonal vegetables and beansprouts grown in organic gardens, all of which result in highly original dishes such as the “vertical” raw fish or the shellfish from Oneglia cooked in a stew with aromatic herbs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1258;Signum;Italy;Malfa;via Scalo, Malfa, 98050, Italy;38.57992;14.83344;28;false;true;Sicilian, Contemporary;Situated in the Aeolian Islands, this charming inn is home to young chef Martina Caruso who, having practically grown up here, has returned home to take up the reins at Signum after formative experiences elsewhere. Today, this young chef leads a team of nine in the kitchen, while her brother manages the charming hotel built to resemble a typical Aeolian hamlet. Martina knows exactly how to bring out the best of the vibrant ingredients sourced from the region, her own kitchen garden and the nearby sea – she allows the power of these ingredients to shine forth yet manages to make light and playful use of their intense flavours, showcasing their qualities instead of trying to hide them. Luca and cousin Raffaele enhance this gourmet experience with excellent wines (some home-produced), also available by the glass, and superb cocktails.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1259;Sud;Italy;Quarto;via Santi Pietro e Paolo 8, Quarto, 80010, Italy;40.8748426;14.1234047;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;Closed for refurbishment June-August 2024Quarto has made its mark on the gastronomic map of Italy thanks to Marianna Vitale’s cuisine and the tribute she pays to southern Italian produce, occasionally combined with more exotic ingredients. Once seated at your table, the only choice you have to make is the number of courses you want (rather than the dishes themselves) from two tasting menus of seven or twelve courses designed by the chef. The surprise menus (which take into account any food allergies or intolerances) have a slight focus on fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1260;Crocifisso;Italy;Noto;via Principe Umberto 46, Noto, 96017, Italy;36.8944278;15.0713855;68;true;false;Contemporary;Situated near the church of the same name in the upper part of Noto’s historic centre, this restaurant is one of the best in the area. In a modern and minimalist setting, Marco Baglieri serves excellent cuisine with an elaborate and Baroque feel, almost as if he were paying tribute to Noto itself, one of the most fascinating towns in Sicily. An extraordinary dining experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1261;Nostrano;Italy;Pesaro;piazzale della Libertà 7, Pesaro, 61121, Italy;43.9136749;12.9193802;100;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;Situated just a few metres from the famous spherical sculpture by Arnaldo Pomodoro, this welcoming restaurant is now even more appealing following its recent refurbishment. Here, owner-chef Stefano Ciotti combines modern techniques with regional flavours on a menu that embraces fish and meat dishes alike.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1262;Le Trabe;Italy;Paestum;via Capo di Fiume 4, Paestum, 84047, Italy;40.4469187;15.0429487;66;true;false;Campanian, Contemporary;This restaurant lies within the Capodifiume estate, a microcosm that is home to the source of the Trabe river (hence the restaurant name) and a hydroelectric power station which supplies the estate with its energy and which guests can visit with the friendly restaurant staff on a short but interesting tour before dinner. A welcome aperitif and canapés are served in the wine cellar, after which guests move to the elegant dining room – a beautiful setting which also takes into account respect for the environment, with various sustainable practices adopted by the restaurant. However, more than anything it is Marci Rispo’s cuisine that is truly memorable, showcased on two tasting menus that are inspired by the culinary traditions of Campania and its seasonal ingredients, such as the famous mozzarella used in the iconic “Bufala, bufala, bufala” dish. You’ll also be impressed by the attentive service offered by sommelier and maître-d’ Simone Munzillo and his team. In short, an enjoyable dining experience that offers an array of elegant and carefully curated dishes that are full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1263;La Capinera;Italy;Taormina;via Nazionale 177, località Spisone, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.863136;15.295927;16;false;false;Sicilian, Creative;Sea & Air - Earth & Fire: the four elements come together on the tasting menus at this restaurant, where some dishes are named after movies (the Benjamin Button dish features fresh pasta “buttons” served with veal ragout and rosemary oil). Other highlights include the “cacao meravigliao”, a dish of delicious seafood tagliolini with red prawns and mozzarella foam, in which the delightfully fresh, raw Mazzara prawns have a wonderful texture. Elegant service, soft background music which creates a pleasant holiday atmosphere, and a vast selection of regional, Italian and European wines complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1264;Iacobucci;Italy;Castel Maggiore;via Ronco 1, Villa Zarri, Castel Maggiore, 40013, Italy;44.5602196;11.3538901;31;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Large, well-spaced-out tables arranged in a charming historic setting make this a restaurant for special occasions, whether you’re here for a romantic dinner or simply for a gourmet experience. Here, chef Agostino Iacobucci serves unmissable classic favourites, from interpretations of raw fish to his famous babà dessert. The restaurant is housed in Villa Zarri, an enchanting late-16C residence surrounded by mature grounds.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1265;Carignano;Italy;Turin;via Carlo Alberto 35, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.065155;7.6840119;20;true;false;Creative;Davide Scabin, one of Piedmont’s most famous chefs who was also awarded two Michelin starts at his Rivoli restaurant, continues to reinvent and apply himself with as much enthusiasm as ever. His backdrop is one of the most prestigious hotels in Turin – the historic Grand Hotel Sitea – where he serves a tasting menu that is both bold and innovative, surprising guests with the order of courses: you start with intense flavours and the dishes become lighter as the meal progresses. Scabin offers a superb gastronomic experience on one long tasting menu that includes traditional Piedmontese recipes and more creative dishes, as well as the occasional more exotic influence.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1266;Gourmetstube Einhorn;Italy;Mules;Campo di Trens, Mules, 39040, Italy;46.8511074;11.5204481;54;false;false;Creative, International;Occupying a 13C post house, this restaurant is part of the elegant Stafler hotel, which means that there are guestrooms available for those not wanting to drive home after dinner. This intimate gourmet restaurant has just five tables laid out in a romantic Stube decorated with wood that dates back to medieval times. Chef Peter Girtler offers guests just one tasting menu (from which they can choose four, five or six courses) which features an array of creative dishes full of different ingredients and colours and a combination of meat, fish and vegetables.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
1268;Relais Blu;Italy;Massa Lubrense;via Roncato 60, Massa Lubrense, 80061, Italy;40.58996;14.3303537;92;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated across the water from Capri, this restaurant boasts one of the most beautiful views of the island from its dining room and outdoor terrace, with its unmistakeable and legendary silhouette visible in the distance. Fumiko Sakai is at the helm in the kitchen, but don’t be fooled by the name – although he was born in Japan, this chef has worked in this region for many years and creates authentically Campanian cuisine, often using vegetables from the restaurant’s kitchen garden. Fish obviously takes pride of place on the menu, but meat also makes an appearance, especially regional breeds such as Nero Casertano suckling pig and Laticauda lamb.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1269;Anna Stuben;Italy;Ortisei;via Vidalong 3, Ortisei, 39046, Italy;46.5723078;11.6732881;69;true;false;Creative;Although many brilliant “Anna’s” have cooked in this family-run restaurant over the years, for the past ten years there has been a superb male chef – Reimund Brunner – at the helm. The romantic ambience of the two Stube-style dining rooms is now famous, having become one of the places that you want to visit every time you return to the Val Gardena. The cuisine is inspired by the Alto Adige, yet also remains open to ingredients from further afield, including fish and seafood, in dishes which are lighter and fresh in style with a reduced use of butter and sugar. The service is excellent and highly attentive to guests’ needs, while the talented sommelier is always on hand to offer recommendations with a smile. Last but not least, the restaurant is housed within the Alpine-style Grödnerhof Hotel & Spa, which offers classically elegant guestrooms which pay little heed to passing trends.;Interesting wine list;[]
1270;Moma;Italy;Rome;via di San Basilio 42, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.90569;12.4909;86;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Situated between Via Veneto and Piazza Barberini, Moma is a modern, multi-faceted restaurant that serves informal dishes at lunchtime and more creative traditional fare in the gourmet restaurant on the first floor, which also includes a small outdoor dining space that allows guests to make the most of Rome’s mild climate. The balance between textures and combinations and the attention paid to presentation and top-quality ingredients are the key features here, resulting in regionally inspired cuisine that also includes creative dishes such as risotto with camomile, smoked eel, honey and oregano. This focus on the region and its fine local producers is also evident on the wine list, which leans towards labels produced by small artisanal wineries. The young staff are attentive and keen to ensure that your evening is a resounding success.;Air conditioning;[]
1271;Lanterna Verde;Italy;Villa di Chiavenna;frazione San Barnaba 7, Villa di Chiavenna, 23029, Italy;46.3284;9.49741;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Thanks to its fireplace, the welcoming, classic-style dining room at this restaurant is perfect for winter dining, while its garden terrace attracts guests in summer. Whatever time of year you visit, you’ll enjoy cuisine which balances traditional recipes with more contemporary options, with a focus on local ingredients, especially fish from the lake. The Tonola family at the helm have been renowned throughout the province (and further afield) for their gourmet cuisine and welcoming hospitality for over 40 years. Their appeal is even greater today, thanks to young chef Roberto who provides a skilful modern touch in the kitchen, while his experienced parents oversee the front of house and make helpful wine recommendations.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1272;Magorabin;Italy;Turin;corso San Maurizio 61/d, Turin, 10124, Italy;45.0684649;7.6960435;48;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;Situated near the Mole building, this restaurant has a modern, minimalist-style dining room with soft lighting, where food takes centre stage. Marcello Trentini is one of the most skilled and versatile chefs not only in Turin but also further afield. On tasting menus dedicated to his classic dishes, as well as a vegetarian menu (with the option of choosing courses à la carte style), this chef demonstrates his masterly, almost magical, skill in carefully designed complex cuisine inspired by Piedmontese and international (including Asian) recipes and flavours. Simple names and just a few words often conceal real masterpieces, with ingredients sometimes prepared in many different ways. Our inspector recommends the spaghettone with butter, anchovies and eel, served with caviar for enhanced flavour, and perhaps accompanied by a fresh and lightly fermented Falanghina Cacciagalli wine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1273;Condividere;Italy;Turin;via Bologna 20/a, Turin, 10152, Italy;45.0802655;7.6911056;88;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;The cast of star-studded names at this restaurant includes Lavazza (the restaurant is situated in the Nuvola complex, where there’s also a coffee museum) and one of the most famous and innovative chefs of all time, Spaniard Ferran Adrià (working here as a consultant), as well as the talented Federico Zanasi, the full-time chef at the helm. In the unique dining room with its famous wall of clocks, choose between three menus that range from the restaurant’s classic favourites to the chef’s most recent creations, each showcasing a vast array of imaginative dishes that often reinterpret classic Italian recipes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1274;Stube Hermitage;Italy;Madonna di Campiglio;via Castelletto Inferiore 69, Madonna di Campiglio, 38086, Italy;46.2131692;10.8244764;38;false;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Situated in a tranquil and secluded location, this restaurant occupies an early-19C Stube-style dining room in the Biohotel Hermitage. Decorated with a profusion of wood and home to just a few tables, the setting is perfect for a romantic evening with a focus on fine dining. During the 2022-23 winter season, young Antonio Lepore (the former sous-chef here) took over the reins in the kitchen, where he now feels free to explore new ideas and fully express his personality on various tasting menus. Elegance is the key word here, both in the ambience and the cuisine. The excellent selection of cheeses is also worthy of note.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
1275;Il Ristorante di Guido da Costigliole;Italy;Santo Stefano Belbo;località San Maurizio 39, Santo Stefano Belbo, 12058, Italy;44.7051429;8.2066746;34;false;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a panoramic location surrounded by beautiful rolling hills, this restaurant occupies an old 17C monastery which has been converted into one of the region’s most elegant and exclusive hotels, namely the Relais San Maurizio. Here, Andrea Alciati and Monica Magnini perpetuate the legendary story started by Andrea's parents Guido and Lidia. Chef Fabio Sgrò, from Cuneo, demonstrates his professional skill to the full on his updated menu while continuing to respect the restaurant’s family traditions, including freshwater fish and several off-the-menu dishes. A vegan tasting option is also available here. The wine list is as impressive as the cuisine, boasting a superb selection that includes vertical options and rare labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1276;All'Oro;Italy;Rome;via Giuseppe Pisanelli 25, Rome, 00196, Italy;41.9140073;12.4730035;18;true;true;Creative, Italian Contemporary;Situated within The H’All Tailor Suite, a smart “tailor-made” hotel which offers its guests bespoke services, this restaurant boasts a pleasantly sophisticated New York-style dining room plus a second room with a vaguely English decor, both of which serve as a setting for creative Italian cuisine. Chef Riccardo Di Giacinto’s culinary philosophy can be summed up in three adjectives: sincere, delicious and tenacious! The extensive and carefully chosen wine selection favours the regions of Piedmont and Tuscany. Enjoy alfresco dining in the welcoming outdoor All’Aria.in summer.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1277;Berton;Italy;Milan;via Mike Bongiorno 13, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4821805;9.1944159;31;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Situated in the heart of Porta Nuova, this restaurant has one wall made entirely of glass, allowing plenty of daylight to permeate its elegant, contemporary-style dining room which is perfectly in tune with the character of this new, futuristic district. The cuisine here continues to focus on just a few ingredients, so that it is deliberately simple in style without being minimalist. Creative and modern, the dishes are prepared with ingredients from all over Italy with no particular emphasis on any one region: the same is true of the excellent wine list. Professional, attentive and efficient service completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1278;Villa Maiella;Italy;Guardiagrele;via Sette Dolori 30, località Villa Maiella, Guardiagrele, 66016, Italy;42.188822;14.2047054;56;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Modern Cuisine;Way back in 1966, Ginetta and Arcangelo probably never dreamed for a moment that their modest tavern would become so famous. Nowadays, the Tinari family comprises mother-and-son Angela and Arcangelo in the kitchen, and Peppino and Pascal front of house, all of whom offer guests a warm welcome in their restaurant on the edge of the Parco della Maiella. Here, you’ll enjoy authentic Abruzzo dishes with the occasional surprising and creative twist on three tasting menus (chosen when you make your booking). A good choice also for beer-lovers, with over a thousand different labels available including a wide selection by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1279;Esplanade;Italy;Desenzano del Garda;via Lario 3, Desenzano del Garda, 25015, Italy;45.4658732;10.5498607;42;false;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;One of Italy’s long-established restaurants, the Esplanade has been a proud holder of a Michelin star since 1992 and is so renowned among food-lovers that its name is practically synonymous with that of Desenzano del Garda. Boasting a superb location alongside the lake, from which it is separated only by its own garden (the summer outdoor space is delightful), it is equally famous for its top-quality cuisine. The menu is one of the most extensive (at this level) in Italy, with an equal balance of meat and fish, and Italian and regional dishes prepared using mainly seasonal ingredients – this is classic Italian cuisine that does not stray too far from its traditional roots yet with delicate modern touches added by chef Massimo Fezzardi. The dining room, where the attentive service is as precise as a metronome, is overseen by two superb characters, namely Marzio Lee Vallio, the sommelier who won the 2024 Michelin Guide Italy Sommelier Award, and the exuberant and flawless Emanuele Signorini, a true professional whose friendly manner is contagious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1280;Cucina Cereda;Italy;Ponte San Pietro;via Piazzini 33, Ponte San Pietro, 24036, Italy;45.698355;9.5909095;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A typical entrance leads into the courtyard of what was a monastery in the late 16C at this restaurant, where the dining room has a classic atmosphere. However, it is the cuisine that steals the show – it is creative, yet down-to-earth with no unnecessary frills, full of flavour, and features meat and fish dishes inspired by Italian traditions with the occasional local twist. There’s a simpler, business-style menu at lunchtime, while among the à la carte options we particularly enjoyed the snails served with morel mushrooms and a careful seasoning of parsley and coriander, and the paccheri pasta with fish soup in which the bouillabaisse-style sauce added a real Mediterranean flavour.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1281;Lido 84;Italy;Fasano del Garda;corso Zanardelli 196, Fasano del Garda, 25083, Italy;45.6251787;10.5755286;100;false;true;Creative;Once you’ve left your car in the car park, a slight descent leads to this small corner of paradise boasting one of the most beautiful views of Lake Garda. Run by two brothers (one in the kitchen, the other front of house), this elegant restaurant is striking for its many decorative details. The cuisine here is full of flavour, with generous portions that give the impression that every meal at Lido 84 is Sunday lunch – joyous, festive and served in a relaxed and informal atmosphere. There’s also plenty of contact with the chefs, who often bring the dishes to the tables themselves. For a special occasion, we recommend booking the table in the small stone building in the splendid garden, with its classic decor and breathtaking views.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1282;Vintage 1997;Italy;Turin;piazza Solferino 16/h, Turin, 10121, Italy;45.068485;7.676379;33;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;The several tasting menus at this restaurant include an on-trend vegetarian option, a Mediterranean menu (with an excellent tuna Chateaubriand and spring onion jelly), the typical Piedmontese “Punt e mes”, and the surprise Luna Park which gives free rein to the chef and is undoubtedly the most exciting option (must be booked in advance). Although not extensive, the wine list boasts interesting vertical options from the Langhe and further afield. The classic-style dining room is skilfully overseen by the owner.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1283;Locanda Margon;Italy;Ravina;via Margone 15, Ravina, 38123, Italy;46.0368038;11.1066465;93;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;This restaurant with views of Trento and the Adige valley is home to chef Edoardo Fumagalli, who puts all his energy and creativity into three tasting menus (one of which has been designed to combine perfectly with the Ferrari sparkling wine made by the winery that owns the restaurant). His menus showcase local ingredients (especially the Straordinario Trentinomenu), which he prepares with technical expertise, occasionally combining them with produce from further afield. Our inspector especially recommends the “Arlecchino” mountain egg with Trentingrana cream, bisque reduction with Chardonnay vinegar and puffed amaranth. Although the adjacent Bistrot is designed to be more informal in character, it offers the attraction of reliable Italian cuisine and the option of alfresco dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
1284;I Castagni;Italy;Vigevano;via Ottobiano 8/20, Vigevano, 27029, Italy;45.2927681;8.8577576;22;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Situated in the countryside outside Vigevano, this rustic country house with a portico has the feel of a private villa thanks to its antique furniture and paintings by local artists on the walls. For more than 30 years, Enrico Gerli, together with his wife, who is charge of the front of house, has run this restaurant with dedication and professionalism, creating classic-modern cuisine which showcases the culinary traditions of Lombardy alongside a few fish-based dishes. Our inspector particularly recommends the black plin ravioli filled with peas and served with a white cuttlefish and mussel sauce. A wine cellar home to around 600 labels from around the world adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
1285;President;Italy;Pompei;piazza Schettini 12/13, Pompei, 80045, Italy;40.74731;14.49951;37;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The menu at this restaurant features traditional dishes from Campania with updated twists, some of which (such as the “sigilinium” bread) even date back to Ancient Roman times. The cuisine, which is always delicious and beautifully presented, is showcased on various tasting menus from which individual dishes can also be chosen à la carte style and swapped from one menu to another. Although we chose to order fish (we particularly enjoyed the “Mediterraneo da scoprire” grouper dish), there is also a vegetable-based option. The front of house is overseen by the chef’s friendly and efficient wife, who is happy to offer wine recommendations and willing to open bottles of finer wines even if you only want one glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1286;Cracco in Galleria;Italy;Milan;Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.46535;9.189977;87;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;The Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II is one of the most iconic sights in Milan and as such it is apt that it is home to this star of Italian cuisine, whose professional career is one of the most impressive in Italy with influences that include the culinary master Alain Ducasse and wine expert Giorgio Pinchiorri. Together with owner Carlo, resident chef Luca Sacchi creates top-quality cuisine with impeccable technique. He showcases his dishes on a carefully composed tasting menu and an à la carte, with references to contemporary Italian cuisine in dishes such as the open ravioli and reinterpretations of classic favourites, such as vitello alla Milanese (breaded veal cutlet). The wine list is an experience in itself, offering one of the best and most comprehensive selections of French wines in Italy, as well as an excellent choice of wines by the glass. Guests also have the opportunity to taste wines from the organic Vistamare estate, owned by the chef and situated in the Romagna hills. The most popular tables are those by the window with views of the Octagonal building – these should be booked well in advance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1287;Alpenroyal Gourmet;Italy;Selva di Val Gardena;via Meisules 43, Selva di Val Gardena, 39048, Italy;46.5588796;11.7463421;96;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;This is the gourmet restaurant at the hotel of the same name, one of the most luxurious in the Val Gardena. The elegant, contemporary dining room has an almost minimalist feel, with a softly lit ambience that would give the impression of a private home were it not for the huge garden (snow-covered in winter) visible through its windows. Although originally from Puglia, chef Mario Porcelli has been working in the Dolomites for many years and is equally at home with local dishes as he is with recipes from his native region. In both cases, his dishes are modern and beautifully presented in a manner that leaves nothing to chance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1288;Zum Löwen;Italy;Tisens;via Tirolo 25, Tisens, 39010, Italy;46.5635107;11.1694582;25;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A charming restaurant housed in a skilfully restored old farm, where everything from the hay barn to the old stalls has been refurbished and enhanced, so that traditional old features from the exterior can be seen in the dining room alongside more modern additions. The cuisine here is in the capable hands of owner Anna Matscher, who creates gourmet dishes from the Alto Adige which can by now be described as “classics”. The ingredients and the cooking methods used add a certain level of tradition to proceedings, although this is hardly a flaw, especially given the precise preparation involved. Examples include the traditional roast goat kid cooked with extra-virgin olive oil and aromatic herbs and served with roast potatoes and a second seasonal vegetable, along with its own delicious jus. Luis oversees the front of house and is always available to offer recommendations for the best wine pairings.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1289;Schöneck;Italy;Molini;via Schloss Schöneck 11, Molini, 39030, Italy;46.8186079;11.8482868;20;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;With over 30 years’ experience behind them, the Baumgartner brothers’ restaurant is an excellent choice for classic specialities from the Alto Adige, offering a menu that focuses on regional dishes yet also includes a few fish-based options. The most important feature here is that all specialities are made from top-quality ingredients (often locally sourced), prepared by chef Karl with an expertise that ignores modern trends and passing fashions. Meals are served in rooms that are elegantly decorated with local wood, including a beautiful lounge space with a piano in front of the bar, Stube-style dining rooms and a veranda, while in summer the cool, shady terrace is particularly appealing. Last but not least, the excellent wine list is as impressive as the cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1290;Gellivs;Italy;Oderzo;calle Pretoria 6, Oderzo, 31046, Italy;45.7828798;12.4946107;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Gellius boasts a unique and atmospheric setting within the Antica Opitergium museum, surrounded by archaeological remains that tell the story of the town from the beginning of the Roman period. It’s just a short hop from this historic past to the present day, where chef Alessandro Breda moves away from the culinary traditions of the region to create imaginative dishes using ingredients from his surrounding area and the Adriatic Sea. If you’re looking for a state-of-the-art cocktail or a glass of good wine, make your way to the Lounge Bar, which looks out over Piazza Grande.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1291;Cannavacciuolo Bistrot;Italy;Turin;via Umberto Cosmo 6, Turin, 10131, Italy;45.0627906;7.7009861;70;false;true;Creative;Situated near the Gran Madre church in Borgo Po, this restaurant is the Turin home of the three-Michelin-starred chef from Villa Crespi Cannavacciuolo. Here, in a succession of small dining rooms decorated in elegant, modern style, Gabriele Bertoli serves contemporary-style cuisine influenced by culinary traditions from all over Italy, with a natural focus on his native Campania, to which he adds his own delightful personalised touches.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1292;Abocar Due Cucine;Italy;Rimini;Via Carlo Farini 13, Rimini, 47921, Italy;44.0626895;12.5663487;58;true;true;Creative, International;Abocar (the word is Spanish for “to get closer”) demonstrates the Argentine origins of this restaurant’s young chef , who aims to offer his guests reasonably priced gourmet cuisine. Seasonal produce and South American influences are to the fore here, resulting in excellent cuisine focused around just a handful of recipes.The dishes are creative, yet with their roots in the classic foundations in which the young chef was trained in Michelin-starred restaurants in France, Spain and Italy – it was during this apprenticeship that he met his partner, Camilla, who assists him in the kitchen as well as overseeing the front of house. This welcoming restaurant hidden among the streets of old Rimini boasts a charming, youthful and unique atmosphere which is far from stuffy and which makes it an excellent choice.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1294;Indaco;Italy;Lacco Ameno;piazza Santa Restituta 1, Lacco Ameno, 80076, Italy;40.75377;13.88421;19;false;false;Creative, Seafood;Although the sun sets behind you at this restaurant, the sky takes on beautiful indigo hues at dusk (hence the name Indaco), so it’s well worth getting here for sunset. Overlooking a small bay at the Regina Isabella hotel, the restaurant boasts sweeping views of Lacco Ameno, Casamicciola, the island of Procida, Vesuvius and Bacoli, all of which unfold in front of your eyes with the sea like a bay enclosed by the islands – an unforgettable sight! At the helm in the kitchen, Pasquale Palamaro from Ischia serves elaborate and creative dishes inspired by his childhood memories, all showcased on two tasting menus (fish takes centre stage although a few meat dishes also feature) from which dishes can also be chosen individually à la carte style. The wine is of the highest quality, both in terms of the extensive selection (more than 1 000 labels) and the recommendations provided by the enthusiastic sommelier.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1295;Oro Restaurant;Italy;Venice;isola della Giudecca 10, Venice, 30133, Italy;45.4271;12.3412;32;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Housed within the Hotel Cipriani, one of Venice’s legendary hotels which is pleasantly located in a tranquil corner of Giudecca island, the round-shaped dining room at the Oro Restaurant boasts views of the lagoon and the lido. Here, chef Vania Ghedini from Ferrara serves an array of Moroccan dishes which bear witness to her professional past. Her Laguna dish is particularly striking thanks to its skilfully mixed flavours and delicate textures. The tasting menu is equally impressive and offers a good introduction to the chef’s cuisine, including dishes from the lagoon alongside a few light vegetarian options. To finish, we recommend the cherry tart (an absolute must for anyone who enjoys fruit desserts) flavoured with a dash of balsamic vinegar.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1296;Accursio;Italy;Modica;via Grimaldi 41, Modica, 97015, Italy;36.8599639;14.7606251;68;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;Situated near the Duomo di San Pietro and the central Corso Umberto, this small, delightful restaurant occupies a historic palazzo and boasts a simple yet elegant decor including attractive floor tiles. Accursio offers three tasting menus with dishes also available à la carte. The restaurant’s symbol (an olive tree inside a boat) gives a good indication of the culinary focus here, namely a creative journey through Sicily’s cuisine on a menu that features both meat and fish options.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1297;Sadler;Italy;Milan;via dell'Annunciata 14, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4726277;9.1926191;97;false;true;Italian, Creative;Housed in the Casa Baglioni hotel, a beautiful Art Nouveau building dating from 1913, this restaurant has a contemporary feel with an elegant dining room featuring colourful armchairs. The cuisine is precise and distinctive, with a harmonious balance of traditional and innovative flavours thanks to the top-quality ingredients used. The wine list is also top-notch, featuring excellent Italian and international wines, including some rare and exclusive labels. An interesting business lunch is available at midday, while the Rooftop Bar on the seventh floor boasts 360° views of Milan and serves a selection of aperitifs designed especially by the chefs (open daily from 6pm-1am).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1299;Iyo;Italy;Milan;via Piero della Francesca 74, Milan, 20154, Italy;45.4866231;9.1595273;100;false;false;Japanese, Asian Contemporary;After significant refurbishment, this restaurant now has a completely new look – its black marble has been replaced by a more contemporary colour scheme that gives it a more international feel, while still maintaining a minimalism that is typically Japanese. At the entrance, guests are greeted by a small lounge and a long open-view kitchen where numerous sushi chefs can be seen at work, which then leads to a dining room decorated in soft, relaxing colours and furnished with striking round tables made from Patagonian marble. The extensive à la carte features all the classic dishes you would expect of a Japanese restaurant, including well-known versions of sushi, sashimi and tempura, alongside more creative fusion recipes which combine influences from Japan, Europe and elsewhere. There’s also an excellent selection of around 500 wines, including the option of ordering wine by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1300;Sedicesimo Secolo;Italy;Pudiano;via Gerolanuova 4, Pudiano, 25034, Italy;45.3985234;10.0093247;23;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Taking its name from the period in which it was built (the 16C), this restaurant boasts a modern decor which adds a light touch to the dining room with its paved floors, original ceilings and fireplaces. The imaginative menu features decidedly modern and creative dishes with an emphasis on meat, although a few fish options and regional specialities are also available. There’s plenty of choice for all tastes here, with carefully designed dishes prepared by a skilful chef who is well versed in the basics of culinary chemistry and who has a fine palate with a light touch. There’s an interesting selection of different breads, while the choice of coffees includes some rare blends.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1301;Josè Restaurant - Tenuta Villa Guerra;Italy;Torre del Greco;via Nazionale 414, Torre del Greco, 80059, Italy;40.7739059;14.3988055;86;true;false;Campanian, Contemporary;Situated in one of the extraordinary villas on Herculaneum’s “Golden Mile”, this restaurant boasts an elegant dining room within this 18C building, as well as a room overlooking the villa gardens where a simpler menu featuring grilled dishes and pizzas is served in summer. At the helm, chef Alberto Annarumma from Campania reinterprets ingredients and traditional recipes from the region, as well as creating dishes from other regions of Italy and even further afield. The impressive wine cellar is home to around a thousand labels, with an impressive wine selection from Campania and the rest of the world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1302;Vecchia Malcesine;Italy;Malcesine;via Pisort 6, Malcesine, 37018, Italy;45.7624261;10.8079125;88;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;Situated in a small alleyway in a tranquil spot above the historic centre of Malcesine, this restaurant opens on to a surprising garden planted with olive trees and boasting fine views of much of Lake Garda. The restaurant is run by chef Leandro Luppi, originally from the Alto Adige, who has been creating superb cuisine in this region for over 20 years and is renowned for his skilful and imaginative dishes. He now showcases his creative, personalised recipes on two tasting menus: “Qcina 24” features his latest creations, while “Our Classic” is dedicated to his iconic specialities. Dishes can also be chosen individually à la carte style.;Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1303;Al Metrò;Italy;San Salvo Marina;via Magellano 35, San Salvo Marina, 66050, Italy;42.0681141;14.7751494;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in what was once the family pastry shop, this gourmet restaurant run by the Fossaceca brothers is minimalist, contemporary and almost neutral in style so that nothing detracts the attention from Nicola’s delicious cuisine (the outdoor space in a small square has a livelier ambience). The chef uses modern techniques to create carefully thought-out recipes that showcase the flavours of his mainly local ingredients to the full (including some of the best fish from the Adriatic) without fuss or unnecessary frills. The naturally leavened bread is made from Abruzzo flour (Senatore Cappelli and spelt) and is always excellent, as are the superb breadsticks made from Solina mountain corn. The restaurant has recently added an incredible coffee menu that includes top-quality coffees from across the globe.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1304;D.One Restaurant;Italy;Montepagano;via del Borgo 1, Montepagano, 64026, Italy;42.6772065;13.9897625;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;The location of this restaurant is certainly unique, with its different spaces (including small dining rooms adorned with modern works of art) for different parts of your meal – almost like a small village within a village. Here, chef Davide Pezzuto blends simplicity with creative experimentation, focusing on the region and its culinary traditions while also including the occasional influence from his native Puglia. He is ably supported front of house by the restaurant owner, who regales guests with interesting stories about the small town’s past. At the end of dinner, guests can order an excellent Turkish coffee, which is made according to an original recipe borrowed from the museum, and which highlights the Saracen dominance of the region around a thousand years ago.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1305;Il Convivio Troiani;Italy;Rome;vicolo dei Soldati 31, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9015408;12.4727932;98;false;true;Contemporary;A long-established restaurant that was opened in the early 1990s by three brothers from the Marche: Angelo in the kitchen, and Giuseppe and Massimo front of house. Since then, this restaurant has become one of Rome’s leading restaurants thanks to its personalised cuisine with influences from Lazio and elsewhere in Italy, with more traditional dishes served alongside recipes reinterpreted with imagination, flair and the occasional bold twist. The excellent wine list boasts around 3 600 labels (wines and spirits), including fine vintages and a good selection of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1306;Amistà;Italy;Corrubbio;via Cedrare 78, Corrubbio, 37029, Italy;45.48968;10.899484;80;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated within the charming Byblos Art Hotel, this restaurant is similar in style to the rest of the villa with its colourful and harmonious blend of the old and the new, all of which is inspired by a real love of art. Echoing the decor, the cuisine served here plays with a combination of the traditional and the modern. Executive chef Mattia Bianchi adds his own creative touches and interpretations to traditional recipes on three tasting menus, one of which is completely vegan. Dishes can also be chosen à la carte style. The interesting wine list features more than 1 500 labels, including some rare options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1307;Il Centro;Italy;Priocca;via Umberto I 5, Priocca, 12040, Italy;44.7905049;8.0624786;81;false;true;Piedmontese, Classic Cuisine;There’s a timeless feel to this restaurant, which is run by the Cordero family and serves some of the best Piedmontese cuisine in the region. Heading the team here are Elide in the kitchen and husband Enrico and talented son Giampiero front of house (the latter a real wine connoisseur who looks after the ever-expanding wine cellar), all of whom continue to maintain the high standards set by Giampiero’s grandparents when they opened this restaurant back in 1956. With skill and dedication, they serve traditional cuisine that is full of substance and flavour, which you could happily eat every day without ever getting bored, including the restaurant’s legendary peppers in a sweet and sour sauce, “agnolotti del plin” and finanziera stew, plus a few lighter fish and seafood dishes added in summer. Every year, after the restaurant re-opens in January and up to spring, the menu focuses on the legendary “fritto misto” made up of 12 courses of sweet and savoury dishes (booking a table for this is becoming more and more difficult!). Accommodation is available in the elegant Dimora Cordero just a stone’s throw from the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1308;La Preséf;Italy;Mantello;via Lungo Adda 12, Mantello, 23016, Italy;46.1505628;9.4898006;24;true;false;Creative, Alpine;Overlooking an internal garden, this welcoming Valtellina-style Stube restaurant decorated in sweet-scented cembra pinewood is the perfect setting in which to enjoy local specialities and vegetables grown in the restaurant’s own garden. Zero-mile ingredients (the restaurant takes its name from the word for “manger” in local dialect and also boasts its own dairy) and visual experimentation are the distinctive features of the regional cuisine served here, with fish from the lake, game, DOP Bitto cheese and even local truffles all appearing on the menu. There are two tasting menus: a creative 7-course menu and a more traditional 4-course option. Comfortable, welcoming guestrooms and a modern spa complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1309;La Credenza;Italy;San Maurizio Canavese;via Cavour 22, San Maurizio Canavese, 10077, Italy;45.217537;7.6319706;15;false;false;Creative;Three dining rooms with a modern atmosphere–one of which overlooking a small garden where in the summer there is room for just three tables, so book early if you want to eat outdoors, weather permitting–and a cuisine that starts from a Piedmont base to then wander off along more creative, sometimes even orientalizing paths. A remarkable wine cellar, approximately 1700 labels illustrated in two volumes in addition to which there is an extensive choice by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1310;La Tortuga;Italy;Gargnano;via XXIV Maggio 5, Gargnano, 25084, Italy;45.6887411;10.6652261;57;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Although the name of this restaurant may conjure up images of the Caribbean Sea and its beaches, La Tortuga is actually located on the square overlooking the harbour right in the centre of Gargnano – its owners, however, are full of the spirit of the eponymous Caribbean island! This small, charming gem of a restaurant is run by female staff in its kitchen and front of house. The cuisine here takes no notice of passing trends, instead focusing on simple and precise cooking methods, so that the flavour of the ingredients (especially the seafood and fish from the lake) really shines through. The wine list is extensive, carefully put together and skilfully explained, with a focus on international wines. La Tortuga has been the proud holder of a Michelin star for over 40 years!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1312;Il Gallo Cedrone;Italy;Madonna di Campiglio;via Cima Tosa 80, Madonna di Campiglio, 38086, Italy;46.2351343;10.8242148;25;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;With its classic Alpine appeal and wood and stone decor, Il Gallo Cedrone at the Bertelli hotel is still at the top of its game! With ever-growing confidence, Sabino Fortunato continues to celebrate the mountain in his cuisine – through the use of game, freshwater fish, cooking with hay and cheese etc – as well as remaining open to influences from the Mediterranean and elsewhere in Italy. His dishes are always well structured and prepared from many different ingredients, which he skilfully combines to produce the best flavours. The inspiration for his “History of venison and ChatGPT in the Parco dello Stelvio with pomegranate, celery, pepper and juniper” dish is the region’s deer management plan and responsible venison consumption. The excellent wine cellar is home to over 800 different labels carefully selected by owner Marco Masè alongside long-established sommelier Giuseppe Greco, plus a wide array of gin and tonics.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1313;Butterfly;Italy;Marlia;SS 12 del Brennero 192, Marlia, 55012, Italy;43.894723;10.5364035;65;true;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;The 19C country house that is home to this charming restaurant is surrounded by its own garden, which can be enjoyed throughout the year thanks to its new glass veranda-style dining room – the veranda opens out into the fresh air in summer and is closed and heated in winter, yet still offers lovely views. The successful partnership of father and son (Fabrizio and Andrea Girasoli) in the kitchen results in an extensive menu featuring meat and fish dishes alike. The culinary techniques in evidence are equally at ease in classic-style dishes (superb langoustine from the Tyrrhenian sea freshly cooked on a lava stone and served with a frothy cocktail sauce, vegetable flowers and fruit) and more creative fare (such as the cocoa cigar stuffed with foie gras, apple and hazelnut – a dish dedicated to Puccini). The restaurant is run in a way that manages to be friendly yet at the same time incredibly professional, while the front of house and service is expertly overseen by the chef’s wife Mariella.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
1314;Osteria della Brughiera;Italy;Villa d'Almè;via Brughiera 49, Villa d'Almè, 24018, Italy;45.7393224;9.626508;59;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Situated amid the foothills outside Bergamo, this elegant country house accessed via a garden boasts rustic features such as parquet flooring, exposed beams and an open fireplace set amid an elegant backdrop that makes it ideal for a special occasion or a romantic meal. The extensive à la carte includes traditional dishes from around Italy alongside more creative fare, with an equal balance of meat and fish options. You’ll also find traditional specialities such as cured meats featuring alongside more sophisticated ingredients such as lobster, caviar and foie gras.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1315;Antonello Colonna Labico;Italy;Labico;via di Valle Fredda 52, Labico, 00030, Italy;41.78292;12.873689;27;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated in a scenically impressive setting nestling in the Vallefredda countryside and housed in an original, avant-garde building, this sophisticated restaurant serves carefully balanced and elegant dishes that underline its proximity to Rome and its close connection with Lazio’s rural traditions. Here, nature and modernity go hand in hand: the restaurant is home to large, almost museum-like rooms adorned with works of art and surrounded by parkland. The dishes, on the other hand, are classic in style, in deliberate contrast to the striking, contemporary backdrop in which they are served, and are inspired by many of Italy’s different culinary traditions. We highly recommended booking a table on the lawn under the mature chestnut trees in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1316;Oasis - Sapori Antichi;Italy;Vallesaccarda;via Provinciale 8/10, Vallesaccarda, 83050, Italy;41.0633639;15.251974;46;false;false;Campanian, Contemporary;Run by the Fischetti family, this gastronomic oasis has been a stronghold for fine cuisine and regional flavours for 35 years now. The restaurant was opened in 1988, a year that is celebrated on the first page of the wine list with an extensive selection of fine labels from that year and also in the ricotta ravioli with walnut and seared garlic created by the restaurant’s founder – a dish still on the menu today. Now, as in the past, it is the women of the family who are at the helm in the kitchen: Michelina Fischetti and her granddaughter Serena Falco continue to conjure up delicious cuisine full of flavour which is prepared using carefully chosen ingredients (mostly organic) from the region with a focus on the passing seasons. The intention here is to create recipes that are open to new food trends and influences, while remaining faithful to a simple style of cuisine that is clean, ethical and inspired by traditional dishes from bygone days. Front of house, the friendly brothers of the family look after guests and oversee the courteous and attentive serving staff.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1317;Venissa;Italy;Mazzorbo;fondamenta Santa Caterina 3, Mazzorbo, 30142, Italy;45.4886784;12.4111088;77;false;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;Far away from the tourist hordes, Venissa is situated in a small walled vineyard dating back to the Middle Ages – complete with 14C belltower – on the small island of Mazzorbo, a magical setting which is perfect for a short stroll before settling down to eat. In addition to the Dorona di Venezia vineyard, the restaurant also has a kitchen garden which provides most of its vegetables, including unusual varieties such as “castraure”, a type of local artichoke. Once out of the garden, you come to a small wooden bridge which links Mazzorbo to neighbouring Burano, where you can complete your visit to the lagoon by exploring the lacemakers’ shops and admiring the colourful local houses. The main focus here, however, is the cuisine – and excellent cuisine it is too! Chefs Chiara Pavan and Francesco Brutto describe their dishes as “ambientale” (environmental) because of the close connection between the lagoon and the Upper Adriatic: the menu features plenty of fish and vegetables and almost no meat. Guests choose their number of courses and the dishes come as a surprise, accompanied by organic wine pairings. At the Osteria Contemporanea next door the dishes are simpler but still full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1318;Atman;Italy;Vinci;Via IV Novembre 20, Vinci, 50059, Italy;43.7862727;10.9260458;24;true;true;Creative;The village where the famous Leonardo was born (we highly recommend a visit to the museum dedicated to the artist) is now home to this renowned restaurant right in the village centre. Atman offers just one tasting menu which changes constantly in line with the seasons and market availability, in order to allow chef Marco Cahssai to express his imaginative talents to the full. Among the creations on the interesting new menu, don’t miss the spaghetti with five types of tomato, which demonstrates a play of techniques and is full of flavour – the dish is served cold in order to allow the aromatic seasoning to shine through. Also worth sampling is the glazed pigeon served with plums which emphasise its succulent texture. Make sure you ask for wine-pairing recommendations – the often intense contrasts of the dishes require careful attention to ensure the right balance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
1319;Marco Martini Restaurant;Italy;Rome;viale Aventino 121, Rome, 00153, Italy;41.880543;12.484601;82;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Situated on the first floor of a beautiful period palazzo, this restaurant recalls the style of a winter garden, where natural daylight, greenery and pretty floor tiles all contribute to the attractive setting. Here, Marco Martini creates imaginative cuisine (with occasionally surprising combinations) that nonetheless remains influenced by the gastronomic traditions of Rome, not so much in the recipes used but in the chef’s love for intense flavours that leave the palate completely satisfied.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1320;Suinsom;Italy;Selva di Val Gardena;strada Puez 12, Selva di Val Gardena, 39048, Italy;46.5565821;11.7597819;15;true;true;Italian Contemporary;The two small pale wood paneled stube are the stage for a gourmet cuisine with a Mediterranean touch and more besides, the charcoal-grilled eel is a striking example, besides being delicious. Among the excellent meats, we recommend the roe deer venison, tender with a rich flavor thanks to its preparation that includes mango, while the Tuscan chef draws on his origins for some first courses, such as pici with lamb ragout and cuttlefish tartar... a truly interesting suggestion! The good wine selection includes various and even international productions on a wine list that is well divided by vine variety.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
1321;Casamatta;Italy;Manduria;contrada Scrasciosa, Manduria, 74024, Italy;40.417763;17.599371;56;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Just a few kilometres outside Manduria, the capital of primitive wine, this restaurant is part of the Vinilia Wine Resort, which occupies an imposing early-20C castle surrounded by splendid grounds planted with mature olive trees. The restaurant is the jewel in the crown of this fine hotel, with its bright, airy dining room and large windows offering views of its outdoor dining space (highly recommended in fine weather). The furnishings are modern in design and the cleverly arranged lighting adds to the charm of the setting. With plenty of experience at leading restaurants behind him, chef Pietro Penna has returned home to his native region, to which he pays tribute in his cuisine. He makes full use of locally sourced produce, often using fruit and vegetables grown in the restaurant’s own kitchen garden in his modern and imaginative dishes. Three tasting menus are available, one of which is entirely vegetarian.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1322;Malga Panna;Italy;Moena;strada de Sort 64, località Sorte, Moena, 38035, Italy;46.376804;11.643984;57;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The story of the Donei family is intertwined with the history of the Alpine farm (“malga”) that was transformed into a restaurant in the 1950s when the parents of the current owner-chef, Paolo, used to prepare delicious dishes for the first holidaymakers to the region. The “malga” is also the symbol of what is now one of the best restaurants in the Fassa valley. All that remains of the “malga” today is its name and the panoramic location above the village and the valley, views of which can be enjoyed from the new veranda dining room decorated in minimalist Alpine style with floor-to-ceiling glass windows. The contemporary, regionally inspired cuisine served here is of high quality, prepared by the skilful owner who is a naturally talented chef. There’s also a tasting menu, which combines Trentino influences with Mediterranean touches. In a nod to the restaurant’s location (on the edge of the woods) and its history, simpler options are also available.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1323;Bistrot;Italy;Forte dei Marmi;viale Franceschi 14, Forte dei Marmi, 55042, Italy;43.9553929;10.1700005;47;true;false;Seafood, Italian Contemporary;Despite its name, this is in fact a gourmet restaurant and not a simple bistro. It is run by the Vaiani, a family of professional restaurateurs and hoteliers who have entrusted the kitchen here to talented chef Andrea Mattei. This partnership has strengthened the style of Bistrot, which is somewhere between traditional and modern in feel and where the quality of the ingredients has always been of utmost importance. The restaurant is particularly renowned for its excellent fish, most of which comes from the Tyrrhenian sea, while it also boasts two wood-fired ovens in which the chef bakes different, truly delicious breads and cooks some of his dishes. The wine selection is a further attraction – the beautiful wine cellar is home to just under 2 000 different labels, with the choice of champagnes and Burgundy wines meriting special mention.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1324;Per Me Giulio Terrinoni;Italy;Rome;vicolo del Malpasso 9, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8973035;12.46747;68;true;true;Italian, Creative;Situated in an alleyway in the historic centre of Rome (a side street off the famous Via Giulia), this restaurant boasts the added attraction of an original and imaginative chef who demonstrates his culinary skills in preparing meat and fish with fine technique and creativity. Sustainability is key here, with a focus on top-quality, carefully chosen ingredients sourced from small-scale local producers, as well as a “zero-waste” approach. In addition to the à la carte, guests can choose from three tasting menus: “Primi Passi” (five of the chef’s iconic dishes), “Testa, Mani, Cuore” (ten dishes with a personal twist), and “Think Green" (five seasonal vegetarian dishes). In summer, be sure to book ahead if you’d like to dine at one of the few tables in the charming outdoor space.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1325;Zass;Italy;Positano;via Laurito 2, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.623268;14.5038074;36;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;The legendary San Pietro is one of the jewels of the Amalfi Coast as well as one of the most famous hotels in the world. Zass, its Michelin-starred restaurant, is extremely popular with visitors (booking in advance is highly recommended) thanks to skilful Belgian chef Alois Vanlangenaeker, who has now been here for over 20 years. His cuisine showcases all the colours and flavours of the Mediterranean with harmony and elegance, focusing mainly on the traditions of Campania, especially in appetisers such as the small bites of lightly baked Pizza Margherita and in creative dishes elsewhere on the menu. Many of his ingredients are sourced from the hotel’s kitchen garden, which he uses to create dishes based on meat and, especially, fish, including his signature John Dory (flavoured with lemon and accompanied by mashed potatoes with bufala yoghurt, seasonal vegetables and his famous Champagne and truffle sauce), and other fish such as mullet, sea bass, scampi and squid. Excellent service, a pianist providing background music, and an idyllic terrace boasting stunning views all play their part in making this a truly memorable dining experience.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1326;Glass Hostaria;Italy;Rome;vicolo del Cinque 58, Rome, 00153, Italy;41.890477;12.4691032;85;true;false;Creative;In the heart of popular Trastevere with its many restaurants, Glass comes as a surprise, housed in what was once a coach-house (as the high ceilings still demonstrate) and now an elegant restaurant (if you want more privacy, there are a few tables set up on the mezzanine). Cristina Bowerman offers a choice of tasting menus (one of which is vegetarian) and a limited selection of à la carte dishes. Her cuisine is creative, with the occasional nod to the culinary traditions of Lazio. The excellent wine list also includes a choice of liqueurs and spirits.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1328;Lux Lucis;Italy;Forte dei Marmi;viale A. Morin 67, Forte dei Marmi, 55042, Italy;43.9516497;10.1758581;61;true;true;Creative, Italian Contemporary;A lift takes guests up to the roof garden of this restaurant housed in the Principe Forte dei Marmi hotel, where a terrace provides the perfect setting for an aperitif with its enchanting views of the coast and (if you’re lucky) beautiful sunsets. From here, you move into the dining room preceded by an open-view kitchen. Originally from the hills around Modena, the chef here likes to include Emilian touches in his perfectly presented dishes. The wine list has an unusual layout, with wines listed according to grape variety and each one accompanied by an interesting description.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1329;La Bandiera;Italy;Civitella Casanova;contrada Pastini 4, Civitella Casanova, 65010, Italy;42.3698762;13.9082843;74;false;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Contemporary;Although it takes a while to reach this restaurant that first opened in 1977, it is definitely worth the journey! Here, an entire family (second and third generations) works together with passion and enthusiasm to provide their guests with real gourmet hospitality. The cuisine, carefully planned and prepared by the parents alongside son Marcello, is based on a real respect for local, seasonal ingredients, some of which are produced by the family themselves (vegetables from the kitchen garden appear in nearly all the dishes, as does a home-produced extra-virgin olive oil). When it comes to technique, dishes have a modern feel, which makes the restaurant a flagship for top-quality Abruzzo cuisine. The couple’s other son, Alessio, works front of house and oversees the wine list, which includes impressive wine-pairing options. The excellent selection also includes a few pages of wines available by the glass, including top-of-the-range labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1330;Antica Corte Pallavicina;Italy;Polesine Parmense;strada del Palazzo Due Torri 3, Polesine Parmense, 43016, Italy;45.0212099;10.0859923;90;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a fairytale setting, this property resembles a castle although it was in fact built as a customs house on the Po river in the 14C. Although the family’s ancestors were once workers on the nearby farm, Massimo Spigaroli now owns everything here (guestrooms, Hosteria del Maiale bistro, spaces for events and business meetings), offering an all-round experience that includes a visit to the unmissable Museo del Culatello as well as his “gastrofluvial” cuisine which has its roots in local traditions. We particularly enjoyed the chicken ravioli cooked in a bladder (a French technique), as well as the Nero Spigaroli suckling pig served with its crispy rind, prawns and green shoots.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1331;Anima;Italy;Milan;via Gaspare Rosales 4, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4812376;9.1884973;80;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;Housed inside the Milano Verticale | UNA Esperienze hotel in the Corso Como district of the city, this new restaurant is run by Enrico Bartolini, the chef with the most Michelin stars to his name in Italy. Elegance, comfort and design are the key words to describe the stylish decor here, while the cuisine showcases the best of Milanese traditions. The focus here is on seasonality not just in the fruit and vegetables, but also the fish and some of the meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1332;Don Alfonso 1890;Italy;Sant'Agata sui Due Golfi;corso Sant'Agata 11, Sant'Agata sui Due Golfi, 80061, Italy;40.6078108;14.3737397;55;false;true;Creative, Italian;In Sant'Agata, poised between two gulfs, Don Alfonso represents an image of southern Italy, the family and Mediterranean cuisine found in few other restaurants. Boasting an enchanting garden, splendid guestrooms and an elegant dining room, Don Alfonso 1890’s reputation was established by Livia and Alfonso, who are still here, greeting guests as though they were old friends. They have now been joined by their sons Ernesto and Mario (the former in the kitchen and the latter front of house). The legendary wine list, as well as a good selection of spirits, plus the organic kitchen garden at Punta Campanella which provides many of the vegetables on the menu, add to one of the most beautiful family stories in Italian gastronomy.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1333;Vineria Modì;Italy;Taormina;via Calapitrulli 13, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.8525201;15.28835;52;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Sicilian;Situated in the historic centre of Taormina, just a stone’s throw from Corso dello Struscio and the many brand-name boutiques that have sprung up here in recent years, this restaurant started out as a wine-bar. The passion for wine remains and is evident not only in the extensive, carefully selected wine list, but also in the enthusiasm of its staff. Nowadays, the wine accompanies fine cuisine prepared by the skilful Dalila Grillo, whose brother Ettore oversees the front of house. Guests have the option of two tasting menus or an à la carte (from which a minimum of three courses must be ordered) featuring creative and elaborate dishes with a Sicilian flavour (as well as influences from elsewhere), all served in an elegant dining room. In summer, the outdoor tables overlooking a pedestrianised street are particularly attractive.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1334;Re Santi e Leoni;Italy;Nola;via Anfiteatro Laterizio 92, Nola, 80035, Italy;40.9282413;14.5266743;64;true;true;Contemporary;Situated in a period building not far from the Duomo, this restaurant has a long dining room which resembles an aisle leading to the open-view kitchen to the rear. The dining room itself is contemporary and minimalist in style and serves as a backdrop for some of the most impressive cuisine in the area courtesy of Luigi Salomone, the talented chef at the helm who is renowned for his Campanian cuisine. Imaginative yet unfussy dishes, top-quality ingredients, and skilfully prepared bread and desserts (all superb, especially the reinterpretation of the typical “pastiera”) add to the appeal. Not to be missed!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1335;Italo Bassi Confusion Restaurant;Italy;Porto Cervo;via Aga Khan 1, Promenade du Port, Porto Cervo, 07021, Italy;41.1345678;9.5375439;55;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;This restaurant has brought a breath of fresh air to the area around the port thanks to its enchanting and distinctive decor. With its mirrors, gold-coloured features, glass and open-view kitchen, ConFusion demonstrates its owners’ real attention to detail, which is even more evident in the creative and technically astute dishes prepared by its chef Italo Bassi, making this a truly memorable dining experience. The clean flavours in this chef’s cuisine are the result of precise cooking methods and skill in combining different ingredients to create balanced and elegant dishes. Sardinian ingredients are to the fore here, with raw fish, top-quality meat, oysters and caviar all featuring on the menu, accompanied by excellent wines and a good selection of renowned champagnes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1336;Il Pellicano;Italy;Porto Ercole;località Lo Sbarcatello, Porto Ercole, 58018, Italy;42.380472;11.1924477;33;true;true;Creative;After a period working in Paris, Michelino Gioia, a native of Campania with a weakness for Tuscany, has returned to Italy to work with the Sciò family, where he demonstrates a new focus on a “less is more” philosophy. He uses just a few ingredients in his dishes, allowing the flavour of these ingredients to shine through in imaginative reinterpretations of traditional recipes with contrasting textures, decisive flavours and an equal focus on meat and fish. With its terrace overlooking the sea and the scent of rosemary in the air, Il Pellicano is one of the most romantic addresses in Italy, enhanced by the friendly, professional service provided by its many staff.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1337;Pipero Roma;Italy;Rome;corso Vittorio Emanuele II 250, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8977856;12.468814;87;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;Situated opposite the church of Santa Maria in Vallicella (known to locals as Chiesa Nuova or new church), this restaurant is named after its owner and maître-d’ Alessandro Pipero. Young chef Ciro Scamardella from Campania is at the helm in the kitchen, where he prepares modern dishes with a focus on the seasons, including a few specialities from his native region. His cuisine demonstrates a continuous search for balance and colour – the recipe that particularly impressed our inspectors was his reinterpretation of mussel soup, in which the full flavour of the sea shone through. A second dining room on the first floor, decorated in the same refurbished style, is available for small groups and private dinners.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1338;Felix Lo Basso home & restaurant;Italy;Milan;via Carlo Goldoni 36, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.4691981;9.2135984;86;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Brilliant chef Felix Lo Basso’s menu is inspired by northern Europe: he offers one single menu that changes regularly depending on market availability and that requires all diners to book ahead and eat at the same time. Although the dishes are inventive and occasionally elaborate, the chef often creates unique reinterpretations of recipes and ingredients from his native Puglia, occasionally with an original Asian twist. Beyond the small rooms used for private dinners, the main dining room features an elegant counter along which guests can sit and watch the chefs at work, with Felice cooking and entertaining his diners with his full range of personal skills to put guests at ease. We’re going to keep the dessert a secret but will give you just one word as a clue – Nuvola (the Italian for cloud).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1339;L'Acciuga;Italy;Perugia;via Settevalli 217, Perugia, 06128, Italy;43.090152;12.3684296;66;true;true;Contemporary, International;You would never guess that there was a gourmet restaurant tucked away in this commercial district on the outskirts of Perugia, but everything changes once you’re inside the bright, original dining room with its open-view kitchen. Here, dishes combine international influences from the chef’s time spent outside Italy with various local ingredients, as well as fish. As is fashionable nowadays, the menu here simply lists the ingredients that make up a dish, even omitting articles and prepositions! Dishes such as CALAMARO, PISELLI (squid and peas) are written in capital letters, with no further description. The impressive wine selection has a special focus on natural and biodynamic labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1340;Ada;Italy;Perugia;via del Bovaro 2, Perugia, 06121, Italy;43.1085426;12.390168;59;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;This new, contemporary-style restaurant is situated in the historic centre of Perugia just a stone’s throw from the town’s Etruscan walls (3C BC). Here, the experienced female chef serves meat and fish dishes full of the colours and flavours of this region and beyond, via two tasting menus and an array of à la carte options. We enjoyed the barbecued eel served in “tegamaccio” (a local freshwater fish soup), as well as our visit to its mysterious wine cellars – once a secret passageway, but now a treasure trove of superb and varied wines overseen by an enthusiastic sommelier.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1341;Mec Restaurant;Italy;Palermo;via Vittorio Emanuele 452, Palermo, 90134, Italy;38.1139131;13.3572594;29;true;false;Sicilian, Contemporary;Occupying a 16C palazzo practically opposite the splendid cathedral in the heart of monumental Palermo, this unusual restaurant is accessed via a number of steps and shares space with an exhibition dedicated to Steve Jobs. Here, three elegant dining rooms with frescoed ceilings are surrounded by memorabilia and photographs that recall the professional career of this computer genius. In this setting, chef Carmelo Trentacosti focuses on Sicilian recipes and ingredients that he reinterprets with a personal twist, such as the famous caponata which is transformed into a creamy sauce (in the shape of the Apple logo) and seasoned with grated Modica chocolate which can be enjoyed with sourdough bread. An excellent cheese trolley (available before the dessert course) and attentive service complete the picture. At the end of your meal, ask to be shown the view of the piazza from the balcony – the perfect way to end a very special evening.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1342;Luigi Lepore;Italy;Lamezia Terme;via Ubaldo de' Medici 50, Lamezia Terme, 88046, Italy;38.9747876;16.3178609;47;false;true;Creative, Calabrian;Although you hardly notice the door to this restaurant from outside, once inside you are immediately struck by the modern elegance of the decor with its vaguely Scandinavian feel. This mini gem occupying a 19C palazzo in Nicastro, the historic centre of Lamezia, is home to owner-chef Luigi Lepore who has returned to his native Calabria after gaining impressive experience in France and Italy. Here, he delights guests with the best regional ingredients which he precisely and skilfully transforms into contemporary dishes with a fine balance of bitter and acidic flavours, and an intriguing hint of citrus fruit. There’s no à la carte, just three tasting menus: Origini (five courses) and A Mano Libera (available with either seven or nine courses). Diners are warmly welcomed with a smile by the chef’s sister, Stefania, who oversees the front of house and describes her brother’s dishes to guests.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1343;Gabbiano 3.0;Italy;Marina di Grosseto;Porto turistico 11, Marina di Grosseto, 58100, Italy;42.7137124;10.9836869;66;true;true;Creative;Overlooking the dock, this restaurant boasts a timber decor and 180° views of the sea and Punta Ala, the islands of Elba, Giglio and Montecristo, and the Argentario – a delightful panorama which is even more spectacular at sunset. At the helm in the kitchen, Alessandro Rossi creates two tasting menus featuring dishes that can also be ordered à la carte style. Not surprisingly, fish takes centre stage, although you’ll also find a few meat options and vegetables, many of which are sourced from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1344;Il Marin;Italy;Genoa;Calata Cattaneo, 15, Edificio Millo, Porto Antico, Genoa, 16121, Italy;44.4087159;8.9274716;86;true;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Situated at the old port, in the same building and on the same floor as Eataly, this restaurant is simple in style so that nothing detracts from the view through its floor-to-ceiling windows. The cuisine focuses on regional traditions while reinterpreting these with modern ideas and techniques. Examples include a “spaghetti Martini cocktail”, which is shaken at your table by the chef and made with Martini bitters and creamed olives flavoured with a misted extra virgin Taggiasca gin, and tortelli with a sauce made with fishheads, guts and bones and a pleasant hint of marjoram to add a final touch of flavour.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1345;Casa Buono;Italy;Ventimiglia;corso Cuneo 28, Ventimiglia, 18039, Italy;43.8460898;7.5886507;86;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;This unexpected Ligurian gem is situated in Trucco, a small village in the Val Roia just inland from Ventimiglia. There’s no à la carte here, just the “Orto e Mare” tasting menu to which guests can also add a meat dish and a selection of cheeses from the well-stocked cheese trolley. Although the dishes are occasionally influenced by Ligurian traditions, they are for the most part creative, surprising and beautifully prepared. Given its success, the restaurant has recently been extended while at the same time retaining its simple, colourful and welcoming ambience. The high-quality service comes courtesy of the chef’s friendly wife, ably assisted by her professional and capable staff.;Air conditioning;[]
1346;Vite;Italy;Lancenigo;viale della Repubblica 3, Lancenigo, 31020, Italy;45.6981936;12.2575026;60;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;Make sure you take a look at the two dining rooms at this restaurant, both of which are striking for their contemporary design, individual character (they are very different from each other) and beautiful furnishings. In the kitchen, Leoluca Brambilla prepares two tasting menus which are fundamentally creative yet at the same time influenced by the region, featuring fish and seafood (especially from the Venetian lagoon) and meat from the inland Marca Trevigiana area.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1347;Osteria degli Assonica;Italy;Sorisole;via Don Santo Carminati 9, Sorisole, 24010, Italy;45.7431411;9.6526781;57;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Situated in the hills just beyond Bergamo, this smart, elegant and well-run restaurant has the Manzoni brothers (Alex and Vittorio) at the helm in the kitchen, where they create some of the most interesting cuisine in the region, while the capable Giovanna Danzo oversees the excellent service in the dining room. Creative and surprising, the dishes here are striking for their complex and original flavours, which combine vegetables with a clever use of herbs and spices without overwhelming the palate. The chargrilled veal sweetbreads (slightly crunchy on the outside and soft inside) are delicious, served with a selection of mushrooms and a fir extract that provides a hint of bitterness. There’s a strong focus on sourcing local ingredients in order to create cuisine which is both contemporary and sustainable at the same time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1349;Imàgo;Italy;Rome;piazza Trinità dei Monti 6, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9059417;12.4836585;69;false;false;Italian Contemporary;The location of this rooftop restaurant could hardly be more glamorous. Head up the most famous flight of steps in the world to the Hassler hotel, where you take a lift up to one of the Italian capital’s most celebrated restaurants. Here, you dine surrounded by floor-to-ceiling windows that offer superb views of Rome, from the twin bell towers of Trinità dei Monti church to a whole host of the city’s iconic monuments – see how many you can recognise! In the meantime, chef Andrea Antonini prepares two tasting menus that showcase his classic dishes alongside more recent creations. His cuisine is often based on recognised recipes and ingredients, while also exploring new ideas, unusual combinations and amusing reinterpretations.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1350;Inkiostro;Italy;Parma;via San Leonardo 124, Parma, 43122, Italy;44.8270877;10.3368273;46;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;Calabrian chef Salvatore Morello brings an innovative air to Parma, a city with a fine gastronomic reputation. Influenced by experience working abroad, he embraces diverse recipes and ingredients, all of which boast finesse, style and originality, and uses top-quality produce and ingredients which, even when they verge on the exotic, are always in harmony with the individual dishes. This chef’s memorable recipes include white skate, pickled Asian vegetables, beans and ramen, and his superb pre-desserts, including a 24-month-old parmesan dessert and delicious small pastries. The selection of beverages is on a par with the food, with beers, sake and spirits on the menu alongside an impressive choice of wine – for the latter, you can rely on the restaurant’s loyal sommelier to provide expert advice.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1351;Porta di Basso;Italy;Peschici;via Colombo 38, Peschici, 71010, Italy;41.9493778;16.0129423;88;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Owner-chef Domenico Cilenti offers a choice of two tasting menus: one dedicated to classic dishes that tell the story of the restaurant and the other a “blind” menu that changes daily depending on the ingredients available in the market. Whichever you choose, the cuisine served is deliberately simple and precise, allowing the full flavours of Puglia’s vibrant produce to shine through. Each dish consists of just a few ingredients arranged in a colourful and elegant presentation on ad hoc porcelain.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1352;Tancredi;Italy;Sirmione;via XXV Aprile 75, Sirmione, 25019, Italy;45.4771961;10.6108961;38;false;false;Creative;Having trained with Antonino Cannavacciuolo, young chef Vincenzo Manicone has, with his wife Sara, embarked on a new venture in this elegant restaurant with a glass-fronted dining room and a terrace suspended between the lake and the sky. Showcased on tasting menus and an à la carte, the chef’s cuisine demonstrates a maturity that pays close attention to colour and flavour, with beautifully presented dishes prepared from top-quality, well-balanced ingredients. Also evident is the aim, currently in vogue, of reducing food waste by using every single part of the animal (as in the case of the excellent amberjack, curly salad and sea urchin dish that we very much enjoyed). In summer, we recommend requesting a table at the front of the terrace, right over the lake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1353;Dolce Stil Novo alla Reggia;Italy;Venaria Reale;piazza della Repubblica 4, Venaria Reale, 10078, Italy;45.1351147;7.6249928;58;true;true;Italian Contemporary;It could be said that this restaurant boasts a regal setting, given that its entrance stands in the inner courtyard of the Reggia di Venaria, the spectacular former residence of the House of Savoy. You then take the lift to the fourth floor and the restaurant’s dining room, elegantly furnished in 1950-60s style, and a summer terrace overlooking the garden. The cuisine here is centred around superb ingredients grown in the valleys of Piedmont, and occasionally further afield in the region and beyond, and is showcased in dishes that combine tradition and creativity.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1354;Gucci Osteria da Massimo Bottura;Italy;Florence;piazza della Signoria 10, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7698043;11.2567125;81;false;false;Italian Contemporary, International;Florence’s cosmopolitan credentials receive a boost with Karime Lopez and Takahiko Kondo’s cuisine, served in this modern, lively restaurant that bears the name of theatrical chef Massimo Bottura. The cuisine overseen by these excellent cooks demonstrates an openness to the rest of the world, with influences and reinterpretations of dishes from other countries, as well as Italy and Modena in particular. In addition to the à la carte, there are two tasting menus (I Nostri Souvenirs and Le Nostre Nuove Memorie) and - only for lunch the Breve Viaggio in Osteria. A visit to the Gucci Garden, an elegant museum on the upper floors dedicated to the famous fashion house, is highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1355;La Speranzina Restaurant & Relais;Italy;Sirmione;via Dante 16, Sirmione, 25019, Italy;45.4931589;10.6085873;25;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;A romantic, Mediterranean-style restaurant in the heart of Sirmione, La Speranzina has a classic, elegant decor in which light colours dominate, while in summer the terrace boasts spectacular views of the lake and castle (a few of the tables stand right over the water). The menu, created by a new chef who trained with Heinz Beck, includes various tasting options featuring elegant dishes with a balance of different, occasionally exotic ingredients that result in inviting, carefully prepared and mouthwatering flavours. We particularly enjoyed the spaghettone with wild broccoli, clams, lemon, Espelette chilli peppers, gobbetto shrimps and cavolo nero. A superbly stocked wine cellar, with an excellent choice of champagnes and renowned labels, and three stunning panoramic suites for an overnight stay complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1356;Paolo e Barbara;Italy;San Remo;via Roma 47, San Remo, 18038, Italy;43.8148723;7.7738025;82;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;Paolo and Barbara have been serving excellent cuisine in San Remo since 1987, demonstrating a real passion for local ingredients and regional specialities. This interest has culminated in kitchen gardens that now provide most of the ingredients used in their dishes, including eggs, olive oil and a small amount of wine. Along with top-quality fish, vegetables form the basis of western Liguria’s cuisine, which Paolo combines in his reinterpretations of traditional recipes. His style is showcased in dishes such as cappelletti (a type of egg ravioli) filled with San Remo crayfish and served with a vegetable and Abruzzo saffron broth, an elegant dish that is full of flavour. Barbara oversees the service front of house and provides guests with wine recommendations.;Air conditioning;[]
1357;Osteria di Passignano;Italy;Passignano;via Passignano 33, Passignano, 50028, Italy;43.5768675;11.2458106;22;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Part of the Antinori estate, this restaurant has an elegant feel despite describing itself as an “osteria” (a more informal inn). It occupies an old site next to the old Badia di Passignano abbey after which it is named, and in whose wine cellars some of Antinori’s best Chianti is laid to age. This charming setting is full of history and references to wine. In the kitchen, the young chef maintains strong connections with the region and its wine, creating a menu with a resolutely seasonal focus. The personalised dishes are modern and cleverly designed to make full use of the property’s two stand-out features – the abbey’s beautiful kitchen garden which provides the chef with his herbs and vegetables, and the wine list which is truly impressive. The Tuscan wines are particularly notable, especially the legendary labels from the restaurant’s own winery.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1358;Horto;Italy;Milan;via San Protaso 5, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4661897;9.1875693;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Organic;Norbert Niederkofler’s arrival in Milan is accompanied by his strong commitment to the environment. The cuisine here is in the capable hands of Alberto Toè, who offers two tasting menus with a focus on locally sourced ingredients (all from within an hour of the city). The outdoor terraces are an added attraction, boasting fine views which extend from the Duomo to the Castello Sforzesco, and are the perfect setting for an aperitif from the restaurant’s extensive cocktail list. The interior dining room has a simple yet elegant feel thanks to its natural-wood tables, making it a good choice for a gourmet supper or a simpler and more casual lunch.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1359;I Portici;Italy;Bologna;via dell'Indipendenza 69, Bologna, 40121, Italy;44.5019817;11.3448122;76;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Occupying the atmospheric setting of the Eden theatre, a former late-19C musical café, this restaurant adorned with beautiful Liberty-style frescoes is the perfect backdrop for elegant, well-balanced Mediterranean-inspired dishes. Young, talented chef Nicola Annunziata offers three tasting menus of five (L’Ora Precisa), seven (La Spudorata) and nine (La Luce) courses with wine pairings recommended by the knowledgeable sommelier. If you’re looking for a quieter and more romantic ambience, book a table in the 14C icehouse, with its glass floor providing glimpses of the well-stocked wine cellar below.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1361;Contaminazioni Restaurant;Italy;Somma Vesuviana;via San Sossio 2, Somma Vesuviana, 80049, Italy;40.8760367;14.4426613;23;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Japanese;It’s worth pointing out from the outset that the dishes served at this restaurant on the slopes of Vesuvius are a far cry from the classic, traditional cuisine of Campania. Here, young chef Giuseppe Molaro offers surprise tasting menus of varying lengths, drawing on his experience working outside Italy, particularly in Japan, where he developed a passion for the cuisine of that country (and not just sushi). His dishes combine Japanese influences with local flavours to create dishes that are sometimes challenging (fermented or acidic flavours occasionally dominate) yet are perfect for anyone keen to try bold, innovative and experimental recipes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1362;Lazzaro 1915;Italy;Pontelongo;via Roma 351, Pontelongo, 35029, Italy;45.2499891;12.0203099;36;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Although it is now home to a welcoming and contemporary family restaurant, this building was once used as a place to rest horses and provide hospitality to workers from the sugar factory opposite. Daniela Siviero oversees the front of house with charm and professionalism, while her brother Piergiorgio is at the helm in the kitchen. The restaurant serves two tasting menus: “DNA”, an 8-course menu showcasing technically creative cuisine that focuses on regional fish and meat options prepared in different ways, and the 4-course “Campagna Liquida” which changes weekly and on which vegetables take pride of place. Daniela will recommend the best wine pairing from a well-structured wine list that includes some real gems.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1363;Osteria Altran;Italy;Ruda;Località Cortona 19, Ruda, 33050, Italy;45.8132892;13.410651;27;false;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;A small gourmet restaurant surrounded by the verdant landscapes of the Friuli countryside. In what was once a simple farm, owner Guido Lanzellotti has brought this seemingly rustic yet delightfully romantic restaurant to life, creating modern cuisine that focuses on top-quality ingredients and careful preparation. The lounge-cum-library adorned with cookery books is available for small private events as well as aperitifs and post-dinner drinks. Our inspector recommends the lobster soup and mixed pasta, a dish inspired by a traditional “buzara”-style recipe, with a delicious shellfish jus and al dente pasta. The dish is served with a “smetana” sauce that is very similar to sour cream and is Russian in origin.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1364;Silene;Italy;Seggiano;Località Pescina 9, Seggiano, 58038, Italy;42.9193337;11.5873607;73;false;true;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;This authentic family restaurant situated in a quiet mountain village with just a few inhabitants serves delicious home-made cuisine. The owner-chef here delights guests with his decidedly Tuscan dishes full of intense flavours and prepared mainly from produce grown in the restaurant’s kitchen garden. His generous offerings include proverbial recipes such as fried egg with leaves and flowers and his classic pigeon with herbs, all seasoned with olive oil produced on the property from Seggiano olives. Excellent wine list, plus thoughtful recommendations to accompany your meal.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
1365;Osteria Acquarol;Italy;San Michele;via Johann Georg Plazer 10, San Michele, 39057, Italy;46.4556659;11.2589442;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Alpine;Centrally located and with a plain, almost minimalist interior and a small charming outdoor space on the pedestrianised street for summer dining, Osteria Acquarol serves dishes which are strongly rooted in the region yet prepared with modern techniques and very much influenced by the character of the owner-chef here. Regionally sourced sustainable ingredients often feature in its highly original cuisine, including aromatic and wild herbs grown in the chef’s own garden. In 2023, the restaurant’s kitchen garden was extended so vegetables now play a more dominant role in the two tasting menus served here (seven and nine courses, with dishes that can be chosen à la carte style) – examples include the cold minestra soup entitled “L'orto dietro l'angolo” (“the garden around the corner”) and the unusual green tagliatelle with its carefully balanced bitter flavours. Originally from Cremona, chef Alessandro Bellingeri showcases the region in interesting and original ways.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
1366;Lorelei;Italy;Sorrento;via Aniello Califano 4, Sorrento, 80067, Italy;40.6298333;14.3813239;27;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Even if the weather isn’t kind and you can’t eat outdoors, make sure you have an aperitif or perhaps just take a look at the terrace with its stunning views of the Bay of Naples, especially at sunset. Once the sun has set, enjoy dishes prepared by chef Ciro Sicignano, who hails from Gragnano and who showcases the specialities of Campania to perfection. The region’s traditional recipes and ingredients are reinterpreted with energy and imagination, with a focus on vegetables (which the chef sources from two kitchen gardens) and a dedicated olive oil menu. The elegant setting of the Lorelei Londres hotel adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1367;Pulejo;Italy;Rome;via dei Gracchi 31, Rome, 00192, Italy;41.9071673;12.4593589;47;true;false;Italian Contemporary;The elegant residential Prati district is home to this equally elegant restaurant, where guests dine in a romantic, subtly lit dining room served by discreet yet ever-present and professional staff. The varied cuisine demonstrates influences not only from Lazio, but also from other places where the chef has worked in the past, with well-constructed dishes prepared from top-quality ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
1368;Cannavacciuolo Countryside;Italy;Ticciano;via Ticciano 137, Ticciano, 80069, Italy;40.6456678;14.4515515;73;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant tells the story of chef Antonino Cannavacciuolo, who created this special place to reconnect with his childhood memories (his grandfather was once the caretaker here) and its sense of hospitality. This chef’s culinary philosophy is ably interpreted by resident chef Nicola Somma, who celebrates the region by combining ingredients from Cannavacciuolo’s adopted home with his native region in a journey that takes guests from northern to southern Italy. The ingredients used are carefully chosen and either sourced from local producers or grown in the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, keeping alive the precious traditions that have influenced this chef’s character and culinary skill. There’s an excellent and constantly expanding wine list, which will more than satisfy even the most demanding wine-buffs. An unforgettable, relaxing gourmet experience in a bucolic setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1369;Acqua Pazza;Italy;Ponza;via Dietro la Chiesa 3/4, Ponza, 04027, Italy;40.8950712;12.9672021;57;true;false;Seafood;Arranged on a series of multi-levelled terraces, the tables at this restaurant boast breathtaking views of the semicircular port, as well as much of the island extending out to sea as far as Gavi and Zannone. Consequently, this restaurant boasts one of the most spectacular views in Italy. The cuisine focuses almost exclusively on fish and seafood in unfussy dishes which allow the ingredients to take centre stage – along with the surrounding scenery!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1370;Taverna del Capitano;Italy;Marina del Cantone;piazza delle Sirene 10/11, Marina del Cantone, 80061, Italy;40.5833911;14.3565359;80;false;false;Creative;A series of hairpin bends lead downhill to Marina del Cantone, one of the most beautiful beaches on this stretch of coastline, situated in a romantic bay sheltered by the Tre Pizzi promontory. Here, you’ll find the Taverna del Capitano, where the Casa Caputo dining room near the entrance serves simple, traditional cuisine, while the Michelin-starred gourmet restaurant boasts a rooftop setting where guests dine overlooking the beach with the sound of the waves as a backdrop. In the open-view kitchen behind the tables, Alfonso Caputo prepares dishes based on local fish, as well as the occasional meat option, all of which have a Mediterranean flavour and a focus on the region’s extraordinary ingredients.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1371;Marotta;Italy;Squille;via Marrochelle 52, Squille, 81010, Italy;41.146241;14.4096379;39;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Nestled amid the verdant hills of the Upper Caserta region, this delightful restaurant is a real gem. Young chef Domenico Marotta serves surprisingly high-quality cuisine with a focus on local ingredients and vegetables (some from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden) which he transforms into modern, minimalist yet generous dishes which are anything but predictable, and are showcased on three tasting menus and a short à la carte. We particularly enjoyed the Leccarda-style pigeon, a reinterpretation of a traditionally Umbrian dish, in which every part of the bird is used. The sommelier/head waiter is as impressive as the talented chef, as he guides guests on their culinary journey with his detailed and enthusiastic explanations.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1372;La Coldana;Italy;Lodi;Cascina Coldana, via del Costino, Lodi, 26900, Italy;45.30426;9.51811;94;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Housed in an old 18C farmhouse on the outskirts of the town on the edge of the countryside, La Coldana is run by two young business partners (recently joined by the young chef Alessandro Proietti Refrigeri) who have gradually transformed it over the years into an eatery serving top-quality and distinctive cuisine, with some dishes now established as iconic favourites. Examples include the “turnips, roots and vegetables” dish made from over 30 varieties prepared in different ways and accompanied, as recommended by the chef, by mallow kombucha. There are three tasting menus available, one of which offers a selection of surprise dishes chosen by the chef.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1373;FRE;Italy;Monforte d'Alba;località San Sebastiano 68, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.5638925;7.9622354;74;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Nestled among the vineyards of the Réva resort less than 4km from the delightful village of Monforte d'Alba, you’ll find the FRE restaurant run by chef Francesco Marchese, who offers a perfect combination of sophisticated French techniques and fine ingredients from the Langhe with refined simplicity. For all their sophistication, the dishes are always full of rich flavours – the ravioli del plin with crispy sweetbreads, onion cooked in milk and dehydrated beer yeast is a perfect example. There’s a superb wine list with labels also available by the glass, while more informal fare is served at the Piccolo FRE Bistrot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1374;Peter Brunel Ristorante Gourmet;Italy;Arco;via Linfano 47, Arco, 38062, Italy;45.8869889;10.8788696;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;In this restaurant situated less than 1km from the shores of beautiful Lake Garda, chef Peter Brunel from Trentino not only creates contemporary cuisine but has also designed many of the decorative details in the dining room, demonstrating a truly artistic soul. The whole place is designed to provide an enjoyable gourmet experience, from the friendly welcome to the sofas and armchairs where guests can sit and enjoy an aperitif accompanied by some enticing appetisers. With the passing of time, Brunel has proven to be ever more skilful in showcasing the Trentino to Italy and the rest of the world, sometimes in nikkei-style dishes, and sometimes in more Mediterranean fare with the occasional flight of fantasy inspired by the chef’s passion for Italian poet Gabriele D’Annunzio. Front of house, the equally brilliant Christian Rainer provides recommendations from the excellent wine list with an acclaimed professionalism that knows few equals.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1375;Moebius Sperimentale;Italy;Milan;via Cappelini 25, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4814199;9.2028665;90;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Occupying an old textile workshop, this restaurant is one of the most attractive in Milan with its modern, chic-industrial setting divided into three separate spaces: a cocktail bar with an impressive selection of gins, a bistro serving tapas, and an experimental restaurant. The restaurant is housed in a glass-enclosed room with space for 30 guests, built on a suspended platform in the centre of the building. Creative and exciting cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1376;Il Visibilio;Italy;Castelnuovo Berardenga;SP 9 di Pievasciata 32, Castelnuovo Berardenga, 53019, Italy;43.391479;11.3899308;76;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;You’ll come to the imposing gate of The Club House hotel at the end of a dirt track which leads from the contemporary art village of Pievasciata into the surrounding cultivated hills. Il Visibilio, the hotel’s small gourmet restaurant, is the setting for the happy partnership between Tuscan chef Daniele Canella and two-Michelin-starred chef Giuseppe Iannotti from Krèsios in Telese Terme. The latter brings to the Sienese countryside a similar formula to the one introduced in his own restaurant, namely a single blind tasting menu. This long gourmet feast features surprise meat and fish dishes as well as an abundant use of vegetables, showcasing technical flourishes that are especially evident in the finger-food appetisers, resulting in a top-quality fine-dining experience. Our inspector recommends the pigeon with its delicious rhubarb and absinthe sauce.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view;[]
1379;The Cook;Italy;Genoa;vico Falamonica 9 r, Genoa, 16123, Italy;44.4080433;8.9339301;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Housed in the beautiful 14C Branca Doria palazzo in Genova’s historic centre with its typical narrow alleyways, this restaurant boasts an extraordinary ceiling decorated with frescoes by Bernardo Strozzi in 1618. Chef Ivano Ricchebono’s cuisine is served on three tasting menus from which guests can choose courses à la carte style, even combining dishes from different menus. The cuisine is largely creative in style, with an equal balance of meat and fish options available.;Air conditioning;[]
1380;Andrea Monesi - Locanda di Orta;Italy;Orta San Giulio;via Olina 18, Orta San Giulio, 28016, Italy;45.7987785;8.4058245;54;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;Situated in the historic centre of one of the most romantic lakeside villages in Italy, and offering a picture-postcard view of bygone days, this small building houses a contemporary-style restaurant (including a recently opened private dining room) with just one table for two on its romantic outdoor terrace. The cuisine here is creative and precise, with a menu that features fish and seafood alongside top-quality meat from the Piedmont. Each recipe is personalised, often focusing on contrasting flavours and textures, while the wine list is overseen by an excellent sommelier who is happy to guide you in your choice. The imaginative desserts are also well worth a mention.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1381;Glicine;Italy;Amalfi;via Mauro Comite 9, Amalfi, 84011, Italy;40.6294267;14.5928504;36;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Situated just outside Amalfi with the elegant Mediterranean landscapes of the Amalfi Coast as a backdrop, this fine-dining restaurant at the beautiful Santa Caterina hotel is perched above the sea and boasts stunning views and a tranquil ambience. Talented chef “Peppe” Stanzione from Salerno is at the helm here, having gained experience in renowned Michelin-starred restaurants in places as far afield as California, Australia, China and Thailand. While his passion for Asia is obvious in some dishes, it is the flavours and recipes of Campania that are to the fore, combined with other more exotic influences. Examples include the delicious tuna cooked in an infusion of sake and soy sauce and accompanied by smoked aubergine cream topped with crispy saffron onions and yuzu. There’s also a good choice of vegan, vegetarian and gluten-free dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1382;Villa Naj;Italy;Stradella;via Martiri Partigiani 5, Stradella, 27049, Italy;45.0767345;9.3006567;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;In the heart of the Oltrepò Pavese region, a minimalist entrance leads into this 19C villa, where the old wine cellars house a modern dining room with a beautiful brick-vaulted ceiling. In this elegant setting, Dario Fisichella, a Sicilian chef with experience working abroad and elsewhere in Italy, prepares dishes that showcase excellent local ingredients while also taking inspiration from the culinary traditions of his native island, to which he adds his own creative twist. The wine list features over 300 labels, including an impressive selection of local and French sparkling wines and a superb choice of fortified Marsalas.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1383;Matteo Grandi in Basilica;Italy;Vicenza;piazza dei Signori 1, Vicenza, 36100, Italy;45.547245;11.5459015;88;true;false;Farm to table, Contemporary;Situated on the first floor of a beautiful building facing the Renaissance-style Basilica Palladiana, this restaurant run by Matteo Grandi and Elena Lanza boasts an elegant, contemporary-style dining room with windows offering views of the piazza. Chef Matteo now offers a new surprise menu, where guests simply decide on the number of courses they want (usually three, five or eight) and he does the rest, creating delicious cuisine prepared from the best ingredients available in the market that day – which means, of course, that the dishes can change daily. What remains unchanged, however, is his expertise and his intention to serve ingredients without adding unnecessary frills, just the occasional Asian twist thanks to his previous experience working in China. Elena continues to welcome guests and oversee the front of house, assisted by the sommelier and an impressive wine list. The bread here is also excellent.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1384;Alici;Italy;Amalfi;via Giovanni Augustariccio 33, Amalfi, 84011, Italy;40.6188758;14.5766031;78;true;true;Campanian, Contemporary;Alici is the fine-dining restaurant at Borgo Santandrea, a beautiful luxury hotel situated just outside the village of Conca dei Marini on the Amalfi Coast, where both the hotel and restaurant represent the best of Italian style. The dining room is furnished with vintage-style decor, although meals are nearly always served on the magnificent terrace which boasts fanciful majolica tiles in shades of azure that echo the colours of the sea and sky. Chef Crescenzo Scotti is fond of beautiful places, having previously worked in Ravello and, before that, at a Michelin-starred restaurant on the island of Vulcano. Here, he returns to his favourite region with skill and craftsmanship, focusing on the flavours of the Amalfi Coast as well as Naples and his native Ischia, while always adding a touch of fantasy to his dishes. He reinterprets a typical dish from Praiano ("Totano e patate alla praianese") by including interesting personal touches such squid in a tomato sauce, fried squid meatballs and raw squid, while the excellent Gragnano pasta, cooked with partly melted potatoes to create a delicious cream, is added at your table. It is then left to the guest to mix everything together to create a truly delicious dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1385;La Caravella dal 1959;Italy;Amalfi;via Matteo Camera 12, Amalfi, 84011, Italy;40.6338537;14.6016228;59;false;false;Campanian, Mediterranean Cuisine;La Caravella’s history is intricately linked to that of gastronomic tourism on the Amalfi Coast, so much so that it’s impossible to mention all the famous personalities who have dined here and fallen in love with the Dipino family’s cuisine. The food is proudly inspired by local and family traditions, while at the same time constantly seeking to reinterpret these traditions and create new imaginative recipes. Examples include pears cooked in Aglianico wine served with raw shrimps and cow’s ricotta cheese, and raw fish and seafood options accompanied by a careful selection of seasonal vegetables. Two important features here are the focus on simple, traditional cooking techniques and the speed of preparation. The menu showcases the best of the area’s fresh fish, including pezzogna (a variety of sea bream), swordfish and tuna, supplemented when necessary by options from the nearby Cilento region. Other ingredients include tomatoes (which feature in almost half the dishes), Amalfi’s famous lemons (the classic lemon soufflé is highly recommended), basil and Agerola bread – you’ll want to order almost everything on the menu! The excellent wine list features reds, whites, sparkling, sweet, young and vintage wines, with legendary labels such as La Tâche listed alongside smaller, unknown, rare and organic wines. Whatever your preference, sommelier Tonino has that rare talent (also found at the Enoteca Pinchiorri) of finding just the right wine for you.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1386;San Martino;Italy;Treviglio;viale Cesare Battisti 3, Treviglio, 24047, Italy;45.5241033;9.5937071;60;false;true;Seafood;One of the best restaurants in the area, San Martino focuses on fish dishes including classic favourites inherited from the chef’s father as well as more creative fare introduced by the new generation. The Colleoni family never fails to impress! Our inspectors particularly appreciated the constant search for perfection demonstrated by owner-chef Vittorio. This perfection is also evident in the private kitchen garden where flowers and vegetables are grown, emphasising the importance that this chef places on the provenance of his ingredients. The chef’s brother Paolo is responsible for the wine list, which is extensive and well structured, with a slight preference for French labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1387;Il Piastrino;Italy;Pennabilli;via Parco Begni 7, Pennabilli, 47864, Italy;43.82111;12.2645054;30;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;The home of Claudia and Riccardo, Il Piastrino is situated amid the beautiful Montefeltro hills. A long-held dream for this couple, which they nurtured for years, the restaurant has been embellished with each passing year and now boasts a magnificent contemporary decor that is in total harmony with the warm rustic nature of its surroundings. The restaurant’s crowning glory is Riccardo Agostini’s technical, creative cuisine, which showcases the best seasonal, regional ingredients. This chef’s dishes are complex and elaborate in style yet never overly fussy. One of our favourite dishes was the spaghetto al verde with pink Adriatic prawns and pecorino cheese – this green-coloured Latini pasta with cavolo nero and chicory is served with delicious whole prawns with intense maritime flavours and just the right amount of pecorino to balance the bitter chicory with the sweet prawns. The interesting “Collina” tasting menu includes ingredients and traditions from the valley that extends from the source of the Marecchia river across the hills to the sea.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1388;Guido;Italy;Rimini;lungomare Guido Spadazzi 12, Rimini, 47924, Italy;44.03226;12.62138;77;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Although from the outside this looks like a simple private beach club with views of the sea in the distance, the interior reveals an unexpected and hushed elegance. Guests flock to Guido’s for its excellent fish and seafood: the dishes sound simple on the menu, yet are actually refined, elegant and beautifully prepared, celebrating the Adriatic in all its glory, with a focus on top-quality fish dishes. The menu features long-established classics (“canocchia si ricorda il gratin”) alongside new dishes such as the pizza ai frutti di mare which are themselves destined to become staples here. There’s a good choice of sparkling wines, as well as a focus on excellent whites and renowned reds.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
1389;Massimo Camia;Italy;La Morra;SP3 Alba-Barolo 122, La Morra, 12064, Italy;44.6267818;7.957004;76;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;In this restaurant decorated with modern furnishings, the attention is drawn to the picture windows offering fine views of the La Morra hills and the surrounding countryside. Here, the cuisine prepared by Massimo Camia and his daughter Elisabetta includes classic favourites from the chef’s much-loved repertoire, such as the delicious rack of lamb beautifully presented on Luserna stone and served with a barbeque sauce, as well as other elegant dishes, including a few fish options. The excellent selection of Piedmontese cheese is also worth a mention. The chef’s son, sommelier Iacopo, skilfully and enthusiastically guides guests through the encyclopaedic wine list which includes an extensive choice of Barolo wines and other local labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1390;Il Flauto di Pan;Italy;Ravello;via Santa Chiara 26, Ravello, 84010, Italy;40.6446307;14.6111085;63;true;false;Creative;It would be no exaggeration to say that this restaurant (part of the Villa Cimbrone hotel) is situated in one of the most romantic and exclusive spots in Italy, surrounded by luxuriant Mediterranean vegetation and with stunning views of the Gulf of Salerno. Once at the restaurant, you make your way to the terrace, where views of the sea with the Cilento mountains in the distance are framed by a beautiful wisteria. The chef from Campania offers guests a superb selection of local produce, prepared in traditional and reinterpreted dishes that are full of the intense and explosive flavours of this extraordinary region. Make sure you book a table in advance!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1391;Luisl Stube;Italy;Algund;via Venosta 4, Algund, 39022, Italy;46.6780899;11.1191355;17;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Schlosswirt Forst is a typical 16C residence that is home to a traditional restaurant, a few guestrooms and the Luisl Stube, a small gem boasting the beautiful old wood and traditional chandeliers of a historic Stube, with more candles than tables (of which there are just four) creating a timeless, intimate and truly romantic atmosphere. In contrast, the cuisine is contemporary in style, prepared by chef Luis Haller, who carefully searches out local produce which he serves alongside a few more exotic ingredients, as well as fish and seafood, on his two tasting menus. Talented sommelier Nicola Spimpolo delights guests with his exceptional wine pairings, exploring old vintages in his constant quest for superb, high-quality labels.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1392;SanBrite;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;Località Alverà, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.5434618;12.1565176;44;false;true;Alpine, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant has just a few tables amid a decor of elegantly recycled old wood, while a large window offers views of the stunning Ampezzo Dolomites outside. Your meal starts in a memorable way: waiters file into the dining room carrying mountains of creamy butter, which is served to every table accompanied by excellent bread with an incomparable texture. Owner-chef Riccardo Gaspari makes careful use of home-produced and regional ingredients, creating delicious cuisine in which mountain traditions are refreshed with modern touches, most noticeably visible in the desserts which are made without adding extra sugar. Sanbrite literally means “healthy pasture”, a name that definitely evokes the qualities of the cuisine served here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1393;Paca;Italy;Prato;via Fra' Bartolomeo 13, Prato, 59100, Italy;43.8771796;11.1021824;100;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Chef Niccolò Palumbo, pastry chef Gabriele Palumbo and maître-d’ Lorenzo Catucci are the three young, dynamic entrepreneurs behind this attractive restaurant just a stone’s throw from the historic centre. The welcoming dining room here provides the backdrop for modern Italian cuisine prepared with carefully chosen ingredients which are sourced, where possible, from small-scale local and zero-mile producers. Mouthwatering Colonnata lardo is often served with the delicious bread, which includes rice- and chestnut-flour options. The excellent service adds to this pleasant gourmet dining experience in the town of Prato.;Air conditioning;[]
1394;Quintessenza;Italy;Trani;via Lionelli 62, Trani, 76125, Italy;41.2814264;16.4150326;88;true;true;Apulian, Contemporary;Having moved to new premises near Castello Svevo and Santa Maria Assunta cathedral, this restaurant now boasts splendid views from its outdoor terrace and a comfortable, historic ambience in its other dining spaces (including a cellar) which are decorated in tasteful contemporary style. Quintessenza remains in the capable hands of the Di Gennaro family – four brothers (including head chef Stefano) who are equally passionate about Puglia and its excellent ingredients, especially fish and seafood, all of which are showcased in the superb, precisely prepared modern cuisine served here. There’s just one table in the splendid wine cellar (book well in advance), which offers a fine selection of wines including a few labels by the glass.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Terrace;[]
1395;La Favellina;Italy;Malo;via Cosari 4/6, località San Tomio, Malo, 36034, Italy;45.6195715;11.4018545;100;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;You follow winding roads up into the Lessini hills to get to this small paradise, a rustic setting which is home to an elegant, family-run restaurant where everyone works hard to ensure that you enjoy your evening. Federico Pettenuzzo and his mother are at the helm in the kitchen (the latter responsible for the delicious pastas), while Federico’s brother Riccardo oversees the front of house. The creative cuisine is prepared from ingredients sourced from all over Italy and further afield, with some occasionally original combinations.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1396;Lorenzo;Italy;Forte dei Marmi;via Carducci 61, Forte dei Marmi, 55042, Italy;43.9565557;10.1722156;59;true;true;Seafood, Italian;This gastronomic institution has been an emblem of the Versilia region for the past 40 years, ever since it opened in 1981, and is now proudly run by daughter Chiara, an expert sommelier who, together with her staff, ensures that guests enjoy the best possible experience. Surrounded by contemporary works of art which change regularly (a passion inherited from great-grandfather Lorenzo after whom the restaurant is named), guests are guaranteed a fine dining experience thanks to the superb quality of the fish served here. The menu features iconic dishes and classic favourites such as warm seafood salad with shellfish served with seasonal vegetables, and top-quality scampi (baked or steamed) accompanied by mayonnaise that is freshly made in front of guests at their table. The wine cellar is also worthy of praise, with its two wine lists (one dedicated to Italy, the other to non-Italian wines) and a particular focus on French labels, especially from Champagne and Burgundy.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1397;Arnaldo - Clinica Gastronomica;Italy;Rubiera;piazza XXIV Maggio 3, Rubiera, 42048, Italy;44.65313;10.78183;31;true;true;Emilian;This restaurant was first awarded a Michelin star in 1959, which makes it the longest-held star (with a break of only two years) in Italy. Housed in a 15C palazzo next to the Aquila d'Oro hotel, the dining room boasts an atmospheric and nostalgic feel. The cuisine has the same traditional focus and celebrates Emilian traditions in all their glory, especially on the trolleys used to display selections of antipasti (sliced ham always features, as does spinach and cheese pie), and desserts (including a delicious zabaione served with pear in red wine and a creamy Sambuca semifreddo. But the undisputed stars of the show are the meat dishes, especially the two trolleys of specialities that are the highlight of any visit to Arnaldo. These include roast and boiled meats, including dishes not often found in a restaurant of this quality, such as calf’s head, tongue and pig’s trotters, all cooked traditionally and served with the usual sauces and gravies. Every morning, the “sfogline” pasta-makers prepare excellent fresh pastas, which are served either in a broth or simply with sage and butter. Arnaldo is not a place for fans of modern cuisine but if you’re keen to try authentic Emilian dishes full of flavour, you’ll be in your element here!;Wheelchair access;[]
1398;L'Erba del Re;Italy;Modena;via Castelmaraldo 45, Modena, 41121, Italy;44.64916;10.92368;42;false;true;Creative;Situated in a period palazzo near one of Modena’s oldest churches (the façade of Santa Maria della Pomposa dates from the medieval period and the church was rebuilt in 1717), this recently restored, modern and minimalist restaurant has just nine tables set some distance apart and is adorned with contemporary paintings on its walls. Talented chef Luca Marchini focuses mainly on creative cuisine, although fans of more traditional fare will also find a few Emilian specialities on the menu. The excellent sommelier is also able to recommend interesting and rare wines from small-scale wineries, including from outside Italy and often by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1399;La Primula;Italy;San Quirino;via San Rocco 47, San Quirino, 33080, Italy;46.0348797;12.6814506;63;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Situated between Pordenone and Aviano in the magical Magredi region, this elegant restaurant – still run by the Canton family – celebrates its 150th birthday in 2023. The attractive, comfortable dining room is dominated by a fireplace and provides the setting for delicious meat and fish dishes prepared by Andrea Canton, whose cuisine is carefully prepared, occasionally imaginative and full of comforting flavours. The excellent wine is divided into three sections: one dedicated to the Friuli-Venezia Giulia region, another to Italy as a whole, and the third to the rest of the world. The same building houses the Osteria alle Nazioni (also open at lunchtimes), where the cuisine is inspired by regional traditions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1400;Vignamare;Italy;Andora;strada Castello, 20 - Colla Micheri, Andora, 17051, Italy;43.9729346;8.150574;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;From Andora, head uphill along a winding road, then leave the car in the car park and follow a path through the vineyards to get to this restaurant, where meals are served either on a panoramic terrace (in fine weather) or indoors in a modern, wood-furnished dining room. Wherever you choose, the regionally influenced cuisine (often with a focus on vegetables) is extraordinary, with many ingredients grown or produced on the property. There are three tasting menus of various lengths, all of which showcase Ligurian cuisine. Similarly, the wine is sourced exclusively from the restaurant’s own estate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1401;Retroscena;Italy;Porto San Giorgio;largo del Teatro 3, Porto San Giorgio, 63822, Italy;43.1799835;13.7928865;67;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;One of the most interesting Michelin-starred restaurants in the region. Situated among houses with brick façades in Porto San Giorgio’s charming historic centre, this restaurant has just a few tables in an elegant, minimalist-style dining room. When focusing on their food, the attention of guests will be also drawn to the open-view kitchen, where the team led by Richard Abou Zaki prepares remarkable and often exciting dishes. Although this young yet highly experienced chef’s cuisine reveals influences from his time spent in Modena, for the most part his dishes are original, personalised and imaginative.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1402;Li Galli;Italy;Positano;viale Pasitea 318, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6283391;14.4841948;46;false;true;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;This restaurant housed within the elegant Villa Franca hotel in the upper part of Positano boasts a small, bright dining room with distinctive black marble tables (just seven of them!), a glass ceiling and floor-to-ceiling windows that open in summer to create an outdoor dining space. The beautiful view looks out to sea and Li Galli, the island after which the restaurant is named. Following the end of the restaurant’s partnership with Nino Di Costanzo, chef Savio Perna (originally from Torre del Greco) now steps into the spotlight on his own. He takes his inspiration mainly from the local region, although the pigeon in one of his more interesting dishes is sourced from one of the best breeders in Tuscany. Much of Perna’s technique focuses on beautiful presentation and a light touch, while the excellent service also adds to guests’ overall enjoyment of the dining experience. The trolleys that display a selection of olive oils, excellent bread and a choice of tempting desserts are also worth a special mention. The wine list practically spans the globe with around 1 000 different labels – France and Italy take centre stage, with a focus on champagne (especially Krug), with many wines also available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1403;Il Circolino;Italy;Monza;via Anita Garibaldi 4, Monza, 20900, Italy;45.5853814;9.2782646;66;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;At Il Circolino, enjoy interesting cuisine designed by Claudio Sadler and prepared by skilful resident chef Lorenzo Sacchi. There’s a café-cum-bistro at the entrance, with its own kitchen and an attractive garden for summer dining, while the elegant, contemporary-style restaurant is hidden behind a folding door. The gourmet meat and fish dishes served here are showcased on various menus from which guests can also choose courses à la carte style. On the “C’era una volta” menu, we particularly enjoyed the spaghetti with missoltino fish and carp butter, which is decorated with colourful flowers and has decisive flavours, while the mullet served with a Spanish-style “suquet” made from carefully chosen ingredients stood out on the “Viaje” menu. Among the desserts, the black lemon, shiso and kombu seaweed has a fresh and exotic flavour. If you enjoy watching the chefs at work, make sure you book the table in front of the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1404;Lunasia;Italy;Viareggio;viale Manin 4a, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.86546;10.24472;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;One of the most original and imaginative chefs in the Versilia region is at the helm in the luxury Plaza e de Russie hotel’s showcase restaurant, where the bright, modern dining room overlooks Viareggio’s famous seafront promenade. Three tasting menus are available here: the first dedicated to fish, the second vegetarian, and the third focusing on meat, with guests able to choose courses freely from each menu à la carte style. Whatever you choose the dishes here are of a rare elegance, with occasionally striking presentations. Chef Luca Landi’s cuisine pays tribute to the region, using excellent ingredients such as local fish and produce from Tuscany’s inland areas.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1406;Rossellinis;Italy;Ravello;via San Giovanni del Toro 28, Ravello, 84010, Italy;40.650822;14.6130382;34;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;The famous fine-dining restaurant at the beautiful Palazzo Avino hotel features classic, elegant dining rooms and a stunning terrace boasting views of one of the most spectacular stretches of the Amalfi Coast. Dinner begins with a flute of champagne served in the fabulous garden below the terrace (offering the same magical views as far as Minori and beyond), accompanied by delicious and imaginative finger food served on superb ceramic tableware. Your experience then continues with fine regional cuisine created by chef Gianni Vanacore, which is full of light and balanced flavours. Skilful sommelier Luigi Nitto is also at hand to assist with your wine selection from an extensive and exhaustive list that includes a vast choice of options from around the world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1407;Atto di Vito Mollica;Italy;Florence;via del Corso 6, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7715205;11.2573751;79;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Behind the cathedral in Florence, this gourmet restaurant is housed in the Corte degli Imperatori at Palazzo Portinari, once the residence of the Salviati family. Here, chef Vito Mollica delights guests with culinary creations that focus on the sea and unusual combinations that come as a pleasant surprise. The ingredients are of the highest quality, from the fragrant home-made bread to the highly distinctive first courses, plus there’s an excellent choice of olive oils (mainly Tuscan and Umbrian). Meals are served in a dining room adorned with original frescoes depicting episodes from the Odyssey, alongside scenes of daily life in the 16C, while the gentle bubbling of a fountain provides a pleasant background soundtrack. The exceptionally professional service enhance this sublime experience that combines artistry and gastronomy.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1408;Andrea Larossa;Italy;Turin;via Sabaudia 4, Turin, 10133, Italy;45.03681;7.68156;53;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Chef Andrea Larossa, a real connoisseur of the ingredients and tradition of Piedmont but equally at ease with more creative cuisine, is at the helm at this restaurant, where a large dining room is the setting for friendly, courteous and professional service. The tasting menus reflect the spirit of the chef’s cuisine, from the more regionally focused (albeit partly reinterpreted) option to a more imaginative menu which combines influences from all over Italy and even further afield. There’s a surprise menu for guests who prefer to rely on choices made by the chef himself.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1409;Otto Geleng;Italy;Taormina;via Teatro Greco 59, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.852584;15.290778;73;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sicilian;The elegant atmosphere at this restaurant is typical of Taormina and of Sicily’s old villas, with just eight tables laid out on a terrace adorned with bougainvillea and overlooking Taormina, the Bay of Naxos and Etna. The decor here shows real attention to detail, with an emphasis on the splendour of a grand old residence, while chef Roberto Toro creates typical Sicilian dishes reinterpreted with his own personal twist. His cuisine is showcased on various tasting menus, including a vegetarian option, from which dishes can be chosen à la carte style. We particularly enjoyed the chef’s signature dish, a memorable spaghetti with roast peppers, prawn, sesame and lime which was recommended by the attentive and discreet serving staff, who skilfully manage to put guests at ease in this impressive setting. More than 400 different wines are available to accompany this gourmet journey, with a choice of regional, Italian and French labels, including several excellent wines from small local wineries.;Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1410;Iyo Kaiseki;Italy;Milan;piazza Alvar Aalto 9N02, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4822057;9.1932579;52;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Situated in the heart of the modern Porta Nuova district, where the face of Milan has changed in spectacular and now iconic fashion, this restaurant is situated at the entrance to the Torre Solaria, one of the area’s most famous skyscrapers. Inside, you’ll find one of the city’s most elegant restaurants, where the decor is a modern mix of wood, stone and glass. Here, they serve kaiseki dishes, a faithful version of the most famous type of Japanese cuisine, including some of its most renowned recipes. There’s also a small dining room to one side with a sushi bar and just a few seats, where you can order the surprise omakase menu. The name “Iyo” may seem familiar to you, as the Michelin-starred Iyo (in the Corso Sempione district) also serves Japanese cuisine although it specialises in more creative and fusion-style dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
1411;Casa Leali;Italy;Puegnago sul Garda;via Valle 1, Puegnago sul Garda, 25080, Italy;45.5738761;10.5079936;21;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Year after year, the young, enthusiastic Leali brothers demonstrate their ability to run a top-quality restaurant: their Casa, elegantly housed in a restored 15C farmhouse, has become a renowned name in the region. In the kitchen, Andrea is precise and attentive in his selection of seasonal produce, preferring to concentrate on just a few ingredients in each dish, which he transforms with technical expertise and imagination. One example is the oysters cooked over the barbecue grill, served with olive pesto and shallots – a truly interesting antipasto, in which the sinuous flavour of the oyster is retained while combining it with other more elegant and subtle bitter tastes. The bread is also delicious. Marco is at the helm front of house, where he also oversees the wine list, demonstrating a real love for champagne and other sparkling wines.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1412;Don Alfonso 1890 San Barbato;Italy;Lavello;SS 93, km 56,300, Lavello, 85024, Italy;41.0348692;15.7714997;47;true;true;Country cooking, Creative;Run by the Iaccarino family, who are renowned for their Mediterranean cuisine at Sant'Agata sui Due Golfi (some of the latter’s dishes feature on the menu here, such as the spaghetto Don Alfonso), this restaurant owes much to its talented chef Donato De Leonardis. His excellent cuisine includes regional influences with a hint of exotic flavour in dishes that are balanced, harmonious and often original without becoming excessively extravagant. We particularly enjoyed the acquerello rice with saltwort, razor clams, green apple and sage, as well as the mullet with pak choi, seafood stew and purple potatoes. The restaurant occupies the first floor of the luxury San Barbato Resort, which has a strong and committed approach to sustainable resource management, and which is also home to three other restaurants, each serving a different type of cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1413;Casa Sgarra;Italy;Trani;lungomare C. Colombo 114, Trani, 76125, Italy;41.270434;16.4341752;73;false;false;Apulian, Creative;Three brothers (two front of house and one in the kitchen) offer a friendly welcome at this modern, elegant restaurant on the seafront at Trani, just a 20min walk from the town’s picturesque port. Although the menu also features dishes from other parts of Italy (especially Piedmont), on the whole the cuisine here is typical of Puglia, featuring local ingredients such a broad beans, almonds from Toritto, burrata and ricotta cheese, truffles and black chickpeas from Murgia, “grano arso” flour and, of course, the region’s excellent olive oils. The friendly, welcoming feel of the restaurant is summed up in the slogan that the three brothers have chosen for their restaurant – “a family story”. And, we would add, a story of fine cuisine!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1414;Cetaria;Italy;Baronissi;piazza della Repubblica 9, Baronissi, 84081, Italy;40.7469801;14.7701282;73;true;true;Contemporary, Campanian;This beautiful restaurant inland from Salerno is run by an enthusiastic couple, with Salvatore at the helm in the kitchen and Federica front of house. The dining room has an intimate ambience and just a few glass tables arranged under a high ceiling which evokes the palazzo’s historic character. Federica’s service is attentive and courteous (she won Michelin’s 2024 Service Award), offering recommendations from the excellent wine list which also features a good selection of wines by the glass – she also painted two of the works of art exhibited in the dining room. In the kitchen, Salvatore uses recipes and ingredients from the region to create mainly fish-based dishes which he reinterprets in a decidedly contemporary and imaginative style, using skilful techniques and extravagant and stunning presentation. The top-quality ingredients are sourced from a local kitchen garden, as well as from a small family farm in Federica’s native Calabria. On the “Amore per il mare” (Love for the Sea) tasting menu, we particularly enjoyed the fragrant, generous flavours of the different small bites served at the beginning and end of the meal, as well as the exquisite bluefin tuna, mushrooms and miso, and the risotto with yellow plum tomatoes, raw red prawns, fingerlime and aromatic herbs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1415;Sensi;Italy;Amalfi;via Pietro Comite 4, Amalfi, 84011, Italy;40.6339198;14.6030985;98;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;All five senses will be satisfied by a visit to the gourmet restaurant of the Hotel Residence. Housed in a splendid 18C palazzo just a few metres from the famous cathedral, the restaurant boasts an interior design which combines modern and functional features with the building’s classic look, using a colour scheme which is typical of the Amalfi Coast. Although the cuisine focuses mainly on Mediterranean fish and seafood, the menu also features a few meat specialities.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1416;Osteria del Viandante;Italy;Rubiera;piazza XXIV Maggio 15, Rubiera, 42048, Italy;44.65333;10.781861;78;false;true;Emilian, Modern Cuisine;Situated on the first floor of the 13C military fort in the centre of Rubiera, this elegant restaurant boasts five dining rooms, each one more delightful than the last and all frescoed, with the exception of the old limonaia which is decorated with wallpaper depicting its former function. This stylish and romantic setting provides the backdrop for young and enthusiastic chef Jacopo Malpeli who, having been born and raised between Parma and Reggio, creates cuisine that reflects the grandeur and opulence of local culinary traditions. Among his many interesting dishes, a particular favourite is the savarin di riso, which pays tribute to the legendary Mirella and Peppino Cantarelli and their former two-Michelin-starred restaurant in Samboseto. The extraordinary wine list includes several French wines alongside Italian labels and champagnes.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1417;La Rucola 2.0;Italy;Sirmione;vicolo Strentelle 3, Sirmione, 25019, Italy;45.4928374;10.6081306;62;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Situated next to the Castello Scaligero in one of the most attractive alleyways of Sirmione, la Rucola 2.0 is striking for its contemporary ambience dominated by a profusion of wood. The cuisine has the same modern feel as the decor, maintaining its creative focus over the years. Saltwater fish and seafood continue to take pride of place on the menu, which also features meat and freshwater fish options. The formula here focuses on tasting menus, although it is possible to choose different combinations of dishes from the à la carte.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1418;Impronte;Italy;Bergamo;via Cristoforo Baioni 38, Bergamo, 24123, Italy;45.7088279;9.6736129;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;To describe this restaurant as a corner of Sicily in Bergamo would be a cliché, as the menu offers so much more. However, there’s no hiding chef Cristian Fagone’s Sicilian origins, which are evident in his convincing reinterpretations of some of the island’s classic recipes, including its street food (such as the grilled “stigghiola” made from intestines) and main courses such as the superb lamb. The restaurant is housed in a converted bus depot, which has been transformed into a modern, vaguely post-industrial dining room. Excellent service, especially from young sommelier Francesco, completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1419;Qafiz;Italy;Santa Cristina d'Aspromonte;località Calabretto, Santa Cristina d'Aspromonte, 89056, Italy;38.2814827;15.9488692;27;false;false;Creative, Calabrian;Although getting to this restaurant is not easy, the pleasant drive that takes you through Calabria’s beautiful countryside dotted with countless olive trees makes it even more worthwhile. At the end of your journey, you arrive at an elegant late-18C villa with its adjoining old olive-oil mill that houses this restaurant crowned by a typical cross-vaulted ceiling. In 2023, a revolutionary refurbishment moved the kitchen into the centre of the dining room where guests sit around the counter-style Chef’s Table or at the single table set slightly to one side, enjoying just one tasting menu which is served to all guests at the same time. The focus here is on Calabrian ingredients (pigeon and oysters are sourced from outside the region), with produce such as the excellent extra-virgin olive oil, aromatic herbs and vegetables produced on the property, all transformed into creative and original dishes in front of guests by the skilful chefs. After your meal, you may like to move to the beautiful Aspro Cocktail Bar for a coffee, a small pastry or a cocktail. If you wish to prolong your stay, accommodation is now available in Casa Qafiz.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1420;Gambero Rosso;Italy;Marina di Gioiosa Ionica;via Montezemolo 65, Marina di Gioiosa Ionica, 89046, Italy;38.2990691;16.3276783;59;true;true;Seafood;Gambero Rosso was founded in the 1970s, when Anna Maria and Giuseppe Sculli decided to pay tribute to the sea that they had previously left as emigrants. Since then, the restaurant has become a focus for the whole family. As a result, a new chapter is now being written with the arrival of a new generation: Riccardo at the helm in the kitchen and Francesco front of house. They source their fish from small-scale fishermen all along the Ionian coast, as far as Reggio Calabria, focusing not only on the quality of the fish but also on the way that it is caught. The raw fish options are renowned here, as are the first and second courses which combine fish and seafood with vegetables. From September 2024, the restaurant will also have a few charming guestrooms available.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1421;Grow Restaurant;Italy;Albiate;via San Valerio 4, Albiate, 20847, Italy;45.659927;9.2560185;81;true;false;Farm to table, Creative;Technique, creativity and a focus on and respect for the past are just some of the criteria that guide chef Matteo Vergine. His modern dishes aim to reflect the ancestral flavours of Brianza and Lombardy in bygone days when hunting, freshwater fishing, growing vegetables and gathering wild herbs were all part of everyday life. In the evening, choose between three tasting menus – in an effort to minimise food waste, guests are required to make their choice at the time of booking. We particularly enjoyed the quail served with its own broth and a brioche, and the gnocchi with stracchino cheese, caramel and venison bottarga. Lighter and less expensive options are available at lunchtime, as well as a convivial table for eight which can be shared with “strangers”. This love for the region extends to the whole of Italy when it comes to the wine list, which is concise yet personal and exclusively features natural Italian wines, all of which are served skilfully and with a wealth of information by sommelier Riccardo.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1422;Līmū;Italy;Bagheria;via Ciro Scianna 177, Bagheria, 90011, Italy;38.0827311;13.5077378;51;false;false;Creative, Sicilian;In a town renowned for its splendid villas built by the Palermo aristocracy, this restaurant occupies a small 16C tower on the edge of the historic centre. The name is a tribute to lemon, a fruit that grows in abundance in Bagheria. The restaurant has two elegant, contemporary-style floors, where dinner starts on the small terrace-cum-lounge – the setting for sampling a whole host of delicious appetisers. This is guests’ first encounter with the cuisine of Nino Ferreri, a skilled and creative chef who uses regional ingredients as the foundation for his imaginative recipes. The courteous and professional service is overseen by the talented Giandomenico Gambino.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1423;Quadri;Italy;Venice;piazza San Marco 121 (primo piano), Venice, 30124, Italy;45.4342534;12.3379939;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated on the second floor of the historic café of the same name, this elegant restaurant,  with chef Sergio Preziosa at the helm of the kitchen, offers skilful reinterpretations of Venetian and Italian classics . With its ornate wallpaper, sumptuous chandeliers, view of St Mark’s Square and carefully restored 16C features, this is truly a restaurant for a special occasion. The opulence of the setting is deliberately lightened by the friendly service, which is occasionally playful and yet impeccable at all times.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1424;In Viaggio - Claudio Melis;Italy;Merano;via Belvedere 17, Merano, 39012, Italy;46.6729096;11.1765125;75;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;The name of this restaurant gives a good indication of the experience you can expect here: a culinary voyage through the chef’s varied selection of recipes and ingredients, some from the Alps, others from countries across the globe. Dishes are served on tasting menus of five, seven or nine courses in a quiet dining room with just a few tables, where the chef himself explains his dishes to guests.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1425;Volta del Fuenti by Michele De Blasio;Italy;Vietri sul Mare;SS 163 Amalfitana km 47,300, Vietri sul Mare, 84019, Italy;40.6622055;14.7138129;30;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Once you’ve passed through Vietri heading towards the Amalfi Coast, you come to the Giardini del Fuenti perched on a cliff sloping towards the sea. This hotel complex boasts a beach, terraced garden and the Riva Restaurant, which is open at lunchtime only and which also hosts various food and wine events. In a spacious dining room with large windows overlooking the beautiful bay, chef Michele De Blasio serves modern, elaborate and minimalist-style dishes based on reinterpretations of classic specialities from Campania, all showcased on two tasting menus and an à la carte. We particularly enjoyed the excellent and copious welcome snacks, with a special mention for the local speciality, Vietrese donkey meat, and the veal sweetbreads with citrus fruit, walnuts and rocket.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1426;Linfa;Italy;San Gimignano;piazza Sant'Agostino 19a, San Gimignano, 53037, Italy;43.4704034;11.0420787;62;true;true;Creative, Country cooking;This small, elegant and attractive restaurant with contemporary works of art on the walls is situated within San Gimignano’s old fortifications yet is easily accessible from the car parks outside the town. Here, chef Vincenzo Martella from Salento serves meat and fish dishes, often casually combining these different ingredients in the same dish (for example, barbecued lamb with peppers and porchetta-style eel). Also well worth sampling is the cuttlefish risotto alla pescatora served as an appetiser and the tortelli maremmani with concentrated apricot and rosehip-infused broth. The wine list is in the capable hands of Cesario Delle Donne, while the choice of using books as a table centrepiece is a nice detail – make sure you admire the book of Tuscan proverbs illustrated by Renato Bellabarba. All in all, a delightful all-round dining experience in one of Tuscany’s real gems.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1427;Cortile Spirito Santo;Italy;Syracuse;via Salomone 21, Ortigia, Syracuse, 96100, Italy;37.0564227;15.2944533;73;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Situated near the castle at the southernmost point of Ortigia, this restaurant is part of the Palazzo Salomone Luxury Suites and is one of the most elegant places to eat in Siracusa. Here, Giuseppe Torrisi prepares creative, technically expert and authentically Sicilian cuisine, which is typical of the island’s elaborate, Baroque soul. It is also a feast for the senses thanks to its exciting, intense and often unforgettable flavours. Our inspector recommends the daily fish specialities (usually snapper, sea bass or other species caught by local fishermen) served with a seasonal accompaniment such as asparagus or peas in spring, and a coulis of yellow Scicli tomatoes. On the wine list, we recommend trying one of the local labels from either Etna or the west coast of Sicily, such as De Bartoli’s Terzavia VS Brut.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1428;Il Refettorio;Italy;Conca dei Marini;via Roma 2, Conca dei Marini, 84010, Italy;40.6207949;14.5770614;22;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed within the Monastero Santa Rosa, one of the most original and iconic hotels on the Amalfi Coast (the monastery was founded in the 17C and some of its original features can still be seen), this restaurant occupies a spectacular terrace in a magical, tranquil setting with views that extend from the garden to the swimming pool and right out to sea. The cuisine comes courtesy of Alfonso Crescenzo, whose slogan “Nothing is more complex than simple cuisine” lies behind his tasteful reinterpretations of Campania’s traditional dishes, which are natural, full of generous flavours and beautifully presented. Our inspector recommends the turbot with bitter chicory, grouper soup, morel mushrooms and smoked provola cheese. There’s an equal balance of meat and fish options, with some vegetables sourced from the property’s own garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1429;Mater1apr1ma;Italy;Pontinia;via Sardegna 8, Pontinia, 04014, Italy;41.4102602;13.0433461;67;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Sara, who is extremely knowledgeable about wines, offers guests an interesting selection of wines and helpful recommendations, while Fabio is at the helm in the kitchen preparing original cuisine full of flavour and colour. His dishes use theoretically “poor” local ingredients such as goat and buffalo, which are served in generous dishes that pay careful attention to flavours and textures. Situated in the centre of Pontinia, this restaurant will surprise you for its original cuisine.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1430;Sine by Di Pinto;Italy;Milan;viale Umbria 126, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.4618683;9.2177246;34;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Sine serves contemporary cuisine influenced by the chef’s native Naples, as well as the local region of Lombardy. The dishes are occasionally playful in style, as demonstrated by the shrimp ravioli served in various ways, including with an intensely flavoured fish stew. The chef’s speciality is his fried pizzetta with palamita fish and courgettes, while his new dishes are showcased on the exciting and creative “Sine Confini” menu, on which he demonstrates his culinary skills to the full. Attentive, courteous service and a constantly evolving wine list which includes some lesser-known labels complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1431;Unforgettable;Italy;Turin;via Lorenzo Valerio 5/b, Turin, 10122, Italy;45.0767241;7.6780009;58;true;true;Innovative, Italian Contemporary;Although it seems incredible today, this restaurant in central Turin, situated just a stone’s throw from the Santuario della Consolata, stands on a street that once marked the boundary between the town and the surrounding countryside – to highlight this fact, after ringing the doorbell you make your way into what was once a farmhouse. Despite the traditional setting, chef Christian Mandura’s focus here is creative and occasionally extremely imaginative with dishes presented on a long tasting menu inspired by his varied experience (vegetables take pride of place in his dishes). Having been greeted by the chefs in the kitchen, guests are then served at a counter where they sit side by side (there are ten seats in total). There is also an original and personalised selection of drinks by the glass (not just wine) sourced by sommelier Jacopo from small-scale producers, including an excellent choice of vermouths.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1432;Don Geppi;Italy;Sant' Agnello;corso Marion Crawford 40, Sant' Agnello, 80065, Italy;40.631762;14.3931433;88;false;true;Creative;There are just five tables at this restaurant in the Majestic Palace Hotel, where the plant-themed decor on the walls echoes the romantic views through the window of one of the most beautiful gardens on the coast. Here, citrus and olive trees (including a thousand-year-old olive tree) are planted alongside a kitchen garden where many of the vegetables used in the dishes served here are grown. Chef Mario Affinita delights guests with his three tasting menus inspired by the region of Campania and his experience abroad. The end result is elaborate, technical and precise cuisine that is more than equal to the superb setting in which it is served.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1433;Oseleta;Italy;Cavaion Veronese;località Cordevigo, Cavaion Veronese, 37010, Italy;45.5252757;10.7912839;83;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;Situated just a few kilometres from Garda on gently sloping hills planted with vineyards, Villa Cordevigo, home to the Oseleta restaurant, is approached via a superb avenue of cypress trees. There are two small dining rooms here – we recommend booking a table in the elegant veranda with picture windows offering views of the verdant countryside and swimming pool, where the service is impeccable. Chef Marco Marras demonstrates his culinary skills on a menu that features fish, vegetarian dishes, specialities from the lake and meat options, all beautifully presented and prepared with surgical precision. Cheese-lovers will appreciate the small yet well-chosen selection of Italian cheeses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1434;Le Monzù;Italy;Capri;via Tragara 57, Capri, 80073, Italy;40.5454969;14.2502024;84;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;This restaurant is situated in one of Capri’s many iconic hotels, the Punta Tragara, which was designed by Le Corbusier and which stands in a superb panoramic location facing Marina Piccola and its surrounding cliffs. The same views can be enjoyed from the restaurant, along with an imaginative and skilfully prepared cuisine.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1435;Il Poggio Rosso;Italy;Castelnuovo Berardenga;località San Felice, Castelnuovo Berardenga, 53019, Italy;43.3880261;11.4599683;15;true;true;Creative;You cross a magical landscape of hills dotted with cypress and olive trees, woodland and vineyards to get to Borgo San Felice, the luxury hotel that is home to Poggio Rosso. Here, multi-Michelin-starred Enrico Bartolini has chosen his child prodigy Juan Quintero, originally from Colombia, as chef at the helm. Despite the chef’s origins, the cuisine is fundamentally creative and regionally influenced, with just a few South American touches here and there. Juan has fallen in love with Tuscany and he interprets the region’s cuisine with real elegance and contemporary flair. All of this in a luxurious yet unstuffy setting, with service which is impeccable and always accompanied by a smile.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1436;Il Saraceno;Italy;Cavernago;piazza Don Verdelli 2, Cavernago, 24050, Italy;45.6304009;9.7650842;66;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The chef’s Amalfi origins re-emerge in great style in this restaurant at the gates of Bergamo, with a chiefly seafood cuisine of great quality. From raw seafood to spaghetti with sea urchins and breadcrumbs, from seabream to the fish of the day, it is a feast for the palate, culminating in the desserts. The quality of the leavened products is noteworthy, from bread to focaccia with oregano and cherry tomatoes. The wine list is good too, starting with the selection of Champagnes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1437;Tivoli;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;località Lacedel 34, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.5338851;12.1222949;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian;This restaurant occupies an attractive Alpine house outside the town centre on the road to the Falzarego pass and at the foot of the Tofane mountains. Here, the chef shows himself to be completely at ease with both traditional cuisine and more creative fare. Using top-quality ingredients from this mountainous region, as well as fresh fish sourced daily from the markets at Venice and Chioggia, owner Graziano Prest creates delicious dishes full of generous flavours. Wine is another of his passions, hence the top-quality labels, historic vintages and renowned French bottles that can be found in the wine cellar here. The panoramic terrace boasts picture-postcard views of Cortina, as does the dining room – but only if you request one of the two tables by the window when you book!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1438;Vecchio Ristoro;Italy;Aosta;via Tourneuve 4, Aosta, 11100, Italy;45.7386406;7.3155868;38;false;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Contemporary;Despite its town-centre location and elegant ambience, this former 17C mill, which has retained its old wheel and millstone in the dining room, almost has the feel of the mountains. Here, the talented chef moves effortlessly between typical Aosta valley specialities, French dishes and international cuisine. The wine list offers well over 200 different labels, including carefully selected unusual wines alongside better-known options from leading producers. Excellent service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1439;Il Palagio;Italy;Florence;borgo Pinti 99, Florence, 50121, Italy;43.7774093;11.2665237;100;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Situated on the ground floor of the Palazzo della Gherardesca and surrounded by beautiful mature gardens, Il Palagio is a gourmet evening restaurant decorated in elegant, refined neo-Classic style. The cuisine focuses on Italian culinary traditions reinterpreted by chef Paolo Lavezzini, who describes himself as “Italian by heart and Brazilian by soul” (he spent many years working in Brazil). Although born in the region of Emilia, Lavezzini’s dishes fully respect Tuscan traditions embellished with the occasional Brazilian influence. Vegetarians are also catered for, with their own tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1440;La Parolina;Italy;Trevinano;via Giacomo Leopardi 1, Trevinano, 01021, Italy;42.8218494;11.8692538;36;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Although La Parolina is situated in Lazio, chefs Iside and Romano bring together the influences of three neighbouring regions in their simply prepared dishes, namely Lazio, Tuscany (the beautiful rolling hills of which can be admired from the restaurant’s summer terrace) and Umbria. Ingredients include mushrooms from Monte Amiata, truffles from the Sienese hills, asparagus from Canino and hazelnuts from Monti Cimini, as well as vegetables from Umbria and fish from the nearby Lake Bolsena and the Tyrrhenian Sea. Partners in life as well as in the kitchen, these two chefs skilfully balance local traditions with more modern influences. A few guestrooms are available at the restaurant’s La Letterina.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
1441;Storie d'Amore;Italy;Borgoricco;via Desman 418, Borgoricco, 35010, Italy;45.5381705;11.9290391;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This small, welcoming restaurant in the province of Padova is run by its two owners, one at the helm in the kitchen, the other overseeing the warm and beautifully decorated dining room. The cuisine is complex and elaborate rather than minimalist, with chef Davide Filippetto either creating different dishes from the same ingredient or preparing different ingredients in imaginative combinations. An abundant and generous menu, which includes an extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1442;Cannavacciuolo Vineyard;Italy;Casanova di Terricciola;via del Teatro 8, Casanova di Terricciola, 56030, Italy;43.5443686;10.6851821;26;true;false;Italian Contemporary;The famous talented chef Antonino Cannavacciuolo has opened one of his Laqua resorts in a lesser-known part of Tuscany that boasts charming verdant landscapes. The resort occupies part of the fully renovated small hamlet, where the comfortable contemporary-style decor in the restaurant is echoed by the precise modern cuisine, which is skilfully presented and perfectly balanced between flavour and elegance. Guests can admire the almost surgical precision of resident chef Marco Suriano as he finishes the dishes in the open-view kitchen. The service is equally impressive, with a team trained by professional staff boasting plenty of experience at home and abroad. The resort also has spacious, comfortable apartments available, with breakfast served in your room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1443;Elementi;Italy;Torgiano;via del Colle 38, località Brufa, Torgiano, 06089, Italy;43.0557212;12.4668702;50;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Originally from the Ciociaria region, Andrea Impero is the chef at the helm in this gourmet restaurant situated within the elegant Borgobrufa hotel. Here, he creates dishes influenced by the culinary traditions of Lazio and Umbria, his adopted region, as well as Campania, where he has spent time working in the past. The result is extraordinary cuisine, elaborate and full of flavour. All in all, a top-quality dining experience of the highest level.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1444;Equilibrio;Italy;Dolcedo;località Martin 13, Dolcedo, 18020, Italy;43.8999334;7.9589059;41;true;false;Ligurian, Contemporary;Consumed by a passion for cooking, young Jacopo Chieppa began his career working with sweet and savoury leavened products and gaining experience in renowned restaurants such as the Mirazur in Menton and Antica Corona Reale in Cervere. He has now opened his own restaurant in an old restored mill, where he serves exciting, delicious cuisine that is contemporary in style yet traditional in its ingredients, some of which are grown in the property’s own kitchen garden next door. We particularly enjoyed the playful (and tasty) opening “picnic”, as well as the mupa (a type of fish) served with asparagus and a clam and parmesan emulsion. Front of house, the chef’s wife Melania displays an equal passion for her work, while in summer there’s an attractive outdoor space for alfresco dining.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
1445;Idylio by Apreda;Italy;Rome;Piazza dei Caprettari, 56/60, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8983053;12.475718;23;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Part of the elegant Pantheon Iconic Hotel but with its own separate entrance directly from the street, Idylio by Apreda boasts a stylish dining room decorated in shades of blue and orange. Here, skilful chef Francesco Apreda from Campania serves Neapolitan cuisine with the occasional addition of spices and Asian touches. There’s no longer an à la carte here, as the focus is on three tasting menus: Firma Iconica, Speziale and Idylio's Butterfly (the latter allows guests to choose four courses from the other two menus). The young, efficient serving staff are full of smiles and more than happy to assist you as you choose between Apreda’s personalised menus.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1446;ARIA;Italy;Naples;via Loggia dei Pisani 2, Naples, 80133, Italy;40.8433646;14.2540383;19;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The ambience at this hushed and discreet restaurant couldn’t be more different from the hustle and bustle of the elegant district in which it is situated. The softly lit dining rooms are elegant and minimalist in style, with lamps creating pools of light illuminating the dishes conjured up by Paolo Barrale. Originally from Cefalù but now settled in Campania, the chef’s cuisine is inspired by the culinary traditions of both regions which he reinterprets with ease, occasionally creating more personalised dishes. Generous in every way, from the warm welcome to the cuisine right up to dessert, Paolo offers guests a top-quality dining experience ably assisted by his well-trained, professional staff.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1447;Gusto by Sadler;Italy;San Teodoro;via Tavolara, località Lu Fraili di Sotto, San Teodoro, 07052, Italy;40.8215359;9.6775825;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated within the exclusive Baglioni Resort to the north of San Teodoro, this restaurant carries the name of Claudio Sadler who, together with resident chef Andrea Besana, creates Mediterranean-style cuisine including a few new creative dishes added in 2023, such as the chargrilled eel kebab with a Cannonau wine and myrtleberry glaze and delicious vegetable couscous. Enjoy a good Luris vermentino as an aperitif and you’re off to a fine start! Meals are served overlooking a beautiful garden and swimming pool to add a real holiday feel to the dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1448;Da Gorini;Italy;San Piero in Bagno;via Verdi 5, San Piero in Bagno, 47021, Italy;43.8587914;11.9745195;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Cuisine from Romagna;This restaurant in San Piero in Bagno’s historic centre takes its name from its young chef Gianluca da Gorini, who prepares original and creative cuisine inspired by the traditions of this beautiful hilly region as well as his own more imaginative creations. Frequently used ingredients include mushrooms, game, freshwater fish and Mora Romagnolo suckling pig, often combined with other more exotic fare. There’s a particular emphasis on dishes cooked over the barbecue grill, which gives ingredients such as lamb, eel and pigeon a particularly pleasant texture and flavour.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1449;Apostelstube;Italy;Brixen;via rio Bianco 4, Brixen, 39042, Italy;46.7194264;11.6532447;29;true;true;Creative, International;Situated in delightful Bressanone, the historic Elephant hotel occupies the oldest part of a late-15C building and is one of the icons of the town (it’s been run by the same family since 1773 and is now in the hands of the eighth generation). The hotel’s first-floor Apostelstube restaurant serves innovative cuisine in an intimate dining room with just four tables and statuettes of the apostles adorning the walls, hence the name. In summer, aperitifs are served in the attractive garden. A delightful welcome is offered front of house by the friendly and efficient Michael and Eleonora, whose theatrical flair helps to make your evening even more memorable, while the imaginative tasting menu created by Mathias Bachmann showcases techniques and ingredients from across the globe, with a particular passion for Japan (hamachi, shiso and red shiso, wasabi). The young chef is a welcome addition to this old hotel, where his personality shines through his exciting, contemporary cuisine.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1451;La Zanzara;Italy;Codigoro;via per Volano 52, località Porticino, Codigoro, 44021, Italy;44.80822;12.252958;15;true;false;Seafood;The small room is characteristic and in the cold season the atmosphere is warmed, in every sense, by the crackling fireplace. The chef suggests all the most varied produce of the lagoon: lots of eel, prepared very simply and charcoal grilled, while the fish of the Adriatic Sea, including excellent squid and small brill, reign supreme. Reaching the farmhouse is an experience all in itself: in the valley of the Po delta, with its rich fauna and thick vegetation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1452;Local;Italy;Venice;salizzada dei Greci, sestiere Castello 3303, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.4356;12.345893;35;false;true;Contemporary;An elegant restaurant with a rustic yet chic atmosphere, where the cuisine manages to surprise without losing its connection to local traditions. Here, ingredients from the lagoon are prepared using modern ideas and techniques, resulting in dishes that are carefully balanced and yet full of contrasting flavours. The young female owner and excellent sommelier are friendly, full of energy and attentive to their guests’ every need.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1453;Octavin;Italy;Arezzo;scalinata Camillo Berneri 2, Arezzo, 52100, Italy;43.4645907;11.8796939;37;true;true;Creative;Housed in two small dining rooms connected by an arch on the ground floor of an old palazzo, this restaurant is decorated with materials that give it a minimalist feel – a combination of stone, wood and iron in the tables, glass in the mirrors and bottles on display, and paper in the books arranged in small niches, just like the lounge of a private home. There are just 20 seats in this warm, intimate and unfussy restaurant, as well as a large counter separated by an arch at the entrance which precedes the recently restructured kitchen. Observation of his own region has shown owner-chef Luca Fracassi that the varied geography of his province is an inexhaustible source of inspiration. As a result, he has embarked upon an impassioned search for ingredients that best showcase the region, combining these in dishes that not only respect the flavours of his produce but also revive traditional local techniques and include the occasional oriental influence. His cuisine is modern yet eschews modern trends, paying careful attention to integrity of flavour and zero waste. In this way, the kitchen becomes a place in which wild ingredients and forgotten flavours are rediscovered and brought back to life. This focus on lost traditions combines ingredients such as snails and game (often neglected in urban restaurants) with a skilful and updated use of contemporary culinary techniques.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1454;Caracol;Italy;Bacoli;via Faro 44, località Capo Miseno, Bacoli, 80070, Italy;40.7827339;14.0834126;66;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;The coast of Campania, and in particular the Bay of Naples, boasts a wealth of breathtaking views – and this is one of the most spectacular. Once you arrive at the Cala Moresca hotel, leave your car in the car park and hotel staff will accompany you to the restaurant. On a tranquil promontory surrounded by greenery, take a seat on a terrace overlooking the sea, with views of the islands of Procida and Ischia in front of you, the unmistakeable silhouette of Capri to your left and the mainland and mountains of Procida to your right – simply magnificent! At the helm in the kitchen, Angelo Carannante is the chef with the daunting task of competing with all this beauty, which he does with real aplomb. His long tasting menu features surprise courses in which he reinterprets regional traditions with freedom, creativity and the occasional exotic touch with outstanding results.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1455;Contrada Bricconi;Italy;Oltressenda Alta;via Bricconi 3, Oltressenda Alta, 24020, Italy;45.922027;9.9503694;67;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Leaving the Val Seriana, you follow a winding road uphill to get to this small stone hamlet dating back to the 15C, with its breathtaking views. Here, a group of young friends have brought this isolated corner of the mountains back to life, reviving old traditions and using a system of crop cultivation and livestock farming that focuses on quality and animal welfare. Young chef Michele Lazzarini has the same sustainable approach in the kitchen, offering an extraordinary gastronomic interpretation of his native mountainous region on an extensive and exciting tasting menu.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
1456;Leon d'Oro;Italy;Pralboino;via Gambara 6, Pralboino, 25020, Italy;45.2676884;10.2144844;55;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;Situated in the historic centre of a small village between Brescia and Cremona in the Po Valley, this restaurant occupies a period palazzo with an interior full of history. From the exposed beams on the ceiling to the open fireplace, every detail here contributes to the traditional ambience in the dining room, which is enhanced by an outdoor space for alfresco dining in summer. The cuisine pays particular tribute to the region, with snails, delicious Brescia-style kid and game all featuring, although there’s also room for a few fish dishes and more creative options on the menu. The wine list clearly demonstrates how much care owner Franco Martini has taken to enhance his cellar over the years, including only those vintages that he knows will delight his guests.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1457;Al Gatto Verde;Italy;Modena;Stradello Bonaghino 56, Modena, 41126, Italy;44.6102868;10.980026;72;true;true;Contemporary, Emilian;Al Gatto Verde is situated within the walls of the Casa Maria Luigia, the welcoming country house run by Massimo Bottura and his wife Laura Gilmore which is popular with a cosmopolitan clientele. Here, the focus is on wood-fired cuisine – several dishes on the menu are finished over the fire, including tortellini au gratin with 36-month aged Parmesan and Montreal lamb, the latter a recipe from the chef’s native Canada which has been reinterpreted, flavoured with spices, cooked on a spit and served with pear purée. Both the dining room and the verdant outdoor space have a welcoming feel, while the service is friendly and attentive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1458;Terramira;Italy;Capolona;piazza della Vittoria 13, Capolona, 52010, Italy;43.5626194;11.8598776;32;false;false;Contemporary, Tuscan;Having gained valuable experience elsewhere, the Scapecchi brothers are now back in Arezzo, where their restaurant offers views of the River Arno from its beautiful and softly lit dining room. Here, two tasting menus (from which guests are free to exchange dishes if they wish) showcase the region’s seasonal ingredients in modern dishes which are precise and yet full of distinctive and authentic flavours. Particular mention must be made of the pigeon served with sauces and seasonal vegetables, a dish in which chef Filippo demonstrates all that he learned from master-chef Gaetano Trovato at Arnolfo di Colle in Val d'Elsa. An excellent wine list completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
1459;Osmosi;Italy;Montepulciano;via Umbria 65, Montepulciano, 53045, Italy;43.1335561;11.8352976;61;false;true;Contemporary, Creative;Osmosi is part of the Fattoria Svetoni, a hotel with beautiful guestrooms housed in a historic villa overlooking vineyards in open countryside, and which also boasts a winery dating back to 1865. The restaurant is situated inside the old building, as well as on a modern veranda with views over the surrounding countryside through its floor-to-ceiling windows. Although Mirko Marcelli’s cuisine features some local specialities, it also includes more creative fare, hence the appearance of the famous local Chianina beef alongside an innovative gentian root rice dish. Other meat options include delicious breaded sweetbreads with peas, teriyaki and goat’s cheese, and duck with chard, confit leek and Cajun spices (a typical North-American spice mix). Guests have real freedom of choice with three tasting menus from which courses can also be chosen à la carte style. Enthusiastic owner Simone, ably assisted front of house by the friendly Elena, is on hand to help with recommendations from the detailed wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1460;Paolo Griffa al Caffè Nazionale;Italy;Aosta;piazza Emile Chanoux 9, Aosta, 11100, Italy;45.7376217;7.3208336;39;true;false;Creative, Italian Contemporary;This historic, centrally located restaurant (and adjacent bar) overlooking the main square in Aosta has been brought back to life by enthusiastic young chef Paolo Griffa, who offers two tasting menus or à la carte. His cuisine is colourful, balanced and contemporary in style, with particular attention paid to harmonious flavours and beautiful presentation. Excellent service and an extensive selection of wines complete the picture.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1461;Fradis Minoris;Italy;Pula;Laguna di Nora, Pula, 09050, Italy;38.9867335;9.0067135;53;false;false;Sardinian, Modern Cuisine;Originally from Sardinia, chef Francesco Stara has returned home to his native island where he focuses on completely “circular” cuisine in this restaurant situated in a protected marine area. The fish is either local or from the Nora lagoon, which also provides the chef with a selection of wild herbs, while the vegetables are sourced from small-scale producers in nearby Campidano. On its two tasting menus (one fish and seafood, the other vegetarian), this excellent restaurant focuses on the best possible seasonal ingredients, as well as protecting the environment and showcasing the island’s traditions in its new, contemporary-style cuisine. Friendly, attentive service and a wine list featuring several regional labels complete the picture.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1462;Olmo;Italy;Cornaredo;Piazza della Chiesa 7, loc. San Pietro all'Olmo, Cornaredo, 20007, Italy;45.48761;9.0124;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Olmo takes its name from the large elm tree that stands in the centre of Cornaredo’s small square, a symbol of the town’s pedestrianised area. This new restaurant opened by chef Davide Oldani has just three tables, which can be pushed together to accommodate a maximum of 14 guests, plus an open-view kitchen. The tasting menu here showcases the chef’s creative, modern dishes which focus on seasonal ingredients, balance and an attractive play between texture and temperature. Riccardo Merli is the young, talented resident chef who, having gained experience in renowned French restaurants as well as at Olmo, has now returned to take over the reins here. Although there is just one 6-course menu available, guests can also choose a reasonably priced 3-course option at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1463;Sintesi;Italy;Ariccia;viale dei Castani 17, Ariccia, 00072, Italy;41.725881;12.6797918;64;true;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;A modern, welcoming restaurant whose motto “Tradition & Innovation” perfectly sums up its cuisine. On the à la carte and tasting menus alike you’ll find classic dishes including risotto with peas, lemon and raw scampi alongside more creative offerings such as grilled pannicolo (hanger steak) with Nemi strawberries and herbs, all presented in a modern and precise manner, and with the occasional nod to Asian techniques and northern European culinary methods (fermentation, marinades, dry aging of fish etc). The wine list changes with the seasons and the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1464;Marco Bottega Ristorante;Italy;Genazzano;via Trovano 3, Genazzano, 00030, Italy;41.81092;12.966885;74;false;true;Creative;Surrounded by hills planted with olive trees and agricultural crops, and situated on a beautiful road leading from the border of the Ciociaria region to the Arcinazzo plateau, this 19C farmhouse is home to Marco Bottega, one of the most interesting young chefs working in the Roman countryside. As well as offering comfortable guestrooms, Aminta Resort also produces its own fruit, vegetables and meat from its 50ha estate, all grown and reared without the use of pesticides. From farm to fork, the ingredients produced here are used to create cuisine with a focus on the traditions of Lazio yet also open to other influences, resulting in authentic dishes full of flavour. The interesting wine list offers a wide selection of champagnes – the chef has also created a room in a separate building where guests can enjoy an aperitif or a wine tasting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1465;Locanda de Banchieri;Italy;Fosdinovo;via Porredo 32, Fosdinovo, 54035, Italy;44.114434;10.0015367;22;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;After spending time working in the Aosta Valley, chef Giacomo Devoto from Sarzana has returned to his native region, where he has converted an old 17C country farmhouse nestled amid tranquil verdant landscapes into an intimate inn with guestrooms and its own farm. Sitting on the panoramic veranda with its views of the sea and the coast, guests are served creative cuisine full of the delicious flavours of the Lunigiana. Devoto’s imaginative recipes are inspired by seasonal ingredients, with many of the vegetables (and the extra-virgin olive oil) grown on the farm itself, while the meat and fish are sourced either from inland or the nearby sea.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1466;Dattilo;Italy;Strongoli;Contrada Dattilo, Strongoli, 88816, Italy;39.2678209;17.0817921;55;true;true;Country cooking, Creative;In a world of haute cuisine still dominated by male chefs, Caterina Ceraudo stands out for her authoritative presence and large personality. Her restaurant is housed in a charming agriturismo which offers simple guestrooms decorated in attractive, rustic style, a beautiful swimming pool shaded by thousand-year-old olive trees, and traditional produce such as wine, olive oil, cedro and orange marmalades, and fruit juices. All of this provides a fitting backdrop for Caterina’s modern, creative and yet unfussy cuisine which is made using local ingredients and showcased on two tasting menus and a fixed-price à la carte. The tour of the property with owner Roberto (the chef’s father), a forerunner of organic agriculture in the region who, together with his family, has dedicated his life to this farm, is both instructive and enjoyable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1467;Hyle;Italy;San Giovanni in Fiore;contrada Torre Garga SS 107, San Giovanni in Fiore, 87055, Italy;39.2851384;16.6441951;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Calabrian;Located on the wooded Sila plateau famous since Greek times, this restaurant aims to take guests on a culinary voyage through the region, from the hills overlooking the sea to the high mountain peaks. Although spanning just a short distance, this covers a fertile area which boasts a rich diversity of ingredients. Enhanced by the experience of chef Antonio Biafora, the restaurant’s focus is on top-quality local produce (vegetables, aromatic herbs, walnuts etc) sourced from local farmers and growers, creating a chain which is both economic and socially responsible. In addition to its à la carte options, guests also have the choice of two tasting menus, the regional character of which is emphasised by their Calabrian names (Pùzaly and Chjùbica). The first, a seven-course menu, takes its name from the Greek word “pisseres” which means resinous, while the second refers to the ancient road that linked Paola to Cirò Marina and consists of eleven courses, all full of flavour. Excellent value for money!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
1468;Une;Italy;Capodacqua;via Fiorenzuola 37, Capodacqua, 06034, Italy;43.0177785;12.7839323;81;false;false;Creative, Umbrian;Situated in the heart of this town nestled amid the Umbrian countryside, Une serves two tasting menus (with varying numbers of courses) which follow the seasons: Acquedotto and Relazioni both feature modern and creative dishes prepared using a whole host of local ingredients. The desserts are absolutely superb – we particularly recommend the namelaka (a soft, delicious cream) with elderberry, the Mundo Novo coffee emulsion, and the date and caper ice cream.;Counter dining;[]
1469;Wistèria;Italy;Venice;fondamenta del Forner, sestiere San Polo 2908, Venice, 30125, Italy;45.43566;12.32682;46;true;true;Contemporary, Venetian;Situated along the Rio de la Frescada, one of Venice’s many quiet side canals, this restaurant’s small entrance overlooks an outdoor dining space enhanced by the wisteria which provides the outdoor tables with shade, and which gives the restaurant its name. Chef Valerio Dallamano has many years of experience with the Alajmo family, delighting guests with dishes made from seasonal ingredients that reflect the diversity of the region. Full of character in terms of its presentation, the cuisine showcases the best of Venice’s gastronomic traditions in contemporary dishes featured on six- or eight-course tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1470;Coria;Italy;Catania;Via Prefettura 21, Catania, 95121, Italy;37.5053157;15.0860216;90;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Sicilian;Having left its previous premises in Caltagirone, this old acquaintance of the Michelin guide has now opened in Catania, right in the city centre between period palazzi and avenues planted with oleander. In a simple yet elegant setting enhanced by works of art by Nunzio Fisichella (a painter devoted to depicting Etna and its many moods), the delicate cuisine continues to focus on Italy with occasional Sicilian influences in its ingredients, sauces, style of cooking and flavouring – nothing here is forced. Special mention should be made of the grilled quail, which is perfectly cooked in Sicilian style, as well as the “Minnuzza di Sant’Agata” – stuffed cuttlefish with potato foam and candied lemon for a hint of freshness. When it comes to wine choices, the talented sommelier can tell you all about the region of origin, whether the wine is from Sicily, Italy or elsewhere in Europe. To finish your meal, make sure you try a glass of Marsala stravecchio from Intorcia.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1471;Colline Ciociare;Italy;Acuto;via Prenestina 27, Acuto, 03010, Italy;41.7921649;13.1806079;56;true;false;Cuisine from Lazio, Creative;Guests who make it to this restaurant situated some 60km from Rome on a road with plenty of winding bends show real commitment, probably because they’ve heard of the culinary delicacies that Salvatore Tassa brings to the table here. There’s a restricted choice but unlimited imagination in dishes which range from traditional Italian classics and recipes from Lazio to bolder, more innovative, fare typical of the culinary world of this chef-cum-poet who eschews all definitions and fashions. At the modern Nù bistro, enjoy some of the chef’s more traditional and long-established recipes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1472;Wood;Italy;Breuil Cervinia;via Guido Rey 26, Breuil Cervinia, 11021, Italy;45.9334388;7.6294846;67;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;As its name suggests, this restaurant is decorated with a profusion of wood, partly because of its mountain location but also because the excellent female chef is originally from Lapland in northern Sweden. Her cuisine is a surprising and successful combination of Scandinavian traditions, Italian flavours and more exotic Asian influences. The result is excellent, original cuisine served at an altitude of 2 000m in the centre of Breuil-Cervinia, accompanied by a wine list featuring top-quality labels (including some rare vintages) with a focus on Piedmont.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1473;Trattoria da Amerigo;Italy;Savigno;via Marconi 16, Savigno, 40060, Italy;44.3903557;11.0739644;68;true;true;Emilian, Regional Cuisine;Situated in the hills immediately outside Bologna, Amerigo pays tribute to the typical Italian trattoria, taking guests on a nostalgic journey back to a time that will be familiar to all Italians and not just the inhabitants of Emilia. Just a few metres from the town’s main square, the restaurant’s entrance is via its own shop selling wine, sauces and other delicacies. From here, you enter the dining room and from there two further rooms on the first floor – one which was home to the first television in the village, now decorated with period ornaments, and a second adorned with frescoes. The cuisine is typical of Emilia and the Apennines, featuring an excellent selection of cured hams and fresh regional pastas, as well as game and truffles from the surrounding hills in season. Tradition, top-quality ingredients and a feast for the eyes as well as the palate.;Terrace;[]
1474;El Molin;Italy;Cavalese;via Muratori 2, Cavalese, 38033, Italy;46.292019;11.4594756;54;true;true;Alpine, Creative;The sound of the creaking old wooden floor welcomes you to this old 17C mill, where owner-chef Gilmozzi acts as your culinary Alpine guide with his single tasting menu (guests also have the option of a slightly shorter menu) which showcases his love and passion for the mountains. Smoked produce and an incredible use of native herbs, bark, lichens and resins feature alongside unique cheeses, intensely flavoured wild game and freshwater fish, while the chef’s creativity and careful research guides his choice of cooking methods. Cuisine from a true artist!;Interesting wine list;[]
1476;Trattoria al Cacciatore - La Subida;Italy;Cormons;via Subida 52, Cormons, 34071, Italy;45.9644549;13.4962756;49;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Situated amid beautiful rolling hills dotted with vineyards, this restaurant is perfect for anyone keen to sample authentic, traditional Friuli cuisine. One the most interesting restaurants in the region, the Trattoria al Cacciatore focuses on carefully chosen recipes and ingredients from this region, which has a rich and varied cuisine thanks to its location on the border with Slovenia and its historic links with Imperial Austria. The family owners will happily guide you through the options, which include wild herbs, frogs’ legs, mushrooms, radicchio, river fish, polenta and wild game, to name just a few of the delicacies on the menu. Among the main courses, the veal shank cooked in the bread oven, beautifully presented and carved in the dining room, deserves a special mention: for our inspectors, this dish is typical of the restaurant’s authentic, generous cuisine. As an alternative, Osteria della Subida serves traditional Friuli dishes and is open daily, including at lunchtime. The restaurant’s own wine and vinegar is available for purchase (also online).;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1477;Aqua Crua;Italy;Barbarano Vicentino;piazza Calcalusso 11/a, Barbarano Vicentino, 36048, Italy;45.42242;11.55369;42;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Welcome to the wonderful world of chef Giuliano Baldessari, a creative chef who enjoys introducing guests to his gastronomic world. There are two dining options here: the tasting menus showcase the chef’s creativity and precise techniques to the full in courses referred to as “provocazioni”, which focus on the use of just a few ingredients per dish. The second option is the à la carte, which features dishes that demonstrate the generous, classic flavours of the 1980s – for example, the main ingredient in these dishes is often served with an array of small bowls containing accompanying ingredients. The service is also more classic in feel, involving the addition of table linen and period-style glasses, plates and even chairs. Both options, of course, are created by the same chef with the same intention, which is to guide guests through an amusing culinary playground in which boredom and banality have been completely banished. It’s no coincidence that the background music is accompanied by a pleasant play of colourful effects.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1478;Damini Macelleria & Affini;Italy;Arzignano;via Cadorna 31, Arzignano, 36071, Italy;45.5174094;11.334968;31;true;false;Meats and Grills, Modern Cuisine;Gourmet food, a wine boutique and luxury butcher’s shop all in one, this restaurant serves remarkable produce and delicious cuisine at the tables behind its gleaming windows, while its wide selection of wines is announced at your table by the owner himself. Without doubt, this is a highly original gourmet experience in which respect for ingredients and culinary expertise results in strong, enticing flavours. It’s no surprise that particular attention is paid to the choice of meat, much of which comes from the restaurant’s own farm in Trezzo sull’Adda: meat is aged on site, with the duration depending on the type of meat (up to 100 days for the famous Gallega and Wagyu). Here, the cuisine appeals directly to the heart and the senses!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1479;All'Enoteca;Italy;Canale;via Roma 57, Canale, 12043, Italy;44.7969211;7.9931019;89;false;false;Piedmontese, Contemporary;A standard-bearer for regional cuisine, Davide Palluda continues to delight guests year after year. Based on faithfully interpreted Piedmontese recipes, such as the excellent plin al sugo d'arrosto or dishes that have been skilfully updated with no unnecessary frills, his cuisine aims to please guests at every turn. The restaurant is situated in a modern room on the first floor of a 19C building with a charming wisteria-adorned terrace. The ground-floor Osteria offers simpler, less expensive fare.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1481;Sapio;Italy;Catania;piazza Antonino Gandolfo 11, Catania, 95131, Italy;37.505208;15.0949852;64;true;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Sapio is a smart restaurant run by a young couple: Roberta Cozzetto provides a courteous, elegant welcome front of house, while Alessandro Ingiulla is in the kitchen preparing modern dishes that are a feast for the eyes as well as the palate, using fresh ingredients from this magnificent island.;Air conditioning;[]
1482;Il Sereno Al Lago;Italy;Torno;via Torrazza 10, Torno, 22020, Italy;45.8589005;9.1175648;86;false;false;Creative;Coming off the street that dissects the village, you head down almost as far as the lakeshore to this restaurant situated in the luxury Il Sereno hotel, an elegant and brand-new property designed by the inventive architect di Patricia Urquiola. In summer, meals are served on the arched terrace, where the view takes in the blue waters of the lake and the small villages on the opposite shore. The superb creative skills of the brilliant Neapolitan chef are expressed with consummate ease and balance in many different types of cuisine, including regional specialities, vegan options, Asian-influenced dishes, the occasional nod to Lombardy and fish from the lake. Options include tasting menus and an à la carte.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1483;Casa Mazzucchelli;Italy;Sasso Marconi;via Porrettana 291, Sasso Marconi, 40037, Italy;44.4125719;11.2578948;54;true;true;Creative;At certain times of day, the tempting aroma of freshly baked bread greets you as soon as you step into this restaurant, leaving you in no doubt as to the nature of the restaurant’s newest venture. Other dishes are also baked in the oven here, such as wild boar served with a red wine babà and sage mayonnaise. There are two tasting menus available (Attimi di cucina and Momento contemporaneo), both of which showcase traditionally influenced cuisine full of distinct flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1484;Ristorante del Lago;Italy;Bagno di Romagna;via Acquapartita 147, Bagno di Romagna, 47021, Italy;43.86577;12.027197;93;false;false;Cuisine from Romagna, Modern Cuisine;Once off the main road, follow a series of twists and turns uphill to reach the village of Acquapartita, at an altitude of almost 800m, where you’ll find one of the best restaurants in the region. Here, the Bravaccini brothers are at the helm, with chef Simone creating dishes that are proudly focused on local ingredients such as mushrooms, trout and game. His signature dish of wild boar is delicious and full of flavour – the meat is sliced tartare-style so that it cooks quickly and is then served covered with soft mashed potatoes sprinkled with juniper. Front of house, his friendly and skilful brother Andrea oversees an encyclopaedic wine list – two volumes featuring almost 1 600 labels, with a focus on Italy and France (almost 40% of the wines are French). The choice of wines is as impressive as the quantity and the service. All in all, an excellent choice!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1485;Principe Cerami;Italy;Taormina;piazza San Domenico 5, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.8502374;15.2833763;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The menu at this restaurant aims to return to the basic principles that lie behind chef Massimo Mantarro’s cuisine, namely the use of local and seasonal niche ingredients. Sicily boasts a bounty of produce full of different flavours and colours, taking guests on a journey from the coast to Mt Etna – as an example, vegetables (which dominate the menu) are grown around the volcano and are full of rich and intense flavours. In addition to the à la carte, guests can choose their own dishes from the “Principe Cerami” tasting menu, which includes fish and seafood from the Ionian alongside a few meat options. Although the wine list focuses on Sicily, it also includes some superb wines from elsewhere in Italy and around the world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1486;Nove;Italy;Alassio;via Privata Montagù 9/1, Alassio, 17021, Italy;44.0118042;8.1720871;83;true;false;Ligurian, Creative;It’s difficult to imagine a more exclusive setting for a restaurant than the Villa della Pergola, a splendid historic residence surrounded by a delightful botanic garden (which can be visited for a fee and by prior appointment), with a spectacular balcony offering views of the sea in the distance – it’s well worth the drive with its narrow hairpin bends to get here. Here, new chef Antonio Romano, who has worked with Heinz Beck, creates modern dishes based on local ingredients and vegetables sourced mainly from the property’s own biodynamic kitchen garden, L’Orto Rampante. Among the many delicious dishes, we particularly enjoyed the glazed veal sweetbreads with paprika, artichokes, black chickpea hummus, and lime from the garden. Added to this are the superb, exclusive guestrooms and tranquil surroundings, despite the proximity to Alassio which extends beyond the villa gardens.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1488;sui generis.;Italy;Saronno;via Roma 35, Saronno, 21047, Italy;45.6249766;9.0412055;89;false;false;Creative;A modern dining-room with an open-view kitchen where young Alfio Nicolosi can be observed at work, ably assisted by friendly and attentive staff front of house. When you book, you’ll be asked if you have any food allergies or intolerances, or any ingredients that you don’t like, as there is just one surprise tasting menu served here. The truly extraordinary dishes are inspired by the chef’s remarkable knowledge of culinary traditions from Italy and further afield (strong Asian and South American influences are obvious), resulting in highly personalised dishes. Nicolosi is one of the most interesting young chefs in Italy at the moment and his exciting cuisine is full of intense flavours, including grilled dishes with a hint of street food and other influences apparent throughout.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1489;Il Fuoco Sacro;Italy;San Pantaleo;strada di Buddeo, San Pantaleo, 07026, Italy;41.0529512;9.4460803;24;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in the magical, rural and secluded setting of the Petra Segreta resort, surrounded by Mediterranean maquis scrubland, the gourmet Il Fuoco Sacro restaurant overlooks a delightful garden and boasts stunning views of the coast. The founder of this hidden paradise is chef-cum-entrepreneur Luigi Bergeretto, who serves modern, Mediterranean cuisine with a focus on locally sourced ingredients, including the excellent aromatic herbs grown on the hotel farm (which also provides the resort with its vegetables, cheeses and some meat). Last but not least, the menu is overseen by Enrico Bartolini – a 100% guarantee of a fine gourmet experience!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1490;Contrada;Italy;Castelnuovo Berardenga;località Monastero d'Ombrone 19, Castelnuovo Berardenga, 53019, Italy;43.3510435;11.56022;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Tuscan;In the charming setting of an old hamlet, chef Davide Canella, who has plenty of experience behind him, serves delicious, elegant cuisine presented on a tasting menu and an à la carte on which meat takes centre stage (although a few fish options also feature). Dishes include exquisite prawns and panzanella, and duck breast served with hosomaki. Manuela, the friendly, professional sommelier, oversees the front of house, offering excellent recommendations on the best wine pairings. In other words, a delightful all-round dining experience thanks to the competence and enthusiasm of all involved.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
1491;Il Cantuccio;Italy;Albavilla;via Dante 32, Albavilla, 22031, Italy;45.8042803;9.1891665;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This welcoming, beautifully kept restaurant in the heart of green Brianza has a romantic and elegantly rustic feel. Here, enjoy opulent and generous cuisine created by chef Mauro Elli who moves easily between classic Italian favourites, occasionally adding his own individual touch to the dishes. His imaginative reinterpretations demonstrate a fascination with the sea (despite the restaurant’s geographical location), while the menu also offers “daily game specials” throughout the year. The focus here is on serving dishes full of flavour, rather than following passing trends.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1492;La Palta;Italy;Borgonovo Val Tidone;Località Bilegno, Borgonovo Val Tidone, 29011, Italy;44.9922314;9.4694233;67;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;Situated on the plain at the foot of the hills visible in the distance, this restaurant resembles a typical country house with an elegant dining room extending into a kind of covered veranda, the windows of which open on to the garden and the greenery of the Bassa Piacentina countryside. The ambience here is pleasant and relaxed, perfect for an elegant dining experience, yet not too formal. Although the menu features local ingredients and recipes, such as the excellent focaccia (bread is a house speciality) served with ciccioli(pork scratchings), the cuisine is creative without being overly fussy, and aims to please rather than amaze the palate. Our inspector recommends the roast donkey meat with “saracca” (herring) and “gorgnalini” – the latter is wild chicory, which adds a bitter taste and dash of bright green to an exquisite dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1493;Il Falconiere;Italy;San Martino;Località San Martino a Bocena 370, San Martino, 52044, Italy;43.2821868;11.9763509;80;false;true;Tuscan, Contemporary;To get to this exclusive restaurant, you drive through an idyllic landscape of small lanes lined with dry-stone walls and fields belonging to the Baracchi farm estate, of which Il Falconiere and the magnificent hotel of the same name are a part. Many of the ingredients served here, such as wine and olive oil, are produced on the estate and the restaurant’s strong connection with its local landscapes is evident. Specialities such as Chianina beef, local garlic and pici pasta feature in dishes spiced with aromatic herbs and full of the strong flavours of Tuscany.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1494;Il Desco;Italy;Verona;via Dietro San Sebastiano 7, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4416145;10.9999722;64;false;true;Italian Contemporary;For more than 40 years, this refined, elegant restaurant housed in a Renaissance-style palazzo in the heart of Verona and embellished with beautiful works of art has been the city’s “drawing room”, making it the perfect choice for a special occasion. The menu showcases renowned classic recipes created by talented chef Elia Rizzo, who has now been replaced by son Matteo in the kitchen. Most of the dishes are created by Matteo and have a light, fresh flavour (the scallops in a Mediterranean tandoori masala are superb), although there are also many of his father’s signature dishes on the menu, such as the memorable butter and mascarpone mousse served with bread at the beginning of the meal. The interesting “Capitolo 4” tasting menu explores traditional, regional flavours and includes some of the restaurant’s iconic dishes spanning the period from when it opened in 1982 to the current day.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1495;Il Bavaglino;Italy;Terrasini;via dei Mille 2/b, Terrasini, 90049, Italy;38.1556478;13.0812287;91;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Although this restaurant now occupies new premises in an old building once used for salting fish, its style of cuisine (featured on three tasting menus, “Storie e passioni”, “Mura di Casa”, and the vegetarian “Erba Terra Foglie”, from which dishes can also be chosen à la carte style) remains unchanged. Inspired by regional traditions, chef Giuseppe Costa creates personalised and imaginative dishes that are influenced by local flavours and his past culinary experience, proving himself to be equally at ease with fish and meat options. Our inspector particularly recommends the local purple prawns, served raw with caviar and olives and a lemon and ginger coulis.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1496;I Pupi;Italy;Bagheria;via del Cavaliere 59, Bagheria, 90011, Italy;38.0803301;13.5116679;72;false;true;Sicilian, Contemporary;Situated amid the streets of the old town, this restaurant boasts an intimate dining room and a pleasant outdoor space with a corner where guests can watch the appetisers being prepared. Chef Tony Lo Coco showcases Sicilian flavours and ingredients (meat and fish alike) which he transforms into personalised and imaginative dishes. His recipes often reinterpret great Sicilian classics, as is the case with his swordfish involtini where the traditional whipped filling is replaced by a cream on which the fish is placed and surrounded by ginger foam, or the famous cassata which he transforms into a transparent bubble in which all the different ingredients are then arranged. Elegant and professional service adds to the enjoyment of the experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1497;Al Gambero;Italy;Calvisano;via Roma 11, Calvisano, 25012, Italy;45.3492146;10.3430573;79;true;false;Lombardian, Classic Cuisine;A long-established restaurant in the Lower Brescia region, where the elegant, meticulous service is skilfully overseen by the owner, Al Gambero is the perfect choice for anyone in search of cuisine that is full of flavour and prepared using skilful, modern techniques, and in which taste is everything. The restaurant opened in 1880 in the oldest house in the village and is now run by descendants of the same family. After so many years in business, the menu has accumulated a number of unmissable signature dishes, from its famous risottos to roast kid.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1498;Dissapore di Andrea Catalano;Italy;Carovigno;via Pietro Micca 15, Carovigno, 72012, Italy;40.7073742;17.6581893;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Apulian;Don’t be put off by the maze of narrow streets leading to this restaurant in the historic town – once you reach your destination, you’ll enjoy delicious classic recipes from Puglia prepared using top-quality ingredients and full of unmistakeable flavours, all served in a charming dining room with lime and stone walls crowned by a domed ceiling. Among the highly recommended dishes, don’t miss the “purely instinctive” scampi with sweet pepper and saffron. Wines from Puglia, elsewhere in Italy and further afield accompany chef Andrea’s eclectic cuisine, while front of house, bubbly and friendly Franca oversees the excellent service. In summer, don’t miss the outdoor terrace overlooking the village rooftops with views of the sea in the distance!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1499;Locanda del Pilone;Italy;Alba;frazione Madonna di Como 34, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.66367;8.04705;84;false;false;Creative;Situated just a few kilometres from the town, this restaurant stands on a hill with 360° views of some of the most breathtaking vineyard scenery in the area, where vines stand in neat rows extending into the distance and take on extraordinary colours in autumn. Here, in a classic and elegant setting, the cuisine features seasonally inspired dishes (on a tasting menu which can be mixed and matched à la carte style) created by a skilful and enthusiastic chef who has solid experience despite his relative youth. In summer, bistro options are also available on the splendid outdoor terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1500;Pashà;Italy;Conversano;via Morgantini 2, Conversano, 70014, Italy;40.9691184;17.1151639;66;false;false;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant housed in the immense and historic Palazzo del Seminario Vescovile (Bishop’s Seminary) boasts a plain yet elegant interior decor, outstanding service and reinterpreted regional cuisine, all of which contribute to a very pleasant dining experience. The cuisine focuses on the region, with the occasional influence from Sicily, the chef’s homeland. Highlights on the menu include caviar and caprese (Altamura buffalo mozzarella with beluga caviar and a cherry tomato salad), and lamb with shallots in which the full flavours and tender textures of the meat shine through. As there’s only one tasting menu, remember to mention any food intolerances or preferences when you book. And when it comes to choosing your wine, make sure you ask talented sommelier Juan Pablo for recommendations – he will delight in taking you on a world tour which includes some really interesting labels!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1501;Saporium;Italy;Chiusdino;località Palazzetto 110, Chiusdino, 53012, Italy;43.1414359;11.1278724;83;true;true;Tuscan, Italian Contemporary;Saporium is the new fine-dining restaurant at the superb Relais Borgo Santo Pietro, an old property where the internal decor demonstrates a rare elegance, especially in the evening when hundreds of candles provide soft lighting and a romantic ambience in the dining room. In fine weather, meals are served under an elegant 13C portico overlooking the garden, with the property’s 100ha grounds and the Valle Serena as a backdrop. Much of the produce used in the cuisine (designed by executive chef Ariel Hagan and transformed by resident chef Luca Ottogalli into modern, delicate dishes) comes from the hotel’s own olive groves, vineyards, orchards and vegetable gardens. The focus here is on seasonal ingredients from this extraordinary region – the saddle of hare with cavolo nero and pear is a perfect example! A whole host of wine-pairing options are possible thanks to a wine list featuring over 1 300 labels. We recommend trying one of the Borgo’s own wines, such as the harmonious and elegant Pinot Nero.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1502;La Stüa de Michil;Italy;Corvara in Badia;strada Col Alt 105, Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.5471597;11.8762348;81;false;false;Creative, International;To get to this restaurant you head up towards the church in the prettiest part of Corvara, where you’ll find the La Perla hotel, one of the best in the valley, on your left. Once inside the hotel, you’ll be accompanied to La Stüa (stube in Ladin), where the profusion of wood lends an intimate and romantic feel to the decor. Although the setting is typical of the region, Simone Cantafio’s cuisine will take you on an extraordinary culinary journey. Originally from Calabria, this chef worked for many years in Japan, just one of his many formative experiences. As a result, his dishes feature different influences, often with a focus on vegetables. The name of the restaurant is a reference to owner and manager Michele Costa, an indefatigable and extraordinary figure in the world of Ladin tourism.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1503;Due Colombe;Italy;Borgonato;via Foresti 13, Borgonato, 25040, Italy;45.62138;10.018;41;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;At this restaurant, the chef’s highly creative approach does not ignore his culinary roots, resulting in a successful reinterpretation of local peasant traditions and top-quality cuisine. Our inspectors highly recommended making your way to this thousand-year-old hamlet, where you dine in a deconsecrated church under a brick-vaulted ceiling. The fine cuisine celebrated here includes historic dishes that have become classic favourites, which can be chosen from the three tasting menus. A good example is the beef cooked with olive oil and served with polenta: “Nonna” Elvira made this dish in the post-war period and her grandson Stefano follows the same recipe today. The menu also includes a few fish dishes, while wine-enthusiasts shouldn’t hesitate to ask sommelier Federica for her recommendations – they won’t regret it!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1504;Il Tino;Italy;Fiumicino;via Monte Cadria 127, Fiumicino, 00054, Italy;41.747204;12.257445;31;true;false;Creative;Enjoying an attractive location in the Nautilus Marina, overlooking the Tiber and the boats moored along it, this restaurant decorated in a modern, minimalist style represents a childhood dream for its chef, who learned his craft from observing his grandparents, both of whom were excellent cooks. Following years spent gaining experience abroad and in Italy, including an informative period with Gualtiero Marchesi at L’Albereta, Usai now creates contemporary cuisine with a strong regional character, prepared from top-quality seasonal ingredients and enhanced with cutting-edge techniques. His cuisine is also open to more exotic influences, including from Asia, the aesthetic quality of which reflects the chef’s own love for elegant presentation. The restaurant’s kitchen garden, visible from the steps leading into the dining room, provides the many herbs that are used skilfully by the chef to add colour and even more flavour to his delicious fish and seafood dishes. Excellent wine list, plus the highly recommended option of starting your meal with an intriguing cocktail!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1505;Nin;Italy;Brenzone sul Garda;via Zanardelli 5, Brenzone sul Garda, 37010, Italy;45.7154863;10.7716421;80;false;true;Creative;Chef Terry Giacomello has taken inspiration from his travels around the world to create his NIN menu, while his CLASSICI option focuses on Italian favourites. His cuisine features a combination of modern techniques and classic influences, with an added dose of creativity and innovation. Although the first-floor dining room overlooks Lake Garda, only a fortunate few will have a table with a view, so booking in advance is recommended!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
1506;Kuppelrain;Italy;Castelbello;via Stazione 16, località Maragno, Castelbello, 39020, Italy;46.6264329;10.8975683;25;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;The many positive adjectives that can be used to describe the Trafoier family can be summed up by simply saying that they are unique! Their individual talents come together in the natural and engaging welcome they offer guests, demonstrating a warmth and professionalism that is typical of the Kuppelrain experience. Chef Kevin, who is as skilful as his father Jorg (now front of house), demonstrates precise, excellent techniques in his search for comforting and appealing flavours that bring out the full flavour of his ingredients with no frills or unnecessary fuss. Local produce takes pride of place, such as fruit and vegetables from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, and meat and fish from the region. The desserts, as well as the imaginative pralines, are made by daughter Natalie. Wine-enthusiasts will also be in their element here, thanks to the excellent wine list (including a fine selection by the glass, as well as magnums and 3-litre double magnums) which is overseen by talented Sonya (the winner of the 2022 Michelin Sommelier Award!), who creates unique wine pairings. Bistro service only at lunchtime.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1507;L'Asinello;Italy;Castelnuovo Berardenga;via Nuova 6, località Villa a Sesta, Castelnuovo Berardenga, 53019, Italy;43.385393;11.4808519;24;false;true;Tuscan, Creative;Situated at the entrance to a romantic village in the Chianti region, this former stable has been converted into a quiet, elegant restaurant by a young couple, with a beautiful garden for summer dining. Here, guests can sit after dinner and enjoy the sound of neighbours calling to each other in the background, a pleasant reminder of life in Italy in days gone by. At the helm in the kitchen, the husband champions traditional cuisine which is minimalist in its choice of flavours and made from just a few well-balanced ingredients. The impeccably kept garden, which is as beautiful and well presented as his dishes, is also the chef’s work (he certainly has green fingers!). A real Italian culinary gem!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1508;Un Piano nel Cielo;Italy;Praiano;via Capriglione 147, Praiano, 84010, Italy;40.6136373;14.5218291;55;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;A delightful panoramic lift leads from the Casa Angelina hotel to this restaurant where, in fine weather, meals are served on the candlelit terrace with its breathtaking views of the coast. Chef Leopoldo Elefante creates Mediterranean cuisine with a focus on fish and seafood, including his signature dentex (a kind of sea bream) – a classic dish with a light modern touch featuring baked Tyrrhenian fish escalope served on diced potatoes and cherry tomatoes with a clam sauce. The menu also includes a few excellent meat specialities. The chef here takes great care with presentation, arranging each ingredient on the plate with attentive precision while also working quickly in order to ensure that dishes are served at the right temperature. He is ably assisted by a friendly and attentive team front of house, where an impressive wine list of over 1 000 labels will delight wine-lovers, especially those keen on French and Italian sparkling wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1509;Materia;Italy;Cernobbio;via Trieste 1/B, Cernobbio, 22012, Italy;45.8383599;9.0685195;53;false;true;Creative;While this restaurant’s recent move has brought a new setting and a change of address, it continues to serve cuisine which is a fusion of Italian, Asian and other influences, with a menu featuring plenty of vegetables, spices and aromatic herbs used by the chef to create dishes full of concentrated flavours. If you enjoy innovative and original combinations, this is the restaurant for you as many of the dishes on the menu (including the desserts) offer something different, including recipes with more challenging and acidic and bitter flavours. Our inspector particularly enjoyed the pickled whitefish served with roe and bitter local salad leaves. In addition to the à la carte, there’s also a lighter menu available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1510;Essenza;Italy;Terracina;via Cavour 38, Terracina, 04019, Italy;41.287274;13.2566963;28;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Simone Nardini’s Michelin star continues to shine in Terracina in this elegant restaurant which is run by young, well-trained staff. The chef serves exciting, creative cuisine, with a careful preparation and presentation of dishes that will appeal to the eyes and tastebuds alike. There’s also an impressive wine list featuring around 800 different labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1511;Acqua;Italy;Olgiate Olona;via Filippo Corridoni 1, Olgiate Olona, 21057, Italy;45.6346559;8.8878287;46;true;false;Seafood, Contemporary;The Possoni continue with their family tradition in this contemporary-style restaurant situated opposite the long-established Ma.Ri.Na. Here, their emphasis is on the quality of ingredients, which is always of paramount importance to chef Menoncin and owner Davide Possoni, who at the beginning of the evening will accompany you to your table and advise you on your choices from the menu. Fish and seafood take centre stage here, showcased in simple, traditional dishes and more complex and creative recipes alike. The menu always features a few raw options, such as the trio of shellfish (scampi, red prawns and what must surely be the largest shrimps you’ve even seen), each of which is served with its own creative and delicate dressing. The wine list includes a number of labels from the Champagne region, plus numerous wines available by the glass. An attractive outdoor space completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1512;I Tenerumi;Italy;Isola Vulcano;via Vulcanello, Isola Vulcano, 98055, Italy;38.4305495;14.9560516;62;true;true;Vegetarian, Creative;We recommend arriving at this restaurant before the sun goes down so that you can enjoy the spectacular sunset in this breathtaking setting with its view of the Aeolian islands. Meanwhile, skilful chef Davide Guidara’s cuisine is just as exciting as the setting, thanks to his single tasting menu prepared in the open-view kitchen. The menu features around twenty small plates prepared by this young and exceptionally talented chef – it’s no surprise that he has already won Michelin’s Best Young Chef award. He enjoys playing with culinary techniques and makes the most of his home-grown produce by using preservation methods such as fermentation, maceration, pickling and salting and then using these preserves along with seasonal ingredients in his dishes. His decidedly personalised cuisine can be paired with original vegetable cocktails (most of which are non-alcoholic), although wine-enthusiasts will be pleased to hear that a wine list is also available. The excellent desserts are prepared by top pastry chef Gianluca Colucci, while the young front-of-house team help to make the evening special with their friendly, attentive service and their ability to put guests immediately at ease. I Tenerumi is a truly unmissable gastronomic experience!;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1513;Orma Roma;Italy;Rome;via Boncompagni 31, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9084005;12.4933748;23;false;true;Fusion, Creative;An oak door with three steps leads into the dining room which extends towards the kitchen in this restaurant designed by a renowned Milanese studio, whose predilection for wood is typified by the beautiful oval-shaped dining tables. Famous chef Roy Caceres (originally from Colombia but now decidedly Roman) is at the helm here, serving a successful combination of ingredients from Lazio and his native country with occasional influences from elsewhere in Italy. The menu features dishes such as Abruzzo mutton with ‘nduja sausage served with Castelfranco radicchio. The chef is happy to introduce himself and share his ideas with guests, adding to the sense of welcome and conviviality here. The wine cellar is as well thought out as the dining room, offering the perfect venue for a quick aperitif, while in summer the outdoor terrace comes into its own for cocktails and bistro dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1514;Iris Ristorante;Italy;Verona;Via Leoni 10, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4397874;11.0005401;33;false;false;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;Not far from the 12C Basilica di San Fermo, this restaurant is housed in the Palazzo Soave (formerly Palazzo Malaspina Bottagisio). This historic address boasts highly elegant rooms with the “fishbone”-style stonework typical of Roman buildings and vaulted ceilings that provide a pleasant contrast to the restaurant’s contemporary furnishings. Your meal begins a journey back through the city’s history, as appetisers are served in their own special setting in the palazzo’s 14C wine cellar which has Roman origins, after which you return to the dining room to enjoy the rest of your meal. The talented chef here creates regionally influenced, balanced and imaginative dishes with a “green” focus. The menu also features fish, especially from the Adriatic, while the wine list boasts over 800 labels with a particular emphasis on France and the Veneto.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1515;Nazionale;Italy;Vernante;via Cavour 60, Vernante, 12019, Italy;44.2437857;7.5334988;63;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the hotel of the same name in a typical mountain-style property, this elegant restaurant offers two welcoming dining rooms with open fireplaces and a profusion of wood, where friendly service adds to the warm atmosphere. Although meat dishes tend to dominate on the menu, a greater focus on vegetables has developed over the years, largely thanks to the three kitchen gardens (two of which are owned by the restaurant) which supply these vegetables. Choose between two tasting menus (one traditional, the other more contemporary in style) and a good à la carte selection. We particularly enjoyed the “bottoni” with tumin del Mel (a fresh cheese that is a symbol of the Varaita valley), lamb gravy and cavolo nero. There’s also now a new bistro in the old bar which serves lighter yet equally interesting dishes.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1516;Zia;Italy;Rome;via Goffredo Mameli 45, Rome, 00153, Italy;41.8870305;12.4679141;75;true;false;Innovative;A young chef of undoubted talent is at the helm of this restaurant situated behind the busier, more tourist-frequented streets of Trastevere. The chef in question is Antonio Ziantoni (hence the name of the restaurant), who creates imaginative cuisine that is nonetheless based on solid classic foundations – this gives his dishes structure, solidity and real appeal, as well as full and rounded flavours. One of the most interesting Michelin-starred restaurants in Rome.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1517;Borgo Sant'Anna;Italy;Monforte d'Alba;Località Sant'Anna 84, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.5777429;7.994414;50;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;Pasquale Laera, originally from Puglia, has by now been working for years in Piedmont and has learned the rules and codes of the regional cuisine, broadening his horizons with suggestions–including tasting of game in season and on the menu–of colorful and generous dishes using ingredients targeting taste much more than appearance. Thorough searching, also outside his vegetable garden, for vegetables that, being from Puglia, he is able to fully enhance, as in the case of his autumn cartoccio: a mix of vegetable flavors to which Castelmagno cheese adds Piedmontese sapidity. The latest new thing is "Anima", a room designated for research into new ideas for the kitchen, but also exclusive hospitality with a table for 8 with a special menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1518;Erth;;Abu Dhabi;North Parking, Al Hosn, Abu Dhabi;24.4829789;54.3569321;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Emirati Cuisine;Meaning ‘legacy’, Erth is made up of many striking elements, from its dramatic location as part of the Qasr Al Hosn cultural site, to its bold architecture. Inside, the polished concrete and bespoke furniture, along with modern majlis, make for a unique environment. Equally memorable is the food which, while modern, is anchored firmly in Emirati traditions when it comes to flavours, cookware and ingredients sourced from farms across the Emirates. A modern take on lamb machboos delivers tender lamb slow-cooked in a sweet and savoury teriyaki sauce, served with fluffy, fragrant rice. We suggest finishing with the Liwa dates batheeta.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
1521;Hakkasan;;Abu Dhabi;Emirates Palace Mandarin Oriental Hotel, West Corniche Road, Al Ras Al Akhdar, Abu Dhabi;24.461469;54.3173868;62;false;false;Chinese;Regulars of this exclusive international brand will instantly recognise the sultry and chic oriental décor within this branch, located within the Emirates Palace hotel. All the time-honoured classics are on the menu, like Peking duck, Chilean sea bass with honey and, on Saturday lunchtimes, their celebrated dim sum, all prepared with enormous skill. Opt for the premium dim sum and any of Hakkasan’s 'signatures', which are highlighted on the menu. A well-chosen wine list delivers an interesting global selection with plenty of top producers. Service is knowledgeable and engaging and the atmosphere vibrant and buzzing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1522;Omakase Table;USA;Atlanta;788 W. Marietta St. NW, Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.7799746;-84.4140292;48;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Here at this serious counter-focused setting, find Chef Leonard Yu and his small team presiding over a multicourse experience that leans traditional while offering a nice balance of variety and seasonality. A smattering of otsumami begin the evening on a strong note with shaved Waygu beef lightly poached in sukiyaki sauce with a quail egg. The chef's signature dish, uni gohan with otoro, is decadent, while corn potage delivers an impressive depth of flavor. Meanwhile, nigiri showcases character without any flash: Kawahagi is topped with flash-frozen liver paste that melts on the tongue, while sharkskin sole with engawa is given a fantastic sear. Not to be outshined, vanilla ice cream is taken to new heights with the addition of aged shoyu.;Car park;[]
1523;O by Brush;USA;Atlanta;3009 Peachtree Rd. NE, #140, Atlanta, 30305, USA;33.8374855;-84.3810816;53;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Brush Sushi is located in a swish shopping center with the likes of Rolex and Dior, but step inside this stylish space to discover O by Brush, a separate omakase counter helmed by Chef Jason Liang. The extensive procession will begin with several starters before moving into nigiri such as beautifully rich shima aji, warayaki sawara that is hay smoked over coals then sliced and filled with rice, and anago tempura temaki finished over binchotan coals. A tasting of dry-aged hirame and kanpachi is a delightful surprise, as is the tamago tasting, featuring the classic style alongside a tender, cake-like version. The wide-ranging sake selection, also available by the glass or carafe, is the perfect complement.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1524;Bacchanalia;USA;Atlanta;1460 Ellsworth Industrial Blvd., Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.795105;-84.427274;22;false;true;American;Dark wood, a black industrial ceiling set with a constellation of Edison bulbs, and brown leather banquettes give Bacchanalia a handsome sophistication, yet there's nothing too precious about this longstanding spot. The multicourse prix fixe involves a bit of flair, with some dishes arriving on carts or nestled inside glass cloches, and the cheese course is a wonderful surprise. Rather than an expected slice, the team presents a clever take with a crumbly oat date cake and a dot of black garlic sauce surrounded by rings of parmesan. Chilled lobster in a ponzu sauce with bright English peas and horseradish oil is also memorable but it may just be the delicate grapefruit soufflé garnished with spicy pistachio crumble and rose crème anglaise that takes the cake.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1527;Lazy Betty;USA;Atlanta;999 Peachtree St. NE, Atlanta, 30309, USA;33.7817;-84.384;44;true;false;Contemporary;Now located in Midtown, Chef Ron Hsu and Chef/co-owner Aaron Phillips oversee a contemporary tasting menu with clever combinations that highlight regional ingredients. The tuna roll is a stunner, made with feuille de brick and filled with lemon, crème fraîche, and wrapped in paper-thin sheets of bluefin tuna. Cod, poached in a ham hock broth, rests atop fava bean and zucchini succotash with a green tomato relish for an especially flavorful plate, while crown-roasted duck with a caramelized miso sauce is another strong savory course. Finished with a blackberry banyuls reduction at the table, it's a beautiful dish. Lemon panna cotta, surrounded by mint granita and covered with a coconut foam is a refreshing finale.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1528;Atlas;USA;Atlanta;88 W. Paces Ferry Rd. NW, Atlanta, 30305, USA;33.8404462;-84.3836692;69;true;true;American;When the night calls for a grand celebration, few places fit quite like Atlas. Snuggled inside the posh St. Regis Atlanta, this restaurant is impossibly elegant. Fine art graces the walls—it's home to The Lewis Collection and its works by Japanese-born painter and printmaker Léonard Tsuguharu Foujita—but it's not just the artwork that impresses. Order à la carte from this seasonal American menu with European influences or celebrate with the tasting menu for dishes like tender lobster plated with smoked paprika butter sauce and heirloom summer squash, and poached halibut composed with a trio of beet preparations. Wagyu beef from Australia is a decadent end to the savory courses. Impressive cocktails, a cheese cart and whimsical desserts complete the well-rounded experience.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
1529;Spring;USA;Marietta;36 Mill St., Marietta, 30060, USA;33.9535173;-84.5509835;40;true;false;Contemporary;Find your way to this small but well-appointed restaurant in Marietta where exposed brick and a vaulted ceiling done in dark wood create an endearing charm. Chef Brian So oversees a tightly edited, contemporary American menu with a strong focus on seasonality. Skillful but simple cooking is the dictum here, where ingredients speak for themselves, and plates are stunning without ever being showy. The house-made sourdough with garlic chive butter is delicious, but don't fill up, as the pan-seared wild king salmon topped with Hollandaise sauce and trout roe is equally appealing. A maple-glazed cruller with sliced almonds in an amaretto crème anglaise is a bold and distinctive dessert, and the wine list is especially impressive.;;[]
1530;Staplehouse;USA;Atlanta;541 Edgewood Ave. SE, Atlanta, 30312, USA;33.7542416;-84.3698666;22;true;true;Contemporary;Open two nights a week for dinner (Friday-Saturday) and located in the Old Fourth Ward, Staplehouse promises a convivial evening of conversation and talented cooking. An open kitchen, exposed brick, and a high ceiling lend a rustic/industrial vibe to this charmingly attended-to place.Here, a contemporary tasting menu flips the script with a hearty, far-from-fussy offering where you may discover a cabbage course that sings with character and flavor. A thick slice of grilled sirloin steak with a crispy morel mushroom is sided by a wedge of grilled gem lettuce with tiny florets of sprouting cauliflower. Finally, a citrus tart with honeycomb candy is spot on.;Air conditioning;[]
1531;Max Cekot Kitchen;Latvia;Riga;Jelgavas iela 42, Riga, 1004, Latvia;56.9299319;24.098951;39;true;true;Creative;Max Cekot’s restaurant is a surprisingly sophisticated place considering its location in a red-brick former warehouse on the edge of the city. Your evening starts downstairs with drinks and amuse bouches, before you head up the narrow spiral staircase for dinner, where Max has designed everything from scratch, from the furniture to the crockery. Numerous elements make up each of the original dishes on the surprise menu, with sweet, savoury and acidic flavours all balancing one another, and delicious sauces bringing each dish together perfectly. Max finishes some of these dishes tableside, where home-grown ingredients are often featured.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1533;Arakel;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue Henri Blanvalet 17, Geneva, 1207, Switzerland;46.2033774;6.1589012;92;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Tucked away in one of Geneva’s liveliest districts, the sleek open kitchen of this dainty restaurant captures your attention right from the start, drawing you into the heart of the action. A blend of modernity and tradition, the score adds an innovative spin to a lineup of classics, illustrated by risotto of mussels, celery, saffron mousse, passion fruit gel or a carpaccio of giant red shrimps, subtly marinated in yuzu, lemon zest and fresh herbs and paired with stuffed carrot rolls and a slightly sweet carrot sauce. The small pavement terrace offers a chance to get a real feel for this delightful quarter. The young, enthusiastic and appropriately irreverent front-of-house team adds to the venue’s lively vibe.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1534;OZ;Switzerland;Fürstenau;Obergass 2, Fürstenau, 7414, Switzerland;46.7210956;9.4461197;30;false;true;Vegetarian, Creative;The beautiful grounds of Schloss Schauenstein are home to OZ, another restaurant opened by Andreas Caminada. The name is derived from the Romansh word for "today" and refers to the contemporary cuisine served here. Entirely vegetarian, it is made with seasonal produce grown in the restaurant's own permaculture garden or sourced from long-standing partners. The ingredients are transformed into a creative nine-course set menu by head chef Simeon Nikolov. Meat-eaters won't miss meat here – the dishes are subtle, packed with flavour and balanced with delicate contrasts. A shining example: lightly sautéed local mushrooms, imbued with a wonderful roasted aroma, arranged on freshly baked puff pastry and garnished with deep-fried celeriac straw, served with aromatic mushroom foam. Diners sit at a U-shaped counter and watch the chefs in action – or strike up a conversation. Incidentally, a donation of two CHF, which goes to supporting young culinary talents, is included in the price of each set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1535;KLE;Switzerland;Zurich;Zweierstrasse 114, Zurich, 8003, Switzerland;47.3715034;8.5209664;37;true;true;Vegan, Innovative;Zineb ("Zizi") Hattab proposes something out of the ordinary in her charming pub. Not only is the modern-creative food entirely vegan, but it also draws on interesting Moroccan and Mexican influences. The chef – the daughter of Moroccan immigrants – was born in Spain and grew up in Costa Brava. Originally an engineer, she followed her passion for cooking, gaining work experience with Andreas Caminada in Switzerland and in Mexican restaurant Cosme in New York, to name but two. Choose four to six courses for the surprise menu served in the evening. Great importance is attached to regionality and sustainability, and that also applies to the wine.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1536;Fahr;Switzerland;Künten-Sulz;Grossacherweg 1, Künten-Sulz, 5444, Switzerland;47.377839;8.3210191;23;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;The trip out here into the countryside is definitely worth it! Clad in Swiss hardwood, the building housing this restaurant stands directly adjacent to a recreational area and close to the Reuss River. Chef Manuel Steigmeier serves up modern cuisine with sustainability at its heart and that is bold, sophisticated and stripped down to the essentials. His ingredients are of the highest quality, and he makes a point of sourcing from Switzerland or the region. A prime example is the wonderfully succulent and perfectly cooked char, with a delicately balanced and rich beurre blanc with lime, potato brunoise and caviar from Frutigen, accompanied by spicy sweet-and-sour pickled celery with a crisp texture. Part of this culinary experience is an extensive wine list featuring around 600 labels, along with a knowledgeable and communicative service team. The decor is sleek and stylish, with striking designer lamps created by the owner's son. The terrace is glorious. A small selection of dishes from the evening menu is available at lunchtime.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1538;GÜTSCH by Markus Neff;Switzerland;Andermatt;Gotthardstrasse 53, Andermatt, 6490, Switzerland;46.6559326;8.6275263;55;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;This restaurant high up on the Gütsch mountain (2 344m above sea level), after which it is named, can be reached on the Gütsch Express cable car – hop on at the lower terminus (departing from Andermatt railway station). Chef Markus Neff and his team, along with the restaurateur trio of Müller, Gruß and Neumüller, put their heart and soul into this venture. The best place to sit is on the spectacular terrace – you could even call it a viewing platform! And if the weather isn't playing ball, it's just as pleasant to sit inside. The decor is modern and simple, which is entirely in keeping with the no-nonsense culinary style and relaxed atmosphere. Markus Neff's classic cuisine encompasses dishes from French haute cuisine as well as more regionally influenced fare – the beef tartar is a must on the à la carte menu – and goes well with the wonderful wines. A tip for your journey back down to the valley: get off the cable car at the middle station and continue on foot – it's a great walk!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1540;Sushi Shin;Switzerland;Zurich;Zinnengasse 7, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3705379;8.5415242;64;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;Temporarily closed.In the centre of Zurich, right next to the historical Münsterhof square, this compact sushi restaurant is tucked away in a side street. Seated at the counter in a sophisticated yet informal interior, guests are treated to a seasonal omakase menu. The charming proprietress will guide you through the evening (in English), and you can also watch the sushi being prepared. In the evening, the set menu is served at two sittings. At lunchtime, there is also a short sushi and sashimi menu. Whether you prefer wine or sake with your meal, there are some real gems to be had – but with a price tag to match. Be sure to reserve, as the restaurant has only eight seats! Given the location just a stone's throw from the River Limmat, you should not miss the opportunity to take a stroll while you are here.;Counter dining;[]
1541;Njørden;Switzerland;Aubonne;Place du Marché 15, Aubonne, 1170, Switzerland;46.4952391;6.3913754;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Scandinavian;As well as the gorgeous little boutique hotel Hemma and Njørd Café, Philippe Deslarzes also owns this fine dining restaurant, Njørden. He cooks fish, seafood and vegetarian dishes that draw on Swiss and Swedish influences. His modern cuisine is packed with contrasts and features many regional as well as Scandinavian ingredients and culinary techniques. Enthusiastic service team, including a savvy sommelier.;Interesting wine list;[]
1542;Birdy's by Achtien - The Nest;Switzerland;Brunnen;Axenstrasse 9, Brunnen, 6440, Switzerland;46.9935811;8.6063937;90;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;A restaurant within a restaurant. In the middle of Birdy's by Achtien - Sharing Restaurant you will find The Nest. The cosy setting is friendly, with pleasing floral touches and enjoyable relaxing background music. Diners can also interact directly with the team working in the open kitchen, which makes for a delightfully communicative atmosphere. Chef Christian Vogel creates a modern surprise menu with five courses that change according to the season. Thanks to the Big Green Egg grill, the juicy, tender Ennetbürgen beef, for example, has a wonderful barbecued note. No less interesting is the very special cooking technique that gives the salmon from Lostallo a fantastic texture. There is space for 12 guests at this gourmet food bar, and the set menu is served to all of them at the same time.;Counter dining;[]
1543;Neue Taverne;Switzerland;Zurich;Glockengasse 8, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3721075;8.5403165;65;false;true;Vegetarian, Modern Cuisine;Nenad Mlinarevic has brought in Fabian Fuchs (previously of EquiTable) to head up the kitchen team here. The cuisine is vegetarian, some of it also vegan – the fantastic creative dishes designed for sharing are also available as a surprise menu. At lunchtime the choice is more limited, with a few dishes from the evening menu. The pleasingly informal atmosphere is reminiscent of a modern gastro pub, and the service is spot on.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1544;Osteria Enoteca Cuntitt;Switzerland;Castel San Pietro;Via alla Chiesa 8, Castel San Pietro, 6874, Switzerland;45.8600788;9.0088473;26;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated just above Mendrisio, a charming small village with a delightful historic centre and church, this elegant restaurant occupies a beautiful Lombardy-style farmhouse. Popular with locals and visitors alike, the restaurant serves regionally inspired Italian cuisine, including several dishes featuring caviar. The impressive and varied wine list includes bottle from the restaurant’s own winery, while two charming terraces provide the perfect setting for alfresco dining in summer.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1545;Torkel;Switzerland;Vaduz;Hintergass 9, Vaduz, 9490, Switzerland;47.1441186;9.5196627;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;With its winning combination of historical and modern features, this restaurant has a really appealing look. The dominant feature of the dining room is a lovingly preserved old wine press (or Torkel in the local dialect), which blends in well with the modern decor that surrounds it. The conservatory is fantastic: the walls open up, so you feel like you're sitting on a terrace, among the vines with views of the Rhine Valley. Owner Ivo Berger and his team propose a contemporary take on modern cuisine. Presented without fuss or frills, the dishes are replete with first-class produce and harmoniously balanced flavours. An attentive and charming front-of-house team provides excellent wine recommendations – be sure to sample the local wines!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1546;Bayview by Michel Roth;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai Wilson 47, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2141318;6.1516872;96;true;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;In addition to a jaw-dropping view over the lake, hence the restaurant’s name, we were enchanted by the high-flying repertory of Danny Khezzar served at the Hotel President Wilson’s fine dining establishment. Under the expert guidance of award-winning executive chef Michel Roth (Meilleur Ouvrier de France and Bocuse d’Or), Khezzar crafts a masterfully creative version of pedigree French classics. The dishes, whose plating is modern and sophisticated, are served in an airy, elegant setting, the centrepiece of which is an incredible suspended table made out of Saint-Louis Amadeus crystal. The experienced and attentive front-of-house team blends in seamlessly with this outstanding dining experience.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1547;Du Cerf;Switzerland;Sonceboz;Rue du Collège 4, Sonceboz, 2605, Switzerland;47.1963569;7.1782266;66;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;Set in the heart of the peaceful village of Sonceboz, this establishment is a culinary landmark in what is known as the Jura Arc and also throughout Switzerland. Chef Jean-Marc Soldati, at the helm for many years now, has played a major role in the restaurant's success. For this alumnus of Crissier, where he worked alongside Fredy Girardet and Philippe Rochat, tradition is a serious business. His classic cuisine is rigorous and harmonious, drawing mainly on local and French ingredients and even the chef's own kitchen garden. The wine list features a selection of regional, Swiss and French wines, as well as terrific picks by the glass. Book yourself into one of the modern, well-appointed guestrooms and stay on after dinner.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1548;Locanda Barbarossa;Switzerland;Ascona;via Muraccio 142, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1519079;8.7928471;40;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Food-lovers and fans of elegant gourmet dining will be in their element at this restaurant, which is one of the best in Ticino. Made from seasonal produce (much of which comes from the restaurant’s own land), Mattias Roock’s cuisine is a successful mix of local dishes and Mediterranean influences which nonetheless remains fundamentally rooted in classic recipes, both on the à la carte and on his two delicious tasting menus. Our inspectors also highlighted the pleasant, tranquil ambience of the setting (the beautiful outdoor terrace is particularly appealing in fine weather) and the wide choice of wines offered by sommelier Sergio Bassi. Excellent service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1549;Alpenblick - Stuba;Switzerland;Adelboden;Dorfstrasse 9, Adelboden, 3715, Switzerland;46.4936682;7.5608287;44;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Fusion;Alpenblick proposes two exciting dining options: there is the lively bistro, where you can tuck into down-to-earth cuisine such as steak tartar or Wiener schnitzel, or you can head to Stuba for its ambitious, high-quality set menu of four to seven courses, including vegetarian options. Here, chef-patron Björn Inniger serves up cosmopolitan modern fare, sourcing much of the produce from the region. His dishes feature subtle nuances, bold contrasts, and they are packed with flavour. The atmosphere is pleasantly laid back, and the setting is warm and welcoming with a touch of elegance. Friendly and attentive service comes courtesy of the charming waitstaff.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1550;Eden Kitchen & Bar;Switzerland;Zurich;Utoquai 45, Zurich, 8000, Switzerland;47.3628206;8.5472792;21;false;false;Italian, International;"Brasserie Deluxe" is an apt description of the restaurant in the tasteful hotel La Réserve Eden au Lac. The atmosphere is laid-back, the interior is chic, and the focal point is the green-tiled open kitchen… and then there is the glass-paned façade overlooking the lake! A highly professional team from Italy is behind the classic Italian, French and internationally influenced cuisine – they operated under the direction of Marco Ortolani, who was previously at the Tuscan Trattoria Enrico Bartolini, as well as at Alain Ducasse in London and Hong Kong. The paccheri pasta, for example, is full of flavour, perfectly cooked and tossed in a tomato-based, spicy crustacean sauce, served with tender lobster tail and claw meat, with fine tips of kale leaves. Service is provided by an experienced team. There is an exclusive wine list and a terrific selection of cocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
1551;Sonne;Switzerland;Wengi bei Büren;Scheunenberg 70, Wengi bei Büren, 3251, Switzerland;47.0886297;7.3756662;96;false;false;French, International;The idyllic setting alone makes the trip to this remote hamlet worthwhile. A pretty historical farmhouse bordering fields and meadows is home to this gourmet restaurant, whose stylish yet comfortable decor extends onto the terrace with its pergola and great view of the surrounding greenery. Then there are your warm and friendly hosts, Iris and Kurt Mösching. While the lady of the house adds a personal touch to proceedings front of house, heading up the professional yet appealingly relaxed service team, the chef-patron focuses on producing modern cuisine that draws on classic foundations. He wins diners over with quality ingredients, technical skill and attention to detail. The fabulous wine list boasts some 600 labels. Alternatively, you can order from the excellent bistro menu in the rustic Gaststube.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1553;Villa Sommerlust;Switzerland;Schaffhausen;Rheinhaldenstrasse 8, Schaffhausen, 8200, Switzerland;47.6945459;8.647056;47;true;true;Innovative, Creative;Led by two young Spanish chefs, Dan Rodriguez-Zaugg and Alejandro Perez Polo, the kitchen team creates highly innovative, exciting and technically complex dishes, such as Swiss Alpine pike-perch ceviche with white soya mayonnaise and jalapeños. The menu showcases a blend of Spanish avant-garde, South American and Asian culinary influences. There is a four- to eight-course set menu with a vegetarian alternative. Options are simpler and more limited at lunchtime, but the evening menu can also be made available upon prior request. Friendly and adept service. The restaurant is housed in a charming villa, just a street away from the Rhine. If you can't get a table on the fabulous garden terrace, the Orangerie is a delightful alternative – with its light and airy atmosphere, it makes you feel almost like you're dining al fresco. Stylish cigar lounge on the first floor.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1554;Restaurant GERBER WYSS;Switzerland;Yverdon-les-Bains;Rue du Four 1, Yverdon-les-Bains, 1400, Switzerland;46.7784323;6.6402494;52;false;true;Classic French, Regional Cuisine;Laurena and Grégory Wyss, along with Séverin Gerber, are the team behind this restaurant in the heart of the town, just a stone's throw from their boulangerie-chocolaterie – the two men were previously chocolate-maker and baker, respectively, at the renowned Restaurant de l'Hôtel de Ville in Crissier. The chef serves up creative dishes that showcase the Swiss terroir: for example, crayfish from Lake Neuchâtel, fennel kimchi and oyster leaves are among the various "instants" comprising the "Signature" set menu. You will be served by an attentive and charming team, and a sommelier who is a fountain of knowledge.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1555;Le Murenberg;Switzerland;Bubendorf;Krummackerstrasse 4, Bubendorf, 4416, Switzerland;47.4545219;7.7386967;45;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Denis and Melanie opened Le Murenberg in March 2012, fulfilling their dream of running their own restaurant. He is in charge of the kitchen, while his wife – a pastry chef by profession – is not only the charming head of service, but also takes care of the desserts. As a native of Alsace, the owner feels a close connection to French cuisine – and the "Breton Weeks" in October are well received. His classic dishes, which draw on modern influences, are as much about the excellent craftsmanship as they are about the high-quality produce. Incidentally, the chef hails from a winemaking family, so you can look forward to a splendid selection – the half bottles are definitely a good option.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1556;The Japanese by The Chedi at Gütsch;Switzerland;Andermatt;Gotthardstrasse 4, Andermatt, 6490, Switzerland;46.6557369;8.6255457;59;false;false;Japanese Contemporary, Fusion;Those who wish to enjoy terrific Japanese cuisine high up in a stunning Alpine setting should head to this restaurant, located 2 344m above sea level, and preferably bag a table on the wonderful terrace set against this grandiose mountain backdrop! Working in tandem, twin brothers Dominik Sato and Fabio Toffolon create classic Japanese cuisine with subtle European influences. Choose from an "Omakase Kaiseki Menu", "Shidashi Bento" and their excellent sushi and sashimi selection. A children's menu is also available. Smooth service is provided by a friendly and attentive team. The setting is minimalist yet inviting, and the open kitchen draws the eye. You can reach the restaurant with the Gütsch Express from the lower terminal at Andermatt railway station).;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1558;Des Trois Tours;Switzerland;Fribourg;Route de Bourguillon 3, Fribourg, 1722, Switzerland;46.8003971;7.1758441;40;true;false;French Contemporary, Innovative;In this 19C patrician house near the centre of Fribourg, diners can savour a harmonious set menu comprising five to seven courses. Stripped back to home in on the essentials, the dishes are also pleasing to the eye. The food is served in a stylish, refined and modern atmosphere, and the service is professional. The interesting wine list focuses on Switzerland and France.;Terrace;[]
1559;Krone;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Tinus 9, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4993105;9.8397439;98;false;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;This long-established restaurant is located in a quiet street a stone's throw from the town centre. With its dark blue fabrics, warm wood finishings and antler chandeliers, the interior is at once upscale and warm and welcoming. The exceedingly friendly service team led by Fabio Rovisi also deserves a mention – charming, efficient and highly organised, they cater to their diners' every need. In the semi-open kitchen, the chefs prepare modern dishes with a strong Italian influence, while also incorporating classic elements. Risotto with horseradish, snails, cashew and raspberry, or scampi with porcini, almonds, wild strawberries and parsley are just two examples of their delicate and elegant creations. There is a five- or seven-course set menu, as well as an à la carte selection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1560;Au 1465;Switzerland;Champex-Lac;Route du Lac 21, Champex-Lac, 1938, Switzerland;46.0304363;7.1153597;36;true;false;French Contemporary;With a wealth of experience at MICHELIN-starred restaurants under his belt, Mariano Buda now heads up the kitchen here. Although his style of cooking has been aptly described as a modernised take on classic cuisine, he incorporates authentic traditional cooking techniques as well. A prime example of this is the impeccably crafted classic pâté served alongside tender poulard fillet. Last but not least, abundant flavour is also provided by carefully selected ingredients, most of which are sourced from the region. The well-curated wine list is presented to you on a tablet – Swiss and French labels are well represented. Incidentally, the name of this chic, modern restaurant is a reference to the altitude of the exclusive little hotel Au Club Alpin in which it is housed – with its breathtaking view of the surrounding mountains is truly delightful.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1561;ZOE;Switzerland;Berne;Münstergasse 39, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.9474398;7.450242;83;false;true;Vegetarian, Modern Cuisine;United by the motto "Vegetables in various facets", restaurateur duo Fabian Raffeiner (kitchen) and Mark Hayoz (service) are following their passion, concocting modern and creative vegetarian dishes that are meticulously prepared and rich in flavour, such as king oyster mushroom, fermented garlic, parsley and buckwheat. There is an seven-course set menu with optional add-ons. Some dishes can also be ordered à la carte. Beverage accompaniments include natural wines, beers and non-alcoholic drinks. Tip for lunchtime: the "business lunch" deal with up to four courses. This two-storey restaurant with its charming minimalist interior is located in the heart of the old town, a stone's throw from Bern Minster. Laid-back, professional front-of-house team. Pleasant little terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1562;Verve by Sven;Switzerland;Bad Ragaz;Bernhard-Simon-Strasse 2, Bad Ragaz, 7310, Switzerland;47.0004645;9.5037451;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant subscribes to the interesting concept of health-and-lifestyle cuisine, which places the emphasis on sustainability and fair trade. Here, they make a point of using seasonal produce sourced from the local region and are keen to exchange ideas with local growers and producers. Their international produce also comes from sustainable farming. The dishes, which are inspired by nature, can be ordered à la carte or enjoyed as a set menu. Then there is the friendly, attentive and professional service, and the modern and refined decor with its soothing, warm tones and pleasing natural materials – the design also reflects the establishment's connection to nature. The glass-walled wine cellar is particularly elegant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1563;Stéphane Décotterd;Switzerland;Montreux;Route de Glion 111, Montreux, 1823, Switzerland;46.4326918;6.9216223;76;true;false;French Contemporary;In a premium location on the heights of Montreux, the restaurant of the Glion Institute of Higher Education commands a fantastic view of Lake Geneva and the mountains. The interior is elegant and modern and the service warm and professional. The legible, unpretentious cuisine of Stéphane Décotterd shines the spotlight on Swiss produce (fish from the lake, regional cheese). The chef regales us with wholesome dishes such as free-range poultry from Gruyère cooked in hay, but his star dish is Dry Aged duck reared in Walzenhausen, roasted whole in wine vinegar (order in advance). Business lunch menu available in addition to the à la carte offering.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1564;Zur Gedult;Switzerland;Burgdorf;Metzgergasse 12, Burgdorf, 3400, Switzerland;47.0572771;7.6266325;49;false;true;International;Fancy a good meal in a relaxed, informal atmosphere? Here in one of the oldest inns in Burgdorf (dating back to 1716), tuck into seasonal cuisine that draws on regional produce. The sophisticated, modern and creative dishes are proposed in the form of a set menu, also available in a vegetarian version.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1565;Brasserie Uno;Switzerland;Zermatt;Kirchstrasse 38, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0192354;7.7474356;66;false;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;A bustling little restaurant of the sort you might expect to find in Berlin or New York, this place is a real gem. The tables are set close together and the atmosphere is pleasingly laid back. You can watch the two chefs in the open kitchen as they prepare a multi-course surprise tasting menu. You need to allow plenty of time for this dining experience, but the 3.5hr are absolutely worth it: the dishes are made with regional ingredients, and great emphasis is placed on seasonality and provenance. Dishes such as pike-perch on a bed of creamed sauerkraut with Swiss caviar, spicy turnip – raw and lightly marinated – and herbs are measured, creative and brimming with bold flavours. A vegetarian or vegan set menu is also available if ordered in advance. Please be sure to mention any dietary restrictions when booking. NB: There is no à la carte or children's menu.;;[]
1566;Wein & Sein;Switzerland;Berne;Münstergasse 50, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.947541;7.4497057;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Hostess Daniela Jaun and chef Pascal Melliger (partners both professionally and privately) put their heart and soul into running this pleasant restaurant nestled in a cellar space with a pretty vaulted ceiling. The chef cooks modern, precise cuisine, showcasing select produce with an impeccable sense of elegance. Take, for instance, his terrific Swiss lamb, served as a beautifully roasted saddle cut, a fantastically spiced, excellent mini merguez and a superbly crafted ragout. The evening set menu is written on a blackboard on the wall and further clarified at the table. You can choose from four to six courses, and a vegetarian version is also available if you pre-order. Service is provided by a very polite, well-trained and experienced team. When it comes to wine, you can rely on the recommendations of the charming and extremely dedicated young owner. In summer, head for the terrace surrounded by the historical houses of the old town. Be sure to allow yourself plenty of time to fully appreciate this harmonious culinary experience!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1568;Wiesner Mysterion - Wiesner - Zauber;Switzerland;Romoos;Bramboden 6, Romoos, 6167, Switzerland;46.9791881;7.9858069;38;false;true;Creative;For the culinary wizardry he displayed at Rössli, the family restaurant in Escholzmatt, Stefan Wiesner earned a name for himself as the "Hexer", as well as a MICHELIN star. Now he has moved on to Weitsicht, a hotel 1 052m above sea level, which hosts special seminars, and first and foremost showcases the chef's very own philosophy of "alchemical natural cuisine". And what could be a more fitting location than the Entlebuch Biosphere Reserve? With mountains and valleys, meadows and forests all around, this environment is a source of the most diverse ingredients and flavours. Pure nature is the essence of Stefan Wiesner's cuisine. His set menu changes to reflect the seasons, and he introduces each of the nine courses with a little story. To do justice to the wonderful view, this unique culinary experience starts at noon. His son Jo's cutlery workshop is also located on the premises.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1569;Le Pérolles;Switzerland;Fribourg;Boulevard de Pérolles 1, Fribourg, 1700, Switzerland;46.8019356;7.1514413;60;false;false;Classic French, Contemporary;Chef Pierrot Ayer, who is the darling of the residents of Fribourg, he rolls out his manifold talents in this swish, designer venue. Done up in a snazzy futuristic vein, Le Pérolles, which is in the basement, provides the perfect foil for delicate, well-curated dishes, whose expressive generosity reflects the chef’s personality, particularly in his inspired new takes on Gallic classics: lamb, wild thyme, chard and pimiento. At lunchtime, there is a more accessible 3- or 4-course menu and, in the evenings, there is also a vegetarian version. Splendid cheese trolley. For a “simpler” experience, head for the ground-floor bistro-cum-grocery store, le Petit Pérolles, open from 9.30am, and dig into fresh regional produce in a more casual vibe.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1570;Ackermannshof;Switzerland;Basel;St.-Johanns-Vorstadt 21, Basel, 4056, Switzerland;47.5631925;7.5846153;95;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Housed in a lovingly restored and converted printing house that dates back centuries, this restaurant is run by a well-coordinated team including head chef Flavio Fermi and maître d' Roland Tischhauser. In a remarkably chic and tastefully designed setting, you can expect a modern take on Mediterranean cuisine that draws on international influences. Tuscan fish soup with chopped tender giant prawns, for instance, is given a harmonious Asian twist by incorporating shiitake mushrooms. The "Fauna" set menu comprises four, six or eight courses – the vegetarian alternative, "Flora", is available by prior arrangement. Opt for the judicious wine pairings or choose from the extensive wine list, which includes a fine selection of champagnes. The stylish bar area is the perfect spot for a nightcap. There is also a pretty courtyard terrace.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1571;Gilles Varone;Switzerland;Savièse;Rue du Stade 5b, Savièse, 1965, Switzerland;46.2501082;7.3506266;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in the heart of this quaint village overlooking Sion, this restaurant may appear unassuming from the outside. You would never suspect such culinary delights to be served at the simple wooden tables, showcasing a cuisine that is entirely dedicated to Switzerland and bursting with rich flavours! Following stints with Anton Mosimann, Gordon Ramsay and Claude Bosi in London, owner and head chef Gilles Varone has returned to his homeland to serve up a pleasantly pared-down cuisine, complete with a focus on sustainability. The restaurant itself, with its unpretentious and simple decor, is a perfect match. The front-of-house team win diners over with their charm and expertise. The wine list is exclusively Swiss – alternatively, you could opt for the house-made kombucha.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1572;Alpenblick;Switzerland;Wilderswil;Oberdorfstrasse 3, Wilderswil, 3812, Switzerland;46.6638943;7.8601193;92;false;false;Creative, Country cooking;This quintessential Swiss inn makes for a seriously appealing culinary experience. It is all down to Richard and Yvonne Stöckli, who have been putting their heart and soul into this long-standing establishment since 1980. Friendly and efficient, she heads up the service team in the charming little dining room (judicious wine recommendations from a great selection), while he showcases his skills in the kitchen, conjuring up dishes distinguished by their craftsmanship, quality ingredients and punchy flavours. His interesting modern and seasonal set menu comprises four to seven courses. Delightful garden terrace – ask for one of the seats beneath the old plane tree. Tip: Cheese lovers should try the Nessleren Alpine cheese! The rustic bistro and pretty guestrooms complete this charming picture.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1573;Panorama - Cayenne;Switzerland;Steffisburg;Hartlisbergstrasse 39, Steffisburg, 3612, Switzerland;46.7872121;7.6208457;90;true;true;Modern French;This establishment has been run by the Fuchs family for 35 years, and these days, it is Rolf and Manuela Fuchs who are in charge. The modern, elegant restaurant atop Hartlisberg boasts not only a chic atmosphere but also a truly magnificent view of Thun and the mountains – a spot on the terrace is a must! The chef-patron's cuisine is no less of a draw. It is modern, yet clearly classical in its foundations, making for dishes that are robust and expressive. As a matter of course, the ingredients are sourced locally as possible. There is a decent wine selection, and astute recommendations come courtesy of the friendly, professional waitstaff.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1574;Le Cigalon;Switzerland;Thônex;Route d'Ambilly 39, Thônex, 1226, Switzerland;46.1991216;6.2209024;66;true;true;Seafood, French;Judging by the fresh fish on the menu, you could be forgiven for thinking that this restaurant is on the doorstep of the Brittany coast. For almost 30 years, the Bessire couple has been shining the spotlight on fish and seafood delivered direct from Roscoff and Audierne fish markets, together with scallops fished by divers from the Norwegian Sea. This star-ranked, high-flying gourmet adventure has been going strong for 26 years! First-class ingredients, flawless craftsmanship, generous helpings and tasteful plating – served alfresco in fine weather. For an ultimate cosy experience, book the table d’hôtes for five and eat in the kitchen!;Car park,Terrace;[]
1575;Sternen - Badstube;Switzerland;Wangen bei Dübendorf;Sennhüttestrasse 1, Wangen bei Dübendorf, 8602, Switzerland;47.4110124;8.6454555;59;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Located in the sleepy town of Wangen, this pretty inn with an attractive 16C barrel vault is a wonderful meeting of the historical and the modern. A dedicated couple have been plying their trade here since 2005 – Matthias Brunner is in charge of the kitchen, while Bettina Brunner-Schill oversees the friendly front-of-house team. The cuisine has classical leanings and is made with only the finest ingredients. Choose between the seasonal set menu (omnivore or vegetarian) and their à la carte "classics" – the regional beef tenderloin served with harissa sabayon, potato roll and winter vegetables whets the appetite. Savvy wine recommendations. At lunchtime there is also a reasonably priced set menu. The cosy, rustic-style Gaststube, serving traditional cuisine, is a nice alternative to Badstube. Gasthof Sternen has comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1576;I Due Sud;Switzerland;Lugano;riva Antonio Caccia 7, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;45.9946751;8.9458534;91;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, International;Situated within the beautiful Splendide Royal hotel (now approaching its 140th anniversary!), this small, welcoming restaurant serves gourmet cuisine prepared by new chef Marco Veneruso, a southern Italian whose respectable CV gives his dishes intensity, strength and finesse. A good example is the linguine with scampi and an anchovy sauce, one of the signature dishes that earned him a Michelin star during his time in Beijing. Here, he offers three menus: "DALLA COSTIERA ALLA SWISS RIVIERA", "VENTO D'ESTATE" and the vegetarian "BOUQUET DALL'ORTO". Dishes can be chosen à la carte style – all you have to do is ask!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1577;Il Lago;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai des Bergues 33, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2068583;6.1466147;41;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;The iconic Four Seasons hotel, Geneva’s oldest luxury hotel (1834), dripping with pilasters and frescoes, is the setting of Il Lago, or Lake Geneva’s classy remake of the dolce vita. The kitchen team offers high-flying Italian cuisine, with the odd Mediterranean accent, rich in aromas, subtlety and delicacy. The quintessence of fine dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1578;Gasthaus Zum Gupf;Switzerland;Rehetobel;Gupf 21, Rehetobel, 9038, Switzerland;47.4310779;9.4918454;98;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Perched 1 083m above sea level and reached by a steep, narrow path, this place is a little slice of heaven! The pretty inn with a wood-panelled interior exudes regional charm and boasts a view of the mountains or the lake, plus a wonderful terrace. Walter Klose cooks up aromatic classic cuisine that follows the seasons and combines finesse with a certain unpretentiousness. When it comes to the service, you are in good hands thanks to the excellent team led by the lady of the house, who serves diners with a warm and easy manner. The wine list is sensational – a tour of the wine cellar with over 30 000 bottles is a real experience! You can also spend the night in the pleasant guesthouse.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1579;La Table d'Adrien;Switzerland;Verbier;Chemin des Creux, Verbier, 1936, Switzerland;46.1035076;7.224638;23;false;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;This smart chalet overlooking Verbier serves tasty, inventive Italian cuisine in the cosy interior of an elegant hotel. The dishes win diners over with their precision and creativity, with the quality of the ingredients and the spot-on marriages of flavours. Opt for the superb wine pairings suggested to enhance the set menu. The experience is topped off by attentive service and a superb view.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1580;LeMontBlanc;Switzerland;Crans-Montana;Chemin du Mont-Blanc 1, Crans-Montana, 3963, Switzerland;46.3151702;7.4628954;69;false;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;The restaurant’s extensive semi-circular windows command a panoramic view of the Swiss Alps that will take your breath away. The subtle, high-flying cuisine merges top-drawer Swiss produce, including treasures from the surrounding fertile countryside, with traditional Gallic recipes that have been treated to an international spin (Simmental veal, Belgian endive, miso, ponzu, kumquat). At the helm, chef Yannick Crepaux (who trained with Guy Martin and Christian Constant) upholds the establishment’s fine dining ethos, to the delight of the regulars! The terrace draws diners likes bees to honey in fine weather, while an open fire burns brightly in the lounge-bar to take the chill off winter evenings. Slick, professional service and a stupendous choice of fine wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1582;Osteria dell'Enoteca;Switzerland;Losone;contrada Maggiore 24, Losone, 6616, Switzerland;46.1683701;8.7577196;90;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in a quiet residential district, this charming, elegant and modern restaurant is run by a friendly and professional young couple who serve delicious and imaginative contemporary-style cuisine. The dining room is dominated by a large fireplace, while in summer meals are also served alfresco in the flower-filled garden. Works of art grace the premises both indoors and out. Interesting selection of wines from Ticino.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1583;Domaine de Châteauvieux;Switzerland;Satigny;Chemin de Châteauvieux 16, Satigny, 1242, Switzerland;46.201566;6.0388597;36;true;false;Modern French, French;Courtesy of chef-patron Philippe Chevrier, this institution that is full of soul and character has had a youthful makeover. All the more reason to come to this culinary landmark in the vicinity of Geneva in an ideal location surrounded by vineyards and off the beaten tourist track. Assisted by a seasoned team, Philippe Chevrier crafts refined French cuisine, ranging from modern to classical, based on outstanding produce and instantly identifiable flavours. Attentive service and a wine list that turns out to feature plenty of treats. Enjoy your meal on the idyllic terrace overlooking the hills. Finally, to digest this culinary experience in style, take advantage of the charming, tastefully decorated guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1585;Damien Germanier;Switzerland;Sion;Rue du Scex 33, Sion, 1950, Switzerland;46.232414;7.365789;60;true;false;Creative;After deciding on the number of courses (from four to ten) with chef Damien Germanier, who can often be found chatting to diners, you will give him carte blanche. His creativity and original ideas, primarily vegetable, are invariably spot on and you need not be fearful of putting yourself in his hands. A modern interior with designer touches, striking photo prints, stylish seating and a rock’n roll soundtrack sets the buzzy scene. The service is attentive and charming.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1586;Segreto;Switzerland;Wittenbach;Abacus Platz 1, Wittenbach, 9301, Switzerland;47.450773;9.3964148;63;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;You may be surprised to discover such a fine place on company premises, but you will immediately be transported to the Mediterranean. You can enjoy an aperitif in the relaxed lounge looking out over the pretty garden. In keeping with the setting, Martin Benninger cooks up traditional Mediterranean cuisine, which he enhances with Asian touches. The interior is modern and elegant – in summer, with its glass front open, the conservatory almost feels like a terrace. The attentive and experienced front-of-house team also provide excellent wine recommendations, and the digital wine list is really well curated. Al Covo is a charming alternative – for pizza, pasta etc (Fri-Sun evenings).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1587;La Chaumière by Serge Labrosse;Switzerland;Troinex;Chemin de la Fondelle 16, Troinex, 1256, Switzerland;46.1624055;6.1476047;83;true;false;Modern French, Farm to table;Feel like a breath of fresh air and getting out of the town centre? This Cottage by Serge Labrosse (who also gives cookery lessons in Geneva) is just the ticket. An elegant, contemporary vibe sets the scene for artfully presented dishes based on painstakingly selected ingredients by a chef who has knocked around a bit…, without forgetting the pretty terrace in fine weather and very convenient private car park. Whether you prefer traditional fare or more modern creations, there is something for everyone.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1588;Schlüssel - Nidbergstube;Switzerland;Mels;Oberdorfstrasse 5, Mels, 8887, Switzerland;47.0463482;9.4185999;15;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A real institution in the canton of St Gallen. Since 1974, the Kalberer family name has been synonymous with exquisite fine dining. Son Roger has now taken over the reins and continues to run the kitchen in the same vein. Dishes brimming with robust flavours are complemented by a fabulous wine list including a decent selection of Swiss wines and an abundance of French labels. Friendly and well-drilled service team. The cosy, refined interior also hits the right notes, with the small Nidbergstube doing full justice to the historical setting of this elegant patrician house dating back to 1811. This restaurant is named after the Nidberg hill in the village, where wine has been grown since the 15C.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1590;L'OURS;Switzerland;Crans-Montana;Route du Pas de l'Ours 41, Crans-Montana, 3963, Switzerland;46.3075598;7.4598456;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine, French;A modern, stylish vibe, depicted by high-quality fixtures and fittings and a profusion of wood and stone, sets the Alpine scene. The quality of the ingredients is equally superlative and chef Franck Reynaud reverently respects the seasons. His classical recipes with a modern twist are rolled out in a surprise menu of 5 to 8 courses and served by a polished front-of-house team. Enticing list of Valais wines. Treat yourself to a night (or two) in the Hostellerie du Pas de l’Ours, as stylish and cosy as the restaurant.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1591;Château Attisholz - Le feu;Switzerland;Riedholz;Attisholzstrasse 3, Riedholz, 4533, Switzerland;47.2283252;7.575171;57;false;true;French, Contemporary;This is a rather grand establishment located just outside Riedholz. A truly splendid historical property houses the exquisitely elegant and tastefully designed fine dining restaurant Le feu, with the garden and courtyard outside being a draw in themselves. Chef-patron Jörg Slaschek proposes a sophisticated modern-classical set menu, but there is also an à la carte selection. It goes without saying that the Bavarian-born chef uses only select produce. A well-curated selection of European wines makes for the perfect accompaniment to your meal. Overnight accommodation is also available: There are really appealing guestrooms that fit perfectly into the overall picture of sophistication.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1592;Restaurant de l'Hôtel de Ville;Switzerland;Ollon;Place de l'Hôtel-de-Ville 3, Ollon, 1867, Switzerland;46.2968491;6.9951099;96;true;true;French Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;In the centre of the village, near the bell tower, this country house champions tradition in all its glory. Beneath the vaulted ceiling of the dining room, you will be served seasonal French cuisine with a choice of menus and courses. Grégory Halgand conjures up creative dishes such as asparagus, grapefruit and pistachio or Brittany lobster, red beetroot, blackberries and fish bisque. The dessert lineup is the work of Audrey Feutren-Halgand, who also respects the seasons, with delicacies such as a medley of apricots (stewed, jellied and grilled), flanked by a frothy coconut mousse. Artwork (paintings and sculptures) graces the interior, and there is a pleasant outdoor patio for a final alfresco flourish. The ‘café’ offers a brasserie-style menu and a more casual vibe.;;[]
1593;1910 Gourmet by Hausers;Switzerland;Grindelwald;Dorfstrasse 53, Grindelwald, 3818, Switzerland;46.6253591;8.0293781;44;true;false;Contemporary;The fine dining restaurant of the Hotel Belvedere welcomes diners in a compact space with just six tables. In the kitchen, Hungarian chef Dávid Imre Rózsa runs the show. His technically modern and pleasingly pared-back style conveys emotions through its flavours, and comes into its own in dishes such as dry-aged pike perch with Oscietra caviar from Frutigen – this also exemplifies the firm focus on using local produce. There is a choice of two set menus, one of which is vegetarian, as well as a good wine selection with the option of ordering by the glass. The kitchen team provide back up to the friendly waitstaff.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1594;Wirtshaus Zur Säge;Switzerland;Flüh;Steinrain 5, Flüh, 4112, Switzerland;47.4883006;7.4980391;73;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;The "Sägi" has long been known for its great food, and Michelin-starred chef Patrick Zimmermann, who has been running this long-established inn for years together with his wife Corinne, is continuing this tradition. He prepares classic French cuisine and sets great store by seasonality. His fine sauces also testify to his cooking skills. Excellent produce forms the basis of his delicious dishes. And the atmosphere? In addition to the cosy, rustic and elegant interior with its wooden panelling and old ceiling beams as well as pictures and pretty floral decorations, there is also the attentive front-of-house team – who will also be happy to recommend good wines. In summer, make a beeline for the charming terrace with its vines and chestnut tree!;Car park,Terrace;[]
1595;Radius by Stefan Beer;Switzerland;Interlaken;Höheweg 41, Interlaken, 3800, Switzerland;46.6865553;7.8575473;88;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Swiss;In his kitchen in the restaurant of the time-honoured Victoria Jungfrau Grand Hotel, Stefan Beer only uses ingredients sourced within a 50km radius (the clue is in the name!). He proposes a conventional set menu and a vegan set menu, as well as a menu for two people sharing, which includes classics finished at your table and large cuts of meat. Diners are talked through the pleasingly uncomplicated dishes – sometimes by the chef. Produce that they harvest themselves is used, as well as local shrimps or caviar from the region. The high standards are also reflected in the tasteful and upscale interior.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1596;META;Switzerland;Lugano;Riva Paradiso 2, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;45.9927279;8.946328;32;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;Guests feel as though they’re sitting in the lounge of a beautiful private house in this restaurant in Palazzo Mantegazza, which boasts spectacular views of the lake. Here, the kitchen team creates an imaginative and seasonal gourmet menu that showcases local specialities alongside more international dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1597;La Micheline;Switzerland;Geneva;Avenue de la Gare des Eaux-Vives 3, Geneva, 1207, Switzerland;46.2007883;6.1658942;28;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, French Contemporary;This restaurant opposite the new station sports a magnificent bistronomy concept over two floors. The Mediterranean cuisine has been stripped of superfluous frills so shine the spotlight on the ingredient and flavour. The service is as smooth as a bearnaise sauce and the vibe is smart and upmarket. La Micheline refers to the first train from Annemasse to Eaux-Vives – equipped with Michelin tyres.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1598;Wöschi;Switzerland;Zurich;Seestrasse 457, Zurich, 8038, Switzerland;47.3405124;8.5380296;19;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Wöschi is located directly at Wollishofen harbour and boasts a magnificent view of the Zürisee, as the locals call Lake Zurich. You may know head chef David Klocksin from 20/20 by Mövenpick, where he delivered Michelin-starred cuisine. Here, he serves up dishes that are a little lower-key, but still punchy, with an emphasis on vegetables. The three- to five-course surprise menu reflects this with pleasingly pared-down yet full-bodied creations such as baked cauliflower with curry and peanut. However, the more "conventional" options, such as the Valais pike-perch or Zurich beef, are just as delectable. This is a truly stylish restaurant, where charming and attentive service comes courtesy of Stephanie Ospelt and team. Gorgeous terrace overlooking the lake.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1599;Gasthaus zum Kreuz - Bijou;Switzerland;Dallenwil;Stettlistrasse 3, Dallenwil, 6383, Switzerland;46.9318372;8.3909237;88;false;false;Asian and Western, Modern Cuisine;Dietmar and Nicole Sawyere call this "micro-restaurant experience" what awaits you in the evening at the "Bijou" in the neat inn dating from 1570. The atmosphere here is pleasantly personal and intimate, the service attentive and cordial. An exciting culinary combination of Swiss and Asian cuisine is offered in the form of a surprise menu with six courses. The menu is called the "Hintersassen Menu" - a reference to the settlers of Dallenwil who moved here from further afield and integrated new ideas. As an alternative restaurant, the house also runs the regionally oriented "Stübli".;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1601;elmira;Switzerland;Zurich;Limmatstrasse 254, Zurich, 8005, Switzerland;47.3888413;8.5265176;94;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This modern restaurant is located in the basement of a former silo on the Löwenbräu brewery site. The open kitchen, which is practically integrated into the dining area, delivers creative dishes with a focus on sustainability and seasonality, often using ingredients sourced from the immediate vicinity. A set menu of five or seven courses is proposed – this can be vegan, vegetarian or include meat/fish. To accompany your meal, there is an interesting selection of wines, or you could sample the house-made juices – the charming, laid-back staff will gladly talk you through your options. The overall atmosphere is pleasingly relaxed and informal, and the chefs might even come to your table for a chat. N.B. There is a reservation system and you pay in advance.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1602;Cà d'Oro;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Mezdi 27, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4825433;9.8333987;91;true;true;Alpine, Swiss;The restaurant in the impressive Grand Hotel des Bains Kempinski St. Moritz exudes classic elegance. From the comfort of your table, beneath the high ceiling with striking chandeliers and moulding, enjoy obliging service in the time-honoured tradition of fine-dining culture. Leopold Ott decamps to Locanda Barbarossa in Ascona in the summer season, and in winter proposes classic-modern cuisine with Mediterranean and international influences – the Cà d'Oro caviar selection is also a mainstay here. Fantastic wine selection.;Car park,Valet parking;[]
1603;Alpine Gourmet Prato Borni;Switzerland;Zermatt;Bahnhofstrasse 55, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0198662;7.7467463;71;false;true;Creative, Country cooking;The fine dining restaurant of the Grand Hotel Zermatterhof, in the town centre, serves two fantastic set menus made with top-notch ingredients: "Heimat" seeks inspiration in the region and "Fernweh" looks to foreign climes. The classically elegant dining area is done out with fine wood panelling, and the front-of-house team provides well-coordinated service. Impressive wine list!;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1604;Capri;Switzerland;Zermatt;Hofmattstrasse 12, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0217959;7.7482352;89;true;true;Italian;You don't have to venture to the island of Capri for fantastic classic Italian cuisine, because the chefs at Capri Palace spend the winter at this restaurant in Zermatt. In the elegant decor of the fourth floor of Le Petit Cervin (adjoining Mont Cervin Palace), tuck into dishes that are prepared using high-quality ingredients and big on flavour. Attentive, professional and slick service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1605;THE VIEW;Switzerland;Lugano;Via Guidino 29, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;45.9873025;8.950395;44;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;At this restaurant, Diego Della Schiava creates beautifully presented cuisine that is truly a feast for the eyes! This chef’s philosophy focuses on seasonal ingredients, which he transforms into Mediterranean and Swiss dishes with an equal emphasis on meat and fish, including highlights such as the delicious scallop tartare with sesame oil, nasturtiums and porcini mushroom puff. In fine weather, we recommend booking a table on the spacious terrace to enjoy its stunning views of Lugano and the lake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1606;EquiTable;Switzerland;Zurich;Stauffacherstrasse 163, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3778541;8.5212339;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The atmosphere here is urban and international. As well as drawing on fairtrade and organic produce, the chefs use top-notch regional ingredients to create interesting, modern and creative dishes – vegetarian guests are also well catered for. The efficient front-of-house team is pleasingly attentive while keeping a low profile.;Terrace;[]
1607;Le Berceau des Sens;Switzerland;Lausanne;Route de Berne 301, Lausanne, 1000, Switzerland;46.5608424;6.6828358;22;true;false;Modern French, Classic Cuisine;Lausanne's EHL Hospitality Business School can be proud of this top-notch restaurant. A crack team of chefs (several Meilleurs Ouvriers de France are on the teaching faculty) work with the students to orchestrate a series of dishes that abound with coherent flavours, bringing their classroom learnings to the table! The dishes, which are perfectly poised between classic and modern, demonstrate a mastery of technical skill. From start to finish, each bite is bliss, and the setting also enhances the experience: the bright interior has a superb view of the surrounding mountains. Hats off!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
1608;Aux Trois Amis;Switzerland;Ligerz;Untergasse 17, Ligerz, 2514, Switzerland;47.0900127;7.1398195;75;false;true;Country cooking;A narrow road leads up to this wonderful restaurant surrounded by vineyards and boasting a pleasantly shaded terrace overlooking Lake Biel – dining al fresco here is an absolute joy! Allow yourself to be pampered by the charming front-of-house team led by maître d' Cynthia Lauper as you savour the "Menu Surprise" conjured up by chef-patron Marc Joshua Engel. This is sophisticated cuisine imbued with creative accents, eg venison fillet with black garlic, asparagus and cherries. Alternatively, there are a handful of à la carte dishes. Your hostess and sommelier will gladly recommend fine wines – including some local gems – to complement your food. Tip: It's best to park in the restaurant's car park and walk the last few metres.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1609;Löwen - Apriori;Switzerland;Bubikon;Wolfhauserstrasse 2, Bubikon, 8608, Switzerland;47.2684196;8.8188114;29;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;You can sense the dedication of hosts Rita and Domenico Miggiano-Köferli, who, since 2000, have been running this lovely inn that is steeped in history. As well as tasteful, individually decorated guestrooms and Gaststube (their everyday restaurant), Löwen is home to Apriori, a fine dining restaurant that has held a MICHELIN star since 2018. The elegant modern interior is done out in warm dark tones and has designer lamps and exquisitely laid tables. Chef-patron Domenico Miggiano puts his heart and soul into his cooking. His culinary style is a modern take on classic cuisine, with Mediterranean accents. In the evening, the "Signature" set menu comprising four or five courses is served, with an optional additional cheese course. The "Business Lunch" deal is popular. The fantastic wine list featuring approximately 350 labels provides a brief description of each winery. The charming maître d' is a trained sommelier and her recommendations are excellent.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1610;Vivanda;Switzerland;Brail;Crusch Plantaun 217, Brail, 7527, Switzerland;46.6539661;10.0336936;25;true;false;Creative, Alpine;Life is good at Vivanda! You will catch a glimpse of the open kitchen as you make your way into the restaurant, which boasts views of the national park and the garden. The chic design features modern lines and warm wood – the Cadonau family has its own woodwork workshop, hence the hotel name (IN LAIN means "made of wood"). The affinity for the region makes itself felt in both the decor and the modern cuisine, which is based on local produce and presented in the form of a surprise tasting menu. Chef-patron Dario Cadonau works with dedication and his own unique style to showcase excellent ingredients in combinations such as aged venison with a silky parsnip cream, parsnip ragout and red cabbage puree. He and the kitchen team also get involved in serving the food. There's a wonderful assortment of cheeses – head to the ripening cellar to choose yours!;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1611;Seerestaurant Belvédère;Switzerland;Hergiswil;Seestrasse 18a, Hergiswil, 6052, Switzerland;46.9833332;8.3117704;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;The fantastic view of Lake Lucerne alone makes it worthwhile coming here, and it's especially enjoyable from the wonderful terrace! But, thanks to the floor-to-ceiling windows, you don't have to miss out on the view if you sit inside the modern and elegant restaurant either. Meanwhile, Fabian Inderbitzin's cuisine is no less sought after. In the evening, two set menus, each with a vegetarian counterpart, are created from outstanding produce. The clear structure of the dishes is pleasing. At lunchtime, the "Gourmet Lunch" set menu and a few classics à la carte form a smaller but equally sophisticated selection. The service is professional, friendly and attentive. Good to know: there are five spaces at the jetty reserved for customers of the establishment.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1612;LA CHAVALLERA in der Krone - Säumerei am Inn;Switzerland;La Punt-Chamues-ch;Via Cumünela 2, La Punt-Chamues-ch, 7522, Switzerland;46.5786998;9.9260661;80;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Alpine;The time-honoured Krone, long renowned as a destination for foodies, is now run with dedication by the well-travelled James Baron (most recently head chef at the Michelin-starred Amber in Hong Kong) and his charming wife Natacha. Entirely done out in Swiss stone pine, the compact dining space brims with atmosphere, further fuelled by the lively energy of the attentive staff. The cuisine is pared down to the essentials and made with top-notch produce, some of it regional. Comprising four, six or eight courses, the set menu features dishes such as pear ravioli, brown butter and sage, or veal, grapes and black salsify. An interesting touch: the cutlery is made by a local blacksmith. Modern Alpine-style guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1614;La Riva;Switzerland;Lenzerheide;Voa Davos Lai 27, Lenzerheide, 7078, Switzerland;46.7356712;9.546549;91;false;true;Modern French, Classic Cuisine;If dining out on the terrace isn't an option, go for one of the tables next to the huge front windows – then you can take in the view of the lake, Heidsee, and the mountains as you savour Dominique Schrotter's ambitious modern take on classic cuisine. For example, king mackerel served as a "tartare tower" and a marinated slice, accompanied by chilled pumpkin balls and a pear gel, which provide a wonderful contrast, and a harmonious, almost clear Périgord truffle dashi. There is also a vegetarian set menu. From a family of restaurateurs, the chef spent some years teaching and travelling, during which time he visited Bangkok and other places. This resulted in a real soft spot for East Asian cuisine, hence the regular "Sushi Festivals". The dedicated and very friendly front-of-house team are also able to provide astute wine recommendations.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1615;Le Chat-Botté;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai du Mont-Blanc 13, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2091162;6.1499175;56;true;false;Modern French, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in the Beau Rivage Hotel, one of the finest palace hotels on Lake Geneva. Get ready to tuck into cuisine designed for the modern palate that showcases local producers (beef, poultry, fruits and vegetables). The whole experience is enhanced by the admirable work of the sommelier, who will guide you through an impressive 1 400-bin wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1616;Maihöfli by UniQuisine;Switzerland;Lucerne;Maihofstrasse 70, Lucerne, 6006, Switzerland;47.0652678;8.3115827;39;false;false;Creative, Innovative;Since its reopening, this lovely restaurant just outside the city centre has acquired a new head chef in Robert Steuri. In the evenings, he and his dedicated team showcase precise craftsmanship and top-notch ingredients in two intriguing and innovative three-, five- or seven-course set menus, one of which is vegan. The dishes are full of finesse and carefully composed, elaborate but not cluttered – a great example is the green asparagus, mushrooms, snow peas and beans. Options are more limited at lunchtime. The attractive setting sees the charming features of this old building, such as high ceilings with decorative mouldings and wood panelling, seamlessly integrated into its sleek and elegant modern design. Professional and well-coordinated service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1617;Table de Mary;Switzerland;Cheseaux-Noréaz;Route du Gymnase 2, Cheseaux-Noréaz, 1400, Switzerland;46.7805014;6.6677225;99;true;true;Classic French;A few minutes from Yverdon-les-Bains, this restaurant enjoys an ideal location overlooking Lake Neuchâtel. It has been run with passion and dedication by Maryline and Loïc Nozahic since 2007. Their simple and beautifully executed take on classic French cuisine is replete with forthright flavours and pronounced aromas and always in tune with the seasons. Example dishes include ballotine of rabbit with mustard seeds and Puy lentil royale. On sunny days, head to the shady, flower-decked terrace, with its magnificent views of the Jura Mountains. Good value for money and regional wines. An inviting establishment.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1618;Tosca;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue de la Mairie 8, Geneva, 1207, Switzerland;46.2027504;6.158218;72;true;true;Tuscan;Tosca, an emblematic address of the Eaux-Vives district, famous for its fountain, takes la cucina very seriously! The interior by a contemporary Italian artist pays a distinctive tribute to the art and culture of the Italian Renaissance in a Florentine-inspired romantic setting. The food is the inspired work of Ivan Baretti, born and bred in Florence, who trained at Arpège in Paris and was a former chef at Il Lago, no less! With a magnificent supporting cast of top-class ingredients, his delicate, refined dishes unveil a strong Tuscan bias and hit the spot every time. Amiable, professional service and knock-out selection of Tuscan wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1619;Wirtschaft im FRANZ;Switzerland;Zurich;Bremgartnerstrasse 18, Zurich, 8003, Switzerland;47.3722302;8.5195348;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Etwas versteck in einem Innenhof liegt das «Franz» - der Name steht für «Frauen im Zentrum» und ist ein Ort für Kultur, Arbeit und Essen. Letzteres bietet man in der «Wirtschaft im Franz» in Form eines durchdachten Überraschungsmenüs. Die ambitionierten modern-kreativen Speisen sind angenehm reduziert und legen den Fokus auf Produktqualität, wobei Gemüse im Mittelpunkt steht. Schön auch das Ambiente dazu: Mit seiner offenen Küche und dem trendigen Bistro-Stil versprüht das Restaurant eine sympathisch-unkomplizierte, freundliche und urbane Atmosphäre.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1620;Jägerhof;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Brühlbleichestrasse 11, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.430792;9.3833953;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Jägerhof is an establishment steeped in culinary history! Since 2016, former sous-chef Agron Lleshi has been at the helm, delivering modern seasonal cuisine that seeks inspiration in the local region and abroad. The chef's mother makes the fresh bread rolls. At lunchtime, the food is somewhat simpler. When you enter the elegant restaurant, take a peek into the kitchen – this is also where the "Küchentisch" (Kitchen Table) is located, which diners can book. An attentive service team does sterling work, and impressive wine advice is also dispensed. A large selection of home-made chocolates is served with coffee.;Terrace;[]
1621;Lucide;Switzerland;Lucerne;Europaplatz 1, Lucerne, 6005, Switzerland;47.0500723;8.3119367;53;false;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;This place ticks all the boxes! It has a central location right by Lake Lucerne, on the first floor of the Culture and Congress Centre, commanding fantastic views of the lake and the city. It boasts a stylish and chic interior. Furthermore, there is a well-staffed, friendly and highly proficient service team. And then there's the food – modern flavoursome dishes made with high-quality ingredients and prepared in an open kitchen. In the evenings, diners have a choice of two four- to six-course set menus, one of which is vegetarian. For lunch, a budget-friendly set menu is available, along with a small selection of items from the evening menu to be ordered à la carte.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1622;ORSINI;Switzerland;Zurich;Waaggasse 7, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3701183;8.5402159;41;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Italian fine dining is the name of the game here at the stylish Mandarin Oriental Savoy Hotel, which dates back to 1838. Via a separate entrance on Waaggasse, you walk into the sophisticated and elegant interior, which provides the foil to Dario Moresco's creative and modern Italian cuisine. Although occasionally replete with striking contrasts, the dishes remain harmoniously balanced and pleasingly light. Their finesse and expression are a delight – we were won over, for example, by the spaghetti twisted into a small tower: served with a mussel and white wine coulis and herb sauce, on juicy, tender shredded crab meat, and enriched with the refreshing citrus note of finger lime pearls. Tasting menu in the evening, set menu at lunchtime, plus an à la carte offering at each mealtime. Antonio Guida from two-star restaurant Seta by Antonio Guida in Milan is the consultant chef.;;[]
1623;L'Aparté;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue de Lausanne 43, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2134994;6.145432;30;false;true;Modern French, Farm to table;Perfectly suited to the swish, intimate vibe of Hôtel Royal in which it is located, take a seat at one of the restaurant’s four tables and let yourself be guided. The chef serves each elegant, immaculately crafted dish himself, explaining the ins and outs of their preparation. You will sample a lineup of outstanding produce – Swiss veal and beef, fish straight from Brittany, Bresse poultry, harnessed to ambitious cuisine packed with character. We recommend booking well in advance, particularly in the evenings, both in light of the seating capacity and its popularity, which is not about to wane. Bogie’s Bar is ideal to kick off or finish your meal in style. Valet parking available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1624;Du Bourg;Switzerland;Biel;Burggasse 12, Biel, 2502, Switzerland;47.1411781;7.2456915;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This 16C town house is one of Biel's architectural monuments. Your dedicated pair of hosts serve up vegetable-based dishes that abound with finesse – you can opt to add in freshwater fish or selected meat from Switzerland, or stick with the set menu in its vegetarian version. There is an interesting choice of wines, as well as alcohol-free pairings made on site.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1625;Auberge de la Croix Blanche;Switzerland;Villarepos;Route de Donatyre 22, Villarepos, 1583, Switzerland;46.8831298;7.0690391;92;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The epitome of calm, serenity and good food. Located in a village called Villarepos (loosely translated: "Restful Villa") and overlooking Lake Morat, this Auberge is a haven of the tranquillity that is so emblematic of Switzerland. With its flower-decked window boxes, this gorgeous house is like something straight out of a fairytale. Christa and Arno, who bend over backwards to make you feel at home, usher you into an elegant, wood-panelled dining area. Classical cuisine and premium regional produce are the watchwords when it comes to the menu. You'll leave feeling sated and happy. Bistro offering and guestrooms available.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1626;Locanda Orico;Switzerland;Bellinzona;via Orico 13, Bellinzona, 6500, Switzerland;46.1921056;9.0189483;85;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;A focus on sustainability is much more than a simple slogan at this restaurant housed in a historic palazzo in the old town. Since 1998 here, the owner-chef works with excellent local suppliers in order to provide the best possible experience for his guests, talking them through each dish and the provenance of its top-quality ingredients. There’s nothing mysterious about the process, which results in healthy Mediterranean cuisine with a combination of French and regional influences, and where the menu changes at the beginning of each season and the tasting menu every month. Dishes here are carefully presented, with meticulous attention to detail and a perfect combination of colours. An interesting selection of renowned wines adds to its appeal, including an excellent choice of local and international labels. A simpler business menu is available at lunchtime, when dishes are announced at your table. A stronghold of fine Ticino cuisine! The restaurant has recently installed a recharging point for electric cars.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1627;Gasthaus Löwen;Switzerland;Menzingen;Holzhäusernstrasse 2, Menzingen, 6313, Switzerland;47.1785896;8.5903795;41;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Dating back to the 16C, Löwen is a lovely traditional inn that has been run by Tanja and Franco Körperich since 2019. She takes care of the service in the charming and elegant wood-panelled dining space on the first floor, and Franco is at the helm in the kitchen. Diners sit at elegantly laid tables to savour a surprise menu comprising four to eight courses, with vegetarian options available if pre-ordered. Top-quality ingredients go into classic dishes that draw on modern and international influences. A shining example is the gently barbecued and mildly spiced king prawn, accompanied by lightly sautéed buck's horn plantain and fine baby peas, all complemented by a tom kha gai beurre blanc with a wonderful aroma and texture. The chef-patron makes a point of offering guidance and presenting his dishes himself. In summer, you can dine al fresco in the pretty Steingarten on the opposite side of the street.;Terrace;[]
1628;Schlüssel;Switzerland;Oberwil;Hauptstrasse 41, Oberwil, 4104, Switzerland;47.5140269;7.5560208;29;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;A meal here is a real pleasure, thanks to Felix Suter and Sandra Marugg Suter, who are truly passionate about what they do – he in the kitchen, she front of house. There are no menus: your extremely cordial hostess will acquaint you with the set menu and explain the dishes. Always on hand, she has a delightfully natural way with guests. Chef-patron Felix Suter (who might be familiar from Säge in Flüh) shows the same passion in his cooking, delivering down-to-earth dishes that prize one thing above all else: flavour! His cooking draws on classical foundations and spurns fleeting modern trends. At lunchtime, a three-course lunch set menu is served. Lovely garden terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1629;La Rôtisserie;Switzerland;Zurich;Weinplatz 2, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3712935;8.5418052;69;true;false;Contemporary, International;Located on the first floor of the Hotel Storchen, La Rôtisserie is every bit as tastefully decorated as the establishment that houses it – which was first mentioned in the 14C. It has a beautiful dining room with high ceilings, large arched windows and elegant, high-quality furnishings – this is a traditional yet contemporary affair. In the kitchen, the chefs work with precision and great skill to produce their own modern, international take on classic cuisine. In fine weather, be sure to head out onto the fantastic terrace – from this wonderful old-town location you can take in views of the Limmat River and the historical buildings laid out on the other side of the water. Fancy a special experience? Then book the Chef's Table in the centre of the kitchen! Brunch is served on Sundays.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1630;After Seven;Switzerland;Zermatt;Hofmattstrasse 4, Zermatt, 3929, Switzerland;46.021962;7.7478621;53;false;true;Creative;A lift takes you up to the fine dining restaurant of the Backstage Hotel. After a relaxed aperitif on the comfortable couch stationed beneath an originally designed chandelier made up of musical instruments, you can look forward to a creative surprise menu composed of four to seven courses, which is prepared in the open kitchen by Florian Neubauer's dedicated team. You will be handed a menu listing some of the main ingredients of the evening – it's up to you to just choose the number of courses! The modern and elegant interior is brimming over with artworks – this is the hallmark of the owner, artist and hotelier Heinz Julen. The centrally positioned fireplace also adds atmosphere. You might like to opt for one of the dishes given the finishing touch at your table!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1631;Truube;Switzerland;Gais;Rotenwies 9, Gais, 9056, Switzerland;47.3661606;9.4606828;31;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Very inviting from the outside, this typical Appenzell country inn is no less beautiful on the inside. Come here to enjoy Silvia Manser's classic cuisine with Mediterranean influences in a pleasingly simple yet upscale setting. This is a chef who isn't averse to spicing things up, infusing her refined dishes with the perfect balance of potent flavours. It goes without saying that her ingredients are of the highest quality. Silvia Manser runs this place together with her husband Thomas, and the two of them work together like a well-oiled machine: while she is at the helm in the kitchen, he competently and cordially takes care of service, making suitable wine recommendations from their excellent selection.;Bring your own bottle,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1632;Neue Blumenau;Switzerland;Lömmenschwil;Romanshornerstrasse 2, Lömmenschwil, 9308, Switzerland;47.4941739;9.3530135;26;true;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;What a lovely place! This attractive building may be a bit out of the way, but it's worth the journey, especially in summer if you can secure a spot on the wonderful garden terrace! It is also pleasant to dine inside, in the elegant restaurant. Whichever space you plump for, you will be treated to courteous service – Bernadette Lisibach, the extremely friendly owner, also makes frequent appearances at the tables. She really puts her heart and soul into running this place, using select ingredients in her fuss-free, tasty and expressive cooking, which leans towards the classical. Diners choose between two set menus. There is a good wine list and a nice selection of cheeses to round off the whole experience.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1633;UniQuisine Atelier;Switzerland;Stansstad;Stanserstrasse 23, Stansstad, 6362, Switzerland;46.9757757;8.3419323;55;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant certainly achieves its goal of making guests feel they are "dining at a friend's place". The "unique" location alone ensures this: the relatively small dining area is laid out in a modern apartment done out in a minimalist chic style on the third floor of a residential and restaurant block. A pleasingly informal and intimate atmosphere prevails, not least thanks to the central open kitchen. Diners are in good hands with head chef Christoph Oliver Aebersold and restaurant manager Agron Tunprenkaj – two consummate professionals who provide friendly, high-quality service. The meticulous cuisine is pared down to the essentials and served in the form of a five- or seven-course set menu drawing on excellent, seasonal ingredients. Enjoy an aperitif on the lovely balcony terrace as you take in the view of the Pilatus and Stanserhorn mountains.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1634;Gasthaus zum Kreuz - Stübli;Switzerland;Dallenwil;Stettlistrasse 3, Dallenwil, 6383, Switzerland;46.9318556;8.390924;73;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Dietmar Sawyere, whom many will know from Andermatt's The Japanese by The Chedi at Gütsch and The Japanese Restaurant, has taken over the reins at this 500-year-old inn. In the charming wood-panelled Stübli, Alpine produce takes centre stage and is put to work with original ideas and a pleasing blend of modern, classical and traditional approaches. A prime example of this is the Arctic char served with garden peas, smoked ham, pine needles and beurre blanc. Diners are invited to choose from an array of options to put together their own menu of four to six courses. To accompany your meal, there is a decent wine list featuring Swiss and French labels. Maître d' Nicole Sawyere heads up a well-coordinated and professional front-of-house team. In summer, make a beeline for the shaded terrace – it's a perfect spot for an aperitif! For overnight stays, this inn – considered to be the oldest in the Engelberg Valley – has attractive modern guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1635;Chesa Stüva Colani;Switzerland;Madulain;Via Principela 20 A, Madulain, 7523, Switzerland;46.586082;9.937879;51;false;false;Innovative, Italian;The interior boasts an exquisite blend of warm and cosy local wood furnishings and elegant minimalist design. Modern Italian cuisine with a strong connection to the region and the seasons is on a menu showcasing excellent ingredients and the head chef's interesting personal touch. Stylish and charming chalet-style guestrooms are on hand for overnight stays. There is also a bistro.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1637;F.P. Journe - Le Restaurant;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue du Rhône 49, Geneva, 1200, Switzerland;46.2034895;6.1510328;40;false;true;Modern French;The great Geneva watchmaker François-Paul Journe and the former chef of Le Chat-Botté, Dominique Gauthier, have set their sights on this legendary institution (listed as a heritage site in the canton of Geneva), a chic upmarket bistro, with its black and white tiled floor, old wooden panelling and ceiling, red velvet banquettes and chairs.Studded with fine produce, the plates turn like fine timepieces, like this saddle of lamb from Chandossel with fennel and artichoke, accompanied by a purée worthy of Robuchon's own. Expect colourful dishes too, such as lobster from Brittany with Green Zebra tomatoes or langoustines roasted with kadaif. In this lively atmosphere, you can also count on perfectly oiled service and excellent advice from the sommelier.;Air conditioning;[]
1638;Yama;Japan;Tokyo;6-16-41 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.643773;139.722916;87;true;true;Creative;Chef Koichi Katsumata pours his devotion into his fruit selections, which he gathers as he calls on farms throughout Japan. Flavours variously embrace citrus fruits, mangoes, peaches, figs, and chestnuts as the seasons change. Each course offers variations in fragrance, texture and temperature, and through the incorporation of vegetables. The chef was born in Yamanashi Prefecture in the imposing presence of Mt. Fuji, hence the name of the establishment (yama means ‘mountain’). Yama demonstrates that, like the rugged Japanese islands so rich in peaks and valleys, pure sweetness can take a wide variety of forms.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1640;Tour D'argent Tokyo;Japan;Tokyo;Lobby floor, Hotel New Otani Tokyo (The Main), 4-1 Kioicho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 102-8578, Japan;35.680691;139.734172;22;true;false;French;The main location in Paris has a real history, having opened in 1582. Renaud Augier, winner of the Un des Meilleurs Ouvriers de France (MOF) award, breathes new life into classic dishes with modern sensibilities. Specialities with an especially solid reputation include young duck roast made with duck that carries a serial number, which was enjoyed by Emperor Showa, and Three Emperor’s style goose foie gras. A luxurious meal here would be a fitting end to a special day.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1641;Koshikiryori Koki;Japan;Tokyo;2-13-6 Nishishimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0003, Japan;35.666703;139.751646;16;true;false;Chinese;The Hong Kong–born chef is affectionately known as ‘Tommy-san’. Tending his woks amid the intimate environment of an open kitchen, he charms his audience, sometimes trading jokes with them. The go-to dish, fried pasted chicken testes, is one of Tomi-san’s proudest dishes and one that keeps customers coming back. Pork, chicken and spiny lobster served on large plates win diners over by bringing the true pleasure of Chinese cooking and showing why a simultaneous start to the meal works.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1643;Piao-Xiang;Japan;Tokyo;5-19-1 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.649081;139.719531;77;true;false;Chinese;Yoshiki Igeta is captivated by Sichuan cuisine. Chilli peppers were first introduced there four centuries ago, but Piao-Xiang weaves a tale of history, reaching back for the good old cooking of Sichuan before chilli peppers and adding a few enhancements. As a result, prix fixe menus are not spicy, giving full rein to the appeal of Sichuan cuisine and its 24 seasonings and 54 preparation methods. The staff’s explanations of his dishes fascinate with their profundity.;Air conditioning;[]
1644;Hiroo Ishizaka;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 5-19-1 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.649081;139.719531;22;false;false;Sushi;The chef is solid on the basics yet leaves room for a distinctive touch. The meal begins with moderately fatty, sweet flesh of tuna sushi, followed by sea urchin wrapped in nori as a way to compare flavours. Pursuing originality, a single piece of shiitake mushroom sushi follows. Sushi of botan shrimp and thick rolled omelette flavoured with soup stock is also distinctive. In summer, the chef serves rolled cucumber sushi, using cucumbers grown by his parents. The meal ends with soy sauce ice cream, a flavour only a sushi shop could offer.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1645;Sharikimon Onozawa;Japan;Tokyo;6-39 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.689236;139.722586;99;true;true;Japanese;Makoto Onozawa finds inventive ways to break the mould while respecting tradition. Soup dishes and sashimi uphold the basics, reassuring the diner. Broiled unagi seasoned in soy-based sweet sauce is served together with broiled unseasoned unagi for a special treat. Rolled sushi of tuna and pickled daikon radish are served in the intervals, bringing satisfaction. The meal concludes on two comfort-food notes: soba and curry. Breaking tradition, after all, is about seeing the job to completion.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1649;Shigeyuki;Japan;Tokyo;2-17-3 Nishihara, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0066, Japan;35.673129;139.67875;54;true;false;Japanese;‘The look surprises, the taste reassures.’ The chef’s passion for creativity makes his culinary spirit unique. Decoratively arranged sashimi are briefly heated to draw out moisture. The chef doesn’t serve soup dishes, as much of his cooking tailors the dashi stock to each dish. His freewheeling personality makes the evening fun, while the folk-art vibe of the interior, including a chest of drawers inherited from the chef’s grandparents, fills the air with memories and the warmth of family.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1650;Tempura Yaguchi;Japan;Tokyo;2-9-7 Nihombashiningyocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0013, Japan;35.686176;139.784022;86;true;false;Tempura;A single issue of a cooking magazine led Kazuki Yaguchi onto the path of the tempura artisan. Apprenticeship under his mentor taught Yaguchi to find his own style while inheriting his master’s culinary philosophy. His tempura is deep-fried in oil at high temperatures using a high proportion of cottonseed oil and features generous portions of vegetables. The batter is fried to fragrant perfection, drawing out the flavour of its contents. Sea urchin is wrapped in perilla leaf to avoid overheating.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1651;est;Japan;Tokyo;39F, Four Seasons Hotel Tokyo at Otemachi, 1-2-1 Otemachi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0004, Japan;35.688162;139.763396;29;true;false;French, Contemporary;Perched on the hotel’s top floor, the dining room affords stunning views of the city below. The modern kitchen, visible through a curtain-glass wall, is full of motion. Chef Guillaume Bracaval creates contemporary French expressions inspired by Japanese ingredients and culture. The map of Japan indicating where the various ingredients come from proclaims the bounty of Japan’s landscape. Desserts are a gorgeous flourish of contemporary art.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1652;LA TABLE de Joël Robuchon;Japan;Tokyo;Yebisu Garden Place, 1-13-1 Mita, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0062, Japan;35.641907;139.714544;62;false;false;French, Contemporary;A dining room in black and lavender, appointed in the style of a French chateau. The theme here is intimacy: Joël Robuchon done casual. The menu includes seasonal specialities and hometown cooking in a contemporary style, with preparations both simple and modern. Attentive service brightens the mood as the cuisine inspires lively conversation. Experience the true joy of gourmet dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1653;La Paix;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-9-4 Nihombashimuromachi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0022, Japan;35.685136;139.775586;96;true;false;French;La Paix is supported by five thematic elements: Japan, harmony, spirit, connection and the senses. The element of Japan enters in the form of ‘French cuisine from Japan’. As a native of Wakayama Prefecture, the chef sources Kishu Ume and makes a type of butter from them. Blancmange of Tartary Buckwheat is a treat found nowhere else. A fusion of Japanese and French influences that fits perfectly in Nihombashi, the crossroads of old and new Japan.;Air conditioning;[]
1654;Waketokuyama;Japan;Tokyo;5-1-5 Minamiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0047, Japan;35.655748;139.723292;87;true;true;Japanese;The young team is led by the chef who took on the duties from the esteemed founder of Waketokuyama. The customer-first policy and the flow of the meal remain unchanged. To showcase true seasonality and ensure that no two visits are the same, the menu is changed every ten days at most. The vast repertoire and elaborate creativity are astonishing. Based on the 72 micro-seasons, the dishes allow guests to savor the abundant gifts of nature in accordance with its rhythms.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1655;Sushi Hashimoto;Japan;Tokyo;1-8-2 Shintomi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0041, Japan;35.673;139.774495;90;true;false;Sushi;Straw-smoked Spanish mackerel is dressed with wasabi and mustard, adding depth to the flavour. Spiced with wasabi, wide strips of tuna are hand-moulded to wrap around the sushi rice, which is served warmer than normal to bring out the sweetness of the fat. Sushi portions are generous but can be adjusted to a preferred size. First-time customers are especially welcomed at lunchtime, to spread the word about the joys of sushi. Diners can experience the true nature of a sushi shop that welcomes all.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1656;BEIGE Alain Ducasse;Japan;Tokyo;10F, 3-5-3 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.67308;139.766511;87;false;true;French;A restaurant produced by an international giant of the culinary world. In an astute reading of the times, he was among the first to include generous amounts of vegetables and cereals in his creations, dialing back the fats and sugars. As a result, both flavour and postprandial feeling are light. BEIGE Alain Ducasse preaches l’art de vivre through gastronomy in an emporium that exudes elegance, from the beige interior to the Jacquard fabrics and the design inspired by Coco Chanel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1658;FARO;Japan;Tokyo;10F, 8-8-3 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.66852;139.761906;48;true;true;Italian;Japan’s wealth of foodstuffs and culture support a creative approach to cuisine. FARO’s staff criss-cross Japan to connect farms with dinner tables. Vegan cooking is embraced here, seen as a lifestyle of the future. The principle of connecting to the good earth shines in desserts crafted with respect for nature and the herbs of Japan. ‘Flower tart’, for example, honours the culture of the rural hills. The possibilities of provincial villages presented in Ginza.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1659;Yakitori Omino;Japan;Tokyo;1-38-4 Oshiage, Sumida-ku, Tokyo, 131-0045, Japan;35.709908;139.815922;74;true;false;Yakitori;The staff, sporting twisted headbands on their close-cropped heads, serve yakitori with passion, keeping the skewers coming until the customer says ‘stop’. The chef uses whole chickens, so you can sample even rare cuts to your heart’s content. Of special note is the use of Kishu binchotan charcoal, grilled close to a roaring flame. Skewers are brushed with dashi stock, soy sauce and oil to wreathe them in fragrance. For best results, make your preferences known when you walk in.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1660;Jushu;Japan;Tokyo;2-16-1 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661832;139.720305;85;true;false;Japanese;The crest on the shop curtain depicts a Eurasian magpie, the official bird of Saga Prefecture, in flight. The same motif is embroidered on the cooks’ whites. From his native Saga, the chef sources rice, Imari beef and yuzu pepper. Serving vessels of Karatsu and mid-Edo-period Imari are a point of pride. In a nod to Osaka experience, each dish is served once the previous one has been consumed. No food is wasted, and for the same reason decorative vegetation is never used. Grilled items are served with rice and soup, as in a set meal, expressing the restaurant's free-spirited character.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1663;ESTERRE;Japan;Tokyo;6F, Palace Hotel Tokyo, 1-1-1 Marunouchi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0005, Japan;35.684502;139.76123;66;true;false;French;Enjoy elegant dining with views of the verdant Kokyo Gaien National Garden and Wadakura Moat. ESTERRE partners with Alain Ducasse, a legend of the gastronomic world, to express the seasons and natural beauty of Japan. The chef, Kei Kojima, who studied under Ducasse, creates a healthful, aesthetically pleasing fusion of French and Japanese cuisines. The accent is on seafood and Kamakura vegetables, as beautiful to the eye as to the palate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1666;Tempura Miyashiro;Japan;Tokyo;2-18-11 Kamimeguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0051, Japan;35.641547;139.697277;88;false;false;Tempura;The set menu with its daily changing dishes is a tapestry of artful tempura and more. Naoaki Miyashiro’s menu is bursting with surprises and joy. Abalone is made into shabu-shabu in liver broth. Leftover broth is added to rice tempura and served as seasoned rice gruel. To wrap up the meal, ‘Tenbara’ is served, rice cooked with tomatoes and topped with kakiage (all-in-one seafood and vegetable tempura blend). The chef applies skills learned in Japanese cooking to add flair to his dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1667;Simplicité;Japan;Tokyo;2-17-13 Ebisunishi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0021, Japan;35.649073;139.705412;35;true;true;French;Chef Kaoru Aihara weaves culinary creations with hints of the sea, drawn from his experiences in the Shonan region of Kanagawa Prefecture and the Brittany region of France. Seafood charcuterie substitutes mackerel for ham and sardine for fromage de tête. Depending on the fish, ingredients may be aged for weeks to bring out their flavour. From the seaweed sauce wafts the briny tang of the sea.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1669;L'ARGENT;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Tokyo Club Bldg, 3-2-6 Kasumigaseki, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0013, Japan;35.670573;139.746524;59;true;true;French;Applying experience in Paris and Copenhagen, the chef layers Scandinavian innovation on top of Japanese ingredients and the French classics. Embodying these influences is ‘Fermented mushrooms’: mushrooms sourced from the chef’s native Shizuoka are fermented and paired with poached eggs. After dinner, baked sweets made with Kakegawa tea grown by his relatives are served. Boundlessly creative modern French cuisine is interwoven with the chef’s roots.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1670;Aroma Fresca;Japan;Tokyo;12F, 2-6-5 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.673665;139.767142;86;false;false;Italian;Italian as only Japan can do, with the spotlight squarely on Japan-sourced ingredients. Shinji Harada creates a cuisine from the interplay of his own sensibilities and experience. Only seasonal ingredients are used, as in the pasta of bamboo shoots and matsutake mushrooms or herb-steamed conger eel. Using traditional cooking methods, Harada expresses the flavours of the season with freewheeling creativity. The restaurant’s name, which means ‘the aroma of freshness’, encapsulates the importance of great ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
1671;Kabi;Japan;Tokyo;4-10-8 Meguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0063, Japan;35.631436;139.703861;71;false;false;Innovative;After studying the wonders of fermentation in Denmark, Chef Shohei Yasuda set out to adapt it into a culinary style of his own that would find favour in Japan. From a foundation of miso, pickles and other fermented products, Yasuda dreams up an assortment of creative dishes. Oils and powders extracted from vegetables and fruits are used to add flavour and texture. In true Japanese style, the set menu ends with a rice gruel filled with a range of ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1672;Miyasaka;Japan;Tokyo;5-4-30 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.662464;139.714216;35;true;true;Japanese;Nobuhisa Miyasaka opened his restaurant in quiet Minami-Aoyama. The interior, with touches of the sukiya style of tea arbours, enfolds the visitor in elegance. Miyasaka was deeply moved by the spirit of the tea ceremony when he lived in Kyoto, and the bowls of stew, starter dishes and appetiser platters in his menu express the essence of tea culture. The soul of graceful hospitality lives in rice served the instant it is fully steamed and the matcha tea prepared by the host.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1674;Seiju;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-16-9 Tsukiji, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0045, Japan;35.666294;139.771164;83;true;true;Tempura;The austere, quiet refinement of the interior instils a feeling of peace. Yoshiaki Shimizu’s passion for tempura is inherited from the style of his mentor. Sparingly battered foodstuffs are fried in freshly pressed sesame oil to bring out their flavours. Two tiger prawns are served in succession, the first to convey the sweetness of the shrimp, the second, served almost raw, to highlight the difference in flavour. Pairing tempura with French wine is another unique touch.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1676;Towa;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 4-11-25 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.659233;139.722303;82;true;false;Japanese;Wagyu beef is the star of this gastronomical show. From the opening decoratively arranged sashimi to simmered items, the chef keeps flavours light, hewing closely to Japanese traditions. From the oxtail spring rolls that follow, the restaurant becomes a wagyu kappo. Tongue and tenderloin are char-grilled, accompanied by seasonal vegetables for a splash of colour. The eye is drawn to the takiawase of oxtail soup and soup stock. Aubergine in summer and Kyoto yam in winter complete an idiosyncratic cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1679;au deco;Japan;Tokyo;2-23-3 Ebisu, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0013, Japan;35.647632;139.720263;55;false;true;French;À la carte dishes and well-aged spirits hark back to the basics of the French restaurant. Terrine, consommé and lamb baked over fragrant grass are prepared as in years gone by. Crab baked in pie filling is an original recipe for a French classic. Forging a connection with wine, sauces are prepared with generous amounts of brandy or well cured sake. Working smoothly in sync, staff serve aged wines to guests’ tastes in a scene from the good old days.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1680;Nishiazabu Noguchi;Japan;Tokyo;1-10-16 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661435;139.724218;63;false;false;Japanese;Honest cooking that respects its ingredients testifies to Shotaro Noguchi’s reverence for the food of Japan. Examples include peony-shaped pike conger sprinkled with kudzu starch and served in soup, and white tilefish seasoned with sake and steamed. To wrap up, two types of rice in earthenware pots are served, one containing freshly cooked white rice and the other a seasonal takikomi gohan – rice with a variety of ingredients. These final dishes bring the seasonal aromas of Gumma, the native prefecture of Shotaro’s wife.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1682;Akiyama;Japan;Tokyo;6-5-3 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.644452;139.724801;34;false;true;Japanese;The gentle disposition of owner-chef Hideto Akiyama pervades the menu and his attentive and quick-witted flow of service is part of the appeal. For guests who prefer to drink, he offers snacks, while he provides a wider variety of dishes to guests who are here to dine. Dishes are generously accompanied by marinated tuna, beef simmered in soy sauce and mirin, and dried young sardines seasoned with soy and Japanese pepper. White rice cooked in earthenware pots closes out the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1683;Tempura Maehira;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 2-8-16 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.655644;139.733863;19;false;true;Tempura;Tomokazu Maehira’s interpretation of tempura does not begin with shrimp, but with the light, plain flavours of icefish and squid. Bundled broad beans and snow peas offer plumpness, while burdock and bamboo shoots bring a pleasing firmness, and sea urchins a creamy touch. The alternation of light and rich flavours and textures are well thought out. Maehira follows the three stages of mastery: the fundamentals, followed by breaking with tradition, then creating one’s own techniques.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1685;Guchokuni;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 4-3 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.701579;139.740034;51;false;true;Japanese;Guchokuni means ‘in simple honesty’, a phrase handed down from the chef’s two mentors. It is the favourite motto of the chef, expressing his no-nonsense approach to cuisine. A unique perspective on food preparation can be seen in the soup dishes. Crab dumplings are fashioned with generous amounts of crab. Fried items coated with rice crackers impart a fragrant aroma to dashi soup stock. Pureed soup made from vegetables in season is pure in flavour. A menu founded on a patiently built foundation and finely honed sensibility.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1686;Kappo Muroi;Japan;Tokyo;2-16-4 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661741;139.720819;57;true;true;Japanese;The name is an homage to the chef’s father, who ran a kappo before him. As an apprentice, the chef studied venerable techniques in Kyoto before being in initiated into more advanced approaches at a restaurant in Tokyo. Rice served at the perfect moment of steaming and the soup-based dishes attests to the chef’s respect for the classics. Desiring freedom and novelty, he does not offer sashimi. New and old alternate on the menu, creating an expression that is Kappo Muroi’s own. Temperature and aroma are prized above all, and careful attention is paid to alternation between cold and hot. Fragrant oolong tea draws the meal to a close.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1687;Yotsuya Minemura;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-21 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.688613;139.722947;46;false;true;Japanese;The menu at this intimate counter kappo gives free rein to the skills and experience the chef acquired as an apprentice. The omakase set meal is a medley of sushi, soba noodles and other Japanese dishes. Graceful soup dishes and decoratively arranged sashimi are served, then steamed seafood sushi, and the meal ends with handmade 100% buckwheat soba. In an intriguing touch, a rolled omelette, created as a sushi artist would, is served as dessert. Culinary variety to entice any diner.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1688;hortensia;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-5-12 Shintomi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0041, Japan;35.672436;139.772791;16;false;false;French, French Contemporary;The themes here are richness and flavours. The flavour of kombu kelp is added to soup stock and other ingredients, creating culinary synergies. The chef’s approach is to focus on the foods of Japan and enhance their creativity. The cuisine weaves together the ‘three harmonies’: harmony with the changing of the seasons, harmony of flavours and gentleness of flavours. Presentation is colourful, flavours light. Traditional craftworks are used for serving vessels and cutlery, proclaiming the culture of Japan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1690;PRIMO PASSO;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-5-11 Tsukiji, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0045, Japan;35.670168;139.771646;97;true;false;Italian;The name ‘Primo Passo’ means ‘first step’. The chef was in charge of pasta at the celebrated Quattro Passi restaurant in Naples before taking his first step towards independence in Shintomicho. His aim is to create ‘Italian cuisine with a Japanese twist’. He uses plenty of dashi and Japanese ingredients. Also incorporating Japanese elements are the coffered ceiling, mud walls and vertically written menu. He serves several small dishes featuring his speciality pasta to showcase a variety of flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1693;Sorahana;Japan;Tokyo;5-3-3 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.662679;139.744266;74;true;false;Japanese;To suggest a closeness to nature, Kanako Wakimoto named her restaurant Sorahana, ‘Sky Flower’. Raised amid the good earth and spreading fields, she reflects the changing of the seasons in her cooking. Appetisers are brightly adorned with flowers and leaves, very much as if the sky were in bloom. Tender flavours lovingly prepared bring a smile to the face. The sheer extravagance of the choices of beef dishes, rice dishes and desserts attests to the chef’s devotion.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1695;MONOLITH;Japan;Tokyo;2-6-1 Shibuya, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0002, Japan;35.660049;139.708365;65;true;false;French;Go Ishii made his way to France in the 1990s. There he experienced a new French cuisine, cultivated by fusing classic cooking with the food cultures of various countries. Chef Ishii calls his approach ‘Neo Classic’ for this reason. His speciality of ‘Monolith Egg’ is a study in contrasts between salty and sweet, hot and cold. His eternal standard is constant creativity. The pie pastry dishes, a legacy of the classics, are recommended but require reservations.;Air conditioning;[]
1697;Nishiazabu Otake;Japan;Tokyo;1-4-23 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661503;139.723895;30;false;false;Japanese;Chef Tatsuya Otake takes Japanese cuisine a step outside its comfort zone, determined to find flavours his customers will find delicious. Croquettes prepared with edamame and porcini mushrooms are his masterpiece. Inaniwa udon with firefly squid, and plum and abalone risotto suggest inspiration from Italian cuisine. Edible wild plants and game meats arrive from Gifu, the prefecture of Otake’s apprenticeship. In a lesson learned from his mentor, he treasures his relationships with producers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1698;Nishiazabu Sushi Shin;Japan;Tokyo;4-18-20 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.658327;139.718789;80;false;false;Sushi;Shintaro Suzuki is a self-taught master of sushi who plunged deep into Tokyo-style sushi traditions to discover his own path in the sushi realm. For different ingredients, he uses different soy sauces, such as onion- or plum-flavoured. The battleship sushi with its two types of sea urchin is an impressive sight. For the true sushi artisan, the path of constant self-improvement never ends. It is a road of progress and experimentation built on respect for proper practices.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1699;CRAFTALE;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-16-11 Aobadai, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0042, Japan;35.647362;139.696486;53;false;true;French;The names of producers the chef deals with are listed on the menu. He visits his suppliers, building bonds of trust with farmers and fishermen. The chef brings each dish fresh from kitchen to table and describes it with enthusiasm, building a bridge linking food, guests and restaurant. Prix fixe meals are modern in preparation while classic in concept. A unique touch is that different breads are paired with different dishes, pursuing unity of flavour between the two.;Air conditioning;[]
1700;SHIGEMATSU;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 6-5-6 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670936;139.761862;92;true;true;Japanese;Shigeyuki Matsubara layers flavour upon flavour to draw out the individuality of each dish. He creates his sharply flavoursome dashi through extravagant use of dried bonito and tuna shavings. White miso is added to lightly deep-fried oysters and lotus-root dumplings are enriched with beef, creating multi-layered flavour profiles. Matsubara handled the design of the restaurant himself and the original imagination of the chef completes both the cuisine and the interior.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1701;abysse;Japan;Tokyo;1-30-12 Ebisunishi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0021, Japan;35.648478;139.705688;87;false;false;French, Contemporary;Chef Kotaro Meguro draws on the character of Japan and his theme is ‘ocean and forest’ and their connection within nature. The pure water of rural hills forms rivers, irrigating the land as they flow into the sea and begin the cycle anew: he expresses this providence in his cooking. Bounty of sea and mountain are intermingled on a single plate, a blend of the foods of water and soil. Meat is forgotten in favour of a celebration of seafoods and good things gathered from the forest.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1702;Sumibikappo SHIROSAKA;Japan;Tokyo;6-3-9 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.670722;139.735674;45;true;true;Japanese;When overseas to sharpen his culinary senses, char-grilling caught owner-chef Hideki Ii’s attention. He cooks seasonal ingredients on low heat, using bincho charcoal for fragrance. He mixes modern culinary theory with traditional techniques, with flexible combinations of ingredients that show off his experience. A fine example is the Cold Tuna and Uni, served with gelatinised dashi and caviar. Ii’s deportment and style in the kitchen inspire confidence.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1703;itsuka;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-14-15 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.670272;139.720168;66;false;false;Chinese;At its core, itsuka is all about affection for the seasons and ‘Chinese cooking as only Japan can do it’. Sourcing foodstuffs grown or raised in Japan, it serves set menus only. The fare is firmly grounded in Sichuan cuisine, but to keep the focus on the ingredients, seasoning is used sparingly. Steamed and stir-fried offerings are prepared with fermented vegetables to top up the flavours. The meal wraps up with a single dish, selected from among items such as dandan noodles, hot-and-sour noodles and hotpot soup noodles.;Air conditioning;[]
1704;Seisoka;Japan;Tokyo;4-2-34 Minamiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0047, Japan;35.64751;139.724008;41;true;false;Japanese;The name means ‘a tranquil space surrounded by lush greenery’. It conveys the richness of Japanese culture, which cherishes the beauty of the changing seasons. Featuring vibrant vegetable and seafood delicacies, the menu reflects the emotions of each season in both presentation and tableware. By serving shojin ryori, the vegetarian cuisine developed by Zen monks, the restaurant aims to preserve ancient culinary tradition. It values its connection to the Zen-sect Tengenji Temple, as it is located in the grounds.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1705;Édition Koji Shimomura;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Roppongi T-Cube, 3-1-1 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.66558;139.738152;62;true;false;French;It is now a quarter-century since Koji Shimomura returned to Japan from France. As someone who has travelled with French cuisine through many transitions, he is a firm proponent of going “forwards and deeper”. He seeks out new ingredients with which to create original cuisine and goes deeper by constantly tinkering with his long-standing specialities, deepening his knowledge and skill. Each new edition impresses, keeping an eye on the horizon while respecting the classics.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1706;Sushi Matsuura;Japan;Tokyo;5-7-8 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.644639;139.727818;33;false;false;Sushi;The stage is a sushi shop and as the curtain rises, instead of his business card the chef offers a negitoro roll (minced tuna with green onion leaves), presented by hand. Sushi rolls of monkfish liver and dried gourd strips are served with sweet, thick kijoshu (sake brewed with sake not water), taking a hint from pairings of foie gras with botrytised wine. All three key requisites of a good sushi shop are present: watchfulness, consideration and smiles. No wonder this performance is so well attended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1707;Ren Mishina;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 7-3-13 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670115;139.760066;92;false;true;Japanese;True to his creed, ‘Life resides in cooking that is free of affectation’, the chef strives to serve food that is honest and down-to-earth. Paying close attention to the strength of his cooking flame, he sources the flavours of each season—bamboo shoots, pike conger, matsutake mushrooms, and puffer fish—and slow-cooks them over charcoal. Indian-ink paintings behind the counter depict lotuses in each season. In the language of flowers, the lotus represents a pure and chaste spirit. The chef’s honesty and respect for foodstuffs are reflected in his carefully pared-down creations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1708;Shimbashi Sasada;Japan;Tokyo;1-23-7 Nishishimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0003, Japan;35.668147;139.751571;50;false;true;Japanese;With his expertise refined at a Kyoto cuisine restaurant, the chef emphasises seasonal ingredients, showcasing his experience in dishes that highlight their finest qualities. He starts with delicacies and aemono appetisers designed to enhance the enjoyment of sake. The warm boiled wild mustard greens with deep-fried tofu is a Sasada speciality perfected over many years. All the dishes are carefully prepared with a focus on simplicity, showcasing the chef’s humble personality and dedication to his craft.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1709;Ginza L’écrin;Japan;Tokyo;4-5-5 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671863;139.765499;72;true;false;French;Orthodox French cuisine as guarded by successive generations of head chefs since 1974. The absence of a long-established menu enables Chef Yuhei Kurita to evolve with the times. The eighth head chef of L’écrin values his sauces, striving for the perfect wine pairings. In keeping with the restaurant’s name, which means ‘jewel box’, a wooden box is presented at the end of the meal – lift the lid and you’ll find little cakes and bonbons, shining like jewels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1710;Daigo;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Forest Tower, 2-3-1 Atago, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0002, Japan;35.66344;139.749184;25;false;false;Shojin;Being originally located in the grounds of Seishoji Temple is why Daigo began serving shojin ryori. What Nomura inherits as the restaurant’s fourth-generation owner is shojin ryori for gracious service. Note that dried bonito flakes are used in the broth, so the meals are not completely vegetarian. The nutrition and flavour of the vegetables and the sukiya architecture put the mind at ease. Relax and enjoy this moment of tranquillity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed;[]
1711;Series;Japan;Tokyo;3-4-11 Azabudai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0041, Japan;35.660599;139.738995;57;false;true;Chinese;Service consists of many dishes in small quantities, hence the name. Creativity abounds, inspired by ingredients and preparation methods from numerous countries. Steamed spicy beef rather than chicken, chicken-wings stuffed with foie gras, and Peking duck wrapped in kadaif pastry show off Series’ talent for arrangement. To accentuate the variety of culinary styles, pairings range widely as well. Pair wine, sake or a cocktail with your meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1712;Héritage by Kei Kobayashi;Japan;Tokyo;45F, The Ritz-Carlton, Tokyo 9-7-1 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-6245, Japan;35.665937;139.731182;81;true;false;French, French Contemporary;‘Héritage by Kei Kobayashi’ is not just a name: The chef has made it his mission to honour and give thanks to the French culinary culture and pass it on to future generations through his eponymous restaurant. Venerable standards such as pâté en croûte, roast dovelet and vacherin are prepared in the traditional way but given a modern arrangement. Homage to the classics and the hospitality of the hotel combine to open new horizons in gastronomy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
1713;Sushi Kojima;Japan;Tokyo;5F, 7-3-8 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670147;139.760576;19;true;true;Sushi;Michio Kojima describes himself as a sushi artisan with a 20th century Showa-era mentality. As such, he prepares sushi with fish floss sandwiched between rice and either a gizzard shad or tiger prawn topping and makes tamago-yaki with Shiba shrimp broth. By visiting Toyosu market every morning, he has built a relationship with wholesalers. Testament to this is his selection of first catch produce, such as very young gizzard shad, which are at the apex of the sushi fish hierarchy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1714;Azabujuban Fukuda;Japan;Tokyo;3-7-5 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.653614;139.735082;42;false;true;Japanese;A menu redolent with seasonal aromas and the kind hospitality of the couple in charge are the true charms of Azabujuban Fukuda. Katsuo-bushi (dried bonito flakes) is shredded, dashi drawn and seafood chopped in front of customers. Kazuto Fukuda uses ingredients from every corner of Japan. In spring, hatsu gatsuo (first bonito of the season) is grilled wrapped in straw. Unagi is smothered in mizansho (green peppercorn). Seasonal clay-pot rice dishes bring the meal to a close.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1715;Les Saisons;Japan;Tokyo;MF, Main Bldg, Imperial Hotel Tokyo, 1-1-1 Uchisaiwaicho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-8558, Japan;35.672455;139.758435;100;false;false;French;Thierry Voisin brings traditional French cuisine in line with the Japanese milieu. Since coming to Japan, he has come to appreciate the rich array of ingredients available here and the importance given to seasonality in cuisine. Inspired by those ingredients, he comes up with dishes that display his sensibilities. Kombu and katsuo-bushi play a role in his creative preparations. Enjoy a fusion of Japanese and French cuisine in a classical dining room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1716;Chugoku Hanten Fureika;Japan;Tokyo;3-7-5 Higashiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0044, Japan;35.656219;139.73846;39;true;true;Chinese;The house boasts two kitchens, one for Shanghainese and the other for Cantonese cooking, each overseen by a dedicated chef. A rôttiseur is in charge of the roasted pork fillet, a dim sum master for steamed buns and gyoza dumplings, each preparing their specialities in the authentic style. The menu ranges from familiar vegetables to dishes using luxury ingredients, along with several creative items. At lunch, the dim sum set and the à la carte menu are both recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1717;Sushi Ryujiro;Japan;Tokyo;2-11-11 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.671287;139.720882;100;true;false;Sushi;Ryujiro Nakamura’ open-hearted character keeps the mood bright in this vibrant, full of laughter restaurant. The fish is flavoursome, the staff youthful and energetic. Rice is seasoned with red vinegar made from sake lees to keep the focus on the tuna. The omakase is original in presentation yet respectful of the traditions taught by his mentor. It begins with nigiri sushi of medium-fatty tuna and ends with soup stock-flavoured thick omelette roll. A good beginning and an end are vital in all things.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1718;FUSHIKINO;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 4-3-11 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.701993;139.740033;25;false;false;Japanese;‘Fushikino’ is a mashup of two words, one referring to a Zen phrase, and the other meaning ‘mysterious’. Together, they suggest things that never before existed. The restaurant’s aim is to create something unprecedented, an unexpected culinary experience made possible through the trinity of food, sake and utensils. The menu lists familiar items of Japanese cuisine, but one-of-a-kind touches manifest in subtle details, such as onion soy sauce and aged ponzu sauce. Drink pairings of one cup per dish, served in sake cups lovingly produced by modern artists, are an entertaining grace note.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
1719;Sushi Masashi;Japan;Tokyo;7F, 2-9-9 Kitaaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0061, Japan;35.671398;139.716725;95;false;true;Sushi;Masashi Yamaguchi says he wants a sushi meal to tell an enjoyable story, with a beginning, twists and turns, and an ending. In his training, he learned how to vary the tempo of sushi using sweet and sour and hot and cold toppings. Taking classic techniques, he has further developed his own style. For example, he marinates the kobujime in kombu dashi and adds flavour to get a soft texture. His originality can be seen, too, in snacks like the tuna sukiyaki.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1721;GINZA OKUDA;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 5-4-8 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671401;139.763076;94;true;true;Japanese;The menu emphasises the season and textures of the ingredients. In spring, razor clams and wild vegetables are made into ohitashi to represent the breath of life. Chargrilled items are the speciality, with unagi from Lake Biwa and ayu from the Tenryugawa River in summer and matsutake wrapped in straw in the autumn. Winter dishes include buri shabu-shabu and crab with rice cooked in an earthenware pot. Each dish showcases the flavours of the ingredients without affectation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1722;Kaiseki Komuro;Japan;Tokyo;35-4 Wakamiyacho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0827, Japan;35.699468;139.738271;30;false;true;Japanese;Mitsuhiro Komuro’s dishes are hearty and beautiful to behold, arrayed on a menu with generous amounts of ingredients from sea, farm and forest. Hassun appetisers delight the eye, celebrating the seasons and the vessels they’re served on. The bones of pike conger and conger eel are finely cut in an entertaining performance, then the flesh is char-grilled. Delightfully rustic elements such as pepper flowers, boar and wild duck enliven hot-pot cooking. The playful spirit and uniquely flowing oratory of the owner-chef, on display in his elegant kitchen, makes every flavour taste even better.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1723;Edomae Shinsaku;Japan;Tokyo;6F, 2-10-11 Nihombashiningyocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0013, Japan;35.685565;139.783986;22;true;true;Tempura;This tempura is the product of research on the theories of steaming, desiccation and roasting. Fish are rested to remove moisture and concentrate umami. Low-temperature frying is adopted to desiccate the pieces. Batter is made fragrant and dark brown through the Maillard reaction, resulting in tempura that seems somehow more grilled than fried. Uniquely, each piece is placed before the guest by hand, as in a sushi shop. The quest for ever-better technique is Edomae Shinsaku’s path to uniqueness.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1724;Oniku Karyu;Japan;Tokyo;7F, 1-14-6 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.672997;139.769792;100;false;false;Beef;Haruka Katayanagi’s love of beef fairly tumbles from a menu sure to tickle the fancy of Black wagyu beef lovers. The presentation of char-grilled chateaubriand sets the mood. The kaiseki does full justice to wagyu irrespective of genre, as sushi, stew and cutlet sandwiches are all on offer. In combination with sea urchin and abalone, it is a taste of luxury. As the beef cuisine brings smiles to guests’ faces, the flawless service of the owner-chef and Team Karyu is a joy to behold.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1726;L'ATELIER de Joël Robuchon;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Roppongi Hills Hillside, 6-10-1 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.6604;139.729046;89;true;false;French, Contemporary;Red and black are the thematic colours of L’ATELIER de Joël Robuchon. The classic Robuchon menu spins a tale like a 19th-century French novel. The menu ranges from famous specialities of years gone by to new arrangements incorporating seasonal Japanese ingredients. This really is ‘Joël Robuchon’s atelier’, where the genius honed his concept of French gastronomy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1727;Sincère;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-7-13 Sendagaya, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0051, Japan;35.676969;139.704359;93;false;false;French;Chef Shinsuke Ishii brings the passion of the producers to your table with his unique recipes. Using underutilised fish species and local ingredients, he passionately conveys human connections. The fish wrapped in pie pastry, resembling taiyaki, hides a playful twist within its sophistication. The chef personally serves his creations, and the whole team unites to engage with guests. The dining experience is filled with energy and a sense of togetherness.;Air conditioning;[]
1728;Yakitori Takahashi;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-10-11 Nihombashi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0027, Japan;35.680982;139.774542;17;false;true;Yakitori;A man of few words, the chef fixes his attention on his grill. He focuses on every detail of yakitori—the state of the charcoal, how the skewers are assembled and grilled—pursuing the subtleties of a cuisine. His favoured type of chicken is game fowl, prized for its supple texture and rich flavour. It is seasoned with a salt base and modulated with added chicken fat or vinegar, then wreathed in smoke as it cooks on the grill. Skewers are interspersed with chicken-based snacks such as cold chicken breast and mincemeat potato salad. A procession of dishes of lively originality.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1729;Sanosushi;Japan;Tokyo;2-18-9 Shiba, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0014, Japan;35.65158;139.75071;26;true;false;Sushi;From the outset, the chef resolved to create an old school sushi restaurant. The no-nonsense shop name, the big, bold sign and the wooden menu board hung on the wall all hark back to the sushi shops of old. The sloping counter with a groove along one side prevents soy sauce spillage—an idea from his mentor. Sushi rice is slightly sour and generously portioned, toppings thick, like in the good old days. Tuna, as a star topping, is served with great care in sets of three nigiri.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1730;Torakuro;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, Imperial Hotel Tokyo Main, 1-1-1 Uchisaiwaicho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-8558, Japan;35.6723;139.75837;41;false;true;Japanese;‘Tradition and innovation always travel together’ is the credo of the Imperial Hotel. ‘Growth and happiness for the future’ is the motto of the Ishikawa Group. Together the partners founded Torakuro, whose cuisine is guided by both convictions. French techniques such as consommé and confit are overlaid with Japanese traditions like dashi soup stock and char-grilling. One of the Imperial Hotel’s founders, Eiichi Shibusawa, once said, ‘Serve the customer courteously and you create a memory for a lifetime’. Here, that spirit is taken to heart.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
1732;NéMo;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 6-15-4 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.659492;139.714261;58;true;true;French;As a boy, Chef Kenichi Nemoto was an enthusiastic angler, and seafood is the focus of the prix fixe menus he arranges. To ensure variety, Nemoto varies his preparation styles: frites, soups, butter roasting, and so on. In gratitude to the natural world of sea and mountain where he encounters his ingredients, he wastes nothing. The chef is earnest in his relations with producers, such as building bonds of trust with the fishermen of Shimoda.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1736;Ginza Kitagawa;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 2-10-11 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.672032;139.768331;93;true;false;Japanese;A sister establishment of Ginza Shinohara, Ginza Kitagawa was opened to explore the subtleties of Japanese cuisine. Extensive discussions with tempura masters persuaded the restaurant to focus on fried foods. Tempura and quick-fried sashimi are incorporated in the menu, creating a unique twist. Instead of takikomi-gohan, rice mixed with kakiage of the season is served. Under the watchful gaze of chef Kazuyuki Kitagawa, a crew of young cooks combine knowledge and skill to proclaim a new Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1737;amarantos;Japan;Tokyo;9F, 5-6-7 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.67096;139.763905;74;false;true;French, Contemporary;This restaurant is currently closed due to relocation in March. The chef’s experience as a pâtissier is put to good use as he fuses a medley of ingredients into a harmonious whole. Guests watch with rapt attention as he works his kitchen and serves each item directly. As guests tuck into their meals with expressions of delight and exclamations of ‘Delicious!’, his joy is tangible. The true pleasure of countertop French dining.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1738;PRUNIER;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Tokyo Kaikan, 3-2-1 Marunouchi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0005, Japan;35.677638;139.761455;58;false;false;French;PRUNIER is the main dining room of Tokyo Kaikan, a meeting-place cherished for generations. The décor conjures images of fish and flowing water, harking back to the restaurant’s earliest days when it specialised in seafood. Here you can enjoy modern French cuisine that reflects the shifting seasons, presented in an elegant setting. Sole bonne femme, handed down from generations of head chefs, keeps a tradition alive and well. Gracious service adds an extra touch to the meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1741;Nishiazabu Taku;Japan;Tokyo;2-11-5 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661308;139.722356;72;false;false;Sushi;Back when there weren’t many sushi restaurants in Nishi-Azabu, the chef was determined to blaze a trail here. And ‘blaze a trail’ is basically what Taku means. The same trailblazing was what led him to be among the first sushi chefs to hire a sommelier, and to spread sushi culture in Hawaii. The variety of his omakase set meals, which start at 30 items, is eye-popping. Nigiri items alternate with drinking snacks. Sushi rice may be seasoned with white or red vinegar, depending on the fish topping—another trailblazing move.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1743;Akanezaka Onuma;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 3-12-2 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.674046;139.737891;80;false;false;Japanese;Mitsuharu Onuma respects the fundamentals of Japanese cooking while reflecting his unique take on it in his menus. The meal starts with fried tofu in season—‘in season’ because the tofu is steeped in seasonal aromas such as sakura shrimp, chestnut and Horikawa burdock. Hand-made soba is served in a chilled broth as an amuse-bouche. Vegetables, fruits and mushrooms raised by his parents in Yamagata are used in appetisers and sweet dishes. This cuisine is supported by the ingredients of Onuma’s birthplace and the bonds of family.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1744;Sushiya Shota;Japan;Tokyo;3-3-10 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.653613;139.735547;66;false;true;Sushi;The South Korea-born chef is in love with the traditions of Tokyo and the skill and sophistication of the city’s artisans. From behind the counter he welcomes guests in a lusty voice, softening the mood with casual conversation. The chef varies his technique based on the characteristics of each fish, and seasons his sushi rice with red vinegar and salt. To encourage guests to sample as many toppings as possible, his omakase set menus are weighted heavily toward nigiri. He respects the teachings of his mentor while not skipping a single detail, and his sushi shows it.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1745;Tanimoto;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 3-1 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.702223;139.741046;36;true;true;Japanese;Amid the refinement of a dignified tea arbour, the chef cooks with sincere devotion. His attentiveness derives from his early work at a ryotei, where he was a doorman in charge of footwear   . Tanimoto’s forte is charcoal grilling, preparing each ingredient with the strictest attention. The meal ends with a generous lineup of various rice dishes including, white rice, takikomi-gohan and chazuke, followed by tea poured by the chef himself. The spirit of graceful service brings satisfaction to the depths of the soul.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1749;Okamoto;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 5-2-8 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.6626169;139.7445216;64;false;false;Japanese;A chef’s work, says Hidetsugu Okamoto, is a process of tinkering to create something more elaborate, which is why he does not serve decoratively arranged sashimi. Soba with salted and dried grey mullet roe is paired with roasted buckwheat seeds. Pepper-flower hotpot offers a taste comparison between pork and beef, an improvement on a dish learned in his apprenticeship. He likes to serve Okayama flavours such as sardinella, eel and Spanish mackerel on Bizen-ware dishes.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
1750;Mētis Roppongi;Japan;Tokyo;5-18-22 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.661115;139.736965;89;true;false;French;This French restaurant with counter service exemplifies ‘Wakon Yosai’ - ‘Japanese spirit with Western learning’. In the kitchen, the chef works the blazing wood fire with the skills he honed in Paris to fashion a harmonious blend of French cuisine with Japanese ingredients and wood-fire cooking. Seafood is wreathed in smoky fragrances, wagyu beef swaddled in flavour from the wood flame and steam. He finds clever ways to expand the possibilities of Japanese ingredients, by for example using sake lees in sauces.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1751;JO;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-24-14 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.660082;139.722546;31;false;false;Beef;Chef Jotaro Okubo uses beef from a breed with longer fattening period than ordinary kuroge wagyu, prized for the dense flavour of its red meat. Billing itself as a ‘meat kappo,’ the restaurant serves up a medley of beef cuts in the manner of a kaiseki feast. The variety is impressive: beef aitchbone and seafood on a small bowl of rice, spring rolls of dry-cured beef ham, sirloin shabu-shabu. Taste the wonders of beef through the imagination of Jotaro Okubo.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1752;L'AFFINAGE;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 5-9-16 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670183;139.764948;32;false;true;French;Chef Yasuyuki Takara was most influenced by Paul Bocuse during his training in France. He was impressed by how the distinguished chef would stay at the restaurant longer than anyone else. He also travelled to various regions to study local cuisine and wines. His speciality is ‘pavé de foie gras’, inspired by the pavers on Azuma-dori in front of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1753;Oryori Tsuji;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-3-9 Higashiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0044, Japan;35.657034;139.738844;95;true;false;Japanese;Yoshiaki Tsuji’s food service reveres the classics. Food is arranged on antique dishes, including plenty of appetiser platters to celebrate the seasons. A light touch with the seasonings shows respect for ingredients. An appearance of rustic, tea-house simplicity sets the heart at ease, with adze-hewn ceilings, cypress counters, carefully finished earthen walls, private rooms with inner gardens, and its basement location put to good use.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1754;Nodaiwa Azabu Iikura Honten;Japan;Tokyo;1-5-4 Higashiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0044, Japan;35.6581;139.743352;98;false;false;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;5th-generation Kanejiro Kanemoto keeps alive the family culinary legacy. Having started helping out at the restaurant as a boy, he has devoted himself to unagi for over 80 years. While hewing closely to Edo grilling styles, he doesn’t forget to add a twist of his own. Unseasoned broiled unagi dressed with caviar is an inspiration from his days wandering from restaurant to restaurant in Paris. Still working the kitchen today, Kanemoto is a master craftsman who has devoted his life to the grill.;Air conditioning;[]
1755;le sputnik;Japan;Tokyo;7-9-9 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.664392;139.729876;27;false;false;French;The name ‘Sputnik’ recalls the world’s first artificial satellite. It is also the Russian word for ‘fellow traveller’, an image that appeals to Yujiro Takahashi: he is the captain, he says, who guides diners in navigating each course. Takahashi’s life work is the discovery of previously unknown ingredients, creating cuisine that transcends time. Beets and foie gras, arranged like red roses, are a striking innovation. Take a glimpse into the unfamiliar world of his imagination.;Air conditioning;[]
1756;Tenoshima;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-3-21 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.671024;139.725138;53;false;false;Japanese;Tenoshima is named after Teshima, the island where the chef’s father was born. As he wields his skills in the kitchen, he remains conscious of ingredients and techniques deeply rooted on the island. Nyumen, a savoury noodle soup, is prepared with dried sardine broth for a beloved taste of home. Using underused fish species supports both sustainability and the livelihoods of fishermen. Bozushi reflects his experience at Kyoto’s Kikunoi. Driven by the chef’s wealth of experience, Tenoshima is broadening the purview of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1757;Sushidokoro Kiraku;Japan;Tokyo;1-12-12 Kyodo, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 156-0052, Japan;35.650521;139.637221;85;false;false;Sushi;Reading the signs of the times, the third owner transformed this sushi restaurant, once known for its catering, into an omakase spot serving appetizers and nigiri. Despite the modern shift, traditional Edomae techniques like ageing, marinating, and curing the fish remain unchanged. The friendly chef creates a welcoming atmosphere, while his wife skilfully handles the grilled dishes. With meticulous craftsmanship and reasonable prices, it’s easy to see why this place is a local favourite.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1759;Il Ristorante - Niko Romito;Japan;Tokyo;40F, Bvlgari Hotel Tokyo, 2-2-1 Yaesu, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0028, Japan;35.67962;139.769211;70;false;false;Italian;Contemporary dining in the Bvlgari style. The wall, evoking the sunset in Rome, is bedecked with portraits of actresses that made Bvlgari famous. Mauro Aloisio runs the kitchen in strict adherence to the culinary philosophy of supervisor Niko Romito, the eminent chef. Simple yet richly flavourful dishes deliver authentic Italian tastes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1760;Yakumo Uezu;Japan;Tokyo;1-3-9 Yakumo, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 152-0023, Japan;35.618768;139.67426;56;false;false;Japanese;The chef draws on a deep well of ideas to conjure delightful surprises. His philosophy is one of constant advancement, as witnessed in his adoption of Western ingredients such as caviar and truffles and the development of unwritten recipes. Sashimi is seasoned individually and, true to his Okinawa pedigree, he marinates beef in Miyako miso and brown sugar. Other items include takikomi-gohan (rice dish boiled with various ingredients) and pureed vegetable soup. His free-flying imagination expands the horizons of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1761;CYCLE by Mauro Colagreco;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Otemachi One, 1-2-1 Otemachi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0004, Japan;35.68734;139.76205;83;true;false;French, Contemporary;‘Circular gastronomy’ from the chef of Mirazur in southern France. Prix fixe menus are composed from four themes—roots, leaves, flowers and fruits—expressing the beauty of nature and the cycle that happens in our world. The fare is modern French woven from Japanese ingredients, but it also beguiles with influences from the chef’s native Argentina, such as tapas and asado. Having stretched out his roots in southern France and budded leaves of creativity, the chef has blossomed in Otemachi.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1762;L'ÉTERRE;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-6-53 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.700406;139.739624;15;true;true;French, Contemporary;L’Éterre was opened by Yoshiaki Ito, chef of L’Archeste in Paris’ 16th arrondissement. Ito entrusted the kitchen here to Akira Tagomori, who was Ito’s junior during his apprenticeship. The classic fare is prepared with traditional techniques, making artful use of firewood, charcoal and straw to draw out the purity of the ingredients. Cheesecake and chocolate truffles are desserts served in both the Paris and Tokyo locations. The bond between Ito and Tagomori binds the two cities as well.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1764;Ubuka;Japan;Tokyo;2-14  Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.688643;139.722412;98;true;false;Crab Specialities;The chef opened Ubuka because he liked the idea of a restaurant that specialises in shellfish. The name means ‘first fragrance’, in recognition of the importance of the aroma of foodstuffs. The menu is all about shrimp and crab. Cooking the shellfish alive, Kato displays the prowess he honed at traditional Japanese restaurants in Kyoto. Crab meat has been picked, so is easy for diners to enjoy. The secret ingredient in his famous fried shrimp is his soy-sauce-infused sauce américaine.;Air conditioning;[]
1767;Ginza Kousui;Japan;Tokyo;8F, 6-12-14 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669181;139.764532;23;true;true;Japanese;Delights of hometown cooking and the traditional culture of Japan as told by the Shizuoka-born chef. The counter, fashioned of hinoki cypress from Shimada, is laden with seafood and sake from Suruga Bay. Soy sauce used to dress decoratively arranged sashimi is enhanced with nori seaweed from Lake Hamana to impart flavour and a unique character. The importance placed on annual events reflects the chef’s Kyoto experience. The menu sports original touches, appealing to the eyes as well as the tastebuds.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1768;Gucci Osteria da Massimo Bottura Tokyo;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 6-6-12 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670459;139.762079;94;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;A restaurant supervised by an innovator of the Italian culinary world, Massimo Bottura. In command of the kitchen is Antonio Iacoviello, who left his homeland to start anew in Tokyo. Iacoviello’s cuisine shines out of careful attention to ingredients, from both Italian and Japanese perspectives. “A Parmigiana that Wants to Become a Ramen” is his description of a creation based on eggplant and ramen. The quirky names he appends to his dishes stoke our curiosity.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1769;The House of Dynasties;China Mainland;Beijing;4F, Rosewood Hotel, Jing Guang Centre, Hujialou, 1 Chaoyangmenwai Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.918808;116.454181;40;false;false;Cantonese;Inspired by Dream of the Red Chamber, an 18C Chinese novel, the decor embodies that era's charm. With well-honed skills, the Cantonese chef from Zhanjiang reinvents his hometown favourites, presenting specialities such as double-boiled duck and fish maw soup, jackfruit wood roast pork, and jackfruit puff pastry. Zhanjiang-style sautéed lobster is jazzed up by sand ginger and black beans for a deep caramelised flavour and a mild kick.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1770;Trb Hutong;China Mainland;Beijing;23 Shatan North Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.927966;116.403524;64;false;true;French Contemporary;As it’s hidden within the courtyard of a historic temple, there’s an extra sense of expectation as you walk into this comfortable, contemporary and professionally run dining room. Local, high-quality ingredients are cleverly crafted into polished and refined dishes. There’s a choice of three tasting menus, all of which change according to the season, but all culminate in Le Grand Dessert finale. The plating is striking and the subtle contrasts in tastes and textures are delightful.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1771;Xin Rong Ji (Jianguomenwai Street);China Mainland;Beijing;5F, Tower A, Yintai Centre, 2 Jianguomenwai Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.906171;116.453263;83;true;false;Taizhou;Having started life as a small shop selling seafood dishes, this chain now has branches in most large cities in China. At the heart of the CBD lies its second outpost boasting butler service for diners – reserve a table ahead and pre-order the freshest seafood flown in from Taizhou every day. Besides the famous wild-caught yellow croaker and fried hairtail, also try blanched baby octopus, braised radish slices, and bean noodles in sea anemone soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1772;Ling Long;China Mainland;Beijing;3F, STEY-Sanlitun Hotel, BEI Zhaolong, 2 Gongrentiyuchang North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.931781;116.454401;83;true;true;Innovative;The dining room feels airy, minimal and fresh, with just one wisteria plant as the centrepiece. In the semi-open kitchen, the young head chef with around ten years of experience deftly prepares his seasonally inspired menus, consisting of up to seven artfully plated inventions that taste unmistakably Chinese. Most of the ingredients are sourced locally, including the beef from Shandong, oyster sauce and fermented condiments which are all made in house.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1773;Blackswan;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Luohong Art Museum, 89 Capital Airport Road, Shunyi, Beijing, China Mainland;40.0419149;116.5682626;36;false;true;French Contemporary;In keeping with the name, feather motifs and graceful curves abound in the pristine white room of this restaurant in an idyllic spot overlooking a pond where swans and koi swim. As for the food, the experienced French chef champions a unique take on traditional French cooking using local ingredients. The menu changes every season – the slow-roast wild-caught turbot boasts firm, juicy meat and the two sauces complement its intense ocean flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1774;Gastro Esthetics DaDong;China Mainland;Beijing;1-2F, Nanxincang Business Tower, 22A Dongsi 10th Alley, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9310024;116.4248265;55;false;true;Chinese Contemporary;The Peking duck chain’s flagship in town got a makeover in 2021 and was re-branded as the chain’s most exclusive branch. The signature roast duck only uses 22-day-old birds, and is served with condiments like pancake, cucumber, scallion, minced garlic and bean sauce. Braised sea cucumber is a sensational tour de force – spiny sea cucumber from Kanto, Japan is prepared tableside à la minute. Seasonal seafood and mushroom dishes are also the highlights.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
1775;Lu Style (Anding Road);China Mainland;Beijing;5F, Uni Elite, Building 6, Courtyard 5, Anding Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.977857;116.398637;99;false;false;Shandong;This elegant restaurant has built up a loyal fan base with its friendly service and quality food at affordable price points. Instead of typical Shandong classics, the chef, who hails from the province, champions a menu that prominently features seafood shipped from Weihai port daily. Try the braised sea cucumber with scallion, which takes five days to prepare. Certain items tend to run out early: pre-order your favourites to avoid disappointment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1776;Lei Garden (Jinbao Tower);China Mainland;Beijing;3F, Jinbao Tower, 89 Jinbao Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9109245;116.4133837;92;false;false;Cantonese;Lei Garden hails from Hong Kong and specialises in traditional Cantonese fare. The décor feels festive and joyous. Most ingredients are sourced from their own farm to ensure quality and freshness. The signature roasted pork belly boasts alternate layers of fat and meat, with crispy skin and juicy flesh. Slow-cooked and double-boiled soups are also recommended. Sago and pomelo in mango purée is the perfect end to the meal.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1777;Il Ristorante - Niko Romito;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Bvlgari Hotel, Building 2, Courtyard 8, Xinyuan South Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.947719;116.452232;83;false;false;Italian;This dining concept by Milanese chef Niko Romito is the epitome of Italian luxe. Lit by Murano glass chandeliers and clad in marble, warm wood and leather, the high-ceilinged space overlooks a manicured garden. Classic recipes are given a subtle, modern twist that adds sophistication and depth. Start your meal with vitello tonnato – the thinly sliced veal in a tangy tuna sauce is a classic antipasto, reworked to cater to the modern palate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1778;Forum;China Mainland;Beijing;2F, Empark Prime Hotel, 2 Wangfujing Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9221144;116.4054586;50;true;true;Cantonese;Forum has long been an institution of deluxe Cantonese fare in Hong Kong. Its first outpost in Beijing is helmed by Chef Lee who perfected his skills throughout his career of over 30 years. The menu offers many of the same dishes as its Hong Kong flagship, such as sauteed lobster with crab meat and pigeon egg that boasts velvety texture and briny-sweetness. The signature fried rice packs rich wok hei whereas braised abalones are not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1780;Zhiguan Courtyard;China Mainland;Beijing;12 Jinyu Hutong, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.91405;116.409091;59;false;false;Dongbei;This restaurant, annexed to an art gallery, sports a dining room complete with historical garden views through its floor-to-ceiling windows. Liaoning fisherman’s-style dishes are re-created here, with produce from Changbai Mountains and fish from Bohai Sea and Liao River. Signatures include green willow clams, and stir-fried sea snail with green onion—both flavoursome and full of umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1781;Huaiyang Fu (Dongcheng);China Mainland;Beijing;198 Andingmenwai Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.95238;116.402769;32;false;false;Huaiyang;This period mansion, complete with a stone garden, brick walls and carved wood windows, befits the refinement and subtlety that define this restaurant’s cuisine. Thanks to a renovation, booth seats are the prized spot for a truly comfortable experience. The menu celebrates the greatest hits in Huaiyang cooking, such as braised pork belly in brown sauce and tofu chrysanthemum in matsutake stock. Seasonal offerings like crystal yellow croaker aspic are also worth saving room for.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1782;Cai Yi Xuan;China Mainland;Beijing;2F, Four Seasons Hotel, 48 Liangmaqiao Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.948977;116.461067;82;false;false;Cantonese;Having worked with various teams within the hotel group for years, Chef Li hailing from Tianjin makes sure every top-notch ingredient is prepared meticulously in his kitchen. The main menu focuses on Cantonese fare, but regulars may refer to another menu for popular dishes they miss. Chef Li is especially proud of his signature wok-fried prawns with fermented black garlic and dried chillies. The wine list also features some great selections.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1783;Poetry‧Wine (Dongsanhuan Middle Road);China Mainland;Beijing;61 Dongsanhuan Middle Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.8976898;116.455034;27;false;true;Beijing Cuisine;The bamboo bush, jade ornaments, ink paintings and cut flowers may prime your brain for a hefty price tag, but a meal in this modern restaurant doesn’t break the bank. Its signature braised fish head is juicy and tender, nicely braised in an aromatic brown sauce. Roast duck uses 40-day-old birds that are chargrilled to perfection and plated gorgeously. Always save room for the creamed yam and osmanthus sweet soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1784;In Love (Gongti East Road);China Mainland;Beijing;Next to East 2 Gate, Workers' Sports Complex, Gongrentiyuchang East Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.927315;116.443233;95;false;true;Hunanese;This is a Hunanese restaurant, but its décor easily passes for a modern bistro with sleek furniture and a muted palette, punctuated by lime green banquettes. The same degree of eclecticism is at work on the menu, as the Hunanese chef puts a new spin on the classics. Steamed fish head with pickled chilli duo uses bighead carp shipped daily from Qiandao Lake in Zhejiang. Pre-order this dish alongside others when booking a table.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
1785;Fu Chun Ju;China Mainland;Beijing;3F, The Puxuan Hotel, 1 Wangfujing Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.922423;116.403739;100;false;false;Cantonese;Designed by the German architect Ole Scheeren, this dining room seamlessly blends pared-down modernism with hutong tradition. Imagine circular booths that create an array of semi-private spaces. The experienced head chef from Hong Kong showcases his solid and astute skills in signature dishes like the roast pigeon. The revamped menu includes many items that are available in individual portion sizes, so diners may sample the length and breadth of his repertoire.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1786;MO Jasmine;China Mainland;Beijing;L307, 3F, CP Center, 20 Jinhe East Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9114456;116.4614246;15;true;false;Beijing Cuisine;The dark green façade and warm grey room impart sophisticated taste. The jasmine centrepiece on each table exudes a pleasant scent and befits the restaurant’s name. On the menu, Beijingese melds with Shandong in refined masterpieces that look and taste divine. The signature classic Peking duck can be ordered in individual portions – in addition to pancake, scallion and cucumber, chargrilled duck breast with crispy skin is luxed up with caviar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1787;Giada Garden;China Mainland;Beijing;3F, China World Hotel, 1 Jianguomenwai Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.908687;116.452731;52;false;true;Italian;In line with the image of the fashion brand, the airy, elegant space exudes feminine sensibility with a pale colour scheme and warm neutrals. For a full-on experience, order the set menu and go for classics like veal Milanese or their house-made pastas. The array of freshly baked Italian bread on offer is also amazing and a wide range of quality Italian wines are available by the glass. Service is formal and precise, but not too uptight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1789;Zijin Mansion;China Mainland;Beijing;3F, Waldorf Astoria Hotel, 5-15 Jinyu Hutong, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.916259;116.414122;50;false;false;Cantonese;Though its name means purple and gold, this cosy dining room is clad in hand-embroidered orange fabric on a bird theme. The menu features a fine mix of Cantonese classics and bold creations, thanks to the head chef’s globetrotting background. The must-try goldfish shrimp dumplings taste as good as they look. Lotus root puff pastry with turnip filling is flaky, flavourful and exquisitely crafted. Wine buffs should check out the cellar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1790;Xin Rong Ji (Jinrong Street);China Mainland;Beijing;B1 Level, Financial Street International Hotel, 11 Jinrong Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.917499;116.353313;75;true;true;Taizhou;This is the first Beijing branch of the Taizhou brand famous for its fresh seafood shipped from the East China Sea daily. The dimly lit dining room dotted with bird cages and other Chinese motifs feels chic and sophisticated. The menu changes according to availability, but the star of the show remains the wild-caught yellow croaker – pre-order the flavourful and umami-loaded yellow croaker soup with matsutake mushrooms, as it takes hours to double boil.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1791;The Beijing Kitchen (Jianguo Road);China Mainland;Beijing;D6007, 6F, SKP Beijing, 87 Jianguo Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.909316;116.473274;69;false;true;Cantonese;With over 20 years of experience, this owner-chef from Hong Kong samples what his team makes daily to keep improving the quality. While he is most proud of his Cantonese barbecue (crispy deep-fried squab, in particular), double-steamed soups, dim sum, and original creations such as steamed tofu with shrimps and goji leaves also impress. And of course, nothing ends a Cantonese meal better than a serving of sago and pomelo in mango purée.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
1794;Mansion Cuisine by Jingyan;China Mainland;Beijing;22 Jianchang Hutong, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9475229;116.4116729;35;false;true;Beijing Cuisine;The high-ceilinged courtyard mansion was remodelled in 2013 to house this classy restaurant. In a similar vein, traditional Beijing dishes have been given a modern and eclectic makeover. Peking duck is served three ways that feature caviar, black truffle or carved into 108 slices the traditional way, boasting crispy skin and juicy flesh. Most dishes are made to order, some with tableside service. The sea cucumber with Peking style pork sauce is phenomenal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1795;Furong;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, The Westin, 9C Jinrong Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.916154;116.35324;99;true;true;Hunanese;Named after the provincial flower of Hunan, it makes perfect sense that this new brand under the Xin Rong Ji Group focusses on the Hunanese cuisine. The Hunanese chefdelivers authentic classics such as fish head covered in chopped chillies that pack a punch of flavour – make sure that it’s ordered in advance. Pork tripe soup with pickled radish and chanterelle is cooked in a casserole over charcoal. Bonus tip—you may order certain items in smaller portions as well.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1797;'t Raedthuys;Netherlands;Duiven;Rijksweg 51, Duiven, 6921 AC, Netherlands;51.9503421;6.0234842;27;false;true;Modern French, Classic French;Striking contemporary art adorns the walls inside this historical property dating back to 1863 – at 't Raedthuys, art and dining go hand in hand. The modern decor beautifully preserves the building's authentic character. A window to the kitchen allows you to see the chef and his team at work. On sunny days, the terrace at the front is the perfect spot for a romantic dinner for two. Prepare to be delighted as hostess and sommelier Karina van der Kolk introduces you to her unique collection of imported wines, which pair beautifully with the culinary creations of Hans den Engelsen. This chef is a traditionalist, who excels at classic dishes such as tournedos Rossini. He has a masterful ability to cook a leg of Dutch lamb to perfection, ensuring it is juicy and seasoned just right. However, he also has a modern edge, delighting diners with artistic plating and surprising textures. Think savoury crème brûlée or Jerusalem artichoke – as chips, as a cream, raw and pickled – with smoked eel. You should definitely sample something from the cheese trolley, which boasts around 30 cheeses. No doubt about it: the real artist is in the kitchen!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1798;Daalder;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Postjesweg 1, Amsterdam, 1057 DT, Netherlands;52.3645161;4.8595734;71;true;true;Creative;With its neon lights, bold graphics, street art and night-club atmosphere, Daalder's new home in Het Sieraad will leave a lasting impression. In this hip spot, Dennis Huwaë says he can really do his thing. He has long been known for his dishes that are creative without being pretentious, and you can see him in action on his 'cooking podium' as he continues to work in this vein. The chef's strong personality is evident in every detail. Chef Huwaë draws on his Indonesian roots and other Asian influences to add pep to his inventive creations, and he is certainly not averse to contrasting flavours. This chef's talent lies in the harmony he achieves with combinations such as chicken satay, anchovies and vadouvan. Sometimes he keeps things a little more traditional, serving up langoustine cooked to perfection with a butter sauce with champagne, orange and Grand Marnier. Subtle, intense, explosive – this is what Dennis Huwaë is all about.Meticulous but generous, he is always looking for variety and the element of surprise. Every plate is designed to be fun. At Daalder, you are guaranteed a blissful dining experience.;Terrace;[]
1799;Versaen;Netherlands;Ravenstein;Marktstraat 19, Ravenstein, 5371 AC, Netherlands;51.7973459;5.6523719;15;false;false;Creative, French Contemporary;Creativity doesn't have to be synonymous with showmanship. Diners need not expect outlandish combinations or countless processes from Hans Derks. His ingenuity lies in striking a balance between a limited number of ingredients. Think fresh langoustine tartare served with a ponzu dressing, dots of miso mayonnaise for that subtle fermented note, and the crispness of sliced radish and green apple. It may sound simple, but this approach demonstrates his technical skill and knowledge of flavours. Chef Derks likes to dabble in the flamboyance of Mediterranean cooking and the intensity of Asian cuisine, and dares, for example, to give tournedos Rossini a modern twist. He chooses his (often local) suppliers carefully and focuses on his sauces, eschewing unnecessary frills in favour of distinct and multifaceted flavours. In this former butcher's shop, with its trendy, pared-down vibe, diners can enjoy an experience that showcases understated creativity and Brabantian hospitality.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1800;Monarh;Netherlands;Tilburg;Bredaseweg 204-08, Tilburg, 5038 NK, Netherlands;51.555637;5.0696473;54;true;true;Creative;The subtle luxury of this restaurant, which occupies the vaulted cellar of an old monastery dating back 125 years, comes as a surprise. The menu features spectacular dishes which are beautifully presented and full of intense flavours. Chef Kappé’s modern cuisine has real style thanks to his use of different techniques, combined with careful and elegant preparation. A fascinating dining experience!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1801;Flavours;Netherlands;Weert;Hoogstraat 28, Weert, 6001 EV, Netherlands;51.254952;5.7079287;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Sweet. Bitter. Salty. Sour. Umami. These five flavours are the basis of every cuisine, but what Ron Lemmens creates with them can certainly be described as unique. His precise cuissons and the depth of his sauces are testament to his expertise. His ability to bring in international influences to produce exciting creations speaks to his knowledge of flavours.For example, he pan-fries cod to perfection and harmoniously combines it with sauerkraut, cream of Jerusalem artichoke, roasted capers and lovage and, most importantly, a jus made from cod in an intensely flavoured beurre blanc. Chef Lemmens does not go in for gratuitous surprises, but resolutely opts for robust flavours. He delighted us with his langoustines, crispy pork belly and carrot with the exotic nuances of ginger, tandoori and curry. His secret lies in the balance of flavours and combinations.At Flavours, you have a choice between one dining area done out in dark tones and a second space decorated in golden hues. Whichever you opt for, the stylish decor is further proof of the restaurant's good taste, right down to the last detail – this place really lives up to its name.;Air conditioning;[]
1802;Au Coin des Bons Enfants;Netherlands;Maastricht;Ezelmarkt 4, Maastricht, 6211 LJ, Netherlands;50.8461782;5.6873764;20;false;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;Au Coin des Bons Enfants is an important part of Maastricht's culinary history, with the restaurant first being awarded a MICHELIN star in 1957. Today, Timo Reichelt and sommelier Lino de Vrede are writing a new chapter that pays all due respect to the past, maintaining the establishment's elegant and romantic ambience, including a fabulous secluded terrace to the rear. The cuisine of chef Reichelt, who for a long time presided at Im Schiffchen in Düsseldorf, puts the ingredients front and centre.He has a rather classic cooking style, enhanced by his knack for seeking out the very best in quality ingredients and his talent for spectacular sauces. The expressive smoky flavour of a rich and buttery beurre blanc, for example, is the ideal accompaniment for a perfectly grilled North Sea turbot served with unripe mango for a hint of freshness.Veal sweetbreads are fried until golden brown, unctuous and crispy, and served alongside aromatic black truffle and a particularly creamy Chablis sauce. This is rich, traditional fare prepared by a young chef with a sound grasp of flavours.The finesse of the dishes is accentuated by the wines (also available by the glass). Ask the sommelier, a devotee of Pinot Noir and Old World wines, for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1803;Restaurant Wolfslaar;Netherlands;Breda;Wolfslaardreef 100, Breda, 4834 SP, Netherlands;51.5607208;4.8038928;22;false;true;Modern French;The Wolfslaar experience begins as soon as you drive onto the magnificent estate. As you approach the former coach house, you will be struck by the natural beauty of your surroundings, which you can enjoy to the full on the terrace. The chic and elegant interior exudes a warmth that comes courtesy of luxury materials such as walnut and marble. In this enchanting setting, Maarten Camps takes you on an exciting adventure, in which each ingredient is thoughtfully prepared in a multitude of ways. He throws in Asian flavours to add depth to his creative process, for instance seasoning hand-cut beef tartare with the perfect amount of soy sauce and XO sauce, combining it with a fresh and sweet tartare of North Sea crab, oyster juice, yuzu gel and pickled celery. The sauces whipped up by chef Camps are also more than worthy of a mention – see, for example, his vibrant, full-bodied beurre blanc, infused with dashi and sake and served with a beautiful fillet of turbot. The sommelier plays his part with an extensive wine list and perfect pairings, making your experience here all the more memorable.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1804;Aan de Zweth;Netherlands;Schipluiden;Rotterdamseweg 480, Schipluiden, 2636 KB, Netherlands;51.9629666;4.3936769;55;false;false;Modern French;Aan de Zweth offers a peaceful retreat between the bustling cities of Rotterdam and Delft. This elegant restaurant right on the Delftse Schie is at one with the water – from the terrace you can almost touch the bobbing boats! Thanks to the attentive service and attention to detail, you will not want for anything here at this warm and welcoming establishment. Chef Joris's creations are sophisticated, even innovative at times but without going overboard. His cooking is very precise, and he knows what a difference a good sauce can make. For example, he complements turbot à la meunière with a sensational bouillabaisse sauce with just the right amount of kick. This chef is as adept at creating an airy cottage cheese and vanilla soufflé as he is at using yuzu to liven up a langoustine dish. His carefully considered garnishes add complexity and elevate the excellent ingredients to new heights. Rather than surprising for surprise's sake, he impresses with his culinary expertise and bold flavours. To complete the experience, there is an exceptional wine list and a knowledgeable sommelier on hand.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1805;Merlet;Netherlands;Schoorl;Duinweg 15, Schoorl, 1871 AC, Netherlands;52.6998032;4.6944638;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Merlet’s unique decor includes stunning features such as a dining room adorned with gold leaf, a moss wall behind the cosy fireplace, 3D effects and a glass wall filled with coloured sand shaped like dunes. The interior reflects the surrounding countryside, making this a fascinating setting in which to enjoy a meal.The chef likes to work with luxury ingredients which stimulate his creativity, whether he’s preparing fresh langoustine or seasonal Jerusalem artichokes. This is a chef who thinks things through, is keen to experiment and likes to combine generosity with finesse, creating complex and harmonious dishes such as perfectly cooked sweetbreads served with different vegetables and a rich jus. An intriguing dining experience from start to finish.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1806;Ratatouille Food & Wine;Netherlands;Haarlem;Spaarne 96, Haarlem, 2011 CL, Netherlands;52.3786385;4.6376627;98;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With Jozua Jaring, not everything is as it seems. He pays great attention to detail in the meticulous presentation of his dishes and likes to surprise diners with contrasting colours and forms. This is a restaurant with a real "wow" factor – chef Jaring puts his own exciting spin on classic flavours, taking your taste buds on a culinary adventure: conjuring up vegetable ice cream concoctions, dabbling with Asian citrus notes or rounding off a dish with a classic, deeply flavoursome vegetable jus. Such inspirations take this chef's top-quality ingredients to the next level. Think sweet and smoky barbecued langoustine accompanied by al dente ravioli stuffed with langoustine meat, along with various textures of carrot and a full-bodied bisque. This chef has mastered the art of working with fish and seafood, and his creativity does not lose any momentum when it comes to devising vegetarian dishes. This characterful building has an equally tasteful decor: a little rustic, a tad eclectic, but very much on trend – with an imposing open Molteni kitchen serving as the hub of the action. And then there is the cosy waterside terrace (specify when booking).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1807;La Provence;Netherlands;Driebergen-Rijsenburg;Hoofdstraat 109, Driebergen-Rijsenburg, 3971 KG, Netherlands;52.0522638;5.282136;37;true;false;Creative French;André van Alten is a fine example of a chef who continually reinvents himself while remaining grounded in his core principles. The unwavering quality of the ingredients, the expertise with which wild duck is roasted on the bone and the depth of the turbot jus complementing an ultra-fresh cut of the fish all showcase his impressive classical training. We also applaud the chef's eagerness to share his experience with younger generations. His ability to keep a cool head as he leads his team in the open kitchen is remarkable. But the chef does not stop there and keeps innovating. He showcases his creativity in the preparation of his garnishes. The diversity of textures, the interplay of hot and cold, the vibrancy of subtle acidity... With such finesse, he creates depth of flavour. He has a preference for fish, although the lamb loin in a sea salt crust is one of the house classics. The delightful hostess's exquisite wine pairings perfectly complement the food. In this intimate setting with its tranquil verdant terrace, diners are assured an exceptional experience. This tradition of excellence has endured for over 50 years!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1808;De Swarte Ruijter;Netherlands;Holten;Holterbergweg 7, Holten, 7451 JL, Netherlands;52.2948139;6.4204764;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;Nature takes centre stage at De Swarte Ruijter. Located on the Holterberg, this charming thatched house boasts stunning views of the nearby pine forest and seamlessly incorporates natural elements into its interior design. Erik de Mönnink draws inspiration from the beautiful surroundings, which fuel his creativity every day. His unconventional cuisine showcases locally sourced produce such as mushrooms, venison and nagelhout (air-dried veal). This chef knows how to captivate his diners, creating fascinating dishes featuring playful contrasts in texture. His daring combinations are sometimes quite astonishing. Think freshly caught North Sea crab encased in a jelly of the same crustacean and then deep-fried. Textures of mango and apple provide an exquisite sweetness. The dish is then finished with a rich, aromatic curry sauce. This chef is a master at balancing bold flavours and bright acidity. Your cordial hostess, Esther, will make you feel right at home as you savour this celebration of Salland's rich bounty.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1809;ML;Netherlands;Haarlem;Klokhuisplein 5, Haarlem, 2011 HK, Netherlands;52.3807364;4.6381713;66;false;true;Creative;ML is a firm favourite for many a foodie. Mark and Liane Gratama's restaurant is housed in an imposing listed building in the heart of Haarlem. The modern decor blends vintage elements with chic design. The Chef’s Bar, next to the open kitchen, is the place to be if you want to watch the enthusiastic Mark Gratama at work. Each dish is a creative masterpiece, playfully combining a delightful variety of textures. His unique ingredient combinations demonstrate his willingness to experiment and push culinary boundaries. For example, he incorporates a hint of seaweed into a blueberry-based dessert and a zesty verjus sorbet. With meticulous precision, he unites the disparate flavours of seared langoustine and hearty beef sausage into a perfectly balanced dish. The finishing touch of an exquisite sauce or broth, frequently drawing on Asian influences, provides extra punch. It is inspiring to watch this consummate professional constantly evolve his craft.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1810;Joelia;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Coolsingel 5, Rotterdam, 3012 AA, Netherlands;51.9239352;4.4776161;64;false;true;Modern French;Joelia's charm permeates every nook and cranny of this restaurant. As you enter, you'll be instantly smitten with the eclectic decor, a captivating fusion of vintage and contemporary design. This space exudes a certain American grandeur, and the open kitchen and the impressive wine collection on show add to the atmosphere. Maître d' Pieter Timmer and chef Sofiane Bons inject a youthful energy into proceedings, including the menu. The passionate chef honours his French roots with meticulously crafted sauces and dishes. He adds pep and intensity by drawing inspiration from far-flung places, especially Asia. Red mullet, for instance, is barbecued to perfection, yielding a wonderfully crispy crust. To elevate the dish, the chef uses the fish bones to create a vibrant sauce packed with character. This is paired with a subtly sweetened mole, its characteristic nuttiness and spice adding another dimension. Pea and asparagus garnishes lend a burst of freshness and playfulness. This chef works with a broad palette of flavours, and these are complemented by an impressive wine collection of no less than 12 000 bottles.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1811;Ron Gastrobar;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Sophialaan 55, Amsterdam, 1075 BP, Netherlands;52.3522317;4.8566529;55;true;false;Creative French;Ron Blaauw is something of a culinary mastermind. In 2013, the popular chef transformed his two-MICHELIN-starred restaurant into this down-to-earth gastrobar, and it was an instant success. This hip urban establishment offers a diverse atmosphere in which to discover chef Blaauw's relaxed fine dining concept.Eschewing any unnecessary frills, the focus lies squarely on original combinations and distinct flavours. Here, you can enjoy simple yet imaginative cuisine that is intelligent, elaborate and bold. Think veal sweetbreads cooked in time-honoured tradition, a spicy blend of lentils, textures of pumpkin and yoghurt with lime zest for body and freshness. The dishes here are brimming with flavour. The impressive menu features classics such as beef Wellington, vegetarian options and premium produce such as wagyu and turbot cooked on the barbecue, as well as an amazing onion Martini (with a Comté foam). You will likely want to order the lot! At Ron Gastrobar, the flavours of the Amsterdam metropolis come alive.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1812;Perceel;Netherlands;Capelle aan den IJssel;Dorpsstraat 3, Capelle aan den IJssel, 2902 BC, Netherlands;51.9219398;4.5849566;39;true;false;Creative;At Jos and Sharon’s Perceel you will experience the talent of a couple with an impressive list of achievements. She takes care of the excellent service, while he focuses on pure and natural flavours, using produce from his own garden. Flowers take pride of place in this beautiful establishment, both in the décor and on your plate!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1815;Restaurant 1857;Netherlands;Roosendaal;Molenstraat 18, Roosendaal, 4701 JS, Netherlands;51.5343696;4.4598749;61;false;true;Creative French;Restaurant 1857 prides itself on being chic but by no means stuffy. A narrow street leads to this former coach house – the old horse trough is still in the open kitchen! – that exudes an elegant combination of authentic charm and contemporary sophistication. Joke, your charming hostess, is also the talented pastry chef behind the restaurant's fabulous desserts.Joey van Heesbeen's creative dishes are technically impressive, visually striking and at times complex. He likes to experiment with bold flavours and the umami-rich nuances of Asian cuisine. In his unique take on beef Wellington, he incorporates miso mustard and a powder made from dried vegetable scraps. He pairs briefly seared langoustine, with a creamy shellfish-based XO sauce. Langoustine mayonnaise, yuzu gel and salty caviar add an extra kick to this intense creation. Round off your meal with a coffee or tea and sample one of the expertly crafted treats from the dessert trolley – another testament to the chefs' skill. As well as the set menu (vegetarian version available), there is a tempting à la carte selection.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1816;Bolenius;Netherlands;Amsterdam;George Gershwinlaan 30, Amsterdam, 1082 MT, Netherlands;52.3361146;4.873797;55;true;false;Creative;Luc Kusters is an ambassador of Dutch cuisine who lays the focus squarely on vegetables and local produce. On a daily basis, he harvests delicious produce from his kitchen garden, located close to the restaurant in the Zuidas business district! Bolenius's elegant minimalist style and urban vibe reflect the purity of the cuisine. The ethos behind this sustainable vision is regularly explained when the kitchen team serve their dishes themselves.The head chef's ingenuity comes to the fore in the stunning presentation and flavour combinations of his dishes. His cuisine is light but brimming with intensity. He prefers to express himself with vegetables and herbs – beetroot grown in clay soil with morels is a signature dish for good reason – but he also works with meat and fish, eg Dutch Kamper lamb or pike-perch from the North Sea. Whether you opt for his plant-based set menu or the "Dutch Menu" (à la carte also available), the versatility and nuances he draws out of treasures from Dutch soil is uncommonly captivating: aromatic cauliflower, green peppers and textures of buckwheat with a clear broth that brings everything together and adds depth. The way chef Kusters turns 'simplicity' into memorable cuisine is truly remarkable.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1818;'t Ganzenest;Netherlands;Rijswijk;Delftweg 58a, Rijswijk, 2289 AL, Netherlands;52.0370964;4.3457403;55;false;true;Modern French;'t Ganzenest will forever be associated with Harry Visbeen, who held a MICHELIN star for many years. Today, Erik Tas is writing a new chapter of this beautiful story. He has cultivated the authentic allure of the building and revamped the restaurant with just the right dose of elegance. A glance at the menu reveals that chef Tas is a fan and connoisseur of top-quality produce such as turbot, veal sweetbreads and wagyu. He enhances these ingredients with the perfect garnishes and expertly done sauces with great depth of flavour. Take, for example, the wonderful cream sauce with chanterelles and the rich veal jus that elevates a fillet of turbot to new heights. He showcases strawberries, for instance, in a beautifully airy soufflé, but also subtly macerated with a ball of super creamy vanilla ice cream and in an elaborate creation with a strawberry coulis brightened with a dash of vinegar. Erik Tas is an astute chef who knows how to get the best out of his ingredients, and understands that less is more. The produce is clearly the star of the show here – the enthusiasm with which the waitstaff present the wines and cheeses is infectious.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1819;Noor;Netherlands;Groningen;Zuiderweg 38, Groningen, 9745 AD, Netherlands;53.2144067;6.5023321;16;true;true;Creative;Having sold De Loohoeve, Marleen and Jeroen Brouwer moved a little further north to Groningen, where they have given the Theresiakapel a facelift. The simplicity of the chapel has been preserved, as have the beautiful stained-glass windows, which are now complemented by a stylish interior design. This is no run-of-the-mill restaurant: upon entering, you are led through the state-of-the-art kitchen. The two chefs have joined forces in the kitchen to better express their creativity. It was already clear that their originality and sense of inventiveness knew no bounds, and here at Noor they continue to refine their personal style. Their dish of celeriac cooked in a salt crust and combined with ingredients including yoghurt and salted lemon is a firm favourite with diners. Another tempting option is the dry-aged sea bass, pan fried until buttery soft and served with baked potato, a beautifully rounded verjus beurre blanc infused with subtle fermented notes, and a salty codium-flavoured oil. Words like "exuberant", "meticulous" and "adventurous" spring to mind, including when it comes to the vegetarian set menu, which showcases "everyday" vegetables (order in advance). An inimitable dining experience!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1820;Bistro de la Mer;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Utrechtsestraat 57, Amsterdam, 1017 VJ, Netherlands;52.3640668;4.8982876;61;false;false;Classic Cuisine;In this cosy bistro it is easy to imagine that you're in Paris instead of Utrechtsestraat, in the heart of Amsterdam. The large oyster bar, the walls adorned with the menus of legendary French brasseries, the vintage crockery on the tables: this place is a celebration of a bygone era. Traditional fish recipes are given a fresh but down-to-earth twist with a sure hand. Richard van Oostenbrugge and Thomas Groot are once again making their mark here with no-nonsense dishes that you can feast on every day of the week – including at lunchtime!For example, a generous portion of perfectly cooked mussels are served, dotted with vadouvan mayonnaise and calamansi jelly, which add freshness and nuance without spoiling the seafood's distinctive flavour. As a nod to the traditional recipe, a creamy vadouvan soup and green celery provide the finishing touch to this delicious reinterpretation. A beautiful piece of turbot roasted on the bone is topped with morels incorporating a mousse created from the fish's barbel, fine slices of lardo di colonnata and a rich beurre blanc. This is next-level fish cuisine. Old school. Original. And it can all be ordered à la carte!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1821;Maeve;Netherlands;Utrecht;Kromme Nieuwegracht 18, Utrecht, 3512 HH, Netherlands;52.0923609;5.1243245;35;false;false;Creative French, French Contemporary;Chef Tommy and maître d' Vera take you on a compelling culinary voyage in this characterful and stylishly designed building. She woos diners with her personable manner, he with his expressive homage to the terroir. Sourced as locally as possible, vegetables play an essential role here, lending depth to the dishes. This is a chef who cooks his ingredients to perfection, shows a light touch with fresh acidic flavours and has fun with temperatures and textures.Veal sweetbreads are briefly fried and then brushed with a reduced veal gravy. A fine brunoise of various vegetables provides a pleasing bite. Tender onion stuffed with Thai basil, strips of white onion and black truffle provide subtle aromatic touches. An excellent sauce based on veal gravy with citrus makes for a fine base. This is a chef who manages to translate interesting ideas into intensely flavoursome creations. The combination of miso and koji in a dessert with quince and chocolate demonstrates his mastery of flavour nuances.The wine list is equally impressive (you can see the wine cellar next to the restrooms), with a particular focus on Dutch and Belgian labels here too.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1822;Zoldering;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Utrechtsestraat 141h, Amsterdam, 1017 VM, Netherlands;52.361354;4.8993625;93;false;false;Modern French;Wine lovers have embraced Zoldering. With three great sommeliers at your service, don't hesitate to ask for advice. The two impressive wine lists offer something for every budget – one lower-key selection and one featuring iconic wineries. The suggested pairings on the menu are by no means redundant either, because you're really spoilt for choice here! This lively neighbourhood bistro has the feel of an old Amsterdam café and provides a relaxed setting in which to savour exuberant revamped French dishes. The vegetarian interpretation of filet americain has already become a classic of chef Tomas Bron's. He creates this appetiser with house-made focaccia and deeply spiced and intensely flavoured tomato for an amazing trompe l'œil effect! His sauces are equally worthy of acclaim, such as the exquisite poultry jus with morels, which elevates the partridge fillet beautifully. There is nothing superfluous here, just ingredients that are replete with flavour and make for a heady balance. Rest assured you'll have a great time at Zoldering.;Interesting wine list;[]
1823;Wils;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Stadionplein 26, Amsterdam, 1076 CM, Netherlands;52.3433421;4.856129;22;false;true;World Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant occupies the third floor of a building by architect Jan Wils, who also designed the Olympic Stadium across the street. No doubt Wils would have been proud of this American-style urban brasserie, which feels both grand and intimate. The cocktail bar is delightfully trendy. The cuisine never fails to impress – especially its use of fire. Chef Joris Bijdendijk and his team love to cook with the charcoal grill and traditional ovens, which they handle with great skill. For instance, they pair fluffy deep-fried bara (a Surinamese-Hindustani snack) and crispy veal sweetbreads with a zesty vinaigrette made with yuzu, raw green tomatillo and herbs picked from their own garden. Bold flavours are given extra depth with a sure hand. Their commitment to sustainability fuels their creativity, as seen in the parfait glacé made with stale bread from their bakery. The chefs have a penchant for plant-forward cuisine and enjoy playing around with spices and contrasts. An exciting dining experience is guaranteed!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1824;RIJKS®;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Museumstraat 2, Amsterdam, 1077 XX, Netherlands;52.3595346;4.8842855;86;true;false;Creative, Modern French;Joris Bijdendijk has put the Rijksmuseum's gem of a restaurant on the map with his highly personal culinary approach, working predominantly with homegrown vegetables spiced with the exotic influences that characterise Dutch cuisine. He whisks his diners away on a unique culinary adventure. Having been completely revamped and done out in natural materials, the interior has a warm feel and creates an even more immersive experience. RIJKS® is a reflection of the bustling city of Amsterdam. The sophistication of the well-considered dishes is immediately striking. With one mind-blowing idea after another, this is captivating and intriguing cuisine. Take his signature dish, which features a millefeuille made of slivers of beetroot, which is beautifully earthy and slightly sweet, finished with a rich beurre blanc elevated with Tomasu soy sauce and fresh parsley oil – simplicity at its most delicious! At Rijks, you will discover Dutch gastronomy 2.0.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1825;De Juwelier;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Utrechtsestraat 51, Amsterdam, 1017 VJ, Netherlands;52.3642868;4.8982025;94;true;true;Modern French;Run by Richard van Oostenbrugge and Thomas Groot, the renowned duo behind Restaurant 212, this is a bistro of the old school. As you enter this charming, lively place in the bustling Utrechtsestraat, you receive a warm welcome from the chefs, and delicious aromas waft towards you. You quickly get the feeling there are no obligations and yet anything is possible. The entire à la carte menu is a real treat for any foodie.The chefs are not afraid to use lesser-known ingredients such as oxtail and zander. The intensity of their no-nonsense dishes makes a convincing case for why this overlooked produce is deserving of more attention. Veal kidneys, for example, are served with an irresistible creamy sauce based on a veal stock with a shellfish jus. The zander is candied in smoked butter, topped with zolderspek (smoky bacon) and goose liver, and combined with roasted quince and the strength and acidity of sauerkraut. At De Juwelier, they keep things straightforward and yet will still surprise you with traditional rich flavours, modern freshness and French finesse – a feast like in the old days!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1826;Marrees;Netherlands;Weert;Stadhuispassage 10, Weert, 6001 KK, Netherlands;51.2510546;5.7034285;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Jan Marrees's trademark is his relaxed approach to gastronomy. A glance at his extensive menu (there are also two set menus, one of them vegetarian) will bring a smile to the face of any foodie. You can opt for one of the chef's specialities such as the crispy fried sweetbreads with an intense veal jus and fruity notes of apple and apricot. Alternatively, there is a variety of small, modern delicacies. Zesty and bitter, powerful and delicate, creamy and crispy: every dish is an exciting interplay of flavours and textures made with top-quality ingredients. This is a chef who certainly does not shy away from contrasts and really showcases his talent in the process. The way he puts his own spin on a dame blanche sundae while respecting classic flavours cannot fail to impress.With labels from around the globe, the fantastic wine list certainly has the perfect accompaniment in store, including some attractive pairings by the glass. As for the modern interior – an atmospheric interplay of leather, marble and striking copper chandeliers, adorned with the shells of Gillardeau oysters by hostess Patricia. A visit to Jan Marrees version 2.0 is a must!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1827;Brass Boer Thuis;Netherlands;Zwolle;Nieuwe Markt 21, Zwolle, 8011 PG, Netherlands;52.5112819;6.095634;38;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Many restaurants may claim to have the kind of atmosphere in which diners feel at home, but here it really is the case. This place is located on the charming Nieuwe Markt and has a terrace that overlooks the square. Inside, driftwood and drying herbs hang from the ceiling, and the large wine wall gives the contemporary decor individuality. This is a cosy setting, and diners clearly come to have a good time. Jonnie and Thérèse Boer have built up a kitchen team that loves working with produce from Zwolle, often cooks on the wood fire and manages to create dishes that are original but not overly complex. Our inspectors were bowled over by a combination of wonderfully crispy veal sweetbreads with a subtly sweet glaze, both raw and deep-fried shrimps, crunchy vegetable accoutrements and an exquisite peanut sauce that elevated the entire dish, enhancing the complex flavour nuances. At Brass Boer Thuis, the chefs are not afraid to use bold flavours, but they always manage to strike the right balance. As a result, the extensive menu is full of mouthwatering options. Who says fine dining can't be a relaxed affair?;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1828;Eden;Netherlands;Waalre;Oude Torenstraat 6, Waalre, 5581 BJ, Netherlands;51.387504;5.4417488;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;Eden is the playground of chef Herman Cooijmans. He has relocated his little slice of paradise to Waalre, and his new restaurant there exudes modern elegance. Natural elements and hues, warm mood lighting and chic decorative features lend this open space a welcome cosiness and sophistication. A fun dining experience awaits. The cuisine is intricate and full of subtleties, drawing on international influences – the chef likes to use Middle Eastern spices and zesty notes to build excitement. He brings together contrasting elements that elevate one another. For example, he serves venison fillet with a rich jus enlivened by pomegranate, alongside beetroot infused with liquorice. Another stand-out dish is based on a combination of octopus and raspberry. There is a choice of set menus, so you can either discover the chef's creative side or savour his slightly more conventional offerings. The wine list is certainly worth exploring.;;[]
1829;Lutum;Netherlands;Wijk bij Duurstede;Markt 15, Wijk bij Duurstede, 3961 BC, Netherlands;51.9729251;5.3450659;49;true;false;Creative, Organic;With a slogan like Volg de natuur ("Follow nature") and a name that refers to the fertile, clay-rich soil of the area, it is immediately clear that terroir is a key focus at Lutum. This vision is carried through into every aspect of the restaurant. The decor has a natural Zen feel, with an abundance of decorative features reminiscent of trees. The menu showcases the freshest ingredients sourced directly from local gardens and food forests.The surprise menu, designed to minimise waste, highlights local produce and adds an international twist with ingredients such as koji and miso. This cuisine is vibrant and exciting. They infuse a variety of pak choi creations, such as a leaf coulis and a stem slushy, with the subtle spiciness of tandoori and the floral complexity of different blooms. The chefs meticulously craft their dishes and regularly amaze diners with their sauces – the depth of flavour of the red wine and cardamom-based sauce they serve with venison is a case in point. The food at Lutum packs a punch!;Terrace;[]
1831;De Moerbei;Netherlands;Warmond;Dorpsstraat 5a, Warmond, 2361 AK, Netherlands;52.1954285;4.5025673;33;true;false;Farm to table, Modern French;Chef Michael Corpel and sommelier Frank de Haas are writing a new chapter in the illustrious story of De Moerbei. In 1996, this old farmhouse was transformed into a stylish restaurant exuding elegance. From its early days to the present day, the ambition of this place has remained unchanged: to delight guests with top-quality produce, be it wine or North Sea sole. Chef Corpel takes inspiration from techniques and ingredients from all over the world, while resolutely forging his own culinary path. His meticulously crafted dishes draw on local produce, enhanced here and there by exotic touches, to showcase his love for the North Sea and the intensity of classic sauces. Turbot fried in beurre noisette, for example, is given a lift by infusing the beurre blanc with dashi and incorporating drops of herb oil. Pieces of lobster tail and flash-grilled green asparagus round out the meal. At De Moerbei, the purity of the flavours takes centre stage, leaving a lasting impression on every diner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1833;Beluga Loves You;Netherlands;Maastricht;Plein 1992 nr 12, Maastricht, 6221 JP, Netherlands;50.8462005;5.6990715;61;false;true;Creative;Start with an aperitif in the trendy lounge before entering the elegant dining area with interior design inspired by the River Meuse. Servais Tielman is a resolutely modern chef who, together with his team, has mastered the art of turning bright ideas into bold flavours. With the playful application of different textures, his dishes come to life courtesy of beautiful presentations and masterful technique.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1834;O&O;Netherlands;Sint Willebrord;Dorpsstraat 138, Sint Willebrord, 4711 EL, Netherlands;51.5525395;4.5917081;72;true;true;Asian, Asian Influences;Danny and Helena Tsang opened their restaurant Nieuw Hong Kong in Sint Willebrord in 1982. It may have been just another Chinese eatery at first, but the owners' ambitions evolved over time and they set their sights on showcasing the true finesse of Asian cuisine. And they have been successful in their quest: today, they invite diners to embark on a culinary voyage from Japan via Hong Kong and China to Thailand, Malaysia and Singapore. Chef Danny's cooking style fuses tradition with creativity. Sweet, sour, zesty and umami flavours are precisely balanced in subtle combinations. He creates exciting dishes in which exotic seasonings meet French techniques for an extra layer of sophistication. East and West become one here. The chef's expertise is evident in his house-made gochujang, his Sichuan chilli sauce, the crispy fried shallot and the star anise and five-spice-flavoured cooking juices that accompany his Peking-style barbary duck. His daughter Monica's expertly chosen wine pairings elevate this delightful dining experience (the wine room itself is a sight to behold). The premium tea selection serves as an equally ideal accompaniment, allowing the subtle nuances of the dishes to truly shine. The Tsang family are proud ambassadors of Asia's culinary richness.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1835;Cheval Blanc;Netherlands;Heemstede;Jan van Goyenstraat 29, Heemstede, 2102 CA, Netherlands;52.3602095;4.6289256;76;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Cheval Blanc is the epitome of a perennial favourite. Set in an elegant and inviting townhouse, this upscale restaurant is the perfect destination for food lovers. The team's enthusiasm is infectious. Maître d' and owner Ton Nelissen gives his diners a warm welcome and is always on hand to provide astute wine recommendations. Chef Huub van der Velden pulls out all the stops to ensure your dining experience is unforgettable. A top-quality main ingredient and some carefully considered garnishes: that's all it takes. For instance, he combines perfectly pan-seared scallops with al dente white asparagus, an unctuous rapini mash, sautéed morels and finely chopped shallots, finished with a vegetable jus, as well as a rich brown butter emulsion. The chef's cooking is all about simplicity and substance, with no frills. Cheval Blanc is a classic that has always kept up with the times.;Terrace;[]
1836;Wiesen;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Kleine Berg 10, Eindhoven, 5611 JV, Netherlands;51.4378387;5.4753117;16;true;true;French;The culinary highlight of the Kleine Berg, a charming shopping street, can be found at no 10. Behind its discreet façade, this elegant fine dining restaurant boasts a stylish yet delightfully cosy interior. And no sooner are you seated than you'll be bowled over by the work of Yuri Wiesen, who specialises in French cuisine. A virtuoso of classic techniques, he is also adept at handling ingredients from around the globe and creating playful texture combinations. What sets him apart is his ability to take familiar flavours and give them an unexpected twist, creating a truly exciting dining experience. He steers clear of unnecessary fuss in his dishes, pairing, for instance, perfectly pan-seared, still translucent Eastern Scheldt lobster tail with al dente white asparagus, the salty bite of sautéed sea lavender and a rich, frothy bisque. If the chef happens to get a delivery of fresh strawberries, he'll be sure to serve them up as his special of the day – coupe Romanoff, anyone? Now that's the mark of a true craftsman.;Terrace;[]
1837;Zarzo;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Bleekweg 7, Eindhoven, 5611 EZ, Netherlands;51.4352972;5.4841506;95;true;false;Creative;Adrian Zarzo Habraken is a man who knows what his customers want. The funky vibe of his lounge-style restaurant is the gateway to his culinary world. You can see the chefs in action in the open kitchen, and a visit to the impressive wine room is an experience in itself. Brace yourself for chef Zarzo's bold fusion of traditional Spanish recipes and progressive ideas. This is complex cuisine, but the focus lies squarely on the flavours. Perfectly fried on the skin, red mullet is combined with braised lacinato kale and fennel, fennel foam and his take on the Catalan suquet fish soup, à la bouillabaisse, with crispy prawn. This is a dish with spirit! His quest for novelty is captivating, as seen in his delectable dessert featuring a unique combination of mushrooms and chicory. Both Zarzo's wine list (with more than 2 000 labels!) and sommelier happen to be among the best in the country. Although the selection includes some excellent wines from around the globe, it is Spanish gems that are given pride of place. This is wine pairing par excellence!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1838;De Kromme Watergang;Netherlands;Hoofdplaat;Slijkplaat 6, Hoofdplaat, 4513 KK, Netherlands;51.377304;3.6031759;23;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;With the Eastern Scheldt and North Sea serving as primary suppliers, and De Zilte Hof vegetable garden across the street providing the chefs with vegetables, fruit and herbs, De Kromme Watergang takes full advantage of the bountiful ingredients Zeelandic Flanders has to offer. That ambassadorial role is also reflected in the respect they have for the produce, which is evident in their nose-to-tail approach. Open since 1993, this beloved restaurant now mostly sees Tom Vinke at the helm of the open kitchen, as he gradually takes over from his father, Edwin.Here, produce is king, elevated by the chef's carefully considered garnishes and spicy exotic seasonings. For instance, he poaches ling from bycatch in butter and barbecues it briefly. He then serves it up with a foamy jus with dill, crunchy peas and herbs from the garden. The bold briny favours of Zeeland are given a sophisticated twist and the occasional international touch.One final tip: Extend your stay by booking one of the lovely suites, and you will fall in love with the beautiful surroundings, just as the chefs have.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1839;Bij Jef;Netherlands;Den Hoorn;Herenstraat 34, Den Hoorn, 1797 AJ, Netherlands;53.0246761;4.7498447;48;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;As soon as you step into Bij Jef, you are struck by a sense of peace and space. The minimalist interior has been specifically designed as a setting in which guests can enjoy Texel's bounty of produce – the local suckling lamb is world famous and, needless to say, also a firm fixture here. But Jef Schuur draws much more from his surroundings. Salty herbs, crustaceans and shellfish… the list goes on. Chef Schuur puts his terroir first – be sure to take a look around the impressive vegetable garden behind the restaurant – and he showcases it elegantly in contemporary-style dishes. His innovative creations often feature invigorating sweet and sour nuances. This is a chef who likes to surprise. Sauces are key: think a rich lamb jus and herb-infused oil to pair with crispy slow-roasted lamb neck. The refreshing flavours of Texel are paired with some real gems from the world of wine, selected by maître d' Nadine, for example the delicate Madeira Rainwater Reserva that brings out all the flavours of the subtle dessert based on blood orange. Divine! You'll also be hard pressed to resist the trolley of pastries to go with your coffee. And as a cosy finale to this wonderful experience, you should definitely consider booking one of the designer guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1840;Central Park;Netherlands;Voorburg;Oosteinde 14, Voorburg, 2271 EH, Netherlands;52.0702283;4.369309;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The stately national monument that houses Central Park is quite a sight to behold. This magnificent palace with breathtaking views of the surrounding grounds is the perfect setting in which to enjoy sophisticated fine dining. Luxury is the name of the game here, but there's nothing stuffy about this place. The service staff are attentive, and the selection of wines and champagnes is really impressive. An overnight stay at the hotel is the perfect way to round off your experience. But first, take the chance to savour a finely crafted take on classic, coherent dishes.Traditional cooking techniques and intense sauces make for wonderfully crisp and vibrant culinary creations. Clever new twists produce surprising results. The earthy, sweet and sour nuances of beetroot combined with fresh blackberries, foie gras and a robust jus with sweet notes of sherry form the perfect accompaniment to duck cooked on the carcass. Grilled fillet of turbot is elevated by textures of carrot, mussels and a beautifully aromatic mussel nage. Come to Central Park for no-nonsense cuisine packed with subtle yet pronounced flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1841;Karel 5;Netherlands;Utrecht;Geertebolwerk 1, Utrecht, 3511 XA, Netherlands;52.0876194;5.1177775;88;true;true;Creative;Leave Utrecht's bustling city centre behind for a while and let yourself be swept away by Karel 5's medieval charm. Luxury meets authenticity in this historical oasis, where you can admire old paintings and sculptures as you dine beneath crystal chandeliers, and, when the weather is fine, have lunch on the beautiful garden terrace. Leon Mazairac and his team conjure up cuisine that does justice to the setting, for a true fine dining experience.Game from the Veluwe, Belgian endive, saffron from Herentals: Chef Mazairac makes a point of working only with top-quality produce that he sources as locally as possible, and he is also passionate about vegetables. As an amuse-bouche he serves a bouquet of seasonal vegetables accompanied by a classic, delicately acidic vinaigrette. The freshness of nature and the richness of the sauces are the hallmarks of this chef's cooking. He has a penchant for vegetarian dishes, and a meat- and fish-free set menu is always available. But when he serves sole, for example, it is poached to perfection and comes into its own thanks to a beurre blanc sauce with vin jaune and fresh trimmings. Karel 5 embodies a marriage of tradition and innovation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1842;De Kromme Dissel;Netherlands;Heelsum;Klein Zwitserlandlaan 5, Heelsum, 6866 DS, Netherlands;51.9848455;5.7586213;86;true;true;Creative, Modern French;De Kromme Dissel represents a piece of Dutch culinary tradition and has had a Michelin star since 1971. Located in a 17C Saxon farmhouse, the restaurant's rich history can immediately be felt in the ambience and the rustic-style interior is extremely cosy and charming. The attentive waitstaff are always on hand and also provide expert wine recommendations.Experienced chef Tonny Berentsen does not rest on his laurels. Although he is classically trained, he dares to show his creative side, drawing on his travels in Asia for the inspiration behind the modern ideas he brings into his dishes. Think fleshy langoustine flavoured with curry panko, combined with sea bass tartare and subtly spicy pumpkin. Diners are just as bowled over by the traditional game jus that accompanies his wild duck or his rich shellfish broth.Chef Berentsen now continues the story of De Kromme Dissel with his own culinary style. This perennial favourite continues to reinvent itself – much to the delight of every foodie!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1844;Voltaire;Netherlands;Leersum;Broekhuizerlaan 2, Leersum, 3956 NS, Netherlands;52.0079012;5.3998084;96;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;At Parc Broekhuizen, which houses this restaurant, you can fully immerse yourself in the breathtaking natural beauty of the Utrechtse Heuvelrug. Dining in this splendid historical manor house, overlooking the stunning grounds and ponds, is an extraordinary experience. The soothing music and understated modern design perfectly complement this gorgeous setting. The chefs contrast the peaceful ambiance with their pronounced, often daring flavours. They add zing to their creative combinations with bursts of acidity and sophisticated garnishes. They elevate the medium-rare pigeon fillet, for instance, with the sweet and bitter interplay of beetroot cream, lovage oil, ripe sweet cherries and velvety mousseline. The sauces are a key element of their dishes, and they strive to reduce them to their most essential form. The modern sophistication of their beautifully presented creations is captivating. The chefs draw inspiration from their natural surroundings, as well as produce from local suppliers and their own herb garden. And why not cap off your culinary adventure with a memorable night's stay at Parc Broekhuizen?;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
1845;Restaurant Kasteel Heemstede;Netherlands;Houten;Heemsteedseweg 20, Houten, 3992 LS, Netherlands;52.0330316;5.1252355;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Admire the grandeur of this fully restored 17C château as you take the road up, walk across the little bridge and immerse yourself in its attractive blend of historical features and contemporary luxury. Heemstede Castle is an exceptional and enchanting location, and in Ollie Schuiling it has a very talented chef at the helm. You can expect a few surprises on the wine list, including some sought-after gems from Europe, as well as a nod to the Netherlands. The wines perfectly complement the intense flavours of the chef's dishes. Exceptionally fresh top-quality produce, sublime sauces and inventive preparations with a "wow" factor make this place the success that it is. The chef has a meticulous approach to his extremely well-crafted and visually appealing cuisine. Take his lightly smoked breast of Anjou pigeon, paired with a giblet mousse, a parsnip mousse and a wonderfully intense sauce infused with garam masala. This really is a fairy tale castle!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1846;De Vlindertuin;Netherlands;Zuidlaren;Stationsweg 41, Zuidlaren, 9471 GK, Netherlands;53.0925254;6.6803737;20;true;true;Modern French;Jilt Cazemier is certainly close to his suppliers: as you make your way to his restaurant, you will even spot the grazing lambs. A champion of local produce, he showcases its quality with consummate skill. When he prepares that locally raised lamb, he utilises the whole animal, from nose to tail. The depth of flavour of his main ingredient is enhanced by his intense sauces. His refined technique is evident in every dish, his playful garnishes providing refreshing contrasts. For example, he elevates lobster with a blend of salty herbs, a carrot puree with a bright orange flavour, a rich lobster bisque infused with coral, a zesty lemongrass emulsion, and a dashi-infused jus for a Far Eastern twist. This chef is constantly evolving, seeking new ways to express his culinary creativity. The attention to aesthetic detail extends to the dining space. The moment you arrive in the charming village of Zuidlaren, you will be won over by the elegance and homely feel of this historical Saxon farmhouse (1719 ). Nab a spot on the terrace overlooking the village green if you really want to experience the true essence of De Vlindertuin.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1847;De Heeren van Harinxma;Netherlands;Beetsterzwaag;Van Harinxmaweg 10, Beetsterzwaag, 9244 CJ, Netherlands;53.0586024;6.0899357;51;false;true;Modern French, Modern Cuisine;Drive onto the sprawling estate, follow the driveway through the rolling countryside and admire the stately mansion that houses Landgoed Lauswolt hotel. What a first impression! Inside, the high ceilings, marble fireplace, large chandelier and period features are enchanting. The terrace affords fantastic views over the golf greens. Everything is perfect down to the last detail, and that includes the food. Each ingredient receives meticulous attention, with sauces, creams and marinades elevating every dish. Classic French flavours and local produce are often accompanied by surprising trimmings. For example, the chef barbecues turbot to perfection and serves it with a rich potato mousseline and strips of smoked eel. He also adds the earthiness of beetroot, as well as the deep nuances of a vanilla-infused beurre blanc. The sommelier responds with some well-chosen gems to pair with these captivating flavours. A top-flight dining experience awaits you here. Even at teatime, this luxurious hotel has plenty of surprises up its sleeve!;Brunch,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1848;Apicius;Netherlands;Castricum;Van der Mijleweg 16, Castricum, 1901 KD, Netherlands;52.5589079;4.6561801;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Modern restaurant run by two passionate brothers, one in the kitchen, one in the dining room. Refined atmosphere, comfortable lounge and international selection of wines including some vintage burgundy wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1849;LIZZ;Netherlands;Gouda;Spieringstraat 1, Gouda, 2801 ZH, Netherlands;52.0106071;4.7134847;80;false;false;Creative French;The exquisite Weeshuis Hotel is housed in THE landmark edifice of the historic city of Gouda. The chic COCO champagne bar is the perfect spot to sample a lavish breakfast, a casual lunch, a wickedly tempting tea or a glass of champagne! Oozing with character, thanks to historic vaults, fresh bouquets of flowers and LIZZ’s signature luxury, you can expect a global experience in the capable hands of gifted Remco Kuijpers.The seasoned chef unveils his culinary sensitivity and flawless technique. Spices and subtle Asian acidity add a new dimension to first-class Dutch produce. He embarks you on a fascinating and occasionally amusing journey. For example, sweetbread acquires a new range of nuances thanks to an clever blend of sherry, umeboshi plums, cumin, sakura vinegar, shiso and pumpkin. High-flying craftsmanship that is rich in surprises, originality and expression without falling into the trap of cloying or staid – an instinctive sense of balance pervades every dish.One final word for the excellent service, attentive yet not fawning and for the mind-blowing wine-food pairing suggestions.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1850;Spetters;Netherlands;Breskens;Kaai 5, Breskens, 4511 RC, Netherlands;51.3952661;3.5681281;98;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;As soon as you enter this lounge-like restaurant, you are greeted by the breathtaking view of the boats bobbing about on the Western Scheldt. Spetters enjoys a prime location between the fish market and Breskens marina – and produce enthusiast Laurent Smallegange could not be happier as he showcases Zeeland's rich bounty, from Eastern Scheldt lobster to Sluis lamb. His cooking style is both creative and unassuming. The dishes are brought to life by international influences and zingy flavours, and the innovative preparation techniques are truly stimulating. Each creation is carefully conceived. He pairs succulent pan-fried sea bass, for example, with the earthiness of chanterelles in a creamy sauce in which the mushroom beautifully complements the richness of a poultry stock. The chef's signature dish, a combination of sweetbreads and Eastern Scheldt eel, is a testament to his culinary skill. No frills, just an abundance of sparkling flavours. If you would prefer to drop by in summer for a slightly simpler, casual lunch, do try Eb & Food just next door.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
1851;Fitzgerald;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Gelderseplein 49, Rotterdam, 3011 WZ, Netherlands;51.9191151;4.4903284;68;true;false;Modern French, International;"Too much of anything is bad, but too much Champagne is just right." This quote by F. Scott Fitzgerald could well have been written about this vibrant restaurant. One can't help but be won over by the Italian marble, the blend of modern and vintage design elements, the large glass windows, the charming courtyard and the chic bar serving delicious snacks and cocktails. Then there's the impressive wine list, featuring both established classics and exciting new finds. Michael Verhagen likes to give those great wines a run for their money by juxtaposing them with modern French cuisine. The sauces showcase his classical culinary knowhow, and he builds his dishes on this foundation. For example, he serves Anjou pigeon, roasted on the bone and seasoned with vadouvan, its rump succulently braised, a velvety pumpkin purée and a rich lentil dhal that perfectly complements the robust flavour of the pigeon and the earthy sweetness of the lentils. A real treat! The subtlety of his approach and the exciting interplay of flavours and textures are testament to his skill as a chef. Fitzgerald has style!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1852;The White Room by Jacob Jan Boerma;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Dam 9, Amsterdam, 1012 JS, Netherlands;52.372726;4.894229;84;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Contemporary design and classical elegance merge harmoniously in this dining space, which dates back to 1885 and is part of the Anantara Grand Hotel Krasnapolsky Amsterdam. The touches of gold in the decor create a sense of luxury. One can almost imagine an Austrian princess walking in at any moment. In this exclusive setting, the talented chef takes you on what will at times be a real adventure. You will immediately notice the use of fresh citrus, exotic spices and produce grown on Dutch soil. Expect vibrant, occasionally daring flavours. The young chef incorporates all this into imaginative dishes that showcase his technical prowess. Just like his team, he likes to come to the table to talk you through his creations. Think perfectly pink-roasted dry-aged lamb accompanied by a patiently reduced lamb jus, anchovies, morels and mushrooms filled with braised leg of lamb and magnolia flowers. Here you will enjoy international cuisine with modern sophistication as its guiding principle. The White Room is a true example of Amsterdam-style grandeur.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1853;Kaatje bij de Sluis;Netherlands;Blokzijl;Brouwerstraat 20, Blokzijl, 8356 DV, Netherlands;52.7265705;5.9611172;92;true;true;Organic, Creative French;Blokzijl is a picture-perfect little slice of the Netherlands. Opt for a table by the window to enjoy the delightful view of the lock and the quintessential brick houses. The wall decorated with cartoons is also sure to draw the eye. When it comes to the food, the dishes on the menu are testament to the creativity of the talented chef. With an eye for detail, he bends organic and local produce to his will. Fine classic flavours are shaken up in occasionally daring combinations. Lobster with blue cheese? Sardines and beetroot? It is the meticulous dosing that creates exciting nuances of flavour. The cheese and wine selections are equally tempting. It is no accident that, bar one year, Kaatje bij de Sluis has retained at least one Michelin star consistently since 1978. Quality reigns supreme here.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1855;Tout à Fait;Netherlands;Maastricht;St-Bernardusstraat 16, Maastricht, 6211 HL, Netherlands;50.8466488;5.6940708;55;false;true;Modern French;Tradition and originality are combined with a sure touch at Tout à Fait. Outside, you have the charm of Maastricht's centre, while inside you can enjoy the ambience of this chic restaurant, where the minimalist design underscores the character of the historical building. This is definitely a place where diners can feel comfortable and all the more so once the food arrives.Bart Ausems is a passionate chef who has accumulated years of know-how when it comes to the classics – you don't need to teach him how to make a beurre blanc sauce to serve with brill. The lightness of the sauce, which also possesses a fine acidity, denotes a real awareness of modern influences. He combines langoustine with an intense sauce made from the carcasses, but also with playful garnishes such as pickled vegetables. This is a chef who also likes to demonstrate his mastery of cuissons by cooking top-notch products such as pigeon on the rotisserie. The mainly French wine selection makes this experience tout à fait special.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1856;Triptyque;Netherlands;Wateringen;Plein 13G, Wateringen, 2291 CA, Netherlands;52.0247891;4.2741909;84;true;false;Creative, Country cooking;Niven Kunz is famous for his 80/20 concept: at Triptyque, vegetables and fruits make up at least 80% of each dish. A true ambassador for Westland, he frequently crosses the region to visit his suppliers. Along with hostess Virginie van Bronckhorst-Kunz, he aims to help you feel at one with nature. They do this subtly, with a certain natural ease. The elegant luxury of the decor also has a natural undertone, with details like dried flowers adding a touch of sophistication.With a highly personal creative approach, the chef puts the terroir in the spotlight. His dishes are defined by their deep, complex flavours. Through a multi-day process, he transforms carrots into a plant-based steak tartare that looks and tastes astonishingly like the real thing. A pickle gel and crunchy croutons add the final touch to this remarkable dish. He blends vibrancy and innovative techniques with rich sauces that provide a powerful foundation. This is purity redefined, paired with outstanding wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1858;De Leuf;Netherlands;Ubachsberg;Dalstraat 2, Ubachsberg, 6367 JS, Netherlands;50.8525486;5.9521343;80;true;false;Creative, Creative French;De Leuf is a really appealing family business run by hostess Sandra van de Bunt, her daughter Michelle, and son Robin, who is in charge in the kitchen. The trio's enthusiasm and dedication is extraordinary. The creative chef draws inspiration from his travels throughout Asia, without turning his back on the classic finesse for which this establishment is known. As soon as you enter, the team at the dining counter prepare a few appetisers for you. A combination of red shiso leaf ice cream, lukewarm rice and a sakura and black sesame seed coulis is a shining example of the intense Far Eastern flavours that are showcased here. Local produce and Asian seasonings complement each other beautifully. Sea bass marinated in miso, for instance, is accompanied by crispy flattened rice and a heavenly sauce based on shiitake and bonito flakes. This cuisine is technically accomplished, sophisticated and inspired. Chef Van de Bunt does not shy away from complexity. De Leuf's revamped decor combines regional materials with a Japanese zen feel. This half-timbered farmhouse (1769) is a paragon of contemporary class and character. Here, the Van de Bunt family propose a totally immersive experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1859;'t Lansink;Netherlands;Hengelo;C.T. Storkstraat 18, Hengelo, 7553 AR, Netherlands;52.2596759;6.7823645;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;'t Lansink is a warm and welcoming haven for food lovers. Established in 1916, this characterful house is located in the heart of the historical Tuindorp neighbourhood with its romantic gardens. The dedicated front-of-house team makes it its mission to pamper you. A friendly chat, expert wine recommendations, or an explanation of their fantastic cocktails? They are here for you, serving up the delicious creations of the enterprising Lars van Galen with real pride. He puts the spotlight on local ingredients such as Twente asparagus and game from the region, adding carefully considered garnishes and deeply flavoured sauces that showcase his culinary talent. Think pan-fried cod served beautifully translucent with aromatic oxtail, fried capers and a beurre blanc with capers for some added kick. At 't Lansink, the main ingredient is allowed to shine in visually appealing dishes. Why not enhance your culinary experience by booking yourself in for a thrilling spectacle at the chef's table or booking an overnight stay?;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1860;Alma;Netherlands;Oisterwijk;De Lind 45a, Oisterwijk, 5061 HT, Netherlands;51.5809993;5.1970972;58;false;false;Modern French;A potted history of the location that now houses Alma: it was once home to De Swaen, the restaurant where renowned chef Cas Spijkers, among others, was awarded one and then two MICHELIN stars. Today, Wouter van Laarhoven and Malou Hagenaars are upholding the restaurant's tradition of excellence. On the ground floor you will find the Bib Gourmand-awarded Alma Bodega, and fine dining restaurant Alma is on the first floor – a modern and elegant establishment with a fabulous terrace overlooking De Lind. Chef Van Laarhoven puts his heart and soul (alma in Spanish) into his dishes, combining inventiveness with technical skill. Authentic finesse lends a sense of coherence, while playful ideas breathe life into the dishes. In Mexico, for example, they got the idea of incorporating chicatana ants into beurre blanc, adding cocoa and umami nuances to their dish comprising briny Irish Mór oysters, buttery otoro sashimi, smoked soy and bone marrow melt. Rich sauces and subtle citrus notes take things up a notch. Rest assured you will find the perfect wine, as the pairings suggested by your hostess, who has a penchant for German wines, hit the spot every time.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1861;Amarone;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Meent 72a, Rotterdam, 3011 JN, Netherlands;51.9223914;4.483346;31;true;true;Modern French;The decor at Amarone is elegant, luxurious and alluring, featuring a white 3D wall by the open kitchen and artistic nods to Japan. This is a fantastic restaurant where you will immediately feel comfortable. Hostess and sommelier Yoshiko adds to the experience with her appealing wine list and astute recommendations. In the kitchen, chef Jan van Dobben expresses his love for classic and Japanese cuisine, expertly combining ingredients such as Wagyu and umeboshi with top-notch local produce. For instance, he elevates hamachi with a sweet and sour vinaigrette made with rice vinegar. He also adds a delightful spiciness to his venison dish, with a patiently reduced jus infused with star anise. The chef's technical mastery and creative flair result in dishes that beautifully balance out contrasting flavours. He reimagines the classics, a feat requiring great talent.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1862;Odille;Netherlands;Sint-Oedenrode;Markt 14, Sint-Oedenrode, 5492 AB, Netherlands;51.5644992;5.4604372;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Everything here revolves around the open kitchen, which is done out in black. Serenity and elegance abound at Odille, with artworks by Daisy Boman dotted throughout. Hostess Lotte Bloem and chef Casimir Evens invite you into their world, where time stands still for a moment as Brabantian generosity meets international finesse.The kitchen is a creative playground where bold flavours are expertly combined. The chef presents the Bresse pigeon at your table, showcasing the bird before it is roasted on the carcass. The finished dish arrives a little later: perfectly medium-rare fillets, a spicy broccoletto cream, bay leaf oil and crunchy vegetable garnishes. A full-bodied pigeon jus infused with summer savoury elevates this indulgent combination of classic and vegetal flavours. This chef brings his colourful creations to life with natural nuances and rich sauces. The finishing touch is provided by the carefully selected wines, which make for a truly harmonious dining experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1863;Restaurant Showw;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Gelrestraat 28, Amsterdam, 1079 MZ, Netherlands;52.337388;4.8928951;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It was at the MICHELIN-starred Bougainville that Chef Dorus Floris and sommelier Lendl Mijnhijmer first crossed paths and the seeds of this partnership were sown. The synergy between them is palpable – in the impeccable service, the lounge-like ambiance of this elegant open-plan restaurant, and especially in the way everything complements the food on your plate. Chef Floris effortlessly experiments with seasonings from around the globe and refreshing nuances. His intricate sauces showcase his exceptional technique. He artfully combines perfectly seared langoustines with Jerusalem artichoke, an intense bisque enriched with espresso and curry oil for just the right amount of heat. A symphony of flavours!Sommelier Lendl Mijnhijmer knows his stuff. He serves the wines without revealing the label, encouraging diners to discover the nuances before he provides his expert commentary. The extensive à la carte menu is testament to the pair's commitment to delighting diners. Showw is the result of two passionate creative minds coming together.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1864;Rijnzicht;Netherlands;Doornenburg;Sterreschans 15, Doornenburg, 6686 MS, Netherlands;51.8902472;6.0226879;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;An oyster shell filled with a goose liver crémeux topped with raw oyster pieces and an apple brunoise, accompanied by a sea buckthorn cream with sambal and oyster juice foam – this is the kind of inventive, highly technical creation that demonstrates Mike Cornelissen's talent. Representing the fourth generation of his family to run this restaurant, he has made it entirely his own. The interior has been transformed into a sleek and stylish space, but the terrace has retained its original charm. But it is his creativity and the beautiful presentation of his dishes that are most remarkable. The beautifully plated dishes are visually arresting. His imagination knows no bounds. Fantastic local produce such as trout from 't Smallert farm and Betuwe cherries are expertly combined with international seasonings. This is a unique culinary adventure that you conclude by toasting a marshmallow yourself on a table-top charcoal fire. The innovative set menu is updated every three months, surprising and delighting diners every time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1865;Restaurant De Burgemeester;Netherlands;Linschoten;Raadhuisstraat 17, Linschoten, 3461 CW, Netherlands;52.0619466;4.9146783;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Anne and Sander Spruijt have set up shop in the former town hall of picturesque Linschoten. The characterful building has retained its original charm and been enhanced with elegant additions. One look at the large glass-walled wine room makes it clear you have come to the right place to sample some first-rate labels. From the warm welcome to the post-dinner coffee and confectionery, you can look forward to genuine hospitality at De Burgemeester. Sander Spruijt is a technically proficient chef who loves to showcase his culinary skills – from marinating and smoking beetroots to dry-ageing beef in butter and herbs, he is a master of his craft, expertly combining textures and bold flavours. Take his succulent pike-perch, topped with a brunoise of Reypenaer cheese and a Jerusalem artichoke cream. Morels braised in butter and a punchy white wine sauce made with Pineau des Charentes add further complexity to this rich dish. His meticulous attention to detail ensures everything is spot on. A firm favourite!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1866;MOS;Netherlands;Amsterdam;IJdok 185, Amsterdam, 1013 MM, Netherlands;52.383797;4.895512;78;true;false;Creative French;The interior is relaxed and chic, the large windows offer a fantastic view of the IJ river, and the food is delicious. MOS is sublime. The chef shows how a little creativity conjures up a variety of prominent flavours, producing balanced combinations that are both rich and refined. Guests are advised to ask about parking when reserving.;Terrace;[]
1868;Restaurant Smink;Netherlands;Wolvega;Steenwijkerweg 2, Wolvega, 8471 LA, Netherlands;52.8763916;6.0017285;23;false;true;Creative, Modern French;Jan Smink is proud of his heritage as the son of a farmer and a Frisian. He is very much at home in charming Wolvega, where he has transformed a former bank branch. The interior is done out in black and incorporates natural materials to create warmth. This is certainly a charismatic and daring chef. His cuisine is carefully considered, challenging and exciting. With a wealth of experience and technical skill, he bends textures, temperatures and flavours to his will.Take one of his signature dishes: Delicate slices of steamed Jerusalem artichoke are placed in layers over a puree of the vegetable mixed with smoked eel to add punch and depth. This is topped with crispy bacon, a spoonful of caviar and also a bubbly sauce based on an aromatic oil. This is Jan Smink all over: creative, thinking outside the box without overcomplicating things. His use of tomato in various ways to enhance yellowtail with umami flavours is typical of his personal cooking style. This is a chef who is going places.;Air conditioning;[]
1869;The Millèn;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Weena 686, Rotterdam, 3012 CN, Netherlands;51.9226379;4.4714977;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Millennium Tower is a landmark in Rotterdam and, thanks to the arrival of this elegant design restaurant, it is now also a destination for foodies. Wim Severein shows his knowledge and inventiveness here by bringing together top quality ingredients and allowing them to interact with one other with a certain playfulness. His colourful compositions really are delicious!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1870;Meliefste;Netherlands;Wolphaartsdijk;Wolphaartsdijkseveer 1, Wolphaartsdijk, 4471 ND, Netherlands;51.5467659;3.8145823;85;false;true;Creative;Thijs Meliefste is a name synonymous with excellence. His restaurant is located in a picturesque setting, with a gorgeous terrace overlooking a marina on Veerse Meer lagoon. The decor in the intimate dining space is rather understated and evokes a sense of tranquillity. The glass-walled kitchen reveals a serene scene of food preparation. But think of it as the calm before the storm, because the arrival of the appetisers at your table brings a burst of intense sophistication. Chef Meliefste's cooking style is characterised by intricate details and a wide range of techniques. The natural bounty of Zeeland's soil and waters are his source of inspiration. His creativity shines through in his intricate dishes, each bite sparking your curiosity. Our inspectors were bowled over by his take on paling in 't groen (eel in a green herb sauce). A local fisherman delivers the fish at around noon, which guarantees exceptional quality. Chef Meliefste has a masterful way of bringing out the eel's natural richness. Garnishes such as crunchy kohlrabi and a watercress cream provide a refreshing contrast. And to top it off, the delectable sauce based on eel fumet and infused with aromatic herbs… Now, that is a dish with character – the artful presentation brings it to life. Captivating cuisine!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
1871;Da Vinci;Netherlands;Maasbracht;Havenstraat 27, Maasbracht, 6051 CS, Netherlands;51.1452279;5.8850739;42;false;true;Classic French;Da Vinci is a beautiful modern restaurant where you enjoy the good care of Margo Reuten. Thanks to the large glass pieces, you can see how controlled she works, which also proves her dishes: well - prepared, technically well - groomed and highly flavored. The sommelier knows perfectly what tasty wine fits with.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1872;De Bloemenbeek;Netherlands;De Lutte;Beuningerstraat 6, De Lutte, 7587 LD, Netherlands;52.319597;6.9978667;60;false;false;Modern French;An aperitif in the cosy salon, followed by attentive service in the stylish restaurant makes for a promising start. The flavourful sauces and well - balanced seasoning reveal the chef's classic training, while also applying modern techniques to achieve variety and finesse.;Car park,Terrace;[]
1873;Sense;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Jeroen Boschplein 6, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5211 ML, Netherlands;51.68833;5.3123;57;false;false;Creative;Respect for the seasons and a penchant for fresh Asian flavours – that is Dennis Middeldorp's creative cuisine in a nutshell. Deep down, however, he is a classical chef, which is evident in his beautifully risen soufflé or the turbot fillet fried in butter and accompanied by a mousseline made in time-honoured tradition. Meanwhile, the modern techniques that he implements for his garnishes and meticulous presentations reveal the chef's playful side.Of course, it is the eating that really counts at Sense. The flavours are full-bodied and powerful yet do not linger on the stomach. The option of ordering both full and half portions is something that many diners appreciate. Chef Middeldorp prefers to work with Dutch produce and also shows his creative streak when it comes to conjuring up dishes without meat and fish.This large, trendy establishment is perfect for those who wish to enjoy a casual meal out. Why not give yourself the time to explore the surrounding city centre at a leisurely pace by booking one of their comfortable guestrooms?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1874;Latour;Netherlands;Noordwijk aan Zee;Koningin Astrid Boulevard 5, Noordwijk aan Zee, 2202 BK, Netherlands;52.2415203;4.4271384;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Here you can admire how the beach merges with the North Sea. Red, yellow and ochre tones dominate the upscale decor in turn. The colourful rugs, art on the walls and classic furniture all add to Latour's luxurious, elegant feel. And then there is the extremely attentive service, which will make you feel like royalty! Kenny Friederichs infuses this magical place with a contemporary sense of style and energy. Terms such as dashi and ponzu are all part of his daily vocabulary. He combines exotic influences to enhance classics such as pan-seared sea bass, and even incorporates them into his desserts. With his perfectly cooked IJsselmeer pike-perch accompanied by various textures of leek and a rich smoked herring and horseradish sauce, he managed to silence our inspectors for a moment. A final word of advice: leave some room for the desserts, which are simply divine!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1875;Restaurant Atelier;Netherlands;Gulpen;Markt 9, Gulpen, 6271 BD, Netherlands;50.8155288;5.8914267;16;false;true;Creative French;At Atelier, you never know what to expect. Creative Hans Kinkartz knows how to link familiarity with excitement and every dish has a surprise in store. A prime example is his pan-seared red mullet, with its crispy skin and juicy flesh, which he pairs with wonderfully briny mussels with layers of lardo di Colonnata. A barigoule sauce and an espuma with baharat seasoning add that extra depth and a burst of freshness. The smoky notes of barbecued pineapple are offset by the subtle bite of ginger, umeboshi and a beautiful quenelle of chai ice cream. Chef Kinkartz is known for his love of Asian flavours, which give his dishes that extra dimension. With creative abandon, this experienced craftsman gives classic cooking techniques a fresh, modern twist. Each and every dinner in this historical half-timbered house, with its elegant symbiosis of contemporary design and industrial austerity, comes with its own surprises. Hostess Ellen, whose passion for wine is infectious, offers exceptional pairings. Atelier is synonymous with bespoke culinary craftsmanship.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1876;'t Vlasbloemeken;Netherlands;Koewacht;Nieuwstraat 8, Koewacht, 4576 AL, Netherlands;51.2254016;3.9770577;46;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Eric van Bochove's goal is to serve up "the best of the sea, soil and livestock", and his honest ingredient-led cuisine does not disappoint. He appreciates the great wealth of local produce at his disposal, such as Eastern Scheldt lobster and Zeeland lamb, which he prepares in the traditional way in order to respect their wonderful flavours. His garnishes give the dishes a more contemporary look. Take, for example, his scallops in a delicate Thai-style marinade and textures of cauliflower elevated by the bold aromas of sea buckthorn berry and a chorizo oil. This chef is remarkably talented. The charming hostess pampers diners with attentive service and astute wine recommendations – the selection is predominantly French. She ensures a comfortable dining experience, whether you are in the stylish interior, with its warm colours and elegant design, or out on the terrace. Satisfaction guaranteed!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1877;Flicka;Netherlands;Kerkdriel;Berm 47, Kerkdriel, 5331 KL, Netherlands;51.7851017;5.3222811;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Flicka is the epitome of a modern restaurant. Thomas van Santvoort has a wealth of experience gained at top-flight establishments such as Parkheuvel and Boreas. It was there that he learned, for example, to cook perfectly crispy sweetbreads. His flawless technique is highlighted by his own unique style. For example, he gives perfectly pan-seared cod an exciting twist with various textures of cauliflower and grey prawn. A jus made from the bones is then rounded out by incorporating a sherry cream emulsion – that’s efficiency that packs a punch! Chef Van Santvoort likes to add a vibrant kick of acidity to his dishes and deftly plays with sweet undertones. This elevates top-quality ingredients like turbot and langoustine to a whole new level. The sommelier cleverly plays on this with exciting wine pairings. Your journey to Flicka will be rewarded with views of the green surroundings and the River Meuse. The cosy decor also incorporates some charming designer touches. Last but not least, delightful suites are available for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1878;De Kas;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Kamerlingh Onneslaan 3, Amsterdam, 1097 DE, Netherlands;52.3522847;4.9302753;68;false;false;Organic;De Kas has grown steadily since it was established in 2001 and has now reached maturity. "From plant to plate" has always been the motto here, a vision of sustainability that seemed a tall order at the outset. But the team persevered and today are a standard-bearer of the MICHELIN Green Star. They grow about 300 varieties of vegetables, herbs and fruit both on site and in their larger field in the Beemster Polder. What is harvested in the morning from the imposing greenhouse will take pride of place on the plate a little later, in light, modern creations. Tip: make a beeline for the fabulous garden terrace. Wim de Beer and Jos Timmer are masters in the art of delicately balancing sweet and sour flavours. Subtle sauces highlight the creative vegetable dishes (sometimes with meat or fish). For example, a soft saffron cream elevates the smoky flavour of barbecued pointed cabbage, and the briny freshness of cockles is accentuated by a lime leaf emulsion. The wealth of natural produce that these chefs have at their disposal is a constant source of inspiration for their seemingly boundless creativity, and that is what foodies really revel in.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1879;Noble Kitchen;Netherlands;Cromvoirt;Deutersestraat 39B, Cromvoirt, 5266 AW, Netherlands;51.6657301;5.2302915;95;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Sushi;Are those UFOs on Bernardus golf course? It may look like that, but this futuristic building actually houses a beautifully designed restaurant that exudes casual luxury. The terrace on the golfing greens is simply divine! Diners are presented with an extensive menu on which each description of a dish is more tempting than the last. You will want to try everything! The chefs draw heavily on Asian influences in their dishes. Start off with a few appetisers and some exquisite sushi, follow it with classic sole, for example, and be sure to sample the high-quality meat served straight from the Robata grill. This cuisine is sophisticated and intriguing, with subtle Eastern touches creating excitement every time. Noble Kitchen is the kind of place you want to go to every day – to discover new taste sensations during a relaxed meal.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
1880;Pieters Restaurant;Netherlands;Bergambacht;Hoofdstraat 73, Bergambacht, 2861 AL, Netherlands;51.9344511;4.7831714;68;true;false;Modern French;You’ll feel very much at home when you dine at Pieter and Paula’s pleasant restaurant. Here, the welcoming interior provides a perfect backdrop for a delightful gastronomic experience created by chef Pieter who calls upon all his experience and an abundance of enthusiasm. Far from being show cuisine, his cooking demonstrates a classical finesse in keeping with traditional techniques, coupled with attractive, playful and highly original touches.;Terrace;[]
1881;Zenith;Netherlands;Apeldoorn;Koninginnelaan 37, Apeldoorn, 7315 BL, Netherlands;52.2229529;5.9561316;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Having both worked at various MICHELIN-starred restaurants, hostess Jody and chef Joey share a deep-seated passion for the culinary arts. Together, they create a dining experience that is flawless down to every last detail. Street art is a key feature of the decor in this restaurant, which is housed in an elegant street corner building. Diners can look forward to attentive service and exceptional wine pairings.Beauty and substance go hand in hand: Joey Stinissen's elaborate creations are pleasing both to the eye and the palate. With a preference for organic ingredients, the chef uses exotic spice blends for just the right kick. For instance, the medium-rare duck breast is enveloped in a crispy gremolata and pumpkin seed coating, delicately sweetened with paprika and elevated with rendang spices. The dish is made complete by a bao bun seasoned with ras el hanout. It is evident in his decision to include more varied dishes in the surprise menu than in the à la carte that this is a chef who does not shy away from hard work. A labour of love.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1882;Vista;Netherlands;Willemstad;Havenhoofd 2, Willemstad, 4797 SR, Netherlands;51.696117;4.443638;85;false;false;Modern French;The view from this elegant pavilion, taking in the Hollands Diep River and the marina, is so enchanting it's almost impossible to describe. The dancing waves, visible through the expansive glass windows, create a mesmerising effect. Henrie van der Heijden marries classic cooking techniques with international influences, adding a vibrant and lively touch. Thanks to the small portions, you can decide which horizons to explore in your set menu. Savour the flavours of France with an unctuous chicken, pata negra and foie gras terrine… Or embark on an Asian culinary voyage and tuck into tender red mullet and poached lobster tail elevated by a fragrant green curry lobster sauce. Chef Van der Heijden adds his distinctive contemporary flair to these beautifully balanced and incredibly delicious dishes. The exquisite sauces and vinaigrettes he uses to complement the main ingredients showcase the craftsmanship of a talented chef.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1883;De Gieser Wildeman;Netherlands;Noordeloos;Botersloot 1, Noordeloos, 4225 PR, Netherlands;51.9019056;4.9391336;71;false;false;Classic French, Creative French;Picture the scene: you are sitting under the thatched roof of a converted farmhouse, surrounded by stylish interior design and pleasing decorative features, looking through the conservatory out onto the beautiful garden and the river. A delightful setting for a culinary escapade! With his mastery of classic culinary techniques, René Tichelaar is not to be outdone by the surroundings.He picks up creative ideas here and there and has a good feel for the current zeitgeist, but the basis of this cuisine lets tradition speak for itself. This is evident, for instance, in the Mediterranean garnishes that give a nice piece of lamb from the Pyrenees the necessary depth of flavour. Or how about scallop ravioli combined with the salty nuances of caviar, the generosity of a beurre blanc sauce and the tanginess of chives? This chef works meticulously and is adept at structuring his dishes.Speaking of harmony, the acclaimed sommelier deserves a mention. Drawing on an extensive selection of wines from around the globe, he comes up with some amazing pairings. The cheerful front-of-house team provide excellent service, as befits this elegant setting. You might want to pinch yourself to check you're not dreaming!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1885;Bougainville;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Dam 27, Amsterdam, 1012 JS, Netherlands;52.3725511;4.8931716;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In Bougainville, a top-class fine dining experience awaits you. Warm fabrics, luxurious design and bronze tones come together in a setting that is intimate and romantic. The contrast with the features of this historical building is indeed something to behold, and the magnificent view of Dam Square is equally remarkable. Tim Golsteijn's cuisine is in keeping with the sophisticated surroundings.He marries flavours from East and West with a creativity that is all his own. For this chef, technical skill and culinary instinct go hand in hand. He effortlessly balances the intensity of ingredients such as Thai green curry and za'atar spices with delicate French aromas. Chef Golsteijn does not shy away from daring combinations, but always ensures that the flavours enhance each other. A fine example of this is the perfectly pan-seared foie gras served with a Madeira wine jus and frozen raspberry pearls. An interplay of flavours, textures and temperatures that you won't be able to get enough of!Every visit to Bougainville brings a fascinating discovery. And it is made all the more exciting by the sommelier's amazing discoveries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1886;Château Neercanne;Netherlands;Maastricht;Von Dopfflaan 10, Maastricht, 6213 NG, Netherlands;50.8186702;5.66746;19;false;false;French Contemporary;This terraced castle is full of character and historical charm. From the herringbone parquet flooring to the impressive chandeliers, this place is a classic restaurant at heart. The views over the Baroque gardens and the Jeker Valley are simply stunning! An aperitif or coffee in the historical Marl Caves is an experience in itself. With a feel for the zeitgeist, Robert Levels breathes new life into French classics. Vegetables are harvested from his own garden (an appealing vegetarian set menu is available), and the sauces are always outstanding. A masterpiece in its own right, his foie gras terrine is served with a compote that provides a refreshing sweetness, along with a rich veal jus vinaigrette. His jus made from seasonal vegetables lends depth to the crispy blade steak. Chef Levels tempers the intense flavours of classical cuisine with exciting exotic touches, giving vegetables the attention they deserve and focusing on palatability. A castle fairy tale par excellence!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1887;De Nederlanden;Netherlands;Vreeland;Duinkerken 3, Vreeland, 3633 EM, Netherlands;52.2295965;5.0324559;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;De Nederlanden bears its name well. The decor, the charming service and the culinary style lend this former country hotel a quintessentially Dutch atmosphere. This building has plenty of character, combining historical charm with contemporary sleekness. From your table you can either watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen or take in the delightful view of the River Vecht and the drawbridge.It is clear from the menu that Wilco Berends loves his terroir. When it comes to produce such as lamb, eel and cheese, rest assured that the chef will serve you the very best the region has to offer. Be sure to try his oyster dishes – a speciality and a great start to your meal! What follows is the result of a blend of classic expertise and contemporary playful creativity. A shining example is the slow-cooked cod that chef Berends presents on crispy fennel brunoise, combined with cockles and mussels, and finished off with a sublime buttery jus based on the cooking water from the cockles and mussels.One final tip: If you want to experience De Nederlanden to the fullest, book one of the magnificent guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1888;Joann;Netherlands;Enschede;Nijverheidstraat 2, Enschede, 7511 JM, Netherlands;52.2202127;6.8911478;19;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Located on the outskirts of Enschede, Joann is an inviting restaurant that seamlessly blends contemporary sophistication with the old-world charm of the 1916 listed building that houses it. The bustling activity in the open kitchen is as captivating as a stage performance. The combined efforts of chef Emiel Kwekkeboom in the kitchen and hostess Mandy and her team front-of-house ensure a memorable dining experience – complete with a fantastic wine list.The chef likes to showcase the best of his own vegetable and herb garden in dishes that strike a perfect balance of heat, acidity and finesse. He gives free reign to his culinary creativity, for instance, presenting perfectly pan-seared red mullet on a brunoise of white grapes and a lemon gel. This is complemented by subtly marinated celeriac and a bagna cauda emulsion infused with the robust flavours of hazelnut and anchovy. At Joann, each plate is brought to life by aromatic sauces and carefully balanced exotic spices. If you prefer, you can upgrade the set menu to a more upscale version, or opt for the vegetarian alternative. In any case, you can expect excellent value for money.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1889;ONE;Netherlands;Roermond;ECI 17, Roermond, 6041 MA, Netherlands;51.1895014;5.9808834;59;false;true;Creative;This place is ONE of a kind. Housed in a converted factory, the restaurant blends raw industrial elements with trendy decor featuring unusual art including murals. The terrace at the Roer River is a fabulous spot in which to unwind. You are in good hands here, which you will sense as soon as the charming Canadian hostess comes to the table. She is your guide as you venture into Edwin Soumang's world of culinary sustainability. The chef boasts an urban kitchen garden of no less than 1 000m2, and he understands that the foundation of any great dish is the quality of its ingredients. What he does not grow himself, he sources as locally as possible. His creativity is inspired by the richness of his terroir. He accompanies Geuldal suckling lamb neck he not only with a rich lamb jus, but also a zingy yoghurt dressing with mint oil and crisp vegetable accoutrements. He incorporates Wellant apple into a soufflé prepared in time-honoured tradition, and serves it with vanilla ice cream and an apple compote. A captivating dining experience!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1890;Zeezout;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Westerkade 11b, Rotterdam, 3016 CL, Netherlands;51.9061331;4.4774595;44;false;true;Seafood, French;With Patrick ’t Hart, you can be sure of one thing – he cooks only the best that the sea has to offer. His original dishes preserve the pure flavour of the ingredients, while his vast experience allows him to use a wide range of culinary techniques and a selection of distinctive and playful garnishes. A maritime dining experience with real style.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1891;Zout & Citroen;Netherlands;Oosterhout;Ridderstraat 86, Oosterhout, 4902 AC, Netherlands;51.6403763;4.8594267;37;true;true;Creative, World Cuisine;Bram Helleman has a knack for elevating everyday ingredients, such as salt and lemon, and his unique combinations and preparations, create dishes with deep flavours and nuances. For instance, he uses miso mayonnaise to give his steak tartare a unusual twist. He seasons pike-perch with tandoori spices without losing the delicate flavour of the fish. These are the creative details that make his colourful dishes stand out. From the very first amuse-bouche, chef Helleman showcases his exuberant vision, which draws on influences from around the globe. With his controlled use of piquancy and oriental spices,he creates dishes that are both flavourful and intriguing. We definitely recommend his signature dish, "Nectar & Ambrosia", which is a combination of foie gras, apricot, honey and truffle. To help you find the perfect accompaniment to this whirlwind of flavours, Sjoerd and Patricia are on hand with astute recommendations from the impressive selection of international wines. With its sleek interior design and views of the magnificent garden, this former coach house is now a delightful culinary oasis. This is the place to come for an elegant contemporary fine dining experience!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1893;Basiliek;Netherlands;Harderwijk;Vischmarkt 57 L, Harderwijk, 3841 BE, Netherlands;52.3512404;5.6209585;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Born and bred in Harderwijk, Yornie van Dijk has taken over the restaurant of his former boss Rik Jansma and made it his own. The interior combines specially commissioned drawings, exposed brick walls and high-end materials. In short: a cosy place where the open kitchen draws the eye. Chef Van Dijk makes the nuances of contemporary cuisine his own, with a sure touch when it comes to balancing acidity and seasonings. It is clear that he is a proponent of Nordic Cuisine, a purist cooking style to which he gives his own spin.Details such as unripe and green strawberries in dry-aged hamachi lend his dishes that extra dimension. Sourced as locally as possible, vegetables and herbs play a key role. And whether it is a delicate beurre blanc to accompany skrei, or red gurnard served with a lemon zest cream and a sea buckthorn berry jus with a robust jus made with the bones, the chef has a unique way of dealing with intense flavours. Rest assured: Basiliek is as much a top destination for foodies as it ever was!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1894;Tante Koosje;Netherlands;Loenen aan de Vecht;Kerkstraat 1, Loenen aan de Vecht, 3632 EL, Netherlands;52.2090905;5.0235487;39;false;false;Modern French;Today, Koosje Edema's former home is a beacon for gourmets. The old-world interior is cosy and charming, and in summer the terrace exudes a Mediterranean feel. The versatile Roland Veldhuijzen gives his dishes a new twist every now and then, but really it is good old-fashioned culinary expertise that sets him apart.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1895;'t Amsterdammertje;Netherlands;Loenen aan de Vecht;Rijksstraatweg 119, Loenen aan de Vecht, 3632 AB, Netherlands;52.2098585;5.0216548;79;false;false;Creative, Fusion;This converted farmhouse is the place to come for an upbeat dining experience in a vibrant and trendy setting. Great music plays in the background, large chandeliers hang from the ceiling, modern art adorns the wall… This is a restaurant with a hip vibe. Working in an attractive open kitchen, André Gerrits's creativity befits the setting. His cuisine has panache and knows no limits.In his international creations he gives pride of place to vegetables from his own garden, along with other gems of Dutch produce. Finishing off a foamy oyster beurre blanc with sereh lemongrass, enhancing a pumpkin gravy by adding kimchi made from vegetables… These culinary creations are playful and lighthearted, but it is the strong flavours that always win over diners. And you can rest assured that Chef Gerrits also has classic recipes up his sleeve, such as sea bass in a salt crust.Amsterdammertje doesn't take itself too seriously, but the execution remains truly professional. Be sure to check out their delicatessen, Marché.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1896;Restaurant Affect;Netherlands;Zwolle;Thorbeckegracht 41, Zwolle, 8011 VN, Netherlands;52.5148152;6.0960319;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Lars Aukema is a chef who does not need top-of-the-range ingredients to create exciting dishes. Having worked under the tutelage of Jonnie Boer for a long time, he has now proven himself to be a dab hand at showcasing flavours from the region and around the globe. He combines, for instance, yellowtail tartare with crunchy kohlrabi, topped with yellowtail sashimi and dusted with black cardamom and kaffir lime zest. Lime gel, marinated green strawberry and a fermented kohlrabi broth add the finishing touches to this understated dish. This is a subtle flavour combination you won't forget. This is a chef who possesses exceptional technique and has the audacity to create bold flavour combinations.Lars Aukema and his team offer a choice between a set menu (vegetarian version available) and a tempting à la carte selection. You can rely on Robin, your knowledgeable sommelier, to recommend the perfect wine pairings. The charming hostess Lisa deserves a special mention. Restaurant Affect is a wonderfully welcoming place for those who appreciate pure, unadulterated flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
1897;Sabero;Netherlands;Leende;Zevenhuizen 6, Leende, 5595 XE, Netherlands;51.3439516;5.5591862;53;false;false;Asian and Western;The names Sonja and Nico Boreas have been synonymous with excellence on the Dutch fine dining scene for many years. Having decided to scale down their operation, they now invite you to this cosy restaurant located on the ground floor of their own home. The couple consistently demonstrate that their expertise is indisputable: in the case of hostess Sonja, she impresses with her wine list and the natural ease with which she works the room, providing service with a personal touch to each and every diner.Chef Nico's personalised cuisine and bold flavours leave a lasting impression. He has a knack for creating complex sauces and sets himself apart with his use of exotic seasonings. Sole fillets, for example, are accompanied by a jus infused with yuzu koshō and a beurre blanc with koji, which adds depth and vibrancy to the dish. Nico Boreas is a savvy chef who can bring out the best in any ingredient. Be sure to add the cheese cart to your set menu – you'll be glad you did. Sabero is, and always will be, a firm favourite!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
1898;Sushi Masuda;Canada;Vancouver;1066 W. Hastings St., Vancouver, V6E 3X2, Canada;49.2876672;-123.1191909;26;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Entering this humble five-seat counter that is tucked in the corner of an unrelated restaurant and through the glass doors of a print shop serves as a pointed reminder not to judge a book by its cover. The plain, spare room is brought to life by the artfully simple, meticulous preparations of Chef Yoji Masuda, whose time spent in a top counter in Tokyo is amply apparent, though his own personality comes through. With the assistance of his wife Akari, who provides a warm, attentive hospitality, the meal proceeds gracefully, from an indulgent savory "pudding" of sweet, pure-tasting monkfish liver to a wonderfully gelatinous beltfish cooked with sake and kombu, before arriving at the impeccable nigiri, which showcase exceptional ingredients alongside a singular delicacy and precision.;;[]
1899;Okeya Kyujiro;Canada;Vancouver;1038 Mainland St., Vancouver, V6B 2T4, Canada;49.2752472;-123.1214293;58;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Hosts dressed in stunning traditional clothing guide you to a dark room, lit only by the faintest glow from votive candles. A black curtain is raised ceremoniously only when the clock strikes the precise minute of your seating. These are the first clues that this is far from your typical omakase. From the premium, hyper-seasonal fish to the demonstration of sasagiri (traditional Japanese bamboo leaf carving), it is a memorable show from start to finish. Highlights include chawanmushi with crab, shatteringly crispy tempura sandbar fish, spicy firefly squid on a bamboo skewer, and a presentation of two uni petals from different Japanese waters served with seaweed jam. Sweet courses garner attention, especially wagashi, fashioned into a flower here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1901;iDen & QuanJuDe Beijing Duck House;Canada;Vancouver;2808 Cambie St., Vancouver, V5Z 2V5, Canada;49.2602703;-123.1144584;98;true;true;Chinese, Duck Specialities;It has a pedigree that traces back to an original location in Beijing from 1864, but the latest outpost in Vancouver proves that this legacy hasn't lost any of its luster. Indeed, the gold-accented dining room is a feast for the eyes, blending classic opulence with strikingly modern design.They are best known for their superlatively crispy and juicy duck. Delicious as the signature fowl may be, there is plenty more: a bevy of other delicacies are on offer, including bird's nest, sea cucumber and even a whole king crab if you're up for a splurge. It's not all razzle-dazzle, though. The cooking displays a deft hand with ingredients of all stripes from simple stir-fried mustard greens with garlic to a broth of abalone and matsutake.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1902;St. Lawrence;Canada;Vancouver;269 Powell St., Vancouver, V6A 1G3, Canada;49.2832679;-123.0978836;20;true;false;French, Regional Cuisine;Charm abounds at this beloved Québécois bistro. Sit close enough to Chef/owner Jean-Christophe Poirier's kitchen to experience the heady aromas of his refined yet indulgent French-Canadian cooking, featuring ethereal sauces and a characteristic use of sweetness. The fixed menu changes seasonally, but signature additions like oreilles de crisse (crispy pig ears tossed in maple syrup and spices) and a savory éclair filled with duck liver mousse, are well worth considering for those who desire an extra hit of richness. Otherwise, the meal begins with thoughtful canapés and proceeds to heartier fare like charcoal-grilled duck with chou-farci and wheat berries. For dessert, you’ll get a final dose of sweetness, perhaps in the guise of a maple St.-Honoré with Chantilly and caramel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1903;AnnaLena;Canada;Vancouver;1809 W. 1st Ave., Vancouver, V6J 5B8, Canada;49.2708003;-123.1468282;96;true;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;You won't find white tablecloths or a formal atmosphere, but make no mistake, you will find one of Vancouver's most polished—and delicious—dining experiences. Effortless service, expertly prepared cocktails, and unusually astute wine pairings are all part of the magic, but of course it's the seasonally inspired tasting menu that really steals the show. Its globally accented cuisine consistently impresses, marrying precise technique and top-flight ingredients together in refined, focused dishes of exceptional clarity and depth of flavor. From a single pristine oyster decked out with apple jalapeño mignonette and finely shaved foie gras, to dry-aged duck breast with impeccable scallop agnolotti and chili oil, each plate is sure to delight discerning palates.;;[]
1904;Published on Main;Canada;Vancouver;3593 Main St., Vancouver, V5V 3N4, Canada;49.2529239;-123.1007713;21;true;false;Contemporary, North American;Timing is everything, but Chef Gus Stieffenhofer-Brandson and his team have a preternatural ability for sensing when produce is at its peak. Whether showcasing it on the plate or pickling and preserving it (those jars even double as decor), they're sourcing and foraging from local farms and forests.The contemporary fare bears the chef's distinct imprimatur. This is food that is at once familiar and surprising. A small dish of asparagus with brown butter crouton and a sauce gribiche is the very essence of spring, while an artful bowl with a pinwheel of side-striped prawns, refreshing apple and cucumber and a cool touch of horseradish delivers a sweet-tart, one-two punch. The roasted halibut's lush and buttery "broth" is unlike anything you anticipated.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1905;Kissa Tanto;Canada;Vancouver;263 E. Pender St., Vancouver, V6A 1T8, Canada;49.2805255;-123.0980763;97;false;true;Fusion, Contemporary;Inspired by the jazz cafes of 1960s Tokyo, Kissa Tanto seduces with a moody vibe complete with white mosaic floors, antique Japanese panels and steely colored walls loaded with artwork and photos. This ambitious kitchen pulls no punches with its mingling of Japanese and Italian cuisine. The "omakase" menu pulls dishes from their à la carte offerings as well as a sprinkling of compelling off-menu items. The region's bounty is on full display in dishes such as roasted and fried celeriac served with onion and mushroom dashi. The cultural collision is best seen in dishes like the tajarin, hand-cut pasta dressed in butter, miso-cured egg yolk and parmesan. Tiramisu takes an Eastern turn with an ethereal, plum wine-soaked tofu filling.;Air conditioning;[]
1906;Burdock & Co;Canada;Vancouver;2702 Main St., Vancouver, V5T 3E8, Canada;49.2609423;-123.1006287;86;false;false;Contemporary, North American;This Mount Pleasant charmer straddles a corner of Main Street in an area rich with top spots, but Burdock & Co stands out with its rustic appeal and Chef Andrea Carlson's farm-to-table cooking. The concise menu highlights the best of the season. First, grilled sourdough, herb-flavored gougère and nori cornbread with aged sake kasu butter prove that this is not your average bread basket. Then, miniature Hazelmere radishes roasted with house-made shio koji deliver unexpected glee. Morels stuffed with halibut mousse resting beside delicate gnocchi in a green garlic sauce embody the fleeting beauty of spring. Finally, the deconstructed chocolate soufflé with miso caramel and smoked mascarpone is a decadent delight.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1908;Restaurant Pearl Morissette;Canada;Lincoln;3953 Jordan Rd., Lincoln, L0R 1S0, Canada;43.1560307;-79.3559402;40;false;false;Contemporary;This 42-acre destination in the picturesque Niagara region is the full experience. A restaurant, winery, orchard, farm, and bakery, Restaurant Pearl Morissette is a powerhouse. With great pride for Canadian ingredients and respect for the seasons, Chefs Daniel Hadida and Eric Robertson make the most of their surroundings to enhance their spontaneous tasting menu's dishes, as in free-range pork, slow roasted over a peach wood fire, glazed with sweet potato miso, and plated with hazelnut jus. Yes, there is plenty of wine available, but don’t miss the accomplished juice pairing either. The meal may conclude sweetly, with a buckwheat sable cookie, honey whipped cream, honeycomb-shaped tuile, and honey ice cream. Meanwhile, the warm team keeps the tasting moving at a friendly clip.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
1910;Quetzal;Canada;Toronto;419 College St., Toronto, M5T 1T1, Canada;43.6565748;-79.4067462;72;true;true;Mexican;It is all hands on deck at this high-style destination. Almost everything on this tight menu passes through the kitchen’s 26-foot-long wood-burning grill that actively roars and smokes. At the end of the line is a single chef at the earthenware comal, who prepares tortillas from heirloom corn that is nixtmalized and ground in-house. Lamb barbacoa packed into griddled, blue masa tortillas and charred maitake mushrooms set in a crema poblana highlight the transformative magic of fire, while dry-aged amberjack aguachile flexes the kitchen’s delicate side. Can’t decide? Servers are happy to build you a tasting menu. All the while, bartenders rise to the occasion with refined, agave-based cocktails in a narrow space that has all the coolness and vibrancy of Mexico City.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1911;Hexagon;Canada;Oakville;210 Lakeshore Rd. E., Oakville, L6M 3R7, Canada;43.4457745;-79.6681049;56;false;true;Contemporary;This stylish restaurant in downtown Oakville could get by on looks alone with its sliding patio doors, wrap-around terrace, and an interior that is at once cool and casual. But for Chef Rafael Covarrubias, he’s got a lot more in mind. The menu reads familiar – beef tartare, oysters, fish – but what emerges from the kitchen are beautiful, soigné works that are refined, original, and substantial. Potato foam, brown butter, and roe are clever pairings with Hokkaido scallop. Pasta is a highlight, like corn agnolotti with Manchego, but so too is the short rib. And for dessert, cheesecake is surprisingly light and savory thanks to strawberries and a nutty almond cookie. To see this kitchen at its most ambitious, guests can book a tasting menu in advance.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
1912;Kaiseki Yu-zen Hashimoto;Canada;North York;6 Sakura Way, North York, M3C 1Z5, Canada;43.7263028;-79.3341896;63;true;true;Japanese;It may be connected to the Canadian Japanese Cultural Center but it’s not until you walk through the labyrinthine passages of this restaurant that you feel you’ve been transported to Japan. This is the very opposite of the see-and-be-seen culture: all guests have their own private room so it’s the perfect choice for that intimate dinner, family celebration or important business deal.Chef Masaki Hashimoto's traditional kaiseki eight-course menu showcases the seasons while celebrating Japanese ingredients. From beautiful sashimi - which could be line-caught sea bream – through to grilled cutlass fish and steamed jackfish, and from delicate soup to grilled Miyazaki wagyu: all the dishes are beautiful to behold, balanced, delicate and rewarding. The Shizouka musk melon will leave you wondering why all fruit doesn’t taste this good.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
1913;Kappo Sato;Canada;Toronto;575 Mount Pleasant Rd., Toronto, M4S 2M5, Canada;43.7034841;-79.3880837;24;false;false;Japanese, Contemporary;Unlike the quiet ceremony of a sushi omakase or the formal structure of a kaiseki, this freewheeling tasting is driven solely by Chef Takeshi Sato, who swims in familiar culinary waters on his own terms. To be clear, this counter situated along the entire open kitchen is no Zen temple. The room is a constant blur of motion thanks to a young team that hurries about preparing multiple courses at once. Sato is their seasoned guide, as he moves with intention, ever masterful with a knife, and works with an impressive bounty of ingredients, most of which are flown in from Japan. Soulful dashi broths weave in and out of view alongside clever courses like tempura fried mackerel with shiso or seared toro nigiri with Japanese green onions.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1914;Edulis;Canada;Toronto;169 Niagara St., Toronto, M5V 1C9, Canada;43.6419055;-79.4063364;55;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;"Sweet" can sometimes be a somewhat pejorative time, but there’s something very earnest and endearing about this charming little house, with its small flower-filled patio in front. The interior is filled with assorted bric-a-brac and comes in a warm yellow palette. The pride and passion of the husband-and-wife chef-owners and their staff is also undeniably evident, and the atmosphere is welcoming and nicely relaxed. The set multicourse menu – for which you pay in full at the time of booking – is largely inspired by the Mediterranean. The kitchen focuses on pairing complementary seasonal flavors, such as Mahone Bay scallops with wild onion, and Newfoundland cod with Manila clams and Butifarra sausage. Freshly carved Spanish ham, cheese and dessert are available as add-ons.;Air conditioning;[]
1915;Osteria Giulia;Canada;Toronto;134 Avenue Rd., Toronto, M5R 2H6, Canada;43.6744503;-79.3967752;49;false;true;Italian, Seafood;It seems nearly impossible to have a bad time at Chef Rob Rossi’s Italian stunner. Flickering candlelight bounces off cream-colored walls and blond-oak tables running down the length of this restaurant that feels, at all times, totally under control thanks to a suave staff. And whereas many Italian menus can look the same, Rossi narrows in on the seafood-rich traditions of Liguria. A superbly light vitello tonnato and a piping hot Ligurian flatbread stuffed with stracchino offer promising starts. There must be pasta, like squid ink spaghetti with Nova Scotia lobster, and there must be panna cotta. A deep Italian wine list and an especially talented cocktail program round out an experience that is as accomplished as it is hospitable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1916;Enigma Yorkville;Canada;Toronto;23 St. Thomas St., Toronto, M5S 3E7, Canada;43.6692078;-79.3908739;71;false;false;Contemporary;Chef Quinton Bennett has an international resume and a well-traveled kitchen team, so influences and techniques can range from the Nordics to Nihon. Dishes are delicate, poised and detailed creations – he certainly doesn’t make life easy for his brigade as there’s always plenty of intricacy happening on each plate. Fortunately, the flavors are always complementary, with Atlantic halibut paired with chanterelles and Australian wagyu with bone marrow. Desserts, like raspberry and yuzu with puff pastry, are often the highlight. The wine pairings are also thoughtfully composed. All you have to do, when you book a table at this handsome Yorkville restaurant, is decide whether you want 6, 8 or 10 of the surprise courses.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
1917;DaNico;Canada;Toronto;440 College St., Toronto, M5T 1T3, Canada;43.6566586;-79.4075777;27;true;false;Italian, Contemporary;Wondering if DaNico is worth a stop? You can take it to the bank—quite literally, as the restaurant is nestled inside a former bank building. Inside, dark colors, linen tablecloths, and plush seating set a sophisticated tone, but the irreverent artwork proves they don't take themselves too seriously. Chef/partner Daniele Corona cooks Italian food with a global influence. Choose from a multicourse prix-fixe or a chef's tasting menu to enjoy items such as wild Pacific crab served over thin, noodle-like vegetables, garnished with trout roe, and finished tableside with a Sicilian green olive coulis. Then, house-made basil bottini filled with smoked burrata is nestled in a creamy sauce for a dish that delivers dialed-in flavor.;Air conditioning;[]
1919;Alo;Canada;Toronto;163 Spadina Ave., Toronto, M5V 2L6, Canada;43.6484741;-79.3960828;47;true;true;Contemporary, French;Everyone has a good time at Chef Patrick Kriss’s beloved Alo. You can sense this much at the lively bar, where walk-ins are treated like VIPs by personable servers.Basking in the light of the open kitchen, the cozy dining room sees just as much excitement, and the talented beverage team offers spot-on suggestions from the well-chosen wine list. The kitchen team seamlessly merges European and Asian sensibilities onto a single tasting menu with dishes like creamy Koshihikari risotto boosted with porcini emulsion or rack of lamb with Thai green curry. They can cook the classics too, like Dover sole with caviar beurre blanc. Showcasing flexibility and talent, Alo is the rare high achiever that never takes itself too seriously.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1921;Aburi Hana;Canada;Toronto;102 Yorkville Ave., Toronto, M5R 1B9, Canada;43.6709928;-79.3923036;64;true;true;Japanese;The air is charged, and as you descend underneath Yorkville, you sense that your evening is headed somewhere interesting. Minimalist in design, Aburi Hana saves the drama for the plates, using handmade Arita pottery that has a history tracing back to the 1600s.Chef Ryusuke Nakagawa presents a modern take on the history-steeped Kyō-Kaiseki menu. His cooking is personal and intricate, weaving multiple techniques and colors into every dish. The signature maguro flower, a rose made from pieces of akami and chutoro, is stunning, and kurobuta kakuni, simmered pork belly over foie gras, dazzles. Aji fry takes fish sourced from the chef's home prefecture and riffs on his mother's recipe for a deeply satisfying effort. Dessert delivers a sweet finale.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
1922;Alma Fonda Fina;USA;Denver;2556 15th St., Denver, 80211, USA;39.7582201;-105.0116429;45;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Chef Johnny Curiel started off in his family’s restaurant in Guadalajara, and after years of high-end culinary experience, he revisits dishes and flavors from his upbringing with creativity and finely honed technique delivering results that are both satisfying and delicious. Resist the temptation to fixate on any one item, as the menu is littered with treasures: perfectly crisped pork belly carnitas make for a brilliant taco on a sourdough flour tortilla, while agave-roasted sweet potato with nutty salsa matcha and luxuriously creamy whipped requesón is a revelation, and vibrant seafood crudos like thinly sliced Maine diver scallop with tomatillo and apple aguachile are downright electric. No desserts are offered for the time being, so there’s no reason to leave any extra room.;;[]
1923;Brutø;USA;Denver;1801 Blake St., Denver, 80202, USA;39.7527561;-104.9969767;21;true;true;Contemporary;This hip spot from Kelly Whitaker's Id Est Hospitality Group is tucked away in the Dairy Block's Free Market. Chef Byron Gomez runs the show here, where the team takes a serious approach to locality and seasonality, including a dedicated fermentation program that highlights both grains and produce. The mastery of the hearth as the primary cooking implement makes this operation special, and infuses each of the tasting menu's courses with distinct notes. The menu, which incorporates Japanese and Nordic elements, has a clear narrative, embodied in dishes like kombu-cured diver scallop with fermented crabapple and chamomile. The non-alcoholic pairings are especially intriguing, as in the lamb fat-washed old fashioned.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1924;Bosq;USA;Aspen;312 S. Mill St., Aspen, 81611, USA;39.18857;-106.81978;15;false;false;Contemporary;At this singular enclave, Chef Barclay Dodge and his team are executing seasonally inspired cooking that focuses on foraging, fermenting and local farms. The dimly lit interior might seem moody and mysterious at first, but everything about the experience is open and accommodating, from the charmingly loquacious staff to the menu format, which allows diners to customize their own tasting of four or more courses. From hand-picked spruce tips to butter from locally sourced cooperative dairy cows, this is a concept that pays attention to details—even ingredients from farther afield, like lobster from New England, gets a hit of local flavor from being grilled over juniper wood.;Interesting wine list;[]
1925;Beckon;USA;Denver;2843 Larimer St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7609504;-104.9824196;15;true;false;Contemporary;More than just a name, it's an ethos at this ambitious RiNo dining room from Chef Duncan Holmes where staff warmly welcome you. Once inside this Scandi-cool space, diners pull up a chair at the 18-seat counter facing the kitchen where a focused team is hard at work. Diners choose between vegetarian or omnivore menu options, but in either case vegetables are a highlight, as in a porridge of Calrose rice with black truffle, pickled hedgehog mushroom, and crispy yuba. Seared quail breast with a confit leg is spot on, especially when paired with date purée and a quail reduction enhanced with orange and foie gras. Desserts are especially captivating, like a memorable chocolate dessert with a lacy cocoa nib tuile, pomegranate jam, and a quenelle of subtle-yet-spectacular nutmeg and salsify ice cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
1926;Frasca Food and Wine;USA;Boulder;1738 Pearl St., Boulder, 80302, USA;40.0193351;-105.2724941;36;true;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;This sleek restaurant is set in the heart of downtown Boulder on a charming street lined with shops and restaurants. All are treated as special guests here, where the cooking is Italian, but in a hyper-specific way: it's the food of the northeast Italian region of Friuli Venezia Giulia. You'll find pasta and seafood on the prix fixe and tasting menus, but Slavic and Alpine elements also appear. Focused and distinct, the menu might showcase a lesser known part of Italy, but the ingredients are clearly Coloradan. The plates are beguiling with a minimal, straightforward approach, as in cjalson, half-moon fresh spinach pasta pockets filled with an English pea and potato purée. Save room for dessert, like the beautifully arranged goat cheese semifreddo.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1927;The Wolf's Tailor;USA;Denver;4058 Tejon St., Denver, 80211, USA;39.77277;-105.01088;49;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;Offering a dining experience as intriguing as its name, this comfortable haven blends together creativity, attention to detail, and charm. Chef Taylor Stark and his team stitch together a thoughtful, delicious multicourse menu from culinary influences near and far. Depending on the season, a meal might include a Berkshire pork dumpling with a turmeric and dill broth, inspired by the flavors of Chiang Mai, or a perfectly wood-fired Colorado spring lamb loin with cherry tonkatsu sauce, offering a Japanese twist to local products. Despite its far-flung influences, the cuisine manages to fit together perfectly, offering a cohesive style that emphasizes excellent ingredients with faultless technique. Paired with effortlessly gracious service and an in-depth beverage program of beguiling cocktails (and their dry counterparts) alongside carefully curated wines, this one-of-a-kind experience stands apart from the pack.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1928;Fang Xiang Jing;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 1, Courtyard 5, China Railway Ludao Art City, 16 Majia Garden Road, Jinniu, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.685754;104.051369;71;true;true;Sichuan;Set in a delicate stone garden, this restaurant in a quaint building offers private dining rooms only. The kitchen team painstakingly and faithfully revives nostalgic Sichuanese recipes. For example, the cabbage in chicken consommé takes hours to prepare and boasts a rich, crystal clear broth with exceptional depth. Contrasting textures and a tingling sensation depict the mapo tofu with diced beef and fish snout. Delicate service adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1929;Hokkien Cuisine;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 326, 3F, North Tower, Chinese Financial Center, 33 Jiaozi Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5836826;104.060726;33;false;false;Fujian;The elegant room with full-length windows feels airy and bright. In addition to booth seats, there are alsoprivate rooms for parties. The Fujian-born kitchen team ensures the authenticity of each dish. The must-try lychee meatballs are deep-fried pork stuffed with chopped water chestnuts for crunchiness. Scallion aromas and pleasing textures depict the Quanzhou speciality, crispy tofu skin rolls with a five-spice pork filling.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1930;Silver Pot;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 532, 5F, M6, ICP Office Building, 300 Jiaozi Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5856;104.056593;45;true;false;Sichuan;The owner’s collection of souvenirs from her trips around the world gives this spacious dining room an endearing quirkiness. Her wanderlust also translates into her quest for quality ingredients from around the globe, to be cooked in an authentic Sichuanese style. Roast pigeon smoked with Sichuan pepper leaves is simply unmissable. Cold appetisers like lamp-shadow sliced grass carp are also well made. You can opt for half portion for some dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1932;The Hall;China Mainland;Chengdu;Canton Hall, Taikoo Li, 8 Zhongshamao Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6553493;104.0797173;58;false;true;European Contemporary;The first Louis Vuitton restaurant in China has Italian chef Leonardo Zambrino at the helm. Stints in prestigious kitchens in Asia and Europe have helped shape his vision – sophisticated European cuisine incorporating Sichuan flavour profiles. The five- and eight-course tasting menus feature season-driven dishes such as an ode to mushrooms, presenting Yunnan's mushrooms in ingenious forms, with contrasting textures, flavours and temperatures.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
1933;Mi Xun Teahouse;China Mainland;Chengdu;The Temple House, 81 Bitieshi Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, 610021, China Mainland;30.654727;104.081984;90;false;false;Vegetarian;Nestled in a quiet hotel next to Daci Temple, this restaurant is an oasis of calm. The courtyard house exudes historical charm, with the open kitchen lending an airy feel. Hand-picked local produce is used to create light, refined and inspired vegetarian dishes, such as vegan mapo tofu with chanterelles. There is also a set menu that supports small local farms near panda habitats, featuring ingredients like Mianyang porcini and Ya'an radish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1934;Fu Rong Huang;China Mainland;Chengdu;3F, 66-16 Guanghuacun Street, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.667097;104.007964;75;false;true;Sichuan;The restaurant prioritises privacy, with its tables separated by wood slat dividers. The experienced kitchen team specialises in traditional Sichuan dishes, many of which are painstaking to prepare, such as the signatures snowflake minced chicken and scrambled egg white with fish tripe. Round it off with the quintessential Sichuan sweet twice-cooked shaobai – pork belly slices layered with red bean paste over glutinous rice.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
1937;Xu's Cuisine;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 1, Block 8, Building & Greenwich Plaza, 1 Wangjiang Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.639715;104.086383;22;true;true;Sichuan;This is the chain’s first outpost and it’s been in business for over a decade. A tank of live fish by the entrance reminds you that river and sea fish are the name of the game here. The menu revolves around novel Sichuan dishes, with a few regional offerings. For an overview of Sichuan cuisine, try the 24-flavour-profile set menu. We also recommend the preserved meat prepared in-house, or the pond loach seared with green Sichuan pepper, depicted by crisp textures and a numbing sensation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1938;Ma's Kitchen;China Mainland;Chengdu;1 East Kangshi Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.653874;104.081227;84;true;false;Sichuan;This popular eatery in the bustling Taikoo Li area started out as a stall in Weishan in 1923. Light years from its humble beginnings, this only outpost of the chain in Chengdu features a vintage hipster interior and Sichuan classics on the menu. Besides their signature duck blood curd with pork offal and sliced eel, also try the crispy fen zheng rou – pork coated in seasoned rice flour, steamed and then deep-fried. Expect to see a queue from the moment it opens.;Air conditioning;[]
1939;ZEA;Taiwan;Taipei;5, Alley 20, Lane 300, Section 4, Ren'ai Road, Da’an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.03634;121.5541294;95;false;false;Latin American;The Argentinian owner-chef Joaquin Elizondo Hourbeigt named the restaurant after the Latin word for maize because it is important in both Latam and Taiwanese cuisines. The 12-course tasting menu pays tribute to his cultural and culinary heritage, embodying the passion and vibrancy of Latam food with the finesse of haute cuisine. Most of the ingredients are sourced locally, including those native to South America.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1940;Paris 1930 de Hideki Takayama;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, The Landis, 41, Section 2, Minquan East Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 10470, Taiwan;25.0628;121.52997;71;false;false;French Contemporary;The pristine interior exudes understated elegance. Expect a local take on executive chef Takayama-san's refined French-Japanese culinary vision. The head chef, an avid tea lover, cleverly incorporates local teas into his cooking – it features in his sauces, amuse-bouches, dinner rolls and his version of Takayama's signature seasonal vegetables with sushi rice. The experience involves all the senses – perfect for romantic dates and special occasions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1941;de nuit;Taiwan;Taipei;175, Section 4, Xinyi Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0334532;121.5505992;50;true;false;French Contemporary;Christened ‘by night’ in French, the room is aptly furnished in black, grey and blue and punctuated by brass trims and velvet upholstery. The young kitchen team are led by the Hong Kong head chef, who worked in some of the pregtious kitchen in Asia. He mindfully layers textures and flavours in every dish, while respecting the French traditions and seasonality of ingredients. Ask the sommelier to pair your food with wines or teas.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
1942;Circum-;Taiwan;Taipei;B2, Regent Hotel, 3, Lane 39, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;24.98707;121.42931;15;true;true;Creative;The Latin "circum-" is related to "circle", a symbol of wholeness and unity in Chinese culture. The young kitchen team traces the footsteps of Chinese emigrants throughout history, exploring how their food culture changes over time and territories. Inspired by classic recipes, childhood memories and anecdotes collected overseas, they deliver an engaging dining experience based on literature, narratives and solid French technique.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
1947;Sushiyoshi;Taiwan;Taipei;12, Alley 19, Lane 216, Section 4, Zhongxiao East Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0402806;121.5537337;60;true;false;Japanese;Well versed in the culinary arts of both Japan and France, founder Hiroki Nakanoue devises omakase menus that meld Edomae sushi traditions and a creative use of Western techniques and ingredients, such as truffles and caviar. The kitchen excels at realising his vision with finesse and precision. While nigiri sushi dominates the lunch menus, the higher priced dinner menu is where the team's creativity, astuteness and skills shine brightest.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1948;GEN;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;8 Fusing 4th Road, Cianjhen District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6042;120.29872;36;false;true;Cantonese;The lofty room is a soothing patchwork of camel and neutral shades set off by gun metal grey. Besides sitting at the arc-shaped counter or round tables, you can also book a room for more privacy. The kitchen brigade from Macau and Hong Kong crafts three set menus, showcasing gourmet dried seafood like bird’s nest and abalone and updating 1980’s Cantonese favourites with novel twists. Concise selection of French wines, but a very varied tea menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1949;Fleur de Sel;Taiwan;Taichung;581-1 Shizheng Road, Xitun District, Taichung, 407, Taiwan;24.160425;120.634515;32;true;true;French Contemporary;The chef worked in France and Italy for 30 years before opening her restaurant in 2003, relocating to this elegant space in 2017. She uses mostly local ingredients in seven- to nine-course prix fixe menus with a choice of mains. Changing every season, the precisely executed menus never fail to surprise with their whimsical ideas and vivid colours. Her signature use of wine, Asian spices and herbs lends her dishes exceptional depth and aromas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1950;Sushi Akira;Taiwan;Taipei;6-3, Lane 25, Shuangcheng Street, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.06614;121.52486;35;true;true;Sushi;With over 20 years of experience, the sushi chef makes diners feel right at home with his warm and gentle personality. This favourite among locals for over a decade is best known for Edomae sushi made with the chef’s precise blend of red vinegars and the finest fish aged according to his experience. The room with counter seats allows for more privacy without missing any of the action.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1951;Haili;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;2F, 264-1 Chenggong 1st Road, Qianjin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6291861;120.2916502;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Having honed his skills in some famous kitchens in Taiwan, Chef Kang, a Taipei native, chose to start his first venture in Kaohsiung. With an open kitchen and counter seats, the earth-toned room exudes warmth and understated elegance. The single set menu that is served features local and Japanese produce astutely prepared in Japanese-French style. The menu changes every season but always includes one course inspired by Kaohsiung culture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
1953;Tien Hsiang Lo;Taiwan;Taipei;B1, The Landis, 41, Section 2, Minquan East Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.062841;121.529965;82;true;false;Hang Zhou;The chef honours tradition with precision and deftness. His unique creation, fairy duck soup, combines two Hangzhou classics: fish ball soup and braised duck with ham. He also occasionally comes up with new recipes drawing on local ingredients. Eating here is a multifaceted experience – besides having tea sommeliers who are well-versed in tea pairings, at dinnertime, calligraphers turn your order into a piece of art for you to take home.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1954;Sens;Taiwan;Taipei;12, Lane 127, Section 3, Minsheng East Road, Songshan District, Taipei, 105, Taiwan;25.0588994;121.5473342;70;false;false;French Contemporary;The 20-seater is not particularly spacious, but the clever use of shiny materials and vertical lines more than compensates. It only opens for dinner with a single tasting menu that changes according to the season (although the ever-popular pâté en croûte remains a firm fixture). The chef’s sauces are second to none and he uses fresh herbs to great effect. In echo of traditional French meals, small cheese bites are served after the main course.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1960;Forchetta;Taiwan;Taichung;2F, 36 Huizhong 7th Street, Xitun District, Taichung, 407, Taiwan;24.16003;120.64085;82;true;true;European Contemporary;Forchetta is hugely popular with those in the know, but newcomers be warned – the sign is easy to miss. A vet by training, the head chef has a real passion for food and gardening as demonstrated by his east-meets-west creations and his miniature garden. From the set menu, choose your main from the six options available. Duck heart and gizzard risotto uses local rice grown using the aigamo method, cleverly referencing the origins of the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1961;INITA;Taiwan;Taipei;1, Alley 52, Lane 12, Section 3, Bade Road, Songshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0460871;121.5505871;94;false;false;Italian Contemporary;INITA, a portmanteau of Italy, Nippon (Japan) and Taiwan, crafts food that is underscored by Italian technique, jazzed up with Japanese twists and made from local ingredients. The tasting menu reflects the Japanese chef-owner’s career spanning 20 years. A gregarious extrovert and born showman, he presents his dishes theatrically and with a great sense of fun. Don’t miss his duck rice dish Ancora, Ciao Formosa.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1962;Ad Astra;Taiwan;Taipei;23, Lane 45, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 10450, Taiwan;25.0544699;121.5241219;84;true;false;European Contemporary;An alumnus of several world-renowned restaurants in New York City, the head chef recounts his eclectic journey with a 10- or 14-course tasting menu in omakase style. Dishes are precisely executed with Asian ingredients and a Japanese culinary ethos, especially in the kamameshi course that melds Japanese and European techniques. Also try his non-alcoholic temperance flight with an ingenious mix of Nordic fermented fruits and veggies.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1963;L'Atelier par Yao;Taiwan;Taichung;2F, 68 Xinfu 16th Street, Taiping District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1528622;120.7051419;98;false;false;French Contemporary;Concrete walls, dark green drapes, wooden furniture and local handmade pottery work nicely together in this elegant room that spans two floors. The young chef, who honed his skills in France, excels in modern French fare with an Asian twist. Try his chargrilled scallop with kombu, peas and parsley sauce for a delightful mix of textures. Desserts made à la minute and tea brewed with herbs that you pick yourself end the meal on a decadent note.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
1964;Oretachi No Nikuya;Taiwan;Taichung;194-1 Gongyi Road, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1509806;120.6564165;82;true;false;Barbecue;Steps away from its previous address, this paradise for beef lovers keeps even the most jaded connoisseur happy – whole cows are shipped monthly from all over Japan and only the most premium cuts make it to the grill. You even get to try some rare cuts not found elsewhere. The young owner-chef knows his bovine so is more than happy to recommend a cut or offal. The friendly service and bustling vibe make it perfect for get-togethers.;Air conditioning;[]
1965;A;Taiwan;Taipei;4F, Building 2, Diamond Towers, Shin Kong Mitsukoshi, 282, Section 3, Zhongxiao East Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0414746;121.5426469;63;true;true;French Contemporary;Chef Alain Huang named his first venture with his initial, promising a grade-A dining experience in an upscale, private space. The pristine room with wood furniture, flowers and art is reminiscent of an art gallery. Two tasting menus with 10-plus courses come with wine or non-alcoholic drink pairings. The dishes are French in origin but influenced by Asian cuisines and made to subvert preconceptions – eg the snack that looks like a cork stopper.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
1966;YUENJI;Taiwan;Taichung;5 Anhe East Road, Xitun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1743625;120.6236048;91;false;true;Taiwanese;The swanky setting seamlessly melds East-meets-West eclecticism with modern elegance. Chef Lin revisits Taiwan’s food heritage and culture, adding a sophisticated spin to family favourites. The Tasting Set Menu allows diners to pick from the main menu for each course, whereas the Chef’s Menu, served omakase style, needs pre-ordering. The iconic sweet Lukang roasted wheat flour soup is creatively mixed with almond milk imparting a creamy, nutty kick.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1968;NOBUO;Taiwan;Taipei;8 Tai'an Street, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0400402;121.5278581;78;false;false;Contemporary;With a Japanese façade and a Nordic-inspired dining room, NOBUO is all about breaking boundaries. Born in Taiwan and raised in Japan, the head chef opened his eponymous restaurant to champion Japanese-French cuisine using Taiwanese produce. The single tasting menu is visually minimalist but packed in intensity. Surf clam with sweet peas is sparingly seasoned with chilli powder to highlight its natural sweetness.;Air conditioning;[]
1969;Wok by O'BOND;Taiwan;Taipei;18 Long Jiang Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104099, Taiwan;25.0479656;121.5402246;46;true;true;Creative;Dark green velvet, red walls and accent lights showcase the bare concrete walls in this chic space. A sister establishment of Tei by O'bond, famous for Taiwanese tea cocktails, Wok excels in deconstructing the flavours of Taiwanese and Asian cooking, and reimagining them in astounding forms with modern French techniques. The themed tasting menu changes every season. The Taiwanese teas and herb-infused cocktails are always a delight.;Air conditioning;[]
1970;Mountain and Sea House;Taiwan;Taipei;94, Section 2, Ren'ai Road, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, 100, Taiwan;25.0380165;121.5313736;48;false;true;Taiwanese;Complete with a courtyard and a high-ceilinged foyer, both the interior and the food of this luxurious mansion are evocative of 1930s glamour. The must-try roast suckling pig uses only 21-day-old hogs, slow-cooked for 12 hours and roasted until crisp and golden. Another speciality, deboned chicken braised in pork tripe, takes six hours to prepare. Round off with azuki bean pancakes topped with a spun sugar nest: a feast for both the eye and the tastebuds.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1971;Sur-;Taiwan;Taichung;3F, 29 Zhongshan Road, Central District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1379723;120.6836711;68;false;false;Taiwanese contemporary;Sur- moved to Central district in 2023 and now occupies the third floor of a quaint building. The minimalist room dotted with wooden furniture and vintage couches sports dark colours. The owner-chef elevates everyday Taiwanese ingredients to haute cuisine using traditional techniques like tempering, charbroiling and smoking in the tasting menu that changes every season. The wine and zero-proof pairings are highly recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
1974;Golden Formosa;Taiwan;Taipei;101 Tianmu East Road, Shilin District, Taipei, 111, Taiwan;25.118368;121.536248;100;false;true;Taiwanese;In the 1960s, the family started serving heavily seasoned food to go with alcoholic drinks. The third-generation owner still follows the same family recipes from the old days. Their signature deep-fried pork ribs are made with local pork, fried twice to seal in the juices and to crisp up the crust. The tonic soup chicken-in-tripe is a deboned free-range bird slow-cooked for seven hours inside pork tripe with various herbs and condiments.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
1975;A Cut;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, Fubon Liaoning Building, 177 Liaoning Street, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104105, Taiwan;25.0530031;121.5427565;40;true;false;Steakhouse;Diners are escorted past the open kitchen into the airy room drenched in natural light and dotted by pops of blue, perfect for business meeting or social gatherings. Set menus featuring premium beef cuts from the U.S. and Australia are served at lunch and dinner. The signature "A Cut" steak, a ribeye cap with even marbling and a tender texture, is the stellar choice. Oenophiles will be thrilled by rare vintages from Bordeaux and Burgundy on offer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1977;Kitcho;Taiwan;Taipei;48, Lane 181, Section 4, Zhongxiao East Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.043045;121.550788;51;true;false;Sushi;The interior follows Japanese tradition with pale wood, warm lighting and fabric-wrapped panels. Niigata rice is seasoned with three vinegars, including akazu that gives depth and umami. The owner also imports sake and the list changes constantly to match the seasonal ingredients available. This relaxed sushi spot also serves cooked dishes if pre-ordered. Note that it is not related in any way to its namesake in Tokyo.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1978;Ban Bo;Taiwan;Taipei;38, Lane 265, Lequn 2nd Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0813272;121.5605264;45;false;false;Taiwanese contemporary;From the chirping of birds and crickets to the custom-made tableware by local artisans, everything in the room conjures up collective memories and heritage. In the same nostalgic vein, a historic map of Taiwan adorns the origami-folded menu. The young chefs turn typical beer snacks, banquet dishes and rustic treats that are close to every Taiwanese’s heart into fine dining gems. Expect to spend a leisurely three hours on the multicourse meal.;Air conditioning;[]
1979;Shin Yeh Taiwanese Signature;Taiwan;Taipei;Marriott Midtown, 199 Lequn 2nd Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0803851;121.5593471;85;false;true;Taiwanese;The encyclopaedic proportions of the menu may be a bit daunting, but the familiar and much-loved dishes of the group’s flagship outlets feature prominently. This branch serves the brand’s greatest hits from the past 40 years, such as the 70s classic, fish-shaped minced shrimp toast, alongside new creations like almond tofu dessert with peanut mochi and pu’er tea. Also check out the hidden items, previously only available to those in the know.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
1980;Nari;USA;San Francisco;1625 Post St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7855421;-122.4288317;82;false;true;Thai, Contemporary;This sleek retreat located within Hotel Kabuki delivers a one-two punch with a dramatic setting and accomplished cooking. Chef Pim Techamuanvivit’s personality and laser-focused palate come through in dishes that utilize fantastic Californian ingredients through a distinct, contemporary Thai lens. Dishes are family style, albeit with a touch of refinement. Intensely aromatic curries achieve a marvelous complexity, as in a brick red bumbai curry with crispy fried eggplant, served with an ethereally flaky roti bread. Crispy shallots and peanuts are a clever addition to bright citrus in yum sum-o. Grilled Monterey squid in a chili-lime dressing is plated with impossibly tender, sticky-sweet pork jowl in a dish so satisfying you'll be scraping every last kernel of sticky rice.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
1981;Uka;USA;Los Angeles;6801 Hollywood Blvd., Level 5, Los Angeles, 90028, USA;34.1017338;-118.3391629;28;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;Chef Yoshitaka Mitsue and Chef Shingo Kato (both formerly of the Permanent Mission of Japan to the United Nations) and two waiters take great care with the details at this sleek hideaway nestled within Japan House at the Ovation Hollywood. Here, the fish is sourced from Japan and flown in twice weekly, then cured or aged in-house. Products are sourced locally for the best quality. It's all part of the kaiseki dining experience at Uka, where guests are invited to savor six or nine courses. Most of the menu leans traditional, as in the kabutamushi, a dumpling made with shredded turnip and filled with Japanese sea bream, while French influences make their way into dishes like grilled abalone with a butter ponzu sauce and wagyu with a red wine jus and miso butter sauce.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Notable sake list;[]
1982;Gwen;USA;Los Angeles;6600 Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, 90028, USA;34.0979419;-118.3332968;99;true;false;Steakhouse, American;During the day, this enticingly arranged butcher shop sells humanely raised meats from local partner farms. By night, Gwen opens into a glowing dining room showcasing the same upscale cuts à la carte and on its multicourse tasting. Named for their beloved grandmother, this collaboration between Chef Curtis Stone and his brother, Luke, conjures Art Deco glamour with crystal chandeliers and a roaring fireplace.The menu is concise and stars house-made charcuterie and wood-fire grilled steaks. Watch from the chef's counter as the crew deftly cooks high quality meat, perhaps a Blackmore Wagyu New York strip, to perfection. Save room for dessert, like a round of cheesecake nestled in a mound of graham cracker crumbs and topped with a quenelle of mango lime sorbet.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1983;Shibumi;USA;Los Angeles;815 S. Hill St., Los Angeles, 90014, USA;34.044155;-118.256134;100;false;true;Japanese, Traditional Cuisine;There may be no more pleasurable place to learn about kappo-style cuisine, which has only recently made inroads into the American dining scene, than this stellar Japanese space, featuring a few tables and a counter crafted from a centuries-old cypress tree. The service is wonderfully engaging and attentive.There are four prix fixe menus, all highlighting the best of the seasons. Chef David Schlosser takes traditional Japanese dishes (and ingredients) and gives them a contemporary boost. Highlights include grilled mochi stuffed with karasumi and tender firefly squid with a sweet soy glaze. Crisp and refreshingly bitter fava beans balance the sweet-savory notes of chawanmushi, and Japanese sea bream with myoga ginger bud and pickled plum paste is a delightful bite.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
1984;Kali;USA;Hollywood;5722 Melrose Ave., Hollywood, 90038, USA;34.0834565;-118.3245399;25;true;true;Californian, Farm to table;This contemporary California restaurant from Chef/co-owner Kevin Meehan feels fresh with its wood and white cushioned seating, and walls accented with blue-and-white paintings. It's a perfect setting for a kitchen with a mission to deliver wholly organic and sustainable cuisine. Expect to see locally sourced and grown vegetables, seafood, and some dry-aged proteins on the à la carte or tasting menus. Discover delightful dishes such as salt-roasted celery with sabayon and grapes, offering a flavorful mix of sweet and savory. Rotating based on the freshest finds at the farmers' market, a salad of vegetables and fruit is a bright beginning before a crispy shell tucked with beef tartare. Meringue gelato with sugar-cured egg yolk grated on top is the perfect finale.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1985;Shin Sushi;USA;Encino;16573 Ventura Blvd., Ste. 14, Encino, 91436, USA;34.1587607;-118.4944008;40;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Taketoshi Azumi is indeed the real deal—he's worked for two decades at top spots on both coasts and comes from a family of sushi connoisseurs. In fact, Shin is named for the Tokyo restaurant run by his late father (spot the sign hanging behind the counter).Despite its pedigree, the vibe is laid-back and the joyful chef keep things entertaining, and solo diners feel a part of the crowd. His approach to shari is singular and it makes a delicate base for some of the more unusual nigiri around, like a tiny bundle of Japanese chives tied with crispy nori and topped with bonito. Then look forward to the very rare and lightly torched cherry trout, or sakura masu, which is a marvel thanks to its smoky outer layer giving way to melting richness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
1986;The Progress;USA;San Francisco;1525 Fillmore St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.78371;-122.43282;94;false;true;Californian;Located around the corner from the epoch-making Fillmore Theater, this sunny NorCal-meets-Nordic destination is as disarming as it is ambitious. The space is two stories of wood, stone and tile with greenery and skylights throughout, and an eager crowd flocks here for all occasions. Colorful, vibrant dishes designed for sharing rise to the formidable task of tasting as good as they look, so order with abandon. Original, boldly seasoned plates, like burrata with fried butter beans and Yerena Farms strawberries, or seaweed noodles with brown butter and dashi, are promising starts. Somebody has to order the Liberty Farms duck, a show-stopping feast complete with a mountain of crispy, peanut fried rice that draws eyes as it moves through the dining room.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1987;Bell's;USA;Los Alamos;406 Bell St., Los Alamos, 93440, USA;34.7440264;-120.279387;66;true;true;French, Californian;After cutting their teeth at top NYC kitchens, Daisy and Greg Ryan settled in the Santa Ynez Valley. Their particular skill lies in blending phenomenal product (90% of products are sourced from within 20 miles), focused flavors and methods. This is cooking that tastes as good as it looks, and crowds keep coming for their unpretentious dishes. Wild snails drip with luscious garlic and parsley butter, while the Santa Barbara uni crêpe cake is layered with crème fraîche and caviar. Lamb en croûte may be next, served over Calabrian chili aïoli with asparagus. The meat is tender and the aïoli perfectly cuts through the rich, savory elements.Desserts are equally worthy—from a buttery gâteau Breton to black pepper cookies laced with dark chocolate.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1988;Knife Pleat;USA;Costa Mesa;3333 S. Bristol St., Ste. 3001, Costa Mesa, 92626, USA;33.6904299;-117.8856979;90;false;false;Contemporary, Modern French;Set on the third floor of South Coast Plaza amidst fashionable stores, this steady operation is small, elegant and well-appointed. Add on a gleaming open kitchen, chef's counter, as well as a secluded patio—and you know you've struck gold. Well-heeled patrons and in-the-know locals pack this place, and everyone is here for Chef Tony Esnault's contemporary take on classic French cuisine.To begin, wedges of heirloom tomatoes plated with coins of compressed sweet watermelon and a smattering of crisp Persian cucumbers taste of summer, while confit duck thigh sided by preserved fig, turnips, cassoulet beans is a savory delight. Layered chocolate cake with hazelnut crunch crust ganache, chocolate cremeux and a gianduja glaze is the ultimate finish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
1991;R|O-Rebel Omakase;USA;Laguna Beach;361 Forest Ave., Ste. 103, Laguna Beach, 92651, USA;33.5434019;-117.7824063;59;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Tucked away in a modest little shopping center, this serene and striking spot feels a million miles away from the hustle and bustle. As its name suggests, omakase is indeed the name of the game here, where two seatings per night are available by reservation and overseen by Chef Jordan Nakasone. Rooted in tradition, the meal skews contemporary with a focus on seasonality and product quality. In addition to standout sushi such as Japanese white salmon and shima aji, there are a surprising number of kitchen dishes, including gindara, a rectangle of cod set in a memorable cauliflower dashi and garnished with tonburi, and a delicious, comforting chawanmushi topped with firefly squid and shaved bottarga.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
1992;Osteria Mozza;USA;Los Angeles;6602 Melrose Ave., Los Angeles, 90038, USA;34.0834246;-118.3386857;41;true;true;Italian;A perennial hit since opening (expect a wait), this decade-old darling continues to please with creative cocktails and Italian cuisine. The décor veers from typical osteria-style, thanks to handsome dark-wood paneling and a white marble counter but nab a seat at the Mozza bar for a prime view of the antipasti preparation.Bread is something of an obsession here, as is the mozzarella menu. Chef Nancy Silverton's team strives to show you around the corners of Italian cooking, The crispy chicken leg is pure and simple comfort food, and pastas are unsurprisingly phenomenal—try the orecchiette with sausage and Swiss chard. Rosemary olive oil cake dusted with powdered sugar, topped with caramelized sugar rosemary brittle and sided by olive oil gelato is the perfect ending.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
1993;Sushi Inaba;USA;Torrance;20918 Hawthorne Blvd., Torrance, 90503, USA;33.8403635;-118.3536365;61;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Chef Yasuhiro Hirano turns out some of the most exciting sushi in town at a separate counter within this sister restaurant, I-naba. His particular magic lies in weaving together a few key components, including exotic fish that he ages before blending with a host of ingredients. He’s mastered dishes that more established pros haven't—and to such precise and polished effect.With just a six-seat counter, this intimate space ensures that diners will be immersed in the process. Chef Hirano enjoys sharing his craft, but you may opt for silence to savor such delicacies as tender mantis shrimp glossed in eel sauce, or plump Kusshi oyster with ponzu gelée. Slow-braised monkfish liver may be presented with a sprinkling of black pepper, while sea bream is enriched by a dot of pickled plum sauce and shiso.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
1994;Chez Noir;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;5th Ave. btw. Dolores and San Carlos Sts., Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93921, USA;36.5569588;-121.9221052;57;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;If Chef Jonny and his wife, Monique Black (who oversees the service team) make you feel as if you're being invited into their own home, well, that's because the second floor of this Craftsman-style residence is their home. The two have an abundance of fine dining bona fides, but here they aim for a more approachable feel. The cooking draws upon French bistro fare and showcases the bounty of the California coast, with seafood, like spot-on sea bass and swoon-worthy abalone, making a big impression. If selecting from the many delectable dishes proves too difficult, opt for a set menu offering a tour of the greatest hits. Just don't skip the ethereal vanilla-scented canelés with an ideal balance of crisp caramelized exterior and creamy, custardy interior.;Wheelchair access;[]
1995;The Shota;USA;San Francisco;115 Sansome St., San Francisco, 94104, USA;37.7915182;-122.4009242;56;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Sequestered within an office building in the Financial District, this counter is a sensory pleasure. The menu combines Edomae sushi with classic kaiseki—and is informed every step of the way with imported Japanese ingredients and local produce. Diners are treated to a breathtaking culinary experience from start to finish.Chawanmushi is delicate and silky, studded with fava beans and borage flowers. Then comes the impeccably knifed nigiri, interspersed with small composed dishes, all highlighting seasonal delicacies. Imagine the likes of kasugo nigiri, featuring jewel-skinned fillets of young seabream, as well as tiny firefly squid with broccoli rabe, white miso, and mandarin. This meal is a consummate study in ingredient purity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
1996;Meteora;USA;Los Angeles;6703 Melrose Ave., Los Angeles, 90038, USA;34.083694;-118.3398317;22;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;This whimsical, immersive space is a touch otherworldly, with its tangled greenery, moody lighting, and trance-y soundtrack, but guests will be happy to fall under its spell when they taste Chef Jordan Kahn’s singular cuisine. Primal live-fire cooking combines with a zero-waste ethos and a treasure trove of sustainably sourced wild and organic ingredients to create dishes that are as memorable as they are delicious. Charred yam with a buttery sauce accented with smoked trout roe and grilled hazelnuts is more than the sum of its parts, and a dish of raw scallops with a vivid macadamia nut leche de tigre, banana, and crunchy kombu manages to both surprise and delight. Drinks, from cocktails made without refined sugars, to wild-harvested herb teas and single-origin coffees, follow the same compelling ethos.;;[]
1998;Hilda and Jesse;USA;San Francisco;701 Union St., San Francisco, 94133, USA;37.80009;-122.41101;55;false;true;American, Contemporary;Offering what may well be the Bay Area’s most creative and ambitious take on brunch, this disarming passion project from co-owners Kristina Compton and Rachel Sillcocks gets its extra shine from the pair’s extensive fine dining experience—each also contributed a grandparent for the restaurant’s name. The hospitality is cheery and warm, matched by a winsome space that calls to mind a modernist diner, and happily the cuisine is every bit as finely tuned. There is nothing precious or manicured about the cooking here. It is often bold and brash, a total riot of flavors mixed with stellar ingredients, and dishes are equal parts unexpected and undeniably satisfying. At dinner, find a rotating, seasonal multicourse menu with a few optional add-ons.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
1999;State Bird Provisions;USA;San Francisco;1529 Fillmore St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.783737;-122.43283;33;true;true;Californian;Welcome to the evolution of fine dining, where streams of plates are passed between guests dim sum-style, and the seasonal cooking is vibrant and surprising. You may not understand all of what you ordered at first, but prices are reasonable so pile on a few extras and try everything. Highlights include pan-seared dumplings with tender guinea hen and shiitake mushrooms accompanied by a tableside pour of umami-rich broth. Heartier plates of fried black cod tail glazed in a delicious tamari-butter, followed by hot-pink rhubarb-and-passion fruit granita over an oat mousse are a fine study in wonderfully unexpected flavors and textures.Be forewarned: getting a reservation here is a challenge, so it's best to avoid nights when large parties are booked.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
2000;Ssal;USA;San Francisco;2226 Polk St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.7972584;-122.4219651;15;false;true;Korean, Contemporary;Hyunyoung and Junsoo Bae have ample fine dining experience but were inspired to strike out on their own to fill what they saw as a void in San Francisco's Korean restaurant scene. The result is this tasting menu that draws upon familiar flavors but sets itself apart with a sense of refined simplicity.Pop a golden puff of sweet potato pancake with a dollop of kaluga caviar straight into your mouth for a delicious bite. Then, scallop mousseline with smoked sable fish wrapped in savoy cabbage is enhanced with a beurre blanc ramped up with Kimpo Yeaju. Finally, a bowl filled with a fluffy pile of bingsu tucked with Madagascar vanilla ice cream and toasted puffed rice is the ideal ending.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2001;n/naka;USA;Los Angeles;3455 S. Overland Ave., Los Angeles, 90034, USA;34.02526;-118.41206;50;true;false;Japanese, Contemporary;Wrapped in neutral tones, this serenely understated room offers one of LA’s most warm and graceful dining experiences. Chef Niki Nakayama presents her interpretation of a modern Kaiseki meal, drawing upon Japanese tradition while at the same time following her own path, offering an intricate procession of seasonally inspired courses that show a uniquely Californian influence. The menu begins with a sip of house-infused sake and small bites, winding through delicate aromatic broths, sashimi courses and heartier fare like grilled fish accented with sansho pepper. The only dish to never leave the menu, an artful twirl of al dente spaghetti dressed with tender abalone, pickled cod roe and black truffle, exemplifies Chef Nakayama’s unconventional approach.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2002;Sorrel;USA;San Francisco;3228 Sacramento St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.788334;-122.44614;91;true;false;Contemporary, Italian;Trained at Quince, Chef Alexander Hong has a true gift for pasta at this Pacific Heights perch where a rooftop garden provides herbs, edible flowers, herbs and seasonal vegetables. Smoky potato zlikrofi drizzled with sharp plum mostarda and shaved horseradish, or thick strascinati bathed in a ‘nduja-infused sauce with tender butter beans and lovage are two highlights. His ricotta gnudi are exemplars of the form: cloud-soft, accented by crisp fried sage and bright pops of sour cherry.In addition to a pair of pastas, discover some deliciously contemporary small bites, including madai crudo with yuzu and cured egg yolk, or dry-aged beef tartare with a hint of pink peppercorn. The duck breast course is truly a sight to behold—complete with its brilliant trinity of golden-crisped skin, juicy meat and earthy red kuri squash purée.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2004;Six Test Kitchen;USA;Paso Robles;3075 Blue Rock Rd., Paso Robles, 93446, USA;35.5757084;-120.6898229;39;true;true;Contemporary;Hidden away in industrial Tin City, Chef Ricky Odbert has, for many years now, quietly and confidently cooked like few others in the region. Dry-aged fish and meats, seasonal produce, and delicious sauces come together in a breezy space with soaring ceilings, charcoal-tinted walls, metal edges and a stunning wood counter that wraps around the kitchen. It’s a fitting stage for food that eats as beautifully as it looks. Recent highlights include dill meringue crowned with trout roe and aged pork loin paired with brown butter and a stunning burnt onion puree. Desserts, like barley koji ice cream with whipped miso, are particularly exceptional and balance sweet and savory. A highly selective wine list brings small producers under the spotlight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2007;Le Comptoir at Bar Crenn;USA;San Francisco;3131 Fillmore St., San Francisco, 94123, USA;37.798435;-122.43581;58;false;true;Contemporary, French;Nestled next door to Atelier Crenn, this counter experience offers an elegant interpretation of bar dining. Seated at a sleek marble countertop, a select handful of diners per evening receive a custom menu that carries the team's commitment to pescatarian-focused, dairy-free cuisine. Diners get a bit a show, as many of the courses are plated right at the bar. The beverage program is well-thought out, and selections pair perfectly with the clever creations, such as a salt-brined beet tartare crowned with caviar that's matched by a Mendocino sparkling rosé. The procession sings to the seasons, as in a springtime meal that included seafood sausage-stuffed morel mushrooms, clay-baked white asparagus, and halibut dressed with ramp "beurre blanc.";Air conditioning;[]
2008;Nozawa Bar;USA;Beverly Hills;212 N. Cañon Dr., Beverly Hills, 90210, USA;34.0683345;-118.398404;15;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Nozawa Bar is secreted away in the back of the Beverly Hills location of Sugarfish, yet this jewel box is entirely independent of the local chain it's housed within.Omakase is the sole dining option here, served as multiple courses of nigiri along with some sashimi and handrolls. Each sequence centers on exceptional seafood, most of it sourced from local waters. Chef Osamu Fujita may be a traditionalist, but the menu includes many novelties. Start with the perfectly crunchy jellyfish dressed with ponzu. This might be followed by an impressive presentation of deliciously tender slivered octopus. Sushi highlights include the delicate halibut fin, ruby-red snapper cut before your eyes and a handroll of mountain yam, ume and shiso leaf.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
2009;Mister Jiu’s;USA;San Francisco;28 Waverly Pl., San Francisco, 94108, USA;37.79371;-122.406654;22;true;true;Chinese, Contemporary;In a sleekly modern space that is undoubtedly one of the city's most well-appointed dining halls, Chef/owner Brandon Jew charts a new path with his uniquely Californian take on Chinese cuisine. He deploys top-flight ingredients to create original dishes that celebrate the Cantonese cooking and the Bay Area's seasonal bounty. The stylish bar area up front supplies memorable cocktails (as does Moongate Lounge, located above the restaurant), and also offers a familiar à la carte menu for walk-in diners. A separate prix fixe menu is exclusive to reserved tables, offering a light repast that can (read: should) be supplemented by signature, family-style items like roast duck with burnished skin or snapper served with sizzling ginger and scallion.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2010;Protégé;USA;Palo Alto;250 California Ave., Palo Alto, 94306, USA;37.427853;-122.14362;17;true;true;Contemporary, Californian;Chef Anthony Secviar and Master Sommelier Dennis Kelly are both alums of The French Laundry, but although the service is adroit (and the wine list excellent), this sleek modern space is far from stuffy. Likewise, expect thoughtful, well-balanced cuisine that shows refinement without being precious. The dining room's multicourse tasting menu includes the likes of Pacific sablefish with sweet onion dashi, 9-layer morel mushroom lasagna with Madeira sauce, and Flannery Beef with green garlic gnocchi. An à la carte menu is on offer in the lounge—think brick chicken with piperade, capers, and chorizo—plus a dessert trolly that features excellent tarts and cookies.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2011;Pasta|Bar;USA;Encino;16101 Ventura Blvd., Ste. 250, Encino, 91436, USA;34.1567212;-118.483862;26;true;true;Contemporary, American;A stylishly modern space hidden inside an unassuming strip mall, this hip concept's tasting menu is one for the books. Offered in a well-appointed front bar, drinks and a snack kick things off, and the staff is wonderfully engaging as they serve a host of delectable, hyper-local items. The eclectic cuisine travels beyond the borders of Italian tradition, offering up such creations as a raviolo filled with king crab, fermented pineapple, and macadamia nuts, or perfectly chewy cavatelli with Iberico pork, chile pasilla mixe, and earthy mole. Australian lamb loin features a merguez sausage made from its belly meat, matched with cherries, cipollini, and dusky rose-hued pasta filled with braised lamb neck. Desserts, like a bone marrow custard filled with blackberry granita and crisp meringue, are equally intriguing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
2012;Holbox;USA;Los Angeles;3655 S. Grand Ave., Los Angeles, 90007, USA;34.017384;-118.27802;30;false;true;Mexican, Seafood;Its namesake is a Caribbean island just off the coast of the Yucatán Peninsula, but this beloved counter, located inside the Mercado La Paloma, is a distinctively Angelino phenomenon. Chef Gilbert Cetina, who previously cooked with his father at neighboring stall Chichen Itza, draws from Mexican coastal cuisines in dishes whose simplicity belies remarkable flavor. Spectacular quality seafood of unassailable freshness leaves an impression, whether in electrifyingly vibrant aguachiles and ceviches, excellent tacos served on house-made heirloom corn tortillas, or skillfully grilled lobster—a panoply of exceptional house salsas gilds the lily. The frequently changing menu offers no shortage of delights, and a tasting menu, offered by reservation only on Thursdays and Fridays, is hotly sought-after.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2013;Kato;USA;Los Angeles;777 Alameda St., #114, Los Angeles, 90021, USA;34.0319303;-118.2383255;34;true;true;Asian, Contemporary;Chef Jonathan Yao is on a mission, deftly drawing on his Taiwanese background to deliver inspired, bold dishes. Far from his first location, the Row DTLA dining room is a cool enclave of polished concrete, steel, plate glass and light wood furnishings, along with an open kitchen that features prominently. It is a beautiful stage for his tasting menu, which is not shy about seasoning. Fish maw with Dungeness crab, custard and caviar comes with a crab shell-infused red vinegar for maximum impact. Spice-crusted duck breast taps into nostalgia with a fluffy bao bun. A recent riff on pig ears with summer tomatoes buzzed with a fiery chili oil. To boot, the cocktail program features impressively crafted alcoholic and spirit-free creations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2015;Caruso's;USA;Montecito;1773 S. Jameson Ln., Montecito, 93108, USA;34.4200948;-119.6257156;31;true;false;Californian, Italian;Located within the posh Rosewood Miramar Beach and fronting the Pacific Ocean, Caruso's has an enviable location. The dining room is beautifully set with leather booths, linen-robed tables, and white chairs, but make no mistake: Chef Massimo Falsini's seasonally driven, seafood-forward, and Italian-leaning prix-fixe takes center stage. From Santa Barbara uni sourced from a local diver to produce grown in the restaurant's onsite garden, there is a strong commitment to regional products, evidenced in dishes like pasta with diced abalone and halved Santa Barbara spot prawns topped with uni in a rich and creamy ramp sauce. Desserts are especially enticing, as in the "S like Strawberry" with a ring of pasta frolla filled with rhubarb sauce, mascarpone, and perfectly ripe strawberries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2016;Camphor;USA;Los Angeles;923 E. 3rd St., Ste. 109, Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.0462901;-118.2341103;64;true;true;French, Contemporary;This popular spot hums with activity from eager diners and a bustling open kitchen. Headed by uber-talented Chefs Max Boonthanakit and Lijo George, Camphor plates seriously good French fare with a sprinkle of spicing from Southeast Asia. Creative cocktails, including the refreshing Saint-Germain, complete the experience.Bubbling hot rigatoni stuffed with artichokes, Swiss chard and Comte delivers one satisfying bite after the next, and steak au poivre arrives resting in a pool of perfect sauce. Expertly seared with a caramelized exterior, it is buttery and tender, but it is the Cognac cream infused with peppercorn that will have you sopping up every last bit. The seasonal fruit tart, whimsically deconstructed, is a stunner.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2017;Heritage;USA;Long Beach;2030 E. 7th St., Long Beach, 90804, USA;33.775291;-118.1667769;24;true;true;Californian, Contemporary;Set in a converted Craftsman in the historic Rose Park neighborhood, this inviting locale is  removed from the hustle and bustle of Long Beach. Brother-and-sister duo Philip and Lauren Pretty run the kitchen and front of house, respectively, curating an experience that’s relaxed, but gets the details just right. On offer is a single multicourse tasting (priced quite reasonably) that highlights top-notch ingredients, including produce sourced from their nearby farm. The cooking has a California accent, and seasonal fruit may form a common thread, as in preserved kumquats paired with roasted beet and impeccably cooked dry-aged duck breast, and yet again in the guise of a frozen yogurt, in a summery dessert of charred strawberries and herbaceous yuzu granita.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2019;Jeune et Jolie;USA;Carlsbad;2659 State St., Carlsbad, 92008, USA;33.1631027;-117.3516968;97;false;false;French, Californian;Flaunting a nouvelle-French sensibility, this very appealing French restaurant from Partner John Resnick and Executive Chef Eric Bost is dressed in shades of rose and flooded with natural light. The food turned out by the wide-open kitchen is top-notch, with a playful twist. This cooking also displays a mature direction, with solid ingredients, unique combinations and beautiful presentations that are "almost" too pretty to eat. Sea bass with crispy skin, resting on a bed of sautéed spinach with a saffron and vanilla sauce is whimsical and delicious. Pale green sweet pea ice cream on a bed of macerated blackberries, bits of eggy, lightly crisp, “clafoutis” pastry, tangy elderflower gelee, and dots of vanilla cream makes a nice finish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2021;Auberge du Soleil;USA;Rutherford;180 Rutherford Hill Rd., Rutherford, 94573, USA;38.49199;-122.40534;23;false;false;Californian;Auberge du Soleil is one of the first restaurants to elevate the Napa Valley to greatness, and Chef Robert Curry has been ensuring its legacy with cooking that is the very definition of Californian cuisine. As might be expected from this perch overlooking the mountains and vineyards, the wine list is notable and proudly showcases local growers.The chef's tasting menu invites guests to control how their experience unfolds. Begin with an elegant soup of sweet white corn poured tableside. Layered with bay shrimp and a cube of toasted brioche topped with tarragon crème fraîche, it is rich and creamy. Dishes continue to dazzle all the way through to dessert, where a stunning fig plate, complete with lemon gelée and fig leaf gelato, is an absolute delight.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2022;Plumed Horse;USA;Saratoga;14555 Big Basin Way, Saratoga, 95070, USA;37.2563623;-122.0352659;56;true;false;Contemporary, American Contemporary;There has been a Plumed Horse in this spot since 1952, though this decade-old iteration is by far the best. The décor exudes warmth, and the setting is elegant, yet comfortable.This inventive kitchen turns out upscale modern cooking. Duck consommé, poured tableside and enhanced with meaty mushrooms and a bright English pea flan, is as impressive to the eye as it is to the palate, while locally sourced abalone is finished with XO sauce for a pop of flavor. The decadent black pepper- and parmesan-soufflé with an uni petal is of the dive-right-in variety.Almond cake with cocoa-nib mousse and orange foam is decadent, but wait for the rows of chocolates from Chocolaterie by Angelica, wheeled over in a glass-domed cart.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2023;The Village Pub;USA;Woodside;2967 Woodside Rd., Woodside, 94062, USA;37.42897;-122.25178;46;false;true;Contemporary, American Contemporary;Despite the sophisticated setting, the cuisine here is surprisingly approachable, from platters of house charcuterie served with fire-warmed artisan bread to the superb lobster bisque with braised new potatoes and fennel available in both the cozy front lounge and more formal dining area. It’s there that the kitchen shines its brightest though, with such elaborate entrées as ricotta gnudi neatly arranged with chanterelles à la Grecque, tender squash and golden raisins. The popular key lime tart is an equally impressive display—its crisp and perfect shell topped with toasted marshmallows, viola petals and meringue batons. Given the clientele, the wine list is designed to court deep pockets with an outstanding selection of French vintages, particularly Bordeaux.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2024;Chez TJ;USA;Mountain View;938 Villa St., Mountain View, 94041, USA;37.39468;-122.08044;81;false;true;Contemporary;Nestled within a charming 19th-century Victorian in the heart of downtown Mountain View, Chez TJ has an old-school air that befits its status as an elder statesman of fine dining. Both an abbreviated prix fixe option and a longer tasting menu weave together luxury ingredients with California produce, including from their own garden. Gently cooked halibut might be matched with a variety of summer squash and pickled garlic scapes, and Australian wagyu is matched with chanterelles and superlatively sweet corn. Desserts, like a frangipane and peach tart with brown sugar Chantilly, hit their mark, and the wine list is a treasure trove, with bottles ranging from heavy-hitters to bargain gems—even the by-the-glass selection is choice.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2027;Valle;USA;Oceanside;222 N. Pacific St., Oceanside, 92056, USA;33.1946237;-117.383446;34;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Celebrated chef Roberto Alcocer brings his refined, modern expression of Mexican cuisine stateside at this elegant space in the Mission Pacific Hotel, overlooking the scenic Oceanside Pier. The name is a nod to the Guadalupe Valley of Baja California, Mexico’s premier viticultural region, and the source of a plethora of interesting options on the wine list. Diners can enjoy an eight-course tasting in the dining room or a chef’s table experience in the kitchen. Dishes strike a winning balance between tradition and creativity, as in a tetela made with heirloom corn masa and hoja santa, filled with juicy chanterelle mushrooms and creamy goat cheese, and paired with a complex salsa of morita chiles—at once earthy and bright.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2028;Kiln;USA;San Francisco;149 Fell St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.7761959;-122.4202917;60;true;true;Contemporary;Industry veterans Chef John Wesley and general manager Julianna Yang have combined their talents at Kiln, where the warehouse space is warmed by personable service and the kitchen delivers artful creations. The tasting menu leans Nordic, highlighting preservation techniques like curing, drying and fermentation in dishes whose simplicity is belied by intricate techniques and compelling flavor combinations. The creative energy is consistent throughout the meal, offering plenty to impress guests. Opening snacks like a crispy curlicue of puffed beef tendon captures this ethos, while others, like a squab breast lacquered with burnt honey and served with a truffled jus, display a classical bent.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2029;Madcap;USA;San Anselmo;198 Sir Francis Drake Blvd., San Anselmo, 94960, USA;37.974712;-122.56168;84;false;true;Contemporary, Asian Contemporary;Upscale yet approachable, Chef/owner Ron Siegel's Madcap is one of the Bay Area’s best for contemporary dining. Well-crafted bites on the prix fixe may include a quenelle of tuna tartare with ginger and sesame seeds tucked with a crisp rice cracker that is deliciously simple. Next, a tender, almost-sweet coin of charred octopus rests over a pureed base of fermented pimentos and Tokyo turnip for a clean counterpoint. Supple slices of tart umeboshi, "noodles" of daikon and a creamy ponzu is a creative, pleasure-packed dish, while a tranche of crisp skin-on trout with cauliflower purée and ribbons of kohlrabi is bested with a tableside pour of dashi. The caramel pot de crème with a double hit of almond crumble and ice cream is perfection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2030;Localis;USA;Sacramento;2031 S. St., Sacramento, 95811, USA;38.5665938;-121.4829661;83;true;true;Californian, Contemporary;Together with his tight-knit team, Chef/owner Christopher Barnum-Dann brings unusual warmth to this intimate setting. His enthusiasm is instantly palpable as he happily explains his inspiration behind particular dishes and even solicits feedback. This is especially true for diners who sit at the spacious counter.The freewheeling tasting menu is thoroughly Californian in its commitment to carefully sourced ingredients, while also drawing upon global cuisines, reimagining flavors from the chef's travels with impressive imagination. Whimsy is a common thread throughout, as in a puffed pillow of crisp potato filled with "Fancy French Onion Dip" and caviar, or "The Dish That Made Us," a single woodfire-roasted octopus tentacle with black peppercorn sauce and pickled cherries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2031;The Kitchen;USA;Sacramento;915 Broadway, Ste. 100, Sacramento, 95818, USA;38.564058;-121.501422;30;true;false;Contemporary, Californian;After more than 30 years of operation, The Kitchen has upgraded to a grander space, but its raucous party atmosphere, led by energetic emcee Chef Kelly McCown, is the same as ever. Diners are encouraged to get up and walk around, even to wander through the kitchen and rub elbows with the cooks. Really like that truffle dish? The chef, who frequently proclaims the menu’s caloric impact, nonetheless invites you to ask for seconds. The menu changes monthly and features far-reaching inspiration while highlighting the Central Valley’s treasure trove of ingredients. Expect dishes like sweet potato cannelloni with brown butter sabayon, or perfectly seared scallops paired with cauliflower, blood orange, and lime leaf—and remember that the central premise is to have fun.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2032;Selby's;USA;Atherton;3001 El Camino Real, Atherton, 94061, USA;37.4685638;-122.2104559;57;false;false;American, Classic Cuisine;This destination-worthy restaurant drips with old-school Hollywood charm, matched by the seemingly effortless poise of the sharply dressed service team.The kitchen team excels at modern takes on classic American cuisine, which get an extra boost from SMIP Ranch—their private farm. Many dishes resemble familiar steakhouse signatures, but they are noticeably elevated here.Your dinner may begin with a fresh-baked Gruyère popover before moving on to an elegant take on vichyssoise. Steaks are cooked to perfection, while Maine lobster vol-au-vent is comforting.The refined take on nostalgic favorites continues through dessert. Standouts have included a slab of midnight chocolate cake as well as enticing old-fashioned crullers, dusted with cinnamon sugar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
2033;Kin Khao;USA;San Francisco;55 Cyril Magnin St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.785267;-122.40951;74;false;true;Thai, Californian;Tucked into an alcove of the Parc 55 hotel, the space is no great shakes in the décor department, but when it comes to layered, vibrantly flavorful Thai cooking with a produce-driven northern California flair, Chef Pim Techamuanvivit is in a league of her own.The menu draws on tradition, but it’s a far cry from run-of-the-mill, with creative interpretations of classics as well as original offerings. A fragrant steamed curry mousse (hor mok), studded with tender mushrooms and served with crispy puffed rice cakes, is a tantalizing starter, and even a familiar dish like green curry is made memorable with slow-cooked rabbit sourced from a local farm. Expect bold, unapologetic flavors—certain dishes feature spice levels not for the faint of heart.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2034;Angler SF;USA;San Francisco;132 The Embarcadero, San Francisco, 94105, USA;37.793167;-122.39213;38;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;A pair of plush rooms makes Angler feel like a hunter’s cabin gone Nordic-chic, but all eyes eventually drift to the gorgeous kitchen, where the cooks tend to a live fire. The touch of those embers can be felt everywhere—from the blush-pink bigeye tuna enhanced by shiso and a perfectly chilled tomato jelly, to ultra-tender pieces of hot fried quail generously flavored with a crispy pepper coating.Meticulousness is the prevailing theme as seen in the transformation of the humble cauliflower into a large, superbly roasted floret seasoned with vadouvan and a splash of lime. Stuffed? Tough. It would be plain wrong to leave without indulging in a delicious soft-serve sundae happily paired with warm salted caramel and cool cocoa nibs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2035;Aphotic;USA;San Francisco;816 Folsom St., San Francisco, 94107, USA;37.7816766;-122.401688;20;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Aptly named after the ocean's sunless depths, this vast, tenebrous space is leagues away from the mundane, offering a rarified pescatarian tasting menu that abounds with personality. Chef Peter Hemsley takes full advantage of California's coastal bounty, sourcing exceptional seafood from small sustainable purveyors and utilizing techniques like dry aging and fermentation to maximum effect. The kitchen’s creativity is displayed in dishes like thinly shaved Monterey abalone with swordfish “bacon” and citrusy dashi broth, as well as a warm bread course paired with a curry-scented hollandaise loaded with sweet Dungeness crab. Even desserts make judicious use of the fruits of the sea, as in a subtly briny oyster ice cream accented with herbaceous vermouth.;Interesting wine list;[]
2036;Osito;USA;San Francisco;2875 18th St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.761698;-122.4108346;86;false;true;Contemporary;Chef Seth Stowaway puts his heart, soul and even his nickname (osito means "little bear") into this rustic, lodge-like spot where live fire cooking takes center stage. Warmth radiates from the central hearth and from the supremely hospitable staff. The multicourse tasting menu is served at an expansive communal table and changes with the seasons. Each iteration highlights a different theme, with past themes including the autobiographical "Growing Up" and a paean to classic old-world cooking techniques. The food is both elemental and elevated, with a subtle perfume of smoke wending through the various courses, seen in dishes like a lightly cooked king salmon with fennel and porcini, or a slow-cooked brisket brushed tableside with an intensely savory mussel BBQ sauce.;Wheelchair access;[]
2037;Auro;USA;Calistoga;400 Silverado Trl., Calistoga, 94515, USA;38.5839271;-122.5671011;31;true;false;Contemporary, French;Soak up the bucolic splendor of Napa’s northern reaches at the Four Seasons resort, the ideal setting for this au courant embodiment of classic Wine Country fine dining. Thanks to skills honed in some of the Bay Area’s most notable kitchens, Chef Rogelio Garcia displays a distinctly Californian perspective, using precise technique in order to highlight exceptional ingredients—most of which are sourced locally, including from on-site gardens. Whether it’s a lively crudo of dry-aged kampachi with golden kiwi aguachile, or an earthy, ultra-silky sunchoke velouté with jamon de Bellota and Périgord truffle, each dish is finely tuned and harmonious. Add in warm hospitality, and here is a meal that strikes a golden balance between modern tastes and old-school luxury.;Valet parking;[]
2039;7 Adams;USA;San Francisco;1963 Sutter St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7861411;-122.4326324;57;false;true;Californian, Contemporary;In this city, finding a five-course menu for under a hundred dollars is a tall order. Chefs Serena and David Fisher make it seem effortless, though, bringing their signature magic to this second act in a sleek new space. The cuisine keeps an unfussy Californian simplicity, featuring solid technique and thoughtful flavor combinations that allow quality seasonal ingredients to shine. Think carefully shaped caramelle pasta that pairs a filling of sweet and nutty kabocha squash with buttery chanterelles, or crisp-skinned black cod with sunchoke confit and a finely tuned shellfish broth. Desserts never fail to end the meal on a strong note, as in a perfectly tender, moist apple crumb cake dressed up with an orange bay leaf ice cream and satsuma granita.;;[]
2040;San Ho Won;USA;San Francisco;2170 Bryant St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.7595744;-122.4100236;31;false;false;Korean, Contemporary;Reservations are difficult to come by at this spot where the prodigious talents of heavy-hitter Chefs Corey Lee and Jeong-In Hwang are on display. Once you've found your way inside, it's safe to expect something special here, where a modern minimalist design is the perfect backdrop for a vibrant and upbeat crowd. The kitchen's assiduously refined technique deftly combines traditional Korean tastes with a sense of novelty, using impeccable ingredients to make for dishes of surpassing depth and purity of flavor, whether it be the humble kimchi or a rarefied cut of beef. The menu includes some typical barbecue items, as well as dishes rooted in home cooking such as pork jowl and aged kimchi jjigae served with soy pickled ramp.;Air conditioning;[]
2042;The Restaurant at JUSTIN;USA;Paso Robles;11680 Chimney Rock Rd., Paso Robles, 93446, USA;35.6563869;-120.9113324;22;true;true;Californian, Contemporary;Make your way through winding roads to find this lush retreat nestled within the Justin Winery. This restaurant champions local product sourced nearby and from the property's own 150-tree orchard, edible flower fields, vegetable and herb gardens and apiary. Whether your table is on the patio or in the dining room, expect to be enchanted by views of rolling hills and vineyards and cared for by a team that is serious about hospitality. Chef Rachel Haggstrom and her team flex their creativity across a single tasting menu. There’s no leaving hungry, and recent highlights include apple and sunchoke velouté, warm gougères filled with mornay sauce, and Santa Barbara spiny lobster with salsify. Back vintages of the estate’s wines are amiably priced.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
2045;715;USA;Los Angeles;738 E. 3rd St., Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.0456789;-118.2369345;82;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Originally from Osaka Prefecture, Chef Seigo Tamura came to the United States with dreams of becoming a professional basketball player. Thankfully for Los Angeles, the only points he's scoring are with diners. The eight-seat counter is wonderfully spacious, and chef mostly keeps to himself as he blends the traditional with the inventive. This is in part evidenced by the surprising number of cooked dishes deployed throughout the meal. All of the seafood comes from Japan, and larger fish like tuna are aged in-house. Rice for the nigiri is on the firmer side with a touch of sugar added as a nod to his Osaka roots. Japanese hospitality reigns, with staff welcoming diners outside, and the chef seeing guests off personally at the conclusion of the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2046;La Dame de Pic Dubai;;Dubai;25th Floor, The Link, One&Only One Za’abeel, Za'abeel 1, Dubai;25.2279953;55.2909409;43;true;true;Modern French;Internationally renowned chef Anne-Sophie Pic made her culinary debut in Dubai with this restaurant set on the 25th floor of the One&Only One Za’abeel hotel. Located in the cantilever known as The Link, the large space features a bar topped with a white marble counter at the front, an open kitchen at the back and soft tones decorating the interiors. Its two set menus, known as Symphony and Harmony, offer modern French cooking that has classic roots and uses top quality ingredients. Dishes such as wild John Dory with razor clams deliver fine, delicate and sophisticated combinations, with a range of spices judiciously used to add extra depth and complexity.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2049;Tasca by José Avillez;;Dubai;Mandarin Oriental Jumeira Hotel,  Jumeirah Beach Road, Jumeirah 1, Dubai;25.2168806;55.2510082;46;false;false;Portuguese;In a lovely location on the 6th floor of the chic, beachside Mandarin Oriental Hotel, you’ll find this bustling yet relaxed restaurant, which is set around an open kitchen and has an infinity pool on its terrace, and both sea and city views. Nothing is too much trouble for the attentive service team, who ensure that your dining experience is well-paced and eminently enjoyable.The eponymous chef is passionate about the culinary traditions of his native Portugal and his kitchen team understand the importance of fresh, great quality produce. The resulting dishes offer Portuguese flavours with a modern edge and are vibrant, innovative and bursting with flavour. The menu offers something for everyone, with plenty of dishes to share – just make sure you leave room for dessert!;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2051;Hōseki;;Dubai;Bulgari Resort Dubai Hotel, 4th Floor, Jumeirah Bay Island, Jumeirah 2, Dubai;25.2106143;55.2351396;54;false;true;Japanese;This little ‘gem’ of a restaurant, set on the fourth floor of the Bulgari Hotel, is elegance personified, with understated, clean-lined décor and stunning views over the Dubai skyline. Nine counter seats make for a comfortable, ultra-intimate meal, where sixth-generation sushi master, Masahiro Sugiyama, and his team show off their considerable knife skills. Taking the individual tastes of their guests into consideration, they blend them with prime ingredients imported directly from Japan to create an omakase experience unique to each diner. This is refined, technically adept and beautifully presented cuisine – and the warm service from staff dressed in traditional kimonos further adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
2052;Hakkasan;;Dubai;Atlantis The Palm, Crescent Road, The Palm Jumeriah, Dubai;25.13243;55.11794;73;false;false;Chinese, Contemporary;Located within Atlantis the Palm Hotel, the Dubai outpost of this ever-growing global brand delivers all you need for a fun night out. It’s moodily lit, with smooth service, a party soundtrack, and lattice screens for added privacy. The best place to sit is in one of the booths to the side of the lounge and next to the back-lit blue bar. The menu of reimagined Chinese dishes includes all the Hakkasan classics, as well as a few exclusive to Dubai, such as the lychee lobster with yuzu pearl. If it’s spice you’re after, go for the Assam seafood toban. Created using quality ingredients, the accomplished dishes are colourful and vibrant with some punchy flavours. Save room for one of the creative desserts.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2053;Orfali Bros;;Dubai;Wasl 51 Mall, Jumeirah 1, Dubai;25.2187603;55.2614595;66;false;false;Contemporary, Middle Eastern;Three Syrian brothers own and run this deservedly popular restaurant: a light and airy space dominated by a striking, two-storey open kitchen. Original, playful small plates are Mediterranean at their core but display global influences. The cooking seamlessly delivers bold, complex and balanced flavours, as well as a lovely contrast of textures. Dishes are made to share – highlights include the playful 'Come with me to Aleppo', the punchy tuna, salsa roja and any of the immaculately-made, beautiful gateaux-based desserts. For the full experience, don't miss the tasting menu. Service is endearing, relaxed and super-friendly.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2055;avatāra;;Dubai;Business Park 1 Dubai Hills Estate Dubai Hills, Dubai;25.107342;55.240847;61;true;true;Indian Vegetarian;The 16 exquisite vegetarian dishes on the set menu take their influences from all over India, but they are all equally beautiful to behold. Each one is constructed with the same supreme care and ability, and they all add up to an experience you won’t forget. There’s a story behind each creation, which the delightful team take time to explain – and it’s extraordinary to think there’s no garlic or onion used. The restaurant, located in Dubai Hills Business Park, is uniquely decorated and painted in a very special light green. The tables face a large, wide altar-like table where chefs are seen adding the finishing touches to each dish.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2056;11 Woodfire;;Dubai;Villa 11, 75B Street, Jumeirah 1, Dubai;25.2156197;55.2512424;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On-trend industrial styling, intimate lighting and a laid-back feel are the hallmarks of this striking modern villa conversion in the residential suburb of Jumeirah – along with the huge open kitchen and grill which gives the restaurant its name. The impressive variety of global ingredients are of excellent quality, with vegetables, seafood and meats grilled to perfection over oak, hickory or hay, each of which impart their own distinctive flavour. The talented kitchen has the experience to know when and how to keep things simple, enhancing the skilfully cooked dishes subtly with well-judged seasoning. Delicious homemade kombuchas partner the dishes, and the relaxed yet professional service adds to the restaurant’s appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2057;Sagetsu by Tetsuya;;Dubai;24th Floor, The Link, One&Only One Za’abeel, Za'abeel 1, Dubai;25.2279352;55.2910345;64;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;In a place where the moon and sand meet, as the name suggests, chef Tetsuya Wakuda's cuisine brings together Japanese precision and French techniques. The tasting menu clearly conveys the essence of the dishes, highlighting balanced flavours made with few ingredients. The signature dishes, such as a sea urchin with Bohan shrimp, are complemented by the restaurant’s remarkable sake selection. An omakase experience is recommended to step into the mind of the chef. The décor is minimal and chic as it uses a lot of stone and wood, helping to create a serene Japanese atmosphere, with views of Dubai’s urban skyline.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2058;Smoked Room;;Dubai;St Regis Gardens, The Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.1148676;55.1378975;71;true;false;Contemporary;2024 saw Chef Dani García bring his popular Madrid restaurant to the St. Regis Gardens on the Palm Jumeirah. Located at the back of Leña, this intimate and dark room with a large semi-circular table seats 14 guests and overlooks a kitchen with an open fire and grills, a style Chef Dani dubs “Fire Omakase”. The experience is immersive and engaging, with chefs guiding diners through the 11-course menu and explaining in detail the creative and technically skilled dishes, such as sea cucumber carbonara. Desserts are a particular highlight, especially the confidently and skilfully executed burnt pumpkin purée and mandarin sorbet.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2060;Akuna;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;9F, Le Méridien Hotel, 3C Ton Duc Thang Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7798895;106.7074227;66;false;true;Innovative;In tune with the restaurant’s name, meaning “flowing water” in the Australian Aboriginal language, the 1,200 light rods hung around the open kitchen evoke a shimmering stream at sunset. Just like flowing water, Chef Aisbett weaves and bends the rules as he casts unexpected light on familiar produce, both local and imported. In the tasting menu, creative European dishes with Vietnamese influences never fail to wow. Aussie and international wine pairing available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2061;Long Trieu;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;4F, The Reverie Saigon, Times Square Building,  22-36 Nguyen Hue Boulevard, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7739539;106.7047515;88;true;true;Cantonese;Housed in one of the city’s luxury hotels, the Royal Pavilion’s lavish dining room boasts jade stonework, traditional gold-leaf painted Chinese scenes and ornate seating. Veteran Hong Kong chef serves a wide range of à la carte and set menus that respect Canton’s culinary heritage. Don't miss the delicious fried prawns with XO sauce or the hot and sour wonton soup. The dim sum menu is only served at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2062;Gia;Vietnam;Hanoi;61 Van Mieu Street, Van Mieu Ward, Dong Da District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0274223;105.8359626;78;true;false;Vietnamese Contemporary;Gia đình, meaning "family", is a reference to chef Sam Tran and partner Long Tran's longing for their homeland during their years working abroad. The restaurant decor draws inspiration from the Temple of Literature just across the road. Their 12-course set menu changes with the seasons and is informed by Vietnamese culinary heritage. Deceptively complex, the beautifully crafted dishes showcase well-judged combinations of subtle flavours, with acidity and texture playing prominent roles.;Air conditioning;[]
2063;Hibana by Koki;Vietnam;Hanoi;Basement 1, Capella, 11 Le Phung Hieu Street, Trang Tien Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0258394;105.8565699;72;false;true;Teppanyaki;Guests are cosseted from arrival to departure for a theatrical experience at a 14-seat counter in the basement of Capella hotel. Affable Chef Hiroshi Yamaguchi skilfully and precisely cooks teppanyaki dishes rich in complex flavour. The menu features a distinctly decadent edge, epitomised by the premium ingredients flown in twice weekly from Japan, such as abalone, spiny lobster, sea urchin, Yaeyama Kyori beef and Hokkaido hairy crab.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
2064;Tầm Vị;Vietnam;Hanoi;4B Yen The Street, Van Mieu Ward, Dong Da District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.02873;105.8393835;27;false;false;Vietnamese;This vintage tea house feels distinctly North Vietnamese with its nostalgic collection of Chinese furniture, hand-written signs and an antique gramophone and telephone. They serve Northern Vietnamese dishes with some central and southern options. The Vietnamese ham with periwinkle chả ốc (snails) comes with fresh herbs, vegetables and rice vermicelli with fish sauce. The subtle crab soup with canh cua mừng tơi (malabar spinach) comes in a clear broth.;Air conditioning;[]
2065;La Maison 1888;Vietnam;Da Nang;InterContinental Danang Sun Peninsula Resort, Tho Quang Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, 55000, Vietnam;16.1218937;108.3066406;51;false;false;French Contemporary;In a recreated Indochinese colonial mansion houses this upmarket dining concept. Getting there, which is half the fun, involves catching a cable car up the hillside! The 5- or 7-course set menu pleasantly surprises with exquisite creations featuring top-notch ingredients from Vietnam, France and Japan. Save room for the dessert which is another highlight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2066;Ănăn Saigon;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;89 Ton That Dam Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 710000, Vietnam;10.7719227;106.7028706;15;false;false;Vietnamese Contemporary;After working abroad in Hong Kong, Chicago and Bangkok, chef-owner Peter Cuong Franklin has returned to Vietnam to open this restaurant in a lively market. He applies modern cooking techniques to authentic street food recipes to create enticing flavours. Whether you order the fresh tuna tartare, a roasted duck-mozzarella-herb mini pizza, shrimp and pork tacos, or bone marrow Wagyu beef phở, every dish is a masterclass of well-balanced flavours and textures.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2067;Boškinac;Croatia;Novalja;Škopaljska Ulica 220, Novalja, 53291, Croatia;44.571006;14.8975384;54;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Surrounded by vines and olive trees, the beautiful country house that is home to this restaurant (as well as an elegant boutique hotel) occupies a peaceful location that offers a real holiday feel. The cuisine makes use of typical ingredients from the region of Pag, such as fish, lamb, vegetables, olive oil and wild herbs, all prepared with a modern and creative touch. There are two tasting menus, one which focuses on the island and the other which is inspired by chef Matija Bregeš’s own experience, while the wine list features excellent labels produced by the Boškinac winery. In summer, tables are laid out on staged terraces surrounded by greenery in an idyllic setting akin to a romantic botanical paradise.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
2068;Nebo by Deni Srdoč;Croatia;Rijeka;Opatijska ulica 9, Rijeka, 51000, Croatia;45.3470174;14.3507329;66;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated on the fifth floor of the brand-new Hilton Rijeka Costabella, this restaurant boasts breathtaking views of the Adriatic, the coast and the unspoilt island of Cres. Just as enticing as the setting is the tasting menu, which is available in varying lengths. Young Deni Srdoč’s dishes tell the story of Croatia’s culinary history, featuring traditional ingredients and regional specialities alongside more exotic fare to create a modern and creative menu that is influenced by the Mediterranean and Croatia’s hinterland and is full of colour and flavour. One of our favourite dishes was the sea bass that had been matured for a few days and marinated just before searing, then served with a Hokaido pumpkin and kale pie – a delicious and well-balanced dish. Highly professional service and an international wine list complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2069;Noel;Croatia;Zagreb;Ulica Popa Dukljanina 1, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.810998;15.9880697;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The tasting menu changes four times a year based on the seasons: in winter the undisputed protagonists are mushrooms and truffles together with winged game, while in springtime they are early vegetables. Dinner is a sensational journey among classic creations made with special care and other more modern creations with an original flavor, as well as several varieties of bread baked in an adjacent bakery. The wine list is outstanding: the different regions of Italy are well represented, without however neglecting Europe and America. Considering the great attention paid to tea (from Chine, Japan and Morocco), the restaurant offers not only wine pairing, but also tea pairing and also pairing with both. Strong zero waste ethics means that no part of the products used in the kitchen are wasted.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2070;Pelegrini;Croatia;Sibenik;Jurja Dalmatinca 1, Sibenik, 22000, Croatia;43.7360494;15.8890466;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the old town, this restaurant occupies the Villa Pelegrini-Tambača, a building with Renaissance origins next to St James cathedral. Chef Rudolf Štefan, who always makes sure that he comes to say hello to guests at the end of their meal, takes time to search out local produce: he produces a dozen wines in partnership with the best wine producers in the region, produces his own olive oil and, for the most part, uses fish and meat from Šibenik and its surrounding region. His six-course tasting menu showcases a modern version of traditional Dalmatian cuisine, with interesting, creative touches and beautiful presentation. One of the house specialities is the pasta with duck, which features slow-cooked slices of duck breast accompanied by a creamy pecorino sauce, confit duck breast and slices of celery that add a fresh and acidic flavour – a traditional dish that has been skilfully reinterpreted. The interesting wine list has more than 500 different labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2071;Alfred Keller;Croatia;Mali Lošinj;Čikat 16, Mali Lošinj, 51550, Croatia;44.5308235;14.4580907;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The town’s most luxurious hotel was designed in 1912 by the Austrian architect Alfred Keller, after whom this gourmet restaurant, which boasts stunning views of Čikat bay, is named. At the helm in the kitchen, chef Michael Gollenz (also Austrian), uses the best local ingredients in his modern, creative dishes which are attractive, full of flavour and prepared using French techniques while remaining open to influences from around the world. A small à la carte is always available, while in the evening there is also a choice of tasting menus. Particularly interesting dishes include scampi tartare in a Thai mint sauce, oxtail ravioli with Istrian truffle foam and foie gras, and a fresh dessert featuring strawberry ragu, basil sorbet, curd cheese and ginger.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2072;Restaurant 360;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Sv. Dominika B.B., Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.6415506;18.1115484;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;In fine weather, once you’ve been greeted at the entrance to this restaurant you’ll be led out on to its spacious terrace, where you’ll be stunned by the superb views of Dubrovnik’s rooftops, small port, the coast and the sea. Then it’s over to chef Marijo Curić, now back in his native city after years working in top restaurants around Europe, who meets guests’ culinary expectations with real skill, creating beautifully presented dishes which combine Croatian ingredients with Asian techniques, such as sous-vide cooking, the use of a Robata grill and skilfully prepared fermentations. There are two tasting menus: the first features the chef’s iconic dishes, while the second showcases the restaurant’s classic favourites. We particularly enjoyed the delicious mackerel with white turnip served with a potato and miso mayonnaise and a bonito vinaigrette which adds a pleasing maritime flavour to the dish. The superb wine list pays tribute to Croatian labels while also featuring bottles from around the world, while the personalised wine pairing includes the option of a few cocktails.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2073;Monte;Croatia;Rovinj;Montalbano 75, Rovinj, 52210, Croatia;45.0826939;13.6310596;83;false;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated next to St Euphemia church in the house where chef Danijel Đekić was born, this family-run restaurant dating back to 1985, originally a traditional tavern, has been transformed into one of the most acclaimed fine-dining restaurants in Croatia. The innovative, regional cuisine is often inspired by old recipes which are then reinterpreted with creative flair. The three menus are named after the colour of their key ingredient: Red for lobster, Green for vegetables and Blue for fish and seafood (but not exclusively). Special mention must be made of the lobster bisque, which features lobster tartare with trout caviar accompanied by a fennel-flavoured fumet and baked squid in black batter. The wine options are also excellent, both for the extensive choice and for the enthusiasm with which the sommelier provides recommendations.;Interesting wine list;[]
2074;Dubravkin Put;Croatia;Zagreb;Dubravkin Put 2, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8188384;15.9725596;66;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Leave the hustle and bustle of the capital behind you and head to this oasis nestled in Zagreb’s surrounding woodland. Dubravkin Put, which takes its name from the forest itself, serves fresh, fragrant Mediterranean cuisine with a focus on raw fish dishes, such as the light, aromatic sea bass and beetroot carpaccio. Among the high-quality meat dishes, the Kobe beef and the Pag island lamb chop served with peas, shallots and thyme are particularly delicious. For those with a sweet tooth, we recommend the Louis XV chocolate, foie gras ice cream and vanilla dessert. After your meal, why not take a stroll through the woods to enjoy the birdsong and natural surroundings?;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2075;LD Restaurant;Croatia;Korcula;Don Pavla Poše 1-6, Korcula, 20260, Croatia;42.9617461;17.1370191;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Using fresh fish caught that day, seasonal vegetables and local olive oil, Marko Gajski skilfully combines Dalmatian ingredients with Asian influences, French techniques (sauces) and fermented produce. His dishes are harmonious and beautifully prepared, the service is very professional, and the setting delightful, with an elegant dining room on the first floor and a summer outdoor space just a stone’s throw from the water offering fine views of the sea and the islands. The restaurant’s iconic dishes, which always feature on the tasting menu, include prawn gyoza with a mousseline sauce and daikon – a justly famous dish that is attractive and skilfully designed. A vegetarian menu is also available.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
2076;Korak;Croatia;Jastrebarsko;Plešivica 34, Jastrebarsko, 10450, Croatia;45.7260304;15.6500062;17;false;false;Contemporary, Croatian;Amidst mature lime trees and rows of vines belonging to the family winery, Bernard Korak has developed his own style of regional, seasonal cuisine after gaining experience with chefs such as Ana Roš and Massimo Bottura. His dishes are prepared using ingredients from the property’s own farm and based on the culinary traditions of the Plešivica region, where rolling hills planted with vineyards meet the mountains. Guests choose one of the two tasting menus (either five or eight courses) and then sit back to enjoy an elegant dining experience which is enhanced by the superb welcome and attentive service overseen by the chef’s sister. A small selection of cigars allows smokers to enjoy a fitting end to their meal, sitting on the terrace with its views of the vineyards.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2077;Art di Daniele Sperindio;;Singapore;National Gallery, #06-02, 1 St. Andrew's Road, 178957, Singapore;1.2908104;103.8520522;42;true;true;Italian;This stylish restaurant above the National Gallery commands sensational views. The tasting menus are inspired by chef-owner Daniele Sperindio's Italian heritage, childhood memories and love of his home country. From the sea to the mountains, his creative, intricate, and exquisitely plated dishes take diners on a gastronomic journey around Italy. The wine list features a superb selection from Italy including an impressive range of Super Tuscans.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2078;Iggy's;;Singapore;voco Orchard, Level 3, 581 Orchard Road, 238883, Singapore;1.3059244;103.8293379;31;false;true;European Contemporary;This stylish room may not offer panoramic views, but all eyes are on the chefs’ culinary performance in the kitchen, visible through a picture frame window. The set tasting menu at dinner features multiple courses that showcase top-notch produce from Japan and around the world, deftly crafted with European techniques. Apple-wood smoked wild-caught yellowtail stands out with intoxicating aromas and intense umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
2079;Alma;;Singapore;Goodwood Park Hotel, 22 Scotts Road, 228221, Singapore;1.3080956;103.8341574;65;false;false;European Contemporary;With an executive chef on board since 2023, Alma now offers two tasting menus at lunch and dinner, featuring well-crafted European dishes strewn with Asian accents. The menus change every three months to keep pace with premium seasonal produce. The venison course is especially impressive depicted by spot-on cooking, juicy meat, fine texture and robust flavour. Whisky lovers should check out the cellar rich in rarities.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2080;Oshino;;Singapore;Raffles Arcade, #01-11, 328 North Bridge Road, 188719, Singapore;1.30516;103.86369;54;false;false;Sushi;The slate- and pebble-covered hallway leads to a cosy, bamboo-clad room with only nine seats. Chef Oshino worked at a renowned sushiya for ten years, before opening his own shop tucked away in a corner of this mall. Sushi is his speciality and forms the backbone of his set and omakase menus, interlaced with sashimi. Sushi rice from his home prefecture Yamagata is dressed with vinegar and hand-pressed into nigiri, though not strictly in Edomae style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2081;Labyrinth;;Singapore;Esplanade Mall, #02-23, Marina Bay Promenade, 8 Raffles Avenue, 039802, Singapore;1.2897489;103.8563;97;false;false;Innovative, Singaporean;Chef LG Han takes recognisable local flavours and tastes remembered from childhood as his starting point – and then reimagines and reinterprets them, using superlative ingredients from across Singapore. The result is an exciting, original and unforgettable set menu that surprises, amuses and satisfies. The restaurant’s black canvas is punctured by razor sharp lighting, while the service team are clued up and very well organised.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2082;Seroja;;Singapore;Duo Galleria, #01-30/31/32/33, 7 Fraser Street, 189356, Singapore;1.29993;103.85802;25;false;true;Malaysian, Contemporary;An alumnus of prestigious establishments in France, the U.S. and Singapore, Chef Kevin Wong opened Seroja in 2022 to pledge his love to the Malay Archipelago. His seafood-focused tasting menus pay tribute to Malaysian culinary traditions with a generous use of local produce, spices and techniques. The plating is meticulous and artful and the flavours subtle and finely balanced. Ask about the food and wine or non-alcoholic beverage pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2083;Summer Palace;;Singapore;Conrad Orchard, Level 3, 1 Cuscaden Road, 249715, Singapore;1.3046521;103.8247494;94;false;true;Cantonese;The serene interior is furnished in contemporary Chinese style, in a palette dominated by warm whites and muted tones. On the menu, wok hei-laden stir-fries such as crocodile fillet in brown sauce, and venison with Chinese kale feature alongside Cantonese classics including baked stuffed crab shell, steamed Chinese marrow rings stuffed with shrimp, and spinach and tofu in crabmeat sauce. Be sure to try the exquisitely crafted dim sum, too.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2084;Marguerite;;Singapore;Flower Dome, #01-09, Gardens by The Bay, 18 Marina Gardens Drive, 018953, Singapore;1.2849725;103.8639515;92;false;true;European Contemporary;Dining in the Flower Dome makes for a back-to-nature moment and Chef Wilson does it with a touch of class. In his tasting menu, gracefully presented courses are underpinned by solid techniques, packed with oomph and flavours bold enough to match the showy, colourful blooms. The wine list showcases some rare labels, including bottles from Lebanon and Morocco, while the temperance pairing is also interesting. Service is seamless and personable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2085;Imperial Treasure Fine Teochew Cuisine (Orchard);;Singapore;ION Orchard, #03-05, 2 Orchard Turn, 238801, Singapore;1.304144;103.83147;17;false;false;Teochew;Since 2016, this restaurant has been serving traditional Teochew fare with an emphasis on fresh seafood. Only 15 oversized swimmer crabs are steamed and served chilled each day, so order ahead to avoid disappointment. Teochew-style, chilled, steamed fish also impresses with irresistible briny-sweetness, tender flesh and buttery belly. Dip in the delicious Puning bean sauce for extra umami. Other classics, like the oyster omelette, are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2086;Nae:um;;Singapore;161 Telok Ayer Street, 068615, Singapore;1.28033;103.84755;87;true;false;Korean Contemporary;The bright room is furnished in a cream and birch colour scheme, imparting calmness and warmth. The Korean chef Louis Han named his restaurant Nae:um, meaning a fragrance that evokes memories. Food culture and recollections of his home country are at the core of his episodic menu that changes with seasons. Innovative courses are precisely executed and presented in an ethereal, refreshing manner, but have inklings of their Korean roots.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2087;Esora;;Singapore;15 Mohamed Sultan Road, 238964, Singapore;1.2935989;103.84174;45;false;true;Innovative;Esora means "painting in the sky" in Japanese. With an omakase menu that changes daily to make use of the best ingredients imported from Japan, Esora – like the ever-changing sky – presents a new experience each time. The Japanese head chef excels at melding Japanese details with French techniques, with elaborate plating and floral arrangements to boot. The tea pairing, with perfectly brewed Taiwanese and Japanese teas, is a real triumph.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2088;Born;;Singapore;#01-01, 1 Neil Road, 088804, Singapore;1.2803952;103.843918;18;true;false;Innovative;Housed in Jinricksha Station, a former rickshaw depot circa 1903, Born boasts a modern dining room adorned by glowing double arches, high glass ceiling and an ethereal paper sculpture. A protégé of André Chiang, Chef Zor Tan cooks up a 9-course tasting menu inspired by the circle of life and his personal journey, melding French gastronomy with Chinese cooking. Dishes are creative and crafted with globally sourced ingredients, delivering contrasts in textures and flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2089;Poise;;Singapore;6 Teck Lim Road, 088384, Singapore;1.2801633;103.8420837;50;false;false;European Contemporary;Chef Steve Lancaster chooses to present his culinary gems in a monochromatic room with theatrical lighting to call attention to the food. His tasting menu reinvents European and Nordic classics that look unassuming with clever and creative combinations, and nuanced layering of textures and flavours. The chicken, bacon and onion dish is a chicken lollipop stuffed with chicken mousse set atop a  shallot puree with bacon and onion that imparts complexity in flavour.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2090;Araya;;Singapore;Mondrian Duxton, #01-08, 83 Neil Road, 089813, Singapore;1.278868;103.841816;81;true;false;Innovative;Chilean chefs Araya and Guerrero worked at the same restaurant in China. Their ingenious creations – deeply influenced by Araya's time in Spain and Japan – use an eclectic mix of Chilean and Japanese produce, with a South Pacific theme. Japanese favourites such as kinki and cod milt are jazzed up by aji amarillo and merkén from Chile, served alongside French pigeon and caviar. They even ferment and roast their own cacao to use in sauces.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2091;Hill Street Tai Hwa Pork Noodle;;Singapore;Blk 466, #01-12, Crawford Lane, 190466, Singapore;1.3052;103.8624;29;false;false;Street Food;Noodles are cooked-to-order with nicely layered flavours and textures in every bite. Crispy dried plaice, fluffy cracklings, and tender pork liver are all meticulously prepared. Expect to queue any time of the day.;Cash only;[]
2092;Lerouy;;Singapore;7 Mohamed Sultan Road, 238957, Singapore;1.293924;103.841922;88;false;true;French Contemporary;Sporting a brand-new image, Lerouy moved to this new address in 2024. Head to the cute little bar for a pre- or post-meal drink. The main dining area overlooks the open kitchen for a chef’s table-like vibe. As always, the food is served omakase style – choose the number of courses and tell the servers about your allergies and dislikes. The kitchen excels in unexpected food and flavour combinations that never fail to pleasantly surprise.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2093;Euphoria;;Singapore;76 Tras Street, 079015, Singapore;1.2775327;103.8441494;62;true;true;Innovative;The head chef once found onion repulsive, but then—by chance—discovered his love for the pungent bulb and went on to be obsessed with it. The allium is hard-wired in Euphoria’s DNA – from the décor and tableware to the sauces and dishes. His oignon jamboree, which makes an appearance in the lunch and dinner prix-fixe, elevates the onion from a supporting role to a leading cast—different varieties of onions cooked five ways are topped with caviar.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2094;Rhubarb;;Singapore;3 Duxton Hill, 089589, Singapore;1.2794339;103.842976;89;true;true;French Contemporary;Opened by two alumni of Au Petit Salut, this exclusive yet snug French restaurant sports an open kitchen. French classics are subtly and intelligently updated without recourse to gimmicks, striking a fine balance between flavour and delicacy. A thoughtfully curated, predominantly French wine list flanks the food. Lunch set menus offer good value. At dinner, choose between a 4- or 5-course set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2095;Chaleur;;Singapore;Level 2, 77 Neil Road, 088903, Singapore;1.279252;103.842122;36;true;true;Innovative;After helming some prestigious kitchens in Singapore, Japanese chef Kawano came up with a 10-course dinner menu that allows diners to appreciate his culinary vision to the fullest. French and Japanese produce is juxtaposed to great effect and finessed by solid French techniques. Dishes are pleasing to the eye as well as the palate. Painstakingly tweaking the consistency of his duck consommé daily, he shows his attention to detail is second to none.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2096;Jag;;Singapore;Singapore Tyler Print Institute, #02-02, 41 Robertson Quay, 238236, Singapore;1.29094;103.84028;62;false;true;French Contemporary;Since 2023, Jag has been housed in this pristine white-walled space with sage green furnishings, brushed brass trims and mid-century rattan chairs. Chef Jeremy Gillon's cooking remains vegetable-forward: French produce picked at peak ripeness – and supplemented by meats and seafood – is key to his ethos. Dishes are light in flavours but strong in creative flair. The cheese trolley impresses with its sheer variety. Round off your meal with a digestif.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2097;Buona Terra;;Singapore;29 Scotts Road, 228224, Singapore;1.3107414;103.8348231;89;true;false;Italian Contemporary;The entrance to this intimate restaurant in a refurbished colonial house is flanked by an imposing display of wine bottles, including many interesting Italian vintages. The interior is elegantly furnished with refined contemporary charm. They serve an omakase-style four-course lunch set and six-course dinner set comprising impeccably executed dishes. Signatures include house-made tagliatelle with freshly shaved and intensely aromatic white truffle.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2098;Whitegrass;;Singapore;Chijmes, #01-26/27, 30 Victoria Street, 187996, Singapore;1.2955388;103.8519798;38;false;true;French Contemporary;Chef Takuya Yamashita’s style is to use French techniques to bring out the best of the mostly Japanese ingredients. The resulting tasting menus are inventive and intriguing and feature delicate and attractive dishes, such as Hokkaido scallop with Mont D’Or, and Miyazaki Wagyu with cognac sauce. The graceful restaurant is housed within a historic converted convent and is divided into two rooms, one of which allows diners to see into the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2099;Sushi Kimura;;Singapore;Palais Renaissance, #01-07, 390 Orchard Road, 238871, Singapore;1.3067825;103.8296924;63;true;false;Sushi;The owner-chef certainly pays attention to detail: a hinoki counter crafted from one 150-year-old tree, organic sushi rice from one specific farm in Yamagata Prefecture, cooked in Hokkaido spring water and top-notch produce and fish exclusively from small farms in Japan. The chef excels in ageing raw fish, but the abalone cooked in sake for eight hours, and his rice bowl with uni, ikura, chopped toro and onsen tamago also deserve special mention.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2100;Shinji (Bras Basah Road);;Singapore;Carlton Hotel, Lobby Level, 76 Bras Basah Road, 189558, Singapore;1.2959028;103.8539;66;true;false;Sushi;This sushi restaurant, under the aegis of Japanese chef Shinji Kanesaka, is located on the lobby level of the Carlton hotel. The entrance is typically discreet and leads into an intimate space with seating at the hinoki cypress counter for 16. Three set menus are offered – but the omakase is often the best route to take. The ingredients are good quality, with fish flown in from Tokyo’s Toyosu market. Reservations recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
2101;Ma Cuisine;;Singapore;38 Craig Road, 089676, Singapore;1.2782652;103.8418934;90;false;false;French;Candles in wine bottles and tables made from wine barrels are among the details that set the authentic small bistro scene here. Wine connoisseurs will be bowled over by the wine cellar and knowledgeable servers, who know every vintage inside out. Classic French recipes are made with local ingredients to cater to the local palate. Many dishes are meant to share, making this lively spot a great place for get-togethers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2102;Chef Kang's;;Singapore;25 Mackenzie Road, 228681, Singapore;1.304735;103.84955;68;false;false;Cantonese;After working in a professional kitchen for over 40 years, Chef Kang has kept his creative fire burning, as the new items on the menu and hidden dishes off the menu demonstrate. Rest assured that signature dishes such as braised tofu with scallops are always available. To reduce food waste, the chef adjusts the portions according to your party size. It is closed when the chef travels, so call ahead to book.;Air conditioning;[]
2103;Candlenut;;Singapore;17A Dempsey Road, 249676, Singapore;1.3058588;103.8100724;77;false;false;Peranakan;The high ceiling makes the dining room feel open and spacious, while bamboo lampshades and rattan chair add a sense of serenity. Influenced by his mother and grandma, the young chef cooks traditional Peranakan fare with a creative twist and an Indonesian touch. The menu features many one-bite dishes, with up to 100 combinations. Those having difficulty making a choice can opt for the 20-course tasting menu. Service is warm and friendly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2104;Hamamoto;;Singapore;58 Tras Street, 078997, Singapore;1.2779413;103.8441838;33;true;true;Sushi;Sourcing the finest ingredients is something of an obsession for Kyoto-born Kazuhiro Hamamoto. And it’s not just his nigiri, whether nodoguro or chutoro, that shows his care and craftmanship – the dishes served before it, like spiny lobster with uni, or smoked meji-makuro, prove just as memorable. There is only one sitting at lunch and dinner at the handsome, curved counter, so you’ll need patience and perseverance when trying to secure a booking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2105;Willow;;Singapore;39 HongKong Street, 059678, Singapore;1.2874604;103.8473514;27;true;true;Asian Contemporary;After working in some prestigious kitchens, Chef Nicolas Tam makes his debut with this intimate, understated and well-run restaurant. His solid French techniques come through in his pan-Asian tasting menu featuring mostly Japanese ingredients, sporting refinement, precision and balance. Served and introduced by the chefs themselves, the courses flow seamlessly and build upon each other. Counter seats overlooking the kitchen are the ones to go for.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2106;Pangium;;Singapore;Gallop Entrance, Singapore Botanic Gardens, 11 Gallop Road, 259015, Singapore;1.3143675;103.8092377;91;true;true;Peranakan;The view of the lush green in the garden is one good reason to visit. But owner-chef Malcolm Lee's exquisite tasting menu that explores the untapped possibilities of Straits cuisine is what makes the experience of dining here unforgettable. Named after the plant that produces buah keluak seeds, a key ingredient in Peranakan cuisine, Pangium pays homage to family recipes passed down for generations with carefully crafted dishes that taste exceptional.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
2107;Nouri;;Singapore;72 Amoy Street, 069891, Singapore;1.28086;103.84713;79;false;true;Innovative;Championing a concept of “crossroads” cooking, the chef explores how cultures, ingredients, and geographical locations intersect with a menu that unfolds like a narrative. Motifs such as vanilla and turmeric are repeated throughout and lighter flavours build up to a tour-de-force climax. The marble table and conjoining chef’s counter are the preferred front row seats to interact with and watch the chefs work.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2109;Burnt Ends;;Singapore;#01-04, 7 Dempsey Road, 249671, Singapore;1.3048886;103.8086664;68;true;false;Barbecue;Years ago, the Aussie owner-chef David Pynt opened a pop-up in London called Burnt Enz to great acclaim. Then his refined barbecue food cooked in a wood-fire brick kiln was taken up a notch with Burnt Ends in Singapore. In 2021, it moved to this location, twice as big as its previous space. The small but interesting snack menu is worth exploring. Meats and fish are well complemented by the Australian wines on offer. Book ahead to secure a table.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2110;Summer Pavilion;;Singapore;The Ritz-Carlton, Millenia, Level 3, 7 Raffles Avenue, 039799, Singapore;1.291284;103.8603;93;true;false;Cantonese;This large, contemporary dining room is surrounded by a relaxing garden. You’ll be well looked after as the engaging staff provide service with plenty of vim and vigour. The extensive Cantonese menu covers all classics as well as seasonal dishes, with seafood being a particular highlight. The double-boiled sea whelk soup with fish maw, sauteed Dong Xing grouper fillet and braised abalone are just some of the specialities.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2111;CUT;;Singapore;The Shoppes at Marina Bay Sands, Galleria Level, #B1-71, 10 Bayfront Avenue, 018972, Singapore;1.2857261;103.8597843;62;false;false;Steakhouse;Synonymous with quality steaks with big flavours, celebrity chef Wolfgang Puck is a seal of confidence for this outpost of his famed namesake in LA. Here steaks are expertly seasoned, chargrilled and finished off under a 1200-degree broiler to leave them juicy and tender. Don’t forget to order the amazing onion rings with your steak. The wine list offers over 650 labels and a cocktail at the bar while waiting for your table adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2113;Waku Ghin;;Singapore;The Shoppes at Marina Bay Sands, Level 2 Dining, L2-03, 10 Bayfront Avenue, 018956, Singapore;1.283175;103.8598;46;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;The contemporary room is divided into three sections: a counter with seats, private rooms and the chef’s table. To stay close to the action, opt for the latter. Dinner features one sitting only with a choice between traditional and seasonal menus. Ingredients are of high quality and the food is nicely crafted. In addition to typical Japanese fare, some dishes are underscored by Western techniques with a pronounced Italian accent at times.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2114;Lei Garden;;Singapore;Chijmes, #01-24, 30 Victoria Street, 187996, Singapore;1.29538;103.85162;17;false;true;Cantonese;Unlike other branches in the group, this one has a European décor echoing the colonial style of the building that hosts it. That said, the menu remains the same as the others. Apart from the main menu, make sure you check out the chef’s selection menu. Double-boiled soups, flavourful and hearty, are unmissable. Deep-fried spare ribs marinated with shrimp paste are crispy and loaded with umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2115;Sushi Ichi;;Singapore;Marriott Tang Plaza Hotel, #01-04, 320 Orchard Road, 238865, Singapore;1.305105;103.8324;36;false;true;Sushi;The silky smooth and tactile counter was fashioned from a 300-year-old cypress and the wooden ornaments on the wall were handmade by a famous carpenter in Nara. Traditional Edomae sushi is made with seasonal seafood and vegetables from Japan. Only the best rice, marinated with red or white vinegar, makes it to the counter. Even the sauces are shipped from their flagship store in Japan to maintain consistency. The omakase menu is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2116;Matera;;Singapore;The Fullerton Waterboat House, #02-01/02/03, 3 Fullerton Road, 049215, Singapore;1.2870906;103.8534838;49;false;true;Italian Contemporary;A stone's throw away from many tourist attractions, the dining concept by experienced German chef Bjoern Alexander pushes the boundaries of Italian cooking with its bold Asian influences. The open kitchen lets diners watch the chefs at work against a backdrop of the Marina Bay Sands and the Esplanade. The signature whole red prawn features the perfectly smoked, juicy crustacean with a crispy prawn toast on the side to add contrasting textures.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2117;Sushi Sakuta;;Singapore;The Capitol Kempinski Hotel, #01-88, 15 Stamford Road, 178906, Singapore;1.2943463;103.8506988;49;true;true;Sushi;The space is simple yet elegant, befitting the hotel that houses it. There is a 10-seat counter made from a 200-year-old cypress tree from Nara, Japan, plus a private room. Owner-chef Sakuta works closely with the all-Japanese kitchen team, creating a season-driven omakase menu based on sushi and Japanese fish, plus premium items like caviar and truffles. Ask the sommelier about the expansive sake and wine selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
2118;Giewont;Poland;Kościelisko;Nędzy Kubińca 4, Kościelisko, 34 511, Poland;49.2904379;19.9217654;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Floor-to-ceiling glass windows ensure that a visit here will be accompanied by spectacular views of the eponymous mountain, which towers 1,895m above sea level. The spacious building is in total harmony with the region – an affluent area popular with skiers. An à la carte is available alongside three tasting menus (comprising classic, seasonal or vegan fare), which are the best way to sample the kitchen’s expressive, consummately seasoned dishes. Influences and produce come from both Poland (superbly cooked sirloin from Zaczyk) and France (excellent, plump asparagus).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2120;Arco by Paco Pérez;Poland;Gdansk;Olivia Centre, Aleja Grunwaldzka 472c, Gdansk, 80-309, Poland;54.4035847;18.5710527;45;true;false;Spanish, Mediterranean Cuisine;Located way up on the 33rd floor of northern Poland’s tallest building, this restaurant affords views over Gdańsk and out to the Baltic Sea. The cooking is equally spectacular, underpinned by Polish produce, driven by Spanish flavours and incorporating a few Italian influences. The superb jamón risotto is a prime example, with the rice infused with melted fat for an intense, meaty flavour. The service is smooth and charming, while the wine list is a treasure trove for oenophiles.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2121;Rozbrat 20;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Rozbrat 20, Warsaw, 00 447, Poland;52.2242187;21.0350918;18;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Managing to retain its neighbourhood feel while serving as a destination restaurant within the city, Rozbrat 20 has continued to evolve onwards and upwards over the years. Today, it’s a smart spot where the front room affords a view of the skilled chefs as they work on intricate dishes that have a creative edge – as with a deep, delicious consommé made from unused bread. Look out for the well-judged butter flavoured with Marmite, which the chef took a liking to while working in London.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2123;Grič;Slovenia;Šentjošt nad Horjulom;Šentjošt nad Horjulom 24d, Šentjošt nad Horjulom, 1354, Slovenia;46.0283624;14.2216299;71;false;true;Farm to table, Creative;Access to Luka Košir’s house and restaurant is via roads that wind their way through rolling hills dotted with small villages, through verdant landscapes that seem to reflect the restaurants “green” approach to cuisine. The same beautiful views can be enjoyed from the new veranda-style dining room, while fans of fancy culinary techniques will prefer a table facing the brand-new kitchen where they can watch the chefs at work. Here, the owner-chef presents his own seasonal, rural and creative vision of Slovenia via two surprise tasting menus described in terms of the duration of the meal (2hr 30 and 4hr respectively), rather than the number of courses. Dishes change daily depending on market availability and always feature top-quality ingredients full of flavour, including vegetables from the restaurant’s own kitchen gardens and eggs and meat (in season) from their own ducks. Fish from the not-so-distant Upper Adriatic also makes an appearance, sourced from three trusted fishing boats. The choice of wines by the glass allows for truly original pairings, in which wine and food complement each other to perfection. A non-alcoholic pairing option with tea, juices and home-made drinks is also available.;Car park,Counter dining;[]
2124;Hiša Linhart;Slovenia;Radovljica;Linhartov trg 17, Radovljica, 4240, Slovenia;46.3408368;14.1750205;84;true;false;Contemporary, Farm to table;Situated in a period building on the main road running through the charming small town of Radovljica, this restaurant is home to chef Uroš Štefelin who showcases the best of the Carnolian region on his 5-9-course tasting menu. Štefelin is expert in getting the best from his local, organic ingredients, which include trout from Lake Bohinj, native apples and pears, local beef, locally grown raspberries and honey made by local beekeepers, all of which feature in reinterpretations of traditional dishes alongside more original and imaginative fare. Influenced by his childhood memories, his delicious and intriguing “polenta” dessert is accompanied by yoghurt, honey and ice-cream with apricot compote. The wine list also focuses on Slovenia, with the exception of champagnes and a few wines from the Collio region of Italy. For a simpler, quicker meal, the bistro menu is available at lunchtime from Tuesday to Saturday.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
2125;Dam;Slovenia;Nova Gorica;Ulica Vinka Vodopivca 24, Nova Gorica, 5000, Slovenia;45.9580845;13.6621231;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;At this restaurant, it is owner-chef Uroš Fakuč himself who takes care of guests. With a friendly, relaxed manner, he divides his time between the dining room and the kitchen, where he creates a single tasting menu based on whatever is available in the market that day, offering a shorter option as well as the “XL” version. His love of fish is clearly evident on the menu, which features freshwater options as well as fish from the Adriatic cooked using modern, precise methods which focus on classic flavours rather than unnecessarily complex recipes. The cuisine is perfectly balanced between Slovenian and Italian influences – the risotto with oysters, sea asparagus and chilli peppers is particularly recommended!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2126;Gostilna Pri Lojzetu;Slovenia;Vipava;Dvorec Zemono, Vipava, 5271, Slovenia;45.8557213;13.9491988;18;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated on a small hill just outside Vipava, this elegant restaurant is housed in a 17C residence with an unusual Renaissance style. A charming dining room with a fireplace acts as the backdrop for excellent cuisine, featuring traditionally influenced dishes alongside more creative and experimental fare. Tomaž Kavčič is one of the best-known chefs in Slovenia and his style perfectly represents the transition between traditional and modern cuisine. We recommend the 7-course menu – if you’re lucky, it will include the delicious radicchio with foie gras and pork rind chips, or the tender beef cheeks served with different vegetable-based sauces. The theatrical and iconic “gin and tonic” will also make a real impression. An enthusiastic sommelier will guide you through the interesting wine list, which has a strong focus on the Vipava valley. We recommend trying the wines from the Burja estate, one of the area’s most representative producers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2127;COB;Slovenia;Portorož;Letoviška 1, Portorož, 6320, Slovenia;45.516425;13.5927606;80;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;COB, an acronym for “Cooking Outside the Box", is run by young Filip Matjaž who comes from a long line of restaurateurs and who greets his guests personally in the dining room before delighting them with his personalised, minimalist-style dishes prepared from almost exclusively local ingredients. His 8-course tasting menu features meat and fish dishes that demonstrate his love for the region through traditional recipes reinterpreted with imagination and creativity. Situated in the upper part of Portorož, the restaurant boasts stunning views of Piran bay from its terrace, as well as a designer-style dining room decorated in shades of grey. Excellent service completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
2128;Restavracija Strelec;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Grajska planota 1, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0489023;14.5092497;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This restaurant is housed in the old and picturesque Archers’ Tower in Ljubljana, one of the city’s most iconic tourist sights. Adorned with decorative murals from the 1950s, the dining room now provides the backdrop for chef Igor Jagodic’s surprise tasting menu (5,7 or 9 courses). Dishes are modern and creative, with occasional French and Mediterranean influences, as demonstrated by the turbot escalope in a lemon breaded crust, which is sautéed in butter and finished with a beurre blanc sauce. We can also recommend the cheese, shallot and beer mousse dumpling. When it comes to choosing wine, either speak with the sommelier or browse through the wine list which includes some excellent Slovenian options, as well as labels from further afield, some of which are available by the glass. We particularly enjoyed the Edi Simčič Triton 2022, a dry, medium-bodied white with interesting vegetal notes.;Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2129;Hiša Denk;Slovenia;Zgornja Kungota;Zgornja Kungota 11A, Zgornja Kungota, 2201, Slovenia;46.6383891;15.6146801;80;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Run by talented owner-chef Gregor Vračko, Hiša Denk is a real culinary institution and is housed in a minimalist and contemporary-style building which blends in harmoniously with the surrounding countryside. The menu features five or seven courses, with additional small dishes added occasionally. The cuisine has its roots in the Styria region although other influences also feature – enjoy Mangalica pork, delicious local trout and succulent lamb, as well as French pigeon and scallops in dishes which are creative, playful and intensely flavoured. Dinner is well paced, with a well-stocked wine cellar adding to the appeal. Comfortable guestrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2130;Pavus;Slovenia;Lasko;Grad Tabor Laško, Cesta na Svetino 23, Lasko, 3270, Slovenia;46.1571174;15.237399;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Dating back to the 13C, Lasko Castle has experienced many changes of ownership and various uses during its long history, right up to its current incarnation as a romantic, gourmet restaurant. We recommend one of the tasting menus (of various lengths) in order to appreciate Marko Pavčnik’s cuisine to the full. This chef pays careful attention to sustainability, sourcing his ingredients from a local eco-farm, as well as foraging and using every part of an animal (the so-called “nose-to-tail” approach). The smoked trout served with an elderflower sauce is sublime, while every course has its own identity and character. The extensive wine list focuses on Slovenia – try one of the whites from Styria, a region that produces wines of real character.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2132;Nineteen18;Lithuania;Vilnius;Dominikonų Gatvė 11, Vilnius, 01131, Lithuania;54.6812129;25.2855231;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Vilnius’ historic centre plays host to a lovely courtyard of shops and eateries, all owned by the same team, with the flagship being this lovely industrial-style restaurant with a refreshingly laid-back feel. You are given a sealed menu – to open either now or later – which comprises a series of around 10 dishes that flow effortlessly into one another. The dumplings with mushrooms are a joy to eat, as is the beautifully cooked Danish beef with a wonderful chicken caramel – and their farm plays a pivotal role when it comes to the produce. The kitchen counter is the place to sit, so that you can interact with Chef Andrius and his genial team.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2133;Pas mus;Lithuania;Vilnius;Pilies Gatvė 28, Vilnius, 01123, Lithuania;54.6822264;25.2892157;86;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Innovative;Pas mus loosely translates as ‘our house’ and that sums up this place perfectly. A truly special spot run by a small team led by Chef-Owner Vita, it exudes passion and energy, as they do everything they can to make your experience thoroughly enjoyable. Candles drip on the walls, you sit at fine wooden tables made by Vita’s partner, and the dishes have personality and purpose. The menu is a seasonal surprise – Vita regularly raids her mum’s garden for produce, as well as going foraging – and the innovative dishes blend together seamlessly, along with the characterful wines. The raspberry snow dessert with white chocolate ganache is heavenly.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2134;Demo;Lithuania;Vilnius;T. Ševčenkos Gatvė 16A, Vilnius, 03111, Lithuania;54.6769416;25.2646205;74;true;false;Innovative;This deliciously different eatery takes the form of a café during the day and then morphs into a restaurant later in the week. The monochrome décor takes in black ash units, black candles and tiny black & white portraits on the walls – an echo of the equal measures of boldness and restraint in the cooking. Chef-Owner Tadas is wise beyond his years and looks at food in a different way to most – feel free to ask questions as he presents some of the dishes. The two imaginative set menus create excitement at every course and the dishes are well matched by some interesting wine pairings. The suckling lamb is a highlight, as are the desserts – and, if you are lucky, Kogel Mogel will feature.;Air conditioning;[]
2135;Suyab Courtyard・Pickmoon Gourmet;China Mainland;Guangzhou;348 Yingbin Road, Panyu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;22.83158;113.483335;17;false;false;Chao Zhou;This building houses a furniture store, a restaurant and a Japanese tea saloon. The restaurant has nine private rooms and a banquet venue which seats over 30 guests. Helmed by the experienced Chef Fai, the kitchen delivers refined Chao Zhou dishes. Menus are tailor-made according to availability of ingredients, as well as guests’ budget and preferences after reservations are made via the texting app. Ingredients are top-notch and the food is impeccably made.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
2136;Stiller;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, LN Garden Hotel, 368 Huanshi East Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.138026;113.280695;79;false;false;European;Named after the owner-chef who also runs Taian Table, Stiller is a different dining concept altogether. Start the meal with a personalised cocktail at the bar or the lounge area by the floor-to-ceiling windows. Then head to the colourful dining room with comfy couch seating. The menu features seasonal offerings alongside some German-inspired dishes which are rare to find in the town. Also ask servers for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2137;Lai Heen;China Mainland;Guangzhou;3F, The Ritz-Carlton Hotel, 3 Xing An Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.11883;113.321816;70;true;false;Cantonese;Lai Heen champions modern Cantonese cooking deeply rooted in tradition and only the best ingredients make it to the table. Its signature steamed sunflower seed-fed chicken needs pre-ordering, while Australian lobster on egg-white custard wins the hearts of many diners. Dishes with Chao Zhou touches also fare well – try boiled, then chilled lime-scented yellow croaker with bean paste, or lemon-infused yellow croaker and thick fish maw soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2138;Yu Yue Heen;China Mainland;Guangzhou;71F, Four Seasons Hotel, 5 Zhujiang West Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.119916;113.317995;79;false;true;Cantonese;The head chef, who hails from Guangdong, has been cooking professionally since the age of 15 and has extensive experience at hotels in Shanghai and Nanjing. Each dish embodies the utmost finesse and attention to detail. The range of dim sum at lunch is dazzling – especially the deep-fried taro dumplings with shrimp and chicken filling. His signature crispy-skin chicken, made with birds from Qingyuan, boasts robust flavours and a velvety texture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2139;Rêver;China Mainland;Guangzhou;5F, North Tower, Guangzhou Media Centre, 370 Yuejiang West Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.109474;113.331346;89;true;true;French Contemporary;With stunning river views and a calming ambience, Rêver lives up to its name. The culinary team has an all-star lineup as most chefs have worked in prestigious establishments. Only one tasting menu is offered at dinner and diners may choose between 6 or 8 courses, all underpinned by solid French techniques and infused with subtle Cantonese overtones. The menu changes every few months to reflect seasonality and most ingredients are sourced locally.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2140;BingSheng Private Kitchen (Tianhe East Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;178 Tianhe East Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.137287;113.328901;95;true;false;Cantonese;This décor re-creates the old-time charm of luxury mansions in the Xiguan district, while the artwork and floral accents add an updated touch. The menu focuses on healthy cooking with seasonal, organic ingredients. Signature dishes include braised Doumen mud crab with hairy squash that imparts robust seafood flavour, roast lemongrass-scented squab that bursts with juices, and velvety ginger milk custard with bird’s nest. Reserve a table 2 or 3 days ahead.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2141;Xin Ji;China Mainland;Guangzhou;270 Changdi Damalu, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.114612;113.25478;31;true;false;Cantonese;This street was once known for the sheer number of seafood restaurants on it. Though most of its competitors were shuttered for good, Xin Ji is still going strong after over 30 years of service. And of course, picking live critters from the fish tank at the door is part of the ritual. If you have no idea what to pick, try their signature eel dishes – freshwater eel braised with roast pork and swamp eel rice, both boasting fatty, firm flesh.;Air conditioning;[]
2142;Jade River;China Mainland;Guangzhou;3F, White Swan Hotel, 1 Shamian South Street, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.108321;113.237649;20;false;false;Cantonese;Diners here unwind with a cup of tea freshly brewed by tea masters. The traditional garden, water features, exquisite woodwork and artisan Manchurian windows give it a serene feel. The food is, of course, no less impressive. Steamed sunflower seed-fed chicken is delivered straight from the farm daily. Baked pigeon with lemongrass and salt is another proud creation of the team. Also try various poultry and meats in white marinade.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2143;BingSheng Mansion (Xiancun Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;5F, Shoufu Mansion, 2 Xiancun Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.117404;113.322958;95;true;true;Cantonese;In a main dining room and 32 private rooms, all exuding understated glamour, this place champions innovative and refined Cantonese fare. It serves hand-crafted dim sum, a rare thing these days. The menu has an array of double-boiled tonics, such as fish maw and ginseng soup. Pre-order to avoid disappointment. Round off the meal with black sesame sweet soup over milk custard for double indulgence. Other signatures include stir-fried flat rice noodles with beef, and juicy roasted goose.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2144;Lingnan House;China Mainland;Guangzhou;5F, Rosewood Hotel, 6 Zhujiang East Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.119891;113.320629;71;false;true;Cantonese;Perforated windows, ceiling fans and chandeliers impart retro Lingnan flair. Chef Feng also bases his recipes on Lingnan traditions and seasonal local produce, but slightly tweaked to the local palate and spruced up with unique creativity. His Shunde minced fish soup perfumed by makrut lime leaves, and roast goose that takes 45 minutes to cook in the oversized grill, tend to sell out fast. End the meal with silky ginger milk curd in Shawan style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2145;Hongtu Hall;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, White Swan Hotel, 1 Shamian South Street, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.108321;113.237649;81;true;false;Dim Sum;Besides river views and stunning murals, Hongtu Hall is prized for its exquisitely crafted dim sum ranging from the classics to novel creations, as well as velvety congee and juicy roast meats. Make sure to try their shrimp dumplings and shrimp shaomai. Tableside tea service is also a nice touch. The restaurant is always busy during opening hours and reservations are accepted for guests staying in the hotel only. Other customers have to simply join the queue.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2146;Imperial Treasure Fine Teochew Cuisine;China Mainland;Guangzhou;L307, 3F, Taikoo Hui, 383 Tianhe Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1372293;113.3268341;38;false;true;Chao Zhou;The Singapore-based chain opened its first outpost here in 2019, specialising in Chao Zhou food. The head chef from Hong Kong makes sure traditions are respected in the kitchen, while adding a refined touch to his repertoire. Classics, such as steamed then chilled swimmer crab and grey mullet, boast natural umami and firm flesh. Marinated dishes are also a big hit – apart from goose meat, goose liver and cuttlefish, also try pork intestines and hock.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2148;Song;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 417, 4F, G.T. Land Plaza Winter, 16 Zhujiang East Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.12226;113.321903;47;false;false;Sichuan;Christened after the dynasty and the owner’s last name, this award-winning space boasts pillars covered with dramatically lit, stainless steel bricks. Gigantic glass-feathered wings are hung from the mirrored ceiling and thereby lend an eerie sense of space. Most items on the menu are Sichuanese, with occasional offerings from other provinces. Signatures include spicy boiled tiger grouper, jujube wood-roasted 42-day Peking duck and spicy crab.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2150;Yu Garden;China Mainland;Guangzhou;6 Tianshun Road, Huangpu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.179545;113.4142336;82;true;false;Fujian;As an art lover, Chef May chose to open her place away from the city, in an airy space adorned by artworks on loan from the gallery nearby. Tables are well spaced out, but consider booking a private room for special occasions. Fujian cuisine prevails on the menu and most ingredients are shipped straight from the province. Specialities such as the umami-loaded sea worm jelly and the aromatic Xiamen ginger duck stew are well executed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
2152;Tapio;Finland;Ruka;Rukatunturintie 9, Ruka, 93830, Finland;66.1665646;29.1386013;95;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located just a stone’s throw from the slopes in the ski resort of Ruka, this endearing little restaurant is run by British Chef Connor and his Finnish partner Johanna. They serve around 20 guests in a warm, relaxed setting with vintage skiing posters on the walls. Excellent produce, be it hand-dived Norwegian scallop or local trout, is the basis for each skilful dish. The accompaniments appear simple, but add real depth of flavour to the cooking, like a rich foraged cep sauce with the scallop.;;[]
2156;Frederiksminde;Denmark;Præstø;Klosternakken 8, Præstø, 4720, Denmark;55.12424;12.049009;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A delightful destination for a romantic weekend, this 19th Century pavilion is located in a park that was historically the garden of a monastery. Today, the building houses both a classically decorated country house hotel and this charming restaurant. Head Chef Jonas Mikkelsen and his team are passionate about sustainably sourced produce, which is invariably of excellent quality and enhanced by the kitchen’s precise technique and harmonious combinations – organic Lolland chicken with fabulous morels, asparagus and ramson is a prime example.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2157;Gastromé;Denmark;Aarhus;Grenåvej 127, Risskov, Aarhus, 8240, Denmark;56.1870316;10.2177829;46;true;true;Modern Cuisine;One of the city’s most elegant restaurants, Gastromé sits within a smartly refurbished villa dating from 1911. The focus here is on the glass-walled kitchen, where luxurious ingredients – including those from their mini farm – are prepared using complex, modern techniques. The result is refined, elegant cooking that has a wonderful balance of both textures and flavours – some leaning towards local traditions and others of a more international bent. You might find grilled scallop with dashi, tomato and radish or wood pigeon with blackberry, pickled beetroot and parsnip.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2159;Lysverket;Norway;Bergen;Rasmus Meyers Allé 9, Bergen, 5015, Norway;60.3893076;5.3289615;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in the KODE 4 art museum, this stylish restaurant offers views over lake Lille Lungegårdsvannet. Larger than life Chef-Owner Christopher Haatuft passionately oversees the whole place, serving dishes and engaging with guests. The 10 course tasting menu is informed by fabulous Norwegian produce, always including scallops landed nearby by Christopher’s close friend. Dishes have a freshness about them and allow the main ingredient to shine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2160;Seafood Gastro;Sweden;Stockholm;Södra Blasieholmshamnen 8, Stockholm, 11148, Sweden;59.3294565;18.0756768;55;true;true;Seafood;The magnificent, imposing Grand Hôtel is the home for this decadent restaurant, where rich flavours and impeccable Nordic seafood reign supreme. The tasting menu takes you through a roll-call of high-end fish and shellfish, whether it’s sweet langoustine, milky raw shrimp or Oscietra caviar, the ultimate premium ingredient. Each one is treated with great skill by the chefs, with Japanese influences like wasabi, yuzu and chawanmushi making an appearance. It all comes at a price, but the luxuriousness of the produce is undeniable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2161;Iris;Norway;Rosendal;Hardangerfjorden, Rosendal, 5470, Norway;59.9846612;5.9339194;18;false;false;Creative;Providing one of the most astonishing dining settings you will find, this restaurant is housed inside a gleaming floating structure known as the ‘Salmon Eye’. Situated in Hardangerfjord, it can be accessed via a short boat ride from Rosendal and presents the opportunity to dine with an unparalleled view of the fjord. Fortunately, this is no example of style over substance, with the kitchen’s technical skill coming across in dishes that make use of foraged and sometimes unglamorous produce, like lumpsucker fish and Norwegian cuttlefish. This is a truly unique experience.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2162;Moss;Iceland;Grindavík;Blue Lagoon, Norðurljósavegur 11, Grindavík, 240, Iceland;63.879826;-22.450119;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Next to the Blue Lagoon, one of Iceland's most famous attractions, sits this modern restaurant. The tasting menu (also available in vegan form) showcases the best of Iceland’s produce in a series of exacting and visually stunning dishes. The moss-covered rocks and lava fields visible outside add to the character and atmosphere, whilst a chef's table is available if you want to watch the team in action.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2164;Project;Sweden;Gothenburg;Södra Vägen 45, Gothenburg, 412 54, Sweden;57.6979745;11.9825147;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This cosy restaurant is personally run by a husband and wife team, whose balanced, seasonal tasting menu sees seafood and local game lead the way. The cooking is refined, original and intensely flavoured, while the eloquent team proudly explain the components of each dish with a smile. There are a number of Japanese influences on the menu too, like in the turbot with yuzu kosho and shiitake. The delicious bread takes five days to make.;Terrace;[]
2165;Koka;Sweden;Gothenburg;Viktoriagatan 12, Gothenburg, 411  25, Sweden;57.6986003;11.9654719;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set beneath an ornate 19C glass ceiling, this warm, elegant restaurant comes with wood-panelling and bespoke furnishings. Carefully prepared dishes are light and refreshingly original. Menu KOKA is the main event, the Farmers Menu offers a slightly lighter option and an even shorter version is available at certain times. All menus are meat-free, focussed instead on quality seafood and plant-led cooking. Well-chosen wines and smooth service complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2166;Operakällaren;Sweden;Stockholm;Operahuset, Karl XII's Torg, Stockholm, 111 86, Sweden;59.3297475;18.0713797;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;If you're celebrating a special occasion, then you've come to the right place. Sweden's most opulent restaurant sits within the historic Opera House, and the stunning, high-ceilinged room comes bedecked with chandeliers, paintings and original gilded oak panelling decorated with carvings.;Interesting wine list;[]
2167;Marchal;Denmark;Copenhagen;Kongens Nytorv 34, Copenhagen, 1050 K, Denmark;55.6806399;12.584676;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;Named after Hotel D’Angleterre’s 1755 founder, this stylish restaurant boasts a floor to ceiling wine cellar and views out over the Royal Square. Precisely prepared dishes are modern in their presentation but built on a classical French base. They also offer an extensive caviar collection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2168;ARO;Denmark;Odense;Østerbro 32, Odense, 5000, Denmark;55.4022012;10.4081362;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Unusually set in an old factory on the edge of town, this contemporary restaurant upholds the theme of having 'craftsmen in its workshop'. The concise menu showcases wonderfully fresh, seasonal produce and dishes mix the rustic with the refined. Choose between a 5 or 7 course set menu with drinks pairings or create your own meal from the 7 small plates listed.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2170;Ti Trin Ned;Denmark;Fredericia;Toldkammeret 9, Fredericia, 7000, Denmark;55.5597311;9.7548686;93;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The elegant Ti Trin Ned affords beautiful sea views – and it is the sea, the kitchen garden and the surrounding land that inspires the menu. Sourcing is central to their ethos, with top quality ingredients providing an excellent base for the original, understated dishes, which showcase strong classical techniques and real depth of flavour. As well as wine flights, you can also accompany the cooking with either juice or beer pairings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
2172;ÄNG;Sweden;Tvååker;Ästad Vingård, Ästad 10, Tvååker, 432 77, Sweden;57.0649323;12.5594919;91;false;false;Creative;This stunningly designed, greenhouse-inspired restaurant is set over two levels and sports a pared-back look. Your visit starts with finely crafted snacks at the chef’s counter, then leads into a no-waste surprise tasting menu that uses fantastic seasonal produce from the surrounding Halland region. Skilfully prepared dishes are delicate, balanced and full of flavour, and the cheese course is taken in a magnificent wine cellar. The Ästad Vingård estate also houses vineyards and a luxury hotel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2173;LYST;Denmark;Vejle;Havneøen 1, Vejle, 7100, Denmark;55.7060238;9.5548961;96;true;false;Creative;This extraordinary building stands directly in the fjord and its unique interior is equally striking. Dinner is an engaging, multi-course affair that begins with snacks served at the gorgeous glass-topped bar. Then it’s through to the aptly named ‘Sail Room’ for the main event, though you may be taken to other areas of the building for some courses. The creative, sophisticated dishes showcase exceptional produce, including Limfjord mussels and wonderful local trout. The passionate service team help to make this a truly special destination.;Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2174;Mon Oncle;Norway;Oslo;Universitetsgata 9, Oslo, 0164, Norway;59.917166;10.7389457;83;true;true;French;Named after a classic Jacques Tati comedy, this intimate restaurant harks back to the founding era of French cuisine. The chefs wear toques and their classical training comes through in dishes like duck à l'orange with glazed turnips, carrots and kumquat confit. There is a pleasing level of refinement in the sauces – like a superb sauce marinière with razor clams royale – and everything is beautifully presented. An impressive French wine list accompanies the food.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2175;Knystaforsen;Sweden;Rydöbruk;Rydöforsvägen 4, Rydöbruk, 31442, Sweden;56.958207;13.1400487;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A meal at Knystaforsen is truly a delight and staying the night further enhances the experience. A former sawmill, it sits in a wonderful spot beside the river, surrounded by woodland, and nature really is at every turn, be that through the panoramic windows or on your plate. Superb ingredients are from the local area and traditional wood-fired cooking adds a smoky edge – one course is even served outside by the campfire. You might sample such delights as moose tartare, trout with lingonberries or duck hearts with wild garlic, which are paired with both wines and interesting non-alcoholic creations.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
2176;Syttende;Denmark;Sønderborg;Nørre Havnegade 23, Sønderborg, 6400, Denmark;54.9139503;9.7833821;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Danish;This restaurant is situated on the 17th floor of the ultra-modern Alsik hotel and boasts views over Flensburg Fjord. The set, multi-course menu offers innovative, beautifully crafted dishes inspired by the local South Jutland region and featuring top quality ingredients from around the globe. Accompanying wine flights are available.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2177;Sushi Sho;Sweden;Stockholm;Upplandsgatan 45, Stockholm, 113 28, Sweden;59.3411916;18.0498009;43;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;With its white tiled walls and compact counter seating, this restaurant couldn't look simpler, but it is not a place to be underestimated. Classic Japanese sushi preparations soar to a high level thanks to the exceptional quality of the local seafood ingredients. Diners are all served at the same time, omakase style, with the signature soy-cured egg and the sake tasting menu proving the highlights.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
2178;Kaskis;Finland;Turku;Kaskenkatu 6A, Turku, 20700, Finland;60.4467293;22.2724407;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Kaskis is a place of contrasts. It’s run by a team with colourful hair and bold tattoos, yet the atmosphere is serene – and the cooking comes with powerful colours and flavours yet a delicate, detailed touch. The skilfully prepared 7 course set menu is accompanied by either wine or non-alcoholic pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2180;FAGN;Norway;Trondheim;Ørjaveita 4, Trondheim, 7010, Norway;63.4339936;10.3962931;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The word 'Fagn' refers to the welcome, food and lodgings given to travellers at rural farmhouses in days gone by – and the team here want their guests to experience the same warmth at this intimate restaurant. Each of the beautiful surprise dishes comes with a story, which is enthusiastically explained.;;[]
2181;Demo;Finland;Helsinki;Itämerenkatu 25, Helsinki, 00180, Finland;60.163377;24.9070483;84;false;false;Modern Cuisine;It might be slightly more challenging than usual to reach the entrance – you receive a code to open the side door before taking the lift up to the 14th floor – but once you’re safely ensconced, the view from this modern office building is worth it. The modern open-plan interior allows you to see into the kitchen where the chefs prepare the interesting set menu. Top quality local and international ingredients come together in flavoursome dishes crafted using classical techniques, with the breads in particular being a highlight.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2183;Alouette;Denmark;Copenhagen;Kronprinsessegade 8, Copenhagen, 1306, Denmark;55.6829942;12.5811647;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Your meal comes as a surprise at this luxurious restaurant, where the menu is built around the regions from which the top-quality ingredients originate. Both the friendly service team and the chefs themselves keep you well-informed however, telling the story of each dish and its well-balanced components – many of which are smoked over the wood-burning fire. While the cooking is pared back, the flavours are sublime, with the seafood dishes being a highlight – you might find hand-dived scallops with habanada peppers or smoked Hokkaido pumpkin with Rossini Gold caviar.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2184;Under;Norway;Lindesnes;Bålyveien50, Lindesnes, 4521, Norway;58.040731;7.1543665;70;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This breathtakingly stunning building half-submerged in the sea provides a singular and spectacular setting in which to dine. The sense of anticipation grows as you descend the beautifully crafted oak-and-steel staircase to the dining room 5m under the sea, where panoramic windows afford an underwater view. It's no surprise to find plenty of seafood on the seasonal tasting menu, where superb produce, like sweet and juicy langoustine tail, is treated with a light touch and welcome restraint to bring out its natural flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2185;DILL;Iceland;Reykjavík;Laugavegur 59, Reykjavík, 101, Iceland;64.1443654;-21.922443;69;false;false;Creative;Palpable enthusiasm emanates from the chefs as they serve the dishes at this first-floor restaurant which overlooks the city's main pedestrianised shopping street. You enter via an unassuming door, before ascending a spiral staircase and being greeted by the chefs in their open kitchen. Sustainability drives everything they do and the team's pride in this is clear. The cooking is not showy or overcomplicated, but soars thanks to clever combinations and an ability to elevate seemingly simple ingredients like the humble potato to something truly special.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2186;Nour;Sweden;Stockholm;Norrlandsgatan 24, Stockholm, 111 43, Sweden;59.3357675;18.071196;47;false;false;Creative;Up on the third floor of a beautiful city centre townhouse, you’ll find this sedate restaurant with a discreet, intimate feel. In a nod to Chef Sayan Isaksson’s heritage and experience, the menu seamlessly fuses Swedish produce with Japanese influences – such as in the okonomiyaki, which uses black truffle from the island of Gotland. Original, well-composed dishes are spread across a tasting menu of 5 or 9 courses.;;[]
2187;Bar Amour;Norway;Oslo;Waldemar Thranes gate 70, Oslo, 0173, Norway;59.928181;10.7492884;96;false;false;Creative;With its low-ceilinged intimacy and bright red décor, the cheekily named Bar Amour contains subtle throwbacks to the brothel that once occupied this space. In these unusual surroundings, an impressively well-run dining experience unfolds. The tasting menu blends superb, recognisably Norwegian produce, like skrei cod and reindeer, with influences from Chef Carlos De Medeiros’ native Portugal. Every dish arrives showcasing refined craft and a harmonious balancing of flavours. It's not that easy to find, hidden away on the first floor of the Tranen pizzeria and café.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2188;ÓX;Iceland;Reykjavík;Laugavegur 55, Reykjavík, 101, Iceland;64.1446561;-21.9234607;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Ring the buzzer labelled 'Amma Don' on the door outside, and around 4 hours later you will leave having had a truly immersive experience. This begins in Amma Don itself, a slightly retro cocktail bar where an aperitif and snacks are served, before a bookcase on the wall opens up and you move through to a 17-seat kitchen counter. The cooking itself is rich and hearty, eschewing unnecessary adornment in favour of deriving maximum intensity of flavour, but with a gentle touch when needed – as with the excellent use of Icelandic-grown wasabi.;Counter dining;[]
2189;Speilsalen;Norway;Trondheim;Dronningens gate 5, Trondheim, 7011, Norway;63.4318148;10.3990388;39;true;false;Contemporary, Seafood;This grand dining room in the Britannia hotel comes complete with mirrors, sparkling chandeliers and even a Caviar Bar. Choose one of the large tables or, if you want to interact with the chefs, opt to sit at the counter, where you’re served at the same time as your fellow guests. The intricate and technically accomplished dishes have a classical base and make great use of the best Norwegian ingredients, with the exceptional snacks a brilliant way to kick things off.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2190;formel B;Denmark;Copenhagen;Vesterbrogade 182-184, Frederiksberg, Copenhagen, 1800 C, Denmark;55.6706842;12.5355099;98;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This friendly, neighbourhood-style restaurant is located in Frederiksberg, the birthplace of designer Finn Juhl, and the seductively lit dining room is graced with examples of his mid-century furniture. In a refreshing take on the tasting menu format, diners choose five courses from around a dozen offered by the kitchen. Each one is beautifully presented with flavours to match, like juicy, sweet langoustine tails with textures of carrot. The wine list offers plenty of fine burgundy and bordeaux, while artisan kombuchas lead the non-alcoholic options.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2191;Tri;Denmark;Agger;Vesterhavsvej 5A, Agger, 7770, Denmark;56.7820975;8.2331898;31;false;true;Creative;In a small coastal town by the North Sea you'll find this contemporary greenhouse-like building. Made from wood and glass, it is a bright and airy space that is filled with customers enjoying quality cooking. Chef Nicolas Min Jørgensen has created a menu themed around seasonal and local produce, which is used with a nose-to-tail, low waste ethos. Dishes provide pure, natural flavours and are prepared with care and precision.;;[]
2192;Domæne;Denmark;Herning;Gødstrupvej 62, Herning, 7400, Denmark;56.1565646;8.8969789;70;true;false;Creative;On the outskirts of town lies this intimate restaurant housed inside an eye-catching wooden dome. There is a certain romance to the interior, which also features plants and artificial grass for a nature-inspired theme. The smooth, professional team serve creative Nordic dishes that vary in style but consistently display an excellent level of skill and refinement.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2193;Dashi;Sweden;Stockholm;Rådmansgatan 23, Stockholm, 114 25, Sweden;59.3426722;18.0657669;82;true;false;Japanese;Two chefs, one Swedish and one Australian, are behind this homage to Japanese cuisine which sports the uncluttered, pared-back décor common to both Nordic and Japanese restaurants. Prime Swedish produce powers dishes that come from an ‘osusume’ menu and have a meticulous, delicate construction. Expect the eponymous broth to make several appearances – like as a marinade for amberjack – while desserts such as their take on a classic Mont Blanc are a highlight. Completing the Japanese culinary experience is a varied sake list that includes some rare selections.;Notable sake list;[]
2194;Sabi Omakase Oslo;Norway;Oslo;Ruseløkkveien 3, Oslo, 0251, Norway;59.9141305;10.7289794;96;false;true;Sushi;Young chef Airis Zapašnikas pours his skill and knowledge of Japanese cuisine into an impressive omakase menu at this intimate restaurant. Just 10 guests sit at a counter whilst the chef works and explains his methods, serving dishes that combine traditional sushi techniques with quality Norwegian fish. At over three hours, this is a extended and enchanting experience, enhanced by wine, sake or juice pairings.;Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2195;Adam / Albin;Sweden;Stockholm;Rådmansgatan 16, Stockholm, 114 25, Sweden;59.3430072;18.0662575;77;true;false;Creative;The eponymous Chef-Owners offer an exciting all-round experience at this intimate restaurant, where they finish dishes at the table while they explain the make-up of these original, intricate creations. Luxury Nordic produce is to the fore in the boldly flavoured dishes, but the influences are global, from Provençal (artichoke barigoule) to Japanese (mushroom chawanmushi). Service is personable and the room has a lovely moody-chic feel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2196;Søllerød Kro;Denmark;Copenhagen;Søllerødvej 35, Copenhagen, 2840, Denmark;55.8134465;12.4951512;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A characterful 17C thatched inn by a pond in a picturesque village, with a delightful courtyard terrace and three elegant, intimate rooms. In keeping with the surroundings, cooking has a classical heart but is presented in a modern style. Dishes have deceptive depth and the wine list is a tome of beauty.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2199;Sabi Omakase Stavanger;Norway;Stavanger;Pedersgata 38, Stavanger, 4013, Norway;58.9699926;5.7432527;86;true;false;Sushi;A 10-seat counter is the stage for this multi-course sushi experience, where each element is introduced and explained to diners by the light-hearted and engaging team. Watch the chefs' deft hands at work as they craft dishes founded on superlative, mostly Norwegian ingredients. The skilful preparations include traditional nigiri as well as more playful, internationally tinged creations like a fish ‘taco’ where nori replaces the usual tortilla.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2200;SK Mat & Människor;Sweden;Gothenburg;Johannebergsgatan 24, Gothenburg, 412 55, Sweden;57.6972648;11.9828127;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s a chic, relaxed vibe to this elegant restaurant where you can watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen. They deliver your dishes too, which are attractively presented and a model of self-restraint, utilising well-thought-through combinations. Quality Swedish and Danish produce helps to achieve good depth of flavour, with a beautiful balance of richness and acidity running through the cooking.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2201;28+;Sweden;Gothenburg;Götabergsgatan 28, Gothenburg, 411 34, Sweden;57.6981746;11.9738899;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic French;This atmospheric, passionately run basement restaurant has been a Gothenburg institution for over 30 years. Carefully judged, classically based cooking showcases prime seasonal ingredients, skilfully blending French and Swedish influences to create intricate, precise, boldly flavoured dishes. There's an exceptional cheese selection and an outstanding wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2202;Grön;Finland;Helsinki;Albertinkatu 36, Helsinki, 00180, Finland;60.1646073;24.9326985;82;false;false;Creative;A seasonal and sustainable ethos runs throughout this cosy, passionately run restaurant – neatly demonstrated by its shelves filled with jars of fermenting foodstuffs. The all-Scandinavian ingredients – like glistening Norwegian cod – are at the heart of the cooking, with a real purity to the best of the dishes. Vegetables get a chance to shine too, and there’s a vegan menu available if you want to experience this to the full. Dishes are brought to the table by the chefs, and the natural wine flights are well-chosen.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2204;Dragsholm Slot Gourmet;Denmark;Hørve;Dragsholm Allé, Hørve, 4534, Denmark;55.771236;11.390805;69;false;false;Creative;An atmospheric cellar restaurant set in the former kitchens of Denmark’s oldest castle. The multi-course menu is called ‘Time and Place’ and offers carefully crafted, innovative and intensely flavoured dishes which showcase local, foraged, seasonal and preserved produce. An impressive wine list accompanies.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2205;Statholdergaarden;Norway;Oslo;Rådhusgate 11, Oslo, 0151, Norway;59.9094664;10.7431174;27;true;false;Classic Cuisine;A charming 17th-century house in the city’s heart plays host to these three elegant dining rooms, where chandeliers hang from wonderfully ornate stucco ceilings and an interesting array of antiques and curios are on display. Expertly rendered classical cooking uses seasonal ingredients in familiar combinations that are given a personal touch when it comes to the seasoning. Dishes could include seared halibut with spiced scallops or langoustine in a deliciously rich bisque. Top-notch service and a comprehensive wine list complete the picture.;Interesting wine list;[]
2207;HYDE;Norway;Oslo;Rosteds Gate 15b, Oslo, 0178, Norway;59.9195698;10.7490285;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;HYDE keeps the lights down low but cranks the music up high – and the laid-back, lively atmosphere makes for a fun evening out. Top quality ingredients are skilfully cooked to create delicate dishes with bold, punchy flavours. Well-chosen natural wines and super-friendly service add to the experience.;;[]
2208;Etoile;Sweden;Stockholm;Norra Stationsgatan 51, Stockholm, 113 44, Sweden;59.3495123;18.0437729;79;false;true;Creative, International;After travelling the world, two friends opened this restaurant to showcase their experiences through food, yet with a decidedly imaginative streak. The cooking is characterised by bold, surprising flavours and creativity – what appears to be savoury may in fact be sweet, and vice versa. The chefs delight in subverting expectations with their playfully named dishes that reference global food traditions, like 'Surf and Turf' and 'Afternoon Tea Party'.;Air conditioning;[]
2209;The Samuel;Denmark;Copenhagen;Hellerupvej 40, Copenhagen, 2900, Denmark;55.7324289;12.5685039;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An extensive renovation has given a pristine shine to this over 100-year-old restaurant inside a red-brick villa. A ring-shaped, marble-topped bar sits in front of a gleaming open kitchen, where the chefs craft boldly flavoured dishes from superb produce – such as Jutland beef tenderloin glazed in cognac, truffle and green Madagascan peppercorns. There’s a sense of classic luxury throughout, typified by the collection of prestige champagnes housed inside an impressive wine cellar.;Interesting wine list;[]
2210;Finnjävel Salonki;Finland;Helsinki;Ainonkatu 3, Helsinki, 00100, Finland;60.1719135;24.9314505;55;true;false;Contemporary;An intimate, elegant and professionally run restaurant with just ten tables – everything from the cutlery to the decanters is made by Finnish craftspeople. Set menus feature modern interpretations of traditional Finnish dishes, with first class ingredients used in detailed, technically skilled combinations.;;[]
2211;VÅR;Finland;Porvoo;Papinkatu 17, Porvoo, 06100, Finland;60.396319;25.6640296;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the city’s Old Town, you will find this 1920s former chocolate factory whose historic exterior is in contrast to the sleek and stylish restaurant within. Dried flowers on the walls impart a ‘back to nature’ feel perfect for their all-encompassing sustainable ethos. The menu's heart is firmly in Porvoo, using seasonal local produce in immaculately presented dishes that are detailed, complex and composed of subtle, beautifully judged flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
2212;Villa Vest;Denmark;Lønstrup;Strandvejen 138, Lønstrup, 9800, Denmark;57.4766654;9.7962815;85;true;false;Creative;Incredible North Sea views wow diners at this beautifully situated first floor restaurant, built on a cliffside and overlooking the waves lashing underneath. Chef Anders Holm is from the area, and his menu gives pride of place to local seafood. This quality produce is enhanced by strong modern techniques, in dishes that are precisely cooked and highly creative. The meat has often been bred by the owner himself, who also owns the nearby Villa Vest Badehotel.;Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2213;Signum;Sweden;Mölnlycke;Hällsnäs Hotell,  Långenäsvägen 150, Mölnlycke, 435 35, Sweden;57.675447;12.1786546;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The shores of Landvettersjön lake provide a beautiful setting for this excellent showcase of Scandinavian seafood. The likes of oysters, langoustines and top-notch turbot come from the on-view kitchen and are often cooked over an open fire. Skill is evident across an extended tasting menu which features bold flavours and original combinations. The service team ensure the whole evening runs like clockwork.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2215;Hot Shop;Norway;Oslo;Københavngata 18, Oslo, 0566, Norway;59.9281988;10.7685963;16;true;false;Modern Cuisine;You’ll be well looked after by the friendly team at this canteen-style neighbourhood bistro. Its quirky name comes not from what it serves but has been kept from its former life as a sex shop. Both the décor and the cooking take on a simple, unfussy style, with the surprise tasting menu formed around the best local ingredients available. Rich, modern dishes are elegant, vibrant and technically adept, with delicate touches and real depth of flavour. Options might include reindeer with an aromatic chanterelle and porcini broth, and the Jura wines in particular are a hit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2216;PM & Vänner;Sweden;Växjö;Storgatan 22, Växjö, 352 31, Sweden;56.8789279;14.8043573;67;false;false;Creative;Their philosophy is based on ‘forest, lake and meadow’, with much of the produce coming from their own garden and bakery. The tasting menu is explained with infectious passion, and cooking is ambitious, elaborate and sophisticated. An extraordinary wine list offers a huge array of vintages from top producers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2217;SAVAGE;Norway;Oslo;Nedre Slottsgate 2, Oslo, 0153, Norway;59.9093941;10.7401093;74;true;true;Creative;Your experience here will be far more pleasant than the name suggests, with a range of global influences resulting in fabulously original dishes. The restaurant is tucked inside the Revier hotel and is enlivened by a bold mural dominating one wall. Counter seats are available to enjoy the beautifully presented and technically impressive dishes which meld flavours, textures and combinations from around the world.;Air conditioning;[]
2218;NOA Chef’s Hall;Estonia;Tallinn;Ranna tee 3, Tallinn, 12112, Estonia;59.4951028;24.8263897;44;true;false;Creative;Set within the same striking building as restaurant NOA is the stylish NOA Chef’s Hall, where you start your evening with an aperitif in the romantic lounge overlooking Tallinn Bay. The on-view kitchen is the heart of the restaurant – with the open fire is used to great effect – and luxury ingredients are to the fore, be that Canadian lobster or preserved, locally foraged produce. The creative 7 course menu keeps you engaged from start to finish, with complex, highly original dishes packed full of complementary flavours and layers of texture.;Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2219;Oizumi Sushi;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Califórnia 785, São Paulo, 04566-061, Brazil;-23.6115894;-46.6837962;96;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Toro nigiri with smoked salmon roe, sea bass sushi, bluefin akami served on a shiso leaf, and a superb combination of sea urchin with salmon roe and rice all feature on the menu in this modest eatery that takes its names from the Japanese town of Ōizumi, in Gunma province, home to the biggest concentration of Brazilian immigrants in the country. Here, the only option is a single 16-course Omakase menu that is meticulously prepared with fresh fish of the day, as well as a selection of other species that chef Danilo Maciel matures in a special cabinet in the restaurant to ensure maximum flavour. Highly attentive and extremely gifted in his slicing techniques, the chef explains the preparation process for each dish, the maturing time (particularly for tuna, his star ingredient) and the provenance of each fish from around the world. Guests can choose between the sushi bar or one of the small private dining rooms set aside for groups of diners.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2220;Kinoshita;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Jacques Félix 405, São Paulo, 04509-000, Brazil;-23.5918216;-46.6712197;37;false;false;Japanese;Located in the quieter Vila Nova Conceição neighbourhood, next to the extensive Parque do Ibirapuera, Kinoshita is one of the most prestigious restaurants in São Paulo as it was a trail-blazer in bringing authentic “kappo” cuisine (“kappo” simply means “to cut and to cook” and is one of the purest forms of Japanese cuisine, to the extent that its chefs are considered true artisans requiring a minimum of 15 years of training) to the city. This attractive eatery, with its exotic feel and lots of greenery on display, features several dining rooms that lead to the main room with a counter around the open kitchen, which is the best place to eat while watching the chef in full flow. The à la carte has plenty of options, including a number of special dishes (Kinoshita uses exclusive ingredients such as scallops from Picinguaba and Yamaguishi organic eggs), although we can recommend the Omakase experience. We particularly enjoyed the squid with sea urchin.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
2221;Kuro;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Padre João Manuel 712, São Paulo, 01411-000, Brazil;-23.5636428;-46.6641507;46;false;false;Japanese;The stars of the show in this Japanese restaurant in the centre of the city close to the Museu de Arte de São Paulo Assis Chateaubriand are the grilled sushi and the grill itself. Here, dishes are cooked using the famous binchotan charcoal, an extremely pure charcoal (high density, high heat yield, very little smoke etc) that endows a very special flavour to dishes cooked on it. Chef Gerard Barberan offers a single Omakase menu at the counter around the kitchen for a maximum of ten guests per sitting (you need to be punctual as service starts even if not everyone has taken their seats). This menu is based around seasonal fish of the best-possible quality with the option of adding extra dishes (we particularly enjoyed the tuna tataki prepared with lightly smoked tuna belly and served with a perfectly cooked poached egg). A Japanese bar serving traditional drinks is located on the first floor and all reservations are only received by WhatsApp!.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2222;Tangará Jean-Georges;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Deputado Laércio Corte 1501, São Paulo, 05706-290, Brazil;-23.6319967;-46.7228448;78;true;true;Contemporary;There are some occasions when we all want to enjoy a special meal and this restaurant within the confines of the luxury Palácio Tangará hotel, an urban oasis surrounded by tropical vegetation in the heart of the Parque Burle Marx, would be the perfect setting. It is overseen by French chef Jean-Georges Vongerichten who reigns over a culinary empire made up of over forty businesses. Resident chefs Filipe Rizzato and Neusi Machado offer serious international cuisine featuring contemporary dishes that focus first and foremost on delicacy and pure flavours. The menu, with specific sections dedicated to caviar, raw dishes and vegetarian and vegan options (asparagus risotto, Puy lentils etc) is complemented by two tasting menus (one of which is vegetarian). There’s also an exclusive Chef’s Table in the kitchen, plus live music in the hotel lobby each evening, making it a pleasant option for a drink.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2223;Maní;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Joaquim Antunes 210, São Paulo, 05415-000, Brazil;-23.5663215;-46.6797249;41;true;false;Creative, Brazilian;Occupying a small house in the heart of the Jardim Paulistano district, Maní comes as something of a surprise with its three inter-connecting rooms featuring a contemporary Mediterranean decor of different white tones and simple furniture. Here, renowned chef Helena Rizzo, who is currently working as part of a successful collaboration with Belgian counterpart Willem Vandeven, aims to offer guests a pleasurable gastronomic experience based around consistency. To do this, she focuses on Brazilian ingredients (the restaurant boasts that 90% of these are organic) which are transformed through cutting-edge techniques and creativity. The choice here is extensive, although for a truly unique experience we recommend the tasting menu, available in a version with three dishes (starter, main course and dessert) or a special menu prepared by the chefs. One of the standout dishes is the refreshing “Atlantic forest salad”, which combines a passion fruit vinaigrette with a charcoal-infused oil. We suggest booking ahead to avoid waiting for a table.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
2226;Kan Suke;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Manoel da Nóbrega 76 - Loja 12, São Paulo, 01401-000, Brazil;-23.5684;-46.64936;78;true;true;Japanese;A small Japanese restaurant that attracts customers from around the world. Discreet and simple in appearance, it also has a somewhat surprising location in a modest shopping centre. It is slightly reminiscent of the more authentic restaurants found in Tokyo (with just a chef, a counter, a rice cooker and a chopping board) and could almost pass unnoticed if you’re not looking out for it. Working alone, chef Keisuke Egashira bases the dining experience on the quality of the ingredients (grouper, tuna belly, squid, red snapper, Japanese amberjack etc), preparing sushi and sashimi with impressive speed and technical skill. Here, every cut is precise and without showmanship or great spectacle, just the time-honoured skills of a true artist of Japanese cuisine. Menus to suit all budgets are available, although it’s not easy to book a table, so we recommend doing so well in advance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2227;Jun Sakamoto;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Lisboa 55, São Paulo, 05413-000, Brazil;-23.563121;-46.6771879;52;false;true;Japanese;A highly unusual restaurant that could almost pass unnoticed as it has no external signage to show that it exists! Here, everything revolves around owner-chef Sakamoto, a man with lots of personality who is said to make the best nigiri in São Paulo. If you have the opportunity, we recommend sitting at the sushi bar, where the focus is on two Omakase tasting menus – one prepared by Jun Sakamoto himself, the other by his right-hand man, chef Ryuzo Nishimura (the price of the menu will depend on which of them does the cooking). For those sitting at the bar, the nigiris (such as yellowfin tuna, salmon from Rio de Janeiro with a light citrus glaze, yellowtail from Argentina with confit lemon, sea bass with a shiso glaze, red snapper with a dash of plum preserve and sesame seeds etc) are served individually as soon as they are ready, while at the table they are served plated and presented two at a time.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
2228;Mee;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Atlântica 1702, Rio de Janeiro, 22021-001, Brazil;-22.9671007;-43.179147;23;false;false;Asian Influences;If you’re looking for an Asian dining experience close to Copacabana beach, make sure you book a table at Mee, an excellent option within the walls of the “Copa” (Copacabana Palace hotel). In this elegant restaurant where modernity and exoticism combine together harmoniously, the focus is on pan-Asian fusion cuisine that takes the tastebuds on a gastronomic journey to discover the flavours of Thailand, Malaysia, Cambodia, Japan, Singapore etc. Chef Alberto Morisawa was born in São Paulo but his family origins are in Madara Shima (Nagasaki, Japan), hence the dominant influence of Japanese cooking in his highly sophisticated dishes, many of which are served raw. The à la carte, teeming with nigiris, temakis, sashimi and dumplings, is complemented by interesting tasting menus (these include an Omakase option as well as a vegetarian menu). The paintings on the walls by Belgian artist Christian Develter, inspired by the tattooed faces of women from the Chin ethnic group in Myanmar, are truly spectacular!;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
2229;Fame Osteria;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Oscar Freire 216, São Paulo, 01426-001, Brazil;-23.5673009;-46.6641133;20;false;true;Italian Contemporary;This modest and discreetly located restaurant has a fascinating history as it started out as an illegal bar before quickly becoming a place of pilgrimage for food-lovers. The small iron door nestled between a gym and ice-cream shop leads to a steep staircase and then a simple space with pure lines and an open kitchen that takes centre stage. If you manage to book one of the four seats at the counter, you can watch chef Marco Renzetti at close quarters as he demonstrates his culinary skill without the need to resort to too much technology. The focus of his single tasting menu is on classic Italian cuisine, albeit with the grill as the mainstay, although vegetarian options are also available. The pasta (cappeletti, cannelloni, tonnarelli etc) is made in-house and the risotto is an ever-popular choice with his customers.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining;[]
2230;Cipriani;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Atlântica 1702, Rio de Janeiro, 22021-001, Brazil;-22.9670428;-43.1794682;35;true;true;Italian;Part of the “Copa” (Copacabana Palace), the city’s most famous hotel thanks to its setting on the world’s most famous beach, the luxurious Cipriani restaurant combines the best of Italy and Brazil. Here, to a backdrop of highly attentive service, you are spoilt by the choice of two tasting menus (there’s also a vegan option) created by Italian chef Nello Cassese, who bases his dishes on Italian ingredients and expertly combines them with others sourced more locally. The end results are classic Neopolitan and Piedmontese specialities (such as fried pizza and vitello tonnato) with a contemporary feel alongside other more creative dishes (we were pleasantly surprised by the organic egg served with artichoke, 36-month-aged Parmigiano Reggiano and truffle). Enjoy views of the splendid swimming pool, discreetly illuminated at night, through the restaurant’s windows.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
2231;Huto;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Jandira 677, São Paulo, 04080-004, Brazil;-23.6094195;-46.6590851;73;false;false;Japanese;This dark and intimate Japanese restaurant, somewhat hidden between the Moema and Indianópolis districts of the city, is definitely worth a visit. As soon as you enter, you’ll be invited to sit at the sushi bar at the centre of proceedings to choose one of Huto’s menus (one features lots of different options, while the two Omakase menus take you on a journey into the chef’s culinary world). Options include brioche with wagyu tartare and Macadamia nuts, oysters with ponzu, and a superb array of sushi – through the latter the chef demonstrates his undeniable skill in front of our eyes (although some diners are happy to order just a single type of sushi). But one dish that we particularly enjoyed was the hot tuna sashimi with tahini: a delicious morsel of red tuna which is very lightly seared and served with a smooth and silky sesame-flavoured sauce.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
2232;Kazuo;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Prudente Correia 432, São Paulo, 01450-030, Brazil;-23.57682;-46.68654;66;true;false;Asian Influences;This restaurant is easy to find in the Plaza Iguatemi, a luxury office building in the heart of the Avenida Faria Lima. Here, the chef Kazuo Harada pays a small homage to his roots by embarking on a culinary journey that takes us to Japan, of course, but also China, Malaysia, Thailand, Korea and even India. One of the features that sets it apart from other Asian restaurants in the city is its ability to create a common thread in dishes that aim to introduce us to the unique attributes of Pan-Asian cuisine, through the use of interesting techniques and elaborately prepared recipes. The à la carte, with its numerous sushi, sashimi, nigiri, maki, temaki and main course options (Peking Duck, crispy prawns, yellow curry with seafood and salmon roe etc), is complemented by an Omakase menu that is only available at the sushi bar. An enclosed terracewith a bar and private spaces is located on the first floor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2233;San Omakase;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Conde de Bernadotte, 26 - Loja 103, Rio de Janeiro, 22430-200, Brazil;-22.98085;-43.22252;84;true;false;Japanese;The specific feature of this small (just eight seats at the counter) but elegant restaurant on the first floor of a shopping centre in the heart of Leblon is its honest homage to Japanese cuisine, which goes beyond culinary concepts in order to teach us more about the country’s culture. Here, good hospitality is a key tenet, so you’ll be welcomed at the door with a glass of sake, while those with little experience of Japanese dining will be given explanations on the preparation process and the special characteristics of the Omakase menu. Chef André Nobuyuki Kawai, who spent several decades working in Japan and was the founder of, and worked as a teacher at, the Nagoya Sushi School, creates an extensive array of nigiri with different sauces in front of your eyes, all of which are perfectly sliced and use fresh fish of an exceptional quality. He also prepares sashimi, the typical Tamago omelette and the ever-popular Chawanmushi among other dishes and is happy to share anecdotes to enhance the overall dining experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2234;Taquería El Califa de León;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Av. Ribera De San Cosme 56, San Rafael, Cuauhtémoc, 06470, Mexico;19.4411427;-99.1592407;49;false;true;Mexican;There is a reason why El Califa de León has endured for more than half a century. This taqueria may be bare bones with just enough room for a handful of diners to stand at the counter but its creation, the Gaonera taco, is exceptional. Thinly sliced beef filet is expertly cooked to order, seasoned with only salt and a squeeze of lime. At the same time, a second cook prepares the excellent corn tortillas alongside. The resulting combination is elemental and pure. Other options are few but excellent, and include bistec (beef steak), chuleta (pork chop), and costilla (beef rib). With meat and tortillas of this caliber, the duo of house-made salsas is hardly even necessary.;Cash only;[]
2235;Em;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Tonalá 133, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4152941;-99.1619808;31;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;A pre-dinner cocktail at the moody 686 Bar upstairs is a smart way to start an evening in the capable hands of Chef Lucho Martinez. Named for his daughter Emilia, the intimate restaurant on the ground floor suits couples well, while the handsome kitchen takes a contemporary look at Mexican ingredients, many of which are seafood. Think a savory, crispy, carrot buñuelo covered in roe or an expertly grilled wedge of corvina with spinach set in a fragrant garlic foam. The signature dessert celebrates all things mamey, arriving as a thin, delicate tart, a light tiramisu, and a refreshing ice cream. Both the a la carte and the tasting menus overlap well enough, so no need to fret. Refined, bold flavors come through clearly in both.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2236;Sud 777;Mexico;Álvaro Obregón;Blvd. De La Luz, 777, Jardines del Pedregal , Álvaro Obregón, 01900, Mexico;19.3091352;-99.2093593;34;false;false;Creative, Vegetarian;Sud 777 enjoys an enviable location in Mexico City's ritzy Pedregal neighborhood. The space is modern and sprawling, with lofted ceilings, dark wood, and earthy colors.Chef Edgar Núñez presides over a multicourse tasting menu as well as a large a la carte comprising starters like kampachi tostada with fermented tomatoes and Oaxacan tamal soup with beans and black mole to main dishes like red snapper al pastor and local turkey with "mole amarillito." Vegetables figure prominently on the tasting menu, and diners may be treated to the likes of beet tartare, avocado with foie gras, and a simple but spectacular spinach, sauteed in sherry and set in a pool of lush almond and garlic puree.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2237;Levadura de Olla Restaurante;Mexico;Oaxaca;Calle de Manuel García Vigil #304, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.064329;-96.7249541;65;false;true;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;One could spend an entire afternoon in the shaded, breezy courtyard of the young talent, Chef Thalía Barrios Garcia. Colorful and creative, she channels traditional Oaxacan recipes as well as memories from her hometown of San Mateo Yucutindoo. Vegetables take priority over meat, evident in starters like the salad of local tomatoes dressed in a fruit vinaigrette and set on beet puree. The meatless tamales, which she learned from her grandmother, are peerless. A recent version featured delicate, full-flavored masa enrobed in a duo of moles and finished with squash blossoms. Heartfelt, comforting cooking can further be found in her machucados, a childhood favorite that blends tortillas and pipian salsa. A selection of ancestral beverages rounds out the experience.;;[]
2238;Esquina Común;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Fernando Montes De Oca, 86, Condesa, Cuauhtémoc, 06140, Mexico;19.4138958;-99.1767786;77;true;false;Mexican, Creative;The address may no longer be a secret, but reservations at this hot spot are closely guarded (and only available by direct messaging on Instagram). The covered rooftop setting is enhanced with bountiful greenery and a lovely, relaxed vibe.Chef Ana Dolores González and a young, talented team cook with plenty of personality and a solid foundation of strong technique and good ingredients. Styled like a tasting menu and portioned for two, these dishes are impressive. Items of note include the pescado del dia, which may be grilled cod set in a luscious green mole with crushed ripe plantain, fava beans, and pumpkin seeds. Staying on theme, the masa and plantain tamal de pescado is filled with chile red-tinted fish with a flavorful salsa macha.;Terrace;[]
2239;Rosetta;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Colima, 166, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4198433;-99.1597893;88;false;false;Creative, Mexican;Chef Elena Reygadas's Rosetta is a perennial favorite, packed with a crowd that comes here for creative cooking that is decidedly Mexican but is inflected with global influences. Dishes are designed for sharing, ideal for those who want to sample more of her ingenious creations like the cabbage tacos with two small rounds of Savoy cabbage, served warm with pistachio puree and romeritos. Blending interesting flavors and textures, this dish is a great play on expectations and its different shades of green are visually arresting. A sweet potato tamal over toasted pumpkin seeds with a buttermilk sauce and salsa macha is equal parts sweet and savory. Honey jelly, cut into perfect cubes and served with a quenelle of brown butter ice cream and vanilla sauce, is an exquisite ending.;Terrace;[]
2240;Animalón;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Carretera Federal #3 Km. 83, Valle de Guadalupe, 22750, Mexico;32.0674475;-116.6002861;73;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Many restaurants claim to be transporting, but how many deliver on the promise? Animalón certainly does. In season, this spot shines with an al fresco dining space under a centuries-old oak tree (during colder months, they move to a pop-up space). It's the very definition of tranquility, yet with owner Javier Plascencia at the helm, it's equally thrilling.The contemporary Mexican cuisine pulls influences from all over the country. The kitchen's vision is apparent in dishes like beer-braised barbacoa wrapped in a banana leaf, steamed and smoked in a pig's bladder, then served tableside for a dramatic presentation. Meanwhile, a tableside pour of tomato broth infused with chocolate clams is equal parts sweet, savory, and gently spicy.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2241;HA';Mexico;Playa del Carmen;Carretera Chetumal - Puerto Juárez Kilometro 282, Solidaridad, Playa del Carmen, 77710, Mexico;20.5893883;-87.1114426;68;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;If you’re not staying at the Hotel Xcaret, be sure to devote extra time to arrive at this restaurant, as it involves some navigation. However, once you’ve found it, you’re in for a treat. The cuisine has a definite French bent, which is perhaps no surprise given Chef Carlos Gaytán’s training, but there is nonetheless a confident use of distinctly Mexican flavors and ingredients. This is cooking with a clear sense of identity and strong technique, and noteworthy for bold, creative flavor combinations. The mushroom beignet decorated with a frilly crisp of cauliflower in a creamy truffle and mint sauce is a standout, as is the seared filet mignon with crispy potato mille-feuille garnished with house-cured ikura. Choose the wine pairing to learn more about Mexican wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2242;Damiana;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Federal Ensenada-Tecate Km. 71, Valle de Guadalupe, 22034, Mexico;32.1384068;-116.5288726;93;false;false;Mexican, Fusion;Damiana boasts a stunning setting, nestled on the Viñedos de la Reina property. Two rows of trees provide shade for the tables lined up on the patio for those who want to dine outdoors. Chef Esteban Lluis celebrates the local valley's products in his multicourse tasting menu that is contemporary Mexican at its core. The kitchen plays with presentation and expectations in fun and creative ways. The dishes are bold and brilliantly executed, as in the perfectly cooked, crispy duck served over pickled cabbage and sided by carrot purée and duck confit wrapped in Swiss chard. Desserts make a lasting impression, especially the pumpkin crème brûlée on a mandarin dacquoise cake or the guava flan with crispy phyllo sheets.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2243;Cocina de Autor Riviera Maya;Mexico;Playa del Carmen;Carr. Cancún - Tulum Km 62, Playa del Carmen, Playa del Carmen, 77710, Mexico;20.6742921;-87.023315;38;false;false;Creative, Mexican;Once inside the opulence of the Grand Velas resort, guests are treated to an indulgent, immersive experience from beginning to end, encompassing live music, assiduous service, and, of course, singular cuisine. As its name indicates, the cooking here is driven by the creative vision of Chef Nahúm Velasco, in the guise of a sophisticated modern tasting menu that emphasizes novel flavor combinations and compelling textures. A meal might progress from spider crab paired with silky jackfruit, to roasted pork with black garlic, cleverly decorated with leaves made from beet and butternut squash, and end with textures of honey from the property's own Melipona beehives. The menu changes regularly, so there’s always an element of surprise alongside the culinary artistry.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2244;Conchas de Piedra;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Carretera Tecate Km. 93.5, Valle de Guadalupe, 22761, Mexico;31.9802589;-116.6530788;71;true;true;Seafood, Mexican;This rustic-chic collaboration from the people behind Deckman’s and Casa de Piedra, one of the many wineries in the valley, brings together what both places do best—seafood and sparkling wine. The outdoor dining area is warm and inviting thanks to communal tables, café lights strung overhead and a jaunty instrumental playlist. It's a compact, seafood-focused menu offering aguachiles, ceviches, and warm dishes like seared abalone. Every dish is stunning, with balanced flavors and bright colors. Clam ceviche, served in two petite clam shells balanced on small pebbles, is just one example. For a heartier dish, consider the crispy oyster taco. A single scoop of cucumber sorbet served in an abalone shell is clever and fresh.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2245;Los Danzantes Oaxaca;Mexico;Oaxaca;Macedonio Alcalá 403, Interior 4, Colonia Centro, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0651301;-96.7239336;24;false;false;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;This Oaxaca favorite can count more than 20 years of history to its name, but that’s not stopping them from forging ahead with their own ideas and sense of refinement. Set in a dazzling, open-air courtyard, the memorable space buzzes as personable servers guide locals and visitors alike. Start with hoja santa filled with local goat cheese and served in a warm tomatillo sauce before moving to the mole sampler, which is a masterclass in sauce work. Salsa borracha is another can’t-miss sauce that shines with tender pork ribs. Getting full? There is always room for the guava cheesecake, which is lighter than expected and crowned with mamey cream. The restaurant even makes its own mezcal, which is used in their finely made cocktails.;Terrace;[]
2246;Pangea;Mexico;San Pedro Garza García;Av. del Roble 660, Valle del Campestre, San Pedro Garza García, 66266, Mexico;25.6496038;-100.3563642;60;false;false;Contemporary, Mexican;After 25 years of operation, Chef Guillermo González Beristáin’s flagship remains a standard bearer for Monterrey’s fine dining scene, offering skillful cooking that combines Mexican cuisine with accents from Asia and France. The stylish space offers diners a choice between an ample à la carte offering and a tasting menu that best highlights the kitchen’s talents. Flavorful dishes, characterized by a sense of balance and astute seasoning, range from a sweet tamal of winter squash paired with crème fraîche and caviar, to a dish of crisp-skinned quail with foie gras mousseline, pistachios, and cherries. Desserts end the meal on an elegant note, like a Pavlova filled with raspberry compote and a sorbet of lychee and white tea.;Terrace;[]
2247;Le Chique;Mexico;Puerto Morelos;Bahía Petempich, Carretera Federal Km. 27.5, Puerto Morelos, 77580, Mexico;20.8958649;-86.8572293;40;true;true;Contemporary, Mexican;Nestled inside the Azul Beach Resort, Le Chique presents a thoroughly charming experience in a swanky setting. The space, service, and presentation all display a high polish, and there is a distinct theatrical sense that lends an air of special occasion to this spot. The tasting menu spans Mexico's regions, showing a clear sense of style and personality while consistently impressing with creativity, excellent ingredients, strong technique, and impactful flavors. Green passionfruit filled with foie gras parfait and vibrant maax ik or brûléed marrowbone with escamoles are just two of the first bites that set the meal off on a luxurious start. Seafood-based bites are then presented with a flourish, followed by heartier compositions. Finally, the sweets course is as tempting as the very first bite.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2248;KOLI Cocina de Origen;Mexico;Monterrey;Río Amazonas 225 ote, Colonia Del Valle, Monterrey, 66220, Mexico;25.6599666;-100.3630254;82;false;false;Mexican, Creative;The three Rivera-Río brothers (Rodrigo, Daniel, and Patricio) combine their talents here, overseeing the culinary, pastry, and front-of-house efforts for this singular establishment. More than perhaps any other, this restaurant embodies the new face of Norteño cuisine, celebrating local ingredients and traditional dishes with a menu that is simultaneously inventive, playful, and bold. A sense of pride in local traditions and ingredients is apparent throughout their immersive tasting menu, whether it’s a suckling pig paired with a distinctive mole neolonés, or an exceptionally tender, reimagined take on cabrito, paired with plum and foie gras. Cocktail pairings, whether with or without alcohol, are both thoughtful and memorable.;;[]
2249;Cocina de Autor Los Cabos;Mexico;Cabo San Lucas;Transpeninsular Cabo San Lucas Km. 17.3, Cabo San Lucas, 23405, Mexico;22.9683133;-109.7917985;86;false;false;Mexican;Located in the bougainvillea-strewn Grand Velas hotel, this plush oceanfront restaurant is sophisticated, amplified by the resort-formal dress code. The terrace is a nice spot for bites and cocktails, and a few choice tables overlook a koi pond.The multicourse tasting menu is Mexican at its heart, with global elements and inspirations woven throughout. This is a kitchen unafraid of taking risks, especially when it comes to flavor combinations. A farm-raised sea scallop served under a miso butter with tom yum and a tempura-fried shiso leaf is delicious. Then, in a triumph of flavors, beef tenderloin is plated with celery root purée, poached beets, and maitake mushrooms. Shaved Comté with a quenelle of honey ice cream is a playful take on the cheese course.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2250;La Terrasse irisée;Japan;Nara;1-34-7 Ayameike Kita, Nara, Nara, 631-0032, Japan;34.698843;135.760581;85;true;true;French;There is a particularly beautiful sunset view from the elegant dining room overlooking Ayameike pond. Susumu Sasaki puts to work his many years of training in Switzerland and France, creating harmony between what he learnt there and the Japanese ingredients. He introduces the local vegetables prior to the meal out of respect for the producers. The name means ‘iridescent’, invoking a rainbowand his desire to span Nara and Europe in his approach.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2251;Oryori Hirooka;Japan;Nara;1-7-1 Hommachi, Gojo, Nara, 637-0041, Japan;34.351673;135.693949;33;true;true;Japanese;Nobuyuki Hirooka was raised locally and brings the bounty of Gojo to his customers. The menu always includes Gojo vegetables picked that morning and paired with fish or meat. His speciality is the oshizushi, for tiding you over. He combines the sushi cultures of Nara and Osaka, wrapping cherry anthias in persimmon leaves in the spring and awabi in the summer. He also creates stories, such as depicting the Milky Way with kudzu somen and Altair with star snapper.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2253;Sushi Kawashima;Japan;Nara;291-1 Ishikawacho, Kashihara, Nara, 634-0045, Japan;34.483144;135.798021;56;true;true;Sushi;The meal starts with seasonal clear soup, which is followed by a piece of nigiri and then seafood tsukuri. Grilled items are decorated with seasonal leaves. Hiroyuki Kawashima trained in Japanese cuisine and his preparation of the sushi toppings and seasoning of the rice with akazu is all from studying it himself. The tamago-yaki at the end is the farewell dish, and he stamps his name on it with a branding iron, imprinting the name on the customer’s mind at the same time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2255;Inada;Japan;Nara;1-10-16 Hikarigaoka, Ikoma, Nara, 630-0141, Japan;34.74072;135.714823;62;true;true;Japanese;Masayuki Inada and his brother breathed new life into a shop passed down from their grandfather. Masayuki is in charge of the preparations and takes great pains with the menu, incorporating the seasons based on his fondness for tea ceremony. Serving the guests are his older brother and mother, drawing on skills they picked up in retail. Ingredients come from a market in Osaka where relationships have been built over generations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2256;L'AUBERGE DE PLAISANCE SAKURAI;Japan;Nara;2217 Taie, Sakurai, Nara, 633-0044, Japan;34.489565;135.839542;85;false;false;French;This auberge overlooks the magnificent Yamato Plains. What the chef says is characteristic of the Nara approach, which is to pursue local production for local consumption—to which end he uses local vegetables, Yamato beef and duck, and deer and boar from Gojo. Prix fixe offerings, intertwined with the history and culinary culture of the old capital, flow as if weaving a tale. The chef also serves Miwa somen, a very Sakurai-style dish. The service will put you at ease.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2257;Musoan;Japan;Nara;70-7-1-2 Suimoncho, Nara, Nara, 630-8208, Japan;34.68574;135.835217;48;true;true;Japanese;This restaurant is named after the Rinzai Buddhist monk said to be the founder of the Muso school. The modern space has an open feel, and the garden is tended by the proprietress, who is a landscape gardener. The chef seeks to convey the intrinsic flavours of ingredients, so does not take the ‘creative’ approach. Soups are made according to tradition, and rice is cooked in an earthenware pot. He grows wild grapes to make wine to complement the dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Shoes must be removed;[]
2258;Ajinokaze Nishimura;Japan;Nara;1023-3 Odono, Sakurai, Nara, 633-0062, Japan;34.518038;135.844418;63;true;false;Japanese;Norihisa Nishimura was born and raised in Sakurai. His aim is to create simple dishes with a sense of warmth. The dishes may look simple but their appeal is in the creative preparation that went into them. In the spring, he deep-fries bamboo shoots from Asuka without breading or batter and then grills them with soy sauce. In the summer, he dresses silken tofu with dashi made from tomato juice. With his creativity, he brings a new perspective to the tastes of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
2259;Chugokusai Naramachi Kuko;Japan;Nara;913-2 Kideracho, Nara, Nara, 630-8306, Japan;34.6745317;135.8345922;46;false;false;Chinese;Kazuyuki Miyamoto abides by the concept of a balanced diet leading to a healthy body, a fundamental of Chinese food culture. He has experience with Cantonese and Sichuan cuisine and also studied yakuzen with his wife, who is in charge of service. He selects quality Nara ingredients and grows Chinese and traditional Japanese vegetables himself. Various fermented seasonings and spices are used, including greens stir-fried with fermented tofu and mapo tofu made with native soybeans.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
2260;LA TRACE;Japan;Nara;2-1-5 Omiyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8115, Japan;34.68209;135.817159;51;true;false;French;‘La Trace’ means ‘footprints’ and Chef Ryo Sato traces the roots of the foodstuffs he uses, building strong relationships with the farmers of Nara. In gratitude to those who grow the vegetables and raise the chicken and pork he serves, he incorporates their stories into his cuisine so they can get an idea of the landscapes he saw there, the personalities of his producers, and what they felt as they nurtured his ingredient. This leaves the footprints of French cuisine in the food culture of the ancient capital.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2261;Da terra;Japan;Nara;884 Kawahara, Asukamura, Takaichi-gun, Nara, 634-0141, Japan;34.472669;135.816499;54;true;false;Italian;Chef Hirokazu Nakai’s culinary process begins when he ploughs and sows his land. His family grows over 100 different crops, which Nakai incorporates into his menu according to their harvest season. The ‘Da Terra (‘from the land’) salad’ brings the fragrance and warmth of the season to the table, capturing the scenery of the fields. He uses a stone mill to grind whole-wheat flour for his handmade pasta. His creativity and the bounty of the land of Asuka become as one.;Air conditioning,Car park,Shoes must be removed;[]
2263;Okada;Japan;Nara;26-2 Imamikadocho, Nara, Nara, 630-8374, Japan;34.680423;135.830455;78;true;false;Japanese;A counter kappo located close to Sarusawa Pond. The chef has never forgotten the importance of interacting with customers – something he learned during his Osaka apprenticeship. His young team move freely about as well, engaging alongside the chef in amiable conversation with customers. Okada uses kaiseki to convey the richness of Nara food. Hassun appetisers are served on large platters, the better to showcase the beauty of Japanese cuisine. The meal ends with a cup of thin tea, poured by the chef himself to convey his gratitude.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2265;Wa Yamamura;Japan;Nara;2-11-15 Shibatsujicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8114, Japan;34.685875;135.812879;99;false;true;Japanese;Japanese cuisine made with colourful ingredients, served on brightly decorated dishes. The owner-chef, who learned his art in the traditional Japanese restaurant world, devotes great efforts to conjure the most elegant cuisine. Highlights include decoratively arranged sashimi served in a bowl of ice and the appetiser plate, which features plenty of drinking snacks. You can choose from several kinds of rice at dinner, and second helpings are topped with chirimen sansho (dried baby fish seasoned with soy and pepper). The hospitality provided by the chef and his wife is heartwarming.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2267;Ajinotabibito Roman;Japan;Nara;2F, VIV Bldg, 2-13 Tsurumai Higashimachi, Nara, Nara, 631-0021, Japan;34.708276;135.750369;24;false;false;Japanese;The owner-chef ’s journey as a chef began at a general eatery. He sought out old cookbooks and honed his skills on his own. Calling himself a taste traveller, Tomio Onda spends all his time cooking. The monthly menu has real character. For example, in June there’s chargrilled ayu, in July curry and in August cold miso soup. He creates a fusion of traditional dishes and home cooking under the theme of a summertime adventure. His daughters work in the kitchen too.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
2268;Jie Xiang Lou;China Mainland;Hangzhou;Seven Villas, 1 Bapanling Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.22914;120.13323;20;false;false;Zhejiang;This restaurant in a bamboo forest exudes otherworldly serenity. The menu is dominated by Jiangnan dishes, which are given a new lease of life by modern Western techniques. Sample all of the signature dishes courtesy of the appetiser platter – veggie beggar’s purse, pork jowl with caviar, marinated goose liver and smoked fish terrine. Their version of Mrs Song’s fish soup uses baby yellow croakers from the East China Sea for their delicate, sweet flesh.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2269;Guiyu (Xihu);China Mainland;Hangzhou;2-1 Manjuelong Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.21818;120.12294;15;false;true;Zhejiang;The sleek, elegant room stands in an osmanthus forest, the sweet scent of which lingers in the air in autumn. Once you set foot inside, the earthy smell of black tea takes over – tea-smoked dishes such as crispy skin chicken exude intoxicating aromas. The menu is dominated by Zhejiang classics made with seasonal ingredients from across the country. Try the river fish cooked with dried bamboo shoot, too. The tea ceremony at each table is quite a spectacle.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2270;Jin Sha;China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, Four Seasons Hotel at West Lake, 5 Lingyin Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, 310013, China Mainland;30.2541799;120.1248861;31;true;true;Zhejiang;In a luxury lakeside hotel, stands this handsome restaurant furnished in classical Chinese style amid ponds and manicured gardens. The kitchen team uses seasonal ingredients sourced all over China to create Zhejiang neo-classics with modern twists. Try braised pork belly with abalone which tastes rich, but not greasy. Crème brûlée with Longjing tea ends a meal the perfect way. Besides the array of teas and wines, also check out the range of Huangjiu on offer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2271;Longjing Manor;China Mainland;Hangzhou;399 Longjing Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2272347;120.1112474;65;false;false;Zhejiang;Tucked away in a quiet alley, this restaurant is surprisingly spacious. As the host walks you to one of the eight traditionally furnished private rooms, you pass an extensive manicured garden with stone bridges and ponds. The experienced head chef prepares poetically named Jiangnan dishes that hark back to the old days – local Zhejiang classics stand out in particular. Without à la carte options, menus are tailored to guests’ liking in advance.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2272;Ambré Ciel;China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, Meifan Plaza Proya, 588 Xixi Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2652928;120.0982588;82;false;false;Innovative;After honing his skills in a number of prestigious kitchens, chef Alan Yu took on this atmospheric restaurant in 2022. The six tables are enclosed by heavily textured stone walls that afford much privacy. There is one private room for ten diners, with multimedia projections for an immersive experience. They serve a single prix-fixe menu at lunch and dinner, with courses rooted in French tradition and boosted by subtle Chinese twists.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2274;Ru Yuan;China Mainland;Hangzhou;11 Yuquan Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2556553;120.1174357;62;false;false;Zhejiang;Ru Yuan stands amid lush vegetation. The menu mostly comprises traditional Zhejiang dishes with refined touches. The mud crab marinated in Xiangxue Shaoxing wine, served with rich, buttery roe, exudes intoxicating fragrances. The river shrimps sautéed with Longjing tea leaves and braised pork belly are not to be missed. The hand-crafted dim sum are also worth trying, as is the floral fruit tea.;Car park;[]
2275;Wild Yeast;China Mainland;Hangzhou;304-305, 3F, Zonia Tide Ginza, 2077 Binsheng Road, Binjiang, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2063031;120.1931297;85;true;false;Chinese Contemporary;A discreet sign and a dedicated lift lead to this eatery. Every table in the softly lit room commands a view of the open kitchen. The head chef hailing from Taizhou designed the set and á la carte menus to highlight the natural flavours of the best seafood shipped from his hometown. Home-style braised yellow croaker in fish stock bursts with umami, while the chef’s signature dish is duck soup with taro and ginger juice, melding classical Chinese culinary arts with Western technique.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2276;Hiden;USA;Miami;313 N.W. 25th St., Miami, 33127, USA;25.8008242;-80.2012828;37;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;True to its name, this favored counter is indeed hidden in the thick of busy Wynwood. The front door is not easy to find and slides open only with a time-sensitive passcode. But beyond the hustle and bustle, Chef Seijun Okano offers a mature, finely tuned omakase for the fortunate few seated at his counter. Fish flown in multiple times a week from Japan are handled with precision, sliced carefully and pressed into lush, vinegar-tinged rice that he makes at the start. Everyone is encouraged to ask questions and drink freely. All the while, the team works in perfect tandem, delivering a well-paced sushi experience to the tune of an upbeat playlist. In the end, diners emerge from the secret room wondering if those around them know what they’ve missed.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2277;Ebbe;USA;Tampa;1202 N. Franklin St., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9536143;-82.4602915;60;true;true;Contemporary;Chef Ebbe Vollmer's eponymous downtown dweller isn't your typical Tampa restaurant. Sleek and contemporary with a space dominated by a U-shaped marble bar, it's hyper-focused with just one tasting menu. Scandinavian elements make their way onto the dishes here, hinting at the chef's Swedish background, and the cooking is both clever and confident without superfluous fuss. Artful plating takes center stage in dishes like the beet roulade with a brown butter and black cherry sauce. Fermented white asparagus beurre monté and sautéed spinach make a beautiful base for tender turbot that comes alive with a quenelle of sturgeon caviar. Braised oxtail with seared foie gras and a brunoise of sunchoke is equally rich and tender.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2278;Ogawa;USA;Miami;7223 N.W. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33150, USA;25.8414428;-80.2006503;30;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;In a nod to the Little River neighborhood that it calls home, Ogawa translates to "small river." Chef/co-owner Masayuki Komatsu commands a presence with an omakase that stuns with a series of enticing cooked dishes and a procession of focused and skillful nigiri. From baby sea eels with a soy-cured quail egg and bigfin reef squid in a shiso-miso sauce to baby snow crab and Japanese-style herring roe, this appetizer of four bites is the first sign that this isn't your typical sushi counter. Then, lotus root, wild yam and langoustine tempura is sided by a thick sauce made from roasted langoustine shells. After the cooked dishes, nigiri comes next with bright and balanced kisu, creamy ebodai, squid topped with osetra caviar and anago dusted with sansho pepper exemplifying the chef's skill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2279;Papa Llama;USA;Orlando;2840 Curry Ford Rd., Orlando, 32806, USA;28.5239631;-81.3464706;96;true;true;Peruvian, Contemporary;Don't be fooled by its modest surrounds, as the interior is modern and cool. Leather chairs are especially inviting, and tables offer a view of the gleaming kitchen. Husband-and-wife duo Kevin and Maria Ruiz prepare modern Peruvian cuisine full of bright ingredients with a bit of polish, and the family-style menu is an approachable (and affordable) way to sample their sincere cooking. Nigiri kicks off the meal with a smart nod to the Peruvian tradition of Japanese fusion, delivering dialed-in flavors with confidence. Bok choy is elevated with bold, contrasting textures, while chicken thigh roulade with aji amarillo aioli is simply spectacular. For dessert, sweet potato donuts over a blueberry compote seal the deal. The natural wine program is impressive.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2280;Camille;USA;Orlando;4962 New Broad St., Orlando, 32814, USA;28.5683554;-81.3259894;73;true;false;Vietnamese, French;Chef Tung Phan has taken the pop-up and given it permanence at this space just off Lake Baldwin. It's boldly sleek with elegant touches (think wood accents and beautiful lighting). Seats at the counter feature the ten-course Vietnamese-French tasting menu, while booths offer an abbreviated version. Rooted in French techniques, Vietnamese flavors are given a refined twist here. The Dungeness crab curry arrives with a tartlet shell, filled with crab meat and mixed with lime, served atop the lid, which when removed, reveals a deliciously hearty curry. Salmon over king trumpet noodles in a tamarind and pineapple sauce is creative, but the best may be saved for last. The sweet potato brioche topped with a "gold" chocolate ice cream and Vietnamese coffee sauce is an elegant finale.;Counter dining;[]
2283;Koya;USA;Tampa;807 W. Platt St., Tampa, 33606, USA;27.94191;-82.46831;100;false;false;Japanese, Contemporary;There is a watchful eye over the experience at this intimate counter, where a multicourse contemporary tasting menu shares a singular interpretation of Japanese cuisine. The dishes are often unexpected yet always thoughtful. Spectacular seafood is a given: staple luxuries like bluefin tuna and uni are flown in weekly from Toyosu Market. Instead of the typical parade of nigiri, dishes offer unique combinations of Eastern and Western culinary sensibilities, as in the A5 olive wagyu with fried capers and aged parmesan or Spanish turbot set in a tomato and miso emulsion. An impressive list of premium sakes and wines available by the glass further enhance a meal that is leisurely paced and overseen by a friendly team that happily engages its guests.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2284;Tambourine Room by Tristan Brandt;USA;Miami Beach;6801 Collins Ave., Miami Beach, 33141, USA;25.8525031;-80.1200819;35;false;false;Contemporary, Asian;Inside the Carillon Miami Wellness Resort on a rather calm stretch of Collins Avenue, find this ambitious dining bijou helmed by Chef Tristan Brandt and his trusted lieutenant Timo Steubing. The duo delivers a colorful, multicourse tasting grounded in French cuisine with notable Asian inspiration. The results are anything but timid: Expect rich, bold sauces and foams made with the likes of parmesan, lobster and saffron, and ginger turbocharging everything from tomatoes to scallops to wagyu. By contrast, the space itself is fairly Spartan, sequestered off to the side of the main hotel bar and defined mostly by oversized oak tables, blue leather chairs and modern light fixtures. Swing for the second seating of the evening for a longer menu.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
2285;Elcielo Miami;USA;Miami;31 S.E. 5th St., Miami, 33131, USA;25.7695211;-80.1915242;30;true;false;Colombian, Latin American;Colombian-born Chef Juan Manuel Barrientos' culinary artistry has garnered international fame, and his burgeoning empire has this Miami location has been going strong since 2015. An open kitchen and backlit bar welcome patrons to the space, outfitted with stone floors and well-sized wood tables. Warm lighting and greenery complement the sleek appeal.Come to experience elevated Colombian food and dramatic presentations, from the tableside "chocotherapy" to the "Tree of Life" bread service. Expect a variety of small bites leading up to the main courses, including an activated charcoal buñuelo with a porcini and black truffle filling, and a fritter made with fresh cheese, corn, and tapioca pearls. Cleanse the palate with a green mango popsicle with a spicy powder coating and a shot of aguardiente.;Air conditioning;[]
2286;Lilac;USA;Tampa;500 Channelside Dr., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.94373;-82.45109;33;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;This concept from John Fraser occupies its own corner of the sleek and stylish Edition hotel. An open kitchen with glossy emerald-green tile overlooks the small dining room and delivers a contemporary prix-fixe with broad Mediterranean influences. Dinner begins with a series of bites like almond croissant with chicken liver mousse or Maine lobster feuillantine. Diver scallops arrive dramatically under a cloche filled with rosemary smoke, while braised rabbit pasta halo comes with an airy parmesan-potato cloud. Entrée highlights include Ora King salmon, Colorado lamb chop, and a particularly sumptuous Dover sole bathed in brown butter and serve with glazed vegetables. A lengthy list of cocktails and rather pricey wines are available as well.-;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2287;Kadence;USA;Orlando;1809 Winter Park Rd., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5687259;-81.3458703;67;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Husband and wife team Mark Berdin and Jennifer Bañagale are the drivers behind this light-hearted operation that began as a mini counter in a market. Impressed? We are too. With limited seats, the mood is anything but solemn: Chef Berdin is a boisterous character whose colorful commentary and fastidious cooking style make for fun foils. To the tune of Frank Sinatra, Eminem, and nightclub beats, expect a progression of dishes that highlight exceptional product, classic methods, and bold flavors. Recent highlights include blue crab fritters, plump oysters with yuzu vinegar, and a beautiful sashimi platter. To be clear, this omakase yields a great deal of food – and that’s before it’s time for nigiri. Hojicha ice cream makes for a sweet ending.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2288;Shingo;USA;Coral Gables;112 Alhambra Cir., Coral Gables, 33134, USA;25.7529994;-80.2567998;87;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Chef Shingo Akikuni, ever gracious and welcoming, has returned, now back in action behind a spacious, 14-seat counter in Coral Gables. Most premium sushi omakases work with half as many seats, but there’s no cause for concern here: Chef Akikuni and his second-in-command handle the crowd without breaking a sweat and even switch sides midway through the meal. Once the room fills with the sharp smell of vinegar to mix into the sushi rice, it’s off to the races. Fish is sourced almost entirely from Japan, sliced in uniform fashion, and, dressed with little more than a swipe of nikiri. They keep a close eye on the seasons too, evidenced by a recent special of high-grade tuna from Aomori prefecture and an indulgent chawanmushi with matsutake.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2289;Capa;USA;Orlando;10100 Dream Tree Blvd., Orlando, 32836, USA;28.4030152;-81.5438057;51;false;true;Steakhouse, Spanish;Calling Capa a steakhouse is like saying flamenco is just a dance. This stunning spot, reigning from the 17th floor of the Four Seasons Orlando, is big on drama -- and that's before the unrivaled views of the nightly Disney World fireworks show. From the subtle design nods to the menu, the Spanish influence is clear. Expect a distinctive experience defined by a hickory-grill that smokes and chars steaks and lamb sourced from Kansas City to New Zealand to Japan. One particular standout is the Iberico pluma served with an almond romesco. Tapas range from familiar (pan con tomate) to creative (octopus with pimenton black pepper glaze). For dessert, consider going classic with a spot-on dulce de leche lava cake paired with silky banana ice cream.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
2290;Cote Miami;USA;Miami;3900 N.E. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33137, USA;25.812906;-80.1914524;29;false;true;Korean, Steakhouse;When staring down the long, neon-lit entrance hallway that booms overhead with a subwoofer and ends with a giant mirror, rest assured that this is a serious operation. Owner Simon Kim and his team know what they're doing in this highly stylized Korean steakhouse, which almost feels like a temple to beautifully marbled and aged beef, much of it on display in a nearby room.Just as you would find at the original location in New York City, top-quality ingredients, astutely seasoned dishes and engaging servers make for a seamless experience. First-timers should start with the butcher’s feast, a generous tasting that includes an assortment of banchan, multiple cuts of beef and two kinds of stews. Round it off with the kimchi Wagyu paella—a marvel on its own.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2292;Soseki;USA;Winter Park;955 W. Fairbanks Ave., Winter Park, 32789, USA;28.5931796;-81.361526;46;true;true;Fusion, Sushi;This intimate operation by Chef Mike Collantes is a prime example of an omakase that blends traditional and contemporary elements seamlessly. The counter is lit like a stage, with bright spotlights, dark walls, sleek wood floors, and ten plush seats. The smaller courses are ever-evolving thanks, in part, to a genuine commitment to local Florida produce. Previous highlights include Scandinavian-style sashimi, pan-seared scallop with cauliflower and caviar, and corn chawanmushi. As for sushi, expect a faultless progression of warm, vinegared rice paired with a wonderful selection of fish, each one scored, sauced, and garnished to exacting standards. Dessert is just as serious, and a recent foie gras and miso flan with churros made for a superb finale.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2293;Kōsen;USA;Tampa;307 W. Palm Ave., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9623377;-82.4638787;80;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;This elegant restaurant takes a minimalist approach to its design, employing a dark color palette instead of the typical blonde wood. Though a two-concept spot (Kaiseki Room is a separate space), all eyes should be on the omakase, which Chef Andrew Huang runs with skill and precision. Delicate sea bream wrapped around sprouts with shaved black truffle delivers dialed-in flavors, while tempura-fried kamasu, served with myoga and chilled, roasted sweet eggplant, is smart and spot on. After a handful of dishes from the kitchen, they progress into the nigiri. There’s plenty of showmanship and style, but the sushi leans traditional without a lot of fuss, as in the kinmedai, seared, then hit with a squeeze of lime.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2295;Stubborn Seed;USA;Miami Beach;101 Washington Ave., Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.770023;-80.135047;71;true;true;Contemporary, American;Standing sentry on a busy corner, Stubborn Seed is sexy and sleek with an industrial chic décor and glass-fronted display kitchen. Whether you’re posted at the bar or in the main dining room, Chef Jeremy Ford brings the heat with an ambitious and brashly creative tasting menu. For sure, this is a kitchen that likes to take risks, weaving in Latin and Asian influences in a manner that is both bold and busy. Dinner begins with a series of small bites—like celery root croquette with beef bacon jam or beef tartare with black truffle, pine nuts, and Japanese milk bread—and escalates with pastas like ricotta gnudi with Manchego foam. Sourcing is a point of pride here too, as many ingredients come straight from the team’s organic five-acre farm in Redland.;Air conditioning;[]
2296;The Surf Club Restaurant;USA;Surfside;9011 Collins Ave., Surfside, 33154, USA;25.878331;-80.1216265;55;true;true;American;Located within the elegantly restored landmark, now in league with the Four Seasons, The Surf Club is a prime location for Thomas Keller's first Florida venture. The restaurant boasts all of the style and elegance of a private, members-only hangout with a handsome vintage bar, plush banquettes and dim, amber-hued lighting. Don't rush—you'll want to soak up all of its Art Deco glamour.Sharp-suited servers exude a certain effortless professionalism—not unlike the impressive Continental cooking. Perfectly seared crab cake with spicy mayonnaise and a thinly sliced cole slaw is at once familiar and new, though sauces are what this team does best, as in the brilliantly reimagined Maine lobster thermidor with sauce Américaine and the coconut chiffon cake with lime-flecked crème anglaise.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2297;Victoria & Albert's;USA;Orlando;4401 Floridian Way, Orlando, 32830, USA;28.411352;-81.5872943;50;true;false;Contemporary;Nestled within Disney's crown jewel, the Grand Floridian Resort, this restaurant is by no means an easy reservation, but the reward is a kind of magic rarely seen these days. The setting is intimate, and the pacing is that of a leisurely, three-hour waltz orchestrated by a gracious brigade of veteran servers.Chef Matthew Sowers cooks with contemporary verve and draws on influences spanning from Asia to the Nordics. Think delicate tarts set with New Zealand langoustine, striking “sandwiches” made with venison carpaccio and red cabbage, and bold sauces like cherry-cola bordelaise. Other details like water lists, an ornate coffee and tea service, and a serious wine program further impress.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2298;EntreNos;USA;Miami;9840 N.E. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33138, USA;25.8656875;-80.1935941;85;false;false;Contemporary;Chefs Evan Burgess and Osmel Gonzalez are at the helm of this original, dinner-only spot where a tightly edited à la carte menu puts the spotlight on Florida's seasons. The eclectic, inviting space may be small, but the cooking here is not to be underestimated: Just-caught seafood and beautifully grown produce from the Sunshine state take on lives of their own in the hands of this bold, creative team. Think shrimp from Cape Canaveral and soft, confit potatoes with chawanmushi or consider the dry-aged, grilled cobia served with a Moujean tea beurre blanc. It all comes to an end much too soon, and before long, you’re digging into a pumpkin flan that’s been churned into ice cream and topped with pepita granola and coffee espumita.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2299;Natsu;USA;Orlando;777 N. Orange Ave., Ste. C, Orlando, 32801, USA;28.5545626;-81.3790486;54;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;At Natsu, there are just two seatings a night at this intimate omakase, where a ten-seat counter dominates a spartan-styled room. Meals begin with four dishes from the kitchen, including chawanmushi and truffle kampachi, served with crispy potato straws and a yuzu truffle vinaigrette for an unexpected flavor combination that is especially memorable. The sushi is impressive and doesn't gild the lily, as in skin-on barracuda with a dynamic char or soy-marinated salmon that finishes ever-so-sweetly. Supremely buttery toro needs no flourish and is melt-in-your-mouth tender. It all rounds out with a hand roll and ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2300;Los Félix;USA;Miami;3413 Main Hwy., Miami, 33133, USA;25.7276768;-80.2428184;79;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Heritage corn sourced from across the Americas and seafood fetched from nearby waters are foundational pillars for this youthful restaurant in Coconut Grove. Such sustainability is a point of pride for Chef Sebastian Vargas, who offers a finely poised expression of Mexican cuisine that leans on subtle flavors and top-notch ingredients. Anyone can throw together a fish taco, but few are willing to source grouper from Key West, grill it in a banana leaf, and pair it with a deceptively addicting hazelnut emulsion. Another recent highlight featured a superb griddled corn cake paired with crab, smoked corn sauce, and charred plantains. The intimate setting attracts a handsome crowd with natural fibers, sleek wood, and a high-energy playlist.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list;[]
2301;LURRA˚;Japan;Kyoto;396 Sekisenincho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0021, Japan;35.010044;135.780637;86;true;true;Innovative;The name is a mashup of ‘Luna’ and ‘Terra’, Earth and Moon, plus a degree sign indicating ‘coordinates’. A trip around the world that starts here. The theme is a showcase of season and culture. Combining the seasons of Japan with food cultures from countries worldwide, the restaurant concocts dishes of exuberant creativity. Uniquely, main dishes are crafted with vegetables from Ohara and Fushimi, and grilled onigiri caps the meal. The many and varied pairings are a source of delight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2302;Chi-Fu;Japan;Osaka;4-4-8 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697434;135.504716;39;true;false;Chinese;Modern Chinese fare from a chef who studied French cuisine, so preparation methods, arrangements and wine pairings incorporate elements of French technique. Fruits are used in combination and Shaoxing wine is applied in sauces. Vegetarian Peking duck uses tofu skin in place of duck, adding vegetables in season for a more modern styling. This is a new take on Chinese cuisine, created with an independent approach.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2303;Pierre;Japan;Osaka;20F, InterContinental Osaka, 3-60 Ofukacho, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0011, Japan;34.70645;135.494552;99;false;true;French;Freshness is number one with the chef of Pierre, so he focuses on ingredients grown and raised in Japan. The menu only lists the ingredients, encouraging guests to give their imaginations free rein. Japanese seasonings such as mustard and chilli peppers mixed with yuzu zest lend a distinctive accent. French cooking techniques are married with Japanese ingredients, which are then prepared with a light touch. Spellbinding views from the spacious dining room high in a tall building add to the ambience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2306;Oryori Mitsuyasu;Japan;Kyoto;908-12 Koyamacho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8157, Japan;35.01947;135.743425;87;false;false;Japanese;The mood of a Kyoto merchant’s townhouse pervades the interior. The chef views a visit to his restaurant as a once-in-a-lifetime experience, so admission is limited to two groups per day. Hassun appetisers of vegetables are prepared simply: steamed, fried, or whichever method best brings out the flavours. Buckwheat mash dressed in white miso is a staple final dish harking back to the chef’s days at a soba shop. Each dish uses as few ingredients as possible, so each one leaves an impression.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Shoes must be removed;[]
2307;Kako Okamoto;Japan;Kyoto;470-4 Tokiwacho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0874, Japan;34.992366;135.77574;29;true;true;Japanese;The draw of Kako Okamoto is fine sake and prized delicacies. Appetisers are served not on a platter but one by one, freshly cooked, to complement the beverage. Spicy pilchard stew with finely chopped bonito flakes keeps the drinks going down easy. The owner-chef, who loves sake above all other drinks, offers pours from an isshobin (1.8 L bottle of sake) as if introducing his own child. Sake can also be ordered by the cup for a fun sake-tasting experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2308;Kodaiji Jugyuan;Japan;Kyoto;353 Masuyacho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0826, Japan;34.998694;135.781565;33;false;false;Japanese;Jugyuan is named after the famous Zen painting series, Jugyuzu, or ‘Pictures of Ten Oxen’. It has a sukiya-style house and beautiful garden. The chef incorporates seasonal festivals into his menu, imparting a sense of the customs of the ancient capital. Part of the attraction of Jugyuan is that meat dishes are a key part of the menu. Western techniques of flame control are applied here, thanks to the involvement of Hiramatsu, famous for its French cuisine. Kodaiji Jugyuan explores new directions while safeguarding the traditions of Kyoto gastronomy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
2310;SEN;Japan;Kyoto;379 Shiogamacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8103, Japan;34.996445;135.763986;71;true;true;Japanese;Seasonal notes and playfulness abound in the menu. Simple preparations etch themselves in the memory. During the Gion Festival, SEN displays a replica of the Naginata Boko, the first float in the festival’s parade, reflecting the city’s traditional events and customs. At the close of the meal, choose from an assortment of comfort foods such as mackerel sushi, chazuke and ramen. The chef learned to ‘read the room’ as an apprentice and is known to change ingredients and preparation styles based on guests’ conversation. The spirit of graceful service, expressed in cooking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2311;Yunagibashi Takoyasu;Japan;Osaka;1-15-5 Yunagi, Minato-ku, Osaka, 552-0004, Japan;34.662338;135.453975;67;true;false;Fugu / Pufferfish;Koji Kimura is the third-generation owner-chef of Yunagibashi Takoyasu and heir to its traditional flavours. He learned in Shimonoseki how to recognize high-quality fugu and inherited from his father the family’s culinary traditions. From the beginning, Yunagibashi Takoyasu accepts only wild fugu weighing 6 kg or more, as these are the most flavoursome. The menu features thick-cut sashimi, chiri nabe flavoured with shirako, and umami-rich zosui.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
2312;Kinobu;Japan;Kyoto;416 Iwatoyamacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8445, Japan;35.000953;135.756597;47;true;true;Japanese;Flexible and creative while revering the classics, Kinobu adds new twists to the way Kyoto cuisine reflects yearly events and the changing of the seasons. At the heart of the chef’s approach is a restless curiosity. He corresponds regularly with overseas chefs to deepen his store of knowledge. His ‘wine menu’ of dishes that pair well with wine is an innovation that broadens the scope of kaiseki. Kinobu began as a caterer and transformed itself into a ryotei. Treading a contemporary path, Kinobu keeps its eye on the future.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
2313;Kanamean Nishitomiya;Japan;Kyoto;562 Honeyanocho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-6084, Japan;35.00663;135.764806;90;true;true;Japanese;Refined traditional multi-course meals fit for a Japanese inn. Guided by the rubric that ‘tradition is just the continuation of innovation’, this is a restaurant that is open to new ideas. The evening begins when the owner-chef guides guests to the kitchen. The head chef makes lively conversation as he prepares the ingredients. He delights in exploring combinations of flavours, such as tuna with caviar and soba with truffles. Dining in a private room in the style of a tea arbor is part of the allure here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
2314;TAKAYAMA;Japan;Kyoto;2F, Good Nature Station, 318-6 Inaricho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8022, Japan;35.002526;135.76915;42;false;true;Italian;The prix fixe selection of numerous small dishes borrows an idea from Spanish tapas. Playful presentation and gorgeous arrangements upgrade Italian cuisine to a modern interpretation. The open kitchen is a stage, the semicircular counter the theatre’s front row. White serving-ware matches the white interior and the whole dining room feels like a canvas, a space to be filled by bright and colourful cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2315;Bini;Japan;Kyoto;445-1 Sambongicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0871, Japan;35.016854;135.760774;41;true;false;Italian;Modern Italian in a charming Kyoto merchant’s townhouse. Keisuke Nakamoto cultivates a strong rapport with farmers in Ōhara, on whose vegetables he relies. Incorporating fermentation techniques he studied in Europe, he overlays flavour with sourness. The signature dish is tagliolini of crab or truffles. Hand-made pasta gets its flavour from eggs from farms he has carefully selected. The natural bounty of farm communities finds expression in his cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2317;Rakushin;Japan;Osaka;1-6-27 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.695461;135.48817;97;true;true;Japanese;The name means ‘spirit of fun’, as he loves nothing more than to cook and enjoy good food. Through interacting with chefs overseas, Chef Katayama learns creative touches to add to his menu. The addition of Western elements flows from the same experience. At the same time, he never forgets reverence for tradition. Lacquered wooden trays and dishes garnished with flowers convey the season. Self-expressive yet respectful of traditional boundaries, Chef Katayama’s goal is the evolution of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2318;Alarde;Japan;Osaka;1-14-4 Awaza, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0011, Japan;34.680779;135.494028;45;true;false;Spanish;‘Basque cuisine you can taste only at Alarde’ is the theme, as the chef matches recipes studied in the Basque Country to ingredients found in Japan. His passion shines in the wagyu beef cooked in a stone oven. Fire is built from charcoal and firewood, then grapevines are added to wreathe the beef in smoky aromas. While you’re waiting for the meat to cook, treat yourself to some pinchos or mixed rice. Experience the world of Basque food culture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2319;Iroha;Japan;Osaka;5F, 1-3-19 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697842;135.495812;80;true;false;Japanese;Dinner at Iroha should be a once-in-a-lifetime experience, the chef decrees, so he lavishes his guests with the flavours of what’s in season. The extensive menu and the chef’s endless ingenuity testify to this commitment. An arranged sashimi dish is prepared using the techniques of skin searing, skin boiling, and kombu pickling. The popular beef cutlets are a hearty meat dish, ensuring that everyone leaves feeling satisfied. True to the restaurant’s name, which means ‘coloured leaves’, dishes are decorated with leaves of the season.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2320;Mokubei;Japan;Kyoto;570-120 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.001993;135.774645;43;false;false;Japanese;Mokubei serves Kyoto cuisine in Hanamikoji Street. The fourth-generation chef weaves the customs of Kyoto into his menu, along with the inquisitive spirit he learned as an apprentice. To pass on the legacy of the ancient capital, dishes are accompanied by waka poetry and Buddhist blessings written in the chef’s own hand. Eel cuisine, the signature fare, is patiently deboned to draw out the fish’s distinctive texture. Painstaking handiwork and graceful service embody the teachings of the chef’s mentor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2321;nent;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 1-5-12 Shibata, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0012, Japan;34.706547;135.497725;97;false;true;French;An intimate restaurant by a chef and sommelier. The team’s experience extends to Italian and Spanish, with French cuisine as the pivot. Imaginative food combinations and spices establish the eatery’s unique character. Creativity is not limited to Western traditions: the team takes pointers from Japanese cuisine as well. The name is Latin for ‘spin’, as the raison d’être is to spin food and wine into a few hours of happiness.;Air conditioning;[]
2322;Honke Tankuma Honten;Japan;Kyoto;168 Izumiyacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8014, Japan;35.000327;135.769089;25;false;false;Japanese;Founder Kumasaburo was a chef who made a name for himself in itamae kappo. Third-generation owner-chef Kumasaburo carries on the Tankuma tradition with his son. They serve ‘monmo’ dishes, in Kyoto dialect meaning ‘as-is’, so as to bring out the natural flavours of the ingredients. The horakuyaki dish featuring barracuda and matsutake smoked with pine needles is an autumn speciality. Enjoy the Higashiyama Sanjuroppo scenery from the premises on the Kamogawa River.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed;[]
2324;Kamanza Nagashima;Japan;Kyoto;726-5 Shimomatsuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0034, Japan;35.011394;135.755809;48;true;false;Japanese;No sign points to this kappo at the end of an alley, but the kind-hearted couple who run it will be waiting there to welcome you. Food preparation is simple, to let the character of the ingredients shine. One nourishing serving follows another, from appetiser platter through iimushi (mochi rice topped with fish and steamed) to white-miso soup. Small-pot dishes vary with the seasons, but the soup stock can be savoured year-round. Each dish is modest in presentation, reflecting the unassuming demeanour of the owner-chef.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
2325;HANA-Kitcho;Japan;Kyoto;3-2 Yamatocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0802, Japan;35.003395;135.772945;91;false;false;Japanese;The ‘Hana’ in the name comes from the restaurant’s location in Kyoto’s geiko quarter (the hanamachi or ‘flower quarter’). The interior is crafted by sculptors on the theme of a modern version of the Rinpa School of Painting. The floral pattern in the traditional washi paper decorating the ground floor corridor is also a nod to the hanamachi. The chequered pattern of moss and marble is a new experiment in décor. This is the only branch of Kyoto Kitcho that offers counter seating. Hassun appetisers are garnished with flowers in season, arranged to suggest views of Mt Arashi.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2326;Enyuan Kobayashi;Japan;Kyoto;125-2 Tominagacho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0078, Japan;35.00434;135.774754;69;false;true;Tempura, Japanese;Try a variety of Japanese culinary styles, with the accent on tempura. The chef apprenticed in traditional Japanese cuisine before taking the road of the tempura artisan. The menu incorporates the food culture of Kyoto. The meal begins with beloved standards such as simmered Pacific herring with aubergine and grilled honmoroko fish before moving on to tempura. Tempura pieces include nama-fu (steamed mixture of wheat gluten and rice flour) and Kyoto vegetables. A small dish of dried sea cucumber gonads also serves as an appetizer, and is another popular standard. Subtle inflections and clever use of ingredients are testament to the chef’s experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2327;Kamigamo Akiyama;Japan;Kyoto;58 Kamigamo Okamotocho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8081, Japan;35.058249;135.762726;17;false;true;Japanese;Amid the simple warmth of a converted old house, we take a brief rest in the waiting area with a relaxing cup of seasonal tea. Thanks to his friendships with nearby farmers, Naohiro Akiyama can express the seasons of Kamigamo through vegetables and wild grasses and flowers from Takagamine. His famous gruel of black rice recalls the diets of prehistory. Describing his dishes with the flair of a storyteller, the chef charms his guests, sometimes trading jokes to lighten the mood. Matcha tea served by Akiyama himself is a once-in-a-lifetime service experience.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2332;Différence;Japan;Osaka;1-16-12 Utsubohommachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0004, Japan;34.684525;135.494209;21;false;false;French;The inspiration for the name ‘Différence’, is a desire to provide a space to spend time away from the quotidian cares of life.The uniform white of the dining room, with its otherworldly milieu, reflects this aesthetic. The concept is ‘French with a sense of Japan’, so the focus is on food grown and raised in Japan. Desserts infused with vegetables to impart a sense of season and pastries combining two favourite Japanese confections, yokan and daifuku, are unique touches. Enjoy flavours and dining a little different from the ordinary.;Air conditioning;[]
2333;Okina;Japan;Kyoto;11 Sagashakado Daimoncho, Ukyo-ku, Kyoto, 616-8422, Japan;35.022746;135.6756;17;true;false;Japanese;The father-and-son team, along with their wives, offer a warm welcome to this kappo with deep roots in Saga. You can order à la carte or omakase style. Fish dishes are the stars of the menu, prepared in a number of ways: steamed with salt and sake, grilled, or however you like. Eel are prepared both unseasoned and dipped in soy-based sauce for you to taste and compare. At lunch the menu of boiled tofu and hiryuzu (deep-fried tofu mixed with thinly sliced vegetable) is the attraction. Treasuring its links with the region it calls home, Okina gets its tofu from Saga.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2334;Gion Mamma;Japan;Kyoto;347-108 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.004949;135.775794;71;false;false;Japanese;The eye settles at once on the big sunken hearth and the pothook hanging from the ceiling. Char-grilled items take pride of place, leaving no doubt as to the shop’s selling point. The owner-chef honed his craft at a traditional restaurant in Gifu, and the influence shows in offerings such as Waragawa sweetfish in summer and mallard and bear in winter. Whatever the item, his aim is to present its true flavours. The cheerful owner-chef devotes himself to gracious service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2335;Ogawa;Japan;Kyoto;515 Anenishinotoincho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8273, Japan;35.008838;135.755203;19;true;false;Japanese;After learning the basics at a ryotei, the chef worked at a kappo, where he discovered how to make dining fun. What he finds compelling about being a chef, he says, is that while the food itself is consumed at once and disappears, the occasion lingers in the memory. His ingenuity comes to the fore in Kyoto cuisine rich in dashi and vegetables. Side dishes such as boiled vegetables and ground soup, skilfully served both cold and warm, make for a treat that is simple yet impressive. Rice cooked in clay pots joins items such as preserves simmered in sweetened soy sauce, dried mullet roe and peppered crepe.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2336;Uozuya;Japan;Kyoto;8 Mibu Higashihinokicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8843, Japan;34.999842;135.735956;99;false;false;Japanese;A procession of dishes that linger in the diner’s memory. Seasonal flavours are used in generous measure, such as Japanese pepper flower, pike conger, matsutake mushrooms and crab. Preparation methods, whether that be grilling, boiling or more, are astutely tailored to each ingredient, showcasing its qualities from every angle. This talent for bringing out the best in food is born of long years of experience. A favourite haunt of the literati, the Uozuya sign calligraphy is by essayist Masako Shirasu.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
2337;KOKE;Japan;Kyoto;287 Takoyakushicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0021, Japan;35.012512;135.7581;27;false;false;Innovative;The theme is ‘water and fire’, as Chef Yusaku Nakamura is fascinated by these polar opposites. The prix fixe begins with soup cooked with water drawn from a well in the courtyard. Some items are grilled over wood, others over charcoal, with the approach varying based on the ingredients. The name of the restaurant is an acronym of Kobe, Okinawa, Kyoto and Español – the four regional influences from which the chef weaves his culinary story.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2338;La Bécasse;Japan;Osaka;3-3-9 Hiranomachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0046, Japan;34.68763;135.502257;36;true;true;French;La Bécasse aspires to greet guests with something new and exciting every time they visit. Rather than follow past recipes, the restaurant enlivens familiar ingredients with creative preparation techniques and sauces. A sojourn in France taught the chef the importance of terroir, the characteristics of the land from which sprouts the character of each ingredient. To convey the blessings of each season, the chef visits markets daily, seeking new ways to reflect Japanese terroir through French cooking.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2339;Sushiroku;Japan;Osaka;4-12-22 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697125;135.502972;73;false;true;Sushi;A counter of hinoki cypress in a cosy interior. The chef is a man of few words, devoting himself to the sushi he’s forming. He uses two types of sushi rice to ensure harmony between rice and sushi toppings: rice vinegar with white-fleshed fish and red vinegar with fatty cuts, for example. Soy-marinaded tuna is wrapped in nori after it is formed, in the style of tekkamaki. The basis is Edomae sushi but with respect for Kansai culture. The inventiveness of the chef’s work makes it all the more impressive.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2340;Muromachi Wakuden;Japan;Kyoto;679 Marukizaimokucho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8106, Japan;35.010146;135.763257;100;false;false;Japanese;This is a counter kappo from Wakuden, which is bringing innovation to Kyoto cuisine. The counter, arrayed around the kitchen, makes guests feel part of a single group. The fare is grounded in a philosophy of ‘rustic beauty and refinement’. This principle is the inspiration for ‘Nariaiyaki’, pike conger at the end of its season, wrapped in matsutake mushrooms and grilled. Rumour has it that the dish is modelled after the view from Nariaiji Temple near Amanohashidate in Miyazu Bay.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2341;Kentan Horibe;Japan;Kyoto;273 Tenjinyamacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8221, Japan;35.004999;135.757018;42;true;false;Japanese;The first feature to catch your eye in the tasteful tea-house style interior is the lacquer counter, which the chef polished and coated himself. ‘Kentan’ means ‘the deep pursuit of self-improvement’. The seasonal interior decoration, serving ware and cuisine combine harmoniously to celebrate the history and food culture of Kyoto. Modern cooking techniques are also adopted here, such as grilling over low flame. A place to appreciate Japanese cuisine in a broader context.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2342;Sushi Rakumi;Japan;Kyoto;332-6 Miyoshicho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0081, Japan;35.006712;135.776041;28;true;true;Sushi;The scroll, which reads ‘ikkan’ (consistency), appears behind the chef as if worn like a mantle. His experience in sushi and other Japanese cuisines shines in his omakase. Salmon roe is pureed and mixed with vinegared rice like putting a raw egg over rice. Chub mackerel pressed sushi is wrapped in dried gourd strips or perilla leaf and toasted over charcoal. Nigiri are formed with rice vinegar or red vinegar, depending on the topping—adopting the best features of sushi culture from East and West Japan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2343;Shinchi Yamamoto;Japan;Osaka;1-1-13 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.696009;135.499915;56;false;true;Japanese;The chef treats his guests to seasonal cuisine of unstinting luxury. The feast begins with bamboo shoots, sweetfish, matsutake mushrooms and crab, representing the four seasons. The spectacle of the kitchen from the counter captivates the heart. For soup dishes, the basic soup stock is drawn directly before the customer. Items grilled on the charcoal brazier or cooked in pots are likewise prepared in view of the customer. Arrangements are simple, to give the ingredients top billing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2344;Sushidokoro Amano;Japan;Osaka;1-13-2 Shitennoji, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0051, Japan;34.655421;135.514117;87;true;true;Sushi;The movements of the owner-chef’s fingers as he works are a marvel to watch. This deftness is apparent in his side dishes and sushi. His knife technique, informed by a deep understanding of the characteristics of each fish, raises the flavour to a new level. Sushi rice is changed frequently to maintain just the right temperature, that of the human body. Rice is gathered in the palm of the hand as if capturing air. Wasabi, applied with the index finger, is apportioned just right, as is the nikiri. Formed with practiced economy of movement, each nigiri is formed perfectly for true flavour.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
2346;Gosho Iwasaki;Japan;Kyoto;660 Otsucho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0885, Japan;35.016879;135.761643;96;true;true;Japanese;As a ryotei cook, the chef learned never to forget the basics of Kyoto cuisine. In a mark of respect, the meal begins with a cup of sake. The chef expresses his commitment to gracious service through the passion he devotes to his cooking. Tilefish sashimi is lightly salted, enhancing flavour. Instead of simmered vegetables, hot-pot cooking is offered. Prizing engagement with his guests, the chef works his magic right before their eyes. The surest sign of a sincere craftsman is earnest devotion to his craft.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2348;Maison Tateru Yoshino;Japan;Osaka;2F, ANA Crowne Plaza Osaka, 1-3-1 Dojimahama, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0004, Japan;34.695687;135.498232;91;false;true;French;Tateru Yoshino’s eponymous restaurant traces his journey in ‘modern classic’ cuisine. The dining room’s décor is inspired by the flowers and coral reefs of Yoshino’s native Kikaijima. Salmon mi-cuit à la Stella Maris was conceived in Paris. Subtle flame control and the ensembles of flavour and acidity inscribed on the menu weave a tale of the age. Yoshino entrusts his kitchen to the next generation of cooks, cultivating up-and-coming talents. Cuisines new and old find voice in Yoshino’s Maison.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2349;Terada;Japan;Osaka;2F, 2-35 Tamatsukurimotomachi, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0014, Japan;34.674331;135.532779;87;false;false;Japanese;‘Good old traditions and colourful, fun Japanese cuisine’ is the credo of owner-chef Shigeru Terada. He works traditional festivals or events into each of his hassun, which he serves with a ready smile. The reason he chooses contemporary plates and bowls is so diners can experience a journey through the present with the artists. Fresh vegetables arrive from his parents in Mie Prefecture, the images on the coaster are painted by his mother, and his elder brother designed the interior.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2350;Kiyama;Japan;Kyoto;136 Kinuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0804, Japan;35.01578;135.763078;58;true;true;Japanese;To prepare dashi soup stock, that indispensable element of Japanese cuisine, the chef draws water from a well on the premises. He shaves dried bonito in front of guests, conveying the original mood of Japanese food service that is in danger of disappearing. After sampling the first draft, guests enjoy the soup stock that flavours the stewed items. With each change in flavour, its impression deepens. On the second floor, the counter seating bears the refined aspect of a tea arbour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2352;Gion Kida;Japan;Kyoto;570-192 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002502;135.776138;18;false;false;Japanese;There is a traditional way of viewing the year as 72 distinct micro-seasons, each lasting no more than a few weeks. The turning of the seasons is but a fleeting moment, and the same is true for the seasons of ingredients. If ingredients are the cause, the effect is cooking, and the natural world is the connection between the two. The chef examines the nature of the foods he sources each day and crafts his results with respect for both cause and connection. The guests receive the life of the ingredient.The principles of cause, connection and effect are all found in cooking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2353;Sawada;Japan;Osaka;4-2-50 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.693041;135.482494;24;true;false;Japanese;With a spirit of gratitude, Toshimitsu Sawada explains his menu like a storyteller. Like the chef, the hostess and apprentice pour their souls into their work, creating food to satisfy hearts as well as stomachs. Appetiser platters expressing scenes of mountain villages and hotpots for sharing attest to Sawada’s schooling in the restaurants of Shiga. Rice dishes in clay pots are deliciously accompanied and come with noodles. A delight from beginning to end.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2354;MASHIRO;Japan;Kyoto;2F, OHG Kyoto Rokkaku Bldg, 234 Donomaecho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8134, Japan;35.007261;135.760822;98;true;true;Contemporary;After Ashiya and Gion, the new frontier for Hiroyuki Koshimo is Karasuma. The shop’s previous name, ‘Roiro’, meant ‘Black as Lacquer’, so Koshimo changed it to ‘Pure White’ to set a different tone. Though his technique is French, Koshimo is not limited by genre, incorporating Japanese elements to broaden the expressive range. Risotto in season, prepared with Yosano rice, is a perennial favourite in this lively and hospitable eatery.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2355;Naniwakappo NOBORU;Japan;Osaka;1-3-12 Oyodominami, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0075, Japan;34.703876;135.490367;37;false;false;Japanese;‘Flavour first’ is the watchword at this kappo-style restaurant, where food is prepared before your eyes. The chef also serves generous helpings of smiles and conversation. Orders are placed in kaiseki fashion but varied by the mood of the day and guest preference. ‘Shinjo o hakari, ninjo wo kurau’— words from the restaurant where the chef apprenticed, serves as an exhortation to be thankful for the good fortune of providing what the diner desires. The craftsman spirit of a Naniwa (Osaka) kappo is enshrined in the name.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2356;Funaokayama Shimizu;Japan;Kyoto;20-2 Murasakino Higashifunaokacho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8228, Japan;35.039073;135.744546;99;true;true;Japanese;You’ll find this Japanese restaurant in a residential area close to Funaokayama Park. The chef draws his water from Daitokuji Temple, gets his vegetables from farmers in Takagamine, and buys ingredients from various regions at the Central Market. He chose this location so he could focus fully on his craft. To honestly convey the flavours of his painstakingly selected ingredients, the chef avoids reliance on garnishes. Stripped to the bare essentials, his fare speaks with its own clear voice.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2357;il Centrino;Japan;Osaka;1-2-2 Kawarayamachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0066, Japan;34.672916;135.514213;44;true;true;Italian;During his time in Italy, the chef was struck by the pride the locals had in their agricultural produce, which is deeply rooted in the natural and spiritual features of the land. He reflects on the places he travelled to, paying respect to local cuisines. Having apprenticed in Piemonte and Veneto, he specialises in the techniques of northern Italy, but expresses his own creative sensibility as well. The arrangements are simple and modern, and the flavours are subtle and light.;Air conditioning;[]
2358;Ichiju Nisai Ueno Minoten;Japan;Osaka;2-5 Minokoen, Mino, Osaka, 562-0002, Japan;34.839017;135.471024;85;false;false;Japanese;The chef avoids the formalities of tea ceremony cuisine, as he wants diners to enjoy their meal and not feel self-conscious. He follows the principle of ‘one bowl of soup and two side dishes’. Appetiser platters are garnished with seasonal flowers and leaves, creating a bright and cheerful presentation. The tempura combo is an essential menu item. Depending on the room, the cook may fry each tempura item individually. Serenaded by the murmuring of the Minō River, dine with relish on the bounty of nature.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
2359;SINAE;Japan;Osaka;2F, 2-4-12 Fushimimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0044, Japan;34.689286;135.504679;98;false;false;French;‘Sinae’ is an acronym for ‘simple, natural, essence’. These principles support the cuisine of Kazuhiko Daito, who values the natural features of the region where he works. The pure white vessels express the notion of ‘French cuisine, but in a uniquely Japanese style’. Daito transforms Japan-grown ingredients using traditional techniques, as exemplified by his bisque of Japanese tiger prawn. Platters with a wide variety of root vegetables roasted or fried remind us of the warmth and bounty of the earth.;Air conditioning;[]
2360;Kenya;Japan;Kyoto;28-22 Okazaki Tokuseicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8351, Japan;35.015957;135.778277;44;true;true;Japanese;There’s no point in cooking, says Kenya, if it doesn’t make the food tasty. Bringing fun and happiness to guests is important above all. Rice and sake both come from Aomori, where the chef comes from. His character reveals itself in his face when he lifts the lid on a pot of freshly steamed rice. Western music, classical music and Showa-era ballads are chosen to suit the cuisine, expressing the joy of good cooking as if weaving a tale. Flavours are fun here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2361;Kashiwaya Osaka Kitashinchi;Japan;Osaka;5F, 1-7-4 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.69685;135.50052;94;true;false;Japanese;This restaurant is a new approach by Kashiwaya, a ryotei in Senriyama. Like the flagship restaurant, the Kitashinchi location’s menu follows the 24 traditional divisions of the lunisolar year known as nijushi sekki. Here, however, the menu is crafted so that the chef can prepare everything at the counter, a feature the ryotei lacks. Wielding his knives to prepare sashimi and arrange it on plates, dressing appetisers and so forth, the chef displays all his skill. This ‘peek behind the curtain’ of the techniques usually not shown to guests is an expression of love for the craft.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2362;Utsubohommachi Gaku;Japan;Osaka;1-14-15 Utsubohommachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0004, Japan;34.68459;135.495405;17;true;true;Japanese;The chef cultivated his free-ranging creativity at a Naniwa kappo, his genial customer service at a bistro. His creative flair is on full display in his combinations of ingredients. Pairings such as sweetfish with peach, barracuda with persimmon, and Spanish mackerel with apple marry fish of the season with the sweetness, tartness and flavour of fruit. Great care is taken to offer a wide selection of organic wines that have affinity for each offering. The chef’s philosophy is that originality must be firmly grounded in the basics, and his cuisine attests to it.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2364;LE PONT DE CIEL;Japan;Osaka;B1F, Nihonseimei Yodoyabashi Bldg, 3-5-29 Kitahama, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0031, Japan;34.692109;135.50233;47;true;false;French;To mark its half-century anniversary, LE PONT DE CIEL broke new ground, converting to a ‘counter French’ format. The open kitchen buzzes with activity as cooks and serving staff attend customers. The key to the fare here is cooking with firewood. Vegetables are roasted, fish smoked, meat wrapped in flame. The name means ‘bridge across the sky’, reflecting the chef’s desire to foster a culture that connects a relaxing time with delicious cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2366;Gion Fukushi;Japan;Kyoto;570-120 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002145;135.774388;20;true;false;Japanese;The chef trained at an itamae kappo. His menu evolves day by day as he converses with guests and discovers their preferences. Kitchen scenes, such as earthen pots and brazier and hamo finely cut to crush the small bones, delight the eye. Dishes tailored to seasonal celebrations such as Hinamatsuri (Dolls’ Festival) and Tanabata (Star Festival) are served on Kyoto ware brightly decorated for each celebration. Sensitive to shifting fashions, main dishes include wagyu beef, while rice and noodles are available to close the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2367;Matsuzushi;Japan;Osaka;3-13-6 Ojicho, Abeno-ku, Osaka, 545-0023, Japan;34.627716;135.510036;36;false;false;Sushi;Matsuzushi has been in business for over half a century. Its second and present owner-chef, Yohei Tanigawa, used the opportunity of the handover from the previous owner to study sushi in detail, embarking on an eating tour of sushi shops in Tokyo. He adds red vinegar to sushi rice to harmonise it with toppings. The first item served is seafood in season. Sushi toppings are fresh from Osaka Bay: egg cockle in spring, pilchard in summer, sea bream in autumn, and Spanish mackerel in winter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2368;Ajikitcho Bumbuan;Japan;Osaka;B1F, Hommachi Garden City, 3-6-4 Hommachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0053, Japan;34.68307;135.501093;28;true;false;Japanese;The name is a mashup of the name of the couple who founded the restaurant and the phrase ‘bumbu-ryodo’, ‘accomplished in both literary and military arts’. The phrase expresses the spirit of the chef, who devotes himself to both cooking and service. The third-generation chef commands the kitchen, guarding the flavours inherited from the first. Unmoved by an age that craves all things new, the chef passes on the handiwork and cuisine of the good old days. The simmered vegetable assortment is one example. With skilful knife work and carefully calibrated addition of dashi, the chef brings guests the flavours of the season.;Air conditioning;[]
2369;capi;Japan;Osaka;6F, 1-10-2 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697954;135.497901;80;true;false;Innovative;The concept is ‘conversations between ingredients’. Pairings of complementary ingredients include Pacific saury with tomatoes, potatoes with cheese and duck with figs. The signature dish of caviar, squid and aubergine brings out a unique flavour profile through the contrast of salt and sweet. The numbers of ingredients on each plate are kept to a minimum, so patrons retain a clear impression of what they ate.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2370;Oryori Horikawa;Japan;Osaka;4-8-17 Temma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0043, Japan;34.693707;135.514269;16;true;true;Japanese;The chef trained at a traditional restaurant, so his menu follows annual events and seasonal themes. For the key five festivals of the year, guests can dine while admiring the seasonal decorations. During the Doll Festival, dolls are displayed and strips of paper inscribed with poems from the Weaver Festival inspire serving dishes. For the Chrysanthemum Festival, fishcakes are squeezed into balls and served in soup as if they were chrysanthemums. While the chef devotes himself to the kitchen, the proprietress describes the serving vessels and customs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2371;agnel d'or;Japan;Osaka;2-4-4 Nishihommachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0005, Japan;34.682548;135.490981;24;false;true;French;Cooking is the art of teasing out the pure flavour of each ingredient. For example, a main dish could be paired with clear consommé drawn from mushrooms or seafood. A delicate finish, light on fats and oils, brings out the pure flavour of each ingredient. Dishes prepared using Japanese ingredients such as Pacific saury, groundnuts and lily bulbs are arranged on vessels produced by modern artists. In France, the chef learned the importance of originality. His inquisitive mind creates uniqueness in his work.;Air conditioning;[]
2372;Yonemasu;Japan;Osaka;1-9-16 Oyodominami, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0075, Japan;34.703019;135.487567;18;false;true;Japanese;A map shows the locations from where the day’s ingredients came from. The chef wants his cooking to give guests a sense of the land and season that produced it. The riches gathered convey the bounty of Japan’s natural features. Flavours in their proper seasons, including bamboo shoots, sweetfish, mushrooms and crab, are broiled over an earthen charcoal brazier to delight all the senses. Arrangements are spare, giving the ingredients top billing. Antique vessels reflect annual events, conveying the culture of old Japan.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
2373;Kaishoku Shimizu;Japan;Osaka;1F, Shin Daibiru, 1-2-1 Dojimahama, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0004, Japan;34.695621;135.499246;100;true;true;Japanese;Toshihiro Shimizu has always been passionate about his culinary research. Artistic presentation and ingenious twists are offered without fanfare. Emulating the principles of kaiseki, he uses rice in his amuse-bouche between courses. Appetisers are garnished with leaves, connoting the seasons’ constant shifting. The restaurant name expresses his desire that his customers heartily enjoy their meal. While preserving the fundamental character of Japanese cuisine, he assembles his menu with an original approach.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2374;PRESQU'ÎLE;Japan;Osaka;2F, Yodoyabashi odona, 4-1-1 Imabashi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0042, Japan;34.690995;135.500142;59;true;true;French;Piped baroque music and service on trolleys recall the goodness of French restaurants in the old days. As befits a restaurant managed by a Yamanashi winery, grape leaves adorn the walls and the company’s own wines are served. A devotee of classic cuisine, the chef excels in dishes baked in pie crusts, and is generous with sauces. The fruit that decorates the tables can be made into crêpes Suzette.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2375;Droit;Japan;Kyoto;49-1 Higashisakuracho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-0858, Japan;35.022379;135.767564;59;false;true;French;A return to the origins of French cuisine. To sublimate the classics, the chef pores over old cookbooks and interprets their recipes for modern ingredients and environments, giving free rein to his curiosity with wine, butter and sauces pungent with spices. He emphasises herbs picked in the morning in Oharano and ingredients from around Kansai, expressing in food his conversations with producers. ‘Droit’ means ‘straight ahead,’ and that’s the steady course this restaurant charts.;Air conditioning;[]
2377;a canto;Japan;Osaka;3-1-10 Uchikyuhojimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0013, Japan;34.678984;135.515695;71;false;true;Italian;The chef’s creed is to weave seasonal elements and refinement into his cuisine. Each item is simple yet distinctive. Bavettine of dried mullet roe and lime is a signature dish using handmade pasta. Pastas showcase the assured touch of a craftsman who was in charge of that department at Enoteca Pinchiorri in Florence. The name means ‘at your side’, as the chef hopes it can be familiar presence for diners who crave the warmth of Italian cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2378;Konoha;Japan;Osaka;2-6-22 Minamihommachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0054, Japan;34.682634;135.504198;34;false;false;Japanese, Tempura;Kaiseki meals puts the chef’s traditional restaurant experience to fitting use. Appetisers, soups and assorted side dishes combine with the serving vessels to paint a picture of the seasons. What really draws out the flavours is the familiar ma-kombu kelp dashi soup stock. Deep-fried items catch the eye, like tempura lightly coated and fried piece by piece. To boost flavour, extra egg yolk is used for a unique coating. Inflections in flavour and texture provide variety but the focus is always on seasonality and sense of ingredients.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2380;ad hoc;Japan;Osaka;Hotarumachi, 1-1-48 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.694143;135.489021;68;false;false;French;The gastronomy of Chef Tatsuhiro Takayama blends a passion for learning from nature with a modern sensibility. To attune his work to the sense of the seasons, he adds layers of texture. His spring ‘Sakuraniku, Sansai’ accents the bitterness of spring vegetables with the texture of buckwheat groats. The menu lists only the ingredients, as a mark of respect to the foodstuff producers. Natural rock tables and wooden ornamental plates eloquently convey the chef’s love of nature.;Air conditioning;[]
2381;Sanso Kyoyamato;Japan;Kyoto;359 Masuyacho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0826, Japan;34.999252;135.78139;30;true;true;Japanese;During the short walk from the front gate to the main buildings, guests can appreciate the history of the buildings while feeling the presence of nature. Classic aesthetics pervade the entire site, from the sukiya design of the buildings to the space reflecting seasonal ceremonies and views of the garden. The chef wants every aspect of Sanso Kyoyamato to be beautiful, so he takes special care with the refinement of his food arrangements and their elegant flavours. The painstaking service of the proprietress and hostess is an agreeable presence. Diners will sense a complete work of Japanese art.;Air conditioning,Great view,Shoes must be removed;[]
2384;Muromachi Yui;Japan;Kyoto;459 Kimbukicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0846, Japan;35.012233;135.758455;47;false;true;Japanese;‘Yui’ means ‘one and only’, and indeed the meals to be savoured in this elegant dining room are to be found nowhere else. Kazuteru Maeda’s basic soup stock is aged for two days to elicit all the umami the kombu kelp has to offer. Edible wild plants and mushrooms, picked in the mountains by the chef himself, are a treat. Maeda works alone, pouring heart and soul into his craft. His goal is a one-of-a-kind restaurant that truly conveys his culinary feelings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2385;Jiki Miyazawa;Japan;Kyoto;553-1 Yaoyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8123, Japan;35.0043254;135.7633929;35;false;true;Japanese;Japan is a land blessed with rice, whose people have given thanks for farming and the workings of nature for countless generations. Just before it is fully cooked, rice exudes a beguiling cloud of steam. The pursuit of such brief moments, with their beautiful fragrance and texture, is integral to the spiritual nature of the Japanese. Steamed rice and okoge (scorched or crispy rice) each offer fleeting moments when their unique appeal is best tasted. Dishes cooked with fermented vegetable peels bring out the flavour of this honest fare.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2386;Mirei;Japan;Kyoto;143-2 Kameyacho, Takeyamachidori Muromachihigashiiru, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0865, Japan;35.016197;135.75848;74;true;true;Japanese;The French painter Jean-François Millet was the inspiration behind the restaurant's name—Western culture being a major influence in the owner-chef Yuzo Nakao's hometown of Nagasaki, an international port city for centuries. Recognising that no two people have the same tastes, he welcomes guests with a varied à la carte menu. Make a point of ordering the pureed soup of young onions, peaches, chestnuts and Kyoto yams which bursts with imagination and the colours of the seasons.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2387;Iwaki;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-6-29 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697482;135.499446;77;false;true;Japanese;Curiosity drives the creative spirit that powers this restaurant. There are no standard menu items: the direction is always forwards, never looking back on past dishes. Technique honed at a ryotei overlays creativity learned at an old-school Osaka kappo. Hamo is deboned, producing a texture of luxuriant plumpness. New techniques create new taste sensations, so eel are salt-grilled, not dipped in sauce. Ingenuity is everywhere, yet the ingredients are always the star.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2388;Vena;Japan;Kyoto;46-3 Kagamiyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0002, Japan;35.015154;135.758097;48;true;false;Italian;Thrown together in an unexpected meeting, chef Hiroki Hayakawa and sommelier Yoji Ikemoto immediately hit it off. Both natives of Kyoto, they felt bound by fate through their names, which both refer to bodies of water, so when they opened their restaurant under joint management, they named it ‘Vena’, Italian for ‘waterway’. The chef’s keen eye for ingredients pairs well with the sommelier’s collection of vintage wines. An interweaving of two Kyoto boys, born and bred in the ‘city of water’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2389;Kyoboshi;Japan;Kyoto;347-92 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.005139;135.775649;45;false;false;Tempura;Kyoboshi serves light-battered tempura unchanged from the day its doors opened in 1947. The recipe features a unique blend of oils, handed down in secret from father to just one son, as well as use of handmade crushed salt to bring out the ingredients. Uniquely, the main ingredients alternate between seafood and vegetables, interspersed with shrimp. The first shrimp is served rare, the second cooked to an intense crescendo. The chef adjusts the flame with practiced skill, modulating the flavour of the shrimp with each serving.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2390;Ryoriya Maekawa;Japan;Kyoto;405 Nambacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8027, Japan;34.998689;135.767871;22;true;true;Japanese;Owner-chef Koichi Maekawa’s goal is to present a ‘ryoriya’ (‘cookery’) that reflects his taste and personality, unfettered by established practice. He strives for originality while leaving core tenets of Kyoto cooking intact. In a witty touch that can’t help but make you smile, fried shrimp-shaped and -patterned yam in tomato sauce is dressed with sakura shrimps. The eatery, with its triangular ceiling reminiscent of a houseboat, is wrapped in an amusing air.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2391;Masuda;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-3-12 Shinsaibashisuji, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0085, Japan;34.673799;135.501957;91;false;false;Japanese;The wooden counter is owner-chef Yoshichika Masuda’s stage. Like a skilled conjurer revealing his tricks, Masuda demonstrates the techniques and traditions of Japanese cuisine he honed during his days at a ryotei. The hassun is especially attention-grabbing. The sculptured beauty formed by ingredients from land and sea is a study in the coexistence of light and shade. The attentive service and the sight of his training his apprentice shines a light on the future of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2392;MUNI ALAIN DUCASSE;Japan;Kyoto;B1F, MUNI KYOTO, 3 Sagatenryuji Susukinobabacho, Ukyo-ku, Kyoto, 616-8385, Japan;35.013637;135.676621;68;true;true;French;The artistic sensibilities of Alain Ducasse find synthesis with Kyoto. The contemporary French cuisine marries French ingredients with Japanese ingredients: clams with caviar, bamboo shoots with truffles, lobster and daikon radishes cultivated in the Kyoto area. Sauce is poured at your table, completing the richly aromatic cuisine. Luxurious surroundings, exquisite cuisine and elegant service welcome you to the world of Alain Ducasse.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2393;Kyoryori Fujimoto;Japan;Kyoto;72 Shimmeicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8207, Japan;35.010396;135.756636;63;false;false;Japanese;The wisdom of the chef’s mentor and what he learned on countless visits to markets made the restaurant what it is today. His approach is not to season but to let ingredients speak for themselves. Serving a great meal is an act of great effort: taking care of guests and serving graciously. Keen to offer a wide range of flavours, the chef incorporates an extensive list of ingredients. These efforts are rewarded when diners tell him ‘gochiso-sama deshita’ (‘thank you for all your efforts’).;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
2394;Zeshin;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 2-9-3 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696365;135.502426;16;false;false;Japanese;Walk through the building’s front gate and descend the stairs to the underground level, and a space spreads out before you. To greet you are the head chef and proprietor, who together share all the joys and sorrows of running a restaurant. The kaiseki meal, which follows Japan’s old calendar, lavishly expresses the season in its flavours. The dining-ware, collected by both, brilliantly accentuates the cuisine. If you’d like to chat with the head chef as you dine, ask for a seat at the counter. Private rooms, with ceremonial décor based on the old calendar, are a treat.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2396;la bûche;Japan;Kyoto;400-3 Ohara Raikoincho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 601-1242, Japan;35.120006;135.829962;19;true;true;French;Recalling the pride French chefs express in their country’s regions, Shohei Mori opened a restaurant in his hometown. The stars of his gustatory show are vegetables, both farmed and wild, river fish, game, and more of the bounty of Ohara. The shop’s name means ‘firewood’, and ingredients here are wreathed in primordial flame. By showcasing the appeal of the region through cooking, Mori repays a debt to the land where he was born and raised.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2397;MOKO;Japan;Kyoto;235-2 Tamauecho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0005, Japan;35.016851;135.757149;84;false;false;French;Alexis Moko was born in Versailles and travelled often from his country of birth to London. Though connections brought him to reside in Kyoto, his native language, culture and ingredients are all foreign to the area. It all began when, feeling disheartened, he cycled through Ōhara and encountered food producers who reignited his ambition. Vegetables and game from Ōhara are prepared in traditional fashion. Preserving classical tradition, Moko never forgets to dress his dishes with sauces.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2398;Nijo Minami;Japan;Kyoto;92-12 Enokicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0931, Japan;35.013142;135.768119;62;true;true;Japanese;The chef honed his craft at a kappo in Gion for a quarter of a century. “I’m grateful to my mentor, who was a man of culture as well as a chef”, he explains. Appetiser platters, soup dishes and takiawase are all part of a lineup that pays homage to old-school cooking. The chef’s first job in the culinary world was to wring out the hot cloths for guests, and he squeezed them with all his might. His favourite saying, passed down to him from that time, is “kindness, freshness, feeling”.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2401;anpeiji;Japan;Kyoto;56 Nakajima Hinokamicho, Fushimi-ku, Kyoto, 612-8465, Japan;34.944128;135.74508;64;true;false;French;Masashi Ampeiji opened his eponymous eatery on the site of a Western restaurant his parents used to run. The shop’s logo, reminiscent of a single hieroglyphic, represents Chef Anpeiji’s filter. Anpeiji expresses the techniques and sensibilities he studied in France in unique dishes. His use of herbs and olive oil to enhance fragrance derives from his experience in the south of France. He turns vegetables grown by his father into purées and garnishes. The bond between father and son is close.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2402;P greco;Japan;Osaka;4-1-20 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696173;135.505946;35;true;false;Italian;In Italy, the chef experienced the fierce pride the Italians have in their home regions. Deeply impressed by the unique cuisines of people who produce and consume locally all their lives, he set his sights on combining Japanese sensibilities with Italian cooking. One example is anago carpaccio: deboned conger eel accompanied by tomato and bagna càuda. The focus on seafood derives from his love of the bounty of the sea, learned at his grandmother’s house in Okinoshima.;Air conditioning;[]
2403;Oryori Yamada;Japan;Osaka;4F, 4-7-7 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696722;135.503816;89;true;true;Japanese;Great ingenuity is poured into the menu to fill it with creative cuisine. Sashimi is garnished with condiments such as deep-fried onions and coarsely grated daikon. Fish cuisine is accented with sauces of mushrooms and vegetables. As a born-and-bred Osakan, the chef gravitates toward Naniwa’s traditional vegetables. The meal wraps up with three types of rice dishes: white rice and several accompaniments, pickled fish on rice and seasonal mixed rice. The generosity of free refills ensures that guests leave satisfied.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2404;Ryoriya Inaya;Japan;Osaka;7F, 1-10-2 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697954;135.497901;28;false;true;Japanese;Hiroki Inaya is the son of a Japanese cuisine chef. He followed in his father’s footsteps out of awe for the magnificent sashimi and funamori (sashimi arranged on a model boat) he fashioned. He stays within the bounds of Japanese cuisine but never forgets to add a playfulness of spirit, delighting customers with crab spawn rolled into balls to resemble crab foam, for example. Two earthenware pots draw the eye: one contains white rice served at the perfect point, the other takikomi gohan, rice cooked and seasoned with a variety of ingredients in season.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2405;Reine des prés;Japan;Kyoto;537-1 Komanocho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-0872, Japan;35.017249;135.769857;84;false;false;French;Owner-chef Fumitaka Nakahara received his training from none other than Alain Passard, once known as ‘the wizard of meat’ but who is today famed for his vegetable cuisine. Calculating how long the meat will take to cook, he serves it together with the all-important vegetables. Focusing on just a few ingredients on a single plate is Nakahara’s trademark. Assembled ingredients bring out the best in each other, leaving guests with clear impressions of the foods they enjoyed.;Air conditioning;[]
2406;Ñ;Japan;Osaka;1-6-3 Azuchimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0052, Japan;34.684008;135.508376;24;true;false;Spanish;At the start of the 21st century, when the ‘modern Spanish’ trend began, the chef was accumulating experience in Madrid and San Sebastián. Today he parlays Spain’s cuisine of many small dishes into a modern prix fixe menu. Refined tapas, arroz suffused with regional character and plancha-grilled items, flamed to bring out the natural flavour of each foodstuff, showcase the pride the chef takes in his work.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2407;Point;Japan;Osaka;2-17-47 Uenohigashi, Toyonaka, Osaka, 560-0013, Japan;34.793027;135.476328;91;false;false;French;The restaurant stands in a residential neighbourhood of Toyonaka, the chef’s hometown. It has an open kitchen with counter seating, so diners can enjoy flavours fresh from grill and oven. The fare is squarely based on the classics on which he apprenticed in Paris. Seafood and consommé jelly and beef wrapped in a pastry shell offer a modern styling with the accent on lightness. The focus at Point is the trinity of guests, producers and ingredients – converging these three on the single point of ‘cuisine’ is the inspiration behind the name.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2408;Ono;Japan;Osaka;6F, 1-2-22 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.69739;135.497797;64;false;true;Japanese;The lacquerware counter surrounds the owner-chef. Proudly displaying both foodstuffs and technique, he regales his guests with his feelings about the people and regions that produced his ingredients. In gratitude to his native Awajishima, he naturally sources his foods from there. Onions shipped straight from the farm are used in savoury egg custard. Wagyu from cattle raised by a friend is grilled over charcoal. The meal concludes with takikomi-gohan and curry of dashi soup stock and spiny lobster.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2410;Yuyu;Japan;Kyoto;8 Koyama Kitakamifusacho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8142, Japan;35.044835;135.759172;66;true;false;Japanese;The shop’s name recalls the phrase ‘yuyu-jiteki’, ‘a life of leisure, free of worldly cares’. True to this proposition, Yuyu offers dining à la carte in the evening, so guests can relax and dine at their own pace. Sashimi plates are accompanied not with soy sauce but with Daitokuji natto. Beef tongue is dressed with white miso, resembling a stew. Yuyu respects the boundaries of Japanese cuisine while mixing in creativity for a distinctive spin. For the final item, flexibility is the order of the day, as guests can choose from rice with toppings, noodles, curry or a wide range of other options.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2411;Nijojo Furuta;Japan;Kyoto;371 Furushirocho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0045, Japan;35.012209;135.753872;78;false;false;Japanese;The chef’s menu boasts creativity and variations in tempo. Anticipating toasts with beer or champagne, fried foods are served early. Sashimi is accompanied with generous condiments, in the spirit of a salad. Fish is prepared simply – chargrilled or as sakamushi – to highlight the chef’s skill in selecting choice seafood.  As a proud Shiga Prefecture native, the chef stocks sake from that region and cooks rice grown by his uncle in Hira in clay pots from Shigaraki.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2412;Ajikitcho Horieten;Japan;Osaka;1-22-6 Kitahorie, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0014, Japan;34.673655;135.494016;57;true;true;Japanese;The name plate features calligraphy by Teiichi Yuki, the visionary who elevated the status of Japanese cuisine. An old bicycle, which the owner-chef once used to gather supplies, leans against a fence. Inside the house, built in the tea ceremony room style, the decor is simple and rustic. The owner, the restaurant’s second, inherited an orthodox kaiseki traditional meal style.  Appetiser platters, garnished with seasonal leaves, delight the eye. The cuisine follows the shifting seasons, creating a beautiful spectacle.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
2413;Sushi Matsumoto;Japan;Kyoto;570-123 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.003377;135.774437;75;false;true;Sushi;A small shop curtain hangs in an alleyway in Gion. Trained in Tokyo on the sushi techniques of old Edo, the owner-chef welcomes guests with the Edo greeting ‘Irasshaimashi!’ Scrupulously sourced toppings are formed with slightly salty red vinegar, orthodox through and through. White-fleshed fish are marinated in kombu, gizzard shad in vinegar. Other offerings include stewed clam and conger eel. To draw out the aromas of each topping, the menu progresses from light- to strong-flavoured items.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2414;Tenjaku;Japan;Kyoto;570 Botambokocho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8475, Japan;35.031403;135.741907;28;false;false;Tempura, Japanese;As the second owner of Tenjaku, Ryo Nishioka never forgets the spirit of his grandfather, who always made customers smile with his cuisine. The menu begins with an appetiser plate that reflects the mood of the season and proceeds to soup, decoratively arranged sashimi, and finally to tempura. The simple, familiar flavour of the tempura tofu, deep-fried and dressed in dipping sauce, warms the soul. The eve-catching hinoki cypress counter, made from a single plank, transforms the interior into a place of quiet dignity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
2416;Oryori Mashita;Japan;Kyoto;246 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.003944;135.773737;96;true;false;Japanese;A small shop curtain flutters along the Gion shopping street. Walk along the cobblestones sprinkled with water to a quiet location where you soon forget the noise of the high street. Seasonal ingredients and dining-ware weave together the beauty of Japanese cuisine. The menu of items connected to Japan’s festivals and ceremonies is part and parcel of Japanese culture. The sincerity behind everything from the appetiser to the tea puts the mind at ease, allowing diners to fully enjoy the flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2420;Yoshiko;Japan;Osaka;1-8-5 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697385;135.500176;68;false;true;Fugu / Pufferfish;In a previous life, this was a sushi shop. The second-generation owner-chef, preparing food at the counter left over from earlier days, apprenticed at a wholesaler, then at a ryotei, before hanging out his shop curtain as a fugu (puffer fish) chef. Wild-caught tora fugu arrive from Shimonoseki. Fugu sashimi arranged in a floral pattern called botan-zukuri is arrayed on celadon plates, and chirinabe hotpots followed by zosui rice gruel are prepared by the book. Patiently aged homemade ponzu sauce, appetisers of fugu skin or jellied fugu, and stone-grilled fugu show off the chef’s individuality and spirit.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
2421;Teruya;Japan;Osaka;2-1-24 Ueshio, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0064, Japan;34.66929;135.517727;36;true;true;Japanese;The care shown to guests by the couple who manage this kappo is heartwarming. The aroma and flavour of dashi soup stock are the focus of the fare, owing to the chef’s background in Kyoto cuisine. In the dashi of Osaka water and ma-kombu kelp, sweetness stands out. Salted and dried grey mullet roe is prepared at year’s end and served year-round, to be spread on iimushi, which is served between courses. Valuing simplicity, the chef creates impressions through combinations of ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2425;Noguchi Tsunagu;Japan;Kyoto;371-4 Kiyomotocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0084, Japan;35.005349;135.77446;49;true;true;Japanese;The menu alternates between omakase set menus and à la carte options. The evening begins with a procession of seasonal dishes, accompanied by wagyu stew rather than soup. Choose additional items from the menu or ask for a presentation of the ingredients of the day. White rice and miso soup wrap up the meal. We recommend the deliciousness of freshly cooked rice with accompaniments such as fried fish, fried chicken or braised pork.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2426;IDÉAL bistro;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-6-5 Tanimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0012, Japan;34.688864;135.517088;52;false;false;French;French cuisine and organic wine, presented by a nature-loving couple. Welcoming you into their parlour are the chef, a disciple of classic gastronomy, and the proprietress, a florist. To present the ideal bistro the name implies, the couple decorate the casual interior with flowers, fresh in season like the ingredients. Vegetables come from the good earth of their home farm in Wakayama, linking city and countryside through cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
2427;La Baie;Japan;Osaka;5F, The Ritz-Carlton, Osaka, 2-5-25 Umeda, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0001, Japan;34.698462;135.492663;40;false;false;French;A dining room fit for a noble mansion, décor of stunning symmetry and graceful service by the waitstaff create a moment cocooned in splendour. Commanding the kitchen is Christophe Gibert, a native of Bretagne. Accustomed to life by the sea, Gibert makes extensive use of seaweed. His preparations, with their strong accent on sauces, convey his spirit of respect for classic cooking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2428;Gion Nishimura;Japan;Kyoto;570-160 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.00274;135.775807;47;true;false;Japanese;The aim of this chef is to serve cuisine that is simple in appearance but makes a lasting impression. He places great store by elements the customer never sees, such as dashi combinations and knife techniques. In the eel and rolled omelette dressed in starchy sauce, for example, he creates synergistic effects by varying the dashi used for the omelette and the sauce. For the assortment of simmered vegetables, each vegetable is cut in a unique way, adding up to a harmonious whole. Customer demand has made the unforgettable sesame tofu and mackerel sushi standard dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2429;Godan Miyazawa;Japan;Kyoto;557 Oecho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8402, Japan;34.997973;135.760946;29;false;true;Japanese;The interior is meticulously styled in the manner of a teahouse. Wickerwork ceiling and earthen walls give an austere, rustic tenor. Cuisine is understated as well, suffused with the spirit of chakaiseki (the light meal served before tea ceremonies). Baked sesame tofu brings the flavours of the four seasons. Vegetables such as garden peas, maize, squash and turnip are kneaded into sesame tofu to herald the arrival of the season. Following tea-ceremony etiquette, rice is served the moment it finishes cooking and served thrice, varying the steaming time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2430;Nakazen;Japan;Kyoto;26 Kitashirakawa Kubotacho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8266, Japan;35.02874;135.79052;83;false;true;Japanese;The owner-chef’s mild demeanour puts us at ease. Generous portions are an expression of thanks for coming all the way out to Kitashirakawa. He hails from Ōhara, so that’s where he sources his vegetables. He obtains his seafood in season from Awaji and focuses all his talents on its preparation. Pike conger, offered in early summer, is singed and served on a block of ice for a refreshing presentation. In late autumn the appetiser is a medley of items, celebrating an abundant harvest.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2431;Kappo Hassun;Japan;Kyoto;95 Sueyoshicho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0085, Japan;35.004865;135.773774;41;false;false;Japanese;Behind a counter oozing Showa-era ambience, the chef plies his trade in his white smock and wooden clogs. As the second-generation chef of Kappo Hassun, he cherishes the history of Kyoto cuisine, populating his menu with dishes inherited from his father and foods associated with seasonal celebrations. Examples include assortments of sweet, steamed and layered egg cakes and burdock-root rolls, deep-fried tofu with thinly sliced veggies held together with hamo meat, and seasoned grilled fish. Gaining ideas from recipes he finds in literature, he brings old-style work to a new generation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2432;Sushi Sanshin;Japan;Osaka;2-7-14 Uchikyuhojimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0013, Japan;34.678144;135.518281;71;false;false;Sushi;Situated in a quiet residential district, Sushi Sanshin is open only at lunchtime. The naturally lit interior presents an austere charm. The chef is schooled in the old ways of sushi-making, but weaves in a few tricks of his own. For example, tiger prawn, filleted ‘double door’ style, is dressed prawn miso rather with than the conventional wasabi. The tamagoyaki, placed on top of the rice like a horse's saddle, hides a small amount of fish flakes underneath. Norimaki made with herbs to evoke vegetable flavours is a speciality found only here. Pursuit of the new, tempered by respect for the classics.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2433;Kokyu;Japan;Kyoto;204 Seiryucho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-0822, Japan;35.031138;135.769534;32;true;true;Japanese;In hope of conveying the feeling of Japanese culture through cuisine, Kokyu reflects scenes of ceremonies throughout the year in its culinary offerings. Appetisers in early spring are garnished with flowers, colourfully expressing the awakening breath of nature. In autumn, appetisers are arranged with taro, chestnuts and soybeans, in the traditional way to pray for a bumper harvest during the harvest moon. Spring water from a well in the restaurant's inner garden is used for dashi soup stock and thin tea. Attentive service warms the body and soul.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2434;Sushi Yuden;Japan;Osaka;3-8-25 Ueshio, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0002, Japan;34.666267;135.516768;21;false;false;Sushi;This is how we remember it: the chef at work behind the old-time sushi counter, in the customer’s line of sight. ‘Sushi is a traditional cuisine of Japan’, says Yuya Nishimura. True to the food culture of Osaka, which prizes freshness above all, Nishimura seeks out the finest of the catch at Kuromon Market with the eyes of a seasoned connoisseur. The ‘Yu’ in ‘Yuden’ is a Chinese character meaning ‘calm’ or ‘everlasting’. Nishimura carries on the traditions, techniques and spirit of sushi with a style indelibly his own.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2435;Sushi Murakami Jiro;Japan;Osaka;1-5-7 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697803;135.497285;66;false;false;Sushi;Twice every evening, the chef and his wife present ‘Murakami theatre’, a comedy act. This gregarious couple are the star attraction at their restaurant. The husband is a sushi craftsman, gathering fish from throughout Japan with a keen eye for quality. The soy sauce and red vinegar from sake lees are sourced from his hometown, as human connections are important to him. Working with focused passion, he starts the nigiri with marinated tuna. The repartee between husband and wife makes for a lively and friendly atmosphere. There’s no script for this performance, which soon has patrons grinning.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2436;Oimatsu Kitagawa;Japan;Osaka;4-12-27 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.6971652;135.5029123;23;true;true;Japanese;Toru Kitagawa is a reassuring presence behind the counter as he supervises his young crew. He dashes between counter and grill, sometimes overseeing, sometimes participating in food preparation, as occasion demands. The menu reflects a sensibility incubated in the kitchens of Kyoto and Osaka. For dashi soup stock with the taste of luxury, he uses Rishiri kombu kelp. Grilled items and stews are seasoned with miso and soy sauce to define their flavour profiles. Kitagawa brings the joy of dining to every table.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2437;Yakitori Torisen;Japan;Osaka;3F, 1-4-26 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.696189;135.498063;51;true;true;Yakitori;The ‘Japanese Jidori’ on the coasters means chicken breeds native to Japan. The chef takes pride in using only such chicken, never mixing them with foreign breeds. The concept here is to eat the entire bird. Rare cuts of chicken are shared between two diners, which is why reservations are only accepted for groups of two or more. To ensure that guests savour the richness of the chicken to the full, there are no dipping sauces. Respect for food producers and passion for yakitori pervade every aspect of Torisen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2438;DODICI;Japan;Kyoto;239 Kamihakusancho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0943, Japan;35.011866;135.765726;20;true;false;Italian;Prix fixe menus combine Italian gastronomic experience with Japanese ingredients, as showcased by the risotto of Japanese rice. Raw tofu lees and Daitokuji natto are uniquely Kyoto. The chef strives for a light palate, making eating a relaxed experience. Salt-pickled vegetables are made into sauces, and utilising the tartness of fermentation brings to mind Japanese cuisine. The open kitchen and the spacious, blue-walled dining room feel bright and fresh.;Air conditioning;[]
2439;La Biographie···;Japan;Kyoto;422-1 Tanakacho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8163, Japan;35.020156;135.742944;72;false;false;French;When he returned home to Japan, the chef was entrusted by legendary Parisian chef and restaurateur Alain Passard with carrying the torch of French cuisine for the next generation. As if to signal his determination to complete the mission, he showcases his techniques in an open kitchen, explaining what he is doing while sometimes adding stories. Egg cuisine is an homage to Passard. The name serves notice that the restaurant is to be his legacy, as does his keen-eyed supervision of his kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2440;Yakitori Ichimatsu;Japan;Osaka;1-5-1 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.695938;135.49702;100;false;false;Yakitori;On the theme of ‘playing with fire’, the chef finds ingenious variations on flame and preparation, resulting in yakitori full of variation and surprises. Smoky aromas billow from wing tips grilled over a wood flame. Helmeted guinea fowl, deep-fried with minimal oil, is an idea borrowed from tempura. Duck is char-grilled and swaddled in ankake sauce. Chicken paté and fruit skewers cleanse the palate between courses. You never know what’s coming next, and that’s part of the fun.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2441;Ayanokoji Karatsu;Japan;Kyoto;113-1 Yadacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8442, Japan;35.002416;135.755563;66;true;false;Japanese;An amiable couple from Nagasaki run this restaurant. The husband, an admirer of Kyoto cuisine, left his family’s kappo restaurant to gain experience in Kyoto. As he studied ways to present food, he fell in love with the bounty of ingredients available and decided to go independent. His habit is to visit producing regions, securing fresh ingredients in season, such as picking wild edible plants and mushrooms in Miyama and angling for sweetfish in Shiga. Under the tutelage of a potter, he makes his own ceramics, on which the couple serve their culinary creations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2442;Doppo;Japan;Kyoto;1-1 Izumoji Matsunoshitacho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8133, Japan;35.042915;135.762222;74;true;false;Japanese;‘Doppo’, meaning ‘unique’, references a tract by Rosanjin Kitaoji. Masato Miyazawa was deeply impressed by the legendary epicure’s pursuit of beauty in all its manifestations. Seasonal furnishings in ceremonial spaces, a lovingly tended garden and antique dinnerware speak of Miyazawa’s devotion to Japanese culture. The cuisine is inventive and often playful. Hand-rolled soba sushi and decorative sashimi of tuna paired with unfiltered sake are signs of a free-ranging imagination.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2443;Mizuno;Japan;Kyoto;245-2 Nakanocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0082, Japan;35.006275;135.775651;37;false;true;Japanese;Mizuno is ‘a shop with good food’ but also a restaurant that never forgets the classics. Yuan’yaki, a grilled fish dish dreamed up by a tea ceremony master includes ginger and onions as ‘secret ingredients’. Partway through the meal, diners are shown the luxury ingredients they’ll soon be enjoying. Bamboo shoots in spring, sweetfish in summer, spiny lobster in autumn, crab in winter are all beautifully prepared in front of the customers. Eel and wagyu, char-grilled, is served with rice salt-and-kombu kelp butter is a clever twist and an excellent accompaniment for the rice.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2445;Nishijin Fujiyoshi;Japan;Kyoto;626-14 Kamitenjincho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-0082, Japan;35.036441;135.751001;87;true;false;Japanese;The ingredients have to be seen to be believed. The owner-chef, Yoshikatsu Imai, personally goes to fetch the water used for cooking. Attentive service to his customers, he says, is one of his joys of life. He also spends great time and effort on his menu. For example, the ma-kombu is drawn over a period of days, for a wonderfully rich umami. The natural flavours of the fish and vegetable dishes served in small vessels go beautifully with the dashi, forming a complete whole.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
2446;Kyo Seika;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 36-3 Okazaki Enshojicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8344, Japan;35.011709;135.780681;94;true;true;Chinese;Shizuo Miyamoto’s quest is for his own style of Chinese cooking with a seasonal aesthetic. Fish in season is stir-fried with chilli peppers. Spring rolls are wrapped in three types of ingredients, so each mouthful tastes different from the one before. Counter seating, right in front of the kitchen, builds diners’ anticipation amidst the clatter of woks and aroma of food. ‘Kyo Seika’ is an abbreviation meaning ‘Chinese cuisine, by Shizuo Miyamoto, in Kyoto’. A concise summation of the offerings by the husband-and-wife team.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2447;Gion Kajisho;Japan;Kyoto;570-127 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002705;135.775145;35;true;true;Japanese;Making Kyoto cuisine accessible to all is the goal of this chef and proprietress. ‘Kajisho’ combines the husband’s surname with his wife’s maiden name, signifying their bond of matrimony. Rolled omelette preserves the legacy of popular delivery items and box lunches from the chef’s apprentice days while recreating the air of a kappo. Seafood sourced from Nagasaki and Goto-udon noodles convey the flavours of the couple’s hometown. À la carte items such as braised pork and chawanmushi are offered in the evening.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
2448;Oimatsu Hisano;Japan;Osaka;4-8-3 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697005;135.504137;52;false;true;Japanese;To stick close to the seasons with his cuisine, the chef gathers flavours from every part of Japan. Sourcing rare vegetables and fruits testifies to his boundless curiosity. The menu is full of creative flair to delight diners. Eschewing the customary dependence on soy sauce, sashimi platters are paired with fish-broth dipping sauce. Freshly cooked rice is seasoned with salt and soy sauce to elicit a pure sweetness. The chef experiments with novel techniques, but always respects the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2450;Noni;Malta;Valletta;211 Republic Street, Valletta, VLT 1118, Malta;35.9005092;14.5160236;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;What was once the home of ‘Xmun Borg & Sons Bakery & Confectionery’ has transformed into an equally charming restaurant. You can enjoy a quiet meal on the ground floor or opt for a livelier atmosphere by heading downstairs, past the kitchen, to the stylish, stone-walled cellar. The restaurant’s moniker comes from the nickname of owner-chef Jonathan Brincat, who brings a refined, modern touch to traditional Maltese and Mediterranean cuisine. His visually appealing, well-balanced dishes are crafted with precision and attention to detail. To minimize waste and offer unique flavors, the restaurant features only a tasting menu that highlights seasonal and fresh ingredients. This sustainable approach extends to the wellbeing of the staff, who have access to local therapists, and the support of local producers. Additionally, the restaurant offers an extensive selection of drinks and cocktails made from sustainable ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
2451;De Mondion;Malta;Mdina;Council Square, Mdina, MDN 1050, Malta;35.8851399;14.4046065;51;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The luxurious Xara Palace Hotel is set in a 16C building in the heart of the beautiful walled city of Mdina where, on the top floor, you’ll find this intimate, elegantly dressed restaurant featuring impressive artwork from around the island. If you’re here in the summer, a table on the terrace is a must, thanks to the stunning views extending across the east of the island to the coast. The cooking is technically adept and the combinations are well-judged, with menus showcasing the best of the island’s produce in sophisticated, classically based Mediterranean dishes – Scottona beef fillet is a speciality. Herbs and vegetables are sourced from the restaurant’s own garden which is cultivated sustainably in accordance with the principles of regenerative agriculture. The impressive wine list offers a broad choice with some great quality vintages – it’s worth asking the sommelier for recommendations from their selection of local wines. Despite the hotel’s sumptuous style, service remains friendly and not overly formal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2452;Bahia;Malta;Balzan;De Paule Avenue, San Anton, Balzan, BZN 9023, Malta;35.8944725;14.4491412;71;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;Occupying an intimate small dining room on the first floor of the elegant Corinthia Palace Hotel, this restaurant offers two tasting menus (“The villages journey” and “Plant Based”), as well as an à la carte priced according to the number of dishes ordered. The cuisine is inspired by local culture (not just gastronomic), taking guests on an extended journey through the island’s different villages with a note relating to the relevant village accompanying each dish. Despite having its roots firmly based in local tradition, the cuisine looks resolutely to the future.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2453;Under Grain;Malta;Valletta;167 Merchants Street, Valletta, VLT 1174, Malta;35.8989233;14.5154686;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Enter the Rosselli Hotel and descend via the lift to this elegant cellar restaurant, where you walk past the kitchen before entering into a dining room with a vaulted stone ceiling and dark, moody décor. Under Grain is inspired by Merchant Street’s former tailor shops and evidence of this theme is all around, from the sewing pattern menu to the clothing displays – and even a pin-cushion bill-holder.As a tailor would create something exquisite from cloth, the chef here does the same with fine ingredients, skilfully applying his talent to produce a beautiful end product. Expertly cooked Mediterranean dishes burst with bold, gloriously harmonious flavours and, while their base may be classic, the overtones are modern. Professional, personable service and a relaxed atmosphere add to the experience. The wine list is well-chosen and contains plenty of gems from the world, especially from Italy and France.;Air conditioning;[]
2454;Fernandõ Gastrotheque;Malta;Sliema;17 Tigne Street, Sliema, SLM 3172, Malta;35.9099793;14.5069007;24;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;This small restaurant arranged over two floors on one of Sliema’s quiet side streets is one of Malta’s culinary hotspots! Here, chef Hiram Cassar serves modern and sustainable cuisine full of flavour and based on classic recipes. His delicious fusion dishes combine Mediterranean and Asian influences and include options such as fresh fish escabeche with dashi, leek and smoked pike roe, and mushroom and white miso chawanmushi with a potato and tarragon emulsion and vin jaune. The efficient service also extends to the excellent wine recommendations from an impressive wine list featuring over 700 different labels, with wines such as Sassicaia and Gaja available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2455;Rosamì;Malta;St Julian's;The Vila, Main Street, Balluta Bay, St Julian's, STJ 1017, Malta;35.9143291;14.493543;82;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Overlooking Balluta bay, Rosamì is a beautiful Maltese-style villa that is home to a classic, elegant and decidedly romantic restaurant. Here, the chef and his team prepare modern dishes with an international flavour proposed in two carte blanche menus (6 and 8 courses) inspired by seasonal and local ingredients that change on a daily basis. The wine list includes labels from around the world as well as local wines, with an excellent selection also available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2456;edl.eins;Germany;Deggendorf;Edlmairstraße 1, Deggendorf, 94469, Germany;48.831168;12.9575939;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine, French;The location is a draw in itself! Named after its address in Edlmairstraße 1, the restaurant is housed on the ninth floor of the Karl Turm high-rise office building. The interior is modern and elegant, with decorative touches such as striking lampshades suspended from an industrial-style ceiling and floor-to-ceiling windows that afford a sensational view of the historical old town and the Danube – the sunsets are wonderful. The integrated bar in the entrance area is the ideal place for an aperitif. The French-influenced modern cooking style is exemplified in dishes such as carabinero with carrot, curry and kaffir lime. You can opt for a set menu comprising five or six courses (with wine pairings on request) or order à la carte.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2457;Eckert;Germany;Grenzach-Wyhlen;Basler Straße 20, Grenzach-Wyhlen, 79639, Germany;47.5532458;7.658225;44;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This fine dining restaurant is as chic as the designer hotel of the same name. Whether in the conservatory or the lounge area, the modern, minimalist decor feels both cosy and stylish. In the kitchen, young chef-patron Nicolai Peter Wiedmer demonstrates his mastery of classic cookery as well as his creative flair – he also likes to incorporate Asian flavours. In the evening, the set menu ("Lieblings Momente") can also be served in a vegan version. At lunchtime, two smaller tasting menus (one vegan) are served, as well as the business lunch. The fabulous wine list comprises around 450 labels, with recommendations to pair with the set menu. In summer, head out to the lovely terrace.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2458;midi;Germany;Sankt Ingbert;Ernst-Heckel-Straße 4, Sankt Ingbert, 66386, Germany;49.2746882;7.1556823;22;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in an industrial estate, this restaurant lays on a reasonably priced buffet at lunchtime on weekdays, hence its name ("midi" is French for "midday"). In the evenings, talented chef Peter Wirbel takes charge, bringing along a wealth of expertise gained at top-flight establishments in the region. He produces delicately balanced dishes brimming with flavour, using locally sourced ingredients whenever possible. An eight-course set menu of amuse-bouches dedicated to the Bliesgau region is served on Tuesdays, and they showcase their "Plats Signatures" in a four-course set menu on Wednesdays. On Fridays and Saturdays, there is the "Midi" menu comprising up to six courses, and the three-course set menu "Rund um die Biosphäre". On Sunday lunchtimes you can order à la carte. The waitstaff are very friendly and well trained - the chef is also on hand to elucidate his culinary concept. Tip: tasty treats to take home are on sale at the Biosphärenmarkt.;Air conditioning;[]
2459;Erbprinz;Germany;Ettlingen;Rheinstraße 1, Ettlingen, 76275, Germany;48.941273;8.4045683;51;false;true;Classic Cuisine, International;Hotel Erbprinz is definitely something of an institution in the Karlsruhe area – and not only for the many conference participants who stay here. This is a foodie hotspot that prides itself on its stylish interior and excellent cuisine – the domain of Ralph Knebel and team. They cook classic dishes that draw on international influences, with an emphasis on seasonal produce. The quality of the ingredients is outstanding. There is a set menu comprising five to seven courses that can also be ordered à la carte. Incidentally, Ralph Knebel's wife, Jasmina, is also on board, producing fabulous desserts in her role as head pastry chef. In summer, the gorgeous flower-decked terrace is a delightful spot in which to enjoy a leisurely meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
2460;Colombi Restaurant Zirbelstube;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Rotteckring 16, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79098, Germany;47.9971187;7.8475694;64;true;true;Classic French, Mediterranean Cuisine;One of the great classics of South Baden gastronomy is located in the internationally renowned Colombi Hotel and, in Henrik Weiser and Sven Usinger, boasts two chefs with experience of Michelin-starred kitchens. French classics are showcased here, prepared with feeling and finesse, and excellent ingredients. There is a set menu with four, five or six courses which you can also choose à la carte. In addition, there is the elegant yet inviting atmosphere of the Zirbelstube with its beautiful wood panelling (which inspired its name). Sit back and relax in the comfortable Falkenstube, which oozes traditional charm. The wine list is excellent!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2461;Philipp Soldan;Germany;Frankenberg;Marktplatz 2, Frankenberg, 35066, Germany;51.0592063;8.8016187;26;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The three lovingly restored historical houses in the middle of the charming old town are really something to behold. Here, the tasteful Hotel Sonne has various catering options, including this restaurant. The fine dining restaurant in the basement of the centuries-old Stadtweinhaus is chic, modern and pleasantly laid back. (If you are not coming from the hotel, you get to the restaurant via Untermarkt.) In the open kitchen, Erik Arnecke oversees the preparation of a creative five-course set menu. Dishes such as North Sea plaice with Irish rock oyster, bacon emulsion and watercress cream are brimming with harmoniously combined flavours. Upgrades include Japanese Wagyu beef and an international selection of cheeses. There is a good choice of wines. Tip for fine dining novices: come on a Sunday afternoon for the three-course set menu. In case you were wondering, Philipp Soldan is the sculptor, whose carved wooden figures adorn the town hall.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2462;Le Flair;Germany;Düsseldorf;Marc-Chagall-Straße 108, Düsseldorf, 40477, Germany;51.2393543;6.7943034;79;true;true;French;Located near Maurice Ravel Park, this is a minimalist-style restaurant with a touch of elegance. It is run by chef-patron Dany Cerf, who hails from French-speaking Switzerland and previously cooked up a storm under Jean-Claude Bourgueil and at renowned establishments such as the Baur au Lac in Zurich. He and partner Nicole Bänder opened Le Flair in 2014. Here he bowls diners over with his "Menu du Moment", which showcases his modern, pleasantly pared-down and well-thought-out dishes, for example: Hamachi tartare, lemon, harissa. You can choose to have four or five courses, with an optional cheese course. As well as wine, there are non-alcoholic beverage accompaniments available. Head straight for the fabulous terrace in summer.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2464;GOLVET;Germany;Berlin;Potsdamer Straße 58, Berlin, 10785, Germany;52.5055114;13.3676288;46;false;true;Creative;Stepping out of the lift on the eighth floor of the Loeser & Wolff building, you will immediately be impressed by the sensational view over Potsdamer Platz and the city. Set up in the rooms of the former 40 Seconds Club, this spacious restaurant is really stylish and boasts a bar. You can watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen from the seats at the counter. There is also an impressive wine list featuring small organic producers. Alternatively, you could opt for the house-made kombucha. Fantastic service.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2465;Bandol sur mer;Germany;Berlin;Torstraße 167, Berlin, 10115, Germany;52.5290651;13.3953009;68;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Sie würden in diesem ungezwungen-legeren Restaurant mit "shabby Chic" keine Sterneküche erwarten? Zugegeben, der kleine Raum - übrigens ein ehemaliger Dönerladen - kommt schon etwas „rough“ daher: Das Interieur ist dunkel gehalten und sehr schlicht, die blanken Tische stehen recht eng, dazu individuelle Einrichtungs-Details, teilweise aus der DDR. In der offenen Küche zeigt Andreas Saul  bemerkenswerte Leidenschaft, Präzision, Originalität und Kreativität. Er kocht mit Bezug zur Region und ist dabei ganz schön innovativ. Wie finden Sie z. B. "Charcuterie von der Karotte"? Hier gibt's - wie sonst bei Salami üblich - mit Edelpilz verfeinerte Karotte. Man fermentiert auch gerne und räuchert selbst. Auch fernöstliche Einflüsse wie Kimchi finden sich. Das Menü ist sehr durchdacht und steckt voller einzigartiger Aromen. Die fünf vegetarischen Gängen können um zwei weitere Gänge mit Fisch/Fleisch ergänzt werden. Schöne Wein- oder alkoholfreie Begleitung. Fazit: richtig hohes Niveau gepaart mit sympathischer Bodenständigkeit.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2466;La Société;Germany;Cologne;Kyffhäuser Straße 53, Cologne, 50674, Germany;50.9285296;6.9372169;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Everything is just right in this small fine dining restaurant in the student quarter of Kwartier Latäng, from the service to the ambience to the cuisine. Not only has it been given a tasteful, modern facelift, but the chef is also a new addition. Since August 2021, Leon Hofmockel has been bringing his own fresh ideas to the table. With consummate skill, he conjures up subtle contrasts, plays with acidity and textures and creates a beautiful balance. The result is intelligently structured dishes full of surprising flavours. Meanwhile, the service is second to none: in a friendly, lively atmosphere, the dedicated team has a cordial and courteous approach to each guest – everyone clearly enjoys what they are doing, which simply cannot fail to put you in a good mood!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2469;VILLINO;Germany;Lindau;Mittenbuch 6, Lindau, 88131, Germany;47.567314;9.673153;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences;From the stylish, airy, high-ceilinged restaurant, which is reminiscent of an orangery, to the charming inner courtyard with a fountain, this pretty property set amid the orchards has an almost Mediterranean feel. It's a real family affair here, enthusiastically run by hostess Sonja Fischer, her daughter Alisa and her brother Rainer Hörmann, a trained sommelier. The front-of-house team provides professional, cordial service, and savvy wine recommendations – and the lady of the house is always present too. Toni Neumann's cuisine is clearly influenced by Mediterranean – principally Italian – cuisine, and also draws on inspiration from Asia. There are three set menus to choose from: "Villino Tradizionale", "Cucina della Passione" and "Cucina Naturale" (vegetarian). Their signature dish is the "Asian mixed appetiser". Tip: Stay overnight in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2470;Landhaus Feckl;Germany;Ehningen;Keltenweg 1, Ehningen, 71139, Germany;48.661195;8.9547833;74;true;false;Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine;Manuela and Franz Feckl are truly exemplary hosts. They have been running their establishment since 1985 and their dedication is plain to see – not least when it comes to the food. The dishes display a sure touch and stand out for their premium ingredients and first-rate technical skill. The cuisine is predominantly classic French but includes some beloved regional specialities. Both a low-carb and a vegetarian version of the set menu are available. The reasonably priced lunch deal is also popular. Wine lovers will appreciate the good selection here, which features one or two rarities. The elegant country-house style makes for an appealing atmosphere on the restaurant floor, which has cosy seating niches – from the window seats you can look out over the fields. The friendly lady of the house is also part of the service team. There are pretty guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2471;Im Schiffchen;Germany;Düsseldorf;Kaiserswerther Markt 9, Düsseldorf, 40489, Germany;51.3015121;6.7338663;84;false;false;Classic Cuisine;If we're talking about Michelin-starred cuisine in a beautiful Baroque brick building on Kaiserswerther Markt, we can only be talking about Jean-Claude Bourgueil's Im Schiffchen. At the helm since 1977, he is without a doubt the doyen of Düsseldorf's fine dining scene. Together with his tried-and-trusted kitchen team, Bourgueil delivers creative French cuisine. Whether it be lobster, game or Wagyu beef, the produce is of the finest quality. To complete the picture, there's the impressive selection of wines, the attentive and well-trained wait staff and the gorgeous decor – this ground-floor restaurant has a tasteful maritime look.;Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
2472;Laudensacks Gourmet Restaurant;Germany;Bad Kissingen;Kurhausstraße 28, Bad Kissingen, 97688, Germany;50.1908345;10.0777456;81;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;In keeping with the rest of Laudensacks Parkhotel & Retreat, the fine dining restaurant is a vision of tasteful elegance. The kitchen here has retained its Michelin star since 1994. For many years now, this has been the domain of Frederik Desch, whose cooking style successfully blends classic culinary tradition and modern innovation. He makes good use of first-rate produce such as Rhön salmon trout or local venison, showcasing his ability to bring their individual flavours to the fore. The wine list features Franconian, regional and international labels. In summer, you can enjoy the fine food and cordial service, including savvy wine recommendations, out on the gorgeous terrace overlooking the grounds. Good to know: They also hold various culinary events.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2473;Landhaus Scherrer;Germany;Hamburg;Elbchaussee 130, Hamburg, 22763, Germany;53.5459914;9.9170486;64;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Heinz O. Wehmann is to Landhaus Scherrer (which has a spruce new exterior!) what St Michael's Church is to Hamburg! Since 1980 he has been head chef in this restaurant that was opened by Armin and Emmi Scherrer in 1976 (and awarded one, and at times even two MICHELIN stars as of 1978). For years the outstanding regional, often organically certified produce has been par for the course here. As classic as the interior – the large-format erotic painting remains the decorative focus! – are also the dishes. The Holstein venison, served with an excellent rosemary sauce, for instance, is absolutely fantastic. The wine cellar, which has grown to over 10 000 bottles, is also impressive! The service is attentive and professional, but by no means stuffy. For an alternative to gourmet cuisine, head to Wehmann's Bistro for good regional dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2474;KARRisma;Germany;Lindau;Alter Schulplatz 1, Lindau, 88131, Germany;47.5474074;9.6854321;74;false;true;Creative, Farm to table;Temporarily closed.Part of the Adara hotel, this is an elegant little restaurant with a modern and inviting interior – the eye-catching decor includes numerous mirrors on the wall. The management is cordial and personable: chef Julian Karr not only cooks, he is also involved in the service. His cuisine is creative and seasonal, and the quality of the ingredients is second to none.  A nice example: Lake Constance pikeperch, spinach leaves, Jerusalem artichokes as foam and vegetables. Tip: The restaurant offers its own wine to accompany the set menu, which changes on a regular basis. Set in the old town, the terrace is lovely. Tip: Leave your car in P4 multi-storey car park, just a short walk away.;Terrace;[]
2475;Bieberbau;Germany;Berlin;Durlacher Straße 15, Berlin, 10715, Germany;52.4796363;13.3336378;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;For those who appreciate not only really good food but also a fantastic setting, this is the place to be! Dating back to 1894, this listed building has been wonderfully restored – Richard Bieber's stucco craftsmanship in the dining area is truly worth seeing! In this unique location, diners are looked after by a friendly and competent service team led by hostess and sommelier Anne Garkisch, while chef-patron Stephan Garkisch cooks up modern dishes at the Molteni stove. He skilfully showcases herbs and spices in his set menus (one is vegetarian), with much of the produce coming from his own garden. Good value for money.;Terrace;[]
2476;Ursprung;Germany;Königsbronn;Struthstraße 17, Königsbronn, 89551, Germany;48.7296752;10.0651509;54;true;true;Creative, Country cooking;Andreas and Anna Widmann (the eighth generation of the family to run this place) have two restaurants, and this is the fine dining option - located in the oldest part of Widmann's Löwen, where the village butcher's shop used to be. On the menu, Swabian tradition meets sophisticated culinary skill. Sourced from local producers, premium ingredients are used in dishes brimming with creativity, flavour and original ideas. There is a set menu of five or seven courses. A trained sommelier, your friendly hostess provides judicious wine suggestions. There are also guestrooms for an overnight stay, plus a shop selling dishes and delicatessen wares to take away.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2478;Tisane;Germany;Nuremberg;Augustinerhof 1, Nuremberg, 90403, Germany;49.4540833;11.0758388;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Located in the chic Augustinerhof building complex in the old town, this is a cool and trendy "chef's table restaurant". Interaction between chefs and diners is a key part of the concept: the open kitchen is the centrepiece, and diners sit at a striking natural stone counter. You experience first-hand how René Stein (previously at Schwarzer Adler) and his team prepare a modern, creative set menu comprising pleasantly pared-down dishes made from first-rate ingredients – pre-order the vegetarian version.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2479;Ratsstuben;Germany;Haltern am See;Mühlenstraße 3, Haltern am See, 45721, Germany;51.7434347;7.1874286;95;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;In the middle of the old town, a stone's throw from Marktplatz and the striking Kirche St Sixtus, is the small Ratshotel. Not only does it have attractive, comfortable guestrooms, but it also boasts an appealing restaurant. Chef-patron Daniel Georgiev prepares a modern set menu using select produce and drawing on international influences. On Tue-Thu there is an additional surprise menu. The excellent wine list features over 300 labels including a decent champagne selection. Friendly, attentive, and professional service come courtesy of charming hostess Petra Georgieva and team. The interior is chic and elegant with a walk-in wine climate cabinet that is sure to draw the eye. For a more down-to-earth alternative, head to Gute Stube for steaks etc.;Air conditioning;[]
2480;Lech-Line;Germany;Landsberg am Lech;Bahnhofsplatz 1, Landsberg am Lech, 86899, Germany;48.0473043;10.8721887;72;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;In the evening, this former railway station building proposes fine dining in an appealingly trendy and informal atmosphere. Christian Sauer serves up a modern take on international cuisine, working with great precision and steering clear of unnecessary frills. High-quality produce is used to create coherent, flavourful dishes that, for all their complexity, retain an air of simplicity. "Gourmet Bistro" is the name of the à la carte menu, which features, for example, ceviche (with fish from Birnbaum fish farm), lime, avocado, chilli, cucumber and coriander. On Fridays and Saturdays, there is also a five-course set menu that changes every month. Tip: Have a cocktail at the bar.;Car park;[]
2481;Maerz - Das Restaurant;Germany;Bietigheim-Bissingen;Kronenbergstraße 14, Bietigheim-Bissingen, 74321, Germany;48.9609392;9.1290315;64;false;false;Creative French, Modern Cuisine;Modern tastes meet regional flair! Brothers Benjamin and Christian Maerz successfully blend both in the fine dining restaurant of their Hotel Rose, hitting the mark in two different respects. First, the interior with its gorgeous wood panelling and clear lines makes for a chic and fashionable yet cosy ambience. The cuisine, too, draws on regional culinary tradition as well as contemporary trends, in the form of a set menu dubbed "Heimweh/Fernweh". The chef uses the finest ingredients sourced from the local area, and seasonings from all over the globe, cleverly married in dishes such as locally caught sturgeon a la plancha with burnt cream and shiro dashi. Christian Maerz will be happy to talk you through the wines or non-alcoholic options. There is a pleasant lounge terrace on which to enjoy a pre- or after-dinner drink.;Car park;[]
2482;Hugos;Germany;Berlin;Budapester Straße 2, Berlin, 10787, Germany;52.506852;13.3455401;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The magnificent view and the chic interior make Hugos, laid out on the 14th floor of the InterContinental hotel, a highly appealing location in the capital. Soft lighting, elegant furnishings and candlelight make for a relaxed and romantic atmosphere. Chef Eberhard Lange's culinary creations more than live up to the attractive setting: in his eight-course set menu (which can be reduced to six courses), he showcases his precise technical skill with classic dishes which he sets off with a modern twist. You are sure to find the perfect accompaniment on the wine list, which comprises around 500 labels. Tip: treat yourself to an aperitif at the bar before dinner.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2483;Pietsch;Germany;Wernigerode;Breite Straße 53a, Wernigerode, 38855, Germany;51.8352945;10.7890106;100;true;false;Creative, Japanese;An interesting modern dining concept. It all kicks off at 7.30pm when the guests for the evening arrive. At 7.45pm service begins. There is only a single seven-course set menu (with additional amuse-bouche and final course) showcasing a global palate with strong Asian influences and delivering bold, distinct flavours. Diners are seated at a counter with 18 spaces facing the open kitchen and can watch chef Luis Hendricks and his team in action. This set-up, where you can witness teamwork at its finest and sense the enthusiasm, fosters a sociable and enjoyable ambiance that aligns well with the trendy urban aesthetic. Tip: As well as wines, there are expertly crafted non-alcoholic beverage pairings – highly recommended! Zeitwerk, another restaurant by Robin Pietsch, is right next door.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2484;Traube;Germany;Efringen-Kirchen;Alemannenstraße 19, Efringen-Kirchen, 79588, Germany;47.6909385;7.5398759;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A beautiful historical house in the small wine-growing village of Blansingen. The couple who run the place have plenty of experience in high-end gastronomy (Maaemo in Oslo, La Vie in Osnabrück), and it's immediately obvious that professionals are at work here. Headed up by the charming Daniela Hasse, the front-of-house team is pleasantly informal, chatty and highly professional. Canadian-born head chef Brian Wawryk never fails to impress with his meticulous craftsmanship and well-balanced dishes. His modern cuisine is creative and focuses on regional products, including ingredients preserved the year before. Insider tip: in winter, try to bag yourself the small table in the "Kuschelecke" ("cosy corner") by the tiled stove! The leafy terrace beckons in summer. Bear in mind that Traube is also a great place to stay overnight.;Car park;[]
2485;Admiral;Germany;Weisenheim am Berg;Leistadter Straße 6, Weisenheim am Berg, 67273, Germany;49.5126055;8.1545397;62;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;An institution in the region, this is a truly charming restaurant, which the owners have been running with dedication for over 10 years now. Chef-patron Holger Stehr serves up his interesting take on modern cuisine in the form of a five- to eight-course set menu, skilfully combining building on classic French foundations with Far Eastern-Japanese influences. Diners are welcomed by hostess Martina Kraemer-Stehr, who is trained as a sommelier and responsible for the friendly and proficient service. The wine list and recommendations are also compelling – you can look forward to wines by the glass that are beautifully matched to the individual dishes on the set menu. Tip: Consider booking the pretty guestroom in the charming sandstone pavilion set in the Admiral Garden. In summer, it is also pleasant to dine on the romantic terrace laid out here in the garden.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2486;Ente;Germany;Wiesbaden;Kaiser-Friedrich-Platz 3, Wiesbaden, 65183, Germany;50.0849814;8.2438995;92;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;This is the epitome of classic fine dining! The luxurious Nassauer Hof grand hotel dating from 1813 provides the stylish setting for the elegant Ente. Diners sit at exquisitely set tables laid out over two levels – a curved staircase with wrought-iron bannisters leads up to the gallery – to savour Michael Kammermeier's modern take on classic cuisine. The dishes are well thought out and meticulously crafted using the finest ingredients and organised into two set menus: "Küchenrunde" and "Querbeet". A duck set menu (for two) comprising three courses can be ordered in advance. The service certainly lives up to the high standards set by the kitchen team: led by Jimmy Ledemazel, the waitstaff are attentive, personable and well trained. You might like to head to the terrace laid out to the front of the building.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2487;Alte Überfahrt;Germany;Werder;Fischerstraße 48b, Werder, 14542, Germany;52.3797969;12.9449636;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This place boasts a delightful setting on the waterside promenade of a small island in the Havel and the restaurant itself is equally attractive with its upscale, modern and elegant interior and almost intimate atmosphere, beautiful terrace by the lake. Then there is the creative cuisine made of regional and seasonal products. It is best to order a vegetarian menu when making your reservation. The dishes are characterised by their precise technical skill, clear structure and beautiful sense of balance – it is plain to see that head chef Thomas Hübner has already plied his trade in some of Germany and Italy's top restaurants. Owner Patrick Schwatke – himself a Michelin-starred chef – runs the show front of house, adding a personal touch to proceedings.;Terrace;[]
2488;Bagatelle;Germany;Trier;Zurlaubener Ufer 78, Trier, 54292, Germany;49.7648216;6.6349596;29;true;false;French Contemporary, Creative;Chef Gerald Schöberl (previously sous-chef for Michelin-starred chef Christian Bau) and his team have brought a breath of fresh air to Bagatelle, a restaurant that has been around for years. Using regional produce alongside top-notch ingredients such as marine fish and lobster, the modern cuisine successfully melds together classic French influences and interesting Japanese accents. The result is sophisticated dishes with beautiful depth – for diners to savour in the smart interior. Friendly, charming service. Take a seat on the delightful sheltered terrace and take in the view of the Moselle just a stone's throw away.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2489;Nobelhart & Schmutzig;Germany;Berlin;Friedrichstraße 218, Berlin, 10969, Germany;52.5051559;13.3906005;71;false;true;Creative, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant on Friedrichstraße may look unassuming but it has a unique philosophy. Proprietor and sommelier Billy Wagner and head chef Micha Schäfer prize the ingredients and the way they are sourced above all else. It goes without saying, then, that they use only the finest seasonal produce – from the region, of course. They even make their own butter. They may have adapted their menu from 10 reduced-portion courses to six slightly larger courses (eg haricot beans, lovage, Heggelbach cheese or lamb, leek, potato), but they remain true to their sustainable concept. The chefs are happy to talk you through their sophisticated dishes, whether at your table or the counter by the open kitchen – these seats are in particularly high demand, by the way! The set menu is accompanied by extremely interesting wines, beers and distillates. Tip: Come Tue-Thu for a more inexpensive meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2491;Jan Diekjobst Restaurant;Germany;Detmold;Lange Straße 19, Detmold, 32756, Germany;51.9338413;8.878516;50;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Dating from 16C, Detmolder Hof not only offers comfortable accommodation in a classically elegant setting, but it is also home to Jan Diekjobst's fine dining restaurant, which has become the real centrepiece of the hotel. After stints at Victor's FINE DINING by Christian Bau in Perl-Nennig and The Table Kevin Fehling in Hamburg, among others, here the chef cooks up a modern take on classic cuisine that attracts throngs of diners. In addition to excellent food, there is very friendly service and a tasteful interior with high ceilings, a striking chandelier, a large mirror and fine floorboards, as well as an open kitchen – all of which makes for a genuinely charming and lively atmosphere. In summer, the terrace in front of the house is a great place to sit.;Terrace;[]
2492;ROTER HAHN by Maximilian Schmidt;Germany;Regensburg;Rote-Hahnen-Gasse 10, Regensburg, 93047, Germany;49.0189139;12.0934977;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This townhouse in the heart of Regensburg has a long history behind it. It has been an inn for centuries, with the earliest written record of it dating back to the 13C. Maximilian Schmidt now represents the third generation of the family to take the helm. In a pleasingly informal atmosphere, they serve up modern cuisine that draws on the best of what the region has to offer, but also seeks inspiration in French and Asian culinary traditions. The highlight is the evening set menu, which comprises five or eight courses, but you can also dine à la carte. On Fridays and Saturdays there is a smaller set menu at midday. Should you wish to stay overnight, individually decorated guestrooms are available in the hotel.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2493;Speiseberg;Germany;Halle (saale);Kröllwitzer Straße 45, Halle (saale), 06120, Germany;51.50501;11.95119;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;You will need to factor in plenty of time, but a meal here in the restaurant of the traditional Bergschenke – a Halle institution – is a real experience! Previously sous-chef at Speiseberg, Christoph Baumgartner has taken the helm in the kitchen and is gradually putting his own unique stamp on the menu. A single eight-course set menu is served, showcasing unique dishes made with the finest ingredients. The serving of the set menu begins at 7.15pm for all guests (max. 12 people per evening), in the modern, rather minimalist interior of this restaurant that enjoys a fabulous location overlooking the Saale River. The friendly and professional front-of-house team talk you through the dishes in detail. In fine weather, you can enjoy your aperitif outside and take in stunning views of Giebichenstein Castle. You can get to Bergschenke via the steps or take the road leading up from behind the premises.;Car park;[]
2494;Le Frankenberg;Germany;Weigenheim;Schloß Frankenberg 1, Weigenheim, 97215, Germany;49.608438;10.2661417;59;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;What an incredible spot! Guests cross a bridge to reach the lavishly restored Schloss Frankenberg, which enjoys a beautiful elevated location. As well as incorporating a hotel and winery, this grand estate is also home to Le Frankenberg, whose stylish and elegant interior exudes historical charm. No stranger to the fine dining scene, Steffen Szabo brings his own sense of expression and balance to the regional and international ingredients he showcases in his seasonal five- to eight-course set menu. A fish course of char teamed with pumpkin purée, foam and roasted seeds, for example, makes for an interesting play on textures. Restaurant manager and sommelier Sandra Tober provides friendly service and judicious wine recommendations.;Car park;[]
2495;Oettinger's Restaurant;Germany;Fellbach;Fellbacher Straße 2, Fellbach, 70736, Germany;48.8339908;9.2634674;75;false;true;Modern French, Country cooking;This family business has a tradition stretching back over 150 years. Michael Oettinger runs the place with his brother Martin, and has now handed over the reins in the kitchen to Kay Lurz, who has been working alongside him here since the spring of 2023. The new chef shows his true colours with his four- to eight-course set menu „Signatur Kay Lurz“, which draws on modern influences. However, Oettinger classics are still available. As ever, the emphasis remains squarely on the quality of the ingredients. In this cosy country house-style setting, you can look forward to friendly, attentive and competent service. For overnight stays, Hotel Hirsch has lovely, comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2496;Michaels Leitenberg;Germany;Frasdorf;Weiherweg 3, Frasdorf, 83112, Germany;47.8046083;12.3074069;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Who would expect to find a restaurant like this in the small town of Frasdorf? This place may be a little out of the way, but the talent and ambition of the young chef definitely make a visit worthwhile. Comprising five, six or eight courses, the set menu presents carefully considered dishes with their own unique flair, incorporating influences from all over the world, from France to Asia to New Zealand. The quality of the ingredients is beyond question. The seasonal Bavarian venison served with a pepper curry, for example, is delicious, not to mention the exquisite desserts. Fantastic wine list. The wine pairings and non-alcoholic alternatives are highly recommended for the set menu. The experience is rounded off by the friendly and obliging waitstaff, as well as the attractive modern setting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2498;Weinstock;Germany;Volkach;Hauptstraße 12, Volkach, 97332, Germany;49.8649712;10.2267305;45;true;false;Creative, Farm to table;The first floor of the long-established Zur Schwane hotel is home to a wonderfully chic restaurant, whose decor embodies a harmonious blend of old and new. A highly adept kitchen team creates modern dishes with classical foundations, homing in on the essentials: ingredients and flavours. The carefully selected produce is sourced locally if possible, and some even comes from the hotel's garden. The chefs also have a penchant for herbs. Only German wines are served, including some from the restaurant's estate (they are all available by the glass, too). It's definitely worth opting for the suggested pairings for the set menu. There is also a wine shop on site. Attractive, individually styled guestrooms are available.;Air conditioning;[]
2499;Adler;Germany;Lahr;Reichenbacher Hauptstraße 18, Lahr, 77933, Germany;48.3299999;7.9249354;76;false;true;Modern French;Having run this establishment with bags of charm and a sure touch for four generations, the Fehrenbacher family has made a real success of its restaurant – it has retained its Michelin star every year since 1990! Daniel Fehrenbacher, who took over the helm of this award-winning kitchen from his father Otto, is the man behind the outstanding modern French cuisine. He attaches great importance to showcasing what the region and the changing seasons have to offer, which is particularly evident in the game dishes. Interesting flavour contrasts are skilfully incorporated into the dishes. The winning combination of modern and classical elements also applies to the decor: a mix of chic, minimalist style and Black Forest charm. Under the direction of sommelier Jochen Hünd, you will be looked after in a friendly and well-trained manner and given expert advice on wine - the selection is well put together and fairly priced.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2500;maiBeck;Germany;Cologne;Am Frankenturm 5, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.9403502;6.9617559;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;What is it about this restaurant run by Jan Cornelius Maier and Tobias Becker ("maiBeck" for short) that makes it so popular? First and foremost, the modern cuisine, with dishes such as gently braised shoulder of German salt meadow lamb, winter spinach from Rommerskirchen, parsley root, mirabelle plum – sophisticated and rife with flavour, but also down-to-earth and accessible. The atmosphere is suitably unpretentious, which is in no small part down to the exceptionally congenial hosts and their well-coordinated team. They may set great store by using quality produce, but the prices are really reasonable! The same goes for the wine list, especially those available by the bottle. Finally, the location in the old town between the cathedral and the Rhine means that the terrace is a place to see and be seen. Tip: Take a stroll through the old town before or after you dine.;Terrace;[]
2501;Zeik;Germany;Hamburg;Sierichstraße 112, Hamburg, 22299, Germany;53.5889364;10.001631;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Maurizio Oster is the name of the chef-owner of this modern, minimalist, almost purist-style little restaurant. His north German roots are also reflected in his cuisine – the region takes centre stage. Excellent ingredients, sourced primarily from small producers and organic farms in the immediate vicinity, go into seasonal, plant-forward dishes that are sustainably prepared. There is a set menu including fish and meat, as well as a completely vegetarian version. Remarkably intense flavours and rich contrasts make for an almost unique culinary DNA, as displayed in dishes such as beetroot with tarragon and horseradish, or venison with celery and apple, which are both exciting and distinctive. The kitchen team also has a real penchant for fermenting, preserving and making vinegar. Service is attentive yet relaxed, and the chefs themselves participate in serving and explaining the dishes. Astute wine recommendations. The menu can also be paired with house-made non-alcoholic drinks.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2502;Maltes hidden kitchen;Germany;Baden-Baden;Gernsbacher Straße 24, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7619983;8.24148;30;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;In the middle of the pretty pedestrian zone of this well-maintained spa town, you will come across this interesting dual concept of coffee shop and restaurant. Coffee and cake are served here during the day, while in the evening the kitchen team, headed up by eponymous proprietor Malte Kuhn, proposes modern dishes – prepared in the "hidden kitchen" tucked away behind a sliding panel. They skilfully pare things down to the essentials, making the ingredients the focus of the 3- to 6-course menu, from which you can also choose à la carte. In addition to the wine pairing, there is also a non-alcoholic beverage pairing based on the teas from the coffee shop. The service is extremely friendly and professional, with the cooks also getting in on the act and the owner always on hand, too. A pleasant, cosy little restaurant with a charm all of its own – dining here makes for a really fun experience!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2504;1876 Daniel Dal-Ben;Germany;Düsseldorf;Grunerstraße 42a, Düsseldorf, 40239, Germany;51.2436309;6.8020825;99;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;At his chic and elegant little restaurant by the zoo, Daniel Dal-Ben serves up classic cuisine with a judicious flourish of creativity. In addition to Italian and French influences, the chef-patron also incorporates Japanese accents from time to time. A good example of interesting contrasts and harmonious balance is "Cannelloni, smoked eel, Caprese foam, pumpkin seeds". He is also partial to decorating his dishes with skilfully integrated herbs and flowers. The "Cicchetti 1876" starter has become a staple of the set menu. Allow plenty of time, as you may be treated to additional courses. Beyond the terrific food, the atmosphere is inviting and almost intimate. Attentive and well-trained front-of-house team.;;[]
2505;Keidenzeller Hof;Germany;Langenzenn;Fürther Straße 11, Langenzenn, 90579, Germany;49.4672666;10.7768228;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Set in a small village, this former farmhouse has been given a fabulous facelift that retains much of its original character while introducing modern details. Wood and stone features blend tastefully and elegantly to create a chic, stylish interior. Chef-patron Martin Grimmer proposes a creative seasonal set menu (a vegetarian version can be ordered in advance). His cooking involves original ideas and subtle combinations – the appetisers, too, hit the mark. His charming wife Vera, who presides front of house, is on hand to propose excellent wine or alcohol-free drink pairings. On Saturdays you can come for the"Gourmet Lunch". Tip: The spice bread that they bake in-house is also available to buy as a baking mix to take home with you. The barn is an ideal party venue. If you can't find a parking space at the restaurant, head for the meadow located about 200m away.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2506;Malathounis;Germany;Kernen im Remstal;Gartenstraße 5, Kernen im Remstal, 71394, Germany;48.793824;9.3423876;91;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Greek;Michelin-starred Greek cuisine? "Modern Greek cuisine" is what it says on the front door, and that's what you get at this charming, tastefully decorated restaurant run by a husband-and-wife team. The dishes are sophisticated and rich in flavour, interspersed with French influences and the light touch of Mediterranean cuisine. Chef Joannis Malathounis clearly draws inspiration from his Hellenic roots, yet he never relies on them too heavily. It's exciting to see this interpretation of Greek cuisine. There are two 4- to 5-course menus, one of which is vegetarian. In the cosy dining rooms, guests are warmly received by the lady of the house, Anna Malathounis, in person. She is also happy to offer recommendations from the selection of fine Greek wines.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2507;Jean;Germany;Eltville am Rhein;Wilhelmstraße 13, Eltville am Rhein, 65343, Germany;50.0273198;8.1215273;93;false;true;Classic French, Mediterranean Cuisine;In addition to its hotel and café, the Frankenbach family also runs Jean in this former wine bar. After working in renowned establishments such as Ikarus in Salzburg, Johannes Frankenbach (the third generation of the family) has been at the helm here since 2012. Even the name "Jean" (a French equivalent of Johannes) is a nod to his love of France, which is as much a part of his ingredient-led, Mediterranean-influenced cuisine as is his knack for creating fine aromas and flavour contrasts. This is accompanied by judicious and fairly priced wine pairings. The setting is also charming: half-height wooden panelling, elegant table settings, old photos... while outside is the pretty plane tree courtyard. The lady of the house waits on diners in a pleasingly friendly and down-to-earth fashion.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2508;Nagaya;Germany;Düsseldorf;Klosterstraße 42, Düsseldorf, 40211, Germany;51.2253636;6.7863334;20;false;true;Japanese;Yoshizumi Nagaya's cuisine really is something special. In a thoughtful, bold and meticulous fashion, he fuses elements of Japanese and western cuisine. During his training in Osaka, Toshiro Kandagawa taught him traditional Japanese cookery, while he learned his innovative approach from Takada Hasho in Gifu. Drawing on both of these experiences, he has developed his own distinctive style. Excellent ingredients are a matter of honour for this chef, from the Wagyu beef to sushi and sashimi. As well as fine wines, there is a splendid selection of sake. Furthermore, the front-of-house team is attentive and professional, and the decor is very modern, stylish and upscale.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2509;Verbene;Germany;Koblenz;Brunnenhof Königspfalz, Koblenz, 56068, Germany;50.3613819;7.5967303;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This delightful little restaurant is nestled in the heart of the old town. Patrons appreciate the inviting interior and the extremely friendly service, not to mention the modern seasonal cuisine. The ingredients are sourced as locally as possible – the restaurant even has its dedicated producers: For example, they have a farmer grow vegetables specifically for them. One of the two set menus comprising four to eight courses is vegetarian. The combination of yoghurt, zucchini, black garlic and lemon oil is a particularly original and well-balanced dish. The charming Brunnenhof is a lovely secluded courtyard where you can dine away from the hustle and bustle of the city.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2510;bi:braud;Germany;Ulm;Büchsengasse 20, Ulm, 89073, Germany;48.4005362;9.9924975;28;true;false;Contemporary, Farm to table;Somewhat tucked away in the old town, not far from Ulm Cathedral, this pleasantly down-to-earth little restaurant is full of charm. The atmosphere in the dining area is inviting and lively, and the waitstaff are friendly. You might even catch a glimpse into the kitchen behind the bar. Here, Alina Meissner-Bebrout and her committed young team prepare an intriguing modern set menu comprising five courses (available in a shortened version). A vegetarian version is also available. The dishes are meticulously crafted without being extravagant or cluttered. Everything is simply really well done. The rather unusual desserts certainly deserve a mention – these include a combination of hot-and-sour marinated radicchio, an aromatic elderberry gel, verjus and a popped amaranth crunch. Edda Brasserie is just a few minutes' walk away.;Terrace;[]
2511;haebel;Germany;Hamburg;Paul-Roosen-Straße 31, Hamburg, 22767, Germany;53.5532432;9.9574392;53;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in the lively St. Pauli neighbourhood, this small restaurant boasts a charming yet stylish bistro atmosphere and an open kitchen. An appealing carte blanche concept is proposed in the form of two set menus: "Fauna" (omnivore) and "Flora" (vegetarian). Eschewing unnecessary frills and showmanship, this cuisine is modern and pleasingly pared down to the essentials. Some of the culinary creations are rather daring, featuring bold flavours. The service comes courtesy of a friendly front-of-house team, who are informal and familiar in their approach – the chefs get in on the act when it comes to serving the dishes. And there's freshly brewed coffee to round off your meal.;;[]
2512;MAIN TOWER Restaurant & Lounge;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Neue Mainzer Straße 52, Frankfurt on the Main, 60311, Germany;50.1124398;8.6717395;97;false;false;Asian Influences, Modern Cuisine;A great location in the heart of Frankfurt. Take the lift up to the 53rd floor and bag a table by the window to experience a view you don't often get to enjoy – the panorama over the rooftops of "Mainhatten" is downright spectacular! The cuisine is equally impressive. A modern set menu comprising five to seven expressive courses is on offer. The clear Asian, mainly Japanese influences can be seen, for example, in "Ikejime Hamachi, Gamba Blanca, Wasabi, 20 year old matured Mirin". First-class product quality. You can sip an aperitif in the lounge before dinner (from 9pm you are also welcome just for drinks). A reservation gets you a free ticket for the lift and also grants you access to the observation deck.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
2513;Troyka;Germany;Erkelenz;Rurstraße 19, Erkelenz, 41812, Germany;51.0588999;6.3320766;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Russian;Chef duo Alexander Wulf and Marcel Kokot propose a one-of-a-kind culinary experience, serving up Russian dishes with a modern twist and packed with flavour. The set menu is served by a highly adept and knowledgeable yet laid-back young team led by sommelier Ronny Schreiber – a real wine connoisseur, he surprises diners with interesting, not always conventional wine recommendations. In summer, the minimalist-style indoor dining space is complemented by a gorgeous terrace. Tip: Nab a seat at the counter facing the open kitchen for some fascinating insights into the chefs' work. There is also a screen showing the action at the kitchen pass. Incidentally, the name, the Russian word troyka means "trio" and refers to Wulf, Kokot and Schreiber – the three men who run this operation like a well-oiled machine and with great dedication. As an alternative to the fine dining set menu, you can order more down-to-earth bistro fare à la carte.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2514;5;Germany;Stuttgart;Bolzstraße 8, Stuttgart, 70173, Germany;48.7800231;9.1780757;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Even after all these years, 5 is still bang on trend. This is primarily down to Alexander Dinter's modern cuisine. Since 2018, he has been the creative force at the helm, successfully incorporating his own original ideas into his seasonally inspired set menu. The location near the Schlossgarten, in what was Stuttgart's first ever railway station, is also unique. A laid-back urban vibe combined with an elegant lounge decor makes for a special atmosphere, which persists as you move from the stylish bar on the ground floor to the "casual fine dining" restaurant on the first floor. Here, guests sit on chic, individually designed chairs at bare tables to enjoy the excellent food and service, which includes expert wine recommendations. The parking garages in the immediate vicinity are convenient for those coming by car. Reservation times in the evening in the gourmet restaurant: 17:45, 18:30 and 19:15. For lunch there is an extract from the evening menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2516;Mod by Sven Nöthel;Germany;Duisburg;Grafschafter Straße 197a, Duisburg, 47199, Germany;51.4770801;6.6674968;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;What a gorgeous spot! Sven Nöthel has opened his elegant restaurant in a lovingly converted stable surrounded by lots of greenery. The sleek modern design is just as eye-catching as the open kitchen, which gives you the feeling of being part of the action. Should you prefer to sit somewhere a little quieter, ask for a table in the Wine Room. The set menus – "Beete & Bauer" (beet & farmer) and vegetarian "Acker & Saat" (field & seed) – or à la carte dishes are served on pottery plates from Wesel. The modern, seasonal cuisine is based on select ingredients, sourced from the region wherever possible. Diners can look forward to convivial service – even the chefs get in on the act and talk you through the dishes. Pretty terrace, too.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2517;Mountain Hub Gourmet;Germany;Munich;Terminalstraße Mitte 20, Munich, 85356, Germany;48.3552067;11.7886069;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The fine dining restaurant of the Hilton Munich Airport hotel, located directly at the airport, draws the eye with its semi-circular layout and chic modern design. Diners take their seats at generously spaced and beautifully set tables to enjoy friendly, attentive and professional service and the modern cuisine of Marcel Tauschek and his team. Pared-down yet robustly flavoured dishes that make good use of high-quality produce, eg pigeon with chanterelles and quince or venison with potato and parsley, showcase original ideas but also draw on classical foundations – the wonderful sauces must be given a mention here! The excellent wine list also has a good selection of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2518;Gourmetrestaurant "fine dining RS";Germany;Salach;Burg Staufeneck 1, Salach, 73084, Germany;48.6917367;9.7666002;38;false;false;French Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The secluded, quiet location up here at Staufeneck Castle is wonderful, as is the view of the Fils valley. Head to Burghotel's fine dining restaurant to drink it all in via the large panoramic windows – in fine weather you can even see Stuttgart airport and the TV Tower! Guests take their seats in tasteful and elegantly minimalist surroundings to enjoy professional and charming service courtesy of the Swabian-speaking front-of-house team – yes, this is an authentic regional experience!  Rolf Straubinger and his long-time chef de cuisine Markus Waibel impress diners with a modern set menu - really elaborate dishes that are agreeably light and subtle and full of interesting flavour contrasts. Alternatively, try out oifach andersch, which proposes traditional Swabian cuisine that also draws on international influences.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2519;Laurentius;Germany;Weikersheim;Marktplatz 5, Weikersheim, 97990, Germany;49.4804625;9.8977926;88;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The Koch family business has virtually all of your needs covered, with its lovely accommodation on Marktplatz, terrific food and ever-obliging service. Proprietors Sabine and Jürgen Koch blend culinary classics and tradition with a modern twist, all while prioritising the use of carefully selected, fresh ingredients. They deliberately avoid frills, focusing instead on expression and flavour. Dishes such as the shoulder of bœuf de Hohenlohe confit reflect a connection to the region. However, there are also more cosmopolitan creations to choose from, such as wild prawn tartare with shellfish stock, coconut and tandoori. A four- to six-course tasting menu is available, with the option to order à la carte as well. To complement your meal, there are wines from the Tauber Valley, Franconia and Baden-Württemberg, but also from France and Italy. The setting is also captivating: a distinctive natural stone barrel vault blends seamlessly with modern elegant interior design. Tip: Head to Hohenloher Märktle and stock up on some quality ingredients to take home with you.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2520;Zeitwerk;Germany;Wernigerode;Breite Straße 53a, Wernigerode, 38855, Germany;51.8353677;10.7890914;47;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;"Welcome to the living room restaurant" are the words that greet you when you first look at your menu, and that pretty much sums up the pleasantly relaxed atmosphere in this establishment, whose upscale interior is modern and stylish with light wood furnishings. Service of the set menu begins at 7.15pm for all guests and the courses are served in sync. You should allow plenty of time for this dinner, but an entertaining evening is assured, with the numerous intriguing small dishes emerging from the open kitchen at a good pace, as well as the competent and charming service team led by Florian Raake (who also provides excellent wine recommendations with tips such as Daniel Mattern's Hop & Grape). This place is somewhat tucked away in a courtyard, where owner Robin Pietsch also has his second restaurant, Pietsch.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2521;Schwarzer Hahn;Germany;Deidesheim;Am Marktplatz 1, Deidesheim, 67146, Germany;49.4082094;8.1874237;77;true;false;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;n institution with a long tradition and a reputation that extends beyond the region for good reason. Here at Hotel Deidesheimer Hof, the dedication of the Hahn family is plain to see, including when it comes to the restaurant. In this beautiful historical building, the contrast between the old cross vault and the modern table settings and colourful decor is spot on. Prepared using select produce, the dishes can be ordered as a set menu or à la carte. It goes without saying that they have the regional classic Saumagen (stuffed pig's stomach) on the menu. Stefan Neugebauer and Felix Jarzina are the faces behind the excellent cuisine. The friendly and experienced front-of-house team will be happy to talk you through the regional wines, which are available on tap.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2522;Friedrich Franz;Germany;Bad Doberan;Prof.-Dr.-Vogel-Straße 6, Bad Doberan, 18209, Germany;54.1437795;11.8423091;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This wonderfully luxurious and elegant gourmet restaurant is situated in the exclusive Grand Hotel Heiligendamm in a wonderful location by the Baltic Sea – also known as the "white city by the sea". The sense of opulence extends to the cuisine, which comes courtesy of head chef Ronny Siewert, who hails from Nienburg (Saale). He and his kitchen team turn out delicately flavoured and elaborately detailed dishes that draw on only the most exclusive produce. The front-of-house team, led by Berlin-born Norman Rex, also knows how to impress: guests can look forward to attentive and elegant service, as well as expert advice when it comes to wine. Try to get a table by the window for a view of the sea!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2523;Spitzner;Germany;Münster;Königsstraße 42, Münster, 48143, Germany;51.9581485;7.6260295;16;false;true;Modern French;Housed in Oerschen Hof, a spruce historical aristocratic palace in the city centre, this tastefully designed restaurant serves a contemporary take on classic cuisine, laying the focus squarely on the ingredients and skill of the chefs. The plating is refreshingly slick and uncluttered. Order à la carte or opt for a menu comprising four to seven courses. The charming and adept service team will be happy to advise you. Chef Karl-Nikolas Spitzner also gets involved in serving from time to time. In fine weather, make a beeline for the terrace.;Terrace;[]
2525;Kulmeck by Tom Wickboldt;Germany;Heringsdorf;Kulmstraße 17, Heringsdorf, 17424, Germany;53.9598339;14.1608992;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Eating here is lots of fun! The cosy modern decor, the rock and pop classics from the 70s playing in the background and, last but not least, the friendly service all play their part in creating a pleasingly laid-back atmosphere. The other major draw is Tom Wickboldt's cuisine. He proposes a seven-course set menu (two further courses can be added or swapped in) that impresses with its clearly structured and coherent dishes, as well as the quality of the ingredients. A shining example is the elegant and super-fresh langoustine tartare. The bread, butter and oil may cost extra, but the home-made sourdough bread is so delicious that it's worth it. The selection of wines is reasonably priced.;;[]
2526;Winzerhof Stahl;Germany;Simmershofen;Lange Dorfstr. 21, Simmershofen, 97215, Germany;49.5232152;10.1045465;58;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Both foodies and oenophiles are in for a real treat at Winzerhof Stahl, which proposes a modern cuisine in the form of a surprise menu comprising nine courses, harmoniously paired with wines from the restaurant's own estate. The small dining space features a charming blend of minimalist interior design and elements retained from the original building such as exposed wooden beams and stone walls. The atmosphere is pleasantly intimate, which is down in no small part to owner Christian Stahl, who personally attends to his diners – his passion for cooking and wine is palpable! He and his experienced kitchen team, which he and Mirko Schweiger head up, serve the food themselves.;Car park;[]
2527;Erno's Bistro;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Liebigstraße 15, Frankfurt on the Main, 60323, Germany;50.1190432;8.6659109;61;true;false;Classic French, Modern Cuisine;Savoir-vivre in Frankfurt! Valéry Mathis's modern and seasonally influenced French cuisine has been held in high esteem for many years. Flavoursome and expertly prepared dishes are served in a charming bistro atmosphere, which is enhanced by the authentic interior with wood panelling and decorative details. Friendly and down-to-earth yet highly competent service courtesy of the team led by owner Eric Huber. You can also look forward to savvy wine recommendations – the emphasis here is on French labels. There is also a delightful terrace. It is no accident that this place is so popular!;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2528;Hannappel;Germany;Essen;Dahlhauser Straße 173, Essen, 45279, Germany;51.4370622;7.1050518;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Run with exceptional dedication, this restaurant is keeping up with the times with its tasteful minimalist interior design and modern cuisine. A seasonal menu comprising four or six courses is served – a vegetarian version is also available. Showcasing the finest ingredients and impeccable craftsmanship, the team led by head chef Tobias Weyers creates pleasingly clearly presented dishes featuring subtle contrasts, such as the aromatic crispy barbecued asparagus, perfectly paired with thinly sliced melt-in-your-mouth white bacon and an intense green cucumber sauce. "Casual fine dining" sums it up perfectly. Rounding it all off is the attentive and professional front-of-house team, whose relaxed attitude adds to the delightfully informal atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2529;Alte Schule - Klassenzimmer;Germany;Feldberger Seenlandschaft;Zur Alten Schule 5, Feldberger Seenlandschaft, 17258, Germany;53.3363536;13.5035697;70;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;Now this is a school you'll be happy to go to! In an idyllic setting, Daniel Schmidthaler serves up an exciting and modern surprise menu comprising five or seven courses in the "Klassenzimmer" where pupils once studied. The menu changes daily thanks to a constant supply of ever-changing ingredients, freshly sourced directly from the region. Wonderful vegetables and herbs, nuts and fruits, as well as fish or meat, go into complex dishes that are rich in flavour and with a harmonious balance of acidity. The chef's Austrian heritage also shines through from time to time – the apricot buns to go with the coffee are terrific! The decor is simple and stylish, with charming features such as an old tiled stove, parquet flooring and tall mullioned windows. Should you wish to stay the night, there are also bright and comfortable guestrooms. Hotel guests take their meals in the beautiful setting of the conservatory.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2531;Seven Swans;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Mainkai 4, Frankfurt on the Main, 60311, Germany;50.1096762;8.6871455;93;false;true;Vegan, Creative;The location is out of the ordinary, as is the philosophy behind the cuisine! Housed in the city's narrowest building, which is still seven storeys high, this stylish and sleek restaurant boasts fantastic views of the River Main through large floor-to-ceiling windows. On the menu: 100% vegan cuisine made from organic produce. Permaculture is the name of the game here, meaning only those regional ingredients that have been produced ecologically and in harmony with nature are used in the dishes. In keeping with this ideology, much of the produce used comes from the restaurant's own local farm. The dining experience lasts about five hours from beginning to end, with the set menu being served to all the guests at the same time. Head chef Ricky Saward provides detailed explanations of the dishes, bringing a performative element to this showcasing of his own philosophy and the resulting elaborate creations. To complement the menu, choose from German wines or house-made alcohol-free beverages. Good to know: It's not easy to get a table here, so book well in advance!;Air conditioning;[]
2532;Yoshi by Nagaya;Germany;Düsseldorf;Kreuzstraße 17, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.2243136;6.785749;76;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Yoshizumi Nagaya's Michelin-starred cuisine can now be sampled in two different locations in Düsseldorf. Not far from the original restaurant, also located in "Little Tokyo", Yoshi opened in October 2016. The food is classically Japanese with subtle European influences here and there. In the evening, the omakase set menu wins over diners with its absolutely ingredient-led and exceedingly precise preparation. It is accompanied by a large selection of sakes. In a way, the minimalist interior design is a reflection of the pared-down style of the dishes. On Fridays and Saturdays, Yoshi is also open for lunch, serving a four- or six-course set menu. Lots of the diners are Japanese – which speaks for itself! Tip for motorists: Use the multi-storey carpark at Kreuzstraße 27.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
2533;Genuss-Atelier;Germany;Dresden;Bautzner Straße 149, Dresden, 01099, Germany;51.0676334;13.7761213;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Fourteen steps lead you down to this friendly, cosy cellar restaurant in a beautiful old villa in Neustadt, where sandstone walls and brick vaults make for a special setting. In a wonderfully informal atmosphere, brother-and-sister team Marcus and Nicole Blonkowski serve interesting, modern and creative cuisine prepared using top-quality produce – and the value for money is hard to beat! There is a nicely curated à la carte selection, but you can also opt to give the kitchen team free rein to put together a surprise menu for you. The wine list features labels from eastern Germany exclusively, and they have made a point of including some lesser-known ones. This place also boasts a delightful terrace.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2534;die burg;Germany;Donaueschingen;Burgring 6, Donaueschingen, 78166, Germany;47.9813093;8.5524568;62;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;The Grom brothers run their restaurant in the centre of this small town. Front of house, Niklas provides excellent service along with astute recommendations from the impressive wine list. Meanwhile, Jason presides in the kitchen, cooking up ambitious modern dishes. Diners can opt for the "burg" set menu, the vegetarian alternative ("gartenliebe") or à la carte dishes from the selection of classics. The dry-aged meat sourced from the neighbouring Leimgrabenhof – various cuts are prepared on the charcoal grill – are particularly recommended. The decor is characterised by premium materials and chic, minimalist design. Vinophiles Flair is testament to the owners' enthusiasm for wine. The same goes for Weinba(a)r, which in the evening serves bar food and burgers, alongside regional classics and specials from the grill. Tip: Events featuring winemakers or barbecue evenings are organised here. For overnight guests, die burg also has modern and functional guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2535;Schiller's Manufaktur;Germany;Koblenz;Mayenerstraße 126, Koblenz, 56070, Germany;50.3693993;7.5814339;76;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Culinary excellence is guaranteed at Hotel Stein, thanks to chef-patron Mike Schiller and his intriguing four- to six-course set menu, in which he skilfully combines Mediterranean and Asian influences. Flavoursome and robust, the stocks and sauces are particularly noteworthy, with the vegetable broth being a standout. Also worth mentioning is the superb quality of the ingredients. A vegetarian version of the set menu and the surprise menu can be ordered (24hr) in advance. Out on the restaurant floor, the friendly maître d', Melanie Stein-Schiller, is in charge of service. The bright conservatory and the charming garden terrace are both delightful spots in which to dine. Top tip: Head to the shop for home-made delicacies to take away.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2536;Le Moissonnier Bistro;Germany;Cologne;Krefelder Straße 25, Cologne, 50670, Germany;50.9510495;6.952216;50;false;true;French, Seafood;The "new" Le Moissonnier has what it takes to become your favourite restaurant: excellent food and bags of charm! In a lovely, bustling interior replete with charming Art Nouveau features, diners are seated at closely spaced tables. Obliging hosts Liliane and Vincent Moissonnier and their friendly team take good care of their guests. Chef Eric Menchon proposes a range of small and larger dishes, including great French bistro classics such as pâté en croûte, fish soup, oysters and mussels. Opt for one of their excellent wines to accompany your meal. A plat du jour is also offered – be sure to book your table in advance! Dining alone at the counter, you can also watch the action unfold behind the scenes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2538;Frieda;Germany;Leipzig;Menckestraße 48, Leipzig, 04155, Germany;51.3594485;12.3624098;64;false;false;Creative, Farm to table;Friendly, refreshing, unpretentious – it's undeniably good fun to eat here. In addition to the pleasantly uncomplicated bistro atmosphere and chic design, the cuisine proposed by this pair of restaurateurs goes down particularly well. Lisa Angermann and Andreas Reinke offer ingredient-led modern dishes in the form of a regularly changing set menu dubbed "Frieda En Vogue" – the vegetarian version "Frieda Naturell" is available upon reservation. In keeping with the restaurant's ecological ethos, when it comes to choosing ingredients, the focus is on the region and the changing seasons. The friendly and accomplished front-of-house team is headed up by the charming proprietor. There is also a lovely terrace and orangery.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2539;360°;Germany;Limburg an der Lahn;Bahnhofsplatz 1a, Limburg an der Lahn, 65549, Germany;50.3844391;8.0614395;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine, International;With a name like 360°, who isn't expecting a great view? The highlight of this sleek, modern restaurant on the third floor has got to be the roof terrace! But you can also enjoy the views over the city from the inside thanks to the large windows. Alternatively, you can watch Alexander Hohlwein and his team at work in the open kitchen as they prepare their creative "Weltreise" set menu in the evening. Heading up the front-of-house team is his partner, Rebekka Weickert, your cordial hostess who also offers expert advice on wine. For lunch there is a pared-down business lunch. Incidentally, they have a bee colony on the terrace and produce their own honey. Our tip: Park in the underground car park of the WERKStadt shopping centre.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
2540;Storchen;Germany;Bad Krozingen;Felix und Nabor Straße 2, Bad Krozingen, 79189, Germany;47.89284;7.69288;96;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Run with great dedication by two generations of the same family, this traditional inn is a real gem. Offering a choice of two set menus – one of which is vegetarian – and a small à la carte selection, the father-and-son team ensures that every diner is catered for. Jochen Helfesrieder and his father Fritz stick to seasonal produce when choosing ingredients for their classic-based cuisine, which is based on select regional as well as international produce. Some of it comes from their own farm garden, but the menu also includes excellent fish from France. This picture-perfect traditional Baden inn dating from 1764 has tastefully decorated dining areas – opt for rustic charm with an old tiled stove and wooden panelling, or more modern decor. There is also a pretty garden terrace with a pond. Cosy and comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2541;Ich weiß ein Haus am See;Germany;Krakow am See;Paradiesweg 3, Krakow am See, 18292, Germany;53.6686169;12.2986817;41;true;true;Classic French;Somewhere between Berlin and Rostock, in the middle of nowhere, you will find this small hotel on a secluded lake. The location is idyllic – the name of the road, Paradiesweg, is apt. But it's not just a cosy place to spend the night: food-wise you'll also get your money's worth. Raik Zeigner, head chef since 2005, bowls diners over with classic cuisine, which has always had a solid reputation. For his four-course set menu, which changes every evening, select ingredients are used. Take, for example, the steamed char or the saddle of venison with chanterelles. In this elegant restaurant with its country-house flair, your cordial hosts Petra and Adi König work with palpable enthusiasm to create a welcoming atmosphere. The owner – virtually a walking wine encyclopaedia – unfailingly recommends the perfect pairings. The next generation is also already getting involved in the running of this delightful family business.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2542;Rosin;Germany;Dorsten;Hervester Straße 18, Dorsten, 46286, Germany;51.7191315;7.0132284;81;false;true;Creative, Classic Cuisine;TV chef Frank Rosin is a household name in Germany. The team led by his head chef and long-time companion Oliver Engelke offers you classic and creative dishes in the chic restaurant, which you can put together your own set menu, including vegan dishes. A la carte choice is also possible. In addition there is the ‘Schmackofatz' set menu with wine accompaniment. The service is second to none: headed up by maître d' Jochen Bauer and sommelier Susanne Spies, the front-of-house team guide you through the meal in a relaxed but professional manner. You may like to sample one of the wines from their own Rosin & Spies range.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2543;taku;Germany;Cologne;Trankgasse 1, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.9418935;6.9564935;72;true;true;Asian, Fusion;A classic grand hotel like the Excelsior Ernst (dating from 1863) may not be the setting you would expect for a restaurant done out in a minimalist Asian style. But for all its classicism, the venerable establishment right next to the cathedral also has a chic, modern side, which taku fits into perfectly. The straightforward, elegant design is complemented by Mirko Gaul's contemporary and well-thought-out dishes. Successfully balancing spiciness, acidity and sweetness, he creates an aromatic fusion of East Asian cuisine and Western/international influences. Here and there, you will also find regional produce among the selected ingredients. The "Degustation" set menu is offered in five or seven courses. The wine recommendation by the glass is nice.;Air conditioning;[]
2544;Goldener Anker;Germany;Dorsten;Lippetor 4, Dorsten, 46282, Germany;51.6630641;6.9652459;70;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The likeable TV chef Björn Freitag is a household name. In 1997, at the age of 23, he took over this long-established restaurant, breathing new life into the kitchen. In 2002 the place was awarded a MICHELIN star, which he and his team have held on to ever since. The setting is lovely, too: the decor is sophisticated and elegant, which is perfectly suited to the classically based cuisine with modern influences. The wonderful flavours of excellent produce are combined in an extremely harmonious way. The charming and accomplished front-of-house team will accompany you through the evening. There is also a cookery school in the same building.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2545;Sahila - The Restaurant;Germany;Cologne;Kämmergasse 18, Cologne, 50676, Germany;50.932944;6.9527411;62;false;false;International, Modern Cuisine;Having made a name for herself at Schloss Loersfeld, Julia Komp struck out on her own to set up Sahila. Inspired by her travels around the globe, this enthusiasticchef from the Bergisches Land region aims to share her culinary impressions by way of an internationally inspired set menu. She skilfully incorporates spices and produce from various countries into her sophisticated, handcrafted dishes. Peppered with Middle Eastern decorative features, the decor creates a stylish setting in which to enjoy the service provided by the highly competent and attentive front-of-house team.;Terrace;[]
2546;mural;Germany;Munich;Hotterstraße 12, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1365989;11.5702579;78;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Das ist schon eine besondere Location. Das Restaurant befindet sich im MUCA, dem "Museum of Urban and Contemporary Art", daran angelehnt das Design des "mural". Aus der Küche kommt ein modern-kreatives Menü mit vier oder fünf Gängen - mit Fisch und Fleisch oder als Veggie-Variante. Die Produkte stammen fast ausschließlich aus Bayern und überzeugen mit Qualität. Dazu sympathischer und freundschaftlicher Service, angenehm unkompliziert die Weinberatung - interessant sind u. a. die Empfehlungen aus dem schönen Angebot an Naturweinen. Tipp: Do. bis Sa. gibt's auch Lunch, sonntags Brunch. Do. bis Sa. öffnet man nachmittags zudem die Vinothek.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2547;Friedrich;Germany;Osnabrück;Lotter Straße 99, Osnabrück, 49078, Germany;52.2746053;8.0282239;21;false;false;Modern French, Creative;In this immaculate townhouse on the diminutive Hans-Callmeyer-Platz, Lars Keiling wins over diners with modern French cuisine into which he incorporates creative twists as well as various flavours from the Mediterranean and beyond. Choose wines by the glass to pair with the six to eight courses on the menu, or solicit the expert advice at hand. Highly attentive to every guest's needs, restaurant manager and sommelier Gina Duesmann is in charge of the charming and professional front-of-house team. The fabulous food and pleasant service are complemented by the tasteful, chic and elegant interior. Alternatively, try the Kleiner Friedrich bistro, which boasts a beautiful terrace under shady chestnut trees.;Interesting wine list;[]
2548;Gasthof zum Bad;Germany;Langenau;Burghof 11, Langenau, 89129, Germany;48.5000851;10.1245163;28;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Taking over the family business was definitely the right decision! Since 2007, chef Hans Häge has been at the helm of this place that used to be run by his parents. He uses select ingredients to produce classic seasonal cuisine with a modern twist. In the evenings, there is a choice of different set menus. The reasonably priced three- or four-course lunch is especially popular. Classics such as Maultaschen in broth and Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) can be ordered à la carte. Diners sit at modern bare wood tables and enjoy great food in an atmosphere that is laid-back and good fun. To the rear you can see Löffelbrunnen Lake – the source is directly under the building. The name Gasthof zum Bad is a reference to the baths that were once housed here. Well-kept guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2549;Leos by Stephan Brandl;Germany;Bad Kötzing;Liebenstein 25, Bad Kötzing, 93444, Germany;49.2157489;12.829388;80;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Contemporary;Rustic wood features and original decorative touches combine to create a high-end, minimalist decor. Beautifully situated in the Bayerwaldhof spa hotel, which overlooks the village, Leos is a modern take on a small Stube (akin to a parlour), with just four tables available. The chic look and pleasantly informal atmosphere are complemented by the relaxed yet highly efficient service and carefully considered, clearly structured dishes that come courtesy of chef Stephan Brandl. Outstanding ingredients are prepared with the utmost precision and creativity, resulting in exciting combinations such as perfectly cooked and tender Vendée sole on a pleasingly salty bacon foam with a dollop of spicy, aromatic onion marmalade. A five- or seven-course set menu is served, with a choice of starter, main course and dessert. There is also a decent selection of wines that can be ordered by the glass. Nice to know: If you dine here as a hotel guest, you pay a much lower price for the set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2550;JUWEL;Germany;Schirgiswalde-Kirschau;Bautzener Straße 74, Schirgiswalde-Kirschau, 02681, Germany;51.0958925;14.4291617;18;true;true;Modern French, Creative;This fine dining restaurant of the wellness hotel BEI SCHUMANN is aptly named, starting with a plush interior done out in chic lilac and black tones and including carefully chosen details such as amethysts and Swarovski crystals. Then there is the modern and creative cuisine, which also draws on more classic culinary traditions – this is the domain of Tobias Heldt. The five to nine courses on the menu include dishes such as "Lamb 'Marrakesh', chickpea, paprika" and "Halibut, edamame, umeboshi plum". And it would be remiss not to mention the exquisite pâtisserie. Another feel-good factor makes the experience complete: the extremely friendly and professional service team, headed up by Patrick Grunewald, who will also share their competent insights when it comes to wine. Tip: there is an extensive champagne selection!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2551;Oben;Germany;Heidelberg;Am Kohlhof 5, Heidelberg, 69117, Germany;49.38722;8.7356572;15;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Geradezu eine kulinarische Insel im Wald ist der historische "Kohlhof", der idyllisch zwischen Wiesen und Obstbäumen oberhalb von Heidelberg liegt. Der gepflasterte Innenhof mit ländlichem Flair lädt zum Aperitif ein, danach geht's in den charmanten Gastraum mit liebevollen Details und angenehm intimer Atmosphäre. In der einsehbaren Küche entsteht ein durchdachtes modernes Menü mit 13 Köstlichkeiten. Küchenchef Robert Rädel kocht kreativ und legt Wert auf regionale und saisonale Produkte. Vieles kommt aus der nächsten Umgebung, darunter auch der Wein. Die Köche servieren mit und erklären die Speisen. Zwischendurch wird man auch mal für einen Gang in die Küche entführt, wo man am kleinen Chefs Table mit dem Team ins Gespräch kommt. Es gibt nur deutsche Weine - wählen Sie selbst im Weinkeller! Hinweis: Man ist sehr gut gebucht - für Nachrückerplätze folgen Sie dem Link auf der Homepage des "Oben".;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
2552;Apicius;Germany;Bad Zwischenahn;Eiden 9, Bad Zwischenahn, 26160, Germany;53.1887445;8.0331566;21;false;true;Modern French;The tastefully decorated Hotel Jagdhaus Eiden, which has been run by the Zur Brügge family for generations, enjoys a beautiful countryside location, just a few metres from the lake. Here you will find the modern and elegant fine dining restaurant, where chef Tim Extra and his enthusiastic team serve modern dishes that are rich in finesse, such as Balfego tuna with radish, buttermilk dashi and N25 caviar. A set menu is proposed, and you can opt to have five or six courses. These can be vegetarian, with meat or mixed. Attentive and well-organised service comes courtesy of a highly professional, but by no means stuffy, front-of-house team. The impressive wine list comprises over 600 labels. Tip: the restaurant has its own casino.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2553;Jellyfish;Germany;Hamburg;Weidenallee 12, Hamburg, 20357, Germany;53.5666172;9.965481;26;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;If you're a fan of fish and seafood, then Jellyfish is the place for you. Come and sample the set menu, which is available with four, six or eight courses. You will also be able to order an excellent "exception" in the form of a meat or poultry dish. With the select ingredients being prepared in a considered, modern and creative way, the technical skill is second to none. A fine example is Canadian Lobster "Som Tam". As for the setting, the restaurant, located in the Schanzenviertel, has a pleasingly minimalist interior, all the better to focus on the interesting, polished cuisine. The experience is rounded out by the smart, attentive and knowledgeable young front-of-house team, who will also help you find your way around the wine list. Small bistro menu at lunchtime Sat-Sun.;Interesting wine list;[]
2554;Mühlenhelle;Germany;Gummersbach;Hohler Straße 1, Gummersbach, 51645, Germany;50.9832866;7.5311837;30;true;false;Modern French;What a fabulous property! With this magnificent villa, Michael and Brigitta Quendler have opted for a highly distinguished setting in which to indulge their guests. Elegant style, warm tones, beautiful wooden floors, large mullioned windows – the overall effect is really inviting. Add to the location the attentive and competent service and Michael Quendler's cooking. Although predominantly a classic affair, his cuisine is still modern and enjoyably pared down – he is adept at weaving the different flavours of his excellent ingredients together, in dishes such as red prawn with mushrooms, leek and mango, or scallop with celery, apple and ponzu. There are two set menus (one of which is vegetarian/vegan) featuring dishes you can also combine as you please or order à la carte. Excellent selection of wines by the bottle – you can rely on your charming hostess for recommendations! Comfortable guestrooms for an overnight stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2555;Piment;Germany;Hamburg;Lehmweg 29, Hamburg, 20251, Germany;53.5822226;9.9795367;100;false;false;Creative, North African;What makes this restaurant so charming? In addition to the beautiful interior decor done out in warm tones and the friendly, competent service, Wahabi Nouri's cuisine should be mentioned first and foremost. You can really feel his passion for food! His cooking owes its personal touch to his respect for his heritage: Nouri comes from Casablanca, so he incorporates subtle North African influences, such as in the Berber vegetable tart or the tajine de sot-l'y-laisse. His two set menus draw on the finest seasonal ingredients, which are skilfully combined to conjure up dishes featuring harmoniously balanced spices and flavours with a whole host of nuances.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2556;Das garbo zum Löwen;Germany;Eggenstein-Leopoldshafen;Hauptstraße 51, Eggenstein-Leopoldshafen, 76344, Germany;49.0779967;8.3879792;55;true;false;Farm to table, Classic French;In the restaurant of Zum Löwen hotel, located in the centre of the village, the attractive decor embodies a combination of rural charm and elegance, with warm wood finishings, a tiled stove, pretty fabrics and high-quality tableware. At the helm, Marcel Kazda cooks up ambitious cuisine with classical foundations and seasonal influences – the quality of the produce is excellent. Well-thought-out, sophisticated and intensely flavoursome dishes come in two set menus comprising four to six courses: "Inspiration à la Kazda Menu" and "Low-Carb Menu" – an appealing contemporary alternative that steers clear of refined sugar. The individual courses of these set menus can also be ordered à la carte. At lunchtime (Wed-Fri), they serve a few classics such as Caesar salad or Wiener schnitzel in addition to the "Business Menü". To accompany the set menus, there are excellent wine pairings, as well as fantastic non-alcoholic alternatives. Philipp Spielmann, an experienced sommelier, heads the outstanding front-of-house team.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2557;Masa Japanese Cuisine;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Hanauer Landstraße 131, Frankfurt on the Main, 60314, Germany;50.1119257;8.7129018;36;true;false;Japanese, Japanese Contemporary;A hotspot for Japanese cuisine is hidden away in this unassuming town house in Frankfurt's Ostend neighbourhood. Having recently expanded his skill set and his knowledge of the Japanese culinary arts in both of Yoshizumi Nagaya's Düsseldorf restaurants, Masaru Oae now proposes two omakase menus composed of seven or nine courses – one with fish/meat, one vegetarian. The quality of the ingredients is second to none. Dishes such as scallops, kale, dashi butter sauce, as well as the excellent sushi, successfully draw on both classic and modern Japanese cuisine, while remaining open to the odd European influence. The aesthetics of the food have a major part to play too, as demonstrated by the elaborately decorated medley of starters. In an unpretentious and pared-back setting that evokes the Far East, diners take their seats at small tables or at the food counter (where they can watch the chef at work). Top tip: Opt for the sake pairings served with the set menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
2558;bidlabu;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Kleine Bockenheimer Straße 14, Frankfurt on the Main, 60313, Germany;50.1142593;8.6742761;79;true;true;Farm to table, International;Located in the heart of the city – albeit somewhat tucked away – this appealing bistro is a lively place with really good food. AndrÉ Rickert (known from the "Weinsinn") forms the dual leadership in the kitchen together with chef Patrick LÖhl. Theirculinary style is pleasingly down to earth yet sophisticated in terms of craftsmanship. Vegetarians are also well catered for. The service comes courtesy of a laid-back yet highly competent front-of-house-team who provide astute wine recommendations for the set menu. Tip: book early to avoid disappointment!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2559;halbedel's Gasthaus;Germany;Bonn;Rheinallee 47, Bonn, 53173, Germany;50.6889689;7.1662272;44;false;false;Modern French;A well-to-do neighbourhood in Bad Godesberg, a Wilhelminian villa with a stylish yellow and white façade, an elegant interior with stucco, parquet flooring and modern touches – the perfect backdrop for Rainer-Maria Halbedel's cuisine. A legend of the German fine dining scene, he started cooking in 1966, received a Michelin star in 1984 at his former restaurant Korkeiche, and has held onto it ever since. He incorporates modern elements into his classic French cuisine and creates harmonious flavour combinations. Only the best produce is used, including eggs from his own hens and vegetables from his extensive garden in the Eifel. Opf for the "Menu Surprise" if you fancy the alternative vegetarian set menu. The handwritten wine list is very pleasing – the chef-patron will be happy to provide you with recommendations himself.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2560;St. Andreas;Germany;Aue - Bad Schlema;Altmarkt 1, Aue - Bad Schlema, 08280, Germany;50.5865356;12.7014864;43;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The long-established Hotel Blauer Engel is home to this small restaurant run by the dedicated and highly skilled Unger brothers. Claudius manages the restaurant floor while head chef Benjamin crafts a creative seasonal menu featuring three to seven meticulously presented courses, including dishes such as veal with beech mushrooms, gooseberry and parsley root. The kitchen team – including the head chef – join in serving and explain. The modern decor with a minimalist feel makes for an elegant and very inviting setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2561;tulus lotrek;Germany;Berlin;Fichtestraße 24, Berlin, 10967, Germany;52.4893627;13.4137112;74;false;true;Modern Cuisine, International;Why is this restaurant run by Ilona Scholl and Maximilian Strohe so popular? For one thing, there is the gorgeous setting. Housed in a pretty old building in Kreuzberg, the dining area boasts high stuccoed ceilings, wooden floors, artwork and original wallpaper. For another, the informal yet well-drilled front-of-house team, which is headed up by Scholl, fosters a friendly, laid-back atmosphere. But it is of course primarily the cuisine that draws diners in. The chef-patron and his kitchen team use premium ingredients to devise really interesting combinations. Their secret? Vibrant stocks and sauces that bring the different flavours together beautifully and give the dishes that certain something. The whole thing comes in the form of two 7-course menus: omnivorous or vegetarian. And don't miss the charming terrace.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2562;Esszimmer im Oberschwäbischen Hof;Germany;Schwendi;Hauptstrasse 9, Schwendi, 88477, Germany;48.1759617;9.975686;21;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;Since returning from his travels, which included stops at renowned restaurants such as Traube Tonbach in Baiersbronn and Söl'ring Hof on Sylt, Julius Reisch has been running his parents' business with unwavering dedication, and his wife Anna-Marie as maître d' and sommelier. The chef-patron creates ambitious fine dining experiences in the form of two set menus, one of them vegetarian. Built on classic foundations with a modern twist, his dishes are bold and flavoursome. The wine pairings are expertly selected – there is also a range of mature wines. The waitstaff are charming and adept, and from time to time the kitchen team also serves the dishes personally. In addition to Esszimmer, Oberschwäbischer Hof hotel has a second restaurant, Lazarus Stube.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2563;KUNO 1408;Germany;Würzburg;Neubaustraße 7, Würzburg, 97070, Germany;49.7904688;9.9305144;61;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This really lovely restaurant located in the centre of the Baroque city has a long tradition dating back to 1408. Kuno von Rebstock is said to have been one of the first owners of the Zum Rebstock estate at that time – hence the name. Today, diners can look forward to the ingredient-led cuisine of chef duo Robin Hofmann and Patrick Grieshaber. Creative modern dishes such as pike ceviche with carrot, egg and parmesan are served as part of a four- to six-course set menu by a well-drilled yet friendly and relaxed front-of-house team who give excellent advice on wine pairings. The restaurant itself is also pleasing on the eye, with its modern, elegant interior done out in warm and earthy tones and furnished with chic armchairs, and designer lamps. For overnight stays, the Hotel Rebstock proposes comfortable, individualised guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2564;Johanns;Germany;Waldkirchen;Marktplatz 24, Waldkirchen, 94065, Germany;48.729862;13.6007906;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;If you are looking to combine real fine dining with designer shopping, then head to the second floor of the renowned Garhammer shopping complex. At your table in the sleek, sophisticated surroundings, you can tuck into Michael Simon Reis's innovative take on Bavarian Forest cuisine. The Passau-born chef-patron has an aptitude for combining modern, traditional and seasonal elements, all the while placing great value on produce sourced from the region. It's fantastic value for money! Opt for the four- to six-course set menu or order à la carte. Dishes range from medium-rare barbecued saddle of venison with a purple curry glaze to lake sturgeon from Breitenberg with orange and chicory, or "Johanns schnitzel" (with meat from straw-bedded pigs) and "Johanns steak". The moderately priced set lunch menu is also popular. Tip: Head to the terrace for fantastic views of the region. Practical for motorists: the multi-storey car park at Garhammer department store, entry via Ringmauerstraße.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2565;Alte Liebe;Germany;Augsburg;Alpenstraße 21, Augsburg, 86159, Germany;48.3575728;10.8969716;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Chef-patron Benjamin Mitschele, a long-standing presence as a restaurateur in Augsburg, presents two concepts here. On Wednesdays and Thursdays, the place operates as a bistro serving small plates à la carte. On Fridays and Saturdays there is an accomplished tasting menu. In both cases, the well-thought-out dishes are full of flavour and personality. Close attention is paid to the quality and seasonality of ingredients, some of which come from the restaurant's own certified-organic nursery. Ambitious wine recommendations. The interior is pleasingly modern and the vibe relaxed. In summer, a nice terrace is set up on the pavement.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2566;Yunico;Germany;Bonn;Am Bonner Bogen 1, Bonn, 53227, Germany;50.718668;7.1525078;88;true;false;Japanese, Modern Cuisine;The name of this restaurant fuses the Japanese word "yu" and the Italian word "unico", hinting at the food served here. "Yunico" is also a reference to the uniquely high culinary standards they uphold. Situated on the top floor of the Kameha Grand lifestyle hotel, thanks to its floor-to-ceiling windows the restaurant affords a fantastic view of the Rhine – a view which is of course even better from the terrace. Then there is the smart, high-quality decor, all done out in red, black and white, as well as the experienced and well-coordinated front-of-house team. Head chef Christian Sturm-Willms delivers a highly contemporary take on Japanese cuisine that also looks to the Mediterranean for inspiration. Opt for the omakase menu if you want to be surprised. Alternatively, choose from the Ōsentikku set menu or the "Filet & Roastbeef" (Kobe beef).;Air conditioning,Great view,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2567;Sterneck;Germany;Cuxhaven;Cuxhavener Straße 86, Cuxhaven, 27476, Germany;53.886445;8.645506;76;true;true;Creative;A breathtaking view of the North Sea, the Elbe world shipping route and the UNESCO-listed Wadden Sea forms the backdrop for first-class cuisine served in the compact fine dining restaurant of Badhotel Sternhagen. This is the domain of Marc Rennhack, whose modern cooking builds on classical culinary foundations. He uses high-quality ingredients and has a knack for creating delicious dishes with just a few simple components. His sauces are particularly noteworthy. With consummate skill, he injects dishes with creative flair and conjures up interesting flavour combinations. His set menu comes in three to seven courses (there is also a vegetarian version). At five elegantly laid tables, diners are served cordially and attentively. The walk-in wine cellar – 3m below sea level – holds a large selection of fine wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2568;faelt;Germany;Berlin;Vorbergstraße 10A, Berlin, 10823, Germany;52.4892069;13.3548455;67;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;Housed in a listed building dating back to 1903, this restaurant is run in a down-to-earth yet professional and carefully considered way – and that goes for the atmosphere, the service and the food. The name (Swedish for "field") is a nod to the Nordic roots of the managing director Björn Swanson and the ingredient-led style of cooking cultivated by the kitchen team around Jan Rzehak. The modern, creative set menu is completely vegetarian and comprises six courses – if you prefer not to go without fish or meat, it is possible to order up to three additional courses. You can watch the chefs at work, as the kitchen is practically part of the dining area in this friendly, vibrant little establishment – perfect for a cosy get-together.;Terrace;[]
2569;Intense;Germany;Wachenheim an der Weinstraße;Weinstraße 31, Wachenheim an der Weinstraße, 67157, Germany;49.4385482;8.1820048;86;true;false;Fusion, Creative;In the centre of Wachenheim, opposite the church, Kirche St Georg, Bettina and Benjamin Peifer present their exciting concept! After welcome drinks and appetisers in Gud Stubb (the former vicarage), you are introduced to their culinary philosophy in the pantry, before taking a seat in the minimalist urban-style restaurant area, either at the counter with a direct view into the kitchen, at one of the small tables or in a koshitsu (a separate nook). A special fusion of the cuisines of the Palatinate and Japan is served. Think top-quality Rhine pike-perch sashimi served with delicately marinated yellow beetroot, lightly cooked slices of Jerusalem artichoke and fine shavings of black truffle, as well as an aromatic sauce with ponzu, soy and Perigord truffle. The open fire plays a major role, producing wonderful roasted flavours! The front-of-house team is always on hand, and the chef often brings out dishes himself. Music adds to the pleasant atmosphere. Hostess Bettina's wine, sake and non-alcoholic drink recommendations are always spot on.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
2570;SKYKITCHEN;Germany;Berlin;Landsberger Allee 106, Berlin, 10369, Germany;52.5282836;13.4565275;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It is worth making your way out to Lichtenberg: up here on the 12th floor of the Vienna House Andel's Berlin you have a fantastic view over the city. The decor has a chic urban feel, but also incorporates some striking vintage details, such as the old doors. Sascha Kurgan's excellent modern set menus, "Voyage Culinaire" and "Vegetarian", combine Mediterranean, Asian and regional accents in dishes such as dim sum made from an excellent noodle dough, filled with a ragout of braised pork chin with a little coriander, and served with a thick jellied dashi stock and a spicy chorizo oil. Complemented by poached egg yolk, edamame and spring onions, this culinary creation is full-bodied and packed with flavour. Pairings (wine or alcohol-free) are available on request. The wine list has an Eastern European focus – you can count on the highly professional yet pleasantly laid-back waitstaff to provide astute recommendations. Tip: Head up a couple more floors to Loft14 for a digestif!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2571;Wachter Foodbar;Germany;Prien am Chiemsee;Bernauer Straße 31, Prien am Chiemsee, 83209, Germany;47.8506316;12.3450485;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;In a former cookery school, chef-patron Dominik Wachter and his team have implemented an attractive modern "counter concept". In a very appealing and cosy atmosphere, you sit comfortably at the large bar in the middle of the space or at one of the high tables, from where you can watch the action at the kitchen pass unfold. Interesting, coherent dishes are created from predominantly regional ingredients and served as a set menu. They also propose a food-wine pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2572;mural farmhouse - FINE DINE;Germany;Munich;Gmunder Straße 27, Munich, 81379, Germany;48.0970386;11.5283963;70;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Committed to an absolutely sustainable farm-to-table concept, executive chef Timo Fritsche and his team are in tune with the times. They source their ingredients locally and use them in their entirety, and they also do their own fermenting and pickling. In their creative set menu, they combine, for example, a perfectly cooked and briefly flame-grilled char from Schliersee with pickled white asparagus from the previous season, a finely emulsified white dressing with slightly acidic notes and a subtly sweet herb sauce. Vegetarian and pescetarian versions of the set menu are also available. An all-you-can-drink water option is offered with the set menu. The wines are organic and biodynamic. Housed in Sendling's WunderLocke hotel, À LA CARTE and FINE DINE form a trendy and stylish dual dining concept. Incidentally, MICHELIN-starred mural is its sister restaurant.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2573;Shiraz;Germany;Wuppertal;Wittener Straße 288, Wuppertal, 42279, Germany;51.3027203;7.2518493;21;false;false;Classic French, Farm to table;It would be easy to drive straight past this small, slate-clad inn, where Serkan Akgün has been going it alone since 2017. Your welcoming host has dedicated more than the last 30 years of his life to hospitality. The world of wines, too, brings him – and his guests – enjoyment. Since October 2020, chef Alexander Hoppe has been creating modern cuisine that is rooted in classical culinary tradition and brimming with finesse and contrasts. Changing with the seasons, the menu includes dishes such as pike-perch served with risotto, dashi beurre blanc and chive oil. Excellent ingredients are just as much the focus here as the craftsmanship, flavour and original ideas. You always have the option of adding to the set menu. This lovely restaurant also has a terrace overlooking the Wupper Valley.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2575;Das Marktrestaurant;Germany;Mittenwald;Dekan-Karl-Platz 21, Mittenwald, 82481, Germany;47.4390442;11.2598384;32;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Much to the delight of his diners, Andreas Hillejan, originally from the Lower Rhine, moved to Upper Bavaria some years ago. Here in the beautiful village of Mittenwald, at the foot of the Karwendel Mountains, he serves up his own refined take on traditional pub food, resulting in some really crowd-pleasing dishes. Take a seat in the pleasingly informal, simple space and opt for one of the two set menus, "Wirtshaus mal anders" (also available in a vegetarian version) and "Heimat". Alternatively, an appealing selection of classics such as fish soup or Wiener schnitzel can be ordered à la carte. Before or after your meal, you might like to take a walk through the colourfully painted houses of this pretty historical town, which is renowned for its violin makers and climatic health resort – you won't have far to go, as the restaurant is very close to the pedestrian area.;Terrace;[]
2576;Cédric;Germany;Weinstadt;Marktstraße 39, Weinstadt, 71384, Germany;48.8044011;9.3885778;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic French;Cédric Staudenmayer is at the helm of this restaurant (formerly known as Krone), which is located in the Beutelsbach district. He cooks up ambitious modern cuisine based on classical foundations. Meat-free dishes such as "potato, onion, mushroom, green pepper" showcase the chef's ability to harmoniously balance bold flavours and contrasts. The set menu, which changes every two months, is also available in a vegetarian version if ordered in advance. Attentive service is provided by a friendly and highly adept front-of-house team. The building dates from 1800, and the classical, traditional interior has been revamped with subtle modern design features. Overnight accommodation is available at the Weinstadt Hotel next door.;;[]
2577;Wolfshöhle;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Konviktstraße 8, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79098, Germany;47.9944494;7.8547474;72;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Martin Fauster has found his feet in Freiburg, turning this restaurant into a mecca for foodies from the local area and beyond. Here in this beautifully maintained historical building in the pedestrian area, he keeps to his established path, serving up classically inspired cuisine. The quality of produce is remarkable, not least when it comes to the game dishes – the highlight being the distinctive, impeccably crafted sauces. The chef's Austrian homeland is also represented on the well-curated menu, with dishes such as Backhendl (breaded fried chicken) and Topfenknödel (curd dumplings). The friendly and professional waitstaff also provide astute wine recommendations. The attractive location in the old town makes the terrace a popular spot in summer. The restaurant is also open for lunch on Fridays and Saturdays, when a set menu is served in addition to the regular à la carte offerings. Parkhaus Schlossberggarage across the street is a convenient parking option.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2578;DIE GOURMET STUBE im Gasthaus Hummel;Germany;Duggendorf;Heitzenhofener Straße 16, Duggendorf, 93182, Germany;49.1161842;11.9136635;77;false;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;An elegant affair: clean lines, lovely natural materials and a palette of pale, warm tones make for a modern yet cosy atmosphere in the fine dining restaurant of the century-old Gasthaus Hummel. On entering the restaurant you can sneak a peek into the kitchen, where a seasonal five-course menu is put together under the supervision of chef-patron Stefan Hummel. Whenever possible, select ingredients for the very precisely prepared dishes are sourced from the region. You can look forward to finesse and an abundance of flavour – and great value for money. The dedication of the Hummel family is also plain to see in the friendly and competent front-of-house team, which is headed up by your cordial hostess. Alternatively, you might like to dine in the establishment's traditional local eatery. There are also four simple guestrooms.;Car park;[]
2579;Solo Du;Germany;Bischofswiesen;Berchtesgadener Straße 111, Bischofswiesen, 83483, Germany;47.6277007;12.9892613;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This space in the multifaceted Kulturhof is geared towards the traditional German card game "Schafkopf". But four days a week, it becomes a fine dining restaurant with four tables. A set menu with pleasingly pared-down dishes is proposed – these range from down-to-earth to classic or modern and creative. A vegetarian version of the menu is also available. Martin Bielik, your dedicated sommelier, provides astute wine recommendations. An amusing touch: the menu and wine list are laid out on the table as if they were a game of cards.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2580;Kettner's Kamota;Germany;Essen;Hufergasse 23, Essen, 45239, Germany;51.3889835;7.0014943;40;true;true;Creative, Alsatian;Chef Jürgen Kettner and his associate, Wiebke Meier, call their concept "New Austrian": Austrian tradition meets modern style in both the trendy, cosy setting and the food. With some originality, the Styrian-born chef uses excellent ingredients to create his own take on dishes from his homeland, which includes a smattering of Asian influences. There is a set menu with four or six courses as well as an additional pub menu with classics such as Backhendl (breaded fried chicken) or Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancakes). The short wine list includes a variety of organic labels and options by the glass. Tip: The shop sells Styrian delicacies.;Counter dining;[]
2581;Schwabenstube;Germany;Asperg;Stuttgarter Straße 2, Asperg, 71679, Germany;48.9046036;9.1352183;25;false;false;Classic French;Dedicated, cordial and consistent service is the name of the game in the Ottenbacher family establishment, a fact which can be put down to their long tradition of hospitality, which spans four generations! Here, they cultivate tradition and yet continue to evolve – as you can see in the spruce half-timbered house with its green shutters, where historical charm meets more modern and elegant design features. Moritz Feichtinger's classic cuisine also draws on the region for inspiration. There is a choice of three menus - including a vegan menu - and à la carte dishes. Diners can also look forward to an excellent wine list. Hotel Adler has comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2582;Masters;Germany;Blankenhain;Lindenallee 1, Blankenhain, 99444, Germany;50.8747844;11.3422232;43;true;false;Modern French, Mediterranean Cuisine;With just 16 covers, the tasteful little restaurant of the Spa & GolfResort Weimarer Land has a pleasantly intimate character. Comfortable armchairs, a beautiful decoration and a cosy atmosphere provide the perfect setting for the set menu devised by chef Danny Schwabe and his ambitious team. The food is a creative take on French cuisine. Sophisticated wine pairings. The friendly and charming service staff are supported on the restaurant floor by the kitchen team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2583;Alte Baiz;Germany;Neuhausen;Hauptstraße 2, Neuhausen, 75242, Germany;48.8182484;8.7698838;46;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;At Alte Baiz, an upscale setting with charming rustic-style overtones and Claudio Urru's modern-inspired cuisine await you. A lot of thought goes into his cooking, and his dishes are always on point in terms of flavour, regardless of whether you opt for the four- to seven-course set menu (you can also order dishes from these à la carte) or choose from the daily specials on the à la carte menu. There is also an interesting selection of dishes for two, such as veal chops, whole roast Kikok chicken (served in two courses) or Breton loup de mer (sea bass). Interesting wine pairings by the glass to accompany the set menu. Friendly and adept service. If you would like a good beer to kick off the meal, try their house-brewed CALVA NIGRA.;Car park;[]
2584;FAVORITE restaurant;Germany;Mainz;Karl-Weiser-Straße 1, Mainz, 55131, Germany;49.9899559;8.289494;34;true;false;Modern French, Creative;Located in Mainz's city park and run by the dedicated Barth family, FAVORITE parkhotel is a sophisticated place to stay, but it is also popular in its own right as a place to eat. Tobias Schmitt is in charge of the kitchen at the fine dining restaurant. His classical style of cooking has a modern edge and features his own cleverly integrated ideas. A shining example of the excellent quality of the ingredients is the first-class halibut from France, which is served with aromatic creamed Savoy cabbage and fruity grape and successfully contrasted with spicy-smoky bacon, as well as a frothy, buttery champagne sauce boasting a beautiful acidity. The set menu dubbed "From Roots to Blossom" is available in a four- to eight-course format, or you can pick and choose à la carte dishes. As for the restaurant itself, it boasts a refined and elegant interior. Your best bet is to ask for a table by the window – or dine on the beautiful terrace overlooking the Rhine and Taunus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2585;Le Jardin de France im Stahlbad;Germany;Baden-Baden;Augustaplatz 2, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7595;8.23999;87;true;true;Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine;Sophie and Stéphan Bernhard have made it their mission to indulge the diners of this city since 1998. Now they operate in the Stahlbad, a beautiful 19C building and former spa hotel in the centre of Baden-Baden, and also previously home to a Michelin-starred restaurant. A delightful ground-level conservatory affords views of the verdant surroundings and converts into a covered terrace in summer. The classic French cuisine by the chef-patron, a native Frenchman, is as much in great demand as it ever was. The dishes are ingredient-led, clearly structured and wonderfully harmonious. The front-of-house team, which includes the proprietress, is exceptionally cordial and accomplished, and the wine recommendations are second to none – the available selection is excellent. Tip: Attractively priced lunch deal Tue-Fri.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2586;The First;Germany;Blankenhain;Lindenallee 1, Blankenhain, 99444, Germany;50.8747868;11.3423392;96;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;The restaurant of the attractive Spa & GolfResort Weimarer Land serves Italian-inspired dishes with classical influences. Head chef Marcello Fabbri has made a name for himself in the region. He proposes a five-course menu made with excellent produce from Italy – his pasta is a real treat. The waitstaff are friendly and highly proficient, and the sommelier's recommendations are spot on. The decor is also lovely and has a partially open kitchen. The terrace is delightful in summer!;Car park,Terrace;[]
2587;Gasthof Alex;Germany;Weißenbrunn;Gössersdorf 25, Weißenbrunn, 96369, Germany;50.188066;11.4062317;68;true;false;Farm to table, Creative;Chef-patron Domenik Alex and Madlen Häckel represent the fifth generation to run this family business, which has been in existence since 1886. "A balance between living tradition and creative zeitgeist" is their motto. The cuisine is seasonal and rich in flavour and finesse, with creative dishes that draw on modern influences, are pared down to the essentials and clearly structured. Some of the ingredients are in fact home-grown. Warm wood and sleek design make for an attractive setting in which to enjoy the friendly and competent service provided by the proprietress. Comfortable guestrooms available, should you wish to stay overnight.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2588;TAWA YAMA FINE;Germany;Karlsruhe;Amalienbadstraße 41b, Karlsruhe, 76227, Germany;48.9958493;8.4659391;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Located in the RaumFabrik business park, FINE is TAWA YAMA's stylish fine dining restaurant. The modern cuisine abounds with original ideas, with subtle dishes taking inspiration from the Far Eastern pantry, as in the hamachi served with oyster cream, yuzu koshō and leek. The set menu is made up of four to seven courses during the week and five to seven courses at the weekend – upgrades are possible. A vegetarian set menu is also available by prior arrangement. In a fittingly modern and sophisticated interior, diners can opt for seats that afford a view through a window into the kitchen. The friendly front-of-house team provides enjoyably unobtrusive service, while the sommelier helps with the wine selection. Incidentally, the Japanese name "TAWA YAMA" means "tower mountain" – a reference to the Turmberg outside Karlsruhe, which you can look out onto from the pleasant terrace. In addition to FINE, there is the trendy EASY. On a practical note: you can use the private parking garage free of charge.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2589;SoulFood;Germany;Auerbach in der Oberpfalz;Unterer Markt 35, Auerbach in der Oberpfalz, 91275, Germany;49.6928628;11.6302869;50;false;true;International, Farm to table;Here, Christine Heß and Michael Laus really deliver on their appealing "soul food" concept. After working side by side at Frankfurt's Villa Merton, the two have fulfilled their dream of owning their own restaurant. Here, in their establishment located right next to Auerbach town hall, the owner demonstrates a knack for creative cuisine. Made using top-notch seasonal produce, his dishes are really interesting and precisely crafted, right down to the last detail – for example, Oriental meatballs, hummus, parsley salsa, sesame, chickpeas, pomegranate, walnuts – this is real soul food, which is also reasonably priced! Diners are given a choice of two set menus: "DasEine" or "DasAndere", and individual courses can also be swapped in or out. The cordial owner looks after guests – furthermore, it is the chef who brings out the aperitif nibbles at the beginning. A lovely modern restaurant that serves simply excellent food!;;[]
2590;Aska;Germany;Regensburg;Watmarkt 5, Regensburg, 93047, Germany;49.0200415;12.0963365;67;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Two restaurants with Swedish names under one roof. In contrast to the original restaurant (Storstad), Aska is a compact sushi restaurant with a decidedly personal touch. The name translates as "ash", and the interior is accordingly dark in hue. Diners sit at the counter or one of the few booth tables to enjoy authentic sushi served just the way it is in Japan. You can choose between an eight- or 10-course set menu – with the option of additional courses. Having learned his craft in his hometown of Osaka, sushi master Atsushi Sugimoto now transforms premium ingredients into the best classic sushi to be found far and wide! The pleasant ambience is also largely down to the attentive and charming front-of-house staff, who will be able to recommend just the right sake to accompany your set menu. Plus there is a "flat rate" for all-you-can-drink mineral water and green tea – a highly unusual offer in Germany!;Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
2591;IKO;Germany;Osnabrück;Stadtweg 38a, Osnabrück, 49086, Germany;52.2697166;8.1281943;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Three areas – "Iko-Flowers", "Iko-Atelier" and "Iko-Restaurant" – have been successfully created here. The result is an appealingly sleek, modern interior with a trendy rustic feel, floral decorations from the adjoining shop and handmade tableware from the integrated pottery workshop. In the open kitchen, select ingredients go into a modern and creative set menu comprising five or seven courses (vegetarian options available). Most ingredients are sourced locally, and the restaurant works closely with its suppliers. The chefs serve the dishes themselves. Ask the charming and well-trained waitstaff about the house's own range of alcohol-free cocktails. Tip: Book a seat at the kitchen counter for an interesting glimpse behind the scenes. Pretty garden terrace. Good to know: They also offer pottery classes.;Terrace;[]
2593;Le temple;Germany;Neuhütten;Saarstraße 2, Neuhütten, 54422, Germany;49.6425213;7.0114426;43;true;false;Modern French;Christiane Detemple-Schäfer and Oliver Schäfer form an absolute dream team. Your friendly hosts have been working side by side here since 1992 and their impressive dedication to the task has made Le temple a permanent fixture on the fine dining scene – not only in the small town of Neuhütten, but also among the Michelin-starred restaurants of Rhineland-Palatinate. This is a modern and creative take on classic cuisine – delicate, elaborate and extremely meticulous – to be enjoyed in the form of set menus, which change with the seasons. The interior of this elegant and minimalist restaurant is tastefully furnished, as is the small cigar lounge next door. If you want to spend a night amid the beautiful landscape of the Hunsrück, you can do so in cosy guestrooms – a delicious breakfast is also available. A nice alternative is the bistro with regional cuisine.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2594;Schwitzer's Gourmet-Restaurant;Germany;Waldbronn;Etzenroter Straße 4, Waldbronn, 76337, Germany;48.9209362;8.4748202;19;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This chic little fine dining restaurant has recently relocated to what was once the bar of Schwitzer's Hotel am Park. Here, owner Cédric Schwitzer proposes classic and at the same time modern cuisine made from high-quality produce. The food is cooked in front of the guests. There is a six-course set menu, either with fish and meat or as a vegetarian version. Diners can either sit at regular tables or the counter, and are waited on by friendly and attentive staff.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2596;1789;Germany;Baiersbronn;Tonbachstraße 237, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5369525;8.3582841;75;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences;Mit dem "1789" hat Küchenchef Florian Stolte seine eigene Bühne und ergänzt das gastronomische Konzept der "Traube Tonbach" perfekt. In zwei 6-gängigen Menüs, eines davon rein vegetarisch, präsentiert er seine eigene Handschrift. Er kocht klar und modern, wobei sich asiatische Einflüsse durch das Menü ziehen und Kontraste schaffen. Die Spitzenqualität der Produkte stellt er gekonnt in den Fokus, wenn er beispielsweise beim klassisch roh servierten, saftig-zarten und subtil gewürzten Langustinen-Carpaccio den Eigengeschmack toll zur Geltung bringt oder beim gegrillten und nur minimal gesalzenen Filet vom Wagyu Beef das wunderbare Fleischaroma hervorhebt. Das Restaurant selbst kommt intim, minimalistisch und zugleich wertig-chic daher, die Atmosphäre ist angenehm locker, der Service sehr geschult, freundlich und gut besetzt.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2597;ZweiSinn Meiers | Fine Dining;Germany;Nuremberg;Äußere Sulzbacher Straße 118, Nuremberg, 90491, Germany;49.4641108;11.1184521;71;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This stylish, modern restaurant just outside Nuremberg's city centre is a welcome addition to the fine dining scene in the Franconian metropolis. Following stints working at first-class establishments such as Louis C. Jacob in Hamburg, Amador in Langen, and under Johanna Maier in Filzmoos, Austria, Stefan Meier struck out on his own a few years ago. Together with a motivated kitchen team, he combines the finest hand-selected ingredients to create imaginative dishes brimming with beautifully balanced flavours. Vegetarians are also catered for. Last but not least, the professional, friendly and attentive service also contributes to the feel-good atmosphere in this chic, minimalist-style restaurant.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2598;Hupperts;Germany;Stuttgart;Gebelsbergstraße 97, Stuttgart, 70199, Germany;48.7613472;9.1513479;64;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Located in the middle of a residential area in the south of Stuttgart, this gem is not easy to find but is well worth seeking out! Run with great dedication, the restaurant has a tasteful interior, and attentive service comes courtesy of an accomplished front-of-house team under the management of Claudia Johnson. But perhaps the main draw is the food served up by chef-patron Michael Huppert. His really innovative set menu cleverly integrates contrasts, with a focus on top-notch, predominantly regional produce. Tip: In summer, be sure to secure a spot on the delightful terrace to the side of the building.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2599;Restaurant Brogsitter - Historisches Gasthaus Sanct Peter;Germany;Bad Neuenahr-Ahrweiler;Walporzheimer Straße 134, Bad Neuenahr-Ahrweiler, 53474, Germany;50.5306779;7.0780355;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;As early as the 13C, this place was known for its wine as the wine estate of Cologne's cathedral chapter. In that regard, nothing has changed to this day, because this enchanting restaurant is now owned by the Brogsitter family, who can look back on a long tradition of winemaking. The cuisine here is classic in its foundations and draws on modern and international influences. The set menu, comprising four to six courses, includes dishes such as lobster carpaccio with picked crab, heart of palm and curry vinaigrette. The wine list is extensive, with a good selection of wines by the glass, including some from the restaurant's own winery. The lunch offerings are also excellent – the "Gourmet Lunch" is a shortened version of the evening set menu. Adept service comes courtesy of a friendly and unflappable team. The interior is chic and elegant, with a high gabled ceiling and a spectacular Murano chandelier. There is also a lovely terrace.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2600;KAI3;Germany;Hörnum;Am Kai 3, Hörnum, 25997, Germany;54.7611439;8.2962752;29;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;"Nordic Fusion" is the name of the game in the fine dining restaurant of the luxurious BUDERSAND Hotel - Golf & Spa marvellously located on the southernmost tip of Sylt. Chef Felix Gabel whisks you off on a creative culinary adventure. He uses select local produce and draws on influences from around the globe, skilfully incorporating a host of different spices and flavours. A choice of two set menus is proposed ("Große Aromenreise" and the vegetarian "Kraut & Rüben"). In keeping with the cuisine, the modern decor has a distinct Nordic charm. And then there is the stunning view of the North Sea afforded by the floor-to-ceiling windows. All this is accompanied by skilful and cordial service which also provides excellent advice on wine. The establishment is also known for its cultural events.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2601;Aubergine;Germany;Starnberg;Münchner Straße 17, Starnberg, 82319, Germany;48.0017757;11.3498541;75;false;true;Creative;Haute gastronomie in a business hotel? Yes – you can experience this in the fine dining restaurant of the comfortable Vier Jahreszeiten Starnberg hotel. In a glass-paned extension reminiscent of a conservatory, sit back and enjoy the creative cuisine of Maximilian Moser in the upscale, elegant and modern interior. In his two set menus (one of which is vegetarian), he brings in international influences, as well as seasonal produce. The service team are courteous and competent, and the wine recommendations are also on point. Tip: Keep an eye on the culinary calendar – you'll find interesting offers here.;Wheelchair access;[]
2602;DiVa;Germany;Scharbeutz;Strandallee 146, Scharbeutz, 23683, Germany;54.0099541;10.7702772;41;true;true;Modern French, International;The Mediterranean feel of the Hotel Gran BelVeder, located right by the Baltic Sea beach, extends to this small fine dining restaurant with an elegant interior done out in warm tones. Despite the beautiful location on the Bay of Lübeck, you will unfortunately have to do without a sea view, unless you sit outside on the terrace! But Gunter Ehinger's classically based cuisine deserves your full attention anyway. He uses excellent ingredients including in-season regional produce such as venison from the Ellerbrock hunters, as well as international specialities. One standout among many sophisticated pairings features delicate langoustine with salsify and cuttlefish noodles, complemented by a refined, gently spiced jalapeño foam and the preserved juice of locally grown tomatoes offering wonderfully natural aromatics. For the set menu there are excellent wine pairings, available by the glass. It is also possible to order à la carte. Attentive, well-trained staff.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2603;ESS ATELIER STRAUSS;Germany;Oberstdorf;Kirchstraße 1, Oberstdorf, 87561, Germany;47.4085094;10.2783328;41;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Upscale furniture fashioned out of salvaged wood, comfortable designer chairs upholstered in lovely check fabrics, edelweiss-shaped lighting fixtures set into the ceiling, and pared-down, elegant tableware – this restaurant has a fresh and modern decor. But it isn't just the chic Alpine look that guests go in for. The dishes conjured up by chef Peter A Strauss are equally inspiring. You will be treated to pleasingly stripped-down classic cuisine that takes inspiration in modern, creative trends. The ingredients are always first-rate and predominantly locally sourced. Only a seasonal surprise menu is served here – no à la carte. The striking glass-fronted wine cooler houses an impressive selection of bottles.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2604;Silberdistel;Germany;Ofterschwang;Sonnenalp 1, Ofterschwang, 87527, Germany;47.4904129;10.2570174;63;false;true;Classic Cuisine;The Sonnenalp Resort, which has been run by the Fäßler family since 1919, is definitely worth a visit for anyone interested in fine dining. Silberdistel's kitchen team uses select seasonal ingredients. The "Weitblick" menu with up to seven courses is offered. Tip: Before, with or between the courses you can order caviar from Walter Grüll from Salzburg. On Fridays and Sundays there are classics. Here on the fourth floor, you are afforded wonderful views, so be sure to ask for a window seat. Having said that, the restaurant interior itself, with its blend of stylish elegance and Alpine charm, is also a sight to behold. Then there is the enthusiastic sense of hospitality, which makes itself felt throughout this traditional establishment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2605;Restaurant auf Schloss Filseck;Germany;Uhingen;Filseck 1, Uhingen, 73066, Germany;48.7000691;9.6048158;52;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;Not only is Schloss Filseck a museum, cultural centre and venue for events, it is also a hotspot for foodies! The decor is classic in style, incorporating modern touches, A wooden ceiling and quarry-stone walls add an old-fashioned, rustic charm to proceedings. There is also a wonderful terrace in the interior courtyard. Head chef Daniele Corona clearly draws much of his inspiration from Italy and elsewhere in the Mediterranean, creating highly ambitious and multi-faceted dishes such as "Toscana" (Chianina beef, rocket, bagnetto verde). In the evening, the fine dining set menu also comes in a vegetarian version. There is a well-stocked wine list, and the staff provide astute recommendations. The concept is completely different at lunchtime: the "mezzogiorno" lunch deal is simpler and inexpensive. The ree shuttle service within a 20km radius of the castle is really handy.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2606;Orangerie;Germany;Timmendorfer Strand;Strandallee 73, Timmendorfer Strand, 23669, Germany;54.0008609;10.7796793;42;true;false;Classic French;To experience a true institution of the Baltic Sea, look no further than this elegant fine dining restaurant in a side wing of the Maritim Seehotel. Classic dishes, prepared by a dedicated kitchen team, are served à la carte or in a three- to seven-course set menu format. Examples include langoustine with Périgord truffle, Jerusalem artichoke and a crustacean jus or cheek and Secreto of Ibérico pork with Brussels sprouts and charcoal aromas. The icing on the cake is the friendly and professional front-of-house team overseen by sommelier Ralf Brönner – you can be confident of judicious wine recommendations. A terrace overlooks the small park and the Baltic Sea promenade.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2607;Anima;Germany;Tuttlingen;In Wöhrden 5, Tuttlingen, 78532, Germany;47.9863428;8.82098;68;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;On the ground floor of a modern building, the minimalist-style dining space offers a view of the outside through floor-to-ceiling windows – only a hedge separates you from the Danube. In the open kitchen, chef Heiko Lacher expresses his personality – this also explains the name "Anima" (the Latin word for "soul"). His style is a creative and equally harmonious combination of different culinary cultures, not least French and Italian. Working with excellent produce, beautiful flavour combinations are achieved, to which home-grown herbs also contribute. Oysters or caviar are available as an optional addition to the set menu.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2608;Gourmetrestaurant Berlins Krone;Germany;Bad Teinach-Zavelstein;Marktplatz 2, Bad Teinach-Zavelstein, 75385, Germany;48.6940108;8.6892208;32;true;false;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;This place has it all: a cosy atmosphere, extremely friendly and well-drilled service, as well as excellent food. Formerly named Gasthaus Krone, the Berlin family's restaurant has been a mecca for foodies for years – no wonder there are so many regulars! Chef-patron Franz Berlin presides in the kitchen, overseeing a successful fusion of classic cuisine and modern influences. The four to seven courses of his seasonally inspired set menu are harmoniously composed and presented with a refreshing clarity, a case in point being the cod, pan-seared with the skin on, with veal head ragout, pak choi and a horseradish and blood orange foam. A vegetarian set menu is also available by prior arrangement. When it comes to wine recommendations, you can certainly put your faith in the sommelier – he has a story to tell about pretty much every wine in his collection. For overnight stays there are comfortable guestrooms and decent spa facilities.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
2609;Délice;Germany;Stuttgart;Hauptstätter Straße 61, Stuttgart, 70178, Germany;48.7702819;9.1762495;54;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;An evening here has a distinctly exclusive feel, which can be attributed not least to the intimate setting – with just a handful of tables, the small and friendly team manages to bring a personal touch to your interactions. As maître d' and sommelier, Andreas Lutz provides courteous and highly competent service and astute wine recommendations. Andreas Hettinger (now also owner of the restaurant) continues to run the open kitchen, where he turns excellent ingredients into harmonious dishes that draw on classic, Mediterranean and creative influences, such as "spaghettini, Oscietra caviar, olive oil, chives" or "cod, potato and fennel purée, pepper, leek, chamomile". These are presented in a seasonal surprise menu, to be enjoyed in an attractive space with a barrel-vaulted ceiling. It is possible to reduce the number of courses from five to four.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2610;Rebers Pflug;Germany;Schwäbisch Hall;Weckriedener Straße 2, Schwäbisch Hall, 74523, Germany;49.1231266;9.7569147;51;false;true;Farm to table;As soon as you enter the restaurant, you will pass the open kitchen, which is sure to whet your appetite. The menu is really wide-ranging, from regional classics such as Tafelspitz (beef boiled in broth) or Rostbraten (roast beef), to the set menu ("Pflüg-Genießer-Menü") comprising three to six courses – these might include cod slices in saffron mussel broth, fennel kimchi, salted lemon and Duroc lardo. There is also a three- or four-course vegetarian tasting menu. And then there are the prized steaks! Naturally, chef-patron Hans-Harald Reber gets his excellent meat from his trusted butcher, who happens to be a second cousin of his. You can soak up the friendly and pleasantly informal atmosphere, safe in the knowledge you will be looked after attentively by the proficient front-of-house team. Plus you have the option of booking one of the comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2612;Eisenbahn;Germany;Schwäbisch Hall;Karl-Kurz-Straße 2, Schwäbisch Hall, 74523, Germany;49.0988122;9.7702979;83;false;true;Modern French;The experience and ideas of two generations are to be found in the Wolf family establishment. This is also true of the food in this restaurant, which has held a Michelin star since 1997. It draws inspiration from both classic cooking and modern, international cuisine. Diners can expect choice ingredients, delicate aromas and an intense hit of flavour. This is a kitchen that focuses on the essentials and eschews frills. The dishes are served in the form of a seasonal set menu, available in a varying number of courses. In addition to the excellent culinary fare, you can look forward to cordial and professional service. The tasteful interior and the pretty terrace behind the house are also inviting. And there is a fabulous international selection of wines. The Bistro s'Bähnle provides more dining options. You can also stay overnight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2613;BODENDORF'S;Germany;Tinnum;Boy-Nielsen-Straße 10, Tinnum, 25980, Germany;54.9010855;8.3328345;82;true;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;The fine dining restaurant of the gorgeous Landhaus Stricker proposes a fun culinary experience that comes courtesy of the team led by Holger Bodendorf and Denis Brühl. Meticulous work goes into preparing a set menu comprising clearly structured dishes based on classical foundations. Top-notch ingredients are used to create delectable combinations such as Breton cod with an intense nut butter foam, or US prime beef onglet with an exquisite peppery jus. The restaurant itself is impressive, too, with its fresh, modern design – a chic backdrop for the friendly young front-of-house team, who provide adept service while maintaining a relaxed atmosphere. Astute wine recommendations are also provided – they have over 1 200 labels. Tip: Head to the trendy Miles Bar for an aperitif before dinner.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2614;Schwarzer Adler;Germany;Vogtsburg im Kaiserstuhl;Badbergstraße 23, Vogtsburg im Kaiserstuhl, 79235, Germany;48.0952162;7.6560639;73;true;true;Classic French;A veritable culinary institution! Here you can experience hospitality that has retained all the charm and tradition of a bygone era despite the odd concession to modern times. Owner Fritz Keller is fully supportive of chef Christian Baur's bid to continue cooking in the classic French style that is synonymous with the legendary Schwarzer Adler. How about a glorious beurre blanc served with a piece of perfectly cooked turbot? The wonderfully robust and flavourful dishes that are carved at your table (for two or more people) are also highly recommended. This cosy, stylish and elegant restaurant will go down well with wine lovers due to a sensational wine list that includes an impressive range of Bordeaux vintages. There are also wines from the house winery, which has been in the family for three generations. Tasteful guestrooms are available should you wish to stay the night. You also have the option of dining at Winzerhaus Rebstock, which serves up simpler and more traditional fare.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2615;Genuss-Apotheke;Germany;Bad Säckingen;Schönaugasse 11, Bad Säckingen, 79713, Germany;47.551733;7.9480494;82;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;All that remains of the pharmacy that once stood here is the mention it gets in this establishment's name. These days, a restaurant with a fresh, modern concept awaits you behind its large windows. Seated at beautifully laid tables in a bright, minimalist interior, diners find their gaze drawn to the open kitchen. Here, chef-patron Raimar Pilz cooks creatively with top-notch ingredients. He always successfully incorporates piquant herbs in his subtle and nuanced dishes, cf. his Black Forest beef, butternut squash, rock salt onion. A fine dining six- to eight- course set menu is served every evening, at a lower price during the week. Another factor in how at home you feel here is the cordial and attentive service team, who also have plenty of astute wine recommendations. Tip: Take a stroll through the beautiful old town!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2617;Balthasar;Germany;Paderborn;Warburger Straße 28, Paderborn, 33098, Germany;51.7152518;8.7638033;84;true;true;Modern French, Farm to table;A porthole window in the entrance area provides a peek into the kitchen, setting the stage for an evening of gastronomic pleasure from the moment you arrive. Once seated at your impeccably laid table, you can appreciate the elegant setting and attentive and professional service overseen by your host and sommelier, Laura Simon. With her refreshingly straightforward manner enhancing the welcoming ambiance, chef-patron Elmar Simon creates contemporary dishes rooted in classic cuisine. There are two set menus: one with meat and one vegetarian. The courses from both can also be ordered à la carte. The superior quality of ingredients and the chef's knack for creating harmonious combinations of elements and flavours are showcased in dishes such as the outstanding, firm-fleshed Breton turbot, accompanied by broad beans, horseradish and an intensely flavoursome beurre blanc sauce.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2618;Wullenwever;Germany;Lübeck;Beckergrube 71, Lübeck, 23552, Germany;53.8696544;10.682255;56;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The exterior of this patrician house (1585) located in the heart of Lübeck is just as beautiful and charming as its interior, which is adorned with decorative artworks. Roy Petermann serves up classic cuisine with Mediterranean accents, in which first-rate ingredients take centre stage. There is a set menu (written in beautiful calligraphy) that changes every three weeks, comprising three or five courses , as well as a seven-course surprise menu, which can be pre-ordered for the whole table. Vegetarians are also catered for. The excellent wine list is principally devoted to labels from Germany and Europe, but it does also venture as far as the New World. Professional service befitting the elegant setting comes courtesy of your charming hostess Manuela Petermann and team. The inner courtyard with its lovely verdant terrace is wonderful!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2619;Wonka;Germany;Nuremberg;Johannisstraße 38, Nuremberg, 90419, Germany;49.4586974;11.0648669;48;true;false;Creative, Asian Influences;Christian Wonka has been running this charming restaurant for over 20 years, serving up ambitious, flavoursome cuisine made using regional produce, eschewing all unnecessary frills. The clear and unfussy composition of the dishes, each of which is made up of just a few components (such as cod, Chinese cabbage, orange) make for a winning formula. Asian influences (eg wan tan, tempeh, miso) result in beautiful, well-balanced contrasts. In the evening, a creative set menu comprising five or six courses is proposed – a vegan version is also available. A pared-down iteration of the set menu, featuring some dishes from the evening selection, is served at lunchtime. In addition to various tastefully decorated dining areas, there is a delightful courtyard terrace. The restaurant is easily accessible by tram.;Terrace;[]
2620;Seesteg;Germany;Norderney;Damenpfad 36a, Norderney, 26548, Germany;53.7075465;7.1389104;91;false;true;Modern Cuisine, International;It is a real stroke of luck that Markus Kebschull, a native of Baden-Württemberg, has set up shop in the far north of Germany. Previously stationed at Cuxhaven's Sterneck, he has been head chef here since 2012. This restaurant is housed in a small boutique hotel of the same name just a stone's throw from the sea on the beautiful island of Norderney. Based on classical foundations, his style of cooking also incorporates the odd modern twist. Top-notch ingredients, sourced locally whenever possible, go into flavoursome dishes such as Helgoland lobster bisque, spring roll, melon. There are two set menus (one of them vegetarian), as well as a small à la carte selection of classics. The interior is welcoming and stylish with its open kitchen and delightful views of the North Sea. Tip: Head for the seaside terrace!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2621;Wirtshaus Meyers Keller;Germany;Nördlingen;Marienhöhe 8, Nördlingen, 86720, Germany;48.8413149;10.493869;18;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;This place is something special. Joachim (also known as Jockl) Kaiser and his wife are the third generation to run this appealingly rustic and trendy restaurant. The kitchen concept is intriguing: In addition to the tavern classics, they propose a seasonal set menu consisting of a "starter", "centrepiece" and "finale". A nice idea: You are free to choose one or more of the "centrepiece" dishes – vegetarian options included. Adept service comes courtesy of an exceedingly friendly and pleasingly down-to-earth front-of-house team. Good to know: Be sure to sample the Culatello ham that they mature in the old beer cellar beneath you! In summer you can sit out on the terrace planted with old lime trees and chestnut trees. Head to the shop if you'd like to buy a souvenir.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2622;THE LISBETH;Germany;Hamburg;Deichstraße 32, Hamburg, 20459, Germany;53.5462616;9.9873002;66;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Chef André Stolle is no stranger to Hamburg, having previously cooked at various places here, including Se7en Oceans. With THE LISBETH, he has struck out on his own in one of the city's oldest streets. Located in a neighbourhood full of Hanseatic charm, this trendy little restaurant has a pleasantly laid-back and intimate feel to it. Hamburg and North German cuisine are given a sophisticated modern twist in a four- to five-course set menu, with intriguing dishes such as "Don't call it Labskaus" – Herring 'Bismarck Style', beetroot, egg yolk & veal.  If you wish, you can choose a classic as an upgrade.;;[]
2623;La Vallée Verte;Germany;Herleshausen;Hohenhaus 1, Herleshausen, 37293, Germany;51.0410088;10.0801288;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine, French;Picturesquely located in a gorgeous landscape of forest and meadows, this wonderful stately home and castle (dating back to 1901) was originally a manor. In this compact restaurant, executive chef and host Peter Niemann and the kitchen team home in on excellent ingredients from the nearby surroundings, including game they hunt themselves. They successfully incorporate the flavours of Brittany and Scandinavia into their fish and seafood specialities. The restaurant's seven- or nine-course tasting menu is an elaborate and detailed affair, from the numerous aperitifs before the meal to dishes such as venison, parsnip and currant. The highly attentive and competent front-of-house team will also be able to help when it comes to expert wine recommendations. Overnight accommodation available at Hotel Schloss Hohenhaus.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2624;Showroom;Germany;Munich;Lilienstraße 6, Munich, 81169, Germany;48.130492;11.587331;93;false;false;Creative;The owners are having a little fun with the name of this restaurant, which, although centrally located, is somewhat tucked away. It has a pleasingly laid-back, modern and unpretentious atmosphere that allows the cuisine to take centre stage. Led by head chef Dominik Käppeler, the kitchen team serves up elaborate, highly detailed and meticulously prepared cuisine that abounds with contrasts and flavours. Dishes such as pike-perch with miso, coffee, celery and date keep diners on their toes. The six- to eight-course surprise menu showcases the finest ingredients and changes every 14 days. Urban-style decor and attentive, friendly and expert service that includes interesting wine recommendations.;Terrace;[]
2625;Zwanzig23 by Lukas Jakobi;Germany;Düsseldorf;Brunnenstraße 35, Düsseldorf, 40223, Germany;51.2061397;6.7789529;87;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;In October 2023, Lukas Jakobi unveiled an intriguing, trendy and modern culinary concept in Düsseldorf's Bilk neighbourhood. The two set menus, "Vegan" and "Nicht vegan", comprise six or nine flavoursome courses made using excellent ingredients. "Taste the Waste – Some sexy stuff", for example, demonstrates the restaurant's commitment to sustainability. With a variety of components it contributes to waste reduction and presents "leftovers" in a sophisticated culinary way. Some 80% of the produce is sourced from the region. Fermented foods, soy sauces, garums and kombuchas are all produced on site, along with extracts and juices. Food is served at counter seats right next to the open kitchen, or you can opt for a standard table.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2626;MIND;Germany;Markt Indersdorf;Dachauer Straße 11, Markt Indersdorf, 85229, Germany;48.3614245;11.3773779;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;With a deft hand, the chefs here reinterpret familiar flavour profiles with their own unique twist without compromising authenticity or succumbing to pretentiousness. Dishes such as beetroot, sour cream and cucumber or liver, potato and boskoop strike a perfect balance between boldness and refinement. The two set menus, "MINDs Choice" and "MINDs Fein & Ohne" (vegetarian), can be extended to include a cheese course. The front of the restaurant offers a view of the kitchen island, where chef Sabrina Fenzl can be seen hard at work. At the back there is a more relaxed space with electronic music playing. The service is professional and pleasingly efficient – the chef is also on hand to talk you through the dishes.;;[]
2628;Das Grace;Germany;Flensburg;Fördepromenade 30, Flensburg, 24944, Germany;54.8119855;9.4556862;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;A former naval building right on the marina houses The James, a sophisticated hotel that is also home to this chic and elegant restaurant. The 7m-high ceiling and chandeliers draped in silk make quite an impression, as do the views of the marina from some of the seats. The exclusive atmosphere is enhanced by the friendly and attentive front-of-house team, who serve up Quirin Brundobler's modern, seasonal cuisine in the form of two set menus: "Farm" and "Fjord". His dishes, such as Hörup pork cheeks or lightly seared sole, may be pleasingly uncomplicated, but they are brimming with flavour. Much of the produce comes from the restaurant's own James Farm or from local fields, meadows and waters. Alternative dining options are to be found at James Farmhouse, where chefs cook in front of diners, and Japanese restaurant Minato. On top of that, you have The Lion bar as well as "Tea Time & More" by the fireplace in the James Livingroom.;;[]
2629;Bonvivant;Germany;Berlin;Goltzstraße 32, Berlin, 10781, Germany;52.4946425;13.3537639;87;false;false;Vegetarian;Bonvivant is an original in many respects. You are offered a vegan set menu with five or six courses. The absence of meat and fish in no way detracts from the experience – intense flavours are often underscored by the use of the barbecue grill. Many of the ingredients used in the high-calibre cuisine are sourced from Brandenburg, providing an insight into local produce. Interesting accompaniments for the delicious mains are also afforded importance, plus there are original and sophisticated drinks and cocktails. In a laid-back, relaxed atmosphere, the dedicated young service team elaborate on the individual courses of the set menu and drink pairings – a successful concept!;Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2631;hallmann & klee;Germany;Berlin;Böhmische Straße 13, Berlin, 12055, Germany;52.4738405;13.4497333;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is located on Böhmischer Platz, which is a lively little square – the hustle and bustle makes the pavement terrace a popular spot in summer. The interior also has its charm: distinctive whitewashed brick walls, attractive floorboards and modern design elements create a charming, almost minimalist urban interior. This is matched by the modern, straightforward and often pared-back cuisine made predominantly from regional ingredients, for example the mashed potatoes with lovage and whey foam. Two chefs, Rosa Beutelspacher and Sarah Hallmann, run the kitchen – the latter is also the source of culinary ideas and, as the proprietor, provides cordial and professional service. The pair complement each other beautifully in this remarkable partnership.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2632;Gasthof Krone;Germany;Waldenbuch;Nürtinger Straße 14, Waldenbuch, 71111, Germany;48.6382832;9.1323653;31;true;true;Classic Cuisine;A delightful inn that is a perfect fit with its surroundings. Erik Metzger serves up appealingly pared-down classic dishes that are replete with harmonious flavour combinations and steer well clear of unnecessary frills. The quality of the produce is beyond question. To complete the picture, there is the cosy, old-fashioned interior. The "Schiller Salon" and "Goethe Salon" are so named with good reason: in the lobby you can see the old tabletop upon which both men left their mark back in the 18C. The service is also on point. Host Matthias Gugeler is the welcoming face of the restaurant: his efficient front-of-house team serves with a personal touch and helps you find your way around the wine list. The lunch menu proposes quality fare at a somewhat lower price.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2633;Dobler's;Germany;Mannheim;Seckenheimer Straße 20, Mannheim, 68159, Germany;49.4810346;8.4761985;90;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Over the last 30-plus years, Gabriele and Norbert Dobler have turned their restaurant into a veritable institution with a loyal following of regulars here in the "City of Squares". Even after handing over the reins to head chef Eric Schumacher (who has been at the restaurant since 2013), they are still committed to their work here. In this sleek and elegant space, Gabriele Dobler oversees the service with charm and professionalism. The cuisine is rooted in tradition but by no means outdated. There is no need for showmanship when you have top-notch ingredients and technical skill as impressive as this. Both at lunchtime and in the evening, you can order à la carte or opt for their seasonal set menu ("Menü zur Jahreszeit"). There is also a three-course lunch deal that offers excellent value for money! Wine lovers will enjoy the appealing selection of labels from the region - the good range of half bottles should also be mentioned.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2634;PAVO;Germany;Pfronten;Auf dem Falkenstein 1, Pfronten, 87459, Germany;47.5702434;10.5917274;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;It has to be said that a spectacular location such as Boutique Hotel Blaue Burg is something of a rarity in Germany. Nestled amid the peaks of the Allgäu Alps, the premises can only be accessed via a private road – the view is breathtaking! The small restaurant is where Simon Schlachter wins diners over with a modern and creative dining concept, which aims to offer a shared experience. He achieves this with a set menu whose courses each consist of several small dishes and are perfect for sharing. Up to 18 dishes full of different components and flavours – this reflects his own elaborate style and creates a sense of complexity. To complete the picture, there is the upscale decor and professional service courtesy of the charming maître d', who happens to be the chef's partner. Alternatively, try out Restaurant 1250 with its regional cuisine (also at lunchtime).;Car park,Great view;[]
2635;restaurant|271;Germany;Burghausen;Mautnerstraße 271, Burghausen, 84489, Germany;48.1550132;12.8274446;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;In Burghausen's old town, not far from the longest castle in the world and the Salzach River, this restaurant lies beyond a historical archway. In an upscale, extremely minimalist-style interior, they serve up ambitious modern cuisine that focuses entirely on excellent ingredients – as a set menu or à la carte. Dominik Lobentanzer (whose CV includes stints at Ikarus in Salzburg, einsunternull in Berlin and Andreas Döllerer's Golling restaurant) bases his cooking on classical foundations, creates flavours that pack a punch and likes to play with contrasts – the ox heart, basil and dashi, for example, is on point. The service is extremely charming. Delightful sheltered terrace. For overnight stays, there are four very tasteful and individually styled guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
2636;Restaurant Karner;Germany;Frasdorf;Nußbaumstraße 6, Frasdorf, 83112, Germany;47.7997713;12.2825454;96;false;true;Creative, Regional Cuisine;This quintessential Chiemgau country inn beautifully combines tradition and modernity. The blend of warm old wood and chic, high-quality modern furnishings fosters a tasteful and inviting atmosphere. The kitchen team proposes a well-thought-out seasonal set menu made with produce from the surrounding area. This is a cuisine that is characterised by delicately balanced flavours and harmonious contrasts – the dishes are also beautifully presented. The desserts, too, are excellent! For the perfect wine accompaniment, recommendations are gladly provided. Alternatively, there is the second restaurant, Westerndorfer Stube. Landgasthof Karner has attractive guestrooms.;Car park;[]
2637;Meisenheimer Hof;Germany;Meisenheim;Obergasse 33, Meisenheim, 55590, Germany;49.7073941;7.6704922;60;false;true;Farm to table;In the pretty little restaurant rooms you can enjoy the ambitious classic and regional cuisine that comes courtesy of your dedicated host and head chef Markus Pape. Wines from the establishment's own nearby winery are also recommended. The various buildings of the Meisenheimer Hof make for an attractive mix of the historical and modern – in the restaurant as well as in the hotel's themed guestrooms. In summer, the terrace between the buildings is delightful. There is also a cookery school.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2638;MARBURGER Esszimmer;Germany;Marburg;Anneliese Pohl Allee 1, Marburg, 35037, Germany;50.8182113;8.7716237;22;true;true;Modern French, Contemporary;"Green Fine Dining" is the name of the concept that Denis Feix has put into practice here. Based on exemplary principles of sustainability that embrace the farm-to-table movement, he presents vegetable-forward dishes made with produce from his own farm in Dagobertshausen – but there is also good fish and meat, if you don't want to go without. The set menu kicks off with an aperitif and finger food in the restaurant's own greenhouse located in the inner courtyard (home to around 50 herb varieties). Diners then move inside to bask in the charming and stylish ambience that is due in no small part to the presence of Kathrin Feix and her extremely attentive front-of-house team. Tip: Stay at the VILA VITA Rosenpark hotel just a few minutes' walk away.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2639;Jae;Germany;Düsseldorf;Keplerstraße 13, Düsseldorf, 40215, Germany;51.2111628;6.7842466;99;true;false;Fusion, Asian Influences;Jörg Wissmann (previously at such top-flight establishments as Vendôme, Nagaya and Agata's) serves up modern fusion cuisine with Asian influences here, reflecting his half-Korean roots and also incorporating classic French elements. The interesting sauces such as the beurre blanc with doenjang, a fermented soybean paste, certainly deserve a mention. His set menu also comes in a vegetarian version. To accompany your meal, you can opt for wine or a non-alcoholic pairing. A winning blend of Far Eastern and Scandinavian styles makes for a bright, minimalist interior – the seats at the counter offer fascinating insights into the work going on in the open kitchen. Scan the QR code with your phone to access the menu and wine list. Practical for motorists: the Creativ Center car park is just a few minutes' walk away.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2640;Hegel Eins;Germany;Stuttgart;Hegelplatz 1, Stuttgart, 70174, Germany;48.7826584;9.1702962;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;You will find this interesting restaurant in the Linden Museum, the city's ethnology museum. Owner Jan Tomasic and his committed team of chefs and front-of-house staff propose a modern and creative set menu comprising eight courses – with the option to reduce to six. In terms of flavour, the various components on the plate are skilfully combined to create a harmonious whole. The quality of the ingredients is excellent. A vegetarian alternative is also available if requested in advance. The really chic interior makes for a lovely atmosphere, and the service is friendly and competent. At lunchtime, there is a simpler menu that is ideal for visitors to the museum – and easy on the wallet.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2641;Casala - das Restaurant;Germany;Meersburg;Uferpromenade 11, Meersburg, 88709, Germany;47.6910309;9.2770749;74;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;At the charming Hotel Residenz am See, two restaurants have been merged into one. With unwavering dedication, chef Markus Philippi and his team create modern and seasonal dishes using top-notch ingredients. You can compile your own set menu of up to six courses from a list of options or simply dine à la carte – the choice is yours. The food is prepared with refined restraint, focusing on the essence of the ingredients. The classic beech-smoked brown trout with sour cream, caviar and rye is undoubtedly a highlight of the menu. With an upscale, tastefully designed interior and a gorgeous terrace overlooking Lake Constance, the setting is certainly appealing. Friendly service.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2642;Sartory;Germany;Augsburg;Maximilianstraße 40, Augsburg, 86150, Germany;48.3651683;10.8985227;80;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The compact fine dining restaurant of this venerable establishment – today Hotel Maximilian's – exudes an air of modernity, thanks to its sleek, contemporary design and classically inspired cuisine. In Simon Lang's kitchen, the food is made with top-notch seasonal ingredients, for example "Grilled Black Cod & Green Apple, Veal Sweetbread Slice, Fermented Shallots, Leek Oil". Choose between the six- to eight-course "Menu du Chef" and six-course vegetarian set menu. Attentive service and on-point wine recommendations. Two different wine flights have been devised to pair with the menu. In addition, there is a five-course tasting menu including wine pairing (Wed-Thu). In case you were wondering, the name is a nod to Johann Georg Sartory, Augsburg's legendary 19C chef.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2643;Schwarz Gourmet;Germany;Kirchheim an der Weinstraße;Weinstraße Süd 1, Kirchheim an der Weinstraße, 67281, Germany;49.537908;8.1805674;80;true;true;French, International;The Schwarz family has been running its two restaurants in this pretty red sandstone building since 2017. One is the chic Schwarz Gourmet, where the chef – who is no stranger to the fine dining scene – proposes a set menu (up to six courses) in which he happily combines international ingredients with those from the local region. The focus lies squarely on the produce, which is of exceptional quality. Fun fact: Manfred Schwarz has already played host to many a celebrity, as you can see from the numerous photos. His friendly wife Angelika takes good care of the guests.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
2644;Zur Post;Germany;Odenthal;Altenberger-Dom-Straße 23, Odenthal, 51519, Germany;51.0324091;7.1150119;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Brothers Alejandro and Christopher Wilbrand have transformed this historical inn into a place where diners can relax and indulge. Their cuisine succeeds in striking an interesting balance between classic gastronomy and a creative brand of modern cooking. They use first-rate ingredients to conjure up two set menus: one regular and one vegetarian. The well-thought-out dishes draw on regional culinary heritage as well as more far-flung European influences. On-point recommendations from the excellent wine list. In addition to their fine dining restaurant, the Wilbrands also preside over the less formal Postschänke and a small hotel with comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2645;Burg Nideggen - Brockel Schlimbach;Germany;Nideggen;Kirchgasse 10 a, Nideggen, 52385, Germany;50.6886805;6.4778448;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;What is it that makes this place stand out? First, the location in a 12C castle above Nideggen, boasting a fantastic view! Secondly, the attractive interior: a historical little dining room with modern design features and wood panelling throughout creates a unique atmosphere. Last but not least, there is the food served up by owners Herbert Brockel and Tobias Schlimbach. Their set menu draws on classic and Mediterranean influences and is based on select seasonal produce. Think sea bream with mussels, Jerusalem artichokes and celery, or suckling pig with quinoa, wild broccoli, cumin yoghurt and lovage. The friendly service team also gladly provide astute recommendations.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2646;Gut Lärchenhof;Germany;Pulheim;Hahnenstraße, Pulheim, 50259, Germany;51.0362026;6.7865908;43;false;true;Modern French, Creative;When Peter Hesseler started out here in 1997, he could never have dreamed that this place would one day make a name for itself as a MICHELIN-starred restaurant. Since 2017, chef Torben Schuster has been at the helm in the kitchen of this gorgeous estate on the high-ranking golf course. His cooking is modern, bold and creative, but never loses sight of its classical foundations. Stand-out dishes include the Portuguese red mullet, bouillabaisse, curry, baby salad, bisque jus and coconut. There is also a somewhat simpler bistro-style set menu available. Host Peter Hesseler and his friendly and well-trained team provide excellent service, including sound wine advice. We recommend heading out to the lovely terrace, which is sure to give you that holiday feeling!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2647;Anthony's Kitchen;Germany;Meerbusch;Moerser Straße 81, Meerbusch, 40667, Germany;51.2571687;6.6826348;18;false;true;Innovative, International;Your host Anthony Sarpong runs what turns out to be an appealing mix of restaurant and cookery school. Heading up a highly dedicated team, this Ghanaian-born chef delivers innovative international cuisine scattered with seasonal influences. There are two set menus on offer: "The Expedition" and the vegetarian "Green Journey" – each comprising well-thought-out creations incorporating interesting combinations of flavours and select ingredients. The dishes are in keeping with the spirit of the times, as is the smart decor and informal atmosphere, with the chefs occasionally delivering dishes to diners themselves. Incidentally, the restaurant is certified organic and attaches great importance to sustainability.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2648;Restaurant Residenz Heinz Winkler;Germany;Aschau im Chiemgau;Kirchplatz 1, Aschau im Chiemgau, 83229, Germany;47.779365;12.3217303;77;true;false;Modern French;Iconic chef Heinz Winkler really put his Residenz hotel on the culinary map. After opening this place in 1991, he remained at the helm, steadily building it up to become a benchmark for classical fine dining at the highest level. Upholding the tradition of the establishment is his son Alexander, as maître d'. A newly assembled and highly motivated kitchen team is sticking to the restaurant's tried-and-tested formula: classic cuisine with modern touches made with excellent ingredients – the turbot with smoked eel lardo bacon and a beurre blanc sauce is a shining example. Opt for one of the set menus or order from the à la carte selection, which includes Winkler's own legendary specialities – these are as much of a draw for diners as the elegant Venetian-style setting. The wine list is impressive and Alexander Winkler's recommendations are spot on. Friendly service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2650;Christian & Friends, Tastekitchen;Germany;Fulda;Nonnengasse 5, Fulda, 36037, Germany;50.5523614;9.676736;58;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;First things first: be sure to make a reservation, because this place is in high demand! This isn't surprising given the fantastic set menu that Christian Steska proposes in this smart townhouse situated in the beautiful old town. The restaurant comprises both Christian & Friends and the adjoining wine bar Bordeaux & Friends with its distinctive wine rack – it has an excellent selection of wines with many top labels offered at fair prices. The open kitchen sends out modern dishes that are built on classical foundations and have a real depth of flavour. The chef has a penchant for regional produce, including caviar – Fulda boasts two sustainable sturgeon farms with their own caviar production. The pleasant atmosphere is down in no small part to the cordial service.;Interesting wine list;[]
2652;Pottkind;Germany;Cologne;Darmstädter Straße 9, Cologne, 50678, Germany;50.9194296;6.9610124;31;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Enrico Sablotny and Lukas Winkelmann, the duo who run this little restaurant, are from the Ruhr Valley. In the kitchen, first-rate ingredients are transformed into distinctly original, creative compositions. Skilfully combined flavours and harmoniously balanced contrasts are particularly evident in dishes such as Eifel salmon trout, apricot with long pepper and chamomile velouté, or boiled beechnuts with radicchio compote and cherry balsamic ice cream. Diners never know what to expect from the carte blanche set menu. Excellent service comes courtesy of very attentive, competent and charming waitstaff, who give the place a pleasantly unpretentious feel. The seats at the counter overlooking the open kitchen are especially popular. In summer, soak up the lively atmosphere of Cologne's Südstadt neighbourhood on the terrace.;Terrace;[]
2653;Bachofer;Germany;Waiblingen;Marktplatz 6, Waiblingen, 71332, Germany;48.8323223;9.316526;44;true;false;Creative, Fusion;Dating back to 1647, this lovely building on Marktplatz is the second oldest in Waiblingen and was once a pharmacy. Today, chic and trendy decor, as well as a lively atmosphere make for an appealing contrast with the historical setting. Nab a seat at the counter for a front-row view into the glass-paned kitchen, where chef-patron Bernd Bachofer conjures up dishes that are cosmopolitan, exciting and meticulously prepared using first-rate ingredients – for instance the perfectly cooked and flamed black cod fillet marinated in miso, or the highly aromatic and tender caramelised suckling pig belly. For the set menu, you can choose to have up to nine courses, plus optional extras – be sure to allow plenty of time! Vegetarian version available. Professional and exceedingly friendly service, including astute wine recommendations. Moderately priced lunch. Tip: There are stylish guestrooms above the restaurant.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2654;Wielandshöhe;Germany;Stuttgart;Alte Weinsteige 71, Stuttgart, 70597, Germany;48.7570062;9.1709218;63;false;true;Classic French, Regional Cuisine;Here in one of Stuttgart's most exclusive residential areas, set amid the lush vines, veteran chef Vincent Klink's Wielandshöhe stands proud. This restaurant is the epitome of elegance with its large windows that afford unobstructed views over the city. Chef-patron Vincent Klink and his right-hand man Jörg Neth deliver classic cuisine that draws inspiration from their Swabian homeland. They steer well clear of gimmickry and frills, instead employing their immense culinary skill to tease out the full flavours of premium ingredients. Unsurprisingly, this place has held a Michelin star almost continuously since 1993.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2655;Philipp;Germany;Sommerhausen;Hauptstraße 12, Sommerhausen, 97286, Germany;49.7056147;10.0242588;63;false;true;Modern French, Classic Cuisine;For more than 20 years, Heike and Michael Philipp have been dedicated to keeping their guests happy. Diners are impressed by their modern take on classic cuisine, which also draws on Mediterranean and Asian influences. When it comes to wine, you can rely entirely on the recommendations of your extremely charming and accomplished hostess and sommelier, Heike Philipp. The setting is also worth a mention: this stylish and cosy restaurant exudes historical flair, housed as it is in a picture-perfect 400-year-old Renaissance palace in the middle of a pretty winegrowing village. In addition, two suites and one double room are available for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
2656;Kucher's Gourmet;Germany;Darscheid;Karl-Kaufmann-Straße 2, Darscheid, 54552, Germany;50.2106931;6.8832352;78;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The Kucher family has run this place with passion and dedication since 1988, constantly investing in and improving their establishment. Now it is the turn of son Florian Kucher and daughter Stefanie Becker, who have breathed new life into this fine dining restaurant. In pleasant, elegant surroundings, diners are offered a choice of two set menus: "Florian's Klassik Menü" and "Modern Art Menü". Steering clear of unnecessary frills, the young chef's culinary creations are expertly crafted and beautifully balanced in terms of flavour. You can look forward to excellently selected wines to accompany the classically based dishes. The wine list comprises about 1700 labels, going back as far as 1868, which is to the credit of wine enthusiast and senior chef Martin Kucher. Guestrooms are available in both the main and new building.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2657;Huberwirt;Germany;Pleiskirchen;Hofmark 3, Pleiskirchen, 84568, Germany;48.3069731;12.5964184;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;This long-established inn has been run by the same family since 1612 and is now in excellent hands with Alexander Huber. Using top-notch ingredients, the chef skilfully incorporates both Bavarian rusticity and modern sophistication into his cuisine, creating dishes that are intense and robust, but not without finesse. Diners are spoilt for choice, with dishes typical of local and regional fare such as veal lights with curd cheese bread dumplings and root vegetables on the one hand, and modern classics such as ox and pork neck ravioli with brown butter, chives, croutons, pointed cabbage and bacon stock on the other. At lunchtime, there is a somewhat pared-down menu. You can eat in the cosy dining area or out on the wonderful, partly covered terrace. The front-of-house team is cordial, attentive and pleasantly down to earth, and they recommend fine wines by the glass to accompany the food. The fantastic value for money is also worth a mention. This terrific place has plenty of charm and a great atmosphere!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2658;BOK Restaurant Brust oder Keule;Germany;Münster;Melchersstraße 32, Münster, 48149, Germany;51.9719525;7.6191805;52;false;false;Farm to table, Creative;A few steps lead down to the attractive, minimalist-style restaurant on the ground floor of this smart corner-plot building. Laurin Kux presides in the kitchen, cooking up modern cuisine with seasonal influences. Dana, the chef's wife, is the woman behind the excellent and elaborate patisserie. The set menus are dubbed "Flora" (vegetarian) and "Fauna" and are available in four- to seven-course versions. The "Schnuppermenü" (Tue-Thu) is a lovely idea, too, offering as it does the option of a three-course meal comprising dishes taken from the full "Flora"/"Fauna" set menu. The ambitious house-made non-alcoholic drinks accompaniment is also recommended. The friendly and professional waitstaff provide astute wine recommendations. Pleasant little terrace in front of the building. Tip: At the bar, you can order nibbles to go with your glass of wine.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2660;Haus Stemberg;Germany;Velbert;Kuhlendahler Straße 295, Velbert, 42553, Germany;51.3313091;7.0914851;69;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;This place has been run by the Stemberg family since 1864. Head chef Sascha Stemberg represents the fifth generation at the helm, and he works with the same passion and commitment as his father before him! The restaurant's unique concept allows for plenty of choice, with a four- to six-course set menu and gourmet dishes à la carte. Things get all the more intriguing when tradition is thrown into the mix and home-style dishes are transformed into haute cuisine. One such creation is the Königsberger Klopse (meatballs) with crispy sweetbreads, caper cream, Amalfi lemon, green vegetables and potato purée. "Oma's Schokoladenpudding" (grandma's chocolate pudding) is a tempting dessert option. The waitstaff are very friendly and laid-back, not to mention attentive. Impressive wine list including a few rare finds. The lovely food and pleasant atmosphere will definitely make you want to come back again!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2661;Merkles Restaurant;Germany;Endingen am Kaiserstuhl;Hauptstraße 2, Endingen am Kaiserstuhl, 79346, Germany;48.1415478;7.7074626;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;It is safe to say that Thomas Merkle made the right decision when, together with his wife, he took over his parents' business and continued the tradition of hospitality that has been cultivated here for over 30 years. Born in Endingen, he proudly showcases his affinity with his homeland by opting for regional ingredients, but also introduces a dash of cosmopolitan flair to his well-thought-out dishes with flavours from far-flung lands. Top-quality produce, accomplished service and an appealing array of wines by the glass. The chef and his kitchen team also like to show their faces in the dining room – contact with the guests is important to them! This historical vicarage with a sleek and elegant interior makes for a pleasant setting. Good to know: Delicious treats in the form of house-made sauces, oils, and salts are also available to take away with you.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2662;ZUR WEINSTEIGE;Germany;Stuttgart;Hohenheimer Straße 30, Stuttgart, 70184, Germany;48.77094;9.187077;97;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;In this long-standing family business, the dedication of the Scherle brothers is plain to see. Their seasonal, modern take on classic cuisine successfully incorporates Japanese influences. The dishes are skilfully structured with cleverly integrated contrasts. There are three menus to choose from, one of which is vegetarian. The decor also appeals with its effective combination of modern elements and rustic details featuring beautiful old oak wood. From the terrace you can admire the large koi carp pool – a true koi enthusiast, Jörg Scherle even has his own koi company. The walk-in vaulted cellar (1870) is home to over 1 600 wines and some 200 spirits! The style of the hotel guestrooms ranges from rural to elegant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2664;The O'ROOM;Germany;Heringsdorf;Kulmstraße 33, Heringsdorf, 17424, Germany;53.9569629;14.1675151;26;false;false;Creative;Absolutely in keeping with the spirit of the times: "casual fine dining" under the same roof as the Marc O'Polo Strandcasino store. The head chef in this stylish little restaurant is André Kähler, whose modern, boldly creative set menu is full of beautifully expressive flavours. Each course comes with a small card explaining the inspiration behind it. The chic interior design and pleasantly relaxed and professional service team are also noteworthy. Tip: The small delicatessen corner where, for example, the wines served can be bought to enjoy at home. For a more casual alternative, head to O'ne, which proposes modern cuisine that puts the spotlight on local produce.;Air conditioning;[]
2665;BECKER'S;Germany;Trier;Olewiger Straße 206, Trier, 54295, Germany;49.7420816;6.6678518;34;true;false;Creative, Classic Cuisine;In keeping with the architecturally interesting design hotel of the same name, a high-quality fine dining restaurant done out in a chic, minimalist style awaits you here. The interior boasts leather shell chairs, elegant parquet flooring and grey panelling on the walls – a lovely setting in which to enjoy a very ingredient-led set menu to the sound of modern background music. Proprietor and head chef Wolfgang Becker deliberately steers clear of gimmickry and instead focuses on flavour. Not only is your host a cook but he also has a penchant for fine wines. He trained as a winemaker and wines from his own vineyard also feature on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2666;Sankt Benedikt;Germany;Aachen;Benediktusplatz 12, Aachen, 52076, Germany;50.7283554;6.1833094;87;false;false;Creative, Modern French;Aachen's Sankt Benedikt has been an established part of North Rhine-Westphalia's Michelin-starred fine dining scene since 1982. In the wake of the recent disastrous floods, the Kreus family was only able to reopen its restaurant at the beginning of December 2021 after a tremendous effort. This was much to the delight of diners, who can once again enjoy Maximilian Kreus's classic cuisine in this listed building in the historical centre of Kornelimünster. His dishes always centre on the finest produce, which he sets about with plenty of feeling and a dash of originality. The service is extremely friendly, and expert advice regarding the wines is readily available – only wines from German wine producers are recommended. In the evening, the gourmet set menu (also available as a vegetarian option) is served, while at midday there is the bistro lunch in the form of a 3-course menu.;Terrace;[]
2667;Cookies Cream;Germany;Berlin;Behrenstraße 55, Berlin, 10117, Germany;52.5163221;13.3880944;65;true;true;Vegetarian;It doesn't get much more quintessentially Berlin than this trendy restaurant! Finding your way here through the backyard (head for the delivery entrance) to ring the bell at the unassuming door is an adventure in itself! After being welcomed at the bar (perfect for an aperitif or after-dinner drink), climb the old stairs up to the first floor to get to the lively restaurant, which was once a fashionable nightclub. In an industrial-chic setting, savour an all-vegetarian set menu dubbed "The Magnificent 7", with the option of enjoying five to seven courses. Meticulously crafted dishes, such as braised peppers, jalapeño and capers, or charcoal-grilled turnip, saffron and olive, balance piquancy and acidity while exploring a variety of textures. You can supplement the menu with a handful of classic signature dishes. The waitstaff are laid back, but no less professional and well organised for it. A hip spot that draws a mixed crowd – Berliners and tourists, fans of plant-based cuisine and foodies from all over the globe.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2669;L'étable;Germany;Bad Hersfeld;Linggplatz 11, Bad Hersfeld, 36251, Germany;50.8677435;9.70618;42;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The only hint that you're dining in a former stable (French: l'étable) is in the name of this restaurant. This spruce historical house in the middle of the tranquil old town used to be a coaching inn. Where travellers and their horses once rested, dinners now settle in and enjoy friendly and attentive service in an ambience of understated elegance. Under the supervision of head chef Constantin Kaiser, the kitchen team employs great craftsmanship and finesse to creatively transform excellent produce into dishes such as "Duck, savoy cabbage, cranberry, chervil root", available in the form of a 3- to 6-course set menu or à la carte. The food is accompanied by a carefully considered selection of wines. For overnight stays, Hotel zum Stern proposes cosy rooms of various sizes. Parking space in the courtyard.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2670;Entenstuben;Germany;Nuremberg;Schranke 9, Nuremberg, 90489, Germany;49.4535946;11.0939143;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Anyone standing in front of this rather unassuming building in the Wöhrd neighbourhood would not necessarily expect to find such a tastefully elegant restaurant inside. This is Fabian Denninger's domain. Following stints at various establishments including Edsbacka krog in Sollentuna near Stockholm, Burg Wernberg and the Waldhotel Sonnora in Wittlich, he first headed the kitchen at Koch und Kellner in Nuremberg, before becoming the chef-patron of Entenstuben in June 2014. He prepares dishes based on classical foundations with a modern twist and plenty of contrasts. This is achieved beautifully, for example, in the lukewarm lobster, to which papaya and chard add a delicately fruity and acidic note. The beautifully presented set menu also comes in a vegetarian version. Tip: The quiet verdant terrace to the rear of the building is delightful.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2671;Gabelspiel;Germany;Munich;Zehentbauernstraße 20, Munich, 81539, Germany;48.1136353;11.5777467;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Located in the middle of Giesing, this small restaurant run by Sabrina and Florian Berger is a real hit! This is partly down to the completely unpretentious and pleasantly informal atmosphere – you can sense the owners' dedication here. Heading up the front-of-house team is the incredibly friendly and professional lady of the house, who ensures that everything runs smoothly. Another major draw is the modern cuisine made from regional produce. With prime ingredients and remarkable skill, Florian Berger creates impressive dishes such as wild boar and egg yolk ravioli with cocoa and barberry. A vegetarian version of his six- to seven-course set menu can be pre-ordered (one day in advance). Well-curated wine list. Harmonious pairings, including non-alcoholic alternatives, are available by the glass for the set menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2672;Acquarello;Germany;Munich;Mühlbaurstraße 36, Munich, 81677, Germany;48.1421393;11.6138327;41;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;The Latin flair of this friendly, elegant restaurant is beautifully in keeping with the Italian/Mediterranean and little French-influenced cuisine served here. Owner and head chef Mario Gamba, who originally trained to be a translator, is self-taught when it comes to cooking, although as the son of a restaurateur, you might say his passion for the profession is in his blood. The focus of his "cucina del sole" lies squarely on the quality of the produce, with the Italian-born chef really getting back to basics. There are, of course, fine wines from Italy to accompany your meal. Seated on stylish upholstered chairs at tables decked with high-quality tablecloths, you are attentively served by a well-trained team. The chef-patron's son, Massimo Gamba, is also part of the staff.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2674;Jacobi;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Herrenstraße 43, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79098, Germany;47.9944889;7.8539514;16;true;false;Innovative;This restaurant housed in the Hotel Schwarzwälder Hof in Freiburg's old town boasts a relaxed atmosphere and food that is by no means run-of-the-mill. The seven-course set menu on offer (which can be extended by a further two courses) steers clear of luxury ingredients, focusing instead on supposedly simpler, but high-quality and strictly regional produce that clearly reflects their philosophy of sustainability. This results in a plethora of highly interesting and innovative flavour combinations, such as fermented kohlrabi that has been cooked in salt dough served on a delicate kohlrabi tartare and finished with a bay leaf and apple stock, a pleasingly tart elderberry and caper vinaigrette and a sweet apricot ragout. The chefs themselves serve the dishes, talking diners through each course and providing information about the local producers of the select ingredients.;;[]
2675;Atlantic Restaurant;Germany;Hamburg;An der Alster 72, Hamburg, 20099, Germany;53.5568271;10.0047017;47;false;false;French Contemporary;The elegant Atlantic Restaurant is entirely in keeping with the Hanseatic flair of the luxe Hotel Atlantic by the banks of the River Alster. Using excellent ingredients, chef Fokke Mick proposes the set menu, "Identité", alongside its vegetarian counterpart, "Flora" – in both cases, diners choose from four to seven courses. In addition, there is a three-course menu for two people with the restaurant's classics, such as lobster bisque and whole sole. The appealing classic decor provides a perfectly fitting setting. Last but not least, the front-of-house team is experienced, extremely cordial and professional.;;[]
2676;Petit Amour;Germany;Hamburg;Spritzenplatz 11, Hamburg, 22765, Germany;53.5513517;9.930977;38;false;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;Petit Amour is back with a new team. Eike Iken, previously sous-chef at Votum, has fulfilled his dream of striking out on his own together with partner and restaurant manager Monique Lingg. While the owner and head chef successfully combines a modern take on classic French fare with Nordic influences (eg his terrific hand-dived scallop, almond, caviar, seaweed), you can sit back and enjoy the friendly and professional service. The chefs themselves also head out to the restaurant floor to explain the dishes. A six-course set menu is served, with three supplementary courses also on offer. Selected wine accompaniment. With just 12 tables, this small restaurant has a friendly, almost intimate atmosphere that makes you feel at home. Tip: Be sure to make a reservation!;Terrace;[]
2677;Bricole;Germany;Berlin;Senefelderstraße 30, Berlin, 10437, Germany;52.5410362;13.4224001;88;true;true;Modern French, Contemporary;The atmosphere here is really neighbourly, almost intimate – you immediately feel welcome! This is due both to the appealing bistro setting and to cordial and professional proprietor and sommelier Fabian Fischer. He has a pleasingly personal touch in his dealings with diners and a clear enthusiasm when it comes to recommending the most suitable wine from a list dominated by German and French labels. Steven Zeidler is in charge in the kitchen, cooking up a creative take on classic cuisine that incorporates Asian flavours. His dish of Korean kimchi, Chinese XO sauce and Japanese dashi is a shining example from the set menu, of which a vegetarian version is available upon request. There are also a few small tables to be had on the pavement in front of the restaurant.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2678;Werners Restaurant;Germany;Gernsbach;Schloss Eberstein 1, Gernsbach, 76593, Germany;48.7495769;8.342642;84;true;false;Classic French, International;If you have always wanted to treat yourself to a spot of fine dining in the historical surroundings of a castle, then Schloss Eberstein is the place for you. Perched on a hilltop above the Murg Valley and surrounded by vines, it commands stunning views! Set on a magnificent historical estate, this lovely hotel with two dining options is run by the Werner family. The elegant fine dining restaurant has made a name for itself with its modern take on classical cuisine. Chef-patron Bernd Werner presides over a dedicated kitchen team that brings balance and intense flavours to the plate. The wine list also features a selection from the hotel's own vineyard – ask for recommendations.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2679;maximilian lorenz;Germany;Cologne;Johannisstraße 64, Cologne, 50668, Germany;50.9445986;6.9608324;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Located near the main train station, cathedral and the Rhine, this restaurant is entirely dedicated to German cuisine. Maximilian Lorenz and his team serve up a creative set menu (also available in a vegetarian version) that combines the modern and the traditional in a skilful and multifaceted way, with dishes such as Saarland sea bass, mussel, samphire, condensed milk. Diners are sure to be impressed by the top-notch ingredients, the culinary prowess of the kitchen team and the exquisite flavours. The interior is upmarket, elegant and minimalist. The extensive wine list has a very good selection of champagnes and sparkling wines. Wine lovers should also check out heinzhermann, the modern, laid-back wine bar located just next door. For those who need to eat on the hoof, there are also simpler street food options to take away.;Interesting wine list;[]
2681;St. Laurentiushof - Schockes Küche;Germany;Birkweiler;Hauptstraße 21, Birkweiler, 76831, Germany;49.2040427;8.0346196;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Since July 2021, Lara and Maximilian Schocke have been breathing new life into St Laurentiushof. Lara, with her warm personality and astute wine recommendations, is in charge of service. Chef Maximilian creates ambitious dishes from the finest ingredients. The "Maximum" set menu comprises four to seven courses and can be made vegetarian by prior arrangement (three to four days' notice required). "MaxPlus" is a selection of further dishes available to substitute or supplement your chosen courses. House-baked sourdough bread can be purchased to take home (order in advance to pick up on Wed and Fri, or subject to availability). Most of the wines are sourced from the surrounding area. Smart guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2683;Tantris DNA;Germany;Munich;Johann-Fichte-Straße 7, Munich, 80805, Germany;48.1697555;11.5882597;77;true;false;Classic French, French;Tantris Maison Culinaire proposes not only Tantris, with its prix fixe menu, but also DNA. Benjamin Chmura is now at the helm in the kitchen here. As before, the five decades spanned by this Munich institution are represented in the form of its house classics, albeit with a slightly original twist, but the menu also includes new creations. The premium quality of the ingredients is evident in dishes such as "Sea bass à la ligne in pastry, caviar, Normande sauce". The service also lives up to the high standards: the front-of-house team is attentive, cordial and highly professional, but by no means stuffy. The wine list is one of the finest in the country – its fantastic selection of Burgundy labels is just one of many possible recommendations!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2684;The Stage;Germany;Dortmund;Karlsbader Straße 1A, Dortmund, 44225, Germany;51.4760427;7.4441431;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The location alone is really something! It takes under 20 seconds for the lift to take you up to the seventh floor of the Dula Centre. Upon entering the restaurant, you can take a peek into the kitchen. In the chic, modern dining space, you have a fantastic view over Dortmund and the Westfalenstadion. The terrace is also gorgeous. Michael Dyllong and his team serve up a meticulously prepared set menu with four or six courses – you have the option to upgrade by adding Japanese Wagyu beef, N25 caviar or a selection of French cheeses. There is a vegan alternative, too. Additionally, the four-course "Marktmenü", made with market-fresh produce, is also available Tue-Thu. The service is extremely professional, thanks in no small part to restaurant manager and sommelier Ciro De Luca, long-time business partner of the chef. Tip: Exciting events, such as the "Table du Chef" with Michael Dyllong, are organised on a regular basis.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2685;Schlossberg;Germany;Baiersbronn;Murgtalstraße 602, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5973809;8.3838147;93;true;true;Creative, Classic Cuisine;Schlossberg has been a culinary institution in the idyllic Murg Valley for decades. The interior is chic and stylish, incorporating modern lines, pale wood and serene hues of grey and beige, and occasional design features. Efficient father-and-son team Jörg and Nico Sackmann serve up classic cuisine as well as modern culinary creations that draw on international influences and ingredients. These dishes range from pared down to complex. There are two set menus comprising five to eight courses, one of which is vegetarian. For overnight stays, Hotel Sackmann has lovely guestrooms and a spa area.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2686;Steins Traube;Germany;Mainz;Poststraße 4, Mainz, 55126, Germany;49.9838324;8.1746485;100;false;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;Thanks to the commitment of the Stein family, what began in the early 20C as a village tavern has evolved over the decades into a modern restaurant serving sophisticated cuisine. Owner and head chef Philipp Stein represents the sixth generation at the helm. There is no doubt about his outstanding culinary talent. What may, at first glance, seem simple is actually exceedingly complex in terms of flavour and harmony, yet accessible for all that. His dishes demonstrate a restrained elegance, but he is also able to draw on a bolder sense of innovation when he deems it necessary. An excellent wine list is also available. Choosing where to sit is not easy, because the smart and modern yet cosy interior is just as inviting as the beautiful inner courtyard. Friendly service comes courtesy of Alina Stein, your cordial young hostess.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2687;Schattbuch;Germany;Amtzell;Schattbucher Straße 10, Amtzell, 88279, Germany;47.6950322;9.757391;92;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Trendy and elegant Schattbuch is a firm fixture in the Allgäu fine dining scene. Chef Sebastian Cihlars serves up modern dishes, always looking to the region for inspiration and giving pride of place to high-quality produce. Finesse and a down-to-earth attitude go hand in hand. In the evening there are two set menus (one of them vegetarian), and at lunchtime you can order gourmet dishes à la carte in addition to lower-priced set menus. Christian Marz's laid-back yet highly accomplished front-of-house team help to create the friendly atmosphere. Head for the terrace in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
2690;Restaurant 1950;Germany;Hayingen;Aichelauer Straße 6, Hayingen, 72534, Germany;48.3202066;9.4323997;27;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This fantastic restaurant is actually housed in what was once a pigpen. The modern and attractive dining area features high ceilings (the hanging herb boxes are an original detail) and an open kitchen. Here, the chefs whip up a vegetarian set menu, which can be extended to include a meat option if desired. Small cards accompanying the dishes (e.g. "Beetroot & parsley" or "Parsnip & pumpkin") provide information about the ingredients, all of which are sourced within a radius of 25km (except for the salt). A cuisine with its own idea, not off the peg and a prime example of sustainability! After being seated at one of only five tables, you can relax and enjoy the friendly and informal service. Chef Simon Tress also gets in on the act front of house – he calls the restaurant his "living room", which is in keeping with the pleasingly convivial atmosphere. Appealing guestrooms.;Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2691;Zur Tant;Germany;Cologne;Rheinbergstraße 49, Cologne, 51143, Germany;50.8520887;7.0086038;28;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;In this well-maintained half-timbered house set in an idyllic location on the Rhine, chef Thomas Lösche celebrates cuisine that puts top-notch ingredients and craftsmanship centre stage. For example, he emphasises the excellent quality and characteristic flavours of Berkshire pork from the Black Forest, cleverly underscoring those flavours with an accompanying sweet-and-sour note. This is cooking that eschews frills in a bid to remain true to the authenticity with which this house is synonymous. The wine list features a good selection of Austrian labels. And then there is the terrace with a magnificent view of the Rhine – best enjoyed at sunset!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2692;Restaurant Villa Merton;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Am Leonhardsbrunn 12, Frankfurt on the Main, 60487, Germany;50.1272242;8.6534434;40;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;For years, owner André Großfeld and the proficient team led by head chef Philippe Giar have been putting their heart and soul into running the elegant Villa Merton, establishing a real destination for connoisseurs. Their cooking style could be summed up as creative, passionate and regionally influenced. The quality of the ingredients is second to none. With its ceiling mouldings, hardwood floors and stylish details, this listed villa in the elegant diplomatic quarter makes for a prestigious setting. To the rear of the building there is a gorgeous terrace. The friendly, professional staff are always on hand, yet discreet. Tip: The Monday evening "Gourmet Special". The Chef's Table can be booked Tuesday to Saturday. In addition to the fine dining restaurant, which is open in the evening, at lunchtime there is a bistro menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2693;Restaurant Kunz;Germany;Sankt Wendel;Kirchstraße 22, Sankt Wendel, 66606, Germany;49.49596;7.1122542;30;false;true;Classic French;The Kunz family have run this establishment in the village of Bliesen for many years, working together like a well-oiled machine. The proprietor and his chef Patrick Jenal propose two set menus ("Signature" and "Traditional"), as well as an à la carte selection as a pleasing and more flexible alternative. Besides classic French dishes such as "carpaccio of wild-caught red shrimp & scallops", there are renowned Kunz classics including "original Wiener schnitzel made from saddle of suckling veal". The quality of the ingredients is outstanding. Through the glass front of the elegant modern conservatory, you get a splendid view of the impressive parish church (St Remigius or "Bliestaldom"). Very friendly service. Alexander Kunz is also known for his event catering and the Alexander Kunz Theatre dinner show in Saarbrücken.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2694;Veles;Germany;Nuremberg;Kernstraße 29, Nuremberg, 90429, Germany;49.4491082;11.0541219;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Head to Nuremberg's trendy Gostenhof neighbourhood for a fine dining experience in a rather alternative setting. Chef-patron Vadim Karasev places the emphasis on regionality and seasonality in his restaurant. Many of the ingredients come from small-scale producers in Knoblauchsland ("garlic country"), which is just down the road. The kitchen is actually in the dining room and, in full view of the diners, the chefs prepare a well-thought-out, creative set menu comprising five to seven courses – a vegetarian version can be pre-ordered. Choose from their selection of biodynamic wines or opt for a house-made non-alcoholic alternative. Hip decor, a relaxed, down-to-earth atmosphere and culinary surprises served by a friendly and enthusiastic front-of-house team.;Terrace;[]
2695;Borst;Germany;Maßweiler;Luitpoldstraße 4, Maßweiler, 66506, Germany;49.2710771;7.5277892;30;true;true;Classic French, Farm to table;Monika and Harry Borst have for many years been synonymous with quality and sophistication at their town-centre establishment. And now they have been joined by their son, Maximilian. In the kitchen, he toes the classic line, using high-quality ingredients to prepare cuisine that is at once pleasingly unpretentious and refined. They serve a set menu comprising three, four, five or seven courses, along with two starters to swap in or add on. This is accompanied by fine wines from the region. You will be treated to cordial and attentive service in the tasteful interior with a modern, elegant feel or on the terrace. There are also well-kept guestrooms should you wish to stay overnight – and, come morning, there is table service at breakfast.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2696;La Cuisine Rademacher;Germany;Cologne;Dellbrücker Hauptstraße 176, Cologne, 51069, Germany;50.9803189;7.0689139;80;true;true;Modern French;This place may not be located in the most attractive area and the city centre is not exactly on the doorstep, but it is very much worth visiting this pleasant restaurant done out in a tasteful modern style. Inside what is a well-kept listed corner building, you will find Marlon Rademacher's dedicated team at work. The chef-patron proposes a sophisticated, modern set menu made from excellent ingredients – also available in a vegetarian version (vegan is possible if ordered when making your reservation). Three days a week, there is a reasonably priced lunch set menu that is equally impressive.;;[]
2697;Eichhalde;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Stadtstraße 91, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79104, Germany;48.0067203;7.8647925;48;false;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;A real must for lovers of Italian food! Federico Campolattano serves up delicious dishes that are scrupulously ingredient-led, pleasingly pared down, and rife with beautifully balanced contrasting flavours. Diners have a choice between "Das moderne Menü": a set menu comprising five, six or nine courses – you might be tempted by the "Octopus and its Neapolitan History" or the cheese menu featuring five DOP Parmesans of varying ripeness. Alternatively, there is "Das traditionelle Menü": a three- or four-course set menu. The wine list is predominantly Italian. Housed in a historical building in a spruce residential area of Freiburg, this restaurant is sleek and rather unadorned, but no less cosy for it. There is also a delightful little terrace. Tip: You can buy jars of pasta sauce to cook at home.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2699;Lamm Rosswag;Germany;Vaihingen an der Enz;Rathausstraße 4, Vaihingen an der Enz, 71665, Germany;48.936683;8.916984;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;What is it that draws foodies to this historical inn in a sleepy little wine village? The passion the proprietors bring to serving and cooking for their guests. Steffen Ruggaber devises creative dishes in the form of set menus that are very precise in their craftsmanship, rich in detail and packed with flavour. Top-notch ingredients and not a little effort go into dishes such as fine beef tartare topped with powdered smoked eel and ice cream, served with an aromatic beetroot gel and cauliflower three ways (grated, creamed and pickled) plus a spicy mustard gel and finely acidic oxalis leaves. A special event: every first Friday of the month, the restaurant offers a four-course menu centred on Swabian roast beef. Sonja Ruggaber provides extremely cordial and experienced service. As an alternative to the well-curated selection of exclusively German wines, they also recommend interesting non-alcoholic accompaniments to the set menu. Tip: Good overnight accommodation is also available.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2700;Jungborn;Germany;Bad Sobernheim;Felkestraße 100, Bad Sobernheim, 55566, Germany;49.7767707;7.6571982;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;Quality is the watchword in the imposing BollAnts hotel complex, and the Jungborn certainly doesn't let the side down: it boasts an elegant interior with its wonderful sandstone barrel vaulted ceiling, and promises cordial service and excellent food prepared by Philipp Helzle. His cooking style is aptly described as "modern classic" – pleasingly pared-back cuisine that builds on French foundations and occasionally draws on international influences. Think Atlantic skate wing, couscous, carrot, pistachio and pineapple, or South African langoustine, sweet potato, broccoli and finger limes. The quality of the ingredients is outstanding. Staff will gladly recommend wines from the region to accompany the two set menus. Incidentally, the name "Jungborn" refers to BollAnts's original incarnation as Felke-Jungborn Kurhaus Dhonau and is a nod to the hotel's healthy-living ethos.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2701;Oswald's Gourmetstube;Germany;Teisnach;Am Platzl 2, Teisnach, 94244, Germany;49.0134357;13.0296421;99;true;false;Modern French, Contemporary;Hidden in the basement of Landromantik Wellness Hotel Oswald is an upscale fine dining restaurant that seems improbable in Kaikenried, a Bavarian Forest village with a population of about 550 people. The space is expansive, supremely chic and sophisticated, verging on the luxurious! With experience at top-flight establishments under his belt, head chef Thomas Gerber creates a four- to eight-course set menu, drawing on contemporary influences. Classic in their foundations crafted with the utmost precision, the dishes are pleasingly pared down to the essentials and highlight the intense flavours of first-rate ingredients. Choose a bottle from the nicely curated wine list (around 350 labels) and enjoy the attentive, ultra-friendly service.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2702;Tipken's by Nils Henkel;Germany;Keitum;Am Tipkenhoog 18, Keitum, 25980, Germany;54.8907917;8.3780691;97;false;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is located in Severin's Resort & Spa, where guests can enjoy a stay in pleasantly understated luxury. In summer, take an aperitif on the quiet, leafy terrace behind the building, before heading inside to the stylish modern dining space to savour René Verse's culinary creations, which are crafted with precision and feel delightfully effortless. Nils Henkel, after whom this place is named, has clearly put his own stamp on the menu. His vegetable-based cuisine, with which he made a name for himself once upon a time, is skilfully integrated here, including in both the "Flora" and "Fauna" set menus. The sea bream with carrot-coriander juice and young carrots is a wonderful example of how he combines vegetables with premium fish. You can also swap out courses or order à la carte. Tip: Book a room in the hotel, then you are free to make the most of the impressive wine list.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2703;Der Zauberlehrling;Germany;Stuttgart;Rosenstraße 38, Stuttgart, 70182, Germany;48.7740561;9.1843343;15;true;false;Creative;Wine lovers will be delighted to see the walk-in glass wine cabinet upon entering the restaurant – it gives a first impression of the 300 or so labels on offer here. The chic interior with its stylish, minimalist design and distinctive details is also sure to draw the eye. This makes for a pleasant atmosphere, as does the charming and accomplished service. A sophisticated setting such as this serves as a perfect backdrop for head chef Fabian Heldmann's contemporary cuisine which is rich in contrasts. Be aware that on Saturdays they only offer their "theme night". Own cooking school. For overnight stays, the small design hotel of the same name boasts a central location and tasteful, individually decorated guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2705;Mittermeier;Germany;Rothenburg ob der Tauber;Vorm Würzburger Tor 7, Rothenburg ob der Tauber, 91541, Germany;49.380077;10.1848018;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Diners walk past the open kitchen into the trendy dining space, where attentive service comes courtesy of a friendly and dedicated front-of-house team. The cuisine is modern and seasonal, with many ingredients sourced from regional producers. Dishes such as ravioli, Parmigiano Reggiano and green olive or guinea fowl, chanterelles and lovage demonstrate a pleasing sense of clarity and coherence with delightful contrasts and perfectly balanced flavours. The small cards providing information about the dishes are a nice idea. Create your own menu by choosing five, seven or nine courses. The staff will be happy to recommend wines from their Tauberhase range. Tip: tasteful hotel accommodation at Villa Mittermeier.;Car park,Terrace;[]
2706;freustil;Germany;Ostseebad Binz;Zeppelinstraße 8, Ostseebad Binz, 18609, Germany;54.4012638;13.6117968;78;false;false;Creative;It is a real stroke of luck for the beautiful Baltic Sea resort of Binz that Ralf Haug, who was born in the Black Forest, has ended up in the far north of Germany. Here, at the fine dining restaurant of Hotel Vier Jahreszeiten, he has been wowing diners with his remarkable creativity and finesse since 2013. For his 12-course set menu (a shorter version is also available), he combines classic elements and regional ingredients to conjure up modern and coherent dishes. These mouth-watering creations include a Nordic bouillabaisse and the bell peppers with seaweed flakes and sour cream. Considering the first-rate quality of the ingredients, the value for money is surely worth a mention! The atmosphere is as pleasingly down-to-earth as the cuisine, which is down to both the casual Nordic-style interior design and the very friendly and attentive front-of-house team.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2708;Atelier Sanssouci;Germany;Radebeul;Augustusweg 48, Radebeul, 01445, Germany;51.1086096;13.6753756;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Atelier Sanssouci – the name alone sounds stylish, and this wonderful 18C estate certainly lives up to it! Not only is the exterior with its magnificent garden a veritable feast for the eyes, but the interior is also a sight to behold. The large dining room done out in an elegant Mediterranean style boasts remarkable chandeliers and a high ceiling. And the sophisticated cuisine is on a par with this romantic setting. First-rate ingredients are used to create a successful blend of classic and modern dishes. Choose five to 10 courses to make up your meal, or just specify the number of courses and let the kitchen surprise you. The food is accompanied by a harmonious selection of wines, and the service is attentive and professional. Tasteful guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2709;Hämmerle's Restaurant;Germany;Blieskastel;Bliestalstraße 110a, Blieskastel, 66440, Germany;49.2362942;7.2693768;99;true;false;Modern French, Creative;A charming, long-standing family business, where Cliff Hämmerle sticks to what he does best: serving classic cuisine, skilfully imbued with creative touches. He works with top-notch ingredients and likes to use lots of vegetables, especially regional produce. The seven-course "Chef's Table Menu" is also available in a vegetarian version. Serving starts at 7pm. In a tastefully modern setting, up to 12 diners are seated at four tables. The chefs prepare the dishes before their eyes, which makes for a thrilling and immersive experience and provides some fascinating insights. The head chef also explains the dishes. You should allow plenty of time for this culinary adventure. A pared-down set menu is served at lunchtime. The whole family is involved in the service, working together with great dedication as a well-coordinated team to make their diners feel at home. The wine pairings for the set menu are fantastic. As an alternative, there is the second restaurant, Landgenuss.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2710;Kaupers Restaurant im Kapellenhof;Germany;Selzen;Kapellenstraße 18a, Selzen, 55278, Germany;49.8639732;8.2551053;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This compact restaurant has the potential to become a firm favourite – so be sure to book! It is somewhat tucked away, but the effort to get there pays dividends, which is down to Nora Breyer and Sebastian Kauper (both trained chefs) and the setting of the Kapellenhof, which dates back over 300 years. Working together here as a well-oiled machine, this affable couple has created an extremely warm and welcoming atmosphere under the gable roof. Your hostess provides friendly service and will also be able to recommend some excellent wines. In his modern, seasonal cuisine, Sebastian Kauper uses only select ingredients. With careful consideration and a deft touch, he marries, for example, a butter-soft piece of Soonwald venison loin with beetroot baked on sea salt, black walnut and cold-stirred cranberries, as well as an aromatic jus. A few heirloom vegetables are grown in the restaurant's own garden. Tip: the beautifully landscaped roof terrace! It's also worth asking about the "Late Lunch" dates (Sun and public holidays from 2pm).;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
2711;Les Deux;Germany;Munich;Maffeistraße 3a, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1393613;11.5745402;64;true;false;Modern French, Creative;You will find Katrin and Fabrice Kieffer's smart restaurant on the first floor of the Schäfflerhof in the heart of the old town, just a few steps away from the Frauenkirche. Diners take their seats in a triangular room with floor-to-ceiling windows that afford a view of the hustle and bustle of the city below. Nathalie Leblond is at the helm in the kitchen, sending out modern French dishes that can be ordered as a set menu or à la carte. The preparation is meticulous, the combinations innovative, the interplay of textures and temperatures skilful - such as black cod, eel dashi, parmesan, spinach, peanut. Headed up by restaurant manager and sommelier Vincent Leblond the front-of-house team is extremely friendly and enthusiastic, as well as adept at providing expert recommendations when it comes to a wine list of over 600 labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2712;Hofstube Deimann;Germany;Schmallenberg;Alte Handelsstraße 5, Schmallenberg, 57392, Germany;51.159252;8.340913;51;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The spa hotel that houses this fine dining restaurant was originally a manor house that dates back to 1880 and has been in the Deimann family since 1917. The single set menu is bursting with bold flavours and demonstrates meticulous craftsmanship. Head chef Felix Weber champions a modern style of cooking and insists on the finest ingredients. The succulent turbot is grilled and then baked in the oven until slightly translucent – with its fine seasoning and wonderfully firm bite, it works beautifully with the delicate, nutty cashew cream, aromatic black salsify puree, cauliflower salad and confit kombu seaweed. Razor-thin slices of Buddha's hand and a thick, intensely flavoursome beurre blanc provide the finishing touches. Service comes courtesy of friendly and professional waitstaff. Sommelier Christian Pufahl has some interesting wine recommendations but also introduces fantastic non-alcoholic pairings with beverages he prepares himself. In the chic, upscale interior, the open kitchen is the centrepiece – being close to the action, diners can gain many a fascinating insight.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
2713;Koch und Kellner;Germany;Nuremberg;Obere Seitenstraße 4, Nuremberg, 90429, Germany;49.4491097;11.0568482;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;A cornerstone of the Nuremberg fine dining scene. The set menu, written up on a large board, comprises nine courses, but for those with a smaller appetite, it can also be shortened. The dishes are crafted from carefully selected ingredients and are quite aptly described as "modernised classics". Besides the chef, owner and waiter Frank Mackert is always on hand with his inimitable Franconian charm. Thanks to his extensive wine expertise, he can confidently guide you through the 500-label list. Clear lines, a warm colour palette and parquet flooring make for a lovely setting. By reservation only: Mon-Sat lunchtime (11.30am-2.30pm).;Interesting wine list;[]
2716;Falconera;Germany;Öhningen;Zum Mühlental 1, Öhningen, 78337, Germany;47.685155;8.8982028;87;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;In a verdant setting close to Lake Constance, this converted mill is an appealing spot with a fabulous garden. It is a centuries-old half-timbered house, in which the Falkenstube and Mühlenstube dining rooms are done up in a tasteful blend of elegant and rustic decor. The many regulars keep coming back for more not only on account of the gorgeous space, but also for the friendly welcome extended by the hosts. On top of that, there is the outstanding cuisine, which demonstrates passion and skill. Chef-patron Johannes Wuhrer draws on fresh, selected produce to cook up classic seasonal dishes. Opt for the "Falconera" set menu or the vegetarian "Gemüsemenü" – alternatively you can order dishes à la carte. At lunchtime there is also a cheaper three-course set menu.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2717;Waidwerk;Germany;Nuremberg;Winterstraße 15, Nuremberg, 90431, Germany;49.4354114;11.0212737;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This fine dining restaurant is the beating heart of Romantik Hotel Gasthaus Rottner. In the kitchen where Stefan was once at the helm, his son Valentin now expertly continues the tradition. He prepares select super-fresh ingredients using modern techniques, and presents them in a five- or seven-course menu, available in a vegetarian version if you pre-order. Alternatively, you can opt for a three-course surprise menu. Sommelier Thomas Wachter heads up the friendly and professional service team. The interior is sophisticated, the minimalist style enhanced by some rustic touches and a hunting theme – this is no coincidence, as the head chef is a keen hunter.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2718;Sparkling Bistro;Germany;Munich;Amalienstraße 89/ Türkenstraße 86, Munich, 80799, Germany;48.1519723;11.5779835;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;"Bistro" may not accurately capture the essence of this restaurant – the name dates back to an earlier era. Tucked away in Schwabing's Amalienpassage, this establishment exudes a pleasingly understated elegance, and the culinary standards are just as exceptional as the exquisite setting. Owner Jürgen Wolfsgruber and his team offer thoughtfully crafted cuisine that is both pared back and intensely flavourful, a case in point being the terrific fresh Vendée turbot served with mildly marinated cauliflower slices, thin slivers of preserved lemon, elderflower capers and a foamy beurre blanc. The chef's predilection for ingredients sourced from his Austrian homeland also shines through in dishes such as Almsee venison hunted by the family themselves. Furthermore, his passion for wine is apparent, as he enjoys joining his attentive and experienced front-of-house team in providing interesting recommendations.;Terrace;[]
2719;HILMAR;Germany;Aerzen;Schwöbber 9, Aerzen, 31855, Germany;52.0692633;9.2520492;61;false;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;Dine like royalty in a castle setting! Could you ask for more splendid surroundings than those of the historical Schlosshotel Münchhausen, a stately home dating from 1570, in which to savour modern dishes inspired by French culinary tradition. Stephan Krogmann, previously head chef at Gutshaus Stolpe, showcases excellent ingredients in his set menu, which comprises five pleasingly pared-down and precisely crafted courses. Take, for example, the Breton-coast monkfish roasted on the bone. The various amuse-bouches are also exquisite. The whole experience is rounded off by friendly, highly adept service and an elegant setting, to which moulded ceilings, chandeliers and parquet flooring lend their historical charm. Thanks to the wonderful location with the park and golf course, as well as the tastefully designed guestrooms, patrons find plenty of reasons to linger.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
2723;SEPT;France;Toulouse;11 rue Théodore-Ozenne, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.5967943;1.4467407;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this location between the Marché des Carmes (covered market) and the antiques quarter, chef Guillaume Monboise has created a new space for foodies. This former tearoom done out in soothing cream hues boasts a brand new kitchen that opens out onto the restaurant floor – ideal for this talented chef who loves to have direct contact with his customers. In keeping with this philosophy, the service is professional and relaxed, and immediately puts you at ease. The dishes are enhanced with invigorating and refreshing seasonings – take the sea bass cooked skin on and served with a green olive sorbet and grated bottarga for saltiness.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2724;Contraste;France;Paris;18 rue d'Anjou, Paris, 75008, France;48.8705248;2.3213463;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The contrasts come thick and fast at this restaurant, starting with the decor, which sees the original elegance of the location set off by more contemporary details. "Contraste" is also the name of a famous champagne vintage from Anselme Selosse – featured, among others, on the extensive wine list. This is a place where you can savour meticulous, up-to-date, flavoursome cuisine based on the finest seasonal produce and presented in a number of tasting menus, each comprising several courses.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2726;Alpage;France;Courchevel;Annapurna, 734 route de l'Altiport, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4012235;6.6369297;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Jean-Rémi Caillon, originally from Roanne, was previously chef at the two-Michelin-starred Kintessence restaurant in Le K2 Palace. He can now be seen in the open kitchens of this restaurant in the Hotel Annapurna. In the intimate space, he aims to deliver an "immersive moonlight dining experience" to a handful of guests. He reveals a very personal culinary approach that combines plants and produce from the terroir: vegetables and herbs take pride of place over animal products, but Savoyard ingredients and recipes (crozets, polenta, Chartreuse) share top billing. His art does not exclude playfulness, a case in point being his beef consommé with caraway crozets and a medley of carrots, a dish in which delicate execution meets refined rusticity.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2727;Le Tout-Paris;France;Paris;Cheval Blanc Paris, 8 quai du Louvre, Paris, 75001, France;48.8588392;2.342155;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This brasserie, whose colourful décor is the work of Peter Marino, is tucked away on the 7th floor of the Cheval Blanc Hotel. Under the guidance of Arnaud Donckele, chef William Bequin, who boasts an enviable CV, is on a roller coaster. While he respects traditional brasserie rules, like allowing diners to choose their sides and how the fish and meat is cooked (grilled, roasted in thyme or steamed in seaweed), each dish is emblematic of his consummate craftsmanship. Examples include a tartlet of mushrooms with a vin jaune emulsion or blue lobster flanked by coral-coloured béarnaise sauce and perfumed in bergamot. The terrace, with its sweeping view over the Seine and the Left Bank, is Instagram perfect!;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2728;Granite;France;Paris;6 rue Bailleul, Paris, 75001, France;48.8610315;2.3419097;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Near the Louvre, this restaurant is the epitome of classy elegance and crisp designer style. The quality of the ingredients is impeccable, and each dish is spot on, crafted delicately and precisely. The chef slips subtle Japanese references into his recipes, such as koshihikari rice with roast scallops, or umeboshi with Racan pigeon. The pastry chef's creations slot seamlessly into this inventive score, a case in point being the ever so subtle white grape dessert. The front-of-house team smoothly and apparently effortlessly supervises every detail of this culinary cocoon. A hipster chilled vibe meets polished professionalism – an unbeatable match!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
2729;Les Foudres;France;Cognac;Chais Monnet, 50 avenue Paul-Firino-Martell, Cognac, 16100, France;45.6910242;-0.3344321;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant of the Hôtel Chais Monnet is housed in the high-ceilinged space where the huge hundred-year-old barrels used for ageing cognac were kept. In the intimate-feeling dining rooms with their hushed atmosphere, no detail has been neglected, from the exquisite contemporary silverware to the crystal glasses. The cuisine is meticulously crafted in order to showcase local ingredients from the Charente terroir: free-range poultry, fish from the fish market, Île de Ré potatoes etc. The chef sets great store by plating his dishes elegantly and perfecting his concentrated sauces: the caramelised celery jus is a seamless substitute for a meat gravy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2732;Flaveurs;France;Valence;32 Grande-Rue, Valence, 26000, France;44.9326634;4.8909199;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A colourful decor with a carpeted floor and chestnut-wood tables provides the setting for this fine gourmet restaurant situated in the heart of Valence’s old town. It was perhaps his grandfather’s job as a caterer that influenced the career choice of young chef Baptiste Poinot, who studied at the hotel school in Vienne, and took lessons with Michel Chabran in Pont-de-l’Isère, as well as with Anne-Sophie Pic and Joël Robuchon. Much thought has clearly gone into each of the dishes created by this sensitive chef, who seeks above all to convey an emotion through his cuisine using top-quality ingredients and highly skilled technique. The resulting flavours – sensations produced both by the taste and aroma of his ingredients – are particularly enticing.;Air conditioning;[]
2733;La Table Mirasol;France;Mont-de-Marsan;2 boulevard Ferdinand-de-Candau, Mont-de-Marsan, 40000, France;43.891157;-0.5036755;51;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this 1912 villa, a genuine Belle Époque period gem, the fine dining restaurant is run by chef Philippe Lagraula. He deftly blends produce from his native Landes with influences from further afield, particularly Peru, his wife's home country. The tasting menu is consummate, striking, creative and well-paced, marrying minimalism and character: squid stuffed with the first ceps of the season, squab in Armagnac with Peruvian chocolate and Aquitaine caviar. The Armagnac selection more than lived up to our expectations…;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2734;Galanga;France;Paris;Hôtel Monsieur George, 17 rue Washington, Paris, 75008, France;48.8729358;2.3025531;94;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The small, exquisitely appointed restaurant of the Art deco-inspired Monsieur George bijou hotel is plush without being starched and ideal for a twinkly date night. Youthful Thomas Danigo conjures up delicate, aromatic dishes, whose elegance and technically flawless craftsmanship pamper the tastebuds thanks to expressive, harmonious combinations. Top-drawer produce is cleverly crafted in tune with the zeitgeist, illustrated by his couscous inspired Lozère lamb, flanked by quinoa tabouleh, lamb stock and home-made harissa. The desserts, also entirely of the chef’s own devising, are equally knockout. The quintessence of fine dining paired with suitably polished but unfawning service.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2735;Ducasse au Château de Versailles - Le Grand Contrôle;France;Versailles;12 rue de l'Indépendance-Américaine, Versailles, 78000, France;48.801401;2.120209;42;true;true;Classic Cuisine, French;This luxurious establishment in the Airelles hotel is steeped in history and inextricably linked to the Palace of Versailles. It combines theatrical staging – with diners being greeted by a valet, and staff in period costume – and cuisine tailored to the occasion. Devised by Alain Ducasse, the menu comprises dishes made with premium produce that reflect the great man's commitment to naturalité. Entrusted to chef Stéphane Duchiron, the food is a masterclass in technical skill, with everything expertly cooked and seasoned, and high-quality sauces and jus bringing out the forthright, distinctive flavours of the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2736;Hélène Darroze à Villa La Coste;France;Le Puy-Sainte-Réparade;2750 route de la Cride, Le Puy-Sainte-Réparade, 13610, France;43.6329148;5.4139364;27;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Hélène Darroze fell in love with the Château La Coste, adding her own stamp to a genuine holistic work of art that showcases contemporary art and wine, on the doorstep of Lubéron. Deep in Provence, the chef has chosen to focus on fruit and vegetables: carrots and aubergines from Bruno Cayron, cherries from Florent Lazare and each dish is named after its producer. The result is delicate food, made with exceptional produce that is exquisitely yet simply presented. The menu also features a few of the recipes that have contributed to the success of this world-famous chef from southwest France, such as Gamberoni in tandoori spices or the Darroze Armagnac baba.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2737;Jardin des Sens;France;Montpellier;Place de la Canourgue, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6117844;3.8747685;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Jacques and Laurent Pourcel are at the helm of the restaurant of the lavish 17C Richer de Belleval Hotel located in the heights of Montpellier. Beneath head-spinning ceiling frescoes or on the exquisite courtyard patio, it is a joy to (re)sample the culinary talents of the Montpellier twins in which every detail is puzzled and preened over as they finetune Gallic recipes adding their hallmark creative stamp. We warrant that Richer de Belleval, botanist and founder of Montpellier’s botanic gardens, would have appreciated this gourmet score!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2738;La Chabotterie;France;Montréverd;Logis de La Chabotterie, Montréverd, 85260, France;46.879939;-1.4064951;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;With delicacies such as monkfish seared in salted butter, radishes and a pearly curry-colza cream, or saddle of lamb rolled in herbs, minty aubergine and jus of confit tomatoes, MOF chef Benjamin Patissier, who boasts stints with Patrick Henriroux at La Pyramide, Pierre Gagnaire and Anne-Sophie Pic, ticks all the boxes: top produce, consummate skill, crisp flavours and artfully dressed plates. His wife, manager and sommelière, adds the final touch to this fine dining portrait, welcoming diners into a contemporary colourful dining room, established in one of the outhouses of Chabotterie Castle.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2739;Anne;France;Paris;28 place des Vosges, Paris, 75003, France;48.8561771;2.3659006;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The Pavillon de la Reine, a magnificent residence in Place des Vosges, is named after Anne of Austria, Queen of France and wife of Louis XIII, who once lived here. In the restaurant, overseen by Mathieu Pacaud, the chef reinterprets classic dishes with skill and real talent, using top-quality ingredients which are full of flavour. An excellent dining experience awaits, whether you choose the intimate and romantic setting of the library lounge or, in fine weather, the lovely verdant courtyard garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2740;Restaurant de Tourrel;France;Saint-Rémy-de-Provence;5 rue Carnot, Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, 13210, France;43.7891048;4.8307716;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine;It was within the walls of this splendid mansion that Charles Gounod played the first bars of his opera, Mireille, to the Provençal author Frédéric Mistral, who wrote the libretto. Today, in an attractive retro-style dining room with the occasional Art Deco touch, guests can sample a culinary score inspired by the region’s finest ingredients, including outdoor Provence tomatoes, Mediterranean squid and crayfish, and lamb from Crau.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2741;Numéro 3;France;Le Tremblay-sur-Mauldre;3 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Le Tremblay-sur-Mauldre, 78490, France;48.777504;1.8770687;46;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This village was once home to famous art dealer Ambroise Vollard, as well as Picabia, Picasso and Cendrars, who is buried here. Julie and Laurent Trochain run their lovely restaurant in a former hunting lodge that they have completely renovated. What a transformation! Gone are the beams, the fireplace and even the traditional façade, replaced by an eminently contemporary, geometrical and designer setting. Laurent Trochain, originally from Maubeuge, trained in some top establishments, not least at Restaurant Pierre Gagnaire. He champions the produce of the Île-de-France region, starting with his own kitchen garden (vegetables and aromatic herbs), and of his beloved small-scale local producers. His vegetarian menu is gaining in popularity.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2742;Maison Decoret;France;Vichy;15 rue du Parc, Vichy, 03200, France;46.1246273;3.4192286;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Jacques Decoret chose to set up his restaurant in a 19C building with a large, boxy extension with a glass-paned front. Now assisted by his sons Alexis and Antoine, the chef is a master of his craft. He proposes refined and aesthetically pleasing dishes that draw on exquisite produce, while steering clear of any ostentation. The amuse-bouches also have bags of personality. If you wish to extend your stay, there are a few maison d'hôte-style rooms designed along the same contemporary lines as the rest of the property.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2744;Le Saint-Martin;France;Vence;2490 avenue des Templiers, Vence, 06140, France;43.7316508;7.1066248;75;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The stylish, yet understated Saint Martin Hotel, whose rooms command sweeping views over the hillsides of Vence and the Mediterranean, is most definitely a treat for the eye. In the plush dining room or on the drop-dead terrace, you will sample intelligently devised dishes underscored by high-flying craftsmanship and the odd gem of an ingredient, such as lacquered tuna and a medley of seafood or suckling pig, aubergines in different textures and tomatoes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2745;Les Agitateurs;France;Nice;24 rue Bonaparte, Nice, 06300, France;43.7005783;7.2843229;88;true;true;Creative;These agitators are far from the hot air breed, indeed they are full of talent! Chef Samuel Victori (former second chef at Passage 53) and his partner, Juliette Busetto, craft dishes rich in texture, flawlessly cooked and subtly seasoned. Local suppliers take the limelight: baker, fishermen, market gardener, breeder and potter. Michel Troisgros is the duo’s mentor and their concept is original, vibrant, amusing, disruptive food, served in a lively, buzzy vibe. Attentive, efficient service. The venue features two dining areas, one on the ground floor and the other in the basement with a wine cellar. The set menu changes regularly in line with the seasons. Just next door, Pirouette, a bistro founded by the same owners, offers dishes to share and natural wines.;Air conditioning;[]
2747;Le Pressoir;France;Saint-Avé;7 rue de l'Hôpital, Saint-Avé, 56890, France;47.6966578;-2.7508368;40;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Originally from Saint-Brieuc, chef Vincent David used to visit this renowned Vannes restaurant with his grandparents when he was a boy – it was here that he developed a taste for Michelin-starred restaurants! Several decades later, having convinced chefs such as Dominique Bouchet and Marc Meneau of his talent, he took over this emblematic restaurant with its now pared-down decor. Passionate about meat and fish combinations, he creates a signature cuisine in which top-quality ingredients are perfectly balanced.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2748;Baieta;France;Paris;5 rue de Pontoise, Paris, 75005, France;48.8501648;2.3523102;86;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;"Here, the bouillabaisse cosies up to the aioli, and the pissaladière (tart with onions, olives and anchovies) competes with the socca (chickpea flatbread), just out of the coal-fired oven." Julia Sedefdjian (formerly of Les Fables de la Fontaine, also in Paris) is now happily thriving in her own establishment. Her colourful and fragrant cuisine is an ode to the Mediterranean (her "Bouillabaieta", a superb take on bouillabaisse, is a must) and fine ingredients, which she selects painstakingly and blends creatively, without forgetting her roots in Nice. The chef now solely proposes a series of surprise set menus. Welcome to Baieta – which means "kiss" in the Nice dialect!;Wheelchair access;[]
2749;Substance;France;Paris;18 rue de Chaillot, Paris, 75016, France;48.8673445;2.2976536;87;true;false;Creative;Matthias Marc, a chef who honed his skills in prestigious eateries (Le Saint-James in Bouliac, Le Meurice and Lasserre in Paris) and who also took part in France’s Top Chef TV show, serves a surprise menu that favours short supply chains and sticks close to the seasons, together with nods to his native Jura. Unorthodox, vibrant cooking with a creative streak and a weakness for vegetables, together with low-sugar desserts in a modern vein. A terrific list of mostly organic or natural wines. What’s not to like?;Interesting wine list;[]
2753;Onor;France;Paris;258 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75008, France;48.8772724;2.3003097;57;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Onor, which used to be Le Marée where the chef kicked off his career, is where Thierry Marx pays tribute to everything he holds dear: the transmission of know-how and a deep respect for nature, individuals, produce and producers, but also a love of culinary innovation. A maritime-inspired interior, doubled with the vibe of a small luxury brasserie, provides the perfect foil for delicate modern cuisine by chef Ricardo Silva: textbook technique, nods to Asia and subtle flavours, strewn with Marxian signature dishes such as soy risotto or his knockout lobster raviole extravaganza.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
2755;Jean Imbert au Plaza Athénée;France;Paris;25 avenue Montaigne, Paris, 75008, France;48.8661718;2.3042735;81;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Media darling, Jean Imbert, is thriving in the iconic luxury hotel on Avenue Montaigne. In the company of a high-flying kitchen brigade, the “chef to the stars” is gleefully, almost mischievously, throwing a new light on France’s culinary heritage (langoustine "en Bellevue", mallard duck and foie gras, truffle-flavoured pullet and a line-up of desserts enthusiastically presented by a duo of pastry chefs). Seated at the majestic marble table d'hôte, surrounded by gilded moulding and chandeliers, how could you not fall under the spell?;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2756;Le Georges;France;Chartres;22 place des Épars, Chartres, 28000, France;48.4440945;1.4833258;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Le Grand Monarque, which is home to Le Georges, has stood the test of time – the hotel’s first mention in the Michelin Guide dates back to 1900! This elegantly appointed establishment is ideally located between Paris and the Loire at a crossroads between the regions of western France. Thomas Parnaud is consistently and devotedly pursuing his mission of shining the spotlight on local producers who respect the environment whilst using a top-to-tail ethos. Notable dishes include gambas from the Loire region with Sologne caviar or a flaky pastry pie of mallard duck with foie gras. It would be a crime to miss his Grand Marnier soufflé, a flawlessly crafted classic that still graces the menu. The impeccably curated wine cellar boasts some 3,000 vintages with a spotlight on Val de Loire wines. Simpler, seasonal fare in the pleasant brasserie patio. The hotel’s charming guestrooms provide the icing on the cake!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2758;Maison Nouvelle;France;Bordeaux;11 rue Rode, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8524805;-0.5721376;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the lively Chartrons market square, this pretty stone building is the newest and latest establishment of chef Philippe Etchebest, also behind Bordeaux’ Quatrième Mur. Guests are greeted like old friends and immediately feel at home in this tasteful, welcoming interior. Philippe’s unwavering commitment to good food and to working only with top local produce shines through and is clearly shared by his talented team. The tasting menu, entirely seasonal, features a few of his signature dishes, such as ravioles of mushrooms and sautéed foie gras, as well as some exquisite vegetarian recipes. Welcome to "Etxe Beste" ("new house" in Basque)!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2759;Don Juan II;France;Paris;Port Debilly, Paris, 75016, France;48.8630387;2.2959142;48;true;false;Creative;Moored next to Passerelle Debilly, a footbridge spanning the Seine, on the right bank, opposite the Eiffel Tower, the Don Juan II is a magnificent Art Deco yacht, with sumptuous wood panelling and thick carpet. Embark on a 2.5hr-long sightseeing and gourmet cruise, with an outstanding chef, Frédéric Anton, at the helm! He has selected some emblematic creations from Le Pré Catelan (curry-scented crab, langoustine ravioli, warm chocolate soufflé…) with which to indulge his passengers. As you glide down the Seine, dinner is served against the backdrop of the most iconic monuments of the City of Light, with commentary by the crew.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
2760;Le Refuge des Gourmets;France;Machilly;90 route des Framboises, Machilly, 74140, France;46.2482745;6.3282703;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this small village near the Swiss border (in Haute-Savoie), which for a long time was a major raspberry-growing area, foodies will find a refuge in this family-run establishment. The plush, Belle Époque-inspired restaurant interior has been entirely refurbished in a contemporary style. Fanny Chanove keeps a watchful eye over the smooth running of proceedings in the dining room, while chef Hubert Chanove cooks up modern cuisine with creative touches, inspired by local ingredients and wild flowers and herbs. His dishes tend to revolve around a particular season or ingredient (fish from Lake Geneva, game, black truffles etc). The bistro is open for lunch Thu-Sat, by reservation only.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2762;La Table - Christophe Hay et Loïs Bée;France;Ardon;200 allée des Quatre-Vents, au golf de Limère, Ardon, 45160, France;47.8220926;1.9124177;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Opposite Limère golf course, here is Christophe Hay's second establishment. The contemporary interior calls to mind nature and the forest, the chef's main sources of inspiration, together with vegetables from his garden. Chef Loïs Bée runs the kitchen. The fine, well-crafted cuisine is seasonal and emphasises local produce and game in season. For example, there's a rack of sturgeon with Sologne caviar, Loire carp with garum and savory vinegar, or perle noire guinea fowl stuffed with hyssop.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2764;NESO;France;Paris;3 rue Papillon, Paris, 75009, France;48.8760396;2.34745;76;true;false;Creative;The charismatic and heavily tattooed Guillaume Sanchez crafts fiery, flame-licked cuisine in a fashionably stark interior, depicted by an impossibly high ceiling and an austere metallic façade. Sanchez’ cooking, emblematic of his flamboyant personality, is only available à la carte, in keeping with his universe and ethos. The menu is divided into four main families, but, technically, nothing has changed: cold-steamed extractions and fermented vegetables. The chef works exclusively with pure-bred French, stellar produce, to which he adds his imaginative hallmark and high-flying technical expertise. The menu unfolds to reveal little bombshells of flavour with varied flavours and textures and art-directed, if unusual plating. Take a seat at the counter for a truly immersive experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2766;Chakaiseki Akiyoshi;France;Paris;59 rue Letellier, Paris, 75015, France;48.8470169;2.2988278;63;false;true;Japanese;Unique in France, Chakaiseki Akiyoshi is the first restaurant devoted to the traditional Japanese tea ceremony. Cha-kaiseki actually refers to the meal that is served with this beverage, while Yuichiro Akiyoshi is the chef’s name. Tucked away behind a suitably low-profile wooden façade, the omakase might include amberjack with ponzu jelly, tempura with grey shrimp bouillon, seabream marinated in a mix of sake, mirin and soy sauce and grilled over charcoal, sushi of mackerel, grilled salmon rice, miso soup with artichoke. Recipes that allow the super-fresh ingredients to sing, prepared in front of the client, assisted by his kimono-clad spouse. Each dish is an exquisite blend of colour and flavour, of visual artistry and zen spirituality. An exclusive, timeless experience in an interior inspired by authentic Japanese teahouses (seats only 16).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2767;La Tête en l'air;France;Vannes;43 rue de la Fontaine, Vannes, 56000, France;47.6606628;-2.7546032;68;true;false;Creative;An enthusiastic and friendly young couple, Clément Raby from Paris and Estelle Mercier from the Gard region, have succeeded in turning heads with what they call their “cuisine libre” (“free cooking”). Served in a relaxed setting, this creative, original cuisine is spot on, with recipes that really work and just the right combination of flavours. On their “blind” menus, dishes aren’t announced until after you’ve tasted them so that guests can really give their senses and tastebuds a workout!;Air conditioning;[]
2768;Pollen;France;Avignon;18 rue Joseph-Vernet, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9493415;4.8035568;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;As you wander through the narrow streets of Avignon, you will come upon this pretty restaurant with a large open kitchen. The chefs themselves deliver the food to your table while you take in the judicious wine recommendations of the enthusiastic sommelier (who is also a connoisseur of biodynamic wines). In the form of a surprise menu, chef Mathieu Desmarest proposes pared-down and balanced cuisine that evolves with the seasons by aligning with local producers. He takes advantage of ingredients of impeccable quality (octopus, bluefin tuna, pigeon). The subtle and creative dishes and marriages of bold flavours effortlessly win over diners.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2770;Vincent Favre Félix;France;Annecy;15 chemin de l'Abbaye - à Annecy-le-Vieux, Annecy, 74940, France;45.9177189;6.1416315;35;true;false;Creative;Vincent Favre-Félix has opened the doors of his stylish, modern villa set in the grounds, adorned with huge bronze statues, of the 16C Cour de l’Abbaye. The chef, who has the build of a rugby player and boasts a fine regional CV (Père Bise at Talloires, Auberge de l’Eridan and Auberge du Lac at Veyrier-du-Lac), never lacks in subtlety or delicacy. Guided by regional produce, his culinary gifts are expressed boldly and creatively through well-designed ‘carte blanche’ menus that unveil his signature dishes, such as arctic char smoked in hay. In summertime, make a beeline for the exquisite patio in the flower-decked garden and savour an alfresco fine dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2771;Le Vieux Logis;France;Trémolat;Le Bourg, Trémolat, 24510, France;44.8757019;0.8297197;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This reliably good traditional restaurant is housed in the utterly charming setting of a converted tobacco drying barn, all done out in stone and painted wood. Indeed, the whole site – the local stone buildings of an old agricultural property that was originally a priory – is delightful. Head chef Vincent Arnould, a Meilleur Ouvrier de France, is an enlightened custodian of tradition. A native of the Vosges who fell in love with the Périgord, he selects the finest produce for his modern and appealing cuisine with solid classical foundations. At lunchtime, the restaurant proposes a reasonably priced set menu featuring what might be described as Périgord-style tapas. A new take on fine dining.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2772;L'Orchidée;France;Altkirch;33 rue Gilardoni, Altkirch, 68130, France;47.6250155;7.2399636;22;true;true;Thai, Asian Contemporary;This orchid invites us on mouth-watering, gourmet voyage. The modern, scrupulously crafted Thai cuisine is elegant and perfumed, illustrated by a tom yam of blue lobster, coconut milk and galanga or Vosges squab, served with sweetcorn, girolles mushrooms, polenta and red curry. Delicious from start to finish and a phenomenal success story.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2773;Likoké;France;Les Vans;33 route de Païolive, Les Vans, 07140, France;44.4040212;4.133207;55;false;true;Creative;Likoké is the most international of Ardèche’s restaurants! Belgian-born Cyriel Huysentruyt, in charge of the front of house and wine, works side by side Colombian chef Guido Niño Torres, who upholds the establishment's globetrotting ethos. Over the course of a single set menu, he presents playful, colourful dishes like invitations to head off on a journey, sometimes inspired by a memory, an encounter, a past event… His signature dishes include ceviche of matured trout, whose composition varies with the season. Everything is sourced locally: cheese, veggies, pigeon, etc... Bang-on confident cooking that never ceases to surprise.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2774;Oxte;France;Paris;5 rue Troyon, Paris, 75017, France;48.8757794;2.2956526;78;true;true;Mexican;This pleasant and cosy little restaurant in the Étoile neighbourhood, near the Arc de Triomphe, serves delicious, contemporary Mexican-influenced cuisine. French ingredients are infused with condiments, herbs and spices by a talented and passionate Mexican chef, who also gets involved with the service. He turns out savvy and perfectly cooked dishes that are skilfully prepared with invigorating seasonings: marinated sea bream with a turnip medley and salsa tatemada, or fish from the market, al pastor, mole with carrot, pineapple or pigeon, mole Oxte, leek and pickled grapes. This colourful, punchy and well-seasoned food is so good you'll soon be back for more!;;[]
2775;Manoir de Lan-Kerellec;France;Trébeurden;11 allée centrale de Lan-Kerellec, Trébeurden, 22560, France;48.7766651;-3.5847022;95;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;In this magical setting, the ceiling's splendid wooden rafters form the shape of an inverted boat hull, while the views extend out to the Channel and local islands. Young chef Anthony Avoine, originally from Normandy and formerly second in command here, is now at the helm of the fine dining restaurant of this beautiful manor house. Breton produce is wonderfully showcased in an unapologetically creative array of dishes that often combine meat and fish. Examples include the lobster, buckwheat cake and pig's trotters, and spider crab on a hazelnut butter foam and marrowbone cooked in the embers. Local ingredients, freshness guaranteed.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
2776;Fleur de Pavé;France;Paris;5 rue Paul-Lelong, Paris, 75002, France;48.8677;2.34333;94;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;At this restaurant that is firmly rooted in the zeitgeist, chef Sylvain Sendra pursues his fascinating culinary process with his usual enthusiasm and flair. He whips up modern dishes that draw inspiration from all over the world, featuring deceptively spontaneous plating and blue-ribbon ingredients, most notably the very exclusive vegetables from the kitchen garden of Asafumi Yamashita (market gardener in Yvelines in the Greater Paris area). Rather than bowl us over with flashy technique, the chef seeks to lay the emphasis squarely on flavours and delivering on the menu's promises. For a restaurant of this size, the quality of the wine list is striking: connoisseurs might like to plump for one of the rare bottles from the selection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2777;L'Ours;France;Vincennes;12 rue de l'Église, Vincennes, 94300, France;48.8476098;2.4367513;81;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Jacky Ribault (Qui Plume la Lune, in the 11th arrondissement) makes no secret that he considers this Ours (bear), near the château de Vincennes, to be the pinnacle of his career. He designed it in his image, mixing volumes and shapes in a felicitous blend of wood, metal, stone and leather, creating a coherent setting for culinary creations of which he has the secret. Guaranteed to lift your spirits, the food is rich in everything we love in this seasoned chef, as talkative as he is enthusiastic: his instinctive hallmark, exquisite plating and raw inspirations that subtly underscore first-class ingredients. For example, the menu features understated Japanese notes, as well as more traditional fare, such as guinea fowl or brill with risotto of Venere rice in beetroot… A place of culinary pilgrimage if ever there was...;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2778;Kasbür;France;Monswiller;8 route de Dettwiller, Monswiller, 67700, France;48.7419047;7.3977237;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Founded in 1932, Kasbür has been linked to the Kieffer family for three generations. The restaurant on the outskirts of Saverne owes its name to the great-grandfather, a farmer who made his cheeses here. Yves Kieffer, his great-grandson, brought this handsome building into the modern era with its semi-circular dining room overlooking the magnificent Alsace countryside. After working in the kitchens of La Tour d'Argent and Marc Meneau's restaurant in Vézelay, the chef returned, driven by his strong sense of heritage and unwavering standards. His cooking showcases quality seasonal produce like this John Dory, marinated and precisely cooked, with green asparagus, young broad beans and fresh peas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2779;Rustique;France;Lyon;14 rue d'Enghien, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7520626;4.8262876;43;false;false;Creative;A wind of audacity has swept through Maxime Laurenson’s restaurant. Precise, legible dishes reveal each ingredient simply, with a firm focus on vegetables and a steadfast commitment to locally sourced produce. The single set menu (no choice) features a dozen or so courses, each of which stars the best of a region that spans Auvergne to the Alps. The interior is clearly inspired by nature (stone, wood, colour, plants) and the vibe is friendly. A down-to-earth establishment that is a favourite with Lyon’s foodies.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2781;Auberge du Vert Mont;France;Boeschepe;1318 rue du Mont-Noir, Boeschepe, 59299, France;50.7929337;2.7033586;88;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Tucked away in the heart of the countryside, chef Florent Ladeyn, an ecological champion from the word go, is a standard-bearer of authentic Flemish fare steeped in gourmet flavours, albeit with a creative, instinctive spin. In a dining room, refurbished from top to toe with exposed rafters and overlooking the West Flanders hillsides, the chef unveils his passion for ember roasting, which he carries out in front of diners. Firmly committed to local produce, he strews his creations with flowers and plants from the region. And while his Maroilles fries covered with a thin layer of caramelised onion has attained almost legendary status, we highly recommend his “blind” menu, which has to be for everyone at the table, rich in gourmet delights!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2782;Shabour;France;Paris;19 rue Saint-Sauveur, Paris, 75002, France;48.8659204;2.3490797;53;false;false;Creative;The man behind Shabour is Assaf Granit, the high-profile Israeli chef. Already owner of a dozen restaurants in Jerusalem and London, he also presents Israeli TV's version of Kitchen Nightmares. He set his sights on this 17C building in a lively neighbourhood between rue Saint-Denis and rue Montorgueil. Here, we rediscover his trademarks: a lively atmosphere, rough and ready decoration with metal technical ducts visible on the ceiling, subdued lighting... and, of course, generous and surprising creative cuisine replete with Mediterranean influences, whose freshness gives it wings – for example, carrots with slow-cooked egg, tahini foam, salmon eggs and tzimmes, seared mullet in an eastern take on bouillabaisse, or semolina pudding with orange blossom and crème anglaise with pumpkin.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
2785;En Marge;France;Aureville;Lieu dit Le Birol, 1204 route de Lacroix-Falgarde,, Aureville, 31320, France;43.49083;1.44087;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Frank Renimel and his wife have transformed a former farmstead into a gourmet loft decked in wood and stone, whose floor to ceiling windows embrace the rolling countryside. Perfectly in tune with the seasons, the chef changes his menu monthly, blending local, rustic fare with noble ingredients such as caviar, truffles or cèpes. The diner is often bowled over by Renimel’s craftsmanship, such are the emotions created by each bite, which is the case with the chef’s version of cassoulet, a firm fixture on the menu. To pleasantly prolong your stay, five exquisitely appointed guestrooms add the final flourish to a gourmet getaway, where the accent is on good taste.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2786;Origines;France;Le Broc;Rue du Clos-de-la-Chaux, Le Broc, 63500, France;45.5014095;3.2436174;48;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Est-ce l'Auvergne, sa région natale, qui inspire à Adrien Descouls cette cuisine pleine de fraîcheur ? Tout près d'Issoire, dans ce bâtiment moderne perché juste à côté d’un château du 14e  s., le chef affirme ses qualités sans jamais en rajouter : choix du produit, capacité à mettre en valeur le terroir local (et le potager de la maison !), et cette jeunesse, qui permet parfois de déplacer des volcans ! Un style plutôt contemporain et épuré, mais qui peut toutefois lorgner vers une cuisine plus classique et réconfortante sur certains plats, à l'image de l’excellent médaillon de volaille farci, sabayon aux cèpes d'été et jus corsé. Au déjeuner, on propose uniquement la carte du bistrot Le Basalte : une option qui permet de profiter de la vue magique et d'apprécier la cuisine du chef dans une version plus simple.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2788;Gordon Ramsay au Trianon;France;Versailles;1 boulevard de la Reine, Versailles, 78000, France;48.8112259;2.1209203;71;true;true;Creative;Opened in 1910 on the edge of the palace grounds, the Trianon Palace hotel makes its authoritative presence known to walkers who get close to it. What better place to host the work – and fiery character! – of Gordon Ramsay, already a three-starred chef in London? Head chef Gabriele Ravasio is on site to bring to life a menu that is a celebration of fine produce, playing on the simplicity and relevance of the dishes. Well-managed creativity, appealing flavours… Everything conspires to make for a most enjoyable experience, and the location certainly plays its part: an elegant and luminous baroque dining space, with bay windows looking straight out onto the grounds.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2789;Quai des Saveurs;France;Hagondange;69 rue de la Gare, Hagondange, 57300, France;49.2534752;6.1646539;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Frédéric Sandrini has settled in this pink sandstone and white fronted edifice opposite Hagondange railway station. Your tastebuds will be delighted by the modern, imaginative craftsmanship of this chef, on a constant quest for suppliers-partners whom he selects meticulously: abalone, hand-harvested by divers in the Bay of St Brieuc, fish from Saint-Quay-Portrieux or Boulogne-sur-Mer and a cheese trolley piled high with produce from “star” cheesemakers. Meals are served in a contemporary, pared-down interior. Two surprise menus and a set lunchtime menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2791;Maison Hache;France;Eygalières;30 rue de la République, Eygalières, 13810, France;43.7609722;4.9499672;65;false;false;Provençal;In his eponymous restaurant, chef Christopher Hache concocts a delicious tribute to Provence and the Alpilles. He does so by scrupulously selecting, in no particular order, his fruit and vegetables, lamb and regional wines: the focus here is on local ingredients and producers. The dishes themselves are simple in form, straightforward, and as natural and forthright as the flavours they exude (such as the superb lamb jus) – without unnecessary fuss or frills. Don't miss out on his grilled Camargue oyster, artichoke barigoule, artichoke leaf jus, or his pieds paquets with bluefin tuna from Le Grau-du-Roi... a real treat! Rounding off the experience: a range of breads made with natural leaven from the nearby Boulangerie Hache, a chic decor, an inspired wine list and wonderfully comfortable guestrooms upstairs. In short, an excellent establishment.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2792;L'Aromate;France;Nice;2 rue Gustave-Deloye, Nice, 06000, France;43.6992157;7.269895;95;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This attractive restaurant is idyllically located near Place Masséna in the heart of Nice. The contemporary decor sports a black, white and gold colour scheme, untreated materials such as wood and granite and a glazed kitchen overlooking the dining room. The scene is set for chef, Mickaël Gracieux, armed with an iron-clad CV (Oustau de Baumanière, Plaza Athénée, Le Bristol, Louis XV, etc), to craft modern, creative and elegantly presented cuisine using top-quality produce from Nice and the Mediterranean (San Remo prawns, trumpet courgettes, local green crab, squid and citrus fruits, etc). A chef with the background and the ambition to achieve his high-flying goals.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2793;JAN;France;Nice;12 rue Lascaris, Nice, 06300, France;43.6998945;7.2848004;27;true;false;Creative;South African chef Jan Hendrik van der Westhuizen, whose former careers involved working as a chef on private yachts in Monaco and as a photojournalist for a top magazine, has already lived several lives… In his cosy (20-seater), romantic eatery near the port, he signs creative, personal cuisine in the shape of a single set menu, in which he plays on sweet and sour combinations, and dabbles in smoky, spicy and acidic flavours, giving us an insight into South African cuisine. When it is time for cheese, you will discover a cheese bar opposite the restaurant with a buffet of some twenty different cheeses, a range of beverages, preserves and dried fruit.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2794;L'Atlantide 1874 - Maison Guého;France;Nantes;5 rue de l'Hermitage, Nantes, 44100, France;47.2012378;-1.5777426;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Just around the corner from the Musée Jules Verne, this fine mansion dating from 1874 overlooks the River Loire and the Île de Nantes. Through the restaurant's large panoramic windows, you can observe the boats as they come and go, Le Hangar à Bananes and the grey Titan crane – an emblem of the port city of Nantes. A Breton (from Vannes) who trained in Alsace at the Auberge de l'Ill before working as a chef in New Orleans and Hong Kong, Jean-Yves Guého conjures up a highly precise and refined array of dishes in which fish takes pride of place. The list of Loire wines is well worth perusing. Pretty, modern guestrooms with a view.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2795;Le Manoir de la Régate;France;Nantes;155 route de Gachet, Nantes, 44300, France;47.2936105;-1.5263375;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;On the outskirts of Nantes in a beautiful residence near the Erdre, a chic and trendy decor and a menu of culinary delights awaits in this enticing restaurant. Chef Mathieu Pérou, who has worked in many Michelin-starred properties, skilfully combines fresh and elegant flavours in his beautifully presented dishes which he prepares using the region’s best ingredients. Front of house, his sister Anne-Charlotte oversees the highly professional service.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2796;Restaurant De Lauzun;France;Pézenas;Route de Nizas, Pézenas, 34120, France;43.4827871;3.4116289;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Pézenas is not only the city of Molière, it is also the HQ of Matthieu de Lauzun. Established in a winery in the priory of Saint-Jean de Bébian, this venue provides a stage for the chef to roll out his manifold talents. A chic neoteric interior, done up in stone, wood and copper, provides the perfect foil to the chef’s delicate, tasty Mediterranean score, liberally scattered with childhood and globetrotting souvenirs. The Grenoble-style skate wing and its gribiche sauce are consummately curated, as are the chicken pastilla with marinated beetroot, a nod to the chef’s roots, and the Ségala veal with an aubergine and feta flan and a punchy red wine gravy. The sommelier can be relied upon to ply you with first-rate tips and to suggest inspired pairings from the extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2798;Le Chantecler;France;Nice;Le Negresco, 37 promenade des Anglais, Nice, 06000, France;43.6943015;7.2580067;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the Promenade des Anglais, Le Negresco, which celebrates its 110th anniversary in 2023, sits majestically in its seafront location. Le Chantecler, its fine dining restaurant, has "Meilleur Ouvrier de France" 2015 Virginie Basselot at the helm. In this exceptional setting, the Normandy-born chef doesn't beat around the bush, training her laser-like focus on serving up creative contemporary cuisine in the form of two set menus (without options, except for the dessert course) and an à la carte menu made from top-notch ingredients. Simplicity wins the day: cf. the poultry, white cabbage, kumquat and pistachio, or the subtle use of olive oil in the sweet dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2800;Moulin de la Tardoire;France;Montbron;6 route du Bounit (Lieu-dit la Forge), Montbron, 16220, France;45.6768252;0.5138297;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Teeming with history, this 16C forge was converted into a flour mill in 1854 and later into an olive oil mill. It now houses a charmingly bucolic restaurant situated by the river and surrounded by greenery. Here, chef Matthieu Brudo serves up seasonal cuisine with a focus on local ingredients, including snails from the Charente, squab and duck breast from Nontron, and other top-quality meats which he buys whole from small producers in the local area. Refined, well-crafted and carefully presented dishes that meet with our approval!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2801;La Réserve Rimbaud;France;Montpellier;820 avenue de Saint-Maur, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6171176;3.8930311;93;false;true;Modern Cuisine;“Montpellier the Gifted”, as the city likes to bill itself, provides the backdrop to this well-hidden restaurant on the banks of the Lez. Slightly off the beaten track, it boasts a divine riverside terrace shaded by plane trees – a refreshing haven in hot summers. This modern and sophisticated Reserve is located in an old country house, an Ali Baba’s cavern of gourmet delights, unearthed from the little-known repertory of Languedoc-Roussillon. Former second of Alain Dutournier at the Carré des Feuillants, Charles Fontès signs intelligent compositions that revolves around the ingredient. Subtle plays of textures and flavours with an overriding goal of authentic simplicity. Seabream, squid and red mullet, Camargues eels and Lucques olives feature among the appetisers – Occitania on the table!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2802;L'Écrin de Yohann Chapuis;France;Tournus;1 rue Albert-Thibaudet, Tournus, 71700, France;46.5656876;4.9078059;23;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;A former orphanage provides an out-of-the-ordinary venue for the cuisine of Yohann Chapuis, who learned the ropes at Lameloise. The chef crafts food rich in “taste and emotion”, which has its own distinct identity and character, thanks to premium seasonal produce, like crayfish from the Saône, turbot caught by small fishing boats, and Charolais beef, all exquisitely presented. Morels, green asparagus, tempura of langoustine or saddle and cutlets of lamb, anchovies, goat and spinach gnocchi and a thyme jus. An excellent wine list and a knowledgeable sommelier complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2803;Une Table, au Sud;France;Marseille;2 quai du Port, Marseille, 13002, France;43.2962224;5.3735291;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Ludovic Turac, who boasts stints at Le Bristol and Guy Savoy, is at the helm of this fully refurbished navy-blue restaurant, firmly anchored in the South of France. Using regional veggies, locally caught fish and meat from the southern Alps, the chef crafts two several-course menus: “From the Sea to the Land” displays a strong Marseillais twang, while the “Spice Crossroads” unveils numerous nods to his travels around the Mediterranean and his own Armenian roots. In short, Turac pays tribute to the countries that have influenced Marseilles’ culinary heritage. His inventive recipes are always packed with flavour and perfectly in tune with the knockout panorama over the Old Port and “La Bonne Mère” (as Notre Dame basilica up on the hill is affectionately dubbed by the locals).;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2805;Le Carmin;France;Beaune;4B place Carnot, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0225391;4.8377091;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;On Place Carnot, not far from the Hôtel-Dieu, this restaurant with a modern façade occupies the ground floor of a picturesque old house. After stints with Robuchon and Ducasse, chef Christophe Quéant crafts modern, seasonal cuisine based on traditional textbook foundations. His top-quality ingredients are transformed into spot-on, straightforward dishes, blessedly free of fancy frills. The contemporary-style dining room, which sports a beige colour scheme and exposed stonework, is the perfect foil for delicious dishes such as caramelised quail breasts and legs, white asparagus and baby carrots and the hot Grand Marnier soufflé – to die for!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2806;Couleurs de Shimatani;France;La Ciotat;35 rue Edgar-Quinet, La Ciotat, 13600, France;43.1751771;5.6101244;49;false;false;Fusion;The seasoned couple of Yuichiro (chef) and Mika Shimatani (pastry chef) decided that they couldn’t choose between the Mediterranean and Japan. In a dinky eatery, bang in the middle of a pedestrian street, they take you on a gourmet cruise from the land of the Rising Sun to the Mediterranean. Exquisitely fresh seafood and vegetables play a central role in a culinary score that bears the Japanese hallmark of high precision cooking, immaculate plating and delicate seasonings. This delicacy also encompasses Mika’s gracious table service. Open lunchtime only (take away meals can be ordered on Saturday evenings only).;Air conditioning;[]
2808;Le Pot d'Étain;France;Danjoutin;4 avenue de la République, Danjoutin, 90400, France;47.6160064;6.8592762;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A few minutes from Bartholdi's Lion de Belfort, Le Pot d'Étain is a treasure trove of culinary gems, thanks to talented chef Philippe Zeiger, who has made his restaurant an absolute must for anyone who loves good food. The chef showcases hearty and delicious French cuisine that he prepares using superb seasonal ingredients, including langoustines, scallops, hare à la royale, turbot and truffles. The desserts also hold their own, particularly the excellent hot soufflé, which comes in a variety of flavours depending on the season. The restaurant also boasts an extensive wine list, and you can look forward to attentive, friendly service courtesy of the chef's wife.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2809;AinTimiste;France;Poncin;4 rue de la Pompe, Poncin, 01450, France;46.0858481;5.4078158;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the doorstep of the Cerdon vineyards, this picturesque medieval village in the Bugey and Revermont region is home to a knockout establishment! Jérôme Busset works tirelessly (in and out of his open-plan kitchen) to craft an intelligent surprise menu with various options. Painstakingly sourced local produce, insightful wine tips and a soothing interior. The epitome of rural Ain.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2810;Le Restaurant des Rois - La Réserve de Beaulieu;France;Beaulieu-sur-Mer;5 boulevard du Maréchal-Leclerc, Beaulieu-sur-Mer, 06310, France;43.7059731;7.33508;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Dating back to 1880 and later extended in a Renaissance Florentine style, this is one of the most opulent luxury hotels on the French Riviera. Since 1900 it has been playing host to monarchs and Hollywood stars, from Rita Hayworth to Frank Sinatra. Dining on the terrace facing the Mediterranean is a magical experience. At the helm is chef Julien Roucheteau, straight from Paris (Table du Lancaster, Scène Thélème). He remains loyal to the establishment's heritage, but adds his signature graphic presentations to dishes characterised by consummate craftsmanship. Each has its own specific theme: fresh, invigorating, luscious, unctuous.;Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2811;Ekaitza;France;Ciboure;15 quai Maurice-Ravel, Ciboure, 64500, France;43.3852589;-1.6674639;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The location, on the docks of Ciboure overlooking the port, is eminently suited to a restaurant called "storm" (ekaitza in Basque). The eatery’s interior, meanwhile, is bright and lively, with pretty carpentry tables from which you can steal glances into the kitchen at the far end of the dining room. Guillaume Roget magnifies the best of the Basque region, in particular fish from Saint-Jean-de-Luz fish market opposite. Creativity matched with fine produce and delicate sweet, acidic or vegetable notes embodies the chef’s signature. His flair for deep, intense sauces will knock your socks off, illustrated by a stock of langoustine shells blended with foie gras, or fish stock perfumed with verbena and then reduced with sweet chestnut honey. A banquet of rich, gutsy flavours that nonetheless deftly sidesteps the trap of being overly cloying or starchy. Something of a culinary landmark on the Basque coast.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2813;Ochre;France;Rueil-Malmaison;56 rue du Gué, Rueil-Malmaison, 92500, France;48.8778387;2.1830535;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Welcome to the world of Baptiste Renouard, so young yet already a seasoned veteran – he honed his skills for over 14 years, completing stints at Lasserre, Robuchon, Alléno, Laurent and L'Escargot 1903, no less! This is vibrant, joyful and technically flawless cuisine, out of which the chef devises a carte blanche menu. Plants play a major role: 70% of the herbs and flowers used are picked by the chef himself on the nearby island, Île des Impressionnistes. The restaurant is located in a small, semi-pedestrianised street in the town centre. The contemporary interior has stone walls, exposed beams and raw natural materials.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2814;L'Empreinte;France;Buxy;2 Grande-Rue, Buxy, 71390, France;46.712869;4.694296;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The young couple at the head of this restaurant have worked in some of the region's finest establishments. Their repertoire is up-to-date and draws on their respective regions of origin: Auvergne for Tiffany and Burgundy for Maxime. The set menus are keenly priced, while the cheese trolley boasts several dozen varieties. A good all-round experience indeed!;Air conditioning;[]
2815;Dan B.;France;Ventabren;1 rue Frédéric-Mistral, Ventabren, 13122, France;43.53894;5.29218;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the heart of the picturesque hilltop village of Ventabren is certainly one of the most elegant in the region. The interior design is strikingly modern: Scandinavian furnishings, angled mirrors on the ceiling and, of course, the superb panoramic view over the Étang de Berre and the valley of the River Arc. Under the direction of Toulon-born chef Dan Bessoudo, the creativity also extends to the fresh, colourful cuisine, which is full of contrasts and is made with carefully selected local produce.;Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
2816;Frédéric Molina au Moulin de Léré;France;Vailly;270 route de Léré, Sous la Côte, Vailly, 74470, France;46.30015;6.53959;97;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Deep in the Brevon Valley, this converted 17C mill is run by two passionate foodies: chef Frédéric Molina, a winegrower's son, who has worked all over Europe, and his partner Irene Gordejuela. Originally hailing from a small village between the Basque Country and Rioja, she extends a warm welcome with a charming Spanish accent. In this rural setting, the pair share a philosophy of eco-responsibility: they promote sustainable agriculture in the village by working with carefully selected producers, and even use biodegradable containers. The six- or eight-course surprise set menu is an absolute delight, as is the excellent local bread, made with natural organic sourdough.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2818;Trente-Trois;France;Paris;Maison Villeroy, 33 rue Jean-Goujon, Paris, 75008, France;48.8652115;2.304464;69;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This plush, wainscoted Belle Époque dining room is located at N°33 in a discreet hotel, set in what is known as the Golden Triangle near the Champs Élysées. Chef Sébastien Sanjou has a knack for selecting premium produce, with which he composes a voluntarily concise menu, signing subtle, up-to-date, seasonal dishes that hit the spot every time from impeccable cooking and superlative jus and sauces to exquisitely balanced flavours. Decadently discreet.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2819;Divellec;France;Paris;18 rue Fabert, Paris, 75007, France;48.8610318;2.3114674;67;false;true;Seafood;The famous restaurant of Jacques Le Divellec (1983-2013) is now the lair of Mathieu Pacaud. The culinary theme continues to demonstrate a seafaring slant and the food keeps pace with the tides, paying a fine tribute to first-class seafood, such as sole meunière from small boats with hazelnut butter or wild young turbot from Brittany. Take a seat on the deck and savour the view over the Esplanades of the Invalides. The establishment has even extended its premises into a former bookshop, creating a winter garden-inspired room depicted by woven wicker panels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2822;Avel Vor;France;Port-Louis;25 rue de Locmalo, Port-Louis, 56290, France;47.7061536;-3.3474837;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A brisk avel vor ("sea breeze" in Breton) depicts this seaside eatery. Camille Lacome and Agathe Richou craft flavoursome recipes rooted in the region (flawlessly fresh seafood, buckwheat, Guémené andouille, gwell, fermented milk) dotted with subtle Mediterranean accents (olive oil, thyme, tomato water). Spot-on, aromatic dishes served in a spacious modern setting.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2823;Miraflores;France;Lyon;112 boulevard des Belges, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7683063;4.8585914;51;true;false;Peruvian;Chef Carlos Camino, a native of Peru, takes you on a cheerful tour of French-Peruvian cuisine in a lovely contemporary-style dining area complete with open kitchen. This chic and refined space is the setting for the sincere and personal cuisine of a chef whose maturity and commitment elevate top-notch produce. Striking flavours and interplays of textures: intelligent, poetic cuisine, such as the hierba luisa ceviche, tiger's milk with black cocoa, or the palo santo braised pota (giant squid), seafoam and nikkei sauce. A tasty and adventurous place.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2826;Allium;France;Quimper;88 boulevard de Créac'h-Gwen, Quimper, 29000, France;47.97616;-4.09825;59;true;false;Creative;Thanks to a crowd funding campaign, Frédérique and Lionel Hénaff have opened the restaurant of their dreams. The chef’s inventive streak is harnessed to a score that focuses on fresh produce and encompasses a multitude of ingredients (herbs, flowers) with a weakness for siphoned sauces. A tasteful, elegant vibe sets the scene in the dining room, which also boasts a handful of seats at the counter facing the open kitchen.;Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2827;La Table de La Butte;France;Plouider;12 rue de la Mer, Plouider, 29260, France;48.6110535;-4.2986479;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Nicolas and Solenne Conraux are the third generation at the head of this establishment, which has become a pioneer in the field of sustainable development and cookery. From the eco-friendly grounds to the staff’s organic cotton apparel, everything is geared towards wellness of mind and body. In the kitchen, Nicolas is as attentive to the Goulven coast, visible on the horizon, as he is to produce from the Brittany countryside. Oysters, lobster, pork, abalone, but also seaweed, vegetables and Brittany cheeses jostle for the leading roles in this star-studded cast of local delicacies. Almost every dish hovers between surf and turf. The bread (baked in the chef’s own bakery) is fiendishly delicious, as are the various Made in Brittany butters (seaweed, fleur de sel, etc). The wine cellar features an interesting selection produced by small, often organic, wineries.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2828;L'Arbre au Soleil;France;Le Lavandou;Nouveau Port, Le Lavandou, 83980, France;43.1372393;6.37491;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine;We first met Yorann Vandreissche at the Carrefour de l'Arbre, by the cobblestones of the Paris-Roubaix race. He enjoyed five successful years there, but is now basking in the sunshine at L'Arbre au Soleil, opposite Le Lavandou's marina. He shines the spotlight on premium quality produce in a menu that displays a distinct penchant for fish and seafood, eg pollack from Brittany, artichokes barigoule and artichoke purée… Refreshing, contrasts, skill: don't hesitate to come!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2829;Tomy & Co;France;Paris;22 rue Surcouf, Paris, 75007, France;48.8605434;2.3095202;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Two minutes from Rue Saint Dominique, this establishment bears the hallmark of Cambodian-born chef, Tomy Gousset, who is forging ahead in a no-holds barred, gleeful approach. A relative latecomer to food (23 years old), he perfected his skills at the Meurice, Taillevent and Boulud in New York. Today he plays a gourmet-bistro score, firmly in tune with his era, placing his “karma” (his own words) at the service of taste and the ingredient in a genuine spirit of local sourcing. His motto: “Simplicity and sophistication”, or, in our words this time: “A slap up good meal”!;Air conditioning;[]
2830;Les Sources de Fontbelle;France;Angoulême;1 bis rue des Meules-à-Grains, Angoulême, 16000, France;45.6288809;0.14218;81;false;false;Creative;Five minutes from the centre, you can’t miss this spectacular modern edifice built out of metal, concrete and glass, overlooking the forest. At its helm is chef Guillaume Veyssière, who signs an innovative repertory underscored by spot-on technique. The eye-catching venue suits the chef and his flair for theatricality down to a T, from the appetisers to the desserts, such as an amazing sweet-toothed concoction of cep mushrooms and parsley. His endeavours to keep it local are laudable and feed into his success, a case in point being Imperial prawns from the Charentes marshlands with smoked dill oil and black garlic. At lunchtime, tuck into a seasonal menu at the Forêt des Sources bistro.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2831;Solstice;France;Paris;45 rue Claude-Bernard, Paris, 75005, France;48.8402902;2.3458979;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;If there are "writers' writers", then there are chefs' chefs. A Meilleur Ouvrier de France, a mainstay of the Ferrandi gastronomy school, promoter of culinary design, restaurateur in Tokyo, Éric Trochon is that sort of chef – admired and yet relatively little known. He and his sommelier wife preside over this modern, intimate-feeling restaurant with a decor that blends designer furnishings and unfinished walls. The menu also errs towards minimalism, with just two on-point proposals (one is an omakase menu). The dishes showcase French cuisine with Japanese and Korean touches, such as volaille du Gâtinais (PGI poultry) with wild cinnamon leaf and its succulent juices with white miso. Two places with a view into the kitchens are available at the counter.;Air conditioning;[]
2832;Signature;France;Marseille;180 rue du Rouet, Marseille, 13008, France;43.2764287;5.3944545;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Cheerful Coline Faulquier celebrates Mediterranean values of sharing by means of fiendishly well-devised tasting menus. The ingredients are carefully selected – from organic market gardeners, wild herb gatherers and local fishing boats, and you will enjoy tucking into her spin on the classic "Aïoli", comprised of a mosaic of crunchy vegetables, monkfish and hake, aioli (both as a sauce and iced) or the catch of the day served with a beurre blanc and tangy pickles… Personality, enthusiasm, flavour: a true signature style.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2833;Rozó;France;Marcq-en-Barœul;34 rue Raymond-Derain, Marcq-en-Barœul, 59700, France;50.6752;3.0909516;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Chef Diego Delbecq and his pastry chef partner Camille Pailleau have channelled all of their energy and talent into this former printing works, turning it into a loft-style restaurant, with tables set out beneath the vast glass roof and its metal beams. Lovely hardwood floors, light-coloured walls and large kitchens separated by glass panes from the elegant dining area, which has a mezzanine on which hors-d'oeuvres are served with the aperitif during the evening service. The chef cooks up creative, inspired and delicate cuisine that shows a penchant for sauces, tangy and bitter notes, condiments and peppers – plus the obligatory nods to the cuisine of this northern region of France (eg endive, tarte au sucre). And he does so with a striking sense of balance when it comes to flavours. For example, Cobrieux asparagus with fresh mint and lime condiment, or roast chicken with peas and meadowsweet sabayon. Regulars can rest assured that the two signature dishes are present and correct: the "terre & mer végétal" starter ("plant-based surf 'n' turf") and the heather honey dessert. Friendly service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2835;Hedone;France;Toulouse;2 impasse Saint-Félix, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.5964008;1.4616287;74;false;false;Creative;Don't be fooled by Balthazar Gonzalez's young age: his game plan is crystal clear! No more than six tables, a surprise menu at lunchtime and dinner and a scattering of à la carte dishes set the scene, giving free rein to his no-holds barred creativity: buttery baked blue lobster, confit of carrots in lobster stock, nasturtium leaves and oil. The antithesis of fast food, expect to spend up to 3 or 4 hours to do justice to this hedonistic experience. Outstanding, fresh produce, with a preference for vegetables and seafood and explosive flavours with some real show-stopping moments. We can only salute his daring and applaud his talent.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2836;Le Royal;France;Champillon;Hameau de Bellevue, 9 rue de la République, Champillon, 51160, France;49.0907189;3.9770727;69;true;false;Creative;Between Reims and Épernay, this luxury hotel, set in a sort of modern-day amphitheatre built out of light-coloured stone, hugs the hillsides of Champagne. The interior celebrates the wine and the gilded ceiling sports a huge chandelier with 36 blown-glass orbs (bubbles). There is also a nod to Napoleon Bonaparte, said to have stopped off here when it was a coaching inn. The perfect foil to high-flying haute cuisine in tune with the seasons and founded on traditions that traverse the annals of French cookery, further enhanced by a crack front-of-house team. The wine cellar is, of course, well stocked in bubbly!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2837;Aux Terrasses;France;Tournus;18 avenue du 23-Janvier, Tournus, 71700, France;46.5590372;4.9143701;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine;After a tour of Saint Philibert Abbey, take a break on these enchanting terraces. Bare stone walls and large untreated solid oak tables set the scene indoors, flooded in light thanks to floor-to-ceiling windows. The peaceful garden and attentive service lavished by the chef’s wife are also outstanding. Chef Jean-Michel is an enthusiast, capable of changing his gourmet offering from one table to another in the same evening. His approach is entirely instinctive. His food is thus rich in emotion and establishes a natural complicity with the region, particularly through the use of first-rate local fruit and vegetables and other top-quality ingredients, whilst compromising nothing in terms of high-precision cooking. His weekday lunchtime Market menu is a bargain!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2838;Ar Men Du;France;Névez;47 rue des Îles, à Raguenès-Plage, Névez, 29920, France;47.7888421;-3.7999121;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Imagine wild moorland buffeted by the ocean with the rocky island of Raguenez glinting in the sunshine just a short distance away. Sustainable gastronomy is the name of the game here: the ingredients are strictly seasonal, harvested from the vegetable garden or sourced from small-scale producers, and the fish is caught locally. Comfortably seated with a view of the sea, diners enjoy Jérôme Gourmelen's dishes, characterised by well-defined flavours and careful presentation, eg his symphony of raw ikejime fish. Friendly service.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2839;La Bastide de Moustiers;France;Moustiers-Sainte-Marie;511 chemin de Quinson, Moustiers-Sainte-Marie, 04360, France;43.8384829;6.2182274;86;true;true;Provençal;A swish handsome bastide sets the scene for a Mediterranean score that stars ingredients from the market and the kitchen garden managed by two full-time staff (don’t miss the adjoining herb garden). The chef pays tribute to the Provençal and Mediterranean repertory so dear to Alain Ducasse, such as lightly seared giant red shrimp paired with courgette flower stuffed with ricotta and ‘nduja. Vegetables take the limelight and boast their own bespoke menu. The pleasant setting, including a plethora of olive trees and a plane tree-shaded terrace, adds to the attraction of this quintessential Provençal postcard.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
2840;La Robe;France;Montaigu;2 rue Neuve, Montaigu, 85600, France;46.9776325;-1.3118794;57;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Established in an elegant, modern edifice laid out around a patio, Xavier Giraudet rustles up a heroic culinary score in which vegetables are often cast in the leading roles. The produce is local, seasonal (often from the family cottage garden), the cooking is confident and the flavours are to die for!;Wheelchair access;[]
2841;Les Clefs d'Argent;France;Mont-de-Marsan;333 avenue des Martyrs-de-la-Résistance, Mont-de-Marsan, 40000, France;43.8870697;-0.5129182;30;false;true;Creative;This eatery, refurbished in a fashionable, low-key vein, is located outside the town centre. The seasoned chef is a champion of nature and local produce and he pays tribute to southwest France (particularly the Landes) with dishes like secreto of pork garnished with apricot and chorizo pickles, or a humus of white pochas beans with crab, peppers and anchovies. The stonking wine bin boasts over 600 references.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2842;Domaine du Colombier;France;Malataverne;270 chemin de Malombre, Malataverne, 26780, France;44.4688517;4.7429648;28;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Built on the ruins of a monastery hermitage in the heart of Provençale Drôme, this proud homestead first woos us with its bare stone walls, vaulted ceilings, vintage furnishings and patio. The cuisine celebrates regional and Mediterranean produce thanks to spot-on recipes: accurate, precise cooking, flavoursome, balanced recipes, all of which in keeping with the establishment’s sustainable development ethos.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2843;Pastis Restaurant;France;Montpellier;3 rue Terral, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6100075;3.8738324;81;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Wend your way along the narrow Rue Terral to this comfortable and attractively appointed restaurant. You will quickly understand why it is one of Montpellier’s most popular eateries! It is impossible to resist Daniel Lutrand’s cuisine, which is both inspired and inspiring, refined and delicate, in a bid to showcase the region’s top producers. An example: green asparagus coated in a gel of nori seaweed, fillet of seabream confit in olive oil flanked by an elderflower emulsion. Two affordable lunchtime menus and a “surprise” menu in the evening whose composition depends on the chef’s inspiration. Cheerful, enthusiastic service by manager and business partner Jean-Philippe Vivant. Knockout wine list with over 600 references.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2844;Omar Dhiab;France;Paris;23 rue Hérold, Paris, 75001, France;48.8652933;2.3421907;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Almost next-door to Place des Victoires, youthful Omar Dhiab, who boasts a cast-iron CV (Lasserre, l’Abeille, Loiseau Rive Gauche), has found himself a minimalist lair with an open-plan kitchen and a splendid white marble counter. His cuisine revolves around a flavoursome score, rich in creative notes, such as marinated seabream with kumquat and lovage condiment or braised matured Jersey beef, jazzed up with green pepper and smoked sardines. The light, tempting desserts sing an ode to the seasons. In the company of a youthful, enthusiastic team, the chef is equally at home in the kitchen as in the front of house.;Wheelchair access;[]
2845;Arborescence;France;Croix;76 rue de la Gare, Croix, 59170, France;50.676915;3.141823;42;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Established in an entirely rehabilitated industrial wasteland (an early-20C textile factory), chef Félix Robert and his wife Nidta, having previously worked for Alexandre Gauthier at La Grenouillère in Tokyo and then at Troisgros, now give free rein to their talents in a stripped-back, stylish interior. The chef's creative and personal repertory is dominated by seafood and vegetables and liberally scattered with nods to Japan and Asia – tempura, bao, Vietnamese coriander and Thai curry are unveiled in set menus. One example is lightly seared langoustine, flanked by a frothy rhubarb jus and subtly perfumed with ginger – stunning and oh so convincing! A restaurant whose dazzling success is well deserved.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2847;L'Ekrin by Laurent Azoulay;France;Méribel;Le Kaïla, 124 rue des Jeux-Olympiques, Méribel, 73550, France;45.3940091;6.5673633;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine;L’Ekrin is the perfect fit for this elegant, luxury hotel, offering its guests an intimate setting in which to enjoy an aperitif by the open fire to the sound of quiet piano music in the background. Chef Laurent Azoulay, himself the son of restaurateurs, worked at the Oustau de Baumanière and for chef Pierre Gagnaire before taking the helm here. Skilfully playing with the flavours and traditions of different regions, Azoulay takes guests on a culinary journey through his native Provence and adopted Savoie. He includes the best Mediterranean fish on his menu, alongside ingredients such as pine honey, saffron and snails from the Savoie, as well as vegetables sourced from Éric Roy in Tours. The result is creative and colourful cuisine which is refined and delicate yet also offers some bold combinations.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2848;Les Trois Rochers;France;Combrit;16 rue du Phare, à Sainte-Marine, Combrit, 29120, France;47.8734453;-4.1191145;30;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the Odet estuary, opposite the pretty port of Bénodet, the view overlooks the sea on one side and a forest of pine and oaks on the other… You could do worse! The chef, who trained in Quimper and has worked in Brittany and Switzerland, aims above all to highlight the work of the craftspeople and producers of Brittany (essentially organic) in his menus. He combines regional delicacies with spices from further afield and fresh herbs on a constant quest to exalt the flavour. His langoustines ravioles and shellfish stock is out of this world!;Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2849;Le Charlemagne;France;Pernand-Vergelesses;1 route des Vergelesses, Pernand-Vergelesses, 21420, France;47.0772707;4.8497698;75;false;false;Creative;This vineyard devoted to Corton-Charlemagne is home to a fine dining establishment, whose peaceful, contemporary interior provides the perfect foil to sample dishes that waver between France and Japan and are dotted with surprising and inspired combinations. Out-of-the-ordinary, highly personal creations, based on the produce of the restaurant’s garden (and hives) and from local, stringently selected suppliers. All of which is flanked by an appropriately awesome wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2850;Le Pavillon des Boulevards;France;Bordeaux;120 rue de la Croix-de-Seguey, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8532133;-0.5926893;88;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A landmark of Bordeaux’ culinary scene for several decades now, this stone town house is emblematic of 18C Bordeaux. At the helm, chef Thomas Morel, whose wife Célia supervises the front of house, gives free rein to his creativity. Underpinned by a solid classical background, the food is dotted with contemporary notes, such as immaculately cooked pollock flanked by an astounding horseradish-flavoured hollandaise sauce. The lunchtime menu is particularly attractive.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2851;Le Art;France;Aix-en-Provence;Château de la Gaude, 3959 route des Pinchinats, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.568911;5.478535;24;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the kitchen of this magnificent 18C bastide, chef Matthieu Dupuis-Baumal serves boldly inventive dishes, in which Provençal notes meet subtle Japanese influences. The flavours are clear and always controlled, and each recipe brandishes a confident culinary personality. The setting is magical, complete with a magnificent terrace, and makes for a sumptuous backdrop for this firework display of flavours. The wonderful wine list includes a selection from the château.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2852;La Nouvelle Auberge;France;Wihr-au-Val;9 route Nationale, Wihr-au-Val, 68230, France;48.0462924;7.2085659;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine;On the doorstep of Munster valley, this “new inn” is a fully refurbished former posthouse. On the ground-floor, an Alsace bistro regales diners on weekday lunchtimes. Upstairs, the gourmet restaurant sports a suitably rustic, half-timbered dining room. Bernard Leray, who hails from Rennes in Brittany, has taken to Alsace like a stork to its nest. After honing his skills at Bernard Loiseau, Leray puts a delicate new spin on local produce. All his dishes demonstrate his painstaking work and consummate technique, as in this fillet of pike-perch with red cabbage and squash “fleischnaka”, red-wine reduction.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2853;Auberge Saint-Walfrid;France;Sarreguemines;58 rue de Grosbliederstroff, Sarreguemines, 57200, France;49.114563;7.044991;36;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Situated on the road from Metz to Strasbourg, this pretty little inn – once a farm belonging to the church in Welferding – has been run by the same family since the late 19C. Having taken over from his father who built up the auberge’s gastronomic reputation in the region, Stephan Schneider (fifth generation) is now at the helm here. Guests dine in a large, plush and warmly decorated dining room with old parquet flooring and cabinets laden with gleaming Sarreguemines earthenware. The chef is a staunch champion of tradition who works with local market gardeners (he also has his own kitchen garden) and buys whole animals that he prepares himself, including cured meats. Spacious guestrooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2855;La Maison de Pierre;France;Hasparren;Hôtel Berria, 68 rue Francis-Jammes, Hasparren, 64240, France;43.38693;-1.30407;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Here in the centre of the village, this duo, whose enthusiasm is infectious, have set up shop in a half-timbered building that sports the Basque Country's characteristic red and white. It was once a Basque pelota ground (the reception still has the old ticket windows and a glass door opening onto the trinquet). Chef Nicolas Montceau and his pastry chef partner Julien Bonnal, who is also in charge of plating up the dishes, swear by local produce. Their multi-course surprise tasting menu in several sequences is a delight, rife with harmonious combinations of flavours, delicious jus and sauces, and an abundance of creativity. Don't hesitate to ask for a table facing the open kitchen so you can enjoy the show! Comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
2856;L'Évidence;France;Montbazon;1 place des Marronniers, Montbazon, 37250, France;47.2873108;0.7133543;82;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Leaving the city of Tours to set up shop in this old property on a small square in the countryside was an easy step to take for Gaëtan Evrard, who feels close ties to the terroir of his Touraine homeland. Vegetables and meat from the region, fish sourced in Brittany – the ingredients are the star of the show, elevated by the market-fresh cooking of a chef who is not afraid to push the boundaries, a case in point being his white asparagus from Richelieu roasted on the barbecue, elderflower and black lemon, or fillet of red mullet cooked skin on, velvet crab jus with squid ink. Choose from the excellent list of wines from the Loire, which provide the perfect foil to the chef's creative cooking.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2857;Les Explorateurs - Hôtel Pashmina;France;Val-Thorens;141 rue des Dalles, Val-Thorens, 73440, France;45.2957656;6.5862441;36;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a magnificent hotel set 2 345m above sea level, this high-flying restaurant is well worth the climb. The eye-catching interior decor sets the tone for exploring the chef's inspired creations based on meticulously sourced high-quality ingredients: scallops with mushrooms from La Motte-Servolex, Arctic char confit with Roussanne butter, AOC Bresse chicken served two ways. Right through to the desserts, the dishes are a resounding manifestation of consummate technical skill and a determination not to be just another luxury hotel restaurant.;;[]
2858;Michel Trama;France;Puymirol;52 rue Royale, Puymirol, 47270, France;44.1870457;0.7973007;48;true;false;Creative;Michel Trama and Puymirol have a long history. This former champion diver and student of the decorative arts in Montparnasse owes his true calling to love… for his wife Maryse. She is the one who introduced him to fine dining. After a string of odd jobs, he settled down and opened a bistro on rue Mouffetard in Paris, with a copy of Michel Guérard's "Cuisine Gourmande" to refer to. In 1979 he set up shop in this splendid 13C country house in Puymirol, in Lot-et-Garonne: you can sit under the medieval vaults or on the lovely terrace, in the old cloister... It is time to indulge in a cuisine that incorporates both tradition and invention in an unchanging menu that makes several references to this establishment's heyday.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2859;La Magdeleine - Mathias Dandine;France;Gémenos;2 rond-point des Charrons, Gémenos, 13420, France;43.2989399;5.6248585;80;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Mathias Dandine made his childhood dream come true when he became chef at this handsome 18C mansion with a terrace shaded by mature plane trees, situated far from the noise of the city. Here, his cuisine is in perfect harmony with the setting, where he celebrates Provence with breathtaking skill. His unfussy, pared-down Mediterranean cuisine shuns unnecessary frills, with no particular effort made to impress foodies. Yet behind the apparent simplicity, the chef’s recipes demonstrate real mastery in cooking methods, textures and balance of flavours. In fine weather, make sure you take a seat on the terrace shaded by Mediterranean trees.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
2860;Villa Salone;France;Salon-de-Provence;6 rue du Maréchal-Joffre, Salon-de-Provence, 13300, France;43.64144;5.0986;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Alexandre Lechêne has taken over this pretty mansion in the heart of Salon-de-Provence. Here he treats diners to truly remarkable creative cuisine served in the form of surprise set menus: the ethos here is "go with the flow"! The beautifully plated dishes showcase market garden produce and local fruit. For instance: printed pasta, a medley of courgettes, flowers, fresh almonds and marigold. Fresh, tasty and perfectly seasoned, it is a real delight for the taste buds! The combinations of ingredients are sometimes daring, but always on point and executed skilfully in the service of a well-balanced whole. The decor is elegant, with mouldings, frescoes on the ceiling and pretty Provençal tiles, not forgetting the pretty little patio terrace, which is very popular in summer. Attentive, efficient service.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2861;Aida;France;Paris;1 rue Pierre-Leroux, Paris, 75007, France;48.850275;2.3186554;85;false;true;Japanese;The whitewashed facade of this small bolthole tucked away in a lane blends in so perfectly with its surroundings that you may even miss it entirely! Behind its spruce façade lies a jealously kept secret, namely exquisite Japanese cuisine. The pristine white interior is both elegant and minimalist, in line with the visual charter commonly associated with restaurants in Japan. Take a seat either at the counter (nine seats only) for a close-up view of the teppanyaki griddles or in the small soberly appointed private dining room with its tatami. As you sample a single tasting menu, you will discover subtle, precise cuisine that carefully crafts culinary ties between Japan and France. The seasonings, cooking, carving, cutting, slicing and chopping are all at the service of the main ingredient, which is presented as simply and as artfully as possible. Sashimi, Brittany lobster, chateaubriand steak or sweetbread, cooked on the teppanyaki griddle, and served with fine Burgundy wines, painstakingly selected by the chef. Dutiful, professional service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2862;Thierry Schwartz - Le Restaurant;France;Obernai;35 rue de Sélestat, Obernai, 67210, France;48.4604843;7.4837134;61;true;false;Creative;Thierry Schwartz, who describes himself as an Alsace native by birth and at heart, believes that nature's rightful place is at the centre when it comes to cooking. This ethos is borne out by his commitment to local producers and by his title of Officer of France's Order of Agricultural Merit. To set the scene: think lots of wood, seasonal vegetables on display and a log-burning fire. Thierry concocts three remarkable set menus in which the produce (from Alsace and permaculture) is sufficient in and of itself: pure spelt, arctic char, wild sorrel, organic farm eggs... to be washed down with a fine, natural wine. The choice is yours – from the 1,500-strong list!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2865;Maison Caillet;France;Valmont;22 rue André-Fiquet, Valmont, 76540, France;49.7446677;0.4919745;23;true;true;Creative;Chef Pierre Caillet, awarded the title of "Meilleur Ouvrier de France" in 2011, not only boasts faultless culinary technique, but also wins us over with his feeling for the ingredients and contagious energy. Original creations (his exuberant scallops in a passion fruit crust are a perfect example), interplay of textures and flavours, fine produce from the Normandy terroir… and let's not forget the judicious use of herbs and vegetables from the extensive kitchen garden: a winning formula. Last but not least, this 19C inn also has inviting, cosy guestrooms with private terraces overlooking the lake.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2866;L'Éveil des Sens;France;Mayenne;429 boulevard Paul-Lintier, Mayenne, 53100, France;48.3060431;-0.6084258;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Here on the outskirts of town, it would be a shame not to stop and admire this original metal fretwork façade. Once inside, wood prevails in the tasteful, understated interior. This is the stomping ground of chef Nicolas Nobis and Isabelle Nobis (husband and wife), who honed their skills under Bernard Loiseau and Georges Blanc. Simplicity and nature are the hallmarks of the chef's cooking, and he loves to work with plants (eg hyssop, verbena etc) and vegetables sourced from local producers. When it comes to cooking and seasoning, precision is the order of the day, as characterised by the Breton lobster, strawberry, snow peas and a light bisque. An experience that gently (re)awakens the taste buds... with a set lunch menu that represents unbeatable value for money!;Air conditioning;[]
2867;Les Hauts de Loire;France;Onzain;79 rue Gilbert-Navard, Onzain, 41150, France;47.5088905;1.1432985;65;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Established in a 19C hunting lodge between Amboise and Blois, the magnificent setting sports a classically appointed dining room and gloriously peaceful alfresco patio. The chef sources premium ingredients, such as Touraine truffles, Sologne caviar, Loire fish, which he carefully crafts into delicious dishes. In season, you will also taste local game and fruit and vegetables from the establishment’s cottage garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
2868;L'Aspérule;France;Dijon;43 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3248221;5.044981;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Keigo Kimura incorporates a Japanese twist into French cuisine in this tastefully appointed Dijon restaurant. He surgically crafts set menus and even a mystery menu in the evening. Like all genuine Japanese chefs, his flair for precision and balance (plating, cooking and flavour) is second to none, and his dishes are also sprinkled with tributes to the region, such as pinot noir or vin jaune sauces and mustard shoots. The memory of his ginger-flavoured gyoza of game in a red wine sauce and his shoulder of lamb, first slow-roasted then grilled on a binchotan griddle and served with a Japanese pancake, linger with us still! Last but not least, the wine cellar is an Aladdin’s Cave for connoisseurs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2870;La Promenade;France;Le Petit-Pressigny;11 rue du Savoureulx, Le Petit-Pressigny, 37350, France;46.920786;0.9188379;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;It may take a little getting to, but this family-run restaurant set in the countryside is a real treat! Fabrice and Clément Dallais, representing the third and fourth generations, create dishes with a modern outlook. Theirs is tasty, festive fare that is deeply rooted in the local land – for example, Racan chicken and pigeon, Géline de Touraine (heirloom poultry), offal and game, organic vegetables from market gardeners, and pike. Tuck into their surprise set menus in an immaculate contemporary setting. Remarkable wine list and judicious recommendations from the sommelier.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2871;Le Faham by Kelly Rangama;France;Paris;108 rue Cardinet, Paris, 75017, France;48.8857122;2.3117036;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The faham is an orchid native to the island of Réunion, famous for its subtle almond scent. Kelly Rangama (a Top Chef 2017 contestant) chose this flower to symbolise her civil and culinary union with pastry chef Jérôme Devreese and their joint creation: this sleek, elegant restaurant tucked away in the Batignolles district. Here the chef proposes a cuisine that abounds in vibrancy and delicacy, spicy but always subtle, with a touch of exoticism that makes all the difference. An example: her toothfish (fished in La Réunion) with sweet-sour carrots and ginger and a concentrate of tomatoes and crunchy rice. A genuine delight.;Air conditioning;[]
2872;La Table de l'Alpaga;France;Megève;Alpaga, 66 allée des Marmoussets, route du Prariand, Megève, 74120, France;45.8524843;6.600987;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;How delightful it is to settle in at your table in this stylish but snug space, in which untreated and premium materials such as marble and oak have been used to create an authentic and timeless decor. At the fine dining restaurant, young chef Alexandre Baule (originally from Isère) brings vegetables to the fore in his bid to elevate Savoie produce. Also of note are the food and cocktail pairings (including alcohol-free options) devised by a talented barman. The bistro, open every day for dinner, serves up a fine regional repertoire. Comfortable guestrooms fitted out in chalets await, should you wish to extend the experience.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2874;Burgundy by Matthieu;France;Lyon;24 quai Saint-Antoine, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7628677;4.8321372;80;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this old building done out in a contemporary decor on the banks of the River Saône, Matthieu Girardon serves up his personal, uninhibited and technically accomplished take on modern cuisine. His jus and sauces elevate many of the dishes, including a pearlescent Arctic char with a fumet emulsion and a beurre blanc with fish roe. The seasons and market availability dictate the contents of his blind tasting menu, which can be adjusted to suit your budget and appetite. Wine pairings – Burgundy takes pride of place, of course – come from the restaurant's exemplary cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2875;Pavyllon;France;Paris;8 avenue Dutuit, Paris, 75008, France;48.8659971;2.3162586;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Under the aegis of Yannick Alléno, the third Pavillon Ledoyen venture is a chic restaurant with, notably, a counter to seat 32. The cuisine is built on fine classic foundations, bolstered by international flavours and details. Pitch perfect, the food is refined and delicate – to be savoured in the smart yet relaxed ambience: an excellent time is sure to be had. Gorgeous terrace surrounded by greenery.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2876;Holen;France;Rennes;2 rue des Carmes, Rennes, 35000, France;48.1083789;-1.676248;52;true;false;Creative;“Seasonality on the plate” is the mantra of this talented chef, who has worked at the prestigious Auberge de l’Ill, as well as with renowned names such as Michel Bras and Emile Jung. His Breton-inspired recipes demonstrate his dedication to top-quality ingredients, including vegetables grown by small local producers using permaculture principles, and fish sourced from small boats that avoid intensive fishing (as a result of which he has been awarded a “Green Food” label). Holen also has his own kitchen garden and makes his own compost. The final result is ethical cuisine that is full of flavour and elegantly presented in the form of surprise menus, all served in a bistro refurbished with natural materials. Delightful!;Wheelchair access;[]
2878;Reflet d'Obione;France;Montpellier;29 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6122303;3.8730671;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Trained in star Swiss, French (and even Australian) establishments, chef Laurent Cherchi is a stalwart champion of the environment. He offers two menus, one of which is lacto-ovo-vegetarian, while the other is all-out vegan (without animal ingredients) – which is nothing if not rare in the universe of French star-rated establishments. All his produce is rigorously sourced locally, from the Cévennes to the Mediterranean (beef from Aubrac, saltbush lamb from Camargue, tomme cheese from Larzac) and the front-of-house team is more than well-versed in the ins and outs of each ingredient’s provenance. Each dish has been endlessly pondered, puzzled over and tweaked, to allow the chef’s impeccable technique (fermentation, extraction) and knife-edged accuracy to showcase the stars of the show: the veggies. Three dining rooms, which sport a stripped back vibe, and the tableware are all made to measure by local artisans.;;[]
2879;Mont Blanc Restaurant & Goûter;France;Hauteluce;16 rue de la Voûte, Hauteluce, 73620, France;45.7498163;6.5843326;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This tastefully refurbished century-old inn at the edge of the village overlooks the Beaufortain mountains. It is the domain of an enthusiastic young chef who previously worked in pastry at a Michelin-starred establishment. Benoît Goulard proposes surprise set menus drawing on the best produce in the region – always seasonal and eco-sourced. His aim is not to tell some sort of story with each dish, but simply to conjure up refined and contemporary-style cuisine that looks and tastes great, showcasing his keen eye for detail and total self-reliance (he works alone). This also goes for the desserts, which are well worth a try! The same approach prevails in the dining area, with its beautifully dressed tables and irreproachable welcome and service courtesy of hostess Hélène Fleury. There is much to admire in their dedication to delivering an exceptional experience in this remote location.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2881;Faventia;France;Tourrettes;3100 route de Bagnols-en-Forêt, Tourrettes, 83440, France;43.590664;6.7319345;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The luxurious Terre Blanche estate, which welcomes you into a privileged setting that feels shielded from the outside world, boasts a terrace overlooking the countryside at sunset that is simply enchanting! Fine Mediterranean-inspired cuisine that showcases superb local produce. Choose from set menus in several courses (one of which is vegetarian).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2882;La Maison dans le Parc;France;Nancy;3 rue Sainte-Catherine, Nancy, 54000, France;48.6941608;6.1849668;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Established in a handsome mansion, abutting the opera house and just behind one of France’s most beautiful squares, chef Charles Coulombeau and his wife Roxane (front of house) are a firm fixture of the culinary scene of Nancy. Having worked at Les Prés d’Eugénie, Lameloise and Gravetye Manor in Sussex, Charles deftly crafts modern cuisine, enhanced by creative flourishes and a nod to Japan (where he worked for a few months). Citrus fruits (such as Buddha’s hand and calamondin orange) and Asian flavours are perfectly paired with premium ingredients such as ikejime Vosges Arctic Char or plump Bresse chicken. Heroically wondrous (without forgetting the knockout terrace overlooking the park…).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2883;Äponem - Auberge du Presbytère;France;Vailhan;4 rue de  l'Église, Vailhan, 34320, France;43.5545013;3.2986749;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The name of this restaurant housed in a 17C presbytery means "happiness" in the Pataxó language and, indeed, a real sense of delight is cultivated in the form of ingredients from the market and the kitchen garden (seven permaculture vegetable plots!). Enjoy your meal in a stunning location overlooking the countryside, or on the charming terrace in the shade of the wisteria.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2884;Leclère;France;Montpellier;8 rue André-Michel, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6067486;3.8739319;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This astonishing restaurant is completely unremarkable from the street... what a surprise, then, beyond the stainless steel-clad tunnel, to enter this attractive room with a sleek decor that blends metal, Montpellier stone, tiles and granite. Chef Guillaume Leclère is committed to what he dubs his "cuisine d'arrivage": he serves a single set menu that changes regularly in line with the ultra-fresh ingredients available (Mediterranean fish, veal from the Pyrenees etc), all sourced via short supply chains. Only the list of ingredients is revealed to diners. The chef's precise, pared-back creations have plenty of personality and panache, cases in point being his dish with asparagus, horseradish and mint, or the meagre and rosemary.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2886;Le 7ème Continent;France;Rixheim;35 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Rixheim, 68170, France;47.7480409;7.4029807;16;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant's incredible decoration (inside and out) was created by painter and decorative artist François Zenner, an amateur naturalist with a passion for plants. Also passionate about his work, and very much influenced by his years with Bernard Loiseau, chef Laurent Haller is never at a loss for ideas when it comes to sharing his love of good food. He likes to revisit the great classics of French cuisine and creates surf and turf combinations. His menu, a veritable ode to the market and its often local produce (lamb from Rixheim, split peas from Petit-landau…), changes every month.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2889;Au Crocodile;France;Strasbourg;10 rue de l'Outre, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.58372;7.747566;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The stuffed crocodile in the window, a souvenir brought back from Egypt by a Napoleonic soldier, underlines the historic character of this iconic Strasbourg establishment, which boasted 3 stars under chef Émile Jung. Following a top to toe refurbishment that has preserved the spirit of the venue, it shines brightly on the culinary scene of Strasbourg. Chef Romain Brillat, former second of Gilles Goujon and a distant relative of Brillat-Savarin, the famous French gourmet, has achieved a balance between classicism and sophistication. Examples include his original take on scallops (ravioli and cream of the trimmings) with squash, or Dover sole with buddha’s hand, root vegetables and shellfish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2890;1741;France;Strasbourg;22 quai des Bateliers, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5805005;7.7535355;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Opposite Palais Rohan, an architectural masterpiece completed in 1741, this ‘1741’ is the quintessence of stylish, depicted by cosy, pleasantly hushed dining rooms and a counter where you can watch the kitchen team and chef Jérémy Page at work. After training with Robuchon, Page signs delicate, precise recipes, strewn with passing nods to Alsace. His inspiration comes to the forefront in sauces and jus, such as a seaweed cream paired with a lightly seared fillet of John Dory, or a Grand Veneur game sauce that flanks a medallion of wild boar. A festival of flavours that is beautifully paired with a splendid selection of Alsace wines (grands crus, organic, etc).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2892;L'Aparté;France;Montrabé;21 rue de l'Europe, Montrabé, 31850, France;43.6449305;1.5107135;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This traditional Toulouse building surrounded by greenery is so pretty that you forget its location in a business park close to a busy road. Its terrace, covered by a bioclimatic pergola, is another asset that proves very popular in the summer months. Originally from Normandy, the chef has been based in France's so-called pink city for over 15 years. He is renowned for his various theme-based set menus, eg black truffles in winter – his vegetable casserole with truffles has reached iconic status. He skilfully juxtaposes contrasting flavours and textures to create generous dishes: turbot fillet stuffed with coral mousseline and coriander, medley of carrots, or roast pigeon supreme with confit leg, melting beetroot and chard gyoza.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2893;Épisodes;France;Paris;8 rue Meissonier, Paris, 75017, France;48.8835815;2.3044589;93;false;true;Creative;As you take a seat in this smart restaurant decked in marble, wood and stone and located in the well-heeled Monceau neighbourhood, you will sample a tasting menu of unabashed modernity that stars outstanding produce and consummate craftsmanship. Suave, delicate dishes like lamb cooked two ways (saddle rare and shredded with mustard seed) and a medley of carrots. Fogo symbolises fire, setting the scene in this urban chic eatery.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2894;Le Cap;France;Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat;Grand Hôtel du Cap-Ferrat, 71 boulevard du Général-de-Gaulle, Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat, 06230, France;43.6770545;7.3314132;32;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Make a beeline for the iconic early-20C Grand-Hôtel du Cap Ferrat. The swish hotel, a favourite with international VIPs, stands at the tip of an exclusive peninsula overlooking the Mediterranean and hidden from view by lush gardens. You have a choice between a stunning dining room or an exquisite terrace shaded by tall Aleppo pines. At the helm of the kitchen, chef Yoric Tièche (born in Aix-en-Provence) finds his inspiration in Provence’s culinary roots, creating superb dishes out of Mediterranean produce. Highlights include red mullet lacquered in sweet harissa, served with a crunchy socca of chickpeas and a floral bouquet of aromatic herbs. The knockout desserts by pastry chef, Pierre-Jean Quinonero, are equally worth writing home about, illustrated by his mandarin and lemon tartlet, to name but one of his fiendishly appetising creations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2895;Sola;France;Paris;12 rue de l'Hôtel-Colbert, Paris, 75005, France;48.8515799;2.3483585;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Japanese;Just a stone's throw from the Seine overlooking Notre Dame, you are definitely in Paris – yet also in Japan! Sola is full of contrasts from the pared-back pale wooden furniture to the coffered ceiling and massive solid wood doors, while the vaulted cellar sports a Japanese-inspired dining platform (be sure to remove your shoes). Japanese chef Kosuke Nabeta serves a delicious fusion of the knife-edge precision we associate with his native cuisine paired with a cornucopia of produce from the French countryside. Nabeta introduces us to traditional culinary techniques that he wields exquisitely (smoking, drying, marinating, fermenting, alternative cooking methods etc) based on ingredients like soya, sake, ponzu and mizuna. Balanced, polished, personal cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
2896;Auberge au Bœuf;France;Sessenheim;1 rue de l'Église, Sessenheim, 67770, France;48.7991675;7.9857074;93;false;true;Modern Cuisine;You can’t help but fall in love with this snug Alsace inn with its church pews, wainscoted walls, regional furniture and small museum dedicated to Goethe… The village was the scene of a love affair between the famous writer and the daughter of a local pastor. The seasonal culinary repertory wavers between modernity and tradition. There is also a Stammtisch, a regional “table d’hôtes”, and 4 luxury guestroom-suites.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2897;Louis;France;Paris;23 rue de la Victoire, Paris, 75009, France;48.8750718;2.3388394;35;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in a quiet street, this compact restaurant has an intimate feel. Breton chef Stéphane Pitré simultaneously pays homage to his father, grandfather and great-grandfather, all named Louis. He devises set menus with several courses comprising small portions (or three courses for a quick lunch). Aligned with market availability and seasonality, this cuisine is packed with Asian influences. For a bistro experience, head for Le Cellier, which serves simple, straightforward cuisine just two houses down the street.;Wheelchair access;[]
2898;Quinsou;France;Paris;33 rue de l'Abbé-Grégoire, Paris, 75006, France;48.8476485;2.325489;78;true;true;Creative;Located opposite Ferrandi, the legendary culinary school, Quinsou ("chaffinch" in Occitan) is well placed to influence the great chefs of tomorrow. In a stark, modern interior (cement tiles, bare light bulbs), chef Antonin Bonnet offers a refined, delicate, sensitive and unpretentious take on artisanal cuisine. The ingredient-led dishes put the focus squarely on premium-quality produce: Axuria veal, hand-dived scallops from Erquy, matured trout from Asturias… They serve a single set menu at this fine restaurant headed by a passionate chef.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2899;Pertinence;France;Paris;29 rue de l'Exposition, Paris, 75007, France;48.8571707;2.3033772;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Ryunosuke Naito and Kwen Liew met at Restaurant Antoine in 2011. Ryunosuke is Japanese and has worked in some of the top houses of Paris (Taillevent, Meurice) and Kwen is Malaysian. Together they have created this elegant minimalist setting, depicted by light wood and Knoll chairs, whose understated, cosy vibe is perfectly in keeping with their characters and ethos. In the kitchen, they craft market-fresh dishes overflowing in powerful flavours, brushing the cobwebs off French culinary tradition along the way. Spot-on cooking as the name suggests…;;[]
2900;Auguste;France;Paris;54 rue de Bourgogne, Paris, 75007, France;48.8561689;2.317003;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In Gaël Orieux's compact restaurant – seating barely 30 people – the elegant contemporary interior with deceptively sleek lines exudes an unexpected calm. It's a chic and "classy" space where you can enjoy judiciously modern cuisine, for instance saddle of veal with a rainbow of sweet and sour carrots or turbot flavoured with wild herbs and artichokes in a pepper sauce... The appeal of the menu lies in its variety and the quality of its produce. Gaël Orieux sources his ingredients from the market and has chosen to serve only species of fish that are not endangered (black mullet, meagre, pout). The wine selection offers the opportunity to try something new without breaking the bank.;Air conditioning;[]
2901;Frenchie;France;Paris;5 rue du Nil, Paris, 75002, France;48.867722;2.3478539;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Grégory Marchand learned the trade in some of the English-speaking world's top restaurants (Gramercy Tavern in New York, Jamie Oliver's Fifteen in London, Mandarin Oriental in Hong Kong). In his compact restaurant in the heart of the Sentier area, the space (with exposed brick, beams and stonework) quickly fills to capacity, thanks to cuisine that is perfectly in tune with today's international inclinations, rooted in meticulous sourcing (from the ceramic plates to the fruit and vegetables from Terroirs d'Avenir opposite). The marriages of flavours are original and ingredient led, and the Anglo-American twist is particularly noticeable when it comes to the desserts. Two services (6.30pm/7pm and 9.30pm).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2902;Benoit;France;Paris;20 rue Saint-Martin, Paris, 75004, France;48.8584427;2.3500715;89;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This genuine Parisian bistro still boasts its period Belle Époque interior (woodwork, copper pots, mirrors, velvet banquettes) and everything down to the plates bears the B monogram, further adding to the authentic vibe. Proudly and heartily traditional, the recipes star country produce: pâté en croûte, calf’s head with ravigote sauce, cassoulet, millefeuille pastry!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2904;Yam'Tcha;France;Paris;121 rue Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75001, France;48.8615065;2.341813;81;false;true;Creative;Adeline Grattard was given – and has cultivated – a rare gift: a feel for her ingredients. In her restaurant on rue Saint-Honoré, the chef chooses two or three ingredients, on which she focuses all her attention. There is no technical showmanship or ostentation, just subtle, rarely seen combinations that seem completely natural. Trained alongside Pascal Barbot (L'Astrance) and after working in Hong Kong for a few years, she combines products of extraordinary quality, mainly from France and Asia: XO sauce, vinegared black rice or shellfish jus come to mind. The food is accompanied by a rare selection of Asian teas, another source of highly convincing pairings (yam'tcha, in Chinese, means "to drink tea"). There's no menu of any kind: just the element of surprise and inspiration that comes with each dish made from the day's market-sourced ingredients.;;[]
2906;L'Anthocyane;France;Lannion;25 avenue Ernest-Renan, Lannion, 22300, France;48.7329096;-3.459947;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine;For chef Marc Briand, the experience is what matters before all else. Installed in the centre of Lannion, he rustles up modern Gallic fare, dotted with Japanese overtones, in tribute to his avowed passion for the Land of the Rising Sun. as a result, some of his high-precision recipes, based on super-fresh Brittany produce (langoustine, lobster, John Dory), are sprinkled with Japanese ingredients such as yuzu, shiitake, miso, etc. Lashings of imagination, art-directed plating, stylish elegance and high-flying technique complete this culinary score. Let’s not forget the warm, colourful interior.;Wheelchair access;[]
2907;En Pleine Nature;France;Quint-Fonsegrives;6 place de la Mairie, Quint-Fonsegrives, 31130, France;43.585293;1.5294347;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Chef Sylvain Joffre promises and delivers fresh, subtle, 100% natural food. This authentic cook-gardener-gatherer makes the most of the herbs and vegetables from his own garden and from painstakingly sourced local producers. Sylvain is conscientious, serious and the antithesis of showy. He aims to serve first-rate food at prices that make sense, crafting each ingredient sincerely and truthfully, adding the occasional flourish by way of jus, coulis, plants and flowers… The tasteful interior is low-key with the bonus of alfresco dining shaded by parasols. Highly committed to the environment, the chef has opened a shop next door that sells pastries, brioche and bread made with organic flour.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2909;Auberge Saint-Laurent;France;Sierentz;1 rue de la Fontaine, Sierentz, 68510, France;47.6540637;7.4539991;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This elegant and authentic 18C coaching inn with a long, flower-filled and welcoming façade is a local family-owned institution, appreciated as much by its regulars as it is by the many tourists on their way across Europe. They all sing the praises of the service and keen sense of hospitality, the snug and appealing guestrooms, and, of course, the excellent cuisine served here. Chef Laurent Arbeit presides over the kitchen, having learned his craft under Haeberlin and Ducasse. A proprietor who is very much in tune with the times, his delicate and harmonious cuisine is replete with well-balanced flavours. A resounding success.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2911;114, Faubourg;France;Paris;Le Bristol, 114 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75008, France;48.8718054;2.3143326;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated within Le Bristol, this brasserie is truly one of a kind! The interior will win you over at first glance: interspersed with imposing gilded columns, it has large luminescent dahlia motifs on its orange walls. At its heart, a grand staircase opens up, leading down to the lower level where tables rub shoulders with the open kitchens. Chic, shimmering, both bustling and intimate, this place hits all the right notes. As for the food, this is a discreetly original take on the French classics we know and love. Dishes are carefully presented and flavours are beautifully combined. This is a lesson in how things should be done.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2912;L'Écrin;France;Paris;Hôtel de Crillon, 10 place de la Concorde, Paris, 75008, France;48.8673;2.32114;69;true;false;Creative;“A quest for the perfect blend” could be the motto of the luxurious Écrin located in the Hôtel de Crillon. Sommelier Xavier Thuizat and chef Boris Campanella have reversed their roles, overturning the traditional order of precedence in an unheard of, exciting approach: here the choice of wine determines that of the food! Each diner thus enjoys a personalised experience depending on the wines and number of courses selected. The range of combinations is staggering when you think of the 2,500-strong wine bin. This approach also demonstrates the unorthodoxy, technical agility and perfect harmony between the teams. The chef conjures up elegant dishes, overflowing in character which seek to mirror the wine’s bouquet as much as possible. A unique sensory experience in the finest traditions of French art de vivre.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2914;La Ribaudière;France;Bourg-Charente;2 place du Port, Bourg-Charente, 16200, France;45.6735606;-0.2248163;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This large villa has a garden that slopes down to the gently flowing Charente below, with the proud silhouette of Bourg-Charente castle, overlooking the vines, visible on the other side of the river. In the dining room with its slate-grey walls and large picture windows offering views of the charming terrace and the banks of the river, chefs Thierry and Julien Verrat (father and son) create fine cuisine where invention goes hand in hand with La Ribaudière’s natural surroundings. The owner of a vineyard and a truffle field, Verrat is passionate about the Charentais region, which is a real land of plenty. Here, he creates dishes that bring out the best of his excellent ingredients with delicacy and conviction, using the full panoply of local produce, ranging from Cognac and Pineau des Charentes to wild snails and fish from the nearby Atlantic.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2915;La Table de Chaintré;France;Chaintré;72 place du Luminaire, Chaintré, 71570, France;46.2604625;4.760257;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This quintessential country house, tucked away in a picturesque village in the heart of the Pouilly-Fuissé vineyards, is the brainchild of a friendly, industrious young couple. He scours the local markets for fine (organic whenever possible) produce, which he unveils in cleverly crafted dishes. For example, green asparagus with Brittany sardines, Normandy lobster with foaming butter, or a slice of farm-reared veal with multicoloured radishes and violet broccoli… The food is naturally enough washed down with a fine selection of Burgundy and Beaujolais tipples. The set menu changes weekly – all the more reason to return regularly!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2916;La Table de Xavier Mathieu;France;Joucas;Le Phébus, 508 route de Murs, Joucas, 84220, France;43.9289042;5.2559385;63;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Raised in Marseille, Xavier Mathieu is a true-blue Provençal lad. He was introduced to the world of haute cuisine by master chef, Roger Vergé, a family friend. He went on to complete his apprenticeship with Joël Robuchon in Paris, before returning to the splendid family home nestling in the Luberon scrubland. The chef, who sports a distinctive shock of white hair, breathes new life into Provençal culinary traditions, giving each dish a new twist on its original form. Tian of black olives from the garden, leg of lamb from the Alpilles cooked in warm sand of the garrigue, two-course pieds et paquets (Marseille-style mutton feet and tripe). Surprising recipes, always with a personal touch, to be sampled in the swish exclusive setting of a luxurious drystone bastide whose foundations date back to the Knights of the Order of Malta.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2917;L'Atelier du Peintre;France;Colmar;1 rue Schongauer, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0765208;7.3580855;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Martin Schongauer, one of the greatest late-15C engravers and painters from the Rhine, had his workshop just across from this establishment, whose walls date back to the Renaissance. The interior however is decidedly 21C and sports a deliberately cosy, modern vibe. Loïc Lefebvre's vibrant personality shines throughout the culinary score. This native of Lorraine, who learned the ropes in Michelin-starred establishments, signs creative, colourful seasonal cuisine. Freshness and subtlety, precision and finesse are the hallmarks of his grilled Arctic char, kohlrabi spaghetti with a cream of tarama and a sabayon of elderberry vinegar or a slab of seabass decorated with slices of scallops arranged like fish scales…;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2918;Le Carré d'Alethius;France;Charmes-sur-Rhône;4 rue Paul-Bertois, Charmes-sur-Rhône, 07800, France;44.8614644;4.8331975;98;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Between the départements of Drôme and Ardèche, this restaurant named after Roman senator Alethius has a distinctly Provençal air about it. The villa is arranged around a square courtyard, a gorgeous verdant patio where you can dine in fine weather. After working for Jean-Michel Lorain at La Côte Saint-Jacques, Olivier Samin occupied the post of sous-chef for Anne-Sophie Pic for a long time. He delivers fresh cuisine that reflects the seasons and market availability (eg regional fruit and vegetables, escargots from Helix Eyrieux, local cheeses), and he also has a tremendous sense of balance: precise cooking and meticulously plated creations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2919;Apicius;France;Clermont-Ferrand;Place du Marché-Saint-Pierre (à l'étage), Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7793794;3.0827699;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Bang in the city centre, on the first floor of Saint Pierre Market, this swanky restaurant enjoys a lofty location. The stylish venue sports a series of beautifully appointed contemporary dining rooms and exquisite tableware. Chef Arkadiusz Zuchmanski, of Polish extraction, decided to move to France to fortify a vocation that took root in the kitchen of his forebears. He confesses an unbridled passion for noble ingredients and for Auvergne, which reminds him of the landscapes of his home city, Drzewica. The focus is on visually striking plating and honest, simply crafted ingredients, such as foie gras with hand-picked wild pepper or sautéed sweetbread with truffle parsnip.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2920;Chez Michèle;France;Languimberg;57 rue Principale, Languimberg, 57810, France;48.7457994;6.858981;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Once a village café, then a family inn, it is now a gourmet table with an enviable reputation in the Moselle “lake district”. This illustrious restaurant is in the capable hands of Bruno Poiré, Michèle’s son, who after learning the ropes in the family business as a teenager, honed his skills with Georges Blanc at Vonnas and Antoine Westermann at the Buerehiesel. He prepares precise, generous dishes in tune with the zeitgeist that reveal a soft spot for Mediterranean recipes. A fine dining experience in a contemporary setting, enhanced by attentive service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2921;Le Vivier;France;L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue;800 cours Fernande-Peyre, L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue, 84800, France;43.9257707;5.0633622;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this restaurant located in a town that is a mecca for antiques dealers, diners are in good hands! Talented chef Romain Gandolphe brings delicacy and subtlety to his carefully crafted dishes, with a focus on both flavours and textures. Sit in the contemporary dining space with an inviting decor, or on the terrace overlooking the River Sorgue and its lush green banks – a real feast for the eyes. Attentive service and an interesting selection of regional wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2922;Auberge de la Forge;France;Lavalette;8 rue Jean-Parisot, Lavalette, 31590, France;43.6376833;1.5951738;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this typical red-brick building, a fireplace and terracotta floor tiles blend with elegant contemporary furnishings. A talented couple (a chef and a pastry chef with a passion for wine) forged successful careers for themselves (Ritz, Meurice, Gabriel, Christophe Bacquié) before opening their own restaurant. This is very personal cooking that brings a smile to your face – fresh and spontaneous, full of flavour, brimming with ideas, juxtaposing subtle nuances of bitterness and acidity: a case in point is the magnificent squab, roasted with verbena until pink, accompanied by a tender artichoke heart, confit frog's legs and giblets with a full-bodied jus, garnished with pan-fried cherries and a tasty cherry blossom vinegar jelly. Excellent bread made with ancient flours by the pastry chef.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2924;Frédéric Doucet;France;Charolles;2 avenue de la Libération, Charolles, 71120, France;46.4334903;4.2751453;36;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Frédéric Doucet's restaurant is a creative and exciting new take on established ideas of terroir and tradition. The son of bistro owners, he was born into the business, and cut his teeth in the kitchens of some of the greats, from Pierre Orsi and Paul Bocuse to the prestigious Maison Troisgros. In his premises nestled in the heart of a village with pointed towers and weathered roofs, the chef breaks it down for diners: nothing but fine ingredients from Saône-et-Loire (including Charolais beef, snails, Crisenon trout and goat's cheese), prepared by means of rigorously applied classic techniques that do not exclude flashes of inspiration. "Jambonnettes de grenouilles laquées aux couleurs des prairies charolaises" or "Le bœuf est dans le pré" are just two of the must-try dishes. The hotel also draws you in with a spa and highly appealing guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2925;Restaurant Girardin;France;Colmar;19 rue des Têtes, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0785765;7.3554964;49;true;true;Creative;The Maison des Têtes, an iconic Renaissance edifice lavishly decorated with grimacing faces, is home to this Restaurant. With the help of their architects, Éric Girardin and his wife have gone all out with a stripped-back, minimalist style, which extends even to the tasting menu. Here, Alsatian produce is to the fore, and each dish is the epitome of beauty, goodness and flavour. You will be won over by the trout gravadlax with pickled turnips, or the hay-smoked veal with chervil roots and an intense veal jus. There is also a brasserie, plus guestrooms that sport a spirit of timeless elegance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2926;Auberge du Cheval Blanc;France;Lembach;4 rue de Wissembourg, Lembach, 67510, France;49.0033254;7.7906578;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Carole and Pascal Bastian welcome you to this imposing 18C coach house, which stylishly pairs Alsace heritage with sharp-edged class. Noble produce takes the limelight in recipes, poised between pure-bred classicism and inspired creativity, crafted by a chef who kicked off his career here, under the auspices of Fernand Mischler. His signature dishes include stuffed morel mushrooms glazed a in meat reducation, locally sourced venison and the Paris-Lembach dessert. Fans of the region will be delighted by the cosy guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2928;Le Gavrinis;France;Baden;1 rue de l'Île-Gavrinis, Baden, 56870, France;47.6232111;-2.8981722;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of this country house is a nod to the nearby island of Gavrinis. The chef, who trained under Pierre Gagnaire, captures the spirit of Brittany as he proudly showcases the produce of this plentiful, vibrant region, with dishes such as his medley of locally grown mushrooms (pleurote, shitake), served roasted, in ravioles, in consommé or his steamed hake in butter served with a white wine, seaweed and Timut pepper sauce. A genuine gourmet halt, further enhanced by the ‘sustainable’ dining room adorned in driftwood and a soft colour scheme of ecru, oatmeal and grey. The exquisite patio, flower-decked in summertime, adds the final flourish.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2929;Tentazioni;France;Bordeaux;59 rue du Palais-Gallien, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8435306;-0.5815909;23;false;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;She hails from Brittany, he is from Sardinia, they met in Corsica... and now they run a small restaurant in Bordeaux that punches above its weight. The chef's dishes are precise and always inspired, especially when they home in on first-rate ingredients: langoustines, spider crab, bluefin tuna and pigeon. Expect very contemporary cuisine, bursting with flavours and littered with references to Italy (put it down to the chef's origins), without ever lapsing into nostalgia or getting caught up in proclamations of identity. The tasting menus change every week depending on the chef's inspiration. It's a real pleasure from start to finish, right down to the lunch menu, which is excellent value for money.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
2931;Les Rosiers;France;Biarritz;32 avenue Beau-Soleil, Biarritz, 64200, France;43.4677289;-1.5534479;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The exterior may be the quintessence of the Basque country, but the interior is 100% modern (pared-back walls, wooden floors and round designer-inspired tables). At the helm, Andrée Rosier (first woman Meilleur Ouvrier of France in 2007) and her spouse craft exquisitely unencumbered food. Our virtuoso never flaunts her technique, seeking rather to coax the taste and flavour out of first-class local produce, wild fish and shrimps and free-range poultry and squab, in particular. Ms Rosier also enjoys jazzing up her dishes with the occasional dash of exoticism ranging from lemongrass and nori seaweed to ginger and lemon preserves. Interestingly, the couple also operates a Basque restaurant in Tokyo.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2932;Auberge des Templiers;France;Boismorand;20 route Départementale 2007, Boismorand, 45290, France;47.80058;2.7394904;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Some things never go out of fashion… This former posthouse, the quintessence of Sologne architecture, whose half-timbered, pink brick façade and stone walls date back to the 17C, boasts former guests of the likes of none other than Mistinguett and Maurice Chevalier. Take a seat in this timeless setting, depicted by massive oak beams, Gien earthenware and crystalware and admire the magnificent grounds planted with hundred-year-old trees from the dining room windows. The labours of neighbouring producers are celebrated in a nose-to-tail, zero waste culinary score. The wine cellar, home to several exceptional vintages, will knock the socks off some of the most blasé wine buffs!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2933;Auberge du XIIème Siècle;France;Saché;1 rue du Château, Saché, 37190, France;47.2464071;0.5436827;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Balzac was a regular guest at the Château de Saché, located right next door to this Auberge housed in a half-timbered building that has retained all its authentic charm behind its ivy-covered façade. Exposed beams, tiled floors, a fireplace and more contemporary tableware: this pair – chef Kevin Gardien and Stéphanie Marques – know how to look after their guests. The spotlight is on local produce from the Loire: poultry from Ingrandes-de-Touraine, trout from a fish farm in Langeais, saffron from Cheillé, cheese from Sainte-Maure-de-Touraine. The chef's cuisine is modern, but not obsessed with fashion, and his dishes are clear and delicious, with lovely sauces such as the one accompanying the Racan pigeon with beetroot in a salt crust, blackcurrant and rose geranium.;Terrace;[]
2934;Maison Medard;France;Boulleret;19 place des Tilleuls, Boulleret, 18240, France;47.4239448;2.874288;52;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Wholesome flavours, jus, emulsions and sauces that melt in the mouth, illustrated by quenelle of sheatfish, white asparagus and langoustine cream or loin of pork and artichokes in a gutsy veal gravy. Their new take on the ubiquitous crottin de Chavignol featuring a light, unctuous, siphoned mousse surrounded by an acidic tomato juice is out of this world. The chef’s up-to-date, intelligent, delicate cuisine sings the praises of local produce, all of which orchestrated into subtle, colourful dishes. Chef Julien Medard and his wife Delphine (in charge of the dining room) warmly greet customers into their welcoming establishment which tastefully marries rustic and contemporary details.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2935;Le Fantin Latour - Stéphane Froidevaux;France;Grenoble;1 rue Général-de-Beylie, Grenoble, 38000, France;45.1899476;5.7324792;99;false;false;Creative;Stéphane Froidevaux has been expanding his culinary repertory and honing his style, armed with lashings of sincerity, year after year. As a result, he has crafted a finely balanced score, as his delectable menu illustrates. Meticulous craftsmanship, tasty and creative without being OTT, Stéphane’s handiwork bears the hallmark of his affinity with nature, depicted by the herbs and flowers he picks himself and which he uses in his “ratatouille”, whose ingredients vary with the seasons. The Brasserie du Fantin serves a bargain priced lunchtime menu, which is a hit with the regulars, as is the summer terrace.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2936;Stéphane Tournié - Les Jardins de l'Opéra;France;Toulouse;1 place du Capitole, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.60391;1.44401;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a bright, stylish dining room (parquet floor, wooden tables, wine cellar), flanked by a leafy interior courtyard covered by a glazed roof, this quiet, peaceful setting comes as a surprise in the midst of Toulouse’s Capitole. The venue is the HQ of virtuoso Stéphane Tournié, with stints at Lucien Vanel in Toulouse, André Daguin in Auch, Taillevent under Philippe Legendre and the Crillon under Christian Constant. We love his knack of getting straight to the point, illustrated by wild pollock and spicy stock of langoustine or duck smoked in grass and herbs from the sweet-scented scrubland. The dishes are often finished tableside by the slick kitchen team, adding a touch of excitement to the meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
2937;Pur' - Jean-François Rouquette;France;Paris;Park Hyatt Paris-Vendôme, 5 rue de la Paix, Paris, 75002, France;48.868617;2.3303786;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Jean-François Rouquette (Taillevent, Le Crillon, La Cantine des Gourmets, Les Muses) has set up shop in this brand-new dining room, signed by a Franco-Mexican designer. The chef continues to roll out his virtuoso talent, illustrated by suckling lamb from the Pyrenees, cooked in several ways (roasted rack, stuffed saddle) and side dishes (baby artichokes stuffed with quinoa and tartare of seaweed). The delicacy with which he marries excellent produce in his creative and inspired cuisine is nothing short of ‘pure’ and utter bliss!;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2938;Septime;France;Paris;80 rue de Charonne, Paris, 75011, France;48.8536287;2.3806905;95;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Always on the lookout for new ideas, the team of Septime led by Bertrand Grébaut stands out by its fresh, confident, always enthusiastic and occasionally even cheeky approach. Septime is the quintessence of the new breed of Parisian restaurants, resolutely hip and trendy, but also unwaveringly committed to good food. In the middle of Rue de Charonne, the venue is the summum of today’s modern codes and its spacious, workshop-cum-loft feel, untreated wooden tables and metal rafters offer a swish version of the current trend for industrial interiors. Slick, professional service. Of course, you may have to wait a while before you can get a foot in the door – in general bookings are made three weeks in advance (only online)…;;[]
2939;Michel Sarran;France;Toulouse;21 boulevard Armand-Duportal, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6072744;1.4345204;38;false;true;Creative;As Michel Sarran puts it, "this is more of a house than a restaurant", where guests are invited to take the time to eat and enjoy the moment in one of two dining rooms – a modern space on the ground floor and a more hushed and elegant ambiance on the first floor. Originally from the Gers département, the chef divided his time between the South-West and the Mediterranean before settling in Toulouse, where he came to be one of the city's culinary ambassadors. With his single set menus that celebrate the region's finest produce, he creates a sun-kissed take on the cuisine of the South of France, whose spices, marinades and confits occasionally meet more far-flung influences (Maghreb, Asia, Caribbean).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2941;Qui Plume la Lune;France;Paris;50 rue Amelot, Paris, 75011, France;48.8590909;2.3683449;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Qui plume la Lune is welcoming, picturesque and romantic. Bare stone walls and natural materials (untreated wood, twigs and branches, etc) set the poetic scene and one of the walls bears a quote from William Faulkner: “We ran out into the moonlight toward the kitchen.” This temple of culinary delicacies is the dedicated work of a team determined to select only the very best produce, in line with a clear environmental ethic, hence the premium organic vegetables. Diners are invited to sample dishes that are a masterclass of expertise and precision, overflowing with vitality, fresh ingredients and flavours. A feast of culinary delights guaranteed to lift your spirits awaits all who enter this sanctuary of good food.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2942;AT;France;Paris;4bis rue du Cardinal-Lemoine, Paris, 75005, France;48.8497742;2.3545943;99;false;true;Creative;A stone's throw from the banks of the Seine, this small, quietly unobtrusive restaurant sports a minimalist interior in line with today’s quest for authenticity rather than hot air! Chef Tanaka, formerly of Pierre Gagnaire, is a fan of fresh ingredients and precision. Armed with boundless creativity and imagination, he conjures up enticing dishes that keep us drooling right up to the very end. The vaulted cellar in the basement is home to a wine bar and delivers take-away meals. It is also nice to know that you will always be surprised here, because the single set menu changes regularly.;Air conditioning;[]
2943;Comice;France;Paris;31 avenue de Versailles, Paris, 75016, France;48.8495058;2.2761393;44;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A Canadian couple, Noam Gedalof from Montreal and Etheliya Hananova from Winnipeg, run this fine Parisian restaurant. The chef draws his inspiration from Gallic traditions, to which he adds a modern spin. His mission is to highlight seasonal ingredients with the utmost care, tailoring the single set menu to the produce of the moment. The flavoursome results are to be sampled in a natty modern interior with vivid blue walls hung with paintings by contemporary artists. The cordial front-of-house team is directed by Hananova, who also welcomes diners in a manner befitting the Canadian reputation for warm hospitality!;Air conditioning;[]
2944;Espadon;France;Paris;Ritz Paris, 15 place Vendôme, Paris, 75001, France;48.8680554;2.329016;26;true;true;Creative;Auguste Escoffier, the first head chef at the Ritz and partner of César Ritz – the founder of the luxury hotel on Place Vendôme in 1898 – established mealtimes there as a symbol of French art de vivre. In an interior characterised by subtly muted opulence, featuring a crystal-leaf ceiling lamp creating an imaginary herbarium, it now falls to Eugénie Béziat to lead the culinary proceedings. From her glass-paned kitchen, the chef skilfully blends reminiscences of her African childhood with Mediterranean influences acquired over her culinary career. The result is both surprising and convincing, thanks to dishes that sensitively combine smoky, tangy and roasted notes. Two dazzling successes are the pressed tomato confit with rosemary and grapefruit, and the grilled lobster with a ballotine of spinach and manioc, seasoned with bissap and crushed raspberries. When it comes to dessert, François Perret's creations are a delight.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2945;Briketenia;France;Guéthary;142 rue de l'Église, Guéthary, 64210, France;43.41952;-1.6059286;99;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The tiny Basque village of Guéthary is the HQ of one part of the Ibarboure family, the rest of whom can be found at the Frères Ibarboure restaurant in Bidart. In this characteristic 1930’s Basque house, formerly a hotel, Martin and his son David are in the kitchen, while Marie-Claude, David’s mum, warmly upholds Basque traditions of hospitality and Camille seamlessly manages the charming front of house. It is the quintessence of a family business, although it must be said that David did skip the roost for a while, spending time with Pierre Gagnaire in Hong Kong. Father and son craft masterful dishes depicted by suave seasonings, a subtle play on transparency and contrast and perfectly ripe produce, most of which is local. Natural, simple flavours before all else.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2947;Clos du Cèdre;France;Beaune;12 boulevard du Maréchal-Foch, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0269835;4.836212;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This elegant winegrower's manor house with a plush feel and bags of character is set in a leafy garden where tables are laid out in summer... It's the perfect setting in which to sample Jordan Billan's cuisine, which is very much rooted in the terroir of Burgundy and showcases the suppliers. The chef's taste for tradition – think matured Charolais beef, bone marrow and a mustard and tarragon jus – does not prevent him from dreaming up more creative dishes with international influences, such as caramelised scallops with black pudding, celery and nashi. Attentive service. Guests will also appreciate the timeless charm of the classically styled guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2948;Le Sergent Recruteur;France;Paris;41 rue Saint-Louis-en-l'Île, Paris, 75004, France;48.8519498;2.3560682;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Alain Pégouret inherited his love of precise, painstaking work from Joël Robuchon. For a first-hand taste of his craftsmanship, you only have to enter Le Sergent Recruteur, a historic tavern on Île Saint-Louis that has morphed into a fine dining establishment. The former chef of the Laurent displays an impressive command of his craft. His delicate dishes abound with crisp flavours – you can taste his solid classical foundations – and linger in the memory thanks to their coherence, the sophistication of the jus and sauces (illustrated by the Périgeux sauce that flanks the egg and black truffle mousseline or the royale sauce that is paired with hare in season and squid all year round), and their spot-on cooking. This establishment exudes a hushed, elegant vibe that artfully blends contemporary design and historic walls.;Air conditioning;[]
2949;Umami;France;Strasbourg;8 rue des Dentelles, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.580961;7.7430965;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of Petite France with its picture postcard half-timbered houses, this restaurant combines flavours from near and far. Its name suggests as much: umami is the fifth flavour in Japanese cuisine, alongside sweet, sour, bitter and salty. A keen globetrotter, chef René Fieger signs market-fresh cuisine scattered with exoticism, yet solidly rooted in tradition. The chef is entirely alone in the kitchen, conjuring up dishes that delight. Highlights include a slab of halibut, finely diced yellow and green courgettes, sliced green beans and an acidic, slightly creamy dashi-kefir dressing.;Air conditioning;[]
2952;ES;France;Paris;91 rue de Grenelle, Paris, 75007, France;48.856449;2.3211774;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This place is run by Takayuki Honjo, a Japanese chef who is a fan of French culture and cuisine. Having trained in prestigious establishments (Astrance in Paris, Quintessence in Tokyo, Mugaritz in the Basque Country), he has designed his restaurant down to the smallest detail: a white, pared-down – almost monastic – space, in which the modern furniture is not there to attract attention. In this context, the meal resembles a kind of ceremony. Foie gras and sea urchins, or pigeon and cocoa: the pairings are striking and the flavours mingle intimately. The harmony of his subtle creations recalls this talented young man's Japanese heritage.;Air conditioning;[]
2953;Helen;France;Paris;3 rue Berryer, Paris, 75008, France;48.8750701;2.3041107;66;false;true;Seafood;Founded in 2012, Helen has already made a name for itself among the fish restaurants of well-heeled Paris. The menu features only wild fish sourced from fishermen who bring in the catch of the day on small boats, which is then lovingly and simply prepared. Rather than fussy frills, the goal is to enhance natural seafood flavours (the fish is served raw, grilled, seared on a plancha, steamed, etc.) – heaven for seafood lovers! The menu varies depending on availability, for example a carpaccio of seabream with lemon caviar, marinaded sardines, young turbot roasted in sage and pancetta, red mullet à la meunière… Everything is a masterclass in precision and know-how and some fish are even filleted and served tableside. The elegant dining room, perfectly at one with this understated ethos, sports a modern, minimalist vibe… Helen is the quintessence of elegant simplicity.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
2954;Le George;France;Paris;Four Seasons George V, 31 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.8687251;2.3007485;80;false;true;Italian;A magnificent Baccarat chandelier, immaculate white colour scheme and delicate floral arrangements all contribute to the chic yet relaxed decor designed by Pierre-Yves Rochon at this restaurant, where guests are left in no doubt that this is part of the exclusive Four Seasons George V hotel! At the helm of Le George since September 2016, Simone Zanoni has definitely made his culinary mark here with his Italian-inspired dishes.And although the menu also features delightful maritime-inspired touches, it is Italy that takes pride of place here. Zanoni’s dishes are light and served in small portions, with particular attention paid to the flavours and cooking methods of the Mediterranean. Meals are served in the dining room or in the high-ceilinged veranda enabling guests to enjoy the courtyard setting whatever the weather.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2955;Restaurant H;France;Paris;13 rue Jean-Beausire, Paris, 75004, France;48.8543896;2.368087;38;true;false;Creative;The "H" is for Hubert Duchenne, a chef hailing from Normandy, whose CV includes stints working for Akrame Benallal and Jean-François Piège. Behind the discreet, elegant façade, the intimate space done out in a chic yet cosy style accommodates fewer than 20 diners. The dishes are deftly done and always on point, whether razor clams with parsley (their signature dish), pollack with amaranth seeds – puffed and as a risotto or barbecued Jersey beef with creamy carrot and activated charcoal: almost every plate enchants the palate thanks to a remarkable balance of roasted and tangy notes. The chef's inventive and skilfully executed dishes, based on premium seasonal produce, form a single set menu – you're in for a treat!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2956;L'Arôme;France;Paris;3 rue Saint-Philippe-du-Roule, Paris, 75008, France;48.8732722;2.3089154;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Breathe in an aroma, a perfume, a bouquet… such is the enticing agenda that awaits diners at this elegant establishment off the Champs-Élysées. A devotee of seasonal produce, chef Thomas Boullault meticulously prepares a polished contemporary line-up. The set menus reflect the seasons and what’s going at the market. You will fall under the spell of his delicate, balanced handiwork: lobster ravioles with Mexican tarragon or loin of venison rubbed with Manakara berries… Scents and flavours to savour and appreciate in a tastefully stylish setting.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
2957;Château de la Treyne;France;Lacave;Lacave, 46200, France;44.8494743;1.5253884;15;true;false;Classic Cuisine;What a splendid spot! The River Dordogne meanders along the foot of this superb château surrounded by greenery, with its manicured driveway and pretty formal garden. The panoramic view from the terrace will take your breath away. The dining room is everything you'd expect: marble floors, wall hangings, coffered ceiling and carved wooden fireplace. Running the show in the kitchen is Stéphane Andrieux, who took up his first post as chef here. You can look forward to dishes such as Quercy lamb (fillet and chop) flavoured with za'atar, lamb shoulder parcels and Oriental-style vegetables, or an aromatic monkfish broth with curry and saffron.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
2958;Jérôme Feck;France;Châlons-en-Champagne;19 place Monseigneur-Tissier, Châlons-en-Champagne, 51000, France;48.9569608;4.3649249;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This charming town is famous for its Cathedral Saint Étienne, Notre-Dame-en-Vaux collegiate church and countless historic sites that bear witness to its illustrious past. At the Hôtel d’Angleterre, chef Jérôme Feck aims to perpetuate Champagne’s gourmet traditions and the heritage of the town’s iconic restaurant. Also a pastry chef, he has worked his way from Langres to Reims via Épernay, so the Champagne region holds no secrets for him… His flair for intense and balanced sauces is particularly notable, where the main ingredients are enhanced by judicious touches of flavour - acidity or smokiness, for example (special mention for his “mayonnaise” with local saffron and herb oil, which partners a fillet of John Dory…) More traditional fare in the next-door bistro Les Temps Changent.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2959;L'Orée de la Forêt;France;Étouy;255 rue de la Forêt, Étouy, 60600, France;49.41545;2.36804;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;On the edge of the forest of Hez, this gracious late-19C mansion, set in peaceful wooded grounds, is ideal for a gourmet weekend in the country. After savouring the peace and quiet of the terrace, the plush bourgeois interior provides the perfect foil for the talents of chef Nicolas Leclercq and his wife Yolaine. Nicolas’ grandmother first opened the restaurant back in 1956, at which time she made her own butter from the milk of her own cow! The large cottage garden (take the time to stroll around it after your meal) supplies the kitchen with fresh vegetables and herbs, which are picked by the chef’s father. Today, the chef, who bakes his own sourdough bread, crafts down-to-earth, mouthwatering, seasonal food.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
2960;La Vieille Fontaine;France;Avignon;Hôtel d'Europe, 12 place Crillon, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9503845;4.8032742;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Wood panelling, mouldings, tapestries and a fireplace set the elegant Provençal scene of this venerable establishment. Pascal Auger is in his element, crafting Mediterranean fare steeped in the aromas and flavours of the south. On sunny days (you’re in Avignon!) you can enjoy these delicacies beneath the ancient plane tree on the terrace facing a fountain.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2963;Auberge Frankenbourg;France;La Vancelle;13 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, La Vancelle, 67730, France;48.2836435;7.3026266;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this small village perched in the foothills of the Vosges, this hotel-restaurant has been welcoming travellers since the start of the last century. The Buecher brothers, who took over the reins of the family-run business from their parents, preside with a cheerful enthusiasm. The delicious and refined ingredient-led cuisine conjured up by the eldest, Sébastien, succeeds in showcasing the best of the terroir in the form of a menu that is always changing. He puts a creative spin on traditional dishes, as in his roasted venison loin, braised lettuce and barbajuan of the shoulder, or his honey-glazed duck with sour cherries and fennel... Most of the fruit and vegetables come from their own garden. The younger brother Guillaume operates front of house, in a setting that combines wood panelling and minimalism. A few guestrooms are available.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2964;La Chapelle Saint-Martin;France;Nieul;33 route Saint-Martin-du-Fault, Nieul, 87510, France;45.8931685;1.1775364;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the doorstep of Limoges, this small castel, once the home of a porcelain manufacturer, is strewn with knickknacks, antiques and old paintings. Chef Gilles Dudognon and his team meticulously scour the region for fine produce, which they blend into distinctive classical recipes, frequently sprinkled with inventive touches. After gazing at the grounds, dig into the “Timeless” Saint Martin porkpie (sweetbread, poultry, foie gras), line-caught seabass or stuffed pak-choi, resembling a ginger-sesame ceviche. Delightful guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2966;Bruno;France;Lorgues;2350 route des Arcs, Lorgues, 83510, France;43.4699245;6.3794424;79;false;true;Classic Cuisine;A restaurant owes so much to its proprietors… and in this rustic and appealingly traditional Provençal house, which in the 1920s was the home of the great-grandmother of the Bruno family, their generous spirit very much makes its presence felt! Having been handed the torch by their father Clément (renowned for his love of truffles), the two brothers – Benjamin in the kitchen and Samuel in the dining room – continue to fly the flag of tradition laced with just the right amount of modernity. They still serve their single truffle-based set menu (the type of truffles changes with the season), but vegetables grown in the new 4 000m2 biodynamic vegetable garden now take pride of place. The olive oil is made in-house, using the eight varieties of olives harvested from the trees in the grounds. Cheerful and attentive service.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2967;Le Pont de l'Ouysse;France;Lacave;Lacave, 46200, France;44.8442311;1.5502327;21;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;On the banks of the Ouysse, an affluent of the Dordogne, this house is located at the foot of a cliff. In the Chambon family for five generations, it was originally built to feed the workers employed to rebuild the former bridge, swept away by a flood in 1966, one arch of which remains. Two brothers now run the family business, one in the dining room and one in the kitchen. Each expertly rendered classical recipe sings the praises of fantastic ingredients, such as pigeon cooked two ways, roast breasts and salmis of legs, or truffles harvested by the family. The patio shaded by linden trees adds the final irresistible flourish. Overnight stays possible in the hotel.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
2968;Jean-Claude Leclerc;France;Clermont-Ferrand;12 rue Saint-Adjutor, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7788173;3.0804584;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Rather than a summons to a hearing, this restaurant near the courthouse extends an invitation to foodies! For over twenty years, Jean-Claude Leclerc has been behind this very popular Clermont-Ferrand hideaway. In an elegant contemporary setting, the chef woos us with his new spin on time-honoured Gallic recipes in keeping with the seasons. In a masterclass of balance and skilful execution overflowing with flavour, you might taste dishes such as pig’s trotters and foie gras wrapped in bacon and underscored by truffle dressing or sole, crab meat, cockles, lemon confit and bouillabaisse jus.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2969;L'Ostal;France;Clermont-Ferrand;16 rue Claussmann, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7810567;3.0879692;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A true-blue local lad, Emmanuel Hébrard was trained by the best (Anne-Sophie Pic and Stéphane Raimbault, among others) and has vowed to defend his homeland (‘ostal’ means ‘house’ in the local dialect). His single set menu is thus deeply ‘local’ and seeks to shine the spotlight on regional ingredients: meat from the local butcher, veg from neighbouring cottage gardeners and cheese and eggs from surrounding farms. Respect for nature and farmers is the backbone of this establishment. The snug dining room (seating for twenty or so) sports a smart, contemporary look and makes ample use of natural materials (wood and stone), in keeping with the establishment’s culinary identity.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2971;Guy Lassausaie;France;Chasselay;3 rue de Belle-Sise, Chasselay, 69380, France;45.8727258;4.7703905;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It was in 1984 that Guy Lassausaie first donned his chef's hat in this family-run establishment, founded four generations earlier in 1906. In a refurbished stylish grey, black and white interior, this "Meilleur Ouvrier de France" continues to regale us with a winning formula that enthusiastically celebrates local (and, more generally, Gallic) culinary traditions, whilst giving a free rein to his inspiration. For instance, fillet of sole cooked on the bone, lemon confit, spinach leaf salad and juniper jus, or breast of Bresse poultry stuffed with the leg confit, an Albufera sauce and a tartlet of poultry livers… Feelgood food that ripples with ambition and comforts the soul.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2972;Moulin d'Alotz;France;Arcangues;Chemin Alotz-Errota, Arcangues, 64200, France;43.4214848;-1.538436;92;false;false;Creative;In this 17C Basque watermill nestling deep in a picturesque vale, a conservatory commands views of the countryside and lush green garden all year round. The venue is emblematic of the ecological, humanist and gastronomic ethos of chef Fabrice Idiart. The chef’s signature menu, “Ital”, demonstrates an exemplary harmony between plant and animal, in which ineluctable veggies are underscored by plant and spicy sauces that exemplify the chef’s distinctive, unorthodox approach. The highlights of this culinary score include a medley of sweet chestnuts from the Basque country perfumed with wild garlic blossom and langoustine served in a frothy coconut mousse, further enhanced by milk flavoured in lemongrass and Espelette pepper.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
2973;La Mirande;France;Avignon;4 place de l'Amirande, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9501365;4.8076612;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The warmth of the sun, the shimmer of colours, the sense of generosity: Florent Pietravalle's delicate, tasty dishes extol the South of France, the produce of its land, and its traditions (langoustine, John Dory etc). Here, everything is on point: from the bold and memorable flavours to the professional, distinguished and smiling service. Note the surprise menu based on remarkable, perfectly sourced seasonal produce from the region (at the end of the meal, you get a map with the names and locations of the suppliers). His dishes, at once technically sound and spontaneous, draw on his time with Jean-Luc Rabanel and especially Pierre Gagnaire. The setting is just as delightful: a superb 18C interior with a gorgeous garden, within the historical walls of La Mirande, a town house right next to the Palais des Papes. Delicious food in an elegant setting.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2974;L'Auberge de Lucinges;France;Lucinges;67 place de l'Église, Lucinges, 74380, France;46.1905123;6.3184274;27;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Benjamin Breton (previously at Fiskebar at the Ritz-Carlton hotel in Geneva) is at the helm of this fine dining restaurant next to his Bistrot de Madeleine. Here in the village of Lucinges, he serves up modern and subtly creative cuisine in the form of a monthly single set menu. The rigorously selected ingredients are locally sourced, give or take a few premium-quality exceptions such as blue lobster and Ferme de Clavisy lamb. Vegetables enjoy the limelight, with beautifully contrasting flavours and sublime sauces, and masterful cooking elevating ingredients such as ikejime Arctic char or the famous blue lobster, which is oh-so-lightly seared. The focal point of the bright, contemporary space is the glass-walled wine cellar, which homes in on top-quality and original natural and organic wines.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2975;Les Reflets;France;La Roche-sur-Yon;227 rue Roger-Salengro, La Roche-sur-Yon, 85000, France;46.66493;-1.44962;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On a busy boulevard a stone's throw from the Église Saint-André d'Ornay, this attractive place is the stronghold of Welsh chef Nathan Cretney and his partner Solen Pineau. A palette of soft hues and bare stone walls contribute to the pleasant and bang-on-trend decor. As for the food, it reflects the quality of the region's splendid produce in a set menu (without options), composed according to what the market has to offer and tending towards the creative.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
2976;Le Kléber - La Maison Bonnet;France;Grane;2 place du Champ-de-Mars, Grane, 26400, France;44.7314765;4.9234014;92;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Julie and Sébastien Bonnet have settled in a pretty country village a few kilometres from Crest, their previous haunt. In an edifice dear to Sébastien’s heart (it was formerly the Demeure de Grane, a local institution where he carried out his apprenticeship), he enthusiastically demonstrates that both his talents and his seasonal fare, equally poised between surf and turf produce, are as enticing as ever. His spot-on, sophisticated, occasionally playful dishes are served in two cosily contemporary dining rooms. The splendid wine list, with Rhône wines in a prominent position, adds the final flourish to this gourmet masterpiece.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2977;Table de Levernois;France;Levernois;Hostellerie de Levernois, 15 rue du Golf, Levernois, 21200, France;46.9927294;4.8776071;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The tradition of hospitality is kept alive in this elegant house situated in the middle of extensive grounds dissected by a river. Here, chef Philippe Augé creates carefully prepared, seasonal cuisine based on classic principles, resulting in dishes such as green Acquerello risotto with frogs’ legs and Burgundy snails, and blue lobster with aubergine moussaka and a coriander and lemongrass shellfish jus. Make sure you save space for the cheese platter which includes over forty different varieties! A wine tasting cellar and shop complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2979;La Mère Germaine;France;Châteauneuf-du-Pape;3 rue du Commandant-Lemaître, Châteauneuf-du-Pape, 84230, France;44.0557551;4.8315131;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine;En route for the French Riviera, the movie stars of Paris, from Mistinguett to Jean Gabin and Fernandel, used to stop off in this village so beloved of wine buffs. The restaurant is still named after its 1922 founder, Germaine Vion. Huge murals depicting Belle Époque Paris, in the style of Toulouse-Lautrec, set the scene indoors and the patio commands a panoramic view. In this attractive location, Adrien Soro, who held a MICHELIN star at his Dordogne restaurant La Meynardie, serves up flavoursome Mediterranean cuisine, with a talent for elevating the ingredients and vegetables of Provence. The splendid wine list features a knock-out selection of Châteauneuf-du-Pape labels.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
2980;Neige d'Été;France;Paris;12 rue de l'Amiral-Roussin, Paris, 75015, France;48.8454303;2.2989942;21;true;true;Creative;Summer Snow – the name is eminently poetic, thus befitting the work of Japanese chef, Hideki Nishi, who trained at Taillevent and the George V in Paris. The oxymoron also hints at the plays on contrast and minimalism that are the hallmark of this craftsman. Painstaking Japanese precision and a repertory as Gallic as the Marseillaise come together in exquisitely curated, subtle recipes with a strong focus on arrivals of fish and vegetables straight from Brittany and barbecued notes. Poised, perfectly judged and rich in counterpoints, the food is as stunning as the snow in summertime…;Air conditioning;[]
2981;Le Pavillon - Hôtel Westminster;France;Le Touquet-Paris-Plage;Avenue du Verger, Le Touquet-Paris-Plage, 62520, France;50.5221852;1.5914671;97;true;true;Creative;Le Pavillon of the Westminster Hotel, a 1930’s luxury hotel and a landmark of the Côte d’Opale, boasts a swish yet subdued dining room, depicted by a black and ochre colour scheme and hung with huge animal-themed tapestries – the perfect foil to sample William Elliott’s creative culinary score. His surf ‘n turf combinations and his balanced dishes hit the spot every time, illustrated by wild turbot, girolle mushrooms, blackberries, spring onions and smoked oil. The terrace overlooks the iconic Canche lighthouse. Simpler fare at La Table du West, the hotel’s other eatery.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2983;Ursus;France;Tignes;Maison Bouvier - Les Suites, 39 rue du Val-Claret, au Val-Claret, Tignes, 73320, France;45.4579161;6.9011983;50;false;true;Creative;Housed within one of the resort’s fine hotels, this restaurant loves nature, with a name that pays tribute to the last species of bear in the Savoie. Its dining room resembles a forest with its slim tree trunks separating each of the tables into little copses, a ceiling covered with a canvas representing leaves, and magnificent tables carved from walnut wood. The chef here also loves gathering wild herbs and plants while out walking in the mountains. Once second in command to Jean-François Piège, he creates contemporary-style Alpine cuisine with real technical wizardry, resulting in generous dishes which are full of flavour while respecting the seasons and constantly searching out the best local ingredients. The cheese selection focuses exclusively on the Savoie and is accompanied by an impressive wine list.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2985;Relais Louis XIII;France;Paris;8 rue des Grands-Augustins, Paris, 75006, France;48.8546533;2.3408104;42;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This edifice, steeped in history, stands on the cellars of the former Grands-Augustins convent and it was here on 14 May 1610, an hour after his father King Henry IV had been assassinated, that Louis XIII learned that he was the next king of France… The memory of this rich heritage lingers on in the ornate dining room which sports half-timbers, bare stone, wainscoting, stained-glass and wall hangings, although the profusion of heirlooms is set off by a few cutting-edge details (glazed cellar, modern sculptures). The setting with a sense of occasion is the perfect foil to the food of chef Manuel Martinez, an ardent champion of Gallic culinary classicism. After training at Ledoyen, the Crillon and the Tour d’Argent, the Meilleur Ouvrier de France (Best Craftsman of France) decided to settle in this prestigious establishment to pursue high-flying French culinary traditions. Enduringly popular with regulars, in particular for the excellent eater-friendly lunchtime prices!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
2987;L'Or Bleu;France;Théoule-sur-Mer;6 boulevard de l'Esquillon, Théoule-sur-Mer, 06590, France;43.4853664;6.9453085;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;After stints in respected Michelin-starred restaurants in Switzerland and Chantilly, Alain Montigny (Meilleur Ouvrier de France 2004) is now the chef of the exquisite Tiara Yaktsa hotel, whose terrace commands a drop-dead view over the sea and the ruddy Esterel mountains. His distinctive Mediterranean-inspired recipes are balanced and delicately flavoured thanks to top-quality ingredients and superb craftsmanship. Highlights include creamy scrambled eggs, truffles and focaccia toast or Brittany spider crab, smoked eel in green apple aspic with an iced cream of lentils and shrenkii caviar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2988;Armani Ristorante;France;Paris;7 place du Québec, Paris, 75006, France;48.8537124;2.3325851;93;false;false;Italian;This restaurant is in an original location on the first floor of the Armani store in St-Germain-des-Prés (not far from the church). The interior is pure and elegant, in the designer's style, of course: a palette of beiges, banquette seating, glossy walls, subdued lighting… Might this be just another shopfront in all but name? On the contrary, this ristorante is one of the best Italian eateries in Paris. Chef Massimo Tringali, former sous-chef at Casadelmar in Porto-Vecchio, works with high-quality ingredients in the spirit of contemporary Italian cuisine. It is fresh, tasty and skilfully done: a fine piece of work.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
2989;La Table - Hôtel Clarance;France;Lille;32 rue de la Barre, Lille, 59000, France;50.638729;3.0571817;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Lille's old town, this former 18C mansion now houses a restaurant that is well worth a visit. The set menus make the most of meticulously sourced local produce, such as fish caught by small boats, and the hotel's own herb garden. Diners can choose to have their meal in one of the rooms that still brandishes its period wood panelling or in the former library (where one private table awaits at the bottom of the handsome spiral staircase) – the decor cleverly blends heritage features with contemporary design elements. In fine weather, why not dine on the terrace overlooking the wooded grounds? Whichever space you opt to dine in, the service here is professional and attentive.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
2990;Alan Geaam;France;Paris;19 rue Lauriston, Paris, 75016, France;48.8714347;2.2923263;78;true;false;Creative;We’ve all heard of the American dream, but Alan Geaam prefers the French version! After a childhood marked by the civil war in Lebanon, he moved to Paris aged 24 with just one idea in mind: to make his way in the world of gastronomy – his true passion. He started out washing dishes, then became a commis and avid reader of cookery books, climbing the rungs of the gastronomic ladder. At the helm of his own restaurant, he has exploded on to the culinary scene as he brings together all that he has learned over the years. His original recipes skilfully combine France’s rich heritage with touches from Lebanon in a true mixing of cultures, and his hard work and passion shine through in each and every dish. A fine dining experience.;Air conditioning;[]
2991;Le Grand Cap;France;Leucate;Chemin du Phare, Leucate, 11370, France;42.9114961;3.0571854;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Erwan Houssin and his pastry chef wife, Pamela, decided to drop anchor in Leucate, which is hardly a surprise when you see the view that embraces the Sète coastline as far as the Albères mountains. Born in Brittany, Erwan grew up in the Hérault mountains and is perfectly at home with meat and fish from the Atlantic to the Mediterranean. He picks the wild fennel, thyme, rosemary and savory himself from the nearby cliffs, creating incredible herbal teas, jus and sauces. Some of his signature dishes include marbled “Fleuron” beef from the Pyrenees, spiced up with a Collioure anchovy sauce or sea urchin served with creamy cauliflower, slow-baked hen’s yolk and a toasted soldier of smoked pike’s eggs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
2992;La Grande Cascade;France;Paris;Allée de Longchamp, Bois de Boulogne, Paris, 75016, France;48.8626663;2.2404762;40;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Transformed into a restaurant for the Universal Exhibition of 1900, Empire, Belle Époque and Art nouveau styles culminate in the charm of a rotunda dining room with a glazed roof and a superb terrace. The business clientele comes here to savour the spirit of a bygone Paris and the ‘country’ air of the Bois de Boulogne. Georges Menut lovingly maintains the image of a “grande dame”, but modernity is ensured with the cooking of chef Frédéric Robert, whose cv includes L’Ambroisie, Le Vivarois and Lucas-Carton, and the desserts of young pastry-chef Joris Vée.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
2993;Le Violon d'Ingres;France;Paris;135 rue Saint-Dominique, Paris, 75007, France;48.8582135;2.3017796;34;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;At this luxury neo-brasserie, the duo of Alain Solivérès (the highly experienced former chef of Le Taillevent) and Jimmy Tsaramanana celebrate the South-West of France with impressive technical skill and high-quality ingredients. The sautéed sweetbreads served with a vin jaune sauce and the millefeuille with its light vanilla cream remain two great classics of the house. As for the feel of the place, authenticity and conviviality reign supreme, thanks to a highly professional team. This is a restaurant frequented by bon vivants, and reservations are essential, as tables get snapped up fast.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
2994;Le Chiberta;France;Paris;3 rue Arsène-Houssaye, Paris, 75008, France;48.8735298;2.2978116;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A sleek, plush vibe, soft lighting and a trendy designer decor depict this restaurant, which is just as suited to romance as to business, in the well-heeled Étoile district. Although the glazed vertical wine cellar is undoubtedly eye-catching, it is Clément Leroy’s culinary score that takes front stage, as he cleverly twists traditional recipes, while respecting the seasons. Consummate technique paired with intelligent combinations of flavours. The “Carné” space serves exceptional, hand-picked cuts of beef (wagyu, Holstein, Blonde d'Aquitaine…).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
2995;Nomicos;France;Paris;16 avenue Hubert-Germain, Paris, 75116, France;48.8702708;2.2830139;57;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Having run the kitchens at Lasserre (one of the temples of classical French cuisine) for many years, Jean-Louis Nomicos is now well installed in this restaurant bearing his name. For this bard of gastronomic tradition, who was born near Marseille and grew up in a world where bouillabaisse is king, culinary arts and techniques are first and foremost about the senses and pleasures of the palate. It is within these parameters that he reveals the full potential of his successful recipes and top-notch ingredients – Mediterranean wherever possible, of course – including his signature macaroni with black truffles and duck foie gras. The contemporary decor provides the perfect foil to this chef’s culinary endeavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
2997;Le Baudelaire;France;Paris;Le Burgundy, 6-8 rue Duphot, Paris, 75001, France;48.8680116;2.3257735;19;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Relax in this stylish, trendy restaurant, nestling in the heart of a snug, arty luxury hotel that embodies the new Parisian chic. The dining room is laid out around an inner courtyard-cum-winter garden, ideal to snuggle up with a good book. This haven of genteel tranquillity is depicted by black lacquered tables, comfy armchairs, floor-to-ceiling windows and sleek white walls. The chef’s well-balanced cuisine revolves around veggies courtesy of painstakingly sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
2998;Alchémille;France;Kaysersberg;53 route de Lapoutroie, Kaysersberg, 68240, France;48.1487566;7.2500389;49;false;true;Creative;This old bar has been transformed into a “living space” by a chef born in the village who has accumulated an impressive number of food awards. The son and grandson of a butcher, Jérôme Jaegle is just as much a market gardener and permaculture enthusiast as he is a chef with an impressive CV, having worked with famous names such as Jean-Yves Schillinger and Christian Têtedoie. Almost Scandinavian in appearance, his restaurant is decorated in light wood and natural materials and is named after Alchemilla, the favourite plant of alchemists. His creative and individual cuisine focuses, unsurprisingly, on herbs and vegetables grown in his kitchen garden, as well as other locally sourced ingredients. The set menus have different themes, with a focus on vegetables and the sea.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3000;Hostellerie de la Pointe Saint-Mathieu;France;Plougonvelin;7 place Saint-Tanguy, Plougonvelin, 29217, France;48.3309222;-4.7706307;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s a real surprise awaiting you in Plougonvelin at the western tip of Brittany, where Nolwenn Corre has taken over the helm of this Hostellerie opened in 1954 by her grandparents and taken over in 1988 by her parents. This family affair has managed to evolve with the times while retaining its traditional appeal, thanks to its old stonework and a monumental fireplace which blends harmoniously with the decidedly contemporary furnishings. The young female chef is very much at ease and full of determination in the kitchen, where her dishes owe as much to her skill as to the 100% local ingredients that she uses, including langoustines from Guilvinec, scallops from Brest harbour, fish from Le Conquet, and vegetables from a neighbouring farm.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3002;L'Atelier Yssoirien;France;Issoire;39 boulevard Triozon-Bayle, Issoire, 63500, France;45.5418256;3.2503873;55;false;true;Creative;This owner-chef, who was born in Auvergne of Dutch parents, deploys his culinary talent in this modern, designer-inspired workshop, depicted by an open kitchen, grey stone floor, rough wood planking and bare light bulbs. An inspired mechanic, he gets a kick out of fine-tuning dishes that are as delicate as they are inventive, made with ingredients from near (Boudes lamb, Mézenc beef, Billom black garlic) and far (Brittany langoustine and eels from Holland). The memory of his delicate al dente carrot greens flanked by a cream of grilled leek, herbs and flowers and underscored by a knockout dashi-flavoured butter and a lemon confit paste lingers with us still. The greeting and the service are both professional and refreshingly unstarched.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3003;Au 14 Février;France;Saint-Valentin;2 rue du Portail, Saint-Valentin, 36100, France;46.951707;1.8650229;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Japan boasts two museums devoted to the cartoonist Raymond Peynet, who created the famous lovers in 1942, immortalised by a postage stamp. Some of his Japanese admirers thus naturally chose the small village of Saint Valentin to celebrate February 14 in culinary style. Take a seat in the new stripped-back, contemporary interior, graced with the occasional poster or lithography by Peynet. The 100% Japanese white-jacketed brigade conjures up a subtle new take on modern Gallic fare, scattered with delicate Japanese notes. Fine wine list and insightful tips.;Air conditioning;[]
3004;La Passagère - Hôtel Belles Rives;France;Juan-les-Pins;33 boulevard Édouard-Baudoin, Juan-les-Pins, 06160, France;43.5648223;7.1155673;72;true;false;Creative;The first thing to strike guests in this hotel, where Scott and Zelda Fitzgerald played out their tumultuous romance in the 1920s, is its jaw-dropping location. It’s not easy for a chef to leave his stamp in such a venue, yet Aurélien Véquaud does just that. In a high-flying menu throbbing with Mediterranean flavours (such as little tunny, semi-baked tomato and roquette dressing), the chef’s Vendée origins still shine through in each plate. Unpasteurised cream jazzes up the signature dish of crab ravioli, caviar and verbena foam, while specialties from the Vendée (préfou and mouclade) are given a new spin and served as appetisers. Let’s not forget the truly heroic desserts by pastry wizard, Steve Moracchini, who conjures up exquisitely delicate delights, such as a delectable mirabelle plum tartlet. The restaurant’s terrace commands a breathtaking view of the sea and the Esterel mountains.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3006;Ed.Em;France;Chassagne-Montrachet;4 impasse Chenevottes, Chassagne-Montrachet, 21190, France;46.9384965;4.7307466;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Ed.Em is a contraction of Édouard and Émilie who met at Régis Marcon. He is a chef with an enviable CV, who started at the Quai d’Orsay, before stints at Philippe Rochat and Lameloise, and she is a talented pastry chef who adds the final flourish to a fine meal composed of a set menu in several courses. The chef’s tasty score, rich in premium ingredients, is full of personality, yet subtly delicate, illustrated by a tataki of Charolais beef with semi-cooked Arctic char (an unusual surf ‘n turf starter), or a delicately cooked loin of zander with an exquisite medley of carrots… A pleasant halt on the wine road.;Air conditioning;[]
3008;G.a. au Manoir de Rétival;France;Caudebec-en-Caux;2 rue Saint-Clair, Caudebec-en-Caux, 76490, France;49.5249389;0.7348884;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This manor house overlooking the Seine is the HQ of David Goerne, a German-born chef in love with French cuisine. He unfussily invites guests to take a seat at the ‘table d’hôte’ in his vintage kitchen, whose walls gleam with copper utensils. In fine weather, meals are served on the panoramic terrace gazing down on the River Seine and Brotonne bridge. David enjoys improvising in front of diners, subtly and creatively incorporating herbs, peppers and other seasonings to highlight the essence of each ingredient. Enhanced by a genuine bouquet of herbs and flowers and a lemon emulsion, his incredible medley of fresh garden veggies on an egg yolk marinated in soy sauce sings an ode to the miracle of nature. Although a fervent champion of vegetables, David is also at home with lobster, foie gras or squab, depending on his whim and the seasons.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
3009;La Bonne Étape;France;Château-Arnoux-Saint-Auban;Chemin du Lac, Château-Arnoux-Saint-Auban, 04160, France;44.0930379;6.0123896;75;false;false;Provençal;This plush Provençal farmstead, a former 18C post house, is steeped in the unmistakable fragrance of Southern France: think thyme, savory, lavender… A family business for generations, chef Jany Gleize is now assisted by his daughter Jane. The focus is on traditional, gourmet Provençal cuisine in a choice of set menus. Swish, spacious guestrooms decorated with period furnishings are also available to prolong your stay in style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3010;Le Valucien - Château de Vault-de-Lugny;France;Vault-de-Lugny;11 rue du Château, Vault-de-Lugny, 89200, France;47.4956359;3.8548891;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The terrace of this stately home overlooking sprawling grounds and a 17C plane tree features in a novel by French author Michel Houellebecq. Mauritian chef Franco Bowanee crafts fine contemporary cuisine, strewn with discerning exotic touches. He doesn't mess around: his delicious dishes shine the spotlight not only on premium ingredients, but also the vegetables from the estate's kitchen garden. Surrounded by floor-to-ceiling glass, the dining room slots into the surrounding nature perfectly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
3011;Hostellerie la Montagne;France;Colombey-les-Deux-Églises;10 rue Pisseloup, Colombey-les-Deux-Églises, 52330, France;48.2225256;4.8874741;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this peaceful Haute-Marne village that was close to General de Gaulle's heart, this fine 17C stone house is surrounded by beautiful grounds that blend into the countryside. Inside, however, not a hint of nostalgia! Neither in the contemporary decor, nor in the cuisine – not even in the set menu dubbed "Je vous avez compris!" (I have understood you! – from de Gaulle's famous speech). Chef Jean-Baptiste Natali has travelled extensively, from Marrakesh to London and New York. He cooks up a contemporary take on French fine dining (with frequent nods to his travels), working with fine produce such as langoustines, red mullet, lobster, Angus beef and calf sweetbreads. HHis broccoli with Galician sea-urchin, his langoustine and foie gras, his calf’s sweetbreads with citron butter and oyster risotto with lime are testament to his expertise. Comfortable, cosy guestrooms.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3013;La Balette;France;Collioure;Route de Port-Vendres, Collioure, 66190, France;42.5244835;3.0890189;32;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Laurent Lemal unveils the full gamut of his talents in this idyllic seaside venue opposite the picturesque bay and village of Collioure. His distinctive cuisine focused on local ingredients exalts the plentiful fare of Catalonia, with a fondness for finely crafted surf and turf dishes (monkfish from small boats, jus of Vaudovan spices and a biscuit of puffed rice and pistachio…). His wife Julie whips up exquisitely delicate desserts. A made-to-measure dining experience which is designed with the maître d’hôtel, who takes the time to talk to each guest before the start of the meal. The best winegrowers of Roussillon figure prominently on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3014;Granit - La Mécanique des Frères Bonano;France;Colombières-sur-Orb;Lieu-dit La Mécanique, Colombières-sur-Orb, 34390, France;43.5783695;3.0232386;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This well-oiled machine on the banks of the River Orb, now home to two brothers – one a sommelier, the other a chef, was a cloth mill in a former life. Inside, granite and wood dominate the decor, while a glazed wine cellar stands in the centre as a reminder of the pivotal role played by wine here. The savvy wine selection demonstrates a penchant for Languedoc-Roussillon (but not exclusively), and the food and wine pairings are judicious. Chef Clément delicately balances a lineup of traditional flavours, illustrated by matured Aubrac beef (incredible meat, consummately cooked) with a confit of shallots, aubergine in basil and foie gras. Friendly atmosphere courtesy of Benjamin's seamless, cheerful front-of-house management. Tapas menus at the Trou du Kru bistro.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3015;Les Terraillers;France;Biot;11 chemin Neuf, Biot, 06410, France;43.6267515;7.0956199;47;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Between Antibes and Cagnes-sur-Mer, this village owes its fame to its art glassware and its pottery, thanks to a soil rich in clay. In fact, Michaël Fulci’s parents opened their restaurant in a former potter’s studio, the kiln of which is now a delightfully snug lounge! In fine weather, the shaded trellis of the alfresco patio attracts diners like bees to honey… Michaël Fulci is a bona fide Mediterranean chef, who learned the ropes with legends such as Alain Ducasse and Roger Vergé, no less… The menu naturally enough overflows with fruit and veg from local markets, from courgette flowers and Menton lemons to figs. Truffles also enjoy the spotlight, be they black from Vaucluse or white from Alba. Sophisticated, flavourful food, drenched in sunshine, scents and flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3016;Le Mascaret;France;Blainville-sur-Mer;1 rue de Bas, Blainville-sur-Mer, 50560, France;49.0671674;-1.583558;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Very attached to his native Manche (the northern département with Cherbourg at its tip), the adventurous Philippe Hardy has worked in some prestigious Michelin-starred restaurants and in the kitchen of the French ambassador in Sofia. It was there that he met his wife, Nadia, a former principal dancer. Together they have transformed this former girls' boarding school into a chic and sweet little hotel-restaurant. All around, the garden and the vegetable garden thrive, providing vegetables and aromatic herbs grown from saved seeds. The other big thing at Le Mascaret is the sea: the chef never misses an opportunity to make a delicious dish with wild fish and shellfish, at a bargain price.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3020;La Table d'Asten;France;Binic;8 boulevard Clemenceau, Binic, 22520, France;48.5992778;-2.8249426;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The first floor of this house overlooking the port sets the scene for many a fine meal. After a remarkable career (Coquillage at Cancale, La Pyramide – Patrick Henriroux at Vienne and the K2 at Courchevel), chef Samuel Selosse now gives free rein to his creativity. Firmly rooted in the zeitgeist and always exquisitely presented, his cooking showcases first-rate ingredients, be they fish or vegetables, giving rise to delicacies such as cauliflower in citrus fruits and fire roasted cuttlefish, brill from small boats, asparagus and seaweed-flavoured hollandaise sauce or a pine-flavoured creamy millefeuille. His sommelière wife runs the dining room with the same drive and sense of purpose.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3021;L'Abissiou;France;Les Sables-d'Olonne;81 rue des Halles, Les Sables-d'Olonne, 85100, France;46.4955501;-1.7873309;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This fine dining restaurant is tucked away in a quiet back street between the indoor market and the beautiful church, Notre-Dame-de-Bon-Port. Its name, in the local dialect, refers to the small fish caught by children in the port. At the helm, a talented pair, Mélanie Roussy and Boris Harispe, trained at Michelin-starred restaurants (including La Villa Madie), have decked the place out in a contemporary style (navy and white walls, designer furniture etc). The menu is packed with seafood dishes (among others) and constantly changes, as the chef scrupulously follows the seasons, works with all ingredients, premium or not, from sardines to scallops, with a keen sense for sauces and cooking techniques. A success.;;[]
3022;La Table de L'Incomparable;France;Tresserve;68 chemin de Belledonne, Tresserve, 73100, France;45.6705497;5.8996741;27;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This knockout location overlooking the Lac du Bourget is the HQ of chef Antoine Cevoz-Mamy, who conjures up elegant, technically spot-on food overflowing in gutsy flavours with a distinct preference for local produce: home-grown veggies, trout, fera, farm-reared veal… Dishes that pack a punch and showcase his weakness for citrus fruit and careful attention to contrasting textures. Finally, the drop-dead panoramic view from the terrace over the lake and Mont du Chat is out of this world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3023;Pavyllon, un restaurant de Yannick Alléno, Monte-Carlo;France;Monaco;Square Beaumarchais, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7384624;7.4258682;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Yannick Alleno’s gourmet counter food, after finding favour with Parisian city slickers, has set up shop in the Hermitage Hotel in Monte Carlo with the same sure-fire recipes. Namely, gourmet fare that boldly asserts a distinctive unorthodox culinary identity. The open kitchen faces the terrace and the impressive tasting counter in metallic wood, in an elegant blue colour scheme that echoes the nearby sea. In terms of food, the accent is on the seasons and wellbeing, anchored in plants, seafood and low-sugar desserts. In fine weather, meals are served on the Mediterranean garden patio commanding a view of the deep blue sea as a bonus.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3024;Guillaume Scheer - Les Plaisirs Gourmands;France;Schiltigheim;35 route du Général-de-Gaulle, Schiltigheim, 67300, France;48.6005284;7.7392002;96;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Do as the locals do and make a beeline for this discreet restaurant with its tasteful contemporary décor. At the helm, a rather remarkable couple – Guillaume Scheer in the kitchen and his partner, Charlotte Gâté, the personification of smiling efficiency front of house. Guillaume, who worked at the Pavillon Ledoyen in Paris and 1741 in Strasbourg, is fully versed in the pleasures of the palate, creating superb sauces and jus, cooking fish to perfection, and focusing on the freshest ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3026;Lait Thym Sel;France;Angers;17 rue Boisnet, Angers, 49100, France;47.4745869;-0.5512482;61;false;true;Creative;We warmly recommend this gem run by a talented couple who have just crossed to the other side of the River Maine to set up shop in attractive premises done out in a contemporary style. Bearded young chef Gaëtan Morvan, who has worked his way through the ranks of Michelin-starred restaurants, serves up an atypical culinary experience in the form of a series of highly original courses that showcase ingredients from the region. Inventiveness, unexpected combinations (enhanced by spices from all over the world)… his culinary style sweeps you off your feet. Fanny Morvan provides efficient service and has excellent, environmentally friendly wines up her sleeve.;Air conditioning;[]
3028;Les Cèdres;France;Granges-les-Beaumont;25 rue Henri-Machon, Granges-les-Beaumont, 26600, France;45.0502101;4.9838433;68;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Some establishments have chosen to shy away from media hype and les Cèdres is in that category. Betwixt Romans and Tain-l’Hermitage in Drôme, venture over the threshold of this restaurant, shaded by cedars and devoted to nature, and sample the work of the Bertrand brothers: Jacques in the kitchen and Jean-Paul in the dining room. Since 1988, they have lavished time, humility and talent on developing their enterprise. As Gallic as Gauloises and Jacques Tati, the menu focuses on flavour rather than fancy technique. The authentic warm welcome adds the final flourish to this hospitable establishment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3029;L'Almandin;France;Saint-Cyprien;Boulevard de l'Almandin, St-Cyprien Sud, Saint-Cyprien, 66750, France;42.6095379;3.036187;41;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This man-made island – home to a hotel complex with swimming pool and spa – separated from the Mediterranean by a barrier beach is, to say the least, a surprising location. The terrace on the water's edge is a delight, as is the generous cuisine cooked up by chef Frédéric Bacquié, who gravitates toward the fine produce of the Catalan terroir and locally caught fish. A sure touch when it comes to cooking and seasoning results in precise, elegant dishes: wild sea bass from Cap Leucate with shellfish sauce, poultry with girolles and a mushroom emulsion, a dessert flavoured with Muscat and saffron… The lunchtime set menu offers excellent value for money. L'Aquarama serves indulgent cuisine in a "chic bistro" setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3030;L'Auberge de Saint-Rémy - Fanny Rey & Jonathan Wahid;France;Saint-Rémy-de-Provence;12 boulevard Mirabeau, Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, 13210, France;43.7885608;4.8333205;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Fanny Rey is at the helm in the kitchen of this grand old Auberge located on the beltway and the old ramparts of this pretty town. In a snazzy designer decor (a curved white ceiling, exposed stone walls, artwork by Francis Guerrier), she skilfully cooks up lyrical market-fresh cuisine, wholeheartedly elevating the ingredients of the Alpilles in set menus with seafood and plants as a common thread. Her partner Jonathan Wahid, an accomplished pastry chef – former French champion –, knows exactly how to showcase the delicious sun-drenched produce of the South of France, such as figs and strawberries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3031;Le Kaïku;France;Saint-Jean-de-Luz;17 rue de la République, Saint-Jean-de-Luz, 64500, France;43.3887002;-1.6644341;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of this seaside resort where Louis XIV married the Infanta of Spain, Maria-Thérèse of Austria, it is a pleasure to step inside what is said to be the oldest building in town (16C). But there is nothing old about the menu served at the cosy, elegant restaurant that lies behind these high walls and mullioned windows. Basque chef Nicolas Borombo (from Bayonne), son and grandson of rugby players, set up shop here after clocking up experience in Paris, at the Hôtel Crillon with Dominique Bouchet and Jean-François Piège, and at the George V with Philippe Legendre. With a love for his region, he creates beautiful, original and refined cuisine that makes the most of regional ingredients.;;[]
3032;Le Saint Placide;France;Saint-Malo;6 place du Poncel, Saint-Servan-sur-Mer, Saint-Malo, 35400, France;48.6296543;-2.010532;74;true;false;Creative;Sheltered from St-Malo’s tourist hordes in a district popular with the locals, this handsome contemporary restaurant sports a decor of organic curves, Fornasetti tableware and pendant lights by Tom Dixon. Chef Luc Mobihan, a wizard when it comes to fish, seafood and regional veggies, boasts stints at the Château de la Chenevière (Port-en-Bessin) and at the Amphitryon (Lorient), where he was the second to Jean-Paul Abadie. He conjures up enticing cuisine in the zeitgeist, such as seared scallops, chutney of confit turnips and Noilly Prat. Meanwhile, his wife Isabelle gives free rein to her love of table arts and her passion for fine wines (Champagne, Loire, Burgundy etc). Attentive service.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3033;La Vieille Tour;France;Plérin;75 rue de la Tour, Plérin, 22190, France;48.5307941;-2.7261477;89;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The contemporary interior, which makes ample use of the light and materials , is admirably paired with the delicate, seafood menu of this country house opposite the estuary. An idyllic setting to sample deftly crafted, first-rate ingredients. Chef Nicolas Adam is not content with awakening your tastebuds, he is also the proud creator of a bakery and of the Rock’n Toques festival that takes place once a year, combining music and quality street food. The glazed wine cellar boasts some 350 references.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3034;L'Archeste;France;Paris;79 rue de la Tour, Paris, 75016, France;48.8617268;2.2782052;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant with an appealing façade and sleek interior (dark brushed-effect painted walls, wooden fittings, large window letting in plenty of natural light) was designed by a chef with a passion for produce. After working at Hiramatsu for 18 years, for 10 of which he was head chef, he now astounds diners with his dazzlingly modern, precise and coherent French cuisine. While casting a spotlight on premium-quality ingredients, he also does a beautiful job of staying true to the seasons. You will find no fixed menu here: the set menus change every day in line with the chef's inspiration. And in case you were curious: The name of this place is an homage to Alain Senderens and his restaurant L'Archestrate, but it is also a clever play on words ("artisanal", "orchestra" and "art"). In the end, what matters is that you enjoy yourself… and you certainly will.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3036;Bellefeuille - Saint James Paris;France;Paris;5 place du Chancelier-Adenauer, Paris, 75116, France;48.8704851;2.2797777;25;true;false;Creative;Built in 1892, this private mansion resembles a small château surrounded by greenery in the very heart of Paris. It became a hotel in the early 1990s, but it wasn't until 2013 that its restaurant opened to non-residents and it is very probably one of the most exclusive establishments of the French capital! The high-flying score, which focuses on vegetables and seafood, is proud to serve produce from the establishment’s own vegetable garden, capable of supplying over 250 varieties of fruit, veg and herbs. This sustainable farming ethos is elegantly and steadfastly championed by the knowledgeable front-of-house team. The wine list is similarly motivated and offers a fine choice of unexpected tipples.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
3037;L'Odas;France;Rouen;4 passage Maurice-Lenfant, Rouen, 76000, France;49.4411004;1.0945346;18;false;false;Creative;In an ideal location in the heart of the old town, this restaurant has three areas: the main dining room with a view into the kitchen, a pleasantly secluded terrace and Le Balcon de l'Odas, a private lounge with a view of the cathedral. Suzanne Da Silva's bold seasonal cuisine highlights both her origins in the north of France and ingredients from Normandy's terroir: the vegetables come from a market gardener in the Eure, mussels from Mont-Saint-Michel, saffron from the Pays de Caux... and she puts it all to good use in a cleverly devised surprise set menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3038;Pages;France;Paris;4 rue Auguste-Vacquerie, Paris, 75016, France;48.8709699;2.2962858;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The passion Japanese chefs show for French gastronomy is once again demonstrated by this surprising restaurant whose bare white walls evoke the unwritten pages of a book. Ryuji Teshima, alias Teshi, learned his craft in top establishments before deciding to pursue his personal and contemporary version of Gallic fare, based on fine produce : shellfish and fish from Normandy and Brittany, poultry from the Perche – there is even a small fridge for maturing beef, including wagyu. The “surprise” menu features a mix of colour and flavours which work like a dream in the mouth, with precision cooking and the occasional use of a small binchotan barbecue to add a distinctive charred note. The open kitchen is always an intriguing and entertaining sight for diners…;;[]
3039;Racines;France;Rennes;4 passage Antoinette-Caillot, Rennes, 35000, France;48.1069433;-1.6829655;51;true;false;Modern Cuisine;When a talented chef from Rennes, Virginie Giboire, embraces her roots (or "Racines"), the result is pleasing, contemporary cuisine in the form of elegant dishes. Boasting an impressive wealth of experience (of which we will only mention her stints alongside Guy Martin and Thierry Marx who, she says, "taught her everything"), she delivers clever and well-defined cuisine that always hits the mark, proposed in a short menu. Interesting interplays of textures, subtle marriages of flavours, and always the finest ingredients, often from small-scale Breton producers. All served up in a lovely, bright and modern setting.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3042;Le Clocher des Pères;France;Saint-Martin-sur-la-Chambre;Le Mollard, 80 impasse du Four, Saint-Martin-sur-la-Chambre, 73130, France;45.3664596;6.3168158;84;false;true;Creative;Perched at an altitude of 600m, this restaurant occupying a former watchtower in the centre of the village looks out over the Belledonne mountains, including the Clocher des Pères. This setting teeming with character sets the scene for enticing cuisine created by Éloïse and Pierre Troccaz, the discreet yet dynamic couple at the helm. The latter, a chef who has patiently guided his career away from the beaten track, creates accomplished and creative cuisine which steers clear of routine and is partly improvised depending on market availability. His recipes are heavily influenced by the traditions and ingredients of the Savoie, as witnessed by dishes such as millefeuille of trout, lobster and diot sausage, and char with a Beaufort cream sauce, Savoie biscuit and blueberries. Charming service and pretty guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
3043;Ima;France;Rennes;20 boulevard de la Tour-d'Auvergne, Rennes, 35000, France;48.106684;-1.684632;29;true;true;Creative;(Temporarily closed, reopening planned for mid-September) “Cooking has always been a means of travel for me”, explains chef Julien Lemarié, who has plied his trade in London, Tokyo and Singapore. At his restaurant, Ima, which means “now” in Japanese, this talented culinary technician conjures up instinctive cuisine showcased on tasting menus that combine subtlety with regional and Asian influences. Lemarié enhances his dishes with broths, infusions, spices, aromatic plants and algae. And for those keen to enjoy the full Japanese experience, make sure you take a seat at the bar. It's now your turn to travel!;Counter dining;[]
3044;Le Grand Cerf;France;Montchenot;50 route Nationale, Montchenot, 51500, France;49.1618024;4.0109723;30;true;false;Classic Cuisine;At the foot of the Montagne de Reims and on the road to Épernay, this imposing inn unabashedly brandishes its opulent style. Come evening, the elegant dining space done out in pale wood takes on a romantic air – the perfect setting for fine classic French cuisine delivered by chefs Dominique Giraudeau (who shone for many years in the kitchens of Gérard Boyer at Les Crayères) and his associate, Pascal Champion. On the menu, top-notch produce, from John Dory to free-range milk-fed veal, as well as game, lobster and truffles.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3045;La Table du Gourmet;France;Riquewihr;5 rue de la 1ère-Armée, Riquewihr, 68340, France;48.1664136;7.2972837;85;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;In Riquewihr, Jean-Luc Brendel has built up an entire ecosystem: in addition to his fine dining restaurant, he has a modern winstub and also offers luxurious guestrooms for overnight stays. At La Table du Gourmet, in the heart of the medieval city, the chef cooks beautiful seasonal ingredients with great care and a dash of creativity, making each dish his own. His set menu showcases produce from his garden (tended according to the principles of permaculture) such as the delicious Petrowski turnip, served with humanely-reared veal, cooked over the embers. Two wine lists, the first dedicated to the fines wines of Alsace, and all this to be enjoyed in surroundings that combine olde worlde charm (the building dates back to the 16C) with contemporary decorative touches.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3048;Château Eza;France;Èze;Rue de la Pise, Èze, 06360, France;43.7276935;7.3610962;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Be prepared for a magical setting – a dazzling panoramic view, variations in the landscape below, mountains plunging into the Mediterranean. But this does not eclipse the cuisine of Justin Schmitt! This chef, who is no stranger to working in the finest restaurants, is a dab hand at cooking up modern cuisine with personality, such as octopus roasted with satay, creamy corn and smoked whisky, or John Dory, courgette flowers, prawns and verbena. The desserts are on a par and the view from the terrace is breathtaking!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3049;Toya;France;Faulquemont;Avenue Jean-Monnet, Faulquemont, 57380, France;49.0564967;6.627029;82;false;false;Creative;Tōya is a famous volcanic lake in northern Japan, in the heart of the Shikotsu-Tōya nature reserve. In the eyes of youthful globetrotting chef, Loïc Villemin, this region is something of a gastronomic Eden where wild fish, plants and herbs thrive and high-quality fruit and vegetables are grown. All of which has inspired this Zen-styled restaurant (overlooking a golf course) with a hip ‘natural’ slant! Our aspiring Buddhist monk chef has spent retreats in the top gourmet sanctuaries of France, notably with Jean-Georges Klein, Nicolas Le Bec, Bernard Loiseau and Arnaud Lallement. His love of fine produce is particularly visible in the mystery, weekly-changing menu. Cutting-edge skill and creativity are apparent in the likes of ikejime trout from Abreschviller, with textures of carrot, ginger and caraway. Unmissable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3051;L'O des Vignes;France;Fuissé;129 rue du Bourg, Fuissé, 71960, France;46.2802;4.74395;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This stone building in the Mâconnais region is surrounded by a landscape of vineyards that extends to the Roche de Solutré. It now houses the restaurant of a true Burgundian, Sébastien Chambru, whose work didn't go unnoticed at Le Moulin de Mougins. He then headed off to Japan and, in Tokyo, was enthralled by the respect the Japanese chefs had for their ingredients. The author of several cookery books, he now conjures up his delicately creative cuisine here in Fuissé, applying his customary finesse and precision and an inspiration that changes in line with seasonal ingredients, eg pike-perch en viennoise with satay, carrot and sauce vierge with capers. In the small adjoining wine bar, they serve hearty fare and fantastic wines.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3052;Les Ducs de Lorraine;France;Epinal;5 avenue de Provence, Epinal, 88000, France;48.169025;6.4491422;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the capital of the Vosges, Stéphane Ringer and Rémi Gornet preside over this neo-Tudor style manor, with high ceilings, stained-glass windows, precious panelling and cornices that combine to provide an exceptional backdrop for your meal. The two chefs deliver modern dishes based on top-notch produce – lobster, langoustines, turbot, caviar, sweetbreads – cooked with precision. Generously stocked cheese and dessert trolleys make for quite a finale, while the cellar boasts a strong collection of bordeaux. Terrasse/conservatory with a sliding roof.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3053;Pierre;France;Mâcon;7-9 rue Joseph Dufour, Mâcon, 71000, France;46.3034378;4.8314285;77;false;false;Classic Cuisine;In the southernmost town of Burgundy, this unassuming house in a pedestrian street is home to a benchmark of local gastronomy. The traditional architecture (bare beams and stonework and an old fireplace) is enhanced by contemporary details. Since 1991, Christian Gaulin has been celebrating the classical union of regional produce and modern techniques. Whenever he can, this virtuoso technician sings a subtle ode to Bresse and Burgundy. Foodies can decadently indulge in tender Miéral pigeon and its millefeuille of cabbage and simmered offal, frog’s legs in garlic cream and parsley sauce, textbook-perfect quenelles of pike, a juicy Charolais tournedos steak and a Grand Marnier soufflé of head-spinning perfection. A believer in fine produce before all else, the chef cooks what he himself likes to eat – to our delight!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3055;Le Manoir du Lys;France;Bagnoles-de-l'Orne;Route de Juvigny-sous-Andaine, Bagnoles-de-l'Orne, 61140, France;48.5623198;-0.4443803;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The huge forest of Andaine surrounding this restaurant, depicted by light wooden wainscoting and a leafy terrace, is undoubtedly its ‘raison d’être’. Poised between Maine, Normandy and Brittany, these green lungs nurture and nourish the forest-inspired cooking of chef Franck Quinton. His way with mushrooms is out of this world: roast cèpes in thyme and laurel, girolles sautéed in rosemary, apricots and hazelnuts, chanterelles in cream of foie gras and parmesan or horn of plenty with ham and ciboule onion… If you stay the night, you can even go picking with him! This wholehearted chef is also a champion of local produce and his pigeons, veg and meat all come from within a few dozen kilometres. Delicate, appetising food served in an elegant, peaceful interior: heaven!;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3057;La Table des Frères Ibarboure;France;Bidart;281 chemin Ttalienea, Bidart, 64210, France;43.4179898;-1.598086;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The third generation of the Ibarboure family quietly presides over the fate of this lovely family property. The sons, chef Xabi and Patrice, Best Pastry Maker of France 2019 who honed his talents in establishments from Paris to New York, rule over the kitchen. Fine Basque produce is showcased in seasonal menus: Adour salmon, Kintoa black pig, red fruit from Mendionde, gingerbread from Ainhoa, Espelette pepper, Pyrenean lamb, Ossau-Iraty cheese. They grow their own herbs, flowers and citrus fruit in the estate’s kitchen garden and greenhouse, concocting dishes such as barbecued Landes green asparagus, vegetarian salad, sorbet of pineapple sage and Meyer lemon. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3058;L'Arnsbourg;France;Baerenthal;18 Untermuhlthal, Baerenthal, 57230, France;48.9500545;7.5440087;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Laure and Fabien Mengus are at the head of this iconic restaurant. Fabien had already made his talent known at Le Cygne, a nearby restaurant. Here, at this former culinary "institution", he shows that he is perfectly at ease building bridges between tradition and modernity – and that applies to the decor as much as to the food. Either ensconced in the lounge or close to the floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the forest, you can expect varied cuisine that showcases great ingredients: pan-fried snails from Farmhouse Ettendorf, perfectly cooked egg and green Chartreuse-spiked herb jus, or pigeon breast grilled on the barbecue and served with chard cannelloni and shredded pigeon leg with cacao.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3059;L'Étang du Moulin;France;Bonnétage;5 chemin de l'Étang-du-Moulin, Bonnétage, 25210, France;47.1975481;6.7214393;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In summer, you may end up in this cosy chalet at the foot of the mountains by a pond, after a daylong hike through the lovely Jura forests, having worked up a healthy appetite. In winter, kick off your snowshoes and admire the Christmas carol picture. The menu features traditional French cuisine and Jacques Barnachon frequently shines the spotlight on the region, with game in the autumn and prime produce (John-Dory, lobster, fillet of Charolais beef). Jacques is also a mushroom specialist, notably the morel, which is the star of his signature ragoût. Wood dominates in the dining room, which also boasts a view of the kitchen. Interesting wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3060;L'Observatoire du Gabriel;France;Bordeaux;10 place de la Bourse, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8413505;-0.5707147;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Located in the central edifice of Bordeaux's iconic Place de la Bourse, opposite the Miroir d'Eau water feature, this establishment is run by the owners of Château Angelus and Logis de la Cadène. The gorgeous 18C parlours have been converted into a single open space and lavishly appointed – oak parquet flooring and thick carpets, wood panelling and mouldings. Youthful Bertrand Noeureuil, who worked under Arnaud Donckele, crafts a seasonal menu of maritime inspiration: “Chambrelent” fillets of young mackerel, Loubésien hake mimosa with morels or kokotxas (Basque fish stew) with wild leeks… He’s also a dab hand at more classical turf dishes, as his “Entre-deux-mers” lamb with spring vegetables and a seafood note consummately illustrates. Over 1 000 labels in the staggering wine list.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3061;Le Prince Noir - Vivien Durand;France;Lormont;1 rue du Prince-Noir, Lormont, 33310, France;44.8779637;-0.5291046;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With its castle stables, glass and concrete cube, views of the Pont d’Aquitaine suspension bridge and rock music as a backdrop, this restaurant has definitely caused a stir amid the gastronomic landscapes of the Bordelais. But not as much as the cuisine of Vivien Durand, a chef bursting with original ideas who reinterprets French culinary convention with a keen gastronomic eye. A daring gamble, given his seemingly complete dismantling of tradition, but we have to admit that he has succeeded! Through dishes such as oysters in a matelote sauce, grilled foie gras served with coffee-infused beetroot, and pigeon with carcass jus, his flavours are often dazzling and his ingredients (the vast majority local) showcased to their best. His cooking has a predominant and attractive “raw state” to it which is instinctive and speaks from the heart. Add to this a sincere eco-friendly approach and you have a winning formula.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3062;La Bastide;France;Bonnieux;550 chemin des Cabanes, Bonnieux, 84480, France;43.821659;5.3174831;71;true;true;Provençal, Modern Cuisine;This iconic Luberon restaurant is run by a talented team headed up by chef Noël Bérard. His modernised take on Provençal cuisine finds joyful expression in two tasting menus, one of which focuses on plants. High-quality ingredients (including veal from Gordes, trout from the River Sorgue, oysters from the Camargue, pork from Monteux etc), bold sauces and jus and a delicate style. There is a magnificent terrace from which you can admire the sunset. Also of note in this enchanting setting in the heart of Provence is the wood-fired cooking at La Bergerie, and of course the comfortable guestrooms and suites.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3063;FIEF;France;Paris;44 rue de la Folie-Méricourt, Paris, 75011, France;48.8636981;2.372288;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;FIEF is a play on words, meaning Fait Ici En France (Made Here In France) and HQ, because its chef, Victor Mercier, who rose to fame in the French Top Chef TV show in 2018, ONLY uses 100% French produce. Sichuan pepper from Gers, Soustons peanuts, Poitou pigeon, Brittany fish, Montpellier yuzu, French satay, Burgundy miso, even the ice cream is flavoured with sweet clover instead of vanilla. On the basis of this culinary ethos, the virtuoso chef flawlessly crafts flavoursome dishes flanked by gutsy sauces rich in character and personality. Take a seat at the counter to enjoy the experience close up and chat with the chef and his team who explain the ins and outs of each dish in real time for a truly fascinating insight into the culinary mindset of Victor and his talented troupe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3064;Pantagruel;France;Paris;24 rue du Sentier, Paris, 75002, France;48.8700016;2.3464362;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Thirty-something Jason Gouzy, who hails from Rennes, is the epitome of generosity, like Rabelais’ well-known character and the restaurant’s namesake, but he is also subtle. He trained at the Ferrandi School before honing his skills at l’Assiette champenoise, the Bristol and the Baudelaire (Burgundy Hotel). Now alone at the helm, he worked with a fashion designer to create this understated gourmet cocoon, both bourgeois and romantic, in the heart of the lively Sentier district. The theatrically glazed kitchen shines the spotlight on his culinary talent from plays on textures to surf and turf recipes without forgetting smoked ingredients and spices, illustrated by smoked beetroot and sardines or the medley of blue lobster.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3065;Le Petit Léon;France;Saint-Léon-sur-Vézère;Le Bourg, Saint-Léon-sur-Vézère, 24290, France;45.010322;1.0897856;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Born in South Africa and raised in New Zealand and Australia where he learnt the craft, Nick Honeyman fell in love with France and its produce following stints at Arpège and above all Astrance. In fact, it was thanks to Pascal Barbot that our globetrotter found his way to this bistro that he has gradually turned into a gourmet establishment. Exquisitely presented, his signature cuisine is a masterfully intelligent festival of emulsions and contrasting flavours. This seasonal restaurant (May-Sept) located in a picturesque village boasts a terrace overlooking the garden’s manicured lawn. In the dining room, Sina, Nick’s German wife and trained sommelière, suggests local wines, fine vintages and the occasional bottle of New Zealand wine.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3066;L'Embrun;France;Brest;48 rue de Lyon, Brest, 29200, France;48.3902009;-4.4914853;89;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Now that the media frenzy has died down, Guillaume Pape is getting back to his roots. After competing on French TV's Top Chef and working with chef Olivier Bellin (Auberge des Glazicks), he has opened his own restaurant in modern premises in his native Brittany. Working in the open kitchen, he serves well-made seasonal cuisine de terroir dedicated to high-quality ingredients, such as sea bass, finely diced beetroot, fresh goat's cheese ravioli, beetroot juice with buttermilk or the chef's signature dessert, "douceur de lait": riz au lait mousse, dulce de leche, vanilla ice cream and milk opaline). His feeling for the visuals (perhaps honed by his time on TV) does the rest.;Wheelchair access;[]
3067;Le Grill;France;Monaco;Hôtel de Paris Monte-Carlo, place du Casino, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7393665;7.4271;65;false;true;Classic Cuisine;On the rooftop of the iconic Hôtel de Paris, Le Grill and its sliding roof, has lost neither its mythical aura nor its breathtaking view! The establishment remains a staunch advocate of high-flying craftsmanship that calls upon excellent and bountiful local produce, adding a whole new dimension to barbecue cooking along the way. Examples include agnolotti piemontesi al plin, slabs of local turbot, rack of lamb with savory or young free-range chicken steeped in Provençal aromas. Other signature dishes include traditional soufflés, such as their mind-blowing hot raspberry and pistachio soufflé.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3069;Arbore & Sens;France;Loches;22 rue Balzac, Loches, 37600, France;47.1274814;0.9965813;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Assisted front of house by sommelier Océane (his partner), Clément Dumont, a young chef from the region with some solid experience, has made this restaurant not far from the Royal Citadel the new place to be. An inspired technician with a love of plants and the seasons, he cooks up creative, at times bold cuisine that is inspired by the village, Loire poultry and fish, and of course the goat's cheese, vegetables from his own kitchen garden, and herbs picked by small-scale grower Juliette Krier. One example is the starter based on white asparagus from the Richelais area, preserved egg yolk, elderberry and sake. A pleasant terrace in the shade of the wisteria.;Terrace;[]
3071;CIBO;France;Dijon;24 rue Jeannin, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3219201;5.0455563;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The pared-back dining room, flanked by a conservatory, is in distinct contrast to the 17C Burgundy stone house in which it is located. Chef Angelo Ferrigno crafts subtly creative modern food and is committed to sourcing his ingredients locally, in fact exclusively within a 200km radius. He rustles up dishes in the zeitgeist, rich in raw, natural and Scandinavian influences, whose art-directed plating is truly exquisite. His fillet of delicately pearlescent, organic trout that melts in the mouth, flanked by puffed buckwheat, trout roe and wafer-thin radish slices, or his immaculately barbecued quail with black garlic pickles, green asparagus, enhanced by a reduction of meat jus and perfumed with coriander seeds, are models of high-flying gourmet craftsmanship. Polished service and insightful tips from the sommelier add a final flourish to this appetising portrait. Be warned: tables are snapped up fast!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3072;Sources;France;Lorient;1 cours de la Bôve, Lorient, 56100, France;47.7458562;-3.3598826;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Hail from Larmor-Plage, Nicolas Le Tirrant are at the helm of this venue in a prime location on Quai des Indes overlooking the docks and sailing boats. A muted soft grey colour scheme underscored by light wooden parquet floors and an open kitchen sets the contemporary scene. The food features a minimalist, highly effective slant, voluntarily low-key so that the ingredients, often maritime, can shout their name and flavour loud and clear: mackerel, langoustine and red mullet. A banquet of flavour, flawless craftsmanship and a genuine regional identity flow unheeded in this source.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3073;Virtus;France;Paris;29 rue de Cotte, Paris, 75012, France;48.8501479;2.3780547;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A stone's throw from the Marché d'Aligre, the stylish dark blue façade of this restaurant conceals a vintage interior with a smattering of Art Deco details. A talented couple is at the helm: Frédéric Lorimier in the kitchen and Camille Gouyer front of house. With an impressive track record of working with the greats (not least Arnaud Donckele in Saint-Tropez), the chef crafts his dishes meticulously, almost surgically. Think seasonal produce, flawless technique and exquisitely aromatic sauces, eg line-caught catfish meunière, pea ragout, stuffed morels and a sauce made with the peapods and vin jaune, or roast chicken supreme, grilled green asparagus and creamy wild garlic braising jus.;Air conditioning;[]
3075;Bacôve;France;Saint-Omer;8 rue Caventou, Saint-Omer, 62500, France;50.7482544;2.2554187;97;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A ‘bacôve’ is a large flat-bottomed boat used by the vegetable growers of the marshes of St Omer to transport their crops. It is emblematic of Camille Delcroix’ inspiration (Top Chef 2018 winner) and of his soothing, nature-inspired restaurant. He crafts razor-sharp menus, inspired by first-rate locally sourced produce in a surf ‘n turf vein. The chef’s preoccupation with presentation shines through, both in the choice of tableware as in the colours and graphics of each plate. Finally, Carla and her smiling team bend over backwards to make you feel at home.;;[]
3076;Auberge de Montfleury;France;Saint-Germain;200 route des Cépages, Saint-Germain, 07170, France;44.5635926;4.4714401;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;From the outside, this roadside inn opposite the station might almost strike you as nondescript, but it is well worth venturing over the threshold. It is in the hands of a couple of enthusiastic and committed pros, Angèle Faure and Richard Rocle. She is in charge of the friendly, yet slick service in the trendy dining room in the zeitgeist, while he crafts up-to-date food, poised between homely rural fare and modernity with a distinct preference for small producers. Pigs raised on pasture, snails, saffron, goat’s cheese, wild herbs picked by hand: everything is local.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3077;Le Mas Bottero;France;Saint-Cannat;2340 route d’Aix-en-Provence, Saint-Cannat, 13760, France;43.6089688;5.330341;96;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this restaurant near Aix-en-Provence, head chef Nicolas Bottero (previously in Grenoble) serves up exciting, flavoursome and fragrant cuisine. As a child, he used to spend time in the region visiting his grandmother, and has retained an affection for the colours of the South of France and an attachment to the land. You can tell as much from the green asparagus from Mallemort, sautéed à la minute, with creamy morels and a vin jaune emulsion, or the blood oranges on a baba au rhum infused with star anise and a refreshing sorbet. Local farmers are among his suppliers, and a small kitchen garden provides the aromatic herbs. The terrace to the rear of the building overlooks a small garden. Discreet, humble and enthusiastic, Nicolas Bottero gets our vote.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3078;Restaurant de la Loire;France;Pouilly-sous-Charlieu;30 rue de la Berge, Pouilly-sous-Charlieu, 42720, France;46.1472011;4.1007524;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set on the banks of the Loire, this inn, refurbished in a tasteful modern vein, is the bolthole of Marie and Fabien Raux (born in northern France, the chef’s eclectic career has taken him to fine establishments from Morocco to Alsace). The chef crafts dishes in the zeitgeist, curated into a single set menu and starring seasonal produce. The vegetables come straight from the nearly 5 acres of garden and orchard that supply 90% of the restaurant’s needs, even in winter! The remainder is sourced from a handful of local producers: Loire zander, lamb, rabbit… Everything tastes of something in this gutsy lineup of flavours served in a warm jovial vibe. In summer, alfresco dining on the lovely terrace shaded by linden trees in the garden is heavenly.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3079;Le Moulin de la Gorce;France;La Roche-l'Abeille;1 route des Aurières, La Roche-l'Abeille, 87800, France;45.5818459;1.2493155;48;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Le Moulin de la Gorce is first and foremost a family affair. In the 1970s, Jean Bertranet, a renowned pastry chef from Limoges, transformed this superb Renaissance mill, set in romantic grounds complete with a lake, into a hotel and restaurant. The chef, who worked for Vincent Auriol back in the day, turned the place into quite an institution in the area. For almost a quarter of a century, his son Pierre followed in his footsteps, flying the flag of fine dining tradition, thanks to his beautifully delicate cooking that reinterprets the French classics and respects the ingredients. Now it is his family and team that will be taking up the mantle and keeping this culinary heritage alive.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3080;La Table du 11;France;Versailles;8 rue de la Chancellerie, Versailles, 78000, France;48.8028642;2.1233414;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Following his first Michelin star in 2016, chef Jean-Baptiste Lavergne-Morazzani has redoubled his efforts, with the support of a solid and efficient team, to win over many more food-lovers in Versailles. His ethos – a natural approach to everything – is clearly apparent on his concise, no-frills menu with a sharp focus on the seasons and starring natural and sustainable ingredients (mainly organic) fish and meat, along with vegetables from his own kitchen garden. The impressive wine list comprises close to 700 labels, with many produced biodynamically. The exclusive location in the timeless Cour des Senteurs near the castle adds further weight to this unique dining experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3082;La Pomme d'Api;France;Saint-Pol-de-Léon;5 rue Saint-Yves, Saint-Pol-de-Léon, 29250, France;48.6842867;-3.9871351;59;true;false;Creative;Jérémie Le Calvez's excellent restaurant is housed in the fine 17C stone-built Le Clos Saint Yves, which was an important religious cabinet-making workshop until the late 19C. The chef leans into the zeitgeist with his array of fresh contemporary dishes. This fine and inventive cuisine highlights the best ingredients of the Breton region, while keeping in step with the seasons. The beautiful dining room with its exposed stonework overlooks a small garden. On the restaurant floor, Jessica runs the show. Charming guestrooms are available, should you wish to extend your stay and explore the region. A high-calibre experience thanks to this young enthusiastic couple.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3083;Le Village Tomohiro;France;Marly-le-Roi;3 Grande-Rue, Marly-le-Roi, 78160, France;48.8672449;2.0941041;16;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The engaging façade of this picturesque inn on a pretty lane of historic Marly hides a modern restaurant in the zeitgeist run by a Japanese couple. The chef crafts surgically precise creations, rich in harmonious notes, textures and flavours, illustrated by his signature dish: goï cuôn of blue lobster and terrine of foie gras, confit of spring vegetables in olive oil and Aquitaine caviar.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3084;Le Panoramique - Domaine de la Corniche;France;Rolleboise;5 route de la Corniche, Rolleboise, 78270, France;49.0227565;1.6096554;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This charming hotel perched on a chalk cliff was commissioned in 1908 by King Leopold II of Belgium so that he could entertain his lover, Blanche de Vaughan, but it now caters to lovers of fine food. Sourcing local produce is central to the Domaine’s philosophy: scallops from the Bay of the Seine River, farm-reared lamb from nearby breeders and fresh fruit and vegetables from neighbours’ gardens and orchards. The resulting food overflows with fresh, crisp, wholesome flavours. When the weather is fine, alfresco dining on the terrace gazing down over the meanders of the Seine is an unforgettable experience in this aptly named establishment.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3085;Le Brittany;France;Roscoff;22 boulevard Sainte-Barbe, Roscoff, 29680, France;48.7245609;-3.9718816;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This elegant Brittany sports a huge stone fireplace and vaulted windows which command a splendid view of the bay of Roscoff. Gourmet marine delicacies figure prominently on the menu thanks to the flawless quality and freshness of the local seafood. Loïc Le Bail’s menu also reveals a soft spot for the homeland of Mishima and Miyazaki, which is far from a coincidence as his wife and sous-chef are both Japanese. The magnificent seaside setting invites us to meditate and wind down.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3086;L'Hysope;France;La Jarrie;25 rue de l'Aurore, La Jarrie, 17220, France;46.1294715;-1.0099137;37;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Nicolas Durif is nothing if not creative! He has taken up abode at the end of a pedestrian street in a quaint little village a short drive from La Rochelle. In an interior that smacks of 19C curiosity cabinets, Nicolas unveils his passion for collections, particularly tableware. Born in Alsace, he has named his restaurant after a plant, of which he uses up to 60 in summertime, sourced from France and the rest of the world. He adds discreet touches from his homeland via a spot of mustard, horseradish or cinnamon here and there. His surprise menus rich in citrus fruits, spices and Asian notes come highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3087;Jacques Faussat;France;Paris;54 rue Cardinet, Paris, 75017, France;48.8830027;2.3066708;33;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Jacques Faussat, born in Gers and proud of it, clearly aspires to the simplicity of his childhood roots. A simplicity also passed down by Michel Guérard and above all, Alain Dutournier. Jacques’ meeting with the latter, also born in Gers, proved to be decisive in his career, starting with ten years spent in the kitchen of the Trou Gascon. He sign flavoursome cuisine made with intelligently crafted produce in a bid to nurture the flavours and aromas. Eater-friendly prices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
3088;Les Terrasses de Lyon;France;Lyon;Villa Florentine, 25 montée Saint-Barthélémy, Lyon, 69005, France;45.76325;4.825745;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Perched up on the higher ground of Fourvière, this Renaissance convent now houses a charming hotel and restaurant with a panoramic glass-paned dining room that affords guests a splendid view over the rooftops of Vieux Lyon, whatever the season: it seems you can almost reach out and touch St Jean Cathedral. This place required a chef with plenty of vision! Enter David Delsart, who has mastered all aspects of French cuisine. He often puts a regional spin on his dishes, smoking his pigeon (or lobster) over Beaujolais vine shoots, cooking whitefish from Lake Geneva, salmon trout from Isère and snails from the Lyonnais mountains. The classic desserts are beautifully made: charlotte, profiteroles, warm soufflé…;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3089;Auberge du Pont d'Acigné;France;Noyal-sur-Vilaine;8 Le Pont-d'Acigné (lieu-dit), Noyal-sur-Vilaine, 35530, France;48.1305627;-1.5346294;15;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Close to Rennes, on the banks of the River Vilaine, this granite building is worthy of our full attention. Owners Sylvain and Marie-Pierre Guillemot met while working for Alain Passard. Sylvain prides himself on his "instinctive, up-to-the-minute cuisine", drawing on regional produce with a sense of invention and real technical skill. He particularly cherishes his relationships with his producer friends, from whom he sources seaweed, chilli, ginger, poultry and, of course, butter. The elegant and light-filled interior, the terrace overlooking the river, and the lovely service add to the pleasure of this gourmet interlude. Very fine wine list.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3090;Les Trois Soleils de Montal;France;Saint-Céré;687 route de Montal, Saint-Jean-Lespinasse, Saint-Céré, 46400, France;44.8626981;1.8642524;19;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This property located on the Causse de Gramat, close to Saint-Céré, has a hotel with its restaurants, a peaceful garden, a pool, and a golf course not far away. This fine dining restaurant wins diners over with its elegant traditional interior looking out onto the summer terrace and the garden. The pre-Impressionist paintings on the walls point to one of the passions of the chef, who was an antique dealer in a previous life. Today, he devotes himself solely to cooking, delighting diners with quality produce and exceptionally fine craftsmanship. This lovely dining experience is also great value for money. Not to mention the attentive service courtesy of Madame Bizat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3091;Astrance;France;Paris;32 rue de Longchamp, Paris, 75016, France;48.8650917;2.2900701;19;true;false;Creative;Pascal Barbot and his partner Christophe Rohat took the gamble of setting up their restaurant in premises that are the stuff of legend – here, Joël Robuchon made a name for himself with Jamin! They have turned it into a slick, modern space, without for all that neglecting to pay tribute to the great chef with the "Salon Joël". With his passion for produce undiminished, the chef creates innovative cuisine in which nothing is out of bounds, with a particular predilection for Asian and plant-based dishes. His fans will be ecstatic to note that his famous button mushroom millefeuille with foie gras marinated in verjuice is still on the menu. The talented maître d' can be counted on to put his guests at ease… and to find them that rare pearl among the vintages that fill the superb glass wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3093;Le Bon Accueil;France;Malbuisson;1 chemin de la Grande-Source, Malbuisson, 25160, France;46.7972986;6.3033347;94;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This aptly named establishment (a warm welcome does await!) is an excellent option in the heart of the Haut-Doubs. For four generations, this inviting and comfortable chalet that is typical of the region has been practising the art of Jura-style hospitality. St Point Lake is across the road, Le Suchet mountain and Switzerland just beyond. Here, they put their heart and soul into providing good food that is an ode to the region. Chef Marc Faivre worked at Georges Blanc, Pierre Gagnaire and Maison Lameloise before returning to his homeland, where his fine and tasty cuisine delights diners: trout with blue cheese or absinthe, free-range chicken, morels and Jura vin jaune sauce (of course!) or roast pigeon, duck foie gras and artichoke.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3094;L'Axel;France;Fontainebleau;43 rue de France, Fontainebleau, 77300, France;48.4049021;2.6973236;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Fontainebleau, this smart, low-key restaurant is the HQ of a Japanese chef who orchestrates a new take on pure-bred Gallic gastronomy whilst scrupulously respecting the seasons. Kunihisa Goto is a fan of French cuisine, wines and iconic produce such as foie gras and snails. After training with the best, he reinvents the classics with panache, incorporating a host of Japanese ingredients: daikon, lotus roots, nori, shiso leaves, Wagyu beef… His version of the slow-cooked egg has become a must. Each dish is a masterclass of plating, balanced flavours and gourmet indulgence. Attentive, courteous service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3095;La Marande;France;Montbellet;1484 route de Lugny, hameau de Mirande, Montbellet, 71260, France;46.4644829;4.872302;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the local dialect, ‘marander’ means ‘go and eat’. On the Tournus road, this handsome house, built out of Burgundy stone and set in a landscaped garden, is definitely worth a gourmet halt before a good night’s sleep. The owners, Élisabeth and Philippe Michel, are clearly determined to bequeath the tradition of hospitality and the love of premium produce to their team in this elegantly contemporary house that feels like a home. In the kitchen, the chef consummately and delicately curates striking dishes rich in generosity. The stonking choice of Burgundy wines and the knock-out patio add the final flourish to this excellent establishment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3096;Le Verbois;France;Chantilly;6 rue la Grande-Folie, à Saint-Maximin, Chantilly, 60740, France;49.2216723;2.4667838;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The reins of this former hunting lodge (1886) have passed down the Guibet family to Guillaume, who is following in his father's footsteps. His clever and creative cooking looks to the seasons, sometimes draws on Asian traditions (not surprising, since he worked at Japanese restaurant Kei, in Paris), and never fails to impress. One fine ingredient after another is prepared with skill and finesse, as in the tuna belly and delicately layered daikon, or the morels, poultry jus, wild garlic risotto and bacon sabayon. The same dynamism is apparent in the decor, with its elegant wood, leather and metal fittings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3098;Origine;France;Dijon;10 place du Président-Wilson, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3158841;5.0442865;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Perfectly at home in this stylish, understated interior, Japanese chef Tomofumi Uchimura impresses with his mastery of Gallic techniques, peppered with discreet Japanese touches. This fan of Burgundy produce elegantly enhances local ingredients: organic veg from a Dijon market gardener, Charolais beef, Auxonne saffron, snails from next-door Jura… Nothing is off limits for the chef as long as the quality is up to the mark, particularly when it comes to fresh seafood. A subtle, surgically precise culinary repertory.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3100;L'Oiseau Bleu;France;Bordeaux;127 avenue Thiers, Bordeaux, 33100, France;44.8442594;-0.552961;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This attractive stone mansion is something of an institution on Bordeaux’ Right Bank, currently in the throes of eco-development. Chef François Sauvêtre crafts pared-down, legible dishes that eschew fancy technique in favour of produce and taste. The surprise menu in several courses unveils the full gamut of his know-how, inspired by the seasons and the harvest of small producers. Meals are served in a fashionably colourful dining room or on the huge south-facing alfresco patio overlooking the garden – heaven in fine weather!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3101;Soléna;France;Bordeaux;5 rue Chauffour, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8405363;-0.5903561;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Slightly out of the bustling city centre, this smart, yet subdued façade reveals a comfortably cosy interior. The chef, Victor Ostronzec has been honing his undeniable talent here since 2016. He stands out from the crowd with his technical, creative cuisine and often inspired plating, and always has something new to offer up his sleeve. His desire to astound is embodied by the fact that he only offers surprise menus in the evening. The polished front of house team adds the final flourish to this culinary portrait.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3102;Les Fresques - Hôtel Royal;France;Évian-les-Bains;960 avenue du Léman, à Neuvecelle, Évian-les-Bains, 74500, France;46.3966417;6.59945;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Take a seat in the majestic dining room of this luxury hotel and admire the Art nouveau frescoes by Gustave Jaulmes. The show continues in your plate, as you tuck into dishes, subtly and precisely crafted with premium ingredients: fish from Lake Geneva (arctic char, perch, crayfish...), fillet of Abondance beef smoked in meadow hay, Bresse chicken with foie gras and yellow wine. The modest, enthusiastic chef, Patrice Vander, works only with noble produce, delving freely and frequently into the estate’s cottage garden. The exclusive, sophisticated ambience, like the breathtaking view and the attentive service add the final touch to this fine dining experience rich in gourmet memories.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3104;La Table d'Hôtes - Le Quatrième Mur;France;Bordeaux;2 place de la Comédie, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.84258;-0.57423;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;At the Grand Théâtre de Bordeaux, a magnificent example of neo-Classical architecture, even dining is theatrical. Chef Etchebest's 12 guests share the same large table in a vaulted cellar, where they are privy to the behind-the-scenes workings of a restaurant, amid introductions to the dishes and the to and fro of the waitstaff. Everything here is a surprise: from the menu to the wine and food pairings, down to the cutlery that you choose yourself. The same spirit is to be found in the chef's dishes, which are unabashedly original and resolved to strike that harmony of flavours. The technique is impeccable (the foie gras des Landes fried and smoked in duck jus with orange!), plus you can enjoy the food while getting to know your neighbours at the table. Even when Philippe Etchebest is absent, he is still there – via video conference with the guests before the meal starts! An experience, truly.;Interesting wine list;[]
3105;Assa;France;Blois;26 avenue du Maréchal-Maunoury, Blois, 41000, France;47.5915007;1.3362808;77;true;true;Creative;Anthony and Fumiko Maubert have temporarily set up shop in the heart of Blois, while awaiting the refurbishment of their establishment on the banks of the Loire. For a long time, Anthony worked alongside Arnaud Donckele (La Vague d'Or), while Fumiko has a twin vocation of nutritionist and pastry chef - her creations stand out for their delicacy and low added sugar. Every morning (“assa” in Japanese), the couple devises the daily menu together, drawing on produce of impeccable quality and numerous Japanese seasonings and ingredients. Sansho berries, wild yuzu, nori seaweed broth, matcha tea and azuki red bean paste are harmoniously combined with ingredients that are painstakingly sourced from local (less than 20 minutes away) producers (among whom Masato Fujisaki, who grows Asian veggies and has been a partner of the restaurant for many a year).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3106;Yoshi;France;Monaco;4 avenue de la Madone, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7408177;7.4279751;50;true;false;Japanese;Monte-Carlo is famous for its casino, its princely family, its clay tennis courts and its high-flying restaurants! That of the Hotel Métropole pays tribute to Japanese cuisine with premium ingredients and flawless technique. Aromatic soups, sushi and maki are crafted with a focus on yoshi (goodness) by chef Takeo Yamazaki, whose cuisine, which is more fusion in style than authentically Japanese, has adapted to suit his international clientele. Examples include ghindara no saiko yaki (fillet of black cod marinated and cooked in sake and wrapped in a Japanese magnolia leaf) or ebi shinjo, kombu-flavoured shrimp balls. Slick, sophisticated service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3107;La Table de Castigno;France;Assignan;33 carriera de la Teuliera, Assignan, 34360, France;43.3983064;2.8875104;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Don't hesitate to come to this establishment in the heart of the Saint-Chinian vineyards. The idyllic Occitan village of Assignan has morphed into a serene foodie wonderland, thanks to a plethora of upmarket guesthouses, art galleries and enticing eateries – including this fine dining restaurant, run by chefs Stéphan Paroche and Justine Viano. They cook up colourful Mediterranean cuisine with a focus on plants, accompanied (it goes without saying) by a fine selection of wines from the region and beyond. Old stone walls, fine produce, an abundance of flavours and charm… This inspired couple also oversees the menus of two other restaurants in the village: the bistro La Petite Table and Le Thaï de Castigno.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3108;Château d'Adoménil;France;Lunéville;7 route Mathieu-de-la-Haye - Adoménil-Rehainviller, Lunéville, 54300, France;48.5649943;6.4627831;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the Lunéville countryside, this charming little Classical château is nestled in wooded grounds. You pass through a solemn series of rooms that have lost none of their historical character: the wood panelling, parquet floors and open fireplaces are all still intact. The restaurant room overlooks the grounds. A few subtle baroque and contemporary touches brighten up this fabulous interior, which is in keeping with the chef's cuisine – traditional with modern touches. Previously a pastry chef, the talented and discreet Cyril Leclerc (who hails from Lorraine) loves beautiful produce. He treats it with respect – you only have to look at the accuracy of his cooking and flavours. Curated by his expert wife, who manages the restaurant floor, the wine list doesn't disappoint.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
3109;Maison Desamy;France;Mareuil-sur-Lay-Dissais;2 rue Hervé-de-Mareuil, Mareuil-sur-Lay-Dissais, 85320, France;46.5348942;-1.2208131;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Previously Alexandre Couillon's sous-chef at La Marine, Simon Bessonnet has set up shop in premises dating from 1860 in the heart of a wine-producing village in the Fiefs Vendéens. But as the contemporary interior he has designed for his restaurant suggests, the chef is very much in touch with the times. Drawing on a regional pantry (trout, scallops, venison), he comes up with bold and original combinations and chooses just the right emulsions, jus and condiments to intelligently boost his dishes (eg citrus clementine on pumpkin, sweet and sour grapefruit with hake). For dessert, his marriage of apple and lovage, fromage blanc mousse and crumble is exemplary.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3110;Il Carpaccio;France;Paris;Le Royal Monceau, 37 avenue Hoche, Paris, 75008, France;48.87577;2.29997;42;false;false;Italian;In the heart of the Royal Monceau, the corridor leading to your table is embedded with thousands of mother-of-pearl shells, in an elaborate and artistic tribute to the nymphs of Italian Baroque. The dining room, set in what looks like a conservatory painted in spring colours, resembles a genuine winter garden flanked by an alfresco area. In the kitchen, Oliver Piras and Alessandra Del Favero subtly conjure up Italian dishes that are deliciously free of fussy nonsense. Their cooking is meticulous, spot on and flavoursome and aims to highlight the natural tastes and flavours of painstakingly selected star ingredients. The same approach is true of the wine cellar which demonstrates a distinct soft spot for Piedmont and Tuscan wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3112;Le Prieuré;France;Villeneuve-lès-Avignon;7 place du Chapitre, Villeneuve-lès-Avignon, 30400, France;43.9631479;4.7962522;74;true;true;Creative;On the other side of the Rhône, opposite Avignon and the Palais des Papes, the small town of Villeneuve-lès-Avignon also boasts its fair share of monuments, of which Le Prieuré is one such. This old cloister, oozing in charm, provides the perfect foil to enjoy creative cuisine made with first-rate ingredients. The surf and turf combinations are sometimes bold but hit the spot every time (langoustine with rhubarb and Bigorre black pork) thanks to big-boned flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3113;Les Funambules;France;Strasbourg;17 rue Geiler, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5869813;7.7678043;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Guillaume Besson has no equal when it comes to juggling dishes! This minimalist and contemporary space is the setting for a delightful dining experience with its white walls decorated with paintings and photos, its parquet flooring and wooden pieces. The set menu dubbed "sur le fil", made with impeccably cooked ingredients, is a masterclass in clear and simple presentation. Modern, clear and precise, occasionally bold, the dishes are always balanced, which is hardly surprising given the name (a funambule is a tight-rope walker!).;Air conditioning;[]
3114;L'Or Q'idée;France;Pontoise;14 rue Marcel-Rousier, Pontoise, 95000, France;49.0501575;2.0976083;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Naoëlle d’Hainaut chose a small side street at the foot of the Pontoise Cathedral to open her first restaurant. The result is an elegant Scandinavian-inspired look depicted by bright colours, a glazed wine cellar and an open-plan kitchen serving flavoursome dishes in the zeitgeist. Examples include Berinda aubergine baked in rosemary-flavoured breadcrumbs, basil, pink garlic cream and grated feta cheese. Each dish rolls out the same technical skill, harmony of flavours and refreshing honesty, underpinned by the well-honed, relaxed, seamless service of a youthful front-of-house team. A restaurant that comes highly recommended!;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3115;La Mare aux Oiseaux;France;Saint-Joachim;223 rue du Chef-de-l'Île-Fedrun, Saint-Joachim, 44720, France;47.3729206;-2.2140297;70;false;true;Creative;A globetrotter and keen ornithologist, (with birds fluttering freely in his garden,) Éric Guérin has invented a universe that is uniquely his own. On an island ringed by circular canals, in the heart of the Brière Regional Nature Park, he has immersed himself in his terroir, all the better to serve up his own superb take on it. Indeed, the chef is an artist at heart, whose first passion is "creating". It is in the kitchen that he has found "his mode of expression", and for that we are grateful to him! Using first-class ingredients, he crafts appealing "natural" dishes that are rife with personality, delicacy, freshness – at times his cooking even borders on the poetic. The charm of the location – not least the "exotic" guestrooms for those who wish to extend their stay – and the warm, efficient welcome of the youthful and enthusiastic team add the finishing touch!;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3117;Le Hittau;France;Saint-Vincent-de-Tyrosse;1 rue du Nouaou, Saint-Vincent-de-Tyrosse, 40230, France;43.6617126;-1.2961309;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You may well miss this former sheepfold tucked away in verdant greenery with its exposed timberwork on the beach road. It is however well worth keeping your eyes open! Chef Yannick Duc treats diners to spontaneous, vibrant recipes that are tailored to modern tastebuds, displaying a strong predilection for first-class seasonal produce, in particular the catch of the day. The chef also enjoys mixing seasonings, spices and peppers, jazzing up his carpaccio of Banka trout with horseradish and black lemon cream and wasabi ice cream or pairing ravioles of lobster with green curry, bisque of fish heads and coconut milk. Served alfresco on the patio in fine weather opposite the herb garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3118;Maison Ruffet - Villa Navarre;France;Pau;59 avenue Trespoey, Pau, 64000, France;43.298212;-0.3474375;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A large 19C villa set in verdant grounds is home to this snugly welcoming establishment with only six tables. The period herringbone parquet flooring and mouldings contrast with the pared-back interior. The single set menu shines the spotlight on first-class ingredients from Bigorre and Béarn in a new take on regional recipes that are as mouthwatering as they are deftly crafted.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
3120;Aux Pesked;France;Saint-Brieuc;59 rue du Légué, Saint-Brieuc, 22000, France;48.5221338;-2.7632962;64;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;You might be in town, but there’s a sense of already being in the countryside at this restaurant decorated in resolutely contemporary style and boasting sweeping views of the verdant banks of the River Gouët. And as you would expect, pesked (“fish” in Breton) takes pride of place here – ultra-fresh and cooked with the utmost care by chef Mathieu Aumont, such as the wild ormer harvested three days before to ensure that their texture is creamy and they are at their best. And when it comes to choosing your wine pairings, make sure you take the advice of Mathieu’s wife Sophie. Maritime-inspired cuisine at its best.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3121;La Table de Cédric Béchade - L'Auberge Basque;France;Saint-Pée-sur-Nivelle;745 vieille route de Saint-Pée - quartier Helbarron, Saint-Pée-sur-Nivelle, 64310, France;43.3675657;-1.5846002;61;true;false;Creative;Close to Saint-Jean-de-Luz and the coast, this old Basque farmhouse has an elegant contemporary wing overlooking the Rhune (Larrun) mountain and the countryside. It is here, in the very heart of the Basque Country, that chef Cédric Béchade and Marion, his wife, welcome you in true 21C innkeeper style. This creative chef (who trained in Biarritz – at the Hôtel du Palais – then worked in the kitchens of the Plaza Athénée alongside Jean-François Piège) uses top-notch ingredients, sourced from as close as possible to the Basque region and lovingly prepared with all the care they deserve. A case in point is the baby squid served with its ink, and the light, delicate dessert with yuzu from nearby Ahyerre. The terrace is very popular in fine weather, as are the guestrooms to extend your stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3122;Logis de la Cadène;France;Saint-Emilion;3 place du Marché-au-Bois, Saint-Emilion, 33330, France;44.8934854;-0.1559683;93;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the town, this logis dating back to 1848 is one of Saint Émilion’s oldest restaurants. Picture plush, cosy dining rooms done up in the same elegant vein as the guestrooms available for overnight stays. The new chef, Thibaut Gamba, crafts delicate, subtle dishes that showcase local produce as much as possible. Some of the fruit and vegetables come from the estate’s farm, as does the honey. Splendid wine cellar, with a knockout selection of Bordeaux reds, ideal when sampled with the establishment’s superlative range of cheeses.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3123;Le Gindreau;France;Saint-Médard;146 rue du Gindreau, le Bourg, Saint-Médard, 46150, France;44.5383407;1.2913203;70;true;false;Creative;In a small village overlooking the hillsides, the old village school has been transformed into a restaurant. Welcome to the Gindreau in Saint Médard. Chef Pascal Bardet, originally from Lot and who worked for Alain Ducasse for 18 years, particularly at the Louis XV, is flourishing in his own kitchen. “My cooking is entirely free of set rules,” confides this shy, but confident craftsman. His knack with regional produce, particularly truffles, is indeed second to none. Take a seat under the shade of the chestnut trees and watch the sun set in Quercy.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3124;Au Vieux Couvent;France;Rhinau;6 rue des Chanoines, Rhinau, 67860, France;48.317236;7.7069299;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;With its decorative half-timbering that is emblematic of this part of Alsace, the inviting mushroom-coloured building catches the eye from afar. Close to the flower-decked banks of the Brunnwasser, it houses this restaurant, where diners can sample the dishes of Alexis Albrecht, who has worked at some top restaurants (Au Crocodile, the Pourcel brothers and Jacques Maximin). The chef's generous seasonal cuisine makes the most of the terroir and local produce, such as fish from the Rhine and game from the Ried… He also draws on an abundance of vegetables and aromatic herbs from the family's kitchen garden, which he and his father cultivate.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3125;L'Escarbille;France;Meudon;8 rue de Vélizy, Meudon, 92190, France;48.8202241;2.2270933;16;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Abutting the railway lines, this town house (once the station café) has morphed into a gourmet restaurant, with a chic, modern vibe and adorned with photos and artwork. The recipes are the work of a seasoned chef, Régis Douysset, who is backed up by a crack team in the kitchen. The ingredient-led cuisine is flawlessly cooked and precisely seasoned, a case in point being the cod, fresh morels and watercress. These dishes are accompanied by meticulously selected wines from small-scale producers. You can also enjoy your meal on the terrace. Valet parking available.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3126;Frédéric Simonin;France;Paris;25 rue Bayen, Paris, 75017, France;48.8799558;2.2943806;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Frédéric Simonin learned the ropes in top restaurants and alongside great chefs, from Ledoyen at the Meurice to Joël Robuchon, before becoming a Best Craftsman of France himself in 2019. Out went the black and white geometric lines as Frédéric set about creating a venue of his very own, depicted by parquet floors, white walls and bevelled mirrors. This “Parisian apartment” (his own words) is the perfect foil for his precise, delicate and poised cuisine – special mention for his reductions and sauces. Not afraid of the odd inventive, even Japanese note, he dares unlikely combinations, particularly in his evening tasting menu. The lunchtime menu is a steal, as is the list of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
3127;Le Gourmet de Sèze;France;Lyon;125 rue de Sèze, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7691128;4.8559442;19;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Bernard Mariller, one of the chefs behind the revival of Lyon’s food scene in the 1990s, has been plying his trade in this street, just a few steps from the restaurant’s original address, for some thirty years. This son and grandson of farmers from the Saône-et-Loire, who boasts stints with Joël Robuchon, Jacques Lameloise and Michel Troisgros, has lost none of his inimitable energy! He crafts delicious modern cuisine based on seasonal, often noble ingredients (scallops from Erquy and line-caught Brittany seabass). His attention to detail and superlative sauce-making talents are still very much to the fore.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3128;La Table d'Hôtes - La Rôtisserie du Chambertin;France;Gevrey-Chambertin;6 rue du Chambertin, Gevrey-Chambertin, 21220, France;47.2240872;4.969631;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Thomas Collomb is at the head of an outstanding table d’hôtes in Gevrey-Chambertin, in which nothing is left to chance! Flawless ingredients, most of which from organic, meticulously selected suppliers, recognisable, artfully presented dishes which unfold during a tasting menu rich in surprises and a stylish smart rustic interior. But there is more to come! The wine list is out of this world (well, this is the region!) and the service is professional and attentive, without being oppressive. The pinnacle of fine dining.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3129;La Licorne Royale;France;Lyons-la-Forêt;27 place Isaac-Benserade, Lyons-la-Forêt, 27480, France;49.3985891;1.4766068;60;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this old half-timbered house in a small Normandy village, the chef has proved himself to be an extraordinary craftsman. Boasting sound technical skills (especially when it comes to sauces and emulsions), he is equally at ease when it comes to allying seafood, local ingredients and the flavours of the South of France. The chic, classically inspired decor features numerous references to the battles fought by Napoleon.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3132;Albert 1er;France;Chamonix-Mont-Blanc;Hameau Albert-1er, 38 route du Bouchet, Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, 74400, France;45.9249264;6.8739886;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Pierre, Marcel, Joseph, Clothilde… since it was founded in 1903, this restaurant has been run by four generations and Perrine Carrier is the fifth of this illustrious family. Chef Damien Leveau's cuisine draws on the culinary heritage of Savoie and Piedmont, using produce from the region (Arctic char and whitefish from Lake Geneva, snails from around Mont Blanc, pork and lamb from the surrounding farms), enhanced by what is grown in the aromatic garden: oxalis, lovage, citrus thyme, savory, lemon balm and sage. Meals are served in a supremely stylish, yet understated interior. The elegant hamlet is also home to Maison Carrier, which serves authentic regional fare in a former Alpine farmstead oozing with charm.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3133;Le 1862 - Les Glycines;France;Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil;4 avenue de Laugerie, Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil, 24620, France;44.9407834;1.0074802;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Colourful, unusual recipes, impeccably cooked and crafted with first-class ingredients, including veggies from the garden: such is the enticing programme that Le 1862, the main restaurant of Les Glycines Hotel, has in store for you. This former coaching inn, located between the railway station and the River Vézère, serves market-fresh cuisine with subtle harmonies of flavours and polished sauces. The chef enhances the finest produce from the surrounding countryside – suckling lamb, saffron, foie gras and the kitchen garden harvest and diners get to sample it all in a smart fashionable venue leading onto a terrace-loggia overlooking the grounds. Slick service and first-rate wine tips from Léa Lombard, the chef’s daughter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3135;Ô Flaveurs;France;Douvaine;Château de Chilly, 42 route du Crépy, Douvaine, 74140, France;46.3018121;6.3139725;98;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The epitome of rural France! With its exposed stonework, beams, floorboards and fireplace, so welcome during cold winter evenings, this authentic little 15C castle will delight those of a romantic disposition, as will the mystery menu of chef Jérôme Mamet, who is a stickler when it comes to plating! This inventive and talented chef works only with carefully selected, often organic, ingredients of the highest quality. Delicious terrace.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3137;Le Jardin des Plumes;France;Giverny;1 rue du Milieu, Giverny, 27620, France;49.0756756;1.5253889;77;false;false;Creative;A short walk from Claude Monet’s house, this half-timbered Anglo-Norman 1912 edifice extends an invitation to relax and enjoy the good things of life. The tasteful interior mixes Art deco features (worn blue and white floor tiles, peacock blue walls) with 1960’s white leather armchairs and glass and rosewood tables, while the lovely patio is flanked by a delightful, wooded garden. Normandy born chef, David Gallienne, who trained at the Manoir du Lys, continues to work with some of his former suppliers from Orne and Dieppe fishermen, whilst sourcing new ones. His inventive recipes feature unorthodox flavours and textures. The chef has opened a nearby guesthouse for overnight stays and a delicatessen in Vernon.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3138;Prairial;France;Lyon;1 place Hubert-Mounier, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7415161;4.8229022;59;true;true;Creative;Chef Gaëtan Gentil's new restaurant in the Confluence neighbourhood is housed in a building that is eco-responsible from floor to ceiling, and that includes the French oak tables. From the open kitchen in the middle of the space, he creates his seasonal cuisine that highlights the produce of the Rhône Valley terroir, using herbs and wild plants to great effect. This creative, instinctive yet carefully thought-out cooking is based on the elevation of ingredients, which are subject to numerous variations and enhanced by sauces packed with flavour. All his chosen suppliers share the same commitment to the environment: permaculture market gardeners, more sustainable livestock farming, wild or more appropriately reared freshwater fish. The 950 organic and natural wines on the wine list follow suit, slotting into a meal that is delicious but does not come at the expense of the planet.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3139;Côté Jardin;France;Gien;14 avenue de Bourges, Gien, 45500, France;47.6803325;2.6296242;69;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;On the left bank of the Loire on the road to Bourges, the breeze comes as much from the river as from the stringently selected fresh ingredients! The kitchen is supplied by a local market gardener who grows over 300 varieties of fruit, veg and herbs. A native of Maubeuge, chef Arnaud Billard, who has a soft spot for fish, signs tasty market cuisine, oozing with subtle combinations of ingredients. Examples include flawlessly cooked John Dory, paired with a silky vanilla-flavoured sauce on a bed of slowly cooked leeks.;Air conditioning;[]
3140;Le Donjon - Domaine Saint-Clair;France;Etretat;Chemin de Saint-Clair, Etretat, 76790, France;49.7064346;0.2123457;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This stylish Normandy manor commissioned a fresco by Jean-Charles Castelbajac for its dining room, creating the perfect foil for the view of the sun setting over the town of Étretat and its cliffs on the horizon. The culinary score has embraced a two-fold seaside/plant theme with just the right blend of balance and harmony as sauces and jus add a welcome gutsy kick greatly appreciated by discerning foodies. Pleasant guestrooms to stay longer.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
3141;La Gouesnière - Domaine du Limonay;France;Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes;Lieu-dit Le Limonay, Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes, 35350, France;48.6150771;-1.9054771;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This hostelry founded in 1936 is a fine dining establishment whose delicate, creative recipes celebrate Brittany’s splendid produce: seafood from Saint Malo Bay, lamb from the salt marshes, buckwheat… A gourmet experience in every sense of the word, further enhanced by the chef’s inimitable flair for jus and sauces.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3142;La Palmeraie - Château de Valmer;France;La Croix-Valmer;81 boulevard de Gigaro, La Croix-Valmer, 83420, France;43.19189;6.588246;44;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Nestling between vineyards, orchards and the sea, this early-20C hotel-restaurant is tucked away in a lush garden dotted with hundred-year-old palm and magnolia trees. Like the Mediterranean vegetable garden that inspires Burgundy-born Alexandre Fabris's three Provençal-style set menus (one vegetarian), it is a real draw in itself. In his cuisine, the chef deftly juxtaposes textures and marries flavours. The restaurant is open from mid-June to mid-September for dinner only, when guests take their seats in the garden or beneath the pergola on the terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3143;La Petite Maison de Cucuron;France;Cucuron;Place de l'Étang, Cucuron, 84160, France;43.773919;5.4387208;36;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This "petite maison" imbued with a genteel Provençal charm and recognisable by its yellow façade is the stomping ground of chef Éric Sapet. He elevates market ingredients like no other: mushrooms, including truffles, to which he dedicates a set menu in season, vegetables from local market gardeners, Provençal cheeses, game and also shellfish. A devoted gourmet and wine-lover, Sapet already has a solid career to his name and delivers classic Provençal cuisine rife with flavours. Be aware that the restaurant often gets fully booked.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3145;La Renaissance;France;Argentan;20 avenue de la 2ème-Division-Blindée, Argentan, 61200, France;48.7391758;-0.0285254;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this small town, the angular modern façade of La Renaissance – a contemporary, coffee-coloured extension to the large main building – doesn't go unnoticed. A native of the region, Arnaud Viel is at home here, as is his neighbour, philosopher Michel Onfray, who prefaces the restaurant's menus. Normandy takes pride of place, with fish and seafood ingredients at their freshest, from Carteret lobster to Veules-les-Roses oysters, monkfish from Port-en-Bessin, sand carrots from Créances and foie gras from the Pays d'Auge. This delicate, modern cuisine is skilfully accomplished and harmoniously balanced.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3146;A Casa di Mà;France;Lumio;Route de Calvi, Lumio, 20260, France;42.5813042;8.8318859;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Lumio, a village in Haute-Corse, is the quintessence of light and flavour... The chef conjures up subtle and delicious fare that is enhanced by creative touches and always respectful of the fine ingredients with which the island abounds. The red tuna with caviar, for example, and the roast veal chop smoked with myrtle, chlorophyll of maquis herbs and a full-bodied jus are sensational. The contemporary interior leads onto a pretty terrace, the ideal setting for sampling this pared-back cuisine drenched in the flavours of the Mediterranean and the Corsican terroir. Friendly, attentive service. Prolong the magical experience of dining at this beautiful place by spending the night at the hotel overlooking the Bay of Calvi.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3150;Louroc - Hôtel du Cap-Eden-Roc;France;Antibes;Boulevard J.-F.-Kennedy, au Cap d'Antibes, Antibes, 06160, France;43.5483167;7.1216544;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The restaurant of this mythical luxury hotel ticks all the boxes. It combines attentive service, tableware produced for the most part by Provençal artisans, a breathtaking view of the Mediterranean, and the talents of chef Sébastien Broda. The pantry abounds with vegetables sourced exclusively in the hotel's own kitchen garden and from local market gardeners, as well as fish from small-scale fisheries and bespoke meats. This Mediterranean cuisine is exemplified by coherent dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3151;Le Relais des Moines;France;Les Arcs;Route de Sainte-Roseline, Les Arcs, 83460, France;43.46639;6.49026;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Nestling amid the greenery, this gorgeous 16C bastide looks out over the Massif des Maures and the picturesque village of Arc-sur-Argens. The son of restaurateurs from the South-West, Sébastien Sanjou has set up shop in the Var, where his early endeavours were supported by Jacques Maximin and Alain Ducasse. This native of Tarbes is savvily making the Mediterranean terroir his own, cultivating, for example, an exceptional partnership with market gardener Philippe Auda. Wonderfully ripe and juicy tomatoes, served with a basil sorbet and burrata and seasoned with olive oil and Baume de Bouteville vinegar, make for a fantastically sunny starter. This is typical of his cuisine: colourful and imaginative, with, at the heart of each dish, a wonderful ingredient that has been carefully prepared with respect for its original flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3152;Mallory Gabsi;France;Paris;28 rue des Acacias, Paris, 75017, France;48.876837;2.2915873;16;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A semi-finalist in French TV's Top Chef in 2020, Belgian chef Mallory Gabsi loves to cook. He communicates his enthusiasm through a varied and deftly crafted score that astutely balances acidic and bitter notes, courtesy of Iranian dried lime or sorbus berries in particular. This refreshing wind of culinary audacity contrasts with the establishment’s plush, muted interior that is reminiscent of a luxurious ocean liner of yesteryear thanks to pale varnished marquetry, wool-upholstered seating and Art deco wall lamps… Gabsi, the darling of a new generation of foodies, signs a “Turquoise Menu” (his favourite colour) scattered with delectable nods to his homeland (such as his version of eels in sorrel, lacquered in beer) and pulls off daring combinations of explosive flavours such as a dessert that features citrus fruit and seaweed or an incredible showpiece that blends tobacco, vanilla and coffee.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3153;Le Belvédère;France;Bozouls;11 route du Maquis-Jean-Pierre, Bozouls, 12340, France;44.4727564;2.719852;42;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This chic, rustic inn commands a breathtaking view of the famous Bozouls Canyon, a natural cirque hewn out of the limestone plateau. The chef has a contagious enthusiasm for traditional farming methods and wines from small-scale producers, as shown by a dish such as house-smoked bacon, green beans, potatoes and herbs, Causses yoghurt.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3154;Le Figuier de Saint-Esprit;France;Antibes;14 rue Saint-Esprit, Antibes, 06600, France;43.5818083;7.1284844;32;false;true;Provençal;Straddling the ramparts of the old town, between the Picasso Museum and the Marché Provençal, this place is redolent of Provence! The fig tree gracing the patio is just the start. At the helm of this family-run country house is Christian Morisset, whose curly moustache has almost become part of the local heritage. With his wife holding the fort front of house, and assisted in the kitchen by his son, the chef loves to cook with fine, tasty ingredients, which he selects every week at the Old Antibes market and the Forville Market in Cannes. His squid-ink cuttlefish cannelloni with a shellfish jus made with fresh basil leaves and his saddle of lamb cooked in Vallauris clay have become real signature dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3155;La Closerie;France;Ansouis;Boulevard des Platanes, Ansouis, 84240, France;43.7381545;5.4649088;77;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This former post office in the Luberon is an ode to Provence where you can choose between the elegant and modern dining room or the small panoramic terrace. Having sourced his ingredients from local producers, Marseille-born chef Olivier Alemany (trained by Jacques Chibois, in particular) enchants guests with traditional cuisine enhanced by Provence’s superb sun-blessed natural bounty with its incomparable freshness. Meanwhile, in the dining room, his wife Delphine provides attentive and meticulous service. To ease their post-meal digestion, sated guests can explore the narrow streets up to the church and château of the charming village of Ansouis.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3157;Nhome;France;Paris;41 rue de Montpensier, Paris, 75001, France;48.8661738;2.3374459;26;false;true;Creative;Matan Zaken has thrown out the culinary rulebook! After globetrotting as the private chef to top fashion houses, with stints at Frenchie in London, the George V with Christian Le Squer and Saturne with Sven Chartier, the French-Israeli chef now host you in this astonishing vaulted cellar opposite the Palais Royal. In the convivial atmosphere created by having one enormous table laid for 20 guests, he proposes a Scandinavian-style set menu that features creative cuisine drawing on multiple influences (notably Japanese and Middle Eastern) and a variety of culinary techniques (low-temperature cooking, binchotan charcoal, fermentation, brine pickling etc). Think superb line-caught turbot with chanterelles, finished with a potent blackberry-sherry vinegar-Kampot pepper condiment and a fermented rye miso sauce. Very attentive service.;Air conditioning;[]
3159;La Table de Philippe Girardon;France;Chonas-l'Amballan;Domaine de Clairefontaine, 105 chemin des Fontanettes, Chonas-l'Amballan, 38121, France;45.456987;4.8107351;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The fourth generation is at the helm of this family business, established in a splendid 18C edifice surrounded by grounds, which was once the holiday home of the bishops of Lyon. The inventive food is the consummate work of a chef who has had a Michelin star since 1993 and who became a MOF in 1997. Top quality regional produce, surgically precise craftsmanship in a classical vein and the occasional more modern technique depict the culinary ethos. This welcoming scene provides the backdrop to dishes such as a soup of frog’s legs with mushrooms and wild garlic, Grenoble-style arctic char, slowly baked in its juices, risotto of soft wheat and beurre noisette.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3160;Il Cortile;France;Mulhouse;11 rue des Franciscains, Mulhouse, 68100, France;47.7474759;7.3340648;70;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;In a pedestrian street in the old part of Mulhouse, welcome to this 16C establishment, whose reputation is firmly cemented among the locals. Since 2001, chef Jean-Michel Feger has been devising Mediterranean-inspired cuisine. Think mouth-watering, technically on point modern dishes with a lilting Italian accent: vitello tonnato, sun-dried tomato pesto, buffalo-milk mozzarella fritters. In fine weather, soak up la dolce vita and enjoy your meal alfresco on the patio in the small courtyard. Pleasant and relaxed service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3162;Sushi Yoshinaga;France;Paris;27 rue du 4-Septembre, Paris, 75002, France;48.8698375;2.3349558;94;true;false;Japanese;This exceptional restaurant has left nothing to chance: ceramics designed by a Japanese artist, rosewood chopsticks set out on a small cedar tray, maple wood panelling and soft lighting. Sushi master Tomoyuki Yoshinaga crafts a feast of outstanding fish, including different varieties of fatty tuna, which he surgically prepares and seasons – all for the benefit of no more than 10 diners at a time. This culinary performance of high-flying precision covers textures, maturations, serving temperatures and a vast array of flavours depending on the omakase menu. We also noticed and applauded more personal recipes and techniques, particularly the house marinades and soy sauces and the subtle selection of warm dishes served at the start of the meal. The final cherry on the cake is the tandem formed by the chef and his maitre d’ which is so seamless and smooth as to be almost invisible, if it weren’t for the duo’s manifest complicity and shared sense of humour.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
3164;Le Chamarlenc;France;Puy-en-Velay;19 rue Raphaël, Puy-en-Velay, 43000, France;45.0442309;3.8828324;55;false;true;Creative;This institution lives on under the stewardship of a young couple who came here from La Mirande (Avignon): chef Yoan Delorme and head waiter Cellia Baudelier. The chef dreams up tasty, precise and imaginative dishes, such as tartlet in the style of a pissaladière with its anchovy pieces, bacon and onion mousse, and a fresh salad of green beans, chard, chervil, tarragon and coriander, or pig's knuckle and a salad of grilled corn with lemon, fermented mustard seeds, preserved lemon paste and creamy polenta. This is of course a success story that goes hand in hand with respect for the seasons and an affinity with the best producers, both locally and beyond (the fish comes from the Mediterranean).;Terrace;[]
3167;Le Cin5 - Au Cœur du Village;France;La Clusaz;26 montée du Château, La Clusaz, 74220, France;45.90452;6.42312;50;false;true;Creative;Vincent Deforce is a fan of the island of Mauritius, from whence he brings back ideas, ingredients and spices that he cleverly mixes with Savoie produce, creating inventive, attractive dishes. Rich in colour, Savoie saffron rubs shoulders with island chilis, marlin and octopus are mixed with sarrazin crozets (local pasta) and zander from Lake Geneva, without forgetting the delicious tartiflette of sweet potatoes and slow-roasted pork – unforgettable!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3168;Loiseau des Ducs;France;Dijon;3 rue Vauban, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3208798;5.0412341;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Housed in the 16C Hôtel de Talmay, a listed historical monument close to the Palais des Ducs, this restaurant is part of the Loiseau Group. The chef continues to perpetuate Burgundian cuisine and the Bernard Loiseau classics, albeit with a more modernist edge, in dishes such as the revisited œuf en meurette with a hay-smoked confit egg yolk, or Burgundy escargots with herbs from around Dijon. A fine selection of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3169;Fontevraud L'Ermitage;France;Fontevraud-l'Abbaye;38 rue Saint-Jean-de-l'Habit, Fontevraud-l'Abbaye, 49590, France;47.1797597;0.0524964;77;true;true;Creative;Saint Lazare Priory is located in the heart of Fontevraud Abbey, one of Europe’s largest monastic complexes. The former’s cloisters have been morphed into a restaurant by designer Patrick Jouin and architect Sanjit Manku, who have staged a marriage between monastic minimalism and untreated materials to set the scene for Thibaut Ruggeri’s cooking. The latter, who hails from Megève and who won the Bocuse d’Or 2013, learnt the trade with iconic culinary names from Michel Guérard to Georges Blanc. A champion of good food and biodynamic farming, local produce takes pride of place (Racan poultry, Anjou pigeon) in a menu that keeps pace with his garden’s production and the moon.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3170;Le Clair de la Plume;France;Grignan;2 place du Mail, Grignan, 26230, France;44.4195003;4.9071356;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Nestling at the foot of a château that is famous for having welcomed Madame de Sévigné as a regular patron, this restaurant is the perfect embodiment of Provence's twin traditions of hospitality and good food: olive oil from Nyons, guinea fowl and diced vegetables from the Drôme are judiciously showcased by chef Benjamin Reilhes in the form of three tasting menus comprising several courses. One of the set menus draws entirely on plants. This restaurant is an ode to the Mediterranean's fine ingredients and Rhône Valley wines. Pastry chef Cédric Perret, meanwhile, creates desserts in harmony with the seasons, often setting them off with an original and striking flourish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3171;Auberge du Cep;France;Fleurie;11 rue des Quatre-Vents, Fleurie, 69820, France;46.1921358;4.6969883;72;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This emblematic Beaujolais establishment, made famous thanks to the talent of chef Chantal Chagny who spent 44 years in the kitchen here, needs no introduction whatsoever! Her successor, Aurélien Merot, is cut from the same cloth courtesy of cuisine that is both generous and delicate. He champions regional produce (zander from the river roasted in its skin, multicoloured carrots from Augustin’s garden and a punchy Beaujolais sauce), with a special focus on jus and sauces. Excellent value for money (the lunchtime menu is a bargain!) plus a fine selection of wines from the region.;Interesting wine list;[]
3172;Nakatani;France;Paris;27 rue Pierre-Leroux, Paris, 75007, France;48.8482237;2.3196445;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After a decade working with Hélène Darroze, Shinsuke Nakatani is at the helm of this elegant, restful restaurant, decked in soothing colours and natural materials. Thanks to his acute flair for seasoning, cooking and presentation, this ultra-talented Japanese chef concocts a pedigree French score in tune with the seasons, in which the flavours and textures are seamlessly combined to create a consistent whole. Guests can savour a single set menu (4 dishes at lunchtime, 6 in the evening and which changes every two months), served by a crack team that is as low-profile as it is professional. Given the limited number of seats (just 16), it is advisable to book ahead.;Air conditioning;[]
3173;Le Feuillée - Le Couvent des Minimes;France;Mane;Chemin des Jeux-de-Maï, Mane, 04300, France;43.9395915;5.7723757;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in deepest Provence, Mane is both picturesque and steeped in history, which is also true of the 17C Couvent des Minimes, whose admirable restoration has retained its period charm. This provençal Arcadia is home to a luxury hotel, with swimming pool, spa and a fine dining restaurant, named after Louis Feuillée, Louis XIV's botanist, who was born in the village. The kitchens are masterfully run by Louis Gachet, MOF 2023, who seamlessly navigates between his native Burgundy and Provence. Bold dishes and exquisite sauces exemplify the creative consummate culinary talent of this virtuoso chef.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3175;Le Puits du Trésor;France;Lastours;21 route des Quatre-Châteaux, Lastours, 11600, France;43.3346453;2.3787415;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Jean-Marc Boyer is a true craftsman, and his passion is unmistakable: he finds inspiration for his cooking during solitary walks in the surrounding hills. Aromatic herbs, wild asparagus and wild garlic are used to dress up his colourful dishes that are rife with clean, well-handled flavours, such as mackerel marinated in cucumber or monkfish with carrots and ricotta ravioli. He arranges everything into a single set menu, over the course of which the surprises keep coming. The interior, designed by Régis Dho in a Japanese vein, provides the perfect foil to the chef's pared-down culinary vision. A note for those who are pushed for time: this is a restaurant with a leisurely pace.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3177;Auberge de l'Abbaye;France;Ambronay;47 place des Anciens-Combattants, Ambronay, 01500, France;46.0070045;5.3605085;55;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located at the foot of the Benedictine Abbaye d'Ambronay, this contemporary place has been designed down to the very last detail by modern-minded owner Ivan Lavaux, who has put time and thought into the choice of materials and colours (including a specially created toile de Jouy!). He moves between the restaurant floor and the kitchen, showcasing the many selected wines from his cellar, as well as the premium ingredients he loves (asparagus, sea bass, lobster etc). Indulge in one of his tempting set menus, served at lunch and dinner.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3179;Le Farçon;France;Courchevel;Immeuble Kalinka, La Tania, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4315173;6.5938711;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away in a spruce forest, the resort of La Tania is so close to, and yet so far from Courchevel! Julien Machet’s restaurant pampers and nurtures his guests and nothing leaves his kitchen that hasn’t been endlessly pondered and preened over. This “Savoyard peddler” (his own words) has devised a gourmet banquet that engulfs you in the history of the Duchy of Savoy by way of the best produce from Savoy, the Val d’Aosta, Valais and Piedmont, as far as the Mediterranean. Seasonal vegetables (a nostalgic nod to his grandmother Mado’s vegetable patch) are also invited to play a star role in the gourmet action at an altitude of 1400 metres. Fine dining with our head in the clouds.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3180;Le P'tit Polyte;France;Les Deux-Alpes;Chalet Mounier, 2 rue de la Chapelle, Les Deux-Alpes, 38860, France;45.0036431;6.120844;61;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The hotel Chalet Mounier is a family affair. It began with Marie and Hippolyte Mounier, who opened this hotel – the first in the resort – in 1933. Then their son Robert took over in 1971, and today Alban and his partner Angélique are carrying on the legacy. The cosy little restaurant has an intimate atmosphere, in which you can enjoy an intelligently designed tasting menu with a strong emphasis on the vegetable component. The chef, who is particularly fond of citrus fruits, does a fine job of selecting the ingredients and presenting them beautifully on the plate. The wine list is excellent, with judicious recommendations from the sommelier. Le P'tit Polyte punches above its weight.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3184;Atmosphères;France;Le Bourget-du-Lac;618 route des Tournelles, Le Bourget-du-Lac, 73370, France;45.6606861;5.8522537;95;false;false;Creative;From Lamartine to Stendhal and Maupassant, many a French author has waxed lyrical about the atmosphere of Lac du Bourget and the view over Mt Revard. For his part, Chef Alain Perrillat-Mercerot has made the lake and mountains the splendid backdrop against which he serves his delicate, creative cuisine that fervently champions the Savoie terroir. Classically trained, his high-precision preparation of freshwater fish, local cheeses and wild blueberries is second to none – choose between two carefully composed single-choice set menus. The fantastic wine list fetes local grape varieties (among others).;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3185;Le Moulin de l'Abbaye;France;Brantôme;1 route de Bourdeilles, Brantôme, 24310, France;45.3631;0.6462835;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this picturesque village where visitors can journey from prehistory to the Renaissance, this restaurant enjoys a truly stunning setting at the base of a cliff. This outbuilding of the Benedictine abbey of Brantôme also features a splendid terrace on the banks of the River Dronne, facing the town’s 16C angled bridge. Here, the chef’s fine, flavoursome cuisine is ably supported by a cast of superb ingredients, perfect cooking techniques and meticulous presentation. All in all, a venerable property with a contemporary and timeless charm.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
3186;Côté Cuisine;France;Carnac;36 avenue Zacharie-Le-Rouzic, Carnac, 56340, France;47.5797015;-3.0786985;71;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Between the town and the beach, this hotel-restaurant is run with a flair for fine dining by a team of professionals who are passionate about what they do. As for the decor, the large contemporary-style space keeps things simple with its waxed concrete floor, partially open kitchen and shelves filled with cookery books. Having trained at Le Bristol and at Taillevent, the pair at the helm deliver a subtle range of dishes that are replete with flavours, beautifully showcasing impeccable regional produce – at very attractive prices. Tuck in by the fireplace in winter, or on the pleasant terrace in fine weather.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3187;Le Duèze - Château de Mercuès;France;Mercuès;Route du Château, Mercuès, 46090, France;44.4963194;1.3947504;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Clinging to a hilltop overlooking the Lot valley, this superb medieval castle, altered countless times, has gracefully weathered the centuries. Having relinquished its position as a seat of episcopal power, it now boasts luxurious guestrooms and a fine dining restaurant definitely in tune with its era. The gutsy culinary repertory pays tribute to the terroir of the Lot with a host of up-to-date spins. Even better when washed down with one of the estate’s excellent wines, and, in fine weather, seated at a table set in the main courtyard.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3190;Ô Saveurs;France;Rouffiac-Tolosan;8 place des Ormeaux, Rouffiac-Tolosan, 31180, France;43.664;1.524975;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a picturesque hamlet a short drive from Toulouse, David Biasibetti elegantly exalts local produce, whilst boldly enriching his culinary palette with flavours from further afield: duck breast, beetroot and acidic cherries or pollock, coconut and vanilla stock and aubergine caviar with black curry… The know-how of this veteran craftsman can immediately be tasted, including in his decadent chocolate desserts – however, you should know that he did train as a pastry chef and makes no secret of his love of cocoa beans. One thing is certain – savour and flavour await you here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3192;Ezia;France;Montlivault;17 rue de Chambord, Montlivault, 41350, France;47.641088;1.4452295;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Nicolas Aubry, previously Christophe Hay's executive chef, has now taken over the reins of his mentor's restaurant. The decor has not been changed and it is a pleasure to be back in this modern space with a view into the kitchen. Organised into single set menus that take their cue from the seasons and from produce sourced in the Loire region, the finely crafted dishes are expressions of his delicate cuisine, which may be subtle but has bags of personality.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3193;Restaurant Hervé Busset;France;Rodez;24 place du Bourg, Rodez, 12000, France;44.3484736;2.5758132;100;false;false;Modern Cuisine;From Conques to Rodez, where he relocated when he took over Émilie and Thomas Roussey's restaurant, chef Hervé Busset continues to present himself as a cook and harvester. The produce he gathers from the surrounding fields and forests is supplemented by purchases from the market opposite his new premises. Hervé's creative cuisine is dictated by nature: comfrey, marigold, hedge nettle, meadowsweet and nasturtium flowers grace the plates with harmony and finesse throughout the surprise set menu. Completely refurbished, the chic, inviting setting ensures privacy for guests. The sommelier has excellent recommendations.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3194;La Bastide Bourrelly - Mathias Dandine;France;Cabriès;Place Albert-Florens, Cabriès, 13480, France;43.4610152;5.3534389;70;false;true;Provençal;Chef Mathias Dandine (one Michelin star at La Magdeleine) fell in love with this old Provençal farmhouse (or bastide) in the village centre. Whether you are dining outside on the terrace shaded by plane trees, or in the elegant, contemporary space done out in Mediterranean style, you are served Provençal cuisine inspired by the famous cookery book of chef Jean-Baptiste Reboul (1897). Top-notch local ingredients are fresh and seasonal, meticulously cooked to perfection, with tasty sauces and precise seasonings: chef Guillaume Lemelle regales us, for example, with grilled yellowtail, fried artichoke with preserved lemon, artichoke agnolotti, and a barigoule jus with olive oil. Guestrooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3195;Auberge de la Mine;France;La Ferrière-aux-Étangs;8 rue de Champsecret, La Ferrière-aux-Étangs, 61450, France;48.6468685;-0.5220022;100;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Formerly the canteen of the local iron ore mine (closed in April 1970), this inn has been the haunt of the same chef for over 30 years. Trained classically, his watchword is simplicity and his food is the epitome of straightforward authenticity, albeit with flawless technique and inspired creativity. Examples include a knockout combination of foie gras, sparkling pear wine jelly and a spicy apple and pear chutney – culinary bliss! This enticing seasonal score is served in two stylishly sleek dining rooms that manage to avoid the stuffy formality that can be characteristic of such places… What a treat to go down the mine!;Car park;[]
3197;La Table de la Bergerie;France;Bellevigne-en-Layon;3 route de la Pierre, Bellevigne-en-Layon, 49380, France;47.26803;-0.59238;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant near Angers, in the heart of the Coteaux-du-Layon vineyards, is well worth your attention. It is the haunt of talented David Guitton, who hails from Loire Atlantique and who has trained under top chefs all over the world from the United States and Britain to Monaco. There is no à la carte menu here, but a voluntarily concise offering that reverently respects the seasons. David sources his ingredients from small, local producers, rustling up dishes that err towards minimalist so that the flavour can take centre stage. Regional wines, including the estate’s organic production, take pride of place on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3198;Datil;France;Paris;13 rue des Gravilliers, Paris, 75003, France;48.8636089;2.3572627;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Manon Fleury notched up a number of experiences in prestigious kitchens (with chefs such as William Ledeuil, Pascal Barbot and Alexandre Couillon) and short-term chef residencies before opening her own restaurant. Her culinary philosophy, based on a respect for nature and human dignity, a championing of short supply chains (sourcing carefully and locally) and a zero-waste policy, stems from a genuine passion for sustainable fine dining. Dishes are primarily plant-based (fruit and vegetables feature in equal measure), with animal protein used sparingly. Her refined cooking style reveals all the aromatic subtleties and complexities of grains in particular (she has written a book on the subject) but also of fruits, in a subtle exploration of their sweet and sour flavours. A decor of waxed concrete floors, velvet banquette, light oak dining chairs. Booking essential.;;[]
3199;Géosmine;France;Paris;71 rue de la Folie-Méricourt, Paris, 75011, France;48.8655091;2.3705908;62;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Geosmin is the wonderful aroma that rises from freshly ploughed or wet soil. Maxime Bouttier's restaurant, in the Oberkampf area of Paris, is located in a two-storey townhouse that has the distinctive feel and decor of the eastern districts of Paris. Hailing from France's Sarthe département, this young chef organises his distinctive, pared-back dishes into a tasting menu that follows the seasons and steers clear of the trap of over-complexity. The wine list will certainly pique your interest with its natural and biodynamic wines, as well as fine Italian, Spanish and Austrian labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3201;La Verrière;France;Olmeto;Hôtel Marinca, lieu-dit Vitricella, Olmeto, 20113, France;41.6913523;8.9026942;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Romain Masset proposes high-precision cuisine that shines a spotlight on Corsica, while also embracing flashes of creativity and the occasional obligatory foray into mushrooms, which he has revered since his years with Jacques and Régis Marcon. His set menus, with their enticing titles, take diners on a veritable tasting tour of olive oil, langoustines, shellfish, red mullet and suckling lamb – all carefully selected ingredients, prepared with finesse and intelligence. As for the setting, it is idyllic, with an unforgettable view of the Gulf of Valinco and Propriano from the terrace.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
3203;Baumanière 1850;France;Courchevel;Le Strato, Route de Bellecôte, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4102934;6.6380783;48;true;true;Creative;Courchevel, the quintessence of Alpine luxury since 1947, is an exclusive ski resort where nothing is too grand or too posh! In this plush, stylish chalet, talented chef Thomas Prod'homme, who trained at L'Oustau de Baumanière in Les Baux-de-Provence, elegantly slaloms between local ingredients, winter flavours and Provençal inspirations. Guided by his memories and personal tastes, he produces high-precision cuisine and does not shy away from presenting bold flavours or comforting, indulgent fare. You can also sense that the chef likes to have fun with his cooking, taking pleasure in the element of surprise and provoking a reaction with playful dishes… that first and foremost hit the mark – and that goes for the impressive desserts, too. Creativity, ambition, risk-taking: the results speak for themselves.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3205;Le Goût du Bonheur - La Fenière;France;Cadenet;1680 route de Lourmarin, Cadenet, 84160, France;43.7487002;5.3642746;55;false;false;Creative, Farm to table;Nadia Sammut is committed to "building a better-tasting world". Gluten, refined white sugar and milk have been banished from her kitchen, in favour of an impressive move towards different types of flour (eg chickpea, split pea and rice flours) and fructose. Her vision is also reflected in the original and bold tasting menu, which has a particular focus on vegetables and draws on the history of the region and Nadia's family. Her partner Ernest, who is passionate about wine, selects and matures fish slaughtered according to the ikejime method. The vegetable garden also has its part to play in creating healthy and natural Southern French cuisine that looks to the future and the Grand Luberon for inspiration.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3206;Les Voiles d'Or;France;Dieppe;2 chemin de la Falaise, à Neuville-lès-Dieppe, Dieppe, 76200, France;49.9320387;1.0893938;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;Thanks to his wealth of experience, Tristan Arhan's restaurant perched atop the cliffs of Le Pollet (looking out over Dieppe) hits all the right notes. For this chef who is passionate about seafood (and works alone in his kitchen!), it is the catch of the day that sets the agenda. Diners can look forward to exceptionally fresh produce showcased with understated finesse. The sleek and pared-down decor is perfectly in sync with the chef's approach. There are a small terrace for sunny days.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3207;Auberge de la Charme;France;Prenois;12 rue de la Charme, Prenois, 21370, France;47.3758124;4.8989819;61;true;true;Creative;In a small Burgundy village, close to the racetrack, this place is both rustic and pared down in terms of its style: exposed stone walls, exposed ceiling beams, a flagstone floor and an old bread oven set into a wall. The restaurant is run by a pair of chefs, Nicolas Isnard and David Le Comte, who met in Gilles Goujon's restaurant in Fontjoncouse. They share the same passion for fine dining and Asia, the reaches of which they regularly explore. They propose a carte blanche menu, the concept of which may be disconcerting, but it works a treat: just let yourself be transported by this creative, generous and multi-influenced cuisine, inspired by the travels of these two globetrotters.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3208;L'Esquisse;France;Annecy;21 rue Royale, Annecy, 74000, France;45.89973;6.12235;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The former second-in-command to Laurent Petit at Le Clos des Sens in Annecy-le-Vieux, Stéphane Dattrino has branched off on his own to create this attractive restaurant. Behind its discreet façade, tables for two predominate and despite its deliberately relaxed feel, the service here is very much on the mark. The chef’s strong imprint is clearly evident in cuisine that is rich in flavour and colour, with a seasonal palette that incorporates high-quality local ingredients including plants and vegetables (wild garlic, wild asparagus etc). Delicious dishes full of finesse include the duxelle de champignons tart with cep pastry, and crispy calf’s sweetbreads with a squash medley.;Air conditioning;[]
3209;Pierre Reboul;France;Aix-en-Provence;Château de la Pioline, 260 rue Guillaume-du-Vair, Aix-en-Provence, 13290, France;43.5084768;5.4047211;29;true;false;Creative;Pierre Reboul has travelled far and wide. He was Michel Chabran's apprentice in Pont-de-l'Isère, then a member of the team under the great Jacques Pic (Anne-Sophie Pic's father) in Valence, before cooking in Paris at Taillevent and Rostang, and ultimately opening his own restaurants in Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, Tain-l'Hermitage and Aix-en-Provence. His playful, creative, slightly molecular style of cuisine comes into its own in the elegant setting of this 16C château. Texture, inventiveness, respect for seasonality (permaculture vegetables and sustainable fishing): he ensures the fundamentals are observed.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3210;Le Prieuré;France;Ambierle;11 rue de la Mairie, Ambierle, 42820, France;46.1039302;3.8962412;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the centre of a winegrowing village on the Côte Roannaise, this restaurant adjoins a magnificent 15C Benedictine priory with a multi-coloured varnished tile roof done out in typical Burgundian style. The restaurant is housed in an attractive traditional granite building. Chef Thierry Fernandes, who hails from the area (as does his wife, who runs proceedings front of house), creates fine cuisine based on classic principles, with the flavours of local ingredients evident in every dish.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3212;Maximin Hellio;France;Deauville;64 rue Gambetta, Deauville, 14800, France;49.3592817;0.0770849;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the seaside resort of Deauville, this restaurant with a sleek, modern frontage had the great idea of leaving part of the façade glass-fronted so as to enable passers-by to watch the chefs at work. Inside, seasoned chef Maximin Hellio offers up three tasting menus, including one that homes in on ingredients from the land and another ingredients from the sea (choose during the online booking process). In the latter, he pays tribute to the full bounty of Normandy, in refined and creative dishes, for example showcasing a new – seafood-based – take on a pithiviers. Interesting food and wine pairings presented on a tablet. The establishment is very popular with locals.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3213;Nicolas Carro - Hôtel de Carantec;France;Carantec;20 rue du Kelenn, Carantec, 29660, France;48.6706639;-3.9127356;15;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;After a successful stint at La Table d'Olivier Nasti in Kaysersberg, Nicolas Carro decided to return to his native Brittany (he is originally from Loudéac). He took over this iconic restaurant in Finistère, formerly run by chef Patrick Jeffroy. While admiring the magnificent view over the Bay of Morlaix, diners can fully appreciate the quality of the food. The menu celebrates local produce, both from the sea (shellfish and small boat fishing) and the land (vegetables and meat such as guinea fowl and lamb from Monts d'Arrée). Expect delicate, refined dishes with pleasantly contrasting textures and that are flawlessly prepared and seasoned... This cuisine that reflects the talent of the chef hits the spot every time.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
3214;Les Genêts;France;Brem-sur-Mer;21 bis rue de l'Océan, Brem-sur-Mer, 85470, France;46.605894;-1.8350415;70;false;false;Creative;This fashionably refurbished country house, which lies a few miles from Sables d’Olonne, is now the haunt of a talented couple, Nicolas and Amélie Coutand. The chef spent time at Troisgros in Roanne and L’Amphitryon in Lorient, among others. An advocate of fresh, seasonal produce, his approach is creative, joyful and flavoursome and regional ingredients, be they noble or less so, such as sardine, mackerel and hake, take pride of place in his menus. A huge 1400m² cottage garden adds a veggie flourish to his light, delicate dishes at prices that make sense.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3215;La Rotonde des Trésoms;France;Annecy;Les Trésoms, 15 boulevard de la Corniche, Annecy, 74000, France;45.8896367;6.1366994;93;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The huge conservatory of this Rotonde commands a splendid panoramic view over Annecy Lake, sweeping diners off their feet, even before their first bite! Originally from Arcachon, Eric Prowalski adds flavours from southwest France to recipes which highlight sustainably grown local produce. This skilled craftsman deftly unfolds a repertory in which creativity never hampers the flavour, developing a delicious "dialogue" between his adopted land and his homeland. The understated interior showcases a subtle blend of warm materials such as leather and oak.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3216;Maison Tiegezh;France;Guer;7 place de la Gare, Guer, 56380, France;47.9056281;-2.1235452;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tiegezh means "family" in Breton, which does rather say it all! The chef’s grandparents founded Brittany’s first factory to manufacture fresh pancakes. Today, Baptiste Denieul, a gifted young chef who honed his skills at the Bristol with Éric Frechon, invites you to enter this stylish interior, which provides the perfect foil to his delicate, bang on cuisine: fish, vegetables from the garden and farm produce. His wife Marion puts the final touch to this family melody. Nowadays, Maison Tiegezh boasts a gourmet restaurant, a bistro and also a modern, sophisticated hotel with six rooms for overnight stays and longer… A delightful break in the heart of Brittany’s enchanted forest of Broceliande.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3217;Jean-Marc Pérochon;France;Bretignolles-sur-Mer;63 avenue de la Grande-Roche, Bretignolles-sur-Mer, 85470, France;46.61923;-1.87165;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Seated behind the restaurant’s floor to ceiling windows, admire the sun’s rays glinting on the ocean. A talented skipper has dropped anchor here in the person of Jean-Marc Pérochon who went to sea at 17, crossing the channel to Scotland, before cruising around Europe and as far as the West Indies. In his hotel-restaurant, his cooking is both minimalist and sprinkled with exotic flavours, extractions, stocks and emulsions, leaving our tastebuds aching for more. He believes in working only with first-rate goods, namely fish and shellfish from the fish auction at Saint-Gilles-Croix-de-Vie (which dominate the menu), but also Challans poultry and vegetables from local growers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3219;L'Hirondelle - Château de Collias;France;Collias;8 bis chemin du Barry, Collias, 30210, France;43.9532821;4.4767976;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This pale stone château is home to a fine dining restaurant (open evenings Thu-Mon) that gives pride of place to ingredients from the South of France, particularly the Mediterranean, crafted with talent. The "Bougainvillier" in the castle’s former dining rooms serves a bistronomic set menu. The owners extend a warm, authentic welcome.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3222;Ōrtensia;France;Paris;4 rue Beethoven, Paris, 75016, France;48.8584133;2.2875568;16;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Most good food buffs agree that Japanese chefs can be relied on to produce truly outstanding French cuisine. At Ōrtensia, the Gallic menu is sprinkled with just the right dose of Japanese accents (daikon radish and yuzu emulsion with spider crab, or a hen-of-the-woods mushroom tempura with john dory). Just like the flower after which it is named (hydrangea in English), the cuisine changes colour with the seasons and weather. A contemporary, minimalist vibe depicts the interior, in which light neutral shades and wood dominate, while mirrors on the walls create a feeling of space. Online bookings only.;Air conditioning;[]
3223;La Coopérative - Domaine Riberach;France;Bélesta;2 route de Caladroy, Bélesta, 66720, France;42.7181258;2.6073514;33;false;true;Creative;Cet ancien chai a conservé sa charpente métallique : l'endroit, très spacieux et confortable, a un charme fou ! La cuisine suit de très près les saisons et s'appuie sur les petits producteurs des environs. Des préparations fines et inventives qui s'arrosent bien entendu des vins du domaine, produits sans intrants en agro-écologie. Agréables chambres pour l'étape.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3225;de:ja;France;Strasbourg;1 rue Schimper, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5873652;7.7685673;61;false;false;Creative;The Scandi-inspired decor hints at the culinary ethos: creativity, extractions, fermentations, plants to the fore, a concern for animal welfare, a natural wine list and haikus instead of the titles of dishes. The textbook technique features precise cooking times, intensely flavoured sauces and jus, and bold combinations that work well. Online bookings only.;Air conditioning;[]
3226;L'Impulsif;France;Châtel-Guyon;19 avenue Baraduc, Châtel-Guyon, 63140, France;45.9196471;3.0660287;83;false;true;Creative;Established on the ground floor of a Belle Époque edifice, chef Rémi Laroque rustles up modern, distinctly globe-trotting food. This Puy-de-Dôme lad with Vietnamese origins scatters his cooking with numerous Asian, particularly Japanese twists. His wholehearted culinary dedication shines through, particularly in the line-up of dishes around a single ingredient (be it lobster or fennel) that fully embody his spot-on knack for pairing. His medallion of monkfish, flanked by fennel, lovage oil and coconut cream, showcases his delicate craftsmanship. Street art on the walls, unusual tableware and amazing plant sculptures set the scene.;;[]
3227;Intuition;France;Saint-Lô;1 rue Alsace-Lorraine, Saint-Lô, 50000, France;49.1144055;-1.0985834;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Make your way upstairs from the Brasserie les Capucines, which serves simpler fare, to this understated, plush restaurant overlooking the castle of Saint Lô. After acquiring a faithful following of regulars in Coutances, Mickaël Marion has returned to his birthplace and opened the floodgates of his creativity. A steadfast champion of local produce, he frequently goes walking in the countryside and marshes to pick plants and herbs. Back in his kitchen, he waves his magic wand/spoon and lo and behold - meadowsweet ice cream, pesto of wild herbs and lovage appear! He is a past master in the art of subtly assembling stellar Normandy produce – scallops, fish from small boats, with a dash of exoticism. A fine dining experience to remember.;;[]
3229;Apicius;France;Paris;20 rue d'Artois, Paris, 75008, France;48.8732881;2.3072835;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a sumptuous 18C private mansion that calls to mind a small palace, Apicius is named after this Ancient Roman epicurean who is said to have written the first cookbook. Chef Mathieu Pacaud is keeping the flame alive at this legendary place with a magnificent terrace that amounts to a remarkably bucolic garden in the city. The dishes perpetuate fine bourgeois tradition and achieve a synthesis between classicism and creativity. Time passes, Apicius changes… but remains!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3230;Le 1201 - Abbaye de Villeneuve;France;Les Sorinières;Lieu-dit Villeneuve, Les Sorinières, 44840, France;47.1232859;-1.5338567;74;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The fine dining restaurant of this charming hotel sports two plush, stylish dining rooms. You will sample a polished, appetising score in the zeitgeist, which demonstrates a distinct regional slant and showcases the chef’s craftsmanship, particularly in the realm of sauces and jus. The impressive wine list starts at very reasonable prices and features a fine selection of regional tipples. Cheerful service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3231;Le Saint Hilaire;France;Saint-Hilaire-de-Brethmas;5 rue André-Schenk, Saint-Hilaire-de-Brethmas, 30560, France;44.0991009;4.1055495;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Sébastien Rath (formerly of le Riche in Alès) and his spouse Gwladys are even closer to the Cévennes (whose wild herbs the chef adores) since they moved to this old inn with a garden terrace and a lovely, light dining room decorated in soft colours. The chef’s love of local produce has not wavered, depicted by the ingredients (monkfish from small fishing boats of Grau-du-Roi, veal from Aveyron and fruit from the surrounding orchards), the cutlery on the tables and even the jeans manufactured in Lozère for his team. The chef’s two blind menus reveal a seasonal inspiration, which echoes the couple’s sincerity and steadfast commitment to their region, illustrated by monkfish, aubergines, miso seasoning and lemon sauce.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3232;Maison Dubois;France;Paris;2 rue de Vienne, Paris, 75008, France;48.8762472;2.321206;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The house spirit reigns supreme in this intimate fine dining restaurant with six tables and a confidential feel. Suffice to say, chef Arthur Dubois – who has clocked up experience in the restaurants of Jacques Maximin, Éric Frechon and Pierre Gagnaire, where he was sous-chef for several years – is in the business of the bespoke. Carefully selected ingredients, tried and tested know-how, impeccable technique: the chef is a dab hand at putting a new spin on classic cuisine. Indeed, the influence of his mentor on rue Balzac makes itself felt in his penchant for "satellite" variations on a theme, as seen in his langoustines "with three flavours" in a buttermilk sauce, or the red mullet with fresh seaweed and rockfish jus with foie gras.;Air conditioning;[]
3233;Hémicycle;France;Paris;5 rue de Bourgogne, Paris, 75007, France;48.8600034;2.3182962;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, whose name is a nod to the nearby Assemblée Nationale, sports a minimalist interior that mixes marble, 1970’s furnishings and Lalique light fittings. The savoury score is the work of Italian chef Flavio Lucarini (from Bistrot Flaubert and Jérôme Banctel’s Gabriel), while Aurora Storari (former head pastry chef at Le Clarence) is in charge of desserts. The chef's cuisine is certainly Gallic, but personal and subtly Italian thanks to acidic, bitter notes, as in the watercress risotto and squid alla Luciana with black lemon powder, or pigeon, cherry kosho, the leg as a tempura, crispy aubergine raviolo. Aurora’s creative desserts demonstrate bags of personality, illustrated by plum confit with hibiscus and sesame crème brûlée.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3235;Calice;France;Béziers;30 boulevard Bertrand-Duguesclin, Béziers, 34500, France;43.3435711;3.2232426;21;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in an Art Deco building with a modern extension: a successful makeover abounding with curving floral forms, with a round dining space done out in soft, natural and organically shaped materials. The chef delivers a modern take on Mediterranean cuisine that pays homage to quality ingredients and conjures up well-defined flavours on the plate. Remarkably warm, attentive and competent service. The menu is constantly evolving in line with the seasons and the markets. The wine list boasts more than 800 labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3236;The Legacy House;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;5F, Rosewood Hotel, 18 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2950422;114.1757655;68;false;false;Shun Tak;This restaurant pays homage to the hotel’s founding patriarch. A variety of Shun Tak dishes – such as minced fish soup and pan-fried fish head – are served, to a backdrop of breathtaking harbour views and modern Chinese décor. It also supports the local economy by ordering ingredients and cookware from local fishermen, artisans and farms directly. A dress code applies for dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3237;Zuicho;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, The Mercer Central, 29 Jervois Street, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.285076;114.15209;97;true;false;Japanese;The head chef worked in some revered establishments in Tokyo for years and all ingredients are shipped from Japan. The highlight is the Satsuma beef fillet with confit egg yolk – the beef melts in your mouth while the egg yolk imparts silky richness. You may order omakase or tasting menu at lunch, but only one omakase Kappo menu that changes monthly is served at dinner. Seats are limited and reservations are mandatory.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3238;Ryota Kappou Modern;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;21F,  18 On Lan Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2806182;114.156779;72;false;false;Japanese;Floor-to-ceiling windows let in natural light and allow expansive views, while designer furniture and artisan tableware exude style. Only a kappo-style set menu is offered and the courses feature the best ingredients in season. The chef’s favourite Omi Wagyu katsu with black truffle and egg confit was inspired by sukiyaki and its flavours are in perfect harmony. The dinner set menu also includes an array of sake distributed by the restaurant itself.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
3239;Louise;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;PMQ, 35 Aberdeen Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2834752;114.1522258;83;false;true;French Contemporary;Chef Julien Royer, of Odette in Singapore fame, opened this restaurant which is decorated in a 1930s colonial style. Start with a drink at the bar downstairs before heading to the dining room for the chef’s delicate creations crafted with quality produce. Must-tries include pâté en croûte Louise with melt-in-the-mouth pastry and a moist filling, and pigeon breast with duck foie gras. Roasted Hong Kong yellow chicken is great for sharing. Ask the sommelier about wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3240;Five Foot Road;;Macau;GF, MGM Cotai, Avenida da Nave Desportiva, Cotai, Macau;22.1457276;113.5680458;20;false;true;Sichuan;The experienced head chef leads a team of Sichuan natives who display their meticulous skills in painstakingly-made dishes. They excel in using various Sichuan spices to complement each ingredient’s character to deliver a diverse range of taste profiles. The perfumed oil used in Sichuan boil dishes, for instance, is made from a complex mix of spices for the right balance between numbing heat and umami. Try pan-fried tofu with minced chicken, marinated abalone, and wok-fried crab.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3241;Zi Yat Heen;;Macau;GF, Four Seasons Hotel, Estrada da Baía de Nossa Senhora da Esperança, Cotai, Macau;22.15029;113.556615;40;false;true;Cantonese;This spacious, elegant yet intimate restaurant boasts a glass-clad wine cellar at its centre. The chef champions a cooking style with reduced amounts of seasoning so as to allow the true flavours of the first-rate ingredients to come through. Recommendations include barbecued pork, stir fried fish maw, crab meat with egg and egg white milk custard with sweetened mashed taro.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3242;Seventh Son (Wan Chai);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, The Wharney Hotel, 57-73 Lockhart Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2783246;114.1710507;34;false;false;Cantonese;The name refers to the owner – the seventh son who learned his culinary skills from his father from the age of 14. The must-try barbecue meats include roast suckling pig which is smoky and rich. The skills of the kitchen team are manifest in traditional dishes like deep-fried egg custard with chicken kidney, and steamed beef patty with dried tangerine peel. The smart room comes complete with teak floors, gold accents and warm lighting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3243;Sushi Saito;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;45F, Four Seasons Hotel, 8 Finance Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.286467;114.15677;95;true;false;Sushi;Supervised and managed by famed Chef Takashi Saito, the team masterfully crafts Edomae-style sushi using the best seasonal seafood. Rice from Akita and Nagano is cooked in spring water from Kagoshima and dressed in a special vinegar blend. But before you get to taste these divine creations at the cypress counter, you must first get a seat, which are always hard to come by – the reservation hotline only works during specific days and times.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3244;Liu Yuan Pavilion;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, The Broadway, 54-62 Lockhart Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2781199;114.1707918;93;true;false;Shanghainese;With its authentic Shanghainese cooking and Shanghainese-speaking clientele, it’s tempting to think you’re in Shanghai. The dining room impresses with understated elegance and the booth seats offering more privacy are especially prized. Specialities include drunken squab whose velvety meat and springy skin exude an intoxicating winey aroma. Stir-fried shrimps, braised pig knuckle and braised ‘lion head’ meatballs are also not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
3246;Belon;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1F, 1-5 Elgin Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2830193;114.1525511;68;true;true;French Contemporary;Belon moved to this spot in 2021, with a room that sports more drama and sophistication than its original Parisian bistro vibe. With Chef Kirkley at the helm, the menu offers popular dishes such as whole roasted chicken, alongside reimagined crowd-pleasers and novel creations. Dishes are rooted in French techniques and made with the best seasonal produce. Consider reserving the kitchen counter and prepay for the curated menu for four.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
3247;Gaddi's;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1F, The Peninsula Hotel, Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.294992;114.17179;63;false;false;French;This grand restaurant opened in 1953 and now occupies what was once The Peninsula’s ballroom – it even has its own dedicated entrance on Nathan Road. The well-versed team looks after the guests so well here you may find yourself loathed to leave. Top quality European and Japanese produce is well prepared in a modern French style. Dishes such as blue Brittany lobster with Romesco sauce are not to be missed. For those wanting something a little different, book the Chef’s Table in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3248;Mandarin Grill + Bar;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1F, Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 5 Connaught Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.2821483;114.1593485;48;false;true;European Contemporary, Grills;This stylish room designed by the late Sir Terence Conran features a glass-fronted kitchen and fan-shaped reliefs on the ceiling, reminiscent of the hotel’s logo. The well-verse team puts a new spin on steakhouse classics like steak tartare and house-smoked salmon. Quality meat cuts from the U.S., Australia and Japan are grilled to perfection and guests can choose a starter and a dessert from the menu on top of their mains to make it a set meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3249;Duddell's;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, 1 Duddell Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2801227;114.1572052;84;true;false;Cantonese;Duddell’s is as much about art as it is about food. It is the venue of regular art shows and screenings, as well as traditional Cantonese fare using luxury ingredients. Certain dishes need pre-ordering, such as the crispy skin chicken over which the chef ladles hot oil 300+ times to make the paper-thin skin crispy and the meat silky. Osmanthus scrambled eggs with bean sprouts, crabmeat and shrimp are fluffy and aromatic, imparting fine wok hei.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3250;Épure;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 403, 4F, Ocean Centre, Harbour City, 3-27 Canton Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2960349;114.1683295;56;false;false;French Contemporary;Have a drink on the patio before sampling a line-up that is French in essence but enhanced by subtle Japanese touches. The Singaporean chef honed his skills in top establishments around Europe and Asia. He ingeniously matches flavours and textures in precisely executed dishes that are not overly fancy. The two tasting menus are paired with carefully curated wines. The next-door cafe is a great spot for afternoon tea.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3251;Man Ho (Admiralty);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, JW Marriott Hotel, Pacific Place, 88 Queensway, Admiralty, Hong Kong;22.2776712;114.1659424;54;true;true;Cantonese;The sophisticated interior inspired by a Chinese garden features cascading glass chandeliers shaped like morning glory, marble moon gates and camellia enamel art. The young but seasoned head chef takes a creative approach to classics, such as Cantonese barbecue, dim sum and seafood. Try the fish soup with fish maw, shrimp cake and bamboo pith – the rich, flavoursome broth is made with three kinds of fish. Certain items need to be pre-ordered.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3252;Cristal Room by Anne-Sophie Pic;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;44F, Forty-Five, Gloucester Tower, Landmark, 15 Queen's Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.2811256;114.1576425;23;false;true;French Contemporary;In keeping with its moniker, literally, the opulent space seduces with sparkles, mirrored panels and jaw-dropping city views. The celebrity chef's second venture in Asia greets diners with an oversize crystal chandelier. The six- or eight-course tasting menu, consists of chef’s signature dishes, is deeply rooted in French traditions, with subtle Japanese twists in terms of produce and condiments – delicate and exciting at the same time.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3253;Yè Shanghai (Tsim Sha Tsui);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;702, 7F, K11 Musea, 18 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.294118;114.1741651;15;false;true;Shanghainese;It may have moved to a swanky mall in 2020, but this household name in Shanghainese food has been on the radar of gastronomes for over two decades. The room is spread across two floors with a modern take on 1930s Shanghai charm. Apart from drunken chicken, and stir-fried river shrimps, try also their cold appetiser sliced pork dressed in garlic sauce – the paper-thin pork is springy in texture, and its richness is balanced by garlic and soy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3254;Andō;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1F, Somptueux Central, 52-54 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2817911;114.1553834;23;true;true;Innovative;Born in Argentina but having honed his skills in Japan, chef-founder Agustin Balbi opened Andō to realise his culinary vision from his unique vantage point. In a minimalistic dining room boasting tasteful details and an open kitchen, his tasting menu takes diners on a personal journey by fusing his ancestral roots with strong Japanese influences. Don’t miss the signature Sin Lola, the caldoso rice – also a homage to his grandma.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3255;Yardbird;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;154-158 Wing Lok Street, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2869992;114.1492298;62;true;true;Yakitori;Yardbird is always jam-packed, so book online or expect to queue. The main draw is without doubt the 20-plus types of yakitori skewers made with local ‘three-yellow’ chicken from beak to tail, grilled over binchotan charcoal. Rare cuts like thyroid and ventricle can be hard to find elsewhere, as are the crispy meatballs with tare and egg yolk. Check out the extensive list of Japanese whisky.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
3256;Shang Palace;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Lower Level 1, Kowloon Shangri-La Hotel, 64 Mody Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.297325;114.177155;48;false;false;Cantonese;This elegant restaurant has been a reliable favourite for classic Cantonese food for over 35 years. Chandeliers and Sung-style paintings create an impressive backdrop for sophisticated cooking that has changed little over time. Signatures include sautéed sliced pigeon fillets with bamboo shoot, black fungus and asparagus, boasting tender meat and contrasting textures. To sample all the house specialities, opt for the chef's signature tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3257;Spring Moon;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1F, The Peninsula Hotel, Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.294943;114.17182;64;true;true;Cantonese;The room, spread over two levels, evokes old-Shanghai circa 1920s – stained glass windows, teak floors and rugs all speak of the golden era. On the menu, however, classics are showcased side by side with novel creations such as scrambled egg white with lobster and crabmeat, and dishes garnished with edible flowers that taste of spring. Dim sum at lunch is also recommended, to be enjoyed with your choice of tea from 30 varieties.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3258;8 1/2 Otto e Mezzo - Bombana;;Macau;Shop 1031, 1F, The Promenade, Galaxy, Avenida de Cotai, Cotai, Macau;22.1465088;113.5553965;99;false;false;Italian;Helmed by Sicilian chef, Riccardo La Perna, the award-winning Macao outpost offers the same exquisite fine-dining experience as its Hong Kong flagship. A single set tasting menu focuses on Sicilian cuisine – the appetisers awaken the tastebuds with ingenious food combinations, the hand-rolled pasta is simply divine and the hazelnut soufflé with a runny centre an exquisite surprise. Caring service befits the quality of the food.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3259;I M Teppanyaki & Wine;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1F, SL Ginza, 68 Electric Road, Tin Hau, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2841392;114.1918676;27;false;false;Teppanyaki;The founder and head chef Mok moved his restaurant to this location in 2021. As always, top notch ingredients like sea urchin, abalone and blue lobsters are flown in daily from Japan and France. But the theatrical cooking now happens in a much bigger room, along with a private room that seats eight. The wine list also sees a lot more choices. Amadai with sea urchin cream sauce stands out in particular, with its crispy scales and juicy flesh.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3260;Fu Ho;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 402, 4F, FoodLoft, Mira Place One, 132 Nathan Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.3006247;114.1720828;55;true;false;Cantonese;Thanks to his considerable experience, the head chef has been enticing diners back here for over a decade with his skillfully executed dishes, such as pan-fried chicken with ginger and scallion, fried Chinese kale with dried plaice, and stir-fried rice in Fu Ho style. Named after the owner, the signature Ah Yung abalone is slow-braised in a secret sauce for up to 20 hours. The dining room now has a contemporary, elegant and relaxing feel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3261;Tosca di Angelo;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;102F, The Ritz-Carlton, International Commerce Centre, 1 Austin Road West, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3032095;114.1599308;23;true;true;Italian;The Sicilian chef champions dishes that may look deceptively unfussy on the plate, but their obvious refinement makes them especially delicious. His signatures include house-made pasta and blue lobster dishes, while his modern take on rum babà is quite something. The set menu comprises seasonal and signature dishes, making it the best way to sample all specialities. Did I mention its sweeping views from the 102nd floor?;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3262;Loaf On;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;49 See Cheung Street, Sai Kung, Hong Kong;22.379858;114.27188;90;true;false;Seafood;It may not boast fancy displays of seafood like its promenade rivals, but this restaurant still stands out because of its cooking. Wonderfully fresh seafood is prepared using traditional home recipes that let the quality of the ingredients speak for themselves. Must-try dishes include pumpkin soup with minced fish, mantis shrimp with chilli and garlic, and steamed fish with sea salt. Ask about the seafood that needs pre-ordering when booking a table.;Air conditioning;[]
3263;Kam's Roast Goose;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, Po Wah Commercial Center, 226 Hennessy Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2777963;114.1755582;53;true;true;Cantonese Roast Meats;For over 70 years, the Kams have been famous for their roast goose and this shop was opened by the third generation. But the goose extravaganza doesn’t stop at their juicy roast goose with crispy skin. Try also their silky, melty goose blood pudding or the decadent blanched noodles tossed in goose fat. Other Cantonese barbecue dishes glistening in the window are also worth trying. With only 30 seats, don’t be surprised to see a queue.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3264;Imperial Treasure Fine Chinese Cuisine (Tsim Sha Tsui);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;10F, One Peking, 1 Peking Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.296177;114.170006;19;true;true;Cantonese;Finding success in Singapore and Shanghai, Imperial Treasure opened its first Hong Kong branch in this sky-scrapping landmark, with panoramic views of the harbour. The stylish dining room is embellished with subtle Chinese touches, such as the ceramic Koi carps and calligraphy. A fish tank in the kitchen ensures live seafood is available every day. Poached garoupa in fish soup with crispy rice and stir fried crab in pepper are worth a try.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
3265;Summer Palace;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;5F, Island Shangri-La Hotel, Pacific Place, Supreme Court Road, Admiralty, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2770061;114.1644721;52;true;false;Cantonese;This long-standing name has long been synonymous with quality food, so it’s hard to get a table, especially at lunch. The room exudes a timeless grace with décor inspired by the palace in Beijing. The menu is a roll-call of Cantonese classics – don’t miss their double-boiled soups and dim sum. Besides signatures like braised pig’s trotters with sand ginger, and braised Yoshihama abalone in oyster sauce, also ask about their seasonal offerings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3266;Lai Heen;;Macau;51F, The Ritz-Carlton, Galaxy, Estrada da Baía de Nossa Senhora da Esperança, Cotai, Macau;22.1464658;113.5547147;77;true;true;Cantonese;If you’re looking to impress, you can’t fail with this Cantonese restaurant atop a skyscraping hotel. The stunningly ornate room is supremely comfortable, as are the private rooms that can be joined into one big one. Chef Ho has years of experience and his tasty creations boast a modern aesthetic, a match for the sumptuous surroundings. Try their double-boiled soups, honey-glazed Iberico char siu, and Australian veal with ginger and scallion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3267;Whey;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;UG Level, The Wellington, 198 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2850438;114.1529127;28;true;true;Asian Contemporary;Championing a zero-waste philosophy and committed to local, sustainable sources, Whey serves a tasting menu comprising modern European dishes with influences from the head chef's native Singapore. Recipes are also informed by his travels and experience working in Asia, Australia and Europe, as well as his childhood memories. Highlights include brioche with buah keluak emulsion, and Maoshan Wang durian ice cream with Cristal caviar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3268;Ming Court (Mong Kok);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;6F, Cordis Hotel, 555 Shanghai Street, Mong Kok, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.318314;114.16933;48;true;false;Cantonese;Diners are greeted at the door by the knockout collection on display in the glazed wine cellar. Chef Li has over 20 years of experience, having worked at Ming Court since it first opened. They import quality ingredients from all over the world to craft remarkable dishes such as roasted crispy chicken, stuffed crab shell with fresh crab meat, and shrimp dumplings made with blue angel prawns. Busy all day long, so it’s wise to book.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3269;Ying;;Macau;11F, Altira Hotel, Avenida de Kwong Tung, Taipa, Macau;22.1619565;113.5551252;21;false;true;Cantonese;Ying is much-loved by locals for its sweeping harbour views, striking décor and most importantly, the well-executed Cantonese classics. The head chef fares well with traditional techniques that bring out the best in every ingredient. Signatures such as flambéed Iberico char siu, and stir fried sole fillet and asparagus in XO sauce are unmissable. Dim sum at lunch also show exquisite craftsmanship and astute judgment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3270;Godenya;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;UG, 182 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.28471;114.1530901;83;false;true;Japanese;Despite having a discreet entrance in a dark narrow alley, this tiny self-proclaimed ‘sake pairing restaurant’ is fully booked months ahead. There is only one omakase menu featuring kappo dishes made with seasonal produce mostly flown in from Japan. Sake pairing is a vital part of the experience as the chef/sake master serves each drink at a different temperature to bring out the best in each course, and that includes some rare small labels.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3271;Roganic;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 8, UG Level, Sino Plaza, 255 Gloucester Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong;22.2813924;114.1821991;37;false;false;European Contemporary;An offshoot of its London namesake, Roganic is the brainchild of British chef Simon Rogan. With its farm-to-table concept, micro-herbs are grown in-house and sustainable produce is sourced from local organic farms. The tasting menus showcase deceptively simple dishes that burst with flavour and amazing textures, a nod to the chef’s philosophy and ethos. The bar serves seasonal cocktails, perfect as pre- or post-dinner drinks and also offers enticing non-alcoholic drink-food pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
3272;Sun Tung Lok;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 401, L4, FoodLoft, Mira Place One, 132 Nathan Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.30099;114.17221;25;true;false;Cantonese;Synonymous with top-quality Cantonese cooking, Sun Tung Lok spares no effort to ensure that every item on the menu is as good as it could be. The experienced team is famous for its deft way with gourmet dried seafood, such as abalone. A number of set menus are available featuring the chef’s innovative creations and imported produce, while the à la carte menu caters more to the local palate. Try the crispy suckling pig stuffed with ‘bouncy’ minced shrimp.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3274;Zhejiang Heen;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;1-3F, ZJ 300, 300-306 Lockhart Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2787;114.17763;82;true;false;Zhejiang;Run by a group of Hongkongers of Zhejiang descent, this traditionally furnished restaurant boasts universal appeal. On the menu, Zhejiang delicacies rub shoulders with Shanghainese specialities. Make sure you pre-order ‘snatched tiger tails’ – seared swamp eel in a brown sauce that reveal exquisite knife work and a springy texture. Also check out the seasonal dishes and excellent buns and pastries. Friendly, unobtrusive service.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3275;Vea;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;30F, The Wellington, 198 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2850013;114.1529424;25;true;true;Innovative;An imposing counter and an open kitchen dominate the room, commanding the best view of chef Cheng in action. You are definitely in for a stellar experience, thanks to his 8-course tasting menu that rolls out a “Chinese x French” concept. Each course tells a story about Hong Kong’s food culture and his childhood memories, using Chinese and local ingredients finessed by blue-ribbon Gallic technique. Creative cocktail-food pairing suggestions.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3276;Estro;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;2F, 1 Duddell Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2801332;114.1572026;35;false;true;Italian;Since opening in 2021, Estro has been impressing diners with authentic Neapolitan cooking by the native head chef. Choose between the 6- and 8-course menus to experience the breadth and depth of his ingenious creations, like handmade bottoni pasta stuffed with parmesan emulsion and drizzled with saffron glaze, and red prawn panna cotta generously topped with caviar. Those who want some one-on-one time with him should consider the chef’s table option.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3277;Pang's Kitchen;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;25 Yik Yam Street, Happy Valley, Hong Kong;22.26921;114.18452;17;false;true;Cantonese;A household name in the neighbourhood since 2001, this restaurant wins many hearts with its traditional, often painstakingly made Cantonese cooking. This family business, now into the second generation, still impresses with its consistently well-made dishes. The signature baked fish tripe omelette in an earthenware casserole features Cantonese pork sausage that adds richness and wine aromas. Try the snake soup, and stir-fried sticky rice, too.;Air conditioning;[]
3278;New Punjab Club;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, World Wide Commercial Building, 34 Wyndham Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2799854;114.155194;52;true;false;Indian, Pakistani;This tandoor grill restaurant serving Northern Indian cuisine is named after a social club founded during the British era – the owner’s father is still a member. The menu covers old-time favourites that match the retro décor and art collection. Start the meal with one of the gin cocktails alongside tandoori anda – a grilled egg snack with langoustine that imparts a distinctive aroma. For mains, murgh methi tikka made with local three-yellow chicken is unmissable.;Air conditioning;[]
3279;Yat Lok (Central);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, Conwell House, 34-38 Stanley Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2825486;114.1552639;25;false;false;Cantonese Roast Meats;Founded in 1957, this family business has been running at this spot since 2011. The unmissable, glistening roast geese are marinated with a secret recipe and go through over 20 preparatory steps before being chargrilled to perfection. You can order the goose by the quarter, best enjoyed with a bowl of lai fun noodles in clear broth with a drizzle of goose fat. Char siu pork, roast pork belly and soy-marinated chicken are also good.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3281;Yong Fu;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 2 at GF & 1F, Golden Star Building, 20-24 Lockhart Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2782025;114.169856;74;true;true;Ningbo;The first outpost of this Shanghai-based brand in Hong Kong features wave-like crystal chandeliers and dangling glass fish in a nod to its fish-centric menu. Fish from the East China Sea is shipped here daily, and local produce is used to create authentic Ningbo fare. Most of the hallmark dishes from the parent branch are available, including some of their most complex recipes. Try raw mud crab marinated in wine, ginger and coriander that boosts the briny sweet meat and flanked by intoxicating rich crab roe. Preorder to avoid disappointment.;Air conditioning;[]
3282;Racines;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, 22 Upper Station Street, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.2849409;114.148281;52;true;true;French Contemporary;Two owner-chefs from Southern France revisit their culinary roots at Racines, literally “roots” in French. Classic heirloom recipes are given a modern makeover and are meticulously crafted with seasonal produce from their home country and Hong Kong. From homemade sourdough with smoked butter to petits-fours in a vintage biscuit tin, every course of the 5- or 7-course menu is a tour de force, weaving a story of terroir, family and friendship.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3283;Nagamoto;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;8F, 18 On Lan Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2806394;114.1566986;25;true;false;Japanese;When Kashiwaya shuttered its doors in 2021, many lamented the loss. Fortunately, it reincarnated a year later at the same spot as Nagamoto, helmed by none other than Chef Teruhiko Nagamoto himself. With only counter seats, all diners can watch his well-honed skills in action. Just one omakase menu is offered, with kaiseki courses crafted out of ‘shun’ ingredients in peak condition, embodying his deep knowledge.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3285;Yat Tung Heen;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;B2F, Eaton Hotel, 380 Nathan Road, Jordan, Hong Kong;22.3080802;114.1717998;63;false;true;Cantonese;The dining room boasts dark wood panels and moody lighting, which is refreshingly different from its formerly conventional décor. Since 1990, the kitchen team has been creating traditional but refined Cantonese fare that highlights the ingredients’ natural tastes. Dim sum, barbecued meats, stir-fries and slow-cooked soups are hugely popular. Regulars also order the abalone and bird’s nest set menu for their banquet dinners in the private rooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3286;Man Wah;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;25F, Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 5 Connaught Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.282213;114.15951;47;true;false;Cantonese;Following a 2020 makeover, this elegant and neo-Chinese chic room now boasts a royal blue theme which works well with wood-rich details and bird cage chandeliers. The menu includes a range of traditional dishes underpinned by skilful preparation and a degree of originality. Try deep-fried matsutake mushroom pudding that melts in the mouth. For adventurous oenophiles looking for surprises, the sommelier also offers blind tasting flights.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3288;Fook Lam Moon (Wan Chai);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;35-45 Johnston Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2768816;114.1708815;31;true;true;Cantonese;With 70+ years of glorious history, Fook Lam Moon is held dear by its faithful regulars as an institution in classic Cantonese cuisine. A stable kitchen team ensures the food is consistently good, be it exquisite dim sum or other traditional offerings. Standouts such as live seafood cooked various ways, deep-fried crispy chicken, baked stuffed crab shell, and gourmet soup in whole winter melon, are true delights. Some dishes need pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3289;Arcane;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, 18 On Lan Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2806189;114.1567744;24;false;true;European Contemporary;Aussie chef Shane Osborn lets diners witness how quality ingredients turn into artistic culinary creations in the open kitchen. Simple recipes are executed with a refined edge which allows authentic flavours to shine through. The affable sommelier is more than happy to pair your food with wine from their extensive cellar covering Europe, Oceania and The Americas - and which includes a lavish Burgundy selection. The reasonably priced lunch set menu is recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3290;Mono;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;5F, 18 On Lan Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2805997;114.1567846;84;true;true;Latin American;The Venezuelan chef serves a tasting menu that reinterprets LatAm cuisine while paying homage to his culinary roots. Colourful dishes deliver bold flavours reminiscent of the vibrancy of the continent’s culture. Danish langoustine is served with fermented Ecuadorian cacao in a rich, dense shrimp stock to accentuate the crustacean umami. The 18-ingredient green mole is silky in texture, striking a balance between aromas, heat and acidity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3291;Neighborhood;;Hong Kong;61-63 Hollywood Road, Central, Hong Kong;22.2830863;114.1529146;24;false;true;European Contemporary;Tucked away in an alley, this casual and bustling spot is the brainchild of owner-chef Lai, a Hongkonger trained in the U.S. The seafood-heavy menu has 20 tapas-style items on rotation, alongside large platters for sharing such as the famous salt-baked chicken rice with giblets and morels, and Hokkaido kinki paella. The daily seafood special is always a highlight – try their smoked fish in spices if available. Large platters need pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3292;Ho Hung Kee (Causeway Bay);;Hong Kong;Shop 1204-1205, 12F, Hysan Place, 500 Hennessy Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong;22.2799312;114.1837574;64;false;true;Noodles and Congee;No discussion about Hong Kong’s historic noodle shops would be complete without mentioning Ho Hung Kee, which originally opened in Wan Chai in the 1940s and is famed for its springy wonton noodles and fresh, sweet soup. More elements have been added here at its new address – dim sum and some Cantonese dishes are now served too. For the interior, they’ve adopted a more contemporary, Western style aesthetic.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3293;The Demon Celebrity;;Hong Kong;Shop 1102, 11F, Food Forum, Times Square, 1 Matheson Street, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2784568;114.1822443;89;false;true;Cantonese;The crossover between two stars of the gastronomy world, Chef Alvin Leung (a.k.a. Demon Chef) and Master Fu of the now-defunct Celebrity Cuisine was eagerly anticipated by all foodies. The two chefs put a new spin on the familiar Cantonese flavours, with collaborative efforts such as fried pork intestine stuffed with minced cuttlefish and black truffle. Chicken wing stuffed with bird’s nest, one of Fu’s specialities, can also be enjoyed here.;Air conditioning;[]
3295;Beefbar;;Hong Kong;2F, Club Lusitano, 16 Ice House Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2800634;114.1576634;29;true;true;Steakhouse;This branch of the Monte Carlo-based group boasts stylish décor that blends marble and leather. Quality steaks from the U.S., Australia, Japan and Korea, including the bestselling ribeye cap, are broiled then chargrilled to seal in the juices under a lightly charred crust. To start, consider beef tartare prepared tableside or one of the lighter ceviches and tacos. Kobe beef street snacks make interesting bites that show refinement as well as flavour.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3296;Chaat;;Hong Kong;5F, Rosewood, 18 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2947649;114.1757148;91;false;true;Indian;‘Chaat’ means ‘to lick’ in Hindi, as the food here is so good that you’d have the urge to lick the plate. The new chef continues to deliver a menu that covers classics from all over India, re-imagined with finesse and acumen. The must-try black pepper chicken tikka from the tandoor oven is best enjoyed with its signature cocktails. The food, the fragrant spices in the glass-clad Masala room, and a terrace affording nice harbour views work together to render a feast for all the senses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3297;Chef Tam's Seasons;;Macau;GF, North Esplanade, Wynn Palace, Avenida da Nave Desportiva, Cotai, Macau;22.1473845;113.5723245;42;true;false;Cantonese;As well as an à la carte offering, the dining concept by chef Tam Kwok-Fung features two set menus – one classic, one seasonal. The latter is based on the Chinese calendar’s 24 solar terms and changes every fortnight in line with the seasons. The traditional appetiser ge zha, or deep-fried egg custard, makes it to the dessert menu, infused with walnut or coconut milk. Roast spareribs in black bean honey sauce are smoky and aromatic. Pairing with Chinese wine and tea adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3298;Feuille;;Hong Kong;5F, The Wellington, 198 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2849272;114.1528886;91;true;true;French Contemporary;Renowned French chef David Toutain’s first venture outside France advocates an eco-friendly ethos, using locally sourced, organic produce with minimal impact on the environment. The multicourse veggie-heavy tasting menu, just like the restaurant’s name, is inspired by nature and the life cycle of plants. Dishes take a root-to-shoot approach, finessed by French techniques. Highlights include cumin-egg-sweet corn, and the photogenic spiny lobster.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3299;Kappo Rin;;Hong Kong;7F, The Landmark Mandarin Oriental, 15 Queen's Road Central, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2805334;114.1579314;54;false;true;Japanese;A collaborative concept by Sushi Yoshitake in Tokyo and Sushi Shikon next door, Kappo Rin specialises in multi-course, season-driven omakase menus with both cooked and raw dishes. The Japanese head chef from Sendai takes pride in his vision of complementing rich flavours with unique condiments. You can pair the food with some of the best sake from Japan. With only 8 counter seats, reservations are a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3300;Sushi Wadatsumi;;Hong Kong;607, 6F, K11 Musea, 18 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.29437;114.1744;20;false;false;Sushi;The longstanding sushi fixture in Sheung Wan moved to this shopping mall in 2021 and has assumed a bigger footprint. The kitchen team delivers a single menu of great value and rest assured that the fish, mostly wild-caught in Japan, is as good as ever. Yamagata sushi rice is dressed in a special blend of red vinegar for optimal acidity. If you’re lucky, you may even get to taste the live baby cuttlefish which are only available for two weeks each year.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3301;SÁLA de João Sá;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua dos Bacalhoeiros 103, Lisbon, 1100-068, Portugal;38.7091407;-9.1339058;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located along one of the Baixa district’s busy streets, this extremely welcoming restaurant with an open kitchen visible at the entrance is a good dining option, particularly as it has now come of age.Here, chef João Sá, who can often be seen passing from table to table serving and explaining his dishes in detail to guests, offers world cuisine with plenty of personality that combines tradition, the very best Portuguese ingredients and an array of globally influenced flavours, with a particular and intense focus on Asia. On his tasting menus, entitled “Horizon at Sight” and “In Search of New Flavours”, savour new textures in options such as couscous with coriander and razor clams, a technically simple dish but highly visual and delicious that delighted us with its ability to combine the unusual couscous, which was completely green in colour, with the sea and notes of citrus. A unique experience!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3302;Ó Balcão;Portugal;Santarém;Rua Pedro de Santarém 73, Santarém, 2000-223, Portugal;39.2318525;-8.6858779;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Ó Balcão is the perfect place for those keen to try new varieties of fish. Rodrigo Castelo is at the helm here – a chef from the Ribatejo province involved in numerous research projects who has found a way to truly showcase ingredients from his home region, with a predominant use of river fish to maintain a balance with the local ecosystem.The restaurant has the feel of an old tavern, with striking tiles that add a contemporary air and provide the backdrop for refined dishes prepared with a delicate touch. The cuisine here has it own distinct identity and is based around fish such as pike, barbel and catfish, some of which are cured in salt. Meat options here include wild boar and wild duck. Dishes on the menu that you won’t to miss include the “coscorão do rio até ao mar” (a crispy pancake filled with salt- and freshwater fish) and the “cremoso” of river crab and crayfish.;Air conditioning;[]
3303;Fortaleza do Guincho;Portugal;Cascais;Estrada do Guincho 2413, Cascais, 2750-642, Portugal;38.7282977;-9.4759076;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the Parque Natural de Sintra-Cascais, this 17C fortification, now converted into a hotel, recalls its military past thanks to the two large cannons at the entrance. The setting is enhanced by the views of the ocean and of Cabo da Rocha, the most westerly point on mainland Europe.In the elegant panoramic restaurant, chef Gil Fernandes’s menus (Memórias: Degustação and Experiência, with the option of ordering single dishes) showcase the property’s maritime inspiration through his reinterpretation of innovative dishes that have a strong focus on aesthetics and locally sourced ingredients. Head here in good time for dinner, as it’s very pleasant watching dusk fall from the tables by the windows... and there’s only enough space for early birds!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3304;Gusto by Heinz Beck;Portugal;Almancil;Estrada da Quinta do Lago, Almancil, 8135-106, Portugal;37.0633302;-8.0301921;45;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Boasting a separate entrance to the luxury Conrad Algarve Hotel, Gusto has plenty of personality as demonstrated by the impeccable private bar at the entrance and the elegant interior dining room, not forgetting the marvellous veranda that elevates the experience even further!The cuisine here is under the baton of the highly regarded German chef Heinz Beck (three Michelin stars at La Pergola restaurant in Rome), hence a similar philosophy which showcases Mediterranean roots and Italian influences alongside a constant balance between modernity and international trends such as the healthy cooking movement. On the menu here you’ll find a choice of highly select dishes alongside two interesting tasting menus with different numbers of courses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3305;Euskalduna Studio;Portugal;Porto;Rua Santo Ildefonso 404, Porto, 4000-466, Portugal;41.147396;-8.600956;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the lower section of the city is very popular with gourmet food-lovers, hence the difficulty in booking a table! After ringing the bell to gain access, you’ll enter an intimate space with its own distinct character in the style of a typical Japanese bar known as an “izakaya”, with a counter in front of the kitchen where every dish is prepared. The tasting menu is one that will definitely leave a lasting impression, showcasing chef Vasco Coelho Santos’s passion for different world cuisines. His consistent approach to cooking sees him toying with flavours to their very limit, enabling him to cook on the grill, age fish, and add a touch of smokiness, alongside interesting seasonings such as herbs with a hint of spiciness. He often incorporates a surprise dish on his menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3306;Pedro Lemos;Portugal;Porto;Rua do Ouro 258, Porto, 4150-554, Portugal;41.1480595;-8.6501319;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;An interesting choice both in terms of its cuisine and its location in Foz do Douro, where the waters of the Douro meet those of the Atlantic.The attractive building, part of the city’s architectural heritage, is split between two levels, with one on the charming ground floor (home to the wine cellar), and the other, the main dining room (with a more cosmopolitan feel), upstairs. Pedro Lemos concentrates his cuisine on three tasting menus (one of which is vegetarian), all of which feature elaborate dishes that highlight the freshness of ingredients from the local area and, more generally, from other regions around the country. We highly recommend hailing a taxi to get here as the restaurant is situated in an historic district of the city with narrow streets where parking is difficult.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3307;Lab by Sergi Arola;Portugal;Sintra;Estrada da Lagoa Azul, Sintra, 2714-511, Portugal;38.762978;-9.397945;45;false;true;Creative;The Penha Longa Hotel is a truly exclusive resort, both in terms of its location in the Parque Natural de Sintra-Cascais and its luxury facilities that overlook a golf course.Lab by Sergi Arola boasts a cocktail bar and an impressive glass-fronted wine cellar. Here, guests are served a choice of aperitifs and tapas in the kitchen and in an adjoining room, before heading to a modern-inspired dining room with incredible views of the greens. Celebrity Spanish chef Sergi Arola, who is always associated with a sense of freedom and a rock & roll spirit, favours innovative, meticulously prepared dishes that abound with flavour and Mediterranean inspiration, but with a subtle nod to his past and splendid Portuguese ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3308;A Cozinha;Portugal;Guimaraes;Largo do Serralho 4, Guimaraes, 4800-472, Portugal;41.4429053;-8.2941256;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The icing on the cake to complete your visit to this beautiful city, the medieval centre of which has received UNESCO World Heritage status.The restaurant, occupying a discreet property in the historic centre, boasts a charming and informal dining room from where the kitchen is visible behind a glass wall. Here, chef António Loureiro offers tasting menus (alongside a limited à la carte with the same dishes) featuring precise, perfectly balanced modern dishes, albeit with a solid basis in tradition, that showcase meticulous presentation and a clear respect for top-quality ingredients. Two particularly interesting features upstairs are the private dining room and the small terrace with an abundance of aromatic plants.;Air conditioning;[]
3309;Feitoria;Portugal;Lisbon;Doca do Bom Sucesso, Lisbon, 1400-038, Portugal;38.6936647;-9.2129467;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If you’re wandering around the city’s historic sights, such as the Monument to the Discoveries and the Belém Tower, make sure you also pay a visit to this charming restaurant. With a backdrop ambience that combines the classic and modern, this space exudes personality and elegance, as well as boasting an exquisite bar at the entrance with views of the Tagus. Taking a seat at one of its tables is an invitation to embark on a journey across the traditional flavours of Portugal through dishes that combine high-level technique and top-quality ingredients. Under the baton of chef André Cruz, the menu has been created with an emphasis on seasonal produce, most of which are from local suppliers, as is reflected on the Semente menu, which comes in four different versions: Leaf, Roots, and two vegetarian options. Classic Portuguese dishes have been enhanced with a touch of sophistication, such as the “Sea Stew” (Cozido do Mar), featuring fish and finished with caviar and seaweed, or the typical convent-inspired Sericaia dessert from the Alentejo, made with eggs and served with honey and native herbs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3310;2Monkeys;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Câmara Pestana 23, Lisbon, 1150-082, Portugal;38.7180859;-9.1400416;17;false;true;Creative, French Contemporary;There are some restaurants that exude positive energy – and this is, without a shadow of a doubt, one of them. The two monkeys after which it is named (and which are also depicted on the logo) refer, somewhat surprisingly, to the two chefs at the helm (Vítor Matos and Guilherme Spalk) and their approach to their work – at the same time as offering a high-quality culinary experience, they are also keen to entertain and have fun!This unique space, occupying the former wine cellar at the luxury Torel Palace Lisboa hotel, recreates, in stunning wood, the concept of a theatrical dining experience for just 12 guests built around a central island that provides the setting for the open kitchen. On the single, creatively focused menu, which includes some French-inspired details, guests can explore flavours from around Portugal (we particularly enjoyed the onion chawanmushi and the violet shrimp). The chefs interact constantly with their guests, who are not restricted to a fixed time schedule, enabling them to manage their own experience in more relaxed fashion.;Air conditioning;[]
3311;Encanto;Portugal;Lisbon;Largo De São Carlos 10, Lisbon, 1200 410, Portugal;38.7099067;-9.1414836;97;false;false;Vegetarian;On the Portuguese culinary scene, chef José Avillez is one of those figures who is constantly raising his already legendary profile through his work in the kitchen and his desire to diversify the cuisine on offer in his restaurants. This small yet welcoming eatery, located next to his award-winning Belcanto, will surprise guests with its contemporary aesthetic (note the designer bookcases on each wall connected to each other via the ceiling) and a culinary approach which features a touch of creativity. In no way does its complete focus on vegetables prevent it from conjuring up dishes that abound in nuance, flavour and technique. The single 100% vegetarian tasting menu is well supported by a wine list of biodynamic labels, craft beers, kombuchas etc.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3312;CURA;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Rodrigo da Fonseca 88, Lisbon, 1099-039, Portugal;38.7257479;-9.155379;93;false;false;Modern Cuisine;CURA is the gourmet dining space in the legendary and luxurious Four Seasons Hotel Ritz Lisbon, where it showcases its own character, helped by having its own separate entrance.Taking its name from the word "curadoria" (or “curatorship” as in an artistic sense), it features a kitchen that opens onto the dining room, providing the backdrop and on modern, bold yet well-balanced cuisine that showcases well-thought-out dishes and surprising technical control. On the menu you’ll find impressive dishes that will challenge the senses, ranging from the dish resembling a Berliner doughnut filled with luxury ingredients such as lobster to more daring options such as the Molho da Bairrada with mustard and orange, served in a similar way to a Mexican taco and which evokes the flavours and textures of the famed suckling pig from Bairrada. Dishes here are only available on a single menu: Origens (with 5 or 10 “moments”) which is accompanied by two vegetarian versions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3314;Bon Bon;Portugal;Lagoa;Estrada de Sesmarias, Lagoa, 8400-525, Portugal;37.116478;-8.480948;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An elegant ambience, professionalism, good service and a true gastronomic experience at dinner are the hallmarks of this restaurant, which works with premium ingredients to create a delicious tasting menu (there’s also a vegetarian option). The lunchtime fare here is much simpler and more moderately priced.Chef José Lopes showcases modern cuisine with a reginal flavour that focuses heavily on recipes from the Algarve - all of which are prepared with a keen eye on presentation, textures and harmonious flavours. In the high-ceilinged classic-cum-contemporary dining room, fascinating details include the hexagonal layout, the wrought-iron fireplace in the centre of the dining room, and the large glass-fronted wine cellar. The pleasant outside terrace is an added bonus!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3315;Le Monument;Portugal;Porto;Avenida dos Aliados 151, Porto, 4000-067, Portugal;41.1484635;-8.6114469;55;false;true;Contemporary;If a high-flying culinary adventure sounds appealing, Le Monument offers the perfect opportunity – to the luxurious backdrop of Le Monumental Palace hotel.French chef Julien Montbabut, a recipient of a Michelin star in Paris, adopts a different take here, taking guests on a gastronomic journey through the different regions of Portugal. He rekindles classic recipes from each area, albeit with a more innovative approach that is based around modern cuisine, but which pays homage to native ingredients and respect for flavour. The dining experience is limited to a single tasting menu (choose between a short or long version), and is accompanied by a booklet that provides an explanation of each dish and a map that offers a visual introduction to the region that inspired it.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3316;Mesa de Lemos;Portugal;Passos de Silgueiros;Quinta de Lemos, Passos de Silgueiros, 3500-541, Portugal;40.577633;-7.98049;16;false;false;Creative;This restaurant full of surprises is an architectural and gastronomic oasis that lights up the night sky in the tranquil Dão wine-producing region.Here, chef Diogo Rocha offers guests traditionally based creative cuisine on two tasting menus (some dishes are also available à la carte). He uses local ingredients as the cornerstone of his cooking (including from his own farm whenever possible), in so doing showing full respect to individual flavours and well-honed techniques. The delightful, reasonably spacious building is modern in design and completely glass-fronted and has a superb design that blends in perfectly with the adjoining vineyards and enhances the fine views. The wines used in the pairings here come, as you would expect, from the property’s own estate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
3317;A Ver Tavira;Portugal;Tavira;Calçada da Galeria 13, Tavira, 8800-306, Portugal;37.12565;-7.651429;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located close to Tavira’s old Moorish castle, this restaurant was created out of a heartfelt homage to the history of this town with its 37 churches. Over the years, however, it has also proved that the cuisine, ingredients and flavours on offer here are just as important as its history.The attentive married couple in charge, Cláudia Abrantes (sommelier and front-of-house) and her chef-husband Luís Brito, at the helm in the kitchen, are extremely committed to creating the perfect experience. The constant aim of the cuisine is to find a balance between vegetables and fish and seafood, presented on four enticing tasting menus: an “executive” menu only available at lunchtime, plus three others (Between Moments, The Journey of Flavour, and The Whole Trip) that include blue lobster, beef from the Trás-os Montes region etc. The restaurant also boasts two attractive terrace-esplanades overlooking the town – one on the same floor for menu-based dining, the other, upstairs, for appetisers.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3318;100 Maneiras;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua do Teixeira 39, Lisbon, 1200-459, Portugal;38.714841;-9.1449507;33;true;false;Creative;The culinary concept behind 100 Maneiras is one of absolute freedom – one that constantly takes risks and seeks to provoke a strong reaction and to leave a lasting mark with guests, often via ingredients referred to as "from the future" or that are little known (the larvae with onions was a dish that definitely came as a surprise!).Everything here revolves around chef Ljubomir Stanisic, a native of Sarajevo (Bosnia-Herzegovina), who arrived in Portugal in his late-teens following the war in his country, healing the wounds of his soul by devoting himself to cooking. His different tasting menus (A História, O Conto and Ecos do 100, the latter vegetarian), are based around innovative cuisine with a constant nod (both physical and emotional) to his origins, although influences from his adopted homeland and further afield are also evident. His more traditional starters and desserts also have an interesting twist given that he used to make these with his mother!;Air conditioning;[]
3319;EPUR;Portugal;Lisbon;Largo da Academia Nacional de Belas Artes 14, Lisbon, 1200-005, Portugal;38.7087383;-9.1398799;100;false;true;Creative;A culinary enclave well worth considering in the historic Chiado district, which toys with Newton’s law of universal gravitation to create its own "Gravitational Taste" concept. Here, behind the robust façade of an old building, you’ll find an informal, more modern interior that includes an open-view kitchen and dining rooms lit in a contemporary, minimalist fashion. Enjoy superb views across the Tagus estuary to a backdrop of geometrically shaped ceilings and azulejo panels which are a silent testament to the past but which add appropriate character and personality.The creative cooking on display is highly visual yet at the same time elegant, pure and with a strong focus on vegetables. French chef Vincent Farges follows the thinking of Leonardo da Vinci in his defence of "simplicity and maximum sophistication", focusing on the essentials to elevate the dining experience via two tasting menus: Inspirações (8 courses) and Epurismo (10 courses).;Air conditioning;[]
3320;Vila Foz;Portugal;Porto;Avenida De Montevideu 236, Porto, 4150-516, Portugal;41.1617684;-8.6850196;80;true;false;Contemporary;A restaurant full of surprises, occupying what was once the luxurious main hall of the Vila Foz hotel &spa, a 19C mansion overlooking the Praia do Homem do Leme.Here, to a backdrop of elegant mouldings, period gilded work and mirrors that take their inspiration from the finest palaces, discover the gourmet cuisine of chef Arnaldo Azevedo, who showcases contemporary cuisine that extols the full flavour of wonderful Portuguese fish and seafood on his menus (Novo Mundo and Maresia). An unusual feature here is a counter (formerly the bar) facing the kitchen which offers a much more personal, close-up and intense option called the Kitchen Seat, reserved exclusively for just two guests and an experience that is heightened by interaction with the chef!;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3322;Al Sud;Portugal;Lagos;Resort Clubhouse, Lagos, 8500-250, Portugal;37.1258637;-8.6405204;46;false;true;Creative;If you’re looking to escape from the stresses of daily life, you’ll find few better places than the elegant Club House at the Palmares Ocean Living & Golf resort, occupying a building that aims to blend into nature and boasts a superb covered terrace perfect for gazing out at the sunset while enjoying views of the bay.Here, chef Louis Anjos conjures up contemporary cuisine with a creative touch, yet free of eccentricity, that takes as its point of reference ingredients from the Algarve and its coastline, with special attention given to fish and seafood that he sources daily from the auction in Sagres, as well as the best local meat. His cooking is based around a single, well-balanced tasting menu entitled "A Discovery", featuring ten courses that encapsulate the surrounding area and its ingredients (prawns, turbot, snapper, Iberian pork, Alentejo lamb etc), and a clear desire to create identifiable flavours. The chef enjoys heading out of the kitchen to greet his guests in person.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3323;Fifty Seconds;Portugal;Lisbon;Cais das Naus, Lisbon, 1990-173, Portugal;38.7747556;-9.0911606;83;true;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;If you’ve never eaten lunch or dinner 120m above ground, you might want to enjoy the experience in this unique dining space in the famous Vasco da Gama tower that dominates Lisbon’s skyline, with its impressive views of the city, the Tagus, and even the magical Troia peninsula (access is via a panoramic lift that takes exactly 50 seconds to reach the top, hence the name of the restaurant). At the helm is Rui Silvestre, a chef with an extensive career working in renowned restaurants and famous for being the youngest chef in Portugal to hold a coveted Michelin star. His cooking is showcased on a single menu entitled “Fauna and Flora” (10, 12 or 14 courses) that is full of surprises thanks to its incomparable flavours and use of local ingredients, as well as spices and citrus notes that result in superb combinations. A good example is his octopus dish, featuring a delicate dash of massala, subtle shavings of beetroot, and a refreshing touch of lemon.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
3324;G Pousada;Portugal;Bragança;Estrada de Turismo, Bragança, 5300-271, Portugal;41.8026186;-6.7541046;66;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Creative;If you’re unfamiliar with the modern cooking of the Trás-os-Montes region, exalted by renowned Portuguese writer Miguel Torga in his book The Marvellous Kingdom, you won’t want to miss this restaurant – a fine example of honest cuisine, passion and a continued desire to improve.The G in its names is a reference to the surname Gonçalves, and the two brothers (Óscar and António) who run this eatery with its classic decor and spectacular views of the local fortress. Chestnuts, wild mushrooms, aromatic herbs, variations on the traditional Portuguese sausage (alheira), and a small cheese trolley take centre stage here, while local products are showcased on various menus with themes dedicated to the famous artists of Porto’s Fine Arts School. A tasting of Trás-os-Montes’ olive oils comes as an added surprise.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3325;Midori;Portugal;Sintra;Estrada da Lagoa Azul, Sintra, 2714-511, Portugal;38.7616883;-9.3962995;91;false;true;Japanese, Creative;The best Japanese restaurant in Portugal, where the connection with the Land of the Rising Sun is evident in the name (Midori means "green", in clear reference to the delightfully verdant surroundings of the Penha Longa hotel. Decorative features here include an open kitchen, walls embellished with vinyl, an attractive mural designed by a Portuguese artist, as well as large picture windows enabling the surrounding greenery to form part of the restaurant experience. The cuisine of talented chef Pedro Almeida, supported every day by the young resident chef Tiago Santo, showcases Portuguese cuisine with a Japanese soul which incorporates techniques from Japan and applies them to the best local ingredients. Two tasting menus, Kiri and Yama, are on offer, featuring bold dishes such as cod misoshiro, squid sashimi with a cured ham dashi, and Iberian pork sukiyaki with bell pepper. You can also choose between a huge array of sakes (served cold, at room temperature, or warm, depending on your preference).;Air conditioning,Car park,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
3326;Vista;Portugal;Portimao;Avenida Tomás Cabreira, Portimao, 8500-802, Portugal;37.125793;-8.53579;27;true;false;Modern Cuisine;When we talk of unique restaurants, we refer to places such as Vista! This restaurant occupies a delightful early 20C palace situated on a promontory in the middle of the Praia da Rocha, hence the authentic picture-postcard views of the immense Atlantic.With an emphasis on sustainability, chef João Oliveira creates meat dishes as part of a culinary repertoire that champions local ingredients, including olive oil. The experience here begins with appetisers in the kitchen before heading into the elegant dining room to choose between two menus: Vista (exclusively based around locally caught fish and seafood) and Terra (vegetarian). To help explain the provenance of ingredients (fish from Sagre, squid from Portimão, Carabineiro red prawns from Vila Real de Santo António, sea salt from Castro Marim, etc), three ceramic pieces are placed on your table that highlight the different areas of the Algarve.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3327;Herdade do Esporão;Portugal;Reguengos de Monsaraz;Herdade do Esporão, Reguengos de Monsaraz, 7200-999, Portugal;38.38073;-7.55312;20;true;false;Contemporary;Thanks to top-quality local ingredients, well-defined textures and harmonious flavours, everything is so delicious here that you’ll want to try every dish!This restaurant, situated on a large farm-wine estate surrounded by vineyards, olive groves and even a reservoir, boasts a modern look with hints of Scandinavian design. It is also self-sufficient in vegetables as it has its own market garden that provides all of its organic ingredients. Chef Carlos Teixeira’s constant focus on sustainability results in modern cooking that is based around seasonal ingredients both from the farm estate and the Alentejo. His dishes (textures of corn, “Lucio perca alentejana” (pork and clams) with potatoes, local lamb with rice and a vegetable salad, etc) are presented on a tasting menu (Carta Branca) on which you can choose between five or seven courses, both available with a wine pairing option which is chosen by most guests. Wine tourism activities are also available, including a visit of the cellar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3328;Loco;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua dos Navegantes 53 B, Lisbon, 1200-731, Portugal;38.7123702;-9.1605213;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this restaurant, located just a few steps from the 18C Baroque Basílica da Estrela, they are keen to highlight their connection with micro-seasonal ingredients to maximise the flavour of each one and to meet their zero-waste criteria. Loco is full of surprises as soon as you step through the door, starting with the tree hanging from the ceiling of the entrance hall – a sensation that is enhanced by its extensive designer features and a completely open-view kitchen. Head chef Alexandre Silva’s culinary philosophy is fully focused on a single surprise tasting menu comprising 16 “moments” or courses, which takes its inspiration from Portuguese tradition, while at the same time constantly evolving and changing from a contemporary viewpoint.We recommend you take a close look at the drinks menu which, as well as featuring superb organic wines from small-scale producers, also includes a range of craft beers, herbal liqueurs and fermented natural juices, most of which are made in-house.;Air conditioning;[]
3329;William;Portugal;Funchal;Estrada Monumental 139, Funchal, 9000-098, Portugal;32.64069;-16.92367;28;false;false;Contemporary;If you’re looking for an exclusive dining space on the delightful island of Madeira, this could be the perfect option! Part of the luxurious Belmond Reid's Palace, this restaurant boasts one of the most dazzling views of the Funchal coast. The name is in tribute to the legendary William Reid, the Scottish visionary who built the hotel over a century ago. Here, chef José Diogo Costa, who returned to his native island after working in several renowned restaurants, offers cuisine that is presented on three tasting menus (one of which is vegetarian) that showcase local ingredients which he combines perfectly with modern techniques in a classic and elegant setting. Dishes such as prawn, buttermilk and fennel, and the “catch from our coast” with a creamy Hollandaise sauce and finished with thin slivers of chayote, reveal the talent of this young chef. Don’t miss the fresh, fruit-inspired desserts featuring textures and flavours that will live long in the memory.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3330;Kanazawa;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Damião De Góis 3 A, Lisbon, 1400-291, Portugal;38.6979595;-9.2256498;54;true;false;Japanese;Named after the chef who opened this restaurant and also the capital of the Ishikawa region, Kanazawa offers a glimpse into a different culinary world.Its traditional Kaiseki cuisine, which became recognised as one of the most refined in Japan after it had been served by the imperial court and featured in traditional tea ceremonies, will delight guests in this tiny, minimalist-style eatery with just a single counter for eight diners, where chef Paulo Morais creates his superb cuisine, explaining each dish in detail. He offers several menus which adhere to the Kaiseki philosophy, albeit with a more liberal approach, but always respecting its true essence, with his dishes taking on a more elaborate and gastronomic feel in the evening. The quality of his fish and nigiris is truly spectacular!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3331;Desarma;Portugal;Funchal;Rua das Maravilhas 74, Funchal, 9000-177, Portugal;32.648641;-16.9194868;79;false;true;Contemporary;Chef Octávio Freitas has shown that it is possible to turn your dreams into reality here on the terrace of The Views Baía hotel, where the dining experience is matched by truly superb views, particularly from the sofas on the patio and once night starts to fall.In this attractive space, featuring an impressive open kitchen and an original interior design that is inspired by a banana plant, the cuisine has a strong local DNA showcased via typical “petiscos” from the island prepared with a contemporary touch. These are complemented by a whole host of accompaniments that, wherever possible, are prepared in-house (cured and matured fish, bread made with local flour, cheese, butter, maritime-inspired “enchidos”). These are highlighted on three tasting menus (Armed with Senses, The Chef’s Battle and The Chef's Bench) the first two sub-divided into different moments: Encounter, Offensive, Attack and Surrender. Desarma’s wine cellar houses one of the world’s best selections of Madeira wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view;[]
3332;Les Pieds dans le Plat;Belgium;Marenne;rue du Centre 3, Marenne, 6990, Belgium;50.2397614;5.4106369;73;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A romantic restaurant, flanked by an engaging patio, where you will sample wholehearted traditional fare and the deft flyaway touch of a seasoned chef. Charismatic Jean-Michel Dienst conjures up vividly expressed dishes steeped in Gallic tradition. He avows a weakness for premium produce such as Anjou pigeon and Challans duck, whose generous flavours he nurtures and enhances.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3333;Bar Bulot;Belgium;Zedelgem;Loppemsestraat 52, Zedelgem, 8210, Belgium;51.14832;3.1488513;93;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Belgian;Bar Bulot is redefining the luxury brasserie concept and is now housed in a handsome farmstead that was home to the star restaurant Hertog Jan for many years. The view of the garden is magnificent, the lush green terrace is utter bliss, while the interior drips in stylish elegance. A high-flying restaurant, whose chef rolls out a stripped back version of gastronomic classics, underscoring their intensity with original touches. Under the auspices of owner Gert De Mangeleer, the chef excels in the art of enhancing a Franco-Belgian score of the likes of sole meunière with buttery mashed potato, a poached egg and Zeebrugge shrimps. The quality of the hanger steak, served blue, yet hot (a rare feat!), is simply out of this world and is served with finely chopped shallots in a bordelaise sauce that sets off the meat’s full-bodied flavours, further flanked by a cognac sauce, while melting foie gras and piping hot crispy fries add the final flourish and a whole new dimension to your run-of-the-mill hanger steak with shallots. Satisfying flavours of stunning simplicity that bring smiles of pleasure to the lips of diners, all the more because of the knockout value for money ratio!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3334;Nebo;Belgium;Antwerpen;Panamarenkoplein 5, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2051513;4.3829209;31;true;false;Contemporary, Modern French;Nebo, which means ‘sky’ in Croatian, is a discreet tribute to the 1-star Michelin restaurant of Dimitri de Koninck’s father, La Luna. In his own swish establishment in the hip Nieuw Zuid district, youthful Dimitri, demonstrates that he learned the ropes with the best. He enjoys pampering his guests with an entirely à la carte menu, flanked by enticing suggestions. The wine list bear witness to the passion for oenology of Michelle, a master sommelier. Connoisseurs of first-class ingredients, such as Anjou pigeon and wild seabass, will be in culinary heaven. The chef faithfully upholds classical culinary traditions, which he pairs with a host of details and unconventional side dishes. Examples include langoustine a la plancha, subtly lacquered in yuzu kosho and flanked with delicately sweet finely-diced mango and jalapeno and then rounded off with a miso-flavoured cream of carrot. De Koninck surgically, generously and lovingly crafts each dish using premium produce. Everything is prepared from scratch and last minute in a bid to offer the diner a genuine global dining experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3335;La Table de Manon;Belgium;Grandhan;rue de Givet 79, Grandhan, 6940, Belgium;50.32419;5.42186;43;true;false;French Contemporary;Manon Schenck, who is nothing if not spunky, has decided to focus mainly on fish and seafood, with a weakness for lobster, in a region that is renowned for its game! Her cuisine is strongly influenced by Alsace, her place of birth, by Brittany, where she worked for a long time and by her new country of adoption, the Belgian Ardennes. Heart-warming food and service in a tasteful contemporary interior. Heaven for foodies!Manon has grown in confidence and daring, particularly thanks to her close ties with Brittany fishermen who supply her with top-quality, fresh produce. Consummate technique, gutsy sauces and fresh tangy flavours paired with exotic ingredients set the scene for this culinary pageant. Her lobster variations are a must, as is the fish of the day. For example, she might pair flavoursome pollock with the fresh, almost bitter taste of artichoke and a sauce made with fish bones, black garlic and a few pieces of ham to add a full-bodied kick. She is not averse to mixing surf and turf ingredients, thus subtly jazzing up her recipes, while lobster and fish from the Belgian Ardennes are also on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3336;Chai Gourmand;Belgium;Beuzet;rue Chainisse 53, Beuzet, 5030, Belgium;50.5296583;4.7456131;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You can’t miss the Chai Gourmand (think ‘winery for foodies’), housed in a truly spectacular concrete, wood and glass architectural behemoth. Lush green countryside soothingly frames and underscores the warm, welcoming minimalist interior dotted with Scandinavian accents. A gifted cook, chef Pierre Massin unveils his know-how whilst managing to steer clear of fussy complexity and yet enable the modern appetising score to showcase his carefully controlled creative streak. He leaves his signature with just a few side dishes, for example, slow-baked whiting is coated in melt-in-the-mouth breadcrumbs and flanked by knockout smoked eel and vegetables that add a subtle refreshing note and a ponzu-flavoured eel jus for a final kick. Food that strikes just the right balance between distinctive flavour and freshness. Even better, the dishes of the set menu are also available on the à la carte menu. In terms of beverages, you won’t go wrong if you trust the sommelier for his inspired food-wine pairing suggestions.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3337;Le Grand Verre;Belgium;Durbuy;Place aux Foires 26, Durbuy, 6940, Belgium;50.3520328;5.4557638;63;false;false;Modern French, International;Surrealist art by Marcel Duchamp and Jacques Charlier sets the distinctive arty scene in this colourful restaurant, enhanced by a warm welcome and a cornucopia of luxury details. Head for the patio in fine weather to make the most of the historic village of Durbuy. Rather than surrealistic, the food embodies the essence of a Michelin one-star establishment: taste! Renowned chef Wout Bru lets his ingenious creations and deftly crafted dishes speak for themselves, zooming in on outstanding produce, which he flanks with unexpected combinations oozing with Mediterranean charm. Langoustine, cooked to perfection, is paired with a big-boned court-bouillon and the salty, buttery flavours of caviar. Various textures of cauliflower add an earthy edge, while a white wine sauce of crunchy samphire adds the finishing touch to this high-flying dish. Each surprise is underscored by familiar flavours, such as saddle of hare that is paired with a gutsy Harlequin sauce. Insightful wine pairing suggestions further heighten the diner’s pleasure, as does the superb cheese platter. The dessert trolley is in a class of its own, piled high with wickedly enticing delights like a Paris-Brest, a millefeuille with vanilla ice cream or a chocolate cake to die for! Every detail has been endlessly puzzled and pondered over at Le Grand Verre.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3338;Le Vieux Château;Belgium;Flobecq;rue du Docteur Degrave 23, Flobecq, 7880, Belgium;50.7374064;3.7337919;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You will be conquered by Le Vieux Château and its drop-dead surroundings before you have even taken a seat. Once over the moat bridge and past the huge oak door, it is impossible not to fall in love with the interior which intelligently and tastefully marries authentic period details such as timber ceilings with a light, contemporary vibe, without forgetting the glazed extension that enjoys unfettered views over the garden and countryside. Once you are comfortably seated, you can bask in the attentive service and infinite creativity of Tanguy De Turck.This chef refuses to limit himself to a single style and joyfully leaps from generous street food or lobster that is jazzed up with a modern grapefruit jelly that adds a fresh bitterness to classically grilled brill on a plancha or a vegetarian menu that reveals his passion for vegetables. Chef De Turck deploys a head-spinning array of techniques to translate his ideas into dishes, resulting in delicate, insightful creations that fascinate, such as fillets of seabass marinated in dashi and paired with a mussels’ jus, a punchy twist of lemon and smoked mussels for depth and character. This precise, generous and unorthodox chef has found the perfect partner in the sommelier whose intuitive wine pairing tips further exalt his cuisine.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3339;Neon;Belgium;Lier;Barbara-Vettersplein 4, Lier, 2500, Belgium;51.13007;4.57375;17;true;true;Country cooking, Creative French;Nils Proost brings his vision of sustainable fine dining to life in this refurbished canteen of a former teacher training college. He sources regional veggies and fruit, North Sea fish and occasionally meat (whole carcasses) in a tribute to the region’s forests, land and sea. Zero waste inspires his creativity (the superb Kombucha for example), adding a fascinating twist to his repertory. Vibrant fermentations, powerful flavours, surprising seasonings and understated sweet fruity notes: the tastebuds are constantly thrilled and enthralled at Neon. Creamy mussels with a subtle smoky BBQ aroma, earthy mushrooms, girolles marinated in an explosive fresh tarragon vinegar and a hazelnut sauce weave an amazing patchwork of delicate culinary flavours and textures. The intrepid chef endeavours to showcase the best of each season and micro-season, rolling out five set menus throughout the year that reflect the breadth of his creative skills. His outlook is as contagious, as his team is enthusiastic.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3340;Fani;Luxembourg;Roeser;51 Grand Rue, Roeser, 3394, Luxembourg;49.5398974;6.1445134;66;true;false;Italian;Roberti Fani deploys his talent and skills to concoct finely balanced, creative dishes that enhance and bring out the best of high - quality ingredients. Do not be misled, the apparent simplicity of each dish is the result of an admirable command of culinary techniques. A combination of elegant and designer details sets the scene in the low - key interior.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3341;Hoeve De Bies;Belgium;St-Martens-Voeren;Bies 4, St-Martens-Voeren, 3790, Belgium;50.7466044;5.8148917;41;false;true;Modern French;The peaceful countryside of Fouron stretches out around the 19C farmhouse whose terrace commands a breathtaking view. Exposed rafters do add character, but don’t expect anything more than that in terms of rusticity, because the interior in fact sports designer materials, an open wine cellar and lounge music. Upstairs, two one-room flats offer the chance to relax in style after your meal, but, before that, let’s do justice to the high-flying talent of Maurice Huynen and Peterhans van Harinxma.Their cuisine is both heartwarming and polished, regional and international. Examples include local trout from Commanderie 7 baked whole and flanked by a punchy marinade and a stock made from fish bones, all of which is smoked for 24 hours to produce an explosion of savours for the tastebuds. Chef Maurice shows infinite respect for the ingredient as he carefully crafts powerful sauces, while Peterhans, in charge of the front-of-house and a sommelier, adds a hint of classicism, courtesy of his cellar of white Burgundies, without forgetting the odd regional and international tipple.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3342;Barge;Belgium;Brussels;boulevard d'Ypres 33, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8569126;4.3468964;15;true;false;Organic, Farm to table;Exceptional ingredients from committed suppliers, staff wellbeing and the belief that our actions impact the lives of our peers: such are some of the topics that are regularly discussed by Grégoire Gillard and his team. In their suitably untreated, trendy street corner establishment, near the fish market, they conjure up their own vision of sustainable gastronomy. The surprise menu shines the limelight on the excellent produce of Brussels and the region, with an underlying commitment to respect the seasons, however short.Nature is what inspires chef Gillard’s creativity. For example, he may treat slow-cooked salmon trout to an Asian twist thanks to savoury nori leaf, crunchy black radish and hints of wasabi and soy. He wins us over with insightful, intense combinations rather than showy demonstrations, illustrated by Belgian buffalo ricotta, Jerusalem artichokes, truffle, coffee oil and lacto-fermentation jus. Each ingredient has a role to play and is designed to interact with the others to create fascinating dishes from the first to the last bite.The enticing wine list was compiled in accordance with the establishment’s dedication to sustainability. Each decision is taken after weighing the impact on the community and the individual, without forgetting the overriding quest for taste.;;[]
3343;Dôme;Belgium;Antwerpen;Grote Hondstraat 2, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.2061996;4.4264854;58;true;false;Classic French;Glance upwards as you enter this grand Art nouveau edifice and admire the jaw-dropping dome and glittering chandelier! A mosaic floor and panels of bold floral wallpaper add further cachet to the striking rotunda dining room. Evangeline, in charge of the front of house, greets guests as if they were old friends, hence the home-from-home vibe. A genuine globetrotter, Frédéric Chabbert learned the ropes in prestigious French houses and in the United States and Asia, as you will quickly taste in his cuisine. Dedicated to exalting the ingredient, he may jazz up a traditional sauce with pigeon entrails which he pours over a pink breast of the same bird or he may contrast the briny tang of caviar with a flan of fresh yeast and a stock of brown miso. This veteran chef delves into his rich background to conjure up fascinating recipes, like his chocolate tart, one of the house signature dishes. Chabbert’s cuisine throws a new light on familiar flavours, all of which is underscored by intelligent wine pairings. Consummate know-how that packs a punch every time.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3344;¡Toma!;Belgium;Liège;boulevard de la Sauvenière 70 bis, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.6437004;5.5661044;67;false;true;Creative;Local lad Thomas Troupin has given the ancient walls of his establishment a smart modern feel. The terrace adjoins the kitchen garden, and the restaurant boasts a fermentation cellar. This high-flying technical master chef buys his ingredients locally and his inventive streak is most noticeable in his vegetable recipes, thanks to his charcoal oven.;Terrace;[]
3345;Fine Fleur;Belgium;Antwerpen;Lange Gasthuisstraat 41b, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2140927;4.4055878;30;false;true;Creative, Modern French;Serenity and contemporary class depict Fine Fleur, one of the splendid eateries that have taken up abode in the swanky Botanic Sanctuary Hotel. Admire the kitchen team at work behind smoked glass, while you are pampered by the enthusiastic youthful front-of-house team. Nothing is left to chance from the inspired wine-food pairings to the chefs who pop out to present their handiwork. Fine Fleur is the brainchild of Jacob Jan Boerma and Thomas Diepersloot, who showcase their personal vision of fine dining here. The exceptional ingredients are flanked by gutsy sauces, a dash of Dutch daring, exotic flavours and fresh twists. Meticulous, spot-on cooking, illustrated by a fillet of plaice, jazzed up with finely chopped kohlrabi mixed with mustard seeds or droplets of dill-flavoured chilled sabayon matched with a subtle buttermilk sauce. A constant quest for perfection depicts the ethos here and let’s not forget the truly inspired flourish of the wholehearted pastry chef at the end of the meal. Fine Fleur adds a whole new dimension to the concept of casual fine dining. In their words: pure indulgence.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3346;Willem Hiele;Belgium;Oudenburg;Kapittelstraat 71, Oudenburg, 8460, Belgium;51.1907161;2.9734058;74;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Rock’n roll and unconventional, Willem Hiele has swapped his dinky fishermen’s hut for an architectural behemoth by Jacques Moeschal. Polders dominate De Keignaert nature reserve and are also a major feature of this imposing brutalist edifice, in which chef Hiele invites you to sample his favourite dishes.He translates the brutality of the sea and nature into dishes that bear his highly personal and delicate hallmark. Intense sauces, vinaigrettes and a smoky live fire focus which showcase regional delicacies such as North Sea fish and veggies. Examples include slow-cooked monkfish flanked by succulent mushrooms, whose texture results from a specific drying technique. The noteworthy Bordelaise sauce is refreshed by shiso that adds depth and harmony. While not a fan of gimmicks, he may however playfully slip a spoonful of caviar into a walnut and bitter chocolate iced dessert. A fascinating experience that is even better if you spend a night in one of the seven guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3347;La Grange d'Hamois;Belgium;Emptinne;Chaussée d'Andenne 10a, Emptinne, 5363, Belgium;50.3343431;5.1037114;67;false;true;Modern French, Classic French;Chef Grégory Gillain and the lady of the house, Hélène Fays, have set up shop in a barn that is over 150 years old. Ardennes materials such as local stone contrast and enhance the modern decorative vibe. Chef Gillain’s personal vision and love of regional produce have reached new dimensions in this establishment.A maestro of textbook techniques, his braised sweetbread has become one of the house’s signature dishes. However, his deep-seated understanding of the ingredient can also be tasted in recipes such as roast hare that melts in the mouth. Suave, inventive side dishes jazz up the meal, adding acidic, spicy or unctuous notes, illustrated by the homemade cannelloni of celeriac, paired with gutsy smoked beef and a mayonnaise of anchovies and watercress oil that adds fresh, spicy and distinctive notes. Rather than fancy frills, you can expect a wholesome tribute to hearty produce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3348;Mosconi;;Luxembourg;13 rue Münster, 2160, Luxembourg;49.6089476;6.1357961;55;false;false;Italian;Gracious Simonetta and veteran chef Ilario Mosconi have been jazzing up the fine dining scene of Luxembourg since 1986. Originally from Lombardy, the couple welcome you into a handsome townhouse steeped in swish elegance and boasting a terrace by the River Alzette. The secret of their success no doubt lies in their overriding desire to please their guests. In true Italian tradition, the cuisine is founded on first-class ingredients, everything is homemade and the crisp, distinctive edge that underscores each dish comes from a voluntarily stripped back culinary approach. Rather than a glut of ingredients, each dish sings a subtle ode to southern Europe. The chef may flank flawlessly cooked squab breast with truffle to highlight its hazelnut flavour. Black beans are cooked in squid juice, the gravy is punchy and powerful and the thighs are rolled in breadcrumbs for a satisfying crispy texture. There is no doubt that there is something to suit everyone on the à la carte menu, which seems endless. The homemade pasta is to die for. Mosconi embodies authentic flavour and bears the hallmark of a genuine talent for entrepreneurship!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3349;Apdikt;Luxembourg;Steinfort;1 rue des Martyrs, Steinfort, 8442, Luxembourg;49.6597175;5.9161488;83;false;true;Creative;Crispy parcels of grey shrimps with a frothy espuma of cod and samphire. The signature appetiser illustrates the high-flying nature of the experience you can expect in this former apothecary, which sports an authentic herringbone parquet floor and subtle references to mangas and comic strips. Chef Mathieu Van Wetteren voluntarily preserves the mystery of his surprise menu.Painstaking and with an eye for detail, he doesn’t however fall into the trap of overworking his recipes. His creativity aims more for simplicity and purity, rather than fussy frills. A rich millefeuille of celeriac cooked in hay and a noisette emulsion, or confit of salmon trout, cooked in soy and mirin, paired with a gutsy beurre blanc flavoured with trout roe, all of which is smoked and marinated in a fermented daikon jus: the menu rolls out a patchwork of big-boned, forthright flavours. This charismatic chef never fails to surprise!;;[]
3350;Le Cor de Chasse;Belgium;Wéris;rue des Combattants 16, Wéris, 6940, Belgium;50.32426;5.52895;93;false;true;Creative;You have arrived in one of the most beautiful villages of Wallonia. Eminently picturesque and set in woodland, Wéris is also home to this characterful restaurant. Behind a traditional Ardennes stone facade lies a classy demonstration of contemporary interior decoration, dripping in elegant comfort and commanding a fine view of the garden. Chef Mario Elias conjures up a creative score that can vary from complex to surprising, depending on his inspiration, but which is always flawlessly balanced, courtesy of his respectful use of fine local produce. He may enhance medium rare venison with red cabbage and kumquat, a terrine of sweet chestnuts and a bao bun stuffed with black tripe. The Elias family bends over backwards to pamper their guests and Jonas, the son, is always close at hand with insightful wine tips. Cooked from scratch with veg from their own kitchen garden. A premium destination for foodies!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3351;Le Pristine;Belgium;Antwerpen;Lange Gasthuisstraat 13, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2154966;4.4051934;89;true;true;Italian Contemporary;In this trendy district of Antwerp, Le Pristine is synonymous with Sergio Herman’s stylish trademark. The hip, laid-back café is open all day (with or without a booking) for casual snacks and nibbles such as mussels from Zeeland flavoured with lovage and savoury pecorino or a mini Mediterranean-style pizza on an aspic theme. The restaurant sports an upmarket, neo-industrial-loft vibe courtesy of a high ceiling, polished table service and a modish interior that mingles designer and vintage details. In the ubiquitous open-plan kitchen, Gianluca Vetrugno rolls out his manifold talents, blending Italian romanticism and seafood delights with great sensitivity. Balanced, fresh and acidic, even surprising at times, illustrated by a carpaccio of gambero rosso, jazzed up by bloody orange and pistachio. We recommend the spinach and ricotta cannelloni stuffed with Eastern Scheldt lobster and paired with a delicate mousseline sauce of champagne and fresh sea buckthorn. Purity and generosity go hand in hand at Le Pristine, which puts on a high-flying, world-class show every time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3352;Sense;Belgium;Waasmunster;Fortenstraat 62, Waasmunster, 9250, Belgium;51.1229343;4.1029001;39;false;true;Modern French;Classy, stylish, attention to detail, flavoursome – words fail us to describe Sense. The experience of veteran chef Michiel De Bruyn and the charm of your hostess, Frederika Vandeleur, are devoted to satisfying the expectations of their discerning diners. The restaurant’s pared down elegance and muted vibe provide the backdrop to a seamless performance without forgetting unusual food-wine pairings that are definitely worth writing home about. Chef Michiel’s minimalist approach seeks to enhance the ingredient: Zeebrugge sole, Guilvinec langoustine, frog’s legs from Dombes - only the best gets onto the menu here. The chef enhances such delicacies courtesy of classical techniques, like spit-roasting, but is equally at home with a Binchotan barbecue to fine-tune each individual texture. He might cook pigeon whole, using every part of the bird from the legs confit in butter to the offal crafted into cannelloni. He’s also a dab hand at subtle side dishes and sauces, such as a last minute velvety hollandaise sauce to die for or savoury veggie dishes, provencal asparagus and gutsy pigeon gravy. At Sense, you are guaranteed to taste authentic produce and flavours crafted by a virtuoso chef who can be trusted to treat you to a fine dining experience of rare delicacy. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3353;Sensum;Belgium;Sint-Denijs-Westrem;Kortrijksesteenweg 1026, Sint-Denijs-Westrem, 9051, Belgium;51.0236852;3.7029908;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The interior of this eye-catching mansion on the outskirts of Ghent is more than a match for its magnificent exterior. The revamp, which has preserved the edifice’s period elegance and historic character, sports a wealth of luxurious contemporary details that are the height of tasteful. Chef Maurice and your hostess and sommelier, Deborah, celebrate life with their guests from start to finish courtesy of a fine dining experience and knockout wines. The chef goes out of his way to source outstanding ingredients with the occasional passing nod to his Zeeland roots. His extensive technical background means that he is at home with a wide range of culinary methods, unusual combinations and international flavours. For example, he might pair king crab with a gutsy beurre blanc of shellfish and a tangy lemon jelly or he may add a kick to scallops courtesy of a dashi of Texel lamb prepared with typical Moroccan spices. The chef has no limits and demonstrates a fondness for servings that are presented in small portions. Sensum lifts your spirits while embarking you on a genuine voyage of the senses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3354;Marcus;Belgium;Deerlijk;Kleine Klijtstraat 30, Deerlijk, 8540, Belgium;50.8488967;3.3826144;100;true;false;Creative;A keen globetrotter, Gilles Joye takes our tastebuds on a world tour right from the appetisers. He has harnessed his creativity to showcasing local and international ingredients and refuses to be bound by a single culinary style. He particularly enjoys jazzing up his dishes with fresh acidic notes, while his stocks and sauces are a masterclass of big-boned intensity. He may cook red partridge medium rare, pairing it with a game sauce for added depth and long-lasting flavour. He then accentuates this wintry dimension by wrapping the thighs in a subtle yet rich Thai sauce. Powerful, yet simple. Quirkily located in a residential neighbourhood near the E17 motorway, you can expect a first-class experience courtesy of the chef’s consummate skill, Heike’s cheerful front-of-house service and the elegant modern interior.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3355;Menssa;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Pierre;Avenue de Tervueren 453, Woluwe-Saint-Pierre, 1150, Belgium;50.8228173;4.446563;99;false;true;Creative, Organic;Take a seat at the undulating counter, beneath the striking carved wooden tree, a tribute to nature, and enjoy the show as you admire the handiwork of the painstaking kitchen team. Menssa offers an all-round global experience and Christophe Hardiquest endeavours to share his vision of sustainable gastronomy, respect for producers and nature with diners.The experienced chef harnesses his knowhow and inventiveness to promoting his region. His knack for pairing mushrooms with a subtle blend of bitter coffee, smoked and marinated egg yolk and a vegetable emulsion demonstrates both his ethos and character. However, he also astounds by dishes like a fillet of Ardennes venison, which melts like butter in the mouth, that he flanks with a subtle game sauce and a truly outstanding and unexpected tempura of sweetbread. The insightful tips of the sommelier hit the spot every time as he finds just the right wine-food pairing – even better at prices that make sense. An establishment that is going from strength to strength.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3356;Hert;Belgium;Turnhout;Turnovatoren 18 (GPS: P.J. Brepolsplein), Turnhout, 2300, Belgium;51.3230729;4.9521178;79;true;false;Modern French, Creative;Alex Verhoeven devotes himself body and soul to his establishment and his industrial-cum-Scandinavian-cum-hip eatery is located in Turnova Tower. The view over the Campine is splendid. The chef deftly showcases outstanding produce in subtle creations, jazzed up by unusual inspirations. Knock-out wine list!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3357;EssenCiel;Belgium;Leuven;Bondgenotenlaan 114, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8805967;4.711476;38;false;true;Contemporary, Modern French;Established in a grand town house, EssenCiel is the lovingly created brainchild of a young couple, Niels Brants and Romina Charels. A smart contemporary style, mingling purity and elegance without losing sight of their signature casual vibe, sets the scene. A seat on the patio near the vegetable garden is heavenly in fine weather. Chef Brants deploys the full gamut of his culinary know-how combined with a flair for unearthing fantastic ingredients. He avows a passion for vegetables and the intricate craftsmanship of his unorthodox recipes is part of his hallmark. Our inspectors were most impressed by the culinary experience he created with three versions of gambero rosso. A stunningly fresh tartare, served with chilled, sweet and acidic sides, a mild chawanmushi of prawn in a Bellota ham aspic and a savoury emulsion of prawn heads with soy seeds macerated in Japanese herbs. The extensive choice of bread rolls means that you won’t have to miss the tiniest drop of the chef’s delicious sauces. Seasoned sommelier Luc Roelandt adds the final flourish with insightful wine tips. Today, more than ever, subtlety is the quintessence of EssenCiel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3358;Tinèlle;Belgium;Mechelen;Goswin de Stassartstraat 90, Mechelen, 2800, Belgium;51.033948;4.4800401;61;false;false;French Contemporary;The historic Predikheren served as a convent and military hospital from the 17C. Today it has morphed into a venue devoted to culture and fine dining. The left wing is home to this buzzy, modern eatery starring Jenny Callens in the dining room, while veteran chef Ken Verschueren joyfully dusts the cobwebs off culinary tradition. Ideal to dig into Franco-Belgian grub, free of futile frills or fuss and at prices that make sense. The chef demonstrates his love of fine produce, crafting dishes that bear witness to his consummate skill in the field of contrasts. Crab is a staple of the menu, with, for example, North Sea crab cannelloni, set off by a stunning marriage of acidic grapefruit and fresh fennel. Chef Verschueren deploys the full gamut of his culinary mastery in flawless slow-cooked shoulder of Kamper lamb, throwing in equal amounts of creativity and precision as he adds goat’s cheese and mustard lamb cooking juices. Tinèlle is synonymous with crisp, distinctive flavours and gutsy sauces. The high-flying wine list further confirms the establishment’s dedication to quality.;Terrace;[]
3359;Léa Linster;Luxembourg;Frisange;17 route de Luxembourg, Frisange, 5752, Luxembourg;49.51803;6.187337;50;true;true;Modern French;Louis Linster is adding a new chapter to this family saga of excellence, which started with his mum, Léa. The first woman to win the Bocuse d’Or award, she built up a distinguished reputation over the years and her son is confirming that elegance and delicacy are part and parcel of the Linster family’s DNA. Louis has seamlessly updated the house signature, courtesy of pared-back recipes that seek above all to get back to basics and to showcase the main ingredient. For example, he may add earthy mushrooms, a miso-flavoured mushroom sauce and a beurre noisette to enhance poached loin of brill. His knack with sauces is second to none, as is his flair for presentation and plating. This quintessentially sleek, classy restaurant is adorned with modern art and boasts a fantastic terrace overlooking the countryside. Léa can be proud of her son.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3360;l'Essentiel;Belgium;Temploux;rue Roger Clément 32, Temploux, 5020, Belgium;50.4754247;4.7387117;42;true;false;Creative French;This former tannery, set in an idyllic rural valley, has been converted into a delightful restaurant. The welcoming decor oozes with romanticism. The chef, whose classical training leaves no doubt, enjoys adding creative twists and spicing up the tastes of well - balanced dishes. Enjoy: that is what counts here!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3361;Table d'Amis;Belgium;Kortrijk;Sint-Maartenskerkhof 8, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.8279213;3.2681339;37;false;true;Modern French, Farm to table;Matthieu Beudaert is taking a fresh look at his gastronomic roots in the shade of St Martin’s Church. The uncluttered interior mingling modern designer and minimalist luxury details illustrates the chef’s immaculate taste. A passion for art continues to provide inspiration for this chef, who began his career in the art world before succumbing to his passion for cooking. His cuisine is a genuine ode to outstanding ingredients, including regional veggies and fish from the North Sea.His classical training comes to the forefront in the establishment’s popular signature dishes, among which smoked sweetbread on tobacco leaves, served with a creamy espresso and vermouth sauce. Matthieu Beudaert makes no secret of his love of the ingredient, as his delicate side dishes and impeccable seasonings demonstrate. Creamy, yet crunchy hispi cabbage, rich in aroma, and subtly spicy endives with a hint of coffee are paired with a perfectly cooked shoulder of pata negra pork.Matthieu Beudaert’s craftsmanship and artistry can be tasted and admired in a single set menu, flanked by a few signature dishes. The perfect place to spend time with friends and loved ones.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3362;Quai n°4;Belgium;Ath;quai Saint-Jacques 4, Ath, 7800, Belgium;50.6313017;3.7784136;96;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After studying at Ath Catering School, then working together (and becoming brothers-in-law), for the last few years Maxence Bouralha and Charles-Maxime Legrand have been business partners and are going from strength to strength at Quai N°4. Their fashionable eatery, which sports a tasteful green and gold colour scheme, attracts a fine dining crowd who flocks here to sample subtle recipes, founded on the chefs’ experience honed in high-flying establishments. They have a knack for striking the right balance between classicism and creativity. For example, they may flank calf’s sweetbread cooked in butter with langoustine and a creamy bisque of langoustine heads for added depth and intensity. Intelligent cuisine that hits the spot every time, paired with subtle sauces. Remember to save space for the desserts crafted by Charles-Maxime, whose virtuoso technique adds a genuine flourish and a refreshing finale to this feast.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3363;La Villa de Camille et Julien;;Luxembourg;5 rue de Pulvermühl, 2090, Luxembourg;49.6089034;6.1505965;63;false;true;French, Seasonal Cuisine;Camille and Julien’s knock-out villa is a genuine ode to fine dining. The elegant, yet quirky interior, strewn with knickknacks and flanked by a lovely cliffside terrace, is the epitome of stylish. Chef Lucas, fiercely committed to sustainable development, works with Luxembourg produce whenever possible and enjoys adding citrus notes to his suave Gallic recipes. Deftly crafted with lashings of know-how.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3364;Le Gastronome;Belgium;Paliseul;rue de Bouillon 2, Paliseul, 6850, Belgium;49.8953387;5.1178395;82;true;false;Contemporary, Farm to table;Jean Vrijdaghs and Sébastien Hankard have added a youthful buzz to this renowned restaurant. The premises and the guestrooms have been restored to their former luxury thanks to a contemporary renovation. Premium ingredients are painstakingly accompanied by vegetables from the restaurant’s garden, with a flawless attention to detail. A hint of acidity subtly completes the culinary score rich in powerful savours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3365;Quadras;Belgium;Saint Vith;Malmedyer Straße 53, Saint Vith, 4780, Belgium;50.2845008;6.1222378;32;false;true;Creative;Fleeing the limelight and media hype, Ricarda Grommes devotes herself body and soul to her elegant, trendy establishment, where you can feel and taste her quest for perfection. Ricarda’s inventive streak shines through in knockout appetisers and it is obvious that she attaches great importance to presentation, demonstrating a consummate grasp of modern techniques. Each dish is intelligently crafted and underscored by side dishes. The chef navigates effortlessly between French tradition and Eastern precision and you will taste regional produce and exotic ingredients. For example, she may coat scallops in white sesame seeds and pair them with raviolis stuffed with a gutsy pumpkin cream, chunks of pumpkin and a creamy sauce enhanced by pickles in vegetable oil. Ricarda Grommes’ cuisine is the quintessence of feminine elegance!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3366;Lettres Gourmandes;Belgium;Montignies-Saint-Christophe;route de Mons 52, Montignies-Saint-Christophe, 6560, Belgium;50.2854392;4.1833145;86;false;true;Creative French, Seasonal Cuisine;Adorned with paper airplanes, a tongue-in-cheek reference to its name, this handsome villa by a main road, backs onto the countryside. These gourmet letters read like a culinary declaration of love. The stylish establishment is the haunt of seasoned chef Christophe Lambert, who neatly avoids the trap of unnecessary complexity. Suave and generous, his inventive cuisine gives rise, for example, to fillets of sole served with a rich vegetable pesto and a fried egg with a perfectly runny yolk and a creamy shellfish concoction. Masterfully creative vegetable side dishes add an exquisite fresh touch combining subtly varied flavours and fascinating details. The enticing, bang-on carte bears witness to its creators’ wholehearted passion for food that is guaranteed to lift the spirits of discerning connoisseurs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3367;Au Gré du Vent;Belgium;Seneffe;rue de Soudromont 67, Seneffe, 7180, Belgium;50.5161633;4.2619825;73;false;false;Farm to table;A meal at Au Gré du Vent offers a splendid opportunity to explore the magnificent Hainaut countryside. Stéphanie and Sébastien Thunus converted a former barn into a fantastic restaurant, whose floor-to-ceiling windows open onto a landscaped garden. The visitor is initially impressed by the venue’s elegance, before sinking into its all-embracing cosy cocoon. Chef Stéphanie Thunus is a perfectionist who aims to make each dish a work of art with a distinct fondness for local, seasonal produce, such as game from Ardennes. Her culinary creations are subtle, distinctive and generous and nothing leaves her kitchen that hasn’t been endlessly puzzled and preened over. For example, she prepares tomatoes grown by her local producer in different ways, further jazzing them up with a bittersweet fresh dressing or she may underscore melt-in-the-mouth Limousin veal with a punchy gravy, a sauce made out of broad beans and agnolotti stuffed with aubergine caviar that will set your tastebuds tingling. Stephanie’s parents' farm, which supplies the butter and cheese among others, is just opposite and Ms Thunus has inherited a farmer’s respect for the ingredient to which she adds her own distinctive culinary flair. Stéphanie and Sébastien also run the Au Fil de l’Eau Hotel, whose elegant guestrooms provide the perfect climax to this fine dining experience.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3368;Innesto;Belgium;Zonhoven;Kapelhof 13, Zonhoven, 3520, Belgium;50.9874928;5.3687051;21;true;false;Creative;Koen Verjans’s cuisine is eminently stylish, in keeping with the classical, elegant décor of his prestigious establishment. His consummate culinary prowess enhances painstakingly sourced, first - class, fresh ingredients. Creativity at the service of food. Very pleasant rooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3369;La Roseraie;Belgium;Modave;route de Limet 80, Modave, 4577, Belgium;50.4541319;5.2866657;97;false;true;Modern French;A meal at La Roseraie is synonymous with a treat for all five senses. The experience starts with the drive through the lovely Ardennes countryside to this handsome 19C edifice, followed by the vision of the landscaped garden, home to welcoming guestrooms and pretty cottages, and the elegant restaurant, depicted by an exquisite blend of luxury details and home-from-home hospitality. Marie Trignon has respectfully and masterfully taken over the reins from her father.You can expect a classical culinary repertory, flanked by a flair for sourcing the best ingredients, without forgetting a passion for spices and a creative streak rich in delicacy. Chef Trignon enhances a fillet of red mullet with a curcuma-flavoured tabouleh, a tomato salad rich in refreshing hints of coriander and dill and sweet-sour broccoli stalks. She has a knack for crafting felicitous seasonings that underscore without overpowering delicate ingredients such as scallops. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3370;FRANQ;Belgium;Antwerpen;Kipdorp 10, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2211509;4.4057647;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;FRANQ is awash in the same restrained glamour as its namesake hotel, i.e., a posh townhouse dripping in well-heeled class and understated luxury. Tropical artwork adds an individual touch, while the secluded patio shelters you from the bustle of the city. The open-plan kitchen showcases Tim Meuleneire and his brigade weaving their magic. The chef is noted for his technical wizadry, in particular in the field of sauces, such as the truffle sauce served with venison. However, his almost ethereal pistachio-flavoured soufflé subtly combined with a hint of strawberry is similarly out of this world. Classical and avant-garde all at once, the culinary score deserves our applause. Subtle nuances and international influences unveil the chef’s voluntarily modern sensibility, yet FRANQ is the antithesis of flashy cookery shows. The focus is rather on dependable elegance and authentic flavours. The sleek attentive service adds the final flourish to this culinary masterpiece.;Terrace;[]
3371;Carcasse;Belgium;Sint-Idesbald;Henri Christiaenlaan 5, Sint-Idesbald, 8670, Belgium;51.1098819;2.6110153;81;false;false;Meats and Grills;At Hendrik Dierendonck’s establishment, the meat comes straight from the butchers to the plate – in fact, Carcasse is literally the extension of his shop in Saint Idesbald. The hip interior provides the perfect foil to the raw vibe of a butcher’s shop. The soundtrack features guitars strumming, but the star of the show is clearly red meat. A glazed ageing cabinet takes pride of place in the centre, while runners on the ceiling bear witness to a bygone era when the carcasses were shunted overhead. A long communal table is designed to encourage diners to share this experience. The exceptional cuts of meat of this renowned butcher are consummately and creatively prepared, perfectly seasoned and cooked in a Josper charcoal oven by chef Timon Michiels. The perfect place to find out more about how meat is aged and about different cattle breeds. Rather than fries or over-powering sauces, you can expect delicate side dishes rich in flavour: thyme-flavoured vinaigrette, subtly spicy horseradish cream and marinated cauliflower are served with a full-bodied carpaccio of beef tongue. In their own words: “Where meat is lord and master and veggies take pride of place!” A treat every time!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3372;Het Gebaar;Belgium;Antwerpen;Leopoldstraat 24, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2138863;4.4068949;72;false;false;Creative, Asian Influences;Roger van Damme’s reputation for stellar desserts needs no introduction and this is the place to sample his creations from a truly wicked dame blanche (vanilla ice cream and hot chocolate) to a tiramisu to die for! But the pastry chef is also a wizard savoury chef, as a trip to his modern “gingerbread house” near Stadsschouwburg will convince you. Following a swish revamp, Het Gebaar - opened in 1994 - sports a luxurious, yet casual vibe. Van Damme’s attention to detail is visible at every stage of your meal and nothing leaves the kitchen that hasn’t been puzzled over and preened to perfection. His distinctive, supremely elegant recipes celebrate familiar flavours, albeit with a creative twist. His talent for traditional dishes such as Beef Wellington is second to none thanks to his consummate pastry skills. The establishment, which only serves lunch and dessert, closes at 6pm, but, beware, the tables are often snapped up fast, so book ahead!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3373;Kamo;Belgium;Ixelles;chaussée de Waterloo 550a, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8193858;4.3615157;95;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Kamo is a slice of Tokyo in the heart of Ixelles. The decor is pared back and contemporary, with wooden finishings providing a distinctive touch. From the bar you can witness chef Kamo's meticulous artistry firsthand. Once you are seated, he serves you an amuse-bouche to cleanse your palate. Then you are all set to experience the finesse of Japanese culinary tradition. Chef Kamo's seemingly effortless dishes showcase the extraordinary quality and freshness of his ingredients. He does not rely on luxury produce to wow his diners. The sashimi of the day is a classic for a reason: it's amazing how pieces of raw fish can be transformed into something so sublime – the epitome of unadorned simplicity! Lunch is slightly more traditional and includes made-to-order sushi. In the evenings, the chef pulls out all the stops with surprise tasting menus. Kamo's sheer subtlety is a celebration of the versatility of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
3374;Sel Gris;Belgium;Knokke;Zeedijk 314, Knokke, 8301, Belgium;51.344112;3.2563193;97;true;true;Creative;Twenty shades of grey comprise the suave, understated interior of Sel Gris, whose cosy comfort is underscored by designer fixtures and luxury finishings. However, the windows take centre stage here, as the restaurant stands on the dike and commands a knockout view of the beach and the North Sea, which are a source of inspiration for Frederik Deceuninck, whose enthusiasm can be tasted right from the appetisers. He mingles creativity and delicacy in expertly crafted recipes, often presented in several plates with a meticulous sense of detail. A few examples of his fascinating dishes: a subtle, elegant association of salmon and asparagus or pheasant served with a champagne and foie gras sauce. Frederick’s culinary flair reaches its summum in the vegetables, acidic flavours and Asian inspirations. Each bite is a festival of unprecedented flavours that interact and complement each other. The ingredient rules supreme at Sel Gris.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
3375;Alter;Belgium;Tongeren;Bilzersteenweg 366, Tongeren, 3700, Belgium;50.8024317;5.4657753;51;true;true;Creative;Alter means “different” or “other”, which illustrates Jo Grootaers’ career. He was just 19 when he became the chef of the Altermezzo, gradually forging his own culinary signature to the point of being awarded a MICHELIN star. Today he and his partner, Lana in the front of house, are at the helm of this restaurant, established in the former village school, which has been treated to a hip, designer makeover. The couple’s shared passion can be tasted in the fine wines and remarkably delicate, creative cuisine. The chef’s attention to detail is particularly notable in the exquisite plating. What’s more, his modern culinary approach is focused on shining the spotlight on the ingredient. Scallops, for example, enjoy the star role, between fresh, succulent celeriac, a beurre blanc with kombu seaweed and a sea urchin cream overflowing in savoury nuances. In addition to cutting-edge precision, the chef firmly believes that sauces should be tasty and generous. Jo Grootaers’ youthful enthusiasm is maturing and blossoming thanks to immaculate craftsmanship. A chef who has found his path!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3376;Rebelle;Belgium;Marke;Rekkemsestraat 226, Marke, 8510, Belgium;50.8039661;3.2218248;40;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative French;Youthful, fuss-free and easy-going, Rebelle aims to serve excellent nosh in a casual vibe. Behind its unassuming façade, you will discover a warm, minimalist interior decked in salmon and terracotta colours. The man behind the creative score, Martijn Defauw, rustles up fascinating food and knockout seasonings, often with an oriental twist, that come up trumps every time. He has a knack for sourcing the best produce, such as flawlessly fresh North Sea fish or locally grown tender young hop shoots. His close relationship with his producers is a source of inspiration, as are his travels. For example, he may coat Miéral duck in honey and a mixture of spices before roasting it on the bone and then serving it with a delicious peppery sauce to enhance and add a further kick to the mouth-wateringly tender meat. Acidic carrots and a gutsy sweet and sour apricot ketchup provide a subtle Asian flourish. The full-bodied flavours of each dish are further enhanced by a superlative wine cellar and the sommeliers may suggest natural or classical tipples to pair with chef Defauw’s culinary masterpieces. To quote them: “Warm, Pure, Unique” - a meal at Rebelle is felicitous from start to finish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3377;Horseele;Belgium;Gent;Ottergemsesteenweg-Zuid 808a, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0171863;3.7336248;70;true;false;Modern French;This match kicks off at the modern stadium of Ghent Football Club. In 24 seconds flat, an elevator whisks you up to the fourth floor and another world! The warm interior, both cosy and urbane, features a piano and works of art in a lounge vibe that brings to mind a Gentleman’s Club. In this establishment, Danny Horseele, a minimum of one Michelin star for over thirty years, rolls out his infinite know-how in the company of a loyal brigade. The food is traditional and polished, yet subtly creative, and combined with a passion for outstanding local ingredients that can be tasted right from the start. His langoustine extravaganza served in three dishes reveals one poached version in particular, flanked by powerful side dishes such as sea buckthorn and oyster leaf, together with puffed quinoa, a reduction of XO sauce, sesame seeds, a truly hearty cream of tomato and a punchy shellfish emulsion. His wizardry with sauces is definitely worth writing home about. The chef’s extensive experience and his team’s contemporary input are melded into an enticing culinary portrait. A blue-ribbon establishment that delivers the goods every time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
3378;L'Envie;Belgium;Sint-Denijs;Helkijnstraat 38, Sint-Denijs, 8554, Belgium;50.7499139;3.3705692;35;false;false;Modern French;Take a seat in this classy establishment to sample the creative food of an experienced chef. Inès will bowl you over with her impressive “Bible” of wines (mainly French with a knockout choice of champagnes), which are paired with David Grosdent’s innovative dishes, rich in fascinating nuances. An uncompromising fan of fine produce, such as scallops from Dieppe or venison from the Ardennes, he deploys his culinary craft in an impressive display of classicism combined with modern, even amusing touches. He smokes the local game in hay before cooking it to perfection, adding a subtle sauce. Winter side dishes, such as beetroot, cranberries and Jerusalem artichokes add an interesting contemporary twist, which is further enhanced by the subtle balance of acidic and bitter flavours. The chef frequently prepares the same ingredient in different ways, deploying consummate craftsmanship, whilst adding his own inimitable hallmark. Fine dining at its best!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3379;La Table Benjamin Laborie;Belgium;Ohain;Rue du Try Bara 33, Ohain, 1380, Belgium;50.6986094;4.4695619;36;false;false;French Contemporary, Creative French;The view over the rolling hills of Lasne cannot fail but draw your eye as you take a seat in this contemporary eatery. Designer and authentic details have been cleverly mixed in this characterful edifice. The tables on the patio are taken by storm whenever the weather permits. Connoisseurs of exceptional ingredients can now devote their attention to the culinary treats crafted by Benjamin Laborie, whose opulent menu features delicacies such as porcini, seabass and venison from Ardennes.The chef’s talent for spot-on cooking is on a par with the world’s master chefs and he enhances carefully sourced produce by delicate creative touches. An emulsion of Jura vin jaune is paired for example with the subtle acidity of a confit of yellow onions from Cévennes, in a bid to exalt each ingredient’s characteristics. Fragrant black truffle and a concentrated stock of onion add an entirely new dimension to onion soup. Knockout sauces and intelligent combinations create a festival of flavours. Without forgetting Guillaume Vegreville, maître d’ hors pair, who ensures that your meal is as smooth as a silky bearnaise sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3380;De Mijlpaal;Belgium;Tongeren;Sint-Truiderstraat 25, Tongeren, 3700, Belgium;50.7803846;5.4616897;65;true;true;Creative;As you explore the oldest town of Belgium, we recommend venturing down this pretty pedestrian lane to number 25. You will first be surprised by the elegant modernity of the interior, rich in cosy details and designer touches. After An has graciously seated you at your table, Jan Menten rolls out his creative talents. Premium ingredients like langoustine and Anjou pigeon reveal all their complexity thanks to consummate traditional technique. The chef adds an unexpected twist to familiar flavours with subtle touches and side dishes of Mediterranean inspiration. He cooks monkfish in a noisette butter, adding depth with chorizo, a subtly, spicy curry cream and panipuri filled with peppers. Chef Menten’s surgically precise and instantly recognisable cooking is dotted with international aromas that invigorate his recipes. Mijpaal means “milestone” and we warrant that this eatery will be a landmark for all discerning food connoisseurs.;Terrace;[]
3381;La Grappe d'Or;Belgium;Arlon;Route de Luxembourg 317, Arlon, 6700, Belgium;49.6610743;5.8492842;63;false;true;French Contemporary, Creative French;Eminently in tune with his region, Clément Petitjean is a proud ambassador of this province of Luxemburg and he works even more closely with local producers since moving to Autelbas near Arlon. The view of the meadows and the natural vibe of the contemporary interior encourage the diner to commune with nature, particularly beneath the fine-meshed cloud structures hanging from the ceiling. Make your pick from the sommelier’s splendid cocktail trolley, before sampling Petitjean’s felicitous cuisine.He cites the names of the suppliers whose ingredients are featured in his cooking, enhancing their hard work with, for example, acidic fermented notes, in a bid to strike the perfect balance between distinctive flavours and the intensity of the core sustainable ingredient. Petitjean may serve duck by Marc Lamy or Malines cuckoo by Steve Pierre, cooked whole, and attaches great importance to the work of the kitchen staff, which he accentuates by side dishes such as creamy confit of carrots or smoky-flavoured Chinese artichoke, a masterclass of subtlety. A highly personal and inspired celebration of the region from the first to the last delicious bite.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3382;Pré de chez vous;Belgium;Bouge;Chaussée de Louvain 380, Bouge, 5004, Belgium;50.4738488;4.8728194;84;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Julien Malaisse pays frequent visits to the best Wallon producers, whose first-class ingredients he has been championing for eons. Beef from Nicolas Debry and veg from Régis unveil all their nuances in the chef’s unorthodox cuisine. Malaisse takes the time to lovingly craft powerful sauces, which he serves himself, adding a wide range of varied yet coherent flavours by way of inventive side dishes.Raviolis stuffed in Jerusalem artichoke and cooked in a salt crust are paired with a clementine jelly, a sabayon of Cantillon beer and a hint of black truffle. The veteran sommelier can be relied on to suggest pairings that may surprise but which will subtly balance your meal thanks to his in-depth knowledge. It feels as if you’re eating in the chef’s home thanks to the log-burning fire and open-plan kitchen - we only wish that this friendly eatery were in our own backyard!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3383;DIM Dining;Belgium;Antwerpen;Vrijdagmarkt 7, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2183721;4.3992103;29;false;false;Asian;DIM Dining is bathed in a calm, cosy vibe, created by a compelling blend of Japanese purity and Western luxury. The best seats are at the counter, which commands a view of the chefs at work. In keeping with the decor, the latter craft an intelligent cocktail of oriental delicacy with gutsy Gallic overtones. Asian cuisine is the playground of inventive chef Simon van Dun and his team, who playfully and unexpectedly work with authentic local ingredients throbbing in rugged tastes and aromas. The diner’s curiosity is constantly tickled as each mouthful seeks to surprise and astound. For example, duck cooked whole and continually basted in wagyu fat results in medium rare meat loaded in big-boned flavours. This is then flanked by a subtle gravy of duck juices and dark strong ale from the OWA Brussels brewery, without forgetting fresh, crisp side vegetables. Renowned sommelier and sake master, Jonas Kellens, rolls out his know-how by pairing the above dish with a 1984 All Koji sake in a match made in heaven! A whirlwind of culinary delight that leaves no one indifferent!;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
3384;Hofke van Bazel;Belgium;Bazel;Koningin Astridplein 11, Bazel, 9150, Belgium;51.1471664;4.3002815;85;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, French Contemporary;When Kris de Roy is not in the kitchen, he's invariably to be found in the impressive cottage garden just down the road (and also well worth a visit!). Nature and a steadfast love of fine produce guide and inspire De Roy’s approach to cooking. From carrots and strawberries to pigeon, only the very best will do and fresh vegetables and herbs form the backbone of chef De Roy’s bold, creative cuisine, whether in confits, glazed, stewed or in frothy juices. He surprises with show-stopping recipes, such as tartare of langoustine and tangy lemon paired with a velvety bisque flan, a flaky pastry biscuit, a cream of parmesan, kohlrabi, green peas and glazed pralines in Greek yoghurt and ponzu. A fresh, vibrant combination depicted by perfectly balanced touches of umami. A feast of delicacy! Take a peek at the caviar bar and possibly treat yourself to a truly indulgent titbit… Rural charm and a romantic vibe create the perfect setting to sample these delights of nature, possibly alfresco in the gorgeous garden that is distinctly reminiscent of northern Italy. This enchanting portrait is further enhanced by a collection of Michelin Guides, a wine cellar (visible through the glazed floor) and luxurious suites for overnight stays just next-door.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3385;Zur Post;Belgium;Saint Vith;Hauptstraße 39, Saint Vith, 4780, Belgium;50.2803313;6.1261435;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The Pankert family has been delighting food lovers for three generations. That dependable experience is reflected in the menu, which features quality ingredients and flawless dishes in a reinvented classic style. And if you start feeling sleepy, just head for that four - poster bed in your room.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3386;Arabelle Meirlaen;Belgium;Marchin;chemin de Bertrandfontaine 7, Marchin, 4570, Belgium;50.4863858;5.2218357;31;true;true;Organic, Creative;Arabelle Meirlaen crafts a highly personal version of healthy food, guided by her intuition and a desire to shine the spotlight on veggies and spices. In fact, a large proportion of the fresh produce comes from her own kitchen garden. Meirlaen is inventive, yet elegant and unafraid of the odd bold touch, whilst steering clear of the trap of surprising us at all costs. An unusual lineup of light dishes, depicted by full-bodied generous flavours. When she cooks fish or meat, she always endeavours to seamlessly craft each ingredient into her polished recipe. Floral aromas are something of her hallmark and the desserts, which are out of this world, are emblematic of this penchant. How about thin slices of watermelon, marinated in rice vinegar and then poached at a low temperature? All of which is served on a seaweed salad with a creamy goat’s cheese, sesame seeds and uda pepper. This knockout recipe embodies the chef’s culinary vision. The bright interior of the splendid restaurant provides the perfect foil to the natural intuitive character and cooking of this grand dame! To finish, take the time to explore the pretty country village of Marchin before or after (or both) your meal.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3387;Hof Ter Hulst;Belgium;Hulshout;Kerkstraat 33, Hulshout, 2235, Belgium;51.0769653;4.793442;37;false;true;French, Classic French;Some establishments just know how to warm the cockles of one’s heart and Hof Ter Hulst is one such. The delightful Campine farmhouse has morphed into a characterful venue and as soon as you set foot inside the door, you understand that Johan Schroven doesn’t mess around with tradition, as his rich score demonstrates. The first bite of the langoustine, which is crafted with textbook precision, bears witness to the outstanding quality of the ingredients, further enhanced by a refreshing zest of lemon, without forgetting a creamy oxtail stew, truffles and a rich gravy that complete this exquisite surf and turf dish. Rather than outlandish fancy frills or jaw-dropping culinary techniques, you can expect wholehearted, feelgood food that warms the soul and the stomach. A lineup of family favourites that hits the spot every time!;Car park,Terrace;[]
3388;Le Pigeon Noir;Belgium;Uccle;rue Geleytsbeek 2, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7920083;4.3482107;52;false;true;Country cooking, Classic French;“A pigeon might be dumber than a dolphin – but at least it can fly…” – this quote on the homepage of Le Pigeon Noir is emblematic of the establishment’s wry sense of humour. The authentic vintage interior is perfectly suited to the cheerful, village cafe vibe of this buzzy bistro. Tightly packed tables, a few seats at the counter, red velvet curtains, traditionally garbed waiting staff and the bonus of a charismatic jovial boss. On the menu: traditional Gallic grub devoid of fussy frills and tiresome modern gimmicks. Wholesome, family favourites take the limelight here in dishes oozing in nostalgia and crafted with no-nonsense textbook perfection. Where else do they still serve a light fluffy soufflé of langoustines flanked by an incredible sauce made with the shells and heads? We also recommend another house signature: smoked herring in olive oil garnished with finely sliced red onions and boiled baby potatoes. The ideal venue for a slap-up meal with all the traditional trimmings…;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3390;senzanome;Belgium;Brussels;place du Petit Sablon 1, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8400093;4.3566706;91;true;false;Italian, Sicilian;Giovanni Bruno adds his own personal spin to nostalgic Italian recipes that he learned in the family restaurant. senzanome has been showered with awards since it opened in 1997. Today its stylish, uncluttered dining room adorned in soft warm colours is the epitome of good taste and perfectly in tune with the well-heeled Sablon district. Chef Bruno pays homage to authentic recipes, transforming them with modern techniques, yet always in a bid to allow the ingredient to shout its name. Italian generosity meets subtle craftsmanship as the Italian chef adds his own hallmark to familiar flavours. His signature dish: a velvety compact mousse of stracciatella with a tomato sorbet and basil-perfumed oil features three ingredients that are blended together in a knockout harmony of taste and aroma. We also recommend the braised seabass overflowing in savoury, sweet and spicy notes and liberally sprinkled in sultana raisins marinated in vinegar. Food lovers who appreciate an extensive choice will be in seventh heaven from the lunchtime menus and à la carte menu to the wine list – paradise for all five senses!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3391;'t Stoveke;Belgium;Strombeek-Bever;Jetsestraat 52, Strombeek-Bever, 1853, Belgium;50.9049469;4.3507766;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Daniel Antuna pampers his guests from the warm welcome to the final goodbye as they leave with a satisfied smile on their lips. An open kitchen ensures that you won’t miss any crumbs of the culinary show in this restaurant, where you will feel both at home and as if you are a VIP guest. Chef Antuna deploys state-of-the-art culinary techniques without betraying his classical training. His unique sense of flavour is superlatively enriched by Asian influences. For example, you might sample a perfectly cooked fillet of halibut with caramelised Belgian endive and an endive cream of Grimbergen beer, beer-flavoured smoked eel stock and a subtle jelly of sweet leeks. Culinary heaven! He manages to add a whole new dimension to familiar flavours. The chef adores cooking veggies, as his mouth-watering vegetarian menu demonstrates. Innovation at the service of the ingredients’ intrinsic flavour is the house motto.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3392;EED;Belgium;Leuven;Vaartstraat 14, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.880639;4.7024848;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;Ambitious Philippe Heylen is proud of his house - made recipes. The preparation of the food runs like clockwork based on a few painstakingly selected ingredients, whose diverse flavours deliciously complement each other. Free of frills, the focus is rather on characteristic, surprising and fascinating ingredients. A cosy, elegant establishment under the sign of youthful enthusiasm.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3393;Fleur de Lin;Belgium;Zele;Lokerenbaan 100, Zele, 9240, Belgium;51.0760145;4.041179;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Nothing leaves the kitchen that Lode De Roover has not preened to make perfect. From the surgically sliced vegetables to the high-flying cooking and inspired plating, this amateur of outstanding classical produce leaves nothing to chance. Sure, he has a creative streak, but his talent lies first and foremost in his 100% reliable cooking. He crafts langoustine in two ways: raw in a tartare with spicy zests of chives, ponzu and playful basil and dill notes. A second plate showcases barbecued langoustine with fermented black lemon, salty seaweed and a knockout sauce of langoustine heads – De Roover has a knack for combining a few highly distinctive ingredients into dishes that impress by their fabulous harmony. All the more reason to book a table at Fleur de Lin. This pared-down, contemporary establishment set in a former linen manufacture illustrates and proves the overriding importance of consistency and quality in the catering business.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3394;Sans Cravate;Belgium;Brugge;Langestraat 159, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2123748;3.2381662;87;true;true;Creative French, Creative;As the name suggests (Without a tie), this eatery is casual in vibe. The snug interior, done up in pastel shades, is bathed in natural light. Despite a lineup of familiar flavours, Sans cravate knows how to surprise the diner. The concise à la carte menu, together with a weekday menu and a several course menu at the weekend, bear witness to the attention lavished on exceptional ingredients by chef Henk Van Oudenhouve. He might mingle textures, such as langoustine and artichoke, with a punchy bisque made out of shellfish heads, and cooks the mullet on a spit in a delicious Mediterranean dish featuring nduja, aromatic herbs and choron sauce. Like a champion downhill skier, Van Oudenhove expertly weaves between classical flavours and international accents. Don’t miss the game season, when you may be able to taste tender juicy partridge. You may even decide to treat yourself and stay overnight in one of the luxurious rooms of the B&B La Suite opposite.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
3395;Nathan;Belgium;Antwerpen;Lange Koepoortstraat 13, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2231806;4.4027957;35;true;false;Modern French;Nathan Van Echelpoel appreciates beauty, as the bold dark marble and wooden fixtures and fittings confirm. Nathan combines the Belgian flair for interior decoration with a Scandinavian ethos. As if art directed, each dish is emblematic of this painstaking attention to the tiniest detail and each plate is a masterpiece of presentation. Virtuoso chef Van Echelpoel mixes his classical culinary background with a playful contemporary streak, jazzing up familiar flavours with Asian acidic notes. Delicately wrapped fillet of cod is offset by a scoop of yuzu, while a foaming white butter sauce perfumed with dashi and yuzu further exalts the floral qualities of the dish. Subtlety and delicacy are second nature to Nathan who is constantly seeking to create and provoke new sensations with an unflagging attention to detail. A treat for the eye as much as for the tastebuds.;Air conditioning;[]
3396;Zet'Joe by Geert Van Hecke;Belgium;Brugge;Langestraat 11, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2097162;3.2321611;63;true;false;Creative French;Geert Van Hecke, who boasted three Michelin stars for twenty years at the Karmeliet, is definitely worthy of the title “Godfather of Belgian gastronomy”. Zet’Joe is more casual and a little bit like walking into the chef’s home. A warm interior and an impressive art collection instantly set the scene. Mireille, his delightful partner in the dining room, wields the cheese trolley with impressive dexterity. Van Hecke harnesses his consummate knowhow and sensitivity to enhancing first-rate ingredients. A silky last-minute béarnaise sauce, made with carrot and orange jus, coaxes out the full flavour of lightly seared scallops, further flanked by an awesome millefeuille of aniseed-flavoured earthy veggies. The chef effortlessly deploys his culinary wizardry and insights in a truly classy act. In addition to food that will set all your tastebuds tingling, you can expect the attentions of an elegant maitre d’, who discreetly embodies the establishment’s friendly vibe. “Bon appétit” is all that is left to say!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3397;JER;Belgium;Hasselt;Persoonstraat 16, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9308782;5.3405435;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Good food has no need of fancy, fussy frills, as Wim Schildermans so masterfully illustrates. In a tastefully restored manor house that has lost none of its period elegance, this high-flying maestro rolls out his “Just Eat Right” concept. First of all, he sources top-drawer, preferably local ingredients, and then deploys his consummate skill and talent. Chef Schildermans cooks boldly and has no qualms about surprising diners, illustrated by pigeon: a perfectly juicy pink breast, a confit of leg, crispy potatoes, a full-bodied pigeon sauce, delicately strewn with coffee and sweet cherry notes and a rose-flavoured mousse that adds the final surprising flourish, bringing together and balancing the formidable range of powerful flavours. Attention to detail is paramount and each bite gives rise to a whole new range of sensations, capturing and pampering the tastebuds from the appetisers to the dessert. The wines are expertly curated and accompanied by the enthusiastic recommendations and explanations of the highly knowledgeable sommelier. Simply good food!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3398;Humus x Hortense;Belgium;Ixelles;rue de Vergnies 2, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8294878;4.3703766;29;false;false;Creative, Organic;Chef Nicolas Decloedt and the lady of the house and sommelière, Caroline Baerten, were championing plant-based cuisine long before it became trendy. Their sustainable ethos and creativity have been a source of inspiration for many, what’s more they publish a sustainability report that can be consulted online by all and sundry. We warrant that a meal in this stylish, street corner building adorned with frescoes of angels and gilded ceilings will be an unforgettable experience.The micro-seasons are reverently respected thanks to their close collaboration with botanist-farmer Dries Delanote and other craftsmen and women. Light years from fads and fashions, zero waste is a state of mind here, leading to a bold, new, innovative look at gastronomy. A personal retake on the Paris-Brest dessert with matured celeriac, foaming quince, punchy horseradish and a celeriac and apple juice to coax all the flavours out of the vegetables. The sommelière deploys her immense talent in creations that may feature amazake, sake, milky oolong tea and vodka, in a bid to further exalt the chef’s exuberant recipes. Each dish triggers our curiosity and awakens our appetites. Humus x Hortense is in a class of its own.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3399;Centpourcent;Belgium;Sint-Katelijne-Waver;Antwerpsesteenweg 1, Sint-Katelijne-Waver, 2860, Belgium;51.0557914;4.463224;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Axel Colonna-Cesari, a master craftsman in every sense of the word, is at the summum of his art, and he and his charming wife, Anneleen, form a splendid team. Their contemporary establishment is a model of classy elegance, sporting soft colours and fashionable furnishings. Centpourcent is a blue-chip value, as is quickly apparent from the crowd of regulars, and is ideal for any occasion from a high-powered business lunch to a romantic dinner. The chef’s consummate know-how and structured creativity can be tasted in light, exuberant cuisine, overflowing in fresh, delicately crafted flavours. Asian inspirations often underscore the fresh ingredients, such as yellow pollock and bouchot mussels with a tangy, acidic combava sauce, veggies and a curry and Granny Smith-flavoured oil. The pinnacle of delicate craftsmanship! You can also trust the sommelier to dig out an unusual vintage, or even beer (he brews his own with his brother!). He can also suggest an excellent lineup of non-alcoholic beverages. Centpourcent is a 100% knockout establishment!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
3400;'t Korennaer;Belgium;Nieuwkerken-Waas;Nieuwkerkenstraat 4, Nieuwkerken-Waas, 9100, Belgium;51.1929468;4.1781069;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Edwin Van Goethem is always on the move. Since the opening of 't Korennaer in 1997, he has continued to evolve. With a sure hand, he enriches his cuisine with subtle international influences. These range from Japanese seasonings to elements of North African culinary tradition. Thanks to trusted suppliers such as butcher Hendrik Dierendonck and asparagus grower Els Vercauteren, top-notch ingredient quality is guaranteed. The chef lets the natural flavours take centre stage in dishes that are very much on trend. First-rate produce such as hop shoots and wagyu meat are elevated with rich sauces, exotic condiments and garnishes that keep diners on their toes. He serves venison fillet, for example, with a fabulous sauce based on sea buckthorn berry, tamarind and meat juices. The sophistication of 't Korennaer is further reflected in the opulence of its stylish interior and the tranquillity of its outdoor seating area. Nevertheless, there is a convivial family atmosphere here, and chef Van Goethem's enthusiasm is infectious.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3401;Bistro Racine;Belgium;Braine-le-Château;place de la Station 3, Braine-le-Château, 1440, Belgium;50.6814685;4.2730837;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This laidback bistro is proof that a MICHELIN star isn’t always synonymous with luxury. In fact, why shouldn’t it simply be a friendly establishment that serves good food, as is the case at the buzzy Bistro Racine? Jimmy Collodoro regales his guests with painstakingly sourced, premium produce. The market-fresh, seasonal dishes, chalked up on a slate, change regularly, without forgetting the house classics, such as beef grilled in a Mibrasa charcoal oven. The food is finely crafted and a tad unconventional, yet refreshingly straightforward. Unexpected details add a humorous twist, illustrated by melt-in-the-mouth mackerel marinated in beetroot juice, flanked by slow-roasted beetroot and whipped horseradish cream to jazz things up. Or you might taste a crunchy meringue, smothered in vanilla custard and topped with chestnut purée and a sweet potato cream. 100% authentic food that surprises and hits the spot every time, whilst remaining blessedly free of prissy, play-it-safe food. Don’t miss the lunchtime menu, which is a steal!;Air conditioning;[]
3402;Aux petits oignons;Belgium;Jodoigne;chaussée de Tirlemont 260, Jodoigne, 1370, Belgium;50.7419555;4.8801357;17;true;false;Modern French, French;Every detail of Stéphane Lefebvre’s aptly named establishment has been endlessly fine-tuned, as the top-to-toe renovation demonstrates. Brightly welcoming, the contemporary interior mingles Scandinavian influences with discreet nods to the Seventies. The attentive table service and cosy vibe instantly make you feel at home. Chef Lefebvre has harnessed his creative talent in a bid to celebrate flavour and ingeniously balances a dish’s bitterness or acidity with a few well-judged side dishes. His attention to detail shines the spotlight on outstanding ingredients such as Piétrain pork and Ardennes game. He might pair immaculately cooked scallops with sweet parsnips, subtly smoky eel and an exquisite drizzle of watercress, without forgetting the final flourish of tartare of smoked scallops, adorned in the roe and mild chili pepper. His stellar talent and know-how have found favour with a large crowd of discerning regulars. The varied seasonal theme (seafood, game, etc.) menus and extensive à la carte offering are packed in enticing appeal and exciting gourmet discoveries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3403;De Bakermat;Belgium;Ninove;Leopoldlaan 95, Ninove, 9400, Belgium;50.8264868;4.0215597;89;false;false;Modern French;Leave busy Leopoldlaan behind you, venture over the threshold of this spruce white villa and bask in the charming welcome of Barbara and chef Kevin. The couple is proud of their stylish establishment, appointed in a more modern vein to the rear and which sports an eye-catching glazed wine cellar. Over the years, De Bakermat has become a firm fixture on Ninove’s culinary scene.The secret to good food resides in the quality of the ingredients, which isn’t as simple as it sounds. Chef Kevin not only sources top-drawer produce such as turbot, truffles and premium breeds of meat, such as Holstein, he deploys immaculate craftsmanship to conjure up succulent dishes. The classic association of foie gras, brioche bread and quince undergoes a touch of wizardry in his deft hands as he enhances the rich velvety liver flavour. He intelligently mixes familiar flavours with exotic ingredients or plays on contrasting textures, such as a mustard and soy sauce served with veal or his knockout medley of aubergine, courgette and almonds. Chef Kevin is a past master in the art of combining generosity and delicacy. The expert tips and insights of the knowledgeable sommelier and the enticing wine list (also available by the glass) add the final flourish to this delectable portrait.;Car park;[]
3404;Brasserie Julie;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Bodegem;Dorpsplein 3, Sint-Martens-Bodegem, 1700, Belgium;50.8611708;4.2126098;84;true;true;Home Cooking, Creative French;Thomas Locus is determined to create an immersive experience for his patrons whether they are dining in his cosy contemporary farmstead or on the comfortable garden terrace, or indeed spending the night at his bucolic B&B. Quality is the name of the game here. The entrepreneurial chef even runs a wine shop and, a little further down the road, another restaurant, Agnes. A meal at Brasserie Julie simply has to start with some of the international appetisers available for sharing. Almejas à la marinera, nobashi shrimp with shichimi… What a feast! It is immediately clear that chef Locus has his own unique way of approaching the classics – a few choice ingredients and creative sides suffice to create an intense taste experience. This is ingredient-led cuisine through and through, by a chef who gives familiar flavours a delicate boost. Even all-time favourites such as steak tartare and Dame Blanche are given an extra dimension here. The game dishes, such as the grey partridge roasted on the bone, are also excellent. This next-level brasserie is a paradise for discerning foodies.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3405;Kelderman;Belgium;Aalst;Parklaan 4, Aalst, 9300, Belgium;50.9301789;4.0417471;35;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Seafood;Charismatic Peter Van den Driesschen’s unstuffy, yet elegant welcome will instantly win you over as he ushers you into his smart, fashionably pared-back restaurant, hung with works of art and overlooking a lovely garden. The scene is set, and the rest of the team pursues Peter’s goal of making every aspect of your meal as perfect as possible. Seafood is cast in the lead roles, but the chef does allow red meat to play the odd guest-star appearance. He aims to highlight each ingredient’s purity in recipes free of unnecessary frills or gimmicks. The emphasis is on allowing the produce to speak plainly rather than shrouding it in mystery. The chef’s immense know-how and mastery of the ins and outs of classical cuisine shine through in recipes such as exquisitely pearly scallops cooked in butter in the shell, to which he gives a kick with a gutsy roe sauce and a subtle accompaniment of slightly bitter leaf chicory. Remember to save room for afters, because the cheese trolley and bites served with coffee are to die for! Kelderman is a culinary landmark in Alost and in the region and has been for many years – all of which is more than justified!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3406;OAK;Belgium;Gent;Burgstraat 16, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0566815;3.7190482;92;false;true;World Cuisine, Creative French;Ready for a whirlwind world tour? Marcelo Ballardin’s Italian-Brazilian roots, his globetrotting past and the international cast of the kitchen team are core to the DNA of this eatery. North Sea clams, Asian flavours or wild manioc roots from the Amazon Forest: the menu has clearly been extremely carefully designed and meticulously crafted. Chef Ballardin aims for simplicity, whilst accepting that this goal may entail a certain degree of complexity. He seeks a subtle balance between crisp acidity and velvety comfort. For example, he enhances quickly seared langoustines in a frothy, powerful sauce crafted from the heads and shells, together with a personal version of chimichurri, made from fregola and mandarins. The delicacy with which each ingredient is underscored bears witness to his creative streak. OAK is happily ensconced in the heart of historic Gent, in a 17C edifice whose elegance is set off by works of art and contemporary decorative fixtures and fittings. A modern culinary approach that aims to provide an “unforgettable experience”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3407;Attablez-vous;Belgium;Namur;Tienne Maquet 16, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.444706;4.8540444;30;false;true;Creative French, Modern French;Take a seat, as the restaurant’s name orders, and admire the ornamental tree that jazzes up the elegantly stylish contemporary interior, also home to an authentic cheese cave where all sorts of delicacies ripen slowly. Now let’s add attentive service and tips from the knowledgeable sommelier, who gets a kick out of suggesting unusual wines, and the scene is set. Chef Charles-Edouard Jeandrain mixes playful ideas with timeless classical flavours, conjuring up a fascinating repertory that demonstrates his respect for the ingredient and his quest for varied textures. He may prepare paella-style rice, adding stuffed txistorra squid, whose powerful flavour he offsets by deep-fried mussels and a coulis and purée of smoked paprika. Art-directed, intelligent plating contributes to whetting the appetite of diners and, even better, it is possible to mix and swap dishes from the different set menus. We recommend the Prestige menu, if you feel like splashing out and treating yourself to exceptional produce.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3408;Philippe Meyers;Belgium;Braine-l'Alleud;rue Doyen Van Belle 6, Braine-l'Alleud, 1420, Belgium;50.6823016;4.3700555;84;true;false;Modern French;Philippe Meyers cannot be faulted for his high - quality produce. His cuisine combines simplicity with limpidity, all of which in a bid to enhance the food’s natural flavour. The lady of the house pampers you in the pleasantly laid - back dining room. A trendy, design interior in star - studded company among a fine collection of Michelin Guides!;Air conditioning;[]
3409;Publiek;Belgium;Gent;Ham 39, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0577461;3.7329964;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Publiek is a one-of-a-kind star restaurant, and its friendly vibe is pivotal to the loft-inspired bistro. The bar even features its old beer pump. The team’s enthusiasm is contagious and the talented chef frequently serves the main course himself. Don’t expect posh, luxury ingredients, because Olly Ceulenaere is a staunch champion of little-known veggies and produce. His intelligent preparations hit the spot every time and he is a past master in the art of unexpected yet felicitous combinations, such as bacon served with celeriac (in cream, crispy and lacquered), or a sauce made out of vegetable peelings which adds just the right amount of bitterness. He juggles with techniques and flavours to exalt familiar ingredients, whose every facet he explores in a fascinating creative quest. The menu changes frequently, in keeping with the chef’s whims and inspiration (different lunch and dinner menu). The sommelier expertly suggests excellent wine-food pairings, featuring traditional and innovative natural wines. Every meal at Publiek is a voyage of discovery.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3410;Souvenir;Belgium;Gent;Brabantdam 134, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0496543;3.7322294;33;false;true;Creative, Organic;Vilhjalmur Sigurdarson’s relationship with nature is highly personal and his cooking is inspired by the seasons: bountiful in summer, earthy in winter. Sustainable before all else, his producers have become friends and the chef crafts their ingredients with passion. Veggies take the limelight, with the occasional fish from the North Sea. His creativity seems to know no bounds and while each dish highlights only a few ingredients, their intensity speaks volumes for his consummate, often off-kilter technique. Whether fermented, smoked, marinaded or grilled, veg takes on a whole new dimension, flanked by exquisite sauces. We tasted a cabbage sauce underscored with spicy sorrel and tarragon notes that added a sensual dimension to the different textures and varieties of cabbage, illustrating the chef’s knack for transforming lowly ingredients into knockout dishes. The lady of the house seamlessly supervises the service, while proffering insightful wine tips. Try and bag a seat at the lively counter for a front row view of the show in what used to be a butcher’s shop. An unforgettable experience awaits you.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3411;Cuines 33;Belgium;Knokke;Smedenstraat 33, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3394371;3.2879658;49;false;false;Creative;A meal at Cuines, 33 is an experience in its own right. As you first relax in the lounge, you are immersed in the soothing colour scheme, a genuine ode to Japanese minimalism. Right from the first bite, Edwin Menue’s cosmopolitan creativity can be tasted in creations like pani puri with razor clams and a dashi, illustrating just how his delicate touch underscores the entire establishment. The chef and the lady of the house, Fleur, then invite you to make your way into the dining area, whose counter seats sixteen. There you have a bird’s eye view of the chefs’ painstaking handiwork as they curate crisp veal sweetbread lacquered in sesame seeds and served on velvety mashed potato with a drizzling of vanilla and coffee oil and shavings of marinated egg yolk. Course after course of exquisite culinary surprises await the diner. The chef may even invite you into the kitchen to sample a bread-based recipe. Finally, make your way back to the lounge where a further lineup of delicacies awaits. Chef Menue’s culinary voyage, packed into a single set menu, is truly amazing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3412;La Belle;Belgium;Geel;Bel 162, Geel, 2440, Belgium;51.1630964;5.0637505;29;true;false;Creative French;Peter Vangenechten has made the small rural village of Bel a landmark of Belgium’s culinary landscape. The chef learned the trade in top establishments before returning to his roots, where he has entirely reworked the stables of a former farmstead. Bare timbers support the tall roof, while the elegant interior paints a cosy picture. The idyllic scene is set for chef Vangenechten to work his magic on regional produce, adding international notes, creative side dishes and a playful mixture of textures that enhances and underscores the main ingredient. Subtly balanced side dishes, such as slowly cooked sweet onions, marinated beetroot, fresh marinated fennel and frothy mashed potatoes, add a touch of perfection to tender, melt-in-the-mouth Holstein beef. A knockout Choron sauce unveils the chef’s knack for jus and gravies. Proud of its distinctive personality and character, La Belle is emblematic of its charismatic chef who is ever happy to pop out and give diners more ample explanations. We recommend the all-inclusive menu to best appreciate the full gamut of the skills of this accomplished chef!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3413;De Kristalijn;Belgium;Genk;Wiemesmeerstraat 105, Genk, 3600, Belgium;50.9696725;5.5534543;54;true;true;Modern French;De Kristalijn cannot fail but catch the eye. The modern edifice in which it is housed seems to hover over the surrounding golf course. Floor-to-ceiling windows command knockout views, while trendy furnishings and designer lighting underscore the establishment’s stylish character. Seasoned chef Koen Somers weaves his magic in the entirely open-plan kitchen as he crafts food depicted by purebred technique and generous ingredients. The chef harnesses his creative streak in a painstaking and precise approach to cooking. Premium seabass is cooked in its skin for crispiness and flanked with a medley of salsify and apple soufflé, stuffed with potatoes and dressed in caviar. The exquisite butter sauce is further intensified and exalted by dashi and bonito flakes. The chef cannot be equalled for his knack for rich nuances. You can expect a fascinating culinary experience, all of which is paired with amazing vintages from the outstanding wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3414;Les Gourmands;Belgium;Blaregnies;rue de Sars 15, Blaregnies, 7040, Belgium;50.360669;3.8873851;60;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Les Gourmands is run by foodies for foodies. The charming authentic interior is ideally suited to the classical fare of Didier Bernard, assisted by Lydia Glacé, who is in charge of the decadent desserts. The veteran, gifted duo, who were awarded their first Michelin star back in 1996, are committed body and soul to celebrating premium produce. You may taste Burgaud duck, respectfully and delicately cooked to just rare, flanked by a gutsy duck jus that is divinely paired with orange marmalade and a powerful duck shepherd’s pie oozing with buttery flavours. Les Gourmands excels in the art of adding a contemporary spin to age-old recipes, whilst remaining faithful to textbook technique down to the tiniest details. The savvy and extensive wine list is the work of sommelier and owner Carlo Zecchin, whose insightful suggestions add the final flourish with pairings that exalt and add depth to each dish – to the delight of discerning connoisseurs.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
3415;La Villa in the Sky;Belgium;Brussels;Avenue Louise 480, Brussels, 1050, Belgium;50.8172539;4.3719965;66;false;false;Creative, Organic;Enter the IT Tower and take the lift up to the 23rd floor, before walking up two more flights of stairs. The jaw-dropping view is truly unique and this glazed Villa in the Sky commands a breathtaking vista over Brussels! The theatrically visible kitchen enables you to admire the precision of chef Alexandre Dionisio, whose food is characterised by first-class produce underscored by playful notes and subtle side dishes. Alexandre’s high-flying culinary wizardry leads him to try out bold combinations such as a silky béarnaise sauce underscored with the subtle, savoury taste of oyster leaf (mertensia maritima) and paired with a succulent veal cutlet from Corrèze. The chef also cleverly blends delicate Asian influences into text-book classical recipes. His creative elegance more than confirms that he is worthy of his star-studded reputation. Nice to know: if you don’t have time for the full-blown menu at lunchtime, you can order à la carte dishes (lunchtimes only).;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3416;Hostellerie Gilain;Belgium;Sorinnes;rue de l'Aiguigeois 1, Sorinnes, 5503, Belgium;50.2562796;5.0377695;53;true;true;Modern French;Alain Gilain, an ambassador of Wallon produce, sources his ingredients preferably from small local farms, like snails from Namur and game from local hunters, always with a focus on quality. He celebrates culinary traditions with generosity and is a fan of nostalgic rustic recipes, which doesn’t prevent him from exercising his creative streak. Snails in a flaky pastry case with garlic cream is a house signature dish. In the same vein, how about an immaculately cooked slice of foie gras flanked with a velvety seafood stock? Autumn is the season for fresh game, such as wild duck in gravy, delicately underpinned by tomatoes and spices. This hostelry unabashedly celebrates pure-bred Ardennes’ cooking rich in big-boned flavours, with the bonus of a romantic vibe and an exquisite view over the surrounding fields and meadows. Even better, treat yourself to a night in one of the comfortable rooms to finish your meal in style…;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
3417;De Pastorie;Belgium;Kasterlee;Houtum 61, Kasterlee, 2460, Belgium;51.2282883;4.9782374;73;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The regular premises of De Pastorie in Lichtaart are currently undergoing extensive renovation work, set for completion by late April 2025. Until then, Carl, Loes, and Wout Wens are operating their restaurant in Kasterlee, at what used to be De Watermolen. They have given the place a French twist: French chansons playing in the background, various paintings adorning the walls, and a striking Eiffel Tower mural. With great dedication and a wealth of expertise, chef Wens reinvigorates classic recipes. His son Wout injects a youthful energy, incorporating occasional bursts of Asian finesse. Their sophisticated cooking engages the senses. For instance, they pair succulent pan-seared langoustines with carrots enhanced by the bright zest of ginger and orange, as well as pineapple variations and a creamy coconut curry sauce for a touch of delicate spice. A symphony of flavours in the warmth of an attractive family-run establishment.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3418;Misera;Belgium;Antwerpen;Michel de Braeystraat 18, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.205483;4.3820393;91;false;false;Creative French, Modern French;Nicolas Misera’s motto, “An artist’s life”, was far from a random choice, as you will quickly realise when you cross the threshold of this à la carte restaurant. Art forms the backbone of the establishment which is a stylish blend of purity and design. An open-plan kitchen and a counter dominate the interior, offering an intriguing insight into the chef’s virtuosity.His personal take on classical recipes, with a weakness for fish and shellfish, is founded on consummate talent. Knockout sauces, high-precision cooking and originality set the fascinating scene between the city and North Sea. Start with a warm brioche, covered in ham shank, lobster and parmesan, a tribute to Misera’s father and one of the establishment’s signature dishes. He endeavours to tell a personal story and transport you to his universe with each dish. A vol-au-vent stuffed with razor clams, lobster, clams and a host of delicacies pays a moving homage to the North Sea and is so rich, fresh and gutsy that we warrant you will want to lick the plate. Nicolas Misera is a true artist in every sense of the word.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3419;Guillou Campagne;Luxembourg;Schouweiler;17 rue de la Résistance, Schouweiler, 4996, Luxembourg;49.5804978;5.9556437;100;false;false;Classic French;Fans of Gallic fare adore Guillou Campagne. This family-run restaurant was for many years in the hands of Pierrick Guillou and the chefs he trained continue to pay tribute to his legacy on a daily basis. Lysianne and Katell, his widow and daughter, also continue to uphold the family tradition of hospitality in this old stone edifice flanked by an exquisite garden terrace. Authenticity and intensity are the watchwords of Guillou Campagne, so you can expect lashings of cream and butter and ingredients such as foie gras and scallops. The focus is primarily on wholesome, hearty flavours, rather than on fancy or fussy plating. Examples include a hunger-obliterating meat pie of pork, veal and foie gras, smothered in a hearty périgourdine sauce flanked by a green salad tossed in a divine dressing. Guillou Campagne pays tribute to recipes of yesteryear and its extensive line-up of dishes reads like a culinary encyclopaedia.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3420;In den Hert;Belgium;Wannegem-Lede;Lededorp 7, Wannegem-Lede, 9772, Belgium;50.8894307;3.5751997;83;true;true;Classic Cuisine;(Temporarily closed) Frederick Dhooge is nothing if not single-minded, as he proved for many years at Huis van Lede and continues to do at In den Hert. His passion for traditional Gallic fare has resulted in a repertory that is as French as the Marseillaise. The road to the restaurant which winds through the hillsides of the Flemish Ardennes offers a foretaste of what you can expect. The characterful edifice on the picturesque village square is the epitome of nostalgic charm and sets the perfect scene for chef Dhooge’s gutsy menu. Knockout produce and rich, authentic flavours characterise his approach, while recipes that traverse the annals of French cookery, like bouillabaisse and vol-au-vent, acquire a new dimension thanks to the chef’s culinary wizardry. A pepper sauce adds a kick to a fillet of venison or an amazing mousseline sauce with baby hop shoots is paired with quail cooked on the bone: the chef’s talent and craftsmanship are crystal clear. Connoisseurs of French gourmet fare will appreciate the à la carte only menu and the wicked lineup of fascinating desserts (the Normandy pancake is to die for!). In den Hert is depicted by a passion for food, throbbingly good flavours and unadulterated dining pleasure.;Terrace;[]
3421;Aurum by Gary Kirchens;Belgium;Ordingen;Ordingen-Dorp 50, Ordingen, 3800, Belgium;50.8167354;5.2388049;42;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The awe-inspiring restored castle of Ordingen sets the scene for special occasion indulgence. The restaurant’s historic Flemish Renaissance interior, mingling period details, modern luxury, glittering chandeliers, gleaming gilt work and oil portraits, will take your breath away. Kick off your meal with a drink in the stylish bar by the open fire, before sitting down to sample the chef’s revamped versions of pedigree French recipes. Chef Gary Kirchens aims to enhance and shine the spotlight on each ingredient. He may underscore tender fillet of lamb with a parsley and nettle crust, while a light foaming harissa brings subtlety, the gravy is given a kick thanks to parsley, nettles and anchovies and white asparagus covered in ground hazelnuts adds the final flourish. Chef Kirchens leaves his culinary stamp on familiar flavours, jazzing up the aromas with playful textures. His cooking demonstrates consummate skill and is dotted with unusual, subtle notes, without falling into the trap of fussy excesses. His dishes are available in set menus or à la carte, but Sunday lunch features 7 courses and generally lasts until 4pm! The epitome of stylish, every detail of Aurum has been puzzled over and preened to make it perfect, including the superlative guestrooms – ideal to luxuriously prolong your stay.;Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3422;Pont neuf;Belgium;Antwerpen;Verbindingsdok Oostkaai 9, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2305591;4.4080126;37;false;false;Seafood;Chic and cosy, the Pont Neuf oozes Flemish good taste, and its terrace is the perfect spot to immerse yourself in the infectious buzzy vibe of this trendy neighbourhood (weather permitting). Dominique Leroy pampers her guests as she shares her love of Italian wines and there is always a bottle of red Barbera d’Alba open for a glass of wine. Chef Tommy Bocklandt’s culinary score demonstrates a distinct preference for North Sea fish. His cooking focuses on preserving the purity of each ingredient, leaving the sauces and side dishes to add complexity. His repertory is traditional, but distinctive. Examples include immaculately steamed brill à la normande, served with an exquisite mussel-flavoured white wine sauce or creamy eel in a bright green sorrel sauce, discreetly seasoned with a hint of celery. Fish, whether it is cooked in stock, braised or fried in butter, is taken to a whole new level thanks to the chef. The only challenge is to make your choice from the extensive à la carte offering!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3423;Arden;Belgium;Villers-sur-Lesse;rue de Montainpré 27, Villers-sur-Lesse, 5580, Belgium;50.1577096;5.0748306;37;true;true;French Contemporary;The stunning Ardennes landscape is the star of the show in this swanky designer restaurant located in a modern wing of a tastefully restored castle (book a room for the night!). The floor-to-ceiling windows command a splendid view of the rural surroundings, while the patio enjoys a view of the Lesse. Definitely a premium location! Nature is also the name of the game for chef Bosmans, who immaculately crafts veggies grown in the garden in a high-flying culinary score. He might enhance the main ingredient with a spicy note, such as warm aromatic herbs from the garden and a vin jaune gravy to perfectly showcase subtly aged North Sea turbot and razor clams. The same gravy may add depth to an unconventional risotto of pine kernels, broccoli oil and poached broccoli stems. Delicately acidic lemon, one of chef Bosmans’ signature ingredients, is used to underpin and exalt the flavours of other produce. His minimalist dishes are not the only surprise that you can expect to sample - make sure you ask to see the Wine Bible!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3424;Ryôdô;;Luxembourg;27 rue Raymond Poincaré, 2342, Luxembourg;49.6023904;6.1170458;30;true;true;Japanese;Ryôdô celebrates and embodies Japanese art de vivre in the heart of Luxemburg’s suburbs. The luminous interior and light wooden furnishings are suitably minimalist and the food is exquisitely served by women attired in kimonos. It is rare to experience such respect for tradition outside Japan and one well worth savouring. The lunchtime score is either à la carte or a range of kaiseki and bento menus, while in the evening, you can choose between Sushi, Vegan or Tasting menus. Chef Ryôdô Kajiwara delicately blends Japanese subtlety with French exuberance, calling upon the pure-bred intensity of outstanding produce, such as A5 wagyu and obsiblue, further underscored by marinades and sauces. Diners are invited to season the tempura of langoustines and tofu, which is surprisingly both crunchy and velvety, with a cucumber dashi. Ryôdô enjoys adding a Western spin, exemplified by stuffing cabbage leaves with wagyu and truffles, served in a beef and truffle stock. The talent of the virtuoso chef and his respect for the culinary heritages of France and Japan mean that you can look forward to a high-flying dining experience! A final word for the splendid sake-food pairings.;Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3425;Da Mimmo;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Lambert;avenue du Roi Chevalier 24, Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, 1200, Belgium;50.8435331;4.418125;83;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Da Mimmo is the epitome of Italian-style sophistication. As soon as you venture over the threshold of this elegant restaurant and meet the charismatic maître d', you know you are in good hands! Chef Louis Verstrepen and his team showcase beautifully presented dishes that embody a creative approach to Italian culinary tradition. His cooking is highly technical and precise. He is not afraid to throw bold flavours together, and his use of diverse textures adds a sense of playfulness. For example, he cooks guinea fowl to perfection so that it is succulent with crispy skin. Then he combines it with maize in various guises, polenta with truffle, a wonderful croquette stuffed with the guinea fowl's giblets and an exquisite poultry sauce. The sommelier's carefully chosen wines perfectly complement the chef's unique take on Mediterranean cuisine. Da Mimmo never fails to surprise and delight.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3426;Philippe Fauchet;Belgium;Saint-Georges-sur-Meuse;rue de Warfée 62, Saint-Georges-sur-Meuse, 4470, Belgium;50.6096505;5.3712656;63;true;true;Creative;Philippe Fauchet enjoys straying from his comfort zone and has developed his own distinctive hallmark in this snug but buzzy eatery deep in the Liege countryside. An artisan at heart, he prepares everything himself (even the bread). While impossible to sum up in a single word, let’s say his style is quirky and scattered with international accents, but with a firm focus on local ingredients and veggies, thanks to partnerships with regional farmers. All of which is combined in intriguing, jazzy, playful recipes, illustrated by his bold mixture of fresh cream, red beetroot and hazelnuts, blanched cabbage, a reduction of Barolo wine vinegar, lemon confit, a dusting of aged parmesan and foie gras. The chef plays with contrasts and textures in a bid to constantly titillate and tease our tastebuds. The wine list and food-wine pairings are fully in line with this amazing experience. Bold, unconventional and distinctive.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3427;Hostellerie St-Nicolas;Belgium;Elverdinge;Veurnseweg 532, Elverdinge, 8906, Belgium;50.8857292;2.818281;29;true;false;Creative;The high-flying talents of Michael Vanderhaeghe and his father Franky set the scene in this temple to fine dining. Knockout sauces and a superlative range of local produce such as hop shoots and Steenvoorde pigeon bear witness to the know-how of this hostelry, that has been a culinary landmark for going on 25 years. Original touches and exotic techniques ensure that the menu continues to evolve and progress. How about slowly cooked free-range chicken coated in a hazelnut sauce and a spicy Flanders cheese, paired with a frothy kohlrabi mousse rich in earthy notes. You will also be surprised by an ordinary looking sweetbread in flaky pastry, which turns out to be stuffed in foie gras and truffles and flanked by a meaty gravy that cleverly blends all these different flavours into a harmonious dish. Multi-facetted culinary creativity and a clever blend of old and new depicts the work of the father and son team. The trendy interior of this charming, luxurious villa, extended by a peaceful garden, provides the perfect foil to this splendid culinary experience. Not far away, the Vanderhaeghe family’s hotel, overflowing in elegant details, is ideal for longer stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3428;Couvert Couvert;Belgium;Heverlee;St-Jansbergsesteenweg 171, Heverlee, 3001, Belgium;50.8629609;4.6596864;33;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant offers a designer interior, modern terrace overlooking the fields, and fine creative cuisine – designed by brothers. Don't fall into the trap of eating too many of the delicious homemade rolls at the beginning of the meal! Astutely combined flavours. Pleasant welcome and service.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3429;Melchior;Belgium;Tienen;Veemarkt 47, Tienen, 3300, Belgium;50.8057989;4.9408671;79;false;true;Modern French, Fusion;Old brick walls, high ceilings, designer furniture and graffiti on the terrace: Melchior would be just the ticket for a fashion shoot. It is here that Gilles Melchior conjures up recipes that waver between purebred French and trendy. The exquisite sauces and vinaigrettes demonstrate the chef’s high-flying craftsmanship. Immaculately cooked turbot on the bone is paired with a subtly acidic lobster béarnaise sauce – to die for! Creative and generous, the chef has no qualms about extending his flavourful repertory to Asian notes such as yuzu and hoisin. His classical mastery shines through in dishes like the superlative roast partridge, served with a reduced stock made from the carcass to which butter is whipped in just before serving, all of which flanked by foie gras and Belgian endive. The savvy wine list is a treasure trove of delights designed to pair with your food. Delicious from start to finish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3430;Benoit en Bernard Dewitte;Belgium;Ouwegem;Beertegemstraat 52, Ouwegem, 9750, Belgium;50.9133244;3.606346;92;false;true;Modern French;The villa of brothers Benoit and Bernard Dewitte sports a zen vibe that is perfectly echoed by its trendy countrified interior, while an irresistible summer holiday buzz sets the scene in the exquisite garden. This pared-back setting is the perfect foil to chef Benoit’s cooking, whose style is both natural and delicate. He frequently calls upon veggies and spices to create harmonies whose interaction gives rise to fascinating, spot-on subtle flavours. Nothing leaves the kitchen that hasn’t been endlessly pondered and puzzled over. Rather than over-complicating venison, he invents amusing side dishes, subtle seasonings and gutsy sauces, such as a juniper berry sauce. When paired with a rare Côtes du Rhône Villages (Ténébi by Domaine du Piaugier with a Counoise grape variety), the full breadth and scope of this dish is unveiled. Everything fits together seamlessly, a bit like the personalities of Benoit and Bernard.;Car park;[]
3431;Hostellerie Vivendum;Belgium;Dilsen;Vissersstraat 2, Dilsen, 3650, Belgium;51.0332774;5.7367212;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;The subtle restoration of this 18C presbytery has done nothing to detract from its original character. Chef Clevers proposes subtle dishes, as full of delicate flavour as they are generous and consummately prepared. Pleasant overnight rooms to ensure you finish your evening in comfort.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3432;Arenberg;Belgium;Heverlee;Kapeldreef 46, Heverlee, 3001, Belgium;50.8608425;4.6655965;26;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Book a table by the bay windows of the orangery or on the lovely terrace overlooking the garden. Such are just a few of the appeals of this restaurant, whose cuisine features a masterful repertory with a new take on traditional recipes. The wine list is worthy of special mention, as is the faultless service and the mouthwatering chocolate desserts.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3433;Maison Alain Bianchin;Belgium;Overijse;Brusselsesteenweg 663, Overijse, 3090, Belgium;50.793583;4.4819428;85;true;false;Creative, Creative French;Alain Bianchin’s romantic abode should be on the bucket list of any self-respecting foodie. The finer points of pedigree classical cuisine have no secrets for this high-flying craftsman. His grasp of what the modern diner appreciates has led him to branch out and experiment with new flavours and techniques, often of Asian origin. For example, he can endow a ballotine of wild duck, butternut and black tripe with a depth that it is reminiscent of jugged hare by consummately blending sweet veggies, gutsy tripe and delicate meaty flavours. He may underscore duck jus with mixed Vietnamese bao chau spices, whose intriguing complexity is further enriched by raw foie gras. The level of sophistication and technique of such a dish is nothing short of exceptional. A genuine master chef, Bianchin effortlessly combines his sensitivity with Asian touches and his mastery of Gallic techniques with fascinating international influences. The kitchen is clearly his playground and a meal in his establishment is the opportunity to sample a fascinating culinary experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3434;De Zuidkant;Belgium;Damme;Jacob van Maerlantstraat 6, Damme, 8340, Belgium;51.2517769;3.2823561;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine;De Zuidkant is emblematic of Damme, which is a beacon for foodies exploring Eastern Belgium and its coastline. From the romantic interior and warm open fire to the charming lady of the house who sees you to your table and the smiling chef who greets you from his open kitchen, it is the quintessence of warm Flemish hospitality. Welcome to the HQ of Patrick and Cora. The chef’s expertise and know-how can be tasted from the first bite of each perfectly balanced, delicate dish. Examples include perfectly cooked young pigeon, flanked by a powerful gravy and a Mediterranean note thanks to subtly sweet carrots and a scattering of ras-el-hanout spices. Chef Patrick has no qualms about adding an unorthodox spin to his cooking, which is nonetheless founded on consummate culinary technique. In the same vein, Cora’s passion for wine can be felt in her presentation of the enticing wine list. This couple is clearly dedicated body and soul to their profession, making De Zuidkant a must for any self-respecting foodie!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3435;Kommilfoo;Belgium;Antwerpen;Vlaamse Kaai 17, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2111875;4.392667;83;false;true;Creative French;Smart yet casual, Kommilfoo will acquaint you with the creative and inventive talent of a dedicated chef. The dishes are both amusing and imaginative, with a clear desire to render contrasting tastes harmonious. Pyrenean goat, the house speciality, is on the menu all year long.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3436;Héliport Brasserie;Belgium;Liège;allée de Érables, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.5789946;5.5961592;89;false;false;Creative French;Héliport is so much more than a brasserie! It is established in a pretty little castle 10km outside of Liège. Depicted by a patchwork of old beams and snug details, it oozes with character and boasts a lovely alfresco terrace for summer dining. The food is also light years from your run-of-the-mill brasserie fare. The recipes may well be traditional, but Frédéric Salpetier gives each one a fascinating personal, sometimes Asian twist. He may pair juicy breast and confit leg of Anjou pigeon with girolles à la Bordelaise, coated in a gutsy gravy and flanked by melt-in-the-mouth mashed potato. The sauces are quite simply out of this world. Rather than prissy, superfluous effects, Frédéric seeks to exalt each individual flavour. Traditional brasserie values are however respected in the lavish helpings. Héliport is the quintessence of innovative tradition.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3437;Le Pilori;Belgium;Écaussinnes-Lalaing;rue du Pilori 10, Écaussinnes-Lalaing, 7191, Belgium;50.5701335;4.1795447;86;false;false;Modern French;Le Pilori is ideal for a meal with the mates. Founded in 1917, it started out as a café-restaurant, before morphing into a jazz club. Marc Leveau and Michel Van Cauwelaert bought it in 1993 and set about bringing it up to date, adding modern art and brightening up the interior. The chef intelligently adds a zest of modernity to produce whose quality is beyond compare. For example, noble ingredients like scallops or cod are served with the simplest of side dishes in a bid to keep the flavours strong and authentic. Examples include a juicy breast of guinea fowl with a crisp golden skin and a punchy white wine sauce. The main ingredient, generally meat, is underscored by side dishes such as morels, salsify, mash with lashings of butter and fermented red cabbage. This is wholesome Belgian fare at its best - oozing in authenticity, flavour and generosity. The final flourish is supplied by the sommelier, who can be relied upon to find just the right wine to pair with your meal from a cellar of predominantly French vintages. With friends or family, this is the place for feelgood food!;Interesting wine list;[]
3438;Ogst;Belgium;Hasselt;Ridder Portmansstraat 4, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9294564;5.3335502;20;true;false;Modern French;Ogst is the epitome of charming. A natural, Scandinavian-inspired decor sets the warm, casual scene in which you instantly feel at home. Sébastien Wygaerts bowls us over with fresh produce and attention to detail, depicted by elegant plating, cleverly devised recipes and gutsy flavours. This modern chef plays with fresh and acidic nuances, including the occasional exotic flavour. For example, he will craft scallops with a subtle soy, mirin and sudachi vinaigrette, while segments of mandarin contrast happily with the vinaigrette and dill adds a spicy note. Subtle before all else, the chef seeks to reinforce the character of a fillet of beef with a madeira sauce. He manages to keep our tastebuds aching for more throughout the meal. The cherry on the cake is provided by Diederik Herbots, an unabashed fan of natural wines, whose amazing Aladdin’s Cave of wine adds the final flourish to a knockout meal. Don’t miss a trip to the delicatessen (two steps from the restaurant) to stock up on delicacies on your way out.;Interesting wine list;[]
3439;Le Coq aux Champs;Belgium;Soheit-Tinlot;rue du Montys 71, Soheit-Tinlot, 4557, Belgium;50.4714671;5.3876393;83;true;true;Creative French;The stripped-back, elegant interior of this Rooster in the Fields is a feast for the eye and this attention to detail can also be tasted in the plate. Christophe Pauly, who carefully considers every tiny detail in his open kitchen, is going from strength to strength. His spot-on dishes conjure up a festival of flavours with a voluntarily concise range of ingredients as he elegantly and precisely pursues his quest for culinary excellence. He plays with sweet and sour flavours to enhance dishes which he underscores with subtle sauces. Courgette flowers are stuffed with langoustines and dipped in a rich tempura batter, which are served with a dollop of soy mayo to accentuate the savoury flavours, while piquillos add a final spicy flourish. Deceptively simple recipes are the hallmark of this high-flying chef in search of culinary perfection. This credo is also visible in the fascinating pairing suggestions made by the knowledgeable sommelier.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3440;The Butcher's son;Belgium;Antwerpen;Boomgaardstraat 1, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.1994236;4.4157849;86;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Meats and Grills;The industrial loft vibe of the trendy, urban Butcher’s son eatery blends seamlessly into De Koninck brewery, in which it is located. The premises are also home to the De Laet & Van Haver butcher’s shop, the main suppliers of Bert Jan Michielsen (who worked there when he was young) and the chef’s open kitchen showcases his ongoing passion for red meat. Chef Michielsen takes family favourites to a whole new level thanks to lashings of talent, sprinkled with modern twists. For example, he may mix fish with a tartare steak conjuring up subtle, savoury nuances or perfectly crisp calf sweetbread might be flanked with morel mushrooms and home-made sausage stuffed with truffle. One thing is certain – choosing between the house signature dishes and the more inventive creations is something of a conundrum. Even though red meat is at the core of Michielsen’s reputation, his fish dishes are equally worthy of mention. The flavoursome palette of appetising side dishes confirms the chef’s high-flying culinary talent.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3441;Goffin;Belgium;Sint-Kruis;Maalsesteenweg 2, Sint-Kruis, 8310, Belgium;51.2119551;3.2417056;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Timothy Goffin is forging his own path. A genuine craftsman, he recognises the importance of full-bodied sauces, whilst also seeking to nurture comforting, fruity flavours. Whether with local or Asian ingredients, Goffin can be relied on to produce delicate, spot-on dishes and his set menu is a masterclass of balance. Right from the unusual appetisers, he takes you on a personal voyage of discovery, reacquainting you with family favourites or introducing you to creative, unexpected flavours. For example, how about a thick slice of beefsteak tomato, smothered in crushed raspberries and a vanilla flavoured ganache, and then further set off by a fruity, slightly vanilla-scented vinaigrette for even more depth? A genuine culinary tightrope walker, chef Goffin constantly seeks to match innovation with delicacy. The wine list, curated by Valérie, is perfectly suited to his imaginative repertory. The pared-back setting is elegant and spruce, combining dark walls, modern art and a vintage tiled floor.;Air conditioning;[]
3442;M Bistro;Belgium;Nieuwpoort;Sint-Sebastiaanstraat 15, Nieuwpoort, 8620, Belgium;51.1280608;2.752673;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;M Bistro is writing a new page of its story since Mattias Maertens and Sofie Billiet have moved shop to a former factory, lovingly converted in line with their tastes. Their ethos has not budged an inkling and continues to focus purely and simply on pleasure. Mattias crafts food that hits the spot every time, demonstrating his creative streak and above all his passion for cooking. Whether it be the acidity of a citrus fruit jelly, the kick of Sichuan pepper or Vadouvan spices, chef Maertens meticulously crafts side dishes in a bid to showcase the main ingredient. While much of his top-quality produce comes from the nearby fish market, he is far from averse to working with less popular ingredients like rabbit, to which he adds his subtle hallmark. A friendly youthful vibe continues to depict the bistronomic spirit of M Bistro.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3444;Maison Marit;Belgium;Braine-l'Alleud;chaussée de Nivelles 336, Braine-l'Alleud, 1420, Belgium;50.663044;4.3835317;52;true;true;Classic French;Dimitri Marit represents the second generation of his family at the helm of the elegant Maison Marit, housed in a property brimming with character. The interior has been revamped with clean lines. The restaurant has its own sheep and deer, which can be seen grazing from the terrace. Foodies have been coming here since 1991 to savour classic French cuisine. Expertise and finesse are the hallmarks of this establishment, and nowhere is this more evident than in the rich, full-bodied sauces. When preparing his risotto, the chef removes some of the liquid and mixes it with a hearty poultry stock and truffle. The result is creamy and intensely flavoursome, the ideal complement to freshly caught scallops. The focus on presentation and freshness. The extra helping offered with some dishes and the careful selection of wines show a commitment to upholding tradition.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3445;Magis;Belgium;Tongeren;Hemelingenstraat 23, Tongeren, 3700, Belgium;50.78176;5.4627023;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This historical house has an entirely refurbished, contemporary interior. The terrace - garden has an ornamental pond and offers views over the basilica. Tasty cuisine with hints of the Mediterranean.;Terrace;[]
3446;Vol-Ver;Belgium;Marke;Watervalstraat 23, Marke, 8510, Belgium;50.7970808;3.2351421;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;Vol-Ver is the epitome of Flemish charm, hospitality and good taste as the handsome brick walls and warm welcome from Sharon and chef Sébastien Verveken bear witness. The set and à la carte menus may seem low profile, but right from the first bite, you will taste the chef’s enthusiastic approach to cooking. Don’t go expecting eccentric gimmicks, however, as chef Verveken is more interested in subtlety and in harnessing his skill to showcasing familiar flavours, albeit with nods to Asia. For example, he may pair fresh langoustine confit with a heroic blend of horseradish sauce, bergamot jelly, seaweed and cucumber stock perfumed with dill oil. This uninhibited chef cooks boldly, but always in a bid to enhance the ingredient. The establishment’s decision to offer beer as well as wine pairings is truly inspired!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3447;Boo Raan;Belgium;Knokke;Edward Verheyestraat 17, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3397049;3.2893828;72;false;true;Thai, Traditional Cuisine;Boo Raan is the best Thai restaurant in Benelux. The buzzy vibe of this exotic establishment immediately incites you to take a seat as you drool over the menu. Dokkoon Kapueak prepares authentic dishes in the open kitchen to order. A festival of fresh ingredients, spices, unctuosity and manifold flavours explain why Boo Raan is such a benchmark locally and nationally.;Wheelchair access;[]
3448;Comme chez Soi;Belgium;Brussels;place Rouppe 23, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8423511;4.3459079;71;true;true;Classic Cuisine;A meal at Comme chez Soi is like biting into a slice of culinary history. Its emblematic Art nouveau Horta interior is classy and characterful, dotted with stained glass and elegant details, while the wine cellar (Riwyne) offers a more contemporary “private dining” experience. The rich heritage of this establishment founded in 1926 owes much to Pierre Wynants. Now, the fourth generation, Laurence and Lionel Rigolet and their son Loïc, is pursuing the story. Together they continue to serve traditional signature dishes, like mousse of Ardennes ham and sole fillets in a Riesling and shrimp sauce. Chef Rigolet lavishes great care and attention on the plating, to which he adds a modern twist, while his mastery in the realm of sauces cannot fail but impress. Neither does he balk at introducing contemporary culinary techniques or exotic flavours. Comme chez Soi definitely remains a landmark of Brussels’ fine dining scene and it can be depended on to deliver first-rate traditional fare, albeit with an eye to the future.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
3449;l'Impératif d'Éole;Belgium;Quévy-le-Grand;Grand'Route 58, Quévy-le-Grand, 7040, Belgium;50.3799155;3.9652916;49;true;false;French Contemporary;The impressive Chant d’Éole wine estate is particularly famous for its excellent sparkling wines. Benoît Neusy also offers visitors the chance of a gourmet experience in a luxurious rooftop location, where an ornamental gold-coloured tree and a glazed wine cellar immediately catch the eye. On your way into the restaurant, you will see the estate’s wines maturing in barrels.The Franco-Belgian wine list is perfectly paired with the chef’s versatile craftsmanship, which finds its source in his travels abroad. A dish of shrimps bears witness to his love of North Sea produce, while the Asian-inspired tuna demonstrates his passion for more exotic fare. An establishment which never fails to deliver a knockout blend of creativity and knowhow. The sauces are similarly inspired, like the smoked eel sauce that flanks lacquered eel and quickly seared foie gras. Generosity is at the core of this Michelin starred restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3450;Le Roannay;Belgium;Francorchamps;Rue de Spa 155, Francorchamps, 4970, Belgium;50.4581496;5.951217;92;false;false;Modern French;The iconic Le Roannay Hotel has been treated to a top-to-toe revamp. The guestrooms, wellness facilities and restaurant are now the picture of stylish contemporary luxury. The exquisite bar is located in a historic barn beneath timber rafters and the heliport is open for business again. The food demonstrates inherent respect for the past with a modern twist.Talented Matthieu Vande Velde is blossoming under the guidance of master chef David Martin. Strewn with Asian notes, Matthieu’s creativity is perfectly paired with familiar family favourites. He exalts the ingredient, thanks to lashings of high-precision technique, resulting in dishes such as melt-in-the-mouth Anjou pigeon with generously seasoned thighs and a creamy sauce made from the intestines. Vande Velde’s flair and knack for sauces is unrivalled, depicted by a vin jaune jus that adds a deft, flyaway touch to flawlessly cooked scallops from Brittany. This intuitive chef’s personality is revealed through consummate skill and respect for the ingredient. A treat for your tastebuds awaits you at Le Roannay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3451;Palate;South Korea;Busan;3F, 154 Dalmaji-gil 65 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48576, South Korea;35.15659;129.17844;60;true;true;Contemporary;Palate offers contemporary French cuisine that is free-spirited and adventurous in style. Its sensuous fare is based on the culinary diversity experienced by Chef Kim Jae-hoon. Ever since he boldly opened this diner in Busan, his hometown, the chef has been taking up diverse epicurean challenges while injecting freshness into the restaurant’s concept. This progressive aspect of Palate is well reflected in the cuisine it serves today. When it comes to dining, Busan has much respect for the old and traditional. This urban dining landscape makes one wonder how the chef’s ever-evolving culinary experiments will translate into gastronomic revolutions.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3452;L'Amant Secret;South Korea;Seoul;26F L'Escape Hotel, 67 Toegye-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04529, South Korea;37.55983;126.97949;57;false;false;Contemporary;Located on the 26th floor of L'Escape Hotel, L'Amant Secret (French for secret lover) is an intimate space inspired by Parisian sensibilities. Chef Son Jong-won, who honed his culinary chops in the United States, strives for a style which he refers to as Korean-style Western cuisine with Korean seasonal ingredients. His modern interpretations are based on local ingredients blended with Western cooking techniques, resulting in creations that are both original and familiar, respectful of the symbiosis between the producer and the ingredients as well as the kitchen and the diner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
3453;Haobin;South Korea;Seoul;2F, Ambassador-Pullman Hotel,  287 Dongho-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04618, South Korea;37.56012;127.00259;62;false;false;Chinese;Haobin is a Chinese restaurant helmed by Chef Hu Deok-juk, celebrated as a living legend of Korean-Chinese cuisine and a trailblazer who led the refinement of Cantonese cuisine. The restaurant’s title, which means “precious guests” in Chinese, reflects the chef’s respect for his diners. Haobin boasts a vast repertoire of signature dishes, including braised whole sea cucumber with Sichuanese sauce and fried noodles with stir-fried seafood. Yet, its best-known offering is the classic soup poetically dubbed “Buddha Jumps Over the Wall,” which was first introduced to Korea by Chef Hu and has remained the icon of his cuisine. “I strive to highlight the genuine flavors of the ingredients from the freshest ingredients.” This quote by the chef carries exceptional weight although it merely reiterates the time-tested principle of culinary art. In addition to diverse gastronomic delights, the establishment also offers various vigor-boosting dishes made with seasonal ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3454;YUN;South Korea;Seoul;805 Seolleung-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06019, South Korea;37.52416;127.03906;60;true;true;Korean;YUN offers familiar Korean dishes with bold twists. Its nutty-flavored perilla oil noodles featuring housemade Korean wheat noodles, various house-aged fish dishes, and newly added umami-rich Korean beef offerings – all hint at the culinary direction the chef is headed towards. With a relocation from Mapo to Gangnam, this restaurant has expanded and renovated its dining hall, which now exudes elegant yet striking vibes. Come to Yun Seoul and experience the precision and audacity that are rarely found in ordinary Korean cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
3456;HANE;South Korea;Seoul;14 Eonju-ro 172-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06017, South Korea;37.5275808;127.0348773;79;false;true;Sushi;When it comes to gastronomy, savoring the freshest natural ingredients that capture the essence of the season is undoubtedly one of the greatest delights. At Sushi Hane, Chef Choi Ju-yong’s quest for natural ingredients is well reflected and can be fully appreciated. When making sushi, he focuses on bringing out the inherent flavor of each product and recreating authentic tastes. The fare itself exudes a unique charm during the entire culinary process – from selecting ingredients to serving sushi to patrons – and genuinely reflects the chef’s gastronomic beliefs. Relishing this food in an elegant fine dining space decorated with modern interpretations of traditional materials also adds to the overall allure.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
3457;VINHO;South Korea;Seoul;#162 Wellstone Bldg, 38 Hakdong-ro 43-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06059, South Korea;37.51866;127.03814;65;true;true;Contemporary;Co-helmed by Chef Jeon Seong-bin and Sommelier Kim Jin-ho, Vinho features expansive window walls and an open kitchen fronted by an elongated counter. This spatial harmony creates a lively communal wine-and-dine ambiance. The vast wine list, coupled with careful service and food pairing, as well as deep-flavored sauces that exquisitely complement seasonal ingredients, makes the eatery a perfect venue to savor the pinnacle of contemporary cuisine. Its yellowtail tartare, which features dices of yellowtail mixed with sourdough crumbs and poached eggs and then wrapped with slightly grilled romaine, is served with a sauce featuring katsuobushi cream, parsley oil and lemon juice. The sweet and nutty flavor of the sauce provides the ideal accompaniment to the yellowtail’s fresh flavors. Vinho delights in showcasing how wine can heighten the allure of fine cuisine.;Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
3458;Kojacha;South Korea;Seoul;17 Hakdong-ro 97-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06072, South Korea;37.52083;127.05519;86;false;true;Asian;Kojacha — Korean (“Ko”) chefs’ Japanese (“ja”) and Chinese (“cha”) cuisine. The shared culinary ambition of Chefs Choi Yu-gang and Jo Yeong-du, who previously cooked at The Shilla Hotel, has given rise to a distinct culinary genre. From its vintage lighting and furniture from the 50s and 60s that creates a singular vibe to a course meal that alternately features Chinese and Japanese dishes, this is a true icon. Signature dishes include chilled abalone salad, served in a replica of the peacock-shaped soap dish used by an empress of the Qing Dynasty, and shark fin braised in thick Chinese Superior Stock. The chefs’ performance-inspired table is a veritable display of their culinary narratives and enriches the eatery’s appeal. All dining spaces are in the form of private rooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
3459;Sushi Matsumoto;South Korea;Seoul;24 Dosan-daero 75-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06015, South Korea;37.52535;127.04573;49;false;false;Sushi;Chef Matsumoto Mizuho is renowned for replicating authenticityin local settings. Rather than chasing after gastronomictrends, this sushiya strives to faithfully reproduce the authenticsushi of mainland Japan amidst the Korean milieu. Such effortsare unmistakable—from the composition and arrangement ofshari (rice) and neta (fish topping) to the knowledgeable serviceprovided. The impressive line of tsumami (appetizers) andthe progression of nigiri sushi —reflecting the natural cadenceof flavors — remain the main culinary appeal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
3460;Evett;South Korea;Seoul;10-5 Dosan-daero 45-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06021, South Korea;37.52334;127.0362;61;false;true;Innovative, Korean;To the adventurous owner-chef Joseph Lidgerwood, who ventures out into the wild to pick ingredients or makes his own soy sauce and soybean paste from scratch, there is no such thing as an obvious or humdrum ingredient. From sikhye (sweet rice punch) sorbet with green tea syrup, which is garnished with handpicked ants for a touch of sour flavor, to tallow tart and perilla leaf juice, Evett’s menu brims with inventive dishes reimagined by the chef that perfectly reflect the seasonal sensibilities of Korea. When paired with its impressive selection of wines, those dishes become even more irresistible.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3461;Soul;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 35 Sinheung-ro 26-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04337, South Korea;37.54533;126.98443;84;false;false;Contemporary;Located in a quaint part of Seoul, this operation is Chef Yun Dae-hyun’s bold experiment in stylish fine dining. Here, the diverse culinary traditions and ingredients one may encounter in modern-day Korea converge with the familiar tastes found in everyday life to form unique fusion creations. Among the many connotations of the establishment’s name is the chef’s desire to serve soul-filled food, and this is palpable in every dish. Along with his wife, Chef Kim Hee-eun, this husband-and-wife duo have partitioned their establishment into several distinct sections, creating impeccable dining spaces for disparate cuisines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
3462;Zero Complex;South Korea;Seoul;11-8 Seobinggo-ro 59-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04384, South Korea;37.52079;126.99285;70;true;true;Innovative;Chef Lee Chung-hu has been consistently presenting innovative interpretations of the ingredients since he first opened his restaurant. The restaurant was relocated twice, but the flavors and creativity of the dishes never wavered. After moving to a larger venue, the number of tables was reduced to focus more on the quality of the food. The restaurant showcases the delightfully bouncy texture and rich, smoky flavor of sea mustard through one of their signature dishes, which is Pacific geoduck served with sides of chewy barley, sea spaghetti, and sea mustard mouse. The restaurant, located in a quiet residential area in Seobinggo-dong, might be a challenge to find but tasting the dishes overlooking the quiet garden will make it worth your while.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
3463;Exquisine;South Korea;Seoul;6 Samseong-ro 140-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06073, South Korea;37.52099;127.04965;87;true;true;Contemporary;Chef Jang Kyung-won at Exquisine has a knack for reinventing flavors. His creativity is driven by his knowledge of local ingredients and understanding of the balance between each component, which leads to dishes that are ultimately his own invention. The restaurant offers a single course menu for lunch and dinner that changes frequently depending on the availability of ingredients. The fresh herbs are from the restaurant's garden. The space is small so make sure you call ahead to reserve a table.;Credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
3464;Onjium;South Korea;Seoul;4F, 49 Hyoja-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03043, South Korea;37.58048;126.97345;85;false;false;Korean;The elegant stonewalled-path of Gyeongbokgung Palace and a modern residential neighborhood stand directly across from each other. A road is all that lies between Seoul's past and present, coexisting side by side. The same contrast is, again, evident in the modern façade of Onjieum Matgongbang and elements of tradition one discovers inside. Helmed by Cho Eun-hee, certified trainee of Korean royal court cuisine, and researcher Park Seong-bae, the space is both a research institute and restaurant. The food it offers clearly reflects the four distinct seasons and the refined beauty of Korean cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view;[]
3465;KANG MINCHUL Restaurant;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 18 Dosan-daero 68-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06064, South Korea;37.522448;127.044515;45;false;false;French, French Contemporary;Chef Kang Min-chul has been greatly inspired by time spent with master chefs, instilling in him a pride and passion for cuisine and culinary philosophy. It's also helped him find his own direction and the fare at this namesake restaurant genuinely reflects his attitude toward gastronomy. The menu comprises dishes offering a kaleidoscope of flavors while highlighting the diversity of refined French cuisine. The restaurant’s small space makes reservations a challenge, but once you secure a table, prepare to be rewarded with an unforgettable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
3466;Muoki;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 12-12 Hakdong-ro 55-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06065, South Korea;37.51896;127.04222;31;false;false;Contemporary;South African dialect for oak tree, Muoki is Chef Park Moo-hyun’s restaurant. The name is a nod to the chef’s cosmopolitan background as well as his straightforward attitude when it comes to cooking. Park has a knack for incorporating new cooking methods into creating a mélange of unpredictable flavors and textures. Tomatoes seven ways, five different kinds of carrot-based desserts, and his take on Jeju-style hairtail and pumpkin soup are good examples of his creativity and insight. Be sure to book ahead.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
3467;Bicena;South Korea;Seoul;81F Lotte World Tower, 300 Olympic-ro, Songpa-gu, Seoul, 05551, South Korea;37.5126;127.10253;29;true;false;Korean, Seasonal Cuisine;Towering above Seoul on the 81st floor of the Signiel Seoul Hotel, Bicena is trying to stay true to the spirit of traditional Korean fine dining. Bicena continues to respect the most fundamental details of slow Korean cuisine such as Jang (fermented sauces) and kimchi, the outcome of time and nature doing their work. The views from the restaurant - officially the tallest traditional restaurant in the world - are unrivaled.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3468;Muni;South Korea;Seoul;16 Dosan-daero 72-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06063, South Korea;37.52291;127.04545;45;true;false;Japanese;Tucked away in a back alley of glitzy Cheongdam-dong, Muni is helmed by Chef Kim Dong-wook, who started working in kitchens to make ends meet. To quench his growing thirst for knowledge in Japanese cuisine, Kim left for Japan to hone his skills, which would one day lay the foundation for this restaurant. To describe his style of cooking as textbook kaiseki is overkill, but his respect for tradition is evident, including in the way he utilizes seasonal ingredients and the way he plates his creations. The chef is a certified sake sommelier (Kikisake-shi), so ask for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
3469;Soseoul Hannam;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 21-18 Hannam-daero 20-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04419, South Korea;37.53528;127.00914;95;true;true;Korean;Inspired by local culinary traditions but dedicated to expressing the modern-day sensibilities of Seoul cuisine, Soseoul Hannam serves up contemporary Korean food using ingredients that are most familiar to the local palate. The chef's creations are an homage to some of the more typical dishes and preparation techniques, including seasoned salads, pan-fried and braised dishes. Kelp chips, rich soybean paste stew, sliced raw fish with gomchwi (Fischer's ragwort) and aged kimchi, and chargrilled webfoot octopus are some of its signature offerings. The restaurant also offers traditional liquor pairings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
3471;Solbam;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 231 Hakdong-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06053, South Korea;37.516;127.03378;88;true;false;Contemporary, Korean Contemporary;Visit Solbam to enjoy modern cuisine that offers an outstanding balance of tastes, aromas and flavors. Here, Chef Eom Tae-jun’s wide range of culinary experience and expertise meet Korean elements. His study of local ingredients (guided by his respect for nature and Korea’s four seasons) and his knowledge of Korean cooking techniques culminate in an uncanny synergy that gives rise to the restaurant’s unique modern dishes. With each course, the chef’s passion and exemplary effort delivera singularly rewarding gastronomic experience to guests.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3472;L'Amitié;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 30 Dosan-daero 67-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06015, South Korea;37.52591;127.04455;82;false;false;French;Since 2006, Chef Jang Myoung-sik has welcomed diners with his consistently warm and comforting French cuisine. At this new location, Jang continues to serve up his passion for French cooking on a plate. Signature dishes include steamed Wando abalone served with abalone intestine espuma, fragrant garlic purée and pickled celery as well as crispy saffron arancini.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
3473;Goryori Ken;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 15-3 Eonju-ro 152-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06021, South Korea;37.52298;127.03478;26;true;true;Contemporary, Japanese Contemporary;This intimate setting, with the main bar seating only eight, allows patrons to watch the chef's every movement. While preserving its unassuming façade on the second floor of the premises, Chef Kim Geon showcases highly seasonal ingredients in creations inspired by the freshness of the produce and his own creative intuition. Consistency and care are things Kim takes very seriously when serving his customers. The drinks menu features an impressive variety of sake produced by small Japanese breweries.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
3474;Mori;South Korea;Busan;#2-4, 2F, 24  Haeundaehaebyeon-ro 298 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48099, South Korea;35.1602;129.16659;49;true;true;Japanese;Co-owned by a Korean chef trained in Japan and his Japanese wife, Mori offers nicely presented authentic Japanese kaiseki dining that will delight both your eyes and palate. Chef Kim Wan-gyu crafts delicate dishes using the fresh seafood and seasonal produce of Busan. He has an unmatched sense of culinary balance as manifested by the perfect harmony of ingredients and a well-controlled sense of rhythm that characterizes Mori’s course meals. Enjoy authentic Japanese cuisine in this cozy space, where the chef’s sincerely crafted cuisine is complemented by the smooth and attentive service of his wife.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
3475;Fiotto;South Korea;Busan;4F, Jwadongsunhwan-ro 432, Haeunedae-gu, Busan, South Korea;35.16177;129.17362;50;true;false;Italian;Located on Dalmaji Hill, Fiotto is a cozy little bistro run by a couple that serves tasting course featuring pasta and more. The menu highlights fresh vegetables from the couple's family farm, premium Jirisan pork, heirloom rice, and other locally sourced ingredients. Nearly every component, from various types of fresh pasta and cured ham to kombucha-based vinegar and syrups, is made in-house. These elements are crafted with care to bring out Fiotto's unique, natural flavors and colors. For those who wish to experience the meticulous preparation and pure taste of nature, making a reservation is essential.;Counter dining;[]
3476;Crocadon;United Kingdom;St Mellion;St Mellion, PL12 6RL, United Kingdom;50.47174;-4.26726;36;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef-owner Dan Cox realised that to cook the best, he needed to first grow the best, so he spent five years establishing the 120 acre farm on which this beautifully restored barn is set. This is the epitome of ‘field to fork’, with the farm – which is run on regenerative principles – delivering much of the produce, and the rest sourced from similarly minded local suppliers. The cooking is assured and original, with dishes delivering wonderfully pure flavours.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3477;Loch Bay;United Kingdom;Isle of Skye;1-2 Macleods Terrace, Stein, Waternish, Isle of Skye, IV55 8GA, United Kingdom;57.51557;-6.57252;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;This pretty crofter’s cottage sits in an idyllic spot on the Waternish Peninsula and offers commanding views across the countryside to the mountains. It’s a pleasingly simple place with a wood-burning stove, Harris Tweed covered chairs and a snug, intimate feel. Stein started life as a fishing village and the cold, pure waters provide plenty of seafood, some of which is landed on the jetty opposite the restaurant. Skilfully prepared, intensely flavoured Scottish dishes have French undertones, with minimal seasoning bringing out the natural flavours.;Car park;[]
3478;Cail Bruich;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;725 Great Western Road, Glasgow City, G12 8QX, United Kingdom;55.8775205;-4.2892809;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Cail Bruich means ‘to eat well’ and this smart restaurant certainly lives up to its name. Experienced Head Chef Lorna McNee has the utmost respect for the quality of her ingredients and a great understanding of how to use them without overcomplicating things. Sauces are a particular highlight – be it a creamy truffle and brown butter emulsion or a rich bisque enhance by XO and chilli – and perfectly demonstrate the classical technique that underpins cooking which also shows a degree of creativity. The kitchen table is ideal if you want to get in on the action.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3479;Elephant;United Kingdom;Torquay;3-4 Beacon Terrace, Torquay, TQ1 2BH, United Kingdom;50.4588679;-3.5248752;17;false;false;Modern British;Simon Hulstone’s bright, laid-back restaurant looks out over Torquay Harbour. Low-backed wooden chairs sit at stone tables – backed by moody coloured walls – and elephant-themed decorations are dotted about the place. The hugely appealing dishes are led by Simon's selection of local, seasonal produce, including some grown and reared on their 96-acre farm. Accompaniments are designed to enhance each main ingredient, and the tasting menu best demonstrates the breadth of his skill.;Wheelchair access;[]
3480;Black Swan;United Kingdom;Oldstead;Oldstead, YO61 4BL, United Kingdom;54.2120881;-1.1879112;100;false;false;Creative British;All the hallmarks of a characterful country pub can be found here: exposed beams, flagged floors and even an open fire. The cooking is driven by produce from their farm, such as superb Herdwick lamb presented in two servings. The chefs work in total harmony with the gardeners, and an array of preservation techniques are used to ensure their ingredients last. The resulting dishes boast bold yet harmonious contrasts and plenty of depth. The entire team has wholeheartedly bought into the restaurant's vision and their enthusiasm is infectious. The antique-furnished bedrooms have private patios.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3481;Sorrel;United Kingdom;Dorking;77 South Street, Dorking, RH4 2JU, United Kingdom;51.2287432;-0.3345537;88;true;false;Modern British;An attractive 300-year-old former school in the town centre is home to this delightful restaurant, which is named after the chef-owner’s favourite herb. Sit on the cosy ground floor or in the intimate upstairs room, where beams divide the area into three. The creative cooking showcases the complex technical skills of the kitchen, while the well-sourced produce provides delicious natural flavours. The finely balanced combinations often look to Japan for inspiration, such as miso with scallop, clam chawanmushi with pork and bonito with sea bass.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3482;Masons Arms;United Kingdom;Knowstone;Knowstone, EX36 4RY, United Kingdom;50.995504;-3.6711138;69;true;true;Classic French;Husband and wife, Mark and Sarah Dodson, run this pretty thatched pub in a secluded little village, which boasts spectacular views over Exmoor’s rolling hills. The cooking is more sophisticated than you might expect to find in a pub, with a concise seasonal menu of attractively presented dishes firmly rooted in British and French classics –  such as an intensely flavoured raspberry soufflé. Mark has plenty of experience and employs the finest local produce to full effect, delivering pronounced, assured flavours. Service is charming, attentive and a perfect match for the food.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3484;Bohemia;United Kingdom;Saint Helier;Green Street, Saint Helier, JE2 4UH, United Kingdom;49.1814937;-2.1021873;83;false;false;Modern Cuisine;If you’ve something special to celebrate, this marble-fronted restaurant inside The Club Hotel & Spa is the place to come – and cocktails in the bar are all part of the experience. It’s a chic place, where bright linen-clad tables stand out against dimly lit, dark wood walls. Eye-catching dishes offer natural, well-balanced flavours and an occasional hint of playfulness, while the chefs clearly understand how to use techniques to enhance rather than overshadow the fine produce. Pescatarians and vegetarians are well looked after.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3488;Lympstone Manor;United Kingdom;Lympstone;Courtlands Lane, Lympstone, EX8 3NZ, United Kingdom;50.6402845;-3.4181281;65;false;false;Modern French;Local chef Michael Caines is behind this tastefully restored Grade II listed Georgian house, which sits in peaceful grounds dotted with sculptures. In summer, the pretty veranda makes the perfect place for a drink before you enjoy the sophisticated, well-balanced cooking. Michael's experience and abundant technical skill shine through in classical dishes elevated by his fine judgement and exceptional produce – such as Sladesdown duck with an exemplary jus providing great complexity of flavour. The bedrooms are beautifully furnished and some even come with a firepit and hot tub.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3489;The Sportsman;United Kingdom;Seasalter;Faversham Road, Seasalter, CT5 4BP, United Kingdom;51.344186;0.9585055;42;true;true;Modern British;An inn has stood here since 1642 and The Sportsman’s reputation continues to bring diners from across the country to this windswept spot by the sea wall. The Thames Estuary provides wonderfully fresh fish and oysters, and the adjacent marshes, woodlands and soils provide meat, game and vegetables. While the place has a comfortingly traditional feel, the dishes mix old favourites (like pot-roast pork loin) with newer ideas. The cooking is assured and satisfying, with seamless flavour combinations and an understated level of complexity. Wooden cabins in the garden are available for a peaceful night's rest.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3490;The White Swan;United Kingdom;Fence;300 Wheatley Lane Road, Fence, BB12 9QA, United Kingdom;53.8392556;-2.2508633;27;true;false;Modern British;The pub formerly known as 'The Mucky Duck' remains a traditional place where you’re guaranteed a laid-back atmosphere and a proper pint. Indeed, it is rare to find somewhere this relaxing that serves food quite this good. The set menu allows the kitchen to concentrate on delivering great value cooking from small batches of top-quality local produce. Seasonal dishes like full-flavoured hogget with morels and asparagus are a prime example, showcasing impressive classical technique and providing delicious depth of flavour.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3491;Outlaw's Fish Kitchen;United Kingdom;Port Isaac;1 Middle Street, Port Isaac, PL29 3RH, United Kingdom;50.5920513;-4.8319372;49;false;false;Seafood;Wonky walls, low ceilings and a host of delicious seafood can be found at this intimate 15th Century fisherman’s cottage, which stands right on the Port Isaac harbourside. Quality and sustainability are the watchwords here and the daily changing set menu – which features some dishes designed for sharing – is dictated not only by the seasons but the weather too. Combinations are kept simple, allowing top-notch and expertly cooked seafood, be it brill or sole, to really shine. Some bold pickled elements, like jalapeño mayonnaise, help to add an extra dimension.;;[]
3492;Dog and Gun Inn;United Kingdom;Skelton;Skelton, CA11 9SE, United Kingdom;54.7107234;-2.8753453;86;true;true;British Contemporary;The Dog and Gun is a proper village pub which does what pubs do best, by providing warmth, honesty and food that puts a smile on your face. Chef-Owner Ben Queen-Fryer cooks with his heart and plenty of natural talent, keeping dishes satisfying and recognisable. Local ingredients, including seafood from Maryport, are showcased in pure, understated compositions with plenty of depth, where flavour comes above all else. You’ll find suet puddings, soufflés and some of the best triple-cooked chips around – not forgetting a great local pint.;;[]
3493;Rogan & Co;United Kingdom;Cartmel;Devonshire Square, Cartmel, LA11 6QD, United Kingdom;54.2008814;-2.9536409;36;true;false;Creative British;L’Enclume’s laid-back cousin sits in the centre of the village and occupies a pretty cottage beside a stream, with dark wood beams and welcoming open fires. Simon Rogan’s influence is clear to see on the menu, which lists skilfully prepared, understated dishes that make great use of creative ingredient and flavour combinations. The clean, uncomplicated approach keeps the focus firmly on each main ingredient, with exceptional produce coming from Simon's Our Farm development in the Cartmel Valley, or carefully sourced from trusted Lake District suppliers.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3494;Upstairs by Tom Shepherd;United Kingdom;Lichfield;25 Bore Street, Lichfield, WS13 6NA, United Kingdom;52.6829118;-1.8277572;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the centre of Lichfield above his father's jewellery shop, this clever conversion provides a warm, relaxing space to show off the eponymous chef’s talents. It’s a deservedly popular place, offering short and long tasting menus that feature impressive dishes where flavour is to the fore and every ingredient has a purpose. Desserts are a highlight and could include the likes of 72% Araguani chocolate with crème fraîche, pecan, caramel and sherry. The attentive, enthusiastic staff genuinely love their restaurant – and you will too.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3495;House of Tides;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;28-30 The Close, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE1 3RF, United Kingdom;54.9679675;-1.6101143;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Vast and characterful, this rustic restaurant is housed in a Grade I listed former merchant’s house on the historic quayside. Flagged floors, cast iron pillars and exposed brickwork feature downstairs, with equal amounts of character upstairs courtesy of sloping floors, wonky ceilings and carved beams. Detailed, original dishes are based around fine produce and offer clear, effective flavours that are well thought through. The young service team run the restaurant well and are refreshingly unstuffy in their approach.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3496;The Barn;United Kingdom;Aughton;Prescot Road, Aughton, L39 6RT, United Kingdom;53.5402555;-2.8902774;46;false;true;Modern British;This rustic restored barn is the more informal sister to Moor Hall, and the two restaurants share the same ethos, with much of the seasonal produce coming from the five-acre grounds in which they both sit. The airy dining room comes with exposed beams and an open kitchen, while the hedge-enclosed terrace by the lake is magical on a sunny day. The cooking is modern and imaginative, and the appealing à la carte offers dishes which are British at heart, with understated elegance and well-judged combinations of punchy flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3497;Frog by Adam Handling;United Kingdom;London;34-35 Southampton Street, Covent Garden, London, WC2E 7HG, United Kingdom;51.51085;-0.12217;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Adam Handling's flagship is a restaurant that keeps up with the times: it’s fun, well-run and offers a friendly, rather uplifting atmosphere. The room's fresh, clean look keeps the focus firmly on the food, which is founded on classical techniques but blends in playfulness and originality to produce colourful, well-crafted dishes which are beautiful to behold. The signature bread served with chicken skin butter and liver pâté is inspired by Adam's sister, who would only eat roast chicken for Sunday lunch. The menu comes in the form of a map of Britain, showing where the ingredients come from.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3499;heft;United Kingdom;Newton in Cartmel;Newton in Cartmel, LA11 6JH, United Kingdom;54.2386388;-2.9190308;79;false;false;Modern British, Regional Cuisine;This 17th-century village inn has been sympathetically restored by Cumbrian born-and-bred couple Kevin and Nicola Tickle – and the locals are loving them for it, with the front bar still open for people to pop in for a pint and freshly made pie. In the rear restaurant, Kevin conjures up a tasting menu inspired by the seasons, the surroundings, his imagination and his local foraging knowledge. The playfully described dishes reveal real depth and originality. On certain days all tables are served at the same time, so be prepared to arrive promptly.;;[]
3500;Shaun Rankin at Grantley Hall;United Kingdom;Ripon;Grantley Hall, Ripon, HG4 3ET, United Kingdom;54.11882;-1.63174;22;false;false;Modern British, Regional Cuisine;This beautifully decorated, formal restaurant occupies what was once the music room of this sumptuous and luxurious 17C country house. Shaun Rankin’s creative, modern cooking is a perfect fit for these surroundings and is inspired by his childhood memories and an insider’s knowledge of the area. There is a bounteous larder in Yorkshire and the tasting menu, which flows in a skilled way, focuses on its very best produce. Adding to the experience is a well-organised and professional service team.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3503;Latymer;United Kingdom;Bagshot;London Road, Bagshot, GU19 5EU, United Kingdom;51.3566975;-0.7088648;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away inside the luxurious Pennyhill Park Hotel is this little culinary oasis. The tasting menu comes in a surprise format, but you can expect top-notch produce like Brixham sea bass and Aynhoe deer to be on there. These fine ingredients are crafted into dishes that use classic combinations which have been refined and reworked in a creative modern style. Flavours, textures and temperatures show wonderful balance and there's nothing superfluous on the plate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3507;House;Ireland;Ardmore;Middle Road, Ardmore, P36 AD89, Ireland;51.9486077;-7.7150846;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in the Cliff House Hotel – a modern, glass-fronted building which, unsurprisingly, hugs the cliffside – this restaurant benefits from a stunning view across Ardmore Bay. Fortunately, the cooking is a match for its surroundings, taking exceptional Irish produce and building on it using skilled technique and a smattering of global influences. Terrific lobster caught in Ardmore Bay, for example, might come with rogan josh sauce and garlic naan for a distinctly Indian touch. Throughout the cooking, the dishes are attractively presented without being showy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3508;The Angel;United Kingdom;Hetton;Hetton, BD23 6LT, United Kingdom;54.0258838;-2.0596882;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Deep within the Yorkshire Dales sits The Angel, a stunning stone-built inn with 15C origins, which now has a modern Nordic style courtesy of polished concrete floors and light wood furnishings. Classic combinations are to the fore but are subtly modernised and refined, with dishes demonstrating a simplicity that allows every ingredient to shine. The exuberant service team enhance the experience, and the bedrooms – which are spread around the village – mix the classic and the contemporary.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3511;Paul Ainsworth at No.6;United Kingdom;Padstow;6 Middle Street, Padstow, PL28 8AP, United Kingdom;50.5415048;-4.9398914;19;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Guests are put centre stage and are treated to a real experience at this restaurant set in a delightful Georgian townhouse. Paul Ainsworth has developed his own style over the years and the menu is a wonderful showcase for his considerable talents. The creative and sometimes playful cooking is underpinned by well-honed classic techniques and the finest Cornish produce, in dishes like the signature ‘Crabsticks and Scones’ and the seasonally changing ‘Compañero baba’. Friendly, well-versed service helps to make your visit a memorable one.;Air conditioning;[]
3513;The Dining Room;United Kingdom;Malmesbury;Easton Grey, Malmesbury, SN16 0RB, United Kingdom;51.5840371;-2.1558527;60;false;true;Creative;There’s a serene, romantic feel to this restaurant inside the charming Whatley Manor country house, which dates back to 1802 and sports 12 acres of formal grounds. The evening starts with snacks in the kitchen, before moving through to the dining room for the main event. Terse menu descriptions belie the detail and creativity in the artfully presented dishes, which come with some intriguing contrasts of texture and flavour. Extend your visit with an overnight stay in one of the luxurious modern bedrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3514;Cottage in the Wood;United Kingdom;Braithwaite;Magic Hill, Whinlatter Forest, Braithwaite, CA12 5TW, United Kingdom;54.6089402;-3.2218372;25;false;false;Modern British;As you make your way up the Whinlatter Pass, you will find this remote black and white inn that boasts some fabulous Lakeland views – best enjoyed from a seat in the conservatory. The cooking comes in the form of a tasting menu and makes use of Lakeland produce like Herdwick lamb from Coniston, with every part of the ingredient put to use. Dishes are well-conceived and blend classical execution with a subtle modernity that highlights a variety of flavours and textures. It’s a cosy little place, with a range of bedrooms available if you wish to stay the night.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3515;Restaurant Hywel Jones by Lucknam Park;United Kingdom;Colerne;Colerne, SN14 8AZ, United Kingdom;51.4562596;-2.2587232;67;false;true;Modern British;This is country house dining at its finest – opulent, formal and sophisticated – and it suits this grand Palladian mansion perfectly. Rich, elegant décor, extravagant furnishings and sumptuous fabrics feature throughout, from the beautiful bedrooms to the drawing rooms where pre-meal drinks are enjoyed. Expertly crafted dishes rely on classic techniques but have a light, modern style, and ingredients are luxurious and of top quality. Structured service comes with as much polish as the silver.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3516;Bybrook;United Kingdom;Castle Combe;West Street, Castle Combe, SN14 7HX, United Kingdom;51.4938103;-2.2319991;86;true;true;Modern British;One of the last true country house hotels, this 14th-century manor sits within 365 acres of formal gardens and parkland in a picture-postcard village – and the immensely charming interior features characterful oak panelling and a host of cosy open-fired lounges. Quality produce plays a pivotal role in the menu, which results in a flavoursome blend of simple and premium ingredients. Dishes are precisely prepared and deliver refined, classic combinations with modern overtones. Luxurious bedrooms are split between the house and mews cottages.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3518;Woven by Adam Smith;United Kingdom;Ascot;Blacknest Road, Ascot, SL5 7SE, United Kingdom;51.4046576;-0.6164597;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed within a luxurious 18th-century property, itself surrounded by 246 acres of beautiful grounds, this elegant restaurant feels like a truly special place. Sporting golden, almost autumnal décor on the ground floor of the Coworth Park hotel, the restaurant is a stage for the eponymous chef to showcase a roll-call of superb British produce. His technically skilled, beautifully presented dishes have a lightness of touch, while also displaying real depth and finesse. The signature chocolate dessert delivers on its promise, ending your visit on a euphoric note.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3519;Nut Tree Inn;United Kingdom;Murcott;Main Street, Murcott, OX5 2RE, United Kingdom;51.8361729;-1.1499072;91;false;false;Modern British;With its 15th-century origins and smartly thatched roof, this may look like a typical English pub, but it's no ordinary village local. Mike and Imogen bought the place back in 2006 and have since put Murcott on the foodie map, whilst also keeping their inn a friendly, welcoming place. Refined, elegant dishes are delivered in the form of a 7 course tasting menu that shows the kitchen's ability to deliver tried-and-tested favourites with great skill. Walk-ins are welcome, with a 'pub classics' menu offering a choice of simpler dishes like steak & chips, plus a roast on Sundays.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3520;Fordwich Arms;United Kingdom;Fordwich;King Street, Fordwich, CT2 0DB, United Kingdom;51.2957384;1.1264202;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine;England’s smallest town is a pretty little place and this elegant Arts and Crafts style building fits it perfectly. It sits in a delightful spot beside the river and its wisteria-covered terrace affords wonderful views. An impressive wood-topped bar and open fires welcome you in and the wood-panelled dining room bursts with charm. The cooking is modern, creative and sometimes playful but this is never at the expense of flavour. Excellent quality ingredients, like plump Scottish langoustines, underpin it all.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3522;Pea Porridge;United Kingdom;Bury St Edmunds;28-29 Cannon Street, Bury St Edmunds, IP33 1JR, United Kingdom;52.249572;0.7144697;67;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Tucked away on a residential square, this neighbourhood restaurant is warmly and personally run by a husband and wife team, and the unusual name is a nod to the old town green which once stood out front. The daily changing menu of North African, Middle Eastern and Mediterranean dishes involves a range of ingredients cooked over charcoal. The sourdough flatbread fresh from the oven kicks things off perfectly and the unfussy dishes deliver bold, well-defined flavours which are skilfully executed. The esoteric wine list champions organic and natural wines, while the lunch menu provides great value.;;[]
3524;Bridge Arms;United Kingdom;Bridge;53 High Street, Bridge, CT4 5LA, United Kingdom;51.2462247;1.1253358;99;true;false;Modern British;In the charming village of Bridge, within the Nailbourne Valley, lies this Grade II listed 16C pub with low beams, open fires and plenty of character. The highly skilled cooking is available in a range of forms, from snacks like buttermilk fried chicken to dishes cooked over charcoal in the Josper oven, which feature on the seasonal à la carte. Prime seasonal produce like line-caught turbot is treated with exacting detail by the chefs, resulting in beautifully seasoned dishes. They have a period cottage nearby for those looking to stay the night.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
3525;Adam's;United Kingdom;Birmingham;16 Waterloo Street, Birmingham, B2 5UG, United Kingdom;52.4799361;-1.9013634;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Adam Stokes’ elegant restaurant feels like it’s been part of the Birmingham dining scene forever. It’s a luxurious place with an art-deco-cum-retro style that includes a smart cocktail bar and a plush dining room. The cooking seamlessly mixes tradition and modernity, offering tried-and-tested combinations in dishes you will recognise in name, but served in ways you’ve probably never encountered. That being said, the primary flavours are left uncrowded, with nothing extraneous on the plate. An impressive wine selection adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3526;Humble Chicken;United Kingdom;London;54 Frith Street, Soho, London, W1D 4SL, United Kingdom;51.5138258;-0.1317621;17;true;true;Japanese;While Chef-Owner Angelo Sato's Japanese heritage provides the basis for this modern, upbeat izakaya, his creative streak ensures the theatrical tasting menu takes on a style all its own. Clever flavour and temperature combinations feature throughout, as do the kitchen's immense precision and technical skill. The shokupan bread serving is a real event, packed with originality and showcasing a range of delicious accompaniments. Pumping music contributes to a great atmosphere, whilst sake 'journeys' are encouraged to add to the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
3527;Lake Road Kitchen;United Kingdom;Ambleside;Lake Road, Ambleside, LA22 0AD, United Kingdom;54.4302532;-2.9622231;21;true;false;Creative;Nordic décor meets the Lake District at this intimate restaurant, where wooden planks line the walls and sheepskins cover the chairs. The Lakes provides much of the top-drawer produce, although the chefs do look further afield, with a few Japanese influences being incorporated, such as in the king mackerel tartare with white soy, mirin and gold grade nori. Dishes often look simple, but are in fact complex, creative and contain impressive depth of flavour – years of culinary experience are evident in every mouthful. Service is smooth, with the detailed dish descriptions delivered with confidence and pride.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3528;Artichoke;United Kingdom;Amersham;9 Market Square, Amersham, HP7 0DF, United Kingdom;51.666449;-0.6162893;55;false;false;Modern British;At the centre of a picturesque town sits this 16C red-brick house: a bijou place, with a heavily timbered interior and a contemporary design-led style. Self-taught chef-owner Laurie Gear brings together his experience from ‘stages’ at The Fat Duck and Noma in an array of menus. Accomplished, modern British dishes are confidently prepared and the well-measured flavour combinations have an understated complexity. Lamb is reared locally and venison is from the Woburn Estate, while seafood from Brixham is a highlight.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3529;Pétrus by Gordon Ramsay;United Kingdom;London;1 Kinnerton Street, Belgravia, London, SW1X 8EA, United Kingdom;51.4995628;-0.1567357;32;false;false;French, French Contemporary;Named after the famous Pomerol estate in Bordeaux, wine plays an understandably pivotal role at this impeccably run restaurant that caters to both well-to-do locals and those looking for a special night out. At the heart of the elegant room is its striking glass-walled wine store, which features over 700 bins, including Château Pétrus going back to 1948. The cooking itself offers sumptuous luxury ingredients from lobster to turbot, presented in precise, refined dishes with a classic French heart and little regard for unnecessary frills.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3531;Sollip;United Kingdom;London;Unit 1, 8 Melior Street, Southwark, London, SE1 3QP, United Kingdom;51.5025583;-0.0846577;90;false;true;Creative;Flying somewhat under the radar, this extremely likeable restaurant is run by a Korean husband-and-wife team who combine skills learnt in Europe’s top kitchens with techniques and flavours from their homeland. The daikon tarte Tatin and Peach pavlova dessert are stand-outs, but all the dishes are polished and poised, rather than showy or over-complicated. The room has a cool, calm and contemporary feel, where you sense that every element has been carefully considered. Wonderfully relaxed and professional service is a perfect fit for the food.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3532;Unalome by Graeme Cheevers;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;36 Kelvingrove Street, Glasgow City, G3 7RZ, United Kingdom;55.8656316;-4.2837872;29;false;true;Modern British;In the lively hub of Finnieston, this elegant spot in a period building represents local chef Graeme Cheevers' desire to create a restaurant for all occasions. His considerable culinary skills pay their respects to the finest of Scottish produce, be it Orkney scallops or North Sea cod, in dishes that display his classical leanings. There is a precision and sophistication to the cooking, and it’s well worth going for the full tasting menu and the thoughtfully considered wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3533;Pentonbridge Inn;United Kingdom;Penton;Penton, CA6 5QB, United Kingdom;55.0798807;-2.8812522;33;true;false;Modern British;There's an inviting, contemporary feel to this 18th-century Cumbrian inn that's situated so far north, it nearly crosses the Scottish border. If you time your visit right, you'll get a glimpse of a truly spectacular sunset. The adept kitchen team match the wonderful surroundings with ease, eschewing unnecessary flourishes and instead delivering beautiful balance and depth of flavour with just a few ingredients – as evidenced by superb vadouvan-spiced scallops. Extend your visit with a stay in one of the smart bedrooms.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3534;mýse;United Kingdom;Hovingham;Main Street, Hovingham, YO62 4LF, United Kingdom;54.1723889;-0.9790181;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a pretty little village on the edge of the North York Moors lies this former pub with stripped-back décor – expect flagstone floors, whitewashed beams and exposed stone walls. The tasting menu features prime produce enhanced by a range of techniques, both traditional and modern, as with the subtle, well-judged use of pickling and preserving. A top wine list and non-alcoholic pairings ensure the food isn’t the only highlight, while cosy, simply decorated bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
3535;Winteringham Fields;United Kingdom;Winteringham;1 Silver Street, Winteringham, DN15 9ND, United Kingdom;53.6877042;-0.5904314;39;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This 16th-century former farmhouse sits in a sleepy village close to the Humber Estuary. It’s an area rich in agriculture, so it’s no surprise to find local ingredients to the fore on the surprise tasting menu, be they from regional producers, nearby farms or the long-standing owners’ smallholding where they rear animals and grow veg. The chef's personality shines through in the full-flavoured dishes, from nods to his Yorkshire roots to refined takes on his favourite foods, like chicken tacos and lamb kebab. Sumptuous bedrooms mix classic character with modern comforts.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3537;Galvin La Chapelle;United Kingdom;London;35 Spital Square, Shoreditch, London, E1 6DY, United Kingdom;51.520295;-0.0783716;18;true;false;French;It might be smaller than the glass-fronted office buildings that surround it but this red-brick, Grade II listed former school certainly holds its own. The magnificent vaulted room lends itself effortlessly to its role as a glamorous brasserie and the atmosphere is buzzy without being overly loud. It’s a family affair, with Jeff Galvin in the kitchen and brother David responsible for sourcing produce at the market. Cooking is classic French with a light, modern touch, and there are no unnecessary fripperies – just reassuringly familiar combinations with the emphasis on bold, harmonious flavours.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3538;The Cross;United Kingdom;Kenilworth;16 New Street, Kenilworth, CV8 2EZ, United Kingdom;52.3503568;-1.5796992;75;true;false;British Contemporary;The front bar of this charming 19th-century, Grade II listed inn makes a cosy place for a beer, while the pretty, foliage-enclosed rear terrace is great for lunch and drinks on a warm day. For dinner, sit in the back room to watch the kitchen team in action, or in the bright, airy former classroom with its eye-catching wall lamps shaped like hand bells. Chef Adam Bennett creates bold, classically based dishes which champion local produce and have been re-mastered and refined to deliver well-judged combinations of flavours and textures. For the full experience, go for the tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3539;Hinds Head;United Kingdom;Bray;High Street, Bray, SL6 2AB, United Kingdom;51.5081037;-0.7020536;60;false;false;Traditional British;Set in the Thameside village of Bray, this sweet, quintessentially English inn is best known as Heston Blumenthal’s informal dining option – but that doesn’t make it any less of an experience. Concise menus offer time-honoured British dishes presented in a clean, modern style, with punchy flavours and the occasional playful element. The combinations work beautifully and dishes are executed with the utmost precision, as with the fabulous 'Crab Soup & Sandwich'. Service is relaxed and friendly, and the atmosphere buzzes with the hum of contented diners.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3540;Pipe and Glass;United Kingdom;South Dalton;West End, South Dalton, HU17 7PN, United Kingdom;53.8953622;-0.5350872;48;true;false;Traditional British;Look for the church spire to help you navigate through the maze of country lanes that lead to this charming 15th-century pub, which was originally the gatehouse of Dalton Park. The Yorkshire larder is well-represented on the menus, with numerous daily specials reflecting what’s best in season. Unfussy, instantly recognisable dishes like dressed crab are elevated thanks to the exceptional ingredients and the kitchen's keen sense of balance. The charming team ensure everyone is looked after with a smile, and smart bedrooms add a luxurious edge.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3541;Murano;United Kingdom;London;20 Queen Street, Mayfair, London, W1J 5PP, United Kingdom;51.5071742;-0.1472229;30;false;true;Italian;Angela Hartnett’s stylish restaurant has been a Mayfair fixture since 2008, but was given a little decorative refreshment in 2023, leaving the room brighter and a little less formally attired. Her Italian heritage continues to inform the appealing menu, with pasta dishes like provolone and smoked potato agnolotti particularly impressive. Prime British ingredients such as Cornish cod and Hereford beef are used to good effect – and the Amalfi lemon tart remains a reassuringly permanent fixture on the dessert menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3543;Quilon;United Kingdom;London;41 Buckingham Gate, Westminster, London, SW1E 6AF, United Kingdom;51.4989023;-0.1379057;70;false;true;Indian;Quilon's longevity is no accident, as it delivers an object lesson in the importance of consistency and reliability. Longtime Head Chef Sriram Aylur and his experienced team put their focus on the cuisine of southwest India and the Malabar Coast, which means that seafood is always going to be a good choice. The recipes and preparation may be traditional, but the presentation is more contemporary, and the kitchen has an assured yet delicate touch. The ingredients are first-rate and the sauces are particularly good.This restaurant is temporarily closed for renovation until May 2025.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3545;The Ritz Restaurant;United Kingdom;London;150 Piccadilly, St James’s, London, W1J 9BR, United Kingdom;51.5069929;-0.1418453;96;true;true;Modern British;With its stunning Louis XVI decoration, this is a room that will take your breath away, and there’s a flamboyancy in the delivery of the dishes that lives up to the surroundings. Equally impressive is the cooking itself, displaying balance, refinement and depth of flavour at every turn. You need only take one glance at the menu featuring dishes like langoustine 'à la nage' to see that classical French techniques and luxury ingredients both play a big role in proceedings. The sharing ‘Arts de la Table’ dishes allow the impeccable service team to keep the theatre of the gueridon trolley alive.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3547;Home;United Kingdom;Penarth;1 Royal Buildings, Stanwell Road, Penarth, CF64 3EB, United Kingdom;51.4361609;-3.1752013;55;false;true;Modern Cuisine;James Sommerin's restaurant is a small, intimate affair that provides an immersive yet warm and friendly experience. As the name implies, it’s staffed almost exclusively by family members, with James and his daughter Georgia working together in the open kitchen. The surprise menu changes regularly and is full of impeccable dishes that make great use of produce provided by local suppliers. Wales should be as proud of this restaurant as any Josh Adams try.;Air conditioning;[]
3548;Trishna;United Kingdom;London;15-17 Blandford Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 3DG, United Kingdom;51.5183427;-0.1529346;30;false;false;Indian;India's southwest coast provides the kitchen with most of its influences and the menu is full of vibrant, exciting dishes, including some original creations from the tandoor. However, the undoubted star of the show is a wondrously rich version of the dish made famous by the original Trishna in Mumbai: brown crab with lots of butter and a kick of red chilli. The various tasting menus often provide the most rounded experience, and all of the dishes are as fresh tasting and beautifully spiced as they are colourful. Much thought has also gone into the matching wines.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3550;Stark;United Kingdom;East Mersea;East Road, East Mersea, CO5 8TQ, United Kingdom;51.7907812;0.9686532;55;false;true;Modern British;Having relocated from Broadstairs to Mersea Island, the family-run Stark has retained all of its intimacy, passion and enthusiasm. Chef Ben Crittenden works alone in the kitchen crafting a 6 course menu which acts as an ode to top-notch produce. Clever and refined flavour combinations are deployed with great precision to enhance already delicious ingredients like shh'annu lamb and prime quality cod – go for the well-constructed wine pairings to ease any indecision. Be sure to check the tide timetable when visiting to ensure The Strood isn't flooded.;Car park;[]
3551;Morston Hall;United Kingdom;Morston;The Street, Morston, NR25 7AA, United Kingdom;52.9546971;0.9880742;26;true;true;Modern British;A few bites in and it’s patently obvious that Galton Blackiston is a chef with a deep knowledge and appreciation of the great produce found in Norfolk. Whether picked from the kitchen garden, foraged from nearby beaches or delivered by local fishermen, the ingredients are superb, and are treated well in dishes with classical flavour combinations. The conservatory looking out over the garden is the place to sit in the summer months, while those staying the night can choose from contemporary country house bedrooms or more luxurious garden rooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3552;Sabor;United Kingdom;London;35-37 Heddon Street, Mayfair, London, W1B 4BR, United Kingdom;51.5114463;-0.1394943;39;false;true;Spanish;Chef Nieves Barragán has created something authentic and truly joyful with Sabor. There are three distinct areas: on the ground floor is the bar and, opposite, a counter serving dishes from all over Spain including fresh seafood from their in-house fishmonger. Upstairs is El Asador – the only area for which bookings are taken – and here you can enjoy specialities from Galicia and Castile. There are two must-haves: the succulent Segovian suckling pig roasted in the specially built oven and the melt-in-the-mouth octopus cooked in vast copper pans. You’ll be licking your lips for hours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3553;Àclèaf;United Kingdom;Plymouth;Boringdon Hill, Colebrook, Plymouth, PL7 4DP, United Kingdom;50.4016374;-4.0566742;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The impressive Boringdon Hall Hotel plays host to this cosy, intimate restaurant, which sits under wooden beams within the former minstrels’ gallery. The building itself dates back to the Domesday book and still exudes a historic feel. Prime seasonal ingredients feature in exciting modern dishes which are refined yet restrained and demonstrate great attention to detail. The range of internationally influenced flavours are knowledgably balanced, aptly demonstrated by the cured hamachi with subtle yuzu ponzu.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3556;Northcote;United Kingdom;Langho;Northcote Road, Langho, BB6 8BE, United Kingdom;53.8091411;-2.4474228;85;true;true;Modern British;The Northcote Hotel's restaurant continues to excel under the stewardship of Executive Chef Lisa Goodwin-Allen. The cooking is underpinned by superb produce, which often comes from local, biodynamic and organic suppliers or their own kitchen garden. This is fashioned into dishes with distinct, bold flavours, brought together in complementary combinations. The extensive wine list includes some exceptional bottles and a glass-walled "Chef's Table" room lets you in on the action.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3557;Meadowsweet;United Kingdom;Holt;37 Norwich Road, Holt, NR25 6SA, United Kingdom;52.9046228;1.0872934;66;true;false;Modern British;A lovingly restored Georgian building is the setting for this charming restaurant. You enter via the back of the building, through an illuminated garden, and are then warmly welcomed into a beautiful dining room, where the lovely handmade tables have the menu and cutlery hidden in a drawer. The finest produce, be it lobster or quail, is delivered via a skilfully prepared tasting menu, where deep flavours come together perfectly and there's the odd playful touch, like dessert served across several dishes to share. Three restful bedrooms provide the perfect overnight escape.;Garden or park;[]
3558;Lumière;United Kingdom;Cheltenham;Clarence Parade, Cheltenham, GL50 3PA, United Kingdom;51.9003929;-2.0771961;69;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the centre of this charming spa town you’ll find an unassuming exterior concealing an elegantly stylish restaurant. Helen runs the service and she’s a natural host, so you’ll be warmly welcomed and well looked after. Her experienced husband Jon runs things in the kitchen and his overtly seasonal cooking demonstrates impressive classical technique and attention to detail, exemplified by the expertly cooked venison with a rich red wine sauce. His more playful side comes out in the crowd-pleasing signature 'Tequila Slammer' sorbet.;Air conditioning;[]
3559;Osip;United Kingdom;Bruton;25 Kingsettle Hill, Hardway, Bruton, BA10 0LN, United Kingdom;51.1047641;-2.4062902;52;false;false;Modern British;Formerly located in the centre of Bruton, Osip is now situated more rurally, in a stunningly renovated former pub that retains the minimalistic elegance of the original. Forward-thinking chef Merlin Labron-Johnson and his enthusiastic team are passionate about their farm-to-table ethos, with the surprise tasting menu showcasing an array of home-grown and locally sourced produce. Dishes like chilled tomato consommé with fig oil shine in their technical precision and pure, natural flavours. The wine pairings highlight organic and biodynamic choices.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3560;KOL;United Kingdom;London;9 Seymour Street, Marylebone, London, W1H 7BA, United Kingdom;51.5147873;-0.1574918;33;true;false;Mexican, Modern Cuisine;‘Mexican soul, British ingredients’ is the tagline of this big, bold restaurant, and it proves an exhilarating combination. The kitchen adds creativity and impressive modern technique to hyper-seasonal recipes rooted in tradition, resulting in wonderful flavour contrasts and imagination in outstanding dishes like the signature langoustine taco with smoked chilli and sea buckthorn. The interesting wine list focuses on lesser-known choices from Central and Eastern Europe, while the downstairs Mezcaleria offers a range of Mexican spirits for those who don’t want the night to end.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3561;Evelyn's Table;United Kingdom;London;The Blue Posts, 28 Rupert Street, Soho, London, W1D 6DJ, United Kingdom;51.5111527;-0.1326051;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;There’s seating for just 12 people at this counter located in the former beer cellar of The Blue Posts pub. Claustrophobes may be hesitant but on offer is an intriguing and rewarding gastronomic experience. There are two sittings a night and as the set menu is served to all at the same time, do be punctual – if you're early, try the top-floor bar of the pub. Prime British ingredients power dishes that are thoughtfully composed and confidently prepared. Expect the occasional whimsical note too, as with the Peking-style mallard created as a nod to the restaurant’s proximity to Chinatown.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3562;Elystan Street;United Kingdom;London;43 Elystan Street, Chelsea, London, SW3 3NT, United Kingdom;51.4916238;-0.1677604;86;true;false;Modern British;Elystan Street is a neighbourhood restaurant, but the neighbourhood it is in is Chelsea, so you can expect to find elegance and style in spades. It’s a collaboration between Philip Howard and Rebecca Mascarenhas, and with its huge windows, well-judged lighting and friendly service, is an equally charming spot for a light lunch or intimate dinner. Cooking is pared-back and unfussy, yet there’s vigour and energy to it which suggests it comes from the heart. Dishes have a classical base but a lightness of touch, and flavours are well-defined and eminently satisfying.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3564;Dysart Petersham;United Kingdom;London;135 Petersham Road, Richmond, London, TW10 7AA, United Kingdom;51.4464732;-0.2996555;23;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A gorgeous Arts and Crafts building houses this warm, homely restaurant. There's a natural ethos running throughout the highly seasonal menus, where impeccably sourced ingredients abound in assured, satisfying dishes that deliver some interesting combinations, underpinned by a classical base. The bold, flavour-packed sauces are a highlight, as are the creative desserts, and the warm, passionate service leaves no detail overlooked.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3565;Ormer Mayfair;United Kingdom;London;7-12 Half Moon Street, Mayfair, London, W1J 7BH, United Kingdom;51.5065597;-0.1453868;26;false;true;Modern British;Hidden away in the basement of the Flemings Mayfair Hotel, this restaurant offers understated elegance and charming, unstuffy service. The tasting menu is served in 5 or 7 courses and features carefully constructed dishes using classic combinations, that are lifted to a new level by hints of originality. The cooking is underpinned by superb ingredients from around the British Isles, such as Cornish mackerel or Scottish langoustines, alongside some produce from the garden at their sister hotel in Essex. The wine list and pairings are both excellent.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3567;Taku;United Kingdom;London;36 Albemarle Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 4JE, United Kingdom;51.5089202;-0.1419157;35;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;The home of internationally renowned sushi chef Takuya Watanabe and right-hand man Long Ng, this 16-seater restaurant is centred around its striking counter fashioned from fine English oak. The omakase menu has a similar focus on quality, using only the finest ingredients, mostly from European waters. There’s a purity and elegance to every mouthful, exemplified by the superlative 'tuna two ways'. There’s one sitting at lunch and two at dinner – and as all guests are served together, be sure to arrive on time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
3568;The Whitebrook;United Kingdom;Whitebrook;Whitebrook, NP25 4TX, United Kingdom;51.759697;-2.686909;71;true;true;Creative British;The very definition of a destination restaurant, this place's isolated woodland feel is all part of its inherent charm. A nature-inspired colour theme and rustic wood flooring suit the location down to a tee. Ingredients are sourced from Wye Valley and their own kitchen garden, and are used in botanically based dishes with natural flavours. Middle White suckling pig is one of their signatures and Hereford raspberries with garden herb sorbet is a fitting end to dinner. There’s also a particularly creative vegetarian menu. Bedrooms follow the theme of bringing nature inside.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3569;Cycene;United Kingdom;London;Blue Mountain School, 9 Chance Street, Shoreditch, London, E2 7JB, United Kingdom;51.5244846;-0.0752056;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Ring the bell and you’re welcomed into an operation unlike any other – the name may be old English for ‘kitchen’, but this is very much a restaurant of the moment. You start with a drink and the first course in the bar, then it’s upstairs for a snack in the kitchen before being seated in the intimate dining room with its bespoke crockery and pottery. It’s easy to see why the chef, who is a keen forager, talks so proudly of his ingredients, whether that’s the Shetland cod or the Highland wagyu. He and his team deliver and explain in detail their delicate, balanced and innovative dishes.;;[]
3570;La Trompette;United Kingdom;London;3-7 Devonshire Road, Chiswick, London, W4 2EU, United Kingdom;51.48946;-0.25431;71;false;true;Modern British;The jewel in Chiswick’s culinary crown remains as popular as ever, thanks to its local feel, relaxed atmosphere and, most importantly, its skilled and generous cooking. Largely British ingredients are combined with influences from France and occasionally the wider Mediterranean. So you can expect carefully prepared dishes like Cornish cod with squid ink cavatelli or Devonshire duck breast with potato galette, where the flavours are as assured as they are satisfying. Bright and delightful on a summer’s day and cosy and warm in winter, this is a restaurant for all seasons and all occasions.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3572;Cedar Tree by Hrishikesh Desai;United Kingdom;Brampton;Farlam Hall Hotel, Hallbankgate, Brampton, CA8 2NG, United Kingdom;54.9341337;-2.6728565;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Named after the ancient tree that stands in front of it, this restaurant sits inside the Farlam Hall Hotel. A historic Cumbrian country house, its refurbishment transformed it into an elegant retreat that deftly mixes the antique with the contemporary. The restaurant offers Indian-influenced cooking in the form of a generous tasting menu or an à la carte, both showcasing British produce – including plenty of ingredients from the kitchen garden – enhanced by skilful spicing. The service team are on the ball and ensure you are well looked after.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
3573;Chestnut;Ireland;Ballydehob;Staball Hill, Ballydehob, P81 X681, Ireland;51.5626443;-9.4607416;16;true;true;Modern Cuisine;There's a laid-back feel to this sweet, intimate restaurant where the shelves are laden with wine, mead and all manner of jars full of produce marinating, curing or fermenting. Skeaghanore duck is among the County Cork produce championed on the constantly evolving tasting menu, where skilfully prepared dishes show a great understanding of textures and tastes, and are pleasingly understated in their pure, natural flavours. Smaller growers are present in the wine pairings, while they make their own juices and cordials for the non-alcoholic option.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3574;Grace & Savour;United Kingdom;Hampton in Arden;Hampton Manor, Shadowbrook Lane, Hampton in Arden, B92 0EN, United Kingdom;52.4287987;-1.7009081;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Its idyllic setting is one of Grace & Savour's many draws. Housed in a relatively new building within the Hampton Manor estate, it's a simply beautiful restaurant where the historic meets the contemporary and diners can look out onto the restored Victorian kitchen garden. Some dishes are eye-catching and elaborate in their make-up, while others are defined by their simplicity, and a modern Nordic touch means you can expect plenty of preserved elements complementing the outstanding British produce – like succulent Cornish lobster. Make it an occasion by booking a bedroom.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
3576;Campagne;Ireland;Kilkenny;5 The Arches, Gashouse Lane, Kilkenny, R95 X092, Ireland;52.655984;-7.2460652;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This long-standing restaurant is owned and run by experienced chef Garrett Byrne – who really knows his craft – along with his partner, Brid Hannon, who provides relaxed, friendly service. The modern interior is sleek, with curved banquettes, spot-lit dark wood tables and striking local artwork hanging on the walls. Top quality Irish ingredients are showcased in richly flavoured, classic dishes: you won’t find foams or smears on your plate here – just confidently cooked, skilfully balanced dishes, with exemplary plating, saucing and seasoning.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3578;Timberyard;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;10 Lady Lawson Street, Edinburgh, EH3 9DS, United Kingdom;55.9465314;-3.2021003;89;true;false;Modern British, Contemporary;A big red door indicates that you have arrived at this rustic warehouse conversion, in which the chefs practise a culinary ethos that centres around the local, the seasonal and letting the produce speak for itself. It takes a lot of skill and no little ability to take just a few prime ingredients and fashion dishes that are so well defined and satisfying, and the kitchen here pulls it off with aplomb. You can warm yourself by the stove in winter or sit in the walled courtyard in the summer. The lovely service team are on the ball and the music’s great too.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3579;The Oak Room;Ireland;Adare;Adare Manor, Adare, V94 W8WR, Ireland;52.5636528;-8.7772396;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant inside the impressive Adare Manor has all the grandeur you would expect, with wood-panelled walls, lavish chandeliers and a glass-enclosed terrace with views over the 850 acre grounds. The assured, refreshingly understated cooking champions top Irish ingredients, with dishes comprising just 3 or 4 components and allowing each one the room to make an impression. Combinations are refined and well-balanced, and great attention is given to the finer details. The wine list is a labour of love and offers a superb range by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3580;Martin Wishart;United Kingdom;Leith;54 The Shore, Leith, EH6 6RA, United Kingdom;55.9755098;-3.1703986;72;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;For over 20 years, Martin Wishart has been welcoming diners to his eponymous restaurant in the historic and characterful port of Leith. Over the years, he has continually tweaked and reassessed the food and the décor, and the bright, modern style of the dining room is a great match for the current cooking. The kitchen shows great skill in marrying top Scottish produce like grouse and Orkney scallops with classic French technique, resulting in dishes that deliver the flavours they promise, with nothing unnecessary on the plate.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3581;SOLSTICE BY KENNY ATKINSON;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;5-7 Side, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE1 3JE, United Kingdom;54.9692585;-1.6084582;24;true;true;Modern British;This intimate, personably run restaurant is just around the corner from the eponymous chef-owner’s flagship, House of Tides, and serves a multi-course tasting menu of well-balanced, highly intricate and complex dishes. The kitchen’s skill allows top-drawer ingredients to shine, whether that be scallops or pigeon, and the meal ends on a high with the varied, exquisitely constructed desserts. The chefs present the plates to guests themselves and provide detailed descriptions of their make-up. Go for the wine pairing for the ultimate dining experience.;Air conditioning;[]
3582;Endo at The Rotunda;United Kingdom;London;The Helios, 101 Wood Lane, Shepherd's Bush, London, W12 7FR, United Kingdom;51.51159;-0.22487;48;true;true;Japanese;The former BBC TV Centre may be an unlikely setting for a restaurant, but it's a match made in sushi heaven for this flagship venture from Yokohama-born Endo Kazutoshi. The experienced, well-travelled chef is a real showman, explaining each finely crafted, subtly flavoured element of the omakase menu in an engaging, charming way. Ingredients are either imported from Japan, such as rice from Yamagata, or are the best that Europe has to offer, like monkfish from Brixham and tuna from Spain.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Notable sake list;[]
3583;Olive Tree;United Kingdom;Bath;4-7 Russel Street, Bath, BA1 2QF, United Kingdom;51.3872068;-2.3630903;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The Queensberry Hotel comprises a series of Georgian townhouses and, while the owners are clearly proud of its architectural heritage, this discreetly combines with 21C comfort. Start with a drink in the delightfully British ‘Old Q Bar’, then head down to the surprisingly airy, modern restaurant where chef Chris Cleghorn brings an innovative, personalised approach to his cooking. Colours, textures and flavours are used to full effect in refined, creative combinations which have plenty of depth and, while they may appear simple, that’s all part of their skilful make-up.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3584;Dining Room at The Goring;United Kingdom;London;15 Beeston Place, Belgravia, London, SW1W 0JW, United Kingdom;51.497523;-0.1456983;76;false;true;Traditional British;The Goring is a model of British style and understatement and its ground floor dining room the epitome of grace and decorum. It appeals to those who ‘like things done properly’ and is one of the few places in London for which everyone appears to dress up. The hotel has long enjoyed a reputation for serving classic British dishes like eggs Drumkilbo, but the kitchen makes judicious use of modern techniques and superb ingredients to produce dishes that display an impressive understanding of balance, flavour and texture.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3585;hide and fox;United Kingdom;Saltwood;The Green, Saltwood, CT21 4PS, United Kingdom;51.0805389;1.0762788;85;true;false;Modern British;Start your night with a cocktail at this delightful neighbourhood restaurant that was once the village shop. There is no small amount of skill on display from the chefs, with dishes that are exquisitely crafted and deliver fabulous flavours and textures, be it an exceptional raviolo or glistening turbot. The very best ingredients from Kent’s larder are a feature, while the wine list looks further afield to up-and-coming regions such as Georgia, Croatia and Macedonia. Service comes from a charming team who work with pride and passion.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3586;City Social;United Kingdom;London;Tower 42, 25 Old Broad Street, City of London, London, EC2N 1HQ, United Kingdom;51.5151615;-0.0840542;80;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The buzz from the bar is the first thing you notice at Jason Atherton’s handsome restaurant on the 24th floor of Tower 42. Dark and moody, with a subtle art deco twist, it boasts impressive views of the City skyline. The menu of generous modern European dishes includes multiple cuts of Cumbrian beef cooked on the Josper grill, from rib-eye to sirloin. The wine list offers an appealing mixture of prices and styles, and there are noteworthy cocktails too.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3587;Interlude;United Kingdom;Lower Beeding;Leonardslee Gardens, Brighton Road, Lower Beeding, RH13 6PP, United Kingdom;51.0201898;-0.2606582;78;true;false;Creative;The 240-acre, Grade I listed Leonardslee Lakes and Gardens were first planted in 1801 and are famous today for their azaleas, rhododendrons and even a wallaby colony. Within the grounds sits an Italianate mansion housing elegant bedrooms and this intimate restaurant. The surprise tasting menu keeps its focus firmly on the local area, with fabulous produce from deer to wild garlic coming from within the estate. The skilfully crafted dishes show good balance in their textures and flavours, and take on a creative, original style. The menu is presented in a shorter form at lunchtime.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3588;Chez Bruce;United Kingdom;London;2 Bellevue Road, Wandsworth, London, SW17 7EG, United Kingdom;51.4464026;-0.1653296;80;true;true;French;Restaurants offering a standard of cooking this high for over 20 years are few and far between, and the numerous regulars of this smart, friendly neighbourhood spot are a testament to its perennial popularity. The reasonably priced menu features traditional, carefully prepared dishes that showcase quality seasonal produce. The wine list is skilfully chosen and features some well-priced rare wines, with an interesting selection by the glass, while a corkage option allows guests to bring a bottle from their own cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3589;Roots;United Kingdom;York;68 Marygate, York, YO30 7BH, United Kingdom;53.9618067;-1.0904831;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in a quiet area of the city, this attractive Arts and Crafts building is little sister to the Black Swan in Oldstead and shares its ethos of seasonality and sustainability. Tasting menus evolve naturally according to the availability of produce – which originates from their kitchen garden, small regional suppliers and chef-owner Tommy Banks’ parents’ farm. Creative, modern dishes are carefully prepared and deceptively simple to look at, yet offer great refinement and depth of flavour. There’s plenty of choice on the well-chosen wine list, with everything available by the glass.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3591;Harwood Arms;United Kingdom;London;Walham Grove, Fulham, London, SW6 1QP, United Kingdom;51.4828975;-0.1964558;21;false;false;Modern British;The Harwood Arms is a pub at heart, so bar snacks are a must: munch on homemade crisps or a venison Scotch egg while you peruse the menu with a pint. The cooking at this pub may be highly accomplished, but it still does what pub food does best: leaves you feeling eminently satisfied. The menu is British to the core and the owners supply much of the expertly cooked deer and game. Well-balanced dishes burst with flavour and allow each main ingredient to shine by keeping things simple.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3592;Pavyllon London;United Kingdom;London;Four Seasons Hotel, Hamilton Place, Mayfair, London, W1J 7DR, United Kingdom;51.5045981;-0.150181;23;false;true;French Contemporary;Yannick Alléno's place among the pantheon of great French chefs is assured, and the Four Seasons in Mayfair was the chosen venue for his first foray into the UK’s dining scene. It’s a smart, spacious dining room, with lots of natural light and a focus on comfort – the large open kitchen, which is led by Chef Benjamin Ferra Y Castell, is skirted by a luxurious counter for those wanting a close-up view. The food is underscored by classic French recipes, but influences can range from Italy to North Africa to Japan. Ingredients are naturally from the luxury side of the ledger and set menus are the best way to go.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3593;Sushi Kanesaka;United Kingdom;London;45 Park Lane, Mayfair, London, W1K 1PN, United Kingdom;51.5064815;-0.1517726;79;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Authenticity abounds here at Chef Shinji Kanesaka’s London outpost. You’re greeted in the lobby of the 45 Park Lane hotel and escorted up to the hidden room on the first floor. The counter seats is made from a single piece of hinoki cypress wood, while the room is traditionally decorated with bamboo, ceramics and kumiko panels. The omakase menu is made up of around 18 pieces, with the stunning nigiri interspersed with dishes such as steamed abalone or grilled Kobe beef. Much of the seafood is from European waters, while the rice is from Yamagata.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3594;Chishuru;United Kingdom;London;3 Great Titchfield Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1W 8AX, United Kingdom;51.5167307;-0.1399754;43;true;false;African;Having attracted a fanbase with her various pop-ups and presence in Brixton Market, Adejoké Bakare’s West African restaurant found a permanent home in this warm, bright spot which comes with a real neighbourhood feel. Delicious, satisfying and full-flavoured dishes showcase cleverly judged spicing, with sauces proving a particular highlight – whether thick scotch bonnet with ekuru, or caramelised onion and lemon with guinea fowl yassa. It's all accompanied by friendly service and a fun atmosphere.;Air conditioning;[]
3595;Akoko;United Kingdom;London;21 Berners Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T3LP, United Kingdom;51.5177438;-0.13691;77;false;false;African, Creative;“We aim to prove that West African cuisine deserves its place in fine dining by highlighting its unique flavours and culinary traditions on its own terms,” says founder Aji Akokomi. With the help of some talented chefs, he is achieving that goal and then some. The tasting menu format allows the kitchen team to take diners on a culinary journey, with refined, beautifully balanced dishes underpinned by quality ingredients – many of them cooked over fire. It’s hard to pick a stand-out from the precise, technically impressive selection, but the jollof rice is truly knock-out. Ask for a spot at the kitchen counter for a ringside seat.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3596;Muse by Tom Aikens;United Kingdom;London;38 Groom Place, Belgravia, London, SW1X 7BA, United Kingdom;51.4994673;-0.1509184;39;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;With seating for just 23 customers, there’s an intimate, almost communal feel to events at this restaurant inside a delightful Georgian townhouse in a charming Belgravia mews – which partly explains the name. ‘Muse’ can also refer to the inspiration behind the cooking, which includes chef-owner Tom Aikens’ parents, his childhood and key moments from his professional career. Each well-judged and sophisticated dish relates to something memorable from Tom's past, whether that was climbing a tree or enjoying the last barbecue of summer.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3598;Angler;United Kingdom;London;3 South Place, Finsbury, London, EC2M 2AF, United Kingdom;51.5189674;-0.086521;78;false;true;Seafood;Top-drawer fish, treated with the culinary skill it deserves, is the main attraction at this restaurant on the top floor of the South Place Hotel. The chefs have the confidence to know that when seafood is this good, it needs little in the way of adornment, and the pared-back cooking allows exceptional produce like roast Newlyn cod to shine through. Dishes are attractively presented and so is the room, with an ornate ceiling and inviting roof terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3603;Aulis;United Kingdom;London;16 St Anne's Court, Soho, London, W1F 0BF, United Kingdom;51.5143368;-0.1343223;96;true;true;Creative British;Simon Rogan is certainly not one for standing still and here, in a narrow alley in Soho, his Aulis restaurant is almost unrecognisable from before. After expanding into next door, there's now room for pre-dinner drinks, while the Italian slate counter – which seats 12 – is a thing of beauty. The impressive chef's table experience is made up of around 14 exquisite, creative dishes and the personable chefs explain in detail the make up of each one. The menu is informed by the seasonal produce of Simon's organic 'Our Farm' in the Lake District.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3605;sō–lō;United Kingdom;Aughton;17 Town Green Lane, Aughton, L39 6SE, United Kingdom;53.5445999;-2.9003591;35;false;true;Modern British;Having worked at various well-regarded restaurants around the country, Tim Allen brought plenty of experience to his first solo venture in this brightly decorated and warmly run converted pub. His contemporary, seasonally pertinent dishes draw their considerable flavour from top-notch ingredients – some are local and others are imported from France, such as the exceptional Landes guinea fowl. The textures of each dish are carefully considered too, with elements like aerated dashi and quaver-like crispy potatoes adding interest. The lunch menu represents good value.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3606;The Muddlers Club;United Kingdom;Belfast;1 Warehouse Lane, Belfast, BT1 2DX, United Kingdom;54.6015177;-5.9273665;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Hidden away in the Cathedral Quarter is this urban, industrial-style restaurant named after a 200-year-old secret society. It’s a simply furnished place, run with palpable enthusiasm by a young team. Chef Gareth McCaughey’s philosophy is to source top ingredients, prepare them well and not overcomplicate things, as proven by the surprise tasting menu spotlighting superb Irish produce like Kilkeel scallops and Wicklow venison. The wine list offers an interesting selection of low-intervention, natural, organic and bio-dynamic wines, all available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3607;OX;United Kingdom;Belfast;1 Oxford Street, Belfast, BT1 3LA, United Kingdom;54.599262;-5.9220051;57;false;true;Modern British;From the terrific buzz in the air to each element of the carefully constructed tasting menu, dining at this understated restaurant is such a pleasant experience. The starting point for the cooking is always the ingredients, with only the very best selected – and in some cases grown – by the kitchen team. This top-notch produce is elevated by the refined, expertly balanced accompaniments – an approach which is clear in dishes like superb Orkney scallop paired with a curry oil that is beautifully judged in both aroma and flavour.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3608;Aniar;Ireland;Galway;53 Lower Dominick Street, Galway, H91 V4DP, Ireland;53.2712451;-9.0569977;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Irish;'Aniar' means 'from the west' and indeed the local area is a key inspiration for both the 'back-to-nature' cooking and the chic, moody décor here. The micro-seasonal menus are finalised based on the day's locally sourced produce, which is showcased in pure, delicate and well-balanced dishes such as exceptional raw beef dressed with top-notch nasturtium oil. The cooking cleverly blends traditional and modern techniques, while contrasts in texture, temperature and acidity are also a feature. Many courses are served by the chefs themselves, some with accompanying poems.;Air conditioning;[]
3609;Heron;United Kingdom;Leith;87-91a Henderson Street, Leith, EH6 6ED, United Kingdom;55.974846;-3.1718853;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;There is such a pleasant feel to this neighbourhood restaurant, courtesy of a bright, clean look that’s matched by warm and unstuffy service. The skilful cooking is founded on fine Scottish produce, whether that be excellent wild sea bass or the finest berries from Fife. The tasting menu will allow you to make the most of the chefs’ talents, and all fits together like a well-crafted jigsaw. Ask for a table by the window if you want to watch the world go by around the Port of Leith, or opt for a seat at the spacious counter.;Counter dining;[]
3611;Hjem;United Kingdom;Wall;Front Street, Wall, NE46 4EE, United Kingdom;55.0142385;-2.1329127;77;true;false;Scandinavian;'Hjem' means 'home' in both Scandinavian and Northumbrian dialects, uniting the birthplaces of owners Alex and Ally. The restaurant is located inside The Hadrian Hotel, with all guests arriving for an aperitif in a part of the building that feels more like the village local, before moving to the contrastingly pared-back dining room. In a nod to Chef Alex's Swedish heritage, the meal finishes with his version of 'fika' – as the table becomes covered in an assortment of sweet treats and snacks, it makes for a generous and fittingly memorable end to a superlative experience.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3612;Bastible;Ireland;Dublin City;111 South Circular Road, Dublin City, D08 RW2K, Ireland;53.3321453;-6.2749102;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This vibrant little restaurant with a lively spirit boasts an open kitchen, from which you’ll find the chefs engaging with guests and delivering some of the dishes themselves. The modern set menu features top class Irish produce at the height of season and each main ingredient is given the space to shine. Dishes are stripped-back, flavours are bold and servings are generous: this is cooking that comes from the heart. Start with an aperitif while you enjoy the delicate snacks.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3613;The Peat Inn;United Kingdom;Peat Inn;Peat Inn, KY15 5LH, United Kingdom;56.2783766;-2.8845087;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Geoffrey and Katherine Smeddle have run this restaurant since 2006, but the history of this whitewashed inn extends back to the 18C. Geoffrey is an experienced and knowledgeable chef who has built up a close web of suppliers which, in conjunction with the seasons, virtually writes the menu. Expect to find ingredients like East Neuk crab, Black Isle lamb and Easter Grangemuir Farm strawberries. All of these are put to great use in vibrant, flavoursome dishes. Stylish, split-level bedrooms are available too, with breakfast served in your room.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
3614;River Café;United Kingdom;London;Thames Wharf, Rainville Road, Hammersmith, London, W6 9HA, United Kingdom;51.4841179;-0.2243521;48;true;false;Italian;It should go without saying, but be sure to ask for a seat on the terrace at this icon of London's Italian restaurant scene. The on-view kitchen with its wood-fired oven dominates the stylish and buzzing riverside room and the menu bursts with authentic Italian flavours which make one’s mouth water in anticipation. The honest, hearty dishes have a rustic Italian simplicity, relying as they do on the quality of their ingredients, whether that be clams, crab or wild sea bass. Arguably the best Italian wine list in London is the icing on the cake.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3615;Wild Honey St James;United Kingdom;London;8 Pall Mall, St James’s, London, SW1Y 5NG, United Kingdom;51.5074316;-0.1321583;83;true;true;Modern British;This brasserie de-luxe occupies a Grade II listed former banking hall within the Sofitel hotel and while that means a certain grandeur, the atmosphere is never overly formal. Anthony Demetre’s cooking proves the perfect fit because it is equally impressive but defined by a refreshing lack of showmanship. His appealing dishes are as generous in size as they are rewarding in flavour, from duck and pork terrine en croute to rabbit with slow-cooked cottage pie. The delicious custard tart is a true speciality and if it was ever removed from the menu there would be protests on Pall Mall.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3618;Trinity;United Kingdom;London;4 The Polygon, Clapham, London, SW4 0JG, United Kingdom;51.4635167;-0.14151;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A rightly popular neighbourhood restaurant, this is a place you can’t help but fall in love with. Located close to Clapham Common, it’s an intimate operation where the open kitchen lets you in on the action. Kick off with a G&T made using their house distilled gin, before enjoying fine British produce like Herdwick lamb T-bone. The chefs pull off a fine blend of the classic and the modern, with understated dishes that pack in plenty of flavour and look great too. The smooth service team bring welcome personality to proceedings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3620;Kitchen W8;United Kingdom;London;11-13 Abingdon Road, Kensington, London, W8 6AH, United Kingdom;51.4990858;-0.1969096;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Relaxed and free from pomposity, there is a lovely neighbourhood feel to this restaurant that provides both great cooking and a warm welcome. The versatility of the place knows no bounds, as it’s as well suited to a romantic dinner as it is to a quick lunch while out shopping or when celebrating with friends. The well-executed, reliably enjoyable dishes are based on classical combinations and deliver satisfying flavours. A good value set menu is available alongside the à la carte.;Air conditioning;[]
3621;Pied à Terre;United Kingdom;London;34 Charlotte Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 2NH, United Kingdom;51.5191109;-0.1352265;25;true;true;Creative;Over the last quarter of a century, few parts of London have seen more restaurants come and go than Charlotte Street, but one constant over that period has been David Moore’s Pied à Terre. Reinventions have kept things fresh over time, be they subtle touches like a new colour scheme or more major changes like the embracing of plant-based cooking with a serious vegan offering. Dishes are based on classical French techniques yet are as satisfying today as they've ever been, bringing together top-notch ingredients in harmonious combinations.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3622;Behind;United Kingdom;London;20 Sidworth Street, London Fields, London, E8 3SD, United Kingdom;51.5392307;-0.0575568;86;false;false;Modern British;A beautiful horseshoe-shaped counter allows guests to see ‘behind’ the scenes at this neighbourhood restaurant with an ersatz-industrial look. Every seat has a view of the talented chefs, who also serve dishes themselves and describe their make-up with palpable pride. The surprise seasonal menu has a seafood focus, but meat dishes, like guinea fowl with pumpkin, are prepared with equal aplomb. The 10 or so courses are all delicate, balanced and skilful little creations that provide great depth of flavour and make for a memorable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3623;D'Olier Street;Ireland;Dublin City;D'Olier Chambers, D'Olier Street, Dublin City, D02 H589, Ireland;53.3460015;-6.2571444;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The high ceilings and original plasterwork of this restored landmark building contribute to the appeal of the contemporary restaurant within. The well-travelled, Australian-born chef prepares a surprise menu and, while there are multiple global techniques and influences at play, the focus of the dishes remains firmly on the top-notch main ingredients. There are seats at the counter for those wanting to see how the beautifully composed dishes are created, and the wine pairings are a great way to go.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3625;The Bishop's Buttery;Ireland;Cashel;Cashel Palace Hotel, Main Street, Cashel, E25 EF61, Ireland;52.5172314;-7.8891443;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A vaulted ceiling and flagstone floors combine with sumptuous, colourful furnishings at this striking restaurant that provides a fair amount of both character and luxury. It helps, of course, that it’s located in the cellars of Cashel Palace, a magnificent Palladian manor house which was once home to the Archbishops of Cashel. Desserts are a highlight among cooking that keeps a focus on each central ingredient, which is then skilfully enhanced with complementary flavours. Service comes from an impeccable team, who work with the utmost pride.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3627;1890 by Gordon Ramsay;United Kingdom;London;Strand, London, WC2R 0EU, United Kingdom;51.5102984;-0.120722;64;false;false;French Contemporary;Named in honour of renowned French chef Georges Auguste Escoffier, who joined the hotel in 1890, this intimate room inside The Savoy features rich, golden hues, art deco touches and just 10 well-spaced tables. The surprise tasting menu is inspired by Escoffier’s classics and delivered with elegance and poise, but with dishes prepared using modern techniques. A shorter, 4 course version of the menu is available Friday and Saturday lunchtimes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
3628;Pine;United Kingdom;East Wallhouses;Vallum Farm, Military Road, East Wallhouses, NE18 0LL, United Kingdom;55.0095322;-1.9266976;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The open kitchen takes centre stage at Cal and Siân Byerley's rustic restaurant, where they're all about showcasing Northumbrian ingredients. Cal knows the local area intimately and, as well as plucking fresh ingredients from their kitchen garden, leads his team on foraging missions and seeks out small independent producers. He and the chefs use this produce skilfully, in dishes which are full of colour and really pack a punch. The wine flight – including several English wines – is worth going for, and they also make their own juices, tonics and teas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3630;Condita;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;15 Salisbury Place, Edinburgh, EH9 1SL, United Kingdom;55.9371131;-3.1787608;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Just outside the city centre you'll find this smart, understated shop conversion with seasonally changing décor and just six large tables. The cooking takes the form of a surprise menu, with a hand-drawn bookmark picturing some of the ingredients the only hint at what is to come. An interesting and individual streak runs through the cooking, with flavour combinations carefully thought through to enhance one another. The skill of the kitchen is most evident in dishes that extract wonderful flavours from seemingly basic ingredients, like kohlrabi with goat's curd.;Air conditioning;[]
3631;Bastion;Ireland;Kinsale;Main Street, Kinsale, P17 NX44, Ireland;51.7057019;-8.524059;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in the very centre of town, Bastion is a contemporary restaurant owned and run by a talented couple: Paul McDonald cooks, while his wife Helen looks after the service. A large bar splits the room in two and twinkling candles add a welcoming touch. Paul is Scottish born but his cooking has a strong Irish base. Natural flavours are kept to the fore and local seafood is a highlight. The skilfully prepared, exacting dishes take on a modern style and often exhibit a playful, innovative element, while at the same time showing depth in their flavours and textures;;[]
3632;The Kitchin;United Kingdom;Leith;78 Commercial Quay, Leith, EH6 6LX, United Kingdom;55.9770648;-3.1725849;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in the historic Port of Leith, this restaurant has been at the forefront of the Edinburgh dining scene for years. It’s no wonder it’s such a success, given the quality found in the balanced, flavoursome dishes that champion seasonal Scottish produce – come in grouse season and you won’t be disappointed. An array of menus includes a well-priced lunch option and the Prestige surprise menu, which offers the most complete experience. Try to get a table by the kitchen, which lets you in on the action via a large viewing window.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3636;Homestead Cottage;Ireland;Doolin;Luogh North, Doolin, V95 KH30, Ireland;52.990241;-9.4046028;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A charming 200-year-old cottage houses this rural restaurant that counts the Atlantic Ocean as its neighbour. The lovely terrace allows you to enjoy a spectacular sunset over drinks, before moving inside to the characterful interior with stone floors, cookery books and rustic wooden tables. Wonderful Irish produce – such as superbly fresh, beautifully roasted Aran monkfish – is used in equally impressive dishes that are clean and modern, with no unnecessary frills.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
3637;mana;United Kingdom;Manchester;42 Blossom Street, Ancoats, Manchester, M4 6BF, United Kingdom;53.4848226;-2.2278659;67;false;false;Creative British, Modern Cuisine;The personality and experience of chef-owner Simon Martin shine brightly at this stylish, modern restaurant, where every one of the well-spaced tables has a view of the kitchen. British produce leads the way, including plenty of seafood because, as Simon puts it, “we live on an island”. There are many Asian techniques on display and the cooking marries complex flavours with a pure, natural approach, in dishes such as a superb roasted hogget with white miso sabayon.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3640;nôl;Japan;Tokyo;1F, DDD HOTEL, 2-2-1 Nihombashibakurocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0002, Japan;35.695272;139.78362;51;true;true;Contemporary;‘Harmony’ and ‘circulation’ are the keywords of this dining experience. Through his partnerships with farmers, the chef returns compost to revitalise the soil. The prix fixe presentation starts with a bowl of soup. Vegetable ends are used in the soup’s creation, expressing a wish for a society that doesn’t waste food. Prepared with French techniques, the fare is simple and light. The grey of the interior creates something of a laboratory feel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3641;Trescha;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Murillo 725, Buenos Aires, C1414AFE, Argentina;-34.600216;-58.4439581;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After an extensive period working aboard, which saw him train at Le Cordon Bleu in London and then in other culinary pantheons such as Azurmendi (Spain), Frantzén (Sweden) and the erstwhile 108 (Denmark), young chef Tomás Treschanski has returned to his homeland with a limitless contemporary repertoire built around diversity. Occupying a remodelled house in the Villa Crespo district, this exclusive restaurant features a bar with an impressive collection of whiskies, an attractive glass-fronted terrace, and a contemporary-style dining room with just a single but elegant cedarwood counter for 10 guests who are able to interact with the chefs. The cuisine is based around a single small-plate 15-course tasting menu (constantly changing throughout the year) created with premium seasonal ingredients and different cooking techniques (emulsions, foams, jellies, braising etc) on the same plate. The Test Kitchen on the first floor is Trescha’s dedicated R+D space.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3642;Azafrán;Argentina;Mendoza;Sarmiento 765, Mendoza, M5500, Argentina;-32.8887775;-68.8491233;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At Azafrán (“Saffron” in English), discover the true essence of Mendoza’s cuisine just a couple of blocks from the Plaza Independencia in the centre of the city. Having gained experienced in numerous restaurants and wineries, chef Sebastián Weigandt has found a true state of contentment here. In his view, the secret to his cuisine lies in the quality of his ingredients – and in this respect Mendoza is a gastronomic paradise. Fully committed to the region, he works with local suppliers and is part of a historical project called DOP that studies foodstuffs that existed in the area’s early settlements. In his contemporary-style eatery, he offers three tasting menus with a touch of modern creativity. On two of these you can select dishes that showcase traditional recipes, such as Weigandt’s version of Mendoza-style Tomaticán stew, and black rice with trout and apple, both with a strong focus on vegetables as well as presentation, with the chef serving some his dishes personally. As you would expect, the restaurant also offers a superb array of wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3643;Don Julio;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Guatemala 4699, Buenos Aires, C1425BUK, Argentina;-34.5862674;-58.4244386;96;false;true;Grills;There are very few people who haven’t heard of the Don Julio restaurant and Pablo Rivero, the owner-chef at one of the world’s best “parrillas”. Walking through the door of this restaurant, where it is always difficult to book a table, is akin to immersing yourself in the culinary culture of Argentina, and enables you to understand its passion for meat, which is seen here as a family legacy (Pablo’s grandmother was a butcher and his parents cattle breeders). They have attained this level of excellence thanks to the exclusive mixed ageing process used, their assiduous selection of meat (Hereford and Angus breeds), and their concept of sustainability and regenerative breeding. The philosophy here is that of a classic steakhouse, although this idea has evolved to include added gastronomic undertones. The meat display counter is a truly spectacular sight, enhanced by the “V-shaped” grill to ensure that no fat drips on to the embers to alter the flavour from smoke from the white quebracho charcoal. The wine cellar, which is focused around Argentinian wines, includes some real jewels!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3644;Casa Vigil;Argentina;Mendoza;Videla Aranda 7008, Mendoza, M5519, Argentina;-33.0446245;-68.7213938;21;true;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;This is the “casa” of famous wine expert Alejandro Vigil, known more widely as “the Messi of Wine”, having been the first to be awarded 100 points by Robert Parker for his Argentinian wines, namely the iconic 2013 Gran Enemigo Single Vineyard Gualtallary and the 2016 Adriana Vineyard River Stone. The restaurant’s setting in Chachingo comes as a something of a surprise, and is inspired by Dante’s Divine Comedy (the story of a journey from hell to paradise, as well as that of the struggle with the inner self, hence his El Enemigo (The Enemy) wine brand). Following a guided tour of the vineyards that surround the building, head to the contemporary yet rustically appointed dining rooms, where the focus is on contemporary menus (one “executive” menu at lunchtime and two more extensive options in the evening) that showcase seasonal ingredients from the Mendoza region. The latter are sourced from its own garden and small-scale local producers, and are present in dishes such as mushrooms with spring onions, pork gnocchi with peas, and goat meat cooked at low temperature with sweet potato. Make sure you try the tomatoes grown by his mother, María Sance, with over 50 varieties that have been revived thanks to the Labrar programme.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3645;Brindillas;Argentina;Mendoza;Guardia Vieja 2898, Mendoza, M5509, Argentina;-33.0057601;-68.9106305;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated in an uninteresting and not particularly attractive area to the south of Mendoza (Vistalba, in the department of Luján de Cuyo), Brindillas is one of those intimate settings with excellent service that will win over food-lovers. Through dishes such as roasted aubergines with a Romesco sauce and salted anchovies, succulent grilled veal with ground pepper, sweet potato and chard, and caramelised peach with amaretto, a light mascarpone foam and home-made almond ice-cream, chef Mariano Gallego, who has worked with famous Spanish chef Carme Ruscalleda and was at the helm in one of her restaurants (Sant Pau, in Tokio), showcases his imagination and modern approach, which ensures that local ingredients are always to the fore. Choose between two tasting menus (short and long options) that will definitely leave a lasting impression thanks to their high levels of technique, delicacy and pleasant textures.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3646;Zonda Cocina de Paisaje;Argentina;Mendoza;San Martín 1745 Bodega Lagarde, Mendoza, M5507, Argentina;-33.023072;-68.8727331;24;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;Transplanting raw ingredients from the field to the plate takes on added value when they are grown on your farm, bringing added personality to dishes and enhancing the culinary narrative when it comes to building recipes. The Lagarde winery in Luján de Cuyo is famous for the excellent quality of its wines (DOC Malbec) and for the fact that it has its own organic fruit and vegetable gardens (tomatoes, lettuce, sweet peppers, chard, pomegranates, aromatic herbs etc), in addition to olives and other crops that it supplies to the restaurant. At Zonda Cocina de Paisaje, the goal is to pay homage to cuisine with a local DNA that is simple, honest in concept but then elevated to haute cuisine standard via delicate textures and fine presentation. In its elegant, rustically inspired dining room, with a terrace overlooking the vineyards, choose between four tasting menus: Experiencia Paisaje, Experiencia Zonda, Cuyano and Gilanco – some of which also include visits to the vegetable gardens and kitchen.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3647;Restaurant 20 Victoria;Canada;Toronto;20 Victoria St., Unit 100, Toronto, M5C 2A1, Canada;43.6498653;-79.3769956;58;true;true;Contemporary, Seafood;On a quiet stretch of downtown Toronto, Chef Julie Hyde is making her talents known in this tiny-but-mighty restaurant that captured the city’s heart the day it opened. Top-notch local produce, pristine seafood and refined sauce work make for a delicious trifecta on a seasonal tasting menu that boasts originality in spades. Recent highlights included smoked beets with oyster cream as well as grilled fish with beurre blanc and eel crumble. The dimly lit dining room is elegantly easy-going, as Hyde and her small team work with laser-like focus from a kitchen that’s simultaneously always in use and always pristine. Service mirrors the kitchen’s unpretentious approach, offering a warm, often jovial sense of hospitality that doesn’t miss a beat.;Air conditioning;[]
3648;Mora;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;40 Upper Lascar Row, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.2850528;114.1494147;28;true;false;Innovative;Mora is located on Cat Street, famous for its antique and junk market. The soothing interior adopts a cream colour scheme with subtle curvy lines. Soybeans are at the core of the menu, taking the forms of bean sauce, tofu skin, soymilk, and fermented beans, whose textures complement other ingredients in each dish well. European techniques are seamlessly melded with local flavours for a varied and interesting experience. Don’t miss their Mapo tofu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3649;Field;Czechia;Prague;U Milosrdných 12, Prague, 110 00, Czech Republic;50.0918645;14.4220871;72;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Two friends run this stylishly understated restaurant done out in a chic, minimalist vein. The Czech dishes present a fusion of classic and modern elements, and some are finished tableside by the dedicated team. They serve a tasting menu (a vegetarian version of which is available) comprising either six or 10 courses. There is also a shorter set menu at lunchtime (one variation on weekdays, another at the weekend). Seasonality is key here, with preserves playing an important role all year round. As well as wine pairings, they have an interesting selection of alcohol-free drinks.;Air conditioning,Booking essential,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3650;La Degustation Bohême Bourgeoise;Czechia;Prague;Haštalská 18, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.0910775;14.4250418;47;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This iconic restaurant is housed in an attractive historical building in the heart of Prague. The interior is stylish – not least on account of striking details such as the sleek glass-fronted wine cabinet, large original chandeliers between vaulted arches, and open kitchen. There is a pleasantly buzzy and laid-back atmosphere. They offer a five-course set menu made up of well-judged and harmoniously seasoned Czech dishes that echo the seasons and successfully bring out the flavours of the ingredients. Wine pairings or an alcohol-free beverage accompaniment are available.;Air conditioning,Booking essential,Interesting wine list;[]
3653;Wörgötter - Wirtshaus;Austria;Ligist;Marktplatz 40, Ligist, 8563, Austria;46.993731;15.2068683;15;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Located right in the town centre, this spruce inn has an eventful history that stretches back to 1800. The success of this inviting family-run restaurant now lies in the hands of Florian Wörgötter, who represents the third generation. Working alongside his father, Mathias, he uses seasonal produce to rustle up Austrian classics with a judicious modern twist. Dishes such as trout fillet with tender wheat, chicory and fennel, or Mariazell venison ragout with sour cream spaetzle, mushrooms and red cabbage are simply delicious. The "Business Lunch" is a moderately priced set menu served Wed-Fri. Renate (the mother) and her partner Julia are in charge of the service. Be sure to make a reservation – this place is always packed! Tip: There is also a fine dining restaurant that serves an ambitious and creative modern surprise menu three days a week.;Terrace;[]
3654;Freigeist;Austria;Lustenau;Raiffeisenstraße 4, Lustenau, 6890, Austria;47.4252658;9.6580146;36;false;true;Farm to table;This place may have a resolutely relaxed atmosphere, but in no way does that detract from the high degree of professionalism in both the service, courtesy of friendly owner Bernd Mossmann, and Paul Hunger's cuisine. The chef turns out fuss-free dishes made using top-notch, mostly organic regional produce – the full-bodied beef broth with root vegetables is a delicious way to kick off your meal. The interesting decor featuring unique decorative elements makes for a charming vintage feel. When the weather is nice, head for the inviting terrace. A somewhat simpler, pared-back menu is served at lunchtime.;Terrace;[]
3655;Schlosskeller Wirtshaus;Austria;Leibnitz;Seggaubergstraße 5, Leibnitz, 8430, Austria;46.778253;15.5243311;28;false;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This cosy restaurant decorated with gorgeous wood panelling is another culinary option within the Schlosskeller world of gastronomy. As an alternative to Gourmetstube, Wirtshaus serves up flavoursome dishes that tap into the regional repertoire and are in step with the seasons. Austrian classics such as Backhenderl (Viennese fried chicken) also feature on the menu. Save room for the apricot dumplings for dessert! The sharing menu for two, comprising eight small courses is also a good idea (Thu-Sat). Pizza is served on Wednesdays. The cordial and highly proficient service extends to competent wine recommendations. The fantastic view of the picture-perfect landscape of vineyards and forests draws guests to the terrace in summer.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
3657;Göttfried;Austria;Linz;Hofgasse 5, Linz, 4020, Austria;48.3058629;14.2854304;17;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Run by husband-and-wife team Simone and Christian Göttfried, this inviting restaurant boasts a charming location in the old town – the main square is just around the corner and the Danube is also very close by. The interior beautifully combines modern style with historical features such as a vaulted ceiling and wood panelling. Front of house, the owner and her team provide attentive service. Meanwhile, chef-patron Christian Göttfried focuses on cooking excellent food – expect regional, seasonal cuisine with a Mediterranean twist. Both the organic veal Wiener schnitzel and the branzino with a parsley vinaigrette are highly recommended. The wine list boasts some 350 labels, principally of Austrian provenance. There is also a small wine shop and tables are laid out in the lovely quiet courtyard. The hotel offers contemporary, cosy guestrooms.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3658;Ziegelwerk Gasthaus;Austria;Wimpassing an der Leitha;Ziegelofengasse 28, Wimpassing an der Leitha, 2485, Austria;47.9148374;16.4304259;18;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This haven of culinary delights is housed in a former brickworks. The design of the interior purposefully drew on and preserved long-standing structures such as brick and quarry stone masonry, combining them with sleek, modern elements. A restored old oven makes for an eye-catching feature. Large windows allow the light to flood in while affording diners views of their surroundings. In summer, you can sit in the glorious beer garden. Owner Werner Tschiedel channels the spirit of a modern inn, serving flavourful, straightforward and strictly regional cuisine, such as greaves dumplings, warm cabbage salad, caraway juice or venison schnitzel in a pumpkin seed crumb, potato salad with mayonnaise, cranberries. To be washed down with a wine from a predominantly Austrian selection, many of which are organic or biodynamic.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3659;'s Paul Restaurant;Austria;Traunkirchen;Mitterndorf 23, Traunkirchen, 4801, Austria;47.8544089;13.7762083;72;true;true;Farm to table;This modern restaurant run by Paul Wieder has a pleasingly effortless and laid-back vibe that does not detract from the stylish ambience. The à la carte selection proposed at both lunch- and dinnertime features very classic fare, such as "braised knuckle of organic lamb, herb polenta, pickled carrots, Mumbai curry". Opt for the fine dining set menu (evenings only) for refined and more modern dishes – for instance, Mühlbach salmon trout, wasabi, organic egg yolk, quince. What they all have in common is their full-bodied flavours. Attentive service.;Terrace;[]
3660;Pollak's Retzbacherhof;Austria;Retzbach;Bahnstraße 1, Retzbach, 2074, Austria;48.7649396;16.0024223;57;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Austrian;The committed hosts put their heart and soul into running this place. Sonja and Harald Pollak have been at the helm of Rezbacherhof for over 15 years. They cook up traditional Weinviertel dishes, such as venison lights, root vegetables, Serviettenknödel (bread dumplings) or Freiland-Wildhendl – breaded fried chicken, breast and deboned leg, potato and green salad. A classic Austrian Sunday roast is also still served here. At lunchtime the appealing dish of the day changes regularly. There is a good wine selection, including by the glass. The team led by Sonja Pollak provide warm and attentive service. In short, a welcoming establishment where you can mingle with the locals.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3661;Mohrenwirt;Austria;Graz;Mariahilferstraße 16, Graz, 8020, Austria;47.0721753;15.4336253;55;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant has the feel of a favourite neighbourhood hangout. Steeped in tradition, it is located in the heart of Graz's old town, between Kunsthaus Graz and the church, Mariahilfkirche. From the terrace, you have a front-row view of the city. This pleasantly modern, rustic-style establishment is run by Romana Maria Pieber and Lukas Lepsic, who are committed to sustainable practices and using organic produce. The menu features regional and traditional Austrian fare with modern and seasonal influences, eg organic Backhendl (breaded fried chicken) in a basket, or organic lamb sugo with aubergine, polenta, sheep's-milk yoghurt and lemon pickle. On Saturdays, there is also boiled organic beef served in a traditional copper pot. Book early to avoid disappointment! Small set menu available 2-5pm.;Terrace;[]
3663;Die Schmiede;Austria;Pfaffing;Pfaffing 7, Pfaffing, 4870, Austria;48.0179084;13.4822103;85;false;false;Austrian, Farm to table;Are you a fan of no-frills cuisine that stands out for its craftsmanship and flavour as well as the quality of its regional ingredients? In addition to classic Austrian fare such as Backhendl (breaded fried chicken), Wiener schnitzel etc, you can indulge in dishes such as fried lake trout with Mediterranean pearl barley and a Riesling foam, or roast lamb with Serviettenknödel (bread dumplings). Diners will appreciate the attentive, friendly service and cosy interior done out in a modern style and warm tones. The gorgeous wine cellar dates back to the 16C. Head for the terrace with a view of the Höllengebirge mountains.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3665;Malerwinkl;Austria;Fehring;Hatzendorf 152, Fehring, 8361, Austria;46.980077;16.0062398;55;false;true;Contemporary;Whether you prefer traditional Styrian cuisine or more sophisticated fare with a modern touch, this restaurant caters to your tastes. Almost exclusively regional ingredients are used in the set menu and à la carte dishes, eg char with kohlrabi, peas and vegetables and a truffle hollandaise sauce. The wine list with a focus on Austria is appealing, and the selection of wines by the glass is also good. You can opt for a table in the main dining area, in the bright winter garden or on the beautiful terrace. The restaurant is located in an "art hotel", which has 10 individual guestrooms and a holiday apartment. Take a look around the garden with its sculptures by Peter Troißinger Sr – chef, sculptor and painter.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3666;Chez Bernard;Austria;Vienna;Mariahilfer Straße 71A, Vienna, 1060, Austria;48.19842;16.35066;39;true;false;French Contemporary;Close to the Mariahilfer Straße shopping drag, on the seventh floor of the chic MOTTO boutique hotel, this restaurant has really distinctive architecture. The tasteful upscale interior will appeal to diners, as will the pleasantly lounge-like atmosphere. Be sure to check out the interesting bar too. The food is uncomplicated and unpretentious. Try the bouillabaisse – one of the classics! – and don't forgo the apricot dumplings. One floor up is the rooftop terrace, which boasts a magnificent view, and, although it only serves a smaller menu, is nonetheless the place to be!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3668;Reiterhof Stückler;Austria;Sankt Margarethen im Lavanttal;Reiterhofstraße 38, Sankt Margarethen im Lavanttal, 9412, Austria;46.8599728;14.8136496;76;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This modern and spacious restaurant enjoys a unique location inside an equestrian centre. Situated on the first floor, it has an appealing decor characterised by an abundance of wood, clean lines and warm tones, but it is the living ceiling that really catches the eye. The windows on all sides afford magnificent views of the surrounding villages, meadows and mountains as well as the on-site riding grounds. Head chef Ralph Kollnitzer and his team propose delicious regional dishes as well as their "Gourmetmenü" – a creative fine dining set menu of four to six courses (pre-order only).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
3669;Meierei im Stadtpark;Austria;Vienna;Am Heumarkt 2a, Vienna, 1030, Austria;48.2045237;16.3811943;62;false;true;Austrian;One floor below the Reitbauer’s gourmet restaurant, you’ll find another upmarket eatery. Alongside some 150 wonderfully matured cheeses, it boasts delicious classics like Wiener schnitzel of suckling calf. Or perhaps you’d prefer a whole Arctic char or some venison goulash? Attractive terrace facing the Stadtpark.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3670;Mochi;Austria;Vienna;Praterstraße 15, Vienna, 1020, Austria;48.2135968;16.3818079;44;false;true;Japanese;A lively, informal restaurant serving authentic Japanese cuisine with some more modern twists, at very moderate prices. You can watch the chefs at work, preparing sushi rolls, yakitori or gyu don. At lunchtime, the food is served in bowls, in the evening the presentation is a bit more elaborate. Tables are much sought after, so book early!;Terrace;[]
3673;Zum fröhlichen Arbeiter;Austria;Apetlon;Quergasse 98, Apetlon, 7143, Austria;47.7428123;16.8360127;41;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This spruce family-run inn has been welcoming diners for 100 years. Owner and head chef Hannes Tschida showcases his love for the Seewinkel region through dishes incorporating plenty of local ingredients. The wide-ranging à la carte options include Grammelknödel (potato dumplings stuffed with greaves), beef goulash, trout ceviche, dry-aged steak and Lake Neusiedl catfish. There is also a four- to six-course surprise menu. To complement the bold flavours of the cuisine, an impressive wine list dominated by Austrian labels is available. The restaurant itself has two indoor dining spaces: one oozing traditional charm, the other more modern with a conservatory feel. The friendly and attentive service is appreciated by regulars and newcomers alike.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3674;Gufer 55;Austria;Brand;Gufer 55, Brand, 6708, Austria;47.1038767;9.7390311;25;false;false;Regional European;Diners are spoilt for choice here! The variety of delicious dishes on offer ranges from wonderful starters such as vitello tonnato and delicious soups to risotto and Thai curry and Austrian classics such as Tafelspitz (beef boiled in broth), Wiener schnitzel or local char – all prepared using good, fresh produce. For dessert, the poppy seed noodles, for example, are extremely tempting. The atmosphere in this lively restaurant in the centre of the village is also inviting with its cosy, modern decor. Friendly service, and in summer be sure to make the most of the lovely terrace in front of the building.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3675;Fossil;Austria;Purbach am Neusiedler See;Kellergasse 6K, Purbach am Neusiedler See, 7083, Austria;47.9158838;16.6908872;58;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The name "Fossil" was not simply plucked out of thin air: This restaurant is actually located in a Muschelkalk limestone wine cellar dating back to 1870. At the entrance on the historical Kellerplatz, you are greeted by a plant-filled Mediterranean-style terrace. Then take just a few steps down, walk past the open kitchen and into the bright and imposing barrel vault, which makes for an enchanting setting. Chef-patron Thomas Daniel Pugel has been cooking here since 2015. Between noon and 9pm, he serves up regional and seasonal cuisine that is rooted in Austrian tradition yet incorporates modern influences – wild pike-perch fillet with fermented beetroot, Jerusalem artichoke and gnocchi, or Backhendl (breaded fried chicken) served with a potato and lamb's lettuce salad. Choose à la carte or the set menu of four or six courses.;Terrace;[]
3676;Woracziczky;Austria;Vienna;Spengergasse 52, Vienna, 1050, Austria;48.1894;16.35299;62;false;false;Austrian;Diners are given a warm welcome In this pleasingly informal inn (pronounced "Vorashitsky"). Both its laid-back atmosphere and Viennese cuisine are a hit, with house specialities such as beef tartare with avocado, or Tafelspitz (boiled veal) served with a creamy chanterelle sauce. The reasonably priced lunchtime set menu, which changes daily, is especially popular.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
3677;Zur Blauen Gans;Austria;Weiden am See;Seepark Weiden, Weiden am See, 7121, Austria;47.9192714;16.8533216;58;false;false;Farm to table;Located close to the lake, this delightful restaurant wins diners over with its delicious seasonal cuisine, attentive service and inviting decor. The wide-ranging culinary options include Backhendl (breaded fried chicken) and whole roasted Oberwasser char – there is also an eight-course set menu. The use of unconventional ingredients such as glazed catfish liver is also intriguing. Food is served inside, in bright, charming rooms with lovely wooden floors, or on the splendid terrace looking out onto the surrounding greenery and the marina.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3678;LOLA;Austria;Vienna;Gonzagagasse 14, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2154704;16.3703883;74;false;true;Spanish;A word to the wise: You should definitely make a reservation because this cosy bistro-style restaurant with the soul of a Spanish tapas bar is extremely popular. For one, the atmosphere is pleasingly lively and the decor is charming, with its high ceilings and striking bar that draws the eye. And then there is the food: they serve tasty tapas from different regions of Spain – these small plates are perfect for sharing! The mouthwatering menu ranges from Iberian ham and Manchego cheese to tortilla de patatas, and grilled red tuna steak with avocado salad to crema catalana. When it comes to wine, the focus is also on Spanish labels.;;[]
3680;Wirtshaus Krainer;Austria;Langenwang;Grazer Straße 12, Langenwang, 8665, Austria;47.5683758;15.6201896;55;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The Krainers offer a comprehensive experience with their family-run restaurant, café and hotel. In a bright and modern conservatory-like setting, Andreas Krainer serves up delicious Austrian dishes made with in-season local produce. Some highlights on the menu include the house goulash, Pöllau beef steaks and Mürztal fish hash, along with traditional Austrian desserts. In addition to the Wirtshaus offering, there is also a fine dining restaurant experience in the evening. And it is certainly worth calling by the cake buffet in the café. Hotel patrons can look forward to cosy accommodation, as well as a stylish and modern sauna and relaxation area.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3681;Wirtshaus Steirereck am POGUSCH;Austria;Turnau;Pogusch 21, Turnau, 8625, Austria;47.5299618;15.334073;22;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;A meal here is a delightful experience! The kitchen team has an abundance of excellent ingredients at its fingertips, from its own farm or from the surrounding area – something you rarely find! On Wednesdays the spotlight is on garden, field and forest, on Thursdays on offal, on Fridays on freshwater fish, and on Saturdays they mix it up. Attentive service courtesy of well-trained staff, who are happy to provide information about the sustainable philosophy. In addition to the inviting series of dining areas ranging from cosy and rustic to light and modern, there is also a terrific terrace with a beautiful view. As a convivial alternative, the ‘Schankkuchl’ offers meals prepared over a fire or steam at a communal table (Thurs.-Sat.). This wonderful estate surrounded by nature is also an unusual place to stay overnight: Here you will find very individual accommodation, from the ultra-modern tree house and former stables to the converted hunting lodge or the glass house.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3682;Hueber der Wirt in Bründl;Austria;Sankt Georgen an der Leys;Sankt Georgen an der Leys 18, Sankt Georgen an der Leys, 3282, Austria;48.0314107;15.2257842;18;false;true;Country cooking;A picture-perfect inn serving up really good food that is also great value. The vibrant cuisine stands out on account of its depth of flavour. In addition to tasty regional classics, there are sophisticated dishes such as sturgeon with baby peas, asparagus and alpine caviar. Friendly service and a cosy and modern ambience. In summer, make the most of the small garden to the rear of the restaurant.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3683;Mörwald Schloss Grafenegg;Austria;Grafenegg;Grafenegg 12, Grafenegg, 3485, Austria;48.43031;15.75015;85;false;false;Farm to table;In the grounds of Schloss Grafenegg, this restaurant is housed in what was once the castle tavern. It comprises a series of tastefully decorated, high-ceilinged rooms with beautiful hardwood flooring, large mullioned windows, chandeliers and classical paintings as well as the rustic and cosy Schlossstube. Tables are also laid out on the lovely terrace in front of the establishment. The friendly and attentive waitstaff serve up predominantly Austrian fare made with market-fresh produce – veal shank carpaccio or Topfenstrudel (curd cheese strudel) are examples of the tempting dishes on offer.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3684;Gasthof Adler;Austria;Schwarzenberg;Hof 15, Schwarzenberg, 6867, Austria;47.4138916;9.8524072;94;false;false;Austrian;Here, the cooking has been taken back to basics, with the focus placed squarely on the first-rate regional produce. The cuisine of Felix Messner – who runs the restaurant together with his brother Florian – is inspired by Austria and Vorarlberg. The simplicity of the fresh, flavourful dishes (eg breaded fried chicken, potato salad, pumpkin seed oil) is in keeping with the decor in this timber building on the village square, which was erected in 1756 and renovated according to historical models. Warm wood panelling from floor to ceiling makes for a cosy interior. There are also smart guest rooms in a modern regional style.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3687;Haslauerhof;Austria;Haslau an der Donau;Hauptstraße 17, Haslau an der Donau, 2402, Austria;48.1179223;16.7162553;99;false;true;Regional Cuisine;A tip to start off with: in summer, don't miss out on the terrace with a view of the Danube – it's idyllic! That's not to say the kitchen doesn't also deliver its fair share of delights: the beautifully prepared regional dishes are packed with flavour, from Wiener schnitzel (made with veal), potatoes and lamb's lettuce salad, to delicious ravioli or Arctic char fillet, to 24hr-braised ox cheek. Be sure to try the house-made vinegar-based lemonades, too. Hot meals served throughout the day.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3688;Carnozet;Austria;Hirschegg;Oberseitestraße 6, Hirschegg, 6992, Austria;47.3486478;10.1717676;31;true;false;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;Tastefully done out in a modern take on Alpine style, this restaurant provides both excellent food and friendly service. The menu features an appealing selection of seasonal dishes, mostly made from locally sourced produce. We highly recommend the grey cattle goulash with Walser Knöpfle (similar to spaetzle).;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
3689;MAST Weinbistro;Austria;Vienna;Porzellangasse 53, Vienna, 1090, Austria;48.2249667;16.361521;39;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Set in a historical town house, this trendy place is a winning combination of modern wine bar and upscale bistro. It is very popular for its great food, is made with seasonal ingredients sourced from local producers – and at fantastic value for money. Organic and biodynamic wines are recommended to accompany your choice of dishes. There is an appealing outdoor dining area, too.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3690;Krone;Austria;Hittisau;Am Platz 185, Hittisau, 6952, Austria;47.4580528;9.959555;96;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The town-centre hotel, Gasthof Krone, dates back to 1838. Today, the restaurant on its first floor serves regional and seasonal cuisine with an emphasis on sustainability. Fantastic ingredients are showcased in delicious dishes such as fillet of char with coriander lentils, ginger and lemon foam, and ricotta gnocchi. Diners can also look forward to charming and attentive service in a thoroughly inviting setting. The tasteful blend of clean lines and warm wood finishings (all the lovely furniture is made by carpenters from the Bregenz Forest) can be found both in the guestrooms and the restaurant.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3691;Saluti;Austria;Matrei in Osttirol;Grießstraße 10, Matrei in Osttirol, 9971, Austria;46.9962871;12.5342203;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Pizza;You can tell that an experienced chef is at work here! Ernst Moser serves up an appealing range of sophisticated dishes, including pizza and pasta, which can be ordered as a set menu or à la carte. Diners choose from options such as vitello forello, pigeon royale, glazed belly of Alpine pork, and spaghetti "Ernesto". Plus there is a well-curated wine list and friendly, attentive service. The restaurant, which adjoins a tennis centre, is not only popular with locals and regulars, so don't forget to make a reservation. You can also make the most of the small terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3692;Gründler's Genießer Wirtshaus;Austria;Achenkirch;Seestraße 35, Achenkirch, 6215, Austria;47.5031981;11.7061518;94;false;false;Regional Cuisine;This is the somewhat simpler and entirely regionally oriented alternative to the Gründler family's small restaurant Gourmet Stüberl. Also located in the Hotel Alpin, the same high cooking standards apply – the food is clearly structured, very carefully prepared and fresh as can be. Shining examples include trout carpaccio, radish, caviar, pumpkin, crab crunch, or lamb liver, apple, potato cream, peas, bacon. The space is bright, the atmosphere friendly, the service attentive and proficient. The excellent wine list has over 250 labels, with Austria particularly well represented.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3694;Jerár;Greece;Athens;55 Agias Varvaras Street, Athens, 172 35, Greece;37.9516;23.735155;16;true;false;International;Although located away from the tourist heart of the city, Jerár is winning new fans thanks to the cuisine on offer here. In this spacious and informal restaurant with a kitchen that opens out on to the dining room, chef Charis Nikolouzos showcases internationally inspired cooking that combines Greek roots (thanks to his connections with small-scale producers who supply him with his fresh ingredients) and French and Italian culinary detail. On the à la carte, featuring abundant dishes made for sharing, we particularly liked the Cacio e Pepe with “Mikrolimano Shrimp”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3695;Pharaoh;Greece;Athens;54 Solomou, Athens, 10682, Greece;37.986981;23.7307473;81;true;false;Greek;This restaurant boasts a concept that takes guests back in time thanks to its focus on the flavours of bygone days. At Pharaoh you won’t find modern cookers as every dish here is cooked using wood or charcoal as in olden days, endowing everything with a sense of simplicity and authenticity. The decor is a show in itself, with its combination of modern and industrial styles, open-view kitchen, plus a spacious balcony on which to enjoy your meal. Chef Manolis Papoutsakis’ cooking revisits Greece’s culinary traditions, but with a contemporary touch, as witnessed in dishes such as Tarama, Dolmadakia, Papoutsakia and Galaktoboureko. In the evening, a DJ adds to the atmosphere with music played on vinyl discs, so if you don’t want to miss out make sure you book in advance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
3696;Cerdo Negro 1985;Greece;Athens;5 Vitonos Street, Athens, 11854, Greece;37.9765222;23.7132013;89;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Fusion;This small taverna with a casual ambience, close to the Kerameikos archaeological site, is run in a relaxed fashion by two brothers who have combined their Greek heritage with a passion for Spanish cuisine. In this single-storey property with an attractive covered patio, they complement their varied à la carte of contemporary Mediterranean cooking (most dishes are cooked over a wood fire), with a six-course Taste of Cerdo Negro menu. Make sure you try the homemade bread and the “Welcome to Cerdo Negro” starter.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3697;Akra;Greece;Athens;12 Aminta, Athens, 11635, Greece;37.9718849;23.7449303;42;false;true;Greek, Contemporary;A unique and special experience in which the chef does the cooking next to your table or at the wood-fired grill in front of you while you are seated at the counter. In addition, there’s also a bakery at the front of the establishment offering delicacies baked in ovens distributed around the room, that dispense their enticing aromas to add to the sensorial experience. Renowned chefs Giannis Loukakis and Spiros Pediaditakis run this small space in the charming Pangrati district of the city, where the young and relaxed vibe provides the backdrop for uncomplicated cuisine that is nevertheless full of personality and prepared with fresh, seasonal ingredients. The menu is refreshed every day, with dishes superbly cooked in the wood-fired oven taking centre stage.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3698;Fine Mess Smokehouse;Greece;Athens;5 Delfon Street, Athens, 10680, Greece;37.9822573;23.7369194;42;true;true;Barbecue;If you’re a fan of smokehouse-style dishes teeming with flavour which take the American barbecue concept to another level, you’ll want to add this eatery to your list, as you won’t find anything remotely similar anywhere else in the city. In this informal restaurant, the only dining option is the à la carte, which features an impressive array of dishes for sharing as well as others that showcase its “Low & Slow” barbecue process. Head chef Elena Kaperda is also the face of the “Lick the Spoon” project – a unique patisserie workshop.;Air conditioning;[]
3699;Nolan;Greece;Athens;31-33 Voulis Street, Athens, 10557, Greece;37.9748437;23.7323284;32;false;false;Fusion;A contemporary bistro in the centre of the city, just a few steps from the busy Syntagma Square. The chef at the helm here (his father is Greek, his mother Japanese), creates contemporary Greek-focused cooking with plenty of Asian influences, and enticing dishes that are fresh, colourful and perfect for sharing. Next door is a separate space called “Sweet Nolan”, a pastry shop that complements the Nolan brand’s other ventures. In the summer months, the restaurant moves to Mykonos, with the whole team, and stays there from July to mid-September.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3700;Iva New Balkan Cuisine;Serbia;Belgrade;Kneginje Ljubice 11, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8197396;20.4610962;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A welcoming bistro with colourful, contemporary-style furnishings and an attractive outdoor space for summer dining. The menu is extensive and based mainly on traditional recipes that have been given a subtle lighter touch while still remaining faithful to their original style and flavour, largely thanks to the use of local ingredients. We particularly recommend the oxtail with caramelized onions, homemade gnocchi with veal brain and bone reduction.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3701;Istok;Serbia;Belgrade;Gospodar Jevremova 50, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8188482;20.4628399;51;true;false;Vietnamese;Situated just a stone’s throw from the lively town centre, this elegant restaurant with a South Asian ambience serves modern Asian comfort food in generously portioned dishes, some of which are available in half-portions allowing guests to sample different specialities. We particularly enjoyed the Miang Kham, a typical Thai appetiser that is not often served in Western countries. Every dish is served with colourful dips to make them even more appetising.;Terrace;[]
3703;Jiwan;Qatar;Doha;4th Floor, National Museum of Qatar, Museum Park Street, Doha, Qatar;25.2884648;51.548653;71;true;false;Middle Eastern;Its name translates as 'perfect pearl' and the location of this restaurant might indeed be perfect. Sitting on the fourth floor of Qatar’s National Museum, a stunning building modelled on the desert rose, it provides far-reaching views of the port and the Corniche promenade. Traditional Middle Eastern dishes are re-invented in a modern style, as with the cumin madroba, which comes with subtle spicing and enticing textural contrasts. Flavour combinations are nicely balanced, while the set menu is a veritable feast that represents very good value.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3704;Isaan;Qatar;Doha;West Bay Lagoon Street, Doha, Qatar;25.3770042;51.5278927;82;false;false;Thai;Sitting in a corner of the Grand Hyatt Hotel’s cavernous ground floor, this large open-plan restaurant boasts three on-view kitchens all producing authentic Thai cooking. Thailand’s influence extends to the décor too, with teak parquet floors and a Thai boat. Dishes are vibrant and flavoursome, with all regions of Thailand covered and ingredients flown in specially. If you’re not sure of your spicing level, ask the warm and friendly service team for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3705;Hoppers;Qatar;Doha;Barahat Musheireb Street, Doha, Qatar;25.2861266;51.5271841;60;true;false;Sri Lankan, South Indian;Sri Lankan and South Indian food is the draw here at this outpost of the popular London original. Spread over two floors, the restaurant is in the smart, redeveloped downtown area and is run by a polite and well-organised team. Order a few snacks and mocktails, then a biryani or a finely judged curry accompanied by dosas and, of course, some of the signature hoppers. Before long, you’ll have a veritable feast to enjoy with friends – and one that won’t break the bank either, so feel free to do some over-eager ordering.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3706;Goli;Hungary;Budapest;Arany János Utca 32, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.5025828;19.0534181;74;true;false;Middle Eastern;Set within the former Goldberger textile factory, Goli refers to the nickname the locals gave to this historic building. It’s a small place with a simple terrace and a colourful, cramped interior, but it’s gloriously friendly and positive vibes simply pour out of the kitchen. Sit at the counter to talk with the chefs, who are eager to guide you through the menu of fresh, tasty Middle Eastern favourites, from warm pita, vibrant salads, and green beans with chilli and lemon, to charred entrecôte with tahini. Deliciously fruity soft drinks and cocktails complete your meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
3708;Sparhelt;Hungary;Balatonfüred;Szent István tér 7, Balatonfüred, 8230, Hungary;46.961086;17.8762512;68;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Head away from the lakeside to seek out this honest all-day bistro with a smart modern interior and a popular terrace. Dishes have a Hungarian heart and perfectly reflect the seasons, with the likes of chilled fruit soups in summer and hearty, warming dishes in winter. Meat-lovers should order the mangalitsa Wellington if they see it on the menu, while fish fanatics should come on Fridays for the special seafood menu. They offer wines from around the world, but don't pass up the opportunity to try some of the superb local Lake Balaton options.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3709;Casa Christa;Hungary;Balatonszőlős;Izabella utca 1, Balatonszőlős, 8233, Hungary;46.9833212;17.8162828;85;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Roads fringed by almond trees and terraced vines lead to this stunning hillside spot with far-reaching views over Lake Balaton. It’s a restful place and comes with seven restored wine press houses which now play host to designer bedrooms with private saunas. Within the grounds sits this beautiful whitewashed restaurant with a simple bistro-cum-farmhouse style and a lovely terrace affording stunning views out over the vines towards Lake Balaton in the distance. The generous cooking has an equally Mediterranean feel, with bright colours and bold, contrasting flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3711;Kistücsök;Hungary;Balatonszemes;Bajcsy-Zsilinszky utca 25, Balatonszemes, 8636, Hungary;46.807404;17.780407;48;true;false;Hungarian;A short walk from the southern shores of Lake Balaton, Kistücsök is part of a small hotel which comes complete with its own swimming pool. Well-regarded locally, the restaurant is known for its consistently good interpretations of classic Hungarian dishes, which have been modernised both in their composition and their look. Flavours are fresh, with the occasional global influence, and prices are reasonable. The ‘Taste of the Region’ menu with wine pairings is always a great choice, and the floating island dessert has become something of a speciality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3712;Anyukám Mondta;Hungary;Encs;Petőfi utca 57, Encs, 3860, Hungary;48.3060516;21.1083033;43;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Anyukám Mondta is everything a good neighbourhood restaurant should be. It offers something to appeal to everyone, while prices cover a wide range to suit all occasions. Excellent produce is prepared with care, resulting in hearty, flavoursome dishes, and service is smooth, well-paced and comes with plenty of personality. Choose from homemade pizzas, refined modern Italian dishes and tempting daily specials – where you might find some Middle Eastern flavours too. The focaccia cooked in the wood-fired oven is a must.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3713;Platán Bisztró;Hungary;Tata;Kastély Tér 6, Tata, 2890, Hungary;47.6476346;18.3185045;77;false;false;Hungarian;Part of the Platán complex – which also includes a hotel and spa – this charming bistro sits within the same historic castle outbuilding as Two Michelin Starred Platán Gourmet. It has a pleasingly relaxed, contemporary style, and in the corner is a small shop selling desserts and ice cream. In summer you can dine beneath the branches of a 230-year-old plane tree on a charming stepped terrace which borders the lake. The concise menu sees robust Hungarian dishes given a refined bistro-style makeover while still staying true to their roots. Service is fittingly warm and chatty.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
3714;Újváros Bisztró;Hungary;Szarvas;Arborétum utca 2., Szarvas, 5540, Hungary;46.8644816;20.5388725;36;false;false;Hungarian;If you’re in eastern Hungary, it’s worth heading over to this ultra-modern restaurant on the banks of the Holt-Körös River. It occupies a space on the ground floor of a modern office building and is accessed via steps that lead to the river path, where you’ll also find the charming terrace with views of Bolza Castle. The menu showcases refined Hungarian dishes presented in a modern style, with catfish a feature, as well as steaks from Hungary, Uruguay and Australia (Wagyu). The interesting selection of Hungarian wines is arranged by region.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
3715;N28 Wine and Kitchen;Hungary;Budapest;Nagymező utca 28, Budapest, 1061, Hungary;47.5039676;19.0594798;31;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;You’ll be greeted as if you’re a regular diner here, even on your first visit, which immediately sets a cheerful tone. The welcoming team come, in part, from the Bock Bistzró stable – and they know how to look after their guests. The surroundings might be modern, but there’s a traditional element to the menu, which looks to the Hungarian larder for its base. Expect seasonally changing dishes such as a tasty vichyssoise soup, followed by juicy wild boar and then a delicious poppy seed cake. 95% of the wines are Hungarian, and everything comes at a great price.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3716;Morzsa;Hungary;Pécs;Király utca 42, Pécs, 7621, Hungary;46.0770872;18.2339024;53;true;true;Contemporary, Hungarian;‘Crumbs’ is a new wave bakery-cum-bistro with a relaxed urban style, owned by a charismatic and exuberant designer. Sit inside to watch the making of the delicious loaves and pastries or head out to the terrace for some people-watching in the part-pedestrianised lane. Modern, flavour-packed small plates are served throughout the day and can be accompanied by something from the biodynamic wine list. Of course, a pastry is a must to finish – the lemon meringue cruffin is a hit.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3717;Odre;USA;New York;199 2nd Ave., New York, 10003, USA;40.7313271;-73.9857639;85;true;false;Korean;What more could you want out of this little charmer in East Village? Always on the move, Hand Hospitality delivers again with a nicely pitched and portioned set menu of comforting Korean flavors. Find sleek degrees of refinement in winners like asparagus and lobster resting in a chilled pine nut sauce or snow crab wrapped in a thin cigar of daikon and set in a warm crab broth. All entrees like grilled duck with endive and black garlic puree come with banchan and a welcome bowl of rice and soup, which are kept warm in three cauldrons at the bar up front. Dessert is extra but worth ordering: A generous scoop of misugaru ice cream with rice caramel and cookie crumble is a sweet finale in this narrow, minimalist dining room.;Air conditioning;[]
3718;Bungalow;USA;New York;24 1st Ave., New York, 10009, USA;40.7236932;-73.9879972;59;true;false;Indian;Chef Vikas Khanna has struck out on his own at this warm and welcoming dining room where pale pink walls, colorful murals, and a bar with carved panels set a stunning tone. It's always bustling and securing a reservation may be difficult, with diners eagerly lining up early to snag a walk-in spot. Once you've found a seat, start with one of their unique cocktails (think turmeric-infused tequila and chili-infused mezcal), then tuck into contemporary Indian cuisine that showcases the diverse culinary traditions of India's 28 states. The kitchen's talent shines in standout dishes like the five cheese kulcha (stuffed flatbread) and yogurt kebabs wrapped in crispy kataifi pastry and served with a bright pickled cabbage puree and spicy mango coulis.;Air conditioning;[]
3719;Covacha;USA;New York;368 Columbus Ave., New York, 10024, USA;40.780955;-73.976205;99;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;New Yorkers have restaurateur Cristina Castañeda to thank for this special Mexican spot with a spirited, warm and welcoming atmosphere. Lime green, yellow and other hues decorate the dining room, which also features a mini loft and an amply stocked bar. The tequila selection is a perfect companion to the Jalisco cooking. It's not your typical Mexican menu: think of everything from delicious and messy shrimp ajillo with hollandaise to torta ahogada with birote salado, pork and oregano-spiked tomato sauce.Every item offered here is an amalgam of smoky, sweet and unique flavors. The dessert selection is concise, but don't miss the nutty-creamy avocado mousse paired with ginger-flavored shaved ice and an achiote meringue.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3720;Sami & Susu;USA;New York;190 Orchard St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7221457;-73.9880552;62;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;As further proof that big things often come in small packages, watch this narrow nook make a regular out of you in no time. On busy Orchard Street, this neighborhood gem hides in plain sight, anchored by a kitchen that doesn’t even have a proper gas stove. Seasonal, bright and unfussy, the menu is small but endlessly tempting as it roams the Middle East for inspiration. Simple, familiar things like tabbouleh chock full of fresh mint and sweet corn spark instant summer joy. Order anything with lamb, whether it’s wrapped in soft cabbage leaves or stuffed into squash blossoms, delicately fried and paired with creamy tzatziki. A punky soundtrack, a natural wine list and staff that will never judge you for over-ordering — what’s not to love?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3721;Badageoni Georgian Kitchen;USA;Mount Kisco;26-28 E. Main St., Mount Kisco, 10549, USA;41.2081435;-73.72809;78;true;true;Central Asian, Regional Cuisine;Mount Kisco locals are rejoicing at the arrival of this impossibly delicious Georgian "kitchen" as well as the new culinary dialect that accompanies it. This is a simple, welcoming dining room with a trestle-like ceiling, soft Edison light bulbs and dark wood bar. Pkhali rolls kick things off, where eggplant is stuffed with zucchini, peppers and topped with pomegranate seeds—the latter an ideal counterpoint to the rich ingredients. Mini khinkali (beef, veal and pork dumplings in a yogurt sauce) are in fact bold and hearty, and no meal is complete without them. The chakapuli with lamb alongside sour plums and white wine-kissed broth, is fragrant.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3722;Lungi;USA;New York;1136 1st Ave., New York, 10065, USA;40.7616417;-73.9602493;29;true;false;Sri Lankan, Indian;Chef/co-owner Albin Vincent, who grew up in Kanyakumari, India with deep roots in Sri Lanka, has penned a love letter to both regions at this Upper East Side restaurant with a contemporary setting. Chef Vincent learned to cook at his grandmother's knee, mastering the art of traditional Sri Lankan and Southern Indian dishes like pan-fried spicy kingfish served on a banana leaf with fried makrut lime leaves or kothu roti, a classic Sri Lankan specialty comprised of roti, meat, and sauteed vegetables mixed with scrambled eggs. Served with raita and a small side of curry with shredded chicken, it's not to be missed. For dessert, mashed carrots cooked down with warming spices and tossed with raisins and cashews is a sweet finale.;Air conditioning;[]
3723;Win Son;USA;Brooklyn;159 Graham Ave., Brooklyn, 11206, USA;40.7072662;-73.9431171;37;true;false;Chinese, Taiwanese;The exterior pays homage to New York's beloved bodegas, but the light-filled interior has a crisp, modern vibe thanks to glossy blonde wood tables, exposed brick walls and a small, polished bar that's perfect for both solo diners and couples. This bright little spot aims to showcase Taiwan's culinary landscape with a fresh perspective. Don’t miss briny clams in a thick bath of Shaoxing rice wine, bobbing with cubes of butternut squash and red kabocha. This may be paired with soft bao—their unique twist is as addictive as it is sloppy—and tailed by thick and chewy zha jiang mian (noodles simmered with tender lamb, chili oil, and Sichuan peppercorn).A word to the wise: scallion pancakes accompany a host of items here, so skip the appetizer order.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3724;Peppercorn Station;USA;New York;66 W. 39th St., New York, 10018, USA;40.7526109;-73.9848926;15;true;false;Chinese, Sichuan;This particular stretch that runs along the southern edge of Bryant Park sports an unusual number of Sichuan restaurants. Among them, Peppercorn Station is easy to spot, standing out with its cheery, brightly lit interior. The menu runs a decent length and offers a comfortable collection of favorites designed for sharing. Fish fillet with pickled cabbage is a must-order with its golden, numbing broth, as is the mapo tofu that’s been turbo-charged with fermented black beans. Sliced pork belly with garlic-chili sauce is a classic starter. Far from aggressive, this efficient kitchen is fairly even keeled when it comes to chilis and spice levels, and seasons just enough to nudge the sinuses. The restaurant has a second location in Jersey City.;Air conditioning;[]
3725;Zaab Zaab;USA;Queens;76-04 Woodside Ave., Queens, 11373, USA;40.7433172;-73.8887392;63;true;true;Thai, Isan;In an explosively colorful dining room that looks more like a children’s ice cream shop, find cooking that is equally vibrant in nature. Elmhurst is rich with talented Thai kitchens, but this one stands out for its fiery Isan-style cooking and prowess with seafood. It would be a mistake to show up without friends – or at least a very serious appetite. Dried shrimp and electric fish sauces are used with abandon on a menu that demands roaming. The house special larb ped udon pulls no punches with duck breast and fried duck skin jolted with fried lime leaves, mint, fried garlic and lime juice. Fried whole fish and bubbling hot pots tempt alongside excellent mainstays like prawn pad Thai and rotisserie chicken marinated in coriander and lemongrass.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3726;Saint Julivert Fisherie;USA;Brooklyn;264 Clinton St., Brooklyn, 11201, USA;40.6878747;-73.995614;38;true;true;Seafood, Spanish;This long-time neighborhood favorite comes courtesy of Chefs Alex Raij and Eder Montero, who also run next-door La Vara. The narrow space does not at all match the kitchen’s outsized talents and imaginative plates, which put seafood front and center. Consider starting with spiced Puerto Rican hushpuppies or shiso steak tartare tacos before diving into the likes of seared scallop tostadas with black garlic and olive agrodolce or mussel toast with fermented cucumber and dill. It’s seafood again come entrees: go for the cod pot pie that’s wrapped in a flaky, golden crust, or the jerked hamachi collar, which is brilliantly grilled and charred. A generous selection of regional wines highlights small producers to match the cooking.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3727;Ishq;USA;New York;202 Ave. A., New York, 10009, USA;40.7294114;-73.9809572;26;false;true;Indian;Promises of “modern Indian” often bring more flash than flavor, but that is not the case at this welcoming restaurant along Avenue A. A striking salmon-pink quartz bar stretches the length of the front area and into a moodier dining room where groups gather around generously spaced tables. The menu is teeming with ideas, and dishes arrive with all the right levels of spice, heat, depth, and nuance. “Jalebi Chaat” is a savory, textural playground with chickpeas, beetroot, and a sweet and sour yogurt. There must be butter chicken, which comes doused in a complex tomato makhani sauce. There must also be lamb shank biryani, portioned for a party and spiced to the hilt. Everything is designed to be shared so plan accordingly.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle;[]
3728;Agi's Counter;USA;Brooklyn;818 Franklin Ave., Brooklyn, 11225, USA;40.6699138;-73.9583561;25;true;false;Creative, Hungarian;You have room for one more dish, right? It’s a question that will come up often at this sweet little diner in Crown Heights. Chef Jeremy Salamon takes inspiration (and the restaurant’s name) from his Hungarian grandmother for a delightfully casual but fine-tuned effort. With walls painted cupcake pink, the kitchen has a real talent for bread. The cheddar-flecked biscuit sandwich with speck is an explosive first bite thanks to an expertly fried egg. It’s a good start to any morning, while the confit tuna melt on a superb Pullman loaf hits the spot come afternoon. Yes, there are crepes — thin, delicate and none too sweet — but there’s also cheesecake, chocolate babka and toast smeared in whipped farmer’s cheese and topped with market tomatoes.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted;[]
3729;Jiang Nan;USA;Queens;133-42 39th Ave., Queens, 11354, USA;40.759154;-73.8327945;78;false;false;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;One Fulton Square is fast becoming the address for the area’s most compelling restaurants, but unlike its neighbors, which stick to single specialties like Sichuan or soup dumplings, Jiang Nan delivers hits from all regions of China. The stylish restaurant group now runs multiple locations across the region, but this Flushing location is the original. Roast Beijing duck is a signature order that comes with thin pancakes on a silver tray. Fiery mapo tofu in a portion fit for four and one particularly thrilling sliced beef in golden pepper sauce are also must-orders. The grand setting is particularly attractive, ideal for dates and business meetings alike, thanks to a handsome Imperial design that mixes lacquered finishes, stone and greenery.;Air conditioning;[]
3731;Yellow Rose;USA;New York;102 Third Ave., New York, 10003, USA;40.7325412;-73.9879053;84;false;false;Tex-Mex;Sorry Texas, this "yellow rose" belongs to the bustling East Village and announces its arrival via a striped awning and bright green sign. Inside, it's quaint and vintage in every way. Amidst this setting of weathered wood and stained-glass chandeliers, diners can be found devouring Tex-Mex food with a focus on tacos and inspired cocktails. Flour tortillas are made in house daily and feature in a myriad of deliciously dressed-down creations—from the shredded chicken verde and barbacoa taco with avocado, cilantro, and spring onion to the heartier carne guisada. Skirt steak and pepper quesadilla is a sumptuous mainstay, but those with sweets on their mind should go straight for the nostalgic Texas sheet cake with candied pecans.-;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3733;Bonnie's;USA;Brooklyn;398 Manhattan Ave., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.717834;-73.9465277;33;false;false;Cantonese, American;Located within earshot of the BQE’s rumble in east Williamsburg in a nondescript corner, Bonnie's is an absolute discovery. Inside, the look is retro Hong Kong diner through and through but Chef Calvin Eng plates Cantonese regional cuisine with modern interpretations. Yeung yu sang choi bao is a wonder, stuffed with shrimp, green mustard and lettuces, then crisped and presented whole. The salt and pepper shrimp is tossed with melted red onions and is ideal for sharing. Don't sleep on the classic Hong Kong street food like cheung fun, with tender, seared rice noodles tossed with shrimp and scallop X.O. sauce and bits of cured pork. The creativity extends through dessert.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3734;8282;USA;New York;84 Stanton St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7215987;-73.9888182;81;true;false;Korean, Fusion;Are there any rules about showering a scoop of honey-infused vanilla cream with grated Parmesan cheese? Is there a consensus on whether an entire orb of creamy burrata goes well with rice cakes and gochujang-marinated chicken? There’s a first time for everything at this rambunctious little restaurant in the Lower East Side. The team works with a solid foundation of Korean flavors and from there, springboards into uncharted waters. Creative, bold dishes – all of which beg to be shared – run up and down this menu. Those wanting to stick to something more familiar will not leave disappointed. The pan-fried scallion-parsley pancake makes for a superb start, followed by tender medallions of grilled Iberico pork galbi resting in a pool of spicy red chili paste.;Air conditioning;[]
3735;Hupo;USA;Queens;1007 50th Ave., Queens, 11101, USA;40.7426369;-73.9533994;68;true;false;Chinese, Sichuan;Sometimes you can hear the sound of sizzling woks in the kitchen of this Sichuan dining venture. It’s a good omen in Long Island City, which isn’t known for its Asian cuisine but may be soon, thanks to Hupo. The sleek space is narrow and long, with dark hardwood floors and lofty ceilings.Such a quaint setting is an apt pairing for the small, focused menu that features regional favorites like spicy mapo tofu, house-made cold noodles slicked in a sweet and spicy chili oil, as well as Chungking spicy chicken. Nothing blasts of heat here, so spice junkies are unlikely to break a sweat. Still, dishes like stewed fish fillet in hot chili soup arrive chock-full of minced garlic and channel the kind of fiery, umami-driven complexity we crave from this cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3736;Rolo's;USA;Queens;853 Onderdonk Ave., Queens, 11385, USA;40.7019454;-73.9035084;66;true;false;American;Ridgewood has a real gem on its hands in this neighborhood grill that goes above and beyond. The first room holds an easygoing bar with a talent for cocktails. Further in, the adjoining dining area comes to life as a roaring wood-fire grill bathes tables in flickering amber hues. Fire here is the key to much goodness, starting with the fluffy, smoky polenta bread smeared with the likes of Calabrian chili butter or sesame and wild oregano. Other favorites include potato croquettes, lasagna, and, for especially big appetites, dry-aged steaks served with green garlic butter. Globe lights, handsome wood floors, and a friendly, casual cadre of servers add more warmth to an already welcoming space where everyone either is a regular or is about to become one.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3738;Burrata;USA;Eastchester;425 White Plains Rd., Eastchester, 10709, USA;40.9562696;-73.8137522;78;false;true;Italian-American, Pizza;Burrata is busy at all times for a myriad of reasons, not the least of which is the Chef/owner Chas Anderson's ability to create gorgeous, flavorful food. Even the open-floor design, with windows aplenty and oyster-tinted walls, is fresh and inviting.Thanks to the use of top-shelf ingredients and a wood-burning oven, this is a menu with not-to-miss pizze, along with starters and mains that deliciously blend New York and Italian sensibilities with a modern take on the beloved "red sauce" joint. Veal polpettine with robiolina cheese and tomato sauce is comfort in a bowl, as is the rigatoni enriched by Rohan duck ragù and porcini mushrooms. Of course, their signature Burrata pizza with its heady fragrance of mushrooms, delivers every time.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
3739;Haenyeo;USA;Brooklyn;239 Fifth Ave., Brooklyn, 11215, USA;40.6751466;-73.9814087;85;true;true;Korean, Korean Contemporary;This is the kind of spot that serves food so memorable you'll find yourself craving the same meal well after your visit. The kitchen is known for surprising diners at every twist and turn, as evidenced by the tteokbokki—spicy rice cake topped with Oaxacan cheese and chorizo. Start your meal with yache pajun, a savory and crisp pancake filled with vegetables. Not to be missed is the daegu jorim, cod fish braised in a luscious, sweet soy sauce served with tender daikon radish and jammy onions. Beat the heat with the mak-gutsu, chilled and icy soba noodles served with chili vinaigrette, then wind down over warm, light and fluffy beignets along with a sip from their wonderful selection of sparkling spirits. Affable service augments the dining experience at this local favorite.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3740;Chuan Tian Xia;USA;Brooklyn;5502 Seventh Ave., Brooklyn, 11220, USA;40.6396599;-74.0090575;22;true;true;Chinese, Sichuan;You’ll almost always find a line stretching out the door of this Sichuan superstar, which has rocked Sunset Park with its sharp renderings of Chengdu classics. The two-story space is light on amenities, with rustic wooden tables and short, backless stools, but the earpiece-wearing staff is as adept and meticulous as the food itself—and happy to dispense menu guidance to novices.While many associate Sichuan fare with buckets of numbing chili oil, these chefs tend to go light on the spice, letting complex flavors shine in dishes like whole fish slathered with sweet peppers or slivered pork in a vinegary garlic sauce. If the burn is still unbearable, a pitcher of fresh watermelon juice and platter of flaky wok-tossed pineapple fried rice will set you right.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3741;Roberta's;USA;Brooklyn;261 Moore St., Brooklyn, 11206, USA;40.70503;-73.93411;43;false;false;Pizza;Entering through this (now) iconic red door is like a trip through the looking glass and into Bushwick’s foodie wonderland. The city’s love affair with Roberta’s seems stronger each year, and for good reason. Everything from the industrial space to the underground bohemian vibe epitomizes Brooklyn-chic. To begin, try the grilled baguettes covered in gigante beans and wilted dandelion green and topped with a soft poached egg before moving on to house-made bucatini tossed in a sungold tomato sauce. Of course, no visit is complete without one of their signature pies, and there's no going wrong with the famous original. Takeaway is always an option, so when the wait for a table is too long, snag a porchetta sandwich to go.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3742;Alley 41;USA;Queens;136-45 41st Ave., Queens, 11355, USA;40.7591074;-73.8276588;71;false;false;Chinese, Sichuan;True to its name, this Sichuan stalwart does not sit in plain sight. A short walk off Flushing’s Main Street leads to an interior that is equally unexpected: A stylish corridor of concrete, curved wood chairs and elegant panel screens. The menu, now entirely electronic, is lengthy but the glamorous photos are accurate reflections of what’s to come. Chicken dumplings sitting in a pool of red chili sauce, and tender rolls of pork belly with sesame cold noodles are sensible starters for a meal that ramps up quite quickly thanks to a lightning-fast kitchen. In a flash, the table crowds with fiery bowls of mapo tofu and cauldrons of braised beef spiked with roasted chilies. Indeed, chilies, spices and heat are used to powerful, delicious effect.;Air conditioning;[]
3743;Tanoreen;USA;Brooklyn;7523 Third Ave., Brooklyn, 11209, USA;40.6309;-74.02772;34;true;false;Middle Eastern;This warm Middle Eastern restaurant is tucked into an unassuming Bay Ridge corner and run by Chef/owner Rawia Bishara and her daughter.Meals graciously commence with pickled vegetables and za’atar-dusted flatbread and are followed by a tableful of unique plates brimming with flavors and colors. Turkish salad is actually a bright red tomato spread, shot with harissa and dressed with bits of diced cucumber and a drizzle of excellent olive oil. Appetizers are numerous (grape leaves are a lively sure thing), but don't miss the mansaf, a homey dish consisting of braised lamb doused in creamy yogurt and served over a mound of fluffy rice. Like so many of the other dishes, it's massive, so come hungry or armed with friends.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3745;Chutney Masala;USA;Irvington;76 Main St., Irvington, 10533, USA;41.0391615;-73.8684871;63;true;true;Indian, Regional Cuisine;This longstanding restaurant in idyllic Irvington is a rather special place. Tucked along Main Street and framed by windows, it is bright and welcoming, thanks to mustard-yellow walls and art, and hand-blown glass light fixtures. A small, inlaid-tile bar out front welcomes one and all to dine on a wonderful, flavor-rich carte from Chef/co-owner Navjot Arora. Local, organic produce star in such complex, boldly spiced dishes as bhindi masala (imbued with tangy amchoor). Chana masala reaches delicious heights when paired with a sweet and nutty Peshawari naan, and pulu rasam, a lentil-based tomato and tamarind soup, and lamb keema pao, a spiced ground lamb dish, are two recent highlights. Mango chutney clearly shines here— so luscious, it may as well be jarred and sold.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3746;MáLà Project;USA;New York;122 First Ave., New York, 10009, USA;40.7272262;-73.9854205;34;false;true;Chinese, Sichuan;This beloved Sichuan haunt now counts multiple locations across the city, but everything started at the East Village original. The winding, cavernous setting includes a communal table, exposed brick, and low ceilings. Dinner could go in any numbers of directions. Some opt for the dry pot in which diners customize their ingredients—meat, seafood, vegetables, rice—and degree of spiciness. The possibilities here are nearly infinite. Those who aren’t up for making so many decisions swing for Sichuan classics. Recent highlights include the cold husband and wife appetizer (braised beef and tripe), warm dan dan noodles, and a particularly elegant white fish with pickled vegetables. Nothing is an intense barn-burner in terms of spiciness.;Air conditioning;[]
3747;Alta Calidad;USA;Brooklyn;552 Vanderbilt Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.6801476;-73.9681126;27;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;This stylish Mexican restaurant is bright and modern, with light-flooded windows and comfy banquettes, while the communal table and cozy bar lined with stools are great spaces to socialize and make new friends.Alta Calidad, means “high quality” and this talented chef certainly puts his money where his mouth is. Crispy tempura shrimp are set atop a tortilla with crunchy cabbage remoulade for an original dish, while paper-thin carne asada sprinkled with Chihuahua cheese and griddled until caramelized and crisp is another standout. Oregano roasted chicken tacos are simply finished with avocado-chipotle aioli and salsa cruda, or order the skewer of octopus, pork belly and potatoes over poblano rice. Churros with acacia honey and chocolate atole sauce are just right.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3748;Falansai;USA;Brooklyn;112 Harrison Pl., Brooklyn, 11237, USA;40.706648;-73.928737;79;false;true;Vietnamese;On a quiet corner in Bushwick, Chef Eric Tran is doing things his own way as he leans into his Vietnamese-Mexican heritage. What does that mean exactly? It means you can order sesame rice crackers topped with guacamole and tuna as well as a spicy green curry with grilled squid, all from the same kitchen. The menu changes often but there are some fixtures, like egg rolls filled with Berkshire pork and wood ear mushrooms or the fried rice with Vietnamese mortadella and Chinese sausage. If you’re with a group, swing for one of the large entrees, like the hulking five-spice lamb neck that’s meltingly tender and comes with salsas and warm tortillas. White brick walls covered in vinyl records add to the homey charm of this personable restaurant.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3751;Tha Phraya;USA;New York;1553 2nd Ave., New York, 10028, USA;40.7743581;-73.9544334;79;false;true;Thai contemporary;Is this the Upper East Side or the streets of Bangkok? Tha Phraya's interior pops with red lamps that dot the dining room, reminding one of a walk down Patpong Alley.There are a few familiar favorites like green curry and Thai iced tea, but that's where the typical offerings end. Instead, discover a unique variety of dishes from all over the Thai region including Northern Thai sausage spring rolls and khao soi to Southern Phuket-style curry served family style. Be sure to order the light and crispy sai-ua spring roll with flavorful Chiang Mai sausage and zabb hang, a bowl of rice noodles tossed with tender, sliced pork, meatball, and more in a homemade brown sauce. Specialty cocktails named after games played at Thai temple festivals are worth a visit alone.;Air conditioning;[]
3752;Little Myanmar;USA;New York;150 E. 2nd St., New York, 10009, USA;40.7229804;-73.9854621;95;false;false;Burmese;Husband and wife Thidar Kyaw and Tin Ko Naing along with their daughter, Yun Naing, run this tiny spot in the East Village. Despite its size, the hospitality is warm and the menu is surprisingly large. Burmese cuisine takes center stage here, and there is everything from soup and athokes, or salads, as well as hearty dishes including paratha chicken and curries. Kick off the meal with a delightfully crunchy Burmese pancake filled with vegetables and toasted sesame seeds but don't miss the house-made roti with rich, creamy potato curry. Kaut swe thoke, or yellow noodle salad, is another hit with tender noodles in a curry sauce studded with chicken, but no matter your selection, the flavors are bold, and the portions are perfect for sharing.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3753;Momofuku Noodle Bar;USA;New York;171 First Ave., New York, 10003, USA;40.72922;-73.98442;73;false;false;Asian;This elder member of David Chang’s culinary empire is hipper and hotter than ever. A honey-toned temple of updated comfort food, decked with wood counters and a sparkling open kitchen, the service here may be brisk. But rest assured, as the menu is gutsy and molded with Asian street food in mind.Those steamed buns have amassed a gargantuan following thanks to decadent fillings like moist pork loin kissed with Hollandaise and chives. Additionally, that bowl of springy noodles doused in a spicy ginger-scallion sauce is just one instance of the crew’s signature work. Other items, including desserts like candy apple truffle, are beautifully crafted and rightfully elevated to global fame.;Air conditioning;[]
3754;Cecily;USA;Brooklyn;80 Franklin St., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7273854;-73.9571173;30;true;true;American;Only good things happen here at Cecily. This little restaurant in Greenpoint has all the makings of a neighborhood essential, thanks to its relaxed staff, an impressively lengthy and thoughtful wine list, and food that goes far beyond the usual meat-and-cheese offerings of a bar. Boldy seasoned and perfectly pitched, the no-nonsense cooking is at once hearty and satisfying. Fried rabbit with ramp agrodolce is a meal on its own, but you’ll also want to order some thick toast piled on with mussels and pancetta and served in a knockout Calabrian chili butter. Any lingering appetites can finish off with a very shareable and very satisfying pan-roasted Berkshire pork chop.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3756;Dhamaka;USA;New York;119 Delancey St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7183105;-73.9881503;62;false;false;Indian;This rousing Indian restaurant in Essex Market is refreshingly unapologetic with its complex spices, fierce heat levels and inspired preparations of more unusual items (kidneys, anyone?). Dhamaka, which means “explosion” in Hindi, is a bold love letter to the country’s more rustic dishes, many of which are drawn from the owner’s childhood. Where else have you had smoky goat belly flecked with coriander seeds and wrapped in cedar wood? How often does your mutton come in a clay pot filled with a deliciously dark chili oil and an entire bulb of roasted garlic? The kitchen grinds many of its spices daily, and the crowds have been quick to recognize such attention to detail. Tables are comically small but bring friends anyway.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3757;Tredici Social;USA;Bronxville;104 Kraft Ave., Bronxville, 10708, USA;40.9404952;-73.8343981;99;true;false;American, Italian;Welcome to this dark, moody, and stylish retreat, where the only thing better than its ace ingredients is the delicious manner in which they are prepared. The tasteful space dons velvet wallpaper, splashes of red and shimmering silver. The fact that it's packed with locals along with servers who know your name simply adds to that sense of conviviality. Over in the kitchen, the chef fearlessly delivers a varied selection of dishes finished with flair. Specials always impress, as do the homemade pastas, like the ravioli stuffed with braised Kobe beef, caramelized onions, black truffle and Fontina di Val'Osta. Battered cod fillet with hand-cut salt and vinegar fries is an upmarket take on fish and chips. Close out with pistachio semifreddo for a lush treat.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
3758;Sagara;USA;Staten Island;98 Victory Blvd., Staten Island, 10301, USA;40.6378423;-74.0797638;17;false;false;Sri Lankan;Visit Sri Lanka by way of Sagara, where the island nation’s rich cultural diversity is on full display in a tiny dining room in the back of a local grocery. Dishes here are delivered at once, so you’ll be nibbling on an appetizer of fish cakes, mas paan, and fritter-like dhal vade, while also tucking in to hearty entrées. It’s a veritable feast as you make your way through the likes of fluffy Basmati rice with piquant curries.This kitchen certainly offers many compelling dishes—especially the hoppers with chicken curry—but the pièce de résistance is lamprais, served on a platter and wrapped in a banana leaf. Unwrap to discover such aromatic treasures within as rice with cashews and a braised protein—including mutton. Typically reserved for special occasions, it makes for the ultimate present to the palate.;Air conditioning;[]
3759;Rafele Rye;USA;Rye;26 Purchase St., Rye, 10580, USA;40.9824806;-73.6841905;47;true;false;Italian, Italian-American;Chef Raffaele Ronca oversees this inviting operation that fits in perfectly among its posh neighbors on Rye's Purchase Street. Step inside to be greeted by a long, marble bar—ideal for dining or good, old-fashioned drinking. Behind, is an open kitchen with a commanding oven.Snacks and small plates, such as a spuntino of caponata with focaccia, are welcome starters. Layers of silky eggplant tucked with fior di latte mozzarella make melanzana a natural choice, and pastas are a worthy option, as in the spaghetti vongole with its garlicky and briny tangle of goodness. To finish, an affogato with a scoop of excellent vanilla ice cream set at the base of a espresso lungo topped with crumbled house-made biscotti is a classic.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3760;Chick Chick;USA;New York;618 Amsterdam Ave., New York, 10024, USA;40.79022;-73.97339;55;true;true;Asian, Chicken Specialities;Occupying a prominent corner of the Upper West Side, this delightful operation arrives courtesy of Chef Jun Park. The space is narrow, deep and neat, with tables offering a view of the whirring open kitchen. Wood-covered walls illuminated by pendant lights result in an atmospheric vibe.Asian cooking with Korean leanings is what this team does best, so await—with bated breath—the likes of piping-hot fried chicken, its crisp amber skin and ivory meat permeated with sticky-sweet black pepper soy. Fried rice, that ubiquitous menu favorite, is studded with Chinese sausage, tobiko, and kimchi, and finished with a runny fried egg for a delicious dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3761;HanGawi;USA;New York;12 E. 32nd St., New York, 10016, USA;40.74666;-73.98482;20;true;false;Korean, Vegetarian;Beyond an ordinary façade lies this serene, shoes-off retreat with traditional low tables, Korean artifacts and meditative music. While wine and beer are available, a pot of royal green tea from Mt. Jilee is a more apt pairing considering the soothing setting.HanGawi is a soft-spoken, vegetarian-only restaurant that cares about what you eat and how you feel. The ssam bap offers a fun DIY experience with a long platter of fillings. Dark leafy lettuce and thin, herbaceous sesame leaves are topped with creamy slices of avocado, crunchy bean sprouts, pickled daikon, carrot, cucumber, radish and three rice options—white, brown and a nutty, purple-tinged multigrain. Topped with miso ssam sauce, each bite is a fresh burst of uplifting textures.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed,Terrace;[]
3763;Pranakhon;USA;New York;88 University Pl., New York, 10003, USA;40.7336446;-73.9931659;36;false;true;Thai;The name may reference Bangkok's original name, Phra Nakhon, but this busy spot is all about the now and just might convince you that you're dining in an alley in the capital city. It's precisely the point, as this restaurant from Intira and Norapol Youngphitak celebrates Bangkok's street eats scene. Dishes are well-executed, especially the hor mok hoy mang phu, a vibrant dish of tender mussels stuffed with curry paste custard and sweet coconut milk sauce. Namtok kor moo yang plates grilled marinated pork jowl tossed with spices and a Thai chili-lime dressing, but the well-executed curry pancake, a roti flatbread stuffed with minced chicken, vegetables, and ajad is a savory delight. It tastes even better while sipping an inventive cocktail named for characters in Thai soap operas.;Air conditioning;[]
3765;Una Pizza Napoletana;USA;New York;175 Orchard St., New York, 10002, USA;40.721645;-73.988464;45;true;false;Pizza;After rallying crowds on both coasts of the country, pizza maestro Anthony Mangieri has settled down into this airy, black-and white-tiled hall lined with canned tomatoes and eager diners. He is serious about his craft and is usually the one tending to the wood-burning oven, which yields glorious Neapolitan-style pies with fluffy edges, papery crusts and minimal toppings that hardly go beyond bubbly gumdrops of mozzarella di bufala and sweet tomato sauce. Indeed, this is a team that cannot be bothered with anything else besides pizza. There is a short list of starters, including a bright dish of roasted sweet peppers, and dessert is limited to sorbet or gelato. Reservations are tough to score, so walk-ins should aim to arrive early.;Air conditioning;[]
3766;LORE;USA;Brooklyn;441 7th Ave., Brooklyn, 11215, USA;40.663062;-73.984411;74;true;false;Contemporary, South East Asian;Welcoming with just the right amount of buzz, Lore embodies the perfect neighborhood spot—if your neighborhood happens to be sophisticated Park Slope. This unique corner storefront at the base of a residential building delivers creative Indian-infused and American fare made even more enjoyable thanks to warm service in an inviting setting. Chef Jay Kumar's food is certainly the star, but the poetic cocktail list is worth more than a cursory glance. Enjoy a three-course menu or order à la carte to revel in smart, refined dishes like roasted butternut squash over babaghanoush, a signature fermented dosa with coconut, tomato and dal chutneys, and duck confit with Indian-spiced bean mash and tamarind sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3767;Dim Sum Go Go;USA;New York;5 E. Broadway, New York, 10038, USA;40.7133818;-73.9974181;43;false;true;Chinese, Dim Sum;This wildly popular joint is still packed to the gills most days, and for good reason: the Cantonese fare and dim sum served here is as good as promised. Even better, they take reservations—and dim sum orders are taken by the staff, thereby ensuring that the food stays fresh. However, guests should avoid shared tables during the weekend rush as service can verge on chaotic. If the price seems a bit higher than its competitors, you’ll find it’s worth it for dishes like sweet shrimp, rolled in rice paper and laced with dark soy sauce. Plump snow pea leaf dumplings are spiked with vibrant ginger and garlic and may be tailed by rich duck dumplings or an irresistibly flaky roast pork pie.;Air conditioning;[]
3769;Tonchin;USA;New York;13 W. 36th St., New York, 10018, USA;40.7501;-73.98443;76;true;false;Japanese, Ramen;Leave it to this Tokyo-based ramen chain to offer one of the city’s best bowls. A refined tonkotsu is the house favorite but the smoked dashi ramen holds its own. All noodles are made in-house and boast proper spring and bounce. Starters also flaunt refinement, including the crisp-seared gyoza packed with pork, ginger, and set in a cast-iron pan sizzling with ramen broth. For something lighter but equally heartwarming, go for the kale salad dressed with an umami-packed vinaigrette and garnished with sweet pomegranate and grapefruit segments. Finish with mango milk shaved ice topped with a dollop of honey cream.The décor is sleek, featuring high ceilings, concrete floors, and everything necessary to make it a slam-dunk among the midtown lunch crowds.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
3770;Bayon;USA;New York;408 E. 64th St., New York, 10065, USA;40.7623778;-73.9591262;100;true;false;Cambodian;Husband-and-wife owners Minh and Mandy Truong offer an elegant peek into traditional Cambodian flavors at their Upper East Side restaurant, where a comprehensive a la carte menu offers a wide selection of everything from Khmer noodles and fried rice to Siem Reap specials, along with sections dedicated entirely to duck and fish. Top picks include chive dumplings, fried to a golden crisp and served with a ginger soy sauce, and nyoam, or thick rice noodles, tossed with a red curry sauce made with ground fish, cucumbers, long beans, and bean sprouts. Don't miss the banh chao crepe, a half-round golden crepe filled with ground shrimp, chicken, and a variety of vegetables and spices, that's intended for stuffing into lettuce wraps for a delicious treat.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3771;Superiority Burger;USA;New York;119 Avenue A, New York, 10009, USA;40.72636;-73.9834395;78;false;true;Vegetarian, Contemporary;What began with a handful of seats and vegetarian burgers has evolved with a new location and new menu. Brooks Headley's first-come, first-served spot, with vintage diner vibes, is squarely in the middle of the East Village and the new menu is equal parts quirky and contemporary, and fully vegetarian (even sometimes vegan). It's very creative, as in sweet and sour beets over jalapeño cream cheese and pretzels. Yes, it sounds weird, but it works. Cabbage filled with sticky rice and oyster mushrooms has plenty of character, and the burger crafted from quinoa, chickpeas, carrots and walnuts is how they made their name. All of the desserts are worth trying, especially the peanut butter pie and the seared malt cake with house-made cream cheese gelato that punches way above its weight.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3772;C as in Charlie;USA;New York;5 Bleecker St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7254254;-73.9926364;18;true;true;Fusion;Chef Eric JaeHo Choi's spot flies a bit under the radar, but with this wildly creative, cultural collision cooking, it deserves to be top of mind. You may become fast friends with your neighbor at this tiny space, but with a warm welcome from the hospitable staff, it's all part of the vibe. A compact menu keeps things tight with around ten dishes, but it's sprinkled with widely appealing Southern- and Korean-minded tapas-style plates. The cooking is straightforward and earnest with bold flavors. They're having plenty of fun from start to finish with items such as Seoul’sbury steak with galbi jus and gruyere grits, shrimp toast rolls and banana pudding with misugaru and meringue. Baby back ribs with a harissa glaze and plum coulis are slap-your-grandma good.;Air conditioning;[]
3773;Pierozek;USA;Brooklyn;592 Manhattan Ave., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7234369;-73.9504293;41;true;true;Polish, Dumplings;Alexandra Siwiec and Radek Kucharski are behind this casual spot in the heart of a historically Polish neighborhood in Greenpoint. There is a service station displaying Bolesławiec pottery, which is also the vessel of choice for their assorted food. Pierogi is their specialty—consider delicate parcels filled with jalapeño, mashed potato, and bacon—but don't sleep on their other Polish favorites including hearty borscht and golabki (cabbage stuffed with pork, rice, and topped with tomato-basil sauce). The savory and smoky kielbasa stands on its own, though whole grain mustard seals the deal. Raspberry and sweet cheese pierogi makes a sweet counterpart to the savory options but be sure to accompany each bite with a shot from their concise selection of Polish liquors.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3776;Hometown Bar B Que New York;USA;Brooklyn;454 Van Brunt St., Brooklyn, 11231, USA;40.674935;-74.016133;64;false;false;Barbecue;You'll know you're approaching Hometown Barbecue when you smell the wood smoke. Settled into a large warehouse in Red Hook with an industrial feel thanks to concrete floors, an exposed wood ceiling, and wood tables and chairs, it may be a bit of a journey from Manhattan, but it's worth it. Order at the counter, where they slice your meat and serve it on metal sheet-trays. Can't decide? Get the black pepper rubbed brisket, with meat that's tender and juicy. Sides—especially the collard greens mixed with shredded smoked pork and a velvety mac and cheese topped with breadcrumbs to order—are nonnegotiable. But don't forget about dessert. Their banana pudding benefits from a fresh crumble of vanilla wafers and is one dreamy-creamy bite after another.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3777;Cho Dang Gol;USA;New York;55 W. 35th St., New York, 10001, USA;40.7502;-73.98616;50;true;false;Korean;For a change of pace in bustling Koreatown, Cho Dang Gol offers the barbecue-weary an opportunity to explore some of this nation’s more rustic cooking. Soft tofu is the specialty of the house and for fitting reason (it’s downright delicious). But, bubbling casseroles and spicy stews are equally heartwarming. The menu also offers favorites like flaky pajeon, satisfying bibimbap and marinated meats. A sautéed tofu trio with pork belly is stir-fried with glassy sweet potato noodles and kimchi, in an excellent sweet and spicy red pepper sauce.The interior has a simple, homey appeal—its cozy dining room simply decorated with close-knit wood tables. The occasional burst of sound drifting down from the upstairs karaoke bar promises a little post-dinner fun.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3778;Enoteca Maria;USA;Staten Island;27 Hyatt St., Staten Island, 10301, USA;40.64187;-74.077255;19;true;true;Italian, International;No need to venture far on Staten Island for excellent Italian. Enoteca Maria is just blocks from St. George Terminal and brought to you by Joe Scaravella, whose cookbook, Nonna’s House, has been earning him (and this tiny gem) much applause. With its Carrara marble and lively vibe, most foodies flock here for a certain authenticity that is rarely sacrificed.Each night, the menu changes depending on which nonna is presiding over the kitchen, as in Nina from Belarus, who might serve a salat Odessa mingling grilled eggplant, red onion, tomato and parsley. Lasagna di Adelina arrives as an inspired layering of zucchini, basil pesto and creamy cheese, all topped with parmesan. And for a bit of sweet, try the torta di vaniglia di Melissa served with whipped cream.;Cash only;[]
3780;Runner Up;USA;Brooklyn;367 7th Ave., Brooklyn, 11215, USA;40.6658055;-73.9829882;66;false;true;American, Contemporary;Next-door sibling Winner may earn the trophy for its bread and desserts (also served here) but Runner Up is likely number one in many hearts given its serious focus on fresh, seasonal produce anchored by savory heavy hitters. Blink and you'll miss this diminutive place drenched in natural light. The good vibes extend to the food, where you may tuck into a sweet-tart citrus salad with aged gouda and cool-crisp fennel. Then, toasted sourdough is served alongside creamy trout rillette for a smoky-savory bite. A play on tortellini en brodo uses paper-thin daikon radish as the "pasta" with crumbles of chicharrón, while chaquicán mille-feuille plates three layers of crisp crackers with Chilean chopped beef stew, Kabocha squash, and salsa verde for a delicious dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
3784;Ammazzacaffè;USA;Brooklyn;702 Grand St., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.711339;-73.94459;75;false;false;Italian, Contemporary;This quintessential Italian gem on Grand Street is bound to surprise the moment you enter. The large and welcoming space draws you in thanks to an impressive wood bar, sleek dining tables and a handsome penny-tiled floor. Both the tables and light olive-tinged walls are dressed minimally—the former with wild flowers and the latter with beautifully framed photos. The garden outside will transport you to a trattoria in Umbria—on a dime. The well-edited menu spins to the season, but start with sea trout tartare, a dish that has been on the menu since the beginning. Follow it up with a plate of pasta or tuck in to dry-aged duck with sautéed faro and cherry amaro sauce. Tiramisu is a classic send-off.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3786;Chavela’s;USA;Brooklyn;736 Franklin Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.6734308;-73.9570421;62;true;false;Mexican;Ordering guacamole may be a reflex for many, but at Chavela’s, what lands on the table is far from the norm. Mexico City native Chef Arturo Leonar is the brains behind this exceptional riff, which mixes smoked trout, pico de gallo and morita chile salsa to thrilling effect. His creativity even extends to other dishes, like taquitos de cangrego with sweet crabmeat and spicy salsa verde, as well as handmade quesadillas stuffed with huitlacoche. Traditionalists may rest easy, as the subtly sweet mole coating chicken and enchiladas alike is bound to delight. Featuring a wrought-iron entrance door, the décor here is an absolute riot of color thanks to vibrant Mexican tiles surrounding the bar and artistic touches like that wall of ceramic butterflies.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3787;Café Mars;USA;Brooklyn;272 3rd Ave., Brooklyn, 11215, USA;40.677848;-73.9859256;22;false;true;Contemporary, Italian;This trendy Brooklyn spot from Chef Paul D’Avino is quirky from start to finish, and that's exactly what makes it shine. The contemporary menu is equal parts modern and nostalgic, with an outlandish creativity to boot. It's all intended for sharing, so come with a gang and kick off the festivities with four squares of negroni Jell-O with Castelvetrano olives suspended inside. Garlic knot monkey bread is topped with dollops of Parmesan butter. Pastas get an equal dose of creativity, as seen in the bucatini naporitan with diced porcini mushrooms and nardello peppers along with Japanese pork sausage links shaped to resemble baby octopuses. Finally, marble olive cake may look typical but it's anything but, with a salty-sweet combination that brings it all home.;Air conditioning;[]
3788;Phayul;USA;Queens;37-59 74th St., Queens, 11372, USA;40.7473463;-73.8912572;22;true;false;Tibetan;Momos are a point of pride for this Tibetan mainstay located in the center of vibrant Roosevelt Avenue. Large, generously filled and properly soupy, these dumplings are a treat steamed and even more so when fried. You could make a meal out of them, but then you’d be missing out on other specialties like fried lamb ribs seasoned with salt and pepper, stacked upon each other, and tossed with sautéed peppers. Steaming bowls of soup filled with noodles and comforting broths balance out sliced beef stir fried with tons of chili and large cubes of laphing. There’s more chili oil and a particularly ferocious hot sauce on the table for fearless spice hounds. Newcomers to this cuisine will appreciate a glossy menu with pages of clear photos of each dish.;Air conditioning;[]
3789;Bohemian Spirit;USA;New York;321 E. 73rd St., New York, 10021, USA;40.7691365;-73.9568423;34;true;true;Czech;It's old-world Bohemia, not hippie-chic, at this Czech beer hall located on the first floor of the National Bohemian Hall building. It exudes a classic European bar vibe with wood paneling, simple wood tables and vintage knick knacks. Naturally, beers and pilsners are the drink of choice, but for grape lovers, there is a nice European-focused wine list sprinkled with Czech wines. Hearty fare is definitely in store here. A large bowl of borscht arrives redolent of dill and is tangy and vibrant with a buttery finish, while grilled kielbasa is smoky and moist, sided by a mustard-forward potato salad. Dumplings litter the menu, even at dessert, where strawberry-filled dumplings topped with crumbled gingerbread are a delicious finale.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
3791;Little Alley;USA;New York;550 Third Ave., New York, 10016, USA;40.747356;-73.977005;50;true;true;Chinese, Shanghainese;Thank Chef Yuchun Cheung for brightening Murray Hill by way of authentic regional dishes from China, with an emphasis on Shanghai. This cooking is accomplished, serious and high quality, but one could still make a very enjoyable meal by just focusing on appetizers and dumplings alone. Signatures, and fittingly so, include toothsome slices of pig’s ear seasoned with chili oil, peppercorns and cilantro for freshness. Also explore dim sum, featuring pork- and crab-soup dumplings or caramelized, juicy and puffy pork buns. The Chinese sausage fried rice is a fragrant and wholly delicious treat.The attractive interior is festooned with wood furniture, dark walls, cozy lighting and a small bar up front. Younger crowds lend the space a lively appeal.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3793;Ruffian;USA;New York;125 E. 7th St., New York, 10009, USA;40.7263854;-73.984228;85;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;Spread over two spaces, including a small chef's counter space and the dining room with communal seating next door, Ruffian changes its menu quarterly to focus on a different Eastern European region. Past menus have focused on Austria, Hungary, the Republic of Georgia, and Macedonia among other spots, and wine is always spotlighted. Recent highlights have smoked trout mousse sandwiched between squares of lemon pound cake for a dish that is equal parts smoky, earthy, and sweet. A half-moon shaped pie crust studded with roasted shredded duck is a comforting dish served alongside a bright salad of mixed greens and diced orange in a citrus vinaigrette.Popular with industry types, it's wise to make reservations, or be prepared to wait.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3794;Miss Ada;USA;Brooklyn;184 DeKalb Ave., Brooklyn, 11205, USA;40.6896523;-73.9723305;63;true;true;Israeli, Middle Eastern;Many stylish Middle Eastern restaurants have opened in recent years, but few have come close to putting a dent in the crowds that rush to Miss Ada nightly. This Fort Greene charmer features a cozy dining room, a darling backyard patio and garden, and a keen menu packed with dips, meats, and veggies. Whipped ricotta with brown butter, sage, and honey is a sweet staple, as is the fantastic hummus topped with tender lamb shawarma. Sharing is the name of the game here, from the vibrant market salads to charred skewers like kofta with pine nut, short rib with cabbage, and halloumi with green tahini. All of it arrives properly seasoned and spiced from a shockingly small kitchen. Though reservations are scarce, walk-ins can find refuge at the bar.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3796;Sobre Masa;USA;Brooklyn;52 Harrison Pl., Brooklyn, 11237, USA;40.7063761;-73.9314679;87;false;true;Mexican;Heirloom corn is revered at this Bushwick restaurant, where chef-owners and husband-and-wife Zack and Diana Wangeman nixtamalize, mill, and knead heritage Mexican corn into beautiful, soft tortillas in house. The tightly edited menu gives equal playing time to those tortillas in a variety of ways while also showcasing Chef Zack's fine dining chops. Traditional dishes range from carnitas to ceviche, while creative dishes like chicken liver tostadas with candied kumquats or wagyu tongue empanadas are boundary pushing in the very best way. Lamb belly barbacoa served with a fresh green chepicha salsa is a simple but satisfying meal. The vibrant, beautifully spiced salsas like avocado-lime, garlicy tuom, chile de arbol, and chile morita are deserve commercial bottling.;Air conditioning;[]
3797;Coqodaq;USA;New York;12 E. 22nd St., New York, 10010, USA;40.7403464;-73.9889011;94;true;false;Korean;It's very hard to snag a table at this hot spot. (Pro tip: join the line out front if you can't get a reservation.) The rigamarole is worth it, as the ambience at this Korean fried chicken spot is just plain fun. There are other items on the compact menu, but you're here for the chicken. Available as a "bucket" that includes chicken consommé to start, followed by two waves of different types of gluten-free fried chicken with house-made sauces, along with cold perilla seed noodles. Finally, yogurt soft serve completes the meal. Stick to the bucket for a reasonable bill, but splurge, add caviar and extras and it climbs quickly. Cocktails play into the theme, but champagne is the star, with a nice range of offerings by the glass, as well as full and half bottles for every budget.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
3798;Potluck Club;USA;New York;133 Chrystie St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7195952;-73.9932226;22;false;false;Chinese, Cantonese;Chrystie Street wins big with this high-energy Chinese restaurant that is always down to have a good time. The stylish room leans on a Hong Kong cinema motif with posters and stills from famous flicks. Further down, a movie marquee hangs above the chef’s counter. Looks aside, the cooking offers a fresh take on Cantonese favorites using top-rate products. Pan-seared pot stickers get their boost from a Berkshire pork and chive filling. Fried tiger shrimp slicked in mayonnaise has never been more appealing. Also worth an order is the salt and pepper fried chicken. The platter comes with fluffy scallion biscuits and a chili-plum jam that should be bottled and sold commercially.;Air conditioning;[]
3801;Oso;USA;New York;1618 Amsterdam Ave., New York, 10031, USA;40.8219;-73.95009;23;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Housed within a brick storefront across from the City College of New York, this welcoming little spot is a true neighborhood gem, thanks to a concise, well-conceived menu, which draws inspiration from the street food of Mexico City. A Dia de los Muertos mural marks the wall opposite the open kitchen, where you’ll see industrious cooks working the grill and pressing house-made corn tortillas at a steady clip, which helps explain why they’re always so wonderfully tender and fresh. The tacos, like a spot-on al pastor, are of course excellent, as are homey offerings like braised chicken salsa verde enchiladas, smothered in melted queso Oaxaca. Save room for irresistible churros, served with chocolate- and cinnamon-caramel sauces.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3802;Nyonya;USA;New York;199 Grand St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7191602;-73.9969395;84;false;true;Malaysian;Nyonya flaunts a comfy setting composed of brick walls and basic wood tables, but really, everyone’s here for their outstanding Malaysian food. Speedy servers steer diners through the varied menu—and perhaps even away from such delicacies as prawn mee, an exceptionally spiced and sour shrimp broth with noodles, pork, vegetables and bean sprouts floating in its goodness.Some know to stick to such faithful and deeply satisfying dishes as nasi lemak, which is a delightful combo of coconut rice, pickled veggies, crispy anchovies, curried chicken and hard-boiled egg. The chow kueh teow, with stir-fried noodles, tiger prawns and squid, is a go-to dish, while coconut batter-fried jumbo prawns are another winner.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Terrace;[]
3803;Speedy Romeo;USA;Brooklyn;376 Classon Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.6874812;-73.959801;17;false;true;Pizza;Named for a racehorse and just as focused and quick, Speedy Romeo is a sure bet. Part tavern, part roadside grill, its kitschy décor and modern touches transform this former automotive shop into a surprisingly attractive spot. The owner benefited from years at Jean-Georges’ empire, and that intelligence and experience is conveyed through the smart accents and whimsical menu that begins with Italian ingredients. Peppers stuffed with chopped salami, cheese, and topped with breadcrumbs make for a nice opener. Then, take a chance on the non-traditional but utterly fantastic pizza combinations, such as the St. Louis, layering a proper crust with meats, pickled peppers and Midwestern Provel cheese.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3804;Untable;USA;Brooklyn;529 Henry St., Brooklyn, 11231, USA;40.6835424;-73.9996362;51;false;false;Thai;This cozy, Thai newcomer in Cobble Hill lists a “What the Hell” fried rice on the menu with 12 chili symbols. True to its name, the entrée is ferociously spicy, but this restaurant is so much more than a fiery dare. Entrees are where chef Rachanon Kampimarn shines brightest as he takes core flavors and delivers them with a certain level of flair. The soupless khao soi with beef tossed in a Chiang Mai-style curry is arguably the most successful riff on the menu, followed closely by a very light yet bold green curry that comes paired with a strikingly tender grilled chicken thigh and a bowl of purple rice berry. Pay close attention to specials: Fried branzino with fried garlic and chili sauce was a bone-in affair worth all the fuss and more.;Air conditioning;[]
3806;Tolo;USA;New York;28 Canal St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7144358;-73.9904615;23;true;true;Chinese;Chef Ron Yan is making a splash with one of the most exciting restaurants in Chinatown in recent memory. Just across from Seward Park, find a finely tuned menu that spotlights a range of familiar Chinese dishes, all prepared with style and refinement. Think tender beef shank buried under a refreshing herb salad or perfect fried cubes of tofu dusted in salt and pepper. One can’t-miss entrée is branzino fried until golden brown and served in a fantastic sweet and sour sauce. A unique feature here is the wine program—it's serious business with a long, thoughtful list and Zalto glasses to boot. With so much to order, your small table fills up quickly, and the small dining room gets busy in a hurry. It’s all part of the charm.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3807;Toki Underground;USA;Washington;1234 H St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.900337;-76.98891;51;true;true;Japanese, Ramen;You’ll go up the stairs, not down to Toki Underground, which shares the same front door as The Pug Bar. Once inside, notice raw wood beams, walls plastered with stickers and scribble, as well as dangling Christmas lights. No longer requiring a queue, it's strictly reservations only here, where counter seats turn quickly and you have slightly more than one hour to slurp to your heart's content. Fried chicken steamed buns, delicately fried enoki mushrooms, or pork dumplings are a good way to start things off, but it's really all about ramen. There are five selections, all freshly made and bursting with flavor. Go big and add extras to pump up your bowl but whatever you do, end your meal with a light yuzu custard.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3810;Taqueria Habanero;USA;Washington;3710 14th St. NW, Washington, 20010, USA;38.9374907;-77.0328526;76;false;false;Mexican;Walk by the kitchen at this Columbia Heights Puebla-inspired restaurant and you'll see a chef forming corn masa into tortillas and cooking them on the griddle. It's the attention to detail that makes this Mexican spot a neighborhood favorite. The menu may be concise, but every dish is made fresh and with great care. Even the green salsa that hits the table as soon as you take your seat is a standout. Start with the tacos—lighter than traditional tortillas—typically layered with crispy-edged, juicy barbacoa and red chili oil-flavored chorizo. Follow that up with the regional specialty—mole poblano with tender chicken and a slightly sweet, slightly kicky Puebla-style sauce. Good news for suburban dwellers—there is a sister location in Maryland.;Air conditioning;[]
3811;Dauphine's;USA;Washington;1100 15th St. NW, Washington, 20005, USA;38.9044539;-77.0349271;97;false;true;Creole, Creative;The old adage "Never judge a book by its cover" couldn't be more apt for this operation, which seems a most unlikely candidate for "serious food." It's vast and spread over three levels, but when you're seated in that perfect nook full of pretty people and tantalizing cocktails you'll start to get the drift.There is no denying Chef Kristen Essig's immense skill, as she prepares a delicious tapestry of New Orleans dishes—with zero fuss and maximum flavor. Make a hearty start with fresh-baked bread and cultured Poirier’s cane butter. Then dive into a platter of silky oysters Dauphine, tailed by blackened soft-shell crab with creamed Prairie Ronde rice. Carry on carb loading at dessert with dark chocolate crémeux and vanilla rice pudding—you won't be sorry.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3812;La Tejana;USA;Washington;3211 Mt. Pleasant St. NW, Washington, 20010, USA;38.93146;-77.03841;69;true;true;Mexican;There isn’t a morning that can’t be made or a long night that can’t be undone thanks to Ana-Maria Jaramillo and Gus May. Once a pop-up, their cooking has found a home wedged in a strip of restaurants in Mt. Pleasant. Quick and efficient, this simple counter serves just coffee and a handful of tacos mined from a time living in Texas. Their breakfast tacos offer a singular kind of satisfaction, each one made with a superb flour tortilla kept warm in tightly wrapped foil. Fillings include soft scrambled eggs, creamy pinto beans, queso and meats like bacon, chorizo and even brisket. These are uncomplicated, unfussy bundles of joy that don’t take reservations or require any other kind of long-term planning. The team is working on expanding upstairs soon.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
3813;Daru;USA;Washington;1451 Maryland Ave. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.8997152;-76.984322;21;false;true;Indian, Regional Cuisine;Rasika vets, Dante Datta and Chef Suresh Sundas, are behind this much-anticipated Indian operation. The corner space, flaunting a windowed façade and white-ringed Sanskrit logo, is an instant attention grabber. Weather permitting, a large sidewalk increases the dining capacity.Inside, at the bar-counter set abuzz with vibrant tunes, the kitchen team takes classic Indian cuisine in a novel direction. Is that blue cheese on your tandoor-grilled chicken kebabs? Yes, indeed. Matched with sour cherry reduction and cashews, it's as enticing a preparation as the boldly spiced minced bison momos. Nariyal lamb shank is rich and robust with saffron, chili and coconut. Sop up the heady sauce with light basmati rice and call it a night.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3814;Astoria DC;USA;Washington;1521 17th St. NW, Washington, 20036, USA;38.9105891;-77.0384634;66;true;true;Asian, Sichuan;This sexy Dupont Circle spot is frequented by a young crowd who keeps coming back for the cool scene and the well-priced modern and locally inspired food that often leans funky but is always delicious. Those seeking value should look no further than the "dishes for one," while those here with a pack of pals will find plenty to share. One dish to not miss is the cumin lamb. The kitchen layers on the flavors, resulting in tender, vibrant meat. La-Zi chicken is braised and fried with sweet leeks, ginger, garlic and plenty of chili, while mapo tofu with ground beef, chili, garlic, scallion and Sichuan peppercorn is always a hit. No reservations or just want a quick bite? The bar always has room.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3815;Sababa;USA;Washington;3311 Connecticut Ave. NW, Washington, 20008, USA;38.933838;-77.05726;76;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;“Sababa,” which means “cool” in Hebrew slang, is exactly as advertised. Sharing a wall and connected by a gorgeous zinc bar to Bindaas next door, this ode to the Middle East is awash in Mediterranean tiles. But despite the hip digs, it’s all about food here. The fine-tuned menu features Israeli salads, dips and kebabs, but small plates are its heart and soul. Start with salatim, a five-salad starter. Then choose from dishes such as charred eggplant with herbed labneh, fried cauliflower with tahini and raisins or pomegranate-glazed chicken liver. The list goes on, but one thing to never skip is the hummus. It’s so much more than the usual that it’s even listed as a daily special. Keeping in line with the spirit is their Israeli- and Greek-focused wine list.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3816;L’Ardente;USA;Washington;200 Massachusetts Ave. NW, Ste. 100, Washington, 20001, USA;38.8992954;-77.0139637;85;false;true;Italian;Many diners walking into East End's shiny Capitol Crossing development already know what they’re ordering. Chef David Deshaies' 40-layer lasagna has captivated the city’s attention and rightfully so. Tender short rib, truffled mornay, and razor-thin sheets of pasta make for a delicious trinity that tastes as good as it looks.With soaring ceilings and windows to match, this Italian kitchen has plenty more to offer. A wood-burning grill and pizza oven allude to its other strengths—sit at the counter to watch them fly out. Bucatini cacio e pepe or gnocchi with meaty lamb ragu are just a few of the dishes that satisfy. Do save room for dessert, especially the seasoned lime mousse with black currant sauce.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
3818;Makan;USA;Washington;3400 11th St. NW, Washington, 20010, USA;38.9318821;-77.0284184;81;false;true;Malaysian;If you've ever considered ordering dessert first, do it here. Flaky, crispy roti canai served with a delicate pandan coconut cream offers a faithful Asian twist on the classic French Toast. It's the kind of cross-cultural deliciousness you can expect from this Malaysian kitchen team, which takes its culinary cues from India and China.To that end, both noodles and rice form the heart of this menu. Char kway teow features seared flat rice strands tossed with shrimp, Chinese sausage and bean sprouts. Hearty pork vindaloo boasts layer upon layer of just the right spice, heat and acid. Fried chicken arrives doused in a yellow curry flecked with curry leaves. Yes, you should share everything, but no, you cannot nap on those turquoise couches after.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3819;Oyamel;USA;Washington;401 7th St. NW, Washington, 20004, USA;38.89489;-77.02183;99;true;false;Mexican;This well-liked mainstay of DC Mexican cuisine comes courtesy of Spanish Chef Jose Andres, whose typical dedication to flavorful cooking and high-quality ingredients still draws brisk business. Snag a seat at the entertaining ceviche bar and sip thirst-quenching drinks while snacking on small plates.The kitchen's dedication to technique and ingredients is clear, with a particular penchant for regionally inflected Mexican cuisine like huevos enfrijoladas, crispy chilaquiles, and gorditas topped with Hudson Valley duck confit. Don’t miss the tarasca estilo pátzcuaro though, an otherworldly black bean soup with avocado leaves, swirls of crema, and crumbled cotija. A special hora feliz menu makes the early evening hours very happy indeed.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
3820;Hitching Post;USA;Washington;200 Upshur St. NW, Washington, 20011, USA;38.94222;-77.01365;95;true;false;Southern, Regional Cuisine;Chef Barry Dindyal is the talent behind this prominent and retro Petworth destination. Diners here will find that time mostly stands still inside, thanks to a simple (by design) aesthetic, dominated by wood with hints of orange, pleather booths and a buzzy bar. Throwback decor aside, most diners are here for the chef's delicate rendition of beloved Southern classics. Crisp, tender and enticingly juicy, fried chicken takes center stage. Like most other items on this menu, it is made-to-order daily and absolutely worth the wait. When coupled with succulent vegan collard greens or homemade French fries, it transforms into a heartwarming delight. Can't manage another morsel? A taste of the lemon cake slathered with butter cream will change your mind in a flash.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3821;Amparo Fondita;USA;Washington;2002 P St. NW, Washington, 20036, USA;38.9096349;-77.0452774;23;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;A onetime pop-up, this contemporary Mexican restaurant now enjoys a permanent home in a minimalist space just off Dupont Circle. Chef Christian Irabién prioritizes exceptional ingredients, as in corn sourced from Oaxaca, then nixtamalized in-house. The menu is wide-ranging with selections from the raw bar, appetizers, sopecitos, and an array of main dishes like halibut with mole. Sides, such as a fried plantain that seems simple but is layered with flavor, shouldn't be overlooked. No matter the selection, every dish tempts with creative and contemporary flair. Take the papaya nixtamal. Cooked in piloncillo and Mexican vanilla, served over a coconut cream and finished with fennel pollen and wildflower honey, it mystifies with mind-bending complexity.;Air conditioning;[]
3825;Unconventional Diner;USA;Washington;1207 9th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.906124;-77.02381;55;false;false;American;With its white walls and seafoam-green booths, this “diner” may look like the classic American translation but is in fact a far cry from your tuna-melt standby (and book ahead, because it's always busy). Instead, this kitchen ramps up known classics by riffing on tradition. Need proof? Look no further than the kale nachos or meatloaf elevated with a hint of sriracha and morel mushroom gravy. Even waistline watchers won't be able to say no to those hearty chicken pot pie poppers. Roasted cauliflower tossed in tahini with fried chickpeas for crunch and pickled red onions for acidity is another win and goes to show that creating new traditions is just as vital as jazzing up the old ones. For salads, sammies, and egg-centric items, be sure to visit during the day for their brunch offerings, and save room for a slice of their spectacular lemon meringue pie.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3826;Stellina Pizzeria;USA;Washington;399 Morse St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.9079122;-77.0000413;33;false;true;Pizza, Italian;Self-appointed as a "Neo-Neapolitan" style pizzeria, this is a bright spot with a line of of colorful tiles, red stools and a blazing open kitchen equipped with—you guessed it—a wood-burning oven. You may even see Chef/owner Matteo Venini manning this mighty machine, as he is known to turn out pies faster than you can say Margherita. It's simple counter service here, yet those crusts are anything but—imagine a series of well-blistered and delightfully chewy pies, like the savory coppa and creamy Taleggio, drizzled with olive oil and sprinkled with fresh thyme. The pizza is served whole, but you get to cut it yourself at the table. The light and crisp fritti makes a great start, just as the tiramisu is a fresh, delicious, wallet-friendly finish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3827;Zaytinya;USA;Washington;701 9th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.8985405;-77.0238266;75;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Chef José Andrés' ocean-blue ode to the cuisine of Greece, Lebanon, and Turkey means an ample, wide-ranging carte. The space too, sleek and modern, speaks to the ease and elegance of the Mediterranean. It's an ideal spot for suits sealing deals, as well as solo diners or friends catching up. Mezze is the menu's focus and the quality of food is solid. Zero in on the mushroom kapnista with dates, walnuts, and labneh for richness. There are a myriad of spreads to be paired with fresh pita, followed by salads and flatbreads (or pide), which are of the dive-right-in variety. Vegetarians will revel in the diversity of dishes, while braised lamb is the Sunday roast everyone deserves.Greek and Lebanese labels are given their due on the exceptional wine list.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3828;The Red Hen;USA;Washington;1822 1st St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.914898;-77.01227;63;false;true;Italian;You’ll want to wake up with the rooster to score a reservation at this rustic Italian gem as it’s incredibly popular, and always packed. Walk-ins can snag a seat at the three-sided bar that anchors the room, decked out in full country charm with exposed brick walls, reclaimed timber and beamed ceilings. What’s so special, you ask? The food, of course, which is terrific. Pastas are spot on and include cacio e pepe “arancini,” crowd-favorite mezzi rigatoni or even the mafalde verde—a sweet-and-savory combo of braised duck ragù, Calabrian chili and pecorino romano. Entrées like grilled short rib or scallops with pickled chili aïoli are also exquisite.The short wine list features unusual selections (Slovenia, anyone?) and very affordable prices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
3829;Lapis;USA;Washington;1847 Columbia Rd. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.921295;-77.043915;93;true;false;Afghan;From its whitewashed walls and stunning Afghan rugs warming the floor to the sepia-toned heirloom photos on the walls, this place exudes warmth and charm, albeit in a highly stylish manner.Husband-and-wife owners Zubair and Shamim Popal share the fragrant cuisine of their native Afghanistan. Light and fresh without the heavy-handed spicing of other regional cuisines, this food is a delicious discovery. Split pea soup may sound basic but here it is layered with flavor. And chopawn is the real deal—this trio of grilled-to-perfection lamb chops is served with sensational cardamom-scented rice and draws you in forkful after fluffy forkful.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3830;Yellow;USA;Washington;1524 Wisconsin Ave. NW, Washington, 20007, USA;38.909454;-77.064597;64;true;true;Middle Eastern;Chef/owner Michael Rafidi and team are behind this daytime casual concept in Georgetown where Levantine cooking takes center stage thanks to a wood-burning oven. It's always humming here, where long lines form for pastries, breakfast sandwiches or shakshuka in the morning and pita sandwiches, spreads and sides (creamy labne with charred corn, urfa chili crisp and smoked feta, anyone?). Fluffy pitas filled with chicken shawarma, Palestinian pickles and green tatbili labne, or tender lamb with smoked peppers, feta and toum are popular. Just try not finishing the batata tots, or golden-brown potatoes with shawarma spices and urfa sauce. To finish, a brown butter and cinnamon cookie, Turkish coffee brownie or soft serve are compelling choices.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3831;Maketto;USA;Washington;1351 H St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.900124;-76.986694;83;false;true;Asian;Credit to chef-owner Erik Bruner-Yang and his team for keeping it fresh, as it were. On ever-changing H Street, this long-favored restaurant at first looks like a clothing store with its glittering display cases lined with chic merch. More impressive, though, is what’s on the menu: A diverse, ambitious, and consistently satisfying roster of dishes inspired by flavors from across Asia. Everything here is designed to share, starting with Cantonese-style shrimp dumplings dressed in Cambodian fish sauce and garnished with dill. What’s next? A Thai-spicy riff on pork laab with bone marrow? An imposing boulder of crispy fried chicken laced in five-spice caramel? There are no rules, no borders, in this house, and diners wouldn’t want it any other way.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3832;Karma Modern Indian;USA;Washington;611 I St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.900967;-77.0206;36;false;true;Indian, Contemporary;Large windows and a navy blue-and-white palette set a distinctly modern tone at this appropriately named Indian bistro. It is a far cry from your everyday curry house, as a great deal of care is taken to coax each dish with distinctive flavors. Even its spices are ground on the premises—while you wait, read about their health benefits in the guide on the back of the menu.The tasting menu offerings are at once traditional and contemporary. Don't overlook the imaginative drinks, both spirit-based and alcohol-free, like the Tiger's Tail made with blood orange, turmeric and chili water. Naan here is a cut above the norm, as in the wild mushroom with a hint of truffle. The use of top ingredients shines through in the elegant, rich and flavorful paneer lajawab.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
3834;Yao Yao;USA;Chicago;230 W. Cermak Rd., Chicago, 60616, USA;41.8530174;-87.6329997;64;true;true;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;The aquamarine tones create a light and airy setting, but don't mistake the pastel tones for something less than serious. Score one of the front tables for a view of the glass-enclosed kitchen, though the wood-crafted banquette is ideal for settling in. Yao Yao pickled fish is the signature dish here, and it comes in three sizes (extra-large feeds up to six people!). Fiery and potent, this plate delivers a one-two punch with a funky seafood quality and the sharp tang of sour greens. Choose the "two flavored pickled" for a taste of Yao Yao pickled fish and boiled beef in a spicy Szechuan sauce. There are also a slew of sides, ranging from celtuce and dry bean curd skin to seaweed knot and konjac noodles to round out the meal.;Air conditioning;[]
3835;Proxi;USA;Chicago;565 W. Randolph St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8843969;-87.6426342;28;true;false;International, Asian;Here at Proxi, Chef Andrew Zimmerman seems intent on presenting his diners with a culinary whirlwind that blows from Thai beef salad to coal-roasted oysters with ssamjang butter and beyond. Otherworldly highlights reveal delicate duck dumplings floating in a pho broth with fried shallots and aromatic herbs. Regardless of the dish’s inspiration, it’s sure to be delicious in this kitchen’s capable hands. Desserts, like avocado mousse, are made with formidable talent.The massive room is effortlessly cool and sleek, with blue-tiled columns set beneath the white-vaulted ceiling. It also features an open kitchen and myriad seating options for everyone—from solo diners to large groups. A front lounge is ideal for lingering and waiting for your party to arrive.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3836;Mott St.;USA;Chicago;1401 N. Ashland Ave., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.90711;-87.667465;88;true;false;Fusion, Contemporary;Offerings at this hip haven in Bucktown crisscross the globe. Chef Edward Kim has a vivid imagination and his cooking takes detours through delicious landscapes, pulling off a rare feat of cooking delicious Midwest/Asian food with a touch of novelty. Take the crispy cauliflower, for one. These wok-fried cauliflower florets are crisp and juicy, then served with a sweet and tangy chili sauce, Szechuan peppercorn and coriander for a savory dish that's both warm and wonderful. Garlic fried rice may be simple and to the point but it's oh-so-good with pungent garlic and flavorful seasoning. Do keep an eye out for the special Chinese New Year menu.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
3837;Dear Margaret;USA;Chicago;2965 N. Lincoln Ave., Chicago, 60657, USA;41.9357213;-87.6629575;57;false;false;Contemporary, French;This quaint spot from Chef Ryan Brosseau pays homage to his French-Canadian mémé, Margaret, and fittingly, resembles a grandma's house. If you're envisioning a blue-painted façade, white-trim windows, and framed paintings all set below a decorative ceiling, you're starting to get the picture here. A small bar in the back and engaging staff keep things homey and abuzz.This is a French-Canadian menu that goes beyond poutine and cheese curds. Comfort and decadence are at the heart of such shareable plates as an heirloom tomato salad starring fromage blanc, pickled shallots and dressed with black garlic-ice wine vinegar. Nanaimo bars are a sweet and salty confection with a graham cracker crumb, cocoa powder and walnut—all finished with chocolate ganache.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3838;Boonie's;USA;Chicago;4337 N. Western Ave., Chicago, 60618, USA;41.9606344;-87.6883937;41;false;false;Filipino;The intoxicating, unmistakable aroma of garlic fills the narrow room every time someone opens the rice cooker. This rice is the foundation of all things that are good at this homey Filipino restaurant that started out as a food stall. To begin, the crispy pork belly hash is an impressive starter that could very well double as an entrée. Pork, in fact, is all over this small menu, arriving as crispy belly or marinated with herbs and spices or presented as sausage. Tender filets of steelhead trout swimming in a burnt tomato and tamarind broth offer a delicate reprieve from the meat. Dessert is a must: A creamy plantain comes wrapped as a spring roll, dusted in brown sugar and deep fried. It’s as close as you’ll ever get to a handheld crème brûlée.;Air conditioning;[]
3839;mfk.;USA;Chicago;432 W. Diversey Pkwy., Chicago, 60614, USA;41.9330403;-87.6405573;61;false;true;Spanish, Fusion;“First we eat, then we do everything else,” said M.F.K. Fisher, the food writer who serves as both the inspiration and namesake for this local darling. Thanks to large windows, whitewashed brick walls and silver-and-white tilework, the subterranean space manages to evoke a breezy oasis. Organized from small to large plates, the thoughtfully composed, Iberian-inspired menu follows suit.  Simple, flavorful dishes, like warm boquerónes, croquettes with Montamoré cheese, or crostini with butter, lemon, and a single anchovy are tempting before main dishes like seared scallops with persimmon gazpacho or sides like roasted parsnips with mole amarillo. A crumbly slice of Basque cake and a cortado end the meal on a high note.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
3840;Giant;USA;Chicago;3209 W. Armitage Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.917324;-87.70744;79;false;false;American;Brought to you by Jason Vincent, this fabulous and friendly restaurant is the epitome of Chicago. Its menu is a listing of familiar dishes (think onion rings, crab salad and baby back ribs), albeit drummed up with unique accents reflecting the chef’s distinctive style. The petite space is simple and lovely, with a modern-rustic décor and genuinely cozy neighborhood vibe. A chef’s counter in the back offers an up-close-and-personal kitchen experience.Kick things off with the excellent Jonah crab salad, served with soft waffle-cut potato fritters and freshly made cocktail sauce. Then move on to the “pici with chew,” where thick strands of noodles are cooked to a conservative al dente, and tossed with smoky bacon, chopped jalapeños and breadcrumbs.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3841;Sifr;USA;Chicago;660 N. Orleans St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.8940266;-87.6372059;28;true;false;Middle Eastern;It is difficult to imagine a dinner here that doesn’t include the hummus. A gorgeous mosaic of charred green chickpeas, crispy chickpeas, zhoug, and za’atar raise this familiar dish to wonderful heights. There’s more on the way: A platter of chicken shish taouk that’s marinated in yogurt, crusted in spices and charred all over or halloumi cheese served with beets and finished in a honey and pomegranate molasses. In this quiet, sun-soaked corner of River North, the team behind Indienne hits the mark with this Middle Eastern charmer where tables crowd with dips, small plates, and items hot off the grill. You’re expected to share but that’s easier said than done. Silky-smooth, house made ice creams make for a sweet send-off.;Air conditioning;[]
3845;Chef’s Special Cocktail Bar;USA;Chicago;2165 N. Western Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9217923;-87.6872963;85;false;true;Chinese, American;Nostalgia is alive and well inside the colorful dining room, complete with oceanic hues, soft cushions, vibrant artwork and a U-shaped bar. A large dining area with proper tables is perfect for groups.This throwback is a loud and happy place, thanks to an extensive menu of heartwarming Chinese-American classics. Crab rangoon and shrimp chips make an appearance, but don't miss those luscious dan dan noodles or "special combo" fried rice, studded with cubes of pork, shrimp and more. The bone-in pork shank with black bean sauce and charred cabbage is designated a "special" for good reason, and fried string beans in a rich, savory broad bean purée are a must. Finish with the sesame cake with jasmine and orange.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3847;Girl & The Goat;USA;Chicago;809 W. Randolph St., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.88418;-87.64785;56;true;true;Contemporary, American;The revolving door never stops turning as Girl & The Goat’s party keeps going. Even on a Monday night, guests linger for hours, shouting over the din at this sceney but always friendly stunner. Appropriately rustic wooden pillars and beams connect a warren of seating areas, from elevated platforms to banquettes to dim private corner nooks.A pick-your-own-protein adventure, the menu is organized by ingredients with a dedicated section for goat. Start with freshly baked ham bread accompanied by smoked Swiss cheese-butter seasoned with coarse mustard and olive tapenade. End with an almost pudding-like “all leches” cake enriched with strawberry-rhubarb sorbet. The kitchen may even send out mini portions of menu items for solo diners—a truly thoughtful touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3850;Table, Donkey and Stick;USA;Chicago;2728 W. Armitage Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.91759;-87.696;44;false;true;Austrian;When American comfort food just won’t suffice, look to Table, Donkey and Stick for a helping of cozy Alpine fare. The rustic inn-inspired setting reflects its reputation as a gathering place where friends meet at the inviting bar or settle in at communal tables for whimsical, creative compositions.To start things off, peruse the extensive charcuterie selection before tucking into boldly flavored and creatively plated dishes. Layered like a tower, the grilled lamb shoulder over a bed of creamy lentils surprises with every bite. Choucroute garni's rich beefy flavor is cut by the creaminess of the sauerkraut purée. Out-of-the box ideas keep coming through to dessert, where a scoop of pretzel ice cream atop a jalapeño caramel is equal parts spicy and sweet.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3852;Frontera Grill;USA;Chicago;445 N. Clark St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.890567;-87.630914;78;false;false;Mexican;This linchpin in Rick Bayless’ empire is decidedly unique in its homage to regional Mexican cuisine and displays a cult-like devotion to local product. From the table-shaken margaritas and the molés to the warm, uplifting music, you'll likely feel you're in Mexico. The ever-changing menu is cohesive, highlighting everything from the ceviches of Baja to the moles of Oaxaca. Begin with the sopa azteca—a nourishing pasilla chile broth poured atop tortilla strips, avocado, grilled chicken and jack cheese. A version of the classic from Morelia, enchiladas a la plaza are first flash-fried, then folded over seasoned cabbage, potatoes and carrots. Pair this with a side of spinach in green chile and you won’t be unhappy.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3853;Pleasant House Pub;USA;Chicago;2119 S. Halstead St., Chicago, 60608, USA;41.8535715;-87.6464616;32;true;true;Gastropub, English;Classic English pies may be the specialty of this house, but don’t let that inspire visions of chintz and tea cozies—the interior here is decidedly modern, with marble-topped tables and hand-crafted pottery.But the crowds come for the pies, and for good reason—they’re fabulous. The crust is flaky and buttery, and the inside, hearty and satisfying. Dig into the steak and ale, with its beef stew filling and side of minty peas, gravy and mashed potatoes, and you’ll be hunting for every last crumb. The comfort food hits also keep on coming, from rarebit mac and cheese with Trooper Ale cheese sauce, to fish and chips on Fridays. Of course, with much of the seasonal greens from local farms, rest assured that even a simple salad will be a revelation.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3855;Sol de Mexico;USA;Chicago;3018 N. Cicero Ave., Chicago, 60641, USA;41.93575;-87.74698;64;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Far more authentic than the average chips-and-salsa joint, Sol de Mexico brightens the scene and palate with a lively atmosphere (cue the mariachi music) and delectable house specialties. Walls painted in tropical pinks, blues and oranges are a cheerful canvas for Dia de los Muertos artifacts. To sample the kitchen’s skill, start with sopes surtidos “xilonen”—four molded masa cups with a variety of fillings like caramelized plantains doused in sour cream, or tender black beans topped with crumbly house-made chorizo. Then, move on to the pollo en mole manchamanteles, which translates to “tablecloth stainer.” Rich and slightly bitter with a comforting nuttiness, the aptly named mahogany sauce begs to be sopped up with freshly made tortillas.;Air conditioning;[]
3856;Ciccio Mio;USA;Chicago;226 W. Kinzie St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.8892692;-87.6353304;83;true;true;Italian, American;The Hogsalt restaurant group isn’t known for restraint and this is certainly true of its latest venture—a saucy, Italian-American looker that goes full-speed ahead in its charming, throwback setting, with bold flavors and hearty portions.Pastas are made in-house, and first timers will want to sample the lasagna Bolognese rotolo, a creative riff on the classic and far lighter than it sounds. Chicken Parmesan is another favorite, but groups should also consider the vesuvio, a Chicago preparation that promises a juicy half-chicken with crisped skin and a moat of impossibly crispy potato wedges in white wine sauce. Stuffed? There must be dessert, especially that towering swirl of fior di latte gelato dusted in fennel pollen and drizzled with chestnut honey.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3857;Superkhana International;USA;Chicago;3059 W. Diversey Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9320109;-87.704885;44;false;true;Indian, Fusion;After five years of pop-ups and multiple kitchen pivots, this friendly restaurant has managed to stay both flexible and fun, which is also how we’d describe the cooking. Indian flavors are mixed and mashed in traditional and unconventional ways, as apparent in naan—a prominent menu fixture—topped with salted jalapeños and mozzarella, or reimagined as a calzone stuffed with butter chicken, brushed with ghee and finished with Maldon salt. It’s not all bread—fiery Kerala crab curry with flaky parotta and a vibrant chana chaat with tamarind and spice are equally impressive.A take-out window offering playful sandwiches during lunchtime is a boon for pedestrians. Exposed white brick, a long handsome bar and smooth warehouse floors make for an airy vibe.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
3858;Ghin Khao;USA;Chicago;2128 W. Cermak Rd., Chicago, 60608, USA;41.8522328;-87.6792863;25;false;true;Thai;The name is Thai for “eat rice,” and you’ll want plenty of it to mop up every last bite of this kitchen's perfectly spicy, salty, sweet and tangy Northern Thai dishes. Operated by chef siblings, Nova and Kami Sasi, this is a fun, lively spot, with graffiti-like signage, hip-hop in the background, and colorful murals bedecking the walls. Every item is perfectly balanced, from the crunchy and subtly spiced fishcakes with cucumber-herb salad to the glorious nam khao tod, featuring crispy rice with ground chicken, pork skin, plenty of fresh ginger, cilantro and green onion.As a bonus, it’s also BYOB, so bring along a crew of friends with a couple of six-packs, and you'll be able to conquer most of the small menu—along with a few specials listed on the board.;Air conditioning;[]
3861;Lula Cafe;USA;Chicago;2537 N. Kedzie Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9278163;-87.7067933;97;false;true;American;This neighborhood gem is just as it’s always been and regardless of whether you're squeezed into the main dining room with friends or seated solo at the spacious bar in the adjacent space, the charm of this mainstay endures. The evolving menu focuses on fresh, seasonal, and original fare, keeping it slammed from morning to night.Barbecued wedges of spaghetti squash topped with Asian pear, daikon, and sesame is impossible not to finish. Nicely grilled steaks are accompanied by a tangle of blistered long beans brushed in a house XO sauce with deliciously chewy bits of dried seafood for maximum flavor. Finish over a tall slice of double-layered carrot cake, complete with crème anglaise and a luxurious spoonful of strawberry preserves.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
3862;Gilt Bar;USA;Chicago;230 W. Kinzie St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.889297;-87.6352819;84;true;true;Gastropub;Doughnuts, dry-aged steaks, and house-made pastas—Hogsalt Hospitality certainly has the lockdown on this corner of River North, but it all started in 2010 with this moody and imposing retreat. The bar up front mixes cocktails to a metronomic rhythm, while the back feels more intimate with studded leather banquettes and nostalgic lighting.True to form, the restaurant excels at big plates and bold flavors. We're hooked on the fried chicken that arrives with a golden-brown crust and rich mashed potatoes. But, who then will order the beef cheek pot pie with bone marrow gravy? You won’t have room for dessert, but order it anyway. A towering slice of carrot cake with spiced cream cheese frosting and toasted coconut counts as a vegetable anyway, right?;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3863;Cellar Door Provisions;USA;Chicago;3025 W. Diversey Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9320843;-87.7034921;45;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Some restaurants try very hard to impress and dazzle their customers. This sunny corner of Logan Square is not one of those places. In a recently refreshed, breezy dining room, Cellar Door Provisions is perfectly content with itself. And why shouldn’t it be? This is an honest restaurant with unfussy, no-nonsense cooking where the seasoning is spot-on and the flavors are clear. No tweezers, no fancy wine glasses, no military-grade kitchen brigade— just good eats, found in a plate of tender runner beans with garlic confit or a smooth scoop of duck liver mousse paired with just-warmed country bread. You could come here on a quiet date or wander in off the street and snag a counter seat. You’ll be happily greeted either way.;Air conditioning;[]
3864;Lardon;USA;Chicago;2200 California Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9218579;-87.6975363;53;false;true;Deli, Italian;The name was your first clue. The cutout of a pig hanging over the door was your second. Specializing in whole hog, snout to tail butchery, this all-day salumeria offers a dazzling selection of charcuterie arranged on wooden boards or layered on soft deli bread. Such craftsmanship is in full view of the dining room, which includes a curing chamber filled with rows of soppressata, finocchiona, and Spanish chorizo. Truffled lardo with rosemary is a must. Need a vegetable? Try the salad with broccolini and zucchini tossed in a tarragon-green goddess dressing.The historic building, with its honeycomb tiled floors and original wood joists, offers a charming old-world vibe. Weekend dinner strikes closer to a bistro with steak frites and duck leg confit.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3865;Birrieria Zaragoza;USA;Chicago;4852 S. Pulaski Rd., Chicago, 60632, USA;41.8050361;-87.723342;45;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;This Mexican institution specializes in a single item—birria—tender, stewed goat accompanied by diced onions, cilantro, and house-made salsa. In fact, goat is all that’s on the menu, though you’ll get a few options as to how to enjoy it: on a plate or in a bowl, in a small or large portion, bone-in or bone-out. Opt for bone-in if possible, as it packs far more flavor. The bowl option drowns the goat in a generous dose of hearty goat consommé, while the plate is accompanied by handmade corn tortillas for build-your-own tacos, with a small side of consommé for dipping. You can’t go wrong either way, but if you’re feeling extra decadent, go for the goat quesadilla, a perfect trinity of pillowy tortillas, gooey cheese, and savory goat meat goodness.;Air conditioning;[]
3866;Union;USA;Chicago;2202 N. California Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9219995;-87.6975894;59;false;true;American, Gastropub;Building on the success of next-door Lardon, the same team now aims to capture the dinner crowd with this handsome gastropub. Edison bulbs cast a warm glow across the dark wood, long high tops and cozy booths, and regulars are likely to hold court at the bar. The menu, meanwhile, balances comfort with creativity. The spicy baby gem is peak salad satisfaction, built on a creamy tarragon dressing and finished with buttery breadcrumbs. Fried cheese curds and lamb meatballs are easy crowd-pleasers, and every table has at least one cheeseburger. More substantial appetites should swing for the shawarma spiced chicken served with grilled flatbread. There’s plenty to drink, and craft beer fiends will dig the thoughtful, locally sourced selection.;Air conditioning;[]
3867;Virtue;USA;Chicago;1462 E. 53rd St., Chicago, 60615, USA;41.7996257;-87.589292;41;true;false;Southern, Regional Cuisine;Occupying a corner of Hyde Park within view of the University of Chicago, this is an inviting retreat with a welcoming bar, striking dining room, and buzzy kitchen helmed by the very talented Erick Williams. His well-executed Southern cooking draws a smart crowd, largely from the university nearby.For starters, imagine skillet corn bread with a steak knife for slicing and slathering on the honey butter, while dirty rice topped with chicken gizzards is just what the soul ordered. Don’t miss the butcher’s snack, a selection of house-made charcuterie with pepper jelly. Southerners seek out the Geechie Boy grits with white cheddar for a stone-ground taste of home, but ganache-filled chocolate cake with Bourbon cherries will have dessert fans back in no time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
3868;The Duck Inn;USA;Chicago;2701 S. Eleanor St., Chicago, 60608, USA;41.8446456;-87.6601691;70;true;false;Gastropub, American Contemporary;Head to the Bridgeport warehouses, where this stylish, modern tavern—helmed by Executive Chef Kevin Hickey—feels like a diamond in the rough. Then make your way past the buzzy bar (pouring heady cocktails) to a semi-open kitchen, which is in full view of the decorous dining room, featuring wood tables and mid-century modern seats.The cuisine may be coined as "working-class fine dining," but there is nothing lowbrow about this menu, which unveils a focused but diverse selection of small plates and mains. Japanese barbecue sauce and sesame seeds are the crowning touch to duck wings, while foie gras mousse with celery fronds and brioche is a study in fine flavors and textures. Of course, regulars know to save room for the Chicago-style duck fat dog.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3870;Daisies;USA;Chicago;2375 Milwaukee Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9242037;-87.6988684;55;false;false;Italian;With the flick of a switch, Logan Square’s beloved pasta restaurant has found a new home just down Milwaukee Avenue. The move is a serious upgrade into a space nearly four times its original footprint. Flooded with sunlight, fitted with a comfortable bar and sporting a private dining room, the restaurant has no shortage of space. And much to everyone’s delight, house-made pastas like pappardelle with mushroom ragu or rigatoni with pork ragu and fermented tomato remain prime attractions. Onion dip with house-made ruffles is still on the menu and still a must-order. A bakery in the back gives this team even more room to play with sweets, and diners can choose between a dazzling selection of pastries, ice creams and sorbet at the meal’s end.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
3872;Agora Pansiyon;Türkiye;Milas;Kapıkırı Köyü, Kapıkırı, Milas, 48234, Türkiye;37.5014068;27.5262707;57;false;true;Turkish, Traditional Cuisine;The area around Lake Bafa is popular on account of its ruins and unusual hiking trails. Be sure to include in your itinerary this little guesthouse, somewhat tucked away in the greenery (just be warned that the paths that lead here can get surprisingly narrow). The splendour of the setting is complemented by the hostess in her generous culinary offerings. Vegetables from her own farm, fish from the lake, beef from neighbouring farmers: she works with top-quality produce. She serves down-to-earth dishes such as barbecued sea bass with onion, tomato, pepper and wintercress. Fried aubergine really comes into its own in a yoghurt salad with a fiery chilli dressing. At Agora Panisyon, the heartwarming fare lets the ingredients speak for themselves.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3873;Aslında Meyhane;Türkiye;Izmir;Yeni Mahallesi, Dere Sokak No:26/A, Urla, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.3215929;26.7667479;82;true;false;Turkish;Hostess Aslıhan's friendly smile and warm welcome will make you feel right at home in this quintessentially Anatolian stone house. The restaurant's historical charm is complemented by the Mediterranean feel of the courtyard terrace. The extensive menu primarily features hot and cold appetisers with a traditional Turkish twist. Think fish soup with freshly caught sea bream, prawns and squid. Or perhaps a succulent kokoreç served with hummus, and a velvety fava bean purée seasoned with lemon and dill… These dishes brimming with flavour are perfect for sharing with friends in a casual setting.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3874;Beynel;Türkiye;Bodrum;Adliye Caddesi No:63, Bitez, Bodrum, 48470, Türkiye;37.040232;27.3774276;22;true;true;Turkish;Take a seat on the terrace of this open-air restaurant, among the mandarin and lemon trees, and prepare yourself for some Anatolian generosity. The mezze- and kebab-style dishes are perfect for sharing with friends or for a romantic dinner for two. Tempting options on the menu include roasted aubergine stuffed with meat seasoned with paprika and a yoghurt dressing, and flatbread with a lamb brochette, lamb pastrami, Golot cheese and an onion salad with sumac and fresh herbs. Discover a world of rich flavours that won't break the bank!;Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3875;Araf İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;AG/E İç Kapı, 19 Mayıs Mahallesi Sümer Sokak Sümko N Blok No:1, No:2, Kadıköy, Istanbul, 34742, Türkiye;40.97826;29.09325;40;true;true;Contemporary, Turkish;Kenan and Pınar Çetinkaya are your cordial hosts at this cosy restaurant, where seating is limited. A spot at the dining counter is best if you want to watch how the chefs expertly tame the open fire. The dishes bring out the core essence of their main ingredient, and their apparent simplicity belies their depth of flavour. The kitchen team conjure up a vegetarian creation centred on beetroot just as deftly as they prepare offal. For instance, they fry the lamb brains twice to achieve a crispy crust and soft interior. A sweet fermented chilli paste, aioli and yuzu sauce, and pickled onion provide a delicately sour counterbalance. Thanks to the small portions, you can explore the enticing menu thoroughly.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3876;Karaköy Lokantası;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kemankeş Mahallesi, Kemankeş Caddesi No:57, Karaköy/Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34425, Türkiye;41.0246399;28.9800505;18;true;true;Turkish;Intensely flavoursome tarama with toasted bread, crispy deep-fried courgette with yoghurt, sea bass elevated by a spicy mustard-based remoulade… With a selection of over 80 mezze, a whole host of sharing platters and other traditional dishes, you're spoilt for choice. The chef uses top-quality ingredients and avoids unnecessary complexity. His dishes pack a punch, with subtle Greek influences appearing throughout. This bustling establishment with its quiet terrace has earned its popularity. Delicious food and great value for money!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3877;Cuma;Türkiye;Istanbul;Firuzağa Mahallesi, Çukur Cuma Caddesi No:53/A, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34425, Türkiye;41.0321658;28.9809849;51;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A stroll through the trendy Çukurcuma neighbourhood, which is famous for its antique shops, should certainly include a meal at Cuma. At this cosy establishment – be sure to secure a spot on the front terrace – you can tuck into a traditional Turkish breakfast or Mediterranean-style lunch or dinner. Seasonal ingredients are showcased brilliantly in tapas such as sea bass ceviche, generously topped pizzettas, aromatic pasta dishes etc. The chef places special emphasis on vegetarian dishes, such as mushroom skewers and halloumi cheese with braised onion, pomegranate and deep-fried polenta. Everyone is sure to find something to their liking here, and at great value for money!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3878;Tavacı Recep Usta Bostancı;Türkiye;Istanbul;Altintepe, Bağdat Caddesi, No:6, Maltepe, Istanbul, 34840, Türkiye;40.952438;29.0972595;82;false;false;Turkish;This spacious restaurant specialises in lamb and mezze. It is here that traditional Turkish cuisine unfolds in all its generosity. It is such a pleasure to feast on dishes like dolması stuffed with minced lamb, tomato and rice, or the delicious grilled aubergine and pepper with juicy minced lamb. No pretension, just pleasingly robust flavours. The numerous photographs of the celebrities who have dined here are proof that this place has been a crowd pleaser for over 40 years.;Air conditioning;[]
3879;Aida - vino e cucina;Türkiye;Istanbul;Caferağa Mahallesi, Ressam Şeref Akdik Sokak No:10, Kadıköy, Istanbul, 34710, Türkiye;40.9855496;29.0255323;85;false;true;Italian;The lively atmosphere of the coastal district of Moda is taken up a notch in this bustling restaurant spread over three floors. As the name suggests, it brings you a taste of Italy. The dishes served here are not unnecessarily complicated, but they have that je-ne-sais-quoi that makes Italian cuisine so beloved. The menu includes mouthwatering options, such homemade salsiccia made with succulent lamb, salty pecorino cheese and pancetta with a celery puree, as well as an original take on vitello tonnato. Rest assured: at Aida Vino e Cucina you can relish delicious food without breaking the bank.;Air conditioning;[]
3880;Asma Yaprağı;Türkiye;Izmir;Ovacık, Kerimoğlu Mevkii, 7152. Sokak, No:143/1, Çeşme, Izmir, 35937, Türkiye;38.2745103;26.3626264;100;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;With its bohemian-style garden where you can dine amid herbs and vegetables, the centrally positioned building draped in grapevines, and the authentic handmade porcelain, this restaurant has a distinct character. Inside, all kinds of fragrant delights are on display, ready for you to select. Freshly baked pumpkin pie with yoghurt, fried courgette flower with ricotta and fresh herbs, or traditional manti stuffed with yoghurt and chilli oil – these generous sharing dishes are simply irresistible! Grown on site, the produce is second to none. That, in combination with the female chefs' home-style cooking, is what sets this place apart. Reservations are required for evening dining – no children allowed.;Car park,Terrace;[]
3881;İki Sandal;Türkiye;Bodrum;Kumbahçe Mahallesi, Cumhuriyet Caddesi No:183-1, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.030888;27.4387976;15;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;It's impossible to pass by this charming meyhane, a traditional tavern, where the conviviality is infectious. The wide range of cold and hot mezze on offer is based on recipes that are sometimes centuries old. Think sea bass steeped in herbs and spices in an earthenware pot for 10 days, or subtly spicy dolmasi stuffed with lentils. And then there is the intensely flavoursome lamb that melts in the mouth… Watch out, or you will end up ordering everything on the menu!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3882;SADE Beş Denizler Mutfağı;Türkiye;Istanbul;Teşvikiye Mahallesi, Akkavak Sokak No:36, Şişli, Istanbul, 34365, Türkiye;41.0520411;28.9922775;27;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The never-ending hustle and bustle of the lively Nişantaşı neighbourhood is what characterises this cosy establishment. Locals and international diners come here for either a quick bite or a substantial dinner with friends. Genuine Turkish hospitality and great value for money are the biggest draws of SADE Beş Denizler Mutfağı. Anatolian delicacies such as spicy beef tongue salad with chilli and manti (Turkish ravioli) served with potato, kokoretsi meat and yoghurt are celebrated here with the generosity you would expect. No fuss, just rich flavours you won't be able to get enough of.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3883;Foxy Nişantaşı;Türkiye;Istanbul;Harbiye, Mim Kemal Öke Caddesi No:1/D, Şişli, Istanbul, 34365, Türkiye;41.05043;28.9901;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;"Foxy" refers to the musty flavour of the Concord grape, but you may also take it as a description of this laid-back establishment. Indeed, chef Maksut Aşkar of the MICHELIN-starred Neolokal and wine specialist Levon Bağış have appointed a team here that understands their philosophy. Here, you can sip wonderful Turkish wines – from natural wines to classic appellations – and savour a fresh, modern and sophisticated take on local classics. For instance, a fresh sea bass tartare, cut à la minute, is combined with a tangy mayonnaise, croutons, grated bottarga, paprika, and subtly smoked beetroot. Prepare yourself for an explosion of flavours! Keep in mind that the menu is more extensive in the evening than at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3884;Ayşa Boşnak Börekçisi;Türkiye;Izmir;Anafartalar Caddesi Abacıoğlu Hanı No:228 Z15, Kemeraltı/Konak, Izmir, 35250, Türkiye;38.4186037;27.1345781;20;false;false;Turkish, Traditional Cuisine;Kemeralti, a maze of streets with a picturesque square, is the heart of Izmir. Aysa, a restaurant full of character, is right at home in this idyllic location. The cold and hot buffet offers a wealth of Bosnian and Ottoman delicacies that you can load up on to your heart's content. For instance, you might start with marinated grape leaves stuffed with a delicious filling of rice and various spices, continue with some lamb stew and finish with some wonderfully moist baklava. NB: Reservations are not accepted, so be sure to arrive in good time!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3885;Arka Ristorante Pizzeria;Türkiye;Bodrum;Çarşı, Cumhuriyet Caddesi No:102, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0329667;27.4355873;63;true;false;Italian, Pizza;With its red-and-white check tablecloths, photographs and paintings from Italy, vintage decor and a terrace overlooking the pebble beach, this trattoria is the embodiment of Mediterranean charm. The menu features an extensive range of tempting traditional dishes. The Neapolitan-style pizzas and creamy risotto with super-fresh seafood are especially popular. There are also 12 different dishes with house-made pasta to choose from. This generosity is just one example of why Arka has been a Bodrum favourite for so long – and rightfully so!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
3886;Nazende Cadde;Türkiye;Istanbul;Caddebostan, Sembol apt, Caddebostan Plaj Yolu Sokak No:13/A, Kadıköy, Istanbul, 34728, Türkiye;40.9672532;29.0634692;81;true;false;Turkish;Head to the neighbourhood of upmarket Bağdat Avenue and experience the cosiness and friendly atmosphere of Nazende Cadde. This is a great place in which to share all kinds of delicacies with friends. The tempting menu changes daily to take advantage of the best market offerings, but the chefs also have a few signature dishes up their sleeves, including succulent barbecued squid rings with a fiery kick. They like working with offal, and spice up lamb liver, for example, with a judicious touch of chilli. This is a lively establishment where generosity comes from the heart.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
3888;Pandeli;Türkiye;Istanbul;Rüstempaşa Mahallesi, Balık Pazarı Kapısı Sokağı No:1/2, Mısır Çarşısı İçi 1 D:2, Eminönü/Fatih, Istanbul, 34116, Türkiye;41.0171904;28.9712697;73;true;true;Turkish, Traditional Cuisine;Take the stairs to the first floor above the Egyptian bazaar and marvel at the characteristically Turkish decor with its blue mosaics on the walls and its historical cachet. In addition to the main dining space, there are two more private rooms if you would prefer a more intimate setting. The chef resolutely sticks to traditional Turkish dishes: think fragrant dolmas stuffed with rice, berries, pine nuts and a dash of vinegar, or courgette flower filled with feta, deep-fried and paired with a rich and spicy yoghurt dip, to name but a few. This perennial favourite never disappoints!;Air conditioning;[]
3889;Hiç Lokanta;Türkiye;Izmir;Yeni Mahallesi, Zafer Caddesi No:52, Urla, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.3221752;26.7649481;89;true;true;Organic, Seasonal Cuisine;This trendy establishment housed in a former Greek theatre in the picturesque old town of Urla is all about sustainability. Respect for the environment is evident in every detail, from the wild-foraged ingredients used to the water conservation and waste management measures in place. The restaurant's freshly pressed olive oil is a highlight of its modern cuisine, which is full of personality. Acidity and spiciness are used to bring life to the dishes, as seen in a salad of wild herbs, berries, and a vinaigrette made from fermented beans and pollen. This is where nature's complexity comes alive!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
3890;EFENDY;Türkiye;Istanbul;Nisbetiye Caddesi No:13, Levent/Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34330, Türkiye;41.0761115;29.0196793;72;true;false;Turkish, Contemporary;Famed local chef Somer Sivrioğlu has assembled a talented team at Efendy, a vibrant restaurant with a warm Oriental ambiance. At this restaurant, traditional Anatolian cuisine is reimagined with a modern twist. Ancient techniques, such as cooking over an open fire, are combined with fresh ideas to create exciting dishes. The sea bass is cooked to perfection, with a crispy exterior and juicy interior. A fermented tomato jus adds a touch of sweetness and acidity, while lime and fennel add zing. A delightful juxtaposition of old and new!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3891;Tavacı Recep Usta;Türkiye;Izmir;Atatürk Caddesi No:364, Alsancak/Konak, Izmir, 35220, Türkiye;38.4406368;27.1425842;40;false;false;Turkish, Traditional Cuisine;As soon as you are seated in this warmly decorated restaurant with a striking modern conservatory, you are served some mezze. This gesture speaks volumes about the generous nature of your hosts. The traditional Turkish cuisine here is bursting with flavour. Try the lamb shoulder that is slowly cooked in the oven with spices, tomato and green pepper. Tea is always served with dessert, such as rich baklava. There is no way that you will still be hungry when you leave!;Terrace;[]
3892;Inari Omakase Kuruçeşme;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kuruçeşme Caddesi No:11, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34345, Türkiye;41.0600397;29.0363013;77;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Inari Omakase Kuruçeşme is a contemporary-style designer restaurant with two faces. In the afternoon, it is a quiet place in which to savour Japanese classics with a smattering of hip Californian influences. In the evenings it feels more like a nightclub, with louder music courtesy of live DJs. Either way, this is a popular destination where you can share mouth-watering creations, and delight in the, at times, surprising flavours and fine textures of nigiri, sashimi, tempura, teppanyaki and more. The fine balance between the fresh, sweet and spicy nuances of the deep-fried squid rings with lime zest, wasabi mayonnaise and chilli is simply irresistible!;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
3893;Tatbak;Türkiye;Istanbul;Valikonağı Caddesi, Akkavak Sokak No:38/B, Nişantaşı/Şişli, Istanbul, 34365, Türkiye;41.0519606;28.9924009;26;true;true;Turkish, Traditional Cuisine;Tatbak has been the go-to kebab place for many an Istanbulite since 1960, and at no point in that time has it compromised on quality. With its lovely stained-glass windows and marble finishings, the vintage-style decor is attractive, but the local vibe and fantastic value for money are the main draws. Take, for instance, the Gaziantep version of spicy lahmacun (Turkish pizza), generously topped with vegetables and parsley, or the kebab with lamb sausages and minced beef – both are house favourites. The experienced chef skilfully balances sweet, spicy and tangy nuances, without losing sight of the importance of the right textures. Tatbak is a mecca for foodies!;Air conditioning;[]
3894;Ali Ocakbaşı;Türkiye;Istanbul;Arap Camii Mahallesi, Tersane Caddesi, Kardeşim Sokak No:45 Kat 4, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34421, Türkiye;41.0225323;28.9728249;60;false;false;Turkish;A narrow street leads you to this somewhat hidden gem. The waterside setting is a draw in itself, but the main attractions are the barbecue and tandoori oven. With a sure hand, the chefs flame-grill aubergine, for example, and then season it with chilli and five-spice powder. Their marinated lamb and beef are cooked to juicy perfection, generously spiced and served with lavash bread that has been briefly crisped up on the barbecue. The various mezze, salads and desserts such as halva stay true to tradition. And for this price point, the value is fantastic!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3895;Adil Müftüoğlu;Türkiye;Izmir;Mithatpaşa Caddesi No:159, Balçova, Izmir, 35330, Türkiye;38.3939177;27.0498603;24;true;false;Turkish;This spacious family-run restaurant welcomed its first diners in 1955. Today, the third generation is at the helm of what has become a firm favourite for many locals, who flock to the large counter to choose their favourite mezze, soups and hot dishes. You can start with the lentil soup, follow that with some spicy spinach with yoghurt and fresh mint, and then finish off with a delicious sweet and creamy rice pudding. Since everything is made fresh here, you should be aware that once it's sold out, it's really gone.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3896;LA Mahzen;Türkiye;Izmir;Kuşçuburun Mahallesi, Başmimar Sinan Caddesi No:81, Yazıbaşı, Torbalı, Izmir, 35860, Türkiye;38.1997089;27.3127004;78;true;false;International;The Lucien Arkas vineyards are well worth a visit. Take some time to stroll among the vines. It's the perfect way to spend a romantic day with your loved one. The spacious and inviting restaurant overlooks the estate and is a real ambassador for the winery (bottles are for sale at the entrance). The chef's Mediterranean dishes are a feast for the senses, with their simple presentation and bold flavours that perfectly complement the quality wines produced here. Courgette flowers generously stuffed with cheese and herbs, creamy mushroom risotto… Here, the focus is on honest flavours, both in the glass and on the plate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3897;Otantik Ocakbaşı;Türkiye;Bodrum;Atatürk Caddesi No:46, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0341659;27.4351857;77;true;false;Grills, Turkish;The barbecue and wood-fired oven will catch your eye as soon as you enter this congenial establishment, which has a cosy terrace in the lane to the rear. The chef expertly tames the open fire to cook delicious dishes, such as kebab and grilled dry-aged steak. The mixed grill is a signature dish here: a variety of juicy meats, oven-fresh bread and a judicious sprinkle of sumac. This restaurant offers great value for the money, serving delicious food without pretensions.;Terrace;[]
3898;Beğendik Abi;Türkiye;Izmir;Tatar Cami Sokak No:12, Urla, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.3221081;26.7669666;65;false;true;Turkish;There is a rustic charm about this place that is reflected in its food. At the counter, there is an impressive selection of mezze and hot dishes that you can also order straight away. The restaurant pays homage to traditional Turkish cuisine. The soft-cooked aubergine filled with minced meat and peppers, covered with tomato sauce and a light potato mousseline, is a perfect example of this. Then there is the crispy baked puff pastry dessert with cottage cheese, caramel and hazelnuts. Here you are guaranteed a delicious and affordable dining experience.;Terrace;[]
3900;De Wen Xia Zai Mian;China Mainland;Quanzhou;149 Dong Street, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9146058;118.5894191;22;false;false;Noodles;A veteran chef hailing from Quanzhou opened this rustic noodle shop in 2022 selling only Hokkien hae mee, or Fujian-style prawn noodles. Bouncy noodles of medium thickness served in a broth simmered for seven hours with complex depth and flavours. Though the signature hae mee is a must, you can add your own personal touch with incredibly fresh and umami-laden seafood toppings such as baby lobster, prawn, crabmeat, squid or razor clams.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3901;Lao A Bo;China Mainland;Quanzhou;600-1 Chengbei Road, Fengze, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9233354;118.5806124;100;true;false;Fujian;For over 10 years, regulars have been flocking here to sample ingredients that are rarely found elsewhere. The owner used to be a food distributer and has always been picky about his seafood. Adventurous eaters may try wild-caught mudskippers braised with shallots and black beans for springy meat. Gigantic sea snails and swimmer crabs are also exceptional and can be paired with home-style staples like braised pork rice, tofu in sa cha sauce or blood curd soup.;Cash only;[]
3902;Zhong Ji Yan Shao Fan Ya;China Mainland;Quanzhou;91 Chongfu Road, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.920777;118.608358;64;true;false;Fujian;This local culinary landmark is famous for braised duck, which is cooked in dozens of claypots that exude heady aromas by the entrance. The most popular item is ginger duck in rice wine. Consider paying extra for the gizzards before they run out. If you don’t fancy duck, you can choose free-range chicken or Silkie chicken instead. Also try Minnan home-style dishes like stir-fried duck blood curd with chives, garlic and bell pepper.;Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3903;Yi Tong Lou;China Mainland;Fuzhou;Zone A, 2F, International Building, 210 Wusi Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.1000107;119.301345;90;false;true;Fujian;This restaurant, which doubles as an art gallery, is adorned in the owner’s art collection. In the kitchen, the young chef from Putian adds a new twist to Fujian fare. Large mactra clams, blanched in boiling chicken stock for 10 seconds by the table, impress with deep umami, perfect cooking and crisp texture. Traditional sliced conch in wine lees sauce is given a new spin, with the red vinasse exuding a unique fragrance.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3904;Zhang Lin A Shan Jiang Mu Ya;China Mainland;Quanzhou;65-6,7,8,9, Xinhua North Road, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9142945;118.5787673;98;true;true;Fujian;Founded in 1999 under a different name, it has ever been popular with local ginger duck fans. On the right side of the entrance, row upon row of claypots make quite a spectacle. Muscovy duck is slow-cooked in rice wine with ginger and other herbs for two hours to build irresistible aromas. The duck is tender and falls off the bone and the broth is gingery, but not spicy. The soft, chewy pork blood sticky rice cake is also recommended.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3905;Hall Thing (Licheng);China Mainland;Quanzhou;24 Gongjie Lane, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9154494;118.5916537;39;false;true;Fujian;Tucked away in an alley, the restaurant is rather hard to find, but look for the small courtyard under a big tree. It is the epitome of vintage and adorned in splendid antique pieces. The menu is also a picture of nostalgia. Yongchun taro noodle soup boasts creamy mashed taro in flavorsome broth. Stir-fried pork liver is cooked perfectly, both tender and crispy. Ask for a table in the courtyard on a sunny day.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3907;Jian Lai Fa;China Mainland;Quanzhou;104-106 Nanjun North Road, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9166117;118.5920053;22;false;true;Fujian;Jian Lai Fa started out as a snack stall back in 1984. Now in its third generation, it has grown into a restaurant that is spread over two storeys. The kitchen team strives to re-create authentic home-style Minnan cooking with a nostalgic tang. Their signature braised duck in rice wine with ginger and salt boasts tender meat that falls off the bone. Other star dishes include marine fish braised in soy and scallion and razor clam in peppered salt.;Cash only;[]
3908;Min Shi Fu;China Mainland;Fuzhou;2-3F, Block A, Xinhuafu Plaza, 173 Wusi Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.1017517;119.3017324;85;false;true;Fujian;Min Shi Fu is well known for its live seafood and local delicacies. There is no menu. Just pick your own ingredients from the live fish tank and ask the server to recommend the best ways to prepare them. In addition to live shrimps, crabs, bivalves and whelks, the signature oyster fritter is very popular and boasts plump oysters, aromatic scallion and crisply fried egg batter. Everything is cooked to order and showcases solid techniques.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3909;Chun Sheng;China Mainland;Quanzhou;125 Bei Huan Shuang Nei Road, Jinjiang, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.8104148;118.509791;18;false;false;Fujian;Away from the city centre, this joint serving home-style Fujian cooking has earned acclaim from locals for over two decades. Like its numerous counterparts, there isn’t a menu – just pick your seafood and meat from the fish tank and chiller, then ask the server for the best way to prepare them. With tender meat and rich aromas, ginger duck stew is a best-seller. Fried green lobster in peppered salt stands out with bouncy meat and crisp flavours.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
3910;Xingxian (Mawei);China Mainland;Fuzhou;66 Qingzhou Road, Mawei District, Fuzhou, China Mainland;25.9936836;119.4686792;41;false;true;Seafood;This is the first restaurant of the chain which opened its doors in 1995. Diners make their choice from live fish tanks, but the restaurant also offers a splendid lineup of traditional Fujian fare. Lychee pork, Fuzhou’s own sweet and sour pork, is half-fatty pork coated in starch, deep-fried till crispy, and tossed in a sweet and sour glaze. Puxian lor mee is prized for its wide range of toppings that deliver layers of flavours and textures.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3911;Ye Jia Hua Sheng Tang;China Mainland;Fuzhou;51 Shijing Lane, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.090573;119.307557;71;true;true;Small eats;This tiny shop in an alley has been around for decades. Without bells and whistles, it has earned a loyal following with its rustic traditional Fuzhou sweets. The concise menu stars a lineup of all-time favourites. Simmered in a claypot for nine hours, the peanut soup is a creamy and nutty delight. Taro paste pleasantly surprises with small chunks of starchy taro which adds to the texture. The lotus root cake and sweet sticky rice are also worth a try.;Cash only;[]
3912;Zhen Zhen Hai Li Jian;China Mainland;Xiamen;184 Xiahe Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4622845;118.0715569;27;false;false;Fujian;Zhen Zhen runs the whole place alone: she's the owner, server and chef. She's picky about seafood, having it delivered a few times daily to ensure freshness. The well-made dishes at bargain prices have secured a loyal fan base. The menu comprises 20 items, mostly small plates, such as braised pork rice, and shrimp ball soup. Her oyster omelette is packed with plump oysters and garlic sprouts.;Cash only;[]
3913;Lu Niang Zi (Huli);China Mainland;Xiamen;161 Jiangtou West Road, Huli, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.5002675;118.1243853;66;true;true;Noodles;This simple shop is famous for beef noodle soup and noodles dressed in beef ragout. The signature beef noodle soup with pickled cabbage is a must – the beef long loin is perfectly cooked to be tender but firm. The beef bone stock is flavoursome, and the pickle cuts through the richness. The red-braised beef noodle soup, and the marinated meat platter with dried tofu, hard-boiled eggs, beef tripe, intestine and shin are also popular.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3914;Yue Hua Sha Cha Mian;China Mainland;Xiamen;78 Zhenbang Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4581397;118.0716689;20;true;true;Noodles;This noodle shop has been around for more than 40 years. What it lacks in space and grandeur, it makes up for in good food. Besides the secret sha cha broth bursting with a deep peanut flavour, diners also appreciate the dazzling and almost infinite array of toppings – pork intestine, pork bladder, dried tofu, fish balls, duck blood curd, pork liver, lean pork... Pair the noodles with roast pork sticky rice dumpling for a truly filling meal.;Cash only;[]
3915;Hao Shi Lai;China Mainland;Xiamen;24 Hubin South Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4766955;118.1070031;44;true;false;Seafood;Into the second generation, this family business founded in 1993 features in many Xiamenians' childhood memories. It prides itself on Minnan cooking, especially fresh seafood dishes. The threadfin blanched in claypot has oily, silky flesh and remarkable umami. The deep-fried baby eels in peppered salt are crispy and flavoursome, the mildly spicy kick making them a perfect companion for alcoholic drinks. The friendly service is a plus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3916;Mei Ya Bo Hua Sheng Tang;China Mainland;Fuzhou;182 Lao Yaozhou Street, Taijiang, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.063113;119.325778;44;true;false;Small eats;In 1937, Grandpa Chen started hawking his sweet peanut soup with a bamboo pole on his shoulder. Today, his grandchildren make the rustic sweets just as he did, but serve them in a neat cosy room at affordable prices. The peanut soup tastes divine, hot or chilled, as melt-in-the-mouth peanuts impart a lingering nuttiness. Taro paste is also well crafted and sports a velvety texture and robust flavour. The toasted sesame topping is to die for…;Cash only;[]
3917;Hou Jie Lao Hua (Yadao Lane);China Mainland;Fuzhou;95 Yadao Lane, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.089459;119.299767;44;true;false;Noodles;Close to scenic spots, this simple shop attracts locals and tourists alike. As its sign says, lao hua, or rice vermicelli in pork broth, is the signature dish. But their hand-pulled noodles and ribbon rice noodles are equally good. For toppings, opt for the classic combos, or customise your own: braised pork intestine and deep-fried dough stick deliver lovely textures and mop up the broth. Bone marrow dressed in scallion oil is also worth trying.;Cash only;[]
3918;Wu Lan Sha Cha Mian;China Mainland;Xiamen;300-1 Jiaotang Street, Zengcuoan, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.43331;118.131721;85;false;false;Noodles;Tucked away in a nondescript alley, this simple shop with its bright red wall can't be missed. Owner Wu Lan has been making sha cha noodles for decades, with a foothold on this spot for over 20 years. She makes her sweet, mildly spicy and deeply nutty broth every morning. Complemented by toppings such as pork liver, shrimps and even abalone, it is addictive! In addition to the sha cha noodles, try her golden and crispy oyster omelette.;Cash only;[]
3919;Z&D Cuisine;China Mainland;Xiamen;Shop 306, 3F, Building A, JFC Center, 1701 Island Ring East Boulevard, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4763301;118.1862835;99;true;false;Fujian;This restaurant focuses on the cuisine found in the catchment area of Jiulong River in the prefecture of Zhangzhou, Fujian. Most of the seafood is sourced from the estuary where it flows into the sea. Bittern tofu simmered with russula mushrooms, clams and dried squid comes in an umami-laden broth. Spicy swimming crab with grated ginger exudes spellbinding aromas. Don’t miss the handmade Xiang Pu cake made with mung bean flour.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3920;Xiao Cheng Xi;China Mainland;Xiamen;4F, Pacific Wharf, 3 Lujiang Avenue, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4521611;118.0729423;15;true;true;Fujian;By the pier, this roof-top dining room commands gorgeous views of Gulangyu. The owner chose to re-create the ancient Fujian-style architecture and landscaping in his stunning venue, complete with a water feature, lush greenery and stone arches. The menu is focused on Minnan fare, illustrated by deep-fried taro dumplings with pork filling. Salt-baked Japanese scad accentuates its oily, natural flavour. Don’t miss the puppet show at night.;Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3921;Lai Cuo Cheng Bian Shi Dian;China Mainland;Xiamen;8 Dayuan Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.462898;118.082851;18;false;true;Small eats;This place dates back to the 1940s, when the founder would carry her mobile kitchen on a bamboo pole balanced on her shoulder and sell her bianshi dumplings on the go. She then settled at this spot and has stayed put ever since. Now run by her son, it has built a loyal following for dumplings – handmade like in the old days. The signature has always been shrimp bianshi soup with springy noodles dressed in peanut and fermented tofu sauce.;Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3922;Panda's;China Mainland;Xiamen;170 Xiangdianli, Huli, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.506308;118.150739;46;false;false;Sichuan;This restaurant is set up in a Fujian red-brick mansion, with a black, white and wood colour scheme punctuated by pops of bright red. Both the owner and the chef are Sichuan natives, specialising in cuisine from the city of Zigong, famous for its salt industry. To ensure authenticity, most condiments are shipped from Sichuan. Try the chilli fish roes and fish maws with pickled cabbage and ginger, or diced rabbit hot pot in Sichuan pepper sauce.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Terrace;[]
3923;Wu Tang Sha Cha Mian;China Mainland;Xiamen;76 Minzu Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4459529;118.0795598;43;false;false;Noodles;With decades of history to its name, this noodle shop is always busy. There is just one thing on the menu – sha cha noodles – but over 20 different toppings to choose from: an array of seafood, including plump razor clams and creamy oysters, and pork offal – even pork heart and pork tripe – are solid options. Less garlicky than its counterparts, its broth is made from toasted, not fried, peanuts to accentuate nuttiness and umami.;Cash only;[]
3924;Chic 1699;China Mainland;Xiamen;3F, Building C, JFC Center, 1705 Island Ring East Boulevard, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.480781;118.198384;91;true;true;Fujian;This is the first flagship of a local restaurant chain. The faux-industrial decor works nicely with the greenery and ocean views. The menu is dominated by local seafood and Minnan dishes, depicted by shrimps in sa cha sauce that boast firm texture, mild heat and a deep nutty flavour. Also try Buddha jumps over the wall, crab roe stewed rice, Angus beef in mustard sauce or Chic’s very own sea perch thick soup with fish maw.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3925;Xian Xiong Qi;China Mainland;Xiamen;29 Houjiangdai Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4685441;118.0891371;22;true;false;Seafood;With live fish tanks lining the entrance, this is clearly the place to be for fresh seafood. The owner sources his fish directly from local fishermen, ensuring his catch is always the best. Minnan-style seafood defines the menu, and the peanut worm salad in a mustard dressing makes for an interesting start. The braised carpet shark belly and liver is another must-try: the liver is creamy, like tofu, and the belly has a fine, springy texture.;Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
3926;Luo Ji Mian Xian Hu;China Mainland;Quanzhou;56 Xianhou Road, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.919876;118.599812;90;true;true;Noodles;By the fading sign and vintage enamelware, it’s not hard to believe this noodle shop opened its doors 40 years ago. It focuses on mee sua gou – a wheat vermicelli soup of porridge consistency. Feel free to jazz it up with toppings like vinegar pork, pork intestine or oyster. Suck up the broth with a fried dough stick. Sautéed pork liver is another must-try: lightly coated in sweet potato starch, the liver has a burnt crust and a juicy centre.;Cash only;[]
3927;A Zhong Shi Fang;China Mainland;Xiamen;111-1 Jinbang Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.47026;118.10543;82;true;false;Fujian;What started out as a street stall over two decades ago has firmly established itself as a favourite dining spot among locals. There is no menu – you just browse the fish tanks and light boxes to see your options. Seafood is their strong suit, but so are authentic Minnan dishes. The a la plancha threadfin with Sichuan pepper sauce boasts umami heightened by aromatics. Try the stir fried pork liver with pickled bamboo shoot, too.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
3928;Cong Hui Tongan Lao Mei Shi Fan Dian;China Mainland;Xiamen;3-102 Dayuan Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4590723;118.0713265;36;true;false;Fujian;This is the third address of the household name since it opened in 1999. It has built a loyal following thanks to its authentic Tong'an home-style cooking. The flavoursome, melt-in-the-mouth Tong'an braised pork belly exudes aromas of garlic, dried shrimps, shiitake, chestnuts and lotus seeds. The pork kidney dressed in coriander sauce boasts a crisp, springy texture. You can order à la carte, or the set menus cater to your party size flexibly.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3929;Ming Yue Xia Mian (Xiahe Road);China Mainland;Xiamen;180-101 Xiahe Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4624612;118.0714178;59;true;false;Noodles;In the old town, this noodle shop with over 20 years of history is always bustling with diners who come for its prawn noodles. Hundreds of prawn heads are used to make the umami-laden broth with orange oil from the tomalley floating on top. Grated garlic adds depth and aromas. In addition to shelled prawns, the noodles are topped with prawn balls, lean pork, char siu, pork intestine and bean sprouts. The prawn ball soup is also popular.;Cash only;[]
3930;Minnan Minnan (Siming);China Mainland;Xiamen;Shop 328, 3F, The Mixc, 99 Hubin East Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4742868;118.1069936;81;true;false;Fujian;Opened by a restaurant group based in the city of Shishi some 30 years ago, this branch has stood the test of time. The kitchen team, trained in the Shishi flagship, is overseen by a Minnan master chef. The interesting menu includes a host of Minnan classics, plus regional small bites. Watch the chefs making the signature scallion buns behind a glass partition. The mackerel fish ball soup with pork tripe and pickled mustard greens is also a must-try.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3931;Shan Gu Tang;China Mainland;Xiamen;386-119 Xiahe Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4637124;118.0802235;98;true;true;Fujian;Its bright red sign may be hard to miss but it's the lingering herbal aromas that draw in customers from near and far. The owner used to run a Chinese clinic and opened Shan Gu Tang to serve food with medicinal value. The small menu is dominated by herbal soups, alongside blanched items, marinated meats and seasoned taro rice. Try the free-range chicken soup with russula mushrooms, or pork intestine soup with lotus seeds.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3934;Longkushan Eatery;China Mainland;Fuzhou;24 Xiyuan Road, Jin'an, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.129055;119.331887;21;false;true;Fujian;In business for over 10 years, this restaurant has become part of the collective food memory of Fuzhou citizens. Despite the remote location and lack of ambience, locals come in droves for well-made home-style dishes and seafood at wallet-friendly prices. The deep-fried Bombay duck in peppered salt seduces with velvety meat and a crispy crust. Drunken spare ribs in sweet and sour sauce feature layers of textures and subtle warmth from the spices.;Cash only;[]
3935;Zhuang Ji Quan Fu Lu Mian Guan;China Mainland;Quanzhou;59-3 Hua Lane, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9115597;118.5841251;26;true;false;Noodles;For over 40 years, this noodle shop has prided itself on its lor mee, or Fujian-style noodles in thick starchy gravy. In his 70s, the owner still helms the kitchen himself and cooks each order of lor mee in individual portions. You may have to wait for your order, but you won’t be disappointed. For toppings, choose from beef, pork liver, oysters or shrimp. Peanuts and garlic make the gravy nutty and aromatic. Made to order vinegar pork and fish roll are also worth trying.;Cash only;[]
3936;A Qiu Niu Pai (Huxin Street);China Mainland;Quanzhou;500 Huxin Street, Fengze, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.912016;118.611967;60;false;true;Fujian;The 40-plus-year-old shop has stayed true to its origins, boasting red wood furniture and old-school vibes. Niu Pai is the Chinese term for beef steak. Rather than being seared on a grill, here, it is braised with curry spices until it melts in texture. Veal from yellow cow boasts robust meaty flavours that work well with the complex, mild heat. With deep umami and faint herbal aromas, double-boiled oxtail soup impresses with a gelatinous texture.;;[]
3937;Jing Li;China Mainland;Fuzhou;3F, Sandi Union Center, Zhenwu Road, Taijiang, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.062379;119.292246;92;false;true;Fujian;Opened in 2020 as the premium version of a longstanding Fuzhou institution, Jing Li targets an upmarket business clientele. Burgundy seats and details grace the elegant wood-rich interior. On the menu, local Minnan classics are creatively melded with other cuisines. The dishes made with red yeast rice wine lees, such as the deep-fried wine lees-marinated eel, and longevity noodles with pork trotter braised in wine lees, are particular standouts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3938;A Xin Xian Lao (Gongnong Road);China Mainland;Fuzhou;9 Gongnong Road, Cangshan, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.048523;119.330674;72;false;true;Noodles;This no-frills shop is famous for lao hua, or Fujian-style noodle soup. First, pick your noodles from the 18 choices, then choose your toppings from dozens of options, ranging from offal and blood curd to oyster and squid. Made fresh daily, their MSG-free pork bone broth boasts depth and umami. Feel free to sprinkle scallion, coriander, pickles and fried garlic on top. Beef brisket fat dressed in a mildly spicy sauce is also a good choice.;Cash only;[]
3939;Homeme18" (Huming Road);China Mainland;Xiamen;24 Huming Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.480825;118.112445;50;false;false;Fujian;This restaurant is all about à la minute cooking, and diners get to witness the action in the glass-clad kitchen. Home-style Fujian dishes are their strong suit: the pork soup with whelks is loaded with umami and briny sweetness. The braised pork trotter with mashed Fuding taro boasts bouncy, flavoursome meat and creamy, starchy taro. All-you-can-eat steamed rice, and sweet potato congee are a nice touch. With only 10 tables, expect a wait.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3940;Wuwei Natural Food;China Mainland;Xiamen;290 Island Ring South Boulevard, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4303374;118.1133653;20;true;true;Vegetarian;Connected to a beachside promenade, this villa restaurant prides itself on its breathtaking ocean views, but also a Zen-inspired decor and plant-based cooking with a touch of finesse. It serves two set menus, both featuring season-driven dishes. Inspired by the Fujian classic Buddha Jumps Over the Wall, the rich and flavoursome Six-Treasure Soup is made with six different mushrooms. Ask for a table on the patio on a balmy night.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Valet parking;[]
3941;Si Xia Li (Huli);China Mainland;Xiamen;2F, Building B3, G Art Park, 566 Jinbian Road, Huli, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4939953;118.1628411;52;false;false;Fujian;The chef-owner has almost 30 years' experience under his belt, with notable stints in various hotel restaurants. Respecting traditions while re-inventing Minnan cuisine by incorporating Western techniques and creative touches, he has come up with a menu that is familiar and fresh at the same time. Try his oyster omelette, in which umami meets the crispness of water chestnut and celery. The slow-cooked pork belly with shiitake is another treat.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3942;Dai Tai;China Mainland;Xiamen;20 Jianye Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4792902;118.0794222;32;true;false;Yunnanese;Dai Tai opened its doors in 2011, specialising in Yunnanese home-style cooking, especially the cuisine of the Dai ethnic group. The all-Yunnanese kitchen team has most ingredients shipped from their home province to ensure authenticity. The food is mostly spicy, but diners can ask the chefs to tone it down. Try the Dai-style deep-fried pork skin starter – a crunchy, zesty treat. Follow up with fresh sweet bamboo shoots stir-fried with Yunnan ham.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
3943;Tong'an Fan Dian (Huachang Road);China Mainland;Xiamen;A103, Zone A, Southeast World, 125 Huachang Road, Huli, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.518481;118.10363;80;false;false;Fujian;Founded in 2003, this restaurant was named after Tongan, the cradle of Xiamen culture. The space is bright and airy, with a wall of oyster shell collage as a focal point. Formerly a fisherman, the owner is picky about his fish. Try the boneless giant mottled eel in claypot – the rich sauce complements the oily fish nicely. The quintessential Tongan classic of seared pork belly with dried oysters, chestnuts and shiitake is also recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
3944;Guan Zhong Wang Shi;China Mainland;Fuzhou;105, Building 4, Fujian Screen Culture Creative Industry Park, 81 Liuhe Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.083858;119.292947;23;true;false;Noodles;The owner from Xi’an couldn’t find any restaurant serving authentic cooking from his hometown, so he opened his own! The spartan room is clean and rustic. The kitchen team from Shaanxi deftly pull noodles by hand. The signature biangbiang noodle – there is only one long noodle in a bowl – is toothsome and expertly crafted. The aromatic spiced oil dressing clings nicely to the noodle, while cabbage, bean sprouts and chives provide crisp textures.;Cash only;[]
3945;Bai Jia Chun Hao De Lai Jiang Mu Ya (Zhongxing Road);China Mainland;Xiamen;40-102 Zhongxing Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4622404;118.0878365;56;false;true;Fujian;Ever since this neighbourhood joint opened its doors in 1996, there have only been four items on the menu – ginger duck stew, duck gizzards, blanched leafy greens and steamed rice. In the most famous restaurant for ginger duck in the whole of Xiamen, rows and rows of claypots containing local Muscovy duck and old ginger sizzle in rice wine and sesame oil, exuding addictive aromas. The duck gizzards tend to run out, so come early.;Cash only;[]
3946;Lucky Seafood;Thailand;Bangkok;28/1 Phran Nok-Phutthamonthon 4 Road, Bang Phrom, Taling Chan, Bangkok, 10170, Thailand;13.7535593;100.4557055;81;true;false;Seafood;This gem of a place serves fresh seafood with Thai flavours, featuring house-made curry and chilli paste. Order in advance or call to check availability. Try the stir-fried crab with bird's eye chilli or the non-spicy stir-fried squid with curry powder.;Cash only;[]
3947;Lung Shall Kitchen;Thailand;Chon Buri;50 Mu 7, Nongmaikean Road, Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.9588;100.89425;78;true;true;Thai;Simplicity and quality go hand in hand at this hidden gem with an intimate atmosphere. Experience food in its most authentic form thanks to skilfully prepared fresh ingredients. The bold yet nuanced stir-fried black squid ink delivers an intense, textured exploration of the sea's flavours.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
3948;Banmai Chay Nam;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;21 Koh Kaew Village, Mittraphap Road, Pak Chong, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30130, Thailand;14.6972011;101.410197;24;false;false;Thai;Transporting diners back in time, this nostalgic eatery overflows with vintage collectibles – navigate your way to your table past retro movie posters, trinkets and antique toys. The signature minced beef curry with fresh coconut milk proves a perfect complement to the crispy fried gourami fish. With over 20 years in business, Banmai Chay Nam draws crowds with its delicious food and scenic views of Khao Yai, especially during peak season.;Car park;[]
3949;Pa Pleung Mhee Kratok;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;1 Mu 8, Chok Chai, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30190, Thailand;14.79599;102.16396;99;false;false;Noodles;Locals flock to Auntie Pleung's for Korat's quintessential noodle dish, Pad Mhee Kratok, served in its purest form – with a soft yet chewy noodle texture that requires no additional seasoning. Her tiny district shop also whips up award-winning spins on Pad Thai and papaya salad.;Cash only;[]
3950;Dan Chicken Rice (San Sai);Thailand;Chiang Mai;45 Mu 3, Old San Sai Road, San Sai Noi, San Sai, Chiang Mai, 50210, Thailand;18.8218137;99.0332853;51;true;false;Small eats;For over 20 years this local favourite has been serving tasty, wallet-friendly chicken rice, first in Sam-Yaek Market in San Sai and now at this larger branch on Old San Sai Road. Show up early, both to beat the crowds and because the food invariably runs out before closing time.;Car park,Cash only;[]
3951;Som Tum Jinda;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;63/1-2 Phichit Rangsan Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.233483;104.8682332;60;false;true;Isan;Chef-owner Jinda is a specialist in somtum dishes. She first plied her trade back in 1974 in the local university before moving downtown. The Isan-style spicy fish maw with bamboo shoot salad has a nice balance of herbs and its powerful aroma is punctuated by the intensity of the Tiliacora juice. The signature, somtum with crispy catfish, dispenses an impressive tang. Somtum Jinda is also famous over the border in Lao where they have another branch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
3952;Nina's Cafe & Restaurant;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;59/1 Mu 6, Thanaratch Road, Nong Nam Daeng, Pak Chong, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30450, Thailand;14.6004974;101.3950463;89;false;true;Thai;Nina’s homely restaurant, surrounded by greenery, has two dining areas. The inside is decorated with vintage furniture, chandeliers, standing lamps and a classic clock, while diners in the garden can enjoy nature’s shade. The dishes are well seasoned and many of the vegetables and herbs Nina uses, such as betel leaves, coriander and basil, are grown on-site. The fried pumpkin coated with salted egg sauce and the deep-fried sea bass with chilli and salt are both divine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
3953;Pladids;Thailand;Chon Buri;60/57 Mu 4, Soi Marp Pra Chan Lang 1, Pattaya, Pong, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.9312838;100.9663345;28;false;true;Thai;This shop serves a Thai samrap (set menu) including jasmine rice cooked with Thai wild almond. The menu has a home-style, local quality, and interesting seasonal options. Each dish boasts complex yet balanced flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
3954;Janhom;Thailand;Bangkok;273/4 Soi Ramkhamhaeng 21, Ramkhamhaeng Road, Wang Thonglang, Bangkok, 10310, Thailand;13.7612406;100.6027874;60;false;false;Southern Thai;Aunty Paew has been serving intense southern Thai cuisine for over 20 years, using daily fresh ingredients to inform a changing menu. The chef makes her own curry paste, and signature dishes include Kaeng Tai Pla fish curry and stir-fried sataw beans with shrimp and aromatic shrimp paste. The deep-fried frog with turmeric is another standout. Chilled watermelon refreshes the palate after this fiery feast.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3955;La Voi;Thailand;Chon Buri;324/61 Chaiyaphruek Road, Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.8794101;100.892055;84;false;true;Small eats;The owner uses premium beef to prepare the broth and toppings. The clear and amber soup, which is cooked with beef for hours, is their secret sauce. For newcomers, it is highly recommended to start with the mixed beef soup, which comes with a variety of beef toppings, including meatballs, different cuts of beef, and beef organs, allowing diners to enjoy all the textures and flavours of beef.;;[]
3956;Khao Mun Gai Nha Jone;Thailand;Pathum Thani;119/239 Soi 17, Chumchon Ruansuk 1, Lam Phak Kut, Thanyaburi, Pathum Thani, 12110, Thailand;14.027787;100.774751;40;true;true;Small eats;There's a real buzz about this perpetually busy shop that is worth the drive from Bangkok. The delicious chicken is tender and juicy, served simply with sauces that add a real kick. Opening times are limited as they often sell out within a few hours – a testament to the quality.;Cash only;[]
3957;Naam Yoi;Thailand;Phuket;63/250 Ruam Phattana Road, Ratsada, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.880155;98.37997;54;true;false;Southern Thai;Going from steam-table hole-in-the-wall to a small cook-to-order eatery to a casual, tree-lined, open-air restaurant, Naam Yoi has cemented its identity as a solid family restaurant with a canon of tried-and-true dishes. Ingredients are obtained daily from local markets by the auntie of the family who is the head chef. Homestyle classics like river snail curry, spicy stir-fry of split gill mushrooms, and braised pork rule the roost here.;Car park,Cash only;[]
3959;Krua Kao Kuk;Thailand;Phuket;47/4 Phatthana Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8806503;98.3801618;24;true;false;Southern Thai;The legacy of the original roadside stall lives on, thanks to the owner's granddaughter. Famous for its boiled rice with fish, this humble restaurant also serves a variety of other home-style dishes that are worth trying. The quality is clear in these bold-flavoured plates. The deep-fried meatballs, made to a family recipe, are a great start to the meal and go well with the fresh fish menu, which is cooked in a traditional Phuket style.;Car park,Cash only;[]
3960;Kaeng Pa Loong Sa-Nga;Thailand;Nonthaburi;285/162-3 Soi Ngam Wong Wan 23 Lane 11, Bang Khen,  Mueang Nonthaburi, Nonthaburi, 11000, Thailand;13.8652189;100.5356793;86;false;false;Thai;Run by the same family for over 20 years, this restaurant is something of a hidden gem for spice-lovers. Their signature dish, jungle curry soup with hand-minced fish, provides suitably lip-smacking flavours using ingredients like red chilli, fingerroot and turkey berry. An outdoor area embraces nature, with curved tree trunk tables and an arboretum. Herbs and spices from the forest are used as seasoning, often with game meats – the succulent stir-fried deer with cumin leaves is a must.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3961;A Pong Mae Sunee;Thailand;Phuket;99 Soi Soon Uthit, Yaowarat Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8858698;98.3875385;41;false;false;Street Food;For over five years, Sunee’s street food stall has been renowned for its Khanom A Pong—delicious coconut crepes. Cooked in mini woks over charcoal, the crepes are unique for their light, crispy shell and soft centre—a perfect balance of sweetness and creamy coconut. Be sure to arrive early at this beloved stall to experience these irresistible snacks.;Cash only;[]
3962;Bunloet (Pom Prap Sattru Phai);Thailand;Bangkok;360 Soi Nakhon Sawan 8, Nakhon Sawan Road, Wat Sommanat, Pom Prap Sattru Phai, Bangkok, 10100, Thailand;13.7597232;100.5121971;56;true;false;Street Food;This enduring street food stall is renowned for its egg noodles with grilled pork, prepared using an unchanged recipe for over 40 years. The secret lies in marinating pork rump slices for four hours in a mix of soy sauce, sugar, salt, and pepper before grilling over charcoal. The well-cooked noodles have a soft, sticky texture, served in a flavourful pork bone broth.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
3963;Pa Lek Boat Noodles;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;Bang Lan Road (opposite to Maha That temple), Tha Wasukri, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3554715;100.5691202;61;false;false;Noodles;This third-generation family-run street food joint has been offering tasty boat noodles for over five decades. Their experience shines through in the delicious broth, well-balanced in flavours. Try their pork or beef boat noodles for great value, or consider the recommended dry tom yum-style egg noodles with pork. The friendly owners' hospitality attracts a bustling lunch crowd.;Cash only;[]
3964;Here Joi Beef Noodle;Thailand;Khon Kaen;127 Mu 20, Kasikon Thung Sang Road, Sila, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4586161;102.8444156;89;false;false;Noodles;Open for almost 4 decades, the shop is named after the owner's father, Joi, who created the menu. The beef noodle soup has juicy slices, tender beef balls and offal. The aromatic soup broth is slow-cooked daily with beef bones. The smoky beef satay skewers are chargrilled and juicy.;Cash only;[]
3965;Krua Apsorn (Dusit);Thailand;Bangkok;503-505 Sam Sen Road, Wachira Payaban, Dusit, Bangkok, 10300, Thailand;13.7742393;100.5064294;56;false;true;Thai;This family-run stall is inevitably a hit with anyone who eats here, including patrons such as the Thai royal family. The simplicity of the exterior belies the gem of a Thai kitchen hidden inside. Some dishes are unique and feature the family's secret recipes. The stir-fried pork with bird's-eye chilli is tender and bursting with herbal aromas. The signature yellow curry with large prawns and crispy lotus root strikes the perfect blend of sour, spicy and sweet.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3966;Baan Suan Lung Khai;Thailand;Ko Samui;4170, Taling Ngam, Ko Samui, 84140, Thailand;9.4293957;99.9485477;43;false;false;Seafood;Uncle Khai’s garden house, located on the chef-owner’s coconut plantation, is a labour of love. He sources seafood from his friends, local fishermen, and serves local and Southern Thai cuisine using the freshest ingredients of the day. Diners, who must book a day in advance, can enjoy fresh oysters and grilled seafood on the alfresco wooden-decked veranda with an open kitchen.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
3967;Pae Araya;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;Rim Khong Road, Khong Chiam, Ubon Ratchathani, 34220, Thailand;15.3191662;105.4998701;36;false;false;Thai;Where the Mekong and Mun Rivers meet, this floating restaurant, whose name means ‘noble raft,’ serves central Thai and Isan fare featuring fish from both rivers. The Tom Yum redtail catfish and local roe served with herbs are both flavourful and recommended. They and everything else on the menu come with cooling river breezes and gentle undulations from passing boats. Arrive early for dinner to catch sunset views over the river and the Laotian landscape beyond.;Car park,Cash only,Great view;[]
3968;Praprai;Thailand;Khon Kaen;345/1-2 Airport Road, Ban Pet, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.47292;102.78071;35;true;false;Isan;Arrivals and departures are better with a stopover at this simple restaurant in front of Khon Kaen Airport. For more than two decades, Prapai’s friendly owners have been serving authentic Isan dishes made with fresh local ingredients that change with the season. To experience traditional Isan cooking, try deep-fried sour fish or the off-menu Somtum in fermented fish sauce with salted crab.;Air conditioning;[]
3969;Jok Guay Jab Tom Sen Bat Queue;Thailand;Khon Kaen;123/20 Namueang Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4290596;102.8338556;95;false;true;Street Food;This eatery has been serving rice porridge, Vietnamese noodles with pork rib soup, and glass noodles with chicken feet for 30 years. Try adding chả lụa ham and soft-boiled egg for extra indulgence. Eat in to avoid the takeaway queue.;Cash only;[]
3970;So Jeng;Thailand;Khon Kaen;599/3-4 Mu 2, Chaeng Sanit Road, Nai Mueang, Ban Phai, Khon Kaen, 40110, Thailand;16.0578636;102.7356329;52;true;true;Isan;With more than 40 years of history, this eatery is now run by the second generation. Locals still frequent it for delicious, budget-friendly meals and cheerful service. The highlights here are the lap dishes and the spicy clear soup with beef and beef offal.;Cash only;[]
3972;Roti Chaofa;Thailand;Phuket;44 Chaofa Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8782532;98.3805976;99;false;false;Small eats;For over 35 years, the locals have flocked to Roti Chaofa for Thai-Muslim breakfasts, curries and Thai-style chicken biryani. The crisp, golden-brown rotis with a fluffy inner, are nicely salted and enjoyed with sweets or savouries. The tangy, juicy Beef Massaman curry is delightful.;Cash only;[]
3973;Por. Pochaya;Thailand;Bangkok;654-656 Wisut Kasat Road, Ban Phan Thom, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.7603746;100.5064441;100;false;false;Thai-Chinese;For over half a century, unwavering quality and rare dishes have kept loyal fans visiting this traditional Thai-Chinese spot, which is now run by the third generation of the same family. Among the top-sellers are crab omelette and stir-fried beef with cumin leaves. Crowds are to be expected, so make sure you book to avoid disappointment. It’s closed on weekends and holidays.;Cash only;[]
3974;Burapa;Thailand;Bangkok;26 Soi Sukhumvit 11, Khlong Toei Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7447602;100.5569288;72;false;false;Thai;This Orient Express-themed restaurant aims to take diners on a journey from east to north-east Thailand via flavoursome cooking that joins culinary elements from Isan and the province of Trat. The ground floor is designed to look like a luxury train bar – perfect for enjoying one of their many signature cocktails –  then the 1st and 2nd floors resemble the business and first-class carriages respectively. The well-priced dishes use recipes from the owner’s mother. Booking is essential.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
3975;Somsak Pu Ob (Charoen Rat);Thailand;Bangkok;199-205 Soi Charoen Rat 1, Khlong San, Bangkok, 10600, Thailand;13.7254396;100.495455;50;true;false;Street Food;This cart serves some of the best steamed crabs or prawns on glass noodles at wallet-friendly prices. Make sure you stir the noodles to soak up the tasty juices. It has a few branches, but this is where it all started. Come early or the wait will be long.;Cash only;[]
3976;Sum Gradang Nga;Thailand;Surat Thani;31/57-59 Soi Donnok 8/1, Donnok Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.135114;99.3249909;90;false;false;Southern Thai;Set in a charming house surrounded by ylang-ylang plants, Sum Gradang Nga is a hit with the locals for its Southern Thai cuisine bursting with gutsy flavours. Take the spicy pork cartilage with piquant seasoning, for example. Alternatively, the crab curry, which exudes umami, is served with vermicelli, fresh vegetables and a sweet-sour cucumber salad. Two dining areas: an alfresco space shaded by trees and a cool interior with a pastel pink décor.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3978;Nai Ho Chicken Rice;Thailand;Nakhon Pathom;88/14 Mu 4, Sisa Thong, Nakhon Chai Si, Nakhon Pathom, 73120, Thailand;13.8211801;100.1469208;91;false;false;Small eats;Singaporean chef, Ah Ho, cooks locally raised chickens using his family’s recipes. The chicken has a succulent meat, thin skin, light soya and sesame sauce, chicken broth and aromatic rice. The chicken offal sells out early every day. Don’t be surprised if the queue takes 1-2 hours.;Car park,Cash only;[]
3979;Ton Mayom;Thailand;Phuket;23/1 Mu 6, Thep Krasattri Road, Ratsada, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.9090367;98.3913607;75;true;true;Southern Thai;The Mayom (star gooseberry) is a local tree located at the front of this outlet that offers a shady setting. They serve fried local fish with an aromatic curry and Southern Thai sour curry soup with seabass and young coconut shoots. The signatures are delicious and a must-try.;Cash only;[]
3981;Jun Hom;Thailand;Ko Samui;8/3 Mu 5, Mae Nam, Ko Samui, 84330, Thailand;9.5798039;99.9559792;55;true;true;Seafood;This unpretentious, open-air eatery is a local gem on the island, offering an affordable opportunity to taste simple, local dishes in a knockout beach location. The portions are hearty, modestly priced and lip-smacking, as the salty, crispy appetiser of deep-fried local silver sillago illustrates. The stir-fried squid is tender and beautifully cooked in a sweet, flavourful sauce and steeped in a lemongrass aroma. Alfresco dining on a blissful beach location.;Car park,Cash only,Great view;[]
3982;Mok;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;115 Phrommarat Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2262786;104.8668296;19;false;true;Thai;Stepping into this two-storey house feels like visiting a friend's welcoming home, with a snug dining room and a plant-filled terrace. Adapted from grandma's Thai and Isan recipes, they offer a variety of menus suited for modern tastes. Don't miss the herb-infused seabass with fermented fish sauce and the unique fermented fish paired with pineapple relish and fresh veggies.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3984;Tang Jai Yang (Bang Kho Laem);Thailand;Bangkok;171 Chan Road, Wat Phraya Krai, Bang Kho Laem, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7097905;100.5118008;52;false;false;Thai-Chinese;Tang Jai Yang’s chef started cooking char siu, or Cantonese-style barbecue pork, for family and friends before selling it online. There, it went viral, so he opened this understated place. Since almost every dish on the menu contains the succulent pork, you can’t really go wrong.;Air conditioning;[]
3985;Krua Praya;Thailand;Phuket;216/19 Mu 3, Soi Hua Tha, Si Sunthon, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9748603;98.371085;77;false;true;Southern Thai;Krua Praya showcases Southern Thai, especially Phuket, cuisine. Its traditional décor and captivating rooftop charm visitors. The menu features skilfully prepared dishes with bold flavours and enticing aromas. The standout pork belly dishes include the signature fried pork belly with curry paste and young coconut shoots, delivering a crispy, spicy delight. Alternatively, the Phuket-style stew offers a rich non-spicy option, served in a satisfying gravy.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
3986;Watsana Khao Man Gai;Thailand;Bangkok;9/275 Phuttha Bucha Road, Bang Mot, Chom Thong, Bangkok, 10150, Thailand;13.6973372;100.471908;29;true;false;Street Food;Despite several moves from its original location, this shophouse has kept its customers so expect queues for its famous chicken rice and the recent addition of noodles. Quality ingredients and consistent cooking are the secret of its success.;Cash only;[]
3987;Rung Rueang Pork Noodle;Thailand;Bangkok;10/3 Soi Sukhumvit 26, Khlong Tan, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.728376;100.5704868;33;false;true;Noodles;Depending on your appetite, choose between a small or large portion of clear minced pork soup and perfectly flavoured tom yum broth. Each steaming bowl is topped with homemade fish balls and, if you so fancy, crispy fish skin. The minced pork balls are also a highlight.;Cash only;[]
3988;Khun Jaeng Guay Tiew Pak Mor Kao Wang;Thailand;Khon Kaen;246/4 Lang Mueang Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4248289;102.8365383;70;false;false;Thai;This shop peddles perfect rice dumplings and tapioca balls – a skill passed on by the chef's mother, who plied her trade in Bangkok for 30 years. The tangy tom yum soup with egg is a must and the garlic chive dumplings are exceptional.;Cash only;[]
3989;Somtum Khun Kan;Thailand;Bangkok;6 Soi Wachira Thammasatit 23, Sukhumvit 101/1 Road, Bang Chak, Phra Khanong, Bangkok, 10260, Thailand;13.685326;100.62123;51;true;true;Isan;Starting from a small shop in Mueang Thong Thani, and then winning a Som Tam (spicy papaya salad) competition in 1999, Khun Kan has earned his reputation through high quality dishes and great flavours. As well as the famous Som Tam, the menu offers a wide variety of mostly Isan dishes along with a few from other areas of Thailand. Try the juicy grilled pork shoulder with honey and herbs, followed by their signature sweet sticky rice with mango for dessert. Live music adds to the atmosphere on Friday-Sunday evenings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
3990;Baan Pu Karn;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;15 Mu 5, Wat Tum, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3919512;100.5297586;86;false;false;Thai;This simple eatery is set in the chef-owner's house. The mouthwatering Thai dishes are made from local ingredients and fresh seafood that’s hard to find in this province. This is good cooking and well-seasoned recipes with lovely herbal aromas and the natural umami of shrimps and crab meat. The kitchen sometimes closes early if dishes sell out, so it’s best to call ahead or arrive early. And booking a table at the weekend is a necessity.;Car park,Cash only;[]
3991;Kai Yang Saeng Thai;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;126 Ratchadamnoen Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9785233;102.0974843;29;true;false;Grills;At this rotisserie stall, they have spent over 50 years perfecting their signature dish of chicken (farmed or domestic) marinated in a secret peppery, herbal blend before it hits the spit. Juicy and tender, with a thin skin, the meat comes served with a sweet chilli dipping sauce.;Cash only;[]
3992;Ann Tha Din Daeng;Thailand;Bangkok;167 Tha Din Daeng Road, Khlong San, Bangkok, 10600, Thailand;13.7328153;100.5023067;79;false;true;Seafood;For over two decades, this restaurant has been serving seafood here in Little China Town, an area whose streets are lined by vendors. The array of mouthwatering dishes on offer captures local savour. The popular stir-fried prawn with salt and pepper boasts a blend of savoury and slightly salty flavours. The clams with sweet chilli paste and Thai basil is another standout dish – the paste adds a hint of sweetness that complements the Thai basil aroma perfectly.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
3993;Aunglo by Yangrak;Thailand;Bangkok;6/8, Decho Road, Suriyawong, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7265062;100.5251145;90;false;true;Thai contemporary;Aunglo presents modern Thai fare inspired by street food culture using an ancient Thai charcoal stove, or aunglo. Presented in a Japanese izakaya style, the counter bar faces an open kitchen with more seating upstairs, suitable for private or group dining. The menu is composed of small dishes, skewers and a few desserts. And the savoury dishes are mostly cooked on the charcoal flame, so a smoky aroma accompanies the intense Thai flavours, herbs and spices.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
3997;Krua Jay Sim;Thailand;Nakhon Pathom;98/17 Mu 2, Soi Khun Kaeo 12, Khun Kaeo, Nakhon Chai Si, Nakhon Pathom, 73120, Thailand;13.7768457;100.2161494;94;true;true;Thai;Four times in a decade, this Thai restaurant changed locations before finally opening on the chef-owner’s land in Nakhon Pathom. Each time, regulars followed along for its flavoursome local dishes, including some, like stir-fried sesbania with shrimp paste, that cannot be found elsewhere. The current digs are in an open-air pavilion on a country lane with tranquil lotus pond views. Try the stir-fried pork loin with jaew sauce and the spicy mackerel soup with madan fruit.;Car park,Cash only;[]
3998;Baan Pee Lek;Thailand;Bangkok;39 Chaloem Phrakiat Ratchakan Thi 9 Soi 9, Nong Bon, Prawet, Bangkok, 10250, Thailand;13.6814034;100.6545778;30;true;true;Thai;Step inside this Northern and Central Thai restaurant hidden on a side street in Prawet District and you enter a charming dining room adorned with an old-fashioned wooden European decor. Opening the menu reveals dishes, many of which are unavailable elsewhere, that honour the owners’ birthplaces, Chiang Mai and Bangkok. Highlights include stir-fried beef with Massaman curry, yum Luang Prabang and fried minced pork with salted mackerel.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
3999;Samuay & Sons;Thailand;Udon Thani;103/8 Si Chomchuen Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.4052353;102.7783308;30;true;true;Isan;After studying and working in San Francisco, brothers Num and Joe returned to Thailand to open a fine dining restaurant not in Bangkok, but in Udon Thani. Samuay & Sons serves a contemporary Isan tasting menu and great value à la carte dishes in a loft-style space. For the full experience, try the excellent seasonal tasting menu, which not only balances flavours but is also nutritionally balanced.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4000;Khanom Ochin;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;91 Jomsurangyat Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9731715;102.0944203;47;true;true;Street Food;Ochin is named after the owner's favourite Japanese film. This second-generation stall only serves takeaway – a range of homemade deep-fried buns presented on a trolley at the front. Their signature is the crispy bun which contains glass noodles, tasty seasoning and vegetables.;Cash only;[]
4001;Sriruen Pad Thai (Ruenchit Road);Thailand;Khon Kaen;48 Ruenchit Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen,, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.425305;102.8391818;52;false;false;Noodles;Chef Sriruen handcrafts exceptional Pad Thai, just as she has done for over 30 years. Originally from Phitsanulok, she serves noodles notable for their bold flavour, imparted by duck eggs. Savour this tasty dish with either thin rice or glass noodles.;Cash only;[]
4002;Roti Pa Day;Thailand;Chiang Mai;In front of Wat Mahawan, Thapae Road Soi 4, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.788065;98.9958975;74;true;true;Street Food;First-timers should order the plain crispy roti with condensed milk to start. The roti dough here is uniquely made without eggs, but slowly cooked to a crispy-chewy perfection in coconut oil. Choose from 20 toppings.;Cash only;[]
4003;Thai Tham;Thailand;Bangkok;28/1 Phraeng Phuthon Road, San Chao Pho Suea, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.751765;100.4967495;36;false;false;Small eats;This well-loved little shop has been passed down the generations for over a century. They specialise in offal, and their signature dish showcases stewed pig's brain, which is prepared fresh each morning by octogenarian owner Sudjit Suranan. Try the starter of Chinese liver sausage, too.;Cash only;[]
4004;Agave;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;153 Phalorangrit Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2305338;104.8646015;22;true;false;Vietnamese;The owner, an agave plant enthusiast, has adorned this cosy space with agave plants throughout. Vietnamese home cooking, enhanced with local Isan spices, fills the air, accompanied by instrumental music in the high-ceilinged room. All ingredients are homemade, offering a choice of pork or fish sausage for the namneung. Don't miss the standout sticky rice waffle served with sun-dried pork, infused with local Isan flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4005;Ruan Thai Kung Pao;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;1/2 Mu 4, Soi Thetsaban 10, Ratchakhram, Bang Sai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13290, Thailand;14.2006569;100.5119654;96;false;false;Thai;This riverside restaurant is a great place to stop for lunch after paying respects at Wat Choeng Len. Diners gather here for some of the finest fresh produce from the river, including grilled prawns and deep-fried sheatfish. The aromatic green curry with clown featherback fish balls is another highlight. Advance ordering of the huge river prawns – expertly cooked over charcoal – is highly recommended, as they are both popular and in limited supply.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4006;Prik-Yuak;Thailand;Bangkok;108 Pradiphat Road, Phaya Thai, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand;13.7916616;100.538568;47;false;true;Thai;Prik-Yuak has flourished for 30 years, starting in the bustling Chatuchak markets and now stationed in a spacious, inviting location. The restaurant maintains its beloved approach to home-style Thai cooking. Signature dishes like the Southern Thai pork belly and egg stew showcase tender meat, boiled eggs, and tofu. The venue charms with light, earth-toned decor, a serene garden, and includes a café and boutique shop to enhance the dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Garden or park;[]
4008;Prasit;Thailand;Khon Kaen;44/4 Ammart Road, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4343115;102.8333789;96;false;false;Isan;The inviting smell of charcoal-grilled sausages wafts from the kitchen at the front of this shophouse restaurant. This family-run business has been serving traditional Isan pork and beef dishes since 1972, in line with their motto: ‘using the best cuts of beef to create flavoursome Isan dishes.’ Dishes like their fried sun-dried beef slices, pork sausages and sliced beef shank in spicy and sour soup live up to the ideal, are reasonably priced and served with a smile. Don't forget to call and reserve the grilled beef tongue in advance.;Cash only;[]
4009;Lay Lao (Phaya Thai);Thailand;Bangkok;65 Soi Phahon Yothin 7, Phahon Yothin Road, Sam Sen Nai, Phaya Thai, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand;13.78172;100.54376;30;false;true;Isan, Thai;Som Tam comes to the beach at this cosy Ari restaurant, where north-eastern style dishes are topped with the freshest seafood. Opened in 2014 by a family from Hua Hin, the place’s owners delight in offering guests the same food they serve family and friends. The result is fare that balances Isan flavours with seafood from Hua-Hin and Petchaburi, and beef from a notable farm. Fried squid with Lay Lao sauce is a standout, as is Luang Phra Bang green papaya salad.;Air conditioning;[]
4010;Sanpakoi Kanomjeen;Thailand;Chiang Mai;Thongkam Market, 11 Soi Thasatoi, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50000, Thailand;18.7859078;99.0086633;39;false;true;Street Food;Established in 1977 and a local favourite at Thongkam Market, this spot offers tasty and affordable Kanomjeen (fresh rice vermicelli) with various curries. Try the Nam-Lo, a mix of spicy pork and chicken curry sauces. If noodles aren’t your thing, swap them for rice. Not only are the street food dishes here delicious, but they’re great value too – especially when you consider that side vegetables are unlimited.;Cash only;[]
4011;Go Benz;Thailand;Phuket;163 Krabi Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8848536;98.3825498;64;true;false;Asian;The constantly busy Go Benz has been serving popular dishes, including their speciality pork with peppery broth and rolled rice noodles, for over 20 years – and it’s easy to see why it’s quite such a popular spot. Many of the dishes often sell out, like the fragrant dry boiled rice with crispy pork and tender pork offal. Also well worth ordering is the crispy pork with sweet soy sauce, which is seasoned wonderfully and has a lovely charcoal-grilled crust.;Cash only;[]
4012;Chai;Thailand;Nonthaburi;4 Soi Samakkhi 38, Samakkhi Road, Tha Sai, Mueang Nonthaburi, Nonthaburi, 11000, Thailand;13.881761;100.53573;27;true;false;Street Food;Fuss-free food, live seafood in tanks cooked to order and a speedy service have earned Chai Phochana its loyal following. The stir-fried squid comes with a rich, creamy salted egg yolk and spring onions. The spicy sour soup with giant catfish roes and vegetables is also tasty. Open till late, for night owls with a hunger pang, this is the place for you.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4013;Khao Tom Thanon Di Buk;Thailand;Phuket;185/11 Phang-Nga Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8835728;98.3974071;94;false;false;Noodles and Congee;This family-run gem serves comforting classics, from aromatic Khao Tom porridge to a secret-recipe Chinese brown soup with various toppings. Weekend specials include braised pork ribs and chicken with fermented soybeans. Adding a twist, they serve sandwiches filled with distinctly flavoured kaya. The perfect balance of casual dining and unique culinary delights is complemented by charming local Thai-Chinese decor.;Cash only;[]
4014;Mekin Farm;Thailand;Khon Kaen;114 Mu 7, Ban Khok Klang, Chorakhe, Nong Ruea, Khon Kaen, 40240, Thailand;16.4678592;102.5414866;72;false;false;Isan;Farm-to-table is the philosophy here. The owner grows fruits and vegetables and raises poultry on the farm. They use simple cooking techniques and focus on the ingredients' natural flavours. Although short, the menu perfectly embodies the Isan spirit. The standout dish is Isan thick curry with local fish, which has a tender and juicy texture. Diners can enjoy their meal in an open-air pavilion and even attend a culinary workshop to learn how to cook the signature dish.;Car park,Cash only,Garden or park;[]
4015;Lian Tai;Thailand;Surat Thani;70 Chonkasem Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.1433054;99.325195;35;true;false;Small eats;Lian Tai specialises in deep-fried doughnuts. The family uses the original fermented dough recipe concocted by their father more than 5 decades ago. Cooked to a crisp, outer golden-brown with a soft, puffy inside, the Patongo is irresistible when dipped in rich sweet pandan custard.;Cash only;[]
4017;Guay Jub Chang Moi Tat Mai;Thailand;Chiang Mai;99/11-12 Chang Moi Tat Mai Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.7901443;98.9987035;78;false;false;Noodles;This place specialises in Guay Jub with Sai Ua sausage, served in a unique peppery broth, featuring with crispy pork and pork liver. They also offer another delightful dish: fresh spring rolls, topped with sliced omelette and aromatic sauce.;Cash only;[]
4018;Sae Phun;Thailand;Bangkok;112 Mahannop Road, Sao Chingcha, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.75356;100.5008;30;true;true;Small eats;Opened since 1926, it has been relocated. This small shop is now run by the third generation. The owner has been cooking with her grandfather's recipes for many years. The signature dish chicken stew is juicy with chicken and rich in sauce. It can be paired with rice or deep fried egg noodles.;Cash only;[]
4019;Pae Brass Pot Porridge 38 Years;Thailand;Bangkok;320 Pracha Rat Sai 1 Road, Bang Sue, Bangkok, 10800, Thailand;13.8074121;100.5217596;62;true;true;Congee;Don't let the name mislead you – "38" is a nod to the founder's lucky number. This porridge hotspot has been simmering since 1962, serving up porridge in its signature brass pots for three generations. Our favourite is the mixed rice porridge option.;Cash only;[]
4020;Gim Nguan Noodle;Thailand;Bangkok;75/70 Soi Chom Thong 16, Chom Thong Road, Bang Kho, Chom Thong, Bangkok, 10150, Thailand;13.7001327;100.4711595;62;false;false;Noodles;This hidden gem, tucked away in a Bangkok alley since 1999, excels in fish ball noodle soup. They offer fresh, umami-rich fish balls, al dente noodles, and a savoury, aromatic broth. Optional toppings like cheese and poached egg, along with large servings and ample condiments, provide great taste and value.;;[]
4021;Chang-Wang-Imm;Thailand;Nonthaburi;44 Mu 4, Soi Wat Bang Chak, Bang Tanai, Pak Kret, Nonthaburi, 11120, Thailand;13.9156915;100.4908793;71;false;false;Thai;Down by the banks of the Chao Phraya, enjoy affordable yet tasty Thai cuisine with relaxing river views from a charming 1950s house. Everything here is vintage, from the old-fashioned décor to the classic cooking techniques and flavours. The traditional Thai curry with pork, shrimp paste and basil is highly recommended. Book table #52 for remarkable private views from the upper deck. Live music adds to the ambience at the weekend.;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
4022;Hia Wan Khao Tom Pla;Thailand;Bangkok;816 Chan Road, Thung Wat Don, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7077875;100.51952;28;true;true;Small eats, Congee;Entirely focused on top-drawer seafood, this eatery offers a wide range of dishes. The soft-boiled rice with silver pomfret comes with a juicy fillet and fresh, clear soup. The baked mung bean noodles with prawns feature sticky mung bean noodles, underscored by a spicy-sour Thai seafood sauce.;Cash only;[]
4023;Phunisa;Thailand;Surat Thani;11/1 Mu 1, Khao Hua Khwai, Phunphin, Surat Thani, 84130, Thailand;9.0650929;99.2322317;95;false;false;Southern Thai;Standing atop a picturesque hill, the restaurant commands splendid views of the Tapi River winding through a green landscape of palm tree plantations and mountains. They serve tasty Southern Thai fare, including salted duck egg and local river prawns. A spicy seafood sauce and chargrill aroma add depth and complexity to the natural umami of prawns, while a spicy Southern Thai curry soup with pork cartilage features intense peppery and spicy flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4024;Khao Phra Ram Long Song Lao Ohw;Thailand;Surat Thani;22 2 Witeetad Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.1455468;99.3241222;59;false;false;Small eats;With a legacy spanning 6 decades, locals flock here for the exquisite satay pork and renowned phra ram long song, an ancient Siamese delicacy. It features tender sliced pork in a curry sauce that masterfully balances rich gutsy paste with creamy coconut milk.;Cash only;[]
4026;Roti Thaew Nam;Thailand;Phuket;6 Thep Krasattri Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8848263;98.3908635;30;true;false;Small eats;Soft, crispy, non-oily roti emerge from a huge charcoal pan. At this 70-year-old Halal breakfast spot, they're shaped, fried and served in the blink of an eye and served with tender beef or chicken curry. The sweeter roti with banana and egg has no added sugar.;Cash only;[]
4027;Surf & Turf by Soul Kitchen;Thailand;Phuket;115 Phangnga Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8837246;98.3903716;33;false;false;European Contemporary;The menu changes every month in this intriguing restaurant. Regular options range from home-made pastas to a signature seafood dish, plus specials that are cleverly curated to showcase Chef Tom's latest culinary creations. The chef artfully prepares his dishes, blending quality ingredients to tantalise the taste buds. And thanks to the ever-changing selection of handpicked wines, there's always something different to sip with your meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4028;Chuan Chim;Thailand;Phuket;37/3 Montri Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8829151;98.3927229;22;true;false;Thai;One of the oldest food shops in Phuket, now run by the second generation, offers the freshest seafood, all prepared à la minute. The chef's impressive wok skills shine through in every dish, with highlights like the aromatic Tom Yam seafood soup and deep-fried squid with garlic and pepper.;Cash only;[]
4029;Saiyut and Doctor Sai Kitchen;Thailand;Chiang Mai;32 Chotana Road Soi 12, Pa Tan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8220965;98.9872938;63;true;false;Thai;Since 2004, Doctor Sai has been serving pan-Thai dishes, including royal fare, following recipes from her mother, Saiyud, a former cooking instructor, in a setting reminiscent of dining at home. Start with an elegant appetiser like fried prawns and peanuts in an egg net, flower dumplings, or deep-fried pork wrapped in egg noodles. By dessert – try the sweet potato in syrup – you’ll guess this home, with its warm service, belongs to a royal from a bygone era.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4030;Keo Pla;Thailand;Surat Thani;560/4 Na Mueang Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.145569;99.3270919;90;false;true;Small eats;This locally renowned noodle shop first opened in 1959. The homemade fish dumplings with celery and fish balls packed with umami invariably attract long queues. The soup strikes just the right balance of sweet and savoury with a herbal aroma. Hearty, generous portions.;Cash only;[]
4031;Krua Chao Baan;Thailand;Ko Samui;438/18 Mu 1, Maret, Ko Samui, 84310, Thailand;9.4509858;100.0289062;19;true;true;Seafood;Krua Chao Baan means local kitchen, which aptly describes the vibe of this eatery specialised in Southern Thai food. The signature omelette is simple: crispy, not oily, with mixed seafood and well-seasoned minced pork. The stir-fried squid with pineapple, a local recipe only found on the island, is depicted by joyful sweet, sour and peppery notes.;Car park,Great view;[]
4032;Here Hai;Thailand;Bangkok;112/1 Soi Sukhumvit 63, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7302744;100.5863744;22;false;true;Seafood;The two floors at Here Hai are packed with diners every day and it's easy to see why. Good-quality fresh seafood is shipped in directly from Surat Thani and cooked Thai style to showcase bold flavours. As dishes come in large portions designed for sharing, they are ideal for groups. The crab meat with fried rice is cooked using a traditional technique for a pleasantly smoky aroma. Diners can ask for the spiciness to be toned down.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4033;Kao.Piak.Sen;Thailand;Udon Thani;20/20 Si Suk Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.437918;102.7774248;97;false;true;Vietnamese;Formerly a street food stall, the owners have upped the quality of the menu and the dining experience. Kao Piak’s stylish restaurant seamlessly blends timeless and contemporary styles, drawing inspiration from Vietnam’s architectural heritage. Their signature aromatic pork broth is simmered for 8 hours yielding exquisitely tender meat. Don't miss out on the grilled lemongrass-marinated pork kebabs and Vietnamese sausage.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4034;Kai Yang Rabeab (Khao Suan Kwang);Thailand;Khon Kaen;99 Mittraphap Road, Kham Muang, Khao Suan Kwang, Khon Kaen, 40280, Thailand;16.8540408;102.8590017;86;false;true;Isan;Throw a stick in Khon Kaen and you’ll likely hit a street food place serving grilled chicken and Isan dishes. You’d be lucky if you landed on this one. Its secret is tender, juicy chicken from three local breeds. A second downtown branch offers the same menu minus grilled offal.;Cash only;[]
4035;Krua Luang Ten;Thailand;Phang-Nga;160 Mu 2, Phet Kasem Road, Khuekkhak, Takua Pa, Phang-Nga, 82190, Thailand;8.7148875;98.2576907;50;true;true;Southern Thai;Krua Luang Ten makes for an unusual setting with its tables arranged on sand-covered floors. Check the whiteboard for the specials, which often feature the catch of the day and seasonal ingredients. The dishes masterfully balance robust Southern Thai flavours for authentic spiciness, and the complimentary vegetables come with tai pla sauce. N.B. The restaurant is closed on the 10th, 20th, and 30th of the month.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4036;Pae;Thailand;Pathum Thani;80/1 Rahaeng Market, Rahaeng, Lat Lum Kaeo, Pathum Thani, 12140, Thailand;14.042349;100.4198724;42;false;false;Thai-Chinese;This hidden eatery in the 100-year-old Rahaeng Market has been serving traditional Thai-Chinese dishes for over 50 years. With a focus on quality ingredients from the market, their homemade dishes like minced featherback fish and pork in tofu sheets are recommended. Arrive early for spicy stir-fried featherback fish and fried sun-dried snakehead fish.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4037;Mon;Thailand;Phang-Nga;46/11-12 Mu 1, Phet Kasem Road, Lam Kaen, Thai Mueang, Phang-Nga, 82210, Thailand;8.5936703;98.2565435;92;false;true;Southern Thai;Established for over 35 years, the restaurant has fostered a close connection with local fishermen, ensuring the delivery of a diverse selection of fresh seafood. The open-air main dining area exudes the charm of an old Thai-Chinese eatery. Popular among divers returning from Mu Ko Similan, the intense flavours authentically represent local cuisine, with generously sized dishes. Standouts include the stir-fried crab with lime and the southern curry featuring river snails and wild betel leaves.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4038;Mor Mu Dong;Thailand;Phuket;9/4 Mu 3 Soi Pa Lai, Chao Fa Road, Chalong, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83130, Thailand;7.843128;98.37198;21;true;true;Southern Thai;Mor Mu Dong takes its name from its owner, Mor, and the Mu Dong Canal, where it is located. Nestled in a mangrove forest, it is housed in a set of rustic pavilions where diners can enjoy seafood and take in the views that change with the tide. In the open kitchen, tanks of live seafood affirm the freshness of the food. Order 3–4 vibrant dishes to share and enjoy the Southern Thai flavours bursting from them.;Car park;[]
4039;Lim Lao Ngow (Samphanthawong);Thailand;Bangkok;299-301 Song Sawat Road, Samphanthawong, Bangkok, 10100, Thailand;13.736215;100.51198;17;false;true;Street Food;After 60 years in business, the family boasts multiple branches, but the original, in Chinatown, is our pick. The bouncy fish ball concept definitely lives up to its name. Made from fresh fish and no flour, they’re served with Chinese noodles and wontons, and leave a joyful aftertaste.;Cash only;[]
4040;Meena;Thailand;Chiang Mai;13/5 Mu 2, San Klang, San Kamphaeng, Chiang Mai, 50130, Thailand;18.73332;99.086865;72;true;false;Thai;Don’t be alarmed when you pass through a rice field driving here, as this hidden gem is worth it. As its name suggests, this alfresco restaurant specialises in rice, alongside new spins on Thai classics. Most are garnished with fruits and edible flowers, giving them bursts of colour. Along with the five-colour rice balls, northern-style spicy minced fish salad is a delight. Vegans will enjoy their many options, including the spicy stir-fried eryngii mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4041;Pho Tha Bo;Thailand;Khon Kaen;3/12 Si Nuan Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4235345;102.8371981;68;true;true;Street Food;This family-run shop serves their own phở noodle soup recipe and other Vietnamese favourites, including fresh and fried spring rolls, doi huyet (blood sausage) and tiết canh (raw blood pudding served with cooked minced pork meat and offal). The pork sausage and beef balls are homemade.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4043;Baannai;Thailand;Bangkok;102/13 Soi Kamphaeng Phet 5, Set Siri Road, Sam Sen Nai, Phaya Thai, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand;13.7797284;100.5304943;98;false;false;Thai;Baan Nai, or ‘inner house’ in Thai, is so called because the owner’s great grandfather built it on the innermost part of his land. The house, and recipes cooked by its occupants, have passed down through the family to the present day where, as a boutique hotel and homely restaurant, it serves delicious time-tested dishes like Taengmo Pla Haeng (watermelon with dried fish flakes) and Khanom Phra Phai (sweet mung bean dumplings). Group booking is required.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
4044;Busarin Cuisine;Thailand;Chiang Mai;133 Rattanakosin Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8006357;98.9972692;82;true;false;Northern Thai;Busarin, the new sister restaurant of Magnolia Café, has high ceilings, a collection of chinaware and leather green sofa booths that contrast with the light pink walls. When you dine here, it’s like being welcomed into Chef Noi’s home. They serve northern-Thai based on family recipes with noodles and roti instead of rice. The standout is a streaky pork that’s braised in a hung lay curry for two days and emits a powerful aroma of ginger and spices.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4045;Peng Duck Noodles;Thailand;Udon Thani;439 Nong Tao Lek Road, Ban Lueam, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.4044283;102.7671631;46;true;false;Noodles;The strength of this shop is its locally sourced free-range meat. The tender braised duck noodles, including neck, wing and thigh, are highlights. Their slow-cooked pork is equally exceptional. Try the duck rice with a smooth blood jelly and five spices.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4046;Niyom Salt Grilled Duck;Thailand;Phuket;5/19 Mu 3, Chao Fah Tawan Tok Road, Wichit, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8661928;98.3493489;41;true;false;Grills;This unassuming gem serves around 30-40 juicy, tender charcoal-roasted ducks every day. Order a half or whole bird and savour the wholesome flavour and crispy skin fresh off the stove with either spicy-sour or tamarind sauce for dipping. Grilled chicken is sometimes an option, too.;Cash only;[]
4047;Sow Jeck;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;183/8 Maharat Road, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9861571;102.0975761;70;false;false;Thai;Chef-owner Anuwat Thiemkreangkrai's 12-year-old stall stands out with its fresh, light MSG-free seafood dishes. His passion shines through in stir-fries that bring out the natural essence of the fresh catch, such as celery with seabass and the beautifully balanced seafood with Thai basil.;Cash only;[]
4048;Kin-Kub-Ei;Thailand;Phuket;81/9 Mu 7, Si Sunthon Road, Si Sunthon, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9801168;98.3334005;42;true;true;Southern Thai;With its shaded garden, recently renovated Kin-Kub-Ei retains its inviting charm, while debuting a casual yet warm new dining area. Chef Tipsuda 'Tubtim' Khanchaijatuwit and Ei prepare southern Thai specialties passed down through the generations, nicely balancing flavours and prioritising quality. The menu ensures affordability without sacrificing taste. The crispy golden-brown local fish with tangy curry paste epitomises their commitment to flavour and tradition.;Car park,Cash only,Terrace;[]
4049;Khao Soi Thai Yai;Thailand;Udon Thani;331/4 Mu 5, Promprakai Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.400048;102.7735599;25;true;false;Northern Thai;The original owners moved to Isan more than 20 years ago and brought the flavours of Northern Thailand with them. The owner doesn't compromise on quality, ensuring the spices are well utilised to produce bold, balanced and authentic flavours. Khao Soi is the speciality here. For groups, order the Northern Thai set – the homemade sausage won't disappoint. Round off your meal with a refreshing dessert.;Cash only;[]
4051;Krua Baan Platong;Thailand;Phuket;167/1 Mu 5, Thepkrasattri Road, Si Sunthon, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9967626;98.3554246;98;true;true;Southern Thai;Popular with Thai celebrities and prominent politicians, this eatery tucked away in a tiny alley in Thalang deserves its excellent reputation. The chefs source quality local ingredients to produce intensely flavoured dishes that encapsulate the essence of Phuket. Highlights include stir-fried banana stalk with plump shrimps and shrimp paste, and melt-in-your-mouth steamed pork belly with their signature southern Thai budu dipping sauce. Booking and ordering in advance are a must.;Cash only;[]
4052;Roti Sai Mai Abeedeen-Pranom Sangaroon;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;32/1 Mu 4, U Thong Road, Pratu Chai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3430049;100.5609138;45;true;false;Street Food;Over 70 years have passed, but this renowned spot opposite Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya Hospital still serves the same perfect rotis with candy floss, made by the same family. Their specialty, the green pandan roti, is known for its delightful gooeyness. As popular as ever, be prepared to queue.;Cash only;[]
4054;Here Klae Pork Satay;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;Pamaprao Road, Ho Rattanachai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3622062;100.5786019;96;false;false;Street Food;Now run by the third-generation grill master, this humble shophouse boasts a history spanning over nine decades and remains one of Ayutthaya’s most cherished spots for charcoal-grilled pork satay. The skewered meat is meticulously marinated, offering an aromatic blend of nine spices. Don't miss the pork offal – it pairs perfectly with the accompanying peanut sauce. Please note: takeaways only, and cash is the accepted payment method.;Cash only;[]
4055;Roe Dang;Thailand;Phang-Nga;55/15 Mu 1, Phet Kasem Road, Lam Kaen, Thai Mueang, Phang-Nga, 82210, Thailand;8.5963563;98.2556289;26;true;false;Southern Thai;Basic furnishings and modest dish presentations belie the skill behind their precisely cooked recipes, which are made to order. Specialising in authentic Southern Thai seafood, they source the day's catch for dishes such as red grouper with bitter melon, and simple stir-fried melinjo leaves with fresh prawns. Their home-made curries use local Phang-nga ingredients. The wall of celebrity photos attests to its popularity.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4056;Maan Muang;Thailand;Bangkok;165/7 Soi Ramkhamhaeng 112, Ramkhamhaeng Road, Saphan Sung, Bangkok, 10240, Thailand;13.7690166;100.6771662;21;true;true;Northern Thai;This lovely wooden Lanna house with rustic charm will magically whisk you off to Chiang Mai. The dining area under the raised house is decorated with traditional Thai wooden furniture and earthenware. The staff too are dressed in Northern Thai fashions and speak in a regional dialect. But it’s the dizzying array of dishes and beautiful blend of northern ingredients that tops it off. The Thai curry soup with pork ribs and jackfruit hits the spot.;Car park;[]
4057;No Name Noodle;Thailand;Bangkok;1F, Room P2, 1/2 Soi Athakravi 1, Sukhumvit 26 Road, Khlong Tan, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7217145;100.5693273;72;false;false;Noodles;Those lucky enough to secure a spot are treated to signature noodle dishes, Shio Soba and Shoyu Tsuke Soba, each with over 30 ingredients. The seasonal noodle and rice bowls use a fermented blend of three types of shoyu for deep umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
4058;Morakot Kitchen;Thailand;Pathum Thani;28 Mu 4, Rangsit - Nakhon Nayok Road, Rangsit, Thanyaburi, Pathum Thani, 12110, Thailand;14.0199232;100.7333033;23;false;true;Thai;For over 120 years, this no-frills kitchen in a wooden house on a main road has been dishing up intensely flavourful, comforting Thai fare. Don't miss the fish cake, made from authentic spotted featherback fish and heavenly spiced, served with the sweet house-special dipping sauce.;Cash only;[]
4059;Lung Khajohn Wat Ket;Thailand;Chiang Mai;Opposite to Wat Ket Karam, Charoenrajd Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50000, Thailand;18.792313;99.0022428;31;false;false;Street Food;For decades, this place has been serving distinctive Khao Kriab Pak Moh, or steamed rice skin dumplings, opposite Wat Ket Karam. These contain a tasty salty-sweet filling wrapped in a coconut-infused rice flour sheet and a side of coconut cream. Tapioca balls with sweet pork are also offered.;Cash only;[]
4060;Krua Laew Tae R-Rom;Thailand;Chon Buri;17/62 Mu 6, Paniad Chang Road, Pattaya, Na Kluea, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.9470985;100.9033966;59;false;true;Thai;With a limited menu, the kitchen excels in seafood, Thai food and home-made curries with bold, rich flavours. The crab, shrimp, clams and fish are served ultra-fresh at reasonable prices, with rare catches often appearing on the menu. The restaurant doesn't open if the line-catch on that day is not successful. Booking a week in advance is necessary.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4061;Tue Ka Ko Na Prince;Thailand;Chiang Mai;Kaeonawarat Road, Wat Ket, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50000, Thailand;18.7962375;99.0062067;76;true;false;Street Food;This Tue Ka Ko – or taro fritter – place has been open for over 20 years opposite The Prince Royal's College, hence the name “Tue Ka Ko Na Prince." Savoury and sweet, their version of the Chiang Mai snack is perfected textured and served with peanut sauce. Deep-fried tofu is also sold.;Cash only;[]
4063;Indochine;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;170 Sappasit Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2362088;104.8580126;34;false;true;Vietnamese;The name Indochine is derived from the connection between two countries - Vietnamese family recipes have been served here for over 50 years. And family is the key to this popular business where everyone pitches in. The restaurant boasts vintage décor, using old wooden furniture and tables made from defunct sewing machines. The Vietnamese rice cake with grille pork is highly recommended, while the signature namnueng comes in a big basket with a mix of fresh local vegetables.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
4064;Go Neng (Wichayanon);Thailand;Chiang Mai;77 Wichayanon Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.7900026;99.0017724;45;false;true;Street Food;Go Neng has been serving deep-fried dough sticks for almost four decades. No matter what shape they take – crocodile, dinosaur, dragon or elephant – each one boasts the same puffy perfection and crispy texture. Other bites, such as the deep-fried bun and fried whole-wheat dough are also great.;Cash only;[]
4065;Baan Ta Ko Rai;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;112/941 Mu 3, Khlong Suanplu, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3448242;100.6123761;75;false;false;Thai;Here at this blue-roofed local favourite they prove there’s more to Ayutthaya than grilled river prawns. Ingredients are carefully selected from produce grown within the community and it uses fish from nearby rivers as the catch of the day. The herb-scented fish cakes are delectable, while stir-fried Chinese kale with deep fried salted fish is equally impressive. Portion sizes are generous, so check before ordering.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
4066;U-Khao;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;99 Mu 2, Khanon Luang, Bang Pa-in, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.2954025;100.5666601;52;true;false;Thai;U-Khao, or ‘land of plenty’, has 2 dining areas smartly decorated in white and blue. The menu serves up the nostalgic flavours of the owner’s childhood, as it’s based on her mother’s Thai recipes. They use traditional cooking methods presented with a modern aesthetic. The old-school style egg stew with pork belly is a flavoursome, intense stew with juicy meat. The grilled shrimp relish with vegetables is also highly recommended for its spicy relish and smoky aroma.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
4067;Plaew;Thailand;Nakhon Pathom;Soi 5, Mu 1, Nakhon Pathom, Mueang Nakhon Pathom, Nakhon Pathom, 73000, Thailand;13.8405113;100.0430583;80;false;false;Noodles;This no-frills outlet is popular with locals for its tom yum noodles and homemade pork balls. They use premium ingredients and jumbo-size seafood. Also check out the homemade fish cakes, with a curry-flavoured spice, served with deep-fried crispy basil and a sweet and sour sauce.;Cash only;[]
4068;Majchapasuk;Thailand;Udon Thani;166 Mu 8, Udon-Nong Khai Road, Mu Mon, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.455291;102.7890064;50;false;true;Thai;A serene pond encircled by wooden pavilions is Majchapasuk's tranquil setting. Each spot in the expansive seating area has a soothing atmosphere, ideal for savouring local seafood steeped in over 40 years of Isan culinary heritage. Standout mains showcase Isan tradition with seabass and snakehead fish. Don't miss the crispy deep-fried spring rolls stuffed with minced pork and pork skin. Evening promises optimum weather conditions and idyllic pond views.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4069;Baan Heng;Thailand;Khon Kaen;54/2 Klang Mueang Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4341513;102.8359528;61;true;true;Thai-Chinese;Baan Heng was born out of a souvenir and grocery shop the owners’ grandparents started in 1957 called Heng Nguan Hiang. It sold products like homemade Chinese sausage, pork floss and pork jerky. Now, the restaurant serves Thai-Chinese breakfast fare, like their signature Baan Heng sandwich and baked rice with sweet pork sausage in a remodelled wood-themed design that exudes old-school vibes. Add a classic hot Thai black coffee or milk tea for the full effect.;;[]
4071;Yok Kheng;Thailand;Surat Thani;5/2 Tonpo Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.1464657;99.3257433;97;true;false;Noodles;Consummately crafted regional specialties are the highlight here, particularly long tong, a Surat Thani delicacy. It features succulent dry noodles in a pink sweet and sour sauce with tender portions of pig’s blood, skin and meat. Leave room for the delectable mango with sticky rice.;Cash only;[]
4072;One Chun;Thailand;Phuket;48/1 Thep Krasatti Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.88518;98.39069;30;true;true;Southern Thai;Merging the owner's fashion design flair and passion for fine fare, One Chun offers a vintage-toned dining experience in a 19C building. Diners still enjoy the family recipes, which have been passed down the generations. Among the specialties is a spicy yet refreshing dish with boiled shrimp and shrimp paste, perfectly balancing the salty and sour notes. Be sure to try "Mu Hong" for its bold flavours and soft, tender pork belly.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4073;Pad Thai Fai Ta Lu (Phra Nakhon);Thailand;Bangkok;115/5 Dinso Road, Bowon Niwet, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.7579542;100.5022182;32;true;false;Noodles;The tempting scent of sizzling pork greets you at this vibrant restaurant by chef Andy Yang. Their signature dish features nicely char-grilled pork loin slices atop savoury Pad Thai. Another recommendation is the Pad Thai with fresh prawns, stir-fried in their shell for sweet, delicious meat. For top-notch Pad Thai and skilled wok-based cooking at a fair price, this is your spot.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4074;Laab Somphit;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;169 Chan Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9792308;102.0874943;66;true;true;Isan;For over 50 years, Granny Somphit has been crafting flavourful Isan cuisine daily, balancing local spices with Thai herbs. Fresh offal cuts and the signature Isan spicy calf beef salad, seasoned with smoky rice powder for crispness, stand out. The homemade beef sausage and fermented meats are also notable.;Cash only;[]
4075;Rasik Local Kitchen;Thailand;Chiang Mai;44/3 Sridonchai Road, Chang Khlan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50100, Thailand;18.781675;98.9954957;47;true;false;Thai contemporary;This chef's table experience showcases seasonal flavours and beloved Thai classics. The talented chef interacts with guests from the open kitchen and uses traditional cooking methods, such as a charcoal stove, to add depth to the dishes. The mild red curry with grilled pork and damask rose looks simple but the authentic taste of homemade Thai curry paste hides inside. The sliced pork is tender and the curry texture is smooth with a rich but balanced flavour.;Air conditioning;[]
4076;Lucky;Thailand;Surat Thani;1 Thathong Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.145183;99.3302287;78;false;false;Thai-Chinese, Southern Thai;Lucky is a 2-storey restaurant with a simple, vintage vibe. The chef-owner has upheld the legacy of previous generations in this family-run eatery. She visits the market every day to select the freshest ingredients and oversees every dish that leaves the kitchen – a selection of Thai-Chinese, southern Thai and seafood cuisine. Don't miss the allure of wok-fried shrimp with chilli and salt, where the enticing blend of salt, chilli, garlic, and pepper creates an aromatic delight.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4077;Kapi Sator;Thailand;Ko Samui;25/236 Mu 6, Tawirat Phakdi Road, Bo Phut, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.5355491;100.0434024;86;false;true;Southern Thai;The restaurant upholds authentic Southern Thai food thanks to a culinary repertory that is hard to find elsewhere. One example is the delectable local squid in sweet coconut milk soup with a hint of lemongrass. The daily fish menu changes according to the catch of the day. If available, the deep-fried whole pomfret topped with spicy Southern Thai curry is highly recommended. They offer indoor and outdoor dining with plenty of parking.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4078;Huen Muan Jai;Thailand;Chiang Mai;24 Ratchaphruek Road, Chang Phueak, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.7998208;98.975429;84;true;false;Northern Thai;Headed up by former TV chef Charan Thipeung, this restaurant – whose name means ‘happy home’ – has been serving authentic Northern Thai food since 2011. Set in a Lanna house with a tree-lined garden, it’s a popular, wallet-friendly destination that offers hard-to-find traditional dishes alongside classic favourites. The uniquely flavoured spicy minced fish salad is highly recommended and if you’re unfamiliar with the cuisine, start with the excellent Northern appetiser sampler.;Car park;[]
4079;Hok Kee Lao;Thailand;Phang-Nga;19 Senarat Road, Bang Nai Si, Takua Pa, Phang-Nga, 82110, Thailand;8.8690419;98.3462373;35;true;false;Thai-Chinese;For over 40 years, this heritage restaurant has been serving up delicious Thai, Chinese, and Southern flavours. It's an ideal spot for family gatherings, offering a warm and inviting atmosphere. The menu includes Chinese favourites such as nicely moist chicken pae sa flavoured with seasoned soy sauce and paired with morning glory. If you are lucky, try the fried tofu with minced pork and shrimp.;Cash only;[]
4080;Krua Khun Nid;Thailand;Udon Thani;64 Soi Nonnivet 1, Udon Dussadi Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.426669;102.7865557;29;true;false;Isan;For over four decades this restaurant has been a mainstay for locals. Focusing on freshwater fish and meat, it serves large sharing portions. Seasonal options and occasional fish specials accompany enduring classics, such as the flavourful deep-fried Pla Som, or snakehead fish in flavoursome tom yum soup. The friendly staff are happy to share their recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4081;Khao Soi Mae Sai;Thailand;Chiang Mai;29/1 Ratchaphruek Road, Chang Phueak, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.804125;98.98513;51;false;true;Noodles;This shop serves the famous Khao Soi, featuring rich and slightly spicy curry notes. You can choose your preferred meat toppings, and the portions are so delicate that you might find yourself wanting another round!;Cash only;[]
4083;K. Panich;Thailand;Bangkok;431-433 Tanao Road, Sao Chingcha, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.7520907;100.4983633;76;true;false;Street Food;This iconic family-run eatery serves delectable mango sticky rice made to a recipe that has been handed down the generations for 80 years. Their preparation is masterful: the flavour of the steamed sweetened sticky rice is enhanced by the richness of coconut milk.;Cash only;[]
4084;Pa Ting;Thailand;Surat Thani;1/8 Mu 5, Don Sak, Surat Thani, 84220, Thailand;9.314854;99.6842039;23;false;false;Seafood;Established in 1967, Pa Ting is run by the founder’s daughter. The restaurant is a basic, open-air building overlooking Don Sak River, serving seafood cooked according to local recipes. The spicy salad with salted Kulao fish bursts with flavoursome Thai herbs. The crab curry with seablite leaves enjoys the natural umami of freshly caught seafood, enhanced with spicy in-house curry paste. Plenty of parking at the front.;Car park,Great view;[]
4085;Samlor;Thailand;Bangkok;1076 Charoen Krung Road, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7303479;100.5155168;79;true;false;Thai;Samlor means ‘tricycle’ in Thai and a traditional one hangs outside this cosy restaurant. Inside the loft-style space, chef Napol creates flavoursome, well-presented elevated Thai cuisine inspired by local street food with specially selected ingredients. They also have an à la carte menu, which includes a cut and catch of the day. Guests need to check with the chef what is available.;Air conditioning;[]
4086;Khon Kaen Grilled Pork Neck;Thailand;Khon Kaen;77/4 Klang Mueang Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4348608;102.8362486;94;false;true;Street Food;This grilled pork spot is among the most popular street places in Khon Kaen, and its grilled pork neck with rice is the reason why. The tender, sweet and salty marinated meat perfectly matches the accompanying spicy tamarind sauce. Also recommended are the spicy salad and soup.;Cash only;[]
4087;The Charm Dining Gallery;Thailand;Phuket;93 Dibuk Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8864034;98.3861911;41;false;true;Southern Thai;Having grown up working in his family's food business, Chef Buriphat always wanted to do something special with their recipes. Over the last few years, he has realised that vision, impressing diners with his honest interpretation of traditional Southern Thai-Peranakan cuisine. Check out the delicious stir-fried pork belly with herbs and sweet dark soy sauce, and be sure to try the pork rib soup with tofu and salted fish.;;[]
4088;Beer Hima (Chatuchak);Thailand;Bangkok;12/21, 99/231 Thetsaban Songkhro Road, Lat Yao, Chatuchak, Bangkok, 10900, Thailand;13.83997;100.54763;33;true;false;Southern Thai;Despite its quirky name and simple interior, Beer Hima offers so much more. The family’s seafood recipes from Nakhon Si Thammarat province are loaded with flavour. The southern Thai sour curry with grouper is packed with turmeric and chilli and delivers the perfect harmony of sour and spicy, while the rich, aromatic shrimp paste in the stir-fried prawns with bitter beans awakens the senses. There’s ample parking and a private room large enough for 30 guests.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4089;Huan Soontaree;Thailand;Chiang Mai;208 Pa Tan Road, Pa Tan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8310278;98.9937575;43;true;true;Northern Thai;Soontaree Vechanont doesn’t just own “Soontaree’s House” – the singer also performs here nightly. Set on the Ping River in an open-air, Lanna-style building with more tables outside, this charming restaurant can accommodate up to 350 guests. Among the Northern Thai cooking they serve is their signature boneless murrel fish stuffed with pork. It’s a creative dish, with the well-seasoned sausage proving suitably fragrant and spicy.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4090;Leng Yentafo;Thailand;Khon Kaen;Klang Mueang Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4349314;102.8359853;30;false;true;Street Food;When Mr. Leng left Bangkok’s Chinatown for Khon Kaen in 1984, he brought a secret recipe for Yentafo, or pink noodle soup, and set up shop. His signature dish, which features toothsome noodles, fresh fishballs, shrimp balls and fish wontons, and a tasty broth, continues to delight.;Cash only;[]
4091;Kin Lookdeaw;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;35 Mu 9, Tha Chao Sanuk, Tha Ruea, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13130, Thailand;14.543095;100.7102141;93;true;true;Thai;The name of the restaurant encourages guests to ‘focus on eating’ at this quaint house with an open-air pavilion overlooking a serene pond. The chefs, veterans in the kitchen, prepare simple Thai dishes and make their own chilli paste from scratch. The regular pounding of the pestle in the mortar reverberates through nature’s own soundtrack. Try the stir-fried crispy fish with aromatic ginger and salted eggs.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4092;Hong Seng;Thailand;Nonthaburi;280 Mu 2, Chaeng Watthana Road, Pak Kret, Nonthaburi, 11120, Thailand;13.9152321;100.4950129;23;false;true;Thai-Chinese;On the Chao Praya by the Rama IV Bridge, this renowned Thai-Chinese spot has been known for reasonably priced flavoursome fare since 1957. Its open-air dining room and wooden terrace set the stage for relaxed meals featuring highlights like grilled giant river prawns with spicy sauce and mini deep-fried crab meat wrapped in tofu skin. Open for lunch, the place extends its hours on weekends. Reach it by boat, or if driving, park in the public space under the bridge.;Cash only,Terrace;[]
4093;Tonfon Bistro;Thailand;Phang-Nga;Krabi 1002 Rural Road, Bo Saen, Thap Put, Phang-Nga, 82180, Thailand;8.4775494;98.6220523;74;false;false;Southern Thai;Since opening its doors in 1995, the chef-owner has consistently cooked flavoursome, well presented southern fare with an emphasis on locally sourced ingredients and authentic recipes. Daily deliveries of fresh seafood and organic produce come from nearby farms. Savour dishes like stir-fried pork with shrimp paste and bitter bean or curry with crab legs and betel leaves. While the menu may be concise, each dish reflects the chef's passion. Indoor and outdoor seating is available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
4095;Phed Phed Bistro;Thailand;Bangkok;The Circle Ratchapruk, 39 Ratchaphruek Road, Bang Ramat, Taling Chan, Bangkok, 10170, Thailand;13.7671054;100.4439937;78;true;false;Isan;Phed Phed Bistro offers comforting Isan favourites steeped in flavour. Don’t miss the herbal pork soup with its tender, crispy cartilage and sweet pumpkin, while the green apple som tum and salty fish sauce with dried shrimp perfectly blends sweet with sour. Large groups of locals pack the place at lunch and dinner. As they don't accept bookings, arrive early to avoid a wait.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4096;Ekachan;Thailand;Chiang Mai;95 Chang Khlan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50100, Thailand;18.7833776;99.0035298;35;false;true;Thai;This new restaurant in the heart of old Chiang Mai is run by a local chef who embraces the slow food concept, using ingredients from around the country. The fried rice with sweet shrimp is nicely cooked with sweet shrimp paste and tasty condiments, including fresh chilli, shallots and mango. The spicy beef turmeric curry is a standout, with an intense mix of herbs and spices. If you’re looking for the spice bomb, they can add fresh Thai chillies.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4097;Thai Niyom;Thailand;Bangkok;Mahatun Plaza, 888/28-29 Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.741953;100.549126;86;true;false;Thai;Hidden in the shadow of skyscrapers is this gem of a restaurant, which got its start serving family recipes, but now offers an array of Thai cuisine from Chiang Mai to Hat Yai. It is a great place to sample delicious Thai cooking from every region on the same table. Quality ingredients are sourced locally and turned into dishes like the recommended Phuket stir-fried pork belly with shrimp paste and the Chiang Mai Combo, a Northern Thai-style appetiser plate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
4098;Bokkia Tha Din Daeng;Thailand;Bangkok;323 Tha Din Daeng Road, Somdet Chao Phraya, Khlong San, Bangkok, 10600, Thailand;13.7336698;100.5025112;65;false;true;Small eats;Tucked away in a small market stall, this family-run dessert shop is famous for its sweet Bokkia. It's a unique treat: egg noodles, topped with crushed ice and syrup, which is amazingly refreshing and not too sweet. The condimental options are also good quality.;Cash only;[]
4099;Krua Suwimol;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;1229 9 Mittraphap Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9594209;102.0562333;30;true;false;Thai-Chinese;This simple, open-air restaurant serves Thai-Chinese fare. The food is distinctive for its simply cooking techniques yet quality dishes with extra-fresh ingredients and intense flavours. They offer a fantastic range, including several seafood and made-to-order options. Deep-fried chicken thigh with fish sauce and stir-fried spicy seafood are recommended.;Car park,Cash only;[]
4100;Sanae;Thailand;Chiang Mai;64/1 Wangsingkham Road, Pa Tan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8062902;99.0031625;57;true;true;Thai;This halal kitchen next to the Ping River is one for beef fans. With indoor and outdoor dining, the big outdoor kitchen cooks a creative à la carte menu with balanced flavours. The beef fat rice topped with egg yolk has a smoky flavour. The spicy Thai soup with beef shank is packed with spice aroma.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4101;Na Chantra;Thailand;Chiang Mai;Chantra Khiri Hotel, 49 Mu 3, Ban Pong, Hang Dong, Chiang Mai, 50230, Thailand;18.7841219;98.8430037;73;false;false;Thai;Set up in the hills inside the Chantra Khiri Hotel, Na Chantra offers gorgeous views of the national park and a menu that features central and northern Thai dishes. Vegetables and herbs come from their next-door farm and everything else – like the savoury northern sausage with chilli paste – is made from scratch. Don’t miss their signature minced pork with fresh veg and spicy sauce, or the piquant yellow curry soup with sea bass. Start your evening outside, with a seat by the infinity pool.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4102;Taberna 5 Mares;Spain;A Coruña;Parque Monte San Pedro, A Coruña, 15011, Spain;43.3774489;-8.4332531;17;true;true;Contemporary, Galician;The cooking at this taberna is fun as well as delicious! And with this in mind, the duo of owner-chefs Iria Espinosa and Luis Veira have strived for what they describe as the offbeat face of gourmet cuisine. This bright space occupying the former café adjoining the Arbore da Veira restaurant reflects the more informal and casual dining option of this award-winning name, which features an à la carte of appetisers and main dishes suitable for all budgets (it also includes a section entitled “landscapes for sharing”), in addition to an affordable tasting menu that showcases several signature dishes (spherical olives, carpaccio of scallops “al ajillo” with black garlic, etc). The impressive views over A Coruña add further appeal!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
4103;Enxebre;Spain;Vigo;Cuba 26, Vigo, 36204, Spain;42.2329025;-8.716614;61;true;true;Contemporary;The first attractive aspect of this restaurant, the Galician name of which translates as something that is pure, authentic and genuine, is that it is run by a young couple, chefs Marcos and Patricia, the former from Vigo itself, the latter from Toledo. This modern space, laid out on two floors and boasting a semi-open-view kitchen, also has a bar counter where guests can dine while watching the chefs hard at work. The contemporary inspired à la carte showcases plenty of technical prowess through signature tapas such as the “cocido stew doughnut” and Enxebre’s own version of a cockle empanada, and is complemented by two tasting menus (Xenuíno and Xeitoso). Make sure you try the creamy cheesecake (which you can also order to take away).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
4104;Lo Ponts;Spain;Ponts;Carretera de Calaf 6, Ponts, 25740, Spain;41.9124164;1.1888272;41;false;true;Catalan;A family-run restaurant that exudes passion and professionalism with a small space selling wines, plus three modern and functional dining rooms. Here, the impressively updated regional cuisine aims to bring personality to every dish, with a focus on locally sourced and, where possible, organic ingredients. These are showcased on interesting menus, including one tasting option (pre-booking required). Specialities such as the ever popular “Lo Ponts” snails and the savoury “cocas de recapte” pastry dishes are particularly recommended. It also boasts a varied wine cellar and organises regular “tasting dinners”.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4105;Mar de Esteiro;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Lugar Ponte Sionlla, Santiago de Compostela, 15884, Spain;42.9269753;-8.4825408;62;false;false;Seafood;One of the best places for top-quality fish and seafood in Santiago. The success of this restaurant situated about 6km from Santiago is undoubtedly down to its superb ingredients, although the building itself is unique – the restaurant occupies an imposing renovated house which is a listed cultural monument. It also boasts an attractive garden with a summer terrace, a private bar and a number of contemporary-style dining rooms occupying what were once the bedrooms. Make sure you try the main speciality here (lobster with rice) as well as some of its popular stews (gurnard, brill, turbot, lobster with broad beans, plus spider crab in season).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4106;Morrofino;Spain;Vigo;Serafín Avendaño 4-6, Vigo, 36201, Spain;42.2383452;-8.7127237;39;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant-cum-taberna that continues to win over foodies, where the simple urban ambience comes as a pleasant surprise. Here, the chef is keen for the open-view kitchen behind the bar to take centre stage, creating exciting, technically adept and contemporary dishes with a creative twist and a street-food feel, while at the same time respecting traditional flavours. The à la carte offers dishes to share, backed up by two tastings menus (Origen and Morrofino) and attractive culinary creations that occasionally showcase interesting, internationally inspired fusions. We were particularly surprised and impressed by the smoked butter croquette with prawns and garlic.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4107;Morro Tango;Spain;Alfaro;Las Pozas 18, Alfaro, 26540, Spain;42.1791718;-1.7507215;97;false;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Centrally located along a pedestrian street, this modern restaurant takes its name from an expression that the area’s older inhabitants once used to refer to those who were attracted to the more luxurious things in life and who wouldn’t eat just anything! The chef, who spent many years working alongside the award-winning Francis Paniego, has embarked on his first solo venture with the firm intention of showcasing the products of the Rioja region from a more contemporary angle, with a strong focus on fresh ingredients straight from the market. The à la carte, split into evocatively named sections, is complemented by two set menus: the daily “Todos los Morros” and the tasting-style “Morro Tango”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4108;La Salinera;Spain;Palamós;Avenida Onze de Setembre 93, Palamós, 17230, Spain;41.8453646;3.1288292;31;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The impressive endeavours of Josep in the kitchen and Montse in the dining room sum up the philosophy of this restaurant, which is easy to find thanks to its location close to the port in Palamós. This is without doubt a restaurant with its own personality and character as it occupies a building that was once a salting factory. The pleasant air-conditioned terrace by the entrance leads to a welcoming modern interior with live seafood tanks and two dining rooms with attractive barrel-vaulted ceilings that come as a pleasant surprise. The Mediterranean-inspired cuisine is heavily influenced by fish and seafood sourced on the Costa Brava.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4109;La Vasca;Spain;Miranda de Ebro;Olmo 3, Miranda de Ebro, 09200, Spain;42.684257;-2.9492449;68;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A gastronomic institution in the city that opened its doors in 1926 and has now been run by three generations of the same family. Located on the first floor of a 19C building, it features a classic-contemporary dining room which is accessed via a staircase lined with old photos of the restaurant and its founder, Ángela Bilbao, who came here from a village in Vizcaya province with her husband, a native of Burgos, and set up the original “casa de comidas”. Here, you can enjoy time-honoured cooking that features game, wild mushrooms in season, traditional offal dishes, cod, roast baby lamb etc.;Air conditioning;[]
4111;Atxa;Spain;Tarifa;Pedro Cortes 6, Tarifa, 11380, Spain;36.013427;-5.6028984;62;false;true;Contemporary;Located along a pedestrianised street in the old quarter, the Basque-named Atxa occupies a restored house dating back to 1864 and is a great dining option in mainland Spain’s most southerly town. The two chefs at the helm both worked for Martín Berasategui for several years, an experience which gave them the confidence to set up on their own. Their contemporary cuisine is based around locally sourced ingredients and includes creative touches and grilled dishes that take guests on a culinary journey back to Northern Spain. Their personal homage to “tranvía tarifeño”, a typical and local millefeuille-style dessert, is well worth a try.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4112;Dos Cuiners;Spain;Mataró;Muralla de Sant Llorenç 18, Mataró, 08301, Spain;41.5388303;2.4436912;33;true;false;Contemporary;Dos Cuiners, which boasts a central location and a relaxed industrial decor, is, as the name suggests, run by two chefs, Òscar Pérez and Mar Arnalot, the latter in charge of desserts. Their cuisine is centred around a menu of small plates/“raciones” perfect for sharing, enabling guests to taste a larger number of dishes (they recommend 3 or 4), with a continual focus on contemporary Catalan cooking with a hint of fusion influence. They also offer a good-value-for-money lunchtime menu, an interesting “Pica Pica” option (a minimum of two people), plus a more gastronomic menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4113;La Sartén;Spain;Tres Cantos;Sector de los Pueblos 2, Tres Cantos, 28760, Spain;40.6109118;-3.7136409;86;false;true;Fusion;A unique, surprising and somewhat eclectic restaurant which, despite its young age, clearly demonstrates the chef’s passion for cooking. In the kitchen, chef Elena García conjures up a contemporary, fusion-inspired à la carte that introduces cooking from different parts of the world to the palate, from the recipes of Latin America to the sublime tastes of Spanish cuisine and the intense flavours of Asia. Media-raciones, plates for sharing and highly interesting dishes that don’t feature on the menu are also available. One dish that we enjoyed in particular was the mussels with a green curry sauce – a delicious fusion between Galicia and the exotic flavours of India.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4114;Huerto Martínez;Spain;Cheste;Carretera Cheste-Chiva, Cheste, 46380, Spain;39.4883113;-0.688372;63;true;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant full of contrasts in which the simple decor is offset by a highly enticing menu. Occupying a country house just a few yards from the town’s sports hall, its traditional home cooking with plenty of modern and fusion influence comes as a pleasant surprise. Rice dishes (over 10 different options) are its speciality, with the creamy rice with rabbit and snails and the vegetable paella the pick of the bunch. Make sure you also try the superb foie gras terrine with a cinnamon galette and violet marmalade. We also recommend taking Toni’s advice when it comes to choosing your wine!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4115;Sierra Quil'ama;Spain;San Miguel de Valero;Paraje los Perales, San Miguel de Valero, 37763, Spain;40.541256;-5.919442;38;false;false;Spanish Contemporary;A hotel-restaurant with a somewhat surprising location in a small village in the Sierra Salmantina and an equally surprising name that refers to an unusual legend, the origins of which are still not completely clear, in which a Moorish princess is kidnapped by the Visigothic king Roderic. The pleasantly rustic dining rooms provide the setting for updated traditional cuisine that is only available via a single menu (from which guests can select from a variety of starters, mains and desserts, and the price of which remains the same at the weekend). We particularly recommend the rice and cep mushroom stew.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4116;Brots;Spain;Poboleda;Nou 45, Poboleda, 43376, Spain;41.23339;0.8445536;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional European;A gastronomic surprise tucked away in this small village in the Priorat region, nestled between mountains and surrounded by vineyards. Here, in this tranquil setting, chef Pieter Truyts, who has been trained in Michelin-starred restaurants in his native Belgium, as well as France and Spain, discovered the perfect place in which to “cook from the heart”, developing creative and highly interesting cuisine that showcases the very best local products, with a gift for combining them to maximise their flavour. Due to its excellent value for money, it is often full. The area is also renowned for its wine tourism.;Air conditioning;[]
4117;Hostal Colomí;Spain;Santa Coloma de Queralt;Raval de Jesús 10, Santa Coloma de Queralt, 43420, Spain;41.5333819;1.3833486;60;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Grills;It’s impossible to mention the Hostal Colomí without recognising the hard work put in by the Camps sisters, Nati and Rosita, as they are the pillars on which this centrally located and very popular family-run restaurant is built. The restaurant offers a welcoming dining room dominated by an open-view grill and a second room on the first floor which is reserved for groups and weekend dining. Full of flavour, the home-cooked dishes which come out of the kitchen are supplemented by numerous regional and traditional recipes. The delicious cep mushrooms with foie gras and fried eggs are well worth tasting!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4118;Ochando;Spain;Los Rosales;Sevilla 78, Los Rosales, 41330, Spain;37.5901344;-5.7333002;47;false;true;Contemporary;Los Rosales, a district on the outskirts of the town of Tocina in the province of Seville, has made its mark on the region’s culinary map thanks to a couple who decided to return to their roots having worked in prestigious restaurants such as Atrio, Casa Marcial, Bardal, etc. In this unpretentiously furnished eatery run by Juan Carlos Ochando (in the kitchen) and Elena Pérez (front of house), the contemporary cuisine on offer is firmly focused on seasonal ingredients, with half-plates available with some dishes. Don’t miss the arroz con leche with coconut, rum-infused pineapple and lime!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4119;Abastos 2.0 - Mesas;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Das Ameas 4, Santiago de Compostela, 15704, Spain;42.8800202;-8.5416156;28;true;true;Galician, Contemporary;Situated next to the busy Mercado de Abastos, this restaurant is highly recommended for anyone looking for a memorable gastronomic experience. The ambience is modern, casual and informal, with a kitchen partially visible from the dining room and, in a demonstration of complete transparency, precise information on the provenance of ingredients and even the distance from suppliers. The modern cooking here is centred on a daily à la carte, that varies in line with market availability, and two menus (Do Mercado and Da Casa), with a focus on Galician culinary traditions and top-quality local fish and seafood. Given its popularity, we recommend booking ahead.;Air conditioning;[]
4120;Bistrot 1965;Spain;Castelló d'Empúries;Santa Clara 31, Castelló d'Empúries, 17486, Spain;42.255818;3.0761205;29;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;There are some places, such as this restaurant occupying the former bar of the Hotel Emporium, that can pass almost unnoticed compared with their more famous siblings (the award-winning and elegant Emporium is also located here) due to the fact that they are simpler in style and more affordable to the public. Despite this, Bistrot 1965 is definitely somewhere with its own personality. Its cuisine, which is also overseen by brothers Màrius and Joan Jordà, is centred around a single fixed-price menu, to which you can also add more dishes from a list of specials. The aim of the tasty dishes designed for sharing is to provide an updated take on traditional recipes and to showcase the native ingredients of the Alt Empordà region.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4121;Aires de Doñana;Spain;El Rocío;Avenida de la Canaliega 1, El Rocío, 21750, Spain;37.1308369;-6.4901517;96;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The highly individual beauty of El Rocío derives from its people, its folklore and its spirituality, not forgetting, of course, its proximity to the superb landscapes of the Doñana National Park. In this restaurant, crowned by a thatched roof and featuring a decor typical of this marshland area, enjoy pleasantly updated traditional cuisine alongside a few typical local dishes such as steamed clams, Mostrenca veal, trammel net-caught prawns etc). The terrace is particularly pleasant with its splendid views overlooking the lagoon and the famous sanctuary of El Rocío as a backdrop.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4122;Cadelo;Spain;Santander;Santa Lucía 33, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.4643313;-3.8013494;15;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant on two floors with a striking façade and a contemporary yet informal decor, the name of which pays homage to a local poet who was renowned in Santander for selling his verses for just five pesetas! Here, you’ll find a concise, modern and fusion-inspired menu which is designed for sharing and supplemented by specials announced at your table. The cuisine is based on Spanish ingredients prepared in line with contemporary tastes and techniques to create dishes from around the world (Mexico, Korea, Peru etc). Make sure you save space for dessert, in particular the unforgettable cheesecake!;Air conditioning;[]
4123;Varra;Spain;Madrid;Hermosilla 7, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.42656;-3.68833;16;false;true;Contemporary;This restaurant in the elegant Salamanca district of the city is run by two young chefs, Jorge Velasco and Joaquín Serrano, and is usually full every day. It offers two highly distinct dining concepts: the informal Varra Fina on the ground floor (with a bar and bare tables), focusing on tapas such as Joselito ham croquettes, crispy bull’s ears, Russian salad etc), and the gourmet restaurant called Varra, upstairs. In the latter, somewhat confined in space but with a more refined decor and an exclusive menu completely different to Varra Fina the floor below, the level of cuisine rises several notches thanks to options such as snow peas with green asparagus and ham, and the chicken cannelloni with a truffled bechamel sauce and game jus. Make sure you book ahead and specify where you want to eat.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4124;La Capilleta;Spain;Plan;Carretera San Juan de Plan 7, Plan, 22367, Spain;42.5801078;0.3367735;68;false;false;Contemporary;One of the best eating options in the Bal de Chistau, a delightful valley nestled amid the mountains where you’ll also find a natural waterfall. Located at the entrance to the village, La Capilleta boasts a cosy dining room with a contemporary-Provençal feel, the occasional vintage touch, as well as a few references to the local “chistabino” dialect. Here, the chef creates seasonally based contemporary cooking alongside traditional dishes, plus a small choice of rice options cooked on the grill, such as rice with cep mushrooms and foie gras. The restaurant is also active in several anti-hunger campaigns.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
4125;Platero & Co;Spain;Gaucín;Los Bancos 9, Gaucín, 29480, Spain;36.5192237;-5.3169818;75;false;false;Contemporary;This village in the heart of the Serranía de Ronda could be described as the archetypal picture-postcard “pueblo blanco” given its setting nestling between mountains and its swathe of whitewashed houses. Run by a Dutch couple, the restaurant is a vision of perfection with its rustic ambience providing a backdrop for internationally inspired cuisine that has been given a more contemporary makeover, but always based around the very best local and seasonal products (chestnuts, cherries, wild mushrooms, goat’s cheese, figs etc). The terrace boasts stunning views of the valley and the Sierra de Grazalema.;Terrace;[]
4126;IZAKAYA Tasca Japonesa;Spain;Castelló de la Plana;Temprado 2, Castelló de la Plana, 12002, Spain;39.9838314;-0.0369147;84;true;true;Japanese;One of those restaurants that is causing quite a stir thanks to its total immersion in everyday Japanese cooking. The aim of this small, modest and informal “tasca”-style eatery (with space for just 16 guests) is to offer the purest Japanese cuisine possible, including powerful and intense flavours. Chef Sergio Ortega enjoys explaining each dish to his customers as well as relating interesting anecdotes from his many trips to Japan (mainly Tokyo). He offers a single surprise tasting menu that changes daily, with more of a focus on hot dishes (ramen, gyoza, edemam, stews etc) than on rice and raw fish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4127;Forastera;Spain;Valencia;Pintor Domingo 40, Valencia, 46001, Spain;39.4747439;-0.3835095;92;true;false;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant takes its name from the humorous description that Txisku Nuévalos gave to his wife Laura (who is originally from Bilbao) when he decided to return to his native region (he was born in Utiel, a town inland from Valencia) to set up his own business. This welcoming contemporary setting, run by the couple themselves, showcases updated traditional cuisine based around seasonal ingredients and a focus on small-scale producers. Choose between two surprise menus (Degustación and Forastera) that change in line with market availability and feature dishes that are delicate, delicious and use just a few ingredients to showcase each flavour.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4128;Eximio by Fernando Martín;Spain;Alcalá de Henares;Victoria 2, Alcalá de Henares, 28802, Spain;40.4801997;-3.3698566;39;true;true;Contemporary;If you’re visiting Alcalá de Henares, the birthplace of the famous writer Miguel de Cervantes, make sure you dine at this restaurant located just a few metres from Alcalá’s “Catedral Magistral” (the restaurant’s name, meaning “eminent” in English, is a nod to the “magistral” status of the cathedral). It is run by a chef who has learnt his trade in some of Spain’s leading restaurants such as at Martín Berasategui in Lasarte-Oria. His updated take on traditional cuisine is showcased on an à la carte, a good-value lunchtime menu (Monday to Friday), as well as on a more elaborate tasting-style menu that changes with the seasons. In the chef’s own words, his aim is to “ensure that every guest who walks through the door has a different gastronomic experience”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4129;Anaco;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Costa de San Domingos 2, Santiago de Compostela, 15703, Spain;42.882361;-8.5396233;20;true;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;We would all love a restaurant like this along our street! This pleasant eatery with its bare stone walls just a few steps from the Museo do Pobo Galego showcases the cuisine of Palencia-born chef Víctor Lobejón who, having trained in several renowned restaurants, followed his girlfriend to Santiago where he has opened his first solo venture. His personalised contemporary cooking gives pride of place to top-quality seasonal ingredients from Galicia on a concise à la carte that he explains in detail and always showcases seasonal Galician ingredients. We recommend booking ahead, allowing yourself time to visit the interesting wine cellar (it is run, as they like to say here, by a proper “wine waiter”) and ordering the #amesaposta menu, which changes daily and provides a splendid insight into his cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4130;La Fundición;Spain;San Ildefonso o La Granja;Plazuela de la Calandria 1, San Ildefonso o La Granja, 40100, Spain;40.9007073;-4.0049042;47;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;In the centre of La Granja, opposite the main post office and just a few minutes’ walk from the royal palace and its stunning gardens. The old building it occupies has given rise to the name of the restaurant (“The Foundry” in English), a reference to its previous incarnation, which provided the plumbing for both the royal palace and the old hospital. Today, as a result of a major revamp of the interior, it boasts several spaces with a unique rustic feel: the bar, the main dining room which once housed the forge, and the patio-terrace of the original infirmary. Choose between the à la carte and a menu featuring updated traditional cuisine with a nod to Asia and top-notch presentation.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4132;ConMimo;Spain;Leon;la Rúa 33, Leon, 24003, Spain;42.59652;-5.5698;97;true;true;International;Located in the centre of León, ConMimo is run by a couple (Javier in the kitchen and Ángela front of house) with a passion for cutting-edge, internationally inspired cuisine. Here, you’ll find dishes with impressive global influences from Italy, Japan, Peru, Mexico, France and elsewhere, as well as dishes influenced by regions closer to home, including Galicia, Andalucia and, of course, their own province of León. It also boasts a terrace (where guests can choose from a tapas-style menu), an informal bar space, plus more serious dining options in the room upstairs, with its open-view kitchen and choice of two tasting menus (Corta Distancia and Larga Distancia).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4133;Origen;Spain;Urdaitz;Carretera N 135, Urdaitz, 31698, Spain;42.9090915;-1.5339959;55;false;false;Contemporary;Located on the ground floor of an old stone building (the same one that houses the two-Michelin-star El Molino de UrdÁniz), Origen showcases the cooking of award-winning chef David Yárnoz, albeit in a much more informal and relaxed format. Directly accessed from the street, it features a rustic-contemporary dining room, bare wood tables and a single tasting menu, featuring dishes such as the delicious glazed and baked organic trout with pickled beetroot and parsnip, that adopts a contemporary take on traditional and regional dishes. The continual focus here is on seasonal and locally sourced ingredients, with the option of ordering half-portions.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4134;Can Ferrán;Spain;Sant Quirze del Vallès;Carretera de Rubí C 1413a, Sant Quirze del Vallès, 08192, Spain;41.5124685;2.0506522;25;false;false;Catalan;A family-run restaurant that is always full and has been delighting local palates since 1949! Located in a wooded area alongside a main road, it boasts a pleasant terrace, an attractive entrance hall and several spacious, bright dining rooms with a functional, contemporary feel and simple table settings. The cuisine here is focused on Catalan dishes with pride of place given to grilled dishes (sausage, rabbit, pigs’ trotters etc) and a variety of local specialities such as the famous Mongetes del Ganxet – tender white beans which are only grown in this part of Catalunya. The restaurant does not take credit cards although it does have an ATM!;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
4135;El Molín de Mingo;Spain;Peruyes;Finca Molín de Mingo, Peruyes, 33540, Spain;43.3855433;-5.0818996;92;false;false;Regional Cuisine;A rustic-style restaurant which continues to grow in popularity thanks to its secluded location surrounded by mountains – the type of place that diners return to time and time again! Here, owner-chef Dulce Martínez (also the wife of the famous chef Nacho Manzano) prepares superb, traditional home-style cuisine which is refined, delicate and full of flavour, with real attention to detail and presentation. There are two menus available here (one shorter than the other), both offering a choice of dishes. Don’t miss the homemade desserts or the unforgettable “pitu de calella con arroz” (a delicious dish made with rice and chicken).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4136;Bacira;Spain;Madrid;Castillo 16, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4338309;-3.6990876;94;true;false;Fusion;A successful business that extols the virtues of friendship, hard work and, above all, a love for cooking. These three pillars underpin this restaurant run with great dedication by the three owner-chefs, Carlos Langreo, Vicente de la Red and Gabriel Zapata, each of whom specialises in a different type of cuisine (traditional Mediterranean, Japanese and Nikkei) but who are receptive to new trends and inclined towards fusion cooking. The atmosphere here is both welcoming and informal with a vintage decor that includes striking wrought-iron columns that extend from the floor to the ceiling.;Air conditioning;[]
4137;El Cigró d'Or;Spain;Vilafranca del Penedès;Plaça de l'Oli 1, Vilafranca del Penedès, 08720, Spain;41.3477866;1.6963295;33;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant with a somewhat surprising location on the second floor of the Mercat de la Carn, hence the guaranteed quality and freshness of its ingredients and produce. Choose between the dining room and a bar counter from where guests can view the live action in the kitchen. In the latter, chef Oriol Llavina’s focus is on an updated take on Catalan cuisine with a constant desire to showcase locally sourced ingredients. The focus midweek is on set options (e.g. a daily menu and a daily tasting menu) with a switch to more à la carte-style service at the weekend. Make sure you try the delicious Gallo Negro chicken from Penedès!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
4138;Pementa Rosa;Spain;Carballo;Reus 1, Carballo, 15100, Spain;43.2166837;-8.6888439;29;false;true;Contemporary;Located in the centre of Carballo, this friendly, family-run restaurant continues to attract new customers daily! Chef Rocío Martínez was keen to spice up the dining options in the local Bergantiños region (“pementa” is the Galician word for “pepper”) with her updated take on traditional and regional cuisine with a touch of fusion, but always focusing on Galicia’s superb seasonal ingredients and paying homage to the gastronomic heritage of the Costa da Morte and with a strong emphasis on detail. A private dining room is also available for those requiring more privacy.;Air conditioning;[]
4139;Finca Alfoliz;Spain;Aljaraque;Carretera A-492 km 6,5, Aljaraque, 21110, Spain;37.2935619;-7.044933;78;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant with a strong focus on sustainability is a dream come true for chef Xanty Elías. Located on a family estate surrounded by fields of crops and protected areas, Finca Alfoliz enables its guests to enjoy its stunning natural surroundings to the full. The restaurant’s modern take on traditional cuisine includes a complete emphasis on seasonal organic products, although it also offers delicious rice dishes cooked in clay pots, grilled meats (including a choice of mature cuts) and fish from the local estuary. We particularly recommend the salted tuna and coriander “picadillo” from the coastal town of Isla Cristina (a typical miners’ recipe from the province of Huelva).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4140;San Sebastián 57;Spain;Santa Cruz de Tenerife;Avenida de San Sebastián 57, Santa Cruz de Tenerife, 38005, Spain;28.4636488;-16.2530444;72;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;An unmissable address in the island’s capital, this restaurant is located just a few steps from the Mercado de Nuestra Señora de África market (also known as La Recova) and is often full thanks to its popularity with tourists as well as a loyal local clientele. In the contemporary ambience of its pleasant, intimate interior, enjoy an updated take on traditional cuisine presented via the à la carte and a menu entitled Caminar. Quality ingredients are key here, contributing to fun, copious and meticulously presented dishes that showcase the essence of Canarian cuisine, with an added nod to the cooking of Cantabria (chef Alberto González hails from Santander) and countries around Latin America. An impressive choice of market-inspired daily specials are also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4141;Espacio Amunt;Spain;Ulldecona;Barri Castell, Ulldecona, 43550, Spain;40.6110033;0.3310067;93;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In this bistro, occupying the first floor of the award-winning L'Antic Molí but with its own separate entrance, chef Vicent Guimerà has diversified the food options available through cuisine which still reflects the essence of his cooking but in a more informal way. Based around tradition but with a few contemporary touches, his two menus (Bistró and Gran Bistró) continue to extol the virtues of seasonal ingredients from the Terres de l'Ebre, Terres del Sénia and the Parc Natural dels Ports. Dishes you’ll find on these menus includes chicken ravioli in broth, rice with cod and romesco sauce, and veal with quince and cauliflower.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4142;Az-Zait;Spain;Seville;Plaza de San Lorenzo 1, Seville, 41002, Spain;37.3968514;-5.9964807;19;true;false;Contemporary;This restaurant, which takes its name from an Arabic word meaning "olive juice" (oil) is constantly developing, demonstrating technical expertise and conviction in all its dishes. It features two classic-style dining rooms in which to enjoy impeccable service, plus extra details such as an impressive cheese trolley and its own home-produced olive oil. Its concise à la carte of traditional and international dishes with modern touches is accompanied by three enticing tasting menus named after olive oil estates: Hacienda el Monje, El Lavadero and Cerro de los Olivos.;Air conditioning;[]
4143;Juan Mari;Spain;San Pedro del Pinatar;Emilio Castelar 113 C, San Pedro del Pinatar, 30740, Spain;37.8276439;-0.7868152;73;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The most striking features of this restaurant are the care and enthusiasm on display every day – a key component in any family-run business. Located in the centre of town, it boasts a contemporary-style dining room and a small outside terrace, where guests can savour locally inspired traditional cuisine with a contemporary touch that is abundant and always well presented. The à la carte, encompassing an array of rice dishes and delicious specialities such as the carpaccio of artichokes with crispy Iberian ham and the mouthwatering turbot with “patatas a lo pobre”, is complemented by a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4144;La Alquería;Spain;Ráfales;Plaza Mayor 9, Ráfales, 44589, Spain;40.8375465;0.0203601;22;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Located on the main square and run by the owner, La Alquería serves updated traditional cuisine of a high standard, including a surprise tasting menu option. In the kitchen, Clara Lapuente demonstrates a strong preference for locally sourced ingredients, and her previous experience as a pastry chef ensures that all dishes are cooked to perfection, including a delicious selection of desserts. The restaurant is located on the ground floor of a charming small hotel, so guests staying the night can take advantage of a special fixed-price dinner menu. Booking is essential.;Air conditioning;[]
4145;Tándem;Spain;Murcia;Cánovas del Castillo 37, Murcia, 30003, Spain;37.9848155;-1.1248484;41;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;María José and Pedro, supported by their enthusiastic team, are the “tandem” behind this small yet welcoming restaurant located close to the city’s bullring. Here, the menu is steered towards simple yet well-executed Mediterranean cooking supported by top-quality ingredients. Dishes come in half portions, are very much designed for sharing, and are showcased on an à la carte that is always “alive” and changes with the seasons – a theme highlighted in its title: “today’s menu, who knows about tomorrow”! Dishes that particularly piqued our curiosity included the delicious anchovies with butter and fig jam, served on a plate held by the figurine of a woman. It’s not a bad idea to eat at the bar to experience every stage of the cooking process.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4146;Moral;Spain;Santa Cruz de Tenerife;Jesús Nazareno 20, c/ Pi Y Margall, Santa Cruz de Tenerife, 38003, Spain;28.4682876;-16.25398;81;true;true;Contemporary;Moral occupies an old mansion that skilfully combines the building’s cutting-edge design with its original structure and floor. The key tenets here are a constant desire to improve alongside plenty of enthusiasm from the young chefs (Icíar and Juan Carlos) at the helm. They are now following their own dream having previously worked in leading restaurants (Icíar Pérez, for example, was the chef at Poemas by Hermanos Padrón). Their cuisine, which first and foremost aims to showcase the flavours of the island, is centred around a concise à la carte plus a creatively inspired tasting menu, with a continual focus on excellent technique and superb textures (as we discovered in the skate with a mussel and parsley sauce). The tasting menu also provides a perfect opportunity to explore the culinary identity of the Canary Islands in more detail.;Air conditioning;[]
4147;Casa Bigote;Spain;Sanlúcar de Barrameda;Pórtico de Bajo de Guía 10, Sanlúcar de Barrameda, 11540, Spain;36.7893085;-6.3514916;84;false;true;Seafood;This family-run restaurant opened its doors in 1951 as a simple seaside “taberna” serving Manzanilla sherry to the weather-beaten fishermen from the town’s Bajo de Guía district. Over the years, Fernando Bigote and his children have gradually expanded the business. Nowadays, it still boasts a typical “taberna”, where you can eat an array of tapas and “raciones”, as well as two neo-rustic dining rooms decorated in a maritime style, with the room upstairs perhaps the more impressive thanks to its views of the mouth of the Guadalquivir. Choose from delicious fried delicacies, fish and seafood stews, local fish and, above all, the spectacular Sanlúcar prawns for which the restaurant is renowned and which are a must here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4148;Los Sentidos;Spain;Linares;Doctor 13, Linares, 23700, Spain;38.0917445;-3.6298343;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Los Sentidos occupies a restored house with an imposing stone façade in the centre of town, behind which the contemporary design of its dining rooms comes as something of a surprise. Owner-chef Juan Pablo Gámez is strongly committed to contemporary cuisine that showcases the bygone flavours and history of Jaén, adapting regional recipes with his modern culinary techniques. The à la carte, which always features plenty of daily suggestions, is complemented by two tasting menus: “GastrÓleO”, which extols the virtues of extra virgin olive oil, and “Un guiño a la TIERRA” (literally, “A Nod to the Land”), the latter only available by booking ahead.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4149;Lavedán;Spain;Tramacastilla de Tena;Navero 19, Tramacastilla de Tena, 22663, Spain;42.7154666;-0.3164658;91;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;A restaurant with a rustic atmosphere that is considered a classic address in the Valle de Tena. Occupying what was once a stable, it is now run by a young couple, with Sergio at the helm in the kitchen and Carla in charge of the dining room. Lavedán has definitely moved with the times while retaining its full personality through its focus on the culinary traditions of the Aragonese Pyrenees area and its “mountain gastronomy”. The cooking here is based around an updated take on local and regionally inspired dishes (Migas de Milagros, blanquette of veal with spices, grilled sturgeon etc), with a choice of the à la carte, a daily menu or a tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
4150;Umma;Spain;Santander;Sol 47, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.4653779;-3.7978523;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant on two levels which we like both for its cuisine and for its informal, New York-style decor, featuring high ceilings adorned with surprising reproductions of cave paintings, and bright brick walls. Here, young owner-chef Miguel Ángel Rodríguez focuses on modern cuisine with a contemporary touch, which he makes accessible to all through delicious and harmonious creations that look to the future while still taking inspiration from the traditions of the past. Attentive service plus copious dishes perfect for sharing complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4151;A Horta d'Obradoiro;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Hortas 16, Santiago de Compostela, 15705, Spain;42.8808002;-8.5469959;19;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This impressively unique restaurant serves interesting cuisine while at the same time showcasing a part of Santiago’s rich history. Run by two chefs, it occupies a house dating back to 1690 which was once home to musicians from the nearby cathedral. It features a combination of contemporary and regional decor, a wine bar made from old beams, colourful details that are reminiscent of old beach huts, a conservatory-style room, plus a garden with a vegetable plot which is a real luxury in this part of the city. Carefully prepared and beautifully presented seasonal cuisine.;Wheelchair access;[]
4152;La Cava d'en Sergi;Spain;Sant Sadurní d'Anoia;València 17, Sant Sadurní d'Anoia, 08770, Spain;41.427102;1.7811167;62;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Sant Sadurní d'Anoia is the capital of sparking cava, so this restaurant provides a great opportunity to round off your day after a visit to some of its famous bodegas. Located in a central street in the heart of the town, it features a single dining room with a classic-contemporary feel, where owner-chef Sergi Torres creates updated traditional cuisine with a good sprinkling of creativity. Choose between an excellent set daily menu popular with guests, and a seasonally changing à la carte. The wine cellar features over 40 different local cavas.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4153;Café de Altamira;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Ameas 9, Santiago de Compostela, 15704, Spain;42.8804902;-8.5414465;25;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Its strapline, “the flavour of the market”, says it all! This friendly restaurant in the Pazo de Altamira hotel (with its own entrance and independent management) comes as a pleasant surprise with its decor of light bulbs hanging from the ceiling, unusual bottle racks and colourful tableware by Sargadelos, all of which create a rustic yet vintage feel. At its large tables designed for sharing, discover pleasantly updated traditional cooking with plenty of personality and a philosophy that showcases the flavours of Galician cuisine (we particularly enjoyed the lightly roasted mackerel with “ajoblanco” and cherry-ponzu tomato) both on the à la carte and its enticing tasting menus (Ameas and Altamira). The restaurant’s location right next to the busy food market also ensures that its ingredients are of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4154;Berdó;Spain;El Puerto de Santa María;Avenida del Puerto, El Puerto de Santa María, 11500, Spain;36.5814202;-6.2575485;81;false;true;Contemporary;In this pleasant restaurant on the ground floor of the Las Suites hotel overlooking the Puerto Sherry, choose between the charming terrace with views of the dock and the pleasure craft moored here or the urban-contemporary interior with its recycled furniture. The chef’s modern cooking, which features ingredients from both the land and sea and which he describes as “entrevientos” (“between the prevailing winds”), extols the full virtues of Andalucian recipes (prawns with garlic, skate fricassee, roasted aubergines, cuttlefish stew etc), almost all of which are available as full or half raciones, enabling guests to try lots of dishes and to create their own personalised menu. The name “Berdó” is a word used in the Caló gypsy dialect to describe a type of boat.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
4155;El Rebojo;Spain;Garachico;Francisco Martínez de Fuentes 17, Garachico, 38450, Spain;28.3737461;-16.764464;54;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;In this attractive restaurant, located close to San Miguel castle, the popular “El Caletón” natural pools” and the many viewpoints found in this delightful fishing community, the focus is on updated Canary Island cuisine. The section of the à la carte entitled “Bocados del Mar” (literally “sea bites”), is a particularly pleasant surprise, with its selection of small plates influenced by the culinary traditions of the Canaries, as are the well-priced options that include drinks (two “bocados” and two wines, and four “bocados” and four wines). Two tasting menus (Marea Vacía and Marea Llena) which focus on the known as the Isla Baja are also available. Make sure you order the delicious cheesecake, made with a local cheese that is smoked as part of its production process.;;[]
4156;Casa Mané;Spain;Palmones;Almadraba, Palmones, 11379, Spain;36.176258;-5.4271564;44;false;true;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;This simple family-run restaurant, located just a few metres from the village beach and boasting views of Gibraltar across the bay, occupies an attractive wood cabin with a bar area and two attractively appointed dining rooms. Although it offers an extensive traditionally based à la carte, its main specialities are fish and seafood from the waters around Gibraltar (Coquina clams, red prawns from Garrucha, tuna in lard etc), with many of its fresh products displayed in a refrigerated counter in one of the dining rooms. It’s best to book ahead here as it is invariably full every day!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4157;La Martina;Spain;Tarancón;La Noria 8, Tarancón, 16400, Spain;40.0169953;-3.0144824;21;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Its owners describe La Martina as “a little gem”, an apt description given that this pretty restaurant occupies part of their own home! Situated in a residential district of chalets on the outskirts of Tarancón, this bright, charming restaurant is striking for its classic-contemporary decor which boasts numerous tasteful details and a predominantly white colour scheme. La Martina features an attractive dining room with a fireplace at one end, plus the Salón de Cristal, a pleasant glass-fronted porch. The cuisine has its roots in the region, reinterpreting the specialities of La Mancha through modern techniques and presentation.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4158;Casa Toni;Spain;San Vicente de la Sonsierra;Zumalacárregui 27, San Vicente de la Sonsierra, 26338, Spain;42.5615699;-2.7582599;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A modern and contemporary restaurant that comes as quite a surprise in this village anchored at the foot of a walled castle-fortress with streets steeped in history and buildings fronted by beautiful stone façades. In this eclectic and unexpected setting, the modern interior, dominated by the contrasts between red and white, features numerous references to wine production, providing the backdrop for cuisine with a strong Rioja flavour that combines typical recipes such as “Patorrillo a la Riojana” (lamb’s tripe and trotters) with other more contemporary-style dishes. An interesting gastronomic menu completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4159;Alba;Spain;Alacant;Virgen del Socorro 68, Alacant, 03002, Spain;38.3514864;-0.4736376;34;true;false;Contemporary;The fusion of local Alicante and Italian cuisine on offer in this attractive and intimate eatery in a residential district comes as a pleasant surprise, and is explained by the culinary experiences of chef Alba Esteve during her stints working in several prestigious restaurants in Italy. Choose between the à la carte (interesting off-menu options such as fresh fish of the day are also available) and an enticing tasting menu. We loved the delicious and refreshing lemon and yuzu tartlet dessert with yuzu and a lime and celery sorbet.;Air conditioning;[]
4160;Perro Limón;Spain;Murcia;Plaza de San Juan 6, Murcia, 30003, Spain;37.9828129;-1.1261415;39;true;false;Fusion;If you’re looking for something different you’ll find it here, as the focus of the couple in charge (María and Miguel Ángel) is on fusion cooking that combines the flavours of India, Morocco, France, Japan etc. It now boasts a more spacious layout following its move to a new central location in Plaza de San Juan as well as an unmistakeable appearance thanks to a striking yellow door that provides access to this relaxed bistro. The à la carte, with its strong focus on sharing, is surprising for its so-called “Bocados del Mundo” (Mouthfuls of the World), which are complemented by a section entitled “Algo más Serio” (Something More Serious) on which we particularly enjoyed the brioche with a veal ragout, spiced butter and white truffle, and desserts under the heading “Un buen recuerdo” (A Happy Memory). A tasting menu (Origen) is also an option here.;Air conditioning;[]
4161;La Taberna de Mike Palmer;Spain;Malaga;Camino de los Almendrales, Malaga, 29013, Spain;36.7443351;-4.3931692;61;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A rustic-cum-contemporary restaurant that oozes tranquillity, simplicity and a sense of calm – virtues that largely stem from its location within an equestrian club on the outskirts of Málaga, behind the hills that frame the city. Here, you can enjoy updated traditional cuisine that will leave its mark and linger long in the memory thanks to its focus on ingredients sourced from the soil and sea which maximise Mediterranean flavours in simply prepared slow-cooked dishes, mainly on the open grill. If possible, book a table on the delightful terrace.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4162;La Taberna de Cuatro Caminos;Spain;Almodóvar del Río;Antonio Machado 24, Almodóvar del Río, 14720, Spain;37.8103332;-5.017674;78;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant that has already enjoyed success in the town under the name La Taberna (the owners also have another eatery in Córdoba called La Taberna de Almodóvar) and has reopened its doors as La Taberna de Cuatro Caminos. Simple terrace, a bar boasting a touch of local colour, plus three dining rooms, all of which are traditional in feel but feature unusual Andalucian detail in their decor. Tasty, regionally inspired cooking with a focus on substantial yet attractively presented local dishes and popular specialities that include its famous croquettes, along with Mazamorra de Almodóvar and Salmorejo Cordobés.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4163;El Molino;Spain;Madrigal de la Vera;Garganta de Alardos, Madrigal de la Vera, 10480, Spain;40.1560532;-5.3610677;88;true;false;Contemporary;Situated on the banks of the Alardos gorge in a natural and peaceful setting, this authentic restaurant occupies a restored mill with old stone walls. There’s an attractive bar area at the entrance (with a fireplace and a few unusual tables made from the mill’s old grinding stones) and a simple dining room, both of which are decorated in a warm, rustic style. The restaurant serves just one surprise tasting menu, which is contemporary in flavour yet with strong traditional roots, and which focuses on fresh, locally sourced vegetables. The wine list features a choice of natural wines from small wine-producers.;Car park;[]
4164;Granero;Spain;Quintanar de la Orden;San Fernando 90, Quintanar de la Orden, 45800, Spain;39.5966829;-3.0474651;64;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family restaurant run by siblings with over half a century of history behind it. One of the culinary jewels in the crown of La Mancha, Granero features a bar at the entrance, serving the set menu and a choice of “raciones”, plus a pleasant à la carte dining room and an attractive patio-terrace. Choose between the à la carte featuring traditional and fusion-inspired contemporary cuisine and a superb tasting menu with a wine-pairing option. The impressive cellar is managed by enthusiastic sommelier Adán Israel, who is always on hand to recommend and promote wines from the local area.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4165;La Tarara;Spain;Olvera;Plaza Andalucía, Olvera, 11690, Spain;36.9348639;-5.264054;91;true;true;Contemporary;La Tarara is one of those restaurants where, having worked in renowned restaurants around Spain, its owners decided to return to their home region to start this highly personal project. Fronting a square in the centre of town, the restaurant boasts a pleasantly surprising contemporary feel along with a few unusual decorative details such as verses from La Tarara by Federico García Lorca (the children’s song from which it takes its name) adorning the walls. The cuisine here is an updated version of traditional Andalucian dishes, in which almost all the ingredients are sourced locally or from the province of Cádiz. Make sure you try its version of the Italian “payogiana” as well as the croissant of red tuna tartare. The tasting menu here is announced “by word of mouth”!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4166;Alma Ezequiel Montilla;Spain;Puente Genil;Cuesta Borrego 3, Puente Genil, 14500, Spain;37.387969;-4.7783671;17;true;false;International;A restaurant that continues to win plaudits, especially following its move to this unique century-old mansion boasting an array of arches, azulejos and Arabian-inspired lattice windows. Its most impressive feature is without doubt the stunning central patio crowned by a glass roof. The culinary experience gained by the chef abroad is obvious in the names of the dining rooms (London, Marrakech, Casablanca etc) and on the menu, where dishes are centred on gastronomic journeys around Spain, Morocco and Europe. Make sure you leave space for the splendid desserts!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4167;Berbena;Spain;Barcelona;Minerva 6, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.3965158;2.1565422;28;true;false;Creative;A diminutive, unpretentious and informal restaurant with a name that pays homage to the traditional “berbena” festivals. Here, you can enjoy chef Carles Pérez de Rozas Canut’s cooking to the full, with his focus on simple yet highly captivating dishes based around seasonal Mediterranean ingredients, but which also feature influences from Asia and South America. Personality in spades, with an open kitchen and enticing recipes that tell us lots about the chef, his travels and his work in other countries. The superb desserts complete the picture!;Counter dining;[]
4168;La Cartería;Spain;Cartes;Camino Real 49, Cartes, 39311, Spain;43.3264173;-4.0687364;50;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Cartes is a small town of particular interest along the historic “camino real” that once connected the region of Castille with the port of Santander. Here, in this 17C mansion that once served as the post office, chef Enrique Pérez offers his guests updated traditional cuisine that is delicate and lovingly prepared, with a focus on presentation and flavours that will leave their mark on the palate. The welcoming, rustically inspired dining room is complemented by a few tables beneath a balcony at the entrance – a perfect setting for a drink as you watch the world go by in one of the country’s most delightful streets!;;[]
4169;Vinoteca Moratín;Spain;Madrid;Moratín 36, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4125625;-3.695362;83;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;One way of describing the food at Vinoteca Moratín would be to say that it partly mirrors the space in which it is served and reflects the passion of its owner-chef Marcos Gil, who heads to the market every day to select the very best ingredients. This intimate restaurant, which is not particularly remarkable or obvious from the street outside, is striking for its smart, modern and minimalist decor and cosy little corners, such as the small shelves where books and bottles of wine are arranged side by side. Personalised service and a concise, traditionally inspired menu featuring delicious soups and stews. Booking is essential!;Air conditioning;[]
4170;Casa Marco;Spain;Vigo;Avenida García Barbón 123, Vigo, 36201, Spain;42.238136;-8.7103685;56;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A particularly interesting option if you’re looking for elaborate traditional cuisine as an alternative to the usual fish and seafood on offer in the area. In addition, the restaurant has a classic, contemporary-style elegance, with a striking dining room to the rear which boasts a large window offering views of the chef at work in the kitchen. The à la carte features a good choice of meats (including IGP Castilla y León lamb), along with some rice dishes, fish straight from the market, and mouth-watering specialities such as baked loin of cod with onions and “panadera” potatoes, fried milk “dados” with orange on light Amaretto-flavoured natillas custard, and the baked local cheesecake with galleta biscuits.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4171;Carmen;Spain;Binéfar;Avenida de Nuestra Señora del Pilar 3, Binéfar, 22500, Spain;41.8515864;0.2928459;92;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant is located in the same building as the largest farming auction in Spain, where the price of beef in other auctions depends largely on prices here. Given the above, it’s no surprise to see this restaurant, which started life in nearby Tamarite de Litera before moving here, taking full advantage of the choice cuts of meats from this area. Chef Iván Vilanova serves up unpretentious dishes with a focus on seasonal ingredients and an impressive menu, always striving to create delicious cuisine where the ingredients themselves take centre stage.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4172;La MaMá;Spain;Madrid;Avenida del Brasil 6, Madrid, 28020, Spain;40.45395;-3.69348;16;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The essence of this restaurant remains unaltered in its new location on Avenida de Brasil, where it is run with total dedication by María Brufau and chef Marcos Toranzo, the latter trained at the Luis Irizar cookery school and at the award-winning El Ermitaño restaurant. In this contemporary setting featuring touches of elegance, choose between an à carte featuring big-hearted traditional cuisine which is impressively complemented by two tasting menus (Los Clásicos and the seasonally inspired De Temporada).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4173;Terra Palencia;Spain;Palencia;Pedro Fernández de Pulgar 6, Palencia, 34005, Spain;42.007787;-4.5333929;61;false;false;Contemporary;Having trained in a string of prestigious restaurants (El Celler de Can Roca, Akelaŕe, Nerua and El Ermitaño), chef Roberto Terradillos has returned to his roots to showcase his new talents, combining the latest techniques with the culinary flavours of his home province. The interior is functional and contemporary in feel, while the cooking follows contemporary trends albeit with a good basis in tradition and a nod to his native region. The à la carte is complemented by several interesting fixed menus: “De Mercado”, available lunchtimes midweek, and three others with a wine pairing option (Gastronómico, Clásico and Degustación).;Air conditioning;[]
4174;Farragua;Spain;Gijón;Contracay 3, Gijón, 33201, Spain;43.5443359;-5.6630782;80;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this unusual bistro-style restaurant just a few metres from the Plaza Mayor and the ever-busy marina, the self-proclaimed aim is to create “inquisitive and evolving” cuisine. What is certain is that Farragua’s updated take on traditional dishes features plenty of fusion influences and nods to Extremadura, the native region of chef Ricardo Fernández Señorán, who is particularly at ease working with locally sourced and seasonal ingredients which he uses to create his signature escabeches. His cooking is firmly focused on his tasting menus: Asina, Mangurrino, Dejalamío and El Miajón. The restaurant has also developed a concept entitled “Arrieros” (named after the men who, in the past, would transport food from one community to the next), as part of which invited chefs help to create four-hand menus.;;[]
4176;La Oveja Negra;Spain;Barbastro;Oncinellas 5, Barbastro, 22300, Spain;42.0359715;0.1264731;75;true;false;Contemporary;With a name that translates as “the black sheep”, this gastronomic restaurant is gradually winning over a larger flock of clientele! The young couple at the helm, Rafa Bautista in the kitchen and María Vegue overseeing the dining room, put their life and soul into every sitting, serving modern dishes with a traditional flavour that showcase the ingredients and produce of the Somontano de Barbastro area but with a constant nod to the south of the country as a reminder of the chef’s roots. The constantly evolving à la carte, featuring “media ración” options, is complemented by a daily menu. We particularly enjoyed the “leche texturizada de Sieso” dessert, made with milk from the Villa Villera farm.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4177;El Recetario;Spain;Gijón;Trinidad 1, Gijón, 33201, Spain;43.5446984;-5.6629946;29;true;false;Contemporary;This restaurant on the edge of the historic Cimadevilla district describes itself as an “urban, market-inspired restaurant”. What is certain is that Álex Sampedro’s cooking has moved away from the more commonplace dishes of the area to focus on an updated take on traditional cuisine that demonstrates high levels of technical skill in dishes featuring subtle seasoning, fine textures and the freshest seasonal ingredients (foie gras pizza, hake balls with a prawn sauce, "El Recetario"-style tripe etc). It also boasts a bar at the entrance where you can order various sharing plates, plus a simple and contemporary-style dining room in the basement. We recommend ordering El Recetario’s daily specials or create your own menu based around a selection of half plates.;Air conditioning;[]
4178;El Racó de Pere i Pepa;Spain;El Pinós;Carretera de Jumilla 26, El Pinós, 03650, Spain;38.4021209;-1.0444166;89;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant run by married couple Pere and Pepa, with the former in the kitchen and the latter in charge of the dining room. Located along the avenue leading into town from Jumilla, it boasts a terrace at the entrance and an interior with two floors decorated in a rustic, contemporary style. On his à la carte and tasting menu, Pepe focuses on regional and a more modern take on Mediterranean cuisine. His aim is to rediscover the flavours of inland Alicante province via an impressive selection of rice dishes (the rice with rabbit, snails and truffles is a must!) and enticing specialities such as the tenderloin with foie gras, apple and port wine sauce, and the traditionally roasted shoulder of goat. Themed food days dedicated to truffles (March) and suckling pig (November) are also organised here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4179;Lalola de Javi Abascal;Spain;Seville;Marco Sancho 1, Seville, 41003, Spain;37.3971909;-5.9919358;85;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Given its location in the 18C One Shot Palacio Conde de Torrejón hotel, this restaurant in Seville’s historic centre is easy to find. The restaurant, which has its own entrance to the side of the building and has its main dining room on an attractive covered patio, is run by a chef who prepares traditional cuisine with a contemporary touch. This is showcased on the à la carte and on an interesting tasting menu which is completely focused around Iberian pork (including the desserts!). Dishes you’ll find here include creamy rice with pig’s trotters and rice, “lagartito” of Iberian pork en papillote with cod, plus different types of game.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4180;Mesón Nelia;Spain;Villalba de la Sierra;Carretera Cuenca-Tragacete, Villalba de la Sierra, 16140, Spain;40.231415;-2.0884093;32;false;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with a good reputation in the region, having been run by the same family for the past three generations. It boasts a modern, functional bar (where the daily set menu is also served), a dining room with a fireplace, and a huge reception room that is used for private events. The owner-chef serves updated traditional cuisine from Cuenca, including dishes such as “copita de ajoarriero” with apricots, cod with “pisto manchego”, and pigs’ trotters stuffed with goats’ cheese featuring on the menu. The restaurant also offers a number of rural houses for rent in the attractive surroundings of the Júcar river.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4181;Terra Olea;Spain;Córdoba;Rigoberta Menchú 2, Córdoba, 14011, Spain;37.8963188;-4.7973683;64;false;true;Contemporary, Andalusian;Located in the Arruzafilla district, close to its previous incarnation, this restaurant boasts a bright dining room from where the kitchen is partially visible to diners. The chef, who serves some of his dishes in person, conjures up cuisine that is contemporary in feel and showcases local products with the minimum of fuss, focusing on the best products from the Córdoba region and in particular its small producers. The cuisine here features a two interesting tasting menus, named Flos and Cibarium respectively, in reference to olives and their historical importance. The unique lamps hanging above the tables look like giant wasps’ nests!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4182;12 Tapas;Spain;Castilleja de la Cuesta;Párroco Antonio Pastor Portillo 2, Castilleja de la Cuesta, 41950, Spain;37.3877013;-6.0481407;46;false;false;Contemporary;A gastro-bar-inspired eatery with the heart and soul of an authentic restaurant run by couple Túe García, who left a career in radio for one in the kitchen, and Carolina Jurado, who was a family doctor before switching to front-of-house restaurant management. 12 Tapas has a name that is somewhat deceptive, as it is the owner-chef’s homage to his mother and to the 12 grandchildren that she had when it first opened (Garcia learnt everything from her and his grandmother – both professional cooks). Here, the traditionally based contemporary cuisine is showcased on a concise à la carte plus two extensive tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4185;Villa de Oro;Spain;Camariñas;Areal 5, Camariñas, 15123, Spain;43.13108;-9.18279;61;true;true;Seafood;If you happen to be travelling along the Costa da Morte and are looking for a good place to eat, it is well worth booking a table at Villa de Oro, a third-generation restaurant that has already celebrated its golden wedding anniversary! Located in the centre of Camariñas, on the ground floor of a residential building, it boasts a recently modernised dining room, a small glass-fronted wine cellar and a live seafood tank. The traditional, regionally inspired à la carte is, as you would expect in this part of the world, heavily focused on fish and seafood, although a choice of meat dishes is also available.;Air conditioning;[]
4186;Pan de Cuco;Spain;Suesa;Barrio Calabazas 17, Suesa, 39150, Spain;43.4408833;-3.7156073;51;false;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This attractive large house by the main road boasts an unusual name (a type of sorrel that is found in fields of maize) and cuisine that comes as a pleasant surprise. It features a pleasant terrace, a gastro-bar with high tables perfect for tapas and raciones, plus a contemporary dining room with a rustic decor. The cooking here takes its inspiration from both the region and what’s in season, including top-quality local fish, delicious steak tartare, and tasty stews prepared with Pedresa chicken, a breed that is commonly known as “picasuelo” in Cantabria. Make sure you try the house Russian salad, a homage to this renowned dish from the Bodega del Riojano in Santander.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4187;Ca´n Boqueta;Spain;Sóller;Avenida de la Gran Via 43, Sóller, 07100, Spain;39.7679667;2.7115715;63;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Located in the centre of Sóller, one of Mallorca’s most picturesque towns, and easily accessible from Palma, including via the island’s historic train with its traditional wooden carriages. The restaurant occupies a typical Mallorcan house with an impeccable rustic decor and a particularly attractive rear patio with fine views of the valley and its famous orange groves. To this backdrop, owner-chef Xisco Martorell offers guests his updated and innovative take on Mallorcan cuisine that can be enjoyed on two tasting menus – a simpler offering at lunchtime with a more elaborate option in the evening.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4188;Las Tortillas de Gabino;Spain;Madrid;Rafael Calvo 20, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4339367;-3.6940302;55;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Impressively run by two siblings, this restaurant adopted its name in homage to the chef at La Ancha, a popular restaurant in Madrid that was founded by his grandfather in the 1930s. Las Tortillas de Gabino is located in the heart of the city’s Chamberí district, where it features a cosy entrance hall, a private section, a glass-fronted wine cellar, and two contemporary dining rooms which interconnect via a corridor that leads to the kitchen, which is always visible to diners. The updated traditional menu is complemented by a superb choice of omelettes (tortillas), the most popular of which are the traditional potato-based Velazqueña, and the Trufada.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4189;El Envero;Spain;Córdoba;Teruel 21, Córdoba, 14011, Spain;37.8985515;-4.7886147;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Although located away from the tourist section of the city, El Envero has fast developed a solid reputation and loyal clientele, who can dine to a backdrop of modern decor in the tapas bar, dining room and private section. The chef here has a passion for contemporary, seasonal cuisine (including daily specials and a media-ración option with some dishes) with a focus on organic produce from local vegetable gardens as well as different types of tuna. The name “Elvero” refers to the moment at which grapes change colour as they begin to ripen.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4190;Arrieros;Spain;Linares de la Sierra;Arrieros 2, Linares de la Sierra, 21207, Spain;37.8793;-6.62185;30;false;false;Regional Cuisine;A great option if you’re visiting the Sierra de Aracena, its nature reserve, or Linares de la Sierra, a beautiful town of attractive cobbled streets. Run and owned by a married couple, Arrieros occupies a typical whitewashed mountain property with a welcoming rustic interior that features an attractive fireplace, wood ceilings and rustic-contemporary furnishings with an eye for tasteful detail. The chef’s emphasis here is on an updated take on regional-style cooking in which Iberian pork takes centre stage, with a particular focus on offal. This focus is showcased on the two tasting menus (Ruta de Jabugo and La Dehesa). Signature dishes include Iberian pork tongue, pork “castañetas” with curry and mashed potato, and the famous tomato soup, Arrieros’ version of the Andalucian “poleá”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4191;Aureum by Picualia;Spain;Bailén;Autovía A4 Madrid-Cádiz KM. 298, Bailén, 23710, Spain;38.09227;-3.79239;61;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re tempted by a dining experience that revolves around extra-virgin olive oil, then Aureum, located inside the Picualia olive oil cooperative, could be the place. In addition to educational tours, tastings and other olive oil-related activities for visitors, you’ll also find a wine bodega next door to this attractive restaurant. In his cooking, head chef Paco Simón clearly demonstrates that olive oil is the star of the show here, with a strong nod to local tradition both on the à la carte and his two tasting menus (Labora Oliva and Fenologicum).;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4192;Kàran Bistró;Spain;Pozoblanco;Plaza de la Constitución 1, Pozoblanco, 14400, Spain;38.3774164;-4.8487398;30;false;true;Creative;In this restaurant, located in the heart of the Los Pedroches valley, they like to say that “you don’t just come here to eat, but also to have fun”. In this intimate and attractive setting, the high level of cuisine comes as a pleasant surprise. The cooking is completely centred on the renowned local Iberian pork, including the finest cuts of acorn-fed ham (pluma, presa etc) as well as produce from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden. Chef Carlos Fernández is committed to showcasing the best possible flavours from the local area on a modern à la carte complemented by two excellent set menus: De Temporada and Nuestra Dehesa.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4193;Can Xapes;Spain;Cornellà del Terri;Mossèn Jacint Verdaguer 2, Cornellà del Terri, 17844, Spain;42.0891914;2.8160663;91;true;true;Contemporary;Can Xapes is much more than a restaurant thanks to its history (it started out as a cinema in 1949). It is also part of the non-profit “AD' Iniciatives Socials” organisation, which provides work opportunities for youngsters with limited financial resources and access to training. Nowadays operating as a restaurant school, it highlights its links with the past via the original Art Deco-style bar counter from the former Rosa cinema. It also features attractive dining rooms where guests can savour Catalan cuisine with a contemporary feel on three menus (De Temporada, De Cine and Degustación) based, where possible, on locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
4194;Mas Concas;Spain;L'Escala;Camí de Cinc Claus, L'Escala, 17130, Spain;42.1373158;3.1006407;48;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Here, the culinary experience is considerably enhanced by the setting in a beautiful farmhouse teeming with history. This stone building, whose origins date back to the end of the 17C, was the summer residence of the writer Caterina Albert y Paradís, who was much better known by the pseudonym of Víctor Català. In its dining rooms, all with high ceilings and rustic in feel yet with a few modern touches, enjoy Mediterranean cuisine with a French influence (note the traditional and delicious French rum baba on the dessert menu) which is always well presented and inspired by locally sourced ingredients. Its enticing set menus can be enhanced by a concise list of cheeses.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4195;Natxo Sellés;Spain;Cocentaina;Juan María Carbonell 3, Cocentaina, 03820, Spain;38.7367312;-0.4407907;44;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A skilfully restored 18C property that now boasts a pleasant glass-fronted porch and two stylish dining rooms, both with a contemporary feel but with rustic details such as wood and open stonework. Owner-chef Natxo Sellés is an advocate of updated traditional cuisine that is keen to extol the virtues of seasonal ingredients (he changes the à la carte several times a year) which he complements with different set menu options (one of which is vegetarian). The stars of the show here are his many savoury rice dishes (both creamy and paella varieties) and the traditional oxtail stew. Gluten-free dishes are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4196;Arotxa;Spain;Legasa;Santa Catalina 34, Legasa, 31792, Spain;43.1301538;-1.6438512;91;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant under the baton of the Lacar brothers who share the duties in the kitchen and dining room respectively. In its attractively appointed contemporary dining rooms, adorned with rustic details that showcase its personality, chef Luismi Lacar conjures up cuisine with a clear traditional focus, enhanced by contemporary touches and interesting daily suggestions. The starters here are excellent and the fish mains delicious, however one of the main signature dishes on the menu is, without doubt, the grilled T-bone steak, cooked over holm oak charcoal in a way that showcases the undeniable aromas and quality that are a continual theme in the meat served here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4197;Mesón Octavio;Spain;Ciudad Real;Severo Ochoa 6, Ciudad Real, 13005, Spain;38.997234;-3.926333;62;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;It’s very rare to come across a restaurant such as this one where every mouthful reminds us of our mothers’ and grandmothers’ cooking! Impressively run by three siblings (Aurora, Belén and José), its focus is on traditional La Mancha dishes teeming with flavour and with a strong emphasis on game (venison, red-legged partridge, wild boar etc) and beef from the Sierra de San Vicente. Highlights on the à la carte, which pays tribute to the female members of this family, include dishes teeming with character such as the “pisto manchego”, the fried breadcrumb and egg-based “migas del pastor & Huevos de gallina feliz”, the popular wild boar meatballs, and the innovative “El Barquero" cod.;Air conditioning;[]
4198;Azafrán;Spain;Villarrobledo;Avenida Reyes Católicos 71, Villarrobledo, 02600, Spain;39.2705907;-2.5952528;36;false;false;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant is guaranteed to please given the ability of chef Teresa Gutiérrez, who is also an ambassador for saffron from La Mancha, to combine the region’s strong flavours with contemporary techniques and an unmistakeable touch of femininity, unsurprising given that the team is 100% female! The à la carte, with its focus on contemporary regional cuisine, is complemented by two interesting menus, including a more extensive tasting option. Artisanal bread, Manchego cheeses and game (in season) also feature, alongside the chef’s mouthwatering array of desserts.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4199;Frisone;Spain;Elche;Borreguet 4, Elche, 03203, Spain;38.26194;-0.69566;87;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;Frisone’s change of location, albeit just a few metres from its original incarnation, has resulted in significant improvements, including a new brighter look created by its large windows, high ceilings, elegant chandeliers and a minimalist-contemporary decor dominated by a variety of white tones. Its local clientele is already familiar with the cuisine created by the Rivas brothers, who continue to focus on updated traditional cooking with a contemporary Mediterranean flavour that maximises the use of locally sourced products. Rice and seafood continue to fly the culinary flag here!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4200;Kimtxu;Spain;Bilbao;Henao 17, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2648138;-2.9329932;53;false;false;Fusion;A somewhat surprising Asian “taberna” in Bilbao, with an informal atmosphere to make you feel at home and open up your mind and tastebuds to new, interesting flavours from around the world. Owner-chef Iván Abril rethinks oriental cooking through techniques acquired in London and Hong Kong, but always using superb Basque products and varying the dishes he offers in line with seasonal ingredients. The backdrop of impeccable, contemporary taberna-style decor is partly inspired by Asian culture. Despite their apparent simplicity, his dishes are tasty, fun and well-balanced.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4201;Prada a Tope;Spain;Treceño;El Ansar 1, Treceño, 39592, Spain;43.31639;-4.29995;46;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant occupies a charming, regionally inspired property that is visible from the main road and features two dining rooms, one with a marked rustic feel, the other a glass-fronted terrace-cum-porch. Both the service and the à la carte perpetuate the traditional recipes of the Prada a Tope name, and have been given a new lease of life since the son of the owners took over the mantle here, gradually and skilfully modernising the dishes on offer. If you’re planning a weekend in the Cantabrian countryside, the property also offers a few welcoming apartments and guestrooms in the same building.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4202;La Cocina de Manuel;Spain;Valladolid;Álvarez Taladriz 4, Valladolid, 47007, Spain;41.6379148;-4.7377547;17;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Located close to the city’s bullring, this restaurant has profited from its change of location to one which offers more space and greater comfort. Boasting a classic-contemporary ambience with an elegant feel, it is professionally run by Manuel and Esther, the former in the kitchen and the latter dispensing her friendly service in the choice of dining spaces on offer here (including the bar). The updated take on traditional cuisine is showcased via generous “raciones”, with a strong focus on the very best seasonal ingredients and an impressive combination of consistent and recognisable flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
4203;Komfort;Spain;Calp;Urbanización Marisol Park 1A, Calp, 03710, Spain;38.6474418;0.0611085;50;false;true;Contemporary;An interesting option (with a name that pays homage to the current trend for comfort food) despite its location away from Calp’s main tourist haunts. Its facilities are part of the gastro-boutique Cook Book hotel and feature a modern bistro-style dining room with large picture windows, bare tables of differing heights, plus countless lamps which define its personality. Enjoy highly varied traditional and international cuisine, including delicious pizzas, cocas (a type of flatbread), grilled and rice dishes, plus a superb steak tartare. A tasting menu option is also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4204;Del Oso;Spain;Cosgaya;Barrio Areños 2, Cosgaya, 39582, Spain;43.1150441;-4.7297281;59;true;false;Home Cooking;If you’re keen to try a delicious Lebaniego stew, you won’t find many better places than this, at the foot of the Picos de Europa, in the heart of the Liébana valley – a permanently verdant and captivating setting in which to enjoy typical and copious mountain cuisine. This well-run family restaurant inside the delightful Hotel Del Oso boasts a pleasantly rustic dining room where you can enjoy simple dishes that are nonetheless full of flavour and bring back memories of bygone days. The homemade desserts are also well worth a mention!;Car park;[]
4205;Silbo Gomero;Spain;San Cristóbal de la Laguna;Volcán Elena 9, San Cristóbal de la Laguna, 38108, Spain;28.4590906;-16.3020968;20;false;true;Contemporary;Mojo is a traditional Canary Island sauce that can be used in various ways and chef Braulio Simancas is a specialist when it comes to using this iconic salsa to bring enhanced flavour to some of his dishes. His delicious cuisine, centred around market-inspired ingredients and rooted in the Canary Islands albeit with a modern touch, is light and delicate and demonstrates impeccable technique. This unpretentious restaurant by a shopping centre close to the Pabellón de Deportes de Tenerife Santiago Martín sports complex is also renowned for the unique cheeses personally matured by the chef.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4206;O Balado;Spain;Boqueixón;Ardesende 3, Boqueixón, 15881, Spain;42.798046;-8.403248;61;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Guests flock here to experience the silence, enjoy the fresh air and, of course, to enjoy O Balado’s “zero miles” cuisine which will leave a lasting memory. Although it is located in a village that is a little hard to find, it is well worth the effort to track down its discreet façade, behind which you’ll find a homely dining room featuring a mix of rustic and modern detail, including a typical open fireplace (“lareira”) used for cooking and as a smokery. Excellent quality, reasonable prices and traditional dishes prepared with love and attention, including smoked eel and Bandeira oxtail stew.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4207;El Equilibrista 33;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Ingeniero Salinas 23, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35006, Spain;28.12999;-15.43104;100;true;true;Creative, Traditional Cuisine;Located close to the Las Alcaravaneras beach, this restaurant with a modern-contemporary feel reflects the personality of the owner-chef. It boasts a cohort of admirers thanks to its focus on quality products that combine perfectly with tradition and innovation to seemingly perform the impossible and to always showcase the region’s different products. If you eat here, make sure you try the egg-based “huevos moles” accompanied by the islands’ typical “gofio” flour, one of its customers’ favourite desserts thanks to its extraordinary and intense flavour. Tradition at its purest!;Air conditioning;[]
4208;Le Bistrot Gastronómico;Spain;Castelló de la Plana;Temprado 12, Castelló de la Plana, 12002, Spain;39.9835877;-0.0370276;88;false;false;Fusion;An unpretentious, friendly and informal restaurant whose aim is to provide maximum enjoyment for its guests and for them to experience a full explosion of flavours. Its owner-chefs, who alternate between working in the kitchen and front of house so that they can explain their dishes to customers, favour contemporary cuisine that combines flavours and ingredients from different parts of the world, to create consistent dishes showcasing delicate textures and meticulous presentation. A large array of formulas and menus are available so that dishes can be shared by the whole table whenever possible.;Air conditioning;[]
4209;Vivanda;Spain;Barcelona;Major de Sarrià 134, Barcelona, 08017, Spain;41.400486;2.1209594;75;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Occupying a renovated house in the Sarriá district of the city, Vivanda is mainly popular with a local clientele. Here, the contemporary interior features high tables for tapas, restaurant-style dining tables, plus a tree-shaded patio-terrace (with a retractable roof) that is understandably very popular during the summer months. Traditional Catalan cooking is to the fore here, making full use of market-fresh ingredients and modern techniques in its “platillos” (small dishes) and “dishes of the month” that revive the flavours of the past. Make sure you order its legendary ham croquettes!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4210;Pau;Spain;Benicarló;Avenida Marqués de Benicarló 11, Benicarló, 12580, Spain;40.4164901;0.4338135;40;true;false;Rice Dishes, Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a modern, relaxed Mediterranean feel where equality is very much to the fore, with the owner-chef often keeping an eye on the dining room and explaining dishes to guests. Although Pau’s delicious rice dishes are particularly renowned, everything is delicious here thanks to a focus on cooking that showcases local products with an added hint of creativity. Choose from three well-crafted menus at lunchtime (including one executive-style menu) and two in the evening, the latter with the option of choosing dishes from the à la carte. The pleasant musical ambience completes the picture here.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4211;Terreo Cocina Casual;Spain;A Coruña;San Andrés 109, A Coruña, 15003, Spain;43.3692094;-8.4039449;19;true;false;Contemporary;A restaurant with a modern feel that everyone is talking about given its aim of creating elaborate yet more informal cuisine based around lighter dishes that still retain incredible flavour. The couple that run it (chef Quique Vázquez mans the stoves while Ana Señarís takes care of everything front of house) like to describe what they offer as “casual” to make their guests feel very much at home, with a focus on delicate sauces, an interesting fusion of raw ingredients (marinated and smoked), plus an extensive array of rice dishes. Half-“raciones” are also an option on the menu here.;Air conditioning;[]
4212;Miceli;Spain;Selva;Àngels 11, Selva, 07313, Spain;39.7542464;2.9009914;38;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant with lots of personality that is as popular as ever with customers, occupying the charming stone house in which Miceli’s female chef was born. Taking its name from the filaments (mycelia) that mushrooms use to extract nutrients from the soil, it features delightful facilities, in particular the idyllic terrace, partially covered by a glass porch and boasting superb views. The chef enjoys passing from table to table to greet guests and to explain her updated take on traditional Mallorcan cuisine, which changes daily in line with market availability. Choose between the à la carte, the daily set menu, and several tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4213;Quinqué;Spain;Madrid;Apolonio Morales 3, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.463467;-3.6841129;37;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A welcoming bistro-style eatery that is full of the hopes and dreams of owner-chefs Carlos Griffo and Miguel Ángel García who are running their own venture for the first time. Having worked in various prestigious restaurants such as Nacho Manzano’s legendary Casa Marcial, they combine the skills they have learnt to create “comida de casa” – traditional home cooking based around seasonal ingredients, albeit in an updated format, but one that still respects their full flavours. Frequent daily suggestions, featuring fish direct from the auction, plus the option of half-“raciones”.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4214;Gala;Spain;Madrid;Espronceda 14, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4406193;-3.6978122;29;false;true;Farm to table;Located closed to the Nuevos Ministerios district, Gala can already be considered a classic address in the Spanish capital, offering high levels of service to loyal customers since 1989. It boasts an attractive dining room plus a private dining space, both contemporary in style, where guests can enjoy updated traditional cuisine inspired by seasonal market produce on an à la carte that also offers half-plate options (the Alistano-Sanabresa breed of beef is excellent) as well as three set menus: Degustación, Gala and De Temporada. The most popular specialities requested by its customers are the steak tartare and dishes featuring red tuna.;Air conditioning;[]
4216;Vapor Gastronòmic;Spain;Terrassa;De la Palla 15, Terrassa, 08221, Spain;41.56301;2.011635;92;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Although the word “Vapor” (the Spanish for “steam”) automatically brings to mind the world of gastronomy, it is also used here to pay tribute to the unusual industrial revolution that took place in Terrassa in the 19C, transforming its textile industry and leading to the town’s reputation as “the town of steam engines”. The simple dining room features an open-view kitchen, plus a menu offering updated traditional cuisine, where grilled dishes are the real stars of the show. Wherever possible, the focus here is on locally produced and “zero-miles” ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4217;Avenir;Spain;Barcelona;Carrer de l'Avenir 72, Barcelona, 08021, Spain;41.3944626;2.1444062;19;true;false;Contemporary;In this simple, taberna-style restaurant with no little charm, it is impossible to leave disappointed due to the friendliness of its service and a philosophy that focuses on the fine detail of its cuisine. It is run by its two owners (Roger and Chesco) who, as fate would have it, became friends at their children’s school and decided to embark upon this venture together with one of them working in the kitchen, the other in the dining room. Here, it is almost “compulsory” to order sharing plates with the idea of trying as many dishes as possible, hence the extensive array of contemporary options, with nods to both the mountains and the sea, and an appreciation of different techniques, impressive textures and a penchant for broths. The à la carte, featuring daily specials, is complemented by several set menus.;Air conditioning;[]
4218;Asador Gonzaba;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Nova de Abaixo 2, Santiago de Compostela, 15706, Spain;42.8753153;-8.5492085;30;false;false;Meats and Grills;If you’re looking for the best-quality meat, you’ll find it in this “asador” which immediately sets out its stall with its maturing cabinet clearly visible as you walk into the dining room. Facilities here include a pleasant bar by the entrance, classically furnished dining rooms, plus an attractive private space, in which you can choose from a traditional à la carte that focuses on different meats, in particular veal and Galician beef. You can also enjoy “churra” lamb (a Spanish breed) and grilled fish which varies according to market availability. The reasonably extensive wine list features a good selection of Galician wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4219;La Cuchara de San Lorenzo;Spain;Córdoba;Arroyo de San Lorenzo 2, Córdoba, 14002, Spain;37.8879589;-4.7693772;30;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Impressively run by two brothers (Narciso front of house and Paco in the kitchen) who named this restaurant in homage to their love, since childhood, of dishes that are literally “eaten with a spoon” (cuchara). Occupying two floors, and more extensive since its renovation in a more contemporary style, its focus is on local and traditionally inspired cooking with a modern touch, with lots of attention to detail and daily specials influenced by market availability. Make sure you try the salmorejo, the veal croquettes, the mini-patatas bravas, the flamenquín, and classic dishes such as oxtail.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4220;La Taberna de Almodóvar;Spain;Córdoba;Benito Pérez Galdós 1, Córdoba, 14001, Spain;37.8897417;-4.78245;100;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Any description of La Taberna de Almodóvar inevitably requires words such as tradition and passion that bring to mind the grocery store where this family first started serving food in Almodóvar del Río. With its spick-and-span classic decor, this restaurant in Córdoba has retained the essence of that first incarnation, reproducing regional cuisine that fully respects authentic local flavours. Make sure you try the trying the famous “Almodóvar” croquettes, the egg-based “Revuelto del Cortijo”, and the legendary “Mazamorra”, a cold soup similar to “ajoblanco”, albeit thicker, that is said to be the forerunner of Córdoba’s “salmorejo”.;Air conditioning;[]
4221;Els Caçadors;Spain;Maçanet de Cabrenys;Urbanización Casanova, Maçanet de Cabrenys, 17720, Spain;42.3841249;2.755083;65;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A great place to recharge your batteries if you’re planning a visit to the Alto Ampurdán region in the Eastern Pyrenees. Located in the basement of the hotel of the same name, its play of contrasts comes as a pleasant surprise, with a decor featuring a combination of sturdy vaulted ceilings and stone walls which provide the perfect counterpoint to the designer-inspired lamps and white furnishings. The traditional, regionally inspired cuisine is somewhat surprisingly complemented by a few dishes from the Far East!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4222;El Yantar La Cocina de Pilar;Spain;Requena;Plaza de Albornoz 8, Requena, 46340, Spain;39.485571;-1.1009446;75;false;false;Fusion, Traditional Cuisine;Sharing a building with the La Villa hotel, this restaurant boasts a meticulous dining room at street level as well as a cave-like dining room excavated out of the rock that is accessed via a narrow flight of steps. Its main courses are centred around traditional cooking and are preceded by somewhat bolder starters with a nod to the fusion cuisine of Asia and the Americas. Note the excellent choice of Utiel-Requena wines!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4223;La Cocina de Ramón;Spain;Logrono;Portales 30, Logrono, 26001, Spain;42.4664453;-2.447447;45;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant restaurant with plenty of personality that reflects the long love affair between owner-chef Ramón Piñeiro and his kitchen. Located in one of the main streets in Logroño’s old quarter, just a few metres from the cathedral, its heavily restored interior of open brickwork provides a warm and welcoming backdrop for cuisine that is strongly influenced by market availability and traditional home-style cooking that has been brought up-to-date and is constantly evolving. Any of the dishes on the menu that showcase the superb vegetables of the Rioja are well worth trying.;Air conditioning;[]
4224;Tepic;Spain;Madrid;Ayala 14, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4278984;-3.6878617;41;true;true;Mexican;This Mexican restaurant steers clear of the more typical and colourful ambience of Mariachi bands and traditional guitars, opting instead for an informal, contemporary space featuring a decor of wood furnishings and a white-inspired colour scheme. It offers reasonably elaborate and authentic cuisine that includes a delicious choice of tacos (such as the exquisite “enmoladas”), as well as “panuchos yucatecos”, “tiraditos” and a choice of soups. Make sure you also sample its beers, elaborately prepared cocktails (including some mocktails), ever-popular micheladas and its superb cinnamon-flavoured “café de olla”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4225;Terraza Carmona;Spain;Vera;Del Mar 1, Vera, 04620, Spain;37.2480034;-1.8675902;62;false;false;Regional Cuisine;A third-generation, family-run restaurant that has always shone a light on the gastronomic traditions of Almería, a fact highlighted and recognised by a statue of its founder Antonio Carmona Gallardo, on one side of the street. Occupying the hotel of the same name, it features a pleasant bar with a food display counter, a regionally inspired dining room, plus an attractive terrace. The extensive, traditionally focused à la carte features dishes from the region, grilled meats, fresh fish and seafood, daily specials, along with an appetising set menu. Unpretentious yet meticulously prepared cuisine based around top-quality ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4226;Cantina La Estación;Spain;Úbeda;Cuesta Rodadera 1, Úbeda, 23400, Spain;38.0116903;-3.3672066;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Although located slightly away from the historic centre, this authentic “cantina” full of surprises is well worth the journey! It features a simple tapas bar in the style of an old railway station, which leads to the dining room, the latter imitating the interior of an old train carriage. The couple in charge, Montserrat and Antonio José, focus on contemporary seasonal cuisine, with the intention of always enhancing what they offer with artisanal breads, a small selection of olive oils, an enticing tasting menu and at least one different stew every day. The reasonably extensive and varied wine list adds to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4227;Blanqueries;Spain;Valencia;Blanqueries 12, Valencia, 46003, Spain;39.4802769;-0.3774551;30;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This bright, modern and cosmopolitan restaurant is easy to find as it’s situated just 100m from the monumental Torres de Serranos, one of the historical gateways to the wonderful city of Valencia. Boasting its own distinctive character, the restaurant is run by two talented chefs who work together to create traditional cuisine with a more up-to-date feel. The philosophy here is clear – to offer reasonably priced, high-quality cuisine made from seasonal ingredients wherever possible. The restaurant focuses mainly on set menus, with cheaper options available at lunchtime and a higher-priced menu in the evening.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4228;La Gruta;Spain;L'Escala;Pintor Enric Serra 44, L'Escala, 17130, Spain;42.1242828;3.1324018;79;true;false;International;Everyone knows that you eat extremely well at La Gruta and this hasn’t changed since it moved to this old stone house with several dining rooms and an attractive patio-terrace with views of the kitchen. The couple in charge (French chef Fabrice Cesar at the stove and Montse in the dining room) showcase French and internationally inspired cuisine prepared with locally sourced and Mediterranean ingredients on a concise à la carte and three interesting menus (Momento, Bistronómico and Descubrimiento).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4229;A Taberna do Trasno;Spain;Cambados;Príncipe 12, Cambados, 36630, Spain;42.5178743;-8.8140217;66;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Fusion;This centrally located restaurant with its modern interior is an unexpected surprise, bringing back to life a delightful stone house over 200 years old. The owner-chef offers guests a varied à la carte on which traditional recipes stand alongside more modern dishes, a few seafood options, plus plenty of grilled specialities cooked over a wood fire. You’ll even find some fusion dishes described as “a journey around the world”. Our recommendations include grilled octopus on a bed of creamy Cachelos potatoes, and the superb grilled Burela hake with clams and an Albariño wine reduction.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4230;Trasiego;Spain;Barbastro;Avenida de La Merced 64, Barbastro, 22300, Spain;42.0339451;0.1201515;81;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The San Julián and Santa Lucía complex, comprising a former hospital and a Renaissance church of the same name, is now home to this attractive restaurant as well as the headquarters of the Somontano wine board with its focus on the world of wine and wine tourism. Here, chef Javier Matinero, a leading light in the culinary renaissance of this area, offers a contemporary à la carte alongside interesting set menus. One of the highlights is the delicious tartare of pink Barbastro tomatoes with a mussel ice cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4231;Antoni Rubies;Spain;Artesa de Lleida;Lleida 6, Artesa de Lleida, 25150, Spain;41.553394;0.7052084;67;false;true;Rice Dishes;If you’re a fan of rice dishes you’ll feel at home in this restaurant, which is one of the best options for rice in the Segrià area of Lleida province. The chef here makes up for the simple decor with a friendly welcome and traditional cooking that remains faithful to locally sourced products. Although the well-composed à la carte, featuring enticing starters, and meat and fish dishes, is an option here, the restaurant’s highlights are its exquisite rice dishes (prepared with different varieties of Molí de Pals rice), which can usually be ordered as a special option on the set menus. A surprisingly good selection of gins rounds things off nicely!;Air conditioning;[]
4232;La Posada de Águeda;Spain;Requena;Carretera N-III, Requena, 46340, Spain;39.4832524;-1.0979317;19;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;It’s a widely held view that this attractive restaurant, occupying a chalet-style property by the main road, is one of the best dining options in the Utiel-Requena area in Valencia province. Here, the family in charge, with Julio manning the stoves and partner Águeda and their daughter at the helm in the dining room, focuses on traditional cooking based around quality ingredients and simple yet impressively prepared dishes, with an emphasis on Spanish and local recipes. It’s also possible to order smaller plates, such as artichokes, oxtail cannelloni, fritters etc.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4233;Es Terral;Spain;Santa Eulalia del Río;Sant Vicent 47, Santa Eulalia del Río, 07840, Spain;38.9856209;1.5346632;22;false;false;French;This charming restaurant, located along a busy pedestrian street, is run by a pleasant couple, with French chef Matthieu Michel Savariaud at the helm in the kitchen. The menu here is based around international cuisine and high-quality ingredients, most of which are organic and seasonal, with a nod to the chef’s French roots and the occasional Arabian-inspired dish. Here, the kitchen team boasts extensive knowledge of local products which Savariaud, who has worked with culinary icons such as Alain Ducasse and Hélène Darroze, showcases and frequently combines with ingredients from further afield.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4234;El Espejo;Spain;Sanlúcar de Barrameda;Caballeros 11, Sanlúcar de Barrameda, 11540, Spain;36.7756305;-6.3542926;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A breath of fresh air for the dining scene in Sanlúcar. This restaurant, located inside the Posada de Palacio hotel opposite the town hall in the centre of the Barrio Alto district, combines a rustic-contemporary layout with antique furnishings in keeping with the architecture of the building (as an example, one of the dining rooms occupies the former stables). The à la carte features modern cooking that showcases local ingredients, alongside two tasting menus with a strong focus on presentation. A large choice of sherries by the glass are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4235;Llantén;Spain;Valladolid;Encina 11, Valladolid, 47153, Spain;41.5892014;-4.7504631;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re celebrating a special occasion and are on the lookout for a restaurant with plenty of charm, look no further than this eatery located in the “Pinar de Antequera”, a residential development on the outskirts of Valladolid, which continues to surprise thanks to its landscaped surroundings and feel of a Menorcan farmhouse – the latter enhanced by the welcoming open fireplaces that provide the perfect ambience for a romantic candlelit supper. Here, the honest, traditional cuisine has been given an impressive modern makeover, including highly memorable dishes such as goat with alioli, beef tripe, 70-day-aged Sanabresa T-bone, as well as Albufera rice dishes that never fail to hit the mark.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4236;El Jardín de la Sal;Spain;Las Caletas;Carretera La Costa-El Faro 5, Las Caletas, 38740, Spain;28.4537437;-17.8418976;48;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;A pleasant surprise both in terms of its cuisine and its secluded location next to the old Fuencaliente lighthouse, which is now an information centre for the La Palma marine reserve. Here, the modern take on traditional cuisine showcases local ingredients, in particular fish sourced daily (such as the typical Vieja and the red rock fish), which you can enjoy in an impressive themed space, plus a café upstairs boasting superb views. The outstanding backdrop here is the play of colours between the blue of the ocean, the black of the island’s volcanic landscapes, and the radiant whiteness of the surrounding salt pans, which have been declared a site of special scientific interest.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4237;L'Algadir del Delta;Spain;Amposta;Ronda dels Pins 27, Amposta, 43549, Spain;40.646976;0.6878907;22;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;Located in the middle of the Parque Natural del Delta del Ebro and within a few metres of its famous rice fields, this restaurant is part of the first Ecolabel-certified hotel in Cataluña, where its quality and self-confidence ensure that it is the undisputed star of the show. Owner-chef Joan Capilla’s clear focus is on “zero-mile” ingredients, sustainability and the latest cutting-edge techniques which he combines to create his updated take on traditional cuisine. The à la carte, including an array of outstanding rice dishes, is complemented by two impressive set menus: Somos Gastronomía and Festival del Chef, both which need to be booked in advance.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4238;Olea Comedor;Spain;Cuenca;Avenida Castilla-La Mancha 3, Cuenca, 16002, Spain;40.0706882;-2.1369292;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Fusion;Honesty is raised to a new level here thanks to the open-view kitchen which is a clear demonstration that this restaurant has nothing to hide! Chef Eduardo Albiol creates cuisine that is both personal and different, adding a modern take to traditional recipes through the use of culinary touches and ingredients from other parts of the world, hence his dishes inspired by the Mediterranean, Asia and South America. His customers are his only benchmarks, so he is constantly attuned to their reaction with the hope that his cuisine will receive their full blessing! Excellent value for money!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4240;El Montañés;Spain;Biescas;Escudial 1, Biescas, 22630, Spain;42.6258852;-0.3249263;18;true;true;Contemporary;A safe bet in the Tena valley. This restaurant has chosen a name that fits it like a glove as the stone façade leads to an interior with a mountain-style decor featuring a mix of open stonework and, above all, a plethora of wood. The humble chef focuses on generous “raciones”, ensuring that guests enjoy his cooking to the full through local, seasonally inspired dishes that feature an added touch of modernity and international flavour. Specialities include the truffle-flavoured wild mushroom risotto and the suckling lamb with a sage emulsion.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4241;Sobretablas;Spain;Seville;Colombia 7, Seville, 41013, Spain;37.3697289;-5.9845016;28;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The culinary interest in this restaurant is on the up thanks to the fact that the young couple here (Camila Ferraro is in charge of the kitchen, with her partner acting as sommelier and running the front of house) met while working at the famous El Celler de Can Roca. The chef’s humble, consistent approach is evident in her modern cooking with clear regional and traditional influences, to which she adds her own distinctive personality to cuisine that includes options for sharing and half plates. This attractive restaurant takes its name from a specific stage of sherry production, after which the sherry-master decides if a wine should become a fino or oloroso.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
4242;Existe;Spain;Puertomingalvo;Carretera A-1701, Puertomingalvo, 44411, Spain;40.3191736;-0.4886189;59;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Following its move from Mosqueruela, this restaurant now provides the culinary inspiration at the Mas de Cebrián hotel, along the road leading to Puertomingalvo. In essence, Existe continues to act as a culinary showcase for the so-called “Empty Spain”, in a setting that is both rustic and contemporary. The couple in charge (with María acting as sommelier in the dining room, and Alberto in the kitchen), offer a single tasting menu that showcases locally sourced ingredients from the province of Teruel, alongside constant nods to the region and its culinary roots. The chef particularly enjoys working with local game and wild mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4243;La Xarxa;Spain;Tarragona;de Sant Pere 38, Tarragona, 43004, Spain;41.1099201;1.2411467;73;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Rice Dishes;A restaurant that has been passed down from the parents to their children and, as a result, is enjoying a new lease of life! Despite this, its true essence, from its early days as a simple fishermen’s bar, remains. This impressively updated restaurant with huge round windows just a few metres from the port boasts a thoroughly modern à la carte with a nod to Asia (dumplings, Thai sauces etc) and an excellent choice of rice dishes. One of its unique features is that the chef’s father is himself a fisherman who has his own boat that he takes out every day, hence the quality and freshness of fish served here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4244;Aimia;Spain;Lleida;Doctor Combelles 67, Lleida, 25003, Spain;41.6128404;0.617187;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that is well worth considering as it is never that easy finding modern cuisine at affordable prices. The restaurant, which takes its name (“a beloved woman”) from an old Catalan language once sung by troubadours, boasts a contemporary interior with a kitchen visible from the dining room and an adjoining bar so that you can watch dishes with a focus on modern fusion cooking with a strong Asian influence being prepared in front of you. We can highly recommend the carpaccio of octopus and the calamares with a fino sherry and black garlic sauce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4245;Can Boix;Spain;Vilamarí;Carretera de Banyoles a l'Escala, Vilamarí, 17468, Spain;42.111946;2.851352;31;false;false;Regional Cuisine;This welcoming family restaurant is a good choice if you enjoy genuine Catalan cuisine. Situated in an attractive stone-walled building just off the main road, Can Boix serves honest, authentic and unfussy cuisine which is typical of the best country restaurants. Here, the Boix brothers (Jordi and Albert) demonstrate their strong preference for traditional fish and meat stews, meat grilled over a natural wood fire and – one of the real highlights – truly exquisite rice dishes (for two), one of which is vegan. Most guests choose one of Can Boix’s extensive menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4246;Casa Chongastán;Spain;Chía;Carretera s/n, Chía, 22465, Spain;42.5200992;0.4668783;44;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;If you enjoy eating high-quality meat, you won’t want to pass up this opportunity. The restaurant occupies an attractive Alpine-style building, however its most interesting feature is that the same family runs the restaurant as well as a farm that breeds native cattle. Here, you can savour delicious homemade stews, wild mushrooms in season, as well as exquisite grilled meats produced from its own cattle, and game. Its veal is famous for having the perfect level of fat between its muscle fibres.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
4247;2 Estaciones;Spain;Valencia;Pintor Salvador Abril 28, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.4626106;-0.3702585;94;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Sometimes referred to as the Valencia’s Soho, the Ruzafa district has developed into one of the most interesting areas for food in the city. The district is home to 2 Estaciones, a restaurant now run by Alberto Alonso and Mar Soler, a couple who are both chefs and business partners in this exciting project. The informal bistro-style restaurant comprises a large bar, an open-view kitchen and some striking tables (covered with tablecloths) made from the legs of old sewing machines. The menu features seasonal Mediterranean cuisine including contemporary-style dishes and a choice of set menus.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4248;Can Poal;Spain;Vallromanes;Avenida Vilassar de Dalt 1b, Vallromanes, 08188, Spain;41.531725;2.2986879;54;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;You’ll definitely enjoy this restaurant occupying a family farmhouse, the origins of which date back to the 14C. The welcoming interior, with its semi-open-view kitchen and contemporary-rustic style, provides the backdrop for traditional Catalan cuisine made from seasonal ingredients which is meticulously presented and carefully cooked in order to showcase the flavours of its organic meat to the full. The restaurant offers a good set menu, daily specials, delicious rice options, stews, plus dishes cooked over the Josper grill which have earned it its excellent local reputation. Don’t miss the delicious pigs’ trotters!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4249;Hostal Jaumet;Spain;Torà;Carretera C 1412a, Torà, 25750, Spain;41.8097276;1.4029806;92;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Opened in 1890, this property by the main road is now run by the fifth generation of the same family. Although described as a “hostal”, the main focus here is on the attractively appointed restaurant, which is classic and traditional in style. The menu featuring Catalan cuisine is complemented by traditional stews, home-style cooking, barbecue options, and the popular “Grandma Ramona’s dishes”, which include the “Ofegat de la Segarra” stew, partridge with a vinaigrette sauce, and cannelloni. The comfortable guestrooms are arranged around a patio with a swimming pool.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4250;Los Fueros;Spain;Bilbao;De los Fueros 6, Bilbao, 48005, Spain;43.259617;-2.923103;33;false;true;Basque;This typical Bilbao “botxero”, a classic feature of Bilbao’s restaurant scene, opened its doors in 1878 under the name Bar Colón. Today, following its impressive renovation which has seen it retain much of its authentic character, it is one of the most interesting restaurants in the city’s old quarter. Its beautiful bistro-style interior provides the backdrop for an impressive à la carte (including “media ración” options) that features Bilbao’s most representative and typical dishes, all presented with a contemporary flair, alongside two enticing tasting menus: “Gourmand” and “De Bilbao de toda la vida”. Don’t leave without trying the legendary grilled prawns!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4251;Mirko Carturan Cuiner;Spain;Caldes de Montbui;Avenida Pi i Margall 75, Caldes de Montbui, 08140, Spain;41.6300201;2.1657336;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The eponymous restaurant of this Piedmont-born chef features a contemporary dining room embellished with cookery books, a patio-terrace, plus a private dining space. The thoroughly modern cuisine has plenty of personality, extolling the virtues of seasonal products, with a focus on texture and meticulous presentation. Day events focusing on different food themes (truffles, wild mushrooms, game etc) are also held throughout the year. From Monday to Friday (excluding public holidays), a particularly interesting “Bib Gourmand Guía Michelin” menu is also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4252;Alberca;Spain;Trujillo;Victoria 8, Trujillo, 10200, Spain;39.4602814;-5.8839687;79;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Alberca adds a new look to Trujillo in this stone house in the heart of the town’s old quarter. The restaurant, which has taken on a new lease of life having passed down a generation, boasts two welcoming dining rooms with a traditional, regional decor, plus a delightful terrace on an internal patio. Updated traditional cuisine is to the fore here, with grilled dishes cooked over hot coals the undisputable stars of the show, the result of the chef having spent almost a year in the legendary one-Michelin-star Etxebarri “asador” in Axpe. The à la carte is complemented by two superb tasting menus: Brasas and Humo.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4253;El Secreto de Chimiche;Spain;Chimiche;Carretera General del Sur 4, Chimiche, 38594, Spain;28.132975;-16.532373;19;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Meats and Grills;If you were to describe this restaurant located away from the tourist trail as a hidden jewel, you wouldn’t be far wrong. In its roadside location, the somewhat unassuming façade conceals an attractively renovated, rustic-style interior with a pleasant bar, plus a dining space on several floors featuring cosy nooks and crannies and pretty terraces. Here, the chef focuses on traditional cuisine full of flavour with its roots in the very essence of cooking from the Canary Islands, plus numerous dishes cooked on the wood-fired grill. Superb aged meats are a particular speciality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4254;La Barra de Kaymus;Spain;Valencia;Avenida Maestro Rodrigo 44, Valencia, 46015, Spain;39.4852594;-0.4030128;20;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a modern feel, located in a residential district, hence its location slightly away from the city centre. It features a single dining room plus a pleasant private space, where Valencian chef Nacho Romero focuses on simply prepared, contemporary-style dishes which are nonetheless skilfully prepared, including rice dishes (here, paella is seen as “a dish that brings families and good friends together”) and reasonably priced menus. Highlights include the Kaymus salad with a seafood salpicón, the croquettes, and the cod fritters.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4255;Garbí;Spain;Castellar del Vallès;Barcelona 52, Castellar del Vallès, 08211, Spain;41.6107945;2.0872822;61;false;false;Catalan;A family-run restaurant named after a thermal wind from the southwest that blows across the whole of the Levante region. The owner-chef, who has taken over the reins following the retirement of his parents, is closely involved with the collective of “Cuina Vallès” chefs, and their straightforward approach to traditional Catalan cuisine. As a result, the menu is bursting with legendary classic dishes such as Mongetes del ganxet white beans from Can Casamada, tripe with chickpeas, crispy fried brains, and the delicious oxtail stew. The daily menu is particularly popular here!;Air conditioning;[]
4256;Las Termas;Spain;Astorga;Santiago 1, Astorga, 24700, Spain;42.4563607;-6.0552439;89;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This family-run restaurant, just a few metres from the palace designed by Gaudí, boasts a spacious dining room featuring ochre walls and wood furnishings that create a very welcoming feel. Although it offers other dishes based around local and regional ingredients, the undoubted star of the show here is its signature and ever-present “Cocido Maragato” stew. The unique feature of this dish is that, contrary to usual practice, it is served in reverse order with the meat first, followed by the chickpeas and lastly the soup. You can also purchase Las Termas’ delicious chickpeas if you’re keen to cook them at home!;Air conditioning;[]
4257;La Bola de Jorge Bosch;Spain;Tegueste;Lomo 18, Tegueste, 38280, Spain;28.512541;-16.3519798;50;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This unique restaurant, which started life as a simple “guachinche” (an unassuming family eatery serving home cooking and its own home-produced wine) has remained faithful to its “gastro-guachinche” concept through this culinary venture in Tegueste. It features a spacious, rustically inspired yet elegant dining room, views of the sea and coast, and informal, contemporary and highly personal cuisine based around Canary Island ingredients. This is accompanied by a clear desire to reinvent the islands’ recipes, and dishes that are plentiful and copious. The à la carte, featuring unique options such as the burrata made with fresh milk from the island’s cows (served with tomatoes from the farmers’ market in Tegueste) and the pork cheek with the restaurant’s own Listan Negro wine, is complemented by two tasting menus (6 and 8 courses). The chillout zone here is also used for private events.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
4258;Treze;Spain;Madrid;General Pardiñas 34, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4267883;-3.6784386;86;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine;A contemporary-style restaurant with modern touches which stands out for its cuisine, which is based on market-fresh produce and wild game, in particular. Although the chef is not a hunter himself, he pays careful attention to the hunting seasons and works around these in his choice of products. The restaurant boasts an attractive bar that surrounds the open-view kitchen, where guests can watch the chefs at work, plus an attractively appointed dining room. Culinary options here are showcased on a tempting à la carte with a choice of medias raciones, and a tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
4259;Cami·Vell;Spain;Alzira;Colón 51, Alzira, 46600, Spain;39.1472451;-0.4376742;35;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;One of those instances where the passing of the generational baton has injected renewed energy into a business, although it’s not uncommon to see its founder, Antonio López, still putting in an occasional appearance! Toni, front of house, and his brother Iván, in the kitchen, are now running the show on their own. In the dining room, which is divided between several spaces with a rustic-contemporary decor, attractive azulejo tiling and an open-view kitchen, the concise à la carte focuses on updated traditional cuisine, with a continual nod to local products, alongside three tasting menus (Xúquer, in homage to Camí Vell’s signature dishes, Casella and Murta).;Air conditioning;[]
4260;El Buey;Spain;Almoradí;La Reina 94, Almoradí, 03160, Spain;38.1067896;-0.7974394;38;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant that prides itself on its honest and professional service. The small bar acts almost as a private space, while the attractive, classic-contemporary dining room is embellished with the occasional rustic detail. The owner-chef here offers a choice of traditional and international dishes, although he also has an excellent grounding in grilled meats, hence the name of the restaurant (the Ox). Nowadays, he pays particular attention to seasonal and locally sourced products, in particular its star product, artichokes from La Vega Baja del Segura. A typical local stew with meatballs (“cocido con pelotas de La Vega Baja”) is served every Sunday.;Air conditioning;[]
4261;Asador La Chumbera;Spain;Agua Amarga;Paraje Los Ventorrillos, Agua Amarga, 04149, Spain;36.9451654;-1.9261464;20;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The best feature of this highly typical whitewashed property is its remote location, which you’ll come to as you leave Agua Amarga on the Carboneras road. The restaurant has two rustic-contemporary dining rooms, both with a white colour scheme and a fireplace, plus a pleasant terrace embellished with cactus and prickly pears, where guests can enjoy traditional cuisine with both Arab and oriental influences. The daily fish specials and the delicious beef entrecôte are particular highlights. If you’re interested in visiting something unusual in the area, this “asador” is located close to the ruins of the Agua Amarga iron ore loading terminus (in operation until 1942).;Car park,Terrace;[]
4262;El Cel de les Oques;Spain;Terrassa;De la Palla 15, Terrassa, 08221, Spain;41.5631112;2.0115738;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A good location in a narrow pedestrianised street in Terrassa’s old quarter. The couple who own it (Imma is in charge of the dining room while Sergio mans the stoves) focus on updated traditional cuisine which, whenever possible, uses locally sourced organic ingredients and tries to revive long-forgotten recipes from local farms, albeit with a modern twist. The name of the restaurant, which translates literally as “the sky of the geese”, is an expression frequently used by Imma’s grandfather to describe anything that was “sublime”. Varied à la carte, set daily menu, plus an extensive seasonal tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4263;Elías;Spain;Xinorlet;Rosers 7, Xinorlet, 03649, Spain;38.415276;-0.9605619;32;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant with a long family history that has manged to change with the times without losing touch with its roots. Located in the centre of the village, its discreet façade conceals a pleasantly renovated interior with a contemporary feel, including a glass-fronted wine cellar and an open-view grill. The most admirable features here are the respect shown for traditional regional recipes and its cooking methods, with many dishes grilled over the embers in time-honoured fashion. Rice dishes are its speciality (the rice with rabbit and snails is particularly impressive), although it also offers typical recipes such as roasted almonds and “gachamiga”, a typical local dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4264;La Teja Azul;Spain;Villena;Sancho Medina 34, Villena, 03400, Spain;38.634167;-0.8681;83;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant surprise, occupying a property with centuries-old walls and lots of stone and exposed beams. The friendly couple in charge, Antonio in the kitchen and Pepi front of house, have been serving traditional Mediterranean cuisine for more than 20 years – a type of cooking much loved by guests thanks to its focus on the very best local ingredients and an honest and caring approach to their dishes. These include meticulously prepared starters, fish and seafood from the fish auction in Santa Pola, delicious grilled meats and, above all, some superb rice options. An impressive tasting menu completes the picture here.;Air conditioning;[]
4265;Casa Chesmy;Spain;Tariego de Cerrato;Camino Hondo, Tariego de Cerrato, 34209, Spain;41.9063675;-4.4894288;28;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you want to eat well and at a reasonable price, head to Casa Chesmy, a restaurant that has been in business for 20 years and is making a name for itself in the Cerrato region in the province of Palencia. Accessed via an attractive tree-shaded garden with an outdoor terrace, the three attractively appointed dining rooms have a rustic feel, one of which features an old kitchen as part of the decor. The traditional, home-style cooking here specialises in farm-reared pigeon and chicken – given that the owner has several dovecots, his own chicken farm, and a market garden that provides Casa Chesmy with many of its vegetables. A tranquil and pleasant experience!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4266;El Risco;Spain;Famara;Montaña Clara 30, Famara, 35558, Spain;29.1185223;-13.5648771;18;false;false;Seafood, Farm to table;If you’re looking to eat somewhere special then look no further, as this restaurant occupies the house designed and decorated by the multi-faceted artist César Manrique for his brother. The decor here is simple but with a subtle maritime-inspired feel, but what stands out most of all are the magnificent views of the Playa de Famara, the surrounding mountains and, peering out across the ocean, the outline of the bucolic island of La Graciosa. Local fish and seafood as well as rice dishes are the main highlights on the menu, although we can also highly recommend the delicious daily specials. Best to book ahead as it is usually very busy!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
4267;El Chaleco;Spain;Almuñécar;Avenida Costa del Sol 37, Almuñécar, 18690, Spain;36.73905;-3.69805;77;true;true;French;A restaurant with an excellent reputation, now run by the daughter of the previous owners, who has managed to maintain its essence but with an exquisite touch and a more modern perspective. In the attractive dining room, divided into two separate spaces, guests can savour French-inspired cuisine which is unusual for this area. The cooking is mainly focused around two menus: a short 3-course option and a 5-course tasting menu. Keep your eye out for El Chaleco’s frequent themed menus (lobster, seafood special, anniversary, Belgian etc).;Air conditioning;[]
4268;Consolación;Spain;Cartaya;Avenida Consolación 2, Cartaya, 21450, Spain;37.2888245;-7.1505648;47;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;One of those places you really enjoy visiting, where the young, serious and professional team of siblings at the helm (the third generation of the same family) provides exceptionally friendly service to its customers. Facilities include a pleasant glass-fronted terrace, a pleasant tapas bar, plus a bright dining room where you can choose from the extensive à la carte of delicious fresh fish (grilled, barbecued, stuffed etc), a variety of rice dishes, excellent meats and seafood priced by weight that will satisfy even the most discerning of guests. We recommend the Huelva shrimps and the cooked prawns, the house speciality!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4269;Casa el Tio David;Spain;Alfafara;Bancal del Clot 2, Alfafara, 03838, Spain;38.7736552;-0.5552538;83;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Run by a friendly husband-and-wife- team who demonstrate a perfect harmony between the kitchen and dining room, this is one of those restaurants that receives plaudits from everybody who eats here. It occupies an early 20C family property with a rustic-regional feel, enhanced by its myriad decorative details, wooden beams and the open fire that is often roaring here. The locally inspired regional à la carte, which also features half-ración options, is complemented by three tasting menus. Specialities here include the potpourri of assorted croquettes and the Al-Ándalus-style shoulder of roast lamb.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4271;La Rebotica;Spain;Cariñena;San José 3, Cariñena, 50400, Spain;41.337964;-1.2236069;41;true;false;Regional Cuisine;“A journey is made easier with bread, cheese and wine” is the popular Spanish saying above the entrance of this local eatery that is a staunch champion of the flavours of yesteryear. This attractive restaurant, in what was once the house of the local pharmacist, features welcoming, rustic-style dining rooms occupying the property’s different bedrooms. The cooking here has a strong Aragonese flavour and is based around native ingredients that are used in dishes such as borage, wild mushrooms and potatoes, and the delicious stuffed meat balls (albóndigas estofadas). Discover local Cariñena wines through the staff’s personal recommendations.;Air conditioning;[]
4272;Sisapo;Spain;Madrid;Trafalgar 14, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4319586;-3.7004854;63;false;false;Fusion;This unique, intimate restaurant, with an interior design that combines Industrial and contemporary details as well as classic decorative features from the past, is located in the authentic Chamberí district of the city. Its unusual name refers to a Roman archaeological site in Bienvenida (Ciudad Real province). The chef at the helm here, Alejandro Aguirre, champions contemporary cuisine that is highly personal and full of strong flavours, ably supported by Asian and South American ingredients that he skilfully combines with native Spanish products. It also boasts a pleasant terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4273;Cruix;Spain;Barcelona;Entença 57, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3781724;2.1524746;15;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant with an informal feel and exposed brick walls is the perfect setting in which to feel very much at home thanks to service that could not be any more friendly. Here, the cuisine is focused around two tasting menus: Classic Cruix (7 courses) and Grand Cruix (11 courses), on which the superb rice dishes are worthy of special mention (the paellas are all served with their special crispy “socarrat” texture at the bottom of the pan!). One of its signature dishes is also served for dessert: the bizarrely named “sad day on the beach”! In fine weather, try to book a table on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4274;Casa Barqueiro;Spain;Negreira;Avenida de Santiago 13, Negreira, 15830, Spain;42.9095997;-8.7352114;26;true;false;Galician;A family-owned restaurant with the perfect blend of talent, friendliness and professionalism. It features a busy wine bar, with a few tables for tapas, an impeccable dining room adorned with a beautiful mural of the bucolic Maceira bridge, as well as a spectacular glass-fronted wine cellar that fills one side of the room. In the kitchen, the focus is on honest and traditional Galician cuisine which stands out for the quality of its meats and its reasonable prices. Whatever you do, don’t miss the magnificent stone-cooked T-bone steak!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4275;Las Musas;Spain;Campo de Criptana;Barbero 3, Campo de Criptana, 13610, Spain;39.4090257;-3.1235193;80;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A safe bet in every sense thanks to the excellent cuisine on offer, enhanced by the impeccable rustic-contemporary ambience and a location right by the legendary giant windmills described in Don Quijote! The restaurant occupies a former night-club, from which it has taken its name, in a town popular with tourists, hence the strong emphasis on the traditional cooking of La Mancha, with the occasional contemporary touch thrown in. Standout dishes include the classic “migas”, the “cocido” croquettes, and the crunchy biscuit topped with fried Valdivieso cheese.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
4277;Donamaria'ko Benta;Spain;Donamaria;Barrio de la Venta 4, Donamaria, 31750, Spain;43.1059274;-1.6862454;17;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The whole family is involved in the running of this restaurant occupying an old 19C inn in the heart of the countryside. The dining room has a welcoming rustic ambience with stone walls, open beams and high-quality antique furniture, where guests can choose between reasonably priced traditional and regionally inspired menus. For dessert, make sure you order the Donamaria-style tiramisu. Several themed food events dedicated to wild mushrooms, game and seasonal product are also hosted here during the year. Pleasant guestrooms can also be booked if you’re planning on spending a few days in the area.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4278;La Cosmo;Spain;Malaga;Císter 11, Malaga, 29015, Spain;36.7205548;-4.4180017;18;false;false;Andalusian;If you’re looking for a modern and informal restaurant which also boasts a central location in the city, then look no further than La Cosmo, situated just a few steps behind the cathedral. Boasting an open kitchen and white-inspired colour scheme, the focus here is on the transparency and quality of all its ingredients and bringing added value to the locally sourced produce it uses. At La Cosmo, chef Dani Carnero, who is also at the helm of two other restaurants in the city (La Cosmopolita and Kaleja), is aiming for a more direct and fluid cooking concept that revives the traditions of Málaga’s cuisine and its maritime-inspired flavours.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4279;Coscolo;Spain;Castrillo de los Polvazares;La Magdalena 1, Castrillo de los Polvazares, 24718, Spain;42.4643866;-6.128479;59;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This delightful village is famous for its “Cocido Maragato”, a dish that for centuries has, against convention, been served here in reverse order (first the meat, then the chickpeas, followed by the soup at the end). At Coscolo, the special feature of this legendary recipe is that it is prepared with products that are smoked, cured and prepared on the property using ingredients sourced from the local area. To this stew the Navarra-born chef here likes to add tiny details that add even more personality, hence the change of name of the dish on the menu to that of his restaurant (“Cocido Coscolo”). Leave your car in the car park at the entrance to the village as only local residents are allowed to drive in.;Air conditioning;[]
4280;Bacaro;Spain;Barcelona;Jerusalem 6, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3811767;2.1715597;26;true;true;Italian;This restaurant, steeped in the essence of Italy but which the team describes as a “Venetian taberna”, is located just a few steps from the emblematic Boquería market, and is one of those places you look forward to visiting given the caring and kindness in evidence as soon as you walk through the door. Bistro in style, and split between two floors, it boasts an eclectic yet simple decor, the idea being not to interfere too much with what is really important, namely the food! The latter is clearly rooted in Italian tradition, with a continual emphasis on flavour. You’ll find pasta here, of course, but don’t miss the typical sardines “in saor”, the Venetian-style veal liver, or the marvellous tiramisù. As you would expect, the wine list includes some classic Italian labels.;Air conditioning;[]
4281;acebuche;Spain;Zafra;Santa Marina 3, Zafra, 06300, Spain;38.4236945;-6.4176702;37;true;true;Fusion;Located in the part of town most popular with tourists, this restaurant is a leading name in Zafra’s culinary heritage. Now completely renovated, it has taken on a new lease of life in the hands of the couple running it. Carmen and Javo, who met at the one-Michelin-star El Invernadero in Madrid, decided to head off on their own and, in so doing, transformed the cuisine on offer here, skilfully combining the cooking of Extremadura with that of Argentina in a nod to their respective origins. Only one concise menu is available, although medias raciones are also an option.;Air conditioning;[]
4282;Agua Salada;Spain;Santander;San Simón 2, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.464222;-3.8025956;73;true;false;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;A modest, friendly and authentic restaurant with no luxurious frills but plenty of charm. Its simple façade on the street corner conceals a welcoming dining room decorated in French bistro style and dominated by shades of green and white, with an old open-view bar, bare marble tables and other intimate and attractive details, such as the bright candles which add a romantic touch. The menu features well-presented and updated traditional cuisine, which is full of well-defined flavours, and also includes the option of ordering half-portions.;Air conditioning;[]
4283;Brel;Spain;El Campello;San Vicente 91, El Campello, 03560, Spain;38.4246546;-0.3903405;41;true;true;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;A family-owned business that, in homage to its origins, takes its name from the famous Belgian singer Jacques Brel, renowned worldwide for his song “Ne me quitte pas”. This restaurant, which initially operated as a pizzeria, boasts a superb beach location and an attractive interior that is bright, spacious and designed in contemporary style, and features a special bar-style table in front of the glass-fronted kitchen. The contemporary Mediterranean menu is high on detail, with specific sections for fresh pasta, innovative pizzas and Asian-inspired dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4284;A Viaxe;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Praza do Matadoiro 3, Santiago de Compostela, 15704, Spain;42.881473;-8.5399848;72;true;true;Fusion;An unusual bistro-style restaurant located in a small square close to the centre of the city. The chef at the helm creates dishes that have the distinct feel of his native Peru, combined with influences he has amassed on his travels around the globe and less popular fish species sourced from the auction. Here, they say that “every dish is a journey”, hence the desire to explain the provenance of each one on the menu (Peru, Colombia, Ecuador, Galicia, Basque Country etc). The cuisine is focused around two menus: 7 Destinos and 9 Destinos. Given its small size, it is advisable to book ahead.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4285;El Rinconcico;Spain;Mora de Rubielos;Santa Lucía 4, Mora de Rubielos, 44400, Spain;40.2504545;-0.7544101;71;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant located in one of Spain’s main gastronomic regions - the Gúdar-Javalambre area is the main producer of the famous black Teruel truffle! Located alongside the River Mora, El Rinconcico features a popular and contemporary gastro-bar with a few tables on the ground floor, and the main dining room upstairs. Here, you can enjoy updated traditional cuisine that makes plentiful use of local ingredients from Teruel province and is enhanced by a few Peruvian touches from the chef’s homeland. We can recommend the delicious Ternasco D.O. de Aragón lamb as well as the popular “potaje de garbanzos de Miguel”, a chickpea stew created in honour of the founder of the restaurant over 30 years ago. The somewhat visually deceptive “Havana morcilla cigar” also impressed us!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4286;Saó;Spain;Barcelona;Cesare Cantù 2, Barcelona, 08023, Spain;41.4169245;2.1397846;40;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the upper part of the city, Saó boasts an evocative name (which translates as “ripeness” in English) that describes the “perfect maturity” of ingredients used here. Valencia-born chef Juanen Benavent develops his menus based on locally sourced seasonal produce, creating traditional dishes with a strong French influence, which comes from four years working at the Goust restaurant in Paris. Choose from three menus (Llavor, Guerminat and Arrels), which vary in terms of the number of dishes they each offer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4287;Arteaga Landetxea;Spain;Mondragón;Garagartza Auzoa 37, Mondragón, 20500, Spain;43.07175;-2.51625;32;true;false;Basque;This restaurant occupies a remotely located farmhouse with centuries of history behind it as well as the benefit of a picturesque backdrop. It is enthusiastically run by Maider Larrañaga and Igor Ezpeleta, with the former in charge of the dining room and acting as sommelier (effortlessly managing a cellar with over 1 000 labels) and the latter conjuring up cuisine that showcases the true soul of the Basque region in the kitchen. In the delightfully rustic interior, you’ll find a splendid “vinoteka”, a welcoming main dining room, plus another smaller space. The traditional and regionally inspired cuisine served up here (we recommend the grilled fish of the day) showcases flavour and champions high-quality ingredients that are always local. The pleasant terrace is an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4288;La Farola;Spain;Altura;Agustín Sebastián 4, Altura, 12410, Spain;39.8506467;-0.5112623;64;false;false;Contemporary;One of those situations in which a restaurant has reinvented itself along with the careers of the couple at the helm. Here, José Vicente has given a new lease of life to the original family-run bar, while María abandoned her job as a biologist to give free rein to her true passion. In this bright eatery, featuring a large glass-fronted wine cellar and a meticulous interior, choose between an interesting à la carte and a set menu that showcases the recipes of the Alto Palancia area (l’Alt Palància). These range from delicious, updated takes on traditional recipes to bolder creations inspired from further afield. The varied wine list is an added bonus.;Air conditioning;[]
4289;Rubén Miralles;Spain;Vinaròs;Travessia de Sant Vicent 9, Vinaròs, 12500, Spain;40.47023;0.47463;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This small restaurant, located along a narrow street just a few metres from the Plaza Parroquial, provides the perfect opportunity to enjoy a true gastronomic experience. The young chef in charge showcases contemporary cooking that combines different trends with a non-zealous approach along with traditionally based dishes featuring top-quality ingredients. His aim is to take guests on a culinary journey from the roots of the local area to more globally inspired tastes that include forays into the cuisine of Arabia, Peru and Asia. His creative market-inspired cooking centres around several interesting menus: the seasonal focused Terreta, Producte, a tasting-style option entitled Rubén Miralles, plus a vegan option (Amarant).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4290;La Montería;Spain;Madrid;Lope de Rueda 35, Madrid, 28009, Spain;40.4203134;-3.6775299;30;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;With its location just a few steps from the Retiro, this restaurant is usually full every day and is well worth considering if you find yourself close to this stunning park. With a history dating back over a half a century, this family-run business has had a facelift and now features a more contemporary bar plus a Nordic-inspired dining room. The culinary theme remains the same, however: honest cooking on an extensive à la carte that always features a game dish, plus excellent set menus (Clásico and Degustación). The prawns in batter dish is one of the most popular on the menu here.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4291;Juan Veintitrés;Spain;Benifaió;Papa Juan XXIII 8, Benifaió, 46450, Spain;39.2873039;-0.420869;90;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Impressively run by three brothers, with one in charge of the kitchen and the other two front of house, this restaurant initially started life as a simple bar, but now features two contemporary-style dining rooms. It has the unusual feature of not having a written menu in order to create a more direct relationship with diners, so dishes available are announced at your table. Traditional seasonal cooking with a modern twist, with a focus on fresh fish (monkfish with linguine, hake with a “pil-pil” sauce) and savoury rice dishes including “arroz a banda”, and rice with lobster, artichokes etc.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4292;Becook;Spain;Leon;Cantareros 2, Leon, 24003, Spain;42.59503;-5.566833;92;false;true;Fusion, Modern Cuisine;Following experience gained in leading restaurants such as the Nerua Guggenheim Bilbao, chef David García decided to return to his roots to give full expression to his creativity in this dining space with its very own personality. Fun and informal in style, Becook boasts a modern bistro-style interior with an open-view kitchen and an internationally inspired menu that showcases contemporary techniques and a mix of Oriental and urban touches. We can highly recommend the “Perfecto" salmon as well as the croquettes (make sure you ask which filling is on offer as it changes weekly depending on the availability of ingredients in the market). An interesting tasting menu is also available.;Air conditioning;[]
4293;Nardi;Spain;Hervás;Braulio Navas 19, Hervás, 10700, Spain;40.2730083;-5.8598402;40;true;false;Regional Cuisine;In a town such as Hervás that is so popular with tourists, it is always encouraging to find a restaurant like this offering contemporary dining but without completely sidelining traditional cuisine, hence its focus on products from the Ambroz valley. Located along a pedestrianised street in the centre of town, it boasts a summer terrace, a bar counter, and a dining room on two floors. Choose between a seasonal à la carte and an impressive tasting menu with its own take on Extremadura nouvelle cuisine. We particularly recommend the orange-infused crispy confit of suckling pig and the “chocolate mushroom” (seta de chocolate).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4294;Pacífico;Spain;Ourense;Pena Trevinca 37, Ourense, 32005, Spain;42.3334068;-7.8611341;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This classic family-run restaurant founded in 1975 by the grandparents of current owner Francisco Domínguez has moved with the times and now presents a much more appealing modern feel. The café-bar at the entrance leads to a bistro-style dining room with an open-view kitchen. Here, the focus Monday to Friday is on a single, contemporary tasting menu based around seasonal and locally sourced products, with an extensive brunch available at the weekend. Given its success it’s advisable to book ahead.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
4295;Vinatea;Spain;Morella;Blasco de Alagón 17, Morella, 12300, Spain;40.6182728;-0.1008078;68;false;false;Contemporary;A homely restaurant occupying a restored 12C house that was once part of an attractive porticoed street in the centre of Morella. Inside, the classic-cum-contemporary dining room shares space with an unusual 13C well and a glass-fronted wine cellar in the basement. The cuisine here is centred around traditional Morella recipes which have been pleasantly updated both in terms of presentation and culinary technique and can be enjoyed via the à la carte and the Raíces (Roots) tasting menu, on which local producers and seasonal ingredients play a prominent role.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4296;Daluan;Spain;Morella;Callejón Cárcel 4, Morella, 12300, Spain;40.6188759;-0.0993829;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;One of the best dining options if you’re visiting this charming town with its sloping streets and alleyways teeming with history. It features a tranquil terrace that occupies almost the entire street plus a tastefully arranged dining room on the first floor. The à la carte (featuring recipes such as Morella-style croquettes and roast shoulder of lamb) has remained faithful to its updated take on traditional cuisine and never fails to showcase seasonally inspired local products and flavours, and is complemented by a surprising tasting menu. Themed events dedicated to wild mushrooms and truffles are particularly popular here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4297;Mesón del Pastor;Spain;Morella;Cuesta de Jovani 7, Morella, 12300, Spain;40.61797;-0.1007192;95;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a classic-cum-regional feel in the historic quarter of this walled town. Behind the attractive stone façade is a two-storey building, the upper floor of which is contemporary and functional and the lower one boasting an elegant rusticity. The chef enjoys working with locally sourced products, particularly game and red meats cooked on the wood grill. Its themed food days dedicated to wild mushrooms (November-December) and truffles (January-February) are particularly popular. The colourful paper figures on the stairs are a reminder of the famous El Sexenni festival, which is held in Morella every six years.;Air conditioning;[]
4298;A Xanela Gastronómica;Spain;Ponteareas;Real 62, Ponteareas, 36860, Spain;42.1762245;-8.5001761;44;false;false;Contemporary;(Temporarily closed for refurbishment) A well-established restaurant with plenty of history behind it, owned by two chefs, Ángel and Víctor, who also happen to be good friends, and who have shared their mutual love of food since they met at the Pontevedra hotel school. In this contemporary setting, choose between eating in the gastro-bar and the meticulously appointed dining room (the two tables by the window overlooking the kitchen are highly recommended for their views of the chefs in action). Although the daily menu is ever popular, there is also a strong focus on a contemporary à la carte with a hint of fusion, which champions Galician produce and ingredients. The focus on the wine is mainly on small-scale Galician producers.;Air conditioning;[]
4299;Almanaque Casa de Comidas;Spain;Cadiz;Plaza de España 5 duplicado, Cadiz, 11006, Spain;36.535654;-6.2939386;45;true;false;Contemporary, Andalusian;A small, charming restaurant occupying a historic building in the old quarter of Cádiz, next to the Plaza de España park, the latter home to the monument to the 1812 constitution. Juan Carlos Borrell, for several years a pupil of award-winning Valencian chef Ricard Camarena from whom it is said he learnt how to cook rice to absolute perfection, showcases cuisine that avoids unnecessary frills to concentrate on safeguarding traditional Cádiz recipes and maximising flavour. On the concise à la carte, which works with the seasons, make sure you try the typical Poleá dessert.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4300;Arrocería Maribel;Spain;El Palmar;Francisco Monleón 5, El Palmar, 46012, Spain;39.3106151;-0.3179962;80;true;true;Rice Dishes;The Parque Natural de la Albufera, with its ecosystem of major ecological interest, is teeming with restaurants and “arrocerías” specialising in the same ingredient, namely rice, so the Maribel stands out even more as a result. Its updated interior highlights the rich rice-growing culture of the region, enhanced by a spacious terrace that is within touching distance of the canal. The à la carte, featuring a traditional section and one which is more creative and contemporary, is complemented by two set menus that extol the virtues of local dishes and the full flavours of the Valencia region. A boat trip on the lake is a must here!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4301;Somiatruites;Spain;Igualada;Del Sol 19, Igualada, 08700, Spain;41.57798;1.614032;80;false;false;Contemporary;The name of this restaurant, which can be translated as “dreamers”, showcases the personality of chef David Andrés and his brother Xavier who are behind the transformation of an old tanning factory next to the Museu de la Pell (Leather Museum) in Igualada. In this industrial-style setting of stone walls, open brickwork, designer furniture and striking leather decoration hanging from the ceiling (a nod to the history of the building), enjoy modern and fun cuisine with its roots in traditional cooking, including a highly affordable set menu during the week. The concise à la carte is restricted to evenings and weekends.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4302;Al Margen;Spain;Bilbao;Muelle Urazurrutia 2, Bilbao, 48003, Spain;43.2544495;-2.9235659;94;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Above anything else, the concept at Al Margen champions "taste through simplicity". This relaxed and informal restaurant alongside the estuary next to San Antón bridge, features a decor of highly original stone columns and hydraulic floor tiles that give it plenty of character, alongside bare tables and a semi-open kitchen at the entrance. The young chefs at the helm here, Adrián Leonelli and Pablo Valdearcos, have created a concise à la carte that showcases updated traditional cuisine that is technically accomplished yet fun and always built around the freshest seasonal produce. A tasting menu is also an option.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4303;La Finca - Villa Xarahiz;Spain;Jaraíz de la Vera;Carretera EX 203, Jaraíz de la Vera, 10400, Spain;40.0666884;-5.753258;28;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant with rooms available for those guests keen to explore the beautiful La Vera region. It is run by two siblings, Pilar and Víctor, who have taken over the reins here with both enthusiasm and dedication. Choose from two menus – a set daily option and a more seasonal offering, the latter changing three times a year. These feature Iberian meats, suckling pig, young local goat, and the famous Grandma Fidela’s “migas”, which are renowned throughout the local area. Víctor is also a lover of rum, hence the choice of over 100 different labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4304;Bar Verat;Spain;Santa Coloma de Gramenet;Avenida Pallaresa 104, Santa Coloma de Gramenet, 08921, Spain;41.455486;2.2065718;86;false;false;Fusion;The name of this restaurant (the Catalan for mackerel) clearly shows its intentions, as it describes a fish which is easily affordable to one and all. The latter concept is the predominant idea behind Verat, the younger sibling of the award-winning Lluerna next door, where chef Víctor Quintillà popularises his cuisine in fusion dishes and “raciones”. Here, in a young and informal ambience full of character, choose between three menus for a minimum of two people (Petit, Verat and Festival) plus a few specialities that should not be missed, such as the crunchy Duroc pork ear with a kimchi mayonnaise, the trio of croquettes, and the Iberian suckling pig terrine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4305;Maskarada;Spain;Lekunberri;Aralar 66, Lekunberri, 31870, Spain;43.01121;-1.90254;45;false;false;Pork, Regional Cuisine;Located on a small industrial estate on the outskirts of Lekunberri, Masakarada is a highly unusual and interesting eatery where everything revolves around the breed of pig known as "Pío Negro" or "Euskal Txerri". The restaurant is perfectly complemented by a shop selling charcuterie, cheeses and fresh meat (jowl, cheek, and special Spanish cuts such as “secreto” and “pluma”). The business operates a 360° strategy that involves the rearing of "happy pigs" in complete liberty in the area around the nearby town of Arruitz. The cuisine here is showcased on two tasting menus: Maskarada and Suletina.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4306;El Aguarde;Spain;Santa Cruz de Tenerife;Costa y  Grijalba 21, Santa Cruz de Tenerife, 38004, Spain;28.4702312;-16.2577629;40;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, which has gained a loyal and predominantly local following over the years, is located just a few metres from the city’s main artery, the Rambla de Santa Cruz. The secret to its success? Maybe patience – a nod, perhaps, to its name (a hunting term that is associated with the wait in a hideout). In the simply furnished dining room, order from a reasonably extensive à la carte that is traditional in feel but with a La Mancha touch that highlights the owner’s origins. Recommended dishes includes stews with beans or chickpeas, the hearty la Mancha dish “Duelos y Quebrantos”, offal recipes, and the ever-popular “tortilla de papas”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4307;El de Alberto;Spain;A Coruña;Comandante Fontanes 1, A Coruña, 15003, Spain;43.3699357;-8.4047628;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A traditional restaurant with countless loyal (mainly local) customers which is entering a new era with its move to centrally located, comfortable and much larger premises just a few metres from both the Orzán and Riazor beaches. Behind the well-maintained façade, with its large windows that bathe the modern dining room in plenty of light, the ever-present figure of Alberto keeps a watchful eye on proceedings, with the main aim of spoiling his guests. The cooking here is an updated take on traditional cuisine, featuring dishes that are copious, increasingly modern in feel and based around high-quality products.;Air conditioning;[]
4308;Santé;Spain;Leganés;Avenida del Dos de Mayo 1, Leganés, 28912, Spain;40.3356553;-3.7627179;82;false;true;Farm to table;A restaurant that comes as a pleasant surprise thanks to the quality of its cuisine, the level of professionalism shown by the young team at the helm, and above all for its setting in an attractive, wooden chalet-style property surrounded by trees and greenery next to the campus of the Carlos III university. In the bright dining room you can savour its traditional market cuisine, with a contemporary touch and a nod to the cuisine of other countries around the world, with the open grill at the heart of most dishes on the menu. One dish that we particularly enjoyed was the grilled Hass avocado with “pico de gallo” sauce, feta cheese, and lime vinaigrette.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4309;El Origen;Spain;Huesca;Plaza Justicia 4, Huesca, 22001, Spain;42.1378049;-0.4048128;98;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;El Origen’s main dining room is dominated by an unusual mural that recalls the history of the square on which it is located, which is affectionately known as “Los Tocinos” (literally “bacon”) because of the pig fair that used to take place here. Owner-chef Beatriz Allué creates traditional cuisine with a contemporary touch both in terms of preparation and presentation, with a clear preference for organic produce from Aragón. Her father, a farmer, supplies her directly with many of these, thus ensuring maximum freshness. Choose between a good-value daily menu and two others (Aragonés and Degustación) that require advance booking. Signature dishes include the stew of La Hoya chickpeas with lamb “chiretas” (a type of local sausage) from de La Puebla de Castro, the traditional “chilindrón” stew made with free-range chicken from Los Monegros and a splash of Rancio wine, and the baked triple cheesecake with coffee-flavoured salted toffee and caramelised almonds.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4310;Canteré;Spain;Hecho;Aire 1, Hecho, 22720, Spain;42.7388911;-0.7512234;24;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;It is well worth visiting this mountain village to eat at this restaurant occupying a typical “chesa”-style house with an impressive old vine adorning the façade. Enjoy a drink in the public bar before heading upstairs to the attractive rustic-contemporary dining room featuring bright dining spaces, a minimum of furniture and impressive lighting. Here, the chef showcases a traditionally inspired menu brought impressively up to date that always tries to champion seasonal and locally sourced ingredients. Canteré’s food-themed events are also highly popular, one of which is devoted to wild mushrooms, and another to game.;Air conditioning;[]
4311;Brigecio;Spain;Morales de Rey;Avenida Constitución 28, Morales de Rey, 49693, Spain;42.0666268;-5.784549;60;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Impressively run by a friendly married couple, this restaurant located in a small village 10km to the northwest of Benavente takes its name from an ancient Asturian hill fort known as “Castro Brigecio”. Behind its façade, you’ll find a single, slightly impersonal contemporary-style dining room, albeit with a welcoming fireplace and excellent service. The extensive à la carte of traditional cuisine (on which you’ll also find the occasional more modern and contemporary recipe) is complemented by a selection of cod dishes (“bacalao a lo Tío” and “bacalao con crestas de gallo” (chicken comb) etc), an impressive daily menu (except in summer), plus a more extensive set option entitled Bib Gourmand in honour of our Michelin distinction! The famous Zamora-style octopus is a must!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4312;La Cantina de Diego;Spain;Monachil;Callejón de Ricarda 2, Monachil, 18193, Spain;37.1309366;-3.5362658;60;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant located in the town’s old quarter, where you can choose between the summer terrace and two attractive rooms, both with a rustic, regionally inspired ambience. In the kitchen, owner-chef Diego Higueras focuses on technically uncomplicated traditional cooking that remains faithful to seasonal products and is increasingly focused towards the “zero miles” philosophy. His specialities include the scrambled eggs with Monachil black pudding, fried cod tacos with tomato, the local sirloin, and Marcelina, a typical dessert.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4313;Deli;Spain;Montellano;Plaza de Andalucía 10, Montellano, 41770, Spain;36.9951721;-5.5734199;18;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A love of cooking with its roots in tradition is behind the values of this restaurant with its impressive array of rice dishes, soups, stews, and specialities such as Segovia-style roast suckling pig. Now run by the third generation of the family, Deli always works with local producers to source its ingredients, focusing on the traditional cooking of inland Andalucia, with some recipes on the menu harking back to the region’s long period of Moorish rule. Specialities here include creamy rice with local partridge, the delicious snails in an almond and dried red pepper sauce, and the exquisite artichokes.;Air conditioning;[]
4314;El Raier;Spain;La Pobla de Segur;Avenida de Madrid 3, La Pobla de Segur, 25500, Spain;42.2498055;0.9661876;91;false;true;Contemporary;This restaurant takes its name from the old Pyrenean tradition of log rafts, used to transport timber by river (there’s a exhibition dedicated to this traditional craft next to the railway station where the historic Tren dels Llacs also makes a stop). We were pleasantly surprised to find this restaurant, which embraces tradition from a more contemporary perspective, in so doing showcasing the so-called “Pallaresa nouvelle cuisine” (noteworthy dishes include the magnum of organic chicken with kimchi mayonnaise and tonkatsu, and the trout belly served with its own roe). This simple yet pleasant eatery, with an open kitchen behind the bar, is run by a friendly duo of chefs, Claudia and Jaime, who showcase their technical yet fresh and fun cuisine, which they skilfully change according to the availability of local, seasonal ingredients. We recommend eating at the high tables by the kitchen counter so that you can watch the two chefs in full flow!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4315;Qiao Ai Lai Lai Xiao Long (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;506 Tianjin Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2381117;121.472547;93;false;false;Dim Sum;This simple little shop tucked away in a bustling alley has been packed with hungry diners ever since it opened its doors 20 years ago. The chefs are always busy in the kitchen making xiao long bao, the crab roe variety being the most popular. Brace yourself for an even bigger crowd in hairy crab season, when wontons, spring rolls and soups are generously loaded with crabmeat and roe. The classic soupy pork buns are another must-try.;Cash only;[]
4316;Tasty Congee & Noodle Wantun Shop;China Mainland;Shanghai;S-B1-05, Stone Zone, Taikoo Li Qiantan, Lane 500, Dongyu Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.1554083;121.476826;47;false;true;Noodles and Congee;After moving from Shanghai IFC to this address in 2021, this branch of the Hong Kong-based chain got a fresh lick of paint in light pink and mint green. Regulars were reassured that the menu, food, kitchen and service teams all stayed the same. As always, wonton noodle soup fascinates with its springy noodles, briny-sweet broth and the freshest shrimp filling. Other famous items like pineapple buns and barbecue meats are also made fresh in-house.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4317;A Niang Mian Guan;China Mainland;Shanghai;36 Sinan Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.219411;121.46196;80;false;false;Noodles;If you arrive at this very popular noodle shop at peak time the first thing you’ll notice is the queue. When you get to the front, place your order and pay at the counter at the entrance before finding a seat. The standouts are yellow croaker noodles, and noodles with stir-fried eels. To better experience the skills of the chef here, it’s also worth ordering side dishes, such as shredded pork with pickled vegetables.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4319;Rong Cuisine;China Mainland;Shanghai;1-2F, 128 Taicang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.221725;121.4756813;84;false;false;Taizhou;A spin-off of Xin Rong Ji, targeting a younger audience at a lower price range. Service may not be as formal and refined as its pricier sister, but is still pleasant and friendly. Both share the same sources of ingredients so freshness is guaranteed. On the menu, grilled fish, seafood and farm-style Zhejiang cooking dominate. Seasoning tends to be light to allow authentic flavours to come through. Reservations are accepted for private rooms only.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4320;Mao Long;China Mainland;Shanghai;134 Jinxian Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.224693;121.456695;73;true;false;Shanghainese;Since 1989 this little gem has been serving no-frills Shanghainese home-style dishes made with the best ingredients available. Converted from a residential home, it’s a 20-seater place with five tables and is run by a mother in her 80s and her daughter – they make sure recipes passed down from grandpa are strictly followed. Seafood makes up a big part of the menu, but they are especially proud of their braised pork.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4321;Cong's Kitchen;China Mainland;Shanghai;158 Luhe Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2392083;121.4700638;74;true;true;Shanghainese;Chef-owner Cong is a retiree in his 70s. Passionate about cooking, he returned to Shanghai and opened this restaurant after stints in Hong Kong. Although his food is largely Shanghainese, the menu includes his own creations in addition to the all-time classics. The sautéed river shrimps with tomalley are loaded with umami. Diners also flock here for his fish liver pâté and marinated skate fish. For dinner parties, there are seven private rooms.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
4323;Polux;China Mainland;Shanghai;No. 5, Xintiandi Beili, Lane 181, Taicang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.223003;121.47053;39;true;true;French;Don’t be perplexed if certain items on the menu seem familiar – this all-day dining bistro is from Paul Pairet of Ultraviolet and Mr & Mrs Bund fame. Some dishes echo the signatures from those establishments, albeit rendered in simpler forms. Onion soup is recommended – rich and well-balanced, with a nice contrast of textures. The classic Parisian décor with an industrial twist works perfectly. Reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4324;Yangzhou Fan Dian (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;345 Middle Fujian Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.237972;121.475334;80;false;true;Huaiyang;This senior member of the Shanghai dining scene is as busy as ever, especially after a facelift in 2017 that added a private room. The dining room is decorated with paintings and wood carvings, while the floor-to-ceiling window on the second floor frames the gorgeous city views. As always, it serves authentic Huai Yang food, impeccably made and reasonably priced. Must-tries include shredded tofu in soup and braised pork balls.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
4325;Jingmei Wuxi Noodles (Jingan);China Mainland;Shanghai;128 Yanping Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2310493;121.436471;76;false;true;Noodles;As well as noodles, this unstuffy stall serves Wuxi dishes and dim sum. Must-tries include noodle soup or scallion oil-dressed noodles with Wuxi-style pork ribs braised in soy paste – the fall-off-the-bone ribs are loaded in flavour. “Three-white” big wontons with white fish, white shrimp and whitebait filling burst with rich umami, while Sichuan pepper in the dip adds contrast. Dim sum like xiao long bao and yu lan cake are worth the wait.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
4326;Xiao Tao Mian Guan;China Mainland;Shanghai;222 Jiashan Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2108612;121.4550625;18;true;true;Noodles;This long-standing neighbourhood noodle shop was renovated a few years back. Noodles are either tossed in shallot oil or served in broth, but the former are more popular. They come with a heap of fried scallion, but you can also add an array of toppings, like spicy ground pork with diced potato, fried pork ribs, braised pork belly, or eel. You can also ask for a free refill of noodles. Come early to beat the peak-time queues.;;[]
4327;The Lakeside Veggie;China Mainland;Shanghai;L2-016-017, Sunny Walk, 230 Ruiping Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.1839757;121.4510119;66;true;false;Vegetarian;The brand started on the banks of West Lake, Hangzhou, hence the name. This outpost near Longhua Temple is especially popular among worshippers. The room is furnished in a modern style, with a show kitchen where diners can see the chefs making dim sum. Try their matsutake soup dumplings, with three mushrooms enrobed in translucent skin. Seared tofu is loaded with smoky peppery flavours. The desserts and drinks are also popular.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4328;YongFu Mini (Pudong);China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 910, 9F, L+Mall, 899 South Pudong Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.233478;121.510812;56;true;true;Ningbo;A spin-off from Yong Fu, this restaurant serves only seafood caught in the East China Sea the same day, such as Miiuy croaker and hairtail, but at a lower price point. The must-try signature '18 chops' – raw crabs marinated in spiced soy and wine – is only available from November to April. Other Ningbo favourites like Shaoxing wine chicken and grilled cabbage are also well executed. Reservations aren’t taken so arrive early to beat the crowd.;;[]
4329;Lao Di Fang Mian Guan;China Mainland;Shanghai;107 Sinan Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.215643;121.477384;48;false;false;Noodles;In business for over 30 years, this noodle shop has recently moved to this new location. Rest assured that the menu and flavours remain the same and all noodles are served with toppings cooked à la minute. Try the toothsome cuttlefish noodles with pickled cabbage for a lovely crunch, complemented by seafood umami. Local favourites such as braised pork belly in spiced dark soy, and tofu skin-wrapped pork are also worth trying.;Cash only;[]
4330;Ho Hung Kee;China Mainland;Shanghai;L324, South Building, HKRI Taikoo Hui, 288 Shimen Yi Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.231354;121.458521;100;false;false;Noodles and Congee;For a noodle shop, the Chinese-inspired faux-industrial decor is lavish – brushed brass ring pendant lamps and black wrought-iron arches perforated with floral motifs. The menu is almost the same as at its Hong Kong counterparts. The must-order shrimp wonton noodle soup comes with springy noodles and crisp sweet shrimps enrobed in a translucent skin. Or try the char siu pork puff pastry with spot-on seasoning and fine noodles with a generous covering of shrimp roe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4333;Lu Bo Lang;China Mainland;Shanghai;115 Yuyuan Old Street, City God Temple, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.22843;121.487434;20;false;false;Shanghainese;After a makeover in 2019, the room now boasts wavy silvery panels on the ceiling and recessed lights emitting a subtle green glow. Despite the update in décor, the menu stays the same so expect food that is as tasty and reasonably priced. Shanghainese dim sum is still the key draw - turnip pastry, osmanthus glutinous rice cake and ‘eyebrow’ pastry are the must-try items. Private rooms on the 2nd and 3rd floors can cater to parties of various sizes.;Air conditioning;[]
4334;Rongjia Noodles Soup with Yellow Croaker (Jingan);China Mainland;Shanghai;L105A-1, 688 Plaza, 688 West Nanjing Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.230911;121.464584;82;true;false;Noodles;Xin Rong Ji is famous for its exclusive source of yellow croakers – this is a spin-off from the brand specialising in handmade noodles in the same rich milky fish broth, but priced a bit more wallet-friendly. The signature is obviously yellow croaker noodles, but the assorted seafood is also good. Don’t miss the Chaozhou-style marinated goose and Taizhou-style dim sum made fresh daily.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4335;Hao Sheng;China Mainland;Shanghai;156 Guangyuan Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.233217;121.488596;84;true;false;Shanghainese;The decor is not much to write home about, but authentic home-style Shanghainese fare – sautéed river shrimps, blanched pork liver – keeps the regulars coming. The drunken chicken steeped in warm Shaoxing wine has silky flesh and an intoxicating aroma. The chef doesn't offer an à la carte menu, but chooses for you according to your budget, allergies, preference and what's fresh. There are just a few tables and one private room, so book well ahead.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4336;Chun;China Mainland;Shanghai;124 Jinxian Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2235893;121.4553952;98;true;false;Shanghainese;After a hiatus of a few years, this famous joint re-opened at the same address and former regulars flocked back for the sorely missed classics. The room has few bells and whistles to steal the spotlight from the food, and the friendly owner always makes the best recommendations. In her 60s, she still hand-picks the freshest ingredients from the market daily. Try deep-fried river shrimps, and stuffed paddy field snails, both meticulously done.;Cash only;[]
4337;Gong De Lin (West Nanjing Road);China Mainland;Shanghai;445 West Nanjing Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.238362;121.489489;73;true;false;Vegetarian;When you see that sweet and sour pork and fried shredded eel are on the menu you may doubt if the food is truly vegan but fear not – all the mock-meat and fish is made with either veggies, soy product or mushrooms. This institution of Shanghainese vegan cooking has been serving plant-based dishes in disguise since 1922. Its annexed shop now sells cake and snacks freshly made in-house, such as the tasty mugwort rice dumplings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4338;Easeful Cuisine (Jingan);China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, 90 South Shaanxi Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.223137;121.452217;49;false;true;Jiangzhe;The owner-chef has over 10 years of experience working in upmarket establishments in Chinese cities and advocates a back-to-basics approach to home-style cooking that brings out natural flavours of the ingredients. His boneless smoked fish boasts fine juicy flesh in a crispy crust, while brown sugar walnut rice cake is nicely charred on the outside, with a chewy centre. On top of the cosy dining room, there are 6 private ones to choose from.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4339;Wang Lu;China Mainland;Shanghai;01-02, 3F, New Bund 31 Mall, No.15, Lane 666, West Haiyang Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.5286479;121.479627;85;true;true;Chinese;The room sports a modern Chinese vibe, dotted with framed orange scarves and table mats in matching equestrian motifs. To suit the local palate, the kitchen dials down the heat slightly, but the food still packs an authentic Jiangxi kick. Rich, flavoursome double-steamed soft-shelled tortoise with fish maw is served according to a ritual that symbolises good fortune. Jiangxi-style three-cup chicken boasts firm flesh and perfect caramelisation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4340;Yu Ge Zhanjiang (Jingan);China Mainland;Shanghai;358 West Yan'an Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2206336;121.4345482;87;true;true;Cantonese;Open until 2am, this restaurant specialising in regional dishes from the Cantonese city of Zhanjiang is a popular choice for a late-night supper. Free-range chicken shipped from the city is steamed or deep-fried for juicy flesh and intense flavour. The pan-fried white pomfret packs an umami punch and brings briny sweetness. Chinese mugwort cake is a rustic snack stuffed with a savoury or sweet filling then steamed. Pre-order dishes to avoid disappointment.;;[]
4342;Yu Du Lao Wei Mian (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;501 Liyuan Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2098589;121.477205;73;true;false;Noodles;The owner hails from Zhoushan, famous for its seafood. His mother taught him how to make noodles and he started this shop over 10 years ago to bring authentic Zhoushan noodles to Shanghai. Noodle soup is typically paired with fish shipped from his hometown, such as yellow croaker braised in bean sauce or the premium deboned beltfish, available only in October and November. The delicious yellow croaker spring rolls are hugely popular.;Cash only;[]
4343;Yunhe Noodle (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;344 Changle Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2221557;121.4533689;80;false;false;Noodles, Shanghainese;Tucked inside a residential neighbourhood, this noodle shop with a subtle sign may not draw much attention from the outside. But the interior is a different world – where neon signs and graffiti murals subvert your expectations. House-made spinach noodles are topped with crabmeat with roe, or ‘shrimp trio’ (shrimps, tomalley and roe), with the option of adding clams or matsutake mushrooms. Seaweed crusted yellow croaker is also good.;Cash only;[]
4344;Chic 1699;China Mainland;Shanghai;L807, 8F, Times Square, 500 Zhangyang Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.229228;121.513247;33;false;false;Fujian;The Chic 1699 brand started out in Xiamen and this is their first venture in Shanghai. In the kitchen, a team of Fujianese chefs prepares authentic dishes with produce and fish mostly from their home province. Steamed mangrove crab with black sticky rice wrapped in lotus leaf boasts briny-sweet crabmeat and buttery roe. The airy, yet cosy room is great for all kinds of get-togethers. Top marks for the thoughtful, attentive service.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4345;Leen's;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;1F, 136A Jalan Burhanuddin Helmi, Taman Tun Dr Ismail, Kuala Lumpur, 60000, Malaysia;3.1531381;101.6228941;90;false;true;Middle Eastern;After delivering home-cooked meals during the pandemic, the Syrian chef opened his brick-and-mortar shop, and it quickly became a neighbourhood favourite. The heady aromas of freshly baked goods fill the space. Unmistakably Middle Eastern, the food is rife with bold colours and flavours. The smoked hummus infused with burnt chilli oil tastes mildly spicy and very smoky. Try the kebab khashkhash – lamb skewers in a sharp, spicy poppy seed sauce.;Air conditioning;[]
4346;Lum Lai Duck Meat Koay Teow Th'ng;Malaysia;George Town;Pasar Lebuh Cecil, 24 Lebuh Cecil, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4073917;100.328729;83;true;true;Street Food;For 40+ years, they have been making their kway teow soup the same way – with duck, pork and fish cake. The broth bursts with umami, the duck is silky, and fried garlic and shallot bits add aroma. Expect to queue at peak hours.;Cash only;[]
4347;Laksalicious;Malaysia;George Town;117A Jalan Hutton, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.4201797;100.3300729;52;false;true;Malaysian;With a caricature of the owner on its sign and a mural deconstructing its signature items, Laksalicious is a cheerful little gem bubbling with character. As its name suggests, laksa is the main event here – choose between Nyonya assam laksa with sour, spicy fish broth or Nyonya laksa lemak with rich, creamy coconut milk broth. Prawn crackers add texture and flavours. Crispy prawn fritters, nasi ulam and gula melacca cendol are also popular.;Air conditioning;[]
4348;Penang Road Famous Jin Kor Char Kuey Teow;Malaysia;George Town;Joo Hooi Cafe, 475 Jalan Penang, George Town, 10000, Malaysia;5.4171171;100.3305642;15;false;true;Street Food;This stall has been around for almost 40 years. Kuey Teow is made to order, topped with shrimps, blood clams, pork sausage and bean sprouts, boasting lovely wok hei. For added punch, opt for duck egg and extra chilli sauce.;Cash only;[]
4349;Siam Road Char Koay Teow;Malaysia;George Town;82 Jalan Siam, George Town, 10400, Malaysia;5.4148507;100.320846;30;true;true;Street Food;Open for half days, this small store draws long queues – mostly tourists and young customers. They serve just one dish: stir-fried koay teow. The wok-fried flat rice noodles emit a charcoal aroma, are well seasoned and come with quality ingredients that can be spiced to taste.;Cash only;[]
4351;BM Yam Rice;Malaysia;Seberang Perai;7 Jalan Murthy, Bukit Mertajam, Seberang Perai, 14000, Malaysia;5.3608822;100.462294;64;false;true;Teochew;Since opening its doors in 2006, this shop has been serving the owner’s family recipe. They pride themselves with their yam rice with pork soup – you can choose to have pork offal in the soup or not. The yam rice is nicely cooked, with strong shrimp flavour. The pork broth is briny-sweet and the pickled mustard green gives it a tangy depth. The offal is cooked to the perfect texture while the pork balls are peppery and flavoursome.;;[]
4352;Duck Blood Curry Mee;Malaysia;George Town;223B Jalan Burma, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.423869;100.3209241;27;true;true;Street Food;Hidden in a Malaysian-style café, this shop serves mee in a savoury-sweet white curry base made with coconut milk. Among the various toppings offered, roasted pork is phenomenal. Make sure you try the homemade chilli sauce.;Cash only;[]
4353;Roti by d'Tandoor;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;82 Jalan Damai, off Jalan Ampang, Kampung Datuk Keramat, Kuala Lumpur, 55000, Malaysia;3.1631794;101.7249867;83;true;false;Indian;A North Indian brand, d'Tandoor opened in Malaysia in 1990 and has since spread to other countries around the world. Located in a residential area, they offer a hearty range of fine Indian cuisine, featuring a consummate blend of herbs and spices. Highlights include well-seasoned butter chicken masala and soft, chewy naan bread, while Kulfi ice-cream – available in a variety of flavours – adds a final flourish to the meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4354;Hor Poh Cuisine;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;36 Jalan 6/38D, Taman Sri Sinar, Segambut, Kuala Lumpur, 52100, Malaysia;3.1892069;101.6528953;88;false;true;Hakkanese;This simple shop has been selling authentic Hakkanese food in an unremarkable neighbourhood for over 20 years. The must-try Hor Poh lui cha is a sheeny green soup served with steamed rice. Made with ground sesame seeds, peanuts and mint leaves, the soup is nutty and aromatic. The Hor Poh dumpling with dried tofu, garlic and pickles enrobed in a thin skin is also popular. With a range of tasty offerings at bargain prices, this place is always busy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
4355;Jalan Ipoh Claypot Chicken Rice;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot 1224, 7 Jalan Batu Ambar, Taman Kok Lian, Kuala Lumpur, 51200, Malaysia;3.2026205;101.673466;16;false;true;Street Food;For over 30 years, this stall has been selling chicken rice cooked to order over charcoal in claypots. The dish comes with Cantonese pork sausage and ginger, and has a crispy crust at the bottom. You can add salted fish, which imparts extra aroma.;Cash only;[]
4356;Bridge Street Prawn Noodle;Malaysia;George Town;533 Lebuh Pantai, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4117853;100.333995;42;false;false;Noodles;This third generation family business with 60+ years of history has helped many Penangese kick-start their day with hearty Hokkien mee. The signature prawn mee features yellow noodles and rice vermicelli in a spicy prawn broth that is loaded with deep flavours. The small shop has indoor and outdoor seating. For an authentic local experience, sit on the covered patio and order an iced drink to go with the noodles. Closes every 1st and 15th of the Lunar calendar.;Cash only;[]
4357;Moh Teng Pheow Nyonya Koay;Malaysia;George Town;Jalan Masjid, off Lebuh Chulia, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4193028;100.3353623;84;true;false;Small eats;In 1933, the owner’s father founded a factory specialising in kuih, a broad term referring to various local cakes, dumplings, pudding and pastries. In 2016, the owner opened a sit-down restaurant behind the factory for guests to try their freshly made kuih, such as kuih lapis, kuih talam, ang koo, and Nyonya chang, alongside a few Nyonya dishes. Head to the rustic patio with exposed brick walls and a vine-covered pergola for some al fresco fun.;;[]
4359;Coast by Kayra;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot G03-G05, GF, The Starhill, 181 Jalan Bukit Bintang, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1473545;101.7139167;39;false;true;Indian;The sister establishment of Kayra stays true to its sea-to-plate ethos, and the turquoise accents in the décor are a nod to the ocean theme. The kitchen excels at reimagining the traditional dishes of Kerala in sophisticated ways. Quality seafood and produce are sourced locally to support small farms and fishermen. The must-try Kerala fish curry is based on a family recipe, with raw mango and yoghurt for acidity. Order naan to mop up the tangy sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
4360;Ravi's Famous Apom Manis;Malaysia;George Town;319 Jalan Burma, George Town, 10350, Malaysia;5.4305366;100.3126657;57;false;true;Street Food;Since 1920, this stall has been selling its famous apom: their crispy crêpes with a soft, puffy centre cooked in claypot over charcoal are fluffier and more coconutty than most. Come early – they tend to sell out by 9:30am.;Cash only;[]
4361;Serabai Istimewa;Malaysia;George Town;18 Astaka Taman Tun Sardon, 25 Pintasan Pemancar 5, George Town, 11700, Malaysia;5.3694231;100.3059378;71;false;false;Street Food;This place has been around since 1978 and its serabai – coconut milk rice pancake with palm sugar syrup dip – is still locals' favourite breakfast. Three options are available: plain, palm sugar or with egg. Come before 10am.;Cash only;[]
4362;Wan Dao Tou Assam Laksa;Malaysia;George Town;1 Jalan Gottlieb, George Town, 10350, Malaysia;5.4336771;100.3031369;47;true;true;Street Food;The third-generation owner makes his famous laksa noodle soup according to his grandparents’ recipe dating back 50 years ago. The soup strikes a fine balance between sweetness, sourness and spiciness, while the cucumber, shallot and pineapple cut through the heat nicely. The starter platter is also worth-trying.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
4363;BM Cathay Pancake;Malaysia;Seberang Perai;8 Jalan Aston, Bukit Mertajam, Seberang Perai, 14000, Malaysia;5.3624331;100.4637019;42;true;true;Street Food;Since 1962, this cart outside Cathay Food Court has been serving only one dish – Apam Balik, or chargrilled pancake with sugar peanut filling. Made on the spot and served piping hot, it’s crispy on the outside, chewy on the inside.;Cash only;[]
4364;Sek Yuen;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;313 Jalan Pudu, Pudu, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1358278;101.7120706;62;false;true;Cantonese;Since it opened in 1948, Sek Yuen remains as popular as ever, although it now takes up three shops on the same street. Depending on where you are seated, the room may feel vintage and nostalgic or simple and bright. The menu is mostly traditional Cantonese – pipa duck with spot-on seasoning, firm flesh and crispy skin is a must. House signatures like eight-treasure duck, and roast suckling pig require ordering two days ahead.;;[]
4366;Rasa Rasa;Malaysia;George Town;59 Gat Lebuh Chulia, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4140577;100.3406223;51;true;true;Peranakan;Potted plants are set nicely against a background of exposed brick walls and industrial accents here. On top of the short à la carte menu, the Nyonya combo set built around pandan nasi lemak with your choice of toppings is especially popular. The rice is plated on a banana leaf and topped with mildly hot homemade sambal. Another speciality is Siam bihun – turmeric rice vermicelli with shredded omelette and sauces. Round out the meal with tub tim krob.;;[]
4368;Restoran Pik Wah;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Basement Level, MABA House, 6 Jalan Hang Jebat, Kuala Lumpur City Centre, Kuala Lumpur, 50150, Malaysia;3.1430068;101.7005017;69;true;false;Cantonese;Tucked away from busy traffic, this restaurant could be hard to find, but your efforts will be rewarded with some of the most authentic Chinese food you can get in town. Apart from familiar staples available in all Cantonese restaurants, the longstanding household name also serves rarer items not found elsewhere, such as frog and venison. Their famous dishes in sizzling claypot are simply unmissable. Reservations are recommended on weekends.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4369;Lai Foong Lala Noodles;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;99 Jalan Sultan, Kuala Lumpur City Centre, Kuala Lumpur, 50000, Malaysia;3.1449023;101.6987243;84;false;false;Noodles;What began as a street stall 10 years ago that shot to local fame now occupies two shop floors on the street corner. Red lanterns adorn the ceilings, and large photos cover the walls like wallpaper. Chinese vintage gadgets, like an abacus, decorate the interior. Lala means “clams” in Malay, and a bowl of flavoursome lala bihun with prawns is a must. The broth, meanwhile, is aromatic with Chinese yellow wine and ginger. Portions are generous.;Air conditioning;[]
4370;Winn's Cafe;Malaysia;George Town;38 Jalan Cantonment, George Town, 10350, Malaysia;5.4282966;100.3106189;100;true;true;Peranakan;Run by a husband-wife team, Winn’s Cafe is situated in a detached house with dining rooms spread over two storeys, the upper floor of which exhibits work by local artists. The menu features Peranakan classics, such as otak otak fish cake seasoned with coconut milk and local herbs grown in their backyard and boasts silky smooth texture. Asam tumis stingray seduces with bouncy, flavoursome meat and a rich, complex sauce made with nine herbs.;Air conditioning;[]
4371;Super Star Koay Teow Soup;Malaysia;George Town;78 Lebuh Kimberley, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.416393;100.3328468;44;false;false;Street Food;This popular food cart dates back to 1960 and is now run by the third-generation owner. Koay teow soup with chicken, pork, fish balls and pork liver is the must-try. The chicken feet braised in spiced soy marinade are simply divine.;Cash only;[]
4372;De. Wan 1958 (Taman U Thant);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Level 2-2, The LINC KL, 360 Jalan Tun Razak, Taman U Thant, Kuala Lumpur, 50400, Malaysia;3.1595059;101.7208803;100;true;false;Malaysian;Sunny and cheerful like the local celebrity Chef Wan, the room is inviting and bustling. Similarly, the food is guaranteed to lift your spirits with big tropical flavours. Whet your appetite with pomelo salad with crispy prawn cheeks in kerabu lime dressing and a hint of fish sauce. For mains, go for bakar bakar, BBQ meat or seafood that comes with your choice of the chef’s mouth-watering sauces. Portion sizes are big enough for sharing.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
4373;Congkak (Bukit Bintang);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;24 Jalan Beremi, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 50200, Malaysia;3.1479298;101.7101568;42;true;false;Malaysian;Named after a traditional Malaysian game, Congkak is located in residential Jalan Beremi, not far from the city’s bustling central district. The restaurant is an expression of national pride and identity serving what visitors would deem as exotic, but are classics for locals. The most popular dish, the nasi ambeng platter, offers a multitude of textures and combinations of spicy, sweet and savoury flavours that go nicely with sambal. Different serving size is available to suit for your party size.;Air conditioning;[]
4374;Sin Kiew Yee Shin Kee Beef Noodles;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;7a, Jalan Tun Tan Cheng Lock, Kuala Lumpur City Centre, Kuala Lumpur, 50000, Malaysia;3.1450903;101.6969561;100;false;true;Noodles;What started as a humble food stall back in 1949 is now a household name, famous for its beef noodles in soup or dressed in an aromatic sauce. Choose between ribbon rice noodles, rice vermicelli and thin, bouncy Hakka noodles. In addition to the signature springy beef meatballs and sliced beef, the thickly sliced beef tripe is prized for its tender texture and rich flavours – all perfectly complemented by the home-made chilli sauce.;Cash only;[]
4375;Ah Boy Koay Teow Th'ng;Malaysia;George Town;1 Lebuh Clarke, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.4208271;100.3313733;75;true;false;Street Food;This friendly family-run shop, now in the second generation, specialises in koay teow th'ng, served in soup or dry. The broth is made from chicken and pork bones. The springy tendon balls have a nice ginger flavour. A tasty option is the braised chicken with bean sprouts.;Cash only;[]
4376;Thara;Malaysia;George Town;5 Lorong Prangin, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.4127473;100.3344135;51;true;false;Thai;The high-ceilinged, comfortable room’s green colour scheme has a soothing effect. The Thai kitchen team makes authentic Thai food with the freshest ingredients, especially seafood. Miang kam is a must – the fresh betel leaves with seven condiments and sweet miang kam sauce make for a great appetiser. The aromatic tom yum seafood soup is equally unmissable, and you can choose between creamy and clear versions.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4377;Sao Nam;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;25 Tengkat Tong Shin, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 50200, Malaysia;3.1458668;101.7075277;53;false;false;Vietnamese;A bright yellow colonial-style house, a red sign with a playful twist, and a colourful room that feels warm and welcoming, Sao Nam checks all the right boxes for a fun-filled Vietnamese meal. Their iconic phở bò – rice noodle soup with sliced beef – packs tons of flavour in a broth that takes more than ten hours to make. Their mangosteen and prawn salad tantalises your taste buds with umami, sourness, sweetness and contrasting textures.;Terrace;[]
4379;Green House Prawn Mee & Loh Mee (223 Jalan Burma);Malaysia;George Town;223 Jalan Burma, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.4191353;100.3273692;76;false;true;Street Food;For over 30 years, the regulars have been returning for its Hokkien prawn mee, loh mee, or a mix of both. The red prawn soup made with pork bones and prawn shells boasts deep umami. Twelve additional toppings are also available.;Cash only;[]
4380;Hing Kee Bakuteh (121 Jalan Kepong);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;121 Jalan Kepong, Taman Usahawan, Kuala Lumpur, 52100, Malaysia;3.2139094;101.6373436;29;false;true;Malaysian;Just as bak kut teh is Malaysia's iconic dish and soul food, this restaurant also has a place in the hearts of locals. It’s particularly popular for lunch. The bak kut teh soup has a characteristic mild flavour that’s well-balanced with a subtle use of herbs and light, sweet flavours. The dry, spicy version has a richer, thicker consistency. The four shop houses that line the boulevard offer plenty of seating and absorb the noise and energy of the street.;;[]
4381;Ming Qin Charcoal Duck Egg Char Koay Teow;Malaysia;Seberang Perai;29 Jalan Betek, off Jalan Sungai Rambai, Bukit Mertajam, Seberang Perai, 14000, Malaysia;5.36109;100.45285;27;true;true;Noodles;This shop celebrated its 20th anniversary in 2022 and moved to this address. Here, as indicated in its name, koay teow is stir-fried with duck egg over charcoal fire that imparts exceptional wok hei. Top it up with an extra over-easy egg, or order sour spicy clams on the side to go with the rice noodles. Despite the lack of fancy décor, regulars queue up at the entrance before it opens and it can get busy into midnight on Fridays and Saturdays.;;[]
4382;Hai Kah Lang (Taman Cheras);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;44 Jalan Kaskas 2, Taman Cheras, Kuala Lumpur, 56100, Malaysia;3.10071;101.74155;45;false;true;Seafood;The owner of this joint also runs a seafood stall on the opposite side of the street. Rest assured only the freshest catch (mostly from northern Borneo) can make it to the table. To sample what it has to offer, first-timers may order mixed seafood noodles with crab, clams, fish, squid, shrimp, and laver seaweed in a briny-sweet fish bone broth that exudes rich aromas of Huadiao wine. Snacks like fried fish cake are also worth trying.;Air conditioning;[]
4383;Bibik's Kitchen;Malaysia;George Town;73 Jalan Sri Bahari, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.42124;100.33207;26;false;true;Peranakan;“Bibik” is an honorific used to address older Peranakan women, and the room is aptly decorated with classic Nyonya motifs. Naturally, the menu showcases the owner’s heirloom Peranakan recipes that are slightly less spicy than their counterparts elsewhere. Dishes come in three sizes – try their jiu hu char (stir-fried yam bean with shredded cuttlefish), and loh bak (deep-fried five-spice pork rolls). Laksa is available only on weekends.;Air conditioning;[]
4384;Sardaarji;Malaysia;George Town;6 Lebuh China, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4170929;100.341149;24;true;false;Indian;Colourful drapes add a cheerful vibe while live performances of Indian instruments creates a vibrant ambiance. This restaurant in Little India serves authentic Northern Indian dishes, such as the must-order fish amritsari made with red snapper in a thick, spicy curry of balanced flavours. Dal makhani, or black lentil soup, is best enjoyed with an extra serving of plain chapati. Lastly, save room for gulab jamun that bursts with milky goodness.;Air conditioning;[]
4385;Nam Heong Chicken Rice (City Centre);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;56 Jalan Sultan, Kuala Lumpur City Centre, Kuala Lumpur, 50000, Malaysia;3.1436885;101.6985081;53;true;true;Malaysian;Since 1938, this household name has been hugely popular among the locals for its famous Hainanese chicken rice. Two kinds of chicken are on offer – “veggie farm” chicken with leaner, firmer flesh and a free-range version with fattier, softer meat. Barbecue meats, such as roast pork belly that boasts crispy skin and alternate layers of fat and lean meat, are also bestsellers. Order crispy, juicy Ipoh bean sprouts to go with the rice.;;[]
4386;Neighbourwood;Malaysia;Seberang Perai;3427 Jalan Kulim, Taman Bukit Mas, Bukit Mertajam, Seberang Perai, 14000, Malaysia;5.3520265;100.47592;19;false;false;European Contemporary;The owner lives nearby and opened this cosy spot for his neighbours to enjoy European fare with Asian influences alongside some chargrilled items. The menu changes every six weeks to keep it fresh, but three dishes great for sharing always remain – half roast chicken au jus, Berkshire pork loin, and fish en papillote. For starters, try fish croquettes, and round it out with their homemade desserts. Consider buying their sourdough bread to take home.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4387;Wong Mei Kee;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;30 Jalan Nyonya, off Jalan Pudu, Pudu, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.139235;101.7110243;82;true;true;Street Food;Open for just a few hours a day, this stall attracts foodies in droves with its coveted siew yok – roast pork with crackling skin and succulent meat. Arrive early and wait for the pork to come out of the oven at noon sharp.;;[]
4389;Taman Bukit Curry Mee;Malaysia;Seberang Perai;Jalan Bukit Kecil, Taman Bukit, Bukit Mertajam, Seberang Perai, 14000, Malaysia;5.3548014;100.4595148;52;true;true;Street Food;This stall has been selling curry mee for almost 40 years and is prized for the creamy soup made with coconut milk and spicy curry paste. The half-cooked cockles in the soup taste briny-sweet and burst with juices.;Cash only;[]
4390;Tho Yuen;Malaysia;George Town;92 Lebuh Campbell, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.4180149;100.333816;35;true;true;Cantonese;The history of this teahouse spans eight decades but the décor and the tableware haven’t changed much – it’s always reassuring to see the tea set with the image of a rooster. Cantonese dim sum are made the traditional way every morning at 3:30 am and tend to run out quickly. Come early and enjoy the bite-size morsels with Pu’er tea. If dim sum is sold out, go for fried noodles, bee hoon or the fish balls, which are also delicious.;;[]
4391;Penang Road Famous Laksa;Malaysia;George Town;5 Lebuh Keng Kwee, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.41663;100.33113;32;false;false;Street Food;This famous laksa shop serves lai fun noodles in a sardine broth with exceptional depth and flavours alongside an array of condiments. For those with bigger appetites, order char koay teow with duck egg to go with the laksa.;Cash only;[]
4392;Heun Kee Claypot Chicken Rice (Pudu);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;59 Jalan Yew, Pudu, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1327996;101.7163087;24;false;true;Cantonese;Set in an old but neatly organised dining area not far from Pudu wet markets, Heun Kee has long been loved by locals. The charcoal stove at the front of the restaurant adds intense heat to the claypot, producing cooked rice with intense charcoal flavours and interesting textures and aromas. Choose from a variety of soups, vegetables and side dishes to enrich your dining experience. However, bear in mind that claypot dishes can take up to 30 minutes to arrive.;Air conditioning;[]
4393;Anak Baba;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;159 Jalan Sultan Abdul Samad, Brickfields, Kuala Lumpur, 50470, Malaysia;3.1329104;101.6902178;18;false;true;Malaysian, Peranakan;Since 2018, this cosy little gem tucked inside the Little India has been serving authentic Southern Peranakan cuisine that melds Indo-Malay flavours with Chinese influences. The must-try nasi lemak with ayam goreng kunyit is the quintessential national comfort food – coconut milk lends a subtle sweetness to the rice, in stark contrast with the juicy fried chicken, fiery sambal and crisp water spinach.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4394;Foong Lian;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;55 Jalan Yew, Pudu, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.132988;101.716413;83;false;false;Cantonese;A firm favourite with the locals, Foong Lian has been feeding hungry diners claypot rice cooked over charcoal since 1986. The experienced chef uses two kinds of rice and controls the heat meticulously so that every pot is perfect. Try the preserved meat option with pork and liver sausage that perfume the rice with flavourful grease or top up with chicken leg and salted fish. Soups and snacks like tofu skin roll are also recommended.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
4395;MTR 1924;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;69 Jalan Thambipillay, Brickfields, Kuala Lumpur, 50470, Malaysia;3.13227;101.6874;86;true;true;Indian Vegetarian;This international chain, which began almost 100 years ago, now has branches all over the world. This outpost has been a popular dining spot among the locals since 2017. Idli is a soft, fluffy steamed cake made out of fermented rice batter, paired with green chutney and lentil sambar. Masala dosa, or crispy crepe with potato curry, packs a real kick. Uddin vada, or black lentil fritter, is also a good choice. Check out the daily specials and mini meals for combos.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4396;My Own Café;Malaysia;George Town;2 Lebuh Cannon, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4152797;100.3367666;87;false;false;Street Food;This charming family-run shop serves Penang asam laksa, Nyonya laksa and fried spring rolls. The light and refreshing red soup of the signature asam laksa strikes the right balance of sour and spicy and is nicely topped off with mint and pineapple. The spring rolls, stuffed with vegetable filling, taste equally good.;Cash only;[]
4397;Nasi Ayam Hainan Chee Meng (Jalan Kelang Lama);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Sub Lot-A1, Batu 4 1/4, Jalan Kelang Lama, Kuala Lumpur, 58200, Malaysia;3.0955277;101.6752549;38;false;true;Malaysian;This family-owned business has been a staple of the local dining scene since 1965 and is now run by the second and third generations. Instead of Wenchang chicken from Hainan, they use local chicken for leaner, softer and juicier meat. Besides steamed chicken, the short menu showcases various chicken dishes, such as fried chicken, sesame honey, salted egg yolk, or even Kung Pao sauce. There are also Malay and Thai dishes. Opt for smaller portions to sample more dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
4398;Sri Nirwana Maju;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;43 Jalan Telawi 3, Bangsar Baru, Kuala Lumpur, 59100, Malaysia;3.1311282;101.6709374;33;false;true;Indian;Bangsar Village is home to numerous buzzy restaurants and shops. In this vibrant district, Sri Nirwana Maju attracts diners for its distinctive flavours – a selection of regional dishes for anyone seeking the authentic taste of India. Go for one of the set menus with rice and vegetable curry on banana leaves, which you can top up with your favourite sides (fish, chicken or lamb). The chicken biriyani boasts moist tender meat and balanced flavours.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4399;Ah Hei Bak Kut Teh;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;33A Medan Imbi, Pudu, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1444195;101.7144029;34;false;true;Malaysian;This 30-year-old shop makes its own bak kut teh daily at 5 am with a blend of 16 Chinese herbs. The soup may look a bit on the dark side, but it boasts not only aromas and flavours, but also health benefits. In addition to the typical spareribs, you may choose other pork cuts, such as tripe, intestine or belly. Or, you may add mushrooms or deep-fried tofu skin to the health tonic served in claypot. Side dishes of fish or veggies are also good.;Cash only;[]
4400;Teksen;Malaysia;George Town;18 & 20 Lebuh Carnarvon, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.4174271;100.3359853;25;true;false;Cantonese;Chinese couplets on the wall and red table cloths give the clean, simple room a festive vibe. This no-frills joint has won the hearts of serious foodies since 1965 with its well-made traditional Cantonese fare and fusion creations with a local twist. Deep-fried homemade tofu in an egg white glaze with prawns and dried scallops is a must. Dishes seasoned with assam tumis or sambal are also worth trying. Expect a long queue at peak hours.;;[]
4401;La Santa Barbacha;USA;Austin;2806 Manor Rd., Austin, 78722, USA;30.2859038;-97.7117699;23;true;true;Mexican;This East Austin eatery isn't your average roadside trailer. Run by the Landaverde siblings, this spot elevates the typical experience with a platform and picnic tables shaded by greenery and a battalion of fans. The food is equally leveled up, with a focus on barbacoa (even the name is a play on it). From the very first bite, it's clear that this meat is special. Get it in breakfast tacos or in that Austin staple, migas tacos, with scrambled eggs, chips, shredded cheese, and sliced avocado. It's also available on its own or in a quesabarbacha, a beet-red tortilla folded with barbacoa, cilantro, and onion, along with gooey cheese. It's decadent, with a good balance of flavor aided by their house-made salsa.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4402;Tejas Chocolate;USA;Tomball;200 N. Elm St., Tomball, 77375, USA;30.0988908;-95.6146151;92;true;true;Barbecue;North of Houston in the city of Tomball, Scott Moore Jr. might be the only chocolatier to become a pitmaster. This wasn’t his plan when he launched a bean-to-bar operation in 2015, but now it is the main reason why customers from all over line up on the porch of this quirky house before doors open. Flintstone-sized beef ribs with salt and pepper barks and melting threads of fat are a notable daily special (Friday only). Other highlights include snappy chile relleno sausages and lovely slices of USDA prime beef brisket, all of which emerge from barbecue pits parked under a shed next to a mountain of chopped wood. Sides are fairly standard, except for the excellent carrot soufflé, which straddles a fine, delicious line between sweet and savory.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4403;nobie's;USA;Houston;2048 Colquitt St., Houston, 77098, USA;29.735365;-95.410043;15;false;true;American;A home away from home, this Montrose favorite is impossible to resist. Set in a charming 1930s bungalow and decorated with vinyl records, the restaurant is as cozy as they come with a staff that treats you like a regular. The food impresses, at once creative and familiar. You could fill up entirely on the superb dilly milk bread with “everything butter” but then you’d miss any one of the creative vegetable offerings like grilled carrots with a coconut curry and peanut sesame crunch. Nori egg noodles with garlic beef and chili butter or fried quail stuffed with German potato salad? Tough decision, but know that there must be pie, all of which are baked daily. A recent slice of banana bread pie with whipped honey mousse made for a stunning finale.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4404;Kemuri Tatsu-ya;USA;Austin;2713 E. 2nd St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.2540513;-97.7130937;62;true;false;Izakaya, Barbecue;What do you get when you blend a Japanese izakaya with a barbecue joint? It's not a punchline—it's Kemuri Tatsu-ya. From the decor (think cowboy boots and whiskey bottles with teapots and lanterns) to the menu (corn bread taiyaki, anyone?), this East Austin spot blends the two worlds in the very best way. It's casual but laser-focused on quality. Choose from snacks and skewers like the grilled scallop and squash plated with saikyo corn brûlée. Smoked options, from brisket in a sesame-pecan rub to salmon collar, can be made into a bento box which arrive with koshihikari rice, serrano limón miso barbecue sauce, house pickles, and guacamole. Most dishes are intended for sharing, making this an ideal spot for groups.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
4405;Distant Relatives;USA;Austin;3901 Promontory Point Dr., Austin, 78744, USA;30.208696;-97.7298256;57;true;false;Barbecue;Meanwhile Brewing is home to a few food trucks, but Chef Damien Brockway's is the one to beat. It's barbecue, but certainly not your grandaddy's barbecue. Instead, there's more than a hint of new school in this cooking, with the chef's African diaspora inspiration coming through in the menu. There is a stern nose to tail and root to stem ethos here, where you'll find everything from pulled pork and brisket to chicken smoked using pecan wood and mixed hardwood. Classic pork sausage flecked with red pepper flakes impresses with its dialed-in flavor, but it's the chicken with chile vinegar butter that is the true standout. A rotating list of sides may include burnt ends with black-eyed peas and smoky spice-rubbed peanuts.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4406;Burnt Bean Co.;USA;Seguin;108 S. Austin St., Seguin, 78155, USA;29.568677;-97.964632;55;true;false;Barbecue;In the town of Seguin, people start to queue long before doors even open. It’s always been this way for pitmasters Ernest Servantes and Dave Kirkland, both of whom were dueling fixtures and frequent victors at countless barbecue competitions before joining forces in 2021. The industrial space fit with iron beams and exposed brick has seemingly endless seating that does indeed fill up. Everyone is after the same thing: The offered meats – brisket, ribs, sausage – are notable for their tenderness, delicate smokiness, and measured levels of fat. Sides like green beans or firm spears of pickled okra balance out such hearty fare. Those who brave the weekend lines will be rewarded with specials like the beef rib or the Sunday-only breakfast menu.;Air conditioning;[]
4407;Cattleack Barbeque;USA;Dallas;13628 Gamma Rd., Dallas, 75244, USA;32.9343049;-96.8366175;32;false;false;Barbecue;If the line wrapped around the building doesn't clue you in, you'll know you've arrived at Cattleack Barbeque when the heady scent of wood smoke drifts along in the breeze. Owner and pitmaster Andrew Castelan highlights the classics, using oak and hickory wood for his barbecued meats, which change daily. Brisket and pork ribs are must-orders, but the specials, like a pork steak or wagyu pastrami brisket, are a close second. The meat is flavorful enough on its own, but bottles of their bright and tangy sauce are on every table. Of course, no barbecue spot worth its salt shirks the sides, and here, greens and burnt end beans or street corn are two winners. When they ask if you want cornbread, the answer is always a resounding yes.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4408;Blood Bros BBQ;USA;Bellaire;5425 Bellaire Blvd., Bellaire, 77401, USA;29.7054588;-95.4758893;91;true;true;Barbecue, Asian;Few smokehouses celebrate the city’s diverse cultural footprint quite like this one, where Texas barbecue traditions merge with Chinese, Vietnamese and Korean flavors. Where else will you find a fried bao soaked in honey, layered with pork belly and topped with hot mustard and water spinach? How many pitmasters glaze their ribs in gochujang? Classic offerings of brisket and ribs satisfy, but the restaurant’s heart lives in the daily specials, which change with great frequency. Take a look around: A nearby table will always have a dish you wish you had ordered. How’s the brisket fried rice? What about that smoked char siu banh mi? Do you have room for the watermelon salad? These are questions for the next visit – and the visits after that.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4410;Barbs B Q;USA;Lockhart;102 E. Market St., Lockhart, 78644, USA;29.8838021;-97.672163;54;true;true;Barbecue, American;Barbs B Q is run by pitmaster Chuck Charnichart and her small team. Waiting in line for good barbecue is a Texas tradition, and this place, with its hours-long lines is no exception. You'll need to stave off your cravings until the weekend though, as it's only open on Saturday and Sunday. The Lockhart gem's compact menu lists a handful of meats that read classic but have been given a twist, as in the Molotov pork ribs finished with lime zest, giving the tender meat just the right amount of zing. Turkey with a black pepper rub is a total standout, and don't miss the unique sides like green spaghetti made with a smoked poblano sauce. Chocolate pudding and cobbler round out the meal.;Air conditioning;[]
4411;Ramen del Barrio;USA;Austin;1700 W. Parmer Ln., Austin, 78727, USA;30.4130047;-97.6867165;87;true;false;Fusion, Ramen;Mexican ramen? You bet, at least at Ramen del Barrio, a concept that marries Mexican cuisine with ramen inside North Austin's Hana World Market. Chef Christopher Krinsky has created something offbeat at this casual spot, but the two cuisines are woven together seamlessly. Bold, spice-driven cooking is the name of the game here. Take the mole tsukemen, a fresh mole negro that has been thinned down to a broth and served next to a tangle of noodles and chicken for dipping. Rich and flavorful, it's savory, spicy, and sensational. If ramen feels wrong on a hot Texas day, opt for aguachile masemen, a cold ramen with thick noodles, poached shrimp, and vegetables in a bright, refreshing aguachile. Round out the meal with karaage or one of their terrific lengua tacos.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4412;Lucia;USA;Dallas;287 N. Bishop Ave., Dallas, 75208, USA;32.7472783;-96.8282388;46;true;true;Italian;Husband-and-wife owners David and Jennifer Uygur have a gem on their hands with this Bishop Arts restaurant, where David runs the kitchen and Jennifer welcomes guests with genuine warmth. The word is out, and reservations are often a feat, though they do save a few seats for walk-ins.Chef Uygur crafts a menu rooted in Italian classics that shifts with the availability of terrific Texan produce. Dishes may appear simple but don't judge them on face value alone, as everything from the Texan tomato salad to the homemade pasta hides a depth of flavor. There may be no better way to begin a meal here than by sharing a salumi board, as the kitchen cures its own meats, and the wine list features interesting bottles, including a nice representation from Italy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4413;Cuantos Tacos;USA;Austin;1108 E. 12th St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.2728845;-97.7283688;54;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Chef/owner Luis "Beto" Robledo's East Austin food truck offers a simple but satisfying promise: Mexico City-style tacos. Order at the counter, then find a seat in the shaded picnic area shared with other food trucks.This place is best known for their suadero taco, served simply with onion and cilantro. The cachate, or beef cheek, is a close second, but if you're seeking something less meaty, the mushroom taco seals the deal. The meats are cooked in a traditional chorizera pan with a raised center, and the tortillas are equally impressive. These bright yellow masa tortillas are paper thin with loads of flavor. Sides, like grilled onions or beans, round out the satisfying meal.;Terrace;[]
4414;Franklin Barbecue;USA;Austin;900 E. 11th St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.27003;-97.7315;72;false;false;Barbecue, Regional Cuisine;This iconic barbecue oasis in the heart of Austin needs no introduction, even further evidenced by the lines snaking out the door. Inside is simple at best, with a corrugated metal ceiling and cement floors, but it's the board above the counter that has everyone's attention anyway. Pork ribs, sausage, turkey, and pulled pork, along with a handful of sandwiches and classic sides (think cole slaw salad and pinto beans) are what's on offer, but you won't ever go wrong with the brisket. Sliced to order, it's wrapped in butcher paper and weighed before being placed on the famous blue tray. Tender and smoky with flavorful marbling and a dark char, it's worth the hours-long wait. Pair it with a cold local beer and it's the perfect duo.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4415;Killen's BBQ;USA;Pearland;3613 Broadway St., Pearland, 77581, USA;29.5640475;-95.2822307;47;true;false;Barbecue;In the quiet city of Pearland, native Texan Ronnie Killen barbecues like few others in the Lone Star state. Everyone waits patiently before doors open at 11 a.m., when the crowd moves fast through, what used to be, the city’s first school cafeteria. Sourcing from Snake River Farms, Killen offers a first-class beef rib smoked just out back that is a silken delight and sings of smoke, salt, fat, and pepper. You could cut it with a spoon. And regardless of what your doctor says, order those melting cubes of pork belly burnt ends tossed in a pepper jelly sauce. Brussels sprouts and collards sopping in potlikker offer some reprieve from the meat. First timers won’t have room for dessert, but veterans never lose sight of the crème brûlée bread pudding.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4416;Gemma;USA;Dallas;2323 N. Henderson Ave., Ste. 109, Dallas, 75206, USA;32.8135203;-96.7773479;65;false;true;American;Gemma is a charming spot from the husband-and-wife team of Chef Stephen Rogers and Allison Yoder. The couple met while working at Napa Valley's Press and returned to Rogers's home state to open this intimate spot in Dallas that highlights contemporary American cooking with a seasonal focus.The evening begins with a simple sounding but sinfully delicious warm raisin scone. Fried Castelvetrano olives mixed with fragrant Texas pecans are a delight, but it's cooking like the roasted heirloom carrots or the Idaho trout almondine that make a meal here memorable. Meyer lemon tart with notes of lavender and kisses of toasted meringue is a perfect send off.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
4417;Rosie Cannonball;USA;Houston;1620 Westheimer Rd., Houston, 77006, USA;29.7429254;-95.4004464;35;true;true;Contemporary, Italian;The name and the flavors alike are punchy at this inviting Montrose favorite, with stylish design and cool, laid-back charm. As an opening volley in a barrage of hospitality, guests are welcomed with a splash of bubbles when they sit, perhaps as an enticement to explore the rest of the impressive wine list. All this is icing on the cake for a crowd-pleasing menu that focuses on a wood-fired oven, from a zingy salad of charred beans to a crisp, gooey focaccia di recco filled with robiola cheese and mortadella—not to mention praiseworthy pizzas and pastas. Speaking of dessert, a meal here is scarcely complete without a wedge of their honey cake with crème fraîche gelato.;Interesting wine list;[]
4418;The Pit Room;USA;Houston;1201 Richmond Ave., Houston, 77006, USA;29.7343595;-95.3938841;17;true;false;Barbecue, Mexican;Who had the brilliant idea to use brisket trimmings to make tortillas? The credit might possibly belong to this Montrose smokehouse, which delivers prime USDA brisket and beef rib excellence. With a side order of warm tortillas and a lashing of sweet sauce, the combination is spot-on. Speaking of sides, the refreshing marinated tomato salad or the surprisingly spicy charred beans pack a lot more flavor than expected. Early risers can drop in for a quick breakfast taco. As a bonus, the wait to order is rarely long, and the amount of seating indoor and outdoor is bountiful. In a region where eating barbecue can require considerable advanced planning, such accommodations are a welcome change of pace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4419;Ngon Vietnamese Kitchen;USA;Dallas;1907 Greenville Ave., Dallas, 75206, USA;32.8137277;-96.770263;56;false;false;Vietnamese;Ngon Vietnamese Kitchen isn't just another restaurant. It's much more personal than that for owner Carol Nguyen, who wanted to share the vibrancy of her homeland's cooking with Dallas diners. From the design, with its rustic wood booths and raised tables ideal for groups, to the décor, with representations of the famous conical hats (non la) on the walls, it's clear Nguyen has put her heart and soul into this spot in the lively lower Greenville area. That same effort is seen on the menu, which was largely inspired by the street vendors of Hanoi where she grew up. Choose from a wide range of authentic dishes, including nourishing phở, flavor-packed spring rolls, and delicately spiced curries.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4420;Emmer & Rye;USA;Austin;51 Rainey St., Austin, 78701, USA;30.2564562;-97.739818;44;false;false;American, Contemporary;Some of Austin's most popular bars and restaurants are here on Rainey Street, and Emmer & Rye is no exception. This place is always packed and humming with a crowd, both outside on the breezy patio and indoors in the contemporary, inviting dining room. The new American menu is well-designed and tightly focused. From the in-house fermentation program and freshly ground heirloom grains figuring prominently on the menu to strong ties with many of Texas's small farms, there's a commitment to sustainability here. Yellowfin tuna crudo tucked with strawberries and cucumber is a refreshing opener before tucking into a plate of house-made cacio e pepe. Velvety and satisfying, it's been on the menu since the very beginning.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
4421;nonna;USA;Dallas;4115 Lomo Alto Dr., Dallas, 75219, USA;32.8210813;-96.8150605;34;true;true;Italian;You could drive right past this place set within a collection of small businesses off a main highway in Highland Park but keep an eye out for the blind-covered windows emblazoned with "nonna" to avoid missing out. Inside, it's the picture of casual chic down to the last piece of modern art displayed on the exposed brick walls. As for the menu, it's dictated by the seasons and what's available, though the white clam pie from the wood-fired oven and the Maine lobster ravioli are always available (and good thing, too). Pasta is plentiful, with up to 10 different choices on offer, including spaghetti and gnocchi. The all-Italian wine list features an appealing selection of old favorites as well as a few hidden treasures.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4422;KG BBQ;USA;Austin;3108 Manor Rd., Austin, 78723, USA;30.2864353;-97.705314;18;false;false;Barbecue, Egyptian;Barbecue is ubiquitous in Texas, but there's something deliciously different about KG BBQ. It's all due to owner Kareem El-Ghayesh. Raised in Cairo, he left behind a career in finance to move here to smoke meat, and Austin is very happy he did. His food truck is located next to Oddwood Brewing, and there's always a line for this food that marries Middle Eastern twists with Texan barbecue tradition. From rubs and sauces that use sumac, cinnamon, and pomegranate to Mediterranean sausage with green olives, sun dried tomatoes, and feta cheese, the mashup is marvelous. Don't skip the boneless chicken thighs marinated in honey, thyme, and sumac and accompanied by a yogurt sauce. End on a sweet note like the rice pudding with pistachio butter and mascarpone.;Terrace;[]
4423;Rosemeyer Bar-B-Q;USA;Spring;2111 Riley Fuzzell Rd., Spring, 77386, USA;30.1045312;-95.3960645;53;false;false;Barbecue;Imagine: a single trailer in Spring parked on the side of the highway next door to a gas station with a sign out front. The setup is as classic as the trailer’s origins. Childhood friends Jordan Rosemeyer and Ben Maxwell started out cooking for fun on weekends, but before long found themselves running this humble operation. There’s no dining room in sight but there are picnic tables. Most importantly, there is great barbecue – and a lot of it. Beautifully smoked brisket takes top billing, but tender pork ribs and snappy, jalapeno-cheese sausages are must-orders as well. Daily specials are another point of pride so keep a close eye on the restaurant’s social media.;Terrace;[]
4424;Ema;USA;Houston;5307 N. Main St., Houston, 77009, USA;29.8033608;-95.3877773;73;false;false;Mexican;From popular bakery pop-up to a brick and mortar in the Houston Heights, this daytime restaurant can do no wrong. Celebrating Mexican traditions and quality coffee, the menu is finely curated and endlessly tempting. We suggest working backwards to make the most of your appetite: Flaky, guava-queso empanadas and the famous horchata cream doughnut are essential desserts that sell out early. Chilaquiles built on superb tortilla chips and tender chunks of brisket is one of many worthy entrees. Heirloom corn is a point of pride here, exemplified by one very large tetela stuffed with mushroom-carrot tinga and set in a zippy salsa verde. There’s more, like the hoja santa French toast or the occasional mole special but save them for next time.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
4425;Nancy's Hustle;USA;Houston;2704 Polk St., Houston, 77003, USA;29.7458139;-95.3521115;26;false;false;Contemporary;There are no wrong choices at this welcoming EaDo hangout that has dazzled the city since opening in 2017. If anything, there are perhaps too many choices. How could one possibly decide between the spicy beef and butter dumplings with sauerkraut and the fluffy Nancy cakes with smoked trout roe? Should chilled carrots with buttermilk ricotta be your entrée or is it finally time to take down the cheeseburger stacked on a housemade English muffin? But then there’s the grilled wagyu tri-tip with beef fat sticky rice. Whatever you decide, expect lively, bold, heart-warming cooking that keeps a close eye on the seasons and never once feels fussy. Dessert is a given, but good luck picking between the corn crepe cake and the parmesan cheesecake.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4427;Cullum's Attaboy;USA;San Antonio;111 Kings Ct., San Antonio, 78212, USA;29.452642;-98.484956;96;true;false;French, American;Set in a little bungalow that’s as cute as a cupcake, this brunch-only, walk-in, counter-style bistro off the St. Mary's strip can do no wrong. Snag a seat at the counter and watch as the open kitchen dabbles in affordable French luxury with the likes of proper omelets and a whole lot of butter, hollandaise, truffles, and caviar offered at every turn. The menu is the right size. Think doughnuts dusted in powdered sugar that rival the best beignets or sandwiches stacked with smoked brisket, egg, and cheese served on beautifully bronzed rolls made in house. One unexpected sleeper hit is the breakfast potatoes, which outclass all other versions by miles. A chalkboard out front encourages diners to try a “Champagne breakfast.” It’s a perfect idea.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
4428;Nam Giao;USA;Houston;6938 Wilcrest Dr., Houston, 77072, USA;29.7024663;-95.5713782;87;false;true;Vietnamese;You could make an entire meal out of the appetizers at this beloved restaurant in Little Saigon, where the elegant cuisine of Hue in central Vietnam is front and center. Everyone starts with those little steamed rice cakes topped with fried pork rinds and chives, and some are content to order these until they’re full. But then you’d miss out on the pork and shrimp crystal cakes steamed in banana leaves or that thrilling banh khoai, a crispy rice pancake layered with beansprouts, shrimp and a riot of fresh herbs. Leave room on the table for the grilled flank steak, which arrives wrapped in vine leaves and is served with spongy bundles of vermicelli. The server will say that you’ve ordered too much, which is how you know you’ve ordered just enough.;Air conditioning;[]
4429;Belly of the Beast;USA;Spring;5200 FM 2920 Rd., Ste. 180, Spring, 77388, USA;30.0746301;-95.498342;69;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;In an unassuming dining room in Spring, Chef Thomas Bille is putting it all on the plate. Unafraid to mix and match the cuisines that inspire him, he cooks largely with Mexico in mind. Think saag paneer with spinach mole verde and a stack of warm, sumptuous tortillas made with half corn and half flour. Other possible starters—all of which are portioned to share— include tuna tostadas with nori or street corn agnolotti. Such twists and turns make for immensely satisfying courses that feel bold and balanced. The smartest twist of all might be the finely spiced cherry mole with Rohan duck breast. It’s unlikely you’ll make it to dessert with much spare room, but do consider the tres leches, cleverly prepared with passionfruit and torched meringue.;Air conditioning;[]
4430;Truth BBQ;USA;Houston;110 S. Heights Blvd., Houston, 77007, USA;29.7690501;-95.3973242;27;false;false;Barbecue;Although the acclaimed original location in Brenham is little more than a roadside shack, this Houston Heights sequel from owner and pitmaster Leonard Botello IV is a gleaming model of modern efficiency. Fortunately, the cooking still has plenty of soul: the brisket is expectedly solid, while smoked pork ribs and house-made sausages are a cut above. Surprisingly, sides like collards, beans and corn pudding—or even the more rarified tater tot casserole with crisp fried onions— might even be the highlight, offering the flavorful, rib-sticking quality of lovingly homemade dishes. If, somehow, you manage not to fill up on the tantalizing savory options, those with an implacable sweet tooth can tip the scales with hefty slices of house-made cake.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4431;Mala Sichuan Bistro;USA;Houston;9348 Bellaire Blvd., Houston, 77036, USA;29.7051419;-95.5478228;64;true;true;Chinese, Sichuan;From Katy to Sugarland to Montrose, this Sichuan restaurant has spread its wings across the Houston area and beyond. The story begins at the original location, which opened in 2011 in Bellaire’s Chinatown. Whereas many Sichuan restaurants submerge everything in pools of chili oil, this kitchen takes a more measured approach. And true to its name, dishes boast a distinct thread of tangy bitterness and tongue-numbing heat but never so much that you’ll sweat. Highlights include silky cubes of tofu sitting in a mala bean curd sauce, firm filets of white fish blanketed in garlic, ginger and red chili powder, and chewy, house-made wheat noodles tossed in a peanut-based vinaigrette. A particularly descriptive menu helps decode dishes to first timers.;;[]
4432;Killen's;USA;Houston;101 Heights Blvd., Houston, 77007, USA;29.7705611;-95.3975782;72;true;false;American, Southern;Ronnie Killen’s Heights hit is the wrong place to count calories or dabble with salads. Quite the opposite, this Southern standout is an all-or-nothing celebration honoring his grandmother. Deviled eggs are crowned with brilliantly smoky bits of pulled pork – a clever nod to his barbecue accolades. Biscuits are warm and flaky. Fried chicken is listed on the menu at least five different times. A favorite is the classic buttermilk version, which is cooked to order and arrives golden-brown and juicy. For sure, this is comfort food that rings familiar, satisfies with ease and all but demands for a nap once you’ve cleared the last crumb. Those who bravely walk in hoping to go meatless can take refuge in the sizeable selection of vegetables.;Air conditioning;[]
4433;Theodore Rex;USA;Houston;1302 Nance St., Unit A, Houston, 77002, USA;29.76777;-95.354029;95;false;true;Contemporary;In the shadow of downtown Houston right off Highway 10 is Justin Yu’s wedge of a restaurant. There’s little else in the area, but the red stop sign at the intersection is, poignantly enough, also at the front door. Counter seating is practically shoulder to shoulder, knee to knee, but it is a prime perch for taking in all that this welcoming restaurant has to offer. The cuisine is hard to pin down but know that everything looks simpler than it really is and seasoned far better than you could have imagined. Highlights include fried bread with tomato fondant, cured carrots blanketed in a savory onion emulsion, and a roast chicken leg coated in vadouvan. Don’t leave without trying the warmbrûléed butter cake smeared with strawberry jam.;Air conditioning;[]
4434;Dai Due;USA;Austin;2406 Manor Rd., Austin, 78722, USA;30.2847517;-97.7167116;72;false;false;American, Regional Cuisine;Texans are known around the world for their inimitable hometown pride, but Chef/owner Jesse Griffiths takes his affection for the Lone Star state to another level at Dai Due, where nearly everything, from produce and meat to olive oil and wine, is sourced from Texas. Brunch is available but it's the evenings when this place shines. Walk past the entrance filled with tempting baked goods and prepared meats to find a rustic back room perfect for hosting the supper club-style service. Skilled butchers tackle everything from wild boar and antelope to goat, and the plates are impressively offbeat. Hits include the cold meat board with antelope salami and wild boar and dill pickle terrine, as well as the smoked pork Porterhouse chop with sauerkraut, Bavarian mustard, and chutney.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4435;The Jerk Shack;USA;San Antonio;10234 Texas 151, Ste. 103, San Antonio, 78251, USA;29.4727289;-98.6975276;21;true;false;Jamaican, Caribbean;Chef and co-owner Lattoia Massey, better known as Chef Nicola Blaque, and her husband Cornelius Massey, are serving up what may be the best Caribbean/Jamaican fare in the city. Set in an industrial location, the interior is brightened by mood-elevating decor and a genuine warmth emanating from the staff. Expect a mix of traditional dishes and playful plates that have been given a modern twist. No matter the selection, this is downhome delicious cooking, from the flavorful jerk chicken to jackfruit tacos and roasted cauliflower curry to the scrumptious sides like caramelized fried plantains or fluffy rice and peas. Be sure to save room for the "bread pudding" made with pancake batter, warm peaches, and rum-caramel sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4436;Briscuits;USA;Austin;4204 Menchaca Rd., Austin, 78704, USA;30.2315;-97.78774;91;false;true;Barbecue;Few things go together as perfectly as biscuits and barbecue, and that's the premise behind this truck from Christopher McGhee and William Spence, located on the Radio Coffee lot. It's popular but they have ordering down pat with a QR code and a call-ahead option that keeps things moving along. Good thing too, as you won't want to wait for a bite of their melt-in-your-mouth brisket and flakey biscuit sandwich with a swoop of smoked strawberry jam thrown in for good measure. Or, try the pork belly with spiced apple pear preserves, a fried chicken biscuit, or even a simple egg sandwich biscuit—it's all good. To top it all off, beef sausage and wings, as well as sides like pimento cheese grits, round out their barbecue staples.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
4437;Micklethwait Craft Meats;USA;Austin;4602 Tanney St., Austin, 78721, USA;30.2731611;-97.6903815;44;true;false;Barbecue, Regional Cuisine;Is East Austin's Micklethwait Craft Meats good? Take one look at the crowd, with everyone from police officers and parents with kids to well-dressed locals, and it's a sure sign that this place is on point. Owner Tom Micklethwait is a master at central Texas-style barbecue, doling out luscious meat from ribs and brisket to sausage, pulled pork, lamb, and barbacoa. Juicy, smoky, spicy, and sweet, it's all good, no matter your selection. While it would be a sacrilege to skip the meat, the sides, including Frito pie, jalapeno cheese grits, and a standout potato salad dressed with cider vinegar, are good enough on their own to warrant a visit. You'll be stuffed, but there's always room for banana pudding, isn't there?;Car park,Garden or park;[]
4438;Odd Duck;USA;Austin;1201 S. Lamar Blvd., Austin, 78704, USA;30.255009;-97.762206;15;true;false;American, Contemporary;Chef Bryce Gilmore of Barley Swine has turned his hit food truck into this popular spot on South Lamar. It's a casual, come-as-you-are concept where guests can pull up a stool at the massive counter or at a nearby table. Everyone is here for the hearty, decadent American fare designed for sharing. Dressed down with a rustic edge, their Southern dishes with global inflections range from ceviche and chicken heart satay to wagyu burgers and stuffed quail with dirty rice and grilled okra. Maltagliati pasta tossed with corn butter and a surprising shrimp sausage is memorable, while meat-forward dishes, like the impossibly tender pork shoulder, are always a hit. Don't skip the sourdough ice cream with pecan streusel and warm diced peaches.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
4439;Ladino;USA;San Antonio;200 E. Grayson St. #100, San Antonio, 78215, USA;29.4439502;-98.4796002;35;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This welcoming San Antonio restaurant is a gem in the Pearl District. With an expansive terrace seating overlooking a verdant courtyard, the kitchen delivers creative, boldly seasoned dishes from across the Mediterranean. A wood-burning oven cranks out hot rounds of sourdough pita to pair with the likes of fire-roasted corn with labneh and sivri pepper or summer squash with grape-leaf chermoula. Seasonal fare figures prominently, and even Romano beans with fermented tomatoes pack far more flavor than you’d expect. Another must-order: Beef and lamb dumplings coated in a sauce of yogurt and smoked chili. Thoughtful cocktails like the green schug margarita add to the charm of this inspired restaurant that is never short on flavor.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4440;Pinkerton's BBQ;USA;Houston;1504 Airline Dr., Houston, 77009, USA;29.7986272;-95.3816874;16;true;true;Barbecue;Barbecue competition is steep in these parts, but in just a few short years, pitmaster Grant Pinkerton, who lives above the restaurant, has made a name for himself. The number of deer heads mounted on the walls of this low-slung joint makes you wonder whether beef is really on the menu, but indeed it is. Everyone starts with the hulking beef rib, which often sells out before midday, and thick, melting slabs of prime-grade brisket cooked over mesquite and oak. Like all good barbecue, neither piece wants for sauce. Not to be outdone are the brilliantly tender St. Louis-style ribs, which are glazed to order in a sweet sauce made with dehydrated vegetables. Keep an eye on the back wall where daily specials are written in small print.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4441;Một Hai Ba;USA;Dallas;6047 Lewis St., Dallas, 75206, USA;32.8121943;-96.762242;97;true;false;Fusion, Vietnamese;You could easily drive right by this standalone building tucked behind an auto repair shop, but one bite of Chef Peja Krstic's cooking and you won't soon forget the address. Inside, wood floors and exposed brick add charm to this narrow space where Serbian-born Krstic turns out contemporary cuisine with Vietnamese and French influences and decidedly Texan touches. The mashup is especially intriguing, offering an interesting journey with dishes such as steamed bao filled with beef brisket and a shallot marmalade, or crispy tempura squash blossoms filled with pork and shrimp with nuoc cham vinaigrette. For dessert, savor the coconut lemongrass panna cotta with orange marmalade and chocolate peanut crumble.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4442;Veracruz Fonda & Bar;USA;Austin;1905 Aldrich St., Austin, 78723, USA;30.2982241;-97.7052205;27;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Sisters Reyna and Maritza Vazquez are well known for their bright blue Veracruz All Natural juice and taco trucks, and this brick-and-mortar spot in Mueller builds off their success (the decor even incorporates their recognizable blue color). The menu spotlights what they're known for—tacos—and adds in antojitos and a few larger plates here. Blue corn tortillas are made in house and are delicious folded around queso fresco and crispy epazote, or a cochinita taco with tender braised pork, fried plantain, and red onion habanero lime escabeche. Conchas are the perfect sweet treat, and here they offer pecan and lime versions as well as the more typical chocolate and vanilla.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4443;Nixta Taqueria;USA;Austin;2512 E. 12th St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.274928;-97.7131134;19;false;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Come as you are, and come early, to this East Austin taqueria from owners and partners Chef Edgar Rico and Sara Mardanbigi. It's a bit scrappy but rewards its visitors with spot-on Mexican-focused cooking. As the name suggests, the menu is all about nixtamalized corn of heirloom varietals. Everything is made in house and the menu presents a great mix of contrasts, featuring dishes employing ancient methods alongside updated items like duck fat refried beans. The duck carnitas taco, served on a thick tortilla made from heirloom pink corn, is impressive, while the carrot tostada is a study in care and composure with charred carrots, whipped herb ricotta, and salsa macha. Finish with something bold and sweet like a blueberry, basil, and ricotta paleta.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4444;Southerleigh Fine Food & Brewery;USA;San Antonio;136 E. Grayson St., Ste. 120, San Antonio, 78215, USA;29.4442477;-98.4802651;54;true;true;American, Southern;Original details lend charm to this landmark space nestled at the base of the Emma Hotel. Once home to Pearl's Brewhouse, built in 1894, it's now a buzzy gathering place for locals and visitors alike. The sprawling interior features a number of different areas for dining, while the bar is a popular perch with a view of the brewery. Sip a beer and snack on fried snapper throats sided by spicy aioli and celery root remoulade before tucking into an East Texas crawfish roll. Imagine a New England lobster roll, only stuffed with tender, sweet crawfish and Creole butter for dipping, with spicy fries for good measure. Still peckish? A slice of their three-layer chocolate cake with ganache and Amarena cherries will certainly do the trick.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4445;Il Tirabusciò;Italy;Bibbiena;via Rosa Scoti 12, Bibbiena, 52011, Italy;43.6950608;11.8175308;93;false;false;Tuscan;This restaurant in the heart of the old town is a must for anyone keen to try the cuisine of the Casentino region. The friendly chef is more than happy to provide information on his ingredients and to offer recommendations – the strong flavours in evidence and his delicious cuisine are sure to leave a lasting memory.;Air conditioning;[]
4446;Osteria dell'Accademia;Italy;Montegridolfo;Via Roma 16, Montegridolfo, 47837, Italy;43.8593;12.68869;75;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Located in a charming medieval hamlet dating back to the 13C, this authentic osteria serves home-style traditional, regional dishes – the chard and ricotta ravioli served with cheese and oil are particularly delicious. For an even more enjoyable experience, book one of the tables on the delightful summer terrace with fine views of the surrounding hills.;Great view,Terrace;[]
4447;Fratelli Bruzzone;Italy;Turin;via Maria Vittoria 34/a, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0655091;7.6908482;68;false;false;Piedmontese;The Bruzzone brothers deserve a round of applause for this restaurant and its extraordinary traditional Piedmontese cuisine. In just two small dining rooms (booking is recommended), guests can choose from an unforgettable array of dishes including anchovies in green sauce, baked onions with bagna cauda (an anchovy-based dip), superb agnolotti (stuffed pasta), tripe, chicken, bonet (a type of dessert) and hazelnut tart with zabaglione. With so much choice, it’s difficult to stop eating – and once you’ve left, you’ll want to return as soon as possible!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4448;Ostaria Pignatelli;Italy;Naples;Riviera di Chiaia 216, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8339281;14.2354339;53;true;true;Campanian;Situated near the neo-Classical Villa Pignatelli and in front of the Villa Comunale gardens, this restaurant offers an outdoor space as well as an elegant taverna-style dining room. “La vita è una, mangiala” (which roughly translates as “you have only one life, so make the most of it!”) is the restaurant’s motto and it’s not difficult to oblige given the delicious cuisine served here. The menu features an extraordinary array of classic favourites from Campania, all full of overwhelming flavours, including aubergine parmigiana, fried anchovies, mixed pasta with potatoes and Provola cheese, “candele alla Genovese” (pasta with beef ragu), Neapolitan-style cod and various lemon desserts.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4449;Altavilla;Italy;Bianzone;via Monti 46, Bianzone, 23030, Italy;46.1896712;10.1084315;17;false;false;Cuisine from Valtellina;The best way to enjoy the delicious cuisine served at this restaurant in the upper part of town, surrounded by woods and vineyards, is to ask for recommendations from Signora Anna, the owner and life and soul of the property. Beautiful panoramic terrace.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4450;La Villa;Italy;Melfi;Contrada Cavallerizza, SS 303 verso Rocchetta Sant'Antonio, Melfi, 85025, Italy;41.0112866;15.6249303;66;true;true;Cuisine from Basilicata, Traditional Cuisine;This country restaurant owes its welcoming atmosphere to the special attentions of the family management. The menus are based on traditional recipes that do full justice to the local produce.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4451;Antica Trattoria Gianna;Italy;Recorfano;via Maggiore 12, Recorfano, 26030, Italy;45.1033105;10.3448888;60;true;true;Lombardian, Country cooking;A delightful family trattoria offering simple, reasonably priced dishes at lunchtime and a copious tasting menu in the evening. The latter features dishes from the Lower Po valley, such as hams and salami, fresh pasta and the excellent beef entrecote with salt and aromatic olive oil.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4452;Oberraindlhof;Italy;Madonna di Senales;Raindl 49, Madonna di Senales, 39020, Italy;46.7144175;10.8830095;44;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The family that run this restaurant occupying an old farmhouse with origins dating back to the 16C has a relationship with the region that goes back decades. In later years, the farm became an inn and it has now been run by the same family for five generations, all motivated by a desire to introduce their guests to the best recipes and ingredients from the Senales valley. Dishes include an excellent roast lamb (raised on the restaurant’s own farm), which is stewed with bones and potatoes and served at the table from a copper cauldron. An excellent wine list and the hotel’s warm and friendly ambience add to the appeal.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4453;Fracia;Italy;Teglio;località Fracia, Teglio, 23036, Italy;46.1706561;10.007899;50;true;true;Cuisine from Valtellina, Traditional Cuisine;Park the car and walk up a short track (about 50m) to this rustic stone farmhouse with panoramic views of the surrounding valley. A traditional oasis serving delicious local cuisine with a light touch and the occasional Mediterranean influence where, in summer, meals are served at stone tables in the delightful outdoor area with stunning views of the surrounding countryside.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4454;Clemente;Italy;Sulmona;piazza Santa Monica, Sulmona, 67039, Italy;42.0507934;13.923711;50;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the charming centre of Sulmona, Clemente has for many years offered guests a simple, welcoming ambience in the restored stables of a palazzo dating from the early 19C. The menu has an exclusive focus on ingredients from the Abruzzi, including home-made pasta “alla chitarra” and the use of saffron from Aquila. The main courses are all meat-based, while among the desserts the Pan dell'Orsosemifreddo is particularly delicious. Although the portions are generous, most of the dishes are also available in half-portions. Aperitifs are served in the bistro-style room.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4455;Dalla Rosa Alda;Italy;San Giorgio di Valpolicella;strada Garibaldi 4, San Giorgio di Valpolicella, 37015, Italy;45.5344148;10.8498371;28;true;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;The undoubted star of this restaurant is the Enbogonè tagliatelle – a pasta made entirely by hand and seasoned with a sauce made from borlotti beans, local extra - virgin olive oil and rosemary – although the menu features many other dishes. Simple, honest cuisine made mainly from carefully selected regional produce, accompanied by an excellent selection of local wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4456;Nida;Italy;Lucca;via Nicola Barbantini 338, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8485511;10.5189835;19;false;true;Japanese;Located outside the city centre about 1km from the city walls, this restaurant is home to chef Masaki Kuroda (the owner of Serendipico in Capannori) who serves traditional Japanese cuisine inspired by memories of his childhood. Dishes include osashimi (raw fish), nigiri, the famous gyoza dumplings, and ramen made with a pork broth typical of his home in southern Japan. At lunchtime, there’s an excellent Japanese teishokuset menu. All you have to do is choose your main course, which is then served with other delicacies chosen by the chef.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
4457;Hostaria Viola;Italy;Castiglione delle Stiviere;via Verdi 32, Castiglione delle Stiviere, 46043, Italy;45.3801999;10.5092241;32;true;false;Mantuan, Lombardian;Having run this simple yet welcoming restaurant for over 100 years, it’s no surprise that the family at the helm here are true connoisseurs of Mantuan culinary traditions! The menu pays tribute to the delicious cuisine of Mantova featuring a host of celebrated and lesser-known specialities, including sorbir (filled pasta in broth), excellent cured hams, pike seasoned with a Mantuan sauce (made from anchovies and capers) served with polenta or mashed potatoes and, to finish, the renowned sbrisolona cake or zabaglione ice cream. There are so many specialities, you won’t be disappointed!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4458;Vez;Italy;San Marzano di San Giuseppe;via Addolorata 7/9, San Marzano di San Giuseppe, 74020, Italy;40.4506478;17.5057769;66;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Delicious modern cuisine based exclusively on local ingredients, including aromatic herbs from the property’s own small kitchen garden. One of the house specialities is the home-made stuffed pasta – a memory of the happy years that the chef spent in Bologna. Each dish is prepared with painstaking detail, resulting in decisive yet carefully orchestrated flavours. The restaurant, situated next to the church of San Carlo Borromeo in the village centre, boasts a spacious dining room with a vaulted ceiling and open-view kitchen, plus an outdoor terrace for alfresco dining in fine weather.;Terrace;[]
4459;Cile's;Italy;Fano;viale Cesare Battisti 35, Fano, 61032, Italy;43.8463162;13.0239803;80;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Situated near the sea, this small, bright restaurant with an almost shabby feel has a decor featuring plenty of wood, along with a blue and white colour scheme that makes it feel like a corner of Provence in the heart of Fano. The cuisine, however, remains firmly rooted in the local region with simple, very reasonably priced fish dishes and specialities from the Marche. An amusing, imaginative touch comes in the names given to these dishes, such as “Ma che fritto fa...” and “Si salvia chi può”. The graceful and smiling service from the all-female team is an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4460;Trattoria Antichi Sapori;Italy;Gaione;via Montanara 318, Gaione, 43124, Italy;44.7559486;10.2862789;99;false;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Just a few kilometres outside the town and yet already in open countryside, this typical local trattoria offers a simple yet warm and friendly ambience and excellent cuisine focused on regional specialities. The stuffed pasta and veal brisket are two of the dishes that we enjoyed the most here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4461;Old Friend;Italy;Cagliari;via Giuseppe Cesare Abba 51, Cagliari, 09126, Italy;39.2172498;9.1197194;23;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated slightly away from the city’s main shopping district, this restaurant has a fresh and trendy feel with music playing in the background and friendly, efficient service in the dining room. Although the dishes change with the seasons, quality and flavour are constant throughout. Our inspector recommends the raw fish with  pico de gallo (a Mexican sauce) and bottarga or the conchiglioni pasta with mutton ragu, bechamel sauce and samphire.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4462;Palmerino - Il Bacalà a Sandrigo;Italy;Sandrigo;via Piave 13, Sandrigo, 36066, Italy;45.6617521;11.621564;61;true;true;Venetian, Seafood;If you like cod, you’ll be in your element in this restaurant which serves this versatile fish in many different ways, from plain to salted (baccalà) and dried ((stoccafisso). The house speciality is the most famous dish of nearby Vicenza, namely bacalà alla vicentina (written with just one ‘l’ in this region and featuring dried rather than salted cod, despite the name). In addition to cod, the menu also includes other classic fish and seafood options as well as a few meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4463;Trattoria da Marino;Italy;Serravalle Pistoiese;via Provinciale Lucchese 102, loc. Ponte di Serravalle, Serravalle Pistoiese, 51030, Italy;43.8969441;10.8219738;29;true;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;In business for a century, this simple yet successful trattoria serves traditional Tuscan cuisine, with specialities such as ribollita stew and rabbit casserole on the menu. There’s just one informal dining room, which is overseen by capable owner Edoardo Innocenti, who delights in guiding his guests through the regional options on the menu. The tasting menu is highly recommended.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4464;Scannabue Caffè Restaurant;Italy;Turin;largo Saluzzo 25/h, Turin, 10125, Italy;45.0583351;7.6789861;19;true;false;Country cooking;This local restaurant is decorated in vintage style with books, furnishings and decor all evoking the early 20C. The cuisine is regional in flavour and includes some surprising technical touches – the “vasocottura” rabbit tuna (cooked in a jar) is superb, while the beef cheek with mashed potato is served with an intensely flavoured gravy. Top-quality, authentic cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4465;Camiano Piccolo;Italy;Montefalco;via Camiano Piccolo 5, Montefalco, 06036, Italy;42.8920383;12.6601425;53;true;false;Umbrian, Traditional Cuisine;Housed in a 16C farmhouse with and outdoor swimming pool, the Camiano Piccolo agriturismo stands on a hill overlooking the Umbrian countryside, 10 minutes’ drive from Montefalco. Here, chef Giuseppe Fabrizi brings the best of the region’s ingredients to the table, from vegetables grown in the restaurant’s own kitchen garden to local wines and olive oils, delicious meat and black truffles in season.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4466;Osteria Le Panzanelle;Italy;Lucarelli;località Lucarelli 29, Lucarelli, 53017, Italy;43.518906;11.311626;31;true;false;Tuscan;This pleasant rural trattoria has a simple, informal ambience, plus an attractive outdoor space in the shady garden. Wherever you sit, you’ll savour generous portions of delicious regional cuisine, including home-made pasta and excellent meat – we particularly enjoyed the pici pasta with garlic and the rabbit stuffed with spinach. Fresh fish from the island of Elba is served on Fridays, while the wine list focuses on Tuscan labels. It’s always a good idea to book ahead!;Terrace;[]
4467;Raieü;Italy;Cavi di Lavagna;via Milite Ignoto 23, Cavi di Lavagna, 16033, Italy;44.2900882;9.380131;54;false;false;Seafood, Ligurian;After more than 60 years in business, this trattoria housed in an old warehouse for storing fishing nets is still a solid choice for quality and price alike. Situated in the centre of Cavi di Lavagna, the restaurant is simple and old-fashioned in feel, while an outdoor space overlooks one of this small village’s narrow alleyways. The restaurant continues to specialise in typical Ligurian fish and seafood, which is simply prepared, copious and full of flavour. The soup is one of the house specialities, the pesto is excellent, and many of the unusual dishes feature local, seasonal ingredients such as Lavagna’s broccoli cabbage stuffed with fish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4468;Antica Trattoria da Miculan;Italy;Tricesimo;piazza Libertà 16, Tricesimo, 33019, Italy;46.1610218;13.2163029;55;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A small bar busy with locals acts as a sort of “antechamber” to this typical trattoria with a summer terrace on Tricesimo’s main square. The restaurant, which boasts traditional regional features, such as the wood-burning stove known as a fogher, serves local specialities alongside a few fish dishes. In summer, there’s a tasting menu which focuses exclusively on fish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4469;Foresta;Italy;Moena;strada de la Comunità de Fiem 42, Moena, 38035, Italy;46.3599668;11.6432225;51;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated in front of a dense fir wood, this restaurant comes as something of a surprise. The dishes are prepared with genuine local ingredients, resulting in food that is full of flavour. Don’t get up from the table without having tasted the pappardelle pasta with mushrooms and speck ham or the fillet of venison with a redcurrant sauce.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
4470;La Tradizione - Cucina Casalinga;Italy;Minervino Murge;via Imbriani 11/13, Minervino Murge, 76013, Italy;41.08729;16.078632;63;true;false;Apulian, Traditional Cuisine;A famous trattoria in the historic centre, next to the Immacolata church. Pleasant, rustic atmosphere with period photos on the walls and typical regional dishes such as troccoli alla murgese (pasta with ricotta and cherry tomatoes) on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4471;Osteria de Börg;Italy;Rimini;via Forzieri 12, Rimini, 47921, Italy;44.0648372;12.5634582;15;true;true;Cuisine from Romagna, Traditional Cuisine;Borgo San Giuliano is situated just a stroll from the sea in old Rimini, a district of narrow alleyways and brightly painted houses that once provided homes for local fishermen. It is also home to this excellent osteria-style restaurant with an outdoor space on the small square for summer meals and two smart dining rooms decorated with rustic vintage furnishings. This is the setting for typical Romagna cuisine which features top-quality cured hams, fresh home-made pasta (don’t miss the cappelletti in chicken broth) and meat including Mora Romagnola pork in various dishes.;Terrace;[]
4472;Antica Trattoria la Grotta dal 1918;Italy;Sasso Marconi;via Tignano 3, Loc. Mongardino Grotta, Sasso Marconi, 40037, Italy;44.4181181;11.2115002;41;true;true;Emilian, Country cooking;It takes a while to get here, along a road which wends its way through the hills, but the cuisine more than compensates for the journey. The food here is based on a careful choice of ingredients (including produce from the restaurant’s own farm) from as far away as the Apennines, with a few ingredients from elsewhere in Italy, with a focus on traditional recipes. Don’t miss the tortellini in brodo, or the game and truffles available in season.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4473;Del Belbo - Da Bardon;Italy;San Marzano Oliveto;valle Asinari 25, San Marzano Oliveto, 14050, Italy;44.7401454;8.3182743;46;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This traditional restaurant has been taking good care of its guests for generations. The delicious, authentic cuisine served here is accompanied by an extensive wine list that will delight fans of wines from the Langhe, Asti, elsewhere in Italy and France. There’s also an attractive outdoor space that is ideal for alfresco dining in fine weather. In short, this is the sort of restaurant you’d love to have as your local!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4474;Trattoria Losanna;Italy;Masio;via San Rocco 40, Masio, 15024, Italy;44.8675184;8.4205078;25;true;false;Piedmontese, Regional Cuisine;This friendly restaurant has a pleasantly convivial and lively ambience. Try a selection of homemade antipasto to start, followed by generous portions of traditional cuisine from Monferrato.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4475;Casa del Vino della Vallagarina;Italy;Isera;piazza San Vincenzo 1, Isera, 38060, Italy;45.8854479;11.0092968;100;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;A standard-bearer for local cuisine, this restaurant housed in the 17C Palazzo de Probizer in the town centre offers an outdoor area for alfresco dining in fine weather. Although the restaurant only offers a restricted set menu, this changes on a daily basis (single dishes can also be ordered from the menu) and there’s an extensive choice of desserts. All the bottles on the wine list, which showcases local wines, are also available by the glass. Attractive guestrooms on the top floors.;Terrace;[]
4476;Angiolina;Italy;Pisciotta;via Passariello 2, località Marina di Pisciotta, Pisciotta, 84066, Italy;40.1017552;15.2284136;58;false;false;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;This trattoria is situated at the end of the marina in Pisciotta, a location which ensures a quiet, tranquil ambience. The excellent, reasonably priced seafood cuisine is another reason that we heartily recommend eating here. With a focus on local fish, the menu features a wide array of specialities from Campania, including anchovies served in different ways (stuffed, “alla scapece”, salted and served with butter, and with spaghetti).;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4477;Osteria Didù;Italy;Imperia;via Felice Cascione 70, Imperia, 18100, Italy;43.8763874;8.013935;18;true;false;Seafood, Ligurian;Situated on an attractive pedestrian street lined with the historic palazzi of Porto San Maurizio, this simple yet pleasant restaurant offers an excellent choice of Ligurian specialities. Highlights include stuffed mussels and Genoese-style borage ravioli.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4478;Osteria Numero 2;Italy;Stradella;via Ghisiolo 2/a, Stradella, 46051, Italy;45.18035;10.8726;58;false;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;A beautiful farmhouse not far from the town, with a friendly, welcoming and colourful feel. Here, the menu features Italian dishes alongside a few local specialities, such as agnoli pasta in broth (also available as an antipasto in a “sorbir” wine broth). Special mention goes to the superb selection of beers chosen by owner Moreno, which ranges from local craft beers to labels from across the globe – there’s even a beer-themed dessert, the Birramisù. Excellent value for money and highly popular, so booking ahead is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4479;Osteria La Solita Zuppa;Italy;Chiusi;via Porsenna 21, Chiusi, 53043, Italy;43.0159011;11.9468611;15;false;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in Chiusi’s historic centre, this restaurant has the feel of a typical Tuscan trattoria with its traditional vaulted ceiling. The chef’s love for regional cuisine is demonstrated by the revival of traditional recipes (including the use of a wood-fired oven), resulting in the full flavours that are so characteristic of this region.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4480;Osteria Zanchetti;Italy;Fossombrone;via Cesare Battisti 1, Fossombrone, 61034, Italy;43.68966;12.80761;66;true;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated at the top of a steep slope in Fossombrone’s beautiful historic centre, this osteria takes guests back to the 1920s thanks to its romantic decor. Here, having risen through the culinary ranks, the owner-chef makes full use of his expert techniques to create dishes that hover between tradition and a sense of fantasy using the best seasonal ingredients that the region has to offer. The concise wine list favours micro-producers and natural wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4481;Trattoria Ai Due Platani;Italy;Coloreto;via Budellungo 104/a, Coloreto, 43123, Italy;44.7687333;10.3794418;32;true;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in a country setting just outside the town, this is one of the most famous restaurants in the province, so booking well in advance is highly recommended. Here, you’ll find cuisine with its roots in the region reinterpreted with a touch of creativity, with dishes that are presented in contemporary style. There’s an impressive selection of cured hams and the fresh pasta (including pumpkin or potato tortelli) is legendary, as is the ice-cream with freshly whipped cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4482;Dell'Alba;Italy;Piadena;via del Popolo 31, Piadena, 26034, Italy;45.1267675;10.3813957;100;false;false;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;In business since 1850, and now run by the sixth generation, this traditional and historic family trattoria is a mecca for fans of Bassa Padana cuisine. The simple yet authentic ambience is warm and welcoming, while the delicious cuisine – an extraordinary combination of specialities from Cremona and Mantova – is a real treat for the tastebuds.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4483;Italia;Italy;Quarona;piazza della Libertà 27, Quarona, 13017, Italy;45.761494;8.270105;44;true;false;Piedmontese;It's a pleasant surprise to discover the well - maintained and friendly modern establishment in this house in the centre of town. Creative dishes of Piedmontese cuisine.;Terrace;[]
4484;Osteria dal Moro;Italy;Giulianova Lido;lungomare Spalato 74, Giulianova Lido, 64021, Italy;42.7482346;13.9734163;18;false;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Seafood;A lively fish and seafood restaurant on the seafront, which is always busy thanks to its excellent value for money – booking ahead is highly recommended! Fish-based dishes only, all of which are announced at your table and which change regularly depending on market availability. The dishes are simple, rustic but full of flavour, which is why it’s easy to forgive the rather restricted choice of wine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4485;Osteria Veglio;Italy;La Morra;frazione Annunziata 9, La Morra, 12064, Italy;44.6372141;7.9552187;80;false;false;Piedmontese;With its own convenient car park and a large terrace boasting views of the Langhe, this minimalist-style restaurant built in the 1920s serves excellent food. As fans of offal dishes, we were delighted to see lamb kidneys in a Marsala sauce on the menu – a dish which certainly did not disappoint! Guests are required to choose a minimum of two dishes from the à la carte, excluding dessert.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4486;Osteria Madonnetta;Italy;Marostica;via Vajenti 21, Marostica, 36063, Italy;45.7449571;11.6543603;52;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Situated just a stone’s throw from the square with its famous chessboard, this authentic trattoria boasts a warm, inviting dining room and an outdoor space shaded by wisteria. Run by the same family for 120 years, the restaurant serves regional specialities such as tripe soup, bigoli pasta with various sauces, Vicenzo-style bacalà (salted cod), Venetian liver and desserts such as zaeti biscuits and macafame bread pudding. As there are just a few tables and the restaurant is very popular, booking ahead is recommended.;Terrace;[]
4487;Buatta Cucina Popolana;Italy;Palermo;via Vittorio Emanuele 176, Palermo, 90133, Italy;38.1171388;13.3651296;29;true;false;Sicilian;This simple yet lively and dynamic restaurant occupying the beautiful, historic rooms of an old shop is always busy with locals and tourists, so booking ahead is highly recommended. Dishes are traditionally Sicilian, such as the “sarde a scottadito” (sardines) and change regularly in line with the seasons. Meat, fish, offal and vegetarian options all feature on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4488;Antica Trattoria Cattivelli;Italy;Monticelli d'Ongina;via Chiesa di Isola Serafini 2, Monticelli d'Ongina, 29010, Italy;45.0969567;9.9062332;58;false;false;Country cooking;As its address indicates, this restaurant is situated on an island formed by a loop in the Po river. Since 1947, the Cattivelli family have been celebrating the best of the Lower Po valley’s cuisine here in a rural, river setting that is typical of the region. Regional dishes take pride of place on the menu, always served in generous portions and often made using locally sourced ingredients, including fresh home-made pastas and excellent ice-cream, as well as conserves made from home-grown produce. Although not particularly traditional, we enjoyed the mushroom macaroni made in-house using organic flour, as well as the veal served with caramelised shallots and potatoes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4489;Contesto Alimentare;Italy;Turin;via Accademia Albertina 21/e, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0623867;7.6862316;89;true;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Situated on the central Via Accademia Albertina, this small, simple and unfussy restaurant with small tables set close together serves top-quality Piedmontese cuisine. Alongside its delicious regional specialities, the menu also features dishes from elsewhere in Italy, including Sicily. The tajarin pasta made from 40 egg yolks and served with a veal ragu is superb, as are the rabbit and pork belly dishes. There’s a focus on meat options, followed by some delicious desserts, which include specialities from Piedmont such as panna cotta and typical bacio di dama biscuits.;Air conditioning;[]
4490;Andrea - Sapori Montani;Italy;Palazzolo Acreide;via Gabriele Judica 4, Palazzolo Acreide, 96010, Italy;37.061565;14.903214;15;true;true;Sicilian;Relocated in via Padre Giacinto 20.The restaurant takes its name from its chef Andrea, while the phrase “Sapori Montani” (mountain flavours) gives a good indication of the type of cuisine served here, from the local truffle-flavoured sausage – which has made Palazzolo Acreide’s name famous throughout Sicily – to trout, black suckling pig and excellent cheeses.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4491;Burro & Alici;Italy;Marotta;lungomare Colombo 98, Marotta, 61032, Italy;43.7665284;13.1445936;89;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;With just a road separating it from the beach (in summer, the large windows open completely, so that the dining room has the feel of an outdoor terrace), this simple restaurant is similar to the many others dotted along the seafront in Marotta. However, it’s the food that is the main attraction – the colourful, generous cuisine of the Adriatic, with fish served in classic recipes occasionally finished with an imaginative and personal twist. Fish also take pride of place on the delicious gourmet pizzas served here.;Terrace;[]
4492;Roma;Italy;Montoggio;via Roma 15, Montoggio, 16026, Italy;44.5139886;9.0436081;97;false;false;Ligurian, Seasonal Cuisine;Over a century of history and various generations of the same family at the helm have given a reassuring solidity to this restaurant in inland Liguria. In the airy, classically furnished dining room, enjoy abundant portions of impressive local and seasonal cooking, with a focus on home-grown fruits and vegetables, home-made pesto, mushrooms and truffles, and superb cuts of meats and tartares. However, part of the menu is also devoted to fish.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4493;Il Ciabot;Italy;Roletto;via Costa 7, Roletto, 10060, Italy;44.9253944;7.3305602;73;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Warmed by an open fire in winter, this welcoming family-run restaurant celebrates the cuisine of Piedmont, although a few fish dishes also feature on the menu. Traditional, time-honoured and overlooked dishes take pride of place, such as boiled meat terrine with a salsa verde, Fassone beef in a crust, plus an excellent giandujotto chocolate mousse. Booking ahead is recommended.;Terrace;[]
4494;L'Oste Dispensa;Italy;Orbetello;strada provinciale Giannella 113, Orbetello, 58015, Italy;42.439444;11.1686422;26;true;true;Country cooking, Organic;The focus at this restaurant is on local ingredients, including sustainably caught fish and seafood. The set menu changes in line with the seasons and the availability of ingredients, while the excellent wine list boasts an impressive selection of organic and biodynamic labels. The wine cellar can be glimpsed through the floor near the cash till, and uninterrupted views of the sea can be enjoyed from the dining room.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
4495;Luna Rossa;Italy;Terranova di Pollino;via Marconi 18, Terranova di Pollino, 85030, Italy;39.9771853;16.297476;42;true;false;Cuisine from Basilicata;This rustic, convivial restaurant in the village centre boasts a panoramic terrace overlooking the valley. A constant search for recipes from Italy’s peasant tradition combines with the passion and talent of the chef to create specialities such as raviolo della memoria.;Great view,Terrace;[]
4496;Al Piave;Italy;Mariano del Friuli;via Cormons 6 - Fraz. Corona, Mariano del Friuli, 34071, Italy;45.921916;13.4820929;53;false;true;Friulian, Seasonal Cuisine;This welcoming family - run trattoria comprises of two attractive dining rooms and a beautiful summer garden. It specialises in regional dishes that vary according to the seasons. Guinea fowl cooked with chives is one of the house specialities.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4497;Taverna dei Caldora;Italy;Pacentro;piazza Umberto I 13, Pacentro, 67030, Italy;42.0499185;13.9908288;54;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Meats and Grills;Situated amid the maze of narrow streets in the old town of Pacentro and occupying the wine cellars of an imposing 16C palazzo, this restaurant celebrates regional cuisine in all its glory in specialities such as spaghetti with saffron and truffles.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4498;13 Comuni;Italy;Velo Veronese;piazza della Vittoria 31, Velo Veronese, 37030, Italy;45.6053;11.09587;72;true;false;Venetian, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the village square, this restaurant is run by a couple – she’s front of house, while he’s in the kitchen – who use top - quality local produce to prepare a mix of traditional and modern dishes. House specialities include gnocchi with sheep’s ricotta cheese and hazel butter (the butter isn’t actually made with hazelnuts but is simply melted), and confit pork ribs in beer. The mountain - style decor continues in the simple guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
4499;Upepidde;Italy;Ruvo di Puglia;vico Sant'Agnese 2, angolo corso Cavour, Ruvo di Puglia, 70037, Italy;41.1147414;16.4869587;86;true;false;Apulian;Undeniably characteristic and refreshing! Dug out of the rock that once formed the old Aragonese walls, the four dining rooms in this restaurant run one into another under brick arches and then lead to the wine cellar, which is open to guests. The regional cuisine is as traditional as the decor, with specialities such as barbecued local meat and beef fillet in a plum sauce with wine and caramelised shallots on the menu.;Interesting wine list;[]
4500;Taverna del Grappolo Blu;Italy;Montalcino;scale di via Moglio 1, Montalcino, 53024, Italy;43.0589313;11.4898268;17;true;true;Tuscan;Accessed via a steep, narrow flight of steps, this restaurant boasts a traditional and friendly ambience. The cuisine is traditionally Tuscan (pici pasta with ragu and tripe are among the most popular dishes on the menu), while the interesting wine list includes a selection of Brunello wines arranged by year, as well as some top-quality vintage options which will delight wine-enthusiasts. The owner oversees the informal yet attentive service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4501;Al Palazzon;Italy;Galliera Veneta;via Ca' Onorai 2, loc. Mottinello Nuovo, Galliera Veneta, 35015, Italy;45.6735429;11.8115922;84;false;false;Venetian, Classic Cuisine;Housed in an early 20C farmhouse, this restaurant boasts the typical ambience of a traditional multi-generational trattoria, while the cuisine focuses on classic dishes that are typical of the Veneto. Highlights include bigoli pasta, bean soup, Vicenza-style baccalà cod and mallard duck.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4502;Serendib;Italy;Milan;via Pontida 2, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4798954;9.1827996;98;false;true;Indian, Asian;Serendib, the old name for Sri Lanka, means “to make happy” – an ambitious promise but one which this welcoming restaurant serving typical Indian and Sri Lankan dishes manages to keep. The tasting menu introduces guests to different specialities and comes highly recommended (especially if it’s your first time here).;Air conditioning;[]
4503;La Pineta;Italy;Sant'Anna;piazzale Sant'Anna 6, Sant'Anna, 12020, Italy;44.4981324;7.3086768;35;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;You will need a certain amount of patience to tackle the winding road through woods and hills to get to La Pineta, but the food makes the journey well worthwhile. There is a restricted choice – just one tasting menu, although the number of courses can be reduced – with the famous house speciality, fritto misto alla piemontese, taking pride of place. Spacious, welcoming guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4504;Stella;Italy;Casaglia;via dei Narcisi 47/a, Casaglia, 06126, Italy;43.1065133;12.4316475;96;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Dining options at this restaurant include an attractive outdoor terrace with views of the surrounding area (in summer) and a friendly bistro-style dining room. We particularly enjoyed the linguine with carp roe, as well as the stuffed pigeon.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4505;Trattoria Lanzagallo;Italy;Gaibana;via Ravenna 1048, Gaibana, 44124, Italy;44.7540004;11.6549983;75;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;Don’t be fooled by the simple decor and unfussy ambience at this restaurant – the Trattoria Lanzagallo is one of the best places in the province for top-quality fish served in delicious, generous and imaginative dishes. The menu is striking for its reasonable prices.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4506;Podere San Faustino;Italy;Fidenza;via San Faustino 33 (SS Emilia Nord), Fidenza, 43036, Italy;44.8734471;10.0340833;55;false;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of the Bassa Parmense region, this old farmhouse has retained romantic reminders of bygone days. The menu also has a traditional feel, featuring dishes such as egg tagliolini with a salami, sun - dried tomato and onion sauce, and braised pork cheeks with a fennel carpaccio in an orange marinade. There’s also a good choice of delicious desserts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4507;Osteria Borsò Gambrinus;Italy;San Polo di Piave;via Capitello 18, San Polo di Piave, 31020, Italy;45.7968129;12.3885415;34;true;false;Venetian, Seasonal Cuisine;A wine bar-cum-osteria with a warm, rustic decor and a menu offering fish and meat dishes, including specialities such as fried scampi, squid, crayfish and vegetables, all seasoned with olive oil. There’s also a good choice of wines by the glass, with a focus on natural wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4508;Osteria la Fefa;Italy;Finale Emilia;via Trento-Trieste 9/c, Finale Emilia, 41034, Italy;44.8331758;11.2958166;84;false;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;The name “Fefa” is a diminutive of Genoveffa, the female owner who founded this restaurant almost a century ago. Today, the new generation provides streamlined service, decidedly Emilian cuisine and careful attention to wine thanks to talented sommelier Edoardo, who is equally at home recommending a French Côtes-du-Rhône as he is with local Sangiovese labels – the extensive wine list (an entire page is dedicated to magnum bottles) will definitely impress wine-enthusiasts. The “primi” are delicious (don’t miss the classic tortellino in Parmesan cream), as are the “secondi”, which include sweet and sour duck leg in a Lambrusco sauce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4509;Antica Trattoria La Toppa;Italy;San Donato in Poggio;via del Giglio 43, San Donato in Poggio, 50028, Italy;43.5354466;11.2344884;98;true;true;Tuscan;The two traditional rooms at this restaurant are perfectly in keeping with the medieval atmosphere of the beautifully preserved village of San Donato. The cuisine is obviously Tuscan in style, delighting guests with its exquisite home-made pasta expertly prepared by young chef Matteo. At certain times of the year, special dishes such as game make an appearance on the menu – the wild boar stew is not to be missed! Among the desserts, make sure you try the caramel panna cotta which is one of the best in the region. The small wine list includes a few labels from famous wineries.;Terrace;[]
4510;Dalla Libera;Italy;Sernaglia della Battaglia;via Farra 52, Sernaglia della Battaglia, 31020, Italy;45.8771069;12.132017;79;true;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;At this restaurant, an American-style barbecue garden (in summer) and a smart, rustic dining room provide the backdrop for carefully prepared local cuisine with a personalised, gourmet twist, such as the home-made gnocchi served with three different types of tomato. The wine list features top-quality labels from Italy and further afield, including a few vintages that will delight wine-enthusiasts.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4511;Apollonia;Italy;Nals;via Sant'Apollonia 3, località Sirmiano Sopra, Nals, 39010, Italy;46.529537;11.186598;23;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Following a road that twists and turns uphill, surrounded at first by vineyards and fruit trees and then by woodland, you climb to an altitude of 900m to reach this restaurant run by the Geiser family, who have been serving simple yet delicious regional (and Italian) cuisine here for three generations. With a focus on seasonal ingredients from the Alto Adige, the menus feature specialities such as potato rosti with beetroot, baked pumpkin, broccoli and porcini mushroom cream, as well as home-made tarts and sorbets. The beautiful views take in Terlano in the middle of the valley and the majestic Dolomites (including Sciliar, Catinaccio and Latemar) in the distance.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4512;L'Acino;Italy;Turin;via San Domenico 2/a, Turin, 10121, Italy;45.0743527;7.6817442;53;false;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of the Roman quadrilateral, in this characteristic and friendly restaurant the traditional Piedmontese cuisine is honored. The specialties include: stuffed onion, vitel tonnè, agnolotti and tajarin, tripe and stracotto. Among the desserts, the bonet and hazelnut cake with zabajone are not to be missed. They have few tables, so we advise booking.;Air conditioning;[]
4513;QuarantunoDodici;Italy;Fiumicino;via Monte Cadria 127, Fiumicino, 00054, Italy;41.747772;12.257375;41;true;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the banks of the river, this seaside osteria run by chef Lele Usai (the Michelin-starred Tino is on the first floor of the building) is the perfect setting for a business lunch or an enjoyable dinner thanks to its excellent fish-based cuisine which is firmly rooted in traditional recipes. As well as the à la carte, the “Diario di Bordo” lists the daily specials, which showcase the freshest fish on offer here.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4514;Boivin;Italy;Levico Terme;via Garibaldi 9, Levico Terme, 38056, Italy;46.0113105;11.3003374;50;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Occupying an old house in the town centre, this restaurant is strongly influenced by the character and ideas of owner-chef Riccardo Bosco, who offers an original mix of traditional Trento cuisine and influences from around the world, including Korean kimchi and Japanese cooking methods such as tataki. A prime example of the latter is one of the restaurant’s signature dishes, namely trout with celeriac purée. Daily specials based on what’s available at the market also feature, while regional wines are to the fore on the wine list.;Terrace;[]
4515;Rosselli 77;Italy;Cuorgnè;via F.lli Rosselli 77, Cuorgnè, 10082, Italy;45.3993734;7.649048;31;false;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;A series of rooms teeming with warmth and atmosphere provide the backdrop for this simple and homely restaurant on the edge of town, where the chef announces dishes at your table. Although the menu can vary, pride of place is given to Piedmontese ingredients and culinary traditions, such as the cream of roasted chestnuts and mushrooms and the delicious snails.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4516;Krone;Italy;Aldino;piazza Principale 4, Aldino, 39040, Italy;46.3684718;11.3543035;53;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The past retains its fascinating appeal in this traditional restaurant situated in a small mountain village, where modern trends are ignored in favour of authentic dishes from the South Tyrol. Originally opened as an inn, the restaurant still offers a few simple and discreet rooms furnished in traditional style, as well as a new and modern sauna.;Terrace;[]
4517;Buscone;Italy;Varzi;Località Bosmenso Superiore 41, Varzi, 27057, Italy;44.7909875;9.2208794;91;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;The difficulty, which perhaps you may encounter when trying to reach this trattoria, is compensated by the very pleasant family atmosphere and genuine home - made cooking.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4518;Antica Locanda al Cervo - Landgasthof zum Hirschen;Italy;San Genesio Atesino;via Schrann 9/c, San Genesio Atesino, 39050, Italy;46.5340136;11.333222;74;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Enjoy generous, regional cuisine influenced by the family’s involvement in the cattle and horse farming business, either in the restaurant’s welcoming dining rooms or on its sunny panoramic terrace. “Zero food miles” produce is much more than a simple slogan here!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4519;Veneziano;Italy;Randazzo;Contrada Arena, SS 120 km 187, Randazzo, 95036, Italy;37.8763419;14.9713893;16;false;false;Sicilian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated just outside Randazzo, one of the villages with typical lava-stone buildings dotted around Mt Etna, this restaurant serves excellent local cuisine. Recipes featuring mushrooms and meat take pride of place on the menu, from antipasti such as the excellent mixed mushrooms to first courses of mushroom soup and mains that include a highly recommended “asado” (mixed grill) and an unmissable Nero dei Nebrodi capocollo ham.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4520;Terme;Italy;Pigna;via Madonna Assunta, Pigna, 18037, Italy;43.92997;7.66846;23;false;false;Ligurian;Not far from the picturesque village of Pigna, this family-run hotel-restaurant has a simple, classic-style dining room where the main focus is on the equally simple and rustic cuisine, including the dish of goats’ meat and beans, a local speciality.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4521;Al Bersagliere;Italy;Verona;via Dietro Pallone 1, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4363246;10.9980274;97;true;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;This long-established restaurant in the Borgo Filippi district overflows with memorabilia (from the juke box to the old coffee machine dating from the 1960s) and owes its continued success to its generous, comforting cuisine that showcases the fine traditions of the Veneto. Specialities include bigoli pasta with duck, pastissada de caval (horsemeat stew) and gelato spiritoso(ice cream flavoured with grappa). Guests can visit the interesting wine cellar, parts of which date back to the early 13C, which focuses on labels from the Verona region (especially Amarone). There’s also an excellent selection of spirits.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4522;Trattoria da Paeto;Italy;Pianiga;via Patriarcato 78, Pianiga, 30030, Italy;45.4693768;12.0355686;98;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This small trattoria hidden among the canals in the countryside is run by a couple of partners who showcase the specialities of the region with professionalism and enthusiasm. The menu includes delicacies such as fish and vegetable couscous, and sfoglia pastry with cream and flakes of chocolate, as well as a few more modern dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4523;Il Sogno;Italy;Vetrego;via Vetrego 8, Vetrego, 30035, Italy;45.4663112;12.0995204;52;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant (once a cultural club) in the Miranese countryside serves simple yet delicious cuisine at reasonable prices. Although the dishes have their roots in the region, they are also influenced by Slow Food traditions from elsewhere in Italy and further afield and boast the occasional personalised touch. In winter, the trolley of boiled meats served with sauces and mostarda makes an appearance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4524;Tre Noghere;Italy;Bigolino;via Crede 1, Bigolino, 31049, Italy;45.8749598;12.0169773;57;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Situated in a peaceful location amid fields and vineyards, this attractive country restaurant run by the same family since 1965 boasts an outdoor space where three walnut trees (“tre noghere”) provide shade in summer, plus a neat and simple dining room. The skilful owner is at the helm in the kitchen, while the younger generation provide a warm and professional welcome front of house. Traditional cuisine, including home-made pastas, are to the fore here – we particularly enjoyed the bigoli with ragu and rosemary, as well as the glazed duck breast with apricots. We asked for recommendations when choosing our wine and we didn’t regret it!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4525;Da Giannino - L'Angolo d'Abruzzo;Italy;Milan;via Rosolino Pilo 20, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.47267;9.21326;54;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;A warm welcome combined with a simple but lively atmosphere and typical dishes from the Abruzzo region make this a popular place to eat. Generous portions and excellent roast dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
4526;Domenico dal 1968;Italy;Rome;via Satrico 23, Rome, 00183, Italy;41.8771101;12.5075051;33;false;true;Roman, Cuisine from Lazio;Situated away from the tourist trail, this authentic neighbourhood restaurant popular with locals serves two types of cuisine, namely fish-based dishes and Roman specialities. Announced at your table, the tempting delicacies include Roman- and Jewish-style artichokes, fried aubergine balls, tripe, sweetbreads and offal. A must-visit address serving authentic local cuisine in simple dining rooms with a family feel. Booking is recommended, as there are only a few tables.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4527;La Campanara;Italy;Galeata;via Borgo  Pianetto 24/a, Galeata, 47010, Italy;43.98591;11.90544;64;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Situated in a village near Galeata, this restaurant boasts a charming small inner courtyard – you walk through here into an idyllic outdoor dining space next to the church surrounded by trees and with views of the hills. The regional cuisine focuses on specialities from Romagna as well as the nearby Marche and (especially) Tuscany. If you’re looking for somewhere to stay, there’s an inn with rooms next door to the restaurant.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4528;La Brinca;Italy;Ne;via Campo di Ne 58, Ne, 16040, Italy;44.35394;9.38928;52;false;false;Ligurian, Traditional Cuisine;This trattoria run by the Circella family – without doubt one of the best in Italy – has been delighting guests since 1987. The menu features dishes and ingredients that are generous, full of flavour and strongly rooted in the region, including “dishes of the year” which go back to 2010. The superb wine cellar boasts a selection of over 1 000 labels, including some rare bottles, for which sommelier Matteo received Michelin’s Best Sommelier in Italy award in 2021. To sum up, this is the sort of restaurant that everyone would like in their neighbourhood!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4529;Sa Mandra;Italy;Alghero;SP 44, km 1, Alghero, 07041, Italy;40.6532916;8.2975279;74;false;true;Sardinian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated on the Azienda Agrituristica Sa Mandra, this restaurant allows guests to savour one of Sardinia’s emblematic ingredients, namely delicious roast suckling pig which is the focus of the single menu offered here. Once seated at your table, you’ll be served a host of small bites and courses, all of which are based on this main ingredient. Make sure you arrive early to watch the pig being cooked – the owners are happy to explain the procedure, right down to the smallest detail. Guestrooms are also available.;Terrace;[]
4530;Borgo Spoltino;Italy;Mosciano Sant'Angelo;strada Selva Alta, Mosciano Sant'Angelo, 64023, Italy;42.71786;13.87886;78;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;Borgo Spoltino occupies a 19C farmhouse amid hills and olive groves with views of the sea and mountains as a backdrop. This is the perfect setting in which to enjoy typical Abruzzi cuisine (most of the vegetables come from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden). These include traditional specialities such as sweet pizza (alternating layers of sponge cake soaked in Kermes liqueur, pudding and custard – a bit like a trifle – with a thick cream and slivers of almond, either on top or in the middle). The wine list features a good selection of regional wines, alongside labels from further afield.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4531;Zeb;Italy;Florence;via San Miniato 2r, Florence, 50125, Italy;43.7641016;11.2612484;20;true;true;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;A new take on traditional cuisine in this unique restaurant in the delightful San Niccolò district. Diners sit side - by - side around a central table, as in a sushi bar, enjoying a selection of delicious homemade dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
4532;Trattoria alla Ruota;Italy;Negrar;via Proale 6, località Mazzano, Negrar, 37024, Italy;45.5696135;10.9565875;22;true;true;Venetian, Modern Cuisine;Don’t be misled by the word trattoria – this is an elegant restaurant offering superb views of the surrounding hills. The cuisine here is constantly changing, with a use of local produce which is transformed into imaginative and elaborate dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4533;Da Burde;Italy;Florence;via Pistoiese 154, Florence, 50145, Italy;43.7940341;11.1858068;99;false;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;Booking in advance is highly recommended at this traditional Tuscan restaurant (home to a grocer’s shop as well as a trattoria) which has a loyal and regular clientele. Most guests come here for the superb Fiorentina steak (cooked over the grill), as well as the classic soups and home-made pastas. The wine list is overseen by Andrea, an enthusiastic sommelier who enjoys organising themed wine-tasting evenings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4534;Locanda del Capitano & Tipico Osteria;Italy;Montone;via Roma 7, Montone, 06014, Italy;43.3635471;12.3268121;17;false;false;Umbrian, Traditional Cuisine;The Locanda del Capitano and the Tipico offer menus showcasing traditional Umbrian dishes (the former serves gourmet cuisine, while the latter offers a simpler menu). The wine list boasts over 400 labels, while the olive oil selection includes the best oils from the region. Our inspector particularly enjoyed the “maritozzo di mazzafegato” (a type of sausage bun) with escarole, caramelised onions and olives.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4535;Da Marchesi;Italy;Novafeltria;Località Ca' Gianessi 7, Novafeltria, 47863, Italy;43.8990174;12.2584081;83;true;false;Country cooking;Situated on a road that climbs through the Apennines between Romagna and the Marche, this small restaurant serves good, simple and traditional Romagna cuisine. The menu features home-made pasta and local meat dishes, as well as daily specials which focus on seasonal ingredients (don’t miss the “fossa” cheese from Perticara and the tortelloni with melted butter and truffles). One of our inspectors’ favourite trattorias!;Car park,Terrace;[]
4536;Le Antiche Sere;Italy;Lesina;via P. Micca 22, Lesina, 71010, Italy;41.8653128;15.3543138;78;true;true;Apulian, Seafood;A small restaurant overlooking the lake in Lesina, where everything revolves around the professionalism and experience of the owner - chef, who selects the best produce from the lake region, including fish and aromatic herbs, and even produces his own mullet roe. Regional flavours are to the fore here, with the occasional modern twist.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4538;Antica Osteria;Italy;Ossana;via Venezia 11, Ossana, 38026, Italy;46.3072076;10.7370371;98;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;A pleasant restaurant with three charming dining rooms, where the whole family pulls together with spectacular results. Delicious regional cuisine is to the fore, with dishes such as venison carpaccio with pineapple and raspberries on the menu.;;[]
4539;La Cuccagna - Giro di Vite;Italy;Crispiano;corso Umberto I 168, Crispiano, 74012, Italy;40.6040474;17.2287707;91;false;true;Apulian;There are many reasons to visit this excellent family - run restaurant in the village centre, the most important of which is the food – fresh vegetables, delicious first courses (the fresh troccoli pasta with wild chicory, cherry tomatoes and broad beans is excellent) and carefully selected meat dishes (the father was once a butcher! ). Close attention is also paid to the wine, with more than 500 labels just waiting to be opened in the beautiful wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4540;Vecchio Porto;Italy;Villa San Giovanni;lungomare Cenide 55, Villa San Giovanni, 89018, Italy;38.2306377;15.6360812;31;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Although travellers may know Villa San Giovanni for its ferry port to Sicily, fans of gourmet cuisine are familiar with the port as the home of the “Vecchio Porto”, one of the best restaurants in the region and one which boasts spectacular views of the Straits of Messina from its second-floor terrace. The menu features classic dishes including fish cooked on the grill and more imaginative options such as the raw antipasti (snapper flavoured with sea-urchin sauce, lumpfish roe, onion and diced cucumber). The remarkable quality of the fish is a constant theme here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4541;Le Miniere;Italy;Traversella;piazza Martiri 1944 4, Traversella, 10080, Italy;45.5091669;7.7508274;74;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Situated on the main square of a charming village, this hotel-restaurant dates back to the late 19C and is run by the friendly Arsini family. The setting here is truly picturesque, thanks to the village’s location on a green and sunny ridge in the Val Chiusella, surrounded by cyclamen bushes and majestic birch and chestnut trees. Meanwhile, the Piedmontese dishes offer excellent value for money, with a focus on local ingredients and produce from the wider region. If you’re a fan of traditional cuisine, don’t miss the tripe alla campagnola with polenta taragna whipped with butter, while in season the roast cardo gobbo served with a delicious bagna cauda and truffle is a must. A stroll around the small village offers the perfect conclusion to your meal.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4542;Locanda Cacciatori;Italy;Ponte dell'Olio;località Mistadello di Castione, Ponte dell'Olio, 29028, Italy;44.8567768;9.661281;63;true;true;Emilian, Home Cooking;This authentic trattoria situated in the hills outside Piacenza is always popular for Sunday lunch but can also get busy on weekdays. The cuisine is typical of the region with dishes announced at your table. The atmosphere evokes that of a traditional, time-honoured restaurant perpetuated here by the expertise and passion of a friendly family that has been involved in the restaurant sector since the end of the Second World War. A welcoming outdoor area for summer dining completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4543;Osteria della Villetta;Italy;Palazzolo sull'Oglio;via Marconi 104, Palazzolo sull'Oglio, 25036, Italy;45.6026934;9.8940244;84;false;true;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;A bulwark of Brescian cuisine for over a century, this restaurant has Art Nouveau - style furnishings, a retro decor and an authentic family atmosphere. It serves delicious specialities such as lake fish, onion soup, tripe, meatballs and beef in olive oil.;Terrace;[]
4544;Green T.;Italy;Rome;via del Piè di Marmo 28, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8976162;12.4792745;69;false;true;Chinese, Asian Contemporary;Not far from the Pantheon, this original restaurant arranged over four floors serves the type of fine Chinese cuisine which has graced official banquets in China ever since the time of Chairman Mao. The menu also features some surprisingly modern Asian dishes, making this restaurant a must for fans of Chinese cuisine!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4545;Da Flavio e Fabrizio "Al Teatro";Italy;Mirano;via della Vittoria 75, Mirano, 30035, Italy;45.4908586;12.1151308;91;false;true;Seafood, Venetian;Choose the ground floor for a quick meal and the first floor for a special dinner in this restaurant near the cinema - theatre. In both cases, the menu focuses on traditional fish dishes from the Veneto, such as black and white tagliolini with squid, scampi and courgettes. The honey semifreddo with caramel is the perfect way to round off your meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4546;Trattoria Cibrèo - Il Cibrèino;Italy;Florence;via dei Macci 122 r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7712441;11.2664192;81;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This trattoria is named after the famous cibreo, a typical stew from Florence that Catherine of Medici was said to enjoy so much that she even attempted, unsuccessfully, to export it to France. It is often crowded, but there is no point in trying to book a table as they don’t take reservations. Roast rack of beef (gran pezzo) is one of the specialities.;Air conditioning;[]
4547;La Chioccia d'Oro;Italy;Vallo della Lucania;via Novi 2, loc. Pietra dei Correnti, bivio  Novi Velia, Vallo della Lucania, 84078, Italy;40.2183495;15.279882;35;true;false;Country cooking, Campanian;For over 40 years, La Chioccia d'Oro has been renowned for its delicious, bountiful cuisine inspired by the Cilento region, including excellent pasta dishes (fresh and dried pasta served with tasty sauces) and equally delicious meat-based main courses. The ambience is decidedly unpretentious and the prices are some of the most reasonable you’ll find in Italy!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4548;Cantina dei Cacciatori;Italy;Monteu Roero;località Villa Superiore 59, Monteu Roero, 12040, Italy;44.7849738;7.9080622;84;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;The original sign painted on this restaurant’s façade hints at a history which dates back over a century. Situated outside the village and surrounded by sweet chestnut trees and tufa rock, what was once an old trattoria now serves typical Piedmontese specialities, such as meat and borage ravioli with butter and crispy pancetta, as well as dishes from further afield. Charming outdoor area for summer dining, plus an early - 20C wine cellar which can be visited by guests.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4549;Lo Stuzzichino;Italy;Sant'Agata sui Due Golfi;via Deserto 1/a, Sant'Agata sui Due Golfi, 80061, Italy;40.6087388;14.3723456;74;false;true;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the centre of Sant'Agata, this welcoming, informal restaurant boasts traditional ceramics and an open-view kitchen. When ordering your meal, make sure you ask the charismatic owner, who is a real connoisseur of Campanian cuisine, for his recommendations. The regional dishes are full of memorable flavours, with a focus on vegetables, many of which are grown in the restaurant’s own kitchen garden nearby. This is somewhere you’d happily come to eat every day!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4550;Taverna 58;Italy;Pescara;corso Manthoné 46, Pescara, 65127, Italy;42.46174;14.213223;15;true;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the district where Ennio Flaiano and Gabriele d'Annunzio once lived, this excellent trattoria has been in business now for over 40 years. Despite changing hands in 2020, the restaurant’s essence remains the same. The cuisine is still simple and rustic, generously portioned and full of flavour, with its roots firmly planted in Abruzzi traditions. The menu features arrosticini (skewered grilled meat), vegetable and goat’s cheese fritters, numerous meat-based main courses (mutton, pork, rabbit, wild boar, veal, beef etc), and a white Abruzzese torrone named Oh pe' la Maiellaby the restaurant. Guests are welcome to visit the medieval and Roman remains in the wine cellars.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4551;Il Conte Matto;Italy;Trequanda;via Taverne 40, Trequanda, 53020, Italy;43.1882927;11.6666371;22;true;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;The castle’s 14C hunting lodge has been converted into a showcase for Tuscan produce with a panoramic terrace overlooking the hills and glimpses of the surrounding countryside from the guestrooms. Specialities include pici pasta in a Chianina beef ragù, veal tagliata seasoned with three salts and herbs from the garden, and cantucci biscuits served with dessert wine.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
4552;Villa Aurora;Italy;Soiano del Lago;via Ciucani 1/7, Soiano del Lago, 25080, Italy;45.53681;10.51391;30;true;true;Classic Cuisine;A typical restaurant in the province of Brescia not far from Lake Garda, Villa Aurora serves Italian cuisine with an equal focus on meat and fish dishes, as well as a few traditional specialities with a light modern twist. A bastion of local cuisine, the restaurant is run by a welcoming and experienced family. Don’t miss the desserts!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4553;La Fratanza;Italy;Nocera Superiore;via Garibaldi 37, Nocera Superiore, 84015, Italy;40.7495611;14.6791142;79;false;false;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;Follow your satnav and you’ll easily find this private residence situated just outside the village. The restaurant is family run and furnished in classic style, with an attractive veranda room overlooking the garden. The friendly owner serves regional cuisine, all carefully prepared using top-quality local ingredients, some of which (such as the delicious lemons and excellent San Marzano tomatoes that appear in a number of dishes) are grown in the restaurant’s own orchard and kitchen garden. Our inspector particularly enjoyed the ravioli di genovese served with onions and pecorino cheese.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4554;Bruxaboschi;Italy;San Desiderio;via Francesco Mignone 8, San Desiderio, 16133, Italy;44.4231154;9.0131106;61;true;true;Ligurian, Traditional Cuisine;You’ll need to allow plenty of time to get to the inland village of San Desiderio, where Bruxaboschi has been run by the same family and delighting guests since 1862, but the journey is certainly worth it. Justifiably famous, the cuisine pays tribute to local traditions (almost exclusively based on meat), starting with an excellent cima alla Genovese (a type of meat loaf), picagge and pansotti pasta dishes, and fried rabbit. Don’t miss the mushrooms in season.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4555;Trattoria da Fagiolino;Italy;Cutigliano;via Carega 1, Cutigliano, 51024, Italy;44.1000069;10.7544173;67;false;false;Tuscan;To get to the dining room at this restaurant you walk past the kitchen, where its stoves are lit and its chefs hard at work. This is the sort of restaurant that you’d love to have as your local, serving delicious traditional cuisine in a simple yet friendly setting. The dishes are resolutely Tuscan and the ingredients are of the highest quality.;Great view;[]
4556;Romani;Italy;Vicomero di Torrile;via dei Ronchi 2, Vicomero di Torrile, 43056, Italy;44.8839459;10.3150109;32;true;true;Emilian;This restaurant has a traditional feel, both in its richly decorated dining room and in its cuisine, the roots of which are firmly planted in the region. This is the place for guests who aren’t keen on reinterpreted dishes or exotic fare but prefer the classic flavours of Parma such as cured hams, fresh pasta, and roast and grilled meat, all served in a typical country farmhouse.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4557;La Cucoma;Italy;San Pancrazio;via Molinaccio 175, San Pancrazio, 48020, Italy;44.3563305;12.0786464;48;true;false;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in a village inland, this restaurant serves some of the best fish dishes in Romagna. The focus here is on classic recipes from the Adriatic with no unnecessary frills or innovations, all prepared using the freshest fish and including raw fish dishes, fried options, spaghetti with clams and fish barbecued over a wood fire.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4558;Trippa;Italy;Milan;via Giorgio Vasari 1, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.45215;9.205526;38;true;true;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;Simple, informal and with a slightly retro feel, this restaurant serves a range of dishes from all over Italy, including the tripe which gives the restaurant its name. Unfussy and uncomplicated, the cuisine prepared by the skilful young chef using top-quality ingredients makes this one of the best trattorias in Italy. House specialities include Milanese risotto with grilled marrow, vitello tonnato and, of course, the ever-present tripe!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4559;L'800;Italy;Argelato;via Centese 33, Argelato, 40050, Italy;44.6414004;11.351547;35;false;false;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Period furniture, regional cuisine and a cheerful ambience are some of the characteristics of this old farmhouse which is named after the 1800s when it was built. Some of the ingredients used, such as snails and frogs’ legs, may come as a surprise: the restaurant specialises in these unusual delicacies, even offering a tasting menu totally dedicated to snails.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4560;Al Convento - Casa Torrente;Italy;Cetara;piazza San Francesco 16, Cetara, 84010, Italy;40.6473603;14.7008016;51;true;true;Campanian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Following renovation work, the frescoed dining room at this restaurant now has the feel of a contemporary osteria, while its attractive terrace boasts tables overlooking the picturesque village’s small square. The menu focuses mainly on fish and seafood (although a few meat options such as tomahawk ribeye and steak also feature), including raw fish, tartares, fried anchovies stuffed with smoked provolone cheese, grilled dishes, and pasta including spaghetti with the local anchovy sauce. If you choose fish from the dry ageing cabinet, you’ll add a little extra to your bill.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4561;Dongiò;Italy;Milan;via Corio 3, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.4517517;9.205139;37;false;false;Calabrian, Traditional Cuisine;If you enjoy Calabrian cuisine and you want to keep to a budget, then Dongiò is the place for you! The menu here offers a good selection of regional specialities, all full of intense and satisfying flavours and served in a simple yet friendly ambience.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4562;Nana Piccolo Bistrò;Italy;Senigallia;via Giosuè Carducci 19, Senigallia, 60019, Italy;43.7168212;13.2173321;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Spanish influences are evident in the cuisine served at this lively restaurant situated in the heart of this bustling town. After years spent working in Spain, the owner-chef has returned to Senigallia where he delights guests with dishes such as Iberian carbonara (made with Pata Negra ham and Manchego cheese) and potato and salted cod omelette. In high season, it’s best to book ahead and maybe even get here early to avoid parking problems – you can always work up an appetite with a stroll through Senigallia’s beautiful historic centre. Young, friendly and efficient female staff add to the appeal.;Terrace;[]
4563;Hosteria Grappolo d'Oro;Italy;Rome;piazza della Cancelleria 80, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8964575;12.4721342;91;false;false;Roman, Traditional Cuisine;Since the turn of the century, this long-established restaurant near Piazza Navona and Campo de' Fiori has been run by five local business partners, one of whom is the chef. Top-quality, classic and generous Roman cuisine (cacio e pepe pasta, roast lamb, salted cod etc) is to the fore here, served in an attractive, rustic-style dining room. The background music – a nostalgic 1970s mix of rock and blues – also deserves a mention.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4564;Locanda da Condo;Italy;Col San Martino;via Fontana 134, Col San Martino, 31010, Italy;45.8969808;12.0885489;76;true;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the delightful Prosecco wine-growing region, Condo is a well-established trattoria which has been in the same family for generations, and which remains faithful to the gastronomic traditions of the Veneto. The dining rooms are welcoming and full of character, while the elegant veranda adorned with climbing plants is an attractive option in summer. The cuisine is both excellent and good value for money, making this restaurant an excellent all-round choice.;Terrace;[]
4565;Alla Pace;Italy;Sauris;via Sauris di Sotto 38, Sauris, 33020, Italy;46.4644403;12.7092398;97;false;true;Friulian, Traditional Cuisine;Sauris is situated in a slightly secluded location which adds to its appeal. Occupying a beautiful 17C house near a charming little lake and picturesque mountain village, this restaurant has been run by the same family since 1804. This enchanting setting acts as the backdrop for a menu featuring delicious regional specialities.;Interesting wine list;[]
4566;La Torre;Italy;Santa Maria Annunziata;piazza Annunziata 7, Santa Maria Annunziata, 80061, Italy;40.6026363;14.3348199;79;false;false;Campanian, Home Cooking;Before sitting down at this restaurant, why not take a short stroll to the nearby viewpoint looking out towards Capri – a perfect prelude to the excellent home-cooked and authentic Campanian cuisine that awaits here. In fact, Capri-style ravioli is one of the most popular dishes at the restaurant, which also serves aubergine parmigiana (highly recommended), potato “gâteau”, and various fish options among the main courses.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4567;Il Latini;Italy;Florence;via dei Palchetti 6 r, Florence, 50123, Italy;43.7716399;11.2493124;56;false;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;True to itself as always, Il Latini is a real Florentine institution, which continues to keep Tuscan traditions alive both in its small, rustic-style dining rooms and in its typical regional cuisine prepared with careful attention to detail and a respectful approach. Florentine steak takes pride of place on the menu, which also features the local hams that hang from the ceiling. Specialities include pappa al pomodoro, Florentine tripe and ribollita stew, as well as cantucci with vin santo, the typical finale to any Tuscan meal. Generations may pass but the appeal of this convivial and welcoming restaurant remains as strong as ever.;Air conditioning;[]
4568;Lokanda Devetak;Italy;Savogna d'Isonzo;via Brezici 22, Savogna d'Isonzo, 34070, Italy;45.8835521;13.5603995;35;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Just two kilometres from the Slovenian border as the crow flies, this restaurant with its dual influences serves top-quality cuisine rooted in the gastronomic traditions of this border region. In business since 1870 and now run by the four children from the sixth generation of the same family, Devetak is an absolute must for anyone visiting the Friuli region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4569;Antiche Sere;Italy;Turin;via Cenischia 9, Turin, 10139, Italy;45.0706512;7.6429555;99;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This renowned osteria situated in a district off the tourist trail is run by attentive and friendly female staff. Its dishes have a regional and traditional focus and are served in three small dining rooms, one of which shares space with the bar. Pleasant outdoor dining in the garden to the rear in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4570;Forma;Italy;Civitavecchia;via Trieste 9, Civitavecchia, 00053, Italy;42.0930835;11.7917883;51;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated away from the sea at the foot of a medieval district, this intimate restaurant boasts a historic decor dotted with modern details such as black parquet flooring and industrial-style pipes. The cuisine created by chef Gianluca Formichella demonstrates the same blend of traditional style and modern touches in imaginative meat and fish dishes with a personalised twist. The tasting menu offers excellent value for money.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4571;Maso Palù;Italy;Brentonico;via Graziani 56, Brentonico, 38060, Italy;45.8126772;10.9400019;80;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Alpine;An annexe to the family farm with its organic apple orchards, this rustic, welcoming restaurant situated on the road leading up towards Monte Baldo has been in business since 1984. Despite its years of experience, the management team here does not rest on its laurels but continues to serve cuisine rooted in regional traditions with just a touch of imagination and modern influence in some dishes. Open every day in summer, but only Friday to Sunday at other times of year.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4572;Coxinendi;Italy;Sanluri;via Sant'Antioco 1, Sanluri, 09025, Italy;39.5638514;8.8975961;68;true;false;Sardinian, Creative;Coxinendi (“cooking” in the Sardinian dialect) is a recently opened restaurant run by talented chef Davide Atzeni, who has plenty of experience behind him. Here, he focuses on creating authentic Sardinian dishes full of traditional flavour.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4573;Agritur El Mas;Italy;Moena;strada de Saslonch 176, località Col de Soldai, Moena, 38035, Italy;46.3835301;11.6620468;49;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Alpine;Situated above the village, this authentic agriturismo raises cows, horses and pigs and produces its own meat, salamis and cheeses, all of which are available online and in its own shop. Other Ladin-inspired specialities from the valley also feature on the menu and are served in an attractive dining room adorned with a profusion of old wood and an open brazier in the middle of the room. While in other restaurants an open-view kitchen may add interest to the dining room, here guests can enjoy views of the cows in their stalls behind a glass screen. Pleasant guestrooms with a focus on “green” construction methods are available in the same building.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4574;Il Sottomarino;Italy;Follonica;via Fratti 1, Follonica, 58022, Italy;42.9219683;10.7550868;70;true;false;Seafood;An elegant dining room and a delightful terrace with sea views – it’s worth making a reservation ahead of time in high season. Excellent fish at reasonable prices, with specialities such as potato gnocchi with baby squid and sage, and mixed fish stew on the menu.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4575;Edelweiss;Italy;Viceno;Località Crodo, Viceno, 28862, Italy;46.22896;8.307799;57;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;A real bastion of local cuisine for over 60 years thanks to the hard work of an entire family. The menu features mountain-style cuisine, including game dishes, a small selection of local cheeses (we highly recommend the Bettelmatt) and home-made ice cream. Relaxed and informal ambience.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
4576;Antica Locanda di Sesto;Italy;Ponte a Moriano;via Ludovica 1660, loc. Sesto di Moriano, Ponte a Moriano, 55100, Italy;43.9242922;10.5267264;97;true;true;Tuscan, Regional Cuisine;The origins of this inn date back to the late 14C, making this one of the Italy’s recognised “Historic Restaurants” – and one that is still flourishing today! The dishes served here are often inspired by Tuscan peasant traditions, while the owner also runs an organic farm which produces wine, vinegar and extra-virgin olive oil. Highlights on the menu include soup with cavolo nero, spaghetti with guanciale (cured pork cheek) served on pecorino cheese, and an array of main courses barbecued on the grill.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4577;Caffè Grande;Italy;Rivergaro;piazza Paolo 9, Rivergaro, 29029, Italy;44.9099838;9.5966921;63;false;false;Emilian, Country cooking;Housed in a charming palazzo with an Art Nouveau façade overlooking the main square of the village, this restaurant has an unexpectedly modern and minimalist-style interior. The menu features an impressive selection of fine local charcuterie (including coppa, pancetta and salami), as well as anolini pasta in broth and ricotta and spinach tortelli. The quality of the meat is outstanding.;Terrace;[]
4578;La Baita;Italy;Faenza;via Naviglio 25/c, Faenza, 48018, Italy;44.2883532;11.8833579;84;true;false;Emilian, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the historic centre, this trattoria-cum-delicatessen focuses on top-quality traditional cuisine. Take a seat in the simple, informal dining room and choose from a vast selection of cheeses and salumi, as well as home-made pasta and meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4579;Osteria Storica Morelli;Italy;Pergine Valsugana;piazza Petrini 1, località Canezza di Pergine, Pergine Valsugana, 38057, Italy;46.0778797;11.2777948;81;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Alpine;The scent of woodsmoke and the cheerful open fire that greet you at this authentic mountain inn tell you all you need to know about the place. The menu features top-quality seasonal ingredients, including delicious maize gnocchi with a ragù made from local game, while the service is friendly and attentive.;Car park;[]
4580;Locanda del Colonnello;Italy;Modica;via Blandini 9, Modica, 97015, Italy;36.8653243;14.7637418;99;true;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;If you like walking, our advice is to approach this restaurant on foot from the lively Corso Umberto, taking the steps up to the Duomo di San Giorgio and then enjoying a pleasant stroll through the alleyways of picturesque Modica Alta, where the restaurant is situated. In this simple setting, the focus here is on the remarkable quality of the cuisine, which includes an eclectic array of Sicilian dishes alongside more creative options, all of which showcase expert technique and stunning flavours.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4581;Vecchia Lama;Italy;Lama Mocogno;via XXIV Maggio 24, Lama Mocogno, 41023, Italy;44.30972;10.73058;26;false;true;Emilian, Meats and Grills;Enjoy a friendly welcome and excellent food in this restaurant that only serves meat dishes. The focus is on mountain specialities from Emilia, as well as truffles in season. Dine alfresco on the terrace overlooking the garden in summer. House specialities include ricotta and nettle tortelloni with porcini mushrooms and the slightly more expensive Fiorentina steak cooked on a hot stone.;Terrace;[]
4582;Dei Cantoni;Italy;Longiano;via Santa Maria 19, Longiano, 47020, Italy;44.0717345;12.3230214;37;true;false;Cuisine from Romagna;Situated in a picturesque historic hamlet with a castle once inhabited by the Malatesta dynasty, this restaurant boasts a charming and traditional dining room. The delicious cuisine is the star of the show here, featuring imaginative dishes showcasing ingredients from the Romagna region, as well as more classic recipes such as pasta with carbonara and amatriciana sauces. All the fresh pasta is home made.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4583;La Bucaccia;Italy;Cortona;via Ghibellina 17, Cortona, 52044, Italy;43.2749644;11.9841148;24;false;false;Tuscan;One of the best places to discover Tuscan cuisine, and that of Arezzo in particular, this restaurant serves exquisite dishes full of flavour. Just a few tables are laid out along the main street in the historic centre, while the two interior dining rooms are rustic and romantic in feel. Friendly and exuberant owner Romano merits a particular mention, providing guaranteed entertainment in between courses.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4584;Osteria dei Segreti;Italy;Appignano;via Verdefiore 25, Appignano, 62010, Italy;43.3777307;13.373358;26;false;false;Cuisine from the Marches, Meats and Grills;Situated amid hills in a secluded and panoramic location, this farmhouse offers guestrooms, a spa and a restaurant, where meat (often cooked over the grill) takes pride of place on the menu, alongside various local specialities such as stuffed pigeon, roast goose and “coniglio in porchetta” (stuffed rabbit).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4585;Dalie e Fagioli;Italy;Manerba del Garda;via Campagnola 45, Manerba del Garda, 25080, Italy;45.55678;10.53301;40;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Having opened this restaurant some ten years ago, owner-chef Fabio draws on all his experience from working at various Michelin-starred restaurants during his career. Using regional produce and local recipes, this technically adept chef creates delicious dishes with an imaginative twist, all accompanied by a discreet choice of wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4586;Lerchner's In Runggen;Italy;Saint Lorenzen;frazione Ronchi 3/a, Saint Lorenzen, 39030, Italy;46.7778091;11.8759349;20;false;false;South Tyrolean, Seasonal Cuisine;Typical of the Alto Adige and situated right next to its own farm from where the beef on its menu is sourced, this restaurant pays careful attention to detail both in its decor (the staff wear local costume) and in its delicious regional cuisine, which is made from the best local ingredients. The house specialities change with the seasons and include geröstl (grilled beef and pork with potatoes, onions and speck ham), tirtlan (rye pancakes), and the unmissable apple strudel. The Alto Adige region also takes centre-stage on the wine list.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4587;La Dispensa di Armatore;Italy;Cetara;via Cantone 1, Cetara, 84010, Italy;40.6461666;14.7015346;24;false;false;Seafood, Campanian;A very small and unusual restaurant with a bistro feel and tables outside only, either at the counter with stools overlooking the sea or in the more traditional outdoor dining space. Although the menu is relatively small, the quality of the fish (including options such as bluefin tuna, anchovies, squid etc) is excellent – which is hardly surprising, as the restaurant owners have been involved in the fishing industry for four generations. The menu features just one dessert, “spumone”, which is made for the restaurant by a nearby artisanal ice-cream parlour, and the restaurant doesn’t serve coffee, but people flock here for the excellent fish and the attractive prices, which are very reasonable given its coastal location.;Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
4588;Da Giocondo;Italy;Rivisondoli;via Suffragio 2, Rivisondoli, 67036, Italy;41.8691706;14.0654103;82;false;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;A simple, rustic trattoria perched among the alleyways in the upper part of the village, where the owners themselves are at the helm in the kitchen and front of house. Delicious home-cooked Abruzzi dishes are to the fore here, with daily specials often announced at your table. The à la carte features specialities such as local cheeses, cured hams and meat dishes (including the region’s renowned arrosticini – skewered grilled meat), as well as traditional home-made pastas, each of which has its own name. The small wine list focuses on the region, with labels from across the province. Booking in advance is recommended.;;[]
4589;Nuova Roma;Italy;Sasso Marconi;via Olivetta 87, Sasso Marconi, 40037, Italy;44.44594;11.19808;46;true;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;A friendly and long-established family-run restaurant on the road between Calderino and Sasso Marconi, which serves generous portions of traditional, regional cuisine with a contemporary flavour. House specialities include fresh pasta, dishes cooked on the authentic wood-fired grill, as well as classic recipes such as Bolognese cutlet. There’s also a comprehensive wine list, with a natural focus on labels from Emilia Romagna. A spacious car park and attractive terrace for summer dining complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4590;Osteria del Gallo e della Volpe;Italy;Ospedaletto d'Alpinolo;piazza Umberto I 14, Ospedaletto d'Alpinolo, 83014, Italy;40.9390634;14.7442689;67;true;false;Campanian, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the centre of this small town is run by the Silvestro family (father and son). In summer, book one of the tables in the charming outdoor space overlooking the square. The menu focuses on local traditional cuisine with the occasional personalised twist, while the wine list features labels from the Irpinia region (and elsewhere) with a good choice of vertical wines and top-quality names such as Aglianico and Taurasi.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4591;Impero;Italy;Sizzano;via Roma 13, Sizzano, 28070, Italy;45.57613;8.43808;23;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Now a culinary landmark in the province, this restaurant is run by two enthusiastic sisters who serve cuisine with its roots in local traditions and prepared using seasonal ingredients. Renovation work over the past few years has added to the style and character of the restaurant, which boasts a small garden for summer dining plus a good selection of wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4592;La Locanda del Falco;Italy;Valdieri;piazza Regina Elena 22, Valdieri, 12010, Italy;44.277054;7.3974799;30;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This is the sort of small family-run restaurant that everyone would like to have as their local, where courteous and friendly service go hand-in-hand with good traditional cuisine. Dishes such as ravioli del plin, vitello tonnato, beef tartare and veal tongue are some of the daily specials marked up on the blackboard here. The wine list comes as a pleasant surprise, with its excellent selection of labels from Piedmont and further afield.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4593;Il Casolare dei Segreti;Italy;Treia;Contrada San Lorenzo 28, Treia, 62010, Italy;43.31765;13.2572;48;true;true;Cuisine from the Marches, Traditional Cuisine;A family - run restaurant with young, enthusiastic staff. Four rustic dining rooms provide the setting to enjoy delicious regional dishes, such as the ever - popular Marchigiana veal steak.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4594;Osteria Platzegg;Italy;San Michele;piazza Municipio 1, San Michele, 39057, Italy;46.4553442;11.2588872;26;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This comfortable and informal “Gasthaus” with a simple yet welcoming and contemporary feel is run by talented chef Herbert Hintner, the undisputed master of Alto Adige cuisine. Housed within a historic building in the town’s pedestrianised centre, the restaurant serves simple cuisine with a focus on regional recipes and ingredients (such as potato ravioli filled with speck ham and spleen crostini in broth) alongside a few Mediterranean-influenced dishes such as arancini in a gorgonzola sauce. The wine list, on the other hand, focuses uniquely on the Alto Adige.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4595;Salotto sul Mare;Italy;Terrasini;via dei Mille 2/b, Terrasini, 90049, Italy;38.1555588;13.0812438;86;false;false;Sicilian, Traditional Cuisine;Steep steps lead up to the first floor of this building, which is home to owner-chef Giuseppe Costa’s main restaurant, Il Bavaglino. Here, the veranda-style dining room boasts spectacular views with the azure sea extending in all directions. The good, honest cuisine is full of flavour and simply prepared from top-quality ingredients, all showcased on an à la carte and three tasting-style menus that are perfect for sharing. In addition to an interesting wine selection, there’s also a choice of cocktails which offer a perfect alternative, even at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
4596;Moi;Italy;Rome;via Antonio Serra 15, Rome, 00191, Italy;41.9436379;12.4723346;56;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Contemporary;Moi is a small yet decidedly smart restaurant which stands out for its quality in the Fleming district in north-west Rome. With years of culinary experience behind him, Thomas uses modern techniques to prepare dishes made from fresh, seasonal ingredients which can change on a daily basis, including meat, fish, vegetables and herbs, all of which are full of flavour and reasonably priced.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4597;Trattoria della Fortuna;Italy;Monterotondo;Via Salaria 57, Monterotondo, 00015, Italy;42.08187;12.6075;72;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This interior of this trattoria occupying an anonymous rural building at a road junction just outside the village comes as something of a surprise. Inside, the dining room has a warm ambience, with a friendly welcome offered by the female staff. The dishes here are authentic and full of flavour, with a focus on regional Italian traditions and top-quality local ingredients – all the pasta and desserts are homemade. We particularly recommend two of the specialities, namely the “Girella e Cartellata” (made using 36 egg yolks) stuffed with ricotta and goat’s cheese and served with a “ciauscolo” (a type of sausage typical of the Marche and Umbria) ragu and a red wine reduction. A small, simple pergola-shaded outdoor space completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4598;Ronchi Rò;Italy;Dolegna del Collio;località Cime di Dolegna 12, Dolegna del Collio, 34070, Italy;46.0236284;13.4866949;15;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;Ronchi Rò is an estate-cum-agriturismo surrounded by the verdant rolling hills and lush woodland of the Collio, a fascinating and enchanting border region famous for its superb wines. Chef Fares Issa’s cuisine is authentic, full of flavour and resolutely seasonal. Although his dishes are influenced by the culinary traditions of the Friuli region, including hams and salamis, goose speck and “frico” (a cheese and potato dish), he also includes the occasional contemporary twist. This is a small and intimate restaurant with just six tables in its attractive, modern dining room, so booking ahead is advisable!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4599;I Tri Siochètt;Italy;Parma;strada Farnese 74, Parma, 43125, Italy;44.7745082;10.2995451;25;false;false;Emilian;Situated just beyond the city’s ring-road, this typical trattoria boasts large dining rooms with a friendly, informal atmosphere. The cuisine showcases the traditions of Parma in delicious, top-quality dishes made from predominantly local ingredients. Not-to-be-missed house specialities include torta fritta (fried pie) with mixed cured meats and zuppa inglese (a kind of trifle).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4600;Rimulas;Italy;Voghera;via Severino Grattoni 8, Voghera, 27058, Italy;44.99336;9.00868;28;true;true;Innovative, Lombardian;At this restaurant situated just a stone’s throw from Piazza Duomo in the historic centre of Voghera, a young chef and his charming wife (who supervises the front of house) are renowned for their reasonably priced excellent cuisine. The chef’s skilfully and imaginatively prepared dishes bear witness to his extensive experience working elsewhere in Italy and further afield. The decor is contemporary, with just a few minimalist-style tables and a hushed ambience.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4601;Ca' d'Frara;Italy;Ferrara;via del Gambero 4, Ferrara, 44121, Italy;44.8363193;11.6226073;30;true;false;Emilian;Tucked away in a corner of the town centre, this restaurant has a small entrance that opens into two bright and airy dining rooms with an elegant feel. The cuisine is typical of Romagna with a focus on home-made pastas and delicious main courses such as tripe alla parmigiana. If you’re not sure what to choose, we suggest opting for the traditional tasting menu which is impressive, both in terms of quality and value for money. Professional yet unfussy service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4602;ChiaroScuro;Italy;Cagliari;corso Vittorio Emanuele II 380, Cagliari, 09123, Italy;39.2206741;9.107065;17;true;true;Sardinian, Traditional Cuisine;In this small neighbourhood restaurant, chef Marina Ravarotto pays tribute to some of Sardinia’s iconic dishes, such as Su Filindeu – a home made pasta very difficult to prepare. The excellent 4-course “Le Radici” menu introduces guests to some of the island’s most typical dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
4603;Mezzolitro Vini e Cucina;Italy;Rho;via Pomè 10, Rho, 20017, Italy;45.5294549;9.042316;52;false;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo;Situated amid the attractive alleyways in the centre of Rho, this simple yet pleasant and friendly restaurant serves delicious local cuisine. Abruzzo specialities are to the fore, including dishes such as spaghetti alla chitarra with meatballs in sauce, various mutton recipes (grilled on skewers, tartare, steaks etc), lamb and different types of ham.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4604;Da Sapì;Italy;Esine;via Giuseppe Mazzini 36, Esine, 25040, Italy;45.9231937;10.2577142;92;false;false;Lombardian, Contemporary;Contemporary-style cuisine with a regional focus and carefully selected local produce are the hallmarks of this restaurant now run by the fourth generation of the same family. The menu features dishes prepared using seasonal vegetables, plus artisanal ice cream made from 100% natural ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4605;Locanda delle Grazie;Italy;Grazie;via San Pio X 2, Grazie, 46010, Italy;45.1564689;10.6940175;38;true;true;Mantuan, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the centre of the charming village of Curtatone which overlooks the river Mincio, this restaurant has been a beacon for fans of Mantuan cuisine for many years. A few Italian favourites feature alongside the local specialities, which include pumpkin tortelli, cured meats, pike with salsa verde and slow-cooked meats, as well as sbrisolona and zabaglione desserts. Simple, yet delicious cuisine, with a focus on home-style cooking and generous portions, all at reasonable prices.;Terrace;[]
4606;L'Ortone;Italy;Florence;piazza Lorenzo Ghiberti 87 r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.770681;11.2674875;75;false;false;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;This Tuscan-style bistro next to Sant'Ambrogio market is simple both in its decor and cuisine, offering a menu which features a few regional dishes alongside imaginative Italian-themed options such as spaghetti with tomato and burrato served with grilled yellow tomatoes. The wine list features impressive regional labels for all budgets, plus there’s a small outdoor space for alfresco dining in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4607;L'Osteria della Trippa;Italy;Rome;via Goffredo Mameli 15, Rome, 00153, Italy;41.8864511;12.4681489;49;true;false;Cuisine from Lazio, Traditional Cuisine;One of the best places in Rome in which to sample the cuisine of Lazio, this restaurant is renowned across the globe for its generous portions of carefully prepared, regional specialities. In addition to the tripe referenced in the restaurant’s name, you’ll also find dishes such as artichokes alla giudia, coratella (lamb offal) and pastas served with the most famous local sauces (amatriciana, carbonara and cacio e pepe) on the menu. Truly delicious!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4609;Vecchia Marina;Italy;Roseto degli Abruzzi;lungomare Trento 37, Roseto degli Abruzzi, 64026, Italy;42.6829548;14.0128495;46;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Vecchia Marina is renowned in the region (and further afield) for its superb fish and seafood and excellent value for money (the tasting menu priced at under 40 euros is truly extraordinary). Situated just a stone’s throw from the beach, the restaurant has a simple, informal feel, where the full focus is on the flavour of the fresh fish served in traditional dishes such as linguine with langoustine, garlic, olive oil and rosemary, and raw fish featuring the catch of the day. As you can imagine, booking well in advance is highly recommended!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4610;La Locanda Gesù Vecchio;Italy;Naples;via Giovanni Paladino 26, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8471624;14.2571093;39;true;true;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated amid the picturesque alleyways of Spaccanapoli, this typical trattoria offers tables set closely together in a simple, informal dining room. Neapolitan cuisine is to the fore here, including popular specialities such as fried mozzarella, aubergine parmigiana, a variety of delicious fried dishes, bean and endive soup, pasta and peas, salted cod, meatballs and pastiera tart. A second restaurant run by the same owners and serving similar cuisine can be found at number 4 on the same street.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4611;Consorzio;Italy;Turin;via Monte di Pietà 23, Turin, 10122, Italy;45.0714727;7.6792853;86;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Despite its simple, no-frills atmosphere, Consorzio serves some of the most interesting and acclaimed Piedmontese cuisine in the city. Specialities include ravioli with either Tumin del Mel cheese or “finanziera”, and traditional meat-filled agnolotti pasta. Meat also makes a strong appearance on the list of main courses, including in less “noble” but equally memorable dishes featuring offal and tripe.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4612;Magazzino 52;Italy;Turin;via Giolitti 52/a, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0631342;7.6928608;21;false;false;Italian Contemporary;This restaurant with characteristic brick-vaulted ceilings has retained the feel of its previous role as a warehouse. Despite the limited choice of dishes on the menu here, there is a strong focus on top-quality ingredients with recipes inspired by the Piedmont as well as the sea. The bottles of wine on display on its shelves can be purchased to take away. All-in-all, an excellent address in one of the city’s most elegant districts.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4613;Oishi;Italy;Teramo;via Mario Capuani 47, Teramo, 64100, Italy;42.660254;13.70142;35;false;true;Japanese, Fusion;East meets West in this attractive restaurant situated in the centre of Teramo. Tribute is paid to Japan in the intimate dining room, where photos of the country adorn the walls and Japanese influences are evident in the fusion cuisine which is prepared using a blend of ingredients from Italy and further afield (raw and marinated dishes, sashimi and nigiri, sushi rolls, tempura etc). The new section entitled “temporary food” has a more seasonal feel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4614;Nerina;Italy;Romeno;via De Gasperi 31, località Malgolo, Romeno, 38010, Italy;46.3805699;11.0936457;79;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Simplicity, hospitality and informality are the keywords to describe this restaurant in the verdant Val di Non, which has been run by the Di Nuzzo family for more than 50 years. Guests come to Nerina time and time again to enjoy excellent Trentino produce, such as the casolèt cheese, Valsugana maize and mortandela salami, as well as its authentic house specialities, often made with ingredients from the restaurant’s own vegetable garden and occasionally with influences from elsewhere in Italy.;Car park,Great view;[]
4615;Ostaria Tyrol;Italy;Moena;piaz de Ramon 8, Moena, 38035, Italy;46.3763283;11.6611421;86;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Regional dishes including home-made pastries and desserts, as well as meat and salumi from the family’s own farm, are to the fore in this typical restaurant with beautiful wooden furnishings created by a local artist. Part of the Post Hotel situated in the centre of the village (in the traffic-limited zone), the restaurant is open non-stop from 11am-10pm and doesn’t take bookings.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4616;Estrò;Italy;Pescara;piazza della Rinascita 23, Pescara, 65122, Italy;42.472985;14.2096135;48;true;false;Contemporary, Country cooking;Boasting a quiet, informal and youthful atmosphere, this restaurant overlooking the main square surprises guests with its simple ideas and impressive culinary technique. It’s immediately obvious from the menu that chef Alfonso Della Croce’s favourite ingredient is meat!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4617;Bros' Trattoria;Italy;Scorrano;SP Scorrano-Supersano km 2, Scorrano, 73020, Italy;40.081012;18.2906161;22;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;Eat amid the verdant surroundings of a large, beautifully kept garden planted with olive trees and embellished with subtle lighting, wooden tables and straw-seated chairs. The highlight here is the wood-fired oven in which nearly all the specialities (available on a single daily menu) are cooked. The strictly traditional dishes include options such as the region’s classic “pucia” bread.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4618;Gerani;Italy;Sant'Antonio Abate;via Stabia 609, Sant'Antonio Abate, 80057, Italy;40.7115883;14.5267472;41;true;true;Italian Contemporary;A journey through colourful inland villages brings you to this restaurant, which serves delicious sourdough bread and home-grown vegetables in its tempting dishes and where a simple, yet friendly welcome awaits. Gerani serves excellent cuisine at reasonable prices, all just a stone’s throw from the main tourist routes.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4619;Podere 39;Italy;Florence;via Senese 39 r, Florence, 50125, Italy;43.7596765;11.2415318;17;true;true;Tuscan, Country cooking;Housing just a few tables (booking is recommended), this restaurant is attractively decorated with an original melting-pot of features which give it a rustic yet elegant feel despite its small size. Some of the ingredients come from the restaurant’s own farm (hence the name “podere”, the Italian for farm), with both meat and fish dishes featuring on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
4620;Da Gregorio;Italy;Morrano Nuovo;strada provinciale 101 136, Morrano Nuovo, 05018, Italy;42.7755985;12.1374042;54;false;true;Umbrian;A family-run trattoria which is simple in style yet offers professional and courteous service. The menu focuses mainly on Umbrian specialities, fresh pasta, grilled dishes and an impressive selection of vegetables.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4621;Coquus;Italy;Lucera;via Luigi Blanch 19, Lucera, 71036, Italy;41.5074929;15.3337179;62;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Apulian;A welcoming contemporary-style restaurant in the town’s historical centre where the young owner-chef has plenty of experience behind him, including in his parents’ restaurant. At Coquus, he serves fresh cuisine which is seasonal, full of flavour and reasonably priced given the quality on offer. Efficient and enthusiastic service, with an outdoor space in the pedestrian area for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4622;Rosmarino;Italy;Genoa;salita del Fondaco 30, Genoa, 16123, Italy;44.4077059;8.9333786;54;false;true;Ligurian;Located just a few metres from Piazza De Ferrari, this restaurant offers an outdoor space and three dining rooms with a pleasant and informal ambience. It is the quality of the cuisine that strikes you at Rosmarino, where the classic Ligurian meat and fish dishes are prepared from top-quality ingredients. Highlights include the “brandacujun” salted cod, the borage ravioli, and the “sbira” tripe.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4623;Locanda Pincelli;Italy;Selva Malvezzi;via Selva 52, Selva Malvezzi, 40062, Italy;44.5560412;11.6275097;56;true;false;Creative, Emilian;Named after the village’s former postman, an important and charismatic character in this small community, this former workers’ club is housed in a rustic restaurant with a beautiful porch where you sit in summer beneath cooling fans. The cuisine steps away from local tradition to offer creative yet never overly fanciful dishes which are always generous and beautifully presented. We particularly enjoyed the mezze maniche pasta with stewed white onion, sour butter and burnt lemon, as well as the leg of guinea fowl browned with paprika, its own juices and horseradish mayonnaise. When choosing your wine, you might like to ask owner Danilo for his recommendations from a list which is not extensive but is certainly interesting and carefully chosen.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4624;Cibus;Italy;Ceglie Messapica;via Chianche di Scarano 7, Ceglie Messapica, 72013, Italy;40.6465;17.51819;73;false;true;Apulian, Country cooking;This restaurant situated in the maze of alleyways that makes up the historic centre of Ceglie boasts tables in a small atmospheric inner courtyard. The restaurant has long been famous for its traditional, regional cuisine and is a must for anyone keen to try typical Puglian specialities. The lamb with roast potatoes is particularly delicious, while the wine list features an interesting selection of regional labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4625;Trattoria al Parco;Italy;Buttrio;via Stretta 7, Buttrio, 33042, Italy;46.0153555;13.3319275;45;true;false;Country cooking, Grills;This elegant house built in brick and stone boasts extensive tree-shaded grounds, a wine cellar next door, plus personalised, welcoming dining rooms. Here, the menu focuses on meat dishes, many of which are cooked over the grill, while the wine list features just a few labels produced by the restaurant’s own winery. A choice of excellent desserts completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4627;Al Cambio;Italy;Bologna;via Stalingrado 150, Bologna, 40128, Italy;44.5286983;11.3668281;46;false;true;Emilian;Despite its out-of-town location, this contemporary, simply decorated restaurant is extremely popular. Fans of traditional cuisine will be in their element here, thanks to the perfectly prepared cuisine which is unfussy yet delicious and full of strong flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4628;Osteria Mondo d'Oro;Italy;Verona;via Mondo d'Oro 4, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.442;10.99624;77;false;true;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;Described as an “osteria” (inn) by its famous, multi-Michelin-starred chef Giancarlo Perbellini, this restaurant provides a relaxed setting in which to enjoy delicious (and reasonably priced) Italian cuisine, including a few vegetarian options. Choose between the cosy dining room and an outdoor space (weather permitting) in a side street off the central Via Mazzini.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4629;Trattoria da Zamboni;Italy;Lapio;via Santa Croce 73, Lapio, 36057, Italy;45.47452;11.5357;60;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Situated in the Berici hills, this restaurant run by a friendly and welcoming family boasts views of the surrounding greenery from its first-floor dining rooms. Although the cuisine focuses on local ingredients (in other words, mainly meat), the menu also includes a particularly delicious baccalà alla vicentina (salted cod).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4630;Trattoria di Via Serra;Italy;Bologna;via Luigi Serra 9/b, Bologna, 40129, Italy;44.5097151;11.3455818;40;false;true;Emilian;It’s well worth heading off the traditional tourist trail to experience this simple and informal trattoria in Bolognina, the city’s historic working-class district which now has a very multicultural feel. Run by a friendly owner, with his talented business partner at the helm in the kitchen, the restaurant boasts a welcoming and friendly ambience that has made it popular, so booking ahead is recommended, even at lunchtime. Top-quality regional cuisine is celebrated here, from fresh pasta (excellent tortellini in broth) to zuppa inglese (a type of trifle).;Air conditioning;[]
4631;Il Ritrovo d'Abruzzo;Italy;Civitella Casanova;Contrada Bosco 16, Civitella Casanova, 65010, Italy;42.4057508;13.8937726;89;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;If you’re not already in the area, it takes time to get to this family-run restaurant situated amid the rolling hills of rural Abruzzo, but the journey through some of the most beautiful scenery in the region more than compensates for the effort. Two brothers are at the helm (one front of house, the other in the kitchen), serving traditional regional cuisine often prepared using home-grown vegetables and with the occasionally more creative dish featuring on the menu. A pleasant outdoor space for summer dining completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4632;Me Cumpari Turiddu;Italy;Catania;piazza Turi Ferro 36, Catania, 95124, Italy;37.506428;15.088407;100;true;false;Sicilian;With its old chandeliers, chairs and tables, this original and attractive restaurant offers its guests a feel of traditional Sicily. The cuisine focuses on typical Sicilian specialities, as well as offering a simpler, less expensive bistro menu. There’s also a shop selling food produce and a cocktail bar, which is open non-stop from 11. 30am until the early hours of the morning.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4633;Antica Filanda;Italy;Capri Leone;SS 157, contrada Raviola, Capri Leone, 98070, Italy;38.08595;14.734261;29;true;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Although the view from this restaurant takes in the sea and the mountains alike, it’s the latter that inspires the menu. It features inland specialities cooked with the best local ingredients. Suckling pig is a particular favourite, appearing in a number of different guises, including cured ham and meat sauces. The restaurant also offers new, welcoming guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4634;Vögele;Italy;Bolzano;via Goethe 3, Bolzano, 39100, Italy;46.4991536;11.3524552;29;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is a Bolzano institution. It is a typical inn whose origins are lost in the mists of time, and is still furnished in traditional Biedermeier - style. The menu focuses on regional cuisine, with an occasional hint of the Mediterranean.;Terrace;[]
4635;Antica Fattoria del Grottaione;Italy;Castel del Piano;via della Piazza, località Montenero d'Orcia, Castel del Piano, 58033, Italy;42.94457;11.47218;88;true;false;Tuscan;Once a farm, this trattoria has an attractive rustic feel with colourful decor in the dining room and stunning panoramic views from the outdoor terrace in summer. House specialities include il peposo (braised beef with black pepper).;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4636;La Pignata;Italy;Ariano Irpino;viale Dei Tigli 7, Ariano Irpino, 83031, Italy;41.1569021;15.0947663;85;true;false;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;For over 40 years the Ventre family have been championing the flavours of Irpinia, seeking out the region’s best seasonal ingredients. These are then used in traditional dishes such as soups, as well as in more personal reinterpretations of local specialities (their “post-modern” arancino is now renowned in the region) that nonetheless retain all their original flavour with influences from both Campania and Puglia. The pizza here is excellent and there’s also a good selection of wine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4637;Il Turacciolo;Italy;Andria;piazza Vittorio Emanuele II 4, Andria, 76123, Italy;41.2259495;16.2967455;42;false;true;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;This informal wine bar in the town centre features paper tablecloths and a menu chalked up on two blackboards. Delicious regional cuisine, including the occasional dish with surprisingly modern and imaginative flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4638;Da Felice;Italy;Chiavari;corso Valparaiso 136, Chiavari, 16043, Italy;44.3177211;9.3145164;17;false;true;Ligurian, Seafood;This welcoming restaurant, in business for many years now, boasts an open-view kitchen to the rear of the dining room. The menu here focuses on fish from the daily market which is prepared in different traditional ways, including carpaccio, fried and oven-baked dishes. Prices are reasonable on the whole, while the short tasting menu offers excellent value for money. A fresh, cool outdoor space adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4639;Trattoria da Probo;Italy;Bagnolo in Piano;via Provinciale Nord 13, Bagnolo in Piano, 42011, Italy;44.7792987;10.6762816;37;true;true;Emilian, Classic Cuisine;A bulwark of traditional local cuisine, this trattoria serves antipasti such as erbazzone (a savoury pie), fried gnocchi and charcuterie, followed by fresh pasta (the cappelletti in broth are excellent), a choice of boiled and roast meat dishes, plus a selection of desserts. Chalked up on a blackboard by the entrance, the daily specials are also classic in style and vary depending on whatever is available in the market that day. Booking ahead is recommended!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4640;Alla Pasina;Italy;Dosson;via Marie 3, Dosson, 31030, Italy;45.6289367;12.2558509;70;false;true;Venetian, Modern Cuisine;In this beautiful, warm and welcoming country house, fresh pasta dishes take up much of the space on the menu – and deservedly so: whether you opt for more traditional or creative dishes, the pasta here is excellent. The region’s famous chicory also makes an appearance, alongside a selection of meat and fish dishes. Guestrooms are available for visitors looking to extend their stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4641;CUCINA.eat;Italy;Cagliari;piazza Galileo Galilei 1, Cagliari, 09128, Italy;39.2202729;9.1223668;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine;One of the most interesting restaurants in Cagliari in terms of value for money, with a choice of classic at-table seating or the more informal, convivial option of sitting at the counter. When it comes to choosing your wine, all you need do is look around at the shelves and ask the helpful staff for recommendations. The cuisine focuses on Sardinian recipes and ingredients, as well as more classic options and even experimental dishes that feature new and original combinations. Simpler options are available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4642;L'Acquario;Italy;Castiglione del Lago;via Vittorio Emanuele 69, Castiglione del Lago, 06061, Italy;43.1271351;12.0518678;65;true;true;Umbrian, Traditional Cuisine;Located in the historic centre of an attractive village by the lake, this restaurant is a good option for anyone wanting to try Umbrian cuisine. Dishes made from freshwater fish (pike, carp, tench, eel and crayfish), as well as the famous beans from Lake Trasimeno and meat such as lamb and wild boar, take pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4643;Nole;Italy;Pescara;viale Regina Margherita 84, Pescara, 65123, Italy;42.4752574;14.2057343;95;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Italian;Situated near the seafront in one of Pescara’s iconic streets, Nole offers guests two different dining options: the bar-bistro section serves excellent breakfasts, light lunches and snacks (closed in the evening), while the minimalist, contemporary-style dining room is home to the main restaurant. The two sections are separated by the open-view kitchen, where the chefs prepare classic, modern meat and fish dishes, with a focus on whatever ingredients are available in the market that day.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4644;L'Ostreria Fratelli Pavesi;Italy;Podenzano;Località Gariga 8, Podenzano, 29027, Italy;44.9839886;9.6846769;37;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Overlooking a 20C courtyard typical of the Bassa Padana area, this restaurant’s name (a play on the word “osteria”) refers to the three (“tre”) brothers who share the work in the kitchen and front of house. It’s clear that the saying “many hands make light work” holds true here: the many dishes served in this simple, friendly dining room include local specialities such as cured hams, salumi, anolini pasta, ricotta and spinach tortelli and “bomba di riso” (a moulded rice dish), as well as main courses of venison and sturgeon and a delicious “zuppa inglese” (trifle) for dessert. Booking ahead is recommended, even for a weekday lunch, as it gets very busy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4645;Osteria dei Maltagliati;Italy;Torano Nuovo;corso Umberto I 36, Torano Nuovo, 64010, Italy;42.8231884;13.7770664;43;false;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;With a very young team led by Maicol and Federica, this rustic restaurant with an exposed-brick decor only opened a few months ago and has already made a name for itself thanks to its fine cuisine. In the dining room, the wood-fired oven and barbecue grill (the latter uses the embers from the former) take centre stage in many of the dishes, so that old, culinary techniques result in delicious cuisine that demonstrates a fine balance of traditional flavours and personalised modern twists. The lamb chops, served with freshly blanched saltwort flavoured with preserved lemon and a light garlic sauce, were truly delicious!;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4646;Osteria Ophis;Italy;Offida;corso Serpente Aureo 54/b, Offida, 63073, Italy;42.9355659;13.6924987;55;false;true;Cuisine from the Marches, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the beautiful historic pedestrianised centre of Offida, this restaurant with a brick-vaulted ceiling is housed in the former stables of an old palazzo with a modern, inviting and intimate feel. Here, owner-chef Daniele Citeroni Maurizi skilfully reinterprets regional cuisine to create precise, imaginative dishes that are full of flavour. The stuffed cannelloni cooked on the barbecue grill are delicious, as is the veal tartare served with a warm meat, herb and vegetable jus on the side. We should also highlight the “low cost” tasting menu available for guests aged under 25.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4647;Al Borgo;Italy;Belluno;via Anconetta 8, Belluno, 32100, Italy;46.1250037;12.2116816;98;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Housed within an 18C villa in a small traditional hamlet, this restaurant with a warm rustic ambience serves regional cuisine. The Gioie del Borgo (home produced salami and sausages), barley and bean soup, and homemade ice cream are all highly recommended.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4648;Gassenwirt;Italy;Kiens;via Paese 42, Kiens, 39030, Italy;46.8092067;11.8414858;77;false;false;Country cooking, Home Cooking;Situated next to the village church, this restaurant has been serving excellent South Tyrolean cuisine since as far back as 1602. House specialities include canederli pressati (dumplings) and Buchteln (a type of sweet bun).;Car park;[]
4649;La Gioconda;Italy;Cagli;via Brancuti, Cagli, 61043, Italy;43.5461484;12.6474362;15;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the historic centre, this restaurant pays tribute to the Cagli region and the Marche hinterland. Dishes feature the best local ingredients, such as truffles in season (both black and white), as well as a dessert in memory of local sculptor Eliseo Mattiacci (the “fabbrica del cosmo” made with yoghurt, wafers and strawberries). The wine list shows a strong preference for the Marche, but also features wines from further afield.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4650;Osteria La Torre;Italy;Cherasco;via dell'Ospedale 22, Cherasco, 12062, Italy;44.6516877;7.8570495;80;false;false;Piedmontese;To get to this welcoming restaurant, it’s best to leave the car in one of the convenient car parks just outside the town walls a short walk from Cherasco’s quiet, picturesque historic centre with its two perpendicular streets. At Osteria La Torre, the friendly female staff will happily guide you through the menu, which features traditional dishes prepared in contemporary style – we particularly enjoyed the egg, cardoon and fondue dish, followed by breaded veal rump as our main course. If you’re a fan of snails, you really must try them here as Cherasco is renowned for this speciality. The extensive wine list demonstrates the same high quality as the cuisine.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4651;Perbacco - Vini e Cucina;Italy;Cannara;via Umberto I 14, Cannara, 06033, Italy;42.9952602;12.5831366;18;true;false;Umbrian;This restaurant began life as a wine - bar, before transforming into an establishment where you can enjoy genuine local cuisine. The onion reigns supreme in this eatery! Two cosy rooms, with frescoed walls.;;[]
4652;Trattoria Porteri;Italy;Brescia;via Trento 52/d, Brescia, 25128, Italy;45.5536988;10.2245503;70;true;true;Lombardian, Regional Cuisine;Situated outside the centre in the equally typical and historic Borgo Trento district, this restaurant has all the warm ambience and character that you would expect of a traditional trattoria. The regional cuisine includes a remarkable array of charcuterie, as well as dishes such as tripe in Brescia-style broth, beef in olive oil and the typical local bocciolo di rosa dessert with zabaglione ice-cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4653;Al Becco della Civetta;Italy;Castelmezzano;vico I Maglietta 7, Castelmezzano, 85010, Italy;40.52995;16.0463;92;true;true;Cuisine from Basilicata;The owner - chef of this restaurant in a small village nestling in the Lucane Dolomites focuses on regional cuisine, serving dishes inspired by her two muses – her mother and grandmother. Dishes are often announced at your table and specialities include the delicious ficotto (fig wine). Stunning views of the grandiose mountain scenery from the guestrooms, which are quiet and welcoming.;Air conditioning;[]
4654;Da Fausto;Italy;Cavatore;Località Valle Prati 1, Cavatore, 15010, Italy;44.63598;8.44158;30;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;With Fausto front of house, his wife Rosella at the helm in the kitchen and daughter Gaia who not only works in the dining room but is also responsible for the desserts, this restaurant celebrates Piedmontese cuisine on a menu that changes weekly in order to ensure that ingredients are fresh and seasonal. Meat takes centre stage, alongside excellent fresh pasta dishes (such as the famous agnolotti) and delicious desserts including fiordilatte ice-cream. The wine cellar is well stocked, thanks to the restaurant’s own production of Pinot Nero (dry and sparkling labels), while for anyone wanting to prolong their stay, attractive guestrooms are available at the Borgo del Gallo.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4655;Borgo Poscolle;Italy;Cavazzo Carnico;via Poscolle 21/a, Cavazzo Carnico, 33020, Italy;46.36565;13.03708;58;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Home - style cooking with a focus on regional specialities is served in this attractive family - run trattoria, which has its own organic vegetable garden and an educational "pet therapy" farm. The search for ingredients produced as close to home as possible is something of an obsession with the owner - chef, who is also passionate about his desserts. Make sure you try the millefeuille with strawberries and cream.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4657;Osteria San Giulio;Italy;Badia di Dulzago;Via Dulzago, Badia di Dulzago, 28043, Italy;45.55002;8.6128;76;true;true;Piedmontese, Country cooking;With its delightful location in an old rural abbey, warm welcome, friendly atmosphere and excellent “home-style” cuisine which focuses on the region’s classic dishes, this restaurant appeals to all the senses. Tastings of cured hams and cheeses from the surrounding area can be arranged in the beautiful garden by prior arrangement.;Air conditioning;[]
4658;Kanton Restaurant;Italy;Capriate San Gervasio;via Antonio Gramsci 17, Capriate San Gervasio, 24042, Italy;45.6111527;9.5270194;32;true;true;Chinese, Modern Cuisine;Capriate is home to one of the best Chinese restaurants in the region and beyond. Although Cantonese specialities take centre stage here, the menu also features dishes from elsewhere in China, including a remarkable selection of cooked and stuffed dumplings. If you want an all-round Chinese experience, there’s also a good choice of teas. The desserts tend to be more European in style.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4659;Sot'Ajarchi;Italy;Ancona;via Marconi 93, Ancona, 60125, Italy;43.6109808;13.5037316;45;false;false;Seafood, Cuisine from the Marches;An informal atmosphere in a small trattoria where you can really feel at ease, perhaps in company, eating tasty seafood dishes, based on the daily fish catch.;Air conditioning;[]
4660;Il Moro;Italy;Capriata d'Orba;piazza Garibaldi 7, Capriata d'Orba, 15060, Italy;44.7299093;8.6888831;15;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Occupying a 17C palazzo in the village centre, this restaurant showcases regional cuisine in all its glory, including specialities such as leek and saffron gnocchi, boiled tongue, pumpkin in the autumn and truffles in season, all accompanied by wines chosen from an extensive wine list. Friendly, informal service, plus an open fire in winter.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4661;Osteria Bartolini;Italy;Milano Marittima;via A. Boito 26, Milano Marittima, 48015, Italy;44.2683552;12.3569147;48;false;true;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;Fish and seafood take centre stage at this restaurant facing the beach and its moored boats, with a menu that showcases classic specialities from the Adriatic, including fried options and daily specials in line with what’s available at Cesenatico fish market. The restaurant does not take reservations.;Terrace;[]
4662;Accademia Ristorante;Italy;Casale Monferrato;via Mameli 29, Casale Monferrato, 15033, Italy;45.1364114;8.4533279;88;true;true;Country cooking;The Inspector's thought was: too bad it's not in my neighborhood, I would come more often! In a historic building, with a classic decor and magnificent frescoed dining rooms, Accademia serves simple but well personalized and surprisingly modern Piedmontese cuisine. The friendly owner will welcome you graciously and provide you with relevant and passionate wine recommendations.;;[]
4663;Trattoria Pennestri;Italy;Rome;via Giovanni Da Empoli 5, Rome, 00154, Italy;41.8734074;12.479981;84;false;true;Cuisine from Lazio, Seasonal Cuisine;An authentic neighbourhood trattoria with just one difference – it is so good that its fame has travelled far beyond the streets of Ostiense in which it is situated and so it is often crowded (as a result, booking is highly recommended). The atmosphere is simple, informal and attractive, while the cuisine focuses on Roman classics such as pasta with carbonara, cacio e pepe, amatriciana and gricia sauces, alongside a few more creative dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4664;Caffè La Crepa;Italy;Isola Dovarese;piazza Matteotti 14, Isola Dovarese, 26031, Italy;45.1760808;10.3123463;96;true;true;Lombardian;Overlooking a picturesque Renaissance square, the café here dates back to the early 19C and the trattoria shortly after. Today, the decor is a nostalgic mix of styles from the mid-19C to the mid-20C, including Art Nouveau. The restaurant not only appeals to the eyes but also to the tastebuds thanks to its careful selection of top-quality local ingredients which are served in family-style dishes typical of the Po Valley, with a broad selection of recipes from the different provinces in this extensive region (stuffed marubini pasta in broth, culatello ham, boiled meats served with home-made mostarda etc). There’s also a boutique selling food and wine for anyone looking for a souvenir to take home.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4665;Osteria Bartolini;Italy;Cesenatico;corso Garibaldi 41, Cesenatico, 47042, Italy;44.200314;12.396823;66;false;true;Seafood;The sister restaurant of the Bologna and Milano Marittima restaurants of the same name, this osteria serves fresh fish with an excellent choice of delicious and generously portioned dishes. As the restaurant doesn’t take bookings, make sure you get here early in high season or during busy periods.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4666;Dentella;Italy;Bracca;via Dentella 25, Bracca, 24010, Italy;45.8233063;9.7074027;44;false;false;Country cooking;Situated in a picturesque village in the Val Serina, this family-run restaurant has a welcoming ambience. The menu features a small selection of mostly local dishes, including specialities such as bresaola orobica, cured hams and cheeses, casoncelli pasta, mushrooms and, of course, polenta prepared in different ways (Bergamo or Taragna style, simply, with strachitunt cheese, or with fried eggs). Enjoy dining on the panoramic terrace in fine weather.;Terrace;[]
4667;Gabbiano 1983;Italy;Corte de' Cortesi;piazza Vittorio Veneto 10, Corte de' Cortesi, 26020, Italy;45.2724821;10.0072355;98;true;false;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;Having successfully been in business for over 40 years, this restaurant continues to shine for its top-quality traditional cuisine, priding itself, as it has always done, on its love for local specialities. Goose dishes take centre stage on the menu (the area is famous for its goose), alongside an excellent selection of traditional boiled meats all of which are sourced locally. There’s also a good choice of wine, which is skilfully displayed and served from a trolley in the dining room from which wines are served by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4668;Futura Osteria;Italy;Monteriggioni;largo Garfonda 10, località Abbadia Isola, Monteriggioni, 53035, Italy;43.3872152;11.1951088;51;true;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;Situated along the Via Francigena near Monteriggioni the small medieval village of Abbadia Isola boasts a superb Romanesque church and a group of old buildings that once housed a monastery and its outbuildings. The Futura Osteria occupies the cellars where the monks once stored their wines, which now provides the setting for simple, delicious and resolutely seasonal Tuscan-inspired cuisine offering good value for money. The refined wine list, simple service and secluded terrace complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4669;Ahimè;Italy;Bologna;via San Gervasio 6/e, Bologna, 40121, Italy;44.4966213;11.337969;69;true;false;Country cooking;Situated near the typical Mercato delle Erbe, Ahimé serves imaginative regional cuisine with a careful focus on seasonal, sustainably produced ingredients. Organic wines, plus service which is friendly yet at the same time professional add to its appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
4670;Vascello d'Oro;Italy;Carrù;via San Giuseppe 9, Carrù, 12061, Italy;44.4796072;7.8784919;51;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;In business since 1887, this restaurant with warm traditional decor is situated in the town famous for bue grasso (“fat ox”), which you’ll find on the menu here from November to Easter. Enjoy typical, popular dishes from the Piedmont, such as meat and vegetable filled ravioli, finanziera stew, fried dishes, Russian salad and, of course, the famous boiled meats, all skilfully prepared in the traditional way. Desserts such as hazelnut cake and bonet provide a final flourish for the tastebuds.;Air conditioning;[]
4671;Romanè;Italy;Rome;via Cipro 106, Rome, 00136, Italy;41.9058387;12.4451294;29;true;false;Roman, Cuisine from Lazio;Situated close to the Vatican, this is one of the best trattorias in Rome, with simple decor and just one, usually very busy, dining room (booking ahead is recommended), as well as delicious cuisine from Lazio. Dishes include artichokes (both Roman- and Jewish-style), pasta with rich local sauces, offal specialities (“quinto quarto”), and delicious roast meats among the main courses. For dessert, we recommend the chocolate “tenerina” cake or the ricotta with sour cherries.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4672;Osteria del Miglio 2.10;Italy;Pieve San Giacomo;via Patrioti 2, Pieve San Giacomo, 26035, Italy;45.13071;10.18788;66;true;false;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;Although the town may not be of major importance, the cuisine served at this modern restaurant (with a convenient car park) certainly is! Focusing on traditional local recipes and using seasonal ingredients, the carefully prepared dishes are both generous and full of flavour. Fair prices complete the picture and make this a restaurant a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4673;Osteria Bartolini;Italy;Bologna;piazza Malpighi 16, Bologna, 40123, Italy;44.4939376;11.3364404;59;false;false;Seafood;The entrance to this restaurant has an almost aristocratic feel thanks to its location in a beautiful palazzo with an attractive outdoor space for summer dining. Fish and seafood take centre stage at the Osteria Bartolini – peruse the menu for the à la carte but don’t forget to consult the interesting daily specials online via the QR code (the catch of the day is supplied by fishermen from Milano Marittima and Cervia). Don’t miss the different versions of Adriatic fritto misto (fried fish), all of which are interesting and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4674;Antichi Sapori;Italy;Montegrosso;piazza Sant'Isidoro 10, Montegrosso, 76123, Italy;41.1722059;16.1411084;56;false;false;Apulian;For the past thirty years, this fine restaurant with a charming and beautifully kept dining room has been serving regional dishes from the Murge, all prepared using top-quality ingredients. The desserts, in particular, are truly delicious and not to be missed. Given the restaurant’s popularity in the region, booking is highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4675;Da Alighiero;Italy;Anghiari;via Garibaldi 8, Anghiari, 52031, Italy;43.54092;12.05549;31;true;true;Tuscan;Hidden in the picturesque centre of Anghiari (famous for the battle with which it shares a name), Da Alighiero serves delicious cuisine prepared by chef Silvia. Highlights include bringoli (an elongated local variety of egg pasta) served with a meat ragu or mushrooms in season, as well as the region’s typical meat dishes, such as tripe in a spicy red sauce and pan-fried liver with sage and white wine.;Air conditioning;[]
4676;Namo Ristobottega;Italy;Tarquinia;via Giovan Battista Marzi 1, Tarquinia, 01016, Italy;42.2506881;11.7555304;95;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;This simple, tiny restaurant stands just outside the walls of Tarquinia, barely a kilometre from the splendid necropolis of Monterozzi (UNESCO World Heritage Site). The female owner-chef pays tribute to the Viterbo region with her imaginative use of seasonal ingredients in light dishes which are full of flavour, while the à la carte demonstrates a wide use of vegetables. The outdoor space offers views extending as far as the coast.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4677;Laghetto;Italy;Brusson;rue Trois Villages 291, Brusson, 11022, Italy;45.7609563;7.7213729;60;false;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Italian;If you’re not already in the area, on exiting the motorway drive up the Val d’Ayas to reach the delightful village of Brusson at an altitude of 1 300m. Here, in the typical mountain-style dining rooms of the Laghetto hotel-restaurant, enjoy delicious local specialities such as cured meats, cheeses, polenta, trout, and plenty of meat options.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4678;Magnagallo;Italy;Campogalliano;via Magnagallo Est 7, Campogalliano, 41011, Italy;44.6775617;10.8520227;94;true;false;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant decorated in typical local style welcomes guests with a mouthwatering display of cakes. But before you move on to dessert, enjoy local specialities such as tortellini in a capon broth and Emilian-style “fritto misto”. The classic accompaniment to a traditional meal in Modena is an excellent Lambrusco – we enjoyed a fresh Reggiano full of intense flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4679;Aciniello;Italy;Campobasso;via Torino 4, Campobasso, 86100, Italy;41.5597957;14.6568008;52;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A simple, authentic trattoria with a family atmosphere and two small dining rooms. One is quieter than the other with bright colours and tables arranged close together. The restaurant’s popularity with locals and the friendly nature of the owners give it a lively atmosphere. Regional specialities on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4680;Osteria Expanificio;Italy;Agrigento;piazza Sinatra 16, Agrigento, 92100, Italy;37.3108491;13.5763684;84;false;true;Sicilian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the historic centre between the Pirandello theatre and the belvedere, this former bakery has been transformed into a modern, welcoming restaurant, with models of bread and rolls on the walls recalling its previous life. The menu features a selection of some of the island’s most famous dishes, including stuffed sardines, Robiola goat’s cheese ravioli, caponata and “involtino alla Siciliana” (Sicilian veal rolls).;Terrace;[]
4681;Osteria Magona;Italy;Bolgheri;Località Vallone dei Messi 199, SP 16/b km 2,400, Bolgheri, 57020, Italy;43.2187801;10.611003;50;false;true;Tuscan, Meats and Grills;You are certain to fall for the charm of this rural restaurant, whose excellent value for money attracts food - lovers from far and wide. Situated among olive groves and vineyards, the Osteria Magona serves a whole host of meat specialities with tartare, beef delicacies and roast dishes all featuring on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4682;Locanda del Barone;Italy;Caramanico Terme;Località San Vittorino, Caramanico Terme, 65023, Italy;42.1438896;13.9941646;37;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo;Situated in a district of Caramanico, this typical stone house is home to an attractive restaurant that is the perfect choice for anyone keen on typical Abruzzo specialities. Prepared from regional ingredients, the dishes are delicious and substantial.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4683;Ai Burattini;Italy;Adrara San Martino;via Madaschi 45, Adrara San Martino, 24060, Italy;45.6996073;9.9481459;71;true;true;Country cooking;This restaurant just a few kilometres from Lake Iseo is one of the best addresses in the region for local cuisine, featuring fish from the lake and local meat dishes. One meal here is not enough given all the tempting dishes on the menu, including Bergamo-style mutton, dried sardines and trout from the lake, meatballs, home-made casoncelli (stuffed pasta) and the delicious baked rabbit served with Rovetta polenta. As well as the desserts, there’s also a good selection of local cheeses.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4684;Locanda Mariella;Italy;Calestano;località Fragnolo 29, Calestano, 43030, Italy;44.586742;10.158748;90;false;false;Emilian, Modern Cuisine;You need to book at least 24hrs in advance at this restaurant by sending an email and your choice of the three menus on offer (traditional, meat or fish). This long-established, legendary restaurant is one of the best trattorias in the province, if not the region. Still run by the same family, it has been delighting guests in this corner of the Apennines since the 1960s.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4685;Da Pode;Italy;San Gimignano;località Sovestro 63, San Gimignano, 53037, Italy;43.4598625;11.0596245;98;true;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant occupies an old far that has retained some of the architectural features typical of its rural past. It serves delicious Tuscan cuisine prepared by Signora Lucia. If you are on a diet, beware!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4686;Battaglino;Italy;Bra;piazza Roma 18, Bra, 12042, Italy;44.6937542;7.8505723;79;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant run by an enthusiastic and friendly family (now joined by the fourth generation) has been serving traditional Piedmontese cuisine since 1919. The outdoor dining space is particularly charming when the wisteria is in bloom.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4687;Palazzaccio;Italy;Castelbuono;via Umberto I 23, Castelbuono, 90013, Italy;37.9317244;14.0876011;63;false;true;Sicilian, Country cooking;A simple, almost rustic restaurant in the pedestrianised historic centre of one of the medieval villages that add to the special attraction of the Parco delle Madonie. Here, the owner prepares seasonal cuisine which is firmly anchored in the region, made from ingredients from the surrounding area. The antipasto is always good, and is served as a selection of five or six small bites made from vegetables, cheese and meat, as well as mushrooms. The home-made bread is excellent – the natural leavening process takes almost four days. A good wine selection completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4688;Boccondivino;Italy;Bra;via Mendicità Istruita 14, Bra, 12042, Italy;44.6961302;7.8551043;63;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is accessed via the internal courtyard of a typical period building, where meals are served alfresco in summer. The menu features a delicious array of Piedmontese specialities, including Bra’s famous sausage, “40-yolk” tajarin pasta, Carmagnola rabbit and “bonet” (a soft, creamy dessert). The simple, informal dining rooms tend to fill up quickly, so booking ahead is recommended, even at lunchtime. This is where the Slow Food movement began!;Terrace;[]
4689;Il Fiorile;Italy;Borghetto di Borbera;via XXV Aprile 6, frazione Castel Ratti, Borghetto di Borbera, 15060, Italy;44.7240966;8.9516851;79;true;false;Piedmontese;A picture - postcard hay barn immersed in the silence of the woods provides the perfect setting to sample traditional recipes. Choose from specialities such as Montebore flan with acacia honey, tajarin pasta with black truffles and apple crème caramel with Moscato granita.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
4690;Osteria La Pimpinella;Italy;Bra;Via San Rocco 70, Bra, 12042, Italy;44.6960382;7.84972;20;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Situated in the historic centre but near a square with a car park, this modern inn serves Piedmontese cuisine which is contemporary in style yet still firmly anchored in local traditions. The generously portioned, well-presented dishes on the menu include vitello tonnato (excellent – we tried it!), tajarin pasta, Bra sausage and casseroles (the soft suckling pig cheek was delicious), all of which are as much a feast for the eyes as for the palate. The restaurant is run by an enthusiastic couple, aided by proficient and courteous staff with a feminine touch.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4692;Violetta;Italy;Calamandrana;via Valle San Giovanni 1, Calamandrana, 14042, Italy;44.750548;8.3211782;90;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;At this family restaurant, the daughter is now at the helm in the kitchen, having taken over from her grandmother a few years ago, while her parents oversee the dining room where the rather old-fashioned 1960s decor is brightened by their attentive service. The menu continues to focus on traditional Piedmontese dishes (especially from Monferrato) cooked in a simple, almost homely style, including specialities such as veal with a tuna sauce (usually known as vitello tonnato), agnolotti monferrini (a type of ravioli), tajarin with porcini mushrooms, finanziera stew, and torroncino parfait. The wine list has the same regional focus as the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4693;Il Cedro;Italy;Moggiona;via di Camaldoli 20, Moggiona, 52014, Italy;43.7828245;11.791567;64;true;true;Tuscan;A few kilometres from the monastery of Camaldoli, Il Cedro celebrates home-style Tuscan cooking, which is simple yet full of flavour. Two sisters are at the helm here: one in the kitchen, and the other offering friendly service front of house, where she announces the daily specials at your table. Fresh produce and specialities from the Casentino are to the fore.;;[]
4694;53 Untitled;Italy;Rome;via del Monte della Farina 53, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8951741;12.4749758;94;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Italian;Situated in the heart of historic Rome not far from Piazza Navona, this small, simple restaurant with just a few tables serves excellent cuisine (booking ahead is recommended). Apart from a few classic dishes from Lazio, most of the options here are more creative, occasionally even with an Asian twist. The tapas-style “morsi e morsetti” (light bites) which head the menu can be ordered as appetisers or main courses, and are followed by a selection of pastas, salumi, cheeses and desserts.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4696;Mika;;Abu Dhabi;Building 7, Yas Marina, Yas Island, Abu Dhabi;24.4657466;54.6092967;19;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;You can taste the Riviera at this lively restaurant in Yas Marina. Appealing and sophisticated, it’s tastefully designed and offers terrace seating - perfect for alfresco dining during cooler winter months. Expect a well-priced Mediterranean-inspired menu with noteworthy specials and vibrant dishes that are as fresh as they are full of flavour. Their breads are freshly baked in-house, they cure their own salmon and even make their own limoncello! Leave some room for 'Nonna's' tiramisu, you won't regret it. The attentive and friendly team add to the warm Mediterranean experience.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4700;Almayass;;Abu Dhabi;Galleria Mall Level 1, Al Maryah Island, Abu Dhabi;24.501757;54.3881576;59;true;false;Lebanese, Armenian;Almayass is where Lebanese and Armenian cuisine meet influences from around the Mediterranean. The original was founded in Beirut in 1996 and this large Abu Dhabi branch, where the circular booths are the prized seats, continues the tradition of offering an extensive and appealing menu of richly flavoured and carefully prepared dishes. Try the Kibbeh karaz, a wonderful marriage of lamb and cherries.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4701;Otoro;;Abu Dhabi;Al Qana Marina South, Al Maqta' Street, Abu Dhabi;24.4027124;54.4933832;82;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;This friendly, contemporary Japanese spot is perfect for a bite to eat when visiting the nearby National Aquarium in Al Qana. The space has a relaxed, funky feel and is dominated by a large open kitchen to watch the team in action. The experienced chef, under the aegis of consultant-chef Akmal Anuar from 11 Woodfire in Dubai, has a diligent brigade supporting him. Ingredients are flown in from various prefectures of Japan, like wagyu from Kagoshima, otoro from Tokyo and uni from Hokkaido. Signatures include yellowtail with green chili and leche de tigre, wagyu striploin with truffle jus and wasabi and of course, the titular otoro nigiri.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
4702;Superica;USA;Atlanta;99 Krog St. NE, Atlanta, 30307, USA;33.757064;-84.3642568;39;true;false;Tex-Mex;There's nearly a dozen of these popular spots around, but it's this original at Krog Street Market that started it all. There is a contemporary industrial feel here, with high ceilings, a large bar, and an open kitchen. A buzzy vibe adds to the amiable ambience, but it's the food that lures the crowds—Tex-Mex cooking that is as enjoyable as it is approachable. Start with the paper-thin tortillas and salsa that arrive almost immediately before moving on to shareable queso fundido that can be pumped up with vegetables, shrimp, or chorizo. Saucy, cheesy enchiladas served with rice and beans are a go-to order or opt for tacos al carbon with flour tortillas norteña, smoked onions, and flavorful protein selections. Ice-cold margaritas are the perfect accompaniment, naturally.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4703;Table & Main;USA;Roswell;1028 Canton St., Roswell, 30075, USA;34.0266107;-84.3616946;82;true;true;Southern;Head to Roswell to find this gem, located inside a converted home, then step inside for Southern charm at its very best. It's packed with a host of well-heeled guests, all chatting and celebrating.Chef Woolery “Woody” Back mans the stoves in a kitchen that focuses on seasonal, elevated Southern food. Cornbread or hogs 'n quilts make for ideal openers, but if you're leaning into the seasons, opt for dishes like asparagus bisque, a piping hot bowl of spring-minded goodness. Fried chicken brims with flavor and is impossibly delicious, and it's a good thing the portion is overly generous, as you'll want to tuck into leftovers later. Mac and cheese or collard greens make for perfect partners on the plate.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
4704;Heirloom Market BBQ;USA;Atlanta;2243 Akers Mill Rd. SE, Atlanta, 30339, USA;33.8986466;-84.447138;64;true;false;Barbecue;Co-Chefs Cody Taylor and Chef Jiyeon Lee have cooked up something entirely new at Heirloom Market. Blending their Southern and Korean heritage and flavors, they've created a mash-up that's nothing short of fantastic inside a small spot that happens to share space with a liquor store. What it lacks in size it delivers in flavor, though, and it's easy to see why the Korean pork, smoked and braised in a sweet-spicy sauce, is a signature dish. BBQ traditionalists will want to dig in to the brisket that's unfussed with but oh-so-tender and tasty. For a clever take on a Southern classic, try the green tomato kimchi mixed with sliced jalapeños and radish. Sauces, like the mustardy Hotlanta and pepper-vinegar Settler, are worth a shake.;Car park;[]
4705;Masterpiece;USA;Duluth;3940 Buford Hwy., B-103, Duluth, 30096, USA;33.9771152;-84.1613663;68;false;false;Chinese, Sichuan;A long-standing favorite for mouth-numbing Sichuan specialties, Masterpiece is a bit out of the way in Duluth in an unassuming strip mall but it's worth the drive. Inside, it's appointed with light tile floors, while creamy yellow walls are lined with red "leather" booths but make no mistake: You're here for the food not the feels. The hearty Sichuan food is served family style with care and focus shown in dishes like dong po pork, a square of meltingly tender pork belly in a dark brown sauce that is sweet and vibrant. Meanwhile, skinned eggplant sliced into thick matchsticks really showcases the kitchen's skills. Lightly fried and dusted with chili powder and pepper ash powder for a fiery kick, these treats have a gorgeous crunch and a creamy center.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4707;Antico Pizza Napoletana;USA;Atlanta;1093 Hemphill Ave. NW, Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.78465;-84.40562;58;false;true;Pizza;Located in Home Park, with owner Giovanni Di Palma's other concepts like Gio’s and Café Antico tucked into that same corner, Antico Pizza Napoletano promises exactly that. Walk through two sets of doors right up to a counter with the menu posted overhead—it's where you'll decide between rosso and bianche pizzas. After picking your preference, find a seat in the cavernous dining room which shares space with the prep kitchen. It's lively here, as the dough is shaped and baked in one of three ovens. The show will whet your appetite for delicious pizzas like the lasagna, topped with deconstructed "meatball," garlic, ricotta and basil and served on a sheet tray. Soft and chewy, it's a delicious treat.Sweet tooth? Swing by next-door Café Antico for gelato and coffee.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
4709;Whoopsie's;USA;Atlanta;1 Moreland Ave. SE, Atlanta, 30316, USA;33.753393;-84.349398;56;true;false;American;Make no mistake— Whoopsie's is a fun, quirky spot where you'll yearn to be a regular. If you do, you won't be bored, as their menu is a constantly evolving mix of cold dishes, hot dishes that also work well as sides, and a daily changing protein (think prime rib one day and roasted chicken thighs with golden-brown skin another), plus a sandwich of the day. You won't leave hungry, as the portions are generous, and the cooking is humble but well executed. Kick things off with the Southern snack tray, served on a plastic cafeteria tray with the various compartments filled with a collection of Southern Classics like pimento cheese spread, chow chow, pickled veggies, and pork terrine. One dessert is offered daily. If it's the pecan pie, it's a fitting finale.;Air conditioning;[]
4710;Arepa Mia;USA;Avondale Estates;10 N. Clarendon Ave. SE, Ste. A, Avondale Estates, 30002, USA;33.7769307;-84.2672933;16;true;true;Venezuelan, Small eats;Founder/owner Lis Hernandez dials up the charm at Arepa Mia in Avondale Estates. Warm hospitality is a hallmark here, where bright walls and colorful metal chairs and tables instantly boost your mood. The Venezuelan menu is all about the namesake arepas, grilled and filled with everything from yucca and plantain flour-encrusted chicken to pernil with caramelized onions. Other items include patacones and cachapas. The cooking and ingredients are quality driven, and the portions are generous. Feast on selections like the hearts of palm and avocado salad to start, then tuck in to a fried chicken arepa with mango salsa, followed by a guava and cheese empanada. Fresh juices slake your thirst, though the full bar has some fantastic rum choices.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
4711;Little Bear;USA;Atlanta;71-A Georgia Ave. SE, Atlanta, 30312, USA;33.7367844;-84.3854039;79;false;true;Contemporary;Chef Jarrett Stieber pulls inspiration from around the globe at this restaurant, nestled within the Summerhill area. He presides over an open kitchen where an eclectic, contemporary menu is frequently changing and a prix fixe offering includes dishes not found on the à la carte. You may dine on items such as house-cured rainbow trout with kraut yogurt, shaved cured egg yolk, and everything bagel powder or pork döner sausage with hoppin’ john fried rice. Leave your expectations at the door, as evidenced in the mushroom soup with a warm, bitter chocolate broth, pickled zucchini, pak choi and a wallop of flavor. La Zi Ji-style chicken thigh with strawberry sauce delivers a spring twist on a classic Chinese dish, while citrus custard with a sweet cucumber relish is a perfect finish.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4712;Fishmonger;USA;Atlanta;674 N. Highland Ave. NE, Atlanta, 30306, USA;33.7730449;-84.3526256;92;false;false;Seafood;It's part fish market, part casual restaurant here, where a single communal table and stools lined up at the windows await guests. Order at the back counter from a compact, seafood-focused menu listing oysters, crudos, sandwiches and soups. This is not your typical fried fish shack, though, and many of the dishes have a Southern slant to them. Peel and eat shrimp is a good standby, while tuna melts level up. Specials are always a good bet, but the house staple—the blackened grouper sandwich—is a winner. A thick piece of generously spiced, blackened grouper is draped over a buttered, toasted seeded bun with Florida sauce, pickled peppers, ripe tomato and lettuce for something far from fussy but totally spot on. Gumbo is flavorful and hearty.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4713;Bomb Biscuit Co.;USA;Atlanta;668 Highland Ave. NE, Atlanta, 30312, USA;33.7615365;-84.3653438;68;false;true;Southern;First a pop-up, then a food stall, this homey spot is now a full-fledged breakfast and brunch restaurant. From the butter yellow walls (a nod to Owner Erika Council's grandmother) to the framed family photos, this place feels like you're hanging out in her home, and that's entirely the point.The menu shows off simple but successful plates ranging from breakfast sandwiches to brunch plates with fried chicken and other staples. Baked goods, like cinnamon rolls with a thick, tangy cream cheese glaze, are exceptional, but given the name, biscuits, ranging from traditional to jalapeno and cheddar, are an absolute must. Go for broke with a hearty biscuit sandwich stacked high with egg and cheese or hot honey chicken with pickles.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
4714;Banshee;USA;Atlanta;1271 Glenwood Ave. SE, Atlanta, 30316, USA;33.7401201;-84.3459125;85;true;false;American;This East Atlanta restaurant is equal parts hip and lively with a quirky New American menu to boot. Inside, wood floors and whitewashed brick walls set an upbeat tone while the kitchen delivers on its promise of creative contemporary cooking. The menu is tightly focused, offering a handful of small plates and main dishes along with seasonal vegetables in a supporting role. Start with the fry bread, served piping hot with a pepperoni butter that's so good they sell it by the pint. Chilled beets sided by sweet blackberries with an aquavit vinaigrette, rye “soil“ and shaved beet chips is a riot of flavors in an eye-catching dish, but you'll never go wrong with an order of pasta, especially the corzetti topped with a mound of tender crab.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4715;Fred's Meat & Bread;USA;Atlanta;99 Krog St. NE, Atlanta, 30307, USA;33.7569561;-84.3639769;93;false;false;American;Located in the Krog Street Market, what this contemporary space lacks in size it makes up for in charm. The concept is straightforward: sandwiches of all varieties from burgers and oyster po'boys to bahn mi and cheesesteaks. Each one is messy-delicious and over the top in the best possible way, as in the pimento cheese club with house-made pimento cheese, roasted poblanos, fried green tomatoes and bacon sandwiched between bread and seared. Meanwhile, the Italian grinder with all the meats, melty provolone cheese, garlic aioli and cherry pepper relish knocks it out of the park. Of course, there must be fries, and the barbecue version, with barbecue seasoning and a white barbecue sauce for dipping, won't disappoint.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4716;Snatch;Latvia;Riga;Elizabetes iela 39, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.9573304;24.1122734;99;false;true;Italian;With its bare concrete, floor-to-ceiling windows and faux-industrial styling, Snatch is one Riga’s more stylish spots. The staff are bright and breezy, there’s a buzz from the open kitchen and the upbeat soundtrack and bespoke cocktail list help contribute to the lively mood. The authentic Italian dishes are carefully cooked – with the homemade pastas being a highlight – and the Italian-focused wine list has some interesting choices.;;[]
4717;Shōyu;Latvia;Riga;Ausekļa iela 20, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.9623049;24.1004265;17;false;true;Japanese, Ramen;The name Shōyu – a type of Japanese soy sauce – is a clue as to what they serve at this tiny little shop, which specialises in classic ramen dishes. The rich, full-flavoured broth complements their homemade noodles perfectly, and there’s a great range of different ingredients to explore. There are also various rice bowls available – and be sure to start by sharing some of the tasty starters like yakitori or tataki. Service is sweet and there’s an appealing buzz to the modern room.;Counter dining;[]
4718;Milda;Latvia;Riga;Kungu Iela 8, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.9460552;24.109604;66;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The figure that stands atop the Old Town’s Latvian Freedom Monument is affectionately named Milda, and this unassuming-looking restaurant shares her name. Traditional recipes from Latvia and neighbouring Lithuania take the lead, but are given a light, modern touch and presented in a contemporary manner. Dishes such as Latvian pelmeni or grey peas with bacon and sour cream sit alongside Lithuanian favourites like cepelinai (potato dumplings). Service is warm and everything is great value.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4719;Multertor;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Am Multertor, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4240166;9.3740992;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Operating as a café, restaurant and bar, this place enjoys a fantastic location in the city centre. One could happily spend the whole day here, as they serve breakfast, then there's a small lunch menu, lights are available throughout the day and, finally, there's the evening menu, as well as a daily special ("Funkes Empfehlung"). This establishment is run by executive chef Tobias Funke and head chef Andi von Gunten – both previously worked together at Incantare in Heiden. Ambitious as ever, they continue to strive for excellence, serving up hearty home-style cuisine. Take, for example, the fish fingers made with wild-caught cod and trout, served with new potatoes, fresh spinach and a miso hollandaise sauce. The atmosphere is relaxed, the vibe is trendy and the centrally positioned bar is especially inviting. Lovely spacious terrace.;Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4720;STÜVA in der Krone - Säumerei am Inn;Switzerland;La Punt-Chamues-ch;Via Cumünela 2, La Punt-Chamues-ch, 7522, Switzerland;46.5786906;9.9260653;93;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The different Arvenstuben (Swiss pine lodges), including the over 300-year-old Jahre old Stüvetta, offer an appealing alternative to LA CHAVALLERA. Here, traditional Engadine cosiness is complemented by modern overtones. The menu features delicious dishes that home in on the essentials, including vegetarian options such as beetroot gnocchi or aubergine ravioli that keep diners coming back for more! Most of the ingredients used are locally sourced and seasonal. In fine weather, you can also eat out on the terrace.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4721;Postigliun;Switzerland;Andiast;Via Principala 41, Andiast, 7159, Switzerland;46.7833612;9.1117536;35;true;false;Regional Cuisine, International;Nestled high above the valley is the Sgier family's exceedingly welcoming restaurant, where father-and-son team Guido and Sandro serve up delicious cuisine. The menu features both regional and internationally influenced dishes. Don't miss your chance to try "Guido's capuns" (stuffed chard rolls)! No less appealing are the dishes made with game they have hunted themselves. The wine list includes gems from the region, as well as from Italy and Austria – the proprietress will gladly recommend wines by the glass. Tip: moderately priced set menu at lunchtime. Well-appointed guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4722;Gül;Switzerland;Zurich;Tellstrasse 22, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3784889;8.5292392;30;false;true;Turkish, Mediterranean Cuisine;This is a place that has all the makings of a cherished favourite restaurant! Tucked away in a courtyard, the atmosphere is lively and pleasantly laid back. Closely spaced tables and Turkish background music add to the bustling and vibrant feel. In the open kitchen, the chefs serve up freshly crafted modern Turkish dishes packed with bold flavours and sometimes with a touch of heat. Be sure to try the çiğ köfte (plant-based or meat kofta) and the baklava! Drawing on Middle Eastern culinary tradition, the menu features an array of snacks and larger platters that are idea for sharing. The "Gülty Menü Sürpriz" is also an excellent choice (by the table only). Tip: Creative cocktails available at the restaurant's own bar.;Terrace;[]
4723;Agorà;Switzerland;Brissago;Via Muro degli Ottevi 10, Brissago, 6614, Switzerland;46.1195601;8.7106467;30;true;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Located in relaxing Brissago, this historic bistro features a pleasantly retro ambience and well-maintained wood furnishings. The courteous service is accompanied by the delicious flavours of dishes that follow the seasons and include traditional and Mediterranean touches. The ravioli del plin stuffed with braised wild boar are a highlight.;Terrace;[]
4725;Alpenblick - Bistro;Switzerland;Adelboden;Dorfstr. 9, Adelboden, 3715, Switzerland;46.4936941;7.5608035;42;false;true;Farm to table;The bistro may be cheaper than this establishment's upscale restaurant (Stuba), but a meal here is still really tasty and fresh. Whether you come for lunch or dinner, the terrific, no-frills market-inspired cooking won't break the bank. They are keen to use produce from the region, in dishes such as "Hüttler's hamburger" or house speciality "Dad's steak tartare". Another of their classics is the spicy Thai red curry, with just the right amount of heat! In keeping with the Alpenblick style, the atmosphere is nice and relaxed, and the service is charming and attentive. There are also some good wines – the wine list is the same as at the fine dining restaurant.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4726;Natürlich;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue de la Coulouvrenière 38, Geneva, 1204, Switzerland;46.2037999;6.1379596;43;true;true;Farm to table, Piedmontese;Just a few metres from the River Rhône and the BFM theatre, this popular restaurant appeals with its trendy and relaxed bistro-style atmosphere. It serves seasonal modern cuisine based on quality regional ingredients, in dishes such as roast cuttlefish, purple potatoes and cime di rapa. The food is accompanied by a terrific wine list including organic options. And for an even more convivial experience, plates are designed for sharing! Friendly service, too.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4727;DAR;Switzerland;Zurich;Gasometerstrasse 5, Zurich, 8005, Switzerland;47.3837072;8.5284634;50;false;true;Vegan, Modern Cuisine;This trendy, understated place is the charming sister restaurant of KLE. The plant-based cuisine draws on the Spanish and Moroccan roots of chef Zineb ("Zizi") Hattab, the daughter of Moroccan parents, who grew up on the Costa Brava. Her modern take on Spanish and Moroccan culinary tradition is served in the form of dishes that are ideal for sharing. With the "DAR Sharing Journey", you can put together your own sharing menu from a selection of around 15 dishes. Drinks are served at the adjoining bar – before or after your meal. Sat and Sun brunch.;Brunch;[]
4728;Grotto della Salute;Switzerland;Massagno;Via dei Sindacatori 2A, Massagno, 6900, Switzerland;46.0112405;8.943635;63;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A rustic grotto-style restaurant with a warm and welcoming ambience, where staff are happy to advise you on the seasonal dishes on offer. A whole page of the menu is dedicated to classic favourites, all of which are influenced by Mediterranean cuisine – the veal shank with mashed potato and salted butter is particularly delicious. There’s also a small menu of daily specials which changes according to market availability. The terrace shaded by huge plane trees provides a pleasant setting for summer dining, while an excellent wine list adds to the appeal.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4729;Asia;Switzerland;Ascona;Via Moscia 4, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1545931;8.7660053;30;false;false;Asian, Sushi;At this restaurant, an Oriental-style decor in dark colours provides the setting for Japanese cuisine, including the usual classic favourites. The menu features traditional and fusion sushi, sashimi, delicious Thai curries, dim sum and many other Asian specialities, plus there’s an interesting set menu (at lunchtime) which changes daily.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
4730;Fischerstube;Switzerland;Weesen;Marktgasse 9, Weesen, 8872, Switzerland;47.1353412;9.0974447;27;true;true;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;At this long-established restaurant, Alain Koenig serves up dishes that are pleasingly down-to-earth and packed with flavour. Fish takes centre stage, but there are also a few meat and vegetarian options. You can dine à la carte or opt for one of two set menus: "Complet" (four courses) and "Degustation" (three to six courses). The tasteful decor is classically elegant in style, the service attentive and friendly. Decent wine list. Tip: For private dining or celebrations, book the historical vaulted cellar.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4731;AuGust;Switzerland;Zurich;Rennweg 7, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3723599;8.5400963;60;true;true;Meats and Grills;This restaurant with its charming brasserie atmosphere is located in what was once the "butcher's quarter" – and in keeping with its history, the meat theme has been taken up here. Besides design features such as lamps and wall tiles, the open kitchen really draws the eye. They rear their own meat or source it from Swiss producers. Vegetarian alternatives are also available.;Terrace;[]
4732;Le Lab by Adel & Niko;Switzerland;Corseaux;Route de la Crottaz 5, Corseaux, 1802, Switzerland;46.46846;6.834545;62;true;true;International;This establishment is located just past the boundary between Vevey and Corseaux. The ground floor dispenses cookery lessons (for enthusiastic individuals and groups), while the basement houses the restaurant proper. The latter sports a modern vibe depicted by warm colours (a striking crimson-claret wall), an understated wine display and a designer-inspired long counter. The owners, charming Adel and jovial Niko, play a key role in their establishment’s buzzy character. A set menu with a choice of courses at lunchtime and creative, tapas-style dishes to share in the evenings. Pleasant dinky terrace.;Terrace;[]
4734;Bazaar;Switzerland;Zermatt;Riedweg 156, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0217841;7.7540897;16;false;false;International, Asian;At this restaurant in the chic Alpine CERVO Mountain Resort – which commands a great panoramic view – you are whisked away to an exotic and predominantly vegetarian world of flavours, ranging from Arabic to Chinese specialities, from Lebanese flatbread (manakish) and pistachio baklava to dim sum and much more. In keeping with its name, this place has a lively and friendly atmosphere, to which original and highly disparate decorative details also contribute.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4735;Njørd café;Switzerland;Aubonne;Place du Marché 15, Aubonne, 1170, Switzerland;46.4952607;6.3913028;68;true;false;Scandinavian, Farm to table;Njørd Café is a spin-off of the restaurant Njørden. It serves fresh and seasonal Scandinavian and Swiss cuisine in a modern, Nordic atmosphere. Breakfast and brunch is also available at the weekend. To the rear of the building, there is a charming terrace planted with herbs and flowers. Hotel Hemma has a number of pleasant guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
4737;Birdy's by Achtien;Switzerland;Brunnen;Axenstrasse 9, Brunnen, 6440, Switzerland;46.993476;8.6067963;88;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Perfect for anyone who loves to share! For lunch and dinner, chef Christian Vogel (aka Birdy) provides an exciting dining experience. With the "Sharing is Love" concept, he puts the onus on communication as much as culinary enjoyment in a relaxed, modern atmosphere. The cuisine is predominantly vegetarian, but can be supplemented with fish or meat – both of which are of the highest quality. Choose à la carte dishes such as cauliflower tempura, soy sauce, peanut, salted lemon, or roast Hokkaido pumpkin, peanut, Thai curry, kumquat, with optional fried Gotthard zander. The sharing surprise menu for two is also on point – ten dishes are served in three courses.;;[]
4738;Alpenblick - Swiss Bistro;Switzerland;Wilderswil;Oberdorfstrasse 3, Wilderswil, 3812, Switzerland;46.663893;7.8601359;56;true;false;Country cooking, Swiss;Bistro makes for a pleasant alternative to Gourmetstübli in the Alpenblick hotel. Diners soak up the cosy atmosphere as they tuck into the excellent food served here. On the menu: delicious regional and seasonal dishes as well as classics such as Kalbfleisch-Geschnetzeltes (slices of Simmental veal in a creamy sauce) and cheese fondue. And be sure to try the rösti! On Tuesday evenings the restaurant hosts a meat fondue buffet.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4739;Ivy 23;Switzerland;Carouge;Rue Ancienne 23, Carouge, 1227, Switzerland;46.1822533;6.1411455;33;false;false;Farm to table, Modern French;A lively restaurant and bar in the historical centre of Carouge. Whitewashed brick walls and 1930s-style decoration, such as lamps and old posters evocative of the prohibition era in the US, make for a distinctive atmosphere, underscored by a soundtrack of jazz/swing sounds. They serve modern and seasonal food with a French twist. Pleasant little terrace in the courtyard to the rear.;Terrace;[]
4740;Ô Bois Sauvage;Switzerland;Hérémence;Chemin des Mélèzes 26, Hérémence, 1987, Switzerland;46.1788081;7.3969407;88;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Situated at an elevation of approximately 1 500m above sea level, this restaurant is just 250m away from Hérémence's high-speed lift station. The breathtaking mountain vistas are undoubtedly one of the restaurant's standout features, best enjoyed on the fantastic terrace. Alternatively, you can savour the view from indoors, where the atmosphere is modern and relaxed. Incidentally, the numerous decorative works of art are available for purchase. This restaurant's commitment to sustainability and its strong attachment to the region are evident in the selection of produce, such as fillet of Swiss grass-fed ox or cheese. The short wine list features labels from the region.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4742;Bistrot du Lion d'Or;Switzerland;Carouge;Rue Ancienne 53, Carouge, 1227, Switzerland;46.1805824;6.1403385;34;true;false;Classic French;In the restaurant of this hotel dating from 1750, the team offers - in a friendly and relaxed atmosphere - delicious French cuisine with seasonal products, such as artichoke, smoked whitefish from the nearby lakes and buckwheat, or pan-fried sweetbreads, morels and asparagus. The well-curated wine list is also worthy of your attention. In fine weather, the pleasant terrace to the rear of the building is a peaceful little haven for diners.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4744;Bären;Switzerland;Utzenstorf;Hauptstrasse 18, Utzenstorf, 3427, Switzerland;47.1291038;7.557588;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The 14th generation of the same family is at the helm of this gorgeous traditional Bernese inn – it was first documented in 1261. Whether you eat in the pretty, inviting dining area or the lovely garden, you will be treated to friendly service and delicious food with a traditional regional character. One speciality of the house is the Solothurner Wy-Süppli (wine soup). The chef will be happy to explain the origins of their rather special "Bärechöpfli" dessert. Slightly reduced menu at lunchtime. There are also stylish salons.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4746;16 ART-BAR-RESTAURANT;Switzerland;Saanen;Mittelgässli 16, Saanen, 3792, Switzerland;46.4895677;7.2593297;80;true;true;Country cooking, International;Diners will feel right at home in this charming and inviting restaurant. Set in a former bell foundry, the atmosphere is welcoming and delightfully down to earth. The blend of rustic and modern styles is interesting, and the art on the walls is sure to draw the eye. You can look forward to very friendly and attentive service, as well as pared-down and exceedingly flavourful dishes prepared by owner Nik Buchs. Popular choices here include true classics such as entrecôte or veal cutlet. The extensive wine list also includes organic and biodynamic wines.;Terrace;[]
4747;Rathauskeller Bistro;Switzerland;Zug;Ober-Altstadt 1, Zug, 6300, Switzerland;47.1660593;8.5150035;28;true;false;Classic Cuisine;The friendly service and relaxed atmosphere here are popular with locals and tourists alike. Diners can choose from the selection of classics such as cordon bleu, Lammhacktätschli (lamb patties) and beef roulades, and there is also a seasonal menu. The tables on the gorgeous terrace in front of the building in the cobbled pedestrian zone are coveted. Tip: Just a stone's throw away, the lakeside is perfect for a stroll.;Terrace;[]
4750;Bistrot Dumas;Switzerland;Geneva;Avenue Dumas 7, Geneva, 1206, Switzerland;46.1917843;6.1549083;59;false;false;French;This buzzy bistro located in the Champel neighbourhood is often fully booked. The interior is done out simply and tastefully – it is the Art Nouveau stained-glass ceiling panels, as well as the columns, that draw the eye. Their classic take on traditional French cuisine is flavoursome and aromatic, plus everything is made in-house. The service is efficient and attentive.;Air conditioning;[]
4751;La Fleur de Sel;Switzerland;Cossonay;Rue du Temple 10, Cossonay, 1304, Switzerland;46.6141623;6.5086372;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French;Regional cuisine and a bistro style atmosphere in the Fleur de Sel.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4753;Casa Casutt - Ustria;Switzerland;Ilanz;Glennerstrasse 18, Ilanz, 7130, Switzerland;46.7742301;9.2073248;45;false;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Linus and Therese Arpagaus offer diners a charming setting in which to tuck into their excellent cuisine made using fresh produce. The menu takes its cue from the region and includes local specialties such as capuns and pizokel. Fans of veal liver, sweetbreads or tripe are also in for a treat. The garden terrace is wonderful, and Sala is another alternative.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4754;Moosegg;Switzerland;Emmenmatt;Moosegg 231A, Emmenmatt, 3543, Switzerland;46.9462747;7.711754;82;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Up here, at an altitude of around 1 000m, there is much to get excited about: the phenomenal view of the Emmental and the Alps – either from the modern, elegant restaurant with its large window front or the magnificent terrace – is complemented by good food with a regional and seasonal focus. For a cheaper but equally indulgent alternative, head to Beiz. The terrific wine selection boasts around 800 different options. Chic guestrooms are available in the adjoining boutique hotel.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4755;Restaurant Schlüssel - Schlüsselstube;Switzerland;Mels;Oberdorfstrasse 5, Mels, 8887, Switzerland;47.0463738;9.4186133;88;true;false;Country cooking;Schlüsselstube is a bistro where they also serve outstanding food – and it represents really great value for money. Classics such as braised veal cheeks are delicious, and the desserts are extremely hard to resist! When it comes to wine, this cosy place also hits all the right notes. The service provided by waitresses in traditional dress could not be more charming!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4756;Zum Alten Stephan;Switzerland;Solothurn;Friedhofplatz 10, Solothurn, 4500, Switzerland;47.2072374;7.5354428;82;false;false;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant in the middle of the old town is not only steeped in history, it is also a treat for epicureans. Top-notch, down-to-earth cooking, staff who go the extra mile and a buzzing atmosphere make for a perfect dining experience. While Tamara Bader heads up the service team with effortless charm, her husband Stefan whips us delectable dishes rooted in classic tradition. Think pan-fried sweetbreads with mashed potato, spring vegetables and a morel sauce. House classics such as the cordon bleu are also in high demand. The impressive wine list is dedicated to Swiss, French and Italian labels. Delightful terrace in front of the building.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4757;Auberge de la Croix d'Or - Bistro;Switzerland;Yens;Grande-Rue 18, Yens, 1169, Switzerland;46.5184953;6.4162323;47;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Claudia and Olivier Hiernard have combined bistro and restaurant at their charming inn. The delicious bistro fare on the blackboard is now complemented by a market-inspired "Menu du Marché", meaning flavoursome dishes are now served in both parts of the establishment. Just don't forget to leave room for dessert! On Friday and Saturday evenings, only a small selection is available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4758;Sonne;Switzerland;Ebersecken;Dorf 2, Ebersecken, 6245, Switzerland;47.1830427;7.9313514;45;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Swiss;At the Häfliger family's lovely 100-year-old restaurant, diners can look forward to fresh, flavoursome food and attentive service provided by experienced staff. Classic Swiss cuisine is served in the form of a seasonal or surprise set menu. Alternatively, you can order à la carte. This place even has its own excellent spring water! Pleasant terrace to the rear of the building. Tip: Delicious cheese is sold in the cheesery next door.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4759;Edo;Switzerland;Crans-Montana;Route Sierre-Montana 43, Crans-Montana, 3975, Switzerland;46.3108192;7.4982631;58;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;You can be in the Swiss mountains and still enjoy authentic Japanese cuisine, including dishes such as Japanese fondue, grilled chicken with Teriyaki sauce, and delicious gyozas and sushi (takeaway dishes are also available). Here, legendary specialities from Japan are prepared in front of you with high-quality ingredients and meticulous care. Terrace with views of the surrounding peaks.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4760;Wirtshus zum Wyberg;Switzerland;Freienstein-Teufen;Oberteufenerstrasse 1, Freienstein-Teufen, 8428, Switzerland;47.5514864;8.5655878;67;false;true;Classic Cuisine;The restaurant on the first floor is a little more elegant and comfortable than the bar. The large menu ranges from a delicious veal schnitzel in morel sauce to the classic saddle of venison grand veneur, not to mention a popular lobster menu which includes home-made ravioli.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4761;Centrale;Switzerland;Losone;via Locarno 2, Losone, 6616, Switzerland;46.1646865;8.7605058;80;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Particularly renowned and popular with locals, this restaurant has a delightful family ambience. It offers delicious regional cuisine that can be enjoyed outdoors on the lovely terrace in fine weather.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4762;Braui;Switzerland;Hochdorf;Brauiplatz 5, Hochdorf, 6280, Switzerland;47.1668742;8.2901803;77;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Housed in the cultural centre that shares its name, braui serves good traditional cuisine in a pleasant, brasserie atmosphere. The menu is made up of seasonal dishes and includes classics such as beef tartare or veal cordon bleu. Smaller choice available at lunchtime. Tip: The public car park, Braui-Parkhaus, is handy.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4763;Adler;Switzerland;Ried-Muotathal;Kappelmatt 1, Ried-Muotathal, 6436, Switzerland;46.98687;8.71306;35;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;The name of the game here is "Gasthaus at its best" – this applies to the cosy space, the cordial, attentive service, and chef Daniel Jann's cuisine. Whether you opt for Murmeltierpfeffer (marmot stew), Gitzi-Bratwurst (a goat meat and beef sausage) or asparagus dishes, meticulous craftsmanship and flavour are guaranteed. The focus lies squarely on the region. Eating here is fun! Stylish guestrooms are available for overnight stays.;Car park;[]
4764;Bistro by Regina Montium;Switzerland;Rigi Kaltbad;Staffelhöhenweg 35, Rigi Kaltbad, 6356, Switzerland;47.0483577;8.4640786;68;false;true;Swiss;Whether you hike up or take the mountain railway (ideal from Vitznau), it's well worth stopping off here. The location is idyllic – at 1 550m above sea level, the terrace is wonderful – and the "natural cuisine" is another big attraction! This includes smaller plates and regular dishes such as Rigi beef ragout or burger with Alpine cheese, many of which are made with produce from the immediate vicinity or grown in their own garden. Individual ingredients are explained in a friendly and competent manner. Why not try a gentian root tonic with Rigi juniper gin before dinner? Both the Bistro, for lunch, and fine dining restaurant, Regina Montium, for dinner, are located in Kräuterhotel Edelweiss, where you can stay overnight after your meal.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4765;Kaiserstock;Switzerland;Riemenstalden;Dörfli 2, Riemenstalden, 6452, Switzerland;46.9465871;8.6650923;79;false;true;Country cooking, International;This charming establishment perched in a small mountain village is your reward after the narrow, steep drive up! The fact that the restaurant has many regular customers is of course mainly down to its tasty traditional cuisine. The dishes are prepared with flair from good, fresh produce from the region. Popular options include stews and ravioli. A four- to seven-course set menu is also available if you pre-book (two days in advance). Seasonal specialities such as venison and chamois or Metzgete (pork platter) are also worth considering. Tip: Soups, sausages, jams and other delicacies can be purchased to take home. There are pleasant rustic-style guestrooms for overnight stays. N.B. Cash only!;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace;[]
4766;Panorama - Bistro;Switzerland;Steffisburg;Hartlisbergstrasse 39, Steffisburg, 3612, Switzerland;46.7872443;7.6208725;69;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This attractive alternative to the Cayenne offers excellent cuisine at a very reasonable price. Although the dishes are simpler in style, they are prepared with equal sophistication using quality regional produce, always with a certain modern twist. Attentive service, plus the same wine list as in the Cayenne. Wonderful views!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4767;Landgasthof Ochsen;Switzerland;Wölflinswil;Dorfplatz 56, Wölflinswil, 5063, Switzerland;47.4611953;7.9980311;82;false;true;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;The food is terrific in this inn dating back to 1288 – the skilful chef clearly pours a lot of love into his cooking. As well as regional dishes and classics, Asian and Mediterranean influences also make their way onto the menu. A meal in their Gaststube is a somewhat simpler affair. There is a lovely terrace overlooking the pond, plus a charming smoking lounge. Pleasant and handy guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4768;Chappeli;Switzerland;Grenchen;Allerheiligenstrasse 218, Grenchen, 2540, Switzerland;47.1955388;7.3683399;92;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;In this pleasantly laid-back restaurant overlooking the village, the Hausmann/Köhli husband-and-wife team propose a really fun dining experience! The chef-patron cooks up delectable dishes that are delightfully down-to-earth: drawing inspiration from the region, they are big on flavour, with options including, for example, leek and bacon ravioli with fresh morels, or pork steak with Meaux mustard, mashed potatoes and vegetables. Nicely curated wine list and highly attentive service courtesy of the lady of the house, whose natural charm shines through. Be sure to bag a table on the delightfully verdant garden terrace!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4769;Gasthaus Schupfen;Switzerland;Diessenhofen;Steinerstrasse 501, Diessenhofen, 8253, Switzerland;47.675254;8.7852825;36;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;With a history dating back to 1455, this lovely half-timbered house is really something special. In an inviting atmosphere, food is served in three charming rooms and on the idyllic terrace overlooking the Rhine. The menu features classics, including Kalbsgeschnetzeltes Zürcher Art (veal ragout), and seasonal dishes such as Kundelfinger trout with boiled potatoes and spinach. If you are looking for a good location for a wedding or event, the premises can also be rented out.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4770;Chez Philippe;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue du Rhône 8, Geneva, 1204, Switzerland;46.2042229;6.1446687;69;true;false;Meats and Grills, International;Philippe Chevrier from the Domaine de Châteauvieux is the brains behind this huge restaurant inspired by New York-style steakhouses. Relaxed atmosphere, meats sourced from the renowned Boucherie du Molard, fish caught by small-scale fishermen, dishes cooked over a wood fire, a truly authentic cheesecake and an expansive wine list. A real favourite!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4771;Bacchus Bistro & Genussmanufaktur;Switzerland;Hildisrieden;Sempacherstrasse 1, Hildisrieden, 6024, Switzerland;47.1507721;8.2287675;83;true;true;French, Seasonal Cuisine;You will feel right at home at this restaurant, thanks to the tasteful, upscale decor, friendly service and – last but not least – good-quality, fresh dishes cooked up by Werner Tobler. There are two set menus: "Du Terroir", comprising three to four courses, and four- to six-course "La Table chez Bacchus". Tip: Genussmanufaktur sells an appealing range of cheeses, spices, cakes, wines etc.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4772;Hardern Pintli;Switzerland;Lyss;Hardern 23, Lyss, 3250, Switzerland;47.0857046;7.3297412;52;false;false;Swiss, Country cooking;This picture-perfect inn is warm and welcoming and certainly looks inviting with its red shutters. Chef-patron Falk Fleischhauer achieves a fine balance between traditional fare and classic cuisine, resulting in delicious dishes that are reasonably priced. Both tripe and sole are to be found on the menu. The service is very friendly and anything but stuffy. In summer, the lovely terrace with its trees is very inviting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4773;Auberge Communale;Switzerland;Saint-Légier;78 rte des Deux-Villages, Saint-Légier, 1806, Switzerland;46.4705418;6.8838173;42;true;false;Contemporary;This rather inconspicuous Auberge is located in a small village set slightly above Vevey. Run by the Konrad family, it not only has guestrooms for overnight stays, but also serves really good food! Whether eating in the refined modern space or on the pretty terrace, choose between delicious bistro dishes and the "Gastro" set menu. It is always tasty and prices remain very competitive.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4774;Bären;Switzerland;Schwarzenburg;Dorfplatz 4, Schwarzenburg, 3150, Switzerland;46.8176503;7.3413206;23;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;At this rather grand establishment with two dining spaces, Gaststube and GnussStube, the wide-ranging menu includes simpler dishes and more sophisticated fare, plus vegetarian options. You can dine à la carte or opt for a set menu – the fine-dining set menu ("MundArt"), has to be ordered in advance. At lunchtime, a reduced à la carte selection and daily specials are available. Ingredients are sourced as locally as possible. There is a decent wine list with a focus on Swiss labels. The waitstaff are friendly, attentive and well trained.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4775;The Mansard Restaurant;Switzerland;Gstaad;Untergstaadstrasse 26, Gstaad, 3780, Switzerland;46.4763964;7.2836958;64;false;true;International, Regional Cuisine;Located on the ground floor of boutique hotel Miiro The Mansard, this restaurant has a modern and elegant brasserie-style interior with an Alpine feel. There is a terrace with a few tables out on the pavement – this is a place to see and be seen. Martin Bieri is in charge of the hotel, restaurant and kitchen. Using top-notch ingredients, many of them Swiss, he and his team cook up flavoursome international cuisine to be ordered à la carte. The menu includes dishes such as Lauenen dried meat with Gstaad mountain cheese, and Balfego tuna carpaccio with a sesame marinade. You can also look forward to a well-curated wine list and friendly service. Tip: For a cool rooftop bar experience with stunning views, head to the bar The Mansard Rooftop on the fourth floor, which serves drinks, cocktails and a small selection of snacks. Thanks to its central location close to the Gstaad Promenade, the hotel is also an ideal starting point for a stroll around the shops.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4777;Schüpbärg-Beizli;Switzerland;Schüpfen;Schüpberg 134, Schüpfen, 3053, Switzerland;47.0230175;7.3945155;40;true;true;Swiss, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant is quite out of the way, but it's worth the journey here to this remote location, where a cosy, rustic-style interior awaits diners, as well as a lovely terrace, which is very popular in summer! But let's not forget the cooking of owner Christoph Hunziker: he prepares home-style Swiss dishes with a modern twist, stamped with his own ideas. In addition to this, you can expect charming service – sometimes the chefs, too, come to the tables.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4778;Colani Bistrot;Switzerland;Madulain;Via Principela 20A, Madulain, 7523, Switzerland;46.5861471;9.9379638;17;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Located just off the reception area of the tasteful and well-appointed Hotel Colani, Colani Bistrot is the alternative to the fine dining restaurant. The food served here – Mediterranean cuisine with a local twist. We can certainly recommend the "Ravioli of the Day". Meat eaters should ask about the main dish centred on venison or veal – showcasing a different cut every day. Friendly service, a laid-back atmosphere and modern interior design featuring light wood and a whole host of decorative details.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4779;SUAHOY;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue Prévost-Martin 25, Geneva, 1205, Switzerland;46.194579;6.1457614;33;true;false;Thai;It quickly becomes clear that this friendly, buzzy venue is not your average Thai eatery. Everything is made fresh, the ingredients are good quality, and the flavours are well rounded and pack a punch – everything you could ask for from this type of cuisine. Cordial staff. In summer, a small terrace is laid out in front of the door. A word to the wise: booking is essential, even at lunchtime!;Terrace;[]
4780;Le Café Valrose;Switzerland;Rougemont;Place de la Gare 2, Rougemont, 1659, Switzerland;46.4886208;7.2083597;52;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Swiss;Part of the same establishment as La Table de Valrose, this bistro has a comfortable rustic-style Alpine atmosphere, both outside, on the terrace shaded by chestnut trees, surrounded by mountains, and inside, by the fireplace, in the wood-panelled space. Relax in the lounge bar with a coffee or cocktail in hand. The menu features tasty seasonal fare in the form of simple dishes, while classics such as Valrose fondue (champagne version available), malakoffs and Valrose burgers (meat or veggie) are permanent fixtures on the menu. The dessert trolley is available all afternoon, for teatime.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4781;Grotto Valmaggese;Switzerland;Avegno;Via Vallemaggia 72, Avegno, 6670, Switzerland;46.2133539;8.745423;65;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in an excellent location slightly above the road, this traditional grotto-style restaurant with a large car park is quiet and cool in summer, with a dining room warmed by a fireplace in winter. In this delightful location, enjoy classic, well-prepared and generous cuisine with personal touches made using top-quality, seasonally inspired ingredients. Make sure you try the venison tartare with marrow gratin and pear jelly, as well as the delicious artisanal ice creams. The highly welcoming and attentive service is clearly in evidence in the dining room.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4782;Barranco;Switzerland;Zurich;Sihlfeldstrasse 141, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3792585;8.5158079;98;false;false;Peruvian;Eat, drink, make merry, meet friends… the Kreis 4 district is to Zurich what the Barranco district is to Lima. Nestled among a host of other restaurants and bars, the Peruvian neighbourhood's namesake serves modern Peruvian cuisine that is bursting with flavour, zing and spices. The dishes are designed to be shared and tasted together. The atmosphere is pleasingly unpretentious in this inviting space with a trendy decor featuring Peruvian murals – the relaxed yet efficient service is the icing on the cake. Great cocktail selection. There is a terrace in front of the building, separated from the pavement by plants.;Terrace;[]
4783;Myò Sushi Bar;Switzerland;Lausanne;Allée Ernest–Ansermet 1, Lausanne, 1003, Switzerland;46.5199155;6.6273188;28;true;true;Japanese;Set in the Esplanade de Montbenon park, opposite the courthouse, this Japanese restaurant will win you over with its peaceful setting and quality cuisine. In summer, the terrace boasts a breathtaking view of the lake. Comfortably perched on a high stool, you can savour a variety of authentic Japanese dishes, including delicate sushi, tasty teppanyaki, beef tartare with wasabi, and a refined take on soba noodles. This is a popular place, so booking your spot at the counter is strongly advised.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
4784;Gaijin Izakaya;Switzerland;Zurich;Birmensdorferstrasse 5, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3728878;8.5275985;21;true;true;Asian Contemporary;This place with a name that translates as "foreigner bar" is a really cool spot that follows the style of Japanese izakayas (casual bars that also serve food). A team led by chef-patron Daniel Shu, who trained in Chicago and New York, and his business partner bring you delicious contemporary Asian soul food. There is a reduced menu at lunchtime. Expect creative cooking such as their spicy Korean pork belly: thin, slightly crispy slices of pork belly marinated in a spicy sweet and sour sauce and accompanied by a beautifully soft egg cooked sous vide and placed on sesame rice. The atmosphere is relaxed, with modern music playing in the background.;;[]
4785;Le Bistro by Décotterd;Switzerland;Montreux;Route de Glion 111, Montreux, 1823, Switzerland;46.4326762;6.9216439;95;false;true;French Contemporary;Like its fine dining counterpart, Le Bistro also promises diners a stunning view! In this worthy alternative with a modern interior, the food is simpler, but absolutely the equal in terms of taste and culinary know-how. Be sure to try the pâté en croûte or tarte au chocolat!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
4786;Flamel;Switzerland;Lugano;Piazza Cioccaro 5, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;46.0045438;8.9498192;89;false;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Housed in the historic, recently renovated LUGANODANTE hotel, this restaurant serves excellent contemporary cuisine, with a simple menu at lunchtime and more elaborate fare in the evenings (tasting menus and à la carte), including carefully selected Swiss meat, herbs and salads from their own organic kitchen garden. There’s also a mixology bar which, in addition to unique cocktails (made from their own home-grown or locally sourced ingredients), offers an array of beers, fruit juices and home-made chocolates.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4787;au violon;Switzerland;Basel;Im Lohnhof 4, Basel, 4051, Switzerland;47.5548115;7.5884012;34;false;true;Classic French, Traditional Cuisine;This place exudes brasserie appeal thanks to its charming, stylish atmosphere and unfussy, honest seasonal menu, which also includes classic dishes. Despite its proximity to the centre, the location is pleasantly quiet – outside, an attractive terrace with shady trees beckons. There are well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays. Tip: Take the opportunity to visit Basel Historical Museum opposite.;Terrace;[]
4789;Albrun;Switzerland;Binn;Binntalstrasse 24, Binn, 3996, Switzerland;46.3637141;8.1847738;89;false;false;Regional Cuisine, International;The journey up to this enchanting mountain village is something of an adventure, but the food makes it worth it! In a rustic chalet-style setting, diners tuck into flavoursome regional dishes prepared with seasonal produce – the chef is always happy to showcase Swiss ingredients. The menu features mouthwatering options such as "Mario's Signature Black Forest" (beef sirloin, sour cherries, cocoa, kirsch 40% volume) and the "Alpen Tapas" starter. Friendly and charming front-of-house team.;Terrace;[]
4790;Nest- und Bietschhorn;Switzerland;Blatten im Lötschental;Talstrasse 16, Blatten im Lötschental, 3919, Switzerland;46.4140265;7.8075203;77;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, International;This cosy rustic restaurant enjoys a wonderful location at 1 490m above sea level. It is housed in the Lötschental's oldest hotel, which opened in 1868 (the modern Alpine-style guestrooms are gorgeous!) and serves exceptionally good food. The dishes are prepared with regional and seasonal ingredients. Tip: leave some room for one of the fabulous desserts! To accompany your meal, there are Valais wines. Overlooking the valley and mountains, the delightful lounge and terrace area is adorned with flowers and herbs. Shorter menu served 2-5pm.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4791;La Bottega di Mario;Switzerland;Zurich;Nüschelerstrasse 6, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3712182;8.5376506;64;true;false;Italian;Housed in a historical building (1913), La Bottega is a wonderfully inviting and lively ristorante and salumeria under one roof. Guests are spoilt for choice between the tasty dishes, clearly influenced by Ticino tradition, and the superb selection of salami and ham at the counter – here, the friendly mastri salumieri serve up the cold cuts. Tip: Try the house wine, Merlot di Ticino, poured from a six-litre bottle!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4792;Brasserie Le Gogant;Switzerland;Le Brassus;Route de France 8, Le Brassus, 1348, Switzerland;46.5810179;6.209927;25;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Both this restaurant and the designer Hôtel des Horlogers in which it is housed exude a stylish and upscale ambiance. A feast for the eyes awaits: aside from the elegant interior design, guests can relish the panoramic vistas of nature through expansive floor-to-ceiling windows, or opt to observe the captivating culinary artistry in the kitchen, visible through a generously sized glass pane. The seasonal dishes harmoniously blend classical and traditional flavours (with rich stocks and delectable sauces), presented in a contemporary fashion. The aesthetics and impeccable quality of these creations seamlessly complement the overall setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
4794;Muntanella;Switzerland;Arosa;Innere Poststrasse 269, Arosa, 7050, Switzerland;46.7747702;9.6647899;99;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The restaurant in the long-established Arosa Kulm Hotel, not far from the ski slopes, has adopted a dual concept: a simpler lunch menu featuring rösti, pasta, burgers etc, and a more ambitious menu in the evening. High-quality regional ingredients such as Grisons lamb or Val Lumnezia Alpine char take centre stage. The glass-walled walk-in wine cabinet is quite something. The terrace is a delightful spot from which to take in the mountain scenery.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4796;Philipp Blaser;Switzerland;Frutigen;Obere Bahnhofstrasse 10, Frutigen, 3714, Switzerland;46.5887963;7.6474038;81;true;true;International, Swiss;A popular place to eat! In this modern interior, where a relaxed atmosphere reigns, diners tuck into tasty and pleasingly unpretentious dishes. The culinary offering here features not only traditional and regional cuisine, but also Asian specialities – see the options in the "Thai Corner" section of the menu. There is also a pleasant terrace, and the small adjoining Hotel National has spruce, trendy guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4797;Les Curiades;Switzerland;Bernex;Vieux-Lully 10, Bernex, 1233, Switzerland;46.1635072;6.072308;65;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;A truly historic restaurant which has been serving food since 1850. The present chef has experience in some of the finest restaurants, and it shows! His cuisine is elegant and refined, including dishes such as chuck beef braised in beer (paying tribute to the chef’s Belgian origins) and a delicious vegetarian menu which is always available. An unqualified success!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4798;D'Chuchi;Switzerland;Schaffhausen;Brunnengasse 3, Schaffhausen, 8200, Switzerland;47.696097;8.6378773;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This small restaurant in a side street in the old town has a charming, down-to-earth and almost intimate atmosphere. It also serves really good food, which owner Jan Schmidlin creates by drawing almost exclusively on regional produce. Shining examples of his delicious modern seasonal fare include veal – saddle, Bäggli, Schupfnudeln (potato dumplings), lettuce, tarragon. There is a four-course set menu and an à la carte selection of dishes. You can also look forward to extremely pleasant, cordial hospitality.;;[]
4799;La Trattoria;Switzerland;Pontresina;Via Maistra 215, Pontresina, 7504, Switzerland;46.4877348;9.9074347;82;false;false;Italian;In the charming Hotel Walther, one of Pontresina's most emblematic hotels, this lovely Trattoria has an authentic, lively atmosphere and a stylish rustic feel. The appetising menu embraces all regions of Italy, with delicious pasta as the centrepiece and the focus firmly on flavour and freshness. Friendly Italian service and a good selection of wines.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4800;Anker;Switzerland;Teufen;Dorf 10, Teufen, 9053, Switzerland;47.3902777;9.3877987;21;true;true;International, Traditional Cuisine;On the first floor, wood panelling and low ceilings provide a cosy setting in which to choose the appealing mix of traditional and international dishes on the menu. The calves’ liver with sage, onions and rösti, for example, is delicious. A significant amount of the restaurant’s meat comes from its own butchery.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
4801;Bauernschänke;Switzerland;Zurich;Rindermarkt 24, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3724542;8.5450913;61;false;false;Country cooking, International;This gem of a restaurant is somewhat tucked away in a narrow alley in the city centre. In a historical setting with a cosy, rustic feel, diners tuck into international dishes such as king mackerel with radicchio tardivo, coconut and calamansi, as well as regional specialities such as pork belly gröstel (a traditional Tyrolean potato-based fry-up) with cucumber and butterhead lettuce. Order dishes to share à la carte or take a punt on the five-course surprise menu. The staff will be happy to provide wine recommendations. The well-curated selection is international and includes a decent range of natural wines (unfiltered and sulfite-free). Options are somewhat reduced at lunchtime.;Terrace;[]
4802;Golden Dragon;Switzerland;Davos Platz;Talstrasse 3, Davos Platz, 7270, Switzerland;46.7914101;9.8201958;82;false;false;Chinese, Sichuan;Davos's restaurant scene is not only about regional food – the Chinese restaurant at the Grischa hotel serves Cantonese and Szechuan-style cuisine. Tip: Some dishes are designed for sharing. If you fancy the Peking duck for two, be sure to pre-order (at least 48hr in advance). You can also combine many of the ingredients yourself according to your preferences. The upscale design features wood, stone, leather and a palette of elegant dark shades for a lovely ambience.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4803;Stiva Grischuna;Switzerland;Disentis;Via Cavardiras 3, Disentis, 7180, Switzerland;46.7059101;8.8560391;99;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In this traditional Bündnerhaus dating back over 300 years, the wood-panelled rooms abound with charm, and the down-to-earth cooking looks to the region for inspiration. Whether traditional dishes such as capuns and maluns or classics such as "Norbert's Stroganoff" and cordon bleu – this is simply tasty fare! The prices are also very reasonable. It's best to book. Locals also dine here.;Car park;[]
4804;Didi's Frieden;Switzerland;Zurich;Stampfenbachstrasse 32, Zurich, 8006, Switzerland;47.3792172;8.5435354;33;true;true;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;A fun dining experience is guaranteed at this delightful restaurant with its inviting decor – the wine glass chandeliers are certainly original! In the evening, there is a set menu comprising three, four or five courses. For each course, you have delicious options such as sea bass fillet on spaghetti alla chitarra with summer vegetables and octopus in a saffron sauce. There is a daily set menu at lunchtime, plus a nicely curated wine list. In summer, the gorgeous spacious terrace beckons.;Terrace;[]
4805;Café de Riex;Switzerland;Riex;Route de la Corniche 24, Riex, 1097, Switzerland;46.4933069;6.7362075;55;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Artisanal seasonal cuisine that showcases small-scale producers and local artisans, featuring hearty meat dishes (pork belly, kidneys, sweetbreads), sauces with real flavour, and delicious home-made ice creams flavoured with herbs from the garden (savory, sage, rosemary). Guests are in for a real treat in this café in the Vaud! The wine list is just as tempting, and features wines produced here in Riex.;;[]
4806;Gasthof zur Sonne;Switzerland;Stäfa;Seestrasse 37, Stäfa, 8712, Switzerland;47.2393856;8.7180143;92;true;false;Swiss, Traditional Cuisine;This 500-year-old heritage-protected inn is run by Patricia and Cäsar Meyer, who represent the second generation of their family here. He has a penchant for fish caught in Lake Zurich, just a stone's throw away – you can't get any fresher or more regional than that! The menu includes some truly rare specialities such as fried livers of fish from Lake Zurich. This attachment to regional produce is, not least, indicative of a commitment to sustainability. The cosy, very well-kept dining rooms are on the first floor, along with the gorgeous balcony terrace, which affords an unobstructed view of the lake. The staff are very attentive and cordial – you're sure to want to come back! Comfortable guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
4807;Eintracht;Switzerland;Kestenholz;Neue Strasse 6, Kestenholz, 4703, Switzerland;47.2814895;7.7534527;86;true;true;International, Traditional Cuisine;In this restaurant dating back to 1870, the dedicated Meier family have cultivated a sense of tradition while also introducing modern influences. This approach makes itself felt in the bistro and the more elegant restaurant area as well as in the cuisine – from classics such as veal cordon bleu to a gourmet set menu composed of three to five courses. Excellent wine selection. Simple daily specials are also available in the bistro.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4808;Zum Pflugstein;Switzerland;Erlenbach;Pflugsteinstrasse 71, Erlenbach, 8703, Switzerland;47.296981;8.6088592;52;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Considered the largest erratic boulder in the canton of Zurich, the Pﬂugstein is located close to this distinguished vineyard farmhouse and lends its name to its fabulous restaurant. The interior comprises an attractive wood-panelled space and a room with a fireplace, while outside there is a truly idyllic terrace. The service team overseen by the charming Jeannine Meili also deserves a mention. Tip: Try the tender boiled beef!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4809;Candela;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Sonnenstrasse 5, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.429436;9.3796912;18;true;false;International;This pleasantly lively place is located right in the city centre. With high ceilings, dark wood panelling, exposed brickwork and large windows, the restaurant is really atmospheric. As well as Swiss classics, the menu includes Mediterranean fare. There is also a decent selection of vegetarian and vegan dishes. Tip: Take the time to peruse the digestif list.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4810;Alla Cantina;Switzerland;Tegna;Piazza Gottardo Zurini 3, Tegna, 6652, Switzerland;46.1865363;8.7440995;84;true;true;Sicilian, Classic Cuisine;Although all the staff at this beautiful historic restaurant on the village square hail from Sicily, they have been working in Switzerland for years. Here, authentic Sicilian cuisine is served in a rustic and welcoming setting that also provides the backdrop for regular music events: the only concessions to Ticino are the polenta-based dishes. Our inspector particularly recommends the sarde in “Beccafico”(stuffed sardine roulade with breadcrumbs, sultanas, pine nuts and orange peel). There’s also a pleasantly cool and tranquil outdoor space for summer dining, plus four attractive and inviting guestrooms on the top floor.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4811;Buech;Switzerland;Herrliberg;Forchstrasse 267, Herrliberg, 8704, Switzerland;47.2887122;8.6298166;76;true;false;Country cooking;An absolutely delightful place: an idyllic location overlooking the village and Lake Zurich, a stylish dining area exuding traditional charm, a uniquely beautiful vine-kissed terrace affording stunning views! The few seats in the "wine huts" are much coveted. In the kitchen, the emphasis is on select produce from the region.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
4813;Netts Schützengarten;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Sankt Jakob Strasse 35, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4297309;9.379009;15;true;false;International, Country cooking;Housed in the Schützengarten Brewery building, this trendy restaurant is popular, not least among the locals! The decor here is lovely – rather rustic at the front, more elegant in the area to the rear. The terrace and beer garden are delightfully secluded – the brewing happens next door, so you're often greeted by pleasant malty aroma. Along with Swiss classics such as Züricher Geschnetzeltes (sliced veal served in a cream and mushroom sauce) or beef Stroganoff, the menu includes Asian-inspired dishes and vegetarian options. Tip: In the courtyard, the brewery has a small bottle museum – well worth a short detour.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4814;Zer Schlucht;Switzerland;Saas-Fee;Blomattenweg 2, Saas-Fee, 3906, Switzerland;46.1069105;7.9280152;65;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This place boasts a fantastic location right next to the rugged and dramatic Saas-Fee gorge, through which the Feeru Vispa glacial stream flows. Hotel La Gorge offers comfortable, modern accommodation and a delightful dining experience at its restaurant, Zer Schlucht, serving regional and seasonal cuisine in a charming Alpine setting. The mouthwatering options on the menu include classics such as ossobuco, specialties such as Thurgau apple-pomace fed pork with apricot, chanterelles, rosemary and spaetzle, as well as vegan dishes such as gnocchi, mushrooms, chard and pine nuts. Request a table by the floor-to-ceiling windows for stunning views of the gorge and forest. Shorter menu available at lunchtime.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4815;Le Bologne;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue Necker 9, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2075881;6.1407696;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Next to the Fine Arts School, this vintage bistro cuts a fine figure with its cement tiles, hanging globe lights and bare bulbs, as well as its bar, banquettes and bistro chairs. The dishes feature high-quality, carefully prepared seasonal ingredients: celeriac "risotto" and foie gras, confit lamb shoulder, cumin, asparagus and labne...;Terrace;[]
4816;Café du Levant;Switzerland;Aire-la-Ville;Rue du Vieux Four 53, Aire-la-Ville, 1288, Switzerland;46.1912667;6.0431852;87;true;true;French, Farm to table;In a quiet little village in an attractive rural setting, you will find this warm and welcoming restaurant with a down-to-earth vibe. The property backs onto fields and the fresh air is a real tonic. They serve flavoursome seasonal cuisine and regional French fare, which you can accompany with your choice from a good selection of wines from the Geneva region. Lovely terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4817;Pensiun Aldier;Switzerland;Sent;Plaz 154, Sent, 7554, Switzerland;46.8169316;10.3376189;93;true;true;Swiss;If you like your food straightforward and pared down to the essentials without compromising on taste, then you'll love the excellent Engadine cuisine here. In the pleasingly unpretentious restaurant of the charming little hotel of the same name, the dishes forgo any frills and instead focus on select, fresh local produce. Good wines at fair prices. Shorter menu at lunchtime.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4818;SALZHAUS;Switzerland;Solothurn;Landhausquai 15a, Solothurn, 4500, Switzerland;47.2063369;7.5367437;61;true;true;Contemporary, International;An attractive blend of urban cool and historical ambiance is the backdrop here and the exposed old brickwork certainly adds to the effect! On regular evenings, the kitchen serves up regionally inspired dishes with an international twist, either as a set menu or à la carte. The chicken cordon bleu with ham, Gruyère, Schupfnudeln (finger-shaped potato dumplings) and spring vegetables is an especially delicious example. Thursday evenings are dedicated to Japanese fusion cuisine. More limited options at lunchtime. Attentive, charming and adept service. Thanks to the beautiful old town location right by the Aare River, tables on the waterfront terrace are coveted in summer.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4819;Gommerstuba;Switzerland;Ernen;Ernerstrasse 53, Ernen, 3995, Switzerland;46.3918298;8.1333041;18;false;false;International;The friendly hosts here serve contemporary cuisine, which can be ordered à carte or as a set menu – there is also a vegetarian set menu. Many regional wines are featured. A restaurant decor blending wood and stone makes for a pleasant atmosphere. The lovely terrace is also inviting!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4820;Bären;Switzerland;Grub;Halten 112, Grub, 9035, Switzerland;47.4428822;9.4975401;51;false;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Diners come here for straightforward seasonal cuisine that is not only prepared with fresh produce but, most importantly, is utterly delicious. In the evening, you can opt for the set menu, which comprises three to six courses, or order à la carte. At lunchtime, the options are more limited, with the three- to four-course "Gourmet Express" set menu, and an à la carte selection. The house specialty is Parmesan cheese wheel spaghetti. The lovingly decorated Gourmetstübli is a particularly appealing space. There is also an attractive room for events.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4821;Osteria della Bottega;Switzerland;Geneva;Grand Rue 3, Geneva, 1204, Switzerland;46.2024354;6.1447982;51;true;false;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;This lively restaurant is located on a steep little street in Geneva's old town. Against a chic industrial-style backdrop with an open kitchen, diners are treated to modern, seasonally inspired Italian cuisine and fine wines, plus attentive and friendly service. It's best to book, as Osteria is very popular! Across the street there is a lovely terrace.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4822;Collonge Café;Switzerland;Collonge-Bellerive;Chemin du Château-de-Bellerive 3, Collonge-Bellerive, 1245, Switzerland;46.2539711;6.2040169;98;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This modern restaurant boasts a great location next to the historical town hall and has a charming terrace laid out in the garden. The seasonally inspired menu successfully brings together modern Italian and French cuisine, while keeping an open mind when it comes to international influences. Cordial and competent service. Tip: the competitively priced lunch menu.;Terrace;[]
4823;Rigiblick Züriberg Beiz;Switzerland;Zurich;Germaniastrasse 99, Zurich, 8044, Switzerland;47.3882068;8.5533404;72;false;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;In this restaurant in the upper reaches of the city, a rather elegant yet relaxed atmosphere awaits you. The kitchen team showcases in-season regional produce, which is used to create really delicious dishes. You can order à la carte or opt for the "Genuss Menü" comprising three or four courses. Maître d' and owner Vreni Giger provides service with a personal touch. In summer, head for the leafy terrace. Tip: It is easy to get here by taking tram no 10 or the Funicular Rigiblick.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4824;Zum Kaiser Franz;Switzerland;Zug;Vorstadt 8, Zug, 6300, Switzerland;47.1685757;8.5147907;94;false;false;Austrian, Seasonal Cuisine;Here, you won't want to miss out on the Austrian specialities such as Backhenderl (breaded fried chicken), Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) or Topfenknödel (curd dumplings)! Available in a large or small portion, the Wiener schnitzel is a real highlight. Be sure to ask about the fish of the day, freshly caught from the adjacent Lake Zug. As well as the good food, diners can look forward to professional and attentive service in a cosy and stylish setting – the Austrian charm of the decor is the perfect match for the cuisine. The lakeside location provides a lovely backdrop. The nearby multi-storey car park is handy.;Terrace;[]
4825;Café de Peney;Switzerland;Satigny;Route d'Aïre-La-Ville 130, Satigny, 1242, Switzerland;46.2006243;6.04439;60;false;true;French, Traditional Cuisine;Located on an arm of the River Rhône, this popular, bustling eatery, decked out in a profusion of nostalgic paraphernalia, calls to mind a vintage picture postcard and also boasts a wisteria-covered terrace. Fine ingredients are consummately and delicately crafted into delicious dishes, examples of which are the flawlessly cooked Black Angus steak or raspberry tartlet with a refreshing raspberry sorbet.;Terrace;[]
4826;Linde;Switzerland;Fislisbach;Niederrohrdorferstrasse 1, Fislisbach, 5442, Switzerland;47.435373;8.2913914;53;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;The secret of Linde's success is a formula of classic Swiss cuisine made from good ingredients coupled with reasonable prices. A lively atmosphere reigns in this attractive, well-run place with its various dining spaces, large bar area and glassed-in kitchen. Steak tartare and Zürcher Geschnetzeltes (veal) are among the permanent fixtures on the menu. For lunch, the offer is somewhat reduced. The wonderful terrace comes into its own in summer, and there are well-kept guestrooms too.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4827;Balm - Bistro;Switzerland;Meggen;Balmstrasse 3, Meggen, 6045, Switzerland;47.0445077;8.3680068;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;The charming and laid-back second restaurant at Hotel Balm also serves ambitious cuisine. This can be enjoyed in the form of a set menu of three or four courses which you can mix and match as you see fit. Options include dishes such as Lake Lucerne whitefish fillet with a champagne sauce, morels, leaf spinach and new potatoes. It is also possible to dine à la carte. At lunchtime on Wednesday to Friday, the moderately priced two-course set menu draws a crowd. The terrace is a delightful spot.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4828;Mont-Rouge;Switzerland;Haute-Nendaz;Route de la Télécabine 23, Haute-Nendaz, 1997, Switzerland;46.1823205;7.2954154;62;true;false;International;The standout features of this mountain-style restaurant are its pleasant, elegant atmosphere and its chef, who has been dedicated to his work here for 20 years. He invites you on a culinary journey, with Swiss, French and international dishes inspired by local produce. Another option is the small adjoining brasserie and its daily specials, including poached sole roulade with home-made sauerkraut and champagne beurre blanc… a real treat! Pleasant guestrooms available.;Terrace;[]
4829;Dal Mulin;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Plazza dal Mulin 4, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4989712;9.8395815;94;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the heart of St Moritz makes diners feel very much at home with its wonderfully stylish and modern take on rustic decor and its charming and attentive front-of-house team. As for the food, it is pleasingly uncomplicated, yet carefully considered and subtle. The wine selection is outstanding – and they even have their own wine shop.;Interesting wine list;[]
4830;Josef;Switzerland;Zurich;Gasometerstrasse 24, Zurich, 8005, Switzerland;47.383905;8.5290737;41;false;true;European Contemporary;This trendy, urban restaurant and bar is located in the middle of a residential area in Kreis 5 (Zürich's fifth district). The atmosphere is lively and bustling, and in light of their interesting concept, it comes as no surprise that the place is well frequented: they serve tasty modern European cuisine with dishes in starter-sized portions (four is a good number to order). Mouthwatering options include the likes of veal shank ragout with mashed potatoes, confit garlic and Trevisano. Alternatively, there is a five-course set menu – available in omnivore and vegetarian versions. Good wine list and cocktail selection.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4831;Gasthof zum goldenen Kreuz;Switzerland;Frauenfeld;Zürcherstrasse 134, Frauenfeld, 8500, Switzerland;47.554156;8.8948547;77;false;true;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is steeped in tradition, and much sought after for its excellent seasonal cuisine. At lunchtime, you can order à la carte or opt for one of four three-course set menus. In the evening, there is a tasting menu in addition to an à la carte selection. Attentive service comes courtesy of a friendly and well-organised front-of-house team. Goethe himself was a guest here – the pretty Goethe-Stübli is named after him – and the well-preserved, painted panelling from the 17C adds rustic charm. The terrace is a delightful spot, secluded from the street by abundant greenery. Modern, functional guestrooms are available for overnight stays. Tip for motorists: public car park behind the building.;Terrace;[]
4832;Les six;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 5-15-25 Minamiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0047, Japan;35.651815;139.722428;61;true;false;French;The chef mixes his own sensibilities into cuisine rooted in French bistro fare. The blackboard menu is a medley of authentic dishes and à la carte items made with seasonal ingredients. Generally, an appetiser and a main course is the perfect amount, but some items can be ordered as half portions, so ask your server.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4833;Ma Poule;Japan;Tokyo;2-19-17 Nishikata, Bunkyo-ku, Tokyo, 113-0024, Japan;35.716254;139.757224;38;true;true;French;The chef opened a small restaurant, Ma Poule to celebrate the appeal of Jura, in eastern France. This region, with its beautiful forests, valleys and wetlands and its wonderful ingredients and people, made a profound impression on the chef. Chicken and morels in sauce vin jaune is a Jura dish in which the chef takes great pride. This dish is paired with specially produced yellow wine. The façade and interior, and even proprietress’s clothing, are yellow as well. A restaurant filled with love of Jura.;Air conditioning;[]
4834;BRASSERIE POISSON ROUGE;Japan;Tokyo;1-53-8 Oi, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 140-0014, Japan;35.604464;139.73374;29;false;false;French;The draw is the generosity of the portions served throughout, from appetiser to dessert. The menu is a tour of France’s regions, with regional favourites including salad Niçoise, fish purée soup and cassoulet de Toulouse. Roast lamb or duck smothered in sauce is a fulfilling meal. Each plateful expresses the chef’s simple message: French cuisine satisfying to both belly and soul. Wine makes the perfect companion.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4835;Fry-ya;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-32-11 Takadanobaba, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 169-0075, Japan;35.71082;139.70387;17;false;true;Tonkatsu, Yoshoku;Tonkatsu, seafood, vegetables—select the ingredients of your choice and the kitchen will prepare an original ‘mix fry’ just for you. As the name says, this is the ‘fry house’. Daytime fare consists of set meals of a variety of items. In the evening, multi-course prix fixe is the theme, with each morsel fried and served fresh. In a couple of unique twists, different types of breadcrumbs are used, depending on the main ingredient, and some items are fried in lard while others are fried in sesame oil. Chicken tenderloin is fried at a low heat carefully calculated to cook every part of the meat.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4836;le bistrot des bleus;Japan;Tokyo;2F, EAT PLAY WORKS, 5-4-16 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.650758;139.721829;23;true;true;French;The ‘blue’ of this ‘bistro of the blues’ refers to the blue in the French flag, which represents liberty. The young chef and sommelier enthusiastically pour out their passion for French cuisine. Home cooking from throughout France, such as choucroute and bouillabaisse, are available à la carte.  Doors open at 3pm. Its location in a narrow restaurant row and the casual atmosphere within capture the bistro’s spirit of freedom.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4837;Japanese Ramen Gokan;Japan;Tokyo;2-57-2 Higashiikebukuro, Toshima-ku, Tokyo, 170-0013, Japan;35.732982;139.717911;31;false;false;Ramen;‘Japanese ramen’ was added to the name from a desire to spread Japan’s culinary culture to the world. As befits the name, the shop specialises in domestic ingredients. It serves two flavours of ramen: soy sauce and salt. The soup layers multiple sources of flavour on top of each other: free-range chicken, Berkshire pork, clams and mussels. Cooking over charcoal introduces a Japanese element. The food looks great, the aroma whets the appetite, the flavour captivates: this ramen sets all five senses tingling.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4838;Pot-Bouille;Japan;Tokyo;5-22-1 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.648619;139.717783;63;false;false;French;The softly lit counter creates a stylish mood conducive to gatherings of friends. French favourites such as rillettes and ratatouille share the menu with international items like tripe, shrimp spring rolls and tom yam goong ramen, stoking the imagination. The restaurant’s name is French for ‘hodgepodge’, an apt metaphor for Pot-Bouille’s medley of gastronomic influences, somehow in perfect harmony. A free-spirited style all its own.;Counter dining;[]
4839;YAKUMO;Japan;Tokyo;3-6-15 Higashiyama, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0043, Japan;35.65014;139.686847;19;false;true;Ramen;Customers flock to Yakumo for its famous wonton ramen. Two types of wonton, one with pork infused with the tang of ginger and the other with shrimp cooked to delightful texture, each play their part in the dish’s popularity. To enjoy both, order the special ‘Tokusei’ ramen. The choice of soups is ‘White dashi’ made with white soy sauce, ‘Black dashi’ using rich, dark soy sauce, and ‘Mix’, a mixture of the two. And choose from thin noodles or flat. This flexibility to tailor your order is a special pleasure of Yakumo.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4840;Sushidokoro Shigeru;Japan;Tokyo;15 Funamachi, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0006, Japan;35.691759;139.721697;77;true;true;Sushi;With his restaurant, the chef depicts a local unassuming sushi shop. The small counter fosters an air of kinship, as does the friendly service. His conviction shows in the meticulous care he pours into each item. Dishes are not only salted, marinated and simmered, they are prepared with knife techniques so practiced as to seem effortless, then formed by hand to finish. An omakase set menu with snacks is on offer, but the focus here is on nigiri sushi, what a sushi shop originally was.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4841;Hatsuogawa;Japan;Tokyo;2-8-4 Kaminarimon, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0034, Japan;35.709758;139.794528;74;false;true;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;Founded in 1907, this restaurant is run by the proprietress and her son. Though the building is new, the interior exudes the same charm diners have loved for decades, parlaying an unchanging old-school elegance to a new generation. Unagi is prepared in the old style, time-consuming in its attention to detail but well worth the wait. Side dishes such as steamed egg custard and soft-boiled soybeans help pass the time until the eel is ready.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4842;ROZZO SICILIA;Japan;Tokyo;1-1-12 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.646974;139.731756;48;false;false;Italian;A Sicilian eatery run by a chef and waiter who struck up a friendship during the former’s apprenticeship. Enveloped in the sunny mood of southern Italy, guests delight in the cuisine of Chef Nakamura and the service of the host, Abe. With fried chickpeas, seafood couscous and cannoli of local confectionaries, the duo serve up authentic flavours of Sicily in a simple, honest way. The ever-present lemon wedges on the table are a nice Sicilian touch.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4844;Tempura Kakiage Yukimura;Japan;Tokyo;6-13-13 Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0004, Japan;35.661982;139.75356;17;true;true;Tempura;‘Cheerful, fun, exciting’ sums up the credo of the owner-chef. The convivial atmosphere and friendly service attracts customers of every generation. The menu reflects this positive attitude, with bowls of rice with toppings, teishoku set meals and à la carte items available at both lunch and dinner. The dish of fame is the kakiage-don, a bowl of rice loaded up with shrimp. The chef treasures the advice he learned as an apprentice: ‘Offer top-rate food at third-rate prices’. He’s always smiling, trading jokes with his guests.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4845;Osobano Kouga;Japan;Tokyo;2-14-5 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.660055;139.722767;26;false;false;Soba;Taste sake and snacks while dining on soba. Think of the culture of the soba shop, the beloved essence of Edo popular culture, plunked down near Nishi-Azabu Intersection for the modern generation to enjoy, and you have the atmosphere of Osobano Kouga. Evenings bring prix fixe presentations that encourage you to linger over cups of sake. Tensui, tempura soba with the soba removed, is an old-timey snack. Soba in season and appetisers of vegetable or fish of the day are a delight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4847;Kinoshita;Japan;Tokyo;3-37-1 Yoyogi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0053, Japan;35.681813;139.69341;34;true;false;French;Jellied pork, soupe de poisson, beef simmered in red wine – filled with respect for classic French cuisine, the chef is keen to serve dishes that warm the soul. The style is universal yet prepared with a unique touch, honed by constant improvement. A collection of Bourgogne wines that have aged along with the restaurant await the discerning tippler.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
4848;Tachigui Sushi Tonari;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-8-7 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.655547;139.734852;43;true;true;Sushi;Sushi Tonari means ‘sushi next door’, and indeed Tachigui Sushi Tonari is tucked away next to its flagship restaurant. The intimate space, quick turnover and experience of the youthful staff achieve a comfortable informality. Ordering is refreshingly casual, too: requesting one piece at a time is fine. The prevailing theme is ‘vinegar and sushi’. Rice seasoned with rice vinegar harmonises beautifully with the oil of the fish. Reservations, orders and billing are all managed on a digital system. Standing and eating, Edo’s street-stall dining culture, updated for the modern era.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4849;L'AMITIE;Japan;Tokyo;2-9-12 Takadanobaba, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 169-0075, Japan;35.712099;139.707969;18;false;false;French;Apprenticing at a bistro in Paris, the chef was captivated by its lively energy. At L'AMITIE, he has put down roots in Takadanobaba with this intimate diner where you can feel like part of the daily life of France. Offerings include meat terrine À la campagne, cassoulet and beef cheek simmered in red wine. À la carte items are prepared for two, so you can enjoy sharing. Savour Gallic culinary culture and the ambience of the French countryside.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4850;REI;Japan;Tokyo;10-8 Motoyoyogicho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0062, Japan;35.670208;139.684517;79;false;false;Chinese;The name REI comes from reimeiki, ‘a new beginning’. The décor is monotone, the food pairing is wine, the fare is modern Chinese. The familiar standards of Chinese dining are on the menu, including Sichuan-style bean curd, steamed chicken with spicy sauce and stir-fried shrimp in chilli sauce. The chef deftly matches home-style seasonings with seasonal ingredients. This is neighbourhood Chinese food refined with a distinctive inspiration, such as twice-cooked pork with spring cabbage, and sweet-and-sour pork.;Air conditioning;[]
4852;Le cabaret;Japan;Tokyo;8-8 Motoyoyogicho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0062, Japan;35.670097;139.685344;47;true;true;French;The restaurant’s name evokes a French nightclub with a stage. Service is informal and relaxed: as music plays in the background, the staff greet customers in their everyday clothes. Dishes are served in traditional style, with each table sharing a single plate. With the feel of a Parisian bistro, this was also the place that first started serving natural wine. With an atmosphere that says ‘café’ and cuisine that says ‘bistro’, the fun of the cabaret never changes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
4853;Ma Cuisine;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-2-14 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.660937;139.7267;60;true;false;French;The chef’s dedication to strong relationships with producers around the country stems from his choice of ingredients. His talents are on full display in bistro fare such as ratatouille and bouillabaisse. An abundance of à la carte items makes choosing part of the fun. Pork preparation is tailored to the characteristics of each cut. Charcuterie, petit salé of boneless rib, and spareribs grilled smothered in herb-seasoned breadcrumbs are all highlights.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4854;Le Monde Gourmand;Japan;Tokyo;2-17-15 Midorigaoka, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 152-0034, Japan;35.608524;139.672178;100;false;true;French;A chef with passion for his culinary art and a proprietress schooled in the ways of graceful service enfold this French restaurant in a warm atmosphere of bustling activity. Dishes listed on the blackboard are orthodox: pâté en croûte, baked fish in pastry, beef cheek stewed in red wine. The restaurant’s name means ‘the world of the aficionado of food’. The world of the good old bistro lures us in.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4855;Les Copains de DOMINIQUE BOUCHET;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 5-1-8 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671997;139.761755;55;true;false;French;A bistro by Dominique Bouchet. The theme is ‘bistronomy’: a bistro with added gastronomic enhancements. Favourites such as pâté en croûte and steak frites are everyday standards in France. Lobster macaroni is a Bouchet speciality that captures the hearts of Parisian epicures. Savour the profundity of French cuisine from popular fare to modern haute cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
4856;Mejiro Shunkotei;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Trad Mejiro, 2-39-1 Mejiro, Toshima-ku, Tokyo, 171-0031, Japan;35.721514;139.70736;28;true;true;Yoshoku;‘Novel yet nostalgic Western food’ is the theme here. Hamburger steaks with dollops of demi-glace sauce and gratin dressed in silky smooth béchamel sauce are prepared in time-honoured ways, bringing back the flavours of the good old days. Decompression-prepared salad offers rich flavours and uniquely fresh textures. Unchanging methods combine with advanced cooking techniques declare a new approach to Western favourites.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4857;there is ramen;Japan;Tokyo;3-10-16 Amanuma, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0032, Japan;35.70737;139.618381;43;false;false;Ramen;This shop’s message is “Life is well lived that appreciates a nice bowl of ramen”. As a young man, the chef learned these words from his grandfather, and they still reverberate in his heart. Like many from the Mogami region of Yamagata Prefecture, he uses light soy sauce. He seeks a natural flavour for his ramen by using dried sardines and the umami of meat to good effect. Ramen here reminds customers of their hometowns. A photo of his grandfather, smiling kindly, watches over the room.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4858;Cristiano's;Japan;Tokyo;1-51-10 Tomigaya Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0063, Japan;35.668592;139.689062;92;false;true;Portuguese;Portuguese cuisine seems distant yet familiar to Japanese people. The word ‘Takoten’ is often heard in kitchens and dining halls and refers to the octopus fritters that recreate the local tastes of Portugal and is also the roots of tempura. Local wine brings out the flavour of this local-style cuisine – flavours that win over the local palate with tastes that seem somehow familiar. The owner-chef’s speciality is bacalhau (dried cod).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
4859;SUSHI KOURIN;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 11-10 Kamiyamacho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0047, Japan;35.66305;139.694706;38;false;false;Sushi;To encourage diners to drop in casually, the chef even accepts orders for single pieces. A blackboard crammed with lists of sushi items and snacks shows his commitment to service. This is the joy of the local sushi shop, where you can choose your items as you sit face-to-face with the chef. While easy to order, each item is still painstakingly prepared. He hangs out his shop curtain at 3 PM, so guests can start drinking while it’s still light out.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4860;SOBAHOUSE KONJIKI HOTOTOGISU;Japan;Tokyo;2-4-1 Shinjuku, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0022, Japan;35.68878;139.7083;85;false;true;Ramen;The shop curtain reads, ‘If the cuckoo (hototogisu) won’t sing, I will want to make it sing’. This maxim, which summed up the character of Toyotomi Hideyoshi, who unified Japan in the 16C, also exemplifies the chef’s labour of culinary love. The clam soup evolved out of endless trial-and-error to find just the right umami components. Each bowl of ramen finely tunes the affinity of the noodles with the more than 60 other ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4861;T'astous;Japan;Tokyo;2-5-21 Minamiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0047, Japan;35.649953;139.737004;21;false;false;French;T’astous presents as a ‘neo-bistro’, the sort of chic bistro you might find in Paris. Regional cooking arranged for a modern sensibility. The chef trained in the south of France, so he excels with foie gras and truffles that are this region’s gift to the world. The restaurant name is the word for a black-truffle canapé in the Cahors dialect. He expresses through his cuisine the wonder he felt upon tasting this delicacy in southwestern France.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4862;Washokuya Taichi;Japan;Tokyo;3-36-14 Kitasenzoku, Ota-ku, Tokyo, 145-0062, Japan;35.604993;139.685082;76;false;true;Izakaya;The owner-chef’s experience in Japanese cuisine is immediately evident. Goma tofu (tofu-like dish of sesame paste) is normally served with sesame sauce, but in summer tomato jelly is substituted. In this season, fragrant roast corn with butter soy sauce is recommended. The corn is shaved from the cob to make it easier to eat, reminding one of food stalls at temple festivals. The pork fillet cutlet sandwich amazes with its super-thick-cut pork. Japanese cuisine prepared with consummate skill.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4863;Tohakuan Karibe;Japan;Tokyo;4-23-19 Kasuya, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 157-0063, Japan;35.663492;139.602984;71;false;false;Soba;With the temperament of an artist, the chef places everything in its proper proportion. Gathering unpolished buckwheat from Nagano and Niigata, he grinds the two together, checking moisture by hand to produce nihachi and juwari noodles. Soba and broth are served in harmony: as seiro, accompanied by soup redolent of katsuobushi, or as kake, steeped in hot katsuobushi broth. Side dishes are soba-shop favourites, such as Pacific herring simmered for days or seafood and buckwheat flour wrapped in nori and deep-fried.;Air conditioning;[]
4864;Tonkatsu Narikura;Japan;Tokyo;4-33-9 Naritahigashi, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 166-0015, Japan;35.697698;139.638723;17;true;true;Tonkatsu;The pork cutlets, refined through a process of tinkering and improvement, are surprisingly light-coloured, thanks to coating in low-carb breadcrumbs and frying at low heat. The pork juices cling to the delicate batter, not going to waste. In addition to loin, tenderloin and belly, there’s even a mille-feuille cutlet. The chef’s approach is trial-and-error: time-consuming and with mistakes along the way, but the result is success. A unique tonkatsu born of theory, experience and instinct.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4866;Homemade Ramen Muginae;Japan;Tokyo;6-11-10 Minamioi, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 140-0013, Japan;35.590775;139.732803;47;false;false;Ramen;One of the essential processes of wheat cultivation is treading the wheat. When the wheat plants bud, farmers tread them down so they grow up strong. The owner-chef named his shop Muginae, ‘wheat seedling’, as a prayer that it would grow as it overcame adversity, a hopeful shoot on the forest floor. Ramen, fragrant and homemade, has a smooth finish. Soup is seasoned with soy sauce, salt and dried sardines. Word has spread like wildfire, and now customers tread the streets of Minamioi from early morning for a cup of this restaurant’s delicious broth.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4867;Yakitori Abe;Japan;Tokyo;3-3-4 Kamiosaki, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 141-0021, Japan;35.633996;139.718071;35;true;false;Yakitori;The chef assembles the sequence of yakitori chicken cuts according to customer preferences. To their delight, he starts beer drinkers off with chicken breast and wine tipplers with chicken heart. Seasoning is simple: salt, sauce or soy sauce, depending on the item—whichever best brings out the flavour. The top recommendation is the chicken wings, which ticks all three boxes. The skin is fragrant, the meat and fat are sweet, and the umami unique to meat on the bone.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4868;Torishige;Japan;Tokyo;2-6-5 Yoyogi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0053, Japan;35.687987;139.698876;24;true;false;Pork;A pork-skewer eatery established in 1949. Yuji Sakamaki, third owner-chef, prizes the flavours he remembers from his youth. Meat-stuffed bell peppers are a popular skewer item from the days of the first chef. Beef dishes are a relative novelty, having been introduced by Sakamaki’s predecessor. For his part, the set menu Sakamaki added allows diners to enjoy dishes from the good old days. Guided by his pet saying, “lifelong training”, he preserves the flavours of Torishige across the generations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4869;grill GRAND;Japan;Tokyo;3-24-6 Asakusa, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0032, Japan;35.716956;139.797534;86;true;false;Yoshoku;The charm of a Showa-era (1926–1989) Western eatery. In true Asakusa style, the whole family pitches in. Brothers race to finish shredding the cabbage, with the winner allowed to prepare food. This time it falls on the elder brother to wait on tables. Hamburger steak, rice-stuffed omelette, beef stew and other ‘Japanese-Western’ favourites remind patrons of the good old days. With the teachings of their grandfather and father in their hearts, the family upholds the goodness of Asakusa.;Air conditioning;[]
4871;Yakitori SANKA;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 64-4 Yaraicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0805, Japan;35.703438;139.732869;47;true;false;Yakitori;The spirit in Takamasa Yamanaka’s heart is one of giving back to his home region. To showcase the appeal of his native Kochi, he sources Tosa chicken. The shop’s name is a portmanteau combining characters from his name and that of his hometown, Kahoku. After dusting his skewers with sun-dried salt from eastern Kochi Prefecture, he grills them over Tosa binchotan charcoal, another point of hometown pride. He lists the names of his producers as a way to express his gratitude.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4872;Ramen Break Beats;Japan;Tokyo;4-21-19 Meguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0063, Japan;35.633515;139.698778;36;false;false;Ramen;‘Break Beats’, the name of a musical genre, is the perfect name for this shop, whose chef wears two hats as an active DJ. The clear base soup uses Amakusa Daio chicken, while black maitake mushrooms add umami for the soy sauce-flavoured ramen, and freshwater mussels does the same for salt-flavoured ramen. Ingredients such as smoked pork fillet and fried enoki mushrooms switch up the flavours. A catchy remix of old ramen favourites.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4873;Sasaki Seimenjo;Japan;Tokyo;4-26-10 Nishiogikita, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0042, Japan;35.708552;139.592358;94;false;false;Ramen;The chef ’s aim is to create a ramen shop beloved by locals. He sources ingredients from greengrocers and butchers in Nishiogi, treasuring his interactions with local people. The distance from the train station is also a blessing, as neighbourhood schoolchildren and their families can be seen sitting shoulder-to-shoulder, happily slurping noodles. As befits the ‘Seimenjo’, or ‘noodle-maker’, in the name, his use of Japanese wheat is a selling point. In addition to standard thin noodles, he also offers flat noodles. The miso flavour is a much-anticipated treat in autumn and winter.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4874;IRUCA TOKYO;Japan;Tokyo;4-12-12 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.664771;139.731691;33;true;true;Ramen;The chef displays his originality in each bowl as he pursues a unique interpretation of ramen. Broths of clam, spiny lobster, free-range chicken and beef combine to create a soup of satisfying depth. Paste of porcini mushrooms and truffles switches up the flavour of soy-sauce ramen. Salt ramen is infused with yuzu flavoured butter to impart a creamy fragrance. ‘Iruca’ comes from the Japanese for ‘dolphin’, a symbol of peace and a message of friendship to spread across the oceans.;Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4875;Kuhara;Japan;Tokyo;2-25-38 Higashi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0011, Japan;35.65356;139.707711;53;false;true;Japanese;The friendly couple who run Kuhara—the chef a disciple of Japanese cuisine, the proprietress a welcoming figure in kappo wear—make us instantly feel at home. The signature fare is duck. In addition to salt-grilled duck, they offer chilled breast stew in summer, and a hot duck stew called jibuni in winter. Dried baby fish with soy and pepper on rice and Kokusho miso soup of root vegetables are must-try items. Unripe pepper is gathered by the couple and their children when they visit her hometown in Tochigi Prefecture. Kokusho miso soup brings back memories for the chef, who sampled it when he applied to a restaurant specialising in shojin ryori.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4878;HARU CHAN Ramen;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Shimbashi Ekimae Ichigokan, 2-20-15 Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0004, Japan;35.666214;139.759538;53;false;false;Ramen;The Chinese soba noodles feature a rich stock made from pork and dried sardines, flavoured with salt and lard. The soup is filled to the very rim of the bowl, a thoughtful gesture by the chef to ensure the noodles stay hot until the last bite. The pork is stewed until exquisitely tender and sliced just before serving, preserving its savoury flavour. Adding a touch of visual charm, the bowl is uniquely adorned with flower-shaped and ball-shaped wheat gluten bread. The generous portion sizes guarantee that you’ll leave feeling satisfied.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4880;Katsuyoshi;Japan;Tokyo;3-4-11 Nihombashiningyocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0013, Japan;35.686215;139.781217;27;false;false;Tonkatsu;You’ll find Katsuyoshi in a back-alley of Ningyocho. The interior of the shop, a refurbished traditional home, uses recycled wood to convey a retro feel. In the kitchen, you’ll see two copper pots. When deep-frying pork cutlets, the owner-chef uses hotter oil for some dishes and cooler oil for others. Fried seafood morsels such as scallop and tiger prawn are popular. If you get a seat at the counter, you can watch the chef’s work, which starts with preparing the meat.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4881;Ginza Katsukami;Japan;Tokyo;5F, 5-6-10  Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670726;139.763641;89;true;false;Tonkatsu;Tonkatsu served prix fixe using a wide range of pork cuts. The restaurant works with multiple brands of pork to make every bite of freshly deep-fried tenderloin, loin and shoulder count. The cut face is placed at the top so that none of the juices are wasted, bringing out the full true flavour of the pork. A variety of other fried items can be added, such as crab croquettes and deep-fried breaded minced pork. Shaved ice with your choice of syrups is a post-prandial treat to look forward to.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4882;BISTRO GLOUTON;Japan;Tokyo;2-33-7 Ikejiri, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 154-0001, Japan;35.648675;139.682312;27;true;false;French;From down a back alley in Ikejiri, light beckons from a counter bistro. Draw closer and a crowded blackboard lists such a range of items, from French regional cuisine to Western-influenced dishes like hamburger steaks and croquettes, that you’ll hardly be able to choose. The menu doesn’t change, to keep quality consistent and high. ‘Glouton’ refers to someone who enjoys their food whole-heartedly. Every item here will tickle your fancy, and once you’ve sampled the food here, you’ll want to return.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4883;roku;Japan;Tokyo;4-1-6 Yoyogi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0053, Japan;35.679151;139.693748;87;true;true;French;The name, meaning ‘six’, comes from this couple’s birthday month, June. The aim is to serve the Sangubashi area with French cuisine rooted firmly in the region. The chef adds a unique touch with ingredients sourced from producers with whom he has strong relations. Edible wild plants, mushrooms and game are products of his native Nagano. Desserts prepared from seasonal fruits are handled by the proprietress. At the counter, which appropriately seats six, the chef’s explanations create a feeling of intimacy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4884;LA BETTOLA da Ochiai;Japan;Tokyo;1-21-2 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.672764;139.771142;87;false;false;Italian;‘La Bettola’ is Italian for ‘the dining hall’. With its casual atmosphere and fare that is good value for money, this trattoria draws throngs of guests day after day. The menu is crammed with regional cuisines and seasonal dishes. The prix fixe selection allows a choice of items—you’ll find it hard to make up your mind. For the appetiser, we recommend the combination platter, generous in both portions and variety. Sea urchin spaghetti is a perennial favourite.;Air conditioning;[]
4885;Negima;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-31-19 Kitaotsuka, Toshima-ku, Tokyo, 170-0004, Japan;35.734057;139.729926;33;false;false;Japanese;Negima has the feel of a small eatery, with the kimono-clad proprietress serving customers. The decor, featuring ship manifests for the Sea of Japan merchant fleet and newspapers from the Taisho period, fosters a retro atmosphere. The name is from negima-nabe, a stew loved by the people of Edo. The signature dish owes its provenance to the proprietress’ younger days when she worked for a researcher in Edo cuisine. The conversations about olden-days food culture and history add to the charm.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4887;Sushi Yoshino;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-30-2 Chuo, Nakano-ku, Tokyo, 164-0011, Japan;35.697528;139.679189;67;false;false;Sushi;The founder of Sushi Yoshino was once an apprentice at a well-known sushi restaurant in Tokyo’s Kyobashi district. When he became independent, he inherited the shop name, and now his heir and son have hung out their shingle together. Sushi toppings prepared in the old-school way are paired with sushi rice made with red vinegar. The shop captivates with the spirit of a true sushi restaurant. Lighting is used effectively in view of the basement location and the long counter of zelkova wood is a striking feature. Enjoy craftsmanship in both the sushi and the décor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4888;Sharikimon Chawambu;Japan;Tokyo;3-22 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.688886;139.722579;93;false;true;Tonkatsu;Tonkatsu is lightly fried in rice oil and cut to the guest’s preferred thickness. Sauce is heated for added pungency. Curry like a pureed vegetable soup wraps up meals. As the aroma of the dashi stock and sweetness of the vegetables waft through the air, we see why the chef switched his calling from a kappo to a tonkatsu restaurant. The essential element of Japanese cuisine, principles assumed without even noticing, is encapsulated in tonkatsu.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4889;TRATTORIA BUCA'MASSIMO;Japan;Tokyo;1-24-11 Tomioka, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0047, Japan;35.670349;139.798513;81;false;false;Italian;Kiyotaka Onuma opened his trattoria after being seduced by Tuscan cuisine, and his passion for the foods he discovered sampling local restaurants is on full display. Be sure to start with the richly varied appetiser assortment, a product of great time and effort. Meat dishes grilled over charcoal are the highlight. Items are served on plates decorated with the Giglio of Florence, a stylized red iris. Sharing is part of the fun here.;Air conditioning;[]
4891;Ponta Honke;Japan;Tokyo;3-23-3 Ueno, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 110-0005, Japan;35.70631;139.773007;53;false;true;Yoshoku;Since its inception in 1905, this Western restaurant has been run by four generations of the same family. The chef’s famous cutlet is deep-fried in lard carefully trimmed from the pork he will fry. Everything is done by hand, as it has been from the first generation. The youthful energy and practiced skill of the chef is evident in every detail, even down to the hand-chopped cabbage. Traditional flavours and skills testify to his mettle. Delicious fare and the gentle ambience of a family enterprise make everyone feel at home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4893;CHARCUT;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-11-5 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.6687883;139.7503781;73;false;false;French;The speciality here is charcuterie. Having learned his craft in a delicatessen in Lyons, Chef Takehiko Machisuji applies the knowledge and techniques of his mentors with patience and diligence. His accomplishment shines in appetisers such as salami, sausage and terrine. Dishes such as soupe de poisson, quenelle and choucroute convey the wonder of regional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4894;Mochibuta Tonkatsu Taiyo;Japan;Tokyo;3-22-7 Koyama, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 142-0062, Japan;35.618815;139.706435;76;true;true;Tonkatsu;The name ‘Taiyo’ means ‘sun,’ invoking the vigour of the sun as it rises each day. To bring out the soft texture of the pork, the meat is fried at a low temperature, using vegetable oil for a light finish. The calligraphy on the wall reads ‘The pork looks bigger on your neighbour’s plate’—a tonkatsu version of ‘the grass is always greener on the other side of the fence.’ Something to share a smile about while you wait for your order.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4895;Tonkatsu Enraku;Japan;Tokyo;6-1-4 Ikegami, Ota-ku, Tokyo, 146-0082, Japan;35.57294;139.704233;34;true;false;Tonkatsu;The veteran owner-chef has devoted his life to tonkatsu pork cutlets. As he fries pork loin and tenderloin, he concentrates on the changing colour of the coatings and the hiss of oil in the copper pot. Cabbage is chopped by hand as the pork sizzles. Deft, precise movements calculated with the final result in mind fill guests with anticipation. This is craftsmanship learned the old-fashioned way, through patient repetition of the master’s lessons. Bookings are accepted for weekday evenings.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4896;Tonkatsu Hinata;Japan;Tokyo;2-13-9 Takadanobaba, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 169-0075, Japan;35.712956;139.707493;82;true;true;Tonkatsu;One advantage of buying whole pig carcasses is the ability to offer everything from sirloin and tenderloin to rare cuts. The evening set menu provides a chance to taste and compare these different cuts: the smooth fleshiness of rump, the richly sweet fat of jowl, and so on. The idea of tasting fried pork with olive oil also piques interest. To end the meal, curry can be added to make pork-cutlet curry. A range of ideas is this shop’s signature.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4898;LANBRoA;Japan;Tokyo;3-11-15 Yoga, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 158-0097, Japan;35.628673;139.636268;93;false;true;Spanish;The menu lists dishes from every corner of Spain, every one a precious memory of the chef. The preponderance of Basque dishes reflects her attendance of a cooking school in San Sebastián and apprenticeship at a restaurant there. We start with pintxo (pinchos), an apt choice for the Spanish pub atmosphere. Piquillo pepper stuffed with dried and salted cod, squid simmered in its ink and other Basque-country favourites are faithfully reproduced here. Experience the food culture of Spain.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4899;Hamacho Kaneko;Japan;Tokyo;3-7-3 Nihombashihamacho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0007, Japan;35.684005;139.788273;83;false;true;Soba;The chef loves the culture of soba-mae, which refers to enjoying sake and snacks before the soba arrives. A full range of drinking snacks are available to tempt you, including baked devil’s tongue coated with miso, and simmered beef sinew. Tempura varies with the seasons, ranging from shrimp and conger eel to edible wild plants, young sweetfish, mushroom and oyster. Soba is 100% buckwheat noodles, cut thin. Dipping sauces are varied as well, including sesame, grated yam and curry. Meoto, meaning ‘married couple’ is a popular dish combining soba with udon.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4901;Los Reyes Magos;Japan;Tokyo;5-55-7 Yoyogi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0053, Japan;35.677867;139.692365;100;true;false;Spanish;The second-generation chef passes on the Catalonian cuisine that the first-generation chef acquired in Barcelona. Salad of sardines and egg like grandma used to make honours the memory of this couple’s mentors. Dried cod and parsley sauce and homemade sausages convey the flavours of Catalonia, while the well-worn pots attest to the popularity of the paella. Cuisine interwoven with warm memories echoes the journey this restaurant has traced.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4902;Lien;Japan;Tokyo;3-5-22 Ikejiri, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 154-0001, Japan;35.651263;139.681147;23;true;true;French;The prix fixe menu dazzles with its range of choices. The chef sources his ingredients from regions with which he is personally connected, mainly from his native Aomori, but also game from Hokkaido. Culinary approaches are varied: terrines, stews and items baked in pie crust are all in the mix. The number of dishes can be increased according to preference. Lien means ‘connection’, a reference to the bonds between guests and producers that are deepened through cooking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4903;jeeten;Japan;Tokyo;3-2-3 Nishihara, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0066, Japan;35.670403;139.68257;62;false;false;Chinese;The billboard says ‘Chinese home cooking, Yoshida style’ and refers to nourishing Chinese food, based on yakuzen (medicinal food). Having experienced the healing power of Chinese cuisine, the owner-chef strives to devise dishes that restore bodily vigour. Helpful comments on the menu detail the effects of each, such as how mapo tofu stimulates the appetite, or sweet and sour pork with black vinegar relieves fatigue. The Beatles and other classics play in the background, making everyone feel at home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4904;L'AS;Japan;Tokyo;4-16-3 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.666014;139.717125;32;true;true;French, Contemporary;Simple yet refined fare, enjoyed in a casual setting. Keen to make French cuisine familiar to his clientele, the chef offers great taste at a reasonable price. Guests can enjoy their meals as if they were gathered around their own dinner tables. The chef changes the menu monthly, greeting diners with something different each time they visit. Cooks also bring dishes to tables for a seamlessly integrated dining experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4905;Shiosoba Jiku;Japan;Tokyo;4-14-7 Takaidohigashi, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 168-0072, Japan;35.689738;139.618974;97;true;false;Ramen;The chef heard the call to the culinary life one day while riding his father’s motorcycle on a long tour around the Seto Inland Sea. When he happened upon a ramen shop along the way, the taste of the salty soba touched his soul. He combines a clear seafood broth with homemade noodles crafted with aroma in mind. The ceiling decoration recalls the roof of an old-time food stall, honouring how ramen culture spread in his native Hiroshima Prefecture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4906;Le Nougat;Japan;Tokyo;6-12-2 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669271;139.764924;37;false;true;French;The restaurant’s name is inspired by a chanson song. Inside, red bench seating, French movie posters and chanson playing in the background all recreate the feel of a Paris bistro. The menu is an assemblage of French village fare. Each plateful serves two, encouraging sharing. With an extensive list of wines from every region of France, many available by the glass, you can delight in the experience of pairing your dish with wines of the same region.;Air conditioning;[]
4908;Sushi Mikata;Japan;Tokyo;4-1-4 Mita, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0073, Japan;35.647756;139.741381;89;true;false;Sushi;The origins of Sushi Mikata go back to a standup sushi bar the chef went to with his father when he was a boy. Aiming to be a place where people could drop in casually for sushi, he emulated this standup format. Guests can order in amounts as small as one piece at a time. Both fish and vinegared-rice portions are generous, to impart the delightful feeling of filling one’s mouth. The chef runs Sushi Mikata with his wife, whose rolled Japanese-style omelettes are a hit with customers. The good-humoured banter between husband and wife keeps the atmosphere light.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4909;Hakodate Shioramen Goryokaku;Japan;Tokyo;3-28-7 Amanuma, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0032, Japan;35.706594;139.62014;93;false;false;Ramen;The owner-chef was born and raised in the Goryokaku district of Hakodate. He pours his heart and soul into salt-based ramen, a Hakodate favourite he has loved since childhood. The kombu kelp and dried scallop adductor muscles used in the salt sauce, as well as the wheat used for the house-made noodles, are all sourced from Hokkaido to convey the flavours of his hometown.  The clear soup has a light seafood flavour. A popular topping here is gagome kombu, a speciality of Hakodate. A bowl of ramen that preserves age-old preparation methods is one of life’s simple pleasures.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4910;Tensuke;Japan;Tokyo;3-22-7 Koenjikita, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 166-0002, Japan;35.705867;139.64872;83;false;false;Tempura;The lines that form outside Tensuke at lunchtime are a part of the Koenji landscape. Inside, one voice after another calls for the ‘Egg Lunch’. Accompanying the speciality of deep-fried egg on rice, tempura items are fried in a set order. Another speciality is the performance of the chef, who tosses the eggshells in the air in poses worthy of a kabuki actor. The idea is to make the waiting time fun, too. Deep-fried eggs fill mouths with yolk and smiles.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
4912;IL BALLOND'ORO;Japan;Tokyo;1-24-10 Ebisu, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0013, Japan;35.646608;139.715464;87;true;true;Italian;The walls are adorned with commemorative photographs and uniforms of Italian football players. The trattoria is named after the Ballon d'Or award presented to the top football players. The chef’s “Golden Risotto” glistens with the colour of saffron and is a testament to his past dreams of becoming a pro footballer. The menu is full of traditional dishes picked up from his travels throughout Italy from north to south.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4914;Chukasoba Ginza Hachigou;Japan;Tokyo;3-14-2 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670563;139.770185;35;false;false;Ramen;Aiming to provide a full-course meal in a bowl, the chef infuses Chinese soba with his experience in French cuisine for a unique touch. Most revolutionary is the absence of sauce. The soup is crafted by extracting flavours as if for a consommé and then perfectly balancing them with the saltiness of cured ham. The wontons are filled with a paste of foie gras and truffles. He combines all the Western ingredients he has mastered over the years into a single bowl.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4915;sugahara;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-14-1 Kotobashi, Sumida-ku, Tokyo, 130-0022, Japan;35.695692;139.811166;94;true;false;Italian;Chef Atsushi Sugahara is all about the cooking of rural Italy. What Sugahara prizes most are the relationships of mutual trust he enjoys with food producers. Vegetables arriving from farmers in Yamagata Prefecture provide ingredients for pasta dishes. Kurobuta pork from Miyagi Prefecture is simmered with tomatoes and white kidney beans. For wine pairings, ask the sommelier, who is thoroughly versed in the chef’s cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4916;noura;Japan;Tokyo;4-10-6 Asakusa, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0032, Japan;35.718455;139.797106;98;true;false;French;The restaurant name means ‘behind’, a humorous reference to how it is located behind its parent restaurant, HOMMAGE. In contrast to that establishment, noura follows the concept of a back-to-roots bistro. The chef, who honed his craft in France, applies classic French techniques to the fullest, capturing their essence in hearty free-range chicken, foie gras and pâté en croûte. Melted into the very fabric of Asakusa, noura is a restaurant where it’s easy to feel at home.;Air conditioning;[]
4917;Tompachitei;Japan;Tokyo;4-3-4 Ueno, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 110-0005, Japan;35.708414;139.773726;86;true;false;Tonkatsu;This shop in Ueno’s Tanuki-koji area opens only for lunch. The tonkatsu, rich in pork-fat aroma, follows a recipe passed from generation to generation. The reason for its loyal following is the work hidden in the batter: when an order is received, the pork is pounded, lightly scored and cooked on a low flame, give the cutlets their distinctive flavour. The pickled vegetables, marinated in a salted-rice-bran bed passed down through generations, play a great supporting role.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4918;Chukasoba KOTETSU;Japan;Tokyo;2-39-13 Kitazawa, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 155-0031, Japan;35.664633;139.66631;15;false;true;Ramen;Eager to court the local community, the chef gave top billing in the shop name to familiar ‘chukasoba’ (ramen). Soup combines meat and seafood dashi for a deep, satisfying flavour. Kaeshi (a mixture of soy sauce, sugar and mirin) is supplemented with squid and fish sauce, enhancing umami. The low-hydration noodles are boiled only briefly, yielding a pleasing al dente texture that lets the flavour of the wheat come out. The taste of soy, smooth and refreshing yet rich and deep, conveys the simple honesty of the dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4919;AlCeppo;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-25-32 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.644588;139.731574;34;false;true;Italian;Italy and Japan have much in common: a geography elongated north to south, for example, and a balance of four seasons. The features of both countries inform the menu of AlCeppo. From his experience touring the length and breadth of Italy, the chef expresses the local cuisine of each region through seasonal ingredients. From spring to summer, the fare of southern Italy is offered, typically focusing on fish and vegetables dressed in olive oil. From autumn to winter, northern cooking, such as mushrooms and stewed game, becomes the focus. A joy to visit in every season.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4922;YAMATO;Japan;Tokyo;16-3 Nihombashitomizawacho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0006, Japan;35.688123;139.784335;64;true;false;Izakaya;Here the speciality is chargrilled vegetables and seafood. Guests gather around the hearth and charcoal brazier to enjoy the rising aroma of the seafood and vegetables while savouring sake. Among the favourites are the large clams and dried, salted ichiyaboshi fish. Seasonal delicacies like bamboo shoots and mushrooms are also available. The proprietress expertly handles the grilling duties, carefully tending to the charcoal fire. ‘Yamato’ is the name of her family's river fish shop, serving as the inspiration for the owner's charcoal cooking.;Air conditioning;[]
4923;LAUBURU;Japan;Tokyo;6-8-18 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.659959;139.716589;19;true;true;French;Chef Shinichiro Sakurai has undying affection for Basque cuisine. During his time in France, he found his calling in the country cooking that drew him the most. The pork dishes listed on the blackboard consist solely of items Sakurai loves to cook, such as brawn, confit of shank, and char-grilled pork loin. The time and toil he devotes to each dish are testament to the respect and passion he feels for the Basque Country.;Air conditioning;[]
4924;Soba Tajima;Japan;Tokyo;3-8-6 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.654728;139.726132;54;false;false;Soba;A soba shop well stocked with vegetable cuisine in season. From the varied and extensive menu, choose an assortment of small items as well as vegetable dishes, and cap the meal with the soba of your choice. The surfeit of options can be bewildering but of course you can order soba one plate at a time. If you arrive at lunchtime, set menus of rice dishes await you as well. Seasoned staff serve with practiced skill and grace, welcoming you like a local no matter when you visit.;Air conditioning;[]
4926;Sennomago;Japan;Tokyo;4-4-2 Nishiogikita, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0042, Japan;35.706387;139.595811;71;false;false;Chinese;The chef devotes himself to good health through a balanced diet, using Chinese medicines as seasoning to serve food that is salutary for both mind and body. Vegetables from his native Oita are grown by natural methods, making them gentle to the constitution. At dinner, there is a wide range of à la carte dishes, leaning toward Sichuan and Shanghai influences. The chef allows himself an individual take with the mapo tofu: drawing on a wealth of experience, he offers a choice of Sichuan, aged doubanjiang (Chinese broad bean chili paste) and salt. Lunchtime set menus are also popular.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4927;Ittoan;Japan;Tokyo;2-16-10 Higashijujo, Kita-ku, Tokyo, 114-0001, Japan;35.763091;139.728912;64;true;true;Soba;The chef helps out on farms all over Japan, forming bonds of trust with farmers. If you’re interested in the differences among various kinds of soba, we recommend the ‘Sanshu Seiro’, three kinds of soba served on a wickerwork tray. He grinds and kneads each soba differently according to type and region of origin, so the character of each shines through. Sometimes, the chef says, he mixes coarse-ground and fine-ground soba from the same region. His tireless curiosity yields a never-ending variety of flavours.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4928;Mejiro Zorome;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-3-1 Mejiro, Toshima-ku, Tokyo, 171-0031, Japan;35.721552;139.706358;34;true;false;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;Unagi are dressed, skewered and grilled over high-grade charcoal. From the counter seats, the whole series of cooking scenes can be observed. The unagi are kept alive in purifying tanks until they are dressed, then dipped three times in sauce and grilled Edo-style. Sauce is used sparingly, letting the flavour of the fish speak for itself. Rice cooked somewhat firm, and freshly ground sansho pepper deliver a distinctive touch. Skilful restraint shows in the short steaming time and sparing use of sauce.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4929;ARROCERÍA La Panza;Japan;Tokyo;1-15-8 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.673366;139.770106;85;false;false;Spanish;Customers who drink like to order tapas and chacolí, a Basque wine, and select their dishes at their leisure. The pouring style is called escancia: the pourer holds the bottle high up and pours it like a waterfall, often to the applause of onlookers. Arrocería (restaurants that specialise in rice dishes) recommends the shrimp caldero. If you’re a panza (food lover), you’ll definitely want to try it.;Air conditioning;[]
4930;Sugita;Japan;Tokyo;3-8-3 Kotobuki, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0042, Japan;35.706397;139.79104;95;false;false;Tonkatsu;Since its 1977 opening, Sugita has put down firm roots in Asakusa. Demonstrating skills passed on from his father, the second owner-chef uses two pots of lard at different temperatures, frying his ingredients in hot oil, then cooler oil, then hot oil again. For tonkatsu, the pork loin, fried in a thin layer of batter with the excess fat trimmed away, is the obvious choice. Watching a true craftsman, his craft honed to perfection as befits a chef of Asakusa, is an unforgettable memory.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4931;Katsuo Shokudo;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 7-12 Uguisudanicho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0032, Japan;35.654087;139.702122;79;false;true;Japanese;Inspired by her grandmother’s miso soup and the sight of her making fresh bonito shavings, Mai Nagamatsu is telling the world about the wonders of katsuo-bushi. The chef piles a helping of bonito shavings on rice, conveying the wishes of her food producers. Customers who want seconds can enjoy shaving the bonito themselves. She thanks each departing customer with her trademark farewell, Arigatsuo! – expressing gratitude that springs from her grandmother’s love.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4933;Kyorakutei;Japan;Tokyo;3-6 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.700778;139.739514;24;true;true;Soba;The queue forms before the doors open. The reason for Kyorakutei’s popularity is the extensive menu, with drinks and snacks to sample between bites of soba. It’s great to visit any time, whether day or evening. Tempura choices are also abundant, and guests can order combination platters or individual items according to preference. Buckwheat is sourced from the chef’s native Aizu, with a focus on delivering the flavour of cold inaka soba (thick soba made with whole buckwheat) with a pleasing finish. Tomato soba, the early summer speciality, is worth waiting for.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4934;Shinjiko Shijimi Chukasoba Kohaku;Japan;Tokyo;2-1-3 Nishirokugo, Ota-ku, Tokyo, 144-0056, Japan;35.551272;139.711199;33;true;false;Ramen;After taking over his mother’s restaurant, the owner-chef opened his doors in the town where he was born and raised. The key to the flavour lies in the shijimi clams from Lake Shinji in Shimane Prefecture, after which the restaurant is named. The soup utilizes the umami of the shellfish’s succinic acid. To enjoy the true taste of the broth, we recommend the salt-flavoured option. The names of the fishermen who caught each day's clams are written on the blackboard, showing respect for both ingredients and producers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
4935;falò;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 14-10 Daikanyamacho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0034, Japan;35.650023;139.704283;21;true;true;Italian;The counter kitchen arrayed around a hearth suggests an open-air bonfire. The eyes are riveted to the chef as he grills the meat, throwing charcoal on the fire. The use of grilling close to the flame, grilling over an open hearth and directly placing ingredients on the charcoal, brings the ingredients and brightly burning charcoal into a tight embrace. Porchetta, patiently cooked for over an hour, is a popular item. Straw-grilled fish and foil-grilled vegetables whet curiosity and appetite. The chef works with practiced ease, laser-focused on the foodstuffs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4936;Hibino Chukashokudo;Japan;Tokyo;1-33-11 Uehara, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0064, Japan;35.669108;139.680787;88;false;true;Chinese;Inside a modern space enveloped in the warmth of wood, the concept is togetherness, complementing daily life in Yoyogi Uehara. Based on Sichuan and Cantonese cuisines, the restaurant offers set meals like mapo tofu and boiled chicken during the day, and an à la carte menu in the evening. Like side dishes at home, the small dishes allow you to sample a variety of flavours. The whole crispy chicken is perfect for sharing. Friendly service makes for a pleasant experience.;Air conditioning;[]
4940;Mono-bis;Japan;Tokyo;2-8-12 Shibuya, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0002, Japan;35.660754;139.707745;88;true;false;French;Mono-bis is a bistro run by MONOLITH a restaurant on the same street. Service is prix fixe, but several choices are available. Classic French fare is on offer here, including boudin noir sausage, choucroute and pork roast. The pairing of smoked salmon with monaka wafer is inspired by canapes. The charm of traditional cuisine, with a few innovations added in.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4942;Hong Fan Qie (Yuyuantan South Road);China Mainland;Beijing;36 Cui Wei South Lane, Yuyuantan South Road, Haidian, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9115003;116.2909257;43;true;false;Hubei;The flagship establishment of the chain has been around for over 30 years. The kitchen team of Hubei natives is picky about its ingredients, most of which are shipped daily from their home province to ensure freshness. The menu changes according to the 24 solar terms in the Chinese calendar and stars the best seasonal produce. Long-snout catfish with tomato boasts silky flesh and a tangy, mildly spicy sauce. Sautéed young lotus seeds are sweet and crispy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
4943;Yu Hua Tai (Xicheng);China Mainland;Beijing;Building 23, Yuzhongxili Residence, Yumin Road, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.971092;116.377761;29;false;false;Huaiyang;With signage inscribed by the younger brother of Puyi, the last emperor of the Qing Dynasty, circa 1921, this state-owned restaurant is a real treasure. Dark wood is a prominent decorative feature, while red tablecloths lend it a rustic, classic vibe. Since 1997, diners have been coming to the current location to enjoy its authentic, no-frills Huaiyang cooking, with dishes like scorched eel with garlic and soy. Only private rooms can be booked ahead.;Air conditioning;[]
4945;Zhong;China Mainland;Beijing;37 Gulou West Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.947313;116.399475;43;true;true;Huaiyang;Tucked inside a converted courtyard house, this tiny gem with seven tables has just a small sign on its door. Chef Zhong from Yangzhou is also your waiter and host. He opened this restaurant in 2020 to showcase his hometown’s delicacies. Try the wine lees-marinated cold appetiser platter with green soybeans, shrimps, duck tongues and abalone – addictively aromatic and refreshing. Sautéed shredded swamp eel boasts a bouncy, velvety texture.;Cash only;[]
4946;Jing Hua Lou;China Mainland;Beijing;No. 202, 2F, Building 111, Huizhong North Lane, Datun North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;40.0041259;116.3995133;88;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;Via the grand entrance with a retro vibe, diners are escorted into a lofty dining room on level 2. Painstakingly crafted Beijing classics define the extensive menu, much of which dates back to the Qing Dynasty. The crispy duo blanched in oil manifests expert judgment of heat – pork tripe and chicken gizzards are both perfectly cooked. Thinly sliced smoked pork head meat is buttery and smoky. Round off with artisan desserts, like rose puff pastry or split pea cake.;;[]
4947;Pang Mei Noodles (Xiang'er Hutong);China Mainland;Beijing;Xiang'er Hutong, 69 Dongsi North Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.937846;116.410128;78;true;false;Noodles;In Beijing, this is the first outlet of the popular brand specialising in Chongqing-style noodles and snacks. The fiery beef noodle soup is the signature here – choose between two sizes and four levels of spiciness. Deep-fried pork with mint leaves and pork brain in ma la sauce are also recommended. Round it out with ice jelly and rice balls in brown sugar syrup to soothe the burn. Reservations are not accepted, so expect a long wait.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4948;Niujie Halal Man Heng Ji;China Mainland;Beijing;14 Ping'anli West Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.930741;116.361468;83;true;true;Hotpot;This restaurant specialises in instant-boiled mutton, a traditional Beijingese charcoal hot pot dish. Prized for its fine lean meat without the gamey taste, lamb from the Mongolian Sunite prairie is used, along with beef from western Shandong. Specify how fatty or lean you want your lamb. The bite-size shaobing flatbread goes well with the hot pot. Round off your meal with sweet shaobing covered in sesame sugar.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
4949;Jingyi (Liulichang East Street);China Mainland;Beijing;2 Liulichang East Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.8938155;116.3831013;35;true;false;Hubei;This small, obscure shop in an alley features an understated grey-brick façade and pared-down décor. The calligraphic menu is short but sweet, heavy on river fish and home-style cooking. Try their braised tofu with fish roe, or hot and sour young lotus root with chicken gizzards. Round it out with grass jelly in Osmanthus honey, or the piping-hot egg-drop glutinous rice wine (in winter). Seats are limited, so come early or expect to wait in line.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4950;The Red Chamber;China Mainland;Beijing;4F, China World Summit Wing, 1 Jianguomenwai Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.912885;116.458486;33;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;Styled a lot hipper than other restaurants of its kind, this aptly named “chamber” is furnished in the requisite colour inside out. The menu is mostly Northern Chinese, with occasional Sichuanese or Cantonese offerings, all very reasonably priced. Dishes are meticulously executed with spot-on flavours. You can see the chefs roasting ducks in the wood-fired oven. Besides consumed on the spot, these bronzed beauties come in a well-designed package to go.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
4951;Lao Chuan Ban;China Mainland;Beijing;5 Gongyuan 1st Alley, Dongzongbu Hutong, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9104351;116.4257122;83;false;true;Sichuan;In 1979, the branch office of Sichuan provincial government in Beijing opened this restaurant to cure the homesickness among travelling Sichuan officials with comfort food from home. It opened its doors to the public in 1995 and has been a popular spot among locals ever since. The room was updated recently, but the prices remain approachable. Come here for the all-time classics: mouth-watering chicken, Fuqi beef offal, and Sichuan boiled fish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
4952;Blossom Vegetarian (Dongcheng);China Mainland;Beijing;144 Dongzhimennei Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9393764;116.4198442;90;false;true;Vegetarian;Dotted with lotus motifs, this bright, airy, ground-floor dining room sports a neutral colour scheme. Private rooms and a banquet hall are located on the upper floors. The chef uses Chinese and western techniques to create photogenic vegan and ovo-lacto dishes that feel novel and vibrant. Start the meal with a spicy, tangy New Zealand bull kelp salad, followed by the treasure trio, the vegan chicken of which is especially good.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
4953;Qiantang Garden;China Mainland;Beijing;59 Shuangyushu North Road, Haidian, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9715724;116.3151524;93;true;true;Ningbo;The owner opened this joint in early 2000s to serve signature dishes from his hometown of Ningbo, especially seafood – his close connections with fishermen back home mean he gets the freshest catch shipped to him daily. Pick from the fish tank, or try specialities such as oil-blanched river shrimps seasoned with a dash of vinegar and grated ginger. Hairtail cooked in myriad ways is also popular, perfect with house-made waxberry juice.;Cash only;[]
4955;Tianchumiaoxiang Vegetarian (Chaoyang);China Mainland;Beijing;0260, Section D, 2F, Chaowai SOHO, Chaowai Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.919141;116.448564;69;false;true;Vegetarian;After converting to veganism and going on to become a monk, the founder of this chain experienced improvements to his life. This inspired him to serve tasty vegetarian dishes eschewing eggs, alcohol and alliums in his restaurants. In the Kung Pao monkey head mushroom, the meat-like texture is harnessed in sweet and sour sauce with peanuts and bamboo shoots. No wonder it has been the restaurant's signature dish since the flagship opened in 2003!;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
4956;Gong De Lin;China Mainland;Beijing;2 Qianmen East Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.899085;116.40527;85;false;true;Vegetarian;This restaurant, like its landmark Shanghai namesake, has plenty of surprises in store. Don't be alarmed to read "pork" or "fish" on the menu, as the chef is renowned for mimicking the look of meat dishes with mushrooms and vegetables. Braised pork belly is in fact winter melon layered with monkey-head mushrooms then fried and simmered in a brown sauce. Sweet and sour fried fish is made with king oyster mushrooms, millefeuille tofu and seaweed.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
4957;Ladychai;China Mainland;Beijing;Building 21, Ganjiakou Residence, Ganjiakou North Street, Haidian, Beijing, China Mainland;39.925242;116.325247;99;false;true;Noodles;The second-generation owner of this family-run shop still follows the original c. 1920 recipes. The establishment is packed at peak times, so expect to queue, serve yourself and share a table with strangers. Order the signature braised beef by the catty – about 0.5 catty per person. Specify whether you want it fatty or lean. Plain noodles in beef broth come in two sizes. The flavoursome broth and toothsome noodles are a match made in heaven.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
4958;Bao Yuan;China Mainland;Beijing;North side of Building 6, Maizidian Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.944026;116.462581;63;false;true;Dumplings;Popular among foreigners, this shop has been serving dumplings and Sichuanese food for the past 20-some years. The colourful dumpling skin is made with natural fruit and vegetable juices, and there are tens of different fillings to choose from. Order them by the tael (about six per tael) and be careful of the scalding filling. For surf and turf in a bite, try the New Year dumplings. Purple cabbage filled with crispy rice affords interesting textures.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4959;Rong Cuisine (Baiziwan South Er Road);China Mainland;Beijing;77 Baiziwan South Er Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9030002;116.4812986;54;false;true;Taizhou;A budget-friendly spinoff of the decidedly upmarket Xin Rong Ji, this offshoot lets diners enjoy certain premium dishes at a fraction of its flagship’s prices. The open kitchen imparts a bustling, down-to-earth vibe which complements the simple, seafaring-themed room. Unlike other Rong Cuisine siblings, this eatery serves a larger menu with more choices in single servings. In addition to its famous yellow croaker, try sautéed squid with wild rice stems and salted potherb mustard.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4960;No. 69 Fangzhuanchang Zhajiangmian (Fangzhuanchang Hutong);China Mainland;Beijing;1 Fangzhuanchang Hutong, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.93683;116.39342;99;true;false;Noodles;Ordering food at this neighbourhood joint is a no-brainer. There is only one thing on the menu – zhajiangmian. But diners come in hordes from the moment the place opens till it closes. These lovely, chewy noodles are dressed with the exceptionally deep and aromatic soybean pork sauce and topped with condiments such as shredded cucumber, radish and leafy greens. Feel free to garnish with pickled garlic and cumin chilli sauce for extra kick.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4961;Fujian Cuisine (Dongsanhuan North Road);China Mainland;Beijing;110-111, Kaidexingmao, 26A Dongsanhuan North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.933899;116.469256;40;true;false;Fujian;The owner and chefs who hail from Xiamen insist on using produce and seafood from their home province to create authentic Fujian dishes, especially country recipes that were the staple diet of the commoners in olden days. Steamed red crab on sticky rice seduces with seafood umami and briny-sweet roe, while the ginger duck is an heirloom recipe passed down for generations, made with Muscovy duck for exceptional depth. Also try the creamy mashed taro dessert.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
4962;Bao Du Jin Sheng Long (Ande Road);China Mainland;Beijing;Lane 1, Liupukang, Ande Road, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.950879;116.384139;41;true;false;Hotpot;Tripe is enjoyed the world over, but not everyone cares about this offal enough to patent a recipe, as the owner here has done. His signature dish, "tripe 13 ways", uses four types of beef tripe and nine kinds of lamb tripe (including the most prized cut: lamb's rumen core) served with a secret-recipe dip. Try the charcoal-burning hot pot with eight halal lamb cuts and ask for the "half cloud" cut with half-fatty meat and a milky aftertaste.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
4963;Alba;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Wibautstraat 105H, Amsterdam, 1091 GL, Netherlands;52.3560542;4.9118194;48;true;false;Creative;With its funky background music and striking colour scheme, Alba has an arty feel indoors, and boasts a spacious terrace outside. The posters adorning the walls make it clear that they are big on natural wines here. The cuisine is on trend yet down to earth. Imagine a Greek-Dutch fusion dish starring juicy smoked trout gravlax, pops of briny trout roe, and a creamy horseradish sauce that adds a kick to the crème crue. The set menu is a journey of bold flavours and clever combinations. Alba offers a relaxed setting in which to savour delicious food.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4964;Nova;Netherlands;Bergschenhoek;Rottekade 31, Bergschenhoek, 2661 JN, Netherlands;51.9725916;4.5457368;57;true;false;Farm to table;Located on the edge of the Bergse Bos forest, with a romantic terrace and a pontoon on the River Rotte to the front, and a cosy, luxurious atmosphere inside, Nova is a really wonderful establishment! Your elegant hostess extends a warm welcome, and chef Vaandrager proposes an appealing menu. His contemporary dishes combine playful ideas with impressive culinary expertise. Whether preparing a salade niçoise with mi-cuit tuna or giving pink-roasted lamb a southern twist with a ratatouille garnish, he puts the focus firmly on bold flavours – and all at excellent value for money. Don't miss the chance to take a boat trip on the Rotte, perhaps with some snacks. You won't be disappointed!;Car park,Terrace;[]
4965;Niemeijer;Netherlands;Groningen;Akerkstraat 20, Groningen, 9612 BE, Netherlands;53.2173827;6.5621403;21;false;false;Creative French;Janick and Leonie Niemeijer's light and airy restaurant has a distinctly natural and serene feel to it. The couple have put together an extensive à la carte menu and take great pride in their garden, from which they source vegetables and honey, among other produce. These are showcased in creative dishes that often incorporate a nod to Dutch culinary tradition. The way the chef cooks quince from the garden in a cassis syrup with hibiscus and combines it with full-fat vanilla yoghurt, almonds and fresh lemon sorbet is testament to his eye for presentation and his talent for marrying flavours. Unbeatable value for money!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
4966;Wils Bakery Café;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Stadionplein 24, Amsterdam, 1076 CM, Netherlands;52.3433407;4.8560325;43;true;false;French;This laid-back establishment has the feel of a traditional bistro but with a Scandinavian twist. As you walk in, you will see the baker kneading dough and the odd customer coming to buy bread. Make no mistake, though: this place has a great menu of well-crafted dishes. This Amsterdam version of a French bistro honours classics such as snails in herb butter, wood pigeon pithivier, foie gras and tarte Tatin. It is rich in flavour, generous and inspired, and the fantastic value for money is an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4967;De Voorburcht;Netherlands;Hattem;Adelaarshoek 18, Hattem, 8051 GR, Netherlands;52.4734112;6.0702257;75;true;false;Creative French, Modern French;Step across the moat, traverse the medieval fortifications and look for the building with a sloping wall. This place certainly makes a magical first impression! Inside, this historical setting has been given a splendid makeover. Here, familiar ingredients are used to produce creative dishes. For instance, the chef combines skate and scallops in a dish reminiscent of a choucroute garnie. This is carefully considered and rich cuisine. At De Voorburcht, new life is breathed into classic fine dining.;;[]
4968;De Grote Frederik Bistro;Netherlands;Groningen;Frederiksplein 7, Groningen, 9724 NH, Netherlands;53.2108191;6.5811284;31;true;true;Farm to table;In this cosy local bistro you immediately get the feeling that guests always come first. This is typified by the excellent front-of-house hospitality of host Marjon, who is delighted to offer advice on a superb selection of wines to accompany chef Arnejan’s unique dishes, which are playful and unpretentious, yet which feature wonderful and surprising flavours.;Terrace;[]
4969;Groenewoud;Netherlands;Nijmegen;Groesbeekseweg 227, Nijmegen, 6523 NW, Netherlands;51.8300013;5.8746657;61;true;true;Modern French;A few authentic decorative features remind us that despite its comfortable and even trendy feel we are in one of the oldest cafés in Nijmegen. The experienced chef at the helm conjures up generous French cuisine with the occasional subtle and surprising touch. Dishes cooked to perfection, a mastery of acidic flavours, intense sauces, plus excellent value for money!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4970;Bouwkunde;Netherlands;Deventer;Klooster 2, Deventer, 7411 NH, Netherlands;52.25342;6.15299;57;true;false;French;A dining experience at Bouwkunde is one to be savoured. After being welcomed by the cordial hostess, you can soak up the warm atmosphere of this charming restaurant. Diners will see that wine plays an important role here. The ostensibly classic and simple cuisine proves to be full of surprises and bold flavours. For example, a beurre blanc with a judicious squeeze of lemon enhances a beautifully translucent fillet of skrei. And all at great value for money!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4971;Chef aan de Werf;Netherlands;Hilversum;Mussenstraat 11, Hilversum, 1223 RB, Netherlands;52.2207419;5.1973007;62;false;true;Farm to table;Enjoy a local beer as an aperitif before discovering Charly de Wijs' selection of international dishes, which feature local, subtly flavoured and sustainably sourced ingredients and draw on inspirations from around the globe. His winning combinations include options such as harissa with a fillet of fish, flatbread with carrots, tahini and feta. Just bear in mind that the chef serves up very generous portions! Housed in an old industrial building, this lively restaurant with its vintage decor is bound to have you coming back for more.;Car park,Terrace;[]
4972;De Beleving;Netherlands;Sint-Oedenrode;Hertog Hendrikstraat 6, Sint-Oedenrode, 5492 BB, Netherlands;51.5615025;5.4602529;79;true;false;Modern French;At this spacious brasserie, perfect for relaxed dining, a warm and welcoming atmosphere awaits. The wide-ranging à la carte selection and surprise menus draw on Dutch, French and Mediterranean influences. The dishes are hearty and satisfying, without being overly complicated. Options include al dente tagliatelle with prawns and a rich lobster bisque, perfectly seared ribeye steak with a robust red wine sauce, hasselback pumpkin, and tiramisu: the choices are seemingly endless! At this Bib Gourmand restaurant, incredible value for money is guaranteed.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4973;L'Auberge;Netherlands;Maastricht;Von Dopfflaan 10, Maastricht, 6213 NG, Netherlands;50.8184748;5.6678474;73;true;true;Classic Cuisine, French;Come for lunch beneath the vaults of Château Neercanne's old chapel – you cannot fail to be impressed by this charming historical setting that has been given a stylish makeover. The terrace affords spectacular views. Chef Remmen serves up his own modern spin on classic dishes, with a focus on quality. Delicious produce is sourced from the region and their own kitchen garden. Cod poached in butter with a delicate white wine sauce, a traditionally prepared rich tarte Tatin: food lovers will be in seventh heaven.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4974;De Uitkijk;Netherlands;Hellendoorn;Hellendoornsebergweg 8, Hellendoorn, 7447 PA, Netherlands;52.38189;6.4414;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With its magnificent natural setting, a lavender-filled terrace with a southern feel, and a restaurant with a country estate atmosphere, De Uitkijk offers a winning combination. Guests can watch the seasons change on the plate, with herbs from the chef's own garden. The elaborate dishes here are full of fresh flavour and boast lots of variety.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4975;La Fleurie;Netherlands;Oirschot;Rijkesluisstraat 4, Oirschot, 5688 ED, Netherlands;51.5034872;5.3088391;98;true;true;Modern French, Creative;You can really taste Martino Verbruggen's passion and experience in every bite of his dishes. His robust sauces are out of this world. Take, for example, the beautifully reduced veal jus that complements the succulent veal tenderloin and crispy sweetbreads. His cuisine is sophisticated and refined, with occasional international nuances adding an exciting twist. A judicious squeeze of kaffir lime adds a refreshing zing to the seasonal fish tartare. Hostess Loes is always on hand and contributes to the laid-back atmosphere that sets La Fleurie apart. A delightful dining experience!;Terrace;[]
4976;Vineum;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Eendrachtsweg 23, Rotterdam, 3012 LB, Netherlands;51.915833;4.4745143;18;false;true;Modern French;The wine list is the linchpin of this warm, aptly named restaurant with an intimate urban garden to the rear. Owner David van Steenderen, a world-class sommelier, has a knack for finding new gems. He takes great pleasure in letting his diners taste his discoveries for themselves, offering a choice of wine pairings. The food is just as sophisticated. Classic techniques meet innovative ideas and expertise, creating dishes that complement the wines beautifully. Savour ceviche made with young mackerel, or salmon tartare with a millefeuille of chicory and sorrel oil. With an extensive à la carte selection and set menus, one is spoilt for choice!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4977;Bistro;Netherlands;Noordeloos;Botersloot 1, Noordeloos, 4225 PR, Netherlands;51.9016065;4.939242;31;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This charming bistro occupies the front room of the farm that is also home to its older Michelin-starred sibling De Gieser Wildeman. The cuisine and name are perfectly matched: traditional, generous and quite simply delicious. One of the highlights on the menu is the crispy duck leg with cabbage. The attractive prices here are as tempting as the cooking!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4978;Le Vieux Jean;Netherlands;Delft;Heilige Geestkerkhof 3, Delft, 2611 HP, Netherlands;52.012291;4.3559388;78;false;true;Classic French;Robert-Jan Polman's romantic restaurant has been delighting French cuisine enthusiasts since 1974. The robust flavours, subtle undertones and timeless cooking methods are a testament to his culinary skill. The rich lamb jus infused with thyme, which accompanies perfectly roasted Dutch lamb, and the crispy veal sweetbread with a lobster and crayfish sauce are simply divine! The incorporation of Dutch produce, notably game, gives his dishes a unique character. Be sure to try the cheeses too! As you might expect, the wine list gives pride of place to French labels, which perfectly complement the menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4979;DiVino;Netherlands;Hapert;Kerkstraat 27, Hapert, 5527 EE, Netherlands;51.368777;5.2529369;93;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;This former school has been transformed into a warm, urban restaurant, including a graffiti portrait of Don Corleone! You can see the chefs working their magic in the open kitchen, where they create French and Mediterranean dishes full of creativity and nuanced flavours. The risotto puttanesca and the conchiglioni served with game stew and a rich jus are intensely flavoured dishes. Thanks to the wide range of sharing dishes and snacks, and the possibility of ordering half portions of the pasta dishes, you can decide how lavish your meal will be. The fabulous Italian wine library is also a hit, with quite a few guests coming in simply for a nice glass of wine or a cocktail. Cosy!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4981;Pouwe;Netherlands;Hoeven;Bovenstraat 4, Hoeven, 4741 AV, Netherlands;51.5801143;4.5875022;31;true;false;Creative;Walter and Vivian Pouwe bring flavours from around the globe to the sleepy town of Hoeven. In their modern lounge-style restaurant, ingredients such as yuzu, tandoori spices and vadouvan are incorporated into creative dishes that pack a punch. For instance, bavette steak really comes into its own in a Mediterranean concoction featuring an interplay with pesto and aubergine caviar. Be sure to sample the enticing cheese trolley – an unconventional selection of international cheeses that the chef presents with great enthusiasm. A Bib Gourmand restaurant with a cosmopolitan twist!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4982;Héron;Netherlands;Utrecht;Schalkwijkstraat 26, Utrecht, 3512 KS, Netherlands;52.0880216;5.1274096;64;true;false;Organic, Farm to table;Pure and honest. These two words encapsulate this vibrant place, though they hardly do it justice. Joyce and Victor's deep respect for the seasons and Dutch produce is truly inspiring. They work closely with their suppliers and encourage chef Josephien Blom to be creative within the framework of their sustainable values. The pig's trotters with a tangy remoulade sauce is a classic of the house, but she also gives potatoes a surprising twist with a seaweed sauce and crispy serrated wrack. Prepare to be amazed!;Counter dining;[]
4983;De Lindeboom New Style;Netherlands;Beek;Burg. Janssenstraat 13, Beek, 6191 JB, Netherlands;50.939037;5.797044;36;false;true;French Contemporary, International;It's hard to resist the style of De Lindeboom on account of the charm of the building (1765), the terrace laid out at the foot of the church tower and the appealing sense of warm Limburg hospitality. And then there is the generous cuisine with which chef Jan Willem Punt has made a name for himself. He seeks inspiration in the fresh flavours of the Mediterranean and draws on international influences, but also delivers a traditional sole dish as well as various vegetarian options. Take his okonomiyaki – Japanese pancake made with spring onion and shiitake, served with sweet-and-sour pickled cucumber, tempura lotus root, Japanese mayonnaise and seaweed. This is a chef who has all it takes to delight diners.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4984;Rijsel;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Marcusstraat 52b, Amsterdam, 1091 TK, Netherlands;52.351624;4.912873;48;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The interior of this lively establishment resembles a classroom, and indeed this building was once a home economics school. Today you can see the 'master' at work preparing his lesson in French gastronomy thanks to the open kitchen. He has a sound knowledge of his ingredients and incorporates a nod to Flemish cuisine into his no-nonsense dishes. Whether you order the intensely flavoured typical Southern French fish soup or côte de bœuf served with a house-made béarnaise sauce and fried potatoes: at Rijsel, every dish is a feast!;;[]
4985;Bistro TWO;Netherlands;Roermond;Roerkade 11, Roermond, 6041 KZ, Netherlands;51.1955572;5.9839903;81;true;false;Farm to table;If you're craving comfort food and a glass of fine wine, Dux hotel's vibrant bistro, with its lovely terrace on Roerkade promenade, is the place for you. With an extensive à la carte selection and a more playful set menu created by Lambert Walter, there's something to suit every taste. A duck liver terrine to start? Then perhaps Livar pork belly with an exquisite shallot sauce, freshly cut fries and a salad with a zingy vinaigrette? Or would you prefer their Mediterranean aubergine dish, before finally tucking into your tarte Tatin? Here, familiar flavours are given a subtle modern twist, without skimping on the portions – and its fantastic value for money!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
4986;Marie;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Nieuwe Doelenstraat 2, Amsterdam, 1012 AC, Netherlands;52.3674471;4.8943852;57;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Marie possesses that charm typical of the South of France. The brasserie decor exudes luxury, but the terrace overlooking the boats and bridges is where everyone wants a table. This tranquil oasis in the heart of the city is enhanced by the Mediterranean finesse of the cuisine. The lamb fillet and cheeks with a perfectly balanced hollandaise sauce, the salt-baked sea bass, the generous beef tartare: these are down-to-earth dishes that pack a punch, and they are simply irresistible. This is what Bib Gourmand is all about!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4987;Bij Erik;Netherlands;Leidschendam;Sluisplein 11, Leidschendam, 2266 AV, Netherlands;52.0798754;4.3981005;91;true;true;Modern French;Wood, metal and leather create an intimate feel, although a table on the terrace is also a good choice: the view of the lock and windmill is magnificent. Erik Tas will have diners' mouths watering with fresh combinations in which stocks and sauces lead to wonderful harmonies.;Terrace;[]
4988;Alma Bodega;Netherlands;Oisterwijk;De Lind 45A, Oisterwijk, 5061 HT, Netherlands;51.5811174;5.1972246;18;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Contemporary;The more down-to-earth little brother of MICHELIN-starred Alma has its own personality. Chic marble and stylish design give this laid-back restaurant flair. You can drop in any time of day to indulge in a fresh take on familiar flavours. The menu features a variety of dishes that will tempt your taste buds, including gyoza, köfte, pâté en croûte, perfectly done entrecôte with a delicious veal jus, rum baba and more. The skilfully prepared and generously flavoured dishes never fail to impress. Curated by Malou Hagenaars, the wine list always includes some exciting finds. Be sure to make your reservation in good time to avoid disappointment!;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
4989;Brasserij Kok Verhoeven;Netherlands;Tilburg;NS Plein 32, Tilburg, 5014 DC, Netherlands;51.5611969;5.0926538;70;true;true;Seafood;Take the left-hand door to a fashionable, cosmopolitan restaurant offering delicious fish and shellfish. Or, the right-hand door to the more relaxed brasserie with an extensive menu (again largely fish), which will win guests over with its quality and powerful flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
4991;Sea Palace;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Oosterdokskade 8, Amsterdam, 1011 AE, Netherlands;52.3756155;4.9071289;70;false;false;Cantonese, Chinese;With statues of Chinese warlords Guan Yu, Liu Bei and Zhang Fei, pagoda motifs and wooden chinoiserie everywhere you turn, the level of detail in the decor of this floating restaurant is extraordinary. You may be just a stone's throw from Centraal Station, but you feel like you are in a Ming dynasty palace. The wide-ranging menu is an ode to authentic Cantonese cuisine. Think steamed dim sum with prawns, stir-fried noodles with beef and soy sauce. The Peking duck (for two) is certainly a tempting option. A memorable culinary adventure that won't break the bank!;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
4992;Dokjard;Netherlands;Groningen;Noorderhaven 63, Groningen, 9712 VJ, Netherlands;53.2198672;6.5571028;18;false;false;Creative;Set in a former warehouse by the picturesque Noorderhaven, this relaxed "brew-bistro" offers a delightful blend of pub atmosphere and attentive service. When you first enter, you will be greeted by the aroma of freshly brewed beer and the sight of towering brewing kettles. The kitchen team pushes the boundaries, effortlessly weaving between the classic and creative. From steak tartare with an Asian twist to melt-in-your-mouth pork cheeks with dukkah and sesame seeds, this cuisine is vibrant and imaginative. The house beers perfectly complement the dishes, adding a personal touch. What a place!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
4993;Rotonde;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Goudsesingel 230, Rotterdam, 3011 KE, Netherlands;51.9240615;4.4913759;84;true;true;Vegetarian, Modern Cuisine;They pick up their vegetables in an electric van. The aim is to utilise every part of their produce, which is grown with respect for nature and the seasons. All of their wines are biodynamic or natural. This vintage-style restaurant is deeply committed to sustainability and is always looking for ways to do better (visit their website to learn more). This vision is brought to life in creative, intriguing and entirely vegetarian dishes that are incredibly flavoursome, sophisticated and full of surprises. Think bell pepper confit and an XO sauce made from mushrooms to elevate a sapid leek stalk. A spot by the open kitchen is a must if you want to watch the chefs tame the flames of their wood-fired barbecue!;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4994;Escobar;Netherlands;Breskens;Spuiplein 15, Breskens, 4511 AN, Netherlands;51.3966964;3.5591863;94;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Spanish;This colourful restaurant has a real holiday feel, with its lively Spanish ambience and friendly, enthusiastic staff. The menu features a wide selection of dishes, from well-known tapas to more unusual and less conventional options. An excellent restaurant in which to enjoy a Spanish meal with friends.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
4995;Restaurant Blauw;Netherlands;Utrecht;Springweg 64, Utrecht, 3511 VT, Netherlands;52.0878315;5.1194579;77;false;false;Indonesian;Tradition, a street food influence, authenticity and purity are the words that best sum up this popular restaurant, which showcases the full array of Indonesian cuisine. The rijsttafel (a medley of dishes with rice – also available in a vegan version) provides an excellent opportunity to discover the chef's talent for seasoning and balancing intense flavours. From the succulence of the lamb, the distinctly nutty flavour of the peanut sauce and the delicate spiciness of the gado gado, you can see that this is a chef who knows how to combine generosity with subtlety. Be sure to try the roast goat meat as well!;Air conditioning;[]
4996;Hofstede de Blaak;Netherlands;Tilburg;Dussenpad 1, Tilburg, 5032 WL, Netherlands;51.5493217;5.0442561;90;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The charm of this authentic English country house (1907), the classic half-timbering and elegant details, the peaceful surroundings – it is hard not to be moved by this setting. The chef loves working with fine ingredients and accentuates their finesse with contemporary seasonings. He is fond of combining diverse flavours to create elegant nuances. Be sure to try the excellent set menu.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
4997;Zilt & Zoet;Netherlands;Maartensdijk;Dorpsweg 153, Maartensdijk, 3738 CD, Netherlands;52.1590092;5.1899938;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The refreshed interior of this countryside villa combines the modern and the vintage, and is a great example of cosy Dutch ambience. The extensive set menu (a choice of three, four or five courses) is impressive. It is created by a chef who creates modern, lavish dishes from largely seasonal produce.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4998;Spandershoeve;Netherlands;Hilversum;Bussumergrintweg 46, Hilversum, 1217 BS, Netherlands;52.2391119;5.1612772;73;false;false;Indonesian;Spandershoeve has been showcasing traditional Indonesian cuisine since 1972. Anita Boerenkamp was the first chef in the Netherlands to put a sophisticated spin on the famous rijsttafel. Her confident take on the fiery and intricate blend of spices was remarkable. She taught Timo, her grandson, all he knows – how to roast goat until it is succulent, how to employ soy sauce to powerful effect, and how to add texture with raw and fried onions. This welcoming neighbourhood restaurant is the perfect introduction to Indonesian generosity and hospitality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
4999;Umami by Han;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Binnenrotte 140, Rotterdam, 3011 HC, Netherlands;51.9226136;4.485997;22;true;false;Asian, Chinese;A colourful restaurant with a winning culinary concept: intensely flavoursome Asian cuisine with a French twist. The extensive menu features a tempting array of dishes that are also perfect for sharing. Exquisite sea bass ceviche, crispy duck with an orange cream, vegetarian gyoza with a kimchi and chilli mayonnaise sauce… deciding what to order will not be easy! With plenty of wonderful vegetarian options and its €25 lunch deal, this place is a real asset to Rotterdam's dining scene.;Terrace;[]
5000;Uit de Kunst;Netherlands;Vijlen;Vijlenberg 76, Vijlen, 6294 AZ, Netherlands;50.789467;5.962875;22;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Hikers and cyclists who test themselves to their limits on the Vijlenberg are rewarded by this modern restaurant situated right at the top. The superb view from the terrace is a feast for the eyes, while the traditional dishes served here are a treat for the taste buds. Simple yet refined and delicious cuisine.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5001;Asian Glories;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Westewagenstraat 74, Rotterdam, 3011 AT, Netherlands;51.9209369;4.4831568;26;true;true;Chinese;The natural light and high ceilings are the first things to catch your eye when you walk into Asian Glories, but it is the view of the church and the canal that really wins you over. Understated Asian art lends a touch of individuality to the decor. The open kitchen affords glimpses of hanging Peking ducks and busy chefs at work. The culinary traditions of Canton and Sichuan prevail here, served up in generous, umami-rich dishes. Dim sum, prepared in house, chicken tempura, a beautifully light and airy steamed bun with pork belly confit: good luck choosing from the extensive à la carte and set menus!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5002;De Basiliek;Netherlands;The Hague;Korte Houtstraat 4a, The Hague, 2511 CD, Netherlands;52.0794311;4.3169553;96;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With its trendy, lively atmosphere, colourful decor and pretty terrace at the front, De Basiliek has a decidedly convivial atmosphere. The tempting menu features fresh Mediterranean dishes full of generous flavours, with vegetables playing an important role. The chef draws on his culinary expertise to deliver exciting cuisine brimming with clever combinations. The impressive wine list proposes plenty of options by the glass and in half-bottles. Excellent value for money!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5003;HAVN;Netherlands;Hoorn;Oude Doelenkade 7, Hoorn, 1621 BH, Netherlands;52.6385018;5.0635382;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Two views, one of the historical harbour and the other of the open kitchen, grab your attention as soon as you enter this restaurant with a buzzing atmosphere. The same playful energy is even more apparent in the creations of chef Robin Blaauw. He is, for instance, as happy to dabble in the rich flavours of South American cuisine as he is to dive into the Asian culinary world. Drawing inspiration from his travels, he works with the finest Dutch produce to conjure up his dishes. Thanks to his eye for detail, this young chef has already made an impressive career for himself.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5004;LEV by Mike;Netherlands;Winterswijk;Badweg 4, Winterswijk, 7102 EG, Netherlands;51.9571861;6.7252001;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;LEV now occupies the first floor of a historical bathhouse, from where diners can enjoy panoramic views of a natural pond and the cosy charm of a modern brasserie. Mike Vrijdag's culinary concept is a hit: the menu features an extensive selection of small plates ranging from comfort food to cutting-edge creations. This chef's technical skills and playful spirit ensure a dining experience that is always engaging. Take, for instance, his freshly caught sea bass tartare combined with tangy pickled cucumber, soy gel, and a wasabi sorbet providing subtly sweet and spicy kick. A symphony of flavours awaits!;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5005;De Schans by Mike & Wes;Netherlands;Montfoort;Willeskop 87, Montfoort, 3417 MC, Netherlands;52.0237624;4.9079181;91;false;false;Creative;When they took over De Schans, Mike and Wes, respectively sommelier and chef, added a trendier, more relaxed vibe, whilst retaining the establishment’s commitment to fine food and wine. The chef crafts dishes in tune with the zeitgeist using cutting-edge culinary techniques to create a subtle blend of textures and unexpected flavours. The set menu is definitely worth sampling!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5006;De Aubergerie;Netherlands;Amersfoort;Kamp 88, Amersfoort, 3811 AT, Netherlands;52.158616;5.3971042;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The sweets that used to be sold in this establishment dating back to the 1700s have given way to delicacies such as lobster and Venus clams. This new direction is reflected in the artistic photographs hanging on the walls of this cosy, intimate-feeling restaurant. Chef Han showcases his ingredients in cutting-edge dishes drawing on solid French foundations and with the odd creative flourish. Take, for instance, his succulent marbré of goose breast and rillette, with the sweet earthiness of textures of beetroot, combined with vibrant pickled mustard seeds and punchy creamed rocket. The friendly atmosphere of De Aubergerie also comes down to the personal service of your hostess Ingrid.;Terrace;[]
5007;Oriole;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Oudezijds Voorburgwal 197, Amsterdam, 1012 EX, Netherlands;52.3710574;4.8952632;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Oriole is a haven of calm in the bustling city centre. The upscale bistro decor is alluring – the bar is terrific – though a spot on the verdant terrace is really the place to be. This is quite the hidden gem! The contemporary take on Mediterranean flavours, with a particular emphasis on vegetables, suits the setting perfectly. The "Oriole Express" set menu, with different options for each course, showcases the cuisine and produce of a given country every month. Whether you're tucking into grilled pimientos de Padrón, pâté en croûte or frango estufado with chicken, this Mediterranean-style feast is authentic, exquisite and inspired.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5008;Fa. Pekelhaaring;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Van Woustraat 127, Amsterdam, 1074 AH, Netherlands;52.3532904;4.9026838;69;false;false;Farm to table, Italian;Welcome to the urban canteen of a number of Amsterdam’s local residents – a relaxed eatery without unnecessary sophistication, but one which is both authentic and welcoming. The cuisine is influenced (but not exclusively) by Italy and the chef enjoys adding his own variations and personal touches (such as crunchy textures and local influences) to his cooking. The varied à la carte is impressive indeed!;;[]
5009;Gym & Gin;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Kralingseweg 224, Rotterdam, 3062 CG, Netherlands;51.9282532;4.536081;93;true;true;International, Asian Influences;The name Gym & Gin is a reference to the balance we all have to find between pleasure and healthy living. After a workout in the gym upstairs, unwind in this lounge-like establishment with its vintage colour scheme and designer furniture. The cocktail/gin list as well as Kevin Valkhoff's set menu and à la carte options are all as impressive as each other. Inspired by exotic subtleties, he brings flavours to life with original flashes of inspiration, such as adding red pepper to cucumber and mango in order to give salmon some extra pep. If you fancy an afternoon aperitif and a light bite, the good news is that Gym & Gin is always open.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5010;Waers;Netherlands;Roermond;Bakkerstraat 30, Roermond, 6041 JR, Netherlands;51.1916938;5.9881951;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Scandinavian;Waers is the incarnation of anti-conformity, which sums up Dennis Vermeulen to a T! In his restaurant showcasing a strong sense of Scandinavian purity, he brings out the very best of market-fresh ingredients and the seasons. There’s no fuss here, just original, well-balanced dishes with a contemporary feel that are well worth discovering and offer excellent value for money.;;[]
5011;Lazuur;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Purmerplein 8, Amsterdam, 1023 BD, Netherlands;52.3910255;4.9433137;60;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This charming neighbourhood restaurant proposes a refined fusion of French and Portuguese cuisine. The appealing set menu offers a choice of dishes including, for example, kale, bouchot mussels and molho de coentro. The chef cooks his ingredients to perfection and adds a dash of Mediterranean flair, as demonstrated in his soft-cooked pulpo, creamy riso venere and espuma of paprika. Be sure to check out the impressive port collection, which contains plenty of surprises.;;[]
5012;MOUT & HOUT;Netherlands;Vessem;Jan Smuldersstraat 24, Vessem, 5512 AZ, Netherlands;51.419311;5.2889604;52;false;false;Barbecue, Grills;Beer and fire are at the heart of this establishment, whose name translates as "Malt & Wood". Next to the Beerze family brewery, which is steeped in history, there is an American-style bar with a stone pizza oven at the front. The back of the restaurant has a raw industrial feel. The chefs like to work with the Josper charcoal oven, parrilla grill and Oklahoma smoker to infuse their dishes with smoky flavours. For example, they put a unique twist on vitello tonnato by searing the veal on charcoal. Of course, meat takes centre stage in these generous and ingredient-led dishes, but there are also vegetarian and fish options on the menu to whet your appetite.;Terrace;[]
5013;Te Koop in Tilburg;Netherlands;Tilburg;Jan Pieterszoon Coenstraat 71, Tilburg, 5018 CP, Netherlands;51.5579929;5.1062055;90;true;false;International, French Contemporary;Crispy fried soft shell crab with broccoli and couscous, tomato tartare with a Manchego foam and herb oil, or beef bavette steak with veal jus infused with cloves and cardamom… Located just outside Tilburg city centre, this cosy neighbourhood restaurant with a warm and welcoming decor has it all. The chef, who enjoys tapping into international flavours and makes sure to cater to vegetarians, showcases his cuisine in an appealing choice of courses from which diners compile their own set menu. What's not to like?;;[]
5014;Café Visscher;Netherlands;Leiden;Stationsweg 7, Leiden, 2312 AS, Netherlands;52.1645428;4.4843476;20;true;true;French;You could definitely call Arie Visscher's "café" a luxury brasserie. An abundance of red velvet, marble and copper give the place a remarkably warm and welcoming feel. Open all day from 11am, it's a great option for lunch, dinner or a quick bite at the bar. Chef Visschers specialises in French classics such as steak tartare elevated with smoked eel, or sea bass with a delightfully buttery potato mousseline and artichoke. He also showcases his creativity with a modern dish based on hispi cabbage. This Rotterdam native sticks to a single set menu, crafting beautifully balanced no-nonsense cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5015;De Wilg;Netherlands;De Mortel;Sint-Antoniusstraat 30, De Mortel, 5425 VE, Netherlands;51.5413498;5.7081595;34;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;The low-mounted coat hooks and ballet bar serve as reminders that the location was once a primary school and ballet hall. But there are no more strict rules here – the building has been transformed into a warm and welcoming restaurant. Boy van Gerwen steers clear of over-complicating matters, winning diners over with, for example, the fresh earthy notes of a beetroot tartare, the vibrant flavours of confit duck leg accompanied by a robust veal jus with morels, but also the spiciness of a lentil dahl. De Wilg represents generous cooking and great value for money.;Terrace;[]
5016;Auberge - cuisine française;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Albert Cuypstraat 58, Amsterdam, 1072 CV, Netherlands;52.3548882;4.8896283;22;true;false;French;This quintessential bistro serves classics of the genre, such as an indulgent take on œufs en meurette with an onion and red wine confit, barbecued baby chicken presented on vintage tableware, profiteroles stuffed with vanilla ice cream and an intense chocolate sauce – every dish is artfully composed. In its wallet-friendly à la carte and prix-fixe menus, there are plenty of tempting options, and the same goes for the expertly curated selection of French wines – Jan is the man to ask for recommendations. The decor is simply enchanting with its copper pans, elegant glass wine cabinet and undeniable je ne sais quoi.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5017;Boompjes;Netherlands;Overloon;Irenestraat 1, Overloon, 5825 CA, Netherlands;51.5712113;5.946087;91;true;true;Country cooking, Cuisine from the Marches;As you enter, you pass the brasserie, where you can enjoy a casual lunch or snack. The space at the rear of the restaurant is like an oasis, with trees, plants and wood setting the tone. The terrace seamlessly merges with chef Jaap Volman's kitchen garden. An ambassador of Dutch cuisine, his cooking style is very much French-inspired, but his creative use of vegetables and fruit adds lightness and freshness . The velvety consommé with its subtle acidity accompanying the succulent pork cheeks was just as delightful as the vibrant medley of garden-fresh vegetables and herbs. What a way to showcase Dutch produce!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5019;Tabkeaw;Netherlands;Maastricht;Rechtstraat 102, Maastricht, 6221 EL, Netherlands;50.8479898;5.6982345;20;true;true;Thai;With its bamboo panelling, “pagoda” bar and typical landscapes on the walls, Tabkeaw’s interior is a journey in itself, with the lively buzz of the Wyck district providing the backdrop. The cuisine here is as traditional as the decor, featuring the authentic aromas of a tom kha kai, and the spicy harmony of fresh fish, curry and coconut. A culinary adventure!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5020;Bij Mette;Netherlands;Linschoten;Dorpstraat 41, Linschoten, 3461 CP, Netherlands;52.0612753;4.9152348;41;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Picturesque Linschoten is worth a visit in its own right, but be sure to look out for this beautifully converted grocery shop with its distinctive spiral staircase located a stone's throw from the leaning clock tower. This is old Dutch charm at its best! Chef-patron Carel Alberts welcomes you personally before showing off his expertise in the French classics. Wonderful local produce, intense sauces, respect for tradition: it all makes for an enjoyable culinary experience. Feel free to ask the chef about his French wine list – he will be happy to tell you more.;Terrace;[]
5021;Promessa;Netherlands;Eersel;Markt 3, Eersel, 5521 AJ, Netherlands;51.360403;5.3080751;39;false;true;World Cuisine;With "Food is art" as their motto, the chefs at this trendy and laid-back restaurant treat their plates like canvases, placing a strong emphasis on aesthetics. But fear not: these visually stunning dishes are also packed with flavour. Koen van den Kerkhof's creativity draws on the culinary traditions of the Netherlands, France and more far-flung locations, with his limitless imagination reflected in a wide-ranging menu. Diners enjoy dishes such as albacore tuna poppadom, classically prepared pheasant breast with a rich veal jus, succulent beef rendang, or spaghetti aglio e olio. They have the art of indulgence down to a T!;;[]
5022;De Watergeus;Netherlands;Noorden;Simon van Capelweg 10, Noorden, 2431 AG, Netherlands;52.1615252;4.8121482;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The walk alongside the canals affords a foretaste of what you can expect in this refurbished restaurant that enjoys a superb waterside location. The chef mixes classical recipes with generosity and modern textures. His culinary palette is diverse and intriguing and the formula is highly recommended. Enquire about overnight stays and boat trips (with a picnic basket) on the Nieuwkoopse Plassen.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5023;Landgoed de Holtweijde;Netherlands;Lattrop;Spiekweg 7, Lattrop, 7635 LP, Netherlands;52.43141;6.9652;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;This estate is a beautiful example of classic rural elegance, offering fine views of the surrounding meadows. The chef employs lavish preparation methods and regional produce to create delightful dishes full of strong flavours. A trip here is well worth the effort!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5025;Raedthuys;Netherlands;Doetinchem;Raadhuisstraat 14, Doetinchem, 7001 EW, Netherlands;51.9649178;6.293137;74;true;true;Farm to table;Just about everything is homemade in this restaurant, which has its own bakery, own patisserie and even its own smokehouse! Choose from the wide selection of generous dishes created by chef Marion, who focuses on genuine traditional flavours with no unnecessary frills. Combine your classic meal with one of the numerous beers on offer here, many of which are on tap.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5026;Bistro Aragosta;Netherlands;Leeuwarden;Voorstreek 12, Leeuwarden, 8911 JN, Netherlands;53.2022697;5.7993673;29;false;true;French;The Aragosta has the warm, intimate feel of a bistro, where your welcoming host will introduce you to cuisine that is mainly French in feel with the occasional Italian influence, ranging from seafood risotto to duck terrine. Overall, the cooking here is classical, highly subtle and very tasty!;Air conditioning;[]
5027;Bistro Nijeholt;Netherlands;Beetsterzwaag;Van Harinxmaweg 10, Beetsterzwaag, 9244 CJ, Netherlands;53.058018;6.0910335;39;true;false;Farm to table;Located on the beautiful verdant Lauswolt estate, this atmospheric bistro is wonderfully relaxed. There is a fantastic set menu with a choice of generous options for each course and no unnecessary frills. An example would be a slice of intensely flavoursome pâté with dried fruit followed by al dente local asparagus, smoked salmon, a poached egg and hollandaise sauce. Top off your meal with a warm clafoutis with blueberries and verbena ice cream, and you will understand why Bistro Nijeholt is the epitome of a Bib Gourmand restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5029;Lucie Cocina;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Kleine Berg 34b, Eindhoven, 5611 JV, Netherlands;51.4367211;5.4749003;26;false;true;Spanish Contemporary, Creative;Lucie Cocina boasts a hip, lively atmosphere that captures the essence of an authentic tapas bar. From the moment you step inside, you will be won over by the decor with its vintage-style globe chandeliers, floral-patterned mosaic floor and bar stools at the counter where the seafood is displayed. The menu features an irresistible array of options, from traditional ham croquettes and tortillas to more inventive tapas creations. How about steamed zamburiñas with antiboise, finely chopped jalapeño and a hollandaise foam? Or rather braised veal cheeks with mojo rojo and deep-fried potato cubes? The fantastic value for money means you can sample a wide variety of dishes without breaking the bank. ¡Buen provecho!;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5030;Basaal;Netherlands;The Hague;Dunne Bierkade 3, The Hague, 2512 BC, Netherlands;52.0735781;4.3157646;17;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;With a delightful waterside terrace for sunny days and a cosy interior with a Scandinavian and vintage feel for when the weather is cooler, this inviting neighbourhood restaurant has plenty going for it. But, of course, the focal point is the kitchen, where chef Daan van Munster creates honest market-fresh cuisine. Whether you prefer to share with your dining companions or go solo, you can compile your own set menu from a tempting list of options, including some rather unconventional dishes. Think creamy veal neck and foie gras terrine, or tender veal tongue with coco de Paimpol beans and a robust veal stock sauce. This chef takes his cue from the seasons, and vegetables are always a key part of his dishes. The moderately priced wine list is the icing on the cake.;Terrace;[]
5031;A-Fusion;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Zeedijk 130, Amsterdam, 1012 BC, Netherlands;52.3731878;4.900192;81;false;false;Asian;A-Fusion immediately captivates diners with its vibrant atmosphere. On the menu is an appealingly exotic blend of Chinese, Japanese, Thai and Korean flavours. On entering, you will see sushi being made to order, and as you head further in you will notice the barbecue and the dim sum and wok kitchen. Thanks to the reasonably priced à la carte menu and small portions, you can try everything. The depth of flavour of the minced pork dumplings, the spice and umami of the XO sauce, the ultra-fresh salmon topping the nigiri... This is one of Amsterdam's best Asian restaurants!;Counter dining;[]
5032;Scheepskameel;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Kattenburgerstraat 7, gebouw 24, Amsterdam, 1018 JA, Netherlands;52.3736022;4.9145821;54;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Scheepskameel is a lively, relaxed establishment, providing honest, straightforward food. Everything here starts with top-quality ingredients, prepared without fuss and beautifully seasoned. The wine list is comprised entirely of German wines and accompanies the food perfectly.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5033;Serre;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Ferdinand Bolstraat 333, Amsterdam, 1072 LH, Netherlands;52.3486469;4.8939984;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A bright space with a gorgeous canalside terrace, Serre has a Japanese minimalist feel. Reflecting the international atmosphere of the luxury Hotel Okura, this restaurant serves fusion cuisine with a slight penchant for Far Eastern influences. Start with a platter of super-fresh oysters and then pick one of the sharing dishes. Alternatively, there is a set menu with mouth-watering options for each course, such as smoked salmon with a refreshing Thai twist. And those who prefer to avoid meat and fish are sure to find something to their liking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5034;Bistrot Regent;Netherlands;Nijmegen;Hertogstraat 71, Nijmegen, 6511 RW, Netherlands;51.8453007;5.8687503;68;true;true;French, Traditional Cuisine;Why travel all the way to France when you can dine at this timeless bistro, where the best of what the country has to offer is showcased in both the excellent wine list and traditional dishes? Think aromatic fish soup with rouille and croutons, or butter-soft duck leg confit with a zesty caper sauce, followed by crisp tarte Tatin for dessert. You can tell that Robbert and Heleen put their heart and soul into running Bistrot Regent.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5035;Restaurant élevé;Netherlands;Leeuwarden;Heliconweg 52, Leeuwarden, 8914 AT, Netherlands;53.1999349;5.7744404;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A superlative view from the top of the WTC Hotel over Leeuwarden is underscored by a hip, casually welcoming ambience. The restaurant is both affordable and yet exclusive. Chef Kalkman’s cooking is modern, subtle and free of unnecessary frills. You can expect premium local produce, jazzed up with the occasional modern twist and generous flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
5036;Café Samabe;Netherlands;Haarlem;Korte Veerstraat 1, Haarlem, 2011 CL, Netherlands;52.3796423;4.6374348;85;false;true;Indonesian, Balinese;The spicy aromas hit you the moment you enter this colonial-era building dating from 1899. An abundance of wood and an exotic colour scheme make for a uniquely charming setting inside – this place calls itself a café because of its casual atmosphere. The home-style Indonesian cuisine, with a slight preference for Balinese specialities, is indulgent and packs a punch. Think aromatic martabak, rich authentic rijsttafels (including vegetarian options) with spicy rendang and intensely flavoursome sambal goreng telor… At Café Samabe, a feast awaits!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5037;Bistrôt Chapeau;Netherlands;Blaricum;Huizerweg 1, Blaricum, 1261 AR, Netherlands;52.2729918;5.2435447;75;true;true;French;Experience the charm of its colourful bistro decor, the peace and quiet of the terrace and a soothing ambience in this restaurant straight out of quintessential Burgundy! Here, Nicky Quarz revives often forgotten French classics without any unnecessary frivolity yet teeming with authentic flavours. Through his sauces, intensity etc, enjoy a welcome return to the very roots of French cuisine.;Terrace;[]
5038;Restaurant ñ;Netherlands;The Hague;Nobelstraat 22, The Hague, 2513 BD, Netherlands;52.0782047;4.3058239;30;true;false;Spanish;The yellow façade of this relaxed restaurant gives it a southern feel, which is further enhanced by the aromas of typical, authentic Spanish and Mediterranean dishes that greet you as you step through the door. The delicious options on the menu include fresh seafood, spicy chilli peppers, and dishes served with fresh, sophisticated sauces, as well as an excellent selection of cheese and charcuterie.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5039;Huson;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Scheepstimmermanslaan 14, Rotterdam, 3011 BS, Netherlands;51.9107362;4.4783432;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Huson is a trendy establishment where a lively industriousness always prevails. Here guests' mouths will water at the marvellous pairing of creativity with international ingredients in small dishes which are as subtle as they are exuberant. The chef is a dab hand at beautifully balancing fullness of flavour with freshness, as his signature dishes show.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5040;De Watermolen;Netherlands;Velp;H. Avelinghstraat 154, Velp, 6881 VW, Netherlands;51.9946924;5.9758051;32;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This watermill, which is over 600 years old, is without a doubt the star attraction of this charming restaurant. Both the warm and welcoming interior and the secluded terrace are popular. Ramon Klaassen takes great pride in his work, which you cannot fail to notice during his interactions with diners. His unique take on classic dishes never disappoints. For example he rolls up soft-boiled duck ham and fills it with a rich poultry mousse. Playful garnishes such as an onion chutney with nuts and reduced balsamic vinegar add that little something extra. The set menu (with options) is a hit – even for those who do not eat meat or fish.;Terrace;[]
5041;Senang;Netherlands;Zwolle;Samuël Hirschstraat 1, Zwolle, 8011 PT, Netherlands;52.5112371;6.0957422;34;false;false;Asian Contemporary, Sharing;Chinese dragon heads and lanterns, Japanese sake boxes, photos of owners Jonnie and Thérèse Boer taken during their travels across Asia: this colourful restaurant embodies a melting pot of impressions, and that certainly goes for the food, too. The menu features dishes that are full of flavour and fresh nuances from the Near, Middle and Far East. Chicken yakitori, ceviche, ramen, wonton… This is a truly wonderful culinary adventure. Be sure to try out the generous "Senang Table"!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5042;Wielinga;Netherlands;Leiden;Nieuwe Rijn 28, Leiden, 2312 JD, Netherlands;52.1577798;4.4927003;86;true;false;Modern French;Housed in a historical building, this charming restaurant has more of an intimate feel at the front than at the back, where there is more natural light. However, the best spot is the canal-side terrace – perfect for soaking up Leiden's vibrant atmosphere. With dishes such as nori-wrapped leek terrine and candied veal in a rich brown stock and red wine sauce, chef Richard de Vries proves his expertise in classic cooking techniques. Served à la carte or as a wonderful set menu with options, this indulgent cuisine keeps diners coming back for more. Expertly curated wine list.;Terrace;[]
5043;Resumé by 6&24;Netherlands;The Hague;Bierkade 16A, The Hague, 2512 AB, Netherlands;52.0748877;4.3188352;66;true;true;International;A glass of crisp rosé with a fine selection of cured meats in the wine bar or on the canal-side terrace, a few small plates to share, or a complete meal in the restaurant, with its floral, slightly tropical-looking decor… You have plenty of options here. The tempting menu includes an intensely flavoursome ceviche, a vegetarian dish based on dry-aged beetroot, and a rich tarte Tatin. The chefs are just as happy to play with exotic seasonings as they are to turn out distinctly Dutch dishes. In short: delicious, inspired and generous!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5044;Gitane;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Jan Pieter Heijestraat 146, Amsterdam, 1054 MK, Netherlands;52.3619414;4.8643503;97;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant's pavement terrace, where you can soak up the atmosphere of the trendy Oud-West neighbourhood, and its round windows certainly draw the eye. The Zen-style interior with its distinctive 1970s feel is equally impressive. This is a casual dining establishment, which opens its doors at 10am, every day of the week. The Mediterranean dishes served here have a lot in common with the recipes of Yotam Ottolenghi. Take, for example, the braised pork cheeks with creamy orzo, crunchy oyster mushroom, Petroto cheese and a fresh yoghurt and celeriac purée – what a beautiful plate of food! The chef makes sure that there are plenty of vegetarian and vegan options on the menu, and he keeps his prices affordable. One of Amsterdam's gems!;Brunch,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5045;Gary’s;Canada;Vancouver;1485 W. 12th Ave, Vancouver, V6H 1M6, Canada;49.2608198;-123.1384381;90;false;true;French, Contemporary;It's easy to be won over by this convivial neighborhood spot, which owes its easygoing charms to the combined efforts of partners Bailey Hayward and Mathew Bishop (who oversee the service and the kitchen, respectively). To match the relaxed, friendly vibe, the cuisine is rustic and approachable, offering hearty dishes that draw inspiration from French country cooking, as in asparagus with saffron rouille, or pork collar with parsley sauce—and don't miss out on the fluffy, freshly baked rye rolls, served with green garlic butter. For a final slather of indulgence, do order dessert, like a rum baba soaked with chamomile-scented syrup and capped with a ribbon of decadent pistachio custard and a cloud of chantilly.;;[]
5047;Sushi Hil;Canada;Vancouver;3330 Main St., Vancouver, V5V 3M7, Canada;49.25546;-123.10126;76;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Natural light floods the dining room at Sushi Hil, where blonde wood furnishings set a clean, contemporary tone. The best seats are naturally at the counter, where guests can watch the talented and engaging Chef Hil Nguy craft his jewel-like pieces with great care and efficiency. Seasonal ingredients and high quality fish shine, as in a dish of Japanese sweet prawns accompanied by the just-removed head, served simply over crushed ice with a dab of wasabi. Aka Isaki, or red grunt, is served with orange to underscore the power play of salinity and citrusy sweetness, while aji (mackerel) from Kagoshima has an added zing with grated ginger-scallion. Other standouts include otoro, ikura and chopped tuna, and black throat perch.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
5048;Farmer's Apprentice;Canada;Vancouver;1535 W. 6th Ave., Vancouver, V6J 1R1, Canada;49.2662673;-123.1397561;43;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Farmer's Apprentice is a true neighborhood gem. This tiny space with rustic appeal brings people together over innovative dishes like shrimp-crusted striped bass with XO sauce or radish and Sieglinde potato salad with chili-miso-tamarind vinaigrette. Fresh sourdough bread is baked daily— served with chicken asiento, it's a can't-miss. Local produce is feted, as in kale rapini with lush vadouvan butter, accompanied by lemony labneh, smoked pickled raisins and toasted hazelnuts. On weekends, Chef Alden Ong switches gears and serves Basta Barbecue at lunch, inspired by Tausug-Filipino cuisine. The 63 Acres beef cheeks with buttery lettuce leaves, nouc cham and sunchoke kimchi will have you planning a repeat visit before your plate is clean.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5049;Karma Indian Bistro;Canada;Vancouver;2741 W. 4th Ave., Vancouver, V6K 1P9, Canada;49.2684501;-123.1671052;55;true;true;Indian, Regional Cuisine;Wood planks, plush banquettes and rustic lighting set a sophisticated tone at Karma Indian Bistro, but its elegant setting isn't the only reason to make a reservation. The food is as pleasing as the surroundings, and the chef's serious vision is outlined on a menu of wonderfully delicious traditional dishes interspersed with bold, innovative plates.Expect richly spiced favorites such as chicken Madras, a fragrant specialty of South India. Coconut rice is the perfect sidekick to sop up all of that delicious, creamy sauce. Savor each bite of the mouthwatering jumbo prawns in a pureed spinach curry, but do leave room for dessert—perhaps the saffron rice pudding or a cooling mango ice cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5050;Motonobu Udon;Canada;Vancouver;3501 E. Hastings St., Vancouver, V5K 0E5, Canada;49.2811743;-123.0282115;22;true;true;Udon, Japanese;It's worth frequenting this spot, where a simple, light-flooded dining room buzzes with tables full of diners slurping bowls of noodles and savoring sides. As the name hints, it's all about udon here, where the noodles are handmade and cut fresh to order. Traditional varieties are available hot or cold, served with tempura bits and fresh green onions or with mentsyu sauce and tempura egg. Specialty bowls, such as the spicy tanton with braised pork belly, Shanghai bok choy in a spiced chicken and dashi broth, are equally enticing. Peruse the add-ons and you may find yourself topping your bowl with piles of tempura treats, and inari and pressed sushi round out the menu. Don't see something you want? Ask, as the accommodating staff aims to please.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
5051;Anh and Chi;Canada;Vancouver;3388 Main St., Vancouver, V5V 3M7, Canada;49.2548465;-123.1008788;79;true;true;Vietnamese, Regional Cuisine;The brother-and-sister team have crafted a clean, cool space outfitted with midcentury modern furnishings while nodding to the past—a blue neon sign by the bar is a relic from the former restaurant. For more than thirty years, their parents' restaurant occupied this spot, but Anh and Chi now welcomes a new generation of diners. The menu is a love letter to Vietnam. Gỏi bắp chuối cua lột, a salad of chopped softshell crab piled high atop a banana blossom, is cool and bursting with flavor. Chạo tôm bánh hỏi is prepared in a classic way, with grilled prawn mousse served with an array of fresh herbs, and there is pho, of course. The dessert menu changes daily, but if on offer, the house-made coffee mousse is a standout.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5052;Fable Kitchen;Canada;Vancouver;1944 W. 4th Ave., Vancouver, V6J 1M5, Canada;49.2683161;-123.1489222;31;true;false;Contemporary, North American;This popular farm-to-table cafe has been drawing crowds to Kitsilano for over a decade. The setting is lively and comfortable, with exposed red brick walls, wood furnishings and two varnished wood counters seating a handful of diners facing the open kitchen. During daytime hours, the team turns out hollandaise-slicked eggs Benedict (and variations), Johnny cakes topped with pulled pork and tomato jam and thickly sliced challah French toast plated with caramelized apples and whipped mascarpone. A side order of rosti, two blocks of uniformly golden-brown finely shredded potato cakes accompanied by chive-flecked sour cream, is always a good idea. Dinnertime eats are equally hearty and satisfying, as in a short rib with polenta and grilled leeks.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
5053;Song (by Kin Kao);Canada;Vancouver;317 E. Broadway, Vancouver, V5T 1W5, Canada;49.2628861;-123.0985348;23;false;false;Thai, Regional Cuisine;You're in for a real treat at Song (by Kin Kao), where diners come for a distinctive take on Thai dishes that aren't replicated anywhere else (well, except at their other outpost). Kin Kao Song's fare is driven by a creative spirit and the region's bounty. The lemongrass wings are a special surprise. These bite-sized beauties are deep fried and tossed in a fragrant lemongrass coating for a flavorful punch that delights. Pad Thai may seem like an obligatory order, but this savory version vies for best in class. Then, northern Thai laab with tender, rich pork is given a lift with tart fish sauce and lime broth along with crisp vegetables. Finally, mango sticky rice has that wonderful sticky-sweet appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
5054;Magari by Oca;Canada;Vancouver;1260 Commercial Dr., Vancouver, V5L 2T6, Canada;49.2734255;-123.0692656;68;false;true;Contemporary, Italian;Although there may be a number of Italian-leaning restaurants and pizza spots scattered around Vancouver, this simple pastificio invites diners to pull up a chair and savor authentic, well-prepared dishes. They have bistro charm down pat, with black-and-white tiled flooring, a chalkboard emblazoned with the daily specials and a window onto an open kitchen. Consider the specials, then peek into the pasta rolling station and watch as your meal is made. The kitchen's singular devotion to the craft of pasta-making is evident in dishes of studied simplicity, like a single spiraled raviolo with a creamy filling of ricotta, mascarpone, and green garlic with sage butter sauce. The facciamo noi tasting option allows diners to sample an assortment of off-menu pastas.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5055;Chupito;Canada;Vancouver;322 W. Hastings St., Vancouver, V6B 1K6, Canada;49.2828369;-123.1108974;25;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;The beach may be missing at this fully covered outdoor taqueria (currently open seasonally) where pebbles crunch underfoot and a shipping container subs in for a bar, but the flavors transport guests to Mexico just the same.Come for a cocktail and the aguachile, but stay for the other winning dishes like a red pozole bobbing with carnitas and plump hominy. Carne en sugo, or flank steak with tomatillo and jalapeño pepper folded with braised beans and bacon, will have you scooping up every last bite. Order a postre even if you're full—you'll want to linger no matter the time of year.;Terrace;[]
5057;Little Bird Dim Sum + Craft Beer;Canada;Vancouver;2958 W. 4th Ave., Vancouver, V6K 1R4, Canada;49.2683634;-123.1718186;75;false;true;Chinese, Cantonese;Longtime local restaurateur Jonathan Lee's vision of pairing classic dim sum with local B.C. craft beer was the impetus behind Little Bird, and trendy Kitsilano is the ideal home for this hip lair. Inside, it's contemporary cool—the floors, tables and walls are created in part from recycled chopsticks. It's a classic lineup of dim sum favorites. Sticky rice studded with savory pork and chicken and sweet goji berries is a must-order. Of course, there must be dumplings, and Little Bird's run the gamut from traditional (ha gow) to surprising, with sweet corn, cilantro and shrimp. Supremely fresh, savory and served steaming hot, these dumplings are the definition of comfort food.  As promised, beer is king here.;Air conditioning;[]
5058;Vij's;Canada;Vancouver;3106 Cambie St., Vancouver, V5Z 2W2, Canada;49.2577227;-123.1148958;81;true;true;Indian, Regional Cuisine;When it opened back in 1994, this local staple was at the vanguard of Indian fine dining in North America, and it continues to make a compelling case for the gastronomic riches of the subcontinent. Namesake chef and owner Vikram Vij hasn’t slowed in spreading the good word, still maintaining a daily presence in the dining room, where he stops at tables to check that every guest is happy. He has little cause for worry, in light of the culinary treasure trove on offer: consider a signature dish of wine-marinated “lamb popsicles,” with a fragrant fenugreek sauce or opt for one of the vegetarian dishes, like a curry made with red bell pepper, portobello mushroom and paneer. A list of unique cocktails offers a perfect foil for the well-spiced cuisine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5059;Lunch Lady;Canada;Vancouver;1046 Commercial Dr., Vancouver, V5L 3W9, Canada;49.2749006;-123.069469;31;true;false;Vietnamese, Regional Cuisine;Much like a grandmother who has prepared a feast for her family, Chef Nguyen Thi Thanh exudes a warm, loving presence as she looks over her bustling dining room. She is a long way from Saigon, where she ran a successful food stall, and with her she has brought her charismatic cooking to East Vancouver. The menu is endlessly enticing and inspires immediate decision paralysis. One could fill up fast on starters like fried black tiger prawns with fish sauce or beef carpaccio buried under a blanket of fresh herbs, pickled onions and lime vinaigrette. Garlic fried noodles are another big hit, but then will you still have room for the wagyu beef noodle soup? At the meal’s end, admirers are quick to approach and thank her like the local celebrity she is.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5060;Berkeley North;Canada;Hamilton;31 King William St., Hamilton, L8R 1A1, Canada;43.257313;-79.8676381;15;false;false;Contemporary;In downtown Hamilton, this restaurant has carved out its place as one of the city’s most popular destinations. Exposed red brick, dangling greenery, and a garage door that opens to the patio make for a come-as-you-are atmosphere. The menu is nicely curated, with cooking that takes its cues from across the globe. Think tuna crudo with citrus ponzu or a riff on Chinese egg rolls that features chickpea potato curry and a ginger-herb dip. Larger plates lean into comfort cooking, like steak frites or pasta. Go for the Cornish hen, which arrives perfectly roasted, glazed in rhubarb barbecue sauce, and paired with a mustardy potato salad. No visit is complete without the Basque cheesecake, a wedge that manages to be decadent, creamy, and light all at once.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5061;Bar Raval;Canada;Toronto;505 College St., Toronto, M6G 1A5, Canada;43.6559669;-79.4100717;91;true;true;Spanish;Are we in San Sebastian or Toronto? Open day and night since 2015, Grant van Gameren’s ode to Spain continues to be just the kind of place to get lost in and lose track of time. The cozy room is a vision, a stunning cocoon of curved, South African mahogany that wraps around every surface. The menu is equally small but offers a striking roster of conservas and pinxtos. Briny boquerones laid over stracciatella are a must, as are the plucky shrimp a la planxa coated in a riot of smoked paprika, cumin and garlic. Indeed, guests will graze and graze until they’ve run out of things to order. There’s plenty to drink here, too, with a host of talented bartenders ready to mix and pour sherries, highballs and smart cocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
5062;Favorites Thai;Canada;Toronto;141 Ossington Ave., Toronto, M6J 2Z6, Canada;43.6473435;-79.4198947;53;true;false;Thai;This vibrant Thai hot spot hides in plain sight along Ossington Avenue. A quick walk through a tiny coffee shop to the very back leads to the actual dining room, anchored by a small kitchen fitted with binchotan charcoal grills. Sunlight bathes the airy, narrow dining room. All the while, guests dig into electric, vibrant Thai cooking that makes the most out of fresh herbs and fiery chilis. You could fill up just on appetizers, like sticky rice spring rolls, fried chicken wings and beef tenderloin tartare enlivened with fish sauce and fried shallots. A particularly clever fried calamari salad demonstrates the creative talents of this kitchen. From green curries with fish to red curries with duck, the curated menu offers wide appeal for groups.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5063;Enoteca Sociale;Canada;Toronto;1288 Dundas St. W., Toronto, M6J 1X7, Canada;43.6495441;-79.4257;47;false;false;Italian, Roman;A home away from home, this venerable Roman favorite recently celebrated its 10-year anniversary with a quick renovation that has paid off handsomely. The restaurant is as inviting as they come, radiating comfort and anchored by a marble bar that welcomes solo diners like long- lost friends. From bread to charcuterie, practically everything is made in-house here, down to the fantastic pastas that make up the very heart of this menu. There isn’t a table in sight that hasn’t ordered either the signature cacio e pepe or the bucatini all’Amatriciana. Comforting starters like golden-fried arancini stuffed with mozzarella di bufula or clever riffs like caprese sformato reflect the many talents of this capable kitchen, which also offers a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5064;Sunnys Chinese;Canada;Toronto;60 Kensington Ave., Toronto, M5T 2K1, Canada;43.6543859;-79.4007706;85;true;true;Chinese;In the belly of Kensington Market, down a hallway that nearly looks like a dead-end, you will find the door to this high-energy hotspot. There’s no turning back, as the packed-out room is constantly buzzing with groups huddled around Chinese homestyle dishes pulled from Sichuan to Guangdong. Spicy, fiery, crispy, smoky – the high-wattage cooking is a total delight, as the kitchen pulls no punches at every possible junction. Tripe and beef shank coated in chili oil is a good start before launching into the charred silver needle noodles. Best of all might be the grilled chicken thigh coated in cumin, chili and pepper. To finish, the crispy Hong Kong French Toast with black sesame jam and oolong condensed milk short-circuits all manner of restraint.;Air conditioning;[]
5065;SumiLicious Smoked Meat & Deli;Canada;Toronto;5631 Steeles Ave., #5, Toronto, M1V 5P6, Canada;43.83251;-79.26732;25;true;false;Deli;In a non-descript Scarborough shopping center, Sumith Fernando’s smoked meat is something of a rite of passage. Fernando spent nearly two decades learning his craft at Schwartz's in Montreal before settling on his own recipe. His halal brisket is marinated in a secret spice blend for days, smoked for hours until tender and finally finished in a steamer. He opened in 2018 and has been behind the counter ever since, building sandwiches out of thinly sliced, peppery brisket piled high on soft, spongy rye smeared with yellow mustard. Against the advice of any physician, complete your order at this no-frills deli with poutine—fries topped with Quebec cheese curds and submerged in gravy. Ask for extra napkins, you'll need them.;Air conditioning;[]
5066;Grey Gardens;Canada;Toronto;199 Augusta Ave., Toronto, M5T 2L4, Canada;43.6538018;-79.4016321;26;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;Everyone is drawn to restaurateur Jen Agg's hip, boisterous venue, which manages both style and substance with confident charm. An excellent wine list is paired with a small, mercurial menu that punches above its weight class, where ostensibly simple, unassuming dishes turn out to be heavy hitters. Raw items like oysters and crudos are commendably fresh, and the house-made pastas are real showstoppers. Take as an example hearty spaghetti twirled with a mackerel-based twist on XO sauce, lifted with fermented chili puree and crunchy potato crumbs: beguilingly complex, indulgent and umami-packed. The menu might only offer a duo of desserts, but they’re just as inspired as the rest—in other words, not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
5067;Guru Lukshmi;Canada;Mississauga;7070 St. Barbara Blvd., Mississauga, L5W 0E6, Canada;43.6375874;-79.7168949;32;true;false;Indian, South Indian;It’s a good thing this South Indian restaurant takes up multiple bays in a sprawling Mississauga shopping center. If the dining room were any smaller, the wait to get in would be endless. Reservations are recommended for this landmark that is the undisputed champion of dosas, offered in dazzling variety like nowhere else in the region. The signature Mysore Bhaji Dosa packed with fantastic aloo masala is a good place to start for first timers, who will question whether they can finish the whole thing before doing just that. But there’s more: Idlys, vadas, and uttapam are made fresh, served hot, and come with warm sambar and refreshing chutneys. All of this food comes and goes in a rapid blur, and return visits are planned before you’re out the door.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5068;White Lily Diner;Canada;Toronto;678 Queen St. E., Toronto, M4M 1G8, Canada;43.6586734;-79.351165;82;false;false;Creative, Bakery;Old school diners are rare creatures these days, but ones that smoke their own bacon, make their own biscuits and donuts, bottle their own hot sauce and grow their own vegetables? Even rarer. A culinary unicorn, this bright yellow nook sets the standard not just for diners but for any restaurant that aspires to serve both people and planet. While also partnering with local farms, husband-and-wife team Ben Denham and Ashley Lloyd live on their 10-acre farm in Uxbridge, which supplies a handful of restaurants and a CSA. Breakfast is the main draw, but guests will be happy at any hour of the day. Verdant green salads, fantastic sandwiches on homemade bread, and a stunningly light hash brown make for a grand meal that gets all the details just right.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
5069;Chica's Chicken;Canada;Toronto;2853 Dundas St. W., Toronto, M6P 1Y6, Canada;43.6653507;-79.4644635;36;true;false;American;This humble corner in the Junction is a faithful tribute to "hot chicken," a fiery, eye-watering style popularized in the American South. Chickens are dry-brined for two days and seasoned with a dark, brooding mix of spices. Diners in a hurry can grab a boneless sandwich and be on their way, but true fans know that excellence takes time and are content to wait the full half hour as bone-in birds are fried to order. Medium heat is an approachable entry into this genre, but daredevils can swing for spicier tiers turbocharged with ghost peppers. An order of deep-fried pickles won’t win you any points with your doctor, but they’re a solid starter while you wait in the bare dining room that booms with rap music.;Air conditioning;[]
5070;La Bartola;Canada;Toronto;588 College St., Toronto, M6G 1B3, Canada;43.6553245;-79.413589;23;true;true;Mexican, Vegan;Chef/owner Ivan Castro developed a passion for cooking at the heels of his mother and grandmother, and he shares the vibrant spirit and bold flavor of his native Mexico City at La Bartola. Bright colors and vivid artwork echo the upbeat mood here, but this isn't your typical taqueria. Instead, traditional and authentic Mexican dishes offer a surprise—they're completely meat-free. Black sesame tostadas with salsa macha negra and sikil pak are a perfect opener. Tacos made from purple corn are eye-catching, while braised hibiscus is a delicious substitute for the typical meat. Quesadillas are filled with a mix of softened roasted potatoes, refried beans, vegetarian cheese and crisped onions. Wash it all down with a mezcal, Mexican beer or tequila.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5071;Wynona;Canada;Toronto;819 Gerrard St. E., Toronto, M4M 1Y8, Canada;43.6671374;-79.3447567;63;false;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Wynona is a lively and friendly neighborhood bistro. The open kitchen is the heartbeat of the place—snag a seat at one of the tables to watch the chefs at work. The young team is relaxed but efficient, and all guests are well looked after, with staff members happily recommending dishes or wines.Seasonality drives their selections, and the menu changes weekly. Clear Italian influences are evident across the menu. Case in point? Thin slices of capocollo ham, topped with pickled banana peppers and drizzled with sweet local honey is certainly a Med-minded opener, and a delicious one at that. You'll never go wrong with homemade pasta, perhaps lumache with sausage crumble, sugar snap peas and a dollop of creamy cheese.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5073;Puerto Bravo;Canada;Toronto;1425 Gerrard St. E., Toronto, M4L 1Z7, Canada;43.6721175;-79.3224687;74;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Puerto Bravo is a quaint little spot on a busy street. The menu is also compact, leaning heavily on seafood while spotlighting regional cooking from Tampico on the Gulf of Mexico. Their itty bitty kitchen is the little engine that could, doling out bold flavors and phenomenal bites made with quality ingredients and executed with care. Salsa macha is made in-house. One dish worth ordering is the wera tostada, a riot of colors and textures. The crispy corn tostada is layered with mashed avocado and thin slices of octopus and shrimp tossed in a spicy macha mayo for a vibrant meal. Finish with something sweet, perhaps the classic carlota. Made with soft Marie biscuits layered with lime, condensed milk and cream cheese, it's a refreshing finale.;Air conditioning;[]
5074;Tiflisi;Canada;Toronto;1970 Queen St. E., Toronto, M4L 1H8, Canada;43.6697833;-79.3015811;80;true;true;Central Asian;East of downtown Toronto in Beaches, the Pkhakadze family delivers some of the city’s best and brightest Georgian cooking. Portions are built to share so bring a friend or two. The cold leek pkhali salad bound in a light walnut sauce is a vibrantly green beginning and especially essential before the Acharuli khachapuri arrives. A celebration of carbs and dairy, this stretch of fluffy bread cradles a pool of melted cheese topped with butter and an egg yolk. There’s more on the way: Large lamb khinkali with warm broth and long skewers of juicy kebabs topped with fried potatoes. Without question, this is hearty food, seasoned beautifully, prepared with care and radiating with all the comforts of home, wherever that may be.;Air conditioning;[]
5075;Alma;Canada;Toronto;1194 Bloor St. W., Toronto, M6H 1N2, Canada;43.6593617;-79.4380115;74;false;false;Asian;Chef Anna Chen dazzles in Bloordale Village from this minimally adorned shoebox of a restaurant. Scallion bread with stracciatella cheese and eggplant dip. Parmesan tapioca fritters. Is this Chinese or fusion? Red lanterns dangling from the ceiling and a ceramic lucky cat waving from the corner hint at the menu's intentions but the chef needn’t be bothered with labels.The menu is at once comforting and imaginative. Start with pan-fried radish cakes dotted with an assertive garlic-chive paste. A wide bowl of addictively chewy noodles with pork wontons is pure comfort. An unlisted rhubarb trifle with coconut makes for a lovingly sweet send-off. All the while, servers roam about pouring natural wines with abandon.;Air conditioning;[]
5076;BB's;Canada;Toronto;5 Brock Ave., Toronto, M6K 2K6, Canada;43.6420034;-79.432464;91;false;true;Filipino;Start your morning or fire up your evening at this groovy Filipino diner bursting with color and coolness. Sea foam green tile, pink booths and turquoise stools set the stage for a hangout that doesn’t take itself too seriously. Brunch is a treat, featuring Adobo fried chicken paired with pineapple habanero hot sauce. The wonderfully sour braised pork loin soup will ward off the longest nights and the coldest winters. Dinner is a different speed. The cocktail bar comes alive, and the kitchen trades in Japanese milkbread French Toast for classic pancit with chili oil, chicken liver mousse and calamansi pie with orange blossom meringue. With a come-as-you-are vibe, this charming restaurant is a welcome winner in Parkdale.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
5077;The Ace;Canada;Toronto;231A Roncesvalles Ave., Toronto, M5R 2L6, Canada;43.6460751;-79.4488027;37;false;false;Gastropub;Set your alarm. This is cooking worth waking up for. Indeed, brunch usually isn’t a kitchen’s brightest moment, but that is far from true at The Ace, a slim vintage diner that first opened in the 1950s. Husband-and-wife team Rafael Badell and Maggie Stackpole are the latest to hold the keys to this historic haunt, and it’s during the day when the cooking really sings. What’s that smell? It’s probably expert wedges of house-made sourdough sizzling away on the griddle. Start with the duck confit and wild mushroom toast crowned with softly poached eggs. Whatever you do, save room for, what is likely, the city’s best French toast. A triumphant square of brioche arrives topped with caramelized pears, vanilla bean whipped ricotta and toasted pistachios.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
5079;Indian Street Food Company;Canada;Toronto;1701 Bayview Ave., Toronto, M4G 3C1, Canada;43.7079405;-79.3758149;88;true;false;Indian;Found in Leaside along a packed row of shops on Bayview Avenue, this neighborhood stalwart delivers a tight menu of street food favorites and regional curries from various corners of India. The dining room is wrapped in reclaimed wood panels and colorful murals, and cushy tables with white cloth invite further lingering. Over-ordering is easy, but friendly servers are quick to offer guidance. Deep-fried cauliflower finished in a sweet chili glaze is a kitchen specialty, but savory chaats, arriving lashed in refreshing chutneys, are worth an order. Order the thalis to see the breadth of this kitchen’s talent in one large, oversized platter featuring delicately spiced lamb curry, rich dhal makhani and a superb south Indian vegetable curry.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5080;Conejo Negro;Canada;Toronto;838 College St., Toronto, M6H 1A2, Canada;43.65443;-79.4228903;59;false;false;Caribbean, Latin American;When the menu packs in Creole, Caribbean, and Latin influences, you can be sure that nothing will want for flavor. That’s especially true at this cozy nook on busy College Street, where three friends have joined forces to open this “black rabbit.” Delicately fried and warmly spiced firecracker shrimp is a fiery way to start the meal. The hits keep coming with fried chicken with smoked hot honey, tender braised beef with cheddar grits, and collards with ham hocks. Generously portioned, the food is designed for sharing. Better yet, assemble a crew and ask about the breezy backyard patio that is surely the seat of the summer. Wood planks and benches, warm lighting, and greenery all over make for a convivial atmosphere that invites lounging.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5081;Campechano;Canada;Toronto;504 Adelaide St., Toronto, M5V 1T4, Canada;43.6457658;-79.4006692;22;true;true;Mexican;If you’re here for anything but tacos, you’ve come to the wrong place. Time flies at this cozy hotspot that sources heirloom corn from Mexico and presses and griddles tortillas every day. The menu is short and sweet, but still, how does one pick between the smoky barbacoa with jalapeño salsa and the flaky, beer-battered haddock with red cabbage? Sautéed mushrooms with double-smoked bacon and chili oil are a sleeper favorite too. The sounds and smells of the kitchen fill the boxy room that’s little more than white kitchen tile and worn wood. Everything arrives fast and hot, and then, in a blink, it’s all over and you’re back outside, plotting your inevitable return. A second location on College Street offers a similar menu in a more spacious setting.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5082;R&D;Canada;Toronto;241 Spadina Ave., Toronto, M5T 2E2, Canada;43.6515356;-79.3972932;28;true;true;Fusion, Chinese;In a match made on primetime, Chef Alvin Leung was one of the judges who declared Eric Chong the winner of "MasterChef Canada’s" first season, before taking on the younger chef as his protégé. Smack dab in the middle of Chinatown, this hip, unconventional eatery is the product of their partnership, serving up just the sort of freewheeling fusion cuisine that made Chong a TV hit. The assortment of decidedly untraditional dim sum serves as a prime example, drawing upon a grab bag of international flavors, including French, Chinese and Korean, as in flaky sou filled with foie gras parfait, or bao filled with kimchi and galbi. Mains are similarly genre-defying, like a signature butter-poached lobster with scallion oil, dashi and vermicelli.;;[]
5083;MAKfam;USA;Denver;39 W. 1st Ave., Denver, 80223, USA;39.7184249;-104.9882371;88;true;true;Chinese;What began as a pop-up back in NYC, where owners and married couple Doris Yuen and Kenneth Wan first met, and then became a stall in a Denver food hall, is now at last a full-service restaurant. The winsome, colorful space and the compact menu both celebrate the pair's Chinese American roots, both having been raised by immigrant families who worked in restaurants. Fried crab and cheese wontons and hand-shaped chicken and chive potstickers are inspired by Chinatown favorites and takeout staples, made with particular care and big flavor. Chicken wings with a spicy, tingly málà seasoning are favorites with good reason, and larger dishes, like the familiar-yet-inventive corned beef fried rice or spicy garlic butter rice cakes, impress as well.;;[]
5084;Basta;USA;Boulder;3601 Arapahoe Ave., Boulder, 80303, USA;40.0150952;-105.2477386;31;false;true;Contemporary;Concrete floors, cream walls and an open kitchen with a wood-burning oven set an industrial-chic tone at Basta. Snag a spot at the bar and you'll have a front row seat to the culinary action, where family-style, contemporary Italian-American cooking is the name of the game. Start things off right with a shareable starter like burrata or the silky chicken liver mousse with peach mostarda that is sided by crusty bread from next-door sister bakery, Dry Storage. Definitely don't skip the smoked dark green olives—they're an unexpected delight. From there, entrees are satisfying, especially the half chicken. End on a sweet note with a plate of five beignet-style doughnuts dusted with powdered sugar and a dulce de leche Chantilly cream.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5085;Glo Noodle House;USA;Denver;4450 W. 38th Ave., Denver, 80212, USA;39.7692729;-105.044811;52;true;false;Ramen;The location in a run of the mill strip mall belies the cool interior at this spot named for Chef/owner Chris Teigland's mother. Inside, dark charcoal and dark wood are offset by pops of bright colors, while overhead, vibrant lanterns of different colors and sizes draw attention.  The kitchen delivers serious flavor on their noodle/ramen-based menu. Kick off with a sweet and savory skewer of marinated tofu skewer served with a miso peach jam and an almond and sesame candy crumble. Ramen options run the gamut from miso bacon and brothless versions to the death wish designed for spice hounds who want the heat without sacrificing flavor. Sweets worth saving room for include the sweet crispy rice cake with smoked caramel and kasu-lime ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5086;La Diabla Pozole y Mezcal;USA;Denver;2233 Larimer St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7551817;-104.9898073;21;false;false;Mexican;This Larimer Street spot from chef Jose Avila is no fuss and no frills but all heart. Inside, it's equal parts cozy and colorful with dark, unpolished wood floors and vibrant walls. In case the name didn't give it away, pozole is the star of the show. They feature the typical rojo and verde broths as well as white, black (with a smoky char from roasted chilies) and vegetarian—eschewing pork for mushroom and chayote. It's an impressive take on a Mexican staple. Customize the protein and opt for the tender and flavorful pork, and order a mezcal from their extensive selection. Should pozole not call your name, there are tacos and pambazos on offer, and on weekends, mornings are met with chilaquiles and a concha French toast that's worth an early wake-up call.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5087;The Ginger Pig;USA;Denver;4262 Lowell Blvd., Denver, 80211, USA;39.77611;-105.03426;100;true;false;Chinese, Asian;The story here begins with Chef Natascha Hess's time as an exchange student in Beijing, where her host family taught her the fundamentals of Chinese home cooking, lessons that sparked a full-bore culinary passion. After several trips back to China, her travels broadened to include Shanghai, Singapore, Bangkok and more—a catalogue of flavors that she then translated into a hugely popular food truck, eventually becoming this lively, rustic brick-and-mortar location (though the truck can still be seen parked in front). It's clear that Chef Hess’s time abroad was well-spent: from hearty boiled pork and cabbage dumplings dressed with chili oil to stir-fried cabbage with Thai chili jam, the cooking bursts with flavor, including a healthy dose of heat.;;[]
5088;Tavernetta;USA;Denver;1889 16th St. Mall, Denver, 80202, USA;39.7531102;-105.0023246;96;false;false;Italian, Contemporary;Tavernetta is an absolute stunner. Every detail has been considered and designed to encourage lingering and relaxing in this unique and beautiful space. The Italian menu nods to more well-known dishes from multiple regions, and the plates are refreshingly uncluttered. The classics are prepared with obvious care, as in a crostini primavera with a sourdough base layered with creamy stracciatella, heritage English peas and lovely spring greens. Crisp and fresh, it's simple but spot on. Spaghetti all'amatriciana is loaded with guanciale, tomato and pecorino romano for a wonderfully savory dish. To finish, tiramisu is a classic for a reason.Come at lunch for a delicious two-course deal, then spring for a dessert.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5089;Ash'Kara;USA;Denver;2005 W. 33rd Ave., Denver, 80211, USA;39.76337;-105.01154;27;false;false;Israeli, Mediterranean Cuisine;At this brightly hospitable neighborhood spot, Chef Reggie Dotson offers up an exploration of contemporary Israeli cuisine, pulling in influences from the Mediterranean, North Africa and Middle East. The menu leads with mezze, featuring top-notch versions of familiar staples like hummus, babaganoush and falafel, paired with excellent wood-fired whole-grain pita made from heritage wheat. Dinner offers more substantial fare, as in savory tagines with eggplant or lamb tenderloin. The cooking is vegetable-forward, and takes pains to accommodate all dietary restrictions (there's even a gluten-free pita option), but there are no gimmicks here, just thoughtful, full-flavored dishes made with high quality ingredients and a bit of extra style.;;[]
5090;Hop Alley;USA;Denver;3500 Larimer St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7669634;-104.9744116;87;true;true;Chinese, Contemporary;Hop Alley refers to the original name for Denver's Chinatown, but there's nothing historic about this sleek restaurant. In keeping with the contemporary look, the Chinese menu with Sichuan leanings features modern adaptations of classics. There's plenty of originality and bold flavors, as seen in dishes like gai lan, a dynamic plate of grilled Chinese broccoli with schmaltz and oyster sauce finished with house-made duck salt and crispy shallots. Shrimp toast topped with whipped shrimp and chicken thigh is far from standard thanks to mustard gastrique and tiger vinaigrette. Dan dan mian noodles are set with ground pork in a Szechuan peppercorn broth that brings the heat.Cocktails, like the bees knees with chili-infused honey, also riff on the classics.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5091;Mister Oso;USA;Denver;3163 Larimer St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7641433;-104.9782822;54;true;false;Latin American;It's laid-back and lively at Mister Oso, a small but stylish spot with a creative menu and clever cooking. Chef/owner Blake Edmunds has a hit on his hands, with a second location opening in recent years. While tacos may be the main event, this isn't your typical taqueria menu. Instead, discover ceviches, salads and dishes bearing Latin American and international influences. Everything is served family style. Pick up a tortilla and start building a delicious treat, as in the mojo tacos with coconut-braised pork shoulder finished with a mojo salsa and pickled red onion served with crispy fried plantains. Coconut rice, served in a piping hot cast iron dish, bridges sweet and savory thanks to pickled shaved peppers and thin, shaved red onion.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5092;Chen Mapo Tofu (Qinghua Road);China Mainland;Chengdu;No.10-12, 10 Qinghua Road, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.665432;104.030406;84;false;false;Sichuan;Mapo tofu is a world-famous Sichuanese classic dating back to the Qing Dynasty. Word has it that this century-old shop is the true original source of this numbing, spicy dish, invented by Lady Chen. Silky tofu, ground beef and spices are cooked in a stone pot that stays hot for a long time, perfect with a bowl of steamed rice. Zhong dumplings and lotus leaf-wrapped steamed pork in spiced rice flour are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5093;Lao Chengdu San Yang Mian;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 6-8, 46 Guojielou Street, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.672154;104.05607;23;true;true;Noodles;This ‘hole in the wall’ may lack bells and whistles, but it’s popular with locals. Soup and tossed noodles are divided into 3 trifectas, namely the ‘old’, ‘new’ and ‘more’. Blanched noodles tossed in spicy meat sauce with diced string beans in the ‘old’ category is the most popular item. Feel free to order wontons with chopped chillies on the side. And nothing cools your mouth better than a bowl of tofu dessert with red bean soup.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5094;Wan San Mian Guan (Jinjiang);China Mainland;Chengdu;No.1, 131 Qinglongzheng Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6476287;104.0869098;33;false;false;Noodles;The owner hails from Yibin County, Sichuan. He opened this shop to serve authentic Yibin-style Ranmian noodles tossed in a chilli paste with ground peanuts, scallion, bean sprouts and sesames. For toppings, choose between the aromatic chilli ground beef or the hearty braised ginger duck. Those who prefer their noodles more toothsome may opt for the thick ribbon variety. On top of that, dried meats and sausages are also offered at dinner.;Cash only;[]
5095;Wu Ji Guai Wei Mian (Jinjiang);China Mainland;Chengdu;108-11, Section 5, Yi Huan East Road, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6667;104.0667;20;false;true;Noodles;In 1989, the founder started his first noodle shop just down the road. After several moves, he is back in his old neighbourhood once again. In his 70s, he still makes his own pork sauce like the old days, although the shop is now run by his son. His signature ‘weird taste’ noodles are dressed in a shiitake pork sauce that is mildly hot, sweet and numbing. Beef noodles in a spicy bean sauce include diced bamboo shoots for a lovely crunch.;Cash only;[]
5097;Yangboying Za Jiang Mian;China Mainland;Chengdu;19-13 Tongsi Road, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6718986;104.0755866;75;true;false;Noodles;The owner-chef who used to work in a famous restaurant uses traditional techniques to make noodle soups and assorted toppings, each boasting a substantially different taste profile. Noodles dressed in meat sauce with sesame paste, red chilli oil and Sichuan pepper is a regional classic exuding intoxicating aromas. Those who prefer less heat may opt for dumplings in seafood soup that cooked with dried shrimp, cuttlefish and scallops.;Cash only;[]
5098;Ting Yuan 399 (Jinjiang);China Mainland;Chengdu;399 Jingjusi, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.623461;104.104228;99;true;true;Sichuan;While some guests may sip tea and play mahjong in the peaceful Chinese garden by a busy road, discerning food lovers flock here for the river fish dishes. Plump swamp eels from inland rivers are poached in a flavourful spiced broth and drizzled with sizzling hot oil at the table, making their flesh tender and juicy, but with a crispy chew. Stir-fried pork liver and kidney with bird’s eye chilli and pickled chilli is another firm favourite.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5099;Nian Feng Restaurant;China Mainland;Chengdu;56-3 Nianfeng Alley, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.647308;104.0897506;32;false;true;Sichuan;Nestled in the old town, the old-meets-new interior pays tribute to the neighbourhood’s past with a touch of modern Chinese chic. It champions a sophisticated take on home-style Sichuan cooking. Their signature dry-braised beef tendon with green chillies boasts finely diced pork belly and king oyster mushrooms in the sauce for extra depth and texture. Sliced pig kidney dressed in red oil seduces with nutty depth, crisp texture and rich flavours.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5100;Gan Ji Fei Chang Fen (Jinniu);China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 1-3, 18 Ma'an North Road, Jinniu, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6793397;104.0843466;39;true;false;Noodles;With over 30 years of history, this tiny gem is no secret to locals in search of a bowl of hearty glass noodle soup with braised pork intestines. The toothsome, springy noodles are made in-house. Choose between mala spicy soup and rich white broth. Optionally, order intestine knots on top for an extra layer of texture. And don't miss the piping hot guokui – crispy flatbread with pork and Sichuan pepper filling.;Cash only;[]
5101;Hu Er Ge Yao Shan Ti Hua;China Mainland;Chengdu;146-19, Section 1, Yi Huan West Road, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6563019;104.0382948;64;false;false;Sichuan;The simple shop has little ambiance to speak of, but that hasn't put hungry locals off from flocking here since 1999. In fact, it's the favourite late-night spot for many who come for its famous pork trotter soup – simmered with Chinese herbs for eight hours until the connective tissues are gelatinous and the soup is loaded with collagen. Stir-fries such as spicy chitterlings, and green chilli pig snout fried rice are also brimming with wok hei.;Cash only;[]
5102;Rongrong Beida Pugaimian;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 2-4, Section 2, Jiefang Road, Jinniu, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6792572;104.0766859;40;true;true;Noodles;Famous for flat noodle soup, this brand always attracts a long queue at the door. Diners can see the four chefs pulling a piece of dough to make the signature noodles – thin, soft, but with a lovely chew. There are two sizes and a few toppings to choose from, all boasting spot-on seasoning of the perfect amount of heat punctuated by a mild sweetness. Be prepared to share a table with strangers at peak hours.;Cash only;[]
5103;Zhuan Zhuan Hui (Lianhua South Road);China Mainland;Chengdu;27 Lianhua South Road, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.638324;104.094566;48;false;true;Sichuan;Despite its hard-to-find entrance, this flagship of the chain has earned solid fandom among locals with its no-frills, home-style Sichuanese cooking that is frugally priced. Instead of an eye-watering kick, expect a mild heat that caters to a broader palate. Specialities from the Leshan area, like tofu pudding and marinated fatty pork intestine, are best sellers. The latter is slow cooked in spiced soy before being sautéed with garlic and celtuce.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5104;Shudidanggui (Wuhou);China Mainland;Chengdu;34-25 Shiwuzhong Street, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6450254;104.0742463;28;false;true;Sichuan;Named after two Chinese herbs, the concept of a therapeutic diet is at the core of this establishment. Diners are greeted by an herbal tea sweetened with stevia, and the menu is built around Chinese medicines. The signature beef noodle soup is infused with dang gui, believed to improve blood circulation, making it a lunch time favourite for many. Yellow croaker with galangal and patchouli is also popular. Some dishes require pre-ordering.;Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5105;Dumpling & Drinks (Lanchao Road);China Mainland;Chengdu;16 Lanchao Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.630182;104.050942;52;false;true;Dumplings;It doesn't take a rocket scientist to figure out the eponymous specialities of the house. Dumplings are freshly made daily in the open kitchen and varieties are served each day, each to be ordered in units of 5. Those filled with pork and mushrooms, or beef and Chinese celery are the highlights. Nestled in a quiet neighbourhood, the cosy room features a clean and modern décor with a light wood and dark green colour scheme.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5106;Organization South;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 209, Block 1, Pebble Walk, 669 Wanxiang South Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.589246;104.047258;55;true;true;Sichuan;The playful, vintage décor with fake tree trunks and red lanterns is aptly matched by a menu disguised as a martial arts instruction book. In addition to famous Sichuanese wok-fried dishes such as green chilli ‘ruthless’ chicken and braised swamp eel, we also recommend the daily specials up on the whiteboard. Seasonal offerings like bitter bamboo shoot and milk cap mushroom are worth a try. Inevitably packed to the seams, book ahead and arrive early.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5107;Yao Guai Mian;China Mainland;Chengdu;49 Longzhou East Alley, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6278248;104.0944178;88;true;false;Noodles;Tucked away in a longstanding residential area, this noodle shop has a loyal following. The noodles are either served in spicy or white broth, or tossed in various seasoning pastes. For noodle soup, try their signature eight-treasure white broth made with chicken, bamboo shoots and dried seafood including shrimps, squids and oysters. Or have your bouncy noodles tossed in the famous mala chilli pork sauce for heady, addictive aromas.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5109;Yongle Restaurant (Wuhou);China Mainland;Chengdu;36 Xiaojiahe Middle Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6333722;104.0411665;93;false;true;Sichuan;You can't miss this shop – just look for the red lanterns, perforated wood windows… and the queue. Since 1985, it's been serving home-style Sichuanese dishes made the traditional way: stir-frying, steaming and shuizhu. The braised eel with eggplant has contrasting textures and the savvy use of Chinese patchouli elevates it to the next level. For non-spicy food lovers, the sticky rice pork ribs and meatball soup are both great choices.;Cash only;[]
5110;Rong Yuan Can Guan;China Mainland;Chengdu;10-2 Shuhan Street, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6436195;104.0424056;78;false;true;Sichuan;This household name located in the old city has been around since 1999. The second-generation owner and the all-Sichuanese team continue to feed diners authentic home-style Sichuan cooking like in the old days. The signature spicy mandarin fish uses a herbal chilli mix with exceptional heat and depth and the fish is flown in daily from Guangdong. The quick-fried pork tripe tip (limited availability) is uniquely satisfying thanks to its springy texture.;Cash only;[]
5111;Gong Zhou · Ba Shu Wei Yuan;China Mainland;Chengdu;64-6 Junlong Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.656042;104.095839;97;true;true;Sichuan;Gong Zhou was the ancient name of Chongqing, the home municipality of the owner and kitchen team. Since opening in a residential area next to Taikoo-li shopping hub in 1998, it has kept its fans coming back for its Chongqing dishes, such as "auspicious" home-style fish – blanched grass carp dressed in a tangy sauce made with spicy bean sauce, pickled chilli and ginger. Try the pork ribs coated in spiced ground rice, stuffed in pork tripe and steamed.;Cash only;[]
5113;Zhu Ji Zhi Mian Pu;China Mainland;Chengdu;194 Yixinqiao South Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6437137;104.0954124;80;true;true;Noodles;Surrounded by furniture shops, this noodle place has a retro feel to it. Wooden tables and bamboo chairs add to the overall rustic flair. The noodles are made fresh in-house, which explains their incredibly silky, bouncy texture. Zha jiang mian is the must-try here: blanched noodles are topped with a soybean-based ground pork sauce that is robust, savoury and mildly spicy. If you enjoy their noodles, you can buy some raw to take home.;Cash only;[]
5114;Mosnack;China Mainland;Chengdu;Shop L101-1-A, Shimao 52+ Mini Mall, 99 Mengzhuiwan Bystreet, Chenghua, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6729048;104.0910142;93;true;true;Noodles;This simple shop is clean and bright, with a picture frame window looking into the kitchen. The menu has three sections: dumplings, wontons, and noodles, all handmade in-house. The pork and chive dumplings in sour soup stand out in particular – the soup imparts deep flavours of laver, dried shrimp and sesame. Try also the wontons in a flavourful pork bone broth that takes six hours to make. Ask for a table on the terrace on a fine day.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5115;Ajisai;Taiwan;Taichung;102 Zhongxing Street, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1486888;120.6635005;85;false;false;Noodles;Stained glass windows and wooden shelving contrast beautifully against the cement walls of this noodle shop. The owner used to run a private kitchen specialising in Jiangzhe cooking. The menu thus revolves around noodles from Jiangzhe area, along with some Sichuanese options. The side dishes she makes every morning are also a reason to visit – try the bitter melon simmered with rock sugar if available. Open 3 days a week. Check social media before visiting.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5116;Jin Shang Hsuan;Taiwan;Taipei;111, Lane 155, Dunhua North Road, Songshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0541826;121.5525346;58;true;false;Taiwanese;With only 6 tables and a private room, securing a reservation at this little gem can be a challenge. What it lacks in scale, it more than makes up for with the owner-chef’s refined take on Taiwanese cooking, ranging from stir-fried beef with coriander and crispy garlic bits, to three-cup braised chicken. Diners may also choose their own seafood and specify how they want it cooked. The room is bright and airy, the service team amiable.;Air conditioning;[]
5118;No Name Noodles;Taiwan;Taichung;69 Shifu Road, Central District, Taichung, 400, Taiwan;24.13963;120.68006;47;false;true;Noodles;With over 70 years of history, this neighbourhood noodle shop is now run by the third generation of the family. Throughout those decades, regulars have been coming for the preservative-free Shanghainese noodle soup served with pork chop, beef shin or zhajiang sauce. The fried-to-order pork chop goes well with iced sour plum tea and the spicy pickled scallion and garlic. Don’t miss other side dishes such as pickled cucumber and string beans.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5119;Moon Pavilion;Taiwan;Taichung;2F, Miyahara, 20 Zhongshan Road, Central District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1378627;120.6834946;87;true;true;Taiwanese;In a restored century-old eye clinic, Moon Pavilion juxtaposes colourful velvet-covered banquettes with original wrought iron and red bricks for an interesting clash of industrial and Victorian styles. The food pays tribute to the old-time Taiwanese palate, showing delicate balance and shrewd judgment. Condiments from different Taiwanese counties make appearances in the recipes, including Hakkanese kumquat sauce and Taichungese Nalta jute.;Air conditioning;[]
5120;Erge Shih Tang;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;145 Cinghai Road, Gushan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6511882;120.2883164;94;false;false;Taiwanese;The room isn’t particularly spacious, but it does exude a homely feel. Similarly, the menu features Taiwanese home-style cooking, that is lightly seasoned and in smaller portions. The signature grilled Pacific saury in honey sauce is braised until the bones are tender and edible, perfect with a bowl of steamed rice, pork lard rice, or braised pork rice. Or you can opt for steamed taro root cake with shiitake and dried shrimps as starch.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5121;Yeh Jia Calamari Rice Noodle Soup;Taiwan;Tainan;142, Section 2, Guohua Street, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9911454;120.1969878;30;false;false;Small eats;Founded in 1935, this shop claims to be the creator of calamari rice noodle soup. Into the third generation, the owner still insists on making thick rice noodles with brown rice for its fragrance and firm texture. Calamari from Indonesian waters are cooked in a clear broth with intense flavour, a hint of peppery aroma and a sweet aftertaste. The shop is a bit congested, but clean and air-conditioned. Expect to queue for a table on holidays.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5122;Cianjin Braised Pork Rice;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;26 Datong Street 2nd Street, Cianjin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6272171;120.2954397;23;false;false;Small eats;This third-generation family business dates back to 1959 and its signature braised pork rice has been the favourite breakfast for generations of Kaohsiungese. Only the back cut is used, with pork skin and a layer of fat that give the dish a complex depth. Feel free to order shredded pork, dried fish floss, marinated tofu, or even a soft-boiled duck egg to go with the rice. It’s always busy and may close early when all food has sold out.;Cash only;[]
5123;Good Friend Cold Noodles;Taiwan;Taipei;Shilin Night Market, 31 Danan Road, Shilin District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0891725;121.525463;56;false;true;Street Food;Noodles dressed in sesame sauce impart a hint of lemony fragrance, a perfect match for egg drop miso soup.;Cash only;[]
5124;Unnamed Clay Oven Roll;Taiwan;Taipei;Nanjichang Night Market, Stall 74, Lane 311, Section 2, Zhonghua Road, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0284359;121.5067445;56;true;true;Street Food;This push cart near the end of the market always attracts a queue. Try their sweet pastry and long shaobing.;Cash only;[]
5125;Chun Lan Gua Bao;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;5 Fusing 1st Road, Sinsing District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6279509;120.3076787;36;true;false;Small eats;Since 2000, this shop has been famous for its oversize steamed bun sandwiches packed with tasty fillings. The must-try is definitely the assorted gua bao stuffed with crisp pickled cabbage, half-fatty soy-braised pork, ground peanut sugar, and the secret red chilli sauce, all working miraculously together. There is even a plant-based version for vegan customers. Healthy drinks such as Job's Tears milk or almond soy milk are also on hand to quench your thirst.;Cash only;[]
5126;Sung Chu Yuan;Taiwan;Taipei;546 Yonggong Road, Shilin District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.1398182;121.5675751;16;false;false;Taiwanese;Apart from rearing its own free range chicken, the restaurant is also famous for wild veggies such as betel flowers, Madeira vine and Okinawa spinach. The must-order bird, either steamed or smoked, boasts juicy, velvety meat and gelatinous, bouncy skin. Braised pork, steamed lamb, chicken soup with mustard greens, and deep-fried mashed taro rolls are also popular. Located in the city’s backyard, it’s the perfect spot for a post-hiking meal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5127;HUGH dessert dining;Taiwan;Taipei;56, Lane 136, Section 3, Chongqing North Road, Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0676278;121.5121712;32;true;true;Creative;Formerly a private dessert lab open by appointment only, Hugh turned into a sleek, minimalistic restaurant with regular hours in 2021. The 6- to 7- course dessert dining menu includes the best sweets in season, not only exquisitely plated, but also subverting preconceptions. Courses flow elegantly from one to another, presenting a variety of depth and textures. It’s also worth paying extra for the hidden improvised course. Booking is mandatory.;Air conditioning;[]
5128;Gulu Gulu;Taiwan;Taichung;2, Lane 13, Wuquan West 4th Street, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1384333;120.6624749;61;false;true;Taiwanese;Next to a tree-lined boulevard, Gulu Gulu exudes rustic chic with its generous display of driftwood and art pieces by indigenous tribes. For over 20 years it has been serving traditional Paiwan cooking famous for chargrilled dishes such as BBQ tribal spring chicken. Try also Makauy sausage and Paiwan traditional galaugal-shell flower rice dumpling. Nightly performances by indigenous singers add to the experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5129;Huang Chia Shrimp Roll;Taiwan;Tainan;268 Sihe Road, Central West District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0028094;120.1925813;61;false;true;Small eats;Over 60 years old, this eatery has moved four times, but that hasn’t deterred its loyal followers who continue to queue up daily before opening time. Shrimp roll is a classic Taiwanese snack and a must-try for all visitors. Huang Chia’s version is stuffed with shrimp and cabbage and is dipped in a potato starch batter before being deep-fried to order, resulting in a fluffy airy crust, with thinly sliced radish on the side for contrast.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5131;Shanghai Food (Nantun);Taiwan;Taichung;537, Section 2, Gongyi Road, Nantun District, Taichung, 408, Taiwan;24.142718;120.6373369;57;true;true;Dim Sum;A Chinese herbalist by training, the owner hails from Shanghai and was spoilt by his grandpa who made him all sorts of treats. After he moved to Taiwan, he spent three years trying to recreate the most authentic pan-fried buns from memory and opened this shop in 2009. The pork buns boast soupy filling with the perfect ratio of fatty and lean meat. The veggie buns are light and flavourful, filled with bok choy, dried tofu and mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5132;Cheng Shi;Taiwan;Tainan;12, Lane 702, Section 1, Simen Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9894932;120.1981005;88;false;false;Noodles;Originally a hawker stall in a residential neighbourhood, Cheng Shi (‘honest’ in Chinese) took up this space in 2020 to serve health-conscious diners with all-natural egg noodle soup. Their clear broth made with kombu is a lot lighter than versions offered by their competitors and the variety generously topped with clams is especially popular. You can even specify how soft or firm you want your noodles. Expect to wait during peak hours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5133;Xie Shopkeeper;Taiwan;Tainan;5, Lane 23, Yunhe Road, Anping District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.99922;120.16172;92;true;false;Small eats;This restaurant is a relative newcomer in this city swamped by century-old stalls, but it has made a name for itself since 2018 thanks to fresh seafood cooked to order. Its renowned milkfish and assorted seafood congee (more like soupy rice) is lavishly topped with fish skin, fish balls, fish meat, shrimps, clams and cuttlefish, imparting deep seafood umami. Steamed seafood in salt is also popular – try steamed giant grouper for its gelatinous texture.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5134;Chao Ming;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;53 Zihciang 1st Road, Cianjin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6305849;120.2931516;85;true;false;Taiwanese;Now helmed by the second generation of the family, this well-known landmark of Taiwanese home-style cooking has been in business for over 60 years. Masterful control of heat and a dexterous use of sauces depict the food, most of which comes in three portion sizes. Hallmark dishes include stir-fried pork belly with garlic sprouts and stir-fried clams with mung bean sprouts. Wild-caught marine fish, braised or pan-fried, is also popular.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5135;Liao Chi Migao;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;119 Ciaonan Road, Ciaotou District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.7543187;120.3123362;19;true;false;Small eats;This no-frills shop near the train station has been famous for their migao, or rice cake, since 1955. Glutinous rice mixed with dried shrimps and shallot is steamed in ceramic ramekins as opposed to bamboo tubes. The rice cake is then turned out onto a serving plate, drizzled with braised pork sauce, topped with pork floss and pickled cucumber. Pair it with the herbal soup known as si shen tang, or pork intestine vermicelli soup as accompaniment.;Cash only;[]
5137;Hsiung Chi Scallion Pancake;Taiwan;Taipei;Gongguan Night Market, 2, Lane 108, Section 4, Luosifu Road, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0129692;121.5357748;22;false;false;Street Food;Crispy on the outside, soft on the inside, the pancake matches perfectly with the honey mustard and basil.;Cash only;[]
5138;Old New Taiwanese Cuisine (Jiuru 2nd Road);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;227 Jiuru 2nd Road, Sanmin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.640741;120.3074876;25;true;false;Taiwanese;The kitchen team has remained the same since this household name opened in 2008. 7- to 8-course omakase menus are offered at different price points, all featuring traditional banquet cooking updated with finesse and sophistication. Note that the locals prefer their food heavily seasoned, so ask the chef to go easy on the seasoning if you prefer. It took up this address in 2011 and had a makeover that captures retro east-meets-west charm.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
5139;Yang Bao Bao (Chaoming Road);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;106 Chaoming Road, Nanzih District, Kaohsiung, 814, Taiwan;22.7241743;120.3279485;84;false;true;Dumplings;In 1993, this dumpling shop began life as a street stall in a local market. Now it has become a household name throughout south Taiwan. Apart from steamed pork and beef dumplings, the variety filled with assorted vegetables also stands out – its plump, full skin enrobes a filling of shredded wood ear fungus, green bok choy, glass noodles and dried tofu. Pancake rolls that are crispy and nicely browned are also popular.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5140;Chin Chih Yuan (Central);Taiwan;Taichung;170 Chenggong Road, Central District, Taichung, 400, Taiwan;24.14131;120.6825015;16;false;false;Taiwanese;Founded in 1978, this shop made its name with its rice – steamed in a soft rush-woven pouch that imparts unique aromas. Though no longer cooked that way, quality local rice is now topped with a dab of house-made pickled potherb mustard for savoury sweetness. Deep-fried pork ribs, and beef in sacha sauce are the hottest choices to go with the rice. The food may take time to arrive as everything is prepared to order. Expect to queue at lunch.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5142;Taj;Taiwan;Taipei;1, Lane 48, Section 4, Civic Boulevard, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0447331;121.5458616;45;true;false;Indian;Bold colours, patchwork and ethnic prints abound in this bustling halal restaurant serving Northern Indian cuisine. The Pakistani owner shops for spices and recruits chefs from India to ensure the cooking aligns with his vision. He is also keen on hosting Indian cultural events at weekends. Signatures include tandoori chicken, and dal Makhani (black lentil curry). Don’t forget to order wholemeal tandoori roti to go with the food.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5143;Mai Mien Yen Tsai;Taiwan;Taipei;106 Anxi Street, Datong District, Taipei, 103, Taiwan;25.0610377;121.5098001;97;false;false;Noodles;This shop on the ground floor of a somewhat dilapidated apartment has over 80 years of history. There is always a queue lining up for their egg or rice noodles, either served in a flavoursome stock made with pork bones, offal and chicken, or dressed in a sweet sauce. Side dishes such as pork offal, boiled chicken and blanched squid are also not to be missed. The signature fried braised pork, crispy and succulent, is only available after 10am.;Cash only;[]
5144;Halal Chinese Beef Noodles (Da'an);Taiwan;Taipei;1, Alley 7, Lane 137, Yanji Street, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0422509;121.5549813;49;true;false;Noodles;For his restaurant with over 60 years of history, the owner insists on using only Taiwanese beef that has never been frozen for the best flavour and texture. The beef stock is simmered all day to develop deep flavours without any greasiness. Apart from their signature braised beef noodle soup, also try fried-to-order flatbread, which is stuffed with stir-fried shredded beef. The beef jerky is also good but is only available in strictly limited quantity.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5145;Saffron Fine Indian Cuisine;Taiwan;Taipei;38-6 Tianmu East Road, Shilin District, Taipei, 111, Taiwan;25.1175507;121.5327248;33;false;false;Indian;The white stucco façade and columns look rustic and elegant, while the full-length windows let in plenty of natural light. The interior of terracotta floor, textured wall, burgundy lanterns and dark wood furniture all help build up an appetite for an exotic meal. Signature dishes include murgh Kerala (Kerala-style roast chicken) and murgh kothmeri (coriander chicken). There are even chefs in one corner making naan bread to order.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5147;Bei Gang Tsai Rice Tube (Yancheng);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;166 Hesi Road, Yancheng District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6317141;120.2851452;23;false;true;Small eats;This third-generation family business dates back to 1956 and many Kaohsiungese grew up with its ‘tube’ sticky rice, which is actually steamed with braised ground pork in a metal tub, turned out on a plate and topped with gravy. Do order a soy-marinated ‘iron egg’ on the side to go with the rice. There are also several soups on the menu, including steamed egg custard soup – the sponge-like custard sucks up the flavourful stock nicely.;Cash only;[]
5148;Wu Wang Tsai Chi;Taiwan;Taipei;Nanjichang Night Market, 29, Lane 313, Section 2, Zhonghua Road, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, 100, Taiwan;25.02878;121.50667;26;true;true;Street Food;Rechristened and moved into an alley, but expect the same tasty popiah roll with 10 different fillings that are packed with layered flavours.;Cash only;[]
5149;Black-faced Spoonbill Canteen;Taiwan;Tainan;17-18, Haipu, Shihfen Village, Cigu District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0828682;120.0629731;63;false;false;Seafood;A must for birdwatchers and seafood lovers, the Canteen is one of the best places to see the endangered black-faced spoonbills in Taiwan. From September to the following May, these migratory birds fly here and feed on the fish in the restaurant owner’s pond. Besides sustainably farmed milkfish and clams straight from his fish farm, the menu also includes other seafood classics, like deep-fried squid in salted egg yolk sauce.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
5150;Shin Yeh Shiao Ju;Taiwan;Taipei;166 Jingmao 2nd Road, Nangang District, Taipei, 115, Taiwan;25.058488;121.616285;33;true;false;Taiwanese;A sister concept spun off from the household brand, it caters to small groups and families with a menu designed for sharing, and champions low-fat and low-sodium Taiwanese cooking. Signatures such as stir-fried thousand-year eggs with green chillies, and omelette with angled luffa and dried scallops are original recipes not found elsewhere. The airy and elegant space is bathed in daylight and adorned with wood and neutral greys.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5151;Tsui Feng Yuan;Taiwan;Taipei;5, Lane 8, Section 3, Bade Road, Songshan District, Taipei, 105, Taiwan;25.0474845;121.5498352;20;false;true;Cantonese;At this sister restaurant to Peng Family, the chef insists on cooking Cantonese food exactly the way his great uncle did. Lamb belly hot pot is a winter speciality made with Australian lamb, red bean curd, sugarcane and ginger. Equally popular is crispy duck stuffed with mashed taro, steamed egg white custard with scallops and fish head hot pot. Service is friendly and warm and reservations are recommended on holidays.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5152;Li Xiao Lou;Taiwan;Taichung;50, Lane 293, Section 2, Xitun Road, Xitun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1766503;120.6425912;66;true;false;Taiwanese;An old property in an alley has been remodelled to house this low-profile restaurant. A pared-down interior and casual vibe set the scene, while a Japanese-style wooden counter frames the open kitchen. Taiwanese home cooking and small plates define the concise menu. Try sorghum liquor-scented Kinmen sausages in a crisp thin casing. Salt-baked chicken leg with sweet corn is another must-try, best enjoyed with a bowl of braised pork rice.;Air conditioning;[]
5153;Talking Heads;Taiwan;Taipei;25 Siwei Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0354792;121.5482005;55;false;true;Hunanese, Jiangzhe;Judging from the name, it’s no surprise to learn that the owner is a die-hard fan of the American rock band. The restaurant has moved a few times in its 30-plus years of history and has been here since 2019. On the menu, home-style, MSG-free cooking from Hunan and Jiangzhe takes centre stage. Try fried hardboiled eggs tossed with chilli, Wuxi-style pork ribs, and Shanghainese cabbage rice. Also check out the catch of the day on the blackboard.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5154;Inn's+;Taiwan;Taipei;8, Lane 28, Shuangcheng Street, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0658284;121.523703;52;false;true;Taiwanese;Tucked away in a quiet alley, the reputation of Inn’s+ is entirely word of mouth. The owner-chef, who used to manage a bistro, re-interprets Taiwanese classics with less fat and less sodium for a health-conscious clientele, without sacrificing flavour or freshness. Her signature baby oyster omelette uses plump, creamy bivalves from Chiayi County, as well as free-range chicken eggs that boast rich flavours. Tailored menus possible for large parties.;Air conditioning;[]
5155;House of Dawn;Taiwan;Taichung;104 Dadun 18th Street, Xitun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1574877;120.6488948;90;false;true;Vegetarian;With just 8 tables, this little gem is its owner’s pride and joy. Much effort went into the fine details – red bricks against terrazzo walls, bespoke hand-thrown ceramic dinnerware against sleek wood furniture. The aptly named ‘noodles extraordinaire’, artisan ramen dressed in a secret chilli and sesame sauce, are quite unique. Golden, crispy potstickers take 30 minutes to prepare but are well worth the wait.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5156;Fresh Fish Stock;Taiwan;Taichung;75 Beitun Road, North District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1612731;120.6921248;37;true;true;Small eats;This simple shop specialising in Tainan cooking has been a staple on Taichung’s food scene for over 30 years. The glistening shrimp rice is flavoursome and the tiny morsels of ham pack savoury oomph. Milkfish shipped daily from the south is cooked nose-to-tail – try milkfish soup, braised milkfish belly or head, or milkfish congee. Cold sides such as braised pork sinew, and seafood like oyster, grouper and tenpounder are also popular with diners.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5158;Hung Chi Rice Shop;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;96 Liwun Road, Zuoying District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6646279;120.3042735;48;false;true;Small eats;As opposed to typical braised pork rice shops that can sometimes feel a little dated, this one boasts a bright, simple interior with full-length windows. The cartoon pig logo also makes it appealing to a younger audience. Despite its fresh look, the menu focusses on good old Taiwanese favourites. Braised pork rice is a must, and you have the option to top it with an over-easy egg. Do also order sides like braised cabbage, and pork tendon.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5159;Yi Wei Pin;Taiwan;Tainan;Shop 111 & 112, Yong Le Market, 177-179, Section 3, Guohua Street, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9975682;120.1988805;44;true;true;Small eats;Splitting from Fu Sheng Hao, a household name in the realm of Taiwanese savoury rice pudding known as wagui, the owner started Yi Wei Pin in 2013 to amplify his grandpa’s culinary legacy. Much darker in colour than its Taipei counterparts, the wagui is made with local rice milk, freshly slaughtered pork, velvet shrimps and house-braised ground pork sauce. Try it with washabi or minced garlic also. Their milkfish thick soup is also popular.;Cash only;[]
5160;Fu Kuei Ting;Taiwan;Taichung;31, Lane 18, Section 2, Sanmin Road, Central District, Taichung, 400, Taiwan;24.1401586;120.6782384;27;false;false;Taiwanese;Many Taichungians have fond childhood memories of this shop as it has over 60 years of history. Its signature goose noodle soup and smoked goose tend to sell out within the first 30 minutes every morning. The soup base features the Chinese herb Dang Gui, while the bird boasts springy flesh and robust flavours. If goose runs out, try the equally appealing duck version. Rice cakes in bamboo stem are also well made. Be prepared to share a table.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5161;Fu Juang Yuan;Taiwan;Taichung;203, Section 1, Meicun Road, West District, Taichung, 403, Taiwan;24.1498664;120.6619496;22;false;false;Taiwanese;One of the most famous places in town for marinated pork trotters, this shop keeps the liquid gold – made with soy, rock sugar, chilli and shallot – on a gentle simmer all day, hence the comforting aroma. While trotters are prized for their gelatinous texture, upper leg cuts strike a balance between fat, skin and meat. Side dishes such as shredded bamboo shoots are also good. Instead of plain steamed rice, try it with a drizzle of marinade.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5163;Tien Hsia San Chueh;Taiwan;Taipei;3, Lane 27, Section 4, Ren'ai Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.038915;121.54525;67;true;true;Noodles;As opposed to the typical cramped noodle shop, this one is lavish and glam. Better still, it also delivers in terms of taste – the signature beef noodle soup with oxtail, shank, tendon and heel muscle lets you sample a range of beef textures. The broth is made with beef backbones and ribs plus four kinds of tomatoes and two kinds of onions for extra depth and dimension. The marinated meat platter, appetisers and pork rib rice are also well made.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
5165;Hsi Lo Tien Beef Soup;Taiwan;Tainan;98 Gongyuan South Road, North District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0015391;120.2073867;33;false;true;Small eats;Its hallmark beef soup is simmered with beef bones, brisket, fat and onion and thin slices of lean beef are added just before serving. Pour on a dash of rice wine for extra fragrance or dip the beef in the fiery home-made chilli sauce for a kick. The assortment soup offers a choice of cuts from beef tendon and brisket to liver and all the soups come with a bowl of steamed rice or braised pork rice. Stir-fries like beef with kale are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5166;Yuan Wei;Taiwan;Taipei;2, Lane 227, Huanyin Street, Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0507831;121.5141359;93;true;true;Taiwanese;Tucked down a small alley behind the train station and without a proper sign, this eatery with over 70 years of history and just four tables is easy to miss. Even the interior feels more like a wood carving store than a restaurant. The menu is easy to navigate, with only 20-odd choices. Stir-fries are the must-try items – Yuan Wei fried rice, and pork jowl, characterised by remarkable wok-hei. Cash only and expect a long wait at peak hours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5167;Kaiyuan Fried Spanish Mackerel Thick Soup;Taiwan;Tainan;307 Kaiyuan Road, North District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0081097;120.2213038;94;false;false;Small eats;The absence of both an obvious sign and air conditioning hasn’t deterred hungry locals from flocking here from 7am till late over the past four decades. With generous chunks of deep-fried Spanish mackerel in a stock made with halibut, bonito and fried garlic, the eponymous thick soup makes a great meal by itself or a snack between meals. If you’re lucky, you may even get to try the deep-fried mackerel skin that offers great seafood umami.;Cash only;[]
5168;Lao Ye Mei Shi Guan (Fengshan);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;54-56 Haiyang 1st Road, Fengshan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6098086;120.3432815;92;false;true;Small eats;The restaurant has been a landmark of Fengshan’s culinary scene for almost two decades. Its speciality, smoked duck glazed in cane sugar, is a masterclass of flavour and is particularly juicy and tender thanks to the duck breed from China. Pan-fried pork belly with lemongrass is another hit, featuring freshly slaughtered local pork and sustainably grown lemongrass from the owner’s farm, without forgetting the fish soup that cooks for four hours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5169;Hsiu Ming;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;41 Yongping Street, Cishan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.88557;120.481423;15;false;false;Small eats;Installed next to Cishan Old Street since 1986, this neat little shop has stood the test of time. Pork offal can be paired with egg noodles, glass noodles or steamed rice. The fleshy and springy pork tongue is the popular dish – best enjoyed with a dab of grated garlic for a kick. Braised ground pork rice topped with a sunny-side-up egg is also a must: pierce the yolk so it runs down over the rice for a mouthful of tasty goodness.;Cash only;[]
5170;Beef Chief (Zihciang 2nd Road);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;18 Zihciang 2nd Road, Cianjin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6224341;120.2966045;21;false;true;Taiwanese;Beef Chief rose from humble beginnings in 1996 as a street stall selling beef soup. Now it serves shabu-shabu hotpot using freshly slaughtered beef shipped from Tainan daily. The amber soup base is made with beef bones, veggies and fruits, boasting subtle sweetness. Apart from being served in hotpot, beef cuts and offal are available as stir-fries – try stir-fried beef tendon. Excellent value and friendly service also explain its popularity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5171;Mu Gong Noodles;Taiwan;Taichung;37 Fugui Street, East District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1497969;120.6955987;44;false;true;Noodles;Thanks to terrazzo floor tiles, metal tube frame furniture, and golden oldies on shuffle, the ambiance is unmistakably 1960s. The teacher-turned owner opened this shop as he missed the authentic Jiangzhe noodles his father-in-law used to make. The springy noodles swim in an aromatic broth that has exceptional depth. Order noodle soup with fried pork chop, shredded pork and pickled mustard stem, or a side of soy-marinated meat.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5173;Ciao Zai Tou Huang's Braised Pork Rice (Ciaotou);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;106 Ciaonan Road, Ciaotou District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.7547237;120.3122203;92;false;true;Small eats;Ciaotou was the centre of Taiwan’s sugar production and this 6-decade-old joint fascinates its fans with terrific braised pork rice boasting a savoury-sweet taste. Pork shoulder and belly in a specific ratio are hand-diced and braised till melting before being drizzled over steamed rice. Pork thick soup, and assorted pork offal make perfect companions with the signature rice. Expect to queue any time of the day. It closes on major holidays.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5174;San Hao Yi Kung Tao Angelica Duck;Taiwan;Tainan;2, Section 1, Fucian Road, Central West District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9890547;120.2107938;54;true;true;Small eats;Circa 1949, it was a hawker stall in the Dongmen Traffic Circle before moving here in the 1960s. Now into the second generation, the family business still attracts a loyal fanbase thanks to its duck noodle soup made with the Chinese herb Dang Gui (a.k.a. Chinese angelica root). The amber broth has rounded flavours, a lingering aftertaste and a hint of bitterness. With freshly slaughtered duck and al dente noodles, it makes for a wholesome meal.;Cash only;[]
5175;Apis Grill;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;80 Baoyang East Street, Sanmin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6395983;120.3488072;87;false;true;Barbecue;Tucked away down an alley with no visible signage apart from a triangle, diners are greeted by the awe-inspiring sight of a giant longan wood-fired kiln and rows of charcoal grills behind the counter. The veteran head chef is keen on straight-forward, back-to-basics cooking, in which meat, fish and veggies are grilled over a wood fire. The menu changes every few weeks, but New Zealand venison is a firm fixture. Order the abalone if available.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5176;Chang Hung Noodles;Taiwan;Taipei;Huaxi Street Night Market, Stall 171, 15 Huaxi Street, Wanhua District, Taipei, 108, Taiwan;25.0394902;121.4985619;29;false;false;Noodles;For almost 50 years, regulars have been coming for its pork cheek noodle soup, boiled chicken and pork tail.;Cash only;[]
5177;Wang's Broth;Taiwan;Taipei;Huaxi Street Night Market, Stall 153, 17-4 Huaxi Street, Wanhua District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.03921;121.49846;47;false;false;Small eats;As well as minced pork and pickled cucumber in broth, try their steamed rice with ‘black gold’ pork sauce.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5178;Fu Din Wang (Central);Taiwan;Taichung;560, Section 1, Taiwan Boulevard, Central District, Taichung, 400, Taiwan;24.1451927;120.6765412;80;false;true;Taiwanese;Diners flock to this semi-self-service shop for pork trotter, hock and leg – braised in a soy-based marinade for up to four hours, the meat is gelatinous, tender and flavourful. It tastes even better with the house-made chilli sauce, cleaner and less complex than with the typical marinade and its strong herbal undertones. The braised diced pork rice and braised fried tofu are also good options. The simple decor makes for a relaxed vibe.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5179;Serenity (Zhongzheng);Taiwan;Taipei;1, Lane 1, Zhenjiang Street, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, 100, Taiwan;25.044366;121.521854;91;true;false;Vegetarian;Taiwan's first Sichuan vegetarian restaurant is headed up by two chefs, one specialising in vegetarian cooking, the other well versed in Sichuan cuisine. As half of the shop is enclosed in glass panes, the place feels airy and bright. Meat-free dishes imbued with deep flavours and plenty of heat can be made vegan or ovo-lacto vegetarian. Must-try items include the basil-scented vegetarian crisp "tripe" – deep-fried king oyster mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
5180;Dayong Street No Name Congee;Taiwan;Tainan;85 Dayong Street, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9898212;120.1932798;27;true;false;Congee;Tainanese don’t need a sign to find good food in every nook and cranny of their city. This shop is one of such joints – a nondescript space clad in corrugated metal sheets, but that doesn’t stop regulars from queuing at the door. Its Tainan-style congee is more like soupy rice than the creamy type. Milkfish fillet, oysters, Chinese celery and rice are drenched in a clear stock to make the brunch favourite of many.;Cash only;[]
5181;Pàng;Taiwan;Taipei;118 Wenchang Street, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.03261;121.55215;61;true;false;Mexican;Orange tables add a pop of colour to this simple room done out in wood tones and neutrals. An Americanophile, the owner-chef worked in a Latam fine dining restaurant before opening this casual joint to realise his culinary vision of refined Mexican fare with Taiwanese ingredients. His signature cochinita pibil taco has layers of flavours with slow-cooked pork, house-made habanero salsa and hibiscus-pickled onion. He even makes his own soft corn tortillas.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5182;Cheng Tsung Duck Rice;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;245 Yucheng Road, Zuoying District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6646256;120.3094563;83;true;false;Small eats;This simple shop is always jam-packed with customers. Its signature is undoubtedly the eponymous duck rice – smoked duck pieces on steamed rice drizzled with a secret sauce. Another speciality, hand-sliced duck leg rice, is available in limited quantity, boasting smoky and juicy flesh. And of course, the duck also goes well with the array of noodles on offer. Try assorted duck offal soup, and side dishes made with bean sprouts.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5183;Hu Dong Beef;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;107, Section 1, Zhongshan Road, Hunei District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.8777542;120.2519723;68;false;true;Taiwanese;Right on the border between Tainan and Kaohsiung, just a stone’s throw from a train station, is this restaurant serving freshly slaughtered beef from Tainan daily. Customers come in droves for evenly marbled, hand-sliced beef to be blanched in a rich beef bone broth. The brisket boasts melting fat and gelatinous sinews, truly a must-try for meat lovers. Make sure you book a table and pre-order your beef. Additional orders are not taken on the spot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
5184;Amei;Taiwan;Tainan;98, Section 2, Mincyuan Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9948568;120.2042929;64;false;true;Taiwanese;A household name for over 60 years, Amei was remodelled after moving to this spot. Red tablecloths pop amid the wood-rich interior with trophies and historic artefacts. The small menu is big on banquet classics and century-old recipes, combining the natural umami of ingredients with locals’ love of savoury-sweet dishes. Signatures include thick shrimp soup with shredded bamboo shoot and wisps of egg, and the duck casserole slow-cooked for 3 hours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5185;Yuan Fang Guabao;Taiwan;Taipei;Huaxi Street Night Market, Stall 161, 17-2 Huaxi Street, Wanhua District, Taipei, 108, Taiwan;25.039542;121.498529;97;false;true;Street Food;A 60-year-old shop selling buns stuffed with marinated pork belly, pickles, ground peanuts and coriander.;Cash only;[]
5188;Ibu Kitchen;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;629, Section 2, Jhongshan Road, Meinong District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.8937396;120.5142027;51;false;true;Taiwanese;Right next to Meinung Folk Village, Ibu Kitchen specialises in Aboriginal Taiwanese cuisine made with produce from the Bunun owner-chef’s hometown in Mount Tengzhi. The menu is dominated by healthy options like fried egg tofu in plum sauce, steamed millet dumpling with pork and sakura shrimps, and free-range chicken braised in plum sauce with shiso leaves. The room is generously adorned with greenery, with commanding and gorgeous mountain views.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5189;Soft Power;Taiwan;Taipei;21, Alley 30, Lane 135, Section 2, Minquan East Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.06425;121.53611;24;false;true;Small eats;This hipster breakfast shop was founded in 2017 before moving to a quiet alley near Xingtian Temple. It prides itself on its egg fritters in south Taiwanese style with a crisp crust and fluffy, soft centre. There are more than 10 fillings to choose from, such as Sichuan pepper sausage, or soymilk chicken. Some of the fillings are also served in the form of rice balls or sandwiched in a steamed dark brown sugar bun like a Taiwanese burger. Everything is made to order.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5190;Mai Yen Shun;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;173 Cinghai Road, Gushan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6512679;120.2869283;48;false;false;Taiwanese;Memorabilia and vinyl records mingle with glamorous portraits and obsolete farming tools in this nostalgic interior. In the same spirit, the menu compiles a list of some much-missed home-style Taiwanese classics of yesteryear. For the perfect companion to a bowl of steamed rice, order the fried chicken leg with old ginger in three-cup sauce, which delivers deep soy, basil and sesame flavours. Ask about the chef's specials on weekends.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5191;Ke Kou Beef Noodles;Taiwan;Taichung;911 Dadun Road, Xitun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1569617;120.6504773;51;false;false;Noodles;Both the owner and his wife are beef lovers and Ke Kou is their brainchild. The signature noodle soup with red braised beef and sinew boasts a complex and rich broth – simmered for hours with 35 different Chinese herbs – that complements the springy noodles and tender Australian beef shin perfectly. Braised ox tripe perfumed with spices and herbs, and the seemingly simple kelp that imparts an intense savoury-sweet flavour are recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
5192;Taichung Meatball;Taiwan;Taichung;529, Section 3, Fuxing Road, South District, Taichung, 402, Taiwan;24.1344609;120.682587;19;true;false;Small eats;One of the best known places for frugal eats, this veritable institution has been around since 1933 and holds a special place in every Taichungese’s heart because of its no-frills tasty food. There are only three items on the menu – the meatball, fish ball soup and glass noodle soup. The meatball is something of a misnomer as it’s closer to a big translucent dumpling with peppery ground pork filling topped with thick soy and sweet sauces.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5194;Zhu Xin Ju;Taiwan;Tainan;69 Sinyi Street, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0003366;120.1950406;57;true;true;Taiwanese;This quaint red-brick mansion built circa 1846 has been home to an omakase restaurant serving traditional Taiwanese banquet dishes since 2015. The room was carefully restored to its former glory, befitting the old-time recipes the head chef got hooked on. For a flat fee per person, your party will be served seven dishes and one soup, all made with local seasonal ingredients like milkfish from Cigu and rice from Houbi. Reservations are mandatory.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5197;Jai Mi Ba;Taiwan;Tainan;159-1 Bao-an Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9907395;120.1937314;21;false;false;Noodles;Its full-length windows and open kitchen may not look like your typical noodle shop. The owner-chef has honed his skills in French cuisine for over 10 years and opened this minimalistic shop in his hometown for Taiwanese noodles to mingle with French techniques and sauces. The short menu shows promising creativity and it changes every week, except seared ox tongue with noodles in truffle sauce, and cheese caramel flan that are always available.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5198;Qin Yuan Chun (Central);Taiwan;Taichung;129, Section 1, Taiwan Boulevard, Central District, Taichung, 400, Taiwan;24.139452;120.682718;63;true;true;Jiangzhe;Run by fourth-generation owners, this 70-plus-year-old family business is usually full of regulars. The dining room is plainly furnished, but customers don’t come for the ambiance, but the authentic Jiangzhe classics such as pork trotter aspic, drunken chicken and stir-fried swamp eel. Steamed-to-order xiao long bao boast thin, translucent skin and soupy pork filling. The take-out counter offers quick service for those on the go.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5199;A Cheng Goose (Zhongshan);Taiwan;Taipei;162 Jilin Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.0566822;121.5300706;89;true;false;Taiwanese;Opened in 2010, this branch of the brand has been focusing on its take-out service since the COVID-19 pandemic. A new three-storey branch right across the street was launched to take care of dine-in customers. Its famous goose from Yunlin County is served two ways – boiled or smoked, the latter being the most popular. Diners can also choose the cut: the leaner, boneless breast or the tender, juicier leg. Try the braised gizzards or blood pudding, too.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5200;Rong Rong Yuan;Taiwan;Taipei;25, Section 4, Xinyi Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0335861;121.5446576;80;false;true;Zhejiang;The chef has been at the helm here for 30 years and each dish is prepared the same way as it was when the shop opened in 1965. The must-try braised pork ribs are slow-cooked in an onion broth for six hours until the meat falls off the bone – the perfect match for the guangbing flatbread. Other signatures include oxtail on a sizzling hotplate, dongpo pork with red yeast rice, and Beggar’s chicken. Most items need pre-ordering. Service is warm and homely.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5201;Huang Chi Lu Rou Fan;Taiwan;Taipei;28, Lane 183, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0636638;121.5241848;79;false;false;Small eats;Without flashy branding and publicity stunts, this decades-old shop has gained the patronage of foodies through word of mouth. Its signature braised pork rice leans more towards the fatty side, but strangely enough, doesn’t taste greasy. The pork sauce packs exceptional depth and a mild gelatinous feel. The thick soup made with bonito flakes and Sa Cha sauce, as well as its braised napa cabbage are to die for! Always busy, despite long opening hours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5202;Küisine (West);Taiwan;Taichung;1, Lane 24, Mofan Street, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1487311;120.6668283;35;false;false;Asian;The unpretentious Küisine emphasises home-like cosiness and intimacy. It’s tucked away in a residential alley and the room feels serene and relaxing. Apart from Taiwanese classics such as plum chicken, and braised beef and fried tofu, Southeast Asian and Japanese influences are also evident in curry, shogayaki and miso dishes. Portion sizes are on the small side so that guests can sample more variety.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5203;Niou Jia Juang;Taiwan;Taichung;19 Xinfeng Street, Dongshi District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.2629382;120.8248237;99;true;true;Hakkanese;This 60-year-old household name is undergoing an 18-month renovation and is temporarily operating at a spot 50 metres from the original shop. From the cartoon cow on the sign to cow-shaped decorations inside, beef is obviously the staple offering here. Local yellow beef is cooked nose-to-tail in traditional Hakkanese ways and the offal is unmissable – try scallion bone marrow, and cold beef tripe dressed in sweet and sour sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5205;No Name Lamb Soup;Taiwan;Tainan;144, Section 2, Fucian Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.99134;120.1945;30;true;true;Small eats;After five decades of business in Guohua Street Market, the lamb soup stall shut its doors in 2013. Regulars lamented the loss but the owner’s nephew quit his job in Taipei to re-open the shop here. The famous soup made with freshly slaughtered local lamb meat and bones is the must-try item, but do order other lamb cuts and offal blanched in the soup and dressed in sesame oil. Come early – everything is sold out before 11 am.;Cash only;[]
5206;Thai Yuan;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;53 Lingya 2nd Road, Lingya District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6179712;120.3014009;95;true;true;Thai;This simple shop has generated lots of buzz on social media since it opened in 2020. Despite the lack of air conditioning, diners love the exotic street vibe in the bright blue setting adorned by Thai knickknacks. As its name suggests, Pad Thai is the signature item, a mildly spicy and tangy noodles dish. Thai coffee is also not to be missed. Order o liang for black, or café yen with milk and condensed milk. Check its Facebook page for days off.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5207;Hao Nung Chia Migao;Taiwan;Tainan;66, Section 2, Jiankang Road, South District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9816143;120.195999;66;true;true;Small eats;In 1946, this rice cake joint opened its doors in South District, away from the city’s busy tourist spots. It has ever been a hit with the locals who can’t get enough of its addictive migao, topped with braised pork sauce, fish floss, cucumber and peanuts. The second-generation owner insists on making migao just like his father did: the sticky rice is soaked, steamed and kept warm in a woven reed tub next to the stove to keep it moist and chewy.;Cash only;[]
5209;Peng Cheng Tang;Taiwan;Taichung;377 Yichang Road, Taiping District, Taichung, 411, Taiwan;24.1449224;120.7137408;34;false;false;Taiwanese;A time capsule circa 1960s and a get-together hotspot for locals, this restaurant takes you back in time with vintage knickknacks and nostalgic home cooking that is inexpensive and generously served. The gua bao set menu is hugely popular – steamed buns stuffed with braised pork belly, bamboo shoot, pickles and ground peanuts, while the stir-fried beef with Madeira wine is gingery and flavourful. Help yourself to the steamed rice with lard.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5210;Da-Qiao-Tou Tube Rice Pudding (Yanping North Road);Taiwan;Taipei;41, Section 3, Yanping North Road, Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0649859;121.5111851;15;false;true;Small eats;Though technically in a night market, this third-generation family business is only open from dawn till dusk. Since 1973, the regulars have been returning for its steamed sticky rice that is chewy but never mushy. Year-old aged rice is mixed with fried scallion and garlic before steamed with lean or fatty pork. It tastes best with homemade sweet chilli sauce and spicy radish sauce. Also try the oyster soup steeped in umami and plump oysters.;Cash only;[]
5211;Chung Chia Sheng Jian Bao;Taiwan;Taipei;Shilin Night Market, 38 Xiaodong Street, Shilin District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0896291;121.5263441;27;true;false;Street Food;This stall sells pan-fried buns with crispy bottoms and fluffy tops. Choose between cabbage and pork fillings.;Cash only;[]
5212;Do It True (Xinyi);Taiwan;Taipei;506, Section 4, Ren'ai Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.037228;121.561034;35;true;true;Beijing Cuisine;The menu at this 60-plus-year-old restaurant offers variations of dishes that the owner’s great uncle once cooked for Empress Cixi of Qing Dynasty. Crispy and juicy, the deep-fried pork balls made with hind leg cuts are an absolute must-try. Pork and cabbage pickle casserole, grouper fillet in distiller’s grain sauce, and giant inch-thick scallion pancakes are also recommended. It’s located on a tree-lined boulevard and comes with large windows and walnut wood furniture.;Air conditioning;[]
5213;Lao Shan Dong Homemade Noodles;Taiwan;Taipei;Shop 15, B1, 70 Xining South Road, Wanhua District, Taipei, 108, Taiwan;25.0435862;121.5059525;17;true;false;Noodles;This household name in the beef noodle scene has been attracting a loyal following with its ribbon noodles and beef broth since 1949. Beef bones and a blend of Chinese herbs give the broth its flavour and depth. Noodles are cut and cooked to order and local and Australian beef is simmered in the broth for hours until tender, so slurping up the broth gives you a burst of flavours. Cold sides such as pork ear in aspic and pickled cabbage are made fresh daily.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5214;Din Tai Fung (Xinyi Road);Taiwan;Taipei;277, Section 2, Xinyi Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.03381;121.5322;21;true;true;Shanghainese;The story of the international chain famous for xiao long bao dates back to 1972 when its first shop opened on Xinyi Road. The former flagship eatery is now takeaway-only, but dine-in service is available on the other side of the street in a 330-seater four-storey venue inaugurated in 2020. Besides the aforementioned soup dumplings, also try the sweet and sour pork, bitter melon pork rib soup and steamed taro buns.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5215;Simmer House;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;226 Guangsi Road, Cianjhen District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6154819;120.3169166;33;true;true;Taiwanese;Converted from Taipower Company former staff housing, this tiny gem serves five Chinese double-boiled soups that come with a side, plus your choice of rice or noodles. Spicy food lovers shouldn't miss the oyster chicken soup with chillies – vegetables nicely complement the umami of free-range chicken legs and oysters from Yunlin . For staples, try Koshihikari rice from Japan mixed with Tainan No. 16 and topped with nori pork floss.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5216;Joes (Gangshan);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;111 Hehua Road, Gangshan District, Kaohsiung, 820, Taiwan;22.7985835;120.2841362;42;false;false;Taiwanese;Gangshan is famous for its goat and you can’t leave without trying caprine dishes. Before opening Joes in 1955, the founder had long been selling goat in the market. With his connections, Joes always has access to the freshest goats. Signature dishes include Angelica goat hot pot, an herbal tonic with ribs and skin-on cuts. Stir-fried goat with bitter melon, and blanched goat slices with chilli bean sauce are also good. Bookings aren’t accepted.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5217;Chang Ying Seafood House;Taiwan;Tainan;484 Cianli, Sanliaowan, Beimen District, Tainan, 727, Taiwan;23.2389728;120.1105684;15;false;false;Small eats;The Council of Agriculture rolled out the ‘Tian Ma Ma’ programme to train and sponsor rural women to start their own businesses selling local specialities. This small shop is one such establishment and prides itself on milkfish farmed by the women themselves and certified additive-free. Its signature milkfish fillet is aged and seared in its own oil, boasting crispness and umami. Try also three-cup milkfish sausage, and dark brown sugar wagui.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5219;Saka;Taiwan;Taichung;7, Alley 9, Zhongshan Road, Daya District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.204956;120.6441243;89;false;true;Taiwanese;At the end of a meandering alley stands this quaint shop with over 40 years of history. The second generation of the family business prides itself on its signature dish – chicken braised in rice wine with Chinese herbs. No water is added and the broth bursts with deep umami. The chicken tastes especially good after being dipped in chilli soy sauce and ground pepper. Parking is available, but the thoughtful servers advise diners to take public transport after sampling the dish.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5220;Xiao Chu Den;Taiwan;Taichung;243 Daye Road, Nantun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.15358;120.648969;68;false;false;Small eats;The owners opened a cosy shop in 2018, specialising in Taiwanese light meals and snacks, before moving to this spot in 2020. With just three tables inside and one outside, this tiny gem is always busy. Braised pork on rice boasts an addictive gelatinous texture and deep flavours, while thickly sliced braised beef noodle soup is another must-try for noodle lovers. Certain items tend to run out early so consider pre-ordering your food by phone.;Cash only;[]
5221;Hsiao Cho Chih Chia;Taiwan;Taipei;420 Jilin Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.065868;121.530352;41;true;true;Taiwanese;This little gem with only five tables opened its doors in 1995 and moved to this address in 2010. The chef has been cooking professionally for over 40 years and he excels in making additive-free, simple but delicious Taiwanese dishes with the freshest catch from the sea. Regulars also come for abalone silkie chicken soup, double-boiled with Chinese herbs for two hours. Grilled pork trotter with gelatinous skin and juicy flesh is also unmissable.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5222;Small Park Danzai Noodles;Taiwan;Tainan;321, Section 2, Simen Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9971812;120.1996507;67;false;true;Noodles;Over 70 years ago, a stall opened by a small park and the owner would sit on a tiny stool to blanch the noodles, to be tossed in pork sauce or served in soup. Nowadays, the park no longer exists, but the owner still sits on a stool like the old days. Soup noodles are recommended – silky, al dente thin egg noodles in a flavoursome broth, topped with velvet shrimps and braised minced pork. Do order sides or braised dishes on top.;Cash only;[]
5223;Lo Cheng Migao;Taiwan;Tainan;241, Section 2, Minzu Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9959996;120.2045826;32;false;false;Small eats;The owner had been selling fried eels and squids for ages before he started serving migao by chance in 1985. Surprisingly, his sticky rice topped with braised pork, sliced cucumber, fish floss and peanut quickly surpassed his original offerings in popularity – and he has focused on migao and sishen herbal soup ever since. The gravy on his migao has a peppery aroma to go alongside the rich and deep flavours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5224;Dong Shang Taiwanese Seafood;Taiwan;Tainan;217, Section 6, Anzhong Road, Annan District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0607491;120.1366261;45;true;true;Taiwanese;For over three decades, the owner-chef has been supporting charitable causes and cooking for the disadvantaged. Regulars come here not just for his classic banquet dishes, but also for his vision of using only local, eco-friendly ingredients. All dishes, including the array of signature milkfish items, and ‘herbal’ prawns farmed without antibiotics and harmful chemicals, are available in three different portion sizes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5225;Chi Chia Chuang (Changchun Road);Taiwan;Taipei;55 Changchun Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.055052;121.526092;35;false;true;Taiwanese;Chicken features heavily on the menu and the owner is picky about them – he uses only pullets from 5 to 6 months old for their tender meat. Specialities include the classic three-cup chicken that imparts rich aromas, perfect with the chewy pork blood cake. The crispy deep-fried chicken rolls, and the rich, flavourful chicken soup are also worth trying. Don’t forget to end the meal with their homemade egg pudding. Service is warm and friendly.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
5227;Noodle House;Taiwan;Taipei;75, Lane 232, Hu Lin Street, Xinyi District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0360863;121.5756054;98;false;false;Noodles;This tiny shop tucked away in a back street has been around since 2007. Their signature is taro rice noodle soup, a breakfast and lunch favourite for many. Instead of rice vermicelli, which are more popular in Taiwan, the owner uses thick rice noodles for their texture and flavour. The broth is redolent with fried shallots, and the starchy taro is tender and flavourful. No wonder it's always busy at mealtimes!;Cash only;[]
5228;Yung Tung Milkfish;Taiwan;Tainan;60 Minquan Road, Syuejia District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.2314193;120.1804515;31;true;false;Small eats;Syuejia District is among the top five milkfish farming areas in Tainan, attracting foodies from all over the island. Yung Tung’s signature milkfish congee uses a fish stock that bursts with umami. Various parts of milkfish are served fried, braised or blanched. The braised fish head, and fish floss rice are especially popular. It also carries grass carp, tilapia and common carp, alongside hot dishes such as braised pork sinew.;Cash only;[]
5230;Feng Chi Goose;Taiwan;Taichung;170 Pingxi Road, Shalu District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.2097324;120.5691427;35;false;true;Taiwanese;For decades, this simple shop has been attracting hungry diners with its signature sliced goose platter boasting juicy flesh and wafer-thin skin. The second-generation owner intentionally leaves some bones and gristles in for diners to gnaw on. Goose offal, marinated meat and other sides are also popular. For starchier dishes, order plain noodle soup, or jazz it up with cuttlefish and thin, flat e-fu noodles.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5231;BUĒ MI . LAB;Taiwan;Tainan;90 Cingnian Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.99189;120.20825;100;false;false;Noodles;With bar stools, a show kitchen and a soundtrack of Mandarin golden oldies, this self-proclaimed lab experiments with noodle recipes from around the world, serving up bold creations that impress with depth and layers of flavours. The menu changes with the seasons, and the same bowl can include produce from different culinary cultures – bopi chillies, red miso, sambal, green papaya and even ratatouille, to name but a few.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5232;Po Jen Tang;Taiwan;Tainan;27, Lane 300, Section 2, Simen Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.996686;120.2003768;39;false;false;Taiwanese;This century-old Chinese medicine shop was converted into a restaurant specialising in therapeutic food. The sixth-generation owner intentionally kept the apothecary cabinets and used some inscribed plaques as dining tables. Eight tonic soups are offered each day, all tasty and mild in herbal flavour – refer to the menu for their medicinal actions. Make it a complete meal by ordering a set – with noodles tossed in sesame oil, a drink and sweet soup.;Air conditioning;[]
5233;Caizong Li;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;159 Chenggong 1st Road, Lingya District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.61597;120.29689;84;true;true;Small eats;The shop may have little ambiance to speak of, but it’s brightly lit and always spotless. Since its founding over 60 years ago, it has focused on two items only – peanut zongzi and kelp miso soup. The kitchen team at the back is always busy wrapping the signature sticky rice dumplings in bamboo leaves, to be steamed and topped with sauces and ground peanuts before served. Consider taking home some frozen zongzi, especially around Dragon Boat Festival.;Cash only;[]
5234;Hang Zhou Xiao Long Bao (Da'an);Taiwan;Taipei;17 & 19, Section 2, Hangzhou South Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.034063;121.523728;80;false;false;Dim Sum;This popular soup dumpling shop was born over 20 years ago after its owners were taught how to make xiao long bao by a Shanghainese chef. Only the freshest pork hind leg cuts are used as the filling and the dumpling ‘skin’ is made simply with flour and water. Their soup-squirting dumplings are also known for their lightness. The red bean pancake uses two kinds of red beans in its silky filling which is complemented by a crisp sesame pastry crust.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5235;A Xing Shi Mu Yu;Taiwan;Tainan;252 Wunsian Road, North District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.0045835;120.1938327;94;false;false;Small eats;This no-frills shop may lack glitzy décor but, for over 15 years, plenty of regulars have been coming here for its freshly slaughtered milkfish. Signatures include fried milkfish belly that boasts crispy skin and tender flesh. Milkfish soup is always served with braised pork rice everywhere in Tainan, but A Xing’s version comes with garlic rice instead. Fried fish intestines run out early in the morning. Come early or pre-order over the phone.;Cash only;[]
5237;Eat to Fat;Taiwan;Tainan;3, Lane 125, Sinmel Street, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9977563;120.2006862;20;true;false;Taiwanese;A devotee of the goddess Mazu, the owner-chef picked this space near the Grand Mazu Temple for his venture. Motifs of the goddess are dotted throughout the restaurant, from its sign to the shrine-inspired décor. Home-style cooking is kicked up a notch with a touch of sophistication. Leafy greens deftly meld the depth and umami of the fresh, salted and thousand-year egg trio. Try the squid and whelk soup, a classic banquet dish rarely found in Tainan. Closed during Mazu festivities.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5238;Shian Jeng Shrimp Bawan;Taiwan;Tainan;609 Yunong Road, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9887025;120.2351537;42;true;false;Small eats;Bawan has been around for over a century in Taiwan – the savoury filling is wrapped in a translucent dough, steamed and served with a sweet-savoury sauce. This shop, opened in 2012, is a relative newcomer, but their smaller version stuffed with spear shrimps and pork shoulder butt have instantly won the hearts of gourmets in Tainan. Try it with a dribble of mustard, or pair it with Sishen soup or shiitake pork soup. Check their media page for closing.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5239;Yuan Zai Hui (Guohua Street);Taiwan;Tainan;99, Section 2, Guohua Street, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9905205;120.1966966;31;false;true;Small eats;Shaved ice is mandatory for anyone spending a summer afternoon in scorching Tainan. But even in winter, shaved ice has its loyal fans. For over 50 years, Ice 8 Bao has been specialising in eight-treasure shaved ice, traditionally with eight toppings. But the owners serve a simplified version allowing customers to choose five toppings out of 10-plus house-made choices. Signature include mini mochi balls, candied taro and tapioca wedges.;Cash only;[]
5241;Molti Amici;USA;Healdsburg;330 Healdsburg Ave., Healdsburg, 95448, USA;38.6115964;-122.870502;77;true;true;Italian;Wine country certainly has no shortage of this sort of casual Italian eatery, with a menu featuring the expected wood-fired pizzas and house-made pastas—but few of them manage to hit their mark quite so dead on as they do here. They may not be reinventing the wheel, but those pizzas are ideally blistered and feature simple but compelling toppings like squash blossom with fontina and balsamic, and the pastas, like a satisfying take on bucatini amatriciana topped with crunchy breadcrumbs, offer an ideally al dente chew. On one of Healdsburg’s not-infrequent balmy days, the enclosed patio, complete with bocce court, is indeed an excellent spot to gather with “many friends,” as suggested by the name.;Garden or park;[]
5242;Mae Malai Thai House of Noodles;USA;Los Angeles;5445 Hollywood Blvd., Unit A, Los Angeles, 90027, USA;34.1020895;-118.3089445;92;true;true;Thai;Just a short walk from their original food stall, this restaurant's strip mall digs are simple but it's a comfortable, welcoming spot with a tempting menu to boot. As the name suggests, their specialty is noodles, particularly boat noodles with a thick, intense broth and your choice of pork or beef, noodle type, and spice level. Fret not if you can't decide, as the bowls are small and ordering two or more varieties might just be the perfect compromise. Don't skip out on their stir-fried dishes, such as the boldly spiced chili holy basil with ground pork, bell peppers, and green beans. For dessert, choose from coconut ice cream or kanom tuay, a two-layer custard featuring a green layer infused with fresh pandan leaf, and a white layer with coconut.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5243;Grá;USA;Los Angeles;1524 Pizarro St., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.066749;-118.260794;79;false;true;Pizza;There's a welcoming vibe at this hip spot where the focus is on natural fermentation with sourdough pizza, seasonal pickled vegetables, and fermented drinks such as tepache. Grá has indoor and covered patio seating, but all eyes will be on the cooks preparing pizzas in their wood-fired oven. It's all about the thin and crispy sourdough crust with high quality toppings. Classics like pepperoni will always rule, but hard hitters like stracciatella and prosciutto with basil and a drizzle of coffee-infused honey are worth noting. While pizza is certainly the scene stealer, don't ignore their salads or appetizers, including grilled maitake with pickled green peppercorn and agretti in a flavor-packed broth. For dessert, go for the soy-sauce caramel sundae or chocolate tart.;Air conditioning;[]
5244;Cedro Italian Restaurant;USA;Newbury Park;2385 Michael Dr., Newbury Park, 91320, USA;34.1833198;-118.9289546;60;true;true;Italian;Three Italian friends banded together to open this welcoming spot, named for their grandparents' love for cedro, or citron, plants. Don't let the strip mall location fool you—this place is especially inviting, and the food is authentic Italian in both technique and flavor. Skillfully made by hand, pasta dishes rank high. Tagliatelle topped with a ragu sauce, grated parmesan and a drizzle of high-quality olive oil is proof positive that good ingredients and extra care always deliver the best results. Ossobuco served over a bed of saffron risotto is wonderfully tender and flavorful, and sized for sharing. End on a sweet note with their tiramisu or panna cotta—neither will disappoint.;Air conditioning;[]
5246;Coni'Seafood;USA;Inglewood;3544 W. Imperial Hwy., Inglewood, 90303, USA;33.930923;-118.33494;16;true;true;Mexican;This local treasure has been earning accolades since it first opened in 1987. It continues to flourish as a family affair, as the founder’s daughter now runs the show. The front dining room is welcoming, but the enclosed back patio is really the place to be. It's the perfect setting for relishing the kitchen’s Nayarit-style cooking that showcases shrimp and fish imported from Sinaloa. Shrimp appear again and again, perhaps breaded and fried in tacos, or sautéed head-on in a bright red sauce of roasted chilies and beer. Enjoy their fish fried, cooked whole or even inside heaping bowls of ceviche with bracing, lemony flavors and a basket of chips.;Terrace;[]
5248;Ippuku;USA;Berkeley;2130 Center St., Berkeley, 94704, USA;37.87022;-122.26734;43;false;true;Japanese;Can’t swing a ticket to Tokyo? Dinner at Ippuku is the next best thing. With its low Japanese-style tables, extensive woodwork and enormous selection of sake and shochu, it feels like an authentic izakaya transplanted into a corner of downtown Berkeley. The low-profile entrance adds to the feeling that you’ve lucked upon a special dining secret—assuming you don’t stroll right past it, that is.Yakitori is the big draw here, with smoky, salty chicken thighs, necks, hearts and gizzards arriving fresh off the binchotan. Other excellent small plates include korokke, or golden-brown Dungeness crab croquettes, crisp on the outside and with a creamy interior, or yaki-imo, caramelized white sweet potato with a sweet-and-salty glaze.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
5250;Jiang Nan Spring;USA;Alhambra;910 E. Main St., Alhambra, 91801, USA;34.0995473;-118.117454;15;false;false;Chinese, Shanghainese;Shanghai cuisine does not feature the bold, tongue-numbing sensations of Sichuan food or the rowdy energy of a dim sum house filled with roaming carts. It is its own style and celebrated happily so at Jiang Nan Spring. The menu is maddeningly long, but gracious servers are more than eager to point out regional highlights. Their guidance should take you down a road of sweet vinegars and fresh seafood, most apparent in plates like tender chicken with sweet wine sauce as well as an irresistible platter of tilapia fried in a tempura-like batter flavored with seaweed. The oddly named “smoked and fresh pork warm soup” bobbing with knots of bean curd is a sleeper favorite. With hardwood floors and high ceilings, the airy space befits this elegant cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
5251;Cesarina;USA;San Diego;4161 Voltaire St., San Diego, 92107, USA;32.7434966;-117.234556;47;false;true;Italian;Step into this charming trattoria and you’ll instantly feel like part of the famiglia. A glass-walled pastificio provides a behind-the-scenes view of the production—from fusilli to tortelli, while a tableside tiramisu brings the show right to you.There's a warm, boisterous atmosphere here, accented by the hand-painted, mismatched pottery on each table, and a musical Italian lilt will make a glass of Valpolicella all the more enticing. Most of the menu is mix-and-match, with a selection of pasta shapes and sauces that can be paired to your liking (though the friendly servers may nudge you away from a bad combo). Those on a quest for indulgence should look no further than the truffled gnocchi with a cream sauce, served in its own copper pot.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5252;Ciccia Osteria;USA;San Diego;2233 Logan Ave., San Diego, 92113, USA;32.6974548;-117.1388338;61;true;true;Italian, Milanese;Set in a converted home in the heart of Barrio Logan, this adorable osteria is a true family operation—Francesca Penoncelli, who hails from Turin, leads the kitchen with her husband Mario, a Milan native, and both share duties serving tables. The quaint former living room now hosts a deli counter (where your bill will be settled) but tables in the welcoming, tree-lined courtyard are most coveted.Despite their limited space, the kitchen team turns out an impressive menu, with more than a dozen handmade pastas (three of them gluten-free). As a freebie, you’ll get to sample the feather-light focaccia with a spicy, savory mascarpone-ricotta dip, but the decadently cheesy mushroom flan and delicate olive-flecked tuna tartare are well worth their modest prices.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5253;Morning Glory;USA;San Diego;550 W. Date St., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7231471;-117.1681432;28;false;true;American;It's strictly breakfast and brunch only at this Little Italy spot, which isn't however just for the bright-eyed and bushy-tailed. The playful décor may look feminine with its plush booths, pink-and-green marble floors and a champagne vending machine, but look closer and you'll find a few skulls and dark touches. Inside, it's always jumping and there's a wait, so plan ahead.It's all about familiar-seeming favorites and of-the-moment meals—hello, avocado toast and shakshuka. Fluffy soufflé pancakes are worth waking up for, and fried rice with pork belly plus two eggs with runny yolks is a great riff on tradition. The dirty scallop slice is a thick rectangle of potatoes au gratin fried to golden, then doused in rich sausage gravy for next-level enjoyment.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
5254;Corazon Cocina;USA;Santa Barbara;38 W. Victoria St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.4235974;-119.7070638;37;true;true;Mexican, Seafood;The Santa Barbara Public Market is full of alluring eateries, but after your first taste of this charming taco stand, you’ll want to pledge your heart. Chef/owner Ramon Velazquez mastered the craft of handmade tortillas and zesty salsas at the feet of his Guadalajaran mother and grandmother, but he also has a few tricks of his own that often involve additions of delightfully unique local produce.Standouts include a cheesy, griddled taco piled with grilled octopus, white shrimp and avocado, as well as a veggie-packed Oaxaca cheese quesadilla bursting at the seams with confit tomatoes, broccolini, and radishes. Definitely say yes to all three of the different salsas handed out with your order.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5255;Playa;USA;Mill Valley;41 Throckmorton Ave., Mill Valley, 94941, USA;37.9065919;-122.54743;100;false;false;Mexican, Tex-Mex;The foggy beaches of Marin County may be a far cry from the sand and surf of Baja, but this lively spot keeps the vacation vibe alive with margaritas, mezcal and madly delicious Mexican cooking. And while Playa feels upmarket with its colorful tiles, blown-glass lights and walls of windows, its food is wonderfully authentic.The menu makes for tough choices: opt for the outstanding al pastor tacos layered with sweet-spicy caramelized pineapple salsa, or the crispy empanadas stuffed with chorizo, currants and green olives, drizzled with chimichurri. Whether you choose a cocktail and a mushroom-squash blossom quesadilla at the bar or bowls of chips and queso fundido with a big group on the sunny back patio, good times are guaranteed.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5256;New Dumpling;USA;El Cerrito;10064 San Pablo Ave., El Cerrito, 94530, USA;37.9019319;-122.3030479;27;true;false;Chinese, Dumplings;It is definitely all in the name at this vivacious and cheery spot where dumplings are the star of the show. Watch them being made in the open kitchen, then consult the chalkboard for featured menu items. Scallion pancakes and beef noodle soup make an appearance, but press forward to some of the more offbeat items. Peanut salad is tossed with bright celery and crinkle-cut carrot shavings to deliver a wonderful texture and flavorful crunch, but oh those dumplings. Bursting with traditional fillings or more unusual combinations like sweet corn and chicken or scrambled egg and tomato, these delicious parcels are a meal unto themselves with hearty portions rounding out each order.You'll leave pleasantly stuffed with plenty of cash remaining in your wallet.;Air conditioning;[]
5259;Ramen & Tsukemen TAO;USA;Buena Park;10488 Valley View St., Buena Park, 90620, USA;33.8097481;-118.0279443;92;true;false;Japanese, Ramen;This unassuming spot in an easy-to-miss location in an open-air mall belies the wondrous steaming bowls found within. The small dining room with space for 20 is strictly no frills but it's of no concern, since you're here for the soul-stirring comfort food made with passion and dedication. The concise menu features a few appetizers, though ramen clearly steals the show. Spicy red miso ramen is rich and creamy, radiates flavor and bobs with springy noodles, while savory chicken ramen is lighter but equally delicious. White miso, tonkotsu ramen and tsukemen (dipping noodles) are also worthwhile choices. Quite simply, these bowls will inspire future visits. Pork buns round out the utterly satisfying experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
5260;Bee Taqueria;USA;Los Angeles;5754 W. Adams Blvd., Los Angeles, 90016, USA;34.0323899;-118.3689054;98;false;false;Mexican;This casual taqueria with serious focus and creative style arrives courtesy of the talented Chef Alex Carrasco (of Scratch Bar and Osteria Mozza fame). Its setting is simple but sweet, with a string of café lights, handful of covered tables, as well as an open-air courtyard outfitted with picnic tables and a blazing fire pit.Tacos, ceviche and tostadas reign supreme on the menu, which draws culinary inspiration from the chef's childhood in Mexico City. Don’t miss the special tender chicken tacos—starring red mole made from bougainvillea and garnished with purple spinach and shaved red onion. If interested in sampling the full scope of this team's talents, opt for the $50 omakase—a taco-heavy tour of flavor combos pulled from...you guessed it...Mexico City.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5261;El Molino Central;USA;Sonoma;11 Central Ave., Sonoma, 95476, USA;38.315018;-122.481964;28;true;true;Mexican;Lovers of regional Mexican food will swoon for this laid-back charmer, which offers full-throttle fare made with quality ingredients. The colorful little building has a strange layout (order at the counter, then pass through the kitchen to dine on the patio), but it still draws a large following—expect to chat with fellow diners hungry for intel on the day’s best dishes.Entrées shift with the seasons, but the preparations are always expert: try the halibut ceviche with house-made chips or the red mole tamales chockablock with chicken and just a touch of masa. The Bohemia beer-battered fish tacos featuring handmade tortillas are a must, as are the addictive poblano-tomatillo nachos verdes. Of course, spice fans can't get enough of the crispy chilaquiles.;Terrace;[]
5262;Ciccio;USA;Yountville;6770 Washington St., Yountville, 94599, USA;38.406544;-122.36687;89;true;true;Italian, Pizza;A pleasant contrast to the sleek new spots around town, this dining room's country-style curtains and front porch are a ticket to another era—and a hot ticket at that, since tables are hard to come by. Indeed, this Yountville gem could pass off as a John Wayne film set, with its wood-framed, 1916-era grocery look.Blistered, puffy crusts boast a tangy flavor of fermentation and a hint of smoke from the fire, an excellent vehicle for hearty toppings like crispy cabbage leaves paired with thinly sliced pancetta and melty gouda. House-made pasta, like chitarra with 'nduja sausage, clams and pea tendrils, are nearly as enticing, and shareable mains, like a hefty pork chop Milanese, should not be overlooked.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
5263;Fable & Spirit;USA;Newport Beach;3441 Via Lido, Ste. A, Newport Beach, 92663, USA;33.6180361;-117.9286747;77;true;false;Californian, American;With its elegant design and backdrop of the sparkling sea, this "fabled" spot doesn't have to try very hard to win fans. And yet, it never rests solely on its good looks. The room is packed with an unmistakable hum of happy diners diving into delicious pub grub. The comprehensive menu offers up a handful of delicious, inventive vegetable items such as the roasted cauliflower with green harissa, curry caramelized onions and almonds. You'll want to order everything, but don't skip the ambitious but well-executed 12-hour Kurobuta porchetta with polenta, romanesco, Calabrian chili, chimichurri, and textbook-perfect smoked braising jus. Dessert is worth a look, especially when brioche bread pudding with blueberry compote and crème anglaise is on offer.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5264;Flavors from Afar;USA;Los Angeles;5652 Hollywood Blvd., Los Angeles, 90028, USA;34.101489;-118.313252;53;false;false;International;A kitchen on a mission, Flavors from Afar works with refugees, asylum seekers and immigrants to highlight recipes from their native countries. Eritrean, Lebanese, Navajo, Guatemalan, Haitian – the rotation is constant, and the culinary reach of the effort is vast. A recent feature on Indo-Fijian cuisine included a creamy onion and coconut milk stew followed by a finely spiced goat pulao enlivened with cardamom, cloves and star anise. This is authentic homestyle cooking in the best of ways, a spotlight on undiscovered talent and a striking reminder of the many flavors the world has to offer. A portion of proceeds benefit the Tiyya Foundation, which supports immigrants and displaced Indigenous communities.;Air conditioning;[]
5265;Cucina Urbana;USA;San Diego;505 Laurel St., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7312497;-117.160145;61;false;false;Italian;Cucina Urbana, like the other siblings in the Urban Kitchen Group family, is an amiable place that promises a good time. It’s casual, festive and popular with the locals—the kind of spot where nearly every table is filled on a Tuesday afternoon.The California-Italian menu has seasonal offerings, such as a burrata and stone fruit salad, as well as a variety of brick oven pizzas with playful twists, like a pepperoni pizza with Calabrian chili and a honey drizzle. Fresh pastas, including the torchio alla norma with eggplant, chili flakes and ricotta salata with basil, are always a good bet. Wine is available by the bottle at retail price with a corkage fee.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5267;Yank Sing;USA;San Francisco;101 Spear St., San Francisco, 94105, USA;37.79186;-122.39265;33;false;false;Chinese, Dim Sum;Yank Sing is arguably the place in town for dim sum. The upscale setting boasts reasonable prices, and while peak hours entail a wait, one can be assured of quality and abundant variety from these carts rolling out of the kitchen. The signature Peking duck with its crispy lacquered skin and fluffy buns makes for a memorable treat, not unlike the deliciously sweet and salty char siu bao. Of course, dumplings here are the true highlight, and range from fragrant pork xiao long bao to paper-thin har gow concealing chunks of shrimp. Don’t see favorites like the flaky egg custard tarts? Just ask the cheerful staff, who’ll radio the kitchen for help via headsets.;Wheelchair access;[]
5268;Sushi Ran;USA;Sausalito;107 Caledonia St., Sausalito, 94965, USA;37.8587;-122.48576;98;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Chefs have come and gone at this Sausalito staple, but its zen-like atmosphere and exquisite selection of raw fish remain unchanged—and that’s just how the regulars like it. With its charming beachside-bungalow ambience, attentive service staff and thoughtfully curated sake selection, Sushi Ran is as dependable as a restaurant can get.Start off with a small bite like shrimp tempura over crisp veggies, tobiko and asparagus, or a steamed red crab salad mingled with seaweed, cucumber and a sweet soy dressing. Then move on to the main event: meticulously sourced, extraordinarily pure hamachi, big-eye tuna, steamed blue prawns and Santa Barbara uni. Whether you choose sashimi or nigiri, rest assured that these talented chefs will steer you right.;Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
5269;LOLA 55;USA;San Diego;1290 F St., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7138053;-117.1530704;20;true;true;Mexican;There may be plenty of taquerias around town, but this East Village gem is of a slightly different breed. The airy space, with its high ceilings, concrete floors and a full bar with lounge, reads über-cool. However, it’s more than just about good looks—their tacos are what draw the crowds. The variations on offer here lean more sophisticated with creative combinations such as baby carrot adobada and squash blossom relleno. Ribeye carne asada cooked to order on the mesquite wood-burning grill or achiote-rubbed pork belly with grilled pineapple are just some of the winners. Posole verde is comfort in a bowl, while fried masa disks are plain delectable.Remember to save room for the Mexican mole-chocolate ice cream and addictively crunchy churros.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5270;Snail Bar;USA;Oakland;4935 Shattuck Ave., Oakland, 94609, USA;37.8367518;-122.2641856;70;true;false;Contemporary, Californian;Although it would be easy to dismiss this perpetually buzzy spot as just another cooler-than-thou hipster haunt for natural wine, here you'll find some of Oakland's most exciting and well-crafted cooking. Chef Andres Giraldo Florez has worked in some of the world’s loftiest kitchens, and although the vibe here is unfussy, his fine dining chops are evident in every precise, flavorful dish. The concise menu changes frequently, but the namesake gastropod is always on offer, served in-shell, bathed in redolent garlic confit and cashew miso butter, topped with a coin of tangy kumquat. There might not be typical main courses, but guests will have no difficulty filling up on the array of creative small plates, from raw bar offerings to impeccable crudités.;Wheelchair access;[]
5271;Carnes Asadas Pancho Lopez;USA;Los Angeles;3328 Pasadena Ave., Los Angeles, 90031, USA;34.0838939;-118.2134391;98;false;true;Mexican;Humble doesn’t even begin to describe this open-air restaurant, which has no walls and is seemingly built out of corrugated metal. But what comes out of the kitchen is anything but simple. In quiet Lincoln Heights, find a limited menu that excels in tender, stewed meats and soulful soups. The chef mines the memories of his hometown of Jalisco with carne en su jugo, a superb, meaty soup made from tomatillos, bacon, pinto beans and beef. Birria en consommé is another warming, brothy hit, packing in more delicacy and nuance than the typical effort. There must be tacos, of course, and tortillas are properly made in-house. We’re partial to the barbacoa doused in a fiery tomato salsa. All the while, a small staff welcomes you with infectious enthusiasm.;;[]
5272;Eat Joy Food;USA;Rowland Heights;18888 Labin Ct., Rowland Heights, 91748, USA;33.9927537;-117.8907006;31;false;true;Taiwanese;It’s a wonder anybody can find this place. Right off the Pomona Freeway, hidden in the back of a Rowland Heights shopping center stacked with restaurants, this Taiwanese favorite lives up to its name. Soft piano music fills the elegant space, which can be unusually relaxed, almost bordering on peaceful. On smooth warehouse floors, the tables are generously spaced, but the menu is like a tome, dense with a wealth of seafood preparations, delicately flavored consommés and classic rice dishes. Three cup chicken braised with garlic, ginger and basil is an obvious order, as is the fantastic salty fish and chicken fried rice, the grains glossy and puffed in a hot wok. Regulars know to ask about dragon whiskers, a seasonal green that rounds out the meal.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5274;Bansang;USA;San Francisco;1560 Fillmore St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7840269;-122.4327725;18;false;false;Korean, Contemporary;The name references the traditional style of serving a communal Korean meal, which dates back centuries to the Joseon royal court, but there's nothing remotely old-fashioned or stuffy about a meal here. The cooking is an unapologetically contemporary take on Korean cuisine, readily incorporating ingredients like parmesan cheese and chorizo into the likes of kimchi fried rice or crispy rice cakes, fitting together seamlessly beside more classic offerings like mulhwe, a dish of raw seafood with a chilled fermented chili broth. Appropriately, the tapas-style menu is geared toward shared plates, though a starter of sweet-tangy soy lime glazed fried chicken, boasting a craggy, ultra-crunchy exterior and juicy, tender meat, is so good you'll want to discard any idea of sharing.;Wheelchair access;[]
5275;Dija Mara;USA;Oceanside;232 S. Coast Hwy., Oceanside, 92054, USA;33.1936183;-117.3775044;21;true;true;Indonesian, Thai and Vietnamese;This industrial Indonesian eatery is every bit as easy-breezy as its Oceanside hometown—imagine cheeky murals, dim lighting and a roll-up garage door entrance. But lest you consider it a divey drinking hole, be advised you’ll find some serious cooking here. Excellent nasi goreng combines fried rice with shrimp, pork belly, chicken and the yolk of a sunny egg, while charred eggplant with smoked tomato sambal and crispy fried shallots is a textural (and flavor-forward) delight.All that spice is sure to put you in the mood for a drink, and their creative cocktails deliver, with unique low-ABV beverages showcasing house-fermented shrubs and other elixirs. On weekends, brunch is replete with inventive, crowd-pleasing eats, like a chili-lime mango tartine.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
5276;CHAAK Kitchen;USA;Tustin;215 El Camino Real, Tustin, 92780, USA;33.7440783;-117.8237414;70;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;The team behind these stoves swimmingly brings the vibrant smoke- and spice-focused cuisine of the Yucatán Peninsula to life. Of course, that same region's rich and complex history simply means diners can expect nothing less than seriously intriguing cooking. Start off with a mezcal cocktail, customized with tamarind and mole bitters, or Mexican wine, by the glass. From there, spoon up every last drop of the charred habanero salsa that accompanies crisp corn empanadas filled with Oaxacan cheese and epazote. Cochinita pibil is prepared with marinated citrus and achiote, resulting in a tender and flavorful meat that's accompanied with freshly made tortillas. Finish with tarta de mamey with a coconut crust and topped with bee pollen.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5277;Pizzeria Bianco;USA;Los Angeles;1320 E. 7th St., Los Angeles, 90021, USA;34.0363497;-118.240532;41;true;true;Pizza, Italian-American;Those who think Los Angeles can't compete with New York when it comes to pizza obviously haven't been to Pizzeria Bianco. There is a reason long lines snake through ROW DTLA and queue up at the takeout window with diners hankering for a taste of Chef Chris Bianco's pizza. Whether you reserved ahead of time or luck is on your side, there are seats indoors and out, but you could always join the rank and file leaning over boxes while standing nearby (it's that good). There are only a handful of pizze on offer, including the "biancoverde" and the "wiseguy," but their perfect margherita makes your heart skip a beat. An antipasto platter with roasted vegetables, spiedini, salads and sandwiches (at lunch) round out the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5278;peasants FEAST;USA;Solvang;487 Atterdag Rd., Solvang, 93463, USA;34.595557;-120.1419776;43;false;true;American;It may seem impossible to be even more charming than its Solvang surroundings, but peasants FEAST doubles down, and delivers. This daytime-only café from Michael and Sarah Cherney  spotlights the seasons on its sandwich-driven menu. There's nothing ho-hum about what's between the bread here. Instead, the cooking is all heart and the selections show off a unique creativity (cue the pastrami smoked salmon sandwich). A cup of soup is the ideal partner—the carrot soup finished with Calabrian chili oil is a gratifying choice. Specials always deserve a glance, since items like the delectable beet greens grilled cheese appear daily. Dashing off to the next winery? Pop across the street to peasants DELI for picnic-ready rations.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5280;La Azteca;USA;Los Angeles;4538 E. Cesar E Chavez Ave., Los Angeles, 90022, USA;34.0404163;-118.1683741;66;true;true;Mexican;La Azteca is an easy restaurant to find. Just look for the line of people snaking out of its front door. This modest counter-service operation has been serving hefty burritos from East LA for many years now. What’s their secret? Flour tortillas are made in-house every day in full view of the dining room and boast a kind of richness and chew that others don’t. There are nearly 20 different burritos on offer, but everyone comes for the winning chile relleno. The tortilla is cooked on a griddle and then filled—not stuffed—with slivers of sweet poblano peppers and gooey cheese. There’s hot sauce if you want it (you do) and a to-go bag if you need it (you won’t).Tacos and quesadillas are also available but certainly not the main attraction.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5283;Kettner Exchange;USA;San Diego;2001 Kettner Blvd., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7253114;-117.1697261;57;false;true;Contemporary, American Contemporary;Hip, laid-back and a model of design, this indoor-outdoor space is at once many things. Inside, relax with a creative cocktail and bowl of lemon-Dijon popcorn while contemplating the entryway’s reflective blue-glass ceiling, the two-way fireplace and that nest of driftwood hanging from an upper floor. If in the mood for a clubbier scene, head to the rooftop cabana, complete with wet bars, TVs and self-service beer taps—just remember to reserve well in advance.The menu presents dishes from around the globe, such as “ribbons” of bigeye tuna tangled with sliced avocado and much more in a flavorful makrut lime- and soy-marinade. Of course, those plump and tender duck meatballs are an instant classic, set over cheesy grits and smothered in tomato sauce.;Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5284;Taquería El Paisa;USA;Oakland;4610 International Blvd., Oakland, 94601, USA;37.770894;-122.2112574;78;false;true;Mexican;This Oakland institution is widely hailed as the temple of tacos. It is strictly no fuss—no air-conditioning—and no service–order at the counter—but after one bite of their juicy meat, dripping with so much savory goodness that the yellow corn tortillas are doubled up, and it's all worth it. Meat is given the star treatment here, and offal, including tripe and cabeza, are of special note. The suadero, a beef-based, carnitas-style taco, and the seared, crumbled chorizo taco with a distinct smoky flavor, exceed expectations. Good things come in threes, so order another—tender and flavorful carnitas is a sure thing. There is a wide selection of aguas frescas ranging from guava and passion fruit to carrot, or go for the old standby—Mexican Coca-Cola.;Terrace;[]
5285;Soba Ichi;USA;Oakland;2311A Magnolia St., Oakland, 94607, USA;37.81691;-122.28472;91;true;false;Japanese;It takes effort to visit this remarkable little noodle bar, as it’s located in deep industrial West Oakland, open only at dinner and waits can run upwards of 45 minutes—if the designated 100 daily orders of soba don’t sell out first. But rest easy as this delay is happily passed with a drink in the sunny garden, and the warm hospitality rewards the hassle.Handmade Japanese noodles come in two varieties: 100% or 90% buckwheat, served hot or cold in dishes like tenseiro, chewy cold soba with feather-light tempura shrimp and vegetables alongside a flavorful dipping sauce. For something warmer, kamo nanban, a rich broth with tender slices of duck breast, hits the spot. Be sure to sample the sake, served here in the traditional “overflowing” style.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5288;Los Carnalitos;USA;Hayward;30200 Industrial Pkwy. S.W., Hayward, 94544, USA;37.6076735;-122.0645252;77;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;From the symphonic blend of top-quality flavors in the kitchen to the brightly hued dining room walls decked with Aztec-inspired figures, this family-run spot delivers a taste of Mexico City. The two brothers behind this operation, which started as a wildly popular food truck, present delicacies like huaraches and quesadilla de huitlacoche that rarely appear on other menus in town. Here, quesadillas are made from house-made tortillas, so try the one filled with squash blossom, queso fresco and tomatillo salsa. Tortas are a draw at lunch, while the pambazo—with bread dipped in guajillo sauce and then seared—is divine at all times.The $2 tacos featuring tender suadero and al pastor are a delightful surprise, not unlike their selection of agua frescas.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5289;Jon & Vinny’s;USA;Los Angeles;412 N. Fairfax Ave., Los Angeles, 90036, USA;34.0786428;-118.3612687;94;false;false;Italian-American;Jon Shook and Vinny Dotolo opened the original location of this easygoing Italian-American café in 2015, and it’s been busy-busy ever since. The slender room is soaked in sun thanks to the skylights and features a long counter that stretches the length of the open kitchen. The team works the wood-fired grill and blazing oven with ease, the servers are on point, and even after all these years, the food is as charming as ever. There are plenty of pizzas, all of them with lightly charred edges and topped with everything from smoked ham to vodka sauce. But don’t slouch on the rest of the menu, like the refreshing salads packed with veggies or the superb, house-made pastas. Spaghetti limone with breadcrumbs is a recent highlight.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5290;Rocio's Mexican Kitchen;USA;Bell Gardens;7891 Garfield Ave., Bell Gardens, 90201, USA;33.960003;-118.15646;67;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Mexican restaurants are lucky if they can pull off one good mole sauce. Chef Rocio Camacho offers more than 10 great ones in this humble Bell Gardens outpost that has little in the way of décor. Indeed, they don’t call her the "The Goddess of Mole" for nothing. From the dark-as-night Oaxaqueno to the spicy-sweet manchamanteles to the vibrant verde, moles here are layered, sophisticated efforts that come paired with your choice of chicken, fish, shrimp, steak or even a massive chile relleno. On a menu that covers a lot of territory, stick to this signature dish, which arrives overly generous in size. Otherwise, a warm basket of chips laced with a handful of sauces and a plate of zucchini blossom empanadas will position you well for the main event.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5291;Sichuan Impression;USA;Alhambra;235 W. Main St., Ste. B, Alhambra, 91801, USA;34.094301;-118.130072;97;true;true;Chinese, Sichuan;Long hailed as one of the top tables in the area, this Sichuan stalwart is settling into its new home just two miles away from its previous address in Alhambra. All of the usual hits are still in play—tea-smoked duck, big mouth ginger frog, mapo tofu—and the kitchen is still armed with its usual scarlet-red numbing oils and fiery, chopped chilis. One recent highlight was a cauldron of fish and rattan pepper boiled in a thrillingly complex broth rippling with numbing, spicy tones. A private room will serve large parties particularly well. All to say, the airy space, with its big windows and bright lights, is a welcome change that has not come at the expense of the cooking. The restaurant has additional locations in Tustin and West Los Angeles.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5292;Union;USA;Pasadena;37 Union St., Pasadena, 91103, USA;34.1468;-118.14981;15;true;false;Italian;Carb-loading has never been more gratifying. In Old Pasadena, this chef-driven restaurant continues to thrive with locally sourced ingredients and a dazzling selection of boldly prepared pastas, all of which are made in house. For sure, there is nothing timid about this cooking – and many dishes should probably be shared. Consider the stack of roasted market carrots set on smooth labneh and blanketed in Aleppo and honey or the fan favorite, platter-sized spaghetti and meatballs, which comes with garlic bread. Best of all might be the torchetti, a tangle of twisted noodles coated in a rich pork ragu and finished with creamy ricotta and fried rosemary. A golden hue cast from dangling Edison bulbs warms the boxy room stacked with exposed red brick.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5294;Sichuan Home;USA;San Francisco;5037 Geary Blvd., San Francisco, 94118, USA;37.7805117;-122.4736306;26;false;true;Chinese, Sichuan;One of the brightest offerings on Geary Boulevard, Sichuan Home lures diners far and wide. Its spotless dining room is a vision of varnished wood panels and mirrors, with plexiglass-topped tables for easy chili oil clean-up and menus that feature tempting photos of each item. A sampling of the wide-ranging Sichuan cuisine should include the tender lamb chops with a crunchy cumin crust or the pot of Chef's special fish stew heated tableside and served simmering with flavor. For dessert, velvety mango pudding, topped with grapefruit sorbet and fresh pineapple, is a tropical treat.Need a little guidance? The friendly staff's recommendations are always on point and they're also especially accommodating to families with young children.;Wheelchair access;[]
5295;Flores;USA;San Francisco;2030 Union St., San Francisco, 94123, USA;37.7975502;-122.4326948;99;false;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;It’s always a fiesta at this lively spot on Cow Hollow’s main drag, where you’re as likely to find young families sharing a bowl of guac as you are Marina girls getting tipsy on mezcal margaritas. Patterned tiles, bright murals and chill beats create a modern vibe, and though you may have to wait (only limited reservations are available), the friendly staff will make it worth your while.Flores is among the city’s best upscale Mexican spots—with the bonuses of heftier portions and a lower price tag. You’ll be able to taste the difference in the handmade corn tortillas that encase an oozy huitlacoche quesadilla, and the tender, citrusy carnitas. Save room for churros: the spicy “Mexican hot chocolate” dipping sauce is well worth the calories.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5296;Kismet;USA;Los Angeles;4648 Hollywood Blvd., Los Angeles, 90027, USA;34.1002978;-118.2907005;73;false;true;Middle Eastern;This enduringly hip Los Feliz favorite is best experienced with friends, but we can’t help feeling a tiny bit selfish when the chicken and pine nut pies wrapped in flaky phyllo arrive or when oyster mushroom skewers with a creamy onion and cashew sauce land on the table. And the Persian crispy rice with egg yolks? Do we have to share this one too? Such is the enduring charm of this Middle Eastern hotspot that prioritizes seasonal vegetables and bright flavors. Nothing feels heavy, ever, and even the most familiar of ingredients can surprise. The staff is equally charming, as cool as the cucumbers with rosewater labneh. Truly, in that eternal quest to find the quintessential neighborhood restaurant, Kismet meets the mark with flying colors.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
5297;LaoXi Noodle House;USA;Arcadia;600 Live Oak Ave., Arcadia, 91006, USA;34.10907;-118.01802;47;false;true;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;The beauty of dining at this noodle house is that you don’t have to guess what they’re good at—the menu is brief, and everything you really need to know is in the name. But, their eight tables fill quickly so plan ahead.This kitchen focuses entirely on slinging noodles inspired by the cuisine of China’s famed Shanxi Province, so start with a chilled bowl of these gelatinous strands slathered with sesame-peanut sauce and the tingling heat of house-made chili oil. Then move on to the slender “wife special” noodles, with their springy, toothsome texture mixing with bits of crisped pork belly and fermented soy sauce. While dumplings are absolutely worth the order, also keep room for savoring some of the chef’s special fried noodles.;Air conditioning;[]
5298;Maccheroni Republic;USA;Los Angeles;332 S. Broadway, Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.050137;-118.248726;50;false;true;Italian-American, American;With its tall mirrors, tiled walls and tin ceilings, this rustic Italian eatery is every inch the classic trattoria. Hidden in plain sight just across from Grand Central Market, it is a known quantity with the local crowd, who fill these tables at all times of day. A few bites, and you'll be ready to pledge allegiance to the Republic, too.The array of excellent handmade pastas is seemingly endless, like long, tubular strands of bigoli della nonna, headlinng an impeccably balanced angus-and-sausage ragout. Then, try to pry yourself away from the noodle nexus and savory tomato-based sauces to savor freshly baked olive oil bread, deliciously paired with bites of polpettine di gamberi. Be sure to finish with a creamy affogato and be on your merry way.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5299;Mariscos Jalisco;USA;Pomona;753 E. Holt Ave., Pomona, 91767, USA;34.0628203;-117.7354583;25;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;When Raul Ortega started his taco truck in Boyle Heights back in 2001, he probably had no idea just how hard the city would fall for him. Today his Jalisco-inspired tacos have become a rite of passage, and he now runs a number of trucks around town, not to mention this modest but cherished spot in Pomona.The menu is the same everywhere, limited to tostadas piled with various lime-kissed ceviches. Inside tip: opt for his signature fried shrimp taco tinged with spicy salsa and creamy avocado slices. It's an unequaled version, complete with a crunchy shell that collapses like tempura, as well as a rich and savory filling. First-time customers start with a single order, while regulars get right to business with a whole plate of them.;Air conditioning;[]
5300;Village Sake;USA;Fairfax;19 Bolinas Rd., Fairfax, 94930, USA;37.986614;-122.58903;21;true;true;Japanese;Set along a bustling stretch, Village Sake is a mighty hot and mod izakaya delivering authentic goods in the heart of quaint Fairfax. All the classic small plates are in full force here: crisp and creamy takoyaki (octopus croquettes), okonomiyaki, tataki (made with silky smoked hamachi) and coconut mochi cake complete with cardamom gelato. If you must have sushi, there’s a small selection of excellent nigiri, too—make sure to sample the shima aji and kinmedai.The look of the room suggests Tokyo, with closely spaced tables, an array of wood accents (including a live-edge wood counter) as well as a friendly staff, many of them Japanese natives. This is a popular spot that doesn’t take reservations, so expect long lines, especially on weekends.;Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5301;Okane;USA;San Francisco;669 Townsend St., San Francisco, 94103, USA;37.770634;-122.403015;15;true;true;Japanese, Izakaya;Can’t afford to indulge in the exquisite sushi at Omakase? Consider heading to its next-door little sib, where the fish is still top-notch (it’s all sourced from Japan) but the atmosphere is more laid-back. Okane draws lots of nearby Adobe and Zynga employees at lunch and big groups at dinner, all sharing bottles of sake and making the most of the small-plates menu.Sushi is, of course, a must: the nigiri is pristine and delicious, as are more Americanized rolls like the Harajuku (filled with shrimp tempura, avocado and salmon and topped with tuna, eel sauce and lotus root chips). But don’t sleep on the non-sushi dishes—cod marinated in sake lees is grilled to perfection, and broiled salmon aburi with avocado and ikura is delicious too.;Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
5302;Outerlands;USA;San Francisco;4001 Judah St., San Francisco, 94122, USA;37.7604361;-122.5050059;59;true;true;Californian;On the fringes of the city, this charmingly rustic salvaged wood retreat is a beloved neighborhood stalwart. Noteworthy above all for baking some of the best bread in the city, sourdough devotees are known to make the pilgrimage from far and wide to partake in the crusty, mahogany-hued levain, served in thick slices with house-cultured butter (loaves are also available to purchase). Beyond the obligatory bread, the small seasonal menu features commendable ingredients served in a simple, hearty style that allows their quality to shine, whether its roasted chicken with market vegetables, or a slow-cooked ragu Bolognese with springy tagliatelle. On weekends, brunch follows a similar formula, with the addition of excellent pastries like a signature sticky bun.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
5304;Luscious Dumplings;USA;Monrovia;919 W. Duarte Rd., Monrovia, 91016, USA;34.1319451;-118.0185111;63;false;true;Chinese;It’s hard to order poorly at this delightful retreat, formerly called Luscious Dumplings. The menu is concise, with half of the items dedicated to the eponymous specialty. Indeed this narrow hot spot has been a city-wide favorite since it opened in 2001, and continues to draw lines so long that servers leave a sign-in sheet outside. The secret to their success? Discipline. While many spots make dumplings ahead of time and freeze them, this kitchen starts fresh every morning.It’s best to begin slow with a tray of boiled pork and celery jiaozi—the wrapping smooth to the touch and boasting just the right amount of bite. Anything pan-fried, though, is the main draw. From juicy pork to fresh chives, these little parcels of goodness have few equals.;Air conditioning;[]
5306;Trestle;USA;San Francisco;531 Jackson St., San Francisco, 94133, USA;37.796303;-122.40457;25;false;true;Contemporary, Californian;In SF's dizzyingly expensive dining landscape, this hot spot offering a three-course menu for under $40, is an incredible steal—provided you’re willing to sacrifice freedom of choice. The two options for each course spin with the season: your repast may feature a creamy heirloom tomato soup with thyme oil, followed by fork-tender short ribs atop luscious parmesan polenta and spigarello—with a final touch of frozen chocolate parfait garnished with crushed cashews.For those with appetite to spare, an additional pasta course (like ziti al forno with dry-aged beef ragù and gremolata topping) can be added for a small supplement. Throw in a lively atmosphere and friendly service to this already alluring deal, and the value proposition is nearly irresistible.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5307;Khom Loi;USA;Sebastopol;7385 Healdsburg Ave., Sebastopol, 95472, USA;38.405194;-122.8300766;69;false;false;Thai;Is anyone surprised that the team behind Ramen Gaijin has another hit on their hands? The chefs here have traveled extensively throughout the Thai regions, which in turn inspired them to bring a taste of Chiang Mai to Sebastopol. For sure, anyone looking for the sweeter, Americanized side of Thai cooking is in for an awakening. This is food that is spiced and seasoned with little hesitation, and fresh and electric at the same time. The house-made Thai sausage, for instance, is superb—grilled and served with a fiery green chili dip. The paste for all the curries are also made in house, with our favorite being the green curry with Manila clams and potatoes.The space, too, is stunning, thanks to lofty ceilings, bamboo lanterns, and a tranquil pond.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5308;Longo Seafood;USA;Rosemead;7540 Garvey Ave., Rosemead, 91770, USA;34.0625014;-118.1047332;99;false;true;Chinese, Dim Sum;The parking lot is likely full and you may have to wait for a seat, but this efficient Cantonese parlor is more than capable of handling its crowds, which haven’t let up since day one. Adding to the buzz of this bright dining room is a massive TV that runs down the length of the wall, as well as a host of keen-eyed servers roaming the restaurant floor.The absence of dim sum carts doesn’t always guarantee quality, but plates turned out of this kitchen are both small and large, freshly prepared and appropriately hot. Golden-brown skewers of sugarcane shrimp, plump orbs of pork siu mai, and fluffy steamed buns filled with chicken and dried scallops all delight. Best of all though may be the rice noodle rolls flecked with barbecue pork or shrimp.;Air conditioning;[]
5309;Yue Huang;USA;Sacramento;3860 Truxel Rd., Sacramento, 95834, USA;38.6380533;-121.5040297;83;false;true;Chinese, Cantonese;Surrounded by a number of standard-issue chain eateries in a Natomas shopping center, this Cantonese restaurant is a hidden treasure. On weekend mornings, Chinese families pack the oversized tables for a spectrum of exquisitely prepared dim sum. Evenings however bring groups of friends eager to sample succulent seafood sourced from the massive live tanks that line this restaurant’s back wall.Over on the menu, the dim sum selection features the standard array of steamed, baked and fried delights, including barbecue pork buns, rice noodle rolls, and dumplings. However, diners are bound to also run across a range of more interesting items, like succulent sticky-rice shrimp balls or steamed buns stuffed with crunchy walnuts and sweet red bean paste.;Car park;[]
5310;Glen Ellen Star;USA;Glen Ellen;13648 Arnold Dr., Glen Ellen, 95442, USA;38.36429;-122.5245;42;true;false;Californian, Pizza;The country charm of this quaint cottage belies the level of culinary chops that will impress even a hardened city slicker. With knotty pine tables, well-worn plank floors and a wood-burning oven, this beloved space buzzes with action the moment their doors open.The menu leans Italian, and Chef Ari Weiswasser ensures that every plate packs a serious punch. Wood-roasted vegetables are a particular strength and even worth building a meal around. Golden beets finished with blood orange oil, or a charred head of cauliflower with tahini and almonds are not to be missed. Daily pizzas like the tomato-cream pie with Turkish chilies are also a thrill. Save room for house-made ice cream in flavors like vanilla maple Bourbon, salted peanut butter or peach verbena.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5311;Maligne;USA;Seaside;600 Broadway Ave., Seaside, 93955, USA;36.6092353;-121.8505232;91;false;true;Californian;The name means “clever” or “cunning,” but you don’t have to be a particularly sharp tool to appreciate the ample charms of this hip, easygoing Seaside gem. The staff is effortlessly hospitable, and the breezy space has a chic loft aesthetic, but it’s the cooking that really makes this place a coup de coeur. The menu draws on Italian-American and French classics (think chicken parm and asparagus with hollandaise), but the feel is thoroughly Californian, with a light, contemporary touch and spectacular local ingredients that make even all-too familiar dishes like Caesar salad memorable—a testament to Chef Klaus Georis’s extensive experience in fine dining. To drive home the point, finish with a spot-on tarte tatin, served warm with softly whipped cream.;;[]
5312;Pollo a la Brasa;USA;Los Angeles;764 S. Western Ave., Los Angeles, 90005, USA;34.0580003;-118.3090295;44;false;false;Peruvian;Peruvian in Koreatown? You bet, at least at this family-owned and run spot that has been at it for more than thirty years. Expect a casual neighborhood restaurant that's a touch warm on the inside from the heat of the live-fire cooking. All of the chicken is cooked over a wood fire that you can smell a block away and delivers smoky meat with a crispy skin that's marinated with their family secret. While there are a few options on the menu, make sure that you order the chicken by itself, or choose from their sides, but don't skip their twice-fried French fries and consider ordering a second container of their spicy green aji sauce.The wait times can be a bit long, so call ahead for take-out or wait patiently.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5313;Jo's Modern Thai;USA;Oakland;3725 MacArthur Blvd., Oakland, 94619, USA;37.79179;-122.1988979;87;false;false;Thai, Californian;The path to this Laurel District hotspot began when owner Kao Saelee, an Oakland native with Thai roots, first introduced his wife Jo to the cuisine, and it’s precisely that spirit of cultural exchange you’ll find embodied here. The menu, designed by Chef Intu-On Kornnawong, displays the bold, balanced flavors typical of Thai cuisine, but isn’t overly concerned with hewing to tradition. That creative, irreverent approach is exemplified in dishes like a signature take on drunken noodles, which features smoky barbecue brisket, or a pork burger seasoned to resemble the complex herbaceous flavors of laab. Diners with delicate palates, fret not: the kitchen offers varying levels of spice. Choose from the unique, mouthwatering cocktail list to round out the meal.;;[]
5315;Yafa;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;Junipero St., Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93923, USA;36.55702;-121.92013;60;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Middle Eastern;This clear hit among locals has even spread to tourists—everyone comes back time and again. The owners bring hospitality to a new level, thanks to a jovial greeting and warm farewells that may involve a hug from the owner.The smell of roasting meats entices passersby with the promise of their excellent kebabs, like deliciously charred yet tender chicken skewered with tomatoes. The Aleppo kafta, combining ground beef and lamb, is richly seasoned and perfectly paired with a side of zippy tzatziki. Be sure to begin any meal with an enormous plate of their mezze, heaped with minty cucumber and tomato salad, hummus as well as a sundried tomato- and feta-dip for scooping up with warm and fluffy pita.Weekends bring a host of live music performances.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5316;A16;USA;San Francisco;2355 Chestnut St., San Francisco, 94123, USA;37.7999626;-122.4421573;80;true;false;Pizza, Italian;Families and tourists alike flock to A16, known for rustic Italian cooking and a vast selection of delicious, unusual wines from all over the boot. Reservations for dinner are a must, especially if you want one of the prime counter seats facing the open kitchen and wood-burning pizza oven. The menu’s pies, pastas, and antipasti shift seasonally, though the maccaronara with ragu napoletana is a staple. Opt for the Vesuvio, a smoky, savory, and spicy pizza topped with tomato, soppressata, scamorza, caciocavallo, and chili. For dessert, look no further than the fig crostata with vanilla gelato. Craving something sweet? Choose from a tempting array including chocolate tart, tiramisu, and panna cotta, as well as house-made gelato and sorbet.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
5317;Izakaya Rintaro;USA;San Francisco;82 14th St., San Francisco, 94103, USA;37.76858;-122.415115;99;false;true;Japanese, Izakaya;Delicate izakaya cuisine with a produce-centric NorCal sensibility awaits at this Japanese sanctum, where wood-framed booths crafted from redwood wine casks and a Hinoki cedar bar create a serene setting.The kitchen transforms even the most humble dishes into works of art. Starters like teba no karaage, or crispy chicken wings with tangy sansho pepper, are perfect for sharing, while Teishoku lunch sets are consistently good. Freshly made soft tofu is infused with fragrant bergamot peel, while meaty king trumpet mushrooms join classic chicken thighs and tender tsukune on the menu of smoky, caramelized charcoal-grilled skewers. The blancmange, infused with white sesame and topped with sweet black soybeans, is particularly unmissable.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5318;Chengdu Taste;USA;Alhambra;828 W. Valley Blvd., Alhambra, 91803, USA;34.078;-118.13248;24;true;true;Chinese, Sichuan;Some Sichuan kitchens temper their heat levels depending on what they think the customer can handle. Not this one. This long-standing veteran has never been one to hold anyone’s hand and their widespread success has not at all cooled their approach. Expect nothing less than the full-throttle Sichuan experience where tongue-numbing, lip-tingling dishes arrive coated in heavy spices, garnished with sliced chilis and, often, doused in fire-engine red chili oil. Toothpick lamb is the house signature, but the crispy-crusted beef is a formidable rival. Fish with mom’s preserved chili sauce is unapologetically sinus-clearing. Even vegetables like the arden lettuce are a powerhouse of stir-fried garlic excellence. Swing by for lunch to avoid the lines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5319;Pine & Crane;USA;Los Angeles;1521 Griffith Park Blvd., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.0904961;-118.2772213;41;true;false;Asian, Taiwanese;Find this laid-back little café opposite the pedestrian plaza, Sunset Triangle. The dining room itself is triangular as well as hipster-friendly with a rustic blend of exposed brick, concrete floors and varnished wood tables.As casual as the vibe may seem, this is a serious kitchen dedicated to Asian cuisine. Be sure to try their vegetarian variations on classics such as pork-free mapo tofu, daikon dumplings and daily specials like the lotus root or seaweed salad. However, the cooking truly shines with Taiwanese specialties. The three-cup jidori chicken is its own simmering feast in a clay pot of dark meat with equal parts soy, sesame oil and rice wine reduced to a deep brown glaze, then studded with chopped green onion, dried chilies and whole garlic.;Air conditioning;[]
5320;Sama Sama Kitchen;USA;Santa Barbara;1208 State St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.4236674;-119.7045301;32;false;false;Asian;This eatery in the heart of downtown is not only good fun but also good for the wallet. Here, the Chefs/partners bring their disparate expertise—one is a barbecue aficionado from Nashville, the other is Indonesian, and together they turn out a menu of thoroughly pleasing Southeast Asian food. Attractions include a well-spiced rendition of green papaya salad, mixing aromatic herbs, chilies and peanuts. Bao can be ordered fried or steamed, which yields a pillowy soft bun to be filled with crunchy fried chicken in a tangy sauce.The interior is appealingly simple, but the back patio is a hidden gem, filled with string lights and communal tables that can be booked for parties. Weekday happy hour simply means steep discounts on a variety of food and drinks.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5321;Moo's Craft Barbecue;USA;Los Angeles;2118 N. Broadway, Los Angeles, 90031, USA;34.0733517;-118.2183724;68;true;true;Barbecue, Regional Cuisine;High school sweethearts Andrew and Michelle Muñoz are living a dream come true. What started out as a backyard hobby smoking meats on weekends has transformed into a full-fledged restaurant in Lincoln Heights. Longtime fans will be happy to know that the handsome space, equipped with a bar packed with craft beer, hasn’t affected what the Muñozs' do best. Smoky, salt-and-pepper-crusted brisket and snappy, spicy sausages packed with cheddar and jalapeños pay homage to the barbecue traditions of Austin, Texas. Sides like Mexican street corn or tres leches bread pudding are a nod to their heritage. Altogether, this is the kind of food that demands a post-meal nap. And just as it was in the beginning, there is always a line stretching out the front door.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5322;Heritage Barbecue;USA;San Juan Capistrano;31721 Camino Capistrano, San Juan Capistrano, 92675, USA;33.5014781;-117.6628795;93;true;true;Barbecue, Regional Cuisine;Barbecue is a veritable religion in America, and chefs in this realm have a near cultish way of doing things. With that in mind, consider this SJC bijou, packed to the gills with focused diners and trays of smoky meat.Punctuality is of the essence as everyone is here, early and eager, for Chef/owner Daniel Castillo's food. His creations draw inspiration from central Texas, so when that sweet scent of California white oak gets going, find yourself transported on a riotous journey, starting with slices of glistening brisket—correctly charred and deliciously rich. Add on a side of chili with more brisket along with a cheddar-jalapeño biscuit and never look back again. Don't forget to save room for desserts like banana pudding or pineapple upside down cake.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
5323;Mentone;USA;Aptos;174 Aptos Village Way, Aptos, 95003, USA;36.9789673;-121.8995341;31;false;false;Italian, Californian;Culinary devotees flock to Aptos for its deluxe food spots, boutique coffee shops, and supermarkets aplenty. Jumping on the bandwagon is this delicious operation with a single mission—to churn out the most memorable and addictive pizzas in town.Soft hues, dark green-framed doors, and a barn-like structure foster a communal sense. The carte is unusual, unveiling fried sardines with Meyer lemon aïoli or white bean soup with chickpeas in a prosciutto broth. Taking the cake however are pizzas, like the "Pesto" shimmering with fromage blanc, Crescenza, and caciocavallo, or Sardenaira with tomato sauce, anchovies, and olives. If great pizza is the stuff of dreams, you may want to skip the house-made pistachio ice cream. But, is that a risk worth taking?;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5324;Pizzana;USA;Los Angeles;11712  San Vicente Blvd., Los Angeles, 90049, USA;34.053474;-118.46568;86;true;true;Italian, Pizza;Every pizza at this area darling begins with a nod to Neapolitan tradition: start with the perfect dough and bake it into a crust that remains crisp and light right through the middle. This careful process and that almighty oven shipped from Italy can be observed with longing through the glass-walled kitchen. The dining room also conjures the homeland through Mediterranean-blue murals and furnishings.To top that crust, many pizzas go on to include premium ingredients like San Marzano tomatoes and fior di latte, which arrives several times a week from Italy. Alternatively, deck your pie with a more creative and locally minded blend of embellishments. A choice of appetizers, gourmet salads and luscious desserts round out the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5325;Mabel’s Gone Fishing;USA;San Diego;3770 30th St., San Diego, 92104, USA;32.7467636;-117.1301426;63;true;true;Seafood, Californian;Charm is in abundant supply at this popular gathering place, from the name and décor (both of which honor an owner's beloved dog) to the easygoing, friendly staff. But it's more than just window dressing that draws in the crowds. A focused menu highlights excellent local seafood with a simple-yet-satisfying approach that blends Californian and Iberian cuisine, and the results are undeniably delicious. Case in point is the crispy, meaty swordfish schnitzel, served with salsa verde and creamy tonnato sauce alongside a salad of caper berries and shaved fennel, for a winningly bright, briny combination. Raw items like oysters and simple crudos are a great way to start, and an assortment of natural wines and gin-based cocktails provide top-notch accompaniments.;Wheelchair access;[]
5326;China Village;USA;Albany;1335 Solano Ave., Albany, 94706, USA;37.89083;-122.291214;98;false;true;Chinese, Sichuan;It takes a village to feed a big group, and this laid-back spot is a favorite with families. A stylish makeover featured a sleek front bar, contemporary chandeliers and dramatic Chinese art, but one look at the scorching-hot menu options—think spicy Sichuan frog and flaky sautéed fish with pickled chili peppers—confirms the authenticity factor.Skip the Hunan, Mandarin and Cantonese offerings in favor of the Sichuan specialties like dry-fried, bone-in chicken laced with ground chilies and numbing peppercorns. And be sure to order the five-spice hot and spicy pork shoulder. A house specialty, this mouthwatering dish is fork- (or chopstick) tender and rests atop a deliciously piquant chili-oil jus with baby bok choy, scallions and garlic.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5327;Sea Harbour;USA;Rosemead;3939 Rosemead Blvd., Rosemead, 91770, USA;34.07984;-118.0733;80;false;false;Chinese, Dim Sum;This highly regarded Cantonese restaurant could easily glide solely on its reputation, and yet, its devoted chefs bring the goods again and again. One of the first of its kind to offer dim sum à la carte, rather than by an actual cart, items arrive piping hot, fresh from the steamer. You really can’t go wrong here, as each is more inventive than the next, flaunting ace flavor and wondrous texture. Bigger plates are all the rage at night—including sweet and sour pork, which finds elevation in this trusty kitchen's hands.Anything with seafood is a sure bet, but don’t miss the preserved salty egg bun with molten yolk. Families can be seen digging into steamed rice noodle rolls studded with bitter melon, or fried durian pastries oozing with the warm fruit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5328;Dha Rae Oak;USA;Los Angeles;1106 S. Western Ave., Los Angeles, 90006, USA;34.05054;-118.309;32;true;true;Korean, Duck Specialities;It’s all about the duck—whole roasted in a clay pot—at this dining delight. And, since the very best things take time, seat-of-the-pants types must know that this platter requires a bit of of planning: order at least a day in advance. However, upon entering this Koreatown gem, one may look forward to being rewarded with a generously portioned dish to dream about for weeks. Stuffed with chestnuts, sweet potatoes, rice and herbs, then wrapped and roasted for hours, the bronzed beauty is plated before your eyes. A spicy dipping sauce and light broth with greens elevates the preparation to epic heights. There's no better way to enjoy this festive feast than with a group, but walk-ins can savor the signature smoked treat, as it's available at all hours.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5329;Phở 79;USA;Garden Grove;9941 Hazard Ave., Garden Grove, 92844, USA;33.7527059;-117.9556132;44;false;true;Vietnamese, Noodles;If you are no stranger to the slurp, then Phở 79 is likely already on your circuit. After all, this place is an institution. Opened in the early 80s, it's widely considered to ladle some of the best and most praiseworthy pho in southern California.The simple interior is enlivened by a bright yellow wall adorned with numerous accolades. It's spartan but clean, and you're here for the pho, not the fashion show. Place your name on the clipboard by the front door and expect a wait. Once seated, peruse the extensive menu, which runs the gamut from egg noodle soups and goi cuon, to appetizers and desserts along with many varieties of the eponymous dish. You'll never go wrong with oxtail—it's the most popular with good reason.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5330;Adana Restaurant;USA;Glendale;6918 San Fernando Rd., Glendale, 91201, USA;34.173664;-118.29869;56;true;true;Middle Eastern;Note: This restaurant is temporarily closed.Come with a group and order with abandon. The food here is so good that it will be hard to hold back. This dining room manages to be both modest and ornate, filled with large round tables covered in purple linen, alongside walls of gold-framed photos and murals. The vibe is so open and friendly that you might see cheese plates being enthusiastically shared among neighboring diners.The cooking is as honest as the servers, who are happy to direct you on how to order best. Dolmeh and chicken kebabs with stewed sour cherries and an irresistible yogurt sauce are the kind of dishes one can imagine eating every day of the week. Fattoush made with crunchy vegetables, verdolagas and dressed in a lemony dressing sprinkled with sumac spells of garden goodness.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5331;Bombera;USA;Oakland;3459 Champion St., Oakland, 94602, USA;37.7994488;-122.215069;87;true;true;Mexican, Californian;Fire provides the central motif for this boisterous community staple, from the venue itself (a former fire station) to the name (Spanish for fire woman), all the way to a crackling wood-fired oven that not only animates the kitchen, but also provides ash used to nixtamalize corn for house-made masa. All of this seems perfectly fitting for Chef Dominica Rice-Cisneros, whose passion has helped to shape Oakland's current Mexican restaurant scene, combining a locavore pedigree and fine dining chops with a respect for the generational knowledge of heritage cooking. The single best illustration might be a dish of beautifully rendered duck leg confit, paired with a delightfully complex, nutty mole verde, just-right black beans and handmade blue corn tortillas.;;[]
5333;Dumpling Home;USA;San Francisco;298 Gough St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.7759271;-122.4227056;32;true;false;Chinese, Dumplings;You can try the pan-fried baos, poke at the crispy green onion pancakes and sample the hand-pulled noodles, but please, read the room—and the awning that wraps around the building. This casual eatery excels in the delicate art of soup dumplings, which arrive with supple skins and spoonfuls of delicious broth far clearer and more distilled than most. From open till close, chefs in the back wrap and fold everything by hand, and unlike most kitchens that are content to offer just a typical pork variety, fillings here include chicken, beef, and our favorite, a Sichuan-inspired numbing pork.A prime corner location in the Theater District lures in the crowds, who clearly work up an appetite by walking by table after table of bamboo steamers stacked to the sky.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5335;Liu's Cafe;USA;Los Angeles;3915 1/2 W. 6th St., Los Angeles, 90020, USA;34.0635942;-118.3085796;89;false;false;Chinese, Taiwanese;Liu's Cafe is just the sort of casual spot you'll come to again and again. Arrive early, as seats fill quickly, then order at the wood counter, where you'll get a sneak peek into the bustling kitchen. You'll also spy their selection of pastries, which definitely shouldn't be overlooked. Order the house-made pork wontons for a tender, tasty treat, and be sure to get the extra egg noodles to soak up that wonderfully kicky chili oil. Braised pork belly rice is another dish of pure comfort, and no matter what you have, everything is complemented by a pot of tea, such as the milk oolong. Finally, the pastries grab attention from the very beginning and closing out with a dessert like the citrus curd tart with shaved fennel salad is everything you want it to be.;Air conditioning;[]
5336;Loquita;USA;Santa Barbara;202 State St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.4140993;-119.6916636;25;false;false;Spanish;Loquita is located just blocks from the beach and inside a cream-tinted building with a red-tiled roof. Small and stylish, the space oozes with creative flair—picture colorful tiles, a humming bar framed by soft pink stools, and starburst light fixtures. Find a perch at the beloved wood counter or outside in the inviting and attractive patio. Servers know the menu by heart, so follow their lead and start with tapas like crusty pan con tomate, before digging into hearty chorizo y pollo paella. An homage to the El Bullí olive is a contemporary signature, while carpaccio garnished with pickled mustard seeds and aged sherry vinegar is fittingly popular.A separate gin and tonic list, complete with iterations of the classic, makes a great kickoff (and sendoff).;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5337;Stockhome;USA;Petaluma;220 Western Ave., Petaluma, 94952, USA;38.2333616;-122.6427194;47;false;true;Scandinavian;Halfway across the globe, the husband-and-wife team of Roberth and Andrea Sundell have brought the flavors of their native Stockholm to their adopted hometown, Petaluma. This cheery, minimal spot plays all the hits: pickled herring, hearty meatballs and house-made sodas (try the subtly sweet sea buckthorn). Heavy Mid-Eastern and light California touches still manage to creep in, as seen in the skagen—a classic dill-shrimp salad that adds avocado to the mix, or farm-fresh berries atop giant pancakes. For the hardcore herring haters, the menu also flaunts tasty nods to Sweden’s Middle Eastern community by way of falafel, tabbouleh and a terrific beef-lamb pita wrap.Jars of black licorice and bulks of other Swedish candies are available for daily binging.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5338;Ramen Gaijin;USA;Sebastopol;6948 Sebastopol Ave., Sebastopol, 95472, USA;38.4023896;-122.8236124;29;false;false;Japanese, Ramen;“Gaijin” is the none-too-polite Japanese term for a foreigner, but the American chefs of this noodle joint clearly take pride in their outsider status, fusing local ingredients with traditional technique. It's surely one of the best bowls of ramen around, and you can smell the soup before you're even past the front door.The best seats are at the counter, where you can chat with the chef as he assembles bowls of light, fresh shoyu ramen filled with thick house-made rye noodles and caramelized pork belly chashu. Appetizers are also notable, like the karaage: crunchy-coated, tender chicken thighs with miso ranch. Desserts, such as the black-sesame ice cream over miso-salted caramel, matcha meringue and coconut flakes, mix sweet and savory for the win.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5339;Frank Fat’s;USA;Sacramento;806 L St., Sacramento, 95814, USA;38.5785995;-121.4968009;24;true;true;Chinese;Celebrated as the “third house” because of its popularity among politicians making deals in the back booths, this venerable Chinese-American jewel has been family owned since 1939. Step inside and you'll be transported into another era by way of a retro bar serving up happy-hour martinis and an elegant dining room attended to by tie-wearing servers and festooned with valuable relics.The menu is as much of a throwback as the décor, with yu kwok (crispy beef, pork and water chestnut dumplings) sharing equal billing with not-so-Chinese items, including banana cream pie. But don’t be dissuaded by the seeming inauthenticity as everything is beautifully executed, from the fried chicken marinated with brandy and ginger to addictive garlic-chili green beans.;Wheelchair access;[]
5341;Pausa;USA;San Mateo;223 E. 4th Ave., San Mateo, 94401, USA;37.5645894;-122.3220038;88;false;true;Italian, Regional Cuisine;Thanks to its modern setting and late hours (by San Mateo standards, at least), a growing crowd of smart couples and tech types flock to this San Mateo sweetie. Everyone is here for the authentic Italian eats from Chef/co-owner Andrea Giuliani, who dishes up the cuisine of his native Veneto.The dining room has a view of the charcuterie-aging room and those artistically presented salumi boards of fennel-flecked finocchiona and exceptional salame al parmigiano. The wood-fired Neapolitan pizzas are equally strong—try the porchetta variation, topped with gorgonzola and radicchio. Of course, the pastas don’t disappoint either: spinach spaghetti amatriciana with house-cured guanciale, piennolo tomatoes, calabrian chilies, and pecorino is downright perfect.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5342;Millennium;USA;Oakland;5912 College Ave., Oakland, 94618, USA;37.847427;-122.252075;97;false;true;Vegan;After more than 20 years in San Francisco, this vegan paradise relocated to Oakland, where it’s continuing to put out some of the most unique, delicious plant-based cuisine in the country. This rustic-chic space is laid-back and unfussy, with lots of dark wood, a patio for alfresco dining and a crowd of young families and professionals attended by welcoming servers.While dedicated vegans are sure to swoon, even hardcore carnivores might reconsider the lifestyle after a dose of Chef/owner Eric Tucker’s culinary creativity, showcased best on a five-course “Taste of Millennium” menu. Roasted pumpkin tamales with pumpkin seed pastor and cashew nut crema are knockouts, as are the crunchy king trumpet fritters with chili-persimmon jam.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5343;Lunasia Dim Sum House;USA;Alhambra;500 W. Main St., Alhambra, 91801, USA;34.09258;-118.13225;90;true;false;Chinese, Dim Sum;Few kitchens can prepare a noodle roll quite like this local Alhambra favorite. Rice wrappers filled with gently cooked lobster meat and finished with a subtly sweet soy sauce arrive on a platter set with the lobster shell itself for a presentation that draws attention from all corners. Indeed, this kitchen puts a fine edge on the area’s dim sum scene. There is not a single cart roaming this elegant dining room, which in turn is managed by a team of fast and friendly servers who will ensure that you never leave less than stuffed. Traditionalists will want to end with a rich egg tart, but for a more soothing finale, order the minced pork congee infused with soy, green onions and wonton chips.The restaurant also runs a second location in Pasadena.;Air conditioning;[]
5344;MAMA Oakland;USA;Oakland;388 Grand Ave., Oakland, 94610, USA;37.8090021;-122.2542995;93;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;Opened by a husband-and-wife team just a few doors down from their wine shop (Bay Grape), this alluring spot has that simple yet chic look down pat. Envision a dark green ceiling, brass-and-glass chandeliers, and live plants scattered throughout. The premise is simple—a reasonably priced, three-course dinner and there are no reservations. Choose one of two options for each course—like a soup or salad tailed by pasta and dessert. Items change often, but one constant is the spaghetti, which also served as the inspiration behind this establishment. Presented as a hearty portion, the twirled mound is tossed with Mama's tomato sugo, featuring braised pork and beef. The wine list is full of interesting labels and employs symbols for easier navigation.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
5346;Teni East Kitchen;USA;Oakland;4015 Broadway, Oakland, 94611, USA;37.8278;-122.25663;43;true;false;Burmese;Burmese food with a California spin is on the menu at Chef/owner Tiyo Shibabaw’s cheery spot in Temescal, where the tea leaf salads come with kale and there’s plenty of flaky, golden roti bread to go around. Everything is affordable here, but the lunchtime specials are an especially good deal: a hot and flavorful entrée (like spicy coconut curry chicken with rice noodles) and a fresh salad—go for the pea shoots topped with radishes and fried garlic in a turmeric dressing.Bright and airy, with exposed wooden beams on the ceiling, Teni draws a crowd of hipsters of all ages. Its dining room can certainly fill up fast at prime hours, but it’s worth the wait for food that’s fresh, flavorful, unfussy and generously portioned.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5347;Bettina;USA;Santa Barbara;1014 Coast Village Rd., Santa Barbara, 93108, USA;34.4226378;-119.6521334;17;true;true;Pizza, Italian;After making a match at NYC’s Roberta’s, Brendan Smith and Rachel Greenspan took their pizza-powered love affair to the West Coast to a gleaming perch in the Montecito Country Mart. Each night, the pair dishes up a bevy of pie varieties tattooed with the delicate char of their wood-fired oven. Even staples like pepperoni are exceptional, thanks to the slow-fermented dough, house-pulled mozzarella, and tangy, ripe tomatoes from Bianco DiNapoli, and seasonal options like a creamed leek pizza with pork sausage and crispy shallot are equally satisfying. Pastas, like a hand-cut tagliatelle with braised lamb shoulder, show similar care. This oven also does a solid sideline in baked goods, so grab some brown-butter chocolate chip cookies or a crusty sourdough loaf on your way out.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5348;The Factory Kitchen;USA;Los Angeles;1300 Factory Pl., Ste. 101, Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.03912;-118.23589;61;false;true;Italian, Regional Cuisine;This “factory” is actually sleek, with cement columns, a modern bar and wide-open garage doors that enhance its lofty feel. However, the heart and soul of its kitchen is dedicated to traditional Northern Italian cuisine. This should come as no surprise, as Angelo Auriana and Matteo Ferdinandi are turning heads with their quickly expanding empire. Devotion to regionally specific flavors is clear in every bite. Ravioli, made in house, tucked with seafood and tossed in an aromatic and savory sauce, is a winner, but don't skip the shatteringly crisp focaccina calda di Recco, filled with Crescenza cheese—it's sublime. Desserts, including the paciugo, are a strong finish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5349;Insalata's;USA;San Anselmo;120 Sir Francis Drake Blvd., San Anselmo, 94960, USA;37.97308;-122.56138;90;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;San Anselmo restaurateur, Chef Heidi Krahling honors her late father, Italo Insalata, at this crowd-pleasing Marin hangout. The zucca-orange stucco exterior alludes to the Mediterranean air within. Insalata’s upscale setting is framed by lemon-yellow walls hung with grand depictions of nature’s bounty, setting the scene for an array of fresh and flavorful cuisine to come.Sparked by Middle Eastern flavors, the kitchen's specialties include velvety smooth potato-leek soup made brilliantly green from watercress purée. Also sample grilled lamb skewers drizzled with cumin-yogurt atop crunchy salad and flatbread. The takeout area in the back is stocked with salads, sides and sandwiches made with house-baked bread. Boxed lunches are a fun, tasty convenience.;Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
5351;Del Popolo;USA;San Francisco;855 Bush St., San Francisco, 94108, USA;37.789772;-122.41141;90;true;true;Pizza, Californian;If you’ve got eyes for pies, you’ll want to make a beeline to this chic and simple Italian hot spot. The open space is centered around a big, blazing oven and crowds arrive early to score every last no-reservations seat.Del Popolo may have gotten its start as a food truck, but one bite of their wood-fired pizzas and it's clear how it earned its address. Chewy, blistered and deliciously caramelized, the crusts arrive laden with toppings both traditional (mozzarella, crushed tomato and basil) and California cool (roasted winter squash, mascarpone, spring onions). Don’t sleep on the antipasti either, since the starters are first-rate. The lightly charred carrots set atop house-made yogurt and garnished with crispy red quinoa are dizzyingly delicious.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5352;Spinning Bones;USA;Alameda;1205 Park St., Alameda, 94501, USA;37.7612014;-122.2456112;32;false;true;Californian;On the quaint island of Alameda comes this causal concept from restaurateurs, Mike Yakura and Danny Sterling. The entrance is in keeping with its industrial interior design, complete with a counter and kitchen in full view, exposed ductwork, and an indigo-blue ceiling.Billing itself as a Californian rotisserie, the menu is also strewn with Hawaiian and Japanese accents—behold such unorthodox sides as a Napa slaw, with pickled red kraut, carrot, and creamy sesame dressing. Top-notch meats take center stage, with starters (corn fritters with strawberry jam, anyone?) to boot. Marinated in koji and fermented rice, these umami-packed cuts are then grilled to rosy perfection. Desserts, like butter mochi cake with whipped cream, boast a light-as-feather texture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5353;Chifa;USA;Los Angeles;4374 Eagle Rock Blvd., Los Angeles, 90041, USA;34.1236509;-118.2212657;78;true;true;Fusion, Chinese;"Chifa" is a term referring to a delicious mashup of Peruvian and Chinese cuisines. If the green velvet chairs and zebra-print walls aren't enough of a clue, look to the team who isn't shy about anything.The succinct menu pulls from family recipes and childhood memories to pack in flavor at every turn. Start easy with Japanese sea bream soaking in an orange and lime sauce, before moving on to char siu, starring pork cheek finished on a wood-fire grill—it's the stuff of barbecue dreams. Your visit would be incomplete without the lomo saltado, featuring tender chunks of filet mignon and sauteed onions coated in an umami-rich gravy and served on a pile of French fries. If, by some off chance, you’re still hungry, finish with a black sesame-cheesecake tart.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5354;Top Hatters Kitchen;USA;San Leandro;855 Macarthur Blvd., San Leandro, 94577, USA;37.7373393;-122.1417697;43;false;true;Contemporary, Vietnamese;A stone’s throw from the 580 but seemingly a world apart, this handsome locale—ensconced in the arbored suburban quietude of San Leandro—offers a uniquely pleasurable experience. Husband-and-wife co-owners Matthew Beavers and DanVy Vu opted to honor this fixture’s former life as a family-owned hat shop by keeping the name—and the well-crafted cocktails are also dubbed with nods to millinery.Chef Vu leads the kitchen, and her skillful contemporary combination of Vietnamese and Californian flavors is tantalizing. Crunchy seared rice cakes come packed with savory goodness, and meltingly tender braised oxtail over creamy grits have unusual depth. For a pillow-soft landing, finish with the signature lemon-ricotta zeppole, offered with a trio of luscious sauces.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5355;Amor y Tacos;USA;Cerritos;13333 South St., Cerritos, 90703, USA;33.8602919;-118.0471398;78;true;false;Mexican;Yet another in the wave of Mexican-American LA chefs transforming the cuisine, Thomas Ortega brings his fine-dining drill to bear on this vibrant offering in his native Cerritos. Here he fuses his specific style of the city’s Mexican cuisine, like handmade tortillas and spicy salsas, with an American twist. Look for that Coca-Cola glaze on his pork belly or the sprinkle of Doritos on chilaquiles, not to mention such luxurious accents as truffles.It’s hard to miss with any of Chef Ortega's tacos, which range from crisp beer-battered cod with smoky salsa de arbol to tender, charred al pastor. Can't decide? Order the tour de tacos for an overview of the flavors the kitchen has to offer. Fried “calamari famoso” is the ideal partner for a spicy michelada.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5356;Ipoh Kopitiam;USA;Alhambra;1411 S. Garfield Ave., Ste. 104, Alhambra, 91801, USA;34.0780108;-118.1230992;42;false;true;Malaysian;Is there ever not a wait at this friendly Malaysian café? Chef Kenji Tang has something of a hit on his hands, and day or night, the line to get in can be as dense as the takeout tickets that pile up on the front counter. Tang fills a void with a fairly succinct menu of well-known Malaysian favorites that stand out in a region known more for its Chinese restaurants. Everybody orders the tender Hainanese chicken, served with a trio of dipping sauces and a dome of seasoned rice. Chicken curry showcases Tang’s ability to layer finely tuned spices – order it with flaky, buttery sheets of roti canai. Best of all might be the char kway teow, flat rice noodles seared in a blistering hot wok and tossed with scallions, Chinese sausage and bean sprouts.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5357;Little Fish;USA;Los Angeles;1606 W. Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.0768498;-118.2577133;79;true;false;American;Once itinerant, Anna Sonenshein and Niki Vahle now welcome guests to their Echo Park location where they share space with a mini market. Come for breakfast or lunch—both are delicious. As their name suggests, the menu is seafood-focused, but steak and vegetarian offerings are also on offer. Mornings are met with items like fish tartines and fish and mushroom congee, while lunch features heartier sandwiches like their signature fried fish. The beer-battered Pacific striped bass is tender and sweet, then topped with American cheese, kewpie mayo and dill pickles on a potato bun for a midday meal that is as satisfying as they come. Not a fan of fish? The broccoli rabe melt with kabocha squash spread, provolone piccante cheese and chili garlic is a standout.;;[]
5358;Lola Gaspar;USA;Santa Ana;211 W. 2nd St., Santa Ana, 92701, USA;33.7462708;-117.8687592;39;true;false;Mexican;This gastropub in downtown Santa Ana isn't new but a post-pandemic reset and a trip to Mexico changed Chef Luis Perez's mindset—and menu. It's all about quality over quantity here, so expect a tightly edited menu featuring tacos, quekas, and churros, but it's all very good. Happy hour discounts make sampling it all a tempting proposition. Tacos are made with handmade flour tortillas topped with a grilled tomato and dried chili salsa and filled with everything from sauteed shrimp to pork shank carnitas and suadero. Quekas feature hand-pressed masa and are served with a habanero salsa. While the vegan mushroom queka is worth ordering by itself with nicely sauteed mushrooms, confit potatoes, and guacamole, you can also opt to add cheese for a wonderful addition.;Air conditioning;[]
5360;Wood Tavern;USA;Oakland;6317 College Ave., Oakland, 94618, USA;37.85076;-122.25265;65;true;false;American;There’s always a crowd at this neighborhood standby, where friends, families, and chic couples congregate for drinks at the copper-topped bar. Flanked by organic groceries, indie bookstores and antique shops, its environs speak of peace, weaving a bohemian spell that captivates both regulars and rookies alike.Seasonal Californian cooking with an Italian bent dominates this tavern's menu, and a "butcher block" of well-prepared charcuterie--like herb-flecked rabbit terrine wrapped in prosciutto--is a prudent way to start your meal. A touch of Calabrian chili adds welcoming heat to the combo of morels, Italian sausage, and sweet corn that sauce a bowl of al dente bucatini. For dessert, warm bread pudding with a coffee-chocolate sauce is utterly devourable.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5361;Villa's Tacos;USA;Los Angeles;5455 N. Figueroa St., Los Angeles, 90042, USA;34.1080789;-118.1968638;77;true;true;Mexican;Sweet smoke from a roadside taco stand blows across the Highland Park parking lot, but the crowd gathered in front of Chef Victor Villa’s taqueria doesn’t budge. This brick-and-mortar marks a milestone for a chef who first started serving out of his grandmother’s house. The signature queso taco is instantly recognizable, built on a blue corn masa tortilla stacked with refried beans, onion, cilantro, guacamole, cotija cheese, crema and a melted skirt of Monterey Jack. Variations with asada and chorizo are favorites, with vegan options on offer as well. Colorful, messy and filling, these tacos thrive on their own but also sing with the homemade salsas, some of which are ferociously spicy. Seating is limited to a few picnic tables outside.;Terrace;[]
5362;Quarter Sheets;USA;Los Angeles;1305 Portia St., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.0757851;-118.2542922;91;false;false;Pizza;Aaron Lindell and Hannah Ziskin's Quarter Sheets Pizza has nailed that haute hipster vibe with its casual styling and vinyl and cassette collection. The word is out on this Echo Park spot, so expect a wait, but one bite of their inch-thick, pan-style pizzas makes it all worth your while. Baked to order, they're prepared with flavorful sauce and quality ingredients. Pepperoni is a classic choice, or opt for the pimento grove, a vodka sauced pizza topped with olives, 'nduja and cheese. And, while you might not expect to get serious pastries at a pizza shop, don't leave without trying at least one of Hannah Ziskin's pastries. There are a few offerings that rotate often but the signature Princess cake is a staple that's worth every bite.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5363;Lalibela;USA;Los Angeles;1025 S. Fairfax Ave., Los Angeles, 90019, USA;34.0573578;-118.3643785;52;true;false;Ethiopian;Light streams in through the windows of this tranquil family affair in Little Ethiopia. Chef/owner Tenagne Belachew and her daughters are congenial fixtures in a simply adorned setting that feels like a humble abode. They are content to let the food do the talking and offer a dazzling selection of vibrant Ethiopian classics with vegetables and meat alike arriving on oversized silver platters lined with injera. Best shared with a group, the "veggie utopia" offers immediate insight into their talents, spotlighting lentils astutely seasoned with berber and turmeric. Finely chopped kitfo is something of a house specialty and the spicy Somali variation, made with lean prime beef flecked with onions and jalapeños, is especially enjoyable.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5364;Petiscos;USA;San Jose;399 S. 1st St., San Jose, 95113, USA;37.330106;-121.8859271;91;false;false;Portuguese, Regional Cuisine;Petiscos are as much a cultural reference as they are a small snack accompanied by drinks. They're fun and approachable—designed to be shared among good friends and family—so it goes without saying that this spot, complete with a bar, knows how to welcome guests. Authentically prepared dishes highlight the flavors of Portugal and feature imported ingredients. The rustic, home-style cooking includes favorites such as broa, a traditional cornbread, and lupini beans, codfish croquettes and a tender octopus salad that is a meal unto itself. Slivers of braised pig ears are tossed with a lively citrus and herb dressing and perfectly paired with cilantro and parsley, and the golden-brown grilled sardines are a pleasure.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5365;Callie;USA;San Diego;1195 Island Ave., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7103575;-117.1538654;79;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Middle Eastern;Chef Travis Swikard comes back to his hometown wreathed in glory, having earned his wings helming restaurants for culinary icon Daniel Boulud in New York City. Hip locals can now reap the benefits of the years he spent honing his craft in fine dining kitchens at this sharply designed and boisterous spot.The cuisine takes advantage of the best ingredients SoCal has to offer in highly shareable dishes featuring the bold, sunny flavors of the Mediterranean. Vegetables and seafood steal the show, with spice as a key supporting character. Behold the  kampachi crudo with an herb-y Israeli hot sauce and black lime, or carrots with crunchy cashew dukkah and burnt orange habanero dressing. Save room for sweets like the warm chocolate chip tahini cookie.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5366;Good Good Culture Club;USA;San Francisco;3560 18th St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.7617533;-122.4229362;35;false;false;South East Asian, Californian;Stroll into this lush, happening spot and your eyes will quickly fall on neon blue letters scrawled above the lively open kitchen: "did you eat yet?" The correct answer is "no": an empty stomach will be amply rewarded by the vibrantly flavorful cooking here. Southeast Asian flavors find unique Californian expressions in dishes like a signature adobo-glazed fried chicken wing stuffed with garlic rice, or a Lao-style sausage with tangy pasilla pepper jaew. A version of halo halo, featuring mango jellies, shiso shaved ice and seasonal fruit, is a particular treat. Reservations go quickly, but if you walk in early (or late), you may find a perch to dine at the bar, where you'll also find an array of creative, tropically inflected cocktails—a match made in paradise.;Wheelchair access;[]
5367;Cobi's;USA;Santa Monica;2104 Main St., Santa Monica, 90405, USA;34.0062773;-118.4881448;85;true;false;Asian;The pink building with green trim is the first sign that Cobi's will charm you, and then there's the dining room, where frilly, floral touches (Pink wallpaper! Mismatched tables and chairs!) and a patio with more flowers set the scene for a lively atmosphere. Discover Thai and Malaysian delights along with other influences on this broad Southeast Asian menu. Start with dumplings, satay or curry puffs, those crispy triangular shells filled with curried split peas and potatoes sided by pickled onion and tamarind ketchup. From there, pick a curry or a wood-grilled main dish such as grilled prawns in a ginger and yellow bean sauce. You won't go wrong with scallops on the half shell or butter chicken with tomato masala, while prix fixe options include a smattering of dishes selected by the chef.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5368;Pijja Palace;USA;Los Angeles;2711 Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.0807208;-118.2703816;84;false;false;Fusion, Indian;“Indian Sports Bar” is not a phrase you hear often, if at all, and so it’s no surprise that this quirky hotspot at the base of a Comfort Inn defies labels. True to its name, large flatscreen TVs showing the day’s game hang on every wall, and people do indeed come here to cheer on their team. The food is equally original, riffing on classic bar dishes but elevating them with astute seasoning and careful preparation. Onion rings are coated in dosa batter. Wings are marinated in cilantro-mint chutney. Rigatoni comes tossed in a creamy tomato masala that evokes a vodka tomato sauce. There are even thin, crisp pizzas. Don’t let the casualness of the space lull you into thinking that reservations are easy. A long line takes shape before doors open.;Air conditioning;[]
5369;Manohar’s Delhi Palace;USA;La Puente;581 Azusa Way, La Puente, 91744, USA;34.0118022;-117.9245279;35;false;false;Indian;Manohar's Delhi Palace is a mainstay thanks to their delicious Punjabi cuisine, and there's a welcoming vibe about this place, where the waitstaff is especially friendly and attentive. Indicative of its north Indian focus, the food here leans on the milder side, so don't expect an onslaught of spices. Order à la carte or go all in on the tandoori dinner but be sure to get an order of the samosas, fried to a perfect crisp with that comforting filling of potatoes and peas. Chicken tikka masala features a generous amount of tender and juicy chicken that's skewered and seared before being added to the vibrant sauce. For dessert, the gulab jamun is a clear winner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5370;Hoe Lee Kow;;Dubai;Building 4, Dubai Hills Estate Business Park, Dubai Hills, Dubai;25.1057048;55.2396297;100;false;true;Asian Contemporary;This relaxing and casual restaurant, set within Dubai Hills Business Park, is another venture from notable local chef, Reif Othman. A playful and colourful space with Korean elements adorning the walls, the contemporary Korean eatery specialises in barbecue, with a nice selection of wagyu beef and a noteworthy marinated grilled salmon dish paired with gochujang sauce. Prices are good, especially the business lunch. Expect warm service from the attentive and smiling team.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5371;Indya by Vineet;;Dubai;Le Royal Meridien Beach Resort & Spa Hotel, Al Mamsha Street, Dubai;25.0846849;55.1406544;64;true;false;Indian;Vibrant, modern Indian cooking is on offer at this fun and funky poolside restaurant, where the charming team provide helpful service with a smile. Street food meets sharing plates on the appealingly eclectic menu, with choices from the earth (vegetarian), land (meat) and sea. Colourful dishes, like the tandoori cauliflower roast, and lamb biriyani kofta, come in generous portions.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5373;DUO Gastrobar-Dubai Hills;;Dubai;Building 4, Dubai Hills Estate Business Park, Dubai Hills, Dubai;25.1054938;55.2396868;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Dubai Hills neighbourhood is the outpost of a small restaurant group from St. Petersburg. This contemporary eatery has a light and airy atmosphere, thanks to its sleek blond wood furnishings, cream décor, high ceiling, and buzzy open kitchen. Diners can opt for an appealing breakfast menu, as well as a hearty lunch with a well-priced selection. This place offers a good range of modern, flavourful dishes, where Asian influences and European accents are found in parallel. Their signature dishes are worth trying, especially the oxtail pie with Tallegio. The well-trained staff work smoothly and discreetly to ensure a charming experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5374;REIF Japanese Kushiyaki - Dar Wasl;;Dubai;Unit 70, Dar Wasl Mall, Al Wasl Road, Dubai;25.193772;55.2449969;45;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;In the residential neighbourhood of Al Wasl, away from the city’s impressive skyscrapers, is a kushiyaki-inspired but friendly restaurant, offering far more than just grilled skewered meats and vegetables. The contemporary Japanese menu also covers a wide range of well-priced snacks, sushi and ramen, like their Tantamen ramen, raw salmon with crispy black rice and Wagyu steamed bun. Be sure to also save room for one of their creative desserts.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5375;Revelry;;Dubai;Building 1, Dubai Hills Estate Business Park, Dubai Hills, Dubai;25.1073252;55.2412057;62;true;true;Indian;Little sister to avatāra, which is directly next door, this Indian 'tapas bar' is more casual and informal in style, with a particularly good range of cocktails inspired by India’s vastly differing seasons. Inside the L-shaped room, the atmosphere is very relaxed with three TV screens showing sports games, including, unsurprisingly, cricket! The appealingly priced menu comprises a good range of well-crafted, balanced, and gently spiced contemporary Indian dishes, which combine tradition and modernity. Three ‘tapas’ and a main course should do the trick and will arrive when ready. Do leave room for the creative desserts, such as Bailey’s tiramisu with Kahlua rasmalai.;Air conditioning;[]
5379;Aamara;;Dubai;2nd Floor, VOCO Hotel, Sheikh Zayed Rd – Trade Centre 1, Dubai;25.2235105;55.2827243;43;true;false;Asian and Western;The clever people of the Trèsind group are behind this vibrant restaurant which takes inspiration for its food and flavours from the Silk Route, covering everything from the Med to Eastern Asia – and it’s easy to see why it’s quickly become many people’s favourite hangout. Dishes are designed for sharing and must-haves include signatures such as smoked jackfruit and corn shami kebab, bouillabase Malai curry and banana bread and Oscietra caviar.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
5380;Berenjak;;Dubai;Dar Wasl Mall - Shop 01 - Al Wasl Rd - Al Wasl, Dubai;25.1957931;55.2465471;96;false;false;Persian;An outpost of the original in London, this Persian eatery is located in Dubai’s smaller malls in the residential area of Al Wasl. It’s a large space decorated with oriental mosaics, carpets and portraits, all adding to the atmosphere. Expect plenty of appealingly priced Persian classics in its selection of hot and cold mezze and charcoal-grilled kebabs, all of which are complemented by vegetables, herbs and aromatics. A separate room for families and large gatherings is also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5383;Konjiki Hototogisu;;Dubai;Mall Of Emirates - 2nd Level, Dubai;25.1193824;55.201576;71;true;true;Japanese, Ramen;On the second floor of the Mall of the Emirates is this very likeable restaurant which is a slightly simplified version of the original with the same name in Tokyo. Here, the menu offers ramen, including the signature shoyu ramen, along with other classic Japanese dishes: gyoza, tempura, and kushiyaki such as chicken skewers with yakitori and sesame sauce. End the meal with a light and sweet matcha mochi accompanied by coconut ice cream. Booking isn’t possible, but service starts before noon and there is usually space available at the counter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5384;Shabestan;;Dubai;Baniyas Road, Deira Creek, Dubai;25.2650584;55.3108484;93;true;false;Middle Eastern;A charming restaurant serving authentic Persian fare and run by the third generation of the same family. It’s set on the second floor of the Radisson Blu Hotel and boasts views over the Creek and Old Dubai. Menus offer traditional Persian dishes, such as Kash E Bademjan (their signature eggplant dish) along with a range of marinated meats, all served in generous portions.;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking;[]
5385;Kinoya;;Dubai;The Onyx Tower 2, Sheikh Zayed Road, Dubai;25.0968233;55.1684001;73;true;true;Japanese;There’s a buzzing atmosphere at this authentic izakaya, set in The Onyx Tower 2 in The Greens. Five ramen dishes underpin the menu, which also lists other Japanese classics including sushi, sashimi, robata and tempura. Ingredients are good quality, cooking is careful, prices are low and flavours, delicious. For a chance to watch the chefs preparing their signature dishes, be sure to book your seats on the counter in advance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5386;REIF Japanese Kushiyaki - Dubai Hills;;Dubai;Building 3, Dubai Hills Estate Business Park, Dubai Hills, Dubai;25.1063339;55.2403029;72;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;This second branch, opened in 2023, is located in the emerging Dubai Hills district. Similar to the original in Dar Wasl but with a few subtle differences, the eatery offers a wide range of colourful Japanese favourites, from kushiyaki (as the name suggests), to fun classics with an international twist, such as their escargot teriyaki and beef gyoza. The restaurant blends contemporary, sleek design with pops of colour.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
5387;Teible;;Dubai;Jameel Arts Centre, Jaddaf Waterfront, Dubai;25.2289489;55.3414444;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Spacious, light and airy, this minimalistic restaurant at the tip of the Jameel Arts Centre boasts beautiful views through its floor-to-ceiling windows. Their mantra, “sustainability, seasonality, simplicity, and locality," is evident throughout their décor and modern dishes. Menus showcase seasonal, local – and occasionally fermented – ingredients in great value plates.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
5388;Miến Lươn Đông Thịnh;Vietnam;Hanoi;87 Hang Dieu Street, Cua Dong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0320059;105.8468122;23;true;false;Noodles;Many restaurants in Vietnam focus on a concise menu starring one key ingredient. In this 40-plus-year-old shop, the menu revolves around eel as in eel noodles, eel congee and eel soup. For the noodles, they use rice vermicelli which is made into noodle soup, or tossed with deep-fried shredded eel, herbs, toasted peanuts and shallots. Shredded pork sausage and shiitake mushrooms are added to the soup and congee to further boost the umami.;Cash only;[]
5389;Nhà Tú;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;129/4 Vo Van Tan Street, Vo Thi Sau Ward, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7753712;106.6898829;73;false;false;Vietnamese;An oasis amid the hustle and bustle of the city, Nhà Tú is depicted by green plants and a nostalgic vibe with the bonus of a lovely top-floor balcony. In terms of food, the owner captures the essence of his childhood with home-style cooking rarely found elsewhere. Steamed snails stuffed with minced pork seduces with umami and lemongrass fragrance. Mixed veggies dressed in a fish sauce reduction with pork crackling are simple, but addictive.;Air conditioning;[]
5390;Bò Kho Gánh;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;029 Lot H, Ngo Gia Tu Apartment, Su Van Hanh Street, Ward 2, District 10, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.761215;106.669885;100;true;false;Street Food;Its famous beef stew known as bò kho is served in a stone bowl. Diners may choose to pair it with bread, noodles or rice. The broth is sweet and tasty, with a robust meaty flavour. Help yourself to condiments and sauces.;Cash only;[]
5391;Bánh Xèo Tôm Nhảy Cô Ba;Vietnam;Da Nang;248 Trung Nu Vuong Street, Binh Thuan Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0545067;108.2197565;90;true;true;Vietnamese;The bright-red lettering looks smart against the artificial turf on a wall. For over 10 years, this small family business has been serving crispy bánh xèo pancakes alongside snacks. Try their bánh xèo tôm nhảy – the wafer-thin crispy crust is done in the style of Binh Dinh province, topped with fresh shrimps. Dip in fish sauce or peanut sauce for complementary flavours. Nem nướng is deep-fried pork sausage with a great peppery taste.;Cash only;[]
5392;Bún Chả Cá 109;Vietnam;Da Nang;109 Nguyen Chi Thanh Street, Hai Chau 1 Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0745199;108.2207547;67;true;true;Noodles;In business for over five decades, it is now run by the third-generation owner. The sign indicates the house speciality – bún chả cá, or fishcake noodle soup. Springy and flavoursome, their house-made deep-fried and steamed fishcakes deserve all the attention they get. But extra tuna, mackerel, crab cake and crab balls make the noodle soup even better. The broth is sweet with a hint of sourness, thanks to pineapple and tomatoes.;Cash only;[]
5393;Quán Nhân;Vietnam;Da Nang;83 Phan Tu Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0464239;108.2455548;18;false;true;Street Food;People flock here for its famous duck porridge. A local duck breed from Cẩm Nam Island, rice, mung beans and coix seeds are slowly simmered in duck broth for a creamy, hearty meal. Poached duck and duck salad are also available.;Cash only;[]
5394;Bún Chả Cá Hờn;Vietnam;Da Nang;113/03 Nguyen Chi Thanh Street, Hai Chau 1 Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0741438;108.2212217;70;false;true;Noodles;Bún chả cá (fishcake rice noodle soup) is pivotal to Da Nang food culture. Now run by the second generation, this hidden family-run gem has been serving the city’s favourite noodle soup for over 30 years. Its signature đặc biệt, or special, is topped with crabmeat as well as fried and poached fishcakes. You can also opt for a slice of mackerel or tuna as a topping. The tomato-based broth tastes sweet and mildly sour, with bamboo shoot overtones.;Cash only;[]
5395;Bún Chả Chan;Vietnam;Hanoi;114 Mai Hac De Street, Le Dai Hanh Ward, Hai Ba Trung District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.010189;105.850778;95;true;false;Noodles;This small bún chả shop has been serving loyal customers for over 10 years. In addition to the typical caramelised pork meatballs on rice vermicelli, you can ask for grilled pork belly or minced beef in betel leaf to go with the noodles – all served with a tangy, sweet broth. The spring roll, deep-fried to order, boasts crispy skin and a juicy filling with layers of rich flavours. Open until noon only, so come early to avoid missing out.;Cash only;[]
5396;Phở Miến Gà Kỳ Đồng;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;14/5 Bis Ky Dong Street, Ward 9, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7839019;106.6820208;66;false;true;Street Food;A true gem in the bustling city, the chicken phở here is nothing short of amazing. The essence of its deliciousness lies in the rich, aromatic chicken broth made by slow-cooking chicken bones for 3-4 hours. The tender chicken slices and rice vermicelli are also to die for.;Cash only;[]
5397;The East;Vietnam;Hanoi;5B Tong Duy Tan Street, Hang Bong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0311887;105.8419136;35;false;false;Vietnamese;In a popular area teeming with eateries and buzzing with energy, The East stands out from the crowd with its excellent Northern Vietnamese cuisine. Start with the crab spring rolls wrapped in a fine, crispy skin packed with savoury filling. The bún chả Hanoi (grilled pork and rice vermicelli) is the signature dish here and a street food staple in the capital. The Vietnamese-style flan rounds off this enjoyable dining experience. The smart two-storey house also sells ceramics created by local artisans.;Air conditioning;[]
5398;Xôi Bát;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;8 Hoang Hoa Tham Street, Ward 7, Binh Thanh District, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.8042901;106.6921163;30;false;true;Vietnamese;Xôi – steamed sticky rice – is a Vietnamese staple popularly eaten as a quick breakfast or lunch. Determined to shatter the stereotype of xôi as a frugal fast food, in 2021 a young team opened Xôi Bát, a charming little eatery with a contemporary design and great attention paid to detail. They put their recipe for a relatively soft sticky rice into dishes such as xôi phá lấu trứng non, which includes quail eggs, pig ears and fried shallots, and is served with soup and kimchi as a simple, appetising meal.;Cash only;[]
5399;Phở Khôi Hói;Vietnam;Hanoi;50 Hang Vai Street, Hang Bo Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.035698;105.8459795;16;false;true;Street Food;Khôi Hói means bald head, referring to the owner’s hairstyle. Come here for phở – beef noodle soup. There are many cuts to choose from, including rare cuts like beef heel muscle. You can also specify how you like your beef cooked.;Cash only;[]
5400;Ngọc Chi;Vietnam;Da Nang;202 Hoang Dieu Street, Nam Duong Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0620931;108.2174064;90;true;true;Vegetarian;For over 10 years, Ngọc Chi has been serving an extensive menu of mostly Vietnamese origin using local veggies and herbs. Some dishes include plant-based meat. Fermented seasonings are put to good use, accentuating big-boned flavours while supporting a healthy lifestyle. Whet your appetite with a bowl of sour soup featuring mixed veggies. Then move on to wontons and spring rolls, hand-wrapped and deep-fried to perfection á la minute.;Cash only,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5402;Bánh Xèo 46A;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;46 Dinh Cong Trang Street, Tan Dinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7895934;106.6913619;98;true;false;Vietnamese;The air-conditioned room may be tempting, but the al fresco seating by the open kitchen promises the most authentic experience. For over seven decades, regulars have been returning for its huge Vietnamese signature crêpes stuffed with mung beans, bean sprouts, pork and shrimp. Pair with pulled chicken salad, as well as chargrilled meat and seafood, among which pork, beef, squid and prawns. Be sure to arrive well before closing time.;Cash only;[]
5403;Mặn Mòi (Thu Duc City);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;32 D11 Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.77653;106.70098;99;true;false;Vietnamese;A landmark of HCMC’s dining scene for 10+ years, Mặn Mòi is renowned for its nature inspired interior and theme – ask for a table in the lush courtyard for an al fresco experience. The extensive menu spans regional specialities from all over Vietnam, including salads, soups, mains, grilled dishes, desserts, as well as claypots and hot pots. Finish your meal with a Vietnamese coffee and browse the gift shop for keepsakes.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5404;Bun Cha Ta (Nguyen Huu Huan Street);Vietnam;Hanoi;21 Nguyen Huu Huan Street, Ly Thai To Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, 100000, Vietnam;21.0343385;105.8545007;48;false;true;Noodles;Popular with tourists, Bun Cha Ta offers various bún chả and fried spring rolls. The classic bún chả features tender, smoky grilled pork, well-seasoned meat patties and smooth rice noodles with a balanced soup base. Among the crispy spring rolls, the seafood crab version delivers a consummate umami flavour, while the chicken is rich and meaty. They also offer rice noodles with fried tofu and tomato sauce and fried spring rolls for vegetarians.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5405;Phở Phượng;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;25 Hoang Sa Street, Da Kao Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.791939;106.704478;23;true;true;Street Food;Like most phở shops, you can order the house special to sample different beef cuts with the ubiquitous noodle soup. But the most popular ingredient here is oxtail – braised for 40 hours until the meat is tender and the skin gelatinous.;Cash only;[]
5406;Phở Hương Bình;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;148 Vo Thi Sau Street, Ward 8, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7871;106.69103;42;true;false;Noodles;This simple stall has been proudly serving Vietnam’s national rice noodle soup dish, phở, since 1958. There are only two items on the menu – phở gà (chicken noodle soup) and phở bò (beef noodle soup). Feel free to order additional toppings such as chicken skin, egg yolk, beef brisket and tendon. The broth is clear and light, rich in full-bodied flavours and a savoury sweetness.;Cash only;[]
5407;Phở Lệ (District 5);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;413-415 Nguyen Trai Street, Ward 7, District 5, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.75529;106.67351;88;true;false;Noodles;Vietnam’s national noodle soup dish has taken the culinary world by storm, and Phở Lệ, one of the leading restaurants in town, insists on making it exactly the same way they have been doing for over 70 years. Come here for authentic southern Vietnamese style phở – in rich broth with a robust meaty flavour and a hint of sweetness from vegetables. Despite its age, the stall is neat and clean, and always jam-packed with hungry locals getting their noodle fix.;Cash only;[]
5408;Chào Bạn;Vietnam;Hanoi;98 To Ngoc Van Street, Quang An Ward, Tay Ho District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0679;105.82236;47;true;true;Vietnamese;In keeping with its name, which means "hello, friend" in Vietnamese, Chào Bạn is welcoming and easy-going. In the kitchen, chef Madame Hang gives traditional Vietnamese recipes a new spin with creativity and aplomb. Her nem rán cua (crab spring rolls) deliver balanced flavours and contrasting textures. The đặc biệt section, which includes prawns in coconut cream, or lacquered pork ribs, is a treasure trove of her creative signature dishes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5409;Phở Gia Truyền (Hoan Kiem);Vietnam;Hanoi;49 Bat Dan Street, Cua Dong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0336032;105.8461911;31;false;true;Street Food;The numerous hearty options include phở tái nạm (slices of flank steak), phở tái (round steak) and phở chín (brisket). Add crispy quẩy (fried dough sticks), to perfect your dish. For the ultimate hunger obliterating meal, splash out on a little extra and order trứng gà (golden egg yolk).;Cash only;[]
5410;Phở Hoà Pasteur;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;260C Pasteur Street, Ward 8, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.77029;106.7031;98;true;true;Vietnamese;This popular restaurant has been serving delicious phở to the locals since it opened in 1968. The interior and service may not be glamorous, but the food is appropriately affordable and their delicious hallmark broth is a masterclass of balanced flavours. The menu offers a wide range of quality toppings including beef brisket, flank, tendon and tripe, as well as meatballs. Small Vietnamese side dishes are also available.;Cash only;[]
5411;Thìa Gỗ;Vietnam;Da Nang;53 Phan Thuc Duyen Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.052986;108.24158;42;false;true;Vietnamese;This two-storey oasis away from the bustling main strip features al fresco seating in a lush green setting. Scan the QR code to learn more about the menu and Vietnamese food in general. Phố nam is a must-try with noodles in a clear beef bone broth loaded with flavours. Order the thập cẩm version to try all beef cuts. Bánh xèo miền tây is another popular choice with crispy pancakes and a generous filling. Cheerful, friendly front-of-house team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5412;Ăn Thôi;Vietnam;Da Nang;114 Bach Dang Street, Hai Chau 1 Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0684464;108.2248426;75;false;false;Vietnamese;A French colonial allure depicts this two-storey restaurant with a blue and yellow façade. A relaxed vibe and its convenient location near the Han River and Han Market make it a popular spot for a meal after shopping. The concise menu features outstanding bánh xèo, boasting crispy, golden pancakes stuffed with carrot, pork, shrimps and squid. Spot-on seasoning, divine aromas and very courteous front-of-house staff.;Air conditioning;[]
5413;Chay Garden (District 3);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;52 Vo Van Tan Street, Ward 6, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.778071;106.6909017;25;true;false;Vegetarian;Located at the end of a quiet pedestrian street in the busy city centre, this vegetarian restaurant crafts delicious, affordable Vietnamese nosh, such as braised eggplant with banana and green beans. The old colonial-style house sports a charming tree-lined patio, which provides the perfect foil to this fine dining experience. The small dining rooms are thoughtfully and attractively furnished and one boasts a colourful fresco.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5414;Bún Bò Bà Rơi (Hai Chau);Vietnam;Da Nang;5 Phan Thanh Tai Street, Hoa Thuan Dong Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0537594;108.2214295;58;true;true;Noodles;The family, who hails from Huế, opened this shop in 2014 to sell Huế’s version of bún bò, or beef noodle soup. The umami-loaded broth with beef meat and bones simmers overnight, building balanced, big-boned flavours. They use medium thick rice noodles. Popular toppings include beef tendon, rib, brisket and tongue, as well as pork trotters and crab balls. If you want to sample all the toppings, opt for the đặc biệt version.;Cash only;[]
5415;Vị Quê Kitchen;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;110 Suong Nguyet Anh Street, Ben Thanh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 710000, Vietnam;10.77159;106.6885232;87;false;false;Vegetarian;Vị Quê Kitchen champions a modern Vietnamese vegan score that incorporates flavours from all over the country with creative twists. Nem vuông is a variation of deep-fried rice paper parcels from Hai Phong city, filled here with assorted mushrooms and glass noodles, rich in texture. Bún vì quê, noodle soup topped with herbs and tofu puffs, features a punchy flavour-packed broth. The cosy vibe and music are a plus.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
5416;Bé Ni 2;Vietnam;Da Nang;228 Vo Nguyen Giap Street, Phuoc My Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.066809;108.244791;45;true;false;Seafood;This bustling, casual spot is open 24/7 – come for rice dishes during the day and seafood at night. Most of the shellfish is sourced locally and the owner ensures the quality is top-notch. Take your pick from the live fish tank and specify how you want it cooked. The grilled shrimp has impressive smoky aromas and simple seasoning that allows the natural umami to shine through. The appetisers, such as quail eggs and poached peanuts, are perfectly made.;;[]
5417;Bún Bò Huế 14B;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;14B Street 46, Ward 2, District 4, Ho Chi Minh City, 754000, Vietnam;10.759416;106.69741;92;false;false;Street Food;This take-out only stall specialises in noodle soup topped with sliced beef, beef tendon and fish fillet. The broth made with onion, beef and pork bones is flavoursome. Add bean sprouts, chilli, lime and fish sauce according to your taste.;Cash only;[]
5418;Bếp Mẹ ỉn (Le Thanh Ton Street);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;136 Le Thanh Ton Street, Ben Thanh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7739937;106.6982066;86;false;true;Vietnamese;Eat like a local at this hidden gem near Ben Thanh Market! Inside, the vivid yellow walls are decorated to echo the exterior of village houses, complete with blue shutters. With its pleasant buzz, the restaurant has a welcoming atmosphere. Perch on one of the wooden stools, as the regulars do, and sample the signature Vietnamese pancake with shrimp and pork, served in a shallow bamboo basket. The fried rice with shrimp and egg, served in a coconut shell, is also worth trying. The service is friendly, portions are perfect for sharing.;Car park;[]
5419;Phở Gà Nguyệt;Vietnam;Hanoi;5B Phu Doan Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, 100000, Vietnam;21.0302935;105.8476631;42;false;false;Street Food;The chicken noodle come with a variety of chicken cuts, but the tender thigh is a favourite – perfect in both soup and dry noodle dishes. Mix and match thigh and wings or wings and breast, adding condiments to taste. Open until midnight, it’s a popular late-night spot.;Cash only;[]
5420;Tuyết Bún Chả 34;Vietnam;Hanoi;34 Hang Than Street, Nguyen Trung Truc Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0416366;105.8472363;37;true;true;Street Food;This stall is famous for its bún chả (rice noodles with fresh herbs and pork), chargrilled to order. Dip the noodles in the flavoursome broth and feel free to order an extra spring roll for added crunchiness.;Cash only;[]
5421;Cô Chủ Nhỏ;Vietnam;Da Nang;36 Phan Tu Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0462151;108.245465;64;true;true;Street Food;This stall sells all things duck. Duck porridge is made with rice and mung beans in a duck broth. Poached duck boasts firm, flavourful meat. When tossed with green mango, green banana, fig and herbs, it makes a refreshing salad.;Cash only;[]
5422;1946 Cua Bac;Vietnam;Hanoi;3 Yen Thanh Alley, 61 Cua Bac Street, Quan Thanh Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0428477;105.8429558;39;true;false;Vietnamese;The signature dish of this conspicuous restaurant, located in a brightly coloured yellow and green house, is the fried crab and rice porridge hot pot. Served in small bowls at the table, the crab, pigeon, beef balls and vegetables combine in a naturally sweet medley of flavours. The staff have only a smattering of English, but English menus are available with an enticing range of authentic Vietnamese dishes. Book in advance to make sure of a seat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
5423;Dim Tu Tac (Dong Du Street);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;55 Dong Du Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7755137;106.7042274;63;false;false;Cantonese;Dim Tu Tac has four restaurants in the city. The Dong Du branch seats over a hundred and is always busy, particularly at lunchtime. They serve traditional Cantonese cuisine in a comfortable, modern setting, including a large selection of dim sum, BBQ dishes, soups, seafood and much more. This is as close to an authentic Cantonese eatery as it gets, using traditional cooking techniques to deliver pleasant textures and delicious flavours at eater-friendly prices.;Air conditioning;[]
5424;Don Duck Old Quarter;Vietnam;Hanoi;29 Bat Dan Street, Hang Bo Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0336866;105.8470844;43;true;true;Vietnamese;Bliss for duck lovers! This eatery in the bustling Old Quarter conjures up almost every conceivable form of your favourite poultry. For an authentic local taste, try the duck phở noodle soup. For a variation of the Chinese classic, order the grilled à la Peking duck or enjoy duck in hotpots, spring rolls, or even deep-fried and tossed in a sweet and sour sauce. Tasty food, a casual vibe and reasonable prices make this place a firm favourite.;Air conditioning;[]
5426;Năm Hiền (Phan Thanh Street);Vietnam;Da Nang;46 Phan Thanh Street, Thac Gian Ward, Thanh Khe District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.064686;108.20793;32;true;true;Vietnamese;Dripping in lush greenery, this simple shop feels like an indoor garden. Its signature dish is a crispy bánh xèo pancake filled with beef, squid or shrimp, alongside herbs and veggies, wrapped in rice paper and dipped in a peanut sauce. Another speciality from Da Nang is bánh tráng thịt heo – rice paper roll filled with sliced pork belly, ribbon rice noodles and fresh herbs. But its umami-loaded fermented anchovy sauce is what delivers the oomph!;Cash only;[]
5427;Phở Bò Ấu Triệu;Vietnam;Hanoi;34 Au Trieu Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0285029;105.8483123;86;false;true;Street Food;The shop, which lacks any signage, boasts a single distinctive feature: phở bò, to the exclusion of anything else on the menu. And why shouldn’t it, when the minced beef noodles here are so good? Served in an intense beef bone stock, cooked for 10 hours, it comes with tender beef flank and tendon.;Cash only;[]
5428;Hồng Phát (District 3);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;389-391 Vo Van Tan Street, Ward 5, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.770509;106.684843;27;true;true;Noodles;Hủ tiếu hồng phát noodles symbolise the culinary marriage of Choazhu and Khmer culture that was introduced to Saigon in the 1970s. Friendly service is de rigueur at this simple shop, which offers all-day dining but where locals particularly flock for breakfast. The soft rice noodle soup comes with minced meat, liver, fresh tiger shrimps or braised blood curd accompanied by an assortment of herbs and bean sprouts. The chả giò tôm cua (shrimp and crab spring rolls) make a great appetiser.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5429;Mr Bảy Miền Tây;Vietnam;Hanoi;79 Hang Dieu Street, Cua Dong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.032104;105.846885;61;true;false;Vietnamese;For over a decade, this small shop has been known for its crispy bánh xèo pancake with various fillings. For first-timers, English-speaking servers helpfully explain how the pancake is wrapped in rice paper with veggies and herbs, and dunked in the tangy fish sauce before being consumed. In addition to the signature pancake, hot pot, spring roll, rice noodles and barbecues are their strong suits.;Cash only;[]
5430;Tiệm Cơm Thố Chuyên Ký;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;67 Ton That Dam Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 70000, Vietnam;10.7716032;106.7030242;78;true;true;Cantonese;Now run by the third generation, this simple shop prides itself on its double-boiled silkie chicken soup, which it has been making the same way since it opened in 1948. The flavoursome clear broth is MSG-free, with mild aromas of Chinese herbs. Another must-try is their steamed rice bowl with beef, chicken or Cantonese preserved pork sausage. Seafood cooked in various ways is also popular. Check with the owner for recommendations.;Cash only;[]
5431;Luk Lak;Vietnam;Hanoi;4A Le Thanh Tong Street, Phan Chu Trinh Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.022512;105.857567;30;true;true;Vietnamese;Spread over three floors, chef Madame Binh's venture in Hanoi opened its doors in 2018. It serves a similar menu to its sister establishment in Da Nang, but with a bigger selection plus seasonal offerings. The chef excels in imbuing traditional Vietnamese fare with unique character. Try her Sapa's pork belly dipped in herbal sauce, grilled to perfection and served with mắc mật leaves that cut through the richness and enliven the flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
5432;Phú Hồng;Vietnam;Da Nang;19 Yen Bai Street, Hai Chau 1 Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0696386;108.2229549;79;false;true;Street Food;You can smell the barbecue from a distance. Bún thịt nướng, or rice noodles with barbecue pork, is the must-try. Or go for barbecue with salad and rice paper – choose from pork, minced pork skewers, pork belly, and beef.;Cash only;[]
5433;Rang;Vietnam;Da Nang;384 Vo Nguyen Giap Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0430524;108.24779;89;false;false;Indian;Rang is the Hindi word for colour and splashes of colour adorn the room, including colourful curries in white, yellow, green and red. The owner-chefs are two brothers, born in India and raised in Australia. They received formal training in Western culinary arts and champion a nouvelle cuisine with international influences. Start with chicken tikka, tailed by dal tadka yellow curry with roti or naan. Rice lovers should try their biryani.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5434;Phở Minh;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;63/6 Pasteur Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.774904;106.7002701;97;false;false;Noodles;It may be tucked away down a narrow alley, but Phở Minh has been attracting hungry Saigonese with its traditional beef noodle soup since 1945. Choose between beef tenderloin, brisket and a variety of different cuts available on the day. With its flaky puff pastry and piping-hot meat filling, their freshly baked pâté chaud is a must. They close at 10am, so come early before the food runs out.;Cash only;[]
5436;Xới Cơm;Vietnam;Hanoi;107, Lane 36, Lang Ha Street, Lang Ha Ward, Dong Da District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0143203;105.813091;87;false;true;Vietnamese;Experience authentic Northern Vietnamese home cooking in this cosy restaurant, whose vintage interior is reminiscent of Hanoi houses in the 1980s and 1990s. The menu options vary daily, with simple yet delicious dishes like stir-fried water spinach with garlic and deep-fried tofu with green onion. A comfortable venue at eater-friendly prices, while the helpful staff is on hand to explain the Vietnamese menu in simple English.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5437;Phở Hoàng;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;460 Nguyen Tri Phuong Street, Ward 9, District 10, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.765992;106.667711;52;true;true;Noodles;This phở shop has been around since 2008 and the owner Mr Hoang is justly proud of his clear beef broth that takes over 12 hours to make. Feel free to customise your beef noodle soup by ordering tendon, flank, minced beef or even a raw egg on the side. Every bowl comes with garnishes like coriander, basil, lime wedges, onions and bean sprouts. For drinks, try their monk fruit herbal tea made with over 10 different herbs.;Cash only;[]
5438;Cơm Tấm Ba Ghiền;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;84 Dang Van Ngu Street, Ward 10, Phu Nhuan District, Ho Chi Minh City, 725000, Vietnam;10.79444;106.66935;37;false;true;Street Food;Since the 1990s, this unassuming stall has been serving what many locals consider to be the best cơm tấm (broken rice dish) in town. Their most popular version is steamed broken rice topped with pork chop marinated in a secret sauce and perfectly grilled over charcoal, along with pickled radish and sweet and sour fish sauce. There is a chicken version as well.;Cash only;[]
5439;Hum Garden;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;32 D10 Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.8042053;106.744484;49;true;false;Vegetarian;This attractive house with a pleasant courtyard, patio and quaint furnishings outside the city centre, nestles on a quiet street in a residential area. The Vietnamese-inspired vegetarian cuisine, rich in modern twists, uses mostly organic, fresh ingredients, sourced direct from farmers. The deep-fried mushroom rolls are simply out of this world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5440;Phở 10 Lý Quốc Sư (Hoan Kiem);Vietnam;Hanoi;10 Ly Quoc Su Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0305286;105.8488224;97;false;true;Noodles;One of three branches in Hanoi, this small phở eatery enjoys a fine reputation, but beware of imitations in the city. The menu offers 10 impressive phở options, including tái and chin (brisket), nạm (flank beef) and bắp trần (beef fillet). A competent team operates the compact corner kitchen, which is visible through a glazed partition. The phở itself is hearty and supremely refreshing with tender pieces of beef that melt in the mouth.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5441;Sol Kitchen & Bar;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;112 Ly Tu Trong Street, Ben Thanh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7742548;106.6975079;18;false;false;Latin American;A relaxed vibe provides the perfect foil to Latin-American recipes crafted by Adrian Chong Yen, a Malaysian chef who worked in Singapore for 12 years. His à la carte menu is eclectic and appetising, featuring empanadas from Mexico, scallop ceviche from Peru and burrata salad from Italy. Sol is also famous for its red meat, including marinated steak served with chimichurri sauce, BBQ ribs glazed with fish sauce, and whole roasted chicken served with mojo sauce.;;[]
5443;Indian Aroma Restaurant;Vietnam;Da Nang;24 An Thuong 6 Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.046911;108.24549;55;false;true;Indian;The restaurant boasts two hand-painted murals – one of Ha Long Bay and one of Hawa Mahal. An experienced Indian chef helms the kitchen and his extensive menu features iconic dishes from the north to the south of his homeland. Kick off your meal with a refreshing papadam dipped in mint chutney. Then try the saag ghosh, a lamb and spinach curry from Northern India, even better with garlic naan to mop up the creamy sauce.;Air conditioning;[]
5444;Mỳ Quảng Sứa Hồng Vân;Vietnam;Da Nang;59 Le Hong Phong Street, Phuoc Ninh Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0637402;108.2210287;55;true;true;Street Food;Open from 6am-1pm, this no-frills shop is packed with people craving their fix of mì quảng. The flavoursome orange-red broth is made with shrimps, and you can top your noodles with a choice of quail egg, pork, shrimp, meatball or springy jelly fish.;Cash only;[]
5445;Cuc Gach Quan;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;10 Dang Tat Street, Tan Dinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7930299;106.6892557;59;true;true;Vietnamese;The restaurant sports two dining rooms facing each other on the same street, flanked by a supremely relaxing koi pond and leafy garden. The menu is mostly traditional Vietnamese, such as đậu hũ chiên sả ớt (deep-fried tofu with finely chopped lemongrass), and the signature canh chua cá hú fish soup, rich in tangy sweetness. Make sure you save room for desserts like deep-fried banana or the sương sâm jelly with an intense herbal flavour.;Air conditioning;[]
5446;Izakaya;Croatia;Zagreb;Selska cesta 90b, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8047118;15.942948;93;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;Although not in a central location, this modern restaurant serving delicious, carefully prepared Japanese cuisine is situated in an area that has a lively evening atmosphere. Don’t miss the chef’s signature rolls, including the excellent Kanji Uramaki (with swordfish tartare) and Age Lobster roll (with lobster in panko bread). The pleasant outdoor space is perfect for an after-dinner cocktail.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5447;Konoba Malo Selo;Croatia;Buje;Fratrija 1, Buje, 52460, Croatia;45.4320136;13.6353543;66;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Meats and Grills;You’re immediately struck by the typical Istrian ambience at this restaurant, which occupies an old stone building with two small dining rooms and an outdoor space and boasts a fireplace used for traditional cooking. We recommend ordering half-portions here so that you can sample different specialities such as the excellent Istrian cured ham (unique in flavour thanks to the way it is aged in the Bora wind), home-made fuzi pasta or tagliatelle served with a mushroom sauce, and fillet of Fiorentina steak grilled over the open fire.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5448;Vuglec Breg;Croatia;Krapina;Škaričevo 151, Krapina, 49000, Croatia;46.149057;15.8396211;91;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Immersed in the countryside just a few minutes’ drive from the capital, this rural restaurant perched on the top of a hill also offers comfortable guestrooms and a modern swimming pool. The traditional regional cuisine includes local specialities such as Zagorska soup flavoured with mushrooms and bacon, and snails baked in the oven with butter and aromatic herbs. The wine produced by the family themselves is a must, as are the delicious desserts and ice creams.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5449;Tač;Croatia;Zagreb;Vrhovec 140, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8268053;15.9476092;17;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Situated on Vrhovec hill in a residential area not far from the city centre, this restaurant run by the Miletić family seems more like a private home than a conventional restaurant. There’s no menu – instead, whatever dishes the kitchen has prepared that day are announced at your table. Options often include fish carpaccio or tartare, fresh scampi from the Adriatic and locally reared meat, all served in traditional recipes that are generous both in flavour and portion size. Sharing dishes is normal practice here, which adds to the enjoyment of the experience. The wines are from Croatia or its near neighbours – again, there’s no wine list but staff are happy to make recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5450;Beštija;Croatia;Zagreb;Masarykova Ulica  11/1, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.810785;15.9729381;52;false;true;Farm to table, Contemporary;Occupying the courtyard of a building in the city centre, this pleasant bistro is simply decorated in a mix of traditional and contemporary styles and attracts a young, mixed crowd. The cuisine, heavily inspired by market availability and Croatian produce, showcases precise, aesthetically pleasing presentation and generous portions, using numerous yet carefully balanced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
5452;Fakin;Croatia;Legrad;Trg Svetog Trojstva 53, Legrad, 48317, Croatia;46.2983292;16.8555191;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Ever since it opened a few years ago, this restaurant has helped to raise the profile of Legrad, a village in northern Croatia. Situated next to the church, the restaurant overlooks the village square and boasts a spacious terrace that is very popular on summer evenings. The interior decor has the same simple, elegant and modern feel as the cuisine, which features dishes from Croatia and Central Europe. Local ingredients plus delicious clean flavours, a hint of creativity and reasonable prices all add to the appeal. The smoked trout with horseradish mousse, barley popcorn and pumpkin oil is excellent. The 11 guestrooms are particularly popular with cyclists, as Legrad is the start and finish of one of Croatia’s popular cycling routes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5453;Konoba Mate;Croatia;Korcula;Pupnat 28, Korcula, 20260, Croatia;42.9508141;17.037417;76;true;true;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;This traditional inn situated in the small village of Pupnat, about 10km from Korčula, is run by a friendly and welcoming family. The menu features charcuterie produced by the family, goat’s cheese matured on site, home-grown vegetables and local wine and olive oil. One of the most delicious dishes is the home-made ravioli with goat’s cheese and sage sauce. The covered terrace is particularly attractive with its solid wood tables and lighting provided by lanterns.;Terrace;[]
5454;Batelina;Croatia;Banjole;Čimulje 25, Banjole, 52100, Croatia;44.82483;13.866587;23;true;false;Seafood;Although advance booking is required and the restaurant doesn’t take credit cards, Batelina’s fame extends well beyond Istria, and for good reason – for the past 20 years, this inn run by owner-chef and fisherman Danilo Skoko has been renowned for the high quality of its freshly caught fish. The focus here is on using the fish in its entirety, from the prestigious cuts and fillets to the entrails which are transformed into delicious appetisers.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5455;Alla Beccaccia;Croatia;Valbandon;ul. Pineta 25, Valbandon, 52212, Croatia;44.91547;13.824558;32;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;A typical example of an Istrian “konoba” (tavern). The fireplace that dominates the cosy, rustic dining room is not merely decorative, while the service here is friendly and attentive and the cuisine delicious. Although the menu often includes different types of game, the restaurant takes its name from the house speciality (“beccaccia” is the Italian for woodcock) – this takes a long time to prepare and so must be ordered in advance. Fresh pasta, home-made desserts and generous portions all add to the appeal.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5456;Konoba Vinko;Croatia;Konjevrate;Uz Cestu 57, Konjevrate, 22221, Croatia;43.7830965;16.014193;49;true;false;Country cooking;A well-run and welcoming country inn where meat takes pride of place on the menu. The simple, delicious cuisine is generously portioned and includes stand-out specialities such as suckling pig. In summer, there’s also a charming outdoor space for which booking in advance is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5457;Fico;;Singapore;1300 East Coast Parkway, 468964, Singapore;1.3105224;103.9463853;49;true;false;Italian;This white house styled after a masseria in Puglia is sited within East Coast Park. The sprawling lawn, spectacular ocean views and sound of the waves all exude a soothing vibe. The Pugliese chef is keen to bring authentic cuisine from his homeland to Singapore, of which focaccina and pasta made from scratch are the highlights. Try his San Marzano tomato focaccina with mozzarella and fresh basil, bursting with intense flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
5458;Lian He Ben Ji Claypot;;Singapore;Chinatown Complex Market & Food Centre, #02-198/199, 335 Smith Street, 050335, Singapore;1.2821566;103.8433055;92;false;true;Street Food;It takes 30 minutes to cook but is more than worth the wait. The rice, cooked in a claypot over charcoal, exudes smokiness with a crispy scorched crust on the bottom. For toppings, choose between chicken, preserved pork and/or sausage.;;[]
5460;Soon Huat;;Singapore;North Bridge Road Market & Food Centre, #01-105, 861 North Bridge Road, 198783, Singapore;1.3058048;103.8636367;55;true;true;Street Food;Choose between "dry" and soup noodles topped with butterflied prawns, fish cake, bean sprouts and fried garlic. The flavoursome prawn soup on the side is also a treat. Not a fan of prawns? Try the pork ribs noodles instead.;Cash only;[]
5461;Heng Heng Cooked Food;;Singapore;Yuhua Village Market and Food Centre, #01-12, Blk 254, Jurong East Street 24, 600254, Singapore;1.343566;103.7380985;17;true;false;Street Food;Both the laksa and prawn mee are made to order and come in three sizes. Their hallmark laksa is doused in a rich aromatic broth and topped with prawns, fried fish cake, fried tofu and cockles.;Cash only;[]
5462;Zhup Zhup;;Singapore;#01-01, 458 MacPherson Road, 368176, Singapore;1.3319636;103.8824999;22;false;true;Noodles;Formerly One Prawn & Co, Zhup Zhup still sees constant queues forming beneath its red awning. Book ahead to cut your wait time. The signature prawn noodles come in a set: a bowl of noodles plus rich prawn soup in a claypot. Out of the four types of noodles, the classic option is yellow noodles with thin bee hoon. The soup is loaded with flavours, imparted in particular by the tomalley of countless prawn heads.;;[]
5463;Fei Fei Roasted • Noodle;;Singapore;Yuhua Village Market and Food Centre, #01-28, Blk 254, Jurong East Street 24, 600254, Singapore;1.3436537;103.7376562;62;true;true;Street Food;Popular stall for roasted meat and dumplings. Duck leg with shrimp wonton noodles is recommended. Come early before the food runs out.;Cash only;[]
5464;The Coconut Club (Beach Road);;Singapore;269 Beach Road, 199546, Singapore;1.3006534;103.8601437;30;false;true;Malaysian;This whitewashed traditional shophouse evokes unmistakably tropical vibes – wicker back chairs, wallpaper with banana leaf prints and cheerful blue-and-white tiled flooring. On the menu, the coconut theme is also obvious – the nasi lemak set is the best seller, but other dishes deserve equal attention too, such as ayam goreng berempah (spiced fried chicken with crispy rempah crumbs), and sago pudding with pandan, palm sugar and coconut cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5465;Fu Ming Cooked Food;;Singapore;Redhill Market, #01-49, 85 Redhill Lane, 150085, Singapore;1.2874936;103.8183732;57;false;false;Street Food;Homemade black and white carrot cake is served. The black one with dark soya sauce is crispy and tasty.;Cash only;[]
5466;Jian Bo Tiong Bahru Shui Kueh;;Singapore;Jurong West 505 Market & Food Centre, #01-27, Blk 505, Jurong West Street 52, 640505, Singapore;1.3492969;103.7183594;62;true;false;Street Food;The rice cake with a sauce of preserved vegetables, sesame, dried shrimp and chilli is spicy and delicious.;Cash only;[]
5467;Cheok Kee;;Singapore;Geylang Bahru Market & Food Centre, #01-35, 69 Geylang Bahru, 330069, Singapore;1.32144;103.870173;45;false;false;Street Food;Its famous soy-marinated duck boasts velvety flesh on a bed of steamed rice perfumed by duck scents. It comes with chilli vinegar that aptly cuts through the richness, plus an aromatic duck soup made with Chinese herbs.;Cash only;[]
5468;Singapore Fried Hokkien Mee;;Singapore;Whampoa Makan Place, #01-32, 90/91 Whampoa Drive 91, 320091, Singapore;1.3230892;103.8549053;44;false;false;Street Food;Their famous Hokkien mee is made with rice vermicelli and yellow egg noodles, which are topped with prawns and squid for that umami flavour – even better with a helping of spicy homemade chilli sauce.;;[]
5470;Cumi Bali;;Singapore;50 Tras Street, 078989, Singapore;1.2781933;103.8442371;44;false;false;Indonesian;Relocated to Tras Street in 2021, this friendly restaurant serves authentic Indonesian cooking in a room enhanced by artifacts and bamboo-styled furnishings. The signature whole grilled squid Cumi Bali – succulent and springy in texture – gives the restaurant its name. It is particularly delicious in their prized homemade sauce made with a myriad of natural spices. Nasi Kunyit is a rice dish jazzed up by 11 spices such as turmeric, cinnamon and pandan leaves.;Air conditioning;[]
5471;Lagnaa;;Singapore;6 Upper Dickson Road, 207466, Singapore;1.306444;103.8522508;69;true;true;Indian;You can specify the level of spiciness of your food at this three-storey restaurant in Little India, though many come for the Chilli Challenge on full moon nights simply to push their limit. But spiciness isn’t all that this chef has to offer – in fact, he balances it with sweet, sour, salty, bitter and astringent flavours. Choose between table seating downstairs and floor seating upstairs. Parties of two have a number of set menus to choose from.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
5472;Fool;;Singapore;21 Boon Tat Street, 069620, Singapore;1.2812755;103.8485355;50;false;true;European Contemporary;This lively wine bar concept is another brainchild of the chef-owner behind Cloudstreet and Kotuwa. The décor is on trend with a retro 1970s look. The wine list is extensive and well-choreographed, with a slight bias towards older vintages. Pair your wine with snacks and small plates hallmarked by precise execution, beguiling presentations and pronounced flavours. In particular, the chicken liver éclair with date and Madeira is not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
5473;Lai Heng Handmade Teochew Kueh;;Singapore;Yuhua Market & Hawker Centre, #01-218, Blk 347, Jurong East Avenue 1, Jurong East, 600347, Singapore;1.3452103;103.7310891;17;true;false;Street Food;(The hawker center it locates is temporarily closed.) Handmade Teochew kueh with various flavours. Steamed or pan-fried versions available.;;[]
5475;Margaret Drive Sin Kee Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Block 40, Stall 5, #01-39, Holland Drive, 270040, Singapore;1.3082682;103.7929491;30;false;false;Street Food;Since this stall opened on Margaret Drive years ago, their chicken rice has been made the same way. The juicy, tender meat is served with aromatic oil rice and an addictive ground ginger sauce. The gizzards are equally good.;;[]
5476;J2 Famous Crispy Curry Puff;;Singapore;Amoy Street Food Centre, #01-21, 7 Maxwell Road, 069111, Singapore;1.2796129;103.8468008;35;false;true;Street Food;The curry puff comes in four flavours, all wrapped in a flaky, crispy pastry crust. As well as the classic chicken and potato curry, try the black pepper chicken, sweet taro or chilli sardine-filled pastry.;Cash only;[]
5477;Indocafé;;Singapore;35 Scotts Road, 228227, Singapore;1.3110605;103.8356878;25;true;false;Peranakan;Dark wood furniture and antiques add to the elegant colonial spirit of this restaurant nestled in a bungalow, also known as ‘The White House’. The menu offers Peranakan cuisine and the dishes look deceptively simple, but involve subtly blended spices and seasoning. Wagyu beef rendang uses the cheek cut for tenderness, while spices, fermented shrimp paste, chilli and coconut milk underscore the rich, deep flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5478;Anglo Indian (Shenton Way);;Singapore;#01-08, 1 Shenton Way, 068803, Singapore;1.279361;103.85043;16;false;false;Indian;If there’s one dish that customers should expect to find in a restaurant called Anglo Indian it’s chicken tikka masala – and sure enough it’s a firm favourite of many here at this simply decorated spot in the heart of the CBD. The dining room may seat only 20, but there’s a large outdoor terrace where everyone congregates for the well-priced cooking. Other popular choices include butter chicken and mutton dum biryani.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5480;Kwang Kee Teochew Fish Porridge;;Singapore;Newton Food Centre, #01-20, 500 Clemenceau Avenue North, 229495, Singapore;1.3118717;103.8393125;100;false;true;Street Food;Fish porridge and fried fish bee hoon. The porridge is sweet with abundant fish fillets.;Cash only;[]
5483;True Blue Cuisine;;Singapore;47/49 Armenian Street, 179937, Singapore;1.2945379;103.8494194;16;true;true;Peranakan;It’s less like walking into a restaurant, more like falling into the warm embrace of a much loved family member. Here it’s about nostalgia and paying homage to the food, history and customs of the Peranakans – you’ll find all the classic dishes, prepared in an authentic way, and the hard part is narrowing down your choice. The setting really is unique and the Ayam Buah Keluak is one of the signature.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5484;Ji De Lai Hainanese Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Chong Pang Market and Food Centre, #01-152, 105 Yishun Ring Road, 760105, Singapore;1.4319385;103.8279349;94;false;true;Street Food;Hainanese chicken rice comes with options like roasted or steamed chicken. Sets with rice, soup and vegetables are reasonably priced.;;[]
5485;Song Fa Bak Kut Teh (New Bridge Road);;Singapore;#01-01, 11 New Bridge Road, 059386, Singapore;1.2890223;103.8477147;56;false;false;Singaporean;Much has changed since Mr Yeo started selling bak kut teh from his pushcart in Johor Road back in the late ’60s – nowadays it’s the second generation of the family who are running the show. They are still selling their celebrated pork ribs and peppery broth but are now doing so from 10+ shops – and this one, the simplest, seems to be the best. Queue, order, pay, and then tuck into your soup – when you’ve finished they’ll top it up for you.;Air conditioning;[]
5486;Yhingthai Palace;;Singapore;#01-04, 36 Purvis Street, 188613, Singapore;1.29648;103.85497;91;false;true;Thai;Founded in the 1990s by a couple with a passion for Thai cuisine, this restaurant is spread over three colourful Thai-style rooms. Added authenticity comes courtesy of the helpful waitresses in traditional dress. The Thai and Thai-Chinese dishes are prepared with fresh ingredients sourced daily. Start your meal with som tom: papaya salad with dried shrimps and peanuts. Consider ordering the set if you find the lengthy à la carte menu hard to navigate.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
5487;Beach Road Fish Head Bee Hoon;;Singapore;Whampoa Makan Place, #01-46, 90/91 Whampoa Drive 91, 320091, Singapore;1.3232442;103.8548346;56;true;true;Street Food;The sliced fish bee hoon (rice vermicelli) comes in a flavourful, milky fish stock, with fried garlic bits for extra fragrance and crunch. Also worth trying are the tom yam soup, seafood soup and fried fish head bee hoon.;;[]
5488;Yong Chun Wan Ton Noodle;;Singapore;115 Bukit Merah View Market & Hawker Centre, #01-56, Blk 115 Bukit Merah View, 151115, Singapore;1.285599;103.82203;74;true;true;Street Food;The owner has his springy eggy noodles tailor-made. They are best enjoyed in its “dry” form – blanched and dressed in a savoury sweet sauce. Wonton with minced pork is fresh and firm.;Cash only;[]
5489;Lixin Teochew Fishball Noodles;;Singapore;Kim Keat Palm Market & Food Centre, #01-20, Blk 19 Toa Payoh Lor 7, 310019, Singapore;1.3352759;103.8569441;91;false;true;Street Food;The owner makes the fish balls by hand to ensure they are springy and bursting with umami. Blanched noodles tossed in chilli sauce with crispy cracklings are the perfect companion to the fish ball soup.;Cash only;[]
5490;Bismillah Biryani;;Singapore;50 Dunlop Street, 209379, Singapore;1.304989;103.8536;67;false;false;Street Food;Biryani is the standout dish in this place specialising in North Indian food. The lamb shank biryani is recommended for its fork-tender texture and meaty flavour. Haleem, mutton nihari and aloo gobi are also good choices.;;[]
5491;Jalan Sultan Prawn Mee;;Singapore;2 Jalan Ayer, Lorong 1 Geylang, 389141, Singapore;1.3111924;103.8727709;23;false;true;Street Food;In operation for over 70 years, this place serves aromatic dry prawn mee in sambal with heaps of fried scallion and depth. The soup version has a prawn broth loaded with natural umami. Choose from three kinds of noodles.;Cash only;[]
5492;Na Na Curry;;Singapore;115 Bukit Merah View Market & Hawker Centre, #01-47, Blk 115 Bukit Merah View, 151115, Singapore;1.285599;103.82203;36;false;false;Street Food;The fish head curry with eggplant, okra and tofu puff stands out with its aromatic spice paste made from scratch, paired with a hint of coconut milk. The fish, lamb and chicken curry are also popular.;;[]
5493;Alliance Seafood;;Singapore;Newton Food Centre, #01-27, 500 Clemenceau Avenue North, 229495, Singapore;1.3121151;103.8395393;85;true;true;Street Food;BBQ seafood such as tiger prawn and cereal prawn. Don't miss the chilli crab or the black pepper crab made using the live crustacean.;;[]
5494;Heng;;Singapore;Newton Food Centre, #01-28, 500 Clemenceau Avenue North, 229495, Singapore;1.3120674;103.8393122;63;false;false;Street Food;The owner has 50+ years-experience serving sweet and savoury carrot cakes. Fried oysters and oyster omelettes are also worth a try.;;[]
5495;Sik Bao Sin (Desmond's Creation);;Singapore;592 Geylang Road, 389531, Singapore;1.314127;103.8878;16;false;true;Singaporean;The second-generation owner-chef makes every dish according to traditional recipes for guaranteed authenticity. The concise menu only features 13 items, but seasonal dishes, not on the menu, are also available. The chef’s signature dish, sweet and sour pork, is made to order, so expect to wait. The ginger chicken is simply divine – tender chicken glazed in a mild chilli sauce alongside zesty pickled ginger shoots. Also, try the kale with prawns.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
5496;Muthu's Curry;;Singapore;#01-01, 138 Race Course Road, 218591, Singapore;1.30965;103.85204;68;true;true;Indian;‘Muthu’ means pearl in Tamil, which befits this gem (with another branche) serving traditional dishes from both the Southern and Northern regions of India. Originally called Muthu Makkan, the owner expanded and renamed the restaurant in 1982. The signature fish head, South Indian-style, uses a secret blend of spices. Swimmer crabs, masala prawns, lamb rack and tandoori chicken are also big hits among diners. Ask about the monthly specials.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5499;Han Kee;;Singapore;Amoy Street Food Centre, #02-129, 7 Maxwell Road, 069111, Singapore;1.2796254;103.8467276;49;false;false;Street Food;There is always a queue at this stall famous for umami-laden soup made with mackerel. Enjoy the soup on its own, or use it as a rich base for porridge or bee hoon with sliced fish or fish head. Come early to beat the crowd.;Cash only;[]
5500;Delhi Lahori;;Singapore;Tekka Centre, #01-266, 665 Buffalo Road, 210665, Singapore;1.3064407;103.8507102;43;false;false;Street Food;The experienced tandoor master knows his clay oven inside out. His fluffy, crispy naans have a loyal following. His grilled-to-order seekh kebab and chicken tikka masala are also exceptional and come in generous portions.;Cash only;[]
5501;Un-Yang-Kor-Dai;;Singapore;#01-02, 57 South Bridge Road, 058688, Singapore;1.2872095;103.8483084;96;false;true;Thai;Though its name means ‘anything goes’, this restaurant is exceptionally specific about the food it serves – Isan cuisine hailing from north-eastern Thailand and famous for its infernal heat. The PenLaos signature chicken is marinated with white peppercorns and coriander for three days before being grilled to perfection. Leng zaab is pork ribs in a spicy sour broth that is simply addictive. Ask for the house-made Isan tamarind dip to dunk the pork in.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5502;Tian Tian Hainanese Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Maxwell Food Centre, #01-10/11, 1 Kadayanallur Street, 069184, Singapore;1.2804903;103.8448118;85;false;false;Street Food;Expect a long queue, but the velvety chicken with springy skin is worth the wait. Even the aromatic oil rice and briny-sweet sauce are perfectly made. Consider ordering half a chicken to share, or an extra drumstick.;Cash only;[]
5503;Eminent Frog Porridge & Seafood (Lor 19);;Singapore;Geylang Lorong 19, 323 Geylang Road, 389359, Singapore;1.3127778;103.8792564;34;false;false;Street Food;Frog is certainly big on the menu – besides the famous frog porridge, try frog fried with ginger and scallion or tossed in Kung Pao sauce. A favourite spot among locals for late-night supper, this place is always packed, so be prepared to wait.;Cash only;[]
5504;Ar Er Soup;;Singapore;ABC Brickworks Market & Food Centre, #01-141, Blk 6 Jalan Bukit Merah, 150006, Singapore;1.2868701;103.8081238;21;false;true;Street Food;Offers 8 kinds of MSG-free long-boiled soups, served with pumpkin rice.;Cash only;[]
5505;Hong Kong Yummy Soup;;Singapore;Alexandra Village Food Centre, #01-51, Blk 120 Bukit Merah Lane 1, 150120, Singapore;1.2863998;103.8044992;52;true;false;Street Food;Here, the second generation of the family sells local-style salad with pineapple, cucumber and deep-fried dough stick, tossed in a special home-made sauce and sprinkled with ground peanuts. Chilli is optional.;;[]
5506;A Noodle Story;;Singapore;Amoy Street Food Centre, #01-39, 7 Maxwell Road, 069111, Singapore;1.2790364;103.8464494;89;false;false;Street Food;The stall has an interesting look and sells local, traditional noodles cooked in an innovative way.;;[]
5507;Chuan Kee Boneless Braised Duck;;Singapore;20 Ghim Moh Road Market & Food Centre, #01-04, Blk 20, Ghim Moh Road, 270020, Singapore;1.3110244;103.788126;38;false;true;Street Food;Juicy and flavoursome braised duck is served with rice, congee, kway teow or noodles, plus optional extras such as duck gizzard, duck liver or marinated egg. The "set" comes with a bowl of bak kut teh.;;[]
5508;Soh Kee Cooked Food;;Singapore;Jurong West 505 Market & Food Centre, #01-44, Blk 505, Jurong West Street 52, 640505, Singapore;1.3498361;103.7184176;94;false;true;Street Food;Serves porridge with chicken, fish or cuttlefish. Sets for one to three people are also available.;Cash only;[]
5509;Tai Wah Pork Noodle;;Singapore;Hong Lim Market and Food Centre, #02-16, Blk 531A, Upper Cross Street, 051531, Singapore;1.2852332;103.8457532;37;false;false;Street Food;Noodles served with soup meat balls, dried fish and pork liver.;;[]
5510;Outram Park Fried Kway Teow Mee;;Singapore;Hong Lim Market and Food Centre, #02-17, Blk 531A, Upper Cross Street, 051531, Singapore;1.2851585;103.8457139;49;true;false;Street Food;The Kway Teow is fried with a dark sauce you can add cockles to the noodles. Always a long queue.;;[]
5511;Hoo Kee Bak Chang;;Singapore;Amoy Street Food Centre, #01-18, 7 Maxwell Road, 069111, Singapore;1.2789952;103.8466824;45;true;true;Street Food;Glutinous rice mixed with salted duck egg yolk pork and chestnut wrapped with bamboo leaf.;;[]
5512;Kelantan Kway Chap · Pig Organ Soup;;Singapore;Berseh Food Centre, #02-39, 166 Jalan Besar, 208877, Singapore;1.3073595;103.85674;41;true;false;Street Food;Pork cuts and offal like belly, trotter, intestines and skin are cooked in a soy-based marinade with spices. The depth and rich flavours of the meat are the perfect accompaniment to the kway chap ribbon noodles.;Cash only;[]
5513;Chey Sua Carrot Cake;;Singapore;127 Toa Payoh West Market & Food Centre, #02-30, Blk 127, Lorong 1 Toa Payoh, 310127, Singapore;1.3380791;103.8447178;28;false;true;Street Food;The pan-fried radish cake is hugely popular. Fried on one side until golden, it allows you to taste the caramelised crispy bits and the soft moist cake at the same time. The cakes are fried to order, so expect a longer waiting time.;;[]
5514;Adam Rd Noo Cheng Big Prawn Noodle;;Singapore;Adam Food Centre, #01-27, 2 Adam Road, 289876, Singapore;1.324031;103.814139;45;true;true;Street Food;The prawn mee cooked à la minute is a recipe from the owner’s father. Opt for “dry” noodles tossed in prawn paste of your desired level of heat, alongside a bowl of prawn soup. Toppings like pig skin add contrasting textures.;Cash only;[]
5516;Chai Chuan Tou Yang Rou Tang;;Singapore;115 Bukit Merah View Market & Hawker Centre, #01-51, Blk 115 Bukit Merah View, 151115, Singapore;1.2856243;103.8220326;44;false;true;Street Food;The mutton soup here can be paired with tripe, meatballs, tendon or even brain. The mutton boasts the right mix of fatty and lean meat, without tasting gamey. The broth has a mildly herbal flavour. Come early as they tend to sell out.;;[]
5519;Tai Seng Fish Soup;;Singapore;Taman Jurong Market & Food Centre, #03-145, 3 Yung Sheng Road, Jurong West, 618499, Singapore;1.3348723;103.7215061;54;false;false;Street Food;This third-generation family business prides itself on its flavoursome fish soup made from scratch and served with sliced fish, deep-fried fish or fish head. Order noodles, rice or congee on the side for a complete meal.;Cash only;[]
5520;Hai Nan Xing Zhou Beef Noodle;;Singapore;Kim Keat Palm Market & Food Centre, #01-06, 22 Lorong 7 Toa Payoh, 310022, Singapore;1.3355032;103.857018;23;true;false;Street Food;Choose between blanched rice noodles tossed in a thick gravy, or soup noodles in a deeply flavourful ox bone broth. Then top with sliced beef, beef tripe, tendon, beef balls, or a combination.;Cash only;[]
5522;Heng Kee;;Singapore;Hong Lim Market and Food Centre, #01-58, Blk 531A, Upper Cross Street, 051531, Singapore;1.2851492;103.8457218;67;true;false;Street Food;This stall, founded in the 1970s, is now run by the second-generation owner. Its hallmark dishes are mild, well-balanced curry broth, custom-made tofu puffs and fish cakes, as well as generous helpings of velvety chicken.;Cash only;[]
5523;Da Shi Jia Big Prawn Mee;;Singapore;89 Killiney Road, 239534, Singapore;1.298469;103.8389954;86;false;true;Singaporean;Guests are spoiled for choices here. First, pick between prawn noodle soup and fried prawn bee hoon. For prawn mee, specify the size of these wild-caught marine crustaceans – from regular to XXL. Then pick your noodles –the yellow variety, kway teow, bee hoon, or any combination of those. For real big eaters, choose extra toppings of fish cake, pork ribs or sliced pork. Don’t forget about snacks like tofu skin prawn rolls and fried prawn balls on the side.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5524;Hong Heng Fried Sotong Prawn Mee;;Singapore;Tiong Bahru Market, #02-01, 30 Seng Poh Road, 168898, Singapore;1.2849649;103.8327193;25;false;false;Street Food;Cooked-to-order, the noodles stir-fried with sliced fish, squid and prawn and served with homemade chilli sauce is a favourite.;;[]
5525;Joo Siah Bak Koot Teh;;Singapore;Blk 349, #01-1215 Jurong East Avenue 1, 600349, Singapore;1.3445639;103.7313626;62;true;false;Street Food;The signature dish here is pepper-flavoured bak kut teh. The soft pork rib goes well with chilli soy sauce. Earlier closing hours on Sunday.;Cash only;[]
5526;Bahrakath Mutton Soup;;Singapore;Adam Food Centre, #01-10, 2 Adam Road, 289876, Singapore;1.324031;103.814139;64;false;true;Street Food;Since 1973, this stall has been serving its secret mutton soup recipe. The broth is rich, dense, and full of herbal flavours. Apart from the popular leg, also try other lamb cuts. Order bread to mop up the broth.;;[]
5527;No.18 Zion Road Fried Kway Teow;;Singapore;Zion Riverside Food Centre, #017, 70 Zion Road, 247792, Singapore;1.292604;103.8312625;49;false;false;Street Food;Kway teow noodles are fried to order and topped with fish cake and cockles. The wok hei impresses with its robust flavours and a hint of spiciness, while the cockles impart extra umami. The wait can be long, but is well worth it.;;[]
5528;Zhi Wei Xian Zion Road Big Prawn Noodle;;Singapore;Zion Riverside Food Centre, #04, 70 Zion Road, 247792, Singapore;1.2924249;103.8312898;96;false;true;Street Food;The soup has a rich prawn flavour. Fresh prawns, chili and pork rinds combine to make a great bowl of noodles.;;[]
5529;Hai Nan Zai;;Singapore;Chong Pang Market and Food Centre, #01-129, 105 Yishun Ring Road, 760105, Singapore;1.4318206;103.8279671;34;true;false;Street Food;Singaporean food such as oyster omelettes, fried prawn mee and carrot cakes. Fried kway teow with cockles and Chinese sausage are cooked-to-order.;;[]
5530;Whole Earth;;Singapore;76 Peck Seah Street, 079331, Singapore;1.2772625;103.8446935;65;true;true;Vegetarian;‘Vegetarian cuisine for non-vegetarians’ is how the team describes their longstanding Thai and Peranakan restaurant. Meat-like textures and flavours are achieved by clever preparations of soy product and tofu. The tangy, crispy mango tamarind tofu roll is jazzed up with Penang rendang, herbs and spices, while the mushrooms deliver a texture that is almost indistinguishable from meat. The cosy interior is simple and bright. Portions big enough to share.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5531;Zai Shun Curry Fish Head;;Singapore;#01-205, 253 Jurong East Steet 24, 600253, Singapore;1.343888;103.73722;37;true;false;Street Food;The fish head curry boasts velvety flesh loaded with umami and is hot and spicy, perfect with steamed rice. Besides its eponymous dish, other equally stunning fish dishes and stir-fries are also available.;Cash only;[]
5532;Koh Brother Pig's Organ Soup;;Singapore;Tiong Bahru Market, #02-29, 30 Seng Poh Road, 168898, Singapore;1.2850432;103.832764;27;true;true;Street Food;Provides a wide range of pork offal like liver, chitterlings and tripe in pepper-flavoured stock.;;[]
5533;Shi Hui Yuan;;Singapore;Mei Ling Market & Food Centre, #02-33, 159 Mei Chin Road, 140159, Singapore;1.2932111;103.8031083;45;true;true;Street Food;Thin, smooth rice noodles and gravy - with chicken, duck or chicken feet toppings.;Cash only;[]
5534;Hui Wei Chilli Ban Mian;;Singapore;Geylang Bahru Market & Food Centre, #01-58, 69 Geylang Bahru, 330069, Singapore;1.32144;103.870173;75;true;true;Street Food;Ribbon noodles made in the stall are served in soup or "dry" – tossed in home-made chilli sauce and topped with minced meat, meatballs, poached egg and fried lard. You can also opt for e-fu or ramen noodles instead.;Cash only;[]
5535;Ru Ji Kitchen;;Singapore;Holland Drive Market & Food Centre, #02-28/29, 44 Holland Drive, 270044, Singapore;1.3081582;103.7928826;73;false;true;Street Food;Two adjoining stalls sell noodle soup or "dry" noodles with minced pork, pork balls or fish balls handmade on the spot. The bouncy-textured, deep-flavoured fish balls made with yellowtail are especially popular.;;[]
5536;Tiong Bahru Hainanese Boneless Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Tiong Bahru Market, #02-82, 30 Seng Poh Road, 168898, Singapore;1.2846286;103.832596;51;true;false;Street Food;The rice that comes with the signature Hainanese boneless chicken imparts a mild turmeric aroma. Tender juicy meat, without too much fat under the bouncy, gelatinous skin. The roast chicken is also recommended.;;[]
5537;Song Fish Soup;;Singapore;Clementi 448 Food Centre, #01-38, 448 Clementi Ave 3, 120448, Singapore;1.313468;103.76461;65;true;true;Street Food;The menu offers blanched sliced fish, deep-fried fish and fish maw, either in fish broth or bee hoon soup. Fish maw double fish soup lets you sample three items at once. Fish head, clams and shrimps are also available.;Cash only;[]
5538;Hewelke;Poland;Gdansk;Jana Kilińskiego 7, Gdansk, 80-452, Poland;54.3829347;18.6081502;21;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Gdańsk’s famous brewer and astronomer Johannes Hevelius lends a variant of his surname to this trendy spot situated in, appropriately enough, a former brewery. The stylish décor includes a vaulted brick ceiling, exposed steel support columns and the odd flash of neon. A bakery by day, in the evening it becomes a restaurant where the cooking adopts global influences, including pan-Asian elements ranging from tom kha to the rightly popular Peking duck. In a nod to Hevelius, the cocktails are named after the planets.;;[]
5539;SPOT.;Poland;Poznan;Dolna Wilda 87, Poznan, 61 501, Poland;52.3889711;16.9242786;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A 19th Century power plant on the edge of Jana Pawla II Park is home to this faux industrial style restaurant. Sit on the terrace overlooking the row of chardonnay vines as you sample something from the exceptional wine list – which champions all things natural and biodynamic, including over 75 native wines. The menu makes a feature of house-smoked ingredients, such as terrific, meaty duck in the beetroot salad. The cooking comes with the added bonus of attractive pricing and generous portions.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5541;Vinissimo;Poland;Sopot;Generała Józefa Bema 6, Sopot, 81-753, Poland;54.443559;18.5674248;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The clue’s in the name: wine takes centre stage at this simply styled and bang on-trend bar-cum-restaurant. On-sale bottles can be glimpsed around the room, while the list contains plenty of great options by the glass. The menu is filled with good value dishes like skrei cod croquettes, which both deliver bags of flavour and show a wise restraint from the kitchen team. Instead of throwing unnecessary ingredients into the mix, they focus on a clean, balanced style of cooking.;Air conditioning;[]
5543;Kieliszki na Próżnej;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Próżna 12, Warsaw, 00 107, Poland;52.2364549;21.0046741;93;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A huge, gravity-defying rack of wine glasses is the first thing you notice when you arrive at this friendly wine bar and bistro. Next, it’s the striking black and white wildlife mural filling one wall. The appealing menus represent good value, especially at lunchtime, and include hearty dishes that are bursting with bold and punchy flavours. An extensive wine list offers plenty of great quality choices to fill all those glasses with, but ‘bring your own’ is welcome too.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5545;MOLÁM;Poland;Krakow;ul. Rajska 3/4, Krakow, 31 124, Poland;50.0648387;19.9276183;36;true;false;Thai;A fun evening out is on the cards at this lively spot inspired by the night canteens of Bangkok. An open kitchen and vintage vibe contribute to the party atmosphere, which is helped along by a range of Thai-inspired cocktails. The authentic menu covers all four regions of Thailand, with vibrant dishes delivering the hallmark blend of sweet, sour, spicy and salty. Sharing is encouraged and the dishes are well-priced, so don’t hold back when ordering.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5546;Treinta y Tres;Poland;Gdansk;Olivia Centre, Aleja Grunwaldzka 472c, Gdansk, 80-309, Poland;54.40351;18.57083;43;true;false;Spanish;The 33rd floor of the Olivia Centre skyscraper provides spectacular panoramic views for this buzzing restaurant where Spanish guitar music soundtracks your visit. The cooking has a similar tone, with a selection of classic tapas to begin – the Ibérico ham croquetas are terrific – before a choice of main dishes. If you’re dining with company, the 800g lobster rice for two is the most eye-catching option on the menu. A genuine warmth from the service team and a comprehensive, largely Spanish wine list complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
5547;Le Braci;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Górnośląska 24, Warsaw, 00 484, Poland;52.2243896;21.028538;88;true;false;Italian;There's a clubby feel to this intimate Italian restaurant thanks to its zinc-topped bar, high ceiling and dark green colour scheme. The appealing Italian menu covers all regions, with dishes proving to be authentic and full of flavour – especially the impressively precise homemade pasta. A superb range of wines includes those from small Italian producers and lesser-seen regions. Charming service helps to create a welcoming atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5548;Folga;Poland;Krakow;ul. Estery 12, Krakow, 31-056, Poland;50.05186;19.94532;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located in the trendy Plac Nowy square in the city’s historic Jewish Quarter of Kazimierz, this busy and buoyant restaurant adopts a chic brasserie-style aesthetic with high-top tables and a terrace that’s ideal for the summertime. The menu showcases appealing variety, with the globally influenced dishes ranging from oysters to arancini and tempura to ceviche. Whatever you choose, there’s a unifying theme of sensible pricing and quality execution from the kitchen team.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5549;1911 Restaurant;Poland;Sopot;ul. Grunwaldzka 4/6, Sopot, 81-759, Poland;54.4444791;18.5693435;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Hidden behind an unassuming façade, you'll find this smart modern bistro with a team that’s eager to please and food that offers fabulous value for money. The concise menu makes sure the kitchen doesn’t overstretch but instead packs heaps of flavour into every unfussy dish, be it shrimp toast or fried skrei cod. Desserts are a highlight, with the kitchen’s creative streak coming through in the likes of milled cornflake ice cream.;Air conditioning;[]
5550;alewino;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Mokotowska 48, Warsaw, 00 543, Poland;52.2252094;21.0220599;23;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Spread across various rooms, this starkly decorated bistro started life as a wine shop. There’s still a range of bottles for sale, along with a wine list that offers plenty of younger and lesser-known producers. The well-priced menu allows guests to order a few plates to share, be that classics like beef tartare or dishes that show off seasonal vegetables such as asparagus and morel mushrooms. Look out for the signpost by the gates when arriving, as the entrance is tucked away off the main street.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5551;Luneta & Lorneta Bistro Club;Poland;Ciekocinko;Ciekocinko 9, Ciekocinko, 84210, Poland;54.7466495;17.7977622;85;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The Pałac Ciekocinko Hotel, a large house dating back to the 1920s, is the home for this smart restaurant with a few plush details in its décor. Situated in the basement, there’s a pleasantly cosy feel to the dining room, which is accentuated by the cheery, welcoming service. A garden terrace is used to fine effect in the summer, while the cooking is admirably light on price and heavy on flavour. Confit duck leg with a fabulous silky jus is a prime example.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
5552;kontakt;Poland;Warsaw;Sandomierska 13, Warsaw, 02 567, Poland;52.2079464;21.0190128;67;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Just outside of the hustle and bustle of the city centre, you'll find this trendy spot with a wine bar on its lower level and a rustic bistro upstairs. The cooking has a Mediterranean heart, with croquetas and cavatelli likely to appear on a great value menu that’s perfect for sharing. The wine list plays a starring role, providing an extensive choice that largely focuses on natural and bio-dynamic wines from lesser-known producers – and the team have an excellent knowledge of their selection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
5553;Ceviche Bar;Poland;Warsaw;Twarda 2-4, Warsaw, 00 105, Poland;52.2355435;21.0019124;60;true;false;South American;Bringing South American flavours to Warsaw, you’ll quickly find that this bright, airy restaurant is much more than a bar and serves far more than just ceviche. The famous Peruvian dish does feature – with sea bass, tuna and oyster among the varieties – but so do empanadas, grilled steaks and picarones. Argentinian Chef-Owner Martin Gimenez Castro imbues them all with freshness and vitality. In the evening, the music grows louder and the pisco sours start emerging from the bar at increasing speed.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5554;Gostilna na Gradu;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Grajska planota 1, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0478785;14.5092591;85;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The Gostilna na Gradu (the “restaurant at the castle”) says it all. You’d be forgiven for thinking that this was a tourist address given its location in the inner courtyard of the city’s busiest, most iconic monument, and yet the dishes here are prepared using carefully chosen Slovenian ingredients and cooked to perfection. Our favourite dishes included beef tongue with onions, a superb dish that was a lot more elaborate than that simple description suggests. The tongue is lightly brined, then smoked and served thinly sliced with turnip mousse, toasted pumpkin seeds and wild-garlic oil, as well as stewed sweet-and-sour onions.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5555;LALU Bistro;Slovenia;Celje;Trg celjskih knezov 3, Celje, 3000, Slovenia;46.2292868;15.2616833;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional European;A glass of Pinot Noir from the Štajerska region (Slovenian Styria) makes the perfect introduction to a meal at this small modern, minimalist-style restaurant with a welcoming feel in the town centre. The friendly service is accompanied by cuisine influenced by Italy, with ingredients such as San Daniele ham on the menu alongside local specialities such as Savinjski želodec (a delicious local ham) served with olives and wild capers. Don’t miss the crème brûlée with passion fruit and coconut sorbet which adds an exotic touch to your meal.;;[]
5556;Jožef;Slovenia;Idrija;Vojkova Ulica 9A, Idrija, 5280, Slovenia;46.006865;14.0277163;26;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;Housed in a modern hotel just outside the town centre, this restaurant boasts an attractive, bright dining room on the first floor that comes as a surprise given its fairly anonymous location. Although the menu is not extensive (and is even more restricted at lunchtime), it changes daily and showcases traditional local dishes reinterpreted with a modern twist. Make sure you try the žlikrofi (delicious potato-filled ravioli) served with a type of lamb stew – a local speciality for which the restaurant is a certified producer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5557;Gostilnica Ruj;Slovenia;Dol pri Vogljah;Dol Pri Vogljah 16, Dol pri Vogljah, 6221, Slovenia;45.7243204;13.8162299;23;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the Karst region above Trieste, this restaurant occupies a small house surrounded by trees, with an entrance directly from its outdoor patio. The cuisine here is local and seasonal and is announced at your table by chef Peter Patajac, an engaging host who will happily share his delight at finding just the right ingredient from local farmers who pay close attention to the natural rhythms of nature. Chatting with him is a real pleasure, enhanced perhaps by a glass of a good Slovenian red wine such as the delicate yet ample Vlkovin 2015, with its elegant spicy aromas.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5558;Gostilna Rajh;Slovenia;Murska Sobota;Soboška ulica 32, Bakovci, Murska Sobota, 9000, Slovenia;46.6220488;16.1489409;69;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant now run by the fourth generation of the family is a real culinary institution in this region, with many of its regular guests having eaten here since they were children. There’s a welcoming bar for socialising and an elegant dining room in which to enjoy classic regional fare such as cured hams, delicious hot beetroot with horseradish, superb Wiener Schnitzel with a fragrant side salad and excellent pumpkin oil, plus unmissable traditional desserts to finish. Offering good value for money, this is a restaurant to return to time and time again.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5559;Restavracija Majerca;Slovenia;Stara Fužina;Stara Fužina19, Stara Fužina, 4265, Slovenia;46.28352;13.89019;17;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant, which is part of an intimate boutique hotel near Lake Bohinj amid the valleys of the Julian Alps, boasts a contemporary-style dining room with relaxing views of the surrounding countryside. Here, the chef creates dishes inspired by typical mountain ingredients (local beef and veal, trout from Lake Bohinj, celeriac, potatoes etc) which are modern yet uncomplicated and fully focused on flavour. In the evening, guests can choose between a 3-, 4- or 5-course menu, while simpler options are available at lunchtime. 90% of the wines are Slovenian.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5560;Gostilna in vinoteka Faladur;Slovenia;Vipava;Ulica Ivana Ščeka 6, Vipava, 5271, Slovenia;45.8464;13.9632;37;false;true;Country cooking;Situated in the centre of Vipava, an attractive little town with pre-Roman origins, this restaurant has the feel of a charming and welcoming inn, with the added attraction of an enchanting terrace for summer evenings. The restaurant is pretty and carefully decorated with interesting bottles of wine for sale displayed on the walls. The menu features regional recipes alongside more modern dishes, such as mackerel sashimi with mandarin and the baked pancetta with spicy chard (our favourite). The service is friendly and attentive (the selection of local wines is presented with real enthusiasm) and there’s an attractively priced menu at lunchtime.;Terrace;[]
5561;Kodila;Slovenia;Murska Sobota;Markišavci 44, Murska Sobota, 9000, Slovenia;46.68362;16.16325;24;false;false;Meats and Grills;The ground floor of this restaurant is home to a café and an opulent delicatessen offering a huge selection of hams that are cured and seasoned on site – the theme continues on the first floor, where guests pass a display of hams on their way to the dining room. It soon becomes obvious that this bistro-style restaurant with a covered terrace is dedicated to local specialities such as seasoned hams, pork chops and delicious pork scratchings. The seasonal dishes include delicious brawn served with pumpkin oil and seeds, smoked prosciutto with fresh horseradish, and calf’s liver with polenta. Kodila is a real paradise for meat-lovers, with specialities that can be enjoyed without spending a fortune. The delicatessen is also worth a visit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5562;Triangel;Slovenia;Gozd Martuljek;Zgornje Rute 9, Gozd Martuljek, 4282, Slovenia;46.4824124;13.8373242;46;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a majestic mountain setting just a few kilometres from the elegant Kranjska Gora ski resort, Triangel is the perfect place to stay and to enjoy a pleasant dinner, with a delightful outdoor terrace that is a must in summer. The cuisine has something for everyone, with a menu offering a combination of modern and traditional dishes. Dishes not to missed include the ričet (a typical Slovenian barley soup with Carniolan sausage), the delicious veal loin with shallot sauce, and perfectly cooked steak. The tasting menus are a convenient option at lunchtime, while the wine list includes a selection of top-quality local and international labels.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5563;Gostilna Mahorčič;Slovenia;Rodik;Rodik 51, Rodik, 6240, Slovenia;45.6247236;13.9801944;30;false;false;Regional European, Farm to table;An unmissable restaurant in a small village in the beautiful Karst region, with a classic, beautifully kept dining room with the intimate feel of a private lounge. The owners here are friendly and welcoming and keen to showcase the best of their region. With enthusiasm and expertise, skilful owner-chef Ksenija Krajšek Mahorčič adds a personal, technical touch to Slovenian ingredients resulting in dishes of the highest quality. Among the appetisers, a good example of his sustainable approach is the puffed wild garlic chip topped with a sea bass cream made from fish scraps. Also recommended is the local roast lamb served with cider from home-grown apples and a garlic potato mash. The same care and attention to detail is found on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
5564;14Horses;Lithuania;Vilnius;Dominikonų Gatvė 11, Vilnius, 01131, Lithuania;54.6807254;25.2857564;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The unusually named 14 Horses is a well-run restaurant with a sleek, pared-back look and a relaxed vibe. Here, many of the dishes are brought to the table by the chef himself, who proudly shows off ingredients from the restaurant's regenerative farm in Radiškis. There’s certainly value on the cards: you receive bread, four courses and a pre-dessert – with the flexibility to choose either three starters or two starters and a dessert. Bold, well-defined flavours are delivered in original combinations. The staff are happy to advise, but the ‘beef from nose-to-tail’ is a must.;Air conditioning;[]
5565;Gaspar's;Lithuania;Vilnius;Pylimo  Gatvė 23-3, Vilnius, 01141, Lithuania;54.6785475;25.277928;23;true;true;Indian;On the border of the Old and the New Town you’ll find Gaspar’s, a neighbourhood restaurant with a long history as an eatery – look out for the original Yiddish restaurant sign above the door (this was once the Jewish Quarter). Chef Gaspar Fernandes was born in Goa, India and is of Portuguese heritage, so his cuisine is an intriguing blend of the two countries. The menu is concise, driven by the produce available and subtle Indian spicing, and dishes are generous and beautifully presented. “My mum’s curry” is available in several varieties and the naan bread uses locally milled whole wheat flour, which adds a unique nuttiness.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5568;Xin Wen Ji (Yuexiu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;1-3F, Sino Trade Centre, 67 Panfu Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1384062;113.2549033;83;true;false;Cantonese;The room is divided into zones with different ambiances – satin tablecloths signal a chic, formal vibe, while distressed wooden tables feel hip and casual. The culinary highlight is undoubtedly the piping hot congee claypot loaded with fresh seafood, from sand shrimps to mud crab. You can also pick your own fish from the tank and ask servers the best way to have it cooked. Cantonese stir-fries and sizzling claypot dishes exude exceptional wok hei.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5569;Jia Yuan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;7 Xingrenli, Guangxiao Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.12662;113.25606;78;false;false;Vegetarian;This restaurant with wood-rich finishes primarily serves dishes made with soybean products or mushrooms – no dairy, eggs, garlic or onion are used. Sweet and sour monkey head mushrooms and vegan meat with pickled cabbage are both tangy creations with layers of textures. The house-made mugwort-scented dumplings and plant-based yoghurt are also popular. Reservations recommended on the 1st and 15th day of every lunar month, when Buddhists go meat-free.;Air conditioning;[]
5570;Mamak;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 082C, East 1 Street, B1F, Fashion Tianhe Plaza, 299 Tianhe Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.136445;113.321528;49;false;false;Malaysian;Named after hawker stalls in Malaysia, this small and cheerful spot in a big shopping mall is boldly decorated with bright yellow hues and Malaysian flags everywhere. Naturally, the menu is loaded with the country’s national dishes, such as laksa (seafood noodle soup) and nasi lemak (coconut rice) served with juicy fried chicken and house-made sambal. For drinks, try teh C special (three-layer milk tea) or teh tarik (hand-pulled tea).;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5571;Liang Jie Nanning Pumiao Shengzha Mifen (Yinghua Street);China Mainland;Guangzhou;242 Yinghua Street, Xiaogang Bay, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.071435;113.288776;31;false;false;Noodles;This friendly neighbourhood shop specialises in sourdough rice noodles. While preserving her hometown culinary tradition, the owner also dials down the sourness to cater to local tastes. Noodles are made to order – fermented rice batter is squeezed into boiling water and then drenched in soup, or tossed with pickled string beans, ground pork and deep-fried tofu. You can also opt for the beef brisket version. Prepare to wait after placing orders.;Cash only;[]
5572;Wen Ji Yixinji;China Mainland;Guangzhou;10 Xuanyuanqiao, 76 Baohua Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.116787;113.236603;80;false;false;Cantonese;This joint expanded in 2020, adding a dining room across from the original shop. Its signature Yixin chicken remains the key draw – birds from Qingyuan weighing about 1.8 kg are slow-cooked in a white marinade with herbs and dried scallops, boasting juicy, silky flesh and glistening, springy skin. Also try its osmanthus roll, an ancient very rare recipe, consisting of fatty pork and salted egg yolk in a duck intestine casing, sliced and doused in honey glaze.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5573;Ease (Yuexiu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;112A, 1F, Newspaper Printing Service Building, 289 Art Park, 289 Guangzhou Middle Avenue, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.126322;113.308971;70;false;true;Sichuan;Nestled in a printing plant-turned-cultural park, the two-storey restaurant boasts an airy, high-ceilinged dining room. Faux-industrial elements work well with wood and bamboo accents for a relaxed ambience. The menu features simple dishes with Sichuanese touches, such as the must-try poached fish with peppercorns on the vine – layered flavours contrast nicely with the velvety fish. Friendly service and sensible prices are also reasons to visit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5574;Xiguan Zhuyuan (Lizhiwan);China Mainland;Guangzhou;C4, Phase 2, Lizhiwan Scenic Area, Huangsha Avenue, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.121364;113.227805;42;false;true;Noodles;Not only is this a noodle shop – nestled in a picturesque park – but it’s also a factory that makes noodles for various restaurants in Guangzhou and Hong Kong. These famous strands made with duck eggs are dried on bamboo skimmers outside the shop. Dried plaice is toasted on charcoal before being added to the flavourful broth along with pork backbones and dried shrimp. Customers who wish to enjoy the same taste at home can buy their pre-packed noodles.;Car park;[]
5575;Zijin Shi Fang;China Mainland;Guangzhou;39-1 Zishan Street, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.0977632;113.2640679;38;true;false;Cantonese;Though Zijin occupies two adjoining ground-floor units, there is barely an empty seat throughout the day. For over 10 years, locals have been fans of the impeccable barbecue meats, which are displayed in all their glory at the front of the shop. The signature goose braised in premium soy boasts velvety meat and deep flavours. Double-boiled soups, stir-fries and claypot dishes are also popular. Come early, as certain items tend to run out.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5576;Hui Xing Yuan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;177 Xiaobei Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1373764;113.2662879;70;true;true;Cantonese;This three-storey building is the brand's first outlet, dating back to 1981. Known for traditional Cantonese food at bargain prices, the restaurant prides itself on meticulous cooking techniques and attention to detail. Their speciality of steamed chicken uses only free-range birds from Qingyuan for their firm, silky flesh and fine, springy skin. The goose intestines blanched in soy sauce are also impeccably made.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5577;Dayang (Wenming Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;160-1 Wenming Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.125249;113.2688829;58;false;true;Cantonese;Among locals, its name is synonymous with double-boiled soups, which dominate the menu here. Apart from the top-selling silkie chicken soup in whole coconut, other popular selections, such as free-range chicken soup with goji berries and yam as well as quail soup are trickier to order as they change every few hours. That means you'll never quite know what exactly is available in advance. Adventurous eaters may also try the turtle jelly with milk and honey.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
5578;Lao Xiguan Laifen (Wenming Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;216 Wenming Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.125193;113.270555;17;false;false;Noodles;As its name suggests, Laifen noodle soup is the key item on offer in this rustic shop – you can have it alongside ingredients, such as barbecue pork, beef balls or octopus. The old-time dish ‘water caltrop’, which is rice noodles shaped like bite-size buffalo nuts topped with shredded omelette, preserved cabbage and barbecue pork, is hard to find elsewhere. Also try homemade preserved radish.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
5579;Chuang Fa;China Mainland;Guangzhou;512-2 Guangfu North Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.124895;113.247211;48;true;true;Cantonese;Since opening in the 1990s, this has been a popular place among locals who can’t seem to get enough of the kitchen's Cantonese home-style cooking, especially the double-boiled tonic soups. The signature “real-taste” chicken is free-range from Shunyi and is prized for its firm, flavoursome meat and silky, gelatinous skin. Large fried pork intestines with basil, and live seafood cooked-to-order are also excellent. Reservations recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5580;Sa Er Ta Dongxiang Shou Zhua;China Mainland;Guangzhou;103 Baohan Zhijie, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.145498;113.268936;28;false;false;Xibei;Tucked in an alley filled to the brim with halal restaurants, this two-storey establishment has a dining room on the ground floor and some private rooms upstairs. Lamb is big on the menu, such as the juicy boiled premium version, which is chopped into chunky pieces with skin on and bone in. Pair it with garlic for extra pungency. Heyan flat noodles and Dongxiang stir-fried chicken are also worth ordering. For drinks, the eight-treasure tea is a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
5581;Zhu Zai Ji Shi Fu (Jiangnan Avenue);China Mainland;Guangzhou;429 Jiangnan Avenue South, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.087732;113.279196;32;false;false;Cantonese;A hawker-stall-turned-restaurant now with two branches – this casual, bustling three-storey joint is prized for its authentic Cantonese food. The juicy, flavoursome roast goose has been a big hit for the past 20 years. Other specialities include salted pork trotters, Zhu Ji steamed chicken, and blackened barbecued pork. Pastured pork soup with mung bean-stuffed lotus root tastes delicious and delivers interesting textures.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5582;Xing Fu Yi Zhan (Yulei Third Street);China Mainland;Guangzhou;8 Yulei Third Street, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.131315;113.317703;41;true;false;Sichuan;Furnished like a vintage staging post, this restaurant whisks you back in time. Feel free to join the servers and dress up in period costume for a selfie. The Sichuanese head chef feeds hungry patrons with Chongqing-style cooking characterised by rich, intense flavours. Stir-fried dried pork with smoked bamboo shoot packs serious wok hei and a hint of smokiness. On the shelves, local liquors are on display, including some brewed in-house.;Air conditioning;[]
5583;Stay Here;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 2, 23 Xigang Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.093254;113.275449;49;false;false;Chao Zhou;This tiny gem has changed hands, but the kitchen is still run by Chaoshan natives. The small menu stars all the greatest hits of Chaoshan cuisine, with raw marinated mud crab that packs tons of oomph standing out in particular. Diners need to book via a texting app and pre-order their food, which does streamline the process immensely. To round out your meal, try the ‘ginger potato’ and split mung bean sweet soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5585;Enning Liu Fu Ji (Donghua East Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;547 Donghua East Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1234401;113.2865462;93;true;true;Noodles;The founder started a shop on Enning Street in the 1940s and invented a unique way to make noodles. Fast forward to present day and his successors still honour his heritage by making bouncy noodles just like the old days – with duck eggs and flour only. The must-try blanched noodles tossed in lard is simple but addictive. The shrimp wontons are big and bursting with seafood flavours. Don’t miss their deep-fried wontons, available on weekends only.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
5587;Xiguan Zhuyuan (Shiba Fu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;107 Shiba Fu South Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1143;113.24075;21;true;false;Noodles;It lacks the views of its Lizhiwan counterpart, but the food here tastes just as good. Duck egg noodles are kneaded with a traditional bamboo pole for a springy texture, before being blanched and tossed in shrimp roe, or in a broth made with dried plaice, pork bones and dried shrimp. Apart from the classic shrimp wonton, there is also the crab roe variety. Don’t miss the beef offal soup, fried savoury dough, beef brisket and pork intestines.;Air conditioning;[]
5589;Hai Men Yu Zi Dian (Yanling Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;1-2F, Jinyan Mansion, 120 Yanling Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.161378;113.322292;85;false;false;Chao Zhou;Next to a glass-walled kitchen where a veritable army of chefs may be seen at work, this high-ceilinged bi-level dining room was remodelled to have entrances on both ends, thereby making it feel even more comfortable than before. It’s essentially an up-market hawker stall experience in an air-conditioned space. Diners pick their food at the entrance, where fresh seafood delivered daily from Swatow is laid out neatly on ice. First-timers may also refer to the menu for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5590;Wei Shi Jia;China Mainland;Guangzhou;598 Jiefang North Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1306966;113.2569204;69;true;true;Cantonese;Shi shi chicken – steamed chicken served with fermented clam dip – ranks among the top 10 chicken dishes in Guangzhou, but it’s hard to come by these days. The chef, who once worked in a prestigious hotel, uses Qingyuan birds for this dish because of their bouncy skin and silky flesh. Besides the clam dip, it comes with soy sauce and ginger scallion dip. Also try the rice noodles made from scratch in-house and dressed in a secret soy blend.;Cash only;[]
5592;Tong Ji;China Mainland;Guangzhou;3 Fuguangli, Changshou East Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.120873;113.244808;21;true;false;Noodles and Congee;Tucked away in an alley, this two-storey, no-frills joint has been in business for over 30 years. You're not here for the ambience, but for the steamed chicken – only free-range pullets before they lay their first egg are used because of their springy skin, oily richness, silky flesh and robust flavour. Boiled chicken intestines, stir-fried ribbon rice noodles and creamy congee are also sound reasons to visit.;Cash only;[]
5593;Yao Ji;China Mainland;Guangzhou;15 Long Yuan Road, Panyu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.0445093;113.4464454;52;false;false;Cantonese;Yao Ji has been a household name in Panyu District for over 40 years. On the menu, classic Cantonese flavours work their magic in painstaking recipes that are a rarity these days. The sweet, steamed lotus root puree is sticky and chewy and well complemented by briny dried shrimps and aromatic scallion. Oyster sauce chicken is nicely browned and boasts an inimitable umami flavour thanks to scallion and ginger.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5594;Temple Street;China Mainland;Guangzhou;10 Dongdi Second Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1188375;113.273377;64;false;false;Cantonese;Since opening in 2018, this tiny shop has been jam-packed with diners, so expect to share a table with strangers at peak hours. It’s named after Temple Street in the owner’s native Hong Kong and focuses on 20+ types of clay pot rice in dai pai dong style, alongside three kinds of double-boiled soups. Try their claypot rice topped with assorted traditional preserved meats, beef loin with perilla leaves or satay beef with onion.;Cash only;[]
5595;Hunan Cuisine;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2842-39 East Xingang Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.08828;113.399661;53;false;false;Hunanese;This design-forward restaurant is located within an industrial park of remodelled factory buildings. Aptly, the décor exudes an industrial chic that complements the origami art hung from the ceiling. Trained as a designer, the owner took care of the décor and furnishings, whereas the Hunanese chef recreates classics from his home province. Dongting fish head, wotou cornbread and sweet fried dumplings are cooked with acumen and dexterity.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5596;Lingnan Haiyanlou (Binjiang East Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;2-3F, Jiangpan Huating, 1040 Binjiang East Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.106869;113.309602;33;false;false;Cantonese;The two chefs in this kitchen once worked at a prestigious hotel and their skills are unquestionable – which is why it’s so hard to get a table here. Try their ‘premium trio’ which was usually saved for state banquets only – rich and buttery foie gras, plum-scented squab with crispy skin, as well as springy goose webs and wings in white marinade. Barbecued meat is grilled daily in limited servings. Arrive early to nab a seat or risk disappointment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5597;Huacheng Yuan (Jinsui Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;5F, Grand Mercure, 62 Jinsui Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.124941;113.317203;97;true;true;Cantonese;Since 2018, Huacheng Yuan has been serving hotel guests and other gourmands with home-style Cantonese fare. The brightly lit space boasts a tasteful décor and there are a number of private rooms of varying sizes. Along with signature dishes such as double-steamed chicken, lotus root starch pancakes, and soy-marinated chitterlings, the milky white, rich and flavoursome slow-cooked pork tripe soup is a must-try. Reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
5598;Xiang Qun (Longjin East Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;853-857 Longjin East Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.12423;113.24633;98;false;true;Cantonese;Standing the test of time since 1988, this operation started out as an ‘ice parlour’ serving cold drinks and light snacks. Now firmly in the 21C, it has morphed into a chain famous for home-style cooking and this branch pays tribute to the charm of historic Guangzhou. Signatures include steamed Qingyuan chicken and soy-marinated goose. The stir-fried eel fillet with French beans seduces with aromas of garlic and shallot as the naturally sweet veggies work wonders with the firm eel flesh.;Air conditioning;[]
5599;Rong Yi Fa Niu Za Dian (Shishu Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;56 Shishu Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1205965;113.2491648;17;true;false;Cantonese;For over 40 years, the owner has been insisting on shopping for fresh beef offal daily, painstakingly preparing and braising it in a rich stock made from scratch with beef and lamb bones. His beef bone marrow boasts a creamy texture and is a perfect match with the house-made radish pickles. Beef tripe tip is another premium cut, available only after 11am. As well as beef offal, also try wonton noodle soup, braised beef brisket and tendon.;;[]
5600;Soodle;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 309, 3F, Adjoining Building, Kingold Century, 62 Jinsui Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.125483;113.317397;49;false;true;Vegetarian;Commanding spectacular city views, the sun-drenched, plant-filled space caters to a well-heeled business clientele. The Western-centric menu focuses on vegetables and mushrooms, as opposed to typical Chinese vegetarian cuisine based on soy faux meats. The bamboo fungus with pickled radish, chilli and rattan pepper has a wonderfully crisp texture and tingling tanginess. The deep-fried Yunnan eggplant with vegan demi-glace is also unmissable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5601;Xin Tai Le (Yuexiu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;1-2F, Sino Trade Centre, 65 Panfu Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.138328;113.25471;23;false;true;Cantonese;Since 1989, this household name for its signature swamp eel rice has attracted a loyal fan base. Of all the branches, this two-storey one in the old part of town is the flagship. Apart from its famous rice dish topped with crisp, flavourful eel that imparts a robust wok-qi, the kitchen also recommends fatty roast char siu, all sorts of stir-fries and seafood dishes. Private rooms of varying sizes are available on the second floor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5602;Ya Yuan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;14 Chaotian Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.126347;113.55284;62;true;false;Cantonese;The three-storey room is furnished with orange tables and leather chairs that evoke 1980s nostalgia. For over three decades, Ya Yuan has been feeding hungry locals with classic home-style dishes such as slow-boiled soups and claypot rice. With its velvety flesh and gelatinous skin, the poached Qingyuan chicken dressed in scallion oil is addictively aromatic. Even the post-meal complimentary mung bean or red bean sweet soups are made with care.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5603;Da Ge Fan (Tangxiayong West Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;1F, Tian Hui Building, 69 Tangxiayong West Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.127803;113.371716;40;true;false;Cantonese;The chain operates branches in Hunan and Guangdong, but everything started in this flagship venue with a landscaped garden and a running stream. Its namesake signature dish is rice cooked in a pigeon and pork bone broth, boasting a crispy golden crust on the bottom and topped with steamed pigeon or a combo of pigeon meat and gizzards. Besides deep-fried or salt-baked fowl, the sautéed squid with cucumber is also a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5604;Dai Yong Town;China Mainland;Guangzhou;59 Tianhe East Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.133389;113.328145;50;true;false;Chao Zhou;A wall map and backlit illustrations lend the rustic interior an artistic flair. The owner and the staff, who all hail from the Chaoshan area, pay homage to the kaleidoscopic food culture of this region using mainly ingredients and seafood from their homelands. ‘Floating’ on dry ice fog, marinated raw crab boasts gelatinous roe loaded with umami and winey aromas. It even comes with hot ginger tea to balance the crab’s ‘coldness’.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
5605;Hua Ge Si Chu;China Mainland;Guangzhou;443 Guangfu North Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1243288;113.2467544;50;false;false;Cantonese;The owner was behind a legendary, now-shuttered restaurant and opened this much smaller spot, keeping some of the menu’s most popular items. The chef has decades of experience and his Hakkanese cooking is a pure delight. The signature salt-baked chicken uses birds from Qingyuan, dry-rubbed in a droolworthy secret seasoning blend. House-made pickles, and winter special, white radish pork balls, are also recommended.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5607;Jian Ji (Liwan);China Mainland;Guangzhou;299-303 Changshou East Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1208479;113.2451162;39;false;true;Noodles;Shops that sell homemade E-fu noodles can be hard to come by. For over 50 years, this one has attracted a faithful following with not only E-fu, but also freshly made raw and cooked egg noodles. The ladies working in the open kitchen show off their swift moves as these particular strands are notorious for their finicky cooking process. The flavourful broth made with dace, pork bones, shrimp roe and dried shrimp matches the noodles perfectly.;Cash only;[]
5609;305;Finland;Helsinki;Toinen linja 3, Helsinki, 00530, Finland;60.1807798;24.9508493;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Friendly service, sensible prices and plenty of buzz in the air – this is the kind of neighbourhood spot we’d all love to have at the end of our street. It’s located in the north of the city, inside a substantial three-storey building dating back to the 19th Century. The unfussy dishes are a great example of Nordic bistronomy: rustic, satisfying and filled with bold, balanced flavours – whether that be fresh herbs adding vibrancy to a burbot dish, or tart lingonberries cutting through the sweetness of meringue.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
5610;Enomania;Denmark;Copenhagen;Vesterbrogade 187, Copenhagen, 1800 C, Denmark;55.6706713;12.5321802;45;true;true;Italian;With a name that means 'Wine Mania' it's no surprise that this Italian restaurant attracts a crowd of dedicated oenophiles. The wine cellar comes with a table for tasting and there’s an excellent list of several hundred bins, mostly from Burgundy and Owner Damiano Alberti's native Piedmont. In his role as Sommelier, Damiano provides wine service that is helpful, passionate and generous. The place itself is simple and trattoria-like, serving straightforward and satisfying dishes like 'spaghetti alla chitarra con gamberoni' from a weekly-changing menu.;Interesting wine list;[]
5611;The Little Pickle;Norway;Oslo;Jens Bjelkes gate 9A, Oslo, 0562, Norway;59.9191099;10.7640471;94;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;It’s not often that restaurants in Oslo are influenced by British cuisine, but that’s exactly what you’ll find at this minimally decorated neighbourhood bistro. Operations such as London's St. John are the inspiration for the kitchen, with dishes like beef brisket pie and mash providing suitably gutsy flavours and hearty generosity. They even serve a traditional roast dinner on Sundays! French influences come into play as well, as with the madeleines for dessert. Friendly service creates a lovely, welcoming atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
5612;Bar Agrikultur;Sweden;Stockholm;Skånegatan 79, Stockholm, 116 35, Sweden;59.3128478;18.0831757;66;false;false;Swedish, Small eats;A warmly run, intimate and cosy wine bar that is a perfect fit for Södermalm. The freshly prepared and delicious small plates are designed for sharing and showcase classic Swedish flavours. The three stainless steel tanks contain home-distilled gin – flavours are changed regularly using various herbs, oils or fruits.;;[]
5613;Lilla Ego;Sweden;Stockholm;Västmannagatan 69, Stockholm, 113 26, Sweden;59.3435589;18.0456255;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;With its pared-back feel, rustic exposed brickwork and buzzy vibe, this is just the place for a lively night out. It remains one of the hottest tickets in town, so try for a counter seat overlooking the kitchen if you haven’t booked. The concise menu includes modernised Swedish classics that are robust, well-composed and certainly deliver on flavour. Service is accommodating, warm and efficient.;Counter dining;[]
5614;no.2;Denmark;Copenhagen;Nicolai Eigtveds Gade 32, Copenhagen, 1402 K, Denmark;55.6724925;12.5842623;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the Christianshavn dockside development is this minimally decorated, no-frills sister restaurant to a|o|c. This approach extends to the low-key service and the laid-back ambiance, while the fresh, flavoursome dishes focus on Danish produce, incorporate some impressive culinary techniques and offer great depth of flavour. The fish of the day is a prime example, showcasing a quality prime ingredient that’s been expertly seasoned and accompanied by a well-judged garnish of caramelised cauliflower purée and foamy mussel sauce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5615;Anarki;Denmark;Copenhagen;Vodroffsvej 47, Copenhagen, 1900 C, Denmark;55.67943;12.554741;97;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;An unassuming and proudly run neighbourhood bistro, set just over the water in Frederiksberg. The regularly changing menu draws its inspiration from the season, the best quality ingredients available and the mood of the chef – and the bold, rustic dishes are bursting with flavour, with some great wines to match.;Interesting wine list;[]
5616;Pluto;Denmark;Copenhagen;Borgergade 16, Copenhagen, 1300 K, Denmark;55.6834672;12.5851631;81;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Concrete pillars and an intentionally ‘unfinished’ feel bring a distinctive vibe at this ever-popular restaurant. The huge numbers they serve whilst maintaining quality and affordability is a testament to both the kitchen and service teams. Sit at wooden tables, at the long metal bar or at communal marble-topped tables to enjoy the extensive selection of unfussy sharing plates, including stand-out pasta dishes and their signature savoury waffles. A selection of natural wines completes the picture.;Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5617;Silberbauers Bistro;Denmark;Copenhagen;Jægersborggade 40, Copenhagen, 2200 N, Denmark;55.6932452;12.5433824;47;false;true;French;Eponymous Danish chef Mathias has taken over the spot previously occupied by Manfreds to create a lively, friendly eatery with a focus on fish and shellfish. The day’s catch gives rise to the concise menu, and the emphasis on top quality produce ensures that the simple, well-priced dishes are full of flavour.;;[]
5620;Mêlée;Denmark;Copenhagen;Martensens Allé 16, Copenhagen, 1828 C, Denmark;55.6759079;12.5426814;81;true;false;French;You will quickly feel at home in this bustling neighbourhood bistro with a friendly, lively atmosphere. The uncomplicated spirit of the restaurant is reflected in modern, country-style cooking, generous portions and bold flavours. There is a French basis to the concise monthly menus, with some Danish influences. The excellent wine list offers an impressive array of vintages.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5621;juju;Denmark;Copenhagen;Øster Farimagsgade 8, Copenhagen, 2100  Ø, Denmark;55.6899193;12.5750746;89;true;true;Korean Contemporary;On the edge of the city centre, near Rosenborg Castle, sits this casual Korean restaurant. A wide selection of small plates like Korean fried chicken and mandoo of pork are ideal for sharing in the simple, bistro-like dining room. Dishes are prepared with knowledge and skill, offering wonderfully intense flavours at a reasonable price tag. Friendly service adds to the appeal.;;[]
5622;Smalhans;Norway;Oslo;Ullevålsveien 43, Oslo, 0171, Norway;59.9237243;10.7397842;55;false;true;Norwegian, Contemporary;A sweet neighbourhood café with friendly staff and an urban feel. Coffee and homemade cakes are served in the morning, with a short selection of dishes including soup and a burger on offer between 12pm and 4pm. In the evenings, they serve a set menu of rustic Norwegian dishes.;;[]
5623;Marv & Ben;Denmark;Copenhagen;Snaregade 4, Copenhagen, 1205 K, Denmark;55.6772861;12.5770331;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The young owners bring plenty of enthusiasm to this little restaurant, where dining is split over two dimly lit floors. Organic produce features in seasonal cooking which displays purity and depth of flavour. They produce 6 dishes each evening, which are priced individually or as 4 or 6 courses.;Air conditioning;[]
5625;Pondus;Denmark;Aarhus;Åboulevarden 51, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.1561762;10.2049453;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set by the narrow city centre canal, the little sister to Substans is a small, rustic bistro with a friendly vibe and a stripped-back style. Bright, colourful dishes are formed around organic Danish produce and represent great value. Wines are either natural or organic.;Terrace;[]
5628;anx;Denmark;Aarhus;Oddervej 19-21, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.124681;10.2088178;66;true;false;Smørrebrød;This nicely styled, well-run annexe to Frederikshøj serves sophisticated yet well-priced smørrebrød, which are classic in their ingredients and modern in their presentation. Contemporary art punctuates the walls and service is charming and efficient.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5629;Ruths;Sweden;Malmo;Mäster Johansgatan 11, Malmo, 21121, Sweden;55.6061556;12.9977834;61;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The open kitchen takes centre stage at this buzzy all-day café/bakery/deli, which has been wholeheartedly embraced by the locals. Lunchtime snacks and salads make room for generously sized, boldly flavoured Mediterranean dishes at dinner. Most of the wines on the concise list are available on-tap.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5630;Bjørnekælderen;Denmark;Copenhagen;Frederiksberg Allé 55, Copenhagen, 1820, Denmark;55.6740601;12.5372477;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The ‘Bear’s Basement’ has been a restaurant for over 130 years, and references to the furry creatures are legion in this cosy, characterful eatery. Smørrebrød are served at lunch, with more substantial dishes in the evening, and the carefully crafted plates have flavour, imagination and a modern touch.;Air conditioning;[]
5632;Allegrine;Sweden;Stockholm;Kammakargatan 22, Stockholm, 111 40, Sweden;59.3391156;18.0606728;52;true;true;French;Set off the busy Sveavägen thoroughfare, this brasserie provides a hidden oasis. Sit on the attractive front terrace or in the chic dining room, where seats at the kitchen counter are in demand. Variously sized dishes are richly flavoured, with a French base, Scandinavian influences and subtle contrasts.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5633;Gabrielle;Denmark;Copenhagen;Vestergade 3, Copenhagen, 1456, Denmark;55.6779957;12.5712;36;false;true;French;Sibling to Norrlyst and Theo in the city, this French-style bistro is run by seasoned local restaurateurs and delivers traditional Gallic fare with an appealing price tag. The kitchen's skilled classical technique is highlighted across the menu, which features the likes of Gillardeau oysters with mignonette sauce and their speciality beef tartare – which is of undeniable quality. Add in linen-laid tables, simple wooden chairs and an all-French wine list and you could easily forget that you're in Copenhagen.;;[]
5636;Paesàno;Denmark;Copenhagen;Jægersborggade 41, Copenhagen, 2200, Denmark;55.6930508;12.5433079;97;true;false;Italian;Down a charming cobbled street in the trendy Nørrebro neighbourhood, where you will find a number of artisan food producers, lies this thoroughly fun restaurant run by a Neapolitan Chef. The short Italian menu is supplemented by blackboard specials and might include ‘cucina povera’ style dishes like 'pasta e piselli' and ‘soffrito napoletano’ – a ragu made using 'the best parts of the pig'. Whatever it is you choose, you can bet it will be colourful, packed with flavour and excellent value.;Counter dining;[]
5638;Bistro Lupa;Denmark;Copenhagen;Marstalsgade 8, Copenhagen, 2100, Denmark;55.7035355;12.5851885;71;false;false;Vegan;Not far from Nordhavnen lies this vegan bistro that comes with simple décor and a lively atmosphere. Sustainability is a big theme, with a focus on local and seasonal produce, some of it foraged or from their own mushroom farm. These ingredients are fashioned into good value dishes with well-balanced flavours, served by a charming and knowledgeable team. The homemade sparkling kombucha is highly recommended.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5640;Møntergade;Denmark;Copenhagen;Møntergade 19, Copenhagen, 1116, Denmark;55.6820829;12.5797229;36;true;false;Smørrebrød;The charming team are a big part of the draw at this lively upmarket brasserie which offers generous, classically based dishes. While the chalkboard displays daily specials, there’s always a place for herring on the menu – with fried, pickled, marinated or even curried options. Their other dishes like Danish beef with black garlic cream and deep-fried goose fat potatoes or apples with white chocolate, lemon verbena and apple sorbet are equally appealing though. There’s a cosy vibe to the place and a small drinks counter where you can chat away with the waiters.;;[]
5641;Nolla;Finland;Helsinki;Fredrikinkatu 22, Helsinki, 00150, Finland;60.1634013;24.9381305;47;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Nolla means ‘Zero’ and this lively neighbourhood restaurant has a zero-waste ethos running throughout it, from using up scraps in their own composter to the uniforms made being from discarded bed linen. Small producers who share the Nolla philosophy provide ingredients for the hearty cooking, which is best enjoyed from the generous ‘Chef’s Choice’ menu. The dishes pack a punch flavour-wise, exemplified by a wonderfully intense, glossy meat reduction sauce to accompany tender roasted deer.;Counter dining;[]
5642;Bobe;Denmark;Copenhagen;Gråbrødretorv 11, Copenhagen, 1154, Denmark;55.67967;12.57605;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a cobbled city centre square stands this attractive townhouse that's now in the hands of Danish celebrity chef, Bo Bech. His simply decorated contemporary bistro offers reasonable pricing and plenty of flexibility on an extensive à la carte menu. There's strong cooking and great produce across the board, but those with a sweet tooth should keep their eye out for the cheesecake with smoked maple syrup. A wine bar in the basement provides ample opportunity to extend your visit.;Interesting wine list;[]
5643;Triton;Sweden;Stockholm;Ringvägen 87, Stockholm, 118 61, Sweden;59.3084063;18.0662154;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Charming in its lack of pretension, this bohemian neighbourhood restaurant has a homely feel. It’s simply furnished and the pared-back cooking has an unfussiness to match. Dishes show technical skill and provide some well-judged flavours using great Swedish ingredients. In an expensive city, the set menu presents good value for cooking of this quality.;;[]
5644;JH Matbar;Sweden;Ystad;Stora Östergatan 34, Ystad, 27134, Sweden;55.4304091;13.8260946;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;You will find this bistro at the southern tip of Sweden, in the centre of a small town with picturesque streets that provided the setting for the Wallander detective TV series. The good value menu offers a wide choice of dishes, with vegetarians and vegans well catered for. Scandinavian produce powers many of the modern dishes, which are prepared and presented with real care.;Terrace;[]
5645;Bona Fide;Finland;Helsinki;Vironkatu 8, Helsinki, 00170, Finland;60.1722528;24.9553307;61;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Clean, natural and uncomplicated cooking is the big draw at this simple little restaurant. Welcoming, helpful service and a good atmosphere add to the appeal too, enlivening the modest surroundings. The chefs have a great understanding of their seasonal ingredients and treat them with care. Flavours are subtle but are put together in well-thought-out combinations, resulting in quality dishes at a reasonable price.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5646;Mantel ja Korsten;Estonia;Tallinn;Poska 19a, Tallinn, 10216, Estonia;59.4359555;24.7819305;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This picture-postcard clapboard house's name means ‘mantel and chimney’ – and, fittingly, a green-tiled fireplace and mantel take centre stage in a room furnished with bright, bold designs. Flavoursome dishes take on an eclectic mix of styles, from truffle risotto arancini with smoked duck and butternut squash for starters to a blend of coconut, cherry, white chocolate and almond to finish. The well-chosen wines have an organic and biodynamic bias, and service is endearing.;Air conditioning;[]
5648;NOA;Estonia;Tallinn;Ranna tee 3, Tallinn, 12112, Estonia;59.495012;24.8268949;35;false;true;Modern Cuisine;You can take in delightful views over both the city and the sea from this stylish waterside restaurant. The cosy room is furnished with natural materials and the full-length windows flood it with light. Seasonal modern menus are inspired by the owner’s worldwide travels and provide plenty of choice.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5651;Lore Bistroo;Estonia;Tallinn;Peetri 12, Port Noblessner, Tallinn, 10415, Estonia;59.4525841;24.7307283;52;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The sister of ‘Lee’ is a characterful modern bistro which sits in a cavernous warehouse overlooking the harbour at Port Noblessner. Steel girders, hoists and concrete pillars provide the backdrop, while an open kitchen adds to the buzz. Assured, modern dishes are inspired by the owners’ travels, ensuring you'll always find something that appeals. Go for the 'Lore Experience' menu if you fancy sharing dishes served 'family-style' – and if you see crêpes Suzette on the menu, be sure to give them a try!;Terrace;[]
5652;Capim Santo;Brazil;São Paulo;Av. Brig. Faria Lima, 2705, São Paulo, 01451-000, Brazil;-23.5798837;-46.6844243;72;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is a reference for contemporary Brazilian cuisine. Located in the heart of São Paulo, it offers a tranquil and relaxing oasis for those keen to escape the hustle and bustle of the city. It occupies the Solar Fabio Prado (formerly the Museu da Casa Brasileira), and features an extensive outdoor space teeming with vegetation, as well as a pleasant internal dining room. Here, renowned chef Morena Leite, who grew up in the kitchens of his family’s restaurant in Trancoso, conjures up comfort food that showcases typical Brazilian ingredients, allied with techniques acquired elsewhere. One of the classic dishes on the menu is the tapioca ravioli filled with Canastra cheese and a delicious herb sauce that will linger long in the memory.;;[]
5653;Mocotó Vila Leopoldina;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Aroaba, 333, São Paulo, 05315-020, Brazil;-23.534537;-46.7318802;83;true;true;Brazilian;A very safe bet, where the experience is such that you will always enjoy a good meal, whether you order the famous “dadinhos de tapioca”, the delicious “torresminhos”, the traditional “rabada” or less conventional but equally superb options, such as the “beijupira ceviche”. The cuisine follows the same pattern as the flagship Mocotó, namely informal and inclusive cuisine that combines influences from the Sertão region courtesy of founder José Almeida (the chef's father) and an innovative approach from renowned cook Rodrigo Oliveira. Even though the original chef is not present In this Vila Leopoldina outpost, it is clear that the brand’s identity remains intact through expressive flavours and seasonings. Simplicity is very much to the fore here, a sentiment enhanced by the cheerful colour scheme and the open kitchen running the length of the dining room and is one of the main reasons it is never empty. If you’re keen to savour the chef's homely cuisine, we recommend arriving early as the restaurant does not take bookings.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5654;Più Higienópolis;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Higienópolis 618, São Paulo, 01238-001, Brazil;-23.5422871;-46.6577731;87;true;true;Italian, Creative;If you’re passionate about Italian cuisine and delicious fresh pasta, you’ve probably already heard of this restaurant, as Più is one of the pioneers of Italian cooking in the Greater São Paulo area. Under the baton of chef Marcelo Laskani, it now has its second outlet in the Shopping Pátio Higienópolis, where the innovative cooking calls upon top-quality Brazilian ingredients. Dishes such as tuna carpaccio stand out for their fresh, light touch, and are raised to an even higher level by a delicious accompaniment of fresh tomato, raspberry vinegar and burrata. No review of Più is complete without mentioning the house speciality, the braised ossobuco which is slow cooked for 12 hours and served with a creamy aligot of manioc with cheese. The superb array of cocktails adds to the experience!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5655;Cora;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Amaral Gurgel, 344, São Paulo, 01221-000, Brazil;-23.5447748;-46.6480109;99;true;false;Brazilian, Farm to table;Located in the heart of the city, in an unusual sixth-floor setting with views of the Minhocão, Cora is one of the most popular restaurants in São Paulo. The kitchen here is run by Argentinian chef Pablo Inca, whose aim is to “share experiences connected with the land for an urban experience”. The concise menu is designed for sharing and changes in line with the availability of the best market ingredients. Having said this, some dishes are permanent fixtures, such as the unmissable squid omelette, which highlights the chef’s roots, and the duck heart accompanied by a delicate roasted cauliflower and onion cream. Another amazing option is the “olhete” fish with caju, lemon and pepper, which is fresh and full of flavour. An excellent choice of wines and other drinks completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5656;Petí Gastronomia;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Cotoxó 110 - Loja Pintar, São Paulo, 05021-000, Brazil;-23.5283406;-46.68242;98;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that will come as something of a surprise given its location inside the Pintar Artistic Materials boutique, in the Pompeia district of the city. Here, you’ll find an unpretentious yet welcoming ambience, plus a glass-fronted patio with an organic garden. Young chef Victor Dimitrow, who gained experience working in leading restaurants in Europe, creates contemporary cuisine which is fragrant, full of taste and highly expressive from fresh and organic ingredients, but without unnecessary frills. The menu is updated every three weeks or so and offers three full options (including cover charge, starter, main course and dessert), a vegetarian version, another that includes the fish of the day, and a fourth with grilled Wagyu beef. These are also complemented by the à la carte. O Petí is only open lunchtimes from Tuesday to Sunday.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5657;Manioca;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Brigadeiro Faria Lima, 2232 3º andar, São Paulo, 01489-900, Brazil;-23.5773311;-46.6890029;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Manioca, a name that is a combination of the Maní group’s other eateries (the eponymous Maní, run by famous chef Helena Rizzo, and Padoca), is its more informal offshoot offering comfort food and signature dishes from the group’s flagship restaurant. The day-to-day cuisine comes courtesy of young chef Thaís Alves Braga who, having found inspiration in leading restaurants around Brazil, returned home to train up in readiness for the head role here. Manioca is located inside the Iguatemi shopping mall, in an extensive space with high ceilings and lots of natural light through its plant-adorned windows. The menu features a variety of “belisquetes” and burgers cooked in the Josper oven or, if you prefer, the famous PF Manioca (fillet steak served with a poached egg and roasted plantain), one of the house specialities. There’s also a mouthwatering selection of fresh fruit juices!;Air conditioning;[]
5658;Banzeiro;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Tabapuã 830, São Paulo, 04533-003, Brazil;-23.5838596;-46.6786397;96;false;false;Brazilian;This culinary jewel in the Itaim Bibi district is a popular restaurant that delights the palate of regulars and new customers alike. Chef Felipe Schaedler is renowned for bringing the flavours of the Amazon to this bustling metropolis. The exotic decor includes vibrant photos and even a canoe called a “banzeiro” that represents the passage of boats along this legendary river. Here, fire and the grill take centre stage, with some dishes prepared using ancestral techniques that are still used in the northwest Amazon. Without a shadow of a doubt, its classic dishes remain the best option, including “ticada” river sardines and the roasted tambaqui, served in portions that make them perfect for sharing. The choice of dessert is easy: the irresistible “cupuaçu” with chocolate brigadeiro!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5659;Miam Miam;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua General Góis Monteiro 34, Rio de Janeiro, 22290-080, Brazil;-22.9558572;-43.1800341;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that opened in Botafogo in 2005 and occupies an old property that belonged to chef Roberta Ciasca's grandmother. After graduating in France, the chef opened this restaurant that encapsulates her origins thanks to the retro furniture, cheerful and colourful decor, exposed brick walls and vintage wooden floors. The menu, which follows the concept of “comfort food”, concentrates on traditional Brazilian recipes which are always meticulously presented and based around the latest techniques, and is divided between Miam Miam’s classic (and most popular) dishes and seasonal options (which change constantly), a tasting menu, plus a midweek “executive” menu. We can particularly recommend the curried chicken and shrimp croquettes, both of which are perfect.;Air conditioning;[]
5660;AE! Café & Cozinha;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Áurea 285, São Paulo, 04015-070, Brazil;-23.5869125;-46.6455873;96;false;false;Brazilian;Occupying a charming property in the trendy Vila Mariana district, this restaurant boasts a simple yet welcoming ambience and is run by chef Ygor Lopes and pastry chef Walkyria Fagundes, both of whom have trained in leading eateries in Spain and Brazil. The cuisine here is strongly focused on sustainability and is showcased on a menu that changes with the seasons. In addition to the à la carte, you’ll find an “executive” midweek menu along with breakfast served on Fridays, Saturdays and Sundays. The menu includes dishes made for sharing, such as the crispy Lua Cheia savoury cheese pastry with a red pepper sauce, and the homemade Cavatelli pasta served with a ragù of mushrooms, macadamia nuts and Tulha cheese. To round off your meal, the tempting desserts are presented in an attractive display cabinet.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
5661;Zena Cucina;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Peixoto Gomide 1901, São Paulo, 01409-002, Brazil;-23.5679072;-46.6641298;36;true;false;Italian;A focal point for lovers of Italian cuisine, with a name that is the Genoese word for the delightful city of Genoa and a decor and cuisine that transport guests to this picturesque city in Northen Italy. In this relaxed, rustic setting, famous chef Carlos Bertolazzi creates Mediterranean-inspired cuisine, including fresh homemade pasta. Standout dishes here include the focaccia (made with extremely fine pasta and generous fillings) and the mandioc gnocchi with an enticing ossobuco ragu, and for dessert the superb cannoli filled with chocolate and oats, and the “doce de leite” with banana. This delightful experience is enhanced by the superb selection of wines and other drinks on offer.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5662;Barú Marisquería;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Augusta 2542, São Paulo, 01412-100, Brazil;-23.5630033;-46.665559;79;false;false;Seafood;You’ll find this small restaurant with a pleasant and relaxed ambience in a charming property called Villa San Pietro tucked away along Rua Augusta. Here, the main focus is on fresh fish and seafood cooked on the grill, as if you were dining by the seaside. Colombian Dagoberto Torres, who arrived in São Paulo when he was a youngster, decided to use all his knowledge of maritime ingredients to the benefit of his own eatery. The menu offers options such as oyster and shrimp tostadas, different types of ceviche and grilled dishes that include the catch of the day, pitù, tuna, squid, octopus etc, all prepared with a creative flair and lots of flavour. We recommend pairing these culinary delights with some of the delicious cocktails on offer here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5663;TonTon;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Caconde 132, São Paulo, 01425-010, Brazil;-23.57449;-46.6583618;81;false;false;French, Regional Cuisine;A charming townhouse in a quiet residential district, where chef Gustavo Rozzino brings together experiences acquired in the various countries in which he has worked. In this bistro-style ambience, he creates uncomplicated cuisine that makes full use of top-quality Brazilian ingredients and Mediterranean techniques. The menu, which ranges from steak tartare and fresh pasta to rack of lamb, also includes standout dishes such as braised beef short rib and the irresistible pork roulade cooked in the oven for 12 hours, plus the exquisite “Bobó Tonton”, served with grilled pink prawns, basmati rice, grilled banana and farofa (manioc flour) which is totally addictive! If you want to take a break from the food here, why not head upstairs to the pleasant bar with its list of incredible cocktails?;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5664;Artigiano;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Epitácio Pessoa 204, Rio de Janeiro, 22471-002, Brazil;-22.9841868;-43.2145699;68;true;false;Italian;This restaurant is a classic address in the city, offering an authentic dining experience courtesy of Emilia-Romagna, one of Northen Italy’s most iconic food regions. As its name suggests, everything is home-made in artisanal style: pastas, pizzas, sauces, breads and desserts are all made daily and cooked or finished to order. We particularly recommend the zucchini flowers stuffed with mozzarella and anchovies and served with a delicious tartare sauce. Another dish that you won’t want to miss is the garganello with lamb ragù, one of Northern Italy’s most characteristic pastas, served with a surprising yet delicious sauce.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5665;Nomo;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Harmonia 815, São Paulo, 05435-000, Brazil;-23.5515407;-46.6907549;69;false;false;Contemporary;A delightful restaurant in the Vila Madalena district of the city, featuring a natural plant-covered façade, a glass-fronted dining room and an open kitchen with restrained tones and a simple decor. Here, chef Nando Carneiro creates innovative cuisine with a contemporary touch and a combination of seasonal ingredients. The superb wine selection is the domain of sommelier and front-of-house manager Patrícia Werneck. The cooking at Nomo is out of the ordinary and includes combinations of high-quality ingredients and impressive flavours that come as a pleasant surprise. One of the standout dishes on offer is the braised cabbage and romaine lettuce served with a sweet contrast of muhammara, dukkah and pistachios. Another amazing option is the smoked cupim cut of meat, accompanied by creamy potato mash, toasted almonds and fried garlic.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5666;Mocotó;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Nossa Senhora do Loreto 1100, São Paulo, 02219-001, Brazil;-23.4866595;-46.5816442;86;false;false;Brazilian;This is the first branch, opened 50 years ago by the Pernambuco-born Zé Almeida and famous thanks to his delicious Mocotó. Nowadays, the kitchen is headed by renowned chef Rodrigo Oliveira, who is keeping his father's legacy alive by offering the best of the Sertão region’s cuisine via the motto “made with the eyes on the world and the feet grounded in the Sertão”. The restaurant has retained its relaxed, simple atmosphere, and its fundamental concept is inclusivity, with no focus whatsoever on social or cultural differences. The chef conjures up a menu that ranges from snacks and full portions to traditional dishes and special cocktails which are in perfect harmony with the cuisine here. As well as the highly-sought-after “dadinhos de tapioca”, make sure you try the perfect “carne de sol” cooked on the grill and served with “bottled butter”, and the “moqueca sertaneja” stew, a vegan option full of flavour!;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5667;Sult;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Fernandes Guimarães, 77, Rio de Janeiro, 22290-000, Brazil;-22.9554938;-43.1816941;83;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Sult is the perfect choice if you’re looking for a relaxed restaurant offering excellent value for money. Located close to the Morro de São João hill, it boasts a modern, uncluttered decor plus an impressive open kitchen and bottles of wine with notes from guests written on them as added decoration in the dining room. Under the baton of Belém-born chef Nelson Soares, it offers dishes that combine his Northern Brazilian identity with the cooking of Italy. An example, and one that delights all his guests, is the fresh fillet of pirarucu fish served with a creamy tucupi and jambu risotto. Having said this, the chef’s signature dish is his classic meat lasagne, which is simply perfect. An interesting selection of natural, organic and biodynamic wines is also available.;Air conditioning;[]
5668;Più Pinheiros;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Ferreira de Araújo 314, São Paulo, 05428-000, Brazil;-23.5602819;-46.6981475;93;false;false;Italian;Occupying a charming small house in the Pinheiros district, Più boasts a pleasant, cosy ambience enhanced by its exposed brick walls, open garden and views of the kitchen and bar. This restaurant was one of the first in the region to offer a unique combination of affordable prices and a fusion between Italian cuisine and high-quality Brazilian ingredients. In the kitchen, run by chef Marcelo Laskani, expect classic dishes such as lasagne bolognese made with green pasta and enhanced with Italian mortadella, and the mouthwatering polpettone gratin stuffed with cheese and topped with a delicate tomato sauce. The chef also surprises guests with innovative dishes such as ravioli stuffed with pear and chilli jam, shimeji and gorgonzola cheese fonduta – an almost indescribable combination!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5669;Shihoma Pasta Fresca;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Medeiros De Albuquerque 431, São Paulo, 05436-060, Brazil;-23.5539738;-46.6859487;48;true;false;Italian;This restaurant has become one of the most talked-about addresses for affordable and delicious fresh pasta, so it’s hardly surprising there’s always a queue out of the door. The project was originally started by chef Marcio Shihomatsu, an aficionado of Italian cuisine, with his home delivery service. Following on from the success of this, and the arrival of chef Bia Limoni to run the kitchen, they opened a restaurant where handmade delicacies are now created daily. The compact interior features an open kitchen, where you can watch pasta being made, enhanced by a pleasant terrace for a relaxed lunch or dinner. The menu is full of excellent options, but the house speciality is the delightful agnolotti di agnello (pasta filled with lamb braised in white wine) with a butter sauce and mint oil – simply divine!;Bring your own bottle,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5670;Pici Trattoria;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Barão da Torre 348, Rio de Janeiro, 22411-000, Brazil;-22.9831234;-43.2052303;69;true;true;Italian;Located opposite the Praça Nossa Senhora da Paz, where the large windows at the entrance will definitely attract your attention thanks to the list of restaurants across Italy from which this trattoria takes its inspiration (such as the Enoteca Pinchiorri and Massimo Bottura’s Osteria Francescana). The enticing cuisine here is at times high on tradition with plentiful portions. On the impressive menu you’ll find standout dishes such as the mouthwatering fettuccine with a truffle and mushroom sauce and free-range egg, and the unmissable Wagyu polpetone filled with mozzarella di bufala and served with taglione in sage butter. Photos of famous jazz musicians and soft music in the background combine to provide a harmonious backdrop.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5671;Tordesilhas;Brazil;São Paulo;Alameda Tietê 489, São Paulo, 01417-020, Brazil;-23.5606478;-46.6674954;67;true;false;Brazilian;Tordesilhas is under the command of chef Mara Salles, who has three decades of experience behind her. The key tenets of her cuisine are a fondness for dishes for sharing and the showcasing of ingredients from the different regions around the country. Located in the charming Jardins district, in a wonderful space that is full of flavor and hospitality. Her cuisine is a journey across the country’s regions, enhanced by dishes with a contemporary touch that are prepared with the utmost care and attention. Options includes à la carte dishes that range from starters such as pirarucu fish balls and shrimp in manioc cream with coconut milk to traditional Moqueca fish stew. On Saturdays, the famous Feijoada features on the menu. We also highly recommend the simply sensational chilli preserves prepared on the premises.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5672;Fitó;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Cardeal Arcoverde 2773, São Paulo, 05407-004, Brazil;-23.568077;-46.694927;87;false;false;Brazilian;It’s not by chance that this restaurant occupies a charming, whitewashed property with blue windows – an external decor that is reminiscent of houses in inland areas of northeast Brazil, a part of the country that provides the inspiration for the cooking here. Under the baton of chef Cafira Foz, the exclusively female team creates cuisine that combines traditional flavours with an international touch. On the menu, options include crab cooked in a shrimp broth, and the authentic “paçoca” (shredded sun-dried beef served with “baião de dois” and plantains), a simple dish yet one full of strong flavours. For dessert, the “pirangi” (whole cashews with apple jam and “requeijão de corte” cheese), showcases genuine Brazilian flavours that will certainly leave their mark. Why not round off the experience with one of Fitó’s innovative cocktails prepared by the skilful and talented hand of bar manager Renata Adoración?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5673;A Baianeira - MASP;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Paulista 1578, São Paulo, 01310-200, Brazil;-23.5612374;-46.6556879;35;true;true;Brazilian;Located inside the emblematic MASP, on basement level two of a building housing the largest collection of European art in Latin America. The Minas Gerais-born chef Manuelle Ferraz, originally from Almenara, not far from the border with Bahia (the region from which the restaurant takes its name), is at the helm of this second Baianeira restaurant, following the success of the first venture in the district of Barra Funda. In this relaxed and simple setting decorated with artisanal pieces from around Brazil, the traditional cooking features redefined flavours in dishes that showcase excellent technique and refinement. To start, why not try the delicious “pão de queijo”, a recipe that has been with the chef since she first started out. Among the main courses, we recommend the traditional “baião de dois” (black-eyed peas with rice) with mouthwatering braised meat, and make sure you save space for the unmissable plantain crème brûlée. Daily specials are also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
5674;Feriae;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Padre Carvalho 171, São Paulo, 05427-100, Brazil;-23.5613095;-46.6964163;61;true;true;Farm to table;A new restaurant in Pinheiros that stands out from the crowd and has impressed local Paulistas with its cuisine. Its Latin name pays homage to agriculture-related religious festivals held during Roman times, and this is exactly what Feriae is looking to showcase. The philosophy champions seasonally inspired organic ingredients sourced from small-scale producers, with a focus on the maximum usage of the produce used, and a reduction in the use of plastic in accordance with sustainable practices that influence the flavour of their dishes. The open grill is the main cooking technique used in a number of dishes such as the grilled leeks served on a bed of romesco sauce and quark cheese, which is an excellent choice as a starter. The organic cooking here is complemented by a selection of natural wines that are in perfect harmony with the dining experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5675;Cuia;Brazil;São Paulo;Av. Ipiranga, 200 - Loja 48, São Paulo, 01046-010, Brazil;-23.5461117;-46.6439476;87;true;false;Creative;Renowned chef Bel Coelho is known for her commitment to healthy food, the use of native ingredients and the preservation of Brazil’s varied food cultures. In this casual and welcoming restaurant shared with the Livraria Megafauna bookshop in the iconic Copan building, guests can enjoy all-day dining between the bookshelves, in front of the kitchen or in the open-air dining space, with options varying between toasted sandwiches and “pão de queijo” to “baião de dois” (black-eyed peas with rice). Dishes you won’t want to pass up include the appetising squid tempura with tapioca and caju ponzu, and the mouthwatering “Our Oswaldo Aranha (grilled filet mignon). The “toucinho do céu” with Brazil nuts, a silky “puxuri” cream and orange is the perfect way to round off your meal, accompanied by a superb array of organic wines and innovative drinks.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5676;The Kith;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Rebouças 3875, São Paulo, 05401-450, Brazil;-23.5738515;-46.6956427;58;false;true;Brazilian;Now located at a new address along the iconic Avenida Rebouças, this restaurant has retained the same cuisine as before, namely traditional Brazilian dishes with an international influence, where the grill plays a leading role. This modern setting is bathed in natural light and features an industrial-inspired decor and glass-fronted kitchen. During the week, the “executive menu” and a lighter option are available, as well as the calorie-balanced Ravenna menu for those keen to maintain a healthy diet. On Saturdays, the service is à la carte. Once seated, guests are served a light focaccia as an appetiser, followed by a selection of dishes such as shrimp ceviche with Peruvian corn and red onion, the famous filet mignon stroganoff and, for dessert, a delicate chocolate mousse tart with chestnut flour.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5677;Maria e o Boi;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Maria Quitéria 111, Rio de Janeiro, 22410-040, Brazil;-22.9825882;-43.2070274;63;false;true;Meats and Grills, International;If you’re keen to try a restaurant serving authentic Brazilian cuisine prepared with ingredients from across Brazil, this rustically inspired house with a plethora of wood and a pleasant outdoor terrace on a charming corner of the Ipanema neighbourhood could be the perfect place. Here, chef Vanessa Rocha conjures up cuisine that brings a smile to your face and warms the heart thanks to superb cuts of meat accompanied by harmonious and balanced combinations of ingredients. The menu offers a range of generously portioned and affordably prices dishes, making it difficult to choose between the attractive creamy vatapá fish and shrimp croquette and the “pato apaixonado” with duck heart and creamy mashed plantain. Follow this, perhaps, with the absolutely perfect coconut and mango pudding!;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
5678;Komah;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Cônego Vicente Miguel Marino 378, São Paulo, 01135-020, Brazil;-23.52668;-46.651875;70;true;true;Korean;The Komah restaurant is renowned for its Korean cuisine with a contemporary touch – a combination of traditional recipes, signature dishes and international culinary techniques. The chef here ensures a unique gastronomic experience that challenges the palate through a panoply of flavours, with a full range from spicy to sweet. The concise menu features ten savoury dishes and three desserts, as well as a tasting option created personally by the chef. Dishes include “yukhoe”, a Korean steak tartare with cured egg yolk and Asian pear, “japchae” (sweet potato pasta with assorted vegetables and honey), and “kimchi bokumbap” with omelette, the house's signature dish, featuring rice sautéed with kimchi with a creamy omelette.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5679;Didier;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Vinícius de Moraes, 124, A, Ipanema, Rio de Janeiro, 22411-010, Brazil;-22.983581;-43.202713;95;false;true;French Contemporary;Now located in Ipanema, Didier boasts a modern, vibrant feel with a dining space on two floors with plenty of natural light. Named after its chef, Didier embraces the essence of French and local cuisine on an à la carte with a tempting array of delicacies to satisfy every palate. Dishes range from French classics such as snails, beef tartare and cassoulet to iconic bistro fare including grilled octopus alla putanesca. Other traditional options with a traditional flavour include the black risotto and the rabbit stew, while those with a more adventurous palate can try the popular and perfectly prepared French-style “moqueca” stew.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5680;Bistrot de Paris;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Augusta 2542, São Paulo, 01412-100, Brazil;-23.5629278;-46.665678;43;true;false;French;This romantic and welcoming dining space inside the charming Villa San Pietro along the busy Rua Augusta has the feel of an authentic Parisian bistro. Run by renowned French chef Alain Poletto, the restaurant showcases classic French cuisine with a focus on traditional recipes and the use of top-quality ingredients. Here, you can enjoy dishes such as the superbly prepared and authentic Pâté de Campagne, and beef bourguignon with home-produced bacon and onions, served with vegetables and a delicious red wine sauce. To complete your meal, the traditional and mouthwatering caramelised Tarte Tatin highlights why this superb restaurant is an absolute must! The choice of beverages on offer here is equally impressive.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5681;Ecully;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Cotoxó 493, São Paulo, 05021-000, Brazil;-23.53148;-46.68427;71;false;true;International;This restaurant located on the rear patio of a century-old property has the added and somewhat surprising bonus of a large wine shop (Grand Cru). Enthusiastically run by young chefs Juliana and Guilherme (a couple who met in the French town of Écully), it features outdoor tables in the courtyard with its abundant greenery, including a large jabuticabeira tree growing between the tables. In this setting, which is particularly romantic at night when candlelit, the cuisine showcases regional ingredients and combines Brazilian, French and Italian influences through dishes such as the shellfish-based “confit do mar” and the delicious suckling pig cooked at low temperature and accompanied by manioc purée, caramelised onion and basil pesto.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5682;Le Bife;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Pedroso Alvarenga 1088, São Paulo, 04531-004, Brazil;-23.5823193;-46.6807291;63;true;false;Meats and Grills;The cuisine here at Le Bife is based around the “bistronomy” concept with its focus on fine dining and reasonable prices. This simple idea involves guests choosing a cut of meat which is then served with fries, a choice of sauces, plus a salad. All-you-can-eat sides are also available, including rice, mashed potato, creamed spinach, and a variety of vegetables, all designed for sharing. Make sure you save space for dessert, as the crème caramel comes highly recommended. The decor here is minimalist in style and features two inter-connecting rooms and an impressive glass-fronted wine cellar. We advise booking ahead as it is always full.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
5683;Corrutela;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Medeiros de Albuquerque 256, São Paulo, 05436-060, Brazil;-23.55524;-46.68576;30;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;In this location next to the famous Escadaria do Patápio staircase, chef César Costa is a strong advocate of sustainability, which sees him adopting initiatives that are totally focused on the environment, such as having his own composting system, managing his own solar power, grinds the corn used in the polenta, and avoiding the use of plastic packaging. In this minimalist setting with an industrial vibe, he creates tasty, uncomplicated dishes in an open kitchen where guests can sit at the counter opposite. On the seasonal menu that changes through the year, standout dishes include the oyster ceviche with Brazil nuts, which is refreshing on the palate. The homemade Corrutelas chocolate tart is prepared with organic cocoa beans from the region of Bahia and chocolate made on the premises.;Air conditioning;[]
5684;Brasserie Victória;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Presidente Juscelino Kubitschek 545, São Paulo, 04543-010, Brazil;-23.5882343;-46.6751687;96;false;false;Lebanese;It is estimated that the Lebanese community and its descendants living in Brazil nowadays is greater than the current-day population of the Lebanon. The first immigrants arrived in the 1880s, consequently, many dishes of Arabian origin became typical Brazilian dishes, such as sfiha and kibe. This brasserie has been serving authentic Arabian cuisine for seven decades, transforming the Victoria into a gastronomic icon in the Greater São Paulo area. Founded by Dona Victória, it has been run by the same family for several generations. The menu offers a wide variety of mouthwatering options such as kaftas, sfihas (open, closed and folded), kibes, labneh and pitta bread. Make sure you save space for the incredible desserts here, such as the nut-filled atayef pancakes topped with a delicious lemon syrup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
5685;Brota;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Conde de Irajá, 98, Rio de Janeiro, 22271-020, Brazil;-22.953481;-43.196034;57;true;false;Vegetarian;Brota occupies a charming mansion in Botafogo and is surrounded by a well-maintained garden. Inside, the elegant ambience features a contrast between striking red mouldings on the doors and large windows, a wood-inspired decor, an impressive bar, and leafy plants that add a touch of freshness to the setting. The kitchen is run by chef Roberta Ciasca from the renowned Miam Miam. The cuisine here is based around innovative vegan and vegetarian dishes designed for sharing. The menu includes classics such as the superb “brotinha” rice balls filled with tomato, pesto and olives or wasabi cream with chutney. The guava compote with Canastra cheese foam and brown sugar crumble is a perfect combination to end your meal!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5686;Kotori;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Cônego Eugênio Leite, 639, São Paulo, 05414-011, Brazil;-23.563422;-46.6810655;41;true;false;Japanese;An innovative dining option in the trendy Pinheiros district of the city. The focus here is very much on Japanese culture, with cuisine inspired by yōshoku cooking which reinterprets Western-style dishes to Asian tastes. Chef Thiago Bañares offers just a single menu option, albeit with a cutting-edge touch and one that includes Brazilian ingredients in his dishes. The latter include a selection of hot options, such as the Eryngil mushrooms, which is combined with chicken broth, tucupi and mustard seeds, plus matured fish cooked on the grill. It’s worth saving space at the end of your meal for the “rabanada de shokupan”, a bread dessert served with a milk ice cream and toffee syrup. To round off the experience to the full, choose from the list of classic and creative cocktails, or the interesting array of sakes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
5687;Balaio IMS;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Paulista 2424, São Paulo, 01310-300, Brazil;-23.556194;-46.662113;83;false;false;Brazilian;If a combination of art and excellent food appeals to you, this restaurant in the Instituto Moreira Salles, recognised as one of the best cultural centres in the city, is definitely the place for you, where you can savour the brilliant cuisine of chef Rodrigo Oliveira. The cooking here is centred around the best ingredients, with everything prepared with faultless skill and professionalism. The aim is to mix the flavours from the diverse cultures across Brazil (a “balaio” is a typically Brazilian “straw basket”), in dishes such as the famous “dadinhos de tapioca”, and the tender braised beef cheek, served with a pleasantly textured sauce and freshly baked focaccia. To finish, the pequi fruit pie with chocolate ganache and a surprising pequi foam gives an indication of why this restaurant is always full!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5688;A Baianeira;Brazil;São Paulo;Dona Elisa 117, São Paulo, 01155-030, Brazil;-23.5301045;-46.6627074;97;false;false;Brazilian;Simplicity has always been key here ever since the business first opened as a modest garage selling nothing more than the traditional “pão de queijo”. Nowadays, owner-chef Manuelle Ferraz makes a point of rekindling her roots through home-style dishes that combine the cooking of the Bahia and Minas Gerais regions, albeit with technical skill and a focus on top-quality ingredients. In this, the chef’s very first Baianeira venture, savour options such as the unmissable pão de queijo filled with “carne de panela” (stewed beef) or “requeijão de corte” cheese. For your main, choose one of the signature dishes such as the beef “picadinho” with egg and plantain, daily specials and, on Thursdays, the superb “feijoada” stew. We can also recommend the “goró de mainha”, an artisanal Cachaça, a spirit made according to a family recipe, which highlights authentic Brazilian flavours to the full!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5690;Los Consentidos del Barrio;Mexico;Benito Juárez;Manzanas 27-B, Tlacoquemecatl del Valle, Benito Juárez, 03200, Mexico;19.3747083;-99.1777389;73;true;true;Mexican;Climb the stairs to this second-story restaurant with a large dining room with wood tables and black chairs. The built-in charcoal grill keeps things toasty in the dining room, so you may want to grab a seat on the spacious patio with tall tables and chairs. The house specialty is tacos al carbon, with thinly sliced meat that is skillfully cooked on the grill, then diced. Proteins are the focus here, but vegetarian tacos aren't forsaken. Sliced poblano, nopales and mushrooms are among the top choices. Another can't-miss menu item? Their arrachera, or skirt steak, with its perfectly pink center.;;[]
5691;Taquería El Jarocho;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Tapachula 94, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4112574;-99.1659833;93;false;true;Mexican;El Jarocho has eighty years of history backing it up, and this Roma Norte spot has been run by three generations of the same family. Come for breakfast, lunch or early dinner to this former tortilleria where a server will take your order. They're known for their guisado-style tacos, offering a wide variety of proteins and vegetables stewed in a number of different ways. And, while you don't need any extra reason to visit here other than their guisado tacos (the pork flank with a morita chile sauce really seals the deal with its spicy, smoky flavor), don't skip their campechano taco with chopped steak and topped with crispy chicharron. Fresh tortillas are made in-house.;;[]
5693;Masala y Maíz;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;C. Artículo 123 116, Colonia Centro, Cuauhtémoc, 06040, Mexico;19.432995;-99.1490523;53;false;true;Fusion;It's small, but Masala y Maiz is always busy, drawing eager crowds of young diners who flock here for the vibe and the food. Run by a couple of chefs who infuse the restaurant with a commitment to social causes, this cuisine is different and highly original. Dishes blend Indian, Mexican, and East African cultures to create intense flavors and interesting nuances. This is food that wins you over and most certainly leaves you with an impression. Highlights include samosas de suadero, camarones para pelar and kuku poussin. Panacotta de té limón is a light and refreshing dessert to complete a highly satisfying meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
5694;Taqueria Los Cocuyos;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Simón Bolívar 67, Centro, Cuauhtémoc, 06000, Mexico;19.43037;-99.1387648;47;false;false;Mexican;This taqueria in Centro Historico has been a mainstay since 1980. Standing by a cauldron of meats bubbling away, a chef at the front wields a cleaver with lightning speed. An expansive dining room speaks to just how busy this place gets. Offerings are numerous but recent highlights include tender, melting cabeza as well as the classic al pastor, both finished tableside with salsas and a squeeze of lime. Swing for the suadero later in the evening when the meats have had plenty of time to braise.;;[]
5696;Raíz;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Schiller 331, entre Horacio y Presidente Mazaryk, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11560, Mexico;19.4321022;-99.1865284;91;false;false;Contemporary, Mexican;Located on the ground floor of a residential building, this restaurant could easily go unnoticed, but one bite of their contemporary Mexican cooking and you won't soon forget its address. A welcoming staff invites you to take a seat and peruse their menu or opt for one of two tastings. A plantain molote with a bit of pickled onion is a nice opener before savoring the flavors of an aguachile in a cuttlefish ink broth. Tostada de camarón is a spot-on treat, then pescado zarandeado delights with its crispy skin. To finish, arroz con leche is comforting and classic.;Terrace;[]
5697;Comedor Jacinta;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Virgilio 40, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11550, Mexico;19.4300983;-99.1962132;60;true;false;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;This cozy restaurant is owned by the renowned chef Edgar Núñez. Here, the premise is traditional cuisine that draws on his childhood memories. The dishes are simple, but tasty, with excellent technique and abundant portions--all at a reasonable price. The menu has a botaneria section, with dishes based on corn, and another section with molcajetes, or dishes made in this traditional mortar from Mesoamerica, accompanied by guacamole and handmade tortillas. Some of the outstanding items include tostada de callo de hacha, tacos de tuétano, and huachinango zarandeado. Flan de cajeta is the perfect dessert.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5698;Molino El Pujol;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Benjamín Hill, 146, Hipódromo Condesa, Cuauhtémoc, 06100, Mexico;19.4077163;-99.1771063;90;false;true;Mexican;This small spot in La Condesa feels like a chic neighborhood place with polished concrete and white tiled walls. It saves most of its precious real estate for the kitchen though there is a wood counter with six seats along with an additional handful of seats outside. The concise menu is focused on items made from corn nixtamalized daily on-site (think tamales, tacos, chilaquiles, and enfrijoladas). There are also items to take home like the excellent tortillas—grab them warm if you are lucky. The tamal de calabaza is a freshly steamed orb of flavorful yellow masa studded with bits of tender pumpkin and plated with a petite salad dressed with candied pumpkin seeds.;;[]
5699;El Vilsito;Mexico;Benito Juárez;Av. Universidad 248, Narvarte Oriente, Benito Juárez, 03020, Mexico;19.3895466;-99.1527829;21;true;false;Mexican;Even though this famous taqueria is indeed connected to an auto repair shop and opens only at night, the setup is anything but piecemeal. There’s plenty of seating and plenty of servers, with flatscreen televisions, a roaring grill, and spinning trompos. Everyone is here for the al pastor, which features a towering stack of tender, shaved pork, sliced pineapple, and a riot of cilantro and onions. The formidable “gringas” version is deliciously messy, arriving on a flour tortilla coated with cheese.;;[]
5700;Comal Oculto;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Manuel Gómez Pedraza 37, San Miguel Chapultepec, Miguel Hildalgo, 11850, Mexico;19.4140655;-99.1835137;71;false;true;Mexican;On a breezy, tree-lined street in San Miguel Chapultepec, everyone sits shoulder to shoulder at a single communal table stretching the length of two parking spaces. The convivial setting suits this unassuming restaurant, which offers an all-day menu of comforting classics that revolve largely around the comal. A single chef weighs, presses, and griddles everything to order. The gordita especial, packed with chicharron and tender, shredded carnitas, is a favorite. Late night out? Swing for the chilaquiles chamorro with salsa verde and kick it up a notch with the fiery salsa on the table. Other hits include crispy flautas stuffed with melting cheese and a picturesque enmolada covered in a sweet mole poblano. Expect a wait come weekend brunch.;Terrace;[]
5701;Siembra Tortillería;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Av. Isaac Newton 300, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11560, Mexico;19.4364918;-99.1851933;25;false;false;Mexican;Chefs Karina Mejía and Israel Montero opened this modern taqueria in Polanco in 2019. Located just a few doors down from their full sit-down restaurant, Siembra Comedor, this sidewalk hotspot shells out a wide variety of tacos built on heirloom corn tortillas and quality proteins. Fish al pastor boasts wonderfully charred spices while the arrachera feels like a play on steak frites thanks to the crispy, shoestring potatoes on top. The kitchen works quickly, and tacos are ample in size.;Terrace;[]
5702;Fugaz;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Orizaba 3B, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4239222;-99.1612934;28;false;false;Mexican, Mediterranean Cuisine;Located in Roma Norte, the low-key vibe of this pleasant cafe belies some very serious and creative cuisine. Simple but attractive, the setting boasts a bright green facade, sandy-hued terrazzo flooring, light wood furnishings and pale unadorned walls.Chef Giuseppe Lacorazza studied in Buenos Aires and spent time in kitchens in Europe and New York City. The cuisine here has a faint Mediterranean accent to its Mexican foundation and is enhanced by vegetable-dominated preparations. The day's catch may be transformed into crudo tossed with white beans and set atop a creamy almond and brown butter puree, and gnudi are served in a light broth with tender slices of white onion and some Parmesan cheese. The Italian sausage sandwich is a meaty option as well.;;[]
5704;Tacos Doña Mary La Gritona;Mexico;Monterrey;Avenida Francisco I. Madero Ote, Centro, Monterrey, 64000, Mexico;25.6861282;-100.3351957;15;true;false;Mexican;Read the menu and be ready to order at this spot named after Doña Mary, affectionately known as "la gritona" or "the yeller" because she gently scolds people who slow down the line. Family-run, this taqueria has been around for over two decades. Order outside, get your tacos, then cross the street and sit inside with plastic chairs and tables.Your first decision will be flour or corn tortillas, but there is no wrong choice since both are made fresh onsite. Toppings include onion, cilantro and your choice of three salsas that range from mild to spicy—don't miss the salsa molcajeteada—and while offerings vary by the day, don't leave without trying the tacos de barbacoa.;;[]
5705;Punta Corcho;Mexico;Puerto Morelos;Av. Rafael E. Melgar, SM01, MZ6, Lt. 01-01, Puerto Morelos, 77580, Mexico;20.8472192;-86.8762427;86;true;true;Seafood, Mexican;You’ll have an excellent vantage to see the nearby shore from this second-floor perch, whose thatched roof and open-air plan allow the welcome ocean breeze to circulate. Better still, you can enjoy the view alongside a bountiful menu of memorable seafood offerings and tropically inflected cocktails. Shareable starters include puffy gorditas filled with roasted octopus, salsa verde, and melty quesillo, as well as an assortment of vibrant and inventive ceviches and aguachiles. Mains are likewise not boxed in by tradition, with typical Mexican flavors alongside the likes of Provençal butter and horseradish aïoli. With so many options to choose from, decisions can be a challenge, but the friendly staff will be only too happy to steer you in the right direction.;;[]
5706;Alfonsina;Mexico;Oaxaca;García Vigil 183, San Juan Bautista La Raya, Oaxaca, 71232, Mexico;16.9804444;-96.7264922;64;false;false;Mexican;At several points en route to this hidden restaurant, you will wonder if you’re lost. But hold steady: A half hour’s drive south of Oaxaca city and down several bumpy dirt roads, this humble, reservation-only destination is as close of an invitation into someone’s home as you’re going to get. Chef Jorge León and his mother Doña Elvia run this idyllic, breezy backyard with tables set under a canopy of trees. The tasting menu is by no means formal or lengthy. Rather, expect a leisurely procession of traditional, comforting dishes like tamal with pickled onions and red cabbage or chile relleno with lentils and avocado slices. A duo of moles with rice and a barbacoa taco round out this homestyle meal complemented with excellent tortillas.;Terrace;[]
5707;Filigrana;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Av. Veracruz 62, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4175252;-99.1740256;90;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;This colorful, sun-soaked address from Chef Martha Ortiz has looks and substance in spades. At the base of a residential building in Roma, find a concrete jungle with purple-cushioned chairs, soaring floor-to-ceiling windows, and fully grown trees woven throughout. And much like the space itself, the cooking is equally stylish with thoughtful, playful interpretations of familiar favorites. Start with the gordita, a delicate, crispy disc packed with tender, shredded tongue and garnished with fried epazote leaves. Is there a prettier tamal around? This one is presented as a toasted cube made with fried portobellos and set in a warm guajillo chili sauce. Another highlight is the pozole brujo, featuring superbly tender chicken and a soulful, spicy broth.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5708;Aleli Rooftop;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Sinaloa 141, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4202488;-99.170114;65;false;true;Grills, International;As its name suggests, Aleli is indeed located on the rooftop, so while the location may not be a surprise, the food is. You'll soon see (and smell) why, as the embers from the grill permeate the air. It's certainly worth snagging a seat at the bar to watch the cook at work on the grill. The menu of traditional Mexican cuisine may not be extensive, but it proudly displays dishes that stand out for their flavor, quality products and presentation. Highlights include brocheta de camarón, pan de papa a la brasa, lomo de pescado zarandeado, and of course the much-loved cheesecake asado. Cocktails and wine complete the sunny picture, but perhaps even more smile-inducing is the palatable price.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5709;Caracol de Mar;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Campeche 340, Col. Hipódromo Condesa, Cuauhtémoc, 06100, Mexico;19.4089529;-99.1735242;48;true;false;Mexican;Caracol de Mar has a prime position in the city center near the Metropolitan Cathedral, but the location isn't the only reason this spot stands out from the crowd. This seafood-focused restaurant showcases Mexican culinary knowledge, and the moderate prices are a boon in an area not known for being wallet friendly. Begin with aguachile de camarón, a deliciously fresh dish that is as beautiful as it is refreshing. Pulpo al carbón de olote is a well-prepared plate with good flavor and a delightful smoky note. To finish, the passion fruit granita, if offered, is as simple as it is delicious.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5710;Galea;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Sinaloa, 67, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4209063;-99.1668636;60;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;This corner charmer boasts a terrace out front, while inside, the use of wood keeps things firmly planted between the old and new worlds. There is an amiable, casual vibe to Galea, and with prices that don't break the bank, it's a favorite among locals. The focused Italian menu is concise but manages to present a varied selection all the same. Be sure to check the dishes of the day (and note the crudo specials, too) and always order a pasta. In fact, all of the pasta dishes can be made as half portions if you're tempted to try more than one. Focaccia made in-house starts things off, then a plate of gnochetti with ragu de mariscos feeds the soul. Fish of the day in a creamy beurre blanc is a hit, but save room for the panna cotta, given a bit of a Mexican slant here.;Terrace;[]
5711;Tacos Los Alexis;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Chiapas 46, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4133903;-99.1569349;84;false;true;Mexican, Creative;Chef Alexis Ayala's taqueria is located next door to his sister spot, Pargot, and the set-up is similar, with a thoughtfully done interior prep area and a handful of tables arranged under a covered sidewalk.Tacos Los Alexis offers a short list of varied preparations that include volcanoes, costras, as well as delightful tacos. The vegetarian taco is an elegant preparation featuring an excellent yellow masa tortilla topped with huitlacoche wrapped in crisped cheese.;;[]
5712;Las Quince Letras;Mexico;Oaxaca;C. de Mariano Abasolo 300, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0641335;-96.7208848;67;false;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Mole is everywhere at Chef Celia Florián’s restaurant, which opened in 1992. You can find it served with plantains, inside large empanadas, and on top of enchiladas. But from amarillo to coloradito to verde, the one that shines brightest is her mole negro. Black as night, smoky, and tantalizingly charred, it needs nothing more except for a tortilla or a bit of rice. This recipe and many others have deep roots: Florián grew up on a farm in La Ciénega and learned to cook from her mother and grandmother. Another highlight is the wonderful garnachas istmenas, crispy masa cakes topped with tender shredded beef buried under a pile of pickled cabbage. Still to this day, Florián enjoys global recognition for her contributions to Oaxacan cuisine.;;[]
5713;Cobarde;Mexico;Oaxaca;Macedonio Alcalá 505, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0663457;-96.7237116;99;true;true;Contemporary;With a primetime terrace that overlooks the Zócalo and across to Santo Domingo, in a space that oozes style, Chef Pako Cortés is cooking like nobody else. Experience in kitchens from Japan to New York has given him the tools to weave in international flavors with conviction. Meals must begin with toasted naan crowned with beef tongue, capers and yuzu aioli. It is as delicate as it is brilliant. Other dishes are not what they sound like: The salad is unexpectedly addicting, warmed in a tandoor and piled high with bacon, peas and parmesan. The chicken dumpling is actually a deboned and stuffed chicken wing glazed in gochujang. It’s a fun time all-around from start to finish.;Great view,Terrace;[]
5716;Mestixa;Mexico;Tulum;Avenida Satélite S/N, Tulum, 77760, Mexico;20.2131167;-87.4587157;100;false;true;Fusion, Mexican;Bustling Tulum is the perfect spot for Chef Hinostroza's second restaurant, Mestixa. This intimate spot beckons with its simple but welcoming ambience. Asian accents, including a snake mural and traditional lighting, hint at what's to come on this highly original Asian-Mexican fusion menu. Order the bao, deliciously stuffed with pickled pear, hoja santa, pickled cucumber and cashew macha sauce. Few dishes define this cuisine as well as the birria ramen, made with egg noodles, beef shank, cascabel chili, and tamarind. It's an excellent mix of textures, colors and flavors, and generously sized. Finally, a waffle taco is tucked with yuzu parfait, dried plum and caramelized white chocolate for a sweet sendoff.;;[]
5717;Tierra del Sol;Mexico;Oaxaca;Reforma 411, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0651829;-96.7220185;37;true;false;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;Chef Olga Cabrera is a force to know. A stone’s throw away from the famous church in Centro Histórico, Cabrera runs three different businesses within a single building. A bakery stocked with sweets perfumes the room, while her Atoleria pours cups of coffee and hot chocolate. The actual restaurant is further back, past the comals cooking tetelas, memelas, tacos and tlayudas, and up the stairs to the shaded rooftop. While serving dishes from her childhood and classics from today, she celebrates farmers and their products, and puts their stories front and center. Salsa made tableside is a welcome touch, followed by fragrant soups and lovely, hearty moles (Laurel mole is  a winner.) Lunchtime brings welcome views of the surrounding mountain ranges.;Great view,Terrace;[]
5718;Cocina de Campo by Agricole;Mexico;El Pescadero;Carretera a Los Cabos Km. 59, El Pescadero, 23310, Mexico;23.37862;-110.1816497;67;true;true;Contemporary;Located in El Pescadero along the highway that leads from Cabo to Todo Santos, this multi- concept space includes a farm shop, as well as a full-service restaurant, set outside within the garden. The contemporary menu leans Mexican with Californian elements, and the cooking is simplified to allow the ingredients to take center stage. Take the tomatoes, for instance. Layered slices topped with Kalamata olives over a coarse basil pesto prove that the best dishes don't need much intervention. Batter-dipped fried fish or the shaved ribeye are winning taco choices. Then, for dessert, the soft vanilla cake with fresh strawberries and cream sauce is a must. The cocktail menu is strong and creative.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5719;Labo Fermento;Mexico;Oaxaca;Manuel Bravo 401, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0654023;-96.7270226;26;true;true;Asian;You won’t find another restaurant in Oaxaca quite like this one. Chef-owner Joseph Gilbert and his team are obsessed with fermentation and go to great lengths to make their own kimchi, shoyu, miso and more. Asian flavors course through the menu in the form of plucky pork wontons glossed in chili oil, Chinese barbecue pork buns and soothing dashi. One can’t-miss item is the fried chicken that’s marinated in shoyu, garlic and ginger and comes with a clever lemon aioli made with sardine stock. This is the kind of food best for sharing in a space that’s sunny, breezy and high-energy thanks to an open-roof and an edgy playlist.A shop in the front sells many of their sauces already bottled, as well as specialty teas and ceramics made by local artisans.;Terrace;[]
5720;La Olla;Mexico;Oaxaca;Reforma 402, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0647582;-96.7218591;40;false;true;Mexican;For a restaurant with decades of history behind it, La Olla looks rather ordinary and would be easy to pass by on the street without a second thought. Alas, Chef Pilar Cabrera is a name to know. A champion of traditional Oaxacan dishes and an ambassador for the region, she has run this restaurant and her own cooking school, Casa de Los Sabores, for over 20 years. A comal by the front door is your signal to start with the maiz sampler featuring squash blossom quesadillas and crispy plantain tacos smeared in a finely spiced coloradito. No meal is complete without the mole negro, which is wonderful by itself but stunning with the clever addition of plantain and sweet potato purees. The menu also features a generous number of vegetarian dishes.;Terrace;[]
5721;Humo y Sal;Mexico;Ensenada;Km 108, Zona Playitas, Ensenada, 22860, Mexico;31.8634374;-116.6541;96;false;false;Seafood, Mexican;The Hussong family is well known in the Ensenada area for their long-running Sano's steakhouse. Located just next door, this sleek box of a dining room bears its own distinct profile. A white tiled open kitchen and bar area are fronted by tables and concrete flooring. The bar menu is displayed on a wall-mounted letterboard and offers local beers and cocktails like the mezcal sour.The menu is concise, focused on seafood, and is impressively prepared. Sashimi, tiradito and oysters are nice precursors to fresh pasta with shrimp, pizza with octopus or the very clever and highly popular tuna al pastor taco with its intriguingly crumbly spice-rubbed fish, pickled onion slivers and avocado puree.;;[]
5722;Villa Torél;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Bodegas de Santo Tomás Km 94.7 Carretera Federal No. 3, 22766, Villa de Juárez, B.C., Valle de Guadalupe, 22766, Mexico;31.9753343;-116.661332;32;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Chef Alfredo Villanueva is at the helm of this spot tucked within the Santo Tomás winery. Framed by lavender bushes and citrus trees, it's entirely outside (read: best visited in season) and shares views of the rolling hills. The breezy ambience is echoed in the casually sophisticated Mexican menu with contemporary French and European touches, as in a crudo of horse mackerel served with blue corn tostadas. Rice with pastrami lengua is a creative dish that manages to be perfectly satisfying, while bold flavors appear in a dish of roasted eggplant with shredded smoked bluefin tuna. Dishes are sized for sharing, and desserts bear the same rustic elegance, with options that span crispy-crinkled layers of phyllo with jocoque, chopped pistachios, and local honey to a wedge of warm date tart.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5723;Flora's Field Kitchen;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Ánimas Bajas, San José del Cabo, 23407, Mexico;23.0799707;-109.6771851;94;true;true;Contemporary;Originally opened by Gloria and Patrick Greene as an organic farm, this ever-so-charming spot has evolved since the late 90s and now features a wine and coffee bar, as well as shops set among the mango trees and this restaurant. It's family run and all heart—they grow their own produce, raise chickens, have an onsite butcher program, and bake all the breads, too. The tempting menu features offerings such as Neapolitan flatbreads, salads, and lighter starters like a flavorful gazpacho. From there choose one of their sandwiches, or an entrée like the pork chop with crispy potatoes. Portion sizes are generous but save room for their sweet treats baked onsite, and house-made ice creams and sorbets.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5724;Cetli;Mexico;Tulum;Carr. Tulum-Coba Km. 2.5, Villas Tulum, Tulum, 77780, Mexico;20.2305289;-87.4588579;50;true;false;Mexican;Cetli is just outside the city and the tourist hustle and bustle, located along the road that leads to the ruins of Cobà. Inside, white walls are enlivened by colorful paintings and antiques, while wood tables and chairs set a rustic tone. Chef Claudia Perez Rivas has fashioned a truly Mayan experience here, where the generous and tasty dishes are as colorful as the art decorating the walls. Meat and fish are the main inspiration, as in dishes like istak, a fish fillet cooked in seawater and doused with a thick, not-too-sweet white almond mole with a touch of parsley, dark chocolate sauce and sesame seeds. Nimbe, a vanilla and chocolate pancake filled with ice cream, is rich and delightful.;Car park;[]
5725;Metate;Mexico;Cabo San Lucas;Av. Crispin Ceseña S/N, Cabo San Lucas, 23454, Mexico;22.9049043;-109.8905764;90;true;false;Mexican;Located in Cabo San Lucas across the highway from the line-up of hotels, this spot down a dirt road is welcoming and attractive. A white stucco entryway leads to a dining area, a portion of which is arranged on a stone patio shaded by trees strung with lights. The kitchen and tiled bar are also open-air.Metate translates to a shallow stone used for grinding maize or other grains, while the foundation of the menu is antojitos and grilled meats cooked over a wood fire. The tacos Baja presents a duo of blue corn tortillas topped with morsels of flaky white fish encased in squid ink-tinted batter and topped with finely shredded pickled cabbage for a visually stimulating presentation.;;[]
5726;La Cocina de Doña Esthela;Mexico;El Porvenir;Rancho San Marcos, El Porvenir, 22755, Mexico;32.0194865;-116.6634692;86;true;false;Mexican;From chef/owner Blanca Esthela Martínez Bueno, what began with humble roots in 2008 making burritos for local vineyard workers has evolved into one of the most famous restaurants in the Valle de Guadalupe. It's loaded with charm, from the heavy wood tables to the boisterous crowd of visitors and locals. Breakfast is served all day, and while a no-reservations policy means a wait, it's worth it to sample dialed-in cooking with hearty portions. Get the café de olla and dig into the menu where you'll find huevos of all kinds alongside chilaquiles and gorditas rellenas. House specialties include fluffy elote pancakes and a Sinaloan-style, dried shredded beef with egg, sliced peppers, and onions with stewed beans that beg to be sopped up with housemade tortillas.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
5727;Axiote Cocina de Mexico;Mexico;Playa del Carmen;34 Nte., M. 65, Lt. 11, Playa del Carmen, 77710, Mexico;20.6341766;-87.067817;53;false;true;Mexican;Here in the Riviera Maya, Axiote Cocina de Mexico walks the line between spotlighting local culinary traditions and giving them a modern boost. Inside, the guano leaf-roof lends a palapa style to the dining room. Carefully presented and beautifully served, the generously portioned plates are one hit after another. Start with the tostadas de mais azul, knowing that the spice levels are indeed as described. Guacamole never fails but skip the tortilla chips and go for the chapulines (grasshoppers) instead. Fried and slightly spicy, they're a house signature. Birria de cordero is fork-tender, with elote, nopal, pickled onion and vegetables, and is especially hearty. Laminado de mango, perfectly ripe and accompanied by honey, orange foam and cocoa, is a superb finish.;;[]
5728;Merak;Mexico;Villa de Juárez;Lerdo de Tejada & Ignacio Comonfort, Villa de Juárez, 22766, Mexico;31.9655959;-116.642355;42;false;false;Contemporary, Mexican;The smell of wood smoke will lead you to this well-appointed outdoor space within the Tres Valles winery, where Chef Joel Quintana presides with a relaxed, affable demeanor. His grill-centric cuisine is hearty and unpretentious, but the flavors and techniques are finely tuned, drawing upon French and Asian influences for cooking that you won't soon forget. A signature dish of alitas de mar ("seafood wings") is a case in point, featuring yellowtail collar impeccably grilled until juicy and lip-smacking, dressed with a luscious tangy sauce that blends guajillo chile oil, ginger, and roasted garlic. More substantial dishes, like grilled beef, lamb, or whole fish, are ideal for sharing, and Chef Quintana will happily curate an impromptu tasting menu upon request.;;[]
5729;Carmelita Molino y Cocina;Mexico;Tijuana;Jiménez 7771, Independencia, Tijuana, 22055, Mexico;32.5240243;-117.0417355;100;false;false;Mexican;Named for Chef José Figueroa's grandmother, who inspired his love of cooking, this charming Tijuana dining room has an airy vibe with warm-toned wood furnishings, tile-and-concrete flooring, and a screen-covered roof. Corn is revered here and is sourced from small family farms around Mexico, then nixtamalized and ground in-house. Tortillas are prepared on the comal up front for the tacos and tostadas that comprise the menu, while ceviche, and egg dishes round it out. You can't go wrong with chilaquiles dressed with salsa borracha, but don't sleep on the tamal of the day. It's big, prepared in a banana leaf, and may be filled with braised beef rib and roasted local cherry tomatoes.;;[]
5731;Ike Edoyakiunagi Asahitei;Japan;Nara;29 Haibara Shimoidani, Uda, Nara, 633-0241, Japan;34.52878;135.950916;30;true;true;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;There is a saying about the depth of skill an unagi chef needs: three years to learn how to skewer it, eight to learn how to dress it and a lifetime to learn how to grill it. While grilling unagi might be the most difficult, Hideki Morimoto was tasked with it from a young age by his father, the then owner. Edo-style grilling includes steaming beforehand and is something the father learned while training in Tokyo. He buys in mostly large unagi and far-infrared grills it.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5732;Unagino Toyokawa;Japan;Nara;3-3-12 Tomio Motomachi, Nara, Nara, 631-0078, Japan;34.69246;135.732245;85;true;true;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;The owner-chef apprenticed at an unagi restaurant in Osaka after becoming enamoured of the world of unagi artisans. He took the name of his teacher’s restaurant out of gratitude and grills plump ‘aote’ unagi, Kansai-style, over bincho charcoal. There is a saying that when it comes to learning unagi, skewering technique takes three years, dressing it takes eight years and grilling it takes a lifetime to master. As such, he has devoted himself to unagi.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5733;le content;Japan;Nara;1-3-8 Ayameike Minami, Nara, Nara, 631-0033, Japan;34.697512;135.761053;40;true;true;French;The restaurant’s name is a play on the French adjective ‘content’, meaning ‘happy’ or ‘satisfied’. It is also a term that the chef’s mentor complimented him with during his apprenticeship. At lunchtime, simple prix fixe are offered, but in the evening diners get à la carte items focused squarely on flavour. Offerings such as pâté de campagne, beef cheek simmered in red wine and tarte Tatin showcase traditional French cooking. Cassoulet de Toulouse captures a flavour that etched itself on the chef’s memory.;Air conditioning;[]
5734;Noto Toto Teuchisoba Tabiki;Japan;Nara;1-3-6 Horyuji Nishi, Ikarugacho, Ikoma-gun, Nara, 636-0114, Japan;34.611572;135.730208;75;false;false;Soba;Seiji Matsushima grows crops and makes pottery. He doesn’t just knead earth, though, he also kneads soba. The thin juwari soba set out on dishes he made himself exudes rusticity and the way of life of a self-described farmer. He grows the buckwheat berries for the sobagaki himself. Basil picked in the field in the summer is served with soba topped with a thick dashi-rich sauce, and winter yuzu is served with hot soba. Grated daikon is used in place of wasabi.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
5735;Shikinoaji Enzu;Japan;Nara;6-5-14 Omiyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8115, Japan;34.685666;135.807866;99;true;false;Japanese;The cheerful hospitality of the owner-chef at this kappo will put you at ease. He offers a wide selection of dishes, including tsukuri, tempura and grilled items. He serves several appetisers so you can snack on them while choosing your main dishes. Regular offerings include deep-fried mugwort fu and eggplant with dengaku miso. Although not on the menu, sushi can be prepared if you place an order. The spirit of service he shows makes this a great place to dine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
5736;Sosakukushinomise Rindo;Japan;Nara;224-1 Tsujimachi, Ikoma, Nara, 630-0212, Japan;34.694948;135.707086;94;true;false;Kushiage;Chef Ueda came up with creative skewers to make use of his experience in both Japanese and Western cuisine. The honekiri-treated hamo requiring very precise cuts is where his Japanese culinary skills shine. The croque monsieur is a French recipe. The menu starts with Western appetisers and incorporates surinagashi, gazpacho and other soups. The free-wheeling culinary ideas on display in the menu have you looking forward to what’s coming.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
5737;YAMAOKA PIZZA;Japan;Nara;455 Onitoricho, Ikoma, Nara, 630-0237, Japan;34.67117;135.685183;69;true;false;Pizza;This restaurant on Mt. Ikomayama overlooks the city. The Italy-trained chef bakes pizzas with his own original take. The key to the taste is Ikoma spring water – the water’s sweetness and softness give the pizza real character. Made using less salt compared to the Italian recipe, the crust has a uniquely fluffy texture. The standard offering is margherita pizza made with vegetables from a local farm. Have your fill of Ikoma pizza you won’t find in Naples or Rome. It’s closed for the month of February.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view;[]
5738;Kushizukushi;Japan;Nara;31 Yanagimachi, Nara, Nara, 630-8353, Japan;34.67858;135.824628;17;true;false;Kushiage;The creative skewers here feature seasonal ingredients and rare ingredients, such as Japanese glass shrimp in the spring, ayu with roe in the autumn and oysters in winter. Items like vegetables pickled in sake lees and goma-dofu give you the full Nara experience. To end comes nyumen that goes down well or dashi chazuke made with rice grown by the owner-chef’s brother. Each item on the set menu is given an extra touch for texture and flavour, making it a truly appealing set meal.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5739;Simple comme Bonjour;Japan;Nara;68-3 Kawaharajocho, Tenri, Nara, 632-0016, Japan;34.600237;135.833375;27;false;true;French;Kotaro Kawaguchi chose the path of French cuisine, following in the footsteps of his father, who was a cook on a cruise ship. He says that training at Pierre Gagnaire in Paris, a restaurant he had long admired, boosted his morale as a chef. There, he learned the techniques to create harmony between ingredients. There are no standard offerings here, as he is always inspired to offer new creations.;Air conditioning;[]
5740;PIZZERIA TRATTORIA MAGAZZINO;Japan;Nara;172-1 Kamada, Kashiba, Nara, 639-0227, Japan;34.520592;135.712308;39;false;false;Pizza;The pizza here is prepared true to how it’s done in Naples, with chef Hironori Noda reproducing those authentic flavours. What Naples has that Nara doesn’t is an ocean so, in response, he came up with the idea of a restaurant that’s all about the fields. He grows the vegetables himself and makes them the main ingredients. The garden is his mother’s, and he harvests the vegetables himself, meaning that the bounty of Kashiba proffered here truly springs from ‘Mother Earth’.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only - lunch;[]
5741;Pizzeria Luna Nuova;Japan;Nara;2-1-35 Omiyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8115, Japan;34.682651;135.817442;48;true;true;Pizza;What drew chef Kenji Akai to pizza was its simplicity, being a complete meal in a single dish. He’s passionate about Neapolitan pizza baked in a firewood oven and uses Italian wheat for lightness and fragrance in the crust. The popular item on the menu is the D.O.C. Pizza of buffalo mozzarella, dried cherry tomato and basil. His experience in Italian cuisine is also evident in the home-style Italian sausage and chargrilled dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5742;Masala an TAKUMI;Japan;Nara;2281 Nakamachi, Nara, Nara, 631-0052, Japan;34.68009;135.742349;78;false;false;Indian;As a veteran of the Indian culinary world, Chef Takumi Sakanaka is a master spice artisan. His ‘eclectic Japanese, Western and Indian’ fare is born from his Japanese sensibility and experience with French cuisine. The Masala Hassun appetizer is inspired by traditional kaiseki multi-course meals. Pâté de campagne infused with dry curry and handmade Miwa pasta are true to Nara. As the phrase on the shop curtain says, this is ‘nouvelle cuisine of India’.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Shoes must be removed;[]
5743;Shunsai Chuka Bar Mitsukan;Japan;Nara;4-4-5 Naizencho, Kashihara, Nara, 634-0804, Japan;34.513999;135.791298;85;true;true;Chinese;This Chinese bar appeals with its casual izakaya-like atmosphere and authentic cuisine. The aim is to be a place where people can come to drink, so they are very particular about the local Nara sake and shochu. The chef being an expert in Sichuan cuisine, the specialities are spicy chicken and mapo tofu. He also incorporates local ingredients and culture, such as using brand name pork from Gojo to make steamed dumplings, and using ‘Kasa-soba’, from the Kasa area of Sakurai.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5744;Kiminami;Japan;Nara;2201-1 Oshikumacho, Nara, Nara, 631-0011, Japan;34.718044;135.764071;58;true;false;Soba;The owner-chef liked how making soba was a very minimalist process, using only buckwheat and water. That approach is behind his decision not to add any filler ingredients. In the summer, he makes the noodles thin so that they go down smoothly, and thick in the winter so that the flavour delightfully fills the palate as you chew. For an appetiser, we recommend the shrimp tempura, which uses batter mixed with marunuki.;Car park,Cash only;[]
5745;Chukasoba Oshitani;Japan;Nara;5-4-30 Shijooji, Nara, Nara, 630-8014, Japan;34.67885;135.78866;63;false;true;Ramen;The owner-chef came up with various creative ramen dishes from his time training. In opening this restaurant in his hometown, he set his sights on Chinese noodles, which was not very common at the time, and to which he adds his signature touch. The ‘Shoyu’ features kaeshi made with kombu and oysters and is completed with porcini-flavoured oil. The ‘Shio’ is an original, flavoured with shellfish adductor muscles and shrimp, and with truffle oil for fragrance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5746;toi Inshokuten;Japan;Nara;30-3 Hanashibacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8266, Japan;34.68571;135.829041;23;false;false;Indian;The ‘toi’ in the name of the restaurant is an acronym for ‘trip of imagination’. The destination is India, and the mission is to provide traditional Indian dishes. There are meat, fish and vegetable curries. They do things Thali teishoku-style and serve several kinds of curry of your choice on a large plate. You can also add individual items like pakora, an Indian-style tempura.;Air conditioning;[]
5747;Menya Ittoku;Japan;Nara;372-2 Kawaharajocho, Tenri, Nara, 632-0016, Japan;34.598622;135.836008;88;false;false;Ramen;Every time there’s an order, you hear the sound of the motorized slicer. It cuts pork fillets thin like uncured ham. The signature dish is salt-flavoured ramen. The dashi is made from whole chicken, kombu and katsuo-bushi, and the glutamic acid and inosinic acid produce a synergy of umami. If you order ‘shimemeshi’, which is rice with chicken, to go with the remaining soup, it’s like you’re having chicken zosui.;Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5748;A VOTRE SANTE;Japan;Nara;6-26 Shinasahigaoka, Ikoma, Nara, 630-0253, Japan;34.68595;135.706132;85;false;true;French;Chef Yaoki Tsujimura says that he wants to communicate the sights he saw in France. He recalls memories from training in southern France in the 1990s. Everything from gougère to bread and small confectionery is freshly baked. Dishes made using a generous amount of butter and garnished with sauce have a nostalgic French aroma to them. When you hear the word ‘santé, it means a fun time is about to begin.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5749;Xin Liu He;China Mainland;Hangzhou;37 Yile Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.285615;120.120452;30;true;true;Hang Zhou;Since 1987, diners have been flocking here for authentic traditional Hangzhou food. The head chef excels at preparing river fish, such as river shrimps in Huadiao wine, a feast of runny roe, briny-sweet meat and mesmerising aromas. With a bit of luck, you will get to savour the tender oily flesh of steamed river eel with Chinese ham – best enjoyed with their home-brewed bayberry wine. Ask the servers about the daily specials.;Air conditioning;[]
5750;Lai Cui Mian Guan (Ji Mao Road);China Mainland;Hangzhou;315 Ji Mao Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.1645882;120.073226;37;false;true;Noodles;For over a decade, this tiny noodle joint has been packed with diners, despite higher prices than its competitors. An array of noodle soups and blanched noodles tossed in sauces are offered with a choice of toppings, all in generous portions and made with quality ingredients. Try the blanched noodles topped with stir-fried pork liver and kidney. Stir the curly hand-rolled noodles in the sauce well and enjoy their springy texture.;Cash only;[]
5751;Definitely Fresh;China Mainland;Hangzhou;2F, Meifan Plaza Proya, 588 Xixi Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2653563;120.0985672;63;true;true;Zhejiang;Nothing speaks of the ethos of this restaurant serving Wenzhou and Taizhou dishes more eloquently than its name – yes, freshness is key. The freshest seafood from southern Zhejiang, such as razor clams, live oysters and mud whelks are prepared in myriad ways. The springy fishcake bursts with seafood umami. The duck soup with Chinese herbal medicine is both tasty and nourishing. The dim sum, eg rice cake or wheat cake, are rustic and comforting.;Car park;[]
5752;Er Ba Jiu Su Mian Guan;China Mainland;Hangzhou;289 Tianzhu Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2367927;120.0987257;57;false;true;Vegetarian;Next to Fajing Temple, this tiny vegan joint is always packed with tourists and locals. The location certainly accounts for its popularity… large portion sizes and very affordable prices play their part too. Their signature noodle soup with assorted vegetables has a rich and sweet tomato broth, plus bamboo shoot, peas, fried gluten, wood ear mushroom and cashew nuts. Consider ordering the dumplings filled with dried tofu and potherb mustard to go with it.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5753;Hui Xin Xiao Chi Dian;China Mainland;Hangzhou;83-1 Deyuan Road, Gongshu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.3036612;120.1563349;84;false;true;Dim Sum;This tiny shop frequented by locals is always jam-packed at lunchtime. With tasty offerings at bargain prices, it's not hard to see why! The menu features just two dishes – wonton and shao mai – but they come with an array of fillings and can be served in soup or tossed in sauces. For example, shao mai with juicy pork and diced bamboo shoot wrapped in paper-thin skin. The oversized wonton with salted egg yolk and pork filling is beautifully folded.;Cash only;[]
5754;Wu Zi Mian Guan;China Mainland;Hangzhou;116 Huansha Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2523209;120.1619374;99;false;true;Noodles;After opening in 2017, Wu Zi shot to fame, becoming the best-known noodle shop in the area. Classic Hangzhou-style noodles are either served in soup or tossed in sauces with various toppings – prepared to the exacting standards of the owner, a chef by profession. The pork kidney and liver are nicely browned while retaining their succulence and a lovely chewiness. Another must-try classic topping: shrimps and eel sautéed with onion, mushrooms and dried tofu.;Cash only;[]
5756;Ge Lang Guan;China Mainland;Hangzhou;130-135, Building 1, My Babini Shopping Mall, 698 Xiaohe Road, Gongshu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.3298557;120.1325285;50;true;false;Zhejiang;It's a bit out of the way, but that doesn't stop diners from coming here in droves for authentic Shaoxing dishes. The menu is written daily on the whiteboard. All ingredients are seasonal and shipped from Shaoxing. The free-range chicken marinated in aged distillers' grains has firm, flavoursome flesh with a hint of wine aromas. The stinky duo, or stinky tofu with fermented amaranth stems, exudes a stench that you'll either love or hate!;Cash only;[]
5758;Qing Chun Perma;China Mainland;Hangzhou;181 Baileqiao, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2468965;120.104276;97;true;true;Vegetarian;Tucked away in a serene garden near Lingyin Temple, this restaurant serves vegetarian dishes that draw on Chinese traditions, as well as Southeast Asian flavours. Most ingredients are organic, including naturally grown grains and rice. In the bright, airy space with an open kitchen, try the delicious, silky smooth hazelnut-brown rice milk. Fresh dim sum are hand-made to order, such as organic dark rye wonton drizzled with house-made chilli sauce.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
5759;Nan Feng Fan Dian;China Mainland;Hangzhou;819 Renmin Road, Xiaoshan, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.1627277;120.2858934;24;true;true;Hang Zhou;This no-frills shop is relatively inconspicuous, so, you may well walk right past it without noticing. But those in the know flock here for authentic Xiaoshan cuisine made with the freshest seasonal produce. There is no menu – pick your own food from the counter or ask the owner for recommendations. The must-try steamed miiuy croaker is silky in texture and loaded with umami. Poached free-range chicken and steamed veggies also hit the spot every time.;Cash only;[]
5760;Bao Zhong Bao Shi Fu;China Mainland;Hangzhou;224 Qingtai Street, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2498499;120.1759195;45;false;false;Hang Zhou;This household name, famous for home-style Hangzhou cooking, has been around for over 20 years. The dining area occupies two floors, but seats are limited: at peak hours, expect to queue or share a table with others. The signature cold appetiser of pork kidney dressed in a sweet tangy sauce is meticulously prepared. The deep-fried tofu skin wrap with a pork and scallion filling and the braised pork with smoked dried bamboo shoots are also well made.;Cash only;[]
5761;Xiao Dian Huang;China Mainland;Hangzhou;205-207, 2F, Building 8, Greenland Central Plaza, Daguan Road, Gongshu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.306121;120.1384528;43;false;false;Zhejiang;The owner, who hails from Shaoxing, insists on driving back to his hometown every other day to source the freshest ingredients for his restaurant – which explains why the menu is handwritten on a white board and different every day. That said, the must-try stinky tofu is a permanent fixture: made with 20-plus-year-old fermenting brine from his family, it has rich deep flavours that complement the lamb brain it is steamed with. Try the river fish, too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Terrace;[]
5762;Fang Lao Da (Shangcheng);China Mainland;Hangzhou;629 Jiangcheng Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2380416;120.1714839;23;false;true;Noodles;Born into a family of chefs, the young owner started as an apprentice and worked his way up. Exacting about his noodles, he has them tailor-made to the texture he wants. All Hangzhou-style noodle dishes are made to order with traditional toppings and sauces. The pork kidney, from pigs slaughtered the same day, has a crisp, springy texture. The pork braised in a dense marinade with dried tangerine peel exudes citrus aromas. Expect to queue at peak times.;Cash only;[]
5764;Yue Ji;China Mainland;Hangzhou;4F, Building 1, Phase 1, Star Avenue, 228 Jiangnan Avenue, Binjiang, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2093797;120.2047897;87;false;true;Zhejiang;A sign that says "stinky" or "rotten" might not usually sound appetising, but Yue Ji prides itself on the six features of Shaoxing cooking: soy sauce, distillers' grains, rottenness, stench, wine and pickles! Try dishes marinated with distillers' grains sauce, such as duck gizzard or pork tongue and belly. No meal here is complete without the notorious deep-fried stinky tofu and steamed minced pork patty with rotten millefeuille tofu skin. Pre-ordering recommended.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
5765;Rong Xian Mian Guan (Qianjiang Road);China Mainland;Hangzhou;629 Qianjiang Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2375011;120.1907208;94;false;false;Noodles;This shop with over 20 years of history moved to this location a few years ago. Its signature sliced fish noodle soup with pickled cabbage isn't commonly found in Hangzhou-style noodle shops: thin slices of lean snakehead fish is briefly blanched in a fish bone stock with spices and pickled cabbage. Traditional noodles such as pian er chuan and ban chuan are best enjoyed with marinated meats such as chicken feet, duck's head or meatballs.;Cash only;[]
5767;Fu Yuan Ju (Shangcheng);China Mainland;Hangzhou;35 Hefang Street, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2413194;120.1720154;28;true;true;Hang Zhou;This acclaimed eatery prides itself on its home-style dishes. Expect queues at mealtimes! The juicy chicken dressed in scallion oil exudes heady aromas. Steamed vegetarian chicken and bamboo shoots with dried pork marinated in soybean paste evoke childhood memories for many a Hangzhou local. Freshwater fish is another strong suit – check out the bream, eels and crabs in the fish tank at the entrance and ask the servers the best way to have them cooked.;Cash only;[]
5769;Fu Xing Mian Wang;China Mainland;Hangzhou;178 Hedong Road, Gongshu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.290021;120.1557906;68;true;false;Noodles;This shop may lack a snazzy decor, and nobody gets a table to themselves, but there are always queues eager to be cooked for by the self-proclaimed "noodle king". The signature tomato sauce noodles with scrambled eggs are tangy and appetising, best enjoyed with a sprinkle of pork cracklings. All made-to-order, the delicious toppings are served piping hot – try the deep-fried carp. Those with a big appetite can even get extra noodles for free.;Cash only;[]
5770;La Natural;USA;Miami;7289 N.W. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33150, USA;25.8422037;-80.200688;61;false;false;Pizza;You wouldn’t think to make reservations for a pizza place in Little River, but think again. The crowds can be relentless at this popular hangout, which feels rather like an underground party by way of concrete floors and dim lighting.Creative toppings like za’atar and Sichuan peppercorns sing on stunning, picture-perfect pies zealously charred in a wood-burning oven hiding behind the bar. We’re partial to the classic burrata and basil pie, which arrives puffy and pillowy thanks to the signature crust that's cold-fermented for 48 hours. An astute selection of starters (try the papaya with kumquat) and one of the city’s longest lists for natural wines only add to the appeal of this essential pizzeria. A personable staff keeps a close watch on every table.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5771;El Turco;USA;Miami;184 N.E. 50th Terr., Miami, 33137, USA;25.821874;-80.192171;36;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This charming café, sheltered within a shopping enclave, hosts a loyal following at outdoor tables shaded by age-old oak trees. Inside, the kitchen team works out of a glass-walled kiosk, dressed up with blue-and-white tile as well as neatly lined cans and bottles.The menu is an enticing offering of breakfast fare, featuring organic eggs that support Turkish mezzes, manti and savory pastries like borek. Baked in-house, this burnished coil is stuffed with spinach, sprinkled with sesame seeds and garnished with cherry tomatoes. The izmir kofte arrives in a mini ceramic dish filled with beef meatballs baked in tomato sauce alongside batons of roasted potato. A single charred jalapeño adds the perfect bit of heat to each mouthful.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5774;Sanguich De Miami;USA;Miami;2057 S.W. 8th St., Miami, 33135, USA;25.7655471;-80.2287433;66;true;true;Cuban;What started out as a little shipping container in 2017 has morphed into this brick-and-mortar hot spot in Little Havana. There is almost always a line of diners vying to squeeze into the narrow space, designed with emerald-green walls, vibrant tile and sleek brass trimmings.Everyone comes for the same thing: a superb Cuban sandwich featuring pork butt that's been marinated for a week in garlic and spices, then pressed between expertly grilled slices of house-made bread. A heavier but equally flavorful alternative is the lechon, starring tender shredded pork slathered in garlic-cilantro aïoli. Thick baton-shaped croquetas also impress if you need a pre-sandwich bite.;Air conditioning;[]
5775;Otto's High Dive;USA;Orlando;2304 E. Robinson St., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5458131;-81.3526243;58;false;false;Cuban, American;This tiny but oh-so-sweet space recalls the charm of Old Florida with its whitewashed brick walls and white tile floors. Billed as a neighborhood rum bar, Otto's High Dive is on point at every turn, from the genuine service to the unfussy but well-executed food. The kitchen delivers a concise edit of Floridian/Cuban fare with oodles of tropical elements. Begin with oysters before moving on to an array of cold and hot plates ranging from a shrimp cocktail that's all grown up with its thick "Bloody Mary" sauce to chicken mojo and ropa vieja with sides like rice and beans. Cinnamon bread pudding topped with a delightfully tangy cream cheese whip is a memorable sign-off. Rum is all around, from the Cuba Libre on tap to the daiquiris available by the pitcher.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
5776;Norigami;USA;Winter Garden;426 W. Plant St., Winter Garden, 34787, USA;28.5644074;-81.5906446;23;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;There are just eight seats at this tiny but mighty spot at the Plant Street Market from Chef David Tsan. This is sushi done in a casual "choose your own adventure" style, as guests pick from various cuts of fish and shellfish and then select as either nigiri, sashimi aburi or temaki. It's all fun and may include winning plates like popcorn hamachi, a surprising dish with avocado puree, dots of whipped cream cheese and finished with popped sorghum. Shima aji displays its buttery best as nigiri, and it's all about the sear on the avocado served with a sweet kabayaki sauce. Good products and solid techniques are on display in the hand rolls, where fillings like shredded blue crab make an impression. Can't choose? The well-priced, ten-piece omakase is a nice option.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
5777;Gorkhali Kitchen;USA;Tampa;10044 Cross Creek Blvd., Tampa, 33647, USA;28.1431883;-82.3264981;30;true;false;Nepali, Indian;Take the short drive from downtown for a taste of Himalayan cuisine at Gorkhali Kitchen. The mirrored glass exterior means the interior is kept a secret until you're through the door but come inside to experience this place's warm hospitality.The menu is large with a Nepalese focus along with some Indian elements. Of course, there must be momo, those iconic Nepalese dumplings that are seared, pan-fried or even in jhol (soup). Chili momo filled with chicken is tossed in a fiery sauce that's not for the faint of heart. Sweet at the start, the heat builds and then finishes with a very spicy kick—perfect for heat seekers. Chicken is a popular protein that appears often on the menu, but don't shy away from the goat specialties. They're falling-off-the-bone tender and savory.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5778;Michael's Genuine;USA;Miami;130 N.E. 40th St., Miami, 33137, USA;25.8133573;-80.1927977;59;false;true;Contemporary, American;This Design District pioneer from Chef Michael Schwartz is as popular now as it was when it first debuted almost 15 years ago. A well-heeled crowd flocks here, but whether it's a requisite respite from boutique hopping, a spot to catch up with friends or a meal to close a business deal, this dining delight is for everyone. The courtyard is a lovely place to linger, thanks to its lush greenery, fans and heat lamps (when necessary). The interior space features concrete flooring and an inviting bar. A jazz playlist adds to the upbeat and conversation-filled air.The menu focuses on unfussy yet skillful cooking. Staples like pizza, house-made pasta, crudo, pan-roasted chicken and wood oven-roasted fish keep fans returning time and time again.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
5779;Streetlight Taco;USA;Tampa;4004 Henderson Blvd., Tampa, 33629, USA;27.9300918;-82.5105475;93;true;true;Mexican;This South Tampa taqueria certainly ups the style quotient on the typical taqueria. From the black-painted, exposed ductwork to the tables lacquered with Mexican comics to the open kitchen, this fast casual spot delivers on contemporary flair, and the food isn't pulling any punches, either. Heirloom corn is nixtamalized in house for a menu featuring tacos, tostadas, salsas, sides and more. Don't skip the Sunday snack tostada, an equal parts sweet-and-savory delight with two blue corn tostadas layered with cream cheese with lump crab, diced sweet mango and a mango habanero sauce. The Japanese eggplant taco with an heirloom bean puree and a chile onza salsa has just the right amount of kick. There's a full bar, but a strawberry horchata goes down perfectly, too.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5780;Sushi Saint;USA;Orlando;400 Pittman St., Ste. A, Orlando, 32801, USA;28.5465297;-81.3838953;40;false;true;Japanese;Mike Collantes, Chef/owner of Soseki, has another hit on his hands with Sushi Saint. Attached to a brewery but with a separate entrance, this downtown temaki spot lures guests with its lounge-y vibe and contemporary design. The team take great care in sourcing high-quality rice and nori for their cone-shaped temaki, and while the hand rolls take center stage, their small plates, like Sichuan cucumbers with chili crunch, are worth trying. From the avocado with serrano lime miso to aburi-style scallop with brown butter to shredded snow crab with truffle, cucumber, and finger lime, the temaki offerings are impressive and the ingredients are top notch.;Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
5781;Zaru;USA;Orlando;1114 E. Colonial Dr., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.552986;-81.3648665;80;true;true;Japanese, Udon;This sleek, Mills 50 eatery is located in the same strip as the Tien Hung Market. With an upbeat playlist and an attractive dining room, the restaurant specializes in chewy noodles made from wheat sourced from Japan’s Kagawa Prefecture. Ikura, tempura and top-notch ingredients like Hokkaido uni and A5 Kagoshima wagyu pair with broths of wonderful smokiness and depth. Starters like tatsuta-age (fried chicken) and yaki gyoza (pork dumplings) are familiar and reliable, but consider opting for the ikura onsen, which features a softly poached egg crowned with crispy garlic. Either way, expect precision and intentionality across the board by the team that’s happy to guide you.;Air conditioning;[]
5782;Bachour;USA;Coral Gables;2020 Salzedo St., Coral Gables, 33134, USA;25.7539198;-80.2610106;42;false;false;Contemporary, Bakery;Welcome to the workshop of Chef Antonio Bachour, a talented baker whose brightly colored tarts and elaborate pastries take center stage in this industrial setting. Open since 2019, an arch of roses marks the entrance to this busy daytime spot. Once inside, a perch at the counter in the back offers diners a front-row view of the glass-enclosed bakery. Seating aside, a simple lunch of ham croquettes, crab tostones, or a salad is the best way to start before going all-in on a dazzling array of sweets. Think mango-passion fruit macarons, flaky croissants striped with vibrant green bands of pistachio, indulgent Parisian flans, and other ornate creations that resemble oranges and raspberries. Don’t worry about overordering – these treats travel well.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5783;Psomi;USA;Tampa;701 N. Howard Ave., Tampa, 33606, USA;27.9500225;-82.4826553;33;false;true;Greek;Owned and run by second-generation Greek-American, Chef Christina Theofilos, this daytime eatery and bakery epitomizes warmth and comfort. Strangers become friends in no time, noshing on breakfast and lunch during the week and brunch on weekends. The menu is laced with Greek items ranging from flavorful and tender octopus ceviche to house-made dolmades that display an added level of care. The farm to your table sandwich is layered with avocado, pickled green tomato, shaved jicama, sprouts and whipped feta. Of course, with a name that translates to bread, there must be baked goods and you'll find it all here. Don't skimp on dessert and order bougatsa, baklava or baklava coffee cake (an impressive marriage of the two).;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5786;Hometown Barbecue Miami;USA;Miami;1200 N.W. 22nd St., #100, Miami, 33142, USA;25.7976937;-80.2154214;27;true;false;Barbecue;From Austin, Texas to Brooklyn, New York, Pitmaster Bill Durney brings his signature barbecue to Magic City. Just like the original location, Durney has built this warehouse-chic space amidst a sea of industry in the Miami Produce Center, where trucks and moving pallets roam the streets. The sheer scale of the space—open kitchen on one side, a long bar on the other, tables in between and a patio just beyond—is something to behold.A hulking beef rib crusted with salt and black pepper, as well as melting, charred slices of brisket are essential orders that have few equals outside of Texas. Satisfying sides, like Frito pie, plancha broccoli and charred summer corn, round out the meal. The food here arrives almost as quickly as it’s ordered, so come hungry.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5787;Mandolin Aegean Bistro;USA;Miami;4312 N.E. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33137, USA;25.8158091;-80.1915611;27;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Turkish;Founded by Ahmet Erkaya and Anastasia Koutsioukis, this charming bistro welcomes diners with a blue door and whitewashed façade. The space features wood tables, lacquered chairs and an outdoor bar, although the focus is on its courtyard dining area, enhanced with mature trees, orchids and electric fans. This mezze-heavy menu may unveil a creamy slab of baked feta with diced tomato, smoked chili flakes and Turkish peppers. Slices of house-baked bread, stuffed into small brown paper bags, accompany the excellent small plates. Salads, a grilled catch-of-the-day sandwich and larger items, like moussaka, are equally beloved.A wedge of honey pie with a salted shortbread crust is highly recommended, and pairs delightfully with that Turkish coffee.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5788;DOYA;USA;Miami;347 N.W. 24th St., Miami, 33127, USA;25.7999753;-80.201337;16;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Greek;This Wynwood operation is particularly beloved, thanks to its lush patio. Inside, the room is vast, open, light-filled and designed with every type of diner in mind. Seats facing the open kitchen offer an intimate experience, while couples may prefer tables armed with powder-blue velvet chairs for a bit of romance.The cuisine bills itself as modern Aegean, and you will discover elements from Greece and Turkey’s coastal regions. Nibble on a refreshing fig salad with greens tossed in a hazelnut-pomegranate dressing before moving on to sea beans with garlic yogurt or some of the most delicate manti in this part of town. Flavors are both correct and comforting, but a scoop of raki ice cream will leave you supremely happy.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5789;Chug's Diner;USA;Miami;3444 Main Hwy., Miami, 33133, USA;25.7274358;-80.2432039;84;true;false;Cuban;What started out as a small café has grown overnight into this full-scale, Coconut Grove essential. All credit is due to Chef Michael Beltran who runs this terrific Cuban diner, fitted with dangling greenery and cozy booths. Truly, if this kitchen were a car, it would break the speed limit, as the team hurries about—opening early, closing late and cooking with panache.One could make a meal out of the oxtail ajiaco alone, a satisfying Colombian stew that cures all ills. But then you wouldn’t have room for the several towering sandwiches, served on fluffy Cuban bread. No meal is complete without at least one of their guava- and cream-cheese pastelitos. Their warm, flaky pastry alone will guarantee a return visit.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
5790;Phuc Yea;USA;Miami;7100 Biscayne Blvd., Miami, 33138, USA;25.8403537;-80.1844276;47;false;false;Vietnamese;There is nothing subtle about Chef Cesar Zapata and Ani Meinhold’s raucous Vietnamese mash-up in the MiMo district. A concrete compound wrapped in glowing red lanterns, the restaurant is practically a club with its sultry lighting, cavernous interior and full-time DJ. Yet, none of it gets in the way of the food, which is boldly seasoned and generously portioned. Stacks of crispy imperial rolls wrapped with mint and tangles of garlic-butter egg noodles aggressively charred on a wok are solid starting points. Everything is meant to be shared, especially the pho, which arrives in a cauldron packed with herbs, rice noodles and a meltingly tender slab of hickory-smoked short rib.All the while, a nearby table might launch into song. You are welcome to join the fun.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
5793;Zak The Baker;USA;Miami;295 N.W. 26th St., Miami, 33127, USA;25.801653;-80.200821;66;true;true;Bakery, American;This all-day operation is the brainchild of baker Zak Stern. He grew up in Miami, then apprenticed at a number of organic farms in Sweden, France and Israel before returning to his hometown to fulfill his culinary dreams. The crux of his menu is baked, as in breads and pastries, along with sandwiches, soups and salads. The "BLT" features salmon bacon, lettuce and tomato all stuffed into a deliciously flaky croissant. For something sweet, get the flourless dark chocolate cookie bursting with whole toasted almonds.This kosher bakery and café is located in hip Wynwood and welcomes diners with a color-splashed façade.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
5794;Isan Zaap;USA;Orlando;4693 Gardens Park Blvd., Ste 113, Orlando, 32839, USA;28.4946387;-81.4233487;18;false;true;Thai;Orlando's Thai restaurants typically dole out southern curry dishes and the ubiquitous pad Thai, but Isan Zaap strays from the pack with its gaze trained exclusively on northeast Thai cuisine with Laotian overlaps. There is an impressive level of attention to detail and a nice balance of spice and fermented flavors, and though impeccably executed curry makes an appearance, there's also an entire section dedicated to som tums that can be topped with fermented crab or fermented pork sausage. House specialties are a hit, as in the unique whole fish larb, cut into bite-sized pieces, tossed with toasted rice powder and fried to a crisp, and crowned with shaved red onion herbs tossed in a sweet yet spicy sauce. For dessert, dig in to durian sticky rice - if you dare.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5795;Rooster and the Till;USA;Tampa;6500 N. Florida Ave., Tampa, 33604, USA;28.0068343;-82.459512;38;true;true;International;It's a low-key spot with a contemporary feel. The bar is central and wraps around an open kitchen, so grab a seat at the counter for the best view. Between the lively tunes and buzzy staff, the aura is anything but stuffy. The plates follow suit—freewheeling, frequently changing and shareable with elements from SE Asia, Latin America and the Levant. Yet, nothing seems out of place, as in sumac-flecked cauliflower with whipped goat's milk feta and falafel-spiced dukkah. Fried cobia collar with nuoc cham boasts a cultish following. Such seductive textures and explosive flavors continue in full force in a dessert of black sesame ice cream with pineapple-cashew jam and Thai tea caramel.The tasting menu, though pricier, is a worthy splurge.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
5796;Tam Tam;USA;Miami;99 N.W. 1st St., Miami, 33128, USA;25.7751362;-80.195085;93;true;false;Vietnamese;Husband-and-husband team Tam Pham and Harrison Ramhofer are throwing a party on their own terms. On the edge of downtown by the county courthouse, you won’t find a glamorous room, a DJ booth, or anybody in stilettos or designer sneakers. There is no bouncer by the door. Instead, come as you are for this celebration of Vietnamese cooking that started out as a supper club. Much of the food doesn’t require silverware: Think wings glossed in fish sauce caramel, smoky lamb with lettuce wraps and banh hoi noodles, and tamarind-glazed pork ribs. Finish with a slice of cheesecake made with cultured cashew cream and topped with passionfruit gelee. Bold, funky, and fun, the restaurant is a good time all around, down to the hidden karaoke machine.;Air conditioning;[]
5797;Domu;USA;Orlando;3201 Corrine Dr., #100, Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5679469;-81.3433285;76;false;false;Ramen, Japanese;Enter Chef/owner Sean "Sonny" Nguyen's trendy ramen haven and you'll find two rooms dressed with concrete floors, a marble bar and wood panels set aglow by a starburst light fixture. The second room cradles the bulk of the crowd. As the name illustrates, this chef makes his culinary "dreams come true" by dint of a classic-meets-creative menu. Beyond the small plates lies the star item—ramen. Creations, like the Ritchie Rich and Curry, are full of bold, memorable flavors and certainly worth a slurp. Tokyo ramen with shoyu chicken broth, fried chicken thigh and duck fat is a sensory feat. Couple it with blistered shishitos for a delicious touch—and bit of crunch.It's all in the family here as sib Tori Tori flaunts a similarly creative izakaya menu.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace;[]
5798;Strand;USA;Orlando;807 N. Mills Ave., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5553237;-81.3643236;98;false;true;American, Contemporary;Husband-and-wife duo Alda and Joe Rees are behind this corner spot nestled within an Art Deco building. Its menu, displayed on the front windows, invites passersby inside to a space that may be short on real estate but utterly captivates with mint-green walls and Mason jars that hang above the glossy tiled bar.The seasonal American menu brims with nostalgic Southern inspiration, and presentations are dialed back to let ingredients shine. From local tomatoes to fresh citrus, dishes exude a homey sense. To wit: chilled shrimp is a wonderful contrast against hot fried green tomatoes, while cobia with mustard sauce and Carolina gold rice requires little augmentation. Close out with a citrus olive oil cake along with a sip from the worthy wine list.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5799;The Ravenous Pig;USA;Orlando;565 W. Fairbanks Ave., Orlando, 32789, USA;28.5932612;-81.3561373;100;false;false;Gastropub;This Winter Park modern gastropub came to be thanks to the vision of noted restaurateurs, James and Julie Petrakis. Housed right beside their eponymous brewery, the space exudes a moody, industrial vibe by way of charcoal hues, rustic wood accents and a gray ceiling marked by exposed ductwork. The open kitchen on the left has frosted glass panels that add a bit of mystery to the culinary proceedings.Chef Clay Miller's menu is a bona fide study of classic pub fare with creative Southern spins—to wit, ranchero sauce-dressed pork burnt ends over cornbread pudding or cured pastrami brisket with pickled cabbage purée and cauliflower giardiniera. The vegetable-forward melon, cucumber and farmer's cheese combo is in fact a rather complex denouement.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
5801;gastroteka bimendi;Japan;Osaka;1-5-9 Utsubohommachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0004, Japan;34.684567;135.497627;27;false;false;Spanish;This bar offers pinchos and tapas, or Spanish cuisine served on small plates. A casual place to enjoy Basque home cooking along with drinks from Spain. The Basque Country is rich with the blessings of mountains and sea, so the range of offerings covers a wide gamut. Each item is simple, the portions generous. Though a continent apart, Spain and Japan share a love of honest cooking in which natural flavours come to the fore.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5802;Akihana;Japan;Kyoto;27 Ichijoji Hinokuchicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8167, Japan;35.039594;135.792333;60;true;true;Chinese;To revisit the basics after studying creative Chinese cooking, the chef adds polish to a selection of Chinese regional cuisines. Sichuan items dominate, including steamed chicken with spicy sauce, twice-cooked pork and shrimp in chili sauce. The signature mapo tofu is a true original, made with wagyu beef sinew instead of ground meat. Faithful to his Shizuoka roots, he prepares his XO sauce fried rice with stardust shrimps and dried fish fry to create a mutual understanding between the cuisines of Kyoto and the Suruga region.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch;[]
5803;Ramen Touhichi;Japan;Kyoto;8-6 Yamabana Itchodacho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8007, Japan;35.050015;135.791384;72;false;true;Ramen;Ramen that’s all about the goodness of chicken, imparting its flavour in purest form. Ramen Touhichi’s signature soy-sauce ramen uses dashi made only with locally raised free-range chicken and water, mixing it with raw soy sauce kaeshi. Other offerings include richly flavoursome chicken boiled in plain water, cold noodles soaked in kombu dashi soup served with dipping sauce of chicken soy sauce, and chicken-oil noodles served without soup. ‘Touhichi’ is named after the house where the chef was born. See him at the counter full of pride in his native Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5805;Ramen Kuon;Japan;Osaka;B2F, Semba Centar Bldg Sangokan, 1-4-3 Sembachuo, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0055, Japan;34.681842;135.507331;55;true;false;Ramen;The chef takes pride in his “Shio Soba” (salt noodles), his quest for a bowl of perfection. Taste the seaweed—sea lettuce and nori—and you can feel the rustle of sea breezes. Triple soup of fish, shellfish and chicken is prepared using Pi-Water, a water that is said to be extremely similar to water in living tissue. High hydration ramen noodles, prepared with a blend of three types of wheat flour, produces a texture similar to noodles kneaded by hand. Three types of chashu are served as well, combining pork and chicken. Bringing out the best in soup, noodles and chashu for a triple treat.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5806;Osteria La Cicerchia;Japan;Osaka;3F, 2-3-4 Kyomachibori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0003, Japan;34.686375;135.492143;38;false;true;Italian;The ‘Marches cuisine specialty restaurant’ certificate from Italy proudly adorns the wall, and indeed the gastronomy of this region on Italy’s Adriatic coast is what the chef excels in. Meat-stuffed olive fritti, homemade salsiccia and rabbit-and-tomato stew are all staples of the Marchese dining board. Cicerchia beans are a classic legume grown in the town where the chef stayed. Their flavour can be tasted in her minestrone soup.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5807;Sobakiri Gaku;Japan;Osaka;7-1-54 Tanimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0012, Japan;34.673326;135.517979;24;false;true;Soba;It’s counter seating only in this modern interior accented with natural materials. The chef likes his soba to have a certain translucency, so he kneads it into ni-hachi, which contains 20% wheat flour. Soba is served cold on wicker baskets, not in soup, so patrons can appreciate the fragrance and firmness of the grain. ‘Kaeshi’, a mixture of soy sauce, sugar and mirin, is used to good effect in the rich dipping sauce, displaying the chef’s Kanto training. ‘Gaku’ means ‘mountain and sky’, signifying the chef’s commitment to attain ever higher goals.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5808;Ramen Hayato;Japan;Osaka;1-2-2 Minamimorimachi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0054, Japan;34.695592;135.510031;39;true;false;Ramen;This long-serving ramen shop is loved by Japanese people for its “Three Great Ramens”: soy-sauce, salt and miso. First-time visitors are recommended to order the soy-sauce ramen, but once you learn that the Hokkaido-born chef studied in Sapporo, you might be tempted to go for the miso ramen. The soy-sauce ramen is served in a double soup of meat-based stock and seafood-based stock. “Ura-Shoyu”, the ‘hidden soy-sauce ramen’ not listed on the menu, uses meat-based stock only. If you’re having trouble deciding, start with the ‘official’ menu.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5809;Sobakiri Karani;Japan;Osaka;2-11-26 Sagisu, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0002, Japan;34.69798;135.481965;26;true;false;Soba;Sobakiri Karani worked with a woodworking artist to create the interior using re-used wooden materials. Large tables with mismatched chairs and unique ceiling paintings express a whimsical spirit. The menu’s appetisers, including tofu pickled in unrefined sake and duck-and-onion miso, tempts one to a cup of sake. Soba is coarse-ground and cut into both thin and thick noodles, furnishing variety in finish and flavours. Enjoy soba the way you like it in a congenial atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5810;Berangkat;Japan;Kyoto;334 Maruyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8086, Japan;35.009672;135.766508;77;true;false;Izakaya;Berangkat means ‘beginnings’ in Indonesian, apt for a restaurant serving creative interpretations of cuisine the owner-chef studied in Southeast Asia. Consider, for example, shiraae dressed with coriander, pidan and Szechuan pickles, drizzled with homemade chilli oil. The grilled meat in cinnamon soy sauce borrows from the fare of the street stalls of Vietnam. The Okinawa cuisine, from the owner-chef’s experiences on Ishigakijima Island, is another of the restaurant’s fortes.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5811;Ishii Jr.;Japan;Osaka;2F, 3-11-4 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.695591;135.506074;29;true;true;Yakitori;Manning the grill at this yakitori shop, sister of Torisho Ishii, is the apprentice of Yoshitomo Ishii, the original shop’s owner-chef. Both the assembly of the skewers and the way they are grilled reflect Ishii’s tutelage, as does the practice of using chicken from different regions, primarily Kumamoto, Wakayama and Akita prefectures. The line-up ranges from perennial yakitori favourites to more unusual cuts such as chochin (chicken yolk sac) and chicken testes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
5813;Asperge Blanche;Japan;Kyoto;313-2 Yokosuwancho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8179, Japan;34.995569;135.759021;84;false;true;French;White is the keynote colour of the antiques-accented interior. The restaurant is decorated with sundries collected at flea markets, while a pendant light wreathes the establishment in its warm glow. The chef prepares traditional cuisine, arrangements stripped to the essentials so the flavours of the ingredients themselves shine clearly. Enamoured of Bincho charcoal, the chef even bakes his bread with it. The name of the restaurant means ‘white asparagus’—no need to ask what their spring speciality is…;Air conditioning;[]
5815;Sumiyakisosaitoriya Hitomi;Japan;Kyoto;96 Okikucho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8376, Japan;35.01341;135.77314;44;true;true;Yakitori;Sumiyakisosaitoriya Hitomi is full night after night and the delicious grilled chicken is only one reason for this success. The other is the character of the owner-chef. He stays in guests’ line of sight at all times as he assiduously works the Kishu-binchotan charcoal. He guides his service staff of students with fatherly kindness and makes guests feel like family. The restaurant offers baby chicken, local chicken and brand-name chicken, for their differences in taste and texture. Enjoy devotion and passion in every skewer.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5816;Tonkatsu Daiki;Japan;Osaka;1-6-2 Higashishinsaibashi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0083, Japan;34.672573;135.505253;18;false;true;Tonkatsu;‘Daiki’ was the full name when the owner-chef’s parents ran it as a teishoku restaurant. The second-generation owner-chef switched to specialising in tonkatsu. Pork from Kagoshima is deep-fried in salad oil to provide the batter with just the right crispness. His experience in Chinese cooking comes to the fore in the piquantly spiced mustard sauce He pays special attention to the rice, too, cooking it in small batches.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5817;BOCCA del VINO;Japan;Kyoto;138-9 Saitocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8012, Japan;35.001869;135.770015;24;true;true;Italian;The quirky name, ‘mouth of wine’, reflects the chef’s fond memories of Italy, where jugs of wine graced every dinner table. The chef studied in the southern Italy, so recipes are simple, prepared with lashings of tomatoes and olive oil. Seafood features prominently in appetisers, meat and poultry in main dishes, based on the chef’s experiences. Pasta is dressed with the familiar oil, tomatoes and ragu. Comfort food that brings to mind daily life in Italy.;Air conditioning;[]
5818;au soleil couchant;Japan;Osaka;1-14-25 Shitennoji, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0051, Japan;34.654418;135.514186;61;false;false;French;The French tricolour flies over the district of Yuhigaoka. ‘Au soleil couchant’ means ‘at the setting sun’, a homage to this couple’s apprenticeship in Lyon and to Yuhigaoka, which means ‘hill of the setting sun’. The chef as culinary artisan commands the kitchen, while his pâtissière wife serves customers. As in any good bistro, portions are generous. Pleasingly, vegetables are used in abundance. Respect for tradition and true French spirit permeate the establishment.;Air conditioning;[]
5819;Az;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 4-4-8 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697477;135.504684;25;true;true;Chinese;Billing itself as a ‘Chinese bistro’, Az serves Chinese fare with wine from an assortment of countries. The menu is resplendent with local colour. If stir-fry of wagyu beef is for you, you can choose your sauce from among Guangdong-style oyster sauce, Sichuan-style yúxiāng and Beijing-style miso. Pairing sweet, sour and spicy flavours with a suitable wine provides an added dimension of fun. At lunch, under the name Bifun Azuma, the restaurant serves fried rice vermicelli (‘bifun’ in Japanese) and Chinese zongzi.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
5820;Soba Rojina;Japan;Kyoto;691 Maruyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0917, Japan;35.014999;135.766879;32;false;true;Soba;To convey the unique character of the soba, the owner-chef prepares juwari with no wheat flour. He made the stone mortar he uses to grind the flour himself, back when he was an apprentice. The entire shop reverberates with the sound of buckwheat being ground slowly so as to retain the fragrance. In addition to soba, Rojina offers items that pair well with alcohol. Tofu with yuba on top and manganji togarashi with jako are two typical Kyoto appetisers served before the soba.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5821;Udondokoro Shigemi;Japan;Osaka;4-7-7 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696732;135.503817;34;true;true;Udon;The chef’s top recommendation is the ‘hiyakake’: nothing but udon noodles in a golden-yellow broth. The dashi is Kansai-style, made with makombu seaweed for umami and finely chopped round herring and mackerel for flavour. Noodles are prepared with techniques learned in Kagawa. The cool broth brings out the supple body and elasticity of the noodles, showing how the goodness of each supports the other. The donburi bowl here brings together the udon cultures of Osaka and Kagawa.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5822;Soba Takama;Japan;Osaka;7-12-14 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0041, Japan;34.714117;135.511103;47;false;true;Soba;‘Mori soba’ means ‘soba piled high’, and it is. Soba is served on seiro (bamboo or wicker baskets) because in the days of the Tokugawa shoguns it was common to steam the noodles. Piling soba into a mountain is another practice rooted in history. Made from buckwheat grains stripped of their black husks, this mori soba has a delicious finish. Inaka soba, made from husked whole buckwheat grains, is gloriously fragrant. Dipping sauce brightened with kombu kelp reflects the dashi stock culture of the Kansai region. We love the generous portions—one plate fully satisfies.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5823;Gombei;Japan;Kyoto;254 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.004141;135.774308;46;true;false;Soba;Fans of Gombei think immediately of udon or soba with kitsune (deep-fried tofu), but certainly not with tanuki (deep-fried tempura pieces). The menu begins with udon, showing how popular it is. Two types of kitsune are available, one with chopped tofu, the other with tofu simmered in sweetened soy sauce. ‘Keiran’ is a warm udon dish topped with a starch sauce of soft scrambled eggs and ginger. Noodles are boiled soft to soak up the dashi. A taste of Kyoto, beloved of kabuki actors, geisha and maiko.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5824;Gion Yorozuya;Japan;Kyoto;555-1 Komatsucho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0811, Japan;35.002752;135.773987;92;true;false;Udon;When Gion Yorozuya was founded, its focus was on meal deliveries to teahouses and playhouses. The restaurant thrived thanks to a favourable reception from geisha and maiko, and today guests queue up at the door well before opening time. The dish of renown is the onion udon. Eager to use Kyoto foodstuffs, the chef smothers his plates in Kujo spring onion. The three pillars of the cuisine that keeps customers coming back are tender noodles, dashi and onions. “Mari”, a dish larded with pickled plums, and “Tsunoda”, enhanced with chicken meat, are named for the celebrities who favour these ingredients.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5825;Hiiragitei;Japan;Kyoto;306-6 Ishibashicho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0066, Japan;35.00666;135.777905;57;true;false;Yakitori;It’s a family affair at this restaurant specialising in locally raised chicken and obanzai: the father prepares the à la carte dishes, the son the yakitori, and the mother attends to customers’ needs. Every morning the son visits a poultry farm in Shiga Prefecture to purchase and dress whole chickens by himself. The speciality of the house is the white liver, a rare part of the chicken, and back liver complemented with the bitter flavour of cacao nibs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5827;Benikurage;Japan;Osaka;5-4 Hommachibashi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0029, Japan;34.682967;135.510223;16;false;true;Izakaya;The owner-chef and his wife tour sake breweries throughout Japan to select their favourites. Not surprisingly, the cuisine is oriented towards how it pairs with sake. The fish for sashimi is aged to enhance flavour. Clear broth soup is a constant companion, as they believe in the match between sake and kombu kelp. Sagohachi pickled lamb is flavoured with rice malt, pairing nicely with sake. The name means ‘immortal jellyfish’, after a creature whose cells regenerate so it never gets old. Similarly, the couple’s passion for cuisine and sake never fades.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
5829;HUNTER;Japan;Kyoto;533-2 Tsuboyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0814, Japan;35.014704;135.760943;65;false;false;French;Chef Imai is as obsessed with meat as a hunter stalking his game. Putting his experience with French cuisine to work, he grills his meat-centric menu on a charcoal grill. In addition to duck, pork and beef, in autumn and winter Imai serves game meats such as boar and deer. Charcuterie such as pâté and rillettes are arranged on plates that look like stumps for a natural look. If you sit at the counter, you’ll have the pleasure of chatting with this personable chef.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5831;Oito;Japan;Kyoto;253 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.004085;135.774304;17;true;false;Oden;The building, in the style of a townhouse, stands on Kiritoshi Alley in Gion. Portraits of maiko adorn the walls, reinforcing the geisha-district ambience. ‘Lunch Oden’ is the only item on the menu. The owner-chef is mindful of retaining familiar and comforting flavours. Lunch consists of five items of the diner’s choice, accompanied by takikomi-gohan. The choice of oden is up to the customer, but if you choose the popular beef tendon, we recommend pairing it with the tofu or konnyaku.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5832;KORISU;Japan;Kyoto;101 Rokurocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0813, Japan;34.997683;135.77426;51;true;false;Yoshoku;A mother and two daughters, in their pure-white smocks, make guests feel at home with their family hospitality. French and other Western dishes are served with generous portions, bringing satisfaction that keeps the restaurant’s reputation strong. Hamburger steak and fried shrimp are flavours from the good old days. Escargot and lamb pair well with wine. With only three tables, and the phone often unanswered, getting a reservation can be a bit of a scramble.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5833;Bistro des Chenapans;Japan;Osaka;2-14-1 Kyomachibori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0003, Japan;34.684861;135.490588;21;true;false;French;The chef of this bistro takes pride in his meat cuisine, having studied meat processing in Paris. Casual prix fixe menus of hamburger steak and the like are popular at lunchtime. In the evening, guests can dine à la carte from the charcuterie, cassoulet and so forth. In a bow to the chef’s roots in Shiga Prefecture, Omi beef is used in the steak and fries. Meat is drizzled in oil as it grills to bring out its aroma, and seasoned simply with salt and pepper.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
5834;Hommachi Seimenjo Chukasobakobo;Japan;Osaka;B2F, Semba Centar Bldg Nigokan, 1-3-2 Sembachuo, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0055, Japan;34.681724;135.508132;85;true;true;Ramen;When you visit this ramen shop launched by a dried foods wholesaler, take note of the soup, which epitomises the brilliance of the dashi soup stock. Its well-rounded fragrance derives from multiple types of dried fish flakes. Kombu kelp, pike conger and chicken bones each add layers of flavour, creating body and finish. Heightening the taste are two types of noodles made on the premises: flat noodles to soak up the soup, round ones for their texture.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5835;Shokudo Akari;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-6-27 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697549;135.499252;21;true;true;Izakaya;Akari shines out of a detached house in the entertainment district. The nest of criss-crossing wooden poles hung from the ceiling represent the handheld pine torches of the Oto Fire Festival in Wakayama, as well as the flame of the chef’s passion for cooking. Expect everything from familiar favourites such as gingered chicken liver, potato salad and deep-fried horse mackerel, to seasonal flavours. Naturally, this true son of Wakayama takes pride in grilling with Kishu Bincho charcoal. Every February 6, the chef returns to his native prefecture to take part in the Fire Festival.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5836;Ayamedo;Japan;Osaka;2-2-26 Andojimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0061, Japan;34.676438;135.51606;56;true;true;Soba;The building used to be a merchant house and now sports a Showa-era vibe. Side dishes such as tofu preserved in miso, buckwheat dumplings and bowls of duck meat fill the menu to accompany drinks. Not a few guests can be seen tipping a cup or two from noon onwards in the retro atmosphere. The soba noodles are generously piled high like a mountain on a wicker draining basket, dazzling the eyes, and each noodle, with its sharp, angular shape, offers a firm yet smooth texture.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5837;Sobashubo Ichii;Japan;Kyoto;62 Hirano Miyanishicho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8357, Japan;35.034336;135.731701;39;false;false;Soba;The marquee dishes here are hand-made soba and duck preparations. Seiro makes sparing use of filler to bring out the suppleness and flavour of the noodles. Osaka Kawachi ducks are used, a good fit for the dipping sauce thanks to their tender flesh and sweet fat. When you savour the kamo nanban or duck seiro, you can taste the affinity between soba and duck. In the evening, imaginative duck creations are on offer, not to mention soba sushi of chicken breast and daikon radish, or Japanese ajillo of gizzard and mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5838;il luogo di TAKEUCHI;Japan;Osaka;5-1-26 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.696969;135.490051;32;true;false;Italian;This is the main branch of Takeuchi, which operates a number of casual Italian trattorias. The owner-chef holds court in the kitchen, directing his cooking staff. At noontime a simple pasta lunch is served, but a full range of à la carte dishes are offered in the evening. The range of pastas is impressive, and the eatery does not skimp on tomato and cream sauces. The aroma of fish and wagyu grilling over charcoal is also compelling.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
5839;Menya Inoichi;Japan;Kyoto;542 Ebisunocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8033, Japan;35.001342;135.766965;27;true;false;Ramen;From the front of the restaurant comes the tempting aroma of dashi, inviting the diner in. True to their Kyoto roots, they pursue a ramen richly suffused with the flavour of dashi. The broth is from Rausu kombu, a type of kelp rich in umami, and several types of dried seafood. The feature dish is ‘Dashi Soba’. The ramen is served in two varieties: the lightly seasoned ‘white’ and the full-bodied ‘black.’ Freshly shaved katsuo-bushi brings out the umami still further.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5840;Taiho;Japan;Kyoto;149 Nishinokyo Hoshigaikecho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8416, Japan;35.01224;135.740464;18;true;false;Chinese;This Chinese restaurant is run by a family, who all support each other. The father’s offerings, which have pleased the locals for generations, sit side-by-side with authentic Szechuan cuisine from the son’s gastronomic studies. One dish for which Taiho has been renowned since its opening is the ‘Teridon Kinshi’. This quintessentially Kyoto dish consists of rice topped with pork and kinshi tamago (ribbons of omelette). Also recommended is the ‘Yodaredori’, steamed chicken with a spicy sauce.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
5841;Muromachi Kaji;Japan;Kyoto;185 Nakanonocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8435, Japan;34.998821;135.757784;82;false;false;Izakaya;This kappo izakaya heaves with customers night after night. Sashimi combinations are arranged as for kaiseki traditional multi-course meals. The inclusion of chub mackerel sushi is gratifying. Potatoes are paired with delicacies to conjure a potato salad for grownups that goes well with sake. Plovers emblazoned on the shop curtain and towels are for good luck, representing the overcoming of rough seas. The staff work as a tight-knit crew to surmount the waves of orders the shop’s popularity brings them.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5845;Bistro Yanagihara;Japan;Kyoto;358 Shimizucho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0911, Japan;35.01365;135.7688;58;false;false;French;A bistro by a chef who apprenticed in Alsace. For appetisers, he showcases his skills with choucroute of salt-pickled fermented cabbage, confit of foie gras and charcuterie of ham and sausages. His main dishes are prepared with no less care: items such as beef simmered in red wine and pâté grilled in a pastry shell have their flavours drawn out over time. Hearty portions ensure a full stomach.;Air conditioning;[]
5846;Chukasoba Mugen;Japan;Osaka;5-5-10 Ebie, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0001, Japan;34.696615;135.472155;53;true;true;Ramen;While eating ramen, salt water from the noodles gradually dilutes the soup. You can experience this for yourself. First, pour a little of the soup into a separate bowl. Finish the noodles in the original bowl, then try sipping the reserved soup—the difference in taste will amaze you. The harmony created by a bowl of ramen goes beyond taste. The slurping of noodles forms a duet with the classical music in the background. The joy of ramen knows no bounds: ‘mugen’.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5847;Sobakiri Arabompu;Japan;Osaka;4-1-11 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696363;135.505318;28;true;true;Soba;‘Arabompu’ was a favourite word of Edo-era haiku poet Kobayashi Issa. It means ‘living a free and ordinary life’. For the chef here, it means approaching his subjects, buckwheat and soba, from a natural stance. To watch his series of tasks—parboiling, washing, then plating the soba noodles—there’s no substitute for a seat at the counter. The ‘Soba Zanmai’ set offers three types of soba—nihachi, juwari, and arabiki—served as half bowls of each for tasting. Kanto-style dipping sauce recalls the days of the chef’s apprenticeship.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5849;Naniwa Okina;Japan;Osaka;4-1-18 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.69622;135.505954;71;true;false;Soba;The third-generation owner-chef decided to switch from machine-rolled to hand-rolled soba, so he learned the technique from a master. After thoroughly straining the soba, but without over-cooling it, he cuts the noodles neither thin nor thick, but just right. Dipping sauce is medium-salty to bring out the aroma of the buckwheat seeds, and the dish is arranged beautifully. A full range of snacks are on offer. We hope Japan will always have soba shops like this one.;Air conditioning;[]
5850;Kanesho;Japan;Kyoto;155-2 Tokiwacho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0079, Japan;35.004549;135.772976;95;false;false;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;The shop was founded at the end of the Edo period as a wholesaler of river fish. Situated at the end of an alley as long and narrow as an eel’s bed, Kanesho is recognisable by the leaping eel emblazoned on its noren. ‘Kinshi-don’, the brainchild of the fourth-generation chef, is renowned. This popular dish incorporates ‘kinshitamago’, omelette cut into thin strips, an essential component of Kyoto favourites such as chirashizushi and steamed sushi. ‘Ochazuke Eel’ is eel simmered in dipping sauce and drenched in green tea, a refreshing flavour. A place where one hopes to gain the vitality of the leaping eel.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5851;Shigetsu;Japan;Kyoto;68 Sagatenryuji Susukinobabacho, Ukyo-ku, Kyoto, 616-8385, Japan;35.015281;135.673591;41;false;true;Shojin;Shojin ryori is a vegetarian cuisine in the Buddhist monastic tradition. It is a part of Buddhist ascetic practice, said to cleanse the soul, suppress worldly desires and promote spiritual growth. It is said that pouring one’s heart into one’s cooking is the secret to true shojin ryori and an act that expresses gratitude for all people. Shojin ryori is a quest not for physical results but for an inner spiritual calm. A guide on the path of life.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed;[]
5854;tanpopo;Japan;Osaka;6F, 1-10-16 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.698073;135.497688;19;false;true;Teppanyaki, Okonomiyaki;The chef has continually upped his culinary game through a quarter-century of self-instruction, hopping from restaurant to restaurant to sharpen his instincts. The result is his cooking with iron and copper plates. Fluffy omelettes and deep-fried knots of fish paste are grilled on copper, pungent stir-fried noodles and beef steaks on iron. Tonpeiyaki (cabbage and pork wrapped in an omelette) is braced with sage for a hint of Italian. Rum is added to crêpes in the French style. Imagination and passion are cooked into every dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5856;Kyogoku Kaneyo;Japan;Kyoto;456 Matsugaecho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8034, Japan;35.007634;135.767929;60;false;true;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;This eel restaurant has been in business for seven generations, dating back to the Meiji period. Every day finds the shop crowded with customers, many seeking its signature dish of ‘Kinshi Don’: rice covered in dipping sauce and topped with Edo-style eel and a large Kyoto-style omelette. What makes this east-west marriage of flavours work so well is the dipping sauce, a staple since the restaurant’s inception. The Kanto-style kabayaki, which involves steaming eel before grilling and dipping it in sauce, is a technique from a cook recruited from Tokyo during the founder’s generation. In both looks and taste, Kyogoku Kaneyo bears traces of Japan’s east and west.;Air conditioning;[]
5857;Yoshokuya Fujiya;Japan;Osaka;2-2-1 Yariyamachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0027, Japan;34.68263;135.513074;51;false;false;Yoshoku;The first-generation owner-chef opened this restaurant in 1935 next to his rice dealership. For four generations, this local eatery has filled the bellies of its regular customers, many of whom have been dining here for years. The hamburger patties with demi-glace sauce are a perennial favourite. The lunchtime set meals that can be enjoyed casually are a welcome idea. Miso soup and pickled vegetables play supporting roles as beloved comfort food. Good, sound cooking on which the locals were raised.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
5858;Eitaroya;Japan;Kyoto;448 Tatsunoikecho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8176, Japan;35.011075;135.758517;92;true;true;Izakaya;Seafood rushed straight from the fisheries and vegetables grown by local farmers are what sell this izakaya. The white-smocked chef stands at the counter, showing confidence in his daily-changing menu. Choose how you want your seafood prepared: stewed, salt-grilled, deep-fried as tempura, and more. The sashimi plate is popular for its variety and generous portions. Sashimi is served atop a big bowl of ice, keeping the fish cool in summer and firm in winter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5859;Sushidokoro Kaihara;Japan;Osaka;5-4 Ikedacho, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0033, Japan;34.706578;135.51217;47;false;true;Sushi;Omakase from a veteran of Japanese cuisine. The meal begins with grated vegetables and appetizers. Nigiri emphasises the toppings, with fish cut thick and sushi rice more modest in quantity. Smaller sushi pieces enable guests to sample a variety of fish to their hearts’ content. An ingenious twist is that the soy sauce varies by topping: shrimp is served with egg yolk steeped in soy sauce, fatty tuna with foamy soy sauce, and so on. This self-taught sushi artisan never stops learning and rewarding guests with the results of his labours.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5860;Hachidori;Japan;Osaka;1-20-2 Miyakojimakitadori, Miyakojima-ku, Osaka, 534-0014, Japan;34.711264;135.529216;36;true;true;Izakaya;Food that pairs well with drinks and the ‘Steam-Warmed Sake’ are popular items at this izakaya. The cheerful couple who run it hail from a line of liquor-store owners. The bill of fare includes sashimi and charcoal-grilled items, with the emphasis on the quality of the ingredients, as well as dishes of Shōnai vegetables the chef procures from the production areas. The type of salt used varies, with some items seasoned with ishiru fish sauce for a twist that makes for a pleasant aftertaste.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
5861;Kushi Tanaka;Japan;Kyoto;310-10 Uradeyamacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8155, Japan;35.004523;135.758838;48;true;true;Kushiage;A tight C-shaped counter surrounds the owner-chef. Imaginatively prepared skewers appear in rapid succession and the variety is extraordinary: mushrooms with soy butter, steamed wheat gluten with yuzu miso, bread filled with cream cheese. The prix fixe offering is called ‘Ippo Tsuko’, meaning ‘one way’, as skewers are placed in front of guests with no consultation. The owner-chef never forgets to show modesty and humour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
5862;Suigyo Murabayashi;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 1-2-17 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.69679;135.498827;19;false;true;Izakaya;Since his apprentice days, the chef has made a habit of touring Japan to build trust with fishermen. The blessing that flows from that effort is the high-quality seafood delivered to him from each region. The first dish offered is sashimi in a large bowl. Fish of the season arrives little by little, in wondrous variety, as the sake flows nicely. Fish stew is prepared in soy sauce and water only, bringing out the natural sweetness of the flesh. The remaining broth is served with fresh-cooked rice, wasting nothing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5863;AKA to SHIRO;Japan;Osaka;3F, 1-1-41 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.696742;135.500532;28;true;true;Sushi;The chef uses two types of vinegared rice: red-vinegared rice for tuna and blue-backed fish, and white-vinegared rice for shrimp and white-fleshed fish. The red vinegar is a style popular in the Kanto region, while the ‘white’ vinegar (rice vinegar with sugar) is a Kansai speciality with strong roots in oshizushi. The combination of red and white, east and west, creates a dialogue between variations, respecting the spirit of each. Aka to Shiro also means ‘red and white’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5864;Izuu;Japan;Kyoto;367 Kiyomotocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0084, Japan;35.004851;135.774488;84;true;false;Sushi;Founded in 1781, Izuu takes its name from its founder, Izumiya Uhee, from a time when lightly salted mackerel from Wakasa was becoming popular in Kyoto, and the custom of eating sabazushi at festivals and ceremonies became common. Seeing an opportunity, Uhee began delivering these treats to the city’s geisha districts. The business passed from generation to generation, and the current, eighth generation owner-chef preserves the tradition of whole-mackerel sushi to this day.;Air conditioning;[]
5865;DELI a Casa;Japan;Osaka;1-2-5 Kawarayamachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0066, Japan;34.672875;135.513943;34;true;false;Italian;The daily fare and hometown cooking of Italy mould the concept here, following the owner-chef’s passion to get people to know the cuisine he grew to love in that country. A beguiling array of appetisers are served on small dishes, after the style of a mix-and-match antipasto misto. Enjoy them bit by bit, like a tour of the regions of Italy. Simple dishes, lovingly prepared, reach deep into the soul.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5866;The New World;Japan;Osaka;B2F, Shinsaibashi PARCO, 1-8-3 Shinsaibashisuji, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0085, Japan;34.673859;135.500978;54;false;false;Izakaya;Its space glittering with pink neon signs and mirror balls, creates a whole new world for izakaya. In similar vein, the cuisine is genre-free: many imaginative offerings break free from the confines of Japanese gastronomy. Examples include a salad of canned mackerel and shiraae of fresh fruit in season with mascarpone. The whole restaurant abounds with originality, as the chef’s playful spirit puts smiles on patrons’ faces.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
5867;Sushitsune;Japan;Osaka;2-4-3 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0041, Japan;34.696659;135.512094;99;false;false;Sushi;The dish of renown here is the bateira, or pressed mackerel sushi, conceived by Sushitsune’s first-generation owner. The fourth-generation chef continues this tradition, now popular throughout Osaka, in which pickled mackerel is pressed onto sushi rice in a boat-shaped wooden frame and dressed with white-sheet kombu. With deft handling, skilfully applying just the right force to unravel the sushi rice, the chef displays the fine skill of long practice. Bozushi, of horse mackerel and conger eel, and temarizushi are exemplars of Osaka food culture. This is the place to sample true Naniwa oshizushi, beloved by ‘Japan’s Kitchen’ of Osaka.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5868;Saketosakana DNA;Japan;Kyoto;559-1 Torocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8401, Japan;35.000113;135.760822;39;false;false;Izakaya;‘DNA’ was appended to the name to evoke the richness of Japanese cuisine and the spirit of Japan as defining features of the restaurant. There’s a reason why the soup using kombu kelp and bonito dashi stock takes pride of place. Fish is shipped directly from Obama, Fukui Prefecture, so there’s a good selection of sake from Fukui, too. Foodstuffs and sake from the same locale tend to get on well together—there’s that DNA again. The warmth of the three family members is a genetic inheritance from father to son and daughter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5869;Tonkatsu Fujii;Japan;Osaka;1-11-5 Sembayashi, Asahi-ku, Osaka, 535-0012, Japan;34.723772;135.554236;65;true;false;Tonkatsu;The chef came over from the world of French cuisine to fry tonkatsu. Ingredients and cooking techniques are a complex mix of various elements, creating flavours found nowhere else. Wielding a blend of multiple oils, the chef lends his skills as a baker to the coating. Red wine accentuates the sauce. Experience inspires the ideas of this chef, who was indelibly impressed by the tonkatsu craftsmen of Tokyo. A chance meeting that changed a life, resulting in beautiful flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5870;Tonkatsu KATSU Hana;Japan;Osaka;2-2-11 Kitakyuhojimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0057, Japan;34.679901;135.506154;96;true;false;Tonkatsu;Only name-brand pork from various regions is used so patrons can learn what truly delicious pork tastes like. The chef is always on the lookout for new pork brands, allowing diners to sample different flavours in tonkatsu every time they visit. If undecided between the tenderloin and the pork loin, the combination platter is the way to go. The restaurant is named ‘Hana’ because that is the name of the chef’s wife. Their warm and affable personalities add to the appeal, heightening satisfaction with the fare.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5871;DEUX FILLES;Japan;Kyoto;199-2 Ayazaimokucho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8072, Japan;35.002555;135.763218;27;true;true;French;Owner-chef Daisuke Iwata bills his fare as ‘modern French’. His purpose in using generous portions of vegetables is to showcase the bounty of Kyoto. The salad with 30 kinds of vegetables is a perennial favourite. Selecting a white plate as a canvas, he colours it in with vegetables he buys himself in places such as Kameoka and Kamigamo. His skill in déclinaison – taking a single ingredient and turning it into sauté, sauce and powder, then serving it as a single dish – is unique.;Air conditioning;[]
5872;Kikunoi Mugesambo;Japan;Kyoto;524 Washiocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0072, Japan;35.001823;135.781546;20;true;true;Japanese;The menu of tea ceremony food conveys the flavours of Kikunoi with the culture of bento. Starting with appetisers, stewed bowls are served ryotei-style. Serving-ware—baskets, lacquer, glasses—changes with the passing seasons, laden with a colourful variety of grilled items and simmered vegetables. The house speciality, Shiguremeshi, is topped with sea bream sashimi smothered in sesame sauce. As you dine, cast your gaze over the stillness of the moss-covered garden.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5873;Vegan Ramen UZU;Japan;Kyoto;146 Umenokicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0905, Japan;35.014672;135.76802;31;true;true;Ramen;‘Earth-friendly dining’ is the mission of Vegan Ramen UZU. The interior artwork, created by art collective teamLab based on their theme of ‘Interconnection between humans and nature and each other’, is a perfect fit for the cuisine. Digital art that reverses left and right on the black tables, and India-ink writing on the walls, speak of harmony between nature and food, and the beauty of all creation. Guests all dine at the same table, underscoring the message that we must live and prosper together.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5874;Sobadokoro Toki;Japan;Osaka;1-3-4 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.696284;135.498115;74;false;true;Soba;Over the front door of this shop in Kitashinchi hangs a shimenawa, a twisted straw rope that wards off evil. Inscribed on a wooden block over the shimenawa is the phrase ‘Senkyaku Banrai’: ‘May customers arrive in the thousands and tens of thousands!’ In hopes the wish will come true, the doors are kept open until late at night. The sprawling menu ranges from appetizers that accompany sake to seasonal soba dishes. At lunchtime, soba accompanied by sushi is a nice surprise. In summer, chilled curry soba is brightly festooned with veggies. In winter, oyster soba in white miso soup warms the body from the inside. The special preparations for each season give something extra to look forward to.;Air conditioning;[]
5877;Mendokoro Janomeya;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 565-23 Nakanocho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8042, Japan;35.004149;135.767897;88;true;true;Ramen;This ramen shop focuses on making soup using locally raised chickens. Its three signature flavours are soy sauce, salt and white broth. Be sure to try the chicken ramen. To make the signature soup, dashi is drawn from chicken bones and whole chickens. Following a time-honoured recipe, flavours are enhanced with soy sauce matured in large wooden barrels. The fragrance of the wheat is drawn out by using thin noodles. The ambience is reminiscent of the aristocratic culture of old Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5879;Nihonshuzammai Utsutsuyo;Japan;Osaka;2F, 3-2-1 Hommachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0053, Japan;34.683176;135.502596;90;true;false;Izakaya;The name of the restaurant is inspired by the expression ‘is this a dream or reality?” and embodies the desire for you to enjoy sake and good food to your heart’s content with a touch of enchantment. The sheer range of local sakes on offer can make choosing hard. Start with an appetiser and decoratively arranged sashimi with your first cup. The drinking snacks are varied too, from tofu preserved in miso and stew of beef tendon to Western items such as sweetfish confit and milt meunière. With such an array of appetisers, the sake slips down easily.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Shoes must be removed;[]
5880;Donostia;Japan;Osaka;1F, Daibiruhonkan, 3-6-32 Nakanoshima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0005, Japan;34.693432;135.493018;30;false;true;Spanish;Donostia is the Basque name for Spain’s gourmet capital of San Sebastián. Pinchos and tortillas line the glass case on the counter, reinforcing the informal vibe of a Spanish tapas bar. Dry-cured ham, marinated sardines, squid frit and other delights are served a little at a time on small dishes. Seafood salsa verde redolent with herbs and bean-and-giblet stew are standard fare. Taste country cooking rich with the distinctiveness of the Basque countryside.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5881;Oribe;Japan;Osaka;1-6-18 Shimmachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0013, Japan;34.676293;135.496178;16;true;true;Teppanyaki, Okonomiyaki;French bistro and teppanyaki cooking are the draw at Oribe. The impressive range of appetisers includes items inspired by French standards such as paté and smoked salmon. Its famous cabbage steak was dreamed up from the essential ingredients of okonomiyaki. Speaking of okonomiyaki, the meal ends with Osaka’s famous savoury pancake, a popular item here. The restaurant was named for the chef’s penchant for Oribe ware, and this style of pottery inspires the green theme for its décor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5882;Bistro Cerisier;Japan;Kyoto;1-3 Tanaka Shimoyanagicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8204, Japan;35.02976;135.774453;52;true;true;French;French ballads warble through a retro interior, recalling the good old days. Regional cuisines such as quenelles from Lyon and cassoulet from Languedoc spill across the menu. Old-school recipes, like white asparagus with Hollandaise sauce in spring and salmis of roast mallard, bring comfort to the soul. Respect for sauces testifies to the commitment to the essence of French cooking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5883;Fuyacho 103;Japan;Kyoto;225 Owaricho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0934, Japan;35.012859;135.765988;57;false;false;Oden;The name is simply the address of this restaurant hidden in a mixed-use complex. Cross the threshold and the interior is filled with the warmth of wood panelling, the coffered ceiling reminiscent of the partitions in an oden pot. The menu ranges from standard fare such as daikon radish and deep-fried tofu to more exotic choices only a former Italian cuisine chef could conjure, such as caciocavallo cheese. Taking a hint from bistecca, the steak is paired with oden dashi soup stock.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5884;Kamigata Rainbow;Japan;Osaka;4-6-3 Katsuyama, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0043, Japan;34.654784;135.52591;99;true;false;Ramen;A rainbow-coloured awning marks Kamigata Rainbow, a shop that pursues individuality even in ramen. The type of noodle differs for each type of ramen, creating unity in each. Soy sauce is redolent with lashings of small, dried sardines. In the curry ramen, curry paste floating in the soup changes delightfully as it melts. The menu includes items limited to each season, tickling one’s curiosity.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5885;Juu-go;Japan;Kyoto;71-6 Jodoji Kamiminamidacho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8405, Japan;35.025573;135.795684;23;true;true;Soba;Akiya Ishibashi tills the field, harvests the grain, kneads the buckwheat. The chef’s passion for soba permeates a menu consisting purely of soba and soba mash. ‘Think of it as cereal’, he says of his dishes rich in rustic goodness. Soba is deliciously fragrant, thick-cut and al dente. Soba mash, served with roasted buckwheat grains, is delightfully pungent. To enjoy the pure flavour of Ishibashi’s soba, try it first on its own, without seasoning.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5887;Canton Shunsai Ikki;Japan;Kyoto;17-5 Tsukimicho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0829, Japan;35.0009;135.777969;37;false;true;Chinese;The restaurant holds its own niche in Chinese cuisine. The talents of the Guangdong-trained chef are on full display. Guangdong is blessed with the bounty of sea, mountain and river, as is Kyoto, and the light flavour of its cuisine, which draws out the flavour of the ingredients, work well with the food culture of the ancient capital. Shrimp wontons are dressed with Hong Kong soy sauce, Cantonese fried rice is accented with lettuce and roast pork.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5888;Izakaya Tokitame;Japan;Osaka;6-9-17 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.699957;135.487931;30;true;true;Izakaya;Before anything else, be sure to order the Obanzai Moriawase. The simple flavouring of this assortment of Kyoto cuisine side-dishes, such as shira-ae and vinegared burdock, makes a great companion for drinks. The line-up ranges from familiar offerings such as decorative sashimi and fried foods to Japanese, Western and Chinese dishes accented with a touch of creativity. The restaurant name derives from a movie about a couple who grew old together. The couple who manage Izakaya Tokitame also gather beautiful moments with their guests as time marches on.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5889;EL ALMA;Japan;Osaka;8-19-12 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.698255;135.483463;89;true;true;Spanish;El Alma feels like a culinary journey, as the dishes hail from every region of Spain. The shrimp-and-mushroom ajillo represents the traditional flavours of southern Spain. Salted cod and almond sauce lend the tapas salad a Catalan flair. The meat dishes are charcoal-grilled for a smoky flavour that evokes the Basque Country. The chef, who’s made numerous trips to Spain, aims for an authentic feel that conveys the richness of regional Spanish cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5890;Sumibiyakitori Ikoka;Japan;Osaka;3-3-3 Otedori, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0021, Japan;34.686151;135.510133;42;false;false;Yakitori;Sumibiyakitori Ikoka would like you to experience as many different cuts of chicken as possible, so a recommended start to your order is a five- or seven-piece omakase. Rather than insist on a particular brand, the owner-chef chooses poultry on quality and freshness alone. Chicken tail drizzled in yuzu and chicken skin covered in oroshi ponzu are a finishing touch. Chicken pieces prepared with slight twists are mixed together to offer a variety of flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5891;Muginoyoake;Japan;Kyoto;12-5 Nishishichijo Kakegoshicho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8881, Japan;34.992681;135.731301;97;true;true;Ramen;The chef has been researching the deliciousness of ramen since he was a schoolboy. In search of a unique flavour, he made ‘Scallop and Japanese Pepper Ramen’ his signature dish. Soup of dashi drawn from chicken, pork and seafood is multilayered and satisfying. The finished Japanese pepper oil imparts a refreshing feeling, and the generous topping of scallop is pure luxury. A carefully calibrated bowl of goodness that is the gift of repeated independent study.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5893;Ogimachi Udonya Asuro;Japan;Osaka;3-8-3 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0041, Japan;34.701752;135.511225;91;false;false;Udon;Located close to Tenjinbashi-suji, Kansai’s longest shopping street. The shop seems to be in competition for the longest queue to get in. The dish of renown is ‘Toriten to Taichikuwaten to Ontama Bukkake’ (udon topped with chicken tempura, sea bream paste cake tempura and soft-boiled egg). If the pure flavour of dipping sauce and noodles is what you’re after, try the ‘Hiyakake’. The clear sauce and delicious noodles are standouts, so the flavour of the seafood broth and the springiness of the noodles have your undivided attention. Choosing your favourite toppings adds to the fun.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5894;via del emme;Japan;Osaka;7-7-10 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.697566;135.484747;98;false;false;Italian;When the chef returned from Italy, he brought with him recipes rooted in the land and techniques for making pasta by hand. He now applies his experiences in Marche, a region rich in the bounty of sea and mountains, to the foodstuffs of Japan. Guests can choose from an impressive list of pasta dishes, some made with seafood and even game. The meat in the Bolognese sauce is hand-chopped, in a nod to Marchese practice. Always attentive to guests’ wishes, Maeda is happy to adjust flavours while hewing true to his cuisine’s Italian roots.;Air conditioning;[]
5895;Oryori Menami;Japan;Kyoto;96 Nakajimacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8004, Japan;35.009215;135.77051;39;true;false;Obanzai;This restaurant began as a place serving obanzai and yakitori, and the sauce that the chicken and green onion skewer is grilled in goes all the way back to then. Kyoto culinary delights line the counter, such as a stew of deep-fried tofu and leafy vegetables, Kujo leek dressed in vinegar miso and boiled nama-yuba. Here you can linger and relax to the gracious hospitality of the tunic-clad proprietress, who keeps her grandmother’s name alive in the name of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5896;Uo China Yo;Japan;Osaka;7-4-25 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.697393;135.48512;66;true;true;Chinese;The concept at this restaurant is Chinese cuisine with an emphasis on fish. First, try the set menu, with your choice of main dishes. Pick four fish dishes you like, which come with an assortment of appetisers including seafood carpaccio. This fully rounded meal even comes with fried rice at the end. Various dishes on the menu make good use of seasonal ingredients such as lobster stew with chili sauce and seafood mapo tofu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5897;JIBUNDOKI;Japan;Osaka;4-5-11 Minamikyuhojimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0058, Japan;34.679389;135.49827;100;false;true;Teppanyaki, Okonomiyaki;The owner-chef pours his creativity into teppanyaki dishes of incredible variety. In true Osaka style, both pork and mixed okonomiyaki are available. Though the batter is thick, the finished texture is light. Imaginative grilled skewers hint at the cuisines of many countries, with offerings such as nama-fu, salmon tartare and tteokbokki. All items are served in bite-sized pieces, so patrons can enjoy sampling a variety of flavours.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5898;Mugito Mensuke;Japan;Osaka;3-4-12 Toyosaki, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0072, Japan;34.711331;135.500009;86;true;false;Ramen;Pursuing an original approach to ramen, the chef works with carefully selected ingredients.  Soup is prepared from free-range chicken and guinea fowl to bring out maximum flavour. Noodles, produced on the premises, are crafted for a delicious finish. Wontons stuffed with wagyu filling are the very flavour of luxury. Counter seating features an earthen wall made by a plasterer and wooden trays typical of Japanese restaurants. A ceaseless drive for improvement is evident in every bowl of ramen.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5899;Ichihana;Japan;Kyoto;264-1 Nijo Aburanokojicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0051, Japan;35.012191;135.753257;63;false;true;Japanese;A typical lunch offering is sashimi and items served in small bowls, while the evening lineup boasts a full complement of sashimi and items served in rice and cooked individually for each guest. Ten ingredients are always available, with gomoku (‘five ingredients’) and wild plants being perennial favourites. To express the seasons through kamameshi, Ichihana offers flavours like bamboo shoots, sweetfish, mushrooms and oysters. While the rice is cooking, enjoy Kyoto flavours such as steamed wheat gluten with sweet miso sauce and steamed tilefish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5901;Kannomiho;Japan;Osaka;2-2-14 Andojimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0061, Japan;34.676136;135.515754;41;false;false;Izakaya;Open the menu and the first line reads, ‘Kannomiho is the shop run by Miho, who loves warmed sake’. Miho offers home-style seasonal fare accompanied by sake and all its appeal. Seared duck is a year-round favourite. As cup follows cup, unwind as the sake warms you right through. Songs of the Showa (postwar) era pipe through the dining room. With sake cup in hand, guests leisurely soak in the pub-like atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
5902;kushiage 010;Japan;Osaka;4F, 1-1-41 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.696723;135.500513;25;true;false;Kushiage;These creative kushiage incorporate culinary influences from many countries. The sheer variety is endlessly fun. For your first skewer, you might start with angel shrimp from New Caledonia. The samgyeopsal (grilled pork-belly slices) wrapped in perilla and Korean lettuce is spiced with gochujang for a real Korean treat. Karaage, marinated in a sauce of spices such as star anise and five-spice powder and sprinkled with tapioca flour, fills the air with the fragrance of Taiwan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5903;La pleine lune;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 55-1 Matsuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0831, Japan;35.013582;135.762028;70;false;false;French;Chef Naoaki Nishii brings ingredients to life using traditional cuisine. One example is the thick-cut smoked salmon, paired with chestnuts in autumn and turnips in winter to emphasise the seasonal feeling. Meat dishes are garnished with kuro shichimi (‘seven black spices’) to add a Kyoto touch. In homage to classic French cooking, he does not spare the sauce, taking care to impart a modern flavouring. Butter and cream are used sparingly for a lighter taste.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
5906;Shichiku Kiko;Japan;Kyoto;16 Shichiku Shimotakedonocho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8412, Japan;35.052722;135.748209;84;true;true;Japanese;The tiled-roof row house on Gen’i-dori makes an immediate impression. The owner-chef, wearing a bow tie, rushes about, unable to rest unless he does everything himself. With his wealth of experience, he takes familiar ingredients and raises them to new levels, creating graceful Kyoto cuisine – and it’s good value for money. Appetiser platters are served with rice at lunchtime and in the evening with drinks. The gentle demeanour of the proprietress makes you feel at home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5907;Shitennoji Hayauchi;Japan;Osaka;1-12-16 Shitennoji, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0051, Japan;34.655611;135.51413;23;false;false;Soba;Oribe stoneware and distinctive Japanese-style paintings give presence to the interior. Crockery is produced by a potter with whom the owner-chef has cultivated a relationship. Recycled materials and earthen walls give the space a rough-hewn feel and a folk-art charm. Two kinds of soba are prepared: fine-ground seiro soba and coarse-ground inaka soba. Both are rolled to the same thickness. At lunchtime, customers start queuing in front of this popular shop before it opens. ‘Soba trays’ of soba with snacks are available with reservations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5908;Oudon Yomogi;Japan;Osaka;2-10-6 Sagisu, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0002, Japan;34.698137;135.482178;98;false;false;Udon;This à la carte udon shop is a project of the proprietress of the Japanese restaurant Miyamoto. The use of bamboo gives the restaurant a kappo feel. In the evening the style is a fixed menu to which drinking snacks can be added. Great care is taken with the use of crockery – this is an udon restaurant with the flair of a soba place. The star of the udon items is the dashi soup stock, which is created with the basic soup stock, particularly drawing inspiration from soup dishes in traditional multi-course meals. A flavoursome lesson in Osaka dashi culture.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
5909;NOODLE SHOP RENNOSUKE;Japan;Kyoto;56-32 Murasakino Shimokashiwanocho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8313, Japan;35.033742;135.739187;35;true;false;Ramen;The residential neighbourhood is a maze and there’s no sign for the restaurant. A spotlight on a bowl of ramen in a showcase indicates you’ve arrived. The industrial space has the feel of a laboratory. ‘Raamen’ is a blend of Kyoto wheat noodles in a clear soup of seafood dashi stock. Thinly sliced roasted pork fillet is from Kyoto-raised swine. Blue bowls of specially ordered Kiyomizu ware set off each meal to its advantage. Custard pudding, sweetened with refined sugar, is a popular item.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
5910;Sakamoto Sushi;Japan;Osaka;1-23-13 Nishikujo, Konohana-ku, Osaka, 554-0012, Japan;34.682444;135.467391;79;false;false;Sushi;With Nishikujo Station to guide them to the spot, every evening customers gather at Sakamoto Sushi, where the familiar chef greets them with a smile. The omakase menu, which begins with a snack, is astounding in variety and breadth. Fish are painstakingly prepared by methods such as marination and searing, and are paired with white sushi rice in the Kansai way. Nigirizushi are interspersed with bozushi and hand-rolled sushi to keep things interesting. The chef uses the highest-grade fish, yet the prices won’t break the bank.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5911;Kushikatsu Gojoya;Japan;Osaka;2-1-11 Uchihiranomachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0037, Japan;34.687233;135.513621;24;false;true;Kushiage;The tempo in the kitchen is lively as cooks deep-fry these imaginative skewers. Order the omakase, which only ends when your belly is full. An amazing 25 types of skewers are normally available—you’ll want to see them all. Korean kimchi, Indian curry, Italian tomato sauce and so on take you on a journey from country to country. A fusion of Osaka’s fried foods with traditional cuisines of the world.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5914;Teuchisoba Kanei;Japan;Kyoto;11-1 Murasakino Higashifujinomoricho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8223, Japan;35.037603;135.746727;41;true;true;Soba;The owner-chef fell in love with soba, so taught himself how to make it. Using a stone mill, he grinds his “Rough-ground Soba” by hand to create wonderfully rustic juwari, or 100% buckwheat noodles. A shark skin grater and stick of wasabi are provided, so you can start grating your wasabi while you wait for your soba. Pre-soba snacks created with drinks in mind are on offer, including broiled miso, itawasa and dashimaki tamago. The ambience of the traditional wooden townhouse looking out on the verandah of an inner garden sets the mood.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Shoes must be removed;[]
5915;Lapintaika;Japan;Kyoto;499 Kitamonzencho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8352, Japan;35.01166;135.778226;17;true;false;Italian;The menu is broad, reflecting the wide range of local Italian cooking styles the chef has studied. Each plate feeds two, so sharing is the order of the day. The assorted appetiser, generous in both portion and variety, is a perennial favourite. A full complement of pasta dishes is on offer—the list of spaghettis alone is extensive. The restaurant’s name means ‘coming back’, and indeed the satisfying weekend lunch draws plenty of repeat visitors.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
5916;Itsutsu;Japan;Kyoto;28 Murasakino Unrinincho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8214, Japan;35.040881;135.747584;88;false;true;Soba;As a Wakuden establishment, Itsutsu embraces their 'soba and cuisine' motto while specializing in seasonal dishes. Soba is made into thin noodles, using only the smallest amount of binder and well water from Daitoku-ji Temple. The chef doesn’t brace the noodles with cold water, so the flavour jumps to the fore. Similarly, soba dipping sauce is mild, based on its salt flavour. At lunchtime, the three-item set with soba is recommended. Mackerel sushi is a popular à la carte item. Reservations are required for the prix fixe Buddhist vegetarian cuisine, which includes soba.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5918;Rubino;Malta;Valletta;53 Old Bakery Street, Valletta, VLT 1454, Malta;35.899322;14.5121358;32;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This sweet little bistro started life in 1906 as a confectionery shop, serving, among other things, cassata Siciliana – which it still offers today. Sit in one of three cosy, traditional rooms and receive hands-on service from the owner. The blackboard menu lists classic Maltese and Italian dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
5919;AYU;Malta;Gzira;209 The Strand, Gzira, GZR 1023, Malta;35.9044112;14.4957256;21;false;false;World Cuisine, International;With a panoramic location near Manoel Island, this restaurant offers a unique culinary experience. The three brothers at the helm here have traveled the world, infusing their menu with global influences. Dishes like sea bream steamed with soy and ginger, and black suckling pig in a Sri Lankan-style curry, are packed with bold and spicy flavors, ideal for those seeking an exotic dining adventure. The excellent value for money and the informal atmosphere make this restaurant on Gzira’s seafront promenade a must-visit.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5920;Grain Street;Malta;Valletta;167 Merchants Street, Valletta, VLT 1174, Malta;35.898901;14.5154391;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the main pedestrianised street in the centre of town, this restaurant with an attractive outdoor dining space serves simple, informal Mediterranean cuisine. Dishes include lasagne with squid, cuttlefish ink and nduja sausage as well as delicious desserts such as passion fruit tart with yogurt ice cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
5921;Commando;Malta;Mellieħa;Misraħ Iz-Żjara tal-Papa, Mellieħa, MLH 1080, Malta;35.9595886;14.3615857;93;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant has a long and very interesting history, starting with the building itself (around 300 years old) and continuing with the history of the family at the helm, who have been here since 1930 and once provided support for the Royal Marines. The dining room boasts a rustic yet personalised decor with exposed brickwork and contemporary furnishings, while the cuisine focuses on fresh ingredients that are full of flavour. Our inspector particularly recommends the pappardelle pasta with a duck ragù and a few chopped hazelnuts for added flavour.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5922;Terrone;Malta;Birgu;Fort St. Angelo, Birgu Waterfront, Birgu, BRG 1734, Malta;35.8914933;14.5193119;81;false;true;Seafood;Tucked away on the tip of the small town of Vittoriosa, just around the corner from the Birgu seafront with its stunning yachts at anchor, this restaurant run by Maltese-Australian chef Adrian Hili serves Italian and Maltese cuisine. The superb Mediterranean-style local fish specialities include turbot with Sicilian clams and cannellini beans. As a result of ongoing restoration work, the entrance is currently to the rear of the building (not particularly attractive), but once inside the elegant decor and outdoor dining space more than compensate.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
5924;Zum Vaas;Germany;Forstinning;Münchener Straße 88, Forstinning, 85661, Germany;48.1597254;11.8989304;92;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;It is always a delight to visit a friendly and welcoming restaurant with a lively atmosphere. This one can look back on over 150 years of tradition and boasts a spruce, upscale interior. The service is cordial and attentive, and the food is delicious and made using high-quality ingredients from carefully selected producers. In addition to the menu of the day, which also features Mediterranean touches, there are the Vaas classics, such as roast Swabian-Hall pork. The impressive wine list comprises a remarkable range of vintage wines from various producers – predominantly from Germany and France, but also from Austria and other Old World countries. Comfortable guestrooms are available in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5925;Lindenhof;Germany;Emsdetten;Alte Emsstraße 7, Emsdetten, 48282, Germany;52.1781706;7.5316;20;false;true;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;Like their hotel, with its cosy individually designed guestrooms, the Hankhs' restaurant is also very popular. This is down to the excellent seasonal cuisine, which has regional and Mediterranean influences. You can order à la carte or opt for a set menu (vegetarian version available). Friendly and competent waitstaff. The small terraces in front of and to the rear of the building are delightful.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5926;Zum Lamm;Germany;Neupotz;Hauptstraße 7, Neupotz, 76777, Germany;49.1174557;8.3173627;87;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This inn is everything you could wish for! Your cordial hosts, Ulrike and Manfred Kreger, put their heart and soul into running this popular restaurant. He is the chef and specialises in regional cuisine – one of his specialities is pike-perch from the Rhine, which is practically on the doorstep! Another equally delicious option is the herb-crusted rack of lamb with mint sauce, grilled watermelon and gnocchi. In summer, the tables in the garden to the rear of the building are in high demand. Smart guestrooms available for overnight stays.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5928;Rössle;Germany;Elzach;Hauptstraße 19, Elzach, 79215, Germany;48.1729463;8.0717333;87;true;false;Country cooking, International;This family-run restaurant serves fresh, flavoursome cuisine made with choice ingredients. Alongside the intriguing "Chef's Menu", there are specials written up on the board, plus a menu of classic dishes – they all go down a treat. To round off your experience, attentive waitstaff, a friendly atmosphere and a delightful terrace. The attractive guestrooms combine warm wood and sleek design.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5929;DELI;Germany;Dresden;Königsbrücker Straße 96, Dresden, 01099, Germany;51.0807167;13.7611912;38;true;true;International, Farm to table;Here, in an appealingly down-to-earth and relaxed atmosphere, you can enjoy interesting international cuisine that is based on the seasons and drawn from select ingredients. The terrace on Niagaraplatz, a square with a waterfall feature, is also charming… The traditional hooded beach chairs are great for really chilling out. Good to know: They serve hot food all day.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5930;Weinstube Brand;Germany;Frankweiler;Weinstraße 19, Frankweiler, 76833, Germany;49.2281379;8.0578853;18;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Here, diners can look forward to really good food which is both fresh and seasonal, as well as cordial service. Everything is pleasantly down-to-earth – just as you would expect in a wine tavern. The wine and game, like most of the produce, come from the region. Whether you opt for the classic rump steak, one of the daily specials or a vegetarian dish, be sure to leave room for the molten chocolate cake – just heavenly! Delightful courtyard terrace. In short: a fun dining experience!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5931;Krone;Germany;Inzlingen;Riehenstraße 92, Inzlingen, 79594, Germany;47.5881908;7.685173;83;false;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;Krone has been properly invested in: from the façade to the hotel rooms, everything is chic and high quality, the restaurant is modern and sleek. The food is very good, with select produce turned into aromatic dishes with plenty of flavour. At lunchtime, a smaller range of interesting options. If you are staying longer, Basel and Alsace are very close by.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5932;Heinzler am See;Germany;Immenstaad am Bodensee;Strandbadstraße 3, Immenstaad am Bodensee, 88090, Germany;47.6610015;9.3553993;45;true;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Whether you are in the mood for regional comfort food or something more international, the Heinzler brothers have got it covered. Their wide-ranging menu includes Swabian Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy), Arctic char and whitefish fillets, and yellowfin tuna sashimi. There is also an appealing selection of barbecue dishes with a choice of side dishes and sauces. You can choose to dine in the cosy Jagdstube ("hunting lounge") with its winning blend of traditional charm and modern design, or the lovely Panorama-Restaurant, whose large windows afford stunning views. Not forgetting the fabulous terrace almost touching the water! The waitstaff are personable and attentive – service is clearly a serious matter here. Tasteful and comfortable guestrooms available at the hotel, which also boasts a private beach area at the lake and a private jetty.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5933;Gehrlein's Hardtwald;Germany;Neupotz;Sandhohl 14, Neupotz, 76777, Germany;49.1221291;8.3131069;67;true;true;Country cooking, French Contemporary;Somewhat tucked away, the Gehrlein family's restaurant boasts a warm and welcoming interior, as well as a lovely garden terrace. Meticulously crafted using the finest ingredients, the dishes served here are remarkably flavoursome. One shining example: Label Rouge guinea fowl, celeriac, carrot, miso, fritter. The friendly waitstaff pull out all the stops to ensure a perfect dining experience. The guesthouse opposite provides comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5934;Fährhaus;Germany;Dornum;Dorfstraße 42, Dornum, 26553, Germany;53.6729297;7.3561764;72;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Practically right behind the dike and just a few minutes' walk from the ferry port, this restaurant serves distinctly local cuisine made with produce sourced from local fishers and farmers. Completely unpretentious and free from unnecessary frills, owner Gerold Janssen's dishes are brimming with freshness and flavour, as in the Helgoland crab cocktail or the crispy baked plaice fillets. Good to know: Well-kept guestrooms are available for overnight stays or holidays.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5936;Anetseder;Germany;Hauzenberg;Lindenstraße 15, Hauzenberg, 94051, Germany;48.614821;13.5963903;40;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Traditional German public house culture is alive and well here, and at the same time they tap into the zeitgeist. The lovely dining space has a high ceiling and a trendy, modern feel and the waitstaff are friendly. They serve fresh and tasty food, with seasonal ingredients, preferably from the region, taking pride of place.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5937;Gambero Rosso da Domenico;Germany;Eibelstadt;Mühle 2, Eibelstadt, 97246, Germany;49.7243573;9.9934917;33;true;true;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;Domenico Cannizzaro has been on a mission to showcase Italian cuisine in Franconia for well over 20 years, and has run this restaurant at the small marina with his wife, Teresa, since 2012. Here, they live and breathe hospitality, serving two set menus, "Domenico" and "Teresuzza", which each comprise three or four courses – it's also possible to mix and match. Astute wine recommendations come courtesy of the chef-patron himself. Gorgeous terrace overlooking the Main River.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5939;Anne-Sophie;Germany;Künzelsau;Am Schlossplatz 9, Künzelsau, 74653, Germany;49.2789069;9.6909185;80;true;false;International, Regional Cuisine;We recommend getting a table in the light and airy winter garden: here you have beautiful views over the garden! The food is tasty and seasonal, with classics such as braised veal cheeks also proving popular. At lunchtime there is a reduced menu as well as inexpensive daily specials. The restaurant is located on the Schlossplatz, some 150m from the main hotel building.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5940;Gasthaus Widmann's Löwen;Germany;Königsbronn;Struthstraße 17, Königsbronn, 89551, Germany;48.7297506;10.0649224;55;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;This cosy establishment serves up classic regional fare and seasonal dishes made from high-quality, fresh ingredients. The Widmann family places great emphasis on their restaurant's connection to the region. Why not try "Widmann's spare ribs"? Alternatively, you could opt for a surprise menu comprising three or four courses? Don't miss the chance to enjoy the lovely beer garden in the summer – it really is a delightful spot! Cookery classes and various other events are also held here.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
5941;Münstermanns Kontor;Germany;Düsseldorf;Hohe Straße 11, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.2226724;6.7740666;43;true;false;International, Traditional Cuisine;What started as a shop selling eggs and butter later became a delicatessen and today this spot is a popular bistro with a pleasingly lively urban atmosphere and an open kitchen. The tasty dishes include German classics such as currywurst and Wiener schnitzel, but also international dishes. The food is accompanied by decent wines by the glass, and the service is friendly. Open from noon to 8pm, last orders 6.30pm. NB: They don't take reservations at lunchtime – so come early, as the place gets very busy.;;[]
5943;Nußbaumerin;Germany;Berlin;Leibnizstraße 55, Berlin, 10629, Germany;52.5013988;13.3129282;45;false;false;Austrian, Traditional Cuisine;In her cosy restaurant, Johanna Nußbaumer recreates a little bit of Austria in the heart of Berlin. Ensconced in a side street off Kurfürstendamm (aka "Ku'damm") since 2008, it has become an institution and an essential fixture. "Authentic... Traditional... Austrian" is the motto here. Tafelspitz aspic on a shallot vinaigrette, Viennese beef goulash with bread dumplings, or apricot dumplings with sweet buttered breadcrumbs are some shining examples. The good selection of wines also originates in the chef's homeland. The restaurant is popular and doesn't have an excess of tables, so be sure to make a reservation! Tip: There are also excellent options to be had at Nussbaumer Heurigen on Breitenbachplatz in Zehlendorf.;Air conditioning;[]
5944;Im Kittchen;Germany;Bad Kreuznach;Alte Poststraße 2, Bad Kreuznach, 55545, Germany;49.8473331;7.8554814;17;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;This little restaurant is located in the middle of the old town, in a narrow side street near the Eiermarkt. The dining area has a rustic feel and tightly packed table, which contributes to the charming atmosphere, as does the cordial proprietress, who is in charge of the service. The delicious options are written on the blackboard and also come in smaller portions as a surprise menu. The impressive wine list features around 230 labels.;Interesting wine list;[]
5945;Scheidels Restaurant zum Kranz;Germany;Kenzingen;Offenburger Straße 18, Kenzingen, 79341, Germany;48.1952255;7.773248;50;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Home Cooking;Conscious of their long family history (the restaurant is now run by the seventh generation), the owners here are committed to maintaining their traditions yet the food remains resolutely down-to-earth. Charming historic ambience, plus warm and welcoming staff. Simple, tasty dishes take pride of place, inspired by regional and seasonal produce. A vegetarian menu is also available.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5946;Gutshof Andres;Germany;Kirchlauter;Pettstadt 1, Kirchlauter, 96166, Germany;50.0505473;10.6953797;90;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Surrounded by venerable old trees, this listed manor house has been owned by the same family since 1839. It boasts a delightful beer garden overlooking a small lake. Your hosts put everything they have into providing friendly service and fresh, seasonal regional cuisine. Their focus on sustainability is apparent in their selection of ingredients, some of which they make themselves. House-made spreads, sauces, brandies etc are also available for purchase. Should you wish to stay the night in this lovely, quiet spot, there are two flats in the former brewery, chic, modern double rooms in the coach house, and a comfortable holiday home – Gutsverwalter Haus. A practical tip: there are two charging stations for electric cars.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5947;Weißes Roß;Germany;Illschwang;Am Kirchberg 1, Illschwang, 92278, Germany;49.448185;11.6844795;64;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;All the meat served by Hans-Jürgen Nägerl comes from the restaurant’s own butchery. This is a fact much appreciated by his guests, as are his ‘chalet snacks’ and ‘kitchen parties’. His delicious cuisine includes Tafelspitz (Viennese-style boiled beef) with herb sauce and roast potatoes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5948;Treibgut;Germany;Ulm;Friedrichsau 50, Ulm, 89073, Germany;48.4118808;10.0124766;33;false;false;Contemporary, International;As a sophisticated alternative to Seestern, Treibgut adds to the gourmet credentials of the Lago hotel. Modern cuisine is served in a trendy and exceedingly stylish interior. There are also dishes for sharing, e.g. steak cuts, whole fish or snack platters. They offer a nice selection of goods from their own bakery, butcher's shop and ice cream factory.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5949;Mühlenhelle - Bistro;Germany;Gummersbach;Hohler Straße 1, Gummersbach, 51645, Germany;50.9834035;7.5312635;33;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This charming bistro set up in a pleasantly light and airy space is an attractive alternative to the fine dining restaurant. The food here is also top-notch, with Michael Quendler preparing delicious seasonal cuisine in the open kitchen. Much of the food also draws on tradition and showcases the region. Take, for example, the variation of Lambachtal salmon trout or the pan-fried Eifel pork blood sausage – two knockout dishes that linger in the memory. An appealing selection of wines is also on offer. Cordial service with a personal touch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5950;Little John's;Germany;Neukirchen-Vluyn;Niederrheinallee 310, Neukirchen-Vluyn, 47506, Germany;51.4382103;6.5351667;54;false;false;Farm to table, International;Housed in a spruce building dating from 1905, Tim Lellau's restaurant is appealingly laid-back with a Scandinavian feel. Here, attentive and well-drilled waitstaff serve high-quality, fresh cuisine. There is a choice of two set menus: "Weide & Wasser" (Pasture & Water) and the vegetarian "Wald & Wiese" (Forest & Meadow) – this can be made vegan by prior arrangement. Alternatively, you can also order à la carte. There is also a reasonably priced three-course set menu at lunchtime. From the entrance area, you can see into the kitchen, which is sure to whet your appetite! N.B. cash payments only.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5951;Sommerau;Germany;Bonndorf im Schwarzwald;Sommerau 1, Bonndorf im Schwarzwald, 79848, Germany;47.8164302;8.2580163;100;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The trip to the Hegar family's restaurant just outside Bonndorf is definitely worth it! Nestled in a quiet valley, surrounded by woods and meadows, the setting could not be more idyllic. There's an inviting terrace, but you can also enjoy the view from inside. The cuisine is regional and seasonal, including French and Mediterranean influences. The dishes are meticulously crafted and packed with flavour. Great care is taken to source ingredients that reflect the restaurant's commitment to sustainability. The wine list showcases a number of gems from the region, with a special emphasis on Baden Burgundy – the selection of half bottles is excellent. In the hotel of the same name, there are cosy, modern guestrooms and a beautiful sauna house, plus a natural swimming pond. And so that you can really unplug and unwind, there's no Wi-Fi or mobile phone reception!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5952;Seehaus;Germany;Dießen am Ammersee;Seeweg-Süd 12, Dießen am Ammersee, 86911, Germany;47.9767109;11.0997022;24;true;false;International, Modern Cuisine;This is a gorgeous spot at any time of the day. In the summer months, the terrace overlooking the lake is perfect for a relaxed lunch or afternoon cake (summer weekends only). In the evening and in winter, you'll be just as happy to sit inside – there's something romantic about this charming restaurant done out in warm rustic wood. They also serve fantastic modern and international cuisine, such as "bouillabaisse à la Seehaus" with lobster, rouille sauce and bread chips.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5953;Lucky Leek;Germany;Berlin;Kollwitzstraße 54, Berlin, 10405, Germany;52.5349458;13.4168487;30;true;false;Vegan;"Fine Natural Dining" is the concept here at this pleasant restaurant. Charming staff serve up fully vegan cuisine in the form of a three- to five-course tasting menu – it's also possible to order à la carte. Made with seasonal vegetables, the creative, plant-based dishes are packed with flavour, and they are just as popular with international visitors as they are with locals. In summer, the best place to dine is on the terrace out front.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5954;Landhaus Lebert;Germany;Windelsbach;Schloßstraße 8, Windelsbach, 91635, Germany;49.3996191;10.2994884;26;false;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;In a small town about 10km from Rothenburg ob der Tauber, this cosy restaurant serves really flavoursome cuisine made from good-quality regional produce – importance is attached to sustainability. In summer, there is a lovely beer garden. Well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays, and a barn for private events. Tip: In the old shepherd's caravan, you can buy products made on site, such as lemon liqueur, spice mixtures, jellies and jams.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5955;Almer Schlossmühle;Germany;Brilon;Schlossstraße 13, Brilon, 59929, Germany;51.4593813;8.6247775;54;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This carefully converted old mill next to the little Schloss Alme is a highly appealing restaurant that abounds with rustic charm. The delicious food features seasonal dishes from the regional repertoire as well as classic fare from the chef's native Austria. Head for the lovely terrace in fine weather. There are also guestrooms for an overnight stay.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5956;Mussumer Krug;Germany;Bocholt;Mussumer Kirchweg 143, Bocholt, 46395, Germany;51.8215955;6.6009305;44;false;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Whether you are seated in the rustic-style old brick building or the laid-back modern annexe, the atmosphere at this restaurant is very pleasant. The menu features modern international dishes such as yellowtail ceviche and traditional specialities, for example braised beef shoulder. A three-course surprise menu is also proposed. The kitchen takes its cue from the changing seasons with a penchant for regional produce. There is a great selection of German wines, and the service is friendly and attentive. Covered terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
5957;Restaurant Villa Esche;Germany;Chemnitz;Parkstraße 58, Chemnitz, 09120, Germany;50.8151713;12.9003974;62;false;false;International, Contemporary;Built in 1903, the former coach house of Villa Esche (now the Henry van de Velde Museum) houses this bright, tastefully designed restaurant where diners can enjoy attentive service and top-notch seasonal cuisine. Opt for the four-course menu or order à la carte. At lunchtime, the options are slightly more limited but include moderately priced daily specials. Delightful terrace overlooking the grounds.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
5958;EssBar fein & pfiffig;Germany;Düsseldorf;Kaiserstraße 27, Düsseldorf, 40479, Germany;51.2338608;6.7785896;55;true;false;International;The outwardly unimposing restaurant run by Daniel Baur and Olga Jorich is situated only a few steps away from the Hofgarten public park. Pleasant atmosphere, plus flavoursome dishes prepared from good-quality ingredients and offering good value for money. Neither will you be disappointed by the wine list! Attractive protected terrace to the rear.;Terrace;[]
5959;Rait'ner Wirt;Germany;Schleching;Achentalstraße 8, Schleching, 83259, Germany;47.7387968;12.4373777;41;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;This beautifully renovated and well-established 17C inn now houses attractive, comfortable guestrooms and exceedingly cosy dining areas brimming with rustic pub charm – it's not uncommon to share a large table with other diners. The glorious beer garden is a real draw in summer! The kitchen serves up hearty regional fare with no frills but plenty of flavour, including roast pork, cheese spaetzle and Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake). Be sure to take a look at the daily specials.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5960;Staudenwirt;Germany;Finning;Staudenweg 6, Finning, 86923, Germany;48.0180371;11.0187956;40;true;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;This well-established restaurant with its spruce little hotel has been run by the same family for three generations. Each dining area has quite a different style, from rustic to pleasingly contemporary, plus there is a delightful terrace. The menu features a diverse range of options, from comforting regional fare such as half a rotisserie chicken, or "Grandma Hilde's Rohrnudel" (oven-baked yeast dumplings) for dessert, as well as modern, seasonal and internationally influenced dishes. Vegetarians are well catered for, too. Fantastic value for money!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5961;Rührberger Hof;Germany;Grenzach-Wyhlen;Inzlinger Straße 1, Grenzach-Wyhlen, 79639, Germany;47.5689975;7.7056066;65;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The historical Rührberger Hof estate, which is home to this long-established family business, has been around since 1902. The fact that it was once used for farming is no longer apparent today. The pleasingly modern interior is an attractive setting in which to savour the excellent cuisine of brothers Christoph und Felix Düster. This is based on classical foundations and takes its cue from the region and the seasons. At lunchtime, the reasonably priced set menu of the day is very popular. There are also well-kept contemporary-style guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5962;Fürstenfelder;Germany;Fürstenfeldbruck;Fürstenfeld 15, Fürstenfeldbruck, 82256, Germany;48.1707619;11.2473851;53;true;false;Contemporary, Country cooking;This former monastery makes for a wonderful setting. In what was once the cattle shed, the impressive Bohemian vaulted ceiling has been incorporated into the modern interior design, with a centrally positioned open kitchen. Out in the courtyard of the Cistercian monastery, there is a lovely terrace, slightly separated from the beer garden. The menu is varied, featuring dishes with a modern twist and made with sustainably produced (organic) regional produce. Options include dishes from the Josper grill, as well as vegetarian and vegan alternatives. Lunchtime buffet.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5963;Zöllner's Weinstube;Germany;Forchheim;Sigritzau 1, Forchheim, 91301, Germany;49.6978376;11.0808146;81;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Surrounded by splendid gardens, this 18C half-timbered sandstone building is as charming on the outside as it is on the inside. Sitting beneath a striking vaulted ceiling, diners can enjoy regional as well as Mediterranean-inspired cuisine made from first-rate produce. There is also an excellent selection of Franconian wines. In summer, the terrace is a must!;Car park,Terrace;[]
5964;Aschbacher Hof;Germany;Feldkirchen-Westerham;Aschbach 3, Feldkirchen-Westerham, 83620, Germany;47.9182288;11.8183901;96;false;false;Farm to table, Bavarian;This pretty country hotel run by the Lechner family offers not only fabulous views of the region and tasteful, cosy rooms but also exceptionally good, fresh cooking. The regional and seasonal dishes include game as well as classics like Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy). Wonderful terrace.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
5965;Zur Krone;Germany;Freiamt;Mussbach 6, Freiamt, 79348, Germany;48.1710672;7.8914622;66;false;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Set in a spruce country house, this establishment has been run with great dedication and a sense of tradition by nine successive generations of the same family for over 200 years. Taking its cue from the seasons, the ingredient-led cuisine is flavoursome. Asparagus dishes are served in spring, game and goose in winter. For those with a sweet tooth, the meringue with cream, vanilla ice cream and egg liqueur is a must-try! Food is served in the cosy interior or out on the gorgeous terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5966;Café Rapp;Germany;Königsfeld;Dörfle 22, Königsfeld, 78126, Germany;48.1613182;8.3784909;49;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Originally a bakery and café, the family business is now also a restaurant, where quality, flavour and price are spot on. The emphasis is on regional and seasonal products – vegetables and meat are sourced from the village, herbs are grown in the kitchen garden. A must in the afternoon: the delicious fresh cakes! Pretty guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5967;Sennhütte;Germany;Kleines Wiesental;Schwand 14, Kleines Wiesental, 79692, Germany;47.7372516;7.7918458;48;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Family hospitality is the name of the game here! Since 1918, the Grether family have put their heart and soul into this place and not least into the good food, made mostly with regional produce. Dishes ranging from traditional to slightly more sophisticated are served in a space divided into smaller rooms or out on the lovely verdant terrace. Snacks and cakes are available throughout the day. They have their own distillery, smokehouse and Alpine dairy. Pretty, comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5968;Weedenhof;Germany;Jugenheim in Rheinhessen;Mainzer Straße 6, Jugenheim in Rheinhessen, 55270, Germany;49.8944814;8.0873792;21;false;true;Farm to table, Mediterranean Cuisine;The restaurant is wonderfully cosy with its rustic exposed timber frame and dry-stone interior. Michael Knöll conjures up cuisine that combines Mediterranean and regional influences, making use of excellent produce to deliver flavoursome dishes. Choose between à la carte options and seasonal set menus, including a vegetarian version. They also have lovely and well-maintained guestrooms.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5969;Landgasthaus Gidibauer-Hof;Germany;Hauzenberg;Grub 7, Hauzenberg, 94051, Germany;48.644564;13.6234676;63;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;You eat well here, and furthermore the regional cuisine comes at very fair prices. The home-reared beef, for example, is sure to whet the appetite. The ambience is friendly, cosy and rustic. The converted cowshed is a great venue for parties. In the hotel of the same name, the guestrooms are furnished with natural wood furniture.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5970;Allgäuer Stuben;Germany;Isny im Allgäu;Lindauer Straße 75, Isny im Allgäu, 88316, Germany;47.6887452;10.0314918;19;true;true;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;The good food and welcoming atmosphere are the main draws of this restaurant run by the Rimmele family, whose dedication to their work is palpable – that is certainly the case for chef Susanne Rimmele. She cooks regional as well as Mediterranean dishes. The front-of-house team are charming and obliging. Tip: the delightful terrace. They also offer cookery classes, tackling eg pasta, asparagus, game. Pleasant overnight accommodation is available at Hotel Hohe Linde.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5971;Capricorn [ i ] Aries Brasserie;Germany;Cologne;Alteburgerstraße 31, Cologne, 50678, Germany;50.9208129;6.9622423;60;true;true;Classic French;Located in a neighbourhood with a unique character, this appealing, laid-back restaurant has plenty of regulars. Welcoming and lively, it's everything a brasserie should be. The menu, too, is down-to-earth, including mouthwatering options – house-made venison ham, brasserie classics such as steak-frites and vegetarian dishes. Tip: Take a punt on the moderately priced surprise menu. Friendly and professional service. Pavement terrace.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
5972;Restaurant Corona im Hotel zur Post;Germany;Hardert;Mittelstraße 13, Hardert, 56579, Germany;50.5161996;7.5157151;15;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;It's a real treat to eat here! In this classic restaurant, Sergio and Kerstin Corona work as a well-coordinated team, providing charming service and Mediterranean-inspired cuisine. In addition to the "Méditerranée" and "Corona" set menus, from which you can also choose à la carte, there is also a bargain to be had in the three-course lunch menu.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5973;Die Windmühle;Germany;Horn-Bad Meinberg;Windmühlenweg 10, Horn-Bad Meinberg, 32805, Germany;51.9130183;8.9743314;31;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;In this former corn mill, the Lemke family now run a restaurant that serves excellent food. There are two comfortable dining spaces – the Mühlenstube and the Kaminzimmer – plus a delightful terrace where you can tuck into delicious seasonal and regional dishes. The friendly and attentive front-of-house team take delight in talking diners through their selection of German wines.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5974;Landgasthof Löwen;Germany;Kirchdorf an der Iller;Kirchdorfer Straße 8, Kirchdorf an der Iller, 88457, Germany;48.0465877;10.1228444;51;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Contemporary;Alexander Ruhland represents the fourth generation of his family to run this traditional country inn, and his kitchen turns out top-notch dishes. He combines classic and modern influences, with the region and the seasons playing a major role. Modern and comfortable guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5975;Poppenborg's Stübchen;Germany;Harsewinkel;Brockhäger Straße 9, Harsewinkel, 33428, Germany;51.9630813;8.227436;89;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This is the more relaxed alternative to Poppenborg's more traditional eatery. Try the Atlantic sea wolf with mustard sauce or the Westphalian-style boiled top-side of veal. Pretty garden terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5977;Zur Krone;Germany;Großheubach;Miltenberger Straße 1, Großheubach, 63920, Germany;49.7249645;9.2250855;24;true;true;Farm to table;In the centre of the village you will find this charming restaurant with its comfortable dining rooms. Ralf Restel serves simple, flavoursome regional fare with international influences. Try the boiled rump of beef with herb sauce and pan-fried potatoes or the breast of corn-fed chicken with stir-fried vegetables and curry sauce. In summer the best tables are those outside on the quiet leafy terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5978;Nil;Germany;Hamburg;Neuer Pferdemarkt 5, Hamburg, 20359, Germany;53.5563348;9.9632635;80;true;false;International;Diners are bound to enjoy their time here! This restaurant in the trendy Schanze district has a delightful ambience, the service is informal and friendly, and you can certainly expect to eat well. The delicious food follows the seasons and draws on international influences. Opt for the five-course set menu. Excellent and reasonably priced short wine list.;Terrace;[]
5979;Gasthaus Egertal;Germany;Weissenstadt;Wunsiedler Straße 49, Weissenstadt, 95163, Germany;50.0994638;11.8892982;22;true;true;Country cooking, International;The Rupprecht family have brought together two concepts in their attractive traditional guesthouse: the elegant restaurant and the bistro serve the same menu. It features freshly prepared dishes with regional and classical influences. Most of the fruit and vegetables are home grown. The terrace out front is lovely in summer.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5980;Wirtsstube im Hotel Burkhard;Germany;Wernberg-Köblitz;Marktplatz 10, Wernberg-Köblitz, 92533, Germany;49.539115;12.161095;51;true;false;Country cooking, Home Cooking;In the second restaurant of the hotel Landgasthof Burkhard, the cuisine is somewhat simpler, which does not detract from the quality. Dishes range from cordon bleu to sea bream with lemon. The dining areas are cosy and prettily done out – you can choose to enjoy your meal in the Wirtsstube or the Esszimmer. The inner courtyard terrace, which is shared with the Kaminstube, is also very appealing.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5982;Long March Canteen;Germany;Berlin;Wrangelstraße 20, Berlin, 10997, Germany;52.5029341;13.4310576;98;false;true;Chinese, Cantonese;Currently one of "the" places to eat, Long March offers a dimly lit interior, informal service and a kitchen open to the diners’ gaze. The menu features Cantonese fare in the form of a variety of dim sum and dumpling dishes. Wide selection of wines, spirits, cocktails and tall drinks.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
5983;Landgasthaus Hirsch;Germany;Winterbach;Kaiserstraße 8, Winterbach, 73650, Germany;48.7848281;9.448115;48;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;The Waldenmaier family (now in their fourth generation) cook excellent, seasonal, regional fare at their traditional country inn. The game is locally hunted, the bread comes from the little bakery next door, and even the schnapps is home distilled. There is also a pretty terrace on the first floor and a lovely rustic beer garden.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5986;Landgenuss;Germany;Blieskastel;Bliestalstraße 110a, Blieskastel, 66440, Germany;49.2362907;7.2693778;29;false;true;Country cooking, International;Run by the Hämmerle family, this restaurant enjoys great popularity, so it is advisable to book well in advance! With a friendly country house feel, charming service and great food, this place is a nice alternative to the gourmet restaurant. Made with plenty of local produce, the dishes served here are seasonal with occasional Mediterranean touches. The wide-ranging menu includes their "Original Wiener schnitzel" and sea bass with rosemary and thyme. In summer, make a beeline for the terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5987;Bergfriedel;Germany;Bühlertal;Haabergstraße 23, Bühlertal, 77830, Germany;48.6831695;8.188156;38;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This establishment has been run by the same family with great dedication for years! The welcoming team serves delicious, fresh food that diners can enjoy as they take in the views over the Bühlertal. They follow a philosophy that is close to nature - and their own chickens in the garden fit in nicely. The wide-ranging menu includes traditional cuisine from Baden, vegetarian/vegan dishes and gourmet specialities. Add to that an extensive wine list. The chic restaurant extension is done out in a modern take on regional style. Pleasant overnight accommodation is available – the rooms and suites ("Natur-Zimmer" and "Natur-Suiten") are done out in locally sourced materials and are contemporary in their design.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5988;Gasthof Brink;Germany;Hövelhof;Allee 38, Hövelhof, 33161, Germany;51.8200985;8.657648;61;false;false;Classic French;A place with charm! The traditional style that is cultivated here will evoke childhood memories for many diners. Family-run since 1880, the restaurant serves classic French cuisine that is down to earth and delicious. The pleasant setting has an elegant feel. The house-made pâtés and terrines are just as popular as the saddle of veal with Béarnaise sauce or the sole meunière.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
5989;Hirsch;Germany;Ellwangen;Maierstraße 2, Ellwangen, 73479, Germany;48.9551532;10.1607622;52;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;"Modern tavern cuisine" is the name of the game in this family-run establishment, which has been in business for 12 generations in a quiet suburb of Ellwangen. At the helm is the son, Dennis Wiche, who has worked in several MICHELIN-starred restaurants. The menu comprises an abundance of appealing dishes, from regional classics such as Zwiebelrostbraten (roast beef with onions) and spaetzle to the chef's more modern creations, such as vitello forello. Be sure to try the house-made maultaschen! The chefs work only with the finest seasonal and regional produce – in fact, the restaurant had its own farm until a few years ago. In summer, you can dine on the terrace, which is sheltered from the wind. Overnight accommodation is available on site, in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5990;Zur Glocke;Germany;Höchstädt an der Donau;Friedrich-von-Teck-Straße 12, Höchstädt an der Donau, 89420, Germany;48.6122434;10.567242;79;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;The Stoiber family have put their heart and soul into running this trendy, modern restaurant. Their commitment is particularly evident in the excellent cuisine, which sticks close to the seasons and draws on quality ingredients. There are two set menus, one of them vegetarian, but you can also dine à la carte from the small menu of the day. The terrace in the front garden is ideal for warm summer days, and there are modern guestrooms ranging from "classic" to "design".;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5991;Zum Fischer am See;Germany;Prien am Chiemsee;Harrasser Straße 145, Prien am Chiemsee, 83209, Germany;47.8465515;12.3698336;15;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine;The name says it all. As soon as you set foot in the small entrance hall you are greeted by a picture of various freshwater fish, and the kitchen specialises in fish dishes. However, the well-curated menu also includes steaks, regional classics such as braised ox cheek, and vegetarian options. The grappa and brandy selection is really impressive and might tempt you to stay for a nightcap. In fine weather, the best spot is the terrace with a view of the lake – small boats can also moor there. Good overnight accommodation available. Motorists will be pleased to know there is a large private car park.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5992;Hirsch & Jägerstüberl - Ostiner Stub'n;Germany;Gmund am Tegernsee;Schlierseer Straße 60, Gmund am Tegernsee, 83703, Germany;47.7456562;11.7608816;28;true;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;This typical regional inn proposes two separate culinary concepts: The fine dining restaurant is open Fri to Sun evenings, and the more rustic Hirsch & Jägerstüberl is open Wed to Fri from 6pm and Sat to Sun 12-2.30pm and 6-9.30pm. The emphasis is on produce from the region, and the dishes take their cue from the changing seasons. The fine dining restaurant also serves set menus. Attentive service. In summer, tables on the lovely terrace overlooking the garden are much in demand.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5993;Schwarzkopf;Germany;Frammersbach;Lohrer Straße 80, Frammersbach, 97833, Germany;50.0610785;9.4770678;59;false;false;Country cooking;Run by Stefan Pumm and his charming wife Anja, this restaurant serves fresh, tasty cuisine including chateaubriand steak with Béarnaise sauce (for two), a popular house speciality. Elegant wood-panelled dining room, inviting terrace, plus good accommodation also available (ask for one of the refurbished rooms).;Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
5994;Schäck's Adler;Germany;Elzach;Waldkircher Straße 2, Elzach, 79215, Germany;48.2135468;8.1420419;63;false;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Christoph and Sandra Schäck have brought to life this picture-perfect hotel. The atmosphere in the wood-panelled dining rooms is really cosy, the service is very friendly, the cuisine is ambitious and tasty – the emphasis is on regional ingredients and seasonal produce. There is also the appealing Strumbel Bar and a number of extremely well-kept rooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5996;Gasthaus Weißenbeck;Germany;Bergkirchen;Ludwig-Thoma-Straße 56, Bergkirchen, 85232, Germany;48.2786488;11.3848389;38;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;You will find plenty of satisfied customers here, and no wonder! The mother and daughter Weissenbeck team cook up a storm using regional and seasonal produce – and the prices are fair. The lovely inn also makes for a cosy setting, and in summer the delightful garden terrace is most inviting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
5997;Zum Rebstock;Germany;Kappelrodeck;Kutzendorf 1, Kappelrodeck, 77876, Germany;48.5816292;8.1051264;58;true;true;Country cooking;A fun place to eat! This handsome historical half-timbered house has been in the same family since 1750. Sit back in the delightful wood-panelled interior as the cordial front-of-house team brings out really good Baden cuisine, which can also be enjoyed on the terrace in summer. The menu includes dishes such as pikeperch-salmon dumplings, and stuffed guinea fowl breast with a chive cream sauce to whet your appetite. Tip: Sample the tempting little starters and desserts (look for the "Versucherle" sections on the menu)! With some 500 labels, the wine list is excellent. To take home: house-made cherry and plum brandies. The establishment also has well-kept guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
5998;ROSE;Germany;Hayingen;Aichelauer Straße 6, Hayingen, 72534, Germany;48.3198901;9.432333;74;false;true;Organic, Country cooking;The Tress family is all about organic produce, with a vegetarian and vegan take on regional cuisine taking centre stage. The complex, aromatic and carefully considered dishes win diners over with their depth of flavour – the pea and broad bean tartare, for instance, make a lasting impression. Meat can be ordered as a side dish – here, they follow the principle of nose-to-tail eating. All the wines are Demeter-certified. Should you wish to stay over, there is the guesthouse opposite.;Car park;[]
6001;Harmonie;Germany;Lichtenberg;Schloßberg 2, Lichtenberg, 95192, Germany;50.3844114;11.6790915;40;false;true;Country cooking;This charming building dating from 1823 has not shed its traditional character – lovely old wood panelling makes it really cosy! Here you will get to enjoy friendly service and regional, seasonal dishes, such as braised leg of venison. At the entrance you can sneak a peek into the kitchens.;Terrace;[]
6003;Zum Goldenen Anker;Germany;Eggenstein-Leopoldshafen;Hauptstraße 16, Eggenstein-Leopoldshafen, 76344, Germany;49.0795086;8.3898405;33;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Not only does this 18C hotel offer a comfortable stay (opt for one of the newer guestrooms), it is also a popular modern take on a rural restaurant. Diners are waited on by a friendly front-of-house team in an attractive modern setting with a rustic touch. The food is flavoursome, fresh and seasonal. The main courses are also available in smaller portions. In summer, make a beeline for the gorgeous terrace to the rear of the building.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6004;HENNE.Weinbar;Germany;Cologne;Pfeilstraße 31, Cologne, 50672, Germany;50.9377245;6.9415735;35;true;true;International;Set in the heart of the old town, Hendrik ("Henne") Olfen's appealing bistro-style restaurant has a pleasantly laid-back atmosphere – and it's really popular! Likewise, the excellent food, which represents great value for money, goes down just as well! There is a simple menu at lunchtime and, in the evening, a range of modern, seasonal tapas-style plates that are ideal for sharing. Decent wine list. Delightful little courtyard terrace.;Terrace;[]
6005;Flux - Biorestaurant Werratal;Germany;Hann. Münden;Buschweg 40, Hann. Münden, 34346, Germany;51.4024615;9.7159871;72;false;true;Country cooking;Unpretentious, natural, simple and honest – that's the motto here. The dishes, which are created using organic seasonal produce sourced from the region wherever possible, are packed with flavour. The menu is vegan/vegetarian, but meat and fish can be ordered as add-ons. Gluten- and lactose-free options are also available. In summer, the garden is idyllic. Cosy guestrooms at Biohotel Werratal.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6006;Seehof;Germany;Immenstaad am Bodensee;Bachstraße 15, Immenstaad am Bodensee, 88090, Germany;47.66363;9.36679;41;true;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Boasting a lovely lakeside location on the marina, this restaurant offers a popular terrace as well as its “Badische Weinstube” and panoramic “Alois” dining rooms. Flavourful and classic artisan dishes feature on the menu. Tip: the local classics ("Alemannische Klassiker"). Accommodation is also available – the “boathouse” and rooms with views are particularly recommended.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6007;Zur Flottbeker Schmiede;Germany;Hamburg;Baron-Voght-Straße 79, Hamburg, 20038, Germany;53.5566991;9.8649527;79;false;false;Portuguese, Mediterranean Cuisine;Experience a slice of Portugal in Hamburg! The setting, a heritage-protected historical forge, exudes traditional German charm with its authentic decor and period open fireplace. It makes for a pleasantly laid-back atmosphere in which to tuck into delicious tapas, freshly made with no fuss. The chef-patron serves up genuine Portuguese cuisine with the occasional South American twist. Try, for example, her "barbecued calamari, marinade, garlic" or quesadillas with braised short rib, cheese and guacamole. The well-curated wine list is dedicated to Portuguese labels.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6008;Feilmeiers Landleben;Germany;Windorf;Schwarzhöring 14, Windorf, 94575, Germany;48.6694807;13.224184;87;true;false;Country cooking, International;This cosy and modern restaurant knows how to makes diners feel welcome. For Johann (who goes by Hans) Feilmeier, his "country life" cooking reflects both a love of his native region and a sense of duty. He cooks regionally and seasonally inspired food. Choose from one of the different set menus or order à la carte. Extremely charming and cordial service - matching wine advice included. Tip: the home-made jams!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6009;Weinhaus Stern;Germany;Bürgstadt;Hauptstraße 23, Bürgstadt, 63927, Germany;49.7147426;9.269194;80;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;A popular address and deservedly so: an inviting, rustic-style interior, a pretty courtyard, friendly service and, last but not least, good seasonal cuisine. Chef Klaus Markert relies on honest craftsmanship and flavours, along with fine wines from the region. Be sure to try the house brandy production. Charming guestrooms are also available, and there are home-made fruit jams for breakfast.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6010;Felsenbirne;Germany;Pirna;Lange Straße 34, Pirna, 01796, Germany;50.9632126;13.9430546;46;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant with a friendly atmosphere and a sleek modern interior is located on a cobbled street in the pretty old town, not far from the Elbe. Chef-patron Felix Mikulla uses seasonal ingredients – his dishes are fresh and delicious, as well as good value. The menu also includes vegetarian and vegan options. In summer, diners can make the most of the terrace in the inner courtyard.;Terrace;[]
6011;Alte Posthalterei;Germany;Zorneding;Anton-Grandauer-Straße 9, Zorneding, 85604, Germany;48.0836356;11.8226984;17;true;true;Farm to table;Regional and seasonal cuisine is served in the delightful interior of this long-established, family-run restaurant. On the menu, classics such as trout meunière, Wiener schnitzel, and beef tenderloin goulash Stroganoff whet the appetite. For those who like to dine al fresco, a cosy beer garden nestles in the shade of the chestnut trees. There are beautiful, spacious guestrooms available for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6012;Gasthaus Wolters - Zur Börse;Germany;Wurster Nordseeküste;In der Langen Straße 22, Wurster Nordseeküste, 27639, Germany;53.6502273;8.5089243;57;true;false;Country cooking;Formerly a livestock exchange, this appealing inn is steeped in tradition. Behind the typical brick and half-timbered façade, tables are laid out in a pleasingly rural interior where diners enjoy a quality take on regional home-style cooking made using excellent produce. Friendly service completes the picture. Be sure to reserve your table – the Gasthaus Wolters tends to get booked up.;;[]
6013;Gasthaus Stromberg;Germany;Waltrop;Dortmunder Straße 5, Waltrop, 45731, Germany;51.623505;7.397321;89;true;true;Farm to table;This old-established restaurant in the pedestrian zone offers minimalist-style and a friendly atmosphere as traditional meets modern. The food is seasonal and regional – try the pumpkin variations with Dorstener goat’s cheese or the beef roulade with speck and curly kale. Werkstatt, just 1. 5km away, is ideal for groups.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6014;Talblick;Germany;Wildberg;Bahnhofsträßle 6, Wildberg, 72218, Germany;48.6235613;8.7449979;55;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Brothers Claus and Rainer Weitbrecht are carrying on the tradition of their parents' business – the dedication of the whole family is palpable. As head chef, Claus Weitbrecht delights diners with both Swabian and international cuisine, including vegetarian dishes. The craftsmanship and harmonious flavours are excellent in equal measure. There is also a well-curated wine list. For a more upscale alternative, head to the hotel's Gourmetrestaurant. Comfortable guestrooms available.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6015;Gasthaus Ödenturm;Germany;Cham;Am Ödenturm 11, Cham, 93413, Germany;49.210919;12.7038514;20;false;false;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;As if straight out of a picture book, this beautiful inn stands on the edge of the forest. Diners can look forward to a friendly, family atmosphere and great food, which can also be enjoyed out on the delightful terrace. The dishes on the menu range from regional to Mediterranean. Whether you order steak, fish or local game, there is something for everyone. Modern yet cosy guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6017;Altdeutsches Restaurant;Germany;Dinkelsbühl;Weinmarkt 3, Dinkelsbühl, 91550, Germany;49.0694959;10.318943;99;false;true;Farm to table, Contemporary;Florian Kellerbauer's kitchen philosophy centres on quality ingredients, with a strong commitment to regional and seasonal sourcing. Diners can opt for a set menu – either with meat or vegetarian – comprising four, five or six courses. You can also order à la carte. The service is friendly, attentive and professional. The restaurant occupies a prime spot in the historical centre – Kirche St Georg just opposite is well worth a visit. For overnight stays, there is Hotel Deutsches Haus, a patrician house dating from 1440, or in the Ehemalige Sparkasse, both just 50m away.;Terrace;[]
6018;Weisses Rössl;Germany;Wasserburg am Inn;Herrengasse 1, Wasserburg am Inn, 83512, Germany;48.0609441;12.2316393;79;false;true;Regional Cuisine, International;Standing in the heart of the beautiful old town is this house with a strikingly painted facade. The many regulars appreciate the pleasant, contemporary-rural ambience, charming service and fresh, tasty dishes, such as marinated salmon with wasabi and cucumber or braised venison with bread dumplings and vegetables. Small terrace in summer.;Terrace;[]
6019;ElbUferei;Germany;Dresden;Leipziger Straße 29, Dresden, 01097, Germany;51.0681599;13.7300956;98;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, International;This friendly restaurant with a gorgeous terrace, bar and open kitchen is just outside the centre, on the Elbe Cycle Route. The atmosphere here, on the ground floor of ARCOTEL HafenCity, is pleasantly laid back, and the modern decor has a maritime feel. The food is predominantly Mediterranean (served à la carte or as a set menu) along with light bites and steaks. Mouthwatering options include dishes such as Arctic char, potato, fennel, mustard and sauerkraut.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6020;Schatzhauser;Germany;Baiersbronn;Tonbachstraße 237, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5368854;8.3582767;86;false;false;International, Regional Cuisine;Another iteration of the Finkbeiner family's Traube Tonbach suite of restaurants. The interior is minimalist and modern, airy and light, with a terrace boasting a great view of the valley. They serve a pleasant mix of international cuisine, seasonal dishes and regional classics, plus steaks cooked on the Lavastein grill. The service courtesy of well-trained staff is very friendly. Incidentally, the place is named after the good forest spirit from a Black Forest fairy tale.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6021;Kaufmann's;Germany;Gersfeld;Schloßplatz 11, Gersfeld, 36129, Germany;50.4519841;9.920434;34;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, International;In this lovingly renovated former castle brewery, nowadays the name of the game is good, fresh cuisine. In an attractive setting of exposed old brickwork, vaulted ceilings and sleek, modern style, the restaurant serves flavoursome dishes with a regional dimension as well as international influences. For example, Rhön trout is served all year round, along with seasonal dishes such as braised haunch of venison.;Car park;[]
6022;Die Bürgermeisterei 1728;Germany;Mühlhausen;Untermarkt 13, Mühlhausen, 99974, Germany;51.2071694;10.4596556;89;false;true;Contemporary;A location steeped in history in which to enjoy a meal! The lovingly restored building, which gives directly onto the market square, was once the mayor's residence and dates back to 1728. The elegant fusion of modern style and historical details lends the place atmosphere. The evening menu is ambitious, fresh and full of flavour, with appetising options such as beef bourgignon, dried fig crumble and potato-parsnip mash. The small selection of seasonal dishes is also proposed in the form of set menus, one of which is vegetarian. In summer, make the most of the secluded terrace.;Terrace;[]
6023;Lotters Wirtschaft - Tausendgüldenstube;Germany;Aue - Bad Schlema;Altmarkt 1, Aue - Bad Schlema, 08280, Germany;50.5864623;12.7016902;53;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Hotel Blauer Engel not only offers lovely guestrooms, it is also home to this restaurant. With 360 years of tradition to its name, it oozes historical charm. Warm wood panelling lends the space a cosy atmosphere, and the old tiled stove is a quaint detail. Added to that is service with a personal touch and very good food – to be sampled à la carte or in set menu form. Lotters Wirtschaft brewery is also pleasant with its rustic-style vaulted ceiling.;Car park;[]
6024;Bistro;Germany;Aachen;Benediktusplatz 12, Aachen, 52076, Germany;50.728385;6.183315;21;false;false;Classic Cuisine;It's no wonder the charming restaurant in this spruce historical building is so popular: the food here is unpretentious and packed with flavour! The combination of a modern yet cosy interior and genuine, personable service overseen by the owner fosters a truly pleasant and welcoming atmosphere. The small terrace overlooking the church and market square is also lovely. At lunchtime there is a small a la carte option or a three-course meal deal and in the evening the  ‘St Benedict’ gourmet menu.;Terrace;[]
6025;Barra;Germany;Berlin;Okerstraße 2, Berlin, 12049, Germany;52.4743643;13.4270437;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Be careful not to overlook the house with the inconspicuous front! A thoroughly and unabashedly trendy concept, from the minimalist urban look and relaxed, pleasantly neighbourly atmosphere to the nicely pared-down modern cuisine served in the form of small sharing dishes. High-quality ingredients with a preference for those sourced in the region. Tip: From the seats at the counter you have a very good view of what's happening at the cooker.;Counter dining;[]
6026;November Brasserie;Germany;Berlin;Husemannstraße 15, Berlin, 10435, Germany;52.5383116;13.4174949;25;false;false;Japanese;This Japanese brasserie in a bustling neighbourhood of Prenzlauer Berg entices diners with an interesting range of Japanese specialities in the evenings – including sushi and sashimi, of course. The flambéed toro nigiri, for example, is a treat. Other draws of this place include competent service courtesy of a friendly and down-to-earth front-of-house team, and the pleasingly bright and modern minimalist-style interior, complete with a small sushi counter, where you can see the chefs at work. In summer, the outdoor tables shaded by trees are highly coveted.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6028;Poststuben;Germany;Meerfeld;Meerbachstraße 24, Meerfeld, 54531, Germany;50.0938388;6.7555967;81;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;It is hardly surprising that this restaurant is so popular. As well as charming and attentive service, diners are drawn by the regionally influenced cuisine conjured up by chef-patron Sven Molitor. Made using carefully selected ingredients, his dishes reveal talent and good craftsmanship. They are down-to-earth, but also show a certain finesse here and there. On the menu, for example, the delicious spinach and cheese dumplings will whet your appetite. The likeable traditional family-run hotel Die Post offers well-kept, contemporary guestrooms for overnight stays – an ideal base for exploring the beautiful surroundings of the village, which is located in the Meerfelder Maar volcanic crater.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6029;Rotes Ross;Germany;Marktbergel;Würzburger Straße 3, Marktbergel, 91613, Germany;49.4415641;10.3640408;89;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;If you are a fan of fresh and seasonal regional cuisine, the Bogner family's restaurant will be right up your street. This place is cosy and the service comes courtesy of friendly and well-drilled waitstaff managed by the lady of the house. As for the wine, the focus is also on the region. In summer, the leafy courtyard terrace is in great demand. You can also spend the night in one of the well-kept, comfortable guestrooms.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6030;Zum Falken;Germany;Adelshofen;Tauberzell 41, Adelshofen, 91587, Germany;49.4477924;10.1152199;62;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Lars Zwick has been running this cosy, rustic-style inn in the charming Tauber Valley for many years. The cuisine is regional and seasonal, and the excellent produce is sourced locally as far as possible. Freshly prepared sausages (made in-house) are served on Thursdays and Fridays. Some of the wines – to pair with delicious dishes such as rack of lamb in a herb crust – come from the restaurant's own vineyard. They also produce their own fruit brandies and keep bees. The old barn serves as a function room and wine tastings are held in the vaulted cellar. The pretty guestrooms exude rural charm.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6031;AS am See;Germany;Bad Saarow;Seestraße 9, Bad Saarow, 15526, Germany;52.2919473;14.0614399;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;"AS" refers to the lakeside location (am See) as well as to owner and head chef Andreas Staack. In this inviting cross between a wine bar and a bistro, the affable chef-patron proposes a modern five-course menu featuring dishes such as venison fillet, wild broccoli, cranberry jus. This restaurant is nestled in a side street in a quiet, leafy residential area, a stone's throw from Kurpark Bad Saarow. Lovely terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6032;Gasthaus Goldener Stern;Germany;Friedberg;Dorfstraße 1, Friedberg, 86316, Germany;48.3242031;11.059657;29;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Run with great dedication by the same family for three generations, this place operates as a traditional gasthaus at lunchtime and as a casual fine dining restaurant in the evening. The attractive interior is modern and cosy. The menu features flavoursome regional and seasonal cuisine that also draws on contemporary influences, with a focus on sustainability. Friendly and adept front-of-house team. The Eichen Loft can be booked for events, and from October to April, the stylish wine shop can be reserved for celebrations (max. 12 people). The pleasant beer garden has a slightly smaller menu.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6033;Stocks Restaurant;Germany;Hamburg;An der Alsterschleife 3, Hamburg, 22399, Germany;53.6681184;10.0911825;68;false;true;International, Seafood;This restaurant is housed in a charming half-timbered building with a thatched roof. The comfortable interior is done out in dark tones that exude an air of chic elegance. Friendly waitstaff serve delicious fish dishes or sushi, and those who prefer meat will also find plenty of tempting options on the menu. There is an additional lunchtime special. Tip: Parking is available to the rear of the building.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6034;Moarwirt;Germany;Dietramszell;Sonnenlängstraße 26, Dietramszell, 83623, Germany;47.8221606;11.5479564;23;false;false;Farm to table, German;Bio-Landhotel Moarwirt is an idyllic escape and on top of that they serve fantastic food! This lovely inn, so typical of the region, boasts a gorgeous interior with modern Alpine-style decor. In this setting, diners tuck into freshly prepared regional cuisine made using predominantly local organic produce. The potato dumplings are a must! The restaurant raises its own chickens and sheep and has a small vegetable and herb garden. In summer, the beer garden overlooking the Isar Valley is the place to be. If you want to stay a little longer, cosy guestrooms are available.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6035;Jägerwirt;Germany;Bad Tölz;Nikolaus-Rank-Straße 1, Bad Tölz, 83646, Germany;47.7994554;11.5750231;59;false;true;Country cooking;With its cosy rustic-style interior, charming service and down-to-earth, flavoursome cuisine, this is the archetypal Bavarian inn at its best. The menu features regional dishes and Mediterranean-influenced options. The chefs make a point of sourcing their ingredients locally and work with trusted producers. Alongside the standard menu, there is a varying menu of the day plus a weekly special. Popular grilled veal and pork hock dishes, as well as goose and duck, are also available if ordered in advance. The rural location is also delightful.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6036;derWaldfrieden;Germany;Todtnau;Dorfstraße 8, Todtnau, 79674, Germany;47.7677871;7.9526309;67;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Run by the Hupfer family, this establishment enjoys a tranquil location on the Herrenschwand high plateau, 1 020m above sea level. Son Volker's culinary expertise shines through in his delectable cuisine, which showcases the finest regional and seasonal ingredients. In addition to set menus (regular or vegan) and à la carte dishes, there is a selection of traditional Black Forest snacks. Pleasant garden terrace. Guestrooms are available in stammHaus and spaHaus.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6037;Gasthof zur Sonne;Germany;Tengen;Hauptstraße 57, Tengen, 78250, Germany;47.7823491;8.6382426;99;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Set directly across from the Swiss border, Gasthof zur Sonne serves fresh, flavoursome cuisine with regional and Mediterranean influences in a country-style setting. Try the emmer risotto with Trollinger and grilled Calabrese salami or the duet of skrei and wild salmon in lemon sauce. The restaurant also offers three simple but beautifully kept guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6038;Knippschild;Germany;Rüthen;Theodor-Ernst-Straße 3, Rüthen, 59602, Germany;51.4520698;8.4233956;36;false;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;With its homely farmhouse furniture this restaurant makes a great first impression. The great regional menu makes an already perfect dining experience even better!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6039;Klösterle Hof;Germany;Bad Rippoldsau;Klösterleweg 2, Bad Rippoldsau, 77776, Germany;48.4259852;8.3300626;35;true;true;Country cooking;Chef Markus Klein and his wife put their heart and soul into running this restaurant. In a charming rustic setting, friendly waitstaff serve delicious regional and seasonal cuisine made using good-quality ingredients. Good to know: Hot meals are available from noon to 8pm. Guestrooms available in three different levels of comfort.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6040;Am Kring - Büschker's Stuben;Germany;Vreden;Kring 6, Vreden, 48691, Germany;52.080968;6.7923156;61;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, International;In the mood for traditional regional dishes like Münsterländer Zwiebelfleisch (beef and onions)? Enjoy your meal in the rustic-style dining room or cosy fireside lounge. In addition, the hotel Am Kring offers modern guestrooms. Attractive location in this village built around the church.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6041;Vetter.;Germany;Stuttgart;Bopserstraße 18, Stuttgart, 70180, Germany;48.7694339;9.1799389;79;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;Located in a residential area, this popular restaurant proposes a pleasant interior in which to tuck into regional classics or Mediterranean dishes. Good, fresh ingredients are skilfully prepared in a refreshingly uncomplicated way. In summer, spaces on the pretty terrace are hotly contested.;Terrace;[]
6042;Gasthaus Hofmann;Germany;Rauhenebrach;Schindelsee 1, Rauhenebrach, 96181, Germany;49.889835;10.6527708;66;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;It is no wonder that this inn run by Bettina Hofmann attracts so many regulars – diners are won over by the cosy, elegantly furnished interior, as well as the exceptional food. Her appetising cuisine is regional, seasonal and dotted with modern influences, and the wines are excellent. In addition, they serve a vegetarian set menu. The service is friendly and well organised. There are also comfortable guestrooms. The eggs served at breakfast are laid by the establishment's own hens!;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6043;Gasthof Berghof - Ursprung;Germany;Presseck;Wartenfels 85, Presseck, 95355, Germany;50.2122699;11.4912483;88;false;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;Rustic wood matched with clean lines and fresh splashes of colour provide an ‘old meets new’ look at this restaurant. The decor is mirrored in Alexander Schütz’s excellent cooking, which comes both as an upmarket set menu or simply a hearty Bratwurst. The delicious food and reasonable prices make dining here a real pleasure.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6045;Tölzer Schießstätte - Hager;Germany;Wackersberg;Kiefersau 138, Wackersberg, 83646, Germany;47.7528472;11.5299634;92;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This gem of a restaurant brimming with traditional Bavarian charm serves exceptional food in an inviting rustic setting. It is understandably popular, so be sure to book well in advance! Andreas and Michaela Hager form a harmonious team and this is clearly reflected in the delicious dishes they craft. Their short menu showcases superb local ingredients in classic dishes such as liver dumpling soup, Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) with horseradish or salmon trout fillet with a mustard sauce. Service comes courtesy of a friendly front-of-house team.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6046;Weinhaus Zum Ritter;Germany;Triefenstein;Rittergasse 2, Triefenstein, 97855, Germany;49.7935249;9.6199383;58;false;true;Country cooking;This converted 500-year-old farmhouse certainly has character. The many regulars come for the cosy atmosphere in the charming dining area (the old Swiss church window draws the eye), the cordial service and, of course, the fresh regional cuisine courtesy of chef-patron Thomas Hausin – his flavoursome dishes are clearly the work of a chef with experience at top-flight establishments! NB: different opening hours in summer.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6047;Landgasthof Rebstock;Germany;Sulzburg;Hauptstraße 77, Sulzburg, 79295, Germany;47.8401758;7.7097437;89;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;In the heart of the wine village, the Keller family runs this cosy, rustic, centuries-old house, where the welcoming hosts offer fresh, seasonally inspired cuisine. They like to use ingredients from the region, but international influences can also be detected on the menu. The service is professional and very attentive. They also have guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6049;Forst's Landhaus;Germany;Riedenburg;Mühlstraße 37b, Riedenburg, 93339, Germany;48.9598278;11.683201;35;false;false;International, Farm to table;Run with great dedication, this restaurant is located by a small stream – tables on the terrace overlooking the water are in great demand! The seasonal menu uses plenty of regional produce, such as lamb from the Bavarian Jura. The vegetarian dishes are also appealing, imaginative and delicious! The friendly maître d' provides good service with a personal touch. There are simple but well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
6050;Landhaus Hohenlohe;Germany;Rot am See;Erlenweg 24, Rot am See, 74585, Germany;49.2543091;10.0192513;57;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Country cooking;This long-standing family business, now with Matthias Mack at the helm, is run according to a winning formula. In a very pleasant informal atmosphere, extremely friendly and experienced waitstaff are always on hand. The delicious food is freshly prepared and feautures regional and international influences. You can compose a three- or four-course set menu from the appealing list of options (also vegetarian) or order à la carte. Appetising dishes include porcini ravioli, baby spinach, Brettenfeld Jerusalem artichokes, truffle fonduta. The restaurant also has its own herb and vegetable garden. Overnight accommodation is available in this well-kept country house nestled in a residential area.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6051;Zur Sonne;Germany;Pappenheim;Deisinger Straße 20, Pappenheim, 91788, Germany;48.9335563;10.9737874;49;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Run by the Glück family, this place serves fantastic seasonal dishes and regional classics. From game to Altmühltal lamb and their unique "Sauerbraten 2.0", the menu is packed with delicious options. With a clear commitment to sustainability and a preference for local produce, the kitchen team serves up dishes that are beautifully balanced in flavour. The bright, modern conservatory is a delightful space, as is the splendid terrace in summer. Comfortable and attractive guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
6052;Gaststube;Germany;Höchst im Odenwald;Rondellstraße 20, Höchst im Odenwald, 64739, Germany;49.81082;8.9810497;26;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Housed inside Krone is this pleasant and down-to-earth restaurant that is also run by the Wölfelschneider family. The Gaststube menu will appeal to those who appreciate traditional regional fare. As well as delicious food, guests can enjoy the friendly service, which contributes to the congenial atmosphere. In summer, the terrace is a dream!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6053;Bärenkrug;Germany;Molfsee;Hamburger Chaussee 10, Molfsee, 24113, Germany;54.2605149;10.0627798;22;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Whether you are seated in the Friesenstube or the secluded courtyard garden with its old chestnut trees and abundant greenery, at the Sierks family's restaurant you can look forward to quality cuisine with a regional and seasonal focus in the form of daily specials, classics or set menus. Tip: Be sure to try the home-made chocolates. The hotel of the same name, also part of this long-standing family business, has attractive, comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6054;Freihardt;Germany;Heroldsberg;Hauptstraße 81, Heroldsberg, 90562, Germany;49.5303657;11.1508744;80;true;false;International, Meats and Grills;Eating here is a real pleasure! The cuisine is international and seasonal, the highlight being the Bavarian beef steaks. They also serve burgers on Wednesdays and Thursdays. Head here on a Saturday for a three-course surprise lunch or on a Sunday for a traditional home-style roast. A friendly atmosphere reigns in the restaurant and its conservatory, and the terrace on the busy street is a place "to see and be seen". Right next door is the restaurant's own butcher's shop, which for many years has employed so-called humane slaughtering methods.;Terrace;[]
6055;Gasthaus Waltz;Germany;Munich;Ickstattstr. 13, Munich, 80469, Germany;48.1280339;11.5731098;98;true;false;Alpine, Regional Cuisine;A fashionable and lively restaurant in Munich's Glockenbachviertel, run by an enthusiastic young team. The secret of its success is the chefs' modern take on Alpine cuisine – sometimes creative, sometimes more traditional, but the presentation is always sharp, and the ingredients are the region's finest. Dishes such as the Tafelspitz-Sülze (jellied prime boiled beef) with horseradish, root vegetables and seed oil vinaigrette or the char with lentils, apple, trout caviar and beurre blanc can be ordered à la carte or together as a set menu comprising four or five courses. Wine is taken very seriously here and, consequently, the list is not only well curated in terms of quality, but also surprisingly extensive. Motorists should note that parking options are limited.;Interesting wine list;[]
6056;Landhotel Krone;Germany;Heitersheim;Hauptstraße 12, Heitersheim, 79423, Germany;47.8718527;7.6616342;55;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;Here, tradition rubs shoulders with current trends in cosy little spaces that feature an attractive blend of old brickwork, wood, steel and glass. The regional and seasonal cuisine is scattered with international influences. Medieval vaulted cellar for events. This family-run business also offers attractive, individually designed guestrooms and wellness facilities.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6057;Kulturhof Stanggass - Gasthaus;Germany;Bischofswiesen;Berchtesgadener Straße 111, Bischofswiesen, 83483, Germany;47.6279549;12.9892627;95;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;The Gasthaus, which annexes the Kulturhof Stanggass located on the road between Bischofswiesen and Berchtesgaden, offers a culinary alternative to the restaurant Solo Du. Done out in light wood, the minimalist-style interior has a modern yet cosy feel. The glass façade affords views of the garden, which includes a children's playground. Book a spot at the "Stammtisch", a long handmade wooden table for 25 diners. The menu draws on the region and nature's bounty – the ingredients are locally sourced. The good food is complemented by friendly service.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6059;CARUSO Pastabar;Germany;Cologne;Kasparstraße 19, Cologne, 50670, Germany;50.9525104;6.9536473;84;true;false;Italian;Neapolitan-born Anna and Marcello Caruso, working with Emanuele Barbaro, have come up with a cool concept: a flavoursome, relaxed and lively dining experience, played out in a chic atmosphere. Service comes courtesy of a relaxed, attentive team under the tutelage of the charming proprietress. They serve a three-course set menu, which you can put together yourself and add to as you wish – the main course is flavoursome house-made pasta! N.B. You should allow about two hours for three courses. There are two seatings: 6pm and 8.30pm. Trendy drinks at the bar.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6060;Weinstube zum Engel;Germany;Baden-Baden;Mauerbergstraße 62, Baden-Baden, 76534, Germany;48.7220504;8.1834425;42;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;With his Weinstube (or "wine tavern"), Christian Beck, son of the owner of the hotel and restaurant Heiligenstein, also located in Neuweier near Baden-Baden, has brought a new layer of culinary enrichment to the village. The cuisine here comprises regional, seasonal and Mediterranean dishes. Vegetarian dishes and small bites are also available. Regional wines are offered. Friendly service in a cosy interior that blends tradition and modernity. The terrace is also lovely.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6061;Rebblick;Germany;Korb;Brucknerstraße 14, Korb, 71404, Germany;48.8455044;9.3551739;32;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Housed in Korb's Remstalhalle, this restaurant has retained a certain 1970s feel, while incorporating chic modern design features and an attractive glass façade. Jochen Gromann serves up flavoursome seasonal cuisine drawing on regional and international influences (including Swabian Zwiebelrostbraten). Managed by Nadine (his wife), the front-of-house team are friendly and well drilled and provide astute wine recommendations. Delightful terrace – with a view of the vineyards, depending on where you sit.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6062;Regional Friesoythe;Germany;Friesoythe;Gerichtsstraße 14, Friesoythe, 26169, Germany;53.0194997;7.860787;84;true;false;German, Seasonal Cuisine;"Regional" is more than a name here, it is a philosophy! Since September 2022, Timo Plenter and Ina Stuke have been running this traditional restaurant in the centre of town and are completely committed to sustainability. The chef cooks honest flavoursome food, sourcing seasonal ingredients from the region and favours local suppliers. You can choose between a three to five-course menu (also vegetarian) and the 7-course "Signature Dish" menu. The interior decor marries modern and rustic elements. Cordial service from the attentive staff. In summer a few tables are set up in front of the building.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6063;Wirtshaus Mättle;Germany;Lörrach;Freiburger Straße 314, Lörrach, 79539, Germany;47.6264979;7.6563503;44;false;false;Farm to table;Dating from 1848, this inn has been given a tastefully modern makeover. High-quality, market-fresh produce is used to conjure up cuisine that looks to the Mediterranean as well as the local region for inspiration. In addition to à la carte dishes (the whole roasted trout, for instance, is a house speciality), a surprise menu is also on offer - conventional or vegan. Guests also like to come for the reasonably priced 2-course lunch menu. Gorgeous terrace. Located in the basement, bar-cum-restaurant THEODOR is ideal for events.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6064;Salt & Silver Levante;Germany;Hamburg;Hafenstraße 140, Hamburg, 20359, Germany;53.5465467;9.9587661;31;true;true;Middle Eastern;Salt & Silver now boasts a new charming urban restaurant serving Levantine cuisine next door to its Latin American eatery in the St Pauli neighbourhood. Here you dine mezze-style, following the example of the cuisine of the southeastern corner of the Mediterranean: Levant-inspired dishes, both big and small, come together to the table and are made for sharing. To really experience what this place is all about, order the "Yallah-Combo", which is ideal for group dining. Overlooking the harbour, the terrace in front of the building is fabulous in summer.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6067;Landgasthof zum Müller;Germany;Ruderting;Passauer Straße 16, Ruderting, 94161, Germany;48.6535649;13.4081284;52;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;At their established country inn, Ingrid and Markus Buchner serve fresh regional and seasonal cuisine with international and Mediterranean influences – responsible for this is chef Marcel von Winckelmann. The service is friendly and cordial, the rustic-style restaurant rooms are inviting, and the leafy terrace with its small open barn ("Salettl") is delightful. They have modern rural-style guestrooms, too.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6068;Hirsch;Germany;Berghaupten;Dorfstraße 9, Berghaupten, 77791, Germany;48.4063369;7.9883183;85;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This picture-perfect Baden country inn boasts tastefully designed, inviting guestrooms and serves excellent food. The owner's son-in-law runs the kitchen, serving up regional cuisine that showcases seasonal produce – dishes such as braised beef cheeks in a Burgundy sauce or saddle of venison with cranberries and spaetzle are especially popular. Putting the emphasis on flavour and proper seasoning, only the finest and freshest ingredients are used. Charming and professional front-of-house team.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6069;das asam;Germany;Aldersbach;Freiherr-Von-Aretin-Platz 2, Aldersbach, 94501, Germany;48.5878399;13.084969;68;false;true;Farm to table;You dine in the Modlersäle, once the refectory, on the first floor of this former monastery building. It has beautiful high ceilings decorated with lovely mouldings and paintings – the historical setting is tastefully combined with an interior design of clean lines. The food is modern and seasonal, and the tasty Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) is a classic. On warm summer days, the terrace in the cloister garden of the monastery courtyard is idyllic! You can stay overnight in well-kept, simply charming guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6070;Die Krone;Germany;Staufen im Breisgau;Hauptstraße 30, Staufen im Breisgau, 79219, Germany;47.8823684;7.7309961;56;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Chef Volker Lahn continues the family tradition in the kitchen at Die Krone. The cosy Baden setting of the dining rooms is matched by good local Baden cooking. The seasonal fare is available in the form of a set menu or à la carte.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6071;Gasthaus Schwanen;Germany;Stühlingen;Talstraße 9, Stühlingen, 79780, Germany;47.7789467;8.4277185;42;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Now in its third generation, this charming family-run inn opposite the church serves very good food. A cosy atmosphere awaits you inside, while the idyllic garden terrace beckons outside. Here, they keep chickens, hunt game and make schnapps, and their own produce often features on the menu. Accommodation options: Gasthaus Schwanen, Villa Pfarrhus with its beautiful garden, and the Malermeisterhaus guesthouse.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6073;Gutsküche;Germany;Tangstedt;Wulksfelder Damm 15, Tangstedt, 22889, Germany;53.7183731;10.1114846;15;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;It is a real pleasure to see the terrific produce gracing the plates at Gutsküche, just outside Hamburg – this is sustainable gastronomy par excellence! The organic ingredients from their own estate, Hofgut Wulksfelde, are the absolute focal point of the cooking, and the menu features vegetarian dishes that can be supplemented with fish, poultry and meat "garnishes". GUT's caprese with hand-scooped buffalo mozzarella, rocket and tomato pesto, for example, is a marvellous seasonal dish – the wonderful aroma of fully ripe tomatoes remains in the memory! Tip: Snacks can be purchased at GutsDeli and delicatessen shop, as well as organic produce in the on-site farm shop. In summer: organic ice cream in the lovely GutsGarten.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6074;Lohmayr Stub'n;Germany;Piding;Salzburger Straße 13, Piding, 83451, Germany;47.770635;12.9146321;89;false;true;Country cooking;Chef Sebastian Oberholzner puts his heart and soul into his cooking, meaning his delicious dishes are much in demand. He uses seasonal and regional ingredients, making sure to know his suppliers and the origin of the produce. There is also a good selection of wines. Diners enjoy charming service in the setting of a fine historical building.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6075;Sticky Fingers;Germany;Regensburg;Unteren Bachgasse 9, Regensburg, 93047, Germany;49.0191115;12.0948647;82;true;false;Contemporary, Fusion;Located in the beautiful Old Town, this is a fashionable restaurant and bar. The decor and background music are very much on trend and lend this laid-back establishment something of a club atmosphere. The appealing international menu features flavoursome dishes including fish and chips, panzanella and paella – all served by very friendly waitstaff. As well as wines, there is an extensive selection of cocktails, another big draw of this place.;;[]
6076;Auers Schlosswirtschaft;Germany;Neubeuern;Rosenheimer Straße 8, Neubeuern, 83115, Germany;47.7798647;12.1349498;30;false;false;Country cooking;It's no surprise that this restaurant, run with dedication for over 30 years, is so popular! Diners are won over by both the cosy space that is beautifully done out to exude rustic charm and chef Astrid Hilse's fresh cuisine, which takes the form of a menu that changes on a daily basis. Top-notch produce goes into seasonal dishes with a definite wow factor, such as braised lemon chicken with roasted vegetables and garlic potatoes, or local lamb prepared two ways and served with olive confit and green beans. The service is friendly – and the chef, too, gets in on the act. Attractive tree-shaded terrace. N.B. Credit cards are not accepted.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6077;Bauernstuben;Germany;Tiefenbronn;Franz-Josef-Gall-Straße 13, Tiefenbronn, 75233, Germany;48.8243688;8.8011255;37;true;false;Country cooking, International;This cosy rustic-style restaurant is housed in the venerable Ochsen Post. The menu features the traditional cuisines of Baden and Swabia, as well as internationally influenced dishes. Along with Maultaschen, Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) and steaks, there are also less conventional options such as sour kidney or tripe soup. Diners can also look forward to a delightful terrace, attentive service and a well-curated wine list that includes a number of rare gems. Tip: You can purchase their wonderful bread to take home, and some meat dishes are also available for takeaway. Lovely guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6078;MundArt2015;Germany;Teisendorf;Holzhausen 2, Teisendorf, 83317, Germany;47.867175;12.8073996;45;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Located in a beautiful spot not far from Salzburg, the attractive Gut Edermann hotel awaits you with tastefully designed guestrooms and a 2 700m2 spa area, as well as appealing dining options including Bauernstube1910 and MundArt2015. Friendly waitstaff serve up the flavoursome seasonal cuisine in a cosy setting. The preference for locally sourced ingredients reflects the restaurant's commitment to sustainability.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6079;Ramster;Germany;Schneverdingen;Heberer Straße 16, Schneverdingen, 29640, Germany;53.1108686;9.8030252;66;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;An inviting family-run restaurant renowned for its fine seasonal cooking. A deep connection to the region is reflected in the use of predominantly local ingredients. The menu features traditional dishes – the Heidschnucke lamb is a house speciality not to be missed. Some dishes can also be ordered in small portions, and there are vegetarian/vegan options available. Lovely terrace overlooking the garden. For overnight guests there are exceedingly cosy guestrooms, some with balconies.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6080;Graf Everstein;Germany;Polle;Amtstraße 6, Polle, 37647, Germany;51.8982686;9.4073978;54;true;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;The Multhoff family's restaurant draws in diners with the promise of skilfully prepared food and wonderful views over the Weser. The friendly and attentive staff serve up beautifully fresh cuisine that sets great store by both seasonal produce and selected ingredients.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6081;Zur Linde;Germany;Stuttgart;Sigmaringer Straße 49, Stuttgart, 70567, Germany;48.7272899;9.1500891;63;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;The Trautwein brothers run this 300 year-old former posting house with its charming mix of historical and modern decor with great dedication. The menu includes Swabian classics such as Gaisburger Marsch beef stew, maultaschen ravioli and veal tripe with braised oxtail, alongside seasonal offerings. The rustic vaulted cellar is available for events.;Terrace;[]
6082;Landhaus Zum Rössle;Germany;Schwäbisch Hall;Zeilwiesen 5, Schwäbisch Hall, 74523, Germany;49.1377903;9.7855218;53;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;Family tradition since 1780! Here the hospitality extended to diners is just as important as the tasty cuisine made from regional produce. Besides classic dishes, a surprise menu is also served. In summer the garden is a delight! There is a fantastic barn venue for parties. You can also stay overnight.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6083;Landhotel zum Hirsch;Germany;Ostrach;Hauptstraße 27, Ostrach, 88356, Germany;47.9517087;9.3809385;46;false;false;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;This traditional inn dating back over 300 years serves regional cuisine made with seasonal and predominantly locally sourced ingredients. The menu ranges from classics such as Hirschwirts Gaisburger Marsch (a traditional Swabian beef stew) and Swabian tripe ragout to Mediterranean-influenced dishes such as fried Atlantic sea bream fillet with a white wine sauce on bell peppers and courgettes with risotto. This elegant family-run establishment has comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6084;Das August;Germany;Bad Nenndorf;Riepener Straße 21, Bad Nenndorf, 31542, Germany;52.3456;9.33416;25;true;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;It's no wonder this place is so popular! The Gehrke family have made it a point of honour to uphold their long-standing tradition of offering outstanding cuisine, plus friendly service and an inviting atmosphere. The food is fresh, seasonal and made with select ingredients. The menu includes, for example, vegetable curry, roast corn-fed chicken breast with mushrooms or local game. There is also an impressive selection of schnitzels. Well-stocked wine cabinet. Attractive guestrooms at Schmiedegasthaus Gehrke.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6085;Feine Speiseschenke;Germany;Nordhausen;Winkelberg 13, Nordhausen, 99734, Germany;51.5405015;10.8175862;46;true;false;Farm to table, International;This friendly restaurant is located in a small village in a quiet side valley surrounded by woods and meadows. It offers seasonal cuisine bearing regional and international influences. They even raise Scottish Highland cattle here. You can choose from various set menus (including a vegetarian one) or go à la carte and opt for one of the classic dishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6086;Das Fetzwerk;Germany;Oberstdorf;Freibergstraße 21, Oberstdorf, 87561, Germany;47.4053131;10.2707118;82;true;true;International, Country cooking;Das Fetzwerk feels modern and pleasantly uncomplicated - this applies as much to the trendy ambience as the food. Tasty, fresh dishes with a certain pizazz are served here. The service is friendly and attentive. The restaurant is located in the comfortable Das Freiberg hotel. Open from 12 noon. Tip for sunny days: the terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6087;RÖHMS DELI;Germany;Lüneburg;Heiligengeiststraße 30, Lüneburg, 21335, Germany;53.2466189;10.4052931;48;true;false;Farm to table, International;A pleasantly straightforward concept that goes down well with restaurant-goers. The seasonal and internationally influenced cuisine is served in a friendly, modern atmosphere. The à la carte menu is complemented by daily specials on the board. At lunchtime, there is an additional dish of the day. For those with a sweet tooth, the counter displaying fine home-made pastries is a highlight! Attentive service. The terrace – in a traffic-calmed area here in the middle of the city – is also pleasant. There is a pretty holiday apartment for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6088;Die Krone;Germany;Sulzbach-Laufen;Hauptstraße 44, Sulzbach-Laufen, 74429, Germany;48.9635858;9.8463056;100;false;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;Owner and head chef Markus Elison previously worked at Herrengass in Gschwend, where he proved his worth in the kitchen. Here, he cooks up delicious dishes made with high-quality ingredients. His cuisine is regional, with some Mediterranean influences. One of his signature dishes is Zwiebelrostbraten in a Spätburgunder wine sauce with spaetzle. Dine à la carte or opt for the seasonal set menu or "Das Krone Menü". Friendly service. Sleek modern decor. For overnight stays, there are functional yet chic guestrooms available – the prices are lower in the guesthouse.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6089;Am Osterfeuer;Germany;Herford;Hellerweg 35, Herford, 32052, Germany;52.1051544;8.6704785;97;true;true;Regional Cuisine, International;Hans-Jörg Dunker and his team have long been synonymous with quality and Westphalian cuisine with an international twist. The restaurant interior is attractive and cheerful, having been given a skilful modern makeover, but care has been taken to leave the traditional character of the building intact. One of the chef's specialities is the wonderful fish and shellfish soup with aioli, bread and parmesan. A gorgeous terrace for summer.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6090;Schorse im Leineschloss;Germany;Hanover;Hannah-Ahrendt-Platz 1, Hanover, 30159, Germany;52.3700264;9.7338238;19;true;true;International, Regional Cuisine;This pleasantly down-to-earth restaurant is the second in the cube-like extension of the Leineschloss, along with Votum. The flavoursome food is made with select ingredients and draws on French influences, for example pan-fried meagre with Champagne cabbage, grapes and herby mashed potatoes. They also serve a simpler quick lunch set menu. Delightful terraces at the Leinewehr and on Platz der Göttinger Sieben.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6091;Froschgrundsee;Germany;Rödental;Schönstädt 14, Rödental, 96472, Germany;50.3491959;11.03117;23;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This appealing country house lies above a small lake, in the town's Schönstädt neighbourhood. Hannes Scammell shows his culinary mettle, cooking up fresh and tasty seasonal dishes. You can also dine outside. At lunchtime, the menu is somewhat reduced. The good cuisine is complemented by the friendly service provided by the hostess. Barbecue fans, take note: they also organise regular evening events dedicated to grilled meats.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6092;Cube by Mika;Germany;Schwerin;Domhof 6, Schwerin, 19055, Germany;53.6294876;11.416357;32;false;true;Izakaya, Sharing;This trendy and lively spot is in the heart of Schwerin – the cathedral is very close by and the castle is also within easy walking distance. The atmosphere is laid-back and casual in this maisonette-style restaurant occupying two levels, and on the lower floor, diners can choose between high tables or counter seats with views of action in the kitchen. This place specialises in delicious izakaya cuisine – predominantly Asian dishes and finger food for sharing. On certain days, they also propose an ambitious tasting menu. Don't forget to book!;Terrace;[]
6093;Jäger & Lustig;Germany;Berlin;Grünberger Straße 1, Berlin, 10243, Germany;52.5133926;13.4480587;77;false;true;German, Seasonal Cuisine;What a cosy and quaint-feeling place, serving what the owners term "Heimatküche": think hearty, fresh, flavoursome cuisine. Classic German dishes are the stars of the show – game and goose are specialities of the house. They are at pains to use regional ingredients and remain aligned with the seasons. Service courtesy of friendly and competent staff. Make the most of the beer garden in summer.;Terrace;[]
6094;Melkhus;Germany;Bad Malente-Gremsmühlen;Rothensande 1, Bad Malente-Gremsmühlen, 23714, Germany;54.1638261;10.5770158;73;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;The former cowshed of this beautifully renovated historical Immenhof estate houses this charming alternative to the Rodesand restaurant. The cuisine is traditional, regional and seasonal, made with top-quality, fresh produce. The classics on the menu include Holstein-style sour meat and roasted suckling pig ham. Vegetarian options are also available. The food is complemented by friendly service and a cosy, rustic atmosphere – the open fireplace is a nice touch. In summer, make a beeline for the terrace, which overlooks the lake. Coffee and cake are served in the afternoon. Pick up some home-made jam, souvenirs etc at the farm shop.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6096;WurzelWerk;Germany;Großbundenbach;Bergstraße 7, Großbundenbach, 66501, Germany;49.3072308;7.4238434;21;true;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant lives up to its name: Wurzel, meaning "root", signifies a dedication to the local terroir, Werk, meaning "craft", highlights a commitment to artisanal cooking techniques – chef-patron Benjamin Bendzko puts both into practice in his market-fresh cuisine. Exceptional and almost exclusively regional ingredients are used to create flavoursome and pleasingly down-to-earth dishes. Two buildings, built in 1875 as a farmstead, now house a guesthouse (with a café at weekends) and this restaurant, whose rustic charm and pretty decor make for a cosy atmosphere. In summer, the garden terrace is the place to be.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6097;MaMi's;Germany;Berlin;Oderberger Straße 13, Berlin, 10435, Germany;52.5390724;13.4086266;72;false;false;International, Modern Cuisine;Having gained many years of experience in the fine dining sector, brother-and-sister team Marcel and Miriam Hertrampf have opened this laid-back little restaurant. The location alone is great: the street lined with tall trees and buzzing with a lively atmosphere has a charm all of its own – the terrace on the wide pavement is especially inviting. In the kitchen, patron Marcel serves up flavoursome modern fusion cuisine, drawing on a wealth of culinary influences from Spanish to Asian, with or without meat. There is also a sharing menu comprising eight or ten small dishes. The service team led by hostess Miriam is charming and professional. She is a professionally trained sommelier and will be happy to guide you through the wine list, which features around 200 different labels.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6098;Berggasthof Schlüssel;Germany;Zell im Wiesental;Pfaffenberg 2, Zell im Wiesental, 79669, Germany;47.7340022;7.8695107;17;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;This mountain inn dating back over a hundred years is located at an altitude of 700m in the district of Pfaffenberg. Your dedicated hosts propose regional dishes that are in tune with the seasons and peppered with modern touches, to be savoured in cosy dining rooms with plenty of rustic charm. If you fancy a bottle of wine with your meal, why not stay over in the well-kept guestrooms?;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6099;Dorfstuben;Germany;Baiersbronn;Hermine-Bareiss-Weg 1, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5206318;8.3269829;96;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;The two charming farmhouse dining rooms (the "Clock Room" and the "Förster Jakob Room", which date back to the 19C, have been lovingly and authentically decorated down to every last detailare. Extremely cordial waitresses in traditional dirndl attire serve excellent seasonal and regional cuisine, including game from the hotel's own hunting grounds and trout from its fish farm. The braised beef roulade in Pinot Noir sauce is equally tempting. "Dorfstuben Classics" such as, such as the Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) with maultasche and sauerkraut are also popular, not to mention the wonderful apple cakes! Tip: Take a look at the set menu of the day.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6100;Alter Esel;Germany;Marktbreit;Marktstraße 10, Marktbreit, 97340, Germany;49.6675364;10.1436967;67;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;The couple who run this restaurant put everything they have into creating a warm atmosphere and serving seasonal cuisine that draws on regional and Mediterranean influences. The set menu also comes in a vegetarian version. In addition to the cosy, lovingly decorated dining area inside, there are a handful of outdoor tables affording views of the historical buildings of this charming little town. This business is a Slow Food member and is committed to sustainability.;Terrace;[]
6101;Michels Stern;Germany;Marktbreit;Bahnhofstraße 9, Marktbreit, 97340, Germany;49.6656949;10.1433009;55;false;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;The Michel family have always run their restaurant with great dedication, and now the fourth generation is at the helm. Two brothers make this an experience to remember: Wolfgang draws on good produce to cook tasty dishes ranging from traditional home-style fare to refined cuisine. Stefan will be delighted to recommend the right Franconian wine to go with your food. Plus well-kept guestrooms.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6102;Funky Fisch;Germany;Berlin;Kantstraße 135, Berlin, 10625, Germany;52.5059106;13.3171625;77;false;false;Asian and Western, International;Are you in the mood for fish of the uncomplicated and Asian-inspired variety? Then head to the trendy and lively Funky Fisch by The Duc Ngo. The centrepiece is the large fish counter, where you choose the fish you want to eat, which is then prepared in the open kitchen. A wide range of Asian food, from Chinese to Vietnamese, is served, with influences from all over the world.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6103;Speisemeisterei Burgthalschenke;Germany;Vöhringen;Untere Hauptstraße 4, Vöhringen, 89269, Germany;48.2879519;10.0992619;57;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The Großhammer family has been renowned for its good cooking for years! Diners can choose between the set menu or classic dishes. The cuisine follows the seasons, with ingredients being sourced in the local area. Laid out over three levels, the restaurant also has a lovely terrace. On a practical note: large car park.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6104;Zum Kreuz;Germany;Sankt Märgen;Hohlengraben 1, Sankt Märgen, 79274, Germany;47.9765364;8.1290991;44;false;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;This inn has existed since 1683. Matthias Schwer is the 4th generation of the family to carry on the tradition. Here, just outside St Märgen at an altitude of approx. 1 030m, a father-and-son team cook up quality seasonal fare, including local game, and classics such as maultaschen and schnitzel. There is an à la carte menu, the "Tradition" set menu and the vegetable "Gemussmenü" (only by ordering in advance). Comfortable guestrooms and holiday apartments for overnight guests.;Car park;[]
6105;Sternenschanz;Germany;Ötisheim;Gottlob-Linck-Straße 2, Ötisheim, 75443, Germany;48.9659729;8.8139015;78;true;true;Home Cooking, Country cooking;A fun dining experience! The Linck family put their heart and soul into running this delightful restaurant. Diners can look forward to friendly service and the chance to eat really well without breaking the bank. The menu focuses on Swabian fare and home-style cooking, with dishes such as Flädlesuppe (pancake soup) and creamy veal goulash. No wonder there are so many regulars! In summer, the gorgeous garden terrace beckons.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6106;Das Jagdhaus;Germany;Oberstdorf;Ludwigstraße 13, Oberstdorf, 87561, Germany;47.4053722;10.2771504;34;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Built in 1856, this charming timber house with three dining areas is a really pleasant alternative to the other restaurants run by the Bolkart-Fetz family in Oberstdorf. Only ingredients sourced from within Germany – and preferably from the region – go into the dishes on the traditional menu, including some excellent game options. As well as the three- or four-course "Prinzregentenmenü", there is a range of à la carte dishes to choose from. Very nice selection of wines. Head for the lovely beer garden shaded by chestnut trees.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6107;Lamm;Germany;Muggensturm;Hauptstraße 24, Muggensturm, 76461, Germany;48.866959;8.2789106;76;false;false;International, Country cooking;A tasteful, modern interior incorporating a sleek design, premium materials and warm tones goes hand in hand with the hospitality of a traditional inn. The menu whets the appetite with an interesting array of regional and international dishes, such as roast Angus beef served with two kinds of onions, warm potato salad and maultaschen>/i> (Swabian dumplings) sautéed in butter or Barbary duck breast accompanied by stir-fried Asian vegetables and Himalayan basmati rice. The five different set menus, which include a vegan one, are also excellent. A very popular establishment – book early if you are looking to come at the weekend!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6108;Stumpenhof;Germany;Plochingen;Am Stumpenhof 1, Plochingen, 73207, Germany;48.7165279;9.4297146;94;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;It's impossible not to feel comfortable when you're in such good hands! The service in this long-standing family business is exceptionally friendly, and the owner herself always has a smile and a friendly word for her guests. The menu has something for everyone, from affordable lunch set menus and daily specials to traditional regional dishes and light bites. Lovely terrace.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace;[]
6109;MEIER;Germany;Pilsach;Hilzhofen 18, Pilsach, 92367, Germany;49.3014799;11.5956557;46;false;false;Country cooking;This restaurant in a fabulous countryside location boasts a delightful garden and terrace. Inside, the decor is a winning blend of tradition and modernity. The Meier family also runs the gorgeous HILZHOF, a hotel with chic guestrooms, and the compact fine dining restaurant HIO. At MEIER, the really delicious cuisine perfectly reflects a house motto that translates as "the field cooks". They make use of organic produce sourced from the region or even from their own vegetable field or herb garden. Culinary pleasure and sustainability go hand in hand here. Charming front-of-house team.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6110;Gasthof Blumenthal;Germany;Spalt;Stiegelmühle 42, Spalt, 91174, Germany;49.197343;10.8870968;23;true;false;Country cooking;A family business in its fifth generation, this is all you could wish for from a Franconian inn. The interior is cosy and the beer garden, which is largely sheltered from the elements, is fabulous. Served in a pleasingly laid-back and extremely charming atmosphere, the menu features down-to-earth, unfussy dishes that are big on flavour and showcase the kitchen team's craftsmanship and good-quality regional and seasonal ingredients. Tip: They breed their own char and trout!;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6111;Gasthof Alpenrose;Germany;Samerberg;Kirchplatz 2, Samerberg, 83122, Germany;47.7762313;12.2336919;26;true;false;Country cooking;This lovely, long-established restaurant is always busy and has a loyal following of regulars. Located close to the church, it has been run by the same family since 1868. Inside it has comfortable dining nooks, outside a secluded beer garden and terrace. The seasonal Bavarian cuisine often draws on ingredients sourced from the surrounding area. Charming guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6112;Kamin- und Bauernstube;Germany;Bad Peterstal;Dollenberg 3, Bad Peterstal, 77740, Germany;48.4576319;8.2506409;72;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Among the dining options at the exclusive Hotel Dollenberg, you can choose to eat in the cosy, rustic-style Bauernstube, the elegant fireside Kaminstube or out on the wonderful spacious terrace – both the terrace and the Kaminstube offer beautiful views of the Black Forest. Whichever space you opt for, you can look forward to high-quality regional and international cuisine. There are various choice set menus and an a la carte offer. A favourite: the set menu of the week. The excellent wine list served in the fine dining restaurant is also available here!;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6113;Zur Linde;Germany;Oberboihingen;Nürtinger Straße 24, Oberboihingen, 72644, Germany;48.6470197;9.3651236;45;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Having made a name for itself decades ago, this restaurant is a local institution. It specialises in both fine dining and traditional Swabian fare that is made with high-quality ingredients, delicious and reasonably priced. The Maultaschen are a standout. When it comes to meat products, they have their own on-site butcher shop to fall back on. The specials, which change every day, are especially popular. Although dominated by regional selections, the wine list also boasts a range of Bordeaux, including some iconic names. Tip: Pick up some soups, sauces, sausages and meats from their shop. The ultra-modern apartments in the annexe are ideal for long-stay guests.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6114;Die Halde;Germany;Oberried;Halde 2, Oberried, 79254, Germany;47.8918398;7.8929768;32;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Situated at an altitude of 1 147m, this stylish restaurant successfully bridges the gap between history and modernity! The food is served in cosy traditional dining rooms, where guests are looked after by friendly, well-trained staff. Local produce is favoured, and the water comes from the house's mountain spring. There are also lovely guestrooms done out in a modern, regional style.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6115;Gasthaus Sternen Post;Germany;Oberried;Hauptstraße 30, Oberried, 79254, Germany;47.9348214;7.9531819;100;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;This beautifully restored 1875 restaurant is a fine example of the dedication of its owner. Diners sit in comfortable rooms complete with tiled ovens to sample delicious dishes such as venison stew with spaetzle (a Swabian pasta speciality) and red cabbage or apple fritters with vanilla sauce. Overnight accommodation comes in the form of lovely country house-style rooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6116;Zum Dückerstieg;Germany;Neuendorf bei Wilster;Dückerstieg 7, Neuendorf bei Wilster, 25554, Germany;53.9472935;9.3492529;64;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;An attractive, cosy restaurant with rural flair which serves seasonal and regional cuisine. Here, you can look forward to flavoursome dishes that pack a punch. The delicious options on offer include salmon, North Sea prawns, sea bass, suckling pig and game. Steeped in tradition, this family-run business – now in its fourth generation – also has attractive, comfortable guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6117;Wirtschaft von Johann Gerner;Germany;Heßdorf;Dannberg 3, Heßdorf, 91093, Germany;49.646982;10.8719577;42;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;The journey out here to the countryside is well worth it, because Detlef Gerner and his wife Tanja live and breathe hospitality par excellence in their cosy restaurant. The hand-written menu features flavoursome dishes based on seasonal and predominantly regional produce – incidentally, they bake their own bread. In summer, you can sit on the terrace out front. Overnight accommodation in the pretty "Häusla" (for two to seven people).;Car park,Terrace;[]
6119;Granit;France;Plouharnel;5 Kerhuéno, Plouharnel, 56340, France;47.5907116;-3.1007175;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Between Carnac and Quiberon, this modern edifice, deep in the Brittany countryside, is a foodie’s paradise! Chef Charles Moreau has knocked around a bit from China to the Belgian kitchens of Sang Hoon Degeimbre (including the 2-star Air du Temps). Brittany whiskey, buckwheat, artichokes, oysters, gwell and Guéméné andouille, the food ticks all the boxes of traditional Brittany fare. The result is spot on, well-crafted and above all balanced, without forgetting the odd, inspired creative note (such as the dessert of black olives, strawberries and burrata). Concise (mainly organic and biodynamic) wine list and a black and white minimalist interior.;Wheelchair access;[]
6120;Topaze;France;Saint-Nazaire;103 rue Aristide-Briand, Saint-Nazaire, 44600, France;47.2793485;-2.225347;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The town centre is home to this couple of professionals who met in Paris at William Ledeuil’s Ze Kitchen. He is in the kitchen, she at the front of house and together they have crafted this irresistible gourmet gem. The chef works with the meticulousness of a jeweller: fresh local produce that varies with the season, high-precision, slow cooking techniques, aromas and colours. We feasted on a beef tartare with an iced oyster cream dotted with samphire, followed by pearlescent cod in a sesame seed and roast buckwheat crust, coated with a punchy jus of saffron-flavoured cockles.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6123;Cabane;France;Nanterre;8 rue du Docteur-Foucault, Nanterre, 92000, France;48.8918373;2.1947908;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Jean-François Bury, who boasts stints at the George V and the Shangri-La, is masterfully regaling Nanterre with modern, bistronomic nosh. Well-crafted recipes, generous helpings and wholesome flavours, such as confit of finely sliced veal belly in oregano, smoked apple puree, sucrine lettuce, or the exquisitely crafted and fiendishly tempting lemon and raspberry showpiece.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6124;Sillage;France;Saint-Pierre-d'Oléron;4 ruelle de la Lanterne, Saint-Pierre-d'Oléron, 17310, France;45.9445762;-1.3056358;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;Piedmontese chef Gabriele Ferri and his wife Marie-Nolwenn run this bistro, which has been given a nautical makeover against a backdrop of pale stone walls and contemporary furnishings. The former chef of Le Verdurier – Château de Drudas serves up seafood cuisine… with Italian influences, of course! Meat, meanwhile, only features during the hunting season. An example dish: pollack poached in seawater, chard with green curry, creamy Piedmont polenta with miso, fragrant consommé.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6125;La Croix Blanche;France;Veuzain-sur-Loire;2 avenue de la Loire (à Veuves), Veuzain-sur-Loire, 41150, France;47.48631;1.11419;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In this former coaching inn on the banks of the Loire, you can enjoy the modern cuisine of chef Jean-François Beauduin, who learned the ropes in starred establishments. His tempting menu abounds in seasonal, local produce and stars a wonderful culinary lineup of dishes such as roast pollock, carrot greens and confit ginger. It would be a crime not to sample the soufflé flambéed in cognac with vanilla ice cream on the side. The menu also features a number of more traditional local dishes, like a “beuchelle tourangelle” (creamed kidneys and sweetbreads). Gracious service by the chef's wife, in a pleasantly rustic setting and special mention for the tree-lined shaded terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6126;La Petite Grange;France;Tournemire;17 rue Edouard-Marty, Tournemire, 15310, France;45.0540365;2.4832587;56;true;true;Regional Cuisine;In this picturesque Cantal village, home to a castle, the traveller is always delighted to take a seat in this tastefully renovated traditional barn (wood, stone and shale). Beneath a stunning raftered ceiling, gaze out at the Doire Valley through the large windows. In the kitchen, chef Olivier Cloteau expertly crafts seasonal dishes that pay homage to the Cantal region and its producers, without forgetting a few nods to his Charentes roots (mouclade (mussels in saffron) as an appetizer). 100% wholesome, hearty nosh.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6127;Brasserie d'Asten;France;Binic;8 boulevard Clemenceau, Binic, 22520, France;48.5992805;-2.8250483;92;false;false;Contemporary;On Binic port, this contemporary brasserie has large bay windows overlooking the sea. The chef with a glittering track record (Le Coquillage – Maison de Bricourt in Cancale, La Pyramide Patrick Henriroux in Vienne and K2 in Courchevel) likes to cook up his enticing brand of "bistronomy" cuisine, incorporated into set menus that represent good value for money.;Great view;[]
6128;Bergamote;France;Lyon;123 rue de Gerland, Lyon, 69007, France;45.7341669;4.839592;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This bistronomic bijou is tucked away in the heart of a district in the throes of renovation. In a cosy, nature-inspired interior, youthful Maxime Pujol rolls out his technical skills as he conjures up seasonal dishes, rich in crisp flavours and beautifully presented – all of which at eater friendly prices at lunchtime. More ambitious score in the evening with a surprise menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6129;L'Estacade;France;Le Croisic;4 quai du Lénigo, Le Croisic, 44490, France;47.2981892;-2.5154108;39;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This pleasant eatery on the quayside, opposite the fish market, is managed by two young people with experience in some elite establishments. They propose hearty and meticulously made food that makes good use of regional produce (fish, shellfish and seaweed, of course, but also meat). The lady of the house is a radiant hostess. Smiling staff and attentive service.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6130;L'Arbre Vert;France;Berrwiller;96 rue Principale, Berrwiller, 68500, France;47.8467812;7.2200675;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The tree mentioned in the name of this restaurant could well be a genealogical one, so closely is its history bound up with that of the Koenig family. Now run by the fifth generation of this family, the restaurant serves specialities from Alsace, which are accompanied by good regional wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6131;La Récré;France;Vaudevant;70 route de Satillieu, Vaudevant, 07410, France;45.1039749;4.6186956;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in a former village school for boys. You will notice evidence of its previous incarnation in the decor with blackboards and geographical maps hanging on the walls. On the menu, the dishes are creative and make good use of locally sourced ingredients. It is enough to make us sign up for evening classes!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6133;Rosemarie;France;Paris;149 rue de l'Université, Paris, 75007, France;48.8611264;2.3055501;29;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Cream, butter, zinc-topped counter, imitation leather and egg mayonnaise – a recipe for happiness! This bistro was opened by two seasoned professionals, Nina and Philippe Cadeau (formerly at Le Beurre Noisette and Christian Constant's Cocottes, respectively), and named after their mothers. Their expertise is still going strong: Nina's enthusiasm continues to shine on the restaurant floor and Philippe turns out delicious traditional and seasonal dishes: leek vinaigrette, country terrine, salmon tartar, pollack, scallops, entrecote and shoulder of lamb for two, custard pie and chocolate mousse. There is a menu on the blackboard – changes daily (around €30 at lunchtime and €40 in the evening) – and an à la carte menu.;Wheelchair access;[]
6135;La Table du Square;France;Beaune;26 boulevard du Maréchal-Foch, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0262483;4.8352348;96;true;false;Farm to table;This bistro on the main boulevard sports a distinctive contemporary decor complete with wooden floors, black and white striped walls and photos of the stars of French cinema enjoying good food. Cooking has no secrets for the chef who rustles up a spot-on, frequently renewed market-fresh menu. Given the location in Beaune, you won't be surprised to learn that the cellar boasts over 1000 labels – so drink up!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6137;Peck & Co;France;Brest;23 rue Fautras, Brest, 29200, France;48.3906794;-4.4910485;56;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;The chef and his partner have turned their former gourmet establishment into a friendlier and trendier venue thanks to a modern makeover and an open-plan kitchen. Talented chef Romain hasn't lost his touch and his market-fresh menu is a masterclass of fragrant, flavoursome and deftly crafted recipes, such as Iberico pluma pork, cream of cranberry beans, chards and a creamy chorizo sauce.;Brunch,Counter dining;[]
6138;Gribiche;France;Angers;9 rue Max-Richard, Angers, 49100, France;47.46576;-0.5580888;96;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;We fell head over heels with this endearing bistro! Traditional dishes, jazzed up for modern tastebuds and served generously, are enticingly chalked up on slate menus: porkpie, calf’s head gribiche sauce, lamb shank and desserts to die for with lashings of salted butter and cream. Fine choice of reasonably priced tipples.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6139;Auberge de La Mère Duval;France;Auzouville-sur-Saâne;Impasse de la Linerie, Auzouville-sur-Saâne, 76730, France;49.7410587;0.9436443;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Alexandre and Mélanie Baranzelli are thriving in a new venue oozing with country charm: picture a stream spanned by two bridges and a watermill! The chef, after honing his skills in top establishments, demonstrates his fondness for traditional recipes from his native Normandy, to which he is increasingly adding his own distinctive culinary hallmark.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6140;YOKO;France;Rennes;20 boulevard de la Tour-d'Auvergne, Rennes, 35000, France;48.1067069;-1.6845853;23;true;false;Japanese;This is the sister restaurant of chef Julien Lemarié's MICHELIN-starred Japanese-style restaurant (IMA). At lunchtime, in a relaxed atmosphere, you can enjoy a variety of Japanese donburi – a bowl of rice with toppings that vary according to the season or inspiration. In the evening, French dishes are skilfully revisited with a Japanese touch, such as leeks with miso and katsuobushi vinaigrette. The service comes with a smile!;;[]
6142;Le 21ème Commis;France;Morlaix;23 rue du Mur, Morlaix, 29600, France;48.5763275;-3.8268436;17;true;false;Farm to table;Located in the centre of Morlaix and surrounded by gorgeous half-timbered buildings, this recently opened restaurant is run by a chef with experience in MICHELIN-starred establishments. His original cuisine combines Breton ingredients and more exotic influences (particularly Asian). Flavour combinations that delight the taste buds and generous portions, as in his indulgent pear and wine dessert.;;[]
6144;Café de la Fontaine;France;La Turbie;4 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, La Turbie, 06320, France;43.7455777;7.4002839;75;true;true;Provençal;A convivial atmosphere, good choice of unpretentious, enjoyable wines, as well as tasty and generous market sourced cuisine of Provencal inspiration. All chalked up on the slate. A memorable culinary experience guaranteed!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6145;Le Bouche à Oreille;France;Tulle;39 avenue Charles-de-Gaulle, Tulle, 19000, France;45.2689144;1.7696377;83;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;An opportunity to discover the work of a likeable, self-effacing chef, who is as modest as his food is good. Seasonal ingredients and premium produce feature prominently in his dishes: duck breast cooked rare with prunes and orange, einkorn risotto. It's tasty, flawlessly crafted and delicious! In fine weather, you can sit out on the pretty terrace in the garden to the rear.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6146;L'Auberge du Pas de Vent;France;Pouillon;281 avenue Pas-de-Vent, Pouillon, 40350, France;43.6014023;-1.0052604;27;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Authenticity is the name of the game in this Landes inn that specialises in hearty, wholesome nosh, light years from fads and fashions. The menu pays tribute to the terroir: Chalosse beef, free-range fattened duck, veal from calves fed on their mother’s milk, pure sheep milk cheese from a village shepherd and home-made sourdough bread (without additives). Examples of the nostalgic score include celery and fennel rémoulade, cream of split peas and crispy slivers of coppa or Jurançon calf’s sweetbread served in a skillet. Warm welcome and attentive, slick service. What’s not to like?;Car park,Terrace;[]
6147;Maison Cachée;France;Rochefort-en-Terre;9 rue Haute-Candre, Rochefort-en-Terre, 56220, France;47.6989923;-2.3368528;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;After stints in leading star establishments (Alain Ducasse, Maison Pic, Crillon), Alban Chartron (savoury) and his partner Sarah Alba (sweet dishes) have set up shop in Rochefort-sur-Terre, a drop-dead historic village, rife in quaint cobbled lanes and half-timbered granite houses. The duo of chefs knows the business inside out as their spot-on cooking (such as the cod of the day), spicy flavours (illustrated by oxtail with kimchi or a curry/peanut stock on fish) and play on textures (think carrot cake with a light, frothy yoghurt mousse) illustrate. Bistronomic cooking at prices that make sense flanked by a buzzy, homespun vibe and a quirky mismatched interior.;;[]
6148;Clément Artisan Culinaire;France;Lauzun;6 rue Eugène-Mazélie, Lauzun, 47410, France;44.62969;0.46069;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This picturesque village of Lot-et-Garonne, which boasts a rich and chequered history, is home to chef Clément Papillaud. Having worked in top restaurants, this craftsman has a sure touch when it comes to crafting dishes such as chicken supreme from the Batailles farm lacquered with wild garlic and served with white asparagus from Fargues and parmesan milk. The chef seems to have a particular penchant for roasted notes such as coffee, in both the main course and the dessert. The country chic interior sports an open kitchen, a coffered ceiling and bare stone walls and rafters.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6149;La Closerie des Roses;France;Varades;455 rue de la Haute-Meilleraie, Varades, 44370, France;47.3712253;-1.0220107;25;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Surrounded by rose bushes, this restaurant, which has stood on the banks of the Loire since 1938, affords a stunning view of the river and the abbey church of St-Florent-le-Vieil. In a tasteful contemporary interior, the chef crafts a traditional lineup drawing on regional fare (hake, pollock, farm-reared lamb, calf sweetbreads) flanked by classic sauces (beurre blanc, shellfish jus, wine sauce).;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6150;Gare aux Goûts;France;Lorient;26 bis rue Louis-Blanqui, Lorient, 56100, France;47.7535075;-3.3651664;76;false;false;Contemporary;Chef Vincent Seviller has come up trumps in this establishment near the railway station. He invites diners on a bistronomic journey in a tasteful, modern setting. An experienced and talented craftsman, each dish is artfully presented, flavoursome and balanced. The lunchtime menu is chalked up on a slate, but more elaborate in the evening.;;[]
6151;Le Bistro d'en Face;France;Bergerac;1 rue Fénelon, Bergerac, 24100, France;44.8474818;0.4824992;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Aurore and Hugo Brégeon's restaurant boasts a terrace with a breathtaking panoramic view over the old town, the Dordogne River and its traditional boats. The tasty, well-crafted food does the vista justice: dynamic neo-bistro cuisine that brilliantly revisits some of the French classics. It is unbeatable value, and there is a good choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6153;Le Manoir de Kerbot;France;Sarzeau;Lieu-dit Kerbot, Sarzeau, 56370, France;47.53658;-2.73911;37;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This 16C manor house (once an orphanage) has been converted into a haven for food lovers. Guests are treated to fairly traditional cuisine – warm oysters, semi-cooked foie gras, catch of the day, pulled pork in a spice crust served with an aromatic reduction: tasty, well-crafted recipes all the way! The service is very attentive, and the terrace overlooking a lake is delightful, as are the lovely guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6154;O2C;France;Bagnères-de-Bigorre;20 place de Strasbourg, Bagnères-de-Bigorre, 65200, France;43.0636999;0.1494891;42;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A former helicopter pilot who now devotes himself body and soul to cooking, Christophe Bellegaud is at the controls of this restaurant, which sports a tasteful cream and chocolate colour scheme. He uses local ingredients to create 100% homemade up-to-the-minute market cuisine that is always spot on. Chantal, the second “c” of this o2c, gracefully caters to diner’s needs.;Terrace;[]
6155;L'Envers du Décor;France;Les Herbiers;23 rue de la Bienfaisance, Les Herbiers, 85500, France;46.8718586;-1.0131786;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This old bakery has been transformed into a smart, contemporary restaurant that sports a minimalist vibe. Chef Aurélien Jousseaume earned his stripes in Michelin-starred kitchens with the likes of Etchebest, Guy Savoy and Guy Martin. To-ing and fro-ing between his open kitchen and the restaurant floor, the chef, who is clearly having a ball, takes the orders and presents the dishes himself. His delicious seasonal cuisine showcases his flair for creating remarkable sauces and jus: creamy jus of trout roe, sabayon enhanced with smoked salt, watercress and horseradish sauce, veal jus with lovage.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6156;Le Bistrot 270;France;Malataverne;270 chemin de Malombre, Malataverne, 26780, France;44.4685997;4.7438463;49;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Le Domaine du Colombier's second restaurant serves well-structured bistro fare inspired by top-quality ingredients. Chef Anthony Monteremal's simple, enticing recipes play on bold flavours and follow the seasons, paying homage to the classics. In winter, the tables set up in the contemporary interior afford views of the striking glassed-in cellar. In fine weather, the terrace overlooking the countryside is the place to be for a moment of indulgence and relaxation!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6157;Les Loges du Jardin d'Aymeric;France;Clara;7 rue du Canigou, Clara, 66500, France;42.5843613;2.4422211;67;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The quintessential country establishment, where they are still passionate about what they do. Mad about great ingredients, the chef uses vegetables from his kitchen garden and citrus fruits from the surrounding area, and makes his own bread made with ancient flours. Unpretentious family service, reasonable prices: an enjoyable experience.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
6158;L'Ermitage;France;Espaly-Saint-Marcel;73 avenue de l'Ermitage, Espaly-Saint-Marcel, 43000, France;45.0535206;3.8558848;70;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This beautifully restored old barn has retained its homely rustic appeal. The chef, whose CV boasts establishments of the calibre of Jacques Maximin and La Grenouillère, conjures up delicate traditional fare. The organic local (Aurillac) beef is sometimes carved in front of diners, as are some fish. The menu includes home-made patés and saucisson and a splendid cheese trolley. Let’s not forget the open fire in winter and the inviting terrace in summertime. What’s not to like?;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6159;La Chênaie;France;Croutelle;Rue du Lejat - lieu-dit La Berlanderie, Croutelle, 86240, France;46.5414198;0.2900667;18;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The focus here is on good old-fashioned fare, in all its generosity and simplicity. Traditional French favourites, enlivened by the occasional more contemporary note, are served in a stylish space or, even better, in the extension overlooking the grounds, which are planted with century-old oak trees. A warm welcome and friendly service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6163;Ô Moulin;France;Carsac-Aillac;1 place Martin-Dolt, Carsac-Aillac, 24200, France;44.8408811;1.2729812;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This couple who earned their stripes in the industry have transformed this charming Périgord mill – a water-powered sawmill, to be precise – into a peaceful country restaurant. The stream that drives the cogs can be seen beneath the restaurant through the glass floor panels. The chef rustles up delicious food that is very much in tune with the times – eg fillet of roast Limousin beef, topped with a good red wine jus and accompanied by Noirmoutier potatoes. They have a lovely shaded terrace, and the proprietress provides attentive service.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6164;Auberge Metzger;France;Natzwiller;55 rue Principale, Natzwiller, 67130, France;48.4363567;7.2581969;15;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Successive generations have been at the helm here since 1885, each leaving its own distinctive signature on this historic establishment in the heart of the forest. A spacious, contemporary dining room provides the perfect foil to sample regional specialities: calf’s head and tongue, choucroute with all the trimmings, fillet of zander in riesling, while a slate menu offers a selection of seasonal dishes. Start your meal with one of their signature dishes, aniseed-flavoured snails à l’alsacienne, before continuing with a risotto of perfectly seared scallops. A cheerful, family-run vibe depicts the front-of-house team.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6165;Le Brélévenez;France;Lannion;1 rue Stang-Ar-Béo, Lannion, 22300, France;48.7379433;-3.455017;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This pretty stone house in Brélévenez (a neighbourhood in Lannion) is run by Monsieur and Madame Le Marrec. Business is going strong, and this is not by chance: the well thought-out and tasty food is in tune with the land and the seasons. One last thing, the space is modern, refined and a pleasant place to be.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6166;Sodade;France;Chaudes-Aigues;21 avenue du Président-Georges-Pompidou, Chaudes-Aigues, 15110, France;44.8516289;3.0032348;39;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Sodade is a song by Cesária Évora and a nod to the Portuguese origins of the late owner, Serge Vieira. In a large designer dining room or on the terrace overlooking the stream, you will sample dishes that are the epitome of tasty and simple. Pleasant guestrooms to stay longer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6167;Le Cygne;France;Gundershoffen;35 Grande-Rue, Gundershoffen, 67110, France;48.9066565;7.6589369;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This picturesque half-timbered Alsace edifice has successfully kept pace with the times and its experienced chef conjures up modern, bistro dishes. Examples include the signature fish casserole with aïoli croutons, or spice-crusted lamb cutlet and fillet with braised vegetables and chickpea cream.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6168;L'Épine;France;Azay-le-Rideau;19 place de la République, Azay-le-Rideau, 37190, France;47.2612347;0.4674999;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of the restaurant means "blackthorn" – a thorny shrub or tree commonly found in the hedgerows of France. Its fruit (sloes) can be turned into sloe gin. Formerly a school dating back to 1866, the premises are tastefully decorated throughout: exposed ceiling beams, large windows giving onto a tree-lined terrace, designer lighting and works of art. The chef cooks up a seasonal bistronomy menu that celebrates local produce and artisans, at affordable prices.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6170;L'Assiette au Jardin;France;Noirmoutier-en-l'Île;9 rue du Robinet, Noirmoutier-en-l'Île, 85330, France;47.0007779;-2.2426451;31;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Imagine a small cheerful bistro-style dining room whose shelves are laden with fine deli produce, a pretty conservatory and a small terrace. The scene is set to sample tasty food in which tradition is cleverly paired with wayfaring influences: Asian and North-African notes flank the Fujiyama oyster (house specialty), the catch of the day and a seasonal vegetable tajine, or “A night in Essaouira” dessert based on dates, fresh dairy ice cream and honey. Delightful.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6171;Le Confidentiel;France;Menthon-Saint-Bernard;24 route des Moulins, Menthon-Saint-Bernard, 74290, France;45.8600546;6.1964034;53;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant – one of many (including some real juggernauts!) surrounding the lake – proves that good things come in small packages. In a compact dining area, you can enjoy dish after dish that is absolutely on point with its bold flavours, such as low-temperature egg, celery and pear, or hake, vegetable noodles and ginger-lemongrass broth. The atmosphere is friendly and relaxed. It really is love at first bite... Now that you're in on the secret, you know what to do!;;[]
6172;SaQuaNa;France;Honfleur;22 place Hamelin, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.421549;0.2329105;89;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Alexandre Bourdas has turned his SaQuaNa into a real social hub, open from morning to night, the idea being to make good food accessible to as many people as possible. The menu is varied, with influences from near and far (including a Japanese section), and, as ever, it boasts a number of must-tries, such as his monkfish in coconut broth and combawa oil, "our house bouillabaisse" or his emblematic pascade (oven-puffed pancake): a talented, confident and inspiring culinary showing featuring a wealth of dishes that are designed "for sharing". Depending on the time of day, SaQuaNa is also a patisserie, bakery and tearoom.;;[]
6173;Auberge de l'Île;France;L'Ile-Bouchard;3 place Bouchard, L'Ile-Bouchard, 37220, France;47.1200762;0.4255419;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this plush restaurant on an island in the River Vienne, chef Pierre Koniecko rustles up recipes that are both tasty and generous, such as his medley of lamb (grilled chop and saddle, confit shoulder pastilla). In summertime, the teak deck patio by the riverside is an undeniable draw!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6174;Double Dragon;France;Paris;52 rue Saint-Maur, Paris, 75011, France;48.8626799;2.3797202;40;true;true;Asian;In this friendly "Asian canteen", sisters Katia and Tatiana Levha offer simple dishes of mixed inspiration (China, Philippines, Thailand etc) in an upgraded "street food" vein. This is cooking that is full of character, with pronounced flavours, and often deliciously spicy. A fun experience and tasty fare.;;[]
6177;Perle des Vosges;France;Muhlbach-sur-Munster;22 route Gaschney, Muhlbach-sur-Munster, 68380, France;48.0277171;7.0802252;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this family-run hotel-restaurant, the first thing you notice is the wonderfully traditional interior (chandeliers and silverware). The dishes range from the classic (marengo chicken supreme) to the regional (veal kidneys with mustard seeds, marrow quenelles and spaetzle), to the occasional more contemporary offering (lobster tempura). The cheese platter from the valley is a real highlight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6179;Côté Bastide;France;Sainte-Foy-la-Grande;4 rue de l'Abattoir, Sainte-Foy-la-Grande, 33220, France;44.8403558;0.2221237;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At a slight distance from the town centre, this is the headquarters of Laurence and Cédric. She is the chef and produces tasty cuisine in step with the seasons. While he is a trained sommelier and chooses the best wines (notably Bordeaux) to accompany the dishes concocted by his partner. A duo that works wonders!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
6180;La Maison de Kerdiès;France;Plougasnou;5 route de Perherel, à Saint-Samson, Plougasnou, 29630, France;48.6855;-3.8398;47;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant at the tip of Trégor province was originally a signal station then a holiday camp before being converted into a restaurant. From inside, you can enjoy a panoramic view over the Bay of Morlaix. But your attention will soon be drawn back to the food, which encompasses both regional dishes (catch of the day with a Roscoff onion sauce) and more traditional fare (chicken supreme with morel mushrooms and garlic-fried potatoes).;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6181;La Chatellenie;France;Availles-Limouzine;1 rue du Commerce, Availles-Limouzine, 86460, France;46.1211416;0.6557141;23;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Talented pair Emilie and Thomas Fournier have thrown themselves wholeheartedly into running this charming inn hidden deep in the Vienne, which gives pride of place to local producers. The delicious dishes are artfully plated and are good value for money. For example: asparagus and duck confit, served with a warm vinaigrette, or their version of devilled egg – flavoured with wild garlic. Well worth the detour.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6182;Atelier Salone;France;Salon-de-Provence;6 rue du Maréchal-Joffre, Salon-de-Provence, 13300, France;43.641406;5.0986434;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Atelier Salone, the bistronomy sibling of Villa Salone, is lavished with attention by Alexandre Lechêne, a chef with a stellar CV (Aux Lyonnais, Louis XV in Monaco) and formerly Michelin-starred in Saint-Véran (Hautes Alpes département). On the day of our visit, the menu included slow-cooked organic egg with pumpkin and truffles, a delicious vol-au-vent and a chestnut and blackcurrant mont blanc dessert with chestnut ice cream. The original style of this early-20C building is underscored by contemporary details.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6184;Bird;France;Yerres;38 rue Charles-de-Gaulle, Yerres, 91330, France;48.7164372;2.490399;80;true;true;Farm to table;In the heart of this charming borough, on a pedestrian square near the town hall, a pocket-sized restaurant run by a young chef with an impressive cv. Market-inspired menu with the likes of fresh pasta with mussels, calamari and langoustines, or poultry quenelles with freekeh... Scandinavian style dining room, terrace overlooking a fountain. Delicious prices.;Terrace;[]
6185;Les 7;France;Tulle;32 quai Baluze, Tulle, 19000, France;45.2692196;1.7724975;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This tiny place (no more than 25 covers) is the haunt of an enterprising young couple. The dishes are carefully presented, the flavours and textures are perfectly paired. Let's not forget to mention the absolutely delightful service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6187;Les Petits Parisiens;France;Paris;49 avenue Jean-Moulin, Paris, 75014, France;48.8250001;2.3204462;47;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This is the place to go for up-to-the-minute bistro fare and time-honoured favourites such as chou farci (stuffed cabbage), often brilliantly modernised. Food lovers won't be able to resist the chocolate mousse with olive oil and fleur de sel, or a must-try like the vanilla-flavoured riz au lait, dried fruit and salted butter caramel.;Air conditioning;[]
6188;20 Eiffel;France;Paris;20 rue de Monttessuy, Paris, 75007, France;48.8594686;2.2985472;24;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;In a quiet street a stone’s throw from the Eiffel Tower, this restaurant offers a understated interior full of light. On the menu, you can choose from a range of updated dishes, prepared by two chefs, all of which place the focus on flavour and taste. For example, a delicious fillet of wild Pollock with squash.;;[]
6189;Chez Davia;France;Nice;11 bis rue Grimaldi, Nice, 06000, France;43.6992114;7.2648092;94;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This likeable establishment, run by the same family since 1953, was founded by grandma Davia and taken over in 1985 by mum, Alda, now retired. Since 2016, Pierre Altobelli, whose impressive CV features star establishments in France and Asia, concocts tempting recipes rich in the aromas of Nice. Every detail is perfect, and the ingredients are meticulously sourced. Served in a welcoming vintage bistro décor steeped in authenticity. Heavenly!;Terrace;[]
6190;Le Bouche à Oreille;France;Le Havre;19 rue Paul-Doumer, Le Havre, 76600, France;49.4925851;0.1010396;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This top-notch establishment is laid out behind a tasteful glazed façade. The chef adheres to tradition when crafting his bold, generous and flavourful cuisine but puts his own stamp on dishes with the odd touch of originality – think prawn tartare, prawn gyoza with coriander and lemongrass, bisque and cashew nuts. His friendly and efficient wife takes care of things front of house, dispensing insightful wine tips along the way.;;[]
6191;C'la Vie;France;Orsan;12 avenue du Jasset, Orsan, 30200, France;44.1297774;4.6653987;83;false;false;Modern Cuisine;From a long line of bakers, chef Richard Durand has made C'la Vie a real mecca for food lovers. The food is good and life is good! The daily menu features terrific ingredients (most of them local), the flavours are distinctive, and the focus is firmly on dining pleasure. Enjoy your meal in the pared-back dining area inside, or on the terrace in the shade of a hundred-year-old plane tree. A fine selection of wines that celebrates the Rhône Valley and Languedoc, and rightfully so.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6192;Erasmo;France;Carhaix-Plouguer;4 rue du Général-Lambert, Carhaix-Plouguer, 29270, France;48.2762187;-3.5728737;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Venetian chef Matteo Vianello chalked up experience in the kitchens of Alain Ducasse and Jean-François Piège before becoming chef at Mensae and at Sellae. Now established nearer the sea, he has dedicated his small contemporary bistro to the island of Sant Erasmo (home of the famous purple artichoke). He has certainly not lost his touch, revisiting the classics in mouth-watering dishes that convincingly draw on Breton and Italian scores – for instance, ravioles of snails, sweet garlic stock, roast buckwheat or tiramisu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6193;Téjérina - Hôtel de la Place;France;Polliat;51 place de la Mairie, Polliat, 01310, France;46.24887;5.12659;51;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The epitome of a family-run inn, where hearty portions of tasty cuisine du terroir are served with a smile in a freshly refurbished dining area. Calf's head, chicken in creamy sauce, chicken liver soufflé and frogs' legs are all on the menu. Well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6194;Le Garriane;France;Perpignan;15 rue Valette, Perpignan, 66000, France;42.6974636;2.8804252;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;"Garriane" is the contraction of Garry and Ariane, and originality is the name of the game here! In the kitchens, Garry, an Australian, concocts seasonal, ingredient-focused cuisine that taps into influences from around the world. The restaurant is now open for lunch, with a menu of vegetarian and vegan options, and operates as a café in the mornings and afternoons (closed evenings and weekends).;Air conditioning;[]
6195;Bistrot Louise;France;L'Albenc;80 place Jean-Vinay, L'Albenc, 38470, France;45.2236759;5.4395128;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The small terrace facing the church resembles a traditional walnut drier… Welcome to this walnut-growing village where Yann Tanneau (formerly of MadaM in Grenoble and who trained at Ducasse) has set up shop. A fan of fine produce, he whisks up gutsy cuisine in menus that change weekly. Guaranteed to please, excellent value for money at lunchtime and refreshingly informal ambience.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6196;Kisin;France;Paris;7-9 rue de Ponthieu, Paris, 75008, France;48.87035;2.31057;38;false;false;Japanese;When a Bib Gourmand chef from Tokyo arrives in Paris, the first thing he does is open a restaurant, tantalising and bewitching our senses. Diners will sample Japanese produce and genuine udon, made in front of the diner. Natural, additive - free ingredients, most of which are imported direct from the Land of the Rising Sun. Healthy, wholesome and succulent.;Air conditioning;[]
6197;Agastache;France;Lyon;134 rue Duguesclin, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7663928;4.8476636;54;false;true;Creative;This unfussy, up-to-date bistro sets the scene for instinctive, well-crafted food in the zeitgeist. Fine seasonal produce and a distinct fondness for vegetables result in dishes that combine formal elegance with flavoursome coherence. Now add lashings of generosity and a friendly vibe and you will find yourself in one of the best establishments on the Left Bank of Lyon.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6198;Les Trois Bourgeons;France;Chablis;10 rue Auxerroise, Chablis, 89800, France;47.8154316;3.7992263;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary bistro with an understated decor has blossomed in an old cellar belonging to Domaine Laroche, famous for producing Chablis. Trained in Tokyo and some top-flight French establishments, the Japanese chef invites his customers to partake in cuisine inspired by regional dishes revisited with imagination. Good value for money.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6199;Simple et Meilleur;France;Saint-Martin-de-Belleville;Place Notre-Dame, quartier de Caseblanche, Saint-Martin-de-Belleville, 73440, France;45.3764595;6.5063173;63;false;false;Savoyard;The brainchild of René and Maxime Meilleur, authentic Savoie produce takes the limelight in this pure-bred alpine establishment, decked in raw wood and cow bells with floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the mountains. On the menu are baked trout, Reblochon fondue, cold cuts and cheeses from the region, blueberry tart, or rabbit cooked in mustard, tarragon with creamy polenta. Even better, you can ski right up to the doorstep!;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6200;Le Laurier Fleuri;France;Vertou;460 route de Clisson, Vertou, 44120, France;47.187256;-1.48276;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This former coaching inn may not enjoy the most appealing of settings, but once seated at your table you will have no trouble understanding the success of this restaurant run by a pair of industry professionals. With plenty of experience in prestigious establishments, the chef concocts a pleasingly refined and fragrant cuisine composed of bistronomy-style dishes delivered at reasonable prices.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6201;La Ferme de Victorine;France;Notre-Dame-de-Bellecombe;141 route du Plan-Dessert, Notre-Dame-de-Bellecombe, 73590, France;45.8054077;6.5512822;82;true;false;Regional Cuisine;An authentic farmhouse with a pretty rustic - style restaurant, from which you can even see the cows in the cowshed in winter. The chef is passionate about Savoyard produce, and always on the lookout for the best cheeses and cold cooked meats. An eminently pleasant restaurant and very tasty dishes!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6202;L'Auberge des Gourmets;France;Le Villars;9 place de l'Église, Le Villars, 71700, France;46.530191;4.9306322;98;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In a charming village above the River Saône, this restaurant has a traditional decor (exposed stones and beams, large colourful frescoes). Guillaume Laublanc, a native of these parts, sets about cooking his bistronomy-style cuisine with locally sourced ingredients and infectious enthusiasm. Cooked at low temperature, the Bresse chicken (from Johan Morand's farm) stuffed with morels and vin jaune cream is sure to win you over!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6203;Villa Mirasol - Bistrot 1912;France;Mont-de-Marsan;2 boulevard Ferdinand-de-Candau, Mont-de-Marsan, 40000, France;43.8911627;-0.5036726;98;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Villa Mirasol has entrusted the fate of its 100-year-old restaurant to Philippe Lagraula, a chef from Landes (Troisgros and Bras), who rustles up a market-fresh, generous, flavoursome score. He is famous for his unconventional flair, plating and balanced flavours that he rolls out in a modern, no-holds barred score. Examples include a crispy egg in herbs and grilled txistora or Geloux trout, coloured beetroot and verbena-flavoured beurre blanc. Sampling the house dessert, a decadent île flottante (egg whites floating on custard) on the riverside terrace in fine weather is a treat not to be missed!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6205;Inspyration;France;Brive-la-Gaillarde;142 avenue du Président-Henri-Queuille, Brive-la-Gaillarde, 19100, France;45.1778959;1.5279217;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Travelling along the main road to Brive-la-Gaillarde, you are bound to notice this Corrèze-style building with its characteristic local stone walls and slate roof tiles. Inside, you'll immediately feel at home, thanks to the tranquil decor (wooden floors, oak tables, leather and fabric-upholstered seating) and the welcoming smile of the laid-back chef. He cooks by instinct, devising blind menus out of locally sourced ingredients. His delicious dishes, such as ox cheek confit in stock, smoked turnips and red cabbage, are never lacking in colour or precision.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6206;La Rochette;France;Labaroche;500 lieu-dit La Rochette, Labaroche, 68910, France;48.1004642;7.1941984;80;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Alsatian;This contemporary restaurant is a real find. A father and son team prepares tasty and refined dishes, such as chicken breast from Alsace with a pumpkin-seed crust and airy dumplings… Attentive service, a good selection of wines and guestrooms to prolong the stay complete the picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6207;Les Mets d'Adélaïde;France;Castres;36 avenue Georges-Alquier-Les Salvages, Castres, 81100, France;43.6326724;2.2717375;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Adelaide and her cooking have taken up abode in the old village school, whose playground doubles as a summer patio. The chef enjoys adding spices and aromatic herbs from distant lands to her culinary repertory. Smiling welcome.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6208;Élise;France;L'Herbaudière;5 rue Marie-Lemonnier, L'Herbaudière, 85330, France;47.0236705;-2.298846;59;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Conveniently opposite the fishing harbour, this seafood restaurant, an offshoot of the gastronomic La Marine, shines the spotlight on exquisitely fresh fish and seafood. The high-flying technique and hallmark of chef Alexandre Couillon can be tasted here. Love at first bite!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6209;Les Grands Arbres - Verte Vallée;France;Munster;10 rue Alfred-Hartmann, Munster, 68140, France;48.0406369;7.1426447;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This smart, contemporary interior is the stronghold of chef Thony Billon, who stylishly adds a new spin to regional ingredients. His flawless modern score is paired with a fine list of Alsace wines. It makes the heart sing!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6210;La Beaugravière;France;Mondragon;214 avenue du Pont-Neuf (N7), Mondragon, 84430, France;44.243922;4.7121761;62;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;After a long and rewarding career, chef Guy Jullien continues to craft a culinary score that is unabashedly devoted to uplifting, traditional nosh with proper French overtones: foie gras flan and cream of truffle soup, fattened Bresse hen with truffles, roast rack of lamb in thyme, vanilla-raspberry ice cream vacherin… without forgetting a lineup of head-spinning truffle menus. As Gallic as La Marseillaise, the flavours are gutsy and big boned, to be savoured on the peaceful terrace in the shade of the trees in fine weather. The wine cellar is a treasure trove of regional gems. Authenticity and a love of good food set the scene in this family-run inn.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6211;L'Éden;France;Houlgate;7 rue Henri-Fouchard, Houlgate, 14510, France;49.3024551;-0.0775493;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine;On a side street of an iconic picturesque village of the Côte Fleurie, the establishment of the Tougard couple, open since the early 2000s, is fronted by a discreet facade. In a snug stylish interior, the chef crafts a score that cleverly slaloms between tradition and modernity. If we were to cite a single example, it would be his talented new take on calf’s head. Flavours and aromas that hit the spot every time. Not to be missed!;Wheelchair access;[]
6212;Le Moulin Fouret;France;Bernay;2 route du Moulin-Fouret, à Saint-Aubin-le-Vertueux, Bernay, 27300, France;49.0613415;0.5962514;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In an Instagram-perfect picture of the French countryside outside Bernay, we fell head over heels with this imposing country house smothered in Virginia Creeper and its waterside terrace shaded by birch trees, without forgetting the historic mill, whose cogwheels are still intact. This idyllic venue is even more so by the fireside in wintertime, providing the perfect foil to chef Cédric Auger’s culinary ethos: first-rate fresh ingredients, consummate craftsmanship and cooking and polished table arts. The regularly changing seasonal menus pay tribute to the chef’s homeland, Normandy. Cosy guestrooms to make the most of this rural paradise.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6213;A Mandria di Pigna;France;Pigna;Village, Pigna, 20220, France;42.59878;8.90319;37;false;false;Corsican;This former sheepfold, a family business for 15 years, is perfectly in tune with its authentic, welcoming village. Corsican produce takes pride of place from the veg and herbs fresh from the garden to the grilled or spit roast suckling pork and tender lamb (wood fired cooking is the house specialty). Savour textbook perfect, generous fare on the refreshing shaded terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6214;Bellavista;France;Prats-de-Mollo-la-Preste;Place du Foiral, Prats-de-Mollo-la-Preste, 66230, France;42.4043058;2.4801504;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Catalan;It is always a pleasure to return to this eatery at the foot of the ramparts of a fortified citadel, no less! The menu positively smacks of the terroir, which is not surprising as the chef uses local produce delivered by the farmers in person. Slow-roasted Catalan lamb in fresh herbs with seasonal veggies, without forgetting cheese from the Pyrenees... Cosy rooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6215;Le Chardonnay;France;Clermont-Ferrand;1 place Philippe-Marcombes, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7793903;3.0864437;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Hugues Maisonneuve is at the helm of this swish bistro. In the kitchen, a young chef rustles up a concise, seasonal à la carte menu and a particularly enticing market-fresh menu. Everything here looks as good as it tastes. Trendy vintage décor, soft lighting and a pleasant patio.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6216;Bistrot DuPont;France;Pont-Sainte-Marie;5 place Charles-de-Gaulle, Pont-Sainte-Marie, 10150, France;48.314106;4.0985415;84;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;By the River Seine, this affably French bistro conjures up vintage recipes served by a cheerful team: slab of foie gras, coq au vin, fillet of beef in cognac, and the house specialty, andouillette. A bustling, friendly vibe depicts this gregarious eatery with atmosphere by the bucket load.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6217;Le Comptoir de La Butte;France;Plouider;12 rue de la Mer, Plouider, 29260, France;48.6110364;-4.2987684;21;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This extension of the gourmet flagship is also rich in culinary appeal. The modern layout sports an open kitchen and a shop to set your taste buds tingling… and they aren't disappointed when it comes to the generous traditional dishes with their roots in Finistère cuisine, nicely organised into a set menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6218;Le Cochon qui Boit;France;Lyon;23 rue Royale, Lyon, 69001, France;45.7706919;4.8373009;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Two former colleagues from MICHELIN-starred restaurant Têtedoie have joined forces here at "The Drinking Pig"! Savour tasty meat dishes (organic Aubrac beef cooked as best suits the day's cut, parsnips and leeks) and try out audacious combinations (braised Jerusalem artichokes, onion purée and coffee sabayon). The well-sourced local produce is cooked just right – and the small batch wines are the perfect accompaniment.;Air conditioning;[]
6219;Brigade du Tigre;France;Paris;38 rue du Faubourg-Poissonnière, Paris, 75010, France;48.8734837;2.3479318;60;true;false;Asian;The duo at the helm of Eels, both of whom trained with William Ledeuil and both of whom are passionate about Asia whose continent they’ve roamed, have now opened a second establishment to celebrate the joyful diversity of Asian cuisine in a two-storey bistro-style bolthole. The result: small fragrant nuggets, concocted from quality produce, such as a pressé of three meats, red wine and citronelle jelly or a pithiviers of black pudding and chistorra (sausage), flanked by tamarind and apricot pickles.;Wheelchair access;[]
6220;Restaurant Dimofski;France;Wœlfling-lès-Sarreguemines;2 quartier de la Gare, Wœlfling-lès-Sarreguemines, 57200, France;49.0940585;7.1903845;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant housed in an imposing 1950’s edifice a dozen or so kilometres outside Sarreguemines is just the ticket for a slap-up meal with all the trimmings. Wholehearted and single-minded, Julien Dimofski’s enthusiasm can be tasted in delectable, carefully crafted dishes overflowing in ambition (snails in potato nests, langoustine gently seared in butter or free-range roasted squab in a simple parsley sauce). The infectiously cosy, voluntarily rustic interior is further enhanced by the warm welcome and service proffered by Véronique, Julien’s mum.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6221;Saveurs de l'Abbaye;France;Saintes;1 place Saint-Pallais, Saintes, 17100, France;45.745458;-0.6249336;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A stone’s throw from the Abbaye aux Dames, now a concert venue, this stripped - back restaurant serves fresh, light, spontaneous food with a distinct preference for fine regional produce from the market, to which chef Vincent Coiquaud, basket in hand, goes daily. Plain, pleasant rooms for overnight stays.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6222;Ti-Coz;France;Quimper;4 Hent-Koz, Quimper, 29000, France;48.0425351;-4.0724331;33;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This picture postcard stone inn offers both country appeal and a modern elegant interior, reminiscent of an English club. The chef is a fan of flavoursome, traditional cuisine that shines the spotlight on the best of Brittany’s ingredients. A former sommelier, he pairs his recipes with a fantastic 500-strong wine bin.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6223;Kalamansi;France;Coutances;10 place du Général-de-Gaulle, Coutances, 50200, France;49.0474072;-1.4425987;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Frédéric Michel opened this delightful restaurant in his home town with his wife Manuella. He cooks up fresh and bold dishes, precisely cooked and with well-defined flavours, relying as much as possible on short supply chains (local fish and market gardening, Normandy beef).;Wheelchair access;[]
6224;La Table;France;Tourtour;1 traverse de Jas, Les Ribas, Tourtour, 83690, France;43.588977;6.3032316;71;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This charming small restaurant has a contemporary decor of paintings and designer chairs on the first floor of a stone - built house. Tasty cuisine showcasing seasonal market produce with an emphasis on vegetables.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6225;Racines by Daniel Gallacher;France;Bordeaux;59 rue Georges-Bonnac, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8402677;-0.584089;58;true;false;Creative;This self-taught chef with Scottish roots rustles up inventive and exuberant cuisine that flies in the face of convention. He changes his menu every week according to what produce is to be had at the market. His fresh and meticulous dishes, such as Atlantic monkfish with carrots, satay and passion fruit, are dependably delicious. Recently redesigned, the restaurant is always busy.;Air conditioning;[]
6227;Spica;France;Dijon;48 rue de la Préfecture, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3248008;5.0425494;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The former Café de la Préfecture is run by Japanese chef Takaya Uchida. Think upcycled furniture, jazz music, a succinct and regularly-changing menu with meticulously prepared market-fresh cuisine, and Burgundy wines at bargain prices. The pâté en croûte crafted in the traditional way made an impression, as did the rib eye steak with a red wine sauce and cardamom espuma: it's bold and it works!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6229;Le Malu;France;Vendôme;1 route de Tours (à Villerable), Vendôme, 41100, France;47.7821898;1.063564;97;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A military barracks under Napoleon III, the site has since been converted into a restaurant, where chef Ludovic Brethenoux brings in the big guns. Originally from Périgord, he trained, most notably, at La Villa Madie in Cassis. His affinity with the Vendômois area is evident in his precise and refined contemporary cuisine. A real treat.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6230;Cozna;France;Annecy;22 faubourg Sainte-Claire, Annecy, 74000, France;45.8973707;6.1227595;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine;After a stint in several prestigious establishments in France and the US, Sandra and Léo have settled in a car-free street in historic Annecy. Tradition is their motto (“cozna” means cooking in the Savoie dialect), a credo with which their diners wholeheartedly agree. The food is delicious food and served with a smile. A genuine good deal.;Terrace;[]
6231;La Loge Bertin;France;Manosque;62 avenue Jean-Giono, Manosque, 04100, France;43.8277724;5.7863878;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Behind the stylish mint green façade, an enthusiastic team is ready to take you on a gourmet adventure. The chef uses only the freshest ingredients to create extremely tasty, beautifully presented market-inspired cuisine. The contemporary bistro-style interior was recently refurbished.;Air conditioning;[]
6233;Au Bon Accueil;France;Paris;14 rue de Monttessuy, Paris, 75007, France;48.8596272;2.2992616;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a quiet street in the shadow of the Eiffel Tower, this friendly, welcoming eatery is fully equal to its name. You will enjoy appetising market-fresh cuisine that mirrors the seasons: tartare of salmon, seaweed salad, followed by calf’s liver, confit of onions and a chocolate extravaganza to finish.;Air conditioning;[]
6234;Voyages des Sens;France;Val-Revermont;33 rue Principale, Val-Revermont, 01370, France;46.298183;5.387954;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;After learning the ropes in the company of legendary chefs, Nicolas Morelle has opened his own establishment in this pretty village. He works hand in hand with small local producers, devising intelligent, subtle dishes that hit the spot every time, such as trout, horseradish emulsion and organic seasonal veggies. A cheerful casual vibe sets the scene and curious connoisseurs can keep an eye on the kitchen and the chef through a window to the rear.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6235;Café A;France;Uriage-les-Bains;280 allée du Jeune-Bayard, Uriage-les-Bains, 38410, France;45.1417508;5.8315318;70;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The beating heart of Maison Aribert, Café A never sleeps – it is open throughout the week from breakfast to dinner. Remaining true to his "village café" theme, which reinterprets recipes handed down from mothers and grandmothers, the chef proposes fine bistronomy cuisine at affordable prices. The simple food is made from carefully selected ingredients. Memorable dishes include a simply addictive pain perdu made with brioche served with ice cream and caramel sauce. A safe bet every time. Brunch on Sundays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6236;Lai'Tcha;France;Paris;7 rue du Jour, Paris, 75001, France;48.8635278;2.3442328;21;false;true;Asian;In this annex of Yam'tcha, located at the foot of Église St-Eustache, you can enjoy simple but straight-to-the-point Chinese cuisine that is fragrant and made with fine ingredients. The short menu offers various dim sums, but also fresh home-made noodles, Imperial sautéed beef and an excellent salad of Galician beef, lamb's lettuce and oyster mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6239;L'Atelier Locavore;France;Le Coteau;2 avenue de la Libération, Le Coteau, 42120, France;46.0314921;4.0823265;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the banks of the Loire, this establishment is now in the hands of a local lad. He aims to serve market-fresh dishes throbbing in flavour with a bargain-priced lunchtime menu and a more elaborate monthly menu. The majority of his ingredients come from within a radius of 200km, albeit with the occasional saltwater fish: his Brittany monkfish spiked with langoustine is truly mind-blowing!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6240;Mova;France;Paris;39 rue des Dames, Paris, 75017, France;48.8841785;2.3233172;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;From a line-up of carefully selected seasonal ingredients (vegetables and fish), François Merle conjures up appetising, modern recipes, illustrated by a fresh, light starter of rillettes of seabream, celery pickles, coriander sorbet and fish eggs, whose distinctive flavours are exquisitely harmonious. Single set menu at lunchtime, tasting menu in the evening.;Air conditioning;[]
6241;L'Épicerie;France;La Borne;1 chemin des Usages, La Borne, 18250, France;47.2851371;2.5780251;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Is the restaurant a grocer’s or is it the other way round? Whatever, this cheerful, two-in-one business quietly feeds us well, which is all that matters! Mathieu (in charge of savoury dishes) and Clémentine (desserts) curate a seasonal menu with 100% regional produce, making their unpretentious eatery a hit with the locals, always a good sign. All the tableware is the handiwork of artisans established in this thriving pottery village. Beware, 20 seats only, so book before you come! An affably French establishment offering a taste of rural life in times past!;Wheelchair access;[]
6242;Les Dilettants;France;Vallauris;1193 chemin de Saint-Bernard, Vallauris, 06220, France;43.5873898;7.055146;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Formerly a salesman for a leading pétanque brand, Thomas Filiaggi changed direction at the age of 30 to satisfy his love of cooking. He proposes an individual cuisine, largely based on fresh vegetables and aromatic herbs from his garden. A gem!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6243;L'Océanide;France;Nantes;2 rue Paul-Bellamy, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2205946;-1.5551373;56;false;false;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;Roasted scallops with cabbage and crunchy buckwheat, red mullet in a shellfish jus... L'Océanide certainly maintains close ties to the sea, although the menu also features duck foie gras simply ‘cuit au naturel’ and veal kidneys sautéed with shallots. Chef David Garrec sources his produce from the famous Talensac Market next-door, hence the unmistakable freshness of the fish! The authentic 1950s vintage interior oozes old-fashioned charm by the bucket load.;;[]
6244;Olive & Artichaut;France;Nice;6 rue Sainte-Réparate, Nice, 06300, France;43.6964964;7.275987;39;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Originally from Nice, the chef moved back to the region with his Breton wife after several stints abroad. He showcases local ingredients in knockout recipes, inspired by the sea and the mountains: pissaladière-style wafer-thin tart with roast black pudding, braised chuck veal with creamy chickpeas and a chocolate and hazelnut praline pie to finish.;Air conditioning;[]
6245;L'Auberge du Pont des Pierres;France;Montanges;754 rue Lieutenant Paul-de-Vanssay, Montanges, 01200, France;46.1634661;5.8015098;100;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant on the road to Monts Jura is invariably busy! Chef Romain Blanc, who hails from the region, has no shortage of talent or ideas when it comes to cooking seasonal local produce: fish from Lake Geneva or nearby fish farms, pork and poultry from the surrounding area, local market gardeners and a herb garden. He also demonstrates a flair for preparing jus and a mastery of cooking processes, and makes a lot from scratch (including ice cream and bread). Bargain prices and service with a smile from Chloé, who will guide you through the nice selection of wines from independent winegrowers.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6246;Le Jardin Les Crayères;France;Reims;7 avenue du Général-Giraud, Reims, 51100, France;49.2408434;4.0505208;33;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The little sister of the Château les Crayères, housed in an outbuilding in the park, is a smart, very contemporary and elegant brasserie with its own veranda and terrace just opposite the herb garden. Flavoursome seasonal cooking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6247;Le Cerisier;France;Tournon-sur-Rhône;1 rue Saint-Joseph, Tournon-sur-Rhône, 07300, France;45.0657729;4.8334326;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The menu at this small restaurant with a modern interior makes your mouth water in anticipation of the hearty, unpretentious dishes and the house speciality, pâté en croûte, made with different ingredients as the seasons change. In the kitchen, a couple is at work, preparing delicious cuisine that highlights local produce such as Ardèche trout. The desserts are particularly meticulous – poached pear with mulled wine, vanilla and speculoos trifle, pear sorbet. The terrific wine list (600 labels) includes a judicious choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6248;Restaurant Anne & Matthieu Omont - Hôtel de France;France;Montmarault;1 rue Marx-Dormoy, Montmarault, 03390, France;46.3190731;2.9562153;93;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Treat yourself to a gourmet interlude in this establishment on the village high street. Chef, Matthieu Omont crafts masterful, boldly creative cuisine, to be enjoyed in a spruce modern setting. A champion of Bourbonnais produce, he also works with top-drawer seafood: fillet of whiting in a crust of cèpes, langoustine cream and risotto of Vernusse pleurote mushrooms, followed by a rum-flavoured raisin pannacotta, finely diced granny smith apples, a pear sorbet and a Piattelli-flavoured emulsion. Comfortable rooms, ideal for an overnight stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6249;Le Bistrot de Guillaume;France;Moulins;13 rue de Pont, Moulins, 03000, France;46.5643976;3.3318984;57;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Right in the centre of Moulins, the small dining area is light and intimate, already setting the tone, and we don't need to be asked twice to be shown to our table. But the best is yet to come: in his little kitchen, the chef-owner composes dishes that are delicate and intelligent to the joy of our tastebuds, such as his textbook perfect Provençal aioli.;Terrace;[]
6250;La Capitelle;France;Mirmande;1 rue du Boulanger, Mirmande, 26270, France;44.6992634;4.8357862;44;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of this charming medieval village in the Drôme Provençale, La Capitelle – the lovely, lilting name denotes a dry stone shelter used by shepherds and winegrowers – serves a small à la carte menu, plus a daily menu that is changed up regularly with the seasons. Traditional recipes are given a contemporary spin, and dishes are served in a pretty vaulted room with an imposing fireplace. In fine weather, the terrace commands views over the valley. They have a handful of guestrooms for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
6252;PY Restaurant;France;Lyon;16 cours Vitton, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7693113;4.851688;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this dinky brasserie in a smart neighbourhood, Pierre (in the kitchen) and Yuko (front of house) make the magic happen. In this contemporary decor, diners sample generous, well-crafted dishes. The à la carte menu in the evening is enriched with premium dishes such as hare pâté en croûte.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6253;Le Muratore;France;Évian-les-Bains;8 place du Docteur-Jean-Bernex, Évian-les-Bains, 74500, France;46.4006543;6.5912584;82;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The Muratore house is named after its former owner, a liquor-maker and confectioner. It stands on a pedestrian street of Évian overlooking an exquisite square with a fountain in its centre. Now a restaurant, it is in the hands of Marc Serres, who crafts wholesome regional fare. The menu is sensibly priced and the à la carte range stars noble ingredients, including fish from the lake, without forgetting a few hearty classics from Lyons. Shaded by a linden tree, the terrace is bliss in summertime.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6254;Winstub du Chambard;France;Kaysersberg;9-13 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Kaysersberg, 68240, France;48.1385904;7.2655719;69;true;false;Alsatian, Traditional Cuisine;The chef, Olivier Nasti, revisits all that Alsace's terroir has to offer: baeckeoffe and choucroute, onion tart and presskopf... Without forgetting the trout from the vallée d’Orbey, with white wine sauce, and an iced kougelhopf to die for. Tasty and generous, an ode to good food! Daily specials on the chalkboard too.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6256;Le Pantruche;France;Paris;3 rue Victor-Massé, Paris, 75009, France;48.8804947;2.3399142;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Pantruche was a 19C slang term for Paris... an apt name for this bistro whose chic vintage décor happily nurtures a 1940s-1950s vibe. As for the food, the chef and his small team put together tasty seasonal dishes in keeping with today’s bistronomic trend. Examples include a light, fluffy, velvety Grand Marnier soufflé, worthy of any fine dining establishment. A bright red awning offers shelter to a few tables on the pavement in typical Parisian fashion. As well as resolutely authentic, this restaurant offers eater-friendly prices.;;[]
6257;Abri Soba;France;Paris;10 rue Saulnier, Paris, 75009, France;48.8747039;2.3444157;90;false;false;Japanese;You may have heard of soba, Japanese pasta made with buckwheat, the reputation of which is currently snowballing around the planet. The chef of this restaurant has made soba his house speciality and serves it lunch and evening in an amazing variety of preparations: hot, cold, in stock or with finely sliced duck. Simply flavoursome – get out your chopsticks!;Counter dining;[]
6258;Winstub À Côté;France;Sierentz;2 rue Rogg-Haas, Sierentz, 68510, France;47.6535372;7.4552974;58;false;true;Regional Cuisine;An extension of Auberge St Laurent, this winstub gives diners a taste of Alsace – tarte flambée with marinated Scottish salmon, "granny's" home-made spaetzle – in a contemporary decor (designer furniture and light fittings, copper-topped counter). Unbeatable value for money and excellent service are the key to the success of this establishment: it's often fully booked!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6260;Les Canailles Pigalle;France;Paris;25 rue La Bruyère, Paris, 75009, France;48.8793235;2.3346319;79;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This pleasant restaurant was opened by a pair from Brittany who can boast impressive culinary backgrounds. Here, the name of the game is bistronomy and seasonal recipes. Specialities include beef tongue carpaccio with ravigote sauce, and rum baba with whipped vanilla cream – a real treat! Tip: if the restaurant is full, go to Le Comptoir Canaille, just a few doors down, where they serve more contemporary cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
6261;Au Pont Corbeau;France;Strasbourg;21 quai Saint-Nicolas, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5791113;7.750496;70;false;true;Alsatian;Experience local gastronomic specialities and traditional decor (Renaissance features, posters) in this restaurant next door to the Musée Alsacien, with its displays of popular art.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6264;L'Araignée Gourmande;France;Laragne-Montéglin;8 rue de la Paix, Laragne-Montéglin, 05300, France;44.3149388;5.8225646;48;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Settle at your table in this bright, modern interior and experience the talent of Thierry Chouin. This Breton chef may have a particular penchant for fish - based fare, but that doesn't mean he snubs lamb and potatoes. He fetes the ingredients with nicely turned - out dishes, each a lovely homage to tradition.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6265;Au Petit Relais;France;Coligny;445 Grande-Rue, Coligny, 01270, France;46.3846303;5.3456859;79;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant proposes exceptionally tasty dishes featuring lobster, fine fish, Bresse specialities and choice wines. The dining room is smart, and the service is friendly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
6266;L'Alcôve;France;Bayeux;31 ter rue Larcher, Bayeux, 14400, France;49.2756464;-0.7019807;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Just behind the cathedral, this restaurant is well known for its expertly crafted, market-fresh recipes as full of flavour as they are flawlessly prepared. Examples include spider crab with a dressing made with crab stock and frothy fromage blanc or saddle of rabbit roasted in butter, cannelloni of grilled aubergines and a punchy gravy. Ever popular, all the more so thanks to its eater-friendly prices.;Terrace;[]
6268;Hostellerie d'Héloïse;France;Cluny;7 route de Mâcon, Cluny, 71250, France;46.4254309;4.6652795;96;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Wholesome regional dishes – Burgundy snails, Charolais beef and a reduction of red wine from Mâcon, together with tempting traditional recipes (roast turbot, mashed cauliflower and veal gravy), have built the reputation of this hostelry, which also proposes more modern dishes and a splendid choice of wines by the glass. Lovely bright conservatory overlooking the River Grosne. Rooms for overnight stays.;Wheelchair access;[]
6269;Art'zain;France;Irissarry;20 place d'Ospitalia (Le bourg), Irissarry, 64780, France;43.2570495;-1.2325073;23;false;true;Farm to table;Artzain means "shepherd" in Basque – a tribute by the owner to his father. Located in the centre of the village, this converted barn has retained its rustic feel, with its exposed stone beams and walls, while sporting a designer style thanks to the furniture by Basque craftsman Alki. The menu features an enticing array of seasonal and predominantly local cuisine that doesn't disappoint, with dishes such as the flavoursome warm terrine of Kriaxera duck, Arto Gorria corn polenta galette, caramelised spring onions and crispy ventrèche.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6270;La Taverne Alsacienne;France;Ingersheim;99 rue de la République, Ingersheim, 68040, France;48.0954506;7.3049688;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Alsatian;Run by the Guggenbuhl family since 1964, this salmon-pink-fronted tavern has earned its reputation. Even those who know nothing about Alsace cuisine are smitten by the enticing regional dishes, washed down by fine wines from near and far! The fillet of zander, sautéed sauerkraut and Riesling sauce we sampled lingers with us still.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
6271;Mets et Vins;France;Bourg-en-Bresse;11 rue de la République, Bourg-en-Bresse, 01000, France;46.2032302;5.2272856;97;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This is the kingdom of Stéphane Prévalet, a champion of local produce and home-made fare who enjoys pushing traditional culinary boundaries. Examples include chicory and blue cheese upside-down pie or Dombes duckling with Bugey blackcurrant. A minimalist interior decorated with birch trunks sets the scene in this trendy establishment.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6272;La Table Bâgésienne;France;Bâgé-le-Châtel;19 Grande-Rue, Bâgé-le-Châtel, 01380, France;46.30794;4.92875;81;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Behind the façade of this former coaching inn lies a contemporary interior, complete with a glazed wine cellar, and hearty Bresse cuisine to make your mouth water… Pommes Anna with frogs' legs sautéed with a garlic butter cream, Bresse poultry with cream and vin jaune, or the traditional nougat glacé. Pleasant, quiet terrace to the rear.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6273;Le Pressoir de Bacchus;France;Blienschwiller;50 route des Vins, Blienschwiller, 67650, France;48.3417043;7.4194472;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Such is the renown of Sylvie Grucker and her son that this pretty restaurant on the wine route is greatly in demand. Sylvie combines traditional recipes with an inventive streak in a bid to showcase regional fare: bacon-flavoured choucroute soup or duck shepherd’s pie, mushrooms and 12-spice sauce, side by side perennial favourites like granddad’s snails, ravioles of carp in a creamy, smoked sauce or Sylvie’s meringue and ice cream extravaganza! Local winegrowers and producers from the village (thirty or so) take pride of place on the enticing wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6274;L'Olivier;France;Munster;2 rue Saint-Grégoire, Munster, 68140, France;48.0407592;7.1360919;42;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Olivier Lamard, former second-in-command to Michelin-starred Julien Binz, now has his own restaurant. He proposes modern cuisine that draws on the terroir of Alsace: soft cheese mousse, potato salad and home-smoked trout, pork from Goettelmann’s farm, and for dessert, pear with sesame. Nicely prepared dishes made from fine ingredients, some of which come from the chef's grandfather's garden. A charming place.;Air conditioning;[]
6275;Le Beaujolais;France;Belleville-en-Beaujolais;40 rue du Maréchal-Foch, Belleville-en-Beaujolais, 69220, France;46.1125928;4.7301958;87;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;With such a name, this Beaujolais could not do otherwise than pay tribute to a region famous for its fine food and wines! The friendly couple that runs this house has hit the nail on the head with hearty wholesome fare. Examples include traditional andouillette, whole grain mustard sauce and sautéed potatoes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6276;Le Rousseau;France;Le Pont-de-Claix;16 bis cours Saint-André, Le Pont-de-Claix, 38800, France;45.1254254;5.6983023;21;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In low-key, tasteful and contemporary premises, the new Le Rousseau is now more spacious and boasts a quiet alfresco area to the rear. Chef Élie Michel-Villaz, who remains forever faithful to his defining mantra, simplicity, rolls out a fresh, carefully crafted repertory, paired with lovingly selected wines (several hundred references – many natural or biodynamic), served in a casual atmosphere. A short supply chain business that is going strong. Simpler menu at lunchtime.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6277;Une Table à Deux;France;Toulouse;10 rue de la Pleau, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.5968455;1.4469377;23;true;true;Modern Cuisine;After learning the ropes in Toulouse, Morgane and Nicolas made a beeline for Korea and Malaysia to research new flavours. Back in their hometown, they have chosen the Carmes district to regale diners with playful recipes that blend Mediterranean and tropical flavours, resulting in impressively curated and beautifully balanced dishes. Fantastic value for money lunchtime menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6278;Balsamique;France;Wambrechies;13 place du Général-de-Gaulle, Wambrechies, 59118, France;50.6873909;3.0529174;84;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The youthful chef has more than one trick up his sleeve and his cuisine, poised between regional and modern, throbs with flavour. Examples include Tatin-style black pudding with cider apples. Daring recipes enhanced by impeccable produce (fish from Boulogne-sur-Mer, for example). Slick service. The peaceful little terrace is a real draw, especially on summer evenings!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6280;Le Bouchon Bourguignon;France;Tournus;1 rue Albert-Thibaudet, Tournus, 71700, France;46.565698;4.908016;33;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Generous, meticulous cuisine inspired by the culinary traditions of Burgundy is served in the contemporary setting of this annexe to Yohann Chapuis's fine dining restaurant. The regional classics are present and correct: "pâté croûte Maison Greuze", eggs meurette (in a red wine sauce), fresh frog's legs in a parsley sauce, Bresse chicken with morels and vin jaune, as well as more refined creations such as carpaccio of Charolais beef with verbena oil, cherry tomatoes and shavings of Comté. It makes a delightful change to see a list of wines served from magnums available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6281;Nougier;France;Fursac;2 place de l'Église, Fursac, 23290, France;46.1463409;1.5129695;28;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;For three generations, this delightful inn has been cultivating the art of hospitality and good food. The chef concocts meticulous dishes that toe the line between tradition and modernity and pay tribute to the seasons. So take a seat and order safe in the knowledge you will eat well!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6282;Mandoobar;France;Paris;7 rue d'Édimbourg, Paris, 75008, France;48.87939;2.3211699;77;false;false;Korean;Good authentic Korean restaurants are not two a penny in Paris, but this little restaurant, where the chef works behind his counter, is one of them: diners look on while Kim Kwang-Loc, as nimble-fingered as he is precise, creates the famous mandu (Korean dumplings) and tuna and beef tartares that make up the bulk of his minimalist menu. Passionate about Korean herbs, he seasons each of his delicate and tasty dishes with addictive flavours, perhaps in a quest to recreate his earliest culinary memories in Korea…;;[]
6283;52 Faubourg St-Denis;France;Paris;52 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Denis, Paris, 75010, France;48.8721222;2.3540461;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fans of neo-bistro aesthetics will love this place done out in bare concrete and exposed stone, where diners tuck into cuisine infused with Asian flavours, as well as time-honoured bistro classics such as pâté de campagne (rustic-style pâté) or leeks in vinaigrette. The food is nicely washed down with fine wines or craft beer, and you can round off your meal with coffee selected and roasted by the owner. Please note: no reservations.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6284;Le Radis Beurre;France;Paris;51 boulevard Garibaldi, Paris, 75015, France;48.8462355;2.3081096;59;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Diners are drawn here by the warm welcome, the buzzing atmosphere, the appetising menu written on a large blackboard and, above all, by the tasty, well-crafted cuisine of chef Jérôme Bonnet. His cooking is influenced by his origins – the South of France – as one can see in dishes such as the appetising shoulder of suckling pig sautéed in a pan with Tarbais beans au jus and roasted vegetables, or the excellent riz au lait with salt crystal dulce de leche. This place is all about comfort food simmering on the stove. A real favourite, and the ideal place to celebrate with friends!;;[]
6286;L'Atelier Flavien Valère;France;Langon;62 cours des Fossés, Langon, 33210, France;44.5549838;-0.247115;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;After honing his talents around southwest France, Flavien Valère has decided to treat Langon to his culinary flair. He knows his stuff, no doubt about that: impeccable cooking techniques, perfect seasonings, premium produce and carefully crafted recipes – everything is from scratch, to our delight! Eater-friendly priced lunchtime menu. Bookings advisable.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6288;Jouvence;France;Paris;172 bis rue du Faubourg-Saint-Antoine, Paris, 75012, France;48.8502734;2.3824694;36;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Not far from rue de Cîteaux, this restaurant in an apothecary-style shop dating back to the 1900s is not merely aesthetically pleasing. It serves modern cuisine packed with quality ingredients: scallop ceviche, fine Angus beef entrecôte… The chef knows how to draw out flavours with a generous touch, and the service is attentive.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6289;Auberge Pyrénées Cévennes;France;Paris;106 rue de la Folie-Méricourt, Paris, 75011, France;48.8680983;2.3685454;98;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Chef Pierre Négrevergne is really flourishing in this house that is over 100 years old. He delights diners with his tasty "grandmother's" cooking, which highlights French gastronomic heritage (home-made terrine, blanquette de veau à l'ancienne and grilled rice, millefeuille), served in generous portions. It is still a treat to eat here.;Air conditioning;[]
6290;Le Tire Bouchon;France;Lorient;45 rue Jules-le-Grand, Lorient, 56100, France;47.7486582;-3.3579756;37;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Pay little attention to the unremarkable façade of this restaurant, as the main focus is on the pretty dining room with its exposed beams and open fire. Refined traditional cuisine that follows the seasons is served. Friendly service with a smile.;;[]
6291;Le CasseNoix;France;Paris;56 rue de la Fédération, Paris, 75015, France;48.8534216;2.2952226;43;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Old signs, clocks and vintage furniture set the scene. As for the food, authenticity is the order of the day: hearty, down-to-earth dishes, such as white pudding and pâté en croûte inspired by those that the chef’s dad (a Meilleur Ouvrier de France no less!) used to make in Orléans… Amusing collection of nutcrackers picked up here and there by the owner's mum. A real cracker!;;[]
6292;La Vieille Forge;France;Kaysersberg;1 rue des Écoles, Kaysersberg, 68240, France;48.1387112;7.2623713;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Beyond the rustic façade of this charming 16C house, some lovely surprises lie in store: chef Laurine Gutleben's dishes give pride of place to fresh produce and free rein to creativity, for instance the scallops with light hollandaise, braised leeks and gomasio popcorn. Well-chosen wine list, particularly from Alsace but not only.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6293;Le Jour du Poisson;France;Saint-Denis-d'Oléron;3 rue de l'Ormeau, Saint-Denis-d'Oléron, 17650, France;46.033275;-1.3797735;38;true;true;Seafood;Run by a youthful team, this friendly little bistro at the tip of the island is often fully booked. The menu, as short as it is tempting, is everything it's cracked up to be: fish, from local fish auctions, features in many guises, short supply chains and natural wines are favoured, the bread is made in-house with flour sourced from Oléron. Agnolotti of langoustines, lemon butter and herbs is the signature dish.;Air conditioning;[]
6294;U Licettu;France;Cuttoli;Plaine de Cuttoli, Cuttoli, 20167, France;41.9639362;8.8458305;77;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Could this pink-rendered villa, decked in flowers and overlooking the gulf, have found the secret of authentic Corsican food? Whatever the case, you can be certain that you will sample wholehearted, full-bodied dishes made with first-class ingredients in keeping with time-honoured culinary traditions: nothing goes to waste from pig’s trotters to tails, the meat is slowly spit-roasted on the open fire or the lady of the house hovering nearby to check you finish your plate. Beverages included in the menu. Highly recommended.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6295;Le Balcon;France;Combeaufontaine;2 Grande-Rue, Combeaufontaine, 70120, France;47.7119734;5.8879472;45;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;Chef Jean-Philippe Gauthier is upholding the traditions of this former coaching inn, which has been in the family since 1951. House specialties include: rabbit terrine with foie gras, chicken with vin jaune and morels, and a knockout trolley of matured cheeses. Meals are served in an interior that blends character and authenticity. Charming welcome and service. Rooms for overnight stays.;Wheelchair access;[]
6296;L'Angle Saint-Laurent;France;Bayeux;2 rue des Bouchers, Bayeux, 14400, France;49.277678;-0.7009128;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The arrival of a new couple at the helm, who worked for many years alongside the former owners, has changed nothing in terms of the establishment’s concept or philosophy: regional produce is cast in the leading role (Bayeux pork, Normandy oysters, Carrouges gruyere) of the appetising lineup. On the corner of Rue St Laurent and Rue des Bouchers, the setting is also as appealing as ever with exposed stone, painted beams and soft lighting. What’s not to like?;;[]
6297;La Maison de Celou;France;Châteauneuf-de-Gadagne;5 rue Saint-Jouin, Châteauneuf-de-Gadagne, 84470, France;43.9288995;4.9456783;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Clinging to the ramparts of this historical village, the delightful Maison embodies the art de vivre of Provence. The chef crafts bright, flavoursome dishes, such as a supreme of free-range poultry, Roman-style gnocchi and meatballs in jus. The decadent desserts are fiendishly tempting. Superlative sweeping view over Mt Ventoux and the Luberon mountain range from the terrace.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6298;Relais de l'Abbaye;France;Charlieu;415 route du Beaujolais, Charlieu, 42190, France;46.1557916;4.173191;40;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This modern Relais, looking out onto the surrounding meadows, is anchored in local culinary traditions. The chef is passionate about fine ingredients and showcases regional producers (Charlieu andouille, Charolais meat, cheese etc) in contemporary, hearty dishes. Pleasant guestrooms for an overnight stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6299;Le Relais des Salines;France;Le Grand-Village-Plage;Port des Salines, Le Grand-Village-Plage, 17370, France;45.8621099;-1.2288191;23;true;false;Seafood;This waterside bistro showcases seafood flavours and super-fresh produce. The menu sails between timeless classics (oysters, confit of octopus, lentils, mustard-flavoured sabayon and the chef’s lemon pie) and more spur-of-the-moment recipes. Inside, this former oyster shed upholds its heritage, while the terrace overlooking the marshes is blissful.;Terrace;[]
6300;Bistrot Saveurs;France;Castres;5 rue Sainte-Foy, Castres, 81100, France;43.6054304;2.2456883;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;British chef Simon Scott worked his way from London to Provence, before setting up shop here in the Tarn département. The vivid red façade leads diners into a vibrant and cosy pop-inspired decor. This eclectic chef and master craftsman works exclusively with good-quality (local) ingredients, in a bid to serve his guests precise, colourful and tasty dishes, such as just-seared bluefin tuna, flame-burnt aubergine caviar, quinoa with three vegetables and shellfish broth with Middle Eastern spices. This Bistrot des Saveurs is certainly aptly named!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6301;Le Flaveur;France;Concarneau;4 rue Duquesne, Concarneau, 29900, France;47.8694755;-3.9166643;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is tucked away in a side street set back from the marina and the walled city. Harmony reigns in the kitchen, where a duo of chefs composes dishes made with ultra-fresh ingredients. Locally sourced produce takes pride of place on the menu: buckwheat, the daily catch of small local boats, Brittany-reared pork, Bruyère Blanche poultry, farm-range eggs, without forgetting the excellent homemade bread.;Wheelchair access;[]
6302;L'Écureuil;France;Clermont-Ferrand;18 rue Saint-Adjutor, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7789926;3.0804584;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This modern bistro with its chic country decor serves appetising market-fresh cuisine: duck breast with black olives, pork cheeks braised in red wine, French toast made with brioche... The short menu is chalked up on the blackboard, and a simpler lunch deal is available at a snip.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6303;Le Beauvoir;France;Bourges;1 avenue Marx-Dormoy, Bourges, 18000, France;47.090477;2.4015398;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Annie and Mickaël Landaud are at the helm of an elegant family establishment which is quite a favourite with the locals. The bluish tones and plant-inspired artwork pay homage to the nearby marshlands… The chef conjures up modern, appetising dishes, adding a playful new spin to a traditional Gallic score. Alfresco dining in the rear courtyard.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6304;Les Quatre Saisons;France;Aurillac;10 rue Jean-Baptiste-Champeil, Aurillac, 15000, France;44.929825;2.4469405;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The cooking of Didier Guibert, whose restaurant is located in a quiet little street in the city centre, is sincere and nicely done. He only works with fresh produce – and in particular meat supplied by his two brothers, butchers by trade. A well-run place.;Air conditioning;[]
6306;Italie là-bas;France;Avignon;23 rue de la Bancasse, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9477652;4.8063376;46;true;true;Italian;This enthusiastic Italian couple is living proof that Italians do it better. While he pampers guests front of house, she rustles up delicious Italian dishes, some highly creative, to propose tasting menus that include a vegetarian option. Buon appetito!;Terrace;[]
6307;La Cour de Rémi;France;Bermicourt;1 rue Baillet, Bermicourt, 62130, France;50.4062836;2.2291703;43;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;After pursuing a career abroad, the chef has returned to his roots, to the family's former hunting lodge, to devote himself to cooking – his earliest passion. In this convivial place, he has perfectly mastered generous traditional cuisine, from cooking to seasoning. We love the terrine with home-made sourdough bread and gherkins from the estate in vinegar. The plus: overnight accommodation in a cabin on stilts!;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6308;Au Bon Accueil;France;Richardménil;1 rue de Laval, Richardménil, 54630, France;48.5916357;6.1659064;97;true;false;Modern Cuisine;You will first be won over by the vintage charm of this 1960’s house, before you meet the talented team of the brother (in the kitchen) and his sister (in the dining room), who are both fast gaining in confidence. The food is on-point, the wine cellar savvy and the terrace very pleasant in season.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6309;Le Martin Bel Air;France;Saint-Martin-du-Tertre;3 place du 19-Mars-1962, Saint-Martin-du-Tertre, 89100, France;48.2123244;3.2584615;15;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This completely renovated country bistro opposite the town hall welcomes you into a natural, contemporary setting (pale wood, cork wall decorations, black ceiling). The chef, who has trained in some of the region's finest establishments, creates modern and sophisticated market-fresh dishes that are unbeatable value for money. Think beef tartare with wasabi, onion pickles and spicy carrot – a punchy starter with harmonious flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6310;La Terrasse;France;Meyronne;Place de l'Église, Meyronne, 46200, France;44.8770129;1.5769684;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The terrace under the vine-shaded pergola is the perfect spot in fine weather, while in winter you can take refuge inside, beneath the medieval vaults of this former 11C stronghold, done out with contemporary furnishings. On the menu: dishes with bold flavours, featuring regional producers: lamb from the Lot, farm-reared pork, and poultry from Mayrac etc. View of the cliffs and the Dordogne.;Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6311;La Croix d'Or;France;Le Pin-la-Garenne;6 rue de la Herse, Le Pin-la-Garenne, 61400, France;48.4408769;0.5461498;24;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This welcoming hostelry, which belonged to the chef’s great grandparents, boasts an authentic family atmosphere. After learning the ropes in prestigious restaurants, the chef has returned to his roots in the company of his wife, who hails from the southwest as you might be able to guess from her accent. A quintessential French country inn, particularly when lunching on the small patio in fine weather.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6313;L'AO - L'Aigle d'Or;France;Rimbach-près-Guebwiller;5 rue Principale, Rimbach-près-Guebwiller, 68500, France;47.905;7.1568596;39;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;A young generation has brought a zest of modernity by way of more contemporary plating techniques and recipes (octopus with miso broth, or braised breast of pork with bbq-style jus and chimichurri…) all the while continuing to celebrate regional traditions (brawn, frogs’ legs, game etc). Practical rooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6315;La Falène Bleue;France;Lannepax;121 place de l'Armagnac, Lannepax, 32190, France;43.8004962;0.2264672;39;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fabien, in the kitchen, and Hélène, front of house, have combined their two first names and come up with La Falène Bleue, where life is good and so is the food. Everything is both simple and delightful, from the carefully presented dishes (featuring ingredients sourced entirely from local producers) to the interior, decorated with paintings and vintage objects. This restaurant in the small village of Lannepax is surrounded by vineyards and has a pleasant terrace to the rear. The lunch set menu changes weekly and is good value for money.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6316;Clamato;France;Paris;80 rue de Charonne, Paris, 75011, France;48.8536111;2.3806195;29;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Inspired by the oyster bars of the East Coast of the United States, this outpost of Septime owes its name to a cocktail that is very popular in Quebec, a Bloody Mary of sorts with the addition of clam juice – needless to say, you can try one here! The place has all the makings of a bistronomy hit, with its trendy decor and short menu that puts fish and seafood and vegetables centre stage, and draws on international influences. The ingredients are chosen with great care and prepared as simply as possible, then presented in plates for sharing. Please note that reservations are not possible: first come, first served!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6318;Côté Saisons;France;Laroque-des-Albères;10 avenue de la Côte-Vermeille, Laroque-des-Albères, 66740, France;42.5224669;2.9358838;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Let's set the scene: a 19C building surrounded by greenery, with large bay windows, a flower-decked garden and a pretty terrace to cater to all seasons. On the menu are tasty, well-crafted dishes, eg warm calf's head with Charroux mustard, Cerdagne pig confit with honey-ginger, tender chuck of beef and pan-fried foie gras. In addition, the service is all smiles.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6319;Au Bon Accueil;France;Juvigny-sous-Andaine;23 place Saint-Michel, Juvigny-sous-Andaine, 61140, France;48.5520169;-0.5083354;22;false;false;Creative;This restaurant with a bright, contemporary interior is true to its name when it promises a warm welcome. Chef Gaëtan Crespin works with good seasonal produce, most of it sourced locally, to craft creative and technically on-point cuisine. A shining example comes in the form of his scallops, endive and clementine, or rack of pork, parsley and spelt… And with excellent value for money guaranteed, what's not to love?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6320;Paris Méditerranée;France;Sète;47 rue Pierre-Semard, Sète, 34200, France;43.40585;3.699485;19;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name pays tribute to singer-songwriter Georges Brassens, a local lad, and also to Mediterranean cuisine which takes pride of place on the menu, depending on the chef’s mood, (a former Parisian) and the catch of the day. In a quiet side street near the canal, the chef deftly crafts fresh, mainly maritime produce, with a weakness for forthright, no-nonsense flavours such as sashimi of flathead grey mullet and cream of smoked anchovy. We tasted a heart-warming slab of hake served with homemade gnocchi flavoured with wild garlic. Fried squid, risotto and spicy stock is another house specialty. The chef’s wife, a native of Sète, smilingly pampers guests in the rustic dining room appointed with red bench seating.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6323;La Méditerranée;France;Paris;2 place de l'Odéon, Paris, 75006, France;48.8500187;2.3386558;43;true;true;Seafood;The frescoes evoke the Mediterranean in this restaurant opposite the historic Odéon Theatre. The maritime inspired cuisine, in which particular attention is paid to first-class ingredients, is influenced by the sunny South of France. House specialties include bouillabaisse, carpaccio of seabass, honey-glazed seabream… Affordable menu, pricier à la carte offering.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
6324;Jeux 2 Goûts;France;Châteauroux;40 rue Grande, Châteauroux, 36000, France;46.81291;1.6941;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Having settled in his native region after several years spent in high - end Parisian establishments, Christophe Marchais is bringing a dose of culinary flair to Châteauroux. He prepares tasty and creative dishes, inspired by a building steeped in history. The best restaurant in the city.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6325;Auberge des Chenets;France;Valloux;10 D606, Valloux, 89200, France;47.5117919;3.841321;89;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;You soon forget the road just outside, as you snuggle up near the fireplace of this pleasant Auberge! The menu stars simple dishes of Burgundian inspiration that are nicely crafted and packed with flavour: slow-cooked egg and snails in a red wine sauce, guinea fowl supreme, puréed potato, braised endive, Bourdaloue tart – and the bill won't break the bank.;Air conditioning;[]
6327;Le Saint-Eutrope;France;Clermont-Ferrand;4 rue Saint-Eutrope, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7813394;3.0824063;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Michael Hazlewood, a New Zealander, and his partner Manon Descombats have struck upon a winning formula: a vintage vibe, friendly atmosphere, low prices, a wine list suggesting a passion for natural wines and unadorned plating that belies the technical refinement of the cuisine. No fancy presentations here, just trendy, family-style cooking (yes, it's possible!).;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6328;Auberge des Aryelets;France;Aulon;Place du Village, Aulon, 65240, France;42.8509638;0.2965653;49;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;You have to gain a little altitude to reach this village high up in the Pyrenees, which champions its exceptional natural heritage with understandable pride. On the central square, a young couple has injected a sense of enthusiasm into this place, honouring the region's traditions and produce: free-range slow-cooked egg with Noir de Bigorre ham. Other dishes are more contemporary, such as royal sea bream with sashimi and asparagus. The appealing wine list boasts almost 500 wines.;Terrace;[]
6329;La Part des Anges;France;Castres;5 boulevard Raymond-Vittoz, Castres, 81100, France;43.6038911;2.244465;39;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The market-fresh menu demonstrates deep respect for the seasons and a desire to highlight the work of local producers. Healthy appetites are encouraged and appreciated and the front-of-house team is pleasantly attentive. Its enduring popularity with the locals says it all!;Air conditioning;[]
6330;Auberge de Combes;France;Combes;Le Bourg, Combes, 34240, France;43.6027001;3.0462342;97;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This quintessential inn – typical of the area – stands on the heights of the Orb Valley. The terroir expresses itself in no uncertain terms: the food and the landscape share a subtle yet rugged edge. Semi-cooked foie gras over grapevine embers, wood pigeon roasted in a wine sauce, sweet chestnut and pear tart… Meals are served within hundred-year-old stone walls or on the patio which commands a sweeping view over the valley. To be washed down with a glass of Faugères, of course!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
6331;L'Ourdissoir;France;Cholet;40 rue Saint-Bonaventure, Cholet, 49300, France;47.0593903;-0.8765558;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Slightly outside the city centre, this modest establishment, whose name refers to a rich weaving heritage, sports a warm interior of stone and wood that provides the perfect foil for spot-on, modern food that generously keeps pace with the seasons. Elegant presentation and a concise, original culinary score, with unexpected combinations, like veal tartare paired with beetroot and raspberries in a masterful blend of fresh, acidic and sweet notes. More traditional but just as deftly crafted and tasty is the combination of Paimpol cranberry beans, loin of cod and a mild curry emulsion. The desserts are fully equal to this feelgood feast of culinary delights.;Air conditioning;[]
6332;L'Auberge du Laminak;France;Montcy-Notre-Dame;Route de Nouzonville, Montcy-Notre-Dame, 08090, France;49.7950025;4.7498852;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this charming inn on the edge of the forest, the Basque country – where the chef is from – meets fine produce from the Ardennes. The result is tasty and skilfully made dishes, such as the slow-cooked egg with piperade and Basque ham.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6333;Le Boudes La Vigne;France;Boudes;Place de la Mairie, Boudes, 63340, France;45.458736;3.184899;21;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Built on old fortifications, this pleasant restaurant lies at the heart of a wine-growing village that produces Boudes, one of the five wines of Auvergne's vineyards. Christian Coutarel, a jovial chef, works away in the kitchen preparing generous and flavoursome traditional cuisine, without ruling out more modern dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6335;L'Émotion;France;Puy-en-Velay;13 place Cadelade, Puy-en-Velay, 43000, France;45.0434718;3.8883818;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine;From one year to the next and from one location to another, local chef-owner Michaël Ruat has been regaling the lucky diners of Puy-en-Velay. The interior sports natural materials and designer details (glazed wine cellar). The food forges a culinary course between regional Haute Loire ingredients (green lentils, Fin Gras du Mézenc beef) and a very modern repertoire of dishes (bluefin tuna, grilled watermelon and feta, sauce vierge and chorizo Bellota).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6336;La Merenda;France;Nice;4 rue Raoul-Bosio, Nice, 06000, France;43.696531;7.2730239;58;true;false;Provençal;A charmingly simple, old-fashioned little restaurant, where Dominique Le Stanc prepares delicious local dishes (pissaladière, tripe à la niçoise, stockfish, chard pie, lemon tart etc) to be enjoyed at tightly packed tables. N.B. no telephone – drop in to book a table.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6337;L'Évidence;France;Dijon;53 rue Jeannin, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3217416;5.04689;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;After honing his skills in top houses, Julien Burdin is enjoying his well-deserved success: knockout plating, premium ingredients and crisp, legible flavours, illustrated by ham and parsley terrine, mustard-flavoured whipped cream and onion pickles. The à la carte range highlights superior produce, like blue lobster, vegetable risotto and a seafood, tomato and wine sauce. Polished service.;Air conditioning;[]
6338;La Table d'Inomoto;France;Saint-André-de-Cubzac;85 rue Nationale, Saint-André-de-Cubzac, 33240, France;44.9929332;-0.4480008;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This endearing bistro has acquired a faithful crowd of regulars, enchanted by the weekly changing menu. Chef Seiji Inomoto expertly crafts fine Franco-Japanese fare, in which "humble" ingredients are taken to new heights thanks to flawless cooking and astute seasoning (panko breadcrumbs, miso, soy marinated veggies). The food is good, often unusual, and you won't believe the value for money. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6339;La Mandale;France;Nantes;32 rue Léon-Jamin, Nantes, 44000, France;47.21951;-1.559135;33;false;true;Farm to table;Picture a Klein blue frontage and a trendy bistro furnished with assorted antiques and numerous knick-knacks that is packed to the seams with smiling diners. It seems that Léo Huet, like other chefs of his generation, has hit upon the recipe for success: intriguing, tangy dishes rich in fresh premium produce, such as smoked mussels, kaffir, Thai basil and pistachio or steak with Gorilla pepper, kimchi, shiso and cherries, all with contrasting flavours that surprise and titillate the tastebuds. At dinner, the food becomes distinctly high flying as diners prepare to take their time to do justice to the excellent dishes recommended and explained by Maximilien, the chef’s associate, in a pleasantly unstuffy, relaxed vibe.;Terrace;[]
6340;Hyacinthe & Robert;France;Pontivy;100 rue Nationale, Pontivy, 56300, France;48.0617678;-2.9673556;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Damien Le Quillec named his restaurant after his two grandfathers. In this unusual setting – previously a garage, cleverly converted into a contemporary loft – he channels his talent into crafting ambitious dishes that appeal to the modern palate. Meanwhile, he has opened a convivial little bistro next door – Numéro 100, where he serves bistronomy fare in a home-from-home atmosphere.;Wheelchair access;[]
6341;Le Saisonnier;France;Roye;56 rue de la Verrerie, Roye, 70200, France;47.6774416;6.5356996;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A chef with an impressive CV and his wife have brought this old farmhouse to life with considerable panache. Expect meticulous, well-crafted, beautifully plated dishes showcasing marriages of flavours that are spot on. This is cuisine that revisits the classics, drawing on ingredients that are firmly rooted in the region: morels, old Comté cheese, vin jaune, Morteau sausage etc. Pleasant, peaceful terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6342;Le Bistrot de Villedieu;France;Villedieu;21 place de la Libération, Villedieu, 84110, France;44.2840228;5.0342051;70;true;false;Provençal;Laurent Azoulay curates Provençal fare in a locally sourced bistro register. Everything tastes of something in the flawlessly executed, characterful repertory and some of the dishes are cooked in the wood-burning oven of the open kitchen. Meals are served in a contemporary bistro setting, or, in fine weather, on the shaded terrace on the village square.;Terrace;[]
6343;Le Margote;France;Le Havre;50 quai Michel-Féré, Le Havre, 76600, France;49.4895114;0.1111413;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;In his restaurant overlooking the Bassin du Roi, chef Gauthier Teissere is assisted by Marguerite (his wife) front of house. He delivers contemporary, creative cuisine, jazzed up with the occasional nod to Asia. The stylish, snug interior is the perfect foil for dishes that reverently respect the seasons. Each dish is a masterpiece – not least the tender pork belly with a celeriac purée and smoked emulsion, or the generous pollack with cauliflower and capers.;Terrace;[]
6344;Les Jardins;France;Parnac;1533 route du Port-de-l'Angle, Parnac, 46140, France;44.4934193;1.3156241;17;true;true;Creative;This country restaurant has put down its roots in a peaceful winegrowing village in a bend of the River Lot. The wine barn of a former winery is the venue for youthful Marius Halter to whisk up delicious modern recipes in which fine local produce features prominently, without forgoing exquisitely balanced creative touches (spices, sweet and sour blends). Concise organic wine list, friendly, smiling table service and pretty patio in the garden.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6346;Briket' Bistrot;France;Guéthary;142 rue de l'Église, Guéthary, 64210, France;43.4196079;-1.6060294;97;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;On the heights of the picturesque village of Guéthary, the Ibarboure family hotel also operates this pleasant bistro, independent from their fine dining restaurant. The chef crafts meticulous, delicate and flavoursome food in an uncluttered setting. Basque ingredients dominate the generous dishes of the concise menu: Bayonne ham, bellota chorizo, Banka trout, Ardi-Gasna cheese. A youthful, friendly team and sensible prices. A real treat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6347;La Table de Pablo;France;Villars;1713 route de Rustrel, Hameau Les Petits-Cléments, Villars, 84400, France;43.9291305;5.4200127;91;true;true;Farm to table;Delicate and decidedly creative cuisine based on good regional ingredients: this restaurant surrounded by vines and cherry trees is a real find. Try the surprise menu, inspired by the offerings of the markets and small-scale local producers. The chef-patron takes care of everything himself, both in the dining room and the kitchen. Special mention for the peaceful terrace, where you can hear the cicadas' call.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6348;Arkadia;France;Vallon-Pont-d'Arc;9 rue du Barry, Vallon-Pont-d'Arc, 07150, France;44.4079089;4.3949041;53;false;true;Creative;In the historical centre of this village near the Ardèche Gorges, the chef, who is originally from Brittany, confidently sets about regaling diners with locally sourced ingredients (vegetables and cheeses in particular). The menu, renewed every month, is packed with indulgent and generous dishes. Front of house, Philippine's good humour sets the tone.;Terrace;[]
6349;Les Plaisirs;France;Peillon;2 rue Puada-dau-Gourguet, Peillon, 06440, France;43.7779818;7.3819396;39;false;true;Regional Cuisine;This friendly family-run inn is tucked away in a village high in the hinterland of Nice. The young owner-chef, descended from a long line of restaurant owners, throws his heart and soul into preparing Provençal recipes using impeccably selected regional produce. Authentic flavours, fuss-free plating, enticing recipes and eater-friendly prices! What more do we need to say?;;[]
6351;Auberge du Pont de la Zorn;France;Weyersheim;2 rue de la République, Weyersheim, 67720, France;48.7105317;7.8003971;16;true;false;Alsatian, Country cooking;Marquetry art from Atelier Spindler, antiques, bleached beams and rough wooden tables: the dining area displays its Alsatian heritage with pride! On the menu: tasty regional specialities, tartes flammées, but also Breton turbot with shrimp bisque and risotto venere, and delicious desserts, like this raspberry-meets-geranium from the garden. Bucolic terrace on the banks of the River Zorn, impeccable welcome and service – this place deserves its success.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6352;L'Alicanta;France;Le Rozier;Route de Meyrueis, Le Rozier, 48150, France;44.1903716;3.2090457;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;L'Alicanta has been on the scene for a while, perched on the banks of the River Jonte, in the exceptional setting of the Gorges du Tarn. The chef puts in a solid performance, his cooking is replete with distinct flavours and his dishes are brilliantly assembled. Everything here is home-made and the menu changes with every season. Absolutely delicious!;Car park,Garden or park;[]
6353;Le Biniou;France;Pléneuf-Val-André;121 rue Clemenceau, Pléneuf-Val-André, 22370, France;48.5895315;-2.5525543;66;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The chef draws his inspiration from deepest Brittany, illustrated by dishes such as crumbly buckwheat in butter and shallots, but is also open to other influences, as the fillet of whiting, lemon balm and watercress coulis demonstrate. Deftly crafted food, cheerful service, a digestible bill and a location just a few knots from the beach. The quintessence of Brittany.;;[]
6355;La Table de Léo;France;Saint-Avit-Sénieur;13 rue de l'Abbaye (Le Bourg), Saint-Avit-Sénieur, 24440, France;44.7746774;0.8159677;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This stone - built house in the heart of the village has a pretty terrace overlooking the church square. Inside, you will discover a great little restaurant with a chef who dares to branch out from the usual regional fare. He pays special attention to his ingredients and how best to present and cook them.;Terrace;[]
6356;L'Hibiscus;France;Orléans;175 rue de Bourgogne, Orléans, 45000, France;47.9002687;1.9111469;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a bustling pedestrian street, the façade is discreet. Venture inside for fresh ingredients, original recipes and modern cuisine, courtesy of Céline Lefebvre, a chef with a proven track record. No à la carte, but a short set menu changing regularly abreast of the seasons and availability. Reasonable prices.;Wheelchair access;[]
6357;Vidal;France;Saint-Julien-Chapteuil;Place du Marché, Saint-Julien-Chapteuil, 43260, France;45.0327554;4.0624497;81;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;At this restaurant, which opened in 1984, the Vidal family serve up a delicious repertoire of dishes that are an intelligent take on tradition: tasty dishes that shine a light on small-scale local producers (of, for example, Noire du Velay lamb, AOP Fin Gras du Mézenc beef). Aurélien's pâté en croûte is quite a technical feat and deserves a special mention. For hearty but simpler fare, head next door to Le Bistrot de Justin, which is only open for weekday lunch. Excellent value for money.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6358;La Belle Étoile;France;La Roque-Gageac;285 promenade de la Batellerie (Le Bourg), La Roque-Gageac, 24250, France;44.8259764;1.1823189;43;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Whether by moonlight or sunlight, welcome to this pretty property in the heart of a Dordogne village. The aromas wafting out of the kitchen have been tantalising diners for four generations now! Beautifully presented recipes that err towards traditional and wholesome, such as crispy sweetbread paired with a crunchy tartlet of celeriac and onion milk. Small guestrooms are available to prolong your stay in this enchanting village.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
6359;Akashon;France;Chamonix-Mont-Blanc;L'Heliopic, 50 place de l'Aiguille-du-Midi, Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, 74400, France;45.9179689;6.8704552;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Part of L’Heliopic hotel resort, Akashon turns out hearty, flavoursome food poised between local gastronomy and more modern fare, such as a tonnato-style tartare of veal and lobster. Untreated metal and granite set the scene in the minimalist interior, the terrace of which commands a fantastic view of the mountains.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6360;Le Nid;France;Flayosc;37 boulevard Jean-Moulin, Flayosc, 83780, France;43.53454;6.3946225;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An establishment run by charming people: Emilie takes care of the customer's every need, while the chef rustles up seasonal cuisine, full of freshness and flavour, making the most of short food supply chains and local producers. A gourmet hideaway that fills up every day and offers excellent value and maximum dining pleasure.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6361;Le Bistro des Glycines;France;Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil;4 avenue de Laugerie, Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil, 24620, France;44.9407447;1.0073713;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine;One of the undeniable bonuses of this hotel is its excellent bistro! The dining room-conservatory serves (lunchtime only) sensibly priced menus in tune with the zeitgeist, such as gravlax of Eyzies trout with a smoked cream cheese sauce or shoulder of lamb, confit and smoked in a casserole dish. Flavour, generosity and respect for the seasons set the tone for chef Pascal Lombard’s creative and enticing culinary score – we’ll be back for more!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6362;Ô en Couleur;France;Oucques;9 rue de Beaugency, Oucques, 41290, France;47.822947;1.2954536;93;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the colourful, contemporary interior with its large glass façade, or on the terrace in the leafy garden, tuck into the chef's well-crafted dishes concocted with the finest ingredients. Gribiche-style head cheese, pan-fried beef and crumbled offal, small pot of cream and a madeleine… Appealing to the palate, it's also easy on the wallet. Comfortable and colourful guestrooms are available, should you wish to prolong your stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6363;La Gazette;France;Evreux;7 rue Saint-Sauveur, Evreux, 27000, France;49.025604;1.1458837;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Inside this small half - timbered building, the trendy decor harmoniously blends refinement with the charm of timeworn beams. As for the seasonal cuisine, it showcases the finest ingredients. A memorable experience!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6364;La Chaumière;France;Font-Romeu;96 avenue Emmanuel-Brousse, Font-Romeu, 66120, France;42.5052975;2.0433532;19;false;true;Catalan;Put your skis away! You won't be able to resist this lovely thatched cottage at the entrance to the resort with an interior where wood predominates. On the menu find a fine selection of Catalan dishes, delicious tapas and good regional wines. The proprietor likes the finer things in life (choice meats, locally grown vegetables) and has even set up a ham cellar!;Terrace;[]
6365;Le Saint-Georges;France;Palavas-les-Flots;4 boulevard Maréchal-Foch, Palavas-les-Flots, 34250, France;43.5265905;3.9312468;43;false;false;Regional Cuisine;In his restaurant, just a roll of the dice from the casino, Paul Courtaux doesn’t gamble with our appetites. He crafts vibrant, flavoursome cuisine, which cleverly shines the spotlight on regional produce, illustrated by frothy cold fish soup with an aïoli of cuttlefish and mussels, or a slice of Ségala veal simmered in lemon, basil, aubergines, tomatoes and parmesan… The splendid regional wine list deserves special mention, as does the charismatic welcome.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6366;Vigne en Foule;France;Gaillac;80 place de la Libération, Gaillac, 81600, France;43.9001435;1.8980057;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A pleasant bar-restaurant serving fine bistro cuisine with a twist, together with a handful of meat dishes designed to share (including suckling pig, veal chop). Tuck into modern and indulgent dishes, such as cod with a fish suquet jus and patatas fritas with rouille – from spring onwards, you can dine on the appealing terrace. The wine cellar boasts a head-spinning selection of almost 300 different wines!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6367;L'Agape;France;Avignon;21 place des Corps-Saints, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9445551;4.8078128;83;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Julien Gleize set up his restaurant on this pleasant square in the heart of the Cité des Papes in June 2014. The chef looks totally fulfilled as he works away in the kitchens, composing hearty, cleverly devised dishes, in which seasonal products are nicely showcased.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6368;Café Brochier;France;Saint-Julien-en-Vercors;4 place de la Fontaine, Saint-Julien-en-Vercors, 26420, France;45.0498477;5.4487788;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This handsome building is an institution in this Vercors village. Dating from 1867, it is home to a historical cafe adorned with frescoes dating back to 1912. Locally sourced ingredients from the Vercors plateau play the lead roles on the menu, which changes regularly. Respect for the seasons goes hand in hand with respect for the produce, culinary skill and flavour. Three guestrooms upstairs.;Terrace;[]
6370;Les Maisons Du'O - Le Bistro Panoramique;France;Vaison-la-Romaine;16 rue Gaston-Gevaudan, Vaison-la-Romaine, 84110, France;44.2390826;5.0723295;80;false;true;Farm to table;Locally grown tomatoes and fruit, Ventoux spelt and pork: the chef hits the spot every time courtesy of modern recipes rich in Provençal accents, like baked croaker paired with fennel in aioli and a foamy bisque or a cassolette of gambas and squid. Excellent value for money and a knock-out view of the Ouvèze from the spacious contemporary dining room.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6371;Cartouches;France;Toulouse;38 rue Pierre-Paul-Riquet, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.60474;1.4542;51;false;false;Farm to table;In the picturesque and lively neighbourhood of Saint-Aubin, this tiny bistro is always busy! Chef Nicolas Brousse and his wife take great pleasure in serving up tasty, carefully prepared dishes. And in keeping with this spirit of conviviality, why not share a fine steak (butcher's choice – for two people)? This goes down very well with a natural wine from the extensive selection. The set menu changes every week.;Air conditioning;[]
6373;Bistrot d'Antoine;France;Nice;27 rue de la Préfecture, Nice, 06300, France;43.69635;7.2762832;63;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The lilting accent of the South of France can be detected in this bistro, where a really convivial atmosphere reigns. Things hot up in the kitchen, with dishes such as old-fashioned pork casserole or knife-cut beef tartare – only the best makes the cut here. Crowded? Well, yes: Antoine has a huge (and well-deserved) success on his hands.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6374;L'Atelier L'Art des Mets;France;Taillades;500 route de Robion, Taillades, 84300, France;43.8438177;5.0806265;34;true;false;Farm to table;The chef proposes neoteric, distinctive cuisine, whose mainstay is wild herbs, which he learned to know through a local herb picker. Goosefoot, wild lemon balm, purslane, mugwort... The culinary score is poetic and rich in flavour, illustrated by Ventoux pork with helichrysum-flavoured poichichade. Consider us smitten!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6376;Le Grand Saint-Benoît;France;Saint-Benoît-sur-Loire;7 place Saint-André, Saint-Benoît-sur-Loire, 45730, France;47.8107648;2.3062427;74;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This warm traditional restaurant boasts a pretty terrace and a spruce interior in the heart of the village, where the poet Max Jacob is buried. An enticing menu of deftly crafted dishes depicted by subtle blends of flavours, such as a quail and foie gras terrine with red onion preserve. This appetising score is the work of a veteran chef for whom French cuisine has no secrets.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6378;Le Comptoir Breizh Café;France;Saint-Malo;6 rue de l'Orme, Saint-Malo, 35400, France;48.6479451;-2.0251233;70;false;false;Breton;Breizh Café is the result of a stroke of genius: the idea of mixing Breton traditions with the Japanese flair for presentation. Inviting modern decor with a counter facing the open kitchen, as in Japan. Local ingredients (100% organic buckwheat, oysters from Cancale, butter from Bordier) and a few contemporary touches, such as buckwheat pancakes rolled up like maki. Good choice of ciders.;;[]
6379;Auberge des Deux Magots;France;La Roche-Bernard;1 place du Bouffay, La Roche-Bernard, 56130, France;47.518524;-2.3025745;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine;All the charm of an old Breton house in a pretty little town full of character. The refined and creative cuisine showcases seasonal regional produce. At lunchtime, there's a mouth-watering market-inspired set menu that represents remarkable value for money. The line-caught pollack served with buckwheat risotto with squid ink is on point! Even better, the chef bakes the bread himself.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6380;Le Carré de l'Ange;France;Saint-Lizier;Chemin du Parc (Palais des Évêques), Saint-Lizier, 09190, France;43.0027665;1.1373639;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Paul Fontvieille presides over the kitchens here with the same enthusiasm and infectious good mood as ever. This passionate chef composes delicious and savvy dishes ranging from the creative, such as artisanal soba noodles made with buckwheat from Ariège in a fresh herb broth, to the more traditional, eg comforting veal axoa. Bag a table on the terrace, which boasts a breathtaking view over the verdant valley… you'll be in seventh heaven!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6381;Au Relais des Ménétriers;France;Ribeauvillé;10 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Ribeauvillé, 68150, France;48.1906505;7.3249812;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The time is long gone when ménétriers or itinerant fiddlers went from inn to inn but hospitality is still the rule at this Relais, as is good food! The chef concocts true traditional French cuisine and buys his vegetables from local farmers. You can't argue with the results, which are generous and tasty.;;[]
6383;Le Saint Joseph;France;La Garenne-Colombes;100 boulevard de la République, La Garenne-Colombes, 92250, France;48.9074103;2.2410229;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This local bistro serves wholesome, updated, tasty fare, in the shape of a menu devised by chef Bordier, whose illustrious career speaks for itself. Diners dig into good food in a friendly relaxed venue, washed down with a selection from the concise wine list, which showcases wine - producing women.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6384;Au Lion d'Or - Chez Théo;France;Rosenau;5 rue Village-Neuf, Rosenau, 68128, France;47.6365191;7.5355895;43;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A pleasant and elegant inn, run by the same family since 1928. The chef brilliantly weaves flavours of today into the wealth of local specialities, without excluding the specialities of other parts of France! The selection of wines by the glass is short but well put together. Make the most of the beautiful terrace in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6385;Le Kitchen;France;Lyon;34 rue Chevreul, Lyon, 69007, France;45.7485041;4.8398381;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the student district of the Louis Lumière and Jean Moulin Universities, this Kitchen is thriving. The interior, a delightful blend of Art deco and Scandinavian (as is the owner), holds only eight small square tables. The pastry display case (to eat in or take away), the work of the owner’s pastry chef companion, sets our tastebuds drooling and the kitchen is open for breakfast and teatime, as well as lunch (but is closed in the evenings). Organic local produce, vegetables mainly, take pride of place on the table.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6387;Le Tiroir;France;Lyon;20 grande rue de Vaise, Lyon, 69009, France;45.7744378;4.8070854;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This establishment in the working-class district of Vaise, appointed in a characteristic trendy bistro vibe, is irresistibly endearing! The work of a youthful team, the food slaloms between iced tomato soup served with a mousse of white balsamic vinegar and a more patriotic Gallic line-up (tartare of beef, foie gras) – the menus and carte are regularly renewed. Excellent value for money and pleasure, including in the evenings.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6388;So;France;Dijon;15 rue Amiral-Roussin, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3196734;5.0410635;29;true;true;Farm to table;After notching up experience in some fine establishments, Japanese chef So Takahashi works alone in the kitchen, and his partner, Rie, is front of house. He uses ingredients that are bought directly at the market to concoct French cuisine interspersed with Japanese inspiration. The result is finely executed, light and flavoursome. So good!;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6390;Auberge du Pont;France;Billy;1 route de Marcenat, Billy, 03260, France;46.2356555;3.4258809;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The cuisine is meticulous, tasty and flavoursome, with sauces to die for… Enjoy crispy shoulder of lamb with red onion and Taggiasca olives, or opt for more surprising original dishes such as gravlax beef glazed with rice vinegar. When the weather is fine, make the most of the shady terrace overlooking the Allier River. At lunchtime, they serve a single set menu – the menu du marché – and amenu-carte in the evening. Not to be missed!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6391;DZ'envies;France;Dijon;12 rue Odebert, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3237399;5.0394574;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This chic, trendy canteen with its white walls, pale wood furnishings and black ceiling serves up an appetising menu in a lively neighbourhood near the indoor market. The menu showcases traditional cuisine and local produce, with a focus on seasonal ingredients such as persillé de Bourgogne (jellied ham with parsley), œufs en meurette (eggs in a red wine sauce) and beef cheeks à la Bourguignonne. The lunch set menu is a steal – enjoy on the terrace in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6392;L'Auberge;France;Caëstre;2590 route de Bailleul, Caëstre, 59190, France;50.7538173;2.6405019;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Not far from Hazebrouck, this Auberge was once a tannery then a tavern true to the traditions of France's northern regions. Now it is a restaurant with a friendly atmosphere showcasing seasonal produce and Flemish roots in reinterpretations of classic local fare (welsh, carbonade). Chef Antonin, who is also a wine enthusiast, pulls off surprising combinations such as snails, haddock and spinach, too!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6393;L'Embellie;France;Sainte-Cécile;245 route de Pont-sur-Grosne (Le Bourg), Sainte-Cécile, 71250, France;46.3904152;4.6250769;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A former stable whose rustic cachet is enhanced by beams, a fireplace and exposed brick walls. In the kitchen, the chef often draws inspiration from his travels, but always returns to certain classics, such as duck foie gras terrine or sautéed veal sweetbreads. The porchetta-style stuffed Burgundy rabbit and cromesquis made an impression. Have a home-made ice cream on the pleasant summer terrace, which only adds to the charm of this place.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6394;Racines;France;Étaples;46 boulevard de l'Impératrice, Étaples, 62630, France;50.5146141;1.6354079;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A stone’s throw from the marina of Étaples and only 5km from Le Touquet, this new restaurant is focused on succulent wholesome fare made with carefully sourced local produce. The recipes of chef Pierre Chavatte hit the spot every time. The interior sports a contemporary vibe with semi-open kitchens and hanging light fixtures surrounded by roots, a passing nod to the restaurant’s name. Highly recommended!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6397;Le Cottage;France;Chonas-l'Amballan;616 chemin du Marais, Chonas-l'Amballan, 38121, France;45.4601507;4.8048385;72;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The restaurant at Le Cottage is the latest venture of Philippe Girardon, a chef whose passion and experience are beyond dispute. He creates bistro - style fare using lovely fresh ingredients. Savour these in the large dining area or outside on the terrace in the shade of the plane trees.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6398;Le Bac à Traille;France;Valence;16 rue des Cévennes, Valence, 26000, France;44.9325366;4.8865415;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Masashi Ljichi, Japanese-born star chef of La Cachette, has made his dream come true in this wholehearted, flavoursome bistro, whose name pays homage to a former shuttle (bac) that used to cross the Rhône by way of a cable (traille). In addition to a high-flying gastronomic score, the chef crafts bistronomic dishes rich in big-boned flavours that are bang on every time. The market-fresh cuisine is impeccably curated, always punchy and heroically tasty, illustrated by poultry terrine, veggie pickles and lentil salad or lacquered pork belly in Timut pepper with fluffy mashed potatoes. We recommend the coconut pineapple and rum soup with tapioca and a velvety pineapple sorbet to finish. Fine selection of regional vintages. Knockout value for money.;Terrace;[]
6399;L'Aillet;France;La Teste-de-Buch;16 place Gambetta, La Teste-de-Buch, 33260, France;44.6312562;-1.1466525;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;The chef may profess a simple, local approach to cooking, but his food finds its place among its trendy bistro peers on account of its definitively contemporary look. A starter of cauliflower, herring, tarragon and peanuts boasts a pared-back presentation and well-balanced flavours. The chef is also a past master in the art of tradition and roasting joints, a skill set we can only applaud! A welcome addition to the Arcachon Bay culinary scene.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6400;L'Air de Famille;France;Toulouse;6 rue Jules-Chalande, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6022865;1.4441196;62;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;L'Air de Famille makes for an appealing place to eat with its period decor (vintage advertising posters, original counter) and unpretentious atmosphere. Tradition and the seasons dictate the menu here, with particular attention paid to flavour combinations and sauces. Calf's head with ravigote sauce and other classics regularly feature… and they boast a well-stocked wine list!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6401;Le Rabelais;France;Saint-Chamas;8 rue Auguste-Fabre, Saint-Chamas, 13250, France;43.5501;5.03234;69;false;true;Farm to table;Housed in the 17C vaulted room of an old wheat mill, this family-run restaurant would very likely have found favour with Rabelais's insatiable Gargantua! Dig into hearty seasonal fare that is meticulously prepared (the menu changes several times a week). The chef is also the author of a delicious signature dish: pâté en croûte (cold meat pie) of poultry and green veggies with a black garlic mayonnaise. The establishment is located in the immediate vicinity of Saint-Chamas' Poudrerie – the black powder mill founded in 1690. History, literature and good food: what’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6403;Chez Yvonne - S'Burjerstuewel;France;Strasbourg;10 rue du Sanglier, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5827917;7.7495037;19;true;true;Alsatian, Country cooking;A buzzy vibe and closely packed tables set the scene in this winstub, whose menu is the epitome of Alsace tradition (cockerel in Riesling, garnished sauerkraut, braised knuckle), albeit with a few more creative dishes, such as their delicate Alsace makis. Don’t miss the chance to sample one of the house specialties: melt-in-the-mouth pork cheeks slowly braised and simmered in a velvety pinot noir sauce – to die for!;;[]
6404;Les Petits Princes;France;Suresnes;26 rue du Val-d'Or, Suresnes, 92150, France;48.8598845;2.2193276;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This inviting restaurant on a corner plot is located close to the tram line. Inside, a partition window provides a glimpse into the kitchen. The menu features up-to-the-minute, appetising and always intriguing dishes, such as roasted magret de canard, vinegar jus, beetroot and hazelnuts, or rice pudding with caramel and puffed rice – incredibly indulgent with its vanilla whipped cream and generous layer of caramel deglazed with semi-salted butter. Verdant courtyard terrace to the rear.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
6406;Le Zeste Gourmand;France;Lyon;93 rue Bossuet, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7682882;4.8549037;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Benjamin Bouvard earned his stripes at Bocuse and La Pyramide before opening this establishment. Expect a minimalist interior that is in tune with the zeitgeist, and food to match. The top-notch produce is well crafted to create variations in texture in dishes such as beef cheek confit cromesqui with a reduced jus, creamy parsley root and pickles. The Dombes chicken with a Thai marinade is a creative and artfully plated dish. Finally, when it comes to dessert, the chocolate and pine feuille-à-feuille pastry shows a mastery of ingredients and a desire to deliver meticulous presentations. Front of house, the service is well-paced and cordial.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6407;La Clé des Champs;France;Favières;13 rue des Frères-Caudron, Favières, 80120, France;50.2378902;1.6617765;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This establishment is run by a professional young couple who go to great lengths to keep their guests happy. The fruit of their labours: modern and well-executed cuisine that puts ingredients from the local terroir in the spotlight, as in their tender and tasty haddock sausage accompanied by Picardy mushrooms, or their stuffed farm-reared guinea fowl, apple and onion, chicory jus.;Wheelchair access;[]
6408;M Restaurant;France;Lyon;47 avenue Maréchal-Foch, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7705693;4.8437151;69;true;false;Farm to table;A cocktail of vitamins! Julien Gautier’s cheerful establishment adds a whiff of exuberance to Lyon’s well-heeled, tree-lined Avenue Foch. The smart interior sports a muted blue and flashy orange colour scheme, felt grey designer armchairs, linen tablecloths, a bar and a wine cellar encircled by a conservatory… The similarly charismatic service is as smooth as a silky béarnaise sauce. In the kitchen, the veteran and talented chef, formerly of Léon of Lyon, rustles up an appetising, market-sourced menu, combining flawless technique and know-how in a bid to pamper our tastebuds with delicate flavours tailored to modern appetites. The honey-flavoured madeleines served with a fromage blanc sorbet are awesome!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6410;La Table d'Hôtes;France;Ouistreham;10 avenue du Général-Leclerc, Ouistreham, 14150, France;49.2835077;-0.2591358;19;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Not far from the seaside resort, this family restaurant is the stomping ground of a couple who have experience working in some fine establishments. Yoann Lavalley has bought the stove which he used during his apprenticeship and uses it to create seasonal cuisine that is both flavourful and indulgent. The sommelier, his wife, has curated a nice wine list that represents excellent value for money. Fish of the day, local meat, Normandy cheeses… A pleasant place.;Wheelchair access;[]
6411;L'Auberge des Montagnes;France;Pailherols;Le Bourg, Pailherols, 15800, France;44.9504857;2.6836877;75;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This farmstead in the heart of a remote picturesque village (ideal for walks in the country) is the HQ of a chef who competently and carefully crafts traditional recipes. Save room for the cheese board and Salers cheese, produced just a few yards away.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
6412;Le Montcenis;France;Montcenis;2  place du Champ-de-Foire, Montcenis, 71710, France;46.7913339;4.3889573;55;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Both the decor (vaulted cellar, exposed stone and beams) and the food are full of character. Laurent Dufour draws on fine produce to create generous and authentic dishes, such as guinea fowl breast with spinach leaves and carrots, and green cabbage cannelloni with smoked bacon. The menu changes regularly and, in winter, features truffles, of which the chef is a big fan! A cordial welcome.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6413;Restaurant du Dauphin;France;La Ferté-Bernard;3 rue d'Huisne, La Ferté-Bernard, 72400, France;48.186594;0.651538;93;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the old town, at the foot of the Porte St Julien, this restaurant in a pretty 16C building serves cuisine for the modern palate. The chefs incorporate a smattering of exotic touches, but always have a handful of classics up their sleeve. The chicken supreme with quince, accompanied by mashed potatoes with walnuts and an amaretto-infused carcass jus is a good example. As for dessert, it is a pleasure to find a vacherin, a rum baba or a moelleux – always a failsafe option! Fine selection of wines by the glass.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6414;Au Colombier;France;Anse;126 allée Colombier, Anse, 69480, France;45.9453427;4.7257478;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This fine 18C building by the River Saône feels like a cross between a hip guinguette and a country house. The food is resolutely contemporary, but for all that does not neglect French classics, a case in point being the wonderful pan-fried frogs' legs. A culinary moment to savour on the peaceful, cosy terrace.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6415;Le Bistronôme;France;Arbois;62 rue de Faramand, Arbois, 39600, France;46.901436;5.7723305;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Small in size, big in quality! In an exquisite location on the banks of the River Cuisance, Lisa and Jérôme have made their establishment a firm fixture of Arbois’ culinary scene. The chef’s seasonal recipes, emblematic of his technique and flair, are a festival of mouth-watering delicacies from his signature dish, Planches trout stuffed with morel and oyster mushrooms, vin jaune sauce to farm-reared Jura pork chop, pepper and tonka bean meat gravy and dauphine potatoes. The desserts are to die for! Their “au fil du jour” daily special is a steal and the service is refreshingly unstarched and friendly: remember to book!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6416;Les Coloquintes;France;Aubenas;18 quai de l'Ardèche, Aubenas, 07200, France;44.6255239;4.3943331;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant installed in a former silk - throwing factory is run by a young couple – he in the kitchen, she front of house. They propose contemporary cuisine, aiming to keep supply channels short and respecting local produce, trout, chestnuts, fruits etc. In summer, get a table in the shade of the lime trees.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6417;L'Aubépine;France;Aubenas;13 boulevard Jean-Mathon, Aubenas, 07200, France;44.6198836;4.3873224;21;false;false;Modern Cuisine;L’Aubépine is flourishing in the hands of a youthful researcher, now on a quest for flavour. Chef Manuel is a staunch advocate of locally sourced produce, whose ingredients he seeks to exalt, respecting both their texture and nutritional value. Everything is made in house and the menu changes weekly depending on the market.;Air conditioning;[]
6418;Le Rendez-vous des Gourmets;France;Bracieux;20 rue Roger-Brun, Bracieux, 41250, France;47.5490863;1.5407975;34;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Since he opened this splendid country restaurant, Didier Doreau has turned it into a genuine gourmet stronghold. Terrine of pike à la Chambord, pâté of game served warm drizzled in jus, traditional calf’s head, Grand Marnier-flavoured baked citrus fruits… You can expect a pageant of traditional Gallic staples, made with fresh, crisp produce, crafted into dishes that exalt and respect the intrinsic flavour of each ingredient. The chef is renowned for his way with game in season (hare, venison, wild boar, etc.), which further adds to the well-deserved success of what has become a culinary benchmark in the region.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6419;Le Gantxo;France;Guiche;130 chemin du Trinquet, Guiche, 64520, France;43.5212561;-1.1974514;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Welcome to the Basque country! Le Gantxo – named after a pass in pelota – gives directly onto the trinquet, the ground where the famous local sport is played. In the kitchen, Isabelle and Laurent Miremont revisit Basque cuisine in a very personal way, composing dishes that are up to the minute, often copious, always tasty. A firm favourite!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6420;Coteaux et Fourchettes;France;Cairanne;3340 route de Carpentras, Cairanne, 84290, France;44.202501;4.9454338;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This cleverly named restaurant (a pun on côteaux meaning hills and couteaux meaning knives) is housed in an old wine cellar. The region is well represented both by the delicious cuisine and by the excellent choice of local wines. Pleasant, contemporary decor and a terrace overlooking the vineyards.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6421;Maison Joanto;France;Briscous;9 chemin du Village, Briscous, 64240, France;43.46048;-1.33373;42;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Joanto means "Little John" in Basque, but there is nothing diminutive about this place! Its fine traditional architecture and convivial ambience are more than worthy of applause, as is the generous cooking of its head chef, who has worked in some top establishments. This is meticulous and indulgent cuisine, with an explosion of Basque Country flavours: pâté en croûte, milk-fed Pyrenean lamb, Armagnac baba. Fantastic value for money.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6422;Le 6 à Table;France;Caromb;6 place Nationale, Caromb, 84330, France;44.1102329;5.1072609;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a peaceful village, this small square basking in the shade of the church is the quintessence of rural France. The chef uses local ingredients whenever possible: trout, strawberries, figs, cheese, vegetables… Seasonal food served on the terrace or in a pleasant conservatory-cum-workshop interior.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6423;L'Ô à la Bouche;France;Cahors;56 allées Fénelon, Cahors, 46000, France;44.44497;1.44051;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At the head of this pleasant restaurant is a foodie couple who travelled to faraway lands and seas before dropping anchor in Cahors. Jean - François concocts gourmet dishes such as: salmon marinated in fennel or wild seabass, pan - fried chard and Lautrec pink garlic cromesquis. Enough to make your mouth water!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6425;Veronatuti;France;Lyon;122 rue Montesquieu, Lyon, 69007, France;45.7496327;4.8477126;29;false;true;Italian;Start with a salad of fennel and orange segments of Sicilian inspiration, followed by a main course from Emilia-Romagna (stracotto of braised beef in red wine, carrots and onions) and a dessert of Lombardy and Piedmont heritage (homemade ice cream made from toasted corn flour (farina bòna) served with a crumble of sbrisolona and a wafer-thin layer of chocolate). The duo who runs this authentic trattoria embarks diners on a whirlwind gourmet tour of Italy. Everything is made from scratch - even the coffee comes from a local artisan roaster. Delicious food without killer prices.;;[]
6426;Le Bel'Art;France;Champcevinel;2 allée Jean-Boiteux, Champcevinel, 24750, France;45.2046356;0.7450092;27;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In a modern building on the higher ground outside Périgueux, Sandrine and Vincent Cardoso's restaurant has a functional dining space. The food represents a complete change of tack, with a different menu on offer every week. Served with good jus, first-rate local ingredients are accompanied by seasonal vegetables that demonstrate the chef's indisputable expertise. Everything is cooked precisely and from the heart. The brandade of salmon with sweet wine, the chicken supreme in a ramekin with bay leaves and farm spinach, or the diced Golden Delicious apple on a buttery sablé reflect the care lavished on each plate. This place is a pleasant surprise, with its enticing set menu at lunchtime served by a friendly, smiling owner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6427;La Table de Nernier;France;Nernier;11 place du Musée, Nernier, 74140, France;46.3655419;6.3036622;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the medieval village of Nernier on the banks of Lake Geneva between Yvoire and Messery, this charming country inn is warm and hospitable. Rustic (rafters, terracotta tiles) and contemporary features (pendant lights, designer chairs) rub shoulders in a match made in heaven. The market-fresh menu errs towards the traditional, whilst demonstrating the utmost reverence for the seasons. The smiling and attentive service is courtesy of the chef's partner, while the paved terrace is everything one expects of rural villagey France.;Terrace;[]
6428;Meraki;France;Nantes;2 rue Menou, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2204773;-1.5629942;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In Greek, Meraki means made with love, passion and creativity, which perfectly echoes the ethos of this warm, friendly bistro. Maxime Bocquier in the kitchen and Clément Richard in the front of house (even if he also trained as a chef) have chosen to focus on vegetables and seafood. All their produce is organic and local, including the burrata cheese from a local dairy. The single set menu changes monthly. Examples: stock of grey shrimp poured over barbecued cucumber and smoked eel, which explodes as your tastebuds are titillated by exciting, unexpected flavours. Mainly organic, sometimes natural Loire wines play the leading roles, without forgetting guest star appearances from other wine-growing regions.;;[]
6429;La Chaumière de Pomper;France;Baden;Le Moulin de Pomper, 14 hameau de Kerhervé, Baden, 56870, France;47.6217962;-2.8724528;61;true;false;Breton;Well - known in the region, this pancake house rustles up crêpes made from 90% organic buckwheat flour and 10% wheat flour, resulting in a mixture so light and airy the crêpes are even crispier than the norm. In fact, it even has a name in Breton kraz! If you can’t make your choice, we suggest sticking to the classics! Impressive list of ciders.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6430;Manoir de la Pommeraie;France;Vire Normandie;L'Auvère, Vire Normandie, 14500, France;48.829562;-0.8610719;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This 18C building, whose conservatory overlooks wooded grounds planted with hundred-year-old trees, is run by a Franco-Japanese couple who continues to knock the socks off our tastebuds. While Masako pours her talents into pastries, Julien finetunes his exquisite, flawlessly balanced culinary score: roast monkfish, girolles, mussels and hay or lightly seared tuna in spices, aubergine and cucumber. Regional ingredients invariably take the limelight (Normandy beef, Cahagnes poultry, cheese from local farms and locally grown veggies) and the chef often waxes lyrical about his suppliers when he pops into the dining room, as is his wont.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6433;Chez Loustic;France;Toulouse;19 rue Reclusane, Toulouse, 31300, France;43.598755;1.43292;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In one of the busiest parts of the Saint-Cyprien neighbourhood, this modern bistro has an industrial feel (aluminium piping, white brick walls, minimalist lighting) that makes for a convivial atmosphere! The pleasant terrace overlooking the square is a bonus. Trained by Christian Constant, the chef won us over with his generous fillet of sea bream on braised leeks, spinach cream and parsnip chips, and his poached peach and rhubarb with cardamom cream. Finely prepared market-fresh cuisine, even sensitive, and very healthily composed.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6434;La Table de Mee;France;Paris;6 rue des Ciseaux, Paris, 75006, France;48.8530426;2.3340394;25;true;false;Korean;In a stripped-back interior dominated by wood (where you can sit at the counter to watch the chef at work at his large plancha), this Korean restaurant celebrates the country's specialities. Spicy flavours and sauces are the order of the day, courtesy of the obligatory kimchi, Korean fried chicken ("KFC") and delicious ssams. The mackerel fillets simmered in a soya, chilli and white radish broth is a standout dish. The total capacity is 24 diners: booking strongly recommended!;;[]
6435;Baca'v - Boulogne;France;Boulogne-Billancourt;33 avenue du Général-Leclerc, Boulogne-Billancourt, 92100, France;48.83182;2.2383199;27;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Chef Émile Cotte has opened a sister restaurant of his Parisian establishment. In a modern bistro setting illuminated by large picture windows (and divided into several areas, including a table d'hôte), the chef serves up the cuisine he loves: generous bistro classics with a modern twist and a focus on simplicity and indulgence, cf. his gridouille (andouille de Vire with a piece of lean pork belly) served with oh-so-buttery mashed potatoes. Dishes often pay tribute to Limousin, birthplace of the chef. His tempting menu includes pâté en croûte, vol-au-vent, sweetbreads, millefeuille and chocolate soufflé.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
6438;Jumo & Co;France;Pau;6 rue Henri-IV, Pau, 64000, France;43.29465;-0.37167;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the old town of Pau, twin brothers, one a chef and the other a pastry chef, have successfully launched their family business in a modern bistro-style setting laid out over two floors, complete with a pastry counter and tea room. The menu is a real draw, and also represents great value for money. This talented pair bring a touch of magic to their apparently simple dishes, drawing on sweet and sour jus and a medley of condiments to enhance their ingenious and generous, yet always light cuisine. Think confit pork belly, barbecue jus, pickled vegetables, radishes, polenta croquette.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6441;Julien;France;Fouday;Route de Strasbourg, Fouday, 67130, France;48.42262;7.18412;76;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Alsatian;Local folklore is celebrated by waiters in traditional costume and a characteristic wooden Vosges decor. In a lively, yet sophisticated atmosphere, you will be treated to tasty, copious regional preparations: sauerkraut, veal kidneys, sweetbread and bouchées à la reine. The food is as heart-warming as the rooms, the grounds and the hotel’s magnificent spa facilities.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6442;Les Épices Curiens;France;Écouviez;3b place de la Gare, Écouviez, 55600, France;49.5244347;5.4564704;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;When strolling around the area you could easily cross over into Belgium without realising it. But the former train station of this border village, since converted into a lovely restaurant, will encourage you to stay in France. Sample the inspired cuisine and nicely prepared dishes, all paired with good local wines. Lots of taste!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6443;Auberge Le Centre Poitou;France;Coulombiers;39 rue Nationale, Coulombiers, 86600, France;46.4851301;0.1848401;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The same family has been honing their gift for hospitality and running this inn, formerly a post house, since 1870. Chef Mathias pours his energy into concocting gutsy food with fine produce, harnessing his immaculate technique and inspired talent to the delight of foodies. An experience to be sampled in an elegant interior, whose vintage charm is dotted with modern touches. Attentive front-of-house service by Martial, the chef’s brother. Simpler bistro score at lunchtime. A few rooms for overnight stays.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6444;Air Accueil;France;Brebières;75 ter route Nationale, Brebières, 62117, France;50.3362215;3.0038801;82;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Near the Vitry - en - Artois airfield, this vast inn used to be an officers' mess. Today it is much more than a simple canteen! The food is delicious, and all the experience of chef Franck Gilabert shines through. There are numerous nods to local specialities, and the flavours really take off!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6445;Iida-Ya;France;Dole;18 rue Arney, Dole, 39100, France;47.0938975;5.4948113;66;true;true;Japanese;Confit pork belly with ginger sauce, sushi, maki, tempura… From the soothingly pared-back and chic dining area, diners have an unhampered view of the Japanese chef as he rustles up refined dishes that bring together French and Japanese cuisine. Fine sake selection. A huge hit in Dole!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6446;Minami;France;Annecy;19 faubourg Sainte-Claire, Annecy, 74000, France;45.8972875;6.1228744;32;true;true;Japanese;This tiny Japanese restaurant is crammed with regulars. The minimalist interior provides the perfect foil to well-crafted Japanese fare with the occasional foray into a traditional Gallic repertory. A few examples: sushi of foie gras, caramelised eel or jasmine-perfumed crème brûlée. A few tables are laid on the patio in fine weather.;Terrace;[]
6447;Épices et Tout;France;Alès;15 avenue Carnot, Alès, 30100, France;44.1212885;4.0825847;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant with an unobtrusive façade will wake up your taste buds. Carefully prepared dishes, fresh produce and judiciously deployed spices. For example, salmon tartare with a duo of lentils, saddle of lamb with mushroom mousseline or spiced poached pear. An appetising menu to relish on the small terrace in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6448;Bistrot du Pollet;France;Dieppe;23 rue Tête-de-Bœuf, Dieppe, 76200, France;49.9271053;1.0836092;77;false;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;Let us make no bones about it: in this bistro, it is the sea that decides, and the dishes depend directly on the local catch. Enjoy squid, foie gras du pêcheur, sole du bistro or scallops with lentils. Quality and freshness are the order of the day, and what generosity in the preparations!;;[]
6450;Bistrot des Anges;France;Le Cannet;Rue de l'Ouest, Le Cannet, 06110, France;43.5716685;7.0145284;45;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This brasserie, run by the team from Villa Archange, sports a modern decor, a friendly vibe and set menus inspired by sunny climes! Tuck into artichokes stuffed with egg mayo, Florentine cream and basil or veal kidneys with mushrooms. For dessert, make your choice from a wickedly tempting sweets trolley filled with treats. You'll be in seventh heaven!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6451;Le Denti;France;Annecy;25 bis avenue de Loverchy, Annecy, 74000, France;45.896455;6.1207042;16;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This dinky restaurant off the busy tourist track is the haunt of a couple with a passion for ‘denti’ (a Mediterranean fish). Both are talented, versatile cooks and together they craft flavoursome market cuisine with a weakness for fish and a reverence for the seasons. With only a handful of tables, bookings are snapped up fast, so book ahead!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6453;En Cuisine;France;Brive-la-Gaillarde;39 avenue Édouard-Herriot, Brive-la-Gaillarde, 19100, France;45.1537272;1.5330328;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Since undergoing a complete refurbishment following a fire, the interior of this refined restaurant displays a degree of Scandinavian flair. The dishes are all about finesse and mouth-watering flavours: eg the soft and tender skate wing accompanied by delicious home-made gnocchi flavoured with lemon and flat parsley, enhanced by a delicious sweet and sour sauce. Everything is well executed – compliments to the chef!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6457;The Presbytere;France;Heugueville-sur-Sienne;16 rue de la Sienne, Heugueville-sur-Sienne, 50200, France;49.0345872;-1.5249411;72;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Gastropub;In a picturesque corner of Normandy, English chef Edward Delling-Williams fell in love with this presbytery that he has turned into a locavore gastro-pub. Untreated wood tables, hunting trophies on the wall, an imposing stone fireplace and exposed rafters set the scene. Here, hungry diners can dig into dishes such as mussels with aioli followed by a duck confit with an original and beautifully refreshing cucumber and mint salad, rounded off with a moist courgette loaf cake. The chef also owns a farm, where he grows his own fruit and vegetables.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6458;Aux Bons Enfants;France;Cannes;80 rue Meynadier, Cannes, 06400, France;43.5516153;7.0120202;86;true;true;Provençal;This family business, opened in 1935, only recently had a telephone line installed, but still accepts cash only! The fourth generation continues to craft authentic Provençal ingredients into heart-warming, hunger obliterating dishes. All the produce, fruit, veg and fish from small boats, comes direct from Forville Market just down the road. We tucked into petits farcis (stuffed vegetables), Niçois-style braised beef cheeks, homemade gnocchi and the house dessert: rum baba with vanilla cream – to die for!;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
6459;L'Ardoise;France;Angers;7 place Molière, Angers, 49000, France;47.4742919;-0.5545996;80;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Although we are on the left bank of the Maine, in an appealing contemporary brasserie interior, the dishes exude all the warmth of the Mediterranean – a selection of antipasti to share, or polish off yourself (e.g. hummus and panisses), followed by appetising mains (pasta with shellfish) and, last but not least, the desserts (tiramisu, pistachio and orange blossom dessert). There are also some more traditional French classics (such as home-made terrine, pâté en croûte and profiteroles). And the bill is very reasonable.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6460;Le Bourgeon;France;Alby-sur-Chéran;8 place du Trophée, Alby-sur-Chéran, 74540, France;45.8172029;6.0205378;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A picturesque medieval village lined in colourful houses and formerly renowned for its tanners and cobblers is the setting of this burgeoning establishment! Helmed by chef Enzo Duchesne and sommelier Adrien Lavorel, Le Bourgeon nurtures a modern gourmet horticultural score whose ingredients are painstakingly sourced. Veggies take pride of place in the menu, with guest star appearances from meat and fish, in spot-on dishes steeped in aroma and flavour, illustrated by a starter that mixes raw and mashed courgette, goat’s cheese, gremolata and confit of egg yolk. Several menus are available at lunchtime and evening with a mystery menu in the evening and on Saturday lunchtime.;Terrace;[]
6461;JK Restaurant;France;Chassy;350 route du Château, Chassy, 71130, France;46.586482;4.1127018;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Jeanne-Louise and Kevin (J+K!) met while working for their mentor Frédéric Doucet, whose Michelin-starred restaurant is very close to their first place – in a small village in the Charolais bocage. Together, the pair create cuisine that is very much in tune with the times, with occasional nods to Italy (the chef's homeland) and in which vegetables are a common thread. The ingredients are meticulously selected: take, for example, the pollack loin fillet with spring vegetables, or the kiwi, strawberry and blackcurrant tartare. Every evening and weekend, the chefs serve a single multi-course set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6462;Maison Devaux;France;Rion-des-Landes;70 rue du Commerce, Rion-des-Landes, 40370, France;43.9349192;-0.9233373;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a half-timbered building that is typical of this part of France, this restaurant is the domain of Mathis Devaux. The son, grandson and nephew of chefs, you could say he was born into the profession. Expect a decor of terracotta floor tiles and exposed beams, with crockery and tables designed and made by local craftspeople. The chef concocts modern bistro cuisine, drawing on local produce (including black Gascon pork) in dishes such as poached monkfish, fondant leeks with aioli and zest of black lemon, or chocolate and fleur de sel Genoise sponge, vanilla mascarpone cream and a cherry gelée.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6463;Aux 2 K;France;Paris;5 rue Louise-Émilie-de-la-Tour-d'Auvergne, Paris, 75009, France;48.8788232;2.3449245;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The two K's refer to Kagy (Samantha, chef) and Kinoshita (Kimiko, pastry chef), a pair who joined forces after gaining a wealth of experience in some prestigious establishments (Violon d'Ingres, L'Ours, Atelier Joël Robuchon, Taillevent). Their abundant technical skill is clearly demonstrated in dishes that are as delicious as their names are enticing, in particular the "speciality" of roasted pigeon, smoked eel and shallot finished with a salmis sauce. A few nods to the South-West of France are a reminder of the influence of Christian Constant. A culinary feat pulled off with great care and finesse, and at lunchtime, a set menu at an unbeatable price.;;[]
6465;Bistrot Lucien;France;Gevrey-Chambertin;La Rôtisserie du Chambertin, 6 rue du Chambertin, Gevrey-Chambertin, 21220, France;47.224128;4.9696133;77;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Bare stone walls, bench seating and a superb wooden counter set the scene in this bistro, which is housed in its parent hotel. Expertly crafted burgundy recipes take pride of place on the nostalgic menu: home-cured ham, poached egg in wine, Bresse poultry, profiteroles... Fantastic wine list!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6467;Le Gibolin;France;Arles;13 rue des Porcelets, Arles, 13200, France;43.6769528;4.6241278;82;true;true;Farm to table;Arnaud Jourdan (stints in the kitchens of La Chassagnette and Les Maisons Rabanel) has adroitly taken over the reins of this bistro, which continues to serve indulgent market cuisine that is both simple and generous. Shining examples include the carpaccio of calf's head with ravigote sauce, the skate wing à la grenobloise with glazed radishes and the delicious chocolate mousse with black olives and fleur de sel. A buzzy, laid-back vibe and, true to its name (slang for "wine"), you can expect a fine selection of natural and biodynamic wines at reasonable prices.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6469;L'Épicurien;France;Albi;42 place Jean-Jaurès, Albi, 81000, France;43.9245935;2.1489925;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Luck has nothing to do with the current reputation of this downtown venue, facing Jean Jaurès Fountain, as the darling of the town’s discerning epicureans. The stripped-back interior sports a distinctly Scandinavian feel, which given the chef’s Swedish origins is hardly a surprise. On the culinary front, he deploys his undisputed talent, adding a new twist to French classics and conjuring up enticing recipes in tune with the era: generous portions, well crafted and oozing with flavour. The intelligent wine list and crack table staff, as professional as they are friendly, add the final flourish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6470;La Table de Michel Dussau;France;Agen;1350 avenue du Midi, Agen, 47000, France;44.1901478;0.6143063;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Just outside the town centre and near the rugby stadium, chef Michel Dussau whips up tasty recipes in a fashionable brasserie setting. He professes a weakness for local and seasonal ingredients, even better when organic. The establishment’s other appeals include a glazed wine cellar, a meat maturing cabinet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6471;Au Plaisir Ambré;France;Briançon;26 Grande Rue, Briançon, 05100, France;44.8999664;6.6435838;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Inside Vauban's fortifications, this converted butcher's places a premium on fine ingredients. Freshness is the watchword of the skilful chef, who knows how to coax out the best flavours. Examples would be the slow-confit farmhouse pork belly, wasabi jus and parsnip purée, and the dark chocolate tart with coconut sorbet. Sheer pleasure.;;[]
6473;Solelh;France;L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue;30 avenue des Compagnons-de-la-Libération, L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue, 84800, France;43.9180452;5.0485989;51;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The owners of the fine dining Le Vivier establishment were happily inspired when they opened this bistro, blessed with a double terrace, in the heart of the Carré des Arts du Luberon. From his open-plan kitchen, the chef rustles up a forthright, modern take on traditional bistro recipes, in addition to nibbles with pre-dinner drinks and choice ingredients grilled on a binchotan barbecue (aged rib of beef, squid, presa iberica, etc.). A concise selection of regional (but not only) wines adds the finishing touch to an excellent, sun-drenched meal…;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6474;Le Moulin de la Santoire;France;Saint-Saturnin;La Plaine, Saint-Saturnin, 15190, France;45.2583308;2.8036229;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant occupies a converted mill built of black volcanic stone and with a slate roof. Set just outside a small village, it overlooks a pretty lake, beside which the terrace is set up in fine weather. The interior keeps things cosy (winters are harsh in the Cantal!) with a stone fireplace, a bar and mismatched traditional wooden furniture. On the plate, diners can expect a beautifully presented, delicious and modern take on classic fare: think beef cheek façon royale or opera cake with chestnut and quince cream, with dishes elevated by hints of spice or Japanese condiments. It is clear that the chef learned his trade in some fine establishments. Most of the produce is sourced in the region (the coffee and cocoa come from a local roastery and chocolaterie). Platter of regional cheeses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6475;L’Abbaye Caladoise;France;Villefranche-sur-Saône;180 rue Georges-Mangin, Villefranche-sur-Saône, 69400, France;45.9910681;4.7388388;46;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This picturesque 17C stone - built edifice has been magnificently transformed into a restaurant. The haunt of discerning foodies (the chef won a 2016 culinary award for his pork pies), the interior has been updated and the menu reflects a distinct regional slant.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6479;Ose;France;Paris;3 rue Durantin, Paris, 75018, France;48.8852338;2.3373871;71;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After stints in top establishments from New York to Paris, two veteran chefs now swap places every fortnight, taking turns in the open kitchen and the dining room. 100% bistronomic cooking from scratch using local, fresh, seasonal ingredients is the backbone of this bistro in the Abbesses neighbourhood. The menu, chalked up on a slate daily, is bang-on confident with a strong French bias and showcases deceptively simple recipes. ‘Ose’ means to dare – so what are you waiting for?;Terrace;[]
6480;Rēpu;France;Marcq-en-Barœul;944 avenue de la République, Marcq-en-Barœul, 59700, France;50.6623595;3.0975604;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Chef Abdeldaker Belfatmi wants his guests to leave satisfied and with a full stomach. His organic soft-boiled egg with peas, his pollack with smooth, buttery courgette cream and lemon hazelnut, and his crunchy crumble with pistachio cream and apricot sorbet certainly do the job! This modern brasserie cuisine shows, if proof were needed, that the chef of the former Michelin-starred restaurant Le Marcq has lost none of his flair in the kitchen.;Air conditioning;[]
6481;Oxalis;France;Marcolès;Place de la Fontaine, Marcolès, 15220, France;44.7814847;2.351852;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This bistro is the more casual sibling of the star Auberge de la Tour, helmed by chef Renaud Darmanin, which is even more reason to stay overnight in the medieval village of Marcolès deep in the Cantal countryside. The dining room takes up the most part of the hotel’s ground-floor and is extended by a terrace overlooking the street. Regional produce takes the limelight in well-crafted recipes, including veg from the cottage garden and other local ingredients such as volcano trout, poultry from the next-door farm, Auvergne cheeses. Examples of dishes: trout, vegetables, garden leaves and a knockout stock of fishbones or the melt-in-the-mouth vanilla and apricot millefeuille.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6482;Le Voyage d'Ernestine;France;Alvignac;182 Grand-Rue, Alvignac, 46500, France;44.825918;1.6922221;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A family affair! A team of three (twins – a brother and sister – plus her partner) take their guests on a culinary journey featuring carefully selected local ingredients (lamb from the Bouscarel farm, vegetables from Tauriac, trout from Le Gouffre du Blagour fish farm etc). Trained as a butcher and charcutier, the brother is an expert when it comes to cuts of meat. As for this widely travelled couple, they punctuate their dishes with international touches (eg labneh, black lemon, lamb jus emulsified with tahini). A top-notch culinary experience in a restaurant that is firmly in tune with the times.;Terrace;[]
6483;Le Bistrot de La Cueillette;France;Meursault;18 rue de Cîteaux, Meursault, 21190, France;46.9780964;4.7723799;27;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Comfortably seated in the vaulted space that once housed the château kitchens, you can expect traditional cuisine, meticulously prepared using carefully selected ingredients: Burgundy snails, Bresse poultry, Charolais beef... Laid-back vibe.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6485;Kwon;France;Paris;7 rue Ernest-Cresson, Paris, 75014, France;48.8325318;2.3296003;59;true;false;Korean;Cinema, TV series and… food! Korean culture has become omnipresent in France – much to our delight. This restaurant's trendy decor has a minimalist, industrial feel, a menu of Korean classics such as barbecue and bibimbap, and above all a keen sense of detail. The care taken over the accompaniments is particularly clear to see, whether you opt for the emblematic kimchi, crunchy beans with a smoky flavour, caramelised lotus flower or cucumber with chilli. This is generous and fresh fare and good value for money!;Air conditioning;[]
6487;Sème;France;Saint-Pair-sur-Mer;33 place Charles-de-Gaulle, Saint-Pair-sur-Mer, 50380, France;48.8154557;-1.5700696;41;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;On the market square, bang in the heart of the village, this buzzy, endearing bistro sports a quaintly quirky decor of wine posters, pepper mills and books about Normandy. The chef, who hails from northern Cotentin, crafts a confident bang-on menu that is as Gallic as La Marseillaise, but with a welcome modern, even irreverent slant at times. Local, regional and seasonal ingredients, together with insightful wine tips.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6490;La Salamandre;France;Saint-Aignan;7 place de l'Église, Saint-Aignan, 41110, France;47.26964;1.3759075;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a picture postcard medieval village overlooking the River Cher, this eatery occupies an outbuilding of the castle of Saint-Aignan and is decked out in a contemporary bistro vibe beneath an attractive timber ceiling. The seasoned Dutch chef rolls out a fresh, colourful lineup, including a vegetarian menu. Terrace nestled at the foot of the chateau.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6492;Cheung Hing Kee (Tsim Sha Tsui);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, 48 Lock Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2976346;114.1716772;78;true;false;Street Food;Besides the typical sheng jian bao with soupy pork filling, this shop serves varieties such as shrimp, mala pork, truffle, crabmeat and roe. The buns are springy, brimming with filling, and crispy on the bottom.;;[]
6493;O Castiço;;Macau;65B Rua Direita Carlos Eugénio, Taipa, Macau;22.15444;113.55887;20;false;false;Portuguese;This cosy hangout has long been attracting a loyal following for its tasty, homespun food at affordable prices. Now run by the late owner’s son, it continues to welcome diners like family, offering carefully crafted, authentic Portuguese fare. Their signature stewed pork with clams delivers balanced flavours and a pleasant kick due to coriander and a secret sauce. The made to order salted cod fritters are served piping hot.;Air conditioning;[]
6494;Sang Kee Foods (Western District);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 4, GF, Wo Yick Mansion, 263 Queen's Road West, Sai Ying Pun, Hong Kong;22.17134;114.08356;69;false;true;Street Food;Come to this place with a nose-to-tail concept for Chiuchow-style marinated goose. Made with grain-fed goose from Chiuchow, it boasts a firm texture and meaty flavour. Try the goose blood curd, web, wing, liver, intestine and gizzard, too.;;[]
6495;Tin Hung;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop D, GF, Yan Yee Building, 88 Kin Yip Street, Yuen Long, Hong Kong;22.4425128;114.0314235;32;true;true;Cantonese Roast Meats;Popular with locals since 2001, this shop sells its signature roast goose in specific cuts, halves or whole. Geese are shipped from Foshan daily, marinated, roasted to perfection, and served piping hot. Other standouts include honey-glazed char siu, roast duck and drunken chicken. Those looking to pair the meats with a local drink should try their herbal tea. Given the reasonable prices and limited seats, it makes sense to arrive early.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6496;Tak Kee;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop G, 3 Belcher's Street, Western District, Hong Kong;22.2855398;114.1322821;43;true;true;Chiu Chow;It started out as a street-side hawker stall in the 1990s and still retains the casual, vibrant vibe. The second-generation hands-on owner shops for groceries every day and sometimes helps the experienced chefs with kitchen chores. Pork tripe and peppercorn soup is a culinary highlight, using peppers from Malaysia and Indonesia. Regulars also come for its spiced marinated goose liver, crispy chitterlings stuffed with glutinous rice and oyster omelette.;Air conditioning;[]
6497;Ho To Tai;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;67 Fau Tsoi Street, Yuen Long, Hong Kong;22.44383;114.02933;62;false;true;Noodles;Traditional shops that make their own noodles from scratch are hard to come by. Founded in 1946, this household name is among the remaining few. Though the nostalgic two-storey shop draws a crowd with its signature wonton soup, zhajiang noodles and beef brisket noodle soup are also popular. Try braised white radish with shrimp roe for the deep umami and briny-sweetness. The owner also runs a dried noodle factory with retail outlets all over town.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6498;Mak Man Kee;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;51 Parkes Street, Jordan, Hong Kong;22.3046799;114.1705644;55;true;true;Noodles;No one is here for the no-frills interior, typical of any noodle shop in Hong Kong. This 60-year-old establishment is all about Cantonese wonton soup noodles – firm and bouncy prawns, visible through the paper-thin translucent skin, with springy duck egg noodles swimming in a flavourful broth. The noodles taste equally great when simply tossed in oyster sauce or shrimp roe, the latter also available as a pre-packaged condiment to go.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6500;Lucky Indonesia;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;46 Tung Ming Street, Kwun Tong, Hong Kong;22.31581;114.22314;68;false;false;Indonesian;For over 30 years, this tiny gem has been famous in the neighbourhood for its authentic Central Javanese cooking. The room feels cosy and youthful after a facelift and the food is as tasty as always. For chargrilled satay exuding an addictive smoky aroma, choose from lamb, pork and chicken varieties. Lontong capgome is sticky rice balls with several side dishes such as beef rendang, opor ayam and pindang egg. Pair with an iced longan drink.;Air conditioning;[]
6501;Din Tai Fung (Tsim Sha Tsui);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 306, 3F, Silvercord, 30 Canton Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2972864;114.1694396;33;false;false;Shanghainese;From the late Mr Yang’s first shop in Taiwan in 1958 grew a multinational chain with branches all over the world. It’s famous for good service, competitive prices and listening to its customer’s feedback, but mostly for its xiao long bao made on the spot. Even the vinegar, free of artificial colours and preservatives, is shipped from Taiwan. Seating accommodates different party sizes, from solo diners to parties of 12. Expect long queues at peak hours.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6504;Takeya;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 1, On Wah Building, 31C1 Tak Man Street, Whampoa Estate, Hung Hom, Hong Kong;22.3061551;114.1882405;69;true;false;Japanese;This intimate 15-seater yakitori shop is the brainchild of a Japanese engineer, now the chef, and his wife, now the maître d'. For over a decade, they’ve been feeding hungry diners in the neighbourhood with quality grilled food, with some ingredients flown in from Japan. Rare cuts such as chicken heart and hatsumoto (artery) are definitely worth a try. Pair them with their selection of sake or home-brewed umeshu. Reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
6505;Shek Kee Kitchen;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;15-17 Ngan Mok Street, Tin Hau, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.283777;114.19232;58;true;false;Cantonese;During the day, this cosy joint in the heart of the city serves light meals and fried noodles. At night, the menu specialises in home-style Cantonese dishes. The owner-chef Mr Shek sources the freshest ingredients from wet markets daily and regulars also call him directly to pre-order certain dishes, such as fried chicken with toasted garlic which needs a day’s notice. The pan-fried hand-minced cuttlefish patties are springy and flavourful.;Air conditioning;[]
6506;Samsen (Wan Chai);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;68 Stone Nullah Lane, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2741218;114.1741767;91;false;true;Thai;This casual Thai noodle shop next to the historic Blue House is aptly named after an area in Bangkok where the Chinese traded with the Thais. Rattan blinds, bare concrete walls and distressed wood furniture give off a street-stall vibe. The signature boat noodles are not to be missed – the flavoursome broth alone takes 6 hours to make. Those with a sweet tooth can round things off with young coconut ice cream. Come early to beat the crowd.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6507;Kung Wo Beancurd Factory;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;118 Pei Ho Street, Sham Shui Po, Hong Kong;22.331143;114.1635554;97;false;true;Street Food;This much-loved shop makes its own tofu that boasts a deep, rich soy aroma. As well as the renowned tofu pudding, it also carries other soy products like soy milk, fried stuffed tofu, tofu puffs and golden fish tofu.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6508;Ah Chun Shandong Dumpling;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;60 Lai Chi Kok Road, Prince Edward, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3239663;114.1666817;85;false;true;Dumplings;The shop has a traditional feel to it. Green wooden window frames on the wall are reminiscent of old-time Hong Kong. Dumplings are handmade daily and only the freshest ingredients are used in the fillings. Try their most-ordered item lamb and Peking scallion dumplings. Or surprise yourself with the specialty, such as mackerel dumplings and cuttlefish dumplings. Shandong roast lamb and meat pie are also recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
6509;She Wong Leung;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop A, GF, 298 Electric Road, North Point, Hong Kong;22.289986;114.194276;99;false;false;Cantonese;In business for over 20 years, this shop is famous for its snake soup. While most people consume snake soup only in winter, the owner formulates a different herbal base for every season to make it a healthy tonic all year round. Set menus comprising of snake soup and home-style dishes offer exceptional value and cater for all tastes. Go for glutinous rice or lamb stew in winter. Double-boiled soups are popular but require pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6510;Shugetsu Ramen (Central);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;5 Gough Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.284133;114.1529359;47;false;true;Ramen;The queues form early for the ramen here, with many of the customers coming for the Tsukemen ramen, as well as the Abura and special soup ramen. The shop makes its own noodles – which you can have thick or thin – but it is the sauce at the base of the slow-cooked soup that really makes the difference: it’s fermented for 18 months in a 100-year-old wooden basket and adds richness and depth.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6511;Fisholic (North Point);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 14, GF, Victor Court, 14-28 Wang On Road, North Point, Hong Kong;22.2883198;114.1920637;98;true;true;Street Food;Famous for snacks and noodles made with fish, this stall sells playful items like deep-fried minced fish in the guise of French fries, or fish skin nachos. Fishotto, where minced fish is shaped like rice grains, is also good.;Air conditioning;[]
6512;Lok Kei Noodles (Patane);;Macau;1-D Travessa da Saudade, Macau, Macau;22.2011387;113.5372218;84;true;true;Noodles and Congee;This busy shop next to the Chun Lei pier still kneads the noodles with a bamboo pole like in bygone days. The owner’s wife then cooks them perfectly, thus explaining their bouncy texture. The broth simmered with an array of seasonal fish boasts depth and sweetness. Dried prawn roe sprinkled on tossed noodles is toasted by the owner himself, imparting umami and aroma. Also try the crab congee and deep-fried wontons with crispy dace balls.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6513;Wing Lai Yuen;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 102-105, 1F, Gourmet Place, Whampoa Plaza, Site 8, Whampoa Garden, 7 Tak On Street, Hung Hom, Hong Kong;22.3062745;114.1912219;51;true;false;Shanghainese, Sichuan;Originally a run-down shop in a squatter village, it moved to this airy and bright location in 2000. But one thing never changed – the food is as delicious and affordably priced as ever. The signature Dan Dan noodles come in two versions: a meat one with ground pork and a traditional one without, plus a spicy or mild broth to choose from. Shuizhu mandarin fish packs numbing heat and the portion size is big enough for a few to share.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6514;Wang Fu;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;168 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.284531;114.1533136;42;false;false;Dumplings;Wang Fu is famous for its Pekingese dumplings – among the great variety of handmade dumplings on the menu, the green onion mutton one stands out most. Apart from dumpling soups, it also serves fried dumplings with light charred crispy skin and juicy fillings. Try also the tomato and egg dumpling, only available after 2 pm. If you fancy more variety, check out their noodles and cold appetisers as well, or ask about the daily special.;Air conditioning;[]
6515;Tsim Chai Kee (Wellington Street);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;98 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2830291;114.1544658;76;false;false;Noodles;The long lunchtime queue happens for a reason – the noodles here are bouncy and the broth is flavoursome. Only three toppings are offered – springy dace balls, wontons generously filled with pork and shrimps, and sliced beef with a robust meaty flavour and tender texture. You can even choose a combination of any two or all three toppings. Expect to share a table with strangers when it’s busy or eat outside of peak times to beat the crowd.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6516;Kwan Kee Bamboo Noodles;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop E, 1 Wing Lung Street, Cheung Sha Wan, Hong Kong;22.33759;114.15815;40;true;true;Noodles;It’s inside a local market but easy to spot, thanks to the big yellow sign. Watch the kitchen at work through the glass wall as noodles are made the traditional way – with the chef seesawing on a bamboo pole to painstakingly knead the egg-rich dough for that stringy texture. Secret techniques are deployed to remove the soapy taste of lye and accentuate the eggy flavour. Don’t miss the signature noodles tossed in shrimp roe and oyster sauce.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6517;Megan's Kitchen;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;5F, Lucky Centre, 165-171 Wan Chai Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2768945;114.1770548;40;false;false;Cantonese;The menu offers many Cantonese dishes, but steamed minced beef patty with dried mandarin peel, and Yu Xiang eggplant in claypot stand out in particular. Better still, all mains come with complimentary rice, soup and dessert. Their famous hot pots spoil diners with an array of soup bases and good quality ingredients. Those who prefer a little privacy will appreciate the booth seating with sliding screens as dividers.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
6518;Eng Kee Noodle Shop;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, 32 High Street, Sai Ying Pun, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2850988;114.1423904;86;true;false;Noodles;This family-run shop is always jam-packed with hungry locals craving Cantonese noodle soup. No matter for dine-in or take-out, expect a reasonable wait. It prides itself on its signature beef brisket – braised one night ahead and steeped in a spiced marinade overnight for silky tenderness and deep flavours. Their oven-grilled char siu is made with pork shoulder and pork neck and has a juicy, springy texture thanks to the fine marbling.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6520;Sister Wah;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop A1, 13 Electric Road, Tin Hau, Hong Kong;22.2833555;114.191605;22;false;true;Noodles;The legendary Sister Wah is no longer at the helm but her sons are running the shop just like she used to. The signature beef brisket in clear soup uses fresh local beef which is braised in a stock with over 10 different herbs. Popular items on the brief menu include homemade pork and cabbage dumplings, drunken chicken, Dan Dan noodles, and braised white radish in beef juices. With only six tables, it fills up as soon as it opens.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6521;Din Tai Fung (COD);;Macau;SOHO, 2F, City of Dreams, Estrada do Istmo, Cotai, Macau;22.140643;113.5603989;17;true;true;Shanghainese;The second floor of COD plays host to a plethora of casual eateries – and in the corner you’ll find this sizeable branch of the international chain. Din Tai Fung is rightly known for its exquisite xiao long bao but also special here is the steamed crab roe and pork dumpling. Other notables from the 70-odd Shanghainese dishes on offer include the excellent braised beef noodle soup. To finish, try the red bean glutinous rice cake.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6522;Chan Seng Kei;;Macau;21 Rua Caetano, Coloane, Macau;22.1168061;113.5514554;53;false;false;Cantonese;This semi open-air restaurant has stood next to an ancient church for over 70 years and the 3rd generation of the family still focus on traditional Cantonese cooking. Seafood is the highlight as the owner works closely with local fishermen to secure the best catch – he prefers wild-caught fish about 500 to 600g for their tender flesh. Also try stewed duck with tangerine peel which takes more than 10 hours to make, with only a few available each day.;;[]
6523;Tai Woo;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;9F, Causeway Bay Plaza 2, 463-483 Lockhart Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2805157;114.182205;53;false;true;Cantonese;One of the district’s most famous names, Tai Woo opened its door in the 80s and moved to this address in 2011 and, while the restaurant may be smaller than before, business is better than ever, with over 1,000 customers served every day. What hasn’t changed is the quality of the cooking – along with a menu of wallet friendly Cantonese seafood dishes, such as fish fried rice with ginger, are favourites like sesame chicken baked in salt.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6526;Yuan is Here (Western District);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;31 North Street, Western District, Hong Kong;22.2825025;114.1291658;62;true;false;Taiwanese;Decorated with memorabilia and buzzing with night market vibes, this street food shop is the brainchild of its Taiwan-born owner. Some ingredients are imported direct from his hometown to ensure that every bite is as authentic as possible. The signature minced braised pork rice boasts depth and a melty texture, while the traditionally-made double egg oyster omelette is both chewy and eggy at the same time. Round off with taro ball sweet soup.;Air conditioning;[]
6527;Yi Jia;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop G04, Lime Gala, 393 Shau Kei Wan Road, Shau Kei Wan, Hong Kong;22.2774544;114.2289404;77;false;false;Shanghainese, Sichuan;A stark contrast of colours, neon lights and retro patterns make the room unorthodox but welcoming. On the menu, you can find Shanghainese and Sichuanese classics like Qili Zhuang drunken chicken in wine lees, and Sichuan boiled fish. But novelty creations such as deep-fried soufflé meringue with mango custard filling are also worth trying. The creator’s sense of humour comes through in the cheeky drinks menu. Set menus are especially well priced.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6528;Little Napoli;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, 6-16 Tai Wong Street East, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2760356;114.1714626;21;false;true;Italian;True to the chef’s hometown traditions, classic Neapolitan pizzas and street foods like ripieno fritto and panuozzo are made with only ingredients from Naples. Pizzas such as Margherita or Vesuviana are made to order, baked in an Italian stone oven at 400°C, and served whole, not sliced, boasting a puffy, nicely charred crust and gooey centre. It’s basically a grab-and-go pizzeria with a few seats, so come early if you want to dine in.;Air conditioning;[]
6530;Tim Ho Wan (Sham Shui Po);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;9-11 Fuk Wing Street, Sham Shui Po, Hong Kong;22.3291186;114.1663677;78;true;false;Dim Sum;The second branch of this famous dim sum chain is roomier than the original, but don’t be surprised to still find a queue of expectant diners at the entrance. Over 20 different dim sum are on offer, all skilfully made and reasonably priced. Some items rotate every two to three months to keep the menu fresh. Don’t miss their shrimp dumplings, baked buns with barbecue pork filling and steamed beef balls.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6531;Twins Liangpi Limited (Mong Kok);;Hong Kong;GF, 99 Hak Po Street, Mong Kok, Hong Kong;22.3195906;114.1721304;20;false;false;Street Food;Now with a dine-in option, the shop has moved to Mong Kok. Glass noodles dressed in a secret blend of chilli vinegar are topped with shredded cucumber, coriander, peas and ground peanuts. Choose your preferred level of spiciness.;Air conditioning;[]
6532;Glorious Cuisine;;Hong Kong;31-33 Shek Kip Mei Street, Sham Shui Po, Hong Kong;22.329836;114.1650113;59;false;false;Cantonese;Picking out live critters from the tank is part of the fun – Hokkaido scallops, Thai marble goby, and even Hanasaki crab if you’re lucky. As well as the signature braised chicken stuffed with abalone and sea cucumber, do try dishes made with chicken offal, such as stock-poached leafy greens with chicken liver. Double-boiled chicken soup with conpoy and Yunnan ham is available in limited quantities, so consider pre-ordering certain items.;Air conditioning;[]
6533;Sang Kee;;Hong Kong;3-4F, Sunshine Plaza, 353 Lockhart Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2795496;114.1789;37;true;true;Cantonese;An iconic landmark of Wan Chai since 1976, Sang Kee has moved shop. The room is brighter, more spacious and offers more seating. But rest assured: the menu hasn’t changed and the food is as good as ever. Despite the lack of fancy plating and luxury ingredients, you’ll find yourself craving their salt-baked chicken, pork liver and wolfberry leaves blanched in stock, and baked fish intestine with egg long after you’ve gone home.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
6534;Man Yuen;;Hong Kong;Shop S02, 2F, Tin Ma Court Commercial Centre, 55 Chuk Yuen Road, Wong Tai Sin, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.343021;114.187282;63;true;false;Cantonese;This newcomer to the East Kowloon dining scene is tucked away on a public housing estate, but that doesn't stop diners coming in droves from near and far for quality Cantonese dishes made with fresh ingredients. The kitchen and front-of-house teams have worked in exclusive clubs, hotels and restaurants – quality of food and service are guaranteed. The menu features all-time classics such as wok hei-laden "king of stir-fries" with fresh, dried and sakura shrimps.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6535;Sing Kee;;Hong Kong;2F, 1 Lyndhurst Tower, 1 Lyndhurst Terrace, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2826018;114.15475;21;false;false;Cantonese;Sing Kee is a bright, tidy spot serving traditional, no-frills Cantonese food – something that’s increasingly hard to find in Central. Standouts include pan-seared salted chicken, and grilled tiger prawns in Malaysian curry sauce with crispy rice crackers. Specialities like double-boiled fish maw and pork lung in almond milk need pre-ordering. Come at lunch to take advantage of some reasonable prices.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6537;Ancient Moon;;Hong Kong;Shop A, 29 Kam Ping Street, North Point, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2902387;114.2000899;39;true;false;Singaporean and Malaysian;On a trip to Singapore and Malaysia, owners Fanni and Lico fell in love with their street food which inspired them to open their fun little spot. The small menu lists about 20 items, but you won’t find typical national dishes here. Instead, it’s among the few places that offer Malaysian chilli pan mee (a flavoursome noodle dish with dried fish and chilli sauce) and free refill of Singaporean bak kut teh, a MSG-free, peppery pork rib soup.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6538;Trusty Congee King (Wan Chai);;Hong Kong;7 Heard Street, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2775458;114.1771157;50;false;false;Noodles and Congee;As suggested by its name, you can really trust the quality of the food served in this long-standing congee shop. The menu has become more versatile in recent years with congee, noodles and snack sets available. All congee is cooked in fish broth that gives an extra dimension of flavour. Many rave about the pork liver and scallop congee, sticky rice dumpling with salted egg yolk and pork, and poached grass carp skin.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6539;Ba Yi;;Hong Kong;43 Water Street, Sai Ying Pun, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2853864;114.1390387;76;true;false;Xinjiang;Despite being somewhat out of the way, lamb-lovers gather here in numbers for items such as stewed lamb and mutton skewers, prepared by the Xinjiangese kitchen team. The signature roasted lamb leg is big enough to share between two and needs pre-ordering. Besides lamb, it’s also worth trying the chicken stew with potato and chilli, as well as the Ketik yoghurt drink. The dining room still features the map of the Silk Road on a stretched canvas.;Air conditioning;[]
6540;Lou Kei;;Macau;Shop H&M, GF, Vang Kei Building, 12 Avenida Da Concõrdia N, Macau, Macau;22.2084446;113.5436374;35;true;false;Cantonese;Though slightly out of the way, Lou Kei is a firm favourite among locals for a simple, good value supper. For over 20 years, its sizeable selection of tasty noodles, congee and Cantonese dishes has won the hearts of countless diners. With heaps of crispy fried garlic and chilli bits, the typhoon shelter-style deep-fried Bombay duck is delicious. Claypot rice with eel in black bean sauce boasts firm, oily fish on crispy scorched rice.;Air conditioning;[]
6541;Chiuchow Delicacies;;Hong Kong;Shop 4, GF, Gain Yu Building, 96 Wharf Road, North Point, Hong Kong;22.2922281;114.1977477;62;true;true;Chiu Chow;This shop isn’t particularly spacious, but that doesn’t stop customers from coming here for their authentic Chiu Chow cooking at wallet-friendly prices. Sliced goose steeped in signature spiced marinade is velvety without being greasy – refer to the mural for the spices used. The variety of chilled steamed fish on offer is quite a spectacle, all oily and delicious. Some dishes need pre-ordering and expect to share a table with strangers when it’s busy.;Air conditioning;[]
6542;Din Tai Fung (Causeway Bay);;Hong Kong;Shop G3-G11, GF, 68 Yee Woo Street, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2793736;114.1863857;40;true;true;Shanghainese;The xiao long bao are good enough to justify the long queues – so worry not. Alongside the traditional soupy pork filling, they also come in novelty versions such as black truffle and angled luffa with shrimps. Ingredients are sourced from the same suppliers as its Taiwan flagship and the same kitchen team here delivers food in consistently high quality. Other standouts include double-boiled chicken soup and braised beef brisket noodle soup.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6543;Café Hunan (Western District);;Hong Kong;420-424 Queen's Road West, Western District, Hong Kong;22.2864263;114.1387421;26;false;false;Hunanese;The kitchen team of Hunanese natives boasts solid skills, especially in quick-fried dishes that sport exceptional wok hei. Ingredients such as chillies and smoked pork are sourced directly from farmers in Hunan. The speciality braised pork elbow involves four complicated cooking steps spanning over 10 hours to develop layered flavours and the right texture. Stir-fried pork with Youxian beancurd and spicy organic cauliflower are also worth trying.;Air conditioning;[]
6547;Ju Xing Home;;Hong Kong;GF, 416 and 418 Portland Street, Prince Edward, Hong Kong;22.32556;114.167496;66;false;false;Cantonese;This hole-in-the-wall is always jam-packed and that's down to chef-owner Ng's cooking, not the decor or service. Cantonese stir-fries prevail, alongside a few spicy options. The must-try salt-baked Wenchang chicken is succulent, flavoursome… and tends to run out early. Live seafood is also big on the menu, eg pan-fried prawn in soy sauce or steamed eel in black bean sauce. Reservations are recommended and it's worth pre-ordering the chicken to avoid missing out.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6548;Kapok;;Macau;60 Rua de Hong Chau, Taipa, Macau;22.1614302;113.555374;72;false;true;Cantonese;With ceiling fans, bowl pendant lights and Lingnan-style stained glass, the room is the epitome of yesteryear glamour. The menu is likewise dominated by traditionally made Cantonese favourites - diced pork fat gives har gow extra depth of flavour and the white sugar sponge is perfectly proofed without a hint of sourness. Don’t miss their green chillies stuffed with minced dace, double-boiled soups or seafood dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
6549;Saya;;Hong Kong;Shop G701, GF, Square Mile II, 18 Ka Shin Street, Tai Kok Tsui, Hong Kong;22.320231;114.1612917;65;true;false;Thai;A turquoise colour scheme, rattan furniture and wall coverings impart a retro tropical vibe. The menu is dominated by Isan cuisine from Northeast Thailand, mindfully prepared by a Thai kitchen team. Khao Soy bursts with aromas from the coconut milk curry and chargrilled chicken. Pla Phao, salt-crusted grilled fish seasoned with lemongrass and pandan, is served with lettuce, rice vermicelli and a tangy sauce. Lunch menu offers great value.;Air conditioning;[]
6550;Tai Wai Dining Room (Tai Wai);;Hong Kong;98 Chik Fuk Street, Tai Wai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3743251;114.1788375;18;false;true;Cantonese;The red lanterns at the entrance are a prelude to the nostalgic, Chinese-style interior. The experienced kitchen team shows respect to Cantonese traditions, but with a subtle sense of cheeky humour. Dim sum dominates the menu at lunch, and all-time favourites like duo sausage rolls and pan-fried chicken sticky rice dumplings particularly stand out. Portion sizes are generous, service is thoughtful – and the food is consistently good.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
6551;Son Tak Kong;;Macau;106A Rua do Mercadores, Macau, Macau;22.19423;113.53838;59;true;true;Shun Tak;Since 1979, Son Tak Kong has been jam-packed with happy regulars, lured by its no-frills, authentic Shun Tak cuisine. A Shun Tak native himself, the owner hires chefs for whom the secrets of Cantonese and Shun Tak food have no secrets. Their signature creamy fish soup calls upon exquisite knife work, first-rate ingredients and rich, slowly simmered fish broth. Also try the sticky rice with Sakura shrimps and pine nuts in a cast iron pot.;Air conditioning;[]
6552;Yue Kee;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;9 Sham Hong Road, Sham Tseng, Hong Kong;22.368364;114.0596883;24;false;true;Cantonese;From humble beginnings as a tiny countryside joint in 1958, this second-generation family business has gone big, but without losing its flair. Owning a farm that breeds Qingyuan black brown geese ensures quality and a steady supply. Chargrilled according to the owner’s family recipe and served after 11:45am, their goose is known for its distinctive smokiness, crispy skin and juicy meat. The menu also includes seafood and stir-fries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
6553;Kai Kai (Jordan);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;29 Ning Po Street, Jordan, Hong Kong;22.3065845;114.1710599;81;true;true;Street Food;Traditional Chinese sweet soups like tofu skin soup with ginkgo and Job’s tears, or black sesame soup boast rich flavours. Top it with glutinous rice balls or a hard-boiled egg for extra texture.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6554;Putien (Causeway Bay);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop A, 7F, Lee Theatre Plaza, 99 Percival Street, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.278337;114.18335;15;false;true;Fujian;The original restaurant was founded in Singapore in 2000 and named after a coastal city in Fujian province – the owner’s hometown. This branch comes with an easy-going atmosphere and its Fujian cuisine is respectful of tradition, with a focus on natural flavours. New items are added to the menu from time to time. Don’t miss their themed offerings that feature a particular seasonal seafood, such as razor clams or oysters.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6556;Samsen (Sheung Wan);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;23 Jervois Street, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.2852363;114.1526142;48;false;false;Thai;Readers may recognize the name it shares with a noodle shop in Wan Chai – yes, this is a spinoff by the same owner-chef, Adam Cliff. While it shares almost the same menu as the Wan Chai branch, certain exclusive dishes stand out. For instance, its signature 11-spice Northern Thai curry takes up to eight hours to make and is the perfect companion to egg noodles. Desserts like young coconut ice cream or mango and sticky rice are also pluses.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6557;Sai Kwan Lo Jo;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop B, 18 Man Yuen Street, Jordan, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3075707;114.1666221;94;false;false;Street Food;This takeout-only shop carries both traditional and novelty snacks. Try hand-made lai fun noodles in Sai Kwan style, deep-fried sticky rice dumpling with Iberico pork, or stir-fried turnip cake with XO chilli sauce.;;[]
6558;Hao Tang Hao Mian (Tai Wai);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, 20 Chik Chuen Street, Tai Wai, Hong Kong;22.3763259;114.1775046;64;false;false;Noodles;An owner-chef with over 20 years of experience in French cooking opened this 20-seater specialising in just 12 noodle soup items, each with a specific soup base and topping. The signature flat noodles in beef soup with Sichuanese beef cheek and French-style braised oxtail takes two days to make, involving eclectic techniques. The dessert menu is equally impressive – try the all-natural sorbets made in-house with fresh fruits.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6559;Fung Shing (North Point);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;62-68 Java Road, North Point, Hong Kong;22.2917566;114.1982237;81;true;true;Shun Tak;This long-standing champion of Shun Tak cuisine sports traditional fixtures and fittings. Locals and tourists come for dim sum in the morning, while painstakingly prepared Cantonese favourites and Shun Tak specialities are served at lunch and dinner. Besides signatures like crispy fried chicken and Daliang-style scrambled egg white with milk, don’t miss their sugar egg puff doughnuts available at weekend lunchtime only. Hearty portions to share.;Air conditioning;[]
6561;Norma;Portugal;Guimaraes;Rua Doutor José Sampaio 35, Guimaraes, 4810 275, Portugal;41.4427754;-8.2905021;28;false;false;Creative, Portuguese;Norma occupies an old building that almost passes by unnoticed, yet boasts delightful views, especially from its terrace, from where the vista encompasses São Gualter church, the iconic symbol of the city. The head chef here is Hugo Alves who, having worked in leading restaurants around Portugal, decided to return to his native Guimarães. His cooking is centred on a tasting menu and an à la carte that change every season. Dishes that are a must include the profiterole made with crab, tomato, sweet basil and cream cheese, and the mouthwatering “bràs”. For vegetarians, we recommended the delicious “feijoada” of celery, sesame, tsukudani and orange.;Terrace;[]
6562;Avista;Portugal;Funchal;Estrada Monumental 145, Funchal, 9004-532, Portugal;32.6398651;-16.925279;18;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Part of the fabulous The Cliff Bay hotel, Avista is run by the prestigious chef Benoît Sinthon (Il Gallo d'Oro, two Michelin Stars) and, like its older “brother”, boasts truly spectacular views, with the coast, the vast Atlantic Ocean and nearby islands as a backdrop. Here, the cuisine Mediterranean highlights the restaurant’s philosophy of informality in which the idea of sharing plates to enable guests to try more dishes is key, along with a focus on fresh ingredients of the very highest quality.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6563;Zunzum Gastrobar;Portugal;Lisbon;Avenida Infante D. Henrique. Doca do Jardim do Tabaco, Lisbon, 1100-651, Portugal;38.7120997;-9.1241681;83;true;true;Contemporary;This elegant, completely glass-fronted gastro-bar, occupying a modern building close to the city’s cruise ship terminal (and opposite the unusual Museu do Lactário or Milk Station Museum), favours high-quality contemporary cuisine that is based around traditional Portuguese recipes, but without closing the door on inspiration, dishes or techniques from further afield. The bright, designer-inspired interior, with its predominant red and white colour scheme, and the terrace boasting pleasant views of the Tagus come as a pleasant surprise.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6564;Camelo;Portugal;Viana do Castelo;Rua de Santa Marta 119, Viana do Castelo, 4925-104, Portugal;41.7093706;-8.772368;26;false;true;Regional Cuisine;This family-run restaurant is always full despite its location in a part of town most people generally pass through without stopping. Its facilities include a bar, which leads to several pleasantly arranged dining rooms, a large marquee-style space for private functions, plus a huge garden patio for outdoor gatherings. The high-quality and varied cuisine on offer here is typical of the Minho, featuring fish and seafood from its own live tank, with a predilection for lamprey, plus an extensive selection of meat dishes and even a vegetarian menu. When in season, the lamprey dishes are a must!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6565;Carvalho;Portugal;Chaves;Alameda do Tabolado, Chaves, 5400-523, Portugal;41.7379667;-7.4705264;32;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located opposite the Tabolado garden and close to the river, in an area with easy parking. Behind the impeccable façade you’ll find a reasonably comfortable and welcoming interior with the main dining room by the entrance and a second space, which is also home to the wine cellar, in the basement. The female owner is at the helm in the kitchen, offering high-quality home-inspired cooking on a menu that changes daily and always includes fresh fish and other typical specialities such as “alheira”, a smoked sausage made with pork and chicken. Superb, friendly service from the front-of-house team completes the picture!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6566;Tasquinha da Linda;Portugal;Viana do Castelo;Rua dos Mareantes A-10, Viana do Castelo, 4900-351, Portugal;41.6887829;-8.8366845;86;false;false;Seafood;One of the best dining options in this attractive town on the Costa Verde, this contemporary restaurant located next to the Castelo de Santiago da Barra occupies a docks warehouse in which the large attractive fish and seafood tanks take pride of place. Its owners are fish wholesalers, hence the top-quality fish and seafood that is on offer here, normally sold by weight and at prices that are highly competitive. You won’t find a single meat dish on the menu here! Make sure you save space for desserts made by the owners’ daughter!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6567;O Javali;Portugal;Bragança;Quinta do Reconco 6, Bragança, 5300-672, Portugal;41.83615;-6.7476006;79;false;true;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant that is well run by a couple who are highly passionate about their work, with the husband running the front of house and his wife in charge in the kitchen. Easy to find given its location by the main road, it features a reasonably spacious car park, a public bar and two rustically themed dining rooms, both boasting stone walls and a hunting-inspired decor. Its menu showcases the traditional dishes of the Trás-os-Montes region (including game), all of which are copious and based around the freshest ingredients. Make sure you try the wild boar stew with chestnuts, the rice with hare, and the Bragança-style lamb.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6569;Dóri;Portugal;Costa Nova do Prado;Rua das Companhas, Costa Nova do Prado, 3830-453, Portugal;40.6111673;-8.7495746;29;false;false;Seafood;Situated between the Aveiro estuary and the Atlantic, on the first floor of a contemporary glass-fronted building offering splendid views, particularly from the terrace. The bar features an enticing display cabinet, while the two dining rooms are bright and functional-contemporary in feel. Although the menu includes delicious meats and a few savoury rice dishes, the speciality here is the wild fish, cooked on the open grill, and the seafood. Don’t leave without trying the fried fish (“fritada de pescado”) or the delicious “ensopado” of turbot.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6570;Solar do Forcado;Portugal;Portalegre;Rua Candido dos Reis 14, Portalegre, 7300-129, Portugal;39.2907546;-7.4294786;66;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located along a narrow, cobbled street in the town’s old quarter, reasonably close to the castle. The modest façade leads to a small but welcoming dining room with a rustic feel and a decor that revolves around the world of bullfighting. Here, the traditional cuisine is focused on meat, with the occasional dish dedicated to bulls in the ring, in homage to the team of “forcados”, a typical aspect of Portuguese bullfights in which both the owner and his father were once involved. Make sure you try the exquisite skewers of bull’s meat, not forgetting the “cozido à portuguesa” stew served every Thursday!;Air conditioning;[]
6571;Casal da Penha;Portugal;Funchal;Rua Penha de França - Beco do Ataíde n.1, Funchal, 9000-014, Portugal;32.642883;-16.919317;69;true;false;Portuguese;A family-run restaurant that extols the virtues of all that is simple yet authentic with a menu which lets the ingredients do the talking. Located in the centre of Funchal, surrounded by large hotels, its modest yet neat and tidy dining room is enhanced by the superb terrace upstairs. The father is in charge of the kitchen, where he prepares dishes with a traditional flavour including lots of regional specialities, delicious fish of the day options, an extensive choice of meats, and tasty rice dishes, including a variety of paellas. Make sure you order the clams “à Bulhão Pato” if available – they are truly delicious!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6572;Ofício - Tasco Atípico;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Nova da Trindade 11, Lisbon, 1200-301, Portugal;38.7122215;-9.1425152;21;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This centrally located restaurant, almost directly opposite the Bairro do Avillez gastronomic complex, defines itself as an "atypical tasco ", where the concept is to offer contemporary Portuguese cuisine perfect for sharing, served in the informal atmosphere of a typical neighbourhood restaurant. Here, you’ll find starters, petiscos, hot specialities, sharing boards and seasonal dishes on the menu, all of which showcase excellent technique, typical flavours and the occasional Mexican touch, given that the chef worked in the famous (and now defunct) Hoja Santa restaurant in Barcelona.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6573;Inato Bistrô;Portugal;Braga;Praça do Município 7, Braga, 4700 435, Portugal;41.5508023;-8.4275041;16;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;The name of this restaurant stems from In“ATO”, which in Portuguese means something that is active or in movement, a theme continued on the menu where dishes are served in different acts (I, II, III and IV). Young chefs Miguel Rodrigues and Tiago Costa have joined forces to showcase their creative cuisine, which makes full use of the best-quality local ingredients. Located opposite the elegant setting of the municipal square in the heart of Braga, Inato reminds us that it is possible to prepare amazing dishes from the simplest of ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
6574;Solar do Bacalhau;Portugal;Coimbra;Rua da Sota 10, Coimbra, 3000-392, Portugal;40.2085689;-8.4309703;46;true;false;Portuguese;A good location in the Baixa de Coimbra, the section of the old town occupied by merchants and artisans in the Middle Ages. If you’re keen to try the famous Portuguese bacalao you won’t find a better place, as this restaurant impresses with its attractive interior design on two floors, stone walls, a glass-enclosed inner patio and lots of natural light. À la carte and set menu options feature a variety of regional specialities, superb cod dishes cooked in different ways, and a good selection of meats. The display cabinets at the entrance provide a welcoming taster of what’s to come!;Air conditioning;[]
6575;Casa Chef Victor Felisberto;Portugal;Abrantes;Rua Francisco Ferreira da Mata 99, Abrantes, 2200-223, Portugal;39.469672;-8.1986648;98;false;true;Meats and Grills, Regional Cuisine;Discover the special vision of regional cooking showcased by Victor Felisberto, a Portuguese chef with an impressive track record who trained in Paris and gained experience in restaurants in France as well as others in London, Barcelona and Andorra. His speciality is meat cooked over a wood fire, in particular Iberian pork and veal, with the unique feature of using very slow cooking techniques to ensure sublime textures and much more intense flavours. He favours traditionally inspired dishes, home-made desserts of a high quality and bread made with his own recipe.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6576;3 Pipos;Portugal;Tonda;Rua de Santo Amaro 966, Tonda, 3460-479, Portugal;40.4971827;-8.0718486;79;false;false;Regional Cuisine;The emblem of this restaurant, which is now into its fourth decade and is spoken of very highly by everyone, is three barrels – a reference to its close connection with the wine sector. It features an entrance hall and several dining rooms with a classic-rustic feel and wine-focused decor, in which the menu showcases the cuisine of the Beira Alta region. The simple, copious dishes on offer include pork rice in a garlic and wine sauce, octopus “à lagareiro”, and the loin of confit cod with spinach and pork sausage. The spacious garden and its wine club that sells direct to the public at affordable prices add to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6577;O Frade;Portugal;Lisbon;Calçada da Ajuda 14, Lisbon, 1300-006, Portugal;38.6978416;-9.1993882;42;true;false;Regional Cuisine;A small corner restaurant named after the family that owns it. Its interior is evocative of a traditional Alentejo “tasca”, with simple decorative details that highlight the production of the famous “vinho da talha”, a wine with a long historical footprint that, in keeping with Roman tradition, is made in large earthenware amphorae and is a highly renowned wine in the Alentejo. Welcoming service, plus an attractive U-shaped bar popular for dining, where guests can savour a variety of “petiscos”, rice dishes and traditional Alentejo recipes with a contemporary touch – all accompanied by an extensive choice of wines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6578;In Diferente;Portugal;Porto;Rua do Doutor Sousa Rosa 23, Porto, 4150-719, Portugal;41.1554566;-8.6768849;20;false;true;International;Despite not being in the centre of town or on any of the main tourist routes, it is well worth heading to this peaceful, welcoming and contemporary-style restaurant. Here, Angélica Salvador, the young chef of Brazilian origin, interprets her personal vision of traditional Portuguese and international cooking through dishes that are elaborate and very well presented. Her aim is to create dishes that are different, personal and showcase innovative detail, extracting maximum benefit from the superb fish delivered to the nearby auctions in Matosinhos and Aveiro, as well as from the region’s outstanding meats.;;[]
6580;Olaias;Portugal;Figueira da Foz;Rua Abade Pedro 2 - Centro de Artes e Espectáculos, Figueira da Foz, 3080 081, Portugal;40.153035;-8.8604194;58;false;false;Portuguese;This is a restaurant that provides you with an excuse to return at any time of year… and why not! The house speciality, the savoury Carolino rice (with rice grown in the Mondego valley), changes constantly with the seasons, and is cooked in a clay oven, which brings added flavour. We recommend starting with the mouthwatering and smooth Rissol da Tia Fernanda, which is absolutely delicious. Next, it has to be rice, of course (with any accompaniment – duck, fish or oxtail – all are excellent choices) and, to finish, the moist “pão de ló” cake with sea salt, which is truly heavenly. The restaurant is located in the Centro de Artes e Espectáculos and has a meticulous yet unpretentious decor, featuring floor to ceiling windows and fantastic views!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6581;O Pastus;Portugal;Paço de Arcos;Avenida Marquês De Pombal 5, Paço de Arcos, 2770-066, Portugal;38.6940104;-9.2929161;73;true;false;Portuguese, Contemporary;This modest yet charming restaurant opposite the Paço de Arcos gardens is characterised by great enthusiasm, painstaking service and the hard work of young Annakaren Fuentes, who is on top of everything. The cooking here can be defined as modern Portuguese, based around respect for traditional ingredients and flavours, showcased in one tasting menu, entitled Cabal (7 courses). Individual dishes can also be ordered à la carte.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6583;Carnal;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua da Misericordia 78, Lisbon, 1200 273, Portugal;38.7124157;-9.1430035;48;true;false;Mexican;This lively, centrally located restaurant has quickly become fashionable given that it is owned by famous chef Ljubomir Stanisic (head of the 100 Maneiras group). Carnal describes itself as a Mexican gastro-bar, and is one of those places that immediately appeals to the senses. In its informal, modern design setting featuring subtle details relating to Mexican culture, enjoy harmonious, well-thought-out cooking with a perfect balance between flavour and spiciness in every one of its superb dishes. Don’t miss the delicious pork tacos or the tacos with fried cauliflower.;Air conditioning;[]
6584;Gruta;Portugal;Porto;Rua De Santa Catarina 447, Porto, 4000-452, Portugal;41.1500107;-8.6057703;36;true;false;International;Gruta’s is one of those of places where you can eat well at a reasonable price. To a backdrop of stylish yet informal decor and a setting in an alleyway just off a shopping street, focuses on a concise menu on which fish and seafood (mainly from the north of the country) take centre stage. Its dishes are high on presentation and flavour, combining Brazilian and Portuguese influences and a contemporary style of cooking.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6585;Marquês de Marialva;Portugal;Cantanhede;Largo do Romal 16, Cantanhede, 3060-129, Portugal;40.34865;-8.59263;81;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The name pays a small homage to this Portuguese nobleman who played a decisive part in several battles during the Restoration War. The restaurant enjoys a certain prestige as well as a good location in an old house that has been restored. It boasts three intimate dining rooms combining classic and rustic decorative detail, one with an open fire, plus a large function room upstairs. Dishes with a distinct traditional flavour can be found on the à la carte, alongside several tasting menus. Make sure you try the “lagareiro”-style baked cod and the exquisite roast kid!;Car park;[]
6586;Machado;Portugal;Nogueira;Rua Doutor António José de Almeida 467, Nogueira, 4475-456, Portugal;41.2404799;-8.5912502;94;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Quality and quantity are both guaranteed at this restaurant occupying an old house in a small village close to Maia. Several separate dining rooms, all with a similar rustic decor, simple table settings and lots of typical decorative details hanging from the walls. Here, it is impossible to leave hungry given the copious portions on the traditional home-cooked menu which teems with local flavours. Make sure you try Machado’s house speciality, the Lafões-style roast veal.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6587;Pátio 44;Portugal;Porto;Passeio De São Lázaro, 44, Porto, 4000 508, Portugal;41.146449;-8.6022694;53;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;At Patio 44, you’ll be pleasantly surprised by the quality of ingredients used as well as the discreet and simple façade. This project was created by three friends, with chefs Simão Soares and Alfonso Ramos in charge of the kitchen – a partnership that developed from experience working together in a previous restaurant. Their cuisine is centred around traditional Portuguese cuisine enhanced by modern techniques and unique flavours. Standout dishes include the cod “punheta” with crunchy rice, followed by a vegetarian option (tofu and mushrooms with a mouthwatering demi-glace) and an impressive fresh cod prepared with a smooth chickpea purée. To finish, we highly recommend the spectacular “pão de ló” sponge cake fresh out of the oven, served with goat’s cheese ice-cream. The reasonable prices here are another pleasant surprise!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6588;Flora;Portugal;Viseu;Grão Vasco 21, Viseu, 3500-138, Portugal;40.6595756;-7.9121616;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Dishes such as spicy polenta with fennel pickle, confit cod, white trevally fish from the Azores and, to finish, the banana treacle ice cream with liquorice-flavoured rice pudding, are accompanied by a choice of "low intervention, biodynamic and organic wines" that are high on quality. This oasis of creativity can be found in a tiny contemporary bistro in Viseu’s historic centre, where it is run by João Guedes in the kitchen and Anna front of house.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6589;PODA;Portugal;Montemor-o-Novo;Rua Sacadura Cabral 25, Montemor-o-Novo, 7050 304, Portugal;38.6494423;-8.2150977;49;true;true;Regional Cuisine;PODA occupies an old agricultural warehouse that has been completely remodelled and decorated in rustic style with a plethora of wood. Chef João Narigueta and his long-term friend Miguel Dominguinhos have joined together to open this dining space in which the traditional cooking of the Alentejo has undergone a renaissance. One of the classic dishes on the menu is the typical “migas gatas” with cod, which is simply presented but with surprising flavour. Another typical regional dish is “enxovalhada”, a sponge cake filled with walnuts and honey and sprinkled with cinnamon. The wine list mainly features local producers.;Air conditioning;[]
6590;Rio by Paulo André;Portugal;Vila do Conde;Praça da República 8, Vila do Conde, 4480-715, Portugal;41.3513451;-8.7415259;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A young and informal eatery with an open-view kitchen located at one end of Praça da República, one of Vila do Conde’s most beautiful squares thanks to its setting on the banks of the Ave river. In a nod to the name of his restaurant, chef Paulo André’s professional career is as surprising and unexpected as the meanders in a river! His cisHisontemporary-style cooking will definitely leave its mark given his passion, technical skill and a strong desire to please, plus a continual focus on using locally sourced vegetables (vegetarian dishes feature on the menu), fish and meat. If the weather’s fine, make sure you eat on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6591;Kok Sur Mer;Belgium;Vlissegem;Warvinge 49, Vlissegem, 8421, Belgium;51.2562422;3.0559647;96;false;false;Modern French;Jean-Philippe Furnémont’s traditional know-how is in the masterclass category, illustrated by melt-in-the-mouth pork cheeks in a subtly sweet sauce, by the tangy lemon that jazzes up crispy asparagus mimosa or by the big-boned beurre noisette that flanks flawlessly cooked North Sea sole. The chef signs a genuine love letter to discerning foodies in his handsome villa-cum-cottage as he forges his own culinary path. The set menu with a choice of dishes is ideal to sample the chef’s audacious hallmark cuisine, all at eater-friendly prices.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6592;Père et Mère;Belgium;Diksmuide;Grote Markt 43, Diksmuide, 8600, Belgium;51.0335097;2.8657983;37;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This family bistro overflows in good humour, as Jelle in the kitchen and Magali in the dining room are still regularly helped out by the restaurant’s founders, Frans and Ria, further upholding their eatery’s legacy. The menu pays a genuine tribute to family cooking, to the delight of foodies everywhere. Cognac and tomato delicately underscore North Sea fish soup, while beer highlights the intensity of rabbit in prunes: the classics have no secrets for the chef, who is determined to keep the prices sensible. Hearty, wholesome, country cooking at its best depicts this mum and dad!;Air conditioning;[]
6593;Le Cabochon;Belgium;Liège;Boulevard Emile de Laveleye 191, Liège, 4020, Belgium;50.619611;5.5916299;16;true;false;Modern French, Cuisine from the Marches;Le Cabochon is always a safe bet for a slap-up lunch in downtown Liège. The concise selection of dishes on the set menu is flanked by daily suggestions that vary according to the seasons and market availability. Traditional textbook technique (such as mouth-wateringly tender beef cheeks and subtle homemade sauces) is married with side dishes oozing with an abundance of diverse influences. Food that hits the spot every time, to the delight of its many regulars.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6594;Le Variétés;Belgium;Ixelles;Place Sainte-Croix 4, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8265632;4.373001;15;false;true;Belgian;Le Variétés is steeped in the Art deco elegance of the Flagey “ocean liner” edifice, an iconic work by architect Joseph Diongre. Exotic wood dominates the sleek brasserie interior, while the terrace plunges you into the buzzy vibe of this lively district. Roast chicken is the house specialty, but the menu boasts a host of other dishes, including a patriotic line-up of Belgian family favourites: tomatoes stuffed with shrimp and vol-au-vent. All the food is down-to-earth, generous and steeped in flavour.;Terrace;[]
6595;Jeux de Goûts;Belgium;Orchimont;Rue de Bohan 91, Orchimont, 5550, Belgium;49.8923622;4.8871946;23;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking;A warm, cosy restaurant flanked by comfortable guestrooms deep in the Luxembourg Ardennes. The scene is set for you to be pampered by Fanny and Jérôme. He adds a modern twist to recipes, rich in bona fide Gallic overtones. Organic, local and traditional ingredients take pride of place on the menu. Refreshing food that pays tribute to the region’s heritage and generosity.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6596;Monsieur V;Belgium;Linkebeek;Dapperensquare 19, Linkebeek, 1630, Belgium;50.7741227;4.3351837;51;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Jan Verhaert cooks what he himself likes to eat: traditional Gallic dishes with the occasional nod to Italy. His cosy neighbourhood restaurant specialises in bistro classics such as pâté en croûte and risotto with seasonal vegetables, and crispy millefeuille with vanilla-rich crème pâtissière for dessert. The flawless precision of the cooking and the chef's penchant for gutsy flavours are truly noteworthy. A champion of French culinary tradition, Monsieur Verhaert delivers exceptional food at a price that won't break the bank.;Terrace;[]
6597;Station 3;Belgium;Kraainem;Statieplaats 3, Kraainem, 1950, Belgium;50.8663153;4.4526105;75;true;true;Chinese;Station 3 is a no-frills restaurant serving up popular specialties from the diverse Chinese culinary landscape. Rich sauces, exotic seasonings, and occasional bursts of sweet and sour are combined with a sure hand. The sea bass steamed whole and paired with an exquisite sauce based on rice vinegar and soy sauce is a must-try for any seafood lover. With so many lobster dishes and vegetarian options to choose from, you're sure to find something to your taste. The har gow – steamed dim sum – are made fresh using traditional methods and delicately seasoned with ginger. A golden opportunity to discover Chinese generosity in all its glory!;;[]
6598;La Charcuterie;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;avenue Paul Dejaer 16, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8262;4.3450017;36;true;false;Sharing, Country cooking;The vintage charm of this former butcher's with its olde worlde tiles and wood panelling is eminently friendly. Walk past the delicatessen-cum-grocery store counter into the teeny bistro. Premium produce, wholesome, unpretentious cooking and mind-blowing flavours. Dishes to share, washed down with a glass of fine wine.;Terrace;[]
6599;Garde Manger;Belgium;Gesves;Chaussée de Gramptinne 37, Gesves, 5340, Belgium;50.4438539;5.0127403;65;false;false;Farm to table;Picture a traditional Ardennes edifice in the Samson Valley whose interior is cosily pleasant and homely… Garde Manger (“larder” in English) inevitably brings a smile to our lips, which is largely thanks to the inspired recipes of Christophe Durand. He subtly reinterprets the authentic flavours of foie gras and juicy cuts of beef, pairing them with deftly crafted side dishes such as seaweed or an espuma of Belgian Herve cheese that add a fascinating kick to the main ingredient. All that remains is to try and solve the dilemma of choosing between the enticing à la carte and set menus…;Terrace;[]
6600;La Marelle Café;Belgium;Blaregnies;Rue des Trieux 36, Blaregnies, 7040, Belgium;50.3599518;3.891834;49;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;Over 500 beers, an enticing menu and bargain prices: fans of traditional fare will love this bustling bolthole. Rather than fussy frills, you can expect unpretentious, authentic grub: homemade terrine, croquettes of calf’s tongue, Belgium’s version of steak tartare and chips (with mayonnaise and horse meat)… La Marelle Café is a goldmine of nostalgic recipes and flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6601;Au gré des Saisons;Belgium;Achet;rue d'Achet 70, Achet, 5362, Belgium;50.3328659;5.1746766;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian;Welcome to the achingly scenic village of Achet in Condroz, the location of an excellent eatery, clad in characteristic Ardennes stone. Gregorio Clavello adds a subtle twist to his Italian roots, rustling up flavoursome modern dishes. Mediterranean tangs and a few judicious oriental notes perfume the food that respects seasonal availability. Balanced, authentic, delicious!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6602;Moonstone;Belgium;Genk;Wiemesmeerstraat 105, Genk, 3600, Belgium;50.98392;5.547772;35;true;false;Modern French;An illuminated moon sculpture dominates the grey colour scheme, hence the name. The setting is further enhanced by the view over the golf course. Chef Roos masterfully celebrates premium produce such as lamb and pheasant, which he crafts into dishes that hit the spot every time, exalting familiar flavours that are also pure, rich and expressive. Don’t miss the extensive market menu!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6603;Car Bon;Belgium;Ixelles;chaussée de Waterloo 552, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8192817;4.3617161;55;false;false;Chinese, Sichuan;Don’t be fooled by the cliché of a tightly packed neighbourhood eatery with an extensive menu and mainly Asian clientele, because Car Bon has plenty of other succulent appeals up its sleeve. The food is authentic, with a focus on the Sichuan region. Wonton pork and veal with a chili oil that adds a subtle spicy note. Gutsy, light and assertive all at once, Chinese cuisine that hits the spot every time. Don’t forget to book!;;[]
6604;Chez Chen Wépion;Belgium;Wépion;chaussée de Dinant 873, Wépion, 5100, Belgium;50.4257564;4.8705114;17;false;false;Chinese;Chinese restaurant on the banks of the Meuse. Exterior made from local stone, bright dining room with just a hint of an Asian feel to it, view of the river thanks to the large bay windows.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6606;Kline;Belgium;Brussels;Rue de Flandre 162, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8529685;4.3435641;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The brutalist concrete interior of the hip Kline restaurant is perfectly matched to the casual dining vibe. Unusual, unpretentious recipes and a few vegetarian options. Plancha-seared gherkin is paired with cream of smoked yoghurt, mustard seeds, dill, chunks of goat’s cheese and curry oil. “Locally sourced and globally inspired” (their own words) is the ethos of this zero-waste, sustainable establishment firmly in the zeitgeist.;Terrace;[]
6607;Plat préféré;Belgium;Snaaskerke;Dorpsstraat 71, Snaaskerke, 8470, Belgium;51.1754294;2.9391928;89;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Are you a fan of fine Flemish fare and time-honoured bistro classics? If so, you can probably bet that your favourite dish will be on the menu here. Chef Gouwy bends over backwards to satisfy his guests and his disarmingly simple, wholesome menu is a treat for foodies: fresh fish served with risotto and beurre blanc – what could be better? The elegant, gilded bicycle that stands next to the kitchen, the chef’s own handiwork, will convince you of his deft craftsmanship.;Air conditioning;[]
6608;Olijfboom;Belgium;Veurne;Noordstraat 3, Veurne, 8630, Belgium;51.0727383;2.6625424;33;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Highly polished silverware, a fantastic collection of bottles and knickknacks set the quirky, antique dealer interior of Olijfboom, so you won’t be surprised to learn that the chef is a keen collector of vintage chinaware. However, his main talent is regaling us with old-school cooking. In keeping with tradition, he unfussily enhances the ingredient which he serves generously, focusing on the flavour. An impressive wine list completes this fine dining experience.;Interesting wine list;[]
6609;Mona Lisa;Belgium;Yvoir;Rue du Colonel Tachet des Combes 19, Yvoir, 5530, Belgium;50.3271487;4.8783814;96;true;false;Italian;A Grimaldi pizza oven immediately catches the eye as you enter this modern eatery, but, make no mistake, you are light years from your run-of-the-mill pizzeria. The Mona Lisa is helmed by a couple of Sicilian parentage, who are proud of their first-rate produce and of lovingly crafting old-fashioned Italian recipes. The gutsy flavours of the ravioli explode in the mouth, underscored by a creamy burrata, while the signature chocolate dessert is deliciously balanced. We highly recommend the set menu with options.;Terrace;[]
6610;Bar Bask;Belgium;Gent;Edward Pynaertkaai 115, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0417364;3.7403538;80;false;false;Spanish Contemporary;Gent now has a trendy tapas bar in the shape of Bar Bask. After perusing the long refrigerated counter piled high with seafood treats, you will make your way to the heat of the open fire to choose one of the many dishes to share of Basque inspiration: pinchos, spit roast turbot or a juicy slice of chistorra… A festival from the Basque country! Exciting flavours and subtle sauces, all of which at eater-friendly prices.;Counter dining;[]
6611;Parc Le'h;Luxembourg;Dudelange;1 rue de la Forêt, Dudelange, 3471, Luxembourg;49.485788;6.0990145;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This trendy brasserie, done up in wood and other natural materials, is in perfect osmosis with the surrounding Dudelange forest. It is run by a veteran who takes the time to listen to his guests. Jean-Charles Albert’s pared-back cuisine is subtle, often surprising but never disconcerting. He may marry creamy risotto, truffles and a skate wing fritter or jazz up steak tartare with Thai or oriental notes, all the while respecting their intrinsic flavours. Something of a culinary landmark in the region.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6612;l'Epicurien;Belgium;Herve;rue des Martyrs 15, Herve, 4650, Belgium;50.6416609;5.7902249;36;true;false;French;Sébastien Brela is a true food lover. His passion for fine ingredients is obvious as soon as you peruse the menu. Distinctive flavours play a central role, while generous sauces add a punchy twist. Unexpected associations and textures create a genuine surprise. The fixed-price menus demonstrate that it is possible to be a gourmet food lover without breaking the bank!;Air conditioning;[]
6613;Masu;Belgium;Mons;rue d'Havré 79, Mons, 7000, Belgium;50.4538652;3.9558958;38;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, World Cuisine;Masu is a bubbly eatery, just like Maxime and Sullivan, the colourful fresco and the cool vibes of the DJ’s soundtrack: youthful, funky and laidback! Every month, the duo of creative craftsmen concocts a new menu that keeps pace with the seasons, often drawing on their binchotan barbecue to add whoomph to inspired recipes. Examples include grilled corn on the cob with a spicy sauce and sweet-sour rings of shallots (the epitome of finger food, of course). It’s party time every day at Masu.;;[]
6614;Maïnoï;Belgium;Braine-l'Alleud;Chaussée Reine Astrid 34, Braine-l'Alleud, 1420, Belgium;50.6857555;4.3796105;17;true;false;Thai;Whilst refreshingly modern, Maïnoï nonetheless remains true to its traditional roots and the characteristic Thai interior creates a warm, welcoming vibe. The seasoned chef deftly crafts exuberant familiar flavours and cannot be rivalled for his way with sauces, jazzing up beef and vegetable side dishes, for example, with flair and talent. The creative menu is bold and daring and pleasant surprises await the diner. We recommend sampling the house signature dishes, marked up on the board.;Terrace;[]
6615;Bazaar;;Luxembourg;46 Place Guillaume II, 1648, Luxembourg;49.6101074;6.1324737;44;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sharing;A hint of Beirut, a whiff of Athens, together with a gust of Tel Aviv and Marrakech: this bustling restaurant brings together the best of the Mediterranean. Kick off your meal with a fresh cocktail and houmous or a mezze, before sharing a roast chicken. Spices and fruity flavours subtly underscore each dish. We must admit to having fallen head over heels with the grilled aubergine in tahini, candied garlic and peaches – to die for!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6616;Nr.12 by Helsen;Belgium;Herentals;Grote Markt 12, Herentals, 2200, Belgium;51.1765588;4.8363938;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You don't even need to step inside to realise that Nr.12 is the hippest restaurant on Grote Markt. It also serves the most delicious food! Veteran chef Frédéric Helsen is a dab hand at rustling up dishes to share (of which we wager you will order too many, so vast is the choice!). He puts his own playful yet fuss-free spin on classic recipes to delight our taste buds. Think succulent boudin blanc with a subtle madeira sauce, or pan-fried plaice with crab and a rich beurre blanc: the menu is sure to make any foodie's heart race. Craving more? Chef Helsen's vending machine (Meidoornlaan 1, Herentals) is open seven days a week.;Terrace;[]
6617;L'Incontournable;Belgium;Rochefort;avenue du Rond-Point 3a, Rochefort, 5580, Belgium;50.1530993;5.2196006;94;true;false;French Contemporary;What does it take to create a Bib Gourmand restaurant? Fresh ingredients, sourced locally if possible (here, they are listed on the menu). Consummate technique. This could be the ability to whip up a classic pepper sauce to accompany a fillet of venison, or slightly more playful ideas such as Jerusalem artichoke and chorizo croquettes combined with scallops and a butter sauce with orange. Of course, value for money is also key. And that is precisely why this warm and welcoming restaurant, with father Stéphane in the kitchen and son Loïk front-of-house, is such an exemplary Bib.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6618;Nénu;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;Rue Dejoncker 21, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8342675;4.3547766;90;true;false;Vietnamese Contemporary;It is neither its sober contemporary décor nor its casual vibe that set Nénu apart from the many restaurants in the Avenue Louise neighbourhood, but its anh nhau concept. This Vietnamese tradition consists in sharing small and large dishes and a fine bottle of wine with friends and family. The kitchen team adds a modern twist to traditional flavours, creating a mouth-watering menu (choose at least three dishes). Spicy wontons, vegetarian red curry, grilled salmon head with sweet-sour flavours and traditional spices…Superlative Vietnamese fusion cooking…;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6619;Le Faitout;Belgium;Baudour;place de la Résistance 1, Baudour, 7331, Belgium;50.4832736;3.837656;25;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, French;Pull up a chair on the delightful terrace and enjoy the lively and infectious ambience of the Faitout. The menu features traditional recipes: Ardennes pork, grilled meats, country terrines and seafood platters… Authenticity and generosity above all else! Take your pick from the varied choice on the menu (with a range of prices), you won’t be disappointed. Open 7 days a week!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6620;Trattoria Bazalia;Belgium;Bazel;Koningin Astridplein 11, Bazel, 9150, Belgium;51.1472461;4.3002965;81;false;true;Italian;This offshoot of the Michelin star Italian restaurant, Hofke van Bazel, is just upstairs from its elder sibling. The trattoria’s romantic interior is perfect for a date night, possibly alfresco on the patio overlooking the picturesque church of St Peter’s. Ingredients from Puglia take the limelight, but the chef also celebrates other regions of Italy with a distinct fondness for authentic Mediterranean flavours. The chef might pair crispy cod with slow-baked sliced potatoes and onions and a creamy sauce of mussels, tomatoes and shellfish. Purebred Italian classics also feature prominently, such as vitello tonnato and ossobuco. Extensive menu (including a vegetarian lineup).;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6621;Den Duyventooren;Belgium;Bellem;Bellemdorpweg 68, Bellem, 9881, Belgium;51.0915708;3.4886779;41;true;false;Modern French;The spruce, traditional façade of this ancestral castle-farmstead hides a vibrant modern interior adorned in warm colours. The peaceful terrace feels light years away from Bellem. The establishment has acquired a faithful cohort of regulars, lured back by Inge Herteleer’s enticing set and à la carte menus. Her seasonal cooking throbs with generosity and is dotted with contemporary touches to which she adds a Mediterranean twist come summertime. The shrimp fritters are stuffed to the brim, while a suave cognac sauce enhances pheasant and green peas and mint contrast with fresh prawns. Searingly good food prepared on the spot! Don’t forget to book!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6622;Au Tour du Vin;Belgium;Éghezée;route d'Andenne 10, Éghezée, 5310, Belgium;50.5913203;4.9135304;52;false;false;Modern French;While wine may not be the only ingredient on the menu, it is clearly a prominent feature of this cheerful bustling bistro. The expert sommelier’s wine selection (excellent tips) is perfectly paired with the creative bistro fare. The chef is a dab hand at reinventing Gallic classics, without forgetting his surprising ‘light’ version of pizza. Bold, spot-on cooking every time. We also recommend the next-door ice cream parlour.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6623;Le Charme de la Semois;Belgium;Alle;rue de Liboichant 12, Alle, 5550, Belgium;49.8468266;4.9694099;26;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The picturesque Semois river and valley set the scene for this delightful riverside Ardennes country inn. The interior is amusingly adorned with a collection of hens, bringing the promise of bygone flavours on the menu. Fiercely traditional, the food is simple and generous and will delight lovers of authentic fare.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6624;Robertissimo;Belgium;Embourg;voie de l'Ardenne 58b, Embourg, 4053, Belgium;50.5935078;5.6063558;44;true;false;Italian;Be forewarned – once you have experienced the joyful vibe and flair of this lively establishment, you will be yearning to return again and again! The big-hearted chef skilfully and generously rustles up genuine Italian fare: immaculately cooked calf’s liver in a gutsy jus served with al dente pasta in butter. Bravissimo for this autentico banquet of Italian delicacies designed to appeal to discerning foodies!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6625;La Branche d'Olivier;Belgium;Uccle;rue Engeland 172, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7878432;4.3396476;18;false;false;Classic Cuisine;With its old tiled floor and leather seats, patinated woodwork, plus the peaceful terrace overlooking Kinsendaal Nature Reserve, this charming bistro is full of character. The many regulars come here to feast on classics such as foie gras maison, cod fillet in a chorizo crust with a saffron white wine sauce, and chocolate mousse for dessert. It is not without good reason that chef Demurger is hailed as a great sauce maker and rôtisseur. This Bib Gourmand restaurant is all about craftsmanship and generosity.;Terrace;[]
6626;Des Ardennes;Belgium;Corbion;rue de la Hate 1, Corbion, 6838, Belgium;49.7966152;5.0096033;43;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;The Maqua family’s charming hotel has been welcoming guests in the Ardennes since 1900 and several generations continue to work in the family establishment. The peaceful rooms overlook the rolling countryside, while in the restaurant, the accent is on satisfying French favourites, albeit in keeping with today’s tastebuds. The cooking is spot on and flavoursome. Splendid wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6627;Le Bistrot d'en Face;Belgium;Liège;rue de la Goffe 8, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.645336;5.5779576;60;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;A nostalgic friendly vibe and good food are the backbone of this inviting local version of a “bouchon lyonnais”. The traditional, extensive menu takes you back in time with dishes such as confit of duck and salardaise potatoes or boulets à la liégoise (meatballs) – among the best in town! Heartwarming, no-nonsense food, served generously and prepared with respect for time-honoured recipes. Spot on every time.;Terrace;[]
6628;Au Cœur de Lacuisine;Belgium;Lacuisine;rue du Fond des Naux 7, Lacuisine, 6821, Belgium;49.7181463;5.3182193;42;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The sleepy village of Lacuisine makes the perfect base camp to explore the Ardennes. Don’t miss Ronny and Christel’s stylish establishment which combines a friendly vibe with modern comforts. The chef cooks regional produce, most of which from scratch, with lashings of generosity. For example, you may taste a terrine of foie gras with smoked duck magret or a fillet of plaice with a pastis-flavoured jus. The enticing range of set menus means that there is something to suit every palate. Even better, stay overnight and jump into the pool before or after breakfast next morning.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6629;Enoteca;Belgium;Liège;rue de la Casquette 5, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.6427414;5.569623;39;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;You will immediately feel at home at the Enoteca, which is depicted by tightly packed tables, a friendly vibe and cheerful service. Food lovers have been flocking here for over thirty years, lured by the unbeatable value for money and the text-book perfect Italian nosh. Farfalle al dente with fresh shrimp, preserved lemons and a knockout tomato sauce – authenticity is the goal! Order the chef’s daily special with your eyes closed and don’t forget the enticing wine list.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6630;Le Moulin;Belgium;Daverdisse;rue de la Lesse 61, Daverdisse, 6929, Belgium;50.0275637;5.1158029;71;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This former watermill is a charming place to experience the beauty of the Ardennes, starting with the view of the babbling river and the typical façade. Inside, cosiness is the order of the day. This is a family-run business, with a mother-and-son team providing friendly service front-of-house. In the kitchen, chef Ludovic puts a subtle modern spin on his father Jean-Pierre's classic cuisine – savour a rich game consommé with venison shank, or scallop ceviche. Foodies will be delighted by the extensive à la carte selection and set menus. Quiet guestrooms available for a pleasant overnight stay.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
6631;Durbuy Ô;Belgium;Durbuy;Warre 26, Durbuy, 6941, Belgium;50.3651363;5.4654266;59;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;This friendly restaurant (which also offers accommodation) is idyllically located to explore the picturesque small town of Durbuy. You will feel right at home here thanks to the family-run vibe and attentive care lavished by chef Timmerman on his guests. The pedigree French repertory is enhanced by local produce, such as scallops and venison. The chef treats all his ingredients with the utmost respect, further enhancing the experience with fascinating sauces and side dishes.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6632;Le Confessionnal;Belgium;Dinant;rue Rémy Himmer 4, Dinant, 5500, Belgium;50.26937;4.907275;93;false;false;French;Opposite Leffe Abbey, this nostalgic neighbourhood bolthole provides a showcase for the owner’s passion for flea markets. Red and white checked tablecloths, decorative soup tureens and silverware set the friendly scene. The traditional fare oozes with the charm of yesteryear and the regularly changing menu offers an array of hearty, traditional dishes, such as duck leg à la bourguignonne or roast shoulder of lamb with garlic confit. Hunger obliterating food free of fussy frills and a treasure trove of French wines at prices that make sense.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6633;Osteria Bolognese;Belgium;Ixelles;rue de la Paix 49, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8363612;4.3660771;36;false;true;Italian;Giacomo’s mission is to redress the hackneyed image of ‘spag bol’ and his mouth-watering tagliatelle con ragù alla bolognese does just that! All his ingredients are sourced direct from Emilia Romagna, ensuring an explosion of flavour in the mouth. Our inspectors were treated to taglioni with flash fried bresaola, a syrupy balsamic vinegar packed in bitter-sweet flavours and spicy rucola. A buzzy, vibrant vibe depicts this delightful osteria that will introduce you to the authentic cuisine of Bologna.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6634;Cadre Culinaire;Belgium;Huy;rue des Rôtisseurs 4, Huy, 4500, Belgium;50.5189769;5.2405126;81;false;true;Modern French;In addition to hailing from Alsace, Grégory Baruthio avows a passion for pastries, as you will soon realise, and his Gugelhupf is truly second to none! Ever enthusiastic, the chef dons his apron to enhance ingredients that suit the modern palate without losing sight of high-precision cooking and traditional generosity. A welcoming establishment with eater friendly prices.;Terrace;[]
6635;L'Espièglerie;Belgium;Namur;rue des Tanneries 13, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.4642792;4.8715038;46;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Since 1988, gourmets have been making a beeline for this romantic hideaway, whose old vaults and bare brick walls lend it masses of cachet and bags of elegance. Choose from the daily special or the menu to sample rich authentic food that has earned this eatery its fine reputation. How about a creative spin on a maki with gambas and smoked eel or cod in lemon breadcrumbs jazzed up with seaweed flavoured cabbage stock? The chef knows how to grab our attention and pamper our taste buds. Gloriously sensibly priced and a splendid selection of beers and Bordeaux wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6636;Le Tournant;Belgium;Ixelles;chaussée de Wavre 168, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8356505;4.3694573;28;false;false;Home Cooking;The lively, vibrant Matongé district is home to an equally buzzy neighbourhood eatery: Le Tournant. People drop in to sample a glass of “natural” wine (trust the sommelier – he knows his job!) and dig into unfussy, nostalgic dishes reminiscent of grandma’s cooking, together with a few more modern bistro recipes. Examples include gutsy beef cheeks braised in Orval beer or lamb in dried figs. Every dish is an authentic festival of flavour!;Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
6637;Le Saint Boniface;Belgium;Ixelles;rue Saint-Boniface 9, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8359208;4.3647629;19;false;false;Cuisine from South West France, Country cooking;Picture tightly packed tables, red and white chequered tablecloths, a collection of biscuit tins and French songs and jazz playing in the background: the scene is set in this friendly welcoming bistro. The locals flock here to sample its specialities from the Basque Country, Lyon and Southwest France. Calf’s brain and tartare sauce, confit of duck leg, veal sweetbread and kidneys rich in regional flavours. Heart-warming authentic nosh steeped in traditional Gallic generosity!;Terrace;[]
6638;Les Potes en Toque;Belgium;Ganshoren;drève du Château 71, Ganshoren, 1083, Belgium;50.8763566;4.3146424;71;false;true;Classic Cuisine, French Contemporary;This renovated farm cottage in the heart of a residential neighbourhood is depicted by a characteristic Belgian blend of rural chic. The menu majors in flawlessly prepared brasserie favourites, served generously.;Terrace;[]
6639;Cul de Poule;Belgium;Binche;avenue Wanderpepen 44, Binche, 7130, Belgium;50.4120446;4.1696559;62;true;true;Modern French;A colourful, cartoon-inspired chicken adorns this small bistro, but the real draw is Arnaud Molle. This seasoned chef lets his creativity run riot in regularly changing menus with a Gallic slant. His food is flavoursome, original and ideally suited to make the most of fresh produce. His flawlessly cooked pheasant served with a creamy Fine Champagne cognac sauce is to die for! The meat, from his parent’s butchery, is first class and the prices are truly eater friendly – what more can we say?;Terrace;[]
6640;De Vous à Nous;Belgium;Montigny-le-Tilleul;rue de Grand Bry 42, Montigny-le-Tilleul, 6110, Belgium;50.3644641;4.3641344;15;true;false;Modern French;De Vous à Nous (From You to Us) sports a stylish interior, a peaceful, lush green landscape and eater-friendly prices. The know-how and generosity of chef François Duvivier are outstanding and he doesn’t hesitate to add a personal flourish to traditional recipes, such as croquettes of pheasant, pigeon with a gutsy sauce or Belle Hélène pear jus that will knock your socks off! A safe bet every time!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6641;Au Petit Château;Belgium;Mouscron;boulevard des Alliés 243, Mouscron, 7700, Belgium;50.740121;3.2591907;57;true;true;Classic French;This endearing villa has, quite rightly, been a firm culinary fixture of Mouscron for eons and its infectiously friendly vibe is nurtured by the cheerful lady of the house. The traditional menu, which features the occasional modern tribute, always hits the spot. Carpaccio of sea bream, frog’s legs, Rossini tournedos… 100% French recipes that pay tribute to the finest traditions of culinary know-how and generosity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6642;Villa Singha;Belgium;Auderghem;rue des Trois Ponts 22, Auderghem, 1160, Belgium;50.8205968;4.4075821;67;false;false;Thai, Asian;Villa Singha has been upholding and celebrating Thai traditions for over thirty years. A characteristic Thai decor and references to the mythological lion, Singha, set the exotic scene, further enhanced by an extensive succulent menu. Crispy Popiah fried spring rolls, Thai dumplings stuffed with ground pork or fried cod in a ginger chili sauce are a few of the generously crafted and spicy, yet balanced dishes. A word of advice – don’t forget to book, although, if the worse comes to the worst, you can always order a take-away!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6643;Maza'j;Belgium;Auderghem;boulevard du Souverain 145, Auderghem, 1160, Belgium;50.8156704;4.426231;35;true;true;Lebanese, Middle Eastern;Maza'j serves dishes bursting with bold colours and exciting flavours. The tables here are decked with authentic Lebanese specialities that delight diners with their distinctive spiciness and generosity. Velvety hummus with pine nuts, barbecued minced lamb with a delicately sweet bell pepper confit, an array of vegetables elevated by a blend of aromatic herbs… You and your dining companions can look forward to sharing a real feast in a convivial atmosphere. Experience the richness of Lebanese culinary tradition!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6644;Le Grand Maur;Belgium;Spa;rue de Barisart 209, Spa, 4900, Belgium;50.485483;5.8600872;30;false;true;Modern French;An air of romantic nostalgia reigns throughout this charming small Ardennes castle. Ideally located for a spot of sight-seeing in Spa, the castle also serves a bang-up meal. The attractive range of dishes demonstrates the chef’s passion for first-class produce, which he prepares generously, flanked by polished side dishes and subtle sauces.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6645;Vilain;Belgium;Charleroi;Avenue Paul Pastur 365, Charleroi, 6032, Belgium;50.3980995;4.4225739;78;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Vilain offers a choice of 10 to 15 dishes to share, which often change weekly in line with the seasons and the suppliers and sports an irresistible vintage vibe, overflowing in good cheer and boasting a lovely garden for alfresco dining. The occasional international twist jazzes up the traditional pageant: butternut ravioles with ricotta, jus of bacon and walnuts. Sharing such delicacies can pose quite a dilemma!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6646;Onslow;Belgium;Brugge;Jeruzalemstraat 53, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2123639;3.2331473;58;false;true;Farm to table;Onslow, a buzzy landmark in the peaceful Sint Anna district, offers casual dining and a terrace bathed in Mediterranean charm. Its international menu with a host of tasty dishes to share is extremely popular with the locals. Lieven Vynck whisks us off to Nice with a pissaladière that is a perfect balance between caramelised onions, anchovies, olives, thyme and lemon peel, unless you would rather sample the fresh, spicy, acidic tang of a mouthwatering ceviche. A feast of flavour awaits you at Onslow: “Food with Drinks, Drinks with Food” is their baseline!;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6647;Au Phil des Saveurs;Belgium;Bois-de-Villers;Rue Émile Mazy 20, Bois-de-Villers, 5170, Belgium;50.3920316;4.8096479;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A quick look at the pool and garden overlooking the countryside confirms the holiday vibe as soon as you set foot inside Phil Garcia’s HQ. The food features an intelligent blend of classical cooking techniques with Mediterranean influences. He offers a new spin on vitello tonnato with cod cooked on the skin, flanked by a velvety mousseline of mashed potato and leek oil. Enticing set menus and the cheerful relaxed service of the lady of the house add the final flourish to this fine dining portrait.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6648;Les 4 Saisons;Belgium;Marche-en-Famenne;Rue de Bastogne 108, Marche-en-Famenne, 6900, Belgium;50.2111394;5.3665525;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The charm of this Ardennes house is encapsulated by the landscaped garden, providing the perfect foil to the warm, inviting interior. Ingredients take the star role in gutsy nostalgic recipes, albeit with a scattering of refreshing creative twists. For example, the chef’s perfectly cooked veal in truffles with Asian flavours. The menu with options is a model of full-bodied generosity. Deliciously eater friendly prices!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6649;il était une fois toi et moi;Belgium;Arquennes;Chaussée de Nivelles 13, Arquennes, 7181, Belgium;50.5569401;4.275554;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic French;Looking for the perfect romantic spot? Look no further: this restaurant ticks all the boxes, starting with the name! A smart lounge interior serves as the backdrop to an exciting culinary story. The extensive menu, which offers made-to-measure options, combines traditional Gallic recipes and more contemporary offerings. The food is both inspired and suave, whilst remaining reassuringly familiar.;Terrace;[]
6650;Ferment;Belgium;Sint-Kwintens-Lennik;Alfred Algoetstraat 1, Sint-Kwintens-Lennik, 1750, Belgium;50.8057181;4.1557195;43;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Sharing;A drop-dead wine list, a knock-out collection of authentic local beers and updated family favourites to share: this bustling restaurant on Lennik market square attracts foodies like bees to honey! They swarm here for shrimp fritters, melt-in-the-mouth asparagus (served with melted butter, finely chopped hard-boiled eggs and parsley), grilled sea bass and a host of other delectable morsels. Generous home-made cooking that shines the spotlight on local produce and know-how.;Air conditioning;[]
6651;L'épicerie Nomad;Belgium;Ixelles;Rue Keyenveld 56, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8345001;4.3615503;68;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Cosmopolitan par excellence, Brussels’ international character is emblematic of this bustling eatery which features tightly packed tables and a slate menu that makes no distinction between starters and main courses. How about a fresh, bitter ceviche of seabass with mango and passion fruit, a Spanish zarzuela of seafood, or shakshuka - a vegetarian one-pan savoury dish? The chef’s creativity, which knows no bounds, is further enhanced by his superlative knack for marrying flavours. Pair this culinary journey with one of the carefully curated tipples to make the most of this fascinating experience.;;[]
6652;Le Sixième;Belgium;Jodoigne;Avenue Fernand Charlot 2, Jodoigne, 1370, Belgium;50.7233367;4.8712735;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There is something for everyone in this modern bistro. Chef Clément draws his inspiration from top-notch ingredients, to which he adds a subtle personal spin. Asian influences, the authentic flavour of marinated beetroot, a velvety beurre blanc and the subtle smoky hints of the wood-fired Josper oven… Splendid harmonies and great value for money. A word of advice: if you would prefer a more romantic vibe, ask for a table in the second room.;;[]
6653;Magnific;Belgium;Lanaken;Tournebride 35, Lanaken, 3620, Belgium;50.9013936;5.6776169;77;true;false;Modern French, Mediterranean Cuisine;Lounge music in the background, trendy urban wall graffiti and the warm hospitality of Limburg: a meal at Magnific is always a treat. All the more so, as the chef cleverly juggles with French and Italian recipes, throwing in the odd Asian theme. Whether you start with cannelloni or continue with a venison steak and a cranberry sauce, you can rely on the stellar craftsmanship and full-bodied flavours to come up trumps every time! The set menu with choices is highly recommended.;Car park;[]
6654;Bienvenue;Belgium;Maaseik;Markt 20, Maaseik, 3680, Belgium;51.0942167;5.791728;70;false;false;Modern Cuisine;John van Leerzem is a fan of tradition and of the ingredient before all else. This institution on the main square of Maaseik does far more than showcase time-honoured classics. The chef happily subverts traditional recipes, particularly thanks to carefully devised side dishes, such as a terrine of veal cheek and tongue that he subtly contrasts with sweet-sour chutney. His stamp can also be tasted in the tournedos and stroganoff sauce that strikes a perfect balance of flavours. A feast for foodies!;Terrace;[]
6655;Au Dos de la Cuillère;Belgium;Verviers;rue Jules Cérexhe 10, Verviers, 4800, Belgium;50.5937791;5.8508777;88;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking;The establishment has been treated to a (forced) makeover after the flooding of 2021 but has lost none of its charm. The chef specialises in Gallic cuisine with a fondness for local ingredients, such as Herve cheese and pork from the Tabreux farm. Everything is generous and homemade, even the praline of the decadent Paris-Brest pastry. Don’t forget to book!;Terrace;[]
6656;La Table du Boucher;Belgium;Mons;rue d'Havré 49, Mons, 7000, Belgium;50.4537797;3.9544531;59;false;true;Meats and Grills, Classic French;Luc Broutard avows a passion for top quality produce, red meat in particular, as you will immediately realise when you cross the threshold of this buzzy brasserie. Seared foie gras, tartare of Salers beef, marinated pork cheeks or grilled tenderloin: carnivores will be in seventh heaven as they drool over the extensive menu. Rich, spot-on cooking, happily free of gimmicks and there are even a few fish dishes. Everyone feels at home at the Table du Boucher, to such an extent that many return in their droves.;Air conditioning;[]
6657;Comptoir de l'Eau Vive;Belgium;Erpent;place des Jardins de Baseilles 14, Erpent, 5101, Belgium;50.4412368;4.9046574;42;true;false;Belgian;Trendy and buzzy, this small eatery is the epitome of a Bib Gourmand. Whether you go for one of the classics on the à la carte menu (like meatballs in tomato sauce or rib of beef with fries) or for the more modern set menu (featuring Mediterranean ingredients such as mullet), all the food is depicted by wholesome, instantly recognisable flavours. The wine list and the sommelier’s suggestions are greatly appreciated, as is the possibility of purchasing cheese and wine, in particular, from the shop. One final word of advice: take a seat at the counter if available, you’re in for a treat!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6658;Arti'Choc;Belgium;Eupen;Haasstraße 38, Eupen, 4700, Belgium;50.6232946;6.0382506;22;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The welcoming interior and Katja’s warm personality provide the perfect foil to this friendly modern stube. Chef Daniel is a fan of fine produce, such as trout and sweetbreads, that he pampers and enhances in traditional recipes. Expect rich flavours and authentic sauces rather than prissy details. You can even take a few preserves and liqueurs home.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6659;l'Amitié;Belgium;Antwerpen;Vlaamse Kaai 43, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2094691;4.3905601;27;false;false;Sharing;As you cross the threshold, it won’t be friendship, but something more akin to love that you will feel in this warm bistro beneath the benevolent eye of a gigantic street art-inspired fish on the wall. Quality produce is revered and lovingly presented in small plates free of fussy frills and designed to be shared. Tartare of seabass with umeboshi served in a shiso leaf is the house signature dish. If you close your eyes while sampling the Padron peppers and croquetas of Iberico jamón, you may well believe that you are in an authentic Spanish tapas bar buzzing in hipster vibes. A place of sanctuary for fans of fine food and friendship.;Terrace;[]
6660;Strofilia;Belgium;Brussels;rue du Marché aux Porcs 11, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8530093;4.3459105;37;true;true;Greek;This always-bustling establishment near the fish market is a hub of authentic Greek hospitality and generosity. Whether you come as a couple or a large group, everyone gets the attention they deserve. The menu features a whole host of delicious mezze to choose from. Tamara with sourdough bread, tender octopus with fava beans, a salad of green lentils with smoked herring, orange and sultanas… This authentic food is packed with vibrant, honest flavours that hit the spot every time. The wine list features an impressive range of Greek options that won't break the bank.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6661;L'Echappée Belle;Belgium;Lanaye;rue de Lanaye 121, Lanaye, 4600, Belgium;50.7726006;5.6902808;44;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;The quintessence of a Bib Gourmand, this eatery is embodied by Grégory and Camille’s warm friendly welcome. The couple has created strong ties with local producers, such as Ferme d’Artagnan and Ferme Fourchette, who have become part of the family. The chef crafts their excellent ingredients generously and creatively, underscoring the distinctive flavour of Belgian endive with braised beef cheeks, crunchy celeriac and marinated onion. Authentic Liège recipes and a fine view of the cottage garden from the terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6663;French Kiss;Belgium;Jette;rue Léopold I 470, Jette, 1090, Belgium;50.8729379;4.3269827;41;true;false;Meats and Grills, Classic Cuisine;A pleasant restaurant renowned for its excellent grilled dishes and impressive wine list. Dining area with a low ceiling and bright paintings adding colour to the brick walls.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6664;dis-moi où ?;Belgium;Nivelles;rue Sainte-Anne 5, Nivelles, 1400, Belgium;50.5991158;4.3230082;55;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Tell me where? Well, here! If you are looking for food that combines tradition and generosity, this upbeat eatery is the place for you (don’t forget to book). Chef Nicolas Michiels not only knows how to concoct good sauces and grill meat to perfection, he is also a dab hand at whipping up more elaborate recipes of great delicacy. He might mix a subtle quenelle of scallops and langoustine with a seafood jus, creating an exquisitely delicate balance. Choosing from the extensive menu may pose something of a conundrum. Why not try one of the excellent whiskeys suggested by the chef at the end of your meal?;Terrace;[]
6665;l'Apropos;Belgium;Neupré;rue Bonry 146, Neupré, 4120, Belgium;50.5429039;5.4875526;27;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;After a facelift, L’Apropos now sports a warm, bright interior with colourful artwork. Chef Fournier shares his love of world, Mediterranean, Asian and North - African food, which he skilfully mixes and prepares, demonstrating a flawless sense of balance.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6666;Tou.Gou;Belgium;Brugge;Smedenstraat 47, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2051428;3.2143953;43;false;false;Farm to table, Creative French;A single glance at the wholesome country menu, featuring rustic staples such as grilled tripe and snails, pork pie and partridge with endives, will set your tastebuds tingling. The veteran chef, a true disciple of text-book Gallic fare, enjoys adding the odd international twist. Gutsy flavours, hearty helpings, culinary proficiency. A take-out delicatessen service is also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6667;Sel et Poivre;Belgium;Hollain;rue de la Fontaine 3, Hollain, 7620, Belgium;50.5390201;3.4265227;73;true;false;Farm to table;Welcome to Nathalie and Alexis’ lovely little restaurant. Their enthusiasm is as communicative as their traditional cuisine. This is made from excellent produce and is enticing without forgetting the occasional dash of humour. A salt - and - pepper combination to which we will happily return.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6668;Borse van Amsterdam;Belgium;Aalst;Grote Markt 26, Aalst, 9300, Belgium;50.9384633;4.0382135;46;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Borse is a landmark of Amsterdam, as much for its colossal architecture and historic Flemish décor as for its restaurant. With its huge terrace overlooking the Grand-Place, it has been a blue-chip value for donkey’s years. The menu focuses on generous helpings of time-honoured family favourites and you will instantly be able to taste the deft hand of a seasoned chef who knows how to enhance authentic flavours.;Terrace;[]
6669;Michel;Belgium;Boninne;rue Arthur Mahaux 3, Boninne, 5021, Belgium;50.4954733;4.9325012;58;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Time seems to have stopped at Michel’s from the warm classy interior to the traditional, no-frills food that hits the spot every time thanks to recipes that star local produce. One of the house signatures is duck foie gras, prepared in a terrine with Maitrank (a local beverage) and served with home-made brioche bread and marinated veggies for a welcome fresh note. The chef also has a penchant for lobster, to which he has devoted an entire menu. A friendly, festive vibe and the guarantee of generous helpings of good food.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6670;L'Ôthentique;Belgium;Han-sur-Lesse;rue des Grottes 15c, Han-sur-Lesse, 5580, Belgium;50.124897;5.188642;76;true;true;Country cooking;All that remains of the former farmstead are the old stone vaults, yet the land and its produce are at the centre of this establishment. Chef Collignon hunts out top-notch ingredients that he deftly crafts into appetising, primarily French classics. Don’t miss the house foie gras and its pageant of fresh, unctuous garnishes. The trout, straight from the aquarium on the terrace, is another house speciality. Authentic generosity.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6671;L'Entre D'Eux;Belgium;Pont-à-Celles;rue Saint-Antoine 84, Pont-à-Celles, 6230, Belgium;50.5015211;4.3438898;18;true;false;French Contemporary;Caroline Druine combines delicacy and generosity in dishes that demonstrate her commitment to local, organic ingredients. For example, she pairs wild boar from the next-door forest with “grandma’s” red cabbage and a gutsy dark brown cocoa sauce that is so good you will be licking your fingers after mopping it up with bread! The casual vibe is further amplified by Alexandre’s natural, friendly service. A small patio in the garden planted with pear trees is ideal for alfresco summer dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6672;De Farmasie;Belgium;Vosselaar;Antwerpsesteenweg 223, Vosselaar, 2350, Belgium;51.3129222;4.8750466;87;false;false;Modern French, Traditional Cuisine;A good meal is just what the doctor ordered! So, book a table in this establishment, whose black and white colour scheme is quirkily adorned with a 17C pharmacy cabinet and wainscoting in tribute to its former vocation. Chef Verheyen, a keen “farm to table” adept and a past master of subtle flavours, is capable of jazzing up salty mackerel with ponzu, underscoring juicy local poultry with a veal gravy or turning out an immaculately cooked rib steak from his wood-burning oven. Generosity is the keyword of this restaurant as the extensive menu demonstrates.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6673;L'Embellie;Belgium;Soignies;rue de la Station 115, Soignies, 7060, Belgium;50.5732237;4.0678216;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Make your day that little bit better with a visit to this restaurant run by charming maître d' Géraldine and seasoned chef Pol. Grab a table at the front of the cosy dining space, or head to the back, where light pours in from the lovely garden – either way, you're in for a treat! When it comes to the quality of his ingredients, the chef refuses to compromise, a pursuit of excellence that is matched by his culinary expertise. This cuisine is incredibly generous, and it shows in every dish, from the rich foie gras terrine served with succulent pheasant to the rich miso jus that lends a subtle spiciness to the sea bream. Pure passion is at play here!;Terrace;[]
6674;De Gebrande Winning;Belgium;Sint-Truiden;Zepperenweg 7, Sint-Truiden, 3800, Belgium;50.8166897;5.1954385;57;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This characterful farmstead with a cafe at the entrance has lost none of its authentic charm. The focus is on beer and premium produce before all else. Indeed, an annual beer festival, an awe-inspiring beer menu and knockout beer associations demonstrate the star role of brewed beverages here. Chef Sainte pairs this ethos with no-nonsense food that shines the spotlight on nostalgic Flemish recipes, albeit with subtle modern touches. Rare beef is served with fresh green peas, asparagus and a gutsy gravy: rugged, generous cooking that hits the spot every time and which never fails to bring a smile to the face of satisfied diners.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6675;BORIS & MAURICE;Belgium;Sint-Amandsberg;Antwerpsesteenweg 329, Sint-Amandsberg, 9040, Belgium;51.0647806;3.752499;84;true;true;Farm to table;It is crystal clear that Boris and Maurice have worked together before (at Bodo). Their friendly neighbourhood eatery with a long counter offers tasty bistro fare with a twist. For example, you may start with deep-fried bites of sole and tartare sauce, followed by a juicy breast of chicken and a masterful Archiduc sauce (mushrooms and cream), finishing with a chocolate mousse. The French wine list adds the final flourish to this appetising banquet.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6676;Ni Shifu;Belgium;Antwerpen;Breydelstraat 8, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2188994;4.4194158;68;true;true;Chinese, Sichuan;Sichuan cuisine is renowned for its hot spices, pungent herbs, rich oils and wok hei preparations and the chef here deftly mixes all these components. Traditional fish soup is prepared with a rich stock and marinated Chinese cabbage, while pork belly and pork neck are braised and cooked in chili and fermented black beans: comfort food so good we warrant you will be wiping your plate squeaky clean. Close your eyes and the bustling ambience of this down-to-earth eatery may well transport you straight to Chengdu. The endless menu is truly mind-blowing. The quintessence of a Bib Gourmand!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6677;Magma;Belgium;Liège;Rue Porte aux Oies 43, Liège, 4020, Belgium;50.6386469;5.586598;82;false;true;Farm to table;It is heaven to spend time in this hip, upbeat eatery. Tom Foguenne has creatively sourced a lineup of local organic produce out of which he crafts mind-blowing flavours. He might mix smoked trout and tomato with subtly spicy oils, or serve fried chickpeas with cream of yoghurt. Each dish is steeped in unusual tastes and savours, further enhanced by the knockout organic, natural wine list. Instinctive cuisine and a frequently changing menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6678;Furbetto;Belgium;Heverlee;Naamsesteenweg 231, Heverlee, 3001, Belgium;50.8619018;4.6960242;57;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;Gust and Jasper have established their friendly eatery a stone’s throw from Heverlee railway station in a smart if somewhat low-key town house. Their love of cooking and devotion to simplicity shine through as you watch them wield their magic in the open-plan kitchen. Homemade is the name of the game here, underscored by a constant quest for superlative local produce. After nibbling on a delicious focaccia appetiser, dig into homemade pasta and subtle dishes, such as blue cheese pie paired with fermented raspberries. Furbetto hits the spot every time, all the more so due to its bargain prices!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6679;Bizie Lizie;Belgium;Antwerpen;Vlaamse Kaai 16, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2112573;4.3928018;43;false;true;Belgian;At Bizie Lizie you can choose from a modern brasserie dotted with vintage details or a swish, bordering on Baroque interior. However, those who find it difficult to make up their mind, may well find the amazing choice on the menu somewhat daunting! The menu that will find favour with lovers of nostalgic nosh features heart-warming brasserie fare, such as shrimp fritters, calf’s tongue in Madeira sauce or eels in sorrel.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6680;Glou Glou;Belgium;Borgerhout;Moorkensplein 27, Borgerhout, 2140, Belgium;51.2133781;4.4332612;27;false;false;Creative French, Fusion;The distinctive sound of fine natural wine “glug glugging” into a glass is the hallmark of this friendly eatery. Let yourself be guided by the expert insights of the sommelier. The chef, for his part, showcases his personal take on contemporary tapas, mingling French, Asian and Italian influences with enthusiasm and generosity. Full-bodied soy flanks aubergine, while fresh, spicy kimchi jazzes up beef hanger steak without forgetting the irresistible lost bread. Everything is impossibly tempting –don’t forget to book!;Counter dining;[]
6681;K restaurant;Luxembourg;Huldange;2 Stawelerstrooss, Huldange, 9964, Luxembourg;50.1615283;6.0282096;59;true;true;Home Cooking, Grills;The imposing K gives you a choice of a modern setting, a more elegant, classical room and a terrace. The fantastic range of dishes is further proof that everyone will find something to suit their palate. From classical dishes and brasserie fare to more elaborate recipes, all prepared generously and, wherever possible, at the last minute. Go on! Treat your taste buds!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6682;Bonifas;Luxembourg;Nospelt;4 Grand-Rue, Nospelt, 8391, Luxembourg;49.6735111;6.0083962;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Bonifas is steeped in the charm of a country inn with welcoming staff and a warm contemporary ambience. Chef Grégory Duranton is an unabashed fan of Gallic cuisine. You can expect rich dishes that star ingredients such as suave foie gras, intense truffle-flavoured pasta and a cut of Limousin beef crafted with textbook perfection and served with a béarnaise sauce of such depth that it will knock your socks off. The lunchtime and set menus are very popular.;Terrace;[]
6683;St Kilda;Belgium;Uccle;Avenue Coghen 44, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.8124738;4.3407196;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;St Kilda is emblematic of Belgium’s capital, whose restaurants strive to please. Established on a lively street corner and depicted by a casual vintage vibe, don’t expect fussy frills. The menu is stuffed with unusual recipes such as terrine of leeks and nori with egg mimosa or a mandarin, honey and speculoos dessert, all packed with depth. Intelligent combinations, loving care and attention lavished on the veggies and bold punchy flavours set the culinary scene, explaining its success. Now add eater-friendly prices and you will quickly understand just why this eatery is so popular!;;[]
6684;Yoka Tomo;Belgium;Schaerbeek;Avenue Félix Marchal 26, Schaerbeek, 1030, Belgium;50.852218;4.3898303;83;true;false;Japanese;A friendly restaurant in a residential neighbourhood with limited seating and a chef who crafts dishes from Southern Japan in his open-plan kitchen. Rather than decadent ingredients, you can expect authentic craftsmanship and seasonings that stimulate the tastebuds. Crispy chicken with a sweet-sour sauce is paired with crunchy vegetables and a rémoulade sauce in a tasty, almost addictive dish. Tomoyuki Ohara has no qualms about surprising us, whilst religiously respecting Japanese culinary traditions. Truly irresistible!;;[]
6685;Gaston Vouzote;Belgium;Dottignies;boulevard des Canadiens 27, Dottignies, 7711, Belgium;50.7291086;3.3137961;51;true;false;Classic Cuisine;If you feel like a slap-up meal with all the trimmings, make a beeline for this authentic brasserie whose vintage interior is paired with a Parisian vibe. Family favourites that warm the soul, such as traditional terrine (depending on the season), steak tartare and soufflé, set the scene on the menu. Homemade, hearty cooking and a festival of flavours. Gaston Vouzoute knows how to satisfy our appetites and our senses!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6686;Mamy Louise;Belgium;Wavre;chaussée de Bruxelles 410, Wavre, 1300, Belgium;50.7450033;4.5743318;80;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, French;This elegant edifice, built out of wood, glass and steel, is home to a brasserie, a cocktail bar with a terrace, lounges and meeting rooms. The equally varied menu ranges from shrimp fritters and sole meunière to veal kidneys and ossobuco in a lineup of Franco-Belgian inspiration, dotted with a few Italian classics, all of which is underscored by a love of cooking and generous helpings. There is something for everyone at Mamy Louise.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6687;Origines;Belgium;Mons;Rue de la Coupe 25, Mons, 7000, Belgium;50.4531449;3.9522093;100;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;A narrow lane near the main square of Mons leads to the endearing restaurant of Céline, the charming and ever cheerful lady of the house. The sunny rear patio features an olive tree in its centre. Chef Watteyne crafts a menu dictated by market availability, the seasons and his innovative ideas. Examples include his personal take on vitello tonnato or a fascinating tomato-strawberry-burrata dessert. Bold, distinctive cuisine crafted by a chef who takes pride in ensuring that each flavour is spot on and punchy.;Terrace;[]
6688;abCd;Belgium;Beauraing;rue de Bouillon 78, Beauraing, 5570, Belgium;50.107864;4.9580899;32;true;true;Contemporary, French;The abC(d) of French cuisine has no secrets for Borg Da Silva as is demonstrated by the succulent appetizers lined up to tempt you as soon as you set foot in his elegant establishment. The subtlety with which he prepares the main courses and the gutsy sauces embody his technical expertise and delicate touch. For example, he may add a twist to local beef (meat and tail) with a gravy of confit of onion, while his iced custard parfait will bowl you over with its painstaking combination of precise yet exuberant flavours. Generosity depicts the DNA of the set menu’s exciting score.;;[]
6689;CCnomie;Belgium;Falmignoul;rue Haute 38, Falmignoul, 5500, Belgium;50.205173;4.889297;77;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;David Coisman seeks to add his signature originality and generosity to regional produce. Rather than gimmicky combinations, he woos us with consummate skill and familiar flavours, adding a fresh twist to pheasant or steak with shallots thanks to inventive side dishes. One thing is certain: a visit to this restaurant, established in a restored 1800 barn on the family farm is synonymous with a festival of flavour.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6690;Brasserie N4;Belgium;Martelange;La Roche Percée 1, Martelange, 6630, Belgium;49.8469775;5.7331363;39;false;true;Modern French, Modern Cuisine;This friendly family brasserie abuts the busy N4 highway, but as soon as you see the rolling Ardennes countryside to the rear, your peace of mind is restored (don’t hesitate to book a room here if you would like to explore the region). Frédéric Bolis finds his inspiration in purebred French classics, to which he is not averse to adding a personal spin. Terrine of foie gras with savoury sides, entrecote steak in a Josper charcoal oven, fresh pasta with truffles: the enticing dishes on the set menu and the à la carte offering of this seasoned chef will win over the most discerning foodies!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6691;JB;Belgium;Brussels;rue du Grand Cerf 24, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8366762;4.3554714;43;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;This stylish, family-run establishment, which is located in a quiet street just a stone’s throw from Avenue Louise and the courthouse, has acquired a loyal crowd of regulars since it opened in 1979. The onus is on authentic classics that hit the spot every time. Asparagus à la flamande with a velvety hollandaise sauce, juicy lamb served with heapings of gratin dauphinois, and a sweet crêpe normande. Know-how, generosity and eater-friendly prices: the epitome of a Bib Gourmand.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6692;De Maurice à Olivier;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Lambert;chaussée de Roodebeek 246, Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, 1200, Belgium;50.8483695;4.4250563;22;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Amusingly, you have to walk past Maurice’s newsagents before reaching the Parisian-style bistro of his son, Olivier. Gallic tradition permeates both the service and the food. Dishes range from a delicious white pudding of poultry, served with chunks of lobster, truffles and a frothy sabayon for a masterful finishing touch. The chef may add the occasional original note, but he remains a steadfast champion of classical French fare. A well-stocked wine cellar and a splendid choice of cigars and whiskeys round off this enticing portrait.;Air conditioning;[]
6693;La Fermette;Belgium;Falaën;rue du Château-Ferme 30, Falaën, 5522, Belgium;50.2774825;4.7999825;47;true;false;Modern French, French;Sarah Bohet and Michaël Vancraeynest are at the helm of this authentic farmhouse in the Ardennes. The chef consummately grills entrecôte steaks on an open log fire, which are then served with a velvety béarnaise sauce. He may also mix scallops with smoked game, flanked by an onion sauce, a compote of plums and a frothy espuma of pumpkin. This exuberant culinary lineup is further enhanced by the wine list painstakingly selected by Sarah. A hit since 2003!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6694;Selecto;Belgium;Brussels;rue de Flandre 95, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8527976;4.3458637;51;true;true;Modern French;This bistro is thriving in the casual vibe of the buzzy, alternative Saint Catherine neighbourhood. Selecto never fails to deliver thanks to its knockout set menu. Bistronomic fare that hits the spot every time, with a dash of Mediterranean flair, such as creamy risotto with shrimps or a sun-drenched tartlet of aubergine, coppa and burratina, throbbing in no-frills, down-to-earth flavours.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6695;Tero;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;rue Saint Bernard 1, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8301607;4.3559096;59;true;false;Organic, Vegetarian;Tero pays tribute to the land and demonstrates great respect for produce like the veggies and pork from its own farm (Rabanisse farm). Each ingredient is assembled in intelligently curated, light dishes that favour a natural approach. A 63° egg with a personal version of shakshouka and croutons. Playful, flavoursome and bang on target. The former workshop of artist Fernand Khnopff provides the backdrop to this sparkling foodie parenthesis so in tune with the zeitgeist.;Terrace;[]
6696;La Cuisine de Yannick;Belgium;Liège;En Féronstrée 111, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.6469673;5.5810823;20;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;Red and white tablecloths set the warm bistro scene, reinforced by a soundtrack starring the likes of Jacques Brel and Georges Brassens and, above all, the personality of exuberant, fun-loving Joelle in the front of house. It is the perfect spot to (re)discover the importance of home-made cooking and the sheer strength of traditional flavours. The regularly renewed menu shines the spotlight on a line-up of classics ranging from beef tongue in Madeira sauce to a consummately crafted, oozing with taste kidney stew. The reasonably priced wine list is equally awesome.;;[]
6697;La Broche;Belgium;Dinant;rue Grande 22, Dinant, 5500, Belgium;50.2567597;4.9156102;22;false;false;Farm to table;This cosy restaurant has been a firm fixture in town since 1998. The secret of its success resides in Eric Fieuw’s generous cooking. Traditional dishes, jazzed up with the occasional modern touch. Save room for pudding - the chef is a trained pastry cook!;Air conditioning;[]
6698;Ciro's;Belgium;Antwerpen;Amerikalei 6, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2089981;4.4023987;23;true;false;Belgian;Ciro’s embodies the soul of Antwerp and its ever buzzy, down-to-earth vibe and delicious nostalgic interior provide a glimpse of the city of yesteryear. The proudly patriotic lineup on the menu also seems to have stepped straight out of the 1960s. Start with haddock pâté, followed by a star-studded lineup of deluxe vol-au-vent, crispy calf’s brains or steak garnished with a sauce so good you’ll be licking the plate clean, finishing with a decadent dame blanche (vanilla ice cream smothered in hot dark chocolate). It was love at first bite - bookings recommended!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6699;La Chapellerie;Belgium;Petit-Rechain;chaussée de la Seigneurie 13, Petit-Rechain, 4800, Belgium;50.6144857;5.835839;25;false;false;Farm to table;Sophie’s grandparents were hatmakers (hence the name), but Sophie’s love was cooking. In a tastefully refurbished brick townhouse, she turns out comfortingly familiar dishes, oozing with elegance. Spot-on cooking, a sprinkling of creativity and punchy, powerful sauces are combined in well-balanced dishes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6700;Nulle Part Ailleurs;Belgium;Couvin;rue de la Gare 10, Couvin, 5660, Belgium;50.0542563;4.4928932;20;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Hospitality is the Corman family’s raison d’être. Spend a night in a pretty room, hunt out a few excellent bottles in the shop (or the restaurant) and sample fine cooking, enhanced by modern techniques. The result is remarkable and fully worthy of a Bib Gourmand!;Interesting wine list;[]
6701;Le Clos des Récollets;Belgium;Durbuy;rue de la Prévôté 9, Durbuy, 6940, Belgium;50.3527642;5.4572404;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The picturesque charm of Durby is fully echoed in this delightful restaurant with a superb terrace. The cuisine, firmly anchored in classical techniques, occasionally delves into a more modern repertory. Each dish is a skilful association of flavours. Stay overnight to finish your meal in style.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6702;Ko'uzi;Belgium;Antwerpen;Leopoldplaats 12, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2123698;4.406656;87;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;This sleek minimalist interior draws sushi fans like bees to honey. Whether it is a classic salmon maki wrapped in a soy crepe or a more inventive sushi of smoked eel and red beetroot, Junko Kawada effortlessly combines purity of flavour with cutting-edge Japanese precision. The offer is varied and also features sashimi and salads, without forgetting a knockout range of teas to take home and sushi lessons.;Terrace;[]
6703;Schnitzel;Belgium;Antwerpen;Paardenmarkt 53, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2249696;4.4093365;100;false;true;Sharing;Good simple food is the ethos of this vintage-inspired bolthole which offers 5-, 6- and 7-course menus. Gert Weyn hits the nail on the head with intuitive personal inventions crafted with just a few ingredients. He has a knack for pairing the gutsy flavours of black pudding with slices of radish, sorrel leaves and herby fromage blanc, for example. Food that is refreshingly hearty, wholesome and oozing with flavour: such is the hallmark of Schnitzel.;Terrace;[]
6704;Ferme des 4 saisons;Belgium;Bourlers;rue de Scourmont 8b, Bourlers, 6464, Belgium;49.9839417;4.3489461;15;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern French;A menu rich in exemplary classical dishes and first - class brasserie fare will set your taste buds tingling, an inspired, innovative chef and an authentic, jazzed up interior combining contemporary and rustic details. Franck and Cathy have breathed new life and vitality into their parents’ brasserie!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6705;Le Barathym;Belgium;Nassogne;rue du Parvis 10, Nassogne, 6950, Belgium;50.128664;5.3406361;37;false;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;Barathym is synonymous with good food in a casual, warm vibe, whether on the terrace or in the updated rustic village cafe interior. The tasty seasonal fare is traditional, although sprinkled with modernity, often in the form of Asian or Mediterranean accents. Don’t expect fussy plating, but rather the simple joy of a tender juicy cut of meat served with a crisp salad dressed in a spicy sauce. Good country cooking that our grandmothers would have been proud to serve adapted to today’s tastebuds and ethos. All of which at unbeatable eater-friendly prices!;Terrace;[]
6706;Les Fines Gueules;Belgium;Charneux;Faweux 794, Charneux, 4654, Belgium;50.6745093;5.8387786;33;true;true;French Contemporary;This bright, airy restaurant is surrounded by the gently undulating green landscapes of the Herve region. Home to an inventive chef, it offers a tempting à la carte selection, as well as a simpler set menu. The chef puts a great deal of effort into his dishes, playing with techniques and combinations without compromising on flavour and generosity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6707;La Fermette des Pins;Belgium;Buvrinnes;rue du Lustre 39, Buvrinnes, 7133, Belgium;50.3873754;4.1866782;42;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;“What you see is what you get” could well be the baseline of this lovely farmstead depicted by old oak rafters, bare brick walls and a terrace that makes the most of its idyllic rural setting. The seasoned chef has perfected the art of sourcing first-class local produce. His eggs are perfectly cooked at exactly 62°C and garnished with a flavoursome espuma of mashed potato and crunchy chicory, unless you wouldn’t prefer a much-loved Belgian staple: steak, fresh fries and a pepper sauce? One thing is certain: everything here bears the hallmark of tradition. All that remains is to choose between the different menus!;Car park,Terrace;[]
6708;Faraya;Belgium;Wemmel;De Limburg Stirumlaan 200, Wemmel, 1780, Belgium;50.9017775;4.3179401;55;true;false;Lebanese, Middle Eastern;The Harika family has morphed the Faraya into an elegant restaurant, whilst retaining its home from home vibe (songbirds included!). True to Lebanese tradition, the authentic dishes are piled high in the middle of the table to be shared by all the guests. Smooth hummus, labneh, mixed grills rich in spices and baklava dripping in honey… Don’t miss the buffet (Saturday evening and Sunday lunchtime).;Terrace;[]
6709;Terminus;Belgium;Watou;Callicannesweg 16, Watou, 8978, Belgium;50.8132336;2.6387985;44;true;false;Classic French, Country cooking;Don't hesitate to stop at this terminus just before the French border, which is as popular with truck drivers as with families and foodies. In the distance, you can see the farm of the Verheyde family, who has turned the nearby gas station into a gourmet delicatessen. Pieter, owner and sommelier, is justly proud of his impressive wine cellar, the fruit of his expertise and passion. The culinary score will delight connoisseurs, particularly those who appreciate big-boned, wholesome nosh. Recipes that hit the spot every time, with meat from the family farm, super fresh cod or shrimp from the North Sea, before finishing with a local specialty, a tarte mazarin de Poperinge… Food that uplifts the hearts of travellers and an irrepressible joie de vivre sets the scene in this terminus.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
6710;Biestro H-eat;Belgium;Bornem;Hingenesteenweg 48, Bornem, 2880, Belgium;51.1003144;4.246376;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This hip bistro never fails to appeal. Trendy lighting, a vintage wood-burning stove and a full view of the chefs working in their flame-licked open kitchen. Ellen graciously and seamlessly supervises the front of house. A patriotic lineup of Flemish classics, complete with Asian twists and Mediterranean flair, are blended into enticing set and à la carte menus. Belgian staples such as eel have no secrets for the consummate chefs, who serve this family favourite in a sabayon of green herbs with heaps of piping hot crunchy fries. Or how about a fillet of halibut with a frothy velvety bearnaise sauce, nobashi shrimps and oyster leaf? Generosity shines through in every detail of this friendly bistro that hits all the right buttons!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6711;Amu;Belgium;Turnhout;Patersstraat 79, Turnhout, 2300, Belgium;51.3263708;4.9494174;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;A stone’s throw from the main square, the Amu Food and Wine Bar sports a marriage of elegant and intimate that is both romantic and sexy. In this intriguing setting, chef Marjanne Moonen rustles up genuine delicacies. Her surprise menu, composed of fascinating dishes based on just a few ingredients, is both free of fancy frills and always spot on. Her distinctive culinary signature is a patchwork of Mediterranean influences, spices and fermentation techniques from the Middle East. Examples include her yoghurt and tahini sauce that adds a kick to a dish of sweet potatoes and carrots, suavely blending depth and balance. The affordable wine list is sourced from all over the world.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6712;Le Baan Thaï;Belgium;Gent;Corduwaniersstraat 57, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0578598;3.7231435;73;false;false;Thai;A whiff of exoticism subtly contrasts with the historic character of the Patershol district in this grand old abode. The welcoming interior sports high ceilings and works of art, without forgetting the walled courtyard - exquisite in fine weather. The dishes are visually appetising and generously presented, revealing the wide range of flavours of traditional Thai cuisine. The ingredients are fresh, steeped in rich perfumes and aromas with just the right balance of spices. A blue-chip value since 1989!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6713;Appel Thaï;Belgium;Anderlecht;rue du Pommier 439, Anderlecht, 1070, Belgium;50.8323994;4.2627659;18;true;false;Thai;Appel Thaï, which is a firm favourite with fans of Asian fare, makes the most of its lush green oasis in Anderlecht. Choose between the peaceful terrace or the buzzier, casual vibe indoors. Fresh, spicy, intense flavours crafted by a veteran chef. Home-made nems served with a tingling sauce, rich massaman curry or a Pad Thai all cooked to textbook perfection: high-flying Thai cuisine in an unstuffy, relaxed setting. Wide variety of choice and dependable first-rate quality.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6714;De Garage;Belgium;Kortrijk;Aalbeeksesteenweg 64, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.8213023;3.2582294;83;false;true;Farm to table;You will probably have guessed from the name and the industrial look that this space to be a garage. Now reimagined as a bistro, the blend of untreated materials and vintage design elements creates a unique atmosphere. The menu puts the emphasis squarely on authentic and familiar flavours, eschewing any unnecessary frills. Think braised pork cheek in a robust sauce, sole meunière with pommes frites or even vegan green curry. Sommelier Fitzgerald Rigole's recommendations are always spot on – and his enthusiasm is infectious!;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6715;ANJU;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;Rue de la Source 73, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8310045;4.3532825;34;true;false;Korean Contemporary;Sang Hoon Degeimbre reveals his Korean roots in Saint Gilles. In a hip, minimalist interior, he has recruited a kitchen team that crafts an extensive range of dishes to share, ranging from gutsy stocks and hot pots to kimchi. Dig into the decadently addictive Korean-style fried chicken with a sweet, spicy sauce. The antithesis of fussy, but with lashings of traditional generosity.;Air conditioning;[]
6716;Pluriel;Belgium;Transinne;Rue de la Colline 58, Transinne, 6890, Belgium;50.0109264;5.1991274;42;false;false;French Contemporary, Creative French;A slightly smoky aroma tickles your nostrils as soon as you reach the carpark of this former farmstead, which tastefully sports untreated materials to create a warm vibe. Loélia Gachadoat and Vadim Poncelet, steadfast champions of barbecue cooking, demonstrate their combined talents, mingling rustic flavours with a creative festival of occasionally surprising nuances. The symbiosis between these two chefs signs the characterful cuisine.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6717;la cantinetta;Belgium;Grivegnée;Rue Haute Wez 191, Grivegnée, 4030, Belgium;50.6274342;5.5892796;16;false;false;Italian, Organic;La cantinetta possesses a distinctly casual and convivial feel that is very appealing. Thomas is the host and sommelier, and his brother Matthias, the chef, showcases the skills his mother taught him, cooking up a bold take on authentic Italian cuisine. For instance, he spices up raw salmon with a zingy tomato broth and various beans that have been imbued with subtle bitterness. A wasabi granita provides an extra kick. Expect generous flavours and original ideas. Great value for money!;;[]
6718;Quatre Vins;Belgium;Brugge;Philipstockstraat 8, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2094474;3.2256457;84;false;true;Sharing, International;Put on your rose-tinted spectacles and bask in the warm, cosy interior of Quatre Vins, without forgetting the walled terrace, which is bliss come summertime. The menu features a line-up of international dishes to be shared in a friendly, buzzy vibe. How about steamed pork belly with crunchy hispi (pointed) cabbage in a rich BBQ sauce and a bread roll on the side, or steamed haddock on a bed of leeks and a light, herb-flavoured sauce? In addition to a fine range of biodynamic and natural wines, Maxinne and Olivier bend over backwards to ensure guests feel at home in their fun-loving establishment.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6719;ANAM;South Korea;Seoul;10 Bukchon-ro 5-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03055, South Korea;37.57939;126.98446;65;true;false;Dwaeji-gukbap;At this humble diner situated in Bukchon Village, Seoul, the pork and rice soup comes in two sizes: medium and extra-meat. In the soup, a special oil made with Cheongyang chili pepper and kale is drizzled on top of the agreeably clean broth, with their culinary harmony creating a unique visual appearance and rich flavors. Plus, the Spanish Duroc baby pork ribs and thin slices of pork butt that complement the dish are exceedingly tender and boast subtle flavors, raising the gastronomic experience to a new crescendo. Visit Anam and enjoy a warm hearty bowl of its trademark soup. One last thing: Feel free to add cilantro to taste.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6721;Tokyo Babsang;South Korea;Busan;34-6 Namcheonbada-ro, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48304, South Korea;35.14839;129.11386;86;false;true;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;The familiar vibrant vibe of Gwangalli Beach, a landmark attraction in Busan, will have given way to that of calm and peace by the time one arrives at the door of Tokyo Babsang, which specializes in unaju (grilled eel over rice) and hitsumabushi (Nagoya-style grilled eel), the two representative Japanese eel dishes. The fare at this diner mirrors Chef Kim Tae-woo’s dedication to authenticity. Each bite of the thick and chewy eel, which stands out with its inherent flavor, goes perfectly with the accompanying sauce brimming with umami. But above all, its harmony with the glossy steamed rice, normally made from newly polished rice, heightens the appetite. The chef’s respect for authentic recipes, coupled with his sensitive culinary creativity, is what keeps the joint’s fare trustworthy.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6722;Anmok;South Korea;Busan;3 Gwangnam-ro 22 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48307, South Korea;35.14492;129.11076;68;false;false;Dwaeji-gukbap;Anmok’s unique take on dwaeji-gukbap, or pork and rice soup, may surprise customers with novel flavors and charm that defy their memories of the dish. The soup is not merely unconventional. It’ll make you nod in appreciation. The dish also has a distinct flavor that evokes those of many other Korean soups. Indeed, the diner has successfully differentiated itself from countless other famed restaurants in Busan, the capital of dwaeji-gukbap, giving the impression that it continues to change and evolve while exploring diverse culinary directions. Though everyone has different preferences, we recommend you savor Amok’s soup offerings as they are prepared without adding chili sauce or salted shrimp.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6723;ARP;South Korea;Busan;35 Taejong-ro 99 beon-gil, Yeongdo-gu, Busan, 49035, South Korea;35.09293;129.04258;86;false;true;Vegan;ARP offers a 100 percent vegan menu. An acronym formed from the phrase “Around Plants,” the eatery’s name symbolizes the positive, ethical kitchen table of the round Earth and the unlimited possibilities inherent in veggie cuisine. Here, customers can enjoy a diverse range of non-meat dishes paired with housemade wine made of rice. And these offerings immediately debunk the common misconception that vegan food is not delicious. For instance, the signature bracken pasta features dried bracken and mushrooms for a maximally chewy texture and pleasant nutty flavors. The vegan cheese, though made from coconut oil, tastes exactly like cheddar cheese. Come and relish the gastronomic charm of ARP’s delectable non-animal-based fare in this elegantly designed space.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6724;Egg & Flour;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 35 Shinheung-ro 26-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04337, South Korea;37.545342;126.984447;31;true;false;Italian;As implied by its name, Egg & Flour is an Italian restaurant specializing in fresh, handmade pasta composed only with egg and flour. Even the entrance to the establishment greets us with sacks of flour and pasta rolling machines. The space is located along a winding alley in Haebangchon, yet the Itaewon skyline seen from the terrace and through the glass wall evokes majesty. The establishment’s signature offering is freshly made Italian pasta with a Korean twist – be it Jeju black pork ragù featuring red chili paste and fish sauce, burrata cheese, or roasted Ecklonia cava.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
6725;Ggupdang;South Korea;Seoul;615 Gangnam-daero, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06524, South Korea;37.5166307;127.0188926;58;true;false;Barbecue;Situated right near Sinsa station, this restaurant specializes in grilled pork butt cured for 15 days before being quickly grilled on a specially made aluminum grate over Binchotan charcoal. Thanks to this method of cooking, the meat is fatty, tender, and juicy. As in the case of sushi, when it is eaten with rice (prepared with a recipe conceived by a Japanese consultant chef) and Korean horseradish, the meat juice is absorbed by the rice, making it even softer. The side orders are not to be missed.;;[]
6726;Haemok;South Korea;Busan;8 Gunam-ro 24 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48094, South Korea;35.16174;129.15977;72;false;true;Japanese;Popular among both tourists and local regulars, Haemok offers accessible Japanese fare. Its blue fence and inexplicably exotic edifice create a vibe that makes this spot stand out in the neighborhood. Its wood-based décor and tatami floor also add to the exotic ambiance. Haemok’s menu includes a few selections of Japanese rice bowls, sashimi, tempura, and tataki dishes. But its signature item is unarguably hitsumabushi (Nagoya-style grilled eel). Coated with umami-rich sauce, the eel features bottomless flavor and is a perfect accompaniment to the rice cooked to perfection. And just so you know, Haemok also has outposts in Seoul.;Air conditioning;[]
6727;Nagahama Mangetsu;South Korea;Busan;57 Udong 1-ro, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48088, South Korea;35.16664;129.15748;72;true;false;Ramen;Tucked deep within the Haeridan-gil area, this establishment stands out with a long line of diners waiting to be seated. This ramen joint in Busan is the first Korean outpost of a restaurant that started during the 1960s in the Nagahama area in Fukuoka, Japan. The ramen is prepared by simmering pig bones for hours until the broth becomes milky and smooth. Combined with a secret homemade soy sauce, the broth tastes rich, but never heavy. You may request your noodles be cooked to your liking, or add raw garlic or a spicy sauce. If you find your new broth a little too salty, feel free to ask for additional broth to savor your dish to the fullest.;Counter dining;[]
6728;FAGP;South Korea;Seoul;136 Wangsimni-ro, Seongdong-gu, Seoul, 04789, South Korea;37.54964;127.04456;87;false;false;Italian;In a city where a plate of pasta is as ubiquitous as a bowl of kalguksu, it takes a good dose of creativity and knowledge of the genre to be recognized for one’s craft. Chef Lee Jong-hyuk is armed with both. FAGP is a casual restaurant that offers a simple yet inventive menu with a focus on the relatively humble pasta. There is a genuine sense of conviviality here, which comes as no surprise, as the chef says he revels in engaging with his customers while cooking in the open kitchen.;Counter dining;[]
6729;A Flower Blossom on the Rice;South Korea;Seoul;3-6 Insadong 16-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03146, South Korea;37.57535;126.98404;19;false;true;Korean;Located in a quiet alley away from the touristy bustle of Insa-dong, A Flower Blossom on the Rice is a restaurant that caters to the health-conscious diner, serving wholesome home-cooked fare using only certified organic ingredients sourced straight from the farm. The signature dish at this restaurant is the Bojagi Bibimbap — a log of cooked rice topped with five different sautéed vegetables in their multi-colored glory, encased in a crépe-thin egg omelet resembling a gift, tied with a seaweed ribbon and presented with a single flower on top.;;[]
6730;Hadongkwan;South Korea;Seoul;12 Myeongdong 9-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04538, South Korea;37.56439;126.98501;94;false;true;Gomtang;This beloved family-owned culinary landmark, located on a busy side street in Myeong-dong, has been serving rustic bowls of beef bone soup since 1939. The version here is served in traditional brass bowls with rice already submerged in the hot soup. The broth is pure and rich with an unmistakable sweetness that can only result from boiling large amounts of beef for a long period of time. This old-fashioned, no-fuss eatery opens early in the morning and closes when its soup vats run dry.;Air conditioning;[]
6731;Woo Lae Oak;South Korea;Seoul;62-29 Changgyeonggung-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04546, South Korea;37.56815;126.99866;22;true;true;Naengmyeon;Lauded as one of the best Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodle restaurants in the city, Woo Lae Oak has been serving consistently stellar food since 1946. The family-operated establishment is tucked away in the back alleys of Euljiro 4-ga, a bustling business hub. The restaurant interior is spacious and spotlessly clean. Indulge in their legendary Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles, served in broth or in a spicy sauce, and their bulgogi, grilled tableside.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
6732;Goobok Mandu;South Korea;Seoul;7 Duteopbawi-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04335, South Korea;37.54501;126.97318;24;true;false;Dim Sum;Run by a Korean husband and Chinese wife, Goobok Mandu is a no-frills establishment that specializes in Chinese-style dumplings. The couple prepare the dumplings from scratch based on an old family recipe passed down to them by her grandmother. The dumplings are freshly made to order each time. Try the restaurant’s signature pot stickers with their glorious wafer-thin web of crispy golden crust as well as the steamed xiao long bao.;;[]
6733;Pildong Myeonok;South Korea;Seoul;26 Seoae-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04624, South Korea;37.56035;126.99689;21;false;true;Naengmyeon;Located near Namsangol Hanok Village by Chungmuro subway station, this restaurant is a Pil-dong landmark that has been serving Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles for decades. The restaurant’s chilled broth has a delicate beef flavor, its subtlety both loved and disputed among cold buckwheat noodle aficionados. Another highlight of the restaurant is the buttery and tender boiled pork slices, served in thick slices with a dipping sauce. Homemade dumplings are also popular.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6734;Geumdwaeji Sikdang;South Korea;Seoul;149 Dasan-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04607, South Korea;37.55705;127.01165;54;true;false;Barbecue;Located along a main road in Sindang-dong, Geumdwaeji Sikdang can be easily spotted by its gold-on-white-tile signage and the queue outside the door long after peak dining hours. The establishment used to serve fine cuts of YBD pig, and recently upgraded the meat quality by switching to premium-grade cuts, enhancing overall standards. The texture of the pork is firm and meaty, with a good balance of flavorful fat that renders the meat supremely juicy. Items are is cooked on a cast-iron grill over coal briquettes that help keep the temperature constant. The restaurant does not accept reservations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6735;Yonggeumok;South Korea;Seoul;41-2 Jahamun-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03036, South Korea;37.57972;126.97088;28;true;false;Chueotang;Since 1932, Yonggeumok has been offering piping hot bowls of loach soup, a popular local dish believed to boost energy, especially during the summer months. This restaurant serves two different versions of the hearty and comforting soup: the chunkier Seoul style with whole loach, and the smoother Jeolla province style with ground loach. Everything on the menu as well as the complimentary side dishes are prepared daily by the longtime owner and chef Han Jeong-ja.;Air conditioning;[]
6736;Gebangsikdang;South Korea;Seoul;17 Seolleung-ro 131-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06060, South Korea;37.51727;127.03942;76;false;false;Gejang;Soy sauce-marinated crab and stylish décor don’t always go hand in hand, but at Gebangsikdang, they do. A collaboration between fashion marketer Bang Geon-hyuk and his parents, veterans of the soy sauce marinated crab restaurant business, Gebangsikdang caters to a trend-conscious crowd with its polished interior and its wide selection of raw crab dishes. For those who find it bothersome to eat crab on the shell, there are options that come with just the crab flesh and crab roe on a mound of hot rice.;Car park;[]
6737;Buchon Yukhoe;South Korea;Seoul;200-12 Jong-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03195, South Korea;37.57034;126.99991;68;false;true;Yukhoe;Occupying a corner of the well-established raw beef alley of Gwangjang Market, Buchon Yukhoe has been in business since 1965, originally started as Buchon Sikdang selling short rib soup. The founding matriarch’s original Jeollado Province-style raw beef, seasoned with red chili paste, gave way to the more popular Seoul-style in the 1980s, seasoned with sesame oil and eaten with matchstick pears. Try the raw beef bibimbap for a more substantial meal. Locally sourced beef is delivered to the restaurant each morning.;;[]
6738;Okdongsik;South Korea;Seoul;44-10 Yanghwa-ro 7-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04035, South Korea;37.55261;126.91449;90;false;true;Dwaeji-gukbap;With his take on dwaeji-gukbap, Chef Ok Dong-sik has managed to singlehandedly change any preconceptions the local diners previously had about the hearty pork and rice soup dish Koreans hold near and dear to their hearts. Think bacon-thin slices of silky tender pork meat piled on a bed of rice, all submerged in his trademark consommé-like clear broth. The 'extra large' portion comes with double the amount of meat. The space is limited and only 100 bowls of gukbap are sold daily so get here early.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6739;Yukjeon Hoekwan;South Korea;Seoul;47 Tojeong-ro 37-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04155, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;77;false;true;Bulgogi;Three generations spanning five decades have kept this restaurant in business since its opening in 1962. At the time, their iconic crispy thin-sliced bulgogi, grilled over open flames, was all that was offered on the menu. The dish became so popular that the name bassak bulgogi was patented. Today, the restaurant stands four stories high, still serving the same dish that has fed generations. Their coagulated beef blood soup with a clear broth is another stunner.;Air conditioning;[]
6740;Jinmi Pyeongyang Naengmyeon;South Korea;Seoul;305-3 Hakdong-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06061, South Korea;37.516114;127.036202;96;false;true;Naengmyeon;According to owner and chef Yim Se-kwon, long time experience in the kitchens of one of the most iconic Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodle restaurants is the secret to the success of this place. The menu here is what you would expect to see in a typical cold buckwheat noodle restaurant. Other than the noodles, it offers staples such as boiled pork and beef slices, bulgogi, dumplings and Pyeongyang-style beef hot pot.;Valet parking;[]
6741;Yangyang Memil Makguksu;South Korea;Seoul;10 Donggwang-ro 15-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06561, South Korea;37.49247;126.98826;70;false;true;Memil-guksu;The not-so-secret secret to the longevity and success of Yangyang Memil Makguksu is that its noodles are made with 100% buckwheat and that they are made to order every time. The proprietor of the restaurant began his business many years ago for one reason only - buckwheat noodles were his favorite food. Although the restaurant specializes in the Gangwon-do Province-style cold buckwheat noodles, it also makes a fine bowl of spicy noodles composed with homemade kimchi. The basic spread is simple, but it’s rustic food at its best, made with love.;;[]
6742;Sarukame;South Korea;Seoul;15 Yeonnam-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03990, South Korea;37.56103;126.92267;98;true;true;Ramen;Sarukame is currently run by its second-generation owner-chef Hiroto Honma. Going beyond merely retaining the title of the restaurant, the current chef is carrying on its culinary legacy by staying in contact with its founder and preserving its original recipes. Such effort, coupled with Chef Honma’s vast experience in the restaurant business and gastronomic sensibility, garnered and developed over the years working in cities around the world, are adding new narrative layers to this establishment. Sarukame continues to create exclusive menus that combine the flavors of trendy ramen in Japan, classic flavors and new original flavors, thereby shaping its brand identity and serving the ever-changing needs of Seoul’s ramen aficionados.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6743;Damtaek;South Korea;Seoul;34 World Cup-ro 8-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04035, South Korea;37.55316;126.91412;57;false;false;Ramen;Damtaek is a cozy little ramen haven nestled in a quiet alley near Hapjeong Station. Chef Jo Won-hyeon has purposefully adorned this quaint space with vintage artifacts. The restaurant’s shio ramen, and associated variations that use the same soup base, are in stark contrast to its homey, down-to-earth vibe. The refined and clean flavors of the soups are singular and inspire lingering addiction. With a passion for creating tastes unbound by culinary convention, the chef has persistently dedicated his craft toward perfecting the art of shio ramen, creating ramen that can delight any palate.;Air conditioning;[]
6744;Loveurth;South Korea;Busan;32-1 Gwangan-ro 49 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48296, South Korea;35.15644;129.1185;20;false;false;Vegan;Tucked away in a back alley near Gwangan Elementary School, Loveurth is a vegan restaurant that serves vegan versions of familiar foods. From casual dishes to filling, hearty meals, this innovative diner continues to embark on diverse experiments that transcend culinary boundaries. Building upon their experience and insight into vegan food, Co-CEOs Kim Han-sol and Jung Myeong-won transform familiar classics, such as rice bowls, pastas, udon dishes, and soups, into vegan equivalents with a fun and playful twist. Since offering an extensive vegan menu is no easy feat, Loveurth instead tweaks its menu every once in a while so that it can better provide customers with gastronomic pleasure derived from a diverse compendium of vegan cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
6745;Mattdol;South Korea;Seoul;63 Seongdeokjeong-gil, Seongdong-gu, Seoul, 04775, South Korea;37.53808;127.05065;33;true;true;Mexican;Mattdol is a Mexican restaurant run by Chef Lee Chang-yun, who has been steadfastly honing his culinary skills with an exceptional adventurous spirit. He has a particular passion for tortilla. At Mattdol, customers can often see the chef kneading masa to make tortilla, just as he learned in Mexico. Anyone who tries its tostada and taco dishes, featuring his housemade tortilla, will instinctively realize that, compared with common tortilla-based dishes with run-of-the-mill flavors and textures, his creations are on a whole other level. Mattdol is where the chef’s training in diverse culinary styles meets Korean seasonal ingredients. And the result is a unique Mexican cuisine with intuitive flavors that can captivate the palates of gourmets.;Air conditioning;[]
6746;PILI PILI;South Korea;Busan;54 Muhak-ro 33 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48268, South Korea;35.16379;129.11807;31;false;false;Thai;Take a stroll around Gwangan-dong, and you’ll come across a restaurant whose exterior and interior design will make you ask yourself whether you are in Busan or Thailand. Piri Piri is a Thai-style dining bar that serves Thai cuisine and exotic cocktails. Its hip vibes, music resonating from a turntable, and generous servings of authentic Thai dishes evoke a magical feeling of traveling in that exotic country. So why not come and indulge in the visual feast of the spectacular Poo Pad Phong Curry (stir-fried crab in curry powder) while imbibing a Thai highball?;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6747;Yurimmyeon;South Korea;Seoul;139-1 Seosomun-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04515, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;18;true;true;Memil-guksu;For over 50 years, this family-run eatery has been serving bowls of noodles to those seeking comforting nourishment. The fresh buckwheat noodles, one of its bestsellers, are made from scratch, daily, using premium salt from Bigeumdo Island in Sinan County, and buckwheat flour from Bongpyeong. Topped with seasoned vegetables, thin strips of egg garnish, and a dollop of sweet and spicy sauce, a bowl of these noodles makes for a satisfying meal. Garak-guksu, wheat noodles in piping hot broth, comes with a generous serving of fishcake.;Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6748;Mijin;South Korea;Seoul;#116-2 le Meilleur Jongno town, 19 Jong-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03157, South Korea;37.5708;126.97985;59;true;true;Memil-guksu;Located in the heart of Gwanghwamun, Mijin has been serving Korean-style cold buckwheat noodles since 1952. The restaurant operates a factory in the basement where the dipping sauce and buckwheat noodles are prepared fresh daily. One portion comes with two stacked tray baskets of noodles, a large kettle of chilled sauce and basic side dishes. Dress your dipping sauce to your desire with grated daikon, light wasabi, crispy seasoned laver and chopped green onions that have already been laid out on the table for you.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6749;Tim Ho Wan;South Korea;Seoul;30 Bongeunsa-ro 86-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06165, South Korea;37.5115769;127.0567982;53;false;false;Dim Sum;Tim Ho Wan has played a major role in making Hong Kong-style dim sum popular in many countries worldwide. The main force behind such growing popularity has been its policy of maintaining the traditional form of Hong Kong dim sum dishes and making them available at affordable prices. This management philosophy has been upheld in its branches in Seoul, making them as authentic as the original. The franchise’s capacious Samseong outpost, which is also the main location in Seoul, can serve up to 110 customers at one time and offers ample parking spaces. It is the perfect place to indulge in a wide variety of traditional dim sum.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
6750;Jin Jin;South Korea;Seoul;60 World Cup buk-ro 1-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04031, South Korea;37.55777;126.91324;81;false;false;Chinese;For over 40 years, Chef Wang Yuk-sung has been committed to popularizing Chinese cuisine in Korea. Unlike most generic Korean-style Chinese restaurants ubiquitous to Seoul, Chef Wang offers a limited menu of just ten dishes to ensure that the quality of the food he serves is consistently high. Some of the most requested dishes include shrimp toast, stir-fried crab meat with egg white, mapo tofu and stir-fried beef with gai lan.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6751;Menten;South Korea;Seoul;305 Samil-daero, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04537, South Korea;37.5619506;126.9885683;15;true;false;Ramen;Menten is a one-chef ramen restaurant that serves only two dishes: shoyu ramen and tantanmen. Solely responsible for the entire cooking process, the chef has streamlined the menu to concentrate his efforts on quality. Based on their clear broth, the two ramen dishes offer an appealing balance between mild and strong flavors. Each ingredient is precisely prepared and cooked, but the shoyu ramen in particular, delivers a mixture of complexity and umami. As the chef puts it, his ramen dishes are “simple and uncomplicated but aim for perfection." The chef is almost always quietly absorbed in his work, thereby reflecting a sense of responsibility and confidence.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6752;Hapjeongok;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 21 Yanghwa-ro 1-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04026, South Korea;37.54944;126.91037;96;true;false;Gomtang;Hapjeongok is a restaurant born of nostalgia. As they were reminiscing one day on the father-in-law’s beef bone soup and boiled beef slices, the latter suggested to his daughter-in-law that they should open a beef bone soup restaurant. The establishment stays true to the inspiration — deeply flavorful beef broth, rice rendered soft and sweet in the piping hot soup, tender slices of beef, and a generous serving of boiled offal. The restaurant’s cabbage soybean paste soup is also a must try. Only around 100 portions of soup are served daily, so go early.;;[]
6753;Base is nice;South Korea;Seoul;20 Dohwa 2-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04171, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;96;true;true;Vegetarian;Base is Nice is a vegetarian-friendly restaurant. Chef/owner Jang Jin-a had a fairly long career overseas as a restaurant consultant, food stylist, and food & beverage planner. The diner’s natural ambience and well-balanced, vegetable-centered dishes are proud manifestations of her lifelong culinary endeavors. Creations of rice and vegetables, accompanied by soup and side dishes, are refined and tasty. As Jang puts it, the restaurant’s menu is a way to experience everyday food through a natural, veggie-centered diet, and not thanks to a conscious approach to vegetarianism. Reservation required.;Air conditioning;[]
6754;Oreno Ramen;South Korea;Seoul;14 Dongmak-ro 6-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04072, South Korea;37.54744;126.91729;59;true;false;Ramen;Foreign foods are not always embraced by local diners. In fact, authenticity is often shunned by many due to its sheer “foreignness. ” But for chef Shin Dong-woo, years of experience in the ramen business has led him to success, and he did it by introducing the authentic flavors of Japanese ramen to local consumers. The restaurant’s tori paitan ramen, with its rich, velvety-smooth chicken stock, and the shoyu ramen, clean yet deeply flavorful, are good examples of Shin’s ramen know-how. The fresh noodles and stocks are prepared in the kitchen, daily.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6755;Bongsanok;South Korea;Seoul;5-6 Banpo-daero 8-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06716, South Korea;37.48336;127.01242;19;true;true;Mandu;Mandutguk, or Korean dumpling soup, is a dish that is deeply rooted in the day-to-day lives of Koreans. Owner Yoon Young-sook became acquainted with Hwanghaedo-style dumpling soup through her mother-in-law, a native of Sariwon, which is north of the border. To emulate the pure taste of the original dumpling filling, Yoon says she follows her recipe to the tee and feels very proud when she hears customers say her dumplings remind them of their own grandmother's.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6756;Mapo Ok;South Korea;Seoul;312 Tojeong-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04165, South Korea;37.53983;126.94332;86;false;false;Seolleongtang;In the realm of Korean comfort food, there is little else more quintessential than seolleongtang — a hearty bowl of soup made by boiling ox bones and beef for hours until the broth turns almost milky white. Mapo Ok, which opened its doors in 1949, makes its signature dish by boiling brisket and ox bones until slightly opaque. The ox bone soup is served with thick slices of tender brisket and rice already mixed into the piping hot broth. Ask for a side of kimchi juice to season your soup for that extra dimension of flavor.;;[]
6757;Hwanggeum Kongbat;South Korea;Seoul;9 Mapo-daero 16-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04205, South Korea;37.5509;126.9567;31;false;false;Dubu;Tucked away in Ahyeon-dong, this hidden gem specializes in rustic homemade bean curd. The unctuously creamy bean curd is made from scratch, daily, at the crack of dawn. The secret to the elevated nuttiness of local soybeans that shine through in Hwanggeum Kongbat’s bean curd is the extra thick soymilk and reduced levels of the coagulant. With a desire to share healthy food with other people, the proprietor also makes and sells homemade rich soybean paste stew and unrefined rice wine.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6758;Kyoyang Siksa;South Korea;Seoul;238 Itaewon-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04400, South Korea;37.53592;126.99994;41;true;true;Barbecue;Sapporo-style lamb barbecue is the name of the game at Kyoyang Siksa, which specializes in tender young lamb less than 10 months old. Flown in from Australia, this meat is juicy and tender and the menu offers three cuts: French rack, ribs, and loin steak. These may be grilled tableside by the staff. Other solid dishes include soup curry with grilled vegetables and aromatic garlic rice served with small sheets of laver to wrap it in. Seating is limited, so be sure to book ahead.;Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
6759;Nampo Myeonok;South Korea;Seoul;24 Eulji-ro 3-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04522, South Korea;37.567269;126.981609;80;true;false;Naengmyeon;Tucked away in a small alley among densely populated office buildings that sees a constant stream of foot traffic, the main building of this long-standing institution recently underwent a major facelift. A longtime favorite among patrons of all ages for its authentic Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles and beef hot pot, Nampo Myeonok continues to charm with its consistently good food and friendly service. Chair seating and floor seating are both available.;;[]
6760;Manjok Ohyang Jokbal;South Korea;Seoul;134-7 Seosomun-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04514, South Korea;37.56324;126.97598;94;false;true;Jokbal;At Manjok Oyhang Jokbal, the beloved Korean braised pig's feet dish is impeccably crafted with the utmost dedication and care to hygiene and quality. The restaurant, armed with a systematic central distribution system, offers consistent quality at all of its franchised locations. Here, the popular pork dish can be enjoyed warm until the very last piece, thanks to the specially designed hotplates installed into the tables.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
6761;Daesungjip;South Korea;Seoul;5 Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03029, South Korea;37.57269;126.96091;79;false;false;Doganitang;For a soul-satisfying bowl of ox knee soup, look no further than Daesungjip. Its reputation for quality and consistency has seen generations of loyal patrons come for the rich, hearty signature so thick with ox knee cartilage that you can stand a spoon up in it. Take a bite of the slow-cooked cartilage doused in the special soy dipping sauce and all is right in the world. A long queue is the norm here but, thankfully, takeaways are also possible.;Car park;[]
6762;Gaeseong Mandu Koong;South Korea;Seoul;11-3 Insadong 10-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03146, South Korea;37.57423;126.98539;28;true;true;Mandu;Established in 1970 by an elderly Gaeseong native, this restaurant has been serving Gaeseong-style dumplings for three generations. The dumplings here are large, plump and filled with a generous amount of shredded napa cabbage and mung bean sprouts. The soup broth is made with beef brisket, and the owners prepare the dumplings by hand daily with the freshest ingredients. The traditional Korean hanok setting is both charming and elegant.;;[]
6764;Myeongdong Kyoja;South Korea;Seoul;29 Myeongdong 10-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04537, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;95;true;true;Kalguksu;Myeongdong Kyoja is a family-owned place in operation since 1966. The restaurant, which offers only four items on the menu, specializes in dumplings and noodle soup. An impressive number of patrons flock here daily, largely because all the dishes, including its signature garlic-laden kimchi, are made in-house. Simple décor and service come with hefty portions at affordable prices. It has a sister operation in the same area of Myeong-dong.;;[]
6765;Mandujip;South Korea;Seoul;338 Apgujeong-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06018, South Korea;37.52785;127.03898;77;true;true;Mandu;Located in a trendsetting part of the city dominated by state-of-the-art fashion, this restaurant has stood its ground for 30 years with a humble dish that has wooed the palates of countless people — dumpling soup. Mandujip specializes in Pyeongando-style dumplings, filled with minced beef, bean curd, mung bean sprouts, green onions and sesame oil. Each order comes with six large dumplings in a clear, flavorful beef broth made with chunks of brisket.;;[]
6766;Hwangsaengga Kalguksu;South Korea;Seoul;78 Bukchon-ro 5-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03053, South Korea;37.58003;126.98065;75;true;true;Kalguksu;No matter what time of day, always expect to see a line outside this beloved establishment, known for their humble noodle soup and dumplings. Originally called Bukchon Kalguksu when it opened in 2001, it changed its name in 2014, but that hasn’t stopped the regulars from coming time and again for its freshly made dumplings and silky-soft noodles served in a rich ox bone broth. Boiled beef slices and noodles in cold soybean soup are also popular.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6767;Samcheongdong Sujebi;South Korea;Seoul;101-1 Samcheong-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03049, South Korea;37.58449;126.89189;26;false;true;Sujebi;This local haunt has been an integral part of Samcheong-dong’s history since 1982. The signature dish here is sujebi — rustic hand-pulled dough soup served in a savory anchovy broth. The restaurant is also known for its potato pancakes, made with grated potatoes that are pan-fried until crispy on the outside and pleasantly chewy on the inside. Avoid the lunch rush if you don’t want to stand in line, but be warned — the restaurant is always busy.;Car park;[]
6768;Halmaejip;South Korea;Seoul;1-5 Sajik-ro 12-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03169, South Korea;37.57563;126.9714;76;true;false;Jokbal;The original matriarch who opened this restaurant is still the heart and soul of the kitchen which has been dishing up legendary pork backbone stew and boiled pig’s feet since 1975. Chili powder is the only spicy agent used to add the pleasant kick to the taste. It’s a common sight to see Mrs. Mun, walking around showing her patrons how to eat her food “the right way. ”;Shoes must be removed;[]
6769;Bao Haus;South Korea;Busan;2F, 62-9 Seojeon-ro 38 beon-gil, Busanjin-gu, Busan, 47294, South Korea;35.15488;129.06335;47;false;false;Taiwanese;When Chef Choi Haeng-rak opened Bao Haus here in his hometown of Busan, his extensive overseas training at last found a place to flourish. His restaurant offers simple and casual Taiwanese-style dishes. By lowering the threshold for fine cuisine, the chef ushers diners into the familiar yet exotic world of the different variations of Chinese cuisine. The menu features dishes loaded with inherent flavors and executed with Chef Choi’s novel twists, including bao (Taiwanese steamed buns), lu rou fan (Taiwanese braised pork rice bowl), mapo tofu, and deep-fried eggplant. Since the eatery is housed in a compact space, the wait can be long without a reservation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6771;Jungin Myeonok;South Korea;Seoul;10 Gukhoe-daero 76-gil, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul, 07238, South Korea;37.5307;126.92167;81;true;false;Naengmyeon;When a restaurant continues to attract large crowds of hungry diners, then it is doing something right. The proprietor of Jungin Myeonok has had just one goal since day one — to continue the legacy of his parents for as long as he can, using only the best ingredients. The establishment’s legendary Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles are based on a tightly guarded family recipe handed down to him by his parents, who both hail from North Korea. The room gets packed quickly during lunch service, especially during the warmer months.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6772;Shunsai Kubo;South Korea;Busan;17 Yangdal-ro 4 beon-gil, Buk-gu, Busan, 46517, South Korea;35.24088;129.01472;58;false;true;Unagi / Freshwater Eel, Japanese;Shunsai Kubo is a hitsumabushi (Nagoya-style grilled eel) restaurant helmed by Chef Lee Jae-wook. Trained in Japan, the chef is continually striving to raise the bar on the flavor and quality of his signature dish made only with live Japanese eels (Anguilla japonica). The rich aroma of the eels, rubbed with a special sauce and carefully grilled, creates a delightful gastronomic harmony with the rice cooked to just the right texture. The restaurant serves a hitsumabushi menu for children, a considerate gesture that caters to families. Shunsai Kubo also offers authentic light bar snacks for long-time regulars with fond memories of its former Japanese kappo cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6773;Buda Myeonoak;South Korea;Busan;2F, 36 Jungdong 1-ro, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48095, South Korea;35.16237;129.16298;71;true;false;Naengmyeon;For those familiar with Buda Milmyeon in Banyeo-dong, the name Buda Myeonoak may ring a bell. Relocated to the present location near Haeundae Beach in 2021, this noodle haven offers Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles made out of 100% buckwheat flour. Unexpectedly resilient, the pure noodles reveal additional nutty flavor with each bite. The broth, made from Korean beef and mixed with vegetable broth, is earthy and mild yet full of umami. When topped with your choice of garnishes that are served separately, such as sweet and sour radish, winter cabbage, and cucumber, the noodles are sensationally addictive.;;[]
6774;Tasty Cube;South Korea;Seoul;22-8 Yeonsei-ro 5da-gil, Seodaemun-gu, Seoul, 03789, South Korea;37.55665;126.93576;89;false;false;Noodles;A combination of Chinese characters for heart, meat, noodles and restaurant make up the four-syllable name Jeongyukmyeonche. The cozy space, which only offers bar seating facing the open kitchen, is the brainchild of a group of friends who wanted to launch an eatery that focuses on a wide array of noodle dishes. Although Chinese and Southeast Asian flavors dominate the menu at present, the owners say the plan is to eventually introduce noodle dishes from other cultures as well. Signature dishes include beef noodle soup and noodles dressed with zhi ma jiang, a savory paste made with crushed sesame seeds.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6777;One Degree North;South Korea;Seoul;8 Hakdong-ro 43-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06061, South Korea;37.516773;127.037424;27;false;false;Asian, Singaporean;As suggested by its name, which denotes Singapore’s geographical coordinate (one degree north in latitude), this establishment is dedicated to popular Singaporean dishes and Asian barbeque specialties. Singapore chicken rice and Cantonese crispy roast pork, are two traditional recipes enhanced by the young chef’s meticulous technical skills. These signature dishes bring popular Singaporean flavors alive in an authentic way, and exploring other cuisines in Seoul is always a fascinating gastronomic experience.;Air conditioning;[]
6778;Jeongmyeon;South Korea;Seoul;88 Neungdong-ro 13-gil, Gwangjin-gu, Seoul, 05012, South Korea;37.54551;127.06866;64;false;false;Noodles;A seven-seat stainless steel table and an open kitchen are all there is to Jeongmyeon, which means “noodles infused with meaning.” This one-chef operation serves noodle soups with meat. White noodle soup and red noodle soup are the only two dishes on the menu, but both offer deep flavor profiles. The broth, made with seafood, pork, and chicken, reveals a rich set of tastes. Garnishes topping the rice noodles, including thin slices of pleasantly chewy pork, onion, and red pepper, are truly a sight to behold. The red noodle soup, which can be made with varying levels of spiciness, is served with a bowl of rice for a filling meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6779;Jaha Son Mandu;South Korea;Seoul;12 Baekseokdong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03020, South Korea;37.59309;126.96603;39;true;true;Mandu;For over two decades, this restaurant has been attracting diners with a rustic dumpling recipe passed down from the owner’s mother and her grandmother. Although humble by nature, dumpling dishes are always elegantly presented. Their signature dish is mandutguk: plump pork, bean curd and vegetable dumplings nestled in a delicate beef broth, seasoned with homemade soy sauce. The main dining room offers a spectacular view of nearby Inwangsan Mountain.;Car park,Great view,Shoes must be removed,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
6780;Limbyungjoo Sandong Kalguksu;South Korea;Seoul;65 Gangnam-daero 37-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06734, South Korea;37.48458;127.02988;25;false;true;Kalguksu;Since 1988, this restaurant has been proving that a humble bowl of noodle soup can be truly memorable when done right. The pleasant texture of their hand-cut noodles, prepared daily from scratch, and immensely comforting broth, served piping hot and packed with flavor from the clams in all their naturally sweet glory, are stellar. Other favorites include Pyeongyang jumbo sized dumplings and noodles in cold soybean soup. Simple but warm service.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
6781;Gwanghwamun Gukbap;South Korea;Seoul;53 Sejong-daero 21-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04519, South Korea;37.5689;126.97541;69;true;false;Dwaeji-gukbap;The restaurant’s clean white signage says it all. Chef Park Chan-il’s dwaeji-gukbap or pork and rice soup looks and tastes unadulterated. Prepared simply by boiling black pork ham and Duroc pork shoulder cuts, the clear broth is fragrant and profoundly flavorful. Although ‘gukbap’ is commonly served with rice already mixed into the hot soup, Park serves the two separately, to preserve the taste of freshly steamed rice. The heaping of chopped chives added to the soup just before it is served renders the broth wonderfully aromatic.;Car park;[]
6782;Kyodaiya;South Korea;Seoul;39 Seongji-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04083, South Korea;37.54681;126.91317;97;false;false;Udon;When one can hear the dull tap of a blade against a wooden board every time a customer places an order, it’s a telltale sign that the chefs are serious about their craft. At Kyodaiya, that craft is Sanuki udon. The thick noodles are always cut to order to preserve their characteristic elasticity and smoothness until the very last minute. In addition to the classic kake udon, flavored with dried and smoked sardines and seasoned with light soy sauce, the chef brothers also offer classics like tempura udon and chilled bukkake udon.;Air conditioning;[]
6783;Hyun Udon;South Korea;Seoul;53 Nonhyeon-ro 149-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06039, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;47;true;false;Udon;Chef Park Sang-hyeon is a well-respected master of the udon craft. At his Nonhyeon-dong location, Park continues to serve up bowls of thick, silky-smooth, home-made udon noodles with their characteristic firmness and elasticity. If you're unsure of what to order, go for his signature tempura bukkake udon. The plump bouncy noodles and the freshly fried light crispy tempura make for a delicious mouthful when dipped in the umami-rich tsuyu sauce.;Counter dining;[]
6784;Tuk Tuk Noodle Thai;South Korea;Seoul;161-8 Seongmisan-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03980, South Korea;37.56514;126.92401;32;false;false;Thai;Authenticity is the name of the game at Tuk Tuk Noodle Thai, a collaborative effort between a local Korean owner and a native Thai chef to bring the real flavors of Thailand to Korea. The components that make up a typically Thai meal — the colors, textures, scents, flavors and the ambience — are present from start to end. If you want to feel the authentic taste and aroma of Thailand, try Thai sausages, or spicy and sour 'larb moo' – stir-fried minced pork. While you are tasting the dishes, the joy of your daily life will increase by a span.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
6785;Niurou mian guan zi;South Korea;Busan;25-4 Suyeong-ro 388 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48311, South Korea;35.14042;129.10832;59;true;true;Taiwanese;A long line under a yellow awning makes spotting this bustling Taiwanese eatery a breeze. Its streamlined menu features homely yet delectable dishes, including pleasantly spicy Taiwan-style braised beef noodle soup, wonton soup, Taiwanese cold noodles, spicy wonton in chili oil, and tripe in mala sauce. The signature braised beef noodle soup features large chunks of beef, bok choy, pickled leaf mustard, and some chili oil for a spicy twist. And a bowl of this particular soup will make you sweat even in the depths of winter. When paired with sweet-flavored mango beer, it’s a match made in heaven.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6786;Hwa Hae Dang;South Korea;Seoul;15 Gukhoe-daero 62-gil, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul, 07236, South Korea;37.52689;126.91706;51;true;true;Gejang;This is the first Seoul branch of the acclaimed Taean County restaurant, located on the west coast of Korea. The name of the restaurant, which translates into “Flower crab house” specializes in soy sauce marinated blue crab, prized for its sweet flesh. Each spring, when local crabs are in season, they are caught and flash frozen to be used throughout the year. The crabs are prepared in Taean and sent to Seoul. The seafood side dishes are also good.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6787;Damiok;South Korea;Busan;#103, 15 Bokji-ro, Busanjin-gu, Busan, 47328, South Korea;35.15186;129.02054;66;false;false;Naengmyeon;Quietly nestled in Gaegeum-dong, Damiok specializes in Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles. As its name suggests, the establishment focuses on presenting refreshingly light and clean flavors. The broth tastes pure and non-greasy, without unpleasant flavors, as it is made only from simmered beef, pork, and chicken. The noodles are housemade, and you have the added option of selecting 100 percent buckwheat noodles, which taste nuttier and may titillate more adventurous palates. In addition to the signature dish, Damiok offers beef bone soup and Pyeongyang-style beef hot pot.;Air conditioning;[]
6788;Yakitori Onjung;South Korea;Busan;9-7 Dongcheon-ro 108 beon-gil, Busanjin-Gu, Busan, 47247, South Korea;35.15866;129.06284;81;false;false;Yakitori;Onjung is a small yakitori bistro run by a couple, who opened their first restaurant here in Busan after acquiring culinary experience in Seoul. Though their yakitori is made with Korean native chicken, the meat is soft in texture as they use poultry appropriately sized for the dish. The brick-arched entrance and low-saturation lighting create a cozy ambiance that accentuates the flavors of this bistro’s wide selection of nihonshu (Japanese sake) and whisky. Why not come and indulge in a drink or two with yummy skewers of yakitori?;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6789;HORAPA;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 37-1 Jahamun-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03040, South Korea;37.57938;126.9711;39;true;false;Thai;A short trip to Thailand and a serendipitous encounter with a local cookbook changed the course of his life and set Son Seung-hee on the path to chefdom. Enamored with the world of Thai cuisine, he has since poured his passion into mastering it, and his culinary dedication has found its culmination in Horapa’s fare. The vibrant flavors of spices and herbs amid the wafting aroma of charcoal – this street vibe in Thailand, and the street foods he savored, serve as continued inspiration for the eatery’s exotic and exclusive dishes. Chef Son seeks to remain true to the heart and soul of Thai cuisine while maintaining unmistakable originality in his fare by capitalizing on locally produced fine seasonal ingredients. This culinary philosophy leaves us awaiting Korea’s novel take on Thai cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6790;Palmito;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;16 Western Road, Brighton and Hove, BN3 1AE, United Kingdom;50.8253742;-0.1568404;43;false;true;Asian, South American;The plates are small and the flavours are big at this wonderful little neighbourhood restaurant. The style of the food is described as ‘spice driven’ and draws on multiple global cuisines across the selection of affordable dishes. The décor is simple and understated, but the cooking is bold and interesting, with an appropriate degree of care taken in the kitchen. Kick your evening off with a colourful cocktail, and make sure to end it with a delicious dessert.;;[]
6792;St. JOHN Bread and Wine;United Kingdom;London;94-96 Commercial Street, Spitalfields, London, E1 6LZ, United Kingdom;51.5196914;-0.0743226;45;false;false;Traditional British;There is an appealingly stripped-back quality to both the food and the décor at this well-priced St. JOHN spin-off. The highly seasonal menu offers dishes that are perfect for sharing, and the cooking is as British, uncomplicated and hugely satisfying as you would expect – accompanied by suitably spartan surroundings. The brand’s nose-to-tail ethos is on show too, with options like roasted bone marrow and crispy pig’s cheek. Don’t leave without trying the baked to order madeleines.;Air conditioning;[]
6793;The Inn at Welland;United Kingdom;Welland;Hook Bank, Drake Street, Welland, WR13 6LN, United Kingdom;52.0599366;-2.2761856;36;true;true;Modern British;Take in delightful views of the Malvern Hills from the charming terrace of this country inn, or cosy up inside the understated New England-esque dining room. There's certainly a degree of style to the place, in both the décor and the attractive presentation of the dishes, which thankfully taste as good as they look, incorporating plenty of punchy flavours like pickled enoki or a rich red wine jus. There's a generosity to the portion sizes, especially in the starters – check out the specials board for some of the best value dishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6794;The Anchor;United Kingdom;Ripley;High Street, Ripley, GU23 6AE, United Kingdom;51.2997747;-0.4929328;77;false;false;Modern British;Taller diners may wish to duck their head as they enter this 400-year-old pub, its low beams a sign of the building’s characterful touches. Wood and stone floors add to the appeal, while modern furnishings blend in with the historic roots. The choice of menus offers something for everyone, from a tasting option to a good value lunch and an à la carte. Across them all is fresh seasonal produce cooked with care in unfussy preparations so the natural flavours shine through. If it’s on the menu, don’t miss ‘The Jaffa’ for dessert.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6796;The Galley;United Kingdom;Topsham;41 Fore Street, Topsham, EX3 0HU, United Kingdom;50.6816212;-3.4646891;17;true;true;Seafood;In the older part of this delightful town, by the edge of the River Exe, you'll find this cosy, rustic bistro that comes with a cheery atmosphere and sensible pricing. Seafood is the primary focus of the fixed-price menu, locally sourced and treated with real care by the chefs. In particular, there is real finesse shown in the use of bold flavours to skilfully enhance less luxurious ingredients, such as hake with cherry tomatoes or mackerel with wasabi and sea herbs. If you aren’t a local, this place will make you wish you were one.;Air conditioning;[]
6797;Hoppers;United Kingdom;London;49 Frith Street, Soho, London, W1D 4SG, United Kingdom;51.5136166;-0.1316524;81;true;false;South Indian, Sri Lankan;Street food inspired by Tamil Nadu and Sri Lanka features at this fun little spot from the Sethi family, who also own Trishna and Gymkhana. The 'hoppers' – bowl-shaped pancakes made from fermented rice and coconut – are ideal with a creamy kari. The ‘short eats’ and the prices are great too.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6798;pahli hill;United Kingdom;London;70-81 Mortimer Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1W 7SJ, United Kingdom;51.5176179;-0.1411106;52;true;false;Indian;This extremely colourful, comfortable restaurant in the heart of Fitzrovia is modelled on the communal living ‘building societies’ of Bombay, and comes with striking posters, a relaxed ambience and an intimate basement bar. The menu is divided into ‘small’ and ‘big’ plates and sharing is encouraged. Dishes are confidently executed, easy to eat and full of fresh, regionally inspired flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
6799;Root;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;Unit 9, Cargo 1, Gaol Ferry Steps, Wapping Wharf, City of Bristol, BS1 6WP, United Kingdom;51.4470817;-2.5993811;52;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This busy, welcoming little restaurant occupies five first floor shipping containers on the old wharf. Produce from small local suppliers is used in simple yet flavour-packed small plates formed around vegetables. They have a modern, sometimes intriguing style and inventive touches.;Terrace;[]
6800;tipo;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;110 Hanover Street, Edinburgh, EH2 1DR, United Kingdom;55.9544928;-3.1980674;23;false;true;Italian;Named after the fine Italian '00' flour that’s used for making pasta, this relaxed and comforting restaurant could quickly become your go-to in Edinburgh’s New Town. British, Mediterranean and Italian cuisines all influence the menu, which provides plenty of flavour and value for money. The small plates selection is mightily appealing, but it's the seriously good homemade pastas like bigoli cacio e pepe that most catch the eye.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6801;The Chequers;United Kingdom;Bath;50 Rivers Street, Bath, BA1 2QA, United Kingdom;51.3874851;-2.3649837;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Whether it's Orkney scallops or Wiltshire pheasant, there’s always an appealingly muscular quality to the cooking at this popular pub set in a smart residential street amid elegant Georgian terraces. You can choose between elaborate dishes with international flavours and touches of originality or those of a more traditional bent. Check out the blackboard specials, which could include prime rib to share, and don't miss the indulgent sticky toffee pudding if you get the chance.;Terrace;[]
6805;Ibérico World Tapas;United Kingdom;Nottingham;The Shire Hall, High Pavement, Nottingham, NG1 1HN, United Kingdom;52.9508467;-1.1441974;69;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Hidden in the basement of the old city law courts and jail is this friendly, long-standing restaurant which comes with a vaulted ceiling, colourful tiling and ornate fretwork. The menu is just as interesting, living up to its name with dishes that incorporate elements from yuzu to dukkah alongside the firmly Mediterranean base. Around four dishes per person is about right, with the 'gambas a la plancha' well worth an order. The ‘Express’ menu available on midweek early evenings represents great value.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6808;Skosh;United Kingdom;York;96-98 Micklegate, York, YO1 6JX, United Kingdom;53.9568532;-1.0894785;67;true;true;Modern British;This bright, lively restaurant is one of the hottest tickets in town, and it's easy to see why. Located just up the road from Micklegate Bar – a 12th-century gateway to the city – its name comes from the Japanese word meaning ‘small amount’, referencing the small plates format the menu adopts. Around 6 or 7 dishes is about right between two, with each one proving to be full of flavour and often taking influences from across Asia, like doenjang-glazed cod or pork belly vindaloo. There's a range of seating options, including up at the counter overlooking the open kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6809;Solas;Ireland;Dingle;Unit 1, Strand Street, Dingle, V92 FEF2, Ireland;52.1394271;-10.2740471;68;false;false;Spanish;Located in a charming seaside village, Solas is the home of a harmonious marriage between Irish produce and Spanish cooking. Larger-than-life Chef-Owner Nicky Foley’s travels in Spain inform the menu, which offers a range of dishes true to the Spanish originals whilst incorporating local ingredients and adding a few subtle twists. There’s a pleasing simplicity here, to both the good value food and the rustic décor, which combine well with the friendly, welcoming service.;;[]
6812;Bao;United Kingdom;London;53 Lexington Street, Soho, London, W1F 9AS, United Kingdom;51.5132537;-0.13654;84;false;true;Taiwanese;There are some things in life worth queueing for – and that includes the delicious buns here at this simple Taiwanese operation. It is a sweet and unpretentious place, helped along by service from a friendly young team. The classic bao and the confit pork bao are standouts, along with ‘small eats’ like fried chicken with hot sauce. They operate a number of other restaurants across London, including in King's Cross and Shoreditch.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6813;BOX-E;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;Unit 10, Cargo 1, Wapping Wharf, City of Bristol, BS1 6WP, United Kingdom;51.4468096;-2.5991738;52;false;false;Modern British;Wapping Wharf is home to Cargo, a retail yard made of converted shipping containers, and on the first floor is intimate BOX-E, a compact restaurant clad in chipboard and plywood. Cooking comes from the heart and dishes are rustic, assured and flavour-packed. The panna cotta is a must!;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6814;Twelve;United Kingdom;Thornton;Marsh Mill, Fleetwood Road North, Thornton, FY5 4JZ, United Kingdom;53.8748962;-3.0116422;65;true;false;Modern British;For over 20 years, this passionately run restaurant has continued to evolve and look to the future, without losing sight of the quality cooking that has made it such a hit for so long. Situated in the shadow of one of Europe's tallest working windmills, the building sports a unique style of décor that blends graffiti art with exposed brickwork, and the permanently busy cocktail bar is a key feature. The kitchen shows great skill in deriving plenty of flavour from deceptively simple dishes like hake with leek and basil broth.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6815;The Spärrows;United Kingdom;Manchester;16 Red Bank, Green Quarter, Manchester, M4 4HF, United Kingdom;53.4924759;-2.2368382;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Nestled under the railway arches in Manchester’s Green Quarter is this somewhat hidden restaurant where you have to ring a bell to enter. Its name is (almost) the English translation of the word ‘spätzle’ – which gives some clue as to the style of food on offer here. The dumplings and assorted pasta dishes are all made in-house and include excellent pierogi. The focus on Eastern Europe carries through to the wine list, which has a leaning towards Polish wines.;Wheelchair access;[]
6816;Bryn Williams at Porth Eirias;United Kingdom;Colwyn Bay;The Promenade, Colwyn Bay, LL29 8HH, United Kingdom;53.2953743;-3.7176795;16;true;true;Modern British;If you’re after a relaxed, friendly environment, this striking beachside brasserie with faux industrial styling, blue leather banquettes and stunning sea views is the place to come. The owner is proud of his Welsh roots and it shows on the menu. Cooking is pleasingly unfussy and local seafood is to the fore.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6818;Cornish Arms;United Kingdom;Tavistock;15 West Street, Tavistock, PL19 8AN, United Kingdom;50.5494467;-4.1473599;45;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A mix of locals and tourists, drinkers and diners, makes for a great atmosphere at this traditional high street pub. The knowledgeable team are genuinely warm and welcoming, and the appealing dishes mix classic elements with some unusual modern twists. Boldly decorated bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6819;Gunpowder Spitalfields;United Kingdom;London;11 White's Row, Spitalfields, London, E1 7NF, United Kingdom;51.5182811;-0.0747543;22;false;false;Indian;While there are now Gunpowders in multiple London locations, it's this small, sweetly run spot that started it all. Unassuming from the outside, it's a loud, buzzing place once you're in, sporting just 10 tightly packed tables – all filled with contented diners. The restaurant's name is a reference to the chef’s daily-made spice mix and his menu is influenced by old family recipes. Among the fresh and original small plates, which take inspiration from across the Indian regions, the Chettinad pulled duck is a stand-out.;Wheelchair access;[]
6820;Galvin Green Man;United Kingdom;Howe Street;Main Road, Howe Street, CM3 1BG, United Kingdom;51.8065495;0.458329;25;false;false;Traditional British, Mediterranean Cuisine;The Essex outpost of the Galvin empire is this big, busy pub, where there’s always something going on, from live music evenings to special events. The friendly team offer a warm welcome and the original 14th-century building provides all the rustic charm you’d expect, while a modern barn extension and a charming riverside garden complete the picture. The extensive menu offers an appealing mix of classic British and Mediterranean influenced dishes which are big on flavour, and the 'Bib Gourmand' menu is a steal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6821;Cin Cin;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;60 Western Road, Brighton and Hove, BN3 1JD, United Kingdom;50.8261338;-0.1617268;33;true;true;Italian;Cin Cin’s loyal band of customers come for its great value Italian food, where fresh ingredients are simply cooked and natural flavours are allowed to shine. You can create a different experience every time you visit by sitting in a different place: in front of the open kitchen, at the horseshoe counter, gazing out the window onto the street or in the calmer rear room. Wherever you choose, the terrific homemade pasta is a must – look out for the daily special on the blackboard. An all-Italian wine list completes the picture.;Counter dining;[]
6822;Charlton Arms;United Kingdom;Ludlow;Ludford Bridge, Ludlow, SY8 1PJ, United Kingdom;52.363659;-2.7172663;17;true;true;Traditional British;A number of terraces offer lovely waterside views at this substantial pub on the banks of the River Teme. The cooking is a mixture of British and French classical recipes, with traditional and appealing options like fish & chips, fish soup and confit duck leg. These straightforward, well-priced dishes don’t disappoint and pack in plenty of flavour. Be sure to hang around for dessert, where a sticky toffee pudding is hard to resist. There are cosy bedrooms upstairs and the location is great for exploring nearby Ludlow.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6823;Haveli;United Kingdom;Ponteland;3-5 Broadway, Darras Hall, Ponteland, NE20 9PW, United Kingdom;55.0360669;-1.7645118;41;false;true;Indian;Satisfying Indian dishes at eye-catchingly affordable prices is the name of the game at this smart spot in an outer Newcastle suburb. Flashes of colour bring a liveliness to the modern interior, where elements of Indian décor are subtly incorporated in place of a full-blown 'curry house' approach. Influences come from all over India, but the north does take precedence on the menu. The chef's signature curries are well worth an order, like the 'jhinga moilley', which combines succulent prawns with a velvety, deftly balanced coconut and ginger sauce.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6824;Broad Chare;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;25 Broad Chare, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE1 3DQ, United Kingdom;54.9699036;-1.6046544;52;true;false;Traditional British;This much-loved 'proper' pub is named after the lane it sits on, in the most historic part of the city. Housed within a converted warehouse by the quay, the operation is split between the cosy ground-floor bar – serving snacks and over 50 different beers – and the rustic upstairs dining room. Here, the kitchen produces a consistently high quality offering of hearty, punchily flavoured dishes like haggis on toast and grilled calves liver with bacon, sage and crispy onions. Fair prices and a friendly team add to the appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
6825;Kilberry Inn;United Kingdom;Kilberry;Kilberry, PA29 6YD, United Kingdom;55.8194385;-5.6501159;93;false;true;Scottish, Modern British;Situated in a magical, highly remote location on Scotland's east coast, this roadside inn is a welcoming place from the moment you enter, with the team exuding a genuine warmth and hospitality. Choose between the "Chef's Menu" and the great value "Bib Gourmand Menu", both of which display the chefs' pride in their local produce, including plenty from the nearby Kilberry Estate. The cooking is classic at its core, avoiding unnecessary gimmicks in favour of honest, satisfying dishes. Stay overnight to see more of the beautiful surroundings.;Car park;[]
6826;Rick Stein's Café;United Kingdom;Padstow;10 Middle Street, Padstow, PL28 8AP, United Kingdom;50.5413741;-4.939904;60;false;false;Seafood, Asian Influences;It may look like a small terraced house from the outside, but this relaxed and popular part of the Rick Stein stable is a surprisingly spacious, nautically themed bistro with bright Cornish artwork on the walls and a compact enclosed terrace to the rear. The concise menu is largely inspired by Rick's travels around various parts of Asia combined with, of course, Cornish seafood. So you can expect the likes of Thai fishcakes, grilled miso salmon and Pondicherry cod curry. The service is cheery, while simply furnished yet comfortable bedrooms are available.;Terrace;[]
6827;Duncombe Arms;United Kingdom;Ellastone;Main Road, Ellastone, DE6 2GZ, United Kingdom;52.9862494;-1.8261734;16;true;false;Modern British;Owners Johnny and Laura Greenall were sad to see the hub of their local village shut its doors, so in 2012 they bought it, smartened it up and reopened it as a stylish dining pub – and it’s been a hit ever since. It’s an attractive place with a delightful terrace and a neighbouring red-brick barn which houses luxurious bedrooms that look out over the fields. The gutsy, keenly priced cooking routinely shows the kitchen's deft skills, from the subtle spicing of a café de Paris butter to the luscious filling of a classic custard tart.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6831;Provender;United Kingdom;London;17 High Street, Redbridge, London, E11 2AA, United Kingdom;51.5799878;0.0236499;76;false;true;French;‘A little piece of France in Wanstead’ is the tagline at this busy and welcoming neighbourhood bistro – and they certainly deliver it. The extensive menu is a roll-call of classic French dishes from escargots and soupe à l’oignon to coq au vin and steak frites. They prove to be well-cooked too, providing satisfying flavours at fair prices. A startlingly good value prix fixe is available throughout the day Tuesday to Thursday and for lunch only on Friday and Saturday.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6833;Padella;United Kingdom;London;6 Southwark Street, Borough Market, London, SE1 1TQ, United Kingdom;51.505121;-0.0898596;100;true;false;Italian;It's not hard to see why this perennially popular pasta spot is so busy. The chefs make their pasta fresh every morning ready for a new wave of hungry customers to enjoy, then cook it with admirable precision and add a range of mouth-watering accompaniments – whether that be cavolo nero with the the cavatelli or regional specialities like a delicious Tuscan gorgonzola sauce with stacci. Don't forget the equally impressive tarts for dessert, too. Arrive in plenty of time to scan the QR code and join the virtual queue, then have a wander round the neighbouring Borough Market.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6834;Westerns Laundry;United Kingdom;London;34 Drayton Park, Holloway, London, N5 1PB, United Kingdom;51.551702;-0.1075123;85;false;false;Modern British;There is a whole lot to enjoy from the daily blackboard menus at this relaxed, understated operation. Both the décor and the cooking have a rustic edge to them, with the latter British-based, seafood-centric and guided by the seasons. Both individual and communal seating are available to enjoy the flavoursome dishes from, as is the kitchen counter, while the attentive team deal well with the buzz of a permanently busy restaurant. Quality sourdough is provided by their sister operation Jolene and while other dishes may come and go, the rum baba remains a constant.;Wheelchair access;[]
6836;The Barbary;United Kingdom;London;16 Neal’s Yard, Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9DP, United Kingdom;51.51455;-0.12632;96;false;true;North African, Mediterranean Cuisine;The fire-centric cooking of our ancestors provides much of the inspiration for this moody yet charming restaurant tucked away in Neal's Yard. All guests cosy up at the zinc-topped counter, gathered round a robata grill and a tandoor clay oven. The smoky treatment is given to ingredients from octopus to cauliflower, while the accompanying flavours are influenced, unsurprisingly, by the former Barbary Coast – so expect the likes of dukkah, harissa and zhoug to make an appearance during your visit. The counter seats just 24, but the compact layout adds to the atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6837;Higher Ground;United Kingdom;Manchester;Faulkner House, New York Street, Manchester, M1 4DY, United Kingdom;53.4795664;-2.2383081;19;true;true;Modern British;What started life as a pop-up in 2020 is now a permanent spot in the heart of the city, owned and run by three friends who also operate wine bar Flawd and a market garden in the Cheshire countryside. The latter provides much of the top quality produce found on the menu, in dishes that are designed for sharing and packed with flavour. Sit at the large counter to see the chefs putting care and pride into every dish, like the terrific malted barley pudding with stout caramel. The whole team, led by the owners, are charming and cheery.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
6839;Home;United Kingdom;Belfast;22 Wellington Place, Belfast, BT1 6GE, United Kingdom;54.5970378;-5.9330515;38;true;false;Traditional British, Mediterranean Cuisine;Bright colours, greenery and local art decorate this spacious, upbeat restaurant. The cooking focuses on semi-rustic versions of British and Mediterranean dishes like celeriac soup or salt and pepper prawns, with good vegan and gluten-free options too, and each plate is packed full of punchy flavours thanks to the quality produce at its core. The friendly team make the whole experience enjoyable, from the warm welcome to the fond farewell.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6840;Blaise Inn;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;260 Henbury Road, City of Bristol, BS10 7QR, United Kingdom;51.5070257;-2.6324229;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the suburbs, close to the famous folly of Blaise Castle, this simply decorated village inn serves good value, traditional British dishes cooked with a skilful, modern approach – make sure you save room for dessert! As well as quality ales and a well-chosen wine list, you'll find a pleasant rear courtyard in which to enjoy them. Personable service completes the picture.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6841;Queen of Cups;United Kingdom;Glastonbury;10-12 Northload Street, Glastonbury, BA6 9JJ, United Kingdom;51.1478135;-2.7186007;67;true;true;Middle Eastern, Mediterranean Cuisine;This deliciously different restaurant sits within a rustic 17C inn in the heart of Glastonbury, and comes with numerous seating areas, including a cosy courtyard for sunny days. Menus showcase West Country produce and the resulting Middle Eastern and Mediterranean small plates burst with colour and flavour. Grab a friend, go for the chef’s selection entitled the ‘Queen’s Feast’ and accompany it with the ‘sharing ciders’.;Terrace;[]
6842;Brutto;United Kingdom;London;35-37 Greenhill Rents, Clerkenwell, London, EC1M 6BN, United Kingdom;51.5198579;-0.1024475;41;true;true;Italian;You can’t help but have a great time at this wonderfully relaxed trattoria. With its gingham tablecloths and walls filled with a jumble of pictures, it's rather like stepping into nonna's house for a couple of hours. The place is perennially packed and it's easy to see why, with a terrific atmosphere accompanying the hearty, meat-centric dishes that never skimp on flavour, whether it's the dough ball ‘cuddles’ or the pork and fennel sausages. The signature negroni is as terrifically well-priced as the food.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6843;Burnt Orange;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;59 Middle Street, Brighton and Hove, BN1 1AL, United Kingdom;50.8215837;-0.142865;98;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Hidden away within Brighton's famous Lanes, it's easy to miss this fun, relaxed spot. That would be a great shame, as it's a terrific place with retro music on the speakers and cocktails flying out from behind the bar. The menu slots in perfectly with the culinary trends of the times, offering a selection of sharing plates based on produce cooked over a wood-burning fire. Look out for the Middle Eastern and North African influences, whether it's zhug with grilled prawns or sumac with BBQ chicken thighs.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6844;Saint Francis Provisions;Ireland;Kinsale;Short Quay, Kinsale, P17 T880, Ireland;51.7055457;-8.5229311;60;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This endearing, laid-back restaurant holds just 13 seats inside, with a heated terrace out front. The concise, daily changing menu offers a range of Mediterranean-inspired small plates created from the best local ingredients. Dishes are delivered from the open kitchen as and when they are ready, and offer punchy flavours and an appealing simplicity. An all natural wine list completes the picture.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6846;Spitalfields;Ireland;Dublin City;25 The Coombe, Dublin City, D08 YV07, Ireland;53.3397366;-6.2757384;74;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Set in a historic area of this city is this fittingly traditional-looking Irish pub, where the charming staff offer a warm and friendly welcome. It’s deservedly busy – drinkers are welcome but most are here for the food. Enticing dishes are fresh, flavoursome and great value, with the likes of oxtail and bone marrow Parker House rolls.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
6847;Table Forty One;Ireland;Gorey;41 Main Street, Gorey, Y25 E1X7, Ireland;52.6755088;-6.2955387;20;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Having worked in various hotels and restaurants around the world, Gorey native Andrew Duncan returned home to open this friendly restaurant situated in the busy town centre. Diners are spread across two rooms, both boasting a wonderfully cosy vibe and welcoming atmosphere. There’s a generosity to the cooking, both in portion size and price, with good produce from County Wexford underpinning the menu – desserts are a strength of the kitchen too.;;[]
6848;Evernight;United Kingdom;London;Unit 1A, 3 Ravine Way Embassy Gardens, Wandsworth, London, SW11 7BH, United Kingdom;51.4818761;-0.130728;29;true;true;Japanese, Izakaya;The traditional Japanese izakaya has found a home in the London dining scene, thanks to this trendy modern take on the concept. The chic, minimalist setting provides a good backdrop for imaginative dishes that combine British produce with Japanese techniques, like British beef used in the short rib donabe to share. The original streak extends to the desserts, where the approach is somewhat reversed by traditional western dishes such as tarte Tatin and English trifle being reimagined with Japanese flavours like miso, shiso and sake.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
6850;EDŌ;United Kingdom;Belfast;3 Capital House, Unit 2, Upper Queen Street, Belfast, BT1 6FB, United Kingdom;54.5969099;-5.9333947;71;true;false;European Contemporary;‘I eat’ is a smart, buzzing and well-run brasserie in the heart of the city, with rustic-meets-faux-industrial styling and seats at the long kitchen counter for those who want to get in on the action. The great value sharing dishes take an international outlook, with traditional Spanish tapas getting a good showing – from pan con tomate to pil pil prawns – and the Bertha oven used for dishes like hanger steak with chimichurri. Don't over-order, as you'll need to save room for the terrific orange, almond and olive oil sponge.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6851;Dill;United Kingdom;Lewes;2 South Street, Lewes, BN7 2BP, United Kingdom;50.8743773;0.0191946;27;false;true;Innovative;There’s plenty of originality on offer in the selection of small plates at this simple yet admirably inventive bistro. The menu adopts a global approach and wide-ranging influences, but nothing feels borrowed or copied from elsewhere with such uniquely put-together dishes. A rustic interior and quirkily-shaped dining room combine with the blackboard menus to give the place an intimate, welcoming feel, that is only enhanced by the knowledgeable and personable service team.;Terrace;[]
6852;Emilia;United Kingdom;Ashburton;2  East Street, Ashburton, TQ13 7AA, United Kingdom;50.5154368;-3.7560547;56;false;true;Italian;The northern Italian region of Emilia-Romagna provides the inspiration behind this classic osteria set within a former bank in the centre of town. The daily changing menu is chalked on the door of the old vault, which now houses the wines, and from the tiny kitchen comes forth flavoursome and generously priced dishes that you feel are doing you good. There’s a daily offal dish and the pasta is made in-house.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
6853;Provender;United Kingdom;Melrose;West End House, High Street, Melrose, TD6 9RU, United Kingdom;55.598304;-2.7225173;57;false;true;Modern British;Melrose is certainly one of the more attractive Borders towns and Provender has become a part of its fabric now. Situated down a passageway just off the main street, it's a versatile place – offering everything from mid-morning eggs Benedict to a celebratory dinner kicked off with Cumbrae oysters. Binding it all together is great use of ingredients from the local estates and producers, be it fish from the North Sea or crab caught off the coast at Eyemouth. The set lunch menu offers good value for money.;Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
6855;Hitchen's Barn;United Kingdom;Oakham;12 Burley Road, Oakham, LE15 6DH, United Kingdom;52.670097;-0.7262041;54;true;true;Modern British;Neil and Louise Hitchen have been working in restaurants around the world together for 20 years, with their latest venture set inside this pretty stone barn. There’s a rustic quality to the décor, which pairs nicely with the lovely warm welcome given by natural host Louise and her bright young team. Neil heads up the kitchen, producing good value, seasonal dishes that are so appealing you might struggle to choose – go for the Cornish turbot on the bone and you won’t be disappointed. The wine list is as well-priced as the food.;;[]
6856;Sardine Factory;United Kingdom;Looe;Quay Road, West Looe, Looe, PL13 2BX, United Kingdom;50.3523883;-4.4549325;32;false;true;Seafood;A converted sardine factory on the quayside plays host to this laid-back and admirably well-run first floor restaurant which affords views across the harbour to East Looe. The extensive menu champions Cornish seafood across a range of tasty, well-priced dishes that have been prepared with evident care. The cooking is appealingly straightforward, with popular fish and shellfish dishes like moules marinière and crab linguine on the menu. Don't forget to try the fabulous sardines too, of course!;Wheelchair access;[]
6857;Beckford Bottle Shop;United Kingdom;Bath;5-8 Saville Row, Bath, BA1 2QP, United Kingdom;51.3865028;-2.3621436;63;true;false;Modern British;In a great location at the top end of the city, this characterful spot combines the relaxed vibe of a wine bar with the great value cooking of a bistro. Tasty, carefully prepared small plates, like Bath chaps with Bramley apple, are served by a cheerful and helpful team. The wine list offers plenty of choice, but you can also choose a bottle from their shop next door and pay corkage to enjoy it while dining. Beckford Canteen, their sister operation, is just up the road and caters for a range of diners with an enticing all-day menu.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6858;Ka Pao;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;Botanic Gardens Garage, 26 Vinicombe Street, Glasgow City, G12 8BE, United Kingdom;55.8771492;-4.2903888;16;false;true;Asian;A few streets from the Botanical Gardens is this fun, buzzy basement restaurant situated in a former garage dating back to the 1900s. Sister to Ox and Finch, it has a similar ethos of laid-back dining and affordable pricing, but here the cooking comes with a distinctly Southeast Asian flavour. The colourful sharing plates range from corn ribs to penang curry, blending sweet and spicy elements with great skill. Another branch is located in Edinburgh’s St James Quarter.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6859;The Clifton;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;16 Regent Street, City of Bristol, BS8 4HG, United Kingdom;51.4539431;-2.617977;51;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The trendy suburb of Clifton is home to this rustic, aptly named pub from the team behind the Hare & Hounds in Aberthin, who've crossed the border to bring the same brand of unpretentious, locally inspired cooking to England. The menu includes both small plates and larger sharing options – like braised short rib or Cull Yaw shepherd’s pie – which are generous in both size and flavour. Well-priced wines and local ales are on hand for extra refreshment, and midweek sees a particularly good value lunch menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6860;La Gordita;Ireland;Dublin City;6 Montague Street, Dublin City, D02 XE65, Ireland;53.3365439;-6.2646686;56;true;false;Spanish;There’s a simple, cosy quality to La Gordita thanks to its narrow dining room with a wooden floor, brown leather upholstery and soft lighting. It’s got a lively atmosphere too, a great accompaniment to the authentic Spanish sharing plates that pack in plenty of flavour – the terrific anchoas de Santoña is a real stand-out dish. Friendly service enhances the experience, and the extensive menu lets you sample as much as possible thanks to the sensible pricing.;Counter dining;[]
6861;Empire Empire;United Kingdom;London;16 All Saints Road, Notting Hill, London, W11 1HH, United Kingdom;51.5180143;-0.2036855;93;true;false;Indian;From the people behind the Gunpowder restaurants comes this neighbourhood spot specialising in cuisines from across Punjab and Northwest India. Expect plenty of biryani and kebabs on a menu that’s so appealing, the hardest decision is choosing what not to order. If you're stuck, the butter chicken is a house speciality and you'd be a fool to overlook the terrific 'King Prawns Kadhai Masala' – a prime demonstration of the kitchen's skill with flavours. There is a loose disco theme and a cool vintage vibe, thanks largely to the fantastic jukebox and a photo booth.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
6862;Marmo;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;31 Baldwin Street, City of Bristol, BS1 1RG, United Kingdom;51.4535493;-2.5943617;23;true;true;Italian;The former Guardian Assurance Building makes a charming spot for a restaurant, thanks to its characterful interiors with high ceilings, parquet flooring and panelled walls. The rustic look is a perfect fit for this osteria-cum-wine-bar, where the concise menu of classic Italian dishes adheres to the old adage that 'less is more' – straightforward options like hand-rolled strozzapreti with wild boar ragu deliver bags of flavour with just a few ingredients. If you needed more reasons to visit, the service is confident and personable, and it all comes with an appealing price tag.;Air conditioning;[]
6863;Primeur;United Kingdom;London;116 Petherton Road, Canonbury, London, N5 2RT, United Kingdom;51.5543915;-0.0900885;38;true;true;Modern British;There's something so appealing about the simplicity of a restaurant like Primeur. A proper neighbourhood operation, it comes with stripped-back décor, a handwritten blackboard menu and a relaxed, bustling atmosphere. Diners can sit around large communal tables or up at the counters around the edges. The cooking, for its part, avoids overcomplication and puts the ingredients first, complemented by a range of European-inspired elements from an Italian tonnato sauce to a French beurre rouge.;Counter dining;[]
6866;Plaquemine Lock;United Kingdom;London;139 Graham Street, Islington, London, N1 8LB, United Kingdom;51.5326532;-0.1004633;92;false;true;Creole, Cajun;A unique and very colourful pub named after a small city in Louisiana and with a menu centred around Creole and Cajun traditions. Dishes like gumbo with okra, blackened chicken, and crawfish with corn and potatoes are carefully cooked and packed with flavour. Big Easy style cocktails add to the fun.;;[]
6867;Yr Hen Printworks;United Kingdom;Cardigan;Carrier's Lane, Cardigan, SA43 1FA, United Kingdom;52.0821267;-4.659609;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A real gem of a property with bucketloads of history, this restaurant's premises has had former lives as a stone chapel and, as the name suggests, a printworks for a local paper. Today the lovingly restored building has a fresh, modern feel and is the setting for seasonally influenced small plates that sometimes feature meat from the owners' family farm. Be sure to choose the cod when available, especially if served with the fabulous romesco sauce. Their strapline is ‘Drink, Dine, Unwind’ and you can easily do all three without breaking the bank.;Air conditioning;[]
6868;The Green;United Kingdom;Sherborne;3 The Green, Sherborne, DT9 3HY, United Kingdom;50.9502139;-2.5174638;67;false;false;Modern British;A pretty, listed stone property with an enclosed garden terrace, this restaurant is a perfect fit for the picturesque market town of Sherborne. The charming interior features antique furniture, fresh flowers on every table and regularly changing artwork. Dishes are based on tried-and-tested combinations, with desserts like crème d'amande tart being a highlight. The friendly, caring team run the restaurant with pride and a smile.;Terrace;[]
6870;Kushi-Ya;United Kingdom;Nottingham;14a Low Pavement, Nottingham, NG1 7DL, United Kingdom;52.95137;-1.14779;63;false;true;Japanese;Head through the arch of Enfield Chambers and you'll be transported to this uber-cool setting. The Japanese cooking revolves around small plates and skewers, cooked over a charcoal grill with consummate skill. Bright, authentic and generous, each dish is a joy to eat and sensibly priced too. If you're coming for lunch, get here early as they don't take bookings and the lunchtime offer is phenomenally good value. Efficient service, a dynamic atmosphere and a courtyard terrace all add to the already considerable appeal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6873;Richmond;Ireland;Dublin City;43 Richmond Street South, Dublin City, D02 X499, Ireland;53.3311904;-6.2647003;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The owner and his team bend over backwards to make sure you have a great time at this welcomingly worn, rustic shop conversion just outside the city centre. Skilfully prepared, traditionally based dishes are robust yet refined and allow each core seasonal ingredient to shine.;;[]
6875;Noto;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;47a Thistle Street, Edinburgh, EH2 1DY, United Kingdom;55.9540219;-3.1993193;18;true;false;Asian Influences, Modern Cuisine;Following the success of aizle, Stuart Ralston took inspiration for his next restaurant from time spent in New York, naming this small plates spot after his NYC roommate, Bob Noto. It’s been a hit ever since, offering well-conceived dishes at sensible prices that are ideal for sharing. The culinary influences span the globe, with a particular focus on a range of Asian cuisines, be that through duck bao buns or a luscious chocolate and miso dessert.;Counter dining;[]
6876;Sculthorpe Mill;United Kingdom;Sculthorpe;Lynn Road, Sculthorpe, NR21 9QG, United Kingdom;52.83726;0.80844;19;true;false;Modern British;Dating all the way back to 1757, this striking former mill looks like it's been taken off the front of a Norfolk picture postcard. Lovingly restored by sisters Siobhan and Caitriona Peyton, it's now a chic dining pub with contemporary bedrooms and a riverside terrace. The cooking doesn't reinvent the wheel, but instead offers well-judged, flavoursome dishes like green gazpacho with Cromer crab. Ensure you save some room for dessert, especially if the terrific Norfolk pear and hazelnut tart is on the menu.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6878;Root Wells;United Kingdom;Wells;12 Sadler Street, Wells, BA5 2SE, United Kingdom;51.2096222;-2.6460622;39;true;false;Vegetarian, Modern Cuisine;The views of Wells Cathedral alone are enough to attract anyone here, but add in an appealing veg-led menu of small plates, great prices and eager-to-please service, and you have a restaurant we’d all like to have on our doorstep. The chefs let the ingredients shine, showing just what wonderful flavours humble vegetables can achieve. While you decide what to order, ask for the fried cheese choux puffs – a smooth, utterly delicious treat.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6879;Sargasso;United Kingdom;Margate;Unit 13, Harbour Arm, Stone Pier, Margate, CT9 1AP, United Kingdom;51.3913176;1.3794152;30;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed inside a former boat shed on the harbour wall, Sargasso really does have the perfect seaside location. Watch the tide come in as you sit back and enjoy the seasonally changing menu, which – just like sister restaurant Brawn in London – puts quality produce front and centre. In this case, that means a bounty of delicious fresh seafood, packing ample flavour into each smartly pared-back dish. The menu is designed for sharing, allowing you to try as much as possible, while the wine list leans towards natural and biodynamic options.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6880;Thyme;Ireland;Athlone;Custume Place, Strand Street, Athlone, N37F1W4, Ireland;53.4236062;-7.9403616;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The chef-owner here is one who’s constantly reinvesting in his beloved restaurant and is always on the search for great new local suppliers – whether that’s fresh vegetables or free-range pork – and the pride he has in his establishment is palpable. The two menus showcase the locality well, with dishes that are satisfying and flavoursome. Do try the cheeses, which are accompanied by homemade crackers made using grains from the brewery next door.;Air conditioning;[]
6882;Uno Mas;Ireland;Dublin City;6 Aungier Street, Dublin City, D02 WN47, Ireland;53.3411166;-6.2653266;21;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The best seats in the house are at the counter in this buzzing, good value restaurant run by enthusiastic, personable staff. Start with some Spanish-inspired nibbles from the ‘para picar’ section before choosing one of the well-executed, unfussy main dishes which come with many layers of flavour and texture. A dedicated sherry list and a vermouth-based cocktail selection offer appealing additions to your visit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
6883;The Reindeer;United Kingdom;Hoveringham;Main Street, Hoveringham, NG14 7JR, United Kingdom;53.0142399;-0.9591836;79;false;false;Traditional British;You’ll find this friendly village pub tucked away down a narrow country lane. After undergoing a major revamp, it's become a bright and modern space, but still with a culinary focus on traditional pub favourites. Unfussy, classic dishes like bangers and mash - along with daily specials - are cooked with great care and using quality ingredients, resulting in appealing, flavourful food. Charming service and a prime view of the local cricket pitch help make a visit here even more enjoyable.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6884;The Scran & Scallie;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;1 Comely Bank Road, Stockbridge, Edinburgh, EH4 1DT, United Kingdom;55.9591825;-3.2146265;41;false;true;Scottish, Traditional Cuisine;Comfort food abounds at this relaxed operation from the Tom Kitchin stable, which positions itself as a real neighbourhood pub, but one that also happens to serve great tasting food. As this is one of the busiest eateries in Edinburgh, you need to make sure to book if you’re to indulge in the hearty joys of steak pie, fish & chips or haggis, neeps & tatties. Leave room for dessert too, as the sweet-toothed are well looked after here.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6885;Ox and Finch;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;920 Sauchiehall Street, Glasgow City, G3 7TF, United Kingdom;55.8657546;-4.2847345;58;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Run like a well-oiled machine, this is a hugely likeable bistro with a rustic edge thanks to its tile-backed open kitchen and wines displayed in a huge metal cage. The Mediterranean dishes are big enough for sharing and showcase skilful use of simple ingredients, with the flavours really shining through. The appeal of the cooking is enhanced by its fantastic value for money, with delicious dishes like tubetti with brown butter, peas and guanciale an absolute steal.This restaurant is temporarily closed for refurbishment and will reopen in February 2025.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6886;Palomar;United Kingdom;London;34 Rupert Street, Soho, London, W1D 6DN, United Kingdom;51.511258;-0.132765;93;true;false;Middle Eastern;The flavours of Jerusalem have found a home in the heart of London’s theatreland, thanks to this stylish and deservedly popular restaurant. A zinc kitchen counter runs back to an intimate, wood-panelled dining room, which is filled with an almighty bustle. Like the atmosphere, the cooking is inviting and invigorating, with the good value dishes including fabulous fresh breads, superior dips and a range of produce cooked over fire.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
6889;Touring Club;United Kingdom;Penarth;4 Washington Buildings, Stanwell Road, Penarth, CF64 2AD, United Kingdom;51.43687;-3.1734;85;true;true;Modern British;Inspired by a restaurant in Patagonia, this slick spot is a great place to while away the hours with a few drinks and accomplished small plates. The relaxed surroundings offer multiple areas to dine in, including a terrace and a kitchen counter bedecked with beautiful blue tiles. The menu ranges from snacks to the more substantial, with the unfussy approach resulting in simple, fresh-tasting dishes like crab on toast. Add in the friendly service and you’ll leave with a smile on your face – just ensure you get here on time as they don’t take bookings.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6890;Lottie's;Ireland;Dublin City;7-9 Rathgar Road, Rathmines, Dublin City, D06 R971, Ireland;53.321629;-6.2669518;18;true;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s a terrific buzz in the air at this stylish brasserie-style restaurant, where the unfussy cooking is a fine accompaniment to the lively surroundings. Irish produce is the bedrock of the menu, in hearty, flavour-packed dishes like Andarl Farm pork chop with cabbage & violet mustard, parsnip and a cider jus. The early evening menu is a steal and an extensive choice of cocktails are on hand to kick things off.;Counter dining;[]
6891;Flint House;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;13 Hanningtons Lane, Brighton and Hove, BN1 1GS, United Kingdom;50.8222444;-0.1399223;80;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Brighton’s famous Lanes district plays host to this fashionable brasserie hidden inside a red-brick and flint-stone house that was one home to the city's renowned Hannington's department store. Enjoy a drink on the terrace of the first-floor cocktail bar, then head down to the buzzy main room dominated by an open kitchen and a stainless-steel counter. There's something for everyone among the colourful small plates that take on global influences and burst with freshness and flavour. Many of the good value wines are also offered by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6892;Kudu;United Kingdom;London;119 Queen's Road, Peckham, London, SE15 2EZ, United Kingdom;51.4738574;-0.0594382;42;false;false;South African;You'll receive a wonderful welcome at this enormously appealing neighbourhood restaurant where a room-full of contented diners fill the air with a vibrant energy. Start with the mouth-watering Kudu bread with bacon butter, then choose from the sharing-style menu with a South African influence most notable in the braai dishes and delicious homemade biltong. Across the board, well-sourced ingredients are crafted into hugely satisfying dishes boasting flavours that are bold and harmonious in equal measure. The fully South African wine list is well-explained by a knowledgeable team.;Brunch,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
6893;The Three Horseshoes;United Kingdom;Fordham;74 Church Road, Fordham, CO6 3NJ, United Kingdom;51.9182374;0.8020003;94;true;true;Modern British;From the wooden beams to the antique furniture, there’s a huge amount of character to this spacious pub that sits inside four former cottages. The welcoming feel of the inglenook fireplace is matched by the warmth and pride of the service team as they serve a selection of modern British dishes mixed with a few pub classics. Great care in the cooking allows strong, complementary flavours to shine through. On a summer’s day, make sure you head straight for the terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6895;Pichet;Ireland;Dublin City;14-15 Trinity Street, Dublin City, D02 T998, Ireland;53.3438552;-6.2622465;86;false;false;French;You can’t miss the neon red signs and striped canopies of this buzzy brasserie – and its checkerboard flooring makes the inside equally striking. Sit in one of two rooms, soaking up the buzz of either the bar or the kitchen as you enjoy a menu rooted in French classics. The likes of tartare, pithivier and tarte Tatin might well appear, despite the odd foray further afield and a commitment to Irish produce throughout. The wine list stretches well beyond France’s borders, with many wines available to order by the glass or, more appropriately, by the pichet.;Air conditioning;[]
6897;Plaza Khao Gaeng;United Kingdom;London;Arcade Food Hall, 103-105 New Oxford Street, Bloomsbury, London, WC1A 1DB, United Kingdom;51.516414;-0.1290631;56;true;true;Thai;With an open kitchen and electric pop blaring, there's a buzzy, vintage vibe at this relaxed, homely spot in the Arcade Food Hall. Chef Luke Farrell grows many of the Southeast Asian ingredients in a tropical greenhouse in Dorset, which are then deftly used to create wonderfully authentic, punchy Southern Thai curries. Start with Miang Phuket (coconut and betel leaf wraps), then go for a curry – perhaps a hearty Massaman (beef shoulder) – or, if you're feeling adventurous, the fiery Khua Kling Muu (dry wok fried pork).;Air conditioning;[]
6898;Cush;Ireland;Ballycotton;by the Pier, Ballycotton, P25 FY94, Ireland;51.8268501;-8.0019275;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;Family owned and run, Cush is a cosy, traditional pub with a smart, modern restaurant, comfy bedrooms and views out over the rooftops to the fishing boats in the harbour. Local produce features in hearty dishes, with seafood naturally to the fore, and guests are well looked after by the friendly team. A set menu is available in the pub area, with an à la carte and tasting menu on offer in the restaurant.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6899;The Loch & The Tyne;United Kingdom;Old Windsor;10 Crimp Hill, Old Windsor, SL4 2QY, United Kingdom;51.4567787;-0.5910703;64;true;false;British Contemporary;Adam Handling’s country inn is named in honour of where he met his co-owner chefs: Scotland and Newcastle. The room has a characterful vintage style, and the terrace sits beside raised beds which supply herbs and vegetables for the attractively presented dishes. Among them are re-worked pub classics like the elegant "King's Trifle" dessert. Complete your visit with a stay in one of the luxuriously appointed bedrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6902;The Bonnie Badger;United Kingdom;Gullane;Main Street, Gullane, EH31 2AB, United Kingdom;56.0351457;-2.8309937;43;false;true;Modern British;Tom and Michaela Kitchin have created their version of a pub in an old coaching inn dating from 1836. The bar serves pub classics, the dining room offers dishes with a 'nature to plate' philosophy and, in the garden, dishes are cooked on a Big Green Egg. Super comfy bedrooms showcase Scottish designers.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6903;Noble;United Kingdom;Holywood;27a Church Road, Holywood, BT18 9BU, United Kingdom;54.6414093;-5.8333093;92;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Hidden away in the centre of town is this compact little restaurant where the service is warm and genuine, and a happy buzz fills the air. Snacks are served in the bar downstairs, while the upstairs is home to the full à la carte of excellent value dishes. Boldly flavoured elements like confit garlic pepperonata enliven the unfussy cooking, whose visual simplicity belies its delicious intensity. Be sure to check out the daily specials on the blackboard and, for dessert, don’t miss the chocolate délice.;;[]
6905;COR;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;81 North Street, Bedminster, City of Bristol, BS3 1ES, United Kingdom;51.4406064;-2.6049987;17;false;true;Modern British;The epitome of a neighbourhood restaurant, COR is imbued with an air of contagious positivity that is a perfect fit for this buzzy area of Bristol. Its look is somewhere between a Mediterranean restaurant and a tapas bar, with some counter dining and shelves bursting with cookery books and wine. The dishes take on a similarly Mediterranean influence, as evidenced by the option of boquerones or burrata to kick things off. Save some room for pudding, because the crème caramel is a real treat.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6906;Waterman;United Kingdom;Belfast;5-23 Hill Street, Belfast, BT1 2LA, United Kingdom;54.6017969;-5.9267975;21;true;true;European Contemporary;Nothing beats the buzz of a big bistro and, judging by the numbers who flock here, the locals heartily agree. The modern, unfussy dishes are influenced by Europe, with Italy holding sway – this is the kind of food you could happily eat every day. Prices, too, are excellent, particularly considering its city centre location. The period building also houses a cookery school and event space.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6908;The Bull;United Kingdom;Charlbury;Sheep Street, Charlbury, OX7 3RR, United Kingdom;51.8727353;-1.4823543;80;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The duo behind The Pelican in London have returned home to the Cotswolds to open this 16C pub that oozes character and boasts flagged floors, timbered ceilings, plenty of exposed Cotswold stone and twin open fires. There is a relaxed and intimate feel to the place, and an understated quality to the simple, traditional cooking. Dishes like cured trout with green tomatoes use first-rate ingredients and deliver bags of flavour. Dining here is a hearty, satisfying experience, while bedrooms in The Barn are the icing on the cake.;Terrace;[]
6909;Amy Austin;Ireland;Dublin City;Unit 1,  Drury Street Car Park, Dublin City, D02 PH26, Ireland;53.3416354;-6.2638842;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences;There is a palpable buzz to the atmosphere as soon as you set foot in this quirky restaurant in a lively area of the city. It’s not just the wine on tap that makes this such a popular spot – although it must help – but the superior small plates that offer detailed, precise cooking for a reasonable price tag. Grab a stool at one of the high-top tables, or perhaps in front of the open kitchen, to enjoy globally influenced dishes like scallop crudo and Moroccan-style lamb rump. Friendly service and signature cocktails help to keep the good vibes flowing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6911;Bis Bistró;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Vicente López 1661 Local 12, Buenos Aires, C1018ABA, Argentina;-34.5919227;-58.3895357;46;true;true;Contemporary;Few places in Buenos Aires are as original as Bis Bistró, located in a charming passageway full of shops that inevitably draws comparisons with the romantic alleyways so typical of Paris. This bistro, which could be described as the younger brother of the renowned Aramburu (located opposite – chef Gonzalo Aramburu is in charge of both), has a classic ambience that comes as a pleasant surprise, having retained its 1950s-style bistro essence and appearance (high ceilings, globe lamps, long banquettes, mirrors etc) alongside a glass-fronted kitchen and a small bar. The reasonably contemporary à la carte (potato omelette, fresh capers and anchovies, rack of Patagonian lamb, pavlova with seasonal fruits etc) aims to re-create delicious recipes with traditional roots and modern tastes, complemented by a two- or three-course weekday lunchtime “executive” menu. The background music here is particularly pleasant.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6912;Mengano;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Jose Antonio Cabrera 5172, Buenos Aires, C1414BGT, Argentina;-34.5889231;-58.4337326;65;false;true;Contemporary;This unpretentious restaurant in the Palermo district, where you’ll need to ring the bell to gain access, is a potentially good option for its informal tapas and its wide array of traditional-style small plates. This bistro-eatery, boasting the appearance and feel of a modest tavern with old photos of the chef’s family adorning the walls, also features a small bar counter (with 4 stools) where guests can watch the kitchen team hard at work. The cuisine here revolves around a concise à la carte that aims to combine local cuisine with tapas and more traditional dishes, while always working with fresh ingredients, a nod to modernity and reasonably affordable prices. Dishes here include spicy meat empanaditas, pizza-style glazed pork belly with fainá flatbread, delicious lamb tartare toasts with quince cream and, for dessert, the Rogel, a cookie from Santa Fé in the form of a tart with lots of crispy and crunchy layers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
6913;La Alacena Trattoria;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Gascón 1401, Buenos Aires, C1181ADA, Argentina;-34.5940227;-58.4228233;22;true;true;Italian;When trying to identify a top Italian restaurant, we either come across places which showcase a strong sense of professionalism and elegance that you associate with a fine dining experience, or those with the informal feel of a traditional trattoria, where regional-style home cooking is always to the fore – at La Alacena, it is definitely the latter. Here, owner-chef Julieta Oriolo puts her heart and soul into Italian cooking, honouring her family roots and demonstrating a true fascination with ingredients from the country. On her à la carte, where you’ll find an enticing selection of antipasti and a few dishes worthy of particular mention (such as the exquisite polpette dal sugo), pasta plays a leading role, handmade with durum wheat flour and free-range eggs (standout dishes include the veal ravioli with a home-made cream and caramelised fennel, and fettuccine with saffron). They also sell their own artisanal pasta two blocks away, at the La Alacena Pastificio & Salumeria.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6914;Anafe;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Virrey Avilés 3216, Buenos Aires, C1426EEH, Argentina;-34.5739293;-58.4590023;16;true;false;Contemporary;The story of Mica Najmanovich and Nico Arcucci, who were already harbouring culinary dreams as students, is a tale of great conviction, as both pursued their ambition to work as chefs on their travels to Australia and Barcelona respectively. Their travels enabled them to assimilate cosmopolitan techniques and knowledge to their repertoire through influences from around the world. On their return, they started to work with pop-ups and, from this came a desire to open Anafe. In this simple eatery in the Colegiales district, their message is to “eat well, drink good wine and do both in a relaxed ambience”, hence their focus on global recipes with Asian, Australian, Jewish and Mediterranean influences, in which smoke and the open grill are the core elements in dishes designed for sharing, in keeping with Argentinian tradition. Their menu features cured fish, oyster mushrooms with cajú purée, grilled chicken with piri piri, and a superb calamari rice, to name just a few dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6915;Reliquia;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Angel Justiniano Carranza 1601, Buenos Aires, C1414COQ, Argentina;-34.5832681;-58.4392531;80;true;false;Argentinian;There’s a palpable sense of authenticity in this friendly restaurant, where the young owners have created a warm and welcoming ambience perfect for a romantic supper. The service is attentive without being excessively formal, while the soft colour scheme contributes to Reliquia’s warmth and intimacy. The menu is equally attractive with options for every taste – the chef has a perfect command of flavours and textures and uses techniques such as escabeche to raise the level of his dishes further, many of which showcase vegetables in a more rustic, home-style manner. We suggest starting with the delicious brioche-style bread with smoked butter, followed by the beetroot, “alcauciles” (artichokes) and the Brussels sprouts (“repollitos”). The agnolotti is a very popular main course with guests, although meat-lovers will also be keen to order the lacquered pork steak (“churrasquito de cerdo laqueado”). Everything possible is done here to avoid waste.;Air conditioning;[]
6916;República del Fuego;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Juncal 2682, Buenos Aires, C1425AYF, Argentina;-34.5898046;-58.4042439;57;true;false;Grills, Argentinian;If you’re an inveterate meat-eater, you’ll want to head to the República de Fuego, a restaurant with a young and informal vibe occupying an old restored house in the city’s Recoleta district. In this setting, which has retained the homely feel of the original building and which has preserved several “vintage” features such as the original and delightful flooring, everything revolves around the traditional Argentinian grill. Dishes have a contemporary twist in their presentation and are always based around premium cuts of meat that chef Patricio Pessio prepares with the greatest of care. Highlights on the menu include “knife-cut” meat empanadas, stracciatella with grilled edamame, a delicious skirt steak with a Creole sauce, ribeye with a fresh herb butter, and grilled pears with a mascarpone mousse and crumble – all presented with impeccable service and with the option of an impressive choice of cocktails.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6917;Caseros;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Caseros 486, Buenos Aires, C1152AAN, Argentina;-34.6267862;-58.3721967;55;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Home Cooking;Honesty is always appreciated when it comes to choosing a restaurant and this is especially the case in districts such as San Telmo, home to the National History Museum, where the standard of dining options is high and a vast array of cuisine is on offer. In this restaurant with a classic decor featuring retro detail and tables packed close together, the full focus is on home-style cooking showcasing consistent, simply prepared dishes teeming with superb flavours. The impressively large windows here provide plenty of natural light as well as occasionally serving as an external display for products such as scones, muffins, tart, artisanal bread etc, either to take away or to savour in relaxed style on the terrace. The highly traditional à la carte based around Argentinian ingredients is complemented by an inexpensive lunchtime menu. Our recommendations include warm prawn salad, aubergine with parmesan, spinach malfatti etc.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6918;Jen Ho Yuan;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, 112, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0606474;121.5226418;99;true;false;Yunnanese;Since 1956, this restaurant has been attracting loyal fans with its authentic Yunnan fare. In 2022, it moved to this new address, with its bright, airy main dining room and private rooms. Rest assured the menu and food stay the same – try the steam pot chicken, the sliced pork cheek cold appetiser, or the green peas in chicken fat. The true showstopper is string beans stuffed with minced shrimp, for the intriguing contrast of textures and layered flavours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
6920;Dejvická 34 by Tomáš Černý;Czech Republic;Prague;Dejvická 34, Prague, 16000, Czech Republic;50.0987928;14.3992062;68;true;false;Italian, Czech;Chef-owner Tomaš Černy worked in the best Italian restaurants in the city for many years before opening his own charming neighbourhood restaurant north of the river. The menu mixes Czech and Italian dishes and showcases some top quality imported ingredients. Dishes are robust and packed with flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6921;The Eatery;Czech Republic;Prague;U Uranie 954/18, Prague, 170 00, Czech Republic;50.1074835;14.4507679;85;false;false;Czech, Contemporary;This highly regarded restaurant in the suburbs delivers much more than its name and industrial styling first imply. The menu evolves from day to day, in line with the latest seasonal produce, and is accompanied by a superb wine list. Ask for a seat at the counter to witness the efficiency of the kitchen team.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6922;Na Kopci;Czech Republic;Prague;K Závěrce 2774/20, Prague, 150 00, Czech Republic;50.0565809;14.4022237;93;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Leave the city behind and escape to this buzzy bistro, whose name means ‘on the hill’. The wallpaper is a montage of pictures of the owner’s family and the atmosphere is warm and welcoming. Classic Czech and French dishes are packed with flavour and the local beers make a great accompaniment.;Air conditioning,Booking essential,Car park,Terrace;[]
6924;Bar Bù;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Van Vollenhovenstraat 19, Rotterdam, 3016 BG, Netherlands;51.9097334;4.4780792;16;true;true;Asian, Fusion;Upon entering this grand property near the marina, you have to decide between taking the stairs on the left to the lounge bar, or those on the right to the restaurant. The cocktail list is definitely worth exploring, but we would nonetheless encourage you to immerse yourself in the refined Asian-inspired ambience of the restaurant. The cuisines of France and the Far East are fused with a sure touch. The dim sum are fantastic, particularly the soft steamed dumplings stuffed with pork and prawn, served with a trout roe vinaigrette. The crispy pork belly, with plum sauce for umami nuances, is also tempting. With such a wide-ranging menu, diners are spoilt for choice!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6925;Oudeland;Netherlands;De Koog;Dorpsstraat 175, De Koog, 1796 CC, Netherlands;53.0971954;4.7630721;58;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking;Urban and trendy, yet warm and welcoming, Oudeland is run by an enthusiastic team who bring the place to life. Their passion shines through in the way they present their impressive selection of natural wines and express their deep connection to Texel. Any produce not grown in their own garden is sourced from local suppliers on the island. Pan-seared haddock, for example, is served with pasta made of locally milled flour, a brunoise of kohlrabi and a shellfish emulsion packed with character. The chefs showcase their terroir in creative dishes, keeping diners on their toes with a new set menu every month.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6926;WY.;Netherlands;Maastricht;Tongersestraat 23 (ingang via Kakeberg 6B), Maastricht, 6211 LL, Netherlands;50.84621;5.68666;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;There are plenty of reasons to fall in love with Wouter and Ylja's cosy fine dining restaurant, located in a picturesque cobbled street in the heart of the Jekerkwartier. At the entrance, the wine bar is the perfect spot for an afternoon drink and a light bite to eat. The expertly selected and at times surprising wine pairings are a highlight of dining at WY. What truly sets this place apart is its impressive array of exquisite dishes. Premium ingredients are showcased here, for example salmon trout from Commanderie 7 fish farm, slow-cooked and served with a subtly spicy herb salad and a rich buttermilk and green herb sauce. This chef has a knack for tantalising taste buds with bold flavours and a delicate hint of acidity. That's why you should book a table here.;Interesting wine list;[]
6927;Tannay;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Zandhoek 14, Amsterdam, 1013 KT, Netherlands;52.3881577;4.8899987;64;true;false;Classic French;The name "Tannay" is a reference to chef Thomas Demuth's birthplace. In fact, his parents still own a vineyard there, and some of their labels feature on the wine list. The French chef has set up shop on Realeneiland, in a building on a corner plot. His restaurant boasts a picturesque waterfront terrace and a romantic decor. Under Alain Caron's mentorship, he crafts familiar dishes that showcase his intimate knowledge of classic French cuisine. Options range from beetroot prepared in various ways with a rich Nantua sauce, to wild duck in puff pastry, and the time-honoured hare à la royale. The ingredients speak for themselves here.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6928;Le bistrot du Kachatelier;Luxembourg;Manternach;2, A Lambett, Manternach, 6850, Luxembourg;49.7036813;6.4225906;29;false;false;Farm to table;This sprawling bistro is housed in an amazing glass and wood arch-shaped structure fronted by a peaceful water feature. Harald and Maximilian Rüssel, first encountered at their Michelin-starred Rüssels Landhaus establishment in Germany, add their own inimitable touch to a regional culinary lineup courtesy of a concise menu packed in big-boned flavours. Examples include impeccably prepared cod à la meunière is garnished with a pumpkin-flavoured risotto, crunchy broccoli and a velvety beurre blanc to die for. Indulgent family favourites with a dash of stylish elegance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6929;Max & Moi;Belgium;Braine-l'Alleud;Grand Place Baudouin Premier 4, Braine-l'Alleud, 1420, Belgium;50.6826767;4.3691891;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French;Max & Pina have set up shop on Place Baudouin 1er in a tastefully refurbished town house dripping in understated glamour and sporting a suitably tasteful colour scheme. The couple works with a talented youthful chef, Julien Hauspie, who prefers to work with local produce while rolling out his experience gleaned in worldclass establishments at home and abroad. The chef’s know-how can be tasted in the beurre blanc that flanks seabass or in his way with carrots, which he might pair with a béarnaise sauce and tarragon and lemon oil, also demonstrating his creative side and fun-loving personality. Vibrant, exciting cuisine that comes in a four- or five-course menu.;Terrace;[]
6930;Le Philippe;Belgium;Rekem;Oude God 7, Rekem, 3621, Belgium;50.9232548;5.7048841;76;false;false;French;Rekem, one of the oldest, most authentic villages of Belgium, is rife in nostalgia, further accentuated by the collection of Fiat 500s mustered in front of Le Philippe. This ex-post office now sports a vintage Parisian vibe, including a soundtrack of French songs and also offers a few suites above the restaurant should you wish to stay longer. Danny Vanderhoven will win you over with his distinctive spin on bistronomic classics: frog’s legs in a creamy tomato, garlic and mild red pepper sauce, or slowly simmered melt-in-the-mouth beef bourguignon served with fries cooked in beef tallow, (which is the only way they should ever be fried!). A casual mood sets the scene for consummately crafted and generously served wholesome fare.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6931;Mémoire;Belgium;Brugge;Dijver 7, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2064741;3.2266291;77;true;false;Modern French;The luxury De Tuilerieën Hotel will leave you with unforgettable souvenirs, including that of a meal in its restaurant, Mémoire. Both its minimalist dining rooms are the pinnacle of unobtrusive opulence and style. Chef Wouter van Tichelen however disrupts this serene portrait courtesy of vibrant powerful cooking. Classically trained, the chef rolls out his know-how in sauces, adding elegant contemporary touches. He may give halibut marinated in salt a mineral edge courtesy of a creamy sorrel and seaweed sauce, while a caviar quenelle adds a final touch to this consummate dish, as does the Albariño wine with which it is paired. Van Tichelen deploys a local, sustainable ethos at the service of fine dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
6932;Coprin;Belgium;Straimont;Rue du Mont 5, Straimont, 6887, Belgium;49.7984458;5.3649161;71;true;true;Farm to table;This log cabin built entirely out of wood stands in quiet countryside amidst forest and woodland. The bucolic scene is set for Olivia, the exuberant lady of the house and chef Adrien to get to work and demonstrate how their shared love of nature has shaped their mindset. Genuine ambassadors of their local producers, they take real pleasure in showcasing outstanding produce. Chef Adrien may skin a perfectly ripe tomato, for example, before filling it with whipped cream jazzed up with horseradish, all of which to accompany velvety gazpacho and roast buckwheat. A fresh seasonal menu packed in rustic, wholesome flavours.;Car park;[]
6933;Carcasse;Belgium;Knokke;Oosthoekplein 1, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.34896;3.32692;85;false;false;Meats and Grills, Grills;An artisan butcher, Hendrik Dierendonck chose to open the first offshoot of his meat-lover’s establishment in Knokke’s Oosthoekplein. On entering, your eye is first drawn to the refrigerated counter and massive glazed aging cabinet, before it is distracted by the chefs in the open-plan kitchen as they craft outstanding produce that is Dierendonck’s signature. Delicacies such as Oedslach ribeye and tongue of Belgian red cattle are enhanced by subtle side dishes that add a wealth of nuances and refreshing notes. Grilled melt-in-the-mouth Menapii pork cutlet is coated in a creamy emulsion of tarragon and other fresh herbs and served on fregula seasoned with the same herbs and a mousse of thyme and coarsely ground hazelnuts. Diners are invited, even encouraged to share dishes, giving you more chance to taste the full scope of the appetising menu.;Air conditioning;[]
6934;La Petite Gayole;Belgium;Thuillies;Place de Thuillies 12, Thuillies, 6536, Belgium;50.294027;4.3296083;72;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, French;This characterful establishment in the picturesque village of Thuillies has become a beacon for all self-respecting fans of traditional nosh. A soundtrack of French ballads, an attractive wooden counter and vintage posters on the walls set the nostalgic scene indoors. The menu stars a patriotic lineup of Belgian staples including vol-au-vent of crunchy sweetbread and fresh fries, juicy kidneys and a dessert of French toast that is the ultimate comfort food. Wholehearted, much-loved family cooking oozing in bountiful generosity and fantastic flavours. We recommend the specials chalked up on the slate that offer outstanding taste for money!;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6935;Bleuet;Belgium;Maarke-Kerkem;Bovenstraat 4, Maarke-Kerkem, 9680, Belgium;50.802247;3.6519409;44;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Time seems to have stopped still at Bleuet, which is confirmed by the view over the rolling hillsides of the Flemish Ardennes from the exquisite terrace and the cosy interior of this cosy cottage. Pieter-Jan is in the kitchen, while Yoran makes sure the dining room never gets too crowded to ensure optimum quality. Yoran can be relied upon to open a bottle of wine for you to taste, which is something of a rarity these days. The chef plays with familiar flavours and international accents, as his seabass fillets in a miso and champagne sauce with a risotto of wheat and crunchy veg demonstrates. Food that throbs with flavour and a felicitous feast of unexpected associations.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6936;ATELIER D THE BISTRO;Belgium;Brugge;Hoogstraat 12, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2094446;3.2287847;85;true;true;French, Belgian;Diego De Baets is clearly at home in this sophisticated bistro, in which art and authenticity go hand in hand with a truly romantic vibe. The chef loves popping into the dining room to add a finishing touch to his dishes. You can expect a Franco-Belgian lineup starring outstanding ingredients, truly memorable sauces and big-boned flavours. Examples include crispy sweetbread coated in a flavoursome gravy further enhanced by sakura vinegar, or a match made in heaven of finely sliced wagyu and scallops paired with a knockout consommé made with the cooking gravy. The à la carte menu, which will have fine food connoisseurs slavering in anticipation, is a treasure trove of Belgian and French staples with a twist. Sheer bliss from start to finish.;Air conditioning;[]
6937;Charlu;Belgium;Uccle;Chaussée de Saint-Job 676, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7949863;4.3653062;76;true;true;French;This imposing 1920’s villa in the heart of the Saint Job neighbourhood is home to a genuine temple of bistronomy. Wainscoting, mirrors and tightly packed tables set the scene. The working language is French in both the menu and the wine list, the owner’s passion about which he frequently waxes lyrical. Hearty wholesome recipes from southwest France are what you can expect, like textbook cassoulet made with proper duck confit, smoked ham and Toulouse sausage, unless you wouldn’t prefer fritters of pig’s trotters or crispy sweetbread. Traditional down to the core and crafted with love is the ethos of Charlu.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6938;eppo;Belgium;Berchem;Coveliersstraat 6, Berchem, 2600, Belgium;51.1990995;4.4165774;81;false;true;Farm to table, Contemporary;Hotel Yust’s casual restaurant mirrors its host establishment’s trendy, globetrotting ethos. Think warm and cosy, untreated materials and a laidback vibe. The à la carte and set menus are similarly nonsense free, with an enticing lineup of vegan, meat and fish dishes. The house-made al dente pasta comes with a delicious sauce made out of genuine poultry stock and lashings of butter and is paired with a sourdough crumble fried in chicken fat, unless you wouldn’t prefer a classic entrecote steak, perhaps followed by an unusual dessert made out of parsnips? You can expect a jubilee of intriguing, down-to-earth dishes bursting with wholesome flavours. Just the ticket for a meal with the mates.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6939;Minato;Germany;Flensburg;Fördepromenade 30, Flensburg, 24944, Germany;54.8120249;9.4554598;90;true;true;Sushi, Japanese;This is just one of the options in the diverse range of restaurants within the Das James hotel, which is housed in a former naval building at the marina. Here you can look forward to truly authentic Japanese cuisine in the form of two set menus: the "James Sushi Menu" and the "Omakase" surprise menu. The chic design with a subtle Far Eastern touch and the friendly, competent service create a harmonious atmosphere. Minato is an appealing alternative to the restaurant's Das Grace and James Farmhouse and, as such, has many regular guests.;;[]
6940;Loumi;Germany;Berlin;Ritterstraße 2, Berlin, 10969, Germany;52.500686;13.4133674;79;true;true;International, Asian;Karl-Louis Kömmler, an ambitious chef who also happens to be self-taught, is at work in this small restaurant in Kreuzberg. His style of cooking is pleasingly pared back, cosmopolitan and entirely ingredient-led – and the quality of those ingredients deserves a mention. Choose between the four-course and eight-course set menus – courses include, for instance, a beautiful slice of grilled Challans duck breast from Maison Gérard Burgaud, harmoniously combined with the superb truffle aroma of the sauce Périgourdine and pleasingly firm maitake mushrooms. There are also various speciality upgrades. The wine list, although quite short, comprises a good selection. The team is charming and highly professional, and the chef himself serves and explains the dishes. The minimalist interior is inviting. Seats are split over two levels, with some at the counter, from which there is a view of the open kitchen. Small covered terrace in front of this corner building.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
6941;Stresa;Germany;Dresden;Augsburger Straße 85, Dresden, 01277, Germany;51.0446177;13.8002142;30;true;true;Classic Cuisine;A chic, modern and pleasingly neighbourly vibe makes itself felt in this restaurant in the attractive historical district of Striesen, which inspired the name of this place. Walls decorated with artwork by local artists, as well as the open kitchen draw the eye. In the evening, there is a choice of two set menus (omnivore and vegetarian/vegan) composed of three to six courses, or à la carte dishes. The menu changes regularly and takes its cue from the seasons. At lunchtime diners take their pick from a range of options on the "Bistro Menu". Friendly and relaxed service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6942;GRETA OTO im Königshof;Germany;Munich;Karlsplatz 25, Munich, 80335, Germany;48.1395918;11.56473;28;false;true;Latin American, International;For starters, the location right on the square known by locals as "Stachus" is nothing short of exclusive. GRETA OTO is housed within the luxurious and contemporary new Königshof hotel, on the ninth floor to be precise, affording fantastic views of the city of Munich and the Frauenkirche. The restaurant is no less chic and sophisticated than the hotel itself. Calm warm hues and dimmed lighting create an intimate atmosphere. The cuisine is Latin American with modern international influences, from Peruvian ceviche to Brazilian fillet steak and grilled octopus. The wine list to accompany the food is international. Tip: They have a private table – "La Mesa" – that you can book for special occasions. There is also a bar and a lounge terrace.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
6943;Matthias;Germany;Berlin;Kollwitzstraße 87, Berlin, 10435, Germany;52.538311;13.4200023;94;true;false;International, French;Set in an attractive building on a corner plot in the Prenzlauer Berg district, this highly inviting restaurant boasting a clean, modern look opened in October 2024. At the helm is a trio of industry professionals with a proven track record: owner Silvio Pfeufer (formerly head chef at einsunternull) presides in the kitchen, co-owner and maître d' Janine Woltaire heads up the friendly service team, which includes experienced sommelier Michael Stiel – the pair were colleagues at another Berlin restaurant, Horváth. There are two set menus (one is vegetarian), each comprising five or six courses. Alternatively, you can order from a range of à la carte options. Diners are presented with a modern, ingredient-led take on traditional French cuisine, a dish of kale, Roscoff onion and black chanterelle being a case in point. The name of this place is a nod to the chef's grandfather, who once had a butcher's shop in this neighbourhood.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6944;Restaurant Überfahrt;Germany;Rottach-Egern;Überfahrtstraße 10, Rottach-Egern, 83700, Germany;47.6966846;11.7582292;36;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Cornelia Fischer, who heads the kitchen at the fine dining restaurant of the splendid Althoff Seehotel Überfahrt, is by no means a newcomer to the culinary scene. After serving as chef de partie here years ago, and following her recent role as head chef in the kitchens of Zur Schwane in Volkach, she now creates contemporary interpretations of classical cuisine. Each of the two tasting menus, one of which is vegetarian, comprises four to six courses and is made from excellent ingredients – standout dishes include an elegant Norway lobster tartare and perfectly aged saddle of lamb en papillote. The sleek and stylish interior design is especially inviting, and the service is delightfully laid back and adept.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6946;Mikuriya;Switzerland;Zurich;Kurhausstrasse 65, Zurich, 8000, Switzerland;47.3726071;8.5732118;20;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;A one-of-a-kind experience awaits in the intimate Japanese restaurant of the venerable, art-filled luxury hotel The Dolder Grand. Upon arrival, diners are received at the hotel's front desk and escorted to a converted suite. The interior design is minimalist and elegant, and the setting has an intimate feel. Up to eight guests can sit at the counter and watch as chef Atsushi Hiraoka prepares the numerous courses of his omakase menu right before their eyes. Some of the ingredients used are locally sourced. Sake makes for the perfect accompaniment. Service begins at 7pm.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
6947;Fiescherblick;Switzerland;Grindelwald;Dorfstrasse 203, Grindelwald, 3818, Switzerland;46.6252587;8.0460994;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Set against a beautiful mountain backdrop, this establishment is run with great dedication by brothers Matthias and Lars Michel – Matthias manages the hotel, which boasts tastefully designed, comfortable rooms, and Lars is the restaurant's charming maître d'. In the kitchen, Aurélien Mettler and his team conjure up the modern and ambitious "Chef's Choice" set menu, which comprises four to six courses. For this, they use seasonal produce and skilfully incorporate Scandinavian and Japanese influences. Sustainability is a key consideration in the selection of the ingredients. If you would like a vegetarian version, it is best to specify this when making your reservation. Choose a bottle from the well-curated wine list, or opt for the recommended pairings by the glass – whether wine or an alcohol-free alternative. The inviting interior is done out in warm tones, featuring light wood finishings and clean lines, lending it a Nordic/Alpine feel. Overall, the atmosphere is pleasingly laid back. In fine weather, you can enjoy your aperitif on the terrace and take in the view of the Eiger North Face.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
6948;Klostergasthaus Löwen - Gaststube;Switzerland;Pfaffnau;Untertor 3, Pfaffnau, 4915, Switzerland;47.2325505;7.8392299;36;true;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;This is Pascal Schwarz's second restaurant on the estate of the former 12th century monastery. In addition to the gourmet restaurant, he also has his ‘Gaststube’ in the historic monastery inn in the St. Urban district - also on the first floor. Modern interiors have been attractively integrated into the traditional setting - on the terrace behind the house you can enjoy the good cuisine of Pascal and his team as well as the view of the imposing monastery church, which is well worth a visit. The cuisine is regional, seasonal and international. In the evening, there is a nice selection of dishes ranging from ‘pastrami burgers’ to ‘pink roast duck breast from France’ and ‘vegetarian carbonara-style mushroom risotto’.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6949;Klostergasthaus Löwen - Negral;Switzerland;Pfaffnau;Untertor 3, Pfaffnau, 4915, Switzerland;47.2325578;7.8392299;74;false;false;International, Fusion;With the ‘Negral’ and the ‘Gaststube’, there are two concepts under one roof here, in the ‘Klostergasthaus Löwen’ dating from 1870 on the grounds of the imposing former Cistercian monastery dating from 1194 in the St. Urban district. On the first floor, Pascal Schwarz and his team offer modern, classically based cuisine in the form of a surprise menu, including vegetarian options, in the chic little gourmet parlour ‘Negral’. The six, eight or ten courses are prepared using excellent seasonal, regional and international produce. The terrace offers a beautiful view of the monastery church. Tip: In good weather, enjoy your aperitif outside in the lounge or round off the evening in the cigar lounge in the vaulted cellar. A business lunch is available at lunchtime.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
6950;Dorfhus Gupf;Switzerland;Rehetobel;Kirchstrasse 2, Rehetobel, 9037, Switzerland;47.4266044;9.4826686;25;true;true;Grills, International;At Dorfstuba, the restaurant of Dorfhus Gupf boutique hotel, you can look forward to friendly and attentive service in a charming setting with a modern Alpine touch. Head chef Sven Vogelsanger champions seasonal produce from the region. Order à la carte or opt for the four- to seven-course set menu – you can also watch your dishes being prepared in the open kitchen. The standout feature is the open Asado grill station, where whole fish and special meat cuts are cooked. Sommelier Johannes Fitz is on hand to recommend the perfect wine from the fantastic selection of international labels.;Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6951;KAISEKI BY MANABU;Switzerland;Vevey;Rue d'Italie 49, Vevey, 1800, Switzerland;46.4584644;6.8480525;92;true;false;Japanese Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;At the Hôtel Des Trois Couronnes, beautifully situated on the lakeside, chef Alastair Long offers authentic Japanese cuisine. Selected products (e.g. Hamachi, Kagashima Wagyu, scallops, etc.) are given pride of place. In the evening, three menus are available: ‘Signature’, ‘Connaisseur’ and ‘Kaiseki’, while at lunchtime a more affordable lunch menu is available. Service takes place in an elegant atmosphere, under high ceilings decorated with stucco. In summer, the terrace is a veritable dream, offering magnificent views of the lake and mountains.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6952;Gourmetstube Hochfirst;Austria;Obergurgl;Gurglerstraße 123, Obergurgl, 6456, Austria;46.8738648;11.0315153;40;false;false;Contemporary;This fine dining restaurant in the Hochfirst, a chic Alpine hotel, has an elegant but by no means stuffy atmosphere. The small, cosy space can accommodate a maximum of 16 guests at beautifully laid tables, with views over the ski slope through large windows. Diners are free to choose the number of courses they would like from the set menu. The contemporary cuisine is appealingly uncomplicated, with dishes such as saddle of young venison with a coffee jus and black salsify. Service comes courtesy of a very friendly, attentive and well-drilled front-of-house team, who also provide wine recommendations. The wine list features over 800 (mostly Austrian) labels, as well as a good selection of champagnes.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
6953;Restaurant Scheucher;Austria;Graz;Schönaugasse 6, Graz, 8010, Austria;47.0662223;15.4413664;24;true;true;Farm to table;The attractive location in the city centre, and the invitingly timeless atmosphere provide the perfect backdrop for the good food served here. The classics are held in high regard, from Wiener schnitzel and steak to baked porcini with tartar sauce and vitello tonnato – regional and international dishes feature on the menu. In summer, the lovely terrace to the rear beckons. Drivers have the option of parking in the Parkgarage Schönaugasse right next to the restaurant.;;[]
6954;KETCHUP;Austria;Goldegg;Hofmark 8, Goldegg, 5622, Austria;47.3175367;13.0995887;86;true;false;Austrian, Regional Cuisine;Felix Schellhorn has succeeded his father Sepp as the new head chef at the restaurant of Der Seehof hotel, a renowned art-focused establishment nestled in a hamlet by the lake – Goldegger Moorsee. A single set menu is served – this changes daily, taking its cue from the seasons and showcasing good-quality regional ingredients. The charming interior features delightfully unique decorative details with endearing individual furnishing details. Tables on the terrace are also much in demand.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6955;Verdi-Einkehr;Austria;Linz;Pachmayrstraße 137, Linz, 4040, Austria;48.3417539;14.2711848;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This is the second restaurant run by the Lukas family, and here, too, the cooking can be described as ambitious. The modern, seasonal cuisine has a regional bent and also draws on international influences – for instance, "tuna mango, miso, lime" or "braised veal cheeks chanterelles, creamed potato, Barolo red wine". As for the division of labour, owner Erich Lukas and his son Philipp work their magic in the kitchen, while maître d' Helga and her dedicated front-of-house team provide cordial service. Finally, there is the gorgeous location on a leafy estate at the edge of a forest overlooking Linz – in summer, you can take in stunning views from the terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
6956;Wirtshaus Kogel 3;Austria;Leibnitz;Kogelbergstraße 62, Leibnitz, 8430, Austria;46.7927412;15.5101357;48;true;true;Farm to table, International;Against the backdrop of vineyards and the rolling hills that surround Leibnitz, the setting is almost heavenly. The marvellous tiered terrace and a lounge area beneath the arcade are, of course, extremely inviting in summer. The interior is equally delightful, with its stylish modern design and floor-to-ceiling windows affording stunning views. Here, you can look forward to contemporary seasonal cuisine paired with an excellent wine list and exceptionally friendly, attentive service.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6958;Gaumenkitzel;Austria;Kirchberg am Wechsel;Tratten 36, Kirchberg am Wechsel, 2880, Austria;47.600338;16.001732;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;"Cook the Gart'l" – that is to say, the garden – is the name of the game here. The modern creative cuisine is the product of a philosophy of regionality and takes the form of the four- or six-course "GENUSSpur" set menu interspersed with various amuse-bouches. Regional ingredients take pride of place in dishes such as Molzbach trout, pumpkin, fennel, buttermilk or Kirchberg venison, Tosca onion, apricot. Chef Peter Pichler took over the Pichler family business in 2015, after earning his stripes at top-flight establishments in Austria and abroad (including Döllerer, Taubenkobel and Vila Joya). At his side is Nina Pichler, who tends to guests in the tastefully modern restaurant – the chef-patron gets involved in serving, too. You also have the option of dining at Wirtshaus. Furthermore, there is a small shop selling gourmet food and regional items. This range of facilities, along with a spa and lovely guestrooms, is all part of the Naturhotel Molzbachhof.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6959;Stefan Haas Fine Dine;Austria;Altaussee;Fischerndorf 80, Altaussee, 8992, Austria;47.6416741;13.7682022;44;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Run by Stefan Haas, this restaurant offers a totally immersive experience. The open kitchen allows you to witness firsthand how the chef-patron transforms seasonal ingredients into flavoursome dishes with his own creative touch. There is no menu in the traditional sense: you are given small cards with sketches and explanations of the dishes – you then compile your own set menu from these options. Modern and minimalist in style, the dining space has only a limited number of tables. Friendly and adept service.;Terrace;[]
6960;Lilli & Jojo;Austria;Gamlitz;Sulztal an der Weinstraße 22, Gamlitz, 8451, Austria;46.6870475;15.5522892;88;true;true;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;Lilli Kollar and Joachim Gradwohl ("Lilli & Jojo") have created something really wonderful here. Along with its fabulous elevated location surrounded by vineyards, their restaurant boasts a delightfully cosy atmosphere and very friendly service. In summer, you should definitely opt for a table on the idyllic terrace if possible. Joachim Gradwohl is a renowned chef, who crafts seasonal dishes, showcasing locally sourced ingredients. To complement your food, there is a nicely curated selection of fine wines from the region and beyond. Tip: Not only are there some fantastic hiking trails in the area, but also some excellent wineries.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6961;Rosi;Austria;Vienna;Sechshauser Straße 120, Vienna, 1150, Austria;48.1861624;16.3218621;53;false;true;International, Austrian;A cool concept that varies over the course of the week, attracting guests all day long. A cosy breakfast is served Thursday to Saturday, at lunchtime on Thursdays and Fridays there is an affordable dish of the day. From Wednesday to Saturday, the evening meal is all about sharing. The interesting menu offers a surprise "Chef's Choice" (only available if ordered by the whole table), or you can choose the delicious dishes yourself and share them. Incidentally, the cooking tends towards the vegetarian. The food is as unfussy as the relaxed and lively atmosphere that reigns in the restaurant, which is done out in a charming minimalist style.;;[]
6962;Hörnlingen Wirtshaus;Austria;Rankweil;Bahnhofstr. 25, Rankweil, 6830, Austria;47.2715044;9.6390826;88;false;true;Alpine, Regional Cuisine;At this restaurant in a beautiful historical house on the road leading to the imposing Basilika Rankweil, the culinary focus is firmly on the region. The young chef serves surprise set menus only. Fresh, seasonal ingredients go into preparing five, seven or 10 courses, all of which demonstrate a personal touch. As an alternative to the "Tellerservice" menu, there is also the option of the "Meal Sharing" menu. The service is extremely friendly and, with its blend of traditional style shown off by modern accents, the interior is charming.;Terrace;[]
6963;Sattlerhof - Wirtshaus;Austria;Gamlitz;Sernau 2a, Gamlitz, 8462, Austria;46.7132918;15.5392703;25;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This renowned winery and hotel enjoys a sensational location amid the vineyards – the terrace overlooking the region beckons in summer! With Wirtshaus, siblings Anna and Markus Sattler propose a charming alternative to their fine dining restaurant. Popular classics and seasonal dishes can be ordered à la carte, and there is also a daily set menu. To complement the dishes, they serve wines from their own estate. Besides the delicious food, the warm hospitality ensures a wonderful dining experience.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6964;Rosso di Acqua e Sole;Austria;Linz;Weingartshofstraße 29, Linz, 4020, Austria;48.2920162;14.2894653;58;false;false;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;In the mood for fresh Italian cuisine that skilfully combines typical cucina casalinga with modern influences? The select ingredients are seasonal, with fish and seafood as the focal point. The ikejime dry-aged sea bass, for example, from the restaurant's own maturing cabinet, is excellent. In addition to the à la carte menu, patron Ingmar Goetzloff will talk you through the latest creations at your table. He will also be happy to advise you on drinks – they have a nicely curated wine list with around 400 labels. The modern, attractively decorated restaurant is located in a residential and office area close to the main railway station and Landestheater.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6965;Broadmoar;Austria;Sankt Joseph;Oisnitz 36, Sankt Joseph, 8503, Austria;46.9091145;15.3567514;18;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Contemporary;This country house, accessible via a narrow driveway, is in a truly idyllic location with stables and paddocks, surrounded by woods and meadows. The food is seasonal and regional, served à la carte or in the form of a set menu. By the way, the dishes are presented on handmade ceramics. On Wednesdays and Thursdays, a moderately priced, slightly shorter set menu is available. The waitstaff are friendly and well-organised, and the wine recommendations are always spot on. Given the beautiful setting, tables on the terrace are coveted – especially in summer.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6966;Kupferdachl - Wirtshaus;Austria;Premstätten;Hauptstraße 275, Premstätten, 8141, Austria;46.9856092;15.4002645;25;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Brother-and-sister team Lisa and Daniel Edelsbrunner are continuing their parents' commitment to Kupferdachl – she in service, he in the kitchen. Based on traditional Austrian recipes, the cuisine takes its cue from the region and the seasons, mindful of the provenance and quality of the ingredients. Aromatic dishes such as oven-baked pumpkin with Nuart sheep's cheese, walnut and chickweed, or Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) from Chianinahof farm in Dobl with roasted apples, chive sauce and apple and horseradish sauce are served à la carte or as a set menu. At lunchtime (Wed-Fri), there is also a moderately priced daily special. The well-curated wine list includes a fine selection of regional and Austrian labels, as well as organic and biodynamic wines. The lovely covered terrace overlooks a well-kept garden complete with a koi pond and knobby olive trees. Tip: Also in the building, fine dining restaurant, Das Edelsbrunner serves an ambitious surprise set menu (open Fri and Sat).;Car park,Terrace;[]
6967;Rotes Haus;Austria;Dornbirn;Marktplatz 13, Dornbirn, 6850, Austria;47.4138385;9.7419539;68;false;true;Austrian;This charming old Rhine Valley building dating back to 1639 is quite something! A Dornbirn landmark right on the Marktplatz (still the market square), it has been sensitively renovated and restored, and now boasts five really beautiful historical rooms. Delicious Austrian cuisine with Mediterranean influences is on the menu – the Wiener schnitzel and fried chicken are as appetising as the pickled char with radish and rhubarb-wild garlic vinaigrette. The spacious terrace, shaded by parasols, is also inviting.;Terrace;[]
6968;Das Schindler;Austria;Innsbruck;Maria-Theresien-Straße 31, Innsbruck, 6020, Austria;47.2654306;11.3944786;59;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;A popular establishment in a prime location in the centre of the old town, right in the pedestrianised precinct. The appealing combination of restaurant and bar (look out for the interesting cocktails) makes for a lively atmosphere with an "urban brasserie" feel. Top-notch ingredients are used to create tasty and contemporary seasonal cuisine, which in the evening comes as a three- or four-course set menu as well as à la carte. The smaller and simpler lunchtime menu includes one or two dishes from the evening menu. Tip for motorists: the multi-storey car park in the Rathaus-Galerien.;Air conditioning;[]
6969;Restaurant Krainer;Austria;Langenwang;Grazer Straße 12, Langenwang, 8665, Austria;47.568388;15.6201765;33;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The second restaurant of the hotel of the same name in the centre of the village offers a classic dining experience with its tastefully designed upscale interior and Andreas Krainer's cuisine. The chef's passion for reinvented classics is evident in dishes such as char from Pretul Saibling fish farm in Langenwang with char caviar, buckwheat and porcini. He prides himself on using regional produce, most of it sourced from the immediate vicinity. The set menu comprises four or six courses and is complemented by a selection of fine wines, as well as attentive service provided by a friendly and adept front-of-house team.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
6970;Lurgbauer;Austria;Mariazell;Lurg 1, Mariazell, 8630, Austria;47.8080138;15.3138417;67;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;Nestled amid forests and meadows at an elevation of approximately 900m, this farmhouse is accessible via a gravel road. Its origins can be traced back to 1390. With bare wooden tables, floorboards and cowhides as decoration, the small restaurant has a clean and modern yet rustic look. Floor-to-ceiling windows afford views of the idyllic countryside, including their own Black Angus cattle grazing in the pasture – they are a focal point of the sustainable culinary approach. At lunchtime, classic dishes are served à la carte or as a set menu. In the evening, you have the choice between two set menus: the seasonal and creative "Lurg-Menü" and the "Klassiker-Menü". The beef soup or boiled beef alone are worth the trip!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6971;Johanns Living;Austria;Bruck an der Mur;Hugo von Montfortgasse 2, Bruck an der Mur, 8600, Austria;47.4081184;15.2713848;33;true;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in a bijou little boutique hotel of the same name. With only two guestrooms, the establishment is tucked away in a quiet side street in the city centre, creating an intriguing architectural juxtaposition with the adjacent district court. The compact restaurant with just four tables has a tastefully modern decor and a cosy atmosphere. Chef Mike Johann delivers seasonal cuisine and takes pleasure in presenting his set menu in person. He will also gladly recommend the perfect accompaniment from a list of over 900 wines.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
6973;Zur Palme;Austria;Neuhofen an der Ybbs;Marktplatz 6, Neuhofen an der Ybbs, 3364, Austria;48.0576444;14.8551689;91;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;After completing stints at renowned establishments, Theresia Palmetzhofer returned home, and she has been running this charming restaurant with her dedicated team since 2016. Modernisation work saw the historical walls and structures of the 500-year-old building carefully preserved and given an inviting, upscale look. In addition, the property boasts a gorgeous terrace. The boss herself also heads up the kitchen, zeroing in on ingredients of regional origin to cook classic and regional dishes with a modern twist. These are organised into a pleasantly manageable seasonal menu. The wine list, too, has an Austrian flavour and includes a selection of natural wines.;Terrace;[]
6974;1er Beisl im Lexenhof;Austria;Nußdorf am Attersee;Am Anger 4, Nußdorf am Attersee, 4865, Austria;47.8828954;13.5220605;85;true;false;Austrian, International;This idyllic lakeside house has been in existence since 1447. With their wood panelling and tiled stove, its rooms have a cosy atmosphere that draws on the region. The cuisine is Austrian-influenced, but also has an international lilt. There is a choice of à la carte dishes or you can opt for the "Genuss-Menü" (set menu), or indeed pick and choose individual courses from the latter. The veal fillet and braised veal cheek, for example, is really delicious. On Mondays, a surprise menu comprising three or five courses is served. The restaurant is located in Hotel Lexenhof, which offers charming, cosy guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
6975;Lilli Fine Dining;Austria;Fehring;Hauptplatz 9, Fehring, 8350, Austria;46.9355541;16.0106008;49;true;true;Contemporary;The fine dining side of Lilli offers foodies the chance to experience the ambitious cooking of Walter Triebl and his team either at lunch or dinnertime. Only the "Wirtshaus menu" is available at lunchtime, but in the evening you also have the option of the "Fine Dining" menu. Comprising four to six courses, this set menu showcases excellent regional and international ingredients in dishes such as carabinero, tuna, tomato and watermelon, or Fehring lamb, mushrooms and corn – with lamb supplied by the mayor! The modern interior of the restaurant is just as inviting as the tables in the garden, separated only by a glass partition that can be fully opened in summer.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6977;Im Hofgassl;Austria;Rust;Rathausplatz 10, Rust, 7071, Austria;47.7999859;16.67598;56;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;A thoroughly enchanting establishment! In a 16C townhouse in the heart of the city, dedicated hosts Susanne and Michael Pilz have created a cosy restaurant featuring beautiful vaulted ceilings and a truly idyllic outdoor dining area with trees, grapevines, shrubs and herbs. The chef-patron crafts regional and seasonal dishes with modern influences (think veal lights with brioche dumplings or sea bass with melted tomatoes and saffron gnocchi), the lady of the house expertly directs the service with warm hospitality. In addition to the restaurant, they operate café-bar 10 B, located on Rathausplatz. Recommended excursions: Lake Neusiedl or the Roman quarry in Sankt Margarethen.;Terrace;[]
6978;fischerhaus;Austria;Moosburg;Pörtschacherstraße 44, Moosburg, 9062, Austria;46.6623695;14.1500954;85;true;false;Contemporary;This lovely country house is located just a stone's throw from Wörthersee. The restaurant boasts a chic, elegant interior, as well as a delightful terrace. The menu features a diverse range of dishes prepared with the finest ingredients, covering everything from Austrian classics and Asian cuisine to truffles and caviar. Regulars and newcomers alike are treated with the same warmth and professionalism by the friendly staff.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
6979;Beletage Zum Schwarzen Kameel;Austria;Vienna;Bognergasse 5, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2100352;16.3682745;83;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The setting alone is a huge draw: the first floor of a 1901 Jugendstil building in a super-central location. The interior decor is at once elegant yet cosy, and the front-of-house team is experienced and pleasingly laid back, while operating in the classical style, like a well-oiled machine. And, of course, there is the exceptional food: a celebration of Viennese classics, elevated by creative seasonal additions. There is a well-curated à la carte selection with a set menu option – diners are spoilt for choice, with dishes such as the rustic hand-carved ham being just as tempting as the oven-baked pike-perch with a ginger and citrus butter.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6980;Die Gersberg Alm;Austria;Salzburg;Gersberg 37, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.811644;13.0997566;36;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Austrian;This restaurant overlooking Salzburg boasts a wonderful location and stunning views. The atmosphere in the pretty wood-panelled dining area is cosy. The cuisine is rooted in the region but also draws on international influences, with a house speciality of Zitronen-Rahm-Herz vom Milchkalb (milk-fed calf's heart in a creamy lemon sauce) featured alongside dishes such as venison yellow curry served with spiced rice. There are set menus, one of which is vegetarian, an à la carte menu and an additional afternoon snack menu – there really is something for everyone. This lovely spot, which is also a favourite among locals, is housed in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
6981;Weitmoser Schlössl;Austria;Bad Hofgastein;Schlossgasse 14, Bad Hofgastein, 5630, Austria;47.1627687;13.0989072;21;true;true;Austrian, Regional Cuisine;In the setting of this picturesque centuries-old castle, you can savour classic cuisine with an Austrian twist. The dishes are meticulously crafted from first-rate ingredients including organic beef from the restaurant's own on-site farm. Be sure to try the Wiener schnitzel and the Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) – the side dishes are also excellent, such as the exquisite creamed spinach. Adept service comes courtesy of a friendly front-of-house team. Delightful terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
6982;Steak Boutique;Austria;Graz;Bindergasse 1, Graz, 8010, Austria;47.0707812;15.4422854;86;true;true;Meats and Grills;The name says it all: it is all about high-quality dry-aged beef from Austria and Nebraska, served as a variety of exquisite cuts. Whether you choose tenderloin, bone-in rib-eye, bone-in New York strip, T-bone or porterhouse, exceptional quality of meat and perfectly cooked steaks are guaranteed. Be sure to sample the wonderful house-made steak fries. Tip: The light-filled atrium with its lovely arched ceiling is especially delightful. The restaurant is housed in the same building as Boutique Dom Hotel building, in the centre of Graz.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
6983;Terra;Austria;Stainz;Rathausplatz 2, Stainz, 8510, Austria;46.8940358;15.2636754;82;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Johann Schmuck runs his chic modern restaurant in the basement of a historical mill that dates back to 1581 – tables on the terrace overlooking the Stainzbach River are coveted in summer. He and Maximilian Grandtner are jointly in charge of the kitchen. They propose a modern and seasonal surprise menu comprising three, five or seven courses, as well as the "All in" version, which has nine courses – including amuse-bouches and petit fours. Most of the ingredients used are locally sourced. A vegetarian set menu is also available. Alternatively, there is the "Mühle" (mill) menu: an à la carte selection of dishes. The friendly and professional service team includes sommelier Joachim Retz, who specialises in wines from Styria and Burgenland. Tip: Enjoy an aperitif in the bar lounge.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6984;Black Sheep;Austria;Sölden;Dorfstraße 114, Sölden, 6450, Austria;46.9647969;11.0073861;59;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;The fine dining restaurant of Bergland hotel boasts a chic interior with a stylish dark colour scheme. The cuisine is entirely dedicated to the Alpine region. Ingredients are sourced within a 200km radius, with Austria and South Tyrol being the main suppliers. Much of the produce comes from the immediate vicinity, including herbs from the restaurant's own garden. They even raise their own sheep. The cooking style is very contemporary and incorporates subtle Japanese influences. For example, the six-course set menu includes dishes such as Alpine prawn katsuobushi with tomato and yuzu bisque, or Tyrolean catfish and broad beans.;Car park;[]
6985;Kliemstein Vino Vitis;Austria;Linz;Obere Donaulände 15, Linz, 4020, Austria;48.3063856;14.2831305;80;false;true;Classic Cuisine, International;You could easily miss the entrance leading into this small restaurant housed in the Salzamt, with its beautiful, brightly lit vaulted ceiling and sophisticated ambience. Michael A Müller – a highly accomplished trained chef and restaurateur – has dedicated many years to this establishment. The owner enjoys interacting with guests and recommending the perfect wine from his extensive cellar of over 1 200 labels and 50 000 bottles. And he has found a congenial right-hand man in chef Andreas Zika. Diners choose from three surprise menus: the shorter "Theater Menu", the "Bistro Menu" and the "Gourmet Menu". The latter features such shining examples as "sashimi of yellowfin tuna, shiso, ginger-kefir broth" and "saddle of venison, gremolata breadcrumbs, Chinese artichoke" – dishes showcasing highly intense and nuanced flavours and exceptional craftsmanship. The wine tasting event that they hold once a month is another interesting date for the diary.;Interesting wine list;[]
6986;Kammer5;Austria;Ort im Innkreis;Kammer 5, Ort im Innkreis, 4974, Austria;48.3078896;13.4302709;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This converted farmhouse has been given an upscale, modern makeover, without any of its original character being lost in the process ("old exterior, new lease of life"). A relaxed, understated elegance reigns in the restaurant housed in what was once the cowshed. The beautiful brick cross-vaulted ceiling lends a special atmosphere to the space. The seasonal set menu, which comprises four or six courses, showcases regional produce. Sophisticated and meticulously prepared dishes, such as mushroom, thyme and sherry, or venison, black salsify and pomegranate, are packed with bold flavours. In addition to wine, there are also delightful non-alcoholic pairings available.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6987;Zum Verwalter;Austria;Dornbirn;Schloßgasse 1, Dornbirn, 6850, Austria;47.4090725;9.7505589;21;true;false;Farm to table;Its origins dating back to the 17C, this site is steeped in history. Today the building houses pretty hotel rooms and an extremely tasteful restaurant with authentic charm – plenty of wood and low ceilings make for a really cosy atmosphere. In summer, the terrace, too, is very inviting. When it comes to the food, the kitchen draws on what the market has to offer. Top-notch ingredients are used to create classic veal tartare with pan-fried sweetbreads, for example. The marvellous selection of 600 wines, including top wines from Austria, Italy and France, is a must for wine lovers. The service is friendly and proficient – while always on hand, the staff's presence is by no means intrusive.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6988;Gutwinski;Austria;Feldkirch;Rosengasse 6, Feldkirch, 6800, Austria;47.2367591;9.5976328;22;false;false;International, Farm to table;This boutique hotel in the centre of the old town is the epitome of elegance – when it comes to both the guestrooms and the restaurant serving excellent cuisine. First-class ingredients – many of which come from the region – go into creating delicious dishes replete with international influences. The pan-fried fillet of Ramschwag char served with grilled baby leek, beluga lentil risotto, and a honey and lime foam is one appetising example. Choose from the set menu and à la carte dishes. At lunchtime, the slightly more limited selection includes a short lunch menu. The wine list, which counts around 250 labels, focuses on Austria. Handy for motorists: the Am Jahnplatz multi-storey car park is just a few minutes' walk away.;Terrace;[]
6989;Goldader - Alpine Kulinarik;Austria;Tamsweg;Gewerbepark Litzelsdorf 281, Tamsweg, 5580, Austria;47.1316675;13.7950673;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Austrian;Housed in a modern building in a rural setting, this is an interesting location. The interior is stylish and minimalist with a soothing colour scheme – don't miss your chance to take in the lovely view from the terrace. The dishes served here are a modern take on Austrian cuisine showcasing the finest local ingredients including game and fresh trout. There is a tasting menu with a flexible number of courses. Friendly and attentive service.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6990;Sitzwohl;Austria;Innsbruck;Gilmstraße 4, Innsbruck, 6020, Austria;47.2661003;11.3969037;71;true;false;Classic Cuisine;The smart, modern interior design of this place verges on the minimalist, creating an inviting and really stylish atmosphere. First and foremost, though, it is Elisabeth Geisler's cuisine that draws guests to this restaurant on the first floor of what was once the Gilmschule, whose listed façade forms an interesting contrast with the modern architecture of the Stadtforum. Aromatic dishes with a clear structure, such as turbot fillet with a beautifully spiced and reduced beurre blanc or crispy tarte Tatin of carrot, parsnip and celeriac are available as part of a set menu or à la carte. A good selection of wines and friendly, efficient service are also part of the experience. Diners may like to go to the bar and the Geislerei delicatessen on the ground floor.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6991;Das Kraus;Austria;Vienna;Große Pfarrgasse 7, Vienna, 1020, Austria;48.2188022;16.3786804;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant comprising six tables is housed in what used to be a coffee house – the sign outside simply reads "K". They serve a six-course set menu made using seasonal ingredients, into which chef Daniel Horner (previously sous-chef at Japanese restaurant Mochi) cleverly incorporates the odd subtle Asian flavour. Sommelier Vanessa Schober will be happy to recommend Austrian wines to accompany your meal. Non-alcoholic tea accompaniment is also possible. The chic and modern interior successfully combines a certain industrial style with a dash of retro flair. There is a pavement terrace in summer. You can also take in temporary art exhibitions here – the proprietor owns a gallery.;Air conditioning;[]
6992;Kutschker 44;Austria;Vienna;Kutschkergasse 44, Vienna, 1180, Austria;48.2267863;16.3447314;95;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, International;This relaxed and friendly, modern restaurant is very popular with locals, and no wonder given the delicious fare on offer. Menu options include chanterelle terrine with walnuts, lamb’s lettuce and bresaola as well as Viennese specialities such as veal lights and Black Angus rib-eye steak. The terrace looks onto the pedestrian zone.;Terrace;[]
6993;Fabios;Austria;Vienna;Tuchlauben 6, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2099702;16.3698015;30;false;true;Italian;The clientele of this fashionable urban restaurant is a veritable Who's Who of Vienna! The Italian cuisine served is modern and pared back, in keeping with the minimalist interior design – two good reasons to come here for a meal! Plump for one of the house classics such as fried calamari or vitello tonnato. Or perhaps you would prefer saffron risotto with Norway lobster? Friendly and attentive service, a large terrace in summer, and a bar that is ideal for a light bite or a pre-dinner drink.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
6994;Döllerers Wirtshaus;Austria;Golling an der Salzach;Markt 56, Golling an der Salzach, 5440, Austria;47.5972924;13.1676968;86;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This place has a long culinary tradition to its name, dating back to 1909. The Döllerer family's inn is located in the town centre, not far from the parish church and the castle. The atmosphere is pleasantly lively and with a cosy, rustic charm. Food is served by friendly waitstaff in two dining spaces with historical vaulted ceilings or on the terrace to the rear of the building. The menu features mouthwatering dishes such as sturgeon with Piedmont hazelnuts or Rauris venison ragout, not forgetting the signature dessert Schwarzbeernock'n (blueberry dumplings) with sour cream ice cream. Delicatessen goods are also available for purchase, including meat products, cheese specialities and delicacies such as jams, Alpine spices, mustard etc. Overnight accommodation available at the adjoining Hotel Döllerer.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6995;Heunisch und Erben;Austria;Vienna;Landstrasser Hauptstraße 17, Vienna, 1030, Austria;48.2049338;16.387971;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Due to its being an interesting mix of wine bar and restaurant, this place has a remarkable wine list and around 120 open wines to accompany the ambitious modern cuisine. Diners put together their own four- to nine-course menu from a lovely selection of dishes. The service is relaxed, attentive and experienced. The terrace is a popular spot on warm summer evenings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6996;Do & Co Restaurant am Stephansplatz;Austria;Vienna;Stephansplatz 12, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2083288;16.3716993;49;true;true;Asian;Up on the seventh floor, this is one of the city's hotspots: a modern, elegant restaurant with a great terrace and a view of St Stephen's Cathedral. In the open kitchen the team cooks up international cuisine. Alongside the many Asian-influenced dishes, including sushi, the menu also features Austrian classics.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
6997;Schloss Restaurant;Austria;Hof bei Salzburg;Schlossstraße 19, Hof bei Salzburg, 5322, Austria;47.808811;13.2559602;98;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Austrian;Set in a phenomenal location, the renowned Rosewood Schloss Fuschl has many admirers, and not only among its hotel guests. With its exceptionally upscale and tastefully elegant interior, the restaurant strikes a perfect balance between grandeur and cosy comfort. The large windows offer a magnificent view of the lake. The set menu and à la carte dishes are prepared with select regional ingredients, including produce from the restaurant's own fish farm. The impressive wine list is extensive and includes some prestigious labels. In fine weather, you can also dine on the lakeside terrace one floor up.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
6998;Paradoxon;Austria;Salzburg;Zugallistraße 7, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7942225;13.051118;21;true;false;Farm to table;The atmosphere here is pleasantly down-to-earth, and the waitstaff laid-back and friendly. The cuisine is modern and seasonal. Along with à la carte options such as char ceviche or local ribeye steak, there is a set menu comprising four or six courses. Tip: Brunch is also served on Sat and Sun (10am-2pm). N.B. cash payments only. The restaurant also has an online shop selling home-made goods (sauces, pesto, jam etc), as well as beer and wine.;Brunch;[]
6999;Gasthaus Haberl;Austria;Ilz;Walkersdorf 23, Ilz, 8262, Austria;47.0548147;15.925253;78;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The Haberl-Fink family is dedicated and passionate about this inn with a tradition dating back to 1924. Just as the establishment itself is divided into a rustic space with a tiled stove and a chic, modern restaurant, there is also a dual culinary concept: traditional regional fare à la carte or a modern and seasonal set menu ("Fine Dining Menü"). A fantastic selection of wines also awaits, especially for fans of Styrian labels. Wednesday is fish night. Fink's Terrassen-Nest is open in summer during the day, serving a small selection of hot and cold dishes, as well as house-made ice cream. Tip: A variety of delicious food items are available for purchase in the delicatessen. Cakes, pastries and other sweet treats can be pre-ordered to take home.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7000;La Torre;Austria;Sankt Veit an der Glan;Grabenstraße 39, Sankt Veit an der Glan, 9300, Austria;46.7671735;14.3550932;16;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;The keep of the medieval St Veit fortress is a truly remarkable setting. Nestled within the historic walls and surrounded by greenery, the small terrace is a particular highlight. This restaurant is run by husband-and-wife team Rosemarie and Ammar Trabelsi, who create a welcoming atmosphere with a personal touch. The Sicilian presides front-of-house and has charm in his blood. His dapper, old-school style is anything but stuffy. She is in charge of the kitchen and cooks up ambitious Italian and Mediterranean cuisine using select ingredients. Her dishes are pared down to just a few components, allowing their natural flavours to shine through. Turbot with samphire and datterini tomatoes or house-made paccheri with wild prawns, tomatoes and rocket are prime examples. Fish and seafood take centre stage and vary depending on what the market has to offer. The tasting menu is definitely worthwhile, but you can also order à la carte. Italian wine list.;;[]
7001;Seespitz;Austria;Velden am Wörthersee;Schlosspark 1, Velden am Wörthersee, 9220, Austria;46.6124968;14.0435519;33;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;An absolute highlight here is the location right by the lake! The trendy, elegantly designed restaurant flows seamlessly into the terrace – you can take in the lake view from every table. Two creatively inspired slow food set menus are on offer, one of which is vegan. In addition, the menu features classics, including familiar favourites such as Wiener schnitzel. Regional ingredients underpin it all. The wine list is predominantly Austrian, supplemented by Old World and a few New World wines, as well as a selection of sparkling wines. Stylish guestrooms at the Falkensteiner Schlosshotel Velden, to which the restaurant is connected via an underground passageway.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7002;Zazatam;Austria;Vienna;Hillerstraße 11, Vienna, 1020, Austria;48.2206455;16.4067237;18;true;true;Asian Contemporary;Located in the basement of the Zola – Palais de Bohème boutique hotel and accessed via a separate side entrance, this restaurant is not particularly easy to find. The vaulted cellar of the elegant, listed city palace provides a distinctive setting for the restaurant and bar-lounge, which boast a chic and stylish interior design. The cuisine comprises a diverse array of Asian and South American dishes, as well as house-made pasta. The menu includes a "Bites to Share" section that includes hamachi ceviche, XO beef or baozi buns, plus dishes such as piri piri chicken or miso eggplant. Groups of two or more can opt for the "Bit of Everything" tasting menu. You can also sip a classic cocktail or signature drink at the bar.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7003;Buxbaum;Austria;Vienna;Grashofgasse 3, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2103126;16.3761534;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Somewhat tucked away, this restaurant is run with great dedication and has a pleasingly friendly and welcoming atmosphere. The charming front-of-house team serves up appealing dishes such as pike-perch with crayfish, garlic and citrus stock. Tip: wines from selected Austrian vintners.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7005;Edlingers Tempel;Austria;Vienna;Praterstraße 56, Vienna, 1020, Austria;48.21623;16.38746;57;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant is somewhat tucked away, but it's well worth seeking out. The atmosphere is cosy, the service is friendly and the regional cuisine tastes fantastic. Staff may also recommend specials that do not appear on the menu. Be sure to look out for the special set menus that reflect the different seasons. In fine weather, the secluded outdoor area beckons. This place is also a good option for a relaxed lunch.;;[]
7006;Duchardt;Austria;Vienna;Sonnenfelsgasse 17, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2092406;16.3768561;81;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Now with a new name and under new management, this listed building in the centre of the old town has plenty of Viennese charm, as well as a wonderful vaulted ceiling in the restaurant. Having taken over from Walter Bauer, chef-patron Marcus Duchardt proposes his own take on classic cuisine imbued with Austrian and French influences – available à la carte or as a set menu.;Air conditioning;[]
7007;Vestibül;Austria;Vienna;Universitätsring 2, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2107038;16.3613574;86;false;false;International;With a penchant for seasonal and regional produce, this restaurant serves flavoursome culinary delights such as freshwater fish dishes or classics like Wiener schnitzel. The imposing historical building, which also houses the famous Burgtheater, makes for a unique location with a stylish interior that has a typically Viennese feel with its striking columns and gorgeous stuccowork.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7009;Huber's im Fischerwirt;Austria;Salzburg;Peter-Pfenninger-Straße 8, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8192375;13.0128917;38;true;false;Austrian, International;At Andrea and Harald Huber's, hospitality par excellence is the name of the game: a charming, elegant space with various dining areas, exceptionally friendly service, plus tasty dishes that straddle classic and traditional cuisine and draw on regional influences and seasonal ingredients. Tip: Don't miss out on the delicious curd dumplings! There is also a delicatessen selling products such as chocolates, jam and spices.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7010;Bergfried - Chefs Table;Austria;Tux;Lanersbach 483, Tux, 6293, Austria;47.1541685;11.7242537;92;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;You're right in the thick of it here! From the high tables in this stylish little space, you have a constant view of the bustling activity in the kitchen – there's a lot to see! The way the individual dishes are presented is also rather unique: with background music and a proper explanation - the service is somewhat in family hands. All in all, an entertaining evening and a culinary adventure are guaranteed! Chef Sebastian Stock proposes a seven-course set menu (supplemented by two surprise courses). His dishes are modern, clearly structured and made from predominantly locally sourced ingredients. When it comes to wine, you can rely on Franz Stock's recommendations. The best place for an aperitif is the cosy bar of Hotel Bergfried, which houses the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
7011;Esskultur by Unterlechner;Austria;Sankt Jakob in Haus;Reith 23, Sankt Jakob in Haus, 6392, Austria;47.4987541;12.5697804;40;false;true;Contemporary;In this small "adults only" boutique hotel, you will find cosy guestrooms and an attractive restaurant with pale wood furnishings. Owners Christian and Nadja Unterlechner put their heart and soul into making you feel at home – it is clear that good service and a rapport with guests are top priorities here. They serve a three- to six-course set menu packed with sophisticated fare that draws on classical culinary foundations and regional ingredients. The food is served on crockery they produce themselves – pottery is one of the owner's passions, wine is another. You can enjoy the judiciously selected pairings or choose from the interesting wine list yourself.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7012;Neuwirt;Austria;Kitzbühel;Florianigasse 15, Kitzbühel, 6370, Austria;47.4443244;12.3946862;94;true;true;International, Regional Cuisine;There's something for everyone here! The varied menu features "Neuwirt Classics" such as beef roulade with mashed potatoes, alongside more international options like halibut with peas and grapefruit. Along with the good food, you can look forward to a pleasant setting combining modern and Alpine decoration. The terrace beneath the arcades in front of the building is also inviting. Skilful and charming service. The restaurant is located in the Schwarzer Adler hotel.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7013;Altes Gericht;Austria;Sulz;Taverneweg 1, Sulz, 6832, Austria;47.2859482;9.6525645;88;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The building itself is really quite something. Dating back to the 13C, this former courthouse – also known as the Schmiedhaus – has retained its original charm both on the outside and in its five dining areas, which feature plenty of old wood and historical details. A cosy atmosphere prevails throughout. Diners are served cuisine in a classical vein that draws on high-quality ingredients. Think variations of scallop – carpaccio au gratin and crispy scallop on a bed of mango and avocado salad. In summer, the garden planted with chestnut trees makes for a romantic setting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7014;Grünerhof;Austria;Obergurgl;Gaisbergweg 2, Obergurgl, 6456, Austria;46.8684227;11.0259149;84;true;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Young chef Maximilian Grüner's cuisine stays close to nature – his dishes take their cue from what the region and the seasons have to offer, and are served à la carte and in the form of a four- to six-course set menu. Among his appetising dishes are a potato and wild garlic soup served with baked egg and Jerusalem artichokes, and Schlutzkrapfen>/i> (Tyrolean ravioli) with cranberries, Gruyère and beetroot. The owner and her friendly, attentive team run the show front of house. Located in the eponymous hotel, which boasts a central location close to the ski slopes and attractive, cosy guestrooms, the restaurant has a lovely modern decor with an Alpine touch.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7015;Fux;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Omesberg 587, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2072245;10.1390495;79;false;true;Fusion, Asian Influences;This chic restaurant is very much at home in Lech. Behind the large glass-paned façade a tastefully designed space with a modern feel awaits. The open kitchen certainly plays its part – you can watch the chefs from almost anywhere. The cuisine is a fusion of Asian and European – a style to which they have been committed for years. The wine list absolutely deserves a mention, being one of the finest in the country – the Champagne and Burgundy selection leaves nothing to be desired. The bar area is also inviting – ideal for an aperitif or a nightcap.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
7016;Thurnher's Restaurant;Austria;Zürs am Arlberg;Zürs 295, Zürs am Arlberg, 6763, Austria;47.171056;10.1631287;68;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Along with its gorgeous guestrooms and exclusive spa facilities, Thurnher's Alpenhof also houses this fine dining restaurant. The setting is tastefully elegant, and the service team go about their work in a remarkably friendly manner, bringing in a personal touch. Cuisine with classical foundations is served in the evening à la carte and in the form of a set menu. The fine wine list is mainly geared towards Austrian and French labels, but Italy and Germany are also represented. At lunchtime, a more down-to-earth offering is served in the bar, but you can also order dishes from the evening à la carte menu if you wish.;;[]
7017;Rote Wand Stuben;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Zug 5, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2010733;10.115325;84;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This charming restaurant in the Rote Wand Gourmet Hotel serves traditional Austrian cuisine at its best, whether it's a perfectly souffléd Wiener schnitzel, delicious buttermilk pancakes or fabulous fondues! Diners can also look forward to cordial service and an extensive and well-curated selection of wines. At lunchtime, only the bistro is open, serving an à la carte menu. In the evening, culinary tradition is showcased in set menus with different options for each course.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7018;Grunstube Bergblick;Austria;Grän;Am Lumberg 20, Grän, 6673, Austria;47.5130993;10.5588729;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Located just above the village, the Hotel Bergblick not only boasts charming guestrooms and attractive spa facilities, but also has a culinary dimension that is well worth exploring. Opening onto the lobby, bar and lounge, this elegant little restaurant skilfully brings a modern touch to regional style. Large windows afford views of the mountains, as does the terrace. The set menu changes every month and showcases select ingredients and successfully, seamlessly integrating Asian influences. The petits fours are a wonderful finale to the meal. The service is friendly and professional – the enthusiastic chef takes the time to describe his creations tableside. Decent wine list dominated by Austrian labels. Pairings by the glass are available to go with the set menu. An impressive collection of clocks is on display, as is a stylish 1912 French vintage car – complete with MICHELIN tyres!;Car park,Terrace;[]
7019;Reznicek;Austria;Vienna;Reznicekgasse 10, Vienna, 1090, Austria;48.2282671;16.3574231;59;false;true;Austrian, Regional Cuisine;All you would hope for from a contemporary-minded traditional inn! The regional and seasonal cuisine, which takes inspiration from classic Austrian fare, showcases carefully selected ingredients and impressive craftsmanship. Diners delight in dishes such as beef soup with shredded pancakes, organic char meunière, Backfleisch (breaded and fried meat) and Palatschinken (crêpes), as well as a selection of increasingly hard to find offal dishes. The extensive and well-curated wine list includes an appealing range of wines by the glass. Service comes courtesy of the friendly and attentive front-of-house team. Guests are seated at simply yet elegantly laid tables in an inviting dining space with all the charm of a Viennese tavern. Be sure to cast an eye over the well-stocked cheese display case.;Interesting wine list;[]
7020;LAGANA;Austria;Villach;Europaplatz 1, Villach, 9500, Austria;46.61497;13.85113;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in Hotel Voco, this elegant restaurant adjoins the bar and has a hip and modern feel. It draws a good crowd with its delightfully lively atmosphere and gorgeous riverfront setting. Opt for the fine dining set menu or order sophisticated international creations and regional classics à la carte. The delicious dishes showcase select produce such as the fantastic lamb or the excellent scallops. Short but well-curated wine list.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7021;Lamark - Stube;Austria;Fügenberg;Hochfügen 34, Fügenberg, 6264, Austria;47.2704088;11.7774346;52;false;false;Farm to table;Located right next to the cable car station, Hotel Lamark is run by Alexander Fankhauser. The restaurant boasts a number of cosy, tastefully designed dining areas with classic Alpine-style decor. The varied menu features both traditional regional fare and more ambitious creations to be ordered à la carte or as part of a set menu. Options include veal lights in a Riesling sauce, Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) with all the trimmings and confit char fillet with pointed cabbage, greaves dumplings and a mustard sauce. There is also a fine selection of wines. Affording panoramic views, the terrace is a delightful spot all year round.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7022;AURUM;Austria;Gmunden;Linzer Straße 4, Gmunden, 4810, Austria;47.9180833;13.8032904;44;false;false;Sharing, Contemporary;Located in the centre of Gmunden, the long-standing Zum Goldenen Hirschen dates back to the 17C. Now a tastefully designed boutique hotel, it is showcasing its interesting culinary side with this appealing restaurant. It serves a set menu that lends itself to sharing: Three courses comprising a total of 12 dishes demonstrate fine craftsmanship and the premium quality of the selected ingredients. The service is very friendly and attentive – the chef enjoys bringing out the dishes himself. Be sure to peruse the nicely curated wine list. There is also much to admire in the setting: A distinctive brick vaulted ceiling, gorgeous hardwood floors and a pleasingly understated yet chic modern style foster harmonious feel.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7023;Animo by Aigner;Austria;Salzburg;Nonntaler Hauptstraße 55, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7860554;13.0522014;36;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Having worked together at Hangar 7, Elisabeth (Lizzy) and Jakob Aigner have now opened their own place here, introducing a charming new concept to the area. While he presides front-of-house, providing friendly and attentive service and astute wine recommendations, she prepares Mediterranean fare in the kitchen. Made from the finest ingredients, her dishes are flavoursome and unfussy – the offerings are written up on a blackboard. The terrace is delightful in summer.;Terrace;[]
7024;Bistro Südsee by Hubert Wallner;Austria;Maria Wörth;Süduferstraße 258, Maria Wörth, 9082, Austria;46.6230864;14.1177091;39;false;true;Regional European;Here, on the southern shore of Wörthersee, you could almost fancy yourself in the South Pacific. This beach restaurant enjoys a gorgeous lakeside location, where the reeds sway to the beat of the trendy background music. Relaxed bistro atmosphere, friendly down-to-earth service and good food including regional classics such as house-made Carinthian Kasnudeln (cheese dumplings) and Mediterranean specialities like freshly made pasta or fish dishes. How about a nice cocktail to top it off?;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7025;muto;Austria;Linz;Altstadt 7, Linz, 4020, Austria;48.3050902;14.2845502;60;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;This charming establishment is situated in a pedestrian area in the old town of Linz. A few steps lead down from the entrance to a brightly lit, vaulted room done out in a modern and minimalist style. The creative cuisine playfully experiments with textures and flavours – hence the restaurant's name, which is derived from the Latin verb mutare (meaning "to change"). The service is really friendly and pleasingly informal – the front-of-house team keeps things casual in its interactions with guests. Tip for motorists: You can park at the Garage Promenade.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7026;Hofmeisterei Hirtzberger;Austria;Wösendorf in der Wachau;Hauptstraße 74, Wösendorf in der Wachau, 3610, Austria;48.3806485;15.4555237;38;false;false;European Contemporary;This building has a long history. Built in 1320, it was originally part of a monastery – Stift St Florian. Today, it is home to a charming and elegant restaurant with a lovely vaulted ceiling. Drawing on Asian influences, the food here is a contemporary take on classic cuisine. As an alternative to the two set menus, a number of classic dishes can be ordered à la carte, and everything is prepared using select ingredients. The fantastic wine list includes an enticing selection of champagnes and Veltliners.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7027;Der Holzpoldl;Austria;Lichtenberg;Am Holzpoldlgut 2, Lichtenberg, 4040, Austria;48.3620798;14.2397355;39;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Manuel Grabner and Claudia Stiglitz describe their concept as a "culinary balancing act between a country inn and a fine dining restaurant". This applies as much to the decor (a blend of traditional and modern) as to the cuisine. Their ambitious tasting menu comprises three to eight courses (eg black halibut "Caprese", tomatoes, pepperwort, spicy burrata caramel) and there is also a sophisticated à la carte selection including classics such as sirloin steak from Simmental beef. The well-curated wine list displays a certain inclination towards Austrian picks, but it also includes international wines.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7028;Liebsteinsky;Austria;Vienna;Schubertring 6, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2027405;16.3754407;78;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Behind the large windows of this pleasant restaurant located between the opera house and the Stadtpark, a charming bistro atmosphere reigns in the airy, high-ceilinged room. The food is presented in two formats: at lunchtime, people come for the casual, no-frills "Business Lunch" deal that won't break the bank, in the evening, the modern dishes and a tasting menu comprising four or six courses take things up a notch in the sophistication stakes. Whether in the "miso salmon - Label Rouge fillet, pan-seared, celery, beetroot & sea asparagus" or "Wiener schnitzel, potato and cucumber salad & cranberry", only the finest ingredients are used.;Air conditioning;[]
7029;Am Mahrbach;Austria;Königsdorf;Apfelstraße 4, Königsdorf, 7563, Austria;47.0234596;16.1864262;62;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine;This U-shaped property is set in a quiet and secluded location in the Königsdorf mountains, surrounded by meadows, forests and greenery – a setting that provides the perfect backdrop for Cathrin Maric and Philipp Kroboth to live out their concept of sustainability and self-sufficiency. On their organic farm, they grow vegetables, fruit and herbs, keep goats and chickens, and source honey from their own bees. Remaining ingredients are sourced from like-minded producers in the immediate vicinity. The seasonal set menu features punchy dishes that showcase the ingredients, with beautifully paired wines available on request. When he can, the owner is glad to explain his organic philosophy to guests in person. Housed in the former stables of the farm, the space is attractive: modern design, wood and stone, a visible kitchen, and floor-to-ceiling windows with an unobstructed view of the outside. The owner also runs her veterinary practice next to the restaurant.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7030;Langwies Wirtshaus;Austria;Bad Vigaun;Langwies 22, Bad Vigaun, 5424, Austria;47.6642356;13.123855;49;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Austrian;A self-proclaimed "lodge hotel for gourmets", Langwies Wirtshaus combines several facilities under one roof: a restaurant, a spa hotel, a conference centre and long-stay apartments. The menu features a contemporary selection of regional classics, steaks and seasonal dishes, as well as vegan and vegetarian options. There are several attractive dining spaces – for example, you can book a table in the cosy, spruce-panelled bay room.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7031;Petrus Café Brasserie;Austria;Bregenz;Anton-Schneider-Straße 11, Bregenz, 6900, Austria;47.5036434;9.7478692;100;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;The popularity of this place is down to the pleasant combination of café and brasserie, the great location in the centre of the old town – and the delicious food. In this centuries-old building (in which it started out as an inn in 1911), in a charming, understated decor, guests enjoy dishes such as beef tartare, pasta, risotto or coq au vin, and then of course there is the house speciality: mussels. Sandwiches are also available at lunchtime. In addition to wine, they serve beer from Belgium, where the owner and his wife lived for a time. The terrace in front of this building in a pedestrianised area is also a nice feature. Tip for motorists: parking at the Rathaus-Parkplatz 50m away.;Terrace;[]
7032;Tiroler Hof;Austria;Kufstein;Am Rain 16, Kufstein, 6330, Austria;47.5932504;12.1818251;72;false;false;Austrian, Regional Cuisine;This pleasant family-run restaurant set in a rather remote location near the German border is well worth the detour. It has a few surprises in store on account of its interesting two-part menu: turn to "Papa Fritz's Wirtshausklassiker" for traditional Austrian cuisine, or opt for "Viktoria Fahringers Fine Dining Karte" for rather more elaborate and creative dishes. Both options make use of carefully selected local ingredients – excellent quality is guaranteed. Take your pick from a selection of Austrian wines. The restaurant is located in the Viktorias Home hotel, which offers lovely apartments for overnight stays.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7033;Die Weinbank - Wirtshaus;Austria;Ehrenhausen;Hauptstraße 44, Ehrenhausen, 8461, Austria;46.7242993;15.5857278;16;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Gerhard Fuchs and Christian Zach opened this tavern as a counterpoint to their fine dining restaurant. Serving seasonal dishes made with regional produce, the concept has proven to be a hit. Gerhard Fuchs brings many years of culinary experience to the table, and the team led by passionate sommelier and host Christian Zach provides attentive service with Styrian charm. Flavoursome dishes such as Leutschach pata negra pork brisket with chanterelle mushrooms and gnocchi with herbs can be accompanied by wine – the list comprises over 4 000 labels – or beer. The interior design is a modern take on rustic style, and there is also a lovely vine-covered terrace. Tip: Due to the popularity of this place, reservations are recommended. Delicious food items and wines can be purchased to take home. The name "Weinbank" is apt: you can hire lockers in which to store your fine wine purchases.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7034;Landgasthaus Essl;Austria;Rossatz;Rührsdorf 17, Rossatz, 3602, Austria;48.398929;15.4844758;54;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Located in the village centre, this delightful inn has an inviting and cosy atmosphere. Pale wood panelling and finishings lend the spruce interior a rustic charm, and the covered garden is a popular spot during the warmer months. The food is regional and seasonal – options range from hearty classics such as Rahmbeuscherl (veal lights ragout) or Backhenderl (breaded fried chicken) to a more sophisticated set menu.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7035;Seerestaurant 1884;Austria;Millstatt;Seestraße 68, Millstatt, 9872, Austria;46.8017098;13.5752268;71;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;As the name suggests, this restaurant enjoys a splendid location. Housed in the long-established See-Villa hotel, right by Lake Millstatt, it has a wonderful terrace that extends right to the water's edge! The elegant interior has floor-to-ceiling windows affording unobstructed views of the lake. The menu is rather diverse, featuring international, regional, traditional, seasonal fare – game and freshly caught fish from the lake take centre stage. The bar in the middle of the restaurant is sure to draw the eye.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace;[]
7036;echt JAN AIGNER;Austria;Gleisdorf;Franz-Josef-Straße 7, Gleisdorf, 8200, Austria;47.1035042;15.7119093;27;false;true;International, Regional Cuisine;Housed in forumKLOSTER, a seminar and events centre, this is a modern and trendy restaurant with artistic decor that would be right at home in a city such as Graz or Vienna. Jan Aigner serves up dishes that draw on international influences and showcase regional and seasonal produce – you can order à la carte or take a punt on the surprise menu. The wine and beverage list is presented in digital form. Friendly and attentive service. There is also a bar and a terrace. Tip for motorists: There is a public car park next door (charges apply until 6pm).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7037;Steirerschlössl;Austria;Zeltweg;Hauptstraße 100, Zeltweg, 8740, Austria;47.1908127;14.746898;55;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This elegant restaurant is located in an attractive Art Nouveau villa in manicured gardens. Beneath the high ceiling, take a seat at beautifully laid tables and relish the friendly, attentive service. The restaurant serves contemporary cuisine made with seasonal ingredients in the form of an à la carte or set menu. The reasonably priced lunch menu is popular. There is a charming terrace with a view of the countryside. Tasteful guestrooms are available for overnight stays in a separate guesthouse and the premises are close to the Red Bull Ring Formula 1 racetrack.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7039;Zum Tischlerwirt;Austria;Reith bei Kitzbühel;Kitzbühler Straße 46, Reith bei Kitzbühel, 6370, Austria;47.4734499;12.3445947;17;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This 150-year-old inn is already an institution in the neighbourhood. Owner Michael "Michi" Naschberger and head chef Milan Hurt are now at the helm, and have introduced a pleasingly relaxed and informal atmosphere, while preserving the traditional charm of the place. Tyrolean cuisine with high standards is the name of the game, eg "Beef Tartare Tischlerwirt" or "grilled veal liver, apple, bacon and onion sauce, parsnip". Rustic wood and a decorative fireplace retain the traditional charm, injected with the odd modern touch. Head for the delightful terrace in front of the house.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7041;Zum Goldenen Hirschen;Austria;Gmunden;Linzer Straße 4, Gmunden, 4810, Austria;47.918076;13.8033234;87;true;false;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;In the centre of Gmunden is this venerable place, an inn dating back to 1624 that is now a boutique hotel and restaurant. Chef Christoph Parzer's craftsmanship is apparent as he prepares fresh ingredients that go into traditional dishes as well as more modern creations – for example, in addition to "Heimischer Tafelspitz im Kuperpfand'l" (local beef boiled in a copper pan), you will also find wild-caught pike-perch, peas, mussels in a beurre blanc sauce, couscous, lovage, black cabbage. They also serve a range of steaks. In keeping with this spirit of eclecticism, the interior also mixes and matches styles: traditional features such as the wooden ceiling and tiled stove meet modern furnishings. Pretty terrace in the courtyard. The lunchtime menu is smaller. Austria is particularly well represented when it comes to the wines.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7042;Keplingerwirt;Austria;Sankt Johann am Wimberg;Sankt Johann am Wimberg 14, Sankt Johann am Wimberg, 4172, Austria;48.4878964;14.1309306;34;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant, which has been run as a family business since 1938, is the beating heart of this modern hotel with welcoming guestrooms. Diners can expect a refined atmosphere and exceedingly friendly service, as well as delicious food prepared by a kitchen brigade headed up by chef Andrea Lunson, sister of owner Heinz Keplinger. On the menu: traditional dishes such as Kalbsrahmbeuscherl (creamed chopped calf's lights) with bread dumpling, but also more modern fare, eg fillet of Piberbach salmon trout in a ratatouille broth with Erbsentascherl (pea pasties) and a coconut-chilli foam.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7044;Ratschen;Austria;Deutsch Schützen;Am Ratschen 5, Deutsch Schützen, 7474, Austria;47.1649451;16.426556;28;false;false;Contemporary;Set in a gorgeous location amid the vineyards, this is an interesting concept combining a restaurant, bistro and charming wooden bungalows for overnight stays. The restaurant is contemporary in style and serves a modern four- to seven-course set menu featuring bold dishes that are brimming with flavour. Nab a table by the floor-to-ceiling windows and take in the stunning views. Tip: At weekends, you can also eat here at lunchtime – there is a smaller à la carte selection including dishes from the evening menu, plus classics such as clear beef soup with liver dumplings.;Car park;[]
7045;Poll's Kaiserterrasse - Gourmet Restaurant im Weissen Rössl;Austria;Sankt Wolfgang im Salzkammergut;Markt 74, Sankt Wolfgang im Salzkammergut, 5360, Austria;47.73793;13.44813;65;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The spectacular lakeside location at Wolfgangsee is one of the main draws of this place. Combined with the stunning views of the lake and mountains, the classically elegant decor and live piano music in the background make for a truly romantic atmosphere. Incorporating local produce and drawing on classic and modern influences, the food is equally impressive. Diners have a choice of three set menus: "Poll's Menü", "Rössl Menü" and "Fondue Erlebnis" (must be pre-ordered). Overnight accommodation is available at Romantik Hotel Im Weissen Rössl, which also houses this restaurant.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
7046;das Schrei;Austria;Salzburg;Rudolf-Biebl-Straße 3A, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8066;13.0269139;36;true;false;Creative, Austrian;Jakob Schmid and Daniel Reifecker are the pair at the helm – an owner and chef duo who take real pleasure in their work here in a somewhat inconspicuous location outside the town centre. They rustle up a surprise menu with four to seven courses (a vegetarian version is also available if ordered in advance) including dishes such as "Enoki. Potato. Onion" or "Salzburg prawn. Pea. Tomato", for example, that demonstrate creativity and terrific ingredient quality. The friendly team competently explains the dishes to you. The food is accompanied by wines, non-alcoholic drinks or a mixture of both. The atmosphere is relaxed and unpretentious. In good weather, they also set up tables on the terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7047;Zur Dankbarkeit;Austria;Podersdorf am See;Hauptstraße 39, Podersdorf am See, 7141, Austria;47.8524495;16.8394633;32;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Steeped in tradition, this inn in the centre of Podersdorf has been run by the same family for four generations. Their attachment to the region is reflected in delicious dishes such as Kalbsrahmbeuschel (veal lights ragout) with bread dumplings, which are made with ingredients from the owner's native Burgenland. The establishment also boasts its own winery, a nearby wine tavern (open Fri, Sat and Sun) and five cosy and inviting double rooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7048;Das Loewenzahn;Austria;Weissensee;Neusach 46, Weissensee, 9762, Austria;46.7160581;13.3216433;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;There are several reasons why you feel at home here: first, there is the charming decor, which is fresh and contemporary yet retains a certain regional flavour, plus the terrace with a lovely view over the lake. Secondly, the food – you can expect cuisine that, although of a regional bent, is also open to international influences. Served in the form of a five- to eight-course set menu, the dishes, such as "octopus, cauliflower, Amalfi lemon, saffron" or "lamb, meadow herbs, tomato, romaine lettuce", always have a modern, creative twist. And then there are your friendly hosts Jakob and Lilly Lilg, who make sure each guest feels well looked after.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7049;Endlich;Austria;Sankt Anton am Arlberg;Dorfstraße 61, Sankt Anton am Arlberg, 6580, Austria;47.1314269;10.268581;91;false;true;Scandinavian, Contemporary;Coming here is like being invited to dine with good friends in their home – such is the feeling conveyed by your very friendly hosts, Henrik Helmuth Olsen and Henriette Hansen, who are the couple at the helm here. In their modern, tastefully decorated restaurant, the Danish-born owners create an incredibly charming, intimate atmosphere and make a point of doting on their guests. There is no menu or wine list. Instead, Henrik prepares a surprise menu made up of three courses, while Henriette is on hand to recommend the wines to best accompany your meal.;;[]
7050;Stammtisch am Paulustor;Austria;Graz;Paulustorgasse 8, Graz, 8010, Austria;47.075021;15.4403679;68;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Near the Hauptplatz, this spruce historical building – once part of the city's defensive wall – now accommodates this chic restaurant. The interior decor sees a beautiful, bright vaulted ceiling successfully combined with clean-lined modern design and pops of colour. The menu features delicious, freshly prepared dishes such as carpaccio of Styrian Alpine ox, veal Wiener schnitzel or steaks cooked on the charcoal grill. From Wednesday to Friday, there is a two-course "Stammtisch Lunch" deal as well as an a la carte selection. The articulate, polite team provides brisk service and is happy to advise you. The terrace in the inner courtyard is also pleasant. Tip: In summer they offer BBQ on Wednesdays. Plus: monthly visit of a guest winemaker including a set menu with wine accompaniment.;Terrace;[]
7051;Gasthaus Csencsits;Austria;Kohfidisch;Harmisch 13, Kohfidisch, 7512, Austria;47.1487613;16.3811117;88;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;There is a good reason why so many diners are drawn to this tranquil, rural village nestled among forests and meadows right by the Hungarian border. Jürgen and Melanie Csencsits run an upscale restaurant that maintains an inviting, laid-back feel. In a kitchen centred on an old wood-fired oven that is core to their culinary philosophy, the chef-patron and his team prepare a seasonal five- to seven-course set menu. Based on produce from the surrounding area, the cuisine mirrors the chef's strong connection to his Pannonian heritage. The charming proprietress manages the service team, who recommend excellent wine pairings by the glass. The extensive wine list is also well worth exploring. Delightful covered wooden terrace. Tip: Ask about their popular Buschenschank evenings, on which good, simple food is served (summer only).;Car park,Terrace;[]
7052;Triad;Austria;Bad Schönau;Ödhöfen 25, Bad Schönau, 2853, Austria;47.4986873;16.2253774;75;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Innovative;Drawing on their experience at renowned restaurants and hotels, Veronika and Uwe Machreich run this idyllic establishment in a quiet, rural village setting. They have a lovingly tended garden that provides herbs and vegetables for the kitchen. The cuisine strikes a good balance between traditional and innovative elements. A shorter version of the evening menu is available at lunchtime – it features modern dishes with a twist, such as Waldviertel organic chicken, pepper and corn pancake and pimientos de Padrón. At lunchtime, delicious options on the "Wirtshauskarte" menu include Kalbsrahmbeuschl (veal lights ragout) or Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy). Or why not take a punt on the surprise menu? There is also a small farm shop selling delicatessen and house-made items. Overnight accommodation available.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7053;Gut Purbach;Austria;Purbach am Neusiedler See;Hauptgasse 64, Purbach am Neusiedler See, 7083, Austria;47.9120197;16.6964466;18;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This beautifully restored 16C farmhouse first became an inn in 1860. Today, it is a modern restaurant serving delicious regional cuisine.;Terrace;[]
7054;Walserstuba;Austria;Riezlern;Eggstraße 2, Riezlern, 6991, Austria;47.3555882;10.1776801;34;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Diners immediately feel at home here! This is thanks to both the cosy atmosphere and the outstanding cuisine turned out by owner Jeremias Riezler, who has embraced a sustainable culinary approach. He uses top-notch seasonal and regional produce, and even rears pigs himself. Select – predominantly organic – ingredients are showcased in a multi-course set menu, the name of which translates as "Culinary Mountain Adventure". Dishes such as fried Walser veal sweetbreads with cranberry aioli demonstrate a distinctive culinary style. The chef presents his dishes himself and talks diners through the idea behind them. In an original touch, he also hand-carves the wooden cutlery with which some of the dishes are eaten. Your hostess heads up a charming front-of-house team. The hotel of the same name provides cosy Alpine-style rooms for overnight stays – the establishment as a whole is certified organic.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7055;DiningRuhm;Austria;Vienna;Lambrechtgasse 9, Vienna, 1040, Austria;48.1903564;16.3647424;54;false;true;Fusion, Japanese Contemporary;Housed in a corner plot building in an inconspicuous location in the 4th district, this restaurant serves an interesting mix of Nippon and Nikkei cuisine – ie Japanese- and Peruvian-inspired dishes are in the spotlight. This unpretentious cuisine also goes wonderfully well with the interior, which is decked out in warm colours and characterised by modern lines. The sushi bar is located in one of the three rooms. Try the delicious finger food, sushi (including lobster nigiri with a creamy spicy sauce) or main courses such as black cod yuzu miso. Attentive service from staff who also provide good wine recommendations from a selection that highlights Austrian labels. Unless you would prefer a sake…;Terrace;[]
7056;Kellerbauer;Austria;Bad Vigaun;Kellerbauerweg 41, Bad Vigaun, 5424, Austria;47.6715364;13.1336973;79;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Your congenial hosts Roman and Maria Mailänder represent the second generation of their family at the helm. They put their heart and soul into running this establishment that is typical for the region, and the service is friendly and welcoming. Imbued with the rustic charm of the Alps and adorned with decorative paintings, the ambience is warm and inviting. Alexander Rettenbacher is in charge of the kitchen and devises two three- to five-course set menus – there are one or two alternative main courses available. The cuisine is modern and seasonal, drawing on regional and Mediterranean influences. Vegetables and herbs from the restaurant's own garden are also used. The west-facing terrace affords views of the surrounding countryside and is a lovely spot from which to enjoy a beautiful sunset. There are a few guestrooms available next door.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7057;OPUS;Austria;Vienna;Kärntner Ring 16, Vienna, 1050, Austria;48.2010311;16.3733435;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is decorated in the style of the Wiener Werkstätte of the 1930s and located in the prestigious historical building that is home to the Hotel Imperial, which has been an integral part of Viennese life since opening in 1873. This is the elegant backdrop against which diners enjoy classic cuisine with seasonal influences. A five-course tasting menu in two versions (omnivore and vegetarian) is served, as well as an à la carte selection. Friendly and professional service.;Wheelchair access;[]
7058;Lackner;Austria;Mondsee;Mondseestraße 1, Mondsee, 5310, Austria;47.8502905;13.343336;17;false;false;Farm to table;The splendid location of this restaurant with a wonderful terrace overlooking Mondsee is as much of a draw as the cuisine of chef-patron Martin Lackner. His dishes have classical leanings and take their cue from the seasons. The quality of the ingredients – many from the region – is exceptional. Order the set menu or à la carte, taking your pick from appetising dishes such as "Hausruck beef tartare, ciabatta-parmesan ice cream, oven-baked tomato". The in-house wine shop is also worth a look. For overnight guests, Seehotel Lackner offers tasteful guestrooms, a beautiful spa and sauna area, plus direct access to the lake.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7059;HAUSBAR Wien;Austria;Vienna;Karlsplatz 5, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2004921;16.3717561;45;true;false;Vegetarian;Tucked away in the basement of the remarkable Künstlerhaus, this appealing modern restaurant also boasts a gorgeous covered terrace in the inner courtyard. The friendly team delivers an imaginative take on vegetarian cuisine (vegan options also available) in the form of a set menu, whose seven courses are only hinted at with pictures of the main ingredients. The waitstaff then proudly talk you through the dishes at your table. If you want meat or fish, you can also order a main course that suits you in advance. A range of perfectly paired cocktails and a fairly priced wine list complete the picture.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7060;Floh;Austria;Langenlebarn;Tullner Straße 1, Langenlebarn, 3425, Austria;48.3325461;16.1152771;42;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Tapping into the region is the name of the game here. In an inviting traditional inn atmosphere, diners tuck into delicious, aromatic dishes that are true to the local ingredients used. There is a wide selection of vegetarian, meat and fish dishes, as well as the classics of this type of establishment. Choosing a wine is no mean feat either – there is a separate menu for Veltliners, white wines, red wines, foreign wines and magnum bottles.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7061;Frierss Feines Haus;Austria;Villach;Gewerbezeile 2b, Villach, 9500, Austria;46.6044885;13.8698696;16;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Fusion;The Frierss family are renowned for their sausages and other meat products. These wares are on site in their butcher's shop and well-stocked delicatessen, and are also to be found on the menu in this modern restaurant. Barbecued steaks feature among the mouth-watering specialities of the house, but there are fish and vegetarian options prepared in the open kitchen. Good selection of wines. A budget-friendly lunch deal is available, too. The staff are incredibly dedicated and friendly. Tip: You can also have breakfast here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7062;Aurea;Austria;Villach;Paracelsusgasse 6, Villach, 9500, Austria;46.6141706;13.8452767;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Alexandra Debre and Armin Rauscher, the dedicated duo behind this fine little restaurant in a side street in the centre of Villach, are elevating the city's culinary scene with their expertise. In the open-plan kitchen, the chef-patron prepares an ambitious three- to five-course set menu. The modern and creative dishes, such as "pumpkin/Thai seasonings/ coconut/BBQ", or "beef/ravioli/horseradish/spinac", are crafted with impressive precision and finesse, using select ingredients. The charming hostess provides service with a personal touch – supported by the chef, who likes to bring his dishes to the table himself – and helps to create a pleasingly intimate and laid-back atmosphere in this upscale modern restaurant.;;[]
7063;Bär & Schaf Wirtschaft;Austria;Völkermarkt;2.-Mai-Straße 18, Völkermarkt, 9100, Austria;46.6603258;14.6362701;33;false;false;Regional Cuisine;What started as a pop-up has now become a permanent fixture in the historical Gasthaus zum Prinz Johann. The proprietor duo, Martin Nuart and Philipp Medved, offer their guests a very personal dining experience. Philipp manages things front-of-house with delightful ease, friendliness, and proficiency, while Martin heads up the sustainability-focused kitchen. His intriguing plant-forward set menu showcases select seasonal ingredients from his family's own farm or neighbouring agricultural producers. In terms of wine, Austria takes centre stage, and is accompanied by offerings from Slovenia and Italy. The setting is wonderfully inviting – with lovely old floorboards, simple wooden benches and chairs and decorative contemporary artwork, the historical charm of the centuries-old inn has been retained with style.;Terrace;[]
7064;Schmidhofer im Palais;Austria;Graz;Sackstraße 16, Graz, 8010, Austria;47.072329;15.4367765;30;false;true;International, Austrian;In close proximity to the Graz Museum, this restaurant has a tasteful, modern interior and a high vaulted ceiling. The street view from the tables right by the window means you can watch the world go by as you eat. The terrace in the courtyard is wonderful in summer. International dishes such as "tuna sashimi rolls meet tuna tartare" are served, as well as Austrian dishes such as the impeccably prepared Wiener schnitzel – the salad of Graz-grown butterhead lettuce is a great accompaniment. The extremely polite and attentive service – the team is always on hand with a smile – also contributes to the pleasant atmosphere.;Terrace;[]
7065;Kolm;Austria;Arbesbach;Schönfeld 18, Arbesbach, 3925, Austria;48.4805947;14.926603;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Here in the natural surroundings of the Waldviertel region, you can enjoy not only the beautiful view of the surrounding area but also the ambitious cuisine of Michael Kolm and his team. The dishes are rooted in the region but with a cosmopolitan edge, as demonstrated by creations such as veal fillet, ravioli, wild broccoli, and hamachi, rutabaga, avocado. You can choose between the set menus – "Bärentrail Menu" and vegetarian "Animal-Friendly Menu" – and à la carte options. The service team is pleasant, cordial and competent – the first appetisers are plated in the restaurant itself. The bright, friendly ambience is aptly described as "casual". In winter, the fireplace is lit for a cosy feel. Interesting fact: The Bärenwald bear sanctuary run by the Four Paws association is right next door. Considering staying overnight? There are five lodges a little way down, set in the greenery.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7067;Umar Fisch;Austria;Vienna;Naschmarkt Stand 76, Vienna, 1040, Austria;48.19883;16.36344;73;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Here at the famous Naschmarkt, the name "Umar" is synonymous with the freshest fish. The establishment has housed a fish shop since the mid-90s and this simple restaurant since 2003. It owes its success to the quality of the fish, which is served in the form of classic dishes.;Terrace;[]
7068;Skopik & Lohn;Austria;Vienna;Leopoldsgasse 17, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2199;16.37657;29;false;true;Austrian;The first thing you’ll notice here is the wonderful painted ceiling, the work of artist Otto Zitko. The service is friendly and attentive, the food flavoursome and the Austrian classics on the menu include Wiener schnitzel with cucumber, potato and sour cream salad and, for dessert, perhaps an île flottante?;Terrace;[]
7069;Zum weissen Rauchfangkehrer;Austria;Vienna;Weihburggasse 4, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2070109;16.3724136;73;false;true;Austrian;This cosy restaurant is divided into four traditionally decorated rooms – in one of them, gentle piano music provides the soundtrack to your evening meal. Delicious Austrian cuisine is the order of the day, including house specialities such as "Rauchfangkehrers Wiener Schnitzel". The wine list is exclusively Austrian and organised according to grape variety.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7070;Le Salzgries Paris;Austria;Vienna;Marc-Aurel-Straße 6, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.212151;16.3732997;34;false;false;Classic French;A slice of Paris in Vienna? Mais, oui! This lively brasserie with a distinctly chic feel has become an institution in the city and – in no small part thanks to patron and chef Denis König – brings to life the concepts of "bistronomie" and savoir-vivre. If you are a fan of fresh seafood, then you've come to the right place: just order the plateau de fruits de mer! The beef tartare is another fine example of the French classics served here. In the evening, you can also choose an even more refined and creative five-course set menu. An exclusively French wine selection and charming service contribute to that Parisian feeling.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7071;UNKAI;Austria;Vienna;Kärntner Ring 9, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2021646;16.3717668;39;true;true;Japanese;A pleasantly light and modern restaurant where you can eat either at authentic teppanyaki grill tables or more conventionally. You will also find the Unkai sushi bar on the ground floor serving a sushi brunch on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
7072;Silva;Austria;Leogang;Hütten 2, Leogang, 5771, Austria;47.4395038;12.7156114;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic French;What must be one of the smallest fine dining restaurants in the country awaits you at Naturhotel Forsthofgut. With space for just 10 diners and stylish interior design, the place has an air of exclusivity. Michael Helfrich is in charge of the kitchen and serves up creative modern dishes that showcase the flavours of the forest. The menu takes its cue from the changing seasons – fermentation and smoking also play a role. The drink pairings are excellent – with or without alcohol.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7073;Gasthof Schloss Aigen;Austria;Salzburg;Schwarzenbergpromenade 37, Salzburg, 5026, Austria;47.7865085;13.0882589;22;false;false;Austrian, Traditional Cuisine;The history of this place dates all the way back to 1402! The kitchen team puts a modern spin on traditional Austrian cuisine, and diners can opt for a set menu or order dishes à la carte. Our tip: Try the boiled beef, which is prepared in a range of different ways. The charming interior is tastefully decorated and exudes an appealing family atmosphere. In summer, don't miss the gorgeous terrace laid out in the courtyard beneath the boughs of the chestnut trees.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7074;Brunnauer;Austria;Salzburg;Fürstenallee 5, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7902425;13.0475544;65;false;true;French, Country cooking;In the lovely historical setting of Villa Ceconi, Sybille and Richard Brunnauer's restaurant is the place to experience fantastic Austrian-style hospitality and cuisine. The dishes draw on French and international influences but give pride of place to the region and the seasons – vegan options included. Tip: reasonably priced lunch set menu. Attractive and stylishly modern interior and a fabulous view of the fortress from the terrace!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7075;Gasthof Auerhahn;Austria;Salzburg;Bahnhofstraße 15, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8205102;13.0485187;21;false;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Run with great dedication, this friendly, family-owned restaurant is located at a slight remove from the city centre, close to the train station, but it's well worth making the detour for the excellent food. The cuisine is regional, seasonal and pleasingly down-to-earth. Their appealing range of dishes includes venison ragout with bread dumplings and chanterelles, as well as delicious desserts such as Topfenknödel (curd dumplings). Order à la carte or opt for the set menu, which comprises three to five courses – a vegetarian version is also available. Dine in the inviting interior or out on the charming terrace to the rear of the building. The adjoining hotel has well-appointed guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7076;Rauter Stube;Austria;Matrei in Osttirol;Rauterplatz 3, Matrei in Osttirol, 9971, Austria;47.0012723;12.5387091;22;true;true;Regional Cuisine, International;An establishment run with dedication by the Obwexer family in a building steeped in history. Old paintings, wood panelling and a tiled stove lend plenty of charm and a certain elegance to the refined, rustic-style decor of this restaurant. Diners take their seats at beautifully laid tables to enjoy pleasingly informal service that includes reliable wine recommendations courtesy of owner Michael Obwexer – you will discover his enthusiasm for Austrian, Italian and French wine estates. In the kitchen, Max van Triel is the man behind flavourful dishes such as pan-fried fillet of turbot, with spinach, horseradish, hazelnut and lemon ravioli… and classic Wiener schnitzel. Opt for the tasting menu or order à la carte. You may also like to spend the night in style at the Hotel Rauter.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7077;Gasthaus Stern;Austria;Vienna;Braunhubergasse 6, Vienna, 1110, Austria;48.1711942;16.4171726;50;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Tucked away in a residential area at a remove from the tourist trail, this restaurant is well worth the detour. In keeping with its charming traditional decor – the floorboards, wooden panelling on the walls and high ceilings evoke the atmosphere of an old-style Viennese inn – it proposes straightforward and delicious regional cuisine, which is popular with locals too. In addition to classic dishes such as Wiener schnitzel, offal and game take pride of place on the menu – the chef is a keen hunter himself. Check out the "Stern im Glas" range for delicious options to enjoy at home.;Air conditioning;[]
7078;FinESSEN;Austria;Kaprun;Tauern Spa Platz 1, Kaprun, 5710, Austria;47.2833164;12.7603943;32;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Located at TAUERN SPA wellness hotel, this small, chic contemporary-style restaurant is separate from the hotel but accessible from inside it. Seating is limited to 14 diners, who are served a six-course ingredient-led seasonal set menu in which ambitious chef Christof Schernthaner showcases the finest produce from the region. Wine pairings are available on request. You can also look forward to friendly service – the chef serves and explains his dishes personally.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7080;Der Luis;Austria;Anger;Hauptplatz 3, Anger, 8184, Austria;47.2737546;15.6892879;91;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Luis Thaller represents the sixth generation of his family to run this establishment, which has been going since 1875. Made primarily from locally sourced ingredients, the dishes served here are sophisticated and packed with flavour. These are presented in the form of an ambitious surprise menu comprising four to seven courses. The chef's signature dish is the farm-fresh egg with celeriac, greaves and pig's head. To complement your meal, there is a good selection of wines and non-alcoholic beverages. The restaurant is housed in Der Thaller hotel along with Wirtshaus, a more down-to-earth alternative.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7081;Wirtschaft Traube;Austria;Klösterle;Klösterle 45, Klösterle, 6754, Austria;47.13196;10.12304;28;true;false;Alpine;Tanja and Tobias Schöpf welcome you to their establishment in a pleasingly laid-back manner. She provides cordial and proficient service in the inviting wood-panelled dining space, occasionally taking a seat alongside diners at their table. Her husband, meanwhile, prepares five tasty dishes using regional ingredients, for you to choose à la carte or as a set menu. He likes to keep things seasonal and close to nature – he goes hunting and collects mushrooms, buds and herbs. The wine pairing is also exquisite – and there is an alcohol-free alternative too.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7082;Gasthof Stanglwirt;Austria;Going am Wilden Kaiser;Kaiserweg 1, Going am Wilden Kaiser, 6353, Austria;47.5149966;12.3441867;67;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Dating back over 400 years, this traditional inn now operates as a combination of organic farm and luxury spa hotel. The regional menu takes its cue from the seasons and also includes classics such as roast chicken and Tyrolean goulash. With 65ha of grassland and 52ha of Alpine pasture, they can produce milk, quark, butter, yoghurt, cheese and bread on site. Food is served in the cosy rustic-style interior – one area has a view of the cowshed – and on a lovely terrace overlooking the garden.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7084;Greisslerei beim Taubenkobel;Austria;Schützen am Gebirge;Hauptstraße 31, Schützen am Gebirge, 7081, Austria;47.8514379;16.6262932;100;true;true;Farm to table, Classic French;Barbara Eselböck and Alain Weissgerber offer a delightful alternative to Taubenkobel restaurant with this charming eatery located in the adjacent building. The atmosphere is friendly, relaxed and completely unpretentious, and the food is simply delicious. Select ingredients go into flavoursome dishes such as Alsace-style snails, Wiener schnitzel and gnocchi with fresh truffles. The interior is wonderfully cosy and has a vintage feel to it, with charming decorative touches and shelves displaying house-made and Pannonian food items, as well as regional wines. By the entrance, there is a counter displaying desserts. A small terrace shaded by an old tree is just outside.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
7085;ice Q;Austria;Sölden;Dorfstraße 115, Sölden, 6450, Austria;46.9463775;10.9727466;71;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Perched at 3 048m above sea level, this place boasts a magnificent setting and impressive futuristic architecture. The large glass cube appeals with the clean lines of its design and its fantastic panoramic view of the mountains. On the ground floor, the restaurant serves up a modern tasting menu (vegetarian version available) as well as an à la carte selection of more classic dishes such as beef consommé, Wiener schnitzel and rib-eye steak. Alternatively, tapas are served in the lounge on the top floor. Guests can also head outside to the lovely terraces. When it comes to wine, the PINO 3000 is worthy of your attention – it is aged at this altitude! This incredible site also served as a filming location for the James Bond film "Spectre".;Great view,Terrace;[]
7086;Starcke Haus;Austria;Graz;Schloßberg 4, Graz, 8010, Austria;47.0749121;15.4364305;22;false;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a truly unique location, clinging to the side of a steep slope – and affording a magnificent view over Graz! In what used to be a winegrower's house (built in 1820), Manuela and Milivoj Novak are at your service. The chef-owner also supports Manuela front of house. Their single "surprise" menu is served to all guests – the meal begins at 7pm. It's best to arrive a little earlier to take in the fantastic view of the city from the small terrace. To get here, you have two options: either a walk along the Schlossbergsteig or the Schlossbergbahn funicular plus a 5min walk to the restaurant.;Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7087;Pichlmaiers zum Herkner;Austria;Vienna;Dornbacher Straße 123, Vienna, 1170, Austria;48.2337649;16.2909019;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Well worth a trip to the outskirts of the city. The inn formerly run by famous Viennese chef Heinz Herkner has been given a successful makeover that combines modernity and tradition – this applies to the warm and charming setting as well as the food. The Austrian and classic French dishes are peppered with modern touches. The pretty terrace extends over two floors.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7088;Kommod;Austria;Vienna;Strozzigasse 40, Vienna, 1080, Austria;48.209436;16.34882;41;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;This popular restaurant offers a set menu with four to six courses, which you can choose with fish and meat or as a vegetarian option. They are careful to select top-quality produce, the vegetables are locally grown. The chef serves guests himself and talks them through the dishes. Wine pairings are available to accompany the set menu. The changing temporary art exhibitions make for an extra point of interest.;;[]
7089;Sonnenstüble;Austria;Hirschegg;Oberseitestraße 34, Hirschegg, 6992, Austria;47.3508906;10.1709351;47;false;false;French, International;Here in the restaurant of the peacefully located Hotel Birkenhöhe, the next generation, in the form of Felix Bantel, is bringing a breath of fresh air to this place. The cuisine incorporates modern trends, while also remaining true to its regional roots and tuning into seasonal produce. The set menu comes in a conventional and a vegetarian version, plus there is a short à la carte menu. To accompany the food, choose from a good selection of wines that includes rarities from Italy and France. Warm wood panelling and a tiled stove make for a cosy atmosphere.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7090;Infinity The Restaurant;Austria;Andau;Resortplatz 1, Andau, 7163, Austria;47.7843489;17.0295543;37;false;false;Contemporary;Located in the architecturally striking Scheiblhofer The Resort hotel, this stylish modern restaurant is nestled amid the vineyards. The glass-walled dining area affords stunning views while you savour contemporary cuisine with a Pannonian twist. The menu features dishes such as hamachi sashimi with caviar, apricots, passion fruit, yellow pepper, leche de tigre and maize, or Pannonian pike-perch bisque. The property also boasts a winery, Weingut Scheiblhofer, and wine is also an important part of the experience – the impressive selection naturally includes many of their own making.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
7092;Rauchkuchl;Austria;Stuhlfelden;Weyerstr. 8, Stuhlfelden, 5724, Austria;47.2881615;12.5262354;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Asturian;Established over 100 years ago, this is a charming traditional restaurant with Alpine-style decor that perfectly complements the cuisine. The Bacher family have made it their mission to showcase local flavours. Led by son Tobias, the kitchen team creates a seasonally inspired surprise menu using excellent regional produce, some of which comes from their own garden. The delicious bread served before your meal comes from the family's village bakery. In one of the dining rooms, food is even cooked on an antique wood-fired stove, right before your eyes – the name of the restaurant translates as "Smoke Kitchen".;Car park;[]
7093;Bergergut;Austria;Afiesl;Oberafiesl 7, Afiesl, 4170, Austria;48.5828395;14.1311754;81;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;This tasteful restaurant in the appealing hotel of the same name promises a modern, elegant decor and a pleasantly quiet, almost intimate atmosphere, as well as attentive and proficient service, and – last but not least – really good cuisine based on selected ingredients. Quality and craftsmanship are evident in dishes such as the dumplings and caviar from wild-caught pike with lime and chives or the Rahmbeuscherl made with Mühlviertel milk-fed veal lights, served with Serviettenknödel (bread dumplings) and fresh marjoram.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7094;Charles' & Frank's;Austria;Atzbach;Ritzling 9, Atzbach, 4904, Austria;48.0668987;13.7052003;93;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This space boasts a sleek, modern aesthetic, featuring exposed concrete and wooden elements. Large windows provide panoramic views of the surroundings. There is also a lovely terrace. In his seasonal set menu, the talented chef prepares select, often local produce in cosmopolitan and contemporary dishes with an exquisite and harmonious flavour profile. The name Charles' & Frank's is a reference to the founders of Peneder, the company in whose building the restaurant is located.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7095;Lois Stern;Austria;Kitzbühel;Josef-Pirchl-Straße 3, Kitzbühel, 6370, Austria;47.4480139;12.3897355;44;true;false;Fusion, Asian and Western;Maria and Lois Stern have been welcoming diners to their restaurant in a traffic-reduced zone in the centre of Kitzbühel since 1994 and have built up a loyal following. An inviting atmosphere reigns in the modern interior. The focal point is the open kitchen, where the chef-patron cooks up Asian-European fusion dishes. The quality of the ingredients is excellent. In addition to the regular menu, there are daily specials. The friendly proprietress and her well-trained team provide attentive service.;Terrace;[]
7097;Goldener Hirsch;Austria;Salzburg;Getreidegasse 37, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7999662;13.0410676;38;true;true;Austrian, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the eponymous hotel in the old town serves modern dishes that draw on international influences as well as Austrian classics. You can dine à la carte or opt for a set menu (vegetarian option). Be sure to peruse the decent wine list with an emphasis on Austrian labels. A striking white vaulted ceiling, lovely parquet flooring and delightful nods to tradition in the decor contribute to the atmosphere. Parking at Altstadtgarage A.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7098;Kehlberghof;Austria;Graz;Kehlbergstraße 83, Graz, 8054, Austria;47.0311553;15.3841378;25;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, International;The location overlooking Graz is a real draw – it is about a 15min drive from the city centre up to this friendly restaurant with a gorgeous view. From the fantastic terrace in particular, you can drink in the view over the surrounding meadows and the city. The cuisine is seasonal and uses predominantly regional ingredients. At lunchtime and in the evening there is an à la carte menu plus a surprise menu comprising six or seven courses, and at lunchtime there is also a small menu of the day. The "Wirtshausklassiker" include Frittatensuppe (pancake soup) and Tafelspitz (beef boiled in broth). Charming service.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7100;SHIKI Brasserie & Bar;Austria;Vienna;Krugerstraße 3, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2041385;16.3709832;33;false;true;Japanese;This minimalist-style brasserie with its large terrace is SHIKI’s less formal eatery. It offers a wider range of dishes from miso soup to tempura and sushi – the latter prepared before you as you sit at the sushi bar.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7101;LABSTELLE;Austria;Vienna;Lugeck 6, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2096518;16.3747318;66;true;false;Country cooking;An appealingly upmarket bistro setting with a relaxed bar area, Labstelle serves ambitious seasonal and regional fare à la carte or as a set menu (conventional or vegan). Examples of the appealing dishes include pickled salmon trout, flank steak, and mushroom goulash. The chef makes a point of working with high-quality produce from Austria. Reduced menu at lunchtime. Gorgeous verdant courtyard.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7102;Pastamara - Bar con Cucina;Austria;Vienna;Schubertring 5, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2024946;16.3761414;50;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;In the luxurious Ritz-Carlton Hotel you will find this modern restaurant with its large bar. A pleasantly relaxed and elegant atmosphere reigns, and the experienced staff are very friendly. Traditional Sicilian cuisine with a modern touch. Interesting: ‘Negroni Experience’ - a classic with a creative twist.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7103;Luckys Restaurant Haus am Hang;Austria;Sankt Gilgen;Mondsee-Bundesstraße 10, Sankt Gilgen, 5340, Austria;47.7709642;13.3614435;37;false;true;International, Classic Cuisine;The "place to be" is a pretty apt way to describe this restaurant from which you can take in a wonderful view of the lake (Wolfgang See), Sankt Gilgen and the surrounding mountains. As you can imagine, the sophisticated terrace is coveted in summer… and then there is the good food added into the mix. Susanne and Lucas Bocsa have been putting their heart and soul into their role as hosts for many years and, over time, have established a chic restaurant where Lucas Bocsa cooks up flavoursome dishes, both classic and international. With the two set menus, "Luckys" and "Luckys All Around the World", you can also dip in and go à la carte. The glass wine cabinet in the entrance area whets your appetite for a good glass of wine off the bat. The friendly and professional service team is headed up by the likeable Susanne.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7105;Weibel's Wirtshaus;Austria;Vienna;Kumpfgasse 2, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2079198;16.3762001;29;false;false;Austrian;Just a few minutes’ walk from St Stephen’s Cathedral, Weibel’s Wirtshaus is the archetypal Viennese restaurant – warm and friendly, rustic and snug! It also has a charming garden in the small alleyway. The food is traditional and Viennese.;Terrace;[]
7106;SHIKI Japanese Fine Dining;Austria;Vienna;Krugerstraße 3, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2041253;16.3710135;47;true;false;Japanese Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;Shiki translates as "four seasons" and, indeed, this tastefully elegant fine dining restaurant takes its cue from the seasons. Using top-quality produce, the kitchen team seamlessly combines classic and Austrian influences with techniques and ingredients from Japanese cuisine to create bold and intriguing dishes. A seven-course set menu is served on Thu, Fri and Sat evenings, as well as on Fri afternoons. The central location is also fantastic, with the State Opera practically around the corner.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7107;Humbachstube;Austria;Riezlern;Unterwestegg 17, Riezlern, 6991, Austria;47.3668156;10.1996801;18;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The Alpenhof Jäger hotel's restaurant may be small but what it lacks in size it makes up for in atmosphere! With plenty of wood, a tiled stove and pretty decorations, the cosy and homely Humbachstube is completely in keeping with the rustic charm of the 380-year-old regional-style building in which it is located. In the kitchen, Florian Jäger and his father Martin cook with market produce, creating dishes based on the classic repertoire, such as sirloin of local mountain lamb roasted with aromatics, fresh spinach leaves and potato and Parmesan gnocchi. The wine list is all about Austria's own production. Diners will enjoy friendly, attentive service with a real family touch.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7108;Crystal;Austria;Sankt Johann in Tirol;Hornweg 5, Sankt Johann in Tirol, 6380, Austria;47.5187115;12.423771;35;false;true;Creative;This restaurant presents a dual concept: Diners choose between creative à la carte options and an intriguing tasting menu. The latter is given the name of a fairy tale or story, such as "Lisa and Lottie", the different chapters of which are then represented in the courses. The dishes are prepared in a contemporary style and made with carefully selected ingredients. The restaurant is housed in the hotel of the same name, not far from the cableway station.;Car park;[]
7109;Brandstätter;Austria;Salzburg;Münchner Bundesstraße 69, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8267276;13.010198;62;false;false;Country cooking, International;A real Salzburg institution! The atmosphere in the various dining areas is perfect for a cosy dinner, but in the summer, you might prefer to sit out on the gorgeous terrace. Traditional Austrian fare dominates the menu, but you will also find dishes that take their cue from the seasons or from global culinary trends. The service comes courtesy of an attentive and well-drilled front-of-house team. Good to know: You can buy house-made jams to take home.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7110;Spitzbuam;Austria;Brixen im Thale;Ahornweg 4, Brixen im Thale, 6364, Austria;47.4508206;12.2469955;45;false;false;European Contemporary;The compact restaurant has a distinctly casual atmosphere fostered by a young team. The small à la carte selection comprises an interesting assortment of modern dishes that win diners over with their full-bodied flavours, from dim sum with prawns to entrecôte or tuna. Alternatively, there is a five-course surprise menu. Consult the wine list for a bottle to accompany your food choice. Friendly, professional waitstaff, joined by the chef, who also gets involved.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7111;Der Unterwirt;Austria;Ebbs;Wildbichlerstr. 38, Ebbs, 6341, Austria;47.6306759;12.214833;99;true;true;Contemporary;This inn dates back to 1490. In cosy, charmingly decorated dining rooms with touches of elegance, or out on the wonderful garden terrace, diners are invited to savour creatively inspired cuisine with regional foundations. Dishes such as "clear mushroom consommé, chive oil, game ravioli", or "red catfish, cucumber, rhubarb" are accompanied by a fine selection of wines with a focus on Austrian winemakers. The guestrooms are a real home away from home.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7112;Hirschen;Austria;Schwarzenberg;Hof 14, Schwarzenberg, 6850, Austria;47.4138969;9.8522128;76;true;true;Regional Cuisine;The concept of sustainability shines through in Jonathan Burger's cuisine. Ingredients are sourced in the region, the fruit and vegetables are predominantly organic or grown by neighbouring farmers, and a nose-to-tail approach is applied to all produce. The latter philosophy is evident, for example, in a dish of grilled chicken hearts, pumpkin, Schupfnudeln (finger-shaped potato dumplings). They also conjure up vegetarian fare, especially in winter when in-house fermentation methods play a major role – for example, their Vetterhof radish with gochugaru and miso broth. The setting is also beautiful: Housed in the Hirschen hotel, a hub of art and tradition that dates back to 1755, the restaurant's tastefully decorated dining rooms draw on a sense of history. At lunchtime, only salads, light bites and cakes are served.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7113;Jägerstube & Walserstube;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Tannberg 228, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.208865;10.1410781;52;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Asian;In the small fine dining restaurant of Hotel Jagdhaus Monzabon, Michael Broger and his team deliver interesting modern cuisine that is big on flavour. Guests will also enjoy the charming service and expert wine recommendations that come courtesy of junior chef and sommelier Tobias Schneider – who also happens to be a sake sommelier. The food, which delves into the region and uses many ingredients from local suppliers, is also decidedly cosmopolitan. From an appealing selection of dishes – for example, "Buddha – red Carabinero prawn, macadamia, Buddha's hand lemon & crustacean bisque" or "Teriyaki venison, morel, pointed cabbage, praline from the leg & kohlrabi" – you can put together a four- to six- course menu of your own. Tip: Make a reservation, as there are only a handful of tables.;;[]
7114;Fliana Gourmet;Austria;Ischgl;Fimbabahnweg 8, Ischgl, 6561, Austria;47.01233;10.29318;92;true;false;French Contemporary;Be sure to book in good time, because this chic and modern Alpine-style restaurant only has a few tables and is very popular! Andreas Spitzer and his team skilfully conjure up creative dishes to offer a choice of two tasting menus: the shorter one comprises five courses and the longer one seven. In winter, some tables afford a view of the ski slope. The restaurant is located in the hotel of the same name, within easy reach of the lower terminus of the Fimbabahn and Pardatschgratbahn cable cars.;;[]
7115;Trippolt Zum Bären;Austria;Bad Sankt Leonhard im Lavanttal;Hauptplatz 7, Bad Sankt Leonhard im Lavanttal, 9462, Austria;46.9638648;14.7907719;94;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;"From the Alps to the Adriatic" is the motto of the Trippolt family restaurant. Dishes such as "pasta mare – In & Out scampi ravioli in a crab stock" will transport you to Mediterranean climes, while the "delicately roasted juniper venison with fluffy raspberry ricotta-filled dumplings, honey lavender and elderflower jelly" highlights their ties to the region, as well as chef Josef Trippolt's passion for hunting. In addition to a set menu and a well-devised à la carte selection, daily specials are featured on the blackboard. The refined, lovingly designed interior of this restaurant steeped in tradition is a pure delight, as is the lovely little garden terrace. In addition, the restaurant has a small on-site shop, where you can buy delicacies to take home, including Bärmut, their own hand-crafted "lifestyle aperitif" based on vermouth – also the perfect way to kick off a meal.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7116;Mama Konstantina;Austria;Vienna;Döblinger Hauptstraße 17, Vienna, 1190, Austria;48.2352411;16.3530009;16;false;true;Contemporary, Greek;Following on from Konstantin Filippou and O boufés, chef Konstantin Filippou has established another culinary hotspot in Vienna – this time in the city's 19th district. The concept is somewhat unusual: at lunchtime, simple dishes for his "Lunch To Go" are served in the large, high-ceilinged space with its snazzy open kitchen, in the evening, guests sit together in the thick of the action at one of the large tables. Two set menus (one vegetarian) comprise four or six courses. First-class ingredients go into creating modern Greek fare, in a nod to the chef's roots. The congenial, charming service includes helpful wine recommendations. You may be interested to know that the owner named his restaurant after an olive farmer friend – and inspiration – of his, who hails from Kalamata.;Air conditioning;[]
7117;Trattoria Martinelli;Austria;Vienna;Freyung 3, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.21169;16.36524;70;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant run by the Barbaro family is in the courtyard of the fine Baroque Palais Harrach. They offer a fresh, authentic take on Mediterranean cuisine, made with fish and other produce that the owners themselves have been importing from Italy for around 30 years. There are also a few seasonal dishes that do not feature on the menu – the friendly waitstaff will be happy to fill you in.;Terrace;[]
7118;ONYX;Austria;Vienna;Stephansplatz 12, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2083525;16.3717669;31;false;false;Asian;The location is fantastic! On the sixth floor of DO & CO Hotel in the avant-garde Haas building, a trendy restaurant with a lounge feel awaits. It boasts a breathtaking view of St Stephen's Cathedral – a table by the large floor-to-ceiling windows is practically a must! The menu features exciting Asian dishes designed for sharing, along with sushi, sashimi and specialities from the Robata grill.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7119;Fuhrmann;Austria;Vienna;Fuhrmannsgasse 9, Vienna, 1080, Austria;48.2108251;16.3479467;39;false;true;Austrian;An exceptionally friendly restaurant that feels almost neighbourly with its inviting, cosy atmosphere and friendly service. As for Mike Feierabend's truly tasty Austrian cuisine, choose à la carte or go for the five-course set menu that changes every month. At lunchtime there is a cheaper three-course menu. Your hosts will be more than happy to recommend a local wine, but big names from Europe are also served, including some spanning numerous vintages. On that note, it would be remiss not to mention owner and sommelier Herman Botolen, whose genuine passion for wine is plain to see. Tip: be sure to book, as places are limited! In summer, make a beeline for the pleasant terrace in the courtyard.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7120;Rote Bar;Austria;Vienna;Philharmonikerstraße 4, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2038965;16.3697935;44;true;true;Austrian, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant in the famous Hotel Sacher, a piece of the city's history, epitomises the charm of this great Viennese establishment with its striking red interior, elegant oil paintings and crystal chandeliers. The menu features dishes that draw inspiration from modern culinary trends as well as Viennese and Austrian traditional specialities, including Tafelspitz and Sachertorte. Gorgeous little veranda.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7121;Léontine;Austria;Vienna;Reisnerstraße 39, Vienna, 1030, Austria;48.1986977;16.384039;99;true;false;Modern French;An authentic little corner of France, tucked away in a quiet yet central location near the Stadtpark. The bistro atmosphere is charming, the service provided by the owner is cordial and professional, and the modern French cuisine is delicious. The dishes revolve around the seasons and are made with select ingredients. The pair serve a five-course tasting menu and an à la carte selection, at lunchtime there is the more affordable "Menu du Midi" – a three-course set menu. The wine list takes you through the regions of France.;Terrace;[]
7122;O boufés;Austria;Vienna;Dominikanerbastei 17, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2108724;16.3798082;90;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Industrial-chic design and soaring ceilings set the tone in this inviting modern bistro, complemented by a cosy bar area for pre-dinner drinks that adds to the laid-back, welcoming vibe. The kitchen serves Mediterranean-Greek inspired dishes, reflecting the cultural heritage of owner Konstantin Filippou, whose fine dining restaurant happens to be located right next door. The dishes are usually served as smaller portions, making them ideal for sharing. For the main course, you can choose between meat, fish and veggie options, which change periodically. There is also a pleasant outdoor dining area.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7123;Meissl & Schadn;Austria;Vienna;Schubertring 10, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2022282;16.3749602;28;false;false;Austrian, Traditional Cuisine;Here, the Wiener schnitzel is the obvious choice – it's best to order it "mit allen Schikanen" (with all the trimmings)! At this attractive restaurant on the Ring that encircles Vienna's old town, good food is accompanied by classical music, Viennese service culture and an elegant yet pleasantly down-to-earth atmosphere. In the open kitchen (which is also visible from outside), you can see the schnitzels being pounded. Why not take part in the weekly schnitzel course. There is even a book for sale: The Wiener Schnitzel Love Book.;Terrace;[]
7124;Die Ente von Zürs;Austria;Zürs am Arlberg;Haus 217, Zürs am Arlberg, 6763, Austria;47.1709314;10.1619982;92;false;false;Contemporary;For many years, this small, classic restaurant in the ‘Albona Nova’ hotel has stood for high-quality cuisine. If you manage to get one of the few seats, you can look forward to a menu with pleasantly reduced and excellently prepared dishes made from excellent products - the eponymous duck is always present, for example in the wonderfully puristic combination of a crispy baked slice of sourdough bread with aromatic, melt-in-the-mouth duck liver cream, carpaccio of fresh tuna and Himalayan salt. The harmonious picture also includes a fine selection of wines, charming service and an intimate atmosphere.;Car park;[]
7127;Lechtaler Stube;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Oberlech 266, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2164411;10.136752;43;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant is located in the car-free village of Oberlech, more precisely in the Burghotel (an almost legendary place that started off as a small milk bar in the 1960s), right by the ski slope. In a cosy and tastefully designed setting, you can savour classic and regionally influenced options (beef tartare, bouillabaisse, fried chicken, Wiener schnitzel etc) for lunch and dinner. In the evening, the seven-course fine dining set menu features mouthwatering dishes such as venison entrecôte Rossini with celeriac done three ways and a truffle jus.;Interesting wine list;[]
7128;Severin*s;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Stubenbach 273, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2215783;10.1569308;93;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The restaurant at the luxurious little hotel The Alpine Retreat has a rather intimate and private feel to it. In a chic setting that combines modern design and Alpine charm, diners choose two, three or four courses from a short menu. The dishes, such as two kinds of ravioli in a nut butter foam with brassato and mascarpone, and sautéed spinach, are made with predominantly regional ingredients. Tip: Don't miss out on your chance to try the Austrian speciality Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake)! The good food is complemented by very friendly, attentive and professional service and an excellent selection of wines.;;[]
7129;Heimatbühne;Austria;Ischgl;Dorfstraße 95, Ischgl, 6561, Austria;47.0086056;10.286256;32;false;true;Austrian, Regional Cuisine;This alternative to the fine dining restaurant at Hotel Trofana Royal also serves culinary delights right next to the ski slope. In an inviting decor, diners can choose from an appealing à la carte selection of freshly prepared Tyrolean dishes. These are made with the finest regional produce, such as Paznaun Highland beef, Diasbach trout and traditional Alpine cheese. Open to the lobby and bar area, and with only a handful of tables, this restaurant is done out in lots of warm wood, creating a pleasantly cosy feel. Exceptionally courteous and friendly service.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7130;Pfeffermühle;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Dorf 138, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2076063;10.1415207;64;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;If you want to savour classic French-influenced cuisine without having to commit to a set menu, the lovely, cosy restaurant of Hotel Pfefferkorn is just the place for you. The à la carte menu lives up to the establishment's name, incorporating a unique touch of exoticism with one of 13 peppers in each dish. Think carabineros prawn with fruity curry, pickled golden beet, tomato, ginger, and Indian mountain pepper, or pigeon à la royale with pear, parsnip, fried onion, and smoked Malabar pepper. There is no reason to worry that the food will be excessively spicy – chef Christian Wild has a light touch with the pepper, so it enhances the flavour without overpowering it. Diners can also look forward to very friendly service and a fine selection of wines.;Car park;[]
7131;Das Vogelhaus;Austria;Klagenfurt am Wörthersee;Domgasse 22, Klagenfurt am Wörthersee, 9020, Austria;46.6226076;14.3096614;44;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Fusion;In the heart of Klagenfurt, Stefanie Falkenberg and Fabian Kautz welcome you to their charming little restaurant with vaulted ceilings and a friendly atmosphere. Courtesy of the restaurateur couple, guests enjoy cordial and attentive service as they tuck into flavoursome and varied cuisine. The food is served in the form of a three- to five-course set menu that changes monthly and is prepared with fresh seasonal ingredients, some from the region. The chef likes to come out of his kitchen and present his dishes to diners. On request, there is a wine pairing to match the food or, alternatively, non-alcoholic beverages, which they produce themselves for the most part.;Terrace;[]
7132;Sicher;Austria;Tainach;Mühlenweg 2, Tainach, 9121, Austria;46.6316259;14.537514;59;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;This is a great place with a host of standout features: picture a converted old sawmill that is set in a quiet, idyllic location and boasts a sensational garden terrace with tables within spitting distance of the neighbouring forest! Works by various artists adorn this charming spot. The interior, too, is beautiful, combining traditional charm (the elaborately carved wooden ceiling is striking) with modern features. On top of this, the cordial Sicher family are strongly invested in their work in the kitchen and on the restaurant floor. They propose an ambitious and creative seasonal set menu as well as more down-to-earth à la carte dishes, such as whole trout or char. Pride of place is given to the restaurant's own fish farm, as well as produce sourced from its own farm or regional producers. The speciality is the famous "Sicher" char caviar.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7134;Gasthof Goldgasse;Austria;Salzburg;Goldgasse 10, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7993023;13.04598;34;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The speciality here is new interpretations of old Salzburg recipes taken from a cookbook published in 1719! The food is a perfect match for the period setting with modern touches and the lively atmosphere – the charming service is the icing on the cake! Try the fried breaded chicken with potato and cucumber salad and cranberries and the apple strudel with vanilla sauce.;Terrace;[]
7135;Eckel;Austria;Vienna;Sieveringer Straße 46, Vienna, 1190, Austria;48.2470722;16.3336383;19;true;false;Country cooking;This family-run restaurant in Vienna's beautiful 19th district has its fair share of regulars who come to sample its range of classic, flavoursome Austrian specialities. On the menu, you will find familiar favourites such as Wiener schnitzel, seasonal dishes with game, but also seafood including lobster. The attentive waitstaff and cultivated atmosphere add to the appeal of this place, not to mention the splendid garden terrace!;Terrace;[]
7136;Glasswing;Austria;Vienna;Kärntner Ring 8, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.2017745;16.3712131;38;false;true;Contemporary;Top-notch ingredients are brought into play when chef Alexandru Simon and his team prepare classic French dishes with regional and Mediterranean touches. For example, the excellent quality of the chicken is showcased in a very special way in the Styrian chicken served with razor clams and green pepper: fried 10 times and then cooled again, it is particularly tender! The dishes are accompanied by an appealing selection of wines. The interior is tasteful, modern and elegant, with designer chairs and semi-circular upholstered bench seating, gorgeous parquet flooring and classic paintings. Insect lovers won't need to be told that the restaurant – like the exclusive hotel in which it is located (The Amauris) – is named after a species of butterfly.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7137;Das Loft;Austria;Vienna;Praterstraße 1, Vienna, 1020, Austria;48.2127618;16.3798;65;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The location on the 18th floor of lifestyle hotel SO/Vienna is undeniably spectacular – the view of Vienna is phenomenal! Add to that the attentive, laid-back service and cuisine that draws on modern influences. Great wine selection. There is also a popular cocktail bar.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7138;Veranda;Austria;Vienna;Burggasse 2, Vienna, 1070, Austria;48.2047652;16.3563468;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Austrian;The restaurant in the Hotel Sans Souci is smart and fashionable. It proposes modern Austrian cuisine, which can be ordered à la carte or as a set menu in the form of a "culinary voyage through Austria". Wine list with a focus on Austria and a wide selection of champagnes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7139;das grander;Austria;Wattens;Dr.-Felix-Bunzl-Str. 6, Wattens, 6112, Austria;47.2930023;11.5915279;24;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Diners come here to enjoy the friendly and vibrant atmosphere and delicious food. In the evening, you can compose your own seven-course set menu from the featured dishes or order à la carte. Alternatively, there is a surprise menu comprising three to five courses as well as a set menu of Japanese cuisine. At lunchtime, they serve a reasonably priced set menu that changes on a daily basis, the "weekly gourmet set menu" and a range of à la carte classics such as beef carpaccio, Kalbsrahmbeuschel (calf lights ragout) or Wiener schnitzel, as well as modern fare such as sea bass with saffron foam. In summer, you can sit on the terrace facing a small square laid out like a park. Tip: Your best bet for parking is the underground car park Am Kirchplatz.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7140;Zum Buberl Gut;Austria;Salzburg;Gneiser Straße 31, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.7784311;13.0496274;94;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;More than just a pretty face, this gorgeous 17C country estate, located on the outskirts of the city, is also a delightful setting for a delicious meal. The cosy interior marries classic elegance with charming regional touches, creating a welcoming atmosphere. In the summer, the lovely garden beckons. The cuisine is a flavoursome blend of Austrian and Mediterranean influences. The wine list, too, is definitely worth a look. Tip: Come at lunchtime for the small, moderately priced menu available.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7141;Flos Restaurant;Austria;Zell am See;Schmittenstraße 79, Zell am See, 5700, Austria;47.3260414;12.7803508;18;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Just above Zell am See and at the foot of the Schmittenhöhe mountain, partner Florian Zillner and Hannah Hagn run this restaurant in the small Boutique Hotel Martha. Together with his kitchen team, the chef conjures up seasonal cuisine with a modern Alpine slant. This is served as a four-, six- or eight-course set menu dubbed "Refined. Innovative" (also available à la carte) or in the form of traditional dishes – don't miss the delicious Topfenschmarrn. Some of the vegetables, fruit and herbs are grown in their own garden. The interior has an appealing rustic charm and the front-of-house team overseen by the lady of the house is warm and friendly. In addition to good wines, there are refreshing house-made soft drinks. Overnight guests can expect cosy guestrooms and a gorgeous natural pool.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7142;Stubn 1972;Austria;Kirchberg in Tirol;Brandseitweg 26, Kirchberg in Tirol, 6365, Austria;47.4481939;12.3325404;89;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Contemporary;Just a short walk from the Fleckalmbahn cable car, Minglers Sportalm hotel boasts tastefully decorated guestrooms, a spa and this charming little restaurant with just four tables. The dining space is done out in light, warm wood from floor to ceiling, which makes for a cosy setting. The kitchen team conjures up a set menu that draws on modern culinary trends – you are free to choose the number of courses. The wine recommendations from a predominantly Austrian list are excellent.;Car park;[]
7144;Fuggerstube;Austria;Alpbach;Alpbach 166, Alpbach, 6236, Austria;47.3985479;11.9452076;22;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Creative;The historical Fuggerstube – dating back to the 15C – is a real gem of a place. The beautiful wood panelling and the old stove cultivate a cosy atmosphere and old-world charm. There are just four tables, at which diners tuck into a seasonal set menu packed with regional ingredients. The wine pairings recommended to go with each course are excellent, and the wine cellar has quite a few bottles from which to choose. The restaurant is located in Der Böglerhof, a wellness hotel that has expanded over the years.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7145;Post Lech;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Dorf 11, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2073077;10.1411608;65;true;false;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;The venerable Gasthof Post has a series of charming Alpine-style dining areas, and in all of them the same à la carte menu is served: an ambitious selection of Austrian classics such as Tafelspitz and Wiener schnitzel, as well as international dishes. An exclusive fine dining set menu is served in the Jägerstube Thursdays to Sundays but you'll need to order in advance. Diners can also look forward to a good wine list and attentive service. Individually decorated guestrooms are available for overnight stays.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7147;Wunderkammer - Herbarium;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Tannberg 59, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2086706;10.1396139;86;false;true;Austrian, International;Located near the Schlegelkopf piste, the luxurious Almhof Schneider hotel, built in 1929, is home to this fine dining restaurant, which is only open during the winter. At lunchtime and in the evening, you can enjoy Austrian cuisine with international influences: the menu includes Fiaker goulash, Wagyu steak, Riesling Beuschel (offal ragout) with bread dumplings and, for dessert, Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake). The wine list, comprising over 1 200 labels, is superb. Meals are served in two tastefully decorated dining spaces: Wunderkammer, designed by artist Paul Renner, and Herbarium, featuring beautiful woodcuts by Christian Thanhäuser.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7148;Gasthof Adler;Austria;Krumbach;Dorf 5, Krumbach, 6942, Austria;47.4829945;9.9347765;41;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This pretty inn, established in 1852, embodies the true spirit of hospitality – and has been doing so for seven generations. The old timber chalet has had a lovely contemporary extension added, without any of its historical character being lost along the way. Whether in the cosy parlours or out in the gorgeous Kastaniengarten, diners tuck into flavoursome seasonal cuisine in a regional vein. Fruit, vegetables, salads and herbs come from the own garden, meat from the own farm, game from the nature park... Cordial and professional service. Food items made in-house can also be purchased to enjoy at home. Well-appointed guestrooms and a holiday flat can be booked for overnight stays.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7149;Verwallstube;Austria;Sankt Anton am Arlberg;Kandaharweg 9, Sankt Anton am Arlberg, 6580, Austria;47.1268155;10.2430241;17;true;false;International, Traditional Cuisine;At an elevation of 2 085m, the gondola ride up here (free with your reservation) is even worthwhile for non-skiers. In addition to the breathtaking view, you can expect ambitious cuisine made from high-quality ingredients that doesn't limit itself to a specific style – rather it showcases traditional, regional, Mediterranean and even Asian influences. Appetising options include yellowfin tuna sashimi, Wiener schnitzel and risotto alla carbonara. The exceedingly friendly and charming waitstaff will be happy to recommend the right wine from the extensive list.;Great view,Terrace;[]
7150;Winterstellgut;Austria;Annaberg im Lammertal;Braunötzhof 4, Annaberg im Lammertal, 5524, Austria;47.5359929;13.4393141;25;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;It is worth making the journey here for the stunning views of the surrounding mountains from the sun-drenched plateau some 1 000m above Annaberg – and they are even better from the terrace. At this 16C farm building, dine in cosy, rustic-style nooks or on the light-filled veranda. The kitchen is open all day, serving traditional regional and seasonal cuisine that draws on the odd international influence, such as Kalbsrahmbeuscherl mit Semmelknöde (veal offal ragout with bread dumplings) and lobster gyoza with an Asian-style bisque. Alternatively, opt for the set menu. Everything is made with good-quality, fresh ingredients, including preserves. Tip: House-made goods can be purchased to enjoy at home. For overnight stays, there are a few attractive guestrooms and suites, plus a natural pond for bathing.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7151;Meissl & Schadn;Austria;Salzburg;Getreidegasse 50, Salzburg, 5020, Austria;47.8000776;13.0402805;57;true;true;Austrian, Traditional Cuisine;"Schnitzel love" is the name of the game at this restaurant in the heart of the old town. Even from the outside you can peer into the open kitchen and see the house speciality, Wiener schnitzel, being prepared. The menu also includes Austrian classics such as Tafelspitz, Esterházy lentils or goose (when in season), as well as desserts such as Salzburger Nockerln. Tip: Leave your car in the multi-storey car park Altstadtgarage A.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7152;Specht;Austria;Vienna;Bäckerstraße 12, Vienna, 1010, Austria;48.20903;16.37633;37;false;false;Austrian;This restaurant in a little side street in the city centre is a wonderfully cosy setting for a pleasant tête-à-tête or meal among friends. Diners can expect delicious traditional Viennese cuisine prepared using local ingredients. The pretty interior combining modern design, wooden floors, dark green wall panelling and partially vaulted ceilings creates a warm atmosphere. There is a U-Bahn station conveniently located close by.;Air conditioning;[]
7154;La Fenice;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Tannberg 187, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.208496;10.1413461;32;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;As well as tasteful, individually designed guestrooms, Hotel Arlberg is home to this elegant restaurant, which is accessed via a separate entrance. Ornate details such as warm wood finishings, a partially painted ceiling, shapely upholstered armchairs and classic-style wall lamps create a cosy atmosphere, and this is complemented by the professional and attentive service. Then there is the food, which the chefs call "Alpine-Mediterranean" cuisine: made from the finest ingredients, it is served as a tasting menu comprising five to eight courses. The fantastic wine list, which is predominantly Austrian, Italian and French, includes over 1 000 labels, with around 15 000 bottles stored in the cellar.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7155;Aurelio;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Tannberg 130, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2097967;10.1396556;99;false;false;Contemporary;This is the restaurant of the luxurious Aurelio Hotel & Chalet Lech, which slightly overlooks the village right next to the Schlegelkopf piste. The interior is chic and the gorgeous terrace affords fabulous views. The well-trained and attentive waitstaff contribute to creating the sophisticated yet relaxed atmosphere that prevails throughout. As well as mouthwatering options such as Bismarck trout with gherkin, new potatoes and horseradish, the à la carte menu includes schnitzel and burgers. There are also daily specials, which are simpler at lunchtime and more ambitious in the evening.;Terrace;[]
7156;Schulhus;Austria;Krumbach;Glatzegg 58, Krumbach, 6942, Austria;47.4803909;9.909227;48;false;false;Classic Cuisine;In a building that once housed the village school, this restaurant has a history that stretches far back. Gabi and Herbert Strahammer never tire of treating their guests to a relaxed yet stylish gourmet experience – their accessible cuisine is always connected to the region. In a friendly, pared-back ambience, they serve pleasantly uncomplicated, fresh and flavourful dishes, such as ravioli with Langenegger Schottenkäse smoked cheese, herbs, spinach, lemon sauce, or pike from Lake Constance, spinach leaves, roast vegetables, ricotta gnocchi. On-point wine recommendations from the owner.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7157;Picea;Austria;Lech am Arlberg;Oberlech 568, Lech am Arlberg, 6764, Austria;47.2174905;10.1386062;75;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Mountains, snow, a fantastic panoramic terrace and great food to boot! With its fresh and down-to-earth regional cuisine, this cosy Alpine-style restaurant at Burg Vital Resort makes a great alternative to Griggeler Stuba. The very friendly and competent waitstaff serve up delicious dishes such as Alpine char with red lentils, artichoke, tomato and winter tarragon. This is complemented by the same sensational wine selection as is served in the fine dining restaurant.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7158;Oniriq;Austria;Innsbruck;Bürgerstraße 13, Innsbruck, 6020, Austria;47.2645784;11.3906091;77;true;true;Creative;This compact restaurant with a modern design is located on the outskirts of the city centre. Interesting glimpses of the chefs going about their work are afforded by the open kitchen. The set menu comprises three or seven creatively and thoughtfully prepared courses, including eel, quince, black salsify, or woodruff, cherry, popcorn. Available in a vegetarian version or with fish and meat, it is accompanied by excellent wine pairings. Attentive, professional service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7159;Hospiz Alm;Austria;Sankt Anton am Arlberg;St. Christoph 18, Sankt Anton am Arlberg, 6580, Austria;47.1277439;10.2156058;25;false;true;Contemporary;Just so you know: This place is a haven for wine connoisseurs! The Gothic wine cellar is a real treasure trove, boasting a unique collection of large bottles that is world-famous, not least for its Bordeaux selection. Magnums, primats: you name it, they have it. Be sure to take a look at the impressive Wine Dome with its private dining table for exclusive tastings. In the restaurant itself, a typical ski hut feel prevails at lunchtime, but in the evening, it's all about fine dining in a lovely cosy setting brimming with Alpine charm.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7161;Sereia;USA;Miami;3540 Main Hwy., Miami, 33133, USA;25.7253952;-80.2449937;75;false;true;Portuguese;Chef Henrique Sá Pessoa runs restaurants across the globe, and now he turns his attention to Coconut Grove. Drawing inspiration from the Iberian coast, the seafood-focused menu spotlights largely Portuguese preparations. Begin with a basket of traditional breads kept warm on hot stones and served with smoked butter. Anything with rice, naturally, is a smart way to go, like the bomba rice with grilled carabineros. Salted cod flecked with crispy shoestring potatoes and capped with black olives and chives is another highlight. Dessert is a particular strength, and a recent favorite featured sweet rice custard, rice foam, and calamansi sorbet. The dining room, meanwhile, is all comfort and class with cream tones, cozy banquettes, and wood accents.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
7162;Torno Subito;USA;Miami;200 E. Flagler St., Miami, 33131, USA;25.7742258;-80.1898173;30;true;false;Italian, Contemporary;“I’ll be back soon” is the English translation of Chef Massimo Bottura’s colorful rooftop restaurant in downtown Miami. Blocks of red, yellow, and green match custom plates by Richard Ginori. As playful as the setting may be, the kitchen is serious about honoring the chef’s vision for modern Italian cuisine. An amuse of leftover bread, tomato pomodoro, and Parmesan foam made from the rinds is as sustainable as it is satisfying. Risotto made with saffron, langoustine, and orange is a light take on a rich classic. And yes, there is the famous tortellini dish drawn from the chef’s childhood and yes, it is as wonderful as one would hope. An Italian-heavy wine list, a spritzy cocktail selection, and a breezy terrace round out the experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7163;Cotoa;USA;Miami;100 Biscayne Blvd., Ste. 104, Miami, 33132, USA;25.7755207;-80.18806;31;false;false;Latin American;Miami is no stranger to ceviche, but the one at this casual Ecuadorian counter inside a cheery food hall in downtown stands out among them. Pristine mahi mahi in a smooth blend of coconut, ginger, and peanut and garnished with thin strips of watermelon radish is a winning combination with plantain chips. Across a nicely curated menu, Chef Alejandra Espinoza has other ideas that show equal levels of tropical flair. Her riff on traditional chicken stew using sweet plantain dough is as satisfying as her local fish wrapped in banana leaf. A scoop of ice cream or a mug of frozen cacao juice make for a refreshing send-off. One bit of housekeeping: Diners are seated and can order from any of the restaurants in the court from their server.;Air conditioning;[]
7164;UniGirl;USA;Orlando;1110 E. Colonial Dr., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5529919;-81.3651089;39;false;true;Japanese, Onigiri;Set within the Mills Market, this casual concept from Chef/owner William Shen (and named for his pup, Uni) draws a line before it's even open. It's no wonder, as everyone is here clamoring for a taste of their onigiri, on offer until they sell out. The menu is a moving target, with ever-changing availability alongside a host of daily specials like a Japanese curry hash brown (if you're lucky). Made and served in sealed bags, the classic triangles are best eaten immediately while the filling and rice are still warm. It's all spot-on, whether filled with a crispy fried chicken thigh or tuna enlivened with mustard. Unagi is a fan favorite, with cubes of barbecued freshwater eel enhanced with a sweet sauce complemented by the well-seasoned rice.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7165;Sorekara;USA;Orlando;4979 New Broad St., Orlando, 32814, USA;28.5689965;-81.3259631;26;true;true;Japanese, Contemporary;In a world of uniformity, Sorekara proudly forges its own path. This Baldwin Park restaurant is unlike anywhere else you've been, offering a surprising and delightful culinary journey that revels in turning expectations on their head. Chef/owner William Shen's tasting menu highlights Japan's 72 micro seasons with highly original dishes infused with a sense of whimsy (note the course designed to mimic a 7-Eleven snack run or the "nigiri"). Whether it's madai sporting a distinctive riff on tradition or a deeply savory bowl of kegani sourced from Hokkaido, there is an elegance and refinement threaded throughout the meal, which progresses through multiple rooms across several hours. Another hint that this is far from typical? Sorekara is open for one seating only a few nights a week.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7166;Ômo by Jônt;USA;Winter Park;115 E. Lyman Ave., Winter Park, 32789, USA;28.5951074;-81.350583;41;false;false;Contemporary;Chef Ryan Ratino's lauded D.C. restaurant, Jônt, is more than just the inspiration for this offshoot. This Winter Park restaurant echoes that spirit and sensibility (think classic French techniques married with pristine Japanese ingredients), albeit with a few Florida touches. The larger space allows for discrete moments at each meal, while three tasting menus run the gamut from tightly edited and more affordable to loaded with luxury ingredients. No matter the selection, expect refined dishes punctuated by the seasons, as in chawanmushi with an autumnal twist of braised sweet potato, kombu, and a brown butter sauce. Scallop prepared two ways demonstrates the kitchen's deft hand while chocolate and hazelnut kakigori is an elegant tribute.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7167;Itamae Ao;USA;Miami;3255 N.E. 1st Ave., Miami, 33137, USA;25.8072307;-80.1929221;74;true;false;Peruvian;A restaurant within a restaurant, this 10-seat counter by Chef Nando Chang in Midtown looks to set a new standard for Nikkei cuisine in the region. Those familiar with the chef’s past work in the Design District will take heart in how classic Peruvian-Japanese flavors as well as signature dishes have been reworked, reimagined, and refined. Searing levels of acidity and spice figure prominently on this bold tasting menu, often in the form of leche de tigre. From lobster bisque with sweet potato gnocchi to creamy rice with Hokkaido scallops and parmesan, the cooking possesses style and substance in spades. Sourcing is a priority, with whole fish flown in from Japan, later to be broken down and occasionally strung up in dry-aging fridges along the wall.;Air conditioning;[]
7168;Palma;USA;Miami;240 N.W. 8th Ave., Miami, 33128, USA;25.7762649;-80.2079497;95;false;false;Contemporary;Dressed head to toe in concrete and lit with candles, this narrow room in Little Havana is out to make a mark. The staff totals less than five, including Chef Juan Camilo Liscano and his sous who cook, plate, and clear with impressive efficiency. The lean team, however, turns out a stylish and agreeably priced tasting menu that changes with great frequency. Grilled baby corn brushed in burnt eggplant aioli and wrapped in aged sirloin is a thrilling start, followed by delicately steamed flounder enrobed in a smooth sabayon made of mussels. Brioche made with roasted plantains is the only staple, and what a staple it is. Beautifully shaped, nicely crusted, and served hot with caramelized coconut butter, it is impossible to resist.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7169;Grand Central;USA;Miami;7919 Biscayne Blvd., Miami, 33138, USA;25.8482778;-80.1845692;61;true;false;Contemporary;This narrow nook of a restaurant by Chef Nuno Grullon hides in plain sight along Biscayne Boulevard. The unassuming location runs in stark contrast to what’s happening in this friendly dining room set with white tablecloths and a bar that stretches the length of the room. Warm buttermilk biscuits garnished with thyme are a welcome start, followed by an eclectic roster of bistro dishes that show wonderful levels of care and thought. Pan-fried baby artichokes are a delightful pairing with pancetta hollandaise. Chicken pot pie gets a makeover with heritage chicken and black truffles, and there’s even a lavish duck pithivier finished with cranberry demi. Dessert hits all the right notes with a proper chocolate ganache cake that is all too easy to finish.;Air conditioning;[]
7170;Bistrot di Pescheria;Italy;Salerno;Via Luigi Guercio 1, Salerno, 84134, Italy;40.679042;14.7754517;60;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;This attractive, contemporary-style bistro is the “low-cost” sibling of the Pescheria restaurant situated in a more upmarket location on Salerno’s seafront. Run by the same management, the bistro aims to serve simpler dishes at more modest prices yet with the same focus on freshness and attention to detail evident in its sister-restaurant. As a result, you’ll find options such as oily fish and local white prawns on the menu rather than oysters and caviar. Don’t miss the squid soup with nduja sausage, potato mousse and crispy bread.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7171;La Taverna delle Follie;Italy;Limatola;via San Biagio 30, Limatola, 82030, Italy;41.145072;14.3898563;79;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant with a discreet sign is situated in a small village overlooked by a splendid Norman castle. Meals are served either in the simple yet comfortable dining room or in the charming outdoor space in fine weather. The reasonably priced cuisine celebrates the sea in its many varied fish and seafood dishes, which range from pasta with shellfish or seafood to fish guazzetto (a tomato-based stew) with green vegetables and even raw fish options. Among the desserts, we particularly recommend the babà.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7172;Fourghetti;Italy;Milan;Via Cardinale Ascanio Sforza 77, Milan, 20141, Italy;45.441999;9.1759541;82;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;A new contemporary-style bistro which has moved to Milan from Bologna, with a Michelin-starred chef (for his cuisine at the Osteria del Povero Diavolo in his native Romagna) at the helm. Here, he offers three tasting menus (simply named Terra, Mare and Vegetariano) from which courses can also be chosen à la carte style. His dishes are colourful, balanced and generous, with a focus on top-quality ingredients and combinations that follow the seasons. You don’t even have to worry about parking – the restaurant pays for two hours at a garage right opposite the building, on the other side of the Naviglio Pavese canal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7173;Sunrise;Italy;Caserta;Corso Trieste 112, Caserta, 81100, Italy;41.0718419;14.3351555;78;true;false;Seafood, Italian Contemporary;One of the most attractive restaurants in the city centre, Sunrise occupies the ground floor of an old Bourbon palazzo, extending right to the back of the building where you’ll find the delightful “literary veranda” and, beyond the large windows, a beautiful outdoor space surrounded by a garden planted with citrus trees. The menu has an exclusive focus on fish, with a combination of classic options and light, modern dishes, while an entire page is dedicated to raw fish and seafood. The wine list includes several champagnes.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7174;Mammà Isola di Capri;Italy;Turin;Corso Castelfidardo 22, Turin, 10138, Italy;45.0663362;7.660934;70;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Campanian;Situated within the multi-functional Sondo building (also home to a museum, offices and exhibition spaces), this large restaurant decorated in contemporary, post-industrial style provides the backdrop for chef Raffaele Amitrano’s Mediterranean cuisine which is strongly influenced by the flavours of Campania. His plin pasta dish pays tribute to the region and is particularly interesting thanks to ingredients such as cacio cheese, pepper and raw prawns. Make sure you arrive early if you want to visit the building and maybe even take advantage of the large sharing table.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7175;Osteria Bar Sport;Italy;Casale Monferrato;Strada Alessandria in San Germano 85, Casale Monferrato, 15033, Italy;45.09853;8.45527;80;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Piedmontese;In what was once a typical sports bar, the friendly owner-chef serves home-style cuisine featuring traditional dishes from Monferrato and further afield. Don’t miss his plin pasta served with a roast meat sauce and a delicate cream of leeks, cotechino sausage and raw Mazara prawns. The atmosphere here is pleasantly informal and relaxed.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7177;Acqua & Sale;Italy;Scafati;Via Monte Grappa 35, Scafati, 84018, Italy;40.74979;14.52523;34;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;The enthusiastic owners of Acqua & Sale have transformed what was originally a simple fishmonger’s into a restaurant with the addition of an informal, well-appointed dining room on the side. Here, guests enjoy unfussy fresh fish dishes, including an array of raw options and Mediterranean recipes with the occasional personal touch. Recipes include grilled octopus with black broccoli and wine-fermented plums, and porchetta-style tuna with a green sauce, fried new potatoes and sweet and sour peppers. The perfect choice for fish-lovers!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7178;hakubi;Japan;Kyoto;481-1 Kiyoicho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0821, Japan;35.001918;135.778411;100;true;false;Chinese;Chinese cuisine with a modern interpretation. Lifting a page from the lavish entertainment of the imperial court, hakubi populates its prix fixe menus with multiple courses of small dishes. Rice vermicelli paired with caviar and chicken wing tips wrapped in foie gras signify cuisine unafraid of incorporating Western elements. Dressings of chilli sauce and mayonnaise for shrimp set up an interesting taste comparison. A whimsical spirit pervades the fare, setting the heart racing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7179;RiVi;Japan;Osaka;1-16-28 Kyomachibori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0003, Japan;34.68719;135.493928;48;true;false;Contemporary;Drawing from experience in Italian and French cuisine as well as pastries, RiVi creates a genre-less cuisine. It is a dialogue between Japanese cuisine, the influence of the chef’s birth and upbringing, and the Western cultures he admires. As his craft is always evolving, he has no standard dishes. The theme of the first half of the prix fixe menu is a celebration of all things Osaka. The meal finishes with seasonal mixed rice because he wants his guests to taste it with the bowl in their hand. Crockery created by an artisan adds beauty to the presentation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7180;Torisho sai;Japan;Kyoto;237 Daimonjicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8315, Japan;35.010691;135.749828;21;false;false;Yakitori;Both charcoal and wood flames are in this restaurant’s arsenal. These ancient heat sources draw out the deliciousness of the free-range Hinai-jidori chicken. The meat is rested in a curing house, judiciously draining moisture to concentrate the flavour. Service begins with a single skewer of breast meat, the better to showcase the poultry’s delicious taste. The kagoyaki technique, which wreathes the meat in fire and smoke, is an idea borrowed from the yakitori traditions of Miyazaki. Dinner ends with a bowl of ginger rice in chicken broth, cooked over wood flame.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7182;ristorante DONO;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 62 Okazaki Enshojicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8344, Japan;35.011584;135.782369;75;true;false;Italian;The dining room overlooks the torii gate of Heian Shrine. Dono means ‘sharing with others what is given’, encapsulating gratitude for the bounty of nature and the seasons. In Italy, the chef learned the importance of taking pride in the fruits of the good earth, and he delights in tilling his own fields, raising vegetables and gathering edible wild plants in hill and dale. The chef, second son of the owner of Sojiki Nakahigashi, joins his father in protecting the food culture of the Kyoto region and carrying on the spirit of Italy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7184;Kikunoi Sushi Ao;Japan;Kyoto;463-30 Shimokawaracho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0825, Japan;34.999895;135.77967;42;true;false;Sushi;A ‘sushi kappo’ opened by the ryotei Kikunoi. Sushi is Japanese food, after all, so inventive steps are taken to incorporate sushi into the proceedings, interspersing nigiri into the flow of appetisers, sashimi and soup. Treatment of ingredients is unique: for example, Japanese tiger prawn is char-grilled and scorched in the shell, and conger eel is seasoned with black seven-spices and buds of the pepper tree. Another thing you won’t find elsewhere is the ability to choose from serving ware and sake decanters crafted by none other than legendary ceramicist and epicure Rosanjin.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7185;Shimogamo Ichima;Japan;Kyoto;93-1 Shimogamo Nishihangicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-0827, Japan;35.043513;135.766053;71;true;true;Sushi;The plump little orbs of temari sushi look adorable. The restaurant began when the chef’s grandfather, emulating the fine craftsmanship of saikuzushi, created sushi small enough for geisha and maiko to consume in a single bite. The range is impressive, encompassing sea bream, tuna, shrimp and much more. The chef shapes the temari sushi gently by hand, so the sushi rice delicately breaks apart in the mouth. Picking out the flavours as one eats is part of the enjoyment. In true Kyoto culinary style, mackerel sushi is offered in autumn, with steamed sushi in winter. A comprehensive range of à la carte items is available in the evenings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7186;Etto;Japan;Kyoto;47 Daikokuyacho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8055, Japan;35.021511;135.753727;88;true;false;Italian;Etto is Italian for ‘intimacy’. It’s hard to tell where the counter ends and the open kitchen begins, so guests and chef become entwined in a single, intimate space. Italian cuisine is accented by Japan’s four seasons. Antipasto misto, served on a Kiyomizu-yaki platter and strewn with leaves of the season, has a hassun sensibility. Five small dishes of salty and sour morsels keep the wine flowing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7187;Ryoriya Kanemitsu;Japan;Kyoto;368 Shijocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8441, Japan;35.002674;135.756584;56;false;true;Japanese;The beams of a merchant townhouse frame a soaring atrium with table seating. As conversation sparkles around the tables, the chef focuses squarely on his cooking, showing the respect for ingredients he learned as an apprentice. The chef visits farmers in Takagamine and Kamigamo, feeling the seasons in his bones as he carefully selects his veggies. Seafood is char-grilled and garnished with vegetables. Presentation is simple, yet the chef’s unique stamp on the fare is unmistakable.;Air conditioning;[]
7188;Tempura Sakugetsu;Japan;Osaka;2-9-26 Shimanochi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0082, Japan;34.669966;135.508211;43;true;true;Tempura;A restaurant under the aegis of Shunsaiten Tsuchiya. The name means ‘new moon’, signifying a new beginning, and indeed Sakugetsu takes tempura in new directions while respecting tradition. The chef entrusted with this restaurant has his own approach, firmly emphasising the quality of the tempura pieces themselves. Those pieces are deep-fried in cottonseed oil mixed with sesame oil. In one innovation, the chef eschews the use of tempura paper, instead draining oil through skilled technique.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7190;Isoyama;Japan;Kyoto;212-3 Nabeyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8015, Japan;35.005038;135.770983;57;true;true;Japanese;Light streams from a small sign in a Pontocho back alley. Inside the cozy interior popular tunes from the Showa era play, creating a pub atmosphere. The omakase set menu is a series of numerous small plates and bowls. Sushi of vinegared mackerel, simmered octopus and roast duck are products of izakaya training, while soups and char-grilled items bring kappo experience to bear. Grilled fish is paired with shuto (pickled and seasoned fish entrails) and konowata (salted sea cucumber entrails) paste, carefully chosen for their affinity with sake.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7191;Takeda;Japan;Osaka;2F, 2-1-6 Tsuriganecho, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0035, Japan;34.688194;135.51402;17;false;false;Japanese;Indigo-dyed norens are a traditional craft of Tokushima. Indigo blue is the keynote colour of chairs and trays as well, symbolising Tokushima and declaring the chef’s birthplace. Seafood arrives from fishermen in Naruto and Minami. Vegetables and soy sauce are also specially sourced, and the brand-name citrus fruit is a point of pride. Soba-gome jiru porridge is hometown cooking prepared with buckwheat seeds and vegetables. Be sure to try the ramen, made with Handa somen. In Osaka, the city of the chef’s apprenticeship, he showcases the charms of his hometown.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7192;Mashino Ken;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-3-6 Awajimachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0047, Japan;34.673359;135.517416;27;false;true;Chinese;The cuisine of Hong Kong touched off a journey of exploration into the depth and richness of Chinese cooking. The chef studied each region’s history and culture to plumb the origins of each. His passion shines as he explains the roots of each cuisine, referring to his own experiences and the menu in Cantonese. Peking duck as standard fare ensures he never forgets where he came from. Patient work making miso and rolling dough drive his zeal for constant improvement.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7193;Shunzen Kiraku;Japan;Osaka;1-3-16 Tohei, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0063, Japan;34.670647;135.518482;46;true;true;Japanese;This Japanese restaurant is in the style of a Naniwa (Osaka) kappo. The procession starts with a combination platter of seafood, vegetables and sushi. The menu ranges from grilled and simmered items that hew close to the basics to offerings with a creative spin such as bisques and frites. The chef’s greatest joy is concocting dishes that connect on an emotional level: indicate a preference and he is happy to prepare your dish the way you like it. He keeps in his heart the teaching of his mentor: the true measure of a chef is the ability to tailor each dish to the taste of the diner.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7194;TimeSpirit;United Kingdom;Aberlour;The Macallan Estate,  Easter Elchies, Aberlour, AB38 9RX, United Kingdom;57.4869367;-3.2089918;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Forming part of The Macallan Estate, this is a beautiful restaurant from top to bottom. It sits on the first floor of the futuristic distillery, with floor-to-ceiling windows affording Speyside views that are just as stunning as the open kitchen, the whisky wall and the wine cellar. There’s immaculate presentation in the cooking too, on a menu overseen by the Roca brothers from the famed El Celler de Can Roca in Girona. Their signature ‘Lactic’ dessert makes an appearance, as do several nods to Scotland. Go for the whisky pairing, as it seems appropriate here.;Car park,Great view;[]
7195;The Braywood;United Kingdom;Bray;Littlefield Green, Paley Street, Bray, SL6 3JN, United Kingdom;51.47779;-0.75426;91;false;true;Modern British;What was once the Royal Oak pub was the beneficiary of a lavish conversion from the team behind The Woodspeen, leaving it as this stunning restaurant. The original premises now act as an entrance into a modern, stylish cocktail bar, then to an understatedly elegant dining room that’s impressive in both size and stature. In the summer, there’s an equally attractive terrace awaiting your arrival. The cooking is based on the finest produce from around the UK, so expect luxury ingredients like Dover sole and chateaubriand to share – all accompanied by a serious wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7196;Sonnet;United Kingdom;Alnwick;41 Bondgate Without, Alnwick, NE66 1PR, United Kingdom;55.4123028;-1.7031102;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A sonnet is a 14-line poem, and so the culinary poetry here takes the form of 14 courses, each one crafted with real care by Chef Gary McDermott. He and his partner Claudia, a natural host, have created a deeply personal restaurant, with many of the dishes coming with a story attached and plenty of attention given to each of the eight tables. The cooking blends classic French techniques with some well-balanced preserved elements. In an endearing touch that is typical of the place, dinner ends with ‘Elevenses’ for you to take home and enjoy the following morning.;;[]
7197;The Plough;United Kingdom;Wombleton;Main Street, Wombleton, YO62 7RW, United Kingdom;54.2476502;-0.9746423;79;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Richard and Lindsey Johns are experience operators in this part of the world. For their latest project, they’ve taken on this attractive 16th-century inn situated between the Howardian Hills and the North York Moors. There’s plenty of character to the place, from the beamed ceiling to the roaring fire for winter and beer garden for summer. Chef Richard offers hearty dishes that are classically and wholly enjoyable, like a generous pork chop cooked with evident skill. Lindsey looks after every table with a genuine warmth and personal touch.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7198;BALOCI;United Kingdom;Birmingham;18 Highfield Road, Birmingham, B15 3DU, United Kingdom;52.4687762;-1.9232544;38;false;false;Asian and Western;An elegant Georgian townhouse has been given a bold and blingy makeover for this opulent restaurant, where the décor blends rich, plush furnishings with flashes of shiny gilt. The cooking is self-described as ‘Indo-Persian’ and indeed the menu is an enticing melting pot of influences, including those from Afghanistan, Turkey and Balochistan. The tasting menu will allow you to try a broader range of cuisines, but if you’re going à la carte then keep an eye out for the Sultani lamb chops, which melt in the mouth and are enhanced by their subtle spicing.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7199;Wildflowers;United Kingdom;London;57 Pimlico Road, Pimlico, London, SW1W 8NE, United Kingdom;51.4903918;-0.1529152;72;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Newson's Yard is a stylish development just off Ebury Street and among its high-end inhabitants is this split-level restaurant. An open kitchen adds to its homely feel, while the bar tucked under the first-floor eaves is perfect for a cosy drink. There’s a firmly Mediterranean heart to the menu, with the produce-driven and slightly rustic dishes proving to be comforting and full-flavoured. One slice of the homemade focaccia will leave you wanting more and the Italian citrus tart is a refreshing way to end. Genuine, friendly service adds to the joy.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7200;Margo;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;68 Miller Street, Glasgow City, G1 1DT, United Kingdom;55.8592772;-4.2507632;100;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;As a sister restaurant to Ox and Finch and Ka Pao, you can probably guess what you’re getting with Margo: a bustling, efficiently run restaurant that’s deservedly popular thanks to its great buzz and flavour-packed, generously priced dishes. It’s a cavernous place spread over two floors, with a semi-industrial feel and its lively atmosphere enhanced by the open kitchen. The sharing plates are a satisfying synthesis of Mediterranean cooking and Scottish produce, borne out in dishes like red prawn agnolotti and ham hough croquettes. Below, you’ll find Sebb’s – a cocktail bar with wood-fired grilling.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7201;The Great Bustard;United Kingdom;Great Durnford;Great Durnford, SP4 6AY, United Kingdom;51.140451;-1.8087444;59;false;false;Modern British;‘Immaculate’ is the best way to describe this beautifully restored 19th-century property, located in a pretty village and surrounded by manicured grounds. The pub area is all country warmth and roaring fires, while the restaurant is bright and modern thanks to its floor-to-ceiling windows. The menu aims to please all-comers, with steaks and burgers joined by more elaborate preparations like sea bass with Morteau sausage and girolles. Make the most of the spectacular renovation by staying the night in one of the 10 bedrooms, split between the main house and courtyard.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7202;Row on 5;United Kingdom;London;5 Savile Row, Mayfair, London, W1S 3PB, United Kingdom;51.5105221;-0.1397601;53;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The name of Jason Atherton’s flagship operation derives from ‘Refinement of Work’ – and indeed there is a great deal of refinement in every inch of this mightily impressive restaurant. The premises, on the iconic Savile Row, have been fitted out with no-expense-spared luxury, while the service is charming and attentive in equal measure. Chef Spencer Metzger leads the kitchen, taking outstanding British produce and adding depth of flavour with utmost skill – like Cornish turbot enhanced by Albufera sauce with turbot liver. The wine list, as you may expect, is an oenophile's delight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7203;Fallachan Kitchen;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;Arch 15, 8 Eastvale Place, Glasgow City, G3 8QG, United Kingdom;55.8640233;-4.2988683;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked underneath a small railway arch near the Kelvingrove neighbourhood, this genially run restaurant is a showcase for Chef Craig Grozier. The rumble of trains overhead only adds to the atmosphere as Craig engages with his small group of guests, all sat around one communal table in front of the open kitchen. The menu changes regularly, such is Craig’s commitment to showcasing the best seasonal Scottish produce, be it Barra scallop or Borders partridge. The punchily flavoured dishes can be paired with a thoughtfully curated wine flight.;;[]
7204;Briar;United Kingdom;Bruton;1 High Street, Bruton, BA10 0AB, United Kingdom;51.1124836;-2.453668;78;true;true;Contemporary, Sharing;Within the charming Georgian hotel that is Number One Townhouse, sits this attractive restaurant which we’d all love to have at the end of our street. It’s the kind of place that warms your heart, run with a genuine friendliness and enthusiasm that’s mirrored by the bright, fresh cooking that can’t help but put a smile on your face. Order three to four of the sharing plates per person and you’ll be treated to great value dishes that burst with flavour – like the buttermilk fried partridge enlivened by pickled shallots and tarragon mayonnaise.;;[]
7205;Three Darlings;United Kingdom;London;241B Pavilion Road, Chelsea, London, SW1X 0BP, United Kingdom;51.4936668;-0.1585939;65;false;false;World Cuisine;A celebration of Jason and Irha Atherton's three daughters, this casual yet elegant modern bistro fits right in among the affluent streets of Chelsea. An all-day operation offering everything from brunch to late-night cocktails, it’s classic Atherton in its lack of pretension and commitment to quality British ingredients. While the likes of Dingley Dell pork and Orkney scallop are the flavourful driving force, the cooking adopts a grab-bag of influences ranging from schnitzel in one course to sobrasada in another, char siu here to katsu curry there.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7206;DA COSTA;United Kingdom;Bruton;Durslade Farm, Dropping Lane, Bruton, BA10 0NL, United Kingdom;51.1087505;-2.4473208;79;false;false;Italian;The stunning Art Farm development makes a fitting home for this equally gorgeous restaurant. As soon as you enter, you’re met with the enticing aroma of wood-fired cooking, emanating from the breathtakingly designed open kitchen. With pots, pans and even chairs hanging from the ceiling, plus an abundance of wooden furnishings, it’s like dining in a particularly chic country kitchen. The menu looks to all things Italian, with terrific hand-cut pasta and hearty, wholesome flavours across the board – bigoli with venison ragu is the epitome of the style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7207;Hem;United Kingdom;Warwick;22 Market Place, Warwick, CV34 4SL, United Kingdom;52.2821987;-1.5907706;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the market square of this historic town, you’ll find a lovely little restaurant. Named Hem in reference to previous incarnation ‘Tailors’ – which before that was an actual tailor’s – it’s a simple and unpretentious place, where long-standing friends Dan and Seb run the show with a smile. Dan is the chef of the pair, cooking hearty and satisfying dishes that are classic in their origins but executed with refinement and a playful touch – such as venison haunch with pear, walnut ketchup and bacon jam. Go for one of the carefully curated wine flights.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7208;FIFTY TWO;United Kingdom;Harrogate;Follifoot, Harrogate, HG3 1JH, United Kingdom;53.9726725;-1.4951622;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Set in the grounds of the Rudding Park hotel and named after the number of raised beds in its kitchen garden, this is a restaurant guided by its produce. It occupies a set of converted shipping containers, furnished with bespoke oak tables, where the chefs lead the service of their creative dishes. There’s a playfulness running throughout, exemplified by ‘Dessert Islands Discs’, where guests can choose a track to play while the puddings are served. Those desserts are a highlight, with exquisite execution of dishes like brown butter custard tart with baked apple.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
7209;Starling;United Kingdom;Esher;3 High Street, Esher, KT10 9QJ, United Kingdom;51.3709737;-0.3630118;64;true;true;Modern British;The first solo opening of experienced chef Nick Beardshaw is this neighbourhood restaurant, where its lack of pretension makes it all the more endearing. The décor inside the surprisingly spacious dining room is simple yet elegant, while the menu consists of the kind of seemingly straightforward dishes that are tricky to pull off yet so easy to eat. Nick’s signature dish of Orkney scallop with Thai green curry sauce is a prime example, the technical skill and balance of flavours shining through. There’s a good selection of steaks and a great value lunch deal too.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7211;Fonda;United Kingdom;London;12 Heddon Street, Mayfair, London, W1B 4BZ, United Kingdom;51.5112286;-0.1396099;32;false;true;Mexican;The foodie hotspot of Heddon Street, tucked away on the edge of Soho, is the setting for this busy Mexican restaurant from KOL founder Santiago Lastra. In Mexico, a ‘fonda’ is a family-owned spot usually with just a few tables – here they have supersized the concept, with diners spread across two floors of the bright, airy restaurant decorated with light wood, foliage and colourful ceramic tiles. Kick off with a cocktail from the extensive list before sharing dishes like slow-cooked carnitas with fresh tortillas. Santiago’s signature cheesecake is a great way to finish.;Air conditioning;[]
7212;Circa Totnes;United Kingdom;Totnes;26 High Street, Totnes, TQ9 5RY, United Kingdom;50.4315317;-3.6884691;88;true;false;Modern British;With stints as both a cobbler’s and a theatre for the Mayor of Totnes, this lovely 18th-century building has lived many lives over the years. Its latest incarnation is a friendly sharing plates restaurant with a bistro buzz, bringing a dose of welcoming hospitality to the charming Totnes High Street. The menu displays a modern outlook in its sharing plates format and incorporation of both fermented elements and open-flame cooking. The service has a genuine warmth to it, with the owners keen to ensure you’re having a good time.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7213;Amari;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;15 Baker Street, Brighton and Hove, BN1 4JN, United Kingdom;50.8318816;-0.1351966;82;true;true;Spanish;Look out for the bright-red exterior that draws you like a beacon to this Spanish-inspired restaurant tucked down a busy side street in the north of the city. The simply decorated setting keeps the focus on the food, with a menu full of dishes that deliver on their promise: the croquetas are creamy, the crudo is refreshing and the suckling pig is prepared with skill. The wine list is expectedly Spanish in its focus, while the selection of sherries is the ideal way to kick off the evening.;;[]
7214;Dishes;United Kingdom;Prestatyn;194 High Street, Prestatyn, LL19 9BW, United Kingdom;53.3328391;-3.4018363;41;false;true;British Contemporary;Chef Andrew Sheridan has returned to his native north Wales to open this stylish restaurant occupying a former cloth shop on the High Street. Take a seat at the counter or a high-topped table and relish the opportunity to delve into a roll-call of terrific Welsh ingredients – be it meaty Menai oysters or caramelised mutton belly from just up the road. Order sharing plates from the à la carte or opt for the chef’s choice if you’re indecisive. A relaxed atmosphere pervades throughout, with both the service team and chefs adept at interacting with their guests.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7215;Satori;United Kingdom;Birmingham;2C St. Mary's Row, Wake Green Road, Moseley, Birmingham, B13 9EZ, United Kingdom;52.4458228;-1.8839352;39;true;true;Japanese;An array of both classic and contemporary Japanese dishes are available at this on-trend restaurant, whose bustling atmosphere suggests it’s a hit with the local diners. The wide-ranging à la carte covers all your Japanese favourites, from sushi and sashimi to super-fine tempura and a choice of cuts from the robata grill. If you want a taste of it all, the well-priced tasting menu is the best option. To finish, ‘Mount Fuji’ is their take on a Mont Blanc, set alight at the table for added volcanic flair.;;[]
7217;OTHER;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;32 Cannon Street, Bedminster, City of Bristol, BS3 1BN, United Kingdom;51.441328;-2.6012076;49;false;false;Sharing;If you were to ask Chef Zak Hitchman what kind of food he cooks, you may not get a clear answer, such is the variety of influences that he skilfully adopts. That’s borne out here in a playful, constantly changing menu served inside this small, modish bistro with bright orange walls. If there’s anything on the menu involving the hot and sour crab sauce, don’t hesitate in ordering it, as it’s the perfect encapsulation of the kitchen’s understanding of flavour. Everything, including the wines, comes with an appealing price tag and the friendly service is the icing on the cake.;;[]
7218;Le Vin Perdu;United Kingdom;Ashburton;11 West Street, Ashburton, TQ13 7DT, United Kingdom;50.5150095;-3.7568707;96;false;true;French;The team behind Emilia, situated just a few doors down, have imparted another gift to the residents of Ashburton with this delightful rustic bistro. Where its sister operation is all-Italian, Le Vin Perdu is full-blooded French in its approach, so don’t be surprised to find the likes of pork terrine or rotisserie chicken on the menu. The décor is understatedly chic, with the bar making a great place for a cocktail or a glass of wine from the blackboard list. If you’re sweet of tooth, the tarte Tatin is a great note to end on.;Terrace;[]
7219;AngloThai;United Kingdom;London;22 Seymour Place, Marylebone, London, W1H 7NL, United Kingdom;51.515139;-0.161181;74;true;true;Thai;‘Rooted in Thailand, Uniquely British’ is the tagline of this joyfully run restaurant from John and Desiree Chantarasak – John is half-Thai, half-British, a duality that informs his cuisine. The exemplary ingredients – from crab to venison – are sourced from across the UK, including from Desiree’s family’s farm, but you can certainly expect more than British ingredients simply married with Thai flavours. There are reimagined and innovative dishes aplenty here too, such as Brixham crab with caviar and coconut ash cracker. Clever sourcing also extends to the furniture, with the tables made from Chamchuri wood by craftsmen in Chiang Mai.;;[]
7220;The Old Manse of Blair Restaurant;United Kingdom;Blair Athol;Blair Athol, PH18 5TN, United Kingdom;56.7722745;-3.9046898;21;true;false;Modern Cuisine;As the name suggests, this restaurant is housed in the former manse to the nearby Blair Castle. This building is impressive in itself, a substantial property situated within 10 acres of grounds and boasting a restored walled garden. The restaurant occupies a newly built orangery, which despite the country house feel to the surroundings has a pleasingly relaxed air. The cooking is Scottish to the core, with produce like Skye langoustine and Perthshire mallard used in dishes with nothing superfluous on the plate. Add in the rooms and chatty service and you have a perfect base for exploring the Highlands.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
7221;The Lamb Inn;United Kingdom;Oxford;High Street, Little Milton, Oxford, OX44 7PU, United Kingdom;51.7038466;-1.105976;96;true;true;English;With its whitewashed exterior and thatched roof, this village pub certainly looks the part. Guests are welcomed by the relaxed team into a low-beamed room, where they can enjoy a full meal or a pint at the bar with nibbles. Pub classics run alongside more elaborate dishes, which are united by their well-sourced ingredients and careful preparation. While it may sound simple, the French onion soup sums up everything the kitchen does well – hearty, big-flavoured cooking that is both straightforward and skilful.;Car park;[]
7222;Jericho;United Kingdom;Plungar;45 Barkstone Lane, Plungar, NG13 0JA, United Kingdom;52.8998791;-0.8543774;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This rustic and rural restaurant in the Vale of Belvoir is located on the farmstead where Chef-Owner Richard grew up, divided across two buildings constructed using reclaimed materials from the farm. The menu takes a surprise tasting format, with an extended series of generous, heartily flavoured courses that often involve cooking over charcoal. Richard’s cuisine is informed by his surroundings, with game and kitchen garden vegetables playing a particularly big role. The wine list has a sustainable ethos too, with natural, organic and bio-dynamic options.;Car park;[]
7224;Horse & Groom;United Kingdom;Bourton on the Hill;Bourton on the Hill, GL56 9AQ, United Kingdom;51.99142;-1.74804;49;true;true;Traditional British;Offering a lovely overall package that includes bedrooms and a warming atmosphere, this cosy pub makes a perfect base for exploring the Cotswolds. The 19th-century building has been renovated into a fine-looking property, with a bar area where every local and their dog can have a relaxing drink. The cooking is generous in both size and flavour, with desserts a highlight thanks to options like the terrific poached pear and almond tart. Several themed evenings offer particularly great value for money, be it ‘pie night’ or ‘steak and a pint’.;Car park;[]
7225;North Street Kitchen;United Kingdom;Fowey;55 North Street, Fowey, PL23 1DB, United Kingdom;50.3374172;-4.6331809;85;true;true;Seafood;In the busy months you might have to queue at this simple, trendy boat house conversion – but it’s well worth the wait. The menu is constantly changing as it’s informed by the freshest catch from nearby waters, with the array of seafood allowed to shine with a delicious purity thanks to the simplicity of the preparations. Fowey oysters are often a favourite, as is the signature brown crab rarebit. Owner Ethan cooks on his own and there’s an endearingly rustic, no-nonsense feel to the place.;Terrace;[]
7227;Adraba;France;Paris;40 rue Véron, Paris, 75018, France;48.8851827;2.3350026;26;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The team at the helm of this trendy restaurant with an upbeat atmosphere is a group of friends headed up by Israeli chef Elior Benaroche, once sous-chef at Balagan and an associate of Assaf Granit since his early days in the heart of Jerusalem's Old City. Tapping into the Levant and the chef's family history, this cuisine is a festival of spices and condiments: hilbeh (fenugreek paste), ezme (Turkish salad of charcoal-roasted vegetables), tahini, zaatar, harif (marinated chillis), tulum (Turkish cheese) – rounded off by a fine cocktail menu. A culinary voyage.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7228;Mirabelle;France;Langres;Clos Vauban, 1 place du Colonel-de-Grouchy, Langres, 52200, France;47.8588399;5.3334099;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Martine and Laurent Petit have chosen to write a new chapter in their story on these premises that used to be an officers' mess – in an elegant townhouse next to the Porte des Moulins. The great chef has teamed up with Valentin Loison (in the kitchen) and Anaïs Bercegeay (front of house) to bring this ambitious project to life. Surrounded by a magnificent vegetable garden, the house has been turned into a hotel that accommodates two restaurants. At Mirabelle, the atmosphere is resolutely warm and convivial, providing the perfect setting for diners to savour the indulgent cuisine made with ingredients from the garden and small-scale local producers: think chicken pâté en croûte with black trumpet mushrooms, trout coated in a bread crust and cooked on one side, or roasted hazelnut millefeuille.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7230;Le Sarment;France;Auxerre;37 rue du Pont, Auxerre, 89000, France;47.79446;3.5747944;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At this restaurant, the name of which means "vine shoot", a pair of chefs work in tandem to cook up honest, unpretentious cuisine. The ingredients and produce – particularly the vegetables – retain all their flavour and remain true to themselves, in dishes such as roast beetroot with beef tataki and a hint of garlic. The desserts, too, are meticulously made, a case in point being the amandine-style pear with green cardamom and yuzu. The menu-carte features mouthwatering dishes!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7231;Jarapea;France;Irouléguy;94 rue du Fronton, Irouléguy, 64220, France;43.1774068;-1.2998546;91;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After spending almost 15 years in Chile, Michel Moutroustéguy and his partner decided to return to the chef’s homeland. In the peaceful Basque countryside, their table is open for lunch on weekdays and on Saturday evenings. The simply presented blackboard menu reveals a concise selection of sensibly priced dishes in a market-fresh vein. The chef seeks to highlight local seasonal produce, rolling out his know-how gleaned all over the world: sauces and gravies that pack a punch, consummate craftsmanship and high-flying seasonings. From starter to dessert, everything is spot on!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7232;L'Angle;France;Laguépie;11 rue du 19-Mars-1962, Laguépie, 82250, France;44.1436624;1.9716662;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This hidden gem is nestled in a village at the confluence of two rivers – the Aveyron and the Viaur. A contemporary take on an artists' bistro, it boasts artwork on the walls and affordable prices. Working solo in his small, glass-walled kitchen, chef Arnaud Ronxin crafts ingenious dishes with the mission of showcasing seasonal produce. Think oven-roasted veal with confit potatoes and chanterelles, or lamb trotters with a red wine sauce. The more ambitious multi-course evening set menu is different every evening.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7234;Turbulent;France;Trouville-sur-Mer;1 rue Durand-Couyère, Trouville-sur-Mer, 14360, France;49.3642225;0.0836383;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Just off the tourist trail, these premises, once a crêperie, are now the new headquarters of Jarvis Scott. The bad boy chef, previously at the helm of Liquide, flaunted his talents on French TV's Top Chef. There is a rock 'n' roll vibe to this stripped-back, minimalist space: an intimate first room centred on an open kitchen and, upstairs, a communal table seating 10 guests in a more refined atmosphere. Far from the culinary mores of a seaside resort, the chef shakes up diners' expectations with uninhibited pairings that make a statement: frog's legs teamed with merguez, whelks mingling with sauce algérienne. The chef's message is loud and clear: bold flavours delivered without unnecessary frills. The wine list gives pride of place to natural and organic wines. Be sure to book to save disappointment! Love at first bite.;Interesting wine list;[]
7235;L’Écrin de Marlène;France;Vichy;6 square de la Source-de-l'Hôpital, Vichy, 03200, France;46.1227974;3.4219946;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Nestled in the spa district, the Fer à Cheval shopping mall surrounds the bandstand and the Source de l'Hôpital, which location lends it an undeniable charm. This is the setting in which chef Marlène Chaussemy has set up shop, creating an attractive contemporary decor for her restaurant. Opt for the dining area overlooking the park. By focusing on freshness and seasonality, this cuisine revolving around top-notch ingredients delivers on its promises: tender rack of pork, flavoursome parsnips, delicious delicately breaded black pudding, chocolate soufflé with ice cream and banana flambéed with rum. For those who want to take things up a notch, there is a set menu featuring more premium ingredients (eg pan-fried foie gras, scallops, lamb fillet).;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7240;Phébé;France;Paris;190 rue de Courcelles, Paris, 75017, France;48.8855872;2.2968054;77;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located next to Place du Maréchal-Juin, this charming little 1900s restaurant has a glass front, green wood panelling and listed ceramic tiles. Chef Pauline Nicolas, who trained at Maison Rostang, conjures up enticingly named dishes that live up to their promise once served. For lunch, a delicious starter of Morteau sausage, mushrooms and a vin jaune sauce, followed by trout with braised baby gem lettuce, and for dessert, it doesn't get more indulgent than the poached pear tartlet. Here, the high-quality ingredients are treated with the respect they deserve.;;[]
7242;Hestia;France;Paris;8 rue de la Huchette, Paris, 75005, France;48.8528713;2.3462539;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Hestia, goddess of the hearth, presides over this restaurant that absolutely oozes cachet, with its white beams, stone walls and mirrors. Normandy-born chef Loïc Dantec (previously at 114 Faubourg) devises a seasonal menu only, with dishes that hit the mark, such as Cantal pork entrecôte cooked over an open fire with sweet spices. All the meat is grilled to perfection on the barbecue, ready to be carved tableside. The chef cooks without showboating, making flavour the priority. His partner Filipe Fernandes competently and assiduously manages the restaurant floor.;Air conditioning;[]
7244;Bulle d'Osier;France;Langres;Clos Vauban, 1 place du Colonel-de-Grouchy, Langres, 52200, France;47.8589048;5.3334675;51;true;true;Creative;A former officers' mess, this mansion standing proud next to the Porte des Moulins is now a charming restaurant, designed and set up by chef Laurent Petit. Both the name and decor of this elegant property surrounded by a large vegetable garden pay homage to the tradition of basket-making in Fayl-Billot – the birthplace of this champion of ingredients from Lake Annecy. The carte blanche menu devised by Valentin Loison (the chef from the Jura previously worked at Le Clos des Sens and Mirazur) is creative and on point, drawing inspiration from foraging (polypody), garden vegetables, local livestock (matured Black Angus beef), Saône fishing (carp ventrèche, matured pike-perch, catfish) and hunting (roe deer). These fine, well-balanced dishes are enhanced by sommelier Anaïs (partner of the chef), who oversees things front of house with professionalism and warmth, dispensing judicious wine recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
7246;L'Altitude;France;Courchevel;Le K2 Altitude, 356 route de l'Altiport, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4024154;6.6379133;44;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;At Le K2 Altitude, this restaurant is comfortably installed in a chic mountain-style decor with an intimate atmosphere. The menu comprises traditional French cuisine, and the eye immediately homes in on the classics, the likes of which are served at the great Parisian restaurants – think calf sweetbread, truffle and crayfish vol-au-vent. Flavour and generosity certainly do not fall short, and the whole experience is thoroughly enjoyable, right through to the desserts by Sébastien Vauxion.;Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7247;Maison Avoise;France;Issy-les-Moulineaux;58 promenade du Verger, Issy-les-Moulineaux, 92130, France;48.8173763;2.2665575;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Having previously worked in some prestigious MICHELIN kitchens, (in the restaurants of Guy Savoy, Yannick Alléno and Jean-François Piège), chef Alexis Voisenet has decided to make his mark by opening his restaurant in the casemates of the old fort at Issy-les-Moulineaux. This historical site is a unique setting, with its beautiful contemporary furniture laid out beneath a stone vaulted ceiling. The chef's creative approach results in refined dishes such as John Dory, samphire, kale and rounds of green meat confit in butter, with a matelote sauce. The front-of-house team, all professionals with plenty of experience in MICHELIN-starred kitchens, provides impeccable service. The restaurant also boasts a cellar, where diners can enjoy home-made charcuterie and house-cured meats.;Wheelchair access;[]
7248;Coup de Main;France;Lille;112 rue Saint-André, Lille, 59000, France;50.6460385;3.0558103;85;true;false;Creative;Victor Berthe (previously at Rozó) and Clément Delécluse (France's Young Sommelier of 2021) have set up shop in the heart of the Saint-André neighbourhood in Vieux Lille. With good humour, the two partners welcome diners to their compact little restaurant and wine shop with an open kitchen and vintage furnishings. The short menu sets the tone: starters for sharing, a choice between fish, meat and a vegetarian main, and just two desserts. For dinner, there's also a tasting menu that brilliantly combines seasonal dishes with playful and varied cuisine based on ingredients from small-scale producers, with whom the duo maintain close ties. Natural wine list.;Interesting wine list;[]
7250;Anata;France;Megève;36 rue Saint-François, Megève, 74120, France;45.8574854;6.6183237;56;false;false;Japanese;Under the same roof as Vous but upstairs, this light wooden counter serves traditional Japanese fare. All the nigiri, California rolls, sashimi, maki, tempura and gyoza are crafted with top-drawer ingredients, such as wagyu beef or Otoro tuna belly. Bento at lunchtime.;;[]
7252;19 Saint Roch;France;Paris;19 rue Saint-Roch, Paris, 75001, France;48.8654057;2.3321759;24;false;false;Creative;Pierre Touitou – one of the emblematic chefs of the new Parisian bistronomy – has already made his mark on the trendiest echelons of the capital's restaurant scene (Vivant etc). Black and white floor tiles pave the way to an open kitchen separated off with a stainless steel-topped counter – eat here for a front row view of the action in the kitchen. The chef and his brigade can be seen conjuring up food in a fresh, creative vein. The seasonings and condiments leave nothing to chance – eg the house-made harissa on the ox tongue and spinach pkaila (Jewish Tunisian stew), or the fresh peas with capers, toasted pine nuts and barberry that accompany the bonito. As you would expect, natural wines take pride of place. Pure dining pleasure.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7255;Première édition;France;Avignon;5 rue Prévôt, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9465983;4.8063679;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this pleasant bistro in the heart of the city, with its industrial-style interior, street art touches and an open kitchen with a waxed-concrete bar, Jonathan provides friendly, professional service. Meanwhile, in the kitchen, chef Aurélie cooks up creative dishes inspired by bistro recipes or comfort food, adding a playful twist by means of spices, herbs, berries or dried fruit. Examples include devilled eggs with red curry, an old-school pita bread with braised shredded beef and a sesame cream, Carnaroli risotto with chanterelle mushrooms, or Aubrac beef tenderloin with a chicken sauce and suji seaweed. This is tasty, lively fare with a sense of fun, and the motto "come, eat, drink" perfectly sums up the simplicity and bon vivant spirit of the place.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7257;fumée;Taiwan;Taipei;B3, Regent Hotel, 3, Lane 39, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.05407;121.52506;62;false;false;Yakitori;The sister restaurant of the Osakan yakitori institution Ichimatsu sports a dark colour scheme, reminiscent of an opera house. The young Japanese chef sources local poultry such as Hsinchu free-range chicken, and Wenchang chicken for his kebabs along with local herbs like prickly ash and maqaw. The set menu with 10+ courses showcases an array of textures and flavours. Consider paying extra for rare cuts such as shiro reba and kinkan.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
7258;J Parc;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;1 Dexing Street, Sanmin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6466668;120.2905605;50;false;true;Creative;After formal training in the US, the chef-owner launched J Parc in 2023. His 10-course prix-fixe aligns with the seasons, presenting audacious creations that celebrate local vegetables and Japanese seafood, underpinned by French, Italian and American techniques. Mildly sweet bread made with chestnut flour is a nod to the harvest season. Ask for counter seats for up-close views of the chef at work in the semi-open kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7260;Su Lai Chuan;Taiwan;Taipei;4, Lane 176, Section 3, Heping West Road, Wanhua District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0350132;121.497697;38;true;true;Small eats;Famous for ba-wan and taro cake, this institution celebrated its 70th anniversary with a facelift in 2024. The third-generation owner still makes ba-wan like his grandparents did – freshly ground rice milk is poured into a bowl before a filling of pork shin, shiitake, chestnut and bamboo shoot is added. The steamed dumpling is then poached in oil, and drizzled with a sweet bean paste and miso sauce. Add garlic purée or home-made chilli sauce for an extra kick.;Air conditioning;[]
7261;Gallina;Greece;Athens;49 Markou Mpotsari & 59 Falirou, Athens, 11742, Greece;37.9645671;23.7260498;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A fine-dining restaurant with a focus not just on the quality of the cuisine but also on a genuine connection between art and gastronomy. Here, chef Pavlos Kiriakis combines French and Greek culinary traditions in dishes that showcase fish and seafood in particular. This harmonious experience extends beyond the boundaries of food thanks to the team of mixologists who create sophisticated cocktails, each one of which is named in honour of a mythological character. In addition, the impressive wine list boasts over 800 labels from different countries. In this vibrant ambience, with its elegant marble tables and a completely open-view kitchen, it is possible to sit in front of the latter to watch the chefs in full action. The floor upstairs is available for a more exclusive and intimate dining experience.;Terrace;[]
7262;Merceri;Greece;Athens;21 Iraklidon Street, Athens, 11851, Greece;37.9757296;23.7170698;86;false;false;Greek;This welcoming bistro, close to the Herakleidon Museum is run by two chefs with experience gained at luxury hotels on the island of Santorini. Here, they showcase their talents through contemporary dishes with an international flavour, but which are based around typical Greek recipes. The offer is available à la carte or in a tasting menu, with wine pairing options.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7263;VERi TABLE;Greece;Athens;8 Aggelou Sikelianou Street, Athens, 11525, Greece;38.0003006;23.7731073;85;false;false;French;A pleasant French-style bistro away from this delightful city’s main tourist haunts but which comes as a pleasant surprise thanks to its cuisine and friendly service. In this informal space, which is nonetheless elegantly decorated in dark tones and bathed in subdued lighting, savour dishes inspired by Provençal cuisine with a Mediterranean touch. True gourmet-lover and chef Aladin Parodi infuses his dishes with superb technical skill, with a focus on top-quality ingredients, as witnessed by the duck à l’orange – an absolute must here. The dining room is overseen by his wife, Christine Parodi, who devotes herself to providing exquisite service as well as managing the enticing wine cellar, featuring an extensive choice of French labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7264;GB Roof Garden;Greece;Athens;1A Vasileos Georgiou A street, Athens, 105 64, Greece;37.9761919;23.7353896;70;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;If you’re on the lookout for a restaurant that is a little bit special, this could be an excellent option on the 8th floor of the Hotel Grande Bretagne, thanks to its elegant setting and superb picture-postcard views of the Acropolis from both the delightful terrace and dining room. Despite not being overly extensive, the Mediterranean-inspired à la carte focuses specifically on fresh seasonal ingredients, with a special emphasis on Italian cooking, including a small section dedicated to pasta and risotto.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7265;Annie Fine Cooking;Greece;Athens;4 Menaihmou Street, Athens, 11743, Greece;37.9649121;23.7307863;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This attractive neighbourhood restaurant, located along a tranquil tree-lined street away from the busy tourist heart of the city, boasts an everyday, informal ambience, along with a simple pavement terrace and striking touches of color in the dining room, with its open kitchen. It’s mainly local clientele flock here to enjoy dishes from the concise à la carte that are an updated take on Greek recipes and based around fresh, seasonal and locally sourced ingredients that showcase the country’s cuisine to the full.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7266;Linou Soumpasis k sia;Greece;Athens;2 Melanthiou Street, Athens, 10554, Greece;37.9793464;23.7257414;100;true;false;Greek;A casual and contemporary “new-age taverna” in the central Psiri district of the city where it occupies a former candle shop (whose products are still sold here to this day). Greek cooking is based around unpretentious yet delicious dishes that always showcase the restaurant’s commitment to organic ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7267;Ovio;Greece;Athens;4 Apollonos, Athens, 105557, Greece;37.97482;23.73274;50;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Run by celebrity chef Panos Ioannidis, this restaurant is, without doubt, an excellent choice for those exploring the busy streets of central Athens. In this spacious setting, divided into three dining areas (one on the ground floor, a few tables upstairs, plus a pleasant terrace) the chef offers a menu based around Italian cuisine. This includes homemade pastas, such as the delicious Gnocchi with a velvety sauce, diced pear, grated walnuts and finished with gorgonzola in two textures. These are complemented by meat dishes and pizzas cooked in the wood-fired oven, plus an extensive selection of Italian wines and a balcony where guests can savour an array of impressive cocktails.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7268;Simul;Greece;Athens;63 Ipsilantou Street, Athens, 11521, Greece;37.977953;23.7503235;64;false;false;Creative;Personality, irreverence, risk, youthfulness, technique and quality are the words that spring to mind when we think of Simul, a restaurant that is always focused on cuisine prepared “in-situ” with the very best seasonal ingredients. In the informal dining room, chef Nikos Thomas (perhaps better known for his appearances on MasterChef) offers his guests a choice between a continually evolving and creative à la carte and an impressive tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
7269;Aleria;Greece;Athens;57 Megalou Alexandrou Street, Athens, 10435, Greece;37.9830707;23.7177024;96;false;true;Greek;Time seems to have stood still in this beautiful restaurant occupying a neo-Classical residence from the mid 1800s, where the delightful patio, contemporary decorative features and 19C spirit come as a pleasant surprise. Here, the focus is on updated Greek cuisine presented in two menus (both with 5- or 6-course options): one entitled Earth & Sea, the other, the vegetarian-based Garden & Nature.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7270;Aneton;Greece;Athens;3 Navarchou Nikodimou Street, Athens, 10 557, Greece;37.9734774;23.7330885;51;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Aneton moved from its previous location in Maroussi to this stylish, two-floored restaurant in the heart of the city, bringing with it its vibrant, eye-catching cooking. Lunch is light, with dinner providing the most interesting options, and the seasons lead the way. Service is friendly and engaging.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7271;Dolli's;Greece;Athens;49 Mitropoleos, Athens, 10556, Greece;37.9758428;23.7280853;60;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Asian;If the thought of enjoying a pleasant meal with an idyllic view appeals to you, then this could be the place. This restaurant is located on the fifth floor of the luxury The Dolli at Acropolis hotel, a historic mansion that has been completely remodelled and boasts picture-postcard views of the Acropolis. The menu here is a combination of Mediterranean cuisine with Asian options prepared by a chef who conjures up dishes within full view of guests in the dining room. Precise and meticulously presented, his dishes are always based around top-quality seasonal ingredients. The gourmet experience is more extensive in the evening and is complemented by the extensive array of wines, including labels from leading wine estates as well as artisanal vineyards.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7272;SENSE;Greece;Athens;5 Dionysiou Areopagitou Street, Athens, 117 42, Greece;37.9695005;23.7308353;81;true;false;Creative;Located on the 7th floor of the AthensWas Hotel, SENSE boasts a stunning panoramic terrace with truly spectacular views of the Acropolis at sunset. The cuisine is centred around two tasting menus plus an additional vegetarian option, on which the innovative dishes are a fusion of international cooking and authentic Greek flavours, with plenty of creative detail as an added touch. Many of the aromatic herbs used in the dishes here are grown on the roof terrace.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7273;Vezené;Greece;Athens;11 Vrasida Street, Athens, 11 528, Greece;37.9747156;23.7507301;63;true;false;Grills;If you’re a fan of wood-fired cuisine, we recommend a visit to Vezené (located next to the Evangelismos metro station), a bistro-style restaurant with plenty of elegant decorative touches and an impressive glass porch. The menu is based around traditional Greek cuisine, in which fire plays a key role and via which the majority of the ingredients are prepared, endowing dishes with their unique flavour. It also includes various types of seafood sourced from local producers, as well as aged meats and impressive pastas. At the weekend, the generously portioned Sunday roast is available, which can be enjoyed with all the family, along with the restaurant’s famous signature dessert and a real must: Ari's Deal Closer!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7274;Le Pavillon;Greece;Athens;31 Perikleous Street, Athens, 152 32, Greece;38.0172918;23.7967943;16;false;false;French Contemporary;(Temporarily closed for refurbishment) As soon as French-born chef Jean-Charles Métayer set eyes on this delightful whitewashed villa he is said to have fallen in love with it and immediately decided to set up a restaurant here. On his menus (one with 9 courses, the other 12), guests can savour contemporary cuisine that constantly interlinks French and Greek culinary influences, as both countries are key components of the chef’s unique career and life. The delicious and unusual “chocolate and mushroom textures” dessert definitely came as a surprise!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7275;Varoulko Seaside;Greece;Athens;54 Koumoundourou Coast, Athens, 18533, Greece;37.9373787;23.6585274;65;true;false;Seafood;If you’re looking for a restaurant with an authentic maritime flavour, this eatery overlooking the small yet attractive port of Mikrolimano will come as a pleasant surprise. Here, the relaxing ambience is in perfect harmony with superb views of the fishing boats moored out front. Traditionally, Piraeus is known as the port of Athens, hence the plethora of tavernas and restaurants specialising in fish and seafood located here. Varoulko Seaside follows the same influence, although chef Lefteris Lazarou takes his maritime cuisine to another level. The freshest ingredients are key to his cuisine which is based around the catch of the day (sea bass, red mullet, grouper, tuna, shrimp, prawns etc) and presented on an à la carte and two tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7276;see|ds;Greece;Athens;14 Oumplianis, 27 Diocharous, Athens, 16121, Greece;37.9730333;23.7536847;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with plenty of personality located in a residential district of the city and which takes its name from the combinations of the word “see” and the initials of young chef Dimos Samouraki to create “Seeds”. The simple, modern cuisine, centred around locally sourced seasonal ingredients and a minimalist aesthetic, is showcased on two tasting menus (Short Talk and Long Story) that show French culinary influence and vary only in their number of courses. In addition, an interesting vegan option is also available. For those who prefer more exclusivity, the floor upstairs has a loft with an elegant dining space for 10 guests, where they can enjoy a more personalised experience seated next to the superb wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7278;Esthiō;Greece;Athens;7 Dimitrakopoulou, Athens, 11742, Greece;37.9667826;23.7282204;100;false;false;Balkan;This restaurant, the name of which translates as “eat and treat” in Ancient Greek, occupies a charming neo-Classical building dating back to 1931 close to the heart of the city. Here, Albanian-born chef Elvi Dimitris Zyba curates Balkan-inspired cuisine which offers a fusion between different cultures and combines the traditional with the contemporary. His cooking takes its inspiration from recipes that his mother used to prepare when he was a child to which he adds a more sophisticated and refined touch. Examples include the traditional “Giaourtotavas”, made with lamb sweetbreads, yoghurt and rice, and various seafood-based options, such as the Octopus stew, wrapped in handmade filo pastry with a sublime salmon roe cream. Desserts also have a Balkan touch, such as the Grape juice cream served with grape must cookies.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7279;Pinus im Seegut;Germany;Friedrichshafen;Ziegelstraße 5, Friedrichshafen, 88048, Germany;47.6691785;9.4070291;30;false;true;Sharing, Regional Cuisine;Following stints at some prestigious restaurants, Philipp Heid has been head chef at the Pinus restaurant at Seegut Zeppelin hotel since May 2024. Here, he has created a laid-back sharing concept featuring modern and light dishes. The menu is predominantly vegetarian, but there are also meat options. Feel free to order as you please – there's no traditional menu progression, and sharing is optional. The dishes are arranged according to their flavour profiles: fruity, spicy, with roasted notes, earthy, plant-forward… In addition to fine wines, they have a wide range of non-alcoholic alternatives. The decor is modern upscale, but the atmosphere is comfortably relaxed. There is also a terrace overlooking the lake and the Alps.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7280;SchwarzGold;Germany;Dortmund;Emscherallee 11, Dortmund, 44369, Germany;51.5420051;7.4101378;98;true;true;Regional Cuisine, International;The journey here is an experience in itself: At 6.30pm, diners are picked up from the main car park by golf cart and chauffeured to this restaurant located on the expansive grounds of the Kokerei Hansa industrial heritage site. In keeping with the name, which refers to coal – known as "black gold", the decor here in the basement of an old gas storage features an elegant black and gold colour scheme. Led by Pierre Beckerling, the kitchen team serves up a modern and very creative take on Ruhr Valley cuisine that, while clearly labour-intensive, adheres to a distinct flavour identity. Setting the stage for the five-course set menu (vegetarian version available) are the amuse-bouches titled "Straight outta Ruhrpot". The chefs bring out all of the dishes themselves and are happy to answer any questions. The bartender's house-made non-alcoholic beverage flight is an excellent alternative to the wine pairings. For an aperitif or a nightcap, head to the large bar on the ground floor – the gallery overlooks the open kitchen.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7281;Restaurant 1250;Germany;Pfronten;Auf dem Falkenstein 1, Pfronten, 87459, Germany;47.5701394;10.5916567;97;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Even the drive up to the Boutique Hotel Blaue Burg is an exceptional experience: the view of the region is breathtaking, with a new photo opportunity at every turn. Against this sensational backdrop, the Schlachter family, known for their dedication to the job and their reliably good food, serves seasonally and regionally minded cuisine at Restaurant 1250 – making it a wonderful alternative to the fine dining restaurant, PAVO. The terrace with a view in the direction of the castle and Austria is simply divine. Good to know: they also serve lunch.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7282;Marcel von Winckelmann;Germany;Passau;Hans-Hösl-Str. 3, Passau, 94036, Germany;48.5802555;13.3986555;17;false;false;International, Fusion;Armed with valuable experience gained in top establishments, Marcel von Winckelmann has struck out on his own with this restaurant with an open and friendly vibe. The centrepiece is the horseshoe-shaped chef's table wrapped around the visible kitchen, where you are right in the middle of the action. You can really sense the young team's enthusiasm for interacting with diners – this creates a personalised and authentic atmosphere. The seasonal cooking uses selected ingredients. There is one five-course and one seven-course set menu, with dishes such as Norway lobster, pumpkin, sea buckthorn or pointed cabbage, stracciatella, calamansi. A cheese course can be added to either menu. A vegetarian option is also available upon advance request. As an alternative to the classic wine pairing, the restaurant has a terrific and completely house-made non-alcoholic beverage pairing. Tip: book ahead! For those who prefer a more discreet experience, the private room can accommodate up to 15 guests. In summer, the sheltered terrace is delightful.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7283;Le petit CINQ;Germany;Saarbrücken;Nauwieserstraße 5, Saarbrücken, 66111, Germany;49.2349079;6.9996045;28;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This is a pleasant alternative to the two-star restaurant Esplanade in the very tastefully designed boutique hotel of the same name. The food is modern, with two set menus, one of which is vegetarian. Each comprises three or four courses and changes on a weekly basis. Le petit CINQ takes up residence in the beautiful rooms of the fine dining restaurant when the latter is closed. David Wottke, long-time sous-chef to Esplanade's head chef Silio Del Fabro, is at the helm in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7284;Marly Privé;Germany;Mannheim;Lameystraße 17, Mannheim, 68165, Germany;49.4868075;8.4789198;17;false;true;French, International;The restaurant previously known as "Marly" has moved and is now operating under the name of Marly Privé. In its new smaller and more exclusive setting, this eatery serves classic French cuisine made from top-notch ingredients – chef-owner Gregor Ruppenthal's love for France is on full display. A maximum of 12 guests per seating are lucky enough to partake in a five- or seven-course set menu in an intimate, elegantly designed space (on Fridays, four or five courses). Dishes have names such as "Our octopus salad depuis 1999" or "Line-caught sea bass from Quiberon, leeks, nori algae, pink onions", and are accompanied by a well-stocked wine list. The service team is friendly and attentive. Tip: Don't forget to reserve your spot!;Air conditioning;[]
7285;Osteria La Fenice;Germany;Cuxhaven;Nordersteinstraße 6, Cuxhaven, 27472, Germany;53.8589774;8.6994133;72;false;true;Italian;A slice of Italy in Cuxhaven! Behind a rather unassuming façade on a busy shopping street, a truly welcoming osteria ambiance awaits – the decor features decorative wine racks, closely spaced marble tables and even a Vespa! Not to forget the authentic Italian cuisine made with high-quality, fresh ingredients – the sourdough bread and pasta are both made in-house. The wine list showcases Italian labels. Tip: Italian food items can be purchased to take home.;Terrace;[]
7286;MiZAR;Germany;Würzburg;Katzengasse 7, Würzburg, 97082, Germany;49.7941767;9.9232488;21;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;In April 2024, Konstantin Kuntzsch – formerly of the restaurant Speiseberg in Halle an der Saale – opened his own establishment near Frankfurt's Main River and old town. His business partner and co-founder Florian Mack is your host and sommelier, and heads up the friendly front-of-house team. Ambitious chef Konstantin Kuntzsch conjures up a creative seasonal seven-course set menu. The top-quality ingredients and wines are sourced locally. The attractive modern interior features eye-catching artwork. Tip: Book well in advance and allow plenty of time (dinner starts at 7pm and ends at 10.30pm).;;[]
7287;Damson;United Kingdom;Winterbourne;Winterbourne, RG20 8BB, United Kingdom;51.4456822;-1.3443605;92;true;true;Modern British;Formerly known as The Winterbourne Arms, this smartly refitted former pub is now home to a quite formal yet intimate restaurant. Guests are spread over several rooms, enlivened by splashes of colour, while the open kitchen lets you glimpse the team at work. The menus range from a well-priced lunch offering and an à la carte to a seasonal tasting menu and a Sunday roast, where the meat changes each week. Whatever you order, ensure you finish with a coffee and warm madeleines straight from the oven.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7289;Cardinal;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;14 Eyre Place, Edinburgh, EH3 5EP, United Kingdom;55.9607463;-3.1996804;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Dark, intimate and moody, Cardinal makes for an atmospheric place to dine in the smart suburb of Stockbridge. The set menu – available in a choice of lengths – takes a modern, sometimes creative approach to Scottish produce from both land and sea. Preservation techniques play a key role in several of the dishes, whether it’s fermented plums to accompany the oysters or pickled walnuts to go with the chicken. An international wine list is on hand to accompany the cooking, with a leaning towards natural and low-intervention options.;;[]
7290;Walled Garden;United Kingdom;Colerne;Lucknam Park, Colerne, SN14 8AZ, United Kingdom;51.4563196;-2.2583719;53;true;true;Modern British;The titular garden is that of the exquisite Lucknam Park, one of the finest country house hotels in all the land. Hidden within the carefully manicured hedges, behind the 18th-century manor house, is this inviting, glass-enclosed brasserie. Sit on the gorgeous terrace or at oversized, marble-topped tables in the bright, pristine dining room and choose from a concise selection of vibrant, proudly executed dishes underpinned by textbook culinary technique. Pastas, risottos and freshly fired pizzas add to the Mediterranean vibe, while the day boat fish is hard to resist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7291;Donia;United Kingdom;London;2.14 Top Floor Kingly Court, Carnaby St, Soho, London, W1B 5PW, United Kingdom;51.5127563;-0.1387825;90;true;false;Filipino;Occupying the site where its neighbours Imad’s Syrian Kitchen and Darjeeling Express both started out, Donia is a hugely likeable Filipino restaurant that’ll have you googling flights to Manila before you know it. The young, Filipino-born owner grew up in the UK so expect to see plenty of homegrown produce along with those sweet and sour flavours. Crisp adobo mushroom croquetas are a must, as are the succulent chicken Inasal and the lechon (suckling pig) served with a lovely liver and peppercorn sauce. Bring friends, ignore the slightly testing acoustics and share the love.;Air conditioning;[]
7292;Ibai;United Kingdom;London;90 Bartholomew Close, City of London, London, EC1 7BN, United Kingdom;51.5178904;-0.0988872;30;false;true;Basque;Large, airy and with an industrial-chic vibe that perfectly matches the buzz of its open kitchen, there’s something quite cool about Ibai. Backed by one of the co-owners of Lurra and Donostia, it takes those restaurants’ love of Basque cooking and leans it further towards the region’s French influences. The signature ‘Croque Ibai’ is a prime example and a delicious pintxo to start your meal with. Quality ingredients are used throughout, treated with care and often cooked over fire. Wine enthusiasts will be impressed by the well-stocked cellar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7294;The Kirkmichael Arms;United Kingdom;Kirkmichael;3-5 Straiton Road, Kirkmichael, KA19 7PH, United Kingdom;55.3457617;-4.6175956;83;true;false;Modern British;A small, well-kept Borders village in the shadow of the ‘Ayrshire Alps’ is the setting for this whitewashed pub with a traditional aesthetic and cosy, homely feel. The extensive menu includes some global influences among the pubby favourites, but it’s the signature country pot pies that catch the eye, with a different filling each week and a generous enough portion to satisfy even the most hearty of appetites. Every dish comes with a wine or cocktail recommendation from the well-priced list, and the warm, welcoming team show a real desire to please.;;[]
7295;Ardor;United Kingdom;St Ives;45 Fore Street, St Ives, TR26 1HE, United Kingdom;50.2139495;-5.4804157;86;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Named after a Latin word meaning ‘fire’ or ‘passion’, Ardor is a smart modern brasserie in the heart of St Ives. Chef-Owner Dorian spent a lot of his childhood in Spain and it shows on the menu from beginning to end, from chorizo pillow bread to crèma catalana. Cornish seafood plays a key role, given a vibrant Mediterranean touch by the chefs, while some produce is cooked over the charcoal grill. Get a table on the lower floor to watch the kitchen in action and begin with a sherry tasting to enhance your Spanish experience.;Counter dining;[]
7296;Aragawa;United Kingdom;London;38 Clarges Street, Mayfair, London, W1J 7EN, United Kingdom;51.50674;-0.14519;58;false;false;Japanese Steakhouse;It’s all about the beef at this elegant Mayfair restaurant. Luckily, it’s beef of such extreme quality – so succulent, so naturally flavoursome and so expertly cooked over binchotan charcoal – that you’ll forever be wishing every steak was this good. The available cuts are all Tajima Wagyu, one of the most delicious and highly prized meats in the world, with only salt and pepper used to season the meat. The restaurant itself feels like stepping into someone’s (extremely well-decorated) living room.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7297;DOSA;United Kingdom;London;Mandarin Oriental Mayfair, 22 Hanover Square, Mayfair, London, W1S 1JP, United Kingdom;51.5132954;-0.144065;92;false;true;Korean;Its stunning marble counter is an instant signal of the quality you will find at this Korean restaurant in the basement of the Mandarin Oriental Mayfair hotel. Students of the cuisine will recognise several elements, from kimchi and bibimbap to multiple forms of jang made in-house. It’s all executed with utmost skill and the mostly British produce is of superb quality. The chefs and well-versed service team work in impressive harmony and have a real desire for you to understand the cuisine, but most importantly to enjoy it – and you very much will.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
7298;Nest Farmhouse;United Kingdom;Docking;Docking, PE31 8RK, United Kingdom;52.8875954;0.653411;55;false;false;Country cooking;Part of a 1,000-acre farm and estate, this spacious restaurant is housed inside an extensively rebuilt former farm building that is impressive in both size and structure. The cooking is the sort of uncomplicated, rustic-style fare that makes you want to order every dish on the menu. Traditional options such as lamb faggot or confit duck leg are executed with suitable skill to ensure they’re highly satisfying. There are bedrooms available and a short walk away is a terrace where you can sit back and enjoy the peace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
7299;Raymond's;United Kingdom;Nottingham;8 Stoney Street, Nottingham, NG1 1LH, United Kingdom;52.9532366;-1.1435743;52;true;false;Modern British, Sharing;In the heart of the city’s historic Lace Market neighbourhood, you’ll find this fun and welcoming restaurant that could scarcely be more on-trend. Sharing plates, counter seating, moody lighting, stylishly understated décor… it’s got the lot – and judging by the buzz it’s a recipe for success. Start with the fish crackling if you can, a totally addictive snack served with punchy homemade tartare sauce – it sets the tone perfectly for a menu full of immensely satisfying dishes that are both generously sized and priced.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7300;Arlington;United Kingdom;London;20 Arlington Street, St James's, London, SW1A 1RG, United Kingdom;51.5066741;-0.1407703;76;true;false;European;The much-missed Le Caprice, a celebrity-laden London icon in the affluent environs of St James’s, has been reborn as Arlington. It has the same charming décor as its predecessor, all black-and-white photographs and ’20s elegance, with the banquettes at the back the best seats in the house. The menu dispenses with anything too trendy and instead keeps things classic and wholly enjoyable – think dressed Dorset crab, chicken Milanese and one of the best fishcakes in London. The service team play their part by running the place with a terrific efficiency.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7301;Mary's;United Kingdom;London;8-10 Pollen Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 1NQ, United Kingdom;51.5133373;-0.1423756;47;true;true;Modern British;The one-time site of Pollen Street Social is now home to this relaxed and accessible member of the Jason Atherton stable. Its aim is to cater to all-comers and the chefs pull it off with aplomb. Those in a hurry can sit in The Blind Pig bar area with a Cumbrian beef burger and one of “Mary’s Blood Marys”, while a prix fixe menu offers good value and there’s a vegan offering too. The main à la carte is centred around prime cuts of British meat and fish cooked over the wood-fired grill with impressive technique.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7303;Sesta;United Kingdom;London;52 Wilton Way, London Fields, London, E8 1BG, United Kingdom;51.54558;-0.06109;49;false;false;European Contemporary;Fans of Pidgin had little time to mourn its closure in 2024 as it quickly reopened as Sesta, thanks to the original restaurant’s former chef. The look of the room is similar, but gone is the tasting menu and in its place is an appealing à la carte, which includes delicious snacks such as pea and ham fritters and a beef ragu toastie. British ingredients like Yorkshire chicken and Chalkstream trout sit alongside European and Asian influences from dolma to tempura. There’s a short but terrific cocktail list and plenty of natural wines – and the delightful staff sashay around the small space in an impressively efficient way.;;[]
7306;NIJŪ;United Kingdom;London;20 Berkeley Street, Mayfair, London, W1J 8EE, United Kingdom;51.5089489;-0.1438828;62;false;true;Japanese;The Japanese concept of ‘katei ryōri’ – home-style family dining – is the driving force behind this slick Mayfair operation. Diners are split across two rooms, one more moody and clubby, the other brighter and featuring a small sushi counter. Endo Kazutoshi has designed the menus, which combine the katei ryōri sharing dishes with a sushi selection and Japanese beef cooked over charcoal. Unifying it all is an attention to prime produce, be it the wagyu, the hamachi for the sushi or roasted turbot with furikake and miso butter. Bookend your visit with a drink in the Nipperkin cocktail bar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
7307;RT Café Grill;United Kingdom;Ryde;Royal Maritime House, 17 St. Thomas Street, Ryde, PO33 2DL, United Kingdom;50.7327661;-1.163207;100;true;false;Traditional British;This detached period house in an enviable position overlooking the Solent is the latest enterprise from renowned Isle of Wight chef Robert Thompson. Here, he has created an accessible bistro de luxe offering something for everyone: pies, burgers, steaks, pasta – you name it, they do it and pull it off with aplomb. The dishes may appear straightforward, but the care and technical skill of the chefs ensure they really deliver on flavour. A large garden makes for a perfect summer terrace and the friendly, unfussy service is pitched just right.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7308;Pollini at Ladbroke Hall;United Kingdom;London;79 Barlby Road, Notting Hill, London, W10 6AZ, United Kingdom;51.5232079;-0.2201775;79;false;true;Italian;The former head office of car manufacturer The Rootes Group is perhaps not where you’d expect to find an Italian restaurant, but Ladbroke Hall is no ordinary venue. Located at the top of Ladbroke Grove, it’s a restored Edwardian building that is now a haven for artistic types, holding exhibitions, workshops and music events within its century-old walls. The cooking is textbook Italian, with an ingredient-led simplicity and terrific homemade pastas such as spinach and mozzarella tortellini.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7309;Akub;United Kingdom;London;27 Uxbridge Street, Notting Hill, London, W8 7TQ, United Kingdom;51.50844;-0.19838;73;true;true;International;Named after the flowering thistle that’s also known as 'cardoon', Akub celebrates traditional Palestinian recipes, while simultaneously invigorating them with contemporary twists. The colours and intense flavours are particularly evident in sharing dishes like the ‘crunchy mansaf’, which consists of crispy golden parcels stuffed with rice and tender lamb shoulder. Everything is served in a bright, airy space situated on an equally colourful Notting Hill street. Accompany the food with wine from a list combining French favourites with options from Palestine and Jordan.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
7310;Quartz;Belgium;Ixelles;Rue de la Réforme 22, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8204375;4.356133;36;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Local foodies still remember the street corner premises that housed La Canne en Ville for many years. Chef David-Alexandre Bruno has retained the soul of this former butcher’s shop with its wall tiles and floor mosaics. Bruno honed his skills and love of classical cuisine in upmarket establishments, as the personal spin he effortlessly adds to familiar recipes demonstrates. His take on Bellevue lobster is a splendid example: he pairs the tail with a skinned tomato stuffed with meat from the claws, samphire, a herby cream and vanilla-flavoured tomato stock. Sauces are one of the pieces de résistance of this chef, whose bold personality seeks to shine the spotlight on preferably local produce – simplicity and harmonious flavours are the goal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7311;Divino Gusto;Belgium;Nivelles;Square des Nations Unies 4A, Nivelles, 1400, Belgium;50.6017819;4.3450346;41;false;false;French Contemporary;Despite the Italian name of this elegant restaurant, Marc Grislain’s style is far from restricted to the bel paese. He may be a fan of Mediterranean panache, but that doesn’t prevent him showcasing his mastery of classical techniques together with Asian notes. For example, he might flank a rare rib of steak with veggies such as cream of squash and ginger and a gutsy cooking gravy flavoured with smoky black tea. The sommelier and owner, Gaëtan Poels, can be relied upon to ply you with insightful wine tips to create the perfect pairing. Hats off to this establishment that is enjoying a new lease of life!;Terrace;[]
7312;Klaver;Belgium;Ieper;Poperingseweg 230, Ieper, 8908, Belgium;50.8540929;2.8229756;25;false;false;Modern French;According to chef Korneel Verhulst, there is no reason you can’t start your meal with fries, even in a fine dining establishment. So should you wish to kick off with piping hot French fries and a caper mayonnaise, then go for it! Such is the down-to-earth outlook of this friendly, welcoming establishment. Before finishing your meal with a pancake and coffee, try out the chef’s main courses, some of which are enhanced with Japanese notes. Finely diced kohlrabi, seasoned with a sushi dressing garnish a tartare of Holstein beef, grated Belper Knolle cheese, caviar and curry. Klaver adds a brand-new youthful dimension to fine dining, embodied by Grace, your charming hostess.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7313;La Maison Thai;Belgium;Ouffet;Grand'Place 2, Ouffet, 4590, Belgium;50.4380856;5.4648564;28;true;false;Thai;Adorned in wood carvings in tropical hardwoods, Buddha statues and paintings from the Far East, the setting is as charming as its name suggests (we especially love the room to the rear). The options on the expansive menu are every bit as authentic as the decor. Savour the classic aromas and depth of flavour of succulent chicken thigh in a fragrant massaman curry, or heavenly sweet and sour chilli sauce that elevates fresh spring rolls: a meal here is a leisurely culinary journey with these timeless dishes. Fans of Thai fondue have also come to the right place, but be sure to pre-order.;Terrace;[]
7314;Rock-Fort;Belgium;Brugge;Langestraat 15, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2097184;3.2322453;64;true;true;Seafood;North Sea fish and natural wines are the bedrock of this bright, elegant bistro. Chef Laurent and Eline, in charge of the front of house, who first came to our notice at Amuzee in Zeebrugge, are going from strength to strength as they settle in here. The menu overflows in the generous produce of the North Sea with a distinctive subtle, sometimes spicy edge. The fascinating culinary score is depicted by almost translucent grilled langoustines, which are paired with a dashi umami edge or raw scallops served with green apples and jalapeno. Rock-Fort is alive and kicking – in every sense!;Air conditioning;[]
7315;Restaurant Cloche;Belgium;Hofstade;Hofstade-Dorp 21, Hofstade, 9308, Belgium;50.9605232;4.0346327;33;false;false;Modern French;The bright, elegant venue of Tobias Clocheret and Wim De Mulder stands in the shadow of the belltower of Hofstade church and the front terrace is heavenly in summertime. Top-drawer produce like langoustines and sweetbread is pampered and delicately crafted into succulent recipes. The chef slices scallops into wafer thin carpaccio, adding a beurre blanc enhanced by fermented asparagus peelings, lovage oil and cauliflower textures. A felicitous feast designed to appeal to today’s tastebuds courtesy of a range of enticing textures.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7316;Bistrot de Pottenbrug;Belgium;Antwerpen;Minderbroedersrui 38, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2223315;4.4043721;80;true;true;French, Belgian;This former café’s wooden bar counter, floral wallpaper, wainscoting and old wood-burning stove set the quintessentially Parisian bistro scene of this characterful town house, providing the perfect foil to a soul-warming culinary score that stars outstanding ingredients. Vincent Greeve enjoys crafting gutsy, big-boned recipes, exemplified by a melt-in-the-mouth house terrine of foie gras with onion preserve or a Rossini steak with a punchy port wine sauce, all of which define the chef’s consummate culinary technique. The Pottenbrug sings a splendid ode to fine produce.;Terrace;[]
7317;Contre-Façon;Belgium;Virelles;Place de Virelles 18, Virelles, 6461, Belgium;50.0625858;4.33354;25;false;true;Modern French;Whether you prefer classic cuisine or something more creative, Loïc Pierard has it covered with his à la carte menu. Whatever you choose, his dishes are built on high-quality (often local) ingredients and precise cooking techniques. Al dente spaghetti in a rich and creamy sea urchin sauce, paired with a spicy langoustine tartare, or barbecued monkfish with crunchy vegetables and an indulgent Choron sauce – the depth of flavour in these dishes is second to none. The charming blend of historical and vintage decor is also sure to impress. Contre Façon is the real deal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7318;Artis;Luxembourg;Hesperange;407 Route de Thionville, Hesperange, 5887, Luxembourg;49.5728384;6.1593999;48;false;true;Modern French;Hao Guo entirely redesigned the interior of Artis with a brand-new colour scheme of soft shades and a cornucopia of contemporary comforts. The food is emblematic of the veteran chef’s experiences in top establishments in Belgium and abroad. While the backbone of his cuisine may be Gallic, he doesn’t hesitate to add international influences. For example, his bouillabaisse reveals the full depth of the salty seafood and is underscored with a rich, yet subtle stock. Chef Guo has an undeniable knack for sauces and his culinary technique is second to none. The extensive menu impresses, as does the spot-on selection of French and Luxembourg wines.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7319;The Twenty Two;Serbia;Belgrade;Bulevar Kralja Aleksandra 69, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8067142;20.4731927;20;false;true;International;Situated on the rooftop of the Metropol Palace Hotel, this restaurant offers fine views of the city and St. Mark’s Church, along with delicious cocktails and gourmet international cuisine. The menu features a good selection of steaks, which we highly recommend, accompanied by a variety of Serbian and international wines. With its soft background music, it’s the perfect place for an aperitif or a post-dinner drink.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7320;Enso;Serbia;Belgrade;Mitropolita Petra 8, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8166101;20.4852764;37;true;true;Creative;The dishes served at this lively, modern and trendy restaurant are based on solid French culinary traditions, skilfully blended with Serbian flavours (the sea bream with Serbian plum gnocchi is both delicious and original) and exotic influences (the miso and mango cake offers a delicious conclusion to your meal). The focus here is on seasonal ingredients cooked and presented with real attention to detail.;Terrace;[]
7321;L'Adresse;Serbia;Belgrade;Svetog Save 10, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.80143;20.46709;28;false;true;European, International;Housed in the Saint Ten boutique hotel not far from the San Sava church in the Vracar district, this contemporary-style restaurant is situated just beyond the modern and welcoming open-plan lounge space. European-influenced cuisine is to the fore here, with a focus on meat (try the Hoisin duck or the Saint Ten beef fillet, the latter the house speciality), although the menu also features a few fish-based specialities, such as tuna fillet and grilled or steamed salmon. Vegetarians will enjoy the kale rolls. The comfortable Lounge Bar is the perfect setting for a relaxing aperitif or post-dinner drink.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7322;Ebisu;Serbia;Belgrade;Studentski trg 9, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.819625;20.4560582;98;false;false;Japanese;As soon as you exit the elevator on the seventh floor of the Square Nine hotel, you immediately step into this intimate and elegant restaurant (named after the Japanese goddess of Fortune) where you can choose to sit on one of the four bar stools or on the terrace boasting fine views of the city centre. The menu features Japanese cuisine, including sushi, sashimi, maki (the tuna maki with jalapeno pepper is particularly delicious), tempura (soft-shell crab served with wasabi mayonnaise and pickled ginger), teppanyaki, at least one ramen, and much more besides. The desserts, on the other hand, are modern European in style. The adjacent bar also offers a menu of “saketini”-based cocktails.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7323;Klub Književnika by Branko Kisic;Serbia;Belgrade;Francuska 7, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8176991;20.4620499;67;true;true;Balkan, Traditional Cuisine;The young chef at this long-established restaurant popular with locals and tourists alike has been at the helm since 2019. Here, guests can choose to eat in a winter garden or in the dining room, where there’s often live music during the colder months. The menu features classic favourites, such as the Krempita dessert which has been served here since the restaurant opened in 1946, and traditional Serbian specialties (there’s a 25-minute wait for the savoury Gibanica dish), with the occasional interesting, personalised touch and a focus on careful presentation. Since its opening at the end of the Second World War, the restaurant has served as a gathering spot for writers, journalists, and politicians. It continues to host cultural events, including exhibitions and concerts. Careful attention is also paid to sustainable practices such as reducing food waste.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7324;Na Ćošku;Serbia;Belgrade;Beogradska 37, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8055525;20.469572;90;true;false;Balkan, International;Situated to the east of the city just outside the historic centre, this restaurant boasts an intimate ambience that comes as a surprise when compared to its exterior. The dining room has the feel of a French bistro, with small tables, background music (often French), and a few cubby-holes that are perfect for couples. The cuisine has solid roots in Balkan tradition, featuring traditional soups and stews, such as lamb in white wine served with mashed potato and seasonal vegetables, various fresh pastas and vegetarian options such as vegan curry with chickpeas, sweet potatoes and green beans.;;[]
7325;Mezestoran Dvorište;Serbia;Belgrade;Svetogorska 46, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8126847;20.4695405;17;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Both the bright decor and colourful tableware at this restaurant demonstrate the light, happy spirit of the Mediterranean, as does the array of tempting dishes on the menu, including chickpea fritters, tzatziki, different kinds of olives, typical “Dokos” from Crete (imaginatively flavoured croutons), as well as chicken and pork gyros. This is a pleasant, informal setting in which to enjoy traditional Greek cuisine, with a cool, relaxed outdoor space in a shady courtyard that adds to its appeal, making it very popular with locals.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7326;Magellan;Serbia;Belgrade;Jurija Gagarina 14ž, Belgrade, 11070, Serbia;44.8052314;20.4091731;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in Novi Beograd, the modern part of the capital, boasts a dining room dominated by a beautiful aquarium. Here, the new local chef, who has plenty of experience behind him, is ably assisted by a professional and attentive front-of-house team. Both the chef’s tasting menu and the extensive à la carte showcase original dishes with a hint of Italian inspiration, including fresh pasta dishes (fish and meat). We particularly enjoyed the excellent sea bass in a herb crust served with zabaglione and blanched fennel, and a highly memorable dessert (“Autumn”) inspired by the season with a mix of textures and just the right amount of sweetness.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list;[]
7327;Bela Reka;Serbia;Belgrade;Tošin Bunar 179, Belgrade, 11070, Serbia;44.8138629;20.3929826;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Inspired by traditional Serbian cuisine, this restaurant proudly showcases local and regional ingredients, many of which (such as their goat’s cheese and hams) are produced on their own farm in the Homolje mountains. In addition to the à la carte, there are two tasting menus based on meat and fish served with seasonal accompaniments sourced from all over Serbia, as well as from the restaurant’s own farm. Both menus offer a wine-pairing option. A professional yet simple outfit that is impressive in the way that it manages to maintain a high quality of cuisine and service despite the large number of covers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7328;SkyLounge;Serbia;Belgrade;Kralja Milana 35, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.804519;20.4659558;98;true;false;International, Asian and Western;As its name suggests, this elegant, modern restaurant with a decidedly international feel boasts stunning views of the city (especially impressive at sunset) thanks to its location on the eighth floor of the Hilton hotel. The chefs here create a varied menu that combines elements of Mediterranean cuisine with Asian influences, with a whole page dedicated to different types of sushi. They have also added lobster from the North Sea and king crabs to the menu, which can be chosen directly from the fish tank. In addition to the wine list, you’ll also find a good selection of other drinks on offer. The lounge-style ambience adds to the enjoyable experience, creating a warm atmosphere in which guests can enjoy contemporary cuisine together with unforgettable views of Belgrade.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7329;Homa;Serbia;Belgrade;Senjanina Ive 2, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8221788;20.4679392;99;true;true;Creative;It might be located in the historic Dorćol quarter, but Homa has a thoroughly modern look and feel. Take a sit on the leafy terrace during the day or in the intimately lit restaurant at night to enjoy creative cooking with subtle Italian influences where you can choose from two tasting menus or an à la carte featuring a selection of vegetarian, fish and meat dishes. The tables are beautifully set with classic cotton tablecloths, while the pleasant outdoor space is perfect for alfresco dining in summer.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7330;Pinòt;Serbia;Belgrade;Omladinskih Brigada 86ž, West 65, Belgrade, 11070, Serbia;44.8122;20.37615;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary-style bistro is situated in Novi Beograd, a modern business and shopping district across the Sava river from Belgrade’s city centre. The menu features seasonal cuisine which changes throughout the year depending on market availability, including a small number of daily specials announced at your table and a tasting menu accompanied by an appropriate wine pairing  (one of the owners, Vuk Vuletiḉ, is a young, award-winning sommelier).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7331;Salon 1905;Serbia;Belgrade;Karađorđeva 48, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8133311;20.4518661;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Balkan;Situated on the first floor of the 19C Geozavod building, this majestic, aristocratic restaurant boasts modern furnishings that provide a pleasing contrast to the marble, stucco, brass and gold-coloured decor which creates a truly spectacular overall effect. This sumptuous setting is the backdrop for cuisine crafted by two young chefs who prepare strictly seasonal menus that successfully reinterpret classic Serbian dishes. Ask for recommendations from the small yet interesting choice of Serbian wines, which are also available by the glass.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7332;GiG;Serbia;Belgrade;Trešnjinog cveta 1a, Belgrade, 11070, Serbia;44.82407;20.41746;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Despite its slightly hidden location among the hotels and modern high-rise buildings in Novi Beograd, this recently opened restaurant is well worth searching out for its warm welcome, beautiful and elegant contemporary-style decor and personalised, modern cuisine. The latter focuses on ingredients sourced from small-scale producers and the restaurant’s own biodynamic vegetable garden, all of which are showcased on three tasting menus and an extensive à la carte. Although the restaurant is owned by the Imperator winery, the extensive wine list also includes international wines and some rare labels, as well as bottles of various sizes. The excellent service is efficient and professional.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7333;Legat 1903;Serbia;Belgrade;Jasenička 7, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.7880554;20.4986732;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Although the best way to experience the international cuisine prepared by this local chef is probably to opt for his tasting menu, there’s also an extensive à la carte selection including a few vegan dishes. The wine list is as international as the cuisine, with labels from the United States and Argentina featured alongside bottles from major European wine-producing countries.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7334;Gušti mora;Serbia;Belgrade;Ulica Radnička 27, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.7862728;20.415648;33;false;false;Seafood;It’s all about fish from the Adriatic Sea at this well-regarded restaurant just outside the city. It’s a comfy place with a rustic look and a long family tradition which started in the bay of Boka Kotorska and arrived in Belgrade in 2003 to share the same passion for good cooking. Italian-influenced cuisine is to the fore here, including a good selection of first courses.;Air conditioning;[]
7335;The Square;Serbia;Belgrade;Studentski Trg 9, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.8195322;20.4562003;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Just behind the busy Knez Mihaliva shopping street, this restaurant takes its name from the Square Nine hotel – one of the most beautiful hotels in the city – in which it is housed. Situated on the ground floor, the elegant dining room has soft lighting in the evening, while a pleasant outdoor space is perfect for alfresco dining. The contemporary-style cuisine focuses on modern Serbian specialties offered in its à la carte menu. The superb wine list is complemented by one of the city’s best selections of cocktails, served in The Lobby Bar.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7336;Metropolitan;Serbia;Belgrade;Milentija Popovića 5, Belgrade, 11070, Serbia;44.813117;20.4366413;83;false;true;International, Balkan;Although this restaurant within the Regency Hyatt hotel is situated away from the centre, it boasts a convenient location for anyone visiting the area for business and is the perfect choice for a relaxing meal, offering excellent service. The menu features international cuisine alongside various local specialties. The "Metropolitan Specials" include beef cheek cooked over a low heat for 24 hours, although it's also possible to create your own dish featuring something from the grill, a side dish and a sauce. The restaurant places great emphasis on ethically sourced produce, such as free-range eggs, and avoids ingredients like shark's fin and foie gras from force-fed geese. Recycling is also a top priority. Additionally, the wine list has been recently upgraded, enhancing the overall dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7337;Comunale Caffè e Cucina;Serbia;Belgrade;Karađorđeva 2-4, Beton Hala, Belgrade, 11000, Serbia;44.819708;20.4483005;90;false;false;Italian;When the sun shines head for this super riverside spot in the shadow of Belgrade Fortress. It’s one of several whitewashed former customs warehouses with open terraces – but this one is owned by an architect, so inside it’s sleek and stylish. The classic Italian cuisine served here features traditional recipes such as tagliatelle al ragù, bruschetta, tiramisu and a few pizzas. Impressive choice of liqueurs and spirits, in particular gin, and good selection of cocktails and mocktails.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7339;Baron;Qatar;Doha;Unit 46, Mina District, Doha Port, Building 415, Zone 19, Street 200, Doha, Qatar;25.3023233;51.5524401;42;false;false;Middle Eastern, Fusion;Baron is sister to a well-known restaurant of the same name in Beirut and occupies a striking, pastel-pink property in the recently redeveloped Mina District, home of the Old Port. It’s a large place with exposed pipework adding a contemporary feel and an open kitchen that’s very much part of the room. The menu offers a wide choice of what they describe as ‘Mediterranean fusion’, which means the addition of some North African and even Asian influences. Dishes like capellini with crab and shrimp toum are generous in size and ideal for sharing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7341;Morimoto;Qatar;Doha;Mondrian Doha, West Bay Lagoon, Doha, Qatar;25.3773916;51.5238379;38;false;true;Japanese Contemporary, Fusion;From the catwalk entrance to the DJ, from the theatrical cocktails to the uber-contemporary hotel in which it sits, it quickly becomes obvious that this is a beautiful restaurant for beautiful people. The sushi counter is striking and there are booths for those wanting privacy, but for most guests a night out here is more about seeing and being seen. The contemporary Japanese menu offers something for everyone, with wagyu a speciality along with items like king prawns and lamb chops cooked on the robata grill.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7343;La Mar by Gastón Acurio;Qatar;Doha;Street 900, Bldg. No. 25, Zone 61, Al Dafna, Beachfront, InterContinental Doha, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.3497091;51.5314168;20;false;true;Peruvian;Come for the beachfront location, stay for the vibrant Peruvian dishes at this whitewashed restaurant within the grounds of the InterContinental Hotel. Gastón Acurio is a fine ambassador for Peruvian food and all bases are covered here, from ceviches to anticuchos. The colourful, rustic dishes deliver plenty of punchy flavours and are perfect for sharing. As you sit and soak up the lively atmosphere, you’ll be struck by what a fun night out it all is. And the wallet-friendly prices make it even more appealing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7344;Curiosa by Jean-Georges;Qatar;Doha;Four Seasons Hotel, The Corniche, Doha, Qatar;25.3251649;51.5398893;99;false;true;Latin American;The eponymous Jean-Georges is none other than the world-famous Vongerichten, who has brought a sassy Latino vibe to the elegant Four Seasons Hotel. Ask for a table in the bar for the Gulf views, and then sit back and wait for the band to start playing as you enjoy a sparkling selection of Latin and globally influenced dishes. That could mean a classic ceviche, tacos and tortillas, sizzling shrimp or crispy fried chicken. End with the ‘Salted Impossible Flan’ or the vast passion fruit sundae and you’ll be gliding out happy.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7345;Nobu;Qatar;Doha;The Corniche, Doha, Qatar;25.3171622;51.5386888;94;true;true;Japanese;The location is a huge draw at what is the largest branch of this globally recognised restaurant brand. Part of the Four Seasons Hotel, this Nobu sits in a stunning futuristic building surrounded by water, located at the end of a narrow peninsula, and offers impressive views of the Corniche promenade. Choose from a wide range of Japanese dishes, with South American influences adding a lovely twist. An open kitchen, stylish bar and cool music ensure a chic atmosphere accompanies the food.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7347;Dalchini;Qatar;Doha;Diplomatic Street, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.3282294;51.5364329;32;true;false;Indian;With a palette of purple, cyan blue and orange, there’s a bright and colourful feeling to this restaurant situated within the Centara West Bay Hotel. The name is Hindi for cinnamon and the cooking is described as ‘Progressive Indian’, with all regions represented on the menu. Dishes are confidently made and neatly presented, with the chefs delivering an original touch and a well-judged balance of vibrant and subtle spicing.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7348;Coya;Qatar;Doha;W Doha Hotel & Residences, Diplomatic Street, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.3287712;51.5304494;24;false;true;Peruvian;Buzzy, colourful and lively, with a hint of Aztec style, this restaurant has all the ingredients for a fun night out. Take a seat in the moody and intimate split-level dining room, where you can see the chefs working in an open kitchen on a range of Peruvian-inspired dishes designed for sharing. Quality ingredients run throughout and there’s a freshness and vibrancy to the flavours. Engaging, attentive service completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7349;Rivaaj;Qatar;Doha;The St. Regis Doha, Al Gassar Resort, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.350498;51.5282934;56;false;false;Indian;‘Heritage Indian Cuisine’ under the aegis of Surjan Singh, better known as ‘Chef Jolly’, is the order of the day at this elegant and moodily lit restaurant at the St Regis hotel. That means a menu offering an appealing range of dishes, from elevated street food to elegant curries and biryanis. The undecided should consider the ‘Signature Board’ offering a range of meats and seafood from the tandoor, plus salad and chutney. The service is always endearingly sweet-natured, adding to the restaurant’s appeal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7350;Desert Rose Café;Qatar;Doha;Ground Floor, National Museum of Qatar, Museum Park Street, Doha, Qatar;25.2884458;51.5485993;80;true;true;Middle Eastern;Beaming smiles greet you from behind the counter at this easy-going and friendly spot tucked away in the National Museum of Qatar. When it comes to ordering, start off with their arancini or ‘Dynamite shrimps’ then go traditional with keema, khabees and Chef Noof’s madrouba that’s made using a special recipe – and no visit here will be complete without the date cake. A great strawberry mojito or a cup from their vast array of speciality coffees will set you up nicely for your museum visit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
7352;Hakkasan;Qatar;Doha;St Regis Doha, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.28164;51.5243;45;true;true;Chinese;This branch of the global brand sits in the grounds of the St Regis hotel but feels entirely independent of it. The dining room features an impressive back-lit counter and remains a place ‘to be seen’ in the city. The extensive menu features plenty of appealingly presented dishes, including all the signature classics – like their Peking duck and dim sum platters – while the desserts are more than an afterthought. If you're not sure what to order, you can't go far wrong by opting for one of their Signature set menus.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7353;Masala Library;Qatar;Doha;Katara Tower, Fairmont Doha, 6th Street, Marina District, Lusail City, Doha, Qatar;25.3900438;51.5315929;63;false;true;Indian;The Fairmont Doha is a striking property by Lusail Marina and this Indian restaurant occupies a position on its first floor, with full-length windows facing the ever-changing landscape. The plush white surroundings are matched by a well-organised service team, while the kitchen produces colourful and artistically plated dishes – their kulcha is a must for enjoying the excellent dals. There is also a subtle influence from West Bengal so you can expect plenty of fish. Be sure to save room for the bebinca dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
7354;MURU;Qatar;Doha;Waldorf Astoria Doha, West Bay, Doha, Qatar;25.3264295;51.5320109;84;true;true;Contemporary;There’s plenty of panache and no little swagger to this large Mauro Colagreco restaurant on the fifth floor of the Waldorf Astoria. The self-styled ‘elemental cooking’ is centred around fire, water, earth and air, with the four elements also providing the different themes for the interior design – a table somewhere between ‘Fire’ and ‘Water’ is the best spot. The global menu offers everything from ceviches and tiraditos to grilled and wood-fired dishes that provide a fusion of exhilarating flavours.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
7355;Liang;Qatar;Doha;Barahat Msheireb Street, Doha, Qatar;25.2859696;51.5270981;63;false;true;Cantonese;Carefully prepared Cantonese dishes, adapted somewhat to suit local tastes, are the order of the day at this elegant restaurant located at the rear of the Mandarin Oriental Hotel. Other regions of China are also represented on the wide-ranging à la carte, with dishes like Kung Pao tiger prawns and Peking duck likely to appear. The attractive and contemporary dining room features modern screens for a sense of privacy, with a charming service team always on hand if you need any recommendations.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7356;SAWA by Sanad;Qatar;Doha;Mohammed Bin Jassim Street, Msheireb, Doha, Qatar;25.2844155;51.5280154;72;false;false;Middle Eastern;The first floor of a private members’ club in Doha’s rejuvenated downtown plays host to this impressively chic dining room. The menu offers a showcase of contemporary Levantine dishes, many of which are perfect for sharing. The kitchen takes things up a notch in the evening, including some dishes served from the trolley for an extra dash of theatre. You don’t need to be a member to eat here, but you’ll be tempted to join up after you’ve experienced the caring service and delicious food.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7357;Dar Yema;Qatar;Doha;Doha Oasis, Al Khaleej Street, Doha, Qatar;25.2864507;51.5184556;18;false;true;Moroccan;Step into this beautiful and spacious dining room and you’ll be warmly welcomed by the gracious team. North African Maghrebian cuisine is the appeal here, with a particular focus on Morocco. Homemade breads are plentiful and delicious, with highlights of the traditional menu including Moroccan tagines – the chicken tagine with lemon and olives is particularly good – and Algerian boureks. The kitchen puts plenty of heart into the cooking and the team even make their own ice cream to satisfy sweet-toothed diners.;Air conditioning;[]
7359;SMAT;Qatar;Doha;Oriental Pearl, Corniche, Doha, Qatar;25.2899083;51.547782;34;false;true;Middle Eastern;At the southern end of the Corniche sits this wonderfully decorated restaurant that features bold colours and an opulent edge, with comfortable sofa seating and polished tiled flooring adding to its appeal. The authentic Qatari and Gulf State dishes are generous in size, eye-catching in looks and yield refined flavours and textures. You could start your meal with crisp Mzatara Samboussa, then move onto one of the particularly good lamb main courses, before the Donafa Ain Helaitan provides a satisfying conclusion.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
7365;Gymkhana;Qatar;Doha;Katara Hills, Doha LXR Hotels & Resorts, Doha, Qatar;25.3525876;51.5233563;64;false;false;Indian;A franchise of the established – and highly acclaimed – London headquarters, this Indian restaurant is located just inside the Hilton Resort in the Katara Hills area. It’s a striking place that resembles a lodge, with a terrace at the back and a clubby, colonial feel inside. The open kitchen, which adds plenty of animation to the room, takes its inspiration from the menu offered in London which was, in turn, inspired by the clubs of India. Lunch represents good value and the service is polite and welcoming.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7366;atelier HANADA by Morimoto;Japan;Osaka;2F, Yodoyabashi odona, 4-3-1 Kitahama, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0041, Japan;34.691074;135.500344;22;false;true;Chinese;A ‘Chinese food atelier’ whose kitchen produces visually stunning cuisine. The chef uses Chinese techniques to create a wide assortment of dishes. Foie gras pickled in Shaoxing wine with smoked daikon pickles, for example, or the exotic aroma of shrimp in chilli sauce wrapped in lime leaves. Mapo-dofu with pork entrails is served piping hot in a clay pot. Modern confections with a French influence and petit four sweets bring a new sensibility to desserts.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7367;Sokkon Fujimoto;Japan;Kyoto;580-1 Matsumotocho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0982, Japan;35.015307;135.766751;48;false;true;Japanese;Sokkon is a Zen term denoting ‘treasuring the present moment’. By so naming his restaurant, the chef professes his devotion to serving delicious flavours fresh from the kitchen. He devotes himself to the tea ceremony, flower arrangement and calligraphy to hone his aesthetic sense and sensitivity. Annual events in the ancient capital are woven throughout his menu, conveying venerable cultural traditions. Rice is available either seasoned with assorted ingredients or topped, doubling the flavour elements to satisfy stomach and palate. An extensive array of offerings expresses the spirit of graceful service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7368;Nakamitsu;Japan;Kyoto;496-2 Sambongi Gochome, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0872, Japan;35.015149;135.760926;50;true;false;Japanese;The chef is an earnest devotee of everything that makes a restaurant great, thanks to careful study of ingredients, culinary technique and attention to every customer. Recipes are tested over and over to get the flavour just right. Knowing that the taste of dashi soup stock changes over time, the chef patiently rests his stock to draw out the flavour. While known to refer to traditional methods, alternations between new and old are a signature of Nakamitsu’s menus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
7369;Zucchero;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 55-1 Matsuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0831, Japan;35.013591;135.762033;70;true;true;Italian;As a seafood wholesaler, Zucchero offers seafood dishes in abundance and having worked in both markets and kappo, the chef has learned the skills of handling fish. The menu changes daily, with an impressive lineup of seafood in season. Dishes are simple, including fare such as carpaccio, fritters and stewed tomatoes. A point of pride is that dishes arrive piping hot. Oven-baked veggies served in the pot and steaming plates of pasta testify to the chef’s passion for his craft.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7370;Rooots Nakanoshima;Japan;Osaka;6-1-45 Nakanoshima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0005, Japan;34.688607;135.486201;94;true;true;Contemporary;At this sister location to a Hiroshima restaurant, a chef who honed his skills in Italy displays his talents. Ingredients are from around the Kinki region as well as the chef's beloved Hiroshima. Italian fare is the base, overlaid with French influences from the flagship restaurant, resulting in a seamless blend of French and Italian recipes. Potato gnocchi is the signature dish. Its culinary roots, so important that the name is spelled with an extra ‘o’, extend deep into both Hiroshima and Nakanoshima.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7371;Nishitemma Ichigaya;Japan;Osaka;2-10-9 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696403;135.50196;76;false;true;Japanese;Nishitemma Ichigaya upholds the traditions of Osaka while incorporating new influences. Creative inspiration and painstaking attention to detail are the watchwords here. Use of ma-kombu kelp to enliven the broth of soup dishes pays tribute to Semba merchant food culture. Traditional vegetables of Osaka showcase the attractions of that great commercial city. From time to time, French methods are employed as well. The seafood with miso sauce américain is a flavour found only here.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
7373;Kiyamachi Ran;Japan;Kyoto;212-6 Nabeyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8015, Japan;35.004956;135.770682;83;false;false;Sushi;This sushi kappo is run by the third-generation owner-chef, who previously worked at Kitcho, and his mother. From below the ledge, water flows to rinse the fingers, stirring fond memories of Showa-era times. Orders are placed old-style too: patrons choose as they converse with the chef. Among the snacks, a favourite is sashimi of the fatty cut of tuna near the collarbone. Grated daikon is wrapped in fatty tuna to create a clean finish. Pickled nigiri oozes the culture of Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7375;Sushidokoro SHIN;Japan;Osaka;7-12-14 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0041, Japan;34.714024;135.511115;17;false;true;Sushi;The chef set his sights on becoming a sushi chef while still in primary school. His family was in the fishing business, so he admired the work of sushi chefs and began by imitating it at home. Restless curiosity supported him in developing a distinctive approach to the craft. For nigirizushi, he focused on techniques for resting and marinating sushi pieces. With an unerring eye for the nature of each fish type, he chooses red-vinegared or white-vinegared sushi rice depending on the fish. The menu interweaves side dishes and nigiri for variation, heightening guests’ sense of anticipation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7376;Miyagawacho Tensho;Japan;Kyoto;4-300-5 Miyagawasuji, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0801, Japan;34.999902;135.771021;46;false;false;Tempura;An omakase feast of tempura and other delights of Japanese cuisine. Guided by his experience at a restaurant with attached inn, the chef starts the meal with sashimi and soup dishes before proceeding to tempura. To bring out their natural aroma, the pieces are lightly battered and deep-fried in pale soy oil. Perennial favourites such as shrimp and whiting are interspersed with creative items like scallops dressed with caviar. Kakiagedon of an all-in-one shrimp and vegetable tempura blend served atop white rice brings down the curtain.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7380;Tokuo;Japan;Kyoto;151 Tennocho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8013, Japan;35.00129;135.769603;52;false;false;Japanese;To usher in the next generation in kappo culture, Tokuo goes all in on à la carte items. Blanquillo, a staple of Kyoto cuisine, is served year-round: at times flame-grilled, at others deep-fried or as sakamushi (seasoned with sake and salt, then steamed). Duck meat dumplings, a heritage from the chef’s apprenticeship days, are lovingly prepared in homage to his culinary mentor. Rice enveloped in grated yam and bean curd skin has been devised as a treat that goes down easy in the summer months.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7381;Kyomachibori Nakamura;Japan;Osaka;1-17-9 Kyomachibori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0003, Japan;34.687054;135.49339;32;true;false;Tonkatsu;The allure of tonkatsu in prix fixe dining. A wide range of cuts, including tenderloin, shoulder and ham, are served by the slice. Pork is deep-fried in lard at low temperatures, slow cooked in the lingering heat to produce meat overflowing with juiciness. Multiple brands of pork loin are on offer, so you can compare the texture of the meat and how the fat melts in the mouth. The meal ends with either katsudon or minced-pork cutlet curry. There’s more to fried pork than you ever realised.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7384;Costes Downtown;Hungary;Budapest;Vigyázó Ferenc utca 5, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.5010814;19.0485638;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set on the ground floor of the Prestige Hotel, this strikingly decorated restaurant brings nature inside with its living wall and ceiling. Ask for one of the booths or sit at the chef’s table for a view of the kitchen. Set tasting menus offer modern interpretations of Hungarian favourites, with some ambitious flavour combinations and the occasional Asian influence.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7385;Botanica;Hungary;Dánszentmiklós;Hotel Botanica, Nyárfa utca 57, Dánszentmiklós, 2735, Hungary;47.2133318;19.5512953;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Lovely gardens surround this delightful, family-owned country house, which comes with bespoke designer bedrooms and charming service. Start with a drink in one of the comfortable lounges before heading through to the elegant restaurant, where a spot on the terrace is a must in summer. The multi-course menu showcases refined, modern creations in dishes which pay tribute to the locality, as well as the chef’s Swabian roots. Both wine and non-alcoholic drinks pairings are on offer, along with fermented beverages crafted from local fruits and vegetables.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7386;KOLLÁZS;Hungary;Budapest;Széchenyi István Tér 5, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.4999796;19.0478164;47;false;true;French;The Four Seasons Gresham Palace hotel is a beautiful art nouveau building which was constructed in 1906 for the Gresham Life Assurance Company. Set in the heart of Budapest, directly opposite the Széchenyi Chain Bridge, its restaurant makes the perfect place to dine when visiting the city. The relaxed, cosy atmosphere is matched perfectly by a menu of familiar French brasserie classics, with a few Hungarian dishes thrown in. The steak tartare is made at the table, the roast chicken for two is carved in front of you and the rum baba is a hit.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
7387;NOON;Hungary;Balatonfüred;Lua Resort, Anna Sétány 3, Balatonfüred, 8230, Hungary;46.945957;17.8805511;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An exclusive lakeside resort plays host to this elegant restaurant (if you’re not staying the night, then pre-booking is essential in high season). Grab a cocktail in the stylish bar before enjoying a carefully curated selection of contemporary Hungarian dishes which fuse tradition with inventive modern touches. Local wines are a feature, and the smooth service shows the team’s knowledge and care. If the chocolate and cherry dessert is on the menu, be sure to choose it.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7389;Bilanx;Hungary;Budapest;Mérleg utca 10, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.4997063;19.050379;47;true;true;Contemporary;Located in an old townhouse midway between the Széchenyi Chain Bridge and St. Stephen's Basilica, Bilanx takes a fresh, modern approach to dining out. Its interior is sparsely decorated, with varnished wooden chairs set at white-tile-topped tables, while neon light strips create glowing archways above and loud pop music plays. The chef offers a tasting menu which comprises his two loves – Hungarian produce and classical French techniques, so you’ll find dishes like mangalitsa pork with choron sauce and parsley root cream. There’s also an interesting 3 course menu available at lunch.;;[]
7390;Arany Kaviár;Hungary;Budapest;Ostrom utca 19, Budapest, 1015, Hungary;47.5065374;19.0282694;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;French and Russian influences guide the cooking here, with dishes ranging from the simple to the ambitious. Sit in the opulent, richly appointed dining room or the more modern extension which opens out onto the garden to sample the Chef’s Menu – or book the Chef’s Table to sample the more creative World Table Menu instead. Hungarian and Siberian caviar is a speciality, with plenty of options to choose from and two caviar tasting experiences are available to kick off your meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7392;Graefl Major Kétútköz;Hungary;Poroszló;Kétútközi utca, Poroszló, 3388, Hungary;47.671505;20.5940024;78;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;25 acres of gardens and grounds surround this wonderfully restored art nouveau mansion house – and it is here that they grow, raise and rear all of the produce that is served in the dining room. If it’s in season, you will find it on the menu, from an incredible array of fruit and vegetables to game. They cure their own meats, use their own wheat for the bread, and their beer is an artisan brew. You can also stay overnight in this gloriously peaceful spot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
7393;Neked Főztem;Hungary;Zánka;Fő utca 7, Zánka, 8251, Hungary;46.8789221;17.6719056;19;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This inviting roadside pub sits in an elevated spot and is fronted by a pleasant terrace. Inside it’s warm and welcoming with a rustic feel – thanks to a log burner crackling away on colder nights. Its name translates as ‘I cooked for you’. The concise menu lists all things Hungarian and the friendly team are happy to talk you through it and offer suggestions. The gutsy home-cooking has plenty of flavour and can be paired with a selection of local wines.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7394;Alkimista Kulináris Műhely;Hungary;Szeged;Kelemen László utca 2, Szeged, 6720, Hungary;46.2503147;20.1476485;35;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Its name means ‘Culinary Workshop’ but that feels like doing it an injustice, as this is a beautiful, elegant spot. It's hidden away behind locked gates in a city centre courtyard and everyone is greeted at 7pm by the infectiously enthusiastic chef-owner. Seasonal ingredients feature on a highly personalised tasting menu which cleverly blends the old and the new. Flavours are memorable, sauces are a highlight and the chef describes every dish with heartfelt passion. The price also includes a carefully curated selection of drinks featuring many local biodynamic/organic wines.;Air conditioning;[]
7396;Kreinbacher Birtok;Hungary;Somlóvásárhely;Somlóhegy, hrsz. 022/14, PF. 3., Somlóvásárhely, 8481, Hungary;47.1304231;17.3707558;32;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;At the centre of the Somló Hill vineyard – which specialises in sparkling wines – sits a futuristic collection of buildings, and inside one is a bright brasserie with a contemporary-rustic feel. Influences from Asia and the Mediterranean blend with typical Hungarian flavours, and each dish comes with a suggested pairing from their winery. Comfy bedrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7397;Alelí;Hungary;Budapest;Wekerle Sándor utca 3, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.4969823;19.0490479;64;true;true;Italian;Romance is in the air at this elegant, high-ceilinged restaurant inside the newly opened Dorothea Hotel in the heart of Budapest. Start with a classic cocktail in the chic bar, then move on to Italian favourites, from delicious focaccias and salads dressed at the table to freshly made pizzas, pastas and risottos. The spaghetti cacio e pepe is not to be missed, and the tiramisu is large enough to share. Much of the produce is imported from Italy and the authentic flavours shine through. Service is friendly and professional, with the staff keen to recommend both dishes and wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7398;Cut & Barrel;Hungary;Budapest;Pacsirtamező Utca 41, Budapest, 1031, Hungary;47.5364782;19.0404581;45;false;false;Meats and Grills, Latin American;Set away from the city centre in the old Goldberger textile factory, this lovely warehouse conversion comprises a wine shop, an impressive bar, a large dining room with a terrace and a smaller anteroom offering counter dining. The stunning shop comes complete with an incredible selection of wines from around the country – including from the owner’s vineyard (Haraszthy Wines in Etyek) – as well as a Harley Davidson, a Porsche and a Rolls Royce. The food has a strong Latin American base but it’s their own charcuterie and succulent steaks from the Josper grill that lead the way.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7399;SHO TIHANY;Hungary;Tihany;Felsőkopaszhegyi út 35, Tihany, 8237, Hungary;46.9016956;17.8957717;26;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;SHO comes from the owner behind Budapest’s Mák. It sits on a peninsula on the north side of Lake Balaton – an area often referred to as the Hungarian Riviera – and is accessed via a narrow lane. Set within the small Echo Residence hotel, the best spot to dine is out on the terrace, which affords wonderful views across the lake. Classic dishes found in Hungarian inns – or csárda – provide the inspiration for the menu, but the recipes are lightened and refined. The soups, such as petyek – the region's version of the fish based halászlé – are worth a try, as is the floating island with local lavender honey.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7400;LAMAREDA;Hungary;Gyor;Apáca utca 4, Gyor, 9022, Hungary;47.6892637;17.633548;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the pedestrianised streets of the beautiful baroque city of Győr, this long-standing restaurant fits in perfectly thanks to its traditional, low-key elegance. Head past the bistro area at the front to the bright room behind, where they serve a menu which mixes Hungarian, Mediterranean and even some subtle Thai influences. The bright, vibrant dishes come in generous portions, with well-judged flavours – be sure to save room for a comforting dessert such as the gundel or zsabo pancakes. The smart pavement terrace is a hit come summer.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7401;Mák;Hungary;Budapest;Vigyázó Ferenc utca 4, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.5011624;19.0480194;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Rustic charm abounds at this laid-back restaurant, from the décor to the vaulted brick ceiling. Seasonality is key here and Chef János takes time to visit his small, artisan suppliers personally. His travels inform the interesting set menu (go for the longer version), with vegetables treated as reverently as meat and fish, and curing, pickling and ageing all playing their part. Knowledgably prepared, consummately seasoned dishes have a delicate touch and could include grey catfish with buckwheat or duck with celery and pine. The unobtrusive, expertly paced service is spot-on too.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7402;Zip's;Hungary;Miskolc;Arany János tér 1, Miskolc, 3526, Hungary;48.1080247;20.7869245;15;false;true;Meats and Grills;Don’t be fooled by the rather unassuming exterior, as once inside you are transported to a totally different world... a world of beer! Sit in one of the booths and enjoy a premium beer (some of which are brewed on site), while studying the proudly local, meat-driven menu. The homemade sausages are outstanding, as is the Mangalitsa, and there’s a myriad of different steaks – all of which arrive in generous portions. Service is endearing, and comfortable apartments complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7403;Hosszú Tányér;Hungary;Hosszúhetény;Fő utca 162, Hosszúhetény, 7694, Hungary;46.1631511;18.3520565;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Hungarian;This pretty little restaurant sits in an attractive courtyard setting and is keenly run by its hands-on owners and their friendly team. Inside it’s cool and modern, with fresh flowers on the tables, and open fires feature both inside and out on the terrace. The menu is concise but provides plenty of appeal and the modern Hungarian dishes are full of bold, hearty flavours. A short, all-Hungarian wine list completes the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
7405;Textúra;Hungary;Budapest;Sas utca 6, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.500061;19.0521376;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set almost opposite its sister restaurant, Borkonyha Winekitchen, is this stylish, design-led brasserie with a relaxed atmosphere, a living wall of moss and a central wooden ‘tree’. Seasonally led dishes are ambitious and creative, and there are some real gems from Hungary on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7406;Avalon;Hungary;Miskolc;H3519 Miskolctapolca, Iglói utca 15, Miskolc, 3519, Hungary;48.063537;20.7259814;63;false;true;Italian;Expectation builds as you follow the winding road that leads up to the Avalon Resort & SPA hotel in the Bükk Mountains. A village unto itself, it’s a family friendly place – and the restaurant’s menu reflects this. There’s something for everyone here, from pizzas and pastas to Wagyu cooked on the Josper grill, while the wine list offers a great selection to accompany your meal. Sit in the stylish bar beside the open kitchen or head through further into the conservatory.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7407;White Salon;Hungary;Budapest;Erzsébet krt. 9, Budapest, 1073, Hungary;47.498635;19.0704452;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The New York Palace Hotel provides baroque splendour in spades and its New York Café is the most photographed dining space in Budapest. However, above it, on a mezzanine level, hides this lesser-known jewel, where an enthusiastic team deliver refined dishes which take inspiration from the former Austro-Hungarian empire. Rich, hearty flavours are balanced by occasional international notes, which adds a welcome freshness to proceedings. The duck confit is not to be missed and it’s always worth considering the set menus. If you’re lucky, there may even be a string quartet playing.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7408;MoszkvaTéЯ Bisztró;Hungary;Budapest;Monastery Boutique Hotel, Fő utca 30, Budapest, 1011, Hungary;47.5017503;19.0388306;79;true;true;Russian;The younger sibling of Arany Kaviár sits on the ground floor of a characterful hotel that was once a monastery. The cuisine here, too, has a Russian theme, with plenty of favourites such as chicken Kiev and some delicious pelmeni (dumplings). The young team are bright and friendly, and a concise list of Hungarian wines completes the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
7409;Zazie Bistro;Hungary;Budapest;Dombóvári utca 28,  MOL Campus, Budapest, 1117, Hungary;47.4680159;19.0592896;54;false;true;Hungarian;Zazie Bistro sits within the tallest skyscraper in Budapest, the MOL Campus, and offers some great views out over the city. It’s a spacious place that incorporates a large open restaurant, a terrace and even a café. The chef brings with him plenty of experience, which shines through in the well-executed, classically inspired, rustic dishes. These could include chilled fruit soups in the summer, or a top-class schnitzel with deliciously creamy potato salad – with the potatoes supplied by the chef’s brother-in-law. There’s also a great value business lunch on offer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7410;Villa Kabala;Hungary;Szigliget;Kamonkői utca 40, Szigliget, 8264, Hungary;46.7921018;17.4421538;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Hungarian;Perched high up the hillside in the Badacsony region, with far reaching views of Lake Balaton, this period villa was once home to artist István Farkas. Now under the ownership of an ambitious and enthusiastic couple, the team here are establishing it as something of a destination restaurant. Go for the well-balanced tasting menu and paired wines – you won’t get much more local than this, with the cheese, salami, sausages, beers and wines all family made. Book a bedroom with a terrace and look forward to a fantastic breakfast.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7411;IKON;Hungary;Debrecen;Piac utca 23, Debrecen, 4031, Hungary;47.5298813;21.6245748;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Hungarian;Set on a main street in the heart of the city, IKON stands out among the other eateries for its smart look, structured service and confident cooking. The chef spent time working in England and his dishes are an intriguing mix of reworked Hungarian classics and some British influences – go for something from the ‘Traditions Reborn’ section and be sure not to miss dessert. For a more immersive experience, book the chic Kitchen Table.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7412;FELIX Kitchen & Bar;Hungary;Budapest;Ybl Miklós Tér 9, Budapest, 1013, Hungary;47.4938364;19.0436395;74;false;false;Meats and Grills;Felix sits behind the breathtaking neo-renaissance façade of the former Várkert Kiosk, in a building which once pumped water to the Royal Palace. It’s a plush place, with a stunningly restored ceiling and an air-conditioned terrace. The luxurious menu sees caviar sitting alongside signature dishes and grills.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7413;Piac 42;Hungary;Esztergom;Simor János u. 26-32., Esztergom, 2500, Hungary;47.7920784;18.7429876;47;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The more casual sister to Michelin-Starred 42 is a smart, informal bistro set amongst upmarket artisan businesses in the recently opened Esztergom Market. Find a seat in the cosy bistro-cum-bar or on the sun-drenched terrace and choose from a concise menu of fresh, flavour-packed dishes crafted from local produce. Tradition leads the way, with the likes of pork rillettes and pancakes with cottage cheese. Come for breakfast, a leisurely lunch or a lively evening out.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7414;Spago by Wolfgang Puck;Hungary;Budapest;Váci utca 36, Budapest, 1056, Hungary;47.4922949;19.0541719;44;true;false;International;The Matild Palace Hotel – one of a pair of matching belle époque palaces bult by the Archduchess of Austria – is a grand building in a stunning setting beside the Elizabeth Bridge. It’s fitting then, that it’s home to a smart restaurant run by an Austrian Chef. Wolfgang Puck’s fun dining concept brings something a little different to Budapest’s culinary scene, with a selection of appealing, well-executed dishes that draw their inspiration from across the world. From Hungarian buffalo steak tartare and Austrian wiener schnitzel to scallop pad thai and some delicious pastas, everything is here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7416;Umo;Hungary;Budapest;Ponty utca 1, Budapest, 1011, Hungary;47.5016489;19.0388197;42;false;true;International, South American;Housed within a boutique hotel, Umo comprises two parts: a contemporary brasserie in the atrium, and an enclosed courtyard towards the back of the building. The latter was formerly a monastery and is a wonderful place to sit – it even comes complete with an open kitchen where dishes are cooked over flames and smoke. Menus showcase the best of Latin American flavours, with everything from a baja shrimp cocktail and delicious tacos – the mangalitsa ones are the best – to a selection of fire-cooked meats. A fine range of gins is on offer alongside the in-depth wine list.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7417;Zelna Borbisztró;Hungary;Balatonfüred;Zákonyi Ferenc utca 3-5, Balatonfüred, 8230, Hungary;46.9532721;17.8913376;42;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A smart, modern wine bar in the livelier part of this seasonal town, Zelna is named after the wine company whose biodynamic wines it serves – and also offers for purchase. This is a place to kick back and relax, and the small menu mixes light bites with more substantial Hungarian dishes so you can tailor-make your own experience – the beef cheeks are a hit and be sure to save room for the golden walnut dumplings for dessert! Every table is located on the large terrace, which stays open until 2am.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7419;Csopaki Resti by Laurel;Hungary;Csopak;Kossuth utca 1, Csopak, 8229, Hungary;46.9745798;17.9311537;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine;There’s no denying that a meal at Csopaki Resti by Laurel provides something a little different: this tiny restaurant comprises just 10 seats and sits within the old village railway station. Little sister to Laurel in Budapest, its multi-course set menu follows the same ethos, with dishes taking on a modern edge while still keeping traditional Hungarian flavours to the fore. Because of its compact size, every diner can watch the chefs preparing the dishes in the on-view kitchen, but the four counter seats are undeniably the best place to be. Wherever you sit, the chefs will serve you personally.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7420;Szaletly;Hungary;Budapest;Stefánia Utca 93, Budapest, 1146, Hungary;47.5085166;19.0948609;83;false;false;Hungarian;Whether you’re after a drink, a snack or a full meal, this neighbourhood spot is for you if you’re after a laid-back vibe. It’s a spacious place, with a large terrace-cum-garden to boot, but the efficient team cope well with the numbers. Dishes offer a diverse range of influences, but there’s always a Hungarian vein running through their hearts. The tasting menus with matching wines are worth ordering, the gödöllő chicken breast is delicious and, for dessert, it has to be the esterházy. You can even buy a post-dessert ice cream for the way home.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7422;füge;Hungary;Tihany;Tihany Yacht Club, Rév utca 7, Tihany, 8237, Hungary;46.8894587;17.8836597;86;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If you’re visiting in season, make for this bright lakeside restaurant with a chilled vibe. Many of the yachts in the nearby private mooring belong to regular guests, who have crossed Lake Balaton to enjoy either modern Asian-inspired dishes, or pizzas fresh from the oven located on the attractive terrace. Attentive service and bedrooms – some with balconies and water views – make this a great all-round package.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7423;Füge;Hungary;Biatorbágy;Szabadság út 19, Biatorbágy, 2051, Hungary;47.4665769;18.8110822;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Most people would simply mourn the loss if their favourite village restaurant closed. Not Edina Szalai-Hencz and her partner Csaba. Instead, they bought it, changed its name to ‘Fig’ – their favourite fruit – and gave it a smart, modern makeover. The large conservatory and small garden – where, pleasingly, you’ll find some potted figs – are the best places to sit. Colourful cooking focuses on traditional Hungarian flavours that are blended with restrained creativity, and herbs and flowers are a feature, adding a freshness to the rich, full flavours.;Air conditioning,Garden or park;[]
7424;Víg Molnár Csárda;Hungary;Csopak;Kőkorsó utca 1, Csopak, 8229, Hungary;46.9732282;17.9289899;98;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This traditional-looking tavern comes with plenty of character and is certainly a hit with the locals. There’s a rustic, slightly Mediterranean feel to the décor, which works well with its location near the lake, but the best place to sit is on the large terrace beside the working water wheel. Fairly priced, hearty Hungarian classics are the order of the day, with the meat-stuffed pancakes a speciality. Children have their own menu too, and you’ll be well looked after by the friendly owners and their team. It’s a place for every occasion, so can get very busy at peak times.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7425;Tati;Hungary;Budapest;Dohány utca 58-62, Budapest, 1076, Hungary;47.4981673;19.0691375;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The owners of this restaurant in the up-and-coming District 7 also have a farm on the outskirts of the city where they grow their own fruit and veg. Menus comprise a mix of meat, fish and plant-based creations, with a natural feel to both the appearance and flavour of the dishes. The use of traditional Hungarian recipes results in hearty, wholesome cooking on the dinner menu, while lunch takes on more of a 'brunch' style. The accompanying natural, bio and organic wines come from vineyards in close proximity to the city.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7427;Horgonyzó Kisvendéglő;Hungary;Tiszalök;Tiszavirág utca 13, Tiszalök, 4450, Hungary;48.0213704;21.3181276;60;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Simplicity leads the way at this endearing restaurant set just a short stroll from the River Tisza. The room has an unfussy lodge style and there’s plenty of outdoor space courtesy of both a front and rear terrace. Cooking is fresh and well-executed, and offers something for everyone, from Hungarian classics to pizzas, burgers and street food. The wood-fired oven plays a key role, and everything is prepared with love and care.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7428;A Konyhám Stúdió 365;Hungary;Fonyód;Ady Endre utca 5, Fonyód, 8640, Hungary;46.7492818;17.5570573;60;true;false;Contemporary;Take the lift to the 3rd floor of the Balaton Üzletház shopping mall and you’ll find this bright restaurant with a smart interior and a partial view over the lake. Chef and well-known personality, Gabriella Szikra – kitted out in her trademark cap – has a genuine desire to please, and her modern Hungarian dishes come with bold flavours and arty presentation. Be sure to go for the excellent local wine pairings.;Air conditioning;[]
7429;VIRTU;Hungary;Budapest;MOL Campus, Dombóvári Utca 28, Budapest, 1117, Hungary;47.4682298;19.059197;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located on the 28th floor of the tallest building in Budapest, the MOL Campus, VIRTU affords stunning views out over this historic city and the River Danube. Start with cocktails in the smart bar, then head through to the spacious, two-roomed restaurant. The menu offers something for everyone, with a pleasing mix of modern and classical dishes. If it’s available, the catfish with river prawns is delicious, as is the mangalitsa chop with fresh pickles. A fine selection of wines and professional service from a caring team complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7430;Teyföl;Hungary;Szentendre;Városház tér 2, Szentendre, 2000, Hungary;47.6677851;19.0751818;65;false;true;Hungarian;Owners Brigi and Bence have created what they feel is their perfect restaurant in Teyföl, whose name translates as ‘sour cream’ – an ingredient used frequently in Hungarian cuisine. The restaurant sits within a characterful period building on a narrow cobbled street in the Old Town, and its bright, modern bistro-style interior provides a complete contrast. Multiple flavours, textures and colours come together in classically based dishes with a well-restrained level of creativity, such as confit chicken pancakes or a gypsy-style roast.;Terrace;[]
7431;Stand25 Bisztró;Hungary;Budapest;Atilla útca 10, Budapest, 1013, Hungary;47.4978729;19.032758;50;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;There’s always a contented buzz to this neighbourhood bistro on the Buda side of the Danube. It’s owned by the same team as Stand, so their ethos around quality is the same, and you’ll be looked after by a slick team. Cooking focuses on Hungarian classics with a Mediterranean edge and, while dishes are hearty with robust flavours, they also have a refined edge.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7432;Kővirág;Hungary;Köveskál;Fő útca 9/A, Köveskál, 8274, Hungary;46.8819982;17.6082191;51;true;false;Hungarian;Located in a lovely little village near Lake Balaton, this delightful thatched farmhouse, with its white-gravelled courtyard, has something of a Mediterranean feel. The interior sports a vintage-chic look, and there’s a pretty candlelit terrace for warmer days. Colourful dishes come with a Hungarian heart and modern overtones, and the cottage cheese fried dumplings with seasonal jam are something of a speciality. Service is incredibly welcoming, and the wines are carefully sourced from the local area. If you’re touring the lake and the wine region, the bedrooms here make an ideal base.;Car park,Terrace;[]
7433;Onyx Mühely;Hungary;Budapest;Vörösmarty tér 7-8, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.497359;19.0506074;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The rebirth of Onyx is underway… starting with Onxy Mühely, a 16-seater test kitchen which offers dishes that will go on to form the core of the menu at the new Onyx. All guests arrive at the same time for drinks and nibbles, before being shown through to an elegant ‘workshop’ with a beautiful open kitchen and a glass-enclosed, galleried library. Diners are also invited to be critics and are encouraged to talk to the chefs and leave written feedback on the menu. Sustainability is a focus of the refined dishes, and the whole experience is interactive and engaging.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7435;Rutin;Hungary;Budaörs;Budapesti utca 51, Budaörs, 2040, Hungary;47.4619385;18.9700089;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in an affluent city suburb, this chic bistro comes with an appealing buzz and smiles all round. The owner cooks but also keeps a watchful eye over proceedings from his open kitchen near the entrance. Concise menus – supplemented by a few specials – come with creative modern touches and vibrant flavours. Their jazz evenings are very popular.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7436;Hoppá! Bistro;Hungary;Budapest;Október 6. utca 15, Budapest, 1051, Hungary;47.5015443;19.0509811;93;true;true;Contemporary;This contemporary eatery stands out amongst the myriad choices on vibrant Október Street, both for its smooth service and its modern, well-presented cooking – and it's certainly a popular spot. Large blackboards announce the daily specials, which see traditional Hungarian recipes brought up-to-date, and the excellent value lunch menu is always a hit. Local beers and wines complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7438;Casa Dani;USA;New York;448 W. 33rd St., New York, 10001, USA;40.7534938;-73.9987615;32;true;false;Spanish, Seafood;There is nothing homey about Chef Dani Garcia’s sprawling new casa, located in the sparkling Citizens food hall in Manhattan West. A buzzy lounge opens into a packed two-story dining room that is full-on glamour with ceilings that reach for the sky, a glassed-in open kitchen, beautiful fabric and texture at every corner and a professional clientele that likes to eat well and look good doing it. Big groups like to swing for the pricey paella, but we suggest building a meal around a wide range of small dishes, starting with any one of the fantastic preparations of tuna. Shrimp tucked with a basil leaf and fried until perfectly crispy are even better with smoky aioli, but don't miss a wedge of still-warm, burnt Basque cheesecake, served tableside.;Air conditioning;[]
7439;Vestry;USA;New York;246 Spring St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7256137;-74.0055581;20;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Tucked inside The Dominick Hotel, Vestry is an ideal destination for guests craving a quiet evening in an intimate setting. The kitchen is steered by Australian-born Chef Shaun Hergatt, whose admiration for Japanese culinary technique and elements is clear and woven into the seasonal vegetable- and seafood-based menu. Roasted Faroe Island salmon atop a bed of herbed fregola and finished with an aerated beurre blanc sauce tempts with shatteringly crisp skin. However, dessert showcases a creative, clever touch—think cheesecake mimicking a wedge of Swiss cheese sided by an apple ginger compote with a mouse tail and ears.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7440;Mesiba;USA;Brooklyn;353 Bedford Ave., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.7117939;-73.9631361;28;true;true;Middle Eastern, Regional Cuisine;Mesiba certainly lives up to its name. This Levantine restaurant tucked at the base of the hip Moxy Williamsburg hotel, means “party” in Hebrew, and indeed its lively ambience alone is a draw. However, Chef Eli Buliskeria's food is equally captivating. From baba ganoush to ktzitzot (red snapper skewers) with Palestinian za'atar to khinkali, he honors this melting pot-style cuisine in a sleek setting reminiscent of Tel Aviv's Bauhaus-inspired architecture. Nibble on nishnushim (hamutzim-pickled vegetables) before tucking in to a crispy striped bass served whole and sided by carrot zhoug, tabila sauce and lettuce leaves. A creamy "risotto" made with freekeh delivers great flavors thanks to head-on prawns and a tangy-tart yogurt. Finish with a thick slice of Basque cheesecake.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7441;Kebab aur Sharab;USA;New York;247 W. 72nd St., New York, 10023, USA;40.7793502;-73.9830232;24;false;false;Indian, Regional Cuisine;There may be plenty of outside seating, but indoors at Kebab aur Sharab, the look is lavish. From the deep, rich colors and a sea-blue tiled wall to the intricate woodwork and wicker seating, this Upper West Side spot is especially transporting.  A versatile menu offers snacks, small plates and main courses, all designed for sharing (though you may want to keep them to yourself). Do as the name suggests and order a kebab—the baby goat one is exceptional. Finely minced goat is formed around a skewer held together by thread, which is then unspooled tableside to deliver the juicy meat with just a whisper of spices and a hint of smokiness. Kerala fish curry is exquisitely spicy and does the Southern Indian classic proud.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7445;Cómodo;USA;New York;23 Lexington Ave., New York, 10010, USA;40.7396;-73.984467;43;false;true;Latin American, Regional Cuisine;Felipe Donnelly and Chef/co-owner Tamy Rofe have resurrected their much-loved SoHo spot, now at the Freehand Hotel. This iteration is wooing patrons with its warm interior and tempting dishes blending Latin American influences from Brazil to Mexico.Kick things off with a zesty-delicious trout ceviche tostada, vibrant thanks to leche de tigre marinade. Next, braised leeks in beurre blanc with guajillo chile oil are meltingly tender, while ajiaco soup is a comforting bowl of Colombian potato sided by shredded chicken, capers, fresh avocado chunks, and a habanero sauce. Bone-in achiote chicken over green Calasparra rice with brown butter mustard is lush, creamy and packed with flavor.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7446;Nudibranch;USA;New York;125 First Ave., New York, 10003, USA;40.727431;-73.9855867;22;false;true;Contemporary, Asian;Chefs Matthew Lee and Jeff Kim are behind the East Village's well-loved Nudibranch. The food is contemporary with strong Asian influences along with a few Spanish elements making an appearance. Portions lean dainty, but nobody seems to care, as they're all nibbling off each other's plates, family style.Begin with fried frog legs finished with bright galangal and lemongrass, then anchor the meal with a golden and crisp dry-aged branzino with Korean sweet potato and beurre blanc and a side of spicy cucumber kimchi. The signature mushroom dish has been on the menu since day one. The rich and creamy masala chai tres leches cake is a delightful way to end your meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7447;Rosella;USA;New York;137 Avenue A, New York, 10009, USA;40.7271207;-73.9828623;24;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;This high dining, hyper-sustainable operation is proudly unbound by tradition. The space is quaint and deviates from the blonde-wood minimalism so prevalent these days. Instead, find hues of cerulean blue and a counter made from a tree. The à la carte menu showcases this restaurant's sourcing philosophy. In terms of cuisine, it's pure contemporary elegance, as seen in shrimp nigiri that's first cured, then seared until it curls into the rice and finished with shrimp head-chili oil. End with amazake, presented as a porridge with white peach-nectarine jam. The impressive wine list sources from the North Fork and West Coast.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7448;Ci Siamo;USA;New York;440 W. 33rd St., Ste. 100, New York, 10001, USA;40.75351;-73.99865;28;false;true;Italian;Efficient, busy from the minute doors open and effortlessly likable, this Italian eatery hiding deep inside the Manhattan West development is everything we’ve come to expect—and enjoy—from restaurateur Danny Meyer. The space features a handsome bar, open kitchen, large windows and ample tilework—all of which will feel familiar to those acquainted with the Union Square Hospitality Group.Chef Hillary Sterling's food is equally inviting. The caramelized onion torta is enough to warrant a return, with melting onions packed into a delicate crust, buried under two kinds of pecorino and finished in the wood-burning oven. Generously rich pastas and hearty proteins are designed for sharing. A simple but arresting lemon torta with mascarpone and olive oil closes out the meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7449;Lord's;USA;New York;506 Laguardia Pl., New York, 10012, USA;40.727706;-73.9993702;48;true;true;English, Contemporary;It feels straight out of London at this meat-centric restaurant with a nose to tail ethos from Chef Ed Szymanski and Patricia Howard, the partners behind smash hit, Dame. It's ever so charming, with cozy nooks and banquettes, and is always packed, but the bar maintains space for walk ins. Come on a cold day for hearty English classics with a touch of creativity (think curried lamb scotch egg). Like most of the dishes, duck-stuffed cabbage with mashed potatoes could feed an army, so order shared plates-style to sample without becoming stuffed. The apple & calvados trifle closes things out with just the right note of sweetness.;Air conditioning;[]
7450;Kanyakumari;USA;New York;20 E. 17th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.737342;-73.9909554;81;false;false;Indian, Regional Cuisine;Compact but contemporary with a buzzy vibe, this restaurant is named for the city at the southernmost tip of India, and appropriately, spotlights the regional fare of south India with a focus on seafood. The cooking is as bold as you’d expect, with a depth of flavor. This kitchen puts their spin on the tried-and-true. Case in point? Mussels Koliwada. It's a dish traditionally made with fish, but here, mussels coated in a spiced, red-tinted rice flour batter are fried, then served alongside a chili dipping sauce. If the server recommends the slow-cooked Black Gold beef, order it. It's impossibly tender beef short rib dressed with Madras onion rings, crispy curry leaves, and tiny green chilies. A nuanced fish curry is complemented by the ghee rice.;Air conditioning;[]
7451;Theodora;USA;Brooklyn;7 Greene Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.685922;-73.9731053;47;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Chef/owner Tomer Blechman is behind this Fort Greene restaurant that seems to have a constant thrum of activity. The scent of wood smoke perfumes the air at this inviting restaurant where the menu leans Mediterranean and there is a clear focus on dry-aged fish and open-fire cooking. Begin with the house-made, wood-fired pita sided by monkfish liver 'nduja hummus for a twist on the traditional opener, then savor a salad of sliced heirloom and cherry tomatoes topped with grilled sardines and a tomato gelée. Seafood cooked over the fire is the restaurant's signature, and the dry-aged black cod with miso beurre blanc doesn't miss a beat, especially with chopped Romano beans on top and grilled fairytale eggplant and grilled endive on the side.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7452;Raf's;USA;New York;290 Elizabeth St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7246102;-73.9933283;53;true;true;European;Raf's has all the charm of an old world bistro, albeit with a modern polish. Chef Mary Attea and Pastry Chef Camari Mick have partnered with Jennifer and Nicole Vitagliano to create a broad European menu with strong Italian and French influences. From escargot and house-made breads (a must-order) to pastas like mafaldine tossed with shredded rabbit and favas in a bright lemon pesto, everything is made with care. There are plenty of shareable dishes (think Sicilian cast iron skillet pizza), and while they aren't reinventing the wheel, they are turning out well-prepared meals with subtlety and style. Dessert is non-negotiable, especially the simple-but-superb white chocolate budino.Didn't plan ahead and get a reservation? Pick your perch at the bar instead.;Air conditioning;[]
7453;Augustine’s Salumeria;USA;Mamaroneck;213 Halstead Ave., Mamaroneck, 10543, USA;40.953762;-73.7357858;93;false;false;Contemporary, Italian;Chef and co-owner Marc Taxiera takes full advantage of the proximity to Westchester's top farmers and fish at Augustine's Salumeria, a full-fledged restaurant with a part-time counter proffering charcuterie and cheese. The space is laidback and modern, with a comfortable "neighborhood" vibe. There's plenty on this Italian-leaning locavore menu but the kitchen also offers a handful of nightly specials that will make choosing one oh-so-difficult. Mafalda never misses with its slow-stewed, grass-fed Longhorn beef resting over pasta topped with a goat milk ricotta. Sourced locally, the pork chop, paired with a pecan and onion ash, is wonderfully moist and grilled to perfection. End with something light and sweet like the cannoli made from freshly pressed pizzelle.;Air conditioning;[]
7454;Osteria Padre Pio;USA;Mamaroneck;501 Halstead Ave., Mamaroneck, 10543, USA;40.95606;-73.73251;60;false;false;Italian, Campanian;Naming a restaurant after a saintly miracle worker is a bold move but there's a reason why locals keep coming back. Chef Andrea Ingenito is  onto something, and is supremely dedicated to offering a true Campanian experience to guests. The interior is inviting and charming, matched only by the warm hospitality and carefully crafted dishes. Nearly everything is made from scratch here, where each table is given a beautiful wooden board loaded with room-temperature caponatina and plenty of house-made focaccia. It's tempting, but but don't fill up, and don't skip the specials. From the baked corvina to the silky pappardelle, come hungry to enjoy hearty portions, then order a house-made limoncello to accompany your dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7455;Gus's Chop House;USA;Brooklyn;215 Union St., Brooklyn, 11231, USA;40.6834596;-73.9993934;96;false;false;Steakhouse;This buzzy chophouse has quickly found footing and favor in Carroll Gardens. Far from the stuffiness of typical steakhouses, the candlelit dining room has its charms, and neighbors are sure to crowd around the bar and order the off-menu burger. As for on-menu, the kitchen showcases surprising creativity in winners like “leek a la wedge” or hash brown with smoked trout roe. Pork porterhouse is the main attraction, though all proteins from lamb loin to the NY strip are finished with a compelling brown butter sauce. Sides like sweet potato pave are equally thoughtful. All the while, wine enthusiasts will find plenty to dig into on this finely curated list stacked with star producers mostly from France.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7456;Nura;USA;Brooklyn;46 Norman Ave., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.7246919;-73.9534864;43;true;false;Fusion;Located on a windswept, wide artery in Greenpoint with retrofitted warehouses and new gleaming residential towers, this former auto-body shop really revs its stuff.Chef Tajeh Porter's menu is deliciously informed by co-owner Michelle Lobo-Hawley's Indian heritage. From coriander garlic naan to maple sweet crumbly corn bread, the fresh bread basket is a marvel, but when coupled with spiced carrot and white bean spread or hummus flavored with smoky blistered poblano, it's a meal unto itself. Have some discipline, though, since you'll want some bread to sop up the electrifying sweet-smoky mezcal- and Urfa pepper-infused sauce accompanying the prawns. Finish with roasted sunchoke ice cream with candied cocoa nibs, crushed cookie and a flourish of flamed black cardamom.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7457;R40;USA;Queens;47-16 Vernon Blvd., Queens, 11101, USA;40.7450882;-73.953442;52;false;true;Argentinian;As the saying goes, the nose knows. These are words to live by at this vibrant Argentinian parilla. With big meats sizzling over a roaring grill, a subtle smoke wafts through the long dining room, built out of sleek wood, exposed brick and dangling greenery. When the nights are cool, the party is further back out on the well-tended patio. Everything here is meant to be shared, starting with the hearty empanadas that come stuffed with everything from filet mignon and raisins to pork shoulder and potatoes. Housemade pastas and chicken milanesa are always tempting, but first timers should dig into favorites like skirt steak with chimichurri. Only serious appetites should order the combination platter featuring steak, ribs, chorizo and sweetbreads.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7459;O Mandarin Chinese;USA;Hartsdale;361 N. Central Ave., Hartsdale, 10530, USA;41.0291868;-73.7900816;37;false;true;Chinese, Sichuan;Its stark exterior does not hint at the warm vibe or enticing bites, bound to tempt even the most stoic eater here. One glance around this buzzy and well-appointed dining room proves that it is cherished by multi-generational groups. The setting paints an intriguing picture, thanks to sleek, intricately carved wooden panels, tables, chairs and vivid artwork. Semi-private booths are ingeniously lit, and most popular.The menu boasts a litany of delightful appetizers, like tender soup dumplings. Classics—like garlic-pepper shrimp with leeks and celery—are prepared with exacting technique and deliver wonderful flavor. Available as half or whole (depending on your party's size), slow-cooked Beijing duck is a sensory thrill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7461;MayRee;USA;New York;58 E. 1st St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7236546;-73.9890955;28;false;true;Thai, Regional Cuisine;Chef/Owner Orawan Sawangphol tells us a story of southern Thai cooking at Mayree, named for a character from the Thai folktale, Twelve Sisters. The space is cozy and charming, as is the compact menu. Spice levels are far from timid, and all of the dishes, including Isan specialties, showcase great personality. Park mor plates rice crepe dumplings with a sweet chopped peanut filling topped with coconut milk and fried garlic. Kua kling is a dry, southern-style roasted curry made with ground pork that really brings the heat and displays incredible flavors. After a fiery meal, refresh your palate with coconut ice cream served in a coconut shell. Sek Saraboon runs the serious cocktail program, while all of the creative sips are named for Mayree's sisters.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7462;Chambers;USA;New York;94 Chambers St., New York, 10007, USA;40.7146945;-74.0075266;23;true;true;Contemporary;Under a new name, wine geeks far and wide can rejoice at the rebirth and return of the late Racines. In a space that feels cool without feeling cold, Master Sommelier Pascaline Lepeltier has built a wine program with adventure, back vintages and surprising affordability in mind. She moves around the room showing equal hospitality to industry insiders and wide-eyed enthusiasts alike. Meanwhile, the kitchen knows its boundaries, delivering seasonal, friendly dishes that never threaten to overpower what’s in the glass. Highlights include lamb with chickpeas and mint and, for dessert, a delicate mascarpone mille-feuille made out of shatteringly thin sheets of phyllo. For a nightcap, don’t miss the mind-boggling selection of chartreuse.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7463;Cha Kee;USA;New York;43 Mott St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7153146;-73.9987634;78;false;false;Asian;Chef Akiko Thurnaeur is the brains behind this family-style beauty, complete with an ultra-modern décor and slightly eclectic vibe. Some flock to the bar up front, while hungry patrons head for the tables in the back to indulge in seriously comforting fare. A banquette on the left and long tables down the center make it a haven among groups.The open kitchen set aglow by gilded light fixtures turns out a menu that displays a clever blend of the flavors and techniques of both Japanese and Chinese cuisines. Naturally what follows is an array of of memorable plates, like soy-braised romaine finished with pumpkin seeds or dan dan noodles enriched by a poached egg.Much to the delight of the teetotaler, mocktails are given ample emphasis.;Air conditioning;[]
7464;Le Jardinier New York;USA;New York;610 Lexington Ave., New York, 10022, USA;40.7581136;-73.9714345;25;true;true;French, Contemporary;Chef Alain Verzeroli's light-filled space is a verdant vision—with olive-green velvet furnishings, green-veined marble flooring, and lush plants at every turn. It’s the perfect effect for the chef's produce-driven menu, where seasonal vegetables, fruits, and herbs play a prominent role—with carefully sourced meats and sustainable fish as the supporting cast. Dishes have included the likes of grilled Spanish octopus, plated with green olives, romesco, and green beans, or Ora King salmon enhanced with smoked chili butter and pak choi. End with a Valrhona chocolate crémeux with a salted caramel sabayon or the delightful lemon tart with tarragon ice cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7467;Hirohisa;USA;New York;73 Thompson St., New York, 10012, USA;40.72452;-74.003006;26;false;true;Japanese, Classic Cuisine;There’s nothing like a discreet entrance to raise expectations—and Hirohisa is nicely concealed on Thompson Street. When you do find it, you enter into a stylish and beautifully understated room. The menu is structured as a kaiseki experience. Two things will quickly become clear: the ingredients are exceptional, and the team's technical skills are considerable. This is food that is as rewarding to eat as it is restorative. Standouts include mushroom zosui, a comforting bowl with a base of rice topped with a multitude of earthy mushrooms. The meal concludes with a satisfying pot of rice enhanced with snow crab, ikura, and crab roe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7468;Café Carmellini;USA;New York;250 Fifth Ave., New York, 10001, USA;40.7450512;-73.9875897;38;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, American;Andrew Carmellini's return to fine dining is housed in the Fifth Avenue Hotel, a former Gilded Age gem now recast as an elegant NoMad stomping ground. The dining room bears a sumptuous throwback ambience with wood plank flooring, curved sapphire-blue velvet booths and caramel leather seating. The open kitchen turns out dishes that whiff of the Mediterranean, as in the crab mille-feuille, a neatly arranged tower of delicate wafers and sweet crabmeat in a golden-yellow Meyer lemon sauce. Scallops Cardoz is a heartwarming composition dedicated to the late Chef Floyd Cardoz and features beautifully seared bivalves with a turmeric-tinted and warmly spiced coconut milk sauce. The squab en croûte pairs rich and rosy breast meat and seared foie gras in a thin layer of pastry.;;[]
7469;Foxface Natural;USA;New York;189 Avenue A, New York, 10009, USA;40.7290222;-73.9814153;21;true;true;Creative;Squid from Point Judith cut into thin noodles, set in a green aguachile, and topped with crispy pork ears? Tartare but made from the loin of a kangaroo and accompanied with coriander-carrot puree and Sardinian flatbread? There are few rules at this easygoing East Village standout, which has no trouble taking risks. The eclectic menu sources local, watches the seasons carefully, and does what it pleases. Case in point: A recent dessert featuring a smooth white asparagus gelato with shards of pink peppercorn meringue and grilled strawberries. Aim to sit at the long bar that anchors the narrow room. It’s where you’ll meet a genuinely friendly host of servers and maybe even one of the owners. Wines are thoughtfully curated and comfortably priced.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7470;The Lambs Club;USA;New York;132 W. 44th St., New York, 10036, USA;40.75665;-73.98454;100;true;false;Steakhouse;Housed within the stylish Chatwal Hotel, this Midtown institution returns, ready again to host power lunches and pre-show dinners. The setting is as sleek as ever with its iconic black walls, scarlet-red booths and polished chrome finishes anchored by a roaring limestone fireplace. Such opulence feels neither stuffy nor forced, while the restaurant brings genuine culinary chops to the neighborhood thanks to a talented team. Dry-aged steaks served with a host of sauces are obvious crowd pleasers, but don’t miss out on some of the more thoughtful offerings like smoked gnocchi with chanterelles, sweet corn and shaved black truffles or a proficient black bass en papillote. Potent cocktails are guaranteed to keep the night going until curtain call.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
7471;Okonomi Market;USA;Brooklyn;290 Graham Ave., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.712337;-73.9438879;76;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;In sharp contrast to lengthy tasting menus fit with all the bells and whistles, this six-seat counter is about as easygoing as they come. The setting is the back room of a long-standing market that sells bento boxes and sushi-grade fish during the day. There are also no servers — just Chef Daniel Lee and his sous cooking and chatting as if they’re hosting a dinner party for friends in their apartment. The casualness of it all is a welcome stage to the nicely pitched menu composed almost entirely of fantastic, locally sourced fish. Think wahoo sashimi topped with a zesty cucumber-seaweed sauce or superb tilefish cured in kombu, wrapped in shiso leaves, and fried in a light, flaky, beer batter. Guests are encouraged to bring their own beverages.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7473;Dame;USA;New York;87 MacDougal St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7290674;-74.0013397;33;true;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Dreamed up by Patricia Howard and Ed Szymanski, this pop-up turned brick-and-mortar is all the rage, so reservations are a must. It's a quaint space, dressed with white and blue hues as well as wood accents. The seafood-focused menu spins to the season, although fish and chips is the dish that catapulted it to fame. Featuring a massive piece of hake with a lacy batter and sprinkling of salt flakes, this cult classic arrives with fries and tartar sauce. For dessert, a slice of olive oil cake with macerated cherries will do the trick. Meanwhile, the wine list is substantial and arranged under two heads—what would James Bond or Austin Powers drink? Naturally, the Bond section features classics, while Powers gets more playful.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7475;The Orchard Townhouse;USA;New York;242 Tenth Ave., New York, 10001, USA;40.7483763;-74.0036007;89;true;false;Contemporary;The Orchard Townhouse is an all-day spot that expertly balances trendy looks with an endearing atmosphere. This downtown bistro is the perfect place to catch up with a friend, but it's equally welcoming for solo diners who want to enjoy a leisurely meal. Every bit the neighborhood gem, it's also so much more than that, with earnest cooking and originality coming from this kitchen. Echoing the look and feel, the menu spotlights contemporary bistro fare with snacks and salads, sandwiches at lunch and main dishes served all day, with the likes of spicy crab spaghetti with roasted tomato, pickled chili and breadcrumbs or a delicious rendition of chicken Milanese. The radish pakora with cucumber-herb yogurt dipping sauce is always a good idea.;Air conditioning;[]
7476;Massara;USA;New York;913 Broadway, New York, 10010, USA;40.7397101;-73.9898143;38;false;true;Italian, Regional Cuisine;This Southern Italian restaurant in the Flatiron District is helmed by Chef Stefano Secchi of Rezdôra. Here, the menu focuses on the regional cuisine of Campania and is designed with a shared plates mindset. The cooking is strong and clever. Kick off the meal with grilled ciabatta or tender pulpo before settling on pasta, the star of the show. Most is made in-house and the dishes are sized for sharing, so order several to sample their handiwork. Standouts include the whimsically named "If pasta fredda was eaten in Amalfi," a thicker noodle served cold and coated in a puréed tomato-based sauce and topped with raw red shrimp and lobes of uni. Cheesemakers raviolini, with six ravioli filled with burrata imported from Campania, is proof positive of this team's skill for pasta.;Air conditioning;[]
7477;Sawa;USA;Brooklyn;75 5th Ave, Brooklyn, 11217, USA;40.6804175;-73.9775811;64;true;true;Middle Eastern, Lebanese;Siblings Samaya Boueri Ziade and George Boueri have partnered on their first restaurant, Sawa, which just so happens to mean "together" in Arabic. This lively spot lures a crowd: by the time they unlock the doors, the line is already long. Everyone is here for the convivial ambience and the standout Middle Eastern food from Chef Soroosh Golbabae. This is a menu thick with options, with labneh and hummus with wagyu beef cheeks kicking things off before a round of mezze like tabbouleh, fried meat pies, and kibbeh nayeh. Don't miss the rakkakat, or akkawi and halloumi cheese wrapped in filo and fried to a golden crisp. Grilled Australian lamb chop with garlic labneh and a generous coating of urfa bibir is a smoky, savory main dish. Finish with the pistachio mafroukeh.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7478;See No Evil Pizza;USA;New York;210 W. 50th St., New York, 10019, USA;40.7614513;-73.9844096;88;true;false;Pizza, American Contemporary;There are just some places that are so New York they couldn't be found anywhere else. See No Evil Pizza is just that. It could be the location in a subway station, or it could be because they're doling out an iconic New York staple—pizza—but don't be fooled by the environs, as a treasure awaits inside. It's casual with a hint of punk, with 80s classics overhead and black-and-white checkered floors. Sit back and let the commuters fly by as you snack on small plates like toast with sardines or a seasonal bowl of beautiful beans in a walnut sauce before moving on to the pizza. There are always specials, but the Hell pie, a thin crust variety topped with spicy meat, is always good. Finish with vanilla soft serve with olive oil and sea salt.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7479;Four Twenty Five;USA;New York;425 Park Ave., New York, 10022, USA;40.76053;-73.97123;57;true;false;Contemporary;Jonathan Benno and Jean-Georges Vongerichten are behind this elegant restaurant named for the address of the sleek building it's located within. Flooded with natural light, it's stunning yet understated.The menu pulls influences from all over, hopscotching across Italy and France to Asia. Dishes, like the foie gras plated with blood orange compote and served alongside warm, spiced madeleines, have a grand flair while featuring earnest cooking. Even a plate of asparagus is elevated, thanks to creamy avocado slices and a punchy vinaigrette. The meal concludes with a teardrop-shaped chocolate tart that delivers on every level with black cardamom crémeux, tonka whipped ganache, and buckwheat caramel sided by marzipan ice cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7480;Carlotto;USA;New York;100 E. 19th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.737643;-73.9878289;82;false;false;Contemporary, Italian-American;Though it's steps from Gramercy Park, an area already brimming with dining choices, Carlotto is a chic and elegant newcomer worthy of attention. It has just the right mix of Southern Italian-American cuisine and impeccable hospitality, where warmly lit interiors and exposed brick walls exude an urban trattoria ambience. The bustling open kitchen in back provides plenty of entertainment. Begin with the beef carpaccio, with tissue-thin slices of beef tenderloin topped with slightly smoky aioli, Burgundy truffle and pecorino. Then, risotto tucked with meaty Alaskan king crab and sweet corn is textbook perfect. Finally, their selection of amari, including vintage varieties, is beyond comprehensive and is a worthy splash in your affogato.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7481;Inga's Bar;USA;Brooklyn;66 Hicks St., Brooklyn, 11201, USA;40.699959;-73.9937257;87;true;false;American;To quote an old sitcom, is this where everybody knows your name? The flickering candles, the tin pressed ceiling, the white brick — there is immediate and irresistible warmth to this restaurant, once a tavern and now beautifully reborn. It will no doubt serve Brooklyn Heights well. Energy and charm are palpable, and equally so, the food warrants repeat visits. There is no culinary North Star beyond a commitment to total satisfaction. Duck poutine croquettes are mozzarella sticks in their most delicious, adult form. Trout with beurre blanc or fork-tender braised rabbit with lardon showcase a more serious, nonetheless satisfying, side. Want something easy? A popular burger and blackout cake with lemon curd will close out the night with ease.;Air conditioning;[]
7482;Lingo;USA;Brooklyn;27 Greenpoint Ave., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7297673;-73.9597012;33;false;true;Japanese, American;Chef Emily Yuen, who has worked around the world in classic kitchens like La Gavroche, now runs the show at this Greenpoint restaurant. Lingo, which means "apple" in Japanese, is an homage to American and European comfort food with elegantly blended Japanese influences. Here, chawanmushi is dressed up with rock shrimp, scallop tartare, bisque foam, and sea grapes for a delightful cultural collision. Roasted bone marrow steak tartare is unctuous and savory with creamy, nutty tones from black sesame but perhaps the best example of Lingo's unique style is their beef pie. Made with Hokkaido-style braised beef curry, this oval pie with a golden pastry crust is a beautiful riff on the classic.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7483;Sweetbriar;USA;New York;127 E. 27th St., New York, 10016, USA;40.7423865;-73.9835546;100;false;true;Contemporary, American;Located at the base of the handsome Park South hotel, Sweetbriar a buzzy spot, where well-dressed diners make for enjoyable people watching. This appealing restaurant delivers New American cooking kissed by the flames of a wood-fired grill and a seasonally directed menu that has something for everyone. A bowl of creamy stracciatella cheese topped with grilled carrots dressed in salsa macha is an enticing opener before tucking into a savory dish of creamy cavatelli studded with meaty clams and golden-fried breadcrumbs. For dessert, the croissant bread pudding with vanilla ice cream and a drizzle of caramel crème anglaise hits all the right notes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7484;Archie's Tap & Table;USA;Bronx;536 City Island Ave., Bronx, 10464, USA;40.852904;-73.789605;27;false;false;American, Contemporary;City Island is lauded for its fresh seafood, breezy style and classic New England vibe. Amidst this scene, discover Archie's—a small space that's simply decorated but ultra warm and inviting.In this kitchen, Chef Alex Pertsovsky devotes his time to cooking with seasonally appropriate ingredients, and correspondingly, his gastropub-inspired menu is full of affordable, top-quality fare. On the one hand there are crispy chipotle-honey chicken wings with Maytag blue cheese dip and wild salmon with cabbage fried rice, while the Detroit pizza is an homage to the years he spent in the Midwest. Desserts, like the sublime banana cream pie, are deserving of your time—and appetite. Order a second one to go if you're so inclined (and you will be).;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7485;Tong;USA;Brooklyn;321 Starr St., Brooklyn, 11237, USA;40.70804;-73.9203333;61;false;false;Thai;One of the first questions a server here will ask is whether you like spicy food. Answer truthfully because this Thai kitchen does not hold back when it comes to those fiery chilies, which seem to find their way into every corner of the menu. It’s all part of the allure at this sleek dining room, built out of concrete warehouse floors and rustic metal walls accented with flecks of gold.The space is indeed a welcome hangout, where friends can crowd their table with a host of small plates, or kub klaem. Highlights like fried banana blossoms with cucumber relish, or crispy rice with fermented pork sausage and shallots deliver a whirl of textures and sharp flavors. The thinly sliced grilled pork jowl and warming khao soi win over many fans.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7486;53;USA;New York;53 W. 53rd St., New York, 10019, USA;40.761648;-73.978359;31;true;false;Asian, Contemporary;It is only fitting that this newcomer dazzles with all the style and smarts of the next-door Museum of Modern Art. The bar and lounge upstairs are but a tease of what’s hiding below: A glowing, expansive dining room with sweeping wood patterns, sleek banquettes and a long bar that never slows down. Courtesy of the Altamarea Group, this Pan-Asian restaurant delivers familiar Chinese and Singaporean favorites with fantastic precision. Soup dumplings imbued with black truffle, kung pao quail with snap peas and hearty clay pots packed with crispy rice are easy favorites. Dessert is another point of pride here – we’re partial to the housemade ice creams and sorbet. The polished service team rounds out an experience that feels distinctly New York.;Air conditioning;[]
7487;Hyun;USA;New York;10 E. 33rd St., New York, 10016, USA;40.7475556;-73.9845154;82;false;false;Korean, Steakhouse;Hyun is a luxurious take on Korean barbecue, focusing squarely on top-notch Japanese A5 Wagyu, butchered in-house and grilled tableside. Enter this temple of indulgent tranquility to discover sleek dark wood, cool slate surfaces, and private rooms.The Hyun-makase is the gateway into this one-of-a-kind meal which takes you on a journey of 12 different pieces of Japanese A5 Wagyu. Each piece is expertly prepared tableside and served alongside house-made fresh kimchi, green lettuce for wrapping, and a crispy scallion salad that balances the unctuous Wagyu. The tasting is complete when the bulgogi is prepared. Diners may also look forward to other indulgences like rice with uni and truffles, or thick noodles with cold beef broth.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7488;Soothr;USA;New York;204 E. 13th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7324059;-73.9874378;24;true;false;Thai;This buzzy hotspot fills up fast – and for good reason. The inside is quaint with vintage touches, like weathered wood beams, a bar fitted out with an antique telephone, and a bright neon sign. Tables with tufted red leather booths, lanterns, and a charming back garden keep the vibe inviting. As for the menu, it’s a sizeable one so bring a crew to make the most of many excellent regional specialties. Roasted eggplant salad is a refreshing start, while the grilled pork salad comes turbocharged in a spicy lime and chili dressing. You could play it safe with chicken khao soi or find a new favorite in the boldly spiced pork blood soup. Whatever direction you take, expect zippy, boldly seasoned dishes. A thoughtful cocktail program is worth exploring as well.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7490;Popina;USA;Brooklyn;127 Columbia St., Brooklyn, 11231, USA;40.6874514;-74.0013993;36;false;false;Italian;This quaint and adorable nook—with small tables set shoulder-to-shoulder—is poised on the waterfront and overlooks the river. Inside, the space is homey and scattered with patrons perusing the limited yet tempting menu. Italian leanings dominate most dishes turned out of the adept kitchen, including pappardelle floating in a parmesan broth with tender ham hock and collards, as well as hearty arancini finished with saffron honey. Other highlights like hot chicken milanese served with crunchy radicchio, and hake with a vibrant green garlic sauce showcase a delightful union of flavors and textures.Oenophiles can also be found appreciating the concise yet thoroughly crafted wine selection, which celebrates top producers and back vintages.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7492;Mint Premium Foods;USA;Tarrytown;19 Main St., Tarrytown, 10591, USA;41.0768001;-73.859404;19;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Gastropub;Both a gourmet market and full-service restaurant, this "premium" haven resides on a charming block in the equally charming Tarrytown. Up front, a retail area teems with food from around the world. Further along the deep and narrow space, find exposed brick walls, antique artifacts and a smattering of tables.The semi-open kitchen turns out a menu that meanders around the Mediterranean, resulting in hearty seafood, savory steaks and charcuterie aplenty. Sip on a beer from their large selection and nibble on grilled dates stuffed with creamy goat cheese and prosciutto as you peruse the menu, taking note of the especially tempting burgers on offer.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7494;Via Carota;USA;New York;51 Grove St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7331146;-74.0035517;62;false;true;Italian;Occasionally, predictability can be a beautiful thing, especially when it comes to rave-worthy Italian cooking. Via Carota is not so much robotically perfect as it is pleasing—in fact it’s the kind of place where dishes can (and should) be piled on. Italian style and artistry combine in this homey space that features bare wood farm tables, sideboards and whitewashed brick. Plan ahead, since reservations fill quickly at this popular spot. Diners may start nibbling on deep-fried olives that are plump, piping-hot and stuffed with pork sausage. Then, a luscious (and unmissable) risotto cacio e pepe arrives loaded with pecorino and fresh pepper. For dessert, the simple-sounding flourless chocolate cake is downright excellent.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7495;4 Charles Prime Rib;USA;New York;4 Charles St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7352707;-74.0004955;50;true;false;Steakhouse;Brendan Sodikoff's destination makes the case that NY should be home to more Chicago influencers. This spot may be named for its street address, but the intimate size and modest exterior make it a charming hideaway. The staff merely enhance this special vibe, by ensuring the comfort of each diner with engaging banter.Some dishes may break with tradition, but offer nothing short of tasty results. Additionally, the menu showcases a sense of depth by going beyond the eponymous dish, which is coincidentally served in three different ways. Others are firmly footed classics, served alongside creamed spinach, roasted garlic, and butter-laden mashed potatoes. Bookend your meal with cocktails and a wedge of Valrhona dark chocolate pie in an Oreo-cookie crust.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
7496;King;USA;New York;18 King St., New York, 10014, USA;40.727753;-74.003293;64;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;It’s an art form to make delicious food look this easy. Chef/owners Clare de Boer and Jess Shadbolt met working at London's esteemed River Café, then banded together with Annie Shi to open King. The popular bar area leads to an intimate rear dining space lined with bright artwork and gleaming mirrors—the overall effect is a sense of ease that restaurants can take ages to acquire.The kitchen brings a deft touch to their small, daily changing menu, with ingredients pulled straight from the greenmarket. Snack on crispy-custardy panisse before tucking in to a plate of house-made ravioli with sauteed broccoli rabe, ricotta salata, and lemon zest or grilled wild striped bass with a white bean mash.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7497;Eulalie;USA;New York;239 West Broadway, New York, 10013, USA;40.7196112;-74.0059001;22;false;false;French, Classic French;New York loves a good throwback and Chef Chip Smith and wife/general manager Tina Vaughn have leaned into that vibe at Eulalie, where reservations are required and made exclusively by phone, the menu is handwritten, and guests are buzzed in at the door. If this all sounds a bit formal, it's not. It's very warm and welcoming. Chef Smith's four-course, French-leaning prix fixe may begin with a delicious opener of duck liver terrine dotted with green pistachio and peppercorns, followed by a savory tart with caramelized onions, Gruyère, and prosciutto. Golden-brown, crispy flounder atop a green tomato beurre blanc is a lovely main dish. Wine pairings, a cheese course, and dessert are also available—do get the coconut cake.;Air conditioning;[]
7498;Miss Mamie's Spoonbread Too;USA;New York;366 W. 110th St., New York, 10025, USA;40.8015558;-73.9607087;65;false;true;Southern, American;Come to Miss Mamie’s and plan to indulge, Southern style. The kitchen embraces such tried-and-true classics as baked turkey wings, homemade meatloaf, Louisiana catfish, Southern-fried chicken sided by candied yams and collard greens, and a creamy red velvet cake for dessert. Grab a fresh-squeezed lemonade and dive into the sampler, stocked with deep-fried shrimp, fall-off-the-bone beef short ribs, fried chicken, and sides of cornbread stuffing and hoppin' John. Desserts are made in house, so a slice of peach cobbler or wedge of sweet potato pie are mandatory.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7499;Meadowsweet;USA;Brooklyn;149 Broadway, Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.710354;-73.96317;34;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, American Contemporary;Tucked next to the steely skeleton of the Williamsburg Bridge, Meadowsweet cuts a stylish industrial figure with its glass-fronted façade, whitewashed brick walls and original mosaic-tiled floors. Inside, the restaurant jumps with a steady stream of locals and regulars, all here for well-priced and well-executed food.The fuss is quite merited. Despite ample competition in this section of town, Owners Polo Dobkin and Stephanie Lempert elevate the kitchen’s dishes ranging from crispy baby artichokes with shaved parmesan and orechiette with blue crab tossed in a lemon beurre fondue to spiced duck breast with sweet corn polenta, grilled escarole and Mandarin orange. It's all done in a lovely, urbane setting with loads of charm and friendly service.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7500;Vinum;USA;Staten Island;704 Bay St., Staten Island, 10304, USA;40.624893;-74.074715;90;true;true;Italian;As its name would suggest, this bijou on Bay Street is centered around wines, with many offered by the glass. Inside, where wooden wine crates double as decor, the place feels like an osteria straight out of Italy.The menu is designed for sharing. “The Meatball Bar” is a treat, with unlikely twists on tired offerings—think truffled veal or lamb. Hearty mains, like a pan-roasted Berkshire pork chop with rosemary, garlic and balsamic vinegar, or a smoky puttanesca pasta are never a bad idea. Chef Massimo Felici’s passion for baking and pastries is clear in the house-made breads, and carries through to desserts that are worth getting excited over.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7502;JoJo;USA;New York;160 E. 64th St., New York, 10065, USA;40.765182;-73.9656;82;false;false;Contemporary;Chef Jean-Georges Vongerichten runs a restaurant empire today that spans the globe, but his journey started here back in 1991. A few years ago, the space underwent a refresh, and now this cozy, two-story townhouse is a contemporary respite for the area’s moneyed residents. The menu isn’t particularly groundbreaking—think roast chicken, seared salmon, and Maine lobster—but you’ll certainly find seasonality, quality product, and astute cooking in good supply. Recent highlights include warm asparagus with vegetable vinaigrette as well as rack of lamb with braised artichokes and peas. For dessert, try something new like the sour cherry pie or indulge in a bit of nostalgia with the likes of molten chocolate cake with vanilla ice cream.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
7503;Faun;USA;Brooklyn;606 Vanderbilt Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.67825;-73.968704;60;false;false;Contemporary, American;This Prospect Heights haven is one that should be on everyone's radar. Adorned with cool marble surfaces and a flaming open kitchen, it is welcoming, intimate, and tranquil. The long bar is lovely for socializing, as is the backyard—which flaunts the kind of charm that diners crave on warm days.Thanks to this kitchen's vision, the menu is concise and dotted with superb items. Start with the fresh-baked focaccia—a veritable dream among carb lovers—that pairs especially well with creamy chicken liver mousse and tangy pickles. Then proceed to devour the wonderfully gamey Colorado lamb chops, tailed by a peach and blueberry tart with vanilla gelato. From a palatably priced flight of amari to the house soda, this team offers an ideal dining experience.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7505;Ernesto's;USA;New York;259 E. Broadway, New York, 10002, USA;40.7143679;-73.9855324;78;true;true;Spanish;It’s all too easy to find favor in this bustling Basque getaway, located at the foot of the Brooklyn and Manhattan Bridges. Sleek coffee-brown tables, globe light fixtures dangling throughout, and a long, marble-top bar exude midcentury-modern style, while a constant crowd fosters a near electric vibe. Indeed, everything is meant to be shared, and everyone is having a good time.A mound of house-made potato chips layered with thin slices of jamón Ibérico is a fitting start, before piling the table with heartier dishes like meltingly tender tripe slow-braised with tomatoes and morcilla. Then linger over an equally rich grilled squad breast served with rice and mushrooms. The wine list is an impressive tomb of small organic and biodynamic Spanish producers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7507;Sofreh;USA;Brooklyn;75 St. Marks Ave., Brooklyn, 11217, USA;40.6797663;-73.9741048;47;false;false;Persian, Regional Cuisine;The buzz surrounding Nasim Alikhani’s pretty Park Slope spot is deservedly strong. The Chef/owner immigrated to NY from Iran over 35 years ago, making her way through many a kitchen before landing her own iteration. It was well worth the wait, for at Sofreh, she has managed to pin Persian cuisine firmly onto the ground. The decor displays no splashes of color, just calm inspiration all around. A bright marble bar welcomes all to her glass-clinking retreat, with high-ceilings and black wood beams.Thanks to this minimalist aspect, the colorful food is able to shine through. Dinner might reveal beef meatballs simmered with sour cherries and set beside string fries, or succulent lamb in a turmeric-and-onion consommé, tucked with fava beans and crisp onions.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7508;Tobalá;USA;Bronx;3732 Riverdale Ave., Bronx, 10463, USA;40.8871043;-73.9069908;77;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Tobalá is one of the most exciting spots to hit the Bronx in years. Inside, it's minimal and modern, with a light and creamy palette punctuated by textural design elements and clay masks, and Oaxacan pottery enhances every table. The food is as dreamy as the setting. Served piping hot in a folded napkin, blue and yellow corn tortillas are made to order and served with spicy salsa verde and a smoky salsa de chile d'arbol. For tacos, the succulent lamb barbacoa piled high atop two blue corn tortillas, is a no-brainer. Enmolada de pato in an earthy and complex mole with notes of fruit and a creeping burn is topped with cooling rings of red onion, a flutter of white sesame seeds, paper-thin slices of calabacitas and shaved serrano peppers for a bit of brightness.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7510;DaXi Sichuan;USA;Queens;136-20 Roosevelt Ave., Ste. 2R, Queens, 11354, USA;40.759773;-73.82923;38;true;false;Chinese, Sichuan;When dining with a crowd, head to DaXi Sichuan. This elegant spot on the second floor of the New World Mall shares a nuanced approach to regional Chinese cuisine—imagine slivers of cold marinated duck in a pool of fiery chili-infused oil. Sliced pork with garlic sauce arrives as bite-sized rolls with thin, tender pork wrapped around batons of cucumber topped with a garlic-chili soy sauce.Then, a large bowl with a steaming, tangy broth arrives bobbing with fish, fresh and pickled vegetables, and red chilis. Even the straightforward house special, featuring a mix of fluffy rice, pork, and potatoes, is known to satisfy many an appetite. Service is efficient, often ferrying dishes at lightning speed.;Air conditioning;[]
7511;Le Gigot;USA;New York;18 Cornelia St., New York, 10014, USA;40.73141;-74.00169;36;false;false;French;At first glance, Le Gigot transports guests to a romantic and inviting little bistro—the kind you’d only find in La Ville-Lumière. The service exceeds expectations with uncharacteristic warmth that brings a welcoming vibe to the nostalgic dining room. Tasty renditions of classic bistro fare dominate the menu, so expect the cooking to be familiar and pleasing. The petit bouillabaisse begins as a saffron fish broth with a red-peppery North African accent to elevate the traditional fish and seafood dish. Their cassoulet is a beloved Toulousaine version with duck confit, bacon, cannellini beans, herbs and luscious pork. Finally, apple tarte tatin, served warm with a dollop of crème fraîche and fresh blueberries, is a perfect closer.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7512;Hart's;USA;Brooklyn;506 Franklin Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.681463;-73.95589;69;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Tucked behind the Franklin Avenue subway stairs, this intimate Mediterranean venue has been causing quite a stir. A pretty slate-blue façade directs you to a small space starring whitewashed brick walls, blonde wood tables and a skylight. A handful of seats at the marble counter offer a view into the mini kitchen. But, there is nothing mini about Chef Nick Perkins’ culinary skills. In fact, he is the master of working magic out of a small kitchen.Start with an heirloom tomato salad laced with olive oil, dried red chili, and paired with escabeche-style mussels. Then perfectly poached hake is served with anchovies and bitter greens for a rustic yet relishable dish. Pork Milanese plated with cucumber and shaved fennel flaunts a great deal of fun and flair.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7515;Dons Bogam;USA;New York;17 E. 32nd St., New York, 10016, USA;40.74689;-73.98429;99;false;true;Korean, Barbecue;At Dons Bogam, the food is fantastic and service indulgent. From the festive bar up front right down to those two-tops sporting blazing grills, every seat is filled, so reserve ahead. Make no mistake: this is no average K-town joint. Inside, a top-notch venting system lets diners enjoy a smoke-free evening of exceptional grilled meats. Start with fried pork mandu, which are on-point and divine. Pork belly marinated in red wine is smoky and supremely tender, but for the ultimate payoff, opt for the beef platter. It features thinly sliced maeun and yangnyeom galbi set beside meaty king trumpet mushrooms. In Midtown for meetings? Pop in for the BBQ lunch, a fun and interactive midday meal that is leaps above a quick grab-and-go salad, yet just as healthy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7518;East Harbor Seafood Palace;USA;Brooklyn;714-726 65th St., Brooklyn, 11220, USA;40.63343;-74.01442;20;false;true;Chinese, Dim Sum;Guests can barely get through this front door, where crowds pack in on weekends for dim sum. They wait patiently as an announcer shouts reservation numbers over a booming speaker—like a game of high-stakes bingo. Dim sum is a well-orchestrated affair, with steaming carts rolling by and waiters ferrying trays into the gold-accented dining room. Eyes can guide the ordering when it comes to the carts, stocked with authentic bites. Highlights include the siu mai, followed by rice noodles wrapped around shrimp and doused in a sweet soy sauce. Black bean spare ribs are flavorful, but don't skip the zongzi—tea leaf-wrapped sticky rice stuffed with pork and mushrooms.Things are more tame on weekdays, but that just means there's no need to fight the lines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7519;Bridges;USA;New York;9 Chatham Sq., New York, 10038, USA;40.713902;-73.9980577;35;true;true;Contemporary;The talented Sam Lawrence is off to an impressive start with this welcome restaurant in the heart of Chinatown. The warm, amber-toned dining room possesses the ease and comfort of a bistro, while the kitchen cooks with noteworthy levels of drive and ambition. The tight menu is sparse on words and doesn’t fit neatly into the box of any one cuisine but know that inspiration and originality are in proper supply. A smooth sea urchin custard topped with shrimp tartare segues nicely into perfectly grilled sweetbreads that rival the very best in town. Finish with fireworks: Velvety-smooth vin jaune gelato matched with passionfruit is an unexpected thriller that, much like the restaurant, has all the makings of a classic. Service is both relaxed and attentive.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7520;Veerays;USA;New York;213 E. 45th St., New York, 10017, USA;40.7527058;-73.9725633;53;false;false;Indian;If the red velvet banquettes, dark brown wooden walls, and decorative accents didn't quite give it away, the menu's "swanky starters," "showstoppers," and "jazzy breads," certainly will. This place exudes that classic 1920s speakeasy vibe, albeit with a twist, as the menu spotlights contemporary Indian cuisine. Bollywood hits and jazz play in the background as you peruse the cocktail list for nods to bootlegging gangsters like Diamond Joe, a slightly sweet gin-champagne cocktail. Rogan Josh, a braised lamb shank with Kashmiri chilis that add subtle heat, is spot on. Fluffy basmati rice with yellow lentils and black mustard seeds is enhanced with coconut for a savory-sweet treat, and don't miss the creamy daal makhani with black lentils and a hint of heat.;;[]
7521;The Dining Room at The Guesthouse;USA;New York;55 Gansevoort St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7395004;-74.006957;45;true;true;Contemporary;What happens when a home design brand dynamo opens a hotel and restaurant? You get this swanky spot, of course. Just around the corner from RH's flagship in the Meatpacking District, this guesthouse and dining room endeavor to make guests feel like they're being welcomed to a private home. As expected, it's styled with that handsome modern look synonymous with the brand. The focused menu is carefully curated, with a small selection of contemporary dishes with live fire elements and unfussy flair. Though far from inexpensive, dishes are executed with precision and utilize quality ingredients. Caviar-studded starters kick things off in style, then opt for the whole wood-grilled branzino. Cap off the meal with butterscotch crème brûlée.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7522;Le Rock;USA;New York;45 Rockefeller Plaza, New York, 10111, USA;40.7592008;-73.9781447;70;true;false;Contemporary, French;No stranger to crowds, the team behind Frenchette has quickly found its footing on the ground floor of bustling Rockefeller Center. Dim lighting blankets this elegant, Art-Deco space where a large bar up front mixes and stirs at a fast clip. They have good reason to be speedy: This is one of the more refined restaurants to open in the area in years, and the crowds have caught on immediately. In line with a French brasserie, the menu offers familiar trappings: seafood platters, hearty pâtés, classic sauces like bearnaise and brown butter, duck confit lentils, and, of course, delicious profiteroles smothered in buckwheat honey fudge. Adding to the fun is a welcome bit of tableside showmanship for dishes like leeks vinaigrette.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7523;Towa;USA;New York;36 W. 26th St., New York, 10010, USA;40.7440971;-73.9897131;39;false;false;Japanese, Contemporary;The small illuminated sign outside is a hint of what's to come at Towa, where low lighting andmulti-hued wood conspire to create a stylish setting. Take a seat in the narrow dining room or at the omakase counter, where Chef Masaya Shirai directs a kaiseki-inspired menu. Dishes like kani hourensou ohitashi, or snow crab and spinach in dashi broth, are focused on seasonality and tradition. Dashi broth-marinated tomato with chia seeds and passion fruit captures the flavor of summer perfectly. Futomaki lives up to its name (fat rolled sushi) with a generous roll filled with tuna, salmon, amberjack, kanpachi and shrimp tempura, along with vegetables. Finally, sake kasu cheesecake with yuzu honey is a dainty dessert.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7525;Octo;USA;New York;1 E. 33rd St., New York, 10016, USA;40.7477018;-73.9843947;18;true;true;Asian Contemporary, Fusion;They may be behind New York's oldest Korean barbecue restaurant, but Steve and Christina Jang aren't resting on any laurels. Chef Segeun Song leads the charge on the à la carte menu that channels a distinctive Korean-Chinese fusion cuisine. A tempting array of dishes includes noodles, rice, and lunch specials. Reserve ahead for their Peking black duck or tuck into signature dishes like beef tangsuyuk or cumin pork back ribs. Of course, one glance at the special dumpling workshop and it's clear they must be ordered.  Pork and Thai chili soup dumplings with a dot of caviar are one way to go, but there's also the delicious spicy poached dumplings in a black vinegar sauce.;Air conditioning;[]
7526;Kyma;USA;New York;15 W. 18th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.73877;-73.9923;99;true;false;Greek, Seafood;As its name in Greek suggests, this stunner is making “waves” in town by way of Roslyn, New York. The space transports diners to the Ionian Sea but it’s not just beauty that bewitches here. All Hellenic meals begin with a panoply of spreads, so using a warm pita, scoop up the pikilia trio with feta, hummus, and taramasalata. Calamari stuffed with four cheeses and served over a Nafpaktos tomato sauce is a winner. Then, a basket full of golden-brown halloumi fries served with two dipping sauces is nothing short of satisfying. The menu also lists a series of freshly caught fish such as  lavraki, a beautiful sea bass served whole, and meat dishes like the short rib youvetsi. Ekmek kataifi, featuring shredded phyllo and semolina custard, is a fine way to end this Greek feast.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
7527;Melba's;USA;New York;300 W. 114th St., New York, 10026, USA;40.80304;-73.95659;16;false;true;Southern, American;With its colorful spirit and lineup of Southern classics, this comfortable spot—as charming and lovely as its namesake owner, born-and-bred Harlemite Melba Wilson—is a perfect reflection of the neighborhood’s flavor, culture, and past. It’s a place to gather and relax over good food and drinks, from Auntie B’s mini-burgers slathered with a smoky-sweet sauce to a golden-brown fruit cobbler that’s nothing short of heaven on a plate. Equally enticing is the Southern fried chicken—darkly bronzed, sweet, and salty when paired with Melba’s iconic eggnog waffles. Expect other surprises like spring rolls stuffed with black-eyed peas, collards, and cheddar cheese, as well as a healthy-minded grilled vegetable Napoleon with buffalo mozzarella.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7528;Loring Place;USA;New York;21 W. 8th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7327626;-73.9974029;67;true;true;American;Named after the Bronx street that his father grew up on, Loring Place is where Chef Dan Kluger serves up delicious, stylistic, and locally sourced Californian cuisine to a downtown crowd. And yet, none of this comes as a surprise as the chef has showcased his talents for years and been the recipient of much acclaim in the city. His skillfully made, vegetable-centric American fare served here is unique and spirited, beginning with wood-grilled broccoli salad with orange, pistachios, and mint. The wood-oven pizzas, made with house-milled whole wheat flour, are a hit at any time. The generously sized room is uncluttered and mid-century chic, with bright orange window frames and boldly striped banquettes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7529;aRoqa;USA;New York;206 Ninth Ave., New York, 10011, USA;40.746166;-74.00148;35;true;true;Indian, Contemporary;aRoqa shares a selection of contemporary Indian food in a format of shared plates. The ambience here is more romantic than family-friendly, featuring moody tones of black and gold, an arched dark wood ceiling, and a bar with shimmering panels.The menu descriptions showcase the chef's creative flair. Try the light and airy breaded squash kofte served in an aromatic bath of turmeric infused creamed corn. The goat keema is deeply savory and saucy and pairs well with the paneer-stuffed jalapeno-flecked naan to sop up all the sauce. Kulcha, or hot wedges of freshly griddled, moist, and tender flatbread, is stuffed with paneer and finely diced green chilies for a hint of heat.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7530;Carbone;USA;New York;181 Thompson St., New York, 10003, USA;40.727966;-74.00017;85;true;false;Italian, Italian-American;The ever-so-stylish Carbone continues to captivate audiences with its striking interior and smartly dressed servers who work the floor with a bit of flirt and flair. Reservations remain scarce and prices sky high at this big and bold ode to Italian-American cuisine. Dinner reigns supreme, though crowds are present at all times, largely thanks to the sense of history that pervades the space—imagine plush banquettes, impressive ceramics and glittering chandeliers.Mid-century classics are the focus of this menu. Antipasti like crusty garlic bread or olive oil-dunked mozzarella may be trailed by evergreen hits like rigatoni alla vodka or spaghetti alla gricia. The blackout cake sounds simple but is pure pleasure.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7531;I Sodi;USA;New York;314 Bleecker St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7328652;-74.0039954;97;true;false;Italian;Manhattan has no shortage of Italian restaurants, but surely Rita Sodi runs two of the most beloved ones. Just down the street from Via Carota, this cozy, buzzy hotspot remains a difficult reservation to score so consider planning on an early-hour walk-in. The kitchen watches the seasons closely in daily specials like grilled tomato and burrata, while also respecting that some signatures can never leave the menu. The perfectly layered lasagna is a must for first timers, and it contrasts wonderfully with a citrusy tangle of pappardelle al limon. Regardless of where you sit – bar, dining room, or further back – the neighborhood restaurant is a constant hive of activity, fueled in part by a busy bar that knows its way around a Negroni.;Air conditioning;[]
7532;Junoon;USA;New York;19 W. 24th St., New York, 10010, USA;40.7430797;-73.9908429;82;true;true;Indian, Contemporary;Pendant lights strung with thick grass ropes, vintage mirrors, and a gleaming white marble bar set a sophisticated tone at this long-standing Indian restaurant. With an eye for presentation and a taste for new ideas, the menu offers a range of dishes. Tuna puchka brings three bite-sized semolina puffs tucked with finely diced raw tuna topped with a dollop of caviar. The tomato-based tile fish Assamese curry offers a delicious spice journey with gentle heat and notes of cilantro. Meanwhile, savory dal makhani calls for a house-spiced naan. To finish, a bright Madras curry-scented whipped cream infused with condensed milk makes for a proper send-off.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7533;Penny;USA;New York;90 E. 10th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7308964;-73.9895173;66;true;false;Seafood;Two cool marble counters stretch the length of the bar and kitchen and run parallel to mounds of ice stacked with bottles of Champagne and crisp white wines. The food is no less refreshing, celebrating mostly pristine seafood expertly sourced and astutely dressed and seasoned. Think razor clams with giardiniera, stuffed squid with fiery harissa, and wax beans dusted in katsuobushi. Dover sole set in an excellent bordelaise would satisfy a meatier appetite, but then again, how about just another round of freshly shucked oysters or maybe a vanilla bean and passionfruit ice cream sandwich? A small number of reservations are available, but most seats are reserved for walk-ins, so arrive early just before doors open.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7534;Moono;USA;New York;29 E. 32nd St., New York, 10016, USA;40.74637;-73.98336;38;false;false;Korean;The front doesn’t look like much, but the latest opening from the talented Jua team on the edge of Koreatown captivates from the start. No need to rush: Start at the intimate bar, where Korean spirits are blended beautifully into sophisticated cocktails. Further in, find a two-story dining room washed over in warm, honeyed tones with stained glass windows and ceilings that reach for the sky. The Korean cooking is elegant without being fussy: Think twice-fried chicken and beef tartare alongside a brilliant, dry-aged branzino that’s grilled until the skin is as chip-crisp and served with soy mustard sauce. Bubbling hotpots, a picture-perfect bowl of Queen’s Gold rice topped with a mountain of uni, and noodles round out the selection.;Air conditioning;[]
7537;Lola Taverna;USA;New York;210 Sixth Ave., New York, 10014, USA;40.7269961;-74.0033051;25;true;false;Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine;This tavern has quickly become the "it" spot in SoHo, where one is almost guaranteed to see a line of fashion-forward diners waiting for a chance to tuck into their famously tender and delicious lamb chops. Inside, it's tight but nobody seems to mind. The dining room's white stucco walls and windows set a warm and welcoming vibe. This is not your average Greek restaurant serving the tired old clichés. Instead, the chef infuses a hint of whimsy into each dish and delivers on flavor and quality. Some standouts include spanakopita spring rolls, chicken gyro bao buns, and moussaka with lamb or vegetarian options. Come Sunday for the well-priced supper and half-price wine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7538;Portale;USA;New York;126 W. 18th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7401493;-73.9960021;83;false;true;Italian, Contemporary;One walk down a charming, interior walkway to access Chef Alfred Portale's chic Chelsea dining room, set in a former 19th-century carriage house. The brick facade remains, while inside, the space has white-painted exposed brick walls and wood plank flooring.The well-curated Italian menu is done up in a contemporary manner and evokes the Mediterranean. Primi are a highlight, as in the agnolotti, featuring fresh pasta pockets filled with creamy ricotta and sauced with a zesty lamb ragu. A fillet of seared Ora King salmon is attractively plated with pesto-sauced cracked wheat and an array of garnishes that remind of ratatouille—diced, roasted eggplant and zucchini, a roasted red pepper vinaigrette, and a creamy-textured black olive vinaigrette.;Air conditioning;[]
7539;Cafe Sabarsky;USA;New York;1048 Fifth Ave., New York, 10028, USA;40.78131;-73.96028;89;false;false;Austrian;This Museum Mile kaffeehaus is so authentic it may as well be set along Vienna’s Ringstrasse. Instead, find it in a Beaux Arts mansion—home to the Neue Galerie, replete with 20th-century Austrian-and-German art and design. This gorgeous ground-floor den is clad in dark-stained wood with diners seated along a banquette covered in Otto Wagner fabric. Order one of the traditional specialties, including the city’s best wiener schnitzel or hearty Hungarian beef goulash, but it's the cakes and pastries that are the stuff of dreams. Linzer torte and Sachertorte are as classic as they are extraordinary. Feuilletine may be described as a chocolate mousse cake but it is anything but simple with its luscious, well-executed layers.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
7540;Farra;USA;New York;71 Worth St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7169774;-74.0057409;25;false;true;Contemporary;The word “Farra” has several meanings, all of which would be appropriate for this sleek retreat. Attractive, fun, and a bona fide party, Farra is a full-fledged restaurant that promises to garner a cultish following. With no charcuterie, cheese plates, or paninis in sight, diners can rest assured of savory, sumptuous cooking.Sharing the same wine cellar (and former sous chef) with next-door Atera, the team shows similar levels of hospitality, attention to detail, and creativity. Maybe you’ve had salmon tartare before, but was it mixed with potato chips for crunch and served with nori? We've all had ravioli, but what about the crown-shaped corona ripiena? Stuffed with lobster, ricotta, and set in a dashi broth, this course is in a league of its own.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7541;Purdy's Farmer & the Fish;USA;North Salem;100 Titicus Rd., North Salem, 10560, USA;41.3280818;-73.6559045;57;false;false;Seafood, American;Plenty of places talk about farm to table cuisine but what about a table at the farm? Purdy’s does just that with its darling white farmhouse with picturesque views of the farm. It’s not just cute—this restaurant walks the walk by using ingredients they grow, smoke or cure on site. From the house-made hot sauce to the carrot bread, thoughtful details are everywhere. Scallop “salad” features three perfectly seared scallops set with farm bacon and a fried egg. The strawberry and crème ice cream cake’s four bright pink layers are not only beautiful, but delicious. Even cocktails are inspired by their great outdoors—the pea martini with cucumber and elderflower is a refreshing change of pace. Stop in to the farm shop next door before heading home.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Terrace;[]
7542;MP Taverna;USA;Irvington;1 Bridge St., Irvington, 10533, USA;41.0399018;-73.8734078;61;false;true;Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine;Chef Michael Psilakis puts the "MP" in this taverna, serving his modern interpretation of Greek cuisine. Just steps from Hudson River, enter through the sleek bar area to arrive inside this 18th-century structure, with rustic brass chandeliers, mahogany panels, and neutral hues mixed with pops of blue. Whether seated at a booth, banquette or table, diners can count on family-style plates.Start with meze, like tzatziki imbued with fresh dill, before savoring mains like gently roasted chicken sporting perfectly crisp skin or aged grilled sausage with a hint of orange peel. Desserts, too, flaunt a contemporary twist, as in a whopping slice of galaktoboureko. Groups should go for the the chef's whole roast animal, but call ahead as it takes time to prep.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7546;Gage & Tollner;USA;Brooklyn;372 Fulton St., Brooklyn, 11201, USA;40.6914325;-73.9876043;42;true;false;Steakhouse, American;Vintage mirrors, cherry wood and brass chandeliers line the length of this historic restaurant, which first opened in 1892. With an amber glow and buzzing crowd, the room immediately charms, down to the no-nonsense all-classic cocktail list. There is plenty to eat here, as the team is not content to merely let history and looks stand in for substance. Seafood towers, big steaks, crab cakes and a superb platter of fried chicken with cornmeal fritters take their cues from the legendary Edna Lewis, who ran the kitchen in the late 80s and whose Southern cooking has inspired countless followers. Dessert is essential and all of them, from the coconut layer cake to the baked Alaska, will make for a fond farewell.;Air conditioning;[]
7547;Sailor;USA;Brooklyn;228 Dekalb Ave., Brooklyn, 11205, USA;40.6894743;-73.9702525;87;true;true;American;The determination required to score a table can almost feel excessive. Almost. With lines perpetually wrapped around this corner of Fort Greene, Chef April Bloomfield returns with familiar dishes that hew to the seasons and boast maximum flavor with minimum fuss. Who knew eggs with celery salt and mayonnaise could be this good? The Caesar salad, Swiss chard, and roast chicken all hit their marks. Some of these are only available during dinner when reservations are in limited supply. Lunch has its benefits too: The spring onion and goat gouda quiche is peerless, plus there’s a superb burger and a towering stack of French fries. All the while, sun beams through the skylight of a bistro that seems well on its way to becoming a neighborhood classic.;Air conditioning;[]
7548;ILIS;USA;Brooklyn;150 Green St., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7335666;-73.9553803;25;true;false;Scandinavian, Contemporary;Chef Mads Refslund is behind this ambitious, idiosyncratic operation. The striking, moody space has an "eco-chic" vibe calibrated to match a sustainable cuisine that reflects his Nordic pedigree. Diners opt between a shorter "Market Menu," where they select from a list of ingredients, each representing an individual dish, or leave things in the kitchen's hands with the "Field Guide Menu," a surprise tasting. Spanning wild-caught seafood like Jonah crab and deep-sea scallop, to game like squab and wild duck, products are of singular quality, with pure flavors accented by diverse accoutrements, from mandarinquat to hoja santa. A seat at the counter gives unhindered views of the at-times frenetic kitchen, matching the bustling feel of the room.;Interesting wine list;[]
7549;Szechuan Gourmet;USA;New York;21 W. 39th St., New York, 10018, USA;40.7522;-73.98324;33;true;false;Chinese, Sichuan;Few would expect to find some of the city’s best Sichuan food along a quiet street near Bryant Park right under the nose of Midtown office workers. But such is the case at this long-established haunt that has finally rebuilt and reopened after a terrible fire in 2018. Miraculously, the kitchen hasn’t missed a beat, and those who long for the tingly heat of Sichuan peppercorns and the burn of bright red chili oil will not leave disappointed. Thin, crispy scallion pancakes and plump pork dumplings in chili oil make for a fine start, before moving on to spicy hot and sour cellophane noodles and braised fish fillets with bean curd. Salt and pepper prawns are also worth an order. As a bonus, the remodeled space is an elegant upgrade from the original.;Air conditioning;[]
7550;Café Alaia;USA;Scarsdale;128 Garth Rd., Scarsdale, 10583, USA;40.9868746;-73.8099321;82;true;true;Italian, Italian-American;Looking for a truly warm and expansive spot serving special Italian cuisine? Come to this rustic-chic café, prettified with double-height ceilings, exposed wooden beams, and an ample bar. There are two rooms, each long and narrow but wonderfully comfortable and always abuzz. Thoughtfully arranged tables may be cradled with such impressively rich plates as tortellini en brodo, where house-made pasta bathes in a rich savory chicken broth, and pan-seared salmon with a mustard-based sauce, fingerling potatoes, and market carrots.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7551;La Devozione: The Oval;USA;New York;428 W. 16th St., New York, 10011, USA;40.7430168;-74.0053029;17;true;true;Italian;The first international outpost from Italy's 110-year-old, family-run Pastificio Di Martino, this multi-concept space nestled within the Chelsea Market houses a pasta shop along with two dining spaces, including The Oval. It is aptly named, as an oval-shaped, 30-seat counter awaits diners who will twirl their forks through a pasta tasting menu. It's all shapes, styles, and sizes, and it's far from dainty, with plate after plate of pasta. The manicotti is filled with sole and served with a bracing butter and caper sauce. Enjoy the penne served with rabbit confit and artichokes, and finish with a refreshing Mojito-inspired dessert with granita and grapefruit foam. As expected, the strong wine list leans Italian.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7552;Chola;USA;New York;232 E. 58th St., New York, 10022, USA;40.760369;-73.96573;54;true;false;Indian, Regional Cuisine;Bright, fresh and elegantly appointed Chola is nestled amidst chic design shops and upscale dining spots. Warm and hospitable servers are at the ready in its dining room, which dons polished wood floors, grey upholstery and cream walls.Dishes arrive in gleaming metal bowls, enticing diners to dig into the likes of tandoor and vegan specialties. However, the underlying theme is southern coastal cuisine, as revealed in a delicious Goan fish curry redolent of coconut milk and tamarind. Your meal may reach a high point with rich and peppery Chettinad chicken curry. Matched with curry leaf-studded lemon rice, it's a match made in heaven.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7553;Shabushabu Mayumon;USA;New York;115 Division St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7144011;-73.9921026;36;false;false;Japanese, Shabu-shabu;This intimate, 10-seat counter in LES offers a well-orchestrated adaptation of classic Japanese shabu shabu. Quiet and confident, the cooks here literally “swish swish” numerous cuts of prime pork belly, A5 Miyazaki wagyu, and American wagyu in boiling broth before finishing them in sauces like sweet soy, pungent, peppery ponzu and nutty miso. The sheer quantity (and quality) of wagyu alone is impressive and never once feels heavy or overwhelming thanks to lighter pairings like lettuce or mushrooms. At times, Spanish and Italian influences make their way into this tasting menu, but the results are largely convincing. Everything happens at the counter, and the team works to meet your pacing, whether that’s a rapid dinner or a leisurely journey.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7554;Southern Table;USA;Pleasantville;39 Marble Ave., Pleasantville, 10570, USA;41.1320052;-73.7914087;91;false;false;Southern, American;Polished concrete floors, steel chairs and whitewashed brick walls emblazoned with animal silhouettes set a modern country look, and the open kitchen’s cacophony is part of the fun. Southern Table is the sort of place that's just right for serving a crowd, so come one and come all to enjoy a menu littered with tasty renditions of Southern classics. Fried green tomatoes, Mama's Cornbread, and shrimp jambalaya are all good bets. Top the meal off with the crispy buttermilk chicken sandwich loaded with toppings like bacon and melting cheese and served with seasoned fries. Bourbon-glazed donuts or key lime cheesecake keep with the theme at dessert.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7555;El Fish Marisqueria;USA;New York;155 Amsterdam Ave., New York, 10023, USA;40.7752661;-73.9838274;63;true;false;Mexican, Seafood;Don't let the name fool you—this is not your average seafood shack. Instead, this Upper West Side restaurant invites guests to settle in to a warm, modern and chic setting complete with a bar that lures locals who sip on cocktails and refreshing zero-proof drinks. Quality seafood is the basis of the flavor-packed dishes here, and while some of the plates feature an Asian flair, choose from the Para Empezar section for a proper marisqueria-style seafood feast. First up is the clam chowder with strips of tortillas and crisp pork rind chicharron in a smoky tomato-chile guajillo. Then, salmon skewers are slicked with a sweet-smoky riff on kung pao sauce for an unexpectedly flavorful dish. Didn't snag a reservation? The raw bar is ideal for walk-ins.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7556;Madre;USA;Brooklyn;214 Franklin St., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7331171;-73.9578699;28;true;false;Contemporary, American;Madre sits at the base of the boutique Franklin Guest House, where industrial elements meet modern elegance. Make your way past stunning carved doors to arrive at the hotel—the restaurant has a separate entrance. Here, diners will find it hard to resist the kitchen team's sensational and contemporary cooking. Dishes that take center stage in this multi-level space include jalepeño cornbread madelines with a housemade whipped honey butter, or tender octopus plated with romesco, green chorizo, nopales and escabeche for a plate that straddles the Mediterranean and Latin America. From there, indulge in couscous with chickpeas, harissa, red peppers and a smoked onion broth. Pot de crème with Mast Brothers chocolate and Maldon sea salt is worth your undivided attention.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7557;Peak;USA;New York;30 Hudson Yards, New York, 10001, USA;40.7541526;-74.0010367;76;false;false;Contemporary;Pop quiz time. Where is the highest outdoor observatory deck in the western hemisphere? If you guessed The Edge at Hudson Yards, you win. And your prize? Dinner at Peak, the next-door restaurant with jaw-dropping views over lower Manhattan and New Jersey. This spot stands above the competition in this high-end complex, and while the crowd of mostly tourists and business types is largely here for those views, the food is far from a concession. Kick things off with dishes like the hiramasa topped with Kirby cucumber and watermelon radish before a skin-on roasted chicken with roasted kabocha squash and kale pesto. Unsurprisingly, the prices skew high.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
7558;Vert Frais;USA;Queens;43-10 Crescent St., Queens, 11101, USA;40.7488818;-73.9423379;93;false;true;Japanese;This sunny, white-walled café in Long Island City does not look like a serious restaurant. It looks like the kind of place where you’d grab a coffee with friends or pull out your laptop at a communal table. But with the backing of Kanoyama’s long-standing chef, the kitchen is not to be underestimated. The classic shio ramen is a must, the broth fragrant and deep with smoky, charred slices of cha-shu and crunchy bamboo shoots. Thin slivers of sushi-grade salmon laced over a mound of warm rice with scallions and topped with poppy ikura are also a source of easy comfort. Dessert is all but bound to set social media feeds on fire: Fluffy, tall, jiggly souffle pancakes that are light as air, none too sweet, and impossible not to finish in a few big bites.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
7559;L’abeille à Côté;USA;New York;412 Greenwich St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7218147;-74.0099643;17;true;true;French, Asian;This jewel box of a restaurant is something of a rarity, as small dining rooms with even smaller menus are harder and harder to come by these days. To describe this as a bistro or remotely casual makes sense only in comparison to its next-door, tasting-menu-only sibling. Otherwise, this is a refined operation with handsome wood floors and tables, marble finishes, and a French-Japanese cooking style that makes the most of high-quality product. Think croquettes but filled with plump lobster meat or risotto finished with a runny Jidori egg and shaved white truffles. Nothing here is inexpensive or everyday, but for those who appreciate intimacy, privacy, and quality, it is a welcome addition to the neighborhood.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7560;Naro;USA;New York;610 Fifth Ave., New York, 10012, USA;40.7581487;-73.9778133;56;true;false;Korean;The group behind Atomix and Atoboy continue to show no signs of slowing down with their latest opening in bustling Rockefeller Center. Named after South Korea’s first successful rocket to space, the restaurant offers a more traditional view of Korean cuisine dating back to the Joseon dynasty. Choose between two tasting menus, one of which is vegetarian, and expect familiar dishes like mandu, bibimbap and shrimp pancake to be reimagined and refined, usually with mild-mannered flavors and always with high-quality ingredients. The boisterous room itself is enclosed in glass, in full view of people milling around the concourse, and is a rather sterile mix of white walls, white tablecloths, white booths and hard warehouse floors.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7561;Asian Jewels;USA;Queens;133-30 39th Ave., Queens, 11354, USA;40.7592586;-73.8332919;38;false;true;Chinese, Dim Sum;Large banquet halls are a rare breed these days, but this Flushing mainstay has endured the test of time. This veteran resident of 39th Avenue is outfitted with oversized round tables, bamboo plants and ornate chandeliers. Before you’ve even had a chance to sit down, a host of carts approach. Questions fly and lids are removed. In a blur, the likes of steamed shumai packed with pork and shrimp, spareribs with rice starch and black beans, chicken and ham wrapped in yuba, and poached jellyfish with scallions and sesame crowd your table. You may or may not see a menu – and you may not even need one. Most don’t. Servers crisscross the room, and everyone tends to everything all at once. Weekends are especially frenetic, so arrive early to score a seat.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7562;Tamarind;USA;New York;99 Hudson St., New York, 10013, USA;40.719215;-74.008865;49;false;true;Indian;Building Tamarind cost a cool five million, and it shows—every inch of this soaring space oozes with grandeur. With its classic TriBeCa edifice and gorgeous marble bar (an ideal perch for post-work indulgence), the glass-fronted behemoth draws a posh crowd of Wall Streeters and well-heeled locals.Most impressive of all is the sleek display kitchen, outfitted with a gleaming tandoor that turns out exceptional Mughlai food like sirkha gosht (lamb in a fiery chili and coriander chutney). Malai halibut, roasted then blanketed in a coconut-ginger sauce with toasted cumin seeds, is a standout. While service is mediocre at best and the kitchen may fall behind at peak times, mains like kolambi pola (prawns in a coconut-and-chili curry) make up for any gaffes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7563;abcV;USA;New York;38 E. 19th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7381964;-73.9894202;91;false;true;Vegetarian, Contemporary;Tucked inside ABC Carpet & Home, this restaurant offers elevated vegetarian food in a beautiful, minimalist space. A clean aesthetic dominates the space, with mismatched chandeliers and bursts of bright colors. An open kitchen, takeout counter and bar lend a buzzy energy to the space.The menu is detailed and clever, offering vibrant dishes for breakfast, lunch and brunch. There must be bread, as in the einkorn and antebellum grits sourdough focaccia served with gently roasted grapes, cultured hazelnut butter, concord jelly and Tropea onion confit. Dosas delight with their blend of crunchy-chewy savoriness. Then, vegetables, whether cauliflower veiled in tahini or smoky tandoori white yam, take center stage. Vegan chocolate cake is decadence on a plate.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7565;Claro;USA;Brooklyn;284 Third Ave., Brooklyn, 11215, USA;40.677395;-73.98615;93;false;false;Mexican;The mood is warm and boisterous at this vibrant spot for Oaxacan cuisine. A smattering of tables, bar counter and wood-fired oven lend a neighborhood feel. The menu changes frequently to reflect the seasons and ranges from traditional dishes to creative riffs on the classics. Masa is one of the cornerstones of the kitchen, stone ground in house from Oaxacan criollo corn and hand shaped into diverse specialties ranging from tortillas and tlayudas to memelas, finished on a wood-fired comal. A dizzying variety of mezcal is on offer, including suggested pairings for each course.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7566;Marea;USA;New York;240 Central Park South, New York, 10019, USA;40.767619;-73.9810681;99;true;true;Seafood, Italian;Ritzy and elegant, Marea couldn’t ask for a better home than Central Park South. This airy dining room, dressed to the nines with Indonesian rosewood, is abuzz with power crowds. It's hard to beat this scene but the food is appealing in its own right. The focus of this Italian cuisine is seafood and offers an array of raw fish and crudo such as diced branzino that is presented with chopped pistachio and flecks of crispy garlic and shallot.Finely made pastas include casarecce with pieces of lump crab, uni puree, and tomato. Finish with a beautifully made dessert like the blueberry filled meringa with whipped white chocolate;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7567;Manhatta;USA;New York;28 Liberty St., New York, 10005, USA;40.7081016;-74.0087716;29;false;false;Contemporary, American;Great views and good food rarely go hand in hand, but this stylish spot breaks that trend. Set in an iconic skyscraper and set some 60 floors up with Manhattan laid out before you, these views truly do not disappoint. The best seats in the house are those closest to the windows, though those with a view of the open kitchen are a close second. Chef Justin Bogle and his team have injected new life into the kitchen with global ingredients and ambitiously creative compositions that make excellent use of seasonal ingredients. Oysters Manhatta with uni and Champagne sabayon is a luxurious start, while the skin-on, seared, dry-aged duck with persimmon, endive and a side of white Japanese sweet potato puree is a standout.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7568;Goosefeather;USA;Tarrytown;49 E. Sunnyside Ln., Tarrytown, 10591, USA;41.04811;-73.85851;29;true;true;Cantonese, Asian;This destination-worthy dining room is coveted for its idyllic setting of sprawling estate grounds with a carriage house, cottage, and two historic, freshly minted mansions. Nestled within these luxurious surrounds is Goosefeather, where guests are greeted by well-appointed nooks, all blending old-fashioned charm with new-world elements.The menu is surprisingly unforgettable as conceived by Dale Talde. Known for his craft with Hong Kong-style food, the talented chef infuses these staples with a modern, seasonal twist. Kung pao chicken wings with a buttermilk dill ranch dip gives a familiar favorite a new lease on life. Bao, with a salty-sweet crispy shrimp filling mixed with cool daikon and cabbage, is an absolute must.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7570;Seppe Pizza Bar;USA;Staten Island;3 Navy Pier Ct., Staten Island, 10304, USA;40.6294612;-74.0740369;15;true;true;Pizza;From the breezes blowing off the water to the natural light flooding its contemporary-chic space, this Navy Pier dining retreat is a breath of fresh air.First things first—peruse the cocktail menu, where savory and spicy drinks are a welcome alternative to too-sweet swizzles. Order a house spritz or a Negroni, then settle in to review the sprawling menu. Start with one of their fantastic pizzas with beautiful crispy bottoms, such as the unusually delicious Morty pizza, finished with a layer of pistachio-based pesto with mozzarella, and garnished with burrata and slices of mortadella. And while there are so many shareable plates, be sure to save room for their baked wings with a perfect char, or decadent pastas, like the cacio e pepe, both of which deliver on flavor.;Air conditioning;[]
7571;Seoul Salon;USA;New York;28 W. 33rd St., New York, 10001, USA;40.7484004;-73.9866175;40;false;false;Korean, Contemporary;In what feels like an adult arcade, this place in Koreatown has warehouse floors, gunmetal grey finishes and neon accents. From the same group that gave us Atomix, the food here is all fun and games, a mishmash of influences pitting Korean rice cakes with basil and stracciatella or a block of cheese with shrimp fried in a thin batter. Maybe the dish that says it all is the whimsical mala pork belly, which is both puzzling to behold but also undeniably delicious. Such savory cooking is in the service of a talented bar that knows how to combine, say, peanut butter cachaça and passionfruit. At the close of the meal, banana shaved ice with banana cream, hazelnuts and orange zest makes for a brilliantly refreshing finale.;Air conditioning;[]
7573;J.G. Melon;USA;New York;1291 Third Ave., New York, 10021, USA;40.77117;-73.95929;30;false;true;American;Posterity will remember J.G. Melon as a coveted NY institution. Make your way into this 1920's structure, marked by a neon sign and set upon a cozy corner, where the timeless vibe, telltale green-and-white checked tablecloth, and cheery staff make up most of its allure. Drinks are steadily churned out at a dark wood bar, so arrive early to avoid the crowds.The draw at this multigenerational saloon is certainly the burger and while everyone comes for it, the cooking is pleasing all around, with items like the chili cup filled to the brim with savory meat chili and topped with onions and cheese, or the turkey club sandwich.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Terrace;[]
7574;Acru;USA;New York;79 MacDougal St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7288322;-74.0016231;29;false;true;Contemporary;Acru is a fresh-faced venture tucked along the warren of Greenwich Village’s crowded streets. The slender bistro is intimate and charming with a small bar and clutch of wood tables in a room appointed with exposed brick and taupe walls.The pedigree of this team is impressive, with Atomix's Junghyun and Ellia Park behind the scenes while Chef Daniel Garwood leads the charge in the kitchen. The prix fixe menu offers rare value and inspired cuisine. It's early days, but items like sea trout tartare dressed with cabbage granita and slow-roasted cherry tomatoes, or roasted carrot soup poured over monkfish liver custard, squid noodles, and toasted grains, indicate a bright future for this establishment.;;[]
7575;Cafe Mado;USA;Brooklyn;791 Washington Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.6728185;-73.962637;65;true;false;American Contemporary;At first glance, it may seem like your typical neighborhood all-day café, but there’s more than meets the eye at Café Mado from Chef/owner Nico Russell. This Prospect Heights café bustles with a coffee shop up front and a skylit atrium with a small bar and dining room. It is here where they sell house-baked bread, breakfast sandwiches, elegant small plates, and handmade pasta by day before shifting to a more refined dinner service by night. Begin with pissaladière, a warm, round loaf topped with anchovies, caramelized red onions, and olive spread or kick things off with a seasonal small plate like summer melon with lime granita and habanada before tucking into a plate of pasta, like pici with pesto Genovese.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7576;Le Veau d'Or;USA;New York;129 E. 60th St., New York, 10022, USA;40.7631842;-73.9681554;58;true;false;French;Originally established in 1937 and steeped in history, this charming bistro is intimate in scale and rocks a decidedly throwback look. Dark wood, a liberal use of red, and small closely set tables draped with linens produce a cozy yet sexy ambience that has diners swooning.The team of Lee Hanson and Riad Nasr, the founding chefs of Balthazar and Minetta Tavern, have ushered in a new era at Le Veau d'Or which offers a prix-fixe menu reverential to classic French cuisine. Pâté en croûte is among the greatest hits, as is the golden-roasted poulet à l'estragon with an unapologetically buttery sauce flecked with tarragon. A small salad arrives after the entree to cleanse the palate, paving the way for sweets, such as a warm gratin au chocolat.;Air conditioning;[]
7577;Bangkok Supper Club;USA;New York;641 Hudson St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7390045;-74.0055465;74;true;true;Thai;This spot with Chef Max Wittawat at the helm is very chic and on trend with a contemporary Thai menu pulling from family recipes while adding a touch of refinement. The product quality and execution are exacting, and even dishes that seem simple, as in the fiery scallop ceviche with watermelon chili granita, are impactful and play on dramatic contrasts. The deep-fried pork cheeks served sliced over savory garlic-baked rice are highly recommended. Loaded with flavor, each bite alternates between the sweet-tender pork and the savory-delicious rice. For dessert, cubes of a coconut chiffon cake topped with a pandan custard are nestled inside a young coconut. A creative cocktail menu showcases as much care as the food.;Air conditioning;[]
7578;Cadence;USA;New York;111 E. 7th St., New York, 10009, USA;40.7265622;-73.984472;78;false;false;Vegan, Southern;Southern cuisine and soul food have always been good, but good for you? Enter Chef Shenarri Freeman, who is remaking the classics with a vegan and plant-based twist at Cadence. The tiny space packs considerable charm but the kitchen is the one that shines, focusing on building flavors and creating dishes with seasonal vegetables rather than alternatives posing as meat. It's one creative riff after another. Collard green wraps are filled with succotash and set in an umami-rich chickpea miso broth. Then, two large oyster mushrooms are fried and tossed in a buffalo sauce, served over a Belgian waffle and sided by lavender maple syrup for a take on chicken and waffles that's so good it's almost blasphemous.The wine list spotlights labels from Black-owned wineries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7579;Koloman;USA;New York;16 W. 29th St., New York, 10001, USA;40.7458323;-73.9881622;34;false;true;Contemporary, European;The Ace Hotel's Koloman has a timeless appeal. A beautiful backlit bar welcomes you before enter the dining room, set with antique mirrors and plush banquettes. Tables with views of the semi-open kitchen are the most in demand. It's old world-meets-new on the menu, where Chef Markus Glocker and his team take French and Viennese classics and render them with modern sophistication. Snapper crudo with spicy citrus is a bright opener before moving on to a textbook soufflé in all of its pillowy perfection sided by mushroom jam. Celery root tartare is a clever take on tradition using vegetables that have been given a boost from Pommery mustard.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
7582;Forsythia;USA;New York;9 Stanton St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7225817;-73.9924978;21;true;false;Italian;This intimate, little nook in Lower East Side is all about pasta. Set menus clock in at just under $100 per person and begin with warm, pillow-like slices of fresh-baked focaccia. The excellent fried cacio pepe risotto suppli is a must, but seasonal preparations can be as satisfying as they are generously portioned. Recent highlights include fried sweet potatoes with stracciatella and chili oil or chestnut soup with porcini. From here, guests choose two different pastas to close out the savory portion of the meal. Truly, Chef Jacob Siwak’s agnolotti packed with short rib and tossed in butter has few equals, and his carbonara never disappoints either. All pastas are made in-house, and aspiring home cooks can sign up for weekly classes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7584;Place des Fêtes;USA;Brooklyn;212 Greene Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.6869589;-73.9628508;80;false;false;Contemporary;Wine bars are rarely known for their food, and sometimes we have to make the most out of a small bowl of popcorn. Thankfully, compromise isn’t on the table at this popular Clinton Hill hangout, courtesy of the talented team behind Oxalis. This casual second act cooks as great as it pours, and both the food and the wines lean Spanish. Simple seafood preparations, thick blocks of grilled toast and thoughtful vegetable courses form the heart of the menu. Plates run small, so consider doubling up if you’re with a group. Bartenders, meanwhile, favor zippy, natural wines from small producers. Both the bar and the open kitchen act as anchors in this cozy space, which ripples with energy and fills up quickly.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
7585;Llama Inn;USA;Brooklyn;50 Withers St., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.716739;-73.950499;18;false;false;Peruvian, Fusion;Upbeat, modern and cool, Llama Inn pays respect to all styles of Peruvian cooking but with the technical flair of Chef Erik Ramirez who has trained in New York’s top restaurants. The result is always fresh, fun and spontaneous cuisine that elevates Peruvian food. Begin your meal with one of the variations of ceviche, ranging from seafood to vegetarian styles. The asparagus is punctuated with a bracing potato leek leche de tigre. Next up is the crispy and cheesy jalapeño tequenos. The pork collar escabeche rounds out the meal or if you're eating with a crowd go for the decadant lomo saltado. Finish with a slice of their key lime pie.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7586;Sushi Yasuda;USA;New York;204 E. 43rd St., New York, 10017, USA;40.75108;-73.97364;35;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;There is a spartan aura to this sushiya, where honey-toned wood and bamboo slats are by far the warmest decorative feature. They require confirmation and punctuality, but to culinary diehards, this is just the cost of admission.The counter is where the action happens. An experience here depends entirely on the itamae in front of you, as their signature style will guide your meal. For the most part, their omakase lives up to the hype by ignoring new trends and sticking to classically assembled sushi. Each item is handled with care, highlighting their robust flavor. Imagine the likes of cherrystone clam, bluefin tuna and sayori with shiso. Nigiri, like Maine and Japanese uni tastings, showcase the subtle differences in these flavorful bites.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7588;Secchu Yokota;USA;New York;199 E. 3rd St., New York, 10009, USA;40.7227804;-73.9831107;24;true;false;Japanese, Tempura;This spot flies under the radar somewhat, and that’s just the way their loyal fan base likes it. Those who understand the fine art of tempura know how pristine the quality is here, where diners are treated to a mouthwatering omakase featuring succulent red shrimp, Japanese eggplant, and lightly battered unagi. You probably won’t need it, but lemon, wasabi salt and seaweed salt are provided as enhancements. The man to thank for these treats is Chef Yokota, who takes his craft (and business) seriously, putting his clients first. Dining here is an intimate and deeply personal experience that highlights ingredients sourced mostly from Japan. As a bonus, his tempura is typically bookended by unique dishes that display his French culinary training.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7590;Lakruwana;USA;Staten Island;668 Bay St., Staten Island, 10304, USA;40.625676;-74.0751404;88;true;false;Sri Lankan;Prepare for a sensory overload the moment you set foot into Lakruwana—the Sri Lankan hot spot is covered from floor-to-ceiling in murals, sculptures, flags, and more. The kaleidoscope of textures and colors is a welcome sight, as is the energetic owner who drifts from table to table.Street food takes center stage here, where you a variety of traditional dishes hit the mark. Don't miss the kottu roti, a stir-fried dish with godamba roti, chicken, vegetables and chicken curry or the traditional hoppers, with its bowl-shaped crepe served with a yellow fish curry. The oversized platter is ideal for sharing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7591;Don Antonio by Starita;USA;New York;309 W. 50th St., New York, 10019, USA;40.762607;-73.9866896;87;false;true;Pizza;The namesake outpost is located in Naples and has been running strong since 1901. Meanwhile in Midtown, Don Antonio by Starita has been slinging authentic Neapolitan-style, woodfired pizza since 2012, thanks to Don's daughter, Giorgia Caporuscio, who learned the family craft and took over the family business here. This kitchen's signature is the Montanara Starita—a lightly fried pizza laced with house-made tomato sauce, smoked mozzarella, and basil, then finished in the wood-fired oven. But really, who could stop there with treasures like the salsiccia e friarielli pizza with fennel sausage or the delicious frittatine, where chopped spaghetti pieces and ham are blended with Buffalo mozzarella, breaded, and fried to a golden crisp.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7592;Ma•dé;USA;New York;22 Spring St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7215302;-73.995057;31;false;true;South East Asian, Seafood;This comforting charmer honors the communal dining traditions of Indonesia’s West Sumatra. Thick, knotted ropes hang overhead in a narrow, intimate room fit with white brick and a tiled wall that nearly looks like white seashells. Chef Cedric Vongerichten delivers a verifiable feast served in little bowls and plates that fill every inch of space on the table. With the exception of your entrée, there are no choices to make for this easy prix fix. After a quick amuse, the rest of the meal lands at the same time, allowing diners to bounce between fluke sashimi dressed in a light sambal hijau, crispy sweetbreads sitting in a gulai curry, and egg balado with Thai basil. Pickles, garlic rice, and crisp tapioca crackers also dot the table.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7594;Claud;USA;New York;90 E. 10th St., New York, 10003, USA;40.7307844;-73.9894199;65;false;true;Contemporary;Owned by Chase Sinzer, who pours the wine, and Chef Joshua Pinsky, who mans the stoves, Claud is a sleek and stylish place a few steps below street level. Inside, it's whitewashed brick meets dark charcoal tiled floors complete with snug seating and an open kitchen at the back. A shared plates style informs the menu, and the cooking is ingredient-focused and values substance over style. Begin with the red shrimp, which arrive sizzling with garlic and olive oil. Main dishes, like the pork chop with smoked onion jus and a classic roasted chicken, are hearty and especially satisfying. Complete your meal with a decadent six-layer Devil's food cake that says it's "for two" but we won't blame you if you eat the whole thing yourself. Reservations are often a challenge, but the bar is always a good option.;Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list;[]
7595;Wenwen;USA;Brooklyn;1025 Manhattan Ave., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.733975;-73.9549668;51;false;true;Taiwanese, Asian;Chef Eric Sze and partner Andy Chuang bring the vibrant flavors of Taiwanese cooking to Greenpoint with Wenwen. The façade is unmissable with its tall and narrow-wood framed windows allowing for a full view of the clean, airy interior. Menu highlights include the celtuce salad with mouth-numbing Sichuan pepper and tart red vinegar, and a robust and aromatic dish water spinach tossed in the wok. Skip the much-hyped fried chicken for the whole striped bass, stuffed with fish paste and glistening in a pool of black sugar-yuzu vinaigrette, red vinegar and fermented black beans.  Treat yourself to black sesame-flavored tangyuan paired with vanilla ice cream, cilantro and powdered peanut butter for a refreshing closer.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7596;Reverence;USA;New York;2592 Frederick Douglass Blvd., New York, 10030, USA;40.8186284;-73.9449974;99;false;false;Contemporary;Proudly Californian, Chef Russell Jackson switched coasts and commands Reverence, set along Harlem's historic stretch of Strivers' Row. The chef weaves his love of California, seasonality, and fermentation into an intriguing tasting menu that features an abundance of local produce. Like the weather, the menu changes quickly but may include the likes of Texas-style toast wrapped in fig leaf with tofu and farmers cheese and a beet reduction. Then, sauteed cabbage and white beans in a luscious sauce is served with a half loaf of bread for soaking up every last bit. Finally, homemade cookies are just the treat you need to end the evening.;;[]
7597;Tadhanà;USA;New York;151 Allen St., New York, 10002, USA;40.7208698;-73.9898801;61;true;true;Filipino, Contemporary;From serving as the private chef to the royal family of the United Arab Emirates to appearances on TV, Chef Frances Tariga has seemingly done it all—except have her own restaurant. Now she's done that too, showcasing a multicourse tasting menu of regional Filipino cuisine with a reimagined and refined touch. Follow along on a regional tour of the 7,000-island archipelago, tasting rice from the mountain region and kinilaw from the central Visayas that appears traditional but is elevated by smoking raw yellowtail, aromatics, and aged coconut vinegar in a covered bowl. A chicken wing stuffed with annatto-seasoned ground meat is another winning dish, as is the grilled pork belly with banana ketchup glaze.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle;[]
7598;Ariari;USA;New York;119 1st Ave., New York, 10003, USA;40.7272279;-73.985779;60;false;true;Korean, Regional Cuisine;This Korean spot has a cool, vintage vibe that comes complete with wood paneling and banquette seating. Framed artwork highlights a maritime theme which comes as no surprise since this contemporary, shared plates-style menu zeroes in on the seaport city of Busan. Seafood specialties span every section and even include a bibimbap made with uni cream. Be sure to try the scallop DIY gimbap, with thinly sliced raw scallops served alongside squid jeotgal, scallion mayo, apple kimchi and crispy gim/seaweed squares for assembling. Corn crème brûlée mixed with shaved white chocolate is a creative take on the classic, with a savory-meets-sweet appeal. Cocktails are definitely worthy of a sip.;Air conditioning;[]
7599;Tatiana;USA;New York;10 Lincoln Center Plz., New York, 10023, USA;40.7715357;-73.9840951;57;false;true;Fusion, American;There's pre-theater dining, and then there's Tatiana. Its Lincoln Center location is a natural choice for Philharmonic ticket holders, but it's worthy of applause in its own right. Its stunning interior, crafted by Modellus Novus, swings to a stylish beat courtesy of its good looks and even better looking crowd. Chef Kwame Onwuachi draws on his West African roots and the flavors of his childhood in the Bronx and elsewhere on this menu with signature dishes like egusi dumplings, filled with crab and sea bass in a brick red sauce. The centerpiece—oxtail—arrives in a large pot with two glistening pieces resting in a thick sauce. Marinated for more than a day, and served with Thumbelina carrots and chayote squash along with rice and peas, it's a proper feast.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
7600;Casa Ora;USA;Brooklyn;148 Meserole St., Brooklyn, 11206, USA;40.7079151;-73.9437907;28;false;false;Venezuelan, Latin American;Venezuela-born chef Isbelis Diaz and her son, Ivo Diaz, share their vibrant cuisine with the Big Apple. The passionate and charming staff busy themselves guiding hungry guests through a cluster of explosively flavorful dishes served on beautiful pieces crafted by local Venezuelan artisan, Victor Serrano. Empanadas are a favorite, especially when stuffed with Guyanés queso. Asado negro, a 48-hour braised short rib in burnt papelón, is positively velvety. Other winning dishes include arepitas, bollitos pelones and mandocas, hand-rolled, tear-shaped fritters made from ripe plantain and yellow corn and hit with a gentle hint of anise for a sweet and savory blend.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7601;Il Fiorista;USA;New York;17 W. 26th St., New York, 10010, USA;40.7440247;-73.9893729;46;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Owners Alessandra and Mario De Benedetti's bright, airy dining room doubles as a flower shop, and its vivid, spring-like décor feels like stepping into a magazine cover. But these gorgeous blooms serve a third, even more exciting, role here, making their way into cocktails and dishes crafted with edible flowers like nasturtium blossoms and hibiscus petals. (They're also crafting a collection of spices, salts and sugars).The results are deliciously unique. Graze on a charcuterie plate or an assortment of small dishes like the thinly sliced and delicately fried lotus root dusted with pine pollen. Next, house-made pasta is a must, especially the campanelle tossed in a cream-based white Bolognese sauce, or opt for the broiled Alaskan salmon on a bed of tossed braised fennel and roasted cauliflower.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7602;Don Angie;USA;New York;103 Greenwich Ave., New York, 10014, USA;40.7377741;-74.0019745;33;true;false;Italian, American;This darling of a dining room is designed with elegant blue-gray leather banquettes, bentwood chairs, and a dark checkerboard floor. Potted plants, moody lighting, and a rustic bar with brass accents make it a dream-worthy refuge for a romantic tête-à-tête. Married couple, Angie Rito and Scott Tacinelli, are the brains behind this venture, where the team takes risks that result in highly creative and enriching cuisine.While the menu feels like an American story as told through an Italian lens, Asian elements also make guest appearances as in the spicy pepperoni fried rice gussied-up with tender grilled calamari. Playful aptly describes the combination of spicy veal tartare and tuna carpaccio. Pastas are similarly prolific, like the paprika-tinted sorpresine with smoked mussels or sourdough pasta in a 'nduja sauce with mezcal-braised chicken. Pesce alla griglia in a clam broth and Sicilian scallop crudo speak of bold flavors and polished methods.Desserts, such as the fior di latte mochi with golden Taggiasca olive oil or black cocoa tiramisu garnished with feuilletine, are just the icing on the cake. Go for over-the-top glee with a sip of house-made root beer amaro.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7603;Moody Tongue Sushi;USA;New York;150 W. 10th St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7344702;-74.0011346;19;true;false;Sushi, Contemporary;Push open a heavy, carved black-painted wood door to this space brimming with old world charm and modern touches. Moody Tongue Sushi is from the folks behind Moody Tongue Brewing in Chicago, albeit with Hiromi Iwakiri's sushi taking center stage. There is an à la carte menu, but the way to go is their nigiri sets creatively paired with beer. Some of the standouts include ora king salmon paired with the Sour Watermelon Saison and madai with orange zest matched with Orange Blossom Blonde. Oak Barrel Aged Flanders Red Ale is paired with sweet jumbo shrimp topped with Hokkaido uni and a dot of caviar for an impressive duo. There are full cocktail and wine lists, but with great beers on tap, why bother? The Shaved Black Truffle Rice Lager is an exclusive, and well worth the price tag.;Air conditioning;[]
7604;Hav & Mar;USA;New York;245 Eleventh Ave., New York, 10001, USA;40.7509279;-74.0057216;99;true;true;Ethiopian, Fusion;How do you share your melting pot heritage without pandering? Just ask Chefs Marcus Samuelsson and Fariyal Abdullahi, the brains behind Hav & Mar. This modern spot pays homage to Samuelsson's Ethiopian and Swedish roots with a seamless and heartfelt approach. The menu pulls from both cultures and their staple ingredients. Start with the bread basket, an impressive collection of lentil roti, oat porridge crisp and teff biscuit. Few dishes represent this cultural collision better than the Swediopian, a berbere-cured salmon shingled between slices of Granny Smith apple, dressed with mustard seed caviar and buckthorn and finished with injera chips. Corn-wrapped snapper served with a bright salsa verde and crispy coconut rice is a can't-miss main.;Air conditioning;[]
7605;Ito;USA;New York;75 Barclay St., New York, 10007, USA;40.7129963;-74.0099765;69;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Chef/owners Masashi Ito and Kevin Kim have no interest in a solemn sushi temple, and in the shadow of One World Trade, their 14-seat counter is full-on revelry. Excellent quality fish, much of it flown in from Japan, deep knife cuts and potent saucing define the nigiri. And whereas some chefs save all of their fireworks for the nigiri progression, appetizers like kampachi with yuzu chive oil and desserts like strawberry panna cotta are compelling bookends. The crowd skews young, leans on whiskey and sake, and, by the meal’s end, are already looking forward to their next reservation, which they booked long before they first walked in.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7606;Altro Paradiso;USA;New York;234 Spring St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7254751;-74.0045848;23;false;true;Italian;Often packed and quintessentially SoHo, this beloved charmer from Chef Ignacio Mattos is as welcoming as ever. The setting is comfortably stylish with its high ceilings, amber hues, and handsome woodwork accented with wine bottles all over. Far from predictable, the menu is a thoughtful, creative curation based on the seasons and on regional specialties. Pastas like the strozzapreti with Meyer lemon or the capellini with tuna and Calabrian chili are made in-house and rotate frequently. Entrees like the roasted half chicken or bronzed Milanese feed groups with ease. Another house specialty? The salads. From winter citrus topped with Formaggio di Fossa to abundant chicories spiked with a sharp vinaigrette, they are worthy complements to any meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7607;Van Đa;USA;New York;234 E. 4th St., New York, 10009, USA;40.7233393;-73.9828147;58;false;false;Vietnamese, Modern Cuisine;Making the point that Vietnamese food is more than just cold banh mi and big bowls of pho, this elegant spot in the East Village celebrates other specialties across the country. Go heavy on starters from the royal city of Hue like shrimp and pork tapioca dumplings wrapped in banana leaves and the crispy turmeric rice pancakes with coconut cream and herbs. Hanoi’s stir-fried pho noodles with trumpet mushrooms benefits from a good lashing of tableside hot sauce. And finally, from Saigon, shaking beef with crispy smashed potatoes and rice is a comforting classic. An attractive bar slinging creative cocktails upstairs is another distinguished addition, as well as a fantastic downstairs dining room that oozes intimacy and comfort.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7608;Kubeh;USA;New York;464 Sixth Ave., New York, 10011, USA;40.73553;-73.998116;50;false;true;Middle Eastern;Chef/owner Melanie Shurka traveled to Israel to learn the art of making kubeh (dumplings) from the immigrant women of Kurdish, Iranian and Syrian descent. Taste the results of her education in this lovely contemporary respite, where old-world heirlooms grace the walls. Though its namesake dish is often difficult to find stateside, they deliver a heartfelt rendition of hand-rolled kubeh filled with meat or mushrooms here. Other can't-miss dishes include kuku sabzi, a classic Persian herb and leek frittata, and tahini-drizzled roasted eggplant. For dessert, there's always baklava, but the warm, gluten-free brownie with whipped cream and a scoop of Turkish coffee ice cream enhanced with cardamom is the winner.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7609;Le B;USA;New York;283 W. 12th St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7376084;-74.0039699;69;true;false;Classic French, Asian;Chef Angie Mar presents a celebration of haute French cuisine married with her Chinese heritage in this luxurious Greenwich Village location. The intimate and opulent space glimmers in sapphire hues and velvet banquettes, while white tablecloths and jacketed staff set the tone for a celebratory night out or an intimate date. Chef Mar weaves together reverence and personality in dishes such as terrine of pork, duck, and kumquat confit. The "rabbit drowned in wine" is an unctuous pasta dish enriched with bone marrow. Lamb chops Roy or halibut and Dover sole soufflé anchor the meal. End with crêpesSuzette, set aflame tableside. Additionally, some of Chef Mar's hits from the past reappear, as in the 45-day aged burger, only available at the bar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7610;Foul Witch;USA;New York;15 Avenue A, New York, 10009, USA;40.7228423;-73.9860619;39;true;true;Contemporary;More fair than foul, this East Village spot is from the same folks behind the late Blanca and Roberta's. From the open kitchen and wood-burning oven to the exposed brick and glass chandeliers, this restaurant has a cozy charm. Its look may lean vintage, but its menu skews contemporary. The fire and ice dish, with house-made 'nduja topped with stracciatella and served with toasted bread bears an Italian influence, while roasted mushrooms in a rutabaga-based broth is soul satisfying. Pastas, like veal agnolotti with amaretto or spacatelli with aged squab, are always a hit. And for dessert, the sake lees cake with cubes of tender yet crispy cake finished with honeycomb and clotted cream is the stuff of sweet dreams.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7611;Apropos Restaurant at The Abbey Inn;USA;Peekskill;900 Fort Hill Rd., Peekskill, 10566, USA;41.2925652;-73.9281862;69;false;false;American, Contemporary;The Sisters of Saint Mary's certainly didn't eat like this, but if you take a one-hour train ride from Grand Central to Peekskill's Apropros Restaurant at The Abbey Inn, you will. This 120-year-old abbey perched high above the Hudson River has been painstakingly restored and transformed into a lovely inn and restaurant. The grounds, and the views, are worth the trip alone but the wine cellar boasting an impressive collection and the farm-to-table kitchen are equally rewarding. The menu leans traditional, with dishes ranging from rich lamb ragù atop tangles of thick pappardelle to grilled petite filet of beef finished with a textbook green peppercorn sauce. Pannacotta flavored with moscato and finished with an apricot and chili preserve is a lovely send-off.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7613;L'inizio;USA;Ardsley;698 Saw Mill River Rd., Ardsley, 10502, USA;41.0122835;-73.8474191;28;true;true;Italian, Italian-American;Husband and wife team, Scott and Pastry Chef Heather Fratangelo, are the brains behind this lovely Italian spot. Simple and demure from the outside, there's something special about this dining room that's perceptible instantly upon entry. Smiling servers guide you to a simple yet comfortable table, framed by bistro seats. Bright unframed paintings adorn the walls, while shelves are lined with canning jars.The menu's chosen language may be Italian but it never strays too far from its American roots. Start with a summer salad of cantaloupe, stone fruit and feta, before indulging in such fine pastas as bucatini with cherry tomatoes, roasted garlic and Parmigiana. Thanks to the ace pastry chef, desserts—like the elaborate cookie board—are not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace;[]
7614;The Inn at Pound Ridge;USA;Pound Ridge;258 Westchester Ave., Pound Ridge, 10576, USA;41.2096808;-73.5749339;63;false;false;American, American Contemporary;This warm and inviting Victorian-style inn exemplifies country charm. After a glimpse of the valet line and attractive white clapboard façade, it’s quite obvious that this restaurant is for a pedigreed crowd. Manicured gardens complete the picture. The mien may be rustic, but the menu conceived by Chef de Cuisine Eric Brach is utterly contemporary. It features a veritable hit list of Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s greatest dishes, albeit in tweaked formats. The classic tuna ribbons from the chef's eponymous Manhattan outpost inspires this kitchen's tuna tartare with avocado, ginger-soy sauce, and chili oil. Crisp, pan-roasted salmon is then set in a fragrant corn-lime broth. Finish with carrot cake with cream cheese frosting.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7615;Al Badawi;USA;Brooklyn;151 Atlantic Ave., Brooklyn, 11201, USA;40.6905192;-73.9950044;78;true;true;Middle Eastern;Scale is everything at this bustling Palestinian charmer, which stands out on Atlantic Avenue because of the colorful faux floral display that graces the front entrance. These flowers again make a statement inside, hanging above the kitchen and on the wall. Such vibrancy and boldness also extends to the cooking. Start with all of the dips by ordering the enormous mezze platter, served with thin, unleavened saj bread that arrives hot out of the domed oven by the door. Mounds of rice piled on with the likes of shredded chicken, garlic tahini and pita chips or bone-in lamb with fermented yogurt sauce arrive ready to feed an army. The best of the kitchen might also be its simplest dish: thin flatbread covered in melted cheese and ground pistachios.;Air conditioning;[]
7617;La Mercerie;USA;New York;53 Howard St., New York, 10013, USA;40.7202691;-74.002183;45;false;false;French, Contemporary;This hot spot is surely an essential SOHO experience, set in an opulent emporium by noted interior design firm Roman and Williams. Especially at lunch, the room basks in its own beauty and in the beauty of the well-heeled patrons who huddle around tiny tables adorned with delicate blooms. The open kitchen, too, is a sight unto itself with sage-green tiles and gleaming cookware. It all feels very chic and very French, accented by a menu that delivers in careful indulgence. Chicken consommé with foie gras is a delicious study in contrasts, while cod steamed in a donabe with grain mustard, leeks, and potatoes offers both sophistication and richness. A wealth of classic desserts like profiteroles, tarte tatin, and crème brûlée taste of sweet nostalgia.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7619;Ensenada;USA;Brooklyn;168 Borinquen Pl., Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.710514;-73.954133;20;true;false;Mexican, Seafood;Ensenada offers a little taste of Baja and beyond in this corner pocket of Williamsburg. Seafood is the star of the show here, where the Chef Luis Herrera's menu is a showcase of their sustainable seafood mission. Choose from a variety of ceviche and aguachile or nosh on the tostada de atun with salsa macha or the taco de pescado where the fish is battered and fried until golden and crisp. Vegetarian friendly options are available. Desserts are limited, but don't skip the hibiscus pie encased in a crumbly cookie crust with hazelnuts and sea salt.Beverage Director Jorsand Diaz stocks the bar with hundreds of Mexican spirits, perfect for happy hour or late nights on weekends, when their basement bar, Black Flamingo, is open for drinks and dancing.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7620;La Vara;USA;Brooklyn;268 Clinton St., Brooklyn, 11201, USA;40.6877663;-73.9956114;48;true;true;Spanish;Chef Alex Raij knows her tapas, helping to kickstart the craze in Manhattan. More than a decade ago, she jumped boroughs to Brooklyn and opened La Vara, which she co-owns with husband, Eder Montero. Billing itself as “cocina casera” or “home cooking,” this kitchen elevates humble cuisine to impressive levels. Product quality is excellent, and the playful spirit behind these dishes is the definition of creative cooking. Menu highlights include huevos rellenos, judías a la plancha, or grilled romano beans and butter beans in a bright Romesco sauce, and cochinillo, or a slow-roasted suckling pig leg with chimichurri.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7621;Casa Enrique;USA;Queens;5-48 49th Ave., Queens, 11101, USA;40.7434588;-73.9542808;21;true;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;You can always find this Mexican favorite by looking for the crowds out front. Chef Cosme Aguilar has long helmed this favorite in Long Island City, and the restaurant is constantly abuzz. On a menu that rarely changes, find family recipes alongside the expected tacos and guacamole, but know this kitchen shines brightest with the bigger plates. Think Branzino prepared “al pastor” and marinated in guajillo and achiote or the braised lamb shank set in a fruity-spicy broth. Above all else, there must be mole, which is excellent in all its forms from chicken enchilada to just chicken and rice. For dessert, tres leches is the classic, sweet finale or just ask your waiter for another round of frozen watermelon margaritas. There’s no wrong answer.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7622;Miss Lily’s;USA;New York;109 Avenue A, New York, 10009, USA;40.7260412;-73.9837461;16;true;false;Jamaican;Authentic Jamaican flavors and thumping reggae go hand-in-hand amid Miss Lily’s brightly colored booths and banquettes, retro artifacts and Formica-topped tables. A well-stocked bar and bins filled with produce set the mood for enjoyable classics brought to you at the hands of glam servers.Start with a classic Jamaican oxtail stew with tender, unctuous meat, beans, and carrots in a rich and savory gravy and chase it with a Pure Passion Margarita with jerk salt. Melvin’s “body good” salad tosses kale, radish, celery and apples in a citrus-ginger vinaigrette for a crisp bite. For the Jamaican specialties—think curried goat, jerk chicken, and callaloo—to a boozy rum cake, this Caribbean queen reigns supreme.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7623;Patricia’s;USA;Bronx;1082 Morris Park Ave., Bronx, 10461, USA;40.8493908;-73.8536198;96;true;false;Italian-American, Italian;Italian in spirit, but far from a red sauce slinging checkered tablecloth joint, Patricia's is convivial and  elegant, with high ceilings featuring exposed brick walls and a semi-open kitchen. The cocktails selection is interesting, and the succinct wine list is carefully chosen with some unexpected (and fun!) Italian varietals.That brick oven churns out pleasing pizzas with lightly charred crusts, like the Regina simply adorned with buffalo mozzarella, torn basil and a drizzle of excellent olive oil. Calamari fritti are light and crispy without a touch of grease, but don’t miss the flaky and gently poached baccalà salad. Seafood risotto is creamy-dreamy with plenty of tender mussels, clams, shrimp and squid.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7624;Community Food & Juice;USA;New York;2893 Broadway, New York, 10025, USA;40.8058889;-73.9657314;99;false;false;American, Contemporary;As part of Columbia University’s sprawl, this address is a godsend for students, faculty and locals from morning to night. Although it’s spacious with plenty of outdoor options, the popular spot doesn’t accept reservations—and has the lines to prove it. They turn out joyful fare, and the weekday blueberry pancake special is just one reason why this place gets so much love. For lunch, a kale salad with artichoke hearts, pickled carrots and crispy chickpeas is anything but rote. Come dinnertime, the fish or steak of the day might reveal pan-seared mahi mahi with roasted cauliflower and black truffle beurre blanc, or grilled strip steak brushed with teriyaki.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7625;Risbo;USA;Brooklyn;701 Flatbush Ave., Brooklyn, 11225, USA;40.656084;-73.9602312;82;false;false;American, Grills;A "Parisian rotisserie with a Brooklyn vibe" seems a perfectly apposite way to describe this affable escape from Chef/owner Boris Ginet. Donning whitewashed walls lined with artistic photos, industrial-chic cement floors and a glorious garden patio, the anchor here is—of course—the open-air rotisserie, churning out a host of delectably roasted items.This menu highlights everything from bowls and platters to seasonal soups, vegetables and grains. Roasted leg of lamb, marinated in herbs and spices for over two days, is the definition of tender, savory deliciousness, especially when coupled with their house-made sauces like aioli and yogurt. The Risbo platter is a house special, underscoring the likes of well-seasoned roasted pork served with hummus, a spicy cabbage salad and plantains.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7626;Ai Fiori;USA;New York;400 Fifth Ave., New York, 10018, USA;40.75013;-73.98357;66;false;true;Italian, French;Nestled within the Langham Hotel with walls of windows overlooking Fifth Avenue, Ai Fiori is a frequent perch for the expense account crowd. The handsome marble bar and lounge is ideal for a post-work cocktail, while large florals, leather chairs, and square columns lure larger groups into the formal dining room. Service is gracious, linens are thick, and every last detail is lovely from lunch until dinner. An Italian menu boasting touches of flair is pleasantly matched to the space. Think Hiramasa crudo cleverly dressed with a creamy sunflower seed sauce or a uniquely shaped sagne pasta arranged with lusciously braised rabbit, fresh mint, and crushed Castelvetrano olives.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7627;Mile End;USA;Brooklyn;97A Hoyt St., Brooklyn, 11217, USA;40.687473;-73.98702;25;true;false;Deli;Boerum Hill’s most bodacious deli serves up killer smoked meats among other treats whose caloric content rivals a week’s worth of eating. This is Montreal Jewish fare, and the stuff comfort food dreams are made of (think cured and smoked beef brisket piled high finished with mustard on rye). Side dishes are as serious as the main ones, like that Canadian classic poutine, finished in a number of ways, including cheese curds, gravy, eggs, and even chicken schnitzel. Still hungry? They have potato latkes and knishes. The tiny space gets lots of traffic, so those who can’t find a seat along the counter or trio of communal tables can feast at home with takeout procured from the sidewalk window.;Air conditioning;[]
7628;Laser Wolf;USA;Brooklyn;97 Wythe Ave., Brooklyn, 11249, USA;40.7208186;-73.9587178;83;true;true;Middle Eastern, Regional Cuisine;Guests of Williamsburg's hip Hoxton Hotel who seek to sip a cocktail while enjoying a stunning sunset over Manhattan need to just hop on the elevator and head to the rooftop to reach Laser Wolf. Of course, scoring a reservation at this hot spot is not as easy. Michael Solomonov's and Steve Cook's skewer house is especially buzzy, where lights are strung overhead and trendy music and a bustling open kitchen add to the vibe.  The menu is festive and focused. It all begins with salatim including the likes of  babaghanoush, mushrooms with Swiss chard and sour cherry, pickles, gigante beans with harissa and more. Meat and vegetable skewers are next, with lamb kofta a winning choice. Finally, brown sugar soft-serve ice cream rounds out the satisfying meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7629;Benoit;USA;New York;60 W. 55th St., New York, 10019, USA;40.76245;-73.97722;37;false;false;French;This Alain Ducasse bistro, housed in the venerable La Côte Basque space, may have been renovated in recent years, but it remains decidedly Old World in look, feel and taste. The setting remains a sight to behold, with its abundant framed mirrors, red velvet banquettes and oak paneled walls. In the front salon, two red wingback chairs are tilted in to face a working fireplace and make an idyllic spot for nibbling madeleines at the end of your meal.The unabashedly French menu is stacked with comfortable, familiar bistro dishes that feature the likes of cassoulet, pâté en croûte and foie de veau. Traditional desserts are a highlight, especially the rum baba with its fluffy brioche served with lightly sweetened whipped cream and a generous pour of rum sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7631;Uzuki;USA;Brooklyn;95 Guernsey St., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.7245115;-73.9534512;78;false;true;Japanese, Soba;Chef Shuichi Kotani brings his passion for buckwheat to this industrial corner of Greenpoint. Born in the Hyōgo Prefecture, he works in a sprawling warehouse fit with factory windows and skylights. In addition to leading classes for making soba and pottery, the restaurant offers a gluten-free menu flush with noodles and vegetables. Start with the red tosaka salad with cucumber, tomatoes, and daikon radish tossed in a yuzu dressing. Cold and hot soba preparations feature plucky, hand-cut noodles with dashi, and each dish arrives in a ceramic bowl that the chef has made himself. Be advised that pricing is steep.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7632;KRU;USA;Brooklyn;190 N. 14th St., Brooklyn, 11249, USA;40.723224;-73.9555176;96;true;true;Thai, Contemporary;Husband-and-wife Chefs Ohm Suansilphong and Kiki Supap are behind KRU, which is Thai for "guru." Indeed, you will get a lesson in traditional Thai dishes albeit ones that have been spruced up in a decidedly contemporary way. Sleek and airy, the interior is equally of-the-moment with exposed brick walls and ductwork along with cement tiled floors. First up? Braised beef shank and tripe in a rich, flavorful broth with pork cracklings, bean sprouts, and Chinese broccoli with a nice balance of sour and spicy. Then, red curry-rubbed branzino over steamed egg and Napa cabbage is served on a banana leaf with white rice.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7633;Peter Luger;USA;Brooklyn;178 Broadway, Brooklyn, 11211, USA;40.709889;-73.9625494;39;false;false;Steakhouse, American;Peter Luger is an idolized classic that runs on wheels by a team of gloriously forthright waiters. This paean to beef doesn’t just serve legendary steaks, but a side helping of history too. Its unapologetically old-school décor tells of family gatherings, friends united and success celebrated. Credit cards remain a fanciful concept, so you’ll need to come with a few Benjamins tucked into your wallet.Start with a thick slice of bacon to get your taste buds up to speed before the steak arrives. These slabs of finely marbled Porterhouse are dry-aged in-house, then broiled to perfection and finally served with their own sauce, as well as a host of sides (think German potatoes and creamed spinach). Of course, there is always room for cheesecake—and schlag.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7634;Sunday in Brooklyn;USA;Brooklyn;348 Wythe Ave., Brooklyn, 11249, USA;40.7142164;-73.9653572;29;true;false;American, Contemporary;With all due respect to Monday through Saturday, the best day may be "Sunday in Brooklyn." In contrast to its rustic bar downstairs, this stalwart now boasts a second-floor dining room, with palm trees and whitewashed walls. A breezy vibe, old-school tunes and stirring sips encourages lingering. Add that to the fact that all baking is done on-site, and it's no wonder this is such a bit hit. Following suit, begin with crusty sourdough and creamy beer butter or warm and sticky buns. It's all all-day spot but is especially beloved at brunch, when their signature Sunday pancakes make an appearance. A single skillet-style pancake topped with a hazelnut-maple praline coating, it's a fluffy delight only improved with a pat of brown butter and thick maple syrup.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7635;Persepolis;USA;New York;1407 Second Ave., New York, 10021, USA;40.76997;-73.95785;66;false;false;Persian;Silky-smooth spreads, homemade yogurt, grilled meats and fragrantly spiced stews have solidified Persepolis’ reputation as one of the city’s finest Persian restaurants. Linen-draped tables, spacious banquettes and big windows facing Second Avenue fashion a look that inspires dressing up (or not). Service is always gracious, if at times too earnest.The kitchen shines with its eggplant halim, a creamy, steaming roasted eggplant and onion dip with tender lentils and a dollop of yogurt on top. A kebab duo of saffron-tinged chicken and grilled beef are both succulent successes, served with basmati rice flecked with sour cherries. For dessert, try the tart-sweet Persian lemon ice studded with bits of rice noodles and doused in a deep red cherry syrup.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7636;Caviar Russe;USA;New York;538 Madison Ave., New York, 10022, USA;40.760685;-73.97355;35;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;With a name like Cavar Russe, there’s no ambiguity about what sort of experience is on offer: a parade of luxury ingredients with eye-watering prices to match. Diners are led up a marble staircase at this posh jewel box, where views looking out over Madison Avenue below feel classically New York Offerings of the namesake range from a relatively attainable dollop of Pacific Sturgeon to 500-gram tins of Osetra that cost more than first-class tickets to the Caspian Sea. The French-inflected menu, available as either a prix fixe or à la carte, straddles classic and contemporary, as in a chilled white asparagus velouté with a tartare of scallop and a touch of caviar. Long Island Pekin duck is elegantly plated and served with a croquette with foie gras.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
7637;Noreetuh;USA;New York;128 First Ave., New York, 10009, USA;40.7274743;-73.9853233;88;true;false;Fusion;For a taste of something different, make a beeline to this unique Hawaiian-flavored spot. Headed by a trio of Per Se veterans, Noreetuh features an intimate setting of two slender dining rooms adorned with hexagonal mirrors and shelving units used to store bottles from the impressive wine list.The kitchen turns out contemporary and sophisticated interpretations of Hawaiian cuisine. Classics like the humble musubi is elevated with the likes of pork jowl and beef tongue, while the parmesan cheese-topped Kalua pork cavatelli's richness is balanced by perfect portions of pickled cabbage. Imported ingredients such as shrimp from Kauai and the famous King's Hawaiian sweet bread are sure to invoke nostalgia among the expats.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7638;Chez Ma Tante;USA;Brooklyn;92 Calyer St., Brooklyn, 11222, USA;40.72686;-73.95745;99;false;true;American Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Aidan O’Neal and veteran New Yorker Jake Leiber have made a name for themselves at this intimate little gem. A recent refresh was in looks only, with the meat-centric mentality along with a modern French-Canadian sensibility thankfully still in place (along with that fabulous kohlrabi salad). Porky dishes and pâtés are part and parcel of this dining experience, so don't leave without tucking in to the pig’s head terrine. Lighter appetites can balance out such heavy leaning dishes with a roasted half-chicken accompanied by charred onions and set atop a bed of nutty and vibrant romesco. Desserts—including the chocolate flourless cake—are equally popular, but it is brunch that warrants a queue of famished locals.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
7641;Pastis;USA;New York;52 Gansevoort St., New York, 10014, USA;40.7393284;-74.0067674;17;false;false;French;Manhattan hot spots come and go (even more rapidly in the trendy Meatpacking District) but Pastis 2.0 is one watering hole that still glows anew. Keith McNally's impressively popular French bistro combines a painted tin ceiling, frosted globe lights, a curved zinc counter stocked with bottles of rosé on ice and precarious wooden stools to great effect.In case the decor didn't tip you off, the menu is classic French. It's open all day, so pop in for a croissant and coffee in the morning, then swing by to satiate that late-night frites craving. Everything from moules to steak is better with frites, but don't overlook the vegetables—asparagus in béarnaise sauce is dreamy. Traditional desserts, such as crème brûlée and baba au rhum, round out the meal perfectly.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7642;Novitá;USA;New York;102 E. 22nd St., New York, 10010, USA;40.7392833;-73.9864906;66;false;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;Enjoyable and quietly elegant, Novitá boasts a genuine Italian sensibility both in setting and service. The small size and low ceilings foster a surprisingly serene ambience that is all but disappearing in the city. Prices are not cheap, but the quality is high. The cooking does not necessarily break new ground, but is nonetheless good. Rather than explore the costlier dishes that perhaps feature Kobe beef or black truffles, it’s best to stick to the tried-and-true favorites.Start with a superb combination of pan-fried shiitake caps filled with shrimp and scallions. Then, move on to tiny orecchiette mingled with just the right amount of slow-cooked and fiery lamb ragù, broccoli rabe and grated cheese. The espresso-soaked tiramisu is a perfect pick-me-up.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7643;Barawine;USA;New York;200 Lenox Ave., New York, 10027, USA;40.804707;-73.94764;44;false;false;Contemporary, French Contemporary;Amid the leafy, brownstone-lined Mount Morris Park Historic District, Barawine is an inviting dining room overseen by Fabrice Warin (formerly the sommelier at Orsay). This eye-catching space entices Lenox Avenue passersby to step in, sip and sup, either perched at the bar area’s communal table or seated in the quieter, more intimate back dining room. Whitewashed walls attractively double as wine storage throughout.The crowd-pleasing menu defies classification and embraces many influences. Quinoa salad with tofu and seaweed will please the disciplined, while mac and cheese loaded with béchamel, Gruyère and diced ham calls out to more indulgent palates. Pan-seared branzino with aromatic herbs and a drizzle of balsamic is a treat for all.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7644;Orsay;USA;New York;1057 Lexington Ave., New York, 10021, USA;40.7724746;-73.9605803;23;true;true;French;Its classic art nouveau styling makes this popular French brasserie de luxe infinitely more 7th arrondissement than Upper East Side. The efficient service is overseen by managers armed with authentic French accents and highly skilled in the art of flirting and flattery—the immaculately coiffured Orcéens may be a sophisticated bunch of customers but they expect a generous side order of Gallic charm to go with their classic French cuisine.All the favorites are here, from escargots to lobster bisque, quenelle Lyonnaise to île flottante, and the kitchen prepares them with a healthy respect for tradition. There are also plenty of salads for those who’ve given up wondering how French women can eat this kind of food without ever going to the gym.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7646;Lupa;USA;New York;170 Thompson St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7276991;-74.0001044;99;false;false;Italian;Is there anything more lovely than a lazy lunch at Lupa? You’d be hard-pressed to convince the regulars otherwise, as they flock in droves to this Thompson Street treasure for its amicable service, interesting wines and otherworldly pasta.Carefully sourced products are scattered throughout this menu—witness perfectly seared octopus alla piastra, starring tender faro with crispy bits of prosciutto and fennel, or a starter of plump, marinated sardines laced with oil, coarse salt and served over diced cucumber and celery. But the highlight of this parade is the pasta, which may include decadent bavette cacio e pepe, a classic preparation from Lazio. It’s nothing short of satisfying, thanks to the addition of sharp pecorino and freshly ground black pepper.;Air conditioning;[]
7647;Avant Garden;USA;New York;95 Avenue A, New York, 10009, USA;40.7259963;-73.983668;33;false;false;Vegan;Open since 2015, this little jewel box of a restaurant courtesy of Ravi DeRossi aims to give vegan food some well-deserved polish. Channeling all the coziness of a treehouse, this East Village mainstay offers a variety of dishes that are thoughtful and attractive. Recent highlights include deep-fried sushi rice topped with carrot, ginger, and avocado as well as artichoke and spinach toast garnished with green beans, jicama, and truffled potato chips. At times, the nicely curated menu goes a bit far in promising Spanish “paella” or Mexican “mole” but for those who appreciate strictly vegan fare in a stylish setting, this intimate restaurant certainly fits the bill.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7648;Wayan;USA;New York;20 Spring St., New York, 10012, USA;40.7213518;-73.9950963;62;true;true;Indonesian, South East Asian;Located in ever-fashionable SoHo, this high-energy Indonesian restaurant is a party in the front and in the back. Warm teak paneling, live plants, and candles set the stage at the close-quartered bar and in the equally rowdy dining room. Chef/co-owner Cédric Vongerichten strikes his own balance of Indonesian and French inspiration, and a menu of satays, light and seafood-heavy small plates, and robust, nicely spiced entrees offers wide appeal to an equally diverse crowd. Escargot rendang with garlic-herb butter is a delight with batons of toasted brioche. Lobster noodles with black pepper butter hit a notch higher on the boldness scale, while the charred chicken lombok is comfort on a platter. A thoughtful cocktail menu adds fuel to the fun.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7649;Fausto;USA;Brooklyn;348 Flatbush Ave., Brooklyn, 11238, USA;40.67612;-73.97174;70;false;false;Italian, American;This sleek and upscale restaurant serves consistently delicious Italian-influenced food courtesy of Chef/owner Erin Shambura, but its overall ethos is guided by restaurateur (and sommelier), Joe Campanale.The kitchen showcases a distinctive take on Southern regional fare that ensures each bowl of pasta is a showstopper. Find evidence in the the kicking spicy capellini neri with rock shrimp, ‘nduja and wild fennel or in the ever-popular bolognese over tagliatelle. Arancini, those crispy risotto croquettes with molten mozzarella and other cheese are a perfect snack. Forge ahead with impressive fish and seafood items before closing out with gelato or sorbet.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7650;Eléa;USA;New York;217 W. 85th St., New York, 10024, USA;40.7873024;-73.9766604;40;true;true;Greek, Seafood;Fitted out with whitewashed brick walls, weathered wood beams, and pretty lighting, this bi-level space exudes all the modern Med feels. Add on the deliciously rustic food and you have a win. Imagine everything from creamy spreads with pita bread to fresh fish. Following suit, ingredients are given the spotlight in the likes of htipiti (feta with roasted chili pepper) as well as whole grilled tsipoura in a lemon, olive oil, and caper sauce. The stuffed tomato filled with arborio rice, golden raisins, pine nuts, and herbs is a savory delight, as is the elevated version of a classic moussaka. Finish with sokolatina, a scoop of Valrhona chocolate mousse topped with cherries and resting atop a chocolate cookie.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7652;Blue Duck Tavern;USA;Washington;1201 24th St. NW, Washington, 20037, USA;38.905373;-77.05128;93;false;false;American, American Contemporary;Set within the Park Hyatt hotel, this upscale American tavern boasts a sleek, urbane and dreamily sprawling interior, with soaring windows, walnut wood seating and highly coveted glass-enclosed booths. Whether dining in the plush room or expansive lounge—which features a separate cheese- and charcuterie-focused carte—the gorgeous space and its well-to-do crowd are the epitome of casual sophistication. Similarly, the product-driven menu has an all-American sensibility, highlighting farms and purveyors. At the center of the open kitchen sits a behemoth wood-burning oven that turns out such classics as whole-roasted fish or the popular duck leg confit. Don't forget to peruse their dessert station and impressive tea list with nearly 30 teas of different levels, including the rare 1985 Emperor's Masterpiece.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7655;Ris;USA;Washington;2275 L St. NW, Washington, 20037, USA;38.90384;-77.04993;47;false;true;American;Ris Lacoste helms the stove at this terrific neighborhood spot, a draw for diners in the company of family, friends, and business associates alike. The sprawling, light-filled dining room is dressed in earth tones and filled with intimate corners for an air of seductive sophistication. And the menu, with its ramped-up takes on the tried-and-true, toes the line between familiar and surprising. Loaded with butter and olive oil and jazzed up with red pepper flakes, linguine with clams is briny and delicious and chicken Milanese has a perfectly zippy tomato topping. The crab cakes are always on point, and the crown of cauliflower is both interesting and complex, thanks to an ensemble of roasted vegetables slicked with mustard cream and an army of flavors.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7656;Café Riggs;USA;Washington;900 F St. NW, Washington, 20004, USA;38.8975559;-77.0242625;23;false;true;Contemporary, French;Inspired by the bustling brasseries of Europe, Cafe Riggs offers grace and modernity in a very polished setting. The historic dining room and bar, kitted out with gleaming brass and marble and velvet-covered Art deco booths, are not short on ambience. The sharp waitstaff makes this a prime business lunch or dinner destination, as well as an ideal post-work watering hole. Classic dishes with quality products shine, as in the delicate Wagyu beef tartare with creamy mustard sauce, tart capers and cornichons. Prawn risotto with saffron, peas and pickled ramps is a vibrant yet delicate, sea-forward course with a surprising refinement. Finally, nothing says goodbye quite like a chocolate soufflé, served here with Grand Marnier caramel sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7657;Thip Khao;USA;Washington;3462 14th St. NW, Washington, 20010, USA;38.932957;-77.032845;42;false;true;Lao;Chef/co-owner Seng Luangrath first opened in ever-transforming Columbia Heights way back in 2014. Her longstanding restaurant has since become one of the most prominent sources for Laotian cooking in the city. The menu, which shows some clear Thai influences, tempts with its sheer variety of options from vibrant starters like the crispy coconut rice salad with fresh herbs and lettuce wraps to warming soups and curries to “jungle menu” favorites like crispy pig ears in tamarind salt or alligator laab tossed with lemongrass. Sticky rice is essential. For sure, this is food that’s ideally meant to be shared. Open only for dinner, the casual dining room is an especially good fit for large groups looking to fill every corner of their table with dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7659;Dōgon;USA;Washington;1330 Maryland Ave. SW, Washington, 20024, USA;38.8837174;-77.0301089;44;true;true;African, Caribbean;Tucked inside the Salamander Hotel, Chef Kwame Onwuachi's restaurant named for the West African Dogon tribe offers a blend of African and Caribbean inspiration alongside nods to Washington, D.C. The tightly edited menu presents a selection of boldly flavored small and large plates intended for sharing. Each dish is presented with flair and nuance, as in the hoe crab, served in a shell with shredded crab and shito alongside plantain cakes with aji verde sauce. Braised cabbage is given a good char, then paired with a coconut vinegar sauce, while rum cake is far from traditional thanks to the surprise of charred gooseberries. A clever cocktail list is complemented by its N/A counterparts, and the wine list is especially thoughtful.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
7660;Royal;USA;Washington;501 Florida Ave. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.914955;-77.018555;21;true;false;Latin American;This airy, quaint, and relaxed all-day spot likes to keep things low-maintenance. The price point too is agreeably lower than its fussier competitors, and the Latin American food is decidedly scrumptious. No wonder, it's a legitimate local favorite.Breakfast is a must, especially if the messy, eggy arepa is on offer. Served wrapped in a white pouch, it resembles a present crafted from seared masa and filled with a fried egg, tomato, cotjia, and avocado. At dinner, hungry fans head to the intimate second-level space—complete with original details—to try their hand at tender pork empanadas laced with aji and the heavenly scent of garlic. The masa “gnocchi” is a rare treat, tossed with braised beef, maitake mushrooms, and loads of herbs.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7663;Reveler's Hour;USA;Washington;1775 Columbia Rd. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.9232554;-77.0420426;64;true;false;Contemporary, Italian;A simple black and glass facade belies the delicious small plates available at this place. Pass a set of double doors to be greeted by a U-shaped bar, arched ceilings, and romantic dining room, Fitted out with muted green-tiled floors and snug tables, the restrooms are perhaps the most unique feature here—displaying clever illustrations of wine descriptions. Unsurprisingly, natural wines are a serious focus and pair wonderfully with the shareable plates.Begin with grilled oysters and garlic butter or crispy arancini. Then indulge in the star of the show—house-made pasta, like house-made bucatini with spicy pork ragu, pickled green garlic, and sesame breadcrumbs. A round of semifreddo with olive oil, grilled citrus, and coarse salt nicely finishes the show.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7664;Rasika;USA;Washington;633 D St. NW, Washington, 20004, USA;38.894913;-77.02162;53;false;false;Indian;With easy access to the Metro, Rasika is a good-looking, loud, and lively spot that lures all types of diners. Everyone is here for their kitsch-free Indian cuisine and laid-back ambience—both of which are as perfectly suited for a casual night out with friends as they are for a formal dinner with colleagues or festive celebration.Rasika is beloved for their popular dishes ranging from well-spiced kebabs and fresh curries to a vibrant lamb rogan josh with layers of flavor. Word to the wise: the breads, especially the naan, are outstanding, so order two because one is just not enough.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7665;Moon Rabbit;USA;Washington;927 F St. NW, Washington, 20002, USA;38.8974196;-77.0250307;41;true;false;Vietnamese;Chef Kevin Tien's highly popular Moon Rabbit hopped across town to a bright and contemporary space on F Street. The crowd's all here for Chef Tien's creative cooking, a mash-up of his Cajun Louisiana and Vietnamese roots. There's a real flair seen in reimagined classics like crab rangoon, with layers of crab, sweet garlic robiola, and pepper jelly. Solid ingredients and the twists on tradition hit all the right notes, as in the fried quail filled with duck sausage served over crispy tomato rice with clementine mustard. Dessert is equally memorable, especially the vegan pandan panna cotta tucked with Okinawa seaweed and surrounded by chocolate cookie crumble. It's a surprising balance of sweet and savory.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
7666;Das;USA;Washington;1201 28th St. NW, Washington, 20007, USA;38.905346;-77.056946;65;false;true;Ethiopian, Regional Cuisine;Nestled inside a classic Georgetown townhouse, Das is a haven of soothing colors and lush fabrics. Great care has gone into its styling, and the warm, generous spirit of the staff ensures that the entire experience is every bit as pleasant and refined.The impressive menu runs the gamut from traditional Ethiopian cuisine to dishes that have the potential to take even the most seasoned and ambitious palate by surprise. Vegetarians have plenty of options, though the flaxseed telba wat, a puree of roasted flaxseeds cooked in a spicy sauce, is a winner. For a meal that won’t disappoint, order the chicken and beef combination sampler, then use the delicious injera to dig into mouthful after flavorful mouthful of surprisingly varied textures and degrees of heat.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7669;Lutèce;USA;Washington;1522 Wisconsin Ave. NW, Washington, 20007, USA;38.9093379;-77.0644252;53;true;true;Contemporary, American;Lucky are the denizens of Georgetown to have this delightful bistro in their backyard. With bottles of wine lining the shelves above, the dining room is a charming, date-night oasis, thanks to exposed brick, hardwood floors and a pressed-tin ceiling. Not far behind the décor, the seasonal menu is tight-knit, offering only a handful of appetizers and mains that could change on a moment’s notice. Chef Matt Conroy and his team are turning out an impressive array of cleverly rendered hits, like scallop crudo sauced with blood orange and yuzu koshō and gently cooked cod plated with razor clam-studded farro. Don't skip dessert, or you'll miss out on the passion-fruit sparked baba au rhum.Cocktails are thoughtfully crafted and accentuate the ebullient vibe here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7670;Ottoman Taverna;USA;Washington;425 I St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.901665;-77.01634;82;false;true;Turkish;This place is fit for royalty. The interior is drop-dead gorgeous with a can’t-stop-staring décor. From its honeycomb patterns on the walls and that large mural of the Hagia Sophia, to its whitewashed walls with glimmering deep-blue pendants, this restaurant brings a little bit of Istanbul to the Mt. Vernon Triangle. Sip a cool apple-rose tea while perusing the menu of Turkish cuisine infused with a modern bent. Kick things off with hot and cold meze, like their falafel with a yogurt sauce or haydari with an herb-flavored labneh. Then try one of their kebabs, perhaps the adana kebab seasoned with red pepper and herbs, accompanied with a bulgar pilav. Turkish coffee is the ideal accompaniment to their in-house made baklava or rice pudding Sutlac.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7672;La Bise;USA;Washington;800 Connecticut Ave. NW, Washington, 20006, USA;38.9003397;-77.0382383;80;true;true;French;This might just be one of the Capitol's most well-known dining rooms, housed at the corner of Lafayette Square and just a stone’s throw from the White House lawn. Furthermore, it has been reimagined as a blast of color, with blue walls, gold-patterned banquettes and vibrant artwork. The space hums with guests gathered around linen-robed tables.The menu is loosely French but with a number of detours, from steak tartare and Rohan duck breast to black truffle risotto and Maine lobster with pineapple. The Ora King salmon coulibiac is a signature for good reason—featuring layers of mushroom duxelles and herbed rice wrapped in puff pastry and served with sauce mousseline. If soufflé is on the menu, order it.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7673;BlackSalt;USA;Washington;4883 MacArthur Blvd., Washington, 20007, USA;38.917763;-77.096695;67;false;false;Seafood, American;It may be part market, but there’s nothing remotely pedestrian about BlackSalt. This lively restaurant’s menu manages to be both approachable and interesting, with sublime shellfish and a concise selection trawling coast to continent for inspiration. Begin with Addie’s mussels bathed in a well-balanced broth—you’ll be sopping up every last drop. Then move on to the ever-warming, saffron-tinged Provençal market stew bobbing with the day’s finest catch, which may include juicy mussels, tender shrimp and flaky swordfish, among others. Finish this aquatic feast with a slice of their tart key lime pie. Served with blueberry compote and freshly whipped cream along with a sesame seed tuille, it is a rich and delicious way to clinch the meal.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
7674;Opal;USA;Washington;5534 Connecticut Ave., Washington, 20015, USA;38.9642691;-77.075535;35;false;true;American;In quiet Chevy Chase, on the border of Bethesda, this buzzy restaurant is well on its way to becoming a neighborhood essential. Far from flashy, the team isn’t out to redefine a cuisine or break any culinary boundaries. Ricotta dumplings, beef tartare, a properly cooked filet of trout – these are familiar flavors handled in a confident manner. There is the occasional surprise, like the excellent lamb-stuffed pita. And for dessert, there is no escaping the tiramisu ice cream, a triumphant finale that nobody will want to share. A reasonably priced set menu appeals to those not in the mood to make any decisions. Either way, the homey space fills up fast, and even the bar can be packed out with guests perfectly content to eat while standing.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
7675;Grazie Nonna;USA;Washington;1100 15th St. NW, Washington, 20005, USA;38.9040763;-77.0342686;78;true;true;Italian-American, Pizza;Chef Gerald Addison and Casey Patten are behind this spot that's long on nostalgia and short on shortcuts. This is hearty food that uses quality ingredients while channeling the memories of Mr. Patten's nonna's cooking. Italian-American classics are leveled up in plates of clams casino, perfectly tender and briny with sweet bacon and crunchy breadcrumbs. A handful of pizza selections includes the classics, but creative ones make interesting detours (try Heather's pie with pickled banana peppers and rings of white onions). Macaroni is given the Sunday supper treatment, but it's not just red sauce—prosciutto and peas, tossed with garlic-spiked cream, is a good bet too. Chicken Vesuvio never disappoints, just like this experience, where a buzzy bar is always packed.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7676;Cranes;USA;Washington;724 9th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.8991984;-77.0244107;21;false;true;Spanish, Contemporary;There is serious heart to be had at the centre of the city, thanks to Chef Pepe Moncayo's elegant spot, where novel ingredients are woven into the "concept" menu. What emerges is a sumptuous mash-up of dishes with Spanish and Japanese influence. Chef flexes his creativity on the omakase, and diners won't leave hungry or feeling pinched. From a sake-infused chawanmushi with pickled watermelon, ajo blanco featuring a pearly white scallop with mustard seeds, to a single oyster tempura, this team loves to take risks and challenge diners. The bar program is serious in its own right, and cocktails, like the "nod to the kurose toji" with its refreshing mix of barley shochu, green apple, and orgeat, are not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7677;Mandu;USA;Washington;453 K St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9026323;-77.0177628;69;false;true;Korean;Credit to Chef Yesoon Lee and her son Danny for showing this city that Korean cuisine is more than just bibimbap and barbecue. You can trace their steps back to 2006 when they opened the original Mandu in Dupont Circle, now reborn as Anju after an unfortunate fire in 2017. Fans who miss the original can still find pointed, fiery stews and broths at this Mount Vernon location, which sports soaring ceilings and a long bar. From plump, steamed beef and pork mandu to vibrant banchan, this is homey cooking that warms the spirit. And regardless of the weather, no visit would be complete without gamjatang, a bubbling-hot soup featuring tender, bone-in pork ribs and potatoes swimming in a devilishly red broth fired up with gochugaru and perilla seeds.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7679;Tiger Fork;USA;Washington;922 N. St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9068986;-77.0248225;74;false;false;Chinese, Cantonese;Tiger Fork feels secreted away. Indeed, its location off the main road makes finding it a challenge, but arrive and discover a sultry Hong Kong-style den. Inside, find brick walls emblazoned with dragons and mountains, Chinese basket-style lanterns, and warehouse floors that show off a sexy, hip look. Then get to sipping on one of their many glorious potions, such as the Bird Market, a chartreuse blended with elderflower, bai zhu and bergamot.Some plates may miss the mark but dishes like the slightly sweet cheung fun and spicy chili wontons are spot on. Glossy, thick pork ribs are brushed with a soy and ginger sauce for umami glory. Crack open that fortune cookie but don’t expect Confucius since you’re more likely to get words of wisdom from Gucci Mane.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
7680;Rumi's Kitchen;USA;Washington;640 L St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9041169;-77.021052;37;true;true;Persian;This large, square dining room is ultra-grand and yet ultra-charming, with a melange of earthy, vivid hues, an inviting bar, and display kitchen fitted out with a tandoor oven. Find a seat at one of the high-backed banquettes or wood tables to start sampling from the classic Persian menu. Get those taste buds going with a yogurt dip accompanied by naan, radishes, feta, and herbs. Then dive full steam into an intensely savory gormeh sabzi—a stew of scallion, beef, and red kidney beans—served with saffron Basmati rice.Desserts enhance the experience, with the staple baklava or a more creative Ice cream sandwich with rosewater and pistachios. Thirsty travelers will appreciate the Glimpse of Paradise cocktail, starring vodka, grapefruit, and cardamom syrup.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7682;St. James;USA;Washington;2017 14th St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.9176595;-77.0317775;95;true;false;Caribbean;Owner Jeanine Prime has done it again—now with this modern Caribbean concept named for the district within Trinidad’s Port of Spain. The contemporary space with industrial touches is enlivened with vivid pops of color, while the shared plates-style menu evokes a convivial spirit. Influences hail from all over the globe, all paired with Trinidadian rum-focused cocktails. Begin with a bowl of Callaloo soup, a deep green blend of puréed spinach, chilies and coconut milk topped with lump crab meat with a great depth of flavor. Don't miss the jerk brisket, which marinates for 12 hours before it's smoked. Follow that up with the Trini-style taro dumplings in a curry sauce, but be sure to get a side of sweet plantains finished with candied ginger.;Air conditioning;[]
7683;Shilling Canning Company;USA;Washington;360 Water St. SE, Washington, 20003, USA;38.8738926;-77.0011749;22;true;false;American, Contemporary;Set in the buzzing Navy Yard, this brainchild of Chef Reid Shilling may be spotted from afar thanks to its distinct sign and inviting garden boxes that burst with all manner of herbs and greens. Inside, it is all modern and masculine, with a commanding bar, gleaming copper kitchen and navy-blue banquette seating.The cooking is mid-Atlantic with contemporary flair, but seasonality rules the roost in both food and drinks. Choose from à la carte or go all in on the tasting menu to savor the likes of pan- fried soft-shell crab over early summer gazpacho and succotash of black-eyed peas, Fresno pepper, and zucchini, followed by a hearty wood-grilled pork chop over cheddar, horseradish, and collard green bread pudding. For dessert, butterscotch pudding with a benne seed tuile is a win.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7684;Cucina Morini;USA;Washington;901 4th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9016285;-77.0159452;83;false;true;Italian;This boisterous spot, and little sister to Osteria Morini is a definite crowd-pleaser. The bar is always packed but guests are here for more than just cocktails, as Chef Matt Adler presides over a Sicilian-leaning menu that teems with choices. There are crudos and small plates aplenty, but the sfincione, especially when dressed up with stracciatella, is an absolute must. This is straight-up comfort food but done with care and skill. Pastas are made in house, and available as half portions if you want to sample more of the menu. One to consider? The thick gramigna noodles tossed with pork sausage, green onion, black pepper, and egg yolk for an almost creamy sauce with a hint of bite. Round out your meal with dessert like bombolini or an affogato sundae.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7687;Seven Reasons;USA;Washington;931 H St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.8999327;-77.0248999;49;true;false;Latin American;There are more than seven reasons to visit this gorgeous bi-level restaurant and good looks are certainly one. The food also makes a splash, thanks to an ambitious menu of dishes from Venezuela, Peru and the Caribbean, prepared in the bright, open kitchen. Their creations are generously portioned and pack a punch. Patacón piña colada reveals slices of fried green plantains topped with pickled pineapple, shredded coconut and a variety of sauces like cilantro mojo and caper mayo. Garnished with purple leafy vegetables, the dish is a burst of color and flavor. Save room for the delicious desserts like the cacao and Laurel dark chocolate basil crumble with milk chocolate cremeux, bay leaves ice cream and quinoa tuile.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7688;Anju;USA;Washington;1805 18th St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.914346;-77.0419403;86;false;false;Korean, Contemporary;Brick walls, funky artwork and wood floors offset by greenery await at Anju. The result is a homey-meets-hip space that feels comfy even when jam-packed. The name refers to Korean dishes best enjoyed with alcohol, highlighting a range of sweet, salty and spicy tastes. Similarly, the menu showcases a series of typical offerings—from fried foods to rich stews along with beer, soju and makgeolli to boot.Start with banchan like Brussels sprouts and apple kimchi, before devouring the perfect pork mandu. Diners longing for a taste of home will find comfort in the items from Chef/owner Danny Lee's mother, Yesoon Lee, like dak jjim (sweet chili-braised chicken with potatoes and onions) or dolsot bibimbap, blending crisped rice with tofu and grilled veggies.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
7689;Balos Estiatorio;USA;Washington;1940 N St. NW, Washington, 20036, USA;38.907101;-77.0446;96;true;true;Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine;With two large rooms dotted with olive trees and decorated with wall hangings and fine pottery, you might just convince yourself that you've left DC for this restaurant's namesake— an idyllic location on Crete. This impressive spot from three friends offers a roll call of Greek favorites (think spanakopita and citrus-toned avgolemono). Choose meats from the grill or regional fish grilled with ladolemono and capers flown in from Greece. There's always the classic chicken souvlaki with wonderful, salty pita bread and creamy tzatziki, but it's those Greek fries that win your heart every time. Of course, when dessert comes around, it's no question: baklava with iced Greek yogurt for the win. Greek wines round out the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7690;Bronze;USA;Washington;1245 H St. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.90006;-76.988691;81;false;true;Contemporary, Caribbean;Visionary and hospitality veteran Keem Hughley has created an imaginary world at Bronze, where a fictional character's travels across Africa serve as inspiration for this wildly creative spot. The stunning space features presents individualized settings by floor (Pre-Earth, Earth and the Crane Room), with chic styling courtesy of leopard-print booths and black brick walls. This Black owned, Black run spot has assembled an A-list team, including acclaimed chef Toya Henry, who impresses with dishes like charred yuzu squid skewers slicked with herb "pesto" and a satsuma and currant glaze. Afro-Caribbean cooking as viewed through a fusion lens is displayed in dishes like grilled Japanese eggplant with a classic West African stew of tomato, onions, garlic and herbs over couscous.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7691;New Heights;USA;Washington;2317 Calvert St. NW, Washington, 20008, USA;38.9237157;-77.0519996;20;false;true;American;In contrast to many of the shiny new restaurants that open every year, this Woodley Park veteran under-promises and over-delivers in the best of ways. Coffee-colored carpet, a tame color scheme to match and a quiet crowd do not sound like the makings of a great dinner, but under new management, the restaurant cooks with delicious confidence. The menu covers a lot of ground but does so admirably. Broccolini with black garlic Caesar dressing, crispy fried oysters with pickled cauliflower, and tempura beach mushrooms dusted in a Moroccan spice blend are enough for a meal on their own. Rack of lamb with salsa verde or halibut with coconut broth strike familiar, satisfying chords. For dessert, the pistachio ricotta cake is a sweet finale.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7694;Del Mar;USA;Washington;791 Wharf St. SW, Washington, 20024, USA;38.87896;-77.02477;18;false;true;Spanish, Basque;Chef Fabio Trabocchi’s restaurant owns a stylish resort-chic vibe by way of coastal blues and whites, polished brass fixtures and large windows overlooking the Potomac.Luxury ingredients find equal footing alongside classic Spanish flavor profiles, and the result is a can’t-miss menu. Barely touched or simply prepared, the beautifully presented fish are a highlight, but make sure to also sample their highly sought-after seasonal tapas, as well as the curated selection of Spanish meats and cheeses. Seasonal dishes have featured asparagus blanco, a thick stalk of French asparagus, poached and served over ajo blanco. Andalusian gambas al ajillo, starring shrimp laced with garlic and chilies, are accompanied by tufts of bread for sopping.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7695;The Pembroke;USA;Washington;1500 New Hampshire Ave. NW, Washington, 20036, USA;38.9104712;-77.0433532;50;false;true;French;This seductive dining room took a cool few million to create, but it is utterly chic and wholly Parisian. Pretty patio-facing marble tables, salmon-hued chairs, tufted banquettes, and greenery create the feeling of dining in a terrarium. Over in the kitchen, the chefs don't cling to any one trend. Imagine a melange of plates like prawn cocktail, lobster bisque, handmade pastas, as well as mains like Dover sole meunière or veal Milanese and you'll start to get their drift. Mediterranean flavors also find their way into dishes like octopus fricassee with black olives and lamb tagine with couscous. Close with a simple yet irresistible lemon tart.Set inside the Dupont Circle Hotel, this smart spot radiates much joy thanks to its genial vibe and solid food.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
7697;Michele's;USA;Washington;1201 K St. NW, Washington, 20005, USA;38.9025771;-77.0283809;66;false;false;American;It would be a mistake to write off Chef Matt Baker’s venture as just another hotel restaurant. This much is clear after an amuse of artichoke velouté. Indeed, freshly baked brioche, crispy duck confit and elaborately prepared vegetables score impressive marks at this French-American brasserie, named after the chef’s late mother and inspired by his upbringing in Houston and New Orleans.The Eaton Hotel, which also houses Baker’s casual café and bakery, is fortunate to play host to such an accomplished team—one that sources well and seasons with panache, all the while running an impressive bar that is as large as the dining room. Seafood towers and caviar service will no doubt tempt the big spenders on a menu that has something for everybody.;Air conditioning;[]
7698;Georgia Brown’s;USA;Washington;950 15th St. NW, Washington, 20005, USA;38.9021648;-77.0345974;24;true;true;Southern, American;This revered dining fixture draws a diverse crowd—from locals and politicos to celebrities and tourists. Everyone is here for the classic Southern cooking that is likely to conjure up many a nostalgic memory. Light walls, bronze accents and tropical greenery give the place a bright and fresh feel, but clearly it's all about the food, with a menu that reads like a delicious lesson in history and culture.Start off with the fried chicken livers accompanied by a mustard-soy emulsion. Then tuck into a steaming and fragrant bowl of Carolina gumbo floating with chicken, andouille, okra and shrimp. Cap it all off with a thick wedge of red velvet cake. If you're thinking Low Country cooking in the heart of the Capitol, you're starting to get the picture.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7699;The Bombay Club;USA;Washington;815 Connecticut Ave. NW, Washington, 20006, USA;38.90126;-77.038155;29;true;true;Indian, Contemporary;A fixture on the DC scene for a number of decades now, this Penn Quarter stalwart, owned by the affable Ashok Bajaj, still functions as a club for politicians and Beltway insiders. Polished and sophisticated with just a hint of spice, Bombay Club’s environs are a nostalgic nod to the clubs of the British Raj.If you can take your eyes off the senator snuggled into the half-moon banquette, the polished Indian cuisine doesn’t disappoint. Palate-pleasing items span the continent to include Northern grilled meats, as well as Southern seafood and coconut-inflected dishes. Tender minced lamb is coaxed with a hint of heat in the Seekh kebab, while the bharli vangi's soft-as-pudding bulbs of stuffed and braised baby eggplant simply burst with flavor.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7700;Estuary;USA;Washington;950 New York Ave. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9014894;-77.0252837;34;true;true;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;This farm-to-table restaurant in the stunning Conrad Hotel is an homage to the Chesapeake. Take the toasted Maryland blue crab and shrimp brioche roll, for instance, which oozes with organic butter and fish sauce-flavored mayonnaise. Old Bay fries make an excellent accompaniment to this item, not unlike the fennel pollen and flurry of micro herbs that enhance a mound of tuna tartare with heat from Calabrian chilies. While seafood figures heavily on the menu, it’s not the sole offering. Desserts, like the peanut butter-cheesecake, make for a rich and memorable sendoff.Views from the space frame the energetic downtown scene. Yet, it's hard not to be drawn to the theatrics of the open kitchen, where cooks work by the glow of library-style lamps.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7701;Supra;USA;Washington;1205 11th St. NW, Washington, 20001, USA;38.90597;-77.027;39;false;true;Central Asian;Supra is a gem for Georgian cuisine, so make those resys. The dining room’s paneling and  wood tables lean elegant, while the hanging sheep hats flaunt regional flair. This chef churns out authentic dishes with a dose of delicious. Start with spreads and cheeses, before devouring soup dumplings or mussels. No diner worth their salt would dare skip the imeruli or ajaruli khachapuri—crusty bread with a pit of molten cheese and runny egg. White pelamushi flaunts a riff on the staple dessert (think: pomegranate caramel and walnut crumble), no feast is complete without wine with selections from one of the world's oldest viticultural regions.Sister restaurant Tabla offers a similar, if slightly more condensed ​​​​​Georgian focused menu, in a casual setting.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7702;Timber Pizza Co;USA;Washington;809 Upshur St. NW, Washington, 20011, USA;38.942;-77.02382;63;true;true;Pizza;Now with multiple locations, Timber Pizza Co is a popular neighborhood hangout that's always buzzing. It's first-come, first-serve here, where you'll likely spy a never-ending stack of to-go orders being whisked out the door. So, what’s all the fuss about? It’s the flavorful cooking, of course. A few bites into the Griffin salad and it’s clear this kitchen knows how to handle itself. Those in the know order a half and half to explore the wide variety of pizzas, available in red, white or green sauce pies. You can't go wrong with a classic Neapolitan-style pizza with puréed tomato sauce, gooey mozzarella and thick pepperoni coins, but choose The Lot for a sauce-less pie topped with shredded braised pork, shaved bread, butter jalapeños and a sweet and spicy pineapple chups.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
7704;Dear Sushi at Love, Makoto;USA;Washington;200 Massachusetts Ave., NW, Ste.150, Washington, 20001, USA;38.9040274;-77.0273913;23;false;false;Sushi, Japanese Contemporary;Are you ready for the toughest decision of your night? At Chef Makoto Okuwa's Love, Makoto, three unique concepts await under one very beautiful roof. You can't go wrong with any of the choices, but Dear Sushi is certainly a winner. This is omakase and à la carte minus the sticker shock, but the price point isn't the only thing that delights diners. Opening snacks, handrolls, nigiri prepared in traditional and new ways—it's all here and it's all delectable. Tokoroten noodles in tomato water hit with sudachi, ginger and topped with fragrant shiso flowers, make for a refreshing treat, and nigiri highlights include akami with burnt negi miso and foie gras, or hamachi with smoked ponzu and chili paste. However, it's the ichigo, or strawberry, served over a cookie base, that seals the deal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7708;Hank’s Oyster Bar;USA;Washington;1624 Q St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.91101;-77.03817;53;false;true;Seafood, Oyster Specialities;The original of three locations, Hank’s Oyster Bar promises a good time and a full stomach. Snag a seat on the spacious front patio or opt for a table indoors where bottles of malt vinegar and Old Bay seasoning are a sign of things to come.Meals begin with a bowl of humble Goldfish cheese crackers, then prepare yourself for a sea, ahem, of dishes. Feast on platters of raw bar beauties (including Hank's signature Salty Wolfe oyster) to oysters any way you want them (Hog Island style includes being doused with tangy lemon garlic and Tabasco butter sauce, sprinkled with buttery breadcrumbs and broiled until caramelized). Lobster rolls, creamy chowder and crab cake sandwiches with Old Bay-seasoned fries conjure up days at the beach from years gone by.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7709;Chang Chang;USA;Washington;1200 19th St. NW, Washington, 20036, USA;38.9061;-77.04344;36;false;false;Chinese, Asian;Named for owner and well-known local chef Peter Chang, this Dupont Circle dweller has a sleek, minimalist aesthetic with a plush look and feel. The kitchen echoes the stylish look with elevated takes on classic Chinese dishes. Walnut prawns are plump and flash-fried, then drizzled with a scant amount of honey mayo. Pork soup dumplings are comfort in a bowl, but here they're precise with superb broth and tender meat. Even something as simple as snow pea shoots with garlic is crafted with care and perfectly complements any main dish. Speaking of, don't let the size of your party dictate your delight, since the crispy, juicy Beijing duck may be ordered in half sizes. Don't leave without enjoying a dessert from Chef Pichet Ong.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7712;Pascual;USA;Washington;732 Maryland Ave. NE, Washington, 20002, USA;38.8955123;-76.9950351;47;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Pascual may be named for the patron saint of cooks and the kitchen, but this spot from Chefs Isabel Coss and Matt Conroy doesn't need any extra blessings (and reservations are a challenge, so plan accordingly). Their casual, contemporary Mexican spot delivers on dishes more often found in Mexico City than in D.C. It's all meant for sharing, and tetelas and tlayudas are always a good idea. Other standouts include a blue corn tamal balanced on pickled onion and tomato finished with crema and charred eggplant sauce. Mains, like the lamb neck barbacoa or smoked chicken, are also intended for tucking into with tablemates. End on a sweet note with the buñuelo: a crispy rosette dusted in cinnamon sugar and served with cajeta and chocolate sauces.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7713;The Imperial;USA;Washington;2001 18th St. NW, Washington, 20009, USA;38.9171787;-77.0414275;27;true;true;American;This bright and bold spot boasts a concise menu with strong American inflections. Enter to discover two colorful dining rooms on either side of the space, as well as a buzzing bar in the back. Spread across a few floors (that culminate in a rooftop bar as your reward for the climb), details like textured metal, marble tables, and artfully lit bottles enhance the convivial vibe.The menu is divvied into mostly raw, vegetables, meats, and larger dishes. Regardless of your pick, these plates are well-executed and show a creative spirit. Start with such sea treats as blackened blue crab claws served with Alabama white sauce, then segue into land by way of the beef Wellington, which sports a golden pastry, braised leeks, and veal jus.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7714;John's Food and Wine;USA;Chicago;2114 N. Halsted St., Chicago, 60614, USA;41.9209735;-87.648767;46;false;false;American;Meet your new neighborhood hangout. With exposed white brick, a comfy banquette stretching the length of the room, and a friendly bar with an engaging wine program, this restaurant isn’t going to struggle to make friends. One caveat: There are no servers so diners have to order at the counter before being escorted to a table. It’s not a tall ask because everything offered tends to be a hit, and you quickly get the sense that they just want to cook good food. Think country ham with fried sunchokes, lobster salad with leek aioli, and dry-aged steaks with potato pave. An order of beef fat fries for the table? Absolutely – this essential starter (or side dish) is impressive enough to trigger a return visit. Another glass of wine? Sure, why not?;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7715;Swift & Sons;USA;Chicago;1000 W. Fulton Market, Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8866946;-87.6520605;58;true;true;Steakhouse, American Contemporary;With the inception of this large steakhouse at 1K Fulton, New York City-based design firm AvroKO adds to their local portfolio in collaboration with the Boka Restaurant Group. A renovated meat and produce warehouse built in the 1920s, this space unwinds from a raw bar aptly named Cold Storage into a plush hangout. Here, striking wood-trimmed arches and concrete columns modulate the scale of the rooms.The kitchen’s contemporary take on steak serves up USDA Prime beef seared at high heat and presented with a trio of sauces. It’s the kind of place where gluttony is rewarded—even the wine list features Coravin selections in three- or six-ounce pours. Extras (like king crab Oscar) or desserts (like Boston cream pie) are worth the calories.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7716;Bar Mar;USA;Chicago;120 N. Wacker Dr., Chicago, 60606, USA;41.883522;-87.63707;36;false;true;Seafood, Spanish;Add this lustrous pearl to the treasury of Chef José Andrés’ culinary empire. The eye-catching décor includes a glowing octopus sculpture that looms above the central bar--a visual cue for the oceanic theme. Business types make up the bulk of the clientele, but a signature sense of whimsy pervades, keeping things from feeling stuffy.The seafood-centric menu deftly juggles Spanish and Latin-American flavors, seen in starters like mussels in escabeche, or a Peruvian-inspired bigeye tuna ceviche with ponzu sauce, puffed quinoa, and furikake. Oysters on the half shell are delicious as is, but a dose of leche de tigre provides further enhancement. You’ll also find elevated takes on standbys like lobster rolls and fried calamari, all done with a deft touch.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7718;Lou Mitchell's;USA;Chicago;565 W. Jackson Blvd., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.87787;-87.64203;97;false;true;American, Regional Cuisine;Strategically set near Union Station, this American institution is beloved by all and sundry. Not only has it stood the test of time—since 1923 to be exact—but thanks to its first-rate comfort food and inviting vibe, it is routinely packed with diners jonesing for classics and signatures.The menu has something for everyone, including soups, chowders, and even a Dutch oven-pot roast or sloppy Joes with coleslaw. Of course, when it comes to grilling, this kitchen is king. Case in point: La Conga Delight, which reveals just the right dot of decadence via slices of buttery brioche stuffed with bacon, tomato, and cheese. Pies and cakes are crafted daily and worth the splurge, especially that dense and creamy chocolate layer cake with frosting to boot.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7719;Elina's;USA;Chicago;1202 W. Grand Ave., Chicago, 60642, USA;41.8913242;-87.6577491;57;false;false;Italian-American, Regional Cuisine;What's the best Italian-American restaurant in town? There is no right answer. Then consider Chef/owners Ian Rusnak and Eric Safin's newcomer and you might just change your mind. With Sinatra crooning overhead, sleek wood overtones, and handsome leather, it's hard not to be besotted by this intimate little gem—and everyone is.A hearty bread basket is the kickoff of dreams, while that cherished classic, clams casino, flaunts a divine blend of taste and texture. Rigatoni a la vodka requires little introduction but a garnish of breadcrumbs makes a welcome surprise. Then, chicken parmesan arrives surmounted with marinara and mozz. If the words nostalgic and classic come to mind, you get the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
7720;Bayan Ko;USA;Chicago;1810 W. Montrose Ave., Chicago, 60613, USA;41.9615594;-87.6750417;81;false;true;Filipino, Cuban;Husband and wife team Lawrence Letrero and Raquel Quadreny are raising the stakes at their intimate restaurant in Ravenswood. In a departure from the usual family-style dishes, they offer a tasting menu in a quest to celebrate their Cuban and Filipino heritages on their own terms. Black rice and lobster poached in calamansi butter come together for their version of arroz caldo. Vaca frita translates here to grilled wagyu beef with black bean and plantain purees. Smeared in mojo and sporting a fine crust, pork belly is a recent highlight. The new format is far from stuffy, thanks to a relaxed dining room and a zippy menu, but those wanting to go casual for the likes of lumpia or pork adobo can visit the couple’s diner next door.;Air conditioning;[]
7721;ROOP Chicago;USA;Chicago;736 W. Randolph St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8844807;-87.6471184;76;false;true;Indian, Contemporary;This bright and beautiful setting, located at the edge of the crowded dining strip of West Randolph, is spread over two floors and outfitted with deep blue velvet seats. Libations poured here have their own flavor matrix—study them if you must but rest assured that all are great.Similarly, the menu is dotted with Indian classics enhanced by such cutting-edge flavors as seen in the deep-fried cauliflower koliwada, accompanied by tempered yogurt and a rice mousse with peanut thecha. Follow this up with hearty beef short rib curry stocked with carrots and marrow kofta. Classic palates will relish the wonderfully creamy dal coupled with a plain naan for scooping, while a baked semolina cake with milk ice cream and pistachios will have sweet teeth swooning.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7723;The Izakaya at Momotaro;USA;Chicago;820 W. Lake St., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8859132;-87.6483063;17;true;true;Japanese, Izakaya;Nestled beneath the ever-buzzing Momotaro is this stylish and serene bolthole where reservations are a must on most nights. The scene plays up the underground lair theme with soft red lights and Japanese lanterns, plus thick curtains to lend an air of privacy. Of course, you're not just here for the look and feel—it's the likable izakaya menu that lures most. Not to outdo its more sophisticated sister upstairs, this menu offers up a few heavy hitters for sushi lovers. Begin with delicious sashimi like shima aji, akami or otoro, only to be followed up with the equally alluring uni pasta. Choose from an array of smaller bites, such as ebi katsu don, with panko breaded tiger shrimp and pickled shishito.;Air conditioning;[]
7724;The Coach House by Wazwan;USA;Chicago;1742 W. Division St., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.9033583;-87.6715241;31;true;false;South East Asian, Indian;Chef Zubair Mohajir's culinary respite is a delicious and welcome surprise. The small, intimate, and historic "coach house" brings a myriad of new flavors and layers of complexity to the cuisines of both South- and Southeast Asia. Born in India and raised in the Middle East, before settling down in Chicago with his family, he pivoted from finance to—his true calling—cooking.Pickling and fermentation play a vital role on the menu, as evident in the array of achars. Most recently, we were enticed by a pavé of sweet potato with a dry spice rub (molaga podi) as well as fara (dumplings) with beet butter and earthy shiitakes. Desserts, like ube jalebi soaked in saffron syrup and served with pistachio ice cream, speak of worlds colliding and has palates tingling.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7726;Osteria Langhe;USA;Chicago;2824 W. Armitage Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.917553;-87.69827;82;false;true;Italian;Open since 2014, this osteria has become an area staple, thanks to its charming space and focused menu that displays a keen eye on hearty Piedmontese cuisine. The staff is as welcoming as the design, which features a garage-like glass façade, glowing bulbs that protrude from the walls, bare wood tables and metal chairs lining the floor.For starters, we’re partial to the thin slivers of poached beef arranged around a tangy tonnato, but just as tempting is the cauliflower and leek flan. Pastas are, of course, made-in house and the specialty is no doubt the tajarin, a plate of deliciously eggy noodles twirled high with a savory ragù. Other regional specialties include hand-pinched ravioli stuffed with la tur cheese as well as prosciutto-wrapped rabbit loin.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7728;Warlord;USA;Chicago;3198 N. Milwaukee Ave., Chicago, 60618, USA;41.9391343;-87.7239019;16;true;true;American Contemporary;The word is out on Warlord, where eager diners line up before it's even open to snag a seat at this first-come, first-serve spot. Chefs Emily Kraszyk, John Lupton, and Trevor Fleming cook over a live-fire grill in an open kitchen, and the most desirable seats are at the chefs' counter. Settle in to feast on the likes of foie gras ganache with grilled hearth bread accompanied by salty-sweet honey butter, whipped foie, and rhubarb dressed with a beetroot reduction. Lacquered, dry-aged duck rests above the grill for a slower cook, but the tender meat is worth the extra time. Even dessert hits the flames, with butter cake grilled to a nicely crisp exterior before being topped with butterscotch amazake cream.;Air conditioning;[]
7729;Kumiko;USA;Chicago;630 W. Lake St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8857908;-87.6441256;42;false;false;Japanese, Asian;It is impressive enough that Julia Momosé has built a worldclass cocktail bar featuring a dazzling collection of Japanese spirits. Servers and bartenders, both dressed in sharp black uniforms, are also so effortlessly warm and cheerful that you want to linger here for hours on end. Now, similar levels of intentionality and sophistication extend to the kitchen. A nicely pitched tasting menu highlights Japanese flavors and ingredients, most of which are seafood. Broth made from tilefish bones is remarkable in its depth, while white asparagus wrapped in tofu skin, grilled, and served with eggplant puree is delicate, original, and memorable. Drink pairings with and without spirits elevate an experience that is confidently fine-tuned.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
7730;Blue Door Kitchen & Garden;USA;Chicago;52 W. Elm St., Chicago, 60610, USA;41.9031918;-87.6307268;48;false;false;American;Thank chef-to-the-stars Art Smith for raising the stakes of the local dining scene with this relaxed bistro. In 1871, this carriage house home is said to have survived the Great Chicago Fire. Today, the cozy and well-appointed dining room makes the most of its parquet floors, Louis XV-style chairs, welcoming bar, and open kitchen where Southern-leaning fare is prepared in full view. Deviled eggs are a solid staple, elevated ever so slightly with pickled peppers, and the juicy, crunchy fried chicken is a hit for a reason. Signature desserts, like the towering slice of hummingbird cake layered with banana and pineapple or the scrumptious bread pudding, are sized to share. This place becomes even more charming when the weather warms and the patio opens.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
7731;The Gage;USA;Chicago;24 S. Michigan Ave., Chicago, 60603, USA;41.88132;-87.62469;20;true;true;Gastropub;For more than a decade, this expansive, eclectic gastropub has catered to the Millennium Park crowds. Handsome banquettes and columns wrapped in celadon tiles lend a clubby allure, but the space’s buzzy vibe never feels overwhelming. While a bar stretching half the length of the restaurant gets its fair share of happy-hour crowds, the rear dining rooms offer a more relaxed setting.Pub classics with flair define the menu, like malt-battered cod with creamy tartar sauce and parsley-flecked thick-cut fries—a solid rendition of fish and chips. Keep it light with crunchy watercress and sugar snap pea salad with house-made burrata, or go all out with a plate of chocolate-toffee cream puffs garnished with tender cocoa-dusted marshmallows.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7732;The Perch;USA;Chicago;1932 W. Division St., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.903269;-87.6761415;89;true;false;American, Gastropub;A whitewashed façade and verdant planters welcome diners to this warm and intimate dining room. In contrast, the interior feels more industrial, by way of large steel vats of beer, for which this bijou is clearly beloved. Other furnishings include a long, welcoming bar lined with green tiles and an array of seats.This is cooking that's certainly both excellent and exciting. Taste the splendor behind the top-shelf ingredients in a seared tuna salad with crunchy greens, sweet mango and soft avocado. Share a plate of potato-bacon croquettes to begin, then tuck into a grilled NY strip accompanied by an arugula salad. There are more than a handful of beers on draft, and tastings ensure decision making is a cinch. Don't miss a slice of their banana cream pie.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7733;Valhalla;USA;Chicago;2020 W. Division St., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.9032953;-87.6777833;42;false;true;Contemporary, Fusion;Ever affable and welcoming, Chef Stephen Gillanders seems right at home in his new location in Wicker Park. A single chef’s counter follows the length of this cool, dark room and gives guests a front-row view of the kitchen. The tasting menu is ambitious in its attempt to trot the culinary globe. Filipino, Mexican, Chinese, and Indian influences make their marks on a range of dishes like ocean trout lumpia, seafood ceviche, prawn toast spanakopita, and a scotch egg riff with lamb and tikka masala sauce. Dessert is more reigned in, and a recent finale inspired by breakfast was a notable highlight. The beverage program is equally thoughtful, offering a wealth of cocktail and wine pairings that are not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
7734;The Gundis;USA;Chicago;2909 N. Clark St., Chicago, 60657, USA;41.9351351;-87.6466238;64;false;true;Central Asian;It's a simple, sleek spot with weathered wood floors, exposed brick, and pendant lights. Leather banquettes along the periphery and tables in the center are some of the other features of this Central Asian culinary operation. The menu is chock-full of Kurdish classics, with similarities from the cuisines of Turkey, Middle East, and even India. Start off with addictive spreads like tirşik and sac tawa, before digging into hearty meats, available at lunch and dinner. Breakfast is no laughing matter though, with black sesame-studded bread, house preserves, kasheri cheese, and cucumbers dressed in olive oil. Eggs scrambled with roasted peppers, onion, and tomatoes are matched with golden cups of coffee as well as bottomless Kurdish tea for a warming treat.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7736;avec;USA;Chicago;615 W. Randolph St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.88426;-87.64343;42;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This West Randolph mainstay has been a smash hit for more than two decades – and for good reason. All day long, fans crowd the long counter and close-knit tables that stretch down the length of a restaurant encased head to toe in wood planks. The Mediterranean menu runs with the seasons, and it’s no trouble finding favor in the bold, colorful plates that come out of this smooth-running kitchen. Dishes like roasted asparagus with za’atar buttermilk or chickpea hummus with oyster mushrooms arrive crowned with all manner of vibrant herbs, sauces, and crunchy garnishes. Generously portioned salads and tartines feature prominently at lunch. A second, more spacious location in River North is better suited for larger groups.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7737;North Pond;USA;Chicago;2610 N. Cannon Dr., Chicago, 60614, USA;41.9301645;-87.6362118;63;false;true;Contemporary, American;In the heart of Lincoln Park, find this comfortable dining room that originally started out as a warming shelter for park ice skaters. Rustic exposed brick and views across that gorgeous eponymous pond with the city skyline just beyond set the stage for Chef Cesar Murillo, who cooks with the seasons and layers on global inflections that lean Latin and Asian. The tasting menu is approachable in length and variety, showcasing a creative range from tuna tartare with chicharron to agnolotti with maple-sunflower cream. One course even featured tomatoes and herbs grown from the restaurant’s very own rooftop garden. For the main course, look forward to wagyu, usually grilled and adorned with clever touches like buttermilk cream and shiso sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7738;Prime & Provisions;USA;Chicago;222 N. LaSalle St., Chicago, 60601, USA;41.8866913;-87.6325989;85;true;true;Steakhouse;Though it would also feel at home in Las Vegas, this glitzy oversized steakhouse fits right in with its swanky Chicago riverfront neighbors. The polished, masculine interior makes its priorities clear from the get-go, showcasing a two-story wine tower and a peek into the dry-aging room under bold, barrel-vaulted ceilings and chandeliers.House-flared, thick-cut bacon seasoned with black pepper, Michigan maple syrup, and dark chocolate starts things off on a decadent note, tailed by a dry-aged NY strip with black pepper crust served with mushrooms and mashed potatoes. Save room for a slice of apple pie.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7739;Hugo’s Frog Bar & Fish House;USA;Chicago;1024 N. Rush St., Chicago, 60611, USA;41.9013922;-87.6279096;47;false;true;American;Housed in a sprawling setting adjacent to big brother Gibson’s, Hugo’s always seems packed. The vast dining room sets white linen-topped tables amid dark polished wood and pale walls decorated with a mounted swordfish, fish prints, and model ships. Hugo’s bar draws its own crowd with abundant counter seating. The menu focuses on a selection of fish, steaks, and chops, supplemented by stone crab claws, oysters, crab cakes, chowders, and sautéed frog’s legs. Family-style sides—creamed spinach or roasted Brussels sprouts in Bourbon maple butter—are a worthy addition.With generous portions all around, you'll need a football team to share a slice of the Muddy Bottom Pie, or just a handful of pals to savor other decadent desserts like the apple pie.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7740;Tied House;USA;Chicago;3157 N. Southport Ave., Chicago, 60657, USA;41.939598;-87.66378;33;true;true;Contemporary;It might come as a surprise that this sleek, good-looker shares the same owners as next-door Schubas Tavern. And like a tavern, its menu paints broad strokes to appeal to a wide range. Start off with a smoked trout and artichoke dip served with house-made salt and vinegar chips before tucking in to the butternut squash schnitzel. Baked, breaded and fried butternut squash served over spaetzle tossed in brown butter with sauerkraut, hazelnuts and cranberries is a delicious riff on the classic. . Of course, this kitchen can do so much more and flexes its culinary muscles in other dishes, like fried sweet potato with salsa macha and cumin yogurt or a winning Spanish mackerel set on coconut-braised garbanzo beans and garnished with fistfuls of parsley and mint.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7741;Demera;USA;Chicago;4801 N. Broadway, Chicago, 60640, USA;41.9693;-87.65935;48;true;true;Ethiopian;Demera’s well-lit corner location welcomes hungry Uptown residents looking to immerse themselves in Ethiopian cuisine. Colorful wicker seating at the dining room’s communal table gives groups an authentic experience, while picture windows offer plenty of people-watching for everyone.Vegetarian and omnivorous offerings abound on the menu, which also features a small glossary of terms to help newcomers. Pleasantly spicy yesiga wot combines tender chunks of beef with onions and ginger in a rich berbere sauce. Served with turmeric-infused split peas and spicy jalapeño-laced collard greens, this stew is a hearty pleasure. Sop up the extra sauce with piles of tangy and soft injera, presented in the traditional manner in lieu of silverware.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7742;Beity;USA;Chicago;813 W. Fulton St., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8867513;-87.6480324;61;false;true;Lebanese, Contemporary;Stone walls, an arched ceiling, and an intimate lower level fit with its own fireplace? Chef Ryan Fakih makes it easy to forget that his tables reside in the Fulton Market District. Drawing on his Lebanese heritage and on family recipes, he makes a strong impression with a mezze of parsley hummus with lamb, falafel in yogurt sauce, and generously charred pita. Such a spread shows both heart and refinement. The tasting menu riffs from there with more stylized interpretations of sayadieh (fish and rice) and mograbieh (chicken stew) and concludes with a flurry of small, sweet bites. A seat at the ever-busy bar offers a casual experience with a limited selection of snacks and thoughtful cocktails made with the likes of arak, Aleppo, and tahini.;Air conditioning;[]
7743;Gaijin;USA;Chicago;950 W. Lake St., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8858803;-87.6515607;91;false;true;Japanese, Okonomiyaki;Gaijin is Paul Virant's love letter to okonomiyaki. Okonomi in Japanese means "what you like” and accordingly guests here are encouraged to choose their own course. Thanks to his time in Japan, the chef displays ace skills and experience. Osaka and Hiroshima are the main styles on his menu, which also flaunts a custom brew from Moody Tongue. While Tuesdays bring a tonkatsu feast, steamed rice with furikake, miso soup, and tsukemono are eternal hits. Desserts, like shirokuma with pineapple-buttermilk sherbet and coconut syrup, are worth the splurge.The room resembles a veritable izakaya, with an okonomiyaki griddle dominating the space—and conversation. Brass accents, exposed brick, and concrete floors add a dash of rusticity to this otherwise premium den.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7744;Pizza Friendly Pizza;USA;Chicago;1039 N. Western Ave., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.9003506;-87.6868496;57;false;false;Pizza, American;Secreted away in one of the many alleyways in Ukranian Village and amidst scores of other venues, this is an alfresco dinning delight. Takeaway is the other alternative, when the weather isn't right. Regardless, the space is especially unique, thanks to a few garden tables and trestles with hanging plants.Chef Noah Sandoval is involved with this project and his talent is clearly under the spotlight, as evidenced by the delicious pan pizzas, salads, and sandwiches. Don't miss out on a pizza square with soppressata, Castelvetrano olives, and maitake mushrooms. A sandwich, featuring perfectly charred rapini, Taleggio, Agrumato, and Calabrian chili, is yet another taste-bud tease. Cool things down with a Pizzaberry tonic and bottle of bubbly Topo Chico.;Terrace;[]
7745;Andros Taverna;USA;Chicago;2542 N. Milwaukee Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9269579;-87.704342;62;false;false;Greek;There is more than one way to enjoy this handsome Greek looker, set just off Logan Square Park. Some make an entire meal out of the mezze by swiping warm pita through dips, like creamy whipped feta, smoky charred eggplant and creamy taramasalata. Others might zero-in on that hulking platter of grilled lamb chops. Then again, a few may stick to the gyro and save themselves for impressive sweets, like custard pie with phyllo, or baklava froyo with pistachio sauce. In the end, no detail goes unnoticed in this breezy space flaunting sleek concrete floors, dangling greenery and a wood-burning oven that kisses nearly everything on the menu.Even the wine list is Greek, thanks to an extensive selection of producers from Macedonia to Santorini.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7746;1308 Chicago;USA;Chicago;1308 N. Elston Ave., Chicago, 60642, USA;41.9056665;-87.6598393;79;true;true;Contemporary, American;It's set within a multipurpose space, but owner Kimberly Moore's lively restaurant is single-minded when it comes to food (think the American South in all of its gustatory pleasure). Try the hot water cornbread with its thick fritters of corn meal pan fried to a crisp and served with blueberry, pimento and B&B pickles for spreading. Then, corn ribs are an inventive twist on a staple. Cut from the cob to resemble the meaty original, then lashed with rich saucing and plenty of pickled onions, it's worth the mess. Milk braised-pork belly is dressed up with a maple-chili glaze and served alongside roasted apples and braised red cabbage puree, and don't tell grandma, but the roasted apple-filled empanada served with caramel sauce and spiced ice cream bests her apple pie.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7747;Tzuco;USA;Chicago;720 N. State St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.8955644;-87.6283518;19;true;false;Mexican;Chef Carlos Gaytán plays host to non-stop crowds at Tzuco. Inside this gorgeous space—awash in homey earth tones and decorated with ceramics imported directly from Mexico—the energy is palpable and seating ample. But there’s no better perch in the house than at the chef’s counter, where the maestro himself leads his merry team and composes creative dishes that feel at once traditional and inspired. Slivers of pristine hamachi resting in an electric pool of cactus aguachile is a good place to start, as is the comforting tinga de pollo topped with a triangle of fried masa full of hearty black beans. Tacos, like ones filled with grilled octopus and puffed chicharron, are always spot on. There's always room for dessert, especially the horchata tres leches.;Air conditioning;[]
7748;Rose Mary;USA;Chicago;932 W. Fulton Market, Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8868305;-87.6510737;69;true;true;Croatian, Italian;Conceived by Chef Joe Flamm, this neighborhood delight in the West Fulton Market is worth every bit of hype—from its singular menu to the airy design. Imagine a setting that evokes Croatia's konobas (akin to a rustic trattoria) featuring whitewashed walls, rustic clay, and hanging plants with seating that can easily accommodate some-100 diners.Well-versed servers are on hand to guide patrons through the menu, which draws inspiration from the Adriatic. High points include tortellini djuvec (eggplant and preserved zucchini in a red pepper cream) as well as burek with ground beef and mozzarella. The charcoal hearth is solely responsible for such sumptuous mains as lamb with blitva and potatoes. Save room for sweet treats like rosewater fritule.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7750;Monteverde;USA;Chicago;1020 W. Madison St., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.881794;-87.653076;32;false;false;Italian, American;Chef Sarah Grueneberg is a local celebrity, so expect her offspring to be packed to the last dining counter stool by 5:30 P.M. Then again this is prime seating, because behind that wood-grain bar lies the pasta station where sheets are rolled, cut, and hung to dry. Her signature Italian cooking—or cucina tipica as the menu lists it—is what draws crowds.That said, this menu is about more than just pasta, beginning with an extraordinary yet humble vessel displaying bundles of cabbage leaves stuffed with herbed breadcrumbs, mushrooms, and  porcini Bolognese. Subbing whey for water in the cacio whey pepe delivers a slight tang and added creaminess, and the al dente pasta, tossed in Pecorino Romano and finished with a four peppercorn blend, is spot on.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7753;Brindille;USA;Chicago;534 N. Clark St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.8919236;-87.6311971;90;false;true;French;This posh bistro is clearly visible to passersby thanks to its large windows and distinctive signage. Hushed and intimate inside, the dining room is awash in a palette of soothing greys and dressed up with herringbone floors along with black-and-white photography. Servers may be casually dressed, but are attentive and engaging.Brindille’s menu bears a strong Parisian accent influenced by the chef’s love for French cuisine. Roasted chestnuts are whirled into a creamy soup and poured over compressed apple, wild mushrooms and puffed rice. Spot-on Dover sole meunière is plated with a purée of watercress and golden-crisp pommes rissolées. And for dessert, preserved cherries are just one option to fill the baked-to-order almond clafoutis.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7754;Coalfire;USA;Chicago;1321 W. Grand Ave., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.8909322;-87.6611279;39;true;true;Pizza, American;Sure, you could come for a salad, but the focus here is on pizza—and yours should be, too. The dining room is cozy, showcasing an open kitchen where pie production is on full display for all to see. And in a playful bit of recycling, empty tomato sauce cans placed on each table become stands for sizzling pizzas churned straight from the 800-degree coal-fired oven.This hot spot has its ratio down to a fine art and knows not to burden its thin and crispy crust that’s blackened and blistered in all the right places. The mortadella is a delight, with chopped garlic and gossamer slices of peppercorn-flecked sausage. But if you wish to go your own way, build the perfect pie with toppings that run the gamut from decadent Gorgonzola to tangy goat cheese.;Air conditioning;[]
7755;S.K.Y.;USA;Chicago;1239 W. 18th St., Chicago, 60608, USA;41.8579186;-87.6577117;19;true;true;Contemporary;Thanks to their ambitious Asian-accented cooking, S.K.Y.'s moniker could easily double as its descriptor. Make your way inside this versatile restaurant to discover a setting that's textbook industrial-chic—a large dining room decked out with metal beams, exposed brick, and distressed walls. The kitchen is open and always humming.The slightly motley menu features everything from cornbread madeleines to foie gras-bibimbap, so this is just the sort of place to bring a friend or group in order to sample more of the eclectic food. Speaking of, embark on a tour of their greatest hits, which may include seared Scottish salmon with cauliflower caponata and white shrimp ceviche. The maitake mushroom salad scattered with goat cheese is revered for good reason.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7756;Itoko;USA;Chicago;3325 N. Southport Ave., Chicago, 60657, USA;41.942452;-87.6638388;95;true;false;Japanese;Located in Lakeview, Itoko occupies a modern, sleek space. Guests are welcomed into this bright space with plenty of natural light, hardwood floors and wood detailing on the ceiling with pops of gray and cream throughout. Meanwhile, the large izakaya and sushi menu offers plenty to consider. From hot and cold appetizers to handrolls, sushi and robata, the items display creative combinations with skilled execution. Start with a tom yum hand roll with sweet diced shrimp tossed in a fiery tom yum sauce or the seared mackerel, then opt for the decadent gyoza or the "slider" skewer with beef tsukune wrapped in bao buns and finished with a line of tangy miso mustard. Dessert is a dynamic finish, as in the donatsu, a donut with a donut hole for dipping in matcha semifreddo.;Air conditioning;[]
7757;Alla Vita;USA;Chicago;564 W. Randolph St., Chicago, 60661, USA;41.8845259;-87.6426089;50;true;true;Italian, Italian-American;The Boka Restaurant Group is no stranger to quality, which you’ll find in spades in this gorgeous room decorated with crystal pendants, hand-painted tile floors, and an amber-tinted sculpture floating overhead. Freshly made pasta, puffy-edged pizzas, and shareable entrées satisfy a range of cravings. There’s the crowd favorite rigatoni alla vodka—at once sweet, creamy, and toothsome—as well as a confident half chicken, roasted and served with grilled lemon. Come lunch time, a long, rustic stone bar is a prime perch where fellow diners happily dig into some of the most satisfying sandwiches in town. You can linger over a bottle of wine or dash in and out for a quick bite. The professional staff will keep everything sailing smoothly either way.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7758;St. Clair Supper Club;USA;Chicago;951 W. Fulton Market, Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8866491;-87.6516736;32;true;true;American, Regional Cuisine;This subterranean dining room is unique in its location, manner and mission. Tucked underneath Roister, it's a sultry and chic reprieve, as guests hand over all decision-making to the team. Celebrating the once popular mid-western "supper club" vibe, St. Clair—also Alinea Group Grant Achatz's birthplace—is furnished with low ceilings, leather banquettes and comfy green chairs.Solo diners head to the bar for a stiff cocktail and slab of prime rib, while larger parties start their meal with smaller bites, like crab cakes and oysters Rockefeller. Prime rib may be the central focus, but sides like "Yorkshire pudding" popovers and caramelized mushrooms with beef balsamic vinegar reduction are comfort to the core. Grasshopper pie completes the classic American feast.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
7759;Les Nomades;USA;Chicago;222 E. Ontario St., Chicago, 60611, USA;41.8934699;-87.62213;31;true;false;French;Though the casual dining movement seems unstoppable, this elegant holdout still likes to kick it old school. Here, along with classical French cuisine, guests are also treated to suited waiters and cart brigade service. In fact, this quaint two-story townhouse, set in the heart of Streeterville and decked out with throw pillow-lined banquettes, fresh-flower arrangements and an upstairs tea salon, makes for the perfect backdrop. Just past the entrance, find a small parlor and polished bar, which also doubles as a fine perch for a pre-dinner martini in an etched glass.Come dinnertime, diners look forward to a prix-fixe menu that allows them to choose between various courses, including an ahi tart, warming mushroom soup and sweet Grand Marnier soufflé.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
7761;Chicago Cut;USA;Chicago;300 N. LaSalle St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.88815;-87.63289;23;true;false;Steakhouse;Chicago Cut is a steakhouse perfectly suited for the City of the Big Shoulders. This finely tailored locale bustles day and night, thanks to wraparound windows along the riverfront, sumptuous red leather furnishings, warm wood trim and a crackerjack service team cementing its steakhouse vibe.Non-meat entrées include cedar-planked salmon with a sriracha-honey glaze, but make no mistake: beef is boss here. Prime steaks, butchered and dry-aged in-house for 35 days, get just the right amount of time under the flame, as is the case with the perfectly cooked-to-order Porterhouse—pre-sliced and plated for each guest. Sides are a must and should include the dome of hashbrowns, creamed spinach redolent of nutmeg or tender stalks of grilled asparagus.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7762;Ina Mae;USA;Chicago;1415 N. Wood St., Chicago, 60622, USA;41.9076108;-87.6724047;66;false;true;Southern, Creole;Straddling a bustling corner, this New Orleans-style tavern feels right at home in vibrant Wicker Park. The interior is vast, with a humming bar up front where patrons line up three-deep behind stools. Beyond that, find a casual dining space buzzing with an amiable, but professional staff. Named for Executive Chef Brian Jupiter’s great-grandmother, Ina Mae, the menu ticks off many NOLA classics. Come for lunch or dinner for staples like their Gumbo Ya-Ya with shrimp, chicken, crawfish, and a scoop of potato salad, or their NOLA po'boys with a variety of options, but don't miss the staff favorite—their Nashville Fried Chicken. End with beignets or their rotating bread pudding offerings.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7763;GG's Chicken Shop;USA;Chicago;3325 N. Southport Ave., Chicago, 60657, USA;41.9424588;-87.6637988;67;false;true;American;Bright and contemporary, this utterly charming spot from Chef Lee Wolen is named for his mother. It's casual, an order-at-the-counter-style spot, and as the name suggests, it's all about chicken. Rotisserie chicken is available by the quarter, half or whole, along with chicken sandwiches (fried and rotisserie) and sides like creamy broccoli slaw with golden raisins and crunchy almonds or  chicken drippings smashed potatoes that will have you hoarding your portion. The comforting menu is rounded out with a few nostalgia-inducing desserts including oatmeal cream pies and a dirt cup topped with gummy worms that makes you feel like a kid again.Despite the downhome digs, the kind and caring staff are incredibly professional, elevating an already enjoyable experience.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7764;Maxwells Trading;USA;Chicago;1516 W. Carroll Ave., Chicago, 60607, USA;41.8874786;-87.6650143;69;true;false;Contemporary, American;It can feel as if half the city is dining in this quiet pocket of West Loop. Conversation and laughter bounce off the hard warehouse floors and large, black-framed windows and travel along a bar that looks almost endless from the front door. The cooking behind all this commotion assuredly plays with Japanese, Chinese, and Thai elements. Think Japanese eggplant with scallion bread, sweet potatoes with Thai green curry, or soup dumpling tortellini with maitake mushroom. Turbot with Swiss chard and kombu beurre blanc was a recent standout. Servers are not fazed by the crowds, while bartenders shake and stir drinks that keep energy levels high. And in stark contrast to the industrial setting, a rooftop herb and vegetable garden helps stock the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
7765;Anelya;USA;Chicago;3472 N. Elston Ave., Chicago, 60618, USA;41.944261;-87.7056144;79;true;false;Eastern European;Named for his grandmother, Chefs Johnny Clark and Beverly Kim bring the flavors of Eastern Europe to Avondale. Throw back a shot of horseradish-infused vodka or sip a glass of Balkan wine in the bar before moving to the cozy dining room.The menu takes a product-focused approach to traditional specialties. An array of hors d'ouevres is displayed on the zakusky cart loaded with the likes of sunflower seed hummus, tart roe tarts, and carrot salad. Green borsch is enhanced with dill and nettles, stocked with boiled egg and slices of fingerling potato, while the freshly baked, butter-glazed, challah-like pampushky bread is a perfect pairing with the soup. Stuffed cabbage, or holubtsi, features finely ground locally raised beef.;;[]
7766;Kyoten Next Door;USA;Chicago;2513 W. Armitage Ave., Chicago, 60647, USA;41.9175576;-87.6906984;63;true;false;Sushi, Japanese;Chef Otto Phan’s latest omakase is something of a gem. Located next door to his flagship counter, which costs exponentially more, this 10-seat experience serves only nigiri and offers both style and substance. The cost is reasonable when you consider the expense of twice-weekly shipments from Japan and the length of the meal. Cut large, scored deep, sauced readily, and then pressed onto generous mounds of rice, the fish make for hearty pieces. Fun quirks include avocado wrapped inside a tuna handroll or an entire Japanese scallop set on an equally-large bed of rice. To finish, the tamago is a silky sensation. The chic space and kindly-priced beverage list add to the swagger of a counter that cares about quality but never takes itself too seriously.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7767;Obélix;USA;Chicago;700 N. Sedgwick St., Chicago, 60654, USA;41.8952439;-87.6386809;65;false;false;French;French bistros are hardly known for restraint, but this River North arrival takes lavishness to another level entirely. On a quiet corner, duck and foie gras run up and down a menu that draws on hearty French classics spanning from pâté en croûte to steak frites to squab pithiviers. Far from rote, everything is made in-house and executed with refreshing clarity. The boisterous, sun-soaked dining room is a sign of equally happy guests, all of whom happily rise to the occasion as seafood platters and bottles of wine grace tables with unusual regularity. If stopping by for brunch, do not expect light fare: foie gras Monte Cristo, anyone? And if possible, save room for dessert. House-made ice creams and excellent, warm pastries await at the finish line.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
7768;Maple & Ash;USA;Chicago;8 W. Maple St., Chicago, 60610, USA;41.901955;-87.62869;32;false;false;Steakhouse;Did someone say scene? Oh darling, that’s half the fun at Chicago’s buzziest steakhouse, Maple & Ash. Deep-set leather couches, clubby music and even a photo booth lend the multilevel marvel an irresistible party vibe.This restaurant is set to the soft glow emanating from the semi-open kitchen, where a wood-fired hearth lights up dry-aged steakhouse classics, cut to generous proportions. Seafood lovers will find plenty to mull over too, like a tangle of octopus and squid, prepared in the wood-fueled oven and served with dill yogurt, arugula and roasted potatoes. Then, a fire-roasted seafood tower is brought tableside, featuring lobster tail, scallops, Manila clams and king crab, all bathed in garlic butter, chili oil and served with house-made pasta.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7769;Herise İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;Reşitpaşa Mahallesi, Kongre Caddesi No:15/A, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34467, Türkiye;41.1091879;29.0404679;66;false;true;Turkish, Regional Cuisine;Asude and Bahadir are ambassadors for Anatolian cuisine. She will gladly tell you all about their concept while providing attentive service and bringing refreshing mocktails to your table (no alcohol served here). He works to a single set menu that celebrates traditional flavours. Variations of tomato and pepper are a common theme in his diverse range of dishes, whether vegetarian or meat-based. His less-is-more approach is exemplified by the millefeuille of dry figs with Aegean olive oil, or the refined combination of rosewater, saffron, currants and rice. Herise Istanbul is one of a kind.;Air conditioning;[]
7770;Ortaya Alaçatı;Türkiye;Izmir;Alaçatı, 12015. Sokak No:6, Çeşme, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.2825651;26.3747346;28;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Turkish;A little removed from the busy tourist area, this open-air restaurant is like a slice of Ibiza. The setting is laid back and trendy, and they serve an appealing range of cocktails and sharing dishes: Think cheesy barley noodles with intensely flavoursome mushrooms and thyme, or pearl couscous cooked al dente in a beef stock, topped with butter-soft shredded beef and a rich paprika oil. The Mediterranean spirit of generosity is celebrated here through delicious food. Be sure to make a reservation!;Terrace;[]
7771;The Red Balloon Yalıkavak;Türkiye;Bodrum;Yalıkavak, Mevkii, Kudur, Şehit Engin Büyüksöylemez Caddesi No:9, Bodrum, 48890, Türkiye;37.1212391;27.2802106;31;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;Walk through the lobby of boutique hotel Avantgarde to access this stunning open-plan restaurant. On the coastline, with its warm white sand, the setting is absolutely idyllic. In the kitchen, the chefs put a modern spin on traditional recipes from the North Aegean. For instance, they give medium-rare barbecued lamb a vibrant twist by incorporating cherries into the accompanying rice and lamb jus, creating a beautifully nuanced dish. The chef's signature creamy rice pudding is the perfect finish to your meal.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7772;Hus Şarapçılık;Türkiye;Izmir;Kuşçular Mahallesi, 8018/1. Sokak No:39, Urla, Izmir, 35437, Türkiye;38.2750333;26.7317648;27;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The terrace of this inviting restaurant is the best place to experience the charm of Hus Wines estate to the full. The sight of the vines and olive trees has an immediate calming effect. Pressed on site, the wines pair beautifully with the revamped Mediterranean dishes that are made to order here. Having started with the addictive house-made focaccia, for example, you could move on to the perfectly cooked medium-rare lamb saddle seasoned with rosemary. Vanilla, isot pepper and a bold zesty cherry sauce elevate the dish's rich flavours. Finish off with a Turkish coffee for a final burst of intensity!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7773;Lokanta by Divan;Türkiye;Istanbul;Asker Ocağı Caddesi No:1, Şişli, Istanbul, 34367, Türkiye;41.0416346;28.9894301;30;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The Divan hotel, close to Taksim Square, boasts a restaurant named Lokanta that exudes the same traditional splendour. The first room is dominated by a piano, which is regularly used for performances. The cocktail bar is the focal point of the second room, and the last room is ideal for family gatherings. In this exquisite setting, you can order à la carte from a selection of traditional Turkish dishes. Tempting options include layers of brick pastry stuffed with braised lamb, tenderised mutton and paprika, and steamed sea bass with an aromatic pil-pil sauce. Lokanta offers a fine dining experience featuring bold, no-nonsense flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
7774;Divia by Maksut Aşkar;Türkiye;Marmaris;Hisarönü Mahallesi, Çubucak Küme Evleri No:80, Marmaris, 48380, Türkiye;36.7661149;28.0521465;65;true;true;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Take the panoramic lift down to the main beach of luxury resort D-Maris Bay. Once you reach the pavilion that houses DIVIA, you will be greeted by a breathtaking vista of the sea and luxury yachts. Chef Maksut Aşkar, the man behind the MICHELIN-starred Neolokal in Istanbul, has put together a team that creatively reimagines traditional dishes with an emphasis on vegetables. Their take on kadin budu features fish rillette that has been briefly fried and combined with potato foam, crispy fish skin, candied lemon peel and a green herb oil. This innovative interpretation of Turkish cuisine delights both the eye and palate!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7775;Isola Manzara;Türkiye;Bodrum;Eskiçeşme Mahallesi, Haremtan Sokak, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0242571;27.4179031;48;true;true;Italian;When you take a seat on the terrace overlooking the beautiful Bodrum Castle, you will feel like you are on an island. For the time of a meal, you are cut off from the rest of the world here, your only task being to enjoy delicious southern Italian cuisine. Parmigiana di melanzane, creamy risotto ai gamberi, sea bass with tomato and capers: the menu features all the classics brimming with those familiar flavours that will transport you to the heart of Italy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7776;The Red Balloon;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yeniköy, Güzelce Ali Paşa Caddesi Salih Ağa Sokak No:5, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34464, Türkiye;41.117256;29.0633402;76;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The Red Balloon is a tranquil oasis in the heart of Istanbul. The terrace is a breathtaking sight, with its contemporary design and towering trees. Chef Ulaş Durmaz sources ingredients as locally as possible to create Mediterranean dishes with a North Aegean twist. For example, he roasts squid from Babakale rendering it intensely aromatic, and he makes his mark by finishing the bold jus with fruity, crisp notes of tangerine. His creative approach and youthful enthusiasm give familiar flavours a new lease of life.;Terrace;[]
7777;Itsumi;Türkiye;Istanbul;KULE - İşkuleleri Kule 2 Entrance floor No:43, 4.Levent/Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34330, Türkiye;41.0829773;29.0123633;36;true;true;Japanese;You'll have to venture out of Istanbul's city centre to find this rather simple restaurant, but you certainly won't regret making the trip. At Itsumi, authentic Japanese cuisine is expertly prepared using the finest ingredients. This is the place to be if you're in the mood for finely cut salmon sashimi, deep-fried prawns in a delicately spiced sauce, or squid and tuna sushi. You can rely on the chef to deliver the specialities of his homeland with all the necessary nuances. NB: The omakase menu has to be booked in advance.;Air conditioning;[]
7778;Alaf;Türkiye;Istanbul;Arnavutköy, Kuruçeşme Caddesi No:19, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34345, Türkiye;41.0603068;29.0365534;25;true;true;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Alaf is a bustling restaurant with a fabulous cocktail bar on the roof terrace – perfect for a romantic dinner for two overlooking Istanbul's eastern coastline. Chef Deniz cooks up dishes with various influences: sometimes it is inspired by Yörük cuisine, sometimes Kurdish, the list goes on. With his wood-fired oven, he enthusiastically melds authentic traditional Turkish recipes with new-age cooking methods. Whether it's al dente squid with an exciting Mediterranean twist using sun-dried tomatoes, or medium-rare goose breast elevated by satsuma and harissa, a diverse journey of discovery awaits your taste buds!;Counter dining,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7779;Şans;Türkiye;Istanbul;Hacı Adil Caddesi, Palmiye Sokak No:1, Levent/Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34330, Türkiye;41.081131;29.0147089;46;true;false;Turkish, Mediterranean Cuisine;This elegantly appointed villa has been a favourite destination for business clientele since 1992. They come for the attentive service, private dining options and expert wine recommendations (be sure to try one of the Turkish reds!). But the principal draw is undoubtedly the cuisine: a fusion of authentic Turkish flavours and Mediterranean influences. From steaming cheese dumplings to a creamy mushroom risotto and slow-cooked lamb neck with barbecued vegetables: generosity is always on the menu here. A firm favourite with many foodies.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7780;Gallada;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kemankeş Karamustafa Paşa, Kemankeş Caddesi No:34, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34425, Türkiye;41.0232069;28.9786542;87;false;false;Asian Influences, Turkish;Gallada is the epitome of luxury. Located on the fourth floor of The Peninsula hotel, this exclusive restaurant seats more than 200 guests! Diners are drawn in by the stunning views of the Bosporus, the upscale decor and delicious cocktails served at Topside Bar. But they mainly come for the captivating fusion of Turkish and Asian flavours over the course of a culinary journey along the Silk Road. The melt-in-your-mouth tuna is first marinated in soy sauce, yuzu and ginger then combined with a tahini and yoghurt cream. You should also definitely try the tandoori duck and the restaurant's own version of baklava. At Gallada, an extraordinary experience awaits you.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7781;Çok Çok Pera;Türkiye;Istanbul;Meşrutiyet Caddesi No:54/A, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34430, Türkiye;41.0306215;28.9734082;60;false;false;Thai contemporary;Exotic artwork by a Singaporean designer gives this elegant restaurant a distinctive South Asian feel. Having spent time in Thailand, the chef has gained an intimate understanding of the nuances of its cuisine. Skilfully balancing spicy and sweet notes, he presents a diverse spectrum of flavours. As an example, he tempers a chilli sauce with the sweetness of fruit and a bold fish sauce. Signature dishes such as green curry with scallops and red curry with duck unfurl their depth and umami-rich profiles here. A slice of Thailand in the heart of Istanbul!;Air conditioning;[]
7782;Ruby;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yıldız Mahallesi, Ortaköy Salhanesi Sokak No:5, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34349, Türkiye;41.0476081;29.0249538;34;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;With stunning views over the Bosphorus, a roof that can be fully opened when the weather is fine, and a terrace that turns into a DJs' playground at weekends: Ruby is one of the hot spots in Ortaköy. The menu comprises dishes for sharing, traditional Turkish fare and a tempting range of pasta and risotto options. And whether you opt for the penne puttanesca or the grilled sea bass with spinach and orzo in a cream sauce, rest assured that your meal will be indulgent and brimming with rich flavours.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7783;Zuma Bodrum;Türkiye;Bodrum;Cökertme Caddesi No:36, Yalıkavak Marina, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1057236;27.2821505;27;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;Zuma is not at all out of place among the impressive yachts and luxury boutiques. This restaurant has a sophisticated feel with its phenomenal sea views, clubby vibe and laid-back atmosphere. They are open from May to October, delighting diners with their trendy take on Japanese cuisine. Think different types of nigiri, or salmon marinated in teriyaki then grilled and served with pickled cucumber. Meat lovers might prefer the 700g dry-aged ribeye. The extensive menu is full of irresistible options! Be sure to cap off your adventure at this hip establishment with a refreshing cocktail at the bar.;Great view,Terrace;[]
7784;Sait;Türkiye;Bodrum;Yalıkavak Marina, Çökertme Caddesi No:2 D:06 Blok, Yalıkavak, Bodrum, 48990, Türkiye;37.1037295;27.2830722;63;false;false;Seafood;While the luxury yachts and chic boutiques may call to mind Saint Tropez, you are in fact sitting on a terrace on Yalikavak's marina. The maritime decor gives away the fact that fish and seafood are the speciality of the house. As you enter, you will see the delicious mezze on the counter, such as marinated sea bass cooked until translucent with a mustard and dill sauce. After that, you can choose your super fresh fish that will be served in a generous and simple fashion. Home cooking is at the heart of this family-run restaurant, and has been its key to success.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
7785;Nobu İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;Süzer Plaza, Askerocağı Caddesi No:6, Elmadağ/Şişli, Istanbul, 34367, Türkiye;41.0402731;28.9924365;46;true;true;Japanese;Located in the Ritz Carlton Hotel, the Istanbul branch of the Nobu restaurant chain embraces the Eastern facets of this cosmopolitan city. Whether you choose a table on the large terrace, in the bar or in the restaurant, the setting is as hip as it is minimalist. The stunning view over the Bosporus and the Asian part of the city is quite a sight to behold. Modern Japanese and South American influences are blended here with great precision. Think sea bass cooked in a light tempura batter and served with a vinaigrette in which chopped pineapple and orange create surprising nuances. The menu is impressive, and the omakase menu aptly captures the essence of the kitchen's offerings. The selection of signature cocktails, Turkish wines, and sakes is simply delightful.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7786;Saku;Türkiye;Istanbul;Bomonti, Cumhuriyet, Silahşör Caddesi, Yeniyol Sokak No:2, Şişli, Istanbul, 34367, Türkiye;41.0584402;28.9774717;81;false;true;Asian;Located in the NOW Bomonti building, Saku is something of a hidden gem, offering an exotic and cosy dining experience. The restaurant's open space and long, extended kitchen are impressive. The cuisine is Asian with a big nod to Japan. The chefs like to let their creativity speak for itself, a case in point being their take on nigiri with tournedos Rossini that really melts in the mouth! Be sure to leave room for dessert, too. After all, you wouldn't want to miss out on a punchy combination of poached peach, buttery crumble and vanilla and umeshu ice cream, would you?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7787;AZUR;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yeniköy Mahallesi, Köybaşı Caddesi No:71, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34464, Türkiye;41.1217414;29.070212;74;true;true;Seafood;As you make your way through this chic restaurant, you will certainly be drawn to the modern works of art and the panoramic view of the Bosporus. But what really catches the eye at AZUR is the seafood on display. The quality is second to none! All that excellent produce is showcased in dishes that fluidly blend Turkish and Mediterranean culinary traditions. Think Atlantic bluefin tuna tartare with creamy stracciatella, super-fresh fish on the plancha, paella or pasta. Meat fans are also well catered for. The servers will be happy to give you a few pointers to help you get the most out of this culinary adventure.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7788;Lucca by the Sea;Türkiye;Bodrum;Göltürkbükü, 314. Sokak No:12/1, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1280224;27.4114826;19;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;The idyllic Lucca by the Sea feels like a secret island getaway. The white sand, the crystal-clear water, the soft materials of the lounge-style decor: this is the Turkish Riviera at its best! Seafood dominates the extensive menu, be it barbecued, on pizzas or in pasta options. The chefs showcase their skills with dishes such as barbecued octopus escabeche garnished with fresh chives, or beef tenderloin tagliata. NB: This restaurant is only open in the evening. Lunch is served at Lucca Beach – the cuisine is the same but the menu is shorter.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7789;Yeni Lokanta;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kumbaracı Yokuşu No:66, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34433, Türkiye;41.0294974;28.9756053;19;true;true;Turkish, Creative;A side street off the famous main road of Istikal Caddesi, a bright Mediterranean decor and the creativity of a discerning chef – welcome to Yeni Lokanta! Here you can enjoy Turkish flavours that draw on original ideas, resulting in fresher and lighter dishes that lose none of their exuberance. Order à la carte or opt for the set menu (a selection from the menu) and discover how the focus on vegetables, local produce and Turkish wines makes this dining experience all the more engaging.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7790;Kasap Fuat;Türkiye;Izmir;1438. Sokak No:18/B, Alsancak/Konak, Izmir, 35220, Türkiye;38.4345228;27.1445359;81;false;true;Meats and Grills, Turkish;You enter a butcher's shop with an impressively well-stocked counter and are guided to the restaurant tucked away at the back. Here, an almost magical atmosphere reigns in the colourful dining areas, and that is added to by the old Turkish classics playing on vinyl records. This place is certainly one of a kind! The restaurant produces its own meat, and the barbecue takes centre stage. Take your pick from the counter, where you'll find top-quality beef burgers and lamb fillets, and order some mezze that are bursting with flavour. For local colour, you need look no further.;;[]
7791;Loft Elia;Türkiye;Bodrum;Gölköy Mahallesi, 325. Sokak No:7, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1155696;27.439798;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The olive trees around you and the views over the bay accentuate Loft Elia's Zen feel. Although this lounge-style restaurant is fully open to the elements, it nonetheless has an intimate atmosphere. The natural vibe suits the menu down to the ground. A commitment to local produce and sustainable practices are part of their ethos underpinned by respect for the planet. The kitchen team's inspired, fine dining-quality dishes are deliciously spicy. For example, their airy feta sponge cake is freeze-dried with three varieties of tomato to give it delicate sweetness and tang. This cuisine is truly inspiring!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7792;AQUA;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yıldız, Çırağan Caddesi No:28, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34349, Türkiye;41.0424175;29.0126519;66;true;true;Seafood;Everything revolves around water at the fish and seafood restaurant of the Four Seasons Hotel, which is also right on the waterfront. Not only can you enjoy a unique view of the bustling strait and Bosphorus Bridge, but this elegant restaurant also provides a romantic backdrop. Delicious seafood is showcased in typical Mediterranean fare, modern Asian creations and dishes cooked on the grill. Aromatic, subtly spiced, accompanied by rich buttery sauces: this is generous cuisine prepared using premium produce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7793;Birinci Kordon Balık Restoran;Türkiye;Izmir;Alsancak, Atatürk Caddesi No:196/A, Konak, Izmir, 35220, Türkiye;38.4337332;27.1382452;79;true;true;Seafood;Fish, fish and more fish – that's what you can expect at this rather simple restaurant. The refrigerated display counter immediately catches the eye as the charcoal grill works overtime in the kitchen. After some freshly prepared mezze, for example, allow the chef to delight you with succulent barbecued calamari rings in a chilli crust, or just as expertly flame-grilled sea bass. Such incredible flavours! No frills here: the focus lies squarely on unadulterated top-quality produce. A gem among the many restaurants on the quayside.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7794;Oro by Alfredo Russo;Türkiye;Bodrum;Gölköy Mahallesi, 312. Sokak No:3, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1305939;27.4087977;15;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Authenticity meets creativity at this gem of a restaurant, which is part of the Maxx Royal resort. The fantastic à la carte menu reads like an ode to the classics of Italian cuisine, but the chef gives them his own sophisticated spin. For instance, he gives extra body to potato and fish gnocchi by servinging them with a shellfish coulis, mussel jus and lime zest. This chef zeroes in on the essence of flavours, deftly weaving together freshness and that quintessential Mediterranean exuberance. The wine list certainly does not disappoint. And it would be remiss not to mention the beautiful natural surroundings, which create a sense of intimacy and elegance… Be sure to book ahead!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7795;Apartıman Yeniköy;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yeniköy, Köybaşı Caddesi No:153, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34464, Türkiye;41.1170806;29.0638518;56;true;true;Turkish, Mediterranean Cuisine;A mostly youthful and hip crowd frequents this pleasant bistro, which matches the energy of its neighbourhood. Lounge music plays in the background, the impressive drinks list features a notable selection of orange wines. The kitchen is run by a female chef who has composed an extensive and enticing menu that combines Mediterranean verve with Middle Eastern spiciness. For instance, she barbecues lamb to medium-rare and serves it with orzo cooked in a kokoreç broth and greengage. Tip: For a truly filling meal, consider ordering an additional starter.;Terrace;[]
7796;Akira Back İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;Ataköy 2-5-6. Kısım Mahallesi, Rauf Orbay Caddesi No:2/1 LB, Bakırköy, Istanbul, 34158, Türkiye;40.97601;28.85687;56;false;true;Japanese;The view of the Sea of Marmara is the highlight of this modern and inviting restaurant located in the JW Marriott hotel. Be sure to go for a spot on the terrace! Akira Back has restaurants all over the world and has appointed one of his right-hand men as head chef in Istanbul. The dishes embody a distinctive fusion of predominantly Japanese and other Asian cuisines. Fine sushi, tasty gyoza, beef tataki that melts in the mouth, perfectly robata-grilled prawns… You will definitely want to come back for this contemporary whirlwind of Eastern flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7797;Sia Eli;Türkiye;Bodrum;Gümüşlük Mahallesi, 1120. Sokak No:108, Gümüşlük, Bodrum, 48970, Türkiye;37.0591274;27.2355621;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;Sia Eli takes full advantage of its environment – they grow vegetables, herbs and fruit in their five acres of kitchen garden, and catch fish in the sea a little further away. The natural splendour of the surrounding hills is also central to this open restaurant, which blends beautifully into the green setting – perfect for a romantic dinner for two! While Tolgar Mireli only serves pizza and burgers in the afternoon, in the evening he pulls out all the stops to showcase his take on Turkish cuisine. He primarily bases his dishes on vegetables, with which he creates small plates and mezze. He also serves lamb skewers, charcoal-grilled until perfectly medium-rare, accompanied by a lamb jus and spiced aubergine. Farm-to-table with a unique twist!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7798;SOTA ALAÇATI;Türkiye;Izmir;Alaçatı Mahallesi, 11039. Sokak No:18, Çeşme, Izmir, 35937, Türkiye;38.2855158;26.3755376;44;true;false;Seafood;The lobster and oyster tanks give away the fact that this open-air restaurant's main supplier is the sea. SOTA's Mediterranean soul is evident in everything from its mosaic tiles to the fresh seafood on the menu. The squid has the perfect firm texture and is seasoned to have just the right amount of zing. The seafood is super fresh and wonderful in combination with al dente tagliatelle. There is also an irresistible selection of sushi. This restaurant is dedicated to showcasing the sea's rich bounty.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7799;Rumelihisarı İskele;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yahya Kemal Caddesi No:1, Rumeli Hisarı/Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34470, Türkiye;41.0883018;29.0567222;65;true;false;Seafood;At this classic waterfront pavilion, every table enjoys panoramic views of the mighty Bosporus, with its endless stream of boats – a breathtaking setting in which to savour the finest seafood. Having sampled the aromatic mezze presented at your table, you pick your fish from the abundant selection and indicate if you would like it steamed, barbecued or deep-fried. The kitchen puts the emphasis squarely on flavour, without any unnecessary flourishes. The Iskele special, a seafood pan with octopus, prawns and more, is seasoned only with paprika and chilli.;Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7800;Sunset Grill & Bar;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kuruçeşme Mahallesi, Yol Sokak No:2, Ulus/Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34345, Türkiye;41.0641374;29.0331619;78;false;true;International;Sunset Grill & Bar could be in a Hollywood film. This spacious, upscale restaurant is located in the heights of Ulus Park, providing a magnificent view of the city and the Bosporus – be sure to ask for a table by the window. The well-heeled clientele is drawn by the attentive service, and the extensive menu, which features classic French cuisine, Asian-inspired dishes and trendy sushi options, as well as the impressive wine list. Treat yourself to one of the barbecue specialities – think butter-soft beef fillet with a brown sauce enhanced with yuzu and mustard. An exhilarating dining experience!;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7801;Tuğra Restaurant;Türkiye;Istanbul;Çırağan Caddesi No:32, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34349, Türkiye;41.0454367;29.0185555;94;true;false;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;At Tuğra you'll feel like royalty. Here you can bask in the historical splendour of the magnificent Çırağan Palace – the luxuriousness never fails to impress. Look beyond the marble pillars and admire the sparkling Bosphorus. Ottoman culinary tradition goes hand in hand with the customs of haute cuisine. Chef Emre Inanir puts his own spin on classic flavours. For instance, grilled beef liver is paired with crispy börek, deliciously unctuous on the inside, and an onion compote seasoned with sumac. What a combination!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7802;Lokanta Göktürk;Türkiye;Istanbul;Göktürk Merkez, İstanbul Caddesi No:16/E, Eyüpsultan, Istanbul, 34077, Türkiye;41.1766824;28.888588;43;false;false;Turkish;Leave the centre of Istanbul, head to Eyüpsultan district and sit down on the terrace or in front of the open kitchen. That's it, your work is done. Now all you have to do is enjoy! Muhsin Ertürk draws inspiration from, and puts a new spin on, recipes from Anatolian tradition, and has a penchant for regional produce. For instance, you can enjoy wonderfully creamy hummus, as well as prawns marinated in ginger then fried in garlic butter and served with creamy risotto, strands of soft cuttlefish and an aromatic clam broth. A creative blend of old and new!;Terrace;[]
7803;Beyti;Türkiye;Istanbul;Şenlikköy Mahallesi, Orman Sokak No:8, Florya/Bakırköy, Istanbul, 34153, Türkiye;40.9735012;28.7937759;17;false;true;Grills, Turkish;Beyti Güler is a living legend in Istanbul. Since the 1980s, Istanbulites have been coming to dine in this stylish building, a fine example of nostalgic Turkish charm, with its little fountains at the entrance and sculptures in the garden. And this historical establishment boasts no fewer than 12 dining rooms! The charcoal grill is at the centre of the kitchen, where the experienced chefs cook all kinds of meat to perfection. Take the imam bayildi, for example: meltingly tender braised aubergine topped with tomatoes, bell peppers and onions, cooked just long enough to bring out all their flavours. And be sure to try one of the kebabs, too. Traditional Turkish fare just as it should be.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7804;Mürver;Türkiye;Istanbul;Novotel İstanbul Bosphorus, Kemankeş Caddesi No:57-59, Karaköy/Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34425, Türkiye;41.0248366;28.980255;66;true;true;Grills, Turkish;Take the lift to the top floor of the Novotel Istanbul Bosphorus and discover the world of Mürver. You can start with an aperitif in the hip cocktail bar, then soak up the romantic atmosphere of the restaurant. Finally, take in the breathtaking views of the metropolis from the fabulous terrace. An open fire is the centrepiece of the kitchen, where you can also see meat and fish drying. Smoky and barbecue notes form the basis of captivating creations featuring regional produce and original combinations. The dishes are spicy, bold and fiery. Think grilled squid rings with green beans and a subtly spicy muhammara sauce, or 28-day aged ribeye. This buzzing establishment is the place to be!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7805;Borsa Restaurant;Türkiye;Istanbul;Vaniköy Caddesi No:12, Adile Sultan Sarayı, Üsküdar, Istanbul, 34684, Türkiye;41.0715736;29.0596794;68;false;true;Turkish;The Adile Sultan Palace is an events venue that is as spectacular as its name suggests. A stroll through the building will give you a sense of its grandeur and splendour – characteristics that Borsa is fortunate to share. To dine against a breathtaking backdrop of the Bosporus, head to the terrace. This upmarket restaurant showcases traditional Turkish cuisine on an à la carte basis. In his dish featuring medium-rare lamb ribs, spinach and roast potatoes, the chef allows the distinctive flavours of the ingredients to shine through. Less is more at Borsa. Make sure you leave room for dessert – the classic katmer (crispy filo pastry filled with pistachio) is very tempting!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7806;Aila;Türkiye;Istanbul;Büyükdere Caddesi No:76/B, Mecidiyeköy/Şişli, Istanbul, 34394, Türkiye;41.0651377;29.0004767;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;Aila radiates luxury and grandeur. Smooth marble, high ceilings, dark wood: the decor is a feast for the eyes. Turkey's rich cuisine is given a contemporary twist, with the focus on spices – they even have a spice library – and getting the most out of top-notch produce. This modern take on tradition should definitely be combined with a glass of raki – what a selection!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7807;İsabey Bağevi;Türkiye;Izmir;Gölcükler Mahallesi, 901. Sokak İstasyon Mevkii No:38, Menderes, Izmir, 35470, Türkiye;38.262711;27.1680009;99;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The Isabey wine estate grows mostly Sauvignon Blanc, but you will find more than impressive rows of vines on its land. Indeed, there is a magnificent terrace on which to dine in the shade of a majestic plane tree that is over 350 years old. This restaurant is committed to serving food and wine of the highest quality. The buttery lamb stock with medium-rare lamb chops and the squid stuffed with minced lamb and accompanied by a fine white wine sauce are testament to the depth and flavour of this classic cuisine.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7808;Orkide Balık;Türkiye;Bodrum;Sahil Sokak No:34, Bodrum, 48483, Türkiye;37.1194496;27.3904794;83;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Seafood;At Orkide Balik, you can almost feel the sand between your toes as you enjoy your meal. The chef takes advantage of the restaurant's location to bring fresh fish straight from the sea to your plate. But before you order your main course, be sure to check out the mezze in the refrigerated counter. The dishes are prepared without any fuss, and with that traditional sense of generosity. Think marinated squid or deep-fried sea bass with aubergine and a bechamel sauce seasoned with mustard. Sometimes the best things in life are the simplest.;Terrace;[]
7809;AŞEKA;Türkiye;Istanbul;Müeyyedzade Mahallesi, Arap Oğlan Sokak No:6, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34425, Türkiye;41.0249897;28.9774394;83;true;false;Creative;Within the walls of this rather unremarkable historical building tucked away on a side street in the Karaköy district, this restaurant with intimate lighting is done out in a tasteful palette of dark brown hues, and displays regularly changing artwork. To showcase his creativity, Ömer Akosman focuses exclusively on an à la carte approach. His dishes are not unnecessarily complicated, but bursting with flavour – spiciness and robust sauces make the difference here. An intense gravy and garnishes such as marinated tomatoes, kalamata olives and crispy polenta are the perfect accompaniment to the patiently braised beef.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7810;Zuma İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;İstinye Park No:461, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34460, Türkiye;41.1116925;29.0536931;77;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;The Istanbul branch of this chic Japanese restaurant is on a par with those in London and Dubai, among other places. That means top-notch ingredients showcased by a contemporary approach to authentic Japanese cuisine. On the menu: sushi, tempura dishes, fish from the robata grill, vegetarian options... High-quality produce and subtle influences from the East always hit the mark. Rest assured, the cosmopolitan Zuma feels right at home amid the most exclusive fashion boutiques.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7811;Mori;Türkiye;Fethiye;Fevzi Çakmak Caddesi No:24, Fethiye, 48300, Türkiye;36.6217452;29.0989774;74;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;With the azure sea against the backdrop of the majestic mountains in the distance and the palatial yachts in the marina just a few metres from your table, the terrace here is the place to be. Located at Yacht Classic Hotel, this restaurant specialised in Italian cuisine eschews unnecessary frills and focuses on flavour. Think al dente linguine with a light velouté sauce and ultra-fresh seafood such as tender squid and pink prawns. The extensive menu will not disappoint!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
7812;Barbarossa;Türkiye;Bodrum;Adnan Menderes Caddesi No:89, Asarlik Mevkii PK 225, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0223418;27.3912515;96;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;The luxurious Caresse resort's Mediterranean restaurant offers a delightfully laid-back dining experience. Watch the chefs at work in the outdoor kitchen while cocktails are shaken in the bar and chill-out music fills the air. The view of the sea and the moored yachts never gets old! Seafood takes centre stage here, cooked up in traditional Greek and Italian ways. Wonderfully crispy deep-fried squid with a fresh tartar sauce, barbecued sea bass with perfectly seasoned vegetables: the best of Mediterranean cuisine served up without any fuss. Reserve a poolside spot ahead of time and enjoy a refreshing swim after dinner.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7813;Seraf Mahmutbey;Türkiye;Istanbul;Mahmutbey Mahallesi, Peyami Safa Caddesi No:38/D, Bağcılar, Istanbul, 34200, Türkiye;41.057927;28.8200666;56;true;true;Turkish;Sinem Özler sets great store by goods from local producers. You can taste and see this for yourself, because they are also for sale in the shop of this spacious, modern restaurant, just outside the city centre. For example, she works with Trakya Kivircik lamb in a bid to keep traditional recipes alive. The İçli Köfte with the same lamb is an absolute must. To bring those ancient Anatolian flavours to the table, this chef likes to use a wood-fired oven, and she never loses sight of the changing seasons and her surroundings.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7814;1924 İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;Istiklal Caddesi, Olivya Geçidi No:7, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34435, Türkiye;41.0328811;28.9761019;76;true;false;Russian, Turkish;The original incarnation of this restaurant was opened by Russian refugees in 1924. Today diners can relive those glory days in a beautifully restored and opulent setting that exudes historical grandeur and features eye-catching panelling and mirrors. Live music makes for a buzzing atmosphere. Here they put a modern spin on Russian specialities. Think generous portions of stuffed pirozhki and beef Stroganoff, juicy meat and amazing flavour. And to drink? A glass of vodka from their impressive selection, of course!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7815;Deraliye;Türkiye;Istanbul;Divanyolu Caddesi, Alemdar Mahallesi, Ticarethane Sokak No:10, Sultan Ahmet, Fatih, Istanbul, 34110, Türkiye;41.0088794;28.9759027;72;false;false;Turkish;Deraliye is a landmark of the historical Sultanahmet neighbourhood, where there is one tourist restaurant next to the other. The colourful, opulent decor immediately catches the eye and, like the cuisine, is a tribute to the Ottoman Empire. The extensive menu features an array of dishes devised for sharing and specialities such as mezze, barbecued offerings and kebabs. Tempting options include duck stew in filo pastry with fragrant spiced rice, or a lamb and tomato dish, slowly simmered in an earthenware pot to let the flavours meld. Here, you can savour sumptuous Ottoman cuisine, occasionally presented with a touch of showmanship. Good to know: Deraliye also organises cookery classes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7816;OCAK;Türkiye;Istanbul;Hobyar Mahallesi, Mimar Vedat Sokak No:5, Fatih, Istanbul, 34112, Türkiye;41.0151056;28.9743556;18;false;true;Turkish, Traditional Cuisine;OCAK has breathed new life into this former tobacco warehouse in the Old City, turning it into an intimate restaurant with exposed brick walls, soft lighting and marble finishings. The chef proposes only a single set menu that showcases his unique take on Turkish cuisine. He elevates chickpeas to new heights in a variety of dishes, including an amazing crispy deep-fried creation. He consistently strikes a perfect balance between tradition and modernity. Your curiosity will be piqued by every dish.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7817;Levan;Türkiye;Izmir;Kuşçular, Kuşçular Caddesi No:3, Urla, Izmir, 35430, Türkiye;38.30095;26.75114;46;true;true;Turkish;Dining with a view of the vineyards, or surrounded by the grapevines on the terrace, is an experience that will leave a lasting impression. Levan offers a convivial atmosphere in a charming and intimate setting. On the chalkboard, you will find a dozen dishes, from mezze to share to main courses to savour on your own. The traditional cuisine of the Aegean coast is given a subtle new twist here. Rice-filled vine leaves served with a yoghurt cream and tomato sauce, and rich lamb stew cooked in white wine: get ready for a Mediterranean feast!;Car park,Terrace;[]
7818;The GALLIARD Vadistanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;Ayazağa Mahallesi, Cendere Caddesi No:109C, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34396, Türkiye;41.1080483;28.9867006;57;false;true;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;The upscale Vadistanbul shopping mall is home to The Galliard, a restaurant that exudes contemporary elegance and boasts a spacious waterfront terrace. The extensive menu comprises international favourites including a unique take on sea bass ceviche, creamy risotto-style creations, generous pizzas, stews quietly simmering in the background… and even soufflés for dessert! Don't be put off by the sheer number of options – these chefs work to the highest standards and their skills are second to none. Those who stay later in the evening can look forward to an electrifying DJ set.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
7819;Seraf Vadi;Türkiye;Istanbul;Ayazağa, Kemerburgaz Caddesi No:7G, İç Kapı No:7, Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34396, Türkiye;41.1113578;28.9862037;19;false;true;Turkish;Start your meal with the içli köfte, a house speciality combining a creamy yoghurt sauce with a steamed bun stuffed with highly aromatic lamb. And be sure to sample the other mezze, such as the imam bayildi: stuffed aubergine with a subtle smoky flavour, caramelised onion and candied red pepper. The main courses featuring various cuts of lamb are to die for. This contemporary restaurant not far from Vadistanbul Shopping Mall is a celebration of Anatolian culinary heritage.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7820;Vogue Restaurant;Türkiye;Istanbul;Süleyman Seba Caddesi No:92, BJK Plaza, A Blok Kat: 13, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34353, Türkiye;41.0429738;29.0018063;58;false;false;International;Iconic photographs from the archives of the illustrious Vogue magazine lend the bright interior a fashion-forward touch, but it is the views of Dolmabahçe Palace and the Bosphorus that really steal the show. The extensive menu includes everything from Turkish classics and pasta to sushi and sashimi. So, you can look forward to both a knife-cut tuna tartare with fresh spring vegetables and a beautifully risen chestnut souffle with caramel and tahini. And why not round off your evening with a refreshing cocktail and a dance?;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7821;Bağarası;Türkiye;Bodrum;Bitez, Pınarlı Caddesi No:59, Bodrum, 48470, Türkiye;37.0343987;27.3832945;78;false;false;Turkish;Authentic and welcoming are two words that sum up what Bağarası is all about. Simply to enjoy delicious food in a relaxed environment, this is the place to come. You can choose from a variety of mezze displayed in the refrigerated counter, including marinated cauliflower in red wine with caramelised onions. At the same time, you can order popular classics, such as grilled kofta or sea bass, for your main course. But do leave room for dessert, because you absolutely must try the sweet artichoke confit with ice cream – a house speciality!;Car park,Terrace;[]
7822;Orfoz;Türkiye;Bodrum;Kumbahçe Mahallesi, Zeki Müren Caddesi No:13/1, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0303417;27.439752;92;false;true;Seafood;The beautiful bay this restaurant overlooks is the pride of the Bozçağa brothers – not only for the azure waters, but also the bountiful fish and seafood they have to offer. The chefs' love for the sea is palpable in every dish, from the tuna sashimi with a light Asian touch to the oysters topped with a parmesan foam, and the perfectly grilled squid. The wine list is worth a look, as it is clearly a passion of the owners.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7823;Lokanta 1741;Türkiye;Istanbul;Alemdar Mahallesi, Profesör Kazım İsmail Gürkan Caddesi No:34, Cağaloğlu Hamamı, Fatih, Istanbul, 34110, Türkiye;41.010548;28.9755321;43;false;false;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;This beautiful contemporary restaurant with a romantic roof terrace is right next to Cağaloğlu Hamam. It serves Turkish culinary classics, some dating back to 1741, with a modern twist. The chef sometimes introduces surprising textures and flavours but never loses sight of tradition. In the evening, they serve only a more sophisticated fine dining menu. Here, you can savour a zesty sea bass ceviche, as well as lamb brochettes with distinct barbecue notes and a punchy aubergine caviar. Oenophiles should definitely take the opportunity to explore the wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7824;Calipso Fish;Türkiye;Istanbul;Küçükyalı Sahil, Cumhuriyet Caddesi No:2, Küçükyalı/Maltepe, Istanbul, 34840, Türkiye;40.9458807;29.105524;17;false;true;Seafood;Istanbul residents come to this sun-drenched restaurant to escape the hustle and bustle of the city. The waiters give expert advice on the wide selection of mezze in the display fridge – the salads are beautifully fragrant! And that's just the beginning, because the traditional preparation methods accentuate the rich flavours of super-fresh fish and seafood. Whatever you choose, the chef will cook it according to your wishes: the bluefish, for example, can be barbecued whole and served with al dente vegetables. This is ingredient-led cuisine that never fails to impress.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7825;The BARN;Türkiye;Istanbul;Gazitepe Mahallesi, Akören Cadddesi, Ören Çiftliği, No:114, Silivri, Istanbul, 34570, Türkiye;41.1363013;28.2804425;33;true;true;Regional European, Turkish;Leave central Istanbul behind and head to Grandma's Wonderland in the Silivri district. This establishment set in verdant surroundings has both a hotel and this cosy restaurant, as well as a farm that supplies poultry, vegetables and other ingredients. Local produce is treated with great respect and, specialising in plant-forward cooking, the kitchen team adopts a zero-waste approach. The menu features skewers, veal tongue pastrami with cherry sauce, kasseri cheese tortellini, spinach and a butter sauce with white wine and sage. The farm-to-table concept is taken seriously here. A spot on the terrace, in the company of the resident dogs, and with a glass of wine from the estate in hand, is a must!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
7826;Kornél;Türkiye;Bodrum;Bitez, Adliye Caddesi No:34/A, Bodrum, 48470, Türkiye;37.0435067;27.3789936;94;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Terracotta and sandy hues perfectly complement Kornél's cosy ambiance, and the terrace to the rear has that appealing Ibiza feel. The bar serves up incredible cocktails that change with the seasons, while in the kitchen, the charcoal oven works overtime baking delicious pizzettas and more. The extensive menu includes a beautiful zesty sea bass ceviche, hearty pasta dishes and a vegetarian creation featuring beetroot and dukkah. Kornél offers a relaxed dining experience with great food all year round.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
7827;Oi Filoi;Türkiye;Bodrum;Koyunbaba, Zeki Üngör Sokak No:2, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0655986;27.2418041;76;false;false;Greek;Oi Filoi is an open-air restaurant shaded by two overarching trees. The charm of this setting is accentuated by warm lighting and Greek background music. The latter is no accident: the kitchen team here specialise in serving up classic Greek dishes with subtle contemporary twists. Think medium-rare lamb souvlaki with fresh tzatziki, barbecued sweet peppers and a toasted bun drenched in meat jus. If you would prefer moussaka, you will also, naturally, find that on the menu. And be sure to take advantage of the sommelier's knowledge – her carefully selected Turkish gems are a perfect match for this cuisine.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
7828;telezzüz;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kuzguncuk, Koç Topluluğu Spor Kulübü, Kuşbakışı Caddesi No:16, Üsküdar, Istanbul, 34674, Türkiye;41.0274506;29.0422078;63;false;true;Vegan;Even before you walk into this colourful establishment, the ornate exterior hints that nature is celebrated at Telezzüz. The location, in a sports complex, is also rather unique. The restaurant clearly prioritises sustainable practices such as local sourcing, a zero-waste approach and plant-forward cooking. The chefs are creative in crafting delicious vegan dishes. Think mushroom ceviche, or deep-fried artichoke with a rich mushroom ketchup, a sweet plum and chilli sauce, olive oil mayonnaise and crunchy vegetables. And what better than a refreshing cocktail to accompany such deliciously natural food?;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7829;Kasap Fuat Çeşme;Türkiye;Izmir;Altınyunus, 3435. Sokak No:66, Çeşme, Izmir, 35930, Türkiye;38.3128604;26.3498586;37;true;false;Meats and Grills, Grills;The moment meat lovers walk into this cosy establishment with its delightful terrace at the back, their spirits are lifted. An array of cuts, expertly prepared by the butcher, awaits in the refrigerated display counter, and in the background, you can see the barbecue where the magic happens. Options include marinated ribeye, perfectly rare and with a crispy fat cap, as well as succulent burgers in house-made buns. What you see is what you get, and it's absolutely delicious!;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7830;Eleos Yeşilköy;Türkiye;Istanbul;Ümraniye Mahallesi, Yeşilbahçe Sokak No:9, Bakırköy, Istanbul, 34149, Türkiye;40.9578365;28.8217369;66;true;true;Seafood;Yeşilköy is a residential area outside the centre of Istanbul with airs of a seaside resort. A couple of streets away from the marina, you will find this exciting restaurant reminiscent of a Greek tavern. Delicious seafood is the speciality of the house. Think various mezze bursting with Mediterranean freshness. The sea bass is grilled to perfection and served simply, allowing the natural flavours of the fish to shine through. This is a great place to enjoy good no-nonsense food made from fresh, simple ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
7831;Malva;Türkiye;Bodrum;Torba, Kaynar Caddesi No:15, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0880232;27.4765606;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;Housed in luxury hotel Susona, this restaurant feels both elegant and hip. But the most stunning feature of all is the breathtaking view of the coastline. The chef and his team will be happy to tell you about their commitment to sustainability, including a zero-waste approach and close collaboration with their suppliers. Their creative cuisine draws on traditional and modern influences, celebrating the authentic flavours of the ingredients. For instance, the courgette flowers stuffed with rice and chopped mussels are seasoned with a classic blend of herbs and a judicious twist of lemon. The charcoal-grilled mussels add delightful smoky nuances. A compelling dining experience guaranteed!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7832;Amavi;Türkiye;Izmir;Alaçatı Mahallesi, 13003. Sokak No:1, Çeşme, Izmir, 35937, Türkiye;38.2840338;26.3759981;81;false;true;Creative;Alaçati is a picturesque town with a lot to offer, but Amavi is the place to be for foodies. Walk through the cocktail bar, where DJs play in the evening, and take a seat in the trendy restaurant, which exudes its own unique elegance. The chef loves working with fish, and there is even a dedicated maturation cabinet in the open kitchen. His cuisine is a vibrant expression of his personality, as seen in his innovative take on ceviche of sea bream with samphire, fried quinoa and a pomegranate jus. Or you might prefer the barbecued dry-aged sea bass with its bold accoutrements. The chef will be more than happy to talk you through his captivating dishes.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7833;Ristorante Pizzeria Venedik;Türkiye;Izmir;1382. Sokak No:10/B, Alsancak/Konak, Izmir, 35220, Türkiye;38.4321134;27.138314;90;true;false;Italian;Venedik has been a popular spot in Izmir for over 40 years. Diners are drawn by the cosy Venetian decor and Italian classics prepared in time-honoured tradition. The tempting menu has something for everyone, from al dente hand-made ravioli with a delicate shrimp filling to crispy pizza alla turca, not to mention the deliciously creamy tiramisu. This is a perennial favourite in every sense of the word.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7834;Scappi;Türkiye;Izmir;Gaziosmanpaşa Bulvarı No:1, Konak, Izmir, 35210, Türkiye;38.4282205;27.1357017;37;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;Take the lift to the ninth floor of Swissôtel and immerse yourself in the elegant setting of Scappi. It's definitely worth trying to secure a spot on the terrace, where you get to take in the views of the bay and the sea – the sunsets are simply divine! But perhaps you would prefer to home in on the action in the partially open kitchen complete with pizza oven. With great skill, the chefs rustle up dishes such as a creamy risotto with barbecued squid, al dente house-made pasta with an aromatic tomato sauce, or freshly caught sea bass with a saffron-infused lime sauce. This is a popular place, so don't forget to make a reservation.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7835;Karnas Vineyards;Türkiye;Bodrum;Çömlekçi, Sokak No:400, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.1542756;27.6545696;77;true;false;Turkish;As soon as you drive onto this family-owned wine estate, you sense that something special is about to happen. The large pond with its fountain draws the eyes, and the terrace overlooking the vines has a delightful Mediterranean feel – it's the stuff of dreams! The allure of this place leaves no one indifferent. Don't miss the chance to sample the estate's wines – the perfect introduction to Bodrum's terroir. The chef operates on a farm-to-fork principle and is also committed to sourcing local produce wherever possible. She sets great store by her ingredients, which often come from her own garden. For example, she perfectly pan-fries ultra-fresh sea bass and combines it with braised seaweed, mandarin marmalade, a butter oil emulsion and lime zest – this is a chef who brings a unique and nuanced perspective to traditional dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7836;Kurul Bitez;Türkiye;Bodrum;Bitez Mahallesi, 1936. Sokak No:2, Bodrum, 48470, Türkiye;37.0414856;27.3778774;62;true;false;Meats and Grills;In the heart of the bustling centre of Bitez, there is a garden where you can unwind amid olive and lemon trees while enjoying delicious food. Welcome to Kurul Bitez, where kebabs are the speciality of the house. You can see this for yourself at the entrance, where the spit is always turning and the bread oven is piping hot. Chef Kemal Karataş gives Gaziantep cuisine a contemporary twist. His kebab with succulent lamb, mild spices, pistachio and a subtle sweet and sour sauce is a shining example. And be sure to try his aromatic mezze appetisers – they are simply too good to be missed!;Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7837;St. Regis Brasserie;Türkiye;Istanbul;Mim Kemal Öke Caddesi No:35, Nişantaşı/Şişli, Istanbul, 34367, Türkiye;41.0477027;28.9928499;61;false;false;Asian and Western, World Cuisine;A stylish luxury brasserie like the one here in the St Regis Hotel would not seem out of place in Paris. The impressive à la carte menu offers something for everyone. Asian gyoza, Turkish mezze, Italian pasta and risotto...the choice is yours. Flavours from all corners of the globe are brought together here with great skill and care, in dishes that are unfussy and generous.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7838;Dereköy Lokantası;Türkiye;Bodrum;Dereköy, Dereköy Caddesi No:133, Bodrum, 48960, Türkiye;37.0429756;27.2858491;99;false;false;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Zişan Altınçaba's culinary approach is creative while maintaining a respect for tradition. She welcomes you warmly in her garden restaurant, where she also has a home accessories shop, and then she lets her cooking do the talking. Fruit is often incorporated for its characteristically refreshing sweetness, eg ripe nectarine lends the scorpionfish ceviche a delicate touch of acidity. However, she proves her classical know-how with her rich pâté of lamb brains and neck. Her dishes are bold – but within reason – with a penchant for fresh and zingy flavours.;Terrace;[]
7839;Aheste;Türkiye;Istanbul;Asmalı Mescit Mahallesi, Meşrutiyet Caddesi No:107/F, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34430, Türkiye;41.0291548;28.9731042;40;false;true;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Once you enter the premises, leaving the bustling Pera district behind, you have a choice between a trendy bistro and a more romantic dining space with a vaulted ceiling. In either case, you'll be charmed by the mystical ambiance and the staff's enthusiasm and dedication – and that's before you've even discovered the restaurant's modern take on mezze! Traditional Turkish specialities, such as barbecued lamb heart with roast potatoes, share the menu with in-vogue options, including vegetarian dishes. The tasting menu offers a wonderful opportunity to savour delicacies such as flaky pastry filled with a creamy tuna tarama.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7840;Giritli;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yenigüvey Sokak No:9, Cankurtaran/Fatih, Istanbul, 34122, Türkiye;41.0036487;28.9806975;70;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In summer, Giritli welcomes you to its atmospheric terrace, where the kitchen is also located. If the weather lets you down, you can always cross the street to the romantic Mediterranean-style sister restaurant. Be sure to explore the enticing mezze set menu (drinks included), which inventively showcases the traditional flavours of Crete. The perfectly seasoned and generously portioned dishes feature impeccably fresh produce. Think marinated sea bass with fresh herbs, or potato salad with a judicious touch of vinegar and vibrant tzatziki. A real feast!;Terrace;[]
7841;Kısmet Lokantası;Türkiye;Bodrum;Çırkan Mahallesi, Çelebi Kaptan Sokak No:3/A, Konacık, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0463589;27.3976748;42;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Turkish;If you're on the hunt for a lively place in which to have lunch among the locals, look no further. Kismet Lokantasi serves delicious food at great value for money in a laid-back atmosphere. Peruse the counter for traditional delicacies prepared by the chef, then choose your favourites. Think succulent meatballs with grilled aubergine and tomato sauce, and, for dessert, a rich patisserie with walnuts and just the right amount of sweet syrup – foodies will be in seventh heaven! This indulgent dining experience will leave a lasting impression.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7842;ROKA;Türkiye;Istanbul;Kılıçalipaşa Mahallesi, Meclis-i Mebusan Sokak No:14/2E, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34433, Türkiye;41.0282307;28.9877909;58;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;Are you in the mood for aubergine gently cooked in miso/soy/sesame with katsuoboshi, or would you prefer chicken given a smoky flavour on the robatayaki grill? Or how about nigiri sushi with sea bream and a crispy squid tempura? At ROKA, lovers of contemporary Japanese dishes will find a great selection to suit their tastes, accompanied by cool cocktails and fine wines. And thanks to the location on the Galataport promenade, you also get to enjoy stunning views of the Bosporus at this stylish, lively restaurant.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7844;Hakkasan İstanbul;Türkiye;Istanbul;Muallim Naci Caddesi No:62, Kuruçeşme/Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34345, Türkiye;41.0570261;29.0356958;16;false;false;Cantonese, Chinese Contemporary;Luxury chain Hakkasan likes to establish itself in vibrant cities, and Istanbul is obviously no exception. This restaurant enjoys a prime location at the Mandarin Oriental Bosphorus, which boasts stunning views over the water and exudes Asian elegance with a personal touch. The crispy duck salad, a classic of the house, is a shining example of how Cantonese cuisine is revamped here: the duck skin is incredibly crispy, the meat combines a fine spiciness with a mild sweetness, and the salad offers an interesting contrast with juicy pomegranate. Delicious! And it's absolutely worth taking a look at the exclusive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7845;Park Fora;Türkiye;Istanbul;Muallim Naci Caddesi No:54/A, Cemil Topuzlu Parkı İçi, Kuruçeşme/Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34347, Türkiye;41.0540913;29.0346905;47;false;true;Seafood;Grilled, meunière, steamed, tandoori – however you like your fish, Park Fora has it covered. At this traditional seafood restaurant, the produce is always in season and super fresh. As you enter, you will see crates of the day's catch stacked and waiting and numerous aquariums filled with king crabs, lobsters and other creatures. Specify your cooking preferences – for us, it was sole à la meunière – and then savour! It will be cooked to perfection and accompanied by carefully prepared accoutrements. Factor in the waterfront location, with views of the boats coming and going on the Bosphorus, and you will really feel like you are on holiday!;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7846;29;Türkiye;Istanbul;Ulus Mahallesi, Ahmet Adnan Saygun Caddesi, Ulus Parkı İçi No:71/1, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34340, Türkiye;41.0645826;29.0320829;90;true;true;Turkish, Mediterranean Cuisine;As soon as you enter, you realise how exceptional this upscale restaurant is. The views of the bustling Bosphorus, the enchanting minarets and the Istanbul skyline are unparalleled! To really make the most of your fine dining experience at the elegant 29, book a table on the expansive terrace. The generosity and spiciness of traditional Turkish cuisine are given a subtle modern twist, often incorporating Mediterranean touches. Both the authentic mezze and the smooth mushroom risotto make this place the trip. Featuring an impressive selection of top-flight labels, the extensive wine menu is worthy of attention.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7848;Banyan;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yıldız Muallim Naci Caddesi & Salhane Sokak No:3/2, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34347, Türkiye;41.0476321;29.0250625;42;true;false;Asian Contemporary;Dinner at Banyan is a real experience. As you take in the view of Ortaköy Mosque and the action on the Bosporus through the large windows, choose an aperitif from the fabulous selection available at the cocktail bar, where a DJ plays the hottest beats. The food is not to be underestimated: expect modern Asian dishes and spicy flavours with fish as the main focus. The menu includes exquisite sushi options, prawn gyoza and chicken with a spicy green curry sauce. And even if you turn up after 10.30pm, the kitchen will still be open with a shorter menu. Very cool!;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7849;Kıyı;Türkiye;Istanbul;Haydar Aliyev Caddesi No:186/A, Tarabya/Sarıyer, Istanbul, 34457, Türkiye;41.1392295;29.0543849;37;false;true;Seafood;If you're looking for an atmospheric seafood restaurant adorned with beautiful paintings and affording breathtaking views of the picturesque marina, then this perennial favourite is the place for you (ask for a table upstairs)! Start with a selection of mezze and then choose from the bountiful array of fish and seafood, which will be prepared according to your desires. Our inspector opted for sole from the display fridge, which was flawlessly pan-fried before being filleted at the table. It's all about the produce here!;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
7850;Atölye;Türkiye;Istanbul;Süzer Plaza, Asker Ocağı Caddesi, Elmadağ Caddesi No:6, Şişli, Istanbul, 34367, Türkiye;41.04042;28.99202;87;true;true;Turkish;The fine dining restaurant of the Ritz-Carlton hotel boasts a laid-back but luxury vibe. The colourful interior and views of the sea and Besiktas football stadium will draw your eye. Authentic Anatolian recipes are prepared with generosity, sometimes with a dash of innovation and often with a fresh Mediterranean touch. Spicy mezze, aromatic hummus, freshly caught sea bass, rich pide: this is the place to come for authentic flavours accompanied by fine wines.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7851;Khorasani;Türkiye;Istanbul;Alemdar Mahallesi, Ticarethane Sokak No:9/B, Fatih, Istanbul, 34110, Türkiye;41.0084723;28.9761704;92;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Grills;The Sultanahmet neighbourhood is known for all its tourist restaurants, where menus consist of photographs of dishes. In that respect it's no different at the rustic-style Khorasani, but what sets this grill restaurant apart is the chef's dedication to quality. The meat, barbecued to order, and the kebabs are second to none. We thoroughly enjoyed the kebab with succulent lamb, crisp vegetables and, of course, the wonderful pita bread that comes with it. For flavoursome food with no nonsense, Khorasani is the place.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7852;Avlu Restaurant;Türkiye;Istanbul;Cankurtaran, Tevkifhane Sokak No:1, Fatih, Istanbul, 34122, Türkiye;41.0065385;28.9802023;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Turkish;Every detail of the Four Seasons hotel in Sultanahmet exudes luxury. One of the hotel's hidden treasures is its Mediterranean-style courtyard. In this tranquil oasis, you can relax and escape the hustle and bustle. Your meal starts with some delicious bread from the wood-fired oven and continues with this fresh take on indulgent Turkish fare. The chef strikes the perfect balance between rich manti stuffed with beef, the freshness of buffalo yoghurt and the pep of spiced butter and a pulled beef marmalade. The extensive and varied selection of Anatolian delicacies is impressive!;Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7853;Çok Çok Thai;Türkiye;Istanbul;Asmalı Mescit Mahallesi, Meşrutiyet Caddesi No:51/A, Beyoğlu, Istanbul, 34430, Türkiye;41.0326396;28.9752061;21;false;false;Thai;Take a seat on the lively terrace at the front or opt for the authentic interior, and let your mind drift off to exotic Thailand. Here you can enjoy typical dishes such as sweet and sour spring rolls with crunchy vegetables and a spicy aubergine and pepper curry. Crisp, fresh produce, authentic flavours and respect for tradition make this a great place to eat.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7855;Spago;Türkiye;Istanbul;Mim Kemal Öke Caddesi No:35, Nişantaşı/Şişli, Istanbul, 34367, Türkiye;41.0479564;28.9927312;52;true;true;International;The rooftop of the upscale St Regis Hotel is the place to soak up those hip Istanbul vibes. Sip a delicious cocktail on the terrace that affords sublime views of the city (such romantic sunsets!), sit at the long bar or simply enjoy the lounge music and modern luxury that surrounds you. The kitchen is overseen by Wolfgang Puck, who creates a unique blend of Italian, Californian and Asian influences. Expect sophisticated flavours and techniques, home cooking and international panache. Be sure to try the smoked salmon pizza, as well as the duck spring rolls with their spicy hoisin sauce and sweet plum sauce.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7856;Lokanta Feriye;Türkiye;Istanbul;Yıldız Mahallesi Çırağan Caddesi No:44, Beşiktaş, Istanbul, 34347, Türkiye;41.0473717;29.02462;77;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Dining in the gardens of the fully refurbished Feriye Palace is a new experience each time. Here on the edge of the Bosphorus – some diners even arrive by boat – you have the ever-evolving backdrop of the constant coming and going of the ships. And there is something magical about the view of the illuminated Ortaköy Mosque and Bosphorus Bridge, especially when you have a delicious cocktail in hand. This restaurant strikes a fine balance between chic and relaxed, and the service is attentive. The chefs, who can be seen at work in the open kitchen, let the ingredients speak for themselves. Their dishes are not overly elaborate, but rather classic fare with subtle zesty and spicy nuances. They give aubergine purée a delightful tang by mixing in yoghurt, making it an excellent accompaniment to barbecued lamb.;Great view,Terrace;[]
7857;Fauna;Türkiye;Istanbul;Küçükbakkalköy Mahallesi, Işıklar Caddesi, Ahmet Muhip Dranas Sokak No:9/A, Ataşehir, Istanbul, 34750, Türkiye;40.9845726;29.1099044;85;true;true;Italian;Lunch at Fauna is the perfect excuse to visit the Ataşehir district, just outside the city centre. You sit at long tables, often next to other diners, and watch the pasta being freshly made behind the counter. At Fauna, Italian and Turkish cuisine come together in rich, shareable dishes. Think ravioli with a hearty Karayaka lamb and walnut filling. The superb sorbet of organic strawberries, with a creamy texture and nicely tart, is just one example of the focus on local produce. Booking is strongly recommended!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7858;Tuti;Türkiye;Bodrum;Yokuşbaşı Mahallesi, Suluhasan Caddesi No:18, Bodrum, 48400, Türkiye;37.0417447;27.4410374;90;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The rooftops of Bodrum, the azure sea, even some Greek islands: the view you have from the top floor of The Marmara hotel is truly breathtaking! The restaurant has a Mediterranean feel and that also applies to the food.. Traditional recipes are revamped with great skill and local produce. The crispy manti with minced meat, yoghurt and chilli oil is a shining example. Be sure to treat yourself to the legendary baklava, too!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7859;Hakkasan Bodrum;Türkiye;Bodrum;Gölköy Mahallesi, 314. Sokak No:10, Bodrum, 48483, Türkiye;37.1284851;27.4111577;23;false;false;Cantonese, Modern Cuisine;Located in the Mandarin Oriental hotel against the wonderful backdrop of the glistening Aegean Sea, and with an elegant dining space done out in wood, this floating open-air restaurant is stunning. Hakkasan is a renowned chain bringing a luxurious take on Cantonese cuisine to your table. Think authentic Peking duck or grilled lamb chops, but elevated with fresh garnishes and rich sauces. For a chic night out, Hakkasan is just the place!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
7861;Aldehyde;France;Paris;5 rue du Pont-Louis-Philippe, Paris, 75004, France;48.85496;2.3554;59;true;true;Creative;In this intimate establishment near the Quais de Seine, Tunisian-born chef Youssef Marzouk cooks up a delicious culinary symphony in his open kitchen-bar. Flanked by two assistants with equally prestigious pedigrees (Cheval Blanc Paris, Carlton, Ritz, Jacques Faussat), at dinnertime he puts together a single surprise set menu featuring a subtle marriage of French tradition and North African flavours. His confident technique shines through in his meticulously plated creations, bolstered by his Tunisian sensibility, which you can detect in his sparing use of spices, herbs and citrus fruits: saddle of lamb done two ways, grilled summer vegetable foam, meat jus with smoked eel etc.;Air conditioning;[]
7862;Les Résistants - La Table;France;Paris;7 rue de la Fidélité, Paris, 75010, France;48.8743773;2.3558924;99;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This new restaurant has been opened by the owners of Les Résistants, enthusiastic advocates of small-scale farming. On the menu: meats from local breeds, seafood from small boat fishing and, to wash it all down, a selection of "living" wines sourced from 150 producers. The natural decor reflects their philosophy: raw materials, wood, stone and glass panes that let light stream in, and a predominantly green colour scheme. The chef delivers modern, instinctive dishes that make the most of seasonal ingredients, such as his starter of agnolotti del plin, lamb ragout and apricot confit.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7865;Fossé Saint Ange;France;Richelieu;2 rue du Chantier, Richelieu, 37120, France;47.0115646;0.3240681;94;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A new duo has taken over this well-known institution in the pretty village built by Cardinal Richelieu in the 17C. The period varnished wood façade opens onto a bistro-style interior with a warm and friendly atmosphere, where good cheer and good food are the order of the day. The chef keeps things simple: a menu that changes every month, featuring traditional dishes that are firmly rooted in the seasons and spiced up with the odd exotic touch, such as an Asian-inspired guinea fowl raviolo. The desserts, too, hold their own.;Terrace;[]
7866;Lo Fieu;France;Saint-Alban-de-Roche;55 route de Lyon, lieu-dit La Grive, Saint-Alban-de-Roche, 38080, France;45.5982769;5.2311456;93;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In his "country-style restaurant with a wood fire" (Lo Fieu means "fire" in the local dialect), Romain Hubert and his friendly young team work hard to keep the traditional cuisine of the Dauphiné region alive. A series of comforting and flavourful dishes are prepared right in front of you: soup from the cauldron with Trept chickpea , fried fish from Lake Bourget, sausage (pork or fish) served with gratin dauphinois, and then there is the trolley packed with appetising desserts. The converted barn, which has been restored in a rustic style and wows with its impressive dimensions, provides the perfect setting.;Car park;[]
7867;Colette;France;Les Salles;La Plagnette, Les Salles, 42440, France;45.8432189;3.8202884;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the Forez region, this group of large stone and timber buildings nestles between a fir forest and a lake. The property is conducive to kicking back on the terrace in summer or, in winter, to embracing the hygge lifestyle by the imposing fireplace in the cosy restaurant room. The cooking of chef Thomas Laurier (Maison Pic and Dame de Pic, Chabichou) proves to be comforting and indulgent: an excellent pâté en croûte (a speciality served in different variations throughout the year) and, for dessert, fresh poached peach accompanied by lemon balm from the garden and buckwheat – a little culinary gem. The chef's partner takes care of the restaurant floor, where there is rarely a free table to be had.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7869;L'Ogustin;France;La Vacquerie-et-Saint-Martin-de-Castries;2 place de l'Ormeau, La Vacquerie-et-Saint-Martin-de-Castries, 34520, France;43.7892849;3.4605124;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Not far from the Cirque de Navacelles, in a small village on the southern edge of the limestone plateau that is the Causse du Larzac, Pricillia Lebon's restaurant is housed in a converted inn. Beneath the stone vaults, the inviting, cosy decor reflects the endearing personality of a chef who has come to this beautiful, isolated setting to cook. The surprise set menu celebrates the Larzac area, with ingredients sourced mainly via short supply chains (not least from local market gardens), as well as from mushroom and plant picking. Plants reign supreme in the intuitive, light and aromatic dishes. The dessert is a tribute to the chef's Malgasy origins, with a sweet potato cream spiked with vanilla. Vegetarian options are also available. A unique and authentic place.;Wheelchair access;[]
7870;La Bistronomie;France;Angoulême;16 rue Raymond-Poincaré, Angoulême, 16000, France;45.6485212;0.163029;97;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this contemporary bistro, the chef cooks up dishes that are as straightforward and satisfying as the name of his restaurant suggests – and it's a joy to experience. Bistro-style recipes (think French onion soup, beef tartare, chocolate mousse) sit alongside traditional specialities, on which he puts a savvy new spin. A case in point would be the grand veneur sauce, in which red wine meets cherries, or the chicken ravioli with tarragon. The indulgent and beautifully prepared desserts are also worth trying – for example, figs roasted in honey and toasted hazelnut crumble with rosemary ice cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7871;Ploc;France;Paris;15 rue Saint-Blaise, Paris, 75020, France;48.8596204;2.405059;70;false;true;Modern Cuisine;"Cities should be built in the countryside, because the air is so much purer there" (Alphonse Allais): this almost seems to be the case in the old village of Charonne, in this neighbourhood bistro tucked away in a bucolic cobbled street. Inside, the atmosphere is laid-back and lively, relaxed and friendly. The menu is inspired by wholesome ingredients, carefully sourced from small-scale producers. When it comes to the dishes, there is no shortage of skill or flavour – just look at the salsa verde that accompanies the leeks, and the bear's garlic pesto on the toasted brioche, topped with a walnut labneh, green asparagus, peas and roasted button mushrooms. Selection of natural wines.;Terrace;[]
7872;Jium;France;Paris;26 rue Tiphaine, Paris, 75015, France;48.8486878;2.2966502;17;false;false;Korean;Behind a rather nondescript façade lies an authentic Korean canteen which boasts a lovely vintage vibe and is popular with a clientele from the land of the Morning Calm. It is the brainchild of photographer and guesthouse owner, Kim Hong-Seung, and his wife Sun-Hee, a former fashion designer. As well as bibimbap classics, the menu is packed with authentic delicacies (soft shell crabs, oyster fritters) and unusual recipes (seafood pancakes, kimchi stew, pork shoulder and tofu, etc). You can season these culinary delights with homemade soy sauce (or not) before finishing with a dessert, also homemade, illustrated by vanilla-flavoured rice pudding with red beans and caramelised pecan nuts.;;[]
7874;L'Altro Frenchie;France;Paris;9 rue du Nil, Paris, 75002, France;48.8676278;2.3474885;91;true;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Grégory Marchand strikes again with his eclectic take on dining! In this modern Italian-style bistro, diners will also detect the British and American influences of which the chef is so fond. On the menu: a crudo misto with a series of ingenious vegetable condiments, classic dishes like pappardelle with rabbit or a must-try cotoletta alla milanese (veal chop for two). As for the chocolate cake, it is a homage to the recipe devised by Jamie Oliver at London's River Café. The wines are supplied by Frenchie, the wine shop just next door.;Air conditioning;[]
7876;Marie Akaneya;France;Paris;12 rue Godot-de-Mauroy, Paris, 75009, France;48.8708104;2.3269424;40;false;true;Japanese, Barbecue;This is Paris's first sumibiyaki-style restaurant. Particularly popular in Kyoto, this cuisine is prepared with top-drawer ingredients, not least the Wagyu that is shipped here from Ito Ranch, a beef farm on the outskirts of the town of Matsusaka – and according to the Japanese themselves, this is the ultimate breed of Kobe beef. Everything is cooked over the famous binchotan charcoal, which is made mainly from Ubame oak wood – every table in the restaurant has its own barbecue taking pride of place. Some of the menus feature Fukuroi's renowned Crown Melon, which can sometimes fetch a price of several thousand euro.;Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
7877;Habile.;France;Paris;16 rue de Lancry, Paris, 75010, France;48.8697513;2.3607333;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Our chefs and their partners are never short of bright ideas for new ways to dine. After the trend for caves à manger and restaurants with delis, this place unites bistro and knitwear. Upstairs, fashion designer Camille Andrieux showcases her sartorial creations, while chef Éric Fontanini cooks up generous, no-frills meals: The pâté en croûte with pork and foie gras, and the line-caught bluefin tuna, simply seared and served on a delicious compote of onions and peppers, are good examples. As an added bonus, the kitchen is open 11am-11pm (excluding the lunch set menu). The colourful decor is delightfully dapper, and you can even eat at the counter and see the chef at work.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7878;Les Incontournables;France;Manosque;3 boulevard Casimir-Pelloutier, Manosque, 04100, France;43.8337645;5.780964;26;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Here, the "incontournables" in question are the ingredients: the cooking revolves around produce sourced within a 100km radius of Manosque, which is lovingly prepared by a pleasant chef who prioritises flavour over technique to create no-nonsense Provençal-inspired cuisine: 7hr lamb shoulder, morel mushroom and walnut wine risotto, organic peach confit... Plus service with a smile.;Air conditioning;[]
7879;Le Socle;France;Nice;17 rue Barla, Nice, 06300, France;43.7019063;7.2829999;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set back from Place Garibaldi, this little bistro has found its place on Nice's restaurant scene. It is run by a team of two chefs who have experience working in top establishments: chef Dominique Roca (L'Atelier Robuchon Étoile, for example) and, front of house, her partner Mikhaël Lyoubi (Flaveur in Nice with the Tourteaux brothers, to cite but one). Carefully chosen, good-quality fresh ingredients, such as the red mullet on this occasion, a choice of accompaniment (eg sautéed potatoes or roasted vegetables), a fine selection of wines that covers all the regions – and with that the deal is sealed. Appealing lunch set menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
7880;Azimut;France;Annonay;21 rue Montgolfier, Annonay, 07100, France;45.2401324;4.6729266;43;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This wine bar/cave à manger serves locavore cuisine whose flavours are drawn from locally sourced and, often, organic ingredients (including free-range poultry, snails from Eyrieu, lentils, fish from a fish farm near Châtillon-en-Diois, olives from Nyons). At lunchtime, there is a short and very reasonably priced set menu, and in the evening you can choose from the list of plates for sharing ("platarges"). To be washed down with organic or sulphur-free wines from a terrific selection – and the recommendations are on point!;;[]
7882;Le Puy Tilleul;France;Tournemire;La Borie d'Hélipse, 5 chemin du Moulin, Tournemire, 15310, France;45.0524654;2.482207;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Dominated by the feudal castle of Anjony (15C), the village of Tournemire has preserved its stone houses with stone slab roofs that are so typical of the Cantal region. This establishment, a splendid stone and corten steel complex, blends in perfectly. The contemporary dining space offers a breathtaking view of the sunset. The menu is an ode to marine ingredients. Sprinkled with seaweed and briny condiments, the menu is a meticulous showcase of fish and shellfish, and also takes in skilful surf-turf combinations. For all that, the Cantal terroir has not been overlooked: market gardeners, livestock farmers and local fish farmers are also well represented. An ambitious culinary affair.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
7884;Chablis Wine Not;France;Chablis;Rue des Moulins, Chablis, 89800, France;47.815152;3.8006993;100;true;false;Meats and Grills, Traditional Cuisine;In this world-famous wine-growing village, a "wine bistro" is bound to be a hit. Picture the scene: a local entrepreneur, two Japanese chefs who are huge fans of French cuisine, top-notch ingredients (house-made tapas, charcuterie and purebred meats that have been perfectly matured), and an amazing wine list at bargain prices (to sample here or take away). Local patrons and wine-loving tourists mingle here, and a positive atmosphere reigns. To be consumed in moderation!;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7887;Minore;France;Paris;4 avenue Trudaine, Paris, 75009, France;48.8819837;2.3459928;74;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This "two-in-one" locale – a cocktail bar with a terrace and a traditional fine dining restaurant – is the brainchild of a pair of industry professionals: Japanese chef Katsuaki Okiyama (known from him previous restaurant, Abri) and bartender Hugo Combe. In this pared-back decor, the chef shows he is a dab hand. Shining examples are his signature dish (artichokes, morels, beef marrow and pan-fried foie gras, shallots and chive flowers, served in a casserole pot), or his recipe for monkfish, courgette and nasturtium flowers, topped with a powerful saffron sauce. This modern cuisine comes in the form of a single set menu, to which you can add other dishes.;Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
7889;L'Atelier du Goût;France;Vire Normandie;20 rue Émile-Desvaux, Vire Normandie, 14500, France;48.8367963;-0.8831974;74;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the upper reaches of Vire, this contemporary bistro was born of a friendship between two chefs, Jordan Lebascle (previously sous-chef at Ivan Vautier) and Clément Gosselet (former sous-chef at Manoir de la Pommeraie). They deliver a modern cuisine de terroir, taking advantage of the abundance of ingredients that Normandy and local producers have to offer – think translucent cod in semi-salted butter, served with crispy potato chips and tarragon cream.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7890;Yut Fei;China Mainland;Fuzhou;3F, Sino International Plaza, 137 Wusi Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.0995918;119.3020893;99;true;false;Cantonese;This smart restaurant comes complete with a manicured garden, a main dining room and lavish private rooms. The Cantonese head chef, well versed in Cantonese barbecue, sizzling claypot dishes, and dim sum, has been practising his art for over 20 years. He prides himself on his double-boiled soups, slow-cooked for four hours to allow flavours to mingle. Stewed Silkie chicken soup in coconut uses coconut juice instead of water for a nutty-sweetness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7891;Fuyuan;China Mainland;Fuzhou;No.40, Huaqiao Xincun, Xierhuan North Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.0900699;119.2763831;88;true;true;Fujian;This pink villa is a private-room-only restaurant specialising in the cuisine of Fuqing City, Fujian, with clear Putian-style culinary influences. Seafood like razor clam and shrimp is the house signature. The crispy Fuqing oyster fritter brims with cabbage, oysters, razor clams and pork. Pickled bamboo shoot gives razor clam soup a kick and the bivalves coated in sweet potato starch stay plump and juicy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7892;Rong Ji Hai Xian Lao Hua (Cangshan);China Mainland;Fuzhou;161 Liaoyuan Road, Cangshan, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.0482035;119.2785651;15;true;false;Noodles;Lao hua, or Fujian-style noodle soup, is usually considered frugal eats. This shop, however, champions a novel lao hua that uses luxury seafood such as live abalone and razor clam. The modern, cosy room is also worlds apart from your average lao hua stall. Just indicate your favourite toppings and noodles to the server. The kitchen team will then cook them to perfection. Also try pork head meat dressed in Sichuan pepper sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
7893;Lvdao Seafood;China Mainland;Quanzhou;447-451 Jiu'er Road, Shishi, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.7347253;118.6291455;58;true;true;Fujian;In 1989, Lvdao opened its doors with only six tables. Nowadays, it has turned into a leading F&B chain in Shishi and this flagship establishment now spans two floors. Though it specialises in Fujian fare, especially seafood, there are some Cantonese options on the menu. Try the umami-laden swimmer crab – the locals prefer it steamed with black sticky rice or taro balls. Round off with custard-filled buns, best enjoyed with sweet peanut soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
7894;Qing You Yu;China Mainland;Quanzhou;2F, 535 Huaifu Road, Fengze, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.890274;118.599983;49;false;true;Seafood;The owner inherited the family business in 2021 and relaunched the restaurant here. As always, the incredible range of live seafood on offer is the main draw – just look at the three-tier fish tanks at the entrance. Diners are expected to choose their own seafood from the tanks, but servers are more than happy to help. Chilled swimmer crab boasts melty roe and firm, flavourful meat. Swamp eel braised with tea seed oil and basil is silky and aromatic.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7896;Jiang Nan Yuan;China Mainland;Quanzhou;401, Building 27, Zone A, Yuanhe 1916 Artdistrict, 610 Xinmen Street, Licheng, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.9167895;118.574563;62;false;false;Vegetarian;Only two set menus are offered, with 11 or 12 ovo-lacto vegetarian courses, which can be made vegan upon request. They change according to the solar terms in Chinese calendar and the more expensive menu includes gourmet ingredients like bird’s nest. As opposed to typically light-tasting vegetarian food, the dishes here pack oomph and intense heat. Richly flavoured, shredded wild rice stem with pea kernels is seasoned with chilli oil and mushroom sauce.;Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
7897;Hatter;China Mainland;Fuzhou;433 Guxi Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.092887;119.295602;50;true;true;European Contemporary;The owner is a returnee from Australia who has worked closely with the chef to develop two tasting menus that mirror the seasons. The menus bear a strong European slant and star first-rate produce from around the world with occasional local ingredients such as Fuzhou condiments like red wine lees and sa cha sauce. The compact dining room sports a casual continental vibe, perfect for date nights and friendly get-togethers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7898;1927 Dong Yuan Si Chu;China Mainland;Xiamen;65 Siming East Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4597408;118.0774134;51;false;true;Fujian;This private dining concept in a historical mansion (c 1927) comes complete with a Suzhou-style garden. Despite its proximity to a busy road, it offers tranquil respite. With just 10 private rooms across three levels, reservations are a must and menus can be tailored. Items available may vary, but you can expect deftly prepared Xiamen fare such as double-boiled pork shank soup with green olives and whelks, or braised abalone with ginger duck.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
7899;Xuanhe Cuisine;China Mainland;Fuzhou;Shop 3013, 3F, Art Mall, Rongqiao Center, 100 Jiangbin West Avenue, Taijiang, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.0623536;119.2731335;65;true;true;Fujian;The wood-rich interior feels warm and cosy and the food, in the same vein, is comforting and familiar. The menu stars the hits of Fuzhou cuisine and cleverly uses local ingredients to create authentic flavours. Expect items like fried pork belly marinated in red vinasse, razor clams and sautéed sticky rice cake with mud crab. The quick-fried crisp duo, jellyfish and pork kidney in sweet and sour sauce, is another bestseller.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
7900;Xia;China Mainland;Xiamen;1F, Lohkah Hotel & Spa, 277 Penang Road, Huli, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.5303837;118.1785038;17;false;true;Cantonese, Fujian;Since 2018, Chef Yang hailing from Jiangsu has been helming the kitchen with a menu that is half Cantonese and half Minnan. Chilled peanut sweet soup is a modified version of the Fujian classic, with a velvety peanut custard over a bed of toothsome algae. The west-facing views over Wuyuan Bay make Xia the perfect spot for a romantic dinner at sunset.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7901;Lucheng;China Mainland;Xiamen;39F, Conrad Hotel, 186 Yanwu West Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.441536;118.09574;74;true;true;Fujian;Perched atop the city’s sail-shaped landmark, Lucheng commands fantastic views. Traditional Chinese motifs are stylised and melded with elegant fixtures and fittings for comfort. The kitchen team of Fujian natives managed by a young Minnan chef excels in Fujian classics with creative twists, showcasing the province’s wide range of produce. Try deep-fried starchy taro in aged vinegar reduction, and braised river eel with fish maw and pickled cabbage.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
7903;Antstory;China Mainland;Quanzhou;7 Buzhengya Lane, Wudianshi, Jinjiang, Quanzhou, China Mainland;24.823816;118.584851;26;false;false;Fujian;Since 2018, Antstory has been running this historic three-storey red brick villa. The young local chef reinterprets traditional Fujian recipes with modern techniques. First-timers can pick from ‘10 classics’, like Shima five-spice pork roll and braised yellow croaker with scallion. The chef’s vinegar pork is a new take on the Quanzhou classic – pork marinated in apple cider vinegar, deep fried and served with wafer and macadamia nuts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
7904;Xing Wang Seafood · Rongting Hui (Siming);China Mainland;Xiamen;Shop 017, 4F, Xinghe COCOPark, 81-89 Zhanhong Road, Siming, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4776885;118.1842222;57;false;false;Seafood;The seafood chain started out as a fishmonger’s back in 1994. It began running a roadside food stall in 2016 and rebranded itself in 2023 with this upmarket flagship in a shopping mall. Live fish tanks are showcased next to a museum-like display of 100+ taxidermy crustaceans. Pick your favourite seafood from the tanks and specify how you want it cooked. The menu also offers other Minnan specialities to accompany your meal.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7905;Harmony Garden (Xierhuan North Road);China Mainland;Fuzhou;No.32, Huaqiao Xincun, Xierhuan North Road, Gulou, Fuzhou, China Mainland;26.0905159;119.2753237;36;false;false;Fujian;With nine private rooms in a two-storey villa, Harmony Garden offers warm, friendly service and Fujian cooking with creative twists. The owner used to run a tea leaf business, which explains the antique tea ware and tea leaves on sale. Signatures include stir-fried sliced conch in red yeast rice wine lees, which marries lingering aromas and a crisp texture. Drunken pork ribs are deep-fried before being tossed in a tangy wine vinegar glaze.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7906;Yin Lu;China Mainland;Xiamen;Building 66, Gulong Inhabitancy Park, Shangzhong East 2nd Road, Huli, Xiamen, China Mainland;24.4937207;118.1628212;90;false;true;Fujian;This household name opened its doors in 1996 and moved to this historic villa in 2009. The kitchen specialises in Xiamen classics and the menu is concise yet appetising. Don’t miss the ubiquitous double-boiled Muscovy duck soup with crab, whose robust meaty flavour melds with seafood umami. It is best enjoyed with Xiamen rice noodles that suck up the goodness. Other favourites include oyster omelette and deep-fried five-spice rolls.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
7907;Pari-;Thailand;Chiang Mai;8-10 Samlarn Road, Phra Sing ,Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7635;98.99289;90;true;false;Asian;The cosy design and small counter foster a vibrant, relaxed dining experience. The small yet high-quality dishes combine Japanese Izakaya style with Thai ingredients, enhanced with wasabi or yuzu. The ham comes from a Yunnan village in Chiang Mai, perilla from Mae Hong Son, sashimi-grade fish from the south, and meat from organic farms. We recommend the corn-fried rice Yunnan ham and the house-made ponzu sauce, elevated by a refreshing Somsa citrus oil.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7908;Kinu by Takagi;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 48 Soi Charoen Krung 40, Charoen Krung Road, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.72394;100.5157;55;false;true;Japanese;Hidden behind sliding wooden doors, Kinu's décor combines Japanese and Thai influences, featuring teakwood crosshatch flooring and a mix of Japanese and northern Thai ceramics. Chef Takagi excels in Kyoto-style Kaiseki, highlighting the natural flavours of top Japanese ingredients. The bar offers an excellent sake collection, and a matcha tea ceremony marks the end of your visit. Additionally, welcome drinks are served in a Japanese-style Minka area.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7910;Fish Club;Thailand;Chon Buri;Andaz Pattaya Jomtien Beach  345 Mu 3, Na Chom Thian, Sattahip, Chon Buri, 20250, Thailand;12.7927363;100.9093742;17;true;false;Seafood;Fish Club's location on a serene beach sets it apart from the typical Pattaya dining scene. With indoor and outdoor dining, the restaurant combines a pleasant view with a lively atmosphere. The menu reveals Western and Asian influences, and the chefs excel at grilling, controlling temperatures perfectly. The peanutty sriracha sauce pairs impeccably with your steamed or grilled seafood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
7911;Ayutthayarom;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;1/1 Mu 7, Ban Pom, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3533407;100.5461571;93;false;true;Thai;Situated in a pleasant, cool, and shady location, the riverside offers seating in small Thai pavilions and boasts views of a golden pagoda. The space is decorated in traditional Thai style, in keeping with the cuisine, which features intense local flavours. Try the sour soup with fresh chilli and squid, and the aromatic, flavoursome fried river fish in chu chi curry. Round off your meal with classic Thai desserts made with fresh coconut milk.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7912;Jamn;Thailand;Bangkok;8 Soi Chan 43 Yaek 41, Bang Khlo, Bang Kho Laem, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7000793;100.5278437;28;true;false;Thai;Jamn offers a private dining experience in a family home. The menu is customised to your preferences or features typical Thai dishes. Their family set menu includes an appetiser, dessert, and a main course presented in the Thai samrap style with five dishes for sharing. We recommend starting with the crispy shrimp paste rice with sweet tiny shrimp and sour mango. A minimum charge per table is required.;Air conditioning;[]
7914;NAVAN NAVAN;Thailand;Chiang Mai;55 Mu 7, San Pong, Mae Rim, Chiang Mai, 50180, Thailand;18.9331204;98.9606077;32;true;true;Creative;Surrounded by rice fields, this stand-alone cement building affords a clear view of the open kitchen. The chef draws on various cuisines and uses a charcoal grill to cook local ingredients. His unpretentious style promotes healthy eating, and each dish highlights the natural flavours of the ingredients. Arrive before sunset to see the beautiful garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park;[]
7915;Palmier by Guillaume Galliot;Thailand;Bangkok;Four Seasons Private Residences,  300/1 Charoen Krung Road, Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7121789;100.5100075;92;true;false;French;In 2024, French chef Guillaume Galliot brought this classic yet relaxed brasserie dining experience to Bangkok. Take a seat outdoors to enjoy views of the Chao Phraya River and a menu composed of classic French dishes, signature creations and innovative offerings. The culinary delights include foie gras terrine and Boston lobster confit. A passionate sommelier is on hand with recommendations from an extensive French-focused wine list to match the food.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7916;Indian by Nature;Thailand;Chon Buri;306 Chateau Dale Complex 64-68 Thappraya Road, Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.9062737;100.8693833;78;false;false;Indian;This fine dining spot delivers authentic Indian cuisine in an inviting ambiance featuring contemporary Indian paintings and decorative touches. With creative twists on North Indian staples, highlights include chicken tikka and dal makhni. Main dishes are thoughtfully served in small pots over a flame to keep them warm. For solo diners, the traditional thali sets comprise tasty samples of signature à la carte dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
7917;Shrimp Noodles Ao Kae;Thailand;Phuket;76 Phoonphol Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8761748;98.3882778;70;true;true;Noodles;It has been crafting meticulous shrimp noodle bowls for over a decade. Tom yum and original shrimp flavour noodles, available as wet and dry options, come with the perfect number of condiments. Pork wontons are the standout! For intense flavour, try the dry tom yum noodles.;Cash only;[]
7919;Chop Chop Cook Shop;Thailand;Bangkok;328 Yaowarat Road, Chakkrawat, Samphanthawong, Bangkok, 10100, Thailand;13.7414382;100.5076979;17;true;false;Thai-Chinese;Housed in a five-storey Art Deco building, this eatery pays homage to its goldsmith heritage through its design. Chef David Thompson has been garnering acclaim for his Chinese cuisine with Thai touches since opening in 2023. High-quality ingredients that elevate tradition go into his refined yet honest food. Start with the crispy prawn wafer, and don't miss the roasted duck soup… but save room for the ginger milk curd – as simple as it is delightful.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7920;Sushi Saito;Thailand;Bangkok;Four Seasons Private Residences, 300 Charoen Krung Road,  Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7125411;100.5100477;41;false;false;Sushi;Located in the Four Seasons Private Residences by the Chao Phraya River, Sushi Saito is the sister branch of the renowned Tokyo restaurant by Chef Takashi Saito. Specialising in Edomae-style sushi, it showcases chef Maruyama’s skills and Edo-period techniques. The restaurant embraces classic Japanese décor, featuring an atrium with a drinks bar and a dining area with a Hinoki cypress counter-table around an open kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7921;Pak Mor Robot;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;82 Benchama Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2282755;104.8534929;58;true;true;Small eats;The chef owner of Pak Mor Robot has satisfied the tummies of locals for over 30 years. She prepares a variety of Vietnamese dumplings in a steamer at the front of this neat little outlet. The signature, her own invention, is the incredibly tasty Vietnamese dumpling with fried eggs.;Cash only;[]
7922;Bangkok Bold (Pathum Wan);Thailand;Bangkok;LGF, Central Embassy, 1031 Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7441907;100.5460855;70;true;false;Thai;Word-of-mouth inspired Chef Nhoi to take the leap from cooking studio in the old town to opening a restaurant in the city centre. Her aim is to preserve the heritage of Thai taste that’s ‘basic and bold’ with creative twists. Check out the unique stir-fried pork and shrimp, hummingbird flowers, fish sauce and scrambled eggs. And the spicy salted beef in coconut cream is tender with balanced flavours, enlivened by fresh shallots and bird's eye chillies.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7923;Fried Banana Rama 5 (Bang Kruai - Sai Noi Road);Thailand;Nonthaburi;116 Bang Kruai - Sai Noi Road, Bang Si Thong, Bang Kruai, Nonthaburi, 11130, Thailand;13.8231029;100.47929;64;false;true;Street Food;This spot is best known for its deep-fried bananas. Coated in crispy batter made from coconut and white sesame, they exude a rich coconut aroma. The sweet potato balls are another standout. Be prepared for queues during peak hours.;Cash only;[]
7924;TAAN;Thailand;Bangkok;25F, Siam@Siam Design Hotel, 865 Rama 1 Road, Wang Mai, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7470692;100.5269622;33;false;true;Thai contemporary;Like the Siam@Siam Design Hotel Bangkok in which it sits, this rooftop restaurant takes a contemporary approach yet retains an authentic Thai character. The chef produces a seasonally changing tasting menu that uses entirely Thai produce, all of premium quality. Dishes are well-presented, showcase great skill from the kitchen team and often have a story behind them. Try one of the restaurant’s signature cocktails, which are also crafted with local ingredients.;Car park,Great view;[]
7925;Wah Lok;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, Carlton Hotel Bangkok Sukhumvit, 491 Sukhumvit Road, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7344739;100.5644051;30;false;false;Cantonese;A Singaporean institution for over 3 decades, Wah Lok boasts a strong following, several awards, and this sibling outside Singapore. The plush carpeted dining room sports high ceilings and a stylish mix of modern and classic details. The food is artistically plated and made with premium imports such as Boston lobster, which is consummately braised and enhanced with ginger and spring onion. Book in advance, especially for the expertly crafted dim sum lunch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7926;Klang Na Pla Khao;Thailand;Chon Buri;5 Mu 9, Nong Tamlueng, Phan Thong, Chon Buri, 20160, Thailand;13.391982;101.0796405;65;false;false;Thai, Isan;This country-style restaurant serves up a splendid array of Isan dishes and Eastern Thai specialties from land and sea. The highlight is a spicy stir-fry with an original curry paste recipe from Chanthaburi province, capturing the authentic essence of Thai cuisine. There's no compromise on bold, genuine Thai flavours. The tranquil outdoor setting affords views of lush green rice fields, and the relaxed atmosphere makes it perfect for friend and family gatherings.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7927;Kang;Thailand;Chiang Mai;Jing Jai Market, 46 Atsadathon Road, Pa Tan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8059769;98.9957837;48;false;true;South East Asian;Opened in 2023, Kang is a fresh addition to Jing Jai Market. It offers a cosy retreat with a laid-back approach to dining, plus a menu that's ideal for sharing the highlights of Indonesian, Malaysian and Thai cuisine with friends. We suggest opting for their signature Nasi Lemak, or one of the bold, aromatic curries. All dishes are made to order, so diners may need to have a little patience while waiting for their delicious meals.;Air conditioning;[]
7928;Khrua Ban Po Ta;Thailand;Chon Buri;23 Soi Pattaya Tai 8, Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.924521;100.8917078;59;true;true;Seafood;The breezy, spacious dining room surrounded by vines and plants makes for a relaxing and laidback coastal ambience. The seafood-based menu features shrimp, squid and crab options cooked several ways. The stir-fried squid with black ink sauce is a showstopper, but diners also enjoy shelling the stir-fried whole crab with curry powder. The sweet local seasoning enhances the food's natural umami.;Car park,Cash only;[]
7929;ÎNT;Thailand;Bangkok;Rooftop F, Best Western Sukhumvit 20, 17 Soi Sukhumvit 20, Sukhumvit Road, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7320324;100.5641362;66;false;false;Thai contemporary;Ascend to this rooftop restaurant to soak up an ambiance of elegant earthy tones blended with a subtle blue hue, all set against the warmth of an open kitchen. The tasting menu reflects Chef Patin 'Knock' Promsawadi and his team's unique, artistic approach to simplicity. Using French culinary techniques, he strikes a masterful balance between Thai and French ingredients to produce contemporary dishes that capture the essence of Thai cuisine. Advance booking necessary!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7930;Khaan;Thailand;Bangkok;14/3 Soi Som Khit, Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7471397;100.5460168;73;false;true;Thai contemporary;The new restaurant of Chef Sujira 'Aom' Pongmorn, Khaan – meaning both "tiger" and "proclaim" in Thai, roars with impressive Thai flavours, while shining a spotlight on ingredients and the provinces from which they're sourced. The chef's use of modern techniques means her culinary creations, served in an elegant space decked out in deep red hues, retain all their characteristic depth. Opt for the tasting menu, paired with wine or tea, to elevate the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7931;Sushi Saryu;Thailand;Bangkok;GF, Kronos Sathorn Building, 46 North Sathorn Road, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7250227;100.5386518;21;true;false;Sushi;Saryu, a name that symbolises the precious passing of time, is set behind a discreet wooden door that leads into a lounge-cum-cave. The minimalist dining area sports a traditional omakase counter made out of Hinoki wood. Chef Seiji Sudo meticulously crafts a 15-course omakase menu based on seafood sourced directly from Tokyo’s Toyosu Fish Market. With a mere 6 seats available daily (or 8 for private groups), reservations are essential.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
7932;Wagyu Steakhouse;Thailand;Phuket;Twinpalms Phuket Resort, 106/46 Mu 3, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9768734;98.281847;65;false;true;Steakhouse;Spanning two floors of the Twinpalms hotel, this restaurant’s elegant yet earthy interior and dimmed lighting make it the perfect setting for steak and wine lovers. Everything is on display: from the chefs in the open kitchen and the nice beef showcase with a small oyster bar, to the choice cuts of top-quality imported meats. Guests can choose their steak from the fridge before it is expertly grilled by the chefs. A choice of five high-end brands of knives is also on offer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
7933;Pa Porn Traditional Pork Noodles;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;121/2 Mu 8, Soi Pa Maphrao 10, U Thong Road, Hua Ro, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3627951;100.5707678;71;true;false;Noodles;Auntie Porn has mastered pork noodle soup for over 50 years, initially on her boat at age 17, now on land. Her Tom Yum soup boasts expertly prepared noodles, rich broth, and toppings like minced pork, fish sausage, or BBQ pork, complemented by red shrimp and peanuts. She also offers tasty fish balls.;Cash only;[]
7934;Nusara;Thailand;Bangkok;336 Maha Rat Road, Phra Borom Maha Ratchawang, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.745672;100.4915418;51;true;true;Thai contemporary;Chef Thitid 'Ton' Tassanakajohn, renowned for his work at Le Du, leads this inviting restaurant, presenting classic Thai cuisine with a modern twist. The cooking style leans more towards tradition, paying homage to Ton's grandmother and family recipes. Quality ingredients from across Thailand shine in impressive dishes, paired ideally with diverse wines. The top-floor lounge offers a perfect spot for pre-dinner champagne with a view of Wat Pho.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
7935;Gaggan;Thailand;Bangkok;68 Soi Sukhumvit 31, Sukhumvit Road, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.74159;100.56737;16;false;false;Innovative;Sit front-row at Gaggan’s immersive 14-seater chef’s counter, an experience featuring changing light effects and a thumping soundtrack. Chef Gaggan’s bold personality shines through in the 22-course tasting menu, sharing apocryphal stories and a vibrant narrative. His progressive Indian cooking, using modern techniques and global ingredients, crafts intriguing dishes, each telling a unique story.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
7937;Sang Thatien;Thailand;Bangkok;75 Maha Rat Road, Phra Borom Maha Ratchawang, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.74468;100.49202;78;false;false;Thai;Formerly an ice factory, this small eatery retains some of the interior structure and incorporates vintage décor in a dining room decorated with basic wooden furniture and collectibles. The chef embraces seasonal Thai ingredients, especially fruit, to produce unique, signature dishes in a home-cooking style, such as strawberry salad with shrimp paste and caramelised pork and spicy plum mango salad. The crab meat with fresh herbs and spicy sauce is unmissable.;Air conditioning;[]
7938;Pa Noi Beef Noodles;Thailand;Udon Thani;57/8 Sisuttha Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.4102877;102.7918669;37;true;true;Noodles;The aroma of beef noodle soup greets diners at this popular eatery. The distinctive tamarind chilli paste pairs perfectly with deep-fried chicken skin or mixed into the noodles. The boat noodles with rich flavours are also a must-try.;Cash only;[]
7939;Bang Dean;Thailand;Phang-Nga;16/10 Mu 1, Phet Kasem Road, Bang Nai Si, Takua Pa, Phang-Nga, 82110, Thailand;8.8688072;98.3447908;15;true;false;Street Food;Nearby the Takua Pa Government Office, this street food place serves Thai-Muslim dishes, including excellent chicken biryani, plus crispy rotis paired with savoury curries or sweet condensed milk and banana. Open for breakfast through late lunch, it closes when the food runs out.;Cash only;[]
7941;Peang-Prai;Thailand;Phuket;101/18 Soi Namtok Bang Toei, Ban Pa Khlok Road, Pa Khlok, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;8.0416989;98.3951171;16;false;false;Thai;In the depths of the forest at the entrance to Bang Pae waterfall, two wooden pavilions stand connected by a terrace walkway. Here, a family-run restaurant faces a lagoon and a verdant wall of forest, while diners are accompanied by the welcoming calls of birds and gibbons. The tranquil ambiance is joined by traditional Thai and Southern Thai cooking, with local Phuket dishes standing out. Seasonal local clams are delicious and can be cooked many ways, including stir-fried with chilli paste.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7942;Khao Kriab Pak Mor Talat Na San Jao;Thailand;Surat Thani;Na San Jao Market, Tonpo Road, Talat, Muaeng Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.1458005;99.3260457;53;true;true;Street Food;The veteran stall-owner has been making her delicious dumplings for decades in this famous food cart in Na San Jao market. The thin steamed rice dumplings combine a sweet, gooey texture with a savoury filling, made with minced pork, crushed peanuts and herbs in creamy coconut milk.;Cash only;[]
7943;Day & Night;Thailand;Surat Thani;83/25 Liang Mueang Road, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.1061059;99.3287262;90;true;true;International;This enchanting, almost English-looking country pub draws tourists like bees to honey. Boasting a bright, breezy vibe, it serves international favourites, from steak to pizzas and light snacks, with a tempting array of cocktails and craft beers. The fresh watermelon topped with dry salmon and served with a spicy salad dressing is sweet and juicy, while another popular local delicacy, bingsu, salted egg yolk, offers a creamy scent and texture. Smooth live music in the evenings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
7944;Lenzi Tuscan Kitchen;Thailand;Bangkok;69/2 Soi Ruam Ruedi 2, Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.737625;100.55078;25;false;false;Italian;It’s a family affair at this authentic Tuscan restaurant, from the top-notch meats and cheeses sourced from chef Francesco Lenzi’s family farm in Pisa to his mother’s limoncello. The chef uses traditional cooking techniques from back home and often pops out of the open kitchen to greet diners like family. Start with antipasti or an iI primi like Risotto Taleggio e Tartufo and then try the flavoursome Filetto Alla Rossini. Reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
7945;Sra Bua by Kiin Kiin;Thailand;Bangkok;GF, Siam Kempinski Hotel, 991/9 Rama 1 Road, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7486372;100.53521;95;false;true;Thai contemporary;Inspired by its sister restaurant, Copenhagen's Kiin Kiin, Sra Bua is one of Bangkok’s original purveyors of modern, innovative Thai cuisine. À la carte and tasting menus are available, with their dishes – from street food starter to dessert – proving creative and original, yet respectful of traditional Thai flavours. Premium international ingredients are used throughout, while both alcoholic and non-alcoholic pairings are available to complete the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7946;Reunros (Yan Nawa);Thailand;Bangkok;Bangkok Square, 762/2 Rama 3 Road, Bang Phongphang, Yan Nawa, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.6727243;100.534187;26;true;true;Chinese;When Ruenros opened 40+ years ago, its owner came from a medical background, hence the focus on herbal and medicinal braised dishes. The 3rd generation heir now runs it and he chooses all the market fresh ingredients himself every day. Specialties include spring rolls using a family recipe, stir-fried goat with celery, fried rice with salted fish and slow-cooked soup, which is packed with flavour. For dessert, try the taro purée with sticky rice.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7947;Canvas;Thailand;Bangkok;113/9-10 Soi Sukhumvit 55, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7288565;100.5807471;51;false;false;Innovative;Food meets art at Chef Riley Sanders' plush establishment. Every dish of the culinary journey is depicted as a painting on the menu, like an art gallery brochure. The talented Texan sources seasonal ingredients from all over Thailand and transforms them with a modern interpretation. Counter seats offer views of the chefs, while tables upstairs offer more privacy. Wine pairings are available to complete the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
7948;Yamazato;Thailand;Bangkok;24F, The Okura Prestige Bangkok, 57 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7426915;100.5480908;85;false;true;Japanese;The Okura Prestige’s Japanese restaurant boasts 3 dining areas: a sushi bar, teppanyaki grills and a stylish dining room. The fish is sourced weekly from Toyosu market in Japan, and they offer a rotating selection of sashimi options, depending on availability. Dressed in traditional kimono, the staff make every effort to ensure that diners have a great experience, while the panoramic high-rise cityscape offers a romantic setting that couples adore.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7949;Ta Khai;Thailand;Phuket;Rosewood Hotel, 88/28, 88/30-33 Muen-Ngoen Road, Pa Tong, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.8863115;98.2715;97;false;false;Thai;Ta Khai means ‘fishing net’, and here diners can choose live seafood from the restaurant’s tank before a chef scoops it up and cooks it. Dishes, including the deep-fried white snapper with fish sauce, are flavoursome, with spicing slightly toned down if you wish, while two set menus offer a variety of items to try. Ask for a table on the lovely terrace for a panoramic view of the bay and cityscape beyond – or for something different, book a BBQ sala.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7950;Aunt Aoy Kitchen;Thailand;Chiang Mai;377 2 Chiang Rai Road, Suthep, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7952137;98.964349;27;true;false;Thai;The décor is simple, with a display of photos and messages on post-it notes from customers gone by. Aunt Aoy spent much of her career cooking in hotel kitchens. Her expertise is realised in the fluffy yet crispy Chef Omelette with stir-fried minced pork, salted egg and pork crackling.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
7953;Baan Landai;Thailand;Chiang Mai;252/13-14 Phra Pok Klao Road, Si Phum, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7941249;98.987436;54;true;true;Thai;Don’t let the slightly unkempt exterior keep you from visiting Chef Landai’s restaurant. The interior exudes charm with its eclectic décor and a window into the kitchen, where chefs whip up pan-Thai dishes like flavourful pork ribs with red wine sauce. The portions are suitable for sharing with friends, and don’t forget to save room for their traditional Thai desserts.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7954;Punjab Grill;Thailand;Bangkok;GF, Radisson Suites Bangkok Sukhumvit, 23/2-3 Soi Sukhumvit 13, Khlong Toei Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7440519;100.5577897;54;true;true;Indian;Like its sister restaurants in India and across the world, Bangkok’s Punjab Grill serves authentic yet contemporary Northern Indian cuisine. The menu features creative twists on dishes like chaat, which includes chutney-dressed avocado and puffed rice with yoghurt espuma. Equally flavourful are classics like biryani and tikka. Vegetarian dishes are offered à la carte and as part of tasting courses. A glass wall in the elegant dining room provides a view of the tandoor action.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7955;The House by Ginger;Thailand;Chiang Mai;199 Mun Mueang Road, Si Phum, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7927655;98.9932033;46;true;false;Thai;Open for decades on the edge of the old city, this stylish and quirky spot serves a mixture of Northern Thai classics and those with a more modern twist. Premium ingredients like New Zealand beef are a feature, as are organic vegetables and daily picked herbs from their nearby Ginger Farm. The seasonally changing menu includes the Chiang Mai platter – an ideal way to sample an array of dishes. Pair your food with one of their many lovely cocktails and to extend your evening, continue on to the House Lounge next door.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7956;Vacca;Thailand;Khon Kaen;99 Mu 20, Airport Road, Sila, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4602343;102.7858119;60;true;false;Italian;Italian chef-owner Fabio Colautti's restaurant near Khon Kaen Airport offers authentic Italian flavours with homemade pasta, wood-fired pizzas, and grilled meats. Opened in 2015, it boasts a classic Italian ambience with a cosy white interior, a large wine cellar, and an open kitchen. Highlights include the Vacca pizza and the grilled Wagyu rib-eye.;Air conditioning;[]
7957;Rimsaun;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;200 Phu Khao Thong Soi 5, Pratu Chai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3537873;100.5509345;76;true;false;Thai;The owner hails from Nakhon Sri Thammarat and has been serving quality southern Thai cuisine in the ancient capital for over 25 years. Despite its simple décor, the restaurant with its high vaulted ceilings, shady garden and lack of walls is well worth visiting. The southern Thai sour curry with fish is a family recipe and a must-try, while the fried prawns are glazed in a delectably sticky tamarind sauce. Keep an eye out for the daily specials on the white board.;Car park,Cash only;[]
7958;Embassy Room;Thailand;Bangkok;9F, Park Hyatt Hotel, 88 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.744175;100.5471335;97;false;false;Spanish, Catalan;Embassy Room offers authentic Catalan cuisine with à la carte options and tasting menus. The chefs are happy to personalise dishes to cater to dietary needs. The Bomba rice dishes are perfect for rice lovers, while the private room is ideal for intimate gatherings. The outdoor seating boasts views of the sky garden. For Spanish wine aficionados, the wine list features over 100 labels from seven regions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
7960;We-La-Dee;Thailand;Chiang Mai;291 Mu 9, Nong Chom, San Sai, Chiang Mai, 50210, Thailand;18.8442104;99.0284337;53;true;true;Thai;We-La-Dee brings central Thai cuisine north in an airy industrial-style dining room marked by playful accents. The restaurant’s large collection of action figures and a floor-to-ceiling installation of artificial flowers inspire photographs. Its extensive menu, which includes some original recipes from the chef, inspire both relaxed meals with family and friends and afternoons spent sipping coffee or tea and enjoying dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7962;Thian Leng Bak Kut Teh;Thailand;Phang-Nga;35 Mu 4, Phet Kasem Road, Khok Kloi, Takua Thung, Phang-Nga, 82140, Thailand;8.294028;98.3009029;97;true;true;Thai-Chinese;Using heavenly recipes from Kedah, Malaysian Bak Kut Teh is a divine pork rib soup with Chinese herbs, served in a clay pot. The succulent slow-cooked meat simply slips off the bone. The chef is so confident about its tastiness, there’s a money-back guarantee for those who disagree!;Cash only;[]
7963;Nern Khao View Talay;Thailand;Phang-Nga;18/6 Mu 10, Soi Namtok Wat Khao, Khok Kloi, Takua Thung, Phang-Nga, 82140, Thailand;8.2922347;98.3116858;84;false;false;Thai;Nern Khao View Talay offers stunning views of mountains and sea from up high on a hill. Serving Thai and southern cuisine, the stir-fried pork with shrimp paste is a highlight. The aromatic paste mixes nicely with herbal notes and deep-fried shallot, while the thick sour curry soup with shrimp has a deep orange colour, tasty acacia omelette and plump shrimps. What about tackling that steep slope? There’s a shuttle service from the car park at the foot of the hill.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
7964;Dhabkwan;Thailand;Nonthaburi;Dhabkwan Resort, 178, 180, 182, 184 Nonthaburi Road, Suan Yai, Mueang Nonthaburi, Nonthaburi, 11000, Thailand;13.8555679;100.4852384;63;true;false;Thai;Located in a teak house in the middle of Dhabkwan Resort, this traditional Thai restaurant opens onto a tranquil lotus pond and inviting gardens. The atmosphere perfectly matches the authentic Thai menu, which includes hard-to-find dishes like Miang Kam with lotus petals and santol curry with roasted pork. Making it even more authentic, meals are served on Benjarong porcelain. Dhabkwan also offers Thai cookery classes and is available for events.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7965;Banrimbung;Thailand;Nakhon Pathom;372/21 Mu 2, Nong Din Daeng, Mueang Nakhon Pathom, Nakhon Pathom, 73000, Thailand;13.8092233;100.0022003;29;false;true;Thai;Serving family-style Thai cuisine on a large pond in Nakhon Pathom since 2001, the spacious restaurant offers waterside seating in five distinct seating areas with live music during dinner. Everything on the menu is fresh, with the fish and seafood kept alive until cooked. Two highlights are stir-fried prawns with shrimp oil and fried seabass with fish sauce and spicy green mango salad. The restaurant is family-friendly, with a kids’ zone in the garden for young diners to enjoy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
7966;Jay Jia Yentafo;Thailand;Bangkok;564 Rama 4 Road, Maha Phruettharam, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7351163;100.522798;82;false;true;Noodles;For 30+ years, office workers have been making a beeline to Jay Jia Yentafo for their eponymous pink-noodle soup and legendary homemade shrimp balls. The soup packs a knockout combination of shrimp, fish, fish sticks and fried wontons and explodes in sour and spicy notes.;Cash only;[]
7967;Jao Nai Fish Ball (Bang Khae Road);Thailand;Bangkok;103/14 Bang Khae Road, Bang Khae, Bangkok, 10160, Thailand;13.697419;100.42131;49;true;false;Noodles;Nestled in a vintage townhouse, this popular street food joint serves up savory fish ball noodle soup. Expect fresh, made-to-order meals that might require a wait due to the frequent bustle. However, the wait pays off with homemade seafood like fish balls, fish dumplings, and fish cakes, all enhancing the soup's umami taste.;Cash only;[]
7968;Samut;Thailand;Phuket;14/119 Mu 1, Rawai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83100, Thailand;7.7818113;98.3101011;54;true;true;Southern Thai;Samut (or ocean) is set in a traditional Thai-Chinese building decorated in an Oriental style, with dark teak wood. Previously the lobby of the adjacent hotel, it’s now a gastronomic destination. The set menu, with more than 10 dishes, tours the island’s coastline, offering seafood caught by local fishermen. The chef respects the traditions of the island, selecting flavours and fruits inspired by local creativity, including a reinterpretation of Phuket dim sum.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7969;J'AIME by Jean-Michel Lorain;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, U Sathorn Hotel, 105/1 Soi Ngam Du Phli, Thung Maha Mek, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7181298;100.5460559;46;true;false;French Contemporary;As you enter this restaurant, your world becomes a little topsy-turvy, with a grand piano suspended from the ceiling and upside-down chandeliers. Protégés of the eponymous Jean-Michel Lorain craft thoughtfully designed set menus that use Thai ingredients while staying true to French roots. The dishes are a masterful fusion of local flavours and French techniques, with each plate narrating the chef’s culinary artistry.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
7970;Royal Osha;Thailand;Bangkok;99 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.734719;100.546135;32;false;true;Thai contemporary;A majestic twist on its sister restaurant in San Francisco, Royal Osha aims to engage the senses with enticing flavours, aromas, textures, sights and sounds. The setting is a sleek, modern dining room decorated with Thai art. Start with a cocktail inspired by Ramakien characters, before enjoying dishes like the excellent tom yum kung mae nam (spicy, sour soup with river prawns infused with Thai herbs) and the (seasonal) chilled rice served with accompaniments.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
7971;Sushi Masato;Thailand;Bangkok;3/22 Soi Sukhumvit 31, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.73445;100.5661107;21;false;true;Sushi;The Japanese seas provide a rich bounty of seasonal delights: spring offers an abundance of fresh shellfish, while winter brings the indulgence of rich, fatty fish. At Sushi Masato, guests enjoy this premium seasonal produce flown in daily from Tokyo's renowned Toyosu Market. The experience is elevated by Chef Masato's exceptional techniques, perfected over his years in Japan and New York. You may request to be served by Chef Masato when making a reservation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
7972;100 Mahaseth;Thailand;Bangkok;100 Mahaseth Road, Si Phraya, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7290445;100.5183206;85;false;false;Isan;This nose-to-tail inspired offal restaurant serves elevated Isan fare made from quality locally sourced ingredients. The chef takes great care to balance the flavours and present attractive plates. The Isan complementary set includes somtam, crispy pork skin with Thai chimichurri and chaeo sauce. The hot and sour soup with baby pork ribs and chamuang leaves has lovely acidity with a hint of shrimp paste. Check the blackboard for Thai aged steak specials.;Air conditioning;[]
7973;Mana;Thailand;Khon Kaen;420 Mu 21, Sri Chan Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.43119;102.83004;99;false;false;Thai-Chinese;After working for years at Thai-Chinese restaurants in Bangkok, chef-owner Mana returned home to open his own outlet. He’s now been serving flavoursome Thai-Chinese-style seafood dishes that are easy on the pocketbook for over a decade. Inside his restaurant’s one-storey white building are two dining areas, one with AC and another open-air one. The oyster omelette and crispy salad with fish maw, shrimp and cashews are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
7974;Baan Suan Mae Rim;Thailand;Chiang Mai;261 Mu 2, Chiang Mai-Fang Road, San Pong, Mae Rim, Chiang Mai, 50180, Thailand;18.9443268;98.945395;20;true;true;Thai;Although this restaurant is outside the city centre, it’s worth the drive for its Thai cuisine, and especially its northern dishes, served in a beautiful, natural setting. Open for more than a decade, the place consists of several northern Thai-style pavilions, which all face a pond – and you can also dine in the open air. Either way, there are tranquil views of the trees, pond, and rice fields. Deep-fried snakehead fish with hot and spicy sauce is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7976;Sornthong;Thailand;Bangkok;2829-31 Rama 4 Road, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7194173;100.5664357;100;true;true;Seafood;For quality seafood that won’t burn a hole in your pocket, look no further than Sornthong. Easily identified by the crowds dining beneath a large yellow sign in Thai and Chinese, this family-run shop has done a booming trade in prime fresh fish for more than 20 years. Ingredients are taken from tanks outside the restaurant, then cooked under the watchful eye of Mr. Chai – fried oysters with creamy eggs and a sweet-sour-spicy chilli sauce are a must-try. Away from the sea, keep an eye out for the well-marinated grilled pork satay.;Air conditioning;[]
7977;Hong Khao Tom Pla;Thailand;Phuket;5 Kra Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.876661;98.3931984;69;true;true;Thai;There is always a queue in front of this small shop. The mainstay on the menu is seafood. Dishes are carefully prepared by the owner, and the fresh prawns are a must. Check the whiteboard for the daily catch.;Cash only;[]
7978;Aeeen;Thailand;Chiang Mai;4/13 Mu 5, Suthep Road, Suthep, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7707417;98.9484343;95;false;true;Vegetarian;Aeeen goes the sound of Ken’s unique laughter, according to wife Yuki. Under the concept of Neo Shojin Ryori, the Japanese couple craft their plant-based menu using seasonal ingredients. The dining areas span two floors of a cute wooden house that feels like rural Japan. Lines of jars contain the fermented ingredients they use in the food. We recommend the perfectly judged soymilk udon noodles and refreshing mango with ginger and honey drink.;Car park,Cash only;[]
7979;Yung Khao;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;111 Mu 4, Thanaratch Road, Nong Nam Daeng, Pak Chong, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30130, Thailand;14.630968;101.4106916;24;true;false;Southern Thai;Originally from Bangkok, they relocated to Pak Chong 10 years ago. The building is made from wood and bamboo, like many rural rice granaries (yung khao). On offer is southern-Thai dishes, using ingredients from the south as well as their own curry paste, to cook grandmother’s recipes. The deep-fried sand fish is a great starter and the yellow curry seabass emits a gloriously pungent turmeric aroma. Diners on the outdoor terrace enjoy a view of the mountains.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Terrace;[]
7980;Methavalai Sorndaeng;Thailand;Bangkok;78/2 Ratchadamnoen Klang Road, Bowon Niwet, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.7561226;100.5021073;85;false;true;Thai;One of the city’s original Thai fine dining restaurants, they’ve maintained a loyal customer base for 60+ years, using the same timeless recipes and cooking techniques. The refined dishes are complex, delivering blasts of flavour. Highlights are crispy rice noodles in sweet and sour sauce, spicy lemongrass salad, and crab meat and acacia red curry. The curry pastes are made from scratch and fishcakes from featherback fish. Small parties should book the private room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
7981;Gen (Vadhana);Thailand;Bangkok;Vibes Ekkamai,  267/31 Soi Sukhumvit 63, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.734352;100.58715;15;true;true;Japanese;This trendy spot for yakitori and drinks has a slight vintage feel not dissimilar to a Japanese whisky bar. Smartly dressed staff offer traditional Japanese service, while the menu includes ingredients flown in from Japan – including the prized Hitachiwagyu beef. A variety of dishes are available, not just yakitori, including sashimi, rice and noodles. If you’re lucky, you’ll get to try one of their multiple Japanese eel dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
7982;Khao Horm;Thailand;Ko Samui;34/36 Mu 4, Bo Phut, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.5616557;100.0606586;15;false;false;Southern Thai;Just 5 minutes from the airport, Khao Horm is a great spot to get your last-minute fill of delicious Southern Thai and local recipes before flying home. The family recipes have been passed down from generation to generation for over a century. We recommend the stir-fried minced pork whose yellow curry paste features a gutsy mix of spices. The main dining room is set in a large open-air pavilion. They also offer AC indoor dining and plenty of parking too.;Car park;[]
7984;Jum Khao;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;104/4 Thetsaban 26 Road, Pak Chong, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30130, Thailand;14.7075293;101.4225221;43;false;true;Isan;Modestly designed, Jum Khao embraces local influences and serves Isan fare with a little flair. There are a few à la carte and seasonal dishes but a wide variety of som tum options, popular comfort food like crispy grilled chicken wings, golden-brown garlic chips and Korat-style stir-fried rice noodles. The tricolour sticky rice combines butterfly pea purple, turmeric yellow and the natural white and is served with three dips and raw vegetables in a cute bamboo basket.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Great view;[]
7985;Maze;Thailand;Bangkok;114/3 Set Siri Road, Sam Sen Nai, Phaya Thai, Bangkok, 10400, Thailand;13.7800618;100.5325814;55;true;true;Northern Thai;Opened in 2020 by chef May Thongthong, this fine dining restaurant serves two set menus: Northern Thai Creations and Seasonal Creative. The first explores Chef May’s Lanna heritage, while the second plays with European techniques and flavours. The contemporary décor and lighting set the stage for the well-presented dishes. The main dining room includes an open-bar kitchen and counter seating. Above it, a private room seats 10.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
7986;Savelberg;Thailand;Bangkok;136/1 Soi Yen Akat 2, Chong Nonsi, Yan Nawa, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7126814;100.5484509;45;true;true;French Contemporary;Food and mood pair well at Dutch chef-owner Henk Savelberg’s eponymous restaurant, now in a contemporary house in Chong Nonsi. The sparkling dining room features an open kitchen, a refined wine cellar and garden views, with private group dining available. The menu boasts adventurous, modern, colourful French dishes with a classical base, made from fine international ingredients. Rounding out the experience is the professional service. Booking is essential.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
7987;Anuwat;Thailand;Phang-Nga;201 Mu 4, Phet Kasem Road, Thai Mueang, Phang-Nga, 82120, Thailand;8.393566;98.2595103;38;true;false;Street Food;There may be a big sign out front, but it’s the aromatic pork that’s been luring in the locals for more than 40 years. The grilled pork, BBQ pork and crispy pork belly are well marinated and grilled till succulent. Try any or all — plus steamed chicken — on a single plate served with rice.;Cash only;[]
7988;Lertrod;Thailand;Phuket;17/7 Nai Yang Road, Sakhu, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;8.1004373;98.3071751;43;false;true;Thai;Across from the airport, this bright air-conditioned restaurant flies under the radar but lands simple, satisfying central and southern Thai fare. The skilled chef sources quality ingredients from local farmers and fishermen. The deep-fried seabass with fish sauce never disappoints. For the spicy southern-Thai sour curry, choose from pickled bamboo, coconut shoots or pineapple. The photo-filled menu, written in Thai, English and Chinese, makes it easy for everyone.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
7989;Kruvit Raft (Ban Laem Hin);Thailand;Phuket;98/7  Ko Maphrao, Mu 6, Ko Kaeo, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.9372108;98.4132289;46;false;false;Seafood;To reach this floating restaurant near Ko Maphrao, take a 5-min boat ride across sparkling waters reflecting the sunshine. Onboard, panoramic views, a gentle breeze and uber-fresh seafood await. The distance from sea to plate couldn’t be shorter. Start with a freshly picked coconut before tucking into delicious southern and central Thai seafood. The grouper soup with Chinese soybean paste and stir-fried black tiger prawns with salt and chilli are highlights.;Great view,Terrace;[]
7990;Rongros;Thailand;Bangkok;392/16 Maha Rat Road, Phra Borom Maha Ratchawang, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.7442674;100.4916545;68;true;true;Thai;Meaning ‘House of Flavours,’ Rongros preserves the taste of traditional Thai cuisine on the banks of the Chao Phraya River with a stunning view of Wat Arun. Highlights include the green curry with rib eye beef served with roti and the tangy glass noodle salad. The vintage décor, including the chandeliers, painted Chinese panels, and wooden furniture only add to the experience. Book a table on the terrace for dinner to take in the view at sunset. Keep in mind that this restaurant is a favorite spot for tourists, so it's a good idea to make a reservation in advance to secure your place.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
7993;Heng Khao Moo Daeng;Thailand;Surat Thani;428/1 Namueang Road, Talat, Mueang Surat Thani, Surat Thani, 84000, Thailand;9.1431188;99.3247196;68;true;false;Thai-Chinese;This simple eatery is always bustling at lunchtime with queues for both dine-in and takeout. The owner's inviting and chatty demeanour sets the scene. His signature barbeque pork comes with crispy pork and sweet sausage inside and a large portion only costs 40 baht.;Cash only;[]
7994;Sripol Seafood House;Thailand;Bangkok;61/11, 12 Rama 9 Road Soi 7, Huai Khwang, Bangkok, 10310, Thailand;13.757461;100.56998;94;false;false;Seafood;For an authentic Thai seafood experience, look no further than this restaurant named after the owner's fishing boat, which also catches most of the produce. Expect premium seafood cooking in the heart of Bangkok and hearty portions suitable for 4 or more people. The signature fried rice with salty fish is particularly noteworthy. We recommend any of the generously served dishes and also calling 2 days in advance to book a table and check on menu options.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7995;The Redbox;Thailand;Chiang Mai;6 Soi Jannsaap, Huai Kaeo Road, Chang Phueak, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8013718;98.9696259;50;false;true;Thai contemporary;With business acumen and cooking techniques gleaned from their travels, Chef Dan and partner Pimmada offer modern Thai with Malaysian and Brunei influences. They import select ingredients like salted eggs from Chaiya, and Gula Melaka (Malaysian palm sugar) to create treats like Siam Ruby, a signature dessert. We recommend the signature creation cocktail with a complexity of flavours before your unforgettable meal. Seating is limited so bookings are essential.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7996;La Gaetana;Thailand;Phuket;352 Phuket Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.876652;98.39357;64;true;true;Italian;It may be tiny, with 6 tables, but La Gaetana, decorated like an Italian house in warm colours, provides a warm welcome and is big on charm. They import most ingredients from Italy and make the sourdough, pasta, gelato and limoncello in-house. Chef Gianni cooks the fettucine with tomato sauce and crab meat using his family recipe from Campania. The menu is largely influenced by such southern classics. As Gianni takes a summer holiday each year, call ahead first.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
7997;Eat Me;Thailand;Bangkok;1/6 Soi Phiphat 2, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7254378;100.5338921;15;true;true;International;Though hidden in a side soi, Eat Me is hardly a secret. Since 1998, it has been known for carefully cooked dishes that join global influences with local flavours. The best meals here start with Thai food-inspired cocktails at the ground floor bar. They continue at the minimalist second-storey dining room or leafy balcony with the star of the menu—mixed clams served with nam, or fermented Thai sausage, and coriander lime broth—and one of the unmissable desserts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
7998;The Smokaccia Laboratory;Thailand;Phuket;116/4 Mu 3, Srisoonthorn Road, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9762871;98.2850193;65;false;true;Creative;Chef Luca Mascolo has invented a complex crispy sourdough which he has named ‘Smokaccia’, which is served with a variety of inventive fillings. Highlights include slow-cooked Australian Wagyu striploin, Surat Thani oysters and cheese from Nonthaburi. The high-ceilinged dining room features both tables and counter seats overlooking the open kitchen. Things step up a gear at dinner with a creative, 18-course tasting menu showcasing modern techniques. Vegan options are also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
7999;Saigon Recipe;Thailand;Bangkok;Piman 49, B3 Building, 46/5 Soi Sukhumvit 49, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7322609;100.5765669;21;false;true;Vietnamese;With its canary-yellow walls, vintage posters and Indochinese décor, this place feels like a home in Saigon, if it was staffed by capable Vietnamese chefs. They carefully select ingredients, including rice wrappers and noodles from Vietnam, to create flavourful rice and noodle dishes, salads and rolls the owner might serve family and friends. Weekday lunches offer set menus that please even the time-pressed. Coffee fans should try the authentic Vietnamese brew.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8000;Saffron;Thailand;Ko Samui;Banyan Tree Samui, 99/9 Mu 4, Maret, Ko Samui, 84310, Thailand;9.4752063;100.0692198;34;false;false;Thai;Elegantly appointed with floor-to-ceiling windows, contemporary lighting and dark wooden furnishings, Saffron also offers alfresco dining with a fantastic view. You can choose from à la carte and tasting menus. The roast duck red curry is paired with a thick sweet and spicy sauce, a fresh lychee and pineapple compote and roasted skin that excite the tastebuds. The fried softshell crab salad with lychee and passionfruit is also a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8001;Blackitch;Thailand;Chiang Mai;27/1 Nimmanahaeminda Soi 7 Road, Suthep, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7981165;98.9698421;89;true;true;Asian Contemporary;Hidden in the city centre in plain sight, this second floor 16-seater is decorated with stone, wood and local blue fabrics in a minimalist style. The creative chef, Phanuphol Bulsuwan, honed his skills under his restaurateur grandmother. He constantly adapts his 10-course meal using Thailand’s seasonal ingredients, uniting Thai, Japanese and Chinese influences. He also ferments kitchen scraps to season his dishes and brews beers and sake for food pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8002;Krua Supanniga by Khunyai Somsie;Thailand;Khon Kaen;Supanniga Home, 130/9 Phothisan Road, Phra Lap, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4122127;102.858754;16;false;true;Thai;Named after the Supanniga flower, this cute shop offers delightful dishes blending flavours from the eastern seaboard and Isan cuisine. Grandma's recipes inspire the food here. Don't miss the must-order chamuang pork—a juicy stewed pork infused with Chamuang leaf's slightly sour flavour. The restaurant provides indoor and outdoor seating, including shaded tables in the tree house.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
8003;Pratunam Baan Ko Noodles;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;22 Mu 5, Ban Ko, Bang Sai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13190, Thailand;14.2332584;100.4771903;48;false;true;Noodles;Set beside a peaceful canal, the crowds flock here for their speciality: beef noodles. The noodles come with offal, beef balls, spare ribs and tender beef slices. The soup is also superb, with a meaty aroma. It’s so popular, the chef prepares 25-30 kg of fresh offal every day.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8004;Lahnyai;Thailand;Bangkok;31 Soi Suan Phlu 2, Thung Maha Mek, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7222474;100.5381171;74;true;true;Thai contemporary;Initially conceived as a tribute to the owner's grandmother, Lahnyai showcases modern interpretations of royal Thai cuisine sourced from the cremation cookbooks of princesses from 1987 to 1992. The refined dining room delivers an intimate ambiance with velvet walls and Jacquard-covered furniture. Infusing a contemporary twist into historical recipes, dishes satisfy with tried-and-tested flavours, like a great massaman curry that strikes a fine balance between spice and sweetness.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8005;Jay Jew Talew Bin;Thailand;Chon Buri;117/17 Mu 2, Soi Bangsai 6, Bang Sai, Mueang Chonburi, Chon Buri, 20000, Thailand;13.3808961;100.9882637;49;false;false;Thai;This local favourite offers the freshest seafood with bold Thai flavours, cooked home-style. The restaurant is simple, without air conditioning. The menu primarily focuses on seafood options, and the chef excels at deep-fried and stir-fried dishes. The rice dishes and daily catch are listed on the blackboard at the front of the shop. Bookings are only taken for groups of 10 or more. Expect to wait for a table on weekends.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8006;Chom Tawan;Thailand;Chon Buri;79 Mu 3, Assadang Road, Tha Thewawong, Ko Sichang, Chon Buri, 20120, Thailand;13.1530399;100.8139953;17;false;true;Thai;Despite its rustic-looking exterior, Chom Tawan has a certain charm, and prices are reasonable, especially considering the freshness and quality of the seafood. The delicious stir-fried squid with minced pork filling and garlic is tempting, but also ask about the special of the day.;Cash only;[]
8007;Preaw Pak;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;6/6 Mu 4, Ammarit, Phak Hai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13120, Thailand;14.4646267;100.3656589;97;true;true;Thai;Preaw Pak specialises in freshwater fish, with a menu focused on fresh catches and local seasonal produce. From the riverside location you can see fishermen at work. The chef's skill is evident in his perfectly cooked dishes, which showcase traditional local flavours. Highlights include deep-fried river prawns with stir-fried garlic and chilli, and fresh snakehead fish in clear tom yum soup made with dry and fresh chilli. The level of spice can be adjusted to taste.;Cash only;[]
8008;Tambu;Thailand;Phuket;Avista Hideaway Phuket Patong - MGallery, 39/9 Muen-Ngern Road, Pa Tong Beach, Pa Tong, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.88122;98.27814;60;false;true;Indian;Inspiration from the opulent Mughal palaces makes its presence felt in this alluring restaurant, where the chef presents modern Indian cooking that embraces the times. He respects the diversity and tradition of Indian cuisine, crafting dishes that showcase his skills and experience. The aromatic plates are packed with spices and enhanced by a smoky flavour, bringing complexity and creative combinations to the palate.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8009;Wansuk;Thailand;Chon Buri;129/10 Mu 1, Soi Boonpleum, Pattaya, Nong Preu, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.95918;100.89349;24;false;false;Thai;In a vintage decor featuring wooden accents, music from the 1980s and 1990s sets the mood. At this locally renowned Thai restaurant, the chef-owner's uniquely creative menu boasts intensely flavoured, unapologetically spicy dishes – though milder versions are available upon request. Seafood is the star, with fresh, expertly cooked offerings served at perfect temperatures. Instead of regular rice, we suggest ordering the signature fried rice with salt.;Car park;[]
8010;Radna Suanmak;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;282 Phoklang Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.975294;102.0933103;55;false;true;Noodles;In over 30 years serving the community, this humble noodle spot has won local awards and built up a dedicated following. Expect a wait for their lovingly prepared dishes, which include deep-fried fish with thick noodles, and flavoursome crispy noodle stir-fry with holy basil.;Cash only;[]
8011;Khao Soi Lung Prakit Kad Kom;Thailand;Chiang Mai;53 Suriyawong 5 Road, Hai Ya, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50100, Thailand;18.7744424;98.9897008;52;false;false;Noodles;This place has been serving Northern Thai-style curry noodle soup for over 40 years. Their signature dish is Khao Soi with beef, which features a savoury curry broth and soft, eggy noodles. Don’t forget to squeeze the lemon over your noodles and pair them with side dishes to enhance the flavours.;Cash only;[]
8012;Mae Khlong Hua Pla Mo Fai;Thailand;Bangkok;198 Phran Nok-Phutthamonthon Sai 4 Road, Bang Phrom, Taling Chan, Bangkok, 10170, Thailand;13.7546526;100.4216636;82;true;true;Seafood;Simple in its design with a white pavilion and modest dining tables, the restaurant has a small garden with some outdoor seating. The owners are hands-on, preparing every dish with care. The stir-fried crab has a naturally sweet meat and wok-fried aroma, and is served with glass noodles, spicy chilli and crunchy mimosa. The large butterfly-cut river fish is nicely char-grilled. The grilled river prawns, meanwhile, are clearly the people’s favourite.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8013;Yu Ting Yuan;Thailand;Bangkok;LF, Four Seasons Hotel Bangkok at Chao Phraya River, 300/1 Charoen Krung Road, Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.703883;100.5057331;88;false;false;Cantonese;There is a luxurious feel to this lavish Cantonese restaurant that is a gorgeously designed space inside the equally stylish Four Seasons hotel. Expansive windows look out onto a reflective pool which comes to life at night with the illumination of contemporary artworks. The Cantonese chef brings a modern and creative approach to the cooking, as well as a Thai twist in places. The extensive menus include tasting and à la carte options, plus a dim sum selection at lunch.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8014;Ojo;Thailand;Bangkok;76F, The Standard Bangkok Mahanakhon, 114 Narathiwas Road, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.72352;100.52825;80;false;true;Mexican;Offering breathtaking views over the Bangkok cityscape, Ojo has the honour of being Thailand’s highest restaurant. Glamorous pink and gold décor adds to the appeal of a truly special location in which to dine, while the authentic Mexican cooking means this restaurant is far more than just its setting. The menu of attractive dishes includes tender cochinillo and a selection of raw seafood. Ask for a table by the window or on the terrace to make the most of the view.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
8015;Nikaku;Thailand;Bangkok;GF, W Bangkok, 106 North Sathorn Road, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7218546;100.5287986;39;false;true;Sushi;This Japanese restaurant originating from Kitakyushu, specialises in authentic Edo-mae sushi. Offering an omakase menu, it serves only 12 diners at a counter, showcasing the chef's skills. Ingredients are sourced daily from Japan, ensuring superb quality fish and shellfish, such as Hokkaido's delicate uni. The chef provides detailed seafood explanations, and diners can opt for special tea pairings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8016;Keller;Thailand;Bangkok;1749 Chan Kao Road, Chong Nonsi, Yan Nawa, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.70625;100.5417693;38;true;false;Creative;The restaurant offers an intimate and engaging dining experience. The interior features a beautiful light beige colour palette, complemented by ample natural light. Boasting bold flavours with a strong Asian influence, the food is a testament to the chef's culinary prowess. Each bite is a harmonious blend of tradition and innovation, and the chef's boundless creativity is expressed in a tasting menu that changes every month.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8017;Phensiri;Thailand;Ko Samui;80/30 Mu 3, Suan Uthit Road, Bo Phut, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.5117039;100.0550677;69;true;true;Thai, Southern Thai;Phensiri is a must-visit for Thai and Southern Thai cuisine. Using high-quality local ingredients, the chef-owner ensures each dish is well-balanced and flavourful. A no-fuss approach delivers authentic flavours, with the spice level adjustable to your liking. The welcoming atmosphere is enhanced by Thai-style décor, and the attentive staff, fluent in English, make things easy for tourists. Popular with both locals and visitors, it is especially busy at lunchtime and dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8018;Larb Duang Dee Mee Sook;Thailand;Chiang Mai;74 Soi Ban Huai Sai, Mu 4, Suthep, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50200, Thailand;18.7592878;98.9429191;16;true;false;Northern Thai;With its simple, rustic look, this quaint eatery specialises in northern larb dishes, paired with a local chaeo dipping sauce with the aroma of toasted sticky rice. The spicy, sour and fragrant beef soup is a must.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8019;Somtum Je Phai;Thailand;Chon Buri;321/26 Mu 12, Jomtien Beach Road, Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20260, Thailand;12.8866482;100.8778378;98;false;false;Isan;This authentic Isan eatery under a PVC tent grills chicken, meat, and pork over charcoal with traditional flair. The owner's passion is palpable as she communicates animatedly with her team. The meat is well-executed and retains its juiciness.;Cash only;[]
8021;Som Tum Jae Kai (Asavamit Road);Thailand;Udon Thani;230/28 Asavamit Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.3979584;102.7860599;66;false;true;Isan;This family-operated lunch spot has been a popular haunt for half a century. The dishes get their distinctive flavour from their home-made fermented fish sauce. This tasty addition elevates favourites such as mixed som tum with pork crackling and fermented sausage.;Cash only;[]
8022;Kinlum Kindee;Thailand;Chiang Mai;172 Mu 3, Mueang Len, San Sai, Chiang Mai, 50210, Thailand;18.8607779;99.0656174;77;false;true;Northern Thai;Truth in advertising may be rare, but Kin Lum Kin Dee, which means “to eat delicious food and eat well” in Lanna, allows Northern Thai food lovers to do just that. Formerly downtown, the restaurant is now in a quiet pavilion in San Sai surrounded by gardens, trees, and fields. Dishes are marked by authentic flavours and fresh ingredients, with some from the garden. Grilled field crab innards with egg yolks and northern Thai herb soup with pork are must-tries.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
8023;Clara;Thailand;Bangkok;69 Soi Prasat Suk, Chong Nonsi, Yan Nawa, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.71638;100.54844;29;true;true;Italian;Popular among both Thai and foreign foodies and housed in a Bauhaus-style villa surrounded by sculpture-filled gardens, Clara is an elegant Italian fine-dining restaurant from a seasoned Italian chef and his wife. The villa’s two-floor interior has a warm minimalist vibe. The set menu balances flavours and complex textures which are matched by the fine service. Pair with wine for a complete experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8024;Favola;Thailand;Chiang Mai;2F, Chiang Mai Marriott Hotel, 108 Chang Khlan Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50100, Thailand;18.7843138;98.9999868;33;false;true;Italian;At Favola, Chiang Mai Marriott Hotel presents authentic Italian cuisine, featuring homemade pasta and ravioli crafted by the Italian head chef, all served in a dining room that blends contemporary style with a classic Italian restaurant ambience. Among the dishes, the pizzas stand out. Feel free to order half or smaller sizes, perfect for when you’re in the mood to try multiple dishes. The excellent wine selection further enhances the experience.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8025;Aheesah Roddee;Thailand;Bangkok;103-105 Tani Road, Talat Yot, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.76035;100.49839;42;false;true;Asian;Helmed by the son of Indonesian migrants, it has been serving aromatic Indonesian-inspired fare since 1975. The menu features tasty dishes such as chicken or beef biryani and satay. We recommend pairing the beautifully spiced chicken biryani with the hot and sour beef soup.;Cash only;[]
8026;Gu Cherng;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;2F, Krungsri River Hotel, 27/2 Mu 11, Rochana Road, Kamang, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3529537;100.5825053;89;true;true;Chinese;Gu cherng refers to the country’s former capital and the dining room, renovated in 2021, mixes elegant modern Chinese style with flashes of the traditional. Popular dishes include a variety of tasty dim-sum. The steamed prawn dumplings with seaweed and steamed rice noodles stuffed with deep-fried prawns use quality ingredients with delicately balanced flavours. The signature Peking duck pancakes use choice cuts of meat, thinly sliced, crispy and with no fat.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8027;Jay Noi Kratoke;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;115 Pibool La-lad Road, Nong Phai Lom, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9667416;102.0899567;68;false;true;Thai;This three-storey house with simple décor is family run and in its second generation. Jay Noi's house special of hao-dong is a popular local treat using sliced pork and spicy Isan sauce, chilli and roasted rice. The four pad mee Korat is also recommended. Its sticky rice noodles are fresh and go really well with the sweet and sour sauce, fresh bean sprouts and chives. You can order the homemade curry puff for take away, with a variety of optional sides.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
8028;Food For You;Thailand;Chiang Mai;25 Mu 3, San Phi Suea, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8538933;98.9835082;52;false;false;Thai;Food For You has been creating flavoursome Thai food using fresh seasonal ingredients from local farms for over 20 years. Meals here are served chef’s table style, from a menu that changes according to the season and customer requests. The crab meat salad with mixed fruit is highly recommended and comes with a dressing that’s the perfect balance of sweet, sour, and salty. As seating is limited, reservations are essential.;Terrace;[]
8029;Baan Ton Sai;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;189/49 Mu 8, Pratu Chai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.352996;100.5516351;65;true;false;Thai;The restaurant's vibrant colours stand out from afar. In the backyard, a banyan tree provides pleasant shade. The menu features straightforward and unpretentious seafood, pork and chicken dishes. Expect large servings of seafood that make the mouth water at wallet-friendly prices. We recommend trying their rat na noodles. Closing times may vary, so it's best to arrive early.;Cash only;[]
8030;Grand Chaopraya;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;42/1 Ban Run, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.300715;100.5641292;52;true;true;Thai;Opened in 2009, this riverside restaurant serves Thai cuisine made with local ingredients, including fish sourced from the river. The dining room features high ceilings, spiral staircases and floor-to-ceiling windows, while the terrace offers scenic views and nightly live music. The menu is packed with recipes from the owner’s mother. Her grilled river prawns and grilled fish and shrimp in pineapple curry are a must. Book ahead for an outdoor table at dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8031;Kor Chun Huad;Thailand;Bangkok;864 Soi Somdet Phrachao Taksin 34, Bukkhalo, Thon Buri, Bangkok, 10600, Thailand;13.7036777;100.4851172;73;true;true;Thai-Chinese;For more than five decades, Koa Chun Huad has been attracting throngs of locals. Named after the chef-owner who has worked in many a kitchen in Chinatown, it serves classic Thai-Chinese dishes at appealingly low prices. The highlights are the boiled pork slices, perfectly complemented by a soybean sauce, and the intense stewed pork with sweet-salty five spice gravy.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
8032;Neon Boat Noodles;Thailand;Chon Buri;395/7 Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.9314083;100.8901686;42;true;true;Noodles;Traditional boat noodles are served here with various toppings in a bold and savoury soup. We also recommend the spicy boiled pork and pork condiments, which have an intensely flavoured sauce and the aroma of fried garlic.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8033;Grok;Thailand;Bangkok;14 Soi Somkid, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7470706;100.545948;47;false;true;Thai;The interior, decorated in elegant dark tones with wood-clad walls, creates a nostalgic ambiance. The menu offers a modern take on Ratchaburi cuisine, where the intense flavours and aromas of each dish pair well with Thai herbs. The duck confit with red curry and the stir-fried minced chicken thigh with Thai herbs and five peppercorns are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8034;Ōre;Thailand;Bangkok;11/31 Sathu Pradit Road, Chong Nonsi, Yan Nawa, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7043427;100.5300097;29;false;true;Creative;With a minimalist design of wood, fabric and natural tones, Ōre promises an intimate culinary journey centred on Thai ingredients with select imports. The chef extols the flavour-enhancing properties of the mineral water that he gets shipped in from a spring near Sai Yok Waterfall to use in his cooking. His creative dishes highlight natural flavours and aromas that deepen throughout the meal, making for an unforgettable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8035;Krua Sa Ros Jad;Thailand;Bangkok;112/1 Soi Vibhavadi 44, Vibhavadi Rangsit Road, Lat Yao, Chatuchak, Bangkok, 10900, Thailand;13.842234;100.5619856;74;false;true;Thai;"Krua Sa Ros Jad" combines the owner's mother's name and a Thai phrase meaning "intense flavour" – an apt description of the boldly seasoned food made with fresh ingredients. Try the deep-fried fish in Choo Chee sauce, the robust, well-spiced flavour of which pairs well with the hot Tom Yum chicken soup with young tamarind leaves. The restaurant boasts a unique collection of Buddha statues and antique European ceramics, as the owner is an avid collector.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8036;Cadence by Dan Bark;Thailand;Bangkok;225 Soi Pridi Banomyong 25, Khlong Tan, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.727079;100.594119;44;true;true;Innovative, Creative;Drawing on his Korean-American heritage and experience in some of Chicago's top restaurants, chef Dan Bark uses a clever array of components to craft progressive American cuisine. The elegant space sets the stage for an artful marriage of Western and Asian flavours. The restaurant's commitment to excellence goes beyond the food, with an impressive wine selection, astutely curated cocktail pairings and charming service from a smartly turned-out team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
8037;Terroir;Thailand;Bangkok;Acmen Complex, 13-15 Ekkamai Road, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7342892;100.5871356;72;false;false;Creative;Chef Hao believes that the land, climate, and farmers are pivotal in produce quality. This belief echoes in his eatery sourcing 90% of ingredients from Northern Thailand, named meaning 'soil' in French. The restaurant delivers exceptional Franco-Japanese fusion, creatively blending two cuisines. Impressive flavour pairings, notably rich, smoky broths, shine consistently. An outstanding wine selection completes the splendid dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
8038;O;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;252/21 Soi Wilai Sena, Prasoet Som Road, Sena, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13110, Thailand;14.3268265;100.4033692;91;true;false;Thai;Set in Sena district's old market, this charming wooden house backs onto the River Noi. The relaxed atmosphere and delicious food make it a local favourite, with popular dishes like stir-fried river prawns with salt and pepper, and deep-fried fish with fish sauce.;;[]
8041;Baan Watcharachai;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;9 Soi Ban Pom 27, Ban Pom, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3528281;100.5461966;87;true;false;Thai;This family-owned restaurant offers central Thai cuisine by the side of the Chao Phraya River. Its name joins those of the family’s father, mother and son and means “house of light and victory”. Recipes have come from the owner’s grandmother, with dishes including sweet, salty and spicy fried snakehead fish with prik-king curry paste – a perfect example of the well-balanced cooking on offer. Guests can dine in the vintage house or outside on the deck or docked boat, both with views of Phra Chedi Sri Suriyothai.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8042;Phi Sao;Thailand;Phang-Nga;136/79 Mu 9, Thai Mueang, Phang-Nga, 82120, Thailand;8.4045539;98.2462619;22;true;true;Thai;Delicious meals have been enjoyed at P’Saw for more than 40 years. Under a whitewashed pavilion-like structure, diners can enjoy the sea breeze, a view of the beach and southern-style dishes. The recipes, passed from the restaurant’s founder to her younger sister, offer something more personal and familial than their neighbouring restaurants. The baegu leaf salad with crispy shrimp and tom yum clear soup with young coconut deliver a delightful and flavourful experience.;Cash only;[]
8043;Ms.Maria & Mr.Singh;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, 68 Soi Sukhumvit 31, Sukhumvit Road, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.740807;100.5676038;53;true;true;Indian;Inspired by a Mexican-Indian love story, two cultures combine in both gastronomy and design at this sensorily striking restaurant. Vibrant oranges and blues make for a colourful setting. The food also makes a statement, playing with spices and textures to twist conventional styles. The well-judged fusion cooking includes dishes like pork vindaloo tacos and papdi chaat served on a mini taco shell. The service team provide fabulous hospitality with their high energy and friendly manner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
8044;Juumpo;Thailand;Phang-Nga;GF, Hotel Gahn Khao Lak, 1/96 Mu 5, Phet Kasem Road, Khuk Khak, Takua Pa, Phang-Nga, 82220, Thailand;8.6722773;98.2526123;56;false;false;Southern Thai;The cuisine of the local Baba (Chinese-Thai) people lives on here. Named in honour of the owner’s grandfather, a 'Juumpo' or chef on a Chinese boat more than 80 years ago and the source of many unique recipes, the open-air restaurant is fitted out with décor that reflects Chino-Portuguese design and culture. Baba-style coconut milk soup with shrimps and Thai herbs, chilli dip with shrimp, and fried fish with sweet and sour sauce are all recommended.;Car park;[]
8045;Tonnam Riverview;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;26/7 Ban Len, Bang Pa-in, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13160, Thailand;14.2234224;100.5738292;55;true;false;Thai;Known for the grilled river prawns it has served since 1991, this family-friendly restaurant on the Chao Phraya River has two dining areas: on a raft and boat, respectively. Either way, diners enjoy gentle breezes and scenic views with their meals. The culinary offerings, which have grown since the restaurant first opened, are skilfully cooked using fresh local ingredients. The speciality, grilled river prawns served with a flavourful spicy sauce, is a must-try.;Car park,Great view;[]
8046;Loong Loy Pa Lan;Thailand;Nakhon Pathom;1010 Phet Kasem Road, Huai Chorakhe, Mueang Nakhon Pathom, Nakhon Pathom, 73000, Thailand;13.8089952;100.0571265;19;false;true;Thai;A passion for wild ingredients like wild boar, frogs, seafood, and even greens, along with a zeal for local flavours—intense, tangy, and spicy—shapes everything on the menu here. The stir-fried wild boar with chilies and the tom yam soup with snakehead fish are both recommended, as is the seafood cooked according to local recipes. The atmosphere is relaxed and homely, with air-conditioned dining rooms and outdoor seating available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
8048;L'Arôme by the Sea;Thailand;Phuket;247/5 Phrabaramee Road, Pa Tong, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.9151582;98.2924952;55;true;false;French Contemporary;Start with a refreshing cocktail and enjoy the sea breeze on the rooftop before descending to the main dining room for stunning ocean views and the 'Vue sur la Mer' tasting menu. The seafood is of high quality, but the roasted pigeon with eggplant is also a standout. Meanwhile, the creamy foie gras and langoustine showcase the chef's culinary skills.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
8049;Lab Mu Worachai;Thailand;Udon Thani;26/3 Posri Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.4103691;102.7826167;96;true;true;Isan;Pork reigns supreme at this traditional Isan eatery, which may be renowned for its namesake Lab Mu – minced pork, skin and liver – but the flavourful Somtum Lao is another standout. Lunchtime can get hectic, but service is swift. The sharing sets of four to six dishes are perfect for groups.;Cash only;[]
8050;Acqua;Thailand;Phuket;324/15 Phra Barami Road, Pa Tong, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.9167408;98.2908321;63;false;true;Italian;Chef Alessandro Frau reinvents Italian fare with Sardinian artistry using premium imports. There’s a huge selection of à la carte, pastas and woodfired pizzas. Try the Tortelli Il Mare stuffed with Burrata cheese, glazed in black squid ink with Sardinian sea urchin and marine plankton. Or let the chef guide you through his tasting menu with signatures like lobster salad or raw Sicilian red prawns. Wine lovers will enjoy the fine vintage collection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8051;Gorjan;Thailand;Phuket;161 Kra Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8724225;98.3906865;70;false;false;Thai;If you're near Gorjan Bridge, consider this simple family-run eatery. Every dish is rife with rich flavours, and many are created from their own recipes. The owner is poised to cook your food to order, which ensures a personalised dining experience.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8052;New York Steakhouse;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, JW Marriott Hotel, 4 Soi Sukhumvit 2, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7416921;100.5520831;38;true;false;Steakhouse;Located inside the JW Marriott Hotel, this restaurant really lives up to its name. Dark wood furniture, oversized leather chairs and monochrome photos of US cities evoke images of a classic Manhattan steakhouse. A selection of cuts are available – including those from the US, Australia and Japan – and the knowledgeable service team are on hand to help guide your decision. Start with the Caesar salad, tossed tableside with a dressing made from scratch, then finish with the creative and equally theatrical ‘Bomb Alaska’ dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8053;Ginza Sushi Ichi;Thailand;Bangkok;3F, Gaysorn Village, 999 Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7449423;100.5406345;55;false;false;Sushi;Spanning Tokyo, Jakarta, Singapore and Bangkok, Ginza Sushi Ichi imports the daily catch from Tokyo’s markets. This Bangkok branch uses the same rice-vinegar formula as the flagship restaurant, importing sushi rice from Yamagata. The quintessentially Japanese decor with neutral pine walls hosts a genial atmosphere. Ten seats circle the marble counter for an omakase experience focusing on nigiri. Private rooms are available and, of course, there’s a good range of sake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8054;Somchai Go Tae (Bang Len);Thailand;Nakhon Pathom;18/13 Mu 1, Bang Phasi, Bang Len, Nakhon Pathom, 73130, Thailand;14.0108613;100.2201909;17;true;true;Thai-Chinese, Thai;Go Tae, the owner of this Thai-Chinese restaurant, got his start almost 80 years ago selling stewed duck noodle soup on a boat, before heading to dry land to open this place. Inside the three-storey building (topped with a giant rooftop duck statue), the simple dining room has a roasting and stewing station. The menu features old-school Thai-Chinese fare, including the recommended stewed duck and live river prawn cooked to your preference.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8056;Heh;Thailand;Phuket;158 Yaowarat Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8894489;98.3870143;45;true;false;Australian Contemporary;‘Heh’ is an expression of curiosity, according to the chef-owner who leads a youthful and creative kitchen. The aim is to bring Melbourne to the Andaman, combining quality ingredients from the Andaman Sea with Australian imports. The chef injects excitement into the unique menu without ever overcomplicating it. The charred broccoli with anchovy-miso sauce and crispy fish scales, and succulent charcoal-grilled Australian Wagyu short ribs are recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
8058;Paste;Thailand;Bangkok;3F, Gaysorn Village, 999 Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7451823;100.5405551;30;true;true;Thai;The food here is as intricate as the spiral silk cocoon sculpture that fills the airy dining room. Drawing inspiration from royal Thai cuisine, the kitchen also employs century-old techniques and plenty of local ingredients. The roasted duck curry with lychee, fennel seed and freshly squeezed coconut milk and the char-grilled pork, fennel seed, and smoked tomato relish are recommended and can be found on the tasting menus and à la carte. Excellent service further enhances the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8059;Bang Por Seafood Takho;Thailand;Ko Samui;56/4 Mu 6, Maenam, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.578356;99.9427848;56;true;false;Seafood;Bang Por boasts an experienced kitchen team composed of local chefs who have worked here for many years. This simple beach-front restaurant is depicted by holiday vibes and Southern Thai seafood fare. The spicy stir-fried squid with herbs is cooked in a spicy curry paste and the grilled fish is sprinkled with mixed Thai herbs. The house shrimp paste is packed with aromatic plants and coconut chili and grilled before serving, hence the pungent aroma.;Great view;[]
8060;Long Dtai;Thailand;Ko Samui;Cape Fahn Hotel, 24/269 Mu 5, Bo Phut, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.5736005;100.0874905;95;false;false;Southern Thai;After crossing shallow waters, you reach this private island resort off Samui’s east coast. From the restaurant’s terrace, diners enjoy panoramic views of the bay as they sample chef David Thompson’s fab creations. His Southern Thai menu is deceptively simple and his consummate culinary talent is revealed in the details. Start with grilled squid, marinated in turmeric and coconut milk to accentuate its freshness. Marine sustainability is the name of the game here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8061;Nan Bei;Thailand;Bangkok;19F, Rosewood Hotel, 1041/38 Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7432557;100.5489366;78;true;true;Chinese;Nan Bei means ‘south’ and ‘north’ so it’s no surprise to discover that this restaurant specialises in China’s southern and northern regions, from where the recipes come and ingredients are flown in. It sits on the 19th floor of the Rosewood Hotel, offering fabulous views of Bangkok while you dine. Braised abalone and braised pork belly shouldn’t be missed, though the prized item is Peking duck. Sit at the counter to see the chefs at work or to watch the birds being roasted over lychee wood. Lunchtime dim sum is also worth exploring.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8062;Baan Phraya;Thailand;Bangkok;Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 48 Soi Charoen Krung 40,  Charoen Krung Road, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7245795;100.5116967;55;true;false;Thai;The original owner of this 120-year-old heritage house served the government as Phraya, one of the highest ranks of Thai nobility. Previously Mandarin Oriental's cooking school, they switched operations in 2022. Chef Patchara serves traditional Thai dishes inspired by those school recipes. Surrounded by shady greens, the whitewashed house has a terrace with stunning sunset views over the river. The dining room inside fits a capacity of 20 guests a night.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
8063;Krua Samchai;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;282/1 Phalochai Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2339591;104.8389958;20;true;false;Isan;Two roosters stand guard at the entrance. Krua Samchai is famous for serving iconic Isan food befitting of the region. Fresh fish from the Mekong and Mun rivers is cooked using the chef's secret mix of herbs and spices that produces a powerful aroma. The grilled chicken has a crispy golden skin from the charcoal flame but retains its juicy meat. The Isan-style spicy fish maw and bamboo shoot soup uses tiliacora juice to perfection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8064;Arunwan;Thailand;Bangkok;LGF, Park X Building, 295 Soi Ekkamai 15, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7361551;100.587971;50;true;true;Small eats;Opened over 60 years ago and now run by the founder’s children, this spot specialises in a pork offal and pickled cabbage soup that they have honed over the years using a family recipe. It’s a fresh-tasting dish and the cabbage combines well with the sweetness of the pork consommé. The crispy pork wontons with sweet black sauce are well worth ordering while you wait for your soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
8065;Go Ang Seafood;Thailand;Phuket;226 Mu 2, Phuket Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8791435;98.3925518;81;true;false;Seafood;From humble origins as a small shop with a zinc roof, it’s now one of the most popular seafood restaurants with a comfortable interior and Chinese décor. Chef-owner Go Ang cooks the entire southern Thai menu. The blue swimming crab, horseshoe crab and mantis shrimp are sourced daily from 5 markets. The steamed crab with tangy seafood dip and fried mantis shrimp with garlic are delightful, while the Southern Thai spicy sour soup with seabass is also a must-try.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
8067;Sawang Noodles;Thailand;Bangkok;264 Si Phraya Road, Maha Phruettharam, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.731989;100.5253347;74;false;false;Noodles;This is the place to enjoy crab noodles in Bangkok. The sweet, giant crab claw meat pairs well with sticky egg noodles and shrimp dumplings. Be sure to try their signature noodles with extra soup and barbecued pork on the side.;Cash only;[]
8068;Chum (Saraphi);Thailand;Chiang Mai;1/1 Mu 7, Tha Wang Tan, Saraphi, Chiang Mai, 50140, Thailand;18.7242045;99.008657;31;false;true;Northern Thai;Chum serves Northern Thai cuisine cooked from the recipes of the family's grandmother. The colourful restaurant is simply decorated with red and yellow walls and brightly coloured parasols of Northern Thai design hanging from the ceilings. The stir-fried pork and liver is well cooked, and packed with Thai herbs, wild pepper and coriander. The mixed Northern Thai starter uses a tasty young chili relish with the scent of green chili that isn’t too spicy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
8069;Jongjit Kitchen;Thailand;Phuket;9/1 Mu 4, Wichit Songkhram Road, Kathu, Phuket, 83120, Thailand;7.9161465;98.3458619;48;false;true;Thai;Southern recipes, affordable prices and down-to-earth hospitality – this is why locals pack out this family-run business at lunch and dinner. Their family recipes pack great intensity. The Phuketian stir-fried pork rump with salt is lovely, with tender meat and lip-smacking pork skin.;Cash only;[]
8070;Suay;Thailand;Phuket;Baan Wana Park, 177/99 Mu 4, Si Sunthon Road, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.980066;98.32934;83;false;false;Thai contemporary;The acronym of ‘sassy, unique, authentic and yummy’ may sound kitsch, but the airy and bright interior with its Portuguese-tiled floor is anything but. Outdoor seating with garden and live music is equally pleasant. Owner-chef Tammasak skilfully updates Thai food with modern techniques and artsy presentation. Dishes, including the signature grilled lemongrass lamb chops with papaya salsa, are seasoned with bold but well-judged spicing. Also try the crab cakes with Sriracha chili aioli and mango chutney.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8071;Enoteca;Thailand;Bangkok;39 Soi Sukhumvit 27, Khlong Toei Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.73723;100.56463;16;false;true;Italian;The name means ‘wine library’, so it will come as no surprise to find a list of nearly 400 bottles here, including a fine selection of Barolo. While it sits in the city’s bustling business district, this Italian restaurant is a haven of tranquillity. Floor-to-ceiling windows offer charming garden views, and the cosy, friendly atmosphere makes you feel as though you’re dining in an Italian home. All regions of Italy are represented, with ingredients flown in from Europe and used in dishes with a modern twist. Risottos are a highlight, and for the Secondi Piatti, don’t miss the Barbecue Pigeon. They also offer set menus for more variety.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
8072;Shirokane Tori-Tama;Thailand;Bangkok;Park Lane, 18 Soi Sukhumvit 63, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7233434;100.58455;59;false;true;Japanese;Experienced chefs from Tokyo have brought authentic yakitori cuisine to Bangkok, here at the group’s fourth branch in Asia. Beak-to-tail cooking is celebrated, where various chicken parts are prepared in several ways to create countless dishes that are full of flavour. Diners seated around the open kitchen in the middle of the dining room get to watch the chefs at work, listen to meat sizzling over hot coals, and take in the intoxicating aromas. Aside from the yakitori, the chicken liver pâté with warm baguette is a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8073;Guang Tang Noodles;Thailand;Khon Kaen;18/15 Pimpasut Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4366495;102.8360228;86;true;true;Noodles;The history of this egg noodle soup spot stretches back more than 70 years to the owner’s grandfather. Today, it still satisfies — especially the noodle soup with wontons and barbecue pork (the noodles and wontons are homemade) and the deep-fried noodles with gravy and pork or beef.;Cash only;[]
8075;Jaras;Thailand;Phuket;InterContinental Phuket Resort, 333, 333/3 Mu 3, Kamala Beach, Kamala, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.962254;98.2837599;64;false;true;Thai contemporary;Despite the luxury setting, Jaras retains honest roots. The intimate design draws influence from the Li Thai, Sukhothai era. The restaurant is named after the owner's grandma whose cooking inspired some of the recipes. Today’s chef embraces sustainability, serving a modern showcase of Thai flavours sourced locally, including microgreens grown on-site. For the full experience, request the Taste of Jaras tasting menu with wine pairing. Book at least 24 hours in advance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8076;Kai Yang Wanna;Thailand;Khon Kaen;271 Mu 11, Mittraphap Road, Kham Muang, Khao Suan Kwang, Khon Kaen, 40280, Thailand;16.8536929;102.8594081;78;false;false;Isan;Grilled chicken is the name of the game at this Isan shophouse restaurant. Launched in 1973 by the current owner’s father, it uses a local breed, spices them using a family recipe and skilfully grills them over charcoal. They only make 200 a day, which always sell out, so reserve a bird or arrive early. Also on the menu are simple Isan dishes, including delicious pork larb. Seating is available inside with or without AC and outside on the veranda.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8078;Beach Grill and Bar;Thailand;Phang-Nga;Devasom Khao Lak Beach Resort & Villas, 79 Mu 3, Khuekkhak, Takua Pa, Phang-Nga, 82220, Thailand;8.6955746;98.2397567;50;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Offering a relaxing setting with indoor and outdoor seating perfect for enjoying cocktails and a delightful mix of Mediterranean dishes, against the backdrop of the evening sunset. Specialising in fresh seafood grilled over a wood-burning stove, the restaurant's standout dish is a seafood pizza with shrimp, squid, mussels, and mozzarella. Complete your dining experience with a delicious dessert like crispy fried bananas served with coconut milk ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8079;Khrua Nong;Thailand;Phang-Nga;132/8 Phet Kasem Road, Bang Nai Si, Takua Pa, Phang-Nga, 82110, Thailand;8.871535;98.36038;25;true;true;Thai;The husband-and-wife team go to market every day to select fresh, local ingredients and seafood and offer a wide selection of Thai dishes. Check the blackboard for the specials which change every day, but the crispy softshell crab with a peppery chilli sauce is unmissable.;Cash only;[]
8080;Khao (Vadhana);Thailand;Bangkok;15 Soi Ekkamai 10, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7290273;100.58784;18;false;false;Thai;Khao presents delightful Thai cuisine in a beautiful dining space that is inspired by traditional rice barns. The menu is all about attention to detail, using premium ingredients and blending diverse flavours that cater to every palate. Whether for casual dining or business meetings, it's an ideal spot to experience a thoughtfully curated meal that stays true to the essence of Thai cuisine. Book the Chef's Table menu for an exquisite culinary journey.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8081;O Tao Bang Niao;Thailand;Phuket;362 Phuket Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8763976;98.3936578;42;true;false;Street Food;Since 1982, this family-run spot has been serving flavoursome O Tao, a stir-fried dish found only in Phuket. Made with seafood and battered taro, O Tao is cooked over a charcoal flame and boasts a combination of soft, gooey and crispy textures. They are well-balanced here, and the smoky aroma from the charcoal also helps to elevate the dish. Other options available include a fried crispy seafood omelette that is well worth ordering.;Cash only;[]
8082;Go La;Thailand;Phuket;11 Kra Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.8766786;98.3930647;50;false;true;Small eats;In its third generation of family ownership, this is one of Phuket’s best Hokkien-style fried noodle joints. Its charm is conjured up by a concoction of special flavours, the sounds of the wok and charcoal smells. Order the yellow hokkien noodles with an extra egg for a creamier texture.;Cash only;[]
8083;Khanom Jeen Mae Ploy;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;7/1 Mu 6, Siriratchathani Road, Muen Wai, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9975141;102.1032772;32;false;true;Street Food;The secret to Mae Ploy’s bouncy yet gooey noodles is the fermented rice flour from Ban Pra Dok. There’s a creamy, peppery spicy fish curry with coconut cream, a red chicken curry with offal, and a sweet, nutty peanut curry. The spicy fish curry has a lovely, aromatic fermented taste.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8084;Sookjailand;Thailand;Khon Kaen;98 Mu 7, Maliwan Road, Nong Bua, Ban Fang, Khon Kaen, 40270, Thailand;16.4670347;102.6146659;75;true;false;Isan;Time drifts past at this tranquil Isan restaurant, where diners eat in private bamboo pavilions dotting a large rice field. There are no tables—meals are served on woven mats on the floor, local style. And the food, which comes in both shareable set menus and à la carte dishes, is just as authentic as the setting. Made from quality, fresh ingredients, simple dishes like the grilled snakehead fish set and the local crab soup with veggies, are highly recommended.;Car park,Cash only,Garden or park,Great view;[]
8085;Baan;Thailand;Bangkok;139/5 Wireless Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.73774;100.5465971;36;true;false;Thai;At this sister restaurant to Le Du, comforting family recipes take centre stage. The intimate venue boasts a contemporary look with marble tables and chic lighting. They prioritise high-quality ingredients, including beef from Pak Chong's Islamic farms and responsibly sourced seafood from southern Thailand. Pair dishes with their selection of biodynamic, organic wines and house cocktails.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8086;Kaithong Original;Thailand;Nonthaburi;164/13-15 Soi Chaeng Watthana-Pak Kret 33, Chaeng Watthana Road, Bang Phut, Pak Kret, Nonthaburi, 11120, Thailand;13.908368;100.537926;75;true;true;Thai-Chinese;This family-run establishment is renowned for its traditional recipes, serving fresh meat and seafood flavours in simple yet refined and lightly seasoned dishes. Catering to different tastes, the stir-fried liver with garlic is made with either pork or chicken liver. The inviting, comfortable space can also accommodate larger groups.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
8087;Khao;Thailand;Chiang Mai;Four Seasons Resort, 502 Mu 1, Mae Rim-Samoeng Old Road, Rim Tai, Mae Rim, Chiang Mai, 50180, Thailand;18.9163599;98.9315887;26;false;false;Thai;Khao serves Northern Thai cuisine, along with some dishes from other regions. The chef, a prestigious culinary school graduate with 10 years of luxury hotel experience, brings an international perspective and a modern identity to traditional Thai dishes. The dining room is contemporary and inviting – crystal chandeliers coexist with carved teak panelling – and the terrace offers serene views of rice fields and hills.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
8088;Tang Sui Heng (Banthat Thong Road);Thailand;Bangkok;649 Banthat Thong Road, Wang Mai, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7468255;100.5237754;24;false;true;Street Food;This iconic family-run shop has been packed with locals for more than 50 years. These days, the family’s second generation runs it, but the founder’s talent for cooking dishes like the signature claypot stewed duck with intestines, blood jelly, and feet clearly runs in the family.;Cash only;[]
8089;North;Thailand;Bangkok;8 Soi Sukhumvit 33, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7335925;100.5675424;52;true;false;Northern Thai;This classic Thai house, painted in green with a lush front garden, offers an oasis in the city. Under Chef Chumpol's guidance, a skilled team led by a northern Thai head chef presents a menu preserving the traditional taste of northern Thailand. The lunch offers à la carte choices, while dinner features a seasonal set menu using ingredients from various regions. Highlights include the herb-packed Northern sharing set, Khan-Tok, and the flavourful Khao Soi.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
8090;Guay Jub Ubon;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;7 Phrommathep Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2252387;104.8580091;20;true;true;Street Food;For over 70 years, this little gem has maintained strict quality control, carefully selecting offal from more than 10kg of offcuts each day. Their specialty is guay jub rice noodles with pork offal in a dark five-spice soup. They also serve delectable egg noodle and wonton soups.;Cash only;[]
8091;Samchai Coffee (Thepyothi Road);Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;168/4 Thepyothi Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2324445;104.8648389;88;true;false;Small eats;The menu boasts a tasty dried shredded pork and a range of sausages. A highlight is the Indochina pan-fried egg served with a side sandwich. The eggs are cooked sunny side up with margarine, then topped with sweet and salty Chinese sausage and peppery Vietnamese sausage slices.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
8092;Antito;Thailand;Bangkok;14F, Eastin Grand Sathorn 33/1 Sathon Tai Road, Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.7190616;100.5222841;91;false;false;Italian;Located on the 14th floor of Eastin Grand Sathorn, Chef Amerigo Sesti’s restaurant-bar offers a creative take on Northern Italian classics from his childhood, complemented by stunning city views. The stylish dining room features pop art and cosy seating. Try the handmade Italian pasta or tiramisu, showcasing the chef’s flair for authentic flavours. A DJ sets the mood from Thursday to Sunday nights.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
8093;Kagero;Thailand;Bangkok;Modernform Forty 9 55/1, Sukhumvit 49 Road, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.70929;100.59795;63;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;At Kagero, a fusion of Japanese and Italian cuisine is created by combining Japanese and European techniques to transform premium ingredients into a sensory delight. Diners can watch the chef at work from the counter or choose a private room for a more exclusive experience. We recommend the Kani Croquet, renowned for its bold flavours, succulent crab meat, and tantalising aroma. Conclude your meal with a delicious kakigōri, featuring a milky ice cream centre.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8094;Buabok;Thailand;Phuket;Amanpuri Resort 118, 1 Si Sunthon Road, Pansea Beach, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9839277;98.2765156;95;false;false;Thai;Buabok is set in a tranquil resort that features reflective pools and swaying palms, creating the perfect backdrop for dining. Enjoy aromatic Thai cuisine beneath the pitched roof of an elegant wooden villa. From Thai salads to smooth curries, the menu is crafted from fresh local produce. Arrive before sunset to embrace the gentle pace of nature and stunning views of the Andaman Sea. Don't miss their rich, flavourful Panaeng Nuea, an Angus beef red curry.;Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
8095;Noodles Soi 12 (Ban Suan);Thailand;Chon Buri;44/8-9 Mu 6, Soi Ban Suan-Setthakit 30, Ban Suan, Mueang Chon Buri, Chon Buri, 20000, Thailand;13.3510035;101.0106119;98;true;true;Noodles;With its wooden furniture and rustic charm, this is a delightful spot for an early breakfast or lunch. The real star here is the soup with aromatic dried squid and pork ribs imparting rich flavour. Each tasty spoonful is testament to the traditional recipe.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8096;Krua Pla Tu Tid Oun;Thailand;Chon Buri;8/1 Nadedee Road Soi 5, Saen Suk, Mueang Chon Buri, Chon Buri, 20130, Thailand;13.2693409;100.9270292;19;false;true;Thai;This place near Bang Saen beach has been popular with tourists for decades. The signature is, of course, pla tu (Thai mackerel), but the menu extends from seafood options such as sillago, sea bass and local scallops – all cooked in classic Thai style – to crispy deep-fried mackerel cheek with a chilli-garlic aroma that's addictive. If you prefer a milder taste, the staff are happy to adjust the spice level to suit your palate.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8097;Baannok Bangkok;Thailand;Bangkok;34/3 VIVRE Building, Lang Suan Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7416843;100.5433475;36;false;false;Thai;Baannok serves authentic Korat-style Thai food, in which the sweetness that is typical to the region is toned down for broader tastes. To awaken the palate, try the sweet and sour Korat sausage salad. The signature Pad Mhee Korat with a giant river prawn is expertly wok-fried with duck egg and accompanied by a smooth sweet sauce. For something comforting, take the Kaeng Liang Kam Thale So, a spicy vegetable soup, fragrant with herbs and spices commonly used in Isan cooking. Advance reservation is a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8098;Uan Ja Noodle;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;45 U Thong Road, Ho Rattanachai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3637608;100.5786227;46;true;false;Noodles;A popular lunch spot for over half a century, they sell a prolific 100kg of meatballs a day. The buoyant balls playfully float in the noodle soup and the condiments are homemade, including a spicy, sour chili vinegar sauce. Fresh-cooked or slow-cooked beef options are also available.;Cash only;[]
8100;Yommarat O-Cha;Thailand;Nakhon Ratchasima;9-11 Yommarat Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Nakhon Ratchasima, Nakhon Ratchasima, 30000, Thailand;14.9788544;102.0985872;66;false;true;Small eats;The standout dish at this local favourite is the yentafo soup with fish balls, soy sauce and tofu. The flavour is pleasantly sweet and sour but this isn’t the spicy yentafo tomyum common in Bangkok. The soup is cooked fresh using a vibrant mix of condiments. Dry and wet options are available and all the great toppings are homemade.;Cash only;[]
8101;Whale Chicken Noodles;Thailand;Khon Kaen;156 Sri Chant Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4307;102.83192;74;false;false;Noodles;The secret to the popularity of this eatery is its tender chicken and flavoursome broth – made with chicken bones and vegetables, it has a rich, meaty and naturally sweet flavour. Enjoy the breeze as you dine on the sidewalk, just like a local.;Cash only;[]
8102;Withee Laab;Thailand;Chiang Mai;94-120 Charoen Muang Road, Wat Ket, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50000, Thailand;18.7871149;99.007336;99;true;false;Northern Thai;This charming wooden building down a narrow alley has been serving delicious laab for years. The spicy minced buffalo meat and zesty cooked minced pork are sure to impress. With surprisingly affordable prices, this is a gem worth seeking out.;Cash only;[]
8103;Baan Rearn Mai;Thailand;Phang-Nga;Ban Khok Kloi - Na Tai, Khok Kloi, Takua Thung, Phang-Nga, 82140, Thailand;8.2783363;98.299873;99;false;false;Seafood;Operating for 25 years, this small eatery offers an à la carte menu focused on seafood. The freshly prepared meals are light, allowing the natural umami of the seafood to shine. In addition to their signature yellow curry crab, the steamed sea bass with soy sauce is a must-try.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8105;Fuego;Thailand;Bangkok;2F, The Taste Thonglor, Thong Lo Soi 11, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7328835;100.5818174;58;true;true;Spanish Contemporary;Helmed by a Spanish chef with a passion for Japanese cuisine, Fuego boldly blends these two culinary traditions. From your seat in this intimate setting, watch premium-quality Spanish and Japanese ingredients being meticulously crafted in the open kitchen. Don't miss the signature paella. Another standout is the tapas, complemented by Japanese whisky and sake. The velvety, multidimensional miso cheesecake is the perfect ending.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
8106;Baan Suriyasai;Thailand;Bangkok;174 Surawong Road, Si Phraya, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7291293;100.5277622;92;false;false;Thai;Located in a restored 100-year-old mansion in the heart of the city, Baan Suriyasai evokes early 20C Thai elegance with time-tested dishes and old-world hospitality. The menu is drawn from royal recipes from the Rama V era and bygone family favourites, including the five-spice stew with boiled eggs, and the stir-fried crispy pork belly, fish flakes and dried shrimp with seasoned paste. Head to the classic Thai cocktail bar upstairs for an after-dinner drink.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8107;Santi;Thailand;Ubon Ratchathani;101-17 Chawala Nok Road, Nai Mueang, Mueang Ubon Ratchathani, Ubon Ratchathani, 34000, Thailand;15.2336056;104.8466068;83;false;true;Thai-Chinese;Diners can sit inside or roadside in this simple, open-air restaurant. Thai-Chinese is the fare and dishes are prepared at the front. The sound of the wok and sight of the flames make an impressive spectacle. The stir-fried minced pork with olives is a must for its smoky, intense flavours. The deep-fried seabass with sweet fish sauce takes a little longer to prepare but the result is a fantastically crispy skin that goes well with the homemade spicy sauce.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8108;Meesapam Khun Yai Chian;Thailand;Phuket;56/8, 65/24 Mu 1, Thep Krasatti Road, Ko Kaeo, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.947671;98.391828;33;true;true;Thai-Chinese;Grandma Chian opened this Hokkien restaurant in 1952. Her great-great grandchildren have stayed loyal to her recipes and proudly exhibit her cooking utensils. Serving Phuket favourites, the Mee Sapam, stir-fried Hokkien noodles with seafood, is great. The stir-fried oysters with crispy egg roll are beautifully crafted with beansprouts, kale and a tasty chilli sauce.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8109;Kiti Panit;Thailand;Chiang Mai;19 Tha Phae Road, Chang Khlan, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50100, Thailand;18.7723871;98.9990343;42;false;true;Northern Thai;Turning their great-great-grandparents’ 1880s mansion into a restaurant, Kiti Panit’s owners decided to create an updated take on traditional Lanna cuisine. The results include intense and complex Hang Le, or northern Thai curry, and savoury grilled chicken salad with coriander. Also recommended are the signature Khao Mao Gorn Rad Gati, or unripe rice with coconut milk, and the creative seasonal desserts.;Air conditioning;[]
8110;Baan Mai Rim Nahm;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;43/1 Mu 2, U Thong Road, Pratu Chai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3480559;100.5696049;60;true;true;Thai;This local favourite has been serving flavoursome Central Thai cuisine in a laid-back setting by the Chao Phraya River for over 20 years. The skilled chef cooks everything, including the recommended Tom Yum with redtail catfish and the huge grilled river prawns, with quality ingredients from local farmers and fisherfolk. Meals can be enjoyed in the air-conditioned dining room, on the terrace, or even on the water if you book the restaurant’s riverboat tour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
8111;Nai Liak Beef Noodles;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;6/7 Pa Maphrao Road, Ho Rattanachai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3621885;100.5786542;15;true;true;Noodles;Mr. Liak, this eatery’s owner, started his business way back in 1961 – before moving to his current roadside location in 1977. He serves delicious beef noodle soup at wallet-friendly prices. Beef offal, braised beef, beef meatballs and stewed tendons are among the options available in the savoury broth – vermicelli, herbs and spices are also packed into this signature dish. Expect a wait during peak hours.;Cash only;[]
8112;Baan Pomphet;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;13/5 U Thong Road, Ho Rattanachai, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3464255;100.5764654;86;true;false;Thai;This Thai restaurant next to Pom Phet (Diamond Fortress) is in the distinctive-looking boutique hotel of the same name. Inside, the stylish dining room is fitted with large windows that frame a view of the restaurant’s deck and the Chao Phraya. Sourcing ingredients from the river and local farms, the chef creates flavourful dishes like standouts grilled river prawns and boiled freshwater snails in red curry soup. Book ahead for a riverside table at dinner.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8113;Sang Ka Sri;Thailand;Phuket;262/8 Yaowarat Road, Talat Yai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.9033455;98.3777623;74;true;false;Thai;This outlet with a red-brown zinc roof offers a menu of both individual and sharing dishes, with nicely balanced flavours. Despite its humble guise, Sang Ka Sri attracts a crowd, so be prepared to wait for a table before enjoying the fresh squid with herbs and tangy dressing.;Cash only;[]
8114;Krua Taan;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;65/16 Mu 7, Soi Mu Ban Chang, Pai Ling, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3602614;100.5920237;58;false;true;Thai;In this spacious, open-air pavilion, Aunty Taan serves traditional-style cooking that has won the hearts of local diners and tourists alike. Do try the prawn and herb spicy salad, which features just-right grilled prawn meat and various refreshing herbs bound together with a flavourful dressing. The fiery stir-fried minced pork cartilage is also delicious and aromatic. This is the perfect stop after visiting the nearby floating market and elephant village.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8115;Suriyan Chandra;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;38 Mu 7, Phra Khao, Bang Ban, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13250, Thailand;14.3249412;100.4524496;69;false;true;Thai;The old mill that houses this riverside restaurant is over 130 years old and provides a unique vintage atmosphere to diners seeking a memorable experience. Delicate titbits such as Toong Thong and the flower-like Chor Muang make delightful starters, before moving on to main courses including the fabulous fried snakehead fish with herbs and deep-fried shrimp with tamarind sauce. They also offer a river tour package along the Noi, which culminates in dining at the restaurant. Booking is essential.;Car park,Cash only,Great view,Terrace;[]
8116;La Cucina;Thailand;Chon Buri;Andaz Pattaya Jomtien Beach  345 Mu 3, Na Chom Thian, Sattahip, Chon Buri, 20250, Thailand;12.7928542;100.910924;98;true;true;Italian;Off the beaten tourist path, La Cucina offers an escape to a lush, tropical garden setting, where blue and white tiled floors, French windows and bossa nova tunes foster a relaxed atmosphere. This restaurant helmed by local chefs and an affable service team has an enticing Italian menu. Handmade pizzas are the stand-out.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8118;Bisou;Thailand;Bangkok;68 Soi Langsuan 9, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7376896;100.5420893;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Antoine Darquin and sommelier Théo Lavergne bring a fresh, fashionable Parisian flair to Bangkok's dining scene. Bisou delivers sexy simplicity through modern French cuisine, prioritising premium ingredients. The stylish yet relaxed space features enchanting lights, a spiral staircase and wall art. The dishes and rare wines contribute to a unique local experience influenced by the latest trends from Paris.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
8119;Mae Pong Sri;Thailand;Chon Buri;42/99 Mu 9, Sukhumvit Road, Pattaya, Nong Prue, Bang Lamung, Chon Buri, 20150, Thailand;12.9283854;100.8993169;52;false;false;Small eats;The go-to spot in Pattaya for pork offal soup with boiled sweet leaf bush, this eatery draws inspiration from Thai cuisine nationwide to offer a plethora of quick street food dishes. From the many noodle and rice options, the stir-fried glass noodles with seafood stand out.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
8121;hom;Thailand;Phuket;InterContinental Phuket Resort, 333, 333/3 Mu 3, Kamala Beach, Kamala, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.9625956;98.2852539;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;After a stroll through a serene garden walkway, you will find this restaurant inside the InterContinental Resort. The Portuguese chef showcases a fermentation-heavy concept on the menu, highlighting new sides to local produce. Leeks, betel leaves and pandan are just some of the ingredients that are given the fermentation treatment, in delicately executed dishes. The natural wine list is in keeping with the restaurant’s ethos, and the intimate atmosphere makes it ideal for a romantic dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
8123;Juksunchae;Thailand;Bangkok;5F, Woodberry Common, 15/3 Soi Ruamrudee, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7405018;100.5494693;28;true;false;Korean, Contemporary;Driven by the chef’s desire to put an original twist on Korean recipes, this restaurant delivers well-known cuisine through a creative lens. The flavours and combinations may be long established, but they’re presented with original touches – such as a painting-like uni bibimbap that will make you see the dish in a completely new light. A few flavour innovations can also be found, such as strawberry doenjang. The contemporary reinvention of classic cooking is reflected in the combination of chic décor and traditional Korean furniture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8124;Den Kushi Flori;Thailand;Bangkok;LGF, Erawan Bangkok Building, 494 Phloen Chit Road, Lumphini, Pathum Wan, Bangkok, 10330, Thailand;13.7436835;100.5406109;56;false;true;Japanese;A collaboration between two Japanese chefs, and their first overseas outpost, this minimalist restaurant consists of a U-shaped wooden counter wrapped around an open kitchen. The chefs have experience in both Japan and France, meaning their 5 or 7 course tasting menus blend French technique with the essence of Japanese cuisine – a few Thai touches, like a spicy watermelon sauce, provide a nod to the locale. Rice cooked with corn is a highlight, well-judged in texture and topped with teriyaki beef.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8125;Small Dinner Club;Thailand;Bangkok;1109 Charoen Krung Road, Si Phraya, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7279501;100.5159868;72;true;false;Innovative;Set in a 2-storey house in the historic town, Small Dinner Club exudes mystery and charm. The dimly lit interior sports a striking black colour scheme. In his own words, Chef Sareen “pulls apart, questions and reimagines Thai cuisine”. Unafraid of challenging conventions, he includes savoury ingredients in sweet recipes and sweet ingredients, like seasonal fruit, in savoury dishes, resulting in intelligently crafted and artistically presented Thai food.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8126;Chuan Kitchen;Thailand;Nonthaburi;50/666 Mu 6, Soi Mu Ban Mueang Thong Thani, Ban Mai, Pak Kret, Nonthaburi, 11120, Thailand;13.915142;100.5426776;25;true;true;South East Asian;With Singaporean chicken rice, Indonesian laksa and Malaysian Bak Kut Teh the highlights, Chuan Kitchen is the only restaurant in Nonthaburi offering this mix of national cuisine. Its stylish design is welcoming, with a high wooden ceiling, and floor-to-ceiling windows, accentuated by black stainless-steel frames and lighting. The fried typhoon soft shell crab stands out with its light crispy texture with a chilli, deep-fried crispy garlic and onion black bean sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8127;Riva del Fiume;Thailand;Bangkok;LF, Four Seasons Hotel Bangkok at Chao Phraya River, 300/1 Charoen Krung Road, Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.711956;100.5108672;90;false;false;Italian;The view from the terrace is of the Chao Phraya, but inside, this modern Italian restaurant in the Four Seasons Hotel feels more like Lake Como with its Euro vibes, open kitchen and wood oven. At the helm is an Italian chef who worked at several famed restaurants in Europe. Here he deftly cooks favourites like his pizza and home-made pasta with quality ingredients imported from Italy. Adding to the experience is the high level of service of the team.;Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8128;Tiffin by La Sala;Thailand;Phuket;Anantara Mai Khao Phuket Villas, 888 Mu 3, Mai Khao, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;8.1585535;98.2979145;36;false;false;Indian;Al fresco dining by a tranquil lagoon is the big draw at this restaurant located in Anantara Mai Khao Villas. The chef, from Maharashtra, takes diners on a journey through authentic Indian cuisine via an extensive à la carte featuring curries, a tiffin chaat platter and dishes from the tandoor oven. The cooking is flavoursome and well-spiced, with their signature lamb vindaloo a stand-out and the freshly baked naan well worth trying. Indoor dining with a view of the open kitchen is also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8129;Ruen Jarung;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;67/3 Mu 2, Ban Wa, Bang Pa-in, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13160, Thailand;14.3017247;100.6016118;28;false;false;Thai;Eating here requires foresight, but your efforts will be rewarded. Booking only opens twice a year for three seatings a day Friday-Sunday. To book, check social media and follow the rules, which change each time — oh, and you’ll also need to choose your order in advance. But once you arrive at the vintage Thai house, you’ll be regaled with generous portions of expertly cooked authentic Thai fare, like the impressive Nam Prik Song Mae.;Car park,Cash only,Great view;[]
8131;Kampun Gai Yang;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;94/7 Mu 6, Rochana Road, Phai Ling, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3505911;100.6022782;42;true;true;Isan;Opened in 2017, this restaurant serves authentic Isan food in a commercial building on Rochana Road. Air-conditioned and filling two floors, the casual dining room is decorated with wood panels and other touches that suggest traditional Thai houses. The skilled chef cooks halal-friendly food following recipes from his grandmother, who is from Nakhon Phanom. His signature dish, Kampun grilled chicken, is recommended. The quality of service adds to the experience.;Car park;[]
8132;Angeum;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;55/17 Mu 7, Khlong Suan Phlu, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3328868;100.6034507;95;true;false;Vietnamese;The story of Vietnamese food in Ayutthaya started over 150 years ago with the Vietnamese community in Bang Sai District. It continues at this modern two-floor restaurant smartly decorated with wooden walls, colourful paintings and a stylish bar. The menu may be short but it’s packed with authentic Vietnamese dishes. The skilled chef prepares everything using fresh quality ingredients. The signature dish, Nem Nuong is a delight to assemble and eat.;Car park;[]
8133;Khaotom Chedi;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;254/14 Rochana Road, Phai Ling, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.3543607;100.5915574;71;false;true;Thai;This popular late-night spot is known for its fresh ingredients and flavourful dishes. The chef-owner warmly welcomes guests and takes orders with a smile. The menu changes daily, depending on the ingredients available. Enjoy dining outdoors with a view of Sam Pluem Temple's chedi.;Cash only;[]
8134;Nitan;Thailand;Phuket;177/38 Mu 6, Si Sunthon Road, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;7.9796984;98.3295793;48;true;false;Southern Thai, Contemporary;Nitan, or ’determination’ in Thai, may refer to the chef’s aim of creating a real gastronomic experience. This is most evident in the tasting menu and wine pairing, where quality seasonal and local ingredients inform the cooking. Contemporary techniques are used to prepare classic Southern Thai dishes, with well-balanced flavours and a dash of creativity. The restaurant has a warm vibe and is minimally decorated, with wooden furniture and a window into the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8135;FishHouse;Thailand;Ko Samui;Kimpton Kitalay Samui, 10/79 Mu 5, Bo Phut, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.5743154;100.0800032;23;false;true;European;Set inside the Kimpton Kitalay resort, FishHouse crafts à la carte European recipes using the freshest local ingredients. Take a seat on the deck overlooking the beach and enjoy the sea breeze and the lively atmosphere by the pool where sunbathers sip cocktails. Start with ceviche, bursting with fresh tropical passionfruit flavours and perfectly marinated diced seabass. The Black Paella with squid and squid ink is ideal to share.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
8137;Jampa;Thailand;Phuket;The Community House, Tri Vananda, 46/6 Mu 3, Thep Krasatti, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;8.0396599;98.3173679;87;true;false;European Contemporary;Chef Dingen’s inventive contemporary European menu embraces a philosophy of sustainability and zero waste. À la carte is available all day, but we recommend the exquisitely prepared Jampa Experience for lunch, which features complex natural flavours that change with the seasons. For a unique lakeside experience on Saturdays, Hideaway’s 4-course lunch, cooked over a wood fire, both tantalises the tastebuds and educates the diner about sustainable farming.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8139;Tumkratoei Sagate;Thailand;Khon Kaen;88-89 Mu 20, Maliwan Road, Ban Pet, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4520331;102.7850221;97;false;false;Isan;The owner is from Roi Et Province (formerly Sagate Province). The place offers flavourful food, warm service and wallet-friendly prices in a relaxed setting. The signature spicy seafood salad with fermented fish sauce is recommended, and beyond the Som Tum dishes, standouts include fried sour fish and spicy chicken soup with glass noodles. Indoors and outdoor seating are available. Nightly live music adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
8140;Sanyod (Bang Rak);Thailand;Bangkok;89 Soi Charat Wiang, Si Lom, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7187862;100.5176462;34;false;true;Chinese;With a history spanning more than half a century, what started as a food stall located in a small alley has since grown into a popular and bustling neighbourhood restaurant. They specialise in Cantonese cuisine, and their roast duck and signature sauces are highly recommended, especially paired with Cantonese-style noodles. The menu also features a deliciously tender clay pot-braised beef.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8141;Loba Bang Niao;Thailand;Phuket;18/61 Mae Luan Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.88271;98.39092;90;false;false;Small eats;Loba was a traditional snack for Fujian Chinese in Phuket and this shop has remained consistent since day one. The semi-crispy pork offal and aromatic spices of the mixed loba blend well with a sweet chilli and crushed peanut sauce. The 4 deep-fried dishes are also mouth-watering treats.;Cash only;[]
8142;Talung Thai;Thailand;Phuket;GF, Paresa Resort, 49 Mu 6, Layi-Nakhale Road, Kamala, Kathu, Phuket, 83150, Thailand;7.932881;98.26248;83;false;true;Thai;The views from Paresa Resort, high on a clifftop, are breathtaking at sunset. It’s an idyllic spot to sip cocktails, before moving to the terrace for sumptuous southern and central Thai cuisine. Start with mixed Thai canapés or the soft shell crab miang, followed by the fragrant stir-fried Phuket lobster. Don't forget to save room for the Thai-styled dessert.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8143;The Thai Library;Thailand;Phuket;Trisara Resort, 60/1 Mu 6, Srisoonthorn Road, Choeng Thale, Thalang, Phuket, 83110, Thailand;8.0357554;98.2759199;37;false;true;Thai;Inspired by local recipes and ingredients, The Thai Library has created a refined, southern menu. Take the Massaman Plamuek for example, which uses local Andaman octopus in a sweet and creamy sauce, while the stir-fried jumbo black tiger prawns, with crispy garlic and chilli, sing subtle herbal notes. To top it off, it’s the perfect romantic experience with an intimate setting indoors and breezy sunset views on the outdoor terrace overlooking a secluded beach.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8144;Huen Lamphun (Taling Chan);Thailand;Bangkok;64/233 Mu 5, Suan Phak Road, Chimphli, Taling Chan, Bangkok, 10170, Thailand;13.793394;100.42802;82;true;true;Northern Thai;Northern Thai food has a special place in the hearts of locals, but finding good food like this outside the region can be tough. So Huen Lamphun is a gem of a find, to such an extent that large groups from the neighbourhood return in droves. Every dish uses organic vegetables grown onsite. The grilled, fermented northern Thai pork in banana leaf explodes with chilli and garlic. Another favourite is Makwan-marinated grilled chicken with a peppery flavour and herbal aroma.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8145;Indus;Thailand;Bangkok;71 Soi Sukhumvit 26, Khlong Tan, Khlong Toei, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7237635;100.5700912;65;false;true;Indian;Indus presents a diverse and approachable selection of Indian dishes, showcasing flavours from Punjab, Kashmir, Goa, and Rajasthan, skilfully adapted to the Thai palate. As a certified Halal restaurant, it upholds the highest standards for both its meat and vegetarian offerings. The signature Raan is available in various sizes. This special lamb leg is slow-cooked for seven hours and then gently grilled to achieve tender, juicy perfection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8146;Saawaan;Thailand;Bangkok;39/19 Soi Suan Phlu, Sathon Road, Thung Maha Mek, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.721809;100.53741;72;true;false;Thai contemporary;"Saawaan", meaning "heaven" in Thai, delivers a transcendent dining experience courtesy of a set menu that artistically plays with Thai flavours and cooking techniques including fermenting, steaming, boiling and grilling over charcoal. Each dish is plated and served in its own unique way, delighting diners. The menu highlights both imported and local ingredients, emphasising the restaurant's commitment to quality and community.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8147;Maadae;Thailand;Chiang Mai;86-88 Thapae Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.788074;99.0009199;79;true;true;Seafood;Meaning ‘come’ in the Southern language, ‘Maadae’ invites you to enjoy delightful seafood in a welcoming atmosphere. Supporting local Chumphon fishermen and sourcing seasonal organic produce, their menu rotates with fresh ingredients. The evening selection offers diverse options, including superb freshly grilled seafood paired with a spicy sauce.;Air conditioning;[]
8148;Talung;Thailand;Chiang Mai;8 Chotana Road Soi 12, Chang Phueak, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.8238549;98.9864371;30;false;false;Southern Thai;Having recently relocated to this ground floor eatery under a residential apartment, Talung is simply decorated with air conditioning, a lively bar and serves Southern Thai. It’s a small family business, the staff are friendly and attentive, and help each other from kitchen to table. The stir-fried squid with squid ink has a rich, well-seasoned sauce and herbal scent. The stir-fried prawns come with a homemade southern Thai shrimp paste and young bitter beans.;Air conditioning;[]
8149;Guay Tiew Pet Tun Saraphi;Thailand;Chiang Mai;80 Mu 3, Liap Thang Rotfai Road, Saraphi, Chiang Mai, 50140, Thailand;18.680254;99.0446951;15;false;true;Street Food;Take a break and make tracks to this wallet-friendly shop that’s mastered braised duck. The duck noodles use the family’s secret blend of spices, while the roasted duck has succulent meat and crispy skin, moistened by the duck's own jus. Northern-Thai and other dishes are available.;Cash only;[]
8150;Koh Thai Kitchen;Thailand;Ko Samui;Four Seasons Resort Koh Samui, 219 Mu 5, Ang Thong, Ko Samui, 84140, Thailand;9.5734478;99.9239852;72;false;true;Thai;Koh Thai Kitchen is located on a hilltop within the Four Seasons Hotel. The restaurant's alfresco dining areas sport a rustic style. Diners can enjoy southern and central Thai dishes made with premium ingredients such as local seafood, Australian lamb and Wagyu beef. All of which while breathing in the fresh air as you admire the drop-dead vista of sprawling jungle and blue sea dotted with nearby islands, as you snap the dramatic Instagram-perfect sunsets.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8151;Kaow Laor;Thailand;Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya;11/4 Mu 6, Soi Wat Thammaram,  Ban Pom, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, Phra Nakhon Si Ayutthaya, 13000, Thailand;14.32963;100.607785;65;false;true;Thai;With a whitewashed interior and views of the garden and river, Kaow Laor feels like a modern country home. The Thai menu is replete with grandma's recipes, offering giant river prawns, featherback fish balls and other local river fish. Each dish is expertly cooked and seasoned, and it’s like eating authentic Thai food at home. The imported mackerel with fish sauce is prepared with a light crispy skin, an aromatic fish sauce, deep-fried edible flowers and a spicy dressing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
8152;Mook Manee;Thailand;Phuket;1120 Wiset Road, Rawai, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83100, Thailand;7.7756537;98.3285527;64;false;true;Seafood;Located near Rawai Beach, Mook Manee stands out for its array of live seafood for diners to choose from, including squid, tiger prawns, a variety of crabs, and 3kg Phuket rainbow lobster. The restaurant holds up to 300, but the best seats offer views of the vibrant seafood market trading outside. Menu highlights include the fragrant stir-fried clams with chilli paste. A wooden terrace on the beach is also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8154;Khun Thip's Satay;Thailand;Phang-Nga;184 Phet Kasem Road, Thai Chang, Mueang Phang-nga, Phang-Nga, 82000, Thailand;8.46182;98.5312725;56;false;false;Street Food;Serving satay, and only satay, since 1975 – it’s now Phang-Nga’s iconic food. The 2-day marinated sauce smothers charcoal-grilled chicken, pork, pork intestine or shrimp. Our favourite is the tender pork satay with coconut aroma, rich peanut flavour and fresh cucumber relish.;;[]
8155;Blue Elephant;Thailand;Phuket;96 Krabi Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.88612;98.38458;42;true;false;Thai;Following the lead of Bangkok’s flagship, their colonial-style mansion with wood-panelled interior, wicker furnishings and louver shutters, set in lush gardens, pulls in the crowds. They serve a roll call of Thai classics, but the main attraction, the Peranakan Menu, for couples to share, is unique to Phuket. The signature Peranakan Tumee King Mackerel comes in large pieces of fish in a rich coconut curry with crispy okra. They also have a great cocktail selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8157;Philippe;Thailand;Bangkok;20/15-17 Soi Sukhumvit 39, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7326935;100.5711587;64;true;true;French;Chef Philippe Peretti’s proudly by-the-book French cooking has been a feature of the city since 1997, so why try and change it? The décor, like the food, doesn’t sway into the innovative – dark wood panels, traditional furniture and white tablecloths give the dining room a traditionally elegant feel. The well-seasoned Burgundy snails are a treat, as is Philippe’s special chocolate soufflé. If you’re searching for the classical French experience, look no further.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8158;Charoen Saeng Silom;Thailand;Bangkok;492/6 Soi Charoen Krung 49, Silom Road, Suriyawong, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7228038;100.516869;52;false;false;Street Food;Stewed in a rich, aromatic gravy with Chinese herbs, the soft, caramelised pork tantalises the tastebuds, and is a Bangkok favourite. The recipe, created by the owner’s grandfather in 1959, was adapted by her father. It’s served with a homemade spicy sauce and pickles and is great value.;Cash only;[]
8159;The Local;Thailand;Bangkok;32 Soi Sukhumvit 23, Sukhumvit Road, Khlong Toei Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7409221;100.5635;28;true;true;Thai;This colonial-style building provides an elegant contrast with the skyscrapers of Bangkok. Its private dining rooms ooze old world charm, while the main restaurant has thick wicker chairs and artful murals. The secret family recipes pay homage to the diversity offered by Thailand’s regions. We recommend the deep-fried seabass: deboned and served in large slices with an intense sweet and sour sauce. The assortment of desserts with homemade ice-cream makes for a refreshing finish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8160;Chef Man (Sathon);Thailand;Bangkok;3F, Eastin Grand Sathorn, 33/1 Sathon Tai Road, Yan Nawa, Sathon, Bangkok, 10120, Thailand;13.719142;100.521736;59;false;false;Cantonese;Hongkonger Chef Man Wai Yi has a stellar reputation for ‘home-style’ Cantonese cuisine, delicious dim sum and legendary Peking duck. The mule duck, from a private local supplier, is roasted for 4 hours. His special recipe and sweet mango combine for a mouthwatering affair. The glutinous crispy shrimp with soya sauce is also good. The restaurant has a classical Chinese décor and each station in the large open kitchen is staffed by chefs from Hong Kong.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8161;Chakrabongse Dining;Thailand;Bangkok;396/1 Maha Rat Road, Phra Borom Maha Ratchawang, Phra Nakhon, Bangkok, 10200, Thailand;13.7439558;100.4929369;24;false;false;Thai;A spectacular setting, where views of the Chao Phraya River and Wat Arun provide the perfect backdrop to your culinary journey inside one of Bangkok’s most precious historic houses. Well-known for its delicate and authentic royal Thai cuisine, the menu offers a different set selection every day. Impressive dishes include river prawns in spicy and sour coconut broth with banana blossom and Chakrabongse roasted duck red curry with mixed fruits.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8164;The Ranch;Thailand;Ko Samui;The Ritz-Carlton Koh Samui, 9/123 Mu 5, Bo Phut, Ko Samui, 84320, Thailand;9.5834827;100.0778936;19;true;false;Steakhouse;The Ranch at The Ritz-Carlton Koh Samui is the place for meat lovers and the only real steakhouse on the island. The premium Australian beef is dry-aged in-house and served on hot plates with a wide range of sauces and side dishes, without forgetting a knockout line-up of grilled dishes and seafood options. High ceilings, wooden furnishings and a splendid display of old and new world wines set the scene in the smart dining room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8166;Kaen;Thailand;Khon Kaen;140/64 Adunyaram Soi 7, Nai Mueang, Mueang Khon Kaen, Khon Kaen, 40000, Thailand;16.4639522;102.8257301;70;false;true;Thai contemporary;‘Kaen’ in Thai is a homonym with many meanings. Owner Chef Paisarn, who worked as executive chef at a 5-star resort, infuses those meanings into this restaurant in his hometown (Khon Kaen). The cuisine is contemporary Thai at its core (kaen), yet also playful, (kaen kaew), as in the recommended Massaman curry with lamb shank. Even the dining room reflects it — a large table with exposed heartwood (kaen mai) made at his family’s wood shop is a centrepiece.;Car park;[]
8167;Rabiang Patchanee;Thailand;Udon Thani;53/1 Bannon Road, Ban Lueam, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.4194777;102.7845975;42;false;false;Thai;Popular with local families, this restaurant focuses primarily on meat and freshwater fish, serving Chinese, Vietnamese, and Thai fare. They trade on authentic Thai flavours and daily specials featuring the freshest ingredients. The highlight dishes, which have been passed down for 30 years, are crispy duck topped with crab meat and gravy, and Vietnamese stuffed omelette. Make sure to book outdoor seats with a view of the pond.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8168;Baan Chik Pork Noodles;Thailand;Udon Thani;89/3-4 Naresoun Road, Mak Khaeng, Mueang Udon Thani, Udon Thani, 41000, Thailand;17.4023448;102.7851461;57;false;true;Noodles;This eatery has thrived in a traditional shophouse for over 30 years. Choose between the original flavour and tasty tom yum with its fresh lime and roasted peanut aroma, served with or without soup.;Cash only;[]
8169;Khanom Jeen Baan Bang Kan;Thailand;Phang-Nga;Mu 4, Mueang Phang-nga-Takua Pa Road, Thung Kha Ngok, Mueang Phang-nga, Phang-Nga, 82000, Thailand;8.5485366;98.4660963;84;true;true;Noodles;For over 20 years, locals have enjoyed this shop’s Khanom Jeen, or rice noodles, which are served with a choice of three curries and more than 20 types of fresh or pickled veggies. Noodles are unlimited, but save room for the refreshing cendol in coconut milk. Closed Thursday and Friday.;Cash only;[]
8170;Khanom Chin Pa Son;Thailand;Phang-Nga;3 Borirak Bamrung Road, Thai Chang, Mueang Phang-nga, Phang-Nga, 82000, Thailand;8.466571;98.5328638;96;true;true;Noodles;Across from a Chinese shrine, this self-service buffet has been drawing devotees for over 30 years with its tasty khanom chin and four curry options to mix and match. Pick from a wide range of condiments, fresh vegetables, boiled egg and crispy anchovies. Lunchtime is always busy, so arrive early.;Car park,Cash only;[]
8171;Jok's Kitchen (Pom Prap Sattru Phai);Thailand;Bangkok;23 Soi Charoen Krung 21, Phlapphla Chai Road, Pom Prap, Pom Prap Sattru Phai, Bangkok, 10100, Thailand;13.7458494;100.511482;48;true;true;Thai-Chinese;In the debate between quality and quantity, this Thai-Chinese spot hidden in a wet market sides with quality. Starting with a single table, it has since expanded to five. The skilled chef, whose family has sold crabs for over 80 years, sources quality ingredients to create an Omakase set menu which he cooks chef’s table-style. The shrimp wonton, deep-fried snow fish with soy sauce and stir-fried kale with salted halibut are recommended. Booking is mandatory.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
8172;Scarlett;Thailand;Bangkok;37F, Pullman Hotel G, 188 Silom Road, Suriyawong, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7259802;100.525907;16;false;false;French;Located on the top floor of the trendy Pullman Hotel, Scarlett offers a fashionable and lively spot to enjoy a creative cocktail and dine while the lights of Bangkok twinkle below. Alongside a list of classic French dishes, prime Australian steaks are broiled on the chargrill – the focal point of the lively open kitchen. Allow the knowledgeable staff to help you choose from the comprehensive list of reasonably priced wines. Desserts are a highlight so save room for something sweet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8173;Jadjan;Thailand;Phuket;4/27 Sakdidet Road, Talat Nuea, Mueang Phuket, Phuket, 83000, Thailand;7.86463;98.38045;75;false;true;Street Food;Chef Suthee, a former 5-star hotel chef, uses expertise to produce simple southern Thai fare that’s packed with flavour. The crab meat curry with betel leaves and southern Thai sour curry with fresh local fish and pineapple get our nod of approval.;Cash only;[]
8174;Tempura Kanda;Thailand;Bangkok;1F, Eight Thonglor Building  88/36, Sukhumvit 55 Road, Khlong Tan Nuea, Vadhana, Bangkok, 10110, Thailand;13.7307029;100.5820163;15;false;false;Tempura;This was one of the first omakase restaurants in the city, which means you’re placing your order in the hands of an experienced chef – in this case one with a mastery of tempura. Seasonal Japanese ingredients are imported, then carefully cooked. The batter is light and crispy, while the filling retains the produce’s natural flavours. The interior décor sticks to a simple approach, with a marble-topped counter adding some charm. Booking is essential.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8175;Somboon Seafood (Bang Rak);Thailand;Bangkok;169, 169/7-12 Surawong Road, Suriyawong, Bang Rak, Bangkok, 10500, Thailand;13.7283257;100.5266804;91;true;false;Thai-Chinese;Known for its fried crab curry, Somboon first put its name on the global culinary map in 1969. Fresh ingredients, impeccable cooking and reasonable prices keep it there. They now have 8 branches around town, but this is the best and the largest, seating up to 200 people. In addition to their famous crab curry, we recommend the deep-fried seabass with sweet fish sauce and Thai seafood spicy soup. Flawlessly fresh seafood and generous portions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8176;Thana Ocha;Thailand;Chiang Mai;29 Ratchawong Road, Chang Moi, Mueang Chiang Mai, Chiang Mai, 50300, Thailand;18.7910975;98.9983395;59;false;true;Noodles;Every day at lunch long lines form in front of this decades-old shop selling Hakka-style noodles. House-made Hakka stuffed tofu, fish sausage and crispy wontons find their way into every dish including tom yum noodles and the classic Yentafo. The latter is highly recommended, with a well-seasoned soup made from fermented bean curd and fresh chilli.;Cash only;[]
8177;5 SEN:SES by Mario Aliberti;Germany;Karlsruhe;Blumenstraße 19, Karlsruhe, 76133, Germany;49.0082085;8.3967232;84;false;false;International, Italian;A fine addition to Karlsruhe's culinary scene. Chef-patron Mario Aliberti fuses Italian cuisine with international – especially Asian – and regional influences. A wide range of dishes is available: Lunchtime features four different moderately priced set menus (individual courses can also be ordered separately), along with additional à la carte options. In the evening, the array of options includes the "Fine Dining Menu", the "Italian Menu" and the "Menü Sharing", as well as an extensive à la carte selection. You can also order whole fish and different cuts of meat. There really is something for everyone's taste! The well-stocked wine list is worth a look, too. The interior is modern and inviting, with a distinct lounge feel. In summer, head for the quiet terrace laid out right in front of the restaurant.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8178;GLORIE;Germany;Hamburg;Brandshofer Deich 68, Hamburg, 20539, Germany;53.5374345;10.0285679;39;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Contemporary;Almost a restaurant within a restaurant. On a mezzanine with a limited number of tables and a bird's-eye view of the open kitchen – practically directly above 100/200 Kitchen – owner Thomas Alfons Imbusch presents his second culinary concept: "Old school, reimagined". From the à la carte menu, diners order dishes that are deeply rooted in regional cuisine, made from select ingredients and prepared with sustainability in mind. The reinterpreted classics include, for example, beef pâté en croûte, sauce gribiche and pickled vegetables, or lobster Thermidor. The interior design is upscale and minimalist, with distinctive features like a striking long wooden table divided by a steel girder, as well as decorative objects, artwork and a piano. The service team, who combine attentiveness with a laid-back yet professional approach, is made up of the same staff who work at 100/200 Kitchen.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
8179;Koer;Germany;Hamburg;Maria-Louisen-Straße 3, Hamburg, 22301, Germany;53.5839548;9.9960681;20;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;A brilliant combination of restaurant and bar! Their "modern, market-fresh cuisine" is served in the form of creative dishes, such as smoked sardine and razor clams from the Dutch coast with grilled peppers, capers and pickled coriander seeds. We recommend opting for the surprise menu, but there is also an à la carte selection that includes bar snacks – it is well worth trying their own creations from the cocktail list. Good to know: Alcohol-free beverage pairings are available for the set menu. A pleasantly lively and fun atmosphere reigns in this chic restaurant. The name is derived from the Low German phrase in de Köör gahn ("to make a choice") and refers to the establishment's dual concept.;;[]
8180;buffet Kull bar;Germany;Munich;Marienstraße 4, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1365613;11.5807487;78;true;true;International, Steakhouse;A word to the wise: Book ahead to avoid disappointment at this trendy restaurant in the centre of Munich! The "French bistro meets New York steakhouse" concept is a hit. The atmosphere is lively, the tables are close together, and the service is both lively and attentive. But above all, it's the cuisine that impresses: Here, the focus is clearly on taste and ingredients – no visual frills needed. The cooking is precise and unpretentious. Mouth-watering options include the NY-style fillet steak with maître d'hôtel butter. For dessert, why not try the tarte Tatin served with vanilla ice cream and crème fraîche?;;[]
8181;Ehemalige Sparkasse;Germany;Dinkelsbühl;Schrannengasse 1, Dinkelsbühl, 91550, Germany;49.0700425;10.3185852;69;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This is the second restaurant run by Florian Kellerbauer in the historical centre of Dinkelsbühl. Housed in a former bank, a short walk from his Altdeutsches Restaurant, the chef-patron has created a dining experience centred on "Heimat" cuisine. Fresh, locally sourced ingredients take pride of place in the seasonally inspired dishes. À la carte options include Franconian beef Zwiebelrostbraten with potato noodles and green salad, and pike-perch fillet, tomato jus, root vegetables and pesto ravioli. The wine list features labels from Franconia, elsewhere in Germany and beyond. In addition to the restaurant, there are also well-appointed guestrooms plus a sauna and workout space.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8183;Silberstreif;Germany;Südharz;Schindelbruch 1, Südharz, 06536, Germany;51.5895097;11.0003542;46;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The Naturresort & Spa Schindelbruch features an ambitious restaurant concept called Silberstreif ("Silver Lining"), named after the 2022 butterfly of the year. Head chef Eric Jadischke and the young team rustle up contemporary cuisine inspired by the Harz region and its seasons. Some of the ingredients come from the garden that was planted with the restaurant's needs in mind. There is a six-, seven- or eight-course set menu, with corresponding wine or non-alcoholic pairings on request. Service is friendly and attentive. You might be interested to know that the dishes are served on Ritter von Kempski collection porcelain, designed by MEISSEN exclusively for this restaurant. The chic, modern ambience is lovely and the impressive pieces by artist Johann Elias Ridinger draw the eye with their hunting and forest motifs – a nod to the restaurant's close connection with nature. The hotel has tasteful guestrooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8184;Yabase;Germany;Düsseldorf;Klosterstraße 70, Düsseldorf, 40211, Germany;51.2248029;6.7887028;43;true;false;Japanese, Asian;Calling all Japanese food aficionados! For an authentic experience, head to this restaurant in the centre of Düsseldorf's Japanese quarter. Behind a rather unassuming exterior an upscale minimalist-style space awaits. The service is friendly and professional. In the kitchen, top-notch fresh ingredients meet expert preparation techniques. The sushi and sashimi offer exceptional value, but more adventurous diners should try the unaju (rice bowl with barbecued eel) or the barbecued tuna head with vinegar for a real explosion of flavour. Complement your meal with some warm sake or Japanese beer. It is rare to get a table on the spur of the moment, so make sure you book in the evening. With a bit of luck, you can dine directly at the counter with its fish display case and watch the chefs at work. Lunch reservations are not possible – diners often queue at the entrance even before opening time.;;[]
8185;THE SCHELLY;United Kingdom;Ambleside;Church Street, Ambleside, LA22 OBU, United Kingdom;54.430997;-2.9623619;71;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A delightful operation from the team behind Old Stamp House just a minute’s walk away, this deservedly busy restaurant is named after a local fish found in only four nearby lakes. It’s indicative of the distinctly Lakeland feel to the menu, which is epitomised by the presence of lip-smacking Herdwick hogget shoulder, plus a dish of ‘mushrooms found around the woods in Ambleside’. Sit at the counter to see the chefs or by the window to people-watch the tourists passing by. The sticky toffee madeleines cooked to order ensure you’ll leave on a sugary high.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8186;Mingary Castle;United Kingdom;Kilchoan;Kilchoan, PH36 4LH, United Kingdom;56.6930767;-6.0802764;57;false;false;Modern British;Situated close to mainland Britain’s most westerly point, the Ardnamurchan peninsula, Mingary Castle is the result of years of restoration work on the original 13th-century building that had been in ruins for over 100 years. Located down miles of single-track roads, it’s a remote yet utterly spectacular location. Today, a hotel and restaurant sit inside the one-time castle, with the latter serving a set menu of robust, hearty and traditionally based cooking, utilising local produce like venison from their own estate.;Car park;[]
8187;Ambassadors Clubhouse;United Kingdom;London;25 Heddon Street, Mayfair, London, W1B 4BH, United Kingdom;51.5112097;-0.1398296;19;true;true;Indian;There’s opulence to spare at this lavishly furnished, no-expense-spared restaurant from the team behind Gymkhana. Soft lighting, wood panelling and colourful décor all add to the atmosphere, which takes its cues from the ‘party mansions’ of the former undivided Punjab. Northern India and Pakistan inspire the menu, which provides a showcase for the chefs’ quality produce and abundant technical skill – both of which are evident in the superb mooli methi bream cooked on the sigri stove. Downstairs, in Ambassy, guest DJs curate a late-night rotation of Punjabi and British dance music.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8188;Matsukawa;Ireland;Dublin City;8 Queen St, Dublin City, DO7 Y683, Ireland;53.3472708;-6.2799745;57;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;With only eight seats around its counter, don’t be put off if you can’t secure a reservation at this sweetly run sushi restaurant at the first time of asking. The omakase menu is based around fine seafood produce, some of it Irish, with multiple servings of nigiri forming a large chunk of the experience – the hamachi and the salmon are particular highlights. The team are endearing and the service is not drawn-out, allowing you to enjoy a satisfying meal that doesn’t take all night. A good selection of sake and other Japanese spirits completes the offering.;Air conditioning;[]
8190;Rare;Ireland;Kinsale;3 Pearse Street, Kinsale, P17 NA72, Ireland;51.7061679;-8.5226004;85;true;false;Indian, Modern Cuisine;Take your seat in this understated, rustic-chic dining room and watch the team at work through the kitchen’s floor-to-ceiling windows. The chef is from Chennai and it is the south Indian region of Tamil Nadu which most influences the cooking, resulting in dishes that make abundant use of chilli, coconut and sweeter elements such as tamarind and date – all underpinned by the abundant West Cork larder. Service is professional and engaging, with the chefs bringing dishes to the table themselves to make for a more personal experience.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8192;Vetch;United Kingdom;Liverpool;29a Hope Street, Liverpool, L1 9BP, United Kingdom;53.4007625;-2.9705859;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located on Hope Street alongside numerous other eateries, there’s a homely feel to this personably and knowledgably run restaurant. The décor is all about understatement, with minimalist furnishings and neutral tones. The modern, well-versed cooking successfully incorporates a range of East Asian influences including shokupan milk bread, Korean chicken wings and char siu pork belly. At dinner, it’s a tasting menu affair which shows the full breadth of the cooking, but keep an eye out for the great value offering at lunch and early evening.;;[]
8193;Sael;United Kingdom;London;1 St James's Market, St. James's, London, SW1Y 4QQ, United Kingdom;51.508868;-0.1332536;41;true;true;Traditional British;Britain, its seasons and its produce are the inspiration behind this Jason Atherton venture that comes with elegant brasserie décor and an overtly seasonal menu of comforting dishes you really want to eat. Kick off with the Marmite custard tart and keep things retro for dessert with jam roly poly or bread and butter pudding. The well-constructed wine list has real depth and quality, while coming with the eye-catching quirk of letting you order by the pint. Head upstairs to the Apples & Pears bar if you want to make it a late one.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8194;Ardfern;United Kingdom;Leith;10-12 Bonnington Road, Leith, EH6 5JD, United Kingdom;55.9727268;-3.1758276;18;false;false;International;Next-door neighbour and sister restaurant to The Little Chartroom, Ardfern is named after a village in Argyll & Bute that brings back fond memories for owner Roberta Hall-McCarron. Describing itself as a café, bar and bottle shop, it has an appealing brunch menu, a relaxed air and a wine list that will delight enthusiasts. You’d be a fool to miss the evening’s small plates, however, which pack in plenty of flavour and have both a heartiness and a pleasing familiarity to them. The hash browns with whipped feta and jalapeño ketchup are a particular treat.;Brunch,Interesting wine list;[]
8195;Nanyang Blossom;United Kingdom;London;12 Knightsbridge Green, Knightsbridge, London, SW1X 7QL, United Kingdom;51.5013484;-0.1624709;52;false;true;South East Asian;The Nanyang region encompasses parts of both China and Southeast Asia, so you can expect influences from a variety of countries at this understatedly chic restaurant hidden down a narrow passageway. The array of menus includes a tasting option, an extensive à la carte and set sharing options for more indecisive diners. The dishes show care, craft and vibrancy across the board – but it’s the signature Knightsbridge crispy beef ribs that steal the show. The endearing service adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
8196;Landline;Ireland;Kenmare;Shelbourne Street, Kenmare, V93 X3XY, Ireland;51.8782798;-9.5807928;80;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated within the grand Park Hotel, overlooking Kenmare Bay, this elegant dining room comes with the added bonus of being decorated with original paintings by Irish artist Sean Scully – the restaurant is even named after one of his works. The kitchen showcases a bounty of prime Irish produce, embellishing it with precise, well-judged accompaniments – a lovely mussel and dulse sauce with halibut is a prime example. Oenophiles will appreciate the strong choice of classic vintages.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8198;Bistrot at Wild Honey;United Kingdom;London;8 Pall Mall, St James’s, London, SW1Y 5NG, United Kingdom;51.5074689;-0.1322075;38;false;false;Modern British;Occupying the ground floor of a Grade II listed former banking hall inside the Sofitel hotel, this restaurant aims to provide a more relaxed and keenly priced alternative to the adjoining Wild Honey St James. The team are undoubtedly succeeding in their mission, with lashings of flavour packed into every deceptively simple dish. Sit at the counter or in one of the dramatically red banquettes, which add to the French bistro feel. The menu incorporates a fair few Mediterranean influences alongside the Gallic staples, and the ‘prix fixe’ is an absolute steal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8199;Cornus;United Kingdom;London;27c Eccleston Place, Belgravia, London, SW1W 9NF, United Kingdom;51.4942405;-0.1477227;17;true;false;Modern British, Seafood;There’s a wonderful fusion of setting and cooking at Cornus. A sister to long-standing Chelsea restaurant Medlar, it’s a refined, simply decorated restaurant with linen-laid tables and understated quality. The same goes for the dishes, which are based around superb produce, much of it seafood from the south-west coast. The likes of sweet Devon crab and beautiful Newlyn cod are made all the more delicious by the kitchen’s restrained approach and consummate technical skill. The chefs know they’re using brilliant ingredients, so never overcomplicate matters.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8200;Saga;United Kingdom;Belfast;43 Malone Road, Belfast, BT9 6RX, United Kingdom;54.5801769;-5.9390885;28;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant formerly known as Blank has been reinvented as this ‘Kitchen and Cellar’ showcasing the best of Irish produce and a wine list with good breadth. Gone is the surprise tasting menu of the Blank days and in its place is a concise à la carte that shines in its quality execution of classic dishes – like a fantastic version of Portavogie scallops with black pudding and apple. Sit in the rear to soak up the buzz of the kitchen, or ask for one of the semi-private booths in the front. Come on Sundays for a roast, or Thursdays for the Chateaubriand to share.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8201;YiQi;United Kingdom;London;14 Lisle Street, Chinatown, London, WC2H 7BE, United Kingdom;51.5115279;-0.1307474;100;true;true;Asian;Thailand, Malaysia and Singapore are the three countries that feature most prominently at this relative newcomer to Chinatown, which opened in 2024. Spread over two floors, it’s run by an eager and professional team who provide attentive service and offer helpful advice when you’re leafing through the extensive menu. The highlights of that menu include moreish salt and pepper squid, flavoursome whole grilled silver pomfret, street food style morning glory and succulent charcoal chicken wings – they’re all generous in size, so come with family or friends and share.;Air conditioning;[]
8202;Yamas;United Kingdom;Looe;The Quay, Looe, PL13 1AH, United Kingdom;50.3529796;-4.4544414;46;false;false;Greek;Yamas is a Greek toast to the health and wellbeing of friends and family, and it’s the authentic flavours of Greece that power this sister restaurant to the Sardine Factory on the other side of the East Looe River. Grab a seat on the terrace to make the most of the quayside location or have a drink in the first-floor bar, before delighting in classic dishes from stifado to souvlaki. The interesting all-Greek wine list offers a good selection by the glass and all at a fair price. Yamas!;Terrace;[]
8203;Mambow;United Kingdom;London;78 Lower Clapton Road, Clapton, London, E5 0RN, United Kingdom;51.5528237;-0.0527759;81;true;false;Malaysian;‘Malaysian Heat + Juicy Wines’ is the strapline of Vanessa Fernandes and Abby Lee’s restaurant – that means exhilarating dishes inspired by Abby's family recipes, alongside natural wines. Start with the terrific '100+ Sour' cocktail and then order plenty of the delicious food to share. While the menu changes frequently, expect eminently satisfying dishes like Otak-Otak prawn toast or squid stuffed with pork belly mince – and don’t ignore the Kerabu section. There's a great atmosphere around the room and there are also a few seats on a semi-covered terrace at the back.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8204;Sotto;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;28-32 Deanhaugh Street, Edinburgh, EH4 1LY, United Kingdom;55.9582182;-3.2095168;25;false;false;Italian;This buzzy wine bar and trattoria is set in the heart of bustling Stockbridge, where you can pop in just for a glass of wine with some olives and salumi around the communal, marble-topped island counter – or choose from the full à la carte of appealingly unfussy Italian dishes. Whether you opt for one of the pastas or the fish of the day, it’s all simple, fresh and wholly enjoyable. The top-notch wine list is almost exclusively Italian, with owner and sommelier James on hand to recommend something to suit.;Interesting wine list;[]
8205;GaGa;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;566 Dumbarton Road, Partick, Glasgow City, G11 6RH, United Kingdom;55.8707528;-4.3153376;81;false;true;Malaysian;After closing Julie's Kopitiam on the south side of the city, Chef Julie Swee Lin relocated over to these larger premises in the suburb of Partick. One side is a former butcher’s shop with the original glazed tiles on the walls, whilst the other is more rustic with colourful pot plants dotted around. Grab one of the booths if you can and start with a cocktail, then dive right into the menu of vibrantly flavoured, Malaysian-inspired dishes – the fried chicken with Sichuan hot sauce and orange zest is a highlight. Lively, delicious and great value, this has all the ingredients for a fun night out.;Wheelchair access;[]
8206;Guildhall Tavern;United Kingdom;Poole;15 Market Street, Poole, BH15 1NB, United Kingdom;50.7141301;-1.9878174;49;true;false;Seafood;While its name and exterior might give the impression that this is a pub, once inside the smart interior you’ll quickly get a different idea. There’s a subtle, refined nautical theme to the décor, including in the teak-furnished Yacht Lounge upstairs that’s ideal for an aperitif. Situated so close to the quayside, seafood understandably plays a key role on the menu and the cooking of it is a real strength of the kitchen – be it sweet scallops or crispy cod. The wine list includes local producers whose wines pair well with the food.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8207;O Secadeiro;Spain;Serra de Outes;Lugar de Banzas 18, Serra de Outes, 15237, Spain;42.8876277;-8.8968902;89;true;false;Farm to table;Once in a while you come across a truly pleasant surprise in a rural setting run by chefs who have returned to their roots with the sole aim of showcasing what they have learnt elsewhere. This is definitely the case with couple Fernando and Eva, two cooks (although she is also in charge of the dining room service) who have restored her grandmother’s house and created their own vegetable garden (which also includes a greenhouse). Their contemporary cuisine has plenty of personality and is centred around a single seasonal vegetarian menu. We loved the roasted aubergines with miso!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8208;Arrocería Pinedo Beach;Spain;Pinedo;Carrera del Riu 426, Pinedo, 46012, Spain;39.4245353;-0.3412383;25;true;false;Rice Dishes, Regional Cuisine;If you’re planning a relaxing day out with a swim, this restaurant located between Valencia and the Parque Natural de La Albufera could be the perfect option for you. Part of the renowned Arrocería Maribel (El Palmar) restaurant group, it has the added bonus of a lounge and pool area where you can relax while enjoying a post-meal swim and drink. The traditional Valencian cuisine on offer features an impressive array of rice dishes (most of its paellas and creamy rice options need to be selected when you make your booking). The perfect setting for a family get-together!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8209;Árido by Ramsés González;Spain;Tudela;Rúa 27, Tudela, 31500, Spain;42.0641279;-1.6065421;46;false;true;Contemporary;This gastronomic restaurant, part of the Santa Ana boutique hotel in Tudela, is the latest venture of award-winning chef Ramsés González. This small, unique eatery, occupying a medieval wine cellar, is striking for the rustic feel of its stone architecture. It only has four tables, and its cuisine follows to a certain extent the successful cuisine offered at González’s Cancook restaurant in Zaragoza. Here, the dishes on offer also bear his signature and are brought to the fore by resident chef Mateo Sierra, who is something of a celebrity in his own right, having reached the final of MasterChef. The single tasting menu champions locally sourced, seasonal ingredients in dishes such as the Menestra from the Ribera del Ebro, the delicious baked onion, plus an unusual smoked “chuleta” that is in fact a pepper stuffed with delicate shavings of ham. On the first floor, which provides access to a roof terrace with views of the town, you’ll find a more informal tapas space called Rambar.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8210;Tragatá Málaga;Spain;Malaga;Alameda Principal 3, Malaga, 29001, Spain;36.7177928;-4.4214488;33;false;true;Contemporary;Located in the heart of the city, Tragatá boasts a modern setting with high tables and chairs and heralds the arrival in the city of famous chef Benito Gómez, who has brought his more casual and informal concept to Málaga from Ronda. Here, you can savour dishes such as his award-winning Russian salad, the popular squid sandwich, and the delicious grilled bone marrow with beef tartare. Since its arrival on the scene, it has been very well received by its new local clientele!;Air conditioning;[]
8211;Imprevisto;Spain;Barcelona;Bailèn 104, Barcelona, 08009, Spain;41.3970272;2.1706687;96;true;false;Contemporary;The four young owners of this unpretentious restaurant, two of whom work in the kitchen and two in in the dining room, were keen that the name of their business was not something banal or vacuous, but rather a name that expressed their philosophy and offered the promise of a relaxed dining experience based around continual new discoveries. The end result is a contemporary style of cooking that is high on detail and focuses on seasonal ingredients, as witnessed by the short à la carte (weekday lunches) and two tasting menus (7 and 10 courses, respectively). The beef tartare with horseradish, blackberries, pickled mustard seeds and demi-glace is teeming with nuanced flavours and textures.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8212;Cova Sacra;Spain;Covadonga;Real Sitio de Covadonga, Covadonga, 33589, Spain;43.308464;-5.0542352;68;true;false;Asturian, Contemporary;If you’re looking for a good restaurant around Covadonga, this option in the Gran Hotel Pelayo won’t disappoint as the cooking comes courtesy of renowned chef Jaime Uz. The à la carte, with its strong roots in Asturian cuisine, is impressively supported by an extensive tasting menu called “La Santina”. The dining room enjoys relaxing views of its spectacular natural surroundings as well as the basilica.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
8213;Los Caños;Spain;Haro;Plaza de San Martín 5, Haro, 26200, Spain;42.57789;-2.84626;52;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;If you find yourself on a tapas and “pinchos” crawl in the La Herradura section of historic Haro, we can highly recommend a refuelling stop at Los Caños, occupying a delightful 16C palatial-style property. In this attractive restaurant, which has tastefully combined historic details with a more contemporary aesthetic, the emphasis is on deep-rooted traditional cuisine that has been able to take classic tapas to a higher gastronomic level, as showcased in options such as the pork sandwich with Morbier cheese, Iberian dewlap and cured egg yolk.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8214;Mambo;Spain;Palma;Paseo de Mallorca 3, Palma, 07011, Spain;39.5725343;2.6414237;37;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This highly original eatery, with its attractive and informal bistro-style ambience, is the fiefdom of Brazilian-born chef Gabriel Conti. He arrived in Palma having spent many years working in Barcelona, which enabled him to acquire a rucksack full of different culinary experiences and expertise, which he now highlights, in particular, in dishes prepared on the grill. If you decide to eat at one of the four seats at the bar counter, the chef will be happy to share the secrets of his dishes with you step by step.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8215;Bistronómika;Spain;Madrid;Ibiza 44, Madrid, 28009, Spain;40.4180215;-3.6733221;40;false;false;Seafood;Part of the Bulbiza (Bulevar de Ibiza) gastronomic project, Bistronómika offers a traditional “No Carta” menu featuring touches of contemporary detail. The specialities here are the top-quality fish and seafood (the catch is displayed here every day to whet our appetite) cooked with minimum intervention, mainly on the open grill. Make sure you try the Gilda kebab-style appetiser, prepared with red tuna from the Mediterranean.;Air conditioning;[]
8216;Can Jepet;Spain;Setcases;Molló 11, Setcases, 17869, Spain;42.3757707;2.3023613;87;false;true;Catalan;A restaurant with a rustic atmosphere in a picturesque mountain village. Named after the family that owns the property, it is a good place to discover the traditional cuisine of the Catalan mountains with its emphasis on grilled meats, game dishes, sausages etc.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8217;La Vaquería;Spain;El Campello;Carretera Benimagrell 52, El Campello, 03560, Spain;38.3900536;-0.4172344;97;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Grills;A brasserie-restaurant with a friendly, informal feel and pleasant terrace. Here, the house speciality, gently influenced by Basque cuisine, are the grilled meats and T-bone steak, although plenty of other options are available, including tapas, flatbreads, seasonal vegetables and excellent fish dishes (make sure you ask about the fresh fish of the day). The à la carte is complemented by a tasting menu for a minimum of two people sharing.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8218;Celler d'en Joan Pàmies;Spain;Riudoms;Masferrer 9, Riudoms, 43330, Spain;41.1366374;1.0511287;34;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Occupying a large 18C house, where the use of locally sourced products is key, as is the maxim of “not rejecting the cooking of bygone days, but adding to it with imagination and vitality”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8219;Augusto;Spain;San Vicente de la Barquera;Mercado 1, San Vicente de la Barquera, 39540, Spain;43.3832136;-4.3996808;37;true;false;Seafood;This longstanding family-run restaurant, located just in front of the local market, boasts a striking nautical decor that provides the backdrop for traditional cuisine that, in perfect harmony with the area’s maritime heritage, champions the highest-quality fish and seafood (priced by weight). This includes seafood stews (“mariscadas”) for sharing and excellent rice options. We can also highly recommend the fried squid (“rabas de calamar”), the legendary “arroz con bogavante” (rice with lobster), a dish for which the family were pioneers, and when it comes to dessert, the delicious cream millefeuille.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8220;Modesto;Spain;Ferrol;Carretera Ferrol-Cobas 89, Ferrol, 15405, Spain;43.499813;-8.24138;30;true;true;Seafood;A restaurant with a classic - contemporary ambience located along the main road. Traditional cuisine that showcases local products, including an outstanding selection of seafood dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8221;Haku;Spain;Valencia;Gran Vía del Marqués del Turia 62, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.46762;-0.36699;96;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;If you enjoy fusion cuisine, this Japanese restaurant is a must as it takes its relationship with the Mediterranean one step further thanks to the unique blend of Japanese-Italian cooking that comes courtesy of young chef Bo Jimmy Zhu, who hails from the town of Asti in Italy’s Piedmont region. His dishes are based around the Omakase philosophy which only works with the very best market-inspired ingredients. These are served at the bar (there is also a private space with a more exclusive ambience) and are centred around three enticing menus: Taibo, Bohan and Honbo. The superb nigiris here are prepared with a 50:50 mix of traditional vinegar and Modena balsamic vinegar.;;[]
8222;A Mar;Spain;Jerez de la Frontera;Latorre 8, Jerez de la Frontera, 11403, Spain;36.6823321;-6.1385788;46;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located along one of the narrow pedestrianised streets in the town’s old quarter, A Mar features two different ambiences with no little personality where the sea is viewed as the restaurant’s huge and bountiful larder. On its extensive, traditionally inspired à la carte, you’ll find a good selection of fish from the display cabinet, premium grilled meats from different breeds (Retinta, Rubia Gallega, Pinta Cántabra etc), plus an impressive array of rice options. Half portions are available for the majority of dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8223;Reccapolis;Spain;Ripoll;Carretera Sant Joan 68, Ripoll, 17500, Spain;42.2088193;2.1998109;50;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a loyal following that features three welcoming and colourful dining rooms with a classic-modern feel, plus an attractive balcony-terrace boasting views of the river. Its updated take on traditional cuisine champions seasonal and locally sourced ingredients in popular dishes such as veal from the Ripollès region, leg of baby goat cooked at low temperature, and fish of the day options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8224;La Ultramar;Spain;Pontevedra;Padre Amoedo Carballo 3, Pontevedra, 36002, Spain;42.4333237;-8.6418722;22;true;false;Fusion;In the historic Sarmiento building, which is part of the Pontevedra museum, you can savour the creative yet more casual and affordable side of chef Xosé Torres Cannas’ cuisine, who is already riding a wave of success at his award-winning Michelin two-star Pepe Vieria restaurant in Raxó. In this restaurant, which boasts a terrace space, bar and semi-open kitchen visible from the spectacular dining room, his philosophy is encapsulated by a single quote inspired by Bruce Lee – “Be kitchen, my friend”, which is also part of the restaurant’s logo. The à la carte is a fun array of dishes combining strong technique and ingredients from Galicia and elsewhere, such as the crispy Galician veal empanadillas, pork and chicken gyozas, tacos etc.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8225;La Llorería;Spain;Madrid;San Lorenzo 4, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4252751;-3.6995575;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that exudes a sense of freedom, excitement and youthful exuberance in equal measure – qualities which combine perfectly with consistency, technique and a passion for hard work. The setting, which takes on the appearance of a bar with just a few tables and has a counter set up for dining, is relatively simple, but this is compensated in spades by contemporary cuisine featuring flavours and textures that are always interesting. Choose between an à la carte particularly designed for sharing, with the option of “raciones” and half plates.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8226;Santa Mariana;Spain;Alaior;Camí de Loreto s/n, Alaior, 07730, Spain;39.9241793;4.1685821;35;true;false;Creative;This restaurant occupies a Menorcan-style country house with plenty of typical charm (including a delightful terrace) that has been converted into a small rural hotel. The cuisine here is based around an à la carte (we loved the pickled “oliaigua” of oxidised tomatoes and sirviola) and two set menus (“Origins” and “Origin, your gaze and mine”) that focus on fun, creative dishes that constantly combine technique and locally sourced ingredients and are enhanced by Mediterranean, French, Asian and Latin American touches. The estate also has its own organic kitchen garden, olive trees, chickens and sheep.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8227;1742;Spain;Eivissa;Major 3, Eivissa, 07800, Spain;38.906983;1.4356286;51;true;true;Creative;If you’re looking for authenticity and exclusivity, the highly chic ambience in this old aristocratic property will provide you with the requisite luxury and VIP service. The experience here, overseen by Dutch chef Edwin Vinke, is centred around a modern tasting menu that champions the island’s native ingredients (organic vegetables, baby goat, red prawns etc) and involves a gastronomic journey that begins in the Es Pratet car park (where vehicles are waiting to transport you to the restricted upper section of the Dalt Vila). A butler welcomes you with a glass of champagne, then escorts you on a short tour of the property (water cisterns, wine cellar and a photocall), before heading into the kitchen to meet the chef, to the panoramic roof terrace for snacks, and finally the main dining room, with its backdrop of lighting effects on the walls, where one surprise follows another (including a live soprano singer). Head back up to the roof terrace for dessert or a post-dinner drink.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
8228;Rural;Spain;Madrid;Marqués de Cubas 8, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.417102;-3.6955708;84;true;true;Meats and Grills;Are you familiar yet with Rafa Zafra’s new venture? The renowned chef in charge of Estimar, with restaurants in both Barcelona and Madrid (the latter just a few metres away from Rural), has teamed up with chef Alberto Pacheco to leave the sea (the leitmotif of his other businesses) behind him in order to focus on the land. In the dining rooms, with their subdued lighting and urban-style interior design, the cooking is focused on a choice of different meats (beef, ox, pork, lamb, poultry, game). This is showcased via premium Joselito cured hams, escabeches, sausages, delicious barbecued pinchos and specialities cooked on the Josper grill, the Basque parrilla, or in the traditional Castilian oven. An impressive and varied wine cellar completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8229;Casa Silvano-Maracaibo;Spain;Segovia;Paseo de Ezequiel González 25, Segovia, 40002, Spain;40.9451959;-4.1218281;67;true;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;Attractive gastronomy which has distanced itself from roast dishes, in well - kept, classical surroundings. Regional flavours and up - to - date dishes make up an extensive and well - balanced menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
8230;Candlelight;Spain;S'Agaró;Plaza de la Rosaleda, S'Agaró, 17248, Spain;41.7908102;3.0556861;22;false;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;This elegant restaurant, located inside the La Gavina hotel, is the best gastronomic option in S'Agaró, one of the Costa Brava’s most coveted destinations. It is overseen by famous French chef Romain Fornell, hence the high levels of technique in evidence in contemporary cuisine that is closely connected to the classic cuisine of his homeland. For a truly memorable and romantic experience, make sure you book a table on the Mediterranean-inspired terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
8231;Las Redes;Spain;San Vicente de la Barquera;Avenida de los Soportales 24, San Vicente de la Barquera, 39540, Spain;43.3852851;-4.3983856;18;true;true;Seafood;A family-run restaurant well situated along the main street running through this small town, where the focus is on sourcing the freshest possible ingredients from the local auction. Traditional à la carte featuring fish, seafood and a few savoury rice dishes. Pleasant terrace.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8233;O Camiño do Inglés;Spain;Ferrol;Espartero 77-79, Ferrol, 15401, Spain;43.4794991;-8.2448745;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This attractive restaurant with an open kitchen close to the port takes its name from the nickname by which everyone knows owner Daniel López, who is referred to as “El Inglés”! The contemporary-style à la carte, with its roots in Galician cuisine but with interesting nods to other countries (Peru, Japan, Italy etc), is complemented by three set menus (Magdalena, Medio Camino and Do Patrón). Half-plates are also available (announced at your table) so that you can try lots of different dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8234;L'Atelier Dagà Clos;Spain;Llagostera;Panedes 31, Llagostera, 17240, Spain;41.828724;2.896069;35;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A contemporary, enthusiastically run family restaurant offering honest and well-prepared traditional cuisine featuring impressive portions and unpretentious time-honoured flavours. Guests can choose between dishes on the concise à la carte or a single tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8235;Asador Lechazo Aranda;Spain;Santander;Tetuán 15, Santander, 39004, Spain;43.4656061;-3.7954727;33;true;true;Meats and Grills;This restaurant boasts an attractive Castilian decor and a menu featuring traditional cuisine, including the occasional seafood dish, top-quality meat and delicious roasts cooked in a wood-fired oven. Roast lamb is the house speciality.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8236;Sábrego;Spain;San Andrés de Camporredondo;O Cotiño, San Andrés de Camporredondo, 32415, Spain;42.3214323;-8.1085261;21;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This stone-built bodega complex is located in a panoramic setting surrounded by vineyards in the heart of the D.O. Ribeiro wine region. Its updated take on traditional cooking highlights a creative touch and is centred on the very best Galician meat and the freshest fish sourced daily. Half a dozen attractive guestrooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8237;Asiakō;Spain;Madrid;Marqués de Riscal 5, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4306194;-3.6916946;60;true;true;Fusion;A small, original restaurant where the Basque-Asian fusion dishes on the menu come as a pleasant surprise and the focus is on Japan in particular. The culinary threads here are the parrilla grill and the top-quality ingredients that are always in evidence. Choose between the à la carte, featuring dishes such as the trilogy of beef (“lomo bajo”, “lomo alto” and rib tartare) and the “pantxineta” mochi, alongside two tasting menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8238;Bell-Lloc;Spain;Santa Cristina d'Aro;Carretera Sant Feliu a Girona, Santa Cristina d'Aro, 17246, Spain;41.8228675;2.9795245;91;false;true;Catalan;Bell-Lloc occupies an old farmhouse with a marked rustic ambience, the origins of which date back to the 17C. Traditional Catalan cooking that is simple yet delicious, including dishes cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8239;El Muro;Spain;Vejer de la Frontera;Paseo de las Cobijadas 1, Vejer de la Frontera, 11150, Spain;36.2522401;-5.9639505;43;true;false;Contemporary, Andalusian;A unique restaurant that takes its name from the nearby walls of Vejer, a delightful “pueblo blanco” that was designated a national “Artistic and Historic Site” in 1976. Having spent time working in leading restaurants elsewhere, local chef Paco Doncel has returned to his roots to embark on his own project in this regionally inspired and casual setting. His cooking centres on contemporary cuisine influenced by local dishes such as his signature cannelloni (the filling depends on seasonal ingredients) and croquettes “de mi madre”, followed by cheesecake with ice-cream.;Air conditioning;[]
8240;Cal Pere del Maset;Spain;Sant Pau d'Ordal;Ponent 20, Sant Pau d'Ordal, 08739, Spain;41.38282;1.795256;41;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant established over half a century ago where you can enjoy cooking with a traditional flavour, including renowned dishes such as baked cannelloni and pigs’ trotters with plums.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8241;Echaurren Tradición;Spain;Ezcaray;Padre José García 19, Ezcaray, 26280, Spain;42.325741;-3.0144575;79;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;With its enhanced space and light this restaurant remains loyal to traditional cuisine, complementing its à la carte (featuring classic dishes from Francis Paniego and his mother) with a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8242;El Remedio;Spain;Ruiloba;Barrio de Liandres, Ruiloba, 39527, Spain;43.391873;-4.2619086;98;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;Surrounded by green spaces, El Remedio enjoys an almost picture - postcard location next to a 19C church and just a few metres from the cliff. The traditionally based cuisine is prepared with high - quality ingredients to create refined dishes full of elegant textures.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8243;Kamín;Spain;Leon;Regidores 4, Leon, 24003, Spain;42.5978761;-5.569504;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This modern restaurant, the name of which is a reference to the chef’s mother (Camino), is located in the heart of the Barrio Húmedo district and features an open-view kitchen. Its bold, contemporary cuisine teeming with strong flavours (they particularly like working with pickles and fermentations) is showcased on two tasting menus, one called Origen (Wednesday to Friday lunchtimes only) and another more extensive option entitled Kamín, both of which feature seasonal, market-inspired ingredients. If you enjoyed their desserts, why not head to La Postrería Kamín, dedicated to sweet treats, which they run in Calle Ancha!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8244;Landua;Spain;Mazaricos;Lugar O Fieiro, Mazaricos, 15258, Spain;42.9071228;-9.1032774;89;true;true;Contemporary;Occupying an old stone house in the heart of the countryside, Landua is run with great enthusiasm by a young couple. In the kitchen, visible as soon as you enter, the entire focus is on a single surprise menu explained at your table by the chef and based around locally sourced ingredients.;Wheelchair access;[]
8245;La Mulata;Spain;Santander;Andrés del Río 7, Santander, 39004, Spain;43.4653713;-3.7961379;80;false;true;Seafood;One of the classic addresses in the Puertochico district of the city, La Mulata owes its name to a species of black crab that lives in the rocks dotted around its docks and jetties. It features a maritime-inspired minimalist interior which includes a bar that is always very busy thanks to its array of tapas and “raciones”, a striking fish and seafood display (close to it there’s also a live lobster tank), plus a pleasant dining room. The à la carte menu also offers a few meat dishes plus an interesting selection of savoury rice options with a focus on the sea. Make sure you try the superb pan-cooked clams and also enquire about the fresh fish of the day.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8246;Veiramar Arcade;Spain;Soutomaior;Avenida Castelao 2, Soutomaior, 36690, Spain;42.3444378;-8.6116919;97;true;false;Seafood;Thanks to the completely glass-enclosed dining room, guests can enjoy delightful views of the mouth of the River Verdugo. Simply constructed dishes that are based around excellent ingredients and with a strong focus on the sea, although high-quality meat and rice dishes are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8247;La Terrazita;Spain;Navalmoral de la Mata;Antigua N-V, Navalmoral de la Mata, 10300, Spain;39.8922309;-5.5292001;35;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant and somewhat unexpected surprise on an industrial estate on the outskirts of town (next to an MOT testing centre). Terrazita’s traditional cuisine focuses on quality ingredients, including excellent grilled meat and seafood. The daily set menu is particularly popular, complemented by an à la carte and an extensive tasting menu with an included wine pairing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8248;Koiné;Spain;Alacant;Bazán, 45, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.346219;-0.4864161;54;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Koiné’s name refers to a variant of the Greek language once used in Ancient Greece. Here, the cuisine has returned to the origins and roots of Mediterranean cooking, working in tandem with the culinary traditions of Andalucia and with a style that has adapted to contemporary tastes. The chef has previously worked in the R&D department of the Dani García Group – a detail that is obvious on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8249;Cal Xim;Spain;Sant Pau d'Ordal;Plaza Subirats 5, Sant Pau d'Ordal, 08739, Spain;41.3836704;1.7963718;97;true;false;Regional Cuisine;A centrally located restaurant that champions seasonal Catalan cuisine, with a focus on the grill and locally sourced meats. Make sure you try its delicious artichokes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8250;El Paladar by Zuriñe García;Spain;Portugalete;María Díaz de Haro 2, Portugalete, 48920, Spain;43.3219549;-3.0176712;63;true;false;Basque;Basque cuisine has found a new home in the Puente Colgante Boutique Hotel, a property designed in a delightful Spanish colonial style. The cuisine here is overseen by chef Zuriñe García, who has already enjoyed considerable success at the legendary Andra Mari in Galdakao. Here, he showcases traditional cuisine deeply rooted in the culinary traditions of Vizcaya that showcases his elegant personal touches alongside top-quality ingredients. The à la carte is complemented by two tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8251;Vicus;Spain;Pals;Enginyer Algarra 51, Pals, 17256, Spain;41.9686962;3.1484922;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This is the successful story of an old family business that initially started life as a café. Located along one of the main streets in Pals, it features a dining room with high ceilings that combines a pleasant contemporary look with more traditional decorative details that link it with its past (bar, floors, furniture etc). The chef, who has trained in a number of leading restaurants, creates elaborate traditional cuisine with an imaginative touch that never fails to please guests and includes several interesting seasonal dishes and a few rice options (such as black rice with squid and a pear aioli and rice with pork rib and confit boletus mushrooms).;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8252;La Sirena;Spain;Petrer;Avenida de Madrid 14, Petrer, 03610, Spain;38.478935;-0.7846724;44;false;false;Seafood;Located next to the bus station, La Sirena’s highlights include an impressive bar-cum-display counter (featuring fish and seafood sourced from nearby fish auctions as well as from Galicia) and its reputation across the region for the quality of its aioli sauces. Its extensive à la carte is based around top-quality products, and is complemented by appetising daily specials, an array of seafood priced by weight, superb rice dishes (for a minimum of two people) and two menu options (Mediterráneo and Degustación). Before you start your meal, make sure you ask for a tasting of aiolis accompanied by a selection of bread (including toasted).;Air conditioning;[]
8253;Capet;Spain;Barcelona;Cometa 5, Barcelona, 08002, Spain;41.3821591;2.1790772;57;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Located in one of the charming narrow streets that endow the city’s Gothic Quarter with its characteristic personality, Capet features a rustic-contemporary look and an original layout with an open-view kitchen on the ground floor (around which guests can sit and eat) and a pleasant dining room upstairs, which overlooks what is happening below. Chef Armando Álvarez champions an updated and sincere take on traditional cooking, showcased via à la carte options and two tasting menus (5 and 8 courses).;Air conditioning;[]
8254;Koma;Spain;Collado Mediano;Paseo de los Rosales 48, Collado Mediano, 28450, Spain;40.6917934;-4.0467294;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Fusion;Part of the La Torre Box Art hotel, Koma occupies a glass-fronted pavilion with access via the garden. It is skilfully run by chef Rubén Amro, who has won several Spanish food awards and has also represented Spain at the prestigious Bocuse d'Or Europe competition. The à la carte, an updated take on traditional cuisine with interesting nods to Asian cuisine, is complemented by a tasting menu. If you have the chance, don’t miss the liquid “cocido” fritters.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8255;Rios O Freixo;Spain;Freixo;Paseo Ribeira 56, Freixo, 15288, Spain;42.7941883;-8.9460133;44;false;true;Seafood, Galician;A family-run restaurant with a superb location overlooking the port, where the quality of ingredients is always to the fore, especially in terms of its shellfish (oysters of different sizes, clams, cockles etc) and superb fresh fish, meat and rice dishes (the rice with sea urchins and Cambados scallops is a delight). For the best views, make sure you book a table by the picture windows.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8256;Cobo Tradición;Spain;Burgos;Plaza de la Libertad 9, Burgos, 09004, Spain;42.3415145;-3.6988404;89;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A superb dining space that flies the flag for tradition on a menu that features grilled fish and meat, hearty stews, croquettes etc. Don’t miss the stuffed mussels with a beurre blanc!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8257;Ikigai Flor Baja;Spain;Madrid;Flor Baja 5, Madrid, 28013, Spain;40.4221579;-3.7096183;22;false;true;Japanese;Consistent, technically accomplished and high-quality cuisine in an informal setting, where the chef creates Japanese cooking that borders on the traditional while at the same time surprising guests with its fusion of French and Spanish influences.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8258;Cambium;Spain;Sallent de Gállego;Plaza del Valle de Tena 7, Sallent de Gállego, 22640, Spain;42.772459;-0.3306931;84;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Located in the centre of the village, Cambium, which is Latin for “change” and is also the word to describe one of the outer layers of a tree trunk, is keen for guests to discover the flavours of the Aragonese Pyrenees from a different perspective. In its pleasant, rustic-style dining rooms, featuring a profusion of wood and views of both the village and its impressive surrounding mountains, choose between an à la carte option and an extensive seasonal set menu with dishes such as trout from Lanuza and IGP Aragón veal, which connect us with the culinary traditions of this part of the Alto Gállego region. An impressive array of D.O. Somontano wines completes the picture!;Great view;[]
8259;Vuelve Carolina;Spain;Valencia;Correos 8, Valencia, 46002, Spain;39.4697776;-0.3744938;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located next door to El Poblet, one of the city’s fabled gourmet addresses, Vuelve Carolina stands out for its casual, informal feel. It is a great place for a fun and relaxed dining experience where you can share dishes with friends, including some of award-winning chef Quique Dacosta’s most iconic dishes (such as his Cuba Libre of foie gras with lemon peel, arugula and brioche bread). Presentation, the pairing of ingredients, and textures are all to the fore on the à la carte (Vuelve Carolina’s “patatas bravas” won an award at the 2024 Madrid Fusión food show) and its unusual menus: A Midday Trip, Around the World, and NotJustFood (the latter a combination of dishes and cocktails).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8260;Es Arraïtzes;Spain;Garos;Plaza Major 7, Garos, 25539, Spain;42.7008602;0.844915;94;true;false;Peruvian, Fusion;This restaurant, which takes its name from the local Aranese word for “roots”, serves fusion cuisine featuring a mix of Peruvian, Aranese and Catalan flavours. The tasting menu is only available if pre-ordered.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8261;Chinchín Puerto;Spain;Vélez-Málaga;Puerto Deportivo Caleta de Vélez, Vélez-Málaga, 29751, Spain;36.748846;-4.0664022;30;true;true;Seafood;A family-run restaurant, the success of which is based on its high-quality products (sourced directly from the fish auction) and its respect for flavour. Terrace overlooking the marina.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8262;Cávala;Spain;Malaga;Alameda de Colón 5, Malaga, 29001, Spain;36.716146;-4.424962;96;true;true;Creative;A contemporary restaurant that stands out for its open-view kitchen and striking wine cellar. The cuisine of Miguel Ángel Mayor, a Barcelona-born chef with Andalucian roots, is centred around two surprise tasting menus (Presagios and Recuerdos) that aim to add a modern perspective to typical Málaga dishes, with a nod to his childhood, while at the same time retaining the full essence of their flavour.;Air conditioning;[]
8263;Aitor Rauleaga;Spain;Bilbao;Colón de Larreátegui 9, Bilbao, 48001, Spain;43.2624599;-2.927777;80;false;true;Basque;A restaurant with a classic-contemporary feel next to the Palacio de Justicia, where the chef conjures up Basque cuisine from top-quality ingredients, including delicious signature stews.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8264;VIA;Spain;Vic;Riera 25, Vic, 08500, Spain;41.9289863;2.2534236;86;false;true;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant occupies the “piano nobile” of the Casa Fontcuberta, an aristocratic property in the centre of town with a striking 19C decor and scenes of local life and customs depicted on frescoes on its walls. Its à la carte, featuring traditional Catalan dishes including several impressive rice and daily fish options, is complemented by a set menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8265;qapaq;Spain;Arona;Avenida de la Habana 14, Arona, 38626, Spain;28.0546255;-16.724928;29;true;false;Peruvian;A simple restaurant serving Peruvian cuisine with a Mediterranean touch that is centred around products sourced from the local market. The à la carte is complemented by a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8266;99 sushi bar;Spain;Madrid;Padre Damián 23, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.4586821;-3.6856124;82;true;false;Japanese;A highly successful restaurant, thanks to its traditional Japanese cuisine served alongside fusion dishes combining Spanish and Japanese influences. The à la carte, which is impressively complemented by a tasting menu, features dishes such as wild boar gyoza dumplings with caramelized onion, Arzúa cheese and a chestnut infusion, and Alaskan king crab gratin with wasabi and yuzu tobiko. Enhance your dining experience further by eating at the bar and watching the sushi chef at close quarters.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
8267;Taberna Pedraza;Spain;Madrid;Recoletos 4, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4221306;-3.6908664;71;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;An attractive taberna renowned for its “cocido” (stew) and its Tortilla de Betanzos, the latter so famous that there is even a counter that shows how many omelettes have been served here since 2014!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8268;Yarza;Spain;Valencia;Císcar 47, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.4642666;-0.3643917;43;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A contemporary-style restaurant that describes its traditionally inspired Valencian cuisine in a single premise: “We cook in the same painstaking way as in the past, but with a modern touch”. On the à la carte, with its focus on traditional, market-inspired cuisine, and featuring an array of suggestions with a focus on wild-caught fish of the day, you’ll also find delicious rice dishes (Arròs del Senyoret, Arroz en Perol Marinero, Paella de Costilla Ibérica with vegetables, Arroz en perol de montaña) which need to be pre-ordered. Make sure you also sample the exquisite cod fritters (Buñuelos de Bacalao).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8269;Por Herencia;Spain;Murcia;Cánovas del Castillo 9, Murcia, 30003, Spain;37.9842988;-1.1259962;76;true;true;Contemporary;In this intimate eatery with a traditional ambience, you have the guarantee of a family with a longstanding reputation in the restaurant business. Also evident is the constant energy of a team that likes to do things differently. The focus of the cuisine here, both on the à la carte and an impressive tasting menu, is on the full favours of Murcian cooking, as well as refined textures, meticulous presentation, and the showcasing of local vegetables and the latest culinary techniques. Standout dishes include the corvina fish with an Iberian beurre blanc and grilled green beans.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8270;Els Jardins del Tancat;Spain;Alcanar;CN-340 KM1059 - Sol de Riu, Alcanar, 43530, Spain;40.5287307;0.5094499;67;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Grills;Located on the Tancat de Codorniu estate, where it offers a much more informal dining option without the need to enter the hotel. The standout feature here is the idyllic and relaxing garden, with its large lawn area and various porches. In terms of cuisine, the specialities here are the paellas, rice dishes and grilled fish, such as turbot, which are usually served whole and which can be seen beforehand in a small display counter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
8271;Vinum;Spain;Torroja del Priorat;Mas d’en Bruno, Torroja del Priorat, 43737, Spain;41.2300915;0.805869;31;true;true;Contemporary;A complete surprise inside the isolated Gran Hotel Mas d'en Bruno, which occupies a restored farmhouse dating back to 1797 and surrounded by vineyards in the heart of the Priorat wine region. To the backdrop of a contemporary decor and open-view kitchen behind a large window, the seasonal cuisine on offer aims to recreate the flavours of inland Cataluña from a more modern perspective and with a focus on meticulous presentation. This is showcased on the à la carte and the option of three tasting menus (one of which is vegetarian). It is well worth eating on the terrace, with its views of the surrounding mountains and the vineyards of the Clos de l'Obac estate.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8272;Prebe by Bret;Spain;Lugo;Rúa Nova 8, Lugo, 27001, Spain;43.0104466;-7.5588005;73;false;false;Farm to table, Meats and Grills;Bret Fernández, the chef at the helm of this restaurant named after the Galician word for “sauce”, defines his culinary concept by the mantra “celebration, abundance and satisfaction". At this tapas bar-style eatery located along a pedestrianised street in Lugo’s old quarter, you’ll find quotes by leading Galician writers plus a meticulous dining room with a rustic feel on the first floor, the latter also boasting an ageing cabinet. The extensive à la carte features hints of fusion, and showcases an impressive array of beef (Friesian, Rubia Gallega etc) and fish (both whole and different cuts, all cooked on the grill). An array of daily specials is also available here.;Air conditioning;[]
8273;Rocacho Plaza;Spain;Madrid;Plaza del Marqués de Salamanca 9, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4299092;-3.6791737;43;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city’s Salamanca district, Rocacho Plaza boasts a pleasant terrace and a menu that focuses on grilled dishes. Among its choice of meats, the selection from El Capricho, the famous farm in Jiménez de Jamuz in the province of León, are a real draw, including its premium “Selección José Gordón” ox chop and its beef chop aged for 90 days. It also offers market-inspired dishes, recipes featuring seasonal vegetables, superb grilled fish, and rice and fideuá options. It also occasionally hosts full-day food events such as those dedicated to the delicious oxtail.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8274;Mesón el Centro;Spain;Puerto de Vega;Plaza de Cupido, Puerto de Vega, 33790, Spain;43.5651474;-6.6467007;21;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re not familiar with Puerto de Vega it is well worth a visit as it is one of the prettiest and most authentic towns along the entire Cantabrian coast. Situated in a pedestrianised section of the old quarter, this pleasantly simple restaurant run by a friendly married couple has lots of personality. Mary, the chef, who often comes out of the kitchen to talk to her guests, focuses on dishes that showcase the finest local products and which always follow traditional recipes, albeit with a modern touch. Choose between the limited à la carte, featuring several fish options priced by weight (turbot, sole, sea bass etc) and a tasting menu (El Centro) that never disappoints.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8275;Es Portal;Spain;Pals;Carretera de Torroella de Montgrí 17, Pals, 17256, Spain;41.98112;3.1534472;26;true;true;Catalan, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant occupies an impressive Empordà-style farmhouse that dates back to the 16C. It features attractive grounds and rustic-style dining rooms which provide a backdrop for seasonal cuisine that takes full advantage of local products. The cosy guestrooms are an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8276;La Huertona;Spain;Ribadesella;Carretera de Junco, Ribadesella, 33560, Spain;43.4531008;-5.0733342;36;false;false;Seafood, Grills;La Huertona features a gastro-bar plus an attractive dining room with panoramic views. Choose between the market-inspired à la carte featuring locally caught fish and an excellent tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8277;Abastos 2.0 - Barra;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Plaza de Abastos, Santiago de Compostela, 15704, Spain;42.879967;-8.541556;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A unique restaurant occupying six small market stalls in the city’s main food market, the Mercado de Abastos, which is the second most visited sight in Santiago after the majestic cathedral. You’ll need to book ahead as the restaurant only has a single shared large table where the focus is on “raciones”, modern tapas and wines by the glass. They also offer personalised menus from 50€ upwards.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
8278;Los Caballeros;Spain;Santo Domingo de la Calzada;Mayor 58, Santo Domingo de la Calzada, 26250, Spain;42.4410093;-2.9532371;33;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Los Caballeros occupies a historic building just behind the cathedral. In the rustically styled dining choose from a regional à la carte menu featuring an impressive array of soups, stews and cod dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
8279;Ozio Gastronómico;Spain;Madrid;Aviador Zorita 37, Madrid, 28020, Spain;40.4505152;-3.698337;35;true;true;Italian;In this small yet welcoming restaurant with a contemporary feel, which has developed as an offshoot of its original incarnation in Palermo, they are happy to boast that they offer Italian cooking with a Sicilian soul. In general, much of the focus here is on the cuisine of Italy, adapting traditional recipes and flavours to a more modern perspective, both on the à la carte and tasting menu. Don’t leave without trying the Oziamisu, a tiramisu that is prepared in front of you at your table.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8280;Asador Marino Tinta Negra;Spain;Almería;Fructuoso Pérez 12, Almería, 04001, Spain;36.8408433;-2.4644979;69;false;true;Grills;Somewhat tucked away in one of the narrow alleyways that dissect the heart of Almería’s old quarter, this restaurant has give a new lease of life to a former “asador”-style eatery. In spacious dining rooms that, despite being renovated, maintain the essence of Castille (one features a beautiful mural depicting a large black and white octopus!), the emphasis is on updated traditional cuisine that has moved away from a complete focus on meat to centre its menu on daily sourced fish and seafood that can be savoured fresh from the grill.;Air conditioning;[]
8281;Polea;Spain;Murcia;Almohajar 2, Murcia, 30002, Spain;37.9809233;-1.131;48;false;false;Contemporary;Polea is impressively run by a couple who decided to return to Spain (the homeland of the female half of the partnership) after many years working abroad. Behind its highly original façade, featuring green azulejos and thick esparto blinds, discover a rustic-contemporary ambience featuring a small bar and a partially open-view kitchen. Polea’s cooking is based around a single, thoroughly modern and highly personal tasting menu that takes its focus from locally sourced seasonal ingredients, with some dishes inspired by its own garden and incorporating various influences from elsewhere (especially Scandinavia). Polea is a restaurant that only uses fish that has been caught using sustainable methods.;Air conditioning;[]
8283;Leartá;Spain;Seville;Padre Tarin 6, Seville, 41002, Spain;37.3951404;-5.9962994;75;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city’s old quarter, just a few metres from the Plaza de la Gavidia, this restaurant exudes a passion for food, for craftsmanship and for what they describe here as “food for thought” and takes its from a word that refers to a meeting place for different Andalucian trades and skills. The focus of the young team at the helm is on a single tasting menu that showcases the flavours of Southern Spain as well as locally sourced ingredients and products (Iberian ham from Cumbres Mayores, white prawns from Isla Cristina, honey from Aznalcóllar etc). At the same time it respects the essence of tradition albeit from a more contemporary perspective, and always with an interesting play of textures and highly delicate sauces and broths.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8284;Shinkai Tastem;Spain;Valencia;Carrer D'Ernesto Ferrer 14, Valencia, 46021, Spain;39.4715978;-0.3550095;28;false;true;Japanese;This restaurant, one of the trailblazers for Japanese cuisine in the city, has embarked on a new path by reinventing both its dining space and its cuisine, with the latter continuing to showcase the essence of Japanese cooking but from a more contemporary perspective. Shinkai, which means “deep sea” in Japanese, highlights a plethora of flavours though its varied and extensive array of maki, temaki, sashimi, tempura and Wagyu beef sourced directly from Japan. It also offers a tasting menu that needs to be booked a minimum of 24hr ahead.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8285;Ronquillo;Spain;Ramales de la Victoria;Menéndez Pelayo 2, Ramales de la Victoria, 39800, Spain;43.2609534;-3.4663406;72;false;false;Regional Cuisine;In this rustic, family-run restaurant, the focus is on updated regional cuisine that includes delicious traditional stews and classic dishes such as squid cooked in its own ink.;Air conditioning;[]
8286;La Cocina Sitges;Spain;Sitges;Sant Bonaventura 19, Sitges, 08870, Spain;41.2372439;1.8075108;68;true;false;Contemporary;In this small restaurant located along a pedestrian street along which it also boasts an outdoor terrace, the contemporary-style menu has a strong focus on nuanced dishes with plenty of flavour, a hint of fusion and lots of personality. Unforgettable dishes include the egg-based Huevo 63º with truffle and the Aberdeen Angus ribeye from Uruguay, in honour of the owner-chef’s home country.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8287;Estimar;Spain;Barcelona;Sant Antoni dels Sombrerers 3, Barcelona, 08003, Spain;41.3841621;2.1816663;64;true;true;Seafood;An intimate restaurant that is somewhat tucked away but which has received many plaudits thanks to the passion for the sea shown by the Gotanegra family and chef Rafa Zafra. Grilled dishes and high-quality products are to the fore here.;Air conditioning;[]
8288;Parada de la Reina-Martina Bistró;Spain;Plasencia;Tornavacas 2, Plasencia, 10600, Spain;40.0327704;-6.0800647;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, which started life as a typical bus station café, has evolved into what could be described as a “gourmet concept”. Nowadays, it is a contemporary bistro serving modern, globally inspired cuisine on an à la carte attractively split into different sections, plus two extensive set menus: Destino and Degusta (the latter needs to be booked 24hr in advance).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8289;A Espiga;Spain;A Coruña;Santiago 4, A Coruña, 15001, Spain;43.3698371;-8.3948142;67;false;false;Farm to table;Located in the heart of A Coruña, very close to the Plaza de María Pita and Los Cantones which showcase the city’s historical heritage, this restaurant (which translates as “ear of corn” in Galician, a play on the name of chef Koke Trigo (“trigo” is the Spanish word for “wheat”) provides the backdrop for cuisine that highlights his full personality. In the intimate interior, featuring stone walls and a kitchen that opens out on to the dining room, the focus is on market-inspired cooking that is continually reinvented in line with fresh ingredients available daily, a fact reinforced by the lack of a freezer here. The menu includes an impressive array of dishes for sharing alongside specialities such as creamy smoked croquettes, “Nuestra Gilda” (a tortilla that changes with the seasons), delicious rice dishes (for two people) etc.;Air conditioning;[]
8290;Hiu;Spain;Cambrils;Avenida del Baix Camp 2, Cambrils, 43840, Spain;41.0730555;1.056209;99;true;false;Fusion;This restaurant, which translates as “to be hungry” in Thai, has transplanted the aromas and flavours of Bangkok to the Costa Dorada’s gastronomic capital. The chef here enjoys creating his own special mixes for his curries, as well as fermented products and kombucha vinegars. He also sources typical ingredients from the local area, such as sea fennel, which are rarely found on restaurant menus. His creativity and personality shine even more brightly on the tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8291;Toshi;Spain;Valencia;Salvador 5, Valencia, 46003, Spain;39.4770564;-0.3740854;93;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Toshi follows the philosophy of Japanese restaurants to the letter in this restaurant with just ten seats at the bar! Conversely, his cooking is inspired by the Mediterranean, with simple, honest dishes based around seasonal, locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8292;Víctor Sánchez-Beato;Spain;Toledo;Alamillos del Tránsito 9, Toledo, 45002, Spain;39.8559749;-4.0284706;33;false;false;Farm to table;This restaurant brings a breath of fresh air to Toledo’s dining scene! Following a trip to Japan, the chef returned home with the idea of setting up a restaurant in which the bar counter would take centre stage, and where he would cook, prepare and present dishes in front of guests as in a typical sushi bar. This extremely comfortable restaurant, designed to seat 16 guests, boasts a surprising design, with a decor of golden tones and a ceiling covered with striking geometric shapes. The single, particularly interesting tasting menu features contemporary, market-inspired dishes such as tuna with white garlic, creamy rice with wild boar, and a “coolant” of marzipan with cheese and passion fruit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8293;La Taberna del Chef del Mar;Spain;El Puerto de Santa María;Puerto Escondido 6, El Puerto de Santa María, 11500, Spain;36.5999;-6.223109;57;true;false;Creative;It was at Aponiente in El Puerto de Santa María that chef Ángel León made his culinary name! His creative cuisine extols the full virtues of the sea here through dishes inherited from Aponiente, alongside an array of “medias raciones”.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8294;Villa Verde;Spain;Ponte Ulla;Lugar de Figueiredo 10, Ponte Ulla, 15885, Spain;42.7800791;-8.4029773;69;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located in a privileged setting in a part of Galicia famous for its vineyards and magnificent country houses. The aristocratic feel of this area is also reflected in this restaurant occupying a delightful stone property whose origins date back to the 18C. Nowadays, it boasts an attractive wine cellar home to a traditional “lagar” wine trough, a rustic dining room with a typical “lareira” fireplace, plus a dining room with an elegant, classic decor. The traditional home-style cooking here is enhanced by seasonal ingredients, with wild mushrooms, angler fish and veal particularly popular. The baked hake with sea urchin is a must!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8295;Alameda;Spain;Fuenmayor;Plaza Félix Azpilicueta 1, Fuenmayor, 26360, Spain;42.4671766;-2.5612914;67;false;false;Regional Cuisine;This family - run restaurant is a respected name in the business thanks to the high quality of its ingredients. Highlights are the dishes cooked on the charcoal grill.;Air conditioning;[]
8296;El Palancar;Spain;Pedroso de Acim;Lugar Convento Palancar, Pedroso de Acim, 10829, Spain;39.8220262;-6.401951;66;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant offering attentive service in the heart of the countryside next to the El Palancar monastery (in the local area, they refer to the latter as the diminutive “conventico” as it is said to be the smallest monastery in the world). Its standout features are its terrace, its glass-fronted dining room with views of the delightful natural surroundings, and its updated take on traditional cooking that includes grilled meats cooked on its signature open grill. Other options include roasted goat and suckling pig, both of which need to be ordered ahead of time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8297;Alenda;Spain;Villaviciosa;Castiello de Selorio 23-A, Villaviciosa, 33316, Spain;43.5046937;-5.3388276;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this delightful rural house, run with great charm by Iñaki and Lola just a few kilometres from the coast, enjoy personally inspired dishes with well-balanced flavours that always champion the local area. The à la carte, dominated by fish purchased daily at the local auction in Lastres, is complemented by a tasting menu. Many of the vegetables here are sourced from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden.;Car park,Terrace;[]
8298;Nexe;Spain;Girona;Abeuradors 4, Girona, 17004, Spain;41.9834264;2.8244733;55;false;false;Contemporary;A restaurant that acts as a culinary link between guests and small-scale local producers, hence its name which translates as “nexus” in English. Choose between the à la carte, a tasting menu and different daily specials that showcase contemporary-style cuisine with a firm focus on the seasons and nods to both Asia and South America.;Counter dining;[]
8299;Alessandro Maino;Spain;Castelló de la Plana;Rei En Jaume 5, Castelló de la Plana, 12001, Spain;39.9856261;-0.0409199;51;false;false;International;This restaurant’s interesting cuisine with a French and Italian influence is showcased on an à la carte and several set menus (an “executive” menu midweek and a gastronomic menu at weekends).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8300;La Villa Agua Amarga;Spain;Agua Amarga;Carretera de Carboneras 18, Agua Amarga, 04149, Spain;36.9414271;-1.9337103;50;true;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with no little charm, occupying a villa with several Mediterranean-style dining rooms and a quiet terrace with tables arranged around a small swimming pool. The contemporary à la carte has a focus on dishes cooked on the open grill.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8301;Mas Albereda;Spain;Sant Julià de Vilatorta;Avenida Sant Llorenç 68, Sant Julià de Vilatorta, 08504, Spain;41.9260464;2.3273494;51;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Occupying a farmhouse with a pleasantly rustic ambience and an attractive glass-fronted terrace. Updated traditional cuisine bearing the signature of chef Nandu Jubany.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8302;El Mesón de Gonzalo;Spain;Salamanca;Plaza del Poeta Iglesias 10, Salamanca, 37001, Spain;40.964181;-5.6640497;66;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;An impressive example of how to adapt to the times. The roast dishes, grilled meats and traditional classics stand alongside an array of more contemporary and fusion - inspired options. The steak tartare is well worth trying.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8303;Fuentelgato;Spain;Huerta del Marquesado;Real 6, Huerta del Marquesado, 16316, Spain;40.1456567;-1.6861979;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fuentelgato is run by chefs Álex Paz and Olga García, a couple who continue to win plaudits galore in the hills of Cuenca province! Here, they offer just a single tasting menu that is always based around seasonal and locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
8304;La Guisandera de Piñera;Spain;Madrid;Rosario Pino 12, Madrid, 28020, Spain;40.4621618;-3.6924811;45;false;false;Asturian;A restaurant that offers traditional Asturian cuisine, including delicious stews and other famous dishes from this region of Northern Spain such as “arroz con pitu de caleya” (a type of chicken paella), La Guisandera’s signature fabada stew, and arroz con leche.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8305;ConSentido;Spain;Salamanca;Plaza del Mercado 8, Salamanca, 37001, Spain;40.9648902;-5.6627429;26;false;true;Contemporary;Situated just a few steps from the Plaza Mayor, ConSentido serves contemporary cuisine that is both technical and in tune with its local surroundings, with a focus on showcasing ingredients from Salamanca province. When placing your order, it is quite normal for the chef to highlight dishes that do not feature on the à la carte and to recommend specific dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8306;Islares;Spain;Bilbao;Mazarredo Zumarkalea, 65bis, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2671415;-2.9353316;83;true;false;Creative;This minimalist restaurant opposite the city’s Guggenheim Museum exudes plenty of enthusiasm as it showcases the traditional cuisine of Northern Spain. Here, under the baton of chef Julen Bergantiños, choose between two unusual menus that change completely with every season and are based around seasonal ingredients sourced from small-scale producers, plus a constant and skilful use of native condiments. These menus are entitled “A-8”, after the dual carriageway that connects Galicia, Asturias, Cantabria and the Basque Country), and N-634 (the beautiful road that runs from Santiago de Compostela to Donostia/San Sebastián). The sauces here are truly delicious!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8307;Lana;Spain;Madrid;Ponzano 59, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4413248;-3.6991787;65;true;false;Argentinian, Meats and Grills;An Argentinian restaurant that continues to gain in popularity, where the open grill is the focal point for everything that happens here. In this pleasant eatery run by two brothers, savour traditional dishes, gaucho specialities and different cuts of meat from a variety of breeds (Aberdeen Angus, Wagyu, Hereford, Vaca Gallega etc). The unusual collection of artisanal knives and the extensive list of Argentinian wines add to its appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
8308;La Bombi;Spain;Santander;Casimiro Sáinz 15, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.4644;-3.79683;44;true;true;Farm to table;A classic address whose success is based upon the bounty of its ingredients, including an enticing fish display counter (often featuring larger species), a live seafood tank, and a few meat dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
8309;Beluga;Spain;Malaga;Plaza de las Flores 3, Malaga, 29005, Spain;36.72015;-4.42214;80;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Located on a small square in the centre of the city, Beluga is run by a couple originally from Alicante, a relevant detail here given the cuisine on offer, which features highly delicate Mediterranean dishes with a contemporary touch, lots of technical detail and plenty of flavour. Savoury rice dishes and fish and seafood are a constant on their menus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8310;Los Marinos José;Spain;Fuengirola;Paseo Marítimo Rey de España 161, Fuengirola, 29640, Spain;36.5712203;-4.5906507;19;true;true;Seafood;Everyone is familiar with or has heard of Los Marinos José, an icon of maritime-inspired dining along the Playa de Carvajal on the Costa del Sol. Completely renovated in a modern, elegant style, it now features a kitchen open to the dining room, its always incredible display cabinets (its fish and seafood are striking for their exquisite quality) and a semi-glass-enclosed terrace. Everything is delicious here, but if we had to make a recommendation we would suggest the shrimp from Motril, the langoustine from Huelva, and the famous red prawns. Much of the catch is from the restaurant’s own boats!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8311;Charolés;Spain;San Lorenzo de El Escorial;Floridablanca 24, San Lorenzo de El Escorial, 28200, Spain;40.5910324;-4.1480754;64;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The Charolés enjoys a well - deserved reputation, both for its attractive decor and stone walls and its traditional, seasonal cuisine. One of its specialities is a hearty "cocido" stew, wich is only served on Mondays, Wednesdays and Fridays!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8312;Material;Spain;Malpica de Bergantiños;Eduardo Vila Fano 3, Malpica de Bergantiños, 15113, Spain;43.3235058;-8.8101968;45;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A centrally located contemporary restaurant offering traditional cuisine that specialises in grilled fish and meats of the highest quality. It even matures some of its meats itself.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8313;Laila;Spain;Mompía;Navalias 10, Mompía, 39108, Spain;43.4382692;-3.9188034;77;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;On the ground floor of a small rural hotel near Santander. Extensive à la carte featuring a modern take on traditional cooking, with the additional option of two tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8314;Faralá;Spain;Granada;Cuesta de Gomérez 11, Granada, 18009, Spain;37.1763702;-3.5952603;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An attractive, centrally located restaurant with plenty of personality where the true essence of traditional Granada cuisine has been given a modern makeover. Regular flamenco shows are also hosted here.;Air conditioning;[]
8315;El Quinto Sabor;Spain;Villaviciosa de Odón;Avenida de Quitapesares 17, Villaviciosa de Odón, 28670, Spain;40.3502055;-3.9005736;85;false;false;Creative, Spanish;A restaurant with a somewhat surprising location surrounded by industrials units, occupying a building with a strong sustainable focus. The exciting cuisine here, centred around four tasting menus, showcases impressive technique and a penchant for flavour and presentation. Some of its dishes include fresh spirulina, a microalgae renowned for its high concentration of nutrients.;Air conditioning;[]
8316;Llisa Negra;Spain;Valencia;Pascual y Genís 10, Valencia, 46002, Spain;39.4695042;-0.3740062;26;true;true;Farm to table;A fashionable restaurant bearing the hallmark of Quique Dacosta. The focus here is on high-quality produce with no artificial flavourings on a menu that features rice dishes and stews. Grilled dishes are a speciality.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8317;Ca l'Esteve;Spain;Castellbisbal;Carretera Martorell-Terrassa C 243c, Castellbisbal, 08755, Spain;41.4994045;1.967278;90;true;true;Catalan;A fourth-generation, family-run restaurant occupying a large stone house. The traditional Catalan menu is enhanced by several daily specials. Impressive choice of rice and grilled dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8318;Detapaencepa;Spain;Vigo;Ecuador 18, Vigo, 36203, Spain;42.2343631;-8.7224025;53;false;true;Contemporary;Two dining options (a tapas bar and a restaurant) under the same roof. In both spaces, guests can order from the same updated traditional menu of tapas, “raciones” and a choice of more elaborate dishes. Impressive wine cellar!;Air conditioning;[]
8319;Éleonore;Spain;Salinas;Pablo Laloux 13, Salinas, 33405, Spain;43.5795158;-5.9544544;81;true;false;Creative;Overlooking the Playa de Salinas and boasting stunning views, this attractive restaurant provides the backdrop for modern creative cuisine that aims to offer a different kind of dining experience through its combination of sweet and savoury ingredients and flavours, an ambition helped by the adjoining bakery and pastry shop. Choose between three menus: two options at lunchtime, and a third, Allegra, in the evening. The restaurant takes its name from local history – the Éleonore was the famous locomotive used by the Mina de Arnao, the first underwater coal mine in Europe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
8320;Rivas;Spain;Vega de Tirados;Carretera 33, Vega de Tirados, 37170, Spain;41.0254669;-5.8873772;51;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant with two distinct ambiences (one modern, the other more traditional) that excels in stews and grilled meats and is complemented by a varied wine list. Rivas also hosts themed food events.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8321;Túbal;Spain;Tafalla;Plaza de Francisco de Navarra 4, Tafalla, 31300, Spain;42.52767;-1.67492;79;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Well - renowned, family - run establishment offering a delicatessen, elegant dining rooms in a classic style and a pretty patio. Menu of cuisine from Navarre and a full wine cellar.;Air conditioning;[]
8322;La Casa de Manolete Bistró;Spain;Córdoba;Avenida de Cervantes 10, Córdoba, 14008, Spain;37.8880151;-4.7847287;79;false;true;Contemporary;A beautiful mansion that was once the home of the bullfighter Manolete, and before him the philosopher José Ortega y Gasset. The chef here creates regionally inspired contemporary cooking, including his signature “salmorejo” specialities.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8323;Puntarena;Spain;Madrid;Alberto Aguilera 20, Madrid, 28015, Spain;40.4299761;-3.7091742;100;false;true;Mexican;Occupying the Casa de México and taking its name from a beach back home, Puntarena offers dishes inspired by the country’s Pacific cuisine in a setting with a contemporary ambience. Choose between traditional fish dishes, fusion recipes and dishes made for sharing. The delicious “pulpo enamorado” (octopus) and innovative cocktails are a must!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8326;Almocadén;Spain;Alcaudete;Fuensanta 38, Alcaudete, 23660, Spain;37.5891593;-4.0763897;22;false;false;Contemporary, Andalusian;An unpretentious local restaurant with a modern feel and superb terrace that takes its name from the former family farm. Options here include an à la carte with a contemporary flavour, excellent off-menu recommendations (we loved the cod “kokotxas”), dishes that change with the seasons, an “executive” menu, plus another more extensive tasting-style menu option that requires a minimum 24hr advance booking.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8327;La Cocina de Colacho;Spain;Playa Blanca;Velázquez 15, Playa Blanca, 35580, Spain;28.8621229;-13.8124042;84;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;An impressive restaurant with an open-view kitchen (where the focus is on updated home cooking), designer decor, and a display of paintings by the female owner on the walls.;Air conditioning;[]
8328;Sa Pleta by Marc Fosh;Spain;Canyamel;Via de les Coves, Canyamel, 07589, Spain;39.6503571;3.4349219;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the Pleta de Mar hotel will definitely leave a lasting impression, a sense heightened by the pleasant views of its surroundings. There’s a more gastronomic feel in the evening, when a tasting menu and à la carte dining are available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8329;Stagier Bar;Spain;Palma;D'Espartero 11, Palma, 07014, Spain;39.5709547;2.6345416;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A small eatery with a relaxed and informal feel where “mini” haute cuisine designed for sharing is very much to the fore, including contemporary snacks and tapas with a strong Latin American flavour. Book ahead as it is always full.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8330;Casa Urola;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Fermín Calbetón 20, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20003, Spain;43.3233295;-1.9844221;21;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in a pedestrian street in the city’s old quarter with plenty of competition and popular with tourists, Casa Urola features a lively pintxos bar leading to a stylish dining room on the first floor. Chef Pablo Loureiro champions the “renewed” tradition of Basque cuisine via impressive market-inspired daily suggestions, some seafood options, as well as fish and meat cooked on the grill. Make sure you try the grilled black monkfish!;Air conditioning;[]
8331;Cooking Almadraba;Spain;Conil de la Frontera;Plaza de Blas Infante, Conil de la Frontera, 11140, Spain;36.2804996;-6.089724;24;true;false;Seafood;A restaurant with a highly attractive and contemporary look in which almost everything, including many of its decorative details, is focused on wild red tuna. It even has its own brand of almadraba tuna (Petaca Chico).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8332;Bomborombillos;Spain;Jaén;Pintor Carmelo Palomino 12, Jaén, 23004, Spain;37.7689214;-3.790553;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with a rustic-contemporary feel that started life as a bar. Today, it offers an enticing selection of tapas, sharing plates, à la carte dishes and a tasting menu (prior booked required) that showcases ingredients and flavours from the region.;Air conditioning;[]
8333;Travieso;Spain;Almería;Lentisco 14, Almería, 04007, Spain;36.8353995;-2.4443001;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in a residential district of the city where the chef at the helm, Dani Muñoz, conjures up contemporary cuisine with hints of creativity that is usually centred around seasonal and locally sourced ingredients. The à la carte, which starts with a section dedicated to informal tapas-style small plates, includes enticing options such as “Joselito” Iberian pork sashimi, red mullet, and glazed Iberian ribs.;Air conditioning;[]
8334;Areia;Spain;Marbella;Ramón Gómez de la Serna 23, Marbella, 29602, Spain;36.5096824;-4.8979308;90;true;false;Farm to table;A Mediterranean-inspired restaurant with a striking decor of light tones and original artisanal fabrics adorning sections of the walls and ceiling. In the kitchen, the emphasis is on internationally inspired cooking, including dishes such as veal shank (for two to share and carved up in front of you), the unmissable beef sirloin Rossini, or the surprising variety of soufflés (with the final flourish and flambé in the dining room). The à la carte is complemented by a tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8335;Ultramarinos Marín;Spain;Barcelona;Balmes 187, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.3967592;2.1528234;99;false;false;Farm to table;A somewhat unusual restaurant that has taken over an old bar and converted it into a simple asador. Options here include “knife and fork” breakfasts, plus a traditional market-inspired À la carte that showcases the full flavours of its ingredients. Fish and meat dishes here are priced by weight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8336;Cañitas Maite Gastro;Spain;Casas-Ibáñez;Tomás Pérez Úbeda 6, Casas-Ibáñez, 02200, Spain;39.2875729;-1.4695057;81;false;true;Contemporary;Run by two local chefs who offer two different menus: “De Barra”, based around contemporary tapas, and “De Producto”, offering modern dishes that showcase the La Mancha region.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8337;ABYA;Spain;Madrid;José Ortega y Gasset 32, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4301627;-3.6812581;82;false;false;Fusion;At Abya, top-quality ingredients, impressive technique and plenty of flavour combine to awaken the senses! Renowned chef Aurelio Morales has embarked upon his latest project in the Palacio de Saldaña, an attractive French-inspired building that is now fully dedicated to gastronomy. His cuisine, which is particularly designed for sharing, champions a contemporary style of cooking that is a fusion between Latin American and international dining and which the chef defines as “free and limitless”.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8338;Olivos;Spain;Barcelona;Galileu 159, Barcelona, 08028, Spain;41.3805162;2.1336938;100;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;This discreet and intimate restaurant close to Sants railway station is one of those that is easy to miss but continues to gain new admirers. Through its name, Argentinian-born chef Ezequiel Devoto pays a mini-homage to the country of his birth –Olivos is the district of Buenos Aires in which he grew up. His Mediterranean and globally inspired cuisine (a fusion of flavours from Argentina, Spain, Italy and elsewhere) is not short on creativity and is showcased on several tasting menus. Given its small size, Olivos only has a capacity for eight guests, so it advisable to book a table in advance.;Air conditioning;[]
8339;Waman;Spain;Bilbao;Avenida Madariaga 5, Bilbao, 48014, Spain;43.2710636;-2.9446092;17;true;true;Peruvian;Peruvian cooking and Basque ingredients are to the fore in Waman’s cuisine, which showcases plenty of personality and highly refined textures thanks to the chef’s roots and a period working alongside the great Eneko Atxa!;Air conditioning;[]
8340;Open;Spain;Alacant;Manuel Antón 12, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.3496847;-0.4864461;76;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Open boasts an eclectic look in keeping with its name. This similar liberal philosophy is also evident in its open-view kitchen (which also features a Japanese-style counter) and on the à la carte, with the option of creating your own media ración-style menu. The chefs here explain and serve their own contemporary dishes centred around market-fresh ingredients. One speciality that is definitely worth ordering is the delicious red tuna “catalana”.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8341;Narbasu;Spain;Cereceda;Palacio de Rubianes, Cereceda, 33583, Spain;43.3860873;-5.269812;87;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;If you’re keen to find a place in which to “lose yourself” and relax in the purest sense of the word, you won’t find anywhere quite like the Palacio de Rubianes, an authentic 14C Asturian-style property surrounded by verdant meadows and with the impressive summits of the Picos de Europa as a backdrop. Facilities here include attractive guestrooms and impressive market-inspired cooking bearing the signature of Esther and Nacho Manzano. Their cuisine is showcased on an à la carte and on two menus (Tradicional and Narbasu), all of which reveal authentic local flavours and include classic dishes from Casa Marcial, albeit from a more local perspective. Added interest is provided by the restaurant’s own kitchen garden on an old golf course, and a restored old mill standing alongside a stream to produce their own cornflour, which they then use to make their superb “tortos” appetisers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8342;Kensei;Spain;Adeje;Plaza Playas del Duque, Adeje, 38679, Spain;28.09169;-16.7424804;53;false;true;Japanese, Contemporary;A Japanese restaurant with a difference, offering contemporary Japanese cuisine with no little creativity and a few surprises in its presentation. Extensive à la carte plus omakase menus.;Air conditioning,Garden or park;[]
8343;Maite;Spain;Saragossa;Plaza San Pedro Nolasco 5, Saragossa, 50001, Spain;41.6529178;-0.8768169;23;true;true;Contemporary;Intimate, personal and well run by a couple who have been trained in some of Spain’s leading restaurants. Maite’s updated take on traditional dishes is showcased on a concise à la carte plus a tasting menu, with lots of attention to presentation and respect shown to classic recipes that are not easy to find these days, such as sole meunière.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8344;Torre de Sande;Spain;Cáceres;Condes 3, Cáceres, 10003, Spain;39.4732281;-6.3714626;82;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;You can enjoy the more casual concept of Atrio’s cuisine in this restaurant occupying a 15C mansion located in the heart of the town’s old quarter, just a few metres from its famous three-Michelin-star sibling. In this informal setting, savour dishes with a more traditional and regional flavour, including Iberian sausage, local cheeses, delicious stews, grilled meats, a few fusion-inspired dishes as well as enticing desserts. In fine weather, it’s well worth booking a table on the attractive terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8345;Gloria;Spain;Gijón;Plaza Florencio Rodríguez 3, Gijón, 33206, Spain;43.542324;-5.6635227;54;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;The name of this designer-inspired restaurant with a relaxed ambience pays tribute, along with the eatery they own in Oviedo, to the grandmother of the award-winning Manzano siblings. Here, they triumph with the more informal side of their cuisine, which is based around a traditional à la carte with hints of fusion that is particularly designed for sharing, alongside two menu choices (one daily option only available at lunchtime midweek, and a second more extensive tasting menu). We recommend ordering the delicious nems with pork cheek and prawns, the potato tortilla, and the legendary Casa Marcial ham croquettes. You can also eat at the bar counter, where you can watch your food being prepared.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8346;Casa Manolo;Spain;Daimús;Paseo Marítimo 5, Daimús, 46710, Spain;38.9752171;-0.1405905;23;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A longstanding family-run restaurant with relaxing sea views that began life as a “chiringuito” (beach bar) and has been gradually evolving ever since. Owner-chef Manuel Alonso offers guests an updated take on traditional cuisine, the aim of which is create a range of sensations and a return to the region’s origins via the à la carte (don’t miss the shrimp from Santa Pola, the iconic tripe, or the thin-noodled “fideuá” from Gandía) and an array of set menus (Calma, Miradas, Escapadas etc).;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8347;Garelos;Spain;Madrid;Blanca de Navarra 6, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4288116;-3.6930868;93;true;false;Galician;A simple Galician taberna on two floors with an unapologetic focus on authenticity. The cuisine here is based around carefully selected ingredients that are used to create traditional home-style cuisine of the type that Galicians would prepare and savour on days when they are nostalgic for their homeland. Specialities include the Tortilla de Betanzos (an omelette which is less cooked on the inside), the exquisite Empanadas Gallegas (the ingredients for which change daily), Cañón de Sanchón (delicious roasted veal), and the creamy Tarta de Queso cheesecake. Seafood takes centre stage here on Thursdays!;Air conditioning;[]
8348;El Pandora;Spain;Avilés;San Bernardo 6, Avilés, 33402, Spain;43.5566696;-5.9233521;40;false;false;Farm to table;A family-run restaurant that will appeal to guests thanks to its contemporary decor with touches of Art Deco, and its cuisine, which is traditional but with a few enticing modern touches that clearly demonstrate that the son, Alejandro Villa, has taken over the reins in the kitchen. The à la carte, which features classic dishes such as sirloin steak tartare and tripe stew with chorizo and ham, is complemented by an impressive array of market-inspired suggestions (fish sourced from local auctions plays a prominent role here) and a tasting menu that changes almost daily. If the weather is fine, make sure you book a table on the charming split-level terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8349;Almazen Salinas;Spain;Salinas de Añana;Real 49, Salinas de Añana, 01426, Spain;42.8007627;-2.9840729;45;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;Amid the surprising landscapes of the Valle Salado de Añana, overlooking its salt pans that date back millennia, you’ll find this rustic-style former salt warehouse that now features the kitchen at its very heart with a bar counter arranged around it. Head chef Beatriz Pascual shows off her skills in front of us, using locally sourced organic fruits and vegetables to create regionally inspired cuisine presented in a contemporary way on a single tasting menu that changes with the seasons and includes dishes such as horse meat steak tartare. She also enjoys working with “muera”, the salt of the earth, an exclusive product.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8350;Jiribilla;Spain;Barcelona;Comte Borrell, 85, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3788615;2.1604429;74;true;false;Mexican;Here, next to the Sant Antoni market, they say that the “Jiribilla”, a Pacific wind that is common in Mexico, is blowing strongly in Barcelona! After almost two decades in Mexico, Catalan chef Gerard Bellver has returned to his native region to showcase his cooking, which shows evident Mexican influences but with a nod to the cooking of his homeland. His various highly seasoned mole sauces, corn tortitas, and aguachiles, among other dishes, are often accompanied by a Mezcal-based cocktail. Dishes that stood out for us included the red prawn aguachile, with a chilli and jalapeño sauce, and the intensely flavoured crab “tetela”.;Air conditioning;[]
8351;Allégorie;Spain;Madrid;Bretón de los Herreros, 39, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.439502;-3.6971;63;true;true;French Contemporary;If you enjoy dining in restaurants that showcase French cuisine, Allégorie is definitely an option for you in the heart of the city’s Chamberí distrct. Here, you can discover the full virtues of Gallic cooking courtesy of young French chef Romain Lascarides, whose mantra is “eating nourishes the spirit, thoughts and the faculty of judgement”. His cuisine varies with the seasons thanks to his total respect for the seasonality of ingredients and for their small-scale producers. A choice of “raciones” is on offer at the counter by the entrance, with à la carte and set menu dining available upstairs. The latter include the Tradición lunchtime option, and the Placer menu which is available for dinner midweek.;Air conditioning;[]
8352;Pur;Spain;Barcelona;Passatge de la Concepció 11, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3945179;2.1601049;67;true;false;Farm to table;Pur bears the hallmark of chef Nandu Jubany, where the emphasis in the open-view kitchen is on dishes that focus on top-quality ingredients “in their purest form” . What stands out in particular, both on the à la carte and the tasting menus, is the extraordinary quality of the ingredients he uses in his dishes (we loved the razor clams from the Ebro delta as well as the seasonal tomatoes served with stracciatella cheese and pine nuts), which are either grilled, cooked on the barbecue or baked in salt. Our advice here would be to sit at the bar and order half-plates so that you can try a little bit of everything.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8353;Pampín Bar;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Ruela das Fontiñas 4, Santiago de Compostela, 15703, Spain;42.8810996;-8.5381375;60;false;false;Regional Cuisine;The modest façade of this restaurant in the historic quarter hides a traditional, slightly retro dining room that comes as a pleasant surprise and where guests will feel completely at home. The restaurant features unusual seating running along the side, a large shared table in the centre of the room and a decor of bare concrete, where the focus is on traditional home cooking full of the flavours of bygone days, which the chef likes to describe as “cocina de barrio” (neighbourhood cuisine). The menu includes homemade empanadas, numerous dishes to share, and a focus on escabeches, stews and freshly caught fish.;Air conditioning;[]
8354;Porto dos Barcos;Spain;Oia;Estrada Xeral 97 Viladesuso, Oia, 36309, Spain;42.0298621;-8.8836006;49;false;true;Seafood;A restaurant in a superb setting by the ocean, where the sea ebbs and flows against the rocks almost at your feet. In the classically furnished dining room, with large picture windows boasting stunning views of the Atlantic, savour Galician cuisine created with ingredients, such as the spectacular fish and seafood, of a quality that can only be found in this region. The extensive terrace is the restaurant’s jewel in the crown!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8355;Don Quijote;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Galeras 20, Santiago de Compostela, 15705, Spain;42.8813078;-8.5491911;73;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A legendary Galician restaurant where, as soon as you walk through the door, you take a journey back in time thanks to the strong focus on top-quality ingredients that are used to create simple yet almost unforgettable dishes in which the flavour of fish and seafood is respected to the full. Nowadays, there are very few places such as this, where you’ll find a live seafood tank at the entrance, in this case full of spider crabs from the estuary.;Air conditioning;[]
8356;Taúlla;Spain;Murcia;Antonio Flores Guillamón 2, Murcia, 30100, Spain;38.0109733;-1.1536029;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This highly unusual restaurant occupies an old paprika mill in the Espinardo district of Murcia, where the basement is home to an attractive private dining space and a themed museum dedicated to paprika (the fascinating and colourful collection of old containers is particularly impressive). The cooking here has its roots in tradition and the local region, albeit with a fun, imaginative and modern makeover, with no little technical skill. Head chef Rodi Fernández showcases his cuisine on an à la carte (the “panigiri” of red tuna and guacamole with a citrus and guacamole cream presented on an hourglass of sand was a complete surprise) and two extensive tasting menus: Molino and Taúlla. The selection of cheeses can be ordered at additional cost before dessert.;Air conditioning;[]
8357;Karmine;Spain;Vitoria-Gasteiz;Los Herrán 2, Vitoria-Gasteiz, 01004, Spain;42.842473;-2.6641824;57;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Located just a few minutes from the historic centre, Karmine is a restaurant that is definitely worthy of interest, run by the brother-and-sister team of Jabi in the kitchen and María in the dining room. The cuisine is a nod to the Valencian roots of their mother, and places as much emphasis on the use of almost obsolete ingredients from Álava province as it does on the reintroduction of local recipes that have been all but forgotten (“cocido vitoriano” stew, asparagus “a la Urcelay”, rice with borage etc), but always from a modern perspective. The focus here is on a single tasting menu (8- and 10-course options) that is constantly changing as a result of the restaurant’s close collaboration with local farmers. We recommended that you allow yourself to be guided in your choice of wines from the local area.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
8358;Mare;Spain;Cadiz;Plaza de la Candelaria 12, Cadiz, 11005, Spain;36.5311693;-6.2955994;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Chef Juan Viu, who defines himself as a “stewmaker”, views his cuisine as “a tribute to time-honoured cooking, to that of mothers, and to the sea”. The Pureza (Purity) menu, which changes almost daily depending on the availability of seasonal ingredients and those purchased from the nearby fish auctions in Conil, Vejer de la Frontera, Chiclana etc, reinterprets classic Cádiz recipes from a more contemporary perspective, with prominence shown to flavours from his childhood as well as maritime-inspired stews. Iconic dishes available year round include the highly original squid-based “calamar guisado en frío” and “grandmother Trini’s sofrito”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8359;A de Totó;Spain;Trasmonte;Lugar de Reino 20, Trasmonte, 15864, Spain;42.8947449;-8.6886196;34;true;true;Grills;On the outskirts of Trasmonte, along a road leading to Negreira and the delightful Ponte Maceira (which has been officially designated as one of the most beautiful villages in Spain), this restaurant delights guests thanks to its honest simplicity both in terms of its decor (the walls are adorned with large photos of Galician landscapes) and cuisine. Although there’s a good choice of starters and several fish options, the main speciality is grilled meat, hence the cabinets full of different cuts (Galician sirloin, Angus ribs from Ireland, aged T-bone etc).;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8360;D'Leria;Spain;Carril;Valentín Viqueira 6, Carril, 36610, Spain;42.61566;-8.77561;80;true;false;Contemporary, Galician;In a traditional fishing community such as this one, famous for the quality of its clams, the quality of ingredients always takes centre stage. This simple family-run restaurant, which has breathed new life into a former bar, is run by a couple – two chefs with a focus on contemporary, seasonal cooking inspired by the sea. This is showcased on a concise à la carte and a tasting menu option (“where the sea takes me”). We particularly enjoyed the black monkfish with a pepitoria sauce.;;[]
8361;Casa Pedro;Spain;Puente Genil;Poeta García Lorca 5, Puente Genil, 14500, Spain;37.3917089;-4.7684271;47;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Named after its owner, the Casa Pedro has been taking orders for over 30 years, during which time it has developed the secret to ensuring its customers always leave happy, based around consistent and professional family-style service. Choose between the tapas bar at the entrance, where you can select from a varied daily menu, the more classically inspired dining room, or a slightly more contemporary private dining space. Traditional, market-inspired cooking of a very high quality, featuring a choice of cured and red meats, fish, seafood and seasonal vegetables, many of which come with a “media-ración” option.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8363;Tragatá Ronda;Spain;Ronda;Nueva 4, Ronda, 29400, Spain;36.741513;-5.1659562;76;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Discover the more affordably priced and informal cuisine of famous chef Benito Gómez, who showcases his culinary repertoire here through an array of small plates and tapas created using the finest ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8364;José María;Spain;Segovia;Cronista Lecea 11, Segovia, 40001, Spain;40.9503864;-4.1225617;61;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;A spacious restaurant with attractive dining rooms embellished in a mix of attractive Castilian-style decor and more contemporary-inspired spaces. The signature dish here is the roast suckling pig reared on the family farm.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
8365;La Cúpula;Spain;San Eugenio;París, San Eugenio, 38660, Spain;28.0886928;-16.7363047;63;true;false;Creative;A panoramic restaurant striking for its colourful dome which brings to mind the explosion of a supernova! International and Canarian cuisine with a contemporary flavour.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8366;Villena;Spain;Segovia;Plazuela de los Capuchinos 2, Segovia, 40001, Spain;40.9520697;-4.1233569;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Villena occupies the former church of the Convento de las Oblatas, where its focus is on consistency and locally sourced products, which it uses to create a modern take on traditional recipes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8367;Sabino;Spain;Sanxenxo;Ourense 3, Sanxenxo, 36960, Spain;42.4016926;-8.8106261;48;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family - run restaurant situated just a few metres from the famous Silgar beach. Traditional Galician dishes with the occasional modern twist, all made from top - quality ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8368;El Carreter;Spain;La Xara;Partida Fredat 12, La Xara, 03709, Spain;38.82913;0.06199;83;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Occupying an attractive old farmhouse by a crossroads, this restaurant has a name that recalls the wheelwright trade in bygone days. It features a pleasant terrace for an aperitif or coffee, several attractively laid-out dining rooms (one with a fireplace), plus a contemporary à la carte and an excellent tasting menu with a focus on Mediterranean ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8369;Cañadío;Spain;Santander;Gómez Oreña 15, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.4636665;-3.8018969;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Considered to be a real institution in Santander, this restaurant comprises a tapas bar, a dining room on the mezzanine level and a second classic, contemporary - style dining room. Good - quality traditional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8370;Muka;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Avenida de la Zurriola 1, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20002, Spain;43.3240377;-1.9793829;43;true;false;Grills;This restaurant, featuring a Nordic-inspired design, pleasant terrace, views of the mouth of the Urumea river and the hallmark of chef Andoni Luis Aduriz, is part of the ever-busy Karsaal congress centre. Relaxed, unpretentious cuisine in which grilled vegetables take centre stage. Choose between the à la carte, a tasting menu and a choice of daily specials.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8371;Miga;Spain;Cáceres;Arco de la Estrella, Cáceres, 10001, Spain;39.4749059;-6.3711555;59;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located on the main square (Plaza Mayor), right next to the legendary Arco de la Estrella which provides access to the medieval walled city, this restaurant occupies an old two-storey house that now brandishes a contemporary interior. The à la carte, featuring dishes with a hint of tradition such as “pringá” gyozas, “migas del maestro” (a speciality made with breadcrumbs) with pork belly and free-range egg, and the grilled Retinta beef tenderloin with apple, is complemented by a tasting menu entitled Las Niñas (The Girls), in honour of the owner-daughters’ father, renowned chef Eustaquio Blanco.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8372;La Suculenta;Spain;Benicàssim;Sequiota 4, Benicàssim, 12560, Spain;40.0532627;0.0620043;53;false;false;Contemporary;Based around the mantra “Taste the unexpected”, this modern, centrally located restaurant run by chef Jorge Lengua (one of the promising new names on the Valencia food scene), offers contemporary-inspired cuisine that is showcased via well-presented dishes that make full use of modern techniques, such as the Iberian ham croquettes with “torrezno” (fried bacon) powder, and the Andalucian-style glass shrimp with fried egg and kimchi mayonnaise. The à la carte, which features lots of small plates, is complemented by an impressive array of rice dishes and several set menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8373;NaDo;Spain;A Coruña;Callejón de la Estacada 9, A Coruña, 15001, Spain;43.3699158;-8.3994616;80;false;true;Creative;Located along a narrow street in the city’s old quarter, yet just a few steps from the boats moored at the Real Club Náutico de A Coruña, NaDo boasts a thoroughly modern look, with an open-view kitchen and just two long tables that can be adjusted according to the number of guests. Here, chef Iván Domínguez, who is constantly moving between the kitchen and the dining room, creates contemporary cuisine with its roots in Galicia and the Atlantic. This is showcased in particular on the Furancho surprise menu, on which the chefs themselves select the dishes to be served.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8374;Can Roquet;Spain;Romanyà de la Selva;Plaça de l'Esglèsia 1, Romanyà de la Selva, 17245, Spain;41.8534456;2.9845488;49;true;true;International;A charming restaurant in a small, idyllic mountain village with a focus on international cooking alongside a few traditional and Catalan dishes. Its relaxing terrace is a must!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8375;Balbuena y Huertas;Spain;Seville;San Jacinto 89, Seville, 41010, Spain;37.3812925;-6.0086554;81;true;false;Contemporary;An attractive restaurant in the heart of the city’s Triana district, where it occupies a beautiful building in the style of the region and which pays a small homage to the architect who designed it. The young Sevilla-chef showcases his ability on three tasting menus (from which individual dishes can also be order à la carte style) which provide an updated take on Andalucian recipes such as lobster salad with pickles, Carabinero prawn tempura, creamy langoustine rice and shrimp socarrat, Iberian pork etc, with a permanent focus on seasonal Andalucian ingredients.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
8376;A Maceta;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;San Pedro 120, Santiago de Compostela, 15703, Spain;42.8817283;-8.5354481;29;true;false;Fusion;This restaurant is situated on the Rúa de San Pedro, the road into the city taken by pilgrims arriving via the Camino Francés, the Camino del Norte or the Camino Primitivo. Here, on the ground floor of an unpretentious stone building with a relaxed, rustic-contemporary ambience, Jorge Gago creates fusion cuisine that combines traditional and Asian recipes (leeks, stracciatella di bufala and almonds, mackerel sashimi and, for dessert, the hazelnut millefeuille). Additional bonuses here are the pleasant patio-terrace – the perfect setting for a relaxed meal or drink – and the extensive wine list featuring an impressive choice of sparkling wines.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8377;Tierra y Vino;Spain;Samaniego;Constitución 12, Samaniego, 01307, Spain;42.5684304;-2.6797272;72;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Tierra y Vino is part of the 18C Palacio de Samaniego, now converted into a luxury boutique hotel. Here, chef Bruno Coelho offers his guests an à la carte that is constantly evolving and centred around locally sourced seasonal ingredients and dishes with added culinary touches from Galicia and elsewhere in Spain. The restaurant also houses a collection of works of art belonging to Baroness Ariane de Rothschild.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8378;Ginés Peregrín;Spain;Almería;Méndez 6, Almería, 04001, Spain;36.8440534;-2.4615731;42;false;false;Contemporary;Through the mantra “A love for cooking”, an expression that encapsulates Ginés Peregrín’s vocation since his childhood, this chef conjures up Mediterranean-based cuisine that showcases his personality by incorporating influences from other cultures (Japan, Mexico, Peru, as well as the Netherlands, where he worked for several years). Choose between the à la carte (we enjoyed the risotto of homemade “gurullos” with wild cep mushrooms and red gambas from the Almería coast) and a surprise 5- or 7-course tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8379;Chivo;Spain;Morales de Toro;Avenida de los Comuneros, Morales de Toro, 49810, Spain;41.5335788;-5.3010727;21;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Behind the unpretentious façade of this restaurant (Chivo is the nickname for the family that runs it), you’ll find a simple bar and two dining rooms, one for the set menu, the other for à la carte dining (the latter also features a private space with a rustic yet elegant feel). The verbally presented menu includes homemade stews and a good daily selection of fish, most of which are cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8380;Goichu;Spain;Ceuta;Independencia 15, Ceuta, 51001, Spain;35.887165;-5.31403;48;true;true;Fusion;Goichu owes its name to owner-chef Hugo Ruiz’s affectionate nickname for his wife. The former, who was the driving force behind the original Bugao restaurant in Ceuta (now operating under the same name in Madrid), is now at the helm of this eatery offering a new and unusual “total fusion” concept between Basque cooking, Asian influence and fish sourced from the waters of the Straits of Gibraltar. The end result? Fun and exciting dishes with lots of flavour!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8381;Goxoa;Spain;Playa de las Américas;Avenida Antonio Domínguez, Playa de las Américas, 38660, Spain;28.0565411;-16.7252936;37;false;true;Grills;An asador-style restaurant with a kitchen and grill visible to diners and a contemporary decor that comes as something of a surprise. Traditional cuisine featuring local Canary Island ingredients and a modern touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8382;La Tavernetta da Ponte;Spain;Ponte do Porto;Outeiro 35, Ponte do Porto, 15121, Spain;43.1376343;-9.1164332;49;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Italian;A highly impressive vinoteca-taberna run by a couple from Galicia and Naples respectively, where guests can choose from copious Galician-style “raciones” and various Italian dishes, including excellent pizzas.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
8383;Ticuí;Spain;Madrid;Cedaceros 6, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4174195;-3.6985192;51;false;false;Mexican;If you‘re hankering for Mexican cuisine in the Spanish capital, at Ticuí (the sister restaurant of Puntarena) you’ll find the true essence of Mexican cooking in an attractively appointed and contemporary setting. The dishes on offer, combining tradition and modernity, are particularly made for sharing. Its corn tortillas are prepared here every morning on a traditional “comal” griddle.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8384;Entre dos Mons;Spain;Palamós;Tauler i Servià 21, Palamós, 17230, Spain;41.8457199;3.1289872;57;false;true;Peruvian;A restaurant offering a fusion between Catalan cuisine and the unique flavours of Peruvian cooking, the chef’s homeland. Entre dos Mons also has its own vegetable garden and maintains a strong commitment to sustainability.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8385;Maràngels;Spain;Sant Gregori;Can Quelot, Sant Gregori, 17150, Spain;41.990223;2.768378;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Housed in a beautiful 17C farmhouse surrounded by a garden, this rustic yet contemporary - style restaurant serves updated traditional cuisine with a selection of different set menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8386;Narru;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;San Martín 22, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20005, Spain;43.3177248;-1.981513;39;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located opposite the city’s Buen Pastor cathedral, Narru boasts a modern dining room in which the menu features traditional, market-inspired cuisine with an unequivocal focus on high-quality ingredients that tries to reflect its own character and provide an element of surprise. It features one informal space perfect for tapas and a second more elegant dining area with tables and tablecloths in which the à la carte (half portions are possible) is complemented by an impressive tasting menu. The restaurant takes its name from the nickname of the chef’s great-grandfather, a former professional pelota player.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8387;Sotavento;Spain;San Vicente de la Barquera;Avenida de Miramar 16, San Vicente de la Barquera, 39540, Spain;43.3824945;-4.3981149;29;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In this intimate family-run restaurant, traditional cooking based around locally sourced products is to the fore, including wild-caught fish and savoury rice dishes. We recommend that you book ahead!;Air conditioning;[]
8388;Casa de La Sirena;Spain;Cuenca;Canónigos, Cuenca, 16001, Spain;40.0779273;-2.1284504;44;true;true;Contemporary;This restaurant has plenty of history behind it, given that it occupies a building located next to the city’s famous “hanging houses” which was once used as a store house. The surprising interior, featuring minimalist and modern furnishings, provides the backdrop for contemporary cuisine that reinterprets well-known local dishes. Once seated, you can choose between two tasting menus with a wine-pairing option, one a shorter 4-course version (only available Wednesday to Friday), the other a longer 6-course menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8389;Poncio WM;Spain;Madrid;Plaza del Niño Jesús 3, Madrid, 28009, Spain;40.4112613;-3.6750194;93;false;true;Contemporary;A good dining option close to the Retiro, just a few metres from the Puerta del Niño Jesús entrance gate to the park. This quiet, attractive eatery, a fusion between a restaurant and a tapas bar, offers a contemporary focused à la carte of tapas and small plates with an Andalucian influence, plus a LQDW menu (Lo Que Diga Willy), in a nod to the owner-chef.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8391;Cuina Sant Pau;Spain;Sant Pol de Mar;Nou 10, Sant Pol de Mar, 08395, Spain;41.6015963;2.6233293;71;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;This iconic restaurant, which held three Michelin stars for many years, has adopted a new, much more informal bistro format featuring numerous images and mementoes that highlight the career of legendary chef Carme Ruscalleda. Her son Raül Balam Ruscalleda and Brazilian chef Murilo Rodrigues Alves are now in charge, offering a contemporary, Catalan-influenced menu that includes unpretentious dishes, Brazilian touches and a nod to the history of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
8392;Loaira Xantar;Spain;Pontevedra;Plaza de Leña 2, Pontevedra, 36002, Spain;42.4327839;-8.6432252;91;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A gastro-bar with a small bar, a bistro-style dining room upstairs, plus an attractive terrace on the square. Contemporary, regionally inspired dishes perfect for sharing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8393;Charolais;Spain;Fuengirola;Larga 14, Fuengirola, 29640, Spain;36.5376214;-4.6228862;64;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the centre of Fuengirola, but just a few metres from the beach, Charolais is a restaurant serving traditional cuisine with a nod to the Basque country on a menu featuring tapas, “raciones” and dishes for sharing. In fact, you’ll find two adjoining and interconnecting restaurants (Charolais and Charolais Tapas) here, as well as a pleasant terrace. Standout options include the Huelva shrimp “al ajillo”, the tartare of avocado and Carabinero prawns, as well any of its meat or fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8394;Manero;Spain;Alacant;Médico Manero Mollá 7, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.3438976;-0.4839376;37;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A unique restaurant that has recreated the ambience of a traditional grocery store, where you can enjoy delicate tapas, Iberian hams, salted dishes, high-quality tinned products and even seafood, many of which are packaged ready to take away.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8395;Roble by Jairo Rodríguez;Spain;Pola de Lena;Robledo 21 B, Pola de Lena, 33630, Spain;43.1530015;-5.8266669;95;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Innovative;Run by a couple (Jairo is in the kitchen, while Paula is at the helm in the dining room), this restaurant on the outskirts of town always comes as a pleasant surprise thanks to the essence of the Asturias region that is in clear evidence here. The à la carte, offering an updated take on traditional cuisine, features superb fish sourced from the Rula de Avilés company, including red mullet cooked at low temperature and wild grouper with an orange velouté, and is complemented by an impressive tasting menu. The cheese trolley and meats carved in front of you add an extra touch.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8396;Casanita;Spain;es Pujols;Fonoll Marí 101, es Pujols, 07311, Spain;38.7231416;1.4536934;34;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Seafood;Occupying a chalet-style building, Casanita’s traditional atmosphere provides the backdrop for an à la carte with its roots in Italian cooking, daily specials posted on the blackboard, and well-prepared fresh fish of the day.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8397;La Rebotica;Spain;Zafra;Botica 12, Zafra, 06300, Spain;38.4259321;-6.4201077;97;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Well located in the town’s historic quarter, La Rebotica occupies the interior of an old house that has managed to bring itself up to date while maintaining its welcoming rusticity. Its updated take on traditional cuisine, with a focus on Retinto beef as well as cod dishes, is well supported by a good selection of Ribera del Guadiana wines. Don’t miss the delicious “trilogy of Iberian meat (“presa”, sirloin and “secreto”)!;Air conditioning;[]
8398;Corral del Rey;Spain;Trujillo;Corral del Rey 2, Trujillo, 10200, Spain;39.4602826;-5.8809799;89;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Corral del Rey’s strong suits are its dishes roasted in the oven and red meats cooked on the grill, although its tasting menu is also a triumph! Idyllic terrace adjoining Trujillo’s magnificent Plaza Mayor!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8399;Sant Miquel;Spain;Vallromanes;Plaza de l'Església 12, Vallromanes, 08188, Spain;41.531511;2.2982296;91;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant with two dining rooms plus a private space in the wine cellar. It offers a choice between a traditional à la carte and two set menus, one daily (available on weekdays) and a second tasting option. Superb choice of wines.;Air conditioning;[]
8400;ReComiendo;Spain;Córdoba;Mirto 7, Córdoba, 14012, Spain;37.9078637;-4.7759612;18;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Fun, flavour, strong technique and time-honoured memories are to the fore here, coupled with the philosophy of chef Periko Ortega, who adds power to every dish. Three tasting menus, each with a wine-pairing option.;Air conditioning;[]
8401;China Crown;Spain;Madrid;Don Ramón de la Cruz 6, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4292207;-3.6863868;72;true;true;Chinese;An elegant restaurant with a decor inspired by the Far East, run by siblings María Li Bao and Felipe Bao, which stands out equally for its high-quality cuisine and its location in the busiest commercial section of the city’s Salamanca district. Here, the team recreates the flavours of Imperial China, including mouthwatering “bao” buns and dim sum, alongside Yuxiang-style Chinese aubergines, spicy diced chicken with chilli and cashews in a Sichuan sauce, plus the restaurant’s signature dish, the exquisite lacquered Peking duck. The extensive à la carte is complemented by a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8402;Barracuda MX;Spain;Madrid;Valenzuela 7, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4188471;-3.6894428;68;true;true;Mexican;A casual and informal restaurant that showcases cuisine from Mexico’s Pacific coast, albeit with a lighter touch and a focus on fish and seafood. Enticing cocktail menu!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8403;Godai;Spain;Ciutadella de Menorca;Vía de Circunvalación, Ciutadella de Menorca, 07769, Spain;39.9276811;3.8336436;34;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Located within the Suites del Lago hotel (Lago Resort Menorca), where award-winning chef Julián Mármol conjures up exquisite Japanese-Menorcan cuisine. The terrace and views of the marina add to its appeal.;Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
8404;Palodú;Spain;Malaga;Sebastián Souvirón 7-9, Malaga, 29005, Spain;36.719137;-4.4241615;89;false;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;One of those restaurants you’ll love visiting thanks to its constant desire to improve, which resulted in the change of location to the centre of Málaga. The couple in charge (Cristina and Diego), helped by the continual support of all the family, have used the initials of their first names to come up with the concept of “Dual Cuisine”. Their cooking is focused on two tasting menus called Alcazul and Palodú, both with a wine-pairing option. The intensely flavoured “sequence” of “red mullet - gazpachuelo – potato” served together is particularly recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8405;La Maruca - Castellana;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana 212, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4638133;-3.6886987;17;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with the same name as its older sibling in Calle Velázquez, although this one is located along an elegant section of the Castellana avenue! This spacious eatery is decorated in pleasant white tones and boasts two terraces (a smaller one by the entrance, and a second, much larger internal one designed in the style of a garden). The essence of the cooking here is rooted in tradition with a nod to Santander, the culinary DNA of the Cantabria region and, in particular, a desire to bring the authentic flavours of the sea to the Spanish capital. We highly recommend the fish soup, served two ways and teeming with flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8406;Estimar Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Marqués de Cubas 18, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4162311;-3.6959358;36;true;false;Seafood;The essence of the sea in the heart of the Spanish capital! Here, top-quality products take centre stage, with superbly prepared fish and seafood that can’t be bettered.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8407;Estrella;Spain;Rupit;Plaza Bisbe Font 1, Rupit, 08569, Spain;42.0241437;2.464958;64;false;false;Catalan;An attractive family-run inn founded in 1946, occupying a stone building in this picturesque medieval village. Choose between a concise à la carte of traditional Catalan dishes and two fixed-price menus, accompanied by an extensive wine list. The attractive guestrooms are an added bonus!;Air conditioning;[]
8408;Noi;Spain;Madrid;Recoletos 6, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.422122;-3.69075;95;true;false;Italian;In Italian, “noi” means “we”, a word that speaks of the importance of teamwork and the idea of a joint project. The young chef, who hails from Puglia (the region occupying the heel of the “boot” in the very south of Italy), proudly showcases a contemporary version of his homeland’s traditional cuisine, moving slightly away from the more commonplace Italian dishes and pizzas to offer a mouthwatering journey across the regions of Italy. As an added bonus, its elegant, meticulous interior recreates the “Italian pop” style of the 70s! Here, they normally use the “green” (verde) room for à la carte dining and the “Rioja” room for the tasting menu (“De sur a norte” (From South to North), featuring dishes such as tuna tonnato, parmigiana, caponata siciliana, linguine alle vongole etc).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8409;Beldade;Spain;Tui;Remesal 9, Tui, 36713, Spain;42.0609697;-8.6781608;80;true;false;Contemporary;A particularly charming stone-built house outside the centre of Tui, where it is surrounded by vineyards and located just a few metres from the Adega Ramesal winery. The contemporary interior covers two floors, with a more bistro-style ambience downstairs and a more formal set-up upstairs, the latter featuring an open-view kitchen. On the à la carte you’ll find contemporary cooking with a focus on seasonal ingredients, with centre stage given to fish purchased from the local auction house and seafood from the town of O Grove. This is complemented by two set menus (Miúdo and Beldade).;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8410;La Milla;Spain;Marbella;Urbanización de los Verdiales, Marbella, 29604, Spain;36.5021795;-4.9218621;85;false;false;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;Located on the sand at the heart of the Playa de los Nagüeles, this former “chiringuito” (beach bar) has been successfully brought up to date to add a stylish decor to its unbeatable setting. Here, you can enjoy traditional Mediterranean cuisine that flies the flag for fish and seafood of the highest quality and which is enhanced by modern touches yet without losing its Andalucian flavour. Although the dining room boasts stunning views, La Milla also features two pleasant terraces. The menu includes a selection of charcoal-grilled dishes, as well as appetising options such as the brioche of white prawns with lemon and the creamy rice with scarlet shrimp.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8411;Cal Marquès;Spain;Camprodon;Catalunya 11, Camprodon, 17867, Spain;42.3110098;2.3654384;80;true;true;Catalan;Cal Marquès is located in the historic centre of Camprodon, one of the prettiest towns in the Ripollès area. Here, within the stone walls of an imposing building that was once owned by the Marquis of Alfarràs, choose from a traditionally inspired À la carte in tune with its surroundings, as well as excellent set menus. Dishes featuring Ripollès lamb reared on the family farm are the undoubted stars of the show.;Air conditioning;[]
8412;Kyoshi Las Cortes;Spain;Madrid;San Agustín 3, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4152509;-3.6967894;54;true;true;Japanese;In the lobby of the Double Tree by Hilton Prado hotel in the heart of the Las Letras district. Honest Japanese cuisine bearing the quality hallmark of the Ricardo Sanz group.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8413;Palacio Ico;Spain;Teguise;El Rayo 2, Teguise, 35530, Spain;29.0606472;-13.5605882;28;false;true;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant with plenty of charm, a focus on select ingredients, and a chef at the helm who, despite his young age, has plenty of experience behind him. Palacio Ico occupies the hotel of the same name in a restored property that still showcases the beauty of the archipelago’s architecture. The contemporary Canary Island-inspired cuisine prides itself on the quality of its ingredients such as smoked salmon from Uga, gambas and Carabinero prawns from La Santa, octopus from Lanzarote, the famous black Canarian pig, and local cherne fish etc. Choose between two tasting menus (one short, one long) that evolve with the seasons and offer a wine pairing option. The well-stocked wine cellar is enhanced by an exclusive selection of champagnes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8414;L'Eixida;Spain;Peratallada;Forn 4, Peratallada, 17113, Spain;41.9771592;3.0892078;86;true;false;Fusion, Mediterranean Cuisine;If you’d like to eat in one of the prettiest villages in the Baix Empordà area with delightful medieval alleyways that give Peratallada its character, you’ll fall in love with this small restaurant with a patio (Eixida translates as ‘exit’ in Catalan). The first thing that is asked of guests is that they arrive with an open mind, given L'Eixida’s focus on fusion cuisine that uses the best local ingredients yet takes the palate on a journey across different countries in Asia and South America. The à la carte, comprising numerous starters and a section dedicated to innovative rice dishes, is complemented by two tasting menus (Menú del Arroz and Torre de las Horas).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8415;Gloria;Spain;Oviedo;Cervantes 24, Oviedo, 33004, Spain;43.3637559;-5.856592;84;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Asian Influences;An informal restaurant where Manzano siblings Esther and Nacho showcase traditional cuisine perfect for sharing, including delicious tapas, “raciones”, a few contemporary dishes, plus two menus (one daily option, including wine, that is available for lunch midweek, and a second more extensive menu named after the restaurant, featuring Gloria’s signature dishes).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8416;Casa Fermín;Spain;Oviedo;San Francisco 8, Oviedo, 33003, Spain;43.3619786;-5.8467476;85;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Here, options include a classic-traditional à la carte that makes full use of top-quality ingredients, a tasting menu, plus an impressive wine list. Make sure you try the CasadiellesFermín, the restaurant’s reinvented signature dessert!;Air conditioning;[]
8417;Le Bistró by El Conjuro;Spain;Granada;Martínez Campos 8, Granada, 18005, Spain;37.1707629;-3.6032515;81;false;false;Contemporary;A relaxed, informal and unpretentious bistro serving dishes that steer clear of traditional interpretation but enjoy toying with plentiful flavours.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8418;BANCAL;Spain;Madrid;Serrano 95, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4382009;-3.6864911;92;true;true;Contemporary;A unique restaurant in every sense of the word, occupying the old Villa Thiebaut, an aristocratic property in the city’s embassy district that is now home to delightful dining rooms full of history (there’s also a more modern private space in what was once the chapel). The property is also home to the MOM Culinary Institute and has its own small city garden. The restaurant’s identity and cooking, under the baton of chef Miguel Vidal, have their focus on contemporary cuisine that always champions the best seasonal ingredients and classic techniques. These are showcased in outstanding dishes such as the prawn croquettes “al ajillo” with a prawn tartare. On the table you’ll also find a glass dome under which fresh sourdough is presented before being taken to the oven to be baked!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8419;Sabores;Spain;Logrono;Plaza del Mercado 2, Logrono, 26001, Spain;42.4665543;-2.4462727;24;false;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with a young, relaxed feel run by two chefs. The delicious contemporary cuisine on offer here is meticulously presented and based around ingredients from the Rioja, with the occasional nod to elsewhere.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8420;L'Alkimista;Spain;Reus;Carnisseries Velles 3, Reus, 43201, Spain;41.1552234;1.1095153;58;true;true;Fusion, Contemporary;L'Alkimista occupies a two-storey property along a pedestrian street in the centre of town that is impressive for its contemporary decor and relaxed ambience. Here, young owner-chef Pola Hany William creates cuisine that constantly blends influences from other cultures, but with its roots in the Mediterranean and the use of Spanish ingredients (he is a particular fan of Rubia Gallega beef and red tuna). His dishes are full of different textures, aromas and flavours that he combines with great skill, accompanied by a strong focus on presentation. The à la carte is complemented by two tasting menus (Phi and Omega) plus a lunchtime menu (Kappa) that always includes a savoury rice dish.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8421;Kuoco;Spain;Madrid;San Bartolomé 14, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4218155;-3.6984647;79;true;true;Fusion;A relaxed, bold and elegantly informal restaurant where the young Venezuelans in charge, Rafa and Andrés, offer a concise yet varied à la carte that is a fusion of cuisines from across the globe (they also have an enticing tasting menu called 360Taste). As a result, you’ll find intense flavours and constant references to Latin American (in particular Mexican) and Asian ingredients, with a special focus on different levels of spiciness. Make sure you order the croquettes, the Peking duck and the delicious chilli crab.;Air conditioning;[]
8422;Casa Mortero;Spain;Madrid;Zorrilla 9, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.416737;-3.6974694;72;false;false;Creative;Located behind the parliament building (Congreso de los Diputados), Casa Montero’s philosophy can be summed up by the phrase “There is virtue in simplicity”. In this restaurant, with its minimalist-industrial decor dominated by simple features such as ceramics and terracotta, the cuisine is full of traditional soul accompanied by the occasional dash of creativity. The concise à la carte features medias raciones, a handful of specials, as well as some superb appetisers (creamy croquettes, crispy bacon “torreznos” etc), mouthwatering stews and a selection of dishes cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning;[]
8423;Tamboril;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Pescadería 2, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20003, Spain;43.3235556;-1.9844525;35;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the heart of the old town, Tamboril is run by the family that owns the legendary Ganbara. The bar is teeming with traditional pintxos, with a special mention for the mushrooms!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8424;Jondal;Spain;Porroig;Cala Jondal, Porroig, 07830, Spain;38.8682622;1.3175975;64;true;false;Seafood;Located in the cove of the same name and popular with a “VIP” clientele, Jondal occupies a bucolic Ibiza-style building where Rafa Zafra, a chef with a passion for the sea, is at the helm. Outstanding fish and seafood are, understandably, the stars of the show here, including an impressive selection of dishes built around caviar and created using a variety of different techniques (grilled, raw, fried, cured, salted etc). Many customers come here for the views, so we recommend booking as far in advance as possible – in summer it is not easy securing a table here.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8425;Trasteo;Spain;Zahara de los Atunes;María Luisa 24, Zahara de los Atunes, 11393, Spain;36.1368452;-5.8454413;16;false;true;Contemporary;A gastro-bar with a pleasant and informal feel enhanced by the decor of unusual recycled objects and furniture! The well-prepared cuisine here is contemporary in style, fresh and light and served in full and half portions. We recommend the mini-Vietnamese-style shrimp omelettes and the spicy “caldereta” stew with white prawns and egg.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8426;Ferran Cerro;Spain;Reus;Plaça del Castell 2, Reus, 43201, Spain;41.1546928;1.1094109;58;true;false;Creative, Traditional Cuisine;If you’ve never tried Steak Tartare-Carpaccio or red tomato ceviche, this is one of the places to be guided and pleasantly surprised by the chef, a native of Reus, who has honed his skills in several prestigious restaurants before setting up on his own here. His creative, contemporary cuisine is highlighted on an à la carte (including a small selection of rice dishes) and several set menus that are similar in style and are named after clothing sizes (S, M and L).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8427;Normal;Spain;Girona;Plaça de l'Oli 1, Girona, 17004, Spain;41.984698;2.825606;84;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This, the more informal of the Roca brothers’ restaurants, offers artisanal cuisine with its roots in the land and top-quality products. The menu here is centred on traditional Catalan recipes, including delicious stews.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8428;Goya Gallery;Spain;Valencia;Burriana 3, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.464247;-0.3688979;25;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Rice Dishes;Occupying a legendary setting in the city (the Mostra de València-Cinema film festival was first established here), this business began life as a bar in 1950. It offers a traditional Mediterranean à la carte featuring an impressive choice of starters (don’t pass up the croquettes or the cuttlefish with mayonnaise) and a superb selection of rice dishes – the house speciality. We strongly recommend booking ahead as the Goya Gallery has a loyal local following.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8429;Amós;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana 22, Madrid, 28046, Spain;40.4301031;-3.6877412;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;The Cantabrian flavours of award-winning chef Jesús Sánchez in the Spanish capital. Choose between the Memoria menu (including dishes chosen from the à la carte) and another tasting-style option called Esencia.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8430;Tradevo Centro;Spain;Seville;Cuesta del Rosario 15, Seville, 41004, Spain;37.3899908;-5.9914213;93;false;false;Andalusian, Farm to table;A modern, lively restaurant on one of the historic centre’s myriad small squares. The enticing display cabinet of different types of fresh fish, hake roe, prawns, squid etc, is a highlight, most of which is priced by weight. Traditionally based cuisine with a contemporary touch and excellent daily specials.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8431;Besta;Spain;Barcelona;Aribau 106, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3903956;2.1567498;47;true;false;Farm to table, Contemporary;A casual neo-bistro run by two chefs who have brought together the cooking of their respective regions, namely Galicia and Catalunya. The market-inspired menu here is influenced by both the Atlantic and the Mediterranean.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8432;La Fortaleza;Spain;Cala Blava;Carretera d'Enderrocat, Cala Blava, 07609, Spain;39.4762857;2.7245999;52;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An elegant, unique and very special restaurant that is a must on the island. It offers two creative menus that showcase the best of Mallorcan cuisine accompanied by superb views from the rooftop terrace in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8434;Uma;Spain;Barcelona;Mallorca 275, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3949332;2.1639358;63;false;false;Creative;This restaurant with an informal yet elegant ambience that is perfect for couples takes its name from the Swahili word for “fork”. In the completely open kitchen, the focus is on a gastronomic experience that is timed to the second, given that every guest ordering the surprise menu starts their meal at exactly the same time.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8435;Pilar Akaneya;Spain;Madrid;Espronceda 33, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4405953;-3.6948655;49;false;false;Japanese Steakhouse;The specific characteristics of this restaurant (the first Sumibiyaki barbecue-style eatery in Madrid) include cooking on traditonal Japanese grills, the sourcing of certified Kobe beef, and the exclusive use of Kishū Binchōtan charcoal from Wakayama. Some of its menus include the famous Crown melon from Fukuroi.;Air conditioning;[]
8436;Basque Eneko;Spain;Bilbao;Gran Vía Don Diego López de Haro 4, Bilbao, 48001, Spain;43.261537;-2.9276172;56;false;true;Basque;In this modern restaurant that stands out for its terrace within the Radisson Collection Gran Vía Bilbao hotel, chef Eneko Atxa champions a concept that offers a fusion between Basque and Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8437;El Roser 2;Spain;L'Escala;Passeig Lluís Albert 1, L'Escala, 17130, Spain;42.1263112;3.1363913;76;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a stellar location on the tip of L'Escala’s old quarter, hence the splendid views of the sea and bay from most of its tables. The maritime-inspired à la carte is extensive, varied and bold and features a selection of traditional dishes, fish and seafood for sharing, plus several enticing menus (De Temporada, Degustación and Gran Mariscada).;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8438;Fismuler;Spain;Madrid;Sagasta 29, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.42802;-3.69715;37;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;Gastronomy meets interior design in this restaurant with an austere retro-industrial feel. Despite this, the service and ambience is relaxed, with a menu that features pleasantly updated traditional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8439;Oliva;Spain;Nerja;Plaza de España 2, Nerja, 29780, Spain;36.7463425;-3.8777531;57;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;A bright and spacious restaurant in a superb location on the Plaza de España where it boasts a pleasant terrace. Mediterranean cuisine based around top-quality ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8440;Cal Travé;Spain;Solivella;Carretera d'Andorra 56, Solivella, 43412, Spain;41.4554958;1.1786472;28;false;false;Catalan, Grills;This long-established, popular restaurant is run by a family, all of whom are involved in the business. It is home to an inviting classic-contemporary-style dining room with a charming open grill and attractive decorative detail on its walls, including old farming implements and a collection of antique clocks. The Catalan cuisine served here focuses on grilled dishes, such as cod and Nebraska entrecôte steak, plus delicious home-made desserts and a selection of wines from Sanstravé, the restaurant’s own wine bodega. They even make their own bread!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8441;SeBE;Spain;Costa Teguise;Avenida de las Islas Canarias 12, Costa Teguise, 35508, Spain;29.0000707;-13.4897444;58;false;true;Rice Dishes, Seafood;A must for visitors to Lanzarote! The interior, which reflects the colours and iconic architecture of the island, provides the backdrop for superb fish and seafood, although Santi’s delicious and intense rice dishes also take centre stage. Make sure you sample the spectacular prawns from La Santa!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8442;La Mesa de Conus;Spain;Vigo;San Roque 3, Vigo, 36200, Spain;42.2265112;-8.7117997;18;true;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;Attractive, modern and different, and designed for just 12 people to dine at the bar, hence our strong recommendation to book ahead. Chef Víctor Conus conjures up contemporary cooking with a focus on quality ingredients, the seasons and his own personal experiences. This is showcased on a single surprise tasting menu built around the best Galician ingredients available daily albeit with a nod to his Andalucian roots. Produce sourced from his kitchen garden in Nigrán are always present (including delicious Loba beans) as are pork-based products (charcuterie, as well as cuts such as “abanico”, “pluma” and “secreto”), given that his family runs the Jamones Doña Lola company in the town of Bollullos Par del Condado, in Huelva province). They always start with a plate of Paleta Ibérica Edición Especial “La Consentida” ham and the famous “de la Yaya” croquettes”!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8443;Doppelgänger Bar;Spain;Madrid;Santa Isabel 5, Madrid, 28012, Spain;40.4114479;-3.6987913;21;false;false;Fusion;A highly informal gourmet bar inside the Antón Martín market offering mouthwatering fusion cuisine with a nod to the Iberian Peninsula, Asia and South America.;;[]
8444;Leña Marbella;Spain;Marbella;Boulevard Príncipe Alfonso von Hohenlohe, Marbella, 29600, Spain;36.5043569;-4.9252752;73;false;false;Meats and Grills, Grills;Josper and charcoal grills, different cuts of matured meat and yakipincho skewers (an adaptation of Japanese yakitori) combine with an international touch and the signature of chef Dani García. In this striking steakhouse, which has twin outposts in Madrid and Dubai, the different cuts of meat on the menu are the real stars of the show here, and include a burger called “The burger that made it all make sense”, a version of the dish that he served in 2019 in his three-star Michelin restaurant. The option for guests to choose their own knife adds a unique touch.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8445;Kiki;Spain;Santa Cruz de Tenerife;Imeldo Serís 19, Santa Cruz de Tenerife, 38003, Spain;28.4658063;-16.2493841;77;true;false;Japanese, Fusion;To a backdrop of Japanese-inspired murals, attractive neon lighting, a sushi bar and an unusual cocktail bar, Kiki serves Japanese-inspired cuisine that showcases the best seasonal ingredients from the Canary Islands. Choose from two à la cartes (one traditional, the other fusion) and two tasting menus (one short, the second a longer menu named after the restaurant). Make sure you try some of the nigiris, such as the Akami-Crunchy nigiri (crunchy rice with spicy tuna tartare and serrano peppers).;Air conditioning;[]
8446;Txitxardin;Spain;Lasarte - Oria;Oria Etorbidea 12, Lasarte - Oria, 20160, Spain;43.2509455;-2.0200677;80;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located in a park, Txitxardin is part of a large-scale project and is just one of the chef’s restaurants in the so-called Casa Humada, offering traditional cuisine based around top-quality products.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8447;Quimera;Spain;La Savina;Avinguda de la Mediterrània 24, La Savina, 07870, Spain;38.7311303;1.4169904;65;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Watching the sun set as its dips below the surface of the sea is a privilege enjoyed almost daily on the terrace at Quimera. In this pleasant and attractive restaurant beneath the Hostal La Savina, enjoy contemporary Mediterranean cuisine that is both delicate and consistent and which also flies the flag for the island’s sustainability and its native ingredients. This explains the focus on produce from La Savina’s own kitchen garden, as well as superb fish from the island’s waters, and locally sourced meat. The perfect dinner venue!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
8448;Sutan;Spain;Hondarribia;Jaitzubia Auzoa 266, Hondarribia, 20280, Spain;43.3476117;-1.8320623;75;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Sutan reflects the partnership between the Txapartegi brothers and a “txakoli” wine bodega (Hiruzta). Traditional cooking with a contemporary touch, specialising in fish and meat cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8449;La Tajada;Spain;Madrid;Ramón de Santillán 15, Madrid, 28016, Spain;40.4561084;-3.6806638;50;true;false;Contemporary;If you were a fan of the erstwhile Desencaja Bistro you’re in luck as its entire team has made the switch to this simple, industrial-style yet intimate restaurant. The cooking here is centred around a traditionally based à la carte (including an array of savoury rice dishes) which has been brought pleasantly up to date and is complemented by several set menus: a value-for-money daily option (El Rayo Verde) available lunchtime Monday to Friday, and a second more extensive menu entitled Viaje a la Luna (Journey to the Moon). We were particularly attracted to the chocolate dessert (six different options with cacao as the common denominator)!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8450;Espacio Montoro;Spain;Alacant;Avenida de la Albufereta 13, Alacant, 03016, Spain;38.365041;-0.4595445;25;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;If you’re looking for something truly out of the ordinary, this restaurant in Alicante is definitely the place to head for, but make sure you book ahead. In this unique space, the dining experience is akin to a game that moves from one space to the next (Black Tech, Hi Line, Cocoon Lab and Geoda Verde), each of which features highly personalised decor and provides a backdrop of different visual effects and even specific aromas for your fine-dining experience. Chef Pablo Montoro’s fun and entertaining cuisine, including creative, travel-inspired dishes that showcase the Mediterranean, is focused around three tasting menus: Espacio, Experiencia and Sentidos. Other interesting aspects include the explanation of ingredients and their provenance by the chefs themselves, as well as an impressive choice of cocktails.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8451;Al Marge;Spain;Badalona;Lleó 79, Badalona, 08911, Spain;41.4481959;2.2480286;25;true;false;Farm to table;An informal, centrally located restaurant on two floors, run by a highly professional couple. The traditional cuisine with a contemporary touch includes several dishes perfect for sharing.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8452;TA-KUMI;Spain;Malaga;Mundo Nuevo 4, Malaga, 29012, Spain;36.7228306;-4.4164708;27;false;false;Japanese;A Japanese restaurant with a pleasant decor where the cuisine of its homeland is featured on an à la carte and several enticing set menus. In fine weather, make sure you book a table on the terrace with its views of the Alcazaba!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
8453;Mint;Spain;Granollers;Sant Josep 10, Granollers, 08401, Spain;41.6076417;2.2844967;38;true;false;Contemporary;A restaurant with a pleasant contemporary decor where the name provides a strong hint of the cuisine on offer – fresh, updated Mediterranean cooking with its roots in Catalan gastronomy. Good set menus!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
8454;Les Corones;Spain;L'Estartit;Avenida Roma 50, L'Estartit, 17258, Spain;42.0514828;3.195517;34;true;true;Grills;This contemporary - style restaurant has close links with the Basque port of Getaria, hence the importance of top - quality products. The menu here specialises in grilled meats.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8455;Arohaz;Spain;Zahora;Carril del Pozo 25, Zahora, 11159, Spain;36.2006934;-6.0359501;29;true;false;Contemporary;A modern, minimalist-style restaurant located close to the beach which has turned its modest appearance into a real virtue. The focus here is on contemporary cuisine with traditional roots that ticks almost every box on its menu (fish and traditionally caught tuna, Spanish meat, rice dishes etc) and which makes use of the very best ingredients from Cádiz province along with touches of fusion influence. The traditional, country-style croquettes (either ham, or cheese and spinach) are a must, while the attractive guestrooms are an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8456;Celia Jiménez;Spain;Córdoba;Escritora María Goyri, Córdoba, 14005, Spain;37.88117;-4.8025284;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is located in Andalucia’s largest sports complex. The chef – widely respected in the world of gastronomy – conjures up Andalucian cuisine brought up - to - date with contemporary cooking techniques and presentation.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8457;Allegar;Spain;Briones;Concepción 37, Briones, 26330, Spain;42.54442;-2.786;83;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Briones is one of Spain’s most beautiful medieval villages and is also home to the superb Vivanco bodega- museum. Named after a local Rioja word that means “to scrape the plate clean”, “allegar” is the perfect way to define the approach to food at this restaurant inside the Santa María Briones hotel, where the culinary focus is on an updated take on Rioja cooking, featuring intense flavours and even the occasional hint of trompe-l’oeil. The restaurant is also home to an old and typical wine cellar, known locally as a “calado”.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8458;Nunuka;Spain;Madrid;Libertad 13, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4209098;-3.6974719;94;false;false;International;If you’re not familiar with Georgian cuisine, this attractive family-style restaurant in the Chueca district of the city is a great place to discover the country’s most iconic dishes and for your first contact with its delicious flavours. Don’t miss the typical Khachapuri bread, filled with cheese, or the traditional Khinkali.;Air conditioning;[]
8459;Omeraki;Spain;Madrid;Duque de Sesto 27, Madrid, 28009, Spain;40.422488;-3.6752797;63;true;true;Fusion, Contemporary;This restaurant occupying a former garage boasts a unique layout that includes access via a corridor lined by bookcases of cookery books, a bright and spacious dining room featuring a host of designer detail, and two kitchens (one a striking open kitchen in the centre of the room, and a second enclosed space that is still visible to diners). The cuisine here bears the strong hallmark of experienced celebrity chef Alberto Chicote, whose constantly evolving contemporary cuisine, showcased on three menus (Express, Festival and Homenaje), is based around Spanish ingredients and fusion dishes with a Far Eastern touch.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8460;Mirador de Ulía;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Paseo de Ulía 193, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20013, Spain;43.3280079;-1.965735;70;true;false;Creative;A special restaurant, particularly given its outstanding views of the city and Zurriola beach that will definitely grab your attention. Located at the top of Monte Ulía, it is run by chef Rubén Trincado, the third generation of the family, who has his own style yet with a culinary legacy rooted in tradition. His creatively inspired cuisine plays with native Guipúzcoa ingredients such as hake, but also focuses on dishes from the world’s “blue zones” where people live longer than anywhere else on the planet. He works with just two tasting menus: Vínculo (vegetarian) and Arraigo, both with a wine-pairing option.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8461;Mar Mía;Spain;Madrid;Plaza de Isabel II 7, Madrid, 28013, Spain;40.4183714;-3.7090518;23;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Located opposite the Teatro Real (in the Ocean Drive Madrid hotel), Mar Mía views itself as an “urban chiringuito” beach restaurant where everything revolves around the Mediterranean. The varied menu features plenty of options (recipes prepared raw, salted, marinated and with caviar, alongside preserves, tapas and rice and grilled dishes). Make sure you try the “gilda MarMía” pintxo and, for dessert, the most delicate of apple tarts! The restaurant also boats an internal terrace teeming with greenery.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8462;Hamarratz;Spain;Zumaia;Artadi Auzoa, Zumaia, 20750, Spain;43.2889633;-2.2403528;71;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A welcoming restaurant with a strong focus on quality ingredients that is most clearly evident in its choice of grilled dishes. Hamarratz has its own vegetable garden next to the restaurant and a grill that only uses natural wood.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8463;Sensato;Spain;Barcelona;Septimania 36, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.4051535;2.1467132;85;false;true;Japanese;Sensato is a good choice for an Omakase dining experience while seated at a traditional Japanese counter. This small, minimalist restaurant, located in an elevated section of Barcelona, is run by a pair of chefs who combine local ingredients with Japanese-style techniques and preparation which they demonstrate in front of just six guests, in so doing showcasing their mastery with the knife. The menu includes a good selection of sashimi, nigiri, gunkan, temaki etc, which alternate with hot dishes such as black cod and miso soup. We recommend booking via WhatsApp.;Air conditioning;[]
8464;Saroa;Spain;Lleida;Torres de Sanui 12, Lleida, 25006, Spain;41.6177436;0.6192739;23;false;false;Contemporary;Contemporary, yet traditionally inspired cooking in the centre of Lleida. Excitement, desire and a youthful approach typify the couple that run Saroa, with Salvador creating everything savoury and Aroa in charge of desserts.;Air conditioning;[]
8465;Casa Garras;Spain;Valle de Carranza;Barrio Concha 6, Valle de Carranza, 48891, Spain;43.2249723;-3.3602918;42;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A third-generation family-run restaurant offering guests updated traditional cuisine with a gourmet touch, including meat from nearby Karrantza, fish from the Cantabrian Sea and Txakoli wine from its own vineyard.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8466;Hábitat Cigüeña Negra;Spain;Valverde del Fresno;Carretera EX-205, Km. 24, Valverde del Fresno, 10890, Spain;40.1948649;-6.8822564;68;true;true;Meats and Grills, Regional European;This rural hotel for adults only shares the beauty of the Sierra de Gata with its guests. Taking its name from the black stork, a migratory bird which nests in several locations on an estate with over 220ha of holm oak and olive groves, it also features a gourmet boutique next to the bar’s lounge area, an organic olive oil mill and a hammam. In its asador-style restaurant, featuring a semi open-view kitchen and large windows through which guests can gaze out at its surrounding pastures, choose from a regionally inspired à la carte strong on grilled meats, especially those it rears itself, including goat, Iberian pork and RetWagyu beef (a cross between Retinto and Wagyu).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8467;Isa;Spain;Madrid;Sevilla 3, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4170768;-3.7003228;58;true;true;Asian Influences;Located on the first floor of the luxury Four Seasons Hotel Madrid, this eclectic restaurant serves sophisticated fusion-style cuisine to an elegant and exotic backdrop, where outstanding and highly refined Asian-influenced street food is to the fore. Superb selection of cocktails, plus a live DJ providing the background soundtrack.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8469;Los Berengueles;Spain;Córdoba;Conde de Torres Cabrera 7, Córdoba, 14001, Spain;37.8865264;-4.7789007;20;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Los Berengueles occupies the former house of the Marquesa de Valdeloro. It is a building with solid Andalucian roots as witnessed by its azulejo decoration and timeless beauty. Traditional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8470;Casamar;Spain;Llafranc;Nero 3, Llafranc, 17211, Spain;41.892944;3.192439;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Part of the Hotel Casamar, this family-run property which has been passed down from the parents to their children, boasts an elevated location with fine views of the beach. The focus of chef Quim Casellas is on traditional and Mediterranean cuisine that skilfully incorporates innovative touches and adds flavours from the local surroundings to his recipes. The à la carte, which includes a special section of rice dishes as well as other enticing options such as white asparagus with a creamy hollandaise sauce, aged pork rib, and puffed rice and caviar, is complemented by two menus (Punta d'en Blanc and Degustación).;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8471;Arbequina;Spain;Córdoba;Ramírez de las Casas Deza 10-12, Córdoba, 14001, Spain;37.8873746;-4.7774208;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;Located within the walls of the Palacio del Bailío hotel, featuring a patio where you can dine above Roman remains! The bold fusion menu also incorporates an array of typical taberna-style dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8472;L'Atelier Robuchon;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana, 12, Madrid, 28046, Spain;40.427985;-3.6892894;28;false;true;Modern French;Whether you’re in Shanghai, Tokyo, Paris, Geneva, Dubai or Miami, every L'Atelier Robuchon restaurant around the world has the same aim: to perpetuate the culinary legacy of the late Joël Robuchon. This modern restaurant on the first floor of the Robuchon Madrid (a multi-faceted space where the “bar” concept takes centre stage and which includes other dining formats such as L'Ambassade and Le Speakeasy), follows the same aesthetic lines as its “siblings”, coupled with an informal ambience with a touch of luxury, plus a large open kitchen in the middle of the dining room. Here, French haute cuisine with touches of modernity is to the fore, yet without neglecting classic Spanish dishes. One dish that will remain imprinted on the memory is the so-called “Imperial Caviar”, which impressed us with its flavour and its exquisite presentation, which was akin to a work of art!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
8473;VIVO Gourmet;Spain;Almería;Marín 14, Almería, 04001, Spain;36.84104;-2.46677;43;false;true;Meats and Grills, Traditional Cuisine;Located in La Vega de Acá, a residential district that continues to expand, VIVO Gourmet features a modern terrace, a bar area where guests can also buy gourmet products, plus a contemporary dining room. The up-to-date à la carte includes dishes with a nod to Peruvian fusion cuisine, but also features an impressive selection of excellent charcuterie from Extremadura, T-bone steaks and an enticing array of aged meats (Rubia Gallega, Frisona, Angus, Wagyu etc).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8474;Ibidem;Spain;Arnuero;Barrio Zoña 1 - Castillo de Siete Villas, Arnuero, 39193, Spain;43.4616069;-3.5414168;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Ibidem occupies a manor house with a somewhat surprising interior featuring an elegant dining room with a designer feel and decorated in shades of white. The cooking here is centred around a single surprise tasting menu with a focus on contemporary cuisine and meticulous presentation.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8475;Trèsde;Spain;Madrid;Cava Alta 17, Madrid, 28005, Spain;40.4121856;-3.7092188;28;false;true;Contemporary;Enjoy informal haute-cuisine in this French bistro-style eatery in the traditional La Latina district of the city. Trèsde is run with great enthusiasm and passion by three life-long friends (in charge of the kitchen, dining room and back office, respectively). The market-inspired menu, which favours vegetables grown in traditional “navazo” gardens found in coastal marshland areas, has revitalised the starter/main course/dessert concept, with a choice of dishes from a concise yet meticulously prepared list.;;[]
8476;Barra de José Álvarez;Spain;El Ejido;Bulevar 46, El Ejido, 04700, Spain;36.7709769;-2.8276097;46;true;false;Contemporary, Andalusian;A restaurant with its own distinct personality despite sharing its kitchen and wine cellar with its older sibling (La Costa). It features a bar area and several bare wood tables where you can choose from a varied array of contemporary dishes, some with a “media ración” option, all prepared with top-quality ingredients. Professional service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8477;ROM;Spain;Roses;Passeig Marítim 43, Roses, 17480, Spain;42.2644853;3.1614337;69;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A spacious two-storey restaurant with terraces, right on the seafront. Updated traditional cuisine is to the fore here, along with a small selection of rice dishes and a tasting menu which needs to be pre-booked.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8478;Vidocq;Spain;Sallent de Gállego;Avenida Huesca, Sallent de Gállego, 22640, Spain;42.7740701;-0.3606055;32;true;false;Contemporary, Fusion;Named after the Frenchman considered to be the world’s first private detective way back in the early 19C, Vidocq is a superb option for those who prefer not to venture too far from the nearby ski slopes. The contemporary, fusion-style cuisine here toys continually with flavour, incorporating interesting Asian nuances (particularly from Thai cooking) into typical Aragonese mountain recipes (the vast majority of its ingredients are sourced from small-scale local producers). A single seasonal set menu (The Sound of Silence) is the mainstay here, inviting guests on an evocative gastronomic journey though this region, with the chef explaining each of his dishes in person.;;[]
8479;El Romero;Spain;Mahon;Plaza de la Conquesta 5, Mahon, 07701, Spain;39.8895774;4.2651836;68;true;true;Farm to table;If you enjoy authentic market-inspired cuisine, this restaurant will definitely appeal to you. Located opposite the Santa María de Mahón church and run by a couple of Italian origin who fell in love with the island, it showcases recipes that are strongly based around Menorcan ingredients which they buy directly from fishing boats and local farms. However, you’ll also find nods to their homeland, including “passatelli”, a typical recipe from Emilia Romagna, which follows the recipe of the chef’s mother (with cheese from the island used instead of parmesan). Choose between several menus: Mar de la Isla, Mar de la Isla Plus, Huerta Gourmet and Mediodía Light. Gluten-free cooking that is suitable for coeliacs.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8480;Método;Spain;Teruel;Francisco Piquer 6, Teruel, 44001, Spain;40.3443143;-1.1071582;16;false;false;Contemporary;In this modern restaurant, located along a pedestrian street in the centre of Teruel’s old quarter, you’ll find a choice of extensive menus that are unashamedly focused on two star ingredients from carefully selected suppliers, namely beef and tuna, and a strong emphasis on meticulous presentation.;Air conditioning;[]
8481;Sol i Neu;Andorra;Soldeu;Dels Vaquers, Soldeu, AD100, Andorra;42.57605;1.66795;95;true;true;Contemporary;A restaurant at the foot of the ski slopes with an ambience inspired by the mountains. The pleasing cuisine on offer, overseen by famous chef Francis Paniego, focuses on traditional cuisine brought up to date with contemporary textures and techniques.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8482;Ovillo;Spain;Madrid;Pantoja 8, Madrid, 28002, Spain;40.4474434;-3.6704219;80;false;false;Creative;A bright, spacious and attractive restaurant with an industrial decor in which the creative cuisine on offer and its philosophy of solidarity (the restaurant is part of the Fundación Raíces’ “Cooking with a Conscience” project that aims to involve vulnerable young people in working and social environments) have won many admirers. The cuisine on offer here is based around an à la carte and three tasting menus (Ovillo, Madeja and Tirar del Hilo), all of which impress with their extensive choice of mini appetisers. We particularly recommend the tripe with haricot beans, which won the world’s best tripe dish award in 2022.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8483;DIREKTE Boqueria;Spain;Barcelona;Les Cabres 13, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3815193;2.1720503;69;true;false;Fusion;A tiny and unusual eatery beneath the arcades of the famous Boquería market, offering a fusion of Catalan recipes, Mediterranean ingredients and Chinese and Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8484;Asador Concepción;Spain;Albacete;Concepción 5, Albacete, 02002, Spain;38.9943443;-1.8552397;35;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant that has passed from one generation to the next and now boasts a more up-to-date look with its glass-fronted wine cellar and two pleasant dining rooms. Its extensive menu showcases La Mancha recipes but also includes maritime-inspired dishes, tapas, filled rolls, select meats, plus an appetising array of soups and stews.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8485;Güeyu-Mar;Spain;La Vega;Playa de Vega 84, La Vega, 33560, Spain;43.4794314;-5.1342888;73;false;true;Grills, Seafood;This restaurant by the beach, with its somewhat unusual and huge kingfish adorning the façade, is an iconic eatery for lovers of grilled fish dishes that are both copious and of the highest quality. The concise à la carte, which is based around ingredients sourced daily from the fish auction, is complemented by an interesting array of homemade preserves which are served in the restaurant or can be purchased to take home. Advance booking is recommended here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8486;The View;Spain;Sant Josep de sa Talaia;Puig Delfin, Sant Josep de sa Talaia, 07830, Spain;38.9514283;1.2200914;72;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;If you’re looking for an elegant restaurant in a stunning location, The View will definitely fit the bill thanks to its clifftop setting boasting spectacular vistas of the azure Mediterranean and the islet of Es Vedrà, particularly at dusk, when the sun merges with the deep blue hue of the sea and dips gently below the horizon. Chef Óscar Salazar’s cuisine takes the form of well-executed dishes that are able to capture the full essence of the Mediterranean, starting from a strong commitment to local ingredients (red mullet, Ibizan red prawns, sustainably fished tuna, lamb from the island etc). Dining choices here include the à la carte, two tasting menus (a shorter version entitled Esencia del Mediterráneo, and a longer Sabor del Mediterráneo option) and, to cater to all tastes, the Experiencia Vegetariana. The live DJ in the chillout section is completely in keeping with the typical party vibe that is so typical of Ibiza.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
8487;Marmitón;Spain;Madrid;Aguas 6, Madrid, 28005, Spain;40.4107604;-3.7121297;67;false;true;Contemporary;An intimate restaurant with a rustic feel, run with great skill by two chefs. Classically inspired cuisine with a contemporary touch and a focus on strong, defined flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
8488;Bambú;Spain;Salamanca;Prior 4, Salamanca, 37002, Spain;40.9649398;-5.6651451;54;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A gastro-bar with a modern design just a few metres from the city’s iconic Plaza Mayor, where the traditional cuisine, including dishes cooked on the open grill, is reinterpreted from a more contemporary perspective.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8489;Daría;Spain;Santander;Bonifaz 19, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.4640456;-3.7971453;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city’s Puertochico district, Daría (named after the grandmother of owner-chef Nacho del Corral) shows the utmost respect for top-quality ingredients, offering guests what it calls “cocina de sabor”, extolling the full virtues of culinary flavours. In this compact space on two floors it comprises a bar area on the ground floor and a handful of tables upstairs. The contemporary cooking, which features a hint of fusion and an impressive tasting menu, is centred fully on organic products (vegetables from the Ontañón farm estate, and fresh fish from the Cantabrian Sea).;Air conditioning;[]
8490;Cuzeo;Spain;Zamora;Rúa de los Francos 6, Zamora, 49001, Spain;41.5020706;-5.7487157;35;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;This restaurant, located along a busy pedestrian street in Zamora’s old quarter and surrounded by the town’s emblematic Romanesque buildings, provides guests with the perfect opportunity to try local and regional dishes that showcase “Zamoran” ingredients (such as the delicious chickpeas from Fuentesaúco) and a strong focus on game (partridge, wild boar, venison etc, mostly sourced from the Sierra de la Culebra). The backdrop here is rustic-modern in feel, with several small dining rooms in which the updated traditional à la carte is complemented by an excellent tasting menu. Make sure you try the highly popular kimchi croquettes or the stewed rib of wild boar with sweet potato and pickles, which we particularly enjoyed.;Air conditioning;[]
8491;Tacande;Spain;Haría;Plaza del Castillo 5, Haría, 35520, Spain;29.146568;-13.4993787;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this pleasant restaurant along a pedestrianised street in the centre of Haría, the main focus is on a series of daily recommendations (an option we recommend) that complement the à la carte, with everything here based around seasonal ingredients. The updated take on Canary Island cuisine is highlighted via dishes such as the pork-based “cochino embarrado” (literally “muddy pig” in English), which showcases high-quality ingredients along with subtle hints of fusion.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8492;Yoko Barbate;Spain;Barbate;Avenida Virgen del Carmen 2, Barbate, 11160, Spain;36.1875311;-5.9264387;67;true;true;Japanese, Japanese Contemporary;A modern restaurant in which the cuisine comes as a pleasant surprise, combining Japanese and Mediterranean cooking with the very best products from the province of Cádiz. An open-view kitchen and enticing menus complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8493;Aitana;Spain;Aranda de Duero;San Gregorio 17, Aranda de Duero, 09400, Spain;41.670408;-3.6843474;79;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re visiting Aranda de Duero and its impressive network of underground wine cellars featuring over 4km of galleries, this centrally located restaurant could be a good option to revive your energy levels. Featuring a tapas section by the entrance and a dining room to the rear (the latter featuring a view of the wood-fired oven), Aitana has a reputation for its red meats and seasonal vegetables, although the menu also includes mouthwatering IGP Castilla y León baby lamb (prior ordering required). The à la carte is complemented by the Ribera set menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8494;Kea Basque Fine Food;Spain;Vitoria-Gasteiz;San Prudencio 21, Vitoria-Gasteiz, 01005, Spain;42.8440315;-2.67145;73;false;false;Basque;A small restaurant divided into two spaces: a taberna and a smart dining room. Traditional Basque cuisine designed for sharing that is simple yet delicious and based around locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
8495;La Cosmopolita;Spain;Malaga;José Denís Belgrano 3, Malaga, 29015, Spain;36.721867;-4.4199537;55;false;false;Farm to table;Situated in the heart of the old town, this restaurant is striking for its rustic and vintage-style decor. Fun, market-inspired cuisine centred on Andalucian ingredients with an exotic touch. Pleasant terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8496;Filandón;Spain;Madrid;Carretera Fuencarral-El Pardo, Madrid, 28049, Spain;40.504894;-3.716757;47;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re looking for a restaurant in which to escape the stresses of daily life, Filandón guarantees a thoroughly tranquil experience on the edge of El Pardo, in the heart of the countryside but just a few minutes from the centre of the Spanish capital. In its pleasant, rustically inspired dining rooms, one of which stands on the terrace, savour traditional cuisine where the focus is always on the best-possible ingredients, ranging from superb fish sourced daily from the Pescaderías Coruñesas company to select cuts of meat and delicious rice. Many of the dishes here are cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8497;Amar Barcelona;Spain;Barcelona;Gran Via de les Corts Catalanes 668, Barcelona, 08010, Spain;41.3913747;2.1714455;63;false;true;Contemporary, Catalan;The Palace Barcelona’s in-house restaurant, overseen by chef Rafa Zafra, has a very strong attachment to both the Mediterranean and the city. On the menu you’ll find excellent oysters and caviar, superb fish priced by weight, traditional Catalan recipes, as well as the hotel’s classic signature dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
8498;Veratus;Spain;Jarandilla de la Vera;Finca los Parrales, Jarandilla de la Vera, 10450, Spain;40.1264472;-5.6679985;28;false;false;Contemporary;A restaurant with a rustic ambience and a delightful setting next to the beautiful stone bridge spanning the river and facing the natural swimming pools that are always popular in summer. The young chef here showcases his contemporary cuisine, while continually aiming to champion local, seasonal inspired ingredients.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8499;A Mundiña;Spain;A Coruña;Real 77, A Coruña, 15003, Spain;43.36917;-8.40164;71;false;false;Galician;Despite its renovated new look, this restaurant continues to offer cuisine with a traditional feel. The star of the show here is undoubtedly the fresh fish from the nearby fish auctions in Laxe, Malpica, A Coruña etc.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8500;Dámaso;Spain;Valladolid;Carabela 1, Valladolid, 47009, Spain;41.6814359;-4.7498494;44;false;false;Farm to table;With his natural humility and technical expertise, chef Dámaso Vergara is the real epicentre of this restaurant, a feeling that comes to the fore when he sits down to curate a bespoke, market-inspired menu for you (including small-plate options). The setting is the tranquil La Galera country club on the outskirts of Valladolid, where the dining room overlooks the golf course’s 9th tee. Dámaso is particularly popular with a regular business clientele.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8501;Casa Pacheco;Spain;Vecinos;Avenida Peña de Francia 12, Vecinos, 37456, Spain;40.7781112;-5.8771176;44;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This legendary restaurant in the Campo Charro area, which has been in the hands of the same family since 1916, is indelibly linked with the world of bullfighting and the matador Julio Robles (who was a friend of its owners), hence the rustic decor themed around this tradition and featuring unique photos of this “torero” as well as some of his bullfighting attire. The chefs at the helm, Cristina Martín and Sara Cámara, showcase traditional cuisine teeming with Iberian charcuterie, meat (including aged meat options), stews (such as the Pardina lentils from La Armuña with dewlap and chorizo picadillo), and delicious game options in season (we particularly enjoyed the loin of venison that is macerated in its own jus).;Air conditioning;[]
8502;Agustina;Spain;Cazalla de la Sierra;Plaza del Concejo, Cazalla de la Sierra, 41370, Spain;37.9287869;-5.760252;61;true;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, the name of which pays homage to the owner’s mother, is one of the best dining options in the Sierra Norte de Sevilla, a region known for its wines and aniseed liqueurs. Run by a friendly couple, it occupies a typical whitewashed house featuring a bar, an attractive terrace, and a dining room on the first floor where guests can choose from a contemporary à la carte steeped in tradition. A good selection of tapas and daily specials is also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8503;Terrae;Spain;Port de Pollença;Verge del Carme 28, Port de Pollença, 07470, Spain;39.9056093;3.0815605;21;true;false;Creative, International;A restaurant with a sustainable ethos, where the menu changes almost daily depending on what’s available from the island’s small producers, with every dish free of chemicals and additives.;Terrace;[]
8504;Atelier Casa de Comidas;Spain;Granada;Sos del Rey Católico 7, Granada, 18006, Spain;37.1662098;-3.5960004;48;false;false;Contemporary;Located just a few metres from its former location but now with more space, this culinary “workshop” has a fresh, bright and neighbourly feel as well as an eclectic functionality that includes a completely open-view kitchen behind the serving station. Raúl Sierra, the highly enthusiastic chef at the helm, focuses on contemporary cuisine that continues to showcase Andalucian flavours and modern techniques with a nod to other countries and meticulous presentation. The à la carte, which features the restaurant’s classic dishes, is complemented by a tasting menu with a continual emphasis on seasonal products.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8505;Javier Montero;Spain;Ribadeo;As Barreiras 18, Ribadeo, 27700, Spain;43.5425643;-7.0407626;88;true;false;Contemporary;This restaurant is located on the outskirts of town, in a property that also operates as a hotel with a handful of pleasant guestrooms. It is run by a couple who are both professional and offer attentive service, with Tita in charge of the dining room and Javier running the kitchen. The contemporary-style cooking here is based around superb Galician ingredients and is showcased on a tasting menu entitled As Catedrais in tribute to the spectacular natural beach located a little over 10km away. The bread served at the restaurant is sourced every day from a family-run bakery.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8506;Sumac;Spain;Roses;Cap Norfeu 22, Roses, 17480, Spain;42.2603213;3.1806955;35;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;The culinary focus in this family-run restaurant, the name of which refers to a type of condiment commonly found in the Middle East, is on local, market-fresh ingredients. The chef, who has developed his skills working alongside culinary maestros such as the late Santi Santamaría, showcases his art on a classically focused à la carte with a modern touch, as well as an impressive set menu. Wagyu from the Empordà is also an option here.;Air conditioning;[]
8507;Pocavergonya;Spain;Girona;Plaza Poeta Marquina 2, Girona, 17002, Spain;41.98097;2.81855;17;true;false;Fusion, Farm to table;A contemporary restaurant that is keen to include diners in the entire creative process. The cuisine on offer here is centred around à la carte dining that occasionally surprises, and features enticing daily suggestions that combine local traditions and Asian influences. The chef, who normally works behind the Japanese-inspired counter, can often be seen in the dining room putting the finishing touches to dishes in front of guests. Make sure you order the sea cucumbers and teardrop peas when in season.;Air conditioning;[]
8508;Le Bistroman Atelier;Spain;Madrid;Amnistía 10, Madrid, 28013, Spain;40.4172148;-3.710909;41;false;true;French;Take your palate on a culinary voyage to France in this attractive bistro with an open-view kitchen at the entrance and a welcoming interior which will delight guests with its combination of classic and rustic decor. Enjoy authentic Gallic flavours on both the à la carte and the gastronomic tasting menu. When in season, don’t miss the delicious snails with a classic persillade!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8509;El Viejo Fogón;Spain;Majadahonda;San Andrés 14, Majadahonda, 28220, Spain;40.4688071;-3.8732519;81;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant has an intimate and rustic ambience and is run by a professional team which is constantly striving to innovate and to please its guests. Contemporary cuisine with touches of fusion on an à la carte (half plates are also available) and two menus, one a tasting option. We particularly recommended the delicious pulled pork brioche.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8510;El Vagón de Beni;Spain;Hoyo de Manzanares;San Macario 6, Hoyo de Manzanares, 28240, Spain;40.6230399;-3.90804;34;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Spanish;A unique restaurant occupying two train carriages in a setting reminiscent of an old railway station. Well - prepared contemporary cuisine. Delightful terrace on the platform.;Car park,Terrace;[]
8511;Soy Kitchen;Spain;Madrid;Zurbano 59, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4359433;-3.6931356;75;true;true;Fusion;At Soy Kitchen, “Julio” Zhang (Yong Ping Zhang) conjures up unique dishes that are a fusion of Asian (China, Korea, Japan etc) and Spanish cuisine. Outstanding Dim Sum, plus several surprise menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8512;Lúa;Spain;Madrid;Eduardo Dato 5, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4328535;-3.6957039;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Although there are numerous Galician restaurants in Madrid, it’s unusual to find one that is so different and with such a highly personal and innovative approach. Here, the cuisine prepared by Orense-born chef Manuel Domínguez, the son of traditional “pulpeiros” (octopus cooks), is served in two dining rooms with a warm rustic feel and works of contemporary art, as well as on the attractive terrace. The dishes on the à la carte and the two tasting menus (Lúa and Lúa Chea) are focused around a fully contemporary culinary approach with a strong Celtic influence, and one which maximises the use of seasonal ingredients that bring out the best of each other. We particularly enjoyed the signature “Pulpo a feira” octopus dish and the “Tarta líquida de Santiago”, a new take on the classic dessert but one which pays homage to the chef’s roots. Luckily for us, this particular moon (lúa in Galician) is shining brightly in the Spanish capital!;Air conditioning;[]
8513;Zalacaín;Spain;Madrid;Álvarez de Baena 4, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4383311;-3.6888851;39;true;false;Classic Cuisine;A major icon of Spain’s restaurant scene, Zalacaín boasts an à la carte featuring a number of its historic dishes (Búcaro “Don Pío” with smoked salmon, quail’s egg and caviar, Tellagorri cod, steak tartare etc), alongside a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8514;Coquetto;Spain;Madrid;Fortuny 2, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.428176;-3.6910318;44;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This informal bistro-style eatery, where elegance has been put to one side, bears the indelible stamp of the Sandoval brothers who enjoy rave reviews daily for their famous two-Michelin-star restaurant Coque located nearby. Here, the emphasis is on traditional cooking (“migas” with free-range egg, “fighting bull” tartare with old-style mustard etc) and seasonal ingredients, plus a menu that covers breakfast, lunch and dinner. Almost every dish can be ordered as a half portion.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8515;Ciclo;Spain;Cadiz;Amaya 1, Cadiz, 11005, Spain;36.5293053;-6.2920346;90;false;false;Contemporary;In this casual, centrally located restaurant divided into two sections (the bar on one side and the gastronomic dining area on the other), the cuisine of Cádiz is given a more contemporary twist. The enticing array of tapas and small plates (Ciclo salad, charcoal-grilled aubergines, tuna “cachopo” etc) is complemented by an excellent tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8516;Taberna el nº 10;Spain;Córdoba;Romero 10, Córdoba, 14003, Spain;37.8800047;-4.7816733;73;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is in the heart of the Jewish quarter. Choose between the outdoor terrace, the illuminated bar, or the dining room, which is split into two sections. The tapas and ‘raciones’ on offer provide a good introduction to the traditional and regional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8517;Casa Rubio;Spain;Córdoba;Puerta Almodóvar 5, Córdoba, 14003, Spain;37.8806709;-4.7839754;67;false;false;Regional Cuisine;It has a tapas bar and two à - la - carte dining areas decorated with wall - hangings in a traditional antique style. An attractive roof terrace with views of the walls.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8518;Casa Chuchu;Spain;Turón;El Parque, Turón, 33610, Spain;43.2096544;-5.7422292;86;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;If the prospect of eating in a typical Asturian “chigre” (cider bar) appeals to you, this unpretentious and authentic restaurant, located just a few kilometres from Mieres in the small parish of Turón and run by the third generation of the family, is a good option. Here, you can enjoy home-style cooking with lots of flavour, including slow-cooked stews, with a focus on high-quality ingredients. Everything is delicious but we can particularly recommend starting with its famous ham croquettes and making sure you save space for dessert – you’ll adore the cream-filled millefeuille!;Air conditioning;[]
8519;Gastrobodega Martín Berasategui;Spain;Rueda;Avenida Mariano Ruiz Rodríguez 1, Rueda, 47490, Spain;41.4135337;-4.9630873;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;If the idea of sampling the cooking of masterchef Martín Berasategui 20m underground sounds appealing, then El Hilo de Ariadna, an incredible 15C maze-like bodega hidden away in the town of Rueda in Valladolid province, is definitely the place for you. Here, the delicate, contemporary and ever consistent à la carte is always centred on the best possible ingredients and is complemented by wines produced by the Yllera family (the owners of the cellar). Interesting wine-focused activities are also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8520;Da Filippo;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Prim 34, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20006, Spain;43.3148687;-1.9801312;26;false;true;Italian;In the former premises of the Amelia restaurant, chef Paulo Airaudo focuses on the flavours of Italy but in a manner that is different to typical trattoria-style cuisine, hence the modern concept to his reinterpreted dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
8521;La Vieja;Spain;Palma;Plaza Raimundo Clar 11, Palma, 07002, Spain;39.5706256;2.6554314;84;true;true;Regional European;A restaurant with a distinct urban feel which is striking for its genuine graffiti (note the huge octopus!) and the influence of the Canary Islands (chef Jonay Hernández’s homeland) in its cuisine. The cooking here is described here as “new Canarian cuisine” that features local ingredients and an American and Mexican touch. It also takes its inspiration from the island’s culinary roots, which is showcased in several dishes that the chef has inherited from his mother. A great option for those who enjoy fish and seafood.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8522;Llama Inn - Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Conde de Xiquena 2, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4219946;-3.6941043;41;false;true;Peruvian;A restaurant with a relaxed, informal feel which sees itself as a clone of the original Llama Inn in Brooklyn (New York), the name of which pays homage to this typical Andean animal and to this traditional type of hostelry that always extends a warm welcome to guests. The aim of the cuisine here is to bring Peruvian flavours to the Spanish capital in dishes that are mainly designed for sharing (scallop ceviche, grouper tiradito, yakimeshi of king prawns etc), alongside others they describe as the “fiesta final” (sautéed beef and duck jerky with rice). A tasting menu, entitled “Trust The Chef” and served to the whole table, is also available.;Air conditioning;[]
8523;La Maruca - López de Hoyos;Spain;Madrid;López de Hoyos 42, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4400618;-3.6808689;62;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In keeping with the focus in its sister restaurants along the city’s Castellana and Velázquez streets, the region of Cantabria takes complete centre-stage here. The standout features in this spacious, contemporary eatery with its large windows looking out onto the street are the welcoming terrace to the rear and an unwavering focus on time-honoured Cantabrian cooking. The latter is based around quality ingredients and simply prepared dishes that retain a strong emphasis on detail. Specialities include anchovies, Santander-style fried squid, brandade fritters, stews (mountain stew and Lebaniego stew from the town of Liébana), and Cachopo, a typical dish combining steak, ham and cheese.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8524;Tora;Spain;Madrid;Padilla 5, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4316841;-3.6858275;27;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;A contemporary restaurant spread across two floors, each of which has its own sushi bar (the one upstairs is a private space). Here, chef José Osuna showcases his contemporary take on Japanese cuisine on an à la carte and a Omakase menu while using Spanish ingredients as the basis for his cooking. An interesting decorative feature is the use of a tiger motif (“tora” in Japanese) on the crockery and uniforms.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8525;Nordestada;Spain;Portosín;Praza Do Curro 11, Portosín, 15999, Spain;42.7592549;-8.9495802;85;false;false;Seafood;A unique dining option, occupying the former fish auction house in Portosín. Here, full homage is paid to the building’s history, with fish (grilled dishes are the only option) taking centre stage, although seafood and some meats are also available. The restaurant takes its name from the northeasterly wind (“nordés”) that is a frequent occurrence in the fishing waters of the Rías Baixas.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8526;Lasai;Spain;Bilbao;Príncipe 4, Bilbao, 48001, Spain;43.2624031;-2.924787;84;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Lasai takes its name from the Basque word for “calm” or “tranquillity”. This discreet restaurant in a narrow street in the centre of the city, just a few metres from the river, invites guests to discover its modern take on traditional cuisine via an à la carte and two set menus, all of which showcase dishes with their roots in the region and time-honoured flavours. The decor changes periodically thanks to the varied art exhibitions hosted here.;Air conditioning;[]
8527;A Gabeira;Spain;Ferrol;Valon 172 Nucleo, Ferrol, 15593, Spain;43.4982804;-8.2740012;50;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A fourth-generation century-old restaurant founded by great-grandmother Jesusa in 1923 which takes its name from a small island nearby. It features a private dining space, two elegant dining rooms and an open-view kitchen, where experienced chef Miguel Ángel Campos focuses on traditional cuisine with touches of creativity, including an impressive selection of seafood and the restaurant’s signature dishes (gratin of turbot with greens, and pan-fried sole with cornflour). A welcoming terrace completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8528;Paprica;Spain;Lugo;Nóreas 10, Lugo, 27001, Spain;43.0106826;-7.5537362;33;false;true;Contemporary;A contemporary, centrally located restaurant with an attractive terrace alongside the Roman walls that comes as a pleasant surprise. Traditional, seasonally inspired cuisine including tapas, à la carte options plus two tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8529;Vertigo;Spain;Córdoba;Doña Berenguela, Córdoba, 14006, Spain;37.8914114;-4.786552;59;false;true;Creative;Impressive dragons, imaginary beings from the subconscious and striking clouds of colour provide the backdrop in this highly original, aesthetically focused restaurant. Here, chef Javier Moreno has created a restaurant that is able to reflect his dreamlike world, in so doing fuelling his creativity to the full. His highly personalised cuisine is uncomplicated and without any single culinary attachment, hence the mix of ingredients sourced from far and wide.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8530;Estrella del Bajo Carrión;Spain;Villoldo;Mayor 32, Villoldo, 34131, Spain;42.2465279;-4.5973569;91;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant whose well-earned culinary reputation has been forged on traditional cuisine that is always superbly prepared. White beans are its particular speciality, although it also offers delicious baby lamb, Tierra de Campos pigeon, and tripe stew.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8531;Alcotán;Spain;Madrid;Claudio Coello 96, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4324273;-3.6855848;40;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A classically elegant restaurant with a focus on traditional cuisine (à la carte only), top-quality ingredients, strong flavours and attentive old-style service!;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8532;SiNoFos;Spain;Girona;Plaza de Cataluña 25, Girona, 17002, Spain;41.98185;2.822935;32;false;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with a contemporary, urban and industrial feel, a black-inspired decor, and a name that has evolved from “si no fós” – a type of public bench where those without work in the past would sit and congregate. Excellent cuisine featuring high-quality ingredients and a Mediterranean influence, including beef from the “LyO” company in Galicia and superb fish direct from the auction in Blanes. The à la carte includes special sections dedicated to tinned goods and spreads, classic dishes, vegetarian options, offal, rice and pasta, the grill etc). Tasting menu options are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
8533;Carballeira;Spain;Lleida;Carretera N II A, Lleida, 25194, Spain;41.5917468;0.585237;16;false;true;Farm to table, Seafood;An elegant, well - run family business with a profusion of wood on display. The owner is Galician, hence the high quality of fish and seafood. Interesting set menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8534;Cataria;Spain;Chiclana de la Frontera;Av. Amilcar Barca, 14, Chiclana de la Frontera, 11139, Spain;36.3476943;-6.1649179;57;true;true;Seafood, Grills;In this restaurant occupying a resort hotel with a pleasant terrace (with occasional live music), the menu is based around produce purchased at the local auction, hence the prominence given to outstanding grilled fish dishes (priced according to weight) which show the clear influence of the famous Elkano restaurant in Getaria.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8535;BiBo Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana 52, Madrid, 28046, Spain;40.4355104;-3.6881987;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;If you are keen to embark on a culinary journey to explore a magical gastronomic world of cosmopolitan cuisine at its finest, you don’t even need to leave Spain’s capital! This restaurant, decorated by the famous interior designer Lázaro Rosa-Violán, will surprise all and sundry with its fun aesthetic, dominated by some 7 000 light bulbs (that take us on a journey to the brilliance of the Málaga fair) and even an aerostatic globe! From a purely gourmet viewpoint, the contemporary, globally inspired cuisine (but with its roots in Andalucia), bears the hallmark of award-winning Marbella chef Dani García. The food here is very much designed for sharing in an informal atmosphere as a couple or with friends, and includes dishes such as foie gras and goat’s cheese millefeuille, almadraba-caught tuna tartare, fried hake, and 100% acorn-fed Iberian pork “pluma”. The à la carte also includes a small section dedicated to the chef’s signature dishes.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8536;Tastavin;Spain;Logrono;San Juan 25, Logrono, 26001, Spain;42.4658116;-2.4443531;68;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A centrally located eatery with a tapas bar on the ground floor (with a choice of wines by the glass) and a more formal dining room upstairs, with the option of dishes for sharing.;Air conditioning;[]
8537;Xanglot;Spain;Valencia;De Avellanas 9, Valencia, 46003, Spain;39.4744775;-0.3744114;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A family-run restaurant along a pedestrian street in the historic centre, just a few metres from the cathedral. In this contemporary yet informal dining space featuring attractive designer detail, it’s well worth keeping a close eye on chef Sandra Jorge, who champions a modern and creative culinary concept that takes the best local ingredients and a strong focus on contrasts as its main focal points. Three tasting menus are the only options here: Xanglot, Degusta and Sentits.;Air conditioning;[]
8538;Tsuro;Spain;Jerez de la Frontera;San Juan de Dios, Jerez de la Frontera, 11403, Spain;36.6871031;-6.1379576;31;true;true;Japanese;This small, centrally located restaurant, that likes to view itself as a passageway (Tsuro in Japanese) between Jerez and Japan, is dominated by a bar at which the chef (the only employee) can be seen hard at work. This intense culinary experience reveals many of the secrets of Japanese cuisine, from the rice ceremony and its preparation to the importance of knife sharpening. The dining experience, which lasts around three hours, is based around an Omakase menu and changes depending on market availability. Booking is essential.;Air conditioning;[]
8539;Mesón do Campo;Spain;Vilalba;Plaza San Juan 10, Vilalba, 27800, Spain;43.2975035;-7.6836314;54;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;With over 35 years of history behind it, this restaurant occupying a typical Galician house is a renowned local eatery. It features an attractive bar and wine cellar, with the floor upstairs set aside for the welcoming rustic-cum-contemporary dining room, where guests can choose from a traditional, seasonally inspired à la carte. Popular dishes on the menu include wild mushrooms and game, such as partridge, venison and wild boar. The owner is passionate about wine and it is not unusual for her to invite guests to her wine cellar so that they can select their bottle personally. An extensive set menu and two wine pairing options are also available.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8540;Tori-Key;Spain;Madrid;Plaza del Descubridor Diego de Ordás 2, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4409744;-3.7004934;40;false;false;Yakitori;A Japanese restaurant with a difference where the standard cold sushi is abandoned in favour of Yakitori-style cuisine, with a particular focus on grilled chicken kebabs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8541;Bistrónomo;Spain;Saragossa;Previsión Social 19, Saragossa, 50008, Spain;41.6424234;-0.8738108;73;true;false;Contemporary;A simple bistro that defines its cooking as haute-cuisine from the “barrio”! Contemporary-style tapas and raciones featuring Asian fusions, vegetables, tripe etc, alongside a more seasonally inspired menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8542;Txoko;Spain;Guía de Isora;Carretera TF 47, Guía de Isora, 38687, Spain;28.171041;-16.799017;21;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant has the feel of a modern Basque “txoko” (gastronomic society) and, in a nod to chef Martín Berasategui’s origins, offers cooking that is very “casual” in style. The glass-fronted terrace can be completely opened in the summer months.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8543;Brunelli's;Spain;Puerto de la Cruz;Bencomo 42, Puerto de la Cruz, 38400, Spain;28.4097031;-16.5662304;69;true;true;Meats and Grills;A splendid steakhouse located close to the entrance to the Loro Parque zoo. This family-run restaurant is a must on the island for meat-lovers given its choice of top-quality meat, with the advantage of many being aged on the premises. Make sure you try Brunelli's steak tartare, its signature speciality, or one of its superb cuts of grilled meat (Uruguayan beef entrecôte, Nebraskas Black Angus T-Bone, German Simmental ribeye, Chateaubriand and Spanish Tomahawk), many of which are sold by weight and designed for two people to share. The particularly impressive picture window here overlooks the sea.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8544;Casa Eutimio;Spain;Lastres;San Antonio 9, Lastres, 33330, Spain;43.5127566;-5.268153;16;false;true;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;Eutimio occupies an attractive property with a homely feel in a unique setting (although parking can occasionally be a problem). The traditionally focused à la carte is centred around fish and seafood, and is enhanced by interesting market-inspired daily suggestions. Several dishes require pre-ordering, such as the “caldereta” of fish and seafood, and the rice with lobster. The same goes for its hugely popular version of the traditional “cachopo” stew (the restaurant’s “Cacholetus” dish won Spain’s inaugural “cachopo” competition).;;[]
8545;Tosca;Spain;Xàbia;Avenida del Mediterráneo 238, Xàbia, 03730, Spain;38.775436;0.188958;31;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Tosca takes its name from the local stone that is an integral part of its interior decor. Enjoy updated Mediterranean cuisine in the dining room or on the pleasant terrace with views of the canal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8546;Andere;Spain;Vitoria-Gasteiz;Gorbea 8, Vitoria-Gasteiz, 01008, Spain;42.849182;-2.679896;31;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city, Andere is considered one of its classic addresses. Nowadays it sports a more modern look including an attractive, covered, winter garden - style patio. Traditional cuisine with a contemporary flourish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8547;Celler d'en Toni;Andorra;Andorra la Vella;Verge del Pilar 4, Andorra la Vella, AD500, Andorra;42.507145;1.531772;32;true;false;Contemporary;A restaurant combining tradition, creativity and flavour, where the à la carte focuses on ingredients of the highest quality, ranging from locally sourced meats to fresh fish direct from the auction.;Air conditioning;[]
8548;Lonxa d´Alvaro;Spain;Muxía;Mariña 22, Muxía, 15124, Spain;43.105108;-9.2169569;69;false;true;Meats and Seafood;A family run restaurant with a contemporary feel, located on the main street opposite the port. The menu here is based around locally sourced fish, seafood and delicious grilled meats.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8549;5 Gustos;Spain;Valladolid;Torrecilla 8, Valladolid, 47003, Spain;41.6559534;-4.7233496;93;true;true;Farm to table;Guests will feel at home in both the gastro-bar and attractive dining room, where the chef conjures up an updated take on traditional and seasonal cuisine, with the occasional nod to South America.;Air conditioning;[]
8550;Posta do Sol;Spain;Cambados;Ribeira de Fefiñans 22, Cambados, 36630, Spain;42.5179041;-8.8160392;21;false;false;Seafood;A restaurant-marisquería with plenty of character and decorative details inspired by the local region. Fish and seafood are the specialities here, along with the “empanadas” (the scallop empanada is a particular favourite!).;Terrace;[]
8551;Es Boldado;Spain;Sant Josep de sa Talaia;Carretera de Cala d'Hort, Sant Josep de sa Talaia, 07800, Spain;38.890575;1.221273;37;false;false;Seafood;Located at the end of a dirt track, from where the views of the sea and the islets of Es Vedrà and Es Vedranell are truly spectacular, thanks to the restaurant’s location on a cliff overlooking the Mediterranean. The simply furnished yet attractively appointed rustic-style dining room provides the backdrop for an à la carte that showcases top-quality ingredients and includes superb rice dishes and fish priced according to weight. One of the specialities here is the Bullit de peix with seafood rice (arroz a banda).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8552;Can Simoneta;Spain;Canyamel;Carretera Artà-Canyamel, Canyamel, 07580, Spain;39.65198;3.437766;65;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A restaurant with a spectacular location on a cliff boasting superb views. Surprising cuisine that combines the flavours of Mexico and Mallorca. The set menus here are a good option.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8553;Zelai Zabal;Spain;Oñate;Carretera Oñate-Arantzazu, Oñate, 20567, Spain;42.9833514;-2.4053609;93;true;false;Basque;A traditional and prestigious family - run restaurant with a long history – it opened its doors in 1898 as a hostel and cheap eatery. Classic Basque cuisine showing the occasional contemporary touch.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8554;Bailara;Spain;Bidania;Eliz Bailara 8, Bidania, 20496, Spain;43.1386453;-2.1539628;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Bailara’s contemporary ambience in a rural hotel in the heart of nature definitely strikes a chord! The modern-inspired cuisine on offer here is centred around a single surprise tasting menu that showcases seasonal dishes and is based around ingredients sourced from local producers (asparagus, teardrop peas, artichokes, cep mushrooms etc) and meat from local breeders. We particularly enjoyed the charcoal-grilled beef tacos!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8555;Casa Osmunda;Spain;San Pedro de Breña Alta;Subida la Concepción 2, San Pedro de Breña Alta, 38710, Spain;28.67516;-17.78126;50;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In this attractive Spanish colonial-style house located at a crossroads, enjoy traditionally inspired Canary Island cuisine with a modern touch, including seasonal dishes that do not feature on the à la carte (the fresh fish here is particularly impressive). It is said that “life is better by sharing”, hence the focus on this philosophy in many of the starters on the menu.;Terrace;[]
8556;Etéreo by Pedro Nel;Spain;Santa Cruz de Tenerife;San Antonio 63, Santa Cruz de Tenerife, 38001, Spain;28.4735;-16.25209;94;false;true;Meats and Grills;A centrally located family-run restaurant with a relaxed feel in which the Colombian-born chef showcases a mix of cuisines that demonstrate a passion for flavours from around the world. This encompasses a variety of starters, fish and rice dishes, plus a special focus on meat that includes aged and premium cuts from breeds such as Rubia Gallega, Simmental, Friesian, Black Angus etc. Many of the dishes are priced for two people, with the idea of sharing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8557;La Sandunga;Spain;Tegueste;San Ignacio 17, Tegueste, 38280, Spain;28.5023621;-16.3568312;41;false;false;International;Occupying a country house with an interior featuring an open - view kitchen and main dining room overlooking the surrounding landscape that will come as a pleasant surprise. Internationally focused menu with a good choice of meats alongside dishes from the Canary Islands, France Japan and Peru.;Car park,Terrace;[]
8558;Cabo Vidio;Spain;Soto de Luiña;Oviñana, Soto de Luiña, 33156, Spain;43.5638808;-6.2437576;88;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This attractive family-run restaurant, featuring a pleasantly surprising rustic-style dining room overlooking a charming landscaped terrace, is run in a friendly spirit and with great professionalism by chef Jairo López (who is in charge of both the kitchen and dining room). His traditional Asturian cooking, including dishes such as broad beans with cod cheek, spider crab cake, and the loin of sea bream with cider, always champions ingredients sourced from the local area. Although many of the dishes here are for two people, it is also possible to order individual portions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8559;L’Hostal de Ca l’Enric;Spain;La Vall de Bianya;Carretera Camprodón N 260, La Vall de Bianya, 17813, Spain;42.2217505;2.4401289;42;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This bright, welcoming restaurant just 100m or so from the award-winning Ca l'Enric is run by chef Isabel Juncà, who shares her passion for seasonally inspired traditional cuisine through affordably priced day-to-day cooking that definitely does not skimp on flavour. The à la carte, featuring savoury rice dishes, grilled fish and meat, cannelloni etc, is complemented by an inexpensive yet well-crafted weekday menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8560;Piripi;Spain;Alacant;Avenida de Oscar Esplá 30, Alacant, 03003, Spain;38.3422549;-0.4941448;76;false;true;Rice Dishes;Standing along one of the city’s main avenues, Piripi is one of the best-known tapas venues in Alicante, featuring a busy tapas bar on the ground floor (you can also eat at the bar counter) and a meticulous dining room upstairs. The extensive à la carte showcases its signature dishes, superb rice options, and an array of daily specials (fish and seafood are sourced daily direct from the fish auctions in Dénia and Santa Pola).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8561;Suculent;Spain;Barcelona;Rambla del Raval 45, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3781869;2.1702491;18;true;true;Contemporary;A culinary jewel in the heart of the Raval district where guests can choose between two contemporary menus (Los Clásicos and Suculent), both featuring fresh and informal dishes that in most cases are presented as small plates designed for sharing. There’s even a hidden table accessed via the rear of the cold room!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8562;Nozomi Sushi Bar;Spain;Valencia;Pedro III El Grande 11, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.46241;-0.3695406;59;true;false;Japanese;A Japanese restaurant with a zen-like ambience that is enjoying considerable success. Modern Japanese cuisine that is easily recognisable to the general public, including a wide choice of starters. We recommend booking ahead.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8563;Boccatti;Spain;Vic;Mossèn Josep Gudiol 21, Vic, 08500, Spain;41.9283042;2.2491568;22;false;true;Seafood, Catalan;A family-run restaurant that has been keeping its customers happy since 1978! Maritime-inspired cuisine that is particularly renowned for its wild-caught fish and seafood. Booking recommended.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8564;El Hogar Gallego;Spain;Calella;Ànimes 73, Calella, 08370, Spain;41.6161526;2.6629693;36;false;true;Seafood, Galician;This culinary “institution” in the Maresme area, and one with many years of business behind it, is a standard-bearer for the fresh catch from the Atlantic and Mediterranean, and more specifically from the fishing fleet in Cambados and the fish auctions in Blanes, Palamós, Arenys de Mar etc. On its extensive à la carte, the most popular dishes are always its superb fish and seafood, although it also offers a good choice of rice and meat options. The simple way of cooking here, either grilled or baked in salt, enhances the ingredients used to the full.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8565;Maestral;Spain;Alacant;Andalucía 18, Alacant, 03016, Spain;38.3666611;-0.4557485;20;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This elegant restaurant occupies an attractive villa surrounded by gardens that are popular for corporate events, private spaces for more intimate gatherings, and a terrace for summer dining that is often full. Choose from an extensive à la carte menu of traditional Mediterranean cuisine based around high-quality ingredients and featuring a small selection of rice dishes. We particularly recommended the delicious Santa Pola shrimp and the red tuna served four ways.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8566;El Portal;Spain;Alacant;Bilbao 2, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.3439808;-0.4836054;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A super-cool gastro-bar with an attractive bar and a variety of tables serving tapas, Iberian hams, seafood, cheeses, rice dishes and a selection of grilled dishes. Cocktails and after-work drinks complete the picture!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8567;El Campero;Spain;Barbate;Avenida de la Constitución 5, Barbate, 11160, Spain;36.1884806;-5.9247645;94;false;false;Seafood;A renowned culinary name in the local area where everything revolves around the famous red “almadraba” tuna. It also offers an extensive à la carte featuring an array of rice dishes and fish priced by weight, alongside a tasting menu (El Susurro de los Atunes) enabling guests to try different parts and cuts of this legendary fish. A superb tapas bar completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8568;A'Kangas by Urrechu;Spain;Alcobendas;Estafeta 4, Alcobendas, 28109, Spain;40.5143272;-3.6532869;41;false;false;Meats and Grills;This elegant eatery, located in the restaurant district as you enter upmarket La Moraleja, boasts a bright terrace and an impeccable interior featuring meat-ageing cabinets and an open grill, all of which are visible to guests. Elaborate traditional cuisine plus superb grilled red meats (Valles del Esla beef, Xata Roxa and Argentinian veal etc) take pride of place on the menu here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8569;Windsor;Spain;Barcelona;Còrsega 286, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3948915;2.1572133;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, with its updated classic decor, is enhanced by an exquisite terrace and several dining rooms that allow for different configurations. Contemporary Catalan cuisine including a good choice of set menus.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8570;El Portalet;Spain;Bossòst;Sant Jaume 32, Bossòst, 25550, Spain;42.7832137;0.6923924;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A rustic-contemporary-style restaurant that has gradually enhanced the comfort of its facilities to create a welcoming ambience featuring open stonework, a plethora of wood, plus an attractive glass-enclosed wine cellar. Its consistent cuisine, modern in composition and mainly built around seasonal ingredients, is centred around the à la carte and two fixed-options. A standout dish is the flame-grilled aubergine ravioli with porcini mushrooms, black garlic, cured egg yolk and confit neck of baby goat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8571;El Terrat;Spain;Tarragona;Pons d'Icart 19, Tarragona, 43004, Spain;41.1138646;1.2523993;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with a contemporary feel that has gradually upgraded its facilities, including an open-view kitchen at the entrance, to create the perfect ambience in which to enjoy the cuisine of chef Moha Quach. In his dishes, the sparkling aromas highlight his Moroccan roots (his father was a humble fisherman and his grandparents kept a flock of sheep) as well as the essence of Mediterranean multi-culturalism, with a particular focus on his beloved Tarragona and the ingredients from its surrounding area (extending from the Camp de Tarragona region to the Ebro delta). The à la carte, which in itself showcases plenty of soul and personality, is complemented by two interesting set menus (Olivus and Mare Nostrum), plus another called Essencia which is only available for lunch midweek. Dishes that we particularly enjoyed included the “romesco” of red Tarragona prawns and the “cremoso” of teardrop peas, egg cooked at low temperature and truffles.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8572;Bodega del Riojano;Spain;Santander;Rio de la Pila 5, Santander, 39003, Spain;43.4640356;-3.8041247;96;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with an abundance of character, history and authenticity, plus a unique museum (Museo Redondo) teeming with works of art. This business, which first started out in the 1930s selling agricultural items and wines, is nowadays a classic address in the city. The traditional menu features dishes such as the popular Rioja-style braised snails, as well as hake with a velouté cream and peppers. We recommend booking a table in advance and enjoying an aperitif in the bar before moving on to the dining room.;Air conditioning;[]
8573;Tunateca Balfegó;Spain;Barcelona;Avenida Diagonal 439, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3938985;2.149936;31;false;false;Fusion;Red tuna is at the heart of everything here! In this highly original restaurant, with a particularly striking ceiling in the main dining room featuring a decor of a school of fish plus some walls adorned with scale-like tiles, there are two à la carte options (one, more Western in taste, where tuna is the main focus, and a second more Asian-inspired menu centred around nigiri, sashimi, uramaki etc) alongside interesting tasting menus (Red and Blu). Occasionally, the restaurant also organises Kaitai experiences where participants can learn first-hand about this time-honoured Japanese fish-slicing technique.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8574;Galaxia Cocina Pepehillo;Spain;Badajoz;Avenida Miguel Celdrán Matute 6, Badajoz, 06005, Spain;38.872945;-6.9756689;68;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant that impresses guests with its interior design and traditional à la carte abounding in fish and seafood but without neglecting Extremadura’s renowned cured hams and sausages. The “revuelto Pepehillo” is a must!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8575;Barahonda;Spain;Yecla;Carretera de Pinoso, Yecla, 30510, Spain;38.5872328;-1.0811773;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Part of the Señorío de Barahonda estate, with views of the surrounding vineyards. Here, in the shape of two tasting menus (Huerto and Terruño), chef Alejandro Ibáñez showcases cooking from the local terroir (albeit through more modern eyes) that is based around ingredients sourced from the local area and his own garden (we particularly liked the pigeon royale and liver flan, as well as the grilled aubergine with Jerusalem artichoke ice-cream, caramel and pine nuts). To enjoy the experience to the full, we suggest joining the wine tour before you eat.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8576;Izariya;Spain;Madrid;Zurbano 63, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4363906;-3.6930846;24;false;true;Japanese;This small eatery is not your customary Japanese restaurant. Here, Izariya pays culinary homage to “omotenashi” (the country’s tradition of hospitality), which it seeks to convey through its exquisite cuisine. We recommend exploring its menus at the kitchen counter, where you can watch the chefs at close quarters and benefit from their explanations. The Omakase menu needs to be booked in advance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8577;El Barril de La Moraleja;Spain;Alcobendas;Estafeta 4, Alcobendas, 28109, Spain;40.5143866;-3.6529505;66;false;false;Seafood;The attractively laid - out terrace and modern, maritime - inspired interior come as a pleasant surprise. The menu specialises in fish and seafood, complemented by a good choice of rice dishes and red meats.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8578;Asador Coto Real;Spain;Rábade;Avenida A Coruña 107, Rábade, 27370, Spain;43.1200123;-7.6271713;69;true;true;Meats and Grills;Located in a small town just over 15km from Lugo, this restaurant is the perfect place for meat-lovers who can choose between dishes roasted in the wood-fired oven (such as baby lamb) or steak cooked on the grill. This “asador”, which shares its name with a charming small hotel, has gradually updated its facilities and is one of the few in Galicia to have a Castilian roasting oven and open grill behind the counter. The “alta selección” beef steak is for two to share.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8579;Torre Simón;Spain;Tona;Doctor Bayés 75, Tona, 08551, Spain;41.8582984;2.2304412;69;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a historic feel, occupying a delightful colonial-inspired villa on the outskirts of Tona. Choose between the contemporary-inspired à la carte and an impressive gastronomic menu with a pre-determined array of interesting and different starters but with the freedom to choose the main course and dessert from the à la carte.;Car park,Terrace;[]
8580;Ca Na Toneta;Spain;Caimari;Horitzó 21, Caimari, 07314, Spain;39.7713338;2.9022032;30;false;false;Regional Cuisine;An honest approach and tradition combine in this restaurant run by two sisters and named after grandma Toneta! Truly excellent and seasonal Mallorcan cooking with a focus on flavours and ingredients unique to the island. Customers can also buy products from the small shop.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8582;La Taberna del Gourmet;Spain;Alacant;San Fernando 10, Alacant, 03002, Spain;38.3444151;-0.4815121;51;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This taverna could almost be described as a tapas museum! Huge choice of tapas on display, all prepared using high quality ingredients, as well as an extensive selection of wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8583;La Terraza de Alba;Spain;Tres Cantos;Alba 5, Tres Cantos, 28760, Spain;40.6010822;-3.706481;90;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Updated traditional cuisine with a selection of rice options and red tuna dishes. One of the highlights on the menu is the steak tartare, prepared to your liking at your table. Half-“raciones” are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8584;El Niu;Spain;Escunhau;Santa Anna 23, Escunhau, 25539, Spain;42.6979363;0.8239765;49;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located alongside a main road, El Niu occupies a stone house with an interior featuring traditional mountain decor, including an open fire, skis, snowshoes etc, plus a notable profusion of wood. The à la carte, traditional in composition but with added French touches, is enhanced by interesting daily specials that the female owner “sings” to every guest (traditional country pâté, leek pudding with a cep mushroom and black truffle sauce, pig trotter stew with snails etc).;;[]
8585;Villa Paramesa;Spain;Valladolid;Plaza Martí y Monsó 4, Valladolid, 47001, Spain;41.6522893;-4.7304016;29;true;false;Contemporary;A family-run restaurant that, as well as maintaining its successful array of tapas, also offers an updated take on a traditional menu that has a strong focus on meat dishes but with influences from further afield.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8587;La Taverna del Clínic;Spain;Barcelona;Rosselló 155, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3888994;2.1512731;93;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run “taverna” featuring a profusion of wood, thoroughly contemporary comfort and two distinct sections: La Taverna and the restaurant itself. Here, the culinary focus is on traditional cooking based around seasonal ingredients, with a particular fondness for stews and great respect shown to time-honoured flavours, albeit from a modern perspective. The extensive à la carte is impressively complemented by various daily specials, with an enticing array of fish sourced from nearby auctions, and “large plate” options perfect for sharing. Several gastronomic menus are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8588;Zelai Txiki;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Travesía del Rodil 79, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20013, Spain;43.3247005;-1.9643795;58;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;A superb location on the slopes of Mt Ulía, hence the impressive views from its panoramic terrace. The extensive, traditionally inspired à la carte has a strong focus on organic ingredients sourced from the restaurant’s own vegetable garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8589;Culuca;Spain;A Coruña;Avenida Arteixo 10, A Coruña, 15004, Spain;43.3633915;-8.4089802;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A spacious, modern and centrally located gastro - bar with a young and informal atmosphere. Enjoy tapas and raciones that mix the traditional with the creative.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8590;Yandiola;Spain;Bilbao;Plaza Arriquibar 4, Bilbao, 48010, Spain;43.2596887;-2.9364208;68;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located inside the Askuna Zentroa civic and cultural centre, where the interior design and meticulous lighting come as a pleasant surprise. Updated traditional cuisine that follows the seasons.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8591;Monastrell;Spain;Alacant;Avenida del Almirante Julio Guillén Tato 1, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.339157;-0.487601;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Monastell’s menus, which also include vegetarian options, focus on “natural” cuisine with a particular relish for fish and seafood direct from the local auction alongside excellent rice dishes. The restaurant has its own market garden just 15km away.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8592;Can Font;Spain;Eivissa;Plaza de España 4, Eivissa, 07800, Spain;38.9071726;1.4377593;97;true;false;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant with an entrance separate from the hotel, located in the upper walled section of the old town, with a pleasant dining room and terrace where the focus is on modern cuisine. On the à la carte and tasting menu (the latter needs to be ordered when making your booking), the chef showcases the island’s fruits, vegetables and olive oils, as well as fish caught sustainably off its coastal waters.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8593;Asador Coruña;Spain;A Coruña;Alcalde José Crespo López Mora 4, A Coruña, 15008, Spain;43.3484415;-8.4125949;40;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant in which maximum respect is paid to the quality of ingredients. A classic - cum - traditional dining room with a profusion of wood, decorative stonework and an open - view kitchen. Excellent Galician meats grilled over a wood fire, as well as delicious fish dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
8594;Nectari;Spain;Barcelona;València 28, Barcelona, 08015, Spain;41.3799299;2.1464448;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Jordi Esteve endows his innovative cuisine with the exquisite nuances that locally sourced ingredients (he works closely with small-scale producers) bring to his dishes. The tasty cooking on offer in this centrally located restaurant with a distinct “barrio” feel is always focused on the seasons and is best represented on his tasting menu, where you’ll find courses such as foie and eel and the superb seafood “bisque” with prawn tartare.;Air conditioning;[]
8595;Fonda de la Confianza;Spain;Madrid;General Gallegos 1, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.461092;-3.6866069;22;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re looking for impeccably prepared traditional cuisine and a focus on quality service, this restaurant is a splendid option, in large part thanks to the presence of Paco Patón, whose awards range from a National Gastronomy Prize to Best Front of House Manager. His cuisine, which is built around time-honoured stews, a few offal-based dishes, delicious rice options and superb escabeches, is complemented by a good selection of daily fish and meat options, with ingredients sourced directly from the auction.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8596;Os Cachivaches;Spain;Lugo;Campos Novos 26, Lugo, 27002, Spain;42.9933254;-7.5525553;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Rice Dishes;This restaurant is run by two siblings in a residential district close to the university. It features a tapas bar with high tables for informal eating plus two dining rooms where guests can choose from an extensive à la carte which impresses thanks to its array of rice dishes (we particularly recommend the creamy rice with marine plankton). Make sure you also leave space for the exquisite desserts, especially the brioche “torrija” with vanilla ice cream, and the delicious cheesecake.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8597;El Conjuro;Spain;Calahonda;Avenida de los Geranios 6, Calahonda, 18730, Spain;36.6997379;-3.4171222;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A minimalist-style restaurant impressively run by two brothers with a liberal approach to contemporary cuisine based around the very best products from the coast, select meats and Asian condiments.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8598;Rubaiyat Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Juan Ramón Jiménez 37, Madrid, 28036, Spain;40.4609856;-3.6866734;80;true;false;Meats and Grills;Discover the authentic flavours of São Paulo in this restaurant where you can order the typical “feijoada” (minimum of two guests) or its extensive selection of meats. Fantastic terrace featuring trees and plenty of greenery!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8599;La Hermosa de Alba;Spain;Santander;Tetuán 34, Santander, 39004, Spain;43.4660929;-3.7926266;67;false;true;Fusion;A restaurant with a fun, modern feel that is enjoying considerable success in the city. The menu here is contemporary in style with elements of fusion cooking and dishes designed for sharing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8600;Nairod;Spain;Barcelona;Aribau 141, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3922152;2.1541091;36;false;true;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city’s Eixample district, Nairod exudes personality everywhere you look, which doesn’t come as a surprise given that David Rustarazo (better known as Rusti) is at the helm – a self-made chef whose success is down to hard work and experience gained abroad. In this intimate, contemporary setting with a bistro vibe, enjoy market-inspired cuisine in which flavour takes precedence, and includes incredible game dishes in season (hare, venison, partridge and, in particular, pigeon). The name of the restaurant is a nod to the chef’s son, Dorian, but written in reverse!;Air conditioning;[]
8601;María de la O;Spain;Granada;Carretera de la Sierra, Granada, 18008, Spain;37.1672779;-3.5871737;44;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;Occupying a small 19C mansion with various options on offer (gastro-bar, private events etc). The cuisine here has a solid technical base enabling it to explore different textures and flavours.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
8602;Playing Solo;Spain;Madrid;Manuela Malasaña 33, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4287886;-3.70519;82;false;true;Fusion;A unique restaurant run in a highly personalised manner, to the extent that you practically eat in the kitchen! Here, the chef focuses on a single, seasonally inspired surprise menu with the details on how each dish is prepared explained to guests.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8603;Benares;Spain;Madrid;Zurbano 5, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.427616;-3.693831;86;false;false;Indian;Following in the footsteps of its London namesake, Benares’ major selling points are its modern take on classic Indian cuisine and its pleasant terrace-garden with a soothing patio pool.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8604;Volta i Volta;Spain;Xàbia;Santa Teresa 3, Xàbia, 03730, Spain;38.7888809;0.1626025;77;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Occupying a building in the town’s historic quarter, where it has retained aesthetic details from the original old house. Tasty Mediterranean cooking with influences from Italy and further afield.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8606;Èter;Spain;Madrid;Granito 20, Madrid, 28045, Spain;40.3931752;-3.6919123;93;true;false;Contemporary;Intimate and minimalist in feel, Èter is run by two brothers who seek the diner's enjoyment inorder to find their own. The creative cuisine is presented in two tasting menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8607;Casa Dirección;Spain;Valverde del Camino;Avenida de la Constitución 98, Valverde del Camino, 21600, Spain;37.5806694;-6.7514703;29;false;false;Farm to table;Very easy to find, thanks to its location next to the beautiful English-style mansion which now houses the ethnographic museum (also known as the Casa Dirección). The restaurant is home to a tapas bar where you can enjoy mini versions of à la carte dishes, a dining room that looks onto a delightful terrace, a landscaped area for private events, and even an amphitheatre! In the bright dining room, the walls of which are somewhat unusually adorned with an array of shoe moulds, choose from an à la carte of updated traditional dishes and several menus, all of which include a wine pairing.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8608;Sukaldean Aitor Santamaria;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;San Martín 45, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20007, Spain;43.3160229;-1.9856533;26;false;false;Contemporary;In this highly original setting in the Hotel Zenit Convento de San Martín, several different gastronomic options are available in a single space, including a sushi bar and an area dedicated exclusively to cheese-lovers! The contemporary à la carte combines Basque and Asian recipes, including local sausages, grilled dishes, and traditional sushi (the latter described as “Euskal Sushi” (Basque Sushi). This is complemented by three tasting menus (Clásico, Akelena and Historias del Queso).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8609;Sua;Spain;Madrid;Moratín 22, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4124475;-3.6962431;34;true;true;Meats and Grills;Part of the Triciclo group, this modern “asador”-style restaurant, the name of which is a nod to Basque mythology, views itself as a “temple of fire” in the Spanish capital. Its most striking feature is its setting in a delightful winter garden in the heart of the Las Letras district. Although Sua offers an excellent choice of starters and grilled vegetables from the town of Tudela in Northern Spain, the star dishes here are those cooked on the open grill, including fish direct from the auction and an array of select meats (Galician T-bone, veal skirt, Iberian pork etc).;Air conditioning;[]
8610;Txirene;Spain;Bilbao;Poza Lizentziatuaren 26, Bilbao, 48011, Spain;43.2620007;-2.9401409;65;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The name of this restaurant, which takes its name from a term specific to Bilbao that describes a person who is something of a joker, is one of those place that locals like to keep to themselves! It is home to a busy “pintxos” bar, hidden behind which is a meticulous, contemporary dining room offering an extensive array of traditional-style cuisine. At Txirene, they are proud to boast that their food is 100% from Bilbao and that what they serve is dictated by the time of year. Despite this, you’ll always find superb seasonal fish dishes on the menu as well as delicious savoury rice options and meat such as the incredibly flavoursome suckling lamb chops. A wide variety of good-value wines is also available here.;Air conditioning;[]
8611;Taberna Noroeste;Spain;Barcelona;Radas 67, Barcelona, 08004, Spain;41.3722164;2.1604463;69;false;false;Contemporary;If you’re keen to move away from the classic restaurant circuit in Barcelona, head to Poble Sec, a quiet district at the foot of the Montjuic hill, and just a stone’s throw from the legendary Paral·lel avenue. This taberna has just a few tables in the dining room, hence the opportunity to watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen behind the bar. The single surprise menu evolves with the seasons (the fish and seafood are outstanding) with meticulous attention paid to creamy textures and the pairing of ingredients. The name of the restaurant (Northwest in English) is in reference to the origins of owner-chefs Javier and David, as one hails from La Coruña, the other from Salamanca, hence the fusion between Galician, Castilian and Catalan cooking. Guests here are all served at the same time so it’s important to arrive punctually!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8612;Ferretería;Spain;Madrid;Atocha 57, Madrid, 28012, Spain;40.4127687;-3.6997063;26;false;true;Contemporary;A visit to this former hardware store (hence its name), and its dining rooms occupying 16C coal vaults, is an absolute must. Updated traditional cuisine prepared with ingredients of the very highest quality.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8613;Juan Carlos Ferrando;Spain;Logrono;María Teresa Gil de Gárate 7, Logrono, 26002, Spain;42.4632219;-2.4490013;27;false;true;Contemporary;A contemporary, family-run restaurant offering elaborate cooking centred on dishes from the Rioja region which have given a modern twist and make the most of the very best local products.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8614;Castillo de Montemayor;Spain;Montemayor del Río;Castillo 10, Montemayor del Río, 37727, Spain;40.3488876;-5.8927658;17;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A unique restaurant in a beautiful natural setting within the walls of an authentic castle. Traditional à la carte with a contemporary touch and signature recipes such as its traditional mashed potato dish known as “revolconas”.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8615;La Barra de Cañabota;Spain;Seville;Orfila 5, Seville, 41003, Spain;37.3934059;-5.9936348;57;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;An unusual tapas bar with a strong focus on fish and seafood that replicates the philosophy of its older sibling (Cañabota). Here, the dishes are somewhat simpler but based around the same principles and ingredients of the very highest quality.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8616;Salitre;Spain;A Coruña;Paseo Marítimo Alcalde Francisco Vázquez 25, A Coruña, 15002, Spain;43.3753396;-8.3936994;62;true;true;Galician, Traditional Cuisine;Salitre’s menu is based around Galician products with a penchant for traditional flavours. On the à la carte we recommend the delicious fish stew (“caldeirada de pescado”) and any of its savoury rice dishes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8617;Lakasa;Spain;Madrid;Plaza del Descubridor Diego de Ordás 1, Madrid, 28003, Spain;40.4408469;-3.7006709;59;false;false;Farm to table;A restaurant that is on the tip of everyone’s tongue and as such is full almost every day. Its updated take on traditional market-based cuisine is constantly being updated and includes the option of half-portions. Don’t miss the signature Idiazabal cheese fritters!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8618;La Cábala;Spain;Toledo;Sinagoga 6, Toledo, 45001, Spain;39.8581551;-4.0239736;27;true;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;A rustic-cum-contemporary restaurant tucked away in a narrow street with plenty of character just a few metres from the cathedral. La Cábala has been completely redesigned, so that the original “taberna” has been transformed into a restaurant featuring dominant white tones and open brickwork. The à la carte, an impressive take on contemporary cuisine, is complemented by a few dishes for sharing and what the restaurant calls “small individual bites”, including the superb 110% Iberian ham croquettes with torrezno-style popcorn.;Air conditioning;[]
8619;La Mira de Gredos;Spain;Hoyos del Espino;Carretera de El Barco, Hoyos del Espino, 05634, Spain;40.3505247;-5.1726843;88;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The large glass - fronted dining room boasts contemplative views of the Sierra de Gredos. Up - to - date traditional cuisine and several set menus. Make sure you try the " patatas revolconas ".;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
8620;Lume;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Das Ameas 2, Santiago de Compostela, 15704, Spain;42.8797475;-8.5417135;23;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Fusion;Chef Lucía Freitas’ more informal eatery features two menus perfect for enjoying at the bar with views of the kitchen and a concise à la carte of “raciones” served exclusively on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8621;Omakase;Spain;A Coruña;Plaza de María Pita 3, A Coruña, 15001, Spain;43.3712058;-8.3953553;92;true;false;Japanese;A restaurant with a restrained decor and a philosophy based on Omakase-style dining (hence the name) in the emblematic Plaza de María Pita of the city, where you’ll find nothing more than a sushi bar and a fish-aging cabinet. Here, Vigo-born chef Adrián Figueroa, a true expert when it comes to slicing techniques and the preparation of tuna, showcases his skills on a single tasting menu (to which you can also add extras such as eel, crayfish etc) that changes according to availability at the daily auction. Bookings need to be made via the restaurant’s website.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8622;Candado Golf;Spain;Malaga;Golf del Candado 2, Malaga, 29018, Spain;36.7218469;-4.3429432;26;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Part of the Real Club El Candado golf club, hence its relaxing terraces and pleasant views. Classic-traditional cuisine plus a good choice of rice dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8623;Canela en Rama;Spain;Linares;República Argentina 12, Linares, 23700, Spain;38.0958185;-3.6310802;88;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;An attractive taberna serving contemporary tapas and “raciones” with a hint of fusion alongside classic signature dishes such as Linares-style patatas bravas, salmorejo etc. From Wednesday to Sunday, two tasting menus (prior booking required) are available upstairs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8624;Cipresaia;Spain;Girona;Bonaventura Carreras Peralta 5, Girona, 17004, Spain;41.9849874;2.8255259;27;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a relaxed ambience and no little personality in the heart of Girona’s old quarter. Here, you can enjoy simple yet delicious traditional cuisine with the addition of a few contemporary touches from around the world. The à la carte also features a number of references to the world of cinema and to director Quico Viader.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8625;La Masía de Chencho;Spain;Elche;Partida de Jubalcoi 1-9, Elche, 03295, Spain;38.2753831;-0.6515032;15;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant delights guests thanks to its setting in an attractive farmhouse with a rustic yet elegant ambience and plenty of space for private events. Good traditional cuisine with a focus on high-quality ingredients, including an appetising choice of rice dishes. The impressive and extensive wine cellar is an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8626;Artabria;Spain;A Coruña;Fernando Macías 28, A Coruña, 15004, Spain;43.3663503;-8.4133481;100;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a historical name (the “Artabrians” were a Celtic tribe who settled in the area) located close to Riazor beach. From the attractively appointed dining room, the kitchen to the rear is partially visible to guests, who can select from a classic à la carte or the option of a varied menu. Specialities well worth trying include the crunchy dish of scallops with a crab cream, smoked salmon rolls with prawn tartare, creamy Carabineros prawns with rice, plus lamprey in season. It is often full thanks to the support of its loyal clientele.;Air conditioning;[]
8627;Casa de Pías;Spain;Getafe;Plaza Escuelas Pías 4, Getafe, 28901, Spain;40.3070687;-3.7312732;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A centrally located restaurant with a classic-contemporary decor dominated by a white colour scheme in its main dining rooms and private spaces. Here, the emphasis is on traditionally inspired cooking that makes full use of farm and market produce, alongside dishes prepared with superb fish direct from the coast (such as braised wild grouper) and top-quality meats (Iberian pork cheek with a yellow curry sauce, grilled Galician T-bone etc). The wide selection of appetisers is complemented by a choice of traditional preserves.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8628;Casa Rubén;Spain;Tella;Carretera de Bielsa km 63 Hospital de Tella, Tella, 22364, Spain;42.5475683;0.1624873;43;false;false;Contemporary;A restaurant with a surprising location beneath a large vaulted stone ceiling. Highly personalised service and updated traditional cuisine based around a single tasting menu. Booking essential.;Car park;[]
8629;Mudrá;Spain;Madrid;Recoletos 13, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4217964;-3.689758;87;false;true;Vegetarian;If you’re a fan of vegetarian cuisine, this centrally located restaurant (the name of which is the Sanskrit word for “gesture”, an important aspect of yoga postures) is the first international franchise in Europe that only uses vegetarian ingredients. Overseen by American chef Matthew Kenney, a leading name in this type of cuisine, it offers a vegetarian à la carte that follows the plant-based food philosophy, and features meticulously prepared dishes such as artichoke tiraditos, wild mushroom ceviche, Omakase nigiri etc.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
8630;Quatre Vents 3.0;Spain;Hostalric;Avenida del Coronel Estrada 122, Hostalric, 17450, Spain;41.7464957;2.6344902;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This family-run restaurant, founded in 1964 by the owners’ grandfather, has retained its original name in homage to its origins, but adding the 3.0 to symbolise the third generation that is now at the helm. Modern and functional in appearance, and with views of the Montseny mountains, it focuses on contemporary cuisine that changes in line with seasonal ingredients. This can be enjoyed on the à la carte (we recommend the “a la llauna” rice dishes) and various set menus: Express and Satisfecho (only available lunchtimes midweek), the De Tapes (available for dinner), and the more extensive Homenaje. An interesting anecdote: in a competition on the TV3 channel called Joc de Cartes, it was proclaimed the best restaurant for cep mushrooms in the Baix Montseny area!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8631;Casa Pepe de la Judería;Spain;Córdoba;Romero 1, Córdoba, 14003, Spain;37.8797244;-4.7812086;98;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant is located in the heart of the city’s Jewish quarter. It has an interior that comes as a pleasant surprise, replete with a typical Andalucian patio, pleasant dining rooms and a charming rooftop terrace. Southern Spanish cuisine with a modern touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8632;Odoloste;Spain;Bilbao;Alameda Recalde 11, Bilbao, 48001, Spain;43.2667157;-2.9333589;56;false;true;Pork;A restaurant located just a few steps from the Guggenheim Bilbao, where pork and pork-based dishes take centre stage. Updated traditional cooking and a contemporary ambience.;Air conditioning;[]
8633;El Disparate;Spain;Seville;Alameda de Hércules 11, Seville, 41002, Spain;37.3984773;-5.994282;73;false;false;Contemporary;This unusual restaurant, located opposite the famous Alameda de Hércules, inside the small Corner House hotel, features two contemporary-style dining rooms plus a pleasant terrace. The seasonal menu is mainly based around local and Andalucian ingredients, although this is spiced up with the occasional influence from around the world (Asia, Mexico, USA etc). Some of the long-established dishes here have evolved from the owners’ past ventures, such as the popular “huevos estrellados” from the erstwhile El Gallinero de Sandra restaurant.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8634;Tellus;Spain;Córdoba;María La Judía, Córdoba, 14011, Spain;37.8972343;-4.7930693;22;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant takes its name from the goddess representing the earth in Roman mythology and is used here as an allegory to the seasonality of the contemporary cuisine on offer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8635;La Tartarería Raw food;Spain;Barcelona;Muntaner 26, Barcelona, 08011, Spain;41.3852465;2.1612755;75;true;false;Contemporary;As its name implies, the leitmotiv of this restaurant is tartare, as demonstrated by dishes featuring salmon, tuna, pumpkin etc, along with other dishes that align with its “raw food” philosophy. Two set menus are also available, one of which is a tasting option.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8636;Borona Bistró;Spain;Cáceres;General Ezponda 3 bajo, Cáceres, 10001, Spain;39.4755043;-6.3720446;39;false;true;Contemporary;A small, centrally located restaurant that takes its name from the famous corn bread traditionally eaten in the north of Spain, particularly in Galicia and Asturias. The couple in charge (Víctor in the kitchen and Rocío front of house) create cuisine that is high on detail and pays dutiful respect to the culinary traditions and flavours of Extremadura, while adding a contemporary touch through modern technique and presentation. The cooking here is based around three tasting menus entitled Jariza, Jaramago and Mercado (the latter, shorter and more affordably priced, is only available on weekdays). One dish that particularly stood out was the suckling pig’s ear with white prawn tartare, which is always on the menu but with a garnish that changes with the seasons.;Air conditioning;[]
8637;Casa Paco;Spain;Chipiona;Puerto Deportivo de Chipiona, Chipiona, 11550, Spain;36.7461879;-6.4280577;94;true;true;Seafood;Casa Paco features a bar, a maritime-inspired dining room and a large terrace overlooking the pleasure boats moored in the marina. Its famous prawns (langostinos del alba) are a must!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8638;Ikigai Velázquez;Spain;Madrid;Velázquez 136, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4396371;-3.6827647;24;false;true;Japanese;The younger sibling of Ikigai boasts a meticulous interior design featuring decorative details inspired by New York apartments of the 1980s. It also boasts a sushi bar that takes centre stage and is visible from every corner of the dining room. Japanese-inspired à la carte plus a set menu option that includes dishes taken from the former.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
8639;Nákar;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Fernando Guanarteme 10, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35007, Spain;28.1386092;-15.4335889;47;true;false;Contemporary;Located close to Las Canteras beach, Nákar boasts a minimalist contemporary decor that provides the backdrop for traditional Basque-Navarre cuisine that is superbly presented and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8640;Umiko;Spain;Madrid;De Los Madrazo 6, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4174926;-3.6979602;64;false;false;Japanese, Fusion;If you’re keen to try a different type of dining experience, this restaurant will surprise you with its size and its choice of dining spaces (when you make your booking, you’ll need to choose either the restaurant itself, the sushi bar or the so-called “Zona Blanca”). The menu here features Japanese fusion cuisine that makes use of Spanish ingredients and showcases influences from different regions across Spain (particularly Madrid) and other countries (France, Italy etc). Umiko works with Japanese “koshihikari” rice that is flavoured with different vinegars. Its desserts always come as a surprise, reminding us of our childhood through reinterpreted takes on Spanish sweet delicacies such as “Pink Panther” and Phoskito (which they have renamed Phosmiko). Don’t miss the tuna belly nigiri with Wagyu fat or the “sam” of Iberian Señorío de Montanera pork ribs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8641;Ferreruela;Spain;Lleida;Bobalà 8, Lleida, 25004, Spain;41.6224765;0.6297269;48;true;false;Farm to table;This rustic-contemporary restaurant occupying an old warehouse serves traditional-Catalan cuisine that changes daily in line with market availability. All the main dishes here are cooked on the open grill.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8642;Mas Romeu;Spain;Lloret de Mar;Av. Mas Romeu, 3, Lloret de Mar, 17310, Spain;41.7152289;2.8325811;45;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A little away from the centre but with a pleasant tree - shaded terrace. This family - run restaurant offers several set menus alongside an extensive à la carte with sections devoted to grilled meats, fish, seafood, stews and house specialities.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8643;Ó Fragón;Spain;Fisterra;San Martiño de Arriba 22, Fisterra, 15154, Spain;42.923523;-9.272529;31;false;false;Galician;A unique restaurant with a modern feel in the upper part of town, hence its impressive views of the port, estuary and Langosteira beach. Ó Fragón’s up-to-date cuisine is inspired by availability in the market and at the fish auction and is presented on an à la carte and two tasting menus. An interesting footnote is the excellent choice of artisanal Galician cheeses, served with delicious homemade bread.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8644;Surtopía;Spain;Madrid;Núñez de Balboa 106, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4355159;-3.681812;34;true;true;Andalusian;A restaurant with a modern ambience that takes guests on a journey exploring the flavours of Andalucia. The menu here features fish and seafood direct from the auctions in Cádiz and Almería, select meat and Iberian ham from Huelva and Córdoba, and cheeses from the Sierra de Grazalema – all prepared with an innovative touch and contemporary technique. Excellent wines from Sanlúcar and media ración options complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8645;O'Grelo;Spain;Madrid;Menorca 39, Madrid, 28009, Spain;40.4193953;-3.6744722;97;true;true;Galician;A classic address for Galician cuisine in the Spanish capital, O grelo has been serving the best fish and seafood from NW Spain for over three decades. The extensive choice on offer, including standout dishes such as spider crab and different cuts of hake from Burela, is complemented by delicious savoury rice dishes and an excellent choice of Galician meats.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8646;Beç;Andorra;Escaldes-Engordany;Copríncep François Mitterrand 2, Escaldes-Engordany, AD700, Andorra;42.51118;1.53799;90;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re looking for a spectacular setting in which to eat near the Caldea spa, this restaurant in a shopping district just two minutes’ walk away could be the place. To a welcoming contemporary backdrop featuring a profusion of wood and an open-view kitchen, enjoy an updated take on traditional cuisine. Standout dishes include aged beef loin tartare, pigs’ trotters stuffed with prawns from Sant Carles and several seasonal specialities such as Maresme peas with wild mushrooms and white prawns.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8647;Tuétano;Spain;Mérida;John Lennon 26, Mérida, 06800, Spain;38.91481;-6.34534;41;true;true;Meats and Grills, Regional Cuisine;Located just a few steps from the city’s historic Alcazaba, and standing above some of Mérida’s Roman remains visible through a glass floor, this restaurant is definitely worth considering for tapas, a meal or just a drink given the pleasant Roof Bar on the first floor. The cuisine here, including a good selection of Joselito-branded starters and select grilled meats, also features two tasting menus (4 and 8 courses), the longer of the two with a wine-pairing option.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8648;TAMPU;Spain;Madrid;Prim 13, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.421894;-3.6934524;94;false;false;Peruvian;TAMPU’s decor stands out for its meticulous combination of slate, wood and wicker, as well for a name that is in reference to old lodgings built along the Inca Trail. Here, you will find classic Peruvian and fusion cuisine that has been adapted to Spanish palates, and portions that that are reasonably substantial. You’ll find lots of interesting dishes on the menu, including standout options such as the Amazon ceviche, “Pachamanquero” ceviche, “Chinese-Creole” sanguchito and the “Lúcuma en texturas”, a dessert based around an exotic fruit that is highly prized in Peru.;Air conditioning;[]
8649;Alabaster;Spain;Madrid;Montalbán 9, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4180855;-3.6898091;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In an excellent location next to the Retiro park, Alabaster is home to a gastro-bar with high tables for an informal supper, an impressive glass-fronted wine cellar, and a spacious dining room complemented by two private spaces. Updated seasonal and traditional cuisine, with the menu divided into two parts (Comparte and Disfruta). Don’t miss the toasted meringue tart with lemon cream!;Air conditioning;[]
8650;La Tasquita de Enfrente;Spain;Madrid;Ballesta 6, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.42133;-3.70362;63;false;false;International;This welcoming restaurant tucked away behind the busy Gran Vía has made a name for itself thanks to its modern take on French-inspired cuisine that can be savoured on an impressive tasting menu. The latter changes daily in line with high-quality and easily recognisable market-fresh ingredients with a permanent focus on local provenance and seasonality. À la carte dining is also an option here.;Air conditioning;[]
8651;La Perla de Jávea;Spain;Xàbia;Avenida de la Llibertat 21, Xàbia, 03730, Spain;38.7714185;0.192579;66;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Located directly on the seafront promenade, hence its perfect sunset setting. In this bright, contemporary restaurant boasting superb views, the full bounty of the sea is honoured through traditional cooking that is always based around the freshest ingredients. Choose between an array of rice (for a minimum of two people) and fideuá dishes, as well as a good choice of meat, plus a selection of superb fish from the auction in Xàbia. The turbot with pilpil is worthy of special mention, thanks to its mouthwatering grilled aromas.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8652;Marcela;Spain;Leon;Plaza de San Marcelo 9, Leon, 24003, Spain;42.5977935;-5.5700503;52;true;false;Farm to table, Meats and Seafood;Marcela boasts an outstanding location just a few metres from the Museo Casa Botines Gaudí. It features two dining spaces: an informal tapas option on the ground floor and a more sophisticated dining room upstairs - between the two is a striking glass floor adorned with a water feature. The cuisine here is based around ingredients of the highest quality and includes a tasting menu and impressive daily recommendations. Thanks to its collaboration with the city’s auditorium, live music concerts are often held here on Fridays and Saturdays.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8653;Las Lías Bilbao;Spain;Bilbao;Juan Ajuriaguerra Kalea 14, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2656446;-2.9324748;33;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Tucked away in the lively and bustling city of Bilbao and boasting a large on-street terrace, this gastro-bar is the perfect setting in which to enjoy the true culinary flavour of the Basque Country. Take your pick between an extensive array of tapas and “raciones” and a small menu, but whatever you choose, make sure you try the flavoursome crab-filled scallops, and the entrecôte of aged Frisona Gallega beef. There’s an extensive choice of local wines that the friendly staff will be happy to serve by the glass.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8654;Kabia;Spain;Zumarraga;Legazpi 5, Zumarraga, 20700, Spain;43.0899079;-2.3151273;32;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In this well-run family restaurant with a strong connection to the land and a focus on traditional cuisine with a contemporary twist, the emphasis is also on an honest approach and locally sourced seasonal ingredients. The cuisine is centred on a single tasting menu featuring dishes such as duck breast tartare, creamy rice with squid and sautéed crayfish, and braised veal cheek with port wine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8655;Quema;Spain;Saragossa;Paseo María Agustín 20, Saragossa, 50004, Spain;41.651257;-0.8901065;23;false;false;Contemporary;Despite its functional appearance, this restaurant situated next to the imposing Pablo Serrano IAACC (Aragonese Institute of Contemporary Art and Culture) building serves cuisine that is high on quality but low on price. In this informal, multi-purpose setting, guests can choose from a reasonably priced contemporary-style menu with a good choice of dishes and observe the chefs at work in the open-view kitchen behind the bar. Half of the wines available come from the local region.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8656;Nito;Spain;Viveiro;Playa de Area 1, Viveiro, 27850, Spain;43.6856118;-7.5807723;87;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Galician;If you’re looking for a recommendation for a restaurant in which to enjoy excellent Galician fish and seafood, it’s well worth jotting down the name of this eatery inside the Hotel Ego, which has been in the hands of the same family since 1970. It takes its name from the owner, who continues to buy fish such as hake and tuna at the auctions in Celeiro and Burela. Standout out dishes here include “salpicón” of lobster, squid in its own ink, and the tuna roll in season. The modern and attractively laid-out terrace enjoys stunning views of the sea, beach and mountains.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
8657;Iki;Spain;Seville;Luis de Morales 2, Seville, 41018, Spain;37.3865676;-5.9726301;91;true;true;Japanese;With its menu of sashimi, tataki, gyozas, uromaki rolls etc, this small Japanese restaurant located just a few metres from the Ramón Sánchez-Pizjuán stadium is gaining an ever-increasing local fanbase. In its attractive dining room, embellished with designer details and a pleasant bar from where the chefs can be observed hard at work (their skill at slicing fish and preparing tempura is particularly impressive), enjoy traditionally inspired Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8658;El Albero;Spain;Ceutí;Mallorca 10, Ceutí, 30562, Spain;38.07749;-1.2721275;73;true;false;International;A pleasantly surprising option in this small town and featuring two distinct ambiences: the unpretentious and original bar serving the daily menu and decorated with bulls’ heads, and the meticulously arranged contemporary dining room for the à la carte and tasting menus. The cooking here varies between an array of tapas-style dishes, a section devoted to fusion-style Japanese cuisine, and what El Albero refers to as El Catarrás, a culinary project that focuses on the traditional Murciana hen.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8659;La Maruca - Velázquez;Spain;Madrid;Velázquez 54, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.427669;-3.6838762;82;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant that exudes a fresh, optimistic approach through two iconic themes, namely Santander and Cantabria. This lively and informal setting features a multi-purpose bar and contemporary dining spaces embellished with the occasional designer detail. Its à la carte reflects cuisine that is 100% traditional, with a predominance of Cantabrian dishes (Cantabrian anchovies, fried squid from Santander, hake direct from the fish auction etc) with an equal focus on preparation and high-quality ingredients. Make sure you try the famous Cañadío cheesecake, the recipe for which has remained unchanged since 1981.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8660;Leña Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana 57, Madrid, 28046, Spain;40.4385494;-3.6913607;91;false;false;Meats and Grills;A restaurant with an attractive interior design and steakhouse philosophy under the baton of award-winning chef Dani García, who oversees everything here. The stars of the show are the dishes cooked on the open grill (the menu also includes plenty of starters and mains to share), with a few grilled fish options and a huge choice of different cuts and matured meats (beef ribeye, veal porterhouse, grilled sirloin, tomahawk etc). Occasionally, and for a limited period, it also serves a few of this famous Marbella chef’s iconic dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
8661;Amparito Roca;Spain;Madrid;Juan Bravo 12, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4327796;-3.6846401;21;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;One of those restaurants that never fails to impress and feels as though it has been a long-standing fixture on the Madrid dining scene, establishing a hugely loyal following in the city in a short space of time, especially amongst its business community. Named after a famous pasodoble, it focuses on well-prepared honest and traditional cuisine on an à la carte featuring copious dishes that always includes one or two game-based escabeches. The decorative detail here comes as an added surprise!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8662;Marcano;Spain;Madrid;Doctor Castelo 31, Madrid, 28009, Spain;40.4204191;-3.6752962;63;true;false;International;This restaurant just a few steps from the Retiro park reflects the culinary passion of chef David Marcano, who trained alongside the San Sebastián-born maestro Juan Mari Arzak. In this contemporary space featuring bare tables, enjoy innovative contemporary dishes showcasing Basque touches and an international influence and with a continual quest for flavour. The friendly kitchen team is happy for guests to order half plates and dishes for sharing.;Air conditioning;[]
8663;La Marmita de Ancha;Spain;Cadiz;Ancha 7, Cadiz, 11001, Spain;36.5341032;-6.2983;51;false;false;Andalusian;A restaurant with a meticulous contemporary decor including paintings that showcase the sea and traditional tuna fishing. Andalucian cuisine featuring high-quality ingredients, Asian influences and a heavy focus on red tuna.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8664;Zaldiarán;Spain;Vitoria-Gasteiz;Avenida Gasteiz 21, Vitoria-Gasteiz, 01008, Spain;42.8444681;-2.6825454;48;true;false;Contemporary;A classic local address which has been brought impressively up to date. Choose between the informal tapas space and the more elegant dining room serving contemporary cuisine with a subtle innovative touch.;Air conditioning;[]
8665;Crudo;Spain;Saragossa;Doctor Cerrada 40, Saragossa, 50005, Spain;41.6455171;-0.8906051;46;false;false;Fusion;This casual, informal eatery describes itself as a gourmet taberna to prepare you for the fact that it isn’t a regular style of restaurant. Its identity is built around raw and marinated ingredients, with dishes featuring on a small à la carte with influences from Japan, the Mediterranean and Latin America, the latter represented by dishes such as the sea bass tiradito. Booking advisable.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8666;Epeleta;Spain;Lekunberri;Aralar s/n, Lekunberri, 31870, Spain;43.0138075;-1.9028523;100;false;true;Meats and Grills;One of those restaurants that is well worth recommending for its welcoming atmosphere and honest cuisine. It occupies an attractive house with a bar and dining room, each of which is carefully furnished in rustic style. The Epeleta prides itself on its excellent grilled fish and meat dishes.;Car park;[]
8667;Al Norte;Spain;Jarandilla de la Vera;Avenida Soledad Vega Ortiz 125, Jarandilla de la Vera, 10450, Spain;40.1300279;-5.6631374;76;true;false;Contemporary, Fusion;A colourful yet unassuming eatery with a kitchen adjoining the dining room. The chef, who has worked in several leading restaurants and has a strong focus on presentation, showcases his talents via a traditionally inspired menu which is particularly designed for sharing. It features modern, fusion-inspired influences that take the palate on a journey around the world through dishes such as tomato “torrija” with smoked sardine, veal cheeks with papaya etc.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8668;Deliciosamarta;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Escritor Benito Pérez Galdós 33, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35002, Spain;28.1060679;-15.4190254;99;false;true;Creative;A restaurant with plenty of personality and an appealing decor along an attractive pedestrian street in the city’s Triana district. Its cuisine is equally impressive, featuring market-inspired cooking with a modern touch and influences from the Canary Islands that is only available à la carte. We recommend booking ahead.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8669;Gresca;Spain;Barcelona;Provença 230, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3913285;2.1570384;26;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A reference for foodies, Gresca features an open kitchen that enables the bar area to be connected to the dining room. The cuisine here is based around delicious small plates with a contemporary feel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8670;Gran Azul;Spain;Valencia;Avenida Aragón 12, Valencia, 46021, Spain;39.469364;-0.3589203;65;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A spacious and modern restaurant that successfully focuses on rice and grilled dishes as highlighted by its own motto. Here, fish sourced directly from the market and top-quality beef take centre stage.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8671;Paco Espinosa;Spain;Valladolid;Paseo Obregón 16, Valladolid, 47009, Spain;41.6658114;-4.7317513;74;true;true;Seafood;This restaurant, located in the La Victoria district of the city, boasts a popular tapas bar by the entrance plus a dining room in which the reasonably varied à la carte stands out for its quality. On it, you’ll find delicious Iberian ham, scrambled egg dishes, home-style stews, as well as superb fish and seafood (red prawns, scallops with onions, baked sea bass with garlic etc), which is unusual given the restaurant’s distance from the sea. The extensive wine list features several international labels.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8672;Ca's Milà;Spain;Sant Josep de sa Talaia;Playa de Cala Tarida, Sant Josep de sa Talaia, 07829, Spain;38.940023;1.2371103;81;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A restaurant in which to savour the flavours, aromas and sea views to the full. Along with its simplicity, Ca's Milà stands out for its homely atmosphere, attentive service and its location right by the beach, practically clinging to the cliff, along with charming terraces and romantic views. Its traditional Ibizan cuisine specialises in fish (mainly cooked à la plancha or on the grill) and rice dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8673;El Almacén;Spain;Ávila;Carretera de Salamanca 6, Ávila, 05002, Spain;40.6575595;-4.7095654;27;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Occupying a former wheat store (almacén) outside of Ávila’s historic centre, this restaurant boasts outstanding views of the city’s imposing medieval walls. À la carte dishes and daily recommendations.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8674;Tony García Espacio Gastronómico;Spain;Almería;Avenida del Mediterráneo 281, Almería, 04009, Spain;36.8496989;-2.4467569;69;true;false;Contemporary;Choose between the informal gastro-bar and an attractive dining room where the fusion cuisine on offer combines the traditional and the contemporary. Products from Almería take centre-stage here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8675;Ajo de Sopas;Spain;Palencia;Paseo del Salón 25, Palencia, 34002, Spain;42.0071336;-4.5276914;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A creative restaurant which focuses on local products and takes guests on a traditional culinary voyage across the Castille region. The highly successful tasting menu is available by prior booking only.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8676;Adrián Quetglas;Spain;Palma;Paseo de Mallorca 20, Palma, 07012, Spain;39.5734906;2.6432285;47;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant that is as original as it is stylish, usually full and always meets with expectations. Located in the heart of Palma, overlooking the bed of the Torrent de Sa Riera canal, it boasts a welcoming, bistro-style ambience with attractive bonuses such as a vertical garden and a pleasant vibe created by the jazz music playing in the background. The owner-chef’s goal is to democratise haute cuisine and showcase cooking full of nuances and variations (including from his native Buenos Aires) with a strong focus on Mediterranean flavours and unequivocal influences from his time working in London, Paris and even Moscow. Choose between the 5- and 8-course tasting menus, both with a wine-pairing option (for a supplement you can also add in options such as pigeon, caviar and a cheese course).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8678;Kava;Spain;Marbella;Avenida Antonio Belón 4, Marbella, 29602, Spain;36.5080487;-4.8874614;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Fusion;A contemporary yet intimate restaurant with a focus on modern cooking which aims to incorporate the traditional flavours of Andalucian cuisine through the use of locally sourced ingredients (it usually focuses on three per month), but without neglecting influences from further afield. The chefs serve their dishes in person so they can explain their dishes in greater detail, including a cheesecake that is out of this world!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8679;Ikaitz;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Paseo Colón 21, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20002, Spain;43.3234738;-1.9767138;51;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This pleasant family-run restaurant in a good location in the Gros district of the city focuses on traditional-regional cuisine and is almost always full, including with many foreign visitors who are attracted by cuisine with an authentic Basque flavour and generous portions. Ikaitz’s à la carte features delicious fish, premium meats and plenty of locally sourced ingredients. These are showcased in dishes such as grilled octopus with a creamy purée and paprika, and boneless oxtail in its own jus, served with vegetables and almonds.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8680;El Santo;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Escritor Benito Pérez Galdós 23, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35002, Spain;28.1063258;-15.41926;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;El Santo boasts an excellent location in the Triana district, a part of the old town with a special beauty and character that result from its original occupation by residents who settled here mainly from Andalucía. The restaurant features a pleasantly surprising decor that combines the stone walls of this restored property with attractive tropical details. To this backdrop, guests can savour bold cuisine that showcases typical Canary island recipes, with a fusion of Mexican cooking visible in some dishes. Don’t miss the black “papa arrugada” potatoes with mojo “snow” and mole mojo!;Air conditioning;[]
8681;Solc;Spain;Barcelona;Paseo de Gràcia 68, Barcelona, 08007, Spain;41.3934967;2.1639185;72;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Catalan;Solc is located on the first floor of the elegant Majestic Hotel & Spa Barcelona, hence the aristocratic air that pervades the entire building. The Mediterranean cuisine in evidence here has a clear Catalan DNA, both on the à la carte and the tasting menu (the latter featuring dishes from the former), and showcases ingredients from the nearby Maresme area, where the restaurant has its own farm which provides much of the produce used here on a daily basis. A hugely popular brunch is also available every Sunday, but given its popularity we definitely recommend booking a table in advance.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
8682;Ají;Spain;Barcelona;Marina 19, Barcelona, 08005, Spain;41.3869412;2.1968022;37;false;false;Fusion, Peruvian;The name, which translates as "chilli pepper" in Peruvian Spanish and "taste" in Japanese, gives us a good insight into the culinary intentions of this restaurant. Japanese cuisine with a focus on well defined textures and flavours.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8683;El Rais;Spain;Mahon;Moll de Llevant 314 (puerto), Mahon, 07701, Spain;39.8874518;4.2749116;77;true;false;Farm to table;Guests will thoroughly enjoy El Rais’ setting and outdoor terraces overlooking the moorings of the Club Marítimo. Here, owner-chefs Marco Antonio Collado and Oriol Castel champion contemporary cuisine based around Menorcan recipes, plus an enticing array of rice dishes that are particularly popular with locals and visitors alike. These include “arroz de senyoret”, black rice, rice with Iberian pork “pluma” with Triguero asparagus etc. Booking ahead is recommended.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
8684;Can Carlitos;Spain;La Savina;Almadrava, La Savina, 07870, Spain;38.7331133;1.4141666;97;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;Can Carlitos occupies an old house in the style of an open terrace right by the beach, where tables are set up practically at the water’s edge! Traditional cuisine overseen and brought up to date by chef Nandu Jubany.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8685;Barmutet;Spain;Vic;De la Ciutat 2, Vic, 08500, Spain;41.9298917;2.2548145;38;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A halfway house between a small bistro and a taberna, Barmutet offers guests a highly varied menu of tapas and “raciones”, grilled dishes, seafood, high-quality canned products and pickles, plus numerous wines and vermouths.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8686;Saiti;Spain;Valencia;Reina Doña Germana 4, Valencia, 46005, Spain;39.4636136;-0.3663875;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An attractive restaurant impressively run by a chef who is a staunch believer in modern cooking with its roots in traditional Mediterranean cuisine. Several tasting menus, including a lunchtime “business” menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8687;El Asador de Abel - Casa Farpón;Spain;Argüelles;La Revuelta del Coche, Argüelles, 33188, Spain;43.3857379;-5.730567;81;false;false;Regional Cuisine;A classic address that has had a new lease of life under the reins of chef Javier Álvarez, who has made the move here from the now-closed Casa Farpón de Mamorana. It has retained its rustic ‘asador’ appearance with the open grill visible from the dining room, where the market-inspired menu is focused around various hearty dishes (the Argüelles stew with “compango”, a mix of different meats, is outstanding), daily specials (such as filled potatoes, the thick Asturian “pote” soup, and Verdina beans with spider crab), fresh, traditionally caught fish from Rula, Trasacar red meats, plus an impressive tasting menu. The extensive cellar features a selection of Asturian wines.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8688;Celeste y Don Carlos;Spain;Alacant;General Primo de Rivera 12, Alacant, 03002, Spain;38.34762;-0.484414;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A gastronomic restaurant offering innovative international- and French-inspired cuisine which is always based around seasonal market ingredients. Tasting menus are the only option here, one of which is inspired by the period the chef spent working in the kitchen of the Hotel Ritz in Paris. Booking essential.;Air conditioning;[]
8689;Tram-Tram;Spain;Barcelona;Major de Sarrià 121, Barcelona, 08017, Spain;41.4007963;2.1204239;48;false;false;Contemporary;Tram-Tram is a classically furnished restaurant, the name of which pays homage to this old form of transport. Updated traditional cuisine along with the occasional international dish, plus a tasting menu option.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8690;Es Cranc;Spain;Fornells;Escoles 31, Fornells, 07748, Spain;40.0571545;4.1320906;17;true;true;Seafood;A restaurant with a simple, rustic feel in a building with whitewashed walls and plenty of character. It is particularly renowned for its lobster stew (“caldereta de langosta”).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8691;Joan Marc;Spain;Inca;Plaza del Blanquer 17, Inca, 07300, Spain;39.7221459;2.9056108;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In this bright restaurant, with its natural and contemporary design in which wood plays a central role, discover seasonal cuisine that always showcases the island’s flavours. It offers a huge array of tapas (vegetarian, classic, meat, fish and seafood, free-range eggs, tapas for dipping etc), along with dishes with a traditional Mallorcan influence and two tasting menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8692;Lilium;Spain;Arrecife;Avenida Olof Palme, Arrecife, 35500, Spain;28.9622091;-13.5389613;46;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The perfect opportunity to discover a modern version of typical Canary Islands cuisine! Located in the new La Marina district, this restaurant boasts a glass-fronted façade, a simple, contemporary-style dining room, plus a terrace with views of the boats moored in the marina. In the completely open-view kitchen, the focus is on island cuisine which has been brought bang up to date. The à la carte, which showcases native Canary Island products, is complemented by a tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
8693;Casa Eladio;Spain;Marbella;Virgen de los Dolores 6, Marbella, 29601, Spain;36.5109688;-4.8847409;27;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;A restaurant with a contemporary, maritime-inspired decor and a long history which has had a new lease of life with the third generation of the family now working the kitchens. The updated traditional cuisine, based around seasonal, locally sourced ingredients, is also heavily focused on the sea without neglecting the country’s iconic acorn-fed Iberian pigs. On the à la carte, which is complemented by two tasting menus (Esencia and Camino del Sur), we particularly enjoyed the red tuna tartare with a white almond cream sauce, young salad leaves and mango.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8694;Don Fadrique;Spain;Alba de Tormes;Carretera de Salamanca, Alba de Tormes, 37800, Spain;40.832726;-5.526464;100;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;At Don Fadrique, there’s a commonsense approach to the cuisine that makes its way from the kitchen to the table. This is showcased on an à la carte (including half portions), with an updated take on traditional cooking and a focus on the seasons, and two tasting menus: “Sabor de la Memoria”, with its homage to tradition and top-quality ingredients (including grilled fish and meat), and Instinto, a more personal and modern option which gives free rein to the chef’s creativity (prior booking required). The chef also presents and serves many of the dishes himself.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8695;Compartir Cadaqués;Spain;Cadaqués;Riera Sant Vicenç, Cadaqués, 17488, Spain;42.2893271;3.2760081;16;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;If you’re visiting Cadaqués, the iconic village along the Costa Brava which provided the backdrop for the love affair between Gala and the mercurial Salvador Dalí, this is the best option in which to pause and refuel! The restaurant, boasting a stunning internal patio-terrace, occupies a rustic property with a decor of slate, stone and wood. The aim of the cuisine, overseen by award-winning chefs from Disfrutar in Barcelona, is to offer a more informal format designed for sharing, with a strong emphasis on local provenance and traditional flavours. The à la carte, with one section attributed to oysters and another to rice dishes, is complemented by a tasting menu served to the entire table. The combined focus on delicate ingredients and superb cooking techniques adds to the dining experience here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8696;La Fábrica;Spain;Burgos;San Juan 3, Burgos, 09003, Spain;42.343159;-3.7003757;30;true;false;Contemporary;Chef Ricardo Temiño’s restaurant, which has now moved to the centre of Burgos (next to the San Juan civic centre), boasts an elegantly minimalist interior which provides the backdrop for high-quality contemporary cuisine teeming with flavour and inspired by traditional and international recipes. The à la carte includes an option to order small plates and dishes for sharing, enabling guests to discover many different dishes. This is complemented by a constantly changing menu called Temporada (Season). An adjoining dining space (Ricardo Temiño), but with the same entrance, offers more personal and sophisticated cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8697;Benet;Spain;Les Borges Blanques;Plaza del 1 de Octubre 21-23, Les Borges Blanques, 25400, Spain;41.521535;0.8676454;27;true;true;Catalan, Traditional Cuisine;This family-run restaurant occupies a building with plenty of history behind it and which once served as a mill and the town hall. Updated Catalan cuisine, including a menu paired with its own olive oil.;Air conditioning;[]
8698;Miga;Spain;A Coruña;Plaza de España 7, A Coruña, 15001, Spain;43.3727266;-8.3963644;29;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;An attractive bistro-style taberna featuring a terrace, a bar where guests can also choose to eat if they wish, and two dining rooms with stone walls. The updated take on traditional cuisine perfect for sharing includes seasonal and market-inspired dishes, daily suggestions and Miga’s signature dishes such as the langoustine salad, the exquisite aged-beef tartare, and the boneless tripe stew (“callos de Miga”).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8699;El Pedrusco de Aldealcorvo;Spain;Madrid;Juan de Austria 27, Madrid, 28010, Spain;40.4338851;-3.6999968;27;true;false;Castilian;A restaurant with an elegant Castilian air in which roast lamb and suckling pig are the undoubted stars on the menu, accompanied by other traditional dishes from the “meseta” which are striking for their lightness of touch yet fullness of flavour. The century-old wood-fired oven is still in operation here!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8700;Regueiro;Spain;Tox;Tox, Tox, 33793, Spain;43.5586387;-6.6368609;76;false;false;Creative, Fusion;This chalet-style property in the middle of the countryside features a dining room upstairs with a contemporary-urban decor, an open kitchen, and attractive views of the surrounding landscape. Regueiro’s particularly tasty cuisine has its roots in India (curry dishes and the tandoori oven are prominent features here) as well as recipes from South East Asia.;Car park;[]
8701;Dos Pebrots;Spain;Barcelona;Doctor Dou 19, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.3829199;2.1683251;19;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;If you’re looking for somewhere that reflects the essence of Mediterranean cooking, this restaurant in the El Raval district, close to MACBA (Museu d'Art Contemporani de Barcelona), is a superb option. In the open-view kitchen, with its signature Josper grill, the focus is on the evolution of gourmet cuisine and the variety of Mediterranean flavours which are showcased on an interesting à la carte (each dish is accompanied by information to explain its history) and three meticulously presented menus. Take a seat at the bar to enjoy the experience to the full.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8702;La Bodeguilla;Spain;Terrassa;Provenza 4, Terrassa, 08226, Spain;41.5724007;2.0258718;41;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;La Bodeguilla’s meticulously appointed interior, showcasing a clear preference for wood, comes as a pleasant surprise. It serves seasonally inspired, traditional cuisine rich in textures and strong flavours.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8703;Tribeca;Spain;Seville;Chaves Nogales 3, Seville, 41018, Spain;37.3849957;-5.9790764;96;false;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;Taking its name from the famous district in New York, Tribeca can now be considered a classic dining address in Seville after two decades in business. The owner-chef, whose primary concern is that his guests are completely satisfied with their experience, works particularly with fresh fish from the Gulf of Cádiz. Choose between the tasting menu and a traditional à la carte with a modern touch, on both of which you’ll find dishes such as clams with manzanilla sherry, Carabinero prawn tartare, and lobster and Iberian pancetta tortilla.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8704;Ticiano;Spain;Villallano;Concepción, Villallano, 34815, Spain;42.7662899;-4.2355681;18;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Occupying former stables in this small village, Ticiano boasts an attractive, rustic dining room with a wood ceiling on the first floor, where the à la carte of traditional cooking stands out for its array of meat dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
8705;La Cuina de Can Simón;Spain;Tossa de Mar;Portal 24, Tossa de Mar, 17320, Spain;41.7165634;2.9324298;64;true;true;Contemporary;Tossa de Mar, the “blue paradise” that so enchanted Marc Chagall, is a medieval town full of opportunities for visitors, who can enjoy a stroll through its alleyways or a swim in its coves. If this appeals, make it the perfect day by heading to this gastronomic restaurant.Here, at the foot of the town’s walls, siblings Lores, Josep María and Xavier conjure up contemporary dishes that pay homage to their grandparents: in their own words, “our family is one of artists and fishermen, and it is from this heritage that our cooking developed, using natural, artisanal and locally sourced ingredients”. In keeping with the traditions of Mediterranean cuisine and the local fishing industry, fish and seafood are understandably their strong suit, sourced daily from the fish auction. However, they also offer dishes featuring rice and select cuts of meats that are more synonymous with the mountainous landscapes of inland Costa Brava.;Air conditioning;[]
8706;Habitual;Spain;Valencia;Jorge Juan 19, Valencia, 46004, Spain;39.4687302;-0.3689512;84;false;false;International, Contemporary;This unusual restaurant, part of chef Ricard Camarena’s stable, boasts a surprising design and layout on the lower floor of the Modernist-style Mercado de Colón. The extensive and affordable à la carte features several of the famous chef’s dishes from the past, with a focus on Mediterranean cooking but with the occasional nod to international cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
8707;Era Coquèla;Spain;Vielha;Avenida Garona 29, Vielha, 25530, Spain;42.701622;0.8003782;46;false;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Over time, this unpretentious restaurant, which takes its name from an iron pan that is typical of this valley, has developed into a culinary reference in the area. Its contemporary cuisine skilfully blends in harmoniously with more traditional dishes such as snails “a la llauna” and the hearty Aranese “olla” soup. Choose between the à la carte and two set menus: one attractively priced lunchtime option and a second more elaborate version called Garona.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8708;Mannix;Spain;Campaspero;Felipe II-26, Campaspero, 47310, Spain;41.4921179;-4.1962121;50;false;false;Lamb Specialities, Regional European;One of Spain’s most renowned Castilian-style “asadores”, this family-run restaurant with years of history behind it is particularly famous for its star dish: suckling Churra lamb which, in line with tradition is quartered, placed in earthenware dishes, then roasted in a wood-fired oven. Although the vast majority of its customers come here to savour this signature dish, other meat and offal specialities are also available (brain, trotters, sweetbreads, kidneys etc). Make sure you call and book ahead.;Air conditioning;[]
8709;Contraseña;Spain;Cadiz;San Francisco 33, Cadiz, 11004, Spain;36.5313279;-6.2931344;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Occupying the same street as its elder sibling (the one-Michelin-star Código de Barra, Contraseña is run by Léon Griffioen, a chef and errant spirit originally from the Netherlands who decided to unpack his suitcase for good in the “little silver cup” as Cádiz is affectionately known in Spanish. His modern, cheerful cuisine, with its roots set firmly in tradition, always aims to showcase local flavours and is centred around an extensive tasting menu with a wine pairing option. Here, guests are encouraged to eat with their eyes, discover with their sense of smell, and savour with their tastebuds!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8710;Cepa 21;Spain;Castrillo de Duero;Carretera N 122, Castrillo de Duero, 47318, Spain;41.6063818;-3.9966595;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A bright, contemporary restaurant on the first floor of the bodega of the same name, one of the best known in the Ribera del Duero wine region. Here, in a dining room boasting stunning views of the surrounding vineyards, savour cuisine with a contemporary touch on two tasting menus, both of which pay plenty of attention to presentation and the use of seasonal ingredients. Wine tours (prior booking required) and shopping in the on-site boutique add to the experience here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8711;Urbisol;Spain;Calders;Carretera N 141 C, Calders, 08279, Spain;41.8020149;2.0206953;70;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with lots of personality as it was the original focus of the business. In this comfortable and friendly setting, choose from an extensive à la carte of updated traditional dishes. The hotel’s attractively furnished guestrooms are an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8712;Er Occitan;Spain;Bossòst;Major 66, Bossòst, 25550, Spain;42.7878492;0.6940504;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A restaurant that has made a name for itself in the Arán valley! Here, the modern-inspired cooking is a surprising combination of locally sourced seasonal ingredients and Asian and Spanish-American flavours.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8713;Daica;Spain;Llubí;Nou 8, Llubí, 07430, Spain;39.7004114;3.0051244;42;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;Daica occupies an attractive townhouse with two rustic-contemporary dining rooms plus a pleasant patio. Here, the focus is on cooking with a traditional feel, enhanced by creative touches and a constant nod to ingredients sourced from the island, showcased exclusively on several set menus (including vegetarian and vegan options).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8714;El Racó;Spain;Sant Climent de Llobregat;Poca Farina 20, Sant Climent de Llobregat, 08849, Spain;41.3371924;1.9961897;79;false;true;Catalan, Traditional Cuisine;Somewhat tucked away along a pedestrian street in the centre of town, this longstanding hidden gem has passed from one generation to the next, in so doing successfully carrying the weight of family history on its shoulders. In its dining rooms, one for à la carte dining, the other next door to the kitchen and focused on the daily menu, enjoy traditional Catalan cuisine that features specialities such as “blue-footed chicken” (Prat breed), grilled Butifarra sausage, “mountain” chickpeas with lobster and, in a nod to the town’s star product, imaginative desserts featuring cherries in season. There’s a reason that chef Gèrard Solís is known locally as the “cherry chef”!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8715;Mesón de Pincelín;Spain;Almansa;Las Norias 10, Almansa, 02640, Spain;38.865561;-1.0949247;86;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In the hands of the same family since 1952, this classic and traditional restaurant boasts an impressive, regionally inspired ambience and decor that have contributed to its reputation over the decades. Choose between the bar section, with its tall tables for informal dining, and a variety of dining room and private spaces. The extensive regionally focused à la carte is complemented by several set menus.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8716;Jauregibarria;Spain;Amorebieta - Etxano;Bideaur Auzoa 4, Amorebieta - Etxano, 48340, Spain;43.212862;-2.7266743;37;false;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with an attractive interior design, occupying a country house over 200 years old surrounded by countryside. A highly contemporary take on traditional cooking, featuring the occasional Basque dish and haute cuisine influence.;Air conditioning;[]
8717;Taberna Canela en Rama;Spain;Baeza;Comendadores 6, Baeza, 23440, Spain;37.9901872;-3.4694712;88;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the town’s historic quarter and boasting a pleasant terrace. The tapas - focused cuisine here is in the same vein as at its older namesake in Linares. Traditional, regional cooking made for sharing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8718;Gaucho;Spain;Pamplona;Espoz y Mina 7, Pamplona, 31001, Spain;42.8163552;-1.6419183;75;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A must for those keen to discover some of the best tapas in Pamplona. Located in the heart of the city, Gaucho is a classic address for this gastronomic art form with its array of innovative and more traditional tapas.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8719;Bugao Madrid;Spain;Madrid;María de Molina 4, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4378032;-3.6890514;69;true;true;Farm to table;If you’re unfamiliar with cuisine from the Spanish enclave of Ceuta, this is now within reach in the heart of the Spanish capital in this highly elegant space with a somewhat surprising colonial glamour. Chef Hugo Ruiz sources his inspiration from the market and the seasons in dishes that feature fish from the Straits of Gibraltar – cooking that he defines as “between two seas”, with a focus on different cuts of mouth-watering red tuna (neck, mid and lower belly etc) that take centre stage on both the à la carte and tasting menu. Make sure you also try the flatbread with Motril shrimps, as well as one of Bugao’s signature cocktails.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8720;BaceLo;Spain;Ferrol;Dolores 44, Ferrol, 15401, Spain;43.4835737;-8.2352258;100;true;false;Contemporary;An informal eatery in a pedestrian street in the centre of Ferrol, where it is impressively run by a young couple, both of whom work in the kitchen. Updated traditional cuisine designed for sharing.;Air conditioning;[]
8721;Raff San Pedro;Spain;Cuenca;San Pedro 58, Cuenca, 16001, Spain;40.0809835;-2.1282603;69;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Part of the Leonor de Aquitania hotel, where it occupies the former stables of an aristocratic stone mansion. Updated traditional cuisine and interesting set menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8722;Es Caló;Spain;Es Caló;Vicari Joan Marí 14, Es Caló, 07871, Spain;38.676888;1.5184314;48;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant restaurant overlooking the sea and its incredible turquoise water. Savour elaborately prepared Spanish cuisine, including excellent fish and delicious savoury rice dishes.;Wheelchair access;[]
8723;Ca na Pilar;Spain;Es Migjorn Gran;Avenida de la Mar 1, Es Migjorn Gran, 07749, Spain;39.9453565;4.0502147;30;false;false;Contemporary, Farm to table;This restaurant occupies a typical 200-year-old house on the approach to Es Migjorn Gran in the centre of the island. It features an interior with a rustic-contemporary feel, plus an attractive patio-terrace that can only be booked for dinner. Here, the culinary focus is on simple, honest cooking with interesting French-inspired touches and dishes based around the best market-fresh local ingredients. We can highly recommended the surf and turf carpaccio with scallops, which comes as a pleasant surprise!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8724;Casa Cantó;Spain;Benissa;Avenida País Valencià 223, Benissa, 03720, Spain;38.7128081;0.0447025;25;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant has several dining rooms. The main one of which has a glass - fronted wine cellar and a large picture window affording views of the whole valley, including the Peñón de Ifach in the distance. Its regional menu is enlivened by a good selection of rice dishes and freshly caught fish.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8725;Ten's;Spain;Barcelona;Avenida Marqués de l'Argentera 11, Barcelona, 08003, Spain;41.3842166;2.1843508;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A minimalist gastro-bar overseen by famous chef Jordi Cruz. The focus here is on individual tapas that include different types of oysters (“natural”, with Bloody Mary, gazpachuelo etc), an impressive array of “raciones” designed for sharing, elaborate desserts, plus a tapas tasting menu entitled Ten's that is only served to the whole table and is the perfect option to get a true insight into the cuisine here. One dish that bowled us over was the Japanese-style tiradito with cured gilthead bream, gazpachuelo, grapes, kumquat and seaweed.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8726;Casa Brito;Spain;Arucas;Pasaje Ter 17, Arucas, 35412, Spain;28.105516;-15.528073;46;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Meats and Grills;Casa Brito is famous on the island both for its cooking, which is traditional and superbly prepared, and the high level of service provided by its staff, who are friendly and used to working with a local clientele. The set-up here includes a private bar and two rustically inspired dining rooms, the main one of which has an open grill and wood ceilings. The speciality here is the perfectly cooked grilled beef from Germany, Uruguay and the Spanish regions of Castilla, Galicia and Asturias. The barbecued chorizo and the delicious grilled chops of young Baifo goat (the island’s native species) are also well worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8727;Paco Meralgo;Spain;Barcelona;Muntaner 171, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3916774;2.1525529;78;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A tapas bar that defines itself as a “high tavern” of this culinary art. Choose from a menu of open sandwiches (montaditos), daily specials, delicious meats, and fish direct from the auction, as well as the occasional rice dish at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8728;Osmosis;Spain;Barcelona;Aribau 100, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3902078;2.1570069;53;false;false;Creative;A restaurant with a pleasant, contemporary ambience split between two floors. The modern tasting menu (short and long versions) is based around seasonal, market-fresh ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
8729;El Bressol;Spain;Valencia;Serrano Morales 11, Valencia, 46004, Spain;39.4694686;-0.3653854;71;false;false;Farm to table;The very best the Mediterranean has to offer! The menu, announced at your table, focuses on fish and seafood and changes daily subject to availability at the fish auction.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
8730;Gotzon Jatetxea;Spain;Bakio;Luzarragako Bidea 2, Bakio, 48130, Spain;43.4300109;-2.8033178;20;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seafood;This family-run restaurant overlooking the beach, where the third generation is now in charge (with Longarai sisters Gotzone in the kitchen and Sorkunde in the dining room), has a long and successful history behind it. Here, guests can enjoy Basque cuisine prepared with seasonal ingredients, meat from trusted suppliers, as well as superb fish (we recommend asking about the catch of the day), and if you don’t mind getting your hands dirty, make sure you order the pan-fried langoustines. It’s well worth booking a dinner table on one of the terraces to enjoy the sunset here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8731;Erre que Erre;Spain;Ibi;Juan Brotóns 11, Ibi, 03440, Spain;38.6277242;-0.572461;32;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The use of the best locally sourced ingredients is strongly in evidence in contemporary-style dishes inspired by the Foia de Castalla area such as octopus with a potato parmentier, veal with wild mushrooms and truffles, and red tuna tartare. Located close to the centre of town, this restaurant with a contemporary yet informal feel combines its attractive and high-quality cuisine with a fair pricing structure with the option of smaller media-ración dishes for sharing. The town’s ice cream-making tradition lives on in Erre que Erre’s superb desserts!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8732;Jaizkibel;Spain;Madrid;Albasanz 67, Madrid, 28037, Spain;40.438917;-3.622285;95;false;true;Basque;In this restaurant located in a residential district of the city, the undisputed stars of the show are the ingredients (such as bonito tuna to which a special section of the menu is devoted in season) and flavour. The extensive à la carte of traditional Basque cooking, including an array of rice and cod dishes and stews, is complemented by a tasting menu. One standout dish that we particularly enjoyed was the “cogote de merluza” – simply cooked and delicious neck of hake drizzled with garlic and parsley oil.;Air conditioning;[]
8733;Xavier Pellicer;Spain;Barcelona;Provença 310, Barcelona, 08037, Spain;41.3959928;2.1633567;28;false;false;Creative;In this centrally located restaurant just a few metres from the city’s emblematic La Pedrera-Casa Milà building designed by Gaudí, the focus is on “healthy” cuisine that is centred around seasonal vegetables. The backdrop is an elegant interior with a rustic simplicity that includes an informal dining space plus a second with a more gastronomic focus called El Menjador. The latter only offers tasting menu options and needs to be booked in advance. The equally interesting wine list includes a plethora of little-known labels.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8734;Follia;Spain;Sant Joan Despí;Creu de Muntaner 17, Sant Joan Despí, 08970, Spain;41.3714008;2.0558744;56;false;true;Contemporary;In this attractive stone property, featuring numerous designer details, the clear focus is on seasonal ingredients. These can be enjoyed in the glass-fronted dining room with views of the surrounding vineyards that produce the property’s own wine, and a small garden full of tomatoes, lettuce, fruit trees and aromatic plants. The cuisine here is centred around three seasonal menus (Seny, Rauxa and Follia), plus a tapas-style option called El Pot del Follia (that is usually served in the wine cellar or in the garden in fine weather). An added bonus is the bread baked on the premises.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8735;El Albero;Spain;Toledo;de la Diputación 6, Toledo, 45004, Spain;39.865185;-4.0266523;28;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This small restaurant, located away from the main tourist area of the city and with many years of history under its belt, is enjoying a second “golden age” in the hands of young owner-chef Ismael Suleiman, who has brought a new lease of life and a more gastronomic feel to the cuisine. The overall feel here is that of a neighbourly and informal bistro with a single dining room plus a pavement terrace. The cooking is traditional in style, featuring seasonal ingredients and meticulous presentation, with a strong focus on delicious stews such as Toledo-style partridge stew with white beans, and stuffed oxtail with red wine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8736;Le Vin Rouge Maître-Cavista;Spain;Oropesa del Mar;Plaza Constitución 4, Oropesa del Mar, 12594, Spain;40.09069;0.13547;27;false;true;French;A restaurant that focuses on a reinterpreted version of French and Central European cooking via a concise à la carte along with interesting wine pairing options. Don’t miss the Apfelstrudel!;Air conditioning;[]
8737;Adaly;Spain;Madrid;Claudio Coello 122, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4368219;-3.6854152;49;false;true;Contemporary;A family-run, bistro-style restaurant with a simple rustic-cum-contemporary decor with the father Julio in charge of the dining room and his son Eduardo manning the stoves. The clear focus on the concise à la carte is on top-quality ingredients which are used to create contemporary dishes with a strong gastronomic base, mainly resulting from the number of years spent by Edu Guerrero working at El Bohío in Illescas, alongside celebrity chef Pepe Rodríguez. The result is honest cuisine that showcases time-honoured flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
8738;Gran Sol;Spain;Hondarribia;San Pedro 65, Hondarribia, 20280, Spain;43.3689344;-1.7941123;57;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The restaurant is named after the legendary fishing grounds of the North Atlantic, an important aspect of the town’s fishing tradition. Make sure you try the pintxos here, including Jaizkibel, Hondarribia and Huevo Mollete.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8739;Palm Court;Spain;Madrid;Plaza de la Lealtad 5, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.4158358;-3.6928029;42;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Located beneath an impressive glass dome in the lobby of the Mandarín Oriental Ritz Madrid hotel. The à la carte of classic and contemporary dishes is complemented by two tasting menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8740;Umm No Solo Tapas;Spain;Logrono;Marqués de Vallejo 10, Logrono, 26001, Spain;42.4659349;-2.445612;88;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the centre of the city where it attracts customers with its huge variety of pinchos, raciones and filled rolls, all extremely well presented and elaborately prepared.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8741;Rekondo;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Paseo de Igueldo 57, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20008, Spain;43.3133172;-2.0114846;54;false;true;Basque;A rustic property along the road up to Mt Igueldo with a classic-contemporary interior that comes as a pleasant surprise. Basque cooking with a focus on the highest-quality ingredients plus a superb cellar featuring some of the world’s best wines!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8742;Tira do Cordel;Spain;Fisterra;Paseo Marítimo 1, Fisterra, 15155, Spain;42.915027;-9.2649063;47;true;false;Seafood;A restaurant occupying a century-old property that was once a salting factory, with a superb location right by one of the area’s most charming beaches. Although simply prepared and presented, the cuisine is centred around the superb ingredients found along the Costa da Morte, with those cooked on the grill particularly popular.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8744;Kintsugi;Spain;Barcelona;Còrsega 289, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3943544;2.1563749;50;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Eel, prawns, octopus, sea bass and savoury rice dishes all feature in Japanese cuisine that showcases the bountiful ingredients and produce from the Terres de l’Ebre region. In this restaurant (part of the Xerta Group) located inside the Ohla Eixample Barcelona hotel, savour a unique gastronomic experience where the Ebro Delta takes centre stage but from a different culinary perspective. Choose between the sushi bar serving an Omakase menu with a strong nigiri focus, and several tables that can be reserved for à la carte dining and the Unagi menu featuring more fusion dishes. The Kaiseki “executive” menu is also available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
8745;Ruta del Veleta;Spain;Cenes de la Vega;Avenida de Sierra Nevada 146, Cenes de la Vega, 18190, Spain;37.1580304;-3.5317809;37;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Very professionally run. Its appealing a la carte menu, regional décor and its location in a luxurious building, earn it unanimous recognition.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8746;El Bálamu;Spain;Llanes;Paseo del Muelle, Llanes, 33500, Spain;43.421307;-4.7494383;92;true;true;Seafood;A bright restaurant with a maritime atmosphere on the first floor of the fish auction house in Llanes, opposite the fishing port, hence the constant coming and going of boats unloading their catch or heading out to sea. In this relaxed and friendly setting, enjoy simply yet meticulously prepared cuisine created with the freshest fish and seafood of an extraordinarily high quality.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8747;Compartir Barcelona;Spain;Barcelona;Valencia 225, Barcelona, 08007, Spain;41.3910731;2.1611268;73;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This Mediterranean-inspired eatery in the heart of the Eixample district, nor far from Disfrutar (its elder sibling), brings to Barcelona the same cooking concept that has been so successful at Compartir in Cadaqués. Its contemporary dishes, featuring a touch of international fusion, are perfect for sharing.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8748;Ca Ses Sauerschell's;Spain;Deià;Sa Vinya Vella 6, Deià, 07179, Spain;39.7470497;2.6494811;78;true;false;International, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant occupies the premises of the legendary Es Racó d'Es Teix. Today, under a new name, it has clearly reinvented itself with a much more casual concept run by the three daughters of the previous owner. The standout feature here continues to be the idyllic terrace with its stunning views over Deià and the Serra de Tramuntana, where you can choose between a concise, internationally inspired à la carte and a tasting menu (3- or 7-course options). It’s well worth booking one of the restaurant’s parking spaces as it is complicated finding a parking spot around the village.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8750;San Huberto;Spain;Ciudad Real;Montiel, Ciudad Real, 13004, Spain;38.9843757;-3.9195716;59;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant-asador with a classic feel where you can enjoy meticulously prepared traditional cuisine. It features a pleasant summer terrace, bar space (note the impressive glass-fronted bodega and fresh fish and seafood display counter) and dining room. The à la carte, which specialises in dishes roasted in a wood-fired oven (baby lamb, Castillian-style suckling pig etc), also features enticing starters, stews and superb fish (including Cantabrian hake, “estuary” sea bass, and red tuna tataki).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8751;La Bien Aparecida;Spain;Madrid;Jorge Juan 8, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4238438;-3.6870858;87;false;false;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;Named after the patron saint of Cantabria, this restaurant is laid out on two floors with different atmospheres. Updated traditional cuisine featuring fine textures and strong flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8752;Agorregi;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Portuetxe 14, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20008, Spain;43.3022145;-2.0116117;30;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Agorregi has a somewhat unusual setting on the Igara industrial estate, where it offers a contemporary, market-inspired à la carte with its roots in Basque cooking, featuring dishes that are always honest yet with the occasional contemporary detail. This is complemented by two tasting menus (Aisa and Belabarce). Some of the desserts here need to be ordered at the start of your meal so that they can be prepared in time. These include the thin-sliced “erezilla” apple cake with natural yoghurt ice cream, and the chocolate and hazelnut cake with banana ice cream.;Air conditioning;[]
8753;Lamian;Spain;Madrid;Plaza Mostenses 4, Madrid, 28015, Spain;40.4236053;-3.7089453;71;false;false;Fusion;If you’re a fan of Asian fusion cuisine, this is definitely the place for you! In this simple restaurant, the name of which refers to the Chinese technique for making hand-pulled noodles, the cuisine combines Chinese, Japanese and Thai recipes created with Spanish ingredients, with many dishes influenced by Asian street food. Many dishes are made for sharing – don’t pass up on specialities such as the delicious Dim Sum or any of the Ramen options, such as the exotically named “Jackie Chan is not Bruce Lee”, made with oxtail.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8754;El Vaixell;Spain;Llançà;Castellar 62, Llançà, 17490, Spain;42.3707406;3.1624628;42;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant in which the owner, an ever-present fixture in both the kitchen and dining room, creates traditional maritime-inspired cuisine featuring delicious rice (minimum two-person order), fish and seafood, plus a set daily menu option. Three different “suquet” stews are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
8756;Les Amis;Spain;Pamplona;Pozo Blanco 20, Pamplona, 31001, Spain;42.8167849;-1.6439658;46;true;false;French;Located in a pedestrianised street in Pamplona’s old quarter, Les Amis serves somewhat unusual cuisine with its roots in French cooking but with added Peruvian and Asian touches.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8757;Batea;Spain;Barcelona;Gran Via de Les Corts Catalanes 605, Barcelona, 08007, Spain;41.388836;2.1671494;85;false;false;Seafood, Farm to table;This cosmopolitan bistro located on one side of the emblematic Avenida Palace hotel has a contemporary interior that provides the backdrop for fusion cooking that combines traditional Catalan and Galician cuisine. The market-inspired small plates on offer here have a constant focus on the Atlantic and the Mediterranean.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8758;TA-KUMI;Spain;Madrid;Claudio Coello 114, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4358715;-3.6852993;38;false;true;Japanese;If you’re looking for a good Japanese restaurant, this option in the Salamanca district of the city, with its impeccable contemporary ambience, won’t disappoint, given that it follows the same successful recipe as its sister franchises in Marbella and Málaga. It features a sushi bar, two dining rooms on different floors and a private room, in each of which guests can select some of the restaurant’s signature recipes alongside the group’s most iconic dishes. Various set menus are also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8759;Yume;Spain;Avilés;Zinc, Avilés, 33490, Spain;43.5574586;-5.9178781;27;false;true;Creative;A restaurant in a stunning location, 20m above ground level in the tower of the emblematic Centro Niemeyer, with its superb views of the town. Taking its name from the Japanese word for “dream”, Yume provides chef Adrián San Julián with a platform to showcase his philosophy of sustainability and zero waste, hence the desire to use just one ingredient (such as onion, cauliflower, spinach, celeriac, cat shark etc) presented in many different ways in the same dish, at the same time exploring its different stages of preparation and intensity of flavours based around strong technique. The cuisine here is showcased on two impressive and bold menus: “Ejecutivo” (lunch from Tuesday to Friday) and the “Degustación” tasting option.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8760;Deliri;Spain;Barcelona;Còrsega 242, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3931589;2.1549436;24;true;true;Contemporary, Catalan;In this urban-industrial-style restaurant, the Catalan cuisine on offer is fun and full of personality, and includes an impressive choice of suggestions as well as game dishes in season (wild boar wrapped in cabbage leaves). The delicious stuffed paccheri pasta (macarras de l’àvia) are a must!;Air conditioning;[]
8761;Barra Alta Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Lagasca 19, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4230655;-3.6857113;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this modern and contemporary restaurant, you can enjoy an updated take on traditional cuisine with a nod to other cultures and a combination of main dishes, raciones and tapas. The à la carte is complemented by two tasting menus with options for sharing.;Air conditioning;[]
8762;Tasca del Puerto;Spain;Castelló de la Plana;Avenida del Puerto 13, Castelló de la Plana, 12100, Spain;39.9717029;0.0122348;92;true;false;Seafood;A family-run restaurant where the love of good cuisine is clearly evident. The cooking here is based around quality ingredients with a maritime flavour, including an array of rice dishes, fish direct from the auction, and seafood.;Air conditioning;[]
8763;Barquet Tarragona;Spain;Tarragona;Gasòmetre 16, Tarragona, 43001, Spain;41.1137376;1.2497577;83;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Rice Dishes;A property with a long history that started life as a coal yard, then a siphon bottle filling factory, before being converted into a bar, and finally a restaurant with a thoroughly contemporary appearance. Enjoy market inspired cuisine based around tasty rice dishes and regional recipes.;Air conditioning;[]
8764;La Fonda Ristol;Spain;Viladecavalls;Antoni Soler Hospital 1, Viladecavalls, 08232, Spain;41.5554834;1.9543439;98;false;false;Catalan;Run with great professionalism by the Ristol family, which has been involved in the restaurant business since 1905. Traditional Catalan cuisine with the occasional contemporary touch, and several set menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8765;Karak;Spain;Valencia;Músico Peydró 9, Valencia, 46001, Spain;39.4721437;-0.3780998;68;true;false;Fusion;Located in the heart of the city, where its celebrity female chef conjures up travel-inspired Mediterranean cuisine and plenty of fusion dishes. Interesting tasting menus add to the mix here.;Air conditioning;[]
8766;Suite 22;Spain;Valladolid;Fray Luis de León 22, Valladolid, 47002, Spain;41.6504755;-4.7213295;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Suite 22 occupies the former stables of the Palacio del Marqués de Castromonte in the heart of the city, where its welcoming barrel-vaulted dining room, combining the past and present, comes as a pleasant surprise. The chef’s cooking, which includes à la carte and various set menu options, has a contemporary slant influenced by self-taught personal touches in dishes with distinct flavours and a desire to push culinary boundaries.;Air conditioning;[]
8767;La Roca;Spain;Pozuelo de Alarcón;Avenida de Europa 25, Pozuelo de Alarcón, 28223, Spain;40.4438655;-3.7849995;40;true;false;Spanish, Fusion;La Roca’s simple contemporary decor provides the backdrop for cuisine that showcases quality ingredients. This comes as no surprise given that is overseen by chef Alberto Molinero from the award-winning Erre de Roca restaurant in Miranda de Ebro. Despite its global influences, the cuisine has a clear Spanish DNA, highlighted in signature recipes such as the oxtail ravioli, an array of hot and cold options, plus a good selection of more substantial dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8768;La Tronera;Spain;Villadepalos;El Caño 1, Villadepalos, 24565, Spain;42.5399874;-6.750129;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine;La Tronera shares a building with a small rural hotel, making it the perfect setting for a short break. The single, seasonally inspired tasting menu is centred on an updated take on traditional cuisine that always champions local ingredients, many produced by the restaurant itself.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8769;San Mamés Jatetxea;Spain;Bilbao;Rafael Moreno Pitxitxi, Bilbao, 48013, Spain;43.2650474;-2.9492403;86;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a unique location inside the Los Leones stadium and overlooking the pitch. Traditional à la carte options, as well as a tasting menu. Closed when matches are being played.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8770;Quadrat;Spain;Palma;Plaza de Sant Francesc 5, Palma, 07001, Spain;39.5690448;2.6527307;40;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Enjoy Mediterranean cuisine with a nod to local ingredients and Mallorcan cooking in this restaurant occupying the former stables of a mansion (now the Hotel Sant Francesc) in the centre of Palma. It is only open for dinner from Thursday to Monday (with a tasting menu option) and for lunch on Sundays, when you can order a set menu on which rice dishes take centre-stage. The inner garden terrace is a pleasant bonus!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8771;Trumfes;Spain;Llívia;Raval 27, Llívia, 17527, Spain;42.4636165;1.9836959;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;At Trumfes, enjoy traditional and creative dishes rooted in Catalan cuisine that make full use of the potato (trumfa) that has lent the restaurant its name. Other options on the menu include market-inspired daily specials, game in season, as well as a delicious mountain-style rice dish. Choose between two dining spaces or the wine cellar-style private room. An excellent tasting menu adds to the appeal.;;[]
8772;VÍTRIC;Spain;Reus;Santa Anna 24, Reus, 43201, Spain;41.1566027;1.1087262;18;false;true;Contemporary;In this quiet pedestrian street we came across this young chef who, having worked in several leading restaurants, returned to his roots to go it alone. In this restaurant that defines itself as a gastronomic taberna, you’ll find an open kitchen at the entrance with a bright dining room to the rear. The contemporary Catalan cuisine here is showcased on an à la carte that includes plates for sharing, an impressive daily menu plus a separate tasting-style option. We can recommend the twice-cooked eggs with parmentier and grilled liver… not forgetting the local vermouth!;Air conditioning;[]
8773;Apicius;Spain;Valencia;Eolo 7, Valencia, 46021, Spain;39.4704875;-0.3554382;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Comprising just one spacious, contemporary-style dining room, this restaurant serves modern, seasonal cuisine. Good choice of set menus, plus interesting themed days based on ingredients such as truffles and wild mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
8774;La Font;Spain;Canet de Mar;Rafael Masó 1-3, Canet de Mar, 08360, Spain;41.591863;2.5736958;60;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A worthwhile dining option in the Maresme area. This pleasant, family-run restaurant located in the upper part of town stands out for its modern ambience and the total dedication of the two brothers and a sister running the business. Contemporary, market-inspired cuisine which, although lacking some sophistication, is of a good standard and based around a good-value weekday menu and a second more elaborate menu at the weekend. One of its best dishes is the deboned shoulder of lamb cooked at low temperature.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8775;La Ereta;Spain;Alacant;Parque de la Ereta, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.3485812;-0.4815287;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;A striking modern property on the ascent up to the Castillo de Santa Bárbara, hence its superb views of the city. Here, Alicante-born chef Dani Frías offers a single, Mediterranean-inspired contemporary menu that showcases fish and seafood. This is demonstrated by one dish we particularly enjoyed: his delicious version of red shrimp stew (“caldereta de gamba roja”).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8776;Adolfo;Spain;Toledo;Hombre de Palo 7, Toledo, 45001, Spain;39.8579162;-4.0241665;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This classic restaurant in the heart of Toledo’s historic quarter boasts a delightful patio-cum-dining room dating back to the 12C, and has had a new lease of life under the command of the sons of the owner, the legendary Adolfo Muñoz. The cuisine is centred around a single seasonal tasting menu that has a strong focus on herbs and vegetables from the latter’s own country estate. The cooking here is also healthy, tasty and respectful of tradition, albeit from a more contemporary perspective, and features options such as organic green asparagus from nearby Camuñas, with turmeric and Melanosporum black truffle, and suckling pig served with its own jus and a fruit compote. Why not complete your dining experience with a visit to the superb underground wine cellar!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8777;Eth Bistro Gastro Espai;Spain;Vielha;Paseo de la Libertat 18, Vielha, 25530, Spain;42.7031892;0.7958927;23;true;true;Contemporary;This intimate and unusual restaurant, home to a whole host of mountain-inspired designer details including stags’ heads made from different materials adorning the walls, has a strong focus on modern cuisine. It features a good à la carte choice (in particular, delicious rice recipes and dishes perfect for sharing) as well as several tasting menus: Bistronómico (short and long options), Swiss Cheese Fondue (for two people), and the ever-successful Palamós Prawn Tasting menu, for which the restaurant has been awarded a certificate of guarantee. It also hosts interesting menus during the course of the year (such as wild mushrooms in autumn) that focus on the best seasonal ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
8778;Nou Manolín;Spain;Alacant;Villegas 3, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.3453029;-0.4851362;65;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;As soon as you enter Nou Manolín, your gaze is immediately drawn to the superb array of shrimp, red prawn, crayfish, oysters etc in the seafood display. Whether you choose the bar on the ground floor or the dining room with a delightful designer-inspired ceiling upstairs, the market-inspired menu (featuring a few media-ración options and a small selection of rice dishes), is identical. To round off your meal in style, make sure you order the chocolate supermousse, with its fresh, airy texture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8779;Lumbre;Spain;Casalarreina;Travesía de los Jardines 15, Casalarreina, 26230, Spain;42.5510995;-2.909682;61;true;true;Contemporary;Occupying a 17C bodega with pleasant dining rooms, an attractive underground cave, an attic-style lounge for post-dinner drinks, plus a contemporary à la carte complemented by set menu options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8780;Javier Martín;Spain;Cáceres;Juan Solano Pedrero 15, Cáceres, 10005, Spain;39.4554765;-6.3808121;61;false;true;Contemporary;Located in the modern Nuevo Cáceres neighbourhood, this restaurant impressively run by Javier and Esther is defined by them as their “life project”, where you can choose between contemporary-style cooking on an extensive à la carte and two tasting menus (Origen and Experiencia) on which seasonal and locally sourced ingredients play a prominent role. Interesting dishes include the carpaccio of Iberian ham, foie gras and “tierra de Ibores”, red partridge stuffed with Pedro Ximénez, truffles and foie gras, and grilled wild red mullet, with salted flakes and olive caviar.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8781;Les Voltes de Sant Sebastià;Spain;Moià;Sant Sebastià 9, Moià, 08180, Spain;41.8131053;2.0962455;80;true;true;Catalan;A restaurant with a rustic feel occupying former stables that have retained their vaulted ceilings. The pleasantly updated cuisine here is Catalan focused, consistent in its quality and always champions local ingredients. Pleasant patio-terrace, plus an unusual cistern that has been converted into a wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8782;La Llotja;Spain;L'Ametlla de Mar;Sant Roc 23, L'Ametlla de Mar, 43860, Spain;40.8838992;0.8012799;49;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with plenty of personality where the focus is on quality products and flavours. Authentic market - fresh cuisine that is in tune with the seasons and is centred around fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8783;El Trasgu;Spain;Torrelodones;Cudillero 2, Torrelodones, 28250, Spain;40.5697505;-3.9250885;59;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;El Trasgu occupies an elegant chalet-style property featuring a bar and three classic-cum-contemporary dining rooms. The traditional à la carte offers a selection of stews, rice dishes and seafood. The superb terrace is a must!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
8784;Venta de Ulzama;Spain;Belate (Puerto de);Carretera NA 1210, Belate (Puerto de), 31797, Spain;43.0329569;-1.6277656;83;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;One of the best dining and accommodation options in the Ulzama valley, this tranquil family-run business with over a century of history behind it is guaranteed to please its guests. It occupies a typical mountain-style property in a delightful natural setting, with the unusual sight of a deer farm next door! It features an attractive bar, a room with an open fireplace, a classically furnished dining room with a profusion of wood, plus a traditional menu accompanied by a good selection of suggestions that change according to the availability of seasonal ingredients (vegetables, mushrooms, grilled fish, game etc). The views from the dining room and terrace are superb!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8785;Laudat;Spain;Santanyí;Sant Andreu 18, Santanyí, 07650, Spain;39.3543499;3.1296113;89;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;Located next to the church, Laudat occupies an old Mallorcan house with a particularly welcoming patio-terrace. Choose between the simple, Mediterranean-inspired à la carte and a set menu featuring dishes taken from the former.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8786;Pont Vell;Spain;Besalú;Pont Vell 24, Besalú, 17850, Spain;42.1993124;2.700489;16;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the heart of Besalú’s old quarter, Pont Vell boasts two rustic dining rooms and an idyllic terrace in the shade of a medlar tree, all with superb views of the river. Traditional and local cuisine, including specialities such as sweet and sour rabbit and oxtail.;Great view,Terrace;[]
8787;Ébano;Spain;Bellaterra;Avenida Josep María Marcet i Coll 24, Bellaterra, 08290, Spain;41.5039785;2.0884706;39;true;true;Contemporary;Ébano occupies an aristocratic property in a residential district, and is surrounded by chalets and a pleasant tree-shaded terrace. In its bright, contemporary-style dining rooms, the focus is on modern cooking with strong traditional roots, seasonal ingredients and an obsession with defined flavours. The à la carte, including a selection of rice dishes (we enjoyed the “arroz del corral” with organic chicken, butifarra del perol sausage and butifarra blood sausage) is accompanied by daily specials, with a focus on fresh fish, and a tasting menu, from which you can also order individual dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8789;Castillería;Spain;Vejer de la Frontera;Pago de Santa Lucía, Vejer de la Frontera, 11150, Spain;36.2698592;-5.9766526;65;false;false;Meats and Grills;Located to the northwest of Vejer, La Castillería features a glass-fronted kitchen and a terrace that blends into the restaurant’s verdant surroundings. Choice cuts of meat take centre stage here!;Terrace;[]
8790;Ivantxu Espacio Bistronómico;Spain;Seville;Virgen de la Victoria 5, Seville, 41011, Spain;37.3767279;-5.9966592;96;false;true;Contemporary;Behind the large glass-fronted façade, the focus here is unashamedly on top-quality ingredients in a location just a few metres from the river. Basque cuisine takes pride of place, centred on select meats from across Spain, Galician seafood, and fish from the auction in Conil.;Air conditioning;[]
8791;Kero;Spain;Vigo;Castelar 6, Vigo, 36201, Spain;42.240196;-8.723353;30;true;true;Peruvian;This bright restaurant, with lots of decorative references to Peruvian culture (Andean shawls, colourful wool, a profusion of wood, plus a name that refers to the ceremonial vases used in Inca culture), has an open-view kitchen and a clear focus on fusion cuisine. This is demonstrated by its desire to find “a balance between typical Peruvian cooking and Galician palates”. Chef Juan Carlos Perret, who has demonstrated his cooking skills at the Madrid Fusión show, highlights his cuisine on à la carte and two interesting tasting menus (Viaje a Perú and Alto Perú).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8792;La Cocina del Principal;Spain;Sos del Rey Católico;Fernando El Católico 13, Sos del Rey Católico, 50680, Spain;42.4954434;-1.2153216;61;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the centre of the historic quarter, this restaurant occupies a charming building which provides the backdrop for a traditionally inspired à la carte featuring numerous grilled dishes. The terrace with beautiful views is an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8794;La Portada de Mediodía;Spain;Torrecaballeros;San Nicolás de Bari 31, Torrecaballeros, 40160, Spain;40.9932353;-4.024872;89;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant is set in a 16C post house with a welcoming rustic ambience in its dining room. Choose from a menu of Castillian cuisine dominated by oven - roasted dishes and grilled meats.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8795;Treintaitres;Spain;Tudela;Capuchinos 7, Tudela, 31500, Spain;42.0598846;-1.6028162;53;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Treintaitrés (33) offers several tasting menus, one of which is exclusively vegetarian, which showcase its culinary expertise in cooking locally grown produce. Updated traditional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8796;Tobiko;Spain;Toledo;Ronda de Buenavista 27, Toledo, 45005, Spain;39.8790934;-4.0364849;65;true;false;Creative;A restaurant serving creative cuisine that exudes great enthusiasm and passion. Its two tasting menus (Tobiko and Tasting, the latter with a wine-pairing option) showcase an element of fusion and a high level of technical skill, with both focusing on delicate textures, well-paired flavours and the occasional visual trompe l’œil.;Air conditioning;[]
8797;Bardeni-Caldeni;Spain;Barcelona;Valencia 454, Barcelona, 08013, Spain;41.40296;2.177073;79;false;false;Meats and Grills;A restaurant in which meat is very much centre-stage. The ambience is that of an old butcher’s shop, with a bar-cum dining counter. Don’t miss the steak tartare!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8798;Mon Restaurant;Spain;Ciutadella de Menorca;Paseo de San Nicolás 14, Ciutadella de Menorca, 07760, Spain;40.000004;3.8350323;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This restaurant includes a waiting area, a light airy dining room and a covered patio where tables are also laid. Contemporary cuisine which aims to prioritise local ingredients. In addition to the restaurant, there are also a few guestrooms available.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8800;La Bodeguilla;Spain;Palma;Sant Jaume 3, Palma, 07012, Spain;39.5717927;2.6471863;90;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Family establishment run by two brothers. Sample wines and tapas in the wine shop and the two - storey dining area where barrels are used as tables.;Air conditioning;[]
8801;Sa Pedrera d'es Pujol;Spain;Sant Lluís;Camino d'es Pujol 14, Sant Lluís, 07710, Spain;39.8391611;4.2599113;71;false;false;Creative;An interesting dining option, where the owner - chef has revived old recipes from yesteryear and updated them with modern culinary techniques and presentation. Several rustic - style dining rooms, one glass - fronted section, as well as a cave - cum - wine cellar in which guests can choose their own wine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8802;Es Ventall;Spain;Sant Antoni de Portmany;Cervantes 22, Sant Antoni de Portmany, 07820, Spain;38.9823633;1.3030203;92;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant has grown as a result of the new generation at the helm, although the wood-fired oven remains key to its cooking. Contemporary dishes with a strong Ibizan flavour that use produce from the family’s own vegetable garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8803;Xerta;Spain;Barcelona;Còrsega 289, Barcelona, 08008, Spain;41.3944177;2.1564642;44;false;false;Creative;If you’re unfamiliar with the natural bounty of the Ebro Delta, a visit to this restaurant in Barcelona is a must to savour the flavours of a region that has been declared a World Biosphere Reserve. Accessed via the lobby of the Ohla Eixample hotel, Xerta boasts a contemporary dining room with views of the kitchen. Chef Fran López, who trained and worked for three years with French maestro Alain Ducasse, showcases the flavours of his home region, providing guests with an opportunity to discover its superb gastronomy (eel, oysters, rice etc - 90% of his ingredients are sourced from here) from a creative perspective. The à la carte, which also features an array of delicious rice dishes and always showcases seasonal ingredients (sea cucumbers, galera shrimp, blue crab, wild mushrooms etc), is complemented by four set menus: Ejecutivo (lunchtimes, excluding public holidays, Monday to Friday), Delta, Degustación and Homenaje.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8804;Port Petit;Spain;Cala d'Or;Avenida Cala Llonga, Cala d'Or, 07660, Spain;39.371062;3.2240569;60;true;true;French;An attractive restaurant with a pleasant terrace offering delightful views of the marina. A mix of Mediterranean and international cuisine with French influence.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
8805;Zintziri Errota;Spain;Bakio;Barrio Arzalde 3, Bakio, 48130, Spain;43.406998;-2.8142142;68;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;This restaurant occupies a bucolic country house dating from 1650 that was originally used as a blacksmith’s (it is said that, in addition to anchors, weapons and farm implements, they also made high-quality shackles for prisoners similar to those referred to by Shakespeare in the pages of Hamlet), and later as a mill for grinding maize. The beautiful rustic interior comes as a pleasant surprise (an old wood-fired oven is nowadays used as a counter, with a second providing heat in the dining room). The home-style cooking has a contemporary feel and features the occasional creative detail. Check out the daily fish specials and start by ordering the spectacularly flavoured baked octopus on a parmentier of Ratte potato.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8806;FM;Spain;Granada;Avenida Juan Pablo II 54, Granada, 18013, Spain;37.19511;-3.60892;84;true;false;Farm to table, Andalusian;A simple restaurant named after the owner Francisco Martín where the fine cuisine is impressively presented and prepared with top-quality products direct from the fish auction.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8807;Ca L'Estrany;Spain;Cabrils;Camí Coll de Port 19, Cabrils, 08348, Spain;41.5307812;2.3601395;31;true;true;Farm to table;This farmhouse-style property has strong links with the brotherhood of fishermen from Arenys de Mar. Make sure you try the savoury rice dishes or any of the daily specials… not forgetting the superb fresh fish and seafood, including octopus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8808;La Vieja Bodega;Spain;Casalarreina;Avenida de La Rioja 17, Casalarreina, 26230, Spain;42.5493979;-2.9078031;56;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Rustic in style and occupying a 17C wine bodega. The chef here views cuisine as a pleasure for sharing through traditionally inspired dishes with a contemporary touch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
8810;365;Spain;Pollença;Carretera Palma-Pollença, Pollença, 07460, Spain;39.864459;3.0243699;52;false;true;Creative;A popular restaurant thanks to its creative cuisine showcased on several menus (including a vegetarian option) that champion sustainable ingredients produced on 365’s own farm estate (different oils, citrus fruit, vegetables, wine etc).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8811;Barra Alta Barcelona;Spain;Barcelona;Laforja 11, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.3997234;2.150566;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this attractive, contemporary-style restaurant, enjoy an array of “raciones” with a focus on quality ingredients and strong flavours, with the occasional nod to international dishes. Tasting menus are also available as are daily specials that do not feature on the à la carte.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8812;La Morena;Spain;Madrid;Paseo de la Castellana 210, Madrid, 28046, Spain;40.4633451;-3.6890756;79;false;false;Fusion;A contemporary yet informal bistro that aims to bring the unique maritime world of the waters off the coast of Tarifa to the Spanish capital, both in terms of its aesthetics and gastronomy. The cooking, featuring an array of light yet extremely delicious dishes, is a fusion of Cádiz, Japanese and Latin American cuisine, and is especially designed for sharing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8813;Manzil;Spain;Seville;Alfonso XII 13, Seville, 41001, Spain;37.3928295;-5.9974162;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This centrally located restaurant boasts an open kitchen and a striking decor featuring large images of animals and vegetables painted on the walls. The dining experience, which begins with appetisers at the counter in the kitchen before continuing at your table, reflects the full personality and passion of the chef (who has worked in several renowned restaurants and who has represented Spain at the prestigious Bocuse d´Or competition) for Andalucian cuisine. His cooking is highlighted on two extensive menus (Morada and Manzil) featuring an array of small plates, superb textures and impressive pairings.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8814;La Bonaigua;Spain;Sant Just Desvern;Carretera Reial 54, Sant Just Desvern, 08960, Spain;41.3786384;2.0773297;35;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Catalan;A family-run restaurant that has been impressively brought up to date. The traditionally inspired à la carte is based around quality ingredients, including fish sourced at the market daily, matured meats, savoury rice dishes etc.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8815;Asador Rio Sil;Spain;Carballo;Rio Sil 43, Carballo, 15100, Spain;43.2084912;-8.6908517;50;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family-run restaurant where the highlights are its top-quality ingredients and the attractive glass-fronted wine cellar in the dining room. Rio Sil is also renowned for its select Galician meats and its interesting day-long food events.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8816;Tess de Mar;Spain;Campos;Nou 10, Campos, 07630, Spain;39.4334965;3.0185699;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with a contemporary feel occupying a former coach house. This renowned restaurant in the local area serves modern zero - miles cuisine overlooking an attractive garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8817;RíasKru;Spain;Barcelona;Lleida 7, Barcelona, 08004, Spain;41.374144;2.1545293;78;false;true;Seafood;This somewhat unusual restaurant is a fusion of two dining spaces (including the former RÍas de Galicia and Espai KRU) and two culinary themes on a single menu: classic Galician cooking (featuring superb fish and seafood) and Japanese-inspired cuisine with a focus on raw dishes (the menu also includes caviar-based specialities). We can particularly recommend the smoked anchovies with Manchego cheese, and the delicious Galician goose barnacles from Roncudo en Corme, Laxe, and Cedeira.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8818;Sushi Bar Tottori;Spain;Madrid;Lagasca 67, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4290796;-3.6849964;97;true;true;Japanese;Have you heard of master chef Haruki Takahashi? Here, you’ll discover his legacy and a focus on the freshest ingredients and tradition in a restaurant that takes it names from a small city in Japan.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8819;Montecruz;Spain;Aracena;Plaza San Pedro 36, Aracena, 21200, Spain;37.89128;-6.56721;60;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This renowned regional restaurant serves traditional mountain cuisine. It is made from typical Iberian produce, enhanced by wild mushrooms in season, savoury rice dishes, and daylong food events centred around local game.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8820;Sa Jambina;Spain;Calella de Palafrugell;Boffil i Codina 21, Calella de Palafrugell, 17210, Spain;41.8886094;3.1858177;37;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a contemporary yet informal feel that has taken on a more updated approach to its cuisine with the next generation of the family on board, but with a continued focus on traditional and local fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8821;Abarike;Spain;Gijón;Melquíades Álvarez 3, Gijón, 33201, Spain;43.5444694;-5.6628934;16;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Oysters, scallops, razor clams, cockles, prawns, shrimp, and an array of white and oily fish take centre-stage in this small, welcoming restaurant with a maritime decor in which the sea is the undisputed star of the show. The aim of Lara Roguez, who everyone knows as the “chef of the Cantabrian Sea”, is to give her dishes an added twist (e.g. in the choice of sides), including influences from other food cultures, without detracting from their individual flavour. The unusual “logbook-style” à la carte, which includes added information that enables guests to identify the traceability of every ingredient, is complemented by two Omakase-style tasting menus: “Marea Baja” (Low Tide) and “Marea Alta” (High Tide). We were particularly impressed by her array of “gilda”-style tapas, prepared with prawns, cured sea bass, smoked eel, blue lobster etc, all of which were equally delicious.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8822;Sorondongo;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Armas 15, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35001, Spain;28.10226;-15.41437;89;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;A restaurant that has burst onto the island’s culinary scene and which takes its name from one of the island’s most typical folklore dances. The young chef at the helm has added a contemporary touch to traditional Canary Island recipes, in so doing incorporating some interesting personal touches and creativity. The cooking here is centred on two tasting menus (Santa Ana and Vegueta), although an à la carte and “media ración” options are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
8823;La Morera de Pablo & Ester;Spain;Salou;Berenguer de Palou 10, Salou, 43840, Spain;41.0808265;1.1321247;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;A couple are at the helm in this welcoming restaurant. The completely glass - fronted dining room is complemented by an attractive open - air terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8824;Haramboure;Spain;Madrid;Maldonado 4, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4339414;-3.6859299;99;true;true;Basque;The minute you walk through the door of this restaurant you have the sense of being transported to a bistro in the north of the country. Chef Patxi Zumárraga and Patricia Haramboure have deliberately opted for a restrained decor here, with stone walls, bare wood tables and seats for dining at the bar very much in keeping with the style of a Basque “bodegón”. The varied à la carte includes a good choice of tapas, individual small plates, delicious vegetables from Aranjuez and the province of Bizkaia, fish from the Cantabrian sea, along with choice cuts of meat. The Zalla red onion tarte tatin is a must!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8825;Marqués de Riscal;Spain;Elciego;Torrea 1, Elciego, 01340, Spain;42.5115422;-2.6176801;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located within the Marqués de Riscal City of Wine in a unique hotel overflowing with design, imagination and creativity and designed by the famous architect Frank O. Gehry. The estate was also recognised as the best vineyard in Europe in 2021.Beneath the spectacular curved roof of pink, gold and silver titanium that represent the red of the wine, the golden hue of the wire mesh decorating Marqués de Riscal’s bottles, and the gold colour of their capsules, discover innovative cuisine with a constant nod to tradition. The cuisine of chef Francis Paniego, who keeps a watchful eye on everything here, is centred on two tasting menus with different numbers of courses (Tierra 7 Ideas and Tierra 10 Ideas). Both share the same appetisers and seek their inspiration in the hills of the Rioja region and in its seasonal local ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8826;La Forquilla;Spain;Barcelona;Aragó 152, Barcelona, 08011, Spain;41.3857448;2.1564185;67;true;true;Creative;La Forquilla is definitely a restaurant with a difference given that owner-chef Vidal Gravalosa takes care of everything, including a huge amount of preparation before every sitting, impressive work in the kitchen, as well as service at the handful of tables. His cooking is centred around a tasting menu plus a creatively inspired à la carte featuring an array of seasonal recipes. Standout dishes include the Maresme peas with baby squid and Iberian pork jowl, and the crispy Segovian suckling pig served with its own sauce, parsnip purée and baby gem lettuce.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8827;Zezilionea;Spain;Olaberria;Plaza de San Juan 3, Olaberria, 20212, Spain;43.027096;-2.2030957;67;true;false;Basque;Occupying an impressively large house in the centre of Olaberria, which is also known as the Balcony of the Goierri region. Traditional Basque cooking, including specialities such as mushrooms baked in the oven.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8828;Hostería de los Palmeros;Spain;Frómista;Plaza San Telmo 4, Frómista, 34440, Spain;42.26792;-4.404835;81;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The extensive local and regional menu here is particularly strong on game dishes (woodcock, wood pigeon, teal etc) and locally grown vegetables (Saldaña beans, “menestra palentina” stew).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8829;Sangiovese;Spain;Mataró;Muralla de Sant Llorenç 32, Mataró, 08302, Spain;41.5386509;2.4440138;68;false;false;Contemporary;A centrally located restaurant with an unusual Art Deco-inspired interior design. The contemporary-influenced à la carte is complemented by a good choice of set menus.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8830;Periplo Portixol;Spain;Palma;Vicari Joaquim Fuster 67, Palma, 07006, Spain;39.5592604;2.6729585;60;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;An informal restaurant that stands out for its pleasant views of Palma bay from its impressive setting in the old Molinar fisherman’s district. The highlights here, on an à la carte mainly featuring dishes designed for two sharing, are the meticulously prepared fish and seafood purchased at the market daily and cooked mainly on the open grill.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8831;Kaoma;Spain;Lleida;Camp de Mart 15, Lleida, 25006, Spain;41.6181945;0.6211729;51;false;true;Asian Contemporary, Peruvian;The simple Japanese decor of wood and almond flowers on the ceiling take centre stage here, endowing Kaoma with its intimate ambience. The Asia-inspired menu also includes ceviches and tiraditos.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8832;Distrikt41;Spain;Alacant;Navas 41, Alacant, 03001, Spain;38.34632;-0.48752;100;true;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with a modern decor and gastro-bar ambience run by two chefs originally from the Netherlands. Here, the contemporary à la carte and menu options (daily and seasonal) feature a combination of Central European, French and Spanish influences. Sauces are a prominent presence, while many dishes are given a finishing touch on the grill.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8833;Tapas 3.0;Spain;Salamanca;Sánchez Barbero 9, Salamanca, 37001, Spain;40.96378;-5.66437;62;false;true;Spanish Contemporary;This centrally located gastro-bar boasts an attractive dining room plus a glass-fronted wine cellar in the basement. Contemporary tapas and “raciones”, plus a takeaway and home delivery menu (Tapas 4.0).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8834;La Carboná;Spain;Jerez de la Frontera;San Francisco de Paula 2, Jerez de la Frontera, 11401, Spain;36.6825442;-6.1325498;41;false;false;Contemporary;La Carboná occupies an old sherry bodega with high wooden ceilings in which the sense of space, welcoming interior design and location in the centre of town come as a pleasant surprise. The à la carte has a contemporary feel but with a firm basis in tradition and is complemented by two interesting tasting menus: Lola Carboná (a homage to the legendary flamenco singer-dancer Lola Flores) and Un Sólo Palo “Amontillado”. Local sherries feature prominently and are included as a wine pairing option with both menus.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8835;KUMA;Spain;Bilbao;Ercilla 8, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2651025;-2.9307385;31;false;false;Japanese;A restaurant with a refined decor in which you can enjoy a Japanese dining experience to the full thanks to chef Daniel Lomana’s frequent visits to Japan to train and to develop his technique further, skills that can you enjoy at close quarters by taking a seat at the bar or at one of its adjoining tables. His focus is on Japanese fusion cuisine that includes interesting à la carte dishes (hamachi sashimi, amberjack with KUMA ceviche, sea bass nigiri, fried aubergines with a white sesame vinaigrette etc), plus a recommended tasting menu. Don’t leave without trying one of KUMA’s mochi rice cakes!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8836;Ca L'Amagat;Spain;Bagà;Clota 4, Bagà, 08695, Spain;42.2523027;1.8623248;75;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Somewhat tucked away in a narrow street in the centre of Bàga, in a stone house that originally served as a “taberna” and then, in the 1950s, was converted into an inn for workers from the mines in Fígols. Today, it has been brought bang up to date by a friendly couple who have designated it a Rustic GastroHotel, with one classically furnished dining room and a second more intimate dining space for more private events. The cooking here is focused around good set menus and traditional dishes inspired by the products from the Berguedà area such as “black” peas and truffles. Simply furnished guestrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
8837;La Despensa del Etxanobe;Spain;Bilbao;Juan de Ajuriaguerra 8, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.265347;-2.9314213;54;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A fun New York - style space next to the Etxanobe Atelier, with which it shares its cuisine. Attractive food display counters and traditional cooking alongside more contemporary - style dishes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8838;Cocina Cabal;Spain;Oviedo;Suárez de la Riva 5, Oviedo, 33007, Spain;43.36057;-5.8474054;70;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;A restaurant that takes its name from chef Vicente Cabal and which features a kitchen visible from the dining room. Cabal is truly passionate about cooking and has had a long career working in leading restaurants across the country. On the à la carte, he conjures up creatively prepared Mediterranean cuisine with a balanced approach between tradition and innovation, which is complemented by a tasting menu named after the restaurant. In 2022, it won the award for the world’s best “fabada” stew!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8839;Terra;Spain;Berga;Paseo de la Pau 27, Berga, 08600, Spain;42.100147;1.8450849;26;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant that goes beyond an enjoyable experience by also focusing on a sense of place. Here, the chef serves traditional Catalan and seasonal cuisine, including several interesting menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8840;Contraban;Spain;Barcelona;Riudarenes 7, Barcelona, 08002, Spain;41.38098;2.1797;50;true;true;Contemporary;Occupying a boutique hotel tucked away in the city’s Gothic Quarter, the Contraban boasts a plush, somewhat secretive ambience. Its contemporary-style cooking, which it describes as being inspired by emotions and feelings (freedom, surprise, longing etc), is based around classical French cuisine. Make sure you visit the panoramic rooftop for its impressive views and its extensive array of tapas and cocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
8841;Remigio;Spain;Tudela;Gaztambide-Carrera 4, Tudela, 31500, Spain;42.0616594;-1.6052331;17;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;A renovated house with plenty of history that in the past has hosted guests such as the famous Spanish poet Gustavo Adolfo Bécquer. Here, the updated take on regional cuisine is showcased on an à la carte and several set menus, with a strong focus on vegetables and farm produce – for over 20 years the restaurant has sourced ingredients from the famous Mejana de Tudela area on the banks of the Ebro river. It also features a gastronomic dining space called Choko del Remigio, with a focus on local, seasonally inspired cuisine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8842;Akase;Spain;Jerez de la Frontera;Fernando Viola, Edificio Málaga, local 8, Jerez de la Frontera, 11404, Spain;36.6915414;-6.1299784;20;true;false;Japanese;At Akase, where the restaurant describes what it offers as “market-inspired cuisine with a Japanese soul”, the focus is on ingredients sourced from in and around Cádiz in order to create surprising Japanese cuisine that is guaranteed to please guests’ palates. Chef Jaime Mena’s cooking, with its emphasis on show-cooking for a maximum of 10 covers per service, is showcased on a single tasting menu (Daimyo) that starts with several Cádiz dishes prepared with techniques from the Far East, and continues (through a selection of nigiris) with typical fish sourced from different towns along the local coast (Chipiona, Rota, Barbate, Chiclana, Conil etc). When it comes to dessert, the emphasis is on classic Japanese dishes which provide an opportunity to explore the bodegas and vineyards of Jerez and its surroundings. We strongly recommend booking ahead.;Air conditioning;[]
8843;L'Hort;Spain;Arnes;Masía L'Hort de Fortunyo, Arnes, 43597, Spain;40.9158465;0.2558161;83;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is part of the rural L'Hort de Fortunyo hotel, a delightful stone farmhouse the origins of which date back to the 18C and which is surrounded by olive trees close to the Parque Natural de Els Ports. The honest cuisine served here, which respects the traditions of the Terra Alta area but with a contemporary touch and a nod to recipes from elsewhere, is always based around ingredients grown in its own vegetable garden. The terrace is particularly delightful!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8845;Hotaru Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Alcalá 99, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4215526;-3.6836676;42;true;true;Japanese, Fusion;Hotaru is one of those places where you can experiment, savour and be guided in complete confidence by the sushi bar chef. Located opposite the Retiro park, and decorated in an elegantly authentic style, this restaurant bases its cuisine around two well-balanced Omakase menus and an extensive Japanese-inspired à la carte (maki, temaki, sashimi, nigiri etc) with interesting and somewhat surprising hints of fusion from Mexico.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8846;El Señor Martín;Spain;Madrid;General Castaños 13, Madrid, 28004, Spain;40.4259241;-3.693746;93;true;true;Grills, Seafood;A restaurant with a modern industrial feel where everything revolves around the sea, with dishes prepared with visually impressive products of the very highest quality. The main focus here is on dishes cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8847;Bodegón Alejandro;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Fermín Calbetón 4, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20003, Spain;43.3235974;-1.9833372;16;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re looking for somewhere to eat in the old town that epitomises Basque values and traditional cooking, the Bodegón Alejandro is the place for you, thanks to its focus on authentic local cuisine. In the simply furnished, rustic yet contemporary interior, choose between a varied à la carte of seasonal dishes (fried anchovies, Donostia-style supreme of cod with pil-pil and crab, Iberian pork loin with mashed potatoes etc) and an impressive tasting menu. Make sure you leave space for dessert as the warm pistachio soufflé with lemon sorbet is absolutely delicious!;Air conditioning;[]
8848;Ana Mari;Spain;Irun;Olaberria Auzoa 49, Irun, 20303, Spain;43.323417;-1.7903494;64;false;false;Grills;This charming Basque “asador”, impressively run by the Bereciartua family, occupies a delightful 16C country house in a riverside location. The open grill, which is completely visible from the dining room, is at the very heart of the Basque-inspired cooking on offer here. Whatever you order, from its splendid meats to its superb fish dishes, make sure you leave room for the cheesecake!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8849;Restaurante 1497;Spain;Vallromanes;Riera de Vallromanes, Vallromanes, 08188, Spain;41.5277571;2.3110242;86;true;true;Contemporary;Part of the EcoResort Mas Salagros, the first 100% eco-hotel in Spain and an oasis of peace and tranquillity in the protected Serralada Litoral area. The restaurant, the name of which is a nod to the year from which the first documents relating to the main farm building originate, has a contemporary feel and shares access with the more informal Cibus eatery, which specialises in grilled and rice dishes. Here, the focus is on modern cooking that is based around seasonal organic ingredients sourced from the kitchen garden by the entrance to the hotel as well as from local farmers. The à la carte is complemented by three tasting menus served to the entire table only: Vegan Experience, Slow, and 1497. They also do their utmost here to reduce waste and to make maximum use of leftover ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8850;Portuondo;Spain;Mundaka;Barrio Portuondo, Mundaka, 48360, Spain;43.398911;-2.6959326;84;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Seafood;A delightful property that stands out for its panoramic views, thanks to its setting overlooking the estuary. The cuisine here showcases top-quality products ranging from fish from the Bermeo auction and primes cuts of meat, all of which are cooked to perfection on the grill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
8851;Albalá;Spain;Jerez de la Frontera;Divina Pastora, Jerez de la Frontera, 11403, Spain;36.6912096;-6.1380991;84;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located close to the Royal Andalucian School of Equestrian Art, this welcoming restaurant offers an à la carte of tapas and “raciones” with different headings (Para Picar and Para Compartir - the latter designed for sharing), along with other sections encompassing an array of stews and soups, fish and seafood, and meat dishes. These include tuna tartare, pan-fried “fideos” (noodles), and Iberian pork meatballs with octopus.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8852;Sollun;Spain;Nerja;Pintada 9, Nerja, 29780, Spain;36.74668;-3.87601;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Sollun boasts a thoroughly modern feel along one of the main shopping streets in the centre of town. The chef, who has been trained in several top Michelin - starred restaurants, serves meticulously prepared, contemporary Mediterranean cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8853;Arcos de Quejana;Spain;Kexaa;Carretera Beotegi, Kexaa, 01477, Spain;43.080875;-3.072399;93;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Restaurant with a rustic atmosphere with visible wooden beams and stone walls.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8854;Alborada;Spain;Murcia;Andrés Baquero 15, Murcia, 30001, Spain;37.9869962;-1.1278293;61;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Well known across the city, this centrally located restaurant boasts an informal bar perfect for tapas plus a stylish, classically furnished dining room with a central section that can be converted into a private dining space. The chef, who describes himself as “pure Murcian stock”, creates traditional, market-inspired cuisine that is showcased on an impressive à la carte (including a choice of stews and rice dishes for a minimum of two guests – the latter need to be pre-ordered), plus an “executive” menu at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8855;Asturiano;Spain;Lalín;Rosalía de Castro 25, Lalín, 36500, Spain;42.6597501;-8.11345;43;true;false;Seafood;A family-run restaurant renowned for its abundant fish and seafood, all purchased from the local auction and cooked in the traditional way. Make sure you try the fish stew (caldeirada) with cider!;Air conditioning;[]
8856;Pa i Raïm;Spain;Palafrugell;Torres Jonama 56, Palafrugell, 17200, Spain;41.9182195;3.1605794;30;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant occupying the former family home of the writer Josep Pla. One classic dining room, a second that is in the style of a winter conservatory, as well as a delightful terrace planted with two linden trees.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8857;Madruelo;Spain;Cáceres;Camberos 2, Cáceres, 10003, Spain;39.4762306;-6.3701195;85;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Discover the true flavours of Extremadura’s pastures and meadows in this regionally inspired restaurant occupying a 19C building just a few metres from the Plaza Mayor. The focus on the reasonably varied à la carte is predominantly on the stalwarts of Extremadura cuisine (morcilla, local sausages, Iberian pork stew etc), although rice options (for a minimum of two guests) and several cod dishes also make an appearance.;Air conditioning;[]
8858;Fonda España;Spain;Barcelona;Sant Pau 9, Barcelona, 08001, Spain;41.379944;2.1728355;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Overseen by chef Martín Berasategui, choose between three menus that can be enjoyed either in Fonda España’s iconic Modernist dining room or the Arnau room with its impressive allegorical fireplace.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8859;El Taller Seve Díaz;Spain;Puerto de la Cruz;San Felipe 32, Puerto de la Cruz, 38400, Spain;28.416585;-16.5531212;20;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;In this restaurant, a visit to which is almost compulsory for food-lovers visiting the island, they are of the firm belief that the customer is always king. We can definitely confirm this approach given chef Seve Díaz’s constant and very natural contact and interactions with his guests. Located just a few steps from the central Plaza del Charco, it occupies the ground floor of a property with a contemporary design that comes as a surprise, with a split-level dining room and open kitchen. The culinary focus here is on two tasting menus (a short option entitled “Sorpresa” (Surprise), and a second simply called “Largo” (Long)), both of which have a contemporary edge and are based around seasonal ingredients from the Canary Islands that are combined with plenty of originality (as an example, the native Canarian black pig and fresh fish caught in local waters are a constant on the menu). One bold, cutting-edge dish that we particularly enjoyed was the red prawns with caramelised prawn heads, tiger’s milk and Guayonje onion.;Air conditioning;[]
8860;Kökosnøt;Andorra;Andorra la Vella;Prat de la Creu 29, Andorra la Vella, AD500, Andorra;42.5069716;1.5257986;83;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;A restaurant that continues to gain a loyal following thanks to its welcoming ambience, its high-quality ingredients and the professionalism of its staff. Delicious, creative cuisine plus a splendid wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8861;Kairiku;Spain;Campos;Nou 10, Campos, 07630, Spain;39.4334844;3.0185936;21;false;true;Japanese;A unique and intimate restaurant with just a single large table for 10 guests. Here, Kairuku’s chef recreates the Japanese “omakase” concept that fully respects tradition but which is not restricted to a set menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8862;Gamberro;Spain;Saragossa;Bolonia 26, Saragossa, 50008, Spain;41.6428881;-0.8829352;38;false;true;Creative;Run by a couple who, in keeping with the name of the restaurant (Gamberro translates as “joker” in Spanish), like to keep the atmosphere here both fun and a tad irreverent! The dishes here showcase flavours and presentation that aim to surprise!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8863;Arrels by Marga Coll;Spain;Ses Illetes;Paseo Illetes 7, Ses Illetes, 07184, Spain;39.5439021;2.5963468;94;true;false;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant offering lovingly prepared, honest cuisine. In the dining room, with its large windows overlooking the sea, enjoy highly personal Mallorcan cooking created using seasonal, market - fresh ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8864;La Encomienda;Spain;Villanueva de San Carlos;Alameda 34, Villanueva de San Carlos, 13379, Spain;38.6088619;-3.8759626;71;true;false;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant with a timeless La Mancha feel occupies an old cheese-making factory. Run by women, it focuses on seasonal, regional cuisine full of home-cooked flavours.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8865;Bresca;Spain;Cambrils;Doctor Fleming 4, Cambrils, 43850, Spain;41.0663268;1.064039;76;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Bresca is a restaurant with a modern, functional ambience where attention is paid to every single detail. The cuisine is a contemporary take on traditional dishes and is enhanced by an impressive selection of herbal teas and dessert wines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8866;Etxanobe Atelier;Spain;Bilbao;Juan de Ajuriaguerra 8, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2653543;-2.9314328;49;true;true;Creative;A restaurant with an unusual setting in a former glass factory in the centre of Bilbao which has managed to retain a few vestiges from its past.Bilbao-born chef Fernando Canales is at the helm of this culinary project featuring an elegant and intimate gastronomic dining room in which he is keen, first and foremost, to impress his guests with creative cooking based around two tasting menus (Chef Atelier and Chef Atelier Plus) and the very best raw ingredients. Elaborate presentation is key here, with fish dishes taking centre stage. Canales is constantly striving to create an ephemeral experience that becomes an unforgettable memory, aided and abetted where necessary by the very latest technology to achieve his goals.;Air conditioning;[]
8867;Sumaq;Spain;Palma;Cotoner 44, Palma, 07013, Spain;39.571339;2.6370479;66;false;false;Peruvian;A restaurant with a strong focus in the kitchen on the flavours and recipes of traditional Peruvian cooking. Its tasting menu is the perfect option for those keen to savour Peru’s renowned cuisine on this Spanish island.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8868;Casa 887;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Gran Vía 9, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20002, Spain;43.3245563;-1.9740584;64;false;false;Fusion, Contemporary;A casual restaurant occupying a stone basement with a modern feel (striking photos, neon lighting, background music etc) run by a Brazilian chef with a passion for fusion cooking, hence dishes with influences from France, Japan, Mexico etc. Discover the chef’s full creativity via an interesting 7-course tasting menu (887's Signature). An array of half-plate options is also available.;Air conditioning;[]
8869;Héctor Oribe;Spain;Páganos;Gasteiz 8, Páganos, 01309, Spain;42.5588451;-2.6048793;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant run by a pleasant married couple is one of those places that you love recommending to others. Here, the traditional cuisine with a contemporary touch is built around seasonal ingredients and showcased on a single tasting menu (a shorter version of the same menu is also available). Interesting dishes that we particularly enjoyed included the “canutillos” of black pudding and pine nuts with a red alubia and piparra pepper cream, the cod taco with chickpea hummus, piquillo peppers and a spinach pil-pil, and the fresh Idiazábal cheesecake with quince and walnuts.;Air conditioning;[]
8870;LUR;Spain;Madrid;Bolívar 11, Madrid, 28045, Spain;40.3922156;-3.691786;28;false;false;Contemporary;Taking its name from the Basque word for “earth”, this unpretentious yet welcoming restaurant boasts a contemporary decor that includes earthenware jars adorned with large tree-like olive branches. The young chef in charge here, Lucía Gutiérrez, is keen that the land and its soil are brought to life, hence their concise, attractive and modern-inspired menu that is based around seasonal ingredients from small-scale producers. Interesting dishes include the rice with aged partridge cooked on the barbecue and served with blood orange, Requesón cheese and Oloroso sherry, and the Tierra de Campos pigeon stew.;Air conditioning;[]
8871;Alberte;Spain;Vigo;Rosalía de Castro 65, Vigo, 36201, Spain;42.2378965;-8.712185;88;false;false;Grills, Farm to table;Here, owner-chef Alberte Gutiérrez’s aim is to offer high-quality, non-gimmicky cuisine based around the very best Galician meat and vegetables but with a special focus on the incredible fish and seafood from the Rías Baixas region (spider crab, lobster, langoustine, shrimp from local estuaries, wild bream etc), almost all of which are sourced from the fish auction in A Guarda. The seasonal à la carte shows a penchant for dishes cooked on the open grill, alongside interesting daily specials and two tasting menus (Esencia and Alberte).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8872;ita;Spain;Madrid;General Oráa 42, Madrid, 28006, Spain;40.4360525;-3.681315;22;true;false;Farm to table, Mediterranean Cuisine;“Ita” is the affectionate nickname by which grandmother Isabel was known by those that knew her, and through it chef Mariela Fernández pays her own small tribute to her personal memories and to family recipes. In this small restaurant in the Salamanca district, the hallmarks are simplicity and honesty, visible via a concise à la carte that changes with the seasons and which features a predominance of locally sourced organic vegetables, plus a few meat or fish options.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8873;L'Àpat;Spain;Molins de Rei;Del Carril 38, Molins de Rei, 08750, Spain;41.4106265;2.0194441;86;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;An efficiently managed family-run restaurant offering a good traditional menu that includes classic dishes such as sautéed Astorga chickpeas with garlic and butifarra sausage.;Air conditioning;[]
8874;Brasería Sansibar;Spain;O Grove;Balea 20-B, O Grove, 36988, Spain;42.4668441;-8.9055791;39;false;true;Grills;A family-run restaurant where everything revolves around the open grill and top-quality products, from Galician meats to fish from the local auction and seafood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8875;âme;Spain;Barcelona;Londres 91, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3930029;2.1500495;98;true;false;French Contemporary;The aim of this unusual bistro, run by two business partners who are also in charge of the kitchen, is to pay continued homage to French cuisine, while at the same time making full use of seasonal local ingredients. The à la carte, which changes on a regular basis, is complemented by a tasting menu that is based around the former’s signature dishes such as the “crêpe de mar” (Palamós red prawn pil-pil with a crispy crêpe), the “arroz caldoso de pato” (rice from the Ebro Delta, duck confit and artichokes from El Prat), and the pudding of Medjool dates, salted butter caramel and Tonka chantilly.;Air conditioning;[]
8876;Brabo;Spain;Barcelona;Séneca 28, Barcelona, 08006, Spain;41.39646;2.15558;20;false;true;Grills;If you’re a diehard carnivore, you’ll want to head straight for this contemporary yet unpretentious “asador” run by two young chefs where meat is the unquestionable star of the show. On the menu, which is particularly designed for sharing, homemade starters include wild boar mortadella, aged beef loin and country-style pâté. The main meat focus is on the rare French Gascon breed of black pig, similar to the Iberian breed. Despite the prevalence of meat on the menu, a fish of the day is always available, along with a varied choice of side dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
8877;Qué Leche;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Torres 22, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35002, Spain;28.1041694;-15.4170792;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine;If, as well as enjoying a meal, you are keen to be part of a gastronomic experience, this restaurant is well worth a visit! Although not overly spacious, this pleasant and informal restaurant is enthusiastically run by Jennise Ferrari, a Venezuelan chef who settled in Las Palmas in 2013. Here, she showcases fresh fusion cuisine that is based around local ingredients, with the added aim of creating attractive dishes inspired by further afield (Mexico, Asia, Japan etc). Many of the dishes are perfect for sharing: we can highly recommend the Saharan squid with a roast onion jus, ginger, squid ink and mature sheep’s cheese.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8878;Curioso;Spain;Peñafiel;Derecha Al Coso 22, Peñafiel, 47300, Spain;41.5955035;-4.11833;67;true;true;Contemporary;It is said that “those who search, will find” and based on this mantra, the young couple at Curioso appear to have found their own paradise! This restaurant, close to the famous Plaza del Coso, offers an attractive market-inspired à la carte featuring an updated take on traditional dishes. This is complemented by the Curioso tasting menu, on which you can savour dishes such as lamb trotter gyoza, venison bolognaise with fresh pasta, and croissant with oxtail and a bearnaise sauce.;Air conditioning;[]
8879;Candeal;Spain;Marbella;Plaza Blas Infante 1, Marbella, 29601, Spain;36.50968;-4.8821586;78;true;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Enjoy the flavours of Castilian cuisine in the heart of Marbella’s old quarter! Chef Pablo Rebollo’s cuisine, which comes as something of a surprise in this part of Spain. Here, he invites guests on a journey to discover creative Mediterranean cooking that has added personality thanks to the inclusion of interesting fermented ingredients, game dishes, pickles and escabeches, as well as a subtle nod to the cooking of his native Valladolid (as an example, the superb bread is delivered every day from Peñafiel). The à la carte is complemented by three tasting menus: Mercado Candeal (lunchtime only), Degustación Candeal and Gran Menú Candeal. The decor here simulates that of a typical bodega.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8880;Es Fanals;Spain;Port de Sóller;Bèlgica, Port de Sóller, 07108, Spain;39.80196;2.69946;66;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;What is particularly striking about this restaurant located within the confines of the Jumeirah Port Sóller Hotel & Spa, and whose name is in reference to the lights that fisherman use to help with their catch, is its location in the upper part of the complex, with a terrace boasting superb views of the Sierra de Tramuntana and the sea. The dining here, which is limited to a dinner service, is centred around three menus (Sabores de Mallorca, Gran Baleárico and Baleárico Verde), with a strong focus on the island’s cuisine. The sunsets here are a spectacle in their own right!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8882;El Ventador;Spain;Barruera;Passeig de Sant Feliu 49, Barruera, 25527, Spain;42.5049168;0.8038713;67;true;true;Contemporary;Carpaccio of tea-smoked Pyrenean venison, creamy mountain-style rice, wild mushrooms and quail, organic baby goat ribs and cheese from Taüll all feature on the menu at this restaurant with an attractive stone façade that blends in harmoniously with the other buildings on this main road. In the small dining room with a pleasant and welcoming ambience, enjoy cuisine that is steeped in Pyrenean tradition, albeit with a few modern and Asian touches added to the culinary mix. Options here include the à la carte designed for sharing, plus a surprise tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8883;Anhelo;Spain;Castelló de la Plana;Maestro Ripollés 6, Castelló de la Plana, 12003, Spain;39.98227;-0.03518;73;true;false;Farm to table, Contemporary;The heart and soul of this small eatery in the centre of town is owner-chef Cristian Granero, who began his career in the restaurant business as a baker and pastry chef, both of which served as a good apprenticeship before he headed to the kitchen stoves. His cuisine, the aim of which, in his own words, is to “wake up the senses and connect with the emotions”, is based around three menus: D'Uixó, Sentidos and Anhelo. The restaurant also boasts a kitchen that is visible to guests seated at one of its five tables. Because of these restricted numbers, it’s well worth booking ahead.;Air conditioning;[]
8884;Iñigo Lavado;Spain;Irun;Avenida Iparralde 43, Irun, 20304, Spain;43.3470346;-1.7873068;63;true;false;Contemporary;Located within the confines of the town’s attractive showground (Ficoba), this restaurant aims to offer a unique experience for its customers both in terms of its decor and cuisine. Its seasonal cooking, deeply rooted in Basque tradition, is showcased on the à la carte and two enticing set menus (Bidasoa and Uniendo Fronteras). Almost every dish on the à la carte can be ordered as half-raciones.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8885;Sol Blanc;Spain;Pals;Barri Molinet 14, Pals, 17256, Spain;41.9803352;3.1502704;22;true;true;Catalan, Seasonal Cuisine;A 19C farmhouse in the middle of the countryside. Honest Catalan cuisine based around local products such as tomatoes from its own vegetable garden to create dishes that include hearty stews.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8886;Las Torres;Spain;Huesca;María Auxiliadora 3, Huesca, 22003, Spain;42.140896;-0.412715;63;false;false;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;A classic-cum-contemporary restaurant with a profusion of wood that has been in business for over 30 years, and which takes its name from the area in which it is situated, known affectionately as “the three towers”. Its à la carte of traditional cuisine with a contemporary touch always features top-quality ingredients and is complemented by a tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8887;Bao Li;Spain;Madrid;Jovellanos 5, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.417069;-3.6967628;21;true;false;Chinese Contemporary;Make sure you don’t miss this luxurious, oriental-inspired eatery which raises the traditional impression of Chinese restaurants to another level thanks to its cuisine and standard of service. In the kitchen, chef Felipe Bao’s aim is to endow his dishes with the philosophy and exquisite nature of imperial Chinese cooking, which is built around solid Cantonese recipes. An excellent option for a romantic meal for two.;Air conditioning;[]
8888;El Petirrojo;Spain;Quintana de los Prados;Lugar de Quintana de los Prados 44, Quintana de los Prados, 09569, Spain;43.0759736;-3.5124855;37;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A welcoming restaurant occupying a stone house with a well-maintained small garden and a rustic interior featuring plenty of attention to detail. The culinary focus from the pleasant couple that owns El Petirrojo is on traditional Basque-influenced cuisine specialising in cod dishes.;;[]
8889;Ganbara;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;San Jerónimo 21, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20003, Spain;43.3234373;-1.9855144;19;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;While the large staff has set the rhythm of service, the quality of its pintxos has taken it to the height of success. It is complemented by an intimate and quaint dining room in the cellar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8890;Carea Bistró;Spain;Leon;Platerías 1, Leon, 24003, Spain;42.5972324;-5.567461;99;true;false;Contemporary;Run by a young couple, this bistro in the city’s Barrio Húmedo district owes its name to a local breed of dog (“carea leonés” or “Leonese sheepdog”). It is laid out on two floors with a small bar on the ground floor and the dining room upstairs. The contemporary-style dishes served here feature a hint of fusion and are based around ingredients from the local area.;Air conditioning;[]
8891;El Alférez;Spain;Vejer de la Frontera;Playa de El Palmar, Vejer de la Frontera, 11159, Spain;36.2265837;-6.0660979;77;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A great option for those keen to eat right by the beach. This family-run restaurant, in business since 1988, boasts a pleasant terrace where the focus is on traditional maritime-inspired fare sourced directly from the auction, a good selection of fried fish, grilled seafood, plus a delicious rice with shrimp dish. It also offers a menu dedicated exclusively to red almadraba tuna from the Petaca Chico fishery.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8892;Bergara;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;General Artetxe 8, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20002, Spain;43.324385;-1.9724306;59;false;false;Basque;A popular eatery in the Gros district of the city which has won various awards for its miniature take on haute cuisine! In its colourful and delightful bar you’ll find a vast array of innovative tapas and pinchos, both hot and cold, such as Txalupa (a gratin of mushrooms with prawns), Itxaso (monkfish with a seafood cream), Udaberri (courgette with a crayfish cream), plus the delicious foie gras with port-braised grapes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8894;Sa Poma;Spain;Orfes;Veïnat de la Palma, Orfes, 17468, Spain;42.190964;2.8550057;59;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A charming restaurant with a delightfully rustic ambience situated in the heart of the countryside. Contemporary Catalan cuisine with hints of Mallorcan influence that makes full use of produce from its own vegetable garden.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8895;MangasVerdes;Spain;Jaén;Bernabé Soriano 28, Jaén, 23001, Spain;37.7668209;-3.7876171;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A somewhat atypical gastro-bar located closed to the city’s cathedral. The à la carte features a choice of contemporary and fusion dishes and is complemented by a tasting menu and an impressive choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8896;L'Auró;Spain;Orís;Carretera C 17, Orís, 08573, Spain;42.0580812;2.240839;65;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A spacious family-run restaurant in a secluded setting. Good traditional menu based around locally sourced ingredients, including daily specials and proper knife-and-fork breakfasts!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8897;Eclectic;Spain;A Coruña;San Andrés 8, A Coruña, 15003, Spain;43.3713343;-8.4006063;73;false;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;A centrally located restaurant with a difference, given that its interior design resembles that of a private house. The team here sees itself at the heart of a culinary utopia which showcases its cuisine on two tasting menus, both creative in feel but with a nod to Galicia and its cooking of yesteryear.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8898;Cabanas;Spain;Lalín;Pintor Laxeiro 3, Lalín, 36500, Spain;42.6599318;-8.112379;76;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The cuisine emanating from the Cabanas’ kitchens is a modern take on traditional dishes, enhanced by a variety of seasonal dishes and game. Make sure you try Lalín’s famous "cocido gallego", a typical Galician stew.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
8899;Guethary;Spain;Palma;Carrer de Marbella 36, Palma, 07001, Spain;39.52352;2.7386;26;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant, with a name that pays tribute to the famous Elkano restaurant in Guetaria, is located within the walls of the Iberostar Selection Playa de Palma hotel. In its sophisticated dining room, with its predominant white colour scheme, chef Aitor Arregui creates cuisine similar to that showcased in his award-winning restaurant in the province of Guipúzcoa, with grilled fish and seafood from Mallorcan waters the undoubted starts of the show. The à la carte, featuring standout dishes such as John Dory and the option of half-plates for some choices, is well supported by two enticing tasting menus.;Air conditioning;[]
8900;Kita;Spain;Vigo;Avenida de Hispanidade 89, Vigo, 36203, Spain;42.2266807;-8.7269549;100;true;false;Japanese, Fusion;Located in a residential district of the city, this restaurant, with its simple minimalist-style decor, showcases Japanese techniques and its array of slicing skills but with top-quality Galician ingredients (hence its Japanese name, which translates as “Fusion of the North”). The cooking here, which is limited to a single tasting menu, features dishes such as Rubia Gallega beef gyoza with kimchi and Galician-style usuzukuri.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8901;Local de Ensayo;Spain;Murcia;Fuensanta 5, Murcia, 30001, Spain;37.9847496;-1.1275943;54;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Located just a few steps from the cathedral, with a completely revamped concept that comes as a pleasant surprise in a setting occupying the former home of the equally successful Ajo y Agua restaurant. The contemporary and elegant interior features an initial dining room with a large table for groups, and then a second dining space from where the kitchen is partially visible to guests. Here, chef David López conjures up cuisine that is high on presentation and showcases a strong creative flair that he describes as “experimentation", with an extensive à la carte and no fewer than three tasting menus (Tradición, Endocardio and Desfibrilador).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8902;D'Berto;Spain;O Grove;Teniente Domínguez 84, O Grove, 36980, Spain;42.4845456;-8.8609056;81;true;false;Seafood, Galician;At D’Berto, you’ll experience the full potential and expression of the local estuary’s produce. For those for whom scale is of little importance, this is definitely the place, where you can enjoy a truly surprising array of fish and seafood accompanied by excellent service. Perfectly cooked grilled dishes and stews are more important here than technique, though the latter is certainly not lacking. Options include an array of shellfish and several classic dishes such as the pan-fried lobster and the spider crab.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
8904;El Refugio;Spain;Oleiros;Plaza de Galicia 8, Oleiros, 15173, Spain;43.33352;-8.316242;41;true;false;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant with a solid track record that opened its doors in 1975. It features a bar at the entrance, plus a dining room bathed in natural light where the extensive à la carte of traditional and international dishes features fish, seafood, excellent meats and a few seasonal game specialities. Dishes worthy of note include the “salpicón de lubrigante” (lobster) and, among the desserts, the popular egg yolk soufflé, which needs to be ordered at the start of your meal to allow time to prepare it.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
8905;Palio;Spain;Ocaña;Mayor 12, Ocaña, 45300, Spain;39.9589018;-3.499857;100;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This centrally located restaurant, with its spacious and stylishly appointed dining rooms, is run by two brothers with a single desire to please their guests. This they achieve via a concise à la carte and the popular “Palio” menu, featuring pleasantly updated traditional cuisine. Their home-baked bread pays homage to their grandfather, who was a baker. Wines from the menu are also available for purchase to take home with you.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8906;Marmurio do Río;Spain;Allariz;Rúa Do Cárcere 7, Allariz, 32660, Spain;42.190297;-7.8014762;84;true;false;Contemporary;A unique restaurant occupying the stone house that was once home to the century-old Casa Fandiño restaurant. Today, the name, which translates as the “murmur of the river” in Galician, pays a discreet tribute to the poem Dark Shadow by the renowned Galician poet Rosalía de Castro. The first thing that strikes you here is the meticulous, rustic-contemporary interior decor, which is almost an extension of the charm found in the streets of Allariz. Madrid-born chef Luis Moreno, who previously enjoyed success alongside fellow chef Daniel Ochoa at the Montia restaurant in San Lorenzo del Escorial, created this project in the town where he always spent his summers. Dining options are based around two tasting menus: one short option entitled “Río” and a second longer one called Marmurio. The chef works with small-scale producers from the locality and the Sierra de Madrid, and even uses lemons from his own lemon tree! Through his menus, he tries to draw comparisons with the tame and at times wilder characteristics of the local River Arnoia.;;[]
8907;Ausiàs;Spain;Pedreguer;de la Cova Santa 2, Pedreguer, 03750, Spain;38.7926443;0.0351295;30;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;If you happen to find yourself in Pedreguer’s old town, this restaurant close to the market will definitely attract your attention thanks to its façade and its meticulous and contemporary interior design. On their two menus (Valentina and Ausiàs March, both with the option of adding an additional tripe dish), the young couple at the helm, Ausiàs Signes and Felicia Guerra, showcase Mediterranean cuisine that they have impressively brought up to date and which is always built around local and regional ingredients. The desserts here stand out – and for good reason: in 2022 (when he was head pastry chef at the renowned Tatau restaurant in Huesca) Ausiàs won the Pastelero Revelación en Madrid Fusión award.;Air conditioning;[]
8908;Beiramar;Spain;O Grove;Avenida Beiramar 30, O Grove, 36980, Spain;42.4955919;-8.8626486;16;false;true;Seafood;An attractive and intimate family-run restaurant with an impressive live seafood tank at the entrance that highlights the cuisine on offer here (superb fish and seafood and a few rice dishes).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8909;Basque Eneko;Spain;Seville;Plaza de la Magdalena 1, Seville, 41001, Spain;37.3912642;-5.9969214;75;false;true;Basque;Discover the contemporary Basque cuisine of award-winning chef Eneko Atxa, who has transported his consistent and highly creative cooking to Seville, using ingredients that are truly sublime.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8910;El Cenador del Azul;Spain;Mieres;Aller 51, Mieres, 33600, Spain;43.2542856;-5.7770744;41;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant that is both classic and contemporary in style where attention to detail is key in every aspect of its unassuming but superb service, which it considers an art form. Updated traditional à la carte with set menu options at lunchtime.;Air conditioning;[]
8911;Pico Velasco;Spain;Carasa;Barrio Angustina, Carasa, 39762, Spain;43.3688338;-3.4447959;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the Parque Natural de las Marismas de Santoña, Victoria y Joyel, and more specifically between Limpias and Carasa, the Pico Velasco boutique hotel is a superb example of 17C Cantabrian civil architecture. On the tastefully renovated interior, award-winning chef Ignacio Solana showcases his traditionally based modern cooking that always aims to highlight the full value of local and seasonal ingredients. Choose between two tasting menus: Albiar (which translates as “sunrise”), and Sincio (a Cantabrian expression that is used to denote a desire or craving). A standout dish here is the trout with acidulated vegetable soup.;Car park,Great view;[]
8912;TA-KUMI;Spain;Marbella;Gregorio Marañón 4, Marbella, 29602, Spain;36.5090426;-4.8965082;33;false;true;Japanese;Well run by its two Japanese owners, TA-KUMI offers extremely friendly service which has become one of its key leitmotifs. Its extensive à la carte menu of Japanese specialities, which now includes delicious personalised mochis, features one particular dish that is definitely worth trying: the California roll with tempura prawns and green asparagus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
8913;Mirasierra;Spain;Mogarraz;Miguel Angel Maillo 56, Mogarraz, 37610, Spain;40.4930055;-6.0496447;66;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Mirasierra occupies a large house with several dining rooms, with those to the rear the pick of the bunch thanks to their attractive views. Delicious Iberian pork stews, wild mushrooms, grilled meats and cheeses all feature on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8914;Arriaga;Spain;Granada;Avenida de la Ciencia 2, Granada, 18006, Spain;37.1620447;-3.6071322;26;false;true;Contemporary;Access to Arriaga is via a lift, given its location at the top of the Centro Cultural CajaGranada Memoria de Andalucía, a unique building that stands almost 60m in height and boasts spectacular views of the city. The cuisine here, based around two tasting menus, is an updated take on traditional cuisine inspired by local recipes but with a nod to other food cultures and painstaking presentation.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
8915;El Olivo;Spain;Vigo;Rúa Oliva 2, Vigo, 36202, Spain;42.2394228;-8.7253155;61;true;false;Contemporary;Located in the heart of the “casco vello”, just a few steps from the Concatedral - Basílica de Santa María de Vigo, this restaurant stands out for its setting in an old renovated manor house that dates back to Templar times and is now a multi-purpose venue that includes a terrace, event spaces, a luxurious cocktail bar etc, plus a mix of tradition (note the stone walls) and design. The cuisine here bears the signature of chef Pepe Solla whose focus is on greater simplicity and individual ingredients compared to his award-winning one-Michelin-star Solla restaurant. His Josper oven takes centre stage as showcased by his standout grilled fish dishes, including his Josper-grilled John Dory. The chef’s table in the kitchen enables guests to watch the chefs at work at close quarters!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8917;Miramar;Spain;Cambrils;Paseo Miramar 30, Cambrils, 43850, Spain;41.065475;1.059861;54;false;false;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;Located next to the 17C Torre del Port, this restaurant is run by the third generation of the same family. Maritime - inspired cuisine with lots of attention to detail, plus an impressive dessert trolley!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8918;Casa Romántica;Spain;Agaete;Carretera de los Berrazales, Agaete, 35480, Spain;28.0828477;-15.6693989;99;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A family run restaurant with a relaxed and informal feel in a highly picturesque setting by the road running through the Agaete valley. The cuisine here showcases Canary Island cooking which has been brought bang up to date and has a strong focus on zero-mile ingredients. This is highlighted on an à la carte, with half-portion options, and above all on its constantly changing tasting menus. The restaurant also produces its own wine and coffee.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8919;Contrastes;Spain;Vilanova i la Geltrú;Unió 44, Vilanova i la Geltrú, 08800, Spain;41.2254399;1.7273014;21;true;true;Fusion, Contemporary;A restaurant with an informal, contemporary feel run by a young Brazilian-born chef. Fusion cuisine that takes much of its influence from Asia and Peru, plus an extensive tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8920;Triciclo;Spain;Madrid;Santa María 28, Madrid, 28014, Spain;40.412926;-3.69725;93;false;true;Creative;When the three chefs who run Triciclo (Javier Goya, Javier Mayor and David Alfonso) opened this restaurant in the Las Letras district, they asked themselves: what type of restaurant would we like to eat in? The result is this minimalist-style eatery with a strong focus on top-quality ingredients and sustainability, featuring relaxed dishes that showcase the very best seasonal produce. Their aim is to recreate pure and traditional flavours without closing the door on the culinary cultures of countries such as Peru and Japan. Choose between two menus (Clásico and Semanal), both with a tasting option.;Air conditioning;[]
8921;Taberna de Libreros;Spain;Salamanca;Libreros 24, Salamanca, 37008, Spain;40.9617619;-5.6672251;35;true;false;International;Located in the very heart of Salamanca’s historic quarter, just a few steps from the monumental Plateresque façade of the university featuring the famous sculpture of a frog (or is it a toad?) popular with tourists, this restaurant boasts a stylish setting with a classic-cum-contemporary feel. Based around seasonal ingredients sourced from around the province, the à la carte includes interesting international influences – the result of experience acquired by owner-chef Alberto Hernández in countries as diverse as China, Indonesia, Japan, Thailand, Mexico etc. Attractive set daily menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8922;Laia Erretegia;Spain;Hondarribia;Arkolla Auzoa 33, Hondarribia, 20280, Spain;43.3577777;-1.8040546;98;true;false;Grills;Laia occupies what were once the stables of an old country house. Here, you can savour different cuts of meat aged over a long period as well as fresh fish, all cooked on the open grill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8923;Alhambra;Spain;Pamplona;Francisco Bergamín 7, Pamplona, 31003, Spain;42.8126659;-1.6412571;62;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, the younger sibling of the award-winning Europa, bears the quality stamp and DNA of the Idoate family, where the brother-and-sister team of Iñaki and Esther run the dining room. It also happens to be one of Pamplona’s classic dining addresses – the reason why it is often full with its regular and loyal customers. The à la carte (with the option of ordering “raciones” so that you can try different dishes) is complemented by two tasting menus. One of its most typical dishes is the cod “ajoarriero” with lobster.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8924;Bido;Spain;A Coruña;Marcial del Adalid 2, A Coruña, 15005, Spain;43.3622106;-8.4058798;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Well - prepared dishes, high - quality products and delicate presentation are to the fore in this restaurant. The designer - inspired decor and contemporary cooking come as a pleasant surprise.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8925;Pahissa del Mas ...;Spain;Pals;Barri Molinet 16, Pals, 17256, Spain;41.982255;3.1513591;18;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant occupies the “straw loft” of the Mas Pou, a farmhouse built in 1352 and surrounded by rice fields. Contemporary cuisine with a highly personal touch in which locally sourced ingredients take centre stage.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8926;99 sushi bar;Spain;Alcobendas;Estafeta 2, Alcobendas, 28109, Spain;40.5148129;-3.6528944;22;false;false;Japanese;This modern Japanese restaurant is located in a pleasant setting that is perfect to escape the hustle and bustle of the city. It is particularly noteworthy for its bar, where the sushi chef prepares dishes in front of guests, and the cascade of water forming a backdrop behind him. The cuisine does not follow the doctrines of Japanese cuisine to the letter, instead creating popular dishes in different ways that will find favour with everyone. Make sure you try the tiger prawn tempura!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8927;El Pescador;Spain;Cudillero;Tolombreo de Arriba s/n, Cudillero, 33150, Spain;43.5587978;-6.1469671;53;true;true;Seafood;A family - run restaurant offering a very extensive menu including a variety of Asturian dishes and above all local fish and seafood (hake, monkfish, bream etc).;Car park,Terrace;[]
8928;Torralbenc Menorca;Spain;Cala en Porter;Carretera Maó-Cala en Porter, Cala en Porter, 07730, Spain;39.8874028;4.1467176;97;false;true;Farm to table;This attractive restaurant, where the cuisine is overseen by renowned chef Gorka Txapartegui (Alameda restaurant in Hondarribia), occupies a farmhouse surrounded by vineyards and boasting a tranquil terrace, all of which comes as a pleasant surprise. It also provides the dining service for the hotel of the same name (awarded one Michelin key) and will delight guests with its tranquil terraces, contemporary European and internationally inspired cuisine, and a constant nod to local flavours and native ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8929;Cau de l'Ateneu;Spain;Manresa;Les Piques 1, Manresa, 08241, Spain;41.7234195;1.8251958;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Occupying the magnificent Ateneo de Manresa, this restaurant is run by a married couple, Xaro and Jacint. Updated traditional cuisine with a focus on carefully selected ingredients and meticulous presentation.;Air conditioning;[]
8930;al kostat;Spain;Barcelona;Ronda San Antoni 41 - 1º, Barcelona, 08011, Spain;41.3826752;2.1635774;54;false;true;Catalan, Traditional Cuisine;Occupying the former Moritz beer brewery where al kostat shares its dining spaces and kitchen with the gastronomic Alkimia restaurant. Here, you can enjoy the more informal and less expensive cuisine of award-winning chef Jordi Vilà on a Catalan-inspired à la carte designed for sharing. We can highly recommend the “kokotxas” (cheek) of hake pil-pil with white Ganxet beans.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8931;Kamikaze;Spain;Barcelona;Roselló 197, Barcelona, 08036, Spain;41.3924339;2.155568;56;false;false;Fusion, Creative;This unpretentious “taberna”, which takes its name from the Japanese word for “divine wine”, is run by two chefs who formed a close bond while working at Disfrutar (now a three-star Michelin restaurant) and went on to launch of their own joint project. Enric Buendia and Aristide Ribalta apply the techniques they have acquired in their quest for a creative approach that looks at Asian cooking (particularly Japanese) from a strong Mediterranean perspective. The end result is cuisine with surprising presentation and a nod to Catalan gastronomy. Choose between an à la carte that changes with the seasons and the Kamikaze tasting menu, available in two versions (short or long).;Wheelchair access;[]
8932;Kaia Kaipe;Spain;Getaria;General Arnao 4, Getaria, 20808, Spain;43.3047331;-2.203494;96;true;true;Seafood;A classic address (the Arregi family opened the restaurant’s doors in 1962) that stands out for its superb views of the port of Getaria (hence its name – “Kaia” translates as “port” in Basque while “Kaipe” means “below the port”) and distinct maritime feel. It features a pleasant terrace, attractive dining rooms, its own live fish and seafood tanks, a superb wine cellar, plus an open grill (the star of the show) out on the street. Make sure you try the prawns (either grilled or fried in batter) and the superb grilled turbot (for two). The impressive wine cellar is home to around 1 500 labels and over 40 000 bottles!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
8933;Keki;Spain;Murcia;Fuensanta 4, Murcia, 30001, Spain;37.9846074;-1.1279867;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant and tapas bar with a modern feel is just a few metres from the cathedral. Contemporary cuisine with an emphasis on impressive textures and interesting combinations of ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
8934;Zapirain;Spain;Bilbao;Juan Ajuriaguerra 22, Bilbao, 48009, Spain;43.2658242;-2.9333955;37;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant with a long history that has finally arrived in Bilbao after half a century and more in Lekeitio! Here, high-quality traditional cuisine is to the fore, specialising in fish and seafood in particular, which the team prepares with as little fuss as possible in order to respect its true essence (we thoroughly enjoyed the grilled white prawns and the hake “kokotxas”). Meat does feature, however, including a mouthwatering T-bone steak. For dessert, the home-made tarts are a must!;Air conditioning;[]
8935;Laua;Spain;Langarica;Langarika 4, Langarica, 01206, Spain;42.835223;-2.4295253;74;true;true;Creative;In this rustically inspired property, the Ramírez brothers entice guests with two meticulous surprise tasting menus, one concise, the other more extensive, but both highlighting a creative touch.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8936;Ca'Suso;Spain;Oviedo;Marqués de Gastañaga 13, Oviedo, 33009, Spain;43.3592958;-5.8432175;78;true;false;Contemporary;A welcoming bistro-style eatery with a rustic-contemporary feel, enthusiastically run by two brothers (Vicente and Iván) who humbly refer to their restaurant as a canteen-like “casa de comidas”. Their more modern take on traditional, Asturian-based cooking includes an à la carte (don’t miss the famous liquid La Peral cheese croquettes or the spider crab ravioli with fennel) and two enticing menus. Some half-plate options are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
8937;Tramo;Spain;Madrid;Eugenio Salazar 56, Madrid, 28002, Spain;40.4481497;-3.6754617;83;true;false;Contemporary;One of those restaurants that flies the flag for sustainability, a commitment that is behind its decision to prioritise the recycling of materials and bioconstruction building methods. In this setting occupying one of the legendary concert rooms of the Movida Madrileña movement (the space was previously home to the El Garaje Hermético bar), its natural resources are put to effective commercial use through this socially inclusive project with an honest approach and a desire to help people who have difficulty accessing the jobs market. On the menu here you’ll find contemporary dishes prepared using ingredients from small-scale Spanish producers, farmers and local breeders.;Air conditioning;[]
8938;El Rincón de Moraga;Spain;Los Llanos de Aridane;San Antonio 4, Los Llanos de Aridane, 38760, Spain;28.6559728;-17.9267838;18;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Creative;An attractive family-run restaurant (enthusiastically led by the Cruz siblings, with Miriam in charge of the dining room and Jorge in the kitchen) occupying an old Canary Island property dating back to the 18C with a delightful rustic-cum-regional-style interior decor. Here, the updated take on traditional cuisine showcases ingredients from La Palma, and combines local dishes with others from further afield. Choose between the à la carte and two enticing tasting menus (Sentidos and Sin Filtros). Don’t miss the spectacularly textured cheesecake!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8939;Cala;Spain;Granada;José Luís Pérez Pujadas 7, Granada, 18006, Spain;37.1604826;-3.608021;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Although located outside the city’s old quarter, Cala is well worth a visit, enhanced by its new decor featuring greater levels of comfort and an open-view kitchen. Its updated version of traditional cuisine always champions seasonal ingredients along with a nod to French recipes (the kitchen is run by French-born chef Samuel Hernández). Choose between a concise gourmet à la carte and the Cala tasting menu.;Air conditioning;[]
8940;Casa Antonio;Spain;Jaén;Fermín Palma 3, Jaén, 23008, Spain;37.7745508;-3.7875808;27;true;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with a terrace, tapas bar and several dining rooms that are contemporary in feel. The menu here features up - to - date dishes with their roots in traditional and regional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8941;Reina XIV;Spain;San Ildefonso o La Granja;Reina 14, San Ildefonso o La Granja, 40100, Spain;40.9018451;-4.0073418;35;false;false;Contemporary;This classically elegant restaurant located close to Parador de La Granja has taken on a new lease of life in the hands of Borja Aldea, who has trained in leading restaurants such as Etxanobe and Disfrutar. It offers two contemporary-style tasting menus (Reina and Felipe V – both with a wine-pairing option) that champion its surroundings and local history and feature courses entitled Campesinos (Peasants), Nobleza (Nobility), Realeza (Royalty) etc.;Air conditioning;[]
8942;Shibui;Spain;Santa Cruz de Tenerife;Paseo Milicias de Garachico 1, Santa Cruz de Tenerife, 38002, Spain;28.468121;-16.24803;58;true;true;Japanese;This Japanese restaurant occupies the space that was formerly the Kazan and can be viewed as a reinvention of the latter. And although chef Gerardo Cruz is at the helm, the award-winning David Arauz (Zuara Sushi, Madrid) still oversees the cuisine here. The word “shibui” refers to the Japanese aesthetic of beauty and minimalism, and as such the aim here is to see beauty in everything around us, including its imperfections, from a respectful and mature standpoint. The à la carte is complemented by the excellent Shibui menu as well as an Omakase-style option that takes guests on a journey of gastronomic discovery. Whatever you choose, as you take a seat at the bar you will develop an even greater appreciation of the Japanese mystique of each dish. The team mainly works with the freshest quality fish caught daily off the island’s coastline. We can also highly recommend the traditional nigiris, created by hand one by one.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8943;Desborre;Spain;Madrid;De la Unión 8, Madrid, 28013, Spain;40.417347;-3.7103989;52;true;false;Contemporary;Offering dishes such as soufflé crackling, chicken in citrus escabeche, and “green chromatic in different textures”, this restaurant in the Austrias district very close to the royal palace is the fiefdom of Rioja-born chef Lucía Grávalos. Here, she showcases her permanent commitment to the land, organic ingredients, free-grazing livestock and sustainable fishing... as well as her rekindling of memories of her grandmother Ana Mari’s recipes and her passion for vegetables, which are always sourced and prepared in strict alignment with her culinary focus. The rustic-contemporary ambience is that of a stylish bistro, with a surprising display counter of fermented products (kombuchas, kefirs, shrubs etc) by the entrance. The contemporary-inspired à la carte is complemented by two interesting tasting menus (Petit and Desborre).;Air conditioning;[]
8944;Regueiro da Cova;Spain;Verín;Alameda 21, Verín, 32600, Spain;41.9417691;-7.4405235;96;true;true;Galician;This restaurant, located along the well-maintained banks of the Támega, the river that criss-crosses the town of Verín in the province of Ourense, is not be missed, with its focus on traditional Galician cooking and the typical flavours and ingredients (organic veal and chestnuts in season) of the Monterrei area, which the chef combines with a more contemporary approach. A standout dish here is the vanilla panna cotta with homemade caramel, made with almond milk, biscuit crumbs, macerated strawberries and fruits of the forest.;Air conditioning;[]
8945;BaLó;Spain;Barcelona;Déu I Mata 141, Barcelona, 08029, Spain;41.390405;2.1391358;84;true;true;Contemporary;BaLó is run by chef couple Lena María Grané and Ricky Smith who met while working in London, hence the unusual name of the restaurant which combines the first syllable of Barcelona and London respectively. The contemporary-influenced cooking here, which also showcases some international influences, is centred around several menus: one, a more reasonably priced “Mediodía” (midweek lunch only), and two more extensive menus entitled Baló and Degustación. This contemporary-style restaurant boasts a stylish and comfortable decor, pleasant lighting, as well as an attractive glass-fronted private dining room. We loved the squid noodles with chicken skin crumble, shiso and chicken tea!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8946;Kabuki Madrid;Spain;Madrid;Lagasca 38, Madrid, 28001, Spain;40.4232066;-3.6856126;69;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;The Kabuki Group’s latest culinary venture, in the heart of the city’s Salamanca district, remains faithful to its roots, inviting guests to explore dishes with their essence in Japanese cuisine but with an Iberian touch – a concept which has been synonymous with the Kabuki brand over the years and its desire to transport guests back to Japan. In this spacious setting, with its restrained lighting and meticulous decor, the cuisine is centred on a tasting menu complemented by an extensive cocktail menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8947;Bakea;Spain;Mungia;Olalde Berezia Kalea 1, Mungia, 48100, Spain;43.3574809;-2.8505789;59;false;true;Regional Cuisine;This minimalist-style restaurant, with its dominant dark colour scheme, pays homage to the local terroir, iron, fire, arts and crafts, and to those meals with family and friends that are forever engraved on our memory. The large central table recalls the spirit of traditional Basque dining societies known as “txokos”, given that the idea here is for guests to share different dishes and experiences. From the unique wood-fired grill, designed by the chef himself, and the space used for hot smoking, the team creates a single, highly personal tasting menu with strong roots in the Basque Country that is always constructed around just a few well-balanced ingredients, all of which are sourced locally and are fully respectful of the seasons.;Air conditioning;[]
8948;Sa Taula;Spain;Donostia / San Sebastián;Segundo Ispizua 27, Donostia / San Sebastián, 20001, Spain;43.3241578;-1.97015;16;true;false;Contemporary;Eating at this diminutive restaurant, in the heart of the Gros district, is like being welcomed to the home of a good friend, such is the warm welcome and the glass of Cava almost imperceptibly placed in your hand on arrival. The two owner-chefs, Carlos and Manel, cook, chat, serve and wash the dishes, seemingly at the same time, and in a highly relaxed atmosphere given that they only attend to a maximum ten guests per sitting, all eating together. They work with a single surprise menu, usually based around ingredients sourced from small-scale local producers. Drinks are included in the price.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8950;Indómito;Spain;Santiago de Compostela;Rúa Do Doutor Teixeiro 28, Santiago de Compostela, 15701, Spain;42.8741569;-8.5456081;86;true;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Just a few minutes from the city’s stunning old quarter you’ll find the latest venture of chef Martín Vázquez (ex head chef at Casa Marcelo), who is following his own path with this relaxed restaurant that showcases his indomitable (“indómito” in Spanish) spirit. In this meticulously arranged setting, where the open kitchen behind the counter tales centre stage, the à la carte features some 20 options that constantly rotate in line with the availability of seasonal ingredients (clam soup, hake from Celeiro, semifreddo of avocado and sea bream with a jalapeño sauce). The chef continually interacts with guests, suggesting dishes so that they can create their own menu, including options for sharing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
8951;Nantes;Spain;Madrid;Maestro Arbós 15, Madrid, 28045, Spain;40.3890093;-3.695072;35;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This simple restaurant with an urban feel and a kitchen overlooking the dining room takes its name from the affection that the chef’s grandfather had for the Nantes variety of carrot that he used to grow in his vegetable garden, then transport in his vehicle to the city’s erstwhile Legazpi market. Here, traditional, seasonal cooking is to the fore, which is unpretentious yet delicious and impressively prepared. This is showcased on a good daily menu that is separate from the à la carte. In the vegetable section of the latter we particularly enjoyed the chickpea stew with cuttlefish and pig’s trotters.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8952;Coto de Quevedo Origen;Spain;Torre de Juan Abad;Paraje Tejeras Viejas, Torre de Juan Abad, 13344, Spain;38.5798141;-3.049219;79;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Thanks to options such as loaves of candeal wheat flour bread baked in the town’s communal oven, delicious home-produced partridge pâté, comforting soups, and chickpea and bean stews, the dining in this restaurant is very much focused on everyday food, in contrast to its award-winning older sibling (Coto de Quevedo Evolución). It is one of those places that is good for the soul, and one which connects guests staying at this charming rural hotel directly with the countryside, accompanied by similarly friendly and easy-going service. Chef José Antonio Medina continues to focus on game, which is part of the restaurant’s DNA, as part of a more traditional style of cooking that is an ode to time-honoured and home-inspired recipes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8953;Rêver;Spain;Las Palmas de Gran Canaria;Armas 7, Las Palmas de Gran Canaria, 35001, Spain;28.10189;-15.41411;96;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, International;Located just a few steps from the Casa de Colón in the heart of the historic Vegueta district, where the city was first established, this restaurant boasts a pleasantly rustic-contemporary decor of sturdy natural stone walls and numerous decorative wood features. The cuisine embraces an array of delicious and copious dishes that are based around classic international fare enhanced by influences from countries such as Spain, France, Italy and the UK. The tartare of tuna belly with Asian flavours and wasabi and avocado sorbet came as a particularly pleasant surprise.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
8954;El Duque;Spain;Medina-Sidonia;Avenida del Mar 10, Medina-Sidonia, 11170, Spain;36.4626722;-5.9306744;29;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This family-run business has a welcoming bar at the entrance, with several tables for tapas-style dining, plus a bright and welcoming “asador”-style dining room surrounded by large windows. Its extensive à la carte is a clear reflection of its passion for meat (e.g., roast shoulder of goat, oxtail stew), game (stuffed partridge) and traditional recipes, although it also includes some good fish and more contemporary-style dishes. Make sure you leave space for some of Medina Sidonia’s typical desserts (Alfajores, Amarguillos, Tortas Pardas etc).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8955;Kotuwa;;Singapore;New Bahru, #01-03, 46 Kim Yam Road, 239351, Singapore;1.2929748;103.8388373;86;false;false;Sri Lankan;Moved to this spot in 2024, Kotuwa is named after the CBD of Colombo. From quintessential Sri Lankan street food to curries, every bite is loaded with big flavours. Seafood is their strong suit, especially crab prepared in myriad ways. With its balanced, layered flavours and the subtle warmth of cinnamon, the crab curry really stands out. Hoppers – crispy pancakes made with fermented rice – are perfect for mopping up the delicious curry sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8956;Solo;;Singapore;45 Amoy Street, 069871, Singapore;1.2806216;103.8469554;90;false;false;Italian;On Amoy Street where F&B outlets abound, Solo stands out with a relaxing vibe, an action-packed open kitchen and a regularly changing Italian menu that celebrates fresh, seasonal ingredients. The 5-course gourmet menu is a great way to sample some of its signature dishes, such as al dente homemade tagliolini topped with Japanese Bafun uni bursting with briny sweetness and umami. At lunch, the 3- or 4-course seasonal set offers great value.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8957;Ki Su;;Singapore;#01-01, 60 Tras Street, 078999, Singapore;1.2778193;103.8441991;83;false;false;Vegetarian;In a minimalistic room, the Taiwanese owner-chef serves an omakase menu of creative vegetarian courses in which Japanese and French culinary traditions converge. Modern cooking techniques like sous vide are used to imbue plant-based ingredients with meaty flavours and textures. Smoked capsicum and pumpkin purée are made to look like akami and uni in their nigiri sushi. The menu changes regularly to keep it fresh.;;[]
8958;Kitchenman Nasi Lemak;;Singapore;CT Hub, #01-08/13, 2 Kallang Avenue, 339407, Singapore;1.3120852;103.8628154;53;false;false;Malaysian;The Malaysian owner opened this simple shop in 2024, specialising in authentic nasi lemak, often considered the national dish of his home country. The chef, who is also Malaysian, cooks rice in coconut milk with pandan leaves, and garnishes it with fried anchovies, peanuts, fried egg, sliced cucumber and spicy sambal. For a substantial meal, add sides such as ayam berempah (fried chicken leg), rendang chicken or ayam kunyit (turmeric chicken).;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
8959;Wok Hei Hor Fun;;Singapore;Redhill Market, #01-94, 85 Redhill Lane, 150085, Singapore;1.2874024;103.8183527;36;true;true;Street Food;For over 30 years, locals have been coming here for the fried hor fun (flat rice noodles) – laden with wok hei, nicely charred and in a sauce that clings to the noodles. Choose from beef, fish or assorted toppings, and don't miss the cracklings.;Cash only;[]
8960;Song Kee Teochew Fish Porridge;;Singapore;Newton Food Centre, #01-37, 500 Clemenceau Avenue North, 229495, Singapore;1.311974;103.839442;70;false;true;Street Food;The fish porridge and fish head bee hoon are the main events here. The porridge is loaded with deboned fresh mackerel that imparts deep umami and sweetness. Chinese celery and coriander instantly brighten the flavour profile.;Cash only;[]
8961;Sir Elly's;China Mainland;Shanghai;13F, The Peninsula Hotel, Bund 32, 32 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.235736;121.450915;75;false;true;European Contemporary;Named after the hotel's founder, the opulent space punctuated by red accents commands gorgeous river views. The upscale ambiance makes this a perfect venue for a date. The kitchen turns local ingredients into original creations with bold flavours, dramatic plating and modern Asian twists. The substantial wine list will keep any oenophile happy. If you're not quite ready to call it a night, consider heading to the rooftop bar for digestifs.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8962;Yè Shanghai;China Mainland;Shanghai;3F, Infinitus Mall, 168 Hubin Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2225898;121.4733099;88;false;true;Shanghainese;Though moved into a shopping mall, the grey-brick façade is reminiscent of Shikumen architecture style. In stark contrast, the interior sports velvet sofas in gold and modern art for a touch of glamour. Start your night with creative cocktails from the bar. Then sample their Shanghainese classics like braised pork belly, sautéed shrimps with wild garlic, or xiao long bao. Try also hairy crab dishes such as stuffed crab shell when available.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
8963;Pop;China Mainland;Shanghai;7F, Bund 3, 3 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.234083;121.490738;18;true;false;European;Blue and white sofas work well with the wood and marble décor to exude a casual, yet elegant vibe, but it’s the breathtaking river views from the terrace that leave everyone in awe. Classic European choices abound on the menu, especially grilled meats and seafood. Try the house-made foie gras pâté, or pasta with black truffle. Pop also serves brunch every morning – so you can start your day with bacon and eggs with gorgeous vistas in the gentle morning sun.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8964;Lin Jiang Yan;China Mainland;Shanghai;216 Fucheng Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.234001;121.497186;30;false;true;Jiangzhe;Remodelled from a heritage building (c 1902), this restaurant is perfect for banquets and entertainment. The main area and private rooms all share the same river views. The young head chef, who used to work for a hotel in Shanghai, updates traditional Jiangzhe cooking with creative twists. Pre-order his Fukubukuro Yanduxian – tofu skin pouches stuffed with ground pork and shepherd's purse in a rich broth of cured and fresh pork with bamboo shoots.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
8965;Xin Yuan Lou;China Mainland;Shanghai;Building No.4, InterContinental Ruijin Hotel, 118 Ruijin Er Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.1983334;121.4651584;16;false;true;Cantonese;A 1920s villa plays host to this Cantonese restaurant boasting plenty of old-world charm thanks to its period furniture, fireplace and Chinese artwork. It’s spread over two floors and includes a bar, a lounge, a tea room and several private rooms. The menu is mostly Cantonese with some Shanghainese dishes. Try marinated meats, roast goose, salt-baked chicken or char siu pork. Seasonal offerings, like the mushroom menu in autumn, need pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8966;Wei Xiang Zhai (Yandang Road);China Mainland;Shanghai;14 Yandang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.225537;121.478169;89;true;false;Noodles;For over 80 years customers have been flocking here for its noodles. No one seems to mind the congested, somewhat tired room – just as long as the flavour in the bowl remains unchanged. The menu is set in two frames: noodles on one side, toppings on the other. Those in the know order a bowl of noodles dressed in sesame sauce, alongside spicy chopped pork topping and beef clear broth. Chilled noodles also hit the spot in summer.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
8969;Cuivre;China Mainland;Shanghai;1502 Middle Huaihai Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.231693;121.482589;89;false;false;French Contemporary;Echoing its name, this welcoming bistro in the French Concession amusingly features copper trimming on its walls and dinnerware. The kitchen excels in reinventing bistro classics with modern techniques and subtle Asian twists. L’agneau, or rack of lamb, is nicely charred on the outside and juicy on the inside. Round off with baba Zacapa. The wine list offers vintages from French small-batch wineries, alongside affordable new world choices.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8970;Coquille;China Mainland;Shanghai;29 Mengzi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.231408;121.492782;32;false;true;French;(The restaurant is temporarily closed for renovation.) Next to Italian trattoria Scarpetta, its younger sibling, Coquille, occupies two floors. On the seafood-focused menu, French classics come with subtle Asian twists. Signature dishes include foie gras crème brûlée and oven-roasted Dungeness crab. Finish off with coconut soufflé – golden and fluffy and with sea salt coconut ice cream on the side. Besides à la carte choices, there is a set menu for two. The beef Wellington needs to be pre-ordered.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
8971;Nan Xing Yuan;China Mainland;Shanghai;Building 12, 1728 Middle Huaihai Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.208399;121.436698;30;false;false;Sichuan;Helmed by a team of Sichuan chefs, this restaurant takes a deposit upon booking and serves only tailored menus, which diners pre-order. A typical menu builds a progression of flavours with classics such as napa cabbage in chicken consommé, and sautéed shredded pork with green chilli. Authentic dishes are meticulously prepared to showcase the 24 flavour profiles of Sichuanese cooking. Only private rooms are available, and reservations are a must.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8972;Scilla;China Mainland;Shanghai;504 Panyu Road, Changning, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2035665;121.4252611;61;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Scilla is a blue-flowered Mediterranean plant, a nod to the fact that this restaurant focuses on the region's food, but with a twist – local ingredients, especially seafood, are given the Mediterranean treatment, for a unique fusion cuisine. The signature BBQ Taizhou yellow croaker with bouillabaisse and rouille boasts crispy skin, rich broth and creamy sauce. The underground wine cellar carries some rare finds from the Mediterranean coast.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list;[]
8975;Xuji Seafood (Xuhui);China Mainland;Shanghai;500 Zhaojiabang Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.203142;121.4498512;93;true;true;Seafood;Since 1999, the Hunan brand has been expanding its footprint across the nation, and this multi-storey branch is its Shanghai flagship. Thanks to close ties with fishermen and farms, locally and globally, it secures sources for the best-quality and freshest seafood. Try the live scallops from the East China Sea blanched at your table in a boiling, milky sea perch stock. Xuji glass noodles in a casserole are the Hunan speciality you can't miss.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
8976;Scarpetta;China Mainland;Shanghai;33 Mengzi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.210344;121.47243;88;true;true;Italian;This two-storey restaurant takes its name from the act of using bread to mop up the last bit of sauce left on the plate. Homemade pizza and pasta, such as pizza vongole, and other specialities like Wagyu carpaccio topped with shaved black truffle slices, mean you’ll certainly not want to waste anything. The last facelift in 2018 left the dining room with a warm and romantic ambiance, making it an ideal choice for a date.;Air conditioning;[]
8977;Dining Room;China Mainland;Shanghai;87F, Park Hyatt, 100 Century Avenue, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.236692;121.503147;97;true;false;Jiangzhe;This high-ceilinged room with full-length windows affords panoramic river views, while the home-style furniture, warm lighting and booth seating make for a cosy feel. On the menu, Jiangzhe classics meet creative recipes that are rarely found elsewhere, such as steamed belt fish with fermented grains. Nicely pleated xiao long bao with umami-loaded soupy filling are simply unmissable – as are the appetisers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8978;La Scene Ronde;China Mainland;Shanghai;LG1-13, The Roof, Lane 458, Madang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2140673;121.470474;71;true;false;Innovative;As the name suggests, the open kitchen is dramatically lit, like a stage with front-row seats at the semi-circular counter. The single tasting menu changes every season, alongside options of wine, tea or non-alcoholic drink pairings. Well versed in classic French cuisine, the Japanese chef deftly uses local seasonal produce and seafood for unique French fare jazzed up by Asian touches. Try his deeply flavoured Wagyu beef stock, and Ibérico ham sushi.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8979;Frasca;China Mainland;Shanghai;1F, The Middle House Residences, 366 Shimen Yi Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.23024;121.46248;75;true;false;Italian;In northeast Italy, a frasca, identifiable by a branch hung over its doorway, was a gathering place for sharing farm-style food. In stark contrast, this stylish hotel restaurant boasts a modern vibe and a menu focused on authentic Italian home-style favourites. The handmade pasta stands out, especially the al dente ravioli. Try their Pinsa Romana and meats roasted on the Josper grill. The wine list has a nice selection of Italian vintages.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8982;1515 West Chophouse;China Mainland;Shanghai;4F, Jing An Shangri-La Hotel, 1218 Middle Yan'an Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.21749;121.466485;94;false;false;Steakhouse;They’ve certainly nailed the classic American look at this nicely styled chophouse. Start with a cocktail in the masculine, wood panelled bar before passing by the inviting bakery into the restaurant. All the favourite steakhouse dishes are here, from Caesar salad mixed at the table to steak tartare and cheesecake. However, it’s the grill that takes centre stage – the various cuts of dry-aged Australian beef are chargrilled to perfection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8984;Shanghai Club;China Mainland;Shanghai;L-418, 4F, North Building, HKRI Taikoo Hui, 789 West Nanjing Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.230546;121.458648;99;false;true;Jiangzhe, Cantonese;A premium brand from the Jardin de Jade Group, the restaurant serves old Shanghai classics with an emphasis on finesse and attention to detail. Walnut-crusted duck fillet square in bean paste is a rare gem that is painstaking to make. Live seafood is another highlight on the menu, while some Cantonese dim sum are served at lunch. Ask the servers about the seasonal offerings which truly embodying the essence of Shanghainese cooking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
8985;Charbon;China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 606, 6F, iapm, 999 Middle Huaihai Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.218122;121.454124;84;true;false;Barbecue;Celebrity chef Paul Pairet's latest venture in Shanghai is housed in a wood-rich space with brass finishes. Chargrilled kebabs are seasoned with Middle Eastern or Southeast Asian spices, and served with a dip made to complement the ingredients. Try frogs' legs with peanut satay sauce that marry springy texture and rich nutty depth. Pair this with Indonesian oxtail soup and citrus smoky rice. Finish off with ice cream in an array of flavours.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8986;De Xing Guan (Guangdong Road);China Mainland;Shanghai;471 Guangdong Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.108875;121.388847;46;true;true;Shanghainese;Founded in 1878, this two-storey noodle shop is something of a local landmark thanks to its gilded sign and elaborate façade. Chefs start work at 4am, making noodles and dim sum from scratch. The ground floor serves 20 different noodle and rice dishes, including the famous three-treasure soup noodles (fried eel, fried fish and pork hock). The dining room upstairs offers more comfort and a bigger Shanghainese menu, from soups to hot dishes and dim sum.;Air conditioning;[]
8987;Hai Wei Guan (Jingan);China Mainland;Shanghai;18 Kangding Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.238925;121.450397;71;true;false;Shanghainese;Behind the white façade of this two-storey building, new and old collide in a charming way. Embracing innovation while respecting tradition, the owner puts a new spin on Shanghainese classics with ingenious creativity. His signature crispy roast chicken with Périgord truffle that imitates Nakhi cooking needs to be pre-ordered. The sautéed conch with diced shrimp on a sizzling pot is wrapped in shiso leaves with crisp rice.;Air conditioning;[]
8988;Épices & Foie Gras;China Mainland;Shanghai;A1-05, 309 Hankou Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.218524;121.428527;45;false;false;French Contemporary;It’s no great surprise that foie gras is the speciality here. It comes in different preparations, so try the ‘Trilogy’ if you want to sample various types. This ‘modern French bistrot’ is run by a young French couple and they wisely also serve other classic Gallic dishes, like roasted lamb rack with crispy pistachio and a light garlic infused cream sauce. Lunch sets offer exceptional value. The main dining room is somewhat diminutive but it is pleasantly decorated.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
8989;Kanpai Classic (Huangpu);China Mainland;Shanghai;5F, Bund 5, 20 Guangdong Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.236464;121.48633;34;false;true;Barbecue;If anything demonstrates how international a restaurant is, it’s this: a Shanghai restaurant from a Taiwanese group, specialising in Australian Wagyu beef that also serves Japanese dishes. Premium Wagyu cuts, along with other meats and seafood, are grilled on charcoal stoves at each table. Caramelised and juicy, the thick-sliced skirt steak strikes a balance between toothsome texture and meaty flavour, with yuzu kosho to cut through the richness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8990;Lin Family of One - The Bund;China Mainland;Shanghai;4F, The Central, 123 East Nanjing Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.24016;121.48311;42;false;true;Taizhou;This upmarket dining concept nests in a shopping mall where century-old buildings are connected by a glass dome. The owner Mr Lin, a Taizhou native, has been cooking since the age of 19 and he ensures dishes are as authentic as they can be. Homestyle braised pomfret boasts a velvety texture and deep flavours, served with hand-made glutinous rice cake. Marinated tofu, and sweet potato noodles with sea anemone are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8991;Shanghai;China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, Central Hotel, 555 Jiujiang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.227133;121.451599;31;true;false;Shanghainese;Perched on the second floor of the Central Hotel is this sister restaurant to the famed hairy crab restaurant, Wang Bao He. You’ll find this speciality here in season but it’s equally known for its authentic Shanghainese cooking. Their classic dishes use quality ingredients and are prepared with care. One highlight is the house-manufactured yellow rice wine, which you can buy to take home with you, along with various other ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
8992;Beef & Liberty (Jingan);China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 111, Shanghai Centre, 1376 West Nanjing Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.236977;121.48599;69;false;true;American;For those times when only a burger will do, there is Beef & Liberty. New Zealand grass-fed beef is ground in-house twice a day, in time for lunch and dinner, and then served in homemade buns. The ribeye burger boasts a juicy, 220g patty cooked medium or medium-well, alongside caramelised onions, mustard mayo and cheese. Their super-rich milkshake, made with just ice cream and whipping cream, is also well worth a try.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
8995;Summer Palace;China Mainland;Shanghai;3F, Jing An Shangri-La Hotel, 1218 Middle Yan'an Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.227067;121.462455;74;false;false;Cantonese;This smart and sumptuously decorated Cantonese restaurant is divided into three distinct areas, each serving a different speciality. You'll find dim sum in the Pantry, claypot dishes in the Lantern and sophisticated Cantonese classics in the Imperial. Every facet of Cantonese cuisine is covered, alongside seasonal offerings such as hairy crabmeat and roe for a Shanghai twist. The private rooms are impressive, as is the wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
8997;Hong 0871;China Mainland;Shanghai;5F, Shanghai Chengtou Holding, 130 Wusong Road, Hongkou, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2485206;121.4858387;16;false;false;Yunnanese;In Chinese, ‘Hong’ means vast and deep, aptly describing the menu and the Yunnanese food culture that the owner from Kunming wants to popularise. Over 90% of the ingredients ship from Yunnan and the mushroom feast in summer is especially spectacular. Start with Nuodeng ham cured for 3 years alongside paper-thin dry cheese called rushan. Try also lard-layered buns, either steamed or deep-fried, with ‘winter melon’ pork and bean sauce filling.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
8998;Ding Te Le Zhou Mian Guan;China Mainland;Shanghai;No 22, Lane 494, Middle Huaihai Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2233192;121.4650451;82;false;true;Noodles and Congee;To the passer-by, this simple shop hidden in an alley on Huaihai Road looks pretty much like any other. What sets it apart, however, are the authentic noodles it serves. It is particularly famous for its shredded pork noodles with scallions, its yellow croaker noodles with pickled vegetables, and its deep-fried pork chops. You can also enjoy congee, rice and snacks – and it stays open 24 hours a day.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
8999;Royal China Club;China Mainland;Shanghai;3F, Bund 5, 20 Guangdong Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.226119;121.500145;88;true;true;Cantonese;Operated by London’s Royal China Group, this Cantonese restaurant specialises in dried seafood like abalone and fish, along with other assorted seafood dishes. The quality of the seafood is good, with some of the ingredients imported from the UK, such as lobsters from Scotland. Dim sum is popular at lunch and, during Chinese festivals, handmade products like glutinous rice dumplings and mooncakes are provided.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
9000;Mr & Mrs Bund;China Mainland;Shanghai;6F, Bund 18, 18 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.235692;121.48893;42;false;false;French Contemporary;On the city's dining scene for over 10 years, Chef Pairet's brasserie never ages. Lovely service, great music, a terrific wine list and bags of French joie de vivre make dining here a real experience. In the modern space – inside a former bank dating from 1922 – diners feast on chilled seafood platters, and charbroiled steaks and seafood. Original creations such as lemon & lemon tart with a sorbet-filled whole lemon also stand out.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9002;Numata Sou;China Mainland;Shanghai;1F, N1 Building, The Bund Finance Centre, 558 Zhongshan Dong Er Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2279908;121.49424;73;false;false;Tempura;The famed tempura institution in Osaka, Japan, opened its first overseas outpost in Shanghai. Chef Numata checks in every couple of months on Chef Sakata, his protégé for 15 years, who is in charge of the kitchen. Changing every month, the single omakase menu features 20 courses of seasonal seafood and vegetables, as well as three choices of starch – ten don, tempura chazuke and egg tempura with runny yolk on rice. Booking recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
9003;Stonesal;China Mainland;Shanghai;1M, 9 Donghu Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.218207;121.448988;64;true;false;Steakhouse;The owner-chef is a culinary veteran with 20 years of experience. He opened Stonesal in 2017 specialising in quality U.S. and Australian steaks house-aged in the Himalayan salt chamber next to the kitchen. Top picks include USDA prime T-bone from Creekstone Farm and M9+ Wagyu from Mayura Station Farm on the Limestone Coast in South Australia. On top of that, their spicy beef soup is simmered for hours to build layers of flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
9004;The Meat;China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, Kerry Hotel Pudong, 1388 Huamu Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.233915;121.49139;58;true;true;Steakhouse;The gloriously blunt name chosen by this hotel restaurant says it all. The beef – mostly Australian, is served in a characteristic steakhouse vibe, sporting antlers and booth seating. On your way in, you will see the room where the beef is aged for 25 to 31 days. The signature dish is New York pressed steak: Aussie Tajima Wagyu sirloin smothered in melted Raclette cheese, served with bourbon whisky sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9006;Hokkien Huay Kuan;China Mainland;Shanghai;5F, Xintiandi Style I, 177 Madang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2213869;121.4701098;59;true;false;Fujian;The interior is inspired by Fujian-style ink paintings, with water features dividing the room into zones. On the menu, premium produce from the province is deftly prepared by Fujian natives for the most authentic experience possible. Try the signature Shuizhu seafood trio – live prawns, razor clams and giant red squid are blanched in a mild mala broth over a bed of pickled broccoli stems, cucumber and bean sprouts for crunch and tartness.;;[]
9007;Bai Rong;China Mainland;Shanghai;1F, N2 Building, The Bund Finance Centre, 558 Zhongshan Dong Er Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2288003;121.4928612;87;true;false;Shandong;Bai Rong – peony – is the floral emblem of Shandong Province. Naturally, this modern restaurant generously adorned with lush greenery focuses on Shandong cuisine, especially live seafood shipped from Jiaodong Peninsula. Order the Jiaodong cold seafood platter to sample sea cucumber, jellyfish, abalone and octopus all at once. Rustic recipes from rural Shandong, such as sautéed Linyi chicken with fish maw, are hard to find elsewhere.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9008;Wan Yan (Changning);China Mainland;Shanghai;Inside Jin Jiang Cypress Hotel, Block 8, 2419 Hungqiao Road, Changning, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.190376;121.356258;60;false;false;Hui Cuisine;Brace yourself for nostalgia aplenty: velvet tufted chairs, walls covered in vintage blue bricks, art pieces from around the world…Most ingredients are shipped from Anhui, including mouldy tofu – a speciality you can’t miss. Wine-scented fermented mandarin fish is another classic slightly adapted to suit the local palate. The Anhui-style braised pork trotter in soybean paste is cooked in a 30-year-old marinade for exceptional depth and layered flavours. On top of the à la carte menu, you can also have one tailored in advanced.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9009;Hong Yu Fang;China Mainland;Shanghai;B1-06, Mix 6, 686 South Xizang Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2190344;121.4789741;23;false;false;Dim Sum;A household name in Huangpu district, this place has been around for 10-plus years. Regulars keep flocking to its new shop since it moved into a shopping mall. Open in the morning only, it always attracts a queue of customers coming for a hearty meal. With their juicy, generous pork filling, Shanghai classic potstickers are a must-try. Cabbage rice with sausage and salted pork is another hit, each grain of rice enrobed in creamy lard.;Cash only;[]
9010;Min He Nan Huan Xi;China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, MIXC East Alley, 111 North Shanxi Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2444595;121.4745732;39;true;true;Fujian;The F&B group has been active in Fujian Province for over 30 years and its Shanghai outpost sports a classy décor. The menu features a line-up of lavish recipes, but even simple dishes like radish rice can be a highlight – long-grain rice is cooked with dried seafood, pork meat and bones for impressive sweetness and depth. Another iconic dish is layered chitterlings that delivers a gutsy mix of texture and flavour. The tea menu is worth exploring.;Car park;[]
9011;Les Nuages;China Mainland;Shanghai;57F, East Tower, Raffles City The Bund, 999 Dongdaming Road, Hongkou, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2548014;121.5039397;61;false;false;Innovative;Sitting atop a skyscraper, this aptly named restaurant boasts high ceiling and commands breathtaking river views. Open for afternoon tea and dinner only, it serves Western classics like beef steaks dry-aged in-house. But it’s the chef’s menu melding Chinese ingredients with European techniques that truly surprises. Try deep-fried seaweed meatballs with runny crab roe and vinegar centres, and Chocolate Trio styled after Shanghainese retro snacks.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
9012;Mercato;China Mainland;Shanghai;6F, Bund 3, 3 Zhongshan Dong Yi Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.215907;121.458294;34;true;true;Italian;From Jean-Georges Vongerichten comes this lively Italian restaurant with Mediterranean twists. The interior sees an eclectic mix of natural materials matched with urban savviness. On the menu, family-style dishes come in sizes large enough for sharing. Signatures such as wood oven-roasted whole Icelandic halibut, and porcini-crusted salmon with warm leek vinaigrette and herbs, are well worth trying. Also ask about the chef’s specials.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9013;Hang Yuen Hin;China Mainland;Shanghai;Xujiahui Park, 290 Wanping Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.199204;121.439814;74;true;false;Cantonese;The restaurant opened in the lungs of the city and the lush greenery outside the windows works magic with the décor to make a relaxing ambiance. The chef has worked in both Guangzhou and Hong Kong, putting his know-how to good use in the authentic Cantonese dishes that are also low in salt and oil. Signature dishes include almond-crusted fried shrimp rolls, and crispy pigeon. Dim sum with family and friends is also a delight here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9014;Shi Chuan Fei Chuan (Xuhui);China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop 603, 6F, iapm, 999 Middle Huaihai Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.218122;121.454124;100;true;false;Sichuan;The kitchen reimagines Sichuan cooking using top-notch produce from around the world, finessed by exquisite plating. Duck and pork tripe soup with pickled radish delivers unsurpassed umami alongside tang and tartness. Fluffy hand-made pork buns burst with the addictive aromas of spiced chilli oil. Cool down your palate with house-made bingfen: transparent jelly noodles made from shoofly seeds in brown sugar syrup. Booking recommended.;Interesting wine list;[]
9015;Dong Ping Chao;China Mainland;Shanghai;1 Dongping Road, Xuhui, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2103732;121.4463024;19;false;false;Chao Zhou;This restaurant in a century-old heritage building reinterprets Chaozhou fare with refined touches and local twists. Quality ingredients, especially seafood, are shipped from Chaoshan region twice a day to ensure freshness. Menus are tailor-made at least one day ahead. The speciality crispy-skin braised sea cucumber provides a nice contrast of texture, with a subtle hint of peanut butter in the abalone sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
9016;Yong Xing;China Mainland;Shanghai;No. 1, Lane 626, Middle Fuxing Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.204543;121.435415;39;false;false;Shanghainese;This cozy little gem is hidden in a tiny alley and its non-descript façade makes it even harder to find. An archway, fireplace and red-brick wallpaper - reminiscent of someone’s home from a by-gone era - set the tone for the warm welcoming service. Yong Xing serves delicious home-style Chinese food at wallet-friendly prices and is hugely popular among locals. Try steamed perch with shredded ginger in Jiangdong style.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
9017;Tea Culture (East Beijing Road);China Mainland;Shanghai;L201A, 2F, Yi Feng Galleria, 99 East Beijing Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.242453;121.4839574;24;false;false;Huaiyang;You can tell from the name that this restaurant is serious about the national beverage – professional tea masters brew the perfect cup, using top quality loose leaves and natural spring water. As for the food, the Guangdong chef displays his skills in a predominantly Huaiyang-inspired menu with some Jiangzhe and Cantonese dishes. The classic Buddha Jumps over the Wall is reworked with head of silver carp from Qiandao Lake (two portion sizes available).;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9018;Canton Disco;China Mainland;Shanghai;2F, The Shanghai Edition, 199 East Nanjing Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.239551;121.481313;95;false;true;Cantonese;A fully-fledged homage to Hong Kong’s discotheque era, neon signs included, may not be to everyone’s taste, but Canton Disco somehow manages to pull it off with sophistication and little cheese factor. In addition to Cantonese menu staples such as dim sum, double-boiled soups, and sweet and sour pork, the experienced chef also puts on his creative hat for some novel items. The various set menus are great for larger parties.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
9019;Nuits;China Mainland;Shanghai;68 Tongren Road, Jingan, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2252095;121.4468001;69;true;true;French Contemporary;The bistro may not have a big shopfront, but its bright orange sign and full-height windows more than compensate in terms of impact. Named after Côte de Nuits in Burgundy, it serves a nice selection from that wine region. Head to the cellar to talk to the sommelier. The menu is mostly classic French and the signature beef tartare is laced with lightly cooked geoduck and oyster liquor, reflecting the bounty of sea and land.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9020;Chaimen Hui;China Mainland;Shanghai;Shop S-L4-04, Stone Zone, Taikoo Li Qiantan, Lane 500, Dongyu Road, Pudong, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.1543302;121.4766074;61;false;false;Sichuan;This outpost of its famed namesake in Chengdu operates in a sleekly furnished space – the centrepiece is no doubt the oversized starburst sculpture over the circular counter. The kitchen is run by a team from the parent restaurant, and their Sichuan menu showcases creative fare and the best produce from around the world. Try the wild-caught yellow croaker braised with pickled chillies, and preserved spare ribs and sausage with Sichuan peppercorns.;Air conditioning;[]
9021;Shaughnessy;China Mainland;Shanghai;No.2201-2202, 22F, East Huaihai International Mansion, 45-49 East Huaihai Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.2281795;121.4778647;68;false;false;Steakhouse;Sitting atop a skyscraper, this American-style steakhouse commands vistas of the Bund and the Huangpu skyline. The menu stars premium cuts of suitably marbled Black Angus beef, all dry-aged in-house for 28 to 180 days. The steaks are artfully carved tableside and served with pan jus. If you’re not a red meat fan, you could opt for the aged squab which is something of a rarity. For more privacy, consider booking your own room.;;[]
9023;Yong Feng Mian Guan;China Mainland;Shanghai;320 Hankou Road, Huangpu, Shanghai, China Mainland;31.23806;121.4817;41;false;false;Noodles;Now run by the second generation, this family-run halal noodle shop has been around since 1962. Forced to close due to urban renewal, many regretted the demise of the original venue. Recently re-opened in a new spot, the original kitchen team proudly delivers its distinctive culinary score. The signature red-braised lamb noodles are served in curry beef stock or tossed in scallion oil. Either way, order an over-easy egg so the yolk spills over the noodles.;Cash only;[]
9024;Frangipaani;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;The Republik, Lot No.M.03, Mezzanine Floor, Jalan Medan Setia 1, Bukit Damansara, Kuala Lumpur, 50490, Malaysia;3.148946;101.651991;78;true;false;Indian;The softly lit interior, outfitted in warm wood and tan leather, sets a rustic mood, while the terrace is relaxing and cosy. Since 2019, the kitchen team has been delivering tasty traditional cuisine, tweaked to suit local tastebuds. Go for the vegetarian samosa chaat and the tandoori specialities. The raan dum biriyani, or whole lamb leg cooked in basmati rice, is great for sharing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
9025;Jwala;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;E-02-01, Block E, The Five@KPD, 49 Jalan Dungun, Bukit Damansara, Kuala Lumpur, 50490, Malaysia;3.1508826;101.6644017;54;true;true;Indian;Named after the Sanskrit word for fire, Jwala is famous for chargrilled dishes cooked in its custom-built tandoori oven. Familiar ingredients like chicken and lamb chop are presented alongside less common offerings such as croissant, cottage cheese and hamachi collar. Tandoori tiger prawns marinated in mustard oil, yoghurt and spices, in particular, boast deep, rich flavours. The knockout curries are seasoned with local fruits and herbs.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9027;Blanc;Malaysia;George Town;Macalister Mansion, 228 Jalan Macalister, George Town, 10400, Malaysia;5.419219;100.318843;87;true;false;European Contemporary;This fine dining restaurant in an 18C castle-turned heritage boutique hotel boasts graceful architecture and a stunning dining room done up in a colonial style with royal blue walls, white window shutters and a giant faux white tree in the centre. The 8-course tasting menu cannot be faulted and á la carte options are also plentiful. Each dish is intelligently devised and balanced. Make sure you save room for the desserts that are too good to miss!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9028;Kayra;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;F-8, 1F, Bangsar Village 1, Jalan Telawi 1, Bangsar, Kuala Lumpur, 59100, Malaysia;3.1297977;101.6709123;81;true;false;Indian;As the culinary heart of southwest India, and productive capital of peppers and spices since ancient times, Kerala has had a profound influence on the dishes here. Kayra builds on Kerala’s venerable traditions, serving contemporary recipes with a rich mix of spices – central to the cuisine's identity – and modern aesthetics. Beef features prominently here. Prices are reasonable and the industrial interior with brick design gives a modern and simple impression.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9029;Kebaya Dining Room;Malaysia;George Town;14A Lorang Stewart, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4191324;100.3380258;34;true;false;Peranakan;The restored heritage building is home to a lavish restaurant with a high-ceilinged room, crystal chandeliers and scarlet velvet drapes. The concise menu showcases a good selection of Peranakan cooking alongside some vegetarian offerings. Meat lovers may try tamarind glazed grass-fed beef from down under, or the prawn geng curry that can be made vegetarian. Round it out with Markisa semifreddo. Also check out the competitively priced wine list.;;[]
9030;Nyonya Willow;Malaysia;George Town;72-1-3 Arena Curve, Jalan Mahsuri, Bandar Sunway Tunas, Bayan Lepas, George Town, 11900, Malaysia;5.3262422;100.2801459;85;true;true;Peranakan;For an authentic slice of Penang culinary life, come to this shop tucked away in a residential neighbourhood frequented mostly by locals. The room decorated with vintage Nyonya photos and motifs heralds a feast of northern Peranakan specialities. The signature gulai tumis (tamarind fish curry) is a sour and spicy recipe passed down by the owner's mother. Their assam prawn is known for its sour-sweetness. Save room for the heart-warming desserts.;Air conditioning;[]
9031;Potager;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;P11, Bamboo Hills, off DUKE, Taman Bamboo, Segambut, Kuala Lumpur, 51200, Malaysia;3.1938146;101.6748433;36;false;true;French Contemporary;A Fukuoka native, the chef worked in Europe for years before opening this place – an oasis set in lush greenery outside the city centre. At dinner, the tasting menus include five or nine courses, meticulously crafted with classic French techniques and using local ingredients. With an array of harmonious textures, the corn dish is inspired by the chef's visit to Cameron Highlands, encapsulating his culinary vision and childhood memories.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9032;Flour;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;12 & 14 Jalan Kamuning, off Jalan Imbi, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1457116;101.7169078;48;false;true;Indian, Contemporary;The spacious, monochromatic dining room commands views of the kitchen via a glass wall. With the prix-fixe menus that change from time to time, the chef reinvents Indian cooking with modern twist, quality ingredients from around the world, and the deepest respect for Mother Earth. He seasons the food sparingly to let its natural flavours sing, and often visits each table to explain his dishes throughout the meal.;Car park,Valet parking;[]
9033;Jaloux;Malaysia;George Town;24 Lebuh King, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4187377;100.3402941;50;false;false;Italian;The concrete building hidden by lush greenery is easy to miss, but Chef Hong’s first-class slow food and artisan hand-made pasta are worth the hunt. Pappardelle with oxtail ragu boasts al dente noodles, balanced between richness and acidity, and generous dollops of fork-tender, melty oxtail ragu. The service can be slow, so just sit back and enjoy the music and wine between your orders. It doesn’t take reservations, so come early to beat the crowd.;Air conditioning;[]
9034;Richard Rivalee;Malaysia;George Town;62 & 64 Lorong Macalister, George Town, 10400, Malaysia;5.416138;100.328399;65;false;true;Peranakan;Fashion designer Richard Rivalee shares his passion for Nyonya culture and Peranakan food in this smart vintage joint, whose knickknacks and heritage premises are a nod to the Baba-Nyonya culture. Deceptively simple, homespun dishes are finessed with spot-on seasoning and loads of punch. Otak-otak, or savoury fish egg custard, combines a velvety texture with just the right amount of heat. To reduce food waste, most items are available in two portion sizes.;Air conditioning;[]
9036;Bee See Heong;Malaysia;Seberang Perai;4166 Jalan Kampung Benggali, Butterworth, Seberang Perai, 12200, Malaysia;5.408959;100.3714999;59;false;false;Malaysian;Since 1966, this simple shop has been welcoming hungry guests who fancy home-style Malaysian food. Every dish is made à la minute and you can hear the wok sizzling after you place your order. Specialties include prawn curry – nice and thick, it has a good kick that goes well with the prawns. The fried threadfin with a sweet black sauce is not to be missed! The crispy fish fillet in sticky caramel soy sauce stands out, too. Arrive early to beat the crowd.;Car park,Cash only;[]
9037;Malai;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;M1 Floor, Menara Ample West, 6 Jalan Puncak, Kuala Lumpur, 50250, Malaysia;3.1520314;101.7062926;15;true;false;Thai;Every detail, from the imported tableware to the authentic Thai dining experience, has been pondered and puzzled over. Malai relocated to this venue at the end of 2022 to offer greater comfort and more spacious dining on two floors. It’s regularly packed with office workers, especially at lunchtime. The mostly Thai team of chefs conjures up a traditional Thai menu with modern twists. Don’t miss the tom yum soup or the gaeng keaw waan (green curry).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9038;Firewood;Malaysia;George Town;15 Jalan Masjid Kapitan Keling, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.418981;100.3393059;46;true;true;Barbecue;The historic building with a lofty ceiling is furnished in faux industrial style, providing the perfect foil for the central open fire grill. Ask for counter seats to make the most of the smoky vibe and high flames. Both set and á la carte menus are available. Start with hay smoked seasonal mushrooms, followed by tiger prawn in sweet, tangy Nyonya sauce. Beef lovers cannot fail but find their favourite cuts here – consider pre-ordering the dry-aged steaks in advance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
9039;Ceki;Malaysia;George Town;11-A Jalan Sri Bahari, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.4211065;100.3322279;27;true;true;Peranakan;Ceki is decorated in a traditional vibe with antique clothing and knick-knacks that tell a story from the past. The extensive menu is chiefly composed of home-cooked style Peranakan cuisine and features interesting dishes that can be hard to find, such as too kwa kean. The high-quality seafood menu features signature dishes such as assam pedas fish and sambal goreng prawns paired with a knockout herbal sauce. With only a few large tables, booking is advisable.;;[]
9040;Tenmasa;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Unit 3.3 (annexe), 2F, Tower 1, Platinum Park, 11 Persiaran KLCC, Kuala Lumpur, 50088, Malaysia;3.1555176;101.7188475;59;false;true;Tempura;Watch the chefs weave their culinary magic from the 10-seater counter, but book in advance. The omakase menus showcase classic signature dishes and seasonal specials made with fresh local produce and high-quality Japanese imports. The seafood and vegetable tempura are lightly battered and deep fried for a light crisp coating. The signature uni with shiso leaf comprises fresh, sweet uni from Hokkaido, served on a tempura shiso leaf.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
9041;Ali Nasi Lemak Daun Pisang;Malaysia;George Town;Sri Weld Food Court, 19 Lebuh Pantai, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4178122;100.3428291;44;false;false;Street Food;This halal stall only sells nasi lemak: the national dish of coconut milk rice wrapped in banana leaf, topped with sambal and one of the six toppings. Try anchovies with a hard-boiled egg. And go easy on the fiery sambal.;Cash only;[]
9042;Fook Cheow Cafe;Malaysia;George Town;122I Jalan Hutton, George Town, 10050, Malaysia;5.4214497;100.3284924;57;false;false;Noodles;Located on a street corner, the signage is inconspicuous, but its popularity with locals mean that it can’t be missed. This simple eatery has been open for some 30 years, but only in the mornings, which makes it just the ticket to sample the local breakfast. The signature dish, koay teow th'ng, is rice noodle soup with fish balls, deep-fried garlic, shredded chicken and lettuce. The tasty soup broth is made from hen and pork bones.;Cash only;[]
9043;Flower Mulan;Malaysia;George Town;266 & 268 Jalan Burma, George Town, 10350, Malaysia;5.4312684;100.3122743;54;true;true;Peranakan;The café sits atop the florist of the same name and serves a small menu of Paranakan food. Sambal tumis ikan pari, or sambal fish curry, is rich and aromatic, whereas assam prawn strikes the perfect balance between sweet and sour. Dimly-lit rooms are decorated in maximalist style with a Chinese theme – red lanterns, flowers, art, sculptures and patterns cover every surface. Intimate service from the friendly owner makes diners feel right at home.;Air conditioning;[]
9044;Skillet;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot 1-01, 1F, Menara Hap Seng 3, Jalan P. Ramlee, Kuala Lumpur, Kuala Lumpur, 50250, Malaysia;3.15302;101.70751;43;false;true;European Contemporary;Relocated to a new address, Skillet now sports a wine cellar and a lounge for drinks before or after your meal. The tasteful venue is adorned in striking dried flower arrangements depicting the seasons, just like the season-driven menu which showcases exquisite dishes underpinned by solid European techniques and sometimes stars local ingredients. Try dried longan bread and ramson-flavoured angel hair pasta. The set lunch menu is a bargain.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
9045;The Brasserie;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;2F, The St. Regis, 6 Jalan Stesen Sentral 2, Kuala Lumpur Sentral, Kuala Lumpur, 50470, Malaysia;3.1370138;101.6888572;23;false;true;French Contemporary;The chef draws from experience working with some of the biggest names in London and in fine dining restaurants across Europe and Asia to create a French contemporary menu with Mediterranean influences and a touch of Asian. They serve a five to seven-course tasting menu, à la carte and plenty of vegetarian options. The beverage list is outstanding, with a good selection of wine and spirits to be paired with the food. The Sunday brunch offers a huge range of fresh seafood.;Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9046;The Pinn;Malaysia;George Town;58 Pengkalan Weld, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4121664;100.3376993;93;false;true;Small eats;The Pinn moved to this spot opposite Lee Jetty in 2023. Like the room, the menu is small but powerful, offering Malaysian-Chinese dishes, dumplings and even some Taiwanese and Indonesian titbits. Homemade mackerel fish balls are their speciality and you can order noodles on top to make it a complete meal. The food tends to be slightly on the sweet side to suit local tastebuds.;Air conditioning;[]
9047;Soleil;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot-13A & 15, 2F, Damansara City Mall, 6 Jalan Damanlela, Bukit Damansara, Kuala Lumpur, 50490, Malaysia;3.1464153;101.6615705;93;true;true;European Contemporary;The European-trained chef has no hesitation in mixing trans-continental influences. His thoughtful use of Asian ingredients delivers a good variety of contemporary European cuisine with local characteristics. Dishes like the Hokkaido scallops with tagliatelle and cod roe butter are good examples of the chef’s deft harmonisation of East and West. From classic dishes to modern cuisine, there’s something for everyone. Take your pick from a broad selection of wines.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9048;Passage Thru India;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;4 Jalan Delima, off Jalan Bukit Bintang, Imbi, Kuala Lumpur, 50400, Malaysia;3.1467502;101.7211091;97;false;true;Indian;Established in 1993, Passage Thru India catches the eye with its artistic interior as much as its cooking. The owner-artist painted the murals on the walls and ceilings to create a technicoloured yet intimate cottage feel. The sizeable menu offers a good variety of traditional Indian favourites, including tandoori, naan and roti from the coal-fired oven. The aromatic biriyani rice puts you right at home and goes well with any of the tapas-sized plates.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9049;Yun House;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;5B, Four Seasons Hotel, 145 Jalan Ampang, Kuala Lumpur, Kuala Lumpur, 50450, Malaysia;3.15944;101.71492;61;false;true;Cantonese;Set under high ceilings, this remarkable dining room with nice views is a great choice for both casual and formal gatherings. A specialist in Cantonese cuisine, the chef has lived in Southeast Asia for many years. His concise menu is pork free with a quality selection of seafood and dim sum. Don’t miss the daily Inspirational Soup or fresh prawns simmered with glass noodles. Wrap up your meal with a crispy red bean pancake. The signature duck must be ordered in advance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9050;Sushi Taka;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;3A, The St. Regis, 6 Jalan Stesen Sentral 2, Kuala Lumpur Sentral, Kuala Lumpur, 50470, Malaysia;3.1368915;101.6886877;100;false;true;Sushi;Since 2016, this upmarket sushi-ya in a prestigious hotel has been prized for their authentic sushi made with the freshest and most seasonal fish flown in from Japan. The Japanese chef is specific about every detail, including the sushi rice from a town in Niigata. To experience his culinary vision in full glory, opt for the omakase menu with 10 nigiri sushi, appetisers and sashimi. Oenophiles should check out the well-curated sake list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
9051;Jit Seng Hong Kong Roasted Duck Rice;Malaysia;George Town;246 Lebuh Carnarvon, George Town, 10450, Malaysia;5.4146356;100.3336249;88;false;true;Street Food;The chef-owner started his own business after years as a chef in a larger restaurant. Open for three hours a day, the shop is famous for his roasted duck with deep-red skin and juicy meat, for which customers are prepared to queue. The roasted pork belly and char siew are tasty extras.;Cash only;[]
9052;Air Itam Duck Rice;Malaysia;George Town;Air Itam Wet Market, Jalan Pasar, George Town, 11500, Malaysia;5.4014798;100.2781148;53;false;false;Street Food;There are many shops in Penang selling roasted duck, but this stall's tender braised duck is packed with flavour, including soy sauce, anise and cinnamon. They also serve braised pork belly, pork intestines, egg and bean curd.;Cash only;[]
9053;Sambal;Malaysia;George Town;300 Lebuh Pantai, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4140594;100.3377767;85;false;true;Asian Contemporary;Located on a buzzy, vibrant street, Sambal serves a tantalising mix of Asian and European flavours. There’s a unique twist to the beloved Lap Mei Fun, with fragrant rice, Chinese sausage, char siew (honey BBQ pork) and crispy pork lard. The Udang Entangled claypot boasts a rich, creamy broth infused with Chinese wine, served with glass noodles and succulent prawns. The standout dessert is taro purée, a modern adaption of creamy Teochew yam.;Air conditioning;[]
9054;Wagyu Kappo Yoshida;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Unit 3-48, 48F, Naza Tower, Platinum Park, 10 Persiaran KLCC, Kuala Lumpur, 50088, Malaysia;3.1546359;101.7186231;51;false;true;Japanese;Based on Kappo cuisine, chef Yoshida's philosophy aims to establish a bond between the diner and the chef. Veteran chef Hattori dons the role of culinary host by tailoring this omakase beef experience at the counter for 12 guests in an intimate setting. This satisfying feast for beef lovers uses different parts of premium Wagyu from Japan in each dish. The chef also makes his own soba, onsen tamago and truffle ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view;[]
9055;Bali Hai Seafood Market;Malaysia;George Town;90 Persiaran Gurney, George Town, 10250, Malaysia;5.4339043;100.3151291;87;true;true;Seafood;Bali Hai has been feeding seafood lovers with the freshest critters and best quality fish for over ten years. Pick your own catch at the live fish tank by the entrance. Specify the way you want them cooked – in Teochew, Nyonya or even Thai style. The must-try “cereal prawns” are tossed in butter and milky oat powder that forms a crispy crust. Stir-fried crab with salted egg yolks that strikes a balance between umami and saltiness is not to be missed.;Air conditioning;[]
9056;Tok Tok Mee Bamboo Noodle;Malaysia;George Town;37 Lebuh Campbell, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.4171937;100.3351542;64;true;false;Noodles;“Tok Tok” is an onomatopoeia of the sound made by a chef when kneading noodle dough with a bamboo pole, a tradition still practised at the entrance of this shop. Cantonese wonton noodle soup is a must-try for its bouncy noodles and flavoursome shrimp filling. Blanched noodles tossed with dried shrimp roe, and Cantonese barbecue meats are also popular. Also try their Chinese pastry – both BBQ pork pie and pandan kaya dumplings are terrific.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
9057;Cilantro;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;MiCasa All Suite Hotel, 368B Jalan Tun Razak, Taman U Thant, Kuala Lumpur, 50400, Malaysia;3.1570082;101.7231886;91;true;false;French Contemporary;Cilantro has stood the test of time as one of the city's favourite formal dining spots for decades. The Japanese chef's dexterous preparation of first-rate ingredients from his home country is underpinned by classic French techniques. At dinner, he serves a three- or four-course set menu with a choice of cold or warm appetisers, main and dessert. Alternatively, you can order à la carte. Try his famous capellini course or Japanese Wagyu.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9058;Fatty Loh Chicken Rice;Malaysia;George Town;21 Jalan Fettes, Tanjung Bungah, George Town, 11200, Malaysia;5.4527042;100.3026347;71;true;true;Street Food;Into the third generation, this shop famous for Hainanese chicken rice also serves other Southeast Asian favourites. Chicken that boasts springy skin and velvety flesh can be ordered in halves or standard portions.;Cash only;[]
9059;Atelier Binchotan;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;5 Jalan 1/109e, Taman Desa Business Park, Kuala Lumpur, 58100, Malaysia;3.0975776;101.6773174;75;true;true;Barbecue;The owner couple opened this culinary hotspot in 2020, serving meat, seafood and vegetables cooked over a binchotan grill. There are just 17 seats around the open kitchen, so all diners can watch the magic unfold. The short menu changes often, but signatures such as kaya toast stay on – the crispy grilled brioche is topped with kaya jam and shaved foie gras terrine. With oily pink flesh and lightly charred edges, the shima-aji is another must-try.;Air conditioning;[]
9061;Feringgi Grill;Malaysia;George Town;Mezzanine Level, Rasa Wing Lobby, Shangri-La's Rasa Sayang Resort and Spa, Batu Feringgi Beach, George Town, 11100, Malaysia;5.4806245;100.2557398;31;true;false;European Contemporary;Sweeping ocean views are nicely framed by brick-red curtains, walls and upholstery. Since 1973, Feringgi Grill has attracted a discerning following and the room retains its old-world romantic charm. On the menu, seafood and Aussie Wagyu beef are popular choices, and nothing starts a meal more theatrically than the tomato soup – prepared tableside and, flambéed with a splash of gin for extra fragrance. The private room seats 20, making it perfect for banquets.;Air conditioning;[]
9062;La Suisse;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;17, Lorong Rahim Kajai 13, Taman Tun Dr Ismail, Kuala Lumpur, 60000, Malaysia;3.1544687;101.6225843;45;false;true;European;Since their opening in 1992, husband-and-wife team Chef Mike Yap and Claudia have maintained alpine levels of excellence. Through their unwavering passion and hard work, they’ve created a restaurant with modern charms and old-fashioned styles that exudes genuine warmth – it’s like being invited into a family home for a meal. The heartwarming menu includes cheesy favourites like raclette and malakow, classic beef dishes and a veal that evokes waves of nostalgia.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle;[]
9063;Vantador;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;38 Jalan 25/70A, Desa Sri Hartamas, Kuala Lumpur, 50480, Malaysia;3.162376;101.6496666;79;true;false;Steakhouse;Vantador’s vintage yet modern interiors are drenched in soft lighting. Aussie and Spanish beef is either dry-aged for up to 30 days in unsalted butter, or vacuum-sealed and wet-aged in its own juices for 14 days. Steaks are precisely grilled over charcoal and wood to desired doneness, striking a fine balance between smoky and full-bodied, meaty flavours. Non-steak dishes are also available, together with meticulously prepared desserts.;Air conditioning;[]
9064;Sushi Ori;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Unit PG-01, GF, Podium Block, Menara Keck Seng, 203 Jalan Bukit Bintang, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.14523;101.70914;79;true;true;Sushi;Tucked away from the main street, Sushi Ori is famous locally for its sushi sets and omakase. The eponymous Japanese chef has lived in Malaysia for over 10 years and opened this traditional restaurant in 2019. Seasonal ingredients are delivered from Japan three times a week. The sushi rice comes from Akita and contains a secret mix of vinegar. With only limited seats at the counter, book well in advance for the personalised omakase experience. Private rooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9066;Li Yen;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;2F, The Ritz-Carlton, 168 Jalan Imbi, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1469006;101.7154141;73;false;false;Cantonese;Embroidered wall panelling, a semi-circular velvet banquette, and mirrors in bronze frames prime diners for a luxury dining experience. On the menu, classic Cantonese takes centre stage – think dim sum, honey-glazed BBQ Iberico pork, and roast goose. Also check out the chef’s recommendations on the first page, often featuring one hero ingredient prepared in a myriad of ways. Most items are available in different portion sizes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9067;Christoph's;Malaysia;George Town;55, Lorong Stewart, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.419123;100.337777;60;false;true;Austrian;The Austrian owner opened this restaurant in 2022 to serve hearty family favourites from his homeland like Wiener schnitzel, a traditional deep-fried breaded pork chop with a crispy crust and juicy meat. A veal cutlet may also be available on request. Salzburger nockerl, a sweet fluffy soufflé with house-made lingonberry sauce on the side, is simply unmissable. Also a wine importer, the owner has curated a splendid selection of Austrian tipples.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9068;Curios-City;Malaysia;George Town;164A-B Lebuh Victoria, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.41337;100.33858;47;true;false;Innovative;You need to look hard to find this place – there is no sign and the exterior looks barren. The stunning, moody interior is furnished in wabi-sabi style with lots of greenery, giving it a cosy and stylish ambience. The chef creates dishes underpinned by European techniques and punctuated by Malaysian twists. He offers three set menus that change every two months. Try the seven-course set to experience his vision in full glory.;Air conditioning;[]
9069;Shanghai Restaurant;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;1F, JW Marriott, 183 Jalan Bukit Bintang, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1478307;101.7137774;66;false;true;Shanghainese;In business since 1999, the restaurant was updated in 2021 and now sports a bright, modern interior. The veteran chef traditionally crafts Shanghainese classics, and his xiao long bao is a must-try – soupy pork filling enrobed in paper-thin, meticulously pleated skin. Stir-fried flat glass noodles with shredded pork and preserved vegetable boasts remarkable wok hei, and the salted potherb mustard greens impart briny umami.;Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9070;Sushi Masa;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot 1-03, 1F, Menara Hap Seng 3, Jalan P. Ramlee, Kuala Lumpur, Kuala Lumpur, 50250, Malaysia;3.15481;101.70874;22;true;false;Sushi;Following the success of his Edomae-style sushi restaurant in Tokyo, acclaimed chef Masakazu Ishibashi brings his expertise to KL. His unique approach to sushi, founded on a 200-year-old tradition, is presented as a beautiful multi-course meal prepared by his apprentice, Chef Yoshi. The omakase menus showcase creative twists on traditional dishes. The nigiri is made with high quality produce sourced straight from Japan, while the Botan Ebi with egg yolk sauce and caviar is packed with umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
9072;Bōl;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;15 Jalan Sin Chew Kee, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 50150, Malaysia;3.143192;101.7049335;84;false;true;Asian Contemporary;Having cooked together since they were young, Singaporean chef-owner and hotel designer, Kian Liew, and partner, Patrick, opened their brainchild in 2022 and have already earned the support of many regulars. Only set menus are available, including one that is entirely seasonal and one for vegans. The focus is on Nyonya style cuisine with Singaporean and Malaysian twists, using a healthy mix of herbs and spices to create a succulent range of flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
9073;Marini's on 57;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;57F, Menara 3 Petronas, Persiaran KLCC, Kuala Lumpur City Centre, Kuala Lumpur, 50088, Malaysia;3.1567422;101.7115501;70;false;true;Italian;At this iconic rooftop venue, diners enjoy superb sunsets and panoramic cityscapes through floor to ceiling windows. Besides the à la carte menu, there are several tasting menus that offer a knockout selection of Italian dishes, featuring innovative elements, choice cuts of imported beef and artisan pasta. The intriguing tiramisu, which comes in a tin of caviar, is made with coffee caviar (rather than fish eggs!).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9074;Tanglin (Bukit Damansara);Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;57G, Jalan Medan Setia 1, Bukit Damansara, Kuala Lumpur, 50490, Malaysia;3.1503107;101.6533012;86;true;false;Malaysian;Founded in 1948, the family-owned Tanglin is now run by the second generation and the two-storey establishment is well known for its nasi lemak. This delicious family recipe is paired with either sotong (squid), daging (meat) or ayam goreng (fried chicken). Its fragrant rice has the right mix of coconut milk and its sambal tumis, the right level of spiciness. Whether dining in or taking away, the queues are long. Generous portions and prices that make sense.;Car park,Cash only;[]
9075;Hide;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Concourse, Ritz-Carlton Residences, 105 Jalan Ampang, Kuala Lumpur, Kuala Lumpur, 50450, Malaysia;3.1566062;101.7057561;89;true;true;Innovative;The entrance to Hide is tucked away in a secluded corner among some paintings. The interior has a trendy feel, with its U-shaped marble counter overlooking the open kitchen. The young head chef once worked in the US, and his season-driven tasting menu embodies the multicultural influences in Malaysian cuisine. Local produce and seafood are prominently used in dishes such as lobster mapo with Sichuan pepper oil, and puff pastry with kaya mousse.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
9076;Nadodi;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Level 7A, Four Seasons Hotel, 145 Jalan Ampang, Kuala Lumpur, Kuala Lumpur, 50450, Malaysia;3.157879;101.713655;46;false;true;Innovative;Check out the spice table at the entrance for a preview of what's to come. Cosy and private, booth seats by the window command sweeping city views. Start with one of the magical concoctions mixed by the mixologists, followed by creative "nomadic" cuisine based on Southern Indian and Sri Lankan fare. The dinner set menu with 10-plus courses features different taste profiles and traditional snacks, best enjoyed with the alcoholic drink pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
9077;Gēn;Malaysia;George Town;Unit 6, 8 Gat Lebuh Gereja, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4160886;100.343212;23;false;false;Innovative;Gēn is Chinese for root. The owner-chef revisits his culinary roots and childhood memories with nostalgic flavours and a tasting menu driven by local seasonal produce, especially fish, whose courses never fail to surprise. The plating is particularly pleasing, and sometimes playful, such as the silky chicken soup in a glass bottle. The wine list boasts over 30 organic and biodynamic tipples that complement the food perfectly.;Air conditioning;[]
9078;Qureshi;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;GF, East Lobby, TPC Kuala Lumpur, 10 Jalan 1/70D, Jalan Bukit Kiara, Kuala Lumpur, 60000, Malaysia;3.1387345;101.6402115;46;false;false;Indian;One of the Indian dining concepts owned by the Qureshi family, this prestigious restaurant is nestled within a country club not accessible by public transport, so you’ll need to drive or take a taxi here. The room is furnished in a modern Indian style with a colourful palette, classic motifs and glitzy details. When it comes to the food, a nice variety of exquisite Indian cooking deeply rooted in traditions is served.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9079;Tamarind Hill;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;19 Jalan Sultan Ismail, Bukit Bintang, Kuala Lumpur, 50250, Malaysia;3.153262;101.7083103;34;true;true;Thai, Burmese;The glowing stairs lead you to a colonial bungalow amid lush greens with a beautiful terrace. Behind the French doors, the high-ceilinged room feels exotic and resort-like, priming diners for a serene culinary retreat just minutes away from the busy city centre. The menu is dominated by authentic no-frills Thai and Burmese cooking. Though without fancy plating, the food is astutely executed with fresh, quality ingredients.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9081;Pitt Street Koay Teow Soup;Malaysia;George Town;183 Lebuh Carnarvon, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.41501;100.33448;33;false;true;Noodles;The shop has been selling Penangese’ favourite fish ball soup for over 60 years and has been in this current spot since 2009. Fish balls are made daily in-house using flavoursome sea eel meat that complement their pork broth. Order “extra minced pork and fish ball” – minced pork refers to the flat pork balls – and top it with lots of crispy garlic bits. Homemade cakes and tarts end a meal perfectly, or take them home to enjoy later.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
9082;Marble 8;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;56F, Menara 3 Petronas, Persiaran KLCC, Kuala Lumpur City Centre, Kuala Lumpur, 50088, Malaysia;3.158135;101.715475;93;true;true;Steakhouse;It takes a few lift rides to get to Marble 8, but as soon as you set foot in the dining room, you know it’s all worthwhile. The stunning skyline with the Twin Towers in the foreground is the perfect backdrop for a sumptuous meal featuring top-quality halal-certified Wagyu and Angus beef straight from Australia. Premium cuts are dry- or wet-aged for at least 21 days for deep flavours and tender texture, and then grilled to perfection.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
9083;Bar Kar;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Suites G-06, GF, G Tower, 199 Jalan Tun Razak, Kampung Baru, Kuala Lumpur, 50400, Malaysia;3.159133;101.720158;31;false;false;Barbecue;Two chefs, who previously worked in Penang, opened this restaurant in 2023 specialising in house-aged meats and seafood cooked over a wood-fired grill. Diners are greeted by an arched entrance and a striking corridor lined with logs for the fire. The 18-seat arc-shaped counter with a view of the open kitchen is the best place to sit. Signatures include oysters cooked on the spot in flaming chicken fat in a flambadou, boasting rich, smoky aromas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
9084;Seed;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;L1-04, Block E, The Five@KPD, 49 Jalan Dungun, Bukit Damansara, Kuala Lumpur, 50490, Malaysia;3.1508826;101.6644017;81;true;false;Innovative;Splashes of earthy colours and cool neutrals adorn the inviting space, whose seats at the wave-shaped counter ensure a fascinating view of the open kitchen. After a stint at Whitegrass in Singapore, the chef flaunts his consummate grasp of French techniques with two prix-fixe menus that fete Japanese ingredients and cuisine. Standouts include the fried local snapper topped with anchovy and black olive crumbs, and chilled Hokkaido sweet corn potage.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
9086;La Vie;Malaysia;George Town;Le Dream Boutique Hotel, 139 Jalan Pintal Tali, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.415451;100.3329716;69;true;false;European Contemporary;This casual neighbourhood dining spot started out as a steakhouse, but switched to serving European cuisine with Asian influences. Their signature kataifi prawn is tiger prawn wrapped in crispy noodles, fried and served in a prawn bisque sauce. Meat lovers should check out the Australian Wagyu ribeye which is cooked to perfection on a charcoal grill. It comes with a range of condiments but the wasabi works best. Wine is available by the bottle only.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9087;Akar;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;109 Jalan Aminuddin Baki, Taman Tun Dr Ismail, Kuala Lumpur, 60000, Malaysia;3.1528453;101.6208917;75;false;true;Malaysian, Contemporary;Akar is Malay for "root" and Chef Low and his team pay homage to their culinary roots, creatively refashioning European dishes with interesting surprises. Local ingredients such as gula apong and engkabang are used in a menu that changes with the seasons and goes beyond the realms of typical Malaysian cooking. Their signature green salad with bagna cauda is packed with flavour. Further to refurbishments, the space feels intimate and cosy.;Air conditioning;[]
9088;Goh Thew Chik Hainan Chicken Rice;Malaysia;George Town;338A-338B Lebuh Chulia, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.418882;100.335424;82;false;false;Street Food;This shop with over 70 years of history serves not just Hainan-style chicken but also grilled chicken with chicken oil rice. The tangy chilli sauce made in-house cuts through the richness of the silky, juicy meat.;Cash only;[]
9089;Entier;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Level 41, Alila Bangsar, 58 Jalan Ang Seng, Brickfields, Kuala Lumpur, 50470, Malaysia;3.1277744;101.6801902;27;false;true;French Contemporary;The airy, minimalist room atop a sky-scraping hotel tower commands breathtaking cityscapes and is the epitome of casual elegance. The Japanese chef honed his skills in prestigious European kitchens before taking the helm here. The deftly crafted French menu sports subtle Japanese twists. Order à la carte dishes or go for the Chef's Degustation menu for dinner. Though the menu changes quarterly, the must-try beef, dry-aged in house, is a firm fixture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9090;888 Hokkien Mee (Lebuh Presgrave);Malaysia;George Town;67-A Lebuh Presgrave, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4111022;100.3306546;38;false;false;Street Food;For 30 years, this small outlet has been serving Hokkien-style noodles in prawn soup. The soup has a beautiful rich red colour and sweet umami flavour. Add a little textural variety to your bowl with tasty options such as braised pork ribs or roasted pork – both highly recommended.;Cash only;[]
9091;Penang Famous Samosa;Malaysia;George Town;45 Lebuh Queen, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4176628;100.3389519;89;true;true;Street Food;This stall in Little India serves a delicious range of samosas, including mutton, chicken, sardine, egg and vegetable. Encased in a crispy shell, the flavoursome fillings are moderately spicy. Prices are fair, too, so no wonder customers are prepared to queue.;Cash only;[]
9092;Bao Teck Tea House;Malaysia;George Town;25 Lebuh Melayu, George Town, 10300, Malaysia;5.4133643;100.3352107;38;false;false;Dim Sum;This is the place to go for an authentic yum cha experience and tasty Cantonese dim sum. The room has historic appeal, with details worth appreciating such as the patterned tile flooring and the moss garden. But it’s the dim sum that sets it apart – try steamed har gow dumplings made with local shrimp, and the deep-fried yam puffs in airy honeycomb crust. The owner also runs a bakery, and their Chinese baked goods are excellent.;Air conditioning;[]
9093;WhatSaeb Boat Noodles;Malaysia;George Town;173 Lebuh Carnarvon, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.4147811;100.3344524;65;true;false;Thai;Come here to get your fix for boat noodles. The owner hires a kitchen team from Thailand to make sure it’s made properly. There are many toppings and noodles to choose from, but pork rice noodle soup with extra pork cracklings will be your best bet. In addition to the noodle soup, the menu also features an array of Thai classics, such as curry, som tum salads and desserts. On weekends, make sure to try their mango sticky rice.;Air conditioning;[]
9094;Il Bacaro;Malaysia;George Town;Campbell House, 106 Lebuh Campbell, George Town, 10100, Malaysia;5.4181066;100.3336452;60;false;true;Italian;Photos from a by-gone era, retro ceiling fans and patterned tiles exude a nostalgic mood. This restaurant, run by a friendly Italian couple (who also own the hotel), has been serving classics from their home country for more than a decade. You can find most Italian classics on the menu, such as antipasto, pizzas, pastas and mains. Start with bruschetta tradizionale for a refreshing and appetising opener. Save some room for their homemade sweets.;Air conditioning;[]
9095;Eat and Cook;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;H6-1, Pusat Perdagangan Bandar Bukit Jalil, Persiaran Jalil 1, Bukit Jalil, Kuala Lumpur, 57000, Malaysia;3.055655;101.65981;64;false;true;Malaysian, Contemporary;Out of the city centre, Eat and Cook is owned by two young, accomplished chefs whose ambition and creativity define the unique dining experience. Featuring local ingredients, the set menu changes every three to four months. While the seasonality of Malaysian cuisine may not be obvious, each new chapter showcases different types of seafood and seasonal vegetables. The counter seats, known as The Stage, offer a knockout view of the kitchen team in action.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
9097;Kota Dine & Coffee (Fort Cornwallis);Malaysia;George Town;Fort Cornwallis, Jalan Tun Syed Sheh Barakbah, George Town, 10200, Malaysia;5.4206837;100.344138;31;true;true;Peranakan;It feels relaxing to sit in the glass-clad room drenched in natural light and furnished in faux-industrial style. In terms of food, they serve a neo-Nyonya menu with a strong East-meets-West concept. On top of Peranakan classics like otak-otak, Western influences are manifested in more adventurous creations such as laksa capellini. Even the desserts take a surprise twist, as in teh-ramisu that uses tea instead of coffee.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9098;Elegant Inn;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;02-01, 2F, Podium Block, Menara Hap Seng, Jalan P. Ramlee, Kuala Lumpur, Kuala Lumpur, 50250, Malaysia;3.15443;101.7151;46;true;false;Cantonese;Since 2008, Elegant Inn has been feeding gourmets Cantonese classics, especially Hong Kong-style favourites. Eat in the traditionally decorated wood-rich interior, or dine al fresco on the balcony. At lunchtime, exquisite dim sum takes centre stage, a highlight being the deep-fried taro pouch. The eight-treasure stuffed chicken wing with a filling of bouncy shrimps and mushrooms boasts crispy skin and layered flavours. The double-boiled soups are not to be missed!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
9100;Teochew Lao Er;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;6 Jalan Brunei, Pudu, Kuala Lumpur, 55100, Malaysia;3.1387218;101.713076;70;false;false;Teochew;In 1984, Lao Er started out as a street stall. In 2011, the third generation opened a restaurant and established itself as a household name in Pudu district. Teochew classics are given a slight tweak to cater to the local palate. The signature dish, meat marinated in spiced soy, is a great hit – try the assorted platter. Teochew congee with pomfret, mackerel, and traditional kueh are also popular.;Car park;[]
9101;Café Café;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;175 Jalan Maharajalela, Kampung Attap, Kuala Lumpur, 50150, Malaysia;3.1359837;101.7034463;47;false;false;French;Founded by two local chefs who plied their trade in France, Café Café is tucked away in a quiet part of the city. The interior, dripping in contemporary Parisian chic and traditional French grandeur, is ideal for a romantic dinner. The à la carte and set menus include classic dishes such as foie gras, escargots and duck confit. The carefully crafted food is perfectly poised between knockout texture and spot-on seasoning. The leg of duck confit has a crispy, delicious skin and succulent meat.;Air conditioning;[]
9102;Limapulo;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;50 Jalan Doraisamy, Chow Kit, Kuala Lumpur, 50300, Malaysia;3.1582761;101.6995291;98;false;true;Peranakan;Opened seven years ago, the restaurant has a rustic edge with vintage canteen-style furniture that evokes waves of nostalgia across a dimly lit venue. Limapulo (which means fifty in Malay), is managed by a team of Malaysian chefs. It’s best to choose plates for sharing and be sure to order the popular Nyonya laksa – a standout dish indeed. The signature sate has a special sauce homemade from star fruits and pineapple. Some menu items are only available on certain days.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9103;Dancing Fish;Malaysia;Kuala Lumpur;Lot T120 & 121, 3F, Bangsar Shopping Centre, 285 Jalan Maarof, Bangsar, Kuala Lumpur, 59000, Malaysia;3.1430703;101.6671335;51;true;true;Malaysian, Indonesian;On the third floor of a shopping mall, Dancing Fish specialises in classic Malay-Indo flavours with a distinct local identity. The nicely fried namesake fish dish boasts tender flesh in crunchy batter. It comes in numerous versions, with different toppings, sambal and savoury sauces. In addition, they serve classic varied cuisine rooted in local culture, including whole fish cooked over coals, barbecue chicken, ribs and beef.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Car park,Valet parking;[]
9104;Teppanyaki Mihara Goten;;Hong Kong;3F, Cubus, 1 Hoi Ping Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2776469;114.1850068;80;true;false;Teppanyaki;After moving from Tsueng Kwan O to bustling Causeway Bay, this 14-seater is hidden behind a sukiyaki joint and a cocktail bar. As always, chef Mihara champions a kappo-style teppanyaki experience using the freshest produce flown in from Japan. In addition to teppanyaki staples such as seafood and beef, his tasting menus include less commonly seen griddle items – silky, umami-laden chawanmushi, and donabe with foie gras, crab, fish or eel.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
9105;Yuan;;Hong Kong;Shop 2, GF, Chinachem Hollywood Centre, 1-13 Hollywood Road, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.281993;114.1543763;75;false;false;Vegetarian;This sleek eatery in the heart of the bustling business district sports warm whites and neutrals. Vegan and lacto-ovo vegetarian dishes are prepared in Chinese style, jazzed up by occasional European touches. Steamed and deep-fried twisted rolls with black olives and preserved cabbage foam on the side impart unique aromas. Delicately cut tofu floats in flavoursome matsutake broth like a chrysanthemum, flaunting exquisite knifework.;Air conditioning;[]
9106;Aji;;Macau;GM Floor,  MGM Cotai, Avenida da Nave Desportiva, Cotai, Macau;22.145594;113.568121;45;true;false;Innovative;Aji is helmed by a young Singaporean chef who fusions French flair with first-rate Japanese produce and Asian flavours. To wit, crispy skinned shima aji is served with sauces made from matcha green tea and 20-year-old dried tangerine peel. The counter is for diners who opt for the tasting menu that relates the chef’s memories. It can be creatively paired with red, white and yellow wines alongside sake and hard liquor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9107;Juno;;Hong Kong;GF, 88 Wing Lok Street, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.28649;114.15105;34;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The mint green façade with brushed brass trimming leads into a bright interior decked in wood, marble and travertine. Hailing from Barcelona, Spain, chef Jordi Vallés Claverol crafts a concise Mediterranean-inspired menu reminiscent of sunny southern Europe. Start your journey with house-made rosemary focaccia, best enjoyed with small sharing plates like charcoal peperonata. The baked Cote d’Azur seabass with crisp skin and juicy flesh is another must.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9108;Chiu Ka Banquet;;Hong Kong;8F, Champion Building, 287-291 Des Voeux Road Central, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.2872086;114.1513213;93;true;true;Chiu Chow;The traditionally furnished room, which used to be a private club, now specialises in home-style cooking from Chiuchow. Pork tripe soup with salted mustard greens and peppercorns is creamy and rich. Braised goose in spiced soy marinade impresses with a robust meaty flavour and subtle herbal warmth and the buttery, velvety goose liver is a must. Ask about the catch of the day and consider pre-ordering dried seafood like abalone and fish maw.;Air conditioning;[]
9109;Lun Kee Rice Roll;;Macau;26 Rua Do Tarrafeiro, Macau, Macau;22.198798;113.538376;96;false;false;Street Food;Since 2011, this simple shop has been serving rice rolls made and steamed to order. His spring onion and whisked egg rice roll is simple but delicious, boasting bouncy texture.;Cash only;[]
9111;Kyoen;Japan;Kyoto;570-118 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.001672;135.774183;15;true;false;Contemporary;Japanese and Italian cuisine in two-part harmony. Prix fixe menus incorporating both styles are the focus, with unique twists thrown in. Soups are mostly traditional Japanese in style, pasta flavours true to Italian roots. To wrap up the meal, rice as well as beef cutlet or curry are served, ensuring a satisfying finish. Appropriately for a menu of Japanese and Western fare, both sake and wine are on offer. A banquet that leaves nothing to be desired.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9113;Tenboshi;Japan;Osaka;7-10-9 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0041, Japan;34.71368;135.51121;97;false;true;Tempura;Tenboshi is managed by Numata, a developer of tempura restaurants. The chain has several locations, but this one is popular for its prices and casual style. Born in Amakusa, the chef gets many ingredients from his native Kumamoto, as well as other parts of Kyushu. Tempura, fried in a blended of fresh-pressed sesame and cottonseed oils, is light and airy. Providing seafood and vegetables alternately, with dipping sauces to set off each item to advantage, is one way to show off individuality.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9114;QUINTOCANTO;Japan;Osaka;3-6-32 Nakanoshima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0005, Japan;34.693317;135.492433;17;false;false;Italian;QUINTOCANTO is a cucina creativa, respectful of Italian tradition yet creative. The chef delves deep into Italian hometown cooking and presents his results with a contemporary feel. While offering perennial favourites such as Catalana of foie gras and spaghetti pomodoro, the restaurant is always conjuring new and creative menu items. Like every restaurant managed by the Salone Group, QUINTOCANTO strives to be a salon that provides guests with graceful service.;Air conditioning;[]
9115;Nishijin Hashimoto;Japan;Kyoto;109 Kanzecho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8441, Japan;35.03101;135.748777;75;true;false;Japanese;A baseball fanatic since his youth, behind the counter the chef demonstrates the strength of will he developed on the baseball diamond. His favourite expression, then and now, is ikkyu nyukon: pour your heart and soul into every pitch. To broaden his menu, he prepares sushi and soba himself. The famous gomadofu is paired with pureed soup of vegetables in season. The proprietress’ handmade sweets make diners feel welcome and the couple’s genuine desire to make every customer happy is palpable.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9116;Ueroku wine;Japan;Osaka;4-15 Higashikozucho, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0021, Japan;34.668227;135.521255;90;true;false;Spanish;A Spanish restaurant by Bordeaux vintner. Spain has two coasts, the Mediterranean and the Atlantic, and Japan is surrounded by seas on all four sides. These geographical features define the food culture and cooking on tap at Ueroku wine. The chef parlays Japan’s unique seafood into cuisine with a distinctive character. A selection of wines from many countries, including the owner’s own, Clos Leo, is available for your enjoyment.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9117;Tsujifusa;Japan;Kyoto;155 Mukadeyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0805, Japan;35.014965;135.763464;55;false;false;Japanese;Fusa means ‘linen’ or ‘hemp cloth’, which is used in Shinto rituals to symbolise cleanliness. The word was chosen for the restaurant’s name because, like Japanese cuisine, it developed from an origin as a sacred offering, and indeed the shop curtain hanging at the shop’s entrance is woven of pure linen. As part of his daily duties, the owner-chef prays at Ujiko Shrine and draws pure votive water from there. The proprietress, a qualified sommelier, suggests pairings of sake and wine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
9118;Kappo Umetsu;Japan;Kyoto;347-93 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.005219;135.775717;44;false;false;Japanese;Kappo Umetsu offers an extensive list of à la carte dishes, the better to entertain diners. In a show of flexibility, staff cater to guests’ preferred preparation method—grilled, simmered, fried and much more. ‘Umetsu’ is the proprietor’s name, but the inclusion of ume, ‘plum’, is significant, as the shop marinates sour pickled apricots to make apricot soy sauce, which it uses to dress parboiled pike conger and beef cutlets. The proprietress in her apron and the finely coordinated service make you feel at home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9119;Daidokoro Kamiya;Japan;Osaka;1-10-12 Kyomachibori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0003, Japan;34.687862;135.495192;20;true;false;Izakaya;Seafood dishes and appetizers are the selling points at Daidokoro Kamiya. White-fleshed fish, an indispensable part of Osaka cuisine, is the essential component here. Potato salad is prepared with vegetables in season, while “Heshiko Pepe” is an udon noodle dish stir-fried with garlic and heshiko (fish pickled in rice-bran paste), inspired by spaghetti peperoncino. Ingredients gathered from every corner of Japan are supplemented with items from overseas, such as Australian lamb.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9120;Shokudo Uchino;Japan;Osaka;4F, 1-4-7 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.696004;135.497798;51;false;false;Japanese;A self-taught chef and his partner with a background in Japanese cuisine were co-workers when they decided to open a restaurant of their own. They named it ‘Shokudo’, meaning ‘cafeteria’ or ‘dining hall’, out of a desire to create an easy-going dining experience. Monthly-changing prix fixe menus include popular items such as chawanmushi and mini burgers. Gyudon is a call-back to an earlier era when they managed a late-night eatery. With creative fare based on Japanese dishes, this shokudo is growing steadily in popularity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9121;Takoyakushi Furukawa;Japan;Kyoto;300 Ichirenshacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8146, Japan;35.006242;135.76044;76;false;true;Japanese;At the entrance is a branch of an izakaya chain, but walk through it to the back to find the sign and shop curtain for Takoyakushi Furukawa. The meal unfolds from the drawing of dashi stock, ensuring that you experience the beguiling aroma and taste of the basic clear stock. The menu is extensive, presenting the flavours of the season a little at a time. The meal wraps up with a rice dish such as white rice, takikomi-gohan or zosui. No effort is spared in expressing passion and pride in each dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9122;Masumasu Masuda;Japan;Kyoto;187-1 Hisashicho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8236, Japan;35.02563;135.749475;80;true;true;Japanese;The name combines the owner’s surname, Masuda, with an expression meaning ‘more and more’ – it’s a prayer that the restaurant will prosper as family members support one another. The menu skews strongly towards the produce of Tochigi Prefecture, where the chef was born and raised. In addition to seasonal vegetables, the restaurant serves trout raised by a friend of the chef in Nikko as oshizushi, and Tochigi wagyu beef as cutlets. Rice cooked on a hearth is sourced in Tochigi as well. You’ll come to love it ‘more and more’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9123;ku:de kiyo;Japan;Osaka;2-16-5 Tsukamoto, Yodogawa-ku, Osaka, 532-0026, Japan;34.713556;135.470402;22;true;true;French;‘Kuude’ is ‘let’s eat’ in Osaka dialect, the chef’s nickname is Kiyo, and the whole name has a French sound to it. A colour scheme of bright blue and green declares the shop’s freedom from convention. The theme is ‘unforgettable cuisine’: each dish features no more than three items, arrangements are minimal, and portions are generous. At lunchtime, set meals of Western items paired with rice and miso soup make ku:de kiyo a local favourite.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
9125;Komedokoro Inamoto;Japan;Kyoto;534-1 Yawatacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8455, Japan;34.997208;135.75511;57;false;false;Izakaya;The proprietor loves rice, so he named his establishment ‘Komedokoro’, meaning ‘Place of Rice’. Taste the freshly-cooked white rice and you’ll understand why it’s so famous. Dishes are served on small plates, encouraging you to try a variety. Order the platter of side dishes and you’re sure to eat more than intended. The chef sources seafood and citrus fruits from his native Ehime. Sake and nibbles served at this ‘place of rice’ vary by the day.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
9126;Sushi Ichiei;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 1-6-10 Sennichimae, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0074, Japan;34.668014;135.504491;75;true;true;Sushi;Inheriting his father’s dream of independence, the chef followed him along the path of the sushi master. The signature item on the omakase menu is tsukuri of botan shrimp. The arrival of ginger wrapped in nori signals the transition from appetizers to sushi. Nigiri are orthodox, though the choice of sweet shrimp hits a distinctive note. The chef’s assured technique shows even in the thick rolled omelette. ‘Ichiei’ means something like ‘forever’, capturing his hope that you will treasure your encounter with his shop and remain a friend to it.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9127;Kurubushi;Japan;Osaka;4-12 Naniwacho, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0022, Japan;34.707452;135.509675;50;false;false;Japanese;The chef of an izakaya opened this kappo as a sister establishment. He favours items with a salty taste, the better to keep the sake flowing. Vintage Japanese serving vessels and antique Western glasses delight the eye. The meal wraps up with seasonal takikomi-gohan or curry rice—with free refills, a welcome bonus. Omakase cooking bursting with creativity—enjoy it to your heart’s content.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9128;Quarter Acre;USA;Dallas;2023 Greenville Ave., Ste. 110, Dallas, 75206, USA;32.8149292;-96.770158;65;false;false;Contemporary;Here the name embodies a pastoral suburban ideal, while the strikingly chic space flaunts a certain airy forest-meets-island aesthetic—both making nods to Chef/owner Toby Archibald’s New Zealand roots. Along similar lines, his cuisine walks a line between flashiness and substance, featuring broadly international flavors anchored by classic French techniques, while showcasing eye-catching presentations and an occasional flair for the dramatic. Take for example an indulgent savory éclair filled with king crab, topped off with a soigné ruffle of feather-light smoked avocado mousse and tangy dots of Meyer lemon, or a seabass grilled “en papillote” inside a banana leaf, served with a vibrant mango salsa and a creamy macadamia nut sauce.;;[]
9129;Jeffrey's;USA;Austin;1204 W. Lynn St., Austin, 78704, USA;30.2805633;-97.759137;67;false;true;Contemporary, Steakhouse;Ensconced in the quiet historical Clarksville neighborhood, this smartly appointed space offers a genteel retreat from worldly troubles. Your table might be shy on elbow room, but posh furnishings and gracious service are sure to put you at ease. The menu features skillfully composed plates of contemporary fare boasting enticing seasonal flavors, as in an appetizer of English pea tortellini with morels and sweetbreads, or a crisp-skinned Pekin duck breast "au poivre." Alternatively, you can choose from array of elevated steakhouse offerings paired with deliciously updated sides like a creamed spinach gratin with Fresno chili and parmesan, or steak fries with horseradish aïoli.;;[]
9130;Hidden Omakase;USA;Houston;5353 W. Alabama St., Ste. 102, Houston, 77056, USA;29.7377986;-95.4692235;29;true;false;Sushi, Contemporary;True to its name, this dark, intimate space is sealed off from the strip mall outside—but when it comes to its reputation for a showy, immersive experience, the secret is certainly out. In the care of Chef Marcos Juarez, this 18-seat counter offers only two services each night and features a wide array of premium seafood prepared with a unique approach that bucks tradition. Think masu with jicama and pumpkin seed furikake or Hokkaido uni with tomato jam and Thai basil. Chefs happily engage with diners and regularly present whole cuts of fish for demonstrations.;;[]
9131;El Carlos Elegante;USA;Dallas;1400 N. Riverfront Blvd., Dallas, 75207, USA;32.7900631;-96.8199455;50;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Don't be fooled by the nondescript exterior, as this lively and friendly place welcomes guests with an appealing rustic and authentic Mexican ambience. Stop in the lounge at the entrance for a drink before heading to your table, though if you enjoy being in the center of it all while watching the team cook over a wood-fired grill, then there's no better spot than a seat at the horseshoe counter. The menu is tightly edited, featuring a handful of dishes ranging from small plates and masas to meatier entrees. Everything is vibrant, full of flavor, and designed for sharing, so order with abandon to sample it all. Their list of tequila and mezcal is impressive, and the helpful staff is always on hand to offer recommendations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
9132;Leche de Tigre;USA;San Antonio;318 E. Cevallos St., San Antonio, 78204, USA;29.4075809;-98.4972506;43;true;true;Peruvian;A ceviche bar, a cocktail menu full of pisco sours, and a cute patio? What’s not to like? This colorful hotspot is buzzing for good reason. Driven by a trio of brothers and their time spent growing up in Peru, this little bungalow emphasizes seafood dressed up in bright, zippy, punchy flavors. Striped bass with ginger leche de tigre thrives with the clever addition of plantains and huacatay oil. Scallops set in a sharp parmesan leche de tigre are paired with capers and garlic chips. Tostadas come piled high with yellowfin tuna tossed with Nikkei ponzu and showered with crispy leeks. Break from the sea with lomo saltado, a bold effort thanks to an umami-packed sauce that coats seared beef tenderloin, crispy-fried potatoes, and charred scallions.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
9133;Bludorn;USA;Houston;807 Taft St., Houston, 77019, USA;29.7589944;-95.3856962;51;false;true;American, Contemporary;Chef Aaron Bludorn and his wife Victoria are the minds behind this buzzy dining room fitted with cushy, royal blue booths, handsome wood chairs, and a gleaming open kitchen. There is something for everyone on this broad menu that pulls inspiration from all corners, swinging from seafood towers to blackened cobia with green gumbo to potato gnocchi with crawfish. Bludorn follows the seasons closely, and his servers follow their guests even closer. Plates are cleared, silverware replaced, and drinks refilled with remarkable swiftness. Dinner must close with a sizeable baked Alaska, made with a range of sorbets and ice creams like pistachio, raspberry, and gianduja all covered in meringue and lit on fire. It is as entertaining as it is satisfying.;Valet parking;[]
9134;Fearing's;USA;Dallas;2121 McKinney Ave., Dallas, 75201, USA;32.7920978;-96.8034666;72;true;false;American, Regional Cuisine;Nestled inside the luxe Ritz-Carlton, Fearing's is elegant and dramatic. The handsome look may read traditional steakhouse but this flagship restaurant from Chef Dean Fearing isn't straightforward. Instead, the American menu with clear Southwestern influences is both complex and composed with buffalo and antelope along with classic-leaning filets. The dishes are surprising, offering bold flavors and new takes on the tried-and-true. Case in point? Their Lone Star mosaic, Fearing's take on carpaccio with tuna, wagyu beef, salmon, and barbecued eel composing a vivid plate resembling stained glass. Baklava S'more riffs on the campsite classic with puff pastry piped with milk chocolate pot de creme, pistachio marshmallow, and burnt rosemary ice cream for a refined finale.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
9136;Signature Restaurant;USA;San Antonio;16401 La Cantera Pkwy, San Antonio, 78256, USA;29.598868;-98.615822;24;false;true;French, American;There is a warm and inviting appeal about Signature Restaurant, set within La Cantera Resort & Spa. Seafood dominates the menu, though there are plenty of other choices, including venison, pork, and beef. If the large menu and comprehensive wine list have you stumped, the attentive staff will keep you on track. Begin with an appetizer such as the Spanish octopus, grilled to a tender and crispy finish, served over an avocado puree and sided by confit potatoes, Spanish chorizo, and a salsa verde. Next, consider the venison, deftly cooked and accompanied by a cherry jus, baby carrots, and potato pave. End the meal on a high note with their warm torta di ricotta with candied almonds, blueberries, and yuzu buttermilk ice cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9137;Rye;USA;Dallas;1920 Greenville Ave., Dallas, 75206, USA;32.81361;-96.76991;35;true;false;Contemporary;Located in Dallas's Lower Greenville district, Rye sports a sexy, cozy vibe with wood plank floors, beamed ceiling, and exposed red brick walls. Guests are cared for with a genuine hospitality and the beverage selection is especially impressive with a range of cocktails on offer (they also operate Apothecary, the cocktail lounge next door).Food-wise, the cuisine is unrestrained and offers diners a taste of wide-ranging inspirations. The à la carte menu serves up the likes of a Texas-raised wagyu beef hot dog or a dish of comforting cacio e pepe. The tasting menu is an extensive affair that may combine a beef tallow and mezcal emulsion drizzled taco, a slice of beet and goat cheese lasagna, and chocolate cake dressed with spruce and rosemary.;;[]
9138;Discada;USA;Austin;1319 Rosewood Ave., Austin, 78702, USA;30.2687661;-97.7244484;79;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Head to East Austin to find this stationary food truck where they only have one thing on their mind—discada. It may be the easiest order you've ever made, as there is no menu posted and the only decision you'll need to make is how many taquitos you want. As for the food, it's all in the name. Discada is a Northern Mexican style of cooking with different cuts of beef and pork cooked together with aromatic vegetables. Their version also adds bacon, onion, and roasted poblano peppers, all cooked down and served taquito style in single layers of yellow corn tortillas. Topped with a pulverized pineapple slaw and served with fresh salsa on the side, it's a delicious style not often seen. Elote and soft drinks round out the hyper-focused offerings.;Terrace;[]
9139;Candente;USA;Houston;4306 Yoakum Blvd., Houston, 77006, USA;29.7340941;-95.3927225;65;false;true;Tex-Mex;If Candente were any larger, it would need its own zip code. The number of tables, the expansive patio, the bar seating that stretches the length of the kitchen – the scale of this Tex-Mex restaurant is considerable. And yet, the cooking keeps up. You could make a whole meal out of the tortilla soup, and there’s a lot to like about the enchiladas, stuffed with cheese or, notably, brisket. But we’re really here for the fajitas featuring excellent prime beef sourced from Niman Ranch. Tender cuts arrive on a sizzling cast-iron with charred onions and come with fantastic tortillas made with brisket trimmings. There’s nothing light or delicate about any of this. This is food that sticks to your bones and wipes you out until you’re ready for more.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9140;Sachet;USA;Dallas;4270 Oak Lawn Ave., Dallas, 75219, USA;32.8215295;-96.8022897;83;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;There’s something about this corner restaurant that makes it look so inviting—and sure enough, the moment you step inside you feel enveloped in the warm embrace of the bright, southern European sun. That’s not just down to the light, open feel of the large room, but also because of the charming service team. This may be the baby sister of Gemma restaurant, but the menu here looks to the wider Mediterranean for its influences, stretching from Morocco to Syria and round to Italy, France, and Spain. Dishes like octopus with freekeh and lamb with gigante beans are as colorful and appealing as they are satisfying and nourishing. If you can’t get a table—and the booths are much demanded—you can try your luck at the large counter bar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
9141;Garcia's Mexican Food;USA;San Antonio;842 Fredericksburg Rd., San Antonio, 78201, USA;29.4517475;-98.5131766;94;true;true;Tex-Mex;Open since 1962, this venerable institution from the Garcia family remains a vibrant, proud part of the city’s dining fabric. At all hours, the squat building has people waiting outside waiting for a table and ready to dig into classic Tex-Mex cooking. The menu is expansive, and one could spend weeks trying to cover it. There are those who come to order eggs over easy, douse them in salsa, and scoop them up in warm flour tortillas. And then there are heartier appetites who launch right into the deluxe dinner, which features enchiladas, a tamale, chili con carne, and a hard-shell taco. Should you also tack on a brisket taco? Of course you should. Adding to the convivial charm of the diner setting is a staff that’s all smiles.;Air conditioning;[]
9142;Pappas Bros. Steakhouse;USA;Houston;5839 Westheimer Rd., Houston, 77057, USA;29.7375654;-95.4812398;54;false;true;Steakhouse, American;Even after more than two decades of service, this Houston institution is as sharp as ever. The menu is focused, offering just a limited number of appetizers and salads to keep all eyes and appetites on the prime, in-house dry-aged steaks. Seasoned and seared properly, the cuts are complemented by generous, finely tuned sides like creamed spinach with ham or oversized onion rings (ask for extra crispy). Part of the genius here is the service: Veteran waiters and friendly sommeliers are effortlessly hospitable regardless of whether you order 1947 Petrus. Altogether, with white tablecloths, glossy wood paneling, and a wine list that has few equals, this restaurant captures a kind of magic that is rarely seen these days but unquestionably appreciated.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
9143;Este;USA;Austin;2113 Manor Rd., Austin, 78722, USA;30.2840914;-97.7196279;32;false;false;Mexican, Seafood;Set in a converted bungalow in East Austin, Este sparkles with a cool vibe while highlighting contemporary Mexican cuisine with a seafood focus. Ceviche amarillo with white fish and a piña turmeric broth is a delicious way to kick off the meal. From there, piña preparada with slices of pineapple topped with a piloncillo salsa and dusted with cacao nibs and chile salt is incredibly simple yet highly memorable. Main dishes are largely inspired by the grill, while the fish of the day is wrapped in banana leaf served with hoja santa salsa verde and refried beans. Round out the meal with one of their desserts, perhaps the pastel de elote, a round moist corn cake topped with candied hazelnuts, blueberries, and a brown butter creme.;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
9144;Barsotti's;USA;Dallas;4208 Oak Lawn Ave., Dallas, 75219, USA;32.8197392;-96.8022364;83;false;false;Italian;Set at a busy junction in the Oak Lawn neighborhood, this popular restaurant is named after the owner's great-grandfather. The contemporary trattoria's bright and bold design is eye-catching, with black-and-white floors and a curved bar with counter seating for taking in views of the open kitchen.Simple and straightforward is the name of the game here, where the emphasis is on terrific homemade pasta dishes. Linguini with shrimp scampi, lasagna Bolognese, or the ever-comforting spaghetti with meatballs are just a few of their hits. Add a selection from the all-Italian wine list to complete the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9145;Joe's Bakery & Coffee Shop;USA;Austin;2305 E. 7th St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.261224;-97.7162581;89;false;true;Tex-Mex;This East Austin standby, run by the Avila family since 1962, is no frills but all heart. Slide into one of their built-in booths to enjoy Tex-Mex offerings available by the plate or platter. Not an early riser? Breakfast is offered all day here, and their twice-fried bacon is legendary for its crisp texture, so a bacon and egg taco is always a good idea. Another morning standout is the Migas tacos. Served on their house-made flour tortilla and filled with scrambled eggs mixed with crispy corn tortillas, peppers, and cheese, it's a delicious treat. Craving something sweet? The bakery case is brimming with conchas and other delights, but if you're not in a breakfast mood, the barbacoa is spot on. Add a tortilla and some pico and you're all set.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9146;Terry Black’s BBQ;USA;Austin;1003 Barton Springs Rd., Austin, 78704, USA;30.2601839;-97.7554625;69;true;false;Barbecue;Scions of the legendary Black barbecue clan (whose original Lockhart location has spawned multiple outlets), left the fold to forge their own path, naming their business in honor of their father. As is expected for central Texas barbeque, beef takes the pride of place: the slow-smoked prime sliced brisket and behemoth bone-in beef ribs are the main events here, but all of their meat offerings, like pork ribs and sausage, demonstrate the team's dedication to their craft. You'll also find respectable sides, like tangy potato salad or fresh green beans. Seating is first-come, first-served, but don't fret, as the sizeable building, decked out like a well-worn roadhouse, offers plenty of space, both indoors and out.;;[]
9147;Mum Foods Smokehouse & Delicatessen;USA;Austin;5811 Manor Rd., Austin, 78723, USA;30.3058715;-97.6805301;48;false;true;Barbecue, Deli;Geoffrey Ellis and Travis Crawford are the brains behind this popular spot in Mueller that is equal parts Texas barbecue and delicatessen. Located in a shared space, it's a classic no-fuss spot with concrete floors and booths made from wooden slats, but you're here for the food, most likely the house-made pastrami sandwich. Brined, then rubbed with black pepper and coriander before being smoked, they take their meat seriously. Piled high on house-made rye sourdough with mustard, it's their signature item for a good reason. Other sandwiches, meat by the pound, a variety of sides like collard greens, potato salad, and chips and pimento dip, plus classics like matzoh ball soup are all worth a try too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9148;Mercat Bistro;USA;Dallas;2501 N. Harwood St., Ste. 225, Dallas, 75201, USA;32.7920309;-96.8061671;27;true;false;French, American;There are occasions for trends and then there are times when tradition reigns, and that's exactly where Mercat Bistro comes in. This amiable restaurant delivers the classic French bistro experience from its wood floors, marble-topped tables, and round-backed chairs to its extensive menu showcasing all of the hits. Discover a litany of favorites, ranging from escargots in parsley butter and French onion soup to moules frites and pot au crème. Come at lunch to indulge in sandwiches like the croque monsieur. In true bistro fashion, nothing is too precious, but it's all comforting and delicious. The service is welcoming and attends to the mix of business diners and locals with skill but be sure to secure a seat in the room with the open kitchen to enjoy a livelier vibe.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
9149;Late August;USA;Houston;4201 Main St., Ste. 120, Houston, 77002, USA;29.734433;-95.382073;16;true;true;Southern, International;Once a Sears department store and now a community tech hub, The Ion is a fitting home for this vibrant restaurant. Cool shades of teal, couches colored burnt orange, and plenty of light streaming in through the windows make for an airy stage for this eclectic menu by chefs Chris Williams and Sergio Hidalgo. The two celebrate cuisine in their own creative ways. Think smoked chicken drumettes with mole or a vibrant garden salad with fry bread croutons and suya dressing. Goat stew with guajillo peppers and collard green rice was one recent heartwarming effort. Much of the produce comes from Fort Bend County, where the group’s philanthropic arm runs a 10-acre farm that supports the community in a myriad of impressive ways.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9150;Comedor;USA;Austin;501 Colorado St., Austin, 78701, USA;30.2676406;-97.7442009;86;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Located in Austin's Central Business District, Comedor is a stunner with a carefully curated sense of cool. Inside, traditional and contemporary furnishings are combined with industrial but refined materials (think leather, polished woods, concrete, and glass), and when the weather permits, the courtyard is the place to be. No matter the time, Chef/owner Philip Speer's spot is nearly always packed, and they're here for more than the scene. Dishes such as bone marrow tacos with smoked butter and pecan gremolata play well with the more traditional tuna aguachile. Campechano de hongos is even better with a fiery salsa, while fish tacos are always spot on. For dessert, the tamal de chocolate with house-made ice cream is a rich and inventive Mexican treat.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9151;Harvest;USA;McKinney;215 N. Kentucky St., McKinney, 75069, USA;33.1985199;-96.6158792;34;false;true;American;Located in McKinney, Harvest at The Masonic ensures that your seasonally minded meal will be served with a side of live music. Most nights of the week, guests are treated to live rock, folk, and country bands, but don't assume the food is an afterthought. This kitchen takes sustainability seriously, crafting their menu from local, ethically sourced products and delivering rustic and bold dishes. Smoked brisket tacos topped with avocado and apricot salsa, crunchy radish, and pickled red onion are kicky, while crispy catfish is sided by a tasty casserole of locally sourced chorizo, celery root, green beans, red onions and cabbage. Dessert was made for pie in these parts and the peanut butter honey chess pie doesn't disappoint.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9153;Lenoir;USA;Austin;1807 S. 1st St., Austin, 78704, USA;30.2473196;-97.7560024;27;false;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Inside this cozy whitewashed bungalow, find a gem of a place with a sprinkling of tables and a few seats at the bar. These tiny digs turn out big, impressive dishes. The farm-to-table menu is one of the most creative around. Owners Todd Duplechan and Jessica Maher tempt guests with the likes of crab fingers, an exquisite dish featuring tiny blue crab legs in leche de tigre green curry with smoked chili oil. A main dish of poached snapper with matchstick radishes and pickled blueberries in a cool dashi is a perfect dish for a warm evening. Choosing between Texas honey pie, corn churros with coffee sugar and Texas pecan ice cream, or a chocolate chunk cookie tucked with buttercream and accompanied by spiced pistachio milk is no easy task.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9154;2M Smokehouse;USA;San Antonio;2731 S. Ww White Rd., San Antonio, 78222, USA;29.3824237;-98.4046035;31;true;false;Barbecue, Mexican;Led by pitmaster and co-owner, Esaul Ramos Jr., 2M Smokehouse is the real deal. There is usually a line to order at the counter and wait for your tray before sitting in their enclosed seating area or outside on the benches. Unlike some spots where you're relegated to one offering by the pound, it's all cut and weighed market style here, so have as much as you want of their terrific offerings. It's all good but make sure to try their juicy brisket or thickly sliced turkey breast with a citrus-pepper seasoning. Mexican influences, such as chicharrón macaroni, pickled nopales, and street corn, also make their way onto the menu, and all orders come with a side of house-made dill pickles.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
9155;Baso;USA;Houston;633 W. 19th St., #A, Houston, 77008, USA;29.8029324;-95.4095137;42;true;false;American, Contemporary;Bring friends to this underground party of a restaurant in the Heights. Heavy beats boom through the austere, concrete dining room fit with moody lighting and a long open kitchen armed with a glowing hearth. Yes, this is where the cool people eat. The tight menu leans into live-fire cooking and pulls ideas from all over: Tataki-style albacore tuna with barley and fried chicken skin, a hands-on Caesar salad, and serious cuts of heritage pork, ribeyes, and wagyu. Sharing really is the best way forward here. The signature Basque cheesecake, topped off with caviar if desired, is a notably indulgent way to finish this big meal, but don’t underestimate a wonderfully smooth scoop of ice cream either.;Air conditioning;[]
9156;Nicosi;USA;San Antonio;221 Newell Ave., San Antonio, 78215, USA;29.4409555;-98.4806909;84;true;false;Contemporary, Creative;You won't need to remember to save room for dessert at Nicosi, as this unusual concept features a dessert-only tasting where no menu is shared and there is a strict no-photo policy to encourage guests to be especially present. The multicourse meal is split into four themes—acidic, umami, bitter, and sweet—with each part featuring two dishes. The menu evolves often, and the chefs weave in unexpected elements not often associated with dessert, as in sponge cake with black garlic ice cream and fermented pineapple sauce or a buñuelo filled with beef jelly and chocolate ganache and topped with cold brew coffee gel. Impressive beverage pairings, like a carrot colada with Austrian carrot eau de vie, rum, beet, and coconut foam, accompany each course.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9157;Ezov;USA;Austin;2708 E. Cesar Chavez St., Austin, 78704, USA;30.2532577;-97.7132955;90;true;false;Israeli;This family-style Mediterranean/Middle Eastern restaurant comes from the same group behind Emmer & Rye. Terrific for groups, it's the kind of place where you want to snack on a little bit of everything. First up, smashed cucumber marinated with amba and set atop luscious labneh is an ideal starter. Beef and lamb kebab on a bed of fire-roasted eggplant and charred onions is even better with dipping sauces like tahini with herbs, schug, and a spicy chili sauce. It's even better with a glass of wine from their keenly organized list. Meanwhile, baklava is a treat enough on its own, but here it's given an extra boost thanks to a scoop of tahini ice cream and brûléed banana.;;[]
9159;Lutie's;USA;Austin;4100 Red River St., Austin, 78751, USA;30.2989952;-97.7220364;73;false;true;American, Regional Cuisine;Located in North Austin at the landmark Commodore Perry Estate, Lutie's is a grand space done in a green and gold palette with windows overlooking a stunning patio with gardens and a fountain. Run by the husband-and-wife team of Chef Bradley Nicholson and pastry chef Susana Querejazu, Lutie's offers a seasonally inspired, refined approach to Texas heritage cooking, available à la carte and as a tasting menu. Their estate bread, made with a decades-old starter and fermented corn grits and given a good sear, is even better with their exquisite cultured butter with layers of brown butter. House-smoked trout roe adds a pop of flavor to the Mt. Lassen trout with crispy skin. Finally, a scoop of Kouign-amann ice cream with a mini Kouign-amann topped with warm caramel sauce is a perfect classic.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9160;Birdie's;USA;Austin;2944 E. 12th St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.2763478;-97.7046812;98;false;false;Contemporary;This East Austin darling from Chef Tracy Malechek-Ezekiel and partner Arjav Ezekiel looks and feels like the quintessential neighborhood place but one glance at the line out the door and it's clear Birdie's is also a destination for visitors. Be prepared for a wait to order at their counter, then find a seat indoors or out on the shaded patio.Everyone is here for a taste of their unfussy but well-executed, contemporary American cooking. Begin with a few small bites like the crispy polenta or the chilled tomato and peach soup with fried sourdough croutons. Pasta, like the house-made tortiglioni in a sauce of slightly sweet Sungold tomatoes, is a must, and nothing beats a gooey chocolate chip cookie with house-made soft serve.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9161;Launderette;USA;Austin;2115 Holly St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.2519418;-97.7227204;54;true;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Chef Rene Ortiz's spot is good, clean fun, and not just because it's a former laundromat converted into this contemporary diner. Inside, tables and bar seating welcome diners, while patio seating is ideal for nice weather. The cocktail selection is notable (think mezcal negronis and other inventive drinks), and their happy hour is a nice way to sample without busting your budget. From beef tartare with tonnato, chestnut mushrooms, and an ash- infused rye bread to grilled octopus served over roasted yellow tomato sauce with Calabrian chili mayonnaise and bottarga, the dishes are creative and craveable. Desserts, like the tonka bean mille-feuille with lemon curd, blueberry jam and crème fraiche ice cream, are worthy of attention.;;[]
9162;Panther City BBQ;USA;Fort Worth;201 E. Hattie St., Fort Worth, 76104, USA;32.7381008;-97.324716;32;false;false;Barbecue, Tex-Mex;Named in honor of Fort Worth's nickname, Panther City BBQ began as a food truck before landing this space with both indoor and outdoor seating. This is central Texas-style barbecue with meat slow-cooked on offset pits. Here, they dole out Texan classics while also leaning into Tex-Mex offerings like brisket burritos, brisket elote, and street tacos. Arrive early to avoid long lines to savor the likes of expertly smoked, thickly sliced brisket with a pepper-heavy rub or tender, shredded pulled pork. As with any good barbecue spot, the sides are attention grabbing, and some of their hits include spicy smoked mac and cheese and potato salad with baked, smashed potato and red potatoes mixed with shredded cheese, green onion, and mayonnaise.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9163;Georgie;USA;Dallas;4514 Travis St., Dallas, 75205, USA;32.8223898;-96.7911089;53;false;false;Steakhouse;This swanky space, decked out in sunny tones of peach and carrot with a retro-meets-modern vibe, certainly looks the part for an elegant night out, especially given the attentive team of uniformed servers. Chef RJ Yoakum is an alumnus of The French Laundry, an influence apparent in his cooking, which combines a reverence for top-quality ingredients with a basis in classic technique along with a hint of playfulness. Take, for example, crispy, creamy potato “churros,” served with a fluffy, creamy caramelized onion dip (and an optional addition of caviar), or a pork tenderloin paired with whipped popcorn polenta and a BBQ cherry gastrique. The prices may be nothing to sneeze at, but guests are certain to be well taken care of—and well fed.;;[]
9164;Apt 115;USA;Austin;2025 E. 7th St., Austin, 78702, USA;30.2618404;-97.7196765;84;true;false;Fusion;Appt 115 is an intimate wine bar with a cozy ambience. It's the sort of place you'll want to stop in for a glass or two of wine paired with a charcuterie board or perhaps a parade of dishes from the full menu. Kick things off with openers like tuna sashimi with grapefruit ponzu and chili crisp or a delightful cheese plate with a strawberry and jalapeno spread that is ideal for smearing on the warm baguette served alongside. Larger plates, like the duck confit with spaetzle and purple carrots in a black tea jus, show effort from the kitchen, while a strawberry panna cotta with mint and moscato syrup makes for a nice finale.;Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
9165;Smoke'N Ash BBQ;USA;Arlington;5904 S. Cooper St., Arlington, 76017, USA;32.6508707;-97.1349168;39;true;false;Barbecue, Ethiopian;Husband and wife Patrick and Fasicka Hicks started like many other barbecue spots with a trailer smoker and weekend pop-ups, but that's where most of the similarities end. This casual Arlington spot with booth and table seating and a welcoming ambience bills its barbecue as Tex-Ethiopian. There are some typical Texan classics, but it's their barbecue seared with awaze, an Ethiopian-spice sauce, that truly stands out. Sold by the half-pound, platters are the way to go if you want to sample more of the offerings like skillfully smoked brisket and tender pulled lamb. They have the classic sides like mac and cheese and potato salad, but try something different like their collard greens, fried okra, or Ethiopian lentil stews.;;[]
9166;Brisket & Rice;USA;Houston;13111 FM-529 Rd., Houston, 77041, USA;29.8783398;-95.6089449;69;false;true;Barbecue, Asian;Brisket fried rice by the gas station? Only in Texas. Chef Hong Tran originally cooked brisket as a backyard hobby but now finds himself running this bustling restaurant with his family in the greater Houston area. Long lines move quickly through this well-oiled operation, which shares a parking lot with people filling up their tanks. Practically everyone is here for the same thing, and Tran’s signature dish is a reflection of his Lone Star upbringing and Vietnamese roots: Jasmine fried rice tossed with fried egg and Chinese sausage packs proper wok flavor, and each order can come with two prime, melting slabs of brisket. No need to bother with the sides when you can fill up on the pork ribs, which are beautifully tender and delicately smoked.;Air conditioning;[]
9167;Stillwell's;USA;Dallas;Hôtel Swexan, 2575 Mckinnon St., Dallas, 75201, USA;32.7927301;-96.8057694;81;false;true;Steakhouse;It's nestled inside the Hôtel Swexan, a tongue-in-cheek play on Swiss hospitality meets Texas, but there's no mistaking the roots of this upscale steakhouse: it's named for the legendary lady rancher, Hallie Stillwell. Ride the elevator to the seventh floor to enter this clubby den, then sip a cocktail as you peruse their extensive menu with all of the classics. Kick things off with a shrimp cocktail, caviar, or treat yourself to the bountiful seafood tower, but of course, steaks take center stage. There are many selections but their bespoke in-house HWD beef—a superb Akaushi beef from their own breeding program just north of the Red River—is the one to beat. All the while, elegant white jacketed staff keep things moving smoothly.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9168;Stock & Barrel;USA;Dallas;316 W. Davis St., Dallas, 75208, USA;32.7494094;-96.8276294;45;true;false;American;Set in the charming Bishop Arts area, Jon Stevens's Stock & Barrel is the perfect neighborhood spot. With an industrial chic design, open kitchen, and convivial bar counter, this restaurant is consistently packed with locals, all here for the inviting ambience. Whether you sit at the bar or in a booth, the friendly staff will ensure an enjoyable time. Expect American and Texas favorites that have been given a twist, as in deviled eggs with pickled rhubarb, meatloaf made with wagyu beef, or a bread pudding from croissants. Flavors are big and bold. Don't miss their caramelized Brussels sprouts charred with chili and cilantro. The wine list features a nice selection of by-the-glass offerings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
9169;Mexta;USA;Austin;106 E. 6th St., Ste. #110, Austin, 78701, USA;30.2681341;-97.7422896;52;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Celebrated Chefs Mikel Alonso Garcia and Jonatan Gómez Luna Torres combine their talents at this stylish East Austin spot, offering refined takes on classic Mexican preparations. Diners can start things off with the requisite guacamole, or choose from a small assortment of carefully prepared ceviches and aguachiles featuring excellent seafood. Sauces especially impress, as in the case of a complex, layered mole manchamanteles made with plantain and pineapple, paired with a masa-based tetela topped with unctuous bites of slow-cooked pork belly. A collection of inventive cocktails adds interest to the meal, and a signature dessert of fluffy, creamy cheesecake, made with three cheeses and baked to order, intriguingly blends savory and sweet.;;[]
9171;Garrison;USA;Austin;101 Red River St., Austin, 78701, USA;30.2619006;-97.7386954;26;false;false;American;Though it's nestled inside the chic, contemporary Fairmont Austin, Garrison has an identity all its own, standing out from the pack with its large open kitchen and live fire cooking. There's plenty of grilling and smoking going on here, but the kitchen's dishes really shine. Start with a balance and bright kanpachi crudo with slightly seared avocado and Espelette pepper or chickpea panisse with lemon aioli and za'atar. A flaky leek tart accompanied by goat cheese and a quenelle of onion and bacon jam is another delicious opener before tucking into the main event—grilled meat like the Akaushi wagyu ribeye. Expertly seared and lush, it's even better sided by hasselback potatoes with saffron rouille, fine herbs, and Bearnaise sauce.;;[]
9172;Tei-An;USA;Dallas;1722 Routh St., Dallas, 75201, USA;32.7923042;-96.7953096;84;true;false;Japanese, Soba;The Arts District and Tei-An are a perfect fit, as this Japanese restaurant provides an elegant and cultured experience in an aesthetically striking environment. Opened back in 2008, it has also played an important role in nurturing the city’s love affair with Japanese cuisine. The menu is varied and extensive, allowing diners to decide their own level of expense and experimentation. There’s everything from tonkatsu to tempura, as well as dishes like grilled freshwater eel (which comes with its crisped spine as you’d get in Japan), but its house-made soba and udon noodles—served cold or hot—are the house specialties. They come with an array of seasonal toppings and dipping sauces, many traditional and some, like Bolognese, more original.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
9173;Ling Kitchen;USA;Austin;8423 Research Blvd., Austin, 78758, USA;30.357947;-97.7156559;46;true;true;Chinese, Contemporary;Chef Ling Qi Wu owns several restaurants around town, but here at Ling Kitchen, she invites guests to experience something entirely different. There is just one seating per evening at this dinner party-style experience where about 20 guests are invited to join her in the kitchen for a tasting menu of elevated Chinese and Asian cuisine. Before long, the mood is convivial as guests chat over dishes like a trio of dumplings with animal shapes and exquisite fillings such as steamed lobster, turmeric-tinted beef, and crawfish with XO sauce. Pan-seared pork belly is beautifully presented wrapped in a lettuce leaf and tied with a chive, while a slice of duck topped with foie gras and caviar, sided by a bao bun featuring an animal cutout, is both whimsical and luxurious.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9174;Birrieria y Taqueria Cortez;USA;Fort Worth;2220 E. Rosedale St., Fort Worth, 76105, USA;32.7310553;-97.2976601;86;false;false;Mexican;Rogelio Cortez Jr. first earned a steady following with a food truck before opening this brick-and-mortar location where music keeps things lively, and the vibe is casual and inviting. The name says it all, as their specialty lies in their wonderfully tender and flavorful birria. It's not just the highlight—it's the only protein offered—but it's served in a number of tempting ways from tacos and flautas to tortas, burritos, and quesadillas. Order their corn tortilla tacos, stuffed with a generous amount of birria and accompanied by onion, cilantro, and lime, or choose their quesatacos, or two corn tortillas filled with mozzarella cheese and birria meat that is crisped at the edges.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9176;La Condesa;USA;Austin;400 W. 2nd St., Austin, 78701, USA;30.26527;-97.74768;72;false;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Blending industrial design accents with soft lighting, this spot has a chic, modern ambience that's just right for bringing people together. La Condesa honors and celebrates the cuisine of Mexico with a particular focus on Mexico City. Seafood enthusiasts can expect a menu featuring the freshest ceviche or tiradito alongside an eye-catching grilled whole fish. Savor the tangy, delicious flavor of silky raw tuna atop a super crisp tortilla with aji amarillo. Sided by creamy cubes of avocado and salsa macha, it's a refreshing way to begin a meal here. Huarache de huitlacoche is a well-known dish prepared with care, and nothing completes the meal quite like cinnamon-dusted churros.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
9177;Little Em’s Oyster Bar;USA;San Antonio;1024 S. Alamo St., San Antonio, 78210, USA;29.4138865;-98.4911541;16;true;false;Seafood, American;From its white facade with striped awning and pink window trim to its dusty rose stools, Little Em's Oyster Bar is downright darling, and the large, welcoming patio is a welcome refuge on nice days, but it's not just good looks that keep this place thrumming. Settle in, then order a plate of oysters with their signature blood orange mignonette. A lobster roll packed with prime, meaty pieces is matched by a heaping pile of shoestring fries with tarragon aioli. Enjoy a richly satisfying plate of linguine, glistening in a garlic-butter sauce and topped with plump, grilled shrimp. Wondering what to drink? A cold glass of rose champagne is not only refreshing—it's on theme.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9179;Crown Block;USA;Dallas;300 Reunion Blvd. E., Dallas, 75207, USA;32.7754264;-96.8088664;33;false;false;American Contemporary, Meats and Seafood;Set atop Reunion Tower, this large circular restaurant makes the most of its stunning views with floor-to-ceiling windows, and with a bit of luck you’ll be seated in the right area to see the sun set. To complement the sophisticated setting, a dress code means your fellow diners will be looking equally sharp. “Rare Steaks, Fine Seafood” is their tagline and the menu doesn’t disappoint—along with a healthy selection of sushi there’s plenty of produce from local farms. If you do go for one of their first-rate steaks don’t miss the excellent triple-cooked fries. The restaurant opened in its current guise in 2023 and proved an instant hit, so you need to book early, despite it seating over 200.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Valet parking;[]
9180;Mister Charles;USA;Dallas;3219 Knox St., Ste. 170, Dallas, 75205, USA;32.8234154;-96.7902462;56;true;false;Contemporary, American;The sweeping, opulent space sets the tone for an indulgent experience—this is a place where guests dress to impress and should expect an extravagant meal. The menu spans classic as well as contemporary luxury, blending French and Italian fare, from carpaccio to crab cakes to corn and truffle beignets. Diners can nibble on canapés like a lobster roll on a petite brioche bun, or sample fusilli with caviar and fontina, and might proceed to more substantial fare, including showy tableside presentations like Dover sole with lobster beurre blanc, or a Texas wagyu beef Wellington. Adroit service is combined with skillfully made cocktails and a substantial wine list, while the signature baked Alaska provides a dramatic grace note.;;[]
9181;Maie Day;USA;Austin;1603 S. Congress Ave., Austin, 78704, USA;30.2477795;-97.7501191;33;true;true;Steakhouse, American;Tucked inside the South Congress Hotel, this festive spot from Chef Michael Fojtasek of Olamaie is always hopping. The menu almost reads like a traditional steakhouse, but this place is anything but, with cooking that is inventive and heartfelt at once. Everything is shareable and seafood-focused starters are a good place to start. Tackle the pile of blue crab claws in a garlic-butter sauce so good you'll be sopping it up with bread. Meats stray from standard with selections like whiskey-brined pork chop and chicken fried steak with black pepper-dotted white gray. The sides are creative and seasonal with just a hint of nostalgia (we see you, blooming onion), but don’t overlook the sensational seasonal vegetables.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9184;Beau Boucot;France;Saint-Michel-Chef-Chef;119 boulevard de l'Océan, Saint-Michel-Chef-Chef, 44730, France;47.1682884;-2.1661524;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Facing the Grande Plage de Tharon, this bright seaside bistro is an offshoot of chef Mathieu Guibert's restaurant, Anne de Bretagne. You can get a taste of the sea, both in the dishes (some of which, such as the seafood platters, are for sharing) and in the surrounding scenery. Vegetarian and meat options are also served. The impeccable quality of the dishes benefits from the chef's network of suppliers. From the fried prawn amuse-bouche to the new take on vitello tonnato, and not forgetting the smoked trout, everything is on point. The service, provided by a young, smiling team, is the epitome of professionalism and friendliness. The wine list is full of surprises. Excellent value for money on the set menu. A good job well done.;;[]
9185;Ineffable;France;Barbentane;3 rue Grande, Barbentane, 13570, France;43.8991167;4.748067;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a small Provençal village with bags of character, Ineffable promises diners a feast for the senses. The restaurant is run by a couple with a passion for what they do: Nicolas Thomas and Marie Salomez (previously of La Promenade, La Flibuste, Château de Courban). This space with a decor of exposed stone walls and contemporary furnishings, and animated by a soundscape of soothing birdsong has just five tables. The chef riffs on poetic culinary leitmotifs, marrying olives and olive wood, plants and seafood (even meat on the larger set menu). A music lover, he has a sense for timing and harmony, as demonstrated by his composition of vegetables topped with a smoked cream.;Air conditioning;[]
9187;La Terrasse des Cigales;France;Mérindol;21 rue des Cigales, Mérindol, 84360, France;43.7564403;5.2037878;15;true;true;Provençal;Between the Durance River and the Sud Luberon, this modern restaurant lives up to its name with a lovely shaded terrasse enveloped by the sound of the cicadas (cigales)… plus, you get attentive, smiling service! Mathieu and Sébastien serve an appetising traditional Provence-inspired menu, as well as a daily special that is great value for money. The delicious dishes are carefully crafted with no messing around. The aim is to keep things simple, flavoursome and generous, while using selected regional ingredients: vegetables and olive oil from the village, lamb from the Alpilles, fish from the Bay of Cannes, beef from the Alpes-de-Haute-Provence. In winter, wood-fire cooking. A pleasant restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9188;Briemm;France;L'Houmeau;1 place du 14-Juillet, L'Houmeau, 17137, France;46.1934482;-1.1874379;29;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;"Briemm" is a contraction of Brice and Emmanuelle, who have partnered up (in business and in life) to found this charming little restaurant in a stone-built house. The chef's cooking is generous, and the lady of the house hosts cordially. The well-priced traditionally inspired menu features a mouthwatering list of dishes that showcase a real eye for detail and a fine bouquet of flavours, eg rabbit terrine with foie gras accompanied by an onion compote with mustard seeds and chilli, or squid with fregola sarda minestrone and chimichurri sauce. The best deal around here!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9190;Racines;France;Laval;99 rue du Pont-de-Mayenne, Laval, 53000, France;48.0691713;-0.7658418;91;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Clément Guyon has returned to his hometown after a culinary odyssey that took him around France (most notably Flocons de Sel in Megève) and abroad (Atelier Crenn in San Francisco). The timber of the façade and terrace tie in with the restaurant's pared-back interior decor. The menu varies depending on the time of day: at lunchtime, simple bistro-style cuisine draws in the business clientele and tourists. In the evening, there's more elaborate bistronomy cooking, featuring local and seasonal ingredients – served in a lively, friendly atmosphere.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9192;Le Bistrot du Chef;France;Manosque;180 avenue Régis-Ryckebusch, Manosque, 04100, France;43.8307812;5.7979837;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Pierre Grein (one MICHELIN star in his eponymous restaurant) has set up his bistro in the wine cellar and delicatessen part of the restaurant: the roomy and pleasant space is set apart and has a contemporary decor enhanced by shelves lined with fine wines and delicatessen wares (jars of conserves, salt, tea etc). The menu features a choice of dishes as well as a set menu without options. The chef's enthusiasm is palpable in his seasonal bistronomy creations, which are really well done and sit alongside the good old bistro classics: truffle croque monsieur, Carnaroli risotto inspired by the Creole dish rougail, steak tartare, or fillet of Charolais beef with chips and Béarnaise sauce. Thank you, Chef!;Air conditioning;[]
9194;Le Bistrot des Docks;France;Nice;2 rue Flaminius-Raiberti, Nice, 06000, France;43.7102812;7.2623764;24;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At a remove from the tourist trail, this unassuming gourmet bistro has opened its doors opposite the Docks de la Riviera covered market, in the area around the market (Marché de la Libération) and the Gare du Sud food hall. The local clientele, who delight in the cuisine of chef Nicolas Mendjisky, have given it their seal of approval. Presented on a blackboard, his mouth-watering short menu showcases fresh, local ingredients. Dishes such as market vegetables on crostini or sea bass with lemon butter embody refined yet generous cuisine that draws on seasonal Mediterranean flavours. The chef's partner, Sofia, provides smiling service and a warm welcome. Concise wine list.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9195;L'Auberge des Arcades;France;Castelnau-de-Montmiral;Place des Arcades, Castelnau-de-Montmiral, 81140, France;43.9656875;1.8200094;42;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Already chef at Vigne en Foule in Gaillac, Julien Bourdariès has opened a new place in a delightful brick and half-timbered house on the emblematic Place des Arcades in this medieval village. For lunch, the lively Auberge (open from morning to evening) proposes an amazing set menu at a bargain price, a choice of starters for sharing (charcuterie from the Tarn, pig's trotter croquettes etc) and dishes such as duck confit or veal fillet cooked in the open fire oven. Savvy selection of regional wines.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9197;La Fontaine - L’Artiste et le Cuisinier;France;Cliousclat;Le village, Cliousclat, 26270, France;44.7161;4.83648;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in a charming village, tucked away in a narrow street, this trendy bistro is accommodated in an attractive old house adopted by a well-travelled couple… They – she is the "artiste" and he the "cuisinier" (or cook) – invite us to sample their contemporary bistronomy cuisine in a friendly, pleasant setting. Following the seasons, their menu draws its bold flavours from the produce of local suppliers. On the restaurant floor, the service is efficient and the wine list is well explained. The bill is absolutely fair, and the cheerful terrace is a real bonus!;Terrace;[]
9200;Burnel;France;Rouvres-en-Xaintois;22 rue Jeanne-d'Arc, Rouvres-en-Xaintois, 88500, France;48.3111097;6.0317932;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Right in the middle of a rural village on the Plaine des Vosges, not far from the spa towns, this hotel-restaurant has been run by the same family since 1919. Hungry travellers make a beeline for this large, brightly coloured establishment with an exposed timber ceiling – once the village washhouse. Chef Maye Cissoko confidently and meticulously rustles up classic seasonal cuisine, in the form of two set menus, in which the finest ingredients enjoy the limelight. A case in point is the line-caught meagre pan-fried in hazelnut butter, served with petits pois à la française, marinière sauce or, for dessert, the burlat cherries jubilee, infused with verbena, lemon chiboust and cherry sorbet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9203;La Table des Matrus;France;Saint-Etienne;26 rue du Grand-Gonnet, Saint-Etienne, 42000, France;45.4429605;4.3831793;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Youth, enthusiasm and creativity: chef Matéo Ravel is a veritable ball of energy, a matru – "kid" in the Saint-Étienne dialect – who is still only in his early 20s. Here in his trendy bistro with an open kitchen and exposed pipes, he nurtures a network of small-scale producers and natural winegrowers in the Loire. Some of his passion for the trade is also dedicated to making items from scratch: fermented drinks made with indigenous yeasts (beers, kefir, lemonades), sourdough bread, salted bacon matured lardo di Colonnata-style with pork from the Cantal region… And as for his dishes, they are packed with flavour: eg aubergine tarte Tatin, moules-frites and mayonnaise with a twist.;Terrace;[]
9204;Donevandro;Italy;Popoli;via Garibaldi 2, Popoli, 65026, Italy;42.1744979;13.8329115;78;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Up until a few years ago, the owner-chef at this restaurant was working as a painter – a fact that is evident from the artistic touch in his cuisine. His recipes are modern and personalised, with careful attention naturally paid to harmonious presentation, while the flavour of his dishes is brought out by ingredients that are skilfully chosen from the Abruzzo inland area. In 2024, the restaurant moved to new, centrally located premises which have an intimate feel and are elegant and minimalist in style.;Air conditioning;[]
9205;Ape Vino e Cucina;Italy;Alba;Piazza Risorgimento 3, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.7005845;8.0361169;25;false;true;Piedmontese, Contemporary;This attractive restaurant in the heart of Alba, the gastronomic capital of the Langhe, is home to chef Damiano Nigro who has previous experience in Michelin-starred restaurants in the area. The restaurant serves aperitif snacks, tapas and top-quality cocktails alongside its delicious, generously portioned meals which, as you might expect in Piedmont, have a traditional flavour. The pasta, bread, desserts and ice-cream are all homemade, while on our last visit in the summer we particularly enjoyed the maccheroncini with scampi and peppers, and the exquisite Fassona beef with a red-wine sauce and seasonal vegetables. Booked ahead is recommended.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9206;Da Bob Cook Fish;Italy;Sorrento;largo Parsano vecchio 16, Sorrento, 80067, Italy;40.6237252;14.3705831;21;false;false;Seafood;Working in partnership with the nearby fishmongers which supplies it with fresh fish and seafood, this restaurant occupies a building once used for storing oranges that dates back 400 years. Although there is a menu, given the restaurant’s close relationship with the fishmongers we recommend asking the serving staff about the catch of the day and taking a look in the glass cabinet where the fish are displayed. Dishes are classic and traditional, allowing the full flavour of the fresh fish to shine through.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9207;DA_MÓ;Italy;Matera;Via Bruno Buozzi 20, Matera, 75100, Italy;40.6624784;16.6113483;63;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;This new, restored restaurant in the upper part of the Sassi (yet still near the centre of Matera and its car parks) has a warm friendly ambience and boasts a small, charming outdoor space. Here, an entire family (father in the kitchen, mother and daughter front of house), who moved to Matera from Venosa (home of the Latin poet Horatio), serves regional cuisine with a contemporary twist and no little skill and professionalism. Various tasting menus are available, as well as an à la carte. An interesting wine list completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9208;Sa Domu Sarda;Italy;Cagliari;via Sassari 51, Cagliari, 09124, Italy;39.2169379;9.1106285;53;true;false;Sardinian;Despite being an island, Sardinia’s traditional cuisine tends to focus on meat dishes, and you’ll find some of its best-known specialities served at this restaurant, with its simple dining rooms and typical local décor. Enjoy evocatively named dishes such as “sitzigorrus cun bagna” (snails in a tomato sauce), Bue Rosso “bombas” (meat balls), delicious Sardinian pastas such as “malloreddus”, “culurgiones” and “fregula”, stews, casseroles and meat fillets, as well as the famous “sebadas” and “su pappai biancu” (a type of blancmange) desserts.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9209;Charleston;Italy;Palermo;via Generale Magliocco 19, Palermo, 90141, Italy;38.1215951;13.3569428;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Before it became famous in Mondello, the renowned Charleston started out here in the centre of Palermo – and it has now returned to its origins, occupying the former Mazzara bar, itself once a favourite with locals. The ground floor is home to a café, cocktail bar and bistro, while the contemporary, Sicilian-style restaurant with an elegant summer terrace occupies the first floor (lift available). Here, young chef Gaetano Verde demonstrates all the skills acquired during his time working at renowned restaurants elsewhere in Italy and further afield. His dishes are clear and precise and often prepared using only three main ingredients – a good example is his grilled beef dish which is served with fermented grapes and sesame cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9210;Alessandro Feo;Italy;Marina di Casal Velino;via Angelo Lista 24, Marina di Casal Velino, 84040, Italy;40.1769364;15.121255;80;true;false;Campanian, Seafood;In a beautiful stone-vaulted building (an old 17C monastery) on the town’s seafront promenade, young owner-chef Alessandro Feo has made his mark in this region that perhaps has fewer gourmet restaurants than many places elsewhere. Here, he creates dishes that combine traditional influences and classic favourites from Campania with his own individual flair and creativity. His focus is on local, seasonal ingredients, including produce from his two kitchen gardens and fish sourced from local fishermen as well as from his own ventures out to sea.;;[]
9211;Dama;Italy;Cervesina;Via Mulino, località San Gaudenzio, Cervesina, 27050, Italy;45.0476388;9.0062926;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated just a few kilometres from Voghera in the Bassa Lomellina area, this gourmet restaurant run by a young chef occupies the old stables of the Castello di San Gaudenzio. Alongside local specialities such as baked onion and 24-month-old Grana Padano cheese, the menu also features more creative dishes based around authentic recipes. The wine list includes some particularly interesting labels from the Oltrepò region.;Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
9212;Il Ristorante Alain Ducasse Napoli;Italy;Naples;Via Cristoforo Colombo 45, Naples, 80133, Italy;40.840277;14.2555922;28;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Alain Ducasse, one of the great names in contemporary fine dining, has arrived in Naples, opening this restaurant in the former premises of the prestigious Ristorante Il Comandante. Situated on the 9th floor of the Romeo hotel overlooking the port, the restaurant boasts fine views of Vesuvius and the Bay of Naples, especially at sunset when the colours are truly spectacular. Meanwhile, the modern dining room, decorated completely in black, is equally as stunning as its surroundings. Alessandro Lucassino, who was born in 1991 and has years of experience working with his mentor, adds a personal flavour to local recipes: by using short cooking times, he preserves the nutritious qualities and flavours of local fish and vegetables while remaining faithful to Ducasse’s “cuisine de la naturalité” philosophy.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
9213;Palazzo Utini;Italy;Noceto;via Antonio Gramsci 6, Noceto, 43015, Italy;44.8087145;10.1788721;30;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;This historic building in the town centre has been brought back to life by the family of local entrepreneurs who bought it years ago and who have given the restaurant their name. Now an exclusive food venue just a stone’s throw from the capital of the “Food Valley” region, Palazzo Utini is home to a bar and bistro on its ground floor, while the first floor is occupied by the gourmet restaurant overseen by chef Enrico Bartolini and run by resident chef Roberto Monopoli who has plenty of culinary experience behind him. Guests can choose individual dishes from the tasting menus à la carte style, plus there’s an extensive wine list. We particularly enjoyed the exquisite turbot saltimbocca and the onion, black cherry and Lambrusco dessert. On the upper floors, elegant and intimate guestrooms are decorated in the same reassuring style as the rest of the building.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9214;Soul & Fish;Italy;Sorrento;via Marina Grande, Sorrento, 80067, Italy;40.6278681;14.3644213;26;false;false;Seafood;From the centre of Sorrento, you follow a succession of roads downhill to Marina Grande, the town’s old, picturesque fishing village that is well worth a visit. Here, facing the water, you’ll find Soul & Fish, a seemingly traditional seaside restaurant that actually serves superb fish and seafood on a menu that combines traditional dishes with more creative options.;Terrace;[]
9215;Etra;Italy;Genoa;piazza De Ferrari 4, Genoa, 16121, Italy;44.4081985;8.9341693;34;false;true;Creative, Italian Contemporary;Etra is an anagram of the Italian word “arte” – an apt name for this restaurant, which is housed in Palazzo Doria De Fornari on the beautiful and famous Piazza Ferrari. This palazzo is one of Genova’s magnificent “Rolli” palazzi (noble palaces once used to house famous visitors to the city). Despite the setting, the dining room is modern in style and adorned with elegant works of contemporary art. Here, chef Davide Cannavino consolidates his reputation with a concise menu of creative dishes: around a dozen meat and fish options inspired by the beauty that surrounds him and showcased on two tasting menus from which individual dishes can be chosen à la carte style.;Air conditioning;[]
9216;20Tre;Italy;Genoa;via David Chiossone 20 r, Genoa, 16123, Italy;44.4087805;8.9331148;44;false;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Run by three partners, this contemporary-style restaurant is situated in the heart of Genova’s historic centre. The cuisine here is prepared using the best seasonal ingredients, all presented in an array of modern dishes. Meat and fish feature on the menu, with a focus on regional recipes and the occasional Asian twist (for example, the amberjack and ponzu bonbon).;Air conditioning;[]
9217;Ménage;Italy;Catania;Via Euplio Reina 13, Catania, 95121, Italy;37.5040814;15.088074;99;false;false;Sicilian, Contemporary;Situated in the heart of the city near the Teatro Bellini and Piazza Università, this restaurant occupies an Art Nouveau-style building. Here, a trio of experienced young chefs from Catania have brought new life to the old “Da Turi Finocchiaro” restaurant, which has always been very popular with the city’s high society. Offering a small outdoor space near the entrance, the quiet, intimate dining room on the ground floor provides the backdrop for reinterpreted, contemporary Sicilian cuisine with an exclusive focus on meat (especially barbecued dishes which are the restaurant’s trademark), while the first floor is home to a cocktail bar run with passion by one of the partners. Two frescoes painted by Giuseppe Barone in 1930 add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9218;Procaccini;Italy;Milan;Via Giulio Cesare Procaccini 33, Milan, 20154, Italy;45.4837396;9.1708465;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Originally from Kosovo, talented chef Emin Haziri grew up in Italy and has plenty of professional culinary experience behind him. Here, he creates contemporary cuisine with a personal flavour, with raw seafood dishes such as oysters, caviar, Sicilian prawns and scampi available alongside his more imaginative options. In the elegant and stylish dining room with a harmonious colour scheme and fine furnishings, the open-view kitchen and marble chef’s table with velvet-covered stools really catch the eye. The restaurant also boasts a cocktail bar where guests can enjoy a drink and appetisers from the small tapas menu which is designed for sharing.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9219;Metodo;Italy;Marne;via Vittorio Emanuele 9, Marne, 24040, Italy;45.6223626;9.5583004;70;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;In the romantic setting of an 18C farmhouse, this restaurant has a rustic dining room enhanced by its elegant decor and furnishings, such as the solid maple tables and refined cutlery. The cuisine is showcased on two tasting menus (from which dishes can also be chosen individually) which are creative and occasionally very elaborate in style.;Air conditioning;[]
9220;Gimmy's;Italy;Aprica;via privata Gemelli, Aprica, 23031, Italy;46.1535475;10.1517783;77;true;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Traditional cuisine reinterpreted with a modern twist, with a whole page of the menu dedicated to meat dishes. Meals are served in an attractive Stube-style room with a warm mountain ambience.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9221;Locanda Perbellini - Ai Beati;Italy;Garda;via Val Mora 57, Garda, 37016, Italy;45.5861354;10.7174171;23;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated amid the foothills around Garda, this restaurant boasts fine views from its verdant terrace which take in much of the southern part of the lake, while its dining rooms occupy the interior of an old olive mill. The menu features freshwater fish such as pike and whitefish as well as seafood and meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9222;Salvo;Italy;Naples;Riviera di Chiaia 271, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8333521;14.2390896;23;true;true;Pizza;Situated opposite the Villa Comunale gardens, this restaurant serves some of the best pizzas in Naples (classic Neapolitan-style pizza which is soft and so big that it spills over the plate) as well as a selection of delicious appetisers, such as superb pasta fritters with various toppings. Welcoming ambience, with a more elegant feel than that of a typical pizzeria.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9223;Innesti;Italy;Pergine Valsugana;via San Pietro 8, Pergine Valsugana, 38057, Italy;46.062605;11.2442274;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Daniele and Elisa are a couple of young restaurateurs who are familiar to us from their time at Blumenstube in Sant'Orsola. Having moved on, they have now opened their own restaurant in Pergine, where both the decor and the cuisine are contemporary-Alpine in style. As in currently in vogue, their dishes are showcased on three tasting menus (short, medium and long) from which dishes can also be chosen à la carte style. All the recipes have a creative feel, demonstrating the chef’s playful approach to his contemporary ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9224;Osteria del Teatro;Italy;Cortona;via Maffei 2, Cortona, 52044, Italy;43.2758393;11.9857699;98;false;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;Enjoy traditional cuisine served in an elegant 16C dining room with a fireplace or in more informal trattoria-style rooms, all of which are decorated with the same theatrical theme. The recipes here focus on local traditions and seasonal ingredients, resulting in colourful, well-balanced and beautifully presented dishes that are full of flavour. There are just a few tables on the small terrace near the entrance overlooking the pedestrianised street, so if you want to sit outdoors make sure you book well in advance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9225;Anticofurlo;Italy;Acqualagna;via Furlo 60, Acqualagna, 61041, Italy;43.6384218;12.7132896;23;true;false;Cuisine from the Marches, Country cooking;Situated in the Gola del Furlo nature reserve, this restaurant is run by the talented and enthusiastic Alberto and Roberta, whose focus is on typical Marche specialities such as fresh pasta, cured hams, fine cheese and regional dishes full of intense flavours. The picturesque grotto carved into the rock is perfect for an aperitif, while the inn also offers charming guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9226;Lupaia;Italy;Torrita di Siena;Località Lupaia 74, Torrita di Siena, 53049, Italy;43.1135781;11.7501772;26;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Situated in a charming Tuscan hamlet nestled in the hills between Montepulciano and Montefollonico, this restaurant boasts stunning sunset views from its garden in the summer months, while guests in the dining room can enjoy views of the open kitchen in winter. The cuisine changes daily, with the chef offering a tasting menu based largely around produce from his own farm. The journey to get here is bucolic to say the least – an occasionally tortuous dirt track of more than 2km which requires careful driving! Booking ahead is essential if you’re not staying in the hotel.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9227;Joca;Italy;Naples;vico Sospiri 10/C, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8344895;14.2402287;83;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a modern, trendy setting, chef Gianluca D'Agostino prepares creative gourmet cuisine with the occasional Campanian influence. In addition to this, in a separate part of the restaurant, guests can choose from a selection of tapas-style dishes which, despite the name, are inspired by traditional Italian and regional classics and have little to do with Spain. The gourmet menu features successful dishes such as sweetbreads, fettuccine and cod, as well as pasta with peas. The main courses include meat and fish.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9228;Nobuya;Italy;Milan;Via San Nicolao 3/a, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.46655;9.17683;81;true;true;Japanese Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Nobuya boasts a minimalist elegance that is typical of Japanese restaurants, with brown tables, dark wooden beams on the ceiling, attractive subdued lighting, plus an illuminated wine cabinet to add a touch of colour. Here, the talented Japanese chef creates top-quality cuisine using the freshest ingredients. At lunchtime, there’s also a lighter “Bento box” and an omakase tasting menu (“Mi affido a te”) which is completely vegetarian.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
9229;Almondo Trattoria;Italy;Turin;piazza Gran Madre di Dio 2/l, Turin, 10131, Italy;45.0622509;7.6985608;53;true;false;Italian;This simple yet charming restaurant located just a few metres from the Gran Madre church serves a fine array of regional Italian dishes. Although specialities from Piedmont understandably take pride of place, the menu takes guests on a culinary journey throughout Italy and the changing seasons, featuring dishes such as scialatielli pasta with seafood, Puglian stuffed meat rolls, and zabaglione with traditional hazelnut cake from the Langhe. There’s also a good selection of gluten-free options.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9230;Truth Restaurant;Italy;Aversa;via Fratelli Cervi 18, Aversa, 81031, Italy;40.960971;14.2101034;25;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A contemporary-style restaurant with an open-view kitchen where two different styles of cuisine can be enjoyed: creative tapas influenced by different traditions, or more classic local dishes. The restaurant is particularly renowned for its choice of around a dozen imaginative small appetisers.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9231;Il Piraña;Italy;Prato;via G. Valentini 110, Prato, 59100, Italy;43.8678128;11.0966872;47;true;true;Seafood;A classic fish restaurant that opts for simply prepared dishes rather than fussy, inventive avant - garde cuisine. The perfect address for those in search of traditional fare.;Air conditioning;[]
9232;Abba;Italy;Milan;via Varesina 177, Milan, 20156, Italy;45.5035705;9.1383706;96;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;Situated in the Certosa district, this modern and minimalist-style restaurant boasts an open-view kitchen, where the chefs at work also serve and explain their dishes throughout the evening. The choice here is between two tasting menus, while at midday those with limited time can choose three individual courses from the menus, à la carte style. Whatever you choose, this is a restaurant that contributes new, interesting cuisine to the options available in Milan thanks to its creative, contemporary dishes. Excellent bread, plus definite hints of Puglia, chef Abbattista’s native region.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9233;Caruso Roof Garden;Italy;Naples;via Partenope 45, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8299478;14.248257;39;false;true;Campanian, Italian Contemporary;In a city that has its fair share of roof-garden eateries, this restaurant stands out as one of the most popular with fine panoramic views that take in the Castel dell'Ovo, Capri, the Sorrentine peninsula and Vesuvius... and, of course, the sea! Here, chef Emanuele Petrosino showcases the best of his cuisine on his tasting menus, which include “Suite 531” (dedicated to the legendary tenor Enrico Caruso), “Nel Blu”, “Per Mano” and “A Modo Mio”. If you’re choosing from the à la carte, we highly recommend the potato gnocchi with sea urchin, flavoured with Amalfi lemons and capers. Whatever you choose here, Campania’s fine produce takes centre stage, along with professional, attentive service and the beautiful Bay of Naples.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9234;Il Tartufo;Italy;Revere;via Guido Rossa 13, Revere, 46036, Italy;45.0468267;11.1275709;20;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Housed in a small villa in the residential area of the village, this intimate and secluded restaurant serves delicious cuisine with distinctly regional roots. In season, locally sourced truffles take centre stage, while fish and seafood dominate the menu at other times of year.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9235;Quintilio;Italy;Altare;via Gramsci 23, Altare, 17041, Italy;44.3327751;8.3468894;50;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;For over a century, and from generation to generation, Quintilio has acted as a junction between two beautiful regions, Liguria and Piedmont – and not just in a geographical sense. These regions take pride of place on the wine list (overseen by the friendly and talented owner Lorena) as well as on the menu, which is created daily with dishes made from top-quality local ingredients full of flavour. Regional specialities such as plin, Ligurian-style rabbit tortelli, risottos, vitello tonnato (veal) and brain are all skilfully reinterpreted with a modern twist by owner-chef Luca Bazzano.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9236;Il Credenziere;Italy;Annone Veneto;via Quattro Strade 12, Annone Veneto, 30020, Italy;45.7923516;12.6932484;61;true;false;Seafood;Situated in a small country hamlet, this restaurant is run by a chef from Puglia, whose origins can be glimpsed here and there in his dishes. The influence of the Veneto, where the chef has been working for some time, is also evident in the local dishes which appear alongside more creative options on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9237;Hostaria del Pavone;Italy;Vasto;via Barbarotta 15/17, Vasto, 66054, Italy;42.1124503;14.710181;26;true;false;Seafood, Farm to table;A small gem for fish enthusiasts, this delightful restaurant situated amid the alleyways of the historic centre (just 2 minutes’ walk away) boasts a quiet ambience with a white colour scheme and minimalist decor chosen by the exuberant owner. Although the menu focuses on fish and seafood (the raw fish dishes are superb), the pasta dishes and main courses are also excellent. To round off a delightful dining experience, the wine list includes some surprising top-quality labels. A must!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9238;Trattoria la Rosa 1908;Italy;Sant'Agostino;via del Bosco 2, ang. via Facchini, Sant'Agostino, 44047, Italy;44.7905538;11.380013;94;false;true;Country cooking;Situated on the outskirts of Ferrara, this reliable, classic-style restaurant now run by the fifth generation of the same family serves carefully prepared cuisine based around local ingredients. Highlights include truffles, sometimes served with fettuccine, butter and parmesan cheese, and the “sformato dell’Artusi” (a type of flan), served with a classic and intensely flavoured velouté.;Air conditioning;[]
9239;Frosch Restaurant;Italy;Varena;via Santi Pietro e Paolo 1, Varena, 38030, Italy;46.3021115;11.4565016;18;true;false;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;Situated in the centre of the small village of Varena (just outside the more famous Cavalese), this romantic and intimate restaurant with modern comforts and a mountain ambience is home to a talented female chef. Her contemporary recipes focus on local produce combined with Mediterranean flavours in some of the fish dishes and international ingredients such as foie gras.;;[]
9240;Exé Restaurant;Italy;Fiorano Modenese;via Circondariale San Francesco 2, Fiorano Modenese, 41042, Italy;44.5378933;10.824509;34;false;false;Italian, Italian Contemporary;This pleasant, elegant and contemporary-style restaurant on the ground floor of the Executive Spa Hotel boasts spacious dining rooms and an extensive menu ranging from traditional dishes to raw fish options, grilled meats (aged by the restaurant itself) and gourmet pizzas. The wine list features an impressive selection of labels, including by the glass, while the talented sommelier will delight wine-enthusiasts with his willingness to open almost any of the bottles in his cellar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9241;Carusu;Italy;Agrigento;passeggiata Archeologica 8, Agrigento, 92100, Italy;37.2983958;13.5908391;16;true;true;Creative;Situated on the road that crosses the archaeological park, this smart and elegant restaurant boasts two dining rooms arranged on two floors. In the kitchen, a young chef with plenty of previous experience working in renowned restaurants creates reinterpreted Sicilian dishes of the highest quality.;Air conditioning;[]
9242;Amo Bistrot;Italy;Verona;Vicoletto Due Mori 5, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4446546;10.9983826;87;true;true;Fusion;Traditional features such as exposed stone walls and wooden ceilings provide a pleasant contrast to the contemporary-style furnishings at this restaurant housed in the charming Palazzo Forti, while the attractive cloister with its old walls and soft lighting is highly recommended in the hot summer months. The cuisine combines traditional meat and fish dishes with Asian fare, including the option of sharing small dishes such as tapas or bao (steamed buns). There’s also an excellent brunch on Sundays.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9243;Evo Ristorante;Italy;Alberobello;via Giovanni XXIII 1, Alberobello, 70011, Italy;40.7875418;17.2350877;47;false;true;Creative;This restaurant at the entrance to the historic centre boasts a delightful garden which leads to a porch where tables are set out in summer – an enchanting setting that feels as though you’re eating in the countryside despite the village location. The chefs’ imagination knows no bounds in complex and elaborate dishes that focus on ingredients from Puglia and are grouped into themed tasting menus.;Garden or park;[]
9244;San Baylon;Italy;Rome;via di Ripetta 232, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9084995;12.4759096;87;false;true;Contemporary;Not far from Piazza del Popolo and Rome’s most exclusive shopping streets, this restaurant is situated in the Palazzo Ripetta hotel, in what was once the refectory of a 17C convent. Today, the ambience here is more informal, with an almost bistro-like feel, while the cuisine is inspired by classic Italian dishes, including various grilled options among the main courses. Meals are served in the palazzo’s inner courtyard in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9245;Locanda Toscano;Italy;Pizzo;via Benedetto Musolino 22, Pizzo, 89812, Italy;38.7359154;16.1603839;52;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;This attractive restaurant with delightful views seems to be perched on the cliff, whereas in fact it’s situated just a stone’s throw from the town’s main piazza and Murat castle. Although inspired by Calabria’s maritime traditions, the contemporary-style cuisine also includes a few meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
9246;L’Alchimia;Italy;Milan;viale Premuda 34, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.4657917;9.2074636;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;The parquet floor, wood-beamed ceiling and exposed brickwork lend a warm ambience to this restaurant, which is bright and airy during the day and romantic in the evening thanks to its soft lighting. With Giuseppe Postorino at the helm, the cuisine here includes classic recipes alongside more personalised dishes all prepared using top-quality ingredients that are typical of Italian cuisine. Additional features include a small, beautiful brick-vaulted wine cellar (open to visitors), plus an adjacent bar-bistro which serves quick lunches and excellent aperitifs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9247;Io e Luna;Italy;Guarene;località Montebello 1, Guarene, 14012, Italy;44.7450662;8.0147385;15;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;This classic-style restaurant serving updated regional cuisine offers views of the surrounding hills from its attractive outdoor terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9248;Il Giurista;Italy;Perugia;via Bartolo 30, Perugia, 06122, Italy;43.113269;12.38963;83;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant is named after Bartolo da Sassoferrato (as is the street on which it stands), a distinguished 14C jurist. From the street, you head down a few steps to the welcoming dining rooms with their historic ambience and brick-vaulted ceilings that keep the temperature pleasantly cool. The cuisine, which focuses exclusively on meat, is traditional and regional in flavour – an entire section of the menu is dedicated to black truffles in season. Friendly and attentive service.;;[]
9249;Bar à Fromage;Italy;Cogne;rue Grand Paradis 20, Cogne, 11012, Italy;45.6066147;7.3558181;93;true;true;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Classic Cuisine;A cosy, elegant Stube-style restaurant where the staff wear typical Aosta Valley costume and the menu features dishes with a particular focus on cheese (including an excellent fondue!) alongside traditional regional fare. Typical decor with refined, personalised furnishings and a profusion of wood.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9250;Da Cesare;Italy;Rome;via Crescenzio 13, Rome, 00193, Italy;41.9053961;12.467996;82;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;As the Florentine lily on the glass at the entrance implies, the specialities of this place are Tuscan in origin as well as seafood. Friendly atmosphere, ample wine list.;Air conditioning;[]
9251;Forte del 48;Italy;San Donà di Piave;Via Carlo Vizzotto 1, San Donà di Piave, 30027, Italy;45.630695;12.575539;62;false;false;Venetian, Country cooking;This pleasant restaurant started life in 1848 as a bastion used by the Habsburg army and was later transformed into an inn. Recognised as a “Locale Storico Veneto”, it’s now run by the third generation of the De Faveri family who serve traditional meat and fish dishes here. Comfortable guestrooms are also available for guests wishing to extend their stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9252;Bistrot 64;Italy;Rome;via Guglielmo Calderini 64, Rome, 00196, Italy;41.93046;12.466211;19;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The classic-style dining room in this restaurant situated in the Flaminio district belies the gourmet discoveries that await here, with echoes of traditions from Lazio that act as inspiration for creative, top-quality dishes with the occasional Asian twist.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9253;Lazaroun;Italy;Santarcangelo di Romagna;via Del Platano 21, Santarcangelo di Romagna, 47822, Italy;44.0640548;12.4443162;39;false;true;Cuisine from Romagna, Traditional Cuisine;The prototype of a typical Romagna restaurant, run by an efficient and friendly family team. Excellent choice of high - quality first and second courses, including fresh pasta, hams and salamis, meat options and grilled dishes. An interesting feature of the restaurant is the presence of ancient tufa caves in the basement. Created around 400 AD and part of an intricate network of underground passages, they were later used by the Malatesta family as an escape route and are now open to the public.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9254;Degusteria Italiana;Italy;Florence;via Lambertesca 7r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7686986;11.2547137;46;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This small, welcoming restaurant in the heart of the city, not far from the Uffizi Gallery, specialises in three typical Italian ingredients, namely cheese, truffles and game, from which it creates intriguing and delicious dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
9255;Cavallino;Italy;Tortona;corso Romita 83, Tortona, 15057, Italy;44.9005761;8.8663602;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Three talented young entrepreneurs who are passionate about good food have taken over this historic restaurant and have given it a new lease of life. The cuisine is contemporary and imaginative, with a firm focus on the region. Local cuisine is also to the fore in the simpler and more informal Trattoria da Ciccio.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9256;Il Giardino del Gusto;Italy;Ventimiglia;piazza XX Settembre 6/c, Ventimiglia, 18039, Italy;43.7922524;7.6085164;18;true;true;Creative;Although not on the seafront, this restaurant is well worth a visit thanks to its excellent owner - chef, who has had years of experience to perfect his French culinary techniques. Exciting tasting menus with dishes which can also be ordered à la carte.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9257;Derby Grill;Italy;Monza;viale Cesare Battisti 1, Monza, 20900, Italy;45.5927421;9.2713814;55;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated opposite the Villa Reale, this restaurant has the same classic, vaguely British ambience as the Hotel de la Ville in which it is situated, with tables also laid out on its elegant adjoining veranda. The menu features carefully prepared creative meat and fish dishes as well as traditional specialities from Lombardy, including risotto with Monza luganega sausage, ossobuco with gremolata parsley sauce and saffron rice, and an excellent costoletta alla Milanese (breaded veal).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9258;Foresta;Italy;Marina di Pisa;via Litoranea 2, Marina di Pisa, 56128, Italy;43.6591027;10.2798543;53;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Overlooking the Tyrrhenian Sea, all the tables at this restaurant offer sea views, whether you’re sitting in the winter dining room or on the outdoor summer terrace. The menu here focuses on top-quality fish dishes, which are classic in style, as is the background music and wine list, although the desserts have a more imaginative flavour.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9259;Taverna Rovita;Italy;Maratea;via Rovita 13, Maratea, 85046, Italy;39.9924293;15.7218212;62;true;true;Cuisine from Basilicata, Country cooking;Situated just a few metres from the main square of old Maratea, this tavern is a historic and typical restaurant with a kitchen area that dates from the 18C and a decor featuring Vietri ceramics. The chef delights in introducing guests to local recipes, such as the “polpo murato” (stewed octopus), one of the house specialities. The wine list boasts around 400 labels, with a particular focus on France and small-scale producers from Italy and further afield. Small groups (a maximum of 6 people) can choose to dine in the wine cellar surrounded by old bottles, many of which are collector’s items.;Air conditioning;[]
9260;Vitello d'Oro;Italy;Udine;via Erasmo Valvason 4, Udine, 33100, Italy;46.0638073;13.2326338;71;false;true;Seafood, Friulian;This restaurant boasts a new, even more beautiful look following its complete restoration in early 2019. However, one thing that has not changed is the excellent fish cuisine which has given the restaurant its fine reputation and drawn guests here since the mid 19C!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9261;Del Fagioli;Italy;Florence;corso Tintori 47 r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7675733;11.2595837;93;false;true;Tuscan;This historic Florentine trattoria now has a slightly new look, with the open-view kitchen visible as soon as you enter the restaurant. The friendly and welcoming ambience here makes it a popular choice, so booking ahead is highly recommended. Delicious, authentic cuisine is to the fore, including delicious Florentine steaks and other classic favourites.;Air conditioning;[]
9262;Mangiare Bere Uomo Donna;Italy;Suzzara;viale Zonta 19, Suzzara, 46029, Italy;44.993989;10.749578;81;true;true;Fusion, Regional Cuisine;She’s from Hong Kong, while he’s from Suzzara – together this couple run this welcoming restaurant where their international focus extends from the dishes which feature on the menu to the wine selection and the couple’s love for applied arts. Once seated, you can either choose traditional fare, including a few delicious fish dishes, or you can be tempted by the decidedly Asian options. Whatever you decide, one thing’s for sure – authenticity and seasonal, locally sourced ingredients are guaranteed.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9263;ES Cantina&Ristorante;Italy;Manduria;contrada Reni, Manduria, 74024, Italy;40.3759418;17.6711765;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated within the Gianfranco Fino wine estate, this tuff building houses a restaurant on its first floor with large picture windows that look out at the vineyards and a spacious terrace offering views of the surrounding countryside. Here, chef Simone Profeta from Naples serves modern meat and fish dishes, often cooked using wines from the estate, such as in the deliciously tender braised veal cheeks served with a full-bodied ES reduction. There’s also a vegetarian menu that features organic vegetables grown in the estate’s own kitchen garden. The wine list showcases the winery’s own labels of different vintages.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9264;Il Gusto di Xinge;Italy;Florence;Viale Belfiore 2, Florence, 50144, Italy;43.7789417;11.2410878;56;true;false;Asian Contemporary, Dim Sum;The dining room at this restaurant is decorated in brown tones reminiscent of a teapot, brightened here and there by dashes of blue and modern leather chairs. The Chinese chef serves cuisine from his native country (including dim sum), while also remaining open to influences from France and Italy. Inspired by the Chinese book of the same name, the Dream of Red Chambers dish (lychee-shaped balls filled with shrimp and melted cheese) is particularly recommended by our inspector.;Air conditioning;[]
9265;Farmacia dei Sani;Italy;Ruffano;piazza del Popolo 14, Ruffano, 73049, Italy;39.9854051;18.2476737;39;false;false;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;Occupying a corner of the central Piazza del Popolo in the delightful historic centre of Ruffano, this family restaurant (also a liqueur-maker) is surrounded by old palazzi which add to the charm of its setting. The Puglian cuisine served here has a modern twist while remaining unfussy in style and firmly anchored in the region. The service is quick, and each guest is greeted with a smile by the Rizzo family.;Terrace;[]
9266;Chicco di Grano;Italy;Castel Mella;viale dei Caduti del Lavoro 5, Castel Mella, 25030, Italy;45.4942256;10.1495251;45;true;true;Lombardian;This rustic, welcoming restaurant (two dining rooms with exposed beams) acts as the backdrop for traditional cuisine featuring meat and fish dishes alike, often cooked on the barbecue grill. The Fiorentina steaks and chops are well aged and cooked to perfection, resulting in extraordinary flavours that will satisfy even the most demanding of palates.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9267;Le Tre Colombe;Italy;Fornace;località Santo Stefano 22, Fornace, 38040, Italy;46.1300714;11.2141252;19;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This intimate and romantic restaurant occupies an old 18C rural house which is situated in a small hamlet in the Cembra valley. In two small dining rooms with a vaguely modern feel, the husband serves just one tasting menu, from which guests can choose two menus of different lengths, featuring delicious, well-presented, contemporary Italian cuisine prepared by his wife.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9268;Locanda Lo Scopiccio;Italy;Perignano;via delle Casine 5, Perignano, 56035, Italy;43.6010738;10.5803663;93;false;false;Tuscan, Creative;Run by the owner-chef and her husband, Locanda Lo Scopiccio is a charming restaurant where careful attention is paid to every detail so that guests feel totally pampered. The cuisine is regional with the occasional hint of creativity, with a choice of two surprise menus or à la carte dining. There’s also a winter garden with a bright yet romantic feel.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9269;Osteria Bertaina;Italy;Mondovì;piazza Maggiore 6, Mondovì, 12084, Italy;44.3887393;7.8299888;40;false;true;Piedmontese, Classic Cuisine;Overlooking the picturesque square in the town’s oldest medieval district and accessed through its arcaded portico, this restaurant boasts two dining rooms with an attractive nostalgic feel and ceilings decorated with early 20C frescoes. The excellent cuisine focuses on local dishes, accompanied by occasionally more creative options.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9270;La Passion;Italy;Vintl;via San Nicolò 5/b, Vandoies di Sopra, Vintl, 39030, Italy;46.8143348;11.7601154;58;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;A small, cosy, completely wood - panelled stube has been set up in this residential building. The menus are traditional but inventive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9271;Brezza fish and chill;Italy;Soverato;Via Marina 24, Soverato, 88068, Italy;38.690953;16.5465149;54;false;false;Seafood, Fish and Chips;An alternative eatery amid the Abruzzo dining options, situated on the beautiful seafront promenade at Soverato. The idea is simple: fish takes centre stage, served in rolls, on "broast" and “friselle” bread, as well as raw or fried, although generous salads and delicious desserts are also available. The ingredients, full of flavour and always simply prepared, result in copious and colourful dishes. Good quality wine is available by the glass, plus a fine choice of cocktails which is enhanced in the evening by the addition of creative home-made options. Friendly female staff, plus excellent background music. A pleasant address serving quality food at very reasonable prices!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9272;Vert Osteria Contemporanea;Italy;Caprino Veronese;Località Bogonza, Caprino Veronese, 37013, Italy;45.60776;10.809;82;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Housed in a rustic building on the green slopes facing the lake, this restaurant has a welcoming feel with its stone and wood decor and large windows looking out at a beautiful, shaded garden where meals are served in fine weather. Delicious Italian cuisine takes pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9273;Gallo Nero;Italy;Sienna;Via del Porrione 65/67, Sienna, 53100, Italy;43.3179114;11.3342758;72;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated on the edge of the Leocorno contrada (district) just a stone’s throw from the Piazza del Campo, this restaurant with medieval origins has a recently renovated, designer-style dining room with a modern feel. Marco Langella from Campania is at the helm in the kitchen, where he reinterprets local culinary traditions in a modern style with a careful focus on flavour. He also offers a special tasting menu featuring meat and fish dishes. We particularly enjoyed the duck with orange, bitters and Taggiasche olives, and (perhaps even more!) the creamy, delicious dessert made with blue Erborinato cheese, dates and French toast. The beautiful wine cellar can also be visited by guests.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9274;Lalibera;Italy;Alba;via Pertinace 24/a, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.6987609;8.0340111;33;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;A modern, designer-style restaurant staffed by a young and efficient front-of-house team. The cuisine showcases traditional Piedmontese recipes created with respect and enthusiasm, resulting in top-quality dishes, generous portions and an attention to detail in the presentation.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9275;Arca;Italy;San Benedetto del Tronto;viale Rinascimento 143, San Benedetto del Tronto, 63074, Italy;42.9264082;13.897645;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Cuisine from Abruzzo;After years of serving fine cuisine in Alba Adriatica, chef Massimiliano Capretta has moved around 15km away to the Hotel Smeraldo. Here, he pays careful attention to the use of organic produce, creating meat and fish dishes that are inspired by local traditions and prepared in a style that is a combination of classic and modern influences. Desserts remain in the capable hands of his sister Dalila, whose millefeuille is one of her standout dishes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9276;All’Ombra del Gabbiano;Italy;Mestre;via Caneve 2, Mestre, 30173, Italy;45.4960257;12.2442495;93;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Vegan;This friendly Mediterranean-style bistro started out 20 years ago as an inn-cum- -cicchetteria (a type of Venetian tapas bar). It now offers 100% gluten-free recipes, including a few vegan options, without compromising in any way on the quality or beautiful presentation of the dishes featured on its well-constructed menu. Friendly, attentive service and summer outdoor dining in the pedestrianised area add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9277;Attico sul Mare;Italy;Grottammare;piazza Kursaal 6, Grottammare, 63066, Italy;42.9914877;13.8709178;29;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Situated on the second and top floor (don’t worry, there’s a lift!) of the historic Kursaal building, this panoramic penthouse-style restaurant has recently been given a new contemporary design after nearly 20 years in business. The same modern feel is evident in the cuisine, which focuses (but not exclusively) on fish and seafood on its inviting menu. Classic local recipes such as seafood salad (with ingredients skilfully cooked in front of guests in the dining room) feature alongside the chef’s more creative options, such as turbot, in which nearly all parts of the fish are served – fillets, cheeks and even the “crackling”. For dessert, we recommend the alkermes cake with Italian pastry cream and chocolate, which is finished directly in front of guests in the dining room.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9278;Alle Ciaspole;Italy;Fondo;località Plazze 4, frazione Tret, Fondo, 38013, Italy;46.479834;11.1428226;46;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The name of this excellent hotel-restaurant on the border with the Alto Adige region is a clear reference to the snowshoes used in winter excursions in Tret, as well as to the local traditions which inspire the cuisine created here by the owner-chef. Precise, classic cooking methods plus the use of locally sourced produce (with the exception of the fish dishes which also feature on the menu) are showcased in the cuisine, with dishes announced by the chef’s wife at your table in the unexpectedly elegant Alpine-style dining room.;Car park;[]
9279;Il Saturnino;Italy;Forio;via Soprascaro 17, Forio, 80075, Italy;40.7378863;13.8574114;17;true;true;Seafood;It was a love story between an American and a local girl from Forio that led, in 1949, to the opening of this restaurant overlooking the port, with its attractive veranda boasting fine sea views. The current management team have made this one of the most interesting restaurants in the region for anyone keen to sample traditional cuisine from Ischia and Campania. Don’t miss the pasta served with local (and very rare) zampognaro beans, mussels and squid, or the Ischian-style rabbit presented in an attractive terracotta dish. A good choice of fish dishes is also available.;Great view,Terrace;[]
9280;N'uovo Vino e Cucina;Italy;Sutri;S.S. Cassia 46,700, Sutri, 01015, Italy;42.2307606;12.258055;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated within the elegant Antico Borgo di Sutri resort in the heart of the verdant countryside around Viterbo, this restaurant boasts an intimate and contemporary ambience, with soft lighting and large picture windows offering views of the surrounding greenery. Here, young, talented chef Simone Lezzereni serves regionally influenced cuisine, including reinterpreted traditional recipes with a focus on top-quality local ingredients and modern techniques.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9281;Artifex;Italy;Brennero;Via Fleres 185, Brennero, 39041, Italy;46.9646182;11.3458131;31;false;true;Contemporary, Creative;This restaurant is situated within the Feuerstein Nature Family Resort, a 5-star property which continues to expand and which nestles in the verdant Val di Fleres, not far from Vipiteno and even closer to the Austrian border. In the small, elegant dining room here, chef Tina Marcelli serves two tasting menus and a selection of desserts, all prepared with a passion that was inspired by the example set by her grandmother, who successfully raised and fed eight children. Dishes are often accompanied by drinks made from fermented fruit and herbs, most of which are sourced from the property’s own kitchen garden where they are grown without the use of any chemicals. Imagination, creativity and respect for seasonal ingredients are the main characteristics of the cuisine, which is prepared and served by an all-female team, ably supported by a young male sommelier. We particularly enjoyed the saddle of farmed venison with scorzonera and cherries, as well as the many sweet treats served after coffee.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
9282;Su Murruai;Italy;Riola Sardo;via Giuseppe Garibaldi 36, Riola Sardo, 09070, Italy;39.9963989;8.5395594;43;false;true;Contemporary;Situated in a small village looking out towards the Sinis peninsula, this restaurant occupies an old mill and is named after the aroma of aged Vernaccia wine (“su murrua” in Sardinian). The cuisine is contemporary yet influenced by traditional recipes and offers some of the best quality in the region. Young chef Ivan Matarese takes traditional ingredients and recipes and reinterprets these to create more modern dishes. Fish from Oristano bay and meat from inland areas take centre stage on the menu, including mutton in a delicious “pintadera” (open ravioli with saffron and liquorice). The chef also adds the occasional influence from Campania, his native region.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9284;Agriturismo Ferdy;Italy;Lenna;Località Fienili, fraz. Scalvino, Lenna, 24010, Italy;45.9246206;9.669272;45;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Alpine;Once you’ve left your car in the car park and crossed the Brembo river, you enter a fairytale setting of meadows and horses surrounded by the Orobic peaks. Here, the cuisine is a declaration of love for the mountains – although occasionally technical and complex, it is always rounded and full of flavour, with meat and dairy produce taking centre stage. Guestrooms and a shop selling typical local produce complete the picture at what is an extraordinary, high-end agriturismo.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9285;Il Mirto;Italy;Forio;via Provinciale Lacco, 284, Forio, 80075, Italy;40.7531204;13.8789992;46;false;false;Vegetarian, Modern Cuisine;When you arrive at the luxury Botania hotel, you’ll be accompanied through 3ha grounds of lush Mediterranean vegetation to the restaurant. You couldn’t have a better introduction to the cuisine that awaits at Il Mirto, where you can choose between two long tasting menus or a shorter four-course option featuring dishes from these menus. One of the menus is vegetarian, the other vegan and almost all the vegetables are sourced from the property’s own kitchen garden or from other local growers from Ischia. A delightful experience in a beautiful natural setting, with excellent service provided by young, friendly staff.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9286;La Locanda dei Narcisi;Italy;Pozzolo Formigaro;via Bettole 35, Pozzolo Formigaro, 15068, Italy;44.80856;8.82527;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Visitors come here for the fresh fish caught in the nearby Ligurian Sea, such as prawns in hazelnut tempura with grapefruit granita and raw fish dishes served with delicious risotto from the Upper Langhe region, as well as meat dishes that include Fassona beef and agnolotti pasta. The cakes and pastries are also well worth a mention, as is the bread which is also available for purchase. In summer, the dining room is supplemented by outdoor tables which offer a pleasant alfresco dining experience.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9287;Hosteria La Cave Cantù;Italy;Casteggio;via Circonvallazione Cantù 62, Casteggio, 27045, Italy;45.012931;9.1267958;86;false;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Situated within the 18C Cantù monastery, now also home to a museum and library, this modern restaurant with a friendly ambience in its dining rooms and wine cellar also boasts an attractive outdoor space and a convenient car park. The menu features personalised cuisine with the occasional exotic influence prepared by the owner-chef (his wife, who works front of house and oversees the excellent wine list, is from Ecuador). The result is colourful, generous and beautifully presented cuisine which is full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9288;Quattro Gigli;Italy;Montopoli in Val d'Arno;piazza Michele da Montopoli 2, Montopoli in Val d'Arno, 56020, Italy;43.6701439;10.760764;28;false;true;Tuscan, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant occupying a 15C palazzo in the centre of a charming village has a warm and welcoming feel. Here, the chef delights his guests with regional meat and fish specialities, which are served in original ceramic dishes. The restaurant also offers a few guestrooms, the best of which boast panoramic views, as does the outdoor terrace used for summer dining.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9289;Alla Lanterna;Italy;Fano;SS Adriatica Sud 78, Fano, 61032, Italy;43.8187502;13.0702106;57;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Despite its not particularly romantic location alongside the road, this restaurant attracts a loyal following who come here for the excellent fish cuisine. Guestrooms are also available for those wishing to prolong their stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9290;Soltojo;Italy;Caiolo;via Caiolo Alto 45, Caiolo, 23010, Italy;46.1490975;9.8147893;82;false;true;Fusion, Creative;Housed in an old wood- and stone-built mill, this restaurant boasts an elegant, romantic and stylish dining room with large windows offering views of a stream surrounded by greenery. Here, the talented chef creates personalised cuisine with a focus on modern fish and meat dishes that include the occasional hint of Asian influence.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9291;Casa Coppelle;Italy;Rome;piazza delle Coppelle 49, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9007751;12.4758761;52;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the city, this delightfully intimate restaurant offers a number of different dining rooms, from a ‘gallery of portraits’ to the British-style library rooms and the ‘herbier’ with prints on the walls. There is something for everyone here, although every guest will enjoy the same modern reinterpretations of Mediterranean cuisine.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9292;Retrogusto;Italy;Otranto;via Tenente Eula 7, Otranto, 73028, Italy;40.147266;18.487043;81;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Although this restaurant is slightly set back from the seafront, the high quality cuisine focusing on the flavours of the Salento makes the short walk well worthwhile. A classic ambience with simple yet tasteful furniture, soft background music and an informal atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9293;Corte Matilde;Italy;Pieve di Coriano;via Pelate 38, Pieve di Coriano, 46036, Italy;45.0261215;11.1206992;86;true;true;Mantuan, Classic Cuisine;The owners' professionalism and passion go hand in hand with a cuisine made with first - class products. The dishes are simply prepared but tasty, exalting the flavour of the ingredients. It is located in a pretty, refurbished farmhouse on the road that Matilda of Canossa once travelled on.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9294;Da Severino il Vecchio - Di Luciano;Italy;Senorbì;largo Abruzzi 2, ang. via Piemonte 23, Senorbì, 09040, Italy;39.526185;9.1334416;71;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This historic restaurant now has new premises with a classic yet modern feel. Mediterranean cuisine with a traditional and regional influence.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9295;La Veranda;Italy;Moltrasio;piazza San Rocco 5, Moltrasio, 22010, Italy;45.8601242;9.101444;15;false;true;Country cooking;Situated a few metres from the lake in the centre of the village, this welcoming and long-established family restaurant boasts a dining room that transforms into a veranda with outdoor dining in summer. The cuisine here is traditional, with generous portions of fish from the lake and sea.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9296;Walser Schtuba;Italy;Ponte;località Riale, Ponte, 28863, Italy;46.4227509;8.4164287;74;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;This delightful Alpine - style restaurant stands in the picturesque upper section of the Val Formazza. The menu features local specialities reinterpreted with a light, modern twist. Outdoor dining in summer.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9297;Amo;Italy;Venice;calle del Fontego dei Tedeschi, Ponte di Rialto, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.4382293;12.3369601;38;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated within the Fondaco dei Tedeschi, once a type of stock exchange where merchants from northern Europe traded with their Venetian counterparts and now a luxury shopping centre for those in search of high-end brands, Amo is the trendiest of the Alajmo group’s restaurants. Gourmet yet casual in style, the restaurant boasts an internal courtyard setting and lounge-style decor by Philippe Starck. The view of the Grand Canal and the rooftops of Venice from the top-floor terrace is stunning (booking is recommended although you may be lucky enough to get a table here when you arrive).;Air conditioning;[]
9299;Tuorlo;Italy;Turin;via Sant'Agostino 15/b, Turin, 10122, Italy;45.0750429;7.680135;83;false;false;Contemporary;Decorated in elegant bistro style and skilfully renovated with contemporary furnishings, Tuorlo serves dishes based on traditional Piedmontese recipes reinterpreted with modern techniques and personal touches. Good choice of wines, plus an attractive little courtyard to the rear for relaxed summer dining.;Air conditioning;[]
9300;Luca's by Paulo Airaudo;Italy;Florence;Via dei Cavalieri 2/c, Florence, 50123, Italy;43.7707;11.25406;96;true;false;Contemporary;Situated in the charming historic centre just behind the central market square, this new hotel is the flagship of a well-known family of Florentine entrepreneurs. On the first floor, a small dining room with a partially open kitchen provides the backdrop for fresh, modern cuisine which bears the signature of Paulo Airaudo, a talented chef from Argentina. Options include a tasting menu (also available in a shorter version) and an à la carte. The wine selection features labels from around the world.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9301;Corte Federiciana;Italy;Apricena;corso Garibaldi 60, Apricena, 71011, Italy;41.7855025;15.4418528;69;true;true;Seafood;The dining room at this restaurant housed in the Palazzo Baronale’s old outbuildings in the historic centre of Apricena boasts an attractive brick-vaulted ceiling. The cuisine, which focuses mainly on fish and seafood (raw, cooked, baked in the oven or served with pasta), effortlessly combines traditional and modern flavours. A delightful welcome and friendly service complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9302;Alla Locanda;Italy;Canazei;strada Roma 23, Canazei, 38032, Italy;46.4764038;11.7672061;75;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;A colourful, contemporary-style restaurant within the Locanda degli Artisti Art Hotel, a new address that is striking for its large art collection displayed throughout its various rooms. The cuisine here focuses on seasonal ingredients which are used to create personalised and imaginative dishes showcased on tasting menus and an à la carte. Interesting wine list, with a special emphasis on labels from the Trentino-Alto Adige region.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9303;Le Beccherie;Italy;Treviso;piazza Giannino Ancilotto 9, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.666269;12.2468354;88;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of Treviso, this restaurant – once a stronghold of traditional cuisine – is now a splendid designer-style bistro. The most atmospheric tables are those by the canal, while the dishes themselves combine regional influence with a touch of fantasy. In addition to the à la carte, guests can choose from two tasting menus: the more creative Ti P'Orto al Mareand the Essenziale, perfect for anyone tasting this style of cuisine for the first time. Traditionalists will be pleased to hear that the famous tiramisù is still on the menu!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9304;Da Gelsomina;Italy;Anacapri;Via Migliara 72, Anacapri, 80071, Italy;40.5417666;14.2114125;70;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Access to this authentic family-run trattoria is either by foot or shuttle bus (phone ahead for the latter). Just a few metres from the restaurant, enjoy breathtaking views of the Parco dei Filosofi.;Great view,Terrace;[]
9305;SaleGrosso;Italy;Marciana Marina;piazza della Vittoria 14, Marciana Marina, 57033, Italy;42.8055611;10.2000785;57;true;true;Seafood;Situated in a corner of the charming little square in Marciana Marina, just a few minutes from Cotone, one of the oldest and most beautiful parts of the town. The restaurant serves Mediterranean dishes and specialities from Elba, all reinterpreted with an individual twist. Raw fish is one of the house specialities.;Air conditioning;[]
9306;Cestello Firenze;Italy;Florence;piazza di Cestello 8, Florence, 50124, Italy;43.770306;11.2436567;37;true;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Situated in the beautiful piazza overlooked by the old church of San Frediano in Cestello, this restaurant serves fish specialities in atmospheric rooms decorated in a range of styles. Cestello Ristoclub’s exacting guests can choose from the creative dishes on the menu or, if they prefer, head to the fish counter to make their selection, which is then prepared in more a traditional way by the chefs.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9307;Coltivare;Italy;La Morra;borgata Brandini 16, La Morra, 12064, Italy;44.6392382;7.9089221;51;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This small restaurant next to the Brandini winery has chef Luca Zecchin at its helm, a true connoisseur of Langhe culinary traditions and one of the more recent disciples of Lidia Alciati (known as the “queen” of Piedmontese cuisine). Nearly all the ingredients used here are sourced locally, some even from the property itself, such as eggs and vegetables from the kitchen garden. The dishes are divided between those which pay tribute to the traditions of the region (don’t miss the “plin”) and others which showcase the chef’s personal style, including a menu dedicated to the barbecue grill. The latter is even used in some of the sweets, such as the smoky-flavoured bread and chocolate dessert. The wine list demonstrates the same affection for Piedmont, as well as featuring a selection of champagnes. During the day, enjoy the splendid view through the picture windows that surround the dining room, which also boasts a large fireplace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
9308;Il Cortiletto;Italy;Toscolano-Maderno;via F.lli Bianchi 1, Toscolano-Maderno, 25088, Italy;45.63496;10.60022;100;true;false;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;Standing on the Lake Garda road, this small, simple, yet far from ordinary restaurant serves Mediterranean dishes with the occasional inventive twist. Two words of advice – opt for alfresco dining in fine weather, and don’t miss the maccheroncini served with perch and lemon pesto sauce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9309;Vineria Derthona;Italy;Tortona;via Lorenzo Perosi 15, Tortona, 15057, Italy;44.8984572;8.8655131;71;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the heart of town, this secluded, busy and welcoming wine bar serves delicious Piedmontese dishes and a good selection of wines by the glass, chosen from the well-stocked wine cellar on a daily basis. House specialities include braised beef in a Barbera Colli Tortonesi sauce and gianduia chocolate semifreddo with mascarpone cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9310;Sabir;Italy;Zafferana Etnea;via delle Ginestre 1, Zafferana Etnea, 95019, Italy;37.6863972;15.1035324;98;true;false;Creative;Colourful Mediterranean cuisine with the occasional creative twist, yet always based on local specialities. This attractive restaurant takes its name from an old dialect once in use in the ports of the Mediterranean – a sort of Esperanto for sea merchants. In summer, ask for one of the tables in the cool and romantic garden.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9311;Wine & Dine;Italy;Canazei;strèdà Roma 5, Canazei, 38032, Italy;46.4764246;11.7701224;57;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Popular with locals, this restaurant has the typical atmosphere of a traditional Alpine hut with its old wood furnishings and romantic corners. Surrounded by high mountain peaks, the restaurant focuses on creative cuisine, including a few fish specialities.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
9312;L'Officina;Italy;Perugia;Borgo XX Giugno 56, Perugia, 06121, Italy;43.1036139;12.3938137;16;true;false;Creative;Tradition and a cosmopolitan spirit combine in this highly original and exciting restaurant which has stepped off the usual gastronomic bandwagon in spectacular fashion! It’s not by chance that L’Officina describes itself as a “cultural restaurant”.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9313;Colline Emiliane;Italy;Rome;via degli Avignonesi 22, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9030135;12.4874484;23;false;false;Emilian, Classic Cuisine;Just a stone’s throw from Piazza Barberini, this simple, friendly, family-run restaurant has just a few tables arranged close together. It serves typical dishes from the Emilia region, including fresh pasta stretched by hand in the traditional way.;Air conditioning;[]
9314;Ai Torchi;Italy;Finalborgo;via dell'Annunziata 12, Finalborgo, 17024, Italy;44.1753615;8.3275775;54;false;true;Seafood, Ligurian;Occupying a 17C olive oil press in the heart of a charming medieval village, this restaurant has retained its old stone mill and wooden press in its vaulted dining room, which provides the backdrop for imaginative fish and seafood dishes prepared using top-quality local ingredients. The delicious Italian-style ceviche is made from the catch of the day, while the Mare Mare mixed fish dish is baked in a casserole with cherry tomatoes, courgettes and bay leaves. If you’re looking for a simpler option, try the I Torchiettibistro on the corner of the same street.;;[]
9315;Extra;Italy;Carrara;viale Turigliano 13, Carrara, 54033, Italy;44.052647;10.069568;31;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated slightly inland behind Marina di Carrara, Extra (the name refers to the quality of the region’s world-famous marble) is a bright, modern restaurant with a menu inspired by the area’s fish and seafood culinary traditions. The menu is slightly more elaborate and the ambience more elegant in the evening and on Saturday lunchtimes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9316;Kisté - Easy Gourmet;Italy;Taormina;via Santa Maria de' Greci 2, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.850777;15.283031;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in the 15C Casa Cipolla, with a romantic terrace for summer dining, Kistè is a treasure trove of gourmet Sicilian cuisine prepared in contemporary style.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9317;Trattoria Via Vai;Italy;Bolzone;via Libertà 18, Bolzone, 26010, Italy;45.3321006;9.6612651;98;true;true;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;Although the original chef has now left, the cuisine remains unchanged with a concise menu of regional specialities and a focus on meat dishes. Poultry takes pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9318;Osteria del Trentino - Da Marco;Italy;Piacenza;via del Castello 71, Piacenza, 29121, Italy;45.052834;9.6851448;30;false;false;Emilian;The name of this historic restaurant alludes to the origins of one of its first owners. The restaurant now serves international dishes such as Tournedos Rossini and Beef Wellington, alongside specialities from Piacenza. There’s an extensive choice of stuffed pasta, which is home-made, as are the ice-creams and sorbets.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9319;Mamma Rosa;Italy;San Polo d'Enza;via XXIV Maggio 1, San Polo d'Enza, 42020, Italy;44.6278667;10.4174269;48;false;true;Seafood;Although from the outside this restaurant looks to be no more than a group of houses on the outskirts of the village, all the effort here focuses on creating fish and seafood dishes made from the best quality fish. Prepared in Mediterranean - style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9320;Osteria del Benedet;Italy;Delebio;via Roma 2, Delebio, 23014, Italy;46.1375374;9.46318;19;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Once an old inn, this family-run restaurant now occupies two floors with the wine bar on the ground floor and the dining rooms above. Inspired by traditional cuisine the dishes here are reinterpreted in modern style with plenty of character. The excellent wine list makes this a good choice for wine aficionados.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9321;Cavallini;Italy;San Severino Marche;viale Bigioli 47, San Severino Marche, 62027, Italy;43.2297161;13.1766876;79;true;true;Seafood, Cuisine from the Marches;A restaurant with light and relaxing tones, run by two brothers, one in the kitchen and the other in charge of the front of house, who continue the family tradition in these new premises. Mostly fish, the chef's true passion, but the menu also offers valid meat alternatives.;Air conditioning;[]
9322;Lucenti;Italy;Montefiorino;via Mazzini 38, Montefiorino, 41045, Italy;44.3579699;10.621784;37;false;false;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;This small, family - run restaurant furnished in warm, pastel shades offers a traditional setting in which to enjoy local cuisine. The dishes served in the younger, more informal Enoteca are even simpler and more traditional in style.;Great view;[]
9323;L'Ottava Nota;Italy;Palermo;via Butera 55, Palermo, 90133, Italy;38.11774;13.371684;26;true;true;Sicilian, Creative;This is one of those bright, pretty and modern restaurants that are very much in fashion nowadays. The cuisine is strongly linked to the region with fish dishes to the fore presented in an attractive and contemporary style.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9324;Gibas;Italy;Pesaro;strada Panoramica Adriatica, Pesaro, 61121, Italy;43.9275954;12.877271;96;false;false;Seafood, Italian;This modern restaurant stands on the road that heads north from the town. It boasts panoramic views of the sea that can be enjoyed from the deck in summer. Contemporary - style fish dishes dominate the menu.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9325;Il Faggio;Italy;Pollone;via Oremo 54, Pollone, 13814, Italy;45.5823083;8.0055232;96;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An elegant dining room with large windows and classic decor provides the setting for modern Mediterranean meat and fish dishes. The wine list features a good selection of labels from the region and further afield.;Car park;[]
9326;Antiche Mura;Italy;Riva del Garda;via Bastione 19, Riva del Garda, 38066, Italy;45.886997;10.838588;77;true;true;Italian Contemporary;At Antiche Mura, savour contemporary cuisine that takes its inspiration and ingredients from both the land and sea, as well as the passing seasons. Situated behind the historic centre, the restaurant also offers an outdoor space for the summer months and ten simple yet comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9327;Aurora;Italy;Feltre;via Garibaldi 68, Feltre, 32032, Italy;46.015656;11.907839;18;false;true;Venetian, Modern Cuisine;Situated just a stone’s throw from the Concattedrale di San Pietro Apostolo, Aurora boasts a cheerful and contemporary-style dining room with colourful furnishings, soft lighting and plenty of wine bottles on display. The carefully prepared cuisine includes Italian and regional meat and fish specialities with a light, modern twist.;Air conditioning;[]
9328;Osteria dai Mazzeri;Italy;Follina;via Pallade 18, Follina, 31051, Italy;45.9546545;12.1195211;58;false;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;Once the town hall of Follina, this building dating from 1704 is now home to a restaurant run by two brothers who serve delicious regional and seasonal cuisine here (in winter, don’t miss the spit-roasted chicken, veal or pork cooked according to local tradition). A beautiful mulberry tree, the old symbol of the village that was once involved in the silk industry, graces the outdoor dining space.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9329;Enoteca L'Armadillo;Italy;Courmayeur;strada La Palud 27, Courmayeur, 11013, Italy;45.8183201;6.9646826;54;true;true;Fusion, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the district of Palaud at the foot of Mont Blanc, this small wine bar with a tranquil ambience serves interesting cuisine prepared by a talented Japanese chef who adds his own personal twist to the valley’s top-quality ingredients. Dishes include a delicate tempura served with tongue or beef, plus some exquisite desserts, while wine is chosen directly from the shelves in the dining room. Booking is recommended in high season.;Terrace;[]
9330;La Fortuna;Italy;Campagnola Cremasca;via Ponte Rino 6, Campagnola Cremasca, 26010, Italy;45.39835;9.6685;40;false;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is constantly reinventing itself, offering a fresh ambience with a minimalist yet welcoming decor. The menu changes in accordance with what’s available at the weekly market – as a result, there are always new, carefully prepared dishes to try. The wine list boasts a selection of more than 200 labels!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9331;Pepenero;Italy;San Miniato;piazza del Duomo 4, San Miniato, 56028, Italy;43.6796919;10.851175;68;true;false;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;In its new home in Piazza del Duomo, in beautiful San Miniato, in the hands of chef Gilberto Rossi Pepenero continues to serve cuisine that showcases the best ingredients (both meat and fish) from this bountiful region, with delicacies such as excellent truffles featuring on the menu throughout the year. Prepared with a light and modern touch, meals are served in a spacious dining room where the many windows offer glimpses of the town centre.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9332;Luminist Cafè Bistrot;Italy;Naples;via Toledo 177, Naples, 80134, Italy;40.8406951;14.24874;33;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Situated on the ground floor of the splendid Banco di Napoli building that is also home to the Gallerie d'Italia museum, this restaurant also includes a bar and pasticceria. The varied restaurant menu features international dishes (for a quicker meal), fish based around recipes from around the world, alongside more creative dishes and regional specialities from Campania. The latter, from the aubergine parmigiana to the candele pasta served with a Neapolitan ragu, and the popular babà, are truly delicious and showcase all the colours and flavours of Neapolitan cuisine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9333;Il Ristorante - Niko Romito;Italy;Rome;via di Ripetta 73, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9067852;12.4758727;66;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated on the fifth floor of the Hotel Bulgari with views of the Mausoleum of Augustus, Il Ristorante - Niko Romito boasts a spacious terrace and an elegant, welcoming dining room with mahogany walls adorned with works of art. The menu features traditional Italian cuisine reinterpreted with a light and imaginative touch as demonstrated by memorable dishes such as the chef’s own take on classic spaghetti in a tomato sauce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9334;Quintogusto;Italy;Savona;piazza Sandro Pertini 54 r, Savona, 17100, Italy;44.3054183;8.4814112;72;true;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Recently opened in the renovated section of Corso Italia in central Savona, Quintogusto is a small, contemporary and minimalist-style restaurant occupying one side of the former hospital. Here, the owner-chef (once sous-chef at the excellent Michelin-starred Il Vescovado in Noli) cements his reputation with Ligurian-influenced cuisine to which he adds his own modern and imaginative touches.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9335;Locanda delle Tre Chiavi;Italy;Isera;via Vannetti 8, Isera, 38060, Italy;45.88918;11.01126;98;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant housed in an 18C building is run by its talented and enthusiastic owners Sergio (front of house) and Annarita (in the kitchen), who do their utmost to provide guests with the best seasonal, regional ingredients prepared in classic dishes full of flavour. The wine list focuses on good-quality labels from the region.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9336;Musciora;Italy;Alghero;via Mazzini 59, Alghero, 07041, Italy;40.5586717;8.317813;63;false;false;Sardinian, Modern Cuisine;Located not far from the town centre, this restaurant offers friendly, professional service and three tasting menus including the particularly appealing 8-course “La vera esperienza Musciora”. The dishes here pay tribute to Sardinia’s culinary traditions, while the ingredients are all sourced from the region, as are most of the wines. Highlights include the cuttlefish, potato and pea, and the Su Filindeu pasta (served in a seafood broth).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9337;Osteria Mercato;Italy;Stresa;piazza Capucci 9, Stresa, 28838, Italy;45.8822178;8.5397648;26;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Contemporary;The anonymous location of this restaurant in a car park just a stone’s throw from the historic centre is more than compensated by its lively and welcoming atmosphere. Attractive outdoor area, plus Italian cuisine reinterpreted with a creative twist.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9338;Bàcaro Il Gusto;Italy;Fossò;via Provinciale Nord 30, Fossò, 30030, Italy;45.386677;12.0493508;46;true;true;Venetian;A simple, modern restaurant where all the attention is focused on the extraordinary skills of the chef. The name is a nod to the typical Venetian bars known as bacari, and, in keeping with them, the restaurant serves a range of snacks, both traditional and creative in style, which allow the chef to demonstrate his culinary skills to the full. Other classic and more imaginative dishes also feature on the menu, alongside a choice of excellent desserts.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9339;Casa Rispoli;Italy;Cava de' Tirreni;piazza san Francesco 7, Cava de' Tirreni, 84013, Italy;40.6963696;14.7099255;98;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Overlooking a piazza surrounded by picturesque arcades in the historic centre (a walk around this district is highly recommended), this restaurant run by the Rispoli family continues to uphold its fine-dining traditions. Although a few meat dishes feature on the menu, it is its fish options (mainly traditional, such as tuna with mussels and escabeche-style aubergine) and occasionally imaginative desserts, such as the cheesecake with toffee and raspberry, that are the main attraction here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9340;L'Arcangelo;Italy;Rome;via Giuseppe Gioacchino Belli 59, Rome, 00193, Italy;41.9065413;12.4687174;80;true;true;Roman, Farm to table;Simple and austere: the rightfully earned fame of this restaurant is due to the search for the best regional (but not only) products. A real passion of the owner who, like an archangel, will guide you to the paradise of the palate and gastronomic niches.;Air conditioning;[]
9341;Eea;Italy;Ponza;via Umberto I, Ponza, 04027, Italy;40.893543;12.964747;91;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Named after the Ancient Greek name for Ponza, this restaurant is situated above the port and boasts fine views of the island’s picturesque houses and rugged coastline from its terrace. With an almost exclusive focus on fish and seafood, the menu features a balance of creative and more traditional dishes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9342;Verbano;Italy;Stresa;via Ugo Ara 2, Isola dei Pescatori, Stresa, 28838, Italy;45.9000678;8.5217885;47;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Within the confines of the small, charming Verbano hotel on the beautiful island of Pescatori, chef Marco Sacco serves top-quality cuisine in what can only be described as a stunning setting. The contemporary-style dining room boasts panoramic windows, while the outdoor terrace with its views of Palazzo Borromeo and Isola Bella is the perfect setting for dinner in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9343;La Tavola;Italy;Laveno;via Fortino 40, Laveno, 21014, Italy;45.9065255;8.6104635;44;true;true;Creative;Situated in the Il Porticciolo hotel, this restaurant will appeal to anyone who enjoys a lakeside setting. Leave your car in the car park, then take the lift down to the dining room with its windows overlooking the water and views of the opposite shore of Lake Maggiore. The lake also takes pride of place in some of the creative, elaborate and personalised dishes on the two tasting menus created by Riccardo Bassetti, many of which feature freshwater fish.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9344;La Brughiera;Italy;Senago;via XXIV Maggio 23, Senago, 20030, Italy;45.5757798;9.1140087;47;true;false;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;This old farmhouse in the Groane Regional Park has never lost its warm family atmosphere. The interior is spacious and attractive and the menus are based on traditional and national specialities.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9345;Gasthofstube Stafler;Italy;Mules;Campo di Trens, Mules, 39040, Italy;46.8511257;11.5204347;37;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant situated in the splendid Stafler hotel on the road to Austria is perfect for a romantic dinner, with a comfortable Stube-style dining room and an internal garden for fine weather. Friendly and welcoming staff and traditional Tyrolean cuisine with a focus on ingredients from the Isarco valley, plus interesting personal twists added by the chef.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9346;Buriani dal 1967;Italy;Pieve di Cento;via Matteotti 66, Pieve di Cento, 40066, Italy;44.7112661;11.3059943;53;true;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;A family-run restaurant in the province of Bologna with an excellent reputation for good food. Whether you choose one of the fish-based recipes or meat dishes, you’ll enjoy cuisine with a balance of classic flavours and modern influences, including a few regional specialities.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9347;Da Nonna Sceppa;Italy;Paestum;via Laura 45, Paestum, 84047, Italy;40.44638;14.978889;49;true;true;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;Founded in the 1960s by Grandma Giuseppa, the inn has today become a restaurant. The management has stayed within the hands of the same family: nephews and great - nephews are spread over dining room and kitchen. Local recipes on the menu, which changes daily.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9348;Vesta Mare;Italy;Marina di Pietrasanta;viale Roma 41, Marina di Pietrasanta, 55045, Italy;43.933229;10.1930984;62;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This new restaurant occupies the premises of the famous Franco Mare, inheriting its fine location and layout. The entrance leads into an elegant dining room with a maritime decor, followed by a swimming pool, an outdoor dining space and then finally the beach and private beach club. The cuisine has also had a makeover, and now focuses on simple, classic recipes and cooking styles, including a good choice of raw fish and seafood dishes. Specialities include the delicious paccheri pasta with a “trabaccolara” sauce and the addition of king crab, as well as the millefeuille with a raspberry coulis. A simpler menu is available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9349;Tantris;Italy;Novara;corso Risorgimento 384, Novara, 28100, Italy;45.4828355;8.6104091;86;true;false;Creative;A single elegant room for a menu that is an invitation to a gastronomic journey with Marta Grassi: at Tantris you’ll find local references, but the offering is essentially creative and freely interprets the products of the region and more besides. Excellent choice of wines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9350;Antica Osteria La Rampina;Italy;San Giuliano Milanese;via Emilia fraz. Rampina 3 ang. via Rocca Brivio, San Giuliano Milanese, 20098, Italy;45.36847;9.31612;83;false;false;Lombardian, Contemporary;It is said that General Radetzky, fleeing from the city during the Five Days of Milan rebellion, camped his troops right in front of La Rampina’s courtyard. Surrounded by nature and full of fascinating history, the restaurant now makes an ideal spot in which to enjoy the various culinary options served by Lino and his young son Luca, which offer a careful balance of local traditional flavour and skilful innovation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9351;Buca di Sant'Antonio;Italy;Lucca;via della Cervia 3, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8427305;10.5017857;37;true;false;Tuscan, Classic Cuisine;Just a stone’s throw from Piazza San Michele, in the heart of the beautiful historic centre of Lucca, the Buca di Sant'Antonio dates back over 200 years and is one of the city’s oldest restaurants. Here, the old copper pots and pans that hang from the ceiling add to the warm, romantic atmosphere, while the cuisine unsurprisingly showcases traditional Tuscan specialities including meat dishes and home-made pasta.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9352;l' Ciocio - Osteria di Suvereto;Italy;Suvereto;piazza dei Giudici 1, Suvereto, 57028, Italy;43.07921;10.67901;23;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Tuscan;Although this restaurant in the historic centre of Suvereto has the welcoming ambience of a traditional trattoria, its cuisine is more creative and elaborate in style (while still offering a few Tuscan classics). One of the house favourites is the “reale familiare”: a delicious cut of beef served with capers and anchovies.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9353;Osteria Vecchio Borgo;Italy;Cuneo;via Dronero 8/b, Cuneo, 12100, Italy;44.3930839;7.5491385;55;false;false;Country cooking;Described as a “meeting point between Piedmont and Liguria”, this quiet, welcoming restaurant in the historic centre of Cuneo focuses on ingredients and recipes from these two regions – the family, all of whom are involved in the restaurant (the women in the kitchen and the men front of house), are from Liguria. The generous, top-quality cuisine is prepared using seasonal produce with a personalised touch and is accompanied by a good selection of wine, also available by the glass.;Wheelchair access;[]
9354;4 Ciance;Italy;Cuneo;via Dronero 8/c, Cuneo, 12100, Italy;44.393135;7.549021;56;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in Cuneo’s historic centre boasts two bright dining rooms, as well as friendly and professional female staff and dishes prepared by two chefs that are a feast for the eyes and the palate! The cuisine here is rooted in tradition, and is prepared with skill, enthusiasm and the occasional contemporary touch. There are two tasting menus from which individual dishes can be chosen, plus a daily special (that varies according to market availability) announced at your table. Meat takes pride of place, as is typical in Piedmont, although a few fish and seafood options also feature.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9355;Ai Mercanti;Italy;Venice;corte Coppo, sestiere San Marco 4346/a, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.4351522;12.3351495;99;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A family-run “gastrosteria” hidden in a small Venetian courtyard, with a modern and elegant decor dominated by beige and black tones. Full of exciting and imaginative flavours, the modern meat and fish dishes prepared by promising young chef Nadia Locatello make a change from the typical specialities of the region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9356;Da Gerry;Italy;Monfumo;via Chiesa 6, Monfumo, 31010, Italy;45.8304724;11.9209252;34;false;true;Classic Cuisine;At this centrally located, contemporary - style trattoria sample local dishes, and much more besides. It also offers excellent accommodation. The Da Gerry’s bedrooms are both comfortable and spacious.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9357;Osteria da Afro;Italy;Spilimbergo;via Umberto I 14, Spilimbergo, 33097, Italy;46.1125533;12.8987118;59;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;An expertly run family restaurant not far from the historic centre. Warm atmosphere in the two dining rooms (especially the one with the fireplace), where the daily specials are marked on a blackboard. A real gem of restaurant, which also has a few charming guestrooms furnished in fir and cherry wood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9358;Le Case della Saracca;Italy;Monforte d'Alba;via Cavour 5, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.5846665;7.9686028;100;true;false;Piedmontese, Italian;Situated in the delightful Saracca district (Monforte’s old historic centre), this restaurant occupies an old, restored house with a glass and steel decor that provides a harmonious contrast with the building’s original features. Tables are arranged on different levels connected by a series of vertiginous staircases. Quiet and intimate, the restaurant serves a dual purpose: there’s a wine bar for aperitifs, while the dining room provides the backdrop for dishes from the region and further afield. Superb wine list with various labels available by the glass, plus guestrooms that offer the chance to spend the night in this unique setting.;Interesting wine list;[]
9359;L'Osteria H20;Italy;Moniga del Garda;via Pergola 10, Moniga del Garda, 25080, Italy;45.52083;10.52629;48;false;false;Creative;This bright, minimalist - style restaurant is situated on the road but its dining room faces the lake. It serves imaginative and personalised cuisine with both fish and meat dishes on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9360;Cavour;Italy;Dossobuono;via Cavour 40, Dossobuono, 37062, Italy;45.3966994;10.9144069;90;false;true;Venetian, Classic Cuisine;Cavour serves top-quality cuisine rooted in regional traditions, making it the type of restaurant that everyone would like as their local. Daily specials with a seasonal focus, such as the ultra-fresh puntarelle chicory salad with anchovies and Parmesan cheese, are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9361;Osteria Il Bagatto;Italy;Limone Piemonte;via XX Settembre 16, Limone Piemonte, 12015, Italy;44.2010853;7.5768821;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a typical mountain - style ambience, enjoy carefully prepared cuisine made by a skilful chef using the best ingredients. The menu includes a good choice of regional specialities, as well as fish dishes and imaginative contemporary fare.;Terrace;[]
9362;Antica Osteria Magenes;Italy;Barate;via Cavour 7, Barate, 20083, Italy;45.3846895;9.0396282;68;false;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;This fascinating restaurant occupying an old house renovated in modern style comes as a surprise given its location in a small village deep in the countryside. Enjoy traditional cuisine reinterpreted in a playful and original way in the well-tended garden, where six exclusive tables provide the perfect setting for an intimate and romantic alfresco dinner.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9363;Alle Corone;Italy;Venice;campo della Fava, sestiere Castello 5527, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.437059;12.3377324;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Modern Mediterranean and Venetian cuisine served in three elegant dining rooms or – on request – in the wine bar surrounded by bottles of wine. Through the windows, enjoy the spectacle of gondolas passing by along the small canal outside.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9364;La Rosina;Italy;Marostica;via Marchetti 4, Marostica, 36063, Italy;45.7745125;11.6603203;92;false;true;Venetian, Classic Cuisine;With over 100 years of history behind it, La Rosina is still looking good, thanks to renovation work carried out a few years ago which has given the restaurant a new look. Situated in an attractive location in the hills around Marostica, this excellent restaurant is a sound choice for good food in the province of Vicenza, serving modern regional and Italian dishes which are full of flavour. Enjoy beautiful views of the surrounding hills from the guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9365;Villetta Annessa;Italy;Riva del Garda;via Monte Oro 9, Riva del Garda, 38066, Italy;45.8863357;10.8381169;79;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Grills;A charming annexe to the Villa Miravalle hotel on the edge of Riva’s historic centre, this restaurant boasts a warm atmosphere and a pleasant outdoor space for summer dining. The regional, seasonal dishes served here are listed on a blackboard brought to your table, while the house speciality is undoubtedly the meat cooked over the sizzling grill – the first sight to greet you as you enter the dining room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9366;La Fossa del Grano;Italy;San Severo;via Minuziano 63, San Severo, 71016, Italy;41.6844115;15.3820992;76;true;false;Apulian, Traditional Cuisine;A must for anyone looking for traditional home cooking and authentic cuisine from Puglia. Make sure you try the antipasti, and then move on to a first or main course.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9367;50 Kalò;Italy;Naples;piazza Sannazzaro 201/b, Naples, 80122, Italy;40.8286403;14.2199723;54;true;false;Pizza;In the Neapolitan tradition of interpreting dreams, 50 means bread (dough), while the word “kalò” has Greek origins and means good – the name “good dough” explains the secret behind the pizzas made by Ciro Salvo, one of the most famous pizza masters in Naples. This chef makes traditional Neapolitan pizzas, which are large in size and have a soft dough. The restaurant doesn’t take reservations – if it’s busy you just leave your name and wait to be called. However, if you prefer not to wait, there’s a second restaurant at 2, Piazza della Repubblica where you can book ahead of time.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9368;Casa Format;Italy;Orbassano;via Tetti Valfrè, Orbassano, 10043, Italy;45.002438;7.5737295;23;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;A sustainable complex, the vegetable garden and a lot of passion are the elements that distinguish this high-quality restaurant. The modern building is characterized by very large windows that make the most of solar energy. The cuisine is authentic, tasty and with original ideas: the ice cream whipped with a Carpigiani machine before service is a delicious example.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9369;La Barca;Italy;Marina di Pulsano;litoranea Salentina, Marina di Pulsano, 74026, Italy;40.3586767;17.3445166;26;true;true;Seafood;Nestled between splendid beaches and bays, this restaurant focuses on the sea, not only in its views but also in its cuisine. The owner takes centre stage in the dining room, while the dishes prepared in the kitchen are varied, generous in size and reasonably priced, featuring classic recipes which allow the full flavours of the top-quality fish to shine through.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9370;Fiorentino e Locanda del Giglio;Italy;Sansepolcro;via Luca Pacioli 60, Sansepolcro, 52037, Italy;43.5714908;12.1398187;73;false;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;Just like the beautiful centre of Sansepolcro in which it is situated, this restaurant has much to boast about, with a history dating back over 200 years. The beautifully decorated dining rooms on the first floor of the palazzo are a picture of elegance, while the service is friendly and more informal. Traditional cuisine from inland Tuscany, plus welcoming guestrooms which add to its appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
9371;Il Sole di Ranco;Italy;Ranco;piazza Venezia 5, Ranco, 21020, Italy;45.7982244;8.569655;45;false;true;Creative;An elegant residence with gardens sloping down to the lake. The charming terrace, where meals are served in summer, offers superb views of the lake, while the cuisine combines the traditional and the modern, including imaginative flavours with a focus on locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9372;Hostaria del Teatro;Italy;Castiglione delle Stiviere;via Ordanino 5b, Castiglione delle Stiviere, 46043, Italy;45.3909991;10.4906348;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;This welcoming restaurant with an open-view kitchen serves cuisine influenced by the traditions of Mantova and the Veneto, alongside more creative dishes inspired by the chef’s imagination. The chef’s wife provides a friendly welcome front of house, plus there’s a delightful garden for alfresco dining in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9373;Locanda 4 Cuochi;Italy;Verona;via Alberto Mario 12, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.44019;10.99397;64;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Situated behind the amphitheatre right in the historic centre, this attractive restaurant serves simple yet top-quality cuisine and is run by two former pupils of chef Giancarlo Perbellini. The menu features contemporary Italian cuisine, including dishes such as creamy risotto with saffron, prawns and lemon curd, and lamb kebabs with aromatic herbs, corn salad, mint yoghurt and black sesame seeds.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9374;Menzaghi;Italy;Fagnano Olona;via San Giovanni 74, Fagnano Olona, 21054, Italy;45.6780491;8.8688605;74;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Once you’ve found the car park, make your way to this restaurant’s small, traditional dining room where you will be warmly welcomed by the owner (a real wine enthusiast) and well looked after by his friendly yet efficient staff. Generous cuisine with plenty of attention paid to local, seasonal ingredients and daily specials that come highly recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
9375;Giglio;Italy;Lucca;piazza del Giglio 2, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8410854;10.5032438;90;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Housed in a beautiful 18C palazzo, Giglio boasts a superb location in one of the many squares in Lucca’s charming historic centre, as well as a delightful outdoor space. The meat and fish dishes on the menu here are inspired by traditional Italian recipes and reinterpreted with a light modern touch – a good example is the siphoned potato which is sprinkled with bottarga and served with a squid sauce, chanterelle mushrooms and spicy parsley cream. The bread is always excellent.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9376;Castello;Italy;Santa Vittoria d'Alba;via Cagna 4, Santa Vittoria d'Alba, 12069, Italy;44.69611;7.9304;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant offers several different options in which to enjoy its delicious meat and fish dishes with a modern twist. In summer, the beautiful veranda with views of the hills and surrounding countryside offers alfresco dining, while in winter the bright, modern dining room is a perfect setting for your meal.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9377;Apollinare;Italy;Spoleto;via Sant'Agata 14, Spoleto, 06049, Italy;42.7335767;12.735434;37;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Surrounded by walls dating back to the 13C, this intimate and romantic setting is typical of old Spoleto. With their exposed beams and stonework, the elegant dining rooms are the perfect backdrop for superb, traditional Umbrian cuisine, to which the chef adds a few fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9378;Tre Noci;Italy;Spirano;via Petrarca 16, Spirano, 24050, Italy;45.5808613;9.6672084;16;false;true;Country cooking, Grills;Situated in the centre of a village in the Bassa Bergamasca area, this long-established, family-run restaurant has a rustic decor softened by the owners’ female touch. The overall feel is that of an elegant trattoria, which provides a pleasant backdrop for delicious specialities from this lowland region, including meat cooked over the large grill in the dining room. There’s also a gazebo for alfresco dining in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9379;Morelli;Italy;Milan;via Aristotile Fioravanti 4, Milan, 20154, Italy;45.4832867;9.1774988;28;true;true;Creative;The new Milan restaurant of renowned chef Giancarlo Morelli, housed in the fascinating, new Hotel Viu. The creative gourmet dinner menu served in the stylish and discreetly lit dining room is complemented by the Bulk mixology and food bar, which serves simpler dishes throughout the day.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9380;Malga Roncac;Italy;Moena;strada de Roncac 7, Moena, 38035, Italy;46.382225;11.651086;78;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;An Alpine farmhouse built from wood and stone with a superb panoramic location on the edge of the woods. Traditional Ladin cuisine served in a typical local ambience.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9381;Salvo Cacciatori;Italy;Oneglia;via Vieusseux 12, Oneglia, 18100, Italy;43.89001;8.040223;17;true;false;Ligurian, Contemporary;This restaurant has come a long way since 1906, when the owner’s ancestors opened a modern inn and wine tavern, evolving into an inviting restaurant with an elegant, contemporary-style decor. The cuisine focuses on traditional fish and seafood recipes reinterpreted with a personalised twist, while the impressive wine list features labels from Liguria and beyond. If you want to eat on the pleasant outdoor terrace overlooking the pedestrianised street it’s best to book ahead.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9382;Ansitz Steinbock;Italy;Villandro;via Defregger 14, Villandro, 39040, Italy;46.6323382;11.5403732;29;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Following recent renovation work, this beautiful castle has an even more romantic atmosphere than ever. The restaurant is typical of the Alto Adige, boasting traditional Stube-style rooms that are furnished with a profusion of wood, from the floors to the walls and ceilings. The menu is more varied than previously, with a classic à la carte available for lunch and dinner, while fine-dining options are only available in the evening. The latter are presented on two tasting menus – “Roots” (dedicated to the local region) and “Creativo” (which includes ingredients from elsewhere) – both of which are striking for their imaginative approach.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9383;La Pajara Gourmet;Italy;Fiera di Primiero;via Venezia 28, Fiera di Primiero, 38054, Italy;46.1768409;11.8360621;47;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Situated within the Castel Pietra hotel, this pleasant restaurant with a combination of traditional and modern decor serves contemporary-style meat (often with a regional focus) and fish dishes which represent the different origins of the restaurant owners: the husband comes from Salento, while the wife is from the mountains.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9384;Osteria Arborina;Italy;La Morra;frazione Annunziata 27/b, La Morra, 12064, Italy;44.6356283;7.9535024;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Although the beautiful Arborina Relais boasts modern, stylish and elegant dining rooms, the main attraction here is the restaurant’s exciting cuisine in which different culinary styles and techniques are showcased in every dish. Inspiration comes from different influences – for example, we chose a menu inspired by the 1980s (a period when Neapolitan chef Fernando Tommaso Forino was not yet born), and particularly enjoyed the mullet in vodka and the dessert trolley. We also liked the idea behind the menu as a whole, namely the no-waste focus, with all parts of the ingredients used yet always with the aim of creating enjoyable dishes. An interesting, classically extensive wine list and excellent service complete the picture.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9385;Olona - "Da Venanzio" dal 1922;Italy;Induno Olona;via Olona 38, Induno Olona, 21056, Italy;45.8465363;8.826291;53;false;false;Country cooking;A bastion of regional cuisine for over a century, this restaurant occupies an attractive group of buildings with a large outdoor summer area shaded by a pergola and a charming dining room with a retro feel. Traditional recipes with interesting and personalised twists take centre stage, including superb ravioli del plin with three roasts and a meat sauce – this is Lombardy, after all! Impressive wine list, including wines by the glass.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9386;Al Palazzo;Italy;Positano;via Dei Mulini 23, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6290681;14.4867101;92;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Al Palazzo is the renowned restaurant at the Palazzo Murat hotel which is run by the Attanasio family. Dine alfresco in the restaurant’s beautiful botanical garden with its tiny vegetable patch, apart from on rare days of bad weather, when guests are served indoors in its small, elegant dining rooms. The Mediterranean cuisine includes meat and fish dishes alike, with slightly different menus at lunchtime (simpler options) and in the evening. Le Petit Murat bar is still open, offering an interesting selection of cocktails to supplement its excellent wine list.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9387;J Contemporary Japanese Restaurant;Italy;Naples;via Agostino Depretis 24, Naples, 80133, Italy;40.8427582;14.2549979;25;false;false;Japanese;Arranged over several floors and in different dining rooms, this smart, elegant restaurant offers excellent service. In this modern setting with subtle lighting, enjoy typical Japanese specialities (almost exclusively fish dishes) which are showcased on an extensive menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
9388;Un Posto a Milano;Italy;Milan;via Cuccagna 2, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.4511034;9.2114879;56;false;false;Farm to table, Italian Contemporary;Un Posto a Milan is a farmhouse in the city: an ideal place to spend a few hours outdoors, but also an agricultural market, a kitchen serving food, a carpentry workshop and a venue offering a host of other activities. The menu features traditional Italian dishes (sometimes given a modern twist), made with top-quality fresh, seasonal and – as far as possible – organic ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9389;Lo Scudiero;Italy;Pesaro;via Baldassini 2, Pesaro, 61121, Italy;43.9092737;12.9142506;98;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;Young, enthusiastic chef Daniele Patti is at the helm at this restaurant housed in the delightful stables of a restored 16C palazzo. Here, he serves a selection of creative dishes, including two tasting menus – the intriguing Vieni in Sicilia con me (inspired by his native Sicily) and the Adriatico  - and an à la carte which focuses on the local region’s abundance of fine ingredients. Wine-enthusiasts can ask to visit the impressive cellar, which also offers a good choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9390;S'Andira;Italy;Santa Reparata;via Orsa Minore 1, Santa Reparata, 07028, Italy;41.2316127;9.1668328;89;true;true;Seafood;In Italian this translates into "he who goes", but you will never feel like leaving this place. Located amidst granite boulders sculpted by the wind, juniper trees and the sea that will tantalize your vision and your palate.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9391;Al Volt;Italy;Riva del Garda;via Fiume 73, Riva del Garda, 38066, Italy;45.8863406;10.8397358;61;false;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;As you explore the narrow streets which lead from the commercial port to the centre, you’ll come across this restaurant comprising several inter - connected dining rooms with low ceilings and antique furniture. The menu focuses on regional cuisine, albeit with the occasional creative twist.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9392;Nni Lausta;Italy;Santa Marina Salina;via Risorgimento 188, Santa Marina Salina, 98050, Italy;38.5596;14.87111;84;true;true;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;Fish plays the starring role here, where the authentic traditional flavours and ingredients of Aeolian cuisine are skilfully interpreted with a touch of imaginative flair. If it’s not too hot to sit outside, ask for a table on the pleasant, shaded terrace on the first floor.;Terrace;[]
9393;Trequarti;Italy;Val Liona;piazza del Donatore 3/4, Val Liona, 36044, Italy;45.409725;11.452485;99;true;false;Creative;This modern and minimalist-style restaurant with three small dining rooms full of character provides the backdrop for contemporary-style cuisine which is constantly evolving. The menu includes a few snack options for those in a hurry or looking to sample a variety of dishes in smaller portions. Open at lunchtime by prior reservation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9394;Antica Osteria Il Monte Rosso;Italy;Suna;via Troubetzkoy 128, Suna, 28925, Italy;45.9310281;8.5400656;51;true;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Situated on the lakeside in the residential district of Verbania, this small, Old England - style restaurant serves a selection of freshwater and saltwater fish specialities. If the weather allows, ask for one of the few tables on the panoramic terrace.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9395;Il Convito di Curina;Italy;Castelnuovo Berardenga;SP 62 24, località Curina, Castelnuovo Berardenga, 53019, Italy;43.34549;11.46541;21;false;true;Tuscan;Tuscan cuisine, accompanied by a wide selection of wines (including regional labels and champagnes made by small producers) is served in the rustic yet elegant ambience of this restaurant. In fine weather, enjoy alfresco dining on the panoramic terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9396;Osteria L'Orciaia;Italy;Montebenichi;via Capitan Goro 10, Montebenichi, 52021, Italy;43.4057953;11.5448434;46;true;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;A small rustic - style hostelry set inside a 16C building, with a cosy summer terrace. Typical Tuscan fare based on excellent produce and with some personal touches.;Terrace;[]
9397;Posta;Italy;Sant'Omobono Terme;viale Vittorio Veneto 169, Sant'Omobono Terme, 24038, Italy;45.8147902;9.5328321;66;false;false;Italian;Situated in the Imagna valley, this welcoming, family-run restaurant serves delicious regional specialities alongside traditional Italian favourites, including a few fish options. Highlights include the dried-cod cannelloni, soft braised “guancialino” and the unmissable zabaglione mousse with sbrisolona-cake crumbs and marzipan ice-cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9398;Hostaria Baccofurore;Italy;Furore;via G.B. Lama 9, Furore, 84010, Italy;40.6204277;14.5486388;39;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;Patience is needed to get to this restaurant from the coast, as a result of the winding road which makes its way through small villages, but once here the view of the sea is breathtaking. The village of Furore is built alongside the road and is famous for the Marisa Cuomo winery situated opposite the restaurant. The cuisine is as impressive as the vista, with its focus on different local ingredients cooked with a mix of traditional influence and imagination. Comfortable guestrooms are also available, almost all of which have been recently renovated and boast impressive views.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9399;Locanda Radici;Italy;Melizzano;SP 21, contrada San Vincenzo, Melizzano, 82030, Italy;41.1752087;14.5126722;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Campanian;A rustic restaurant with contemporary Mediterranean-style decor surrounded by the greenery of the Sannio region, which can be admired through the large windows. Modern cuisine made from locally sourced ingredients by the owner-chef, who has vast experience working in top restaurants, both in Italy and abroad.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9400;DanielCanzian;Italy;Milan;via Castelfidardo 7, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.478596;9.189223;61;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Venetian;Situated in the heart of Brera and refurbished in the autumn of 2019, this restaurant showcases Italian artisanal skills through its bespoke furnishings, creating a fine setting for Canzian’s superb cuisine. A great choice for anyone looking for classic Italian dishes plus a few more inventive options, all of which are prepared using the very best ingredients. Simpler fare available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9401;Onda Blu;Italy;San Mauro a Mare;via Orsa Minore 1, San Mauro a Mare, 47030, Italy;44.16286;12.449604;63;false;true;Seafood;Almost appearing to rise up directly out of the sand, this unexpectedly elegant restaurant is home to a simple yet stylish dining room with large windows overlooking the sea. Fresh fish of the highest quality takes pride of place on the menu, served in classic, traditional dishes from the Adriatic. Daily specials fresh from the market feature alongside the à la carte, such as the excellent porcini mushrooms we enjoyed on our last visit here, which were served with passatelli pasta, shrimp and scallops. Although individuals may change, an enthusiastic and professional approach is typical of the entire team here. The excellent wine list includes labels from outside Italy, with a particular focus on France.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9402;Ilario Vinciguerra;Italy;Gallarate;via Roma 1, Gallarate, 21013, Italy;45.6619731;8.7895018;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This beautiful Art Nouveau-style villa is a restaurant, bistro and lounge-bar in one – the ideal setting for a meal, whether you’re planning a business lunch or a romantic dinner. Guests will feel immediately at ease both with Ilario’s modern, Mediterranean cuisine and the vaguely private feel of the small dining rooms. There’s also an original collection of Romano Levi grappas, plus several rare labels on the wine list that will definitely appeal to wine buffs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9403;Osteria del Borgo;Italy;Galliate;via Pietro Custodi 5, Galliate, 28066, Italy;45.4780716;8.697357;61;false;false;Creative;Situated in the heart of the old town, this restaurant is run by friendly and welcoming staff. The menu features a mix of meat and fish dishes that are prepared in traditional style with the occasional personalised touch.;Air conditioning;[]
9404;Il Santo Bevitore;Italy;Florence;via Santo Spirito 64/66 r, Florence, 50125, Italy;43.7690773;11.2466192;94;false;false;Tuscan;Both the simple, friendly atmosphere and the cuisine served at this restaurant are typical of a Tuscan trattoria. The menu features classic favourites from Tuscany (highlights include pappa al pomodoro and cured hams), which are full of the strong traditional flavours that you would expect to find in Florence and are occasionally reinterpreted in more contemporary dishes. For guests keen to take a culinary souvenir home with them, the Santino delicatessen is just next door.;;[]
9405;Al Cavallino Bianco;Italy;Polesine Parmense;via Sbrisi 3, Polesine Parmense, 43016, Italy;45.020774;10.0907645;38;false;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated near the banks of the River Po, this century - old, family - run restaurant serves regional specialities, such as the famous culatello ham. You will find reasonably priced local dishes at the ‘Tipico di Casa Spigaroli’ at lunchtime during the week, and themed menus at the weekend.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
9406;Moscatello Muliner;Italy;Pozzolengo;località Moscatello 3/5, Pozzolengo, 25010, Italy;45.3913037;10.6404351;34;false;true;Country cooking;Situated in a rural setting on a huge agricultural property, this attractive restaurant is dominated by an early 20C millstone. The menu combines traditional Italian fare with regional specialities, all at reasonable prices.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9407;ME Restaurant;Italy;Pizzo;SP per Vibo Marina, località Ponte di Ferro, Pizzo, 89812, Italy;38.7239647;16.1479385;73;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Occupying an old restored farmhouse, this large, spacious and attractive restaurant is run by a couple who offer their guests Mediterranean cuisine which is full of flavour. The focus here is on the traditions of Calabria, but the chef’s native region of Campania is also evident in many of the dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9408;El Filò;Italy;Pozza di Fassa;strada Dolomites 103, Pozza di Fassa, 38036, Italy;46.42843;11.68419;64;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Following recent refurbishment, El Filò is now even more comfortable than ever, boasting an Alpine-influenced decor that is striking for its contemporary style. The Dolomites and Ladin culinary traditions are still very much to the fore in the cuisine, which is prepared by the excellent owner-chef, although modern touches and influences from outside the region also feature. The wine list offers a fine selection of options from the region.;Car park;[]
9409;L'Oste e il Sacrestano;Italy;Licata;via Sant'Andrea 19, Licata, 92027, Italy;37.1000891;13.9388331;57;true;false;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;A small welcoming restaurant full of Sicilian charm. Chiara welcomes guests front of house, and Peppe works in the kitchen creating fine, traditional cuisine reinterpreted with his own personal touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9410;Papaveri e Papere;Italy;San Miniato;via Dalmazia 159/d, San Miniato, 56028, Italy;43.6668854;10.8391901;23;false;true;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;The cuisine at this restaurant focuses on local recipes and ingredients yet also has a light, modern flavour and beautiful contemporary presentation, as seen in the pici pasta with roast peppers, sweetbreads and pecorino cheese. The chef here is equally at ease with meat and fish, and particularly keen on vegetables, with white truffles from San Miniato featuring on the menu in the autumn.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9411;Trippi;Italy;Sondrio;via Stelvio 297, loc. Montagna in Valtellina, Sondrio, 23020, Italy;46.1699887;9.901579;70;true;false;Cuisine from Valtellina, Lombardian;This long-established restaurant just outside Sondrio has been run for the past decade by Gianluca, whose experience injects new life into traditional dishes from the local region, as well as introducing the occasional Mediterranean twist. There’s a simpler menu at lunchtime, plus a good selection of local wines and cheeses on sale at takeaway prices near the restaurant entrance.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9412;Regina Lucia;Italy;Syracuse;piazza Duomo 6, Ortigia, Syracuse, 96100, Italy;37.0588133;15.2931068;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Overlooking a square of monumental beauty where tables are laid out for alfresco dining in summer, Regina Lucia is well worth a visit even when it’s not fine enough to sit outside. In a dining room with plenty of historic character, enjoy classic Sicilian cuisine reinterpreted with a creative twist – and make sure you don’t miss the delicious desserts!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9414;La Locanda di Piero;Italy;Montecchio Precalcino;via Roma 34, strada per Dueville, Montecchio Precalcino, 36030, Italy;45.6556659;11.5580231;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Housed in a small country villa with the ambience of a private residence, this restaurant boasts a dining room with a welcoming fireplace in winter and a veranda full of natural light, giving it a classic feel that makes it perfect for an elegant and romantic dinner. The cuisine is distinctive and full of substance, featuring a selection of meat and fish dishes that includes classic and creative options alike.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9415;Il Galeone;Italy;Fano;piazzale Amendola 2, Fano, 61032, Italy;43.8511366;13.01097;100;true;false;Seafood, Italian;Housed on the ground floor of the Elisabeth Due hotel, this restaurant enjoys a fine reputation in the area around Fano. In recent years, the owner-chef has intensified his efforts to source seasonal fish and other ingredients from the region, which he uses to prepare dishes that showcase a perfect balance of classic and modern influences.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9416;Entrà;Italy;Finale Emilia;via Salde Entrà 60, località Entrà, Finale Emilia, 41034, Italy;44.832888;11.1856644;15;false;true;Country cooking;Make sure you use your sat-nav to get to this restaurant as finding the right road through the countryside can be a challenge, although once you’re here you’ll be glad you made the effort. The trattoria occupies a wine shop dating from 1919, from which it has retained a few attractive and nostalgic touches despite its renovation. The cuisine focuses on a few regional dishes which are announced at your table by the owner himself.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9417;Filippino;Italy;Lipari;piazza Municipio, Lipari, 98055, Italy;38.4685552;14.9564985;29;true;true;Seafood, Sicilian;Opened in 1910, this historic restaurant with an attractive shaded outdoor pergola serves an extensive array of delicious local fish prepared in traditional recipes. Enjoy a selection of typical Sicilian specialities prepared by the Bernardi family, including the highly recommended “Nonno Filippino” fish soup.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9418;Marcelin;Italy;Montà;piazzetta della Vecchia Segheria 1, Montà, 12046, Italy;44.8144512;7.9585452;50;true;false;Country cooking, Creative;If you are in search of creative and innovative cuisine in this region renowned for its great gastronomic tradition, then Marcelin is the place for you. This is thanks to its occasionally complex and always beautifully presented dishes (including a few fish options). Housed on the first floor of an old sawmill, the restaurant boasts a restrained yet elegant decor.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9419;La Torre;Italy;Monselice;piazza Mazzini 14, Monselice, 35043, Italy;45.24177;11.7507885;83;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Grills;Overlooked by a medieval tower in the main town square, this restaurant is perfect for anyone keen on classic, traditional cuisine. House specialities include dishes cooked over the barbecue grill.;Air conditioning;[]
9420;Ca' Del Moro;Italy;Grezzana;località Erbin 31, Grezzana, 37023, Italy;45.5313227;11.0581539;46;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated within the La Collina dei Ciliegi wine estate amid the verdant Valpantena hills, this first-floor restaurant (lift available) is home to two chefs – he is from Calabria, while she is from Puglia. Together they create exciting, modern Mediterranean cuisine using ingredients from their native regions, including their signature dish – homemade spaghetti served with a delicious, well-balanced 'nduja, smoked ricotta and tomato ristretto sauce. Top-quality local ingredients take pride of place, as demonstrated by the Brogna mutton, which is raised on site, barbecued and served with an exquisite caper sauce and seasonal mushroom pie. The concise wine list features labels from the Veneto alongside a few French options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9421;Viva il Bistrot;Italy;Noto;via Rocco Pirri 19, Noto, 96017, Italy;36.8918976;15.0692098;69;false;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Situated just a stone’s throw from the cathedral, this restaurant has tables set out on Noto’s attractive pedestrianised street in fine weather, although if these are all taken the contemporary-style dining rooms are just as appealing. Viviana Varese, a Michelin-starred chef from Milano, oversees the interesting menu which showcases Sicilian cuisine prepared from local ingredients alongside more exotic fare.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9422;Il Fenicottero Rosa Gourmet;Italy;Faenza;via Emilia Ponente 23, Faenza, 48018, Italy;44.2947451;11.8539981;66;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;Situated within the Villa Abbondanzi luxury hotel, this restaurant is surrounded by a large park home to a flock of flamingos (fenicottero is the Italian for flamingo). Stylish and elegant dining rooms provide the backdrop for equally impressive cuisine, which is elaborate and full of imaginative touches. The same attention to detail is evident in the wine list, which includes several natural wines and from which the talented sommelier will find the perfect choice for you. We particularly enjoyed the Alto Adige Sauvignon Weingut In Der Eben: a rich and complex 2019 wine which was the perfect pairing for the entire meal, including dishes with real character.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9423;I Due Buoi;Italy;Olivola;via Vittorio Veneto 23, Olivola, 15030, Italy;45.037953;8.3667204;73;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant offers three tasting menus: Stile Libero, Tradizione e Territorio, and Quinto Quarto , the latter featuring various types of offal which the chef transforms into creative dishes, plus an à la carte that includes local specialities and a good choice of bread. Top-quality wines with a focus on Asti and its surrounding area, as well as on the Langhe region.;Car park;[]
9424;Bites;Italy;Milan;via Lambro 11, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.4743013;9.2095483;74;true;false;International, Small eats;The cuisine at this tiny, simply furnished restaurant includes barbecued dishes and fermented ingredients, all of which feature on a tasting menu. Guests can also choose à la carte: the small portions (as the restaurant name suggests) make it possible to taste several dishes at a reasonable cost. Booking is essential in the evening and also advisable at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9425;Il Fico trentacareghe;Italy;Lerici;Località Fiascherino 7, Lerici, 19032, Italy;44.0657653;9.9235847;46;false;true;Seafood;Situated on one of the region’s most beautiful coast roads, this restaurant with a charming garden of olive trees boasts stunning views of the sea which can be admired either from the dining room or, even better, from the summer terrace. The cuisine is equal to the setting, with a focus on fish and seafood dishes influenced by Ligurian traditions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9426;L'Uva e il Malto;Italy;Grosseto;via Mazzini 165, Grosseto, 58100, Italy;42.758942;11.1139463;75;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;A talented couple run this modern, intimate restaurant with a wine-bar right in the town centre. Fish takes pride of place on the menu, with the catch of the day announced at your table, including delicious shellfish. The female owner oversees the extensive wine list, which features reasonably priced and mostly Tuscan labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9427;I Banchi;Italy;Ragusa;via Orfanotrofio 39, Ragusa, 97100, Italy;36.926517;14.7454195;87;true;true;Sicilian, Contemporary;Housed in a palazzo full of history – the building was a synagogue before the 1693 earthquake and has retained its ritual bath in its charming room of mirrors – this restaurant bears the imprint of renowned chef Ciccio Sultano, holder of two Michelin stars at the nearby Duomo restaurant. The cuisine is eclectic yet with a Sicilian focus, plus the wine list is complemented by a choice of interesting cocktails.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9428;Maso Burba;Italy;Commezzadura;via Pietro Bernardelli 32, località Piano, Commezzadura, 38020, Italy;46.3208346;10.823971;89;true;false;Country cooking, Alpine;Having spent time working in top-quality restaurants, Gianpaolo Burba – alongside his partner Paola who works front of house – has returned home to the family restaurant in a small village in the Val di Sole region. Here, he makes the most of his experience and skills acquired elsewhere to showcase the best of the region’s ingredients in his beautifully presented dishes (although fish does make a rare appearance on the menu). The dining rooms, including a covered veranda, are bright, elegant and typically regional in style.;Car park;[]
9430;Osteria la Fontanina;Italy;Verona;portichetti Fontanelle Santo Stefano 3, Verona, 37129, Italy;45.4492275;11.0006288;46;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Situated just a stone’s throw from the Roman Theatre and Ponte Pietra, Osteria La Fontanina is one of Verona’s oldest restaurants with a history that dates back over 200 years. The restaurant has a “bohemian” feel, with old mirrors, prints, silverware and plants that combine well with the subdued lighting (even at lunchtime) and just about enough space for the small tables. The cuisine showcases Italian and regional flavours, while the impressive wine list focuses on red wine vintages from the Verona region.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9431;La Taverna del Leone;Italy;Positano;via Laurito 43, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6248114;14.5076383;90;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Situated three kilometres east of Positano, this family-run restaurant has been in business for almost 60 years and is one of the most popular in the region – and for good reason. The classic-style dining room with a striking open-view kitchen adorned with local blue-and-white ceramics provides the setting for meat and fish dishes (mainly local) prepared from top-quality ingredients with the occasional personal touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9432;Controcorrente;Italy;Noli;via Colombo 101, Noli, 17026, Italy;44.205749;8.4134555;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Ligurian;In this minimalist restaurant, situated below the medieval San Giovanni tower in the picturesque pedestrianised historic centre of Noli, the owner-chef serves contemporary cuisine that echoes the dining room’s modern decor. The menu features meat and fish dishes alike, all prepared from almost exclusively Ligurian ingredients, including delicious purple Sanremo prawn tartare with celery mayonnaise, lemon cream and plankton chips, as well as lamb cooked in its own juices with Albenga artichokes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9433;Li Lioni;Italy;Porto Torres;SS 131 km 244,400 - regione Li Lioni, Porto Torres, 07046, Italy;40.80912;8.43872;73;true;false;Sardinian, Home Cooking;The highlights of this restaurant just outside the tourist centre of Porto Torres are its informal atmosphere, spacious garden and traditional cuisine. The frattaubread is well worth sampling (also available in a vegan version), as is the legendary porceddu(suckling pig), which must be ordered when you book. When choosing wine, we recommend the well-structured and intense house red.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9434;Taverna La Cialoma;Italy;Marzamemi;piazza Regina Margherita 23, Marzamemi, 96018, Italy;36.7420586;15.1197108;59;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant housed in Marzamemi’s old tuna fishery boasts an outdoor terrace with tables overlooking one of the most picturesque squares in Sicily, as well as an indoor dining room and another terrace to the rear facing the sea. Wherever you choose to sit, you’ll find authentic Sicilian cuisine on the menu, with just a few simply prepared dishes in which the full flavours of fresh fish shine through.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9435;La Sosta di Ottone III;Italy;Levanto;Località Chiesanuova 39, Levanto, 19015, Italy;44.17155;9.64716;37;false;false;Ligurian;Ask for directions to this restaurant when you make your booking, as you’ll need to leave your vehicle in a private car park at the entrance to the village and then make your way uphill on foot. Situated in one of Liguria’s most typical and picturesque inland villages with views of the sea in the distance, the restaurant offers outdoor dining under a wisteria in fine weather. The menu features a small choice of regional dishes, with the same focus on Liguria evident on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9436;Le Baccanti;Italy;Nola;via Puccini 5, Nola, 80035, Italy;40.9313683;14.5251246;75;false;true;Campanian, Classic Cuisine;Simple premises with two large windows overlooking its kitchens. It serves imaginative dishes where tradition and creativity become one. Informal service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9437;Oberlechner;Italy;Algund;località Velloi 7, Algund, 39022, Italy;46.69601;11.117554;89;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;From Merano you climb to an altitude of 1 000m to this restaurant, which boasts breathtaking views of the town and surrounding mountains. The menu here focuses mainly on local ingredients which are carefully prepared without too many creative twists, resulting in delicious and generous dishes such as braised beef with a Lagrein sauce (accompanied by rice and vegetables). All the attractive guestrooms have a balcony and the same stunning view.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9438;Osteria della Chiocciola;Italy;Cuneo;via Fossano 1, Cuneo, 12100, Italy;44.3938765;7.5509969;69;false;false;Piedmontese, Classic Cuisine;Situated in the historic centre just a stone’s throw from the elegant Via Roma, this restaurant is decorated with paintings by renowned modern artists such as Pignatelli, Andy Warhol, and Valerio Berruti. The ground floor is home to a colourful wine bar, while the first-floor restaurant serves traditional cuisine made from local ingredients with a natural focus on Piedmont. There is also a fish alternative for non-meat-eaters.;Interesting wine list;[]
9439;Menarosti;Italy;Trieste;via del Toro 12, Trieste, 34125, Italy;45.6508;13.7790259;76;true;true;Seafood;Dating back to 1903, this historic restaurant has a warm, welcoming feel. Excellent fish and seafood prepared using top - quality ingredients, where simple preparation allows the flavours to shine through.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9440;Al Bagatto;Italy;Trieste;via Cadorna 7, Trieste, 34124, Italy;45.6485947;13.7652132;46;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;A small, elegant restaurant in the city centre decorated in warm colours. Two private rooms (one very intimate, just for two people, the other slightly larger) are also available. Fish - based cuisine with a modern touch.;Air conditioning;[]
9441;Portanova;Italy;Urbino;via Cesare Battisti 67, Urbino, 61029, Italy;43.7275489;12.6373808;35;false;true;Cuisine from the Marches, Italian Contemporary;A new restaurant in Urbino’s beautiful old town, where the designer-style decor blends harmoniously with the historic architecture. The modern, contemporary-style cuisine finds inspiration in ingredients from the Marche, as well as featuring flavours and traditions from other regions of Italy such as Sardinia, Campania and Lazio.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9442;Contrasto;Italy;Cercemaggiore;via Roma 55, Cercemaggiore, 86012, Italy;41.4592138;14.7200502;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Having returned to his native village, owner-chef Lucio Testa has opened this restaurant in a former sheepfold on the outskirts of the village perched at an altitude of 937m. The restaurant boasts a perfectly preserved stone façade, various small rooms arranged on different levels, exposed beams and contemporary-style lamps which give the dining room a modern feel. The creative cuisine features reinterpretations of traditional recipes from the Molise, which combine local and seasonal ingredients (including produce from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden) with culinary techniques such as sauces, seasonings and emulsions acquired by the chef from his time working in France. Moulard duck is a favourite ingredient, while various tasting menus and an à la carte showcase the region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9443;Bolle;Italy;Lallio;via Provinciale 30, Lallio, 24040, Italy;45.65983;9.62902;88;true;false;Italian Contemporary;We are in the Agnelli showroom, a well-known manufacturer of cookware for professional kitchens. The modern shop is located on the ground floor, while the first floor hosts the restaurant with its elegant tables in a refined minimalist and contemporary environment. On the menu, dishes with an impressive balance of ingredients, including occasionally exotic choices.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9444;Futura;Italy;Chieti;piazza San Giustino 7, Chieti, 66100, Italy;42.35107;14.1673768;76;true;true;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;Situated in the heart of the historic centre overlooking the monumental Piazza San Giustino, this restaurant has a traditional feel in keeping with its location, enhanced by typical brick walls in dining rooms arranged on two floors. In contrast, the predominantly meat-based cuisine is contemporary in style, with some interesting technical and creative twists.;Air conditioning;[]
9445;Blaue Traube;Italy;Algund;strada Vecchia 44, Algund, 39022, Italy;46.6831586;11.1228848;95;true;true;Modern Cuisine, South Tyrolean;This extremely old restaurant (its name is said to have existed as early as the mid 17C) has been given a new lease of life in 2019 by its young chef Christoph Huber, who puts to good use the many experiences gained over the years in different restaurants, including Michelin-starred addresses. His dishes pay tribute to Southern Tyrolean recipes and ingredients with an added contemporary twist.;Terrace;[]
9446;Saur;Italy;Barco;via Filippo Turati 8, Barco, 25034, Italy;45.3794034;9.9010106;18;true;false;Italian Contemporary;In a tiny rural village, this contemporary, almost minimalist-style restaurant serves modern cuisine with an emphasis on seasonal, regional produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9447;Valli di Lanzo;Italy;Céres;via Roma 11, Céres, 10070, Italy;45.3146596;7.3882607;21;false;false;Piedmontese;The sign outside this restaurant in the centre of the typical village of Céres bears the words “Ristourànt Valàdess at Lanss con Oubèrgi”. Enjoy regional cuisine with a personalised twist, with local products from the valley featuring in many of the specialities served here, all accompanied by a good selection of regional, Italian and international wines. Outdoor dining area available in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9448;Cuoco di Bordo;Italy;Senigallia;lungomare Dante Alighieri 94, Senigallia, 60019, Italy;43.709146;13.2336576;39;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;An attractively furnished restaurant on the seafront with a small dining room and a veranda offering partial views of the sea. Fish takes pride of place on the menu, which focuses on raw fish dishes and classic recipes. The wine list is excellent, especially the whites (although the reds also include some impressive options) with many different vintages of the same wine available.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9449;Le Colonne;Italy;Santa Maria Maggiore;via Benefattori 7, Santa Maria Maggiore, 28857, Italy;46.1350178;8.4676249;34;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;In the small historic center of town, a couple with comprehensive management experience operates this well maintained, modest restaurant offering eclectic cuisine.;;[]
9450;Nives;Italy;Selva di Val Gardena;via Nives 4, Selva di Val Gardena, 39048, Italy;46.5561093;11.7569582;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Housed within the Boutique Hotel Nives, this contemporary, Alpine-style restaurant focuses on specialities from the Alto Adige (with the addition of a couple of fish dishes that nearly always feature on the menu), as well as large cuts of meat for sharing, served on a hot stone. An interesting wine list completes the picture.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9451;Ratanà;Italy;Milan;via G. de Castillia 28, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4857472;9.1930965;18;true;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;This lively, dynamic restaurant is in a converted building that once housed a cinema and later belonged to the railways. Top quality ingredients take pride of place here, while the pleasant outdoor area overlooking a small park is an added attraction.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9452;Soho;Italy;Genoa;via al Ponte Calvi 20 r, Genoa, 16124, Italy;44.41187;8.928815;59;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Situated in the heart of the historic centre just a stone’s throw from the aquarium, this designer-style restaurant has retained some of the palazzo’s historic features. Specialities here range from raw fish dishes to baby squid in a Genovese pesto sauce and slow-cooked octopus tentacles served with mashed potatoes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9453;Al Dragone;Italy;Vieste;via Duomo 8, Vieste, 71019, Italy;41.8817611;16.1810822;88;false;false;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;Occupying a natural cave, this typical restaurant serves traditional regional dishes prepared with care and imagination. House specialities include scampi in an almond crust.;Air conditioning;[]
9454;Scrigno del Duomo;Italy;Trento;piazza Duomo 29, Trento, 38122, Italy;46.0674352;11.1209763;23;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a stunning setting that includes Roman foundations, 15C frescoes and 19C furnishings. Choose between two types of cuisine: traditional ham, salami and regional dishes in the Wine Bar, or more sophisticated, inventive fare in the old cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9455;L'Osteria dell'Orologio;Italy;Fiumicino;via di Torre Clementina 114, Fiumicino, 00054, Italy;41.7714217;12.2303655;50;false;true;Seafood, Creative;Chef Marco Claroni brings style and finesse to this excellent restaurant which offers a good selection of fish dishes with an emphasis on carefully chosen local fish, including the occasional rare variety. The menu features raw dishes, classic marinated options (some with an Asian influence), cured fish and seafood and the restaurant’s own home-made bottarga (cured fish roe).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9457;Li Jalantuùmene;Italy;Monte Sant'Angelo;piazza de Galganis 9, Monte Sant'Angelo, 71037, Italy;41.7071157;15.955461;33;true;false;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;This rustic restaurant is faithful to the culinary traditions of the area, with an added spirit of discovery. It is located in a charming square. Pleasant outdoor area for summertime.;Terrace;[]
9458;Osteria Vecchia Noce;Italy;Vicopisano;Località Noce 39, Vicopisano, 56010, Italy;43.6907213;10.5333892;54;false;true;Tuscan, Classic Cuisine;This former 18C mill, located in the centre of a tiny medieval district on the outskirts of Uliveto Terme, boasts a warm, elegant ambience full of character. Expertly run by the same family for the past 35 years, it serves honest, traditional cuisine with a focus on regional recipes and an equal balance of meat and fish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9459;Bel Ami;Italy;Maglie;via Roma 86, Maglie, 73024, Italy;40.1234831;18.2971156;64;true;false;Seafood;A 19C palazzo renovated in modern style in its guestrooms and restaurant alike. The menu features fish and seafood, including raw dishes, and champagnes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9461;Alpenrose;Italy;Brixen;via delle Sette Chiese 1, loc. Pinzago, Brixen, 39042, Italy;46.706382;11.6390082;38;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated in a panoramic location a few kilometres outside Bressanone, this simple yet modern restaurant serves regional, classically prepared cuisine with an equally simple, contemporary feel plus a few dishes with the occasional Mediterranean influence. There are also elegant apartments available, plus a wellness space, for anyone wishing to extend their stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9462;Il Molo;Italy;San Leone;via Falcone Borsellino 2, San Leone, 92100, Italy;37.2631586;13.5788859;15;true;false;Sicilian, Classic Cuisine;Situated on the seafront facing the small tourist harbour of San Leone, this elegant restaurant boasts an attractive summer terrace with a relaxed ambience. Here you can savour a selection of regional fish and meat dishes prepared by the owner-chef with ingredients of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9463;Vecchia Sorni;Italy;Sorni;piazza Assunta 40, Sorni, 38015, Italy;46.1722192;11.1235507;55;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Situated in the northern wine-producing area of Trento, this trattoria is a real highlight, thanks to its delicious, beautifully presented cuisine which is always full of flavour. The menu includes regional dishes as well as more modern specialities (plus a few fish-based options) which can be enjoyed either in the typical dining room or out on the veranda (also open in winter) with its stunning views of the Adige valley.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9464;Alessandro Mecca al Castello di Grinzane Cavour;Italy;Grinzane Cavour;via Castello 5, Grinzane Cavour, 12060, Italy;44.6533268;7.9953423;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s no shortage of classic Piedmontese ingredients (such as anchovies, peppers and veal) on the menu at this restaurant, where traditional recipes are reinterpreted with a personalised and contemporary touch. Dishes from outside the region, including various fish-based options, also feature, while the restaurant aims to avoid food waste by using every single part of its ingredients where possible. The location in a splendid castle with 11C origins, once the home of Camillo Benso, count of Cavour, adds to the appeal.;Terrace;[]
9465;Albergaccio di Castellina;Italy;Castellina in Chianti;via Fiorentina 63, Castellina in Chianti, 53011, Italy;43.47298;11.27994;21;false;false;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;This rustic but stylish establishment is in wood and stone. Find Tuscan cuisine that leans towards imaginative dishes, without betraying regional flavours and produce.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9466;La Capuccina;Italy;Cureggio;via Novara 19/b, località Capuccina, Cureggio, 28060, Italy;45.6735288;8.4622472;28;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;A 16C farmhouse right out in the countryside, with its own working farm complete with livestock, vegetable gardens and vineyards. The enthusiastic family at the helm serve dishes made from their own produce alongside other top-quality, locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9467;La Corte;Italy;Follina;via Roma 24, Follina, 31051, Italy;45.9525845;12.1180814;37;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Nel lussuoso hotel Villa Abbazia, gli ambienti sontuosi impreziositi da camino, affreschi e decorazioni d'epoca, e l'altrettanto elegante servizio all'aperto per la bella stagione sono la cornice ideale per la cucina di Giuseppe Francica, giovane cuoco quasi allevato in casa. Declinata in menù vegetariano o degustazione scomponibili anche in piatti alla carta, la proposta dello chef è fresca, colorata, con erbe e verdure dall'orto di proprietà e materie prime provenienti da fidati produttori per lo più locali. Ottima scelta enoica con particolare passione per il Riesling. Il risultato è un'esperienza serale a tutto tondo, completata dal bistrot per una sosta più informale a pranzo.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9468;Cucina;Italy;Florence;Via Giano della Bella 3r, Florence, 50124, Italy;43.7648074;11.2401345;35;false;true;Tuscan, Home Cooking;At this restaurant, local ingredients (mainly from the market) take pride of place on the daily menu which changes in accordance with whatever produce is available at the time. The rustic-style dishes are full of intense flavours, with meat and vegetables often cooked in the wood-fired oven. The pleasantly informal dining room with its many cookery books dotted here and there was designed by the owner-architects themselves.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9469;Casamare;Italy;Salerno;corso Giuseppe Garibaldi 214, Salerno, 84121, Italy;40.676859;14.7640743;33;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Elegant and refined, this top-quality restaurant is the perfect choice for special occasions. Vietri ceramics, an open-view kitchen, fish on display and a successful mix of traditional and modern decor all combine to create an atmospheric setting in the dining room. As the restaurant’s name suggests, this is a good option for anyone who enjoys delicious classic fish and seafood dishes (mostly from Campania).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9470;Koinè;Italy;Legnano;vicolo Filippo Corridoni 2/c, Legnano, 20025, Italy;45.5931637;8.9194081;39;true;true;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;Whether you dine in the modern dining room at this centrally located palazzo or in the small courtyard in fine weather, Alberto Buratti offers a choice of tasting menus (including the vegetarian “1MQ d’orto”), alongside a concise à la carte. His cuisine includes a combination of local dishes (from classic risottos to breaded veal) and more creative fare.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9471;Dina;Italy;Gussago;via Santa Croce 1, Gussago, 25064, Italy;45.5838633;10.1562101;78;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;As is so often the case with the beautiful things in life, Dina showcases the culinary passion of owner-chef Alberto Gipponi who puts all his energy into preparing creative dishes and searching out elegant, vintage-style furnishings (mostly from the 1950s) which give Dina its delightfully unique atmosphere. The chef’s two tasting menus (one short, the second longer) take his guests on intimate journeys through Japanese cuisine, while highlighting the techniques and extraordinary ideas that define his personal style. These occasionally go hand-in-hand with regional recipes, such as in the delicious casoncelli pasta with Grana Padano cream (a speciality which calls for an encore!), and sometimes take the form of unusual dishes with the occasional hint of French influence. The chef’s main aim, in all cases, is to entertain his guests and in this he certainly succeeds!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9472;Sogno;Italy;San Felice del Benaco;via Porto San Felice 41, San Felice del Benaco, 25010, Italy;45.58019;10.55525;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This aptly named restaurant (“sogno” is the Italian for dream) really is a dream come true, especially in summer when you can dine on the romantic lakeside terrace. The delicious Mediterranean-style cuisine will more than satisfy your tastebuds, while there’s also the option of staying in the hotel of the same name. Private mooring available.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9474;Villa De Winckels;Italy;Tregnago;via Sorio 30, località Marcemigo, Tregnago, 37039, Italy;45.520783;11.1535074;41;true;true;Venetian, Classic Cuisine;This 16C villa, a period residence with many intimate dining rooms, boasts a picture-postcard setting. The cuisine is typical of the Veneto region, with dishes such as home-made pasta (with or without stuffing) and home-produced charcuterie on the menu. Named after General De Winckels who once lived here, the Cantina del Generale offers a wide selection of the best vintages which include local wines and labels from further field, with a focus on Amarone wines.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9475;Beccaccino;Italy;Sorico;via Boschetto 49, Sorico, 22010, Italy;46.167914;9.3935389;31;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated within a nature reserve, this recently renovated restaurant makes the most of its natural materials and bright, airy feel. The menu focuses on fish dishes made from freshwater and saltwater fish alike.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9476;Antico Albergo;Italy;Limito;via Dante Alighieri 18, Limito, 20096, Italy;45.482127;9.3298984;21;false;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;With its exposed bricks and beams, this restaurant housed in an 18C building has a historic feel. Delightful wisteria-shaded summer terrace, plus a menu featuring fish dishes and more creative options alongside traditional specialities from Lombardy.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9477;Dodici Fontane;Italy;Linguaglossa;contrada Arrigo, Linguaglossa, 95015, Italy;37.827248;15.126535;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The scenery that you drive through to get to this restaurant on the slopes of Mt Etna is as breathtaking and impressive as the charming luxury Villa Neri hotel in which it is housed. In the modern dining room, the chef serves personalised cuisine with a focus on Sicilian ingredients, resulting in occasionally complex dishes (meat and fish) which are showcased on his tasting menus. Guests can also choose dishes à la carte style, while the wine list includes an excellent and highly recommended selection of local Etna labels, including the property’s own wine (they also produce their own extra-virgin olive oil).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9478;Tana de 'l Ors;Italy;Forno di Zoldo;via Roma 28, Forno di Zoldo, 32012, Italy;46.3461088;12.1785249;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;A favourite with food-lovers, this restaurant serves lighter meals at lunchtime which are nonetheless carefully and imaginatively prepared (don’t miss the orsoburger!). In the evening, the best daily ingredients are prepared with a lightly modern touch – meat is the undisputed start of the show, although a few fish dishes also feature. One-room and two-room apartments are also available.;;[]
9479;Terrazza Danieli;Italy;Venice;riva degli Schiavoni, sestiere Castello 4196, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.433869;12.3420972;22;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Mirrors and fabrics add to the luxurious atmosphere in the dining room at this restaurant, but it is the outdoor terrace (open between May and October) with its 180° views of the lagoon and islands that is its crowning glory. The menu changes regularly in line with the seasons, and features fresh, local ingredients with the occasional hint of exotic spices as is only fitting for Venice!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9480;Il Ridotto;Italy;Venice;campo S.S. Filippo e Giacomo, sestiere Castello 4509, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.4351501;12.3416761;45;true;true;Creative;Both father and son are in the kitchen at this simple yet elegant small restaurant, serving up imaginative dishes that focus not only on local recipes and ingredients but also on gastronomic influences from the whole of Italy.;Air conditioning;[]
9482;La Cucina di Donna Carmela;Italy;Riposto;contrada Grotte 7, località Carruba di Riposto, Riposto, 95018, Italy;37.676624;15.179596;84;false;false;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Enjoy Sicilian specialities and the best produce from the hotel’s orchards and vegetable garden. Dine in a welcoming dining room or on the attractive outdoor terrace in the shade of the palm trees. All dishes are presented with contemporary - style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9483;Trattoria della Posta;Italy;Monforte d'Alba;Località Sant'Anna 87, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.5744898;7.9886563;54;true;false;Piedmontese, Classic Cuisine;Standing in open countryside, this country restaurant is decorated with elegant and romantic touches, such as silverware and candles. The menu features regional cuisine, including an excellent selection of the best local cheeses. Friendly welcome and experienced service.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9484;Il Calandrino;Italy;Rubano;via Liguria 1, loc. Sarmeola, Rubano, 35030, Italy;45.4216067;11.8095767;93;true;true;Contemporary, Italian;Situated next to the three-Michelin-starred Le Calandre (and run by the same family), Il Calandrino is an elegant and eclectic restaurant which includes a bar-cum-pasticceria that is well worth visiting at any time of day. The cuisine here ranges from creative dishes such as hare cappuccino in red wine to classic house favourites such as Erminio’s legendary tartare and the pazientina cake with zabaione.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9485;Coppola Rossa;Italy;Manfredonia;via Maddalena 28, Manfredonia, 71043, Italy;41.6267253;15.9154397;38;true;false;Seafood;Situated in the historic centre not far from the sea, this typical family - run restaurant specialises in fish and seafood. There is an antipasto buffet and a good choice of fish, as well as an open - view grill used in winter for cooking meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9486;Da Manuela;Italy;Isola Sant'Antonio;frazione Capraglia, Isola Sant'Antonio, 15050, Italy;45.0352935;8.8253002;88;true;true;Country cooking;Specialities from Lower Piedmont and the Lomellina region are accompanied by a few freshwater fish dishes and traditional frogs’ legs on the menu at this restaurant, which also offers a fine array of delicious cheeses. The wine selection is also excellent.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9487;Hostaria alla Tavernetta;Italy;Udine;via Artico di Prampero 2, Udine, 33100, Italy;46.0617002;13.2372018;83;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This fine restaurant immediately puts you at your ease thanks to a very jovial and friendly atmosphere. The lit fireplace, wood furniture with stylish linen runners and background music make for an excellent break. In addition to traditional courses such as cjarsons or the typical frico, there are more seasonal and Mediterranean fish dishes. Vegan menu available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9488;Trattoria 'petito;Italy;Forlì;via Corridoni 14, Forlì, 47121, Italy;44.2179267;12.0461155;79;true;false;Cuisine from Romagna, Seasonal Cuisine;Located on the outskirts of Forlì’s charming historic centre, this simple, modern yet attractive restaurant serves eclectic and varied cuisine. More traditional fare on offer includes an excellent selection of hams and grilled meats, as well as delicious tagliatelle al ragù, while the menu also features a few more creative options including a few fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9489;Federico II;Italy;Termoli;via Duomo 30, Termoli, 86039, Italy;42.0043381;14.9973442;93;true;false;Seafood;A quiet restaurant right in the historic centre, just a stone’s throw from the cathedral. The young owner prepares creative dishes from the fresh fish and seafood that he purchases on a daily basis.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9490;La Braja;Italy;Montemagno;via San Giovanni Bosco 11, Montemagno, 14030, Italy;44.981582;8.3208927;70;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;A traditional Piedmontese restaurant, where owner Giuseppe Palermino welcomes guests to his elegant dining room with his consummate style. The specialities here have a regional focus with the occasional influence from further afield. The “tajarin al ristretto di coniglio” (shredded rabbit pasta) and the superb cheese trolley are particularly recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9491;Patauner;Italy;Settequerce;via Bolzano 6, Settequerce, 39018, Italy;46.5112328;11.2740597;31;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Despite its simple appearance, this restaurant on the side of the road dates from the 17C and has been run by the same family for the past century. Today, the third and fourth generations work side by side in the kitchen, preparing dishes with a strong regional flavour. Highlights include the white Terlano asparagus in season and offal dishes throughout the year.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9492;Da Nilo;Italy;Cetona;piazza Garibaldi 31, Cetona, 53040, Italy;42.9645008;11.9004364;73;false;true;Tuscan;Overlooking the picturesque main square of Cetona, which can be admired from the outdoor tables, this restaurant has a classic ambience. Typical Tuscan cuisine with an emphasis on meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9493;Quartopiano;Italy;Rimini;via Chiabrera 34/c, Rimini, 47924, Italy;44.04775;12.59455;37;false;false;Creative, Seafood;Perhaps because of its out - of - the - way location in a business district where you would never normally expect to find a restaurant, this restaurant has made every effort to become one of the best in the region, aided by its skilful and gifted chef. Creative cuisine accompanied by an excellent wine list, with a panoramic roof garden for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9494;Ristorante Da Anita - Chalet Prà delle Nasse;Italy;San Martino di Castrozza;via Cavallazza 24, località Prà delle Nasse, San Martino di Castrozza, 38054, Italy;46.2631715;11.79799;24;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Alpine;This family-run restaurant is surrounded by views of the Dolomites that are particularly impressive from the outdoor terrace in summer. A historic culinary stalwart among San Martino di Castrozza restaurants, Prà delle Nasse focuses on regional mountain cuisine, although a few more personalised dishes also feature on the menu. The desserts include the grandmother’s traditional tarts alongside more contemporary options.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9495;Da Politano;Italy;Boves;via Santuario 125, Boves, 12012, Italy;44.3328613;7.5238243;27;true;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;At the kitchen in this restaurant, father-and-son team Claudio and Luca (the latter with experience in numerous renowned restaurants) reinterpret local traditions in their enticing, generous and contemporary-style dishes (fish also features on the menu). The result is top-quality cuisine, which is served by Luca’s friendly and enthusiastic mother Ivana.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9496;Antica Osteria del Ponte;Italy;Cassinetta di Lugagnano;piazza Gaetano Negri 9, Cassinetta di Lugagnano, 20081, Italy;45.4259722;8.9098057;89;true;true;Italian Contemporary;This renowned restaurant in Lombardy has made its mark on the history of Italian cuisine and now has a new young couple at the helm and a new classic-contemporary menu. There’s also an interesting and reasonably priced three-dish menu at lunchtime, as well as the option of ordering an informal gastronomic picnic box. The beautiful natural setting of Cassinetta di Lugagnano and its canal completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9497;Scaraboci;Italy;Marciana Marina;via XX Settembre 27, Marciana Marina, 57033, Italy;42.80472;10.19958;87;true;true;Creative, Seafood;Located just a few metres from the enchanting seafront at Marciana, this restaurant is one of the island’s gastronomic gems, offering a menu that features interesting combinations of beautifully presented meat and especially fish dishes There’s also a private terrace for romantic dining in summer (book well in advance) and although wines are not available by the glass, choosing a top-quality half-bottle is always an option.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9498;Cacciani;Italy;Frascati;via Diaz 15, Frascati, 00044, Italy;41.8075835;12.6788993;56;false;true;Cuisine from Lazio, Classic Cuisine;One of the most famous restaurants in the Castelli Romani region in 2022 celebrated 100 years of life under the management of the same family: the Cacciani. Authentic and excellent regional cuisine, served in a welcoming dining room, with the open - view kitchen on one side and a panoramic terrace on the other.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9499;La Terrazza;Italy;Torbole;via Benaco 24, Torbole, 38069, Italy;45.8689645;10.8749638;82;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;A small indoor dining room and a veranda with a lake view and sliding windows which open completely in summer provide the setting for regionally inspired dishes and lake specialities at this restaurant.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
9500;Sichelburg;Italy;Pfalzen;via Castello 1a, Pfalzen, 39030, Italy;46.8144957;11.8829237;40;true;false;Creative;Treat yourself to a great meal in an idyllic setting in this village restaurant occupying the first floor of a castle dating back to the 13C. The romantic dining rooms are furnished with wood, while the creative cuisine focuses on typical mountain produce.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9501;Il Verso del Ghiottone;Italy;Dogliani;via Demagistris 5, Dogliani, 12063, Italy;44.5279714;7.9490561;27;true;false;Piedmontese, Seafood;This restaurant housed in an 18C building has a warm, rustic feel with terracotta, stone and brick decor and black tables with American-style place mats, resulting in a vibrant yet elegant atmosphere where the service is informal and yet also highly professional. The cuisine is inspired by regional recipes which are reinterpreted and given a lighter flavour. There’s no shortage of interesting fish dishes, including the exquisite red shrimp, which is half-cooked, half-raw and served with passion-fruit caramel.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9502;Trattoria del Nuovo Macello;Italy;Milan;via Cesare Lombroso 20, Milan, 20137, Italy;45.4560446;9.2267357;91;false;true;Lombardian, Modern Cuisine;Named after the slaughterhouse opened opposite the premises in 1927, this restaurant was taken over 30 years later by the grandfather of one of the current partners, as he was convinced that the restaurant’s busy location would contribute to its success – and he wasn’t wrong! The traditional, regional cuisine served here is reinterpreted with a contemporary flavour and includes delicious specialities such as cotoletta alla milanese made from meat matured for 40 days.;Air conditioning;[]
9503;Antica Pesa;Italy;Rome;via Garibaldi 18, Rome, 00153, Italy;41.8906;12.46638;95;true;true;Roman, Cuisine from Lazio;Typical Roman dishes made from carefully selected ingredients grace the menu of this restaurant, which is housed in a grain storehouse that once belonged to the neighbouring Papal State. Large paintings by contemporary artists hang on the walls and there is a small lounge with a fireplace near the entrance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9504;Osteria dei Vespri;Italy;Palermo;piazza Croce dei Vespri 6, Palermo, 90133, Italy;38.114758;13.3658272;30;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the palazzo where the famous ball scene in the “The Leopard” by Luchino Visconti was filmed, this restaurant serves cuisine that moves with the times, featuring modern dishes made from local ingredients, while a friendly welcome from the long-established owners adds to the appeal. Cocktails, tapas and simpler yet equally delicious cuisine is served in the Occhiovivo! Bistrot next door, the name of which refers to a Sicilian saying which means “Be careful!”.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9505;Riva;Italy;Ponte dell'Olio;via Riva 16, Ponte dell'Olio, 29028, Italy;44.8568639;9.6288342;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a small village with a fascinating crenellated castle, this restaurant is run by a husband and wife team. They offer a refined cuisine that is a balanced blend of local recipes and creativity.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9506;Antica Trattoria del Gallo;Italy;Vigano;via Privata Gerli 3, Vigano, 20083, Italy;45.3799348;9.0245013;22;true;false;Lombardian;A splendid example of a country trattoria, which has been delighting its guests with typical dishes from Lombardy for over a century. Meals are served either in the attractive vintage-style dining room or, in fine weather, outdoors under the Virginia creeper and mature wisteria. Truly enchanting!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9507;San Michele;Italy;Fagagna;via Castello di Fagagna 33, Fagagna, 33034, Italy;46.114908;13.0877924;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated next to the ruins of the old castle and the small church of San Michele, this 13C building, thought to have once housed a guardroom, is now home to a small restaurant serving regional, seasonal cuisine with a modern twist. During the week, the restaurant offers a lunchtime menu of top-quality snacks (the Venetian “cicchetti”), as well as a few “primi” and desserts.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9508;L'Angolino da Filippo;Italy;Marina di San Vito;via Sangritana 1, Marina di San Vito, 66038, Italy;42.3083754;14.4459796;68;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;A red door just a few metres from the sea marks the entrance to this long-established restaurant (a family-run business for over a century), which boasts two small dining rooms with brick-vaulted ceilings and a lively atmosphere. Unsurprisingly, the menu focuses on fish and seafood specialities, which showcase a combination of delicious modern and traditional flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
9509;L'antica Pizzeria da Michele;Italy;Naples;via Cesare Sersale 1/7, Naples, 80139, Italy;40.8497214;14.2634903;100;true;false;Pizza;You can really sense the history of Naples in this pizzeria, which was founded in 1870 and boasts a lively, convivial atmosphere – if you sit alone, you’re sure to find yourself sharing travellers’ tales with fellow diners by the end of your meal! Note that the restaurant only serves two types of pizza – Margherita (tomato and mozzarella) and Marinara (tomato, oregano and garlic). Numbered tickets are issued to diners, who then take a seat and are called in turn (open all day). A second restaurant has recently been opened nearby.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
9510;Pierre Alexis 1877;Italy;Courmayeur;via Marconi 50/a, Courmayeur, 11013, Italy;45.7894165;6.9742888;63;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a house dating from 1877 (as the name suggests) in the pedestrian heart of old Courmayeur, this restaurant serves traditional cuisine with an imaginative twist. In spring, wild herbs picked in the surrounding valleys are added to the dishes.;;[]
9511;Da Gigetto;Italy;Miane;via De Gasperi 5, Miane, 31050, Italy;45.942004;12.0900375;88;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A long-established restaurant with a renowned reputation thanks to the enthusiasm of the family at the helm and the excellent cuisine on offer. The carefully designed menu focuses mainly on classic regional dishes, yet also includes more contemporary options and even a few fish-based specialities, while the impressive wine list features more than 1 000 different labels, including some surprising names and various vertical wine-tasting options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9512;La Maison Delfino;Italy;Moncalieri;via Lagrange 4, borgo Mercato, Moncalieri, 10024, Italy;45.0001263;7.6736825;70;true;true;Seafood;This small, elegant restaurant outside the centre is enthusiastically run by two brothers: round tables and well - kept dining room for savoring seafood specialities.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9513;Doppio Gusto;Italy;Milazzo;via Luigi Rizzo 1/2, Milazzo, 98057, Italy;38.2200717;15.241736;50;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Fish specialities take pride of place on the menu of this elegant, contemporary - style restaurant with friendly, informal service. Good selection of wines, also available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9514;Aquariva;Italy;Padenghe sul Garda;via Marconi 57, Padenghe sul Garda, 25080, Italy;45.49376;10.51139;62;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Renowned for its fish, this restaurant offers a good choice of raw fish and a delicious plateau royale. The elegant, spacious dining room boasts a restful colour scheme and views of the lake through its picture windows.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9515;Fana Ladina;Italy;San Vigilio di Marebbe;via Plan de Corones 10, San Vigilio di Marebbe, 39030, Italy;46.6997472;11.9311374;44;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;This restaurant occupies one of the oldest houses in San Vigilio. It serves typical Ladin specialities in wood - clad dining rooms and has a delightful Stube. Among the various specialities on the menu, the crafun (savoury krapfe stuffed with a ragú sauce) are particularly worth sampling.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9516;L'Accanto;Italy;Vico Equense;via Santa Maria Vecchia 2, loc. Seiano, Vico Equense, 80066, Italy;40.6584322;14.4213407;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Having left the busy coastal road behind you, you come into the peaceful and luxurious enclave of the Angiolieri hotel and its classically elegant L’Accanto restaurant. As soon as the weather allows, dinner is served outdoors on one of the most spectacular terraces in the area, overlooking the Bay of Naples and its breathtaking sunsets. The top-quality cuisine focuses mainly on the abundant recipes and ingredients of Campania.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9517;All'Olivo;Italy;Lucca;piazza San Quirico 1, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8429692;10.5054482;47;true;true;Tuscan, Classic Cuisine;Situated in one of the typical squares of Lucca’s beautiful historic centre, this restaurant boasts four dining rooms – the central room is adorned with shelves of wine bottles, while the others are decorated with drawings by authors who have visited the legendary Lucca Comics festival. The cuisine is regional, with fish and meat dishes featuring on the menu, plus there’s an attractive outdoor space for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9518;Il Funghetto;Italy;Latina;strada Litoranea 11412, località Borgo Grappa, Latina, 04010, Italy;41.3919837;12.9460743;39;false;false;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;Fish and seafood take pride of place on the menu at this restaurant just a few minutes’ drive from the beach. The owner-chef (the second generation since 1973) is happy to advise guests on food and wine choices alike, offering a wide choice of wines from all over Italy and around the world. Welcoming dining room and shady arbour. Gluten-free options available.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9519;Alex;Italy;Marina di Pietrasanta;via Versilia 157/159, Marina di Pietrasanta, 55045, Italy;43.923157;10.2039446;69;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;Modern, personalised dishes with something for everyone and a careful balance between meat and fish options. The three tasting menus showcase the chef’s culinary philosophy, all served in a trendy atmosphere with an ethnic touch. The wine list is one of the restaurant’s highlights, featuring an excellent selection of international labels, all of which can be purchased at the wine bar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9520;Osteria della Corte;Italy;La Spezia;via Napoli 86, La Spezia, 19122, Italy;44.108524;9.815648;37;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This small restaurant with 17C stone walls and exposed stone arches also boasts a courtyard for summer dining, while the delicious yet simple cuisine focuses on fish and seafood. Rich flavours are a must for chef Silvia Cardelli, whose classic dishes include spaghetti with seafood and Tournedos Rossini. There’s also an excellent selection of wines (700 labels), with interesting recommendations provided by the sommelier.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9521;Antico Ristorante Forassiepi;Italy;Montecarlo;via della Contea 1, Montecarlo, 55015, Italy;43.8496128;10.6703504;95;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;This restaurant is renowned in the province of Lucca, thanks to the reliable owners who have been at the helm here (the restaurant’s history goes back to the early 20C) since 2004. With its elegant decor and courteous and attentive service, the restaurant has a charming ambience in summer when meals are served alfresco with stunning views of the typical Tuscan hills, valleys and villages all around. The restaurant also owes its success to its cuisine, which focuses on regional specialities (both meat and fish) reinterpreted with a modern twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9522;Chichibio;Italy;Roccaraso;via Guglielmo Marconi 1, Roccaraso, 67037, Italy;41.846474;14.080086;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Cuisine from Abruzzo;Despite its lack of awards, this restaurant stands out for the quality of its cuisine. Situated in the town centre, it has a small intimate dining room with just a few tables (it’s best to book ahead) that acts as a backdrop for good-quality dishes made from local, seasonal ingredients, as well as a few modern and imaginative fish options. Highly recommended!;Air conditioning;[]
9523;Da Andrea;Italy;Marina di Cecina;viale della Vittoria 68, Marina di Cecina, 57023, Italy;43.29478;10.49746;75;false;true;Seafood;This white, modern and minimalist - style restaurant has lovely views of the Tyrrhenian sea from its dining room and summer terrace. Not surprisingly, fish and seafood take pride of place on the menu, with daily specials based on the catch of the day announced at your table.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9524;Ippogrifo;Italy;Genoa;via Gestro 9 r, Genoa, 16129, Italy;44.3973;8.9453;25;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This elegant restaurant with a smart, classic feel is situated in the Expo Fiera area not far from the city centre. Ever since it opened in 1982, this restaurant has been a reliable choice for top-quality fish (although meat also features on the menu), which is prepared using classic techniques and recipes. Highlights include dishes such as tuna and amberjack carpaccio, warm seafood salad, grilled fish, fish cooked in typical Ligurian style with potatoes and Taggiasche olives, and fish soup with croutons.;Air conditioning;[]
9525;Enoteca San Nicola;Italy;Bobbio;contrada di San Nicola 11/a, Bobbio, 29022, Italy;44.7668479;9.3853918;85;true;false;Country cooking;This fascinating little restaurant set in the maze of narrow streets around the abbey of San Colombano invites you to its succession of small dining rooms decorated with pictures and wine bottles. Atmospheric rooms, each with an open fire.;Interesting wine list;[]
9526;Ai Gondolieri;Italy;Venice;fondamenta de l'Ospedaleto, sestiere Dorsoduro 366, Venice, 30123, Italy;45.4303027;12.3307402;64;true;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated behind the Guggenheim museum, this rustic restaurant with wood panelling on the walls offers a meat-based menu that focuses on traditional, regional cuisine (the braised rack of lamb with spinach tortino with butter and parmesan cheese is superb). The well-stocked wine cellar is home to a huge selection of white, red and sparkling wines, plus there’s an extensive choice of cocktails. At Ai Gondolieri, enjoy a good glass of wine accompanied by typical Venetian fare such as cured hams and sweet-and-sour vegetables.;Air conditioning;[]
9527;Tavola di Guido;Italy;Castellina in Chianti;Località Le Piazze 41, Castellina in Chianti, 53011, Italy;43.4535857;11.2410406;23;false;false;Tuscan;This restaurant is as comfortable as the rest of the hotel, while its outdoor dining area allows guests to enjoy the peace and tranquillity of the beautiful garden. Chef Guido creates dishes with a regional influence, some of which are more modern in flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9528;Svevia;Italy;Termoli;via Giudicato Vecchio 24, Termoli, 86039, Italy;42.0056596;14.9973612;73;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in the wine cellars of a historic palazzo, this restaurant is a successful combination of the traditional and the modern. The cuisine focuses on the fish and seafood specialities of the Molise region, with only a few meat dishes on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
9529;Santa Teresa;Italy;Genoa;via di Porta Soprana 55 r, Genoa, 16123, Italy;44.4062279;8.9335702;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Located just a stone’s throw from the house thought to have belonged to Christopher Columbus, this restaurant boasts welcoming dining rooms where the experienced Scala family serve seasonal, regional cuisine with a focus on fish and seafood dishes (often including the famous Genovese “cappon magro”, a type of seafood salad). The menu also features a few meat dishes, beautifully presented and with a light contemporary touch. The good wine list means that you’ll have no problem finding a suitable pairing for your meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9530;ZELO;Italy;Milan;via Gesù 6/8, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.46964;9.195502;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The elegant ZELO restaurant enjoys a beautiful setting in the garden of a 15C inner courtyard, which also boasts an attractive summer terrace. The cuisine is modern in style, created by a chef who uses the best Italian ingredients to prepare creative and contemporary dishes, as well as a few Italian classic favourites such as vitello tonnato and breaded veal. Some dishes are not available at lunchtime, when they are replaced by salads, while in the evening raw fish and seafood options take centre stage.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9531;Da Oscar;Italy;Barcuzzi;via Barcuzzi 16, Barcuzzi, 25017, Italy;45.4890609;10.4967641;40;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Standing on the hills overlooking Lake Garda, this attractive, spacious restaurant has an elegant atmosphere. There is a delightful terrace for alfresco dining in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9532;Il Cascinalenuovo;Italy;Isola d'Asti;SS 231  Asti-Alba 15, Isola d'Asti, 14057, Italy;44.8264017;8.1694186;77;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Having been in business for over 50 years and with a newly expanded team, Il Cascinalenuovo continues to serve its classic favourites (such as veal’s tongue millefeuille and foie gras with port jelly, and Piedmontese tonnato) while also extending its repertoire to include new options, including fish. The Ferretto brothers are still at the helm here, one front of house, the other in the kitchen. If the weather allows, book a table in the attractive outdoor space overlooking the garden and swimming pool.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9533;Da Fausto;Italy;Fondi;piazza Cesare Beccaria 6, Fondi, 04022, Italy;41.361339;13.4235667;60;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated in these premises since 2015, Fausto has become a local favourite thanks to the quality and style of its cuisine which combines classic flavours and regional influences. Two of the chef’s great passions (chocolate and ice cream) always feature on the dessert menu, while the cool outdoor space near the entrance adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9534;Al Grop;Italy;Tavagnacco;via Matteotti 7, Tavagnacco, 33010, Italy;46.1261624;13.2085225;50;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;A long - established, rustic - style restaurant with an impressive open fireplace in the middle of the dining room. The cuisine is seasonal, with grilled meats and white asparagus on the menu at certain times of year. Comfortable apartments with a kitchen area, as well as a delightful courtyard.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9535;Canapone;Italy;Grosseto;piazza Dante 3, Grosseto, 58100, Italy;42.7592993;11.1140761;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In elegant settings or, in the summer, overlooking the splendid Piazza Dante, you will find a fragrant Maremma cuisine based on excellent ingredients. The solid family management makes it a valid point of reference. Next door, Osteria Canapino offers more traditional and informal cuisine.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9536;Osteria del Mirasole;Italy;San Giovanni in Persiceto;via Matteotti 17/a, San Giovanni in Persiceto, 40017, Italy;44.6389772;11.1856784;17;false;true;Emilian;A delightful restaurant overflowing with memories of the past, where the top-quality cuisine has strong roots in the gastronomic traditions of this region, including a selection of meats cooked over the charcoal grill. Fans of Emilian cuisine will be happy to return to this restaurant time and time again, never tiring of its delicious regional fare.;Air conditioning;[]
9537;Il Sanlorenzo;Italy;Rome;via dei Chiavari 4/5, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8953002;12.4741868;50;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;A historic palazzo built over the foundations of the Teatro Pompeo is home to this atmospheric restaurant, which brings together history and contemporary art. However, the real star is the fish on the menu, most of which comes from the island of Ponza, and is served either raw or cooked very simply in a modern style.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9538;El Primero;Italy;Origgio;largo Umberto Boccioni 3, Origgio, 21040, Italy;45.602239;9.0256959;16;true;false;South American, Grills;Situated in a building with a striking appearance (the Uruguay Pavilion in Expo 2015), this restaurant boasts stunning views of the mountains in the distance. Inside, the large dining room acts as a backdrop for South American cuisine with a focus on grilled specialities. A simple atmosphere and friendly service add to the appeal.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9539;Don Camillo;Italy;Syracuse;via Maestranza 96, Ortigia, Syracuse, 96100, Italy;37.0607669;15.2967023;88;false;false;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Miteco, Artemide, Archestrato, and La Nostra Storia are the names of the menus at this restaurant, all of which showcase the ambitious Sicilian cuisine created by chef Guarneri, a lover of beauty and fine wine. The dining room is traditional in style, with tufa walls dating from the 15C, period wood furnishings and wrought-iron chandeliers. The delicious cuisine is expertly prepared, while the service is attentive and professional.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9540;Dim Sum;Italy;Milan;via Nino Bixio 29, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.4724299;9.2110853;98;true;true;Cantonese, Contemporary;This restaurant with a partially open kitchen introduces its guests to the delicious specialities of Guangzhou and Southern China in rooms full of decorative details. The small dishes which characterise the culinary traditions of these regions have been refined with just a hint of contemporary flavour. A truly authentic Chinese dining experience.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9542;La Ferrata;Italy;Pordenone;via Gorizia 7, Pordenone, 33170, Italy;45.954875;12.6595471;20;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Copper pots and lids and photos of locomotives adorn the walls of this friendly and welcoming trattoria. Enjoy generous portions of local specialities, including delicious snails cooked in butter.;Air conditioning;[]
9543;Il Tufo Allegro;Italy;Pitigliano;vicolo della Costituzione 5, Pitigliano, 58017, Italy;42.6339811;11.6670793;88;true;false;Tuscan;In the heart of the Etruscan resort, close to the synagogue: Tuscan dishes, a small restaurant with a well stocked wine cellar and two dining rooms hewn out of the rock.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9544;Sa Musciara;Italy;Portoscuso;lungomare C. Colombo 15, Portoscuso, 09010, Italy;39.2032205;8.3791258;62;true;true;Seafood;A modern, fresh restaurant situated next to the town hall, with views of the sea from the dining room. Fish and seafood carefully prepared by the owner - chef (also a sailing enthusiast) take pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9545;Durnwald;Italy;Gsies;via Nikolaus Amhof 6, località Durna in Selva, Gsies, 39030, Italy;46.767593;12.1789264;48;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A delicious plate of Schlutzkrapfen (ravioli stuffed with spinach and ricotta) is just what’s needed after a good day’s skiing or a hike through the woods. And that’s not all – Durnwald is an excellent place to appreciate the Alto Adige, both in terms of its landscapes, which can be admired from the dining room windows, and its cuisine, which keeps alive the genuine traditions of the region. Specialities include Valle Aurina cheese with pumpkin seed oil, and sfoglie di patate (potato fritters) with sauerkraut, sausage and mustard sauce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9546;Tanzer;Italy;Issengo;via del Paese 1, Issengo, 39030, Italy;46.8150207;11.8623126;20;true;true;Creative;Situated right under the bell tower in a small hamlet, this restaurant has two romantic Stube - style dining rooms. One is decorated in elegant 19C - style, while the other is simpler and more rustic in feel, dating from the 17C. Local cuisine with the occasional modern twist.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9547;La Péniche;Italy;Marina di Massa;via Lungo Brugiano 3, Marina di Massa, 54100, Italy;44.0105909;10.0990077;22;true;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;This little corner of France right on the Brugiano canal occupies a house-on-stilts and has a unique, warm and romantic ambience thanks to its combination of colonial style and Parisian decor. Specialities include raw fish and seafood, including oysters, although you’ll also find meat-based dishes on the menu. The tables on the deck – which brings to mind a barge on the Seine – are very popular in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9548;Il Cipresso - Da Cioni;Italy;Loro Ciuffenna;via Alcide De Gasperi 28, Loro Ciuffenna, 52024, Italy;43.5883319;11.6270812;75;false;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;Standing on a round terrace, this restaurant with a fairly plain interior serves dishes made from some of the best produce of the region – cured hams, bread, pasta and famous Tuscan meats. The restaurant also offers simple, rustic - style guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9549;Bove's;Italy;Cuneo;via Dronero 2/b, Cuneo, 12100, Italy;44.392628;7.549974;44;false;true;Meats and Grills;The grandson of Martini, one of the most famous butchers in Italy, focuses almost entirely on meat dishes in this restaurant in Cuneo, as well as a few first courses, salads and gourmet hamburgers. The two nostalgic dining rooms have a typical 1940s bistro ambience.;Terrace;[]
9550;QB DuePuntoZero;Italy;Salò;via Pietro da Salò 23, Salò, 25087, Italy;45.6037558;10.5199691;28;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;On the lakefront facing the small port, this modern, simply styled restaurant has a pleasant area for summer dining. Contemporary cuisine made from carefully selected produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9551;Bistrot Donatella;Italy;Oviglio;piazza Umberto I 1, Oviglio, 15026, Italy;44.8600974;8.486985;92;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant in a small village dominated by a bell tower boasts a charming inner courtyard which provides a romantic setting for a meal in fine weather. The Piedmontese cuisine served here is prepared using top-quality ingredients. A friendly welcome completes the picture, making this an enjoyable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9552;La Masseria;Italy;Modena;via Chiesa 61, località Marzaglia, Modena, 41123, Italy;44.6513;10.80694;86;false;false;Apulian;What used to be an old watermill is now a welcoming restaurant with a rustic feel and a beautiful garden for summer dining. Home-made bread and pasta, typical specialities from Puglia, savoury pies and grilled meats all feature on the menu.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9553;Innocenti Evasioni;Italy;Milan;via Giuseppe Candiani 66, Milan, 20158, Italy;45.5044912;9.1686366;39;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Chef Tommaso Arrigoni’s restaurant has a wonderful new location, where floor-to-ceiling windows in the spacious modern dining room overlook a large Mediterranean garden that is just as appealing as the Zen-inspired outdoor space at his previous venue. The chef’s colourful cuisine is showcased on three tasting menus, from which dishes can also be selected à la carte. The interesting “Delle Mezze” menu allows guests to sample several small portions of different dishes.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9554;Winter Garden Florence;Italy;Florence;piazza Ognissanti 1, Florence, 50123, Italy;43.7721696;11.2450988;85;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Horse-drawn carriages once entered the old courtyard of the St Regis hotel, now converted into an elegant winter garden which also includes a cocktail bar with sofas and armchairs. Seasonality and local gems are fundamental pillars of the modern Mediterranean cuisine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9555;L'Oste Scuro;Italy;Verona;vicolo San Silvestro 10, Verona, 37122, Italy;45.4382876;10.9880573;86;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Nice family trattoria atmosphere in a popular, central fashionable location that stresses the freshness of the proprietor's dishes: fish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9556;Kandoo Nippon Restaurant;Italy;Cremona;piazza Cadorna 15, Cremona, 26100, Italy;45.1324181;10.0162531;23;false;false;Japanese, Classic Cuisine;Dark colours and a modern decor are the main features of this excellent restaurant which occupies two floors and is highly recommended for its gourmet Japanese specialities. Cooked and raw dishes feature on the menu, plus there’s a quicker “combo formula” available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9557;Rosita;Italy;Finale Ligure;via Manie 67, Finale Ligure, 17024, Italy;44.1791461;8.366972;22;true;false;Ligurian, Classic Cuisine;Decorated in the same simple and rustic style as the Hotel Rosita in which it is housed, this restaurant boasts an attractive terrace overlooking the sea and the coast (call in advance to book one of the tables with the best view), which more than compensates for the narrow, winding road that you have to follow to get here. The delicious cuisine is regional in flavour, including seafood options such as the excellent stuffed baby squid in a sauce served with mashed potatoes, and meat dishes that include a tasty rabbit casserole.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9558;La Quartina;Italy;Mergozzo;via Pallanza 20, Mergozzo, 28802, Italy;45.9613357;8.4554218;62;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Outdoor service in the summer on the terrace with an exceptional view of the lake. Original furnishings and extremely well kept rooms. Menu including lake specialities. The rooms are simple, comfortable and always neat and tidy.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9559;Locanda '800;Italy;Negrar;via Moron 46, Negrar, 37024, Italy;45.5168102;10.9270138;71;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Whether you dine indoors, on the bright veranda or in the wine cellar with its barrels and wines produced by the estate, you’ll enjoy cuisine at this family-run restaurant which has gained a reputation in the region for its balance of meat and fish dishes. Excellent service and a pleasant setting in a rustic building surrounded by greenery.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9561;Filippo;Italy;Pietrasanta;via Barsanti 45, Pietrasanta, 55045, Italy;43.9559386;10.2325299;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;In this modern and elegant restaurant, Filippo chooses three products every day and creates a surprise meal for guests with these ingredients. An original idea which is certainly worth a try, but for less adventurous diners there is also a small menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9562;Bislakko;Italy;Vercelli;via Thaon de Revel 87, Vercelli, 13100, Italy;45.3037404;8.4461672;80;false;true;Country cooking, Creative;This unusually named restaurant (bislacco is the Italian for eccentric) delights guests with its fine cuisine, especially its delicious chocolate desserts. There is even a chocolate fountain for guests.;;[]
9563;Grantosco;Italy;Grosseto;via Solferino 4, Grosseto, 58100, Italy;42.7599627;11.1155178;55;true;true;Tuscan, Country cooking;This elegant yet informal bistro - style restaurant is in the town centre. It is the ideal place to sample excellent cuisine made largely from local produce from the Maremma. You are sure to receive a warm welcome from the owner, who is the life and soul of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9564;Il Michelaccio;Italy;Genoa;via Frugoni 49 r, Genoa, 16121, Italy;44.4035;8.939671;19;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;A veritable bistro in a modern style and in a central position, a short distance from the famous Via XX Settembre, where the chef patron turns his hand to a fragrant cuisine, from the market, often dedicated to the Ligurian tradition (cream of potato with Genoese sea snails), but opening up to Italian flavors (pappa al pomodoro and burratina). He sometimes allows himself an imaginative touch, as in the risotto with anchovies and raspberries. Only natural wines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9565;Trattoria Leoni;Italy;Barbian;via Ricò 42, Barbian, 43035, Italy;44.6677462;10.2376867;88;true;true;Emilian, Regional Cuisine;Situated amid gently rolling hills, this restaurant with large picture windows boasts fine views of the surrounding countryside, which can be enjoyed even more from its summer terrace. For many years, the Leoni family have served Parma specialities here, including excellent salumi and recipes handed down by their grandmother, as well as typical mountain ingredients such as mushrooms and game.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9566;Al Vedel;Italy;Vedole;via Vedole 68, Vedole, 43052, Italy;44.9223062;10.3592101;27;false;false;Emilian;A temple for the production of culatello ham, which feature in the dishes served, and is also matured on the premises (the maturing rooms are well worth a visit). Al Vedel also serves other regional specialities such as typical stuffed pasta dishes, as well as more imaginative fare. An elegant, long - established restaurant now run by the sixth generation of the same family.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9567;La Serra;Italy;Positano;via Marconi 169, località Belvedere Fornillo, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6262458;14.4785098;40;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Despite its bright, elegant and airy feel, the panoramic dining room at this restaurant takes second place to the delightful, romantic terrace which boasts splendid views of the sea, the port and the hills around Positano. Here, a new chef with an impressive CV delights guests (and non-residents) at the charming Le Agavi hotel with his selection of tasting menus. Top-quality ingredients take centre stage, some sourced from his own organic kitchen garden, as well as traditional dishes to which he adds modern and updated twists.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9568;Il Sale;Italy;San Vincenzo;via San Bartolo 100, frazione San Carlo, San Vincenzo, 57027, Italy;43.0900139;10.568827;39;false;true;Tuscan;Il Sale stands in a region where the typical hills, cypresses and olive trees of Tuscany meet the sea. The connection between the land and the quality of the cuisine served here is reinforced by the amount of produce grown by the restaurant itself.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9569;28 Posti;Italy;Milan;via Corsico 1, Milan, 20144, Italy;45.4527541;9.173279;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The main focus of 28 Posti is its ethical stance, with seasonal ingredients sourced from small producers and an emphasis on making the most of each and every ingredient in order to keep food waste to a minimum – a philosophy that has been important to the restaurant for many years now. New chefs Franco Salvatore and Andrea Zazzara, both from the Abruzzi, have brought their own personal touches to cuisine which has its roots in the rich gastronomic traditions of central Italy and their native region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9570;InGalera;Italy;Milan;via Cristina Belgioioso 120, Milan, 20157, Italy;45.522552;9.101541;82;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Thanks to its location inside Bollate prison, InGalera offers a unique dining experience. Here, guests eat in a room within the prison itself, while dishes – of equal quality to other restaurants in the area – are prepared with the contribution of prison inmates. In this subdued ambience, choose from meat and fish dishes, with a restricted choice at lunchtime and the option of ordering a single dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9571;Cibrèo;Italy;Florence;via A. Del Verrocchio 8 r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7711187;11.2664401;44;true;true;Tuscan, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant has an informal, fashionable atmosphere, with young, confident staff and fine, inventive cuisine inspired by traditional dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9572;Perbacco;Italy;Pisciotta;contrada Marina Campagna 5, Pisciotta, 84066, Italy;40.1153394;15.2220903;74;true;true;Campanian, Home Cooking;A rustic restaurant offering an authentic taste of the Cilento area, both in its setting amid lush Mediterranean vegetation and in its regional cuisine. Fish and seafood dominate the antipasti selection, while the main courses focus more on meat and vegetable dishes. Good choice of regional wines, plus the option of a few pleasant guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9573;Imperialino;Italy;Moltrasio;via Regina 26, Moltrasio, 22010, Italy;45.8599702;9.1012683;30;true;false;Creative;Treat yourself to dinner in this elegant restaurant right on the lakefront, dining in summer in the beautiful garden within a stone’s throw of the lake. The menu features imaginative Mediterranean specialities (meat as well as fresh- and saltwater fish) on two tasting menus and an extensive à la carte.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9574;Osteria Fernanda;Italy;Rome;via Crescenzo Del Monte 18/24, Rome, 00153, Italy;41.8754069;12.466636;79;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;In the district famous for its Porta Portese market, this restaurant run by two talented business partners is definitely worth a visit. Andrea oversees the minimalist-style dining room, while Luca demonstrates real passion in his creative cuisine made from locally sourced ingredients, as well as produce from further afield. Among the desserts, we highly recommended the Porter beer ice-cream with black garlic mousse, chocolate and tuber peelings.;Air conditioning;[]
9575;Parma Rotta;Italy;Parma;strada Langhirano 158, Parma, 43124, Italy;44.7711267;10.3244781;65;true;true;Grills;Here, where the Parma river once broke its banks, you’ll find an attractive trattoria with pleasant dining rooms and excellent cuisine cooked over a wood and herb fire, one of the oldest culinary techniques in the world. The main courses feature meat only, with an extensive number of dishes on the menu. Among the home-made desserts, we recommend the fior di latte ice-cream, which is served with a choice of delicious sauces.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9576;Pomiroeu;Italy;Seregno;via Garibaldi 37, Seregno, 20831, Italy;45.6512011;9.2043109;34;true;false;Creative;This restaurant, one of the finest in the region, is run by its owner Giancarlo Morelli and celebrated its 30th anniversary in 2023. Situated in the centre of Seregno, the restaurant is intimate and welcoming with walls adorned with beautiful works of contemporary art thanks to the restaurant’s partnership with a local art gallery. The cuisine here is modern yet unfussy and the chef is equally at ease with meat, fish and vegetable dishes. One of the few restaurants around Monza to still offer a cheese course!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9577;Forentum;Italy;Lavello;piazza Plebiscito 16, Lavello, 85024, Italy;41.0487815;15.8005646;96;false;true;Country cooking;This rustic, family restaurant in the historic centre serves local specialities, some of which are made using produce grown in the family vegetable garden. The inner dining room has a charming ambience, thanks to a natural cave which is hundreds of years old. Simple yet well - equipped guestrooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9578;Spin Ristorante-Enoteca;Italy;Genoa;via Carlo Barabino 120 r, Genoa, 16129, Italy;44.4005919;8.9468644;27;true;false;Ligurian, Classic Cuisine;Originally a wine shop, it was then converted into a restaurant that also opens for happy hour: the interiors closely resemble those of a bistro and bottles of wine, especially Italian ones, and of spirits are spread about, while the cuisine focuses on mostly Ligurian flavors (brandacujun, Genoese stuffed pumpkin flowers, trofie al pesto,...) and Italian ones, with fish and meat. Quality regional and national food and wine products are also for sale.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9580;La Kuccagna;Italy;Dovera;via Milano 14, località Barbuzzera, Dovera, 26010, Italy;45.3822527;9.5238907;44;false;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Boasting a fresh, top-quality feel, La Kuccagna is run by a young and energetic management team. The menu features meat and fish dishes alike, including cuts of meat cooked over the ever-present barbecue grill. An excellent wine list including labels from outside Italy, an exquisite rural location and a modern, comfortable decor complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9581;Marina del Nettuno;Italy;Messina;viale della Libertà-Batteria Masotto, Messina, 98121, Italy;38.197887;15.558124;23;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;As its name suggests, this restaurant and lounge bar is situated right on the jetty of the Yachting Club Messina. Elegant and minimalist - style decor, as well as creative cuisine with a focus on fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9582;Aimo e Nadia BistRo;Italy;Milan;via Matteo Bandello 14, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4639032;9.1673607;49;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This bistro with a small yet charming and original dining room is a simpler and more informal version of the famous starred restaurant. The focus is the same, with an emphasis on Italian ingredients used in dishes which bring out their full flavour and integrity.;Air conditioning;[]
9583;Cielo;Italy;Ostuni;via Scipione Petrarolo 7, Ostuni, 72017, Italy;40.7344962;17.5791501;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Cielo is the gourmet restaurant at the splendid and aptly named La Sommità hotel, which is housed in a typical old mansion right at the top of this whitewashed town with its limestone steps. The restaurant offers the perfect setting for a romantic summer dinner, either among the citrus trees in the small inner courtyard or in the dining room crowned with a vaulted ceiling. Boasting a highly respectable CV, the chef from Martina Franca serves modern reinterpretations of Puglian cuisine, while the delightful terrace is perfect for an aperitif at sunset. A simpler menu is available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9584;I Sette Consoli;Italy;Orvieto;piazza Sant'Angelo 1/a, Orvieto, 05018, Italy;42.7186979;12.1146421;69;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;In this simple restaurant boasting an attractive outdoor summer garden and splendid views of the Duomo, chef Anna Rita focuses on carefully selected ingredients from the region and beyond. Highlights include soft egg, pan-fried courgettes and spring onions, and pecorino crumble, as well as soft veal rump, Jerusalem artichoke sauce and home-made pickled vegetables. The wine and spirits selection is particularly appealing – as an example, the Orvieto Classico Superiore Doc “Vendemmia Tardiva” is the perfect pairing for your dessert.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9585;Hanswirt;Italy;Rablà;piazza Gerold 3, Rablà, 39020, Italy;46.6693991;11.0600354;37;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated in an old farmstead, this elegant and pleasant establishment has a warm and typically Tyrolese atmosphere.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9586;Terrazza Costantino;Italy;Sclafani Bagni;rione Sant'Antonio 24, Sclafani Bagni, 90020, Italy;37.8236762;13.8561003;97;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;In just a few years, young owner-chef Giuseppe Costantino has turned what was once the family trattoria into an elegant restaurant serving delicious reinterpretations of local specialities. There is just one tasting menu which features either meat or fish (although this can be discussed when you make your booking, which is essential). Given the excellent quality of the food here, this menu offers exceptional value for money.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9587;Locanda Perbellini;Italy;Milan;via Moscova 25, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4767006;9.1897053;94;false;true;Italian;Highly renowned in his native Verona, Michelin - starred chef Giancarlo Perbellini has now opened a restaurant in Milan, where he continues to offer traditional Italian cuisine from the north and south of the country, with a nod to new techniques and contemporary trends. Situated in the central Brera district, his warm and welcoming restaurant is small, discreet and, of course, highly elegant.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9588;Ai Cadelach;Italy;Revine;via Grava 2, Revine, 31020, Italy;45.9975067;12.2470269;31;false;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;Enjoy local cuisine in a rustic - style dining room or alongside the swimming pool in summer. The menu focuses on meat dishes (especially grilled meat), such as traditional Fiorentina steak and Alpago lamb. Wine lovers will appreciate the excellent wine cellar kept by Ezio, one of the restaurant owners.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9589;Al Covo;Italy;Venice;campiello della Pescaria, sestiere Castello 3968, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.434174;12.3476275;70;false;true;Venetian, Seafood;Authentic family hospitality for this renowned restaurant, which makes niche products - mainly seafood - its flagship, even if some land specialties are always present on the menu. Almost all of the vegetables come from the Osti in Orto property garden on the island of Sant'Erasmo.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9590;Capo Santa Chiara;Italy;Genoa;via al Capo di Santa Chiara 69, Boccadasse, Genoa, 16124, Italy;44.38971;8.974857;17;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;The chef at this modern, renovated restaurant at the end of the romantic Boccadasse beach serves creative cuisine that is the result of years of experimentation. Charming terrace overlooking the sea for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9591;Trattoria del Pesce;Italy;Rome;via Folco Portinari 27, Rome, 00151, Italy;41.8685979;12.4494124;51;false;true;Seafood, Italian;A good selection of fresh and raw fish dishes served in a welcoming, vaguely bistro-style restaurant with young and competent staff. Parking can be difficult, but your patience is definitely rewarded!;Air conditioning;[]
9592;Miranda;Italy;Riva di Solto;via Cornello 8, Riva di Solto, 24060, Italy;45.7810311;10.0447336;16;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated in a superb location overlooking Lake Isea, this restaurant boasts superb views of the lake and Monte Isola from its outdoor terrace and dining room alike. The menu features fish (mainly from the sea) and meat dishes with a creative twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
9593;Manuelina;Italy;Recco;via Roma 296, Recco, 16036, Italy;44.3691057;9.1501288;81;false;true;Ligurian, Modern Cuisine;Very few restaurants in Liguria can compete with the long gastronomic tradition of this restaurant, which was named after its original owner back in 1885! It was Manuelina herself who made the typical focaccia of Recco famous, offering it as a dish in her tavern. The fourth generation of the family now runs the business with the same passion and enthusiasm – part of the building houses the typical Focacceria, where family traditions are kept alive, while the other is home to the restaurant itself (even here the legendary and highly recommended focaccia is on the menu) with its round tables. The cuisine is traditional yet with modern touches and based on Ligurian ingredients with a focus on fish (although meat also features).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9594;Bagatto;Italy;Loano;via Ricciardi 24, Loano, 17025, Italy;44.1277571;8.2597607;47;false;false;Ligurian, Classic Cuisine;Hidden down an alleyway in the town centre, this friendly trattoria boasts an attractive ceiling with exposed brickwork. An excellent address for fans of Ligurian cuisine, fish and seafood. House desserts include sour orange semifreddo.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9595;Osteria la Lanterna;Italy;Valsolda;via Finali 1, frazione Cressogno, Valsolda, 22010, Italy;46.0244726;9.0722789;53;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Situated on the road leading to Lugano in Switzerland, this charming restaurant with elegant furnishings and a rustic decor boasts bright dining rooms and a pleasant terrace for summer dining. The dishes are prepared with a focus on locally sourced, seasonal ingredients and are inspired by traditional recipes reinterpreted in contemporary style.;Terrace;[]
9596;Oscar;Italy;Ardenza;via Franchini 78, Ardenza, 57128, Italy;43.516251;10.3215893;38;true;false;Seafood;Situated off the tourist trail in a charming residential district, this restaurant is popular with locals from Livorno who come here to enjoy the fresh fish on offer – the vast selection on the buffet makes dining here a real treat. In summer, choose a table on the delightful outdoor veranda.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9597;Osteria Frangipane;Italy;Trani;via Maraldo da Trani 5, Trani, 76125, Italy;41.2783765;16.4105077;83;true;true;Seafood;This osteria on the edge of the historic centre is run by two young brothers who have one clear aim – to serve local fish dishes which are both delicious and imaginative. Pleasantly informal atmosphere.;Air conditioning;[]
9598;Bacucco d'Oro;Italy;Mutignano;via del Pozzo 10, Mutignano, 64025, Italy;42.5885057;14.0338289;27;true;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;From the coast, you take a winding road uphill to this family-run trattoria which boasts sea views from its terrace. Apart from the salted cod, the menu only features meat dishes, with a focus on simple, traditional Abruzzo specialties. These include arrosticini (skewered grilled meat), fragrant mushrooms, barbecued meat and delicious “pizza dogge”, the latter a type of layered dessert with sponge cake, custard, confectioner’s cream and Alkermes liqueur. The concise wine list also focuses on the Abruzzo.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9599;Acanto;Italy;Milan;piazza della Repubblica 17, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4793466;9.1964968;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;At Acanto, the young new chef at the helm, Matteo Gabrielli, who has experience of working abroad, focuses firmly on traditional cuisine – the risotto alla Milanese remains one of the highlights here! In a classic-style dining room inside the Principe di Savoia hotel, enjoy Italian meat and fish dishes prepared using modern techniques that allow the quality of the ingredients to shine through. Attentive, professional service adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9600;La Perla del Mare;Italy;San Vincenzo;via della Meloria 9, San Vincenzo, 57027, Italy;43.1061608;10.539158;93;false;true;Seafood;The occasional creative touch is evident in the fish and seafood dishes served in this welcoming Mediterranean - style restaurant with an attractive outdoor terrace. The restaurant stands right on the beach!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9601;La Conchiglia d'Oro;Italy;Pineto;via Nazionale Adriatica nord, Pineto, 64025, Italy;42.6142651;14.0610184;22;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;The rather anonymous location does not in any way detract from the quality of this historic restaurant, which is renowned for its excellent fish and seafood. The menu showcases fish from the Adriatic cooked using classical techniques with the occasional modern twist, such as in the tuna tartare seasoned with caramelised onions and citrus powder-flavoured mayonnaise. Considering the quality of the fish here, the prices are very reasonable. The beautifully presented desserts are an added bonus.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9602;Le Grenier;Italy;Saint-Vincent;piazza Monte Zerbion 1, Saint-Vincent, 11027, Italy;45.7515866;7.6479615;35;true;true;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Saint Vincent, this restaurant has a hint of an old granary (grenier in French) with tumbling grain, a fireplace and period tools on the walls. But the surprise doesn’t end there: the kitchen seduces its guests with unexpectedly modern dishes, some reminiscent of the Val d’Aosta tradition.;Air conditioning;[]
9603;Baia del Silenzio;Italy;Sestri Levante;via Cappellini 9, Sestri Levante, 16039, Italy;44.2699348;9.393904;25;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Ligurian;In a beautiful position inside the bay, the restaurant serves dishes with a contemporary twist that enhance the local products and the good ingredients. The offer is divided between the bistrot for lunch, the gourmet dinner and the wine bar. In summer you can dine alfresco on the outdoor terrace or directly on the beach.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9604;The Cesar;Italy;Ladispoli;località Palo Laziale, Ladispoli, 00055, Italy;41.933255;12.1037651;92;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant offers Mediterranean dishes prepared mostly with organic produce from the restaurant’s own garden. Dine in a romantic setting overlooking the blue expanse of the Mediterranean sea.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9605;Vairo del Volturno;Italy;Vairano Patenora;via IV Novembre 58, Vairano Patenora, 81058, Italy;41.336734;14.128015;88;false;true;Campanian, Contemporary;Showcasing regional produce, from vegetables to meat and mozzarella to fish from the nearby Tyrrhenian sea, is a real mission for the owner-chef of this elegant restaurant, who makes the most of these ingredients in his contemporary-style cuisine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9606;Rio Bistrot;Italy;Riomaggiore;via San Giacomo 46, Riomaggiore, 19017, Italy;44.0989631;9.7379136;24;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;Situated on the street that heads down to the port in charming Riomaggiore, this lovely, well-kept restaurant offers a small selection of dishes split between Ligurian specialities and more creative options. Dine in the rustic, elegant dining room or on the outdoor terrace.;Terrace;[]
9607;Mondschein;Italy;Sappada;borgata Palù 96, Sappada, 33012, Italy;46.5611322;12.6847131;42;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;You’ll feel immediately at home in this gourmet restaurant in Sappada, where Paolo Kratter and his family offer a warm welcome to guests. In the romantic setting of an elegant mountain hut on the edge of the village, skiers can enjoy simple, informal dishes at lunchtime (the ski slopes are just behind the restaurant), while in the evening the cuisine is more elaborate and of the highest quality. A true taste of the Dolomites!;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9608;Osteria La Sangiovesa;Italy;Santarcangelo di Romagna;piazza Simone Balacchi 14, Santarcangelo di Romagna, 47822, Italy;44.0636873;12.4443436;66;true;true;Cuisine from Romagna, Traditional Cuisine;This simple and informal inn is the perfect setting in which to get together with friends, sitting around small tables laden with piadine flatbreads and slices of ham and salami. There’s also a restaurant here – a network of small rooms laid out in the cellars of an old palazzo – where portraits of local historical characters can be made out in the subtle lighting. Here too, the cuisine is inspired by the region and its traditions, with top-quality ingredients (cured hams, meat, oil, wine, vermouth etc) all coming from the restaurant’s own farm and estate.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
9609;Alla Corte Lombarda;Italy;Mornago;via De Amicis 13, Mornago, 21020, Italy;45.7463645;8.7497849;15;false;false;Lombardian, Modern Cuisine;Housed in a restored hay barn on the edge of the village, this charming rustic restaurant offers traditional cuisine with a modern twist, a good selection of wine and an excellent choice of beer. Every week, the menu features five records which played a major role in the history of music or which represent an important moment in time for the restaurant owner.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9610;I Savi;Italy;Scorzè;via Spangaro 6, località Peseggia di Scorzè, Scorzè, 30037, Italy;45.5689488;12.1719102;93;false;false;Seafood;Situated in a small rural hamlet, this restaurant is one of the best in the Venetian hinterland for top-quality fish. Served in welcoming dining rooms, the fish and seafood dishes here are traditional and unfussy in style, and full of natural flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9611;Ora d'Aria;Italy;Florence;via dei Georgofili 11r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7684515;11.2547889;84;true;false;Contemporary;Situated behind the Uffizi, this restaurant boasts a large open-view kitchen and an original approach that focuses on creating meaningful dialogue between guests and the chefs in the kitchen. The restaurant owes its name to the old Florentine Le Murate prison nearby, as well as to its stated aim of providing guests with time to breathe and relax. The dishes here are influenced by Tuscan traditions and Italian cuisine alike yet reinterpreted with a creative touch and a greater emphasis on vegetables. The tasting menus include the Menu Bendato, which features specialities chosen by the chef, and the La Bistecca alla fiorentinaoption (available by prior booking only), on which the famous Florentine steak is presented in different guises. An impressive wine list completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9612;Locanda del Feudo;Italy;Castelvetro di Modena;via Trasversale 2, Castelvetro di Modena, 41014, Italy;44.502912;10.9427622;45;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the historic upper section of this picturesque village, this romantic restaurant serves imaginative and colourful cuisine including some excellent local cured hams. There are also six elegant, recently renovated suites with a historic feel, plus a small, charming outdoor space overlooking the main street.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9613;Dama Restaurant;Italy;Venice;Fondamenta Savorgnan 461, Cannaregio, Venice, 30121, Italy;45.444402;12.3236768;63;true;true;Creative;The cuisine served at this restaurant comes from a deep knowledge of the region, is inspired by tradition and yet constantly evolving. At Dama , guests will find creative cuisine with an equal balance of meat and fish dishes. Housed within Ca’ Bonfadini, the restaurant boasts an outstanding location overlooking Cannaregio canal, while the attractive dining room has just three elegant wooden tables that encourage sharing and can accommodate up to 10 guests.;Air conditioning;[]
9614;aede dining & wines;Italy;Rome;via Federico Cesi 22, Rome, 00193, Italy;41.9072612;12.470643;22;true;true;European Contemporary;A small gem of a restaurant with a contemporary minimalist-style decor. The highly creative and technically modern cuisine has the same Nordic style as the dining room, influenced by the chef’s experience working in a number of Michelin-starred restaurants in Scandinavia. The menu changes every month and consists of twelve different dishes, with a minimum of four in the evening. Organic wines and a small outdoor dining space complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9615;Osteria a "Le Due Spade";Italy;Trento;via Don Arcangelo Rizzi 11, Trento, 38122, Italy;46.0670041;11.1203145;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This beautiful Stube-style restaurant in the city centre has existed since the Council of Trent, with a succession of chefs and owners serving food here ever since the 16C. Still run with skill and expertise today, the restaurant boasts a small, intimate Alpine-style dining room where Trento specialities (char, apple strudel with vanilla ice cream) are served alongside typical Italian fare (risotto with mussel power and parsley pesto). All the dishes are cooked with an imaginative touch, resulting in a perfect balance of tradition and modernity!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9616;Poldo e Gianna Osteria;Italy;Rome;vicolo Rosini 6/7, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9022264;12.4772745;59;false;true;Roman, Traditional Cuisine;This cheerful and attractive contemporary restaurant near the Parliament building serves traditional Roman cuisine made from interesting seasonal ingredients. There’s a pleasant outdoor space (book well in advance), plus an unexpected wine cellar which is extremely well stocked and includes some top-quality wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9617;Benso;Italy;Forlì;piazza Cavour 7, Forlì, 47121, Italy;44.224657;12.0400813;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Situated in a small garden in the historic centre, this modern bistro has a light, airy feel thanks to its large windows and its outdoor tables perfect for alfresco dining in summer. The young kitchen staff, supervised by a talented chef and with plenty of experience behind them, serve contemporary cuisine with an individual flavour. Simple aperitif-style options are available between 6 and 8pm.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9618;L'Osteria di Santa Marina;Italy;Venice;campo Santa Marina, sestiere di Castello 5911, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.4383688;12.3390224;50;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;This classy inn is managed by young professionals who serve seafood and traditional dishes, but they also offer some interesting culinary innovations.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9619;La Corte;Italy;Palazzolo sull'Oglio;via San Pancrazio 41, Palazzolo sull'Oglio, 25036, Italy;45.6060502;9.8981073;28;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Mediterranean-style dishes take pride of place in this attractive restaurant which serves meat and fish dishes and prioritises seasonal ingredients. A visit to the well-stocked wine cellar is highly recommended!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9620;Agli Amici Dopolavoro;Italy;Venice;isola delle Rose, Venice, 30133, Italy;45.4054719;12.3201218;59;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;You cross a small garden-cum-olive grove to get to this romantic and elegant restaurant situated on the enchanting Isola delle Rose, a private island accessible only by boat. Overseen by chef Emanuele Scarello, the resident chef here is the young and talented Lorenzo Lai who serves two tasting menus: “LagunAmare” features top-quality fish while the “Giardino delle Rose” is a vegetarian menu based on vegetables grown in the restaurant’s own garden. Both menus showcase the rich selection of produce available in the lagoon and the biodiversity of the island itself. On summer evenings, an aperitif on the charming outdoor terrace is highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9621;Ponte Pietra;Italy;Verona;via Ponte Pietra 34, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.44733;10.999518;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;An old building next to the Roman bridge Ponte Pietra, with a couple of romantic small balconies overlooking the river. Charming dining rooms provide the backdrop for regional cuisine with creative touches and a carefully selected wine list. An attractive apartment is also available for anyone wish to extend their stay here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9622;Da Vincenzo;Italy;Positano;viale Pasitea 172/178, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6278082;14.485111;70;true;true;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;It's never easy to find the right balance between quality and quantity, especially in a town that is very much on the tourist trail. However, Da Vincenzo has succeeded in doing just this for years, ever since it was first opened by the family’s grandfather Vincenzo in 1958. Today, the founder’s grandson (who shares his grandfather’s name) is at the helm here, creating dishes which focus mainly on fish. Pleasant atmosphere, with a few small tables on the pavement of the street that runs through the centre of Positano. A choice of cocktails supplements the wine selection from lunchtime onwards.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9623;La Notizia 53;Italy;Naples;via Caravaggio 53/55, Naples, 80126, Italy;40.8357424;14.2099366;65;true;true;Pizza;Although situated away from the tourist centre, Enzo Coccia’s pizzeria continues to be considered one of the best places for pizza in Campania. Featuring classic Neapolitan pizzas with soft, stringy dough, the menu offers traditional and creative toppings alike. The “'mpustarella”, a five-grain and wholemeal flour roll with different fillings, more than compensates for the lack of “fritti” on the menu. The first historic restaurant at number 53 has now been joined by a second address at number 94/a nearby.;Air conditioning;[]
9624;Osaka;Italy;Milan;corso Giuseppe Garibaldi 68, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4763226;9.1841301;52;false;true;Japanese, Traditional Cuisine;Tucked away in a short arcade on the old road from Milan to Como, this restaurant has a simple, minimalist style with a bar where diners can watch the skilful chefs slicing and preparing the fish. Set menus dominate at lunchtime, while in the evening the à la carte options include sukiyaki, a celebratory dish in Japan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9625;Al Segnavento;Italy;Zelarino;via Gatta 76/c, località Santa Lucia di Tarù, Zelarino, 30174, Italy;45.5357421;12.2159387;21;false;false;Venetian, Seasonal Cuisine;An elegant restaurant run by an entire family, whose philosophy could be summed up in the phrase “from farm to fork”. Fruit, vegetables, mutton, lamb, pork, plus a delicious breed of duck are all showcased in this zero-kilometre restaurant. If you’re looking for simpler fare and wine by the carafe, the restaurant also has a more informal bistro nearby. Charming guestrooms also available for visitors wanting to prolong their stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9626;San Lorenzo;Italy;Spoleto;piazza Sordini 6, Spoleto, 06049, Italy;42.7344912;12.7348655;29;false;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;Situated within the Clitunno hotel, this well-managed family-run restaurant serves classic, seasonal meat and fish dishes, including generous portions of black truffles in some dishes. Recently refurbished, the intimate, elegant dining room also occasionally features live music at weekends, while the outdoor terrace on the small square offers pleasant alfresco dining. Guests are advised to park outside the ZTL (restricted traffic zone) and make their way on foot, via a short walk through the beautiful historic centre.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9627;Da Annetta;Italy;Capolago;via Fè 25, Capolago, 21100, Italy;45.7937434;8.8075834;37;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;In an 18th Century building, a rustic yet elegant atmosphere with a particular attentiveness at the tables and in the cuisine, which has a traditional base, but also knows how to add imaginative variations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9628;La Palomba;Italy;Orvieto;via Cipriano Manente 16, Orvieto, 05018, Italy;42.718052;12.108641;94;false;false;Umbrian, Traditional Cuisine;Boasting the attractive ambience of a typical Italian trattoria, La Palomba has been run by the Cinti family since 1965 and is now in the hands of the third generation. The menu features Umbrian specialities including delicious home-made umbrichelli pasta served with various sauces.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9629;SaQua by Il Frantoio;Italy;Montescudaio;viale Vittorio Veneto 40, Montescudaio, 56040, Italy;43.3249891;10.6276167;31;false;true;Tuscan, Contemporary;This restaurant, previously known simply as “Il Frantoio”, now has new out-of-town premises but any regret you may have at leaving the town centre will soon disappear, thanks to the wide range of modern Tuscan dishes prepared by the chefs in the new, larger kitchen. A further attraction is the outdoor space which boasts beautiful sunset views in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9630;Osteria Boccolicchio;Italy;Manfredonia;via Arco Boccolicchio 15, Manfredonia, 71043, Italy;41.627777;15.91779;85;true;true;Apulian, Seafood;Having gained experience in various restaurants throughout Europe, Tespi has now returned home to open this delightful small osteria in the historic centre, just a stone’s throw from the sea. His huge passion for fish is evident from the menu, where fish dishes feature in numerous regionally influenced recipes. The excellent wine cellar includes a good choice of sparkling wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9631;Arva;Italy;Venice;calle Tiepolo, sestiere San Polo 1364, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.4370679;12.3315175;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Dine surrounded by a decor of stucco and paintings or alfresco overlooking the Grand Canal in this highly luxurious restaurant. Arva, from the Latin "cultivated land", pays homage to the sea, the land and its best seasonal ingredients purchased from the Rialto market and the islands of the Venetian lagoon. Chef Matteo Panfilio, who has an international experience in good restaurants, pays great attention to local vegetables.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9632;Locanda del Falco;Italy;Rivalta Trebbia;Castello di Rivalta 4, Rivalta Trebbia, 29010, Italy;44.9499571;9.5906482;69;true;true;Country cooking, Italian Contemporary;Housed in a medieval hamlet, this traditional restaurant serves typical specialities from Piacenza, as well as other dishes full of creativity and imagination. All are accompanied by wines from the region (the wine list seems to have them all! ) and elsewhere in Italy. Winter evenings are brightened by the large indoor fireplaces, while a 100 year - old wisteria provides shade in the welcoming inner courtyard in summer.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9633;Ristorante Alpes & La FuGa;Italy;Sarentino;via Ronco 24, Sarentino, 39058, Italy;46.6243914;11.3623949;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Innovative;At this restaurant, choose between three tables in the elegant, contemporary-style purple Stube, and another three in the more rustic, historic and romantic Stube. Wherever you choose to sit, you’ll enjoy creative, sophisticated dishes that will particularly appeal to anyone keen on innovative and imaginative cuisine. At the helm, chef Mattia Baroni has an unusual background, having moved from computer studies to working in renowned restaurants around the world.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9634;Zero Milano;Italy;Milan;corso Magenta 87, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4658869;9.166515;100;false;true;Japanese, Fusion;There’s absolutely zero compromise on attention and quality in this restaurant, where the cuisine is made from top-quality ingredients using all the technical expertise typical of Japanese cooking. Chef Hide is now assisted by two of his compatriots who are real sushi experts, emphasising Zero Milano’s ambition to be one of the best Japanese restaurants in Milan, with its menu featuring Japanese specialities alongside dishes with a more contemporary Western flavour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9635;Mater Terrae;Italy;Rome;largo Febo 2, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8998749;12.4721696;56;false;false;Vegetarian, Contemporary;Situated on the top floor of the Raphaël hotel just behind Piazza Navona, this restaurant serves some of the best vegetarian cuisine in Rome. Each of the elaborate dishes boasts numerous ingredients and every single course is a delightful surprise. Equally stunning is the panoramic terrace overlooking the city’s rooftops, where meals are served in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9636;La Leggenda dei Frati;Italy;Florence;costa San Giorgio 6/a, Florence, 50125, Italy;43.764355;11.25606;28;false;true;Creative;After an uphill approach if you’re arriving here on foot, you come into the Villa Bardini museum complex and from there into this elegant and welcoming restaurant which provides the setting for delicious, creative and modern cuisine. Here, chef Filippo Saporito, never one to rest on his laurels, continues to experiment and perfect his cuisine, which focuses mainly on Italian culinary traditions and a scrupulous selection of top-quality ingredients, preferably from sustainable supply chains (various types of meat, bread and pasta), all showcased on different menus, including a vegetarian option. In summer, enjoy your meal on the romantic terrace surrounded by greenery and the scents of herbs, with a glimpse of Santa Croce church as a backdrop. Although the centre of Florence is not far away, it seems as though you’re already in the Tuscan hills, even with the occasional sound of cicadas in the background.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9637;Tosca;Italy;Casole d'Elsa;località Querceto, Casole d'Elsa, 53031, Italy;43.3249529;11.0832378;20;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant has a charming decor that combines classic elegance and typical Tuscan features such as stone arches and walls, as well as stylish sofas and comfortable armchairs. The cuisine is heavily influenced by local traditions, albeit with a fresh and innovative twist.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9638;Rovello;Italy;Milan;Via Ariberto 3, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4576004;9.1748674;97;false;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;This lively and welcoming bistro furnished with smart wooden furniture is the setting for cuisine which focuses on carefully chosen ingredients presented with the minimum of fuss. Although the menu features a few specialities from Milan, most of the dishes here are Mediterranean in style. Interesting wine selection, including by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9639;Acaja;Italy;Pinerolo;corso Torino 106, Pinerolo, 10064, Italy;44.8856657;7.3353915;17;false;true;Italian, Contemporary;Central, elegant and modern, the cuisine of Acaja winds along two lines: the traditional regional one, with ravioli del plin, cardi gobbi, Piedmont veal and hazelnuts to mention just a few that cannot be missed, but also various fish dishes that are truly remarkable, with a touch of contemporaneity, starting with excellent raw materials.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9640;Controcorrente;Italy;Morciano di Romagna;via XXV Luglio 23, Morciano di Romagna, 47833, Italy;43.9124479;12.6467282;66;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;A welcoming restaurant with a rustic - style dining room, a young, lively atmosphere and beautifully prepared dishes with an emphasis on fish – it is difficult not to be impressed!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9641;Trattoria Al Passo;Italy;Venice;via Passo Campalto 118, Venice, 30173, Italy;45.4805719;12.29823;37;true;false;Seafood;Successive generations of the same family have run this pleasant restaurant just outside the city for over 70 years. Enjoy a selection of fish and seafood dishes (raw, grilled or fried with numerous condiments to accompany your starters) in a maritime themed dining room or on the light and airy veranda. There is a good selection of desserts to round off your meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9642;Bistrot;Italy;Rieti;piazza San Rufo 25, Rieti, 02100, Italy;42.4021456;12.8620159;21;true;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Overlooking a delightful, quiet little square, this romantic, welcoming restaurant serves traditional local specialities, often with an individual flavour. The menu includes some fish dishes, although the house speciality is the maltagliati pasta served with ‘Bistrot’ sauce.;Terrace;[]
9643;Osteria del 36;Italy;Parma;Strada Aurelio Saffi 26/a, Parma, 43121, Italy;44.8023183;10.3347971;64;false;true;Emilian, Classic Cuisine;The oldest osteria in the town centre, this restaurant has delighted locals and visitors in two simple yet convivial dining rooms since 1880. The cuisine here is regional, with many dishes freshly prepared, from the excellent pasta to the delicious ice cream. Specialities include duck breast in a raspberry sauce with parmesan cheese flan.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9644;Osteria Manzoni;Italy;Barzago;via Roma 87, Barzago, 23890, Italy;45.75679;9.31183;84;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant housed within a colourful, skilfully restored historic building with exposed stonework has a young friendly couple at the helm. The menu features delicious, refined and traditional Italian cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
9645;Ansitz Romani;Italy;Termeno sulla Strada del Vino;via Andreas Hofer 23, Termeno sulla Strada del Vino, 39040, Italy;46.3134785;11.2187143;41;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;An attractive, well-kept restaurant in a historic building with a romantic, rural feel, especially in the beautiful garden. Although the menu is not that extensive, the chef is highly skilled, and it doesn’t feel as though anything is missing here. The dishes reflect the flavours of the region, making use of local ingredients such as venison and asparagus from Termeno accompanied by home-produced speck ham. The menu also features a couple of fish-based recipes and all dishes are modern and imaginative in style. Beautiful guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9646;Da Guido;Italy;Jesolo;via Roma Sinistra 25, Jesolo, 30016, Italy;45.5432677;12.6507932;74;false;false;Seafood;The story of this restaurant began in 1967, when Guido and Giovanna Fasan, both of whom still work front of house, met in Germany. They then moved back to Italy, where they opened Da Guido in the early 1990s. White dominates in the elegant, contemporary-style dining room, while the cuisine features delicious seafood dishes with a focus on grilled specialities. In summer, there’s a welcoming bar in the garden, which boasts a romantic atmosphere. Together with other restaurant-owners from Venice, the Fasan family also have a kitchen garden on the Venetian island of Sant’Erasmo, where they focus on sustainable growing methods.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9647;La Valle;Italy;Trofarello;via Umberto I 25, località Valle Sauglio, Trofarello, 10028, Italy;44.9861358;7.7537482;60;true;true;Contemporary;A well - run restaurant in a quiet area just outside the village, where the owner - chef serves modern cuisine with the occasional regional influence. Careful attention is given to the use of seasonal produce and natural herbs, and there is a small selection of fish - based dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9648;La Sponda;Italy;Positano;via Colombo 30, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6284968;14.4880344;17;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;An elegant restaurant within Le Sirenuse, one of the most prestigious and glamorous hotels on the Amalfi coast, with an attractive outdoor terrace for summer dining with views of Positano’s colourful houses clinging to the cliff face. Whether you choose to eat inside or out, a romantic atmosphere is guaranteed thanks to the hundreds of candles lit every evening. At the helm, Neapolitan chef Gennaro Russo maintains the restaurant’s high standards with his Mediterranean dishes, often influenced by Campania and inspired by classic favourites. The flavours of southern Italy are showcased in delicious dishes such as lemon risotto with capers.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9649;Oberwirt;Italy;Marlengo;vicolo San Felice 2, Marlengo, 39020, Italy;46.65752;11.14034;62;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The various Stube-style dining rooms in the Oberwirt hotel restaurant have a typical Tyrolean ambience, while the cuisine is decidedly traditional with its focus on seasonal and regional ingredients, although a few fish options also always feature on the menu. Wine-enthusiasts will be delighted with the excellent wine selection.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9650;La Coccinella;Italy;Serravalle Langhe;via Provinciale 5, Serravalle Langhe, 12050, Italy;44.5579712;8.0599063;25;true;true;Piedmontese;Three brothers, all of them experts, are the enthusiastic managers of this very fine restaurant. Recent renovation has increased the comfort and popularity of the place. The cuisine is Piedmontese.;Car park;[]
9651;Le Lampare al Fortino;Italy;Trani;via Tiepolo, molo Sant'Antonio, Trani, 76125, Italy;41.280422;16.422161;93;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Built over a medieval church, this old fort that once guarded the port has become the enviable location of a restaurant. It serves delicious fish and seafood specialities with the distinct flavour of Puglia.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9652;Braunwirt;Italy;Sarentino;piazza Chiesa 3, Sarentino, 39058, Italy;46.6427018;11.3569038;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A modern and welcoming restaurant in the heart of the town, where the modern design is echoed by the contemporary cuisine which combines regional dishes with influences from elsewhere in Italy. Food-lovers will enjoy creating their own tasting menu by choosing dishes from the à la carte. Friendly service and a cosmopolitan clientele.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9653;Boccadoro;Italy;Noventa;via della Resistenza 49, Noventa, 35027, Italy;45.4230025;11.9456731;33;false;false;Venetian, Classic Cuisine;Situated on the outskirts of Padova, this classically elegant restaurant is very popular with locals – and for good reason! The menu includes skilfully prepared dishes influenced by the traditions of the Veneto (from bigoli pasta to dried cod and liver Venetian-style) as well as a selection of grilled options.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9654;La Locanda del Notaio;Italy;Pellio Intelvi;Via Piano delle Noci 42, Pellio Intelvi, 22024, Italy;45.9764501;9.0443315;81;false;true;Creative;An elegant restaurant with a warm atmosphere embellished by a central fireplace. Chef Marco Moretto creates modern dishes which are elegant and balanced, with a focus on seasonal produce from the region and elsewhere – in this region of lakes, just a stone’s throw from Switzerland, you’ll be surprised by the fragrant seafood specialities which feature on the menu alongside freshwater fish dishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9655;Bon Wei;Italy;Milan;via Castelvetro 16/18, Milan, 20154, Italy;45.4846784;9.1643511;52;false;true;Chinese, Asian;China on a plate! This attractive restaurant with an intriguing decor combining elegance, modern style and Asian influences serves a wide selection of Chinese specialities. Dishes include appetisers, dumplings, noodles and meat options, as well as a huge array of specialities from eight different regions, from the spicy dishes of Szechuan to the delicate flavours of Zhejiang.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9656;Colonne;Italy;Santa Maria del Monte;via Fincarà 37, Santa Maria del Monte, 21100, Italy;45.8606672;8.7911375;29;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Beautiful views of Lake Varese and its surrounding countryside, especially from the attractive summer terrace. At lunchtime, the upper section of the restaurant houses the bistro, while the elegant dining room provides the backdrop for more creative cuisine in the evening. Chef Silvio Battistoni is very well known in the region.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9657;MikEle;Italy;Maranello;via Flavio Gioia 1, Maranello, 41053, Italy;44.5284906;10.8683522;91;false;true;Seafood;Located in a residential district on the edge of town, this unexpected, elegant fish restaurant offers a refreshing change from the typical boiled meat dishes of Modena. Guests can choose their fish from the display cabinet, with classic Italian seafood recipes taking pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
9658;Kleine Flamme;Italy;Vipiteno;via Cittanuova 31, Vipiteno, 39049, Italy;46.8973392;11.432459;98;true;true;Fusion, Creative;In his small open-view kitchen situated in the centre of this restaurant, chef Bacher Burkhard develops his vision of fusion cuisine with energy and precision, combining flavours from Italy and the Alto Adige with Asian spices and techniques to create delicious and imaginative dishes. His tuna tataki is superb, seasoned with salty lemon oil and accompanied by intriguing bitter herbs that (as Professor Montanari has noted in a recent book) are particularly popular with Italians. The chef’s wife Annelies works front of house, where she looks after guests in a friendly and professional manner.;Terrace;[]
9659;Lapprodo;Italy;Vibo Valentia Marina;via Roma 22, Vibo Valentia Marina, 89900, Italy;38.7161233;16.1221031;66;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Definitely one of the most reliable restaurants in this area, Vibo Valentia Marina overlooks Vibo Marina port and is the perfect choice for anyone keen on classic Mediterranean cuisine with a focus on fish (most of which is caught locally), although meat dishes also feature on the menu. The restaurant also offers guestrooms in its Cala del Porto hotel.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9660;Bacco e Arianna;Italy;Trezzano sul Naviglio;via Circonvallazione 1, Trezzano sul Naviglio, 20090, Italy;45.4197975;9.0739012;43;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Enjoy attentive service from the female owner in this small modern restaurant situated on the outskirts of Milan. The cuisine has an equal focus on meat and fish – our inspector particularly enjoyed the lobster roll with avocado, celeriac and pan brioche, as well as the roasted scallops with lentils, salicornia and creamed potatoes. An interesting and reasonably priced lunch menu is available at midday.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9661;La Chiocciola;Italy;Quartiere di Portomaggiore;via Runco 94/f, Quartiere di Portomaggiore, 44015, Italy;44.71051;11.75692;37;false;false;Country cooking;A restaurant and an inn in a small country village, it’s the right place if you’re looking for hospitality and you appreciate the regional cuisine, made of snails and frogs, but also fish from the nearby sea. Something for every palate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9662;Osteria Numero Sette;Italy;Rastignano;via Andrea Costa 7, Rastignano, 40067, Italy;44.4462;11.3583;85;false;true;Emilian;There’s been a recent change in management at this informal, friendly restaurant which serves generously portioned, carefully prepared dishes from the region and elsewhere in Italy, all at highly competitive prices. Although the cuisine might not be particularly modern, this is good solid cuisine served in a welcoming atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9663;LeoneFelice Vista Lago;Italy;Erbusco;via Vittorio Emanuele 23, Erbusco, 25030, Italy;45.6017335;9.9744178;70;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;The new chef at this restaurant focuses on highlighting produce grown in the property’s own kitchen garden, as well as meat from the farm in the Grosseto area that is also run by the Andana estate. The classic-style cuisine on the à la carte features occasional personalised touches (for example, aubergines baked in fig leaf with oregano, and perch or sea bass fillet served with coloured beets and soft potato), while in the evening a tasting menu is served in a dedicated part of the restaurant. The expertly explained wine list focuses on the estate’s own labels and the Franciacorta region in general, yet at the same time includes a selection of wines from elsewhere in Italy and further afield.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9664;Da Giovanni;Italy;Cortina Vecchia;via Cortina 1040, Cortina Vecchia, 29010, Italy;44.8731723;9.9243205;74;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The 18C ceramic stove, bright, colourful decor (both period and vintage), long family tradition and excellent cuisine all contribute to making this restaurant which opened half a century ago a bastion of fine cuisine in Piacenza and the wider Po valley. Meat and fish both feature on the menu, although it is the latter that has become renowned as the restaurant’s speciality over the years. The excellent service is friendly and informal yet highly professional, while the extensive wine list also includes a good selection of wines by the glass.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9665;Darmagi;Italy;Mercenasco;via Rivera 7, Mercenasco, 10010, Italy;45.3515984;7.8849938;79;false;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Small villa in secluded position with warm, homely atmosphere, especially in the nice room with fireplace. The range of cuisine is rich in tradition.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9666;L'A Gourmet L'Accademia;Italy;Reggio Calabria;via Largo C. Colombo 6, Reggio Calabria, 89125, Italy;38.1139931;15.6505925;31;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;From the classic restaurant on the first floor (no lift) of this early 20C palazzo, you’ll enjoy fine views of the sea and the Strait of Messina. Here, skilled chef Filippo Cogliardo prepares fish-based dishes which include classic recipes (raw seafood and amberjack with rapini) as well as more modern options (cuttlefish tagliatelle with avocado cream, cucumber and salted lemon). A few meat dishes also feature on the menu. Definitely the best restaurant in town!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
9667;La Fugascina Ristorante;Italy;Mergozzo;piazza Vittorio Veneto 8, Mergozzo, 28802, Italy;45.9605376;8.4492947;65;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Country cooking;Situated on a small square with an attractive outdoor space, this restaurant offers a menu which features fish from the lake and other seasonal produce prepared with both modern and traditional techniques, but always with a contemporary flair. The focus is on locally sourced (zero-mile, wherever possible) produce.;Terrace;[]
9668;Riso Amaro;Italy;Fondi;viale Regina Margherita 22, Fondi, 04022, Italy;41.3581162;13.4294783;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This elegant, contemporary-style restaurant is situated right in the historic centre. The menu features a host of gourmet dishes as well as more modern fish and meat options, all created by the talented owner-chef.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9669;Al Capitan della Cittadella;Italy;Verona;piazza Cittadella 7/a, Verona, 37122, Italy;45.4369536;10.9936108;64;false;true;Seafood, Italian Contemporary;Situated just outside the town walls, Al Capitan has been one of the most renowned fish restaurants in Verona for over fifteen years. Classic Italian dishes with a contemporary twist added by the owner-chef take pride of place here, with an emphasis on top-quality ingredients. The wine list includes a good selection of French wines, with a particular focus on champagnes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9670;Trattoria alla Pergola;Italy;Fagnano;via Nazario Sauro 9, Fagnano, 37060, Italy;45.2587117;10.9414325;20;false;false;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;An old-fashioned trattoria with a simple, homely atmosphere which attracts guests from all over the province who are drawn here by the classic, unfussy regional cuisine. Although the menu is concise, it includes specialities such as tortelli, tortellini, the region’s famous risottos (this is rice-growing country) and renowned boiled meats. Make sure you leave room for the tempting dessert trolley.;Air conditioning;[]
9671;Hosteria Giusti;Italy;Modena;via Farini 75, Modena, 41121, Italy;44.6472912;10.92823;65;true;true;Emilian;Situated in an attractive retro-style room to the rear of an elegant delicatessen, this restaurant offers just four tables and a restricted menu of top-quality, traditional Emilian dishes. In the evening, the restaurant is open by reservation only for groups of at least 12 people with a pre-arranged menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9672;Trattoria I Masenini;Italy;Verona;via Roma 34, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4394132;10.9885667;78;true;true;Italian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in an attractive part of Verona right opposite the famous Castelvecchio, this restaurant boasts a relaxing ambience with wood ceilings, classic yet informal furnishings, subtle lighting and soft background music. The menu features regional dishes alongside typical Italian fare, as well as the house speciality – meat kebabs cooked on a skewer. There’s also an outdoor space for alfresco dining in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9673;Giorgio e Flora;Italy;Velo;via Baldonò 1, lago di Velo d'Astico, Velo, 36010, Italy;45.7963;11.34109;44;false;false;Venetian, Modern Cuisine;This small chalet - style villa overlooks the valley. It has an attractive, elegant and quiet dining room decorated with a feminine touch and a panoramic outdoor terrace. Modern cuisine from the Veneto takes pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9674;Quellenhof Gourmetstube 1897;Italy;Saint Martin in Passeier;via Passiria 47, Saint Martin in Passeier, 39010, Italy;46.7459911;11.2044911;65;true;true;Creative;Situated in a refined and elegant setting (also home to an intimate private dining area separated from the main room by a few steps), this new gourmet restaurant offers various tasting menus with a distinctly creative flavour.;Air conditioning;[]
9675;Marcandole;Italy;Salgareda;via Argine Piave 7, Salgareda, 31040, Italy;45.6985092;12.4785183;29;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant managed with passion has become a cornerstone of Treviso restaurants thanks to a fish cuisine contaminated by contemporary inspirations. Do not miss the raw specialties!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9676;Gino Sorbillo;Italy;Naples;via dei Tribunali 32, Naples, 80138, Italy;40.8503612;14.2552584;97;false;false;Pizza;Situated along the "via della pizza", this historic restaurant boasts a simple yet lively ambience with a local and international feel. Excellent pizzas made from quality - label produce. You’ll need plenty of patience if you’re here at busy times and if you choose to share a table, you’ll really enjoy the convivial atmosphere!;Air conditioning;[]
9677;Menegaldo;Italy;Monastier di Treviso;via Pralongo 216, Monastier di Treviso, 31050, Italy;45.645096;12.485602;40;false;false;Seafood;This restaurant, once referred to as “l’osteria dei cava’i” in reference to the cart drivers and their horses who used to stop here after the First World War, has a history dating back 100 years. Now specialising in fish and shellfish from the Adriatic, Menegaldo has become one of the area’s most popular restaurants.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9678;Al Fogher;Italy;Piazza Armerina;strada statale 117 bis, Piazza Armerina, 94015, Italy;37.41098;14.383366;65;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This small, rustic-style restaurant just outside the centre of Piazza Armerina serves personalised cuisine in which local ingredients take pride of place. Influences from elsewhere in Italy are also evident, with dishes such as artichoke pansotti (stuffed pasta) with local tuma cheese and black truffles on the menu.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9679;Trattoria di Coronate;Italy;Morimondo;Cascina Coronate, Morimondo, 20081, Italy;45.3456746;8.9657392;18;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Housed in a splendid 16C farmhouse just a few minutes from the beautiful Morimondo abbey, this restaurant has an elegant and friendly ambience. The wooden ceiling and furniture in the dining room gives it a warm and welcoming feel, while the cuisine, deeply rooted in the region, is reinterpreted with a contemporary twist. The delicious options on the menu include highlights such as quail breast with a thigh-meat “lollipop” and ravioli stuffed with braised beef.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9680;Muraglia - Conchiglia d'Oro;Italy;Varigotti;via Aurelia 133, Varigotti, 17024, Italy;44.1817608;8.3955959;86;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Here, choose between the simply furnished, bright dining room with a proudly vintage feel that dates back to its opening in the 1970s and a tiny yet attractive terrace with sea views (there are just a few tables, so it’s best to book in advance). Fish has always been – and still is – the house speciality, with fresh, top-quality dishes simply prepared according to classic methods such as the barbecue grill visible in the dining room. The fish is so fresh that the handwritten menu changes daily.;Terrace;[]
9681;Gratschwirt;Italy;Toblach;via Grazze 1, Toblach, 39034, Italy;46.7310953;12.2045905;75;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Housed in a building which dates back to the 16C and is part of the hotel of the same name, this Stube-style restaurant at the foot of the Tre Cime is typical of the Alto Adige, as is the simple, abundant regional cuisine served here. Highlights on the menu include dumplings in broth, herb-crusted lamb, apple strudel and the less traditional but excellent beef tartare which is seasoned at your table.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9682;L'Archivolto - Osteria Nostrale;Italy;Ovada;piazza Garibaldi 25/26, Ovada, 15076, Italy;44.6401551;8.6480495;71;true;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Situated on Ovada’s main square, this restaurant has the pleasant friendly ambience of an attractive trattoria, while its menu takes guests on a delicious culinary journey through the Piedmont region, including local specialities such as home-made tajarin pasta, braised beef in Ovada wine with mashed potato, and the local bunet dessert (finanziera stew also makes an occasional appearance). The restaurant is also a wine bar/boutique offering a selection of wines, including different Barolo labels (presented area by area) and aperitifs served both at lunchtime and dinner.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9683;Trita Pepe;Italy;Manoppello Scalo;via Gabriele D'Annunzio 4, Manoppello Scalo, 65024, Italy;42.30439;14.054071;56;false;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo;Situated on the road that passes through Manoppello Scalo, this restaurant with a car park right in front of the building boasts a spacious, simple dining room and is our recommended choice in the region for anyone keen to try typical Abruzzo cuisine. Meat takes pride of place among the main courses (with an exception for salted cod), while menu highlights include excellent fried gnocchi with local salumi and cheese.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9684;Bistrot de Venise;Italy;Venice;calle dei Fabbri 4685, sestiere San Marco, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.435544;12.3364804;67;true;false;Venetian;Diners will enjoy the lengthy wine list (available by the glass) and "historical" cuisine at this restaurant in a location known for its atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9685;Io Osteria Personale;Italy;Florence;Borgo San Frediano 167r, Florence, 50124, Italy;43.77038;11.24062;53;false;false;Creative;The young owner of this restaurant has an interesting background – a former vet with a passion for food. He has opened one of the most fascinating restaurants in Florence, serving original dishes to diners looking for a change from more traditional fare.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9686;Hidalgo;Italy;Postal;via Roma 7, Postal, 39014, Italy;46.61744;11.18844;86;true;false;Grills;Although fish dishes also feature on the menu, Hidalgo has long enjoyed a reputation for its excellent meat options thanks to its different cuts of steak and beef sourced from all around the world and cooked mainly (but not exclusively) on the barbecue grill. In a separate room(Aomi, a kind of restaurant within the restaurant), guests can choose from a menu dedicated uniquely (from antipasti to main courses) to Japanese Wagyubeef.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9687;La Martinatica;Italy;Pietrasanta;via Martinatica 20, Pietrasanta, 55045, Italy;43.9486764;10.2424169;40;false;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Housed in an old mill, this restaurant boasts a warm and welcoming dining room crowned by wood beams and elegant furnishings. The menu offers a selection of meat and fish dishes, although the latter are the main speciality of the owner-chef, who can usually be seen taking orders in the dining room. The raw seafood option demonstrates the skill and imagination of the chef, with its array of small bites which are both creative and delicious. The attractive outdoor space is perfect for summer dining.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9688;Rezzano Cucina e Vino;Italy;Sestri Levante;via Asilo Maria Teresa 34, Sestri Levante, 16039, Italy;44.2719487;9.3950266;65;true;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant is constantly improving and now boasts a comfortable dining room, which has been slightly enlarged thanks to a few adjustments and a reduction in the number of guests allowing for more space between tables. The cuisine pays careful attention to the seasons and to local traditions, with a particular focus on top-quality fish. The small outdoor space in the piazza makes a pleasant setting for dinner.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9689;Il Melograno;Italy;Trani;via Bovio 193, Trani, 76125, Italy;41.27565;16.41995;59;true;true;Seafood;In the village centre and therefore not right by the sea, this successful, well - established restaurant is decorated in elegant contemporary style. The menu focuses on fish dishes reinterpreted with a touch of imagination.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9690;Villa Giulia - Al Terrazzo;Italy;Valmadrera;via Parè 73, Valmadrera, 23868, Italy;45.860847;9.365469;42;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Housed within an elegant late-19C hotel overlooking the lake, this romantic restaurant offers stunning views from its outdoor terrace. The cuisine is mainly Italian, with the occasional modern and imaginative twist. Add in a charming stone wine cellar stocked with top-quality labels, plus modern guestrooms for anyone wanting to prolong their stay.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9691;Umberto a Mare;Italy;Forio;via del Soccorso 8, Forio, 80075, Italy;40.7370555;13.8550343;82;true;false;Seafood;Situated in a breathtaking location below the Chiesa del Soccorso, this restaurant boasts views of the sea and sunset that are hard to beat, while its fine, elegant cuisine, based on updated Campanian recipes, is more than a match for the spectacular setting. Featuring delicious dishes such as tagliatelle with squid, lemon and soya milk, a reinterpreted version of parmigiana, “mescafrancesca” (mixed pasta) with prawns and Controne beans, and a mouthwatering dessert trolley, Umberto is one of the island’s unmissable restaurants. The impressive wine cellar (which can be visited) is home to more than 1 000 labels, including a fine selection of champagnes.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9692;Da Gigi;Italy;Crandola Valsassina;piazza IV Novembre 4, Crandola Valsassina, 23832, Italy;46.0225142;9.3789354;34;false;false;Lombardian, Country cooking;Enjoy specialities from Valsassina in this friendly restaurant in a panoramic location. There is a rustic ambience in the dining room with cuisine focusing on local ingredients (many of which are organic), and produce from the restaurant’s own garden.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9693;Alla Laguna - Vedova Raddi;Italy;Marano Lagunare;piazza Garibaldi 1, Marano Lagunare, 33050, Italy;45.7631856;13.1655106;98;false;false;Seafood;Situated in a charming small town criss-crossed by canals, this restaurant serves traditionally inspired fish-based dishes. The restaurant stands on the port facing the fish market, so it’s no surprise that the fish served here is of the freshest quality.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9694;Corte Visconti;Italy;Somma Lombardo;via Roma 9, Somma Lombardo, 21019, Italy;45.6838676;8.7063043;32;true;true;Country cooking, Creative;A classical, rustic style environment with walls in stone and brick vaulted or wood and stone ceilings. The cuisine is authentically local but with a pleasant touch of creativity.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9695;La Terrazza;Italy;Rome;via Ludovisi 49, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9063787;12.4860308;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Innovative;Situated on the rooftop of the Eden hotel, this modern restaurant boasts enchanting views of the historic centre of Rome, from the Quirinale to St Peter’s. At the helm in the kitchen, Salvatore Bianco creates two imaginative tasting menus from which dishes can also be chosen à la carte style. A superb fine-dining experience overlooking the rooftops of Rome.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9696;Corte Sconta;Italy;Venice;calle del Pestrin, sestiere Castello 3886, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.4347913;12.3479192;81;true;true;Seafood, Venetian;From its flooring to its tables, this restaurant has the charming, nostalgic feel of a typical trattoria in its simple dining room, while the outdoor space in an inner courtyard under a vine-shaded arbour is a charming place to eat in fine weather – a real gem right in the centre of Venice. The cuisine is as simple in style as the decor, with traditional Venetian fish and seafood dishes taking pride of place on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9697;Trattoria Glisenti;Italy;Vello;via Provinciale 34, Vello, 25054, Italy;45.7564348;10.0790684;85;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated on the lakefront with beautiful views from its terrace, this restaurant focuses on freshwater fish, while also serving a selection of classic regional specialities. Careful attention is paid to natural ingredients, with vegetarian options also available. An elegant restaurant which belies its description as a “trattoria”.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9698;Sapereta;Italy;Porto Azzurro;via Provinciale Ovest 73, località Mola, Porto Azzurro, 57036, Italy;42.760967;10.370911;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a historic winery, this simple, rustic - style restaurant is surrounded by a well - kept garden where farmyard animals roam freely. Don’t be fooled by appearances, however – the cuisine here is modern, with meat dishes taking pride of place on the menu.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9699;La Filanda;Italy;Asola;via Carducci 21/e, Asola, 46041, Italy;45.2198465;10.4064164;85;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Housed on the first floor of an old silkworm factory, with a contemporary-style dining room that opens out on to a beautiful terrace in fine weather, this restaurant is one of the few in the province to serve top-quality fish and seafood, including a good selection of raw options. The cooked dishes on offer demonstrate a light modern touch and are prepared whenever possible using vegetables from the restaurant’s own garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9700;Due Pini;Italy;Madonna di Campiglio;via Spinale 37/bis, Madonna di Campiglio, 38086, Italy;46.2282;10.82951;96;true;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Although recently restored, this restaurant has retained its strong Alpine character. The cuisine is regional in style and reinterpreted with an imaginative and contemporary twist.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9701;Enoteca Del Duca;Italy;Volterra;via di Castello 2, Volterra, 56048, Italy;43.401191;10.8602737;79;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Tuscan;Despite the change of ownership at this centrally located restaurant right behind the castle and the main square, there’s a certain continuity to the cuisine which remains focused on classic dishes with a regional flavour (with the option of steak on the menu). The dining room features old stone walls, plus there’s also an attractive outdoor space for summer dining.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9702;La Cantinella;Italy;Montemarciano;località Montemarciano 70/g, Montemarciano, 52028, Italy;43.587955;11.6099216;24;true;true;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;A little country restaurant with pleasantly distinctive interiors and summer service al fresco on the terrace. Traditional Tuscan cuisine on the menu, with a modern touch.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9703;La Lumira;Italy;Castelfranco Emilia;corso Martiri 74, Castelfranco Emilia, 41013, Italy;44.5935952;11.057083;33;false;true;Emilian, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a village famous for its “tortellino in brodo” dish, Lumira serves Emilian cuisine with a modern twist. Highlights on the menu include fresh home-made pasta such as traditional tortellini and modern tagliatelle verdi with a beef and pea ragù, as well as the highly recommended veal fillet in a traditional balsamic vinegar sauce, which is full of intense flavours. Contemporary decor and welcoming service add to the relaxing dining experience. Among the Sangiovesi wines from Romagna on the wine list, we recommend Lillybet, a well-structured red with superb floral notes.;Car park;[]
9704;Trattoria Ceriati;Italy;Salsomaggiore Terme;Località Cangelasio Ceriati 18, Salsomaggiore Terme, 43039, Italy;44.8130607;9.9396271;89;false;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in attractive countryside where the plains give way to rolling hills (a perfect destination for a Sunday outing), this simple yet well-kept trattoria serves all the usual traditional local specialities. The typical fresh pasta and the desserts are all home-made.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9705;Villa Arcadio;Italy;Salò;via Palazzina 2, località Villa di Salò, Salò, 25087, Italy;45.59214;10.50393;32;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;The new chef at this restaurant prioritises beautiful presentation in his modern interpretations of Italian dishes, which are even more enjoyable in summer when meals are served outdoors, surrounded by greenery and with fine views of the southern part of Lake Garda and its shoreline.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9706;Cascina Vittoria;Italy;Rognano;via Roma 26, Rognano, 27010, Italy;45.2894891;9.0895631;56;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;Situated in a rural setting surrounded by rice fields outside Milan, this restaurant specialises in home-made pasta and breads, vegetables grown in its own garden, and Piedmontese meat cooked in traditional fashion over a barbecue grill. Takeaway produce is also available for purchase.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9707;Il Favri;Italy;San Giorgio della Richinvelda;via Borgo Meduna 12, San Giorgio della Richinvelda, 33095, Italy;46.0373064;12.8233123;49;false;true;Friulian, Traditional Cuisine;This inn, which has been serving food since the early 19C, boasts a warm atmosphere with a rustic feel. The beautiful garden makes a delightful setting in fine weather, while the cuisine focuses on traditional dishes from Friuli, such as “frico” (potato, onion and cheese fritter) and cured ham.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9708;Il Trillo;Italy;Massa;via Bergiola Vecchia 30, Massa, 54100, Italy;44.04829;10.139887;52;false;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Situated in the hills overlooking the town, this restaurant occupies an old house that is also home to the estate’s wine cellars. Charming setting and cuisine full of flavour, with the option of alfresco dining on the panoramic terrace in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9709;I Tigli;Italy;San Bonifacio;via Camporosolo 11, San Bonifacio, 37047, Italy;45.3947884;11.270984;95;true;true;Pizza, Sharing;An iconic pizzeria which has brought Italy’s favourite street-food snack right up to date! With almost 30 years’ experience behind him, Simone Padoan knows how to make difficult things easy: he uses a mix of wholemeal flours and pays meticulous attention to natural leavening processes to create a dough which has a crispy crust yet soft interior. He also focuses on different types of toppings, including fish, meat and vegetables – whether your preference is for traditional or more imaginative pizzas, every option is of the highest quality. A choice of excellent desserts provides the perfect conclusion to your meal!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9710;Tola Rasa;Italy;Padua;via Vicenza 7, Padua, 35138, Italy;45.4116299;11.8628222;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Having mastered his culinary repertoire working in other restaurants, the chef at the elegant and minimalist Tola Rasa creates successful reinterpretations of classic Italian dishes by adding exotic spices and other ingredients (often from Asia) to his dishes. The gourmet dining room on the ground floor is supplemented by a wine bar in the annexe which serves a selection of snacks. Book a table facing the kitchen to watch the chef at work!;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9711;Pacifico;Italy;Milan;via Moscova 29, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4768452;9.1885942;86;true;true;Peruvian, Asian Influences;Although its dining rooms are fairly small, this restaurant, which acts as an ambassador for Peruvian cuisine with the occasional Asian influence, has an attractive, trendy ambience and a theatrical feel. Excellent choice of ceviche – raw fish or seafood dishes marinated in lemon and flavoured with spices such as chilli pepper and coriander – which are a typical speciality of Latin American countries along the Pacific coast.;Air conditioning;[]
9712;La Cantina di Manuela;Italy;Milan;via Carlo Poerio 3, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.46841;9.2102;31;true;false;Classic Cuisine;The dining room in this young, dynamic restaurant is surrounded by bottles of wine. Elaborate dishes feature on the menu, with antipasti available in the evening. At lunchtime these are replaced by various salads aimed at a business clientele in a hurry. Milanese-style cutlets are the house speciality.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9713;Voltalacarta;Italy;Genoa;via Assarotti 60 r, Genoa, 16122, Italy;44.4111952;8.9407747;42;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;A tiny doorway leads to this simple, friendly and intimate restaurant with just a few tables, where booking in advance is highly recommended given the restaurant’s excellent reputation in the city. Its renown stems from the owner-chef’s cuisine, which focuses mainly on top-quality fish prepared in imaginative and personalised recipes using classic techniques. If it’s on the menu, make sure you try the “cappon magro” (a type of seafood salad), which is so good that it even has its own identity card!;Air conditioning;[]
9714;Opera|02;Italy;Levizzano Rangone;via Medusia 32, Levizzano Rangone, 41014, Italy;44.4980553;10.9174599;92;false;false;Emilian;A farm with rooms, a spa, a bistro and a gourmet restaurant! At the latter, enjoy regional cuisine with a creative twist added by the chef, on two tasting menus that can be modified as required. Don’t miss the chocolate soufflé served with hazelnut ice cream and caramel sauce. The farm’s own produce can also be purchased here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9715;La Filanda;Italy;Manciano;via Marsala 8, Manciano, 58014, Italy;42.5859791;11.5154382;99;true;false;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the historic centre, this restaurant occupies an old spinning mill ("filanda")  that has been completely restored without losing any of its original charm. Here, self-taught chef Barbara serves traditional dishes reinterpreted with real flair, such as the involtino di ciaffagnone filled with Maremma beef on a bed of melted pecorino cheese and crispy leek. The chef’s husband oversees the wine list, which includes a selection of Tuscan labels.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9716;Da Noemi;Italy;Ferrara;via Ragno 31/a, Ferrara, 44121, Italy;44.8330924;11.618959;32;true;true;Emilian;The mother of the current owner opened this busy restaurant in a medieval alleyway in the historic centre, giving it her own name. The historic dishes here reflect the culinary traditions of Ferrara, with specialities such as salama da sugo (pork sausage) and pasticcio di maccheroni (a baked pasta dish) on the menu. A must for anyone looking to sample local dishes already famous during the time of the Este family.;Air conditioning;[]
9717;Da Bibe;Italy;Galluzzo;via delle Bagnese 1r, Galluzzo, 50124, Italy;43.7429996;11.2153083;97;true;false;Tuscan;Immortalised by the Italian writer Montale in his poetry, this trattoria has been run by the same family for almost two centuries. The menu features traditional Tuscan dishes, such as pici pasta with wild boar sauce. Alfresco dining in summer. There are also apartments with kitchens for guests that wish to extend their stay.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9718;Il Liberty;Italy;Milan;viale Monte Grappa 6, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4804651;9.1912581;86;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Occupying an Art Nouveau-style palazzo, this small restaurant with two rooms and a loft area has a friendly, welcoming atmosphere. The menu includes a selection of fish and meat dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
9719;Punta Lena;Italy;Stromboli;via Monsignor Di Mattina 8, località Ficogrande, Stromboli, 98055, Italy;38.8054864;15.2402537;58;true;false;Sicilian, Seafood;At this restaurant, dine under a pergola with superb views of the sea and Strombolicchio – the perfect setting for any occasion. The menu focuses on fish, including raw and dry-aged fish options. The first courses have a local flavour and are particularly delicious.;Terrace;[]
9720;Il Merlo;Italy;Lido di Camaiore;via Bernardini 660, Lido di Camaiore, 55041, Italy;43.9069174;10.2154761;57;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;Situated right on the beach, Il Merlo boasts a welcoming dining room decorated in elegant, contemporary style. The owner is at the helm in the kitchen, where he creates dishes with a focus on fish and seafood, such as the raw seafood platter and the salt-baked catch of the day. A few delicious meat options, such as plin pasta and pigeon, are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9721;Battipalo;Italy;Lesa;viale Vittorio Veneto 2, Lesa, 28040, Italy;45.8289297;8.5659778;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A young couple opened this attractive restaurant next to the ferry dock some years ago. The large windows offer romantic views of the lake, while the distinctly modern cuisine focuses on meat and fish alike. Excellent care has been taken in selecting the wine list. There is also a pleasant outdoor area for alfresco dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9722;Il Capestrano;Italy;Milan;via Gian Francesco Pizzi 14, Milan, 20141, Italy;45.436924;9.201944;15;false;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo;This restaurant takes its name from the warrior statue dating back to the 6C BC which was discovered in Capestrano (Aquila province) in 1934. The statue, carved from a single block of local stone, is one of the most mysterious finds in history. No such mystery surrounds the dishes served in this restaurant, which focuses on cuisine from the Abruzzo, including top-quality hams and cheeses produced by small-scale producers, as well as mutton, lamb, beef, barbecued lamb kebabs and other culinary delights.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9723;Meltemi;Italy;Parma;piazzale Carbone 3, Parma, 43121, Italy;44.8004168;10.3284359;18;true;true;Seafood;A maritime focused oasis in a city where the traditional specialities revolve around meat, this restaurant serves fish dishes with various options ranging from raw fish to antipasti. Pleasant ambience with an attractive modern decor.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9724;Trattoria del Vicolo;Italy;Lipari;vico Ulisse 17, Lipari, 98055, Italy;38.469032;14.954721;58;true;false;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Overlooking the piazza for almost 50 years, this restaurant has been modernised but has nonetheless managed to retain its friendly ambience, especially in the outdoor space facing the narrow alleyway. The owner-chef serves regional specialities reinterpreted with his own individual twist, such as his famous swordfish rolls served in a type of pie.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9725;Casa D'Angelo;Italy;Fara Filiorum Petri;via San Nicola 5, Fara Filiorum Petri, 66010, Italy;42.2478801;14.1832014;83;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Seasonal Cuisine;Housed in what was once an old family home, this elegant restaurant serves delicious regional cuisine. The menu includes dishes that have been skilfully and imaginatively enhanced by the chef, such as warm pheasant terrine with apple, alongside more traditional fare, from cured ham to charcoal-grilled local lamb and potato gnocchi with a duck sauce. The restaurant’s own extra-virgin olive oil often adds further flavour to the dishes. The 4-course tasting menu deserves a special mention for its excellent value for money.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9726;Ba Restaurant;Italy;Milan;via Raffaello Sanzio 22, Milan, 20149, Italy;45.468098;9.151806;79;false;true;Chinese, Asian Contemporary;Two huge red lamps welcome guests to this minimalist-style restaurant decorated in dark, typically Asian colours. The carefully prepared cuisine focuses on modern, reinterpreted Chinese dishes, while the wine list also includes a good selection of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning;[]
9727;Taverna Kus;Italy;San Zeno di Montagna;contrada Castello 14, San Zeno di Montagna, 37010, Italy;45.6424504;10.7347888;73;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;An attractive restaurant situated on the western slopes of Monte Baldo overlooking Lake Garda, with a number of rustic yet elegant and welcoming dining rooms, including a bright veranda with partial views of the lake (enjoy the full vista from the outdoor terrace). Various culinary options feature on the menu, including meat, fish and vegetarian dishes, all colourful, full of flavour and beautifully cooked and prepared using mainly local and seasonal ingredients. The well-stocked and carefully chosen wine list deserves a special mention: among the 1 000 or more bottles stored in the old giasàra (underground cellar), you’re sure to find something you’ll enjoy.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9728;La Taverna di Fra' Fiusch;Italy;Revigliasco;via Beria 32, Revigliasco, 10024, Italy;45.0184894;7.7359813;34;false;true;Piedmontese;Nestling in a charming hill town, this restaurant will delight visitors looking for traditional cuisine with an updated, contemporary flavour. Specialities include agnolotti (a type of ravioli) and Piedmontese fritto misto (fried seafood and vegetables).;Air conditioning;[]
9729;Il Ristorante - Niko Romito;Italy;Milan;via Privata Fratelli Gabba 7/b, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.470812;9.1897291;60;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Housed within the Bulgari hotel, a secluded haven of elegance right in the heart of the most exclusive district in Milan, this restaurant alternates the trusted chefs at its helm, all of whom continue to serve light, contemporary Italian cuisine in dishes that focus more on substance than form. Choose between tasting menus and a generous à la carte selection featuring meat and fish dishes alike, including classic local favourites such as risotto and vitello alla Milanese (breaded veal cutlet).;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9730;Orto;Italy;Monopoli;contrada Tortorella, Monopoli, 70043, Italy;40.8565538;17.288577;57;false;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Orto is the restaurant of the delightful Nina Trulli resort. In its beautiful Mediterranean courtyard, enjoy personalised, well-presented dishes where meat and fish are balanced by the use of fruit and vegetables, many of which come from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden and orchard. Reservation strongly recommended.;Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9731;Profumi di Cous Cous;Italy;San Vito lo Capo;via Regina Margherita 80, San Vito lo Capo, 91010, Italy;38.1751048;12.7358368;43;true;true;Sicilian, Seafood;As the name of this restaurant suggests, couscous takes pride of place on the menu, although other Sicilian specialities can also be sampled here. Delightful atmosphere, especially in summer when meals are served in the internal courtyard among the citrus trees.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9732;Da Nicolo;Italy;Carloforte;corso Cavour 32, Carloforte, 09014, Italy;39.1468203;8.3080589;95;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Located in an advantageous spot along the promenade, where there is a summer dining area, this restaurant is really patronized for the quality of its food. Serving seafood and Carlofortinian specialties.;Terrace;[]
9733;Lo Scalco Grasso;Italy;Mantua;via Trieste 55, Mantua, 46100, Italy;45.1534154;10.7963241;61;false;false;Mantuan, Modern Cuisine;A small, intimate restaurant with a welcoming ambience and simple yet lively feel, where the owner-chef at the helm in the kitchen also makes an appearance front of house. Mantuan traditions are evident in the generous portion sizes as well as in dishes such as the legendary pumpkin tortelli (served with butter or a tomato and sausage sauce), while other options are more creative in style – the Emilian lamb tartare delicately flavoured with its own cooking juices, and served with sautéed chard, savoury sbrisolona cake and black truffles from the lower Mantova region in season is particularly delicious.;Air conditioning;[]
9734;Ca' Apollonio Gourmet;Italy;Romano d'Ezzelino;via Molinetto 5/a, Romano d'Ezzelino, 36060, Italy;45.7856666;11.7574494;92;false;true;Creative;This restaurant is housed in the Salone delle Colombe (the name comes from the fresco of doves on the ceiling) of a villa which dates back to the 16C, although its present appearance dates mainly from the 19C. Here, chef Alessio Longhini serves two tasting menus prepared partly using ingredients from the property’s own kitchen garden, which is surrounded by 18ha of grounds. Elaborate, creative and top-quality dishes served in an elegant setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
9735;Locanda dei Salinari;Italy;Cervia;via XX Settembre 67, Cervia, 48015, Italy;44.260866;12.3504612;34;false;true;Seafood, Cuisine from Romagna;In the old village of Salinari, a young enterprising chef runs this simple restaurant. His creative cuisine is prepared with the best regional produce of Romagna.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9736;Essenziale;Italy;Florence;piazza di Cestello 3 r, Florence, 50124, Italy;43.7703309;11.2435173;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;As its name suggests, this restaurant (once a garage) on Piazza di Cestello has a young, minimalist ambience. The welcome and service here are friendly, while the cuisine is never ordinary, offering combinations that are pleasantly contrasting without being too bold. The chef, who is originally from Livorno, is particularly adept at creating fish and seafood dishes. You’ll find your cutlery in a drawer in your table, in an interesting nod to household traditions of bygone days.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9737;L'Antico Giardino;Italy;Ravalle;via Martelli 28, Ravalle, 44123, Italy;44.92783;11.51125;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Choose from an interesting, traditional à la carte and two tasting menus (one autumn-based, the other traditional, both excellent value for money) at this comfortable restaurant, where guests are welcomed by the friendly owner who is on hand to offer wine pairing recommendations. The menu features meat tartares and flans, agnolotti and ravioli pasta, and superbly cooked, top-quality cuts of meat, with truffles often making an appearance in season. We visited in autumn and particularly enjoyed the pumpkin cappellaccio with butter, sage and almonds – a dish that stood out for its delicious, creamy flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9738;Stella d'Italia;Italy;Pastrengo;piazza Carlo Alberto 25, Pastrengo, 37010, Italy;45.4925531;10.7993215;99;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Regional specialities, including snails and pike, in a historical establishment, once an inn now an elegant establishment under the management of Signor Umberto.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9739;La Braseria;Italy;Osio Sotto;via Risorgimento 15, Osio Sotto, 24046, Italy;45.615921;9.5914181;57;false;false;Meats and Grills, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant is a paradise for meat-eaters – its signature dishes are prime cuts of meat (mostly beef) from different breeds, which are displayed in the refrigerated cabinet at the entrance. There’s an extensive à la carte, with various appetiser options and a small choice of “primi”, but all the attention here is on the main course. The meat is either smoked and grilled over beech wood or roasted in the wood-fired oven – there’s something here for every taste! A cheese selection and delicious desserts complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9740;De Gustibus - Maurizio;Italy;Palmi;viale delle Rimembranze 58/60, Palmi, 89015, Italy;38.3556846;15.8466654;72;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Simple, modern fish dishes full of flavour take centre stage at this family-run restaurant in the charming historic centre of Palmi. The raw fish dishes served here include a delicious carpaccio made with the catch of the day and seasoned with a delicate home-made vinaigrette and cherry tomatoes, while the “Intrusi” menu offers three or four meat options for non-fish eaters. Desserts are announced at your table and always include a delicious cannolo. The wine list features mainly Italian labels, as well as a choice of champagnes. An intimate and warmly recommended restaurant.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9741;Baccanti;Italy;Matera;via Sant'Angelo 58/61, Matera, 75100, Italy;40.665718;16.6125726;54;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Facing Matera’s picturesque cave churches in one of the most charming parts of the old town, this restaurant is housed in a complex of old caves. Despite being inspired by local traditions, the cuisine is modern and creative in style and always of the highest quality.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9742;Botero;Italy;Crema;via Giuseppe Verdi 7, Crema, 26013, Italy;45.3634877;9.6842952;23;true;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Close to the town centre and within walking distance of the Duomo, this restaurant is housed in a beautiful historic palazzo. The cuisine is delicious, with a menu featuring fish dishes (depending on market availability) and a few more traditional recipes such as sweet tortelli and the excellent nettle and angler fish gnudi. The friendly welcome and streamlined service explain the restaurant’s popularity at both lunch and dinner, so booking is recommended!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9743;Lipadusa;Italy;Lampedusa;via Bonfiglio 16, Lampedusa, 92010, Italy;35.5038155;12.6116345;17;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;In the centre of the village, a classic very simple atmosphere for this family run establishment with typical gastronomic dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9744;Pierino Penati;Italy;Vigano;via XXIV Maggio 36, Vigano, 23897, Italy;45.72778;9.3263;93;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Surrounded by the greenery of the Brianza hills, this villa on the outskirts of the village boasts a delightful garden and an elegant dining room with a veranda. Although the cuisine here is traditional in style, it showcases the best of the Mediterranean in dishes that often feature modern preparation and combinations. Special attention is paid to the desserts, many of which are highly innovative, including one that pays homage to the Rubik’s cube. The impressive, well-structured wine list includes a selection of renowned labels from Italy and further afield alongside some younger, lesser-known options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9745;Da Odino;Italy;Quarto d'Altino;via Roma 87, Quarto d'Altino, 30020, Italy;45.5843;12.35232;56;false;true;Seafood, Venetian;This restaurant has stood on this square for many years, having been built as a “casone” and previously used as a dance hall. Despite its large size, the atmosphere is pleasant and convivial, helped by the staff here who are friendly yet professional. Situated just a stone’s throw from the Park Hotel Junior, a modern hotel under the same ownership, the restaurant specialises in fish and seafood, although you’ll also find meat and vegetarian options on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9746;La Gritta;Italy;Palau;Vicolo del Faro, Palau, 07020, Italy;41.1858812;9.3800602;95;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Two of your senses will experience powerful marine sensations in this place. Your sight will be delighted with the enchanting view, especially from the terrace, and your taste will be tantalised by the imaginative, top - quality cuisine.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9747;Al Paradiso;Italy;Paradiso di Pocenia;via Sant'Ermacora 1, Paradiso di Pocenia, 33050, Italy;45.8679453;13.1455303;58;false;true;Regional Cuisine;A small gem of a restaurant housed in an old farmhouse adorned with beautiful drapes and decorations. Although there’s a new chef here, the long family tradition of regional cuisine (mainly meat dishes and game) remains unchanged, with a large spit for roasting meat in the fireplace in the main dining room.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9748;Sibilla;Italy;Tivoli;via della Sibilla 50, Tivoli, 00019, Italy;41.9666953;12.8003138;97;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This long-established family-run restaurant occupies a stunning location at the foot of the Temple of Vesta, which can be admired from the attractive outdoor terrace. The classic cuisine served here is prepared mainly with local ingredients, although a few fish dishes also feature. Grilled dishes are among the house specialities.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9749;Mildas;Italy;Giustino;via Rosmini 7, località Vadaione, Giustino, 38086, Italy;46.1510361;10.7676124;90;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Housed in what was once the chapel of a medieval monastery, Mildas serves classic specialities from Trento alongside a selection of dishes created by Mirko, the late founder of the restaurant, which is now run by his son. The wine list features illustrations and descriptions.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9750;Degusteria del Gigante;Italy;San Benedetto del Tronto;via degli Anelli 19, San Benedetto del Tronto, 63074, Italy;42.9511109;13.8754968;32;false;true;Country cooking, Cuisine from the Marches;Situated in the charming historic centre of the upper part of the town, right behind the Torre dei Gualtieri, this restaurant occupies a 19C building with 15C foundations. Regional cuisine skilfully reinterpreted with a modern twist takes pride of place on the menu, where the focus is on flavour and seasonal ingredients rather than a vast selection of dishes. House specialities include options such as boned caramelised rabbit served with its own jus (inspired by the better-known traditional Marche dish), while daily visits to the market usually result in one or two fish-based recipes.;Terrace;[]
9751;Next2;Italy;Positano;via Pasitea 242, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6284701;14.4816249;82;true;true;Contemporary;This restaurant is renowned for its excellent, modern and inviting cuisine. The menu showcases mostly regional ingredients (including meat) that are transformed into delicious recipes – the spinach ravioli with braised beef and blue bufala cheese, and the raw and cooked tuna with burrata, cherry tomatoes and basil are highly recommended. The impressive wine list and selection of cocktails can also be enjoyed as an aperitif or post-dinner drink at the wine bar.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9752;La Fiaschetteria;Italy;Besenzone;via Bersano 59/b, Besenzone, 29010, Italy;44.9829442;10.011612;81;true;true;Emilian;Enjoy excellent reinterpretations of Emilian classics in this large 18C farmhouse. It is lit with modern designer - style chandeliers and warmed by a large fireplace. The three splendid guestrooms combine elegance with typical regional decor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9753;Balin Sestri Levante;Italy;Sestri Levante;viale Rimembranza 33, Sestri Levante, 16039, Italy;44.27093;9.393551;28;true;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;An intimate restaurant on the seafront with a tiny dining room and small veranda, and a young, contemporary ambience. The Mediterranean-style cuisine is modern and creative with a focus on Ligurian ingredients to which the chef adds the occasional Asian twist, often in the sauces. Booking ahead is recommended given the limited number of tables here!;;[]
9754;Osteria dalla Peppa;Italy;Fano;via Vecchia 8, Fano, 61032, Italy;43.8406532;13.0191918;78;false;false;Cuisine from the Marches, Traditional Cuisine;Already popular in the late 19C, this inn in the town’s historic centre has retained its vintage atmosphere, period furnishings and decor. The cuisine focuses on local produce, with fresh pasta a house speciality.;Terrace;[]
9755;La Cascina 1899;Italy;Rocella Jonica;strada statale 106, Rocella Jonica, 89047, Italy;38.31031;16.37146;90;true;true;Calabrian, Classic Cuisine;Situated on the main road running alongside the sea, this pleasant restaurant with a large car park occupies a late-19C building that has been transformed into an attractive, rustic-style eatery with plenty of outdoor areas and air-conditioned rooms with exposed-stone walls and wooden ceilings that provide welcome respite from the heat of summer. It’s no surprise that fish and seafood take pride of place on the menu, although meat dishes also feature. The shop next door sells regional specialities, some produced by the restaurant itself, including the famous local bergamot citrus fruit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9756;Corsaro Nero;Italy;Marina di Arbus;Località Portu Maga, Marina di Arbus, 09031, Italy;39.5779213;8.4661307;41;false;true;Seafood;A wide choice of fresh fish and a menu with a firm focus on fish and seafood served in a large dining room offering views of the spectacular sunsets.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9757;Crotto Valtellina;Italy;Malnate;via Fiume 11, località Valle, Malnate, 21046, Italy;45.8023266;8.8712122;64;true;false;Cuisine from Valtellina;With a bar or wine cellar located just inside the entrance, followed by a rustic dining hall, this restaurant serves strictly Valtellinese cuisine. Outdoor service in the summer, in the area below the cliff.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9758;Cavalluccio Marino;Italy;Lampedusa;contrada Cala Croce 3, Lampedusa, 92031, Italy;35.4994591;12.5954512;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Imaginative cuisine in a long - established family restaurant, which is constantly updated by each generation. Situated away from the town centre, yet easily accessible, the restaurant boasts an enviable seafront location. Excellent selection of local and international wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9759;Nicolin;Italy;Lecco;via Paisiello 4, località Maggianico, Lecco, 23900, Italy;45.835037;9.414134;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Run by the same family for over 30 years, this restaurant has recently been fully renovated. It serves traditional cuisine, as well as some imaginative dishes and a good choice of wine. Alfresco dining on the terrace in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9760;Tre Galline;Italy;Turin;via Bellezia 37, Turin, 10122, Italy;45.075979;7.6818915;60;true;false;Piedmontese;A bastion of traditional Piedmontese cuisine, the main dining room at this restaurant boasts a profusion of wood from its parquet flooring to the wood panelling and exposed roofbeams. The warm, hearty cuisine features local specialities such as vitello tonnato, agnolotti pasta with roast meat sauce and a selection of mixed boiled meats, as well as a cheese trolley.;Air conditioning;[]
9762;Osteria 1126;Italy;Poggibonsi;località Cinciano 2, Poggibonsi, 53036, Italy;43.506123;11.176454;20;false;true;Tuscan;The 1126 in the name of this restaurant refers to the year in which the hilltop hamlet in which it is situated was founded. Today the hamlet is home to apartments with their own kitchen, as well as the main villa. In the restaurant, a young enthusiastic couple serves contemporary - style cuisine made from local ingredients.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9763;Casa del Nonno 13;Italy;Mercato San Severino;via Caracciolo 13, loc. Sant'Eustachio, Mercato San Severino, 84085, Italy;40.7689224;14.7048003;79;true;false;Campanian, Modern Cuisine;Recently re-opened under new management, this charming restaurant winds its way from room to room until you finally arrive at the palazzo’s old cellars, the jewel in its crown. The cuisine here has quickly made a name for itself, focusing on strong links with regional traditions and showcasing local favourites on a menu full of tempting options, including salumi, local vegetables, pasta dishes, grilled meat options and typical local ingredients such as San Marzano tomatoes. The delicious cuisine pays tribute to the fine culinary traditions of Campania.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9764;Estro Vino e Cucina;Italy;Venice;calle Crosera, sestiere Dorsoduro 3778, Venice, 30123, Italy;45.4360388;12.3250367;44;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated slightly off the beaten track, this modern wine bar is also a restaurant serving Mediterranean cuisine accompanied by a selection of 700 organic wines. Snacks are available at aperitif hour.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9765;Christian & Manuel;Italy;Vercelli;corso Magenta 71, Vercelli, 13100, Italy;45.3198162;8.4327203;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant features sophisticated, creative cooking and top quality ingredients, without forgetting the culinary traditions of the area and region. Therefore, don't be surprised by the special attention reserved for rice: the menu offers a selection of twenty risottos, but also a lot of delicious land and sea specialities.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9766;Duo Ristorante;Italy;Lecce;via Giuseppe Garibaldi 11, Lecce, 73100, Italy;40.3561839;18.1754414;82;true;true;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;This elegant, intimate restaurant with subdued lighting is the perfect choice for a romantic gourmet dinner. The chef offers several different menus, allowing guests to choose their main course from any of these. Creative cuisine, with a strong focus on ingredients from Puglia.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9767;Gatto Rosso;Italy;Taranto;via Cavour 2, Taranto, 74123, Italy;40.474326;17.238965;93;true;true;Seafood;This small, long - established restaurant has been run by the same family for three generations, as depicted by the black - and - white photos on the walls. Simple and well - maintained dining room, plus a menu which focuses uniquely on fish dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
9768;Umberto De Martino;Italy;San Paolo d'Argon;via Madonna d'Argon 4/6, San Paolo d'Argon, 24060, Italy;45.6939;9.804207;47;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Part of the Florian Maison hotel in a bucolic setting of rolling hills, this large, elegant restaurant serves as a backdrop for tasting menus from which guests can choose dishes (three or more) à la carte style on weekday lunchtimes. Originally from the Sorrentine peninsula, chef Umberto Sorrentino’s origins clearly influence some of his recipes, which feature vegetables and plenty of fish alongside a few meat options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9769;Rifugio Fuciade;Italy;San Pellegrino;località Fuciada - Soraga di Fassa, San Pellegrino, 38035, Italy;46.3941786;11.8290076;93;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Alpine;To give you an idea of the Alpine location of this restaurant framed by the Costabella mountain chain, suffice it to say that for centuries it was used for mountain pasture. There’s a breathtaking view of the Dolomites which extend into the distance as far as Pale di San Martino, while the menu here focuses on regional recipes such as canderli dumplings on a bed of cabbage, veal stew with polenta and chanterelle mushrooms, and polenta gnocchetti with herb pesto, smoked ricotta and lemon thyme. The wine cellar is home to more than 600 labels, plus accommodation is available in a choice of tranquil guestrooms.;Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9770;Il Capriolino;Italy;Vodo di Cadore;via Nazionale 108, Vodo di Cadore, 32040, Italy;46.421549;12.2410254;82;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;This elegant restaurant has been run by the same family for years and has a history dating back over two centuries. It serves regional yet creative cuisine and has a distinctly Middle European ambience with its hunting trophies, clocks and frescoes.;Car park;[]
9771;Cucina Bacilieri;Italy;Ferrara;via Terranuova 60, Ferrara, 44121, Italy;44.833508;11.622814;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;There are just a few tables in this excellent restaurant, which takes its name from its owner - chef. It serves modern and occasionally creative cuisine with strong links to typical regional specialities, such as eel and pasticcio ferrarese (a baked pasta dish).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9773;La Meridiana;Italy;Domodossola;via Rosmini 11, Domodossola, 28845, Italy;46.1143171;8.2906172;50;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;In business for over 50 years, this long-established, centrally located restaurant has changed its look over the years and is now a modern bistro with an attractive outdoor summer space overlooking the magical town centre. Here, the owner-chef serves fish prepared in two different ways, either in typical Italian tradition or in a style inspired by his native Spain – his paella is definitely worth sampling! The front of house is overseen by the owner’s friendly wife, who is also at hand to help with your wine choices.;Air conditioning;[]
9774;SaleGrosso;Italy;Milano Marittima;viale II Giugno 15, Milano Marittima, 48015, Italy;44.2685332;12.3543831;18;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;One of the town’s authentic favourites, this fish restaurant has a pleasant, light - coloured decor inspired by the sea. The eclectic cuisine includes tapas and raw fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9775;Satricvm;Italy;Le Ferriere;strada Nettunense 1227, Le Ferriere, 04100, Italy;41.511547;12.742595;64;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Their experience in London, as well as in restaurants around the world, is evident in the pleasant yet somewhat unexpected international atmosphere created by this husband-and-wife team. Using modern techniques and locally sourced produce, the chef succeeds in showcasing the Agro Pontino area in his cuisine which is contemporary while still respecting the traditions of the region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9776;Cocchi;Italy;Parma;via Gramsci 16/a, Parma, 43126, Italy;44.805573;10.30785;42;false;false;Emilian;This restaurant adjoining the Daniel hotel is the town’s pride and joy. Here, two quiet, rustic-style dining rooms provide the backdrop for typical Parma specialities that change with the passing seasons – the “tortelli alle erbette” (tortelli pasta with herbs) with parmesan and melted butter is particularly delicious – all accompanied by an excellent choice of wines. Booking in advance is highly recommended as the restaurant is extremely popular with visitors and locals alike.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
9777;Parizzi;Italy;Parma;strada della Repubblica 71, Parma, 43121, Italy;44.7996181;10.3367404;23;false;true;Creative;Based around carefully chosen ingredients sourced from the best local producers, the cuisine served at this restaurant is light and yet tasty. You’ll find typical Parma dishes on the menu here alongside more creative fare, with a slight emphasis on fish and seafood although meat and game (one of the chef’s passions!) also make an appearance. Together with his wife Cristina who oversees the front of house, chef Marco Parizzi continues his family’s tradition of providing a warm welcome and excellent cuisine. Guestrooms (this is a convenient central location) are also available.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9778;Antica Locanda del Villoresi;Italy;Nerviano;via Sempione 4, Nerviano, 20014, Italy;45.56193;8.96935;33;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;What was once a post station is now a renowned restaurant overlooking the Villoresi canal. Although the attractive dining room has retained some of its historical features, the decor here is more contemporary in feel. The Mediterranean-style cuisine focuses mainly on fish and is beautifully presented, with dishes such as fried artichokes with red prawns and bottarga on the menu in season. Raw fish dishes are also occasionally available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9779;Le Viole;Italy;Castelnovo di Baganzola;strada nuova di Castelnuovo 60/a, Castelnovo di Baganzola, 43126, Italy;44.866642;10.327356;62;true;false;Emilian, Modern Cuisine;Regionally based cuisine with the occasional hint of creativity and a good choice of à la carte dishes are the highlights at this friendly restaurant on the outskirts of Parma. An authentic, genuine welcome, with an attractive lounge near the entrance and the warm ambience of a private home.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9780;Il Basilisco;Italy;Treviso;via Bison 34, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.665562;12.2693492;38;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Situated in a residential district on the outskirts of town, this simple restaurant with a colourful decor serves excellent cuisine. Although many of the dishes are typical Italian favourites, it is the local specialities, such as the sopa coada di piccione (a type of warm pigeon soup), that particularly won us over. The menu also features a few fish options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9781;Da Concettina ai Tre Santi;Italy;Naples;via Arena alla Sanità 7 bis, Naples, 80137, Italy;40.8574297;14.2531973;36;false;true;Pizza;Situated in the heart of the ancient, lively and often chaotic working class district of Sanità, this excellent pizzeria has been run by the Oliva family for over 60 years. It has succeeded in reinventing itself with each generation while retaining its traditional roots. Modern and imaginative pizzas feature on the menu alongside various fried specialities.;Air conditioning;[]
9782;Ma.Ri.Na.;Italy;Olgiate Olona;piazza San Gregorio 11, Olgiate Olona, 21057, Italy;45.6342966;8.8883882;93;false;false;Seafood;The classic and timelessly elegant Ma.Ri.Na restaurant has been a bastion for fish and seafood enthusiasts for decades. The menu features classic Italian specialities alongside more creative options, including a good selection of raw dishes as well as delicious seafood pastas and risottos. The wine list is also impressive and includes an array of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9783;Franceschetta 58;Italy;Modena;strada Vignolese 58, Modena, 41124, Italy;44.638753;10.9316204;83;false;true;Emilian, Regional Cuisine;This lively, welcoming restaurant serves simple and traditional regional cuisine, especially from Emilia Romagna, alongside more creative fare. The “Tradizione in evoluzione” menu features classic favourites such as gramigna pasta with cream and sausage, while the “I love Modena” menu showcases more imaginative recipes, including a sweet cacio e pepe dish as a dessert. The menu also includes tortellini made by the Il Tortellante association founded by Massimo Bottura, a rehabilitation centre where young people and adults on the autistic spectrum learn to make fresh pasta by hand. The wine list has just a few carefully chosen wines, with a whole page dedicated to Lambrusco.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9784;Sa Corte;Italy;Oliena;via Nuoro 138, Oliena, 08025, Italy;40.282924;9.3976647;37;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Local gastronomic traditions are demonstrated at their best in this rustic restaurant, which serves delicious pasta, excellent meat and fragrant Sardinian wines. Our favourite dishes include the goat kid with artichokes and the almond and flower petal desserts.;Air conditioning,Garden or park;[]
9785;Regio Patio;Italy;Garda;via San Francesco d'Assisi 23, Garda, 37016, Italy;45.5742513;10.7082466;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated just a stone’s throw from the lakefront, this elegant gourmet restaurant in the Regina Adelaide hotel boasts an attractive English-style garden, as well as a beautiful outdoor patio and stylish dining room. The two tasting menus served here (one of which is vegetarian) showcase the traditions of Lake Garda and its surrounding region with a creative twist using vegetables from the property’s own kitchen garden and a focus on seasonal ingredients. There’s also an extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9786;Teresa;Italy;Pegli;piazza Lido di Pegli 5 r, Pegli, 16156, Italy;44.4244448;8.803161;29;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Over half a century has passed since this restaurant was opened in 1968 by “mamma” Teresa and “papa” Giuseppe – and it’s still going strong! And although the staff here are proud of the restaurant’s long history and sense of tradition, they are not bound by it, as demonstrated by dishes that have successfully moved with the times, incorporating modern touches to the classic recipes, while always retaining a focus on fresh, high-quality ingredients (especially when it comes to choosing fish).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9787;Il Mecenate;Italy;Lucca;via del Fosso 94, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8456709;10.5101093;95;false;false;Tuscan, Country cooking;Occupying the premises of a historic local laundry along the city “moat”, this authentic trattoria has a friendly, convivial ambience. The menu showcases local dishes to the full, including specialities such as “tordelli lucchesi” (ravioli stuffed with different meats, thyme and nutmeg and always served with a meat ragù), tripe and bread pudding, the original recipe of which dates back to the 18C. A picturesque outdoor terrace facing San Francesco church and an excellent wine selection complete the picture.;Terrace;[]
9788;Osteria del Guà;Italy;Bagnolo;via Risaie 1/2, Bagnolo, 36045, Italy;45.3575174;11.37135;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Guà was the name in local dialect of the River Novo, alongside which the property is situated. Dine under the arcades of the barchessa in fine weather, soaking up the tranquil atmosphere of the park, and in the intimate, romantic dining room in winter, which boasts the same elegant style as the rest of the hotel. Enjoy refined reinterpretations of local specialities in the evening, and simpler fare at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9789;Ristorante 1500;Italy;San Vigilio;via Pavicolo 43, funivia per raggiungere il ristorante in via Villa 3, San Vigilio, 39011, Italy;46.6211118;11.140872;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;If you’re not a guest at the Vigilius Mountain Resort hotel where this restaurant is situated, leave your car in Lana and take the short cable-car ride to Monte San Vigilio where you’ll find the hotel at an altitude of 1 500m (remember to check the time of the last cable-car back down the mountain!). Decorated with a profusion of wood, the dining room has the same modern feel as the creative mountain cuisine prepared by the new chef who started here in 2023.;Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9790;Vino Buono;Italy;Grumello del Monte;via Castello 20, Grumello del Monte, 24064, Italy;45.6366149;9.8714751;43;true;false;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;Housed in an old 17C hay barn near the Duomo belltower, this interesting wine bar offers around 400 different labels to accompany an array of simple yet well-prepared traditional dishes (including a few fish options). Highlights include the cured hams, cheeses and the excellent starters.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9791;Finger's Garden;Italy;Milan;via Keplero 2, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4927692;9.1985423;22;false;true;Fusion, Asian Contemporary;Firmly aimed at a trendier crowd, this restaurant has soft lighting and an Oriental feel. The chef here skilfully creates a range of dishes, including raw fish options and original fusion cuisine with a hint of Brazilian flavour. Gourmet diners will be happy to give full rein to the chef on his surprise menu.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9792;Emilio;Italy;Fermo;via Girardi 1, loc. Casabianca, Fermo, 63900, Italy;43.210065;13.7824585;99;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;With 60 years of history behind it, Emilio can definitely be described as a leading light on the region’s restaurant scene. The restaurant is renowned for its excellent fish, which is usually cooked in classic style (fish stew and mixed steamed fish served on steamed vegetables are prime examples) and often announced at your table, although a concise menu is also available. The elegant dining room is enhanced by a collection of striking works of art.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
9793;da Omar;Italy;Lido di Jesolo;via Dante Alighieri 21, Lido di Jesolo, 30016, Italy;45.5069144;12.6472815;84;true;false;Seafood;Passion and enthusiasm overcome all obstacles and lead to the best results: this summarises the professional journey of the chef at this restaurant. He prepares fish dishes inspired by classic Italian cuisine, sometimes with a modern twist, but always using the best quality produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9794;Belle Parti;Italy;Padua;via Belle Parti 11, Padua, 35139, Italy;45.408798;11.8742425;41;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seafood;Occupying the ground floor of the historic Palazzo Prosdocimi in a delightful arcaded alleyway in Padova’s pedestrianised centre, this charming restaurant has a warm and romantic atmosphere thanks to its decor of paintings, mirrors and wood panelling, plus a beautiful ceiling with exposed wooden beams. The menu follows the changing seasons, offering a selection of delicious, classic dishes, with meat and – especially – fish (mostly from the Veneto) featuring on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
9795;Campiello;Italy;San Giovanni al Natisone;via Nazionale 46, San Giovanni al Natisone, 33048, Italy;45.9723045;13.398605;44;false;true;Seafood;Although the homemade breadsticks and preserves (available for purchase) at this long-established restaurant should not be missed, Campiello’s highlights are its fish and wine – the fish served here is among the best in the region. We highly recommend the fish soup served with shellfish and a Buzara sauce, while the wine cellar is home to a selection of 25 000 bottles, with wines from the nearby Collio and Colli Orientali vineyards taking centre stage. A selection of renowned labels from Italy and abroad also features, offering an incredible choice of the highest quality for wine connoisseurs. There’s also the option of dining at the informal osteria next door.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9796;L'Acchiatura;Italy;Racale;via Marzani 12, Racale, 73055, Italy;39.96073;18.09482;58;false;false;Apulian, Traditional Cuisine;Delicious cuisine from Puglia, including excellent orecchiette pasta with clams and chickpeas, served in a delightful ambience with a number of different rooms and internal patios. The same traditional atmosphere is evident in the attractive, well - equipped guestrooms, as well as in the picturesque swimming pool housed in a grotto.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9797;Degli Angeli;Italy;Magliano Sabina;località Madonna degli Angeli, Magliano Sabina, 02046, Italy;42.38605;12.49566;51;true;true;Cuisine from Lazio, Traditional Cuisine;The family that runs this excellent restaurant with views of the surrounding countryside has been doing so with passion and experience for over a century. The menu here focuses on the culinary traditions of Lazio, while the wine and extra-virgin olive oil are also sourced locally. The restaurant is part of a hotel and includes a shop (La Bottega delle Delizie) selling home-made produce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9798;Trattoria al Ponte;Italy;Lusia;via Bertolda 27, località Bornio, Lusia, 45020, Italy;45.0819;11.66184;46;true;false;Country cooking;Meat and freshwater fish feature on the menu at this restaurant, where the chef creates traditional dishes with an imaginative twist, such as his legendary risotto (made from seasonal ingredients) and breast of guinea fowl with mustard. An oasis surrounded by greenery, situated right by a bridge, and embellished by a small illuminated pool.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9799;Palazzo Petrucci;Italy;Naples;via Posillipo 16 b/c, Naples, 80123, Italy;40.8217366;14.2151622;80;false;false;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;The entrance from the street does little to prepare you for the surprise that awaits once you’ve taken the lift down to this restaurant, where the dining room looks out at the beach and guests dine with the sound of the waves as a romantic backdrop. In a modern and minimalist setting, chef Lino Scarallo offers a choice of tasting menus, include a surprise option on which he has carte blanche, and others based on signature dishes that include raw fish options and meat specialities.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9800;Il Pozzo;Italy;Reggio Emilia;viale Allegri 7, Reggio Emilia, 42121, Italy;44.70167;10.6293;58;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;This restaurant is housed in a historic palazzo. It has a traditional dining room, as well as an area that was once home to a wine bar (vaulted ceilings and more convivial atmosphere). A full range of Italian specialities are served.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9802;A Spurcacciun-a;Italy;Savona;via Nizza 41 r, Savona, 17100, Italy;44.2903777;8.4530366;81;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Always a good choice for gourmet cuisine, this lovely restaurant within the Hotel Mare boasts a fine location with a garden for summer dining overlooking the beach and the sea. Whether you’re soaking up the views outside or sitting comfortably in the attractive contemporary-style dining room, it’s Simone Perata’s cuisine that will convince you that you’ve chosen the best place in town. The menu is teeming with delicious dishes made from top-quality ingredients (especially fish, such as the delicious whitebait with grilled artichokes and green curry sauce), all prepared with a modern twist and beautifully presented. The excellent wine list (including a few vintage labels) provides the perfect accompaniment to your dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9803;Aquadulcis;Italy;Vallo della Lucania;contrada Tenda, Vallo della Lucania, 84078, Italy;40.2185852;15.2731101;42;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;Following careful restoration, this old mill has been transformed into a gourmet restaurant with just a few tables. Here, skilful young chef Vincenzo Cucolo delights guests with his cuisine – a combination of creative dishes and old recipes focusing on traditional Cilento ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
9804;Langosteria;Italy;Milan;via Savona 10, Milan, 20144, Italy;45.4555197;9.1682937;52;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;If you are looking for fish specialities, you will find this restaurant a real revelation. Raw dishes, oysters and seafood take pride of place on the menu, alongside freshly caught fish. An excellent wine selection and a glamorous ambience complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9805;La Perla;Italy;Varese;via Carrobbio 19, Varese, 21100, Italy;45.8160744;8.8255591;56;false;true;Seafood, Contemporary;Housed in a historic palazzo on the charming Piazza della Motta in the town centre, this restaurant is one you will immediately want to share with family and friends thanks to its delicious cuisine. The menu focuses mainly on fish and seafood (including impressive raw fish dishes) although a few meat options are also available. Good choice of wines and spirits.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9806;Maxi;Italy;Vico Equense;via Luigi Serio 8, SS 145 Sorrentina km 14,500, Vico Equense, 80069, Italy;40.6750958;14.4358353;76;false;false;Creative;From the entrance to the Capo la Gala hotel, you head down to the seafront to this restaurant, where a long terrace overlooks the rocks – if you’re looking for a romantic place to eat, this is one of the best options on this coastline (there’s also an indoor dining room for inclement weather). The cuisine is equal to the setting, thanks to the chef from Ischia who skilfully creates imaginative dishes using ingredients from Campania.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9807;Punto G;Italy;Monza;via Gian Francesco Parravicini 34, Monza, 20900, Italy;45.5839266;9.2704495;76;false;true;Contemporary;Situated not far from the town centre, this restaurant has two different spaces – a ground-floor bistro, plus a gourmet dining room on the first floor, both beautifully maintained and decorated with simple elegance. Here, a young chef from Campania who has experience working both in Italy and abroad creates modern, elegant and contemporary cuisine. In the bistro, the choice of gourmet pizzas is a reminder of the chef’s origins.;Air conditioning;[]
9808;L'Ambasciata;Italy;Quistello;piazzetta Ambasciatori del Gusto 1, Quistello, 46026, Italy;45.0092085;10.9793406;72;false;false;Mantuan, Italian Contemporary;This has long been one of those restaurants in Italy where the opulent interior decor has no equal – at Christmas, the mirrors, rugs, silverware, chandeliers and piles of books are joined by the largest and most ornate Christmas tree that you’ll ever see in a restaurant. The cuisine created by owner-chef Matteo Ugolotti is inspired by Mantuan traditions and the restaurant’s previous famous owners, occasionally going all the way back to the Renaissance. Special mention should be made of the extraordinary chocolate salami – a dessert coated with a delicious, frothy, warm zabaglione poured from a copper pan at your table. The menu also features more modern recipes and tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9809;Marixx;Italy;Ventimiglia;Passeggiata Marconi 5, Ventimiglia, 18039, Italy;43.7903443;7.5981458;45;true;false;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;Located well away from the busy city centre and overlooking the luxury yachts and boats moored in the harbour, this restaurant opened in the summer of 2021, at the same time as the modern Cala del Forte marina in which it is situated (the name of the marina comes from the Forte dell'Annunziata, the ruins of which are visible from the side facing the sea). Fish and seafood take pride of place here (especially raw fish dishes), served with classic, seasonal accompaniments, as well as snacks, while an oyster bar is an added attraction. Although the best tables are in the glass-fronted veranda overlooking the pedestrian promenade, the contemporary-style dining room is also attractive. The owner-chef has plenty of experience behind him, especially working in the region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9810;Locanda Nelli;Italy;Pietra Ligure;via Vittorio Veneto 15, Pietra Ligure, 17027, Italy;44.1493177;8.2829625;98;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;A friendly and welcoming little restaurant in the heart of the town’s historic centre. It’s no surprise that the specialities here focus mainly on fish and seafood, with an emphasis on Mediterranean cuisine, homemade pasta and the use of extremely fresh ingredients – the menu changes daily depending on market availability. The charming outdoor space boasts tables set out along the small pedestrianised street.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9811;I Giardini dei Rodo;Italy;Pantelleria;via Bonomo Alto - Scauri, Pantelleria, 91017, Italy;36.7594738;11.9891114;73;false;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;As its name suggests, this restaurant’s guests can enjoy their meal surrounded by verdant gardens, which are planted with palms, flowers and citrus trees. Regional flavours take centre-stage in the modern dishes in this romantic and original setting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9812;La Cucina dei Frigoriferi Milanesi;Italy;Milan;via Piranesi 10, Milan, 20137, Italy;45.460635;9.2260824;81;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An interesting location in the artistic-cultural setting of the Frigoriferi Milanesi industrial complex for this restaurant with a modern feel both in its decor and its market cuisine.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9813;Osteria Borgo Ronche;Italy;Fontanafredda;via Silvio Pellico 54, Fontanafredda, 33074, Italy;45.97329;12.586193;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;Just a few tables and an elegantly contemporary decor provide the setting for cuisine with a focus on the sea, with simpler dishes available at lunchtime and more creative fare served in the evening. There’s just one thing left to do and that’s book a table!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9814;Da Nando;Italy;Mortegliano;via Divisione Julia 14, Mortegliano, 33050, Italy;45.9453382;13.1776686;72;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The whole family is involved in running this typical trattoria, which has become one of the standard - bearers of the region. The decor is classic and elegant, while the menu focuses on local specialities such as excellent hams, good fish and, in season, superb truffles. The huge wine cellar is home to 120 000 bottles, so you are bound to find a wine that suits!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9815;Osteria Bellavista;Italy;Paderno del Grappa;via Piovega 30, località Farra, Paderno del Grappa, 31017, Italy;45.8125945;11.8696986;15;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Country cooking;An excellent modern inn offering a warm, family welcome. Imaginative yet traditional dishes made from market-fresh ingredients, with a balance of fish and meat dishes featuring on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9816;Osteria Il Principe e Il Pirata;Italy;Pantelleria;località Punta Karace 7, Pantelleria, 91017, Italy;36.8095164;12.0297886;95;false;true;Sicilian, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in a typical island house with rustic furniture and a large terrace with sea views. Here, the Casano family look after guests, are responsible for the impressive wine list and, of course, prepare the cuisine that focuses on top-quality ingredients and Sicilian recipes. Specialities include couscous with fresh fish and vegetables, cuttlefish “alla fiamma” and courgettes marinated in mint, as well as typical desserts such as the “bacio pantesco”.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9817;Gong;Italy;Milan;corso Concordia 8, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.4677288;9.2085964;22;false;false;Chinese, Asian Contemporary;East meets West in a harmonious fusion of flavours at this restaurant, which takes its name from the imposing gongs dotted around the modern, elegant dining room. The attentive and thoughtful staff are always on hand to explain the different dishes, which are influenced by Chinese traditions yet often have an innovative feel. Beautiful presentation and carefully chosen ingredients typify the contemporary international flavour of this type of cuisine, with an extensive and varied selection of dishes on the à la carte and various tasting menus. One of the latter is dedicated to Peking duck, the restaurant’s signature dish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9818;Ruris;Italy;Isola di Capo Rizzuto;Via Spiaggie Rosse, località Mazzotta, Isola di Capo Rizzuto, 88841, Italy;38.935787;17.10719;20;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Despite its rural setting inland, this restaurant is still situated within the Capo Rizzuto e Mar Ionio protected marine reserve, which helps to explain the focus on fish and seafood dishes demonstrated by owner-chef Natale Pallone on the menu. The wine cellar boasts over 200 different wines and more than 60 internationally renowned spirits.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9819;Le Due Lanterne;Italy;Nizza Monferrato;piazza Garibaldi 52, Nizza Monferrato, 14049, Italy;44.7731085;8.3531213;92;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the town centre, this typical family-run trattoria is highly popular with locals and offers excellent value for money. Iconic dishes on the menu include rabbit all'Arneis and Piedmontese battuta (a type of beef tartare), while the extensive wine list features a good selection of labels. We recommend booking a table in the first, more comfortable dining room.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9820;Ai Campi di Marcello;Italy;Monfalcone;via Napoli 11, Monfalcone, 34074, Italy;45.7994807;13.5334935;27;false;false;Seafood;Not far from the shipyards, simple but pleasant atmosphere in a family-run restaurant with good seafood options. Among the many specialties, we recommend the cold soup with raw and cooked fish. Curious note: the owner's passion for rum translates into an intriguing and unexpected selection of this liqueur.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9821;Armani/Ristorante;Italy;Milan;via Manzoni 31, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4704;9.19308;87;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Asian Influences;Elegant and carefully prepared contemporary cuisine served on the seventh floor of a palazzo which is totally dedicated to the world of Armani. Superb views of Milan combine with a decor of black marble and backlit onyx to create an exclusive and fashionable ambience.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
9822;Al Cjasal;Italy;San Michele al Tagliamento;via Nazionale 30, località San Giorgio al Tagliamento, San Michele al Tagliamento, 30028, Italy;45.7844849;12.9721736;71;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;A new generation is now at the helm in this warm and elegant restaurant decorated with a profusion of wood, adding a more modern touch to the cuisine while maintaining its regional character and excellent local ingredients. The menu has its own unique flavour thanks to the option of numerous cicchetti (tapas-style snacks) options available, either in half- or full portions, enabling guests to create their own menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9823;Terrazza Fiorella;Italy;Massa Lubrense;via Vincenzo Maggio 5, Massa Lubrense, 80061, Italy;40.6113139;14.3406507;32;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Housed in the Villa Fiorella Art Hotel, this restaurant boasts a stunningly located terrace with spectacular views of the Bay of Naples and its islands. The cuisine pays tribute to Campania and its top-quality ingredients which the chef uses to create imaginative dishes reinterpreted with his own personal twist.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9825;A' Cuncuma;Italy;Palermo;via Judica 21/23, Palermo, 90134, Italy;38.11678;13.356125;93;false;false;Creative, Sicilian;In 2022, young sous-chef Gianfilippo Gatto became the owner-chef of this simple and intimate restaurant situated in Palermo’s historic centre. The key attraction here is the quality of the cuisine, which features colourful dishes and modern interpretations of Sicilian recipes (meat and fish alike). Examples include arancina stuffed with young caciocavallo cheese and cooked in the oven, then topped with orange prawn tartare and served on a prawn bisque. The excellent wine list is completely Sicilian, with separate sections dedicated to the Etna wines produced in different parts of the region, many of which are young, promising and highly recommended!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9826;Soprattutto;Italy;Santa Maria di Sala;via Noalese 124, Santa Maria di Sala, 30036, Italy;45.5074704;12.0307818;58;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This tiny, welcoming restaurant with a bright, simple decor has long since come of age, having been opened and run by the same family for years. The wife supervises the front of house, while the husband (whose past experience includes working as a metalworker as well as a chef) is at the helm in the kitchen, where he creates classic fish dishes which are full of flavour and simply prepared from top-quality ingredients. As the restaurant is very popular with its regular clientele, booking in advance is essential – you won’t be disappointed!;Terrace;[]
9828;Gina;Italy;Aosta;via Croce di Città 25, Aosta, 11100, Italy;45.7367641;7.3167877;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;In the old town, a simple and informal location (but on the floor below there are two rooms between the Roman walls of Aosta!) for a cuisine of remarkable quality: the chef often starts from local traditions to develop them into more creative dishes, whose protagonists are often mountain products.;Terrace;[]
9829;Secondo Tempo;Italy;Termini Imerese;via Vittorio Amedeo 55, Termini Imerese, 90018, Italy;37.9848444;13.693866;85;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Situated on the first floor of a building (formerly home to an apartment owned by chef Salvatore Campagna’s family), this intimate restaurant dates back to the 1920s, as do the frescoes on the ceiling and the Art Nouveau-style flooring. In contrast, the cuisine is modern Italian with obvious Sicilian influences, including a focus on seasonal vegetables (there’s even a tasting menu that is completely vegan). All the extra-virgin olive oil used for cooking and as a condiment is home produced.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9830;Motelombroso;Italy;Milan;Alzaia Naviglio Pavese 256, Milan, 20142, Italy;45.4268405;9.1695741;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;An old, carefully restored road worker’s house on the Alzaia Naviglio Pavese canal is the setting for this modern, stylish restaurant where Alessandra and Matteo welcome guests in a graceful, elegant and yet informal manner. The menu features contemporary meat and fish dishes accompanied by a good choice of wines. If you’re curious about the restaurant’s name, ask the owners for an explanation: could it be something to do with the private dining room perhaps?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9831;Osteria Billis;Italy;Tortona;viale Piave 5, Tortona, 15057, Italy;44.8995569;8.8623259;97;false;true;Contemporary;The former bar of the railway station (situated in the park next to the station) has been transformed into this glass-fronted restaurant with a terrace for summer dining. Exciting, personalised dishes based around regional traditions and seasonal ingredients feature on the menu here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9832;DaV  Mare;Italy;Portofino;via Roma 2, Portofino, 16034, Italy;44.3032249;9.2093075;46;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The classic, wrought-iron outdoor dining space at this restaurant overlooks one of the most romantic little squares in Italy, while the view takes in the promontory dominated by its castle – a picture-postcard view that is famous around the world. The experienced Cerea family from the famous three-starred Michelin Da Vittoria restaurant in Bergamo are at the helm, serving consistently top-quality cuisine whether you’re here for a quick lunch or a gourmet dinner. It’s best to book ahead as the few tables are much in demand!;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9833;MaMe Restaurant;Italy;Viareggio;via Michele Coppino 56, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.8644236;10.2504123;82;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Situated in central Viareggio near the town’s shipyards, MaMe occupies a long, narrow space that is reminiscent of Oriental restaurants with its long bench running alongside one wall and small bistro-style tables. This informal yet beautifully kept dining room is the backdrop for cuisine with interesting technical details such as the home-made mayonnaise served with the highly recommended steamed fish dish, and the delicious sourdough loaf which is freshly baked and served warm.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9834;Locanda Marchesani;Italy;Pomezia;piazza Bellini 13, Pomezia, 00071, Italy;41.6737693;12.49847;79;false;false;Contemporary;In addition to specialities such as oysters and caviar, this restaurant serves sophisticated classic, traditional cuisine reinterpreted with a modern twist. Choose between à la carte options or tasting menus prepared with refined ingredients of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9835;Aria;Italy;Lavagna;Via Costa 18, Lavagna, 16033, Italy;44.30022;9.37766;98;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The Villa Riviera resort home to this restaurant is situated slightly inland and uphill from the sea in a tranquil oasis of greenery. The modern, minimalist veranda-style dining room is welcoming and elegant, while the summer terrace has a romantic ambience with superb views of the coast, especially at sunset. The menu features modern, occasionally creative cuisine with Ligurian influences evident in dishes such as the “La mia Liguria” dessert which combines ingredients such as basil and olives with white chocolate, pine nuts and fiordilatte ice cream.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9836;Rada Rooftop;Italy;Positano;via Grotte dell'Incanto 51, Positano, 84017, Italy;40.6274841;14.4893297;27;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Right at the end of Positano beach, and above the ground-floor night club, this restaurant on the first floor of an old fishermen’s warehouse offers breathtaking views of the village and the sea. Creative cuisine inspired by Mediterranean traditions.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9837;Locanda La Raia;Italy;Gavi;Località Lomellina 26, Gavi, 15066, Italy;44.71576;8.7983716;66;false;true;Piedmontese, Contemporary;The magnificent biodynamic La Raia farm, an enchanting 180-hectare oasis between Novi Ligure and Gavi, is home to a contemporary art foundation, the Rossi Cairo family winery, a Steiner school for employees’ children, guest accommodation, and this restaurant which benefits from a fertile ecosystem that provides much of its zero-mile produce. The cuisine is rooted in local traditions which have been reinterpreted in contemporary style. In the evening (and at lunchtime at weekends), choose between an à la carte, a tasting menu inspired by wines from the property’s estates between Gavi and Langhe, and a delicious “Sei mezze” menu featuring small samples of the restaurant’s most iconic dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9838;Specus;Italy;Valmontone;Via Casilina 315, Valmontone, 00038, Italy;41.7754172;12.9239378;44;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This charming restaurant’s name comes from the Latin and refers to the small grotto carved out of the tufa rock in the courtyard, which is home to just a few tables. The restaurant is run by a young couple, with Flavia front of house and Alessio at the helm in the kitchen. The cuisine is authentic in style, with imaginatively named dishes such as “Quel viaggio che non scordo” (“This journey I’ll never forget”) and “Dal 2014” (“From 2014”). The Riso Acquerello with fermented goat’s cheese, black truffle and herb pesto is truly memorable, while the desserts (especially the apple strudel) are equally delicious.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9839;Cucine Nervi;Italy;Gattinara;corso Vercelli 117, Gattinara, 13045, Italy;45.61078;8.37214;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed within the Cantine Nervi in the town centre, this contemporary restaurant with a completely open kitchen offers guests the choice of eating at the large counter facing the kitchen or at one of the more traditional tables. Very chic ambience, with a focus on imaginative and creative cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
9840;Olio;Italy;Origgio;SP233 Varesina 1, Origgio, 21040, Italy;45.6004849;9.0282762;73;false;true;Seafood;Housed within The Box, a multi-functional space that is home to vintage cars and contemporary art works surrounded by a garden with splendid olive trees, this restaurant serves excellent fish and seafood (there’s also a bistro serving quicker lunches from Tuesday to Friday). The delicious, substantial dishes are prepared using top-quality ingredients and a focus on traditional recipes with just the right amount of creativity. Pastas, risottos, fried dishes and soups all feature, followed by an excellent selection of desserts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9841;Da Carla;Italy;Gambolò;via Necchi 3/5, fraz. Molino Isella, Gambolò, 27025, Italy;45.26507;8.92589;51;false;true;Lombardian, Traditional Cuisine;Once a mill, this restaurant still stands next to its old canal which lends the setting a delightful bucolic ambience echoed in the warm, welcoming dining room. Highlights on the menu include risottos, frog’s legs, snails and goose - based dishes, as well as cured meats. Inviting guestrooms complete this delightfully rustic picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9842;Hosteria Toblino;Italy;Sarche di Madruzzo;via Garda 3, Sarche di Madruzzo, 38070, Italy;46.0451034;10.952054;90;false;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;The most welcoming section of the extensive Cantina Toblino complex is home to the large, contemporary and minimalist-style Hosteria. Here, a young chef serves simple reinterpretations of regional dishes with a focus on zero-mile produce with the occasional yet astute use of ingredients from further afield.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9843;Jamantè;Italy;Polignano a Mare;via San Vito 97, Polignano a Mare, 70044, Italy;40.9978139;17.2126493;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located not far from the historic centre and the picturesque Lama Monachile beach, Jamantè is an elegant restaurant with well-spaced-out tables perfect for a stylish night out. With a focus on fish and seafood, the dishes have their roots in Puglian traditions yet have been successfully reinterpreted with personalised touches by the chef.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9844;Gimmi Restaurant;Italy;Lecce;via San Pietro in Lama 23, Lecce, 73100, Italy;40.3435723;18.1570943;46;false;true;Contemporary;Despite its location in a Dominican monastery dating from 1442 (also home to a boutique hotel), this restaurant is decidedly modern and minimalist in style, with a light-coloured floor, imposing stone columns, a cross-vaulted ceiling, and a dining room with a view of the glass-fronted wine display. The service here is friendly, attentive and highly efficient, while the top-quality cuisine includes highly recommended specialities such as Capelli d’angelo Benedetto Cavalieri, angel-hair pasta with mantis shrimp, seaweed spaghetti, Galateo saffron, celery and sweet pepper.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9845;Filo;Italy;Lezzeno;SP 583 - Località Bagnana 96, Lezzeno, 22025, Italy;45.9452961;9.1867367;32;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This restaurant boasts a superb lakeside location, offering views of the opposite shore, Comacina island and Villa Balbianello. The experience is enhanced by the modern cuisine, in which dishes from all over Italy are created by the young chef from Campania, from the opening appetisers to the coffee-paired desserts at the end of the meal. The recipes are sophisticated without being overly complicated, offering a choice of tasting menus or à la carte options. The full flavours of Italian cuisine delight the palate, while the beautiful presentation provides a feast for the eyes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9846;Dry Aged;Italy;Milan;via Cesare Da Sesto 1, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4568763;9.1737929;68;true;false;Contemporary, Grills;Two partners with significant experience opened this lively venue: the rooms combine modern and classic styles in an industrial-New York style decorated with works by major street artists. At the entrance, the glass counter shows off meats of different breeds to be enjoyed even charcoal grilled, but there are also other specialties: appealing dishes with a modern preparation and homemade pastas.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9848;Bottega Culinaria;Italy;San Vito Chietino;contrada Pontoni 72, San Vito Chietino, 66038, Italy;42.3029465;14.4259026;39;false;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Nestled amid a charming landscape of olive groves, this restaurant is not particularly easy to find, so make sure that you use a satnav or ask for directions when booking. A simple, minimalist-style dining room provides the backdrop for imaginative cuisine which includes plenty of vegetables and is full of contrasting flavours and reinterpreted regional influences.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9849;Antica Trattoria Centro;Italy;Levanto;corso Italia 25, Levanto, 19015, Italy;44.1693062;9.6100282;71;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Situated in the heart of Levanto just a stone’s throw from the sea, this trattoria serving traditional fish and seafood (as well as a few meat options) has been run by the same owners for almost 20 years. Friendly ambience, good service, plus a few tables in a small outdoor space which need to be booked well in advance.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9850;Bebop;Italy;Palermo;via Riccardo Wagner 3, Palermo, 90139, Italy;38.1241378;13.3584633;85;false;true;Contemporary;Having studied classics, this young self-taught chef decided to follow his true passion, namely cooking. He prepares dishes inspired by Sicilian traditions yet reinterpreted with a personal twist, using the best regional products. The restaurant, situated in the heart of Palermo, is quiet and elegant yet also pleasantly informal in its service.;Air conditioning;[]
9851;Corbezzoli;Italy;Bologna;via Altura 11 bis, Bologna, 40139, Italy;44.4625741;11.3944139;78;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Situated in the Relais Bellaria hotel on the outskirts of the city, this contemporary-style restaurant serves equally modern cuisine which ranges from vegetarian dishes to meat and fish options, all of which are featured on three tasting menus and an à la carte. In the kitchen, the chef from Campania skilfully combines the flavours of his native region with those of his adopted Emilia in dishes which are both copious and colourful.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9853;Radici;Italy;Modica;via Grimaldi 55, Modica, 97015, Italy;36.8603153;14.7603888;97;true;true;Sicilian, Traditional Cuisine;Accursio Craparo from the nearby Michelin-starred Accursio restaurant is the chef at the helm at Radici. In two simple yet elegant dining rooms, he serves more traditional and authentically Sicilian cuisine than at Accursio, offering guests the opportunity to sample dishes created by a great chef at a reasonable price.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9854;L˜ARIA;Italy;Blevio;via Enrico Caronti 69, Blevio, 22020, Italy;45.8489326;9.1081554;38;true;false;Contemporary, Asian Influences;Occupying a modern lakeside building nestling in botanic gardens, this restaurant has an elegant and contemporary feel. Although the dishes served by new chef Massimiliano Blasone have a cosmopolitan flavour with the occasional hint of Asia, the selection of delicious desserts that follow are prepared with a combination of regional and exotic ingredients.;Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9855;San Domenico;Italy;Pizzo Calabro;via Colapesce 2, Pizzo Calabro, 89812, Italy;38.7368891;16.1636667;35;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;Perched high on the tufa cliffs overlooking the Costa degli Dei, this contemporary-style restaurant boasts superb views from its dining room and especially from its panoramic summer terrace. The cuisine served by the young owner-chef is as modern as the setting – dishes are light and almost exclusively focused on local fish.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9856;Antica Trattoria Giovanelli;Italy;Sarturano;via Centrale 5, Sarturano, 29010, Italy;44.974308;9.5089055;74;false;true;Country cooking;Situated in a charming rural setting at the foot of the surrounding hills, this trattoria has been run by the same family (now on the third generation) since 1939. Regional cuisine is to the fore here, with cured hams and roast and boiled meats all featuring on the menu, as well as its highly recommended homemade pastas and the almond tart with zabaione.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9857;iPalici;Italy;Viagrande;via Antonello da Messina 3, Viagrande, 95029, Italy;37.615884;15.1000181;29;false;false;Sicilian, Contemporary;Situated behind Acireale at the foot of Mount Etna National Park, this restaurant is located within the Relais San Giuliano. Deceptively uninteresting from the outside, this historic building and its inner courtyards boast a charm and grandeur that will take your breath away. A huge 16C wine press provides the backdrop for fine cuisine that is more than equal to its impressive setting. Here, the menu makes full use of vegetables and other Sicilian ingredients in dishes that are influenced by the island’s culinary traditions yet reinterpreted with a skilful contemporary twist by the chef.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9858;Modì;Italy;Torregrotta;via Bucceri, Torregrotta, 98050, Italy;38.1946117;15.356928;54;false;true;Sicilian, Contemporary;This restaurant has moved from its previous location in central Torregrotta to a more secluded setting slightly above the town centre, where it aims to offer its guests an even better dining experience. The owner-chef has more than achieved this, serving excellent Sicilian dishes reinterpreted with careful precision and a contemporary twist. A good wine list completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9859;Opera;Italy;Turin;via Sant'Antonio da Padova 3, Turin, 10121, Italy;45.0684854;7.6662476;97;false;true;Italian Contemporary;The former nineteenth century refectory of the nearby church has become the laboratory of a chef who is as skillful as he is creative: wrapped in the warm atmosphere of the brickwork of the evocative dining room, all the dishes have fruit as a recurring ingredient, which adds a touch of acidity and flavor to dishes of creative cuisine, whether of meat or fish, further enhanced by the work of an excellent sommelier.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9860;Autem*;Italy;Milan;via Serviliano Lattuada 2, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.4534577;9.2040052;46;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a lively district just a stone’s throw from the Porta Romana, this modern restaurant with an open-view kitchen (also visible from outside) now has a new wine cellar which is accessed via a flight of stairs and also doubles as a convivial dining room. Menus are handwritten on rice paper by the chef, emphasising the artisanal approach here, with recipes then explained by staff at your table. Luca Natalini, originally from Tuscany but also with experience from around the world, creates personalised meat and fish dishes such as red mullet and seasonal vegetables with a hollandaise sauce and lobster reduction.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9861;Canova Restaurant;Italy;Venice;sestiere San Marco 1243, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.43326;12.33718;30;true;true;Contemporary;Housed in an elegant hotel just behind St Mark’s Square, this gourmet restaurant is home to chef Gennaro Balice, who prepares visually impressive dishes from carefully chosen ingredients. Guests can choose from an à la carte or two tasting menus, one creative and Venetian in style, the other vegetarian. Simpler fare is available in the bistro next door or at tables on the outdoor terrace in fine weather.;Air conditioning;[]
9862;L'Insolita Trattoria Tre Soldi;Italy;Florence;via Gabriele d'Annunzio 4r/a, Florence, 50135, Italy;43.7750043;11.2889584;26;true;true;Creative;A long-established trattoria opened by a married couple in the 1950s and now run by their son Lorenzo who serves highly personalised cuisine with a focus on local ingredients. The dishes have amusing and entertaining names such as “Amici per la pelle” (“Friends for life”), “Non è un pomodoro” (“This isn’t a tomato”), and “Solo un chicco di caffè” (“Just one coffee bean”). In addition to a classic menu, an intriguing "Unconventional Experience" is offered, in which guests have to guess the ingredients of the dishes by following some clues.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9863;Rear Restaurant;Italy;Nola;SS 7bis Km 50, Nola, 80035, Italy;40.9326272;14.5122565;100;false;true;Italian Contemporary;This restaurant with a modern, elegant dining room in which an entire wall is taken up by the open-view kitchen serves varied cuisine. In addition to more elaborate dishes, there’s also a choice of street food such as fried dishes, sandwiches, Spanish prosciutto and tacos, as well as raw fish and seafood, classic and more creative options, and various fish and meat main courses, many of which are cooked over the barbecue grill. The superb wine list includes a fine array of champagnes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9864;Quel Fantastico Giovedì;Italy;Ferrara;via Castelnuovo 9, Ferrara, 44121, Italy;44.831357;11.6197083;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Two small modern dining rooms with contemporary paintings on the walls provide the backdrop for classic specialities from Ferrara, as well as the chef’s renowned fish dishes at this restaurant, where booking is highly recommended, even at lunchtime!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9865;Le Cicale in Città;Italy;Genoa;via Macaggi 53, Genoa, 16121, Italy;44.40222;8.94195;37;true;true;Seafood, Italian;A classic-style dining room adorned with mirrors and silverware acts as the backdrop for fish and seafood dishes at this restaurant. The raw fish is particularly excellent, as are the mupa (a little-known fish that lives in the deep waters of the Mediterranean), prawns (in season) and home-made primi served with delicious sauces, such as the chicken plin with brown gravy. For special occasions, we recommend the table to the rear of the room near the arte povera-style dresser. Cheerful, friendly service adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
9866;La Maison de Filip;Italy;Trento;piazzetta Nicolò Rasmo 7, Trento, 38122, Italy;46.0711527;11.1247675;67;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Situated at the entrance to the pedestrian section of the beautiful city of Trento, this intimate restaurant has a modern, minimalist and vaguely Nordic style, with just a few solid wood tables and stools of different sizes. The menu features a concise selection of carefully thought-out dishes, with starters, first and main courses (meat, fish or vegetarian) that are elegant, well prepared and contemporary in style. Beautiful presentation completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9867;Duo;Italy;Chiavari;via Senatore Dallorso 10, Chiavari, 16043, Italy;44.3174523;9.3232846;82;true;false;Contemporary, Italian;In this restaurant housed in a historic palazzo in the centre of Chiavari, the owners have used the structural beauty of the building to showcase the skills of local artisans, resulting in a very attractive ambience. The modern cuisine is simple in style, allowing all the flavour of the ingredients to shine through.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9868;Hazama;Italy;Milan;via Savona 41, Milan, 20144, Italy;45.4534407;9.1619599;65;true;false;Japanese, Classic Cuisine;Japanese cuisine served in a small restaurant where both the cuisine and decor are minimalist in style. Here, young chef Satoshi Hazama creates light dishes full of Japanese flavour, all made from top-quality ingredients. The kaiseki menu served in the evening consists of seven or nine different courses.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
9869;Il Marchese - Osteria Mercato Liquori;Italy;Milan;via dei Bossi 3, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4675105;9.1865103;29;false;true;Roman, Italian;Boasting a sumptuous Art Deco setting that contrasts pleasingly with the traditional cuisine served here, this restaurant is the Milanese sibling of Il Marchese in Rome which pays tribute to the famous Italian film “Il Marchese del Grillo” starring Alberto Sordi (it is also the first bar in Europe to offer more than 600 “amaro” liqueurs). The culinary philosophy here is based on traditional Roman cuisine with a contemporary flavour, including delicious specialities such as pasta with carbonara, matriciana and gricia sauces, veal saltimbocca, pork belly and much more besides!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9870;GioEle;Italy;Stradella;via Mazzini 26, Stradella, 27049, Italy;45.0771712;9.3021182;45;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated in the town centre, this colourful and discreetly elegant restaurant offers friendly and professional service. The classic cuisine served here is modern in style, offering a choice of meat and fish dishes as well as a convenient business lunch menu. In summer, tables are arranged outdoors on the terrace and in the small courtyard.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9871;Radici Osteria Contemporanea;Italy;Gallarate;via Giuseppe Mazzini 13, Gallarate, 21013, Italy;45.6603438;8.7906603;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Having moved to the pedestrianised section of historic Gallarate, Radici Osteria Contemporanea has also adopted a new look, with a lounge-bar ambience that is young and trendy, making it the perfect setting for its aperitifs and superb cocktails. The restaurant’s excellent, modern and personalised cuisine remains unchanged, however.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9872;Aprudia;Italy;Giulianova;largo del Forno 16, Giulianova, 64021, Italy;42.7508655;13.957713;51;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;At this restaurant in the historic centre, where the vaulted brick ceiling provides a striking contrast with the modern furnishings, the chef celebrates the seasons through a whole range of ingredients to create truly delicious cuisine. Interesting tasting menus add to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9874;Antica Macelleria Cecchini - Solociccia;Italy;Panzano;via Chiantigiana 5, Panzano, 50022, Italy;43.5445111;11.3164788;97;false;true;Meats and Grills;One of the most famous butchers in Italy has now turned his hand to cooking. At two locations, Solociccia or Officina della Bistecca, the menu is unique and served at a specific time with a meat proposal or a vegetarian option. Solociccia is only open for lunch.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9875;Brindo;Italy;Cusago;via Libertà 18, Cusago, 20047, Italy;45.44692;9.03405;66;true;false;Lombardian;The service is characterized by a cohesive and friendly team in welcoming guests to their small home. Brindo is an informal reality, where the cuisine is fun, engaging and more than simply territorial: raw foods, tartar and fish of the day are at the top!;Air conditioning;[]
9876;Ceresio 7;Italy;Milan;via Ceresio 7, Milan, 20154, Italy;45.4838968;9.1801177;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This designer-style restaurant is housed on the fourth floor of the historic ENEL palazzo, remodelled and converted into the Dsquared2 building. It combines the use of brass, marble and wood to create a successful blend of attractive colours and vintage decor. The view of Milan (even better from the long outdoor terrace with its two swimming pools) completes the picture, while the cuisine reinterprets Italian classics with a contemporary twist.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9877;L'Aia dei Cappellani;Italy;Trecchina;contrada Maurino, Trecchina, 85049, Italy;40.0353088;15.7820677;89;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;In the dining room there are old photos and equipment from country life, from the terrace the entire valley. Among widespread grasslands and olive trees enjoy fresh produce and home - cooked local dishes. In the dining room there are old photos and equipment from country life, from the terrace the entire valley. Among widespread grasslands and olive trees enjoy fresh produce and home - cooked local dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9878;Serendepico;Italy;Capannori;via della Chiesa di Gragnano 36, Capannori, 55012, Italy;43.8723544;10.6239469;21;true;false;Fusion, Japanese;An entertaining culinary experience, thanks to the Japanese chef who serves his own “fusion” cuisine influenced by Italian dishes (and occasionally European, such as the Basque cheesecake) with the occasional Japanese twist. On Thursdays, the menu is completely Japanese with a focus on typical specialities such as sushi, sashimi, tempura and gyoza dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9879;Caffè Dante Bistrot;Italy;Verona;piazza dei Signori 2, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.44355;10.99831;45;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant boasts an outdoor terrace overlooking one of the most beautiful squares in Verona, plus an equally attractive 19C-style room for indoor dining. The menu features a good balance of local and Italian specialities, with an emphasis on grilled main courses and a careful selection of high-quality meat. The extensive wine list includes labels from around the world.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9880;Locanda Sensi;Italy;Rivergaro;località Case Negri 116, Rivergaro, 29029, Italy;44.8948534;9.6081628;94;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;We highly recommend this pleasant country restaurant run by friendly and enthusiastic staff, where the owner appears frequently in the dining room. The ambience is modern and comfortable, the outdoor dining area boasts typical views of the Piacenza hills, and – last but not least – the food is excellent! The options on the fine-dining menu range from regional specialities to fish-based dishes, as well as various delicacies cooked on the barbecue grill, such as pigeon breast (served with pigeon leg, marinated breast, offal and rice timbale). The wine selection is also excellent.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9881;Le Cedrare;Italy;Illasi;stradone Roma 8, Illasi, 37031, Italy;45.4696236;11.1817991;84;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in the 18C Villa Perez - Pompei - Sagramoso, in a room once used as a conservatory for orange and lemon trees. It serves excellent, inventive and regional cuisine in a charming location.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9882;Osteria da Pietro;Italy;Castiglione delle Stiviere;via Chiassi 19, Castiglione delle Stiviere, 46043, Italy;45.3929003;10.4898173;30;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Housed in an elegant period building in the historic centre, this restaurant is run by a friendly couple, with the wife at the helm in the kitchen and the husband keeping a skilful eye on the front-of-house staff. Highlights on the menu include pumpkin tortelli and rose tart with Muscat zabaglione.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9883;Il Convito della Venaria;Italy;Venaria Reale;via Andrea Mensa 37/g, Venaria Reale, 10078, Italy;45.1351493;7.6258865;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is run by an enthusiastic couple, with Lucia front of house in the classic and welcoming dining room and Christian at the helm in the kitchen. The menu is lighter (and less expensive) at lunchtime with a wider choice of regional and Italian fare in the evening, plus a few more creative options, including fish dishes. Comfortable guestrooms are also available, two of which have views of the royal palace.;Terrace;[]
9884;Wicky's Innovative Japanese Cuisine;Italy;Milan;corso Italia 6, Milan, 20122, Italy;45.4598093;9.1879947;23;true;false;Japanese, Asian Contemporary;Although the contemporary, minimalist-style decor is typical of Japanese restaurants, the cuisine will come as more of a surprise, with its magical blend of classic Japanese dishes made from Mediterranean ingredients, beautifully presented and full of flavour. There are two dining rooms: one overlooking the road, and the other with an open-view kitchen and sushi bar, where the chef serves an evening tasting menu for guests happy to put their faith in his imaginative improvisational skills.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
9885;Piazza dei Mestieri;Italy;Turin;via Jacopo Durandi 13, Turin, 10144, Italy;45.081818;7.659965;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Piedmontese;Situated on a redeveloped industrial site and part of a training school, this restaurant offers a more concise menu at lunchtime with lower prices than the evening, but with the same high-quality cuisine. Our inspector recommends the spaghetti with spring onion and bottarga, accompanied by one of the craft beers produced on site. There’s also an attractive terrace for alfresco dining in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9886;CiPASSO;Italy;Rome;via Metastasio 21, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9020011;12.4759493;30;false;true;Roman, Mediterranean Cuisine;This contemporary bistro with a hint of vintage style in its decor now has a new location. The menu is inspired by Roman traditions, with the occasional imaginative twist and other more Mediterranean-inspired dishes, all showing a strong focus on seasonal ingredients. The excellent wine list includes a whole page dedicated to wines by the glass. Friendly yet professional service from the young team completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9887;Osteria alle Testiere;Italy;Venice;calle del Mondo Novo, sestiere  Castello 5801, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.4370846;12.3402061;33;true;false;Venetian, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, now one of the most popular bistros in Venice, started out as a typical Venetian “bacaro”. The cuisine focuses on traditional Mediterranean and Venetian dishes, including vegetables, many of which are grown in a kitchen garden on Sant'Erasmo island (Osti in Orto) – an initiative which sees a number of small restaurants coming together to grow and share produce. The menu changes in line with market availability. With just a few tables, booking well in advance is highly recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
9888;Bacchus;Italy;Olbia;via degli Astronauti 2, Olbia, 07026, Italy;40.908688;9.513562;62;true;true;Sardinian;Ideal for visitors to Olbia, this modern, fresh and young restaurant serves typical regional specialities alongside more imaginative fish dishes. In fine weather, ask for a table on the lovely terrace overlooking the swimming pool.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9889;Maso Runch-Hof;Italy;Pedraces;via Runch 11, Pedraces, 39036, Italy;46.6116075;11.8885636;83;true;false;Regional Cuisine, South Tyrolean;Surrounded by woods, a trip to this restaurant housed in an 18C farmhouse is like taking a journey back in time. Take a seat in one of the wood-adorned Stube-style rooms and enjoy generous portions of delicious home-cooked Ladin specialities featured on a single tasting menu, including cajinci t’ega (spinach-filled ravioli), excellent pork ribs with polenta, and apple strudel. The small wine list has the same local focus, featuring labels from the Alto Adige region. A recent addition, the restaurant also now has a few spacious, welcoming chalets available for guests.;Car park;[]
9890;Impronta;Italy;Albairate;via Pisani Dossi 28, Albairate, 20080, Italy;45.422034;8.9378778;98;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Occupying the site of a restaurant that was highly successful in the 1980s and 90s, Impronta is home to a young local chef who showcases skills acquired in a leading Michelin-starred restaurant in Sicily. As a result of this experience, his enticing dishes have a light Mediterranean feel, embellished with the occasional personal twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9891;Antica Osteria Moirago;Italy;Moirago;via Pavese 4, Moirago, 20080, Italy;45.3693364;9.1370235;39;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Seafood;This old monastery in Moirago, overlooking the Naviglio Pavese canal, was founded in 1250 and converted into an inn as early as 1478. Centuries may have passed, but the tradition of hospitality continues in the building’s enclosed painted portico, as well as in its two warm and atmospheric dining rooms. The chef’s Puglian origins explain the abundant use of vegetables and raw fish dishes, while in winter the cuisine takes on a more northern Italian flavour. Good selection of wines by the glass.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9892;Cuculia;Italy;Florence;via dei Serragli 3r, Florence, 50124, Italy;43.7687552;11.2462521;78;true;true;Contemporary, Creative;This beautiful restaurant with a smart and elegant decor has the feel of a stylish French bistro with a small library-style dining room displaying books on cookery and other subjects. Chef Oliver Betancourt left his home country of Venezuela to train in well-known restaurants in France, Spain and Italy, experiences which have resulted in multi-faceted cuisine influenced by different traditions and prepared using seasonal Italian produce as well as more exotic ingredients such as kombu, soy sauce and koji. The menu offers a good selection of vegetarian dishes, as well as a few vegan options. The wine list includes extensive information on the different labels featured, including an excellent red from Bolgheri Acciderba.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9893;Locanda Viola;Italy;Pagazzano;via Morengo 164, Pagazzano, 24040, Italy;45.532284;9.6742914;22;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Asian Influences;In this elegant restaurant with chairs and tables of different designs and original workmanship, it is skilful chef Filippo Moriggi’s cuisine that really captures your attention. The interesting appetisers take guests on an exotic journey, featuring options such as empanadas, fish bao (steamed buns, also available with a barbecue sauce) and Chinese dumplings. Other dishes are more typically Italian in style, with pastas, risottos and Bergamo-style mutton all on the menu. Desserts include a selection of ice-cream and affogato.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9894;AlpiNN;Italy;Brunico;Plan de Corones, alt. 2275, Brunico, 39031, Italy;46.7384367;11.9557234;54;false;true;Alpine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated at an altitude of 2 000m in the Plan de Corones ski area, this restaurant stands next to Lumen, a museum dedicated to mountain photography. To get here, you take the cable-car from Riscone and then, in winter, walk for around 150m through the snow. This impressive project by Norbert Niederkofler, holder of three Michelin stars, showcases the chef’s “Cook the Mountain” philosophy, where a modern approach and Alpine traditions combine to create perfect dishes full of flavour and historic appeal. The memory lingers long after your return back down the mountain (NB: the last cable-car leaves at 5pm!).;Counter dining,Great view;[]
9895;Duo;Italy;San Felice del Benaco;via Cavour 7, San Felice del Benaco, 25010, Italy;45.5858285;10.5466283;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated in the historic centre of the charming small village of San Felice del Benaco, Duo is the project of young chefs Daniele Ghedini and Federico Pelizzari (the latter also oversees the front of house). Their personalised, modern cuisine is Mediterranean in style and features meat-based dishes, vegetarian options and fish recipes (salt- and freshwater), with a focus on freshly caught fish which even has its own dedicated tasting menu. This colourful restaurant also boasts an outdoor space shaded by a pergola and surrounded by walnut trees.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9896;Senso Alfio Ghezzi Lake Garda;Italy;Limone sul Garda;via IV Novembre 86, Limone sul Garda, 25010, Italy;45.824318;10.812279;68;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Country cooking;Eala is a new luxury, designer-style hotel jutting into the lake, where top chef Alfio Ghezzi from Trento is at the helm in the restaurant. The gourmet formula on offer here, already successfully tried and tested at the Mart in Rovereto, consists of just one single tasting menu (guests choose the number of courses and some of the dishes), with precise, well-balanced cuisine made from carefully selected seasonal ingredients, including plenty of vegetables.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
9897;Al Petes;Italy;Trieste;Via dei Capitelli 5/a, Trieste, 34121, Italy;45.6480887;13.7672762;41;false;true;Seafood, International;Situated amid the alleyways of the historic centre, Al Petes has a pleasant contemporary feel and is run by young, welcoming and friendly owners. Marko’s menu demonstrates an obvious preference for seafood, most of which comes from the Adriatic, and which is served with Mediterranean and even occasional Asian influences. The surprise tasting menu is highly recommended. Just around the corner, the restaurant’s small hotel (James Joyce) is the ideal choice for overnight accommodation.;Air conditioning;[]
9898;La Foresteria;Italy;Menfi;Contrada Passo di Gurra  SP 79 km 91, Menfi, 92013, Italy;37.5995162;12.9223075;73;false;true;Contemporary;A luxurious guesthouse belonging to the famous Sicilian winery Planeta and surrounded by beautiful vineyards is the setting for this restaurant serving top-quality Sicilian cuisine. Home-grown ingredients make an appearance in some dishes, while the extensive wine list obviously features a good selection of Planeta’s own labels.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9899;Ca' del Profeta;Italy;Montaldo Scarampi;via Montaldino 19, Montaldo Scarampi, 14040, Italy;44.8241263;8.252505;88;true;true;Contemporary;Situated in a tranquil location overlooking the vineyards, this winery and elegant restaurant is owned by the “Prophet” Hernanes, a Brazilian footballer who played for many years in the Italian championship. The menu here features regional dishes alongside a few more creative options, while five modern guestrooms (some with a view) and a panoramic swimming pool complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9900;i-Fame;Italy;Rimini;viale Regina Elena 28, Rimini, 47921, Italy;44.0600315;12.5892022;42;true;false;Creative;Enjoy creative cuisine made from excellent, locally sourced produce in this attractive restaurant. It is decorated in the same white colours and modern style as the hotel.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9901;Kirchsteiger;Italy;Foiana;via prevosto Wieser 5, Foiana, 39011, Italy;46.5889205;11.1462829;75;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant has long been one of the most interesting in the area. It has a pleasing combination of traditional and modern cuisine created by the expert chef. The dining rooms have the same blend of old and new with an elegant use of local materials in the decor. Ask for one of the newer guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9902;Da Orlando;Italy;Cusago;piazza Soncino 19, Cusago, 20090, Italy;45.4457731;9.0336515;67;false;true;Italian;Simply arriving in Cusago near Milan, where the imposing castle dominates the attractive centre, puts you in a good mood. At Da Orlando, the menu is equally balanced between top-quality fish dishes such as the “bollita di mare” and meat-based dishes that will delight food-lovers, such as snails with trumpet mushrooms and duck breast with ginger. Two elegant dining rooms are the perfect setting for a romantic evening, while the attractive outdoor space comes into its own in summer. A good restaurant with over 40 years of history.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9903;Da Ercole;Italy;Crotone;viale Gramsci 122, Crotone, 88900, Italy;39.07291;17.1296597;23;false;false;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;Situated on Crotone’s seafront, Da Ercole is a culinary institution for anyone who loves fish, with the benefit of 40 years in the business behind it! The salty tang of the Ionian sea is celebrated on an extensive menu, although if you really want to enjoy yourself to the full, let owner-chef and old-school host Ercole guide you in your choice (including some excellent raw fish dishes).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9904;La Rosa dei Venti;Italy;Milan;via Piero della Francesca 34, Milan, 20154, Italy;45.4836808;9.1643696;43;false;false;Seafood;This small restaurant is perfect for anyone keen on fish prepared simply with a personal touch – and with the added bonus of providing good value for money. The restaurant belongs to the AIC network (Italian Association for Coeliacs) and therefore offers a good selection of gluten - free dishes, including bread and pasta.;Air conditioning;[]
9906;L'Ancora della Tortuga;Italy;Monterosso al Mare;salita Cappuccini 4, Monterosso al Mare, 19016, Italy;44.1458615;9.6544181;79;true;true;Seafood;Decorated in maritime - style, this restaurant is literally perched on the cliff (one of its walls is actually rock). The views from its upper terrace are breathtaking. Fish takes pride of place on the menu, which also features a few meat dishes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9907;Taverna dello Spuntino;Italy;Grottaferrata;via Cicerone 20, Grottaferrata, 00046, Italy;41.789047;12.668739;50;false;true;Cuisine from Lazio, Home Cooking;This Roman trattoria has a particularly striking interior. From its old tufa passageways converted into a wine cellar in the basement, to its charming dining rooms with brick - vaulted arches where hams, flasks of wine, fruit and antipasti all form an attractive display.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9908;Piacentino;Italy;Bobbio;piazza San Francesco 19, Bobbio, 29022, Italy;44.7690632;9.3869786;51;true;false;Emilian;Restaurant with pension near the old town, where you can enjoy Piacentine dishes served outdoors in nice weather and in the airy indoors dining hall during the colder months. The rooms are in two styles, one with wrought iron beds and Arte Povera furniture, the other being more modern.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9909;Le Logge del Vignola;Italy;Montepulciano;via delle Erbe 6, Montepulciano, 53045, Italy;43.0951163;11.7826219;72;false;false;Tuscan;This small establishment is a good spot in the old town centre. Its tables are a bit cramped but they have smart table settings and well - prepared, regional ingredients are served.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9910;Tubladel;Italy;Ortisei;via Trebinger 22, Ortisei, 39046, Italy;46.5706268;11.6789715;67;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Although this restaurant with wood-adorned dining rooms has the rustic and romantic ambience of an old Alpine hut (the name “tubladel” is the Ladin for hay barn), it is actually situated just a stone’s throw from the centre of Ortisei. The cuisine focuses on local ingredients such as meat and game, with dishes such as venison pappardelle and roast pork shank on the menu, and very few fish options. Good selection of wines by the glass.;Car park,Terrace;[]
9911;La Corniola;Italy;Pescocostanzo;via dei Mastri Lombardi 24, Pescocostanzo, 67033, Italy;41.8871637;14.0692187;32;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Cuisine from Abruzzo;Known throughout Italy for its pillow lace, the small town of Pescocostanzo in the Parco della Maiella is one of the most beautiful in Italy. It is also home to the Relais Ducale hotel and its La Corniola restaurant, which is renowned for its excellent modern Abruzzo cuisine, including delicious, seasonal dishes made from different vegetables, potatoes and onions grown in the hotel’s own kitchen gardens. Simple yet elegant dining room.;Wheelchair access;[]
9912;Terre Alte;Italy;Longiano;via Olmadella 11, località Balignano, Longiano, 47020, Italy;44.090206;12.337544;63;false;true;Seafood;One of the best-known addresses in this region for fish enthusiasts, this restaurant serves freshly caught fish prepared in simple, traditional dishes that allow the quality of the flavour to shine through. A good wine list (particularly champagnes) and a panoramic terrace add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9913;Antico Morer;Italy;Treviso;via Riccati 28, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.6671;12.24052;96;true;true;Seafood;Not far from the Duomo, this historic restaurant takes its name from the mulberry tree (morer in local dialect) that once stood in front of the building. Elegant, simple decor in the dining room, which is adorned with a wooden - beamed ceiling. The menu features fish and seafood, including a good choice of raw dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9914;Ca' Mia;Italy;Alserio;via Cascinette 1, Alserio, 22040, Italy;45.7770357;9.1962493;29;false;false;Italian, Creative;This welcoming restaurant in the hills surrounding Lake Alserio makes guests feel completely at home. The two young chefs with plenty of experience behind them create modern dishes with a preference for quick cooking methods and a focus on a wood-fired oven and barbecue, as well as fermented ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9915;Dulchemente;Italy;Olbia;via Romeo Papandrea 10, Olbia, 07026, Italy;40.925562;9.5027418;60;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;A contemporary-style restaurant which serves modern dishes alongside simpler, more classic options, with a notable focus on fish. A splendid outdoor terrace for alfresco dining and friendly, professional staff complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9916;Piccolo Lord;Italy;Turin;corso San Maurizio 69 bis/g, Turin, 10124, Italy;45.0672734;7.6974119;60;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Professional service in a welcoming, modern restaurant run by a young couple. He works in the kitchen while she (having also worked as a chef in the past) runs the front of house. Delicious Mediterranean cuisine with a seasonal focus.;Air conditioning;[]
9917;Villa Fiordaliso;Italy;Gardone Riviera;corso Zanardelli 150, Gardone Riviera, 25083, Italy;45.622208;10.56996;55;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Villa Fiordaliso is one of the beautiful early 20C villas that line the lake front. Surrounded by verdant grounds and extending out into the lake on a pontoon, the restaurant serves creative, modern cuisine. The chef is equally at ease with fish and meat dishes, while the extensive wine list suggests that you’ll have no problem finding your favourite wine here.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9918;Osteria Antico Brolo;Italy;Gardone Riviera;via Carere 10, Gardone Riviera, 25083, Italy;45.6221753;10.5619225;75;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the upper part of the town near the Vittoriale estate, this rustic 18C building is the setting for regional cuisine prepared using seasonal ingredients. The charming small courtyard offers shade for summer dining, while the interior dining room also includes a single table on a small balcony which needs to be booked well in advance.;Terrace;[]
9919;Osteria del Borro;Italy;San Giustino Valdarno;località Borro 52, San Giustino Valdarno, 52024, Italy;43.5403299;11.7152709;67;true;false;Tuscan, Contemporary;Decorated in soft colours, the elegant gourmet restaurant on the first floor (lift available) serves classic regional dishes reinterpreted with a contemporary flavour and hint of modernity. At the Tuscan Bistro on the ground floor, the menu is simpler in style but just as delicious and firmly rooted in the traditions of the local area.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9920;Capriccio;Italy;Augusta;via Filippo Turati 81, Augusta, 96011, Italy;37.2473395;15.2202918;98;false;false;Contemporary;Young chef Graziano Accolla has returned to his native city where he serves creative cuisine of the highest quality, while at the same time raising Augusta’s gastronomic profile. Thanks to his experience in Michelin-starred restaurants, he offers highly interesting dishes which focus on the use of top-quality ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9921;Sora Maria e Arcangelo;Italy;Olevano Romano;via Roma 42, Olevano Romano, 00035, Italy;41.8596733;13.0343862;39;true;false;Cuisine from Lazio;Those who judge only by appearance will walk on, those who do not will cross the threshold of this small restaurant to savour the delight of local recipes reinterpreted in modern form.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9922;Al Vecchio Convento;Italy;Varese;viale Borri 348, Varese, 21100, Italy;45.7892898;8.8494638;71;false;true;Tuscan, Grills;Ask for a table in the main dining room, with a classic atmosphere and elegant furnishings, to taste the dishes of a cuisine, which is seasonal and mainly Tuscan.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9923;Le Cupole;Italy;Rapallo;via Aurelia Orientale 369, Rapallo, 16035, Italy;44.3433058;9.2445572;32;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Ligurian;Situated on the sixth floor of the Grand Hotel Bristol, this restaurant is home to an experienced chef whose unique cuisine has a light modern touch and encompasses the whole of Italy, with a particular emphasis on regional specialities. Fish take pride of place on the menu, which also features vegetarian dishes and a few meat options. And last but not least, the restaurant’s roof-garden location gives it breathtaking views of the Portofino promontory.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9924;Filia Ristorante;Italy;Verona;via Francesco Anzani 19, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4469573;10.9894087;30;false;false;Creative, Italian Contemporary;An intimate and modern restaurant with just five tables and a minimalist design (with the exception of the “hip-hop” bathroom). Filia expresses the full character of its owner Michael Silhavì who has chosen Borgo Trento, a residential district not far from the city centre, in which to fulfil his dream of opening his own restaurant. He serves two tasting menus here (although he also sensibly also offers à la carte options), which are creative in style and occasionally play with traditional recipes such as the “Polpo alla Luciana” octopus dish. Simpler, faster options available at lunchtime. A colourful restaurant in every respect!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9925;Tamo;Italy;Spoltore;via del Mulino 6, Spoltore, 65010, Italy;42.455208;14.1331166;95;true;false;Contemporary;This new restaurant occupies  a historic palazzo in this small town. Served by the owner (outdoors in summer with views of Città Sant’Angelo in the distance), the cuisine is authentic, unfussy and prepared using top-quality ingredients with a focus on vegetables from a nearby farm.;Great view,Terrace;[]
9926;Gunè San Frediano;Italy;Florence;via del Drago d'Oro 1r, Florence, 50124, Italy;43.7698742;11.2427247;94;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Tuscan;The chef at this small gastronomic restaurant serves cuisine which acts as a bridge between Basilicata and Tuscany, the two most significant regions in his life, resulting in creative, delicate and beautifully presented dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9927;Milano;Italy;Pallanza;corso Zanitello 2, Pallanza, 28922, Italy;45.9206695;8.5538107;53;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;This historic restaurant, run by the same family for many years, is situated right on the lake (with its own private mooring), which can be best appreciated from the charming veranda. The current owner-chef has retained the cuisine’s classic style, while adding his own contemporary touch to top-quality meat and fish dishes (including freshwater fish).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9928;MARdiVINO;Italy;Treviso;strada del Nascimben 1/a, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.6487674;12.2357736;74;true;false;Seafood;Francesco is in the kitchen and his partner is front of house in this bright, modern and elegant restaurant serving beautifully prepared dishes in which fish takes pride of place. Contemporary cuisine with the occasional Puglian influence in a nod to the chef’s native origins.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9929;Kosmo Taste the Mountain;Italy;Livigno;via Bondi 473/a, Livigno, 23041, Italy;46.5373174;10.1418221;59;true;true;Alpine, Contemporary;Just a stone’s throw from the centre and also accessible from the ski slopes, this contemporary, Alpine-style restaurant boasts a spacious dining room and large picture windows. Traditional regional and mountain cuisine with a modern twist and a wine cellar focusing on mountain wines from producers working  sustainably.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9930;Gainn;Italy;Rome;via dei Mille 18, Rome, 00185, Italy;41.9039109;12.5031102;39;true;false;Korean, Asian;Since 2007, Gainn has showcased the fascinating and delicious flavours of colourful Korean cuisine, with its rice-based dishes, soups, meat, fish, plenty of vegetables and soya. The best way to experience the food here is to order a selection of different dishes to be shared with your dining companions. Those with a sweet tooth, be warned – there are no desserts on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
9931;Cosmo Restaurant;Italy;Pompei;viale Giuseppe Mazzini 103, Pompei, 80045, Italy;40.7483403;14.5045954;23;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Although the cuisine at Cosmo is influenced by the ingredients and culinary traditions of Campania, this restaurant is also an excellent choice for those in search of more elaborate and creative fare. Top-quality, complex dishes prepared by two young chefs.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9932;Vitique;Italy;Greve in Chianti;via Citille 43/b, Greve in Chianti, 50022, Italy;43.6078617;11.3019118;60;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;Providing a splash of modernity in the Florentine Chianti region, this restaurant is highly contemporary both in its decor and its cuisine, the latter available in the form of tasting menus only (guests can choose the number of courses they want). Meat and fish are cooked with expert precision and prepared with real creative flair.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9933;Guallina;Italy;Mortara;via Molino Faenza 19, località Guallina, Mortara, 27036, Italy;45.2532653;8.7910448;66;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in a small house in an outlying village in the countryside, this is a simple, inviting restaurant where you can enjoy seasonal local cuisine. Excellent wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9934;Cavallino;Italy;Maranello;via Abetone Inferiore 1, Maranello, 41053, Italy;44.5300002;10.8650464;93;true;false;Emilian, Contemporary;Il Cavallino, a long-established restaurant which pays tribute to Ferrari – a symbol of Maranello and Italy across the globe – now has the added attraction of Massimo Bottura’s creative cuisine. Traditional regional dishes, such as the delicious tortellini del Tortellante, are given interesting, personalised twists, as evidenced by the crème caramel made with 36-month-aged Parmesan cheese, chives and 12-year-old balsamic vinegar. Trendy decor, plus a flower-decked garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9935;Osteria del Tasso;Italy;Bolgheri;via Bolgherese km 3,9, località San Walfredo, Bolgheri, 57020, Italy;43.2031974;10.6098381;83;false;false;Italian, Meats and Grills;Just a stone’s throw from the famous Viale dei Cipressi avenue in one of Italy’s best-known wine-producing areas, this restaurant occupies one of the region’s most famous wineries, namely Guado al Tasso, renowned for its excellent wines. In fine weather, guests can dine in the shade of plane trees looking out over the vineyards. Simple, delicious and well-prepared cuisine, mostly traditional in style, plus specialities such as cured hams and grilled dishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
9936;La Madernassa;Italy;Guarene;località Lora 2, Guarene, 12050, Italy;44.7352143;8.0112719;65;false;true;Creative;Situated in one of the most magical locations of the Roero region, this restaurant boasts a terrace with breathtaking views of the Langhe. Here, Giuseppe D'Errico serves dishes on a series of set menus with surprise options that vary according to the chef’s inspiration. The cuisine isn’t necessarily rooted in the region but features top-quality ingredients that are presented in the style of famous contemporary artists such as Jackson Pollock and Alberto Burri – dishes are also given unusual and imaginative names such as “Grande Rosso” and “Inedita Croccantezza”.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9937;Vivace;Italy;Brescia;vicolo Rizzardo 2, Brescia, 25121, Italy;45.5391252;10.2178411;21;false;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated right in the heart of Brescia, this new 4.0 restaurant with geothermic heating and technologically controlled energy serves contemporary-style cuisine in a modern bistro with a “wine theatre” in the middle of the dining room. There’s also an attractive space with a brick vaulted ceiling in the basement.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9938;Mogano;Italy;Formello;via del Praticello Alto 7, Formello, 00060, Italy;42.0812669;12.3887081;77;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Aiming to promote craft beers as a worthy pairing for gourmet cuisine, the Faenza family opened Mogano – a modern, elegant restaurant with a wood-inspired decor, soft lighting and just five tables, right next to their Ritual Lab brewery. One of the sons (Matteo, the chef here) greets guests before dinner with an aperitif served in the kitchen. With plenty of international culinary experience behind him, he combines Italian flavours with influences from all around the world. Despite the focus on beer, a wine list is also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
9939;Zàghara Restaurant;Italy;Caltanissetta;Contrada Bigini snc, Caltanissetta, 93100, Italy;37.47557;14.01067;54;true;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Housed in the elegant Relais Villa Flora, this restaurant occupies a natural terrace with breathtaking views of the Nissene hills. The dishes are predominantly regional in style yet reinterpreted with a modern twist. There’s also a good wine selection with a focus on Sicilian and Italian labels.;;[]
9940;Materia Prima;Italy;Castel di Sangro;Località Piana Santa Liberata, Castel di Sangro, 67031, Italy;41.7782026;14.0979496;47;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a pleasant terrace overlooking a small man-made lake used for water sports, as well as a simple, modern dining room with picture windows offering the same view. The minimalist style of the decor is echoed in the cuisine, which is creative with occasionally more technical twists. The desserts offer a fitting end to your meal – the interesting selection includes one striking dish featuring the unusual combination of chocolate and saffron.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9941;Vecio Macello;Italy;Verona;via Macello 8, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4358243;10.9993649;23;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Although Vecio Macello has retained a few unusual features on the ceiling from its former life as a meat-processing plant (such as the old pipes used to provide steam for the plant’s pasteurisation and meat preparation processes), this restaurant now has a strong focus on fish. The menu offers a selection of raw dishes and classic seafood recipes alongside a few regionally influenced meat options.;Air conditioning;[]
9942;Scatto;Italy;Turin;piazza San Carlo 156, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0682914;7.6825254;49;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Piedmontese;From Turin’s beautiful Piazza San Carlo, you head through an inner courtyard to this restaurant’s modern dining room with its open-view kitchen. Whether you opt for the à la carte or tasting menu, you’ll find a balance of traditional Piedmontese and more creative dishes, all of remarkable quality, in keeping with the superb wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
9944;Ichikawa;Italy;Milan;via Lazzaro Papi 18, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.4511942;9.2078702;23;false;true;Japanese, Asian;Ichikawa is one of the culinary masters who played a part in introducing Japanese cuisine to Italy. After decades in the country working in various restaurants, this chef has finally opened his own eatery, where he serves top-quality Japanese cuisine ranging from familiar favourites such as sushi and sashimi to other less-known family dishes and street food from the land of the Rising Sun. A good place to discover the joys of Japanese cuisine!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9945;Le Macine;Italy;Vittorio Veneto;via Lino Carlo del Favero 11, Vittorio Veneto, 31029, Italy;45.978663;12.3092023;29;false;true;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;Housed in a recently renovated 18C mill on the banks of the Meschio river, this restaurant is run by brothers Giuseppe (front of house) and Adriano (in the kitchen), who serve top-quality cuisine with its roots in local traditions and the occasional imaginative twist with warmth and professionalism. It is even more appealing in summer, when meals are served on the beautiful outdoor terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9946;Le Cementine;Italy;Roncade;via Sile 6, Roncade, 31056, Italy;45.5647626;12.4074651;47;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;This rustic, vintage-style country restaurant run by the Alajmo brothers stands on the banks of the Sile river, just a few minutes from the Venetian lagoon, and overlooks a vegetable garden, vineyard and beautiful green meadows. The cuisine demonstrates a strong focus on seasonal, regional ingredients, featuring meat and fish alike, with vegetables taking centre stage in many of the dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9947;Casa Vicina;Italy;Turin;via Ermanno Fenoglietti 20/b, Turin, 10126, Italy;45.0350554;7.666969;56;false;false;Piedmontese;Renowned over the years for its traditional Piedmontese cuisine, Casa Vicina is situated near the Lingotto factory (easily accessible by metro if you don’t have a car) on the top floor of the “Green Pea”, a building that showcases sustainable and environmentally friendly products. Meat dishes (including specialities such as Fassone steak in a tuna sauce, rabbit and ossobuco-filled agnolotti pasta) dominate the main courses although fish options are also available. Make sure you leave room for desserts such as ice cream, zabaglione and Ivrea tart.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
9948;La Società Milano;Italy;Milan;via Panfilo Castaldi 19, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4772598;9.2020085;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated near Porta Venezia and its lush gardens, Giulia and Andrea’s restaurant boasts a warm and original ambience. Three dining rooms adorned with tapestries and an entrance with a fine white marble fireplace act as the setting for Mediterranean cuisine with the occasional exotic twist. Don’t miss the amberjack caponata in which the ceviche flavours contrast with the sweetness of the fried breaded aubergine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9949;Campocori;Italy;Rome;via di Santa Maria de' Calderari 49, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.89323;12.47573;48;true;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;This gourmet fine-dining restaurant, the brainchild of the South African designer Tristan Du Plessis, has arrived in the Italian capital where it’s overseen by chef Alessandro Pietropaoli. Here, choose from the à la carte or opt for one of the tasting menus (5 or 7 courses). Elegant, contemporary and cosmopolitan cuisine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9950;Radicì;Italy;Iseo;via Mirolte 53, Iseo, 25049, Italy;45.6588449;10.0509609;64;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated beneath the walls of Castello Oldofredi in the centre of this delightful lakeside village, not far from the lake itself, this restaurant with a young team at the helm has a light contemporary feel, both in its decor and cuisine. The modern design contrasts with the restaurant’s setting in a historic building, while the dishes are inspired by the recipes and ingredients of the region. Influences from elsewhere in Italy as well as further afield are also in evidence on the menu.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9951;Delicato;Italy;Contigliano;via Umberto I 2, Contigliano, 02043, Italy;42.4092142;12.7659505;60;true;true;Country cooking;Situated in a picturesque medieval hilltop village in the province of Rieti on the border with Umbria, this restaurant serves cuisine that is influenced by different regions and traditions. Choose between the minimalist-style dining rooms with exposed stone walls and, in fine weather, a charming outdoor space at the foot of Contigliano’s church. Here, chef Carlotta Delicato brings out the best of local ingredients in dishes that are kept deliberately simple and unfussy yet are full of flavour. We highly recommend the “spaghettone mare e lago” with a light brunoise of courgettes. As the restaurant is situated in Lazio, guests can enjoy good local wines made by small-scale producers, such as the Cabernet Sauvignon Masseria Baroni, which is of medium intensity with broad and pronounced aromas. .;Terrace;[]
9952;Nugolo;Italy;Florence;via della Mattonaia 27r, Florence, 50121, Italy;43.773003;11.268848;80;false;false;Contemporary;A restaurant with a friendly ambience and a chic, colourful decor and design that includes an open-view kitchen. In the latter, the young, talented chef uses seasonal ingredients to create contemporary-style dishes with an imaginative twist. The enthusiastic front-of-house team provides friendly and attentive service.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9953;Osteria Ricanatti;Italy;Ostuni;corso Cavour 37, Ostuni, 72017, Italy;40.7310026;17.5794529;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Enjoy delicious updated regional cuisine made from carefully chosen ingredients at this restaurant, where all the vegetables are sourced from the property’s own kitchen garden just a few kilometres from the village. Dishes are showcased on various tasting menus and an à la carte, and feature options such as pecorino cheese and potato tartare with a chimichurri sauce (a typical green sauce from Argentina), and paccheri pasta cooked al dente with a sauce made from two types of tomato, raw red tuna and fried capers. Enthusiasm and modesty are the key characteristics of the chef at this restaurant, which also offers a warm welcome and excellent service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9954;TerraMadre;Italy;Nettuno;via del Baluardo 7, Nettuno, 00048, Italy;41.4569587;12.659848;100;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;This small, modern and minimalist restaurant is tucked away among the alleyways of the historic centre. The predominance of black combined with a dark colour scheme gives the dining room an elegant feel, while the cuisine, prepared using regional ingredients, is contemporary and creative in style.;Air conditioning;[]
9955;Altatto Bistrot;Italy;Milan;via Comune Antico 15, Milan, 20125, Italy;45.5035529;9.2092688;41;true;false;Vegetarian, Contemporary;Situated on the edge of old Milan, this former bakery has been converted into a tiny restaurant serving vegetarian cuisine in a contemporary-style setting. The two tasting menus include delicious, colourful and beautifully presented dishes which can also be ordered à la carte. Booking is essential.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
9956;Altriménti;Italy;Milan;via Monte Bianco 2/a, Milan, 20149, Italy;45.4745344;9.1510147;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;An informal and contemporary restaurant which is elegant and yet retains a bistro feel. The cuisine is modern with meat and fish dishes featured on the menu, as well as a good number of vegetarian options. Good wine list.;;[]
9957;La Torre;Italy;Spilimbergo;piazza Castello 8, Spilimbergo, 33097, Italy;46.1104932;12.9061438;75;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Housed in the picturesque medieval castle of Spilimbergo, this restaurant boasts a splendid façade adorned with 14C frescoes, plus two rustic yet elegant dining rooms. If you’re looking for somewhere for a romantic dinner and modern cuisine, then this is the place for you!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
9958;Comi 107;Italy;Como;via Borgo Vico 107, Como, 22100, Italy;45.8116386;9.0702401;56;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;Situated near the lake at the entrance to a narrow street dotted with various shops, this small contemporary-style restaurant boasts an equally tiny outdoor space for summer dining and is run with skill and professionalism by a young couple. The friendly, welcoming wife oversees the front of house, while her husband creates dishes full of character in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9959;Fè Ristorante;Italy;Noci;via Giulio Pastore 2, Noci, 70015, Italy;40.7882324;17.1289381;55;false;false;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;Situated near the centre, this restaurant occupies a small group of eight carefully restored trulli which provide an elegant and charming setting, with just 20 seats arranged throughout its small buildings. Traditional, regional cuisine reinterpreted with a skilful modern twist.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9960;Cucina Rambaldi;Italy;Villar Dora;via Sant'Ambrogio 55, Villar Dora, 10040, Italy;45.1117378;7.3836001;25;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Regional dishes with the occasional subtle contemporary twist are to the fore here. The chef’s culinary techniques bring out all the flavour of the carefully selected and preserved ingredients, with a focus on cooking temperatures and the cut of the meat, resulting in excellent cuisine. The menu also features a few specialities from Ferrara, the chef’s native city.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9961;Madama Piola;Italy;Turin;via Ormea 6 bis, Turin, 10125, Italy;45.0590594;7.6854084;17;true;false;Piedmontese;The aptly named Madama Piola (in Piedmontese dialect, “piola” is a village inn) has a simple yet attractive and friendly ambience that serves as a backdrop for typical Piedmontese dishes. Highlights include the memorable stuffed onion, as well as tonnato, braised cheeks and hot zabaglione. Regional wines take pride of place on the wine list, which includes a good selection by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
9962;Osteria Bakaré;Italy;Peschiera del Garda;Via Venezia 30, Peschiera del Garda, 37019, Italy;45.44113;10.70111;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This small but beautifully kept restaurant set back from the lakeside serves contemporary-style cuisine that includes a good balance of meat and fish recipes, all made from top-quality, seasonal ingredients. Dishes are creative and full of individual character, with the occasional nod to Asia. Attractive enclosed veranda.;Wheelchair access;[]
9963;Carlo e Camillo;Italy;Turin;via Carlo Alberto 35, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0651049;7.6838793;89;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This quiet and elegant bistro, the Grand Hotel Sitea’s second restaurant, offers a charming setting in which to enjoy skilfully prepared Piedmontese-influenced cuisine. The venue is also perfect for an aperitif, with excellent wines and cocktails.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9964;Remo Villa Cariolato;Italy;Vicenza;strada di Bertesina 313, Vicenza, 36100, Italy;45.5579033;11.5883955;30;false;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Long recommended by the Michelin Guide, the historic Remo moved a few years ago from its old premises to this beautiful villa typical of the Veneto region, once the home of an Italian hero, one of Garibaldi’s famous “Thousand”. Large and small dining rooms, perfect for special events, act as the backdrop for good regional and Italian cuisine, with a menu divided between meat and fish options. The latter comes almost exclusively from Chioggia market.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9965;PS Ristorante;Italy;Cerreto Guidi;via di Petriolo 7, Cerreto Guidi, 50050, Italy;43.74317;10.84993;31;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the beautiful countryside outside Cerreto Guidi, PS Ristorante is housed in the magnificent Medici Villa Petriolo which is also home to 36 luxurious guestrooms. The restaurant’s appeal is enhanced not only by the charm of the villa and its delightful garden (overlooked by the restaurant terrace), but also by the property’s delicious home-produced ingredients, such as extra-virgin olive oil, wine, Cinta Senese pork, meat and chicken, produce from the kitchen garden, traditional cereals and other zero-mile ingredients, all reinterpreted in a creative, modern style by the chef (as in the egg and artichoke dish). The estate’s wine is also highly recommended – we particularly enjoyed the organic red Golpaia, a medium-structured blend of Merlot and Sangiovese with characteristic soft aromas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9966;Diana's Place;Italy;Rome;via Volturno 54, Rome, 00185, Italy;41.9037245;12.5006592;81;false;false;Contemporary;Facing the square in front of Termini station, this wine bar-cum-restaurant is striking for its fresh and creative approach to cuisine. Nearly all the top-quality ingredients are local and can be purchased from the food counter. The excellent staff are happy to help with your choice of wine, which is also available by the glass.;Air conditioning;[]
9967;Enotavola Pino;Italy;Padua;via dell'Arco 37, Padua, 35122, Italy;45.405163;11.8755179;81;false;true;Seafood;The entrance to this restaurant through a wine-bar can be misleading, as you are eventually led to simpler – yet still attractive – dining rooms. In this wine-themed setting, enjoy delicious fish and seafood dishes with the occasional creative twist, accompanied by a particularly extensive selection of wines by the glass. A highly recommended address for fish lovers, situated right in the historic centre of Padova.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9968;Il Presidente;Italy;Lucera;via de Nicastri 10, Lucera, 71036, Italy;41.5077056;15.3356586;74;true;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant situated in an alleyway in the historic centre just a few metres from Lucera’s cathedral was once home to the stables of an old palazzo. Nowadays, the dining room, which is crowned by a stone-vaulted ceiling and decorated in shades of black and gold, is divided into small sections. In the middle room, two glass cabinets display the wine selection, which includes over 400 different labels. The Mediterranean cuisine served here is modern and colourful, with vegetables often accompanying the fish and seafood (red tuna, swordfish, prawns, scampi and a delicious seafood focaccia). The ingredients are more important than the technique, resulting in dishes that are full of flavour!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9969;Osteria della Tana;Italy;Asiago;località Kaberlaba 19, Asiago, 36012, Italy;45.8546287;11.4971365;98;true;true;Venetian, Traditional Cuisine;Occupying the same red house as chef Alessandro Dal Degan’s gourmet restaurant, the Osteria is where this chef turns his attention to more traditional dishes (meat and fish alike), which are often typical of the Veneto. There’s one highly recommended exception, however, namely the carbonara dell’Osteria, prepared with top-quality ingredients from the region. Also popular are the baccalà alla vicentina (dried cod) and the tripe, both of which feature on a menu with a wide selection, including renowned dishes from the chef’s Michelin-starred restaurant. Full-bodied flavours that will delight the palate.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9970;Trattoria da Me;Italy;Bologna;via San Felice 50/a, Bologna, 40122, Italy;44.4974146;11.3323073;94;false;false;Emilian, Contemporary;This lively and very busy trattoria run by the energetic Elisa owes its success to a winning combination of traditional dishes (the fresh hand-made pasta, also sold in the shop next door, is a particular highlight) and specialities reinterpreted with a touch of imagination by the female chef, such as the ossobuco cut lengthways. You may like to try both by choosing a typical Bolognese dish as a starter followed by one of the chef’s more original options for your main course.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9971;Seta Sushi Restaurant;Italy;Bologna;corte Isolani 2, Bologna, 40125, Italy;44.4930591;11.3486654;52;true;true;Japanese;It was friendship and passion for Japanese cuisine that prompted two young business partners to open this quiet, welcoming restaurant in the heart of Bologna. Situated in a courtyard with medieval origins, Seta Sushi Restaurant has a modern bistro-style dining room, as well as plenty of outdoor space for summer dining. The menu features an impressive selection of traditional Japanese dishes with the occasional personalised touch, all made from top-quality ingredients. Don’t worry if you’re new to Japanese cuisine – Maurilio is front of house to offer guests friendly, expert advice on both food and beverage. The latter includes a choice of sake for those wishing to immerse themselves fully in the Japanese dining experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9972;La Chandelle;Italy;Breuil Cervinia;via Piolet 1, Breuil Cervinia, 11021, Italy;45.9316973;7.6296967;24;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Decorated in the same classic, elegant style as the famous Hermitage hotel in which it is located, this spacious restaurant offers an impressive menu of modern yet unfussy dishes alongside a selection of more traditional options. Grilled meats are cooked over the imposing charcoal grill in the evenings, while the fine views of the surrounding mountains and an excellent wine list add to the enjoyment of your dining experience.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9973;Balìce;Italy;Milazzo;via Ettore Celi 15, Milazzo, 98057, Italy;38.2186394;15.2381358;21;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The chef patron Giacomo Caravello in the short span of a few years has created his “space” in the area, definitely becoming one of the best places in Milazzo: the contemporary interiors are truly refined and airy, while the cuisine–which grows year after year–is assured thanks to modern techniques and Sicilian and Mediterranean references. The wine selection is accompanied by an intriguing range of cocktails.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
9974;L'Ostì;Italy;Corvara in Badia;strada Sassongher 2, Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.5523767;11.8735655;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A minimalist-style restaurant featuring a wood decor, an extensive display of bottles, and some windows boasting partial yet splendid views of the Dolomites. The chef here prepares creative cuisine using local ingredients alongside produce sourced from other regions. The wine list includes a wide selection of natural wines.;Car park;[]
9975;La Locanda dei Beccaria;Italy;Montù Beccaria;via Marconi 10, Montù Beccaria, 27040, Italy;45.03443;9.312667;41;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Housed in the village’s historic wine cellar, this well - kept, rustic - style restaurant with typical wooden ceilings serves traditional, regional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9976;Palazzo Petrucci Pizzeria;Italy;Naples;piazza San Domenico Maggiore 5-7, Naples, 80134, Italy;40.8484519;14.2546489;15;true;false;Pizza;Situated right in the city centre, this pizzeria with the same name and owners as the gourmet restaurant has a contemporary, minimalist feel, plus an attractive outdoor space on the piazza. Among the excellent pizzas made from top-quality ingredients, you’ll find a few created by the young, skilful pizza chef, as well as one by chef Scarallo. Don’t miss the desserts!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9977;Cortile Arabo;Italy;Marzamemi;vicolo Villadorata, Marzamemi, 96018, Italy;36.7417654;15.1196579;40;true;false;Contemporary, Sicilian;In one of Sicily’s most iconic fortified villages which once prospered as a tuna fishery and is now a popular tourist attraction, Cortile Arabo serves carefully prepared and occasionally elaborate dishes of the highest quality, with a focus on fish (the menu also features a few meat dishes). The terrace on the rocks overlooking the sea, where the sound of the waves provides a soothing backdrop, is one of the highlights here.;Great view,Terrace;[]
9978;Acciuga;Italy;Rome;via Vodice 25, Rome, 00195, Italy;41.9181416;12.4614513;48;false;true;Seafood;This restaurant with a simple dining room and open-view kitchen serves some of the most interesting fish cuisine in the Della Vittoria district. Chef Federico Delmonte skilfully searches out “poor” varieties of fish which are nonetheless full of flavour on an open menu that is adjusted according to the catch of the day. The chef’s native Fano makes an appearance in a few recipes from the Marche, including the famous brodetto (a typical fish soup).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9979;Giannino dal 1899;Italy;Milan;via Vittor Pisani 6, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4809165;9.1996251;58;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, International;A renowned name in Milan, this restaurant is the setting for a Mediterranean cuisine  with an international twist. Although recently renovated, the dining room has an attractive old-fashioned feel with old photographs of celebrities who have eaten here since it opened more than 120 years ago.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
9980;Bottega Lucia;Italy;Milan;via Carlo Ravizza 4, Milan, 20149, Italy;45.4675598;9.1524732;20;true;true;Contemporary;Bottega Lucia serves a cuisine which is mainly Italian in style, with the addition of a few specialities from the Iberian Peninsula and other countries. Home-made pasta, meat and fish can be enjoyed in an attractive New York-style bistro, while the American bar serves drinks and a selection of delicious, tempting snacks in the evening.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9981;Concezione Restaurant;Italy;Catania;via Giuseppe Verdi 143, Catania, 95129, Italy;37.5108999;15.0926827;65;true;false;Creative, Sicilian;This minimalist-style restaurant is home to one of the most interesting young chefs in Catania. In this historic building with beautiful ceilings, enjoy top-quality Sicilian cuisine created by Manuel Tropea, who focuses in particular on specialities from Catania which he interprets in a highly personalised way with a real focus on tradition. Dishes such as “L’Asina e la lattuga” and “Good morning in Catania” are good examples. The chef’s surprise menu takes guests on a culinary journey full of contrasts which is inspired by his own memories and experiences.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9982;Meraviglioso Osteria Moderna;Italy;Polignano a Mare;largo Gelso 16, Polignano a Mare, 70044, Italy;40.9971639;17.2168149;44;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;This attractive, welcoming modern restaurant stands in Polignano’s main street, scene of the town’s evening “passeggiata”, not far from the statue of the great Domenico Modugno, a native of this beautiful town. Although the lunch menu is simple in style, it is still inspired by fresh fish and seafood, while in the evening the young yet experienced chef creates more imaginative and inventive fare. There’s a convenient private car park nearby: if you want to take advantage of this, make sure you advise the restaurant of your arrival time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9983;Gennaro Amitrano;Italy;Capri;via Marina Piccola 120, Capri, 80073, Italy;40.5456676;14.235691;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The large picture windows at this restaurant offer fine views of the Tyrrhenian sea, while the menu features imaginative recipes with a focus on fish and seafood. The most popular dishes include “Mamma Maria’s parmigiana”, the fish and shellfish soup, and the lemon dessert.;Great view;[]
9984;Locanda Perbellini al Mare;Italy;Montallegro;Bovo Marina, Montallegro, 92010, Italy;37.3804508;13.3079456;20;false;true;Sicilian, Contemporary;Enjoy imaginative Sicilian dishes created by multi-starred Michelin chef Perbellini in this beach restaurant that was once a family-run trattoria. The delightful natural setting acts as the perfect backdrop for Giancarlo’s original and exciting cuisine.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
9985;Il Giardinetto;Italy;Mandello del Lario;piazza Garibaldi 10, Mandello del Lario, 23826, Italy;45.91301;9.31639;87;true;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Looking out over the calm blue water, this classic restaurant serves traditional cuisine with the occasional imaginative twist. Fish from the lake feature on the menu, as do meat and seafood options with something for everyone. There’s also a small outdoor terrace where guests can enjoy a pre- or post-dinner drink.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9986;Locale;Italy;Florence;via delle Seggiole 12r, Florence, 50122, Italy;43.7713968;11.2600385;65;false;true;Contemporary, Creative;Situated within a palazzo full of history, from the medieval basement to the Renaissance-style architecture of the restaurant itself, Locale is also home to an old courtyard with a lounge bar and large cocktail counter, as well as some beautiful rooms to the rear of the building. Enjoy creative, innovative cuisine with personalised touches influenced by the chef’s professional experience around the world (Australia, Japan, France). Our inspector particularly enjoyed the Risoni pasta with cuttlefish liver and cherry tomatoes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
9987;Fàula;Italy;Cerretto Langhe;Località Talloria 1, Cerretto Langhe, 12050, Italy;44.589415;8.0407424;35;true;true;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Fàula is the restaurant at the Casa Langa hotel, a large property which opens out like an amphitheatre to offer panoramic views of the valley. Here, the young chef skilfully creates cuisine which blends the culinary traditions of the Piedmont with more modern dishes. A good selection of wines from the region, plus a biodynamic kitchen garden add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9988;Asina Luna;Italy;Peschiera Borromeo;via della Resistenza 23, Peschiera Borromeo, 20068, Italy;45.4391114;9.2948791;75;false;true;Meats and Grills, Contemporary;A restaurant with an attractive atmosphere, thanks to its profusion of wood, soft lighting and contemporary colour scheme. Meat aged for different periods takes pride of place on the menu. Sourced from different countries, it includes sweet Piedmontese Vicciola beef fed on hazelnuts and tender and delicately marbled Australian Scottona beef. Good selection of strongly flavoured and aged meat options.;Air conditioning;[]
9989;Il Barolino;Italy;Carpi;via Giovanni XXIII 110, Carpi, 41012, Italy;44.7936775;10.8758994;92;true;false;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;The friendliness and Emilian genuineness of the Barolo brothers and of the whole team cheers a break here where you can enjoy the authentic regional cuisine. Parmesan cream tortellini are a must: large portions and top quality of these little pasta bundles still strictly made by hand! The room is simple and suitable above all for informal meetings among friends and colleagues.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
9990;Il Rivale al Lago;Italy;Padenghe sul Garda;via Marconi 93, Padenghe sul Garda, 25080, Italy;45.4931277;10.5124048;78;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;Situated just a stone’s throw from the lake, this multi-faceted restaurant serves classic Italian dishes, often with a creative twist, alongside top-quality international ingredients such as Cantabrian anchovies and Japanese Wagyu beef. Grilled meats and vegetable dishes also make an appearance on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9991;Lillotatini;Italy;Panicale;piazza Umberto I 13-14, Panicale, 06064, Italy;43.0291675;12.0992757;79;true;false;Umbrian, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the heart of a small medieval castle-hamlet, this traditional-style restaurant with an attractive terrace on the historic square provides the setting for local specialities such as freshwater fish and truffles in season. There’s also a wine boutique on the same piazza (reached as soon as you come into the historic centre), which sells typical local produce and a good selection of wine. The latter also features on the restaurant’s wine list, with the family on hand to offer recommendations.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9992;Boccon DiVino;Italy;Montalcino;via Traversa dei Monti 201, località Colombaio Tozzi, Montalcino, 53024, Italy;43.05227;11.49878;70;true;true;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;In a farmhouse on the edges of town, this restaurant has a rustic dining area with modern tables and chairs and a beautiful summer terrace with a view. Authentic local dishes.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9993;Il Giardino "Da Felicin";Italy;Monforte d'Alba;via Vallada 18, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.5825745;7.9673803;29;false;true;Piedmontese, Classic Cuisine;A bastion of classic Piedmontese cuisine, this restaurant housed in a beautiful period palazzo boasts a panoramic terrace and a romantic garden for alfresco dining. The dining rooms echo the palazzo’s sumptuous and traditional feel, as does the timeless, regional cuisine which is carefully prepared and full of delicious flavours. The building is also home to an “albergo diffuso” hotel, with some guestrooms in the building itself and others dotted around the village, including in Palazzo Boeri which also has a small spa (reservation required). The owners are happy to share their knowledge of the Langhe, either on their own guided tours or visits led by another local expert.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9994;Antica Locanda dell'Orco;Italy;Rivarolo Canavese;via Ivrea 109, Rivarolo Canavese, 10086, Italy;45.3335077;7.7267256;85;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Fans of Piedmontese cuisine will find one of its best exponents in this restaurant located at the end of a beautiful porticoed street in the historic centre. Savour some of Italy’s most exciting regional cooking, such as snails, bagna caoda, agnolotti pasta, a few (mainly freshwater) fish dishes, braised and boiled meats, “finanziera” stew and some extraordinary desserts – all prepared in magnificent style.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
9995;Le Vele;Italy;Misano Adriatico;via Litoranea Sud 71, Bagni 70, Misano Adriatico, 47843, Italy;43.97567;12.70971;87;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This modern, minimalist - style restaurant is practically on the beach and almost within touching distance of the sea. It specialises in fish dishes with a contemporary flavour.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
9996;Risorgimento;Italy;Sirmione;piazza Carducci 5/6, Sirmione, 25019, Italy;45.492478;10.607502;51;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant situated in the centre of Sirmione just a stone’s throw from the lake is striking for its elegant outdoor terrace. This refined setting provides the backdrop for creative meat and fish dishes full of individual character. A fine display of wines adorns the shelves in the lounge-cum-wine bar on the first floor.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
9997;Giardinetto;Italy;Pettenasco;via Provinciale 1, Pettenasco, 28028, Italy;45.8218724;8.4023087;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the lakeshore in the elegant Hotel Giardinetto (now approaching its centenary), this restaurant boasts stunning views of the lake and San Giulio island. The focus here is on Mediterranean cuisine with the occasional imaginative twist, while the hotel’s Roof Top Bar is the perfect place for an aperitif or after-dinner drink.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
9998;Kro;Italy;Ponte di Legno;via Tollarini 70/c, località Pontagna di Temù, Ponte di Legno, 25050, Italy;46.25104;10.480131;49;false;true;Alpine, Regional Cuisine;The courteous service, stylish mountain decor of wood and stone, and regional cuisine with a modern twist are just some of the attractions of this restaurant, whose name loosely translates as “inn”. A real treat for the eyes and the tastebuds!;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
9999;Trattoria di Campagna;Italy;Sarre;Località Saint Maurice 57, Sarre, 11010, Italy;45.7174664;7.2612561;16;false;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Modern Cuisine;This famous trattoria, now run by the third generation of the same family, serves traditional, seasonal cuisine from the Aosta valley, enhanced by the occasional imaginative and personalised touch. The new well-stocked wine cellar includes a table for a dozen guests, while sommelier Beatrice is on hand to assist guests with their choice of bottle. Excellent array of delicacies from the dessert trolley.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10000;Makorè;Italy;Ferrara;via Palestro 10/18, Ferrara, 44121, Italy;44.8370614;11.6227331;41;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Seafood;Makorè’s new gourmet venture offers guests a delightful dining experience where the focus is on vegetables, as well as fish from the adjacent fishmongers. The chef demonstrates his culinary skills and techniques on three surprise tasting menus (of different lengths) and an à la carte, featuring dishes such as the familiar yet far from ordinary grilled squid (with a fragrant tuna and stracciatella stuffing) and a selection of boiled fish including cod tongue, ventresca tuna, tuna and cuttlefish sausage, gurnard, giardiniera vegetables and potatoes. We asked the excellent sommelier for recommendations and enjoyed a deep-gold Abate wine made from red Fortana grapes in line with local tradition. An elegant restaurant that has really made its mark in Ferrara.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10001;Lo Stornello;Italy;Stresa;via Cavour 35, Stresa, 28838, Italy;45.8842105;8.5389585;96;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Offering quality and professionalism in a tourist setting, this small restaurant is popular with locals as well as visitors. The menu focuses on imaginatively presented Mediterranean cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10002;Il Chiosco di Bacco;Italy;Torriana;via Santarcangiolese 62, Torriana, 47825, Italy;43.9860678;12.40206;93;false;true;Cuisine from Romagna, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a rural location in the Montefeltro region, to which half the menu is dedicated (fresh home-made pastas, salumi, porchetta-style rabbit etc). The other half focuses on meat dishes, with an interesting selection of steaks and ribs from Italian and Scottish breeds (including more expensive beef that has been left to age for a month). You’ll find the perfect wine pairing on the excellent wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10003;Antica Moka;Italy;Modena;Via Emilia Est 1496, Modena, 41126, Italy;44.6225361;10.9828687;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated on the Via Emilia, this elegant, owner-run restaurant has for decades been renowned for its top-quality regional cuisine with an updated twist, as well as its reinterpreted fish specialities. Our inspector very much enjoyed the cuisine here, with a particular mention for the home-made pastas and excellent wine selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10004;Almatò;Italy;Rome;via Augusto Riboty 20/c, Rome, 00195, Italy;41.9154553;12.4546959;49;false;false;Contemporary;Situated in the elegant, residential streets of the Prati district, this modern, minimalist-style restaurant is the setting for top-quality creative cuisine. For the most part, the menu eschews traditional Lazio dishes making this a good choice for anyone looking for something a little different.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10005;Razzo;Italy;Turin;via Andrea Doria 17/f, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0639963;7.6850158;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;A quiet restaurant with a relaxed, young and modern feel serving contemporary cuisine prepared from seasonal, regional products. Charming romantic outdoor area with soft lighting.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10006;3.0 Ciro Cascella;Italy;Naples;via San Pasquale 68, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8359663;14.2363274;91;true;false;Pizza;Fans of Neapolitan pizza will be in their element at this restaurant, where the pizzas are light, with a larger and softer crust, thanks to the long fermentation and leavening process – some people come here simply to eat the crust, it’s so good. There’s also a wide choice of excellent toppings, including top-quality ingredients from Campania. Gluten-free options and dough made from different flours are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
10007;Baracca - Storica Hostaria;Italy;Trebaseleghe;via Ronchi 1, Trebaseleghe, 35010, Italy;45.59254;12.04119;54;true;false;Italian, Venetian;A classic, attractively elegant restaurant which boasts an extensive choice of dishes on its menu. The varied options here range from meat to fish dishes, often prepared in regional recipes such as tagliatelle with duck ragù and toasted hazelnuts, chicken liver risotto, Vicenza-style baccalà and meat casserole.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10008;Nascostoposto;Italy;Terni;via Sant'Alò, Terni, 05100, Italy;42.5621827;12.6445805;16;true;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Easily found despite its name (nascosto posto means “hidden place”), this restaurant lies in the alleyways of Terni’s old town. In its modern, minimalist-style dining room, an enthusiastic couple (she runs the front of house, while he’s in the kitchen) delight their guests with delicious and imaginative cuisine with regional, Italian and unexpectedly exotic influences.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10009;Duanima;Italy;Cagliari;via Sebastiano Satta 28, Cagliari, 09128, Italy;39.2166046;9.1217347;29;false;true;Contemporary;This is one of Cagliari’s most interesting restaurants – a real must if you find yourself visiting Sardinia’s capital city. In its long, narrow dining room with modern furnishings, enjoy simple, unfussy cuisine that is full of intense flavours. Most of the dishes are influenced by the chef’s experience working abroad, while also demonstrating his re-connection with his native island, with a focus on Sardinia’s top-quality ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
10010;Adelaide;Italy;Rome;via dell'Arancio 69, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9044658;12.4764949;60;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Although it’s not obvious from the exterior, once you’ve crossed the threshold of the Vilòn hotel you step into a succession of highly decorated rooms that are full of charm. The cuisine is of the highest quality, showcasing dishes from chef Gabriele Muro’s native Campania alongside the famous pasta specialities of his adopted city (amatriciana, carbonara, cacio e pepe etc), and finishing with the superb “l’oro di Procida” dessert.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10011;Al Persef;Italy;Livigno;via Saroch 1272, Livigno, 23041, Italy;46.5201886;10.124835;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A small yet very comfortable dining room with large windows and just a few tables provides the setting for modern, creative cuisine prepared by a young and ambitious chef. Locally sourced ingredients are prioritised here, plus there’s an excellent wine list.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10012;CENERE - Museum & Bistrot;Italy;Pompei;via Plinio 39, Pompei, 80045, Italy;40.7486425;14.4936834;30;true;false;Campanian;Fans of Campanian cuisine will be in their element at this restaurant situated opposite the archaeological site. Here, the chef serves traditional regional favourites alongside more creative recipes, often prepared using local specialities such as purple artichoke from Schito, chickpeas from Teano, Provola cheese from Agerola, red sausage from Castelpoto and Black Casertona pork. Of the two dining rooms, the one in the cellar is particularly charming.;Air conditioning;[]
10013;Livello 1;Italy;Rome;via Duccio di Buoninsegna 25, Rome, 00142, Italy;41.8298125;12.4892791;82;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the suburbs off the main tourist trail, this fish restaurant also has a fishmonger’s next door. The fish and seafood cuisine served here is highly interesting, featuring modern recipes made from top-quality ingredients. There’s also a small lounge in which to enjoy a cocktail, plus a selection of good wines. The open-view kitchen allows guests to observe the skilful chef at work.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10014;W Villadorata Country Restaurant;Italy;Noto;contrada Portelle, Noto, 96017, Italy;36.8674713;15.0383198;96;true;false;Country cooking, Creative;Part of the Country House Villadorata resort in the hills outside Noto, this restaurant boasts a delightful setting with the sea as a backdrop, surrounded by gardens which provide many of the vegetables used in the cuisine. Viviana Varese, a Michelin-starred chef from Milan, is in partnership here with Matteo Carnaghi, who is at the helm in the kitchen, with excellent results. The cooking is rooted in Sicilian ingredients, with one weekday evening in summer dedicated entirely to barbecue-grilled dishes.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10015;Josto;Italy;Cagliari;via Sassari 25, Cagliari, 09124, Italy;39.2165191;9.1103353;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;One of Cagliari’s most interesting restaurants, Josta boasts two small dining rooms with an original decor that combines modern design with a few traditional features – the room by the entrance has the open-view kitchen to the rear. The menu focuses on Sardinian specialities reinterpreted with a contemporary twist, such as the delicious ham (from a typical Sardinian breed of pig), fregula pasta, mullet, and traditional Saba dessert.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10016;Bramea;Italy;Palazzo San Gervasio;viale Villa d'Errico 10, Palazzo San Gervasio, 85026, Italy;40.9379252;15.9740352;82;false;true;Creative;This gourmet restaurant with just a few tables is run by two young friends, now business partners at Bramea, with one at the helm in the kitchen, the other front of house. Extensive tasting menus are the focus here, featuring creative and original dishes often made from local ingredients. The end result is fascinating and of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10017;Toe Drûe;Italy;Sestri Ponente;via Corsi 44 r, Sestri Ponente, 16154, Italy;44.4258298;8.8407606;31;false;false;Ligurian, Modern Cuisine;Soak up the ambience of historic Genova in this restaurant which serves specialities such as panissa rice, seafood salad and Ligurian fish dishes in its informal and comfortable dining room. The building dates back to the early 19C: fans of naval history may be interested to know that the REX transatlantic liner was built right opposite. There’s also a small lounge space where you can savour a glass of wine and a selection of cheeses.;Air conditioning;[]
10018;Dimora Ulmo;Italy;Matera;via Pennino 28, Matera, 75100, Italy;40.6651164;16.6102076;76;false;false;Cuisine from Basilicata, Modern Cuisine;The three tasting menus (Contaminazioni, Dimora Ulmo and A mano libera) served at this restaurant housed in an old restored palazzo with a splendid summer terrace overlooking the Sassi feature a balance of modern cuisine and traditional local dishes. The dining room is equally attractive, while the interesting wine list includes labels from the region alongside a selection of wines from elsewhere in Italy and further afield.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10019;Fattoria delle Torri;Italy;Modica;vico Napolitano 14, Modica, 97015, Italy;36.856315;14.7596559;63;false;false;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;A small slice of paradise in the historic centre of Modica, where the daughters of owner-chef Peppe Barone continue the family culinary tradition while adding their youthful influence to the innovative and yet traditional cuisine served here. In fine weather, dine among lemon trees on the attractive outdoor terrace.;Terrace;[]
10020;Momento al 25;Italy;Carpi;via San Francesco 20, Carpi, 41012, Italy;44.7797015;10.8818081;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a late-19C palazzo, this restaurant serves a good selection of meat and fish dishes with both traditional and creative cuisine on the menu. Delicious flavours typical of the Emilia region.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10021;Buca di Bacco;Italy;Pietra Ligure;corso Italia 149, Pietra Ligure, 17027, Italy;44.1518199;8.2897517;90;true;false;Seafood;The seafood specialities, the care in the choice of rare produce and the originality of the Proprietor characterise this establishment, situated as it is in the basement of a building.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10022;Da Miky;Italy;Monterosso al Mare;via Fegina 104, Monterosso al Mare, 19016, Italy;44.1452613;9.6465188;49;false;false;Seafood;Situated right on the seafront, Miky is one of the best restaurants for fish (including the famous Monterosso anchovies) in the region, serving cuisine which is more and more exciting and individual every year. There’s also a small shop selling local produce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10023;Osteria Il Maialetto;Italy;Monsummano Terme;via Della Repubblica 348, Monsummano Terme, 51015, Italy;43.8638368;10.8170887;87;true;true;Tuscan, Meats and Grills;This lively restaurant with a young, vibrant atmosphere stands next to the butcher’s shop run by the same family. The menu features delicious Tuscan cuisine, including dishes such as pappa al pomodoro and Florentine steak, which you choose from the display counter. Good wines and friendly service add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10024;Posillipo;Italy;Gabicce Monte;via dell'Orizzonte 1, Gabicce Monte, 61011, Italy;43.9639309;12.7722742;76;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Boasting a superb location above Gabicce Monte, this excellent restaurant run by the third generation of the same family offers breathtaking views of the Romagna coast. Posillipo’s superb fish dishes have made the restaurant a must in the region, with options ranging from raw fish to traditional pasta specialities and delicious main courses (fish fillets, catch of the day, fried options etc). There’s also a tempting dessert trolley and an excellent wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10025;La Pineta;Italy;Genoa;via Gualco 82, località Struppa, Genoa, 16165, Italy;44.4447179;8.9990585;49;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Meats and Grills;Now a gastronomic institution in the city, in a secluded setting immersed in nature, La Pineta occupies the ground floor of a nondescript building in which the simple, “dated” yet comfortable decor provides the backdrop. Although there is a menu (but no wine list), the dishes are usually announced in person at your table by the owners. Simple, traditional and abundant cuisine which is mainly cooked on the open grill in the centre of the room, including meat (its signature speciality) and fish.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10026;Stefano Paganini alla Corte degli Alfieri;Italy;Magliano Alfieri;piazza Raimondo 2, Magliano Alfieri, 12050, Italy;44.7667927;8.0684173;49;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Occupying a superb 17C castle, this restaurant has two dining rooms: one is decorated with works by local artists which change throughout the year, while the other, more romantic in feel, is adorned with roses and boasts splendid frescoed ceilings. There’s no choice here, just a tasting menu (although guests can select just a few courses if they wish), but the cuisine is of excellent quality and offers good value for money.;;[]
10028;Porcino;Italy;Badia;strada Damez 2/a, Badia, 39036, Italy;46.6075518;11.8938127;43;false;false;Alpine, Mediterranean Cuisine;After gaining experience in top-quality restaurants, chef Marco Verginer has embarked on a new adventure running his own brand-new restaurant in the equally new Badia Hill hotel. In an elegant and spacious setting, enjoy modern, occasionally creative cuisine which skilfully blends Alpine flavours and ingredients with delicious Mediterranean influences.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10029;Essenza Bistrot;Italy;Olbia;via delle Terme 8/A, Olbia, 07026, Italy;40.9248365;9.5027825;72;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A welcoming and original bistro-restaurant in the historic centre, where the stone walls are typical of the region’s architecture and an attractive outdoor area offers a few tables just in front of the entrance. The experienced owner-chef is at the helm in the kitchen, preparing beautifully presented, contemporary-style dishes which are full of flavour. The menu also features a selection of raw fish and seafood options.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10030;La Gallina;Italy;Gavi;frazione Monterotondo 56, Gavi, 15066, Italy;44.7132;8.8251;99;true;false;Piedmontese, Contemporary;This attractive restaurant offers three tasting menus featuring traditional and more creative dishes, in which influences from Piedmont, Liguria and Campania (the chef’s native region) combine, with truffles taking centre stage in autumn and home-grown vegetables in spring. Culinary highlights include Piedmontese-style Fassona beef tartare (the beef is sourced from the La Granda consortium) and cream ice-cream whipped in a 1982 Carpigiani machine served with a selection of sweet delicacies. The decision to offer wine uniquely from Champagne and Piedmont is somewhat unusual but works well – we recommend the house Barbera del Monferrato, preferably one that has been laid down for a few years.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10031;Acqua;Italy;Vieste;lungomare Amerigo Vespucci 50, Vieste, 71019, Italy;41.8854572;16.1780243;53;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated slightly above the marina, this elegant restaurant has a young chef at the helm who has cemented his reputation via contemporary, occasionally creative dishes which showcase the best local ingredients, including fish and seafood. The fact that the latter come directly from the family’s own fishmongers adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10032;Gagini Restaurant;Italy;Palermo;via dei Cassari 35, Palermo, 90133, Italy;38.1184687;13.3661866;39;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;Situated in the lively heart of Palermo between the Vucciria and the small Cala port, this restaurant boasts a modern design and bold colours which are all the more striking for the charming old building which it occupies – the 16C studio of sculptor Antonello Gagini (hence the restaurant name!). The cuisine focuses on showcasing the quality of local ingredients, including wild rabbit from Pantelleria and donkey meat from the Nebrodi region, in dishes that are contemporary in style and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10033;Menabò Vino e Cucina;Italy;Rome;via delle Palme 44 d/e, Rome, 00171, Italy;41.8890879;12.5639458;29;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Two brothers have brought fresh life to this exciting bistro in the heart of the Prenestino-Centocelle district, where the delicious cuisine is prepared by Paolo and the wine selection overseen by Daniele. The menu features a good balance of meat, fish and vegetarian dishes with a focus on seasonal ingredients and the best market produce. Very popular, so booking is recommended!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10034;Il Poggio;Italy;Poggiridenti;via Panoramica 4, Poggiridenti, 23020, Italy;46.1749169;9.9189094;90;false;true;Country cooking, Italian Contemporary;This simple yet welcoming family-run restaurant is situated on the wine route that wends its way through the hills behind Sondrio, less than 5km away. The dining room boasts a cheerful open fireplace (also used as a grill), while an attractive outdoor terrace offers fine views of the valley. In the kitchen, the family’s second generation combine traditional recipes and ingredients with the occasional modern twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10035;Tenne Lodges;Italy;Colle;strada Racines di Dentro 51, Colle, 39040, Italy;46.8648828;11.3068524;32;true;false;Alpine, Contemporary;Situated near the ski slopes in the Gourmethotel Tenne Lodges, this restaurant is decorated with a profusion of wood. The large dining room is the backdrop for delicious modern cuisine which is regional in focus yet also influenced by the chef’s professional experience around the world. Excellent wine list offering plenty of choice, plus a stone wine cellar which makes a charming setting for a pre-dinner drink.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10036;Osteria Il Cappello;Italy;Trento;piazzetta Bruno Lunelli 5, Trento, 38122, Italy;46.06961;11.12538;53;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;The outdoor terrace at this restaurant overlooks a pleasant pedestrian piazza in the historic centre, while the welcoming dining rooms are decorated in a style typical of the Trentino. The cuisine – reliable, seasonal and full of flavour – is traditionally Italian, yet with a contemporary touch. The menu also features a few regional options as well as the occasional fish dish. The quail stuffed with acacia honey, pumpkin purée and stewed radicchio is superb.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10037;Bentōteca;Italy;Milan;via San Calocero 3, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4582847;9.176373;50;true;true;Fusion, Asian Contemporary;Top-quality Japanese cuisine with heavy Mediterranean influences takes pride of place at this restaurant, where talented chef Toku Yoji Tokuyoshi creates dishes such as horsemeat tataki with a pizzaiola sauce, and barbecued fish neck with friggitello pepper. If you opt for a seat on the large bench facing the kitchen, you’ll be able to watch the chefs at work and admire the precision required to prepare different types of sushi. Modern, understated decor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
10038;Signore te ne ringrazi;Italy;Macerata;via Pescheria Vecchia 26, Macerata, 62100, Italy;43.3005511;13.454439;29;true;false;Cuisine from the Marches, Creative;At this restaurant in the charming historic centre of Macerata, chef Michele Biagiola serves dishes inspired by rural culinary traditions, with herbs gathered in the fields nearby featuring in some of his recipes. Elaborate, gourmet cuisine is served at lunchtime, while the evening menu focuses on simpler, less expensive fare.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10039;Burjè 1968;Italy;Corvara in Badia;str. Burje 11, Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.5478163;11.8724653;55;false;false;Contemporary;Ambitious Italian cuisine including some dishes inspired by French traditions, all creatively prepared with the occasional use of more exotic ingredients. If you’re having problems choosing from the à la carte, why not opt for the 5- or 7- course tasting menu?;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10040;La Ciambella;Italy;Rome;via dell'Arco della Ciambella 20, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8968476;12.4769553;15;true;false;Roman, Italian;Originally from Testaccio, the district of Rome that is historically associated with butcher’s shops, chef Francesca Ciucci serves some of the best meat dishes in the Italian capital, including offal such as sweetbreads, a delicious Roman-style tripe dish and her own reinterpretation of “coda in carrozza” (an oxtail recipe). Meat dishes, often with a creative twist, take centre stage here, offering a delightful gastronomic experience that is not to be missed!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10041;Incàlmo;Italy;Este;viale Rimembranze 1, Este, 35042, Italy;45.2305496;11.6594581;28;false;false;Contemporary;“Clean”, almost naive dishes full of clear and defined flavours take centre-stage at Incàlmo, where the cuisine is distinctly unfussy with no unnecessary frills. As a result, ingredients are clearly recognisable (as is the way they are prepared), allowing guests to focus on their contrasting textures and flavours. In the chef’s view, “if one element does stand out, it’s probably the bitter flavours that we enjoy playing with,” says the chef, “while at the same time balancing this with other elements. We also prioritise the use of vegetables.”;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10042;Bino;Italy;Savona;via Ambrogio Aonzo 31r, Savona, 17100, Italy;44.3081678;8.4824464;84;false;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;Situated in the historic centre near the ceramic museum (some of its pieces are also on display in the restaurant), Bino Ricchebuono boasts an attractive outdoor space in a charming small square. Michelin-starred chef Ricchebuono from Noli is the brains behind this restaurant, which serves fish and meat dishes prepared with a touch of creativity.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10043;Cortile Pepe;Italy;Cefalu;via Nicola Botta 15, Cefalu, 90015, Italy;38.0387336;14.0215432;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;Situated among the narrow streets of the historic centre just a stone’s throw from both the cathedral and the sea, this restaurant boasts a dining room with an old, vaulted ceiling and an attractive outdoor space. Here, the chef (who has plenty of experience working in Michelin-starred restaurants) serves regional cuisine reinterpreted with elegant and modern touches that result in precise, colourful and beautifully presented dishes. Attentive, friendly and welcoming service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10044;Casu Osteria Contemporanea;Italy;Giarre;corso Italia 294, Giarre, 95014, Italy;37.7292736;15.1934203;64;true;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;Situated on Giarre’s main street, this small, simple restaurant has just a few tables and an informal atmosphere. The menu offers a small selection of reasonably priced dishes with a focus on Sicilian cuisine made from top-quality ingredients that guarantee delicious flavours.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10045;Bianca sul Lago;Italy;Oggiono;via Dante Alighieri 18, Oggiono, 23848, Italy;45.8000413;9.355424;82;true;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in a smart hotel, this modern and minimalist-style restaurant boasts large picture windows which allow guests to enjoy some of the most beautiful sunsets in the region, either from the dining room or perhaps while sipping an aperitif in the lounge bar. The new chef serves contemporary Mediterranean cuisine with the occasional international influence, in which his creative flair is enhanced by expertly applied modern techniques. Good wine selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10046;Mirabelle;Italy;Rome;via di Porta Pinciana 14, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9078782;12.4867135;72;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Without a shadow of a doubt, the view of Rome from this restaurant situated on the penultimate floor of the Splendide Royalhotel has few equals: from Villa Medici to Trinità dei Monti, and St Peter’s to the Gianicolo, the only way to enjoy a better view is to head up a floor to the hotel’s new Adèle lounge bar for an aperitif or after-dinner drink. Excellent service (especially in the evening) and modern yet traditionally influenced cuisine make this one of Rome’s best fine-dining restaurants.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10047;Il Portolano;Italy;Porto San Paolo;via Molara 11, Porto San Paolo, 07020, Italy;40.8799943;9.6356984;46;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;This simple restaurant right on the seafront facing the island of Tavolara is run by a highly experienced couple working alongside an excellent chef who creates modern cuisine from the best fish in the region, as well as offering a few local meat dishes. Reservations are highly recommended in summer when the large outdoor panoramic terrace is always teeming with customers.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10048;Il Bikini;Italy;Vico Equense;SS 145 Sorrentina km 13,900, Vico Equense, 80069, Italy;40.678535;14.437112;46;true;true;Seafood;This Mediterranean - style restaurant surrounded by a small outdoor terrace stands slightly above the beach club of the same name. Its elevated position gives it stunning views, which guests can enjoy as they savour the top - quality meat and fish dishes on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10049;Abraxas Osteria;Italy;Pozzuoli;via Scalandrone 15, località Lucrino, Pozzuoli, 80078, Italy;40.832253;14.070577;49;true;false;Campanian;Situated inland at a slightly higher altitude than the coast, this restaurant on two floors focuses all its attention on its regional cuisine and its wine list. Very good value for money, although you will spend a bit more (and it’s worth it! ) if you choose one of the grilled meat options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10050;Henri Restaurant;Italy;Viareggio;viale Ugo Foscolo 10, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.8683192;10.2447506;25;true;true;Italian Contemporary;The name of this restaurant refers to its owner Henri Prosperi, who returned to his beloved Viareggio in 2021. This accomplished maître d' from another era will introduce you, with both charm and professionalism, to his daughter Serena’s dishes, which are finely balanced between classic and modern flavours, with the occasional French influence. The chef’s menu features meat and fish dishes, with a firm focus on luxury ingredients. The same is true of the wine list, which includes renowned labels such as Petrus and Sassicaia, as well as some of the best French and Italian sparkling wines. Welcome back, Henri!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10051;Deste;Italy;Porto Rotondo;piazza Rudalza 6, Porto Rotondo, 07026, Italy;41.0285499;9.5422852;80;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Set back slightly from the port, this restaurant boasts stunning views from its terrace which is highly recommended in fine weather. The culinary focus here is on modern dishes with an interesting choice of meat and fish options. Tea and kombucha offer an alternative to wine, while the home-produced gin is definitely worth sampling.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10052;De' Minimi;Italy;Tropea;contrada Paola 6, Tropea, 89861, Italy;38.6765326;15.9059125;61;false;false;Calabrian, Contemporary;Situated within the beautiful Villa Paola hotel just outside Tropea, this gourmet restaurant is named after the Frati Minimi (Order of Minims) who once occupied this old monastery. The cuisine here is modern and occasionally creative, especially the à la carte dishes (meat and fish), all of which are prepared from the best Calabrian ingredients including many vegetables and citrus fruit grown on the property. The small wine list also has a regional focus and is complemented by a choice of cocktails served at the bar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
10053;De Gustibus;Italy;Chieri;via Martiri della Libertà 9, Chieri, 10023, Italy;45.0073562;7.8222492;38;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Enjoy modern, Mediterranean-influenced cuisine in an elegant restaurant with an attractive vintage-style ambience, where the excellent menu is announced at your table and varies according to daily availability. Very friendly and attentive service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10054;Il Rivale in Città;Italy;Brescia;via Antonio Gramsci 10, Brescia, 25122, Italy;45.5364088;10.2187291;95;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Situated in a beautiful 18C palazzo right in the centre of Brescia, this elegant restaurant consists of several small dining rooms of different colours, fabrics and furnishings yet all with the same historic atmosphere – the room with just one table is truly intimate! The cuisine features substantial recipes with a contemporary Italian flavour including top-quality options such as potato puff pastry, scampi, caviar and hazelnut cream, while one of the highlights of the new formula is the wooden dessert trolley on which a selection of tempting home-made delicacies is presented. The wine list (easily consulted on a tablet) is also impressive, with a particular focus on labels from nearby Franciacorta.;;[]
10055;Kohaku;Italy;Rome;via Marche 66, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9088815;12.4902485;23;true;true;Japanese Contemporary, Japanese;As if by magic, once you step over the threshold at this restaurant you feel as though you are in Japan, thanks to the soft music, elegant ambience and stylish decor. Japanese Kaiseki dishes take pride of place here, all made from seasonal ingredients with a real respect for integrity. We particularly enjoyed the duck with miso cooked at low heat for eight hours. An interesting sake selection and a lighter menu at lunchtime add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
10056;Salsedine367;Italy;Lido di Savio;via Marradi 11, Lido di Savio, 48125, Italy;44.30601;12.34584;25;false;true;Seafood, Contemporary;Meals are served outdoors at this beach restaurant, which is also a private beach club. Here, the cuisine focuses on imaginative and personalised dishes that stand out for their excellent ingredients, among other things! The “blind” tasting menu is based around the chef’s inspiration, while the varied à la carte offers dishes with generous portions.;Terrace;[]
10057;Flurin;Italy;Glorenza;Laubengasse 2, Glorenza, 39020, Italy;46.6706565;10.5533644;55;false;true;Farm to table, Contemporary;Flurin occupies an old medieval tower in Glorenza, a small hamlet in the Val Venosta which is surrounded by walls that also date back to the Middle Ages. Furnished in a modern style that contrasts with its old vaulted ceiling, the restaurant serves contemporary cuisine that the enthusiastic owner-chef prepares from carefully selected seasonal ingredients from the region. His creative and imaginative recipes include dishes such as Alpine char ceviche with grapefruit, cucumber and sesame seeds. A bar and guest suites complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10058;Al Malò - Cucina e Miscelazione;Italy;Rovato;piazza Cavour 28, Rovato, 25038, Italy;45.5668698;9.9990896;76;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Vegetarian;Under the porticoes of the evocative Piazza Cavour you can see the double entrance: the door for the evening cocktail bar on the ground level, while–hidden on the left–there is a lift to the first level where there is the restaurant: the contemporary dining room is animated by bright wallpaper that seems almost to reveal in advance the imaginative cuisine of the chef-patron. Colorful, contemporary, with neat creative presentations he skilfully alternates meat (their signature is tongue mille-feuille, on the menu since the opening in 2019) and fish, but there is no lack of vegetarian dishes. Half portions are available. The fun grows with the mixology option of the cocktail list–in the evening–as well as the good wine list that, ça va sans dire, has great consideration for Franciacorta.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10059;Il Cavallo Scosso;Italy;Asti;via al Duca 23/d, Asti, 14100, Italy;44.9165713;8.2055856;53;true;true;Contemporary, Seafood;A young and modern restaurant situated in a residential area about 2km from the centre, where the owner-chef offers three tasting menus: Territorio e Tradizione, Il Cavallo Scosso and the more creative Fuori Gara.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10060;Scuderie Sabaude;Italy;Pollenzo;via Amedeo di Savoia 5, Pollenzo, 12042, Italy;44.6833705;7.8942951;81;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant just a stone’s throw from the Università del Gusto di Pollenzo is accessed via an old courtyard with a beautifully tended garden. Housed in the rustic setting of the former royal stables, the restaurant serves a delicious Piedmontese cuisine, light and impeccably presented. The “Tistot”, a delicious panna cotta, is a must!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10061;Nello;Italy;San Casciano in Val di Pesa;Via IV  Novembre 66, San Casciano in Val di Pesa, 50026, Italy;43.6574806;11.1867902;15;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Tuscan;Michele, in the kitchen, and pastry chef Chiara, who also works front of house, have renovated this historic local address and transformed it into a restaurant offering a modern interpretation of Tuscan cuisine. On the varied and intriguing menu, you’ll find dishes such as the intense and highly technical ravioli filled with Parmesan cream (made with milk from Reggiana “red cows”) with chanterelle mushrooms and onions. The concise wine list focuses on nearby Chiantis but also includes bottles from elsewhere.;Air conditioning;[]
10062;Terrazza Gallia;Italy;Milan;piazza Duca d'Aosta 9, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4857326;9.2022544;26;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated on the seventh floor with panoramic views of the city, this restaurant is an excellent choice for a light lunch, a cocktail or an informal dinner. Two young brothers from Naples are at the helm here, creating traditional Italian and Lombardian dishes with a creative and contemporary touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10063;Teresita by Giardino di Mari;Italy;Viareggio;terrazza della Repubblica 7, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.8833328;10.2331864;49;true;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in the private beach club of the same name, this elegant restaurant serves fish and seafood dishes made from carefully selected and top-quality ingredients. A whole page of the menu is dedicated to oysters and raw fish options. An attractive outdoor dining space completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10064;Marc Lanteri;Italy;Castagnito d'Alba;Via Serra 21/d, Castagnito d'Alba, 12050, Italy;44.7543254;8.0518105;23;false;true;Piedmontese, Contemporary;Situated right next to the Fratelli Massucco winery, with which it shares its comfortable outdoor spaces as well as stunning views of the surrounding hills and vineyards, this restaurant is run by Marc Lanteri and Amy Bellotti, partners in life and work, who have chosen this setting for their new Piedmontese adventure. Their cuisine is full of individual character, with three tasting menus (including a vegetarian option featuring produce grown in their own garden) and dishes also available à la carte style. Local ingredients and recipes naturally take centre stage, always enhanced by small touches of colour and imagination. The wine list showcases the property’s own wines, as well as offering a choice of labels from elsewhere in Italy and further afield.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10065;Locanda San Martino;Italy;Chies d'Alpago;via Don Ermolao Barattin 23, Chies d'Alpago, 32010, Italy;46.1816792;12.3923716;81;true;true;Venetian, Seasonal Cuisine;Founded in 1952, this inn has been run by the same family – and especially its female members – ever since. It now boasts the presence of a chef whose many years of experience are evident in his dishes. Much of the meat (especially lamb) is raised in the restaurant’s own farm nearby, while the dishes on the menu are seasonal and classic in style yet with a hint of modern flavour. When the weather allows, make the most of the large terrace boasting fine views of the sunset over the surrounding Alpago region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10066;Il Principe;Italy;Pompei;via Colle San Bartolomeo 4, Pompei, 80045, Italy;40.7483504;14.4983755;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This restaurant focuses on a skilful and creative reinterpretation of Campanian specialities, serving the type of cuisine that you’d be happy to eat every day. Although the dishes are inspired by the chef’s childhood memories and his grandmother’s cooking, he adds his own contemporary touch and careful presentation. Both meat and fish feature, showcasing all the colour and imagination of the best regional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10067;Café Cracco;Italy;Milan;Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4655423;9.1899588;16;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Italian;The bar-pasticceria in Milan par excellence, this café run by the famous Michelin-starred chef (his gourmet restaurant is on the first floor of the same building) also makes a pleasant choice for food, with a menu which moves easily from Milanese specialities to international dishes, including pizza. The display of sweet options at the dessert counter is a feast for the eyes and the palate. This extraordinary corner of Milan’s famous Galleria also offers outdoor tables.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10068;Luciano Cucina Italiana;Italy;Rome;piazza del Teatro di Pompeo 18, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8962136;12.4729286;70;false;true;Creative, Italian;It is widely accepted that the best carbonara in Rome is served in this restaurant. We have to agree – and this is no mean feat, given that this is one of the capital’s iconic dishes. However, Luciano Monosilio’s culinary experience also extends to other equally delicious dishes, some inspired by the traditions of Lazio, others more creative in style, but all full of intense flavours.;Terrace;[]
10069;L'Imbuto;Italy;Lucca;piazza del Collegio 8, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8458125;10.5030555;56;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;One of the most talked about and controversial chefs in Italy, thanks to his creative dishes and original combinations, Tomei has made his home in the former stables of the 17C Pfanner palazzo-museum. Here, guests choose the number of courses they want, let the chef know if they have any allergies and then sit back and enjoy whatever surprising dishes he creates for them.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10070;Josef Stube;Italy;Madonna di Senales;Località Certosa 29, Madonna di Senales, 39020, Italy;46.7054703;10.9099406;33;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Run with passion by the two owners who continue the long family tradition in this hotel-restaurant is one of the most picturesque sights in the Val Senales. Its beautifully kept dining room is romantic and typical of the region, providing a backdrop for just a few dishes which are prepared by the chef with a focus on local ingredients. A hint of Mediterranean influence adds to the appeal.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10071;La Barca;Italy;Rho;via Ratti 54, Rho, 20017, Italy;45.536579;9.0428519;75;false;true;Seafood, Apulian;Run by the Virgilio family since 1967, this popular restaurant pays tribute to historic Bari with its delicious fish dishes and specialities from Puglia. Don’t miss the grilled fish and the reinterpreted cannolo dessert made with sheep’s milk ricotta, pear sauce and pistachio waffles.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10072;Casa Perrotta Restaurant;Italy;Cernobbio;via Cinque Giornate 72, Cernobbio, 22012, Italy;45.8379154;9.0698219;23;true;true;Italian Contemporary;This small, welcoming restaurant with a hint of minimalism and just a few tables serves personalised meat and fish dishes which aim to offer something a little different, with a choice of three tasting menus and an à la carte. Having previously gained experience outside the area, the young family team from Campania runs the restaurant with enthusiasm and a real love for the region’s cuisine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10073;Impronta;Italy;Bassano del Grappa;via Angarano 7, Bassano del Grappa, 36061, Italy;45.7674783;11.7305971;97;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;All'inizio del Ponte Vecchio, icona cittadina nell'incantevole centro storico, il ristorante si sviluppa su diverse sale, a cui si aggiunge un romantico servizio all'aperto di fronte al fiume (quest'ultimo con pochi tavoli, quindi meglio prenotare). Cucina molto creativa ed elaborata, chi ama le sorprese e gli accostamenti originali troverà in questo ristorante un ottimo indirizzo.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
10074;Faletta 1881;Italy;Casale Monferrato;Regione Mandoletta 81, Casale Monferrato, 15033, Italy;45.1012346;8.4341845;31;true;false;Piedmontese, Contemporary;Nestled amid the wine estates and rolling hills of Monferrato, this historic farmhouse has been carefully restored its enthusiastic owners. The restaurant here serves contemporary dishes inspired by regional and Italian recipes, as well as offering welcoming guestrooms (one or two with their own kitchen), a saltwater swimming pool and the relaxing ambience that comes with this rural setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
10075;Osteria Grande;Italy;Arezzo;piazza Grande 26, Arezzo, 52100, Italy;43.4645755;11.8848153;30;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant overlooking the magnificent Piazza Grande and the Loggia Vasariana that takes up one whole side of the square was opened in the summer of 2022 by the enthusiastic Fatjon and Lorenzo (if you ask, they’ll happily share their knowledge of Arezzo’s history with you). The former is at the helm in the kitchen where he expresses his passion for cuisine in seasonal, contemporary-style dishes such as pigeon breast, leg and fillet (each cut is prepared in the appropriate way) served with sweet onion and cocoa nibs, while the latter oversees the wine selection and recommends suitable pairings to guests. For the chef’s pigeon speciality, he may, for example, suggest an original Maturato Tiberini 2018 (a white wine made from grapes that are left to ripen on the vine). Cocktail staff are also hand for guests keen to choose an aperitif or an after-dinner drink from the extensive cocktail list.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10076;Armando al Pantheon;Italy;Rome;salita de' Crescenzi 31, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.899017;12.4762745;59;true;true;Roman, Classic Cuisine;This small restaurant just a few metres from the Pantheon has been run by the Gargioli family since 1961, with the third generation now at the helm. Popular with locals and visitors alike for its traditional cuisine, which includes Roman and Lazian dishes, meat and fish options, and specialities such as offal, veal intestines, spring lamb, fresh anchovies, and sour-cherry tart.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10077;Vite;Italy;Coriano;via Montepirolo 7, località San Patrignano, Coriano, 47853, Italy;43.986595;12.54202;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated within the San Patrignano community, which grows its own crops, raises its own livestock and makes its own cheeses, Vite is now the setting for new, talented chef Giuseppe Biuso’s cuisine, which is made from top-quality ingredients using modern, creative techniques. His Mediterranean dishes are also inspired by his native Sicily, and include several vegetarian specialities. In summer, don’t miss the outdoor dining space which offers fine views of the surrounding countryside.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10078;Quadri Bistrot;Italy;Milan;Via Solferino 48, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4788921;9.1885427;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;A modern bistro with a cocktail-bar, trendy decor, soft lighting and lounge-style background music, as well as a small outdoor space on the pavement which needs to be booked well in advance. The imaginative cuisine comes courtesy of a talented chef who creates dishes full of character from top-quality seasonal ingredients. Our inspectors particularly enjoyed the Bresse chicken stuffed with a cherry sauce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10079;Trattoria dall'Antonia;Italy;Mira;riviera Silvio Trentin 8, Mira, 30034, Italy;45.4342596;12.1303561;35;true;false;Seafood;Housed in a delightful 19C house facing the Naviglio del Brenta, this restaurant has been fully renovated to offer a welcoming space in which fish and seafood reign supreme. Prepared wherever possible from local fish, the dishes served here are simple, traditional and either from the Veneto or elsewhere in Italy.;Air conditioning;[]
10081;aldìVino;Italy;Corciano;via Antonio Gramsci 201, Corciano, 06073, Italy;43.1036814;12.294458;64;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Shelves stacked with wine bottles line the walls at this smart bistro-style restaurant, which also boasts a quiet outdoor space for summer dining. The cuisine is contemporary and creative, and is showcased on three tasting menus from which dishes can also be ordered à la carte. We particularly enjoyed and can highly recommend the chef’s two signature dishes (“piatti firma dello chef”), squid “dripping” and spaghetti with smoked butter, oysters and raspberries. Courses here are divided into meat, fish and vegetable sections (Terra, Acqua and Vegetale).;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10082;Selvatico;Italy;Rivanazzano Terme;via Silvio Pellico 19, Rivanazzano Terme, 27055, Italy;44.9317851;9.015184;16;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Opened in 1912 and now run by the fourth generation of the same family, this is one of the best restaurants in the Oltrepò Pavese area. If you’re looking to sample the gastronomic delights of this region, you’ll find a whole host of delicious specialities on offer, from charcuterie and stews to boiled meats and excellent fresh pasta. Attractively furnished guestrooms with the same nostalgic feel as the restaurant are also available.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10083;Il Marchese - Osteria Mercato Liquori;Italy;Rome;via di Ripetta 162, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.90437;12.47528;61;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Roman;This genuinely Roman restaurant which takes its name from the Marchese del Grillo, a film which symbolises the spirit of Rome, is elegant and noble in style yet with a hint of irony. Although the focus is on traditional cuisine, the stylish decor, beautiful furnishings and dishes full of delicious flavours will instantly appeal to visitors from other cultures as well as locals. There are no fixed times for eating and drinking here: you can enjoy the fried meatballs, amatriciana pasta, stuffed chicken or a quick spaghetti with a tomato sauce at any time of day.;;[]
10084;Locanda La Posta;Italy;Cavour;via dei Fossi 4, Cavour, 10061, Italy;44.7851123;7.3752862;26;false;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This traditional restaurant boasts small dining rooms adorned with wooden ceilings, which were redecorated a few years ago with evocative photos and documents depicting its history. The restaurant’s interesting cuisine is also traditional in style, featuring home-made pastas, a typical boiled meat trolley (“carrello dei bolliti”), and an excellent rabbit stew served with a generous portion of peppers. The selection of delicious home-produced fare includes vegetables, preserves and pastries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10085;Prato Gaio;Italy;Montecalvo Versiggia;Località Versa, bivio per Volpara, Montecalvo Versiggia, 27047, Italy;44.9652928;9.291065;81;true;true;Country cooking;The restaurant trade is in the family genes: already an inn in the 19C, the Prato Gaio takes inspiration from the cuisine of the Oltrepò region. A selection of traditional specialities alongside dishes reinterpreted with flair and imagination are served. An essential stop for anyone looking for local flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10086;I Rodella;Italy;Deruta;strada esterna vicinale della Rocca 2, Deruta, 06053, Italy;42.9529723;12.4031515;63;false;false;Innovative, Umbrian;This complex, which also includes two junior suites and seven guestrooms, dates back to the early 17C and was commissioned by the Church as a stopping off point for travellers on their way to Rome. For many years now, the restaurant has been run by a Venetian family with twin brothers (both highly experienced) working in the kitchen and a third brother, a sommelier, at the helm in the dining room. The cuisine is inspired by local and Venetian traditions, with a modern approach to the combinations of flavours (including home-grown herbs) and to the presentation of its delicious, generous dishes. We recommend that you do as we did and follow Samuele’s advice when making your choice from the dishes prepared by Stefano and Andrea with great skill and passion.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10087;Materia | Spazio Cucina;Italy;Catania;via Teatro Massimo 29, Catania, 95131, Italy;37.5040089;15.0915737;27;true;true;Sicilian, Modern Cuisine;The entrance to this restaurant is typical of an old residential-style building, giving the impression that you are stepping into the chef’s own home. Here, the beautiful dining room boasts shared tables and an entire wall covered with shelves of jars containing dried fruit, pumpkin seeds and red lentils. The classic-style cuisine focuses on grilled dishes and modern cooking methods to create typical Sicilian meat and fish dishes that pay careful attention to the seasons. The first courses are excellent, including the spaghetti with butter and anchovies, which is served with Favignana tuna bottarga and muddica atturrata(spiced breadcrumbs) made from Perciasacchi flour.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10088;Stefenelli Desk;Italy;Aosta;via Claude d'Avise 14, Aosta, 11100, Italy;45.736147;7.3161241;77;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is situated in an alleyway in the historic centre of Aoste. Full of character and accessed via a staircase from the entrance hall, the dining room is housed in what were probably the palazzo’s 18C stables. Under a brick-vaulted ceiling and arches, enjoy cuisine from the Aosta valley with a creative twist.;Terrace;[]
10089;Vescovo Moro;Italy;Verona;via Pontida 3, Verona, 37123, Italy;45.4438842;10.9794643;80;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Situated 50 metres from the basilica of San Zeno (the patron saint of Verona), this restaurant housed in a renovated workshop boasts plenty of outdoor space for summer dining. Here, enjoy eclectic cuisine with an equal balance of Mediterranean and traditional flavours, including an excellent array of raw fish dishes and a small selection of Italian caviar.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10090;Il Narciso;Italy;Carrara;viale Amerigo Vespucci 32, Carrara, 54033, Italy;44.0370312;10.0345978;93;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Housed in the Polda baths near the marina, this recently opened small restaurant on the beach serves cuisine with a contemporary yet classic flavour. The restaurant boasts excellent bread, home-made pasta, traditionally cooked dishes such as chicken casserole and creative desserts. Highly recommended, especially the terrace with its fine sea views.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10091;Osteria 1861;Italy;Santa Maria di Castellabate;via Valentino Izzo 1, Santa Maria di Castellabate, 84048, Italy;40.284492;14.9458799;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Accessed via a narrow alleyway behind the beach, this restaurant housed in an old warehouse once used for smoking cured meats and drying Cilento figs boasts stone-vaulted ceilings, a romantic ambience and a small terrace embellished by beautiful plants. Chef Antoni Tafuri’s cuisine features on various tasting menus (including vegetarian and vegan) and an à la carte and demonstrates careful combinations that aim to showcase his regional ingredients to the full.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10092;La Musa Restaurant & Rooftop Terrace;Italy;Cima;Località Cini 29, Cima, 22018, Italy;46.02691;9.09779;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Just six intimate tables in a modern restaurant with fine views of the lake through its large windows – the view is even more delightful from the summer terrace. The chef blends the flavors of his Sardinia with alpine ingredients, creating tasting itineraries that enhance the territory and the season.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10093;Santamonica;Italy;Genoa;lungomare Lombardo 27, Genoa, 16145, Italy;44.39134;8.96498;84;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Head down to the beach along a narrow street parallel to Corso Italia in the Albaro district of the city to reach this restaurant, where the views from both the dining room and summer terrace embrace the sea to the full. And it is, of course, from the latter that most of its ingredients are sourced (it’s not a coincidence that half a page on the menu is dedicated to raw fish dishes), with Santamonica’s chefs creating modern dishes with a strong emphasis on beautiful presentation. As an example, the traditional, fresh and crispy marinated anchovies are plated with geometric precision and attractively embellished with pine nuts and confit cherry tomatoes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10094;Enoteca di Buttrio;Italy;Buttrio;via Cividale 38, Buttrio, 33042, Italy;46.0167091;13.3365071;76;false;true;Seafood;Housed in a beautiful historic building, this business, originally a wine bar (hence the name “enoteca”), gradually developed into a restaurant over the years. The menu focuses uniquely on fish, almost all of which comes from the Adriatic, showcased in traditional dishes enhanced with a creative twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10095;Locanda Belvedere;Italy;Saludecio;via San Giuseppe 736, frazione San Rocco, Saludecio, 47835, Italy;43.8797072;12.6753928;49;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Using local ingredients, this restaurant offers regional cuisine with some creative touches. Pretty and inviting rooms, tastefully decorated and with period furniture. All overlooking the valley.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10096;Antica Trattoria al Gallo 1909;Italy;Ravenna;via Maggiore 87, Ravenna, 48121, Italy;44.42064;12.191586;44;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;It is an unavoidable reference point in the gastronomic panorama of Ravenna and, as a matter of fact, it is almost always full! An "Historical Establishment of Italy", and rightly so considering that it has been run by the same family for over 100 years, this restaurant is a trattoria only in its name, given the blaze of art nouveau decorations inside. As regards the cuisine, you can expect regional dishes: truffles, succulent meats and local fish. In the dining room everyone is involved, while the young owner will illustrate the wine selection with the typically delightful congeniality of Romagna.;Air conditioning;[]
10097;Osteria Il Granaio;Italy;Rapolano Terme;via dei Monaci, Rapolano Terme, 53040, Italy;43.287373;11.601818;71;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Although it calls itself an osteria, Il Granaio is really a restaurant. It has elegant brick - arched dining rooms occupying a 17C palazzo in the historic centre of Rapolano. On the menu you will find Tuscan specialities such as pici pasta cooked with various sauces, peppery Tuscan beef stew and a selection of fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10098;Osteria L'Abbiccì;Italy;Seregno;via Medici da Seregno 29, Seregno, 20831, Italy;45.6487575;9.2037394;64;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Lombardian;Situated in the centre of Seregno, this modern inn boasts a bright, spacious dining room with an ambience which is both friendly and yet respectful of guests’ privacy. The cuisine is overseen by Davide, who trained with Mauro Elli, the owner-chef of Il Cantuccio in Albavilla. Here, he creates dishes full of character, with a focus on top-quality ingredients and skilful presentation techniques. For a memorable dining experience, the chef’s surprise menu makes an excellent choice. Impressive wine selection and professional service overseen by Gabriele add to the appeal. The business lunch offers excellent value for money.;Air conditioning;[]
10099;Spoon;Italy;Teramo;via Mario Capuani 61, Teramo, 64100, Italy;42.6601179;13.701862;55;true;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Contemporary;Located in the heart of the historic centre, just a stone’s throw from the beautiful 13C cathedral, this small, simple restaurant with an outdoor space is home to owner-chef Marco Cozzi, whose cuisine is the main attraction here. Having trained with Niko Romito, this chef creates dishes from seasonal, regional ingredients, reinterpreting traditional recipes to give them a contemporary flavour (for example, he transforms pancotto into a cream of bread and Navelli saffron, which he then crowns with Robiola cheese, cime di rapa and triangles of cured pork loin). His two tasting menus focus entirely on meat and feature an impressive selection of vegetables.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10100;Voce Aimo e Nadia;Italy;Milan;piazza della Scala 6, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4674271;9.190171;60;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Situated in the heart of Milan, this restaurant owned by the historic Aimo e Nadia in Via Montecuccoli is accessed via its bar-cum-pastry shop which includes a bistro serving a selection of simpler dishes. From here, you enter the main dining room with an open-view kitchen serving excellent Italian dishes reinterpreted in contemporary style. Voce in Giardino, the restaurant’s outdoor summer dining space adorned with interesting sculptures, is a green oasis in the heart of the city.;Air conditioning;[]
10101;Sottovoce;Italy;Como;piazza Cavour 24, Como, 22100, Italy;45.8133581;9.0812671;19;false;true;Italian Contemporary;One of the first rooftop restaurants in Como, Sottovoce boasts an elegant, contemporary feel, while its cuisine makes full use of Italy’s wealth of ingredients, with a particular focus on local produce such as fish from the lake which is served in an array of creative and imaginative dishes (vegetarian options are also available on the à la carte, plus there’s a dedicated vegetarian menu). Facilities here include a quiet, intimate dining room, a private balcony for groups (a maximum of eight people) and a spectacular outdoor Infinity Bar in which to enjoy a late-afternoon aperitif while admiring the beautiful views of the lake.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10102;Felter alle Rose;Italy;Salò;via Gasparo Da Salò 33, Salò, 25087, Italy;45.60674;10.521176;67;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine;This historic trattoria has been brought back to life by a local family with years of experience in the hospitality industry and a real commitment to quality. Convenient private parking, an indoor dining room, a closed veranda and a few tables set out in the wine cellar for tastings and aperitifs are just some of the attractions here. The short menu features simple yet carefully made dishes prepared from seasonal ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10103;Locanda della Luna;Italy;San Giorgio del Sannio;via delle Oche 7, San Giorgio del Sannio, 82018, Italy;41.05654;14.84925;97;false;true;Campanian, Classic Cuisine;In a remote location in the Sannio, this authentic inn offers fine views from its well-kept dining room-cum-veranda and outdoor terrace. The owner-chef creates dishes with a regional flavour using produce from his own garden, without straying too far from local traditions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10104;Hostaria di Bricai;Italy;Varallo;via Fiume 1, Varallo, 13019, Italy;45.817917;8.2520162;26;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the gardens next to the Sacro Monte funicular, this beautiful and bucolic residence overlooks the village. In this relaxing setting, Giorgio serves traditional local cuisine: the rabbit leg in porchetta with mountain-style purée is one of the highlights.;Terrace;[]
10105;Osteria dello Strecciolo;Italy;Robbiate;via Indipendenza 2, Robbiate, 23899, Italy;45.69081;9.44196;66;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Situated in the centre of the village, this popular and professionally run restaurant has an informal atmosphere. The cuisine is inspired by Mediterranean recipes and more regional traditions, with great care taken in the choice of ingredients and beautifully presented dishes. A business lunch menu is also available.;;[]
10106;Il Frantoio;Italy;Colle di Val d'Elsa;via del Castello 40, Colle di Val d'Elsa, 53034, Italy;43.4220531;11.1197927;18;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The 19C millstone, press and cisterns can still be seen in the dining room at this restaurant, bearing witness to its past as an olive oil mill. Situated in spectacular Colle di Val d’Elsa, Il Frantoio boasts old stone and brick walls and vaulted ceilings, as well as tables set out in the piazza for summer dining. Although the setting suggests simple and rustic cuisine, the chef surprises guests with top-quality dishes which are technical and often highly creative, such as liver with sour cherries and pistachios, and smoked spaghetti with an anchovy sauce, capers and black garlic cream.;Terrace;[]
10107;Il Grifone;Italy;Castel San Pietro Terme;via Ca' Masino 611/a - loc. Varignana, Castel San Pietro Terme, 40024, Italy;44.402175;11.5066308;58;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;This fine-dining restaurant housed in the 18C Palazzo Bentivoglio Bargellini is part of the luxurious Palazzo di Varignana resort (with which it shares the Il Grifone symbol), the latter also home to a farm producing olive oil, wine and fruit. In the evening, choose between two tasting menus and an à la carte offering a selection of meat and fish dishes on which the modern recipes feature a careful balance of colours and flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10108;Indigeno;Italy;Montepulciano;Via di Villa Bianca 15, Montepulciano, 53045, Italy;43.08295;11.79339;64;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Tuscan;Boasting an unusually beautiful setting within the Salcheto Organic Winery amid the rolling hills around Montepulciano, this 13C farmhouse has been converted into a wine estate that also includes a restaurant. Simple, home-style cooking with a focus on local traditions takes pride of place here, with dishes made from ingredients either produced on the estate itself or sourced from small-scale local producers. Guests sit at large shared tables made from Amiata oak, or outdoors in summer, where they can enjoy home-made bread and numerous other specialities, including bread gnocchetti with creamed broad beans and bitter herbs, and roast goose leg.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10109;Riccio Restaurant;Italy;Bacoli;via Molo di Baia 47, Bacoli, 80070, Italy;40.8167162;14.0716849;59;false;false;Seafood;Overlooking the port, this restaurant serves top-quality fish and seafood with interesting and personalised touches added by its young chef. We recommend starting with the excellent selection of cooked fish (although there’s also a choice of raw fish should you prefer it), following which you can choose from classic seafood dishes such as spaghetti with clams and fried fish, and a selection of original, top-quality dishes such as dry-aged, smoked and preserved fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10110;MU Dimsum;Italy;Milan;via Aminto Caretto 3, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4827848;9.1996683;18;false;true;Chinese Contemporary, Cantonese;Already visible from the pavement outside this restaurant, the large kitchen where its staff can be observed busy at work is testament to its success. Inside, the dining room is modern and elegant, with careful lighting effects creating a muted ambience in the evening. The extensive menu features classic Chinese dishes – in addition to different types of delicious dim sum, Peking duck also takes pride of place among the main courses.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10111;La Limonaia;Italy;Turin;via Mario Ponzio 10/b, Turin, 10141, Italy;45.0674448;7.6233151;57;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant occupies a large veranda decorated with an original array of tastefully arranged objects and furnishings. The cuisine is both contemporary and exciting, featuring a few interesting fish dishes alongside regional specialities (including from outside Piedmont) such as mandilli (pasta) in a grouper stew with peas and aromatic herbs, brodetto (fish stew) “alla vastese”, and mutton cooked over charcoal embers.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10112;Hosteria del Platano;Italy;Varenna;via Statale 29, Varenna, 23829, Italy;45.99987;9.291888;35;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Situated on the main road overlooking the lake, this pleasant family-run restaurant serves excellent traditional cuisine with a focus on local fish. Atmospheric dining room with stone walls and vaulted ceilings, plus an attractive outdoor space, and friendly, attentive owners.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10113;Il Molo;Italy;Passignano sul Trasimeno;via Aganor Pompili 9, Passignano sul Trasimeno, 06065, Italy;43.1834467;12.1366653;45;true;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;Situated in the historic centre of Passignano, where the village seems to jut out into the Lake Trasimeno (some tables in the main dining room boast views of the lake – make sure you book in advance), Il Molo has become a popular choice for guests keen to try top-quality fish from the lake as well as excellent poultry dishes. We highly recommend the delicious stuffed quail served with mushrooms and liver and accompanied by an excellent glass of local biodynamic red wine. There’s also a good choice of sparkling wines and champagnes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10114;Casa Federici;Italy;Montoro;via Pellegrino Federici, Montoro, 83025, Italy;40.8031612;14.7721381;51;true;true;Contemporary, Campanian;The area around Montoro, famous for its cipolla ramata (copper onion), is now also home to a gourmet restaurant thanks to young chef Francesco Cerrato, whose cuisine is inspired by locally sourced ingredients from this inland region as well as fish and seafood from the coast. The menu also features creative, carefully prepared dishes served by the attentive young staff. Minimalist-style ambience.;Air conditioning;[]
10115;Locanda Martinelli;Italy;Nibbiaia;piazza Mazzini 11, Nibbiaia, 57016, Italy;43.4643371;10.4159811;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It’s well worth leaving the coast and climbing into the foothills to get to this small restaurant serving excellent cuisine. Housed in a rustic-style house with individual furnishings, in what could be the sitting room of a private house, the restaurant serves meat and fish specialities prepared with imagination from local produce and ingredients from further afield. As well as being a wine expert, the female owner gathers herbs, flowers and berries to flavour her recipes.;Air conditioning;[]
10116;Chat Qui Rit;Italy;Venice;calle Tron, sestiere San Marco 1131, Venice, 30124, Italy;45.4344421;12.3361994;77;false;true;Contemporary, Fusion;The generous, colourful and carefully prepared dishes served at this Italian bistro just a stone’s throw from St Mark’s Square could be described as “lagoon fusion” cuisine, thanks to one of the two chefs who demonstrates his love of Japanese flavours in some of his creative recipes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10117;El Brite di Larieto;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;Località Larieto, strada per Passo Tre Croci, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.5519115;12.1756742;27;true;false;Alpine, Traditional Cuisine;If SanBrite boasts a collection of Michelin stars (a classic star for its cuisine and a green star for its sustainable approach), it’s also thanks to this agriturismo’s location in a small larch wood, where it is surrounded by the spectacular Dolomites. Opened 20 years ago and renovated over the years, this smart agriturismo is also home to a stable annexe, where its restaurant celebrates the flavours of Alpine culinary traditions in its meat and charcuterie, cheeses, creamy butter and ice cream, as well as herbs, berries and other local ingredients.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10118;Borgia Milano;Italy;Milan;via Giorgio Washington 56, Milan, 20146, Italy;45.4621437;9.1547585;51;false;true;Contemporary, Creative;This Milanese restaurant with a young talented chef at the helm boasts a breakfast area, as well as a lunchtime bistro and evening wine bar. The atmosphere in the dining room is lively and modern, allowing plenty of privacy, while the service is highly attentive to guests’ needs. This is especially true on the flagship “Psyche” menu, on which the chef creates special dishes in accordance with the guest’s personal preferences. The cuisine is creative, contemporary and technically adept as demonstrated in the carefully prepared pigeon served with hibiscus, blackberry and juniper cream. The interesting wine list includes bottles from across the globe, including some rare labels.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Interesting wine list;[]
10120;La Cucina de' Mibabbo;Italy;Milan;corso Lodi 19, Milan, 20135, Italy;45.4500615;9.20644;56;true;false;Tuscan, Meats and Grills;The name (“My grandfather’s cooking”) says it all: this restaurant serves cuisine from the owner’s native Tuscany, with a focus on Tuscan ingredients prepared with an updated and modern twist. Good selection of Tuscan specialities such as grilled meats and dishes cooked in a wood-fired oven in the evening, while the lunchtime menu is more restricted and Italian in feel.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10121;Al Baccanale;Italy;Piombino;via XX Settembre 20, Piombino, 57025, Italy;42.9224072;10.5270934;15;true;true;Tuscan;Situated in the heart of the historic centre just a stone’s throw from Piombino’s former Medici fortress, this quiet restaurant boasts a backdrop of exposed stonework and vaulted ceilings and just a few tables, so booking ahead is recommended. Here, the enthusiastic and talented owner-chef serves traditional cuisine reinterpreted with a modern and highly individual twist.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10122;Da Attilio;Italy;Naples;via Pignasecca 17, Naples, 80134, Italy;40.845245;14.2483589;16;true;true;Pizza;Situated in one of the liveliest working-class neighbourhoods of Naples, this restaurant serves traditional Neapolitan pizzas, including a few unusual innovations such as pizzas in the shape of an 8-pointed star. In business since 1938 and now run by the third generation of the same family, Da Attilio has just a few tables arranged in two small dining rooms and doesn’t take reservations. Although you may have to wait at the busiest times of day, you’ll find the wait well worthwhile!;Air conditioning;[]
10123;Da Luciano;Italy;Passignano sul Trasimeno;via Nazionale 11, Passignano sul Trasimeno, 06065, Italy;43.18376;12.13689;68;false;true;Italian, Seafood;Enjoy beautiful views of Lake Trasimeno from the outdoor terrace of this restaurant, where the menu focuses mainly on fish, alongside original ingredients such as beans and Umbrian truffles which are used in typical specialities such as tegamaccio (fish stew).;Great view,Terrace;[]
10124;Stefano Mocellin al Padovanino;Italy;Padua;via Santa Chiara 1, Padua, 35123, Italy;45.4034021;11.8769179;26;true;false;Creative, Italian Contemporary;Situated in the historic centre of Padova, this restaurant is home to owner-chef Stefano Mocellin, whose colourful, creative and personalised cuisine is influenced by his past culinary experience in cities such as Milan and Venice. From Milan, for example, he has taken the legendary “cassoeula”, to which he gives a lighter touch thanks to his use of more than one type of meat (pork and duck), while his “saor” and the sardines that he uses to stuff his plin pasta are inspired by Venice. Underlying all of this is his passion for cooking over the barbecue grill, the main focus of almost all the dishes on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10125;Il Frantoio;Italy;Assisi;via Fontebella, 25, Assisi, 06081, Italy;43.072257;12.6094475;82;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant has undergone a skilful refurbishment with a focus on colour, light and furnishings which combine harmoniously with the valley below, as well as with the dishes in which extra-virgin olive oil takes a starring role (not just as a condiment but as an ingredient in its own right). The view through the floor-to-ceiling windows, which extends along the valley as far as San Pietro abbey in Assisi, is as enticing as the cuisine.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10126;Palazzo Branciforte;Italy;Palermo;via Bara all'Olivella 2, Palermo, 90133, Italy;38.1213379;13.3622661;86;true;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;A relaxing oasis in the city centre which offers friendly service from staff who obviously want to ensure that your experience here is memorable. The dishes served are carefully prepared and full of flavour, boasting the occasional modern touch yet also inspired by local traditions. Try the "Capricciosa vista mare": toasted black bread with capers and oregano served with red prawn, dried tomato, artichokes, basil and buffalo mozzarella mousse.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10127;Carter Oblio;Italy;Rome;via Giuseppe Gioachino Belli 21, Rome, 00193, Italy;41.907119;12.4704271;31;true;false;Contemporary;Following years of experience in renowned restaurants, owner-chef Ciro Alberto has achieved his dream of opening his own place. With its clean lines and natural colour scheme, his restaurant has a slightly Nordic feel, while the reasonably priced cuisine demonstrates the imagination and creativity of a chef who is keen to stand out. Expertly prepared and attractively presented contemporary dishes are to the fore here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10128;1908;Italy;Soprabolzano;via Paese 18, Soprabolzano, 39054, Italy;46.5282559;11.405296;64;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;The name of this restaurant refers to the year in which the hotel in which it is located (the Park Hotel Holzner) was opened, while the design is a nod to the Liberty style of the period. Despite this, both the ambience and the cuisine bear the modern and imaginative hallmark of Stephan Zippl. Paying careful attention to sustainability, this chef selects the best regional produce for his dishes – even the Wagyu beef is raised in the chef’s native Renon region. This strong connection with the Alto Adige is also evident on the excellent wine list, which features almost 400 labels from the region and provides perfect pairings for the chef’s tasting menu. Other options include non-alcoholic drinks such as apple juice and alcohol-free cocktails.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10129;La Risacca Blu;Italy;Milan;via Tunisia, angolo via Tadino, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4770356;9.205881;46;true;true;Seafood;The first thing you see when you enter this restaurant near the central railway station is its large display of fresh fish, all delivered daily. The menu features a selection of classic and authentic fish and seafood options, with pride of place given to its raw fish dishes.;;[]
10132;Bis Osteria Italiana Contemporanea;Italy;Colle di Val d'Elsa;Via 20 Settembre 50, Colle di Val d'Elsa, 53034, Italy;43.4209554;11.1168188;21;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Tuscan;In the glorious premises of the old Arnolfo restaurant in the old town, this restaurant is run by the same management as previously, although with a new young chef at the helm in the kitchen. The delicious yet concise menu features “Italian specialities” (the name given to all the main courses) with a focus on meat and fish, accompanied by excellent bread options (you can even order “scarpetta” dipping bread for mopping up the remains of a Cinta Senese pork sauce). The house speciality is a delicious pigeon dish. In fine weather, guests can dine on the beautiful, tranquil terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10133;Oro Nero;Italy;Sauris;Località La Maina 10, Sauris, 33020, Italy;46.452541;12.7267437;49;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Local ingredients such as Sauris trout, Malga cheese, eggs and herbs feature on the menu at this charming restaurant with spectacular views of the surrounding peaks. In a modern dining room where the colours black and gold dominate, Andrea serves delicious creative recipes such as his signature dish of pigeon cooked two different ways with a sweet and sour bitter cherry, peanut and shallot sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10134;Dallo Zio;Italy;Rimini;via Santa Chiara 16, Rimini, 47921, Italy;44.0567555;12.5700557;71;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;A beautifully kept restaurant just a stone’s throw from the Arch of Augustus. Warm and welcoming, the restaurant’s vintage style echoes the 19C origins of the building as well as the 1970s, the decade when it first opened. Divided into two floors with small tables set close together, the menu features meat dishes and, more especially, “fresh fish from Rimini’s fishing boats” prepared in delicious, classic recipes that often have their roots in local traditions.;Air conditioning;[]
10135;Between;Italy;Rivoli;viale Partigiani d'Italia 98/c, Rivoli, 10098, Italy;45.076191;7.5150913;86;false;true;Contemporary;This top-quality restaurant occupies just one simple, minimalist-style dining room, where the young female chef serves a happy combination of Piedmontese ingredients and more creative dishes acquired during her time working abroad.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10136;Il Colmetto;Italy;Rodengo Saiano;via Finilnuovo 9, Rodengo Saiano, 25050, Italy;45.57434;10.10229;36;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;A true gourmet agriturismo, Il Colmetto changes its menu almost week by week in line with the changing seasons. Full of flavour, the ingredients here (many of which are produced on the property, while others are sourced locally) are cooked with precision, avoiding overly fussy and complicated techniques. Instead, the focus is on good, honest cuisine with its roots in peasant traditions, in which the aim is to create comforting dishes that will appeal to the palate. The barbecued specialities, such as the sweetbreads and the excellent Jerusalem artichokes, are particularly delicious, while the superb goats’ milk butter, served soft and fluffy as a cloud with bread and focaccia, is truly delicious – its only drawback is that it can be addictive!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10139;Giano;Italy;Rome;via Liguria 28, Rome, 00187, Italy;41.9062891;12.4887055;62;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Conveniently situated in a quiet setting just behind Via Vittorio Veneto, Giano is housed within the modern Hotel W with which it shares a comfortable cocktail bar and attractive garden. The atmosphere here is modern and informal, with simple fare served at lunchtime and more gourmet dining options in the evening. The resident chef is supported by skilful and experienced Ciccio Sultano who provides valuable input on menus and ingredients. Iconic dishes such as the spaghetto taratatà (with a tuna and bottarga sauce), the em>caponada, and the carpacci are highly recommended, as are desserts such as the reinterpreted millefoglie . Sicilian cuisine takes pride of place here and the service is excellent.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10140;Il Pescatore;Italy;Cala Gonone;via Acqua Dolce 7, Cala Gonone, 08022, Italy;40.2842545;9.6395541;73;true;false;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;This Mediterranean-style restaurant has the evocative feel of a seaside village with its beautiful photos of the coast on the walls. It’s best to book ahead if you want one of the tables on the small terrace overlooking the sea. To avoid confusion, note that the Il Pescatore that we recommend is situated at 7, via Acqua Dolce.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10141;Bottega Aleotti;Italy;Crevalcore;via Paltrinieri 62, Crevalcore, 40014, Italy;44.7237395;11.1463474;43;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Emilian;Situated in a secluded street in the town centre, this restaurant run by a couple boasts an elegant dining room with an attractive dark parquet floor. The cuisine is a good example of how to add a light modern touch to local specialities as well as typical Italian dishes, while the menu also includes a few fish-based options. Don’t miss the home-made pasta!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10142;Marelet;Italy;Treviglio;viale Cesare Battisti 17, Treviglio, 24047, Italy;45.5242169;9.5952355;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian;The name of this restaurant discreetly hidden away in an alleyway on the edge of the town centre is a dialect word meaning “old bachelor”. Small tables set close together give the ambience of a French brasserie and provide the setting for modern, Mediterranean-inspired cuisine. There’s a simpler menu at lunchtime, including salads, tapas and sandwiches, while more choice is available in the evening. Lively atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10143;Langosteria Paraggi;Italy;Paraggi;via Paraggi a Mare 1, Paraggi, 16038, Italy;44.3113972;9.2094107;77;true;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;The elegant Milanese style of the famous Langosteria restaurant has been given a maritime and holiday feel in its seasonal sibling which is housed within the Bagni Fiore overlooking the small yet stunning Paraggi bay. Langosteria Paraggi boasts a vintage decor which is at the same time glamorous and up-to-date, views of the beach and the sea, and a menu focusing on delicious fresh fish and seafood such as oysters and shellfish.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10144;Mammaròssa;Italy;Avezzano;via Giuseppe Garibaldi 388, Avezzano, 67051, Italy;42.0256779;13.4339512;74;true;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Contemporary;At this restaurant, owner-chef Franco Franciosi focuses on the Abruzzo in dishes which are both traditional and modern. The cuisine showcases the best ingredients from the region, including home-grown vegetables from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden and excellent bread made with solina wheat (typical of the Apennines), amid a decor that focuses on sustainability. Daniela looks after guests front of house, offering recommendations from the short yet carefully chosen wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10145;Hostaria del Vicolo;Italy;Sciacca;vicolo Sammaritano 10, Sciacca, 92019, Italy;37.5085;13.08324;58;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Situated in a central yet secluded location, this intimate and elegant restaurant serves typical Sicilian cuisine with a focus on fish, vegetables from the kitchen garden and delicious cheeses. A good wine selection completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10146;20 Posti;Italy;Empoli;via della Murina 4/a, Empoli, 50053, Italy;43.7210585;10.9472176;72;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;A small bistro-style restaurant with an evening lounge bar, situated in a narrow alleyway in the town centre. The young team here serve imaginative Mediterranean meat and fish dishes prepared from an array of carefully chosen ingredients.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10147;La Ciotola;Italy;Porcia;via Sant'Antonio 19, Porcia, 33080, Italy;45.9687603;12.6109708;47;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated along the SS13 which leads to nearby Pordenone, this restaurant has a fresh, busy feel. At lunchtime, the service is quicker, the menu smaller and the prices lower, while in the evening guests can choose from a full menu. Whether you’re here for lunch or dinner, you’ll enjoy meat and fish dishes made by the Cover brothers from top-quality ingredients and prepared simply yet with an imaginative touch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10149;Hostaria Ducale;Italy;Genoa;Salita di San Matteo 29 r, Genoa, 16123, Italy;44.4077498;8.9339308;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated just behind the beautiful Piazza De Ferrari, this restaurant with a quiet ambience and elegant decor provides the backdrop for young chef Daniele Rebosio’s superb, ever-evolving cuisine, which is modern, creative and imaginative and yet inspired by regional traditions. Equally at ease with meat and fish, Rebosio occasionally combines the two in one dish, as evidenced by his veal tongue served with langoustine (carpaccio marinated in passion fruit and salted biscuit stuffed with tartare) or with ravioli with rabbit and mussels dedicated to Fabrizio De André’s song Crêuza de mä .;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10150;Osteria Contemporanea;Italy;Gattinara;via Francesco Mattai 4, Gattinara, 13045, Italy;45.6135926;8.3682171;15;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Housed in an old butcher’s shop right in the village centre, this intimate and elegantly simple “osteria” is run by a young couple. In the kitchen, Agnese Loss, who was born in 2001, has already acquired significant experience since leaving catering school. She creates personal and carefully prepared cuisine with real passion, with one menu that is dedicated exclusively to offal (all we’ll say about this is that we particularly enjoyed the tongue and sweetbreads – we’ll leave it to you to find out how these dishes were prepared!). The other two tasting menus (to be ordered by the whole table) reflect her own tastes, as well as those of her partner Davide, who runs the front of house with elegance and competence, including overseeing the wine list. A la carte options are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
10151;Casa Bertini;Italy;Recanati;via le Grazie 7b, Recanati, 62019, Italy;43.40711;13.53811;90;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;This unexpected gourmet restaurant is housed in a sports centre just outside the historic centre of Recanati, birthplace of famous Italian poet Giacomo Leopardi. At the helm in the kitchen, young, talented chef Andrea Bertini has returned to his native region where he reinterprets the traditions of the Marche (especially meat) to create light, simple and unfussy dishes. The same simple style is echoed in the decor, which is elegant and very understated.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10152;Marechiaro;Italy;Bolzano;via Vicenza 14, Bolzano, 39100, Italy;46.4940329;11.3416189;74;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This smart, elegant restaurant, which has a particularly romantic ambience in the evening, has been serving top-quality fish in Bolzano for over 20 years. Prepared in traditional Italian style, the dishes here focus on the flavour and quality of the fish and seafood on offer, most of which comes from the Mediterranean. The two friendly brothers who run the restaurant are originally from Naples, which explains the specialities from Campania and the excellent pizza which also features on the menu. A simpler selection of dishes is available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10153;Campamac;Italy;Barbaresco;strada della Valle 1, Barbaresco, 12050, Italy;44.7249488;8.0805241;29;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;A real gourmet inn which serves traditional Piedmontese dishes made from excellent ingredients alongside top-quality meats cooked on the barbecue grill. An elegant ambience with a deliberately retro feel, which is beautifully maintained and has plenty of charm.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10155;Lineadombra;Italy;Venice;Ponte dell'Umiltà, sestiere Dorsoduro 19, Venice, 30123, Italy;45.4294583;12.3347372;70;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Boasting a splendid location with an outdoor dining space on a kind of raft-cum-platform, this restaurant boasts one of the most delightful views in Venice, with the Giudecca on the opposite side of the canal. Contemporary cuisine with a focus on fish and the occasional creative twist.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10156;Sustanza;Italy;Naples;Galleria Principe di Napoli 13, Naples, 80135, Italy;40.8525964;14.2503742;76;false;true;Creative;The entrance to this restaurant in the Galleria Principe di Napoli is through the 19CScottoJonno café chantant, from where you take a lift to the restaurant’s Liberty-style dining rooms with their elegant, historic feel. In contrast, the cuisine is modern in flavour, featuring complex and elaborate dishes that have their roots in the traditions and ingredients of the entire Mediterranean (including North Africa), as well as fermented products and the occasional grilled option. The end result is a surprising experience for anyone looking for a change from the usual traditional fare.;Air conditioning;[]
10157;Radici;Italy;Castel Giorgio;Località Borgo La Chiaracia, Castel Giorgio, 05013, Italy;42.703998;11.9564988;33;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;Served in an elegant dining room or on the delightful outdoor terrace in fine weather, the highly creative cuisine at this restaurant has its roots in regional traditions and excellent local producers, while its stunning location within the luxurious Hotel Borgo La Chiaracia among the region’s verdant winding valleys makes it difficult to leave. With a choice of à la carte and tasting menus, our inspectors were particularly impressed by the Origini 20menu, on which all the ingredients are sourced within a 20km radius of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10158;Osteria Origano;Italy;Minervino di Lecce;via Giuseppina Scarciglia 18, Minervino di Lecce, 73020, Italy;40.09191;18.42251;17;false;false;Contemporary, Apulian;A small wine boutique at the entrance to this osteria in the village centre, displays the restaurant’s own wines, which are the perfect complement to your meal, as well as being available to purchase and take home with you. To the rear, an attractive closed veranda and an outdoor space are the perfect settings for hearty, traditional cuisine which ranges from spit-roasted meats to local salumi and home-made pastas. A few fish options are also available.;Air conditioning;[]
10159;Innocenti Wine Experiences;Italy;Poggibonsi;via Cassia nord 2/F, Poggibonsi, 53036, Italy;43.4835043;11.1489215;98;true;false;Contemporary;As you enter this restaurant, you’re struck by the sight of hundreds of bottles of wine lining the walls. First and foremost a wine bar, Innocenti Wine Experiences is transformed into a restaurant for lunch and dinner, serving creative cuisine which focuses mainly on meat dishes with the occasional elaborate and original twist. There’s obviously no problem choosing your wine – just look around you!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10160;Da Lorenzo;Italy;Scala;via Fra' Gerardo Sasso 8, Scala, 84010, Italy;40.6568953;14.6104972;53;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Slightly off the beaten track in the lesser-known village of Scala opposite Ravello, this authentic family trattoria offers an informal change from the many Michelin-starred luxury restaurants dotted along the Amalfi Coast. Da Lorenzo has been serving simple yet excellent fish and seafood cuisine for decades, with a wonderful and highly recommended array of fresh fish on display. A popular panoramic terrace adds to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10161;Mirepuà Food Lab;Italy;Cremolino;via Umberto I 69, Cremolino, 15010, Italy;44.6361062;8.5863841;45;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Piedmontese;Situated in a picturesque medieval village in the Monferrato hills, this restaurant serves classic Piedmontese cuisine with plenty of meat options, alongside a few specialties from the chef’s native Liguria, including fish and seafood dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10162;La Corte Gourmet;Italy;Lainate;piazza Angelo Borroni 1, Lainate, 20045, Italy;45.5712615;9.0280547;75;true;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;An interesting choice of wine with plenty of options by the glass, attentive service in a classic yet contemporary-style dining room, and good, honest cuisine prepared by owner-chef Paolo. The seasonal menu features classic favourites such as Fassona beef tartare and breaded veal cutlets cooked in butter alongside imaginative pasta dishes and truffles (in season). Guests have the option of dining in the attractive “champagneria”, surrounded by exposed brickwork and bottles that have been carefully selected by Antonella, the life and soul of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10163;Lucia;Italy;Giulianova Lido;via Lampedusa 12, Giulianova Lido, 64021, Italy;42.7474502;13.9722905;58;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Having just celebrated their 50th anniversary (they opened in 1971), this restaurant and hotel of the same name remain a solid culinary reference on the Abruzzi coast. The menu here is dedicated solely to fish and, as a result and is often the case, the wine list focuses almost exclusively on white wines. The fish (almost all of which comes from the Adriatic) is carefully sourced, while in the kitchen the chefs prepare classic dishes (such as enormous local langoustines cooked – and served – in a pan with oil, wine, garlic and rosemary) and a few more modern recipes (crispy mullet served with the award-winning spicy Ventricina salami).;Air conditioning;[]
10164;Antica Osteria del Mare;Italy;Milan;via Ascanio Sforza 105, Milan, 20141, Italy;45.4381627;9.1750117;27;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the Naviglio away from Milan’s bustling nightlife, this rustic-style restaurant is decorated with a profusion of wood. As the name suggests, fish and seafood take pride of place on the menu, with a good choice of antipasti to whet the appetite, as well as inviting trays of raw fish dishes (shared by the whole table), followed by delicious traditional pasta and grilled options.;Wheelchair access;[]
10165;med;Italy;Treviso;piazza del Quartiere Latino 13, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.66483;12.24899;75;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;In the pedestrian area of the town, with views of the Sile river from the ground floor, this attractive restaurant serves regional cuisine with a focus on local ingredients, prepared in a classic style attentive to modern tastes. There’s an excellent wine list, plus live music and a pleasant outdoor space for fine weather dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10166;Forme Restaurant;Italy;Brescia;Via Codignole 52, Brescia, 25124, Italy;45.5103894;10.1970917;53;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Having worked in Michelin-starred restaurants such as Miramonti l'Altro, Arianna Gatti has now achieved her dream of opening her own restaurant. In this restored old building featuring designer-style details and a charming outdoor space, she serves an extensive selection of intensely flavoured dishes from her native Abruzzo and the region of Lombardy where she trained as a professional chef. A delightful all-round dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10167;Osteria de' Mercati;Italy;Sassari;via Mercato 2, Sassari, 07100, Italy;40.7276061;8.5628406;38;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Slightly set back from the bustling streets of the historic centre yet still in the heart of the town, this delightful small restaurant is a recent addition to Sassari. It boasts a modern, elegant decor, friendly staff and a menu featuring carefully prepared fresh, seasonal dishes. Our inspector particularly recommends the seafood risotto. A choice of regional wines completes the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
10168;Gallery Bistrot Contemporaneo;Italy;Troia;via Regina Margherita 3/b, Troia, 71029, Italy;41.3632895;15.3128249;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Modern, tasty and carefully curated cuisine, which is prepared using the best seasonal ingredients. There is also a creative touch to some of the dishes, such as the vitello tonnato in which the meat (Fassona veal from the Piedmont) takes on the appearance of raspberries, or the delicate duck breast served with veal jus. The restaurant offers just 20 seats in a long dining room where the walls and ceiling form a sort of light wood-panelled arch that creates a real sense of movement.;Air conditioning;[]
10169;Veranda;Italy;Cesenatico;viale Giosuè Carducci 140, Cesenatico, 47042, Italy;44.1991935;12.4065654;27;false;true;Seafood;Alberto Faccani, the two-Michelin starred chef at the Magnolia restaurant in the hills inland from Cesenatico, oversees the cuisine at this restaurant. Fish takes centre stage here, in unfussy dishes that faithfully reflect the maritime traditions of the Adriatic. Primi courses include raw dishes, gratins, seafood salads, pasta and risotto, while secondi feature a selection of grilled, baked and fried fish (depending on the day’s catch).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10170;La Nicchia;Italy;Cavour;via Roma 9, Cavour, 10061, Italy;44.7851524;7.3748027;29;false;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;This tastefully decorated restaurant is housed in a late - 18C building, which is marked on an old map from the Napoleonic era. Here the best local ingredients are selected to create regional dishes with the occasional contemporary twist.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10171;Bistrot La Perla;Italy;Corvara in Badia;strada Col Alt 105, Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.547083;11.8761907;95;false;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Take a culinary journey from the north of Italy to the south from the comfort of your table at the Bistrot La Perla, where guests are enthusiastically introduced to the many delightful flavours and ingredients this beautiful country has to offer. Excellent fish specialities also available.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10172;Pascalucci;Italy;San Nicola Manfredi;via Appia 1, San Nicola Manfredi, 82010, Italy;41.0942246;14.8327808;47;false;true;Campanian, Seafood;A traditional restaurant serving regional cuisine, as well as skilfully prepared fish dishes made from fresh produce. Specialities include Beneventano beef fillet and octopus in aspic jelly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10173;Unterwirt;Italy;Gudon;Gudon 45, Gudon, 39043, Italy;46.6484396;11.5995819;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Occupying a private house, this restaurant boasts a couple of old Stube-style dining rooms, one of which is highly romantic and dates back to the 13C – although it looks as though the vintage wood may have come from elsewhere, it has in fact all been here for centuries. The owner-chef creates carefully thought-out dishes which combine precision and classic comfort with the occasional modern touch, harmoniously combining the flavours of the Alto Adige with Mediterranean influences, with a particular focus on fish. A welcoming outdoor terrace for summer dining completes the picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10174;Tenuta del Gallo;Italy;Macchie;Strada degli Ortacci 34, Macchie, 05022, Italy;42.5997785;12.3696881;90;false;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Whether you dine indoors in the charming, romantic dining room or outdoors with views of the surrounding countryside, you’ll enjoy traditional local cuisine and classic Italian favourites at this restaurant. Our inspectors particularly enjoyed the excellent beef carpaccio with truffles and the local guinea fowl with chickpeas. Comfortable guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10175;Crotasc;Italy;Mese;via Don Primo Lucchinetti 63, Mese, 23020, Italy;46.3110112;9.3812333;24;false;true;Cuisine from Valtellina, Modern Cuisine;Here one can choose between a smaller, typically mountain style dining room with stone paving and open fireplace and a larger room in contemporary rustic style. In summer one can dine on the terrace.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10176;Il Baretto;Italy;Albignasego;via Europa 6, Albignasego, 35020, Italy;45.3468396;11.867622;58;false;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Il Baretto on the outskirts of Padova is a must for anyone who loves classic, traditional fish and seafood, thanks to its menu which includes a number of typical Venetian dishes. The top-quality fish is skilfully prepared to bring out its full flavour and distinctive characteristics, providing a real treat for the tastebuds in this inland temple to the sea.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10177;La Luge;Italy;Breuil Cervinia;Perreres, loc. Varvoyes, Breuil Cervinia, 11021, Italy;45.90739;7.6139812;82;false;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Italian;This attractive, rustic - style restaurant is situated just a few kilometres from the centre of Cervinia. It stands in a tranquil, panoramic basin where the only neighbours are the marmots in the hills around. Popular with passing tourists, as well as locals who feel the journey out here is well worth the effort. The restaurant offers a good range of choices for all palates. This includes soups, different cuts of meat, typical specialities from the Aosta valley and even a few fish dishes. This address is also worth a mention for the attractive guestrooms available.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10178;Osteria Cascina dei Fiori;Italy;Borgo Vercelli;Regione Forte, Borgo Vercelli, 13012, Italy;45.35148;8.46273;28;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant’s warm, elegant and rustic atmosphere with wooden furniture and exposed beams provides the setting for its seasonally inspired, regional cuisine. The experienced owners are welcoming and attentive, while the menu features specialities such as frogs’ leg and courgette flower risotto.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10179;Paolo Teverini;Italy;Bagno di Romagna;via del Popolo 2, Bagno di Romagna, 47021, Italy;43.83294;11.9581;26;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Situated in the charming village of Bagno di Romagna and surrounded by beautiful rolling hills, Teverini is a culinary name full of history in this area. The cuisine here demonstrates different traditions – the local region is an obvious influence (especially its mushrooms), but fish and seafood also feature along with plenty of vegetables.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10180;Antica Osteria dei Camelì;Italy;Ambivere;via Marconi 13, Ambivere, 24030, Italy;45.7195137;9.5473766;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Occupying an attractive farmhouse dating back to the 16C, this restaurant boasts an interesting combination of antique elegance and modern style. The cuisine is equally impressive, offering a selection of traditional and innovative dishes that pay close attention to nutritional balance and the healthiness of the combinations of ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10181;Roscioli;Italy;Rome;via dei Giubbonari 21, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8942487;12.4742332;52;false;false;Roman, Italian;This restaurant is part of one of the best food outlets in Rome, which offers delicacies such as typical Roman pastas, cooked and raw fish, meat, an impressive selection of cured hams and cheeses, as well as top-quality ingredients such as anchovies and mozzarella. Excellent home-baked bread and a varied wine list complete the picture. Make sure you book ahead, as it’s hard to get a table here without a reservation.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10182;Osteria degli Angeli;Italy;Malnate;via Giuseppe Brusa 5, Malnate, 21046, Italy;45.8006366;8.8792188;86;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;An attractive restaurant which offers a friendly and informal welcome and service, alongside an elegant, personalised yet classic decor. The cuisine is mainly Mediterranean in flavour, emphasised by the use of local and seasonal ingredients. The self-taught chef here is passionate about his cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10183;Casa Fantini/Lake Time;Italy;Pella;piazza Motta, Pella, 28010, Italy;45.8013764;8.3882327;70;true;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;Situated on the lakefront in the attractive town of Pella, this modern and welcoming restaurant occupies an old building which has been restored and furnished with a stylish and harmonious decor. Offering simpler options at lunchtime, the restaurant serves traditional cuisine reinterpreted and presented with a contemporary flavour. A lounge, garden, swimming pool and 11 guestrooms add to the exclusive appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10184;La Taverna di Bacco;Italy;Nettuno;largo Luigi Trafelli, 5, Nettuno, 00048, Italy;41.4575676;12.6582805;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A small restaurant just a stone’s throw from the sea which is memorable for its chic decor and intimate ambience. The cuisine combines traditional influences with an innovative approach resulting in ambitious, creative and modern dishes. The wine list is particularly worthy of note.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10185;Novo Osteria;Italy;Borgonovo Val Tidone;piazza De Cristoforis 30, Borgonovo Val Tidone, 29011, Italy;45.0143347;9.4472594;64;true;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Originally a monastery, this building dating back to the 11C was later transformed into an inn. Having closed at the beginning of this century, the building has now been fully renovated and restored to its original function, while retaining much of its original architecture. In addition to the restaurant, which serves traditional local cuisine with a modern focus and plenty of flavour (we particularly enjoyed the savoury zabaglione gnocchi with porcini mushrooms, Jerusalem artichokes and currants), there are also seven guestrooms available in the adjoining Locanda Borgo Impero.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10186;Aqua;Italy;Torbole;lungolago Conca d'Oro 11, Torbole, 38069, Italy;45.8682988;10.8769404;61;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Italian;The most attractive space in this restaurant is its contemporary, almost Milanese-style veranda-dining room which boasts relaxing views of Lake Garda, with sailboats bobbing on the water ruffled by the famous Ora wind, and the peaks of Trentino in the distance. The Italian cuisine served here is prepared simply, allowing the quality of the ingredients (many of which are sourced locally) to shine through. Fish from the lake takes pride of place, although saltwater fish also features. There’s also a good selection of wine.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10187;Konnubio;Italy;Florence;via dei Conti 8 r, Florence, 50123, Italy;43.7746881;11.2529333;72;false;true;Italian Contemporary;An informal yet attractive setting in which to enjoy modern cuisine, including a choice of tasting menus with a focus on meat, fish or vegetables. We particularly enjoyed the beef fillet in a seed crust, which was pink and succulent and served with radicchio and buttery mashed potatoes. The interesting wine selection includes labels from Italy and further afield, which are subdivided by grape variety. If you want to eat at the romantic little table on the step, make sure you book well in advance!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10188;Osteria della Foce;Italy;Genoa;via Eugenio Ruspoli 72r, Genoa, 16129, Italy;44.3984887;8.9477154;80;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;This simple restaurant stands out for its delicious, authentic cuisine which is influenced by Ligurian and Italian traditions alike. The culinary techniques used are classic, both in its meat dishes (the roast veal is excellent) and fish options (raw fish dishes often feature on the menu). First courses include a home-made bronze-cut pasta (“trafilata al bronzo”) which is served with sauces inspired by whatever is in season or available in the market.;Terrace;[]
10189;ConTatto;Italy;Frascati;via Gioberti 11, Frascati, 00044, Italy;41.8080418;12.6820784;78;true;true;Cuisine from Lazio;Situated in a small town just a few kilometres from the capital, this restaurant run by two young food enthusiasts serves regional dishes with a modern touch, such as cuttlefish with asparagus and a Bernese sauce. Guests can visit the interesting tufa-rock cellar, where the chef experiments with old preserving techniques and special flavourings. In addition, the cellar is used as a venue for exhibitions by different art galleries every season.;Air conditioning;[]
10190;Il Grano di Pepe;Italy;Ravarino;via Roma 178/a, Ravarino, 41017, Italy;44.7238155;11.0996024;88;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;While you’re trying to decide between the tasting menu and the à la carte at this restaurant, you can tuck into its excellent bread, including the “sfincione” – a type of tomato-flavoured focaccia from Palermo which makes the journey here worthwhile on its own! If fish is your preference, we recommend the “Palermo and Marseille” fish stew, an intense dish full of bold and delicious flavours. Minimalist decor and a friendly welcome from chef Rino Duca complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10191;Angiò-Macelleria di Mare;Italy;Catania;viale Africa 28/h, Catania, 95129, Italy;37.5158518;15.104726;94;true;true;Seafood;The phrase “macellaria di mare” translates as “fish and seafood butcher’s”, a reference to the cured and seasoned fish that features on the menu here. The restaurant offers an original formula in which guests chat to the chef and choose their dish at the counter where ingredients are displayed, before taking a seat in the simple yet attractive dining room with its open-view kitchen. Our advice is to give young chef Alberto Angiolucci free reign – the result is a new take on fish and seafood cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10192;Emozioni;Italy;Campobasso;via Guglielmo Marconi 129, Campobasso, 86100, Italy;41.5604699;14.6571809;100;true;false;Contemporary;Situated in the heart of the historic centre, this quiet restaurant with attractive stone walls and wooden ceilings boasts a pleasantly elegant and relaxed atmosphere. The chef pays particular attention to local ingredients which he reinterprets with modern and highly personal touches.;Air conditioning;[]
10193;Trattoria del Cimino dal 1895;Italy;Caprarola;via Filippo Nicolai 44, Caprarola, 01032, Italy;42.326814;12.239228;53;true;false;Cuisine from Lazio, Traditional Cuisine;Situated on the hill leading to Palazzo Farnese, this restaurant occupies the oldest building in the village, which dates back to 1370. Since 1940, the Calistri family have been delighting their guests with delicious specialities from Lazio, including excellent cured hams, fresh pasta (the amatriciana is particularly renowned), grilled meats and an impressive selection of cheeses and desserts. Excellent wines and spirits complete the picture.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10194;Le Colonne;Italy;Caserta;viale Giulio Douhet 7/9, Caserta, 81100, Italy;41.0725177;14.31933;54;true;false;Campanian, Modern Cuisine;You’d recognise this cuisine as southern Italian even if you were blindfolded, thanks to its strong and intense flavours. Imaginatively prepared and presented dishes, many of which showcase the region’s mozzarella cheese, plus a delicious selection of desserts and pastries. All in all, an excellent choice!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10195;Acqua Pazza;Italy;Bologna;via Murri 168/d, Bologna, 40137, Italy;44.4730162;11.3695149;79;true;true;Seafood;Although this restaurant is not in the centre, if you’re looking for excellent fish (mostly from the Mediterranean) personally selected by the owner - chef, then it’s well worth the few minutes it takes to find a parking space here. Beautifully cooked food, which is simply prepared using top - quality produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10196;Sale Grosso;Italy;Bologna;vicolo De' Facchini 4/a, Bologna, 40124, Italy;44.4973069;11.3482487;32;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A simple, bistro - style restaurant serving well - prepared, mainly Mediterranean - style cuisine. Although fish and seafood dominate the menu, there are also a few vegetarian dishes and vegan specialities available.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10197;Trattoria Battibecco;Italy;Bologna;via Battibecco 4/b, Bologna, 40123, Italy;44.493474;11.3412365;27;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seafood;Situated in a narrow street in the city centre, this stylish, elegant restaurant is renowned for its traditional dishes and seafood specialities. Simpler fare at more moderate prices available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10198;SottoSopra;Italy;Baveno;corso Garibaldi 40, Baveno, 28831, Italy;45.9107304;8.5043938;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A pleasant and colourful restaurant in the village centre, divided into several dining rooms. The owner-chef prepares a range of eclectic dishes with passion and enthusiasm, offering a menu which includes meat dishes alongside fish options (salt- and freshwater), as well as a few regional specialities.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10199;Madama Vigna;Italy;Baldichieri d'Asti;via Nazionale 41, Baldichieri d'Asti, 14011, Italy;44.9032949;8.091008;49;false;true;Piedmontese, Farm to table;This restuarant has a good wine list with a focus on local labels, as well as an excellent selection of regional specialities on the menu. Dishes include agnolotti (a type of stuffed pasta) with fondue, Piedmontese beef, Villanova chicken and the inevitable bunet dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10200;La Capanna di Eraclio;Italy;Codigoro;Località per Le Venezie 21, Codigoro, 44021, Italy;44.8672276;12.0457984;62;true;true;Seafood;Whenever we visit Capanna di Eraclio, we have the strange yet wonderful feeling of coming home. Opened in 1922 and now in the hands of the fourth generation of the family, this restaurant has changed little – to our relief – since the time when a kitchen was first added to the inn that already stood here. The atmosphere is that of a simple, traditional family trattoria, yet with unexpected touches of elegance. The cuisine, meanwhile, focuses on the best ingredients that the Po delta has to offer, from scallops and small sole to superb eel and blue crab served steamed in its shell to bring out its full flavours, with a fresh mayonnaise on the side. It's interesting to note that this unique restaurant is situated seven metres below sea level!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10201;San Marco;Italy;Canelli;via Alba 136, Canelli, 14053, Italy;44.7198462;8.2799189;63;false;false;Piedmontese, Classic Cuisine;This long-established restaurant in the Asti region has been open for over 70 years and is still renowned for its regional cuisine served in a classic-style dining room. Dishes include cardoons with Raschera cheese fondue, the famous agnolottini del plin (a type of ravioli), and the Piedmontese bunet which is part of a trio of desserts that includes hazelnut tart and zabaglione with Canelli muscat wine.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10202;Bacco;Italy;Barletta;piazza Marina 30, Barletta, 76121, Italy;41.3223875;16.2844955;96;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The focus at this restaurant is on a variety of local ingredients and specialities that even a novice food-lover would recognise as typical of this region. The owner-chef at this intimate and elegant gem of a restaurant is Ruggiero Doronzo, whose mantra is “simplicity and seasonality”.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10203;Carne & Spirito;Italy;Brescia;via dei Gelsi 5, Brescia, 25125, Italy;45.5178242;10.1776993;68;true;false;Steakhouse, Italian Contemporary;The environment here is elegantly rustic thanks to fine furnishings and colourful décor – an attractive background to the variety of creative and imaginative specialties on offer. Rooms are neat and simple. Charming rooms, furnished in different styles with elegant simplicity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10204;Osteria Al GiGianca;Italy;Bergamo;via Broseta 113, Bergamo, 24128, Italy;45.6934038;9.6465415;54;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Although the out - of - town location is a slight drawback, this restaurant passionately run has a welcoming atmosphere. Seasonal, regional cuisine, plus a good choice of wine and beers.;Air conditioning;[]
10205;Vicolo Colombina;Italy;Bologna;vicolo Colombina 5/b, Bologna, 40123, Italy;44.4924017;11.3421624;83;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Situated right in the heart of the historic centre among the narrow alleyways near the market and Piazza Maggiore, this restaurant serves traditional cuisine (no fish) with a subtle contemporary twist. Two modern dining rooms with modern decor, plus a wine list with a focus on regional labels.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10206;Taverna Kerkira;Italy;Bagnara Calabra;corso Vittorio Emanuele 217, Bagnara Calabra, 89011, Italy;38.2842082;15.8004227;93;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Kerkira (Corfu in Greek) owes its existence to the chef’s Greek mother, who passed on the culinary traditions of her native island to her son. These traditions are alive and well in this taverna, which also features Calabrese and Mediterranean dishes on the menu. Simple dining room with a friendly ambience, not far from the centre and seafront in the village where singer Mia Martini was born.;Air conditioning;[]
10207;Benedikto;Italy;Assisi;via Eremo delle Carceri 1/a, Assisi, 06081, Italy;43.0705679;12.6199671;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Situated in the elegant setting of the Nun hotel on the edge of Assisi’s historic centre, Benedikto serves typical Umbrian ingredients which are transformed into creative and imaginative dishes by talented chef Enea Barbanera. In fine weather, dinner is served on the romantic outdoor terrace with views of Assisi’s castle.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10208;Zunica 1880;Italy;Civitella del Tronto;piazza Filippi Pepe 14, Civitella del Tronto, 64010, Italy;42.772535;13.6692461;96;false;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Modern Cuisine;The pleasant outdoor space and some of the hotel rooms at Zunica overlook Civitella del Tronto’s central square on which this restaurant stands. For more than 100 years, Zunica 1880 has been a proud standard-bearer for typical Abruzzi cuisine, as well as dishes influenced by the nearby Marche region. Seasonal vegetables take pride of place on the menu, served with carefully selected meat (make sure you try the lamb and pigeon!), all prepared with a fine balance of traditional and contemporary styles.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10209;La Maison du Gourmet;Italy;Coloreto;strada Budellungo 96, Coloreto, 43123, Italy;44.7692136;10.3785223;17;false;true;Contemporary;Housed in a fully renovated old farm in the countryside outside Parma, this gourmet restaurant serves top-quality meat and fish dishes with a focus on creativity rather than local traditions. The starters are particularly delicious!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10210;Aubergine;Italy;Abano Terme;via Ghislandi 5, Abano Terme, 35031, Italy;45.35044;11.77494;56;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Situated in a town famous for its thermal baths, this classically elegant restaurant serves meat and fish cuisine including specialities from the Veneto such as Berico ham, bigoli pasta with sardines, and veal liver with onions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10211;Serpillo;Italy;Bevagna;via di Mezzo 1, località Torre del Colle, Bevagna, 06031, Italy;42.9439497;12.5781303;35;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated in a charming medieval village which is also home to a couple of small hotels, this attractive, rustic restaurant in an old olive mill acts as the backdrop for regional and Italian cuisine. Dishes with a touch of modern flavour are presented on a menu which, although not extensive, offers good value for money.;Terrace;[]
10212;Il Ristorantino - Da Dino;Italy;Anzola dell'Emilia;via XXV Aprile 11, Anzola dell'Emilia, 40011, Italy;44.5493699;11.1907781;56;false;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Tucked away in an unexpected location in a residential district, this restaurant is nonetheless popular with its loyal and regular clientele. And the reason is obvious – the high quality of the cuisine served here. Bologna’s traditional specialities and other Italian dishes are joined on the menu by a few fish options on Thursdays and Fridays.;Air conditioning;[]
10213;Cacciatori;Italy;Cartosio;via Moreno 30, Cartosio, 15015, Italy;44.5935867;8.4205801;64;false;false;Piedmontese, Seasonal Cuisine;You pass through beautiful hilly scenery to get to Cartosio, where you’ll find this typical country house specialising in local cuisine. Although it’s been in business for several decades, during which nine different generations have been at the helm, the formula has (fortunately!) hardly changed, with a focus on Piedmontese dishes made from top-quality local and seasonal ingredients, with the main courses still cooked on the wood-fired stove. The wine list includes some excellent vertical labels, especially from the main wineries in the Langhe. Simple yet attractive guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10214;L'Angolo d'Abruzzo;Italy;Carsoli;piazza Aldo Moro 8, Carsoli, 67061, Italy;42.0956419;13.0807684;55;false;true;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Traditional Cuisine;For almost 40 years, the Angolo d’Abruzzo restaurant has been home to the Centofanti family, who act as excellent ambassadors for the region by offering the best local, seasonal ingredients (for this reason, there’s no fish on the menu) in a host of traditional, regional recipes. Specialities such as cured meats, local ham, bruschetta and fresh home-made pasta (including “chitarra” spaghetti) take centre stage, while main courses include grilled dishes (porcini mushrooms in season, cuts of beef and veal at any time of year) and stews (mutton etc). When it comes to dessert, make sure you try the crème caramel with Navelli saffron. A misleading sign saying “sagrestia” (sacristy) actually indicates the well-stocked wine cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10215;VeRo - Venetian Roots;Italy;Venice;Riva Ca'di Dio 2181, Venice, 30121, Italy;45.4330725;12.3490106;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated within the elegant Hotel Ca' di Dio in the Arsenale district where the Venice Biennale is held, VeRo is an elegant, exclusive and trendy restaurant. Despite the ambience, however, it’s the cuisine that is the real attraction here, thanks to excellent local and Italian ingredients which are transformed into creative dishes with references to the Venetian lagoon. Influences from other Italian regions also feature, including the occasional nod to skilful chef Luigi Lionetti’s native Campania.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10216;Alajmo Cortina;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;Località Ronco 123, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.5430865;12.1260741;96;false;true;Contemporary, Alpine;Situated in the restored premises of the historic El Toulà restaurant, Alajmo Cortina is home to a bar on the ground floor, with the restaurant occupying the two upper floors (no lift). Although traditional in feel with a profusion of wood, the restaurant is run by a young and enthusiastic team. The cuisine focuses mainly on the region, although the menu also features fish and other imaginative options on tasting menus and an à la carte.;Car park,Great view;[]
10217;Mirko's;Italy;Castellammare del Golfo;discesa Annunziata 1, Castellammare del Golfo, 91014, Italy;38.0280753;12.880544;45;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;This small restaurant, located near the steps to Cala Piccola, is run by an entire family and is beginning to earn an excellent local reputation. The son is at the helm in the kitchen. Having gained experience elsewhere for many years, he decided to start his own venture, which shows every sign of having paid off. Enjoy excellent fish and seafood specialities cooked in Mediterranean and Sicilian style in a quiet, beautifully kept dining room.;Terrace;[]
10218;La Bottega del 30;Italy;Castelnuovo Berardenga;via Santa Caterina 2, località Villa a Sesta, Castelnuovo Berardenga, 53019, Italy;43.3850498;11.4800311;71;false;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;There’s a story behind the name of this restaurant: on the 30th day of every month a travelling salesman used to stop in this small, delightful village. In the meantime, a young French chef, Hélène, arrived here and fell in love with Chianti and its cuisine. She named her restaurant after the travelling salesman and the name has been kept in his memory. In a typical setting of stone walls and old rural objects from bygone days, Hélène is now front-of-house taking care of guests, while Nadia Mongiat has replaced her in the kitchen, where she continues with the restaurant’s tradition of creating simple Tuscan cuisine. The focus here is on preparing ingredients in traditional ways, such as pork liver (the thinnest part of the liver is used) cooked at a low temperature and then stored in lard with fennel for a few days before being re-heated sous-vide in a bain-marie. As a result, the liver (served lukewarm on a bed of Tuscan green beans) is soft and delicious.;Terrace;[]
10219;Galileo;Italy;Civitanova Marche;via IV Novembre conc. 25, Civitanova Marche, 62012, Italy;43.3174;13.7227;56;true;true;Seafood;Boasting a dining room overlooking the beach, Galileo is a typical Adriatic restaurant serving fish and seafood dishes that are popular with many Italians. Options include seafood salad, a selection of antipasti, fish and seafood pastas, assorted small fried fish, and grilled recipes. In other words, delicious, traditional and unfussy cuisine in which fish takes centre stage.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10220;La Bul;Italy;Bari;via Villari 52, Bari, 70122, Italy;41.1264379;16.8644214;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Here, in one of Bari’s most interesting restaurants, chef Antonio Scalera serves top-quality cuisine accompanied by intelligently chosen wines with fascinating stories behind them. The dishes often feature traditional recipes and ingredients from Puglia yet are creative and of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10221;Trattoria Toscana al Vecchio Forno;Italy;San Quirico d'Orcia;via Poliziano 18, San Quirico d'Orcia, 53027, Italy;43.0598574;11.604681;49;false;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;If you are looking for a place to eat that is centrally located and has good prices, you have found it. Captivating trattoria atmosphere. Pretty summer garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10222;Caffè delle Rose Bistrot;Italy;Verbania;via Ruga 36, Verbania, 28922, Italy;45.922741;8.5512755;66;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Occupying an early 20C building in the heart of Pallanza’s picturesque historic centre, this authentic bistro now has a young and contemporary feel. Run by Massimiliano Celeste, a talented chef who is very well known in the region, the restaurant specialises in Mediterranean cuisine prepared with a touch of imagination. There’s a small chef’s table in front of the kitchen, plus an old ice-house (now a small wine cellar housing some excellent wines) which is well worth visiting.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10223;I Carracci;Italy;Bologna;via Manzoni, 2, Bologna, 40121, Italy;44.4963357;11.3429519;97;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The ceiling at this restaurant is adorned with superb frescoes thought to be by the school of the Carracci brothers, whose painters were definitely responsible for decorating other rooms in this palazzo. This is one good reason for choosing this restaurant, and the cuisine is another – the new chef here creates dishes which are appealingly creative without being overly fussy or excessive.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10224;Alle Codole;Italy;Canale d'Agordo;via XX Agosto 27, Canale d'Agordo, 32020, Italy;46.3570318;11.913779;35;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;‘Codole’ is the nickname of the family that runs this restaurant and whose ancestors once worked in the copper mines in the area. Today, the family has exchanged mining for cooking, offering guests specialities such as ricotta and black truffle ravioli with a lamb ragù, and loin of venison in a porcini mushroom crust.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10225;Al Carroponte;Italy;Bergamo;via De Amicis 4, Bergamo, 24127, Italy;45.6880938;9.6562166;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;This restaurant is renowned in Bergamo for its good choice of varied cuisine, as well as its lively, buzzing atmosphere. The excellent, tasty cuisine is typically Italian and contemporary in style, and includes luxury ingredients such as lobster and caviar, while the “classic” à la carte is enhanced by a selection of cured hams, cheeses and finger food. But the Carroponte’s beating heart is owner Oscar Mazzoleni’s passion for the world of wine, with an incredible selection of over 2 000 labels that puts many more famous Michelin-starred restaurants in the shade.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10226;Barbieri;Italy;Altomonte;via Italo Barbieri, Altomonte, 87042, Italy;39.6949455;16.1291378;82;true;true;Calabrian, Traditional Cuisine;Enjoy your meal in the classic - style dining room or on the outdoor terrace in fine weather. The menu here is seasonal, with a focus on delicious Calabrian cuisine, while the wine list also features exclusively local options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10227;Matteo Ristorante;Italy;Biella;piazza Duomo 6, Biella, 13900, Italy;45.5658857;8.0528998;56;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The soft-toned decor is modern and intimate, while the cuisine also has a contemporary feel. Dishes include meat and fish options, plus numerous types of risottos, many of which feature distinctly modern ingredients. Coffee service and aperitifs in the near Laboratory, at n 10.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10228;Villa Tiboldi;Italy;Canale;via Case Sparse 127, località Tiboldi, Canale, 12043, Italy;44.7955746;7.9747841;49;true;true;Piedmontese, Contemporary;A delightful combination of good food and a romantic ambience in this old restored farmhouse surrounded by hills. Top - quality cuisine and a wine cellar that is well worth a visit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10229;Trattoria la Colonna;Italy;Rottofreno;Via Emilia Est 6, località San Nicolò, Rottofreno, 29010, Italy;45.0558734;9.6092702;41;true;false;Seafood;This classic-style restaurant with a recently renovated dining room is situated on the street that runs through the village of San Nicolò. Although the menu features some meat dishes (on Sundays in winter, this includes specialities such as boiled meats, anolini pasta in broth, and typical desserts such as ciambella cake with zabaglione), it is particularly renowned for its wide selection of fish options. At lunchtime during the week, there’s a choice of simpler recipes, but if you ask, staff will be happy to offer you the longer evening menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10230;Lord Nelson;Italy;Chiavari;corso Valparaiso 27, Chiavari, 16043, Italy;44.3173709;9.3151046;87;true;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Situated right on the seafront, this restaurant plunges its guests back in time with its polished wood, mirrors and classic decor giving it the feel of an English galleon. Mediterranean cuisine made from top-quality ingredients takes centre stage here, while the extensive wine list features some vintage labels. The American bar offering a good selection of cocktails is perfect for the winter months.;Great view;[]
10231;Macelleria Motta;Italy;Bellinzago Lombardo;strada Padana Superiore 90, Bellinzago Lombardo, 20060, Italy;45.5462837;9.4498531;64;false;false;Meats and Grills, Italian;Motta has established a reputation for quality, especially for its meat which is carefully sourced from farms in the Piedmont region. Some of the excellent options on the menu are aged in a large fridge near the entrance, along with different types of delicious salumi which are produced and cured by the restaurant. Various types of meat feature here – these are cured or cooked using classic methods with the occasional modern touch. Piedmontese beef is one of the highlights, with different cuts grilled on the barbecue or served boiled. Make sure you try the 300g hamburger with Aosta valley Toma cheese, BBQ sauce and caramelised onions served in a sesame-seed bun. Enjoy alfresco dining in a typical Lombardy courtyard in summer.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10232;Frosio;Italy;Almè;piazza Lemine 1, Almè, 24011, Italy;45.7400891;9.6150933;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a 18C villa which was once a family inn, this restaurant is run by the dynamic and professional Frosio family who have over 30 years’ experience in the restaurant business. There’s nothing improvised about Frosio, where Camillo guarantees impeccable service front of house and Paolo is at the helm in the kitchen, creating carefully prepared dishes with a classic-modern feel and an equal emphasis on meat and fish, often made from traditionally “gourmet” ingredients such as scampi, lobster, foie gras, pigeon and caviar. The wine list continues to offer an excellent selection, with one section dedicated to Italy and another to the rest of the world. Decorated with austere elegance, the wine cellar in the 13C tower is home to more than 1,000 different labels. Attractive outdoor space for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10233;Ristorante Mas-cì;Italy;Clusone;piazza Paradiso 1, Clusone, 24023, Italy;45.8896483;9.9446745;73;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Situated in the charming historic centre, this hotel and restaurant are now run by the third generation of the same family. Welcoming dining rooms with a fireplace provide the setting for cuisine which makes the most of local produce while also including dishes from elsewhere in Italy. Don’t miss the black truffle specialities!;Car park;[]
10234;Pantagruele;Italy;Brindisi;salita di Ripalta 1/5, Brindisi, 72100, Italy;40.63923;17.94697;90;true;false;Seafood;Situated in the town centre just a stone’s throw from the port, this small, typical trattoria is renowned for its delicious fish and seafood, including an excellent antipasto buffet and fresh fish cooked mainly on the grill. The large outdoor area is perfect for summer dining. Informal service.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10235;Locanda Gulfi;Italy;Chiaramonte Gulfi;Contrada Patria, Chiaramonte Gulfi, 97012, Italy;37.06754;14.680672;26;true;false;Sicilian;Situated in a secluded area of olive groves and vineyards, Locanda Gulfi also produces its own oil and wine, as confirmed by the view of the wine cellar from the dining room. The cuisine features an attractive selection of classic Sicilian dishes, while guestrooms are available for anyone keen to extend their stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10236;La Madia;Italy;Brione;via Aquilini 5, Brione, 25060, Italy;45.6385828;10.1483613;74;true;false;Lombardian;This authentic rural trattoria overlooking the valley and Franciacorta specialises in regional produce and typical Italian cuisine. Each dish on the menu lists the origin of the ingredients used, plus the name and address of the producer. Specialities include tagliolini pasta sautéed in a walnut sauce with tuna. Top quality cuisine offering excellent value for money.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10237;Carlo Magno;Italy;Collebeato;via Campiani 9, Collebeato, 25060, Italy;45.5748305;10.1904216;26;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant housed in a country house dating from the 19C offers elegant period dining rooms and a menu featuring Mediterranean-style meat and fish dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10238;Oblige;Italy;Vignola;Via Jacopo Barozzi 6, Vignola, 41058, Italy;44.4770216;11.0089734;87;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This new address with a cocktail bar and bistro (Noblesse) in the centre of historic Vignola is also home to a gourmet restaurant (Oblige), where chef Angelo serves easily identifiable yet technically skilful dishes. We recommend the game dishes cooked over the barbecue grill, such as the delicious local guinea fowl served with mustard mashed potato and sautéed radicchio. The wine list features labels from Italy and further afield with something suitable for every dish, including a few bottles that will appeal to wine connoisseurs.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10239;Pierre - Trattoria Sartoriale;Italy;Treviso;viale dei Mille 1/c, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.6655324;12.2544608;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated on the edge of the historic centre, this simple restaurant with just a few tables serves beautifully presented dishes. The menu features a limited number of options, all made with the best of whatever the market has available, and creatively prepared with little fuss and a focus on bringing out the ingredients’ full flavour.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10240;Podere Belvedere Tuscany;Italy;Pontassieve;via San Piero a Strada 23, Pontassieve, 50065, Italy;43.8228589;11.4601067;36;true;true;Tuscan, Creative;Occupying a tower house dating from 1700, this restaurant is surrounded by typical Tuscan scenery of olive groves and vineyards, as well as vegetable gardens and farms which produce many of the ingredients featuring in the dishes here. The friendly self-taught chef celebrates the best of Tuscan country cuisine, with a focus on meat, including grilled dishes and top-quality vegetables, as well as the occasional more creative dish – the result is cuisine of a very high standard. The restaurant also has a few guestrooms – a convenient option given the property’s attractive secluded location.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10241;Antica Farmacia;Italy;Palaia;via del Popolo 51, Palaia, 56036, Italy;43.6050076;10.7720725;52;false;false;Tuscan, Seasonal Cuisine;As its name suggests, this restaurant was used as a pharmacy until the late 1970s. In 2010, it was taken over by owner-chef Juri who now runs his own restaurant here, serving Tuscan-inspired cuisine made using local ingredients and recipes which he reinterprets with a light touch. Full of flavour, dishes include highlights such as baked marrow and Tuscan Chianti beef stew.;Air conditioning;[]
10242;Locanda San Michele;Italy;Montorio al Vomano;SS 491 3, Contrada Camerale di Tossiccia, Montorio al Vomano, 64046, Italy;42.5647767;13.6391665;67;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Practically on the slopes of Gran Sasso with views of the verdant landscapes of the Abruzzo, this restaurant is home to a local chef who has returned to his roots having spent time away gaining experience in Michelin-starred restaurants. Here, he serves regional cuisine with a modern, contemporary twist and a focus on meat and fish alike (examples include tuna tartare with strawberries finished in the dining room with lemon “snow”) in generous portions that are typical of the Abruzzo.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10243;[àbitat];Italy;San Fermo della Battaglia;via Henry Dunant 1, San Fermo della Battaglia, 22020, Italy;45.814;9.0315;76;true;true;Innovative;A young, enthusiastic and professional couple has taken over the reins at this modern and welcoming restaurant, serving cuisine that is inspired by a sustainable and seasonal approach. Ingredients include herbs harvested from their own garden, as well as typical produce from the mountains and the sea, all sourced from trusted suppliers who demonstrate full respect for nature and animals. Food waste is kept to a minimum to ensure a circular-based cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10244;La Porta Antica;Italy;Brescia;via Quarto dei Mille 16, Brescia, 25128, Italy;45.5483096;10.2200033;58;true;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Having gained experience elsewhere in Italy, especially in Liguria where he gained confidence preparing the best-quality fish and seafood, Augusto Valzelli has returned home to demonstrate his own modern approach to fish cuisine. Fish-lovers will delight in his “gran crudo di mare” (raw fish selection) which allows the quality of the fish – the restaurant’s main attraction – to shine through. If you want to order this particular dish, it’s best to mention it when booking.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10245;Parco Gambrinus;Italy;San Polo di Piave;via Capitello 18, San Polo di Piave, 31020, Italy;45.7967527;12.3886881;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;A rustic and romantic setting provides the backdrop for the traditional and creative cuisine served here. It is made from typical local produce with an emphasis on ethical and sustainably produced ingredients (vegan and gluten - free options are also available). Exotic animals inhabit the park, where a stream is home to the house specialities of crayfish, eels and sturgeon. The restaurant also offers a few comfortable guestrooms nearby.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10246;Taverna da Ciacco;Italy;San Quirico d'Orcia;via Dante Alighieri 30/a, San Quirico d'Orcia, 53027, Italy;43.0596966;11.6045275;69;false;true;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;A welcoming restaurant with a rustic feel. The owner - chef delights guests with his traditional yet imaginative delicacies, such as pici pasta with Pachino cherry tomatoes, garlic and chilli peppers and the renowned Chianina steak. Fish occasionally features on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
10247;Osteria del Mare già il "Votapentole";Italy;Castiglione della Pescaia;via IV Novembre 15, Castiglione della Pescaia, 58043, Italy;42.764017;10.8831779;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This charming restaurant right in the town centre boasts colourful decor and a lively, relaxed atmosphere. Fish and seafood from the nearby Mediterranean are served in imaginative dishes full of character, including highly recommended raw dishes and the popular “caciucco” (Tuscan fish stew).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10248;Ai Do Campanili;Italy;Cavallino;via Marco Polo 2, Cavallino, 30013, Italy;45.4656073;12.4563395;47;true;true;Seafood;Both the building in which it is housed and the dining room of this restaurant are on the small side, but the quality of the food more than compensates for the lack of space. Run by young and enthusiastic staff, the restaurant specialises in fish and seafood with raw options and modern dishes featuring on the menu. Excellent selection of wine, also available to take away.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10249;Osteria dai Coghi;Italy;Albarè di Costermano;via Alcide De Gasperi 9/13, Albarè di Costermano, 37010, Italy;45.5730306;10.7555283;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This well-kept, welcoming restaurant with a colourful decor and wine bottles adorning the walls serves imaginative dishes with modern combinations – our inspector particularly enjoyed the guinea fowl supreme with smoked black tea, carrots and beluga lentils. The well-chosen wine list features labels from Italy and further afield.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10250;Locanda dell'Arcimboldo;Italy;Coriano Veronese;via Gennari 5, Coriano Veronese, 37050, Italy;45.2760826;11.2871374;100;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seafood;At the town gates, a friendly inn with a family atmosphere in a fine building, with a pleasant veranda. Fish dishes prevail on the menu, featuring an interesting selection of oysters. At midday there is also an easier set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10251;Babette;Italy;Albenga;via Michelangelo 17, Albenga, 17031, Italy;44.0368952;8.2113613;99;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Ligurian;Situated just beyond the centre of Albenga in a beautiful location right on the beach (with only a small private beach club separating it from the sea), this restaurant has been in business for over 20 years (10 years on this site, and 10 in the town centre before that). It is renowned for its excellent, modern cuisine that focuses on top-quality, fresh and seasonal fish. A lighter (yet equally excellent) menu is also available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10252;Lu Pisantinu;Italy;Arzachena;viale Giovanni Maria Orecchioni snc, loc. Liscia di Vacca, Arzachena, 07021, Italy;41.1363679;9.5219499;36;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;A terrace framed by granite columns overlooks the coast and Porto Cervo at this restaurant, which is decorated in light shades and pastel tones echoing the colours of the sea. Imaginative fish cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10253;Agriturismo Il Cavallino;Italy;Semproniano;SP 55 Saturnia-Semproniano, località Fibbianello, Semproniano, 58055, Italy;42.6918653;11.5231198;16;false;true;Country cooking, Italian Contemporary;Situated in a very quiet and secluded location, this restaurant is run by an enthusiastic young couple: he has inherited the family business and, having gained experience in other restaurants in the region, is now at the helm in the kitchen, while his partner oversees the front of house. The options on the à la carte and wine list, the latter featuring a small yet impressive choice of wines, have a strong regional focus.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10254;Zur Kaiserkron;Italy;Bolzano;piazza della Mostra 1, Bolzano, 39100, Italy;46.4984779;11.353475;40;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Now under new management, this historic restaurant in the centre of Bolzano occupies the ground floor of the attractive Palazzo Pock overlooking the square. Here, elegant, contemporary-style dining rooms with charming vaulted ceilings provide the setting for Mediterranean-influenced cuisine with a distinctly contemporary flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10255;La Kucina;Italy;Foggia;via Giulio De Petra 67, Foggia, 71121, Italy;41.446014;15.5498279;80;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Grills;This modern, welcoming restaurant on the outskirts of town serves contemporary cuisine on a varied menu which also includes simpler options to suit all budgets, especially at lunchtime. In the dining room, a cabinet for ageing meat houses some excellent Iberian hams.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10256;Feria;Italy;Treviso;via della Quercia 8, Treviso, 31100, Italy;45.6694425;12.2198612;15;false;true;Indonesian, Fusion;Feria has two different spaces – a bistro-bar serving cocktails and street food, and a gourmet restaurant where chef Feltrin and his team showcase the full range of their culinary skills. The dishes here are colourful, full of flavour and carefully thought out, demonstrating Indonesian influences that recall the chef’s personal and professional experiences in this Asian country. Options include two tasting menus (a good starting point that allow you to appreciate the chef’s creativity to the full) and an à la carte. The excellent wine list is overseen by sommelier Régis Ramos who skilfully assists guests with their choices.;Wheelchair access;[]
10257;Coeur de Bois;Italy;Cogne;viale Cavagnet 31, Cogne, 11012, Italy;45.6091814;7.3538732;67;false;true;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Classic Cuisine;The name of this elegant restaurant was inspired by its wooden ceiling. Surrounded by spruce decor dating from the 18C, antique furniture and paintings, enjoy interesting traditional cuisine in this excellent gourmet restaurant, which is all the more attractive thanks to its location in the Gran Paradiso national park.;Garden or park,Great view;[]
10258;Michelasso;Italy;Naples;via Santa Brigida 14/16, Naples, 80132, Italy;40.8391919;14.2493909;99;false;false;Contemporary;Situated in the city centre, this refined restaurant with an elegantly classic decor is perfect for a romantic, intimate dinner. The menu features meat and fish, with traditional dishes reinterpreted thanks to the chef’s expertise and proven experience. In summer, choose a table on the pleasant outdoor space overlooking the lively Via Santa Brigida.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10259;Locanda di Nonna Ida;Italy;Marano di Valpolicella;Località Pontarola 12, Marano di Valpolicella, 37020, Italy;45.57248;10.91523;61;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian;A welcoming inn nestled amid the last vineyards of Valpolicella and the first pasturelands of the lower Lessinia region, where a young chef serves cuisine with a focus on local ingredients and classic Italian recipes with a modern twist. In summer, the terrace offers a fresh, cool setting with extensive views. The barbecued meat is superb.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10260;Cappuccini Cucina San Francesco;Italy;Cologne;via Cappuccini 54, Cologne, 25033, Italy;45.5940715;9.9387228;76;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Creative;Housed in the resort of the same name, this elegant restaurant is full of historic charm, enhanced by its white damask linen and beautiful candlesticks. The wine list pays obvious tribute to the famous Franciacorta region and also includes an excellent choice of champagnes, while the modern cuisine shows touches of traditional influence alongside more creative twists. Seasonal ingredients are to the fore here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10261;Locanda dei Cantù;Italy;Carona;piazza Vittorio Veneto 3, Carona, 24010, Italy;46.0202168;9.7822976;80;false;false;Country cooking;At the bottom of a steep valley, a rustic restaurant that offers fine cuisine, much appreciated in the area, with a great preference for local products. Old traditional recipes are revisited with a personal touch.;;[]
10262;Oltre.;Italy;Bologna;via Majani 1/b, Bologna, 40121, Italy;44.49698;11.33803;81;true;false;Emilian;This restaurant in the lively Mercato delle Erbe district has an entrance adorned with hundreds of stickers, giving it the appearance of a record shop rather than a contemporary-style eatery with a bar counter and a highly original surfboard table near the entrance. The modern cuisine has its roots in the region yet also includes skilfully prepared dishes from around the world. There’s also a choice of cocktails to start or round off your meal. Booking is highly recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
10263;Villa Pignano;Italy;Volterra;località Pignano 6, Volterra, 56048, Italy;43.4165316;10.9615533;81;false;true;Contemporary, Tuscan;A veritable Garden of Eden just 15km from Volterra, this 300ha estate is home to a restaurant with a strong zero-mile philosophy. This is backed up by its careful use of ingredients grown or produced on the estate itself, such as vegetables, olives and grains, as well as chicken, pork and honey – a sustainable approach that results in delicious, contemporary cuisine. The dishes here are fresh and full of flavour yet elaborate and modern in style (note the simpler menu at lunchtime). The interesting wine list explores Tuscany through its choice of top-quality organic labels as well as including wines produced from the estate’s own vines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10264;Mater Bistrot;Italy;Milan;via Pasquale Sottocorno 1, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.4654461;9.2076996;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;An informal bistro where the imaginative cuisine prepared by the owner-chef showcases the best Italian recipes while remaining open to influences from other parts of the world, resulting in strong, unique and captivating flavours. Guests also have the option of smaller dishes to share, but if you really want to get to know the essence of this restaurant, it’s best to go for the guided menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10265;Locanda Stella d'Oro;Italy;Soragna;via Mazzini 8, Soragna, 43019, Italy;44.9284623;10.1244937;50;false;true;Emilian;The original flavour and magic of a trattoria can still be found in this establishment. The cuisine is traditional with a personal touch.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10266;Osteria dell'Arco;Italy;Alba;piazza Michele Ferrero 5, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.697;8.0345512;32;true;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Enjoy a warm family welcome at this centrally located restaurant with an internal courtyard, where the menu features a good choice of traditional and authentic dishes full of flavour. The restaurant is run by the same friendly managers as the renowned and popular Boccondivino in Bra, where the Slow Food concept was born. Booking ahead is always a good option.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10267;Andree;Italy;La Spezia;via San Martino della Battaglia 16, La Spezia, 19121, Italy;44.1046382;9.8202609;20;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant in the centre of Spezia boasts a striking open-view kitchen in its small brick-vaulted dining room. Modern cuisine with a focus on superb fish dishes, accompanied by professional service and a wine list full of character.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10268;Tre Scalini;Italy;Novara;via Sottile 23, Novara, 28100, Italy;45.449049;8.6102929;95;true;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;The menu at this restaurant features meat and seasonal ingredients served in personalised recipes and contemporary-style dishes. There are also three tasting menus: the main one consists of eight courses prepared by the talented chef. The restaurant brings to mind a modern bistro with its warm ambience and attentive service.;Air conditioning;[]
10269;Le Nove Scodelle;Italy;Milan;viale Monza 4, Milan, 20127, Italy;45.4873742;9.2171657;70;false;false;Chinese, Sichuan;Now available everywhere in Italy, ethnic cuisine is gradually becoming more specialised, as is the case in this restaurant serving specialities from the province of Szechuan in south-west China. Exciting and original cuisine full of spicy flavours.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10270;La Locanda di Fabio e Vale;Italy;Offanengo;via Brescia 1, Offanengo, 26010, Italy;45.3791324;9.7471882;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Young, informal and friendly owners Fabio and Vale welcome guests to their restaurant in Offanengo, just a few kilometres from Crema. A good choice for anyone keen to sample moderately creative cuisine, including a good selection of fish-based dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10271;Casa Coloni;Italy;Paestum;via Tavernelle 86, Paestum, 84047, Italy;40.4267989;15.0022711;22;false;true;Contemporary, Campanian;Situated opposite the archaeological site, this restaurant occupies an old farmhouse which is part of a splendid 19C residence converted into an elegant hotel following a long and meticulous restoration. In fine weather, tables are set out under a cane pergola in a charming setting in the romantic garden. Here, the chef from Paestum serves his own reinterpretations of regional dishes with superb results. Impeccable service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10272;Ad Astra;Italy;Santa Maria della Versa;via Cavour 11/13, Santa Maria della Versa, 27047, Italy;44.9870931;9.3001821;23;false;true;Contemporary;This small yet smart restaurant in the Oltrepò Pavese region is a dream come true for owner-chef Alessandro Folli, whose cuisine shows the influence of his experience working in different restaurants around Europe. Ad Astra delights guests with dishes which demonstrate a perfect balance between modern and classic culinary styles. Bravo!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10274;Azotea;Italy;Turin;via Maria Vittoria 49/b, Turin, 10123, Italy;45.0636339;7.6949405;57;true;true;Peruvian, Japanese;Situated in a central location with a small outdoor space, this restaurant boasts a striking interior with old walls, a verdant decor and climbing plants that add a South American feel. The cuisine shines the spotlight on the chef’s native Peru, with appetisers such as potted umbrine tacos and delicious yet atypical antipasti such as raw squid with saltwort and peas. Soy sauce, umeboshi, and yuyo seaweed sauce provide added exotic flavour. We highly recommend one of the excellent cocktails, such as the slightly sour Americano with yuzu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10275;Terrazza Tiberio;Italy;Capri;via Croce 11, Capri, 80073, Italy;40.5510647;14.2466467;82;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Housed on the first floor of the Tiberio hotel, this elegant restaurant boasts a terrace overlooking the rooftops of Capri. The regional and island specialities on the menu leave a lasting memory, such as the “montanara” (fried pizza), “casatiello” (a savoury bread from Naples) and the caprese-style ravioli, although more creative options also feature, especially among the desserts. All in all, an elegant dining experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10276;Cracco Portofino;Italy;Portofino;Molo Umberto I 9, Portofino, 16034, Italy;44.302429;9.2103994;92;false;true;Seafood, Contemporary;Famous chef Carlo Cracco has opened a restaurant in what was once Il Pitosforo, right opposite the small harbour in Portofino, so that his lucky guests enjoy fine views of the water, the small square and the enchanting bay. Here, skilful and competent executive chef Mattia Pecis serves lightly modern cuisine with occasional references to Ligurian recipes (such as cappon magro salad) and ingredients (many of the vegetables are sourced from Iva’s kitchen garden on the hills nearby), with a new cooling cabinet in which fish are “aged”. The delightful terrace, open in summer from 6.30pm onwards, is the perfect setting for alfresco aperitifs and dinners.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10277;KELINA Fine Dine;Italy;Corvara in Badia;Strada Lech de Boà s.n., Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.5268226;11.8623869;72;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;From Corvara, take the ultra-modern Boè cable-car to this restaurant (accessible also on skis or by foot) which is one of the dining options at the Piz Boè Alpine Lounge (for access, turn right as you exit the cable car). Open at lunchtime only, KELINA serves unexpectedly gourmet cuisine in a minimalist-style dining room which allows the stunning views of Sassongher, Santa Croce and La Varella to take centre-stage through the restaurant’s large floor-to-ceiling windows. There’s a restricted choice of dishes, all of which are creative and based on Alpine ingredients, with a new, highly experienced chef at the helm since early 2024. An excellent wine list completes the picture.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10278;Chalet Gerard;Italy;Selva di Val Gardena;via Plan de Gralba 37, Selva di Val Gardena, 39048, Italy;46.5366668;11.7791315;73;true;true;Country cooking, Creative;In a breathtakingly beautiful natural setting between the Sassolungo peak and the majestic Sella mountains, this restaurant serves simple mountain fare alongside a few more modern dishes, all of which are prepared from typical ingredients from the Alto Adige. Although you can’t book at lunchtime, bookings are required in the evening. Beautiful guestrooms are also available.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10279;Casa della Rocca;Italy;Dolcedo;via Ripalta 3, Dolcedo, 18020, Italy;43.9074746;7.9487091;67;false;true;Ligurian, Creative;Situated in picturesque Dolcedo, this restaurant occupies an early 20C mill complete with millstone and press. The cuisine focuses on an interesting selection of traditional Ligurian dishes with a satisfying balance of meat and fish (occasionally on the same plate), plus creative touches and hints of the Piedmont, all of which combine to make a trip to this inland restaurant well worth while!;Terrace;[]
10280;Pellico 3;Italy;Milan;via Silvio Pellico 3, Milan, 20121, Italy;45.4655602;9.1889938;42;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated in the luxury Park Hyatt hotel just a few metres from the Galleria Vittorio Emanuele, this restaurant is home to a young chef who serves elegant and occasionally complex cuisine. His dishes include sauces and traditions learned from his time working in France, as well as plenty of vegetables and Mediterranean influences.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10281;Masseria Moroseta;Italy;Ostuni;Contrada Lamacavallo, Ostuni, 72017, Italy;40.7384409;17.6113501;67;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Chef Giorgia Eugenia Goggi offers a unique and authentic gastronomic experience that focuses on fresh ingredients (mostly vegetables), many of which are sourced from small organic gardens. The 90€ menu celebrates Mediterranean cuisine to the full, with colourful dishes that are full of flavour and in which the freshness of the ingredients is allowed to shine through. The beautifully kept, rustic dining room provides an ideal setting for an unforgettable dinner, while the selection of natural Italian wines offers the perfect accompaniment to the chef’s dishes, further enhancing your dining experience. There are six comfortable guestrooms available should you wish to extend your stay and immerse yourself in these peaceful rural surroundings. Booking in advance is highly recommended given the restaurant’s popularity and unique appeal.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10282;Trattoria Margherita;Italy;Arborea;corso Roma 31, Arborea, 09092, Italy;39.7753123;8.5824987;22;false;true;Sardinian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Don’t be fooled by the relatively simple ambience of this trattoria which is situated in the centre of a town with an interesting history linked to the reclamation of the marshes and the dairy industry. Dedicated to the owner’s two grandmothers, the restaurant serves some of Sardinia’s best-known meat and fish specialities.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10283;Belvedere;Italy;Porto Cervo;località Farina, Porto Cervo, 07021, Italy;41.0960486;9.5287226;45;true;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Over the years, this family restaurant has become one of the most popular along this coastline. An informal dining room provides the backdrop for the decidedly Mediterranean cuisine served here, where the focus is the fish display cabinet that changes daily and from which guests can make their choice. The friendly and professional approach of the two brothers that run the restaurant has contributed to its success, while the brand-new terrace-lounge, with its stunning view, is the perfect spot for an aperitif or after-dinner drink.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10284;Millo Ristorante;Italy;Santa Teresa Gallura;via Garibaldi 4, Santa Teresa Gallura, 07028, Italy;41.2428918;9.1897674;54;true;false;Sardinian, Traditional Cuisine;An attractive restaurant serving reasonably priced fish and seafood (try the delicious squid with an orange and chicory sauce). There’s also a charming summer terrace from which to watch the town’s bustling nightlife.;Terrace;[]
10285;Amanõ;Italy;Cagliari;via Sidney Sonnino 68, Cagliari, 09125, Italy;39.2130873;9.1191723;71;false;true;Contemporary;The tilde accent over the “o” in the name of this restaurant is a subtle allusion to the sea that lies between Campania (the chef’s native region) and Sardinia (his adopted home). With just a few tables and an open-view kitchen, the dining room here is adorned with hand-made decorations, hence the name of the restaurant (“a mano” means “by hand”). The chef makes full use of Sardinian ingredients in his elaborate and creative cuisine, so this is a good choice for anyone seeking a change from traditional fare.;Air conditioning;[]
10286;Bistrot Royal;Italy;Courmayeur;via Roma 87, Courmayeur, 11013, Italy;45.7891036;6.9731865;98;true;false;Alpine, Regional Cuisine;In the refined rooms of Grand Hotel Royal e Golf, the dining room with its glass wall looks like a stage overlooking the chain of Monte Bianco and Dente del Gigante. The gastronomic proposal is one of the most appealing in the area: creative rather than local, the dishes are refined and technically elaborate.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10287;Ai Porteghi Bistrot;Italy;Padua;via Cesare Battisti 105, Padua, 35121, Italy;45.4062379;11.8810599;17;false;true;Contemporary;Situated under the picturesque arcades on Via Cesare Battisti, this restaurant is home to a young chef whose cuisine is inspired by traditional and well-known recipes which he reinterprets with his own personal touch to create highly interesting dishes. Simpler and more reasonably priced options are also available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10288;Stilla;Italy;Colognola ai Colli;Località Casette 1, Colognola ai Colli, 37030, Italy;45.4246544;11.2071958;17;true;true;Contemporary;Run by an enthusiastic and committed young couple who left the big city to restore the family home and transform it into an elegant, welcoming restaurant, Stilla stands in a tranquil location surrounded by vineyards. Here, Silvia creates original, generous and colourful cuisine which is showcased on an à la carte with just a few dishes which change regularly. We particularly enjoyed the freshly seared bonito served with wild spinach, sour cherries and a cherry barbecue sauce. Meals are served on the outdoor terrace in summer. Accommodation is also available in five beautiful yet functional guestrooms. Well worth a visit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10289;Cocun Cellar Restaurant;Italy;San Cassiano;strada Prè de Vì 31, San Cassiano, 39036, Italy;46.560614;11.9571789;86;true;false;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;At this restaurant within the elegant Ciasa Salares hotel, guests dine in a wine cellar with a pleasantly informal and friendly atmosphere. In addition to the excellent cuisine, the fine cheese selection comes highly recommended, as does a visit to the room dedicated entirely to chocolate.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10290;Oltremare;Italy;Maiori;via Diego Taiani 3, Maiori, 84010, Italy;40.644876;14.6475241;43;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;Situated on the fifth floor of the Due Torri hotel, the restaurant has recently been refurbished, giving it an even more charming and atmospheric feel than before. The cuisine is creative in style, almost always using ingredients and recipes from Campania as its inspiration – a good example is the many different ways tomato is used, including tomato water distilled in an alembic still. Chef Alfonso Crisci’s recipes are complex and always full of different ingredients and colours, with a selection of delicious and generous desserts to finish your meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10291;Remulass;Italy;Milan;via Nino Bixio 21, Milan, 20129, Italy;45.47234;9.209951;88;false;true;Modern Cuisine;“Cooking with roots” is the mantra at Remulass, a phrase that has inspired the restaurant’s name (“wild radish” in the local Milanese dialect). This small, lively restaurant gets very busy in the evenings when booking is highly recommended. The attractively modern and colourful dishes here always feature plenty of root vegetables and aromatic herbs. We recommend the fermented vegetables with baked ricotta and a gin dressing.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10292;Pentole e Provette;Italy;Fasano;Via Musco 37, Fasano, 72015, Italy;40.8365964;17.3618341;56;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant run by Luca Trabalzini and his partner Rossella is a real gem in the small town of Fasano. Their story, which began in Australia, adds a fascinating touch to this gastronomic project. The atmosphere here is warm and lively, making this the perfect setting in which to enjoy the chef’s innovative cuisine, which he showcases on three distinct menus dedicated to meat, fish and vegetarian dishes respectively. Luca’s cuisine is modern and elegant, with particular attention paid to flavours and textures so that each and every dish offers a fully rounded sensorial experience.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10293;Urubamba;Italy;Naples;via Gaetano Filangieri 16/c, Naples, 80121, Italy;40.8361738;14.2406752;98;false;false;Fusion;Situated amid luxury boutiques and historic palazzi in one of Naples’ most exclusive districts, this restaurant boasts a chic and romantic dining room with soft lighting on the first floor, as well as an exclusive outdoor terrace for fine weather. The cuisine is totally in keeping with the trendy setting, featuring a successful combination of two different gastronomic cultures (namely Peruvian and Japanese) that blend together perfectly.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10294;L'Agave;Italy;Framura;località Chiama, Framura, 19014, Italy;44.1999789;9.5570426;98;true;false;Ligurian;Perched on the cliff overlooking the small port of Framura, the terraces at this restaurant boast one of the most stunning views in the area. The dishes served up by the young chef are a declaration of his love for Liguria (as is the wine list), featuring a remarkable selection of top-quality regional ingredients such as artichokes and asparagus from Albenga, beans from Pigna, pine nuts, prebugiun (a mixture of wild plants), Taggiasca olives and of course local fish and seafood.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10295;San Tommaso 10;Italy;Turin;via San Tommaso 10, Turin, 10122, Italy;45.0709541;7.68178;21;true;true;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;In 1895 Luigi Lavazza opened here a grocery store where he immediately began blending coffee. 129 years later the place hosts a modern restaurant with a superb kitchen run by a chef who, despite hailing from the Marche region, treats guests to one of the most authentic interpretations of Piedmontese cuisine in the city, often with a creative touch. Among the options on offer here, the trolley of antipasti is a must.;Air conditioning;[]
10296;Il Tempo Nuovo;Italy;Ugento;via Castello 13, Ugento, 73059, Italy;39.9294116;18.1618541;64;true;true;Contemporary, Apulian;Now occupied by a charming boutique hotel, the Castello di Ugento is also home to this restaurant where the Puglian chef reinterprets the traditions of Salento in contemporary dishes that feature an array of meat, fish and vegetables. The staff will be more than happy to recommend the best accompaniment to your meal, whether this is a good wine from the plentiful wine list or a delicious cocktail.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10297;Zanze XVI;Italy;Venice;fondamenta dei Tolentini, sestiere Santa Croce 231, Venice, 30135, Italy;45.4388376;12.3212634;52;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Although the setting and convivial atmosphere in this restaurant recall that of a typical Venetian bàcaro , the cuisine is completely different in feel. The ingredients are sourced from the best markets and local producers, resulting in unique dishes that reflect the culinary traditions of the lagoon and its surrounding area. The few tables arranged outdoors with views of the tranquil canal add to the appeal, while the professional yet friendly service helps to put guests completely at ease.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10298;Principe di Belludia;Italy;Noto;contrada Belludia sp 51, Noto, 96017, Italy;36.8448679;15.0018149;69;true;false;Creative;The Principe di Belludia is the gourmet restaurant at the Il San Corrado di Noto hotel, a luxurious resort in a secluded rural location with two enormous swimming pools. The new executive chef Martin Lazarov showcases his love for Sicily, with a particular attention to vegetables dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10299;SOMS;Italy;Pescara;via Piave 61, Pescara, 65122, Italy;42.4713925;14.2067878;81;false;false;Cuisine from Abruzzo, Contemporary;Situated in a pedestrianised area of the old town, the historic “società operaia di mutuo soccorso” (SOMS – a workers’ mutual aid association) has been transformed into a bright, welcoming restaurant where the chef creates dishes influenced by the traditions of the Abruzzi yet decidedly original in style (barbecued dishes are one of the specialities). Classic decor, plus a pleasant outdoor space for alfresco dining in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10300;Cut;Italy;Caravaggio;via Amilcare Bietti 28, Caravaggio, 24043, Italy;45.49439;9.63953;46;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Situated right in the heart of the Bergamo plain in the small town of Caravaggio, famous for the painter of the same name and for a much-visited pilgrim shrine, this welcoming restaurant boasts a modern decor and vintage furnishings. At lunchtime, it serves a good, competitively priced business menu, while in the evening the more elaborate à la carte features contemporary-style meat and fish dishes (mostly the latter).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10301;Maragoncello;Italy;Montichiari;via San Giovanni 1, località Vighizzolo, Montichiari, 25018, Italy;45.4268188;10.367252;40;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in a small village in the Bassa Bresciana region, this restaurant comes as something of a surprise due to its focus on fish, with the selection of raw seafood options and the good-value-for-money tasting menu particular highlights. Personalised cuisine which is full of flavour, served in modern, convivial dining rooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10302;Anastasia;Italy;Civitanova Marche;via Bainsizza 3, Civitanova Marche, 62012, Italy;43.3035996;13.7354778;95;true;true;Seafood;This cocktail bar on the seafront is also a restaurant specialising in fresh fish served in a selection of classic dishes (such as tartare) and more elaborate recipes. The dining room is modern and spacious, plus there’s an outdoor terrace for alfresco dining in fine weather. Guestrooms and luxury apartments are also available (swimming pool on the roof).;Terrace;[]
10303;Qualia;Italy;Cefalu;via Giovanni Amendola 16/b, Cefalu, 90015, Italy;38.0381222;14.0211888;35;false;true;Italian, Sicilian;Situated in a side street in the centre of this charming small town, this restaurant boasts a dining room with exposed brickwork and glimpses of the kitchen, plus a small outdoor space with a few tables for alfresco dining. The dishes here are full of flavour and focus on regional ingredients and fresh fish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10304;Al Moro;Italy;Marina Di Campo;via Pietri 1277, Marina Di Campo, 57034, Italy;42.7431631;10.2192624;46;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated away from the main tourist area, in a rustic building that is striking for its attractive outdoor space shaded by a wooden gazebo, this restaurant boasts an informal and relaxing atmosphere. The Mediterranean cuisine is full of character and prepared with top-quality ingredients, including a small selection of oysters.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10305;Li Somari;Italy;Tivoli;Piazza Rivarola 21, Tivoli, 00010, Italy;41.9655435;12.7994909;62;true;true;Cuisine from Lazio, Traditional Cuisine;Transferred to piazza Rivarola 21, Tivoli.Adriano Baldassarre’s small, intimate restaurant is situated in historic Tivoli, which is renowned for its fascinating history and Hadrian’s Villa. Popular with food-lovers, the restaurant serves delicacies such as oxtail ravioli and tripe, with a whole page of the menu dedicated to offal dishes, as well as panzanella and char by Alessandro Narducci, the latter paying tribute to a chef friend of Baldassare’s. A few tables set out on the promenade provide outdoor dining options, while the restaurant’s sustainable approach to dining is explained at the top of the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10306;Cala Luna;Italy;Cefalu;via Vincenzo Cavallaro 12, Cefalu, 90015, Italy;38.0336752;14.037633;87;false;false;Contemporary, Sicilian;The elegant fine-dining restaurant at Le Calette boutique hotel, Cala Luna boasts an attractive dining room (Rizz'i Mari) where meals are served in low season, as well as an open-air garden on Via Presidiana for summer dining where, just like the dining room, the views take in the Caldura rocks and the La Rocca outcrop, albeit from a slightly different perspective. Chef Dario Pandolfo uses creative techniques acquired during his time working at renowned restaurants, which he applies to Sicilian ingredients and traditions. The result is exciting and colourful cuisine which is creative and full of Mediterranean flavours.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10307;Antiche Carampane;Italy;Venice;rio Terà delle Carampane, sestiere San Polo 1911, Venice, 30125, Italy;45.4386687;12.3310933;15;true;false;Venetian;From the typical flooring to the decoration on the walls, the warm and appealing decor in this restaurant highlights its historic feel, providing a setting to which guests happily return time after time. The local fish and seafood specialities served here include sarde in saor (sardines), salted cod, fried soft-shell crab and cuttlefish in black ink – skilfully prepared dishes which remain faithful to traditional recipes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10308;Phi Restaurant - Giancarlo Morelli;Italy;Baia Sardinia;località Forte Cappellini, Baia Sardinia, 07021, Italy;41.1423061;9.4673947;47;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Glamour and fashion are the hallmarks of this restaurant in Phi Beach, one of the most attractive nightclub-cum-lounge bars on the Costa Smeralda. Take a seat on the terrace right by the water and soak up the romantic sunsets and sea views as you enjoy Italian and Mediterranean dishes created by a famous chef from Lombardy who adds just the right touch of contemporary flavour. Also open for lunch, with some of the evening menu dishes available alongside an array of simpler options.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10309;Lanzani Bottega & Bistrot;Italy;Brescia;via Albertano da Brescia 41, Brescia, 25127, Italy;45.5482028;10.1793875;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;This modern restaurant (open from 7am to 11pm), once the family butcher’s, also acts as a delicatessen and wine boutique. Full restaurant service in the evening with simpler dishes and a more restricted choice at lunchtime. Situated some distance from the centre.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10310;Clandestino Susci Bar;Italy;Portonovo;Baia di Portonovo, Portonovo, 60020, Italy;43.5654162;13.5918668;41;false;true;Creative, Seafood;Built on stilts, the Clandestino is a unique restaurant with a simple yet trendy ambience, which overlooks a beautiful unspoilt beach with views of the sea from all the windows and a distinctly romantic feel at night. Here, Moreno Cedroni focuses on gourmet cuisine at lunchtime as well as in the evening. In addition to two tasting menus (Eros & Susci and Susci Memories), for lunch there’s a small à la carte.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10311;La Conchiglia;Italy;Arma di Taggia;Lungomare 33, Arma di Taggia, 18011, Italy;43.830084;7.8485144;53;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This small restaurant with a vaulted ceiling provides the setting for dishes that have by now become classics thanks to their focus on top-quality ingredients. The cuisine is light and simple rather than bold and elaborate, with a focus on bringing out the full flavour of the fish (a few meat dishes are also available). If you’re keen to learn more about Ligurian gastronomic specialities, take time between courses to chat with the friendly owner, who has an impressive knowledge of the region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10312;Le Petit Bellevue;Italy;Cogne;rue Grand Paradis 22, Cogne, 11012, Italy;45.6067309;7.3556842;77;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Cuisine from the Aosta Valley;Situated in one of the region’s most famous and romantic hotels, this small gem of a restaurant offers just a few seats at period-style tables in a small dining room, in addition to two tables with scenic views of the valley and Gran Paradiso. Here, the Tuscan chef focuses on specialities from the Aosta Valley, including popular dishes such as Lillaz char with roe and a butter sauce, and “zuppa del bosco” (stewed seasonal mushrooms served with Aosta blue cheese and a pinch of fresh marjoram), followed by an extraordinary cheese trolley that focuses on regional specialities. Last but not least, talented sommelier Rino Billia (a previous winner of the “passion for wine” award) demonstrates skilful understanding of guests’ requirements as he chooses the most suitable wine for them out of the more than 1 600 labels on the wine list.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10313;L'Argaj;Italy;Castiglione Falletto;via Alba-Monforte 114, Castiglione Falletto, 12060, Italy;44.622997;7.974684;48;true;false;Creative;In the Piedmontese dialect, “Argaj” translates as “satisfaction” and never has a restaurant name seemed more appropriate! In a simple, colourful and welcoming dining room with windows looking out at the hills, all the attention is on cuisine which is skilfully balanced between classic local dishes and more creative options. Choose between the à la carte and tasting menus, all accompanied by an excellent array of wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10314;Oste Scuro - Finsterwirt;Italy;Brixen;vicolo del Duomo 3, Brixen, 39042, Italy;46.7157558;11.6565447;27;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Run by the capable Mayr family, this long-established restaurant has occupied a narrow alleyway in the centre of Bressanone (Brixen) since the late 19C. The dining rooms are decorated in historic style, plus there’s a charming terrace for alfresco dining in summer. Dishes are presented on different tasting menus with the option of choosing traditional or Mediterranean dishes à la carte style – we highly recommend the soup made with Sylvaner wine from the Isarco valley, as well as the Tirtl (fried pie) stuffed with ricotta, spinach and cinnamon. Guestrooms are available in the nearby and recently renovated Adler Historic Guesthouse, which is run by the same owners.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10315;Gardenia;Italy;Caluso;corso Torino 9, Caluso, 10014, Italy;45.3034572;7.8896044;48;true;false;Piedmontese, Modern Cuisine;Even if you’re not a local, you’ll feel at home in this old property which offers a glimpse of the Piedmont of old. In this 19C building, with a typical balcony running along the inner courtyard, the atmosphere continues into the dining room and, of course, via the dishes on the menu. Here, regional cuisine is celebrated to the full, so you’ll find lots of meat (although some fish options are also available), accompanied by a carefully selected choice of vegetables, some grown in the restaurant’s own garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10316;Il Portico;Italy;Appiano Gentile;piazza Libertà 36, Appiano Gentile, 22070, Italy;45.733696;8.979538;34;true;true;Farm to table;Chef Lopriore returns to his native region with this new restaurant which offers an original format – the lunchtime menu focuses on single course options, while in the evening the tasting menus comprise an interesting combination of imaginative fish, meat and vegetable dishes which can be combined as you wish. Cuisine with an emphasis on seasonal market ingredients where locally sourced produce takes pride of place.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10317;85 Bistrot;Italy;Sesto San Giovanni;piazza Martiri di Via Fani 85, Sesto San Giovanni, 20099, Italy;45.5342494;9.2306544;58;true;true;Lombardian, Italian;This simple, modern, family-run trattoria with a welcoming ambience is the kind of restaurant that everyone would love to have as their local. The owner-chef, who has plenty of experience working in Milanese restaurants, is a real culinary expert who creates traditional dishes from Milan but also from further afield. Here, the popular breaded cutlet is served thick so that the delicate flavour of the veal can be enjoyed to the full.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10318;Strattoria;Italy;Montrigiasco;Piazza Angelo Gnemmi, Montrigiasco, 28041, Italy;45.7715102;8.5130006;28;true;true;Contemporary;Situated in the foothills around Lake Maggiore, this colourful and welcoming restaurant has a pleasantly relaxed ambience. The skilful chef creates cuisine inspired by the region (as well as further afield) that showcases top-quality ingredients, including dishes such as veal tongue with barbecued prawns and carrots. An interesting wine list and friendly service complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10319;Belé;Italy;Milan;via Angelo Fumagalli 3, Milan, 20143, Italy;45.450007;9.1702014;99;true;false;Italian Contemporary;The name says it all – in Milanese dialect, “belé” means beautiful and the word is an apt description of this restaurant. Belé is charmingly lit by an old-fashioned chandelier on which the pieces of crystal create a play of light resembling an intricate and shifting lace-like pattern. The dining rooms are decorated in attractive contemporary colours, with comfortable armchairs and acoustics perfect for conversation, while the cuisine is Italian with a modern twist.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10320;Pietramare Natural Food;Italy;Isola di Capo Rizzuto;SS 106, loc. Praialonga,, Isola di Capo Rizzuto, 88841, Italy;38.93424;16.9935;38;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;In an elegant setting of dry-stone walls and Mediterranean vegetation, this stylish restaurant boasts personalised decor right down to the smallest detail. The new chef prepares modern dishes inspired by the region and more generally by southern Italy, with a menu that focuses on fish rather than meat, as well as a vegetarian menu. There’s also a charming cigar room with small lounge areas and a fireplace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10321;Salamensa;Italy;Montichiari;via Monsignor Oscar Romero 29, Montichiari, 25018, Italy;45.4157774;10.4012442;29;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;A multi-function open space, with a bar for breakfasts and a classic restaurant serving pizzas made from naturally fermented dough. Although the ambience is modern, friendly and minimalist, the attention paid to the choice of ingredients and preparation of dishes is of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10322;Café Quinson;Italy;Morgex;piazza Principe Tomaso 10, Morgex, 11017, Italy;45.75689;7.03578;54;false;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Regional Cuisine;The Café Quinson has reopened! In this rustic yet elegant “mountain restaurant”, the whole family makes guests feel welcome, serving a selection of regional dishes with an imaginative and contemporary touch. Excellent choice of wines, almost all of which are available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10323;La Botte;Italy;Stresa;via Giuseppe Garibaldi 8, Stresa, 28838, Italy;45.8835969;8.5410813;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A modern and welcoming contemporary bistro situated in the heart of Stresa’s historic centre. Run by an entire family, the restaurant serves modern and imaginative fish and meat dishes where the focus is always on seasonal ingredients. The interesting wine list also includes a selection of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10324;Gennaro Di Pace;Italy;Monforte d'Alba;vicolo della Chiesa 8, loc. Perno, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.6119183;7.9755322;25;false;false;Italian, Contemporary;The owner-chef’s Calabrian origins are evident on a menu that combines Mediterranean cuisine (including fish and seafood) with Piedmontese specialities and showcases beautifully presented dishes prepared using contemporary techniques. This small modern restaurant situated near Perno castle is also open at lunchtime (by prior reservation only).;Air conditioning;[]
10325;Essentia;Italy;Castrocaro Terme;piazza San Nicolò 2, Castrocaro Terme, 47011, Italy;44.1713217;11.9468717;46;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated at the foot of the fortress in the historic centre of Castrocaro, this restaurant has an interesting young chef at the helm, Andrea Giacchini. The cuisine often (but not always) has a local influence and demonstrates remarkable technical expertise that is neither overly ostentatious nor an end in itself, but rather a way of skilfully showcasing the top-quality ingredients used.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10326;San Martino 26;Italy;San Gimignano;via San Martino 26, San Gimignano, 53037, Italy;43.4699456;11.0419316;41;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;Occupying the wine cellars of an old palazzo in the historic centre, this restaurant has a fashionable feel with just a few tables and a selection of contemporary - style dishes inspired by classic recipes (from Tuscany and elsewhere) on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10327;Da Cecco;Italy;Torre del Lago Puccini;piazza Belvedere Puccini 10/12, Torre del Lago Puccini, 55049, Italy;43.83215;10.306611;65;false;true;Tuscan;A cosylittle restaurant at the beginning of the lakefront. Mainly seafood dishes, though in the winter there is also game. Rustic atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10328;Trippini;Italy;Civitella del Lago;via Italia 14, Civitella del Lago, 05023, Italy;42.7107716;12.2812758;70;true;true;Umbrian, Contemporary;Just a few tables and spectacular views of Lake Corbara characterise this restaurant, which has been run by the same family since 1964. The delicious cuisine is regional in flavour, showcasing home-cooked recipes and typical Sunday favourites yet with a contemporary twist that incorporates plenty of intense flavours.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
10329;Osteria Taviani;Italy;Bientina;piazza Vittorio Emanuele II 28, Bientina, 56031, Italy;43.7103695;10.6189082;97;false;true;Tuscan, Modern Cuisine;This pleasant, warmly decorated restaurant is run with passion and enthusiasm by Elena and Alessandro, the former supervising the front of house, the latter at the helm in the kitchen. The cuisine here is modern and full of flavour, with a focus on meat dishes (although a few fish options also feature) with their roots firmly anchored in Tuscan traditions (such as the fried steak). During the hunting season, the contemporary-style game dishes are particularly delicious. The wine list includes a few French labels.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10330;Il Labirinto;Italy;Brescia;via Corsica 224, Brescia, 25125, Italy;45.5230057;10.1959907;68;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the outskirts of Brescia, this long-established restaurant has an elegant retro atmosphere. The cuisine is varied with a balance of fish and meat dishes, as well as some excellent home-made salumi.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10331;Lou Ressignon;Italy;Cogne;via des Mines 22, Cogne, 11012, Italy;45.6077032;7.3593237;47;true;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Classic Cuisine;A pleasant family trattoria which has been in business since 1966, this restaurant serves simple and authentic cuisine which showcases the products of the Aosta Valley, as well as excellent meat, most of which comes from outside Italy. In addition to the first-floor dining room, there’s also a historic taverna, while four welcoming guestrooms are available for anyone wishing to extend their stay.;Car park;[]
10332;Daniela;Italy;San Casciano dei Bagni;piazza Matteotti 7, San Casciano dei Bagni, 53040, Italy;42.871054;11.875456;23;true;false;Tuscan;Just a little under 100m from the Sette Querce hotel and situated opposite a lovely viewpoint, this restaurant is housed in the castle’s old stables. The vaulted ceilings and old stone create a charming ambience, while the excellent local cuisine will definitely appeal to the palate.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10333;L'Osteria del Castellazzo;Italy;Salsomaggiore Terme;via Borgo Castellazzo 40, Salsomaggiore Terme, 43039, Italy;44.815369;9.9787597;15;false;true;Country cooking;The determined and enthusiastic young owner of this restaurant graduated with a literature degree before giving in to her passion for food. She swapped her pen for a ladle and now creates delicious local specialities such as braised veal cheeks, alongside dishes from Pïacenza and Mantua, such as pisarei (a type of gnocchi) and sbrisolona cake.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10334;Pescarino-Sapori di Terra e di Mare;Italy;Montemarcello;via Borea 52, Montemarcello, 19031, Italy;44.0523468;9.9521972;45;false;false;Contemporary, Ligurian;This warm, welcoming restaurant with a wooden ceiling and walls serves simple dishes as well as more creative, elaborate fare. The focus here is on showcasing the top-quality ingredients used (especially fish and seafood) in dishes which are influenced by Liguria, as well as elsewhere in Italy. Given the secluded location, the guestrooms on offer here are a good option.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10335;Badessa;Italy;Casalgrande;via Case Secchia 2, Casalgrande, 42013, Italy;44.6255198;10.7485293;57;false;false;Emilian;This restaurant has a surprising location in a 19C cheese factory which once produced parmesan cheese. Although the purpose of the building has changed, the love of the region remains the same: the chef goes out of his way to source local ingredients and serve traditional Emilian dishes, often with a modern twist. One of the best restaurants in rural Reggio Emilia.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10336;La Porta Restaurant;Italy;Bologna;piazza Vieira de Mello 4, Bologna, 40128, Italy;44.5114605;11.3572839;100;true;true;Creative;Housed in a futuristic building, La Porta Restaurant is a multi - purpose establishment which offers a bar for aperitifs and a highly modern cigar room, as well as a well - stocked wine cellar offering the best wines from Italy and elsewhere. The cuisine is creative with a particular focus on fish recipes, while lighter options are available in the Café from 7. 30am to 7pm.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10337;La Veranda del Color;Italy;Bardolino;via Santa Cristina 5, Bardolino, 37011, Italy;45.5430437;10.7252429;42;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This aptly named restaurant in the Color Hotel just a short distance from Lake Garda boasts a modern, colourful decor and cuisine worthy of its name. Dishes are inspired by Mediterranean traditions and are showcased on a number of different tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10338;Loewengrube;Italy;Bolzano;piazza della Dogana 3, Bolzano, 39100, Italy;46.5002845;11.3608536;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian;This building has been home to a restaurant since the 16C, making it one of the oldest in Bolzano. Today, it houses an elegant restaurant that serves a combination of traditional Alpine cuisine and classic Italian dishes with a contemporary twist, such as carbonara tortelloni filled with parmesan cream and crispy bacon. The attractive wine cellar boasts a selection of approximately 1 000 wines from the region and elsewhere in Italy, as well as a choice of labels from further afield.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10339;Retrobottega;Italy;Rome;via della Stelletta 4, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.9016565;12.4753274;58;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Minimalist decor and clean lines characterise this restaurant decorated in dark tones, where the two owner-chefs have both worked in various Michelin-starred restaurants (and others) over the years. Modern cuisine which showcases seasonal ingredients in regional yet refined dishes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10340;Già Sotto l'Arco;Italy;Carovigno;corso Vittorio Emanuele 71, Carovigno, 72012, Italy;40.7071485;17.6590721;42;true;false;Italian, Creative;A historic gourmet restaurant, with an equally historic setting on the first floor of a Baroque palazzo fronting an elegant piazza. A fine staircase leads up to the simple yet stylish dining room, which is skilfully run by a father and his offspring. In the kitchen, his wife Teresa prepares creative, regional cuisine, which is showcased on a surprise menu of four, six or eight courses and which features locally sourced meat and fish. If you’d like to book the delightful table on the small terrace for just two fortunate guests, make sure you do so well in advance!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10341;Saffron;Italy;Arezzo;piazza Sant'Agostino 16, Arezzo, 52100, Italy;43.4625448;11.8810875;76;true;false;Seafood;If you like fish and you find yourself in Arezzo, then this is the place for you. Saffron serves a range of traditional and imaginative raw fish dishes inspired by different traditions, from the Mediterranean to Japan, alongside a few cooked fish options and the occasional Japanese speciality such as tempura and Japanese spaghetti and ravioli.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10342;La Terrazza;Italy;Asolo;via Collegio 33, Asolo, 31011, Italy;45.8030132;11.9139009;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The aptly named Terrazza is a delightful open - air restaurant overlooking Asolo’s historic centre. In an elegant, fashionable ambience enjoy innovative delicacies that nonetheless make full use of the best local traditions and produce. Ideal for a romantic dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10343;La Locanda del Cardinale;Italy;Assisi;piazza del Vescovado 8, Assisi, 06081, Italy;43.070105;12.614407;93;false;false;Creative;A medieval house with stone arches, built over the remains of mosaics from a Roman villa – the location alone makes this restaurant truly memorable. Add to this modern, beautifully prepared cuisine with a focus on regional ingredients, and all that’s left to do is book your table!;Interesting wine list;[]
10345;La Fermata;Italy;Spinetta Marengo;strada Bolla 2, Spinetta Marengo, 15122, Italy;44.8790669;8.6599622;74;true;true;Piedmontese, Contemporary;Situated in the countryside around Alessandria, this 18C farmhouse has a modern, minimalist decor which serves as a backdrop for traditional Piedmontese cuisine with a clever modern twist. The chef offers just the right amount of creativity, with a focus on meat dishes and satisfying, memorable flavours that appeal to the emotions as well as the palate. Adding to the appeal, the elegant and exclusive ambience is the result of careful refurbishment, which has transformed the dining room into a triumph of art and design.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10346;John Restaurant-Casamadre;Italy;Afragola;via Santa Maria la Nova 35, Afragola, 80021, Italy;40.9336554;14.3506078;98;false;true;Creative;Follow the signs to Casamadre (the specialist food shop next door) to get to this gourmet restaurant, where the chef surprises guests with modern cuisine that is full of character. The dishes served here are inspired by classic recipes which are reinterpreted with creativity and a respect for local traditions, resulting in highly distinctive flavours. Each course reflects the region’s history, with a common thread running through the menu to create an authentic culinary experience. To accompany your meal, the wines are presented on a practical tablet which makes it easy to explore the different labels available. Among the different options, the excellent Costa D'Amalfi “Selva delle Monache” 2022 is particularly striking thanks to its fresh, earthy aromas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10347;Cascina Lautier;Italy;Chieri;strada Baldissero 121, Chieri, 10023, Italy;45.0261605;7.8269632;24;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Situated outside the town on top of a small hill, this elegant restaurant serves modern country cuisine, with some personal interpretations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10348;Januarius;Italy;Naples;via Duomo 146/148, Naples, 80138, Italy;40.8523593;14.2588742;77;true;true;Campanian;Named after San Gennaro (St Januarius) whose relics are said to lie in the cathedral nearby, this restaurant celebrates traditional, authentic specialities from Campania, such as octopus alla Luciana, zito pasta in a traditional ragu and salted cod with Napolitan-style endives. The entrance opens into a boutique selling top-quality ingredients (mainly charcuterie and cheeses), with two original dining rooms on either side.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10349;Taverna del Castello;Italy;Torrechiara;via del Castello 25, Torrechiara, 43010, Italy;44.6561141;10.2749088;94;false;false;Emilian, Seasonal Cuisine;Occupying a 15C castle in a medieval village, this restaurant offers fine views of the majestic hills all around. The chef here uses top - quality regional ingredients with a focus on seasonal produce to create tasting menus full of imagination and artistic flair. Excellent meat and fish dishes inspired by Italian traditions.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10352;Antinè;Italy;Barbaresco;via Torino 16, Barbaresco, 12050, Italy;44.725571;8.080728;58;false;true;Piedmontese;Manuel Bouchard’s cuisine impressed our inspectors thanks to striking features such as his minimalist approach and the use of just a few well-chosen ingredients. Traditional recipes, such as plin pasta and Fassona beef, feature on the menu alongside more alternative, imaginative dishes (including fresh- and saltwater fish). This elegant restaurant is located on the first floor of a building in the old town, just a stone’s throw from the medieval tower. A warm welcome and an excellent wine list complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10353;Il Carpaccio;Italy;Acri;contrada Cocozzello 197/d, Acri, 87041, Italy;39.4807559;16.2928963;16;false;false;Calabrian, Traditional Cuisine;This traditional family restaurant has been recently renovated to include an attractive veranda - style dining room overlooking the valley. Typical dishes from Calabria, fish specialities by prior arrangement, and a good wine list all add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10354;Feel Como;Italy;Como;via Diaz 54, Como, 22100, Italy;45.8096946;9.0809621;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Wild regional produce, game and freshwater fish take pride of place on the menu at this elegant restaurant which celebrates nature in all its glory, despite its town-centre location. The dishes prepared by chef Federico Beretta have a contemporary feel, while the tasting menu is dedicated to wild ingredients foraged from the woods.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10355;Walter Redaelli;Italy;Bettolle;via XXI Aprile 26, Bettolle, 53040, Italy;43.205414;11.809369;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this old 18C farmhouse with exposed brickwork, roof beams and an impressive fireplace, enjoy delicious Tuscan cuisine prepared from local ingredients, with a particular focus on meat. Specialities on the menu include pappa al pomodoro, home-made pici pasta, and sliced veal. Comfortable chairs add to the cosy and enjoyable dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10356;Il Pavone;Italy;Alghero;piazza Sulis 3/4, Alghero, 07041, Italy;40.5564645;8.3152583;29;false;false;Seafood;Situated in the heart of Alghero and with a beautiful veranda overlooking the sea, this restaurant serves delicious fish and seafood made from top-quality ingredients. Highlights include the “Alessandrina” fried fish and the octopus salad. If available, make sure you try the goats’ cheese made by the owner himself, although be warned – the flavour is quite strong!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10357;Osteria le Logge;Italy;Sienna;via del Porrione 33, Sienna, 53100, Italy;43.3184521;11.3333516;83;true;true;Contemporary;Having retained its old shop counter and glass - fronted display cabinets, this former grocer’s shop is perfect for anyone in search of old - world charm. However, the cuisine is the real draw with its focus on quality of the highest level. Wine buffs can ask to visit the wine cellar nearby, housed in a tunnel of Etruscan origin. Simpler dining room on the first floor.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10358;RistoFante;Italy;Alzano Lombardo;via Mazzini 41, Alzano Lombardo, 24022, Italy;45.7322736;9.7292663;24;true;true;Seafood, Italian;The motto of this restaurant is “In step with the times yet inspired by tradition”. The cuisine here is made from fresh, seasonal ingredients (with a particular focus on fish) prepared using modern techniques. Elegant dining room, plus a shaded outdoor space for the summer months.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10359;Sarti del Gusto;Italy;Cagliari;via Vico II Vincenzo Sulis 1/a, Cagliari, 09124, Italy;39.2167238;9.1175893;52;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;A small, beautifully maintained restaurant offering a concise selection of carefully prepared and attractively presented dishes. The cuisine here is often creative yet inspired by Sardinian traditions, with an equal focus on meat and fish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10360;Stube Ladina;Italy;Arabba;via Precumon 24, Arabba, 32020, Italy;46.49546;11.868114;63;false;false;Alpine, Traditional Cuisine;The hotel owner is also the chef, serving carefully prepared and well - presented dishes made from regional produce in a quiet Stube - style dining room. An interesting wine list provides the icing on the cake.;;[]
10361;Osteria de l'Umbreleèr;Italy;Cicognolo;via Mazzini 13, Cicognolo, 26030, Italy;45.1625063;10.1959046;81;false;false;Lombardian;Situated in Cicognolo in the Lower Po valley, where early morning mists create an evocative atmosphere in autumn, this traditional restaurant with a rustic feel serves specialities from Lombardy with a focus on delicious starters and top-quality meat. Our inspector particularly recommends the white onion gratin soup and the Burgundy-style snails. A simpler menu is available at lunchtime and there’s a small garden for alfresco dining on summer evenings.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10362;Da Peppe;Italy;Rotonda;corso Garibaldi 13, Rotonda, 85048, Italy;39.953684;16.0397112;83;false;false;Cuisine from Basilicata, Italian;Situated in the historic centre of a small village in the Parco del Pollino, this long-established restaurant serves traditional and copious local dishes that are always expertly prepared. Guestrooms are also available in the family B&B of the same name.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10363;Ventuno.1;Italy;Alba;via Cuneo 8, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.6974689;8.0364653;15;true;false;Piedmontese, Mediterranean Cuisine;Closed for renovations until April 2024.Two natives of Campania who have settled in the Langhe run this centrally located restaurant, where the black and white decor has a modern feel. The menu focuses on fish and seafood, in addition to meat dishes and truffles in season.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10364;Osteria Ardenga;Italy;Diolo;via Maestra 6, Diolo, 43019, Italy;44.9722466;10.1543563;97;true;false;Emilian, Country cooking;An authentic trattoria which is a joy to visit, where time seems to have stood still for decades. Situated on the border between two provinces, the restaurant focuses on specialities from Parma, many of which are made from home - grown produce. Homemade pickles and chutneys are also sold here.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10365;Roof Garden;Italy;Bergamo;piazza della Repubblica 6, Bergamo, 24122, Italy;45.6981456;9.6672047;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Make sure you ask for one of the tables next to the glass wall in this restaurant, which boasts romantic views of Bergamo’s Città Alta. The innovative, inventive cuisine is tempting and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10366;Villa Baroni;Italy;Bodio Lomnago;via Acquadro 12, Bodio Lomnago, 21020, Italy;45.7945545;8.7556142;74;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This romantic restaurant on the lakeshore has a welcoming, elegant ambience and a delightful terrace for summer dining. The cuisine pays particular attention to top-quality, seasonal ingredients prepared in traditional recipes with a focus on fish. Cosy, Provençal-style guestrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10367;Il Giardino delle Esperidi;Italy;Bardolino;via Mameli 1, Bardolino, 37011, Italy;45.5483964;10.7201346;19;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;The ideal starting point for an exploration of the area. In summer one dines on the terrace located in the heart of the historic centre while drinks and cigars may be enjoyed in the lounge bar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10368;Molteni;Italy;Adria;via Ruzzina 2/4, Adria, 45011, Italy;45.0548986;12.0555485;38;true;false;Seafood;Hospitality abounds in this establishment where the cuisine is inspired by local traditions, especially fish, in a favourably located restaurant in the historical centre on the banks of the Bianco canal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10369;Doc;Italy;Borgio Verezzi;via Vittorio Veneto 1, Borgio Verezzi, 17022, Italy;44.1598132;8.3063314;85;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Quiet, well - kept restaurant located in an aristocratic, early twentieth - century villa surrounded by a pretty garden.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10370;Osteria dell'Oca Bianca;Italy;Cavaglià;via Umberto I 2, Cavaglià, 13881, Italy;45.4058986;8.0924561;90;false;true;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of a small town, right opposite the church, this typical village osteria run by a friendly family serves traditional cuisine from the Piedmont, including goose dishes. Highlights here include the rustic, welcoming ambience, an excellent wine list, a wine cellar that can be visited, and a charming glass-fronted veranda that is used throughout the year. There are also three beautiful guestrooms reserved exclusively for guests dining at the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10371;Essencia Restaurant;Italy;Naples;piazza Santa Maria la Nova 9, Naples, 80134, Italy;40.8438248;14.2524835;57;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Fusion;Having spent many years living in Spain, the young chef at this quiet, elegant restaurant offers an appealing combination of Spanish and Italian dishes, resulting in his own interesting interpretations of Mediterranean cuisine. Situated in the heart of the historic centre, the restaurant has an open-view kitchen and chef’s table for four guests near the entrance, while the main dining room is on the first floor.;Air conditioning;[]
10372;Locanda del Molino;Italy;Cortona;località Montanare 10, Cortona, 52044, Italy;43.254763;12.0662076;52;false;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;This rustic yet charming restaurant occupies an old family mill. It has attractive guestrooms that reflect the elegant simplicity of the Tuscan countryside. In the kitchen, the female chef creates traditional specialities such as fried rabbit and nettle with ricotta cheese gnudi (ravioli filling without the pasta) in a fresh tomato sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10373;Maré;Italy;Cesenatico;Molo di Levante 74, Cesenatico, 47042, Italy;44.2067786;12.4029481;92;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;An unexpected gourmet restaurant in a typical private beach club on the Romagna coast, with a dining room that opens on to the beach with its long line of beach umbrellas. The dishes here are carefully prepared and occasionally creative, and all of good quality. We particularly recommend the monfettini (fresh egg pasta) mantecati with cuttlefish, clams, mantis shrimp and ink, which looks like a risotto and is absolutely delicious. The restaurant also boasts a good wine list with an excellent choice of champagnes.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10374;Indiniò;Italy;Raveo;via Norsinia 21/b, Raveo, 33029, Italy;46.4343104;12.8697139;61;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;This restaurant (the name Indiniò means “nowhere” in old Carnian dialect) is run by an enthusiastic female owner-chef who left her former job to realise her dream: namely, to create personalised cuisine of the highest quality with ingredients from her local region and elsewhere, while her partner takes charge of the dining room. Indiniò is both welcoming and elegant, with just a few tables, an intimate ambience and a small space for more private dining.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10375;La Canonica;Italy;Verona;vicolo San Matteo 3, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4418856;10.9938588;53;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;A small, minimalist restaurant in the town centre, where both the ambience and the cuisine are contemporary in style with a hint of Sardinian influence (the chef is originally from the island). Some of the dishes features fermented ingredients prepared on site.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10376;Quattro Sensi;Italy;Brufa;via del Colle 38, Brufa, 06089, Italy;43.0552896;12.4664105;92;true;false;Umbrian, Contemporary;After working in top-level restaurants both in Italy and abroad, the young chef at this restaurant in the Borgobrufa hotel offers a host of interesting dishes featuring excellent Umbrian ingredients, often sourced from local growers and farmers. Meat dishes dominate the menu, alongside a good selection of vegetables.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10377;Calvi Ristorante;Italy;Altamura;via Bari 134, Altamura, 70022, Italy;40.83617;16.56198;47;false;true;Contemporary;This welcoming, contemporary-style restaurant with a large open-view kitchen serves two different types of cuisine – one regional and Mediterranean in style, the other more creative allowing the chef’s culinary skills to take centre stage. The black rice tacos with roasted eel, green beans, soya bean sprouts and spicy hummus mayo are truly delicious – definitely to be eaten with the hands!;Air conditioning;[]
10378;Hostaria dai Musi;Italy;Alba;Piazza Michele Ferrero 4/d, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.696673;8.0338445;99;true;true;Piedmontese, Seafood;Offering a limited à la carte that includes fish dishes (including raw options) which vary according to market availability, this restaurant serves what it describes as “typically modern cuisine”. The breaded and fried anchovies with a typical saor sauce and lemon gel are particularly good, plus the menu features a selection of typical regional specialities. The pleasant setting is enhanced by the backdrop of the large central square in a pedestrianised area on the edge of the old town. The drinks menu includes an excellent selection of wines, plus a good choice of local beers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10379;Opificio;Italy;Noventa Padovana;via Roma 131, Noventa Padovana, 35027, Italy;45.4124222;11.9498026;66;true;false;Contemporary, Meats and Grills;A modern restaurant in the province of Padova which, over the past ten years, has grown and evolved from a gastro pub to the top-quality eatery that it is today. The cuisine is fairly eclectic, featuring meat and fish dishes alike, with the option of a lighter menu at lunchtime. The best dishes are showcased on the à la carte and are often made using luxury ingredients such as foie gras, scampi and Wagyu beef. The impressive wine list demonstrates a passion for international sparkling wines, while the excellent selection of wines by the glass is further enhanced by a choice of cocktails (also available at midday).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10380;Osteria del Posto;Italy;Corciano;via Calderini 15, loc. Chiugiana, Corciano, 06073, Italy;43.1061939;12.3095201;96;true;true;Umbrian, Contemporary;It's well worth the climb up to this restaurant, where you can be sure of a friendly welcome and professional service. With advice on hand from courteous female staff, choose from a selection of imaginative, locally influenced dishes that are full of flavour. We particularly recommend the pigeon (piccione di tutto un po’), accompanied by a glass of the potent Gamay del Trasimeno Opra red wine with an alcohol content of 14.5°!;Terrace;[]
10381;Enoclub;Italy;Alba;piazza Michele Ferrero 4, Alba, 12051, Italy;44.6969031;8.0339102;76;true;true;Piedmontese, Italian Contemporary;Under the arcades of a piazza named after Michele Ferrero, this restaurant has a simple, modern ambience with walls covered with wine bottles, as well as friendly, efficient female staff. The beautifully prepared Piedmontese cuisine is showcased on an à la carte and a tasting menu, accompanied by an impressive selection of quality wine.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10382;Locanda del Marinaio;Italy;Cefalu;via Porpora 5, Cefalu, 90015, Italy;38.0409839;14.0225187;58;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;Delicious cuisine full of the flavours of the Mediterranean (prepared by the German owner - chef! ) in a delightful little restaurant in the bustling centre of Cefalù. Simple surroundings but excellent food!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10383;La Veranda;Italy;Cernobbio;via Regina 40, Cernobbio, 22012, Italy;45.843091;9.0778706;44;true;true;Italian Contemporary;As its name suggests, the dining room at this restaurant is a splendid and elegant veranda, which transfers out onto the terrace overlooking the lake in fine weather. A perfect setting for the modern, international and Italian influenced cuisine served here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10384;Trattoria del Bivio;Italy;Cerretto Langhe;localtà Cavallotti 9, Cerretto Langhe, 12050, Italy;44.5880877;8.0747632;27;false;false;Piedmontese, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the Alta Langa region, this old restored farmhouse is now home to an elegant restaurant with a contemporary rural feel. The cuisine has strong regional roots, although the menu also offers a few fishes dishes. Excellent food, as well as attractive guestrooms and a warm, family welcome.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10385;La Casa degli Spiriti;Italy;Costermano;via Monte Baldo 28, Costermano, 37010, Italy;45.6144758;10.7229645;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;The Chignola family has been welcoming guests in this beautiful, restored farmhouse – a luxurious residence with one of the best views of Lake Garda – for almost 30 years. The ground-floor restaurant occupies a veranda surrounded by greenery facing the lake, where young chef Filippo (following in his father’s footsteps), together with his brother, sommelier Lorenzo, offers his guests an enjoyable dining experience with its roots in the cuisine of the region. The first-floor terrace is home to the Osteria Spiritino, which is more informal in both its cuisine and atmosphere. The remarkable wine cellar is housed in a room adorned with 18C frescoes and boasts more than 1 300 labels, with a particular focus on champagnes.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10386;I Salotti;Italy;Chiusi;Località Querce al Pino, SS 146, Chiusi, 53043, Italy;43.01881;11.90397;63;true;true;Creative;In summer, the outdoor spaces at this restaurant, such as the garden gazebo, are the perfect setting for a candlelit dinner in total harmony with nature, while in winter, the elegant dining room with just a few tables (book well in advance) really comes into its own. Creative cuisine prepared using produce from the restaurant’s own farm, plus a long-established wine cellar that has been extended over the years so that it now boasts over two thousand different labels from the region and elsewhere in Italy, many of them of the highest quality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10387;Il Doretto;Italy;Cecina;via Pisana Livornese 32, Cecina, 57023, Italy;43.3358312;10.5058965;27;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seafood;Restaurant within a refined farmstead. The ancient structure has maintained the rustic style in spite of several hints of elegance in the furnishings. On the menu: interesting offer of meat and seafood (with a slightly more limited wine cellar at lunch). Pleasant exterior for summer service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10388;Kürbishof;Italy;Anterivo;via Guggal 23, Anterivo, 39040, Italy;46.2746922;11.372941;53;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This romantic inn with guestrooms occupies an old farm with a hay barn. In two typical Stube-style rooms, one of which offers views of the Cembra valley, enjoy cuisine prepared by a mother-and-son team. They work side by side, preparing dishes from mainly regional ingredients (the menu often includes the names of producers) each in their own individual way, which is highlighted on the menu: to the left, you’ll find the traditional dishes made by the mother, Sara, while on the right you can choose from a selection of modern, creative options prepared by young chef Mathias. Our inspectors were delighted with their combination of choices from both lists!;Car park;[]
10389;Faraglioni Restaurant;Italy;Aci Castello;lungomare dei Ciclopi 115, loc. Aci Trezza, Aci Castello, 95021, Italy;37.56007;15.1597116;21;true;true;Seafood;Situated next to the hotel of the same name (a reference to the Faraglioni islands just off the coast here) but with its own entrance, this restaurant overlooks the beautiful Riviera dei Ciclopi. Sicilian ingredients take pride of place here in traditional and creative dishes with a focus on fish and seafood (vegetarian options are also available).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10390;All'Osteria Bottega;Italy;Bologna;via Santa Caterina 51b/55, Bologna, 40123, Italy;44.4911535;11.3326794;99;true;true;Emilian, Traditional Cuisine;Enjoy top-quality Emilian cuisine at this restaurant, which focuses on the region’s most traditional, best-known and authentic recipes. Featuring a superb selection of hams and salamis, fresh pastas, meat and desserts, the menu offers a real feast for the tastebuds that will linger long in the memory.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10391;Tano Passami l'Olio;Italy;Milan;via Francesco Petrarca 4, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.4715781;9.1696159;27;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Tano Simonato, chef-patron of this stylish modern restaurant located in a fine residential district, offers his creative cuisine that reinterprets Italian flavors in a modern key: food for him is not just nourishment, but also fun. He will then come to your table to advise you and tell you about his dishes, suggesting the best wine pairing, also thanks to a well-stocked cellar. The inspector recommends: Tiramisù of cuttlefish and potatoes, as well as Almond Cannoli stuffed with mousse of ricotta with almonds, candied lemon and chocolate drops, with citrus fruit cream and almond jam.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10392;Ensama Pesce;Italy;Sala Bolognese;via Aristide Dondarini 4, Sala Bolognese, 40010, Italy;44.6105112;11.2558128;40;false;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;A menu which focuses only on fish (from the daily market) which is prepared with a hint of Puglia, the chef’s native region. As soon as guests are seated at their table, they are brought a selection of homemade breads, including taralli bread rings and focaccia. Owner-chef Sabino is the heart and soul of this restaurant, where guests can be sure of a memorable culinary experience!;Air conditioning;[]
10393;Restaurant 700;Italy;Ostuni;largo Michele Ayroldi Carissimo 14, Ostuni, 72017, Italy;40.7299792;17.5770215;60;true;true;Contemporary;Situated at the entrance to Ostuni’s historic centre, this restaurant is part of the luxury Paragon 700 hotel. The charming dining room combines historic features with a more modern decor, while the exclusive garden is perfect for dining alfresco in fine weather. The menu offers a concise selection of classic Italian dishes at lunchtime, while in the evening the chef conjures up more high-level and elaborate dishes showcasing strong technique.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10394;Osteria alla Chiesa;Italy;Monfumo;via Chiesa Monfumo 14, Monfumo, 31010, Italy;45.8302987;11.9210025;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A young couple has brought life back to this old country inn, retaining its rustic ambience while introducing a menu which focuses on creativity and innovation. Claudio creates a host of meat, fish and vegetable dishes with imagination and originality, while one of the highlights remains the menu dedicated to donkey meat.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10395;uovodiseppia Milano;Italy;Milan;via Amerigo Vespucci 11, Milan, 20124, Italy;45.4812369;9.1928136;37;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sicilian;This completely renovated restaurant is situated in a pedestrianised area near Piazza Gae Aulenti, a new elegant restaurant district in Milan. Here, a wood-fired stove, attractive bar counter and small bistro-style tables provide the setting for carefully prepared Sicilian cuisine. Octopus, grouper and Mazara red prawns are just some of the top-quality Sicilian ingredients on the menu here, which includes reinterpreted recipes such as the “fuori Norma”, where the pasta is wrapped around the stuffed aubergine to create a dish full of Mediterranean flavours and aromas. The outdoor dining space in the pedestrianised street is perfect for early summer evenings, with its almost bohemian feel.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10396;FØRMA contemporary restaurant;Italy;L'Aquila;via Fortebraccio 53, L'Aquila, 67100, Italy;42.3489089;13.4017873;60;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;Situated in a secluded residential district that is part of L’Aquila’s historic centre, this intimate restaurant with an elegantly minimalist ambience is home to skilful owner-chef Simone Ciuffetelli. Having gained experience working abroad, Ciuffetelli showcases local ingredients in his creative, contemporary dishes, with the occasional use of fermented products and a frequent focus on just three ingredients. A good example is his dessert featuring cream and crunchy toasted hazelnuts generously coated with a white-chocolate mousse that is “disguised” as an Italian-style meringue thanks to a sprinkling of liquorice powder.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10397;Campo Cedro;Italy;Sienna;via Pian d'Ovile 54, Sienna, 53100, Italy;43.3228359;11.3312107;66;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated just a stone’s throw from the centre yet away from the tourist crowds, this restaurant is well worth the effort needed to find it! Here, Japanese chef Sugihara, who has more than 20 years’ experience working in Italy, creates modern and skilfully prepared Italian meat and fish dishes which are fresh and elaborate. You’ll nearly always find seafood risotto on the menu, which is made with fish, mussels and finely chopped shrimps all cooked together with rice and then sprinkled with crumbled seaweed and dotted with tomato paste. Excellent value for money!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10398;Enoteca Meucci;Italy;Cortona;Località Riccio 71, Cortona, 52044, Italy;43.2243467;12.0049727;29;false;false;Tuscan, Contemporary;Comprising a wine boutique and a wine bar in its rustic-style room on the ground floor, Enoteca Meucci is also home to a restaurant in the more elegant, classic-style rooms on the first floor. The expertly prepared cuisine is colourful and contemporary in style, with a focus on regional ingredients. Beautiful outdoor area for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10399;Granoturco Bistrot;Italy;Castagnole Piemonte;via Cavour 1, Castagnole Piemonte, 10060, Italy;44.8983738;7.5663275;94;false;false;Piedmontese;Although the external façade of this restaurant recalls its former life as a pub, the building is now home to a restaurant run by a young chef whose experience working abroad has done nothing to dim his love of the Piedmont. Here, he serves some of the best regional cuisine in the area, with a few more creative options also featuring on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10400;Anto e Robi;Italy;Robbio;Piazza della Libertà 8, Robbio, 27038, Italy;45.2898439;8.594069;38;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in the heart of a small town surrounded by rice fields, this restaurant has a charming and personalised feel. The cuisine is often (but not always) based around fish, which is showcased in dishes inspired by regional traditions. While Robi oversees the front of house with skill and expertise, offering recommendations on wine (over 300 labels, including many by the glass) and rum (his particular passion), Anto prepares a host of delicious recipes in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10401;Casa Rapisarda;Italy;Numana;via IV Novembre 35, Numana, 60026, Italy;43.51088;13.62254;31;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Seafood;This small welcoming restaurant on the famous Scalinata della Costarella in Numana, with a tiny terrace for summer dining and just a few tables, serves delicious cuisine with an imaginative twist. Originally from Sicily, the highly talented owner-chef has spent much of his life in the Marche and has plenty of experience in leading restaurants. Given the limited capacity here, booking is essential, especially in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10402;Radimare;Italy;Monopoli;via Beato Piergiorgio Frassati 5/a, Monopoli, 70043, Italy;40.9564457;17.297695;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;There’s no tasting menu at this restaurant but instead a tempting à la carte featuring modern Mediterranean cuisine based on top-quality seasonal ingredients, with fish and seafood taking centre stage. Citrus fruit and a few spices, especially ginger, are used carefully and sparingly, as are aromatic herbs which add a touch of fresh flavour to the dishes. The contemporary decor, enhanced by plants and a profusion of wood, plus friendly service add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10403;La Loggia Bistrò;Italy;Verona;Corte Sgarzarie 7, Verona, 37121, Italy;45.4433263;10.9957797;28;false;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Slightly off the beaten track yet still in the town centre, this restaurant boasts a courtyard setting for summer dining plus an intimate interior room with just a few small square tables, subtle lighting and an attractive decor featuring old wine bottles. A far cry from the classic tourist fare often available elsewhere, the cuisine served here is imaginatively presented with a focus on the use of seasonal ingredients.;Terrace;[]
10404;Sücar Brüsc;Italy;Mantua;via Cavour 49, Mantua, 46100, Italy;45.1598974;10.7950722;63;false;true;Contemporary, Lombardian;This interesting new restaurant in the historic heart of Mantova takes its name from a phrase in local dialect with translates as “sour” sugar. The cuisine here is regional yet modern, served in an informal dining room where traditional Mantuan sayings are written on the ceilings. For some months now, the restaurant has also offered an interesting caviar menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10405;I 5 Sensi;Italy;Cuneo;via Dronero 4, Cuneo, 12100, Italy;44.3927332;7.5497669;31;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The whole family (mother and four children) is involved in the running of this restaurant, both front of house and in the kitchen. If you’re looking for top-quality cuisine which focuses on local ingredients yet is also creative and innovative, then this is the place for you! Classic-style dining room with the occasional modern decorative touch, plus a well-stocked wine cellar offering a selection of 700 labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10406;Da Marino al St Remy;Italy;Cagliari;via San Salvatore da Horta 7, Cagliari, 09124, Italy;39.21508;9.11635;88;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sardinian;Situated on the edge of the pedestrianised area near the Bastione di Saint Remy, this restaurant is named after its charismatic owner Marino, who helps guests with their choice of menu and is happy to tell them all about the history of the restaurant (the street in front of the restaurant, for example, has not always been there). At the helm in the kitchen, his wife Silvana prepares Mediterranean dishes with a Sardinian flavour – the fish and seafood options are particularly delicious.;Air conditioning;[]
10407;Repubblica di Perno;Italy;Monforte d'Alba;vicolo Cavour 5, loc. Perno, Monforte d'Alba, 12065, Italy;44.6094368;7.9743963;17;false;false;Piedmontese;Situated in the heart of the gastronomic Langa region, this small, renovated restaurant in the centre of town (reservations required) is imbued with the passion of the couple at the helm (he’s in the kitchen, while she’s front of house). In keeping with Piedmontese tradition, you catch a glimpse of the open-view kitchen as you make your way to the first floor, which is laid out with just five tables. Enjoy traditional cuisine in a rustic, bistro-style setting where the daily menu showcases dishes with a strictly regional focus. Three guestrooms are also available.;Terrace;[]
10408;Lofficina;Italy;Sirolo;via Piave 11, Sirolo, 60020, Italy;43.52627;13.61662;20;false;false;Creative, Contemporary;This building with a minimalist, contemporary design is situated on the edge of the historic centre at the Sant'Erasmo belvedere from where, in summer, panoramic views extend over Monte Conero and the sea (booking ahead is recommended). In the kitchen, owner-chef Davide Breccia conjures up creative dishes featuring original combinations and mainly inspired by the sea. Our inspector’s favourite dish was the marinated amberjack with passion fruit, black pepper and vanilla. The freshness of the fish is enhanced by the chef’s balanced and individual approach.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10409;Il Cugnolo;Italy;Torre di Palme;contrada Cugnolo 19, Torre di Palme, 63900, Italy;43.1376;13.81738;79;true;true;Italian Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This gourmet restaurant housed in a restored period residence that once belonged to the counts of Adami is surrounded by the green maquis and hills of the Marche, with the sea visible in the distance just a few miles away. Here, the young Neapolitan chef creates cuisine that is surprising for its attractive, clean lines, providing a real explosion of flavours and a tribute to the region and the Mediterranean in general. The restaurant also owns a nearby agricultural estate which provides many of the wines and olive oils served during tastings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10410;La RiMa;Italy;Novara;viale Dante Alighieri 11/c, Novara, 28100, Italy;45.4487514;8.6153729;66;false;true;Contemporary;This restaurant in the heart of the city provides an elegant setting in which to enjoy excellent contemporary Mediterranean cuisine, all with a personalised twist added by the talented chef. Female staff provide the service and the friendly welcome.;Air conditioning;[]
10411;Frades La Terrazza;Italy;Porto Cervo;SP94 - Località Abbiadori, Porto Cervo, 07021, Italy;41.0943843;9.5285309;28;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sardinian;Situated in a panoramic location on Cala di Volpe bay, this trendy restaurant serves excellent cuisine with a focus on Sardinian specialities and other Mediterranean dishes. There’s a beautiful terrace for an aperitif, plus tapas options to share and a good selection of sparkling wines. Young and enthusiastic staff.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10412;Pescheria;Italy;Salerno;corso Giuseppe Garibaldi 227, Salerno, 84122, Italy;40.6767873;14.7634393;48;true;false;Seafood, Italian;The name of this restaurant between the historic centre and the seafront refers to the main item on its menu, which is dedicated almost exclusively to fish (fresh and not farmed). Fish and shellfish are displayed in a glass cabinet and aquarium respectively, both of which are situated to the rear of the long, narrow dining room near the open-view kitchen. Classic fish dishes full of flavour (served raw, baked, cooked in salt, in water or grilled) are to the fore here.;Air conditioning;[]
10413;Riva;Italy;Numana;Via Flaminia 109, Numana, 60026, Italy;43.50966;13.62223;79;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Riva is the Hotel Vista’s fine-dining restaurant, situated just behind Numana’s beach with fine panoramic views. The restaurant serves top-quality ingredients from the Adriatic and surrounding countryside in creative dishes full of flavour which are showcased on tasting menus and an à la carte.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10414;Dogma;Italy;Rome;piazza Zama 34, Rome, 00183, Italy;41.8760196;12.5093837;40;true;false;Seafood;This restaurant may be small (booking is recommended) but it has a big personality. The focus here is on fish and seafood, with nearly all the dishes cooked (at least partially) over the barbecue grill, including desserts! The talented, original young chef creates dishes full of intense and convincing flavours.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10415;Osteria il Moro;Italy;Trapani;via Giuseppe Garibaldi 86, Trapani, 91100, Italy;38.0177393;12.5122901;98;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Boasting an attractive outdoor space on Trapani’s main street, Osteria il Moro focuses on dishes that are deeply rooted in Sicilian tradition yet enhanced by original and creative touches, resulting in cuisine that is full of flavour and personality thanks to owner-chef Nicola Bandi. The menu features plenty of fish dishes as well as meat, including beef fillet in a red sauce with spices and wild herbs, and Trapani-style mullet. The impressive wine list includes a good selection of regional labels.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10416;La Casina;Italy;Drena;località La Casina 1, Drena, 38074, Italy;45.9612596;10.9516043;43;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Alpine;This large farmhouse with attractively renovated rooms overlooks the verdant landscapes of the Sarca valley from its wisteria-shaded summer pergola. Young chef Giada Miori prepares regional ingredients with skill and precision, serving specialities such as traditional potato fritters and “carne salada” (salted meat) preserved by the restaurant itself, as well as char, meat from the Trentino region and mushrooms. The Miori family also grow their own red berries, which often make an appearance in their desserts, along with their own sweet chestnuts.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10417;InAlto Alfio Ghezzi Dolomites;Italy;Moena;via San Pellegrino 32, stazione a monte della funivia Col Margherita, Moena, 38035, Italy;46.3790012;11.8014773;15;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Innovative;Situated on Col Margherita at an altitude of 2 550m and accessible in winter via a cable car (from the San Pellegrino pass in Moena), this new ski bar bears the name of Alfio Ghezzi, the Michelin-starred chef at the Mart museum in Rovereto. Options include burgers and a children’s menu as well as a more elaborate and creative selection of some of the chef’s best-loved dishes. In summer the bar can also be reached on foot or by bike (for the truly athletic!) with recharging stations available for e-bikes.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10418;Hostaria da Franz;Italy;Venice;salizada Sant'Antonin, sestiere Castello 3499, Venice, 30122, Italy;45.435407;12.3467382;83;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Founded in a different venue by an Austrian soldier in the late 19C, this historic Venetian restaurant is now run by owner Maurizio, who oversees the front of house in a courteous yet friendly manner. He introduces guests to its variety of dishes, which aim to please rather than surprise. Fish specialities are to the fore here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10419;Locanda Solagna;Italy;Quero;piazza I  Novembre 2, Quero, 32038, Italy;45.9389356;11.9357476;72;true;false;Italian Contemporary, Country cooking;Although this restaurant has been in business since the 1950s, it feels much more modern thanks to its updated appearance. Renowned for its excellent regional cuisine served in the evening, the restaurant pays careful attention to seasonal ingredients. At lunchtime, the ”osteria”-style menu is much simpler. Excellent wine selection.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10420;Locanda Altobelli;Italy;Terracina;via Santissima Annunziata 121, Terracina, 04019, Italy;41.2899998;13.2513079;67;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant little restaurant that differs from the many fish options in town with its traditional regional meat-based cuisine. There’s a real alchemy here between the young owner who is passionate about wine and the talented chef who boasts an impressive CV. Carefully chosen ingredients sourced directly from small local producers are the basis for its exciting, delicious dishes, while the wine list features some interesting organic wines. Small outdoor space for alfresco dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10421;Savô;Italy;Laigueglia;piazza XXV Aprile 8, Laigueglia, 17053, Italy;43.9776356;8.1591594;91;false;false;Italian Contemporary;The reopening in 2022 of the Hotel Windsor with its romantic vintage decor, is a real bonus for Laigueglia, especially the hotel’s new gourmet restaurant Savô (which translates as “flavour” in Ligurian dialect). Here, a contemporary dining room and an outdoor space with views of the beach and the sea provide the setting for modern cuisine prepared from regional, seasonal ingredients with a focus on fish (there is also a meat option for each course). The impressive selection of wine and choice of cocktails from the elegant Windsor Bar adds to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10422;Il Grottino;Italy;Gualdo Cattaneo;piazza Beato Ugolino 5, Gualdo Cattaneo, 06035, Italy;42.9090284;12.5556707;88;false;true;Meats and Grills, Umbrian;Situated in the old medieval village of Gualdo Cattaneo, amid the gentle valleys not far from Foligno, Il Grottino is the perfect choice for anyone keen to sample the authentic flavours of Umbrian cuisine. Here, truffles and zero-km produce take pride of place on the menu, with a particular focus on meat which is carefully cooked on the open-view barbecue grill. Alongside locally sourced produce, you’ll also find a choice of carefully selected Prussian beef. Comfortable and welcoming guestrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10423;Osteria da Fiore;Italy;Venice;calle del Scaleter, sestiere San Polo  2202/a, Venice, 30125, Italy;45.4386827;12.3293006;30;true;false;Venetian;An osteria in name only, this restaurant has an elegant ambience, with two romantic tables overlooking the canal. If you enjoy Venetian cuisine you will be in your element here, as Signora Mara skilfully combines traditional local dishes with her own personal touch.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10424;Castel Toblino;Italy;Castel Toblino;località Castel Toblino 1, Castel Toblino, 38076, Italy;46.0562632;10.9670517;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated in a bucolic location in the Trentino where the excellent Vino Santo is produced (we recommend rounding off your meal with a glass of the equally superb grappa), this restaurant and adjacent bar occupy a fascinating medieval castle (tours of which can be arranged) jutting out into the lake of the same name. The generous, modern meat and fish dishes are featured on various tasting menus, along with an extensive à la carte. In summer, make sure you book a table on the charming terrace overlooking the lake.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10425;U' Vulesce;Italy;Cerignola;via Cesare Battisti 3, Cerignola, 71042, Italy;41.264648;15.9036082;33;true;false;Apulian, Traditional Cuisine;First opened over 60 years ago, this restaurant has been built up into a successful business over the years by the Di Donna family, who serve top - quality produce from this fertile region, including meat and fish dishes, cured hams and cheeses, all accompanied by a selection of good wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10426;Cravero - Osteria Contemporanea;Italy;Caltignaga;via Novara 8, Caltignaga, 28010, Italy;45.5162919;8.5912111;87;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Warm colours such as teal and ochre give this restaurant a cosy and welcoming ambience. The cuisine here is authentic and traditional in style, with dishes based on top-quality local ingredients accompanied by a choice of regional wines. There’s also an outdoor area for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10427;Miseria e Nobiltà;Italy;Campobasso;via Sant'Antonio Abate 16, Campobasso, 86100, Italy;41.56109;14.6587518;95;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The name of this restaurant occupying a late-18C palazzo with attractive flooring and Murano glass chandeliers alludes to the peasant traditions that influence its cuisine (miseria) and the creative, elegant dishes served here (nobiltà). The menu features excellent home-made pastas, vegetables and meat dishes, including boned rabbit with leeks and Annurca apples and white and black truffles from the Molise in season.;Air conditioning;[]
10428;Ginevra;Italy;Ancona;Rupi di via XXIX Settembre 12, Ancona, 60122, Italy;43.616116;13.507044;54;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Situated on the fourth floor of the Seeport hotel, this restaurant boasts a summer roof garden offering stunning sea views. The chef, a native of Ancona who trained with Gualtiero Marchesi, serves traditional local dishes prepared using ingredients from the region, as well as remaining open to the rest of the world (just like his town and its port). Lighter fare is available at the Seeport Bistrò.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10429;Al Camin;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;località Alverà 99, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.544327;12.150794;69;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;On the road to Misurina lake, this friendly restaurant with a modern Alpine style offers dishes of the regional tradition with imaginative touches and modern technique. So a great deal of practicality, then, as in the beef tenderloin wrapped in speck dry-cured pork with cep mushrooms and Ampezzo-style potatoes. The chef and sommelier Fabio Pompanin manages a wine list with approximately 200 labels. In the warmer season, take advantage of the open-air service.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10430;San Quintino Resort;Italy;Busca;via Vigne 6, Busca, 12022, Italy;44.5274401;7.4732865;45;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Once you have crossed the plain and climbed up into the San Quintino hills, you come to this restored farmhouse surrounded by an attractive garden. The restaurant is divided into a brick - walled dining room and a winter garden, while the charming guestrooms make this a romantic place to stay. Creative dishes with a focus on local ingredients and a few fish specialities feature on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10431;Malenco;Italy;Chiesa in Valmalenco;via Funivia 22, Chiesa in Valmalenco, 23023, Italy;46.2739486;9.8515438;82;false;true;Alpine, Regional Cuisine;Modern furnishings in the dining room, with panoramic windows looking out over the valley, typical local menu: traditional dishes at reasonable prices.;Car park,Great view;[]
10432;Evan's;Italy;Cassino;via Gari 1/3, Cassino, 03043, Italy;41.4890294;13.828005;62;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seafood;This restaurant is run with great enthusiasm by the Evangelista family (hence the abbreviation Evan’s). It specialises in delicious fish and seafood prepared mainly in a classic style, although local dishes also feature on the menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10433;Luigi Pomata;Italy;Cagliari;viale Regina Margherita 18, Cagliari, 09124, Italy;39.2129934;9.1157851;38;true;false;Seafood;This famous classic restaurant in Cagliari serves top-quality cuisine in its modern dining rooms and on an outdoor terrace. The menu features interesting reinterpretations of Sardinian dishes among other options, including their own tuna (the house speciality), which is also available in tins to take away.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10434;Caffè Meletti;Italy;Ascoli Piceno;via del Trivio 56 (piazza del Popolo), Ascoli Piceno, 63100, Italy;42.8543036;13.5750901;84;false;false;Cuisine from the Marches, Italian;Housed on the first floor of the historic café where the aniseed liqueur of the same name was created, this restaurant serves simple yet creative, regional and maritime - inspired cuisine. Don’t miss the terrace with views of Piazza del Popolo. Faster options available at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10435;IO Luigi Taglienti;Italy;Piacenza;via Pietro Giordani 14, Piacenza, 29121, Italy;45.0468867;9.6924674;65;true;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;In this charming restaurant in Piacenza, where tables are arranged in the courtyard of the deconsecrated church that is also home to the Galleria Volumnia, Luigi Taglienti delights guests with his elegant and refined cuisine. The chef’s personal and decidedly contemporary reinterpretations of classic Italian and international favourites will linger long in the memory, while the interesting menu "Riscoperta" features  local dishes at an attractive price.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10436;Claudio Ristorante;Italy;Fabbrico;via Ferretti 109, Fabbrico, 42042, Italy;44.8852991;10.7869918;87;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;An unexpected surprise in the heart of the lowlands. In this charming farmhouse situated in open countryside, Claudio prepares top-quality, almost exclusively fish and seafood cuisine with a southern Italian influence (especially from his native Puglia). There’s also a simpler, cheaper menu on weekday lunchtimes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10437;Le Vie del Borgo;Italy;Toceno;via alla Piazza 6, Toceno, 28858, Italy;46.1436973;8.4675804;73;true;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;Le Vie del Borgo is situated in a restored rustic building situated in the historic centre of the picturesque village of Toceno in the Val Vigezzo. Here, a young couple with a real passion for cuisine serve recipes from the region and elsewhere, as well as dishes that demonstrate remarkable modern techniques, all made from top-quality seasonal ingredients and accompanied by an interesting selection of wines. The restaurant consists of several intimate dining rooms decorated in Alpine style, with an elegant feel and carefully chosen furnishings. The attractive outdoor space with just a few tables is popular in summer, so advance booking is recommended!;Terrace;[]
10438;Mater;Italy;Moggiona;via di Camaldoli 52, Moggiona, 52014, Italy;43.7817842;11.7954217;41;true;false;Creative;Nature plays a starring role here, both in terms of the restaurant’s location at the foot of the Camaldoli monastery and in the seasonal cuisine made from locally sourced ingredients. Choose 3 courses from à la carte or opt for the tasting menu Deeper.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10439;L'Atelier 26;Italy;Saint-Christophe;località Gerandin 26, Saint-Christophe, 11020, Italy;45.7434008;7.3504867;43;true;true;French, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in a secluded location, this small gem of a restaurant boasts a skilfully restored stone dining room with a welcoming feel. The menu here has a clear French influence evident in both the style of its dishes and ingredients used. Our inspectors particularly recommend the young chef’s iconic snails and duck breast dishes.;Terrace;[]
10440;Terrazza Bartolini;Italy;Milano Marittima;via A. Boito 30, Milano Marittima, 48015, Italy;44.2683528;12.3568364;39;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Following its reopening in 2020, this seafront restaurant overlooking the beach and small harbour now offers its guests a choice between its indoor dining room or the panoramic terrace in fine weather (if you prefer the latter, it’s best to book ahead due to its popularity). The cuisine here focuses entirely on simple, unfussy fish dishes, with raw options and cooked dishes which make much use of the local Cervia salt. Daily, market-fresh specials are announced at your table.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10441;Tenuta Casa Virginia;Italy;Villa d'Almè;via Cascina Violo 1, Villa d'Almè, 24018, Italy;45.7535753;9.6172554;75;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Surrounded by the property’s own vineyards, this restaurant nestlings at the bottom of a gentle hill features an elegant dining room and a beautiful terrace for outdoor dining in fine weather. The cuisine is contemporary (yet not excessively so), with a few freshwater fish also featuring on the menu, while the wine list showcases a good selection of wines. The property’s own wines are available for purchase in the shop.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10442;Osteria da Cippi;Italy;Frisanco;Borgo Valdestali 5, Frisanco, 33080, Italy;46.2072604;12.7585631;86;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Italian;We particularly enjoyed this restaurant for its out-of-this-world feel. Housed in a charming chalet with an open fireplace, Osteria da Cippi serves cuisine made from typical local ingredients. At the helm in the kitchen, Nazzarena Del Fabbro is inspired by the seasons, using wild herbs from Valdestali in spring, vegetables from the restaurant’s small kitchen garden in summer, and seasonal fruit from the surrounding forests in autumn. Make sure you try the cjarsons. Guests are required to book in advance.;;[]
10443;Il Riccio;Italy;Anacapri;via Gradola 4/11, Anacapri, 80071, Italy;40.5609576;14.203649;65;false;true;Seafood;Situated just a few metres from the Blue Grotto and perched right above the water, Il Riccio is the quintessential Mediterranean fine-dining restaurant thanks to its tasteful and elegant decor. Undoubtedly one of Capri’s iconic addresses, it focuses uniquely on fish and seafood dishes. Whether you have a sweet tooth or not, a visit to the tempting dessert buffet to admire its array of delicacies is a must!;Great view,Terrace;[]
10444;Rosso di Sera;Italy;Castelletto sopra Ticino;via Pietro Nenni 2, Castelletto sopra Ticino, 28053, Italy;45.7155611;8.5911082;15;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated closed to the motorway exit, this restaurant’s rustic exterior belies its young, colourful and contemporary interior. The dishes are as modern as the decor, yet they have their roots in strong local traditions. The owner has a real passion for French and sparkling wines, including around 160 different champagnes and a wide selection of Burgundies, plus a good choice of wines by the glass, craft beers and cocktails.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10445;Osteria del Tempo Perso;Italy;Ravenna;via Gamba 12, Ravenna, 48121, Italy;44.420345;12.197758;75;false;false;Italian Contemporary, Italian;Situated in a hidden corner of the historic centre, this small bistro-style restaurant has a friendly and welcoming atmosphere, with photos alternating with books, wine bottles and glasses on the walls (the wine list includes a few labels from elsewhere in Europe). Small tables set close together, warm, subtle lighting and an almost Parisian ambience make this a perfect choice for a romantic dinner or a meal with friends. There’s also a small outdoor space for fine weather but seats are limited, so it’s best to book ahead!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10446;Laurin;Italy;Bolzano;via Laurin 4, Bolzano, 39100, Italy;46.4980585;11.3570705;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;In the magnificent setting of the exclusive Parkhotel Laurin, this restaurant is one of the best in Bolzano, boasting a Liberty-style dining room and tree-shaded tables in the garden for summer dining. The traditional cuisine also includes a few modern touches with ingredients and techniques from all over Italy and beyond, such as the grilled trout and leek terrine wrapped in nori algae in the shape of a flower. The menu features meat and fish dishes, with a small section dedicated to traditional local specialities.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10447;Posta;Italy;Bologna;via della Grada 21/a, Bologna, 40122, Italy;44.4973648;11.328168;57;false;false;Tuscan, Traditional Cuisine;A corner of Tuscany in Bologna, where famous soups such as ribollita and pappa col pomodoro are followed by pappardelle pasta with wild boar, tripe, beef pepper stew and, of course, Fiorentina steak, although there’s also room on the menu for local specialities such as tagliatelle and tortellini. Many of the wines served also come from Tuscany.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10448;Lio Pellegrini;Italy;Bergamo;via San Tomaso 47, Bergamo, 24121, Italy;45.7035284;9.6755047;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Despite its location in the town centre, the attractive outdoor terrace of this restaurant offers a peaceful atmosphere with its decor of light drapes. The red - coloured dining room makes a pleasant backdrop for the modern, Mediterranean cuisine served here. Elegant ambience.;Terrace;[]
10449;Regallo;Italy;Biella;via Tollegno 4, Biella, 13900, Italy;45.574481;8.0517711;24;false;true;Seafood;Situated slightly on the outskirts, this contemporary-style restaurant occupies the unusual setting of an old factory. Here, picture windows in the dining room overlook the stream below, with the sound of the water adding an almost musical note to the ambience. In the open-view kitchen, skilful chef Claudio Ravinetto prepares dishes with an exclusive focus on fish, including delicious house specialities such as scallops with anchovy cream, tomatoes and basil, and the “Sicilia” dessert which pays tribute to the island with its ricotta cream topped with chocolate shavings, orange jelly and dried capers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10450;Rifugio Col Alt;Italy;Corvara in Badia;strada Col Alt, Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.5524411;11.8864378;91;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Alpine;During the day this restaurant can be reached in just a few minutes by cable car, providing you with breathtaking views of the Dolomites, while in the evening (when the service is more attentive – things are faster paced at lunchtime) you have to arrange transport via snowcat. The name “refuge” refers only to the location as the cuisine is definitely that of a restaurant: although the menu features hearty mountain fare, it also includes modern options and a few fish-based recipes, including oysters. Last but not least, there’s a good selection of wines.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10451;Ca' 7;Italy;Bassano del Grappa;via Cunizza da Romano 4, Bassano del Grappa, 36061, Italy;45.779289;11.7415811;93;false;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Housed in a charming 18C villa, this elegant restaurant overlooks its attractive garden in a magical setting which is typical of the Veneto. The cuisine also has a regional focus, with classic recipes featuring on the menu alongside more creative dishes (fish appears more often than meat).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10452;Zafferano;Italy;Città della Pieve;viale Icilio Vanni 1, Città della Pieve, 06062, Italy;42.9540242;12.0057342;89;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Famous for its saffron, Città della Pieve is also well worth a visit to admire the Baciadonne alley (“one of the narrowest streets in Italy”) in its beautiful historic centre. This welcoming restaurant in a quiet and elegant hotel boasts an attractive veranda for summer dining that provides the perfect backdrop for delicious cuisine that is influenced by Umbria and Tuscany alike.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10453;Castello Malvezzi;Italy;Brescia;via Colle San Giuseppe 1, Brescia, 25133, Italy;45.5755269;10.249472;93;true;false;Creative;This elegant 16C hunting lodge offers a modern menu of fish dishes and regional specialities. Particular attention is paid to the excellent Calvisano caviar, with a dedicated menu. There’s an attractive outdoor dining area facing the gardens with views of the city of Brescia.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10454;Particolare di Siena;Italy;Sienna;via B. Peruzzi 26, Sienna, 53100, Italy;43.3225911;11.3367701;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A fine-dining restaurant which changed tack in 2020, reducing its number of tables to just ten and embracing a sustainable approach to its cuisine. It now prioritises local suppliers and certified organic and environmentally friendly ingredients, while the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, featuring produce grown in line with biodynamic techniques, provides some of the best seasonal ingredients used in the dishes here.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10455;Baita Fraina;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;Località Fraina 1, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.5236962;12.152584;83;true;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;Warm little bar rooms, reminiscent of the German wine bars or "Stube", a summer terrace and well - prepared regional dishes: for those who want to escape the mundane life of Cortina for the silence of an isolated "baita" [mountain hut]. Delightful rooms, colourfully furnished in warm tones so you can better enjoy the silence and scents of the mountains.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10456;I 5 Campanili;Italy;Busto Arsizio;via Maino 18, Busto Arsizio, 21052, Italy;45.620154;8.8475578;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Contemporary cooking with an emphasis on Mediterranean fare in tune with the seasons is to the fore in this elegant restaurant occupying a 20C building with an attractive veranda to the rear. Fish takes pride of place on the menu, with a particular focus on raw dishes and shellfish, but the splendid desserts are also worthy of note, such as cherries in sour cherry juice with fior di latte ice cream.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10457;Vitis;Italy;Brixen;vicolo del Duomo 3, Brixen, 39042, Italy;46.715773;11.6565591;15;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;A modern wine bar in the centre of Bressanone (Brixen), situated in the same building as the delightful family restaurant, the Oste Scuro. Here, small armchairs, benches and stools are dotted among low square tables and higher tables, all surrounded by walls completely lined with wine bottles. The contemporary cuisine features tempting, generous dishes such as cod with cauliflower, cavolo nero and beurre blanc. Accommodation is available just two minutes’ away in the historic Adler Historic Guesthouse run by the same owners.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10458;Osteria da Nando;Italy;Aosta;via Sant'Anselmo 99, Aosta, 11100, Italy;45.7387983;7.3262368;76;false;false;Cuisine from the Aosta Valley, Traditional Cuisine;Opened in 1957, this osteria in the heart of the historic centre is one of the town’s leading restaurants for anyone wanting to sample the cuisine of the Aosta valley. Delicious regional specialities such as cured meats, polenta and fondue are prepared with the best ingredients and served in a simple dining room with plenty of character. Wide choice of excellent wines by the glass.;Terrace;[]
10459;Elephant;Italy;Brixen;via Rio Bianco 4, Brixen, 39042, Italy;46.7191054;11.6535404;17;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Situated in the famous Elephant hotel (with which it shares a name), this restaurant has a unique, historic ambience thanks to its decor of antique wood panelling. The cuisine here is regional with a modern twist, featuring dishes such as char with cream of celery and green apple on a bed of fragrant elderflowers. The interesting wine list boasts a selection of almost a thousand different labels.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10460;A' Paranza;Italy;Atrani;via Traversa Dragone 1, Atrani, 84010, Italy;40.636899;14.6082597;16;false;false;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;For more than 30 years, this restaurant run by the Proto brothers has been a popular choice for visitors to the beautiful Atrani valley. Simple cuisine served in a simple and informal setting (dishes are nearly always announced at your table rather than listed on a menu), with a focus on Mediterranean and Campanian dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
10461;Baretto di San Vigilio;Italy;Bergamo;via al Castello 1, San Vigilio, Bergamo, 24129, Italy;45.70842;9.65015;71;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Situated in the small square in front of the cable-car entrance, this typical bar-cum-restaurant with a retro, vaguely English feel serves generous traditional cuisine reinterpreted with a modern twist, including home-made bread and desserts. In summer, meals are served on the terrace with enchanting views of the town, while the two winter dining rooms have a rustic yet elegant feel.;Terrace;[]
10462;L'Acciuga;Italy;Ravenna;viale Francesco Baracca 74, Ravenna, 48121, Italy;44.417719;12.1925247;40;false;true;Seafood;Anchovies, king prawns, cuttlefish and freshly caught fish are just some of the options available in this restaurant specialising in fish and seafood, where guests will be delighted by the fresh flavours of the ingredients. The small wine list, which also includes a few non-Italian labels, offers good value for money. The maritime-style decor evokes the interior of an old ship, while the warm welcome is typical of the region. All in all, an excellent choice!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10463;Agorà;Italy;Rende;via Rossini 178, Rende, 87036, Italy;39.345249;16.242226;21;true;true;Seafood, Contemporary;Michele Rizzo is the owner-chef of this interesting restaurant situated in a modern part of Rende. His menu focuses mainly on fish (although a few meat dishes are also available) which he prepares in light, modern dishes with an emphasis on local ingredients. There’s also an interesting wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10464;Le Chiavi d'Oro;Italy;Arezzo;piazza San Francesco 7, Arezzo, 52100, Italy;43.4649614;11.8805991;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated in Arezzo’s historic centre, this restaurant boasts an original, minimalist ambience with an elegant wood decor. The main focus here is on the cuisine, which is among the best not only in the city but also in the region. Skilful interpretations of traditional dishes, with a focus on Tuscany, where the gastronomic pleasure increases with each course.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10465;Dispensa Franciacorta;Italy;Torbiato;via Principe Umberto 23, Torbiato, 25030, Italy;45.6084857;10.001314;72;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;An informal restaurant with bottles of wine from the enoteca on the walls adding a charming touch. The menu features delicious traditional dishes made from top-quality Franciacorta ingredients, including vegetables grown in a large organic garden supported by the restaurant. Many of the ingredients used by the chef (pasta, cheese, ham and salami etc) are served as snacks at the lively bar throughout the day.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10466;Fiamma Cremisi;Italy;Calvisano;via De Gasperi 37, località Viadana, Calvisano, 25012, Italy;45.37821;10.34027;58;false;false;Italian, Modern Cuisine;This country restaurant serves regional cuisine with an innovative twist. Dine either in the main dining room warmed by an open fireplace or outdoors under a gazebo in summer. Lunchtime options are restricted to a business menu or a shorter and more reasonably priced menu.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10467;Marsupino 1901;Italy;Briaglia;via Roma Serra 20, Briaglia, 12080, Italy;44.4003047;7.8789728;30;false;false;Piedmontese;The Marsupino family has been running this trattoria enthusiastically and warmly since 1901. The chef's suggestion pays homage to the territory in accordance with tradition and the wine cellar, managed by the friendly expert Luca, is immense, with an excellent choice by the glass. Five rooms and two suites in the adjacent late nineteenth-century palazzo.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10468;Ladinia;Italy;Corvara in Badia;strada Pedercorvara 10, Corvara in Badia, 39033, Italy;46.5468459;11.877733;18;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Italian Contemporary;Both the Berghotel Ladinia and its restaurant of the same name boast a warm, vintage Alpine-style ambience, with wood decor that tells the story of this business which opened as a simple inn back in 1930. Little has changed since then and guests return here time after time thanks to the warm welcome and attention to detail offered by the Costa family. The traditional cuisine has the occasional modern twist, while the few Ladin-style guestrooms are decorated with a profusion of wood.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10469;La Locanda di Pietracupa;Italy;San Donato in Poggio;via Madonna di Pietracupa 31, San Donato in Poggio, 50028, Italy;43.5316232;11.2420871;97;false;false;Tuscan;Housed in a beautiful early-20C residence with a panoramic terrace overlooking the hamlet of San Donato in Poggio, this restaurant comprises a dining room and a winter garden to the rear of the building. Tuscan classics take pride of place on the menu, which features a selection of familiar and popular dishes. Four guestrooms are available for anyone looking to extend their stay.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10470;Locanda Alpina;Italy;Brez;piazza Municipio 23, Brez, 38021, Italy;46.43114;11.10719;43;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the enchanting Val di Non with its castles and apple orchards, this restaurant housed in a 19C building has been run by the same family since 1933. It serves excellent cuisine that makes good use of regional produce alongside occasional ingredients from further afield, such as the delicious pistachio ice cream.;Wheelchair access;[]
10471;Feva;Italy;Castelfranco Veneto;Borgo Treviso 62, Castelfranco Veneto, 31033, Italy;45.6720316;11.9321644;32;false;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the historic centre of Castelfranco Veneto, this restaurant has an intimate, elegant and contemporary-cum-minimalist feel despite its period courtyard setting and original wooden beams in the first-floor dining room. Nicola Dinato’s cuisine is showcased on two tasting menus, namely Anima and Corpo. The former offers a selection of new dishes created by the chef, who is constantly updating his cuisine, while the latter features his historic signature specialities (don’t miss the artichoke, crab, fig and leek dish). A lighter, less expensive menu is also available at lunchtime. The impressive wine list includes many French labels – unsurprisingly, perhaps, as the sommelier (and chef’s wife) is from France!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10472;Trattoria Rigoletto;Italy;Brescia;via Fontane 54/b, Brescia, 25133, Italy;45.573784;10.242922;49;false;true;Seafood, Italian;A simple environment, manages to create an interesting cuisine. The menu is quite extensive, the dishes are authentic and the atmosphere is welcoming.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10473;Antico Ristorante Pagnanelli;Italy;Castel Gandolfo;via Gramsci 4, Castel Gandolfo, 00073, Italy;41.7495226;12.648721;30;false;false;Classic Cuisine;In business since 1882, yet constantly evolving, this restaurant boasts a superb location overlooking the lake. The menu features meat and fish dishes, enhanced by wild herbs. The extensive wine selection is presented on two wine lists. Don’t miss the famous wine cellars built into the rock, plus the small wine museum.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10474;La Sosta;Italy;Brescia;via San Martino della Battaglia 20, Brescia, 25121, Italy;45.5337317;10.2210584;29;true;false;Lombardian;Housed in a 17C palazzo, this charming restaurant is very popular with locals. Alfresco dining in summer (just a few tables, so it is best to book), as well as efficient and attentive service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10475;Enoteca di Canelli - Casa Crippa;Italy;Canelli;corso Libertà 65/a, Canelli, 14053, Italy;44.7155011;8.2882991;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Piedmontese;Occupying a late-19C palazzo, in what was a historic wine cellar right up to the late 1960s, this well-run family restaurant serves regional cuisine with a contemporary twist. The basement dining room is accessible by stairs only.;Air conditioning;[]
10476;Residenza del Lago;Italy;Candia Canavese;via Roma 48, Candia Canavese, 10010, Italy;45.3272604;7.8848734;43;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Boasting a tranquil, homely atmosphere typical of the region and with a name that pays homage to Lake Candia, this restaurant occupies a mid-18C farmhouse that is now located within the town. Its traditional cuisine includes popular dishes such as potato cake with seared shrimp and artichokes, “tajarin vecchio Piemonte” (pasta with a meat sauce), and beef cheeks cooked in Erbaluce di Caluso wine.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10477;Molin Vecio;Italy;Caldogno;via Giaroni 116, Caldogno, 36030, Italy;45.6096315;11.524484;30;false;false;Venetian, Seasonal Cuisine;In the idyllic setting of a 16C mill with a garden and small lake, this restaurant boasts an equally magical dining room with a warm, friendly and traditional feel. Top-quality dishes from the Veneto include a delicious sopressa(the region’s cured ham), Vicenza-style baccalà (cod) with Marano polenta and a soft guancetta served with a superb pendolòn (potato polenta).;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10478;El Gato;Italy;Chioggia;corso del Popolo 653, Chioggia, 30015, Italy;45.2218635;12.2798212;91;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Chioggia is famous as one of the more active fishing ports in the region and this restaurant takes full of advantage of the local catch. Situated on the central promenade of this picturesque town, the restaurant serves fish of truly exceptional quality served in traditional recipes from the Adriatic.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10479;Dolia Gaeta;Italy;Gaeta;piazza Conca 22, Gaeta, 04024, Italy;41.210569;13.5820891;34;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;This brand-new restaurant boasts an elegant, chic decor and a relaxed and informal ambience. The very young team here is overseen by a talented chef who prepares modern and creative dishes with a focus on fish from the local gulf, as well as elsewhere. The wine list is also particularly interesting, featuring a remarkable choice of champagnes and a special emphasis on labels from Lazio.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10480;Romolo Mare;Italy;Bordighera;lungomare Argentina 1, Bordighera, 18012, Italy;43.7769699;7.6731692;84;false;true;Seafood;Situated in a private beach club facing the sea, this restaurant combines a relaxed atmosphere with an elegant feel thanks to its professional owners who have worked as restaurateurs for many years. Here, they serve excellent fish and seafood cuisine with a focus on raw dishes, plus a choice of daily fish specials. A selection of interesting local wines completes the picture.;Terrace;[]
10481;Da Miro alla Lanterna;Italy;Viareggio;via Coppino 289, Viareggio, 55049, Italy;43.8635054;10.2478156;80;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;It would be difficult for the menu at this restaurant to convey the beauty and quality of the fresh fish on display near the kitchen, where guests can make their own selection. Here, all sorts of shellfish and different fish of all shapes and sizes are transformed into delicious dishes full of flavour. Classic decor, professional service, an excellent wine selection and good value for money all add to the appeal. An address which has been delighting guests ever since 1954!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10482;Pernambucco;Italy;Albenga;viale Italia 35, Albenga, 17031, Italy;44.0469607;8.223478;28;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a garden setting with a pleasant outdoor dining space, plus a long, narrow interior decorated in decidedly classic style. Fish and seafood take pride of place on the menu, with a focus on local fish, including excellent tartare (usually either seabream or tuna, depending on the catch of the day) and shellfish (cooked in salt, baked or grilled). The vegetables are sourced from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10483;Lamberti;Italy;Alassio;via Gramsci 57, Alassio, 17021, Italy;44.0103712;8.1772583;36;false;true;Seafood;This restaurant is situated just a stone’s throw from the sea in a building dating from the 1930s. It serves traditional, regional dishes made from carefully selected ingredients. Don’t miss the fish and the pesto sauce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10484;Collina;Italy;Almenno San Bartolomeo;via Ca' Paler 5, Almenno San Bartolomeo, 24030, Italy;45.7583892;9.5707144;94;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A family style trattoria has now been converted into these modern premises that, while jealously upholding their homely origin, offer dishes of contemporary inspiration. One small dining hall has an open fireplace and the other gives a panoramic view.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10485;Le Cicale;Italy;Spinetta Marengo;via Pineroli 32, Spinetta Marengo, 15122, Italy;44.87612;8.69275;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The owners of this pleasant restaurant, once owned by their grandparents, have given it a light, modern feel. A married couple welcome guests front of house, while the wife’s brother creates delicious Italian and regional dishes in the kitchen. Delightful outdoor area to the rear surrounded by greenery.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10486;Mistral;Italy;Bellagio;via Teresio Olivelli 1, Bellagio, 22021, Italy;45.98775;9.26198;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated at the tip of Bellagio’s promontory where the two branches of the lake meet, this villa occupies a superb panoramic location, with its restaurant housed in a covered veranda boasting delightful views of the opposite shore, its little villages and exclusive residences. The atmosphere here is reminiscent of a grand hotel, with background piano music in the evening and guests from all around the world. The moderately creative cuisine offers a choice of Italian dishes alongside more international options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10487;Stube Gourmet;Italy;Asiago;corso IV Novembre 65/67, Asiago, 36012, Italy;45.8734842;11.5098715;24;true;true;Creative, Contemporary;Situated in a pedestrianised area in the centre of Asiago, this small restaurant on the first floor of the Hotel Europa has just five tables and is certain to attract food-lovers thanks to its exquisite cuisine. Now with a new chef at the helm, Stube Gourmet continues to delight guests who are lucky enough to dine here. Classic traditional cuisine based on carefully selected local ingredients with a keen eye for what’s in season provides the foundation for this chef’s dishes. There’s also an excellent wine list that continues to expand, plus a wine shop on the street outside.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10488;Magiargè Osteria Contemporanea;Italy;Bordighera;via Dritta 2, Bordighera, 18012, Italy;43.7810218;7.6732415;93;true;true;Ligurian;The dining rooms in this lively, typical restaurant in the upper, historic part of Bordighera appear to be almost dug out of the rock. Here, a local chef with plenty of experience behind him creates predominantly Ligurian cuisine (and not just fish and seafood), accompanied by an excellent and extensive wine list, including labels from outside Italy and a good selection of champagnes. Attentive service completes the picture here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10489;Alla Fassa;Italy;Castelletto di Brenzone;via Nascimbeni 11, Castelletto di Brenzone, 37010, Italy;45.6908541;10.7523726;37;true;false;Seafood, Italian Contemporary;Although the beautiful views of the lake (with only a cycle path between the restaurant and the water) and mountains on the opposite shore can be admired from the dining room, in fine weather it’s a race for the outdoor tables just a few metres from the water. The cuisine is as impressive as the setting, with a fine balance of classic and modern dishes featuring fish from the lake (such as the “il lago in un piatto” – the lake in a dish – starter) and the sea. A few guestrooms with views of the lake are also available.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10490;I Pifferi;Italy;Sala Baganza;via Zappati 36, Sala Baganza, 43038, Italy;44.7161428;10.215919;55;true;true;Emilian;This restaurant occupying an old post house that dates back to the time of Marie Louise, Duchess of Parma, lies amid the verdant landscapes of the Parco Regionale dei Boschi di Carrega, just a kilometre outside the village of Sala Baganza. This stunning setting is the backdrop for typical dishes from Parma, such as Nonna Lina’s herb tortelli served with melted butter and parmesan cheese. In summer, dine alfresco in the cool, shady garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10491;Nido del Picchio;Italy;Carpaneto Piacentino;viale Patrioti 6, Carpaneto Piacentino, 29013, Italy;44.9125495;9.793899;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant with a low-key, hushed atmosphere has the feel of a tastefully furnished private home, with an open fire lit in winter and a cool, welcoming outdoor dining space for the warmer months. The restaurant has built up a well-deserved reputation for its fish dishes, although the menu here is equally divided between fish and meat. Options such as anolini in brodo (filled pasta in broth) pay tribute to the region’s traditions, while most of the dishes served here are highly creative. Originally English, the owner’s wife runs the front of house with skill and a warm, friendly manner. The wine cellar is home to more than 700 of the best Italian and international wines, with a curious emphasis on labels from cooler climes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10492;Pinocchio;Italy;Borgomanero;via Matteotti 147, Borgomanero, 28021, Italy;45.68877;8.45695;92;false;true;Piedmontese;This glorious, elegant restaurant is surrounded by a delightful garden where guests can dine à la carte or order copious appetisers in the summer months. The recipes focus on the gastronomic traditions of the Piedmont reinterpreted with a modern flavour, as well as more contemporary dishes with original combinations. Meat and fish dishes (including fish from the lake) always feature, alongside some of the restaurant’s classic house specialities.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10493;Ortica;Italy;Pieve Ligure;via Giovanni Migone 4, Pieve Ligure, 16031, Italy;44.3775228;9.0966738;80;false;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;You drive along 4.5km of winding, narrow (occasionally extremely narrow) roads to get to Ortica, the restaurant at the Tenuta Golfo Paradiso about 35min from Genoa. As is often the case, once at your destination the extensive views of the Tyrrhenian Sea from the restaurant more than compensate for the effort of getting here. Neither will you be disappointed by the cuisine, which is prepared using top-quality ingredients such as vegetables from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, local fish and carefully selected meat. Dishes are fresh and modern, and occasionally cooked over the barbecue grill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10494;Blum;Italy;Taormina;via Nazionale 147, Taormina, 98039, Italy;37.85599;15.30046;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Although there is an extensive à la carte at this restaurant, it is on the tasting menus that the chef showcases his creative cuisine to the full. His Suggestioni menu features dishes such as scampi carpaccio with green apple and caviar, while the vegetarian Naturalmente option includes a robustly structured black garlic and almond noodle dish full of decisive flavours, which is well worth trying. The romantic, modern platform where tables are set out is practically on the beach, which means that the restaurant is closed in bad weather.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10496;Miil;Italy;Cermes;via Palade 1, Cermes, 39010, Italy;46.62567;11.147209;68;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Housed in a converted 15C mill on the Kränzelhof wine estate, this smart, elegant restaurant provides the backdrop for excellent, contemporary-style cuisine prepared wherever possible using locally sourced (and always top-quality) ingredients.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10497;Frades Porto Cervo;Italy;Milan;via Giuseppe Mazzini 20, Milan, 20123, Italy;45.461581;9.1883869;29;false;false;Sardinian, Modern Cuisine;This new Milan venture is the brainchild of three brothers who already run a restaurant and delicatessen in Porto Cervo. Elegant and extremely contemporary in style, the restaurant serves modern Sardinian cuisine, while a corner reminiscent of their delicatessen allows guests to taste the island’s hams and cheeses by the slice.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10498;Villa Salina;Italy;Moretta;Via Santuario 25, Moretta, 12033, Italy;44.7642736;7.5322252;17;true;true;Piedmontese, Seasonal Cuisine;Named after Edoardo Salina, the chef to the House of Savoy, this villa from the mid-1800s features several rooms embellished with frescoed ceilings. The bold owner-chef here has completely restored the building, bringing it back to life and using it as a backdrop for his evolving culinary skills which started out in the family pasticceria. Nowadays, this “multi-tasking” modern restaurant offers a regionally inspired à la carte alongside fish dishes and a business menu option at lunchtime, while in the evening the menu includes a selection of high-quality pizzas. In summer, the dining room opens out onto a beautiful veranda and guests can also wander through the well-kept garden, which is now owned by the local municipality.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10499;Scola;Italy;Castelbianco;via Pennavaire 166, Castelbianco, 17030, Italy;44.1123062;8.0586737;23;true;false;Creative;Instead of the simple, rustic-style dishes you might expect at this restaurant, the cuisine is actually elaborate and of the highest quality – an excellent reason for venturing out here!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10501;Baita Piè Tofana;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;Località Rumerlo, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.54099;12.09893;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;On the slopes of the Tofana and directly overlooking the ski slopes, a characteristic and romantic mountain lodge with a contemporary touch, whose design manages to combine tradition and modernity, is also a source of inspiration for the cuisine. Dishes with a contemporary taste–Rossini al mare (beef, foie gras, cuttlefish and Teriyaki sauce) is excellent–made with considerable use of charcoal grilling, in both summer and winter, and ample use of local raw materials. With friends, experience the convivial Larin table, with a central built-in fireplace around which the seats are arranged. The wine list is worthy of note with a large choice of Champagnes and Italian bubbly.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10503;12 Ristorante;Italy;Cesenatico;via Armellini 12/a, Cesenatico, 47042, Italy;44.1983653;12.3938933;45;true;true;Seafood;An original ambience with real character, as well as top quality fish and seafood. There is also a charming outdoor area overlooking the canal where old boats from the Museo della Marineria are moored.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10504;Duomo;Italy;Alessandria;via Parma 28, Alessandria, 15121, Italy;44.9122;8.6191122;20;true;false;Italian Contemporary;This small restaurant with a bright and welcoming dining room stands out for its contemporary-style cuisine (based around seasonal ingredients) and many home-cooked dishes. The two brothers at the helm create interesting, often regionally inspired recipes with clever personalised twists. On the autumn menu, we particularly recommend the venison with cauliflower, almonds and Barbera wine sauce. Those with a sweet tooth will enjoy the panna cotta with a persimmon coulis (delicious but not too sweet!), while wine-enthusiasts will find plenty to interest them on the extensive wine list. The restaurant also boasts a superb location, nestled in the narrow streets of the centre just a stone’s throw from the Duomo.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10505;Locanda Baggio;Italy;Asolo;via Bassane 1, località Casonetto, Asolo, 31011, Italy;45.8111209;11.9088151;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Standing in a quiet location behind Asolo, this restaurant with an attractive summer garden serves authentic cuisine with an emphasis on top quality ingredients. Wine lovers will appreciate the good selection of international wines on offer here.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10506;Da Tonino;Italy;Capri;via Dentecala 14, Capri, 80073, Italy;40.548478;14.253413;65;false;true;Campanian, Traditional Cuisine;Allow a good half-hour to get to this small restaurant with a simple ambience and an airy terrace which is perfect in the heat of summer. The cuisine has its roots in local traditions – its first courses are particularly good. There’s also an excellent wine selection.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10507;Osteria Casale Ferrovia;Italy;Carovigno;via Stazione 1, sulla SP 34, Carovigno, 72012, Italy;40.7365002;17.6852297;15;true;false;Apulian, Modern Cuisine;Housed in what was once the 20C dwelling of an old olive mill, this restaurant boasts elegant decor, including a few antique family pieces and Art Deco - style tables. The female owner - chef prepares light and modern dishes with a regional flavour, while the wine list also showcases the best of Puglia. As the name suggests, the railway lies to the rear of the property, although there’s very little noise and no disturbance at all.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10508;Villa Pizzini;Italy;Stresa;Località Mottarone, Stresa, 28838, Italy;45.8768;8.4586;97;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;From Lake Maggiore you climb up Mottarone mountain to an altitude of around 1 400m to reach this 19C hunting lodge, where a young couple of self-taught chefs provide a warm and friendly welcome. The cuisine here speaks for itself – delicious meat dishes, plus a few specialities from the lake which are also served outdoors to a backdrop of stunning views. This couple are passionate about using seasonal ingredients and learning about every different stage in their supply chain. Local game dishes are highly recommended.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10509;MOI Omakase;Italy;Prato;Viale Piave 10, Prato, 59100, Italy;43.8783258;11.0986903;99;false;false;Sushi;Situated in the centre of Prato, with views of the Castello dell’Imperatore, this restaurant takes guests on a culinary voyage to Japan without leaving Italy! All guests eat the same single menu, starting at 9pm, as part of which the chef prepares his selection of sushi and sashimi directly in front of them in the dining room. Omakase means “I trust you” – an act of trust that you certainly won’t regret. Our inspector recommends the miso and monkfish soup with kelp and green onions.;Air conditioning;[]
10510;Mima;Italy;Vico Equense;via Madonnelle 9, Vico Equense, 80069, Italy;40.6596932;14.4311256;34;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;You’ll be won over by the seasonal Mediterranean cuisine created by the young yet experienced chef at this restaurant. Accommodation is also available in modern guestrooms, plus there’s an enchanting roof garden in which to sip an aperitif while the sun goes down.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10511;Al Baliaggio;Italy;Venosa;via Vittorio Emanuele II 136, Venosa, 85029, Italy;40.9636;15.82133;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a 15C building in the centre of town, this restaurant boasts beautiful vaulted ceilings and a smart, elegant ambience. The young owner-chef serves cuisine with a traditional focus which is reinterpreted in modern style and made from excellent regional ingredients, as well as a few fish options. Efficient, punctual service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10512;Osteria Mood;Italy;San Bartolomeo al Mare;via Cesare Battisti 58, San Bartolomeo al Mare, 18016, Italy;43.9236402;8.0970532;40;false;true;Ligurian, Modern Cuisine;Situated just a few minutes from the seafront promenade in a quiet, residential district, this restaurant with a relaxing ambience serves delicious Ligurian cuisine with a focus on organic vegetables, fish and seafood (local whenever possible), and home-made bread, desserts and fresh pasta. In summer, meals are served by the swimming pool in the garden, while in winter, the welcoming covered veranda boasts extensive sea views.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10513;Suscettibile Salerno;Italy;Salerno;via dei Principati 45, Salerno, 84122, Italy;40.6788381;14.7661808;22;true;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;Separated from a street in the centre of Salerno by an inner courtyard, this restaurant is a peaceful oasis with comfortable chairs arranged on a modern and stylish veranda (which opens almost completely in summer) and in an equally elegant dining room. Young chef Mario Quarta (born in Battipaglia) combines influences from his native region with techniques learned in renowned restaurants elsewhere in Italy and abroad, including Michelin-starred addresses. The French influence evident in his cooking techniques makes his Campania-focused cuisine even more exciting and contemporary. Our inspector particularly enjoyed the “Rombo R-otto” – four mouthwatering textures of meaty turbot served in a beautifully presented dish. Elegant, professional service overseen by manager Marco Sesso completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10514;Gnocchetto;Italy;Tavernerio;via Primo Maggio 56, Tavernerio, 22038, Italy;45.801;9.14181;17;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This long-established family-run restaurant (opened in 1926) with an updated contemporary decor continues to serve cuisine that is classic and generous in style yet adapted to modern tastes. Individual dishes take pride of place on the menu at lunchtime, although you can also order from the À la carte if you wish. There’s also an outdoor space for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10515;La Piemontese;Italy;Mariano Comense;via San Martino 48, Mariano Comense, 22066, Italy;45.70517;9.18446;22;true;true;Piedmontese, Contemporary;The focus at La Piemontese, a simple yet modern restaurant with a convenient car park, is mainly on meat dishes, although game and fresh truffles also feature in season, plus there’s a generous business menu at lunchtime. An enjoyable dining experience that offers good value for money.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10516;Meta Ristorante;Italy;Celle Ligure;via Generale Pescetto 5, Celle Ligure, 17015, Italy;44.3409071;8.5444326;43;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Situated in the picturesque historic centre of Celle, this old boathouse with a typical brick ceiling is now home to an excellent gourmet restaurant, where a young chef creates some of the most interesting dishes in the region.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10517;Capogiro;Italy;Baia Sardinia;Località Li Mucchi Bianchi, Baia Sardinia, 07021, Italy;41.1283048;9.4720013;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated on a panoramic terrace with views of the sunsets over Baja Sardinia, a stone’s throw from the Costa Smeralda, this restaurant serves creative cuisine with a focus on local and Italian ingredients in unexpected combinations. Our inspector particularly enjoyed the cacio e pepe cannelloni with raw prawns, salicornia and cuttlefish ink.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10518;Shiroya;Italy;Rome;via dei Baullari 147, Rome, 00186, Italy;41.8962633;12.4724383;51;false;true;Japanese, Asian;One of the most popular restaurants in the historic centre of Rome, Shiroya has just a few tables, so booking ahead is recommended. Served with courtesy and professionalism, dishes include well-known Japanese specialities such as home-made gyoza (dumplings) with various fillings, tempura and other fried options, the inevitable raw fish in all the classic combinations, ramen, different rice dishes and much more besides.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10519;Hebbo Wine & Deli;Italy;Toblach;Località Lago di Dobbiaco, Toblach, 39034, Italy;46.7066182;12.2185029;48;false;true;Innovative, Contemporary;Situated on a campsite on the shores of Lake Dobbiaco, this new restaurant demonstrates its owner’s passion for wine and contemporary cuisine. The young Austrian chef here has plenty of experience behind him – in the evening, his dishes are showcased on surprise tasting menus of seven or nine courses, while at lunchtime, there’s also a 5-course option. His recipes feature plenty of vegetables and exciting combinations, such as burnt leek, Romanesco sauce and potato or trout, or alternatively, dried beetroot, reduced cream, thyme and Schüttelbrot. Ingredients are sourced from trusted producers, as well as family members who run a biodynamic farm nearby. The superb wine list demonstrates the friendly, competent owner’s passion for wine.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10520;Sotto l'Arco;Italy;Bologna;via Aretusi 5, Bologna, 40132, Italy;44.50801;11.28821;90;true;true;Italian, Creative;Villa Aretusi is a pleasant 17C villa surrounded by its own garden on the outskirts of Bologna. At the hotel’s gourmet restaurant, Sotto l’Arco, on the first floor (lift available), the skilful chef creates modern, interesting Italian dishes, while at the Trattoria on the ground floor the focus is more on traditional Emilian cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10521;Sa Cardiga e Su Schironi;Italy;Capoterra;strada statale 195 rotonda per Capoterra, Capoterra, 09012, Italy;39.1519524;9.0187872;80;true;true;Seafood;Since 1967, this small restaurant has been delighting locals and visitors alike with its vast array of fish and seafood dishes, including grilled and skewered specialities. The fresh fish display cabinet at the restaurant entrance is one of the highlights here, as is the extensive selection of antipasti which includes tuna and mullet bottarga, “agliata alla bosana” (blue shark with tomatoes in a light sweet and sour sauce) and “burrida alla cagliaritana” (with dogfish). Other dishes include fresh and pasta with various seafood sauces, fried fish, soup, lobster, barbecued fish and even eel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10522;Erbaluigia;Italy;Pisa;via San Frediano 10/12, Pisa, 56126, Italy;43.7184362;10.3999667;64;false;false;Contemporary, Country cooking;This attractive restaurant with a simple, minimalist decor stands almost opposite the thousand-year-old church of San Frediano. The inviting menu here focuses on regional dishes with a successful combination of traditional and modern styles, including a section dedicated to barbecue options. Meat takes pride of place, although offal, cheese and a few vegetarian options also feature.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10523;Locanda 53 Supper Club;Italy;Arco;via Vergolano 53, Arco, 38062, Italy;45.9195014;10.8841028;19;false;false;Contemporary;Partners in life and business, Evelyn and Carlo are a young couple who have settled in Arco’s old town where they have restored this old inn, embellishing it with three modern and comfortable guestrooms. The restaurant offers two tasting menus featuring meat or fish – guests are asked to make their choice when booking. Once that’s done, all you have to do is sit back and enjoy the intimate atmosphere of the couple’s small “supper club” and leave everything to the talented Evelyn in the kitchen and skilful Carlo front of house. The recipes here are modern yet unfussy, with a focus on carefully selected ingredients that are prepared with respect and real attention to detail. Fine cuisine and an exquisite welcome combine to offer a truly memorable dining experience.;Air conditioning;[]
10524;Osteria Europa;Italy;Asiago;Corso IV Novembre 65/67, Asiago, 36012, Italy;45.87348;11.5098328;38;false;true;Venetian, Seasonal Cuisine;Despite its simple appearance, this restaurant housed in the hotel of the same name serves interesting, traditional cuisine which is well prepared and full of flavour.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10525;Peperosa;Italy;Lucca;piazza dell'Anfiteatro 4, Lucca, 55100, Italy;43.8454659;10.505623;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Tuscan;Despite its idyllic location facing the picturesque Piazza dell'Anfiteatro, this restaurant has avoided becoming a tourist trap, evolving instead into one of the most interesting restaurants in Lucca. The menu is finely balanced between meat and fish dishes with more than just a hint of added creativity, plus there’s now a new chef at the helm.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10526;Eggentaler;Italy;Cardano;via Val d'Ega 47, Cardano, 39053, Italy;46.4909623;11.3945865;82;false;true;Meats and Grills, Classic Cuisine;Renowned for being one of the best places in the region for steak cooked over a barbecue grill, this excellent restaurant has a varied menu which also includes a few fish dishes. There’s also a very good wine list, plus the restaurant also offers comfortable guest accommodation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10527;Crub;Italy;Cava de' Tirreni;corso Umberto I 125, Cava de' Tirreni, 84013, Italy;40.697891;14.7097243;60;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;A modern restaurant with an elegant, contemporary decor situated on the main pedestrian street in the town centre. The menu features an excellent selection of raw dishes, as well as a good choice of oysters and caviar, plus an equally delicious house speciality: fried pizza marinara with San Marzano tomato cream, garlic mayonnaise, black olive ash and Cetara anchovies. Sparkling wines are to the fore on the wine list.;Air conditioning;[]
10528;/gu.stà.re/ oltrecucina;Italy;Borgomanero;via Antonio Gramsci 20/b, Borgomanero, 28021, Italy;45.6984614;8.4657234;86;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An attractive contemporary-style restaurant right in the town centre, with a striking colour scheme and minimalist decor. The cuisine is inspired by traditional Piedmontese recipes which are reinterpreted with an imaginative touch by young, talented chef Valentina Maioni who selects top-quality ingredients and cooks with real passion.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10529;Rendenèr Alpine Food;Italy;Pinzolo;Via Sorano 35, Pinzolo, 38086, Italy;46.1616602;10.7632894;35;true;false;Contemporary;Situated within the Lory hotel, this restaurant has a contemporary decor and wooden tables that give it an informal ambience. Here, the young talented chef creates Alpine cuisine from carefully chosen seasonal ingredients, with menus changing throughout the year. In spring, for example, ingredients include Alpine sow-thistle, Mugo pine shoots, woodruff and lichen, while in summer herbs and flowers from the restaurant’s own organic kitchen garden add extra flavour to dishes. An interesting wine list with a focus on regional labels completes the picture.;Car park;[]
10530;Umami;Italy;Badalucco;Via Ugo Secondo Partigiano 1, Badalucco, 18010, Italy;43.9198701;7.8439315;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A young chef with experience in renowned restaurants has taken over the old kindergarten in this village and transformed it into a delightful restaurant. Here, he serves contemporary cuisine, often influenced by local traditions and showcased on tasting menus from which individual dishes can be ordered à la carte style. In summer, there’s an attractive outdoor space practically on the banks of the Argentina river, which gives its name to the valley in which this village is situated.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10531;Visione Restaurant and Living;Italy;Barbaresco;Strada Nicolini Basso 34, loc. Tre Stelle, Barbaresco, 12050, Italy;44.7065543;8.0839593;24;false;true;Contemporary, Piedmontese;At this restaurant, new chef Emanuele Bellomo serves three tasting menus – one focuses on traditional dishes, another has a more modern and imaginative flavour, while the third is a surprise menu which allows the chef to demonstrate his skill to the full (all dishes are also available à la carte style). Situated in the Casa Nicolini hotel in a quiet, panoramic location, the restaurant boasts fine views of the hills through its dining room windows and from its terrace, where a bar and bistro with a more concise and reasonably priced menu are set up in the summer months.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10532;Ristorante de LEN;Italy;Cortina d'Ampezzo;Via Cesare Battisti 66, Cortina d'Ampezzo, 32043, Italy;46.53884;12.13403;46;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Just a stone’s throw from the central and very busy Corso Italia, this restaurant has an elegant Alpine feel. Here, subtle lighting, soft background music and larch wood cladding on the walls create an ambience with an attractive blend of the modern and traditional. The cuisine takes inspiration from the local region, with specialities interpreted with a contemporary twist, including a focus on vegetable- and cheese-based dishes such as the excellent “fonduta di Saporito d'alpeggio” (fondue).;Wheelchair access;[]
10533;AceroRosso;Italy;Vodo di Cadore;Via Ruvignan 1, Vodo di Cadore, 32040, Italy;46.4108978;12.2787883;29;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This secluded mountain chalet immersed in verdant woodland boasts a welcoming dining room with a decidedly Alpine feel thanks to the profusion of wood and a warming open fire. The cuisine is also regional in style, featuring local recipes and ingredients albeit with a contemporary touch. Popular dishes include the rack of lamb cooked at low temperature and served with creamed sweetcorn, leek fondant and its own jus.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10534;Café Les Paillotes;Italy;Pescara;piazza Le Laudi 2, Pescara, 65129, Italy;42.4548186;14.2397968;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;This old acquaintance of the Michelin Guide now has a new chef at the helm! Although the decor and furnishings remain the same with a slightly old-fashioned feel, the cuisine is modern yet with no unnecessary frills and has a fresh and generous flavour. Highlights on the menu include the new raw fish options, which have an entire tasting menu to themselves. The well-stocked wine cellar is home to around 500 labels which offer good value for money.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10535;Meylas;;Abu Dhabi;Al Raha Beach, Al Muneera, Abu Dhabi;24.4524283;54.604805;39;true;true;Emirati Cuisine;It may be a little hard to find but this all-day eatery hidden away among the apartment blocks of Al Muneera Island is well worth seeking out. It began life as a food truck but now the two sisters behind it have a thriving business where their passion for their country and its food culture are clear for all to see. The chefs in the on-view kitchen prepare a menu of authentic and satisfying Emirati dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10536;Punjab Grill;;Abu Dhabi;The Ritz-Carlton Hotel, Grand Canal, Venetian Village, 3rd Street, Al Rawdah, Abu Dhabi;24.4130131;54.4866037;22;true;false;Indian;There are Punjab Grills dotted around the world and this outpost, located in the Venetian Village, part of the sprawling acreage of the Ritz-Carlton hotel, is one of the more established branches, having opened in 2015. Ask for one of the booths and sit back and enjoy the Northern Indian specialities and the attentive service. They also have an attractive waterfront location and a terrace from which to enjoy it.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10537;Em Sherif Sea Café;;Abu Dhabi;Rosewood Abu Dhabi Hotel, Zayed the First Street, Al Maryah Island, Abu Dhabi;24.499465;54.38686;68;true;false;Lebanese;Meaning “mother of Sherif” in Arabic, this restaurant pays homage to the original Beirut branch first opened in 2011. Situated inside the Rosewood hotel, this light, contemporary space offers far reaching views of the water surrounding Al Maryah Island and interiors boasting Portuguese Azulejo hand-painted wall tiles. The authentic menu is seafood focused – make sure you check out the seafood counter as you arrive – and has a wide variety of vibrant, well-balanced Lebanese dishes made for sharing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10540;NIRI;;Abu Dhabi;Building 9, Mamsha Al Saadiyat, Abu Dhabi;24.5383551;54.4068304;32;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;Grab a seat at the counter of this contemporary Japanese restaurant to watch the chefs prepare your dishes over the robata grill. The ingredients are top-notch, and the kitchen is clearly motivated. The pared-back interior is very on-trend and comes complete with a sakura tree. People-watchers and anyone who enjoys a good sea view will prefer a seat on the terrace as this spot on Mamsha Al Saadiyat is hard to beat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10541;Paradiso;;Abu Dhabi;Yas Bay Waterfront Pier 71, Yas Island, Abu Dhabi;24.4580979;54.6006106;72;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;A partnership between celebrated French chef Pierre Gagnaire and Nicole Rubi of La Petite Maison in Cannes resulted in this bright and colourful restaurant. It’s the perfect backdrop to their favoured cuisine – that of the Mediterranean, so expect everything from snails and roast poussin to fritto misto, pizza and assorted pasta dishes. The terrace overlooking the water is nicely decked out and a very pleasant spot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10543;Cipriani;;Abu Dhabi;Building 1, Yas Marina, Yas Island, Abu Dhabi;24.4668982;54.6093523;29;false;false;Italian;Elegance and style are hallmarks of all Cipriani restaurants and Abu Dhabi’s branch of this well-known international group occupies an appropriate glamourous position overlooking Yas Island Marina, with a beautiful terrace to make the most of the great views.  There are Japanese dishes available, but Italian is really the way to go here – and they offer all the classics, from carpaccio to cannoli.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10544;Li Jiang;;Abu Dhabi;The Ritz-Carlton Hotel, Grand Canal, Al Maqta, Abu Dhabi;24.4115601;54.485099;66;false;false;Asian;Southeast Asian dishes lead the way at this restaurant within The Ritz-Carlton hotel. All dishes are prepared with equal care – the Szechuan chilli lamb loin will certainly get your taste buds excited – but it’s the wok dishes that are their speciality. Order dishes like wok-fried scallops and butter prawns, then watch the chefs working dexterously and skilfully behind the glass screens. The friendly team run the place well and service is smooth and professional.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
10545;Li Beirut;;Abu Dhabi;Conrad Abu Dhabi Etihad Towers Hotel, West Corniche, Abu Dhabi;24.4592252;54.3214567;27;true;true;Lebanese;Its contemporary styling, views of the harbour, well-choregraphed service and good food make this Lebanese restaurant a favourite of many. The core of the menu is classic Lebanese, but the kitchen works hard here to impress, especially when it comes to presentation and the subtle addition of modern touches to some dishes. Whilst the main menu is a little more concise than many places, it is supplemented by a very useful selection of fixed price menus.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10546;Broadway;;Abu Dhabi;Emirates Palace Mandarin Oriental Hotel, West Corniche Road, Al Ras Al Akhdar, Abu Dhabi;24.4619597;54.3137286;27;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This modern, American brasserie located in the Emirates Palace Mandarin Oriental hotel is perfect for a lively evening in a Broadway-inspired setting. Combined with a DJ, live music on Saturday night, sharp service by a well-drilled team and a concise menu delivering a roll call of classics, you’ve got the ingredients for a glamourous night out with friends. The experienced chef delivers comforting dishes such as omelette Arnold Bennett, lobster bisque and their signature beef Wellington to share. Don’t miss steaks cooked to perfection and the glorious tart Tatin. They also offer a brunch on Saturday and a traditional roast on Sunday.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10547;Maté;;Abu Dhabi;Park Hyatt Abu Dhabi Hotel and Villas, Al Saadiyat Island, Abu Dhabi;24.5451318;54.4350347;40;false;false;Argentinian, Meats and Grills;Descend the stairs to the sound of pumping music and you’ll find yourself transported to Buenos Aires at his atmospheric restaurant in the Park Hyatt Hotel. The centrepiece is the open kitchen and the flaming wood-fired grills here. The menu does have some Lebanese influence but it’s really all about Argentinian dishes with great charred flavours and top ingredients, be they prawns or beef. If you really want to feel part of the action, sit at the counter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park;[]
10548;Byblos Sur Mer;;Abu Dhabi;Intercontinental Hotel, King Abdullah bin Abdul Aziz Al Saud Street, Abu Dhabi;24.4555093;54.3289003;89;false;false;Lebanese;Start your visit on the wonderful terrace and spend time admiring, or indeed coveting, the boats bobbing in the marina that it overlooks. Sharing is everything at this two-level restaurant, where the service is affable and organised. The Lebanese menu offers bags of choice – the grilled section is a good place to head to, where lamb-lovers should look no further than machawi mchakaleh. Friday and Saturday evenings see live music and entertainment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10549;Villa Toscana;;Abu Dhabi;St. Regis Hotel, Nation Towers, Corniche, Abu Dhabi;24.4641792;54.3272605;48;true;true;Italian;As you’d expect from the name, you can find many a classic Tuscan dish here at Villa Toscana, which sits within the St. Regis hotel on the Corniche waterfront. Familiar favourites like spaghetti alle vongole mix with plenty of pizzas and a wide range of other dishes to form a menu with something for everyone. On weekdays, they serve a good value business lunch comprising an extensive buffet of antipasti and desserts, plus a freshly cooked main course.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10550;Moksh;;Abu Dhabi;Conrad Etihad Towers Hotel, West Corniche, Abu Dhabi;24.4586442;54.3219763;90;false;false;Indian;Step into this bright and colourful Indian restaurant and the world will instantly seem a happier place. The menu offers a wide-ranging selection, from popular street snacks to classic favourites originating from various regions across the country. But what makes the food a little different is that the kitchen is unafraid of adding its own contemporary touches, while all the while respecting traditional flavours. We suggest starting off with the colourful chaat served in fine and crisp puris and ensure you finish with the well-presented kulfi.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10551;Namak;;Abu Dhabi;Dusit Thani Hotel, Sultan Bin Zayed The First Street (Al Muroor Road), Abu Dhabi;24.4568086;54.3934778;74;true;false;Indian;A culinary voyage around India drawing on myriad influences is the draw here at this colourful restaurant within the Dusit Thani hotel. The passion of the kitchen team really comes through in the carefully prepared dishes. The lamb specialities are particularly good, whether that’s Kashmiri Rogan Josh or Kakori Reshmi Seekh. There’s plenty for vegetarians too, including sharing platters.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
10552;José by Pizarro;;Abu Dhabi;Conrad Etihad Towers Hotel, West Corniche, Corniche Road, Abu Dhabi;24.4580443;54.3211887;91;false;false;Spanish;A small space on the ground floor of the Conrad Etihad Towers Hotel is the chosen venue for José Pizarro's first venture outside London but, instead of adopting a similarly rustic look for his tapas bar, the designers have used plenty of marble to create a more elegant environment. The small sharing plates include great anchovies, satisfying meatballs in a spicy tomato sauce and the unmissable chocolate pot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10553;Coya;;Abu Dhabi;The Galleria, Four Seasons Al Maryah Island Hotel, Abu Dhabi;24.5021364;54.3878606;42;false;true;Peruvian;Whether you like your Peruvian flavours complemented with Japanese, Chinese or Spanish influences, you’ll find you have plenty of options. Ceviche is always a great choice to begin, while the ‘Chilean sea bass rice iron pot’ is a popular signature dish. Several elegant dining rooms provide a colourful stage for the vibrant food, while the floor to ceiling windows make the most of the waterfront location. The set lunch menu is always good value.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10555;Mijana;;Abu Dhabi;The Ritz-Carlton Hotel, Grand Canal, Al Maqta, Abu Dhabi;24.4118139;54.4846033;36;false;true;Lebanese;Classical Lebanese cooking is served here against an elegant and stylish backdrop provided by the luxurious Ritz-Carlton hotel. The menu offers a comprehensive array of traditional dishes from the region, a large selection of hot and cold mezzeh, and plenty of satisfying options from the grill – the mashawee mshakaleh includes four different meats. Finish the night with a shisha pipe on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10558;Zuma;;Abu Dhabi;Abu Dhabi Global Market,  The Galleria Al Maryah Island, Abu Dhabi;24.5006304;54.3879978;65;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Gliding down the softly lit staircase allows everyone to feel like they’re about to arrive at the best party in town – this really is Fun Central, with the music to prove it. As with all other Zuma branches around the globe, the menu covers a multitude of Japanese bases, with seafood from the robata grill being the standout, although the signature corn-fed baby chicken rightly has many admirers too.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10559;Yadoo's House;;Abu Dhabi;Al Nasr Tower 2, Al Murror Street, Abu Dhabi;24.4303082;54.4335086;47;true;false;Emirati Cuisine;Sitting beneath an apartment block in the suburb of Rabdan is this likeable spot. The purpose-built white space was always going to be a challenge when it came to giving it personality, but assorted artefacts and articles like spice sacks and a sewing machine go some way towards creating the look of ‘Grandma’s house’. The Emirati cooking is done with care and respect for tradition and the portions are as big as the prices are low. We suggest starting with the katlees, followed by the majbous and save room to finish off with the luqaimat.;Air conditioning;[]
10560;Finz;;Abu Dhabi;Beach Rotana Hotel, 10th Street, Al Zahiyah, Abu Dhabi;24.4949487;54.3854615;44;false;false;Seafood;Eating seafood by the sea – there aren’t many things in life that can beat it. At Finz the fish and shellfish come in a variety of styles to suit all tastes, so if you want to feel you’re holidaying on the Med you can order fruits de mer or moules marinières, while those who prefer a more Asian theme can try the tempura roll or teriyaki salmon. The charming service is another delight here.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10561;Al Farah;;Abu Dhabi;Khalidiyah St, Al Khalidiyah, W8, Abu Dhabi;24.4707987;54.3442316;96;true;true;Middle Eastern;The first thing you’ll notice at this bright, contemporary restaurant is a queue of people picking up their orders of manaqeesh and the fresh breads coming out of the oven. The extensive menu offers a range of flavoursome Middle Eastern dishes and it’s a popular destination for breakfast. The restaurant is right in the heart of Al Khalidiyah and is part of a group of family-owned establishments.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10563;Mazi;;Abu Dhabi;St. Regis Saadiyat Island Resort, Abu Dhabi;24.5394965;54.4243809;67;false;true;Greek;If you have a hankering to holiday in the Greek Islands, then bring some friends here to get yourself in the mood. Mazi began life in London in 2012 and continues here at the impressive St. Regis Saadiyat Island Resort, where olive and palm trees decorate the charming terrace. Flavours are traditionally Greek but modernised with smart twists, and the fresh tasting dishes are designed for sharing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10564;Oii;;Abu Dhabi;Al Qana Marina South, Al Maqta’ Street, Abu Dhabi;24.4020853;54.4958903;15;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Meaning ‘hi’ in Portuguese, Oii is located in Al Qana Marina, next to The National Aquarium. On the inside, this relaxed and casual spot is light and airy, thanks to its floor to ceiling windows, while the outside’s spacious, shaded terrace is ideal al fresco dining. Expect a wide-ranging breakfast menu, followed by a Mediterranean-inspired selection of smaller and larger colourful plates, snacks and salads. One way to start your meal is with a grilled octopus with vibrant mojo rojo, followed by the spiced peri peri baby chicken and finish with fruity passion fruit semi freddo.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
10565;Martabaan by Hemant Oberoi;;Abu Dhabi;Emirates Palace Mandarin Oriental Hotel, West Corniche Road, Al Ras Al Akhdar, Abu Dhabi;24.4614192;54.3174599;25;true;false;Indian;In contrast to the huge Emirates Palace hotel in which its located, this Indian restaurant occupies a surprisingly small and intimate space. Its eponymous chef has considerable experience around the world and the menu encompasses all his favourite dishes. The tasting menu is the best form of discovery. The enthusiasm of the service team is thoroughly infectious, and their recommendations are always worth heeding.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10566;Butcher & Still;;Abu Dhabi;Four Seasons Al Maryah Island Hotel, 2 Global Market Street, Al Maryah Island, Abu Dhabi;24.5019257;54.3880649;15;false;true;Meats and Grills;Those who like a classic steakhouse will find this one at the luxurious Four Seasons ticks all the boxes. Leather banquettes? Check. Prime American beef? Check. Great cocktails? Check. Start with the generously proportioned crab cake before diving into a steak – there are plenty on offer, from ribeye to porterhouse. To finish, there’s New York cheesecake of course, but the more adventurous should take on the challenge of the Tribune Tower chocolate cake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10568;Grand Beirut;;Abu Dhabi;Unit 12100-1201 (FB), Level 2, The Galleria Al Maryah Island, Adgm Square, Al Maryah Island, Abu Dhabi;24.5011831;54.3901097;88;true;true;Lebanese;Under the same management as Beirut Sur Mer, this restaurant offers just the thing for refuelling after a gruelling day of shopping around Abu Dhabi. The Lebanese dishes are designed for sharing and generously sized, while proving to be full of flavour and founded upon quality ingredients. Be sure to leave room for their delicious kunafa.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10570;Bord Eau by Nicolas Isnard;;Abu Dhabi;Level 3, Lobby Level, Shangri-La Qaryat Al Beri Hotel, Abu Dhabi;24.4065423;54.4906788;82;false;true;French;This outpost of French chef Nicolas Isnard from Auberge de Charme, in the Côte-d'Or in France, champions inventive French classics and dishes inspired by his travels around the world. It's a spacious and high-ceilinged room, decorated with contemporary chandeliers and large tables. Choose between an à la carte or one of two tasting menus: 'French classics' or 'Travels around the world', which takes influence from the chef’s adventures around the globe. The ambitious and generously sized dishes are boldly flavoured, suitably adventurous, combine classics with a modern flare and use first class ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10571;terra;;Abu Dhabi;Al Qana, Rabdan, Abu Dhabi;24.4030185;54.4926709;66;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;At the quieter end of Al Qana yet still with a view of the boats in the marina, sits terra – relatively new to Abu Dhabi but with a well-established branch in Dubai. Being a Mediterranean restaurant, it’s appropriately relaxed in style and the great music makes it a particularly good choice for dinner. Most of the countries that line the Med get a mention and all the classics are here, including raw dishes and pizza, starters like burrata and croquettes, and plenty of pasta dishes and meats from the Josper oven.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
10572;HAUT;Belgium;Oostende;Leopold III-Laan 2 28.01, Oostende, 8400, Belgium;51.2275327;2.9245179;16;false;false;Modern French;The 28th floor of SKY Towers is entirely occupied by Belgium’s highest restaurant. The natural serenity of the venue together with the stunning view of the North Sea and the Belgian coast are worth the trip alone. All the more so, when you learn that chef Dimitri Proost’s cooking is fully equal to this high-flying setting. The cuisine is depicted by subtly distinctive Japanese notes, illustrated by a juicy seabass served in a dashi made from fish bones, which he pairs with clams and a velvety smoked butter sauce. Natural and blissfully legible thanks to the subtle talent of a chef you can trust with flavours.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10573;The Black Knife;Belgium;Wellen;Plattestraat 41, Wellen, 3830, Belgium;50.8514642;5.3418579;49;true;false;French Contemporary;The pared-back, industrial interior of The Black Knife is far more stylish than its exterior may suggest. Maitre d’ and sommelier Thomas greets diners elegantly and warmly, while chef Yanaika Skrzyszkowia brings her “food art” to life. She avows a weakness for Asian notes and her way with punchy, gutsy sauces can be tasted immediately. For example, she might marinate hamachi to enhance its subtle acidity before scattering shavings of red beetroot for visual appeal and then adding a coulis of beetroot and a sorbet of red shiso. This rebellious chef has matured and her creativity both convinces and astounds.;Air conditioning;[]
10574;Le Beau Rivage by Curtis;Belgium;Dave;Rue du Rivage 8, Dave, 5100, Belgium;50.4146843;4.8851005;56;true;false;Modern French;Curtis Maquet has breathed new life into the Beau Rivage. This landmark of Namur is idyllically located on the banks of the Meuse and its elegant interior commands a fine view of this picture postcard scene. The youthful chef learned the trade at La Table de Maxime, hence his delicate, expressive repertory, steeped in familiar and elegant, yet punchy flavours. His salmon trout cooked in its skin is a masterclass of culinary virtuosity, whose intense flavour is enhanced by a cream of white cabbage, savoury bouchot mussels and apricot jelly, and then further heightened by a beurre blanc and a vegetable oil. The sommelier’s insightful wine tips and the attentive service of the maitre d’ add the final touch.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10575;L'Orangerie de Moulbaix;Belgium;Moulbaix;Place Henri Stourme 1, Moulbaix, 7812, Belgium;50.602233;3.7133527;65;false;true;French;The bright and airy orangery at Moulbaix Castle presents itself as a tasteful blend of the old and the new. The terrace overlooking the vines, the castle and the windmill in the distance are simply idyllic! Maxence Bouralha and Charles-Maxime Legrand, the chef duo behind Quai no. 4, join forces with Philippe Lartigue to create meticulously prepared hearty French brasserie classics. Think sautéed mushrooms with finely chopped shallot topped with an indulgent potato emulsion, an œuf parfait (slow-cooked egg) that really lives up to its name, as well a touch of orange to provide a bright and zesty finish. Other tempting options are prawn croquettes, vol-au-vent or andouillette. The extensive menu is sure to please.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10576;Auberge du Château de Leignon par Isabelle Arpin;Belgium;Leignon;Rue du Sacré-Coeur 1, Leignon, 5590, Belgium;50.2720744;5.1103309;59;true;true;Farm to table;Today, the neo-Gothic Château de Leignon is home to a variety of businesses, including a brewery and, of course, this charming restaurant run by Isabelle Arpin, whose market-fresh cuisine showcases ingredients from local producers. Look forward to playful dishes that draw inspiration from all over the world – for example, she pairs brill with barley infused with coffee, artichoke, a creamy fish sauce and a sabayon with aged rum. Be sure to sample the creations of the local brewery, whose beers frequently find their way into the desserts.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10577;Wan Thai Food;Belgium;Châtelet;Rue du Commerce 4, Châtelet, 6200, Belgium;50.4046242;4.521417;57;false;true;Thai;A meal at Wan Thai Food is an education in just how irresistible authentic Thai cuisine can be. The decor featuring plenty of wood and bamboo, lanterns, Buddha statues and other Asian-inspired touches has a distinct street food feel. The extensive menu features all the classic dishes of the genre, freshly prepared by chef Wanna. Tempting options include handmade chicken gyoza served with an exquisite umami-rich soy sauce, as well as a rich fruity and spicy curry with perfectly seared scallops. The delicious sauces are definitely worth a mention! Why not add a refreshing cocktail to your order for an extra exotic kick?;Air conditioning;[]
10578;Vividu;Belgium;Harelbeke;Eikenstraat 90, Harelbeke, 8530, Belgium;50.8360283;3.3234012;83;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;The sun always shines in Gavermeer thanks to Vividu, a restaurant established in a villa that is reminiscent of Tuscany, albeit with a rock n’ roll soundtrack. The spontaneity of Nicky who is never far from your table makes the experience even warmer. Chef Laurent Messine demonstrates his passion for outstanding produce and Italy, adding his own inimitable stamp. For example, he may coat a loin of Iberico pork in a crust before cooking it in milk and then using ragusano cheese to create a gutsy sauce, all of which flanked by super-fresh side dishes. The legendary bistecca di Chianina is the house specialty, but requires pre-ordering.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10579;Tabernakel;Belgium;Bonheiden;Dorp 41, Bonheiden, 2820, Belgium;51.0223397;4.5474932;92;true;true;French Contemporary, International;Brothers Steven and Bart refuse to be hampered by a single style. As a result, you may sample an appetiser of fresh, mildly spicy baba ghanoush or a playful new twist on the traditional tomato-mozzarella bruschetta, followed by a rack of lamb in a rosemary jus. Versatile and talented, they create appetising set menus and a splendid à la carte lineup. Kim enthusiastically supervises the front-of-house, bending over backwards to ensure that you savour every morsel of your meal to the full. An elegant, neoteric industrial vibe with just the right dose of authenticity.;Air conditioning;[]
10580;Babam;Belgium;Watermael-Boitsfort;Avenue du Bois de la Cambre 25, Watermael-Boitsfort, 1170, Belgium;50.8095939;4.3957625;41;false;false;French Contemporary;Babam is the sort of neighbourhood restaurant next-door to which we would all like to live. Bistronomic cuisine is second nature to the youthful team of chefs, who all trained in top establishments. They might prepare shrimp fritters with textbook precision, flanked by a yuzu jelly and a light bisque. Alternatively, they might jazz up a wing of poached skate with an exciting contrasting touch of fresh acidity. Their crème brûlée dessert is to die for. Whether you pop in for lunch (concise menu) or the full works in the evening, we warrant you will wish you could take out a monthly subscription to Babam!;;[]
10581;Norman's Neighbourhood Kitchen;United Kingdom;Kirkburton;22A North Road, Kirkburton, HD8 0RH, United Kingdom;53.6127335;-1.7049829;19;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Asian Influences;The name (almost) says it all here: it is indeed an endearing neighbourhood bistro, but Norman is not in fact the owner – instead, it’s the name of both the owner’s dog and his grandfather. Rustic décor adds to the welcoming feel, as do the polite, helpful service team. The great value sharing plates incorporate influences from both the Mediterranean and Japan, while the ‘eggy bread’ with bacon jam shows off the chefs’ playful side. The wine list is concise but, refreshingly, it’s all available by the glass.;;[]
10582;1887;United Kingdom;Achnasheen;The Torridon, Achnasheen, IV22 2EY, United Kingdom;57.52892;-5.52819;100;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated on the banks of Upper Loch Torridon with majestic mountains in the background and manicured gardens outside, this vibrantly decorated restaurant inside The Torridon hotel is in a truly stunning location. The kitchen’s local and sustainable ethos results in superb Highlands produce from hand-dived West Coast scallop to Ross-shire lamb, in dishes that demonstrate a mature ‘less is more’ approach where the accompaniments enhance rather than mask the central ingredients. An extensive global whisky collection adds to the appeal.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10583;Tassili;United Kingdom;Saint Helier;Esplanade, Saint Helier, JE2 3QA, United Kingdom;49.187297;-2.1161601;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Overlooking St Aubin's Bay, this intimate restaurant inside the Grand Jersey Hotel offers a haven of luxury, not only in its opulent surroundings but also in the ingredients used. While you relax in the elegant room with linen-clad tables, you can expect to enjoy Jersey produce from blue lobster to Angus beef, not to mention excellent wild turbot. While their components are classically luxurious, there’s some playfully creative touches to the dishes. Bespoke wine flights are available to complement the cooking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10584;Kioku by Endo;United Kingdom;London;Raffles London at The OWO, 6th Floor, 2 Whitehall Place, Whitehall, London, SW1A 2BD, United Kingdom;51.5056158;-0.1263321;46;false;false;Japanese Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Enjoy a cocktail or two in the elegant ground-floor bar before heading up to this restaurant at the top of the Raffles hotel inside the spectacular Old War Office. Superb city skyline views await you, while a seat on the terrace is a must in warmer weather. With a name meaning ‘memories’, the menu fuses Endo Kazutoshi’s Japanese heritage with his Mediterranean training, resulting in dishes ranging from lobster fregola to stand-out nigiri. For a special occasion, book the chef’s table or even the private room in a turret.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10585;Cloth;United Kingdom;London;44 Cloth Fair, City of London, London, EC1A 7JQ, United Kingdom;51.5188725;-0.1000817;58;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A hidden gem within the City of London, this sweetly run restaurant is just a stone’s throw from Smithfield Market, tucked down a narrow lane inside a period house which was once home to the poet Sir John Betjeman. It’s now under the watchful eye of Chef Tom Hurst and wine merchants Joe and Ben, who operate the tightly packed space as part bar, part restaurant, but all full of atmosphere. The cooking is pared-back and ingredient-led, with fine produce like Dorset crab and Somerset lamb given the space to shine. The wine list, as you’d expect, is extensive and full of interesting choices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10586;Goat On The Roof;United Kingdom;Newbury;1 Bridge Street, Newbury, RG14 5BE, United Kingdom;51.4014054;-1.3242528;38;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Bright, colourful décor welcomes you into this former banqueting hall, where the shelves are filled to bursting with pickled and foraged ingredients. It’s an elegant spot, with marble-topped tables lending the place an upmarket bistro feel. The menu is appealingly varied, with ‘smaller’ and ‘bigger’ plates joined by breads, dips and skewers – none of which will break the bank. The Trealy Farm ham and Winchester cheese croquettes, along with some knockout crispy potatoes, are great examples of the kitchen’s talents. The impressive wine list includes a broad range by the glass.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
10587;The Tartan Fox;United Kingdom;Summercourt;Carvynick Farm, A3058, Summercourt, TR8 5AF, United Kingdom;50.3686984;-4.9844695;25;false;false;British Contemporary;The location in the middle of Cornwall may be a long way from Scotland but, as the name suggests, Adam Handling finds a way to incorporate his Celtic heritage into this stone-built country pub. Another venture in his ever-expanding empire, it’s a sympathetically refitted 17th-century inn located on a popular holiday caravan park. You can expect to find the likes of a haggis Scotch egg and even a deep-fried Mars bar among the extensive menu of generous pubby favourites filled with bold, well-balanced flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10588;Baba'de;Ireland;Baltimore;The Mews, Baltimore, P81 TC64, Ireland;51.4832514;-9.3728825;59;true;true;Turkish;With a name meaning ‘Baby Dede’, this second Baltimore venture from Chef Ahmet Dede is an ode to his family and comes with all the homespun charm you’d expect. Located mere feet away from his acclaimed flagship restaurant, this is a more relaxed affair but the great value sharing plates retain the older sibling’s ethos of Turkish flavours married with Irish produce. Each dish – from a unique take on oyster chowder to Ahmet’s signature ‘içli köfte’ – is bright, fresh and wholly satisfying.;Air conditioning;[]
10589;AGORA;United Kingdom;London;4 Bedale Street, Borough Market, London, SE1 9AL, United Kingdom;51.5054399;-0.0900645;30;false;false;Greek;Located on the edge of Borough Market, underneath its sister restaurant OMA, is this simple yet brilliantly effective ‘souvla bar’. Skewers are at the core of the menu – like the excellent slow-roast pork souvlaki – but it would be foolish to overlook the wonderful range of dips and beautifully puffed flatbreads served straight from the oven. It’s stripped-back cooking done with great skill, resulting in dishes so satisfying you’ll want to order them twice. They're deservedly busy, so make sure you snap up one of the limited bookings or get here for midday when they open.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10590;allta;Ireland;Dublin City;1 Three Locks Square, Grand Canal Dock, Dublin City, DO2 A5W7, Ireland;53.3449113;-6.2313238;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;After years of moving around Dublin at festivals and pop-ups, the talented team behind allta finally have a permanent home in this spacious dockside building in a swish area of the city. The space is split into two parts: an industrial-chic cocktail bar complete with DJ and a separate dining room with an open kitchen where guests can sit at the counter. The cooking has a strong Irish base, with quality seafood from Union Hall prawns to day-boat sole making an appearance. If you like your dessert with a side of nostalgia, go for the soft serve ice cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
10591;The Hero;United Kingdom;London;55 Shirland Road, Maida Vale, London, W9 2JD, United Kingdom;51.5243387;-0.188812;27;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Maida Vale residents hit the jackpot when the owners of Notting Hill’s The Pelican and The Bull in Charlbury chose this neighbourhood for the location for their third venture. The Hero is like a blueprint for how to sympathetically restore and update a pub, and has been understandably packed since Day One. The ground floor offers a great value list of classic pub dishes, from fish pie to sausage and mash. Upstairs is ‘The Grill’, where things are taken up a level with dishes like sweetbreads and lobster gravy.;;[]
10592;mrDeanes;United Kingdom;Belfast;28-40 Howard Street, Belfast, BT1 6PF, United Kingdom;54.5957807;-5.9327602;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Its full name, ‘mrDeanes Bistro, Bar and Social’, paints a perfect picture of this spacious addition to Michael Deane’s ever-evolving Belfast empire. Grab a cocktail at the bar before taking your seat in a restaurant that’s bursting with vitality. The eminently appealing menu offers well-executed takes on dishes from all over the world, be it Gaeng Phed red curry or ‘entrecôte au poivre’. There's a palpable generosity to the place too, with the food and wine both offering great value for money.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10593;Lita;United Kingdom;London;7-9 Paddington Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 5QH, United Kingdom;51.520828;-0.1526149;100;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Cooking with fire is all the rage these days and Lita, which opened in 2024, is another expert practitioner, although it also offers so much more. While there’s a strong Mediterranean and southern European element to the menu, prime British ingredients – such as Scottish langoustines and Norfolk quail – along with big, bold flavours and well-made sauces really make the dishes sing. Many of the plates are designed for sharing, like succulent Cornish lamb with smoked aubergine and sheep’s milk. This is roll-up-your-sleeves sort of food – the type that leaves you licking your lips and planning your return.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10594;Gorse;United Kingdom;Cardiff;186-188 Kings Road, Cardiff, CF11 9DF, United Kingdom;51.4861304;-3.2000614;21;false;false;Modern British;You get a good feeling about this intimate, personally run restaurant from the moment you arrive and are greeted by the chefs in the open kitchen. Go for the longer of the tasting menus and you won’t regret your decision, as local chef Tom and his team show a great understanding of flavour and balance across dishes founded upon the bountiful Welsh larder – from seaweed and seafood to Gower salt marsh lamb. The service is genial and unobtrusive, perfectly befitting of such an impressive operation.;Air conditioning;[]
10595;Elements;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;19 New Kirk Road, Bearsden, Glasgow City, G61 3SJ, United Kingdom;55.9200727;-4.3331739;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A smart neighbourhood restaurant in a very smart neighbourhood, Elements occupies a swish, lavishly renovated premises blending royal blue fabrics with dark wood and gold furnishings. The kitchen applies classical techniques to top-quality Scottish ingredients, while incorporating some subtle international influences – West Coast langoustines combined with chawanmushi and vadouvan is a prime example. Each dish delivers an interesting range of flavours and textures, without ever being too showy in its makeup. The on-display wine is a nod to the well-stocked list featuring something for every palate and purse.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10596;AVERY;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;54 Saint Stephen Street, Edinburgh, EH3 5AL, United Kingdom;55.9578621;-3.2064362;18;true;true;Creative;When American chef Rodney Wages visited Edinburgh on holiday, he fell in love with the city so much that he decided to move himself, his family and his restaurant here. And that's how Avery, which once graced the streets of San Francisco, came to be located in a classic Georgian townhouse in Stockbridge. Rodney has wholly embraced his Scottish surroundings, taking the country's bountiful produce and treating it with a Californian lightness, while providing bold, distinct flavours – like Orkney scallop dressed with pineapple jus. The drinks flight combines wine, sake, sherry and, of course, a wee single malt whisky.;Air conditioning;[]
10598;Dallmayr Bar & Grill;Germany;Munich;Dienerstraße 14, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1382946;11.5771646;45;false;false;Farm to table, International;Located next to the delicatessen on the ground floor, this Dallmayr restaurant is steeped in tradition and offers a lively and relaxed, yet stylish dining experience. At closely spaced tables, diners enjoy prompt and adept service provided by a courteous and well-staffed front-of-house team in white uniforms. From oysters and caviar to seafood and Bavarian ribeye with balsamic pearl-glazed onions, the international menu certainly whets the appetite. Be sure to sample the beef tomato with feta, honey and sesame. The bar is another highlight, perfect for unwinding with a pre-dinner drink.;Air conditioning;[]
10599;Waldschlössle;Germany;Fellbach;Auf dem Kappelberg 2, Fellbach, 70734, Germany;48.7977602;9.2851825;20;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;After driving past seemingly endless rows of vines, you will eventually reach this small vineyard, where a traditional mountain inn has been reimagined as a trendy and modern dining destination. Floor-to-ceiling windows showcase breathtaking panoramic views of the region. There is also a terrace. "Fine Swabian cuisine" is the name of the game at this restaurant, which is run by a young couple – Annika Braun presides front-of-house and her husband, Manuel, is the chef. He mainly uses locally sourced ingredients, following the seasonal availability of produce, and also likes to incorporate elements of other cuisines. The menu includes dishes such as vitello forello (medium-rare boiled veal, smoked trout cream, Fellbach verjus) and Brunnenhof Mäusdorf rooster with crispy skin accompanied by a sour vegetable chutney, artichoke purée and polenta sticks.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10600;Ziegler;Germany;Weinheim;Sachsenstraße 39, Weinheim, 69469, Germany;49.5203285;8.66885;31;true;true;International, Contemporary;It is well worth making the trip to Jacqueline and Alexander Hahn's restaurant in the Hohensachsen neighbourhood, where you will be rewarded with a pleasant atmosphere and really good food. Not only is the quality spot-on, but there is also an impressive array of dishes, ranging from classic options like Zwiebelrostbraten or Wiener schnitzel to international offerings such as Kashmir curry soup or beef fillet tataki. Food is served in an upscale, tastefully modern setting featuring clean lines and soothing tones.;;[]
10601;NIGHTINGALE;Germany;Dachau;Augsburger Straße 19, Dachau, 85221, Germany;48.2599619;11.4327862;79;true;true;Thai, International;Having spent years in the bustling metropolis of Bangkok, Dominik and May Carqueville are bringing a slice of the Far East to Dachau. Born and raised in Thailand, the chef has an innate talent for working with authentic Thai flavours. She skilfully incorporates contemporary influences and locally-sourced ingredients into the traditional cuisine of her homeland. Using only the freshest ingredients, she crafts dishes such as Ma Hor (caramelised minced pork with peanuts, pineapple, coriander and chilli) or pan-seared sea bass fillet in a choo chee curry sauce with kaffir lime leaves. Dishes can also be ordered to share. The trendy and chic setting is a combination of restaurant and bar – the latter serves cocktails, beer, wine and house-made soft drinks, as well as finger food. The name "Nightingale" is a nod to Bangkok's vibrant nightlife.;Terrace;[]
10602;Landgasthof zum Kaffelstein;Germany;Kreuzwertheim;Hauptstraße 18, Kreuzwertheim, 97892, Germany;49.7649687;9.5160472;73;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Contemporary;Having already proven his talent at Kuno 1408 in Würzburg, Daniel Schröder has now struck out alone here with a dual concept: In addition to fine dining at La Boucherie, you can look forward to delicious seasonal cuisine in this lovely alternative. The menu is pared down to a limited number of dishes that focus on the essentials, leaving nothing to chance in terms of expression and flavour. In summer, the terrace in the courtyard is a pleasant place to sit. The hotel also has spruce, modern guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
10603;Die Speiserei im Maier;Germany;Friedrichshafen;Poststraße 1, Friedrichshafen, 88048, Germany;47.6697839;9.4149085;37;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The restaurant at Hotel Maier, a family-run establishment since its founding as a café and guesthouse in 1936, showcases fresh seasonal produce that is for the most part organic and sourced as locally as possible. Order à la carte or opt for one of three set menus (one of them is vegetarian), each comprising three to four courses. The setting is inviting: the original traditional character of the interior has been preserved with the addition of subtle elegant and modern touches. There is also a spacious courtyard terrace for those who prefer to dine al fresco. Friendly and professional service.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10604;au lac 51;Germany;Rottach-Egern;Seestraße 51, Rottach-Egern, 83700, Germany;47.6959005;11.7630112;29;false;false;International, Seasonal Cuisine;The location on the promenade is fabulous – in summer, tables on the terrace overlooking the lake are in great demand! But you can also take in the vista from indoors – the window seats here are popular, too. The owners of this cosy modern restaurant, Dieter Maiwert and Frank Heppner, are a well-established team with a strong reputation on the culinary scene. Featuring a diverse range of options, from classic favourites to Mediterranean and Asian-inspired dishes, the menu has something for everyone. Friendly and adept service.;Terrace;[]
10605;Tiny Lou's;USA;Atlanta;789 Ponce De Leon Ave. NE, Atlanta, 30306, USA;33.7737467;-84.3614692;98;true;true;French;Named for the popular 1950s dancer in the Clermont Motor Hotel’s “Gypsy Room,” Tiny Lou's is tucked inside the hip Hotel Clermont. Look for the pink neon sign, then descend the stairs to the trendy space set with a moody tone and French vibes. French classics mingle with American comfort food on a menu that showcases Georgian ingredients and a bit of Southern style. The cooking is approachable and earnest, as in wild striped bass with skin that's been crisped to perfection. Served with asparagus, it's the kind of plate where every component is well-executed. The desserts are also a must, with varied takes of the crépe cake and blondie always on the menu, and others always changing. If that means you need to order a few, then so be it.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
10606;The Deer and the Dove;USA;Decatur;155 Sycamore St., Decatur, 30030, USA;33.7747044;-84.2951899;31;true;false;Contemporary, Southern;Chef/owner Terry Koval and his talented team create memorable dishes at this restaurant with a lovely, rustic feel. First up? House-made salted yeast rolls, served hot alongside garden herb butter, then the harvest plate with a beautiful display of vegetables, that's perfect for sharing. House-made pappardelle tossed with morels, whipped lemon ricotta and parmesan is an elevated dish of comfort, while the smoked duck hits the spot. Crisply skinned duck served alongside duck leg pâté en croûte with Hudson Valley foie gras and a glossy duck bone jus is just right. Cocktails are especially fun, as in the "There's Always Money in the Banana Stand," with Horyzon koji rice spirit, house banana liqueur, house orgeat and tiki bitters.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10607;Delbar;USA;Atlanta;870 Inman Village Pkwy. NE, Atlanta, 30307, USA;33.7617129;-84.3601768;94;false;true;Middle Eastern;This Middle Eastern spot from Fares Kargar is all about bringing people together over flavorful and authentic food. There is a generous spirit here, where the name translates to "heart, captured." The menu, a nod to the dishes Kargar grew up with, is designed for sharing, with spreads and small bites to start, an entire section dedicated to tahdig, that festive Persian crispy rice dish, and meats. Add the dill labneh to the house bread opener, then go for the lamb neck that is falling-off-the-bone tender, and sabzi polo, a basmati rice dish flavored with scallions and herbs and topped with crispy onions. Conclude the evening with a decadent treat like baklava ice cream or pistachio lava cake with cardamom ice cream.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10608;Woo Nam Jeong;USA;Atlanta;5953 Buford Hwy. NE, Atlanta, 30340, USA;33.912964;-84.2618609;40;false;true;Korean;Anchoring the corner of a shopping center along Buford Highway, this busy spot features an expansive Korean menu. With so many options, it may be difficult to pick just one but start with a seafood or kimchi pancake or their seared mandu and you won't go wrong. Then, plenty of specialties tempt but you're here for one in particular: the house specialty "stone bowl" bibimbap. Take a peek at the neighboring tables and nearly everyone is tucking into one of these signature dishes. Bulgogi, or tender beef, is the classic order, and it arrives in the stone bowl sizzling long after it is set atop the table. Rice that has been crisped sits at the base, with beef, vegetables, and a sunny side up egg on top for a delicious one-pot dish that will make you a regular in no time.;;[]
10609;Marcel;USA;Atlanta;1170 Howell Mill Rd. NW, Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.7857171;-84.4121167;88;true;false;Steakhouse;Here on the west side of town, take a step back in time at this vintage steakhouse named for French boxer, Marcel Cerdan. From the low lighting to the red leather banquette, Ford Fry has created a speakeasy-style space that checks all the boxes. It comes with a high price tag, certainly, but who cares when you're having this much fun? The menu features a few French and European elements in addition to classic dishes. Start with a salad or go big with steak tartare with bone marrow and sourdough. The many steaks include a bone-in côte de boeuf or 60-day dry-aged ribeye. Don't skimp on the sides with French leanings, including pommes aligot and pommes Dauphinoise. Keep things decadent through dessert with a slice of rich chocolate cake.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10611;Hen Mother Cookhouse;USA;Johns Creek;11705 Jones Bridge Rd., Johns Creek, 30005, USA;34.0653715;-84.210747;95;false;false;American;Located up in Johns Creek, Hen Mother Cookhouse has a setting that befits its name. This charmer has kitschy farmhouse down pat with blue walls, white-painted bench seating, and wood tables, while Chef/owner Soraya Khoury's menu of breakfast and brunch favorites has exactly what you want. From avocado toast and quiche to Southern classics like sourdough waffles with fried chicken, if you want (and you most certainly do), mornings are met with a bevy of delicious choices, but it doesn't end there. Come lunch and BLTs, burgers, and baked goods are the perfect order. No matter your selection, it's all prepared with skill and care, and you'll have a hard time putting down your fork (though the portions are generous, and sides are shareable).;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10612;Nàdair;USA;Atlanta;1123 Zonolite Rd. NE, #15, Atlanta, 30306, USA;33.8064869;-84.3441301;54;false;false;Scottish, Southern;From the pops of plaid and the jade-green painted wood panels to the rugs inspired by the tartan worn by the chef's grandfather in the Scottish Royal Regiment during World War I, there is no mistaking the inspiration behind Chef Kevin Gillespie's restaurant. It's a tribute to his heritage in more than just looks, though. The Scottish-leaning, contemporary menu (prix fixe or a multicourse tasting) is at once clever and approachable. Smoked sweet Georgia shrimp, clams and mussels in a butter and shellfish foam with crumbled oatcakes is just one of the successful dishes. A round of Stornoway white pudding topped with a single roasted Maine scallop is bold yet balanced. To finish, the “Tipsy Laird” trifle is straightforward yet simply fantastic.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10613;The Chastain;USA;Atlanta;4320 Powers Ferry Rd. NW, Atlanta, 30342, USA;33.8731698;-84.3964879;91;true;false;American;Set on the verdant edges of Chastain Park and surrounded by trees, this restaurant feels like a modern oasis with charming details (think butterscotch leather booths, exposed brick elements and gas lamps). The setting is stunning, reminding one of a restored carriage house, but Chef Christopher Grossman's seasonally focused American menu with Southern nods is a solid match.  Wondering what to order? You won't go wrong with the beer-battered Dover Sole with sauce gribiche and arugula fennel salad. Mac and cheese is a perfect side, and don't skip dessert, especially the apple-pecan frangipane tart with orange blossom cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
10614;Food Terminal;USA;Atlanta;5000 Buford Hwy., Atlanta, 30341, USA;33.888008;-84.2871274;29;true;false;Malaysian;Chef/owner Amy Wong's Food Terminal may have multiple locations, but the Buford Highway original will always stand out from the rest. Located within a cavernous space that sports a contemporary feel (think exposed ducts, charcoal-gray walls and metal chairs), it's designed to resemble a night market. As for the food, it's Malaysian at its core. The massive menu is matched only by the portions, perfect for enjoying family style. It's a celebration of the cultural mash-up that is Malaysia with dishes like garlic noodles, made in house and tossed in a garlic sauce with spinach and mushrooms. It's so good it's nearly impossible to put your chopsticks down. Fried curry chicken nasi lemak features their take on the classic dish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10615;LanZhou Ramen;USA;Atlanta;5231 Buford Hwy. NE, Atlanta, 30340, USA;33.8951385;-84.2820048;56;false;true;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;Located on Buford Highway in a busy shopping center, LanZhou is both the name of a Chinese city and a type of hand-pulled noodle that just so happens to be this spot's main attraction. Those delicious noodles are available in hearty soups with a variety of proteins, and also come broth-less. From there, broad Sichuan-leaning dishes tempt diners. Fried pot stickers sport a beautiful crispy, lacy base and delight with a savory goodness. Roast duck hand-pulled noodle soup is pure, unadulterated satisfaction, slurp by glorious slurp. Served in a massive bowl bobbing with bouncy noodles, baby bok choy, roast bone-in duck and scallions, it's loaded with flavor and will certainly cure whatever ails you.;Car park;[]
10616;Chai Pani;USA;Decatur;406 W. Ponce De Leon Ave., Decatur, 30030, USA;33.7761573;-84.3011185;79;true;false;Indian, Regional Cuisine;Decatur's Chai Pani is a festive place, where strings of lights and colorful artwork keep things high spirited, and the kitchen looks to locally sourced ingredients to create the seasonally minded South Asian dishes. The versatile menu is detailed with enticing descriptions that may just to convince you to try one more dish, and there are plenty of options for family-style dining. Whether dining a deux or with a group, enjoy the likes of butter chicken, that deliciously rich staple of boneless chicken in a tomato-cream butter sauce, or fried okra, with its ever so easy to eat lightly seasoned shards. Gobi pepper fry, a popular hybrid Chinese and Indian dish, is given a unique slant here with battered cauliflower that's both tart and spicy.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10617;Lyla Lila;USA;Atlanta;693 Peachtree St. NE, Atlanta, 30308, USA;33.7736342;-84.3846983;71;true;false;European;It bears repeating that Chef/owner Craig Richards' Lyla Lila is a good find. Sharing a contemporary design with a darker, moody color palette, the focus is on southern Europe with pasta as a focal point. They're a must, with house house staples like the crispy duck lasagna with a cocoa béchamel as well as seasonal dishes like the ricotta-miso gnocchetti. They're also available in appetizer portions, though their starters deserve equal billing. Don't fill up too much, as there's roast chicken, veal Milanese or snapper topped with pistachio pesto to be had. End on a sweet note with chocolate orange mousse cake or an ice cream sandwich with cherry gelato, "magic shell" and pizzelle cookies.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10618;Xi'an Gourmet House;USA;Atlanta;955 Spring St. NW, Atlanta, 30309, USA;33.7813762;-84.3887889;44;false;false;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;You won't get a lot of fuss at this Midtown spot, an offshoot of the original in Duluth. You'll order at the counter and then pick up a paper plate, but what they may lack in niceties, they make up for with dialed-in cooking. Spotlighting the Xi'an region of China, the menu focuses on biang biang noodles and as well as boiled dumplings and dishes featuring plenty of cumin and other spices. Noodles are the way to go, though it’s never a bad idea to supplement with the boldly flavorful cucumber salad, and there must be dumplings, of course. Here, they are available on their own or with soup. Choose from pork and lamb and then tuck in to a baker's dozen of simply boiled treats served with a house-made dipping sauce that brings them alive.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10619;Miller Union;USA;Atlanta;999 Brady Ave. NW, Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.782123;-84.4129161;21;true;true;American;Miller Union is named after the former Miller Union Stockyards that once encompassed a full city block in the old meatpacking district. Nestled within the refurbished warehouse on the former site, the restaurant from Steven Satterfield and Neal McCarthy is a perennial favorite. It's likely because of their seasonal American menu with a Southern twang. Start with the roasted oysters, a plate of six delicate oysters with green garlic cream, strawberry sofrito and breadcrumbs. Then tuck in to a roasted pork loin served with two scallion Johnny cakes, braised chard and roasted carrot and radish that's bested with a rhubarb chutney. It's tempting to fill up, but save room for dessert, especially the blondie, topped with apricot and orange compote and rum raisin ice cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
10620;Gunshow;USA;Atlanta;924 Garrett St., Ste. C, Atlanta, 30316, USA;33.7406252;-84.3575142;19;false;false;American;It's almost a decade in, but this spot from Top Chef contestant Chef Kevin Gillespie is firing on all cylinders. It's fun and lively, making it ideal for groups, while the multicourse menu served family-style gives the place a dinner party vibe. The cooking here is experimental and creative—you'll always discover something new.A mini tart filled with green garlic and strawberry, then topped with radicchio whipped cream and strawberry pop rocks shows off an ingenious sweet-savory blend and is proof positive that this meal is far from standard. Melting-off-the-bone pork ribs with a tamarind and rose glaze are tangy and tender, while a scoop of salted grapefruit sorbet on a Camembert cheese foam with parsnip olive oil cake is another inventive twist.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10621;Little Sparrow;USA;Atlanta;1198 Howell Mill Rd. NW, Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.7866582;-84.4123801;42;false;true;French;We'll forgive you if you're looking through rose-colored glasses after a meal here. After all, Little Sparrow was singer Édith Piaf's nickname, and this très French bistro hits all the right notes from its design to its dishes. The menu, though compact, features all the favorites albeit with a little Southern flair. Meals begin with a warm baguette and delicious butter before moving on to a fragrant and hearty onion soup and beef tartare. Entrées run the gamut from pork belly to chicken schnitzel with a mound of seasonal greens. Of course, there must be fries, and these house-made delights are thick cut and triple fried, accompanied by aïoli, Bearnaise sauce, or Raclette cheese service. End with a traditional chocolate soufflé or opt for a unique soft serve sundae.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
10623;Ticonderoga Club;USA;Atlanta;99 Krog St. NE, Ste. W, Atlanta, 30307, USA;33.7569204;-84.363891;25;true;true;Contemporary;This restaurant from Chef David Bies is located in the Krog Street Market. There's a slight tropical vibe, evidenced by the multicolored lights and vintage, mismatched stools at the bar. It's a contemporary menu split between house classics and seasonal dishes, and most are designed for sharing. Creative but uncomplicated with global touches throughout, the cooking draws a loyal following. Steak tartare is a classic, and a good beginning before moving on to mussels steamed in a flavorful sake broth. Go smaller with a plate of wok vegetables or go big with a bone-in pork chop with a pan gravy and roasted vegetables. If the tiki vibe wasn't a tip-off, there are enough rum-based cocktails here to keep any sailor happy.;Car park;[]
10624;The Alden;USA;Chamblee;5070 Peachtree Blvd., Chamblee, 30341, USA;33.88838;-84.31426;78;false;true;American, Contemporary;Warm, attentive service and a sexy, upscale dining room make The Alden a natural choice for a night out. It's the kind of place where plush leather banquettes invite guests to linger a bit longer. Atlanta native Chef Jared Huck is running the show, and his vision internationally inspired cooking is unique. Some dishes might not read regional, but local ingredients and flair ensure pride of place. Case in point? The deliciously gamey knobs of lamb bathed in a white gravy with pink peppercorns. Hot and sour red snapper is Asian inspired but locally sourced, resulting in an elegant but approachable dish. Finish with ruby red grapefruit curd over tandoori shortbread crumbs sided by a scoop of vanilla gelato with beet-hibiscus sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10625;Nam Phuong;USA;Atlanta;4051 Buford Hwy. NE, Atlanta, 30345, USA;33.8613323;-84.3078551;23;false;false;Vietnamese;Chef/owner Du Nguyen and co-owner Hoa Phan have created a welcoming spot at Nam Phuong, located in a shopping center on Buford Highway, but comfortable booths aside, all eyes are on the large menu. Staples like vermicelli noodles and fried rice are on offer, and you'll never go wrong with a bowl of pho (try pho gâu, which bobs with tender brisket and bouncy noodles). However, it's the Vietnamese street food section that demands attention with treats like bôt chiên, pan-fried rice flour cubes with egg and a sweet soy dipping sauce. No matter your selection, the dishes take some time to come out of the kitchen, since they're not cutting any corners. Come with a group, as family-style menus are designed for up to ten, sample a wide variety and offer great value.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10626;The White Bull;USA;Decatur;123 E. Court Sq., Decatur, 30030, USA;33.7751071;-84.2958783;15;true;false;American;Chef Pasquale Pascarella has created a contemporary space in the heart of Decatur. There are subtle nods to Ernest Hemingway, who famously said the blank page was his "white bull," though this is far from a theme park. This New American, seasonally minded menu has an array of small dishes, house-made pastas and main dishes, all displaying subtle and thoughtful cooking. From churning their own butter to milling their own flour, they take extra steps to ensure freshness. Kick things off with mahi crudo, then tuck in to tortelli in a butter sauce with roasted corn, fresnos, pickled enoki and parmesan. Finally, a fresh peach hand pie with lemon buttermilk gelato seals the deal.;Air conditioning;[]
10627;Snackboxe Bistro;USA;Duluth;1960 Day Dr. NW, Ste. 1000, Duluth, 30096, USA;33.9533939;-84.1321967;92;false;false;Lao, Street Food;Chef/owner Thip Athakhanh may have moved to the United States as a toddler, but her roots in western Laos come shining through at Snackboxe Bistro. The broad menu also overlaps with Thai and Vietnamese cuisine for a likeable selection of dishes that come piled so high you'll have leftovers for days (hint: bring a friend or three). Plates to not miss include wings coated in a funky-sweet jeow bong sauce with just a hint of spice, and nam khao, a classic crispy rice salad, that is a riot of flavors and textures. Made with fermented pork sausage, herbs, onions and peanuts with fish sauce, lime, rice vinegar and sugar, it's positively delicious. End on a sweet note with a slice of coconut cake or fried donuts with condensed milk.;Car park;[]
10628;Home Grown;USA;Atlanta;968 Memorial Dr. SE, Atlanta, 30316, USA;33.7468395;-84.3560586;72;false;false;American, Southern;Located in the Reynoldstown neighborhood in East Atlanta, Home Grown is a classic all-day breakfast and lunch spot complete with knotty pine paneling and booth seating. While it has a retro feel to it, don't assume you know everything on this menu. Instead, expect oodles of Southern charm and definitely ask about the daily specials, since you may come across items like house-made tamales, Gulf red snapper tacos, lasagna or even a pu pu platter with frog legs and crab claws. The focused menu stays largely local in both theme and sourcing, delivering country cooking that never disappoints. Case in point? That open-faced buttermilk biscuit layered with perfectly crisp chicken drowned in hearty pork sausage gravy, of course.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10629;Kamayan ATL;USA;Atlanta;5150 Buford Hwy. NE, Atlanta, 30340, USA;33.8936215;-84.2852336;54;false;true;Filipino;You'll see the sign, but the crowd out front will signal that you've arrived at Kamayan ATL. Once a pop-up, this place from owners Mia Orino and Carlo Gan has a serious fan base, so reservations are a must. The tables are tight but it's homey, and the busy cadence, coupled with the tropical island decor, adds to the vibe.  Tagalog for "by hand," kamayan is the traditional Filipino form of dining. Choose from a menu of family-style dishes, with a good dose of classics mixed with regional items. Lumpia are always a hit, while the sinigang, with tender pork ribs bobbing in a tamarind-based broth, is spot on. Sided by rice, it's a feast unto itself. Halo halo is on offer, but most of the items are packaged from local Filipino bakery, Hapag.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10630;Tomo;USA;Atlanta;3630 Peachtree Rd. NE, Ste. 140, Atlanta, 30326, USA;33.8545631;-84.3583142;98;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;This spot, at the bottom of the chic and modern Ritz-Carlton Residences, is a contemporary space where floor-to-ceiling windows make a big impression. In addition to tables and a sushi bar, there are four seats reserved exclusively for the omakase, arranged well in advance of your visit. Slightly Americanized, the chef's tasting menu offers eight plated courses before progressing into sushi. One dish, chu-toro nuta, presents three pieces of lightly seared tuna in a miso and rice vinegar sauce, balsamic reduction, crumbled pistachio and seared scallions for a rich and satisfying plate. Sushi, such as the decadent and flavorful kawahagi, is equally impressive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
10631;BoccaLupo;USA;Atlanta;753 Edgewood Ave. NE, Atlanta, 30307, USA;33.7547945;-84.3627584;19;false;true;Italian-American;What's not to love about a place that doesn't take itself too seriously yet cares deeply about their food? Chef/owner Bruce Logue is at the helm of this cute and casual spot  where smart cooking and modern takes on Italian-American classics lure a steady stream of regulars. It's comfort food at its best (think Southern fried chicken parm with pasta and creamy collards). Order a la carte or tuck in to a four-course tasting menu, with pasta tagging along on the savory courses. Fresh, local produce stars in many of the dishes like garganelli pasta with seared scallops and sugar snap peas in a tomato water sauce. Quirky cocktails, such as "What are you, the police?" are conversation starters (it's a gin-based milk punch clarified with Greek yogurt).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10633;Kimball House;USA;Decatur;303 E. Howard Ave., Decatur, 30030, USA;33.7718701;-84.2928828;85;true;true;Contemporary, Shellfish Specialities;Tufted leather booths, a carved bar and dark wood set a swanky tone at Kimball House, an elegant spot located in a renovated rail depot. It's the place to sip well-crafted cocktails and snack on more than 20 types of oysters (tasting notes make it easy to choose). Beef tartare with sweet-onion jalapeño chips, capers and green olives, crisp garlic and a confit egg yolk is excellent. Grouper crudo is prepared with a tomatillo and pineapple "agrodolce," for a very refreshing dish. Dessert is always a highlight. Butternut crunch cake is layer upon layer of deliciousness, with brown butter-almond sponge cake, butternut squash mousse, hickory foam, and ginger-thyme ice cream. Paris Brest is bested with hickory roasted pineapple, ginger ganache and cashew praline.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10634;Twisted Soul Cookhouse & Pours;USA;Atlanta;1133 Huff Rd. NW, Ste. D, Atlanta, 30318, USA;33.7891524;-84.4256743;86;false;true;Southern;Grab a seat at the bar, a free-standing table or slide into one of the banquettes for a taste of local chef Deborah VanTrece's Southern and soul food. Just don't expect your grandmama's cooking. Instead, Southern staples are showcased in unique ways. Try the spread sampler with pimento cheese fondue, black-eyed pea salsa and a creamy collard dip. Other starters include crawfish deviled eggs and fried green tomatoes, served with a drizzle of their comeback sauce and a corn and pepper relish. Fried chicken is always a good choice, especially when served with three-cheese mac and cheese and a collard green roll with sweet potato, apple and golden raisin chutney. Don't skip the peach cobbler, served piping hot in a Mason jar.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10635;Georgia Boy;USA;Atlanta;1043 Ponce de Leon Ave. NE, Atlanta, 30306, USA;33.7736609;-84.353001;65;true;true;Contemporary, American;You don't just walk in off the street to Georgia Boy. First, it's secreted away within Southern Belle. Then, if you're one of the diners with reservations, you'll be seated in the "library" for drinks, snacks and a hint of what's to come. Find the chef's favorite book on the shelf and voila!, a secret door opens, revealing an open kitchen. Here, Chef Joey Ward orchestrates a delicate harmony of flavors and textures in dishes such as seared diver scallop bathed in a chocolate-dark truffle and sunchoke sauce or roasted monkfish wrapped in Tennessee country ham over a spring pea raviolo and farm egg. Other courses honor seasonal ingredients, as in a silky Vidalia onion soup. Desserts, like the "lick the beater" with German chocolate cake-flavored pudding, ramp up the fun.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10636;Southern Belle;USA;Atlanta;1043 Ponce de Leon Ave. NE, Atlanta, 30306, USA;33.773943;-84.353155;72;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Southern Belle isn't just this restaurant's name—it's a description. It's oh-so-charming here, where a neon blue "Bless Your Heart" sign anchors the bar. It's also a showcase of Southern-inflected food, thanks to Chef Joey Ward and the passionate team who dole our creative dishes like gazpacho with strawberry relish and a goat milk feta foam. Seasons are played up with local vegetables taking center stage, and each course is better than the next. Roasted lamb loin is braised for hours before hitting the grill, resulting in a tender and delicious meal. Wine pairings are terrific, but the non-alcoholic pairings are a nice alternative. Don't miss the Georgia olive oil cake with lime curd and spring pea ice cream, if it's available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10637;Poor Hendrix;USA;Atlanta;2371 Hosea L. Williams Dr. SE, Bldg. 2, Atlanta, 30317, USA;33.7510299;-84.3094351;23;true;false;Contemporary;While it looks like your average corner restaurant, Poor Hendrix is so much more. It's all about the vibe at this intimate, slightly quirky spot. It’s first come first serve, and the menu changes daily with new specials that you'll want to check out (seared trout over couscous, perhaps?). Expect contemporary, updated bar food with Southern and Asian elements. Don't expect a fuss, since they don't take themselves too seriously. You'll feast on dishes like shrimp skewers dusted with a barbecue rub and served with a white Alabama-style barbecue sauce, and refreshing cold spicy peanut noodles with just the right kick. Even their cocktails hit the spot and fit perfectly at the bar, in the dining room or on their back patio.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10638;Talat Market;USA;Atlanta;112 Ormond St. SE, Ste. A, Atlanta, 30315, USA;33.731849;-84.384043;41;true;true;Thai;Located in the Summerhill neighborhood, Talat Market is equal parts industrial and vintage, with colorful design elements adding a decorate punch. This trendy no-reservations spot from Chefs/owners Parnass Savang and Rod Lassiter is all about traditional Thai flavors, utilizing the best of Georgia produce, and the bar echoes that ethos. The menu begins with a section devoted to oysters and crudo, then progresses into small plates like crispy rice salad and som tum. Yum phonlamai is a refreshing fruit salad tossed with sesame dressing—perfect for chasing the spicier dishes. Other plates like gaaeng kiew wan, a crab and pork curry, deliver subtle flavors, and curries, many using house-pressed coconut milk, are always a good idea.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10640;Entresol;Latvia;Riga;Elizabetes iela 22, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.9497103;24.1219738;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set on the ground floor of a grand city centre property, this small restaurant offers two experiences in one. The front area is filled with memorabilia and has more of a vintage lounge feel, while the raised area behind has a less-cluttered look. The good value tasting menu changes twice a year and offers a selection of modern dishes with a pleasingly unfussy approach, allowing the flavours of the excellent quality produce to shine.;Air conditioning;[]
10641;Chef's Corner;Latvia;Riga;Jeruzalemes iela 5, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.9578198;24.1139306;19;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Meats and Grills;A friendly team welcome you into this chic city centre brasserie, where you’ll do well to start with a cocktail while choosing from the classic brasserie-style menu. The emphasis is on steaks from the Netherlands, the UK and the USA, with the steaks to share proving a popular choice. Other options include everything from tartares and oysters to burgers and pastas, which are hit with locals and visitors alike.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10642;MO;Latvia;Liepaja;Friča Brīvzemnieka Iela 7, Liepaja, 3401, Latvia;56.512259;21.007816;48;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Beside the promenade in the historical canal area sits Julianna’s Courtyard, where the 19C printing house and later 20C factories have been lovingly restored to create one of Liepāja's go-to areas. Here you’ll find MO, which offers a satisfying meal out at a fair price. Ask for a table either on or overlooking the terrace, then choose from the wide-ranging menu that includes tartares, carpaccios, sharing plates and main dishes such as beef with truffle mash. Locally produced beers and cocktails make the perfect accompaniment.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10643;TAURO;Latvia;Riga;Ranķa dambis 30, Riga, 1048, Latvia;56.94697;24.08138;71;false;false;Meats and Grills;This über-smart steak restaurant is secreted away on the ground floor of the Zunda Towers skyscraper and comes with cowhides mounted to look like bulls, hence the name. Forgo starters and enjoy a generous plate of cured meats and salamis from their farm, then move on to a superb steak from Latvia, Spain, California, Japan or Australia. Accompany this with a side – the crispy potatoes with thyme are a must – and one of their freshly made sauces in myriad flavours. The 300+ bin wine list is beautifully curated, with some of the North American classics creating the perfect pairings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10644;Pavāru māja;Latvia;Līgatne;Pilsoņu iela 2, Līgatne, 4110, Latvia;57.2353497;25.0421338;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;A former maternity hospital on the edge of a rural village plays host to this smart, modern restaurant. Here, you are encouraged to relax in their lovely nature observation garden – a place to sit back, listen and watch – before taking time to really savour your meal. Their raised beds and foraging trips provide the kitchen with vegetables and herbs, while the rest of their produce is locally sourced. The 4 course lunch and 8 course dinner are informed by what’s fresh and available each day.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10645;Akustika;Latvia;Valmiera;Diakonāta iela 6, Valmiera, 4201, Latvia;57.5365858;25.420595;21;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Set on the ground floor of the well-known Post and Telegraph building, this faux-industrial neighbourhood bistro was created by three friends and designed as a place they themselves would like to dine. Tasty, modern dishes are informed by the seasons, with local produce taking the lead, be it pikeperch from nearby Lake Burtnieks or locally reared lamb, while the Latvian char is a real hit. Be sure to ask the team for their advice when it comes to both the food and the wine. Occasional music performances add to the appeal, as does the terrace in the warmer weather.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10646;COD;Latvia;Riga;Tērbatas iela 45, Riga, 1011, Latvia;56.9560618;24.1259207;67;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Make for the sultry basement bar for a cocktail or two before heading back up to the atmospheric ground floor restaurant with its dim lighting and on-trend soundtrack. The chefs here might be Latvian, but the cuisine is contemporary Japanese. Start with a selection of sushi and tempura, then choose something from the robata grill. The gyoza ‘of the day’ is a must, the black cod with sweet miso is a hit, and the mochi ice cream is the perfect way to finish. There’s a vibrancy and freshness to the cooking, yet it still respects the fundamentals of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10647;3 Chefs;Latvia;Riga;Torņa iela 4, Jekaba Arcade 2b, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.9515972;24.106845;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in Jacob’s Barracks – a restored 18C building overlooking the Powder Tower and Swedish Gate – this restaurant lives up to exactly what you might expect. It’s run by three chefs – who help serve the dishes and love chatting with their guests – and the menu sticks with the traditional theme by offering classical flavour combinations, albeit updated with touches of creativity and a little refinement. The tasting menu is the best route to having a great all-round experience, and they hold cookery classes for those who like to get hands-on.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
10648;LOWINE;Latvia;Riga;Dzirnavu iela 43, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.9572805;24.1157425;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Naturally, wine leads the way at this snug bar located on the very edge of the city. Inside it has a rustic look and a laid-back feel, and on warmer days you can sit outside in the enclosed rear courtyard. The appealing, keenly priced wine list keeps natural wines to the fore and changes weekly, providing plenty of interest for the regulars. Similarly, the menu also lists something for everyone, from the traditional to the modern, with an extensive brunch menu offered earlier in the day and the likes of salmon with ponzu sauce followed by entrecôte with herb cream in the evening.;Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10649;Kest;Latvia;Cēsis;Valmieras iela 1, Cēsis, 4101, Latvia;57.3152387;25.2758348;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The town’s former fire station is now home to a restaurant which provides an experience of two parts. You start in the bright restaurant, where you dine from a 5 course tasting menu made up of modern dishes which keep local produce to the fore – and this is accompanied by an interesting alcoholic drinks flight which also includes cocktails. After dessert, you head through to the dark, moody lounge for the second part of your night: a coffee and time spent over a relaxing post-meal drink. The team really do run the place with genuine warmth.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10650;Ferma;Latvia;Riga;Valkas iela 7, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.962509;24.102259;92;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Sit inside at the chef’s table for a view of the chefs hard at work, or outside on the large terrace to take in views of the city’s oldest park. Chef-Owner Māris’ dishes reflect his love of native produce, with local beef and seafood to the fore, especially herring. The à la carte menu is concise and supplemented by a great value option at lunch, and friendly service completes the picture.;Terrace;[]
10651;Seasons;Latvia;Riga;Pils iela 12, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.95024;24.10296;88;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The luxurious Grand Palace Hotel plays host to this sumptuous restaurant, as well as a supremely comfortable bar which comes packed with antiques and fine art – be sure to either start or end your night here. The seasonal dishes showcase Latvian produce where possible and are themed around the world’s greatest painters. If you spot it on the menu, the wonderful lightly smoked trout with bearnaise sauce is a joy to eat, while the toffee pudding with buttermilk sorbet is a must. The wine list contains some premium bottles, while the plush bedrooms provide a chance for you to sample more than one.;Air conditioning;[]
10652;Barents;Latvia;Riga;Smilšu iela 3, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.950497;24.1076318;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An early 20C art nouveau property on the edge of town plays host to this spacious restaurant with a large front terrace and a distinct Nordic style. The seasonally changing menu comprises modern dishes that are made up of numerous elements and combine many flavours and textures in great harmony. Seafood is a strength – with some sourced from the Barents Sea – and the produce is displayed on ice in the middle of the room and explained to diners as they arrive. The champagne selection provides a noteworthy accompaniment.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10653;Whitehouse;Latvia;Riga;Vermane Park, Terbatas iela 2, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.9518905;24.1165378;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The former Biblioteka – which was something of an institution – reopened in 2020 as Whitehouse, and its dining terrace remains one of the most sought-after in the city thanks to its views over the colourful flower displays of Vērmanes Garden. It’s a sizeable place, with a long, narrow room, stylish décor and even a living wall. The menu blends modern European influences with subtle Asian touches, and there’s a touch of theatre to the presentation. Desserts are a highlight, as are the signature cocktails, and the place really comes into its own in the evening.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10658;Tails;Latvia;Riga;Antonijas iela 6a, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.9576885;24.1103179;47;false;false;Seafood;There’s a choice of two bistro-style dining rooms at Tails, but the raw bar counter really is the place to sit to make the most of the experience. The chefs take fish seriously here by adopting a tail to gill approach – and there’s even a drying room on show. They cure their own fish, make their own ceviches, and their sharing shellfish platter is something to linger over. Keep an eye out for the daily specials too, which often feature something a little different. For the ultimate indulgence, accompany your meal with a bottle of champagne.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10659;Stage 22;Latvia;Riga;Aspazijas bulvāris 22, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.9493558;24.1129813;65;true;true;Japanese;Set on the top floor of the Grand Hotel Kempinski Riga, this sumptuous restaurant affords superb views out over the park and the city skyline. Start with a drink in the chic cocktail bar or out on the lovely narrow terrace, then settle into plush chairs to enjoy your evening. This is an ideal place for celebrating and you will be looked after with consummate ease by the professional team. The wide-ranging Asian menu includes the likes of spicy tuna roll and Argentinian beef fillet with shallot cream, while the crispy vegetable tempura with dashi sauce is not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10660;BABO;Latvia;Riga;Dzirnavu Iela 42, Riga, 1001, Latvia;56.9564664;24.116781;24;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Opened in the summer of 2024, BABO is currently something of a lesser-known gem. Set up by a pair of experienced restaurateurs, it’s split between two rooms and a smart terrace. One of the owners hails from Georgia and it’s this that informs the menu. Delicious breads are cooked in the pizza oven and the charcoal grill adds a lovely flavour to the various meats and fish. Order 2 dishes each and share – maybe beef and pork khinkali (dumplings), salmon in bazhe (walnut) sauce or chicken tabaka with salt and lemon. The superb wine list showcases a great mix of classic and modern Georgian wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10661;H.E. Vanadziņš;Latvia;Cēsis;Rīgas iela 15, Cēsis, 4101, Latvia;57.3118585;25.2727931;48;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;You’ll find plenty of locals here, from the serving team to the regular guests, which creates a welcoming vibe and a convivial feel. The lengthy menus cover all bases, from flavour-packed soups and salads to delicious flatbreads and hearty mains inspired by northern Latvian cuisine. There’s a lovely terrace hidden to the rear that's worth seeking out, and bedrooms are available should you wish to stay the night.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10662;Riviera;Latvia;Riga;Dzirnavu iela 31, Riga, 1010, Latvia;56.9590185;24.1124539;38;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This large restaurant has a warm Mediterranean style and a menu to match, offering an appealing selection of dishes from oysters and tartares to fish and steaks, followed by old favourites like tiramisu. Everything is generously sized, with well-defined flavours and textures, and the sizeable wine list (1,000+) offers some great choices from around the globe. There’s a choice of two rooms in which to dine, but the terrace is the place to be when the weather’s right.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10663;Le Dome;Latvia;Riga;Miesnieku iela 4, Riga, 1050, Latvia;56.9498367;24.1035113;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away down the cobbled streets of the Old Town is a 400-year-old building which is home to both a boutique hotel and this intimate restaurant. Black and white photos of Riga adorn the walls of the long, narrow dining room, while in summer the operation relocates to the rooftop terrace which overlooks the Daugava River. Menus are modern and creative, with subtle international influences in evidence. The prime ingredients originate mostly from the Baltic region and Barents Sea, with Mother Nature leading the evolution of the dishes throughout the year.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
10664;36.Line;Latvia;Jurmala;Baznīcas iela 2B, Dubulti, Jurmala, 2015, Latvia;56.9714977;23.7695194;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Beachside locations don’t come much better than this, as you can walk straight in off the sand. Those after some respite from the sun can stay inside, while those wanting to feel the sea breeze should head for the glass-fronted terrace. The accessible menu covers all options, from lighter sushi and tartares to dumplings and hearty grilled fish and meat dishes. The tiramisu laced with the famous Black Balsam – their national drink – is a must-try, and the extensive selection of wines and cocktails is perfect for watching the sun go down.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10665;Les Ateliers;Switzerland;Vevey;Rue des Deux-Gares 6A, Vevey, 1800, Switzerland;46.4640854;6.8423943;39;true;false;Modern French;After having been deserted for some 25 years, this former stainless-steel workshop just behind the railway station has been revived by Jean-Sébastien Ribette and Sahondra Verdan (formerly of Auberge de la Veveyse). An off-kilter, smart industrial vibe sets the scene for a choice of culinary options: brasserie fare to the fore, or more ambitious (and surprise) set menus in the gourmet section. Market availability dictates the menu, hence the freshness of the ingredients. For example, scallops, roasted and tartare, with pumpkin and cloves, roast monkfish in cider butter with textured vegetables, perfectly roasted Bresse pigeon with apple molasses.;Air conditioning;[]
10666;Apollo;Switzerland;Davos Platz;Talstrasse 3, Davos Platz, 7270, Switzerland;46.7914018;9.8201949;32;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The name is a nod to the owners' deep-seated interest in NASA's famous programme. The space theme is also evoked through the elegant, dark interior, adorned with reprints of original photos from various missions, accompanied by captivating descriptions. Complementing the setting perfectly is the small open "satellite kitchen", where chef Thomas Huber and sous-chef Sergiu Midori prepare two set menus, one of which is vegetarian. Their predominantly Mediterranean-style dishes are always modern and creative, occasionally incorporating international influences, such as pike-perch, mussel broth, fermented fennel and sherry, or Davos Wagyu, pointed pepper, green beans and Roscoff onions. The restaurant is located in Hotel Grischa, which offers plenty of comfortable accommodation options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10667;Artis by Tristan Brandt;Switzerland;Arosa;Prätschlistrasse 64, Arosa, 7050, Switzerland;46.789844;9.674509;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Under the patronage of Tristan Brandt, head chef Fabian Saalfeld and his team present an array of ambitious dishes. They draw together strands of both classic and regional cuisine in equal measure, also incorporating Asian influences here and there, for example in their aromatic slices of raw scallop with a spicy jalapeño cream and slivers of green apple, served with a clear broth boasting strong umami flavours. Choose between a three- to five-course surprise menu and the à la carte offer. The restaurant is located in Hotel Prätschli, which stands in a quiet location above the village, not far from the ski slope.;Car park;[]
10668;Osteria Del Centro;Switzerland;Comano;Via Cantonale 50, Comano, 6949, Switzerland;46.0365245;8.9548663;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Vegetarian;This small, very friendly restaurant offers a successful mix of tradition (the setting is an old house in the centre of Comano), minimalist furnishings and modern cuisine. In the evening, enjoy a surprise tasting menu (five or seven courses) which is almost entirely vegetarian, with the option of choosing your main course. 95% of the ingredients are organic and the owner-chef will be happy to discuss his philosophy on organic food during the course of your meal. The elegant, original dishes include options such as beef wellington with kohlrabi, chimichurri and mushrooms, accompanied by artisanal wines from Switzerland and further afield.;Terrace;[]
10669;il tiramisù;Switzerland;Frauenfeld;Balierestrasse 10, Frauenfeld, 8500, Switzerland;47.5550701;8.8949507;17;true;false;Italian;This restaurant is near the centre but slightly tucked away – it goes without saying that it is a joy to sit on the terrace overlooking the River Murg. The atmosphere is friendly, the service attentive. In the open kitchen, the team meticulously prepares seasonal Italian dishes that are flavoursome and fun! It is definitely worth trying the pasta dishes, smaller portions of which are also available as a starter. Of course, the dessert after which the restaurant is named features on the menu. In the evening, order à la carte or opt for a surprise menu comprising three to four courses. Tip: moderately priced set menu at lunchtime.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10670;Le Jardinier;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai Wilson 37, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2121934;6.1523596;78;true;false;French Contemporary, Farm to table;This restaurant on the first floor of The Woodward hotel is a magical place, boasting an unobstructed view of the lake from its terrace, and promising attentive service and fresh, harmonious dishes. At the helm is Alain Verzeroli, who, along with chef Olivier Jean, has created a delicious culinary offering that espouses nature, the seasons and the ingredients. And, true to the name (meaning "gardener"), they give plants pride of place. Tasting menu or à la carte choice, plus a wide selection of vegetarian and/or gluten-free dishes. The restaurant also serves an exceptional breakfast and afternoon tea.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10671;SACHI;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai Turrettini 1, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2055825;6.1411316;99;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;The luxurious Mandarin Oriental hotel complex houses this restaurant presided over by chef Mitsu – a former disciple of master chef Nobu Matsuhisa, who has earned his spurs in the world of Japanese fine dining. In a resolutely contemporary setting, he serves set menus rife with delicious modern marriages of flavours, plus a fine selection of sushi. You might like to sample these at the counter of Omakase Bar, as you watch the master at work. Alternatively, head for the terrace alongside the Rhône.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10672;L'Écorce;Switzerland;Carouge;Rue du Collège 8, Carouge, 1227, Switzerland;46.1833065;6.140793;26;false;false;French Contemporary, Farm to table;In this convivial, tastefully furnished restaurant in Carouge’s old town the chef conjures up fresh, aromatic cuisine that combines classic and modern dishes such as mi-cuit tuna with a beetroot and watermelon bouillon and raw and cooked vegetables. Charming service, plus a small summer terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10673;Bären;Switzerland;Grüningen;Stedtligass 26, Grüningen, 8627, Switzerland;47.284607;8.7631473;42;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;In this old 17C inn, a passion for gastronomy is shared with diners! Owner Christian Mutschler is always on hand, recommending and serving, but also sharing stories about the eventful history of the place. The no-frills food is tasty, and most of the ingredients come from the region. The game dishes are definitely worth trying – made with game hunted by the owner, they could hardly be fresher or more seasonal. At lunchtime, meanwhile, the menu is significantly pared down. The wine list is also dominated by Swiss labels, and there are plenty of good bottles to choose from. Be sure to make the most of the terrace and the great view it offers!;Terrace;[]
10674;Zermatt Kitchen;Switzerland;Zermatt;Uferweg 1, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0206849;7.7495791;43;false;false;International;A trendy and casual dining concept split between two buildings: Brücke and Ascot. There are a variety of options on offer: breakfast (until 4pm), house-made pastries – their freshly baked croissants are very popular – and the menu of the day featuring international fare (until 6pm). In the evening, Brücke becomes "Zermatt Pho" and serves Vietnamese cuisine. In nearby Ascot, a more multifaceted and modern take on international cuisine is served at dinnertime. Here, there is a spacious terrace with a lounge area. The central location is another draw – the Matter Visper River flows right past Brücke. Incidentally, the coffee comes from the establishment's own roastery in Zermatt.;Terrace;[]
10675;Café des Banques;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue de Hesse 6, Geneva, 1204, Switzerland;46.2019643;6.1405527;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the banking district, this chic and contemporary bistro is the latest venture for Yoann Caloué. Here, the MICHELIN-starred chef serves confident modern cuisine, made with high-quality fresh ingredients to exacting standards. The desserts are also meticulously prepared, cf. his lemon tart, basil sorbet and limoncello sabayon. Those curious to see the chefs at work can sit at the counter facing the kitchen. Business lunch menu (without options). A very appealing restaurant.;;[]
10676;Osteria San Gallo;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Schwertgasse 1, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4267738;9.3775907;76;true;false;Italian;This pleasingly animated little osteria is located at the start of the pedestrian precinct, with the terrace area laid out in front of the entrance. The attractive interior is comfortable, with simple bistro chairs, wooden tables and the activity in the kitchen visible to diners. Authentic Italian dishes are served by an ambitious team – try, for example, the agnolotti piemontesi (handmade dumplings filled with veal).;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10677;La Croix d'Or;Switzerland;Ballaigues;Place du Château 1, Ballaigues, 1338, Switzerland;46.7296519;6.4158748;69;false;true;French, Mediterranean Cuisine;In the centre of the peaceful village of Ballaigues, not far from the French border, this restaurant is housed in a magnificent historical building. Two French chefs, David Sauvignet and Damien Lanza, run the show with professionalism and a passion for good food. Their ambitious take on seasonal French cuisine is full of finesse and infused with subtle Mediterranean influences. Pretty terrace.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10678;Afghan Anar;Switzerland;Zurich;Fierzgasse 22, Zurich, 8005, Switzerland;47.3840227;8.5317197;49;false;true;Afghan;Take advantage of the rather rare opportunity to discover Afghan cuisine! Here you can sample some of the country's most popular dishes, such as bolani, kabuli pulao or baklava. The atmosphere is laid back and down to earth, which is in part down to the open kitchen and authentic decor. As an alternative to the conventional tables and chairs, you have the option to dine on traditional mats.;Terrace;[]
10679;Bergwelt - BG's Grill Restaurant;Switzerland;Grindelwald;Bergwelt 4, Grindelwald, 3818, Switzerland;46.6243223;8.0397023;60;false;true;Contemporary;Modern chic with an Alpine touch: Done out in warm tones, with lovely parquet flooring, striking designer lamps and an open kitchen complete with an impressive barbecue, this restaurant – part of the equally attractive Bergwelt Grindelwald hotel – has a truly unique atmosphere. The cuisine has a Mediterranean feel but also draws inspiration from the region. The menu is full of tempting dishes, such as the butter-soft octopus starter. For meat lovers, the fragrant, golden-brown Wiener schnitzel is sure to whet the appetite, and the same goes for the top-quality signature cuts from the barbecue. There are plenty of options for vegetarians, too. The well-curated wine list predominantly features Swiss and French labels.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10680;Zum Löwen;Switzerland;Messen;Hauptstrasse 42, Messen, 3254, Switzerland;47.0915758;7.4483983;32;true;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Having first worked as sous-chef here, then as head chef, Jonas Ingold now represents the seventh generation of his family at the helm of this picture-perfect establishment, whose charm and atmosphere could not be more inviting. Near the entrance, the bar displays bottles from the wine list (ideal for an aperitif or digestif) and, just next to the bar is the open kitchen. In an attractive interior with a modernised rustic feel, an ambitious tasting menu is served both at lunchtime and in the evening – a vegetarian version is also available. The à la carte selection features simpler options that are nonetheless excellent. Many of the ingredients are sourced from the region. Attentive service is provided by friendly waitstaff. The terraces are delightful in summer.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10681;Mapo;Switzerland;Chêne-Bourg;Rue de Genève 40, Chêne-Bourg, 1225, Switzerland;46.1941795;6.1949712;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Fusion;Mapo is run by Emmanuelle and Paul, a talented couple who have opened this refreshing restaurant that breaks with the city’s more traditional dining options. A concise yet mouth-watering menu, meticulously prepared dishes teeming with energy and freshness, and all at a moderate price. A favourite haunt where a delightful experience is guaranteed.;Terrace;[]
10682;Les Montagnards - Brasserie;Switzerland;Broc;Rue de Montsalvens 4, Broc, 1636, Switzerland;46.6031118;7.1001385;63;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Fine dining is not the only option! Hotel Les Montagnards offers a culinary experience that goes beyond its renowned restaurant Le Sommet. The Brasserie can hold its own! The attractive modern interior featuring warm wood and sleek design is as much of a draw as the friendly service and, last but not least, the good cuisine. Here, the focus is on the region and the changing seasons. One of the house specialities, for example, is stuffed morels with a cream sauce. The pike-perch, fished from local lakes, is another popular choice. Tip: Try to get a window seat, then you can take in the view of Gruyères Castle and the surrounding area while you eat!;Wheelchair access;[]
10683;Izumi;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai des Bergues 33, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.206863;6.1469748;38;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;The atmosphere is truly international: top-notch ingredients go into a fusion cuisine of Japanese and other Asian influences. Perhaps you will be tempted by the Wagyu beef gyoza with a spicy ponzu sauce, or the izumi rolls? The lively atmosphere and chic, modern look of this restaurant on the seventh floor of the Four Seasons Hotel are just as much of a draw as the food. Don't miss the rooftop terrace, one floor up, with its breath-taking view over Geneva, the mountains and the lake. Make a reservation without delay!;Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
10684;Helvetia;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Vonwilstrasse 39, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4188376;9.35678;18;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;With the arrival of Svenja and Adrian Nessensohn (both previously employed at Lampart's in Hägendorf), Helvetia has gained two dedicated and friendly hosts who keep abreast of the latest culinary trends. They are also committed to a sustainable approach and the use of locally sourced ingredients. Some of the meat is even provided by the chef's brother, who runs his own farm. Get comfortable in this pretty restaurant, where a relaxed atmosphere reigns, and savour an appealing set menu with dishes designed to be shared – also available in a vegetarian version by prior arrangement. In summer, make a beeline for the gorgeous terrace. The restaurant is also open at lunchtime on Thursdays – the set menu is shorter but also includes vegetarian options.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10685;Tredecim by Monika Jans und Thomas Huber;Switzerland;Sihlbrugg;Sihlbrugg 4, Sihlbrugg, 8816, Switzerland;47.2185625;8.5789631;75;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Thomas Huber (the 13th generation) and Monika Jans are dedicated to their work in the Krone, an establishment steeped in history. While she is responsible for the cordial and professional service, he takes care of things in the kitchen, preparing seasonal, traditional dishes. They will also prepare a creatively inspired set menu if you order in advance. The cheese trolley selection is fantastic! The wood-panelled interior exudes charm and contributes to the delightful atmosphere. Should you wish to stay overnight, there are attractive individually decorated guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10686;Beaufort;Switzerland;Brunnen;Gersauerstrasse 91, Brunnen, 6440, Switzerland;47.0009663;8.5802452;18;true;false;Contemporary;This small restaurant is located in the Marina Fallenbach clubhouse, on the outskirts of Brunnen. The place has a lovely friendly atmosphere, refined decor and beautiful views of the marina, lake and mountains, not to mention a wonderful terrace! Their modern and cosmopolitan cuisine is made with good, fresh seasonal produce. In addition to à la carte dishes, there is also a three- to five-course seasonal set menu. Inexpensive lunch menu.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10687;Madre Nostra;Switzerland;Zermatt;Riedweg, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0219222;7.7542814;43;false;false;Italian;Classic Italian cooking is served in the charming restaurant of the modern hotel CERVO Mountain Resort, which is located a little above the village and right next to the slopes. The produce and flavour are the main focus here. At lunchtime, they offer a limited selection from the evening menu, as well as highlights from the establishment's other restaurants. The terrace is impressive!;Great view,Terrace;[]
10688;Loy Fah;Switzerland;Feusisberg;Schönfelsstrasse 3, Feusisberg, 8835, Switzerland;47.1858182;8.7368637;66;true;false;Thai contemporary;This chic restaurant on the fourth floor of the tasteful Panorama Resort & Spa boasts a stunning panoramic view over Lake Zurich. Inside, you are served by an extremely friendly and attentive team. The food is a modern take on authentic Thai cuisine, which is also adapted to European palates in terms of spiciness. You can put together your own menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10689;L'instinct;Switzerland;Granges;Route d'Ollon 2, Granges, 3977, Switzerland;46.2668011;7.460938;21;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Chic and relaxed, this restaurant delights the taste buds with its French-Mediterranean dishes and grilled meats (matured in the display case that was hewn directly out of the stone between the bar and the kitchen). They also like to perpetuate the tradition of serving flambé dishes, lit in the dining area, as well as classic dishes (still recommended!). In keeping with the terrace surrounded by vines, the wine list has a thousand references. Insider tip: come with at least two people and opt for the set menu.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10690;La Muña;Switzerland;Zermatt;Bahnhofstrasse 5, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0230771;7.7477996;30;false;true;Fusion;In this elegant and contemporary-style setting, the friendly waitstaff serve food that is an interesting fusion of Peruvian and Asian cuisine. Housed in Schweizerhof hotel, this restaurant is only open on winter evenings, offering a choice between raw (crudo) and hot (caliente) dishes – the ceviche comes highly recommended. Don't miss out on the desserts either! Incidentally, la muña is the name of a medicinal plant in the Andes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10691;Buffet de la Gare;Switzerland;Céligny;Route de Founex 25, Céligny, 1298, Switzerland;46.3484208;6.1998423;45;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;An old-fashioned restaurant of the type that is quite hard to find these days. It has Art Deco-style wood panelling, enamel plaques and coloured windows, as well as a terrace overlooking the surrounding greenery. There is also a traditional feel to the menu, which includes perch from Lake Geneva.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10693;Ristorante della Stazione;Switzerland;Centovalli/Intragna;Piazza Stazione 5, Centovalli/Intragna, 6655, Switzerland;46.1778099;8.7023809;25;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;There’s a change of guard at this Ticino dining institution where young couple Eloa Geiser and Yanick Walker have taken over the running of both the kitchen and front of house service. Eloa, the charming female half of the partnership, is also a qualified sommelier and takes very good care of her guests, while Yanick, adds his classic-French culinary stamp without neglecting his Valois roots, although he is not averse to adding some Mediterranean flair to his cuisine. In addition to its usual menu, on Tuesdays guests can order the “Stazione” veal liver, and on Saturdays the special braised beef with Merlot. The gracious building housing the restaurant with its beautiful views remains unchanged, as do the comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10694;Brasserie du Poisson;Switzerland;Auvernier;Rue des Epancheurs 1, Auvernier, 2012, Switzerland;46.9752575;6.8787701;87;false;false;Seafood;This contemporary brasserie close to the lake offers unpretentious cuisine. Fish has the starring role (tuna tartare, perch fillets), as well as hearty traditional recipes such as croûte aux morilles (with morel mushrooms) and veal cutlets. A real treat for the taste buds, particularly as everything (including the bread and ice cream) is homemade.;Terrace;[]
10695;EMOTIONS by Guy Ravet;Switzerland;Vevey;Rue d'Italie 1, Vevey, 1800, Switzerland;46.4576871;6.8523818;77;true;true;Classic French;The classic elegance of the Grand Hôtel du Lac, designed by architect Ernest Burnat, is the perfect setting for Chef Guy Ravet's ambitious cuisine. The finest ingredients are used with mastery and skill, as in the case of the fillet of wild turbot, seared, with cauliflower mousseline, red onion and mustard seed condiment and beurre blanc with chives.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
10696;Aroleid Restaurant;Switzerland;Zermatt;Furi 151, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0015365;7.7302936;100;true;true;Creative, World Cuisine;Located right by the ski slopes just above Furi gondola station, this restaurant is housed in a modern and stylish chalet that exudes rustic charm. As well as stunning views, diners can look forward to a diverse menu of delicious dishes inspired by the chef's international travels. Incidentally, the coffee comes from the hotel's own roastery and the crockery is also made in-house. For those who don't mind the long walk, it's a 1.5hour hike from Zermatt to the restaurant.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10697;Zwyssighaus;Switzerland;Bauen;Im Dorf 10, Bauen, 6466, Switzerland;46.9362273;8.579363;53;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This charming 18C restaurant named after the composer of the Swiss national anthem enjoys a fine location and a view of Lake Lucerne. Wood sets the tone inside, while outside you'll find two wonderful terraces – one on the balcony. A modern take on classic cuisine is served in the form of a three- to six-course menu, accompanied by a decent wine list. For overnight stays there are four simple yet cosy guestrooms.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10698;Repas;Switzerland;Biel;Bahnhofstrasse 14, Biel, 2502, Switzerland;47.1345132;7.2440578;24;true;true;Contemporary;Fancy a delicious meal above the rooftops of Biel? On the sixth floor of the Hotel Elite, in this central location near the railway station, you get a great view of the city and the Jura. The atmosphere is unpretentious, the service is friendly and the cuisine is contemporary, with regional and Mediterranean influences. If you're coming as a group, order a few of the finger food dishes ("Amuse") to share.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10699;Da Adriano;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Mezdi 27, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4827013;9.8333225;24;false;true;Italian;As a true Italian, maître d' Adriano Feraco, after whom this ristorante in a side wing of the Grand Hotel des Bains Kempinski is named, treats diners to an authentic experience. In an attractive setting (here, elaborate moulding, herringbone parquet flooring and pretty details such as wine racks and the unique-looking service station are sure to draw the eye), dedicated and charming waitstaff serve typically Italian cuisine including mouth-watering options such as spaghetti with clams or "duo of lamb".;Car park;[]
10700;Römerhof;Switzerland;Arbon;Freiheitsgasse 3, Arbon, 9320, Switzerland;47.5163138;9.4338111;43;true;false;Classic French, International;This beautiful building, the origins of which date back to the 16C, is run with dedication by Dominique and Gerald Bergue-Hunziker. Classic and international dishes are served in an elegant setting – the coffered ceiling is striking. In the evening, there is a choice of two set menus (one of which is vegetarian), each comprising three to six courses, and an à la carte menu. At lunchtime there is a shorter menu including a reasonably priced set menu. You can also relax in the cigar lounge or the pretty salons. Cosy and charming guestrooms are available in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10701;Gasthaus am Brunnen;Switzerland;Valendas;Am Platz 11, Valendas, 7122, Switzerland;46.7878977;9.2829095;44;true;true;Country cooking;The picturesque Gasthaus am Brunnen sits in the centre of this Graubünden mountain village. Locals meeting for lunch or a drink favour the rustic dining room, while the smart, minimalist-style restaurant is more elegant. The food is modern and uses exclusively local produce. Try the veal tenderloin cooked on a rock salt slab and served with herb caviar, mustard and garlic risotto and vegetables. The female chef's desserts are delicious.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10702;Ilge;Switzerland;Stein am Rhein;Rathausplatz 14, Stein am Rhein, 8260, Switzerland;47.6599145;8.8591268;52;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in an old half-timbered building in the heart of this idyllic little town. The interior design is chic and tasteful, and in fine weather there is a lovely terrace overlooking the pedestrian zone. Serbian-born Zoran Baratovic presides in the kitchen, turning out dishes that draw on classical and Mediterranean influences. We highly recommend the mouthwatering veal shank ravioli. And to accompany your meal, the attentive maitre d', who is always on hand, will provide you with a well-curated wine list that includes one or two interesting magnums.;Terrace;[]
10703;Guarda Val;Switzerland;Lenzerheide;Voa Sporz 85, Lenzerheide, 7078, Switzerland;46.7115885;9.5403887;71;false;false;International, Modern Cuisine;In the fine dining restaurant of the wonderfully located Maiensäss Hotel Guarda Val, the rustic charm of a 300-year-old cow byre meets modern simplicity. Service comes courtesy of a friendly and experienced team. When it comes to the food, the spotlight is shone on regional specialties. The two set menus (one is vegetarian) and the à la carte dishes are made almost exclusively from Swiss produce. At lunchtime, the offer is somewhat simpler – there is a three-course lunch menu, as well as à la carte dishes.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10704;Villa am See by Sandro Lüthi;Switzerland;Goldach;Seestrasse 64, Goldach, 9403, Switzerland;47.4868379;9.4759949;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Housed in a beautifully located villa, this restaurant has been run with great dedication by young couple Sandro Lüthi (kitchen) and Paulina Soares (service), along with their friendly little team, since spring 2024. They propose two set menus, one of which is vegetarian, plus an à la carte selection. They also serve a "Business Lunch" in the winter season. The cuisine is contemporary, seasonal and ingredient-led – predominantly French and Mediterranean in style, complemented by international twists and a healthy dose of creativity. A pleasantly relaxed atmosphere awaits in the modern and elegant interior. But it's the terrace, separated from the lake by a mere strip of greenery, that is the jewel in the crown! Including an enclosed, glass-walled pavilion offering a cosy retreat on chilly days.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10705;noumi;Switzerland;Berne;Kochergasse 3, Berne, 3000, Switzerland;46.9467031;7.4470766;72;false;false;World Cuisine, Fusion;The restaurant in the basement of the venerable grand hotel Bellevue Palace (Switzerland's official accommodation for foreign dignitaries) used to be Bern's mint – the name is a derivation of "numismatics". The atmosphere is cosmopolitan, chic and relaxed (the resident DJ plays in the evening). In the open kitchen, the chefs prepare "world food" incorporating influences from Asia, Peru and the Mediterranean. The dishes are made with excellent ingredients and are also suitable for sharing. Competent and laid back in their approach, the waitstaff provide recommendations from the selection of fine wines and interesting cocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
10706;Weinlaube;Switzerland;Schellenberg;Hinterschloss 15, Schellenberg, 9488, Switzerland;47.2329431;9.555857;54;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Countrified and charming, congenial and friendly! This former farmhouse in a quiet little hamlet not far from the border with the Vorarlberg region offers cosy Stube-style dining rooms and a beautiful outdoor terrace. The menu here features unfussy cuisine with a focus on classic, regional, seasonal and international dishes and the occasional use of the smoker.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10707;Fiskebar;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai du Mont-Blanc 11, Geneva, 1211, Switzerland;46.2077648;6.1484673;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Scandinavian;A Nordic enclave at the Ritz Carlton in Geneva, Fiskebar has made a name for itself thanks to its delightful fish- and seafood-based cuisine. The finest ingredients are sourced via short supply chains and skilfully prepared by an expert kitchen team. Diners are treated to fresh and healthy Scandinavian cuisine, enhanced with subtle Mediterranean touches – smoking and fermentation techniques are also put to good use. In a setting that tastefully combines rustic materials with more modern touches, diners take their seats at tables that look onto the open kitchen or afford a view of the lake. On top of that, the wine list abounds with pleasing discoveries, including a range of biodynamic wines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10708;Le 1913;Switzerland;Villars-sur-Ollon;Route des Hôtels 28, Villars-sur-Ollon, 1884, Switzerland;46.2975266;7.0575271;82;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This elegant restaurant, complete with a terrace commanding a knockout panoramic view of the mountains and valley, is located in the recently refurbished Villars Palace. The ambitious, structured cuisine combines regional and Mediterranean dishes in four- or six-course set menus. The creativity of the "Gambero Rosso", for example, a carpaccio of red prawns contrasted with a perfectly presented dill sorbet, is a case in point. The open kitchen means you can see Christian Bertogna's team at work!;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10709;Auberge de la Couronne;Switzerland;Enney;Route de l'Intyamon 36, Enney, 1667, Switzerland;46.5659614;7.08366;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in a tastefully renovated traditional edifice, the Auberge de la Couronne morphs from a simple bistro at lunchtime into a fine dining gourmet establishment in the evenings. Generosity and indulgence are the order of the day in dishes such as crisp golden roasted sweetbread served with fresh crayfish and crunchy glazed mini vegetables. The front-of-house team is on hand to help you find the perfect food-wine pairing as you take a seat in the handsome vaulted dining room.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10710;Millennium - La Brasserie;Switzerland;Crissier;Chemin de Mongevon 25, Crissier, 1023, Switzerland;46.549459;6.5706448;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in the prestigious Millenium complex, a state-of-the-art business and conference centre, the elegant La Brasserie is under the expert supervision of Fabien Foare. This is the go-to place for a business lunch. A pared-down, less expensive lunchtime menu gives way to more ambitious fare in the evening, with a choice between "Les Inspirations", dishes created to reflect the seasons (cooked and raw Puits d'Amour melon), and "Les Incontournables" such as free-range guinea fowl supreme or fillets of perch from Lake Geneva). Not to mention the trolleys laden with charcuterie and pastries, which will have your mouth watering from the aperitif right through to dessert! The gourmet grocery shop is open in the afternoons.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10711;Esprit par Guy Ravet;Switzerland;Vevey;Rue d'Italie 1, Vevey, 1800, Switzerland;46.4576944;6.8523738;77;false;false;French;The setting by Lake Geneva is truly outstanding and, in the summer, the terrace becomes a standout feature courtesy of its jaw-dropping view! The restaurant is housed in the luxurious Grand Hôtel du Lac, which dates back to 1868. The sleek polished interior, extended by a bright, airy conservatory, is fully equal to the location, as is the food. The menu by executive chef Guy Ravet is seasonal and based on regional produce. The wine list demonstrates a weakness for Lavaux wines. Unobtrusive, slick service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10712;Schloss Wartegg;Switzerland;Rorschacherberg;Von Blarer-Weg 1, Rorschacherberg, 9404, Switzerland;47.4785116;9.5298861;35;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The elevated location between Lake Constance and the Alpstein is quite something! As in the small castle hotel, the focus in the restaurant, too, is on the organic and ecological. This translates into sustainably produced ingredients and organic produce from local suppliers, plus vegetables and herbs from the hotel's own 2 500m2garden. From the terrace there is a wonderful view of the countryside and Lake Constance.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10713;Le Roc;Switzerland;Rougemont;Chemin des Palettes 14, Rougemont, 1659, Switzerland;46.48792;7.2022196;24;false;false;Swiss, Mediterranean Cuisine;The restaurant of the Hôtel de Rougemont serves classic French cuisine with a contemporary twist. The house-smoked salmon, green asparagus in breadcrumbs, salsa verde emulsion and citrus fruits makes a lasting impression… enjoyed in a delightful Alpine interior, tastefully decorated (old wood, light-coloured banquettes and seats, modern lighting), or on the terrace, with views of the mountains.;;[]
10714;Haberbüni;Switzerland;Liebefeld;Könizstrasse 175, Liebefeld, 3097, Switzerland;46.9350625;7.4152935;87;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The atmosphere here is one of a kind! Housed in the airy hayloft of a 19C farmhouse with rustic beams, this place has a special feel to it. The tasteful interior is complemented by a secluded garden terrace with trees and shrubs. The food is fresh and made with high-quality ingredients. In the evening, there is a set menu and an à la carte selection. The latter is also available at lunchtime, supplemented by daily specials and a "Business Lunch" option. Excellent wine list featuring plenty of rarities and magnums.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10715;Principe Leopoldo;Switzerland;Lugano;via Montalbano 5, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;45.9929427;8.9397411;28;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Situated in a panoramic and picturesque location outside the town centre, Principe Leopoldo is the gourmet restaurant of a classic-style hotel with an intimate ambience. Take a seat on the veranda with its stunning views of the lake and mountains or make yourself comfortable in the elegant dining room in winter. The cuisine here is based on solid traditional technique and is prepared from seasonal local and Mediterranean ingredients, with an equal balance of meat and fish dishes. The wine list has something for all tastes, including a selection of memorable vintages.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10716;Eden - Belle Époque;Switzerland;Spiez;Seestrasse 58, Spiez, 3700, Switzerland;46.6897602;7.6818423;69;false;true;Country cooking, International;At the restaurant of the Hotel Eden Spiez, diners can savour classic cuisine that showcases regional and seasonal produce including homegrown fruit and berries. The hotel also has its own herb garden. Take in stunning views of Spiez Castle, Spiez Bay and the imposing mountains from the stylishly elegant interior or the covered terrace – both spaces are equally delightful. A shorter menu is available at lunchtime.;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10717;Panorama;Switzerland;Aeschiried ob Spiez;Aeschiriedstrasse 36, Aeschiried ob Spiez, 3703, Switzerland;46.6444073;7.7254432;42;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The name says it all! The location at an altitude of over 1 000m makes for a fantastic panoramic view of the surrounding mountains – it would be a crime not to enjoy it from the terrace in summer. The Rindisbachers have been running their establishment since 1985 already, serving food influenced by tradition, made with quality ingredients and paired with good wines. The pasta is manufactured in their own workshop. Panoteca sells delicatessen wares.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10719;Marée;Switzerland;Vaduz;Mareestrasse 29, Vaduz, 9490, Switzerland;47.1471628;9.5236017;49;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Park Hotel Sonnenhof's wonderful location and comfortable accommodation options are not its only trump cards. The restaurant, run by chef Hubertus Real, is also in high demand. In a tastefully elegant setting, at attractively laid tables, diners are served classic cuisine made with first-rate ingredients. The friendly and attentive front-of-house team also provide expert advice on their very extensive selection of wines. The magnificent terrace also has a viewpoint – the "Adlernest" (eagle's nest) – from which you can take in the stunning view.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10720;Da Valentino;Switzerland;Locarno;Via Torretta 7, Locarno, 6600, Switzerland;46.1703672;8.7960063;39;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Although it is the beautiful terrace that first catches the eye at this restaurant, the friendly welcome and attentive service offered by Valentino in the kitchen and Sabine front of house add to the appeal. Mediterranean specialities and traditional classic dishes feature on the menu, while an open fireplace creates a warm ambience in winter.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10721;The Omnia;Switzerland;Zermatt;Auf dem Fels, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0202774;7.7456516;94;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Vegetarian;A lift whisks you up here from the pedestrian area – to some breath-taking views! In the restaurant of the eponymous hotel, the focus lies squarely on vegetarian cuisine. Nevertheless, you have the option to supplement the dishes with fish or meat specialities. Those in the mood for a culinary adventure should opt for the "OMNIA Experience" surprise menu, which comprises four courses, complete with beverage pairings. The interior is modern and upscale, featuring clean lines and large granite-topped tables. Tip: Enjoy an aperitif by the fireplace.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10722;Tao's;Switzerland;Zurich;Augustinergasse 3, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3715144;8.5401203;22;true;false;Fusion, International;Tao's has you covered if you are in the mood for Euro-Asian cuisine. The wide-ranging menu includes sushi and sashimi, steak tartare, poke bowls and dim sum, plus "Signature Grill" dishes such as Thai-style fillet of sea bass, lime, herbs, ginger, soy. The dishes are accompanied by a fantastic and extensive international wine list. A pleasantly relaxed yet stylishly elegant atmosphere prevails. In summer the cosy terrace is a huge draw, and there is also a bar.;Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
10723;Gasthaus Bären;Switzerland;Reichenbach;Dorfstrasse 21, Reichenbach, 3713, Switzerland;46.6254908;7.6942264;34;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Swiss;This restaurant serves flavoursome traditional cuisine made from local produce à la carte or in the form of an ambitious set menu comprising three, four or five courses. There are also appetising options for two, such as Chateaubriand. Berner Haus, which first appears in records as a tavern in 1542, makes for an enchanting setting with its charming wood-panelled interior. The lovely old turquoise tiled stove, adorned with Langenthal porcelain, provides comforting warmth in the winter months.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10724;Bianchi;Switzerland;Zurich;Limmatquai 82, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3734854;8.5429159;83;false;true;Seafood, Italian;A slice of la dolce vita! Located right by the Limmat River, this ristorante boasts a bright and modern interior where excellent service comes courtesy of a cheerful and adept front-of-house team. Made with top-notch produce, the Mediterranean-style fish and seafood dishes here are in high demand. Gorgeous little terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10725;La Bagatelle;Switzerland;Gstaad;Neueretstrasse 43, Gstaad, 3780, Switzerland;46.4783476;7.2903617;40;false;false;Classic French;Here you can look forward to classic French cuisine made from top-notch ingredients, including an appealing selection of dishes for two. The cosy ambience created by warm wood, soft lighting and a touch of elegance is inviting. Plus they have a terrace with a stunning view. The service is charming, and there is a terrific wine list – half bottles are available, too. For an overnight stay: Hotel Le Grand Chalet has cosy rustic-style guestrooms.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10726;Stiva Veglia;Switzerland;Ilanz;Miez Vitg 6, Ilanz, 7130, Switzerland;46.7774261;9.1785471;41;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Situated in an idyllic little village, this lovingly restored Graubünden house dating back to 1761 is replete with Alpine charm. The interior is exceptionally pretty with its wood-panelled rooms that are welcoming and stylish in equal measure. Make a beeline for the terrace in summer. Tino Zimmermann delivers modern regional cuisine. There is a set menu of up to nine courses. A classic of the house is the "Schmauser 45-minute egg". A vegetarian menu is also available upon request. Fantastic produce such as Val Lumnezia Arctic char demonstrates a clear connection to the region. Diners are waited on by a dedicated and friendly front-of-house team, with the chefs themselves making an appearance from time to time in order to talk diners through their dishes. Tip: house-made specialities such as liqueurs, grape jelly, herb salt and lemon salt are also available to buy.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10727;Al Braciere;Switzerland;Ronco sopra Ascona;Via Livurcio 50, Ronco sopra Ascona, 6622, Switzerland;46.1500584;8.7336699;42;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated just above Ascona, about 1km from the town centre, this friendly hotel boasts panoramic views of Lake Maggiore, the surrounding mountains and the island of Brissago. Enjoy modern, carefully prepared cuisine in the comfortable dining room or on the idyllic outdoor terrace in summer.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10728;FIVE;Switzerland;Crans-Montana;Route des Zirès 14, Crans-Montana, 3963, Switzerland;46.3066423;7.4707354;79;true;true;Lebanese;Ensconced in the ski resort, with views of the Swiss mountains, elegant restaurant FIVE – part of the Guarda Golf Hotel – creates a contrast with its Levantine cuisine, which features mezze for sharing, among other dishes. Diners can also enjoy the European flavours of the desserts, including chocolate tart and fruit mousse.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10730;Ciani;Switzerland;Lugano;Piazza Indipendenza 4, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;46.0047009;8.9556424;25;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;A fashionable restaurant housed in the Palazzo dei Congressi, where famous chef Dario Ranza delights guests with his fresh, Mediterranean cuisine. Don’t miss the delicious risottos, including his recipe with saffron, chanterelles, courgettes and Robiolino cheese. Excellent wine selection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10731;Esprit Ravet;Switzerland;Gstaad;Bahnhofstrasse 2, Gstaad, 3780, Switzerland;46.4751483;7.2846847;38;false;false;French Contemporary;The Ravet family from the L’Ermitage restaurant in Vufflens-le-Château have brought their own style to Hotel Bernerhof in the centre of Gstaad, in the form of this chic brasserie, which now serves ambitious modern French Ravet-style gourmet cuisine. The service is attentive and friendly. A special feature of the brasserie is a flambé trolley.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
10732;Le Cerf;Switzerland;Rougemont;Rue des Allamans 8, Rougemont, 1659, Switzerland;46.4898153;7.2107273;23;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This century-old culinary institution is a renowned name in the region. Reinvented from top to bottom, it now serves good old unpretentious dishes in a traditional vein: for example, strips of veal from the Pays d'Enhaut, golden rösti and green salad… and let's not forget the malakoffs – fried cheese balls made with PDO cheese from the old fort in the valley – and the fondues! Cosy, rustic-style ambience, plus a superb terrace with mountain views.;;[]
10733;S.Zimmer;Switzerland;Adelboden;Dorfstrasse 13, Adelboden, 3715, Switzerland;46.4935253;7.5604877;97;true;false;Contemporary;This cosy and intimate little restaurant is run by chef Stefan Zimmermann and hostess Tünde Tamàs. A most cordial family atmosphere awaits you, as well as flavoursome cuisine, with many of the ingredients being sourced from the region. They serve a set menu of up to seven courses. The wine list in particular shows influences from Hungary – the owner's homeland – and you should certainly consider her recommendations! Although located inside the building of Hotel Viktoria Eden, the restaurant is run independently.;Wheelchair access;[]
10734;Perroquet Vert;Switzerland;Biel;Zentralstrasse 15, Biel, 2502, Switzerland;47.1390078;7.2444917;32;false;false;French, Traditional Cuisine;This intimate, lively restaurant on the Place de la Fontaine exudes the Belle Epoque charm of the Parisian brasseries of old. A feel that chimes perfectly with the traditional, French dishes chalked up on the blackboard. Favourites include scallop risotto, entrecôte and tarte tatin.;Terrace;[]
10736;L'Arabesque;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai Wilson 47, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.214065;6.151552;69;false;false;Lebanese, Middle Eastern;The Arabesque’s attractive decor of gold mosaics, white leather and black lacquerware conjures up pictures of the mysterious Orient, in particular Lebanon. It provides the perfect foil for a pedigree Mediterranean lineup, including hot and cold mezzes and Kibbeh Labanieh, the chef’s signature dish of meatballs, and Samak mechoui, grilled seabass with a sesame sauce. Excellent range of vegetarian dishes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10737;Pfändler's Gasthof zum Bären;Switzerland;Birmenstorf;Kirchstrasse 7, Birmenstorf, 5413, Switzerland;47.4611738;8.2476743;70;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;Steeped in over 200 years of history, this building makes for a really delightful setting: Bärenstube and Orangerie are full of charm and attention to detail. The garden is also attractive – a truly idyllic spot! The seasonal food has regional and Mediterranean influences. You will feel right at home in the pretty guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10738;Seven;Switzerland;Ascona;via Moscia 2, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1548225;8.7664557;32;true;false;Creative, Italian;The views extend from the lake to the mountains in this informal restaurant, where windows into the kitchen allow guests to watch the chefs busy at work. The menu features creatively reinterpreted, classic-style dishes, with the option of choosing between meat and fish, while the delicious bread comes from the Bottega del Gusto in Porto Ronco. At lunchtime, there’s a bistro-style menu with lighter but equally delicious options such as salads, antipasti and primi, hamburgers, club sandwiches, baked seabass and grilled Tomahawk steak. There’s also a lounge bar plus a wine bar of the same name, the latter offering an interesting array of labels (also available by the glass), as well as cocktails which are a perfect pairing for the dishes on offer. Given the restaurant’s superb location, the tables on the terrace are much sought after in summer, so it’s best to book ahead! Three luxury apartments are also available if you’d like to extend your stay here.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10739;Essort;Switzerland;Berne;Jubiläumstrasse 97, Berne, 3005, Switzerland;46.9354875;7.4461182;53;true;false;International;This inviting restaurant is housed in what was once the US embassy. Its interior design features a harmonious combination of clean lines, warm wood finishings and muted tones. The terrace to the rear of the building beckons in summer. In the evening, a seasonally inspired tasting menu comprising three to six courses is served, with the option to add wine pairings. At lunchtime, a shorter set menu as well as the "Business Lunch" are available.;Terrace;[]
10740;Käserei;Switzerland;Brail;Crusch Plantaun 217, Brail, 7527, Switzerland;46.653995;10.0336471;33;true;true;Cheese, Fondue and Raclette, Swiss;This restaurant with a modern yet rustic feel and a cosy atmosphere is located in the former cowshed of a typical Engadin house. The restaurant still has a focus on cows and dairy products today, serving dishes such as cheese fondues, raclette, capuns and even Chinese fondue. Cheese-making demonstrations are held regularly in the evenings.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10741;Spettacolo;Switzerland;Lenk im Simmental;Badstrasse 20, Lenk im Simmental, 3775, Switzerland;46.4542811;7.4362674;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the Lenkerhof spa resort's elegant restaurant, hotel guests can look forward to a great half-board set menu, while à la carte diners are treated to a high-quality and modern take on classic cuisine that also draws on international influences. You can put together a menu of variable length from a selection of 15 dishes. The attractive wine list includes small bottles, as well as magnums. Friendly and proficient service.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10742;Wildenmann;Switzerland;Buonas;St. Germanstrasse 1, Buonas, 6343, Switzerland;47.1421716;8.4565892;96;true;true;Classic French;Set in a lovely Zug house built in 1708, Wildenmann serves classic fare with menu favourites including local Zugersee Arctic char and perch. It also offers charming service, welcoming dining rooms and a lovely terrace.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10743;Pinte;Switzerland;Baden;Sommerhaldenstrasse 20, Baden, 5405, Switzerland;47.451571;8.2872145;80;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Set in a 19C building, Pinte offers something for everyone in its cosy dining room and comfortable restaurant. Menu offerings include ravioli with pear, Jersey Blue and walnuts and pot roast with Ticino polenta and purple carrots. Delightful terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10744;LOFT FIVE;Switzerland;Zurich;Europaallee 15, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3784291;8.5339322;72;false;false;Contemporary, International;This stylish restaurant stands directly on Europaallee, not far from the railway station (Hauptbahnhof). But it's not only the chic interior and relaxed atmosphere that are inviting – the food is also a definite draw! Flavoursome modern-inspired international cuisine is on the menu. The service is friendly and competent, and there is a good selection of wines and cocktails.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10745;La Place;Switzerland;Plan-les-Ouates;Route de Saint-Julien 143, Plan-les-Ouates, 1228, Switzerland;46.1682979;6.1178249;71;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Cristina and Vincenzo De Rosa run this restaurant with passion and enthusiasm. Throughout the year they delight guests with their modern and colourful cuisine, with dishes such as lobster ravioli in a Thai red curry sauce featuring on the menu.;Terrace;[]
10746;Landhaus;Switzerland;Rheineck;Appenzellerstrasse 73, Rheineck, 9424, Switzerland;47.4620914;9.5815808;68;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This 16C farmhouse is now a really charming restaurant boasting a splendid view of Lake Constance. Featuring warm wood finishings and sleek design, the decor embodies a winning combination of the old and the new. Regional cuisine is served in the cosy parlour. Reduced menu at lunchtime. In summer, make a beeline for the gorgeous terrace. There is a hall for events in the modern converted barn.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10747;Chez Vrony;Switzerland;Zermatt;Findeln, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0119335;7.7675578;68;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Swiss;All the wood and pleasant decor make for a cosy, rustic atmosphere indoors, but with the spectacular view you have at 2 100m above sea level, the terrace is unsurprisingly popular too! Traditional regional cuisine is served by the charming waitstaff. Incidentally, they produce their own dried meat and sausages here.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10748;Arté al Lago;Switzerland;Lugano;piazza Emilio Bossi 7, Lugano, 6906, Switzerland;46.0050531;8.9702949;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Modern, impeccably presented cuisine with a Mediterranean influence and an equal emphasis on meat and fish in a restaurant whose name lives up to its promise. Interesting wine selection, including a choice of international labels.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
10750;Rössli;Switzerland;Zollikon;Alte Landstrasse 86, Zollikon, 8702, Switzerland;47.3379619;8.5745738;47;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The first-floor dining area of this 16C half-timbered house is a really pleasant setting in which to dine: the space has a cosy, rustic atmosphere, plus a small conservatory overlooking the lake. Seasonal influences can be detected in the traditional cuisine, while the menu also features classics such as Wiener schnitzel with warm potato salad.;;[]
10751;Löwen;Switzerland;Walenstadt;Seestrasse 20, Walenstadt, 8880, Switzerland;47.1245671;9.3136926;93;false;false;Regional Cuisine;In this cosy little restaurant in the vaulted cellar, you can look forward to the "Gourmet Menu", which is served at lunch and dinner, with the option of up to seven courses. At lunchtime, Beiz serves a set menu, as well as a choice of à la carte dishes. There is also a decent wine selection, and the front-of-house team is friendly and competent.;Terrace;[]
10752;Stapferstube da Rizzo;Switzerland;Zurich;Culmannstrasse 45, Zurich, 8006, Switzerland;47.3821604;8.547464;32;false;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Here at Stapferstube, a well-known Zurich eatery, Italian dishes such as tris di pasta della casa, gamberoni aglio olio peperoncino, and brasato di manzo al Barolo are a hit with diners. In this vibrant and welcoming restaurant, regulars and first-time guests alike are treated to Mediterranean hospitality and a cosy atmosphere. Their quick lunch at a reasonable price is also popular.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10754;Le Maguet;Switzerland;Les Evouettes;Route Cantonale 95, Les Evouettes, 1894, Switzerland;46.365367;6.8749489;82;false;false;Classic French;The Le Maguet brothers, Jonathan (serving) and Benjamin (cooking), are carrying the culinary torch of their father Olivier with their sustainable and 100% local concept! They use organic and/or wild ingredients that are of excellent quality, and draw on both traditional know-how and the most modern techniques, resulting in simple and tasty cuisine. For example, pata negra pork shoulder and salsify, slowly and perfectly cooked. Thirty years on, the dessert trolley is still the domain of their mother, Pierrette: don't leave the table without trying her tartlets!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10755;Cavigilli;Switzerland;Flims;Via Arviul 1, Flims, 7017, Switzerland;46.8372406;9.2830774;44;true;true;Swiss, Traditional Cuisine;Combining modern features with the original wood and stone, plus cordial service and a pleasingly down-to-earth atmosphere, this charming 15C Grisons building provides a wonderful setting in which to enjoy seasonal ingredient-led cuisine. The focus is on the essentials, so the flavoursome dishes are served in pared-down combinations. Tip: Make the most of the quiet terrace in summer! There is a small and simple lunch deal.;Terrace;[]
10756;Sapori;Switzerland;Interlaken;Höheweg 41, Interlaken, 3800, Switzerland;46.6862628;7.8572884;31;false;true;Italian, Pizza;Worth a visit for its stylish historic interior alone, Sapori promises a wonderful parquet floor and an impressively high painted ceiling complete with stucco work. The Italian menu includes tasty stone-baked pizzas.;Terrace;[]
10757;Gildo's Ristorante;Switzerland;Gstaad;Palacestrasse 28, Gstaad, 3780, Switzerland;46.4727829;7.2899069;19;true;false;Italian;If you’re in the mood for some authentic, upmarket Italian food, you should try the line-caught sea bass, cime di rapa, garlic, pine nuts and peperoncino at this restaurant. Expect excellent service, plus a stylish Alpine ambience.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
10758;4 Saisons;Switzerland;Charmey;Gros-Plan 28, Charmey, 1637, Switzerland;46.6212687;7.1623336;66;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Attractive picture windows, elegant pale wood, and a menu that takes the four seasons as its starting point, as reflected in the market-fresh ingredients. Locally grown vegetables, fish from the nearby lakes and Swiss meats are accompanied by an appealing wine list that focuses on local producers. Delight in dishes such as morel stuffed with Agria potatoes and Vully asparagus tips. Friendly service and attractive guestrooms at Hotel Cailler.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10759;Du Cheval Blanc;Switzerland;Bulle;Rue de Gruyères 16, Bulle, 1630, Switzerland;46.6169297;7.0571062;43;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The former chef at L'Écu, in Bulle, has turned Du Cheval Blanc into a veritable haven for foodies. In this convivial light-filled restaurant, he delights diners with his well-crafted, unfussy and straightforward take on traditional cuisine, prepared with care and served by a professional team. The real deal.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10761;La Terrasse Brasserie;Switzerland;Interlaken;Höheweg 41, Interlaken, 3800, Switzerland;46.6861765;7.856995;91;false;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Befitting the elegance that characterises the Victoria Jungfrau Grand Hotel & Spa, which is steeped in tradition, a classically refined atmosphere awaits you here. The location against the impressive backdrop of the mountains is a real draw in itself. In summer, make a beeline for the terrace on the promenade! The menu includes a broad assortment of Arab, Asian, Mediterranean and Swiss dishes – flavoursome food made from high-quality ingredients.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10762;Paradiso;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Engiadina, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4933938;9.8080225;27;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Alpine;In good weather, you can take in breathtaking views up here at 2 181m above sea level. This down-to-earth Mountain Club restaurant appeals to diners of all ages. You can look forward to good food and a great wine selection, as well as a relaxed atmosphere, partly thanks to the music and DJs. Note: there is an entry fee for non-members. Accessible by chairlift and a short walk (10min).;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10763;Verena;Switzerland;Olten;Bahnhofstrasse 4, Olten, 4600, Switzerland;47.3489466;7.9061512;64;false;false;Contemporary, Farm to table;This charming historical customs house dating back to 1786 has undergone a transformation under Dave Wälti, who previously worked in the kitchens at Eisblume in Worb and Casino Bern. The cuisine is contemporary, with vegetarian components playing a major role – but not to the complete exclusion of fish and meat. Warm wood tones and clean lines make for a lovely atmosphere, and the service comes courtesy of a friendly, laid-back and professional team.;Terrace;[]
10764;Restaurant Pony;Switzerland;Sigigen;Grabenstrasse 1, Sigigen, 6019, Switzerland;47.0637648;8.1333252;18;false;false;Swiss, Mediterranean Cuisine;A family-run restaurant, now in the third generation. In the elegant Pavillion dining room, friendly staff serve classic cuisine with Mediterranean influences, while the cosy Beizli is an inn-style room offering more everyday cooking. Pleasant terrace.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10766;Le Jardin des Alpes;Switzerland;Villars-sur-Ollon;Domaine de Rochegrise 23, Villars-sur-Ollon, 1884, Switzerland;46.2932599;7.0621503;69;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;There’s a new chef and a new concept at this gastronomic restaurant within the walls of the Chalet RoyAlp luxury hotel & spa. In this elegant yet welcoming setting, savour dishes such as snails with herbs and a potato mousse, and fettuccine with parmesan and Alba white truffle sauce, complemented by highly professional service and an impressive wine selection. The terrace is a must in fine weather!;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10767;Motto del Gallo;Switzerland;Taverne;via Bicentenario 16, Taverne, 6807, Switzerland;46.0644094;8.9300034;98;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A historic gem of a restaurant, part of a tiny hamlet of 15C houses, featuring a cool, shaded outdoor space for summer dining. Elegance and refinement are to the fore inside, enhanced by antique furniture and works of art, while the menu takes its inspiration from the local region and the Mediterranean. The Chateaubriand is an absolute must!;Car park,Terrace;[]
10768;Marktküche;Switzerland;Zurich;Feldstrasse 98, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3787189;8.5233338;70;false;true;Vegan, Seasonal Cuisine;One tip at the outset: be sure to reserve in good time – this restaurant always gets booked up, so it's hard to get a table! The clue is in the name: the cuisine takes its cue from what the market has to offer, dispensing with meat and fish. Diners can look forward to a vegetarian surprise menu made up of four to eight courses. There is also a lunch menu available on the penultimate Friday of every month.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10769;Elisa - Bistro & Terrasse;Switzerland;Brienz;Axalpstrasse, Brienz, 3855, Switzerland;46.7352612;8.023246;42;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Vegetarian;Le Tapis Rouge has been reincarnated as Elisa - Bistro & Terrasse, but the commitment to local sourcing and sustainable practices remains unchanged. This restaurant is located in the venerable Grandhotel Giessbach (built in 1875), right at the foot of the waterfalls of the same name, and boasts a wonderful view of Lake Brienz. The food is delicious, contemporary in style and primarily made using produce grown in the hotel's own 2ha vegetable garden. The other ingredients are locally sourced and from small-scale producers: fish comes from Lake Brienz, veal from a neighbouring farmer. On the menu, vegetables take centre stage, with dishes such as Giessbach agnolotti with Meiringen cream cheese and broccoli. Tip: In the evening, opt for the "Tour du Domaine" surprise menu for sharing (for two or more people).;Great view,Terrace;[]
10770;Chrüz;Switzerland;Eschenbach;Rapperswilerstrasse 1, Eschenbach, 8733, Switzerland;47.2390948;8.9213722;47;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This centrally located inn has tables in the stylish conservatory or a simpler dining room where you can tuck into traditional fare that often draws on international influences. The wide-ranging menu includes spaetzle with Sbrinz (hard cheese) and truffle, cordon bleu with Alpine cheese, "Vorässä 2.0" (beef stew with a twist) and salmon green curry. The service is friendly and attentive. Lunchtime options are more limited and moderately priced.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10771;Seebistro Belvédère;Switzerland;Hergiswil;Seestrasse 18a, Hergiswil, 6052, Switzerland;46.9833368;8.3117497;86;true;false;Country cooking;The location right by the lake is superb! The modern bistro is just in front of the fine dining restaurant – the same kitchen team works at both. There is a seasonal set menu with Mediterranean influences and made with regional produce, plus a choice of classics.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10772;Oberer Mönchhof;Switzerland;Kilchberg;Alte Landstrasse 98, Kilchberg, 8802, Switzerland;47.3260059;8.5450314;48;false;false;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;The dining rooms in this lovely, centuries-old half-timbered building are tastefully and comfortably furnished. Outside a fabulous terrace is laid out under chestnut trees overlooking the lake. The cuisine is seasonal, traditional and international with an additional tasting menu on offer at lunchtime and in the evenings.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10773;Gasthaus Höhwald;Switzerland;Klosters;Monbielerstrasse 171, Klosters, 7250, Switzerland;46.8615232;9.9177607;59;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Alpine;In this gorgeous restaurant boasting a stunning view, the atmosphere could hardly be more welcoming. Since December 2023, a dedicated couple have been at the helm, bringing their superlative fine dining experience to the table: Mara Graef cheerily oversees the team front of house, while Thomas Graef prepares tasty seasonal dishes. His is regional cuisine for the most part, but some dishes are clearly influenced by the owners' Austrian homeland: for instance, their classic Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef), available as a Monday special. Hot meals are served throughout the day. Wonderful terrace. Tip for motorists: You can reserve a parking space in the garage.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10774;Mulania Brasserie;Switzerland;Laax;Via Murschetg 15, Laax, 7031, Switzerland;46.8191287;9.2655755;48;false;false;International, Seasonal Cuisine;With its combination of sleek, contemporary style and rustic ceiling beams, this old Graubünden building provides an attractive setting. Host couple Yvonne Marx and Sascha Meyer have reimagined their place as a brasserie, serving tried-and-tested regional specialities such as capuns (chard rolls) or quark pizokels (buckwheat spaetzle), plus brasserie classics like moules frites or beef bourguignon. Last but not least, there are some delicious seafood options – the chef's first love. Delightful terrace. Open from 3pm.;Terrace;[]
10775;La Soupière;Switzerland;Zurich;Bahnhofplatz 7, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3769588;8.5394521;20;true;true;French;This sophisticated restaurant on the first floor boasts a stylish interior and professional service. As for the menu, it offers modern variations on classic French cuisine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10776;La Croix d'Ouchy;Switzerland;Lausanne;Avenue d'Ouchy 43, Lausanne, 1006, Switzerland;46.511597;6.629689;72;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant boasts a loyal following of regulars in Lausanne, attracted here by cuisine that features superb traditional flavours alongside a few pasta dishes with an Italian touch, in a classic setting with plenty of character. Prior booking essential.;Terrace;[]
10777;La Brasserie du Royal;Switzerland;Lausanne;Avenue d'Ouchy 40, Lausanne, 1006, Switzerland;46.511218;6.628555;49;true;true;Classic French;The Royal Savoy hotel was one of the favoured haunts of the Spanish court. The brasserie’s culinary focus is highly enticing menu that features dishes such as pâté royal en croûte, goose foie gras, and a mousseline of crayfish from Lake Geneva, as well as seasonal recipes such as hare à la Royale. A truly chic experience!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10778;Vieux-Bois;Switzerland;Geneva;Avenue de la Paix 12, Geneva, 1202, Switzerland;46.2269636;6.138174;93;false;false;French, Farm to table;Just behind the United Nations, this 18C building houses Geneva's hotel management school (EHG) and its restaurant, where tradition reigns supreme. Under the expert supervision of their teachers, students prepare the meals and wait tables. The terrace is also very pleasant.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10779;Hirschen;Switzerland;Erlinsbach;Hauptstrasse 125, Erlinsbach, 5015, Switzerland;47.4064397;8.0070279;61;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Classic, seasonal and regional food is the name of the game here. Guests can enjoy fine dining and vegetarian options in the Zeitgeist restaurant, as well as house classics, including the signature dish: chateaubriand. Tip: The chocolate cake with coffee is sensational! Alternatively, you can order burgers, pasta etc in the cosy Hirschenstube. Popular terrace for summer meals, plus comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10780;Kindli;Switzerland;Zurich;Strehlgasse 24, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3723035;8.5406871;67;false;false;Classic French;A place steeped in history and full of charm – from the hotel's pretty, individually designed guestrooms to the restaurant, in which old wood panelling exudes cosiness. In a pleasant and lively atmosphere, they serve good classic cuisine in the form of dishes such as sea bass with a lemon and caper butter, or Geschnetzeltes Kalbsfilet Zürcher Art (veal strips in a mushroom and cream sauce). At lunchtime, check out the additional daily specials for a quick meal. Tip: Don't forget to make a reservation, as they always get booked up!;Terrace;[]
10781;White Elephant;Switzerland;Zurich;Neumühlequai 42, Zurich, 8006, Switzerland;47.3828756;8.5402571;96;true;false;Thai;This restaurant in the Marriott Hotel is a must for fans of authentic Thai cuisine. Made with market fresh produce, the food is authentic and authentically spicy! Whatever you do, don’t miss the curries.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10782;Da Enzo;Switzerland;Ponte Brolla;Via Ai Grotti, Ponte Brolla, 6652, Switzerland;46.1880895;8.7537409;94;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This Ticino-style stone house boasts a sun-blessed, verdant setting and a beautiful garden-terrace. Take a seat at one of its typical granite tables, either crowned by stone vaulting or shaded by trees, where you can savour exquisite Mediterranean on several tasting menus (including vegetarian) and an à la carte that includes daily specials. Other features include a well-stocked wine cellar and two romantic rustic-style guestrooms. Open for over three decades, Dan Enzo is now run by the second generation of the family.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10783;La Coupole - Matsuhisa;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Serlas 27, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4977215;9.8412784;99;true;false;Fusion, Asian;"Irasshaimase" – this is the exclamation with which diners are greeted here. Housed in the building that was once home to Europe's first indoor tennis courts, Nobuyuki Matsuhisa's restaurant buzzes with infectious vibrancy. The wide-ranging menu features a fusion of Japanese and Peruvian cuisines – everything is prepared in the open kitchen (there is also a sushi bar). The black cod miso is definitely worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
10784;Le Bocca - Restaurant;Switzerland;Saint-Blaise;Avenue Bachelin 11, Saint-Blaise, 2072, Switzerland;47.0127229;6.9860609;59;false;true;French Contemporary;This restaurant serving mouth-watering cuisine has been taken over by Alexandre Luquet and Ana Ronc! Whether seated in the bright, elegant dining space or out on the pretty, leafy terrace, you can enjoy ambitious, contemporary French cuisine, such as the "langoustine and fresh peas" starter or the sole meunière made with fish from small-boat fishing, black garlic and braised endives, which is as tender and juicy as can be! They have a good wine cellar (including Swiss wines) that is open to visitors.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
10785;Restaurant Chastè;Switzerland;Tarasp;Sparsels, Tarasp, 7553, Switzerland;46.779583;10.264588;55;false;true;Classic French;In their delightful little hotel, the Pazeller family offers not only attractive, comfortable guestrooms but also sophisticated cuisine. The restaurant combines two concepts: "Ustaria Chastè" with an upscale evening menu and a simpler lunchtime menu, and "Bocca Fina Chastè" with an evening fine dining set menu. The interior is tasteful and cosy, the service friendly and attentive.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10786;Restaurant de l'Hôtel DuPeyrou;Switzerland;Neuchâtel;Avenue DuPeyrou 1, Neuchâtel, 2000, Switzerland;46.9940248;6.9336034;59;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This exquisite 18C palace ticks all the boxes: elegant yet unconventional, classical yet quirky and even better, it is located right in the heart of town! You will taste the cuisine of Edmond Bavois who works with premium produce, adding an Asian spin to a classical repertory.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10787;Ornellaia;Switzerland;Zurich;St. Annagasse 2, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3723753;8.5377181;82;false;true;Italian;Modern-inspired Italian dishes, such as carne cruda, filetto di vitello Rossini and ravioli carbonara, are prepared in kitchens that are visible from the dining area. The appealing wine list includes a selection from the famous Tuscan wine-growing estate, Ornellaia – from which the restaurant takes its name. You are waited on by a friendly team assembled around host Antonio Bordone, who puts his heart and soul into serving you. This gem of a restaurant is located in a beautifully refurbished building that was once a bank – the door even opens automatically. Sleek design meets historical-looking sandstone walls and decorative art, lending the distinctive high-ceilinged space a modern and elegant Tuscan ambience. At lunchtime there is a small selection of additional dishes.;;[]
10788;Zum Goldenen Schäfli;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Metzgergasse 5, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4266425;9.3755816;30;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Located in the last surviving guild house in the town (1484), this restaurant is full of charm and atmosphere with an all-wooden interior that is especially pleasing. One quirk of the Zunftstube (guild room) is its sloping floor – you might find yourself walking uphill! The cuisine is classic and seasonal, with a Mediterranean touch. Attentive service.;Terrace;[]
10789;La Sorgente;Switzerland;Vico Morcote;portich da Sura 18, Vico Morcote, 6921, Switzerland;45.9302212;8.9210751;37;false;false;Creative;This welcoming restaurant overlooking the lake in the charming village of Vico Morcote serves simple cuisine with a focus on local ingredients, many of which (biodynamic wines, vegetables, olive oil etc) come from the restaurant’s own farm. It’s fantastic to be able to enjoy such fresh produce at reasonable prices – make sure you try the open ravioli with a rabbit ragu, Gotthard cheese fondue and pepper. Guests are advised to leave their car at the garage at the entrance to the village and then walk the short distance to the restaurant. In summer, meals are served under a pergola on the charming terrace.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10790;Schotte-Sepp-Stube / Flickflauder;Switzerland;Weissbad;Im Park 1, Weissbad, 9057, Switzerland;47.3097512;9.4330351;41;false;true;Farm to table, International;Whether you choose to dine in the cosy Schotte-Sepp-Stube, the bright Veranda or the contemporary, minimalist-style Flickflauder, you’re guaranteed good-quality, seasonally inspired cuisine and friendly service at this restaurant, which hosts an “Appenzell evening” with a buffet every Wednesday. The à la carte is available to non-resident guests from 8pm onwards.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10791;Casa Alva;Switzerland;Trin;Via Visut 31, Trin, 7014, Switzerland;46.8277639;9.3616841;99;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant has an upscale, modern interior that beautifully incorporates original architectural features from the former parsonage in which it is housed. The cosy setting is complemented by the warmth and dedication of your hosts, creating a truly inviting atmosphere. A single set menu, "Berg & Küste" ("Mountain & Coast"), is served. Attractive guestrooms available for overnight stays.;;[]
10792;Rössli;Switzerland;Bad Ragaz;Freihofweg 3, Bad Ragaz, 7310, Switzerland;47.0032581;9.5018184;20;true;true;International;Rössli is a pleasant restaurant decorated along clean, modern lines in warm colours. Enjoy the smart place settings and friendly service led by the lady of the house and Ueli Kellenberger’s flavoursome, contemporary cuisine. The mouthwatering offerings include open ravioli with spinach, egg, parmesan and beurre noisette.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10793;Le Bistrot des Ours;Switzerland;Crans-Montana;Route du Pas de l'Ours 41, Crans-Montana, 3963, Switzerland;46.3075393;7.4598232;86;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;It's easy to feel at home in this bistro with its rustic, mountain-inspired atmosphere, complete with terrace commanding a magnificent view of the valley and the surrounding mountains. Here they serve ambitious French-Mediterranean cuisine that caters to all food lovers, courtesy of chef Franck Reynaud, who also cooks at the Michelin-starred restaurant, L'Ours. You'll want to come back for more of this delicious fare that will have your taste buds tingling!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10794;Locanda Locarnese;Switzerland;Locarno;Via Bossi 1, Locarno, 6600, Switzerland;46.1690711;8.794555;79;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Hidden in an alleyway, this pleasant, modern restaurant serves Mediterranean cuisine made from top-quality ingredients. Don’t miss the “Terreni alla Maggia” risotto and the chocolate dessert with a passion fruit sauce. A large fireplace adds to the cosy ambience, making diners feel as though they are guests in a private house. Friendly service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10795;Bel Etage;Switzerland;Basel;Leonhardsgraben 49, Basel, 4051, Switzerland;47.55585;7.58646;85;true;true;Classic French, International;Lovely old parquet flooring, beautiful double doors and high ceilings with crystal chandeliers, as well as decorative art on the walls... Here on the first floor of Der Teufelhof hotel, the stylish salons of the Bel Etage blend harmoniously into the historical setting. In the kitchen, Michael Baader and his team focus on preparing classic cuisine. Diners can either order à la carte or choose between the two set menus – one with three courses, the other with six. The front-of-house team is friendly and professional, providing savvy wine recommendations – the fabulous list is very well curated and comprises 450 labels. In good weather, make a beeline for the pretty terrace and grab a table under the sun awning in the hotel's garden.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10796;Au Chat Noir;Switzerland;Lausanne;Rue Beau-Séjour 27, Lausanne, 1003, Switzerland;46.5175554;6.6371787;62;false;false;Classic Cuisine;In this lively, welcoming restaurant close to the theatre, guests will be tempted by delicious dishes (such as oxtail parmentier – something of a speciality here), a menu of market-inspired specials (on this particular day, a delicious cep fondant as a starter), classic and rather fine flavours. In short, Au Chat Noir is the type of bistro you'd be happy to come across more often. Be sure to book!;Air conditioning;[]
10797;Trübli;Switzerland;Winterthur;Bosshardengässchen 2, Winterthur, 8400, Switzerland;47.4989435;8.7262196;89;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine;There are plenty of reasons to stop off at this historical inn (1785) located in the heart of the old town – the cosy and relaxed atmosphere, the friendly and experienced service team, the wonderful food. In the evening, the concept is a surprise set menu comprising three courses (a vegetarian version is also available), to which you can add an extra dish and/or a dessert. The extremely dedicated chef brings a personal touch to the service, and his passion for wine is palpable, not least in his excellent recommendations drawn from the nicely curated wine list with a focus on German estates. There is a pretty terrace in front of the house. Tip for motorists: the public car park 200m away.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10798;Auberge du Prévoux;Switzerland;Le Locle;Le Prévoux 10, Le Locle, 2400, Switzerland;47.0368623;6.7024294;50;true;true;Classic French;This inn on the edge of a forest in the heart of the Neuchâtel mountains is well known to food-lovers, who head here to enjoy French cuisine with a focus on the very best products selected by a chef who enjoys working with lake fish and different types of game, in particular. Good value for money in the brasserie at lunchtime, with more ambitious cuisine on offer in the evening.;Car park;[]
10799;Drei Könige;Switzerland;Lucerne;Klosterstrasse 10, Lucerne, 6003, Switzerland;47.049515;8.300933;82;true;false;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant has a charming bistro feel and serves delicious food expertly prepared with fresh, carefully selected ingredients. At lunchtime, there is a set menu with options, and the atmosphere is upbeat and lively. In the evening, the pace is a little slower, and the food even more sophisticated.;;[]
10800;Gandria;Switzerland;Zurich;Rudolfstrasse 6, Zurich, 8008, Switzerland;47.3570168;8.5575216;35;true;true;Italian;Chef-patron Adriano Peroncini is originally from Puglia, but his years of travelling took him through Italy and far beyond. Since 2016 he has had his own restaurant, here in Zurich's Seefeld district. In this nice, cosy space, where an inviting atmosphere reigns, he introduces diners to his fresh southern Italian-inspired cuisine – good choices from the menu include the octopus or Piedmontese Fassona beef and, of course, the delicious pasta dishes! In addition, there is an exclusively Italian wine list that covers most of the wine-growing regions, as well as "servizio alla maniera italiana" – authentic service that will make you feel at home!;Terrace;[]
10801;Bad Schauenburg;Switzerland;Liestal;Schauenburgerstr. 76, Liestal, 4410, Switzerland;47.491764;7.712748;54;false;false;Classic French;Whether you're seated in the Basler Stübli, the Gaststube or the Veranda, the fine dining restaurant of Hotel Bad Schauenburg serves classic French cuisine that takes its cue from the seasons in all its lovely rooms. Some of the produce comes from the hotel's own garden. The highlight in summer is of course the delightful terrace!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10802;De la Gare - La Table des Suter;Switzerland;Lucens;Avenue de la Gare 13, Lucens, 1522, Switzerland;46.707607;6.8414575;43;false;false;Classic French;This family-run institution housed in a large ochre-coloured building in front of Lucens train station is a real hit. This is undoubtedly down to its winning combination of professionalism and a very warm welcome. The set menus include ambitious classic French dishes made from top-quality ingredients, eg "grand cru" beef cooked two ways, with a Pinot Noir sauce, Swiss chard and stuffed parmentine potatoes. The adjacent bistro also represents excellent value for money. And if you would like to extend your stay, there are neat and practical guestrooms available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10803;Le Monument;Switzerland;Lens;Place du Village 3, Lens, 1978, Switzerland;46.2793916;7.4464805;91;false;false;Classic Cuisine;In this welcoming and well-maintained auberge near the church in the centre of the village, the kitchen team has mastered the classics (the different tartare dishes on the menu are particularly memorable!) as highlighted in cuisine that showcases subtle Italian influences. Recommended.;Terrace;[]
10804;Rechberg 1837;Switzerland;Zurich;Chorgasse 20, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3740149;8.546173;85;false;true;Innovative, Swiss;The Rechberg 1837 is a pleasant restaurant with a unique philosophy – it only uses regional produce that was available around 1837 (the year the house was built), i. e. before industrialisation. Innovative dishes such as slices of country pork on pea puree with fried barley and pickled onion are served in the evening, with a more traditional selection available at lunchtime. Cosy atmosphere and charming service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10806;Minamo;Switzerland;Lucerne;Haldenstrasse 10, Lucerne, 6002, Switzerland;47.0552235;8.319624;51;false;false;Japanese;With its pared-back Far Eastern decor and an eight-course traditional Japanese omakase menu served to all diners at the same time, this restaurant brings countertop dining and a slice of Japan to the exclusive Mandarin Oriental. From your comfortable seat at the counter, you can watch, for example, various nigiri being prepared before your very eyes – the chef will gladly expound on his work and philosophy. NB: There are a maximum of eight places available, so it is essential that you book!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10807;al lago;Switzerland;Ascona;Via Circonvallazione 26, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1523909;8.7709275;52;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Housed in a type of winter garden with a charming terrace (the jewel in the crown!), this restaurant serves dishes that combine modern influences with more classic touches, all prepared using ingredients of the best quality. Make sure you try the risotto made from Carnaroli rice with red pepper, green sauce and Cantabrian anchovies, as well as the Guanaja chocolate mousse and ice cream with mixed berries. An excellent selection of wine and young, friendly service complete the picture.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10808;Riva;Switzerland;Ascona;Piazza G. Motta 25, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1541286;8.768582;15;true;false;Seafood;Perhaps the only true fish restaurant in Ascona where fish specialities are nothing short of exceptional, but meat lovers will not be disappointed either.Situated inside the Seven Boutique Hotel, Riva offers a maritime atmosphere with colourful touches that recall the blue expanse and a tasty cuisine declined in tasting or à la carte menus, from ‘I Crudi’ with oysters & co. to ‘Sogliola alla mugnaia with lettuce, capers and spring onion’. Definitely a great address!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10809;Gourmet Louis;Switzerland;Bottmingen;Schlossgasse 9, Bottmingen, 4103, Switzerland;47.5236569;7.5703533;21;false;true;Classic French;This idyllic 13C water castle is a tranquil haven nestled just outside Basel. Surrounded by a moat, the property with its old trees can be accessed from two sides via wooden bridges. This establishment boasts two culinary concepts: a brasserie and this fine dining restaurant. Head chef Guy Wallyn, having already worked at the castle for several years, serves up classic French cuisine in the form of a four- to six-course set menu, which can be supplemented with cheeses from the trolley. To complement this, a selection of fine wines is available. Up to 20 guests can be accommodated in the lavishly renovated historical Steinsaal (or "stone hall") in the left wing of the castle – the 18C stuccowork is stunning. The small private dining space in the tower is ideal for groups. Tip: Enjoy an aperitif or coffee in the castle's courtyard.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10810;Brasserie du Château;Switzerland;Bottmingen;Schlossgasse 9, Bottmingen, 4103, Switzerland;47.5236654;7.5701876;79;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The brasserie is a wonderful addition to the gourmet restaurant ‘Louis’ on the magnificent historic castle estate. Here you can enjoy French brasserie cuisine made from fresh produce, from ‘Beef tartare classique’ and ‘Moules marnière’ to ‘Veal ragout Blanquette de Veau’ or dishes for two, such as ‘Chateaubriand’, in a classic ambience for lunch and dinner. The well-stocked and extensive wine list is the same as that of the ‘Louis’. In summer, the terrace facing the moat under shady old plane trees is an idyllic spot.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10811;Badalucci;Switzerland;Lugano;Viale Cassarate 3, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;46.0063929;8.9604973;37;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;A historic restaurant with its roots in Italian cuisine. Originally from the island of Procida in southern Italy, the chef here focuses mainly on fish-based dishes, although the menu also features delicious meat options and vegetarian recipes for each course – whatever you order, seasonal ingredients are to the fore in this urban-style eatery situated slightly away from the centre. The wine list highlights the owners’ passion for champagne via highly respected labels from interesting small-scale producers.;Air conditioning;[]
10812;PURO;Switzerland;Basel;Aeschengraben 25, Basel, 4051, Switzerland;47.5492803;7.5925907;82;true;false;Fusion;The restaurant on the first floor of the Mövenpick Hotel serves interesting and ambitious cuisine. This comes in the form of a very appealing fusion concept of Asian and Latin American-inspired dishes made with plenty of regional produce, but also ingredients from around the globe. The food is down to earth, flavoursome and fresh! This is complemented by an international wine list, extremely friendly service and a stylish interior.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10813;Rosa Pulver;Switzerland;Winterthur;Stadthausstrasse 10, Winterthur, 8400, Switzerland;47.5006037;8.7268265;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Comprising four, five or seven courses, the "Rosa Pulver" set menu is the perfect choice for fans of modern and creative cuisine based on regional and seasonal ingredients – a vegetarian version is also available. Alternatively, there is an à la carte selection including dishes such as ravioli with a goose egg filling, a potato medley, wild herbs and rapeseed. Individual wine pairings are available for the set menu. In keeping with the traditional setting of the restaurant, rustic elements have been preserved and incorporated into the minimalist-style modern decor. Friendly, easy-going waitstaff.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10814;Equo 1706;Switzerland;Weggis;Seestrasse 52, Weggis, 6353, Switzerland;47.031759;8.4249367;18;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Records of this building go back to 1706, at which time it was a tavern. Today, the restaurant of the Rössli hotel, which is not far from Vierwaldstätter See, has a nicely pared-back interior and a pleasant terrace. It serves ambitious modern cuisine with seasonal and international influences – you can order à la carte or opt for the surprise menu. Hotel patrons get to relax in well-kept guestrooms and the spa facilities.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10815;Le Partage;Switzerland;Crans-Montana;Chemin du Béthania 1, Crans-Montana, 3960, Switzerland;46.3085686;7.476398;61;false;false;French Contemporary, Sharing;Located in the luxury Aïda Hotel and Spa, this restaurant’s concept is downright intriguing. The set menu is served in courses, each of which is comprised of several small dishes and diners choose either 10 or 15 "tasting portions" to be shared. The ambitious cuisine rolls out a regional score courtesy of a wide range of local ingredients. Established on two floors, the Alpine-inspired interior is both welcoming and stylish thanks to a profusion of reclaimed wood and dressed stone, elegant herringbone parquet flooring and an open fireplace, complemented by high-quality fabrics and splendid solid wood tables, without forgetting the knockout view from the terrace. The front-of-house staff is friendly, attentive and polished. Teatime in the lounge and brunch on Sundays.;Terrace;[]
10816;Silex;Switzerland;Zurich;Freyastrasse 3, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3715042;8.5245449;90;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is located in a lively residential area. Plenty of Swiss produce goes into the modern seasonal dishes, which are created in the partially visible kitchen. The restaurant is just as committed to sustainability as it is to wine – selected by connoisseurs, the distinctive wine list is testament to a true passion for the grape. British-born chef George Tomlin, previously sous-chef at London's The Clove Club, expresses his creative streak in dishes such as grilled slices of elm mushroom with roasted black onions and a creamy buttermilk and roasted yeast espuma. You can opt to go à la carte or take the five-course tasting menu (also vegetarian). The vibe is deliberately kept simple, with a decor boasting clean lines, and there is a nice terrace outside, in front of this corner plot. The service is friendly and laid back. Just the sort of restaurant you would want in your neighbourhood!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10817;Au Vieux Manoir;Switzerland;Monthey;Route de Choëx 155, Monthey, 1871, Switzerland;46.237952;6.958157;65;true;true;French Contemporary;This spot is truly the stuff of dreams! Built in 1882 by renowned physician Dr Victor Guénebaud, the property boasts historical charm and a magnificent location, complemented by what is probably one of the finest terraces in the Valais canton! Inside, aesthetically pleasing details such as a wonderful old parquet floor, a beautifully crafted wooden ceiling and striking fabric wallpaper make for a stylish setting. The chef-patron's French-based cuisine alone merits a visit – the dishes are expertly prepared with top-notch, super-fresh ingredients. Should you wish to spend the night in this wonderful place, book one of the five comfortable guestrooms done out in a tasteful, classical style.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10818;Rosmarin;Switzerland;Lenzburg;Eisengasse 32, Lenzburg, 5600, Switzerland;47.3876095;8.1808479;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Following its relocation within Lenzburg, Rosmarin entices diners with a cool concept: The modern setting allows for up to 12 guests to sit at a counter right by the open kitchen, where chef-patron Philipp Audolensky prepares a creative surprise menu comprising five to seven courses (vegetarian or vegan options are available by prior arrangement). Appetisers and pastries are prepared by Céline Huber. They make a point of using select regional ingredients and combine them with seasonings from around the globe. The chef himself serves the food and recommends the perfect wine pairings, which adds a charming personal touch to your dining experience. Water, soft drinks and coffee are included in the price. There is a beautifully restored old vaulted cellar for groups. Tip for motorists: Sandweg multi-storey car park.;Counter dining;[]
10819;Le Deck Restaurant;Switzerland;Chexbres;Route de la Corniche 4, Chexbres, 1070, Switzerland;46.4800801;6.7736966;69;false;true;French;The restaurant is part of Le Baron Tavernier, the chic little spa hotel opposite, and boasts a magnificent location with panoramic views. In addition to a fabulous vista over Lake Geneva, this place promises ambitious and tasteful French cuisine, prepared with top-notch produce, as well as friendly and attentive service. In summer, the open-air bar is the perfect spot for a drink.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10820;Le Vingt Deux - Table d'hôtes;Switzerland;Verbier;Route des Creux 22, Verbier, 1936, Switzerland;46.0974359;7.2298133;24;true;false;French Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;It is well worth venturing into this discreet and exclusive fine dining table d'hôte concealed by a secret door behind the bar. A handpicked group of 15 or so guests are welcomed by the owner himself, who is then on hand throughout the meal to ensure that everything runs smoothly. The kitchen sends out elegant and carefully crafted classic dishes based on excellent regional ingredients – some with subtle Mediterranean touches. An intimate and hospitable atmosphere reigns here, with the same relaxed style as in the lively, bustling bar. You'll need to book well in advance.;;[]
10823;Le Rossignol;Switzerland;Lausanne;Avenue du Léman 36, Lausanne, 1005, Switzerland;46.5153976;6.6493036;21;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;At Le Rossignol (which is French for nightingale but also happens to be the chef's name), Willy Rossignol finds a captive audience for his smooth classical repertoire of indulgent, flavoursome and well-balanced dishes, prepared using fresh ingredients. Mara, his wife, extends guests an attentive welcome in the simple, well-kept space or out on the terrace in fine weather. Dishes to try include the Gragnano paccheri with wild mushrooms with an aged Parmigiano Reggiano gratin, or thinly sliced chamois with Kampot pepper.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10824;MOzern;Switzerland;Lucerne;Haldenstrasse 10, Lucerne, 6002, Switzerland;47.0552286;8.3196883;33;false;true;International, Asian;This part of the Mandarin Oriental's culinary portfolio serves food all day. In addition to lunch and dinner, you can have breakfast and afternoon tea here – all in tasteful surroundings that combine a stylish, old-world feel with a brasserie atmosphere. The menu features international cuisine including classics like Angus beef tartare and raclette cheese burger, as well as Asian bar snacks such as crispy duck rolls. The bar serves an excellent assortment of drinks. Tip: Drop in at the Grand Casino next door.;Wheelchair access;[]
10825;Le Grill;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai du Mont-Blanc 19, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.21003;6.150915;85;true;false;Meats and Grills;The knockout view of Lake Geneva and its iconic Jet d’Eau is unquestionably one of the highlights of this fine establishment. However, that afforded by the kitchens, the rotisserie and the cold room where the superb cuts of meat are stored is equally uplifting. Unsurprisingly, specialities include grilled fish and meat but there is also tofu. The set menu known as "Le Grill Experience" is an excellent option for those with a healthy appetite, as is the Grill Burger! Impeccable service.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10826;Le Restaurant / Le Relais;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Serlas 27, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4978101;9.8415458;83;false;true;Classic Cuisine;If you are looking for excellence and elegance, you are in the right place at Le Restaurant or Le Relais of the venerable Badrutt's Palace! In an atmosphere of luxury, the attentive front-of-house team provides classic service. The flavourful cuisine is made from exclusive ingredients and the menu also features a number of dishes that are prepared at your table, e.g. flambées, tartar etc. Whatever you opt for, there is a first-class selection of wines from the best vineyards to accompany your meal. Tip: You can also have breakfast here - accompanied by views of the lake and mountains.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
10827;Baur's;Switzerland;Zurich;Talstrasse 1, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3676556;8.5391476;26;false;false;International, Classic Cuisine;The chic, rather imposing deluxe brasserie of the famous Baur au Lac hotel does full justice to the top-notch spirit of gastronomy with which the grand hotel is synonymous. It serves international cuisine firmly rooted in the classics and made with excellent ingredients. The wine list is compiled by one of the best sommeliers in the world.;Air conditioning;[]
10828;Casino Restaurant;Switzerland;Berne;Casinoplatz 1, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.9472595;7.448286;21;false;true;Modern French;In the beautiful building of the Casino Bern, which opened in 1909 in the centre of the old town, the mixture of a great historical setting and brasserie chic exudes a special flair, which continues in summer on the wonderful large terrace - here you can enjoy the view of the Aare under shady trees. The menu features classic dishes as well as Italian influences. There is a menu (also vegetarian) as well as an a la carte offer in addition to ‘Grosses pièces’ for two people. Next to the restaurant is the ‘Salon d'Or’ with bistro bar - here you can enjoy coffee and cake as well as wines and cocktails throughout the day.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10829;GLACIER;Switzerland;Grindelwald;Endweg 55, Grindelwald, 3818, Switzerland;46.621507;8.0300702;96;true;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;What a great location right in front of the Eiger North Face! The fine dining restaurant of the chic boutique hotel (also called GLACIER) makes the most of its surroundings with a floor-to-ceiling window front – and a wonderful terrace for a magical view! The cuisine is ambitious, modern, creative and seasonal. In the evening, a set menu is available in three formats: "Découverte" with three courses, "Promenade" with five courses and "Excursion" with seven courses (the last two courses are surprise dishes). There are vegetarian versions of all three. Great emphasis is placed on selecting high-quality ingredients, with a preference for supplies from local producers. The 320-year-old wine cellar is home to around 500 labels, 160 of which are also available by the glass. An enthusiastic sommelier provides astute recommendations.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10831;Franz;Switzerland;Lucerne;Haldenstrasse 4, Lucerne, 6006, Switzerland;47.054762;8.3146312;47;false;false;Austrian, Classic Cuisine;Here in the elegant restaurant of the Grand Hotel National, you could almost be in Vienna: marble columns and high ceilings, waltz music (as well as more modern tunes) playing quietly in the background, and classic Austrian dishes, from Tafelspitz and Wiener schnitzel to apple strudel. Choose from a list of good Austrian wines. Great view of the lake, especially from the terrace. Smaller menu in the afternoon. Cakes are also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10832;Sablier;Switzerland;Zurich;The Circle 23, Zurich, 8053, Switzerland;47.45269;8.562208;43;false;false;French Contemporary;Definitely one of the coolest restaurants in town! On the eighth floor of a newly built section of the airport, the incredibly high ceilings, chic interior design, two large glass-fronted wine cabinets and stylish bar are really impressive. The menu features French-inspired cuisine, with an additional lunch deal available daily and brunch served every Sunday. The rooftop terrace has to be the highlight! Tip for motorists: park in Parkhaus 4, south exit.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
10833;L'Etoile;Switzerland;Noville;Chemin du Battoir 1, Noville, 1845, Switzerland;46.3819609;6.899839;17;true;true;Classic French;Whether you are seated in the chic bistro, in the winter garden or in the attractive shaded garden, this family-run establishment offers a warm welcome and a friendly atmosphere. The seasonal menu, with dishes prepared to order, features local producers. The thick and creamy crème brûlée, delicately flavoured with orange, is unforgettable. The set lunch menu is a must!;Car park,Terrace;[]
10834;Auberge de l'Abbaye de Montheron;Switzerland;Cugy;Route de l'Abbaye 2, Cugy, 1053, Switzerland;46.5902002;6.6640386;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Located in a former Cistercian monastery that dates back to 1442, this restaurant proposes food that is very much of the moment. The original and exciting dishes draw heavily on local organic produce and heritage vegetables. Diners are won over by thoroughly modern fare that has been devised with a genuine concern for sustainability, such as suckling lamb served with pak choi and rhubarb. Appealing terrace on the edge of the forest, and a young and trendy atmosphere. A winning formula.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10835;Spices Kitchen & Terrace;Switzerland;Obbürgen;Bürgenstock 17, Obbürgen, 6363, Switzerland;46.99684;8.378948;75;true;false;Asian, Sushi;The aromas that waft out of the large show kitchen here are sure to get your taste buds tingling with their promise of pan-Asian delights from Japanese to Chinese, Thai and Indian dishes, all authentic and made using the very best ingredients. There’s also a stunning view!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10836;Restaurant Burgstrasse9;Switzerland;Thun;Burgstrasse 9, Thun, 3600, Switzerland;46.7595711;7.6317559;15;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Dating back over 300 years, this establishment, once a smithy and locksmith's shop, has a rustic-meets-historical charm that beautifully incorporates more modern features. French-born chef-patron Stephan Koltes uses exclusively regional produce to create modern cuisine that is full of contrasts. The individual courses of his set menu are each available in the form of two small dishes made from the same ingredients – an enticing option. Tip for motorists: Use the Schlossberg multi-storey car park.;;[]
10837;OX'n;Switzerland;Schenkon;Dorfstrasse 23, Schenkon, 6214, Switzerland;47.1721199;8.1387888;63;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Where the old Ochsen inn once stood, the new OX'n stands today with its eye-catching modern design – all the glass gives the place an airy feel and a pleasing sense of transparency. The overall atmosphere is trendy yet inviting. In good weather, the terrace beckons. Friendly service. A surprise menu is served Wed-Sat evenings, and there is an additional à la carte selection Wed-Thu. At lunchtime, a simplified version of the evening surprise menu is available. Alternatively, you could opt for the set menu that changes every week, or something from the à la carte selection. Featuring ingredients sourced from local producers, this is flavoursome seasonal cuisine. The Entlebuch trout with asparagus and beurre blanc is a must-try. Tip: If you fancy an after-work beer or a cocktail, pop into the bar for a quick drink, or feel free to stay a while longer.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10838;Ochsen;Switzerland;Muri;Caspar-Wolf-Weg 1, Muri, 5630, Switzerland;47.2737449;8.3364144;40;true;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Located just metres from the monastery, the venerable Ochsen dates back to 1596. In its current iteration with an avant-garde look, it is part of the three-building Hotel Caspar, which has stylishly designed guestrooms. In the open kitchen, regional ingredients go into modern and creative cooking – interesting cuisine that is "close to nature", with fire, aromatic woods, smoked and grilled dishes play a central role.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
10839;ROSI;Switzerland;Zurich;Sihlfeldstrasse 89, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3764246;8.5162879;86;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;With its vibrant atmosphere and unique charm, this inviting self-proclaimed "neo-Bavarian" restaurant stands out from the crowd. It embodies a fusion of trendy, urban-casual vibes and cuisine inspired by the owner's Allgäu roots. In the four-course "Schmankerl Menu", the 12-course "Wirtshaus Maximus Menu" and the small à la carte selection, Markus Stöckle transforms traditional dishes into original creations packed with flavour. A prime example is the "Radi Wickerl" (braised leaves, sansho, pickled kombu and radish). The wine list, which includes a selection of natural wines, is also impressive. The service is pleasingly down-to-earth and friendly – the charismatic proprietor is also on hand, making sure each guest feels well looked after.;Terrace;[]
10840;Käserei;Switzerland;Murten;Rathausgasse 34, Murten, 3280, Switzerland;46.929268;7.117568;35;false;false;International;Whether you are seated at a bare or beautifully set table, in this listed former cheese dairy, the dedicated hosts serve high-quality international and regional cuisine that is not only a hit with the locals. Tip: From Tuesdays to Fridays, an inexpensive lunch is served. Incidentally, the building is located in the heart of the pretty old town – perfect for a stroll!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10841;Brasserie 1809;Switzerland;Saas-Fee;Lomattenstrasse 6, Saas-Fee, 3906, Switzerland;46.1109505;7.9293168;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The restaurant is done out in a modern Alpine style, with an interior that is upscale, sleek and at the same time inviting. As for the food great store is set by regional produce and sustainable farming. Select ingredients go into creating tasty seasonal dishes. It is pleasant to eat on the lovely terrace, and not only in summer! The Capra hotel has wonderful inviting guestrooms.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10842;mille sens - les goûts du monde;Switzerland;Berne;Spitalgasse 38, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.9483505;7.4412253;59;true;false;International;At this pleasantly lively, modern restaurant in the Schweizerhof Passage near the train station, chef Domingo S. Domingo takes you on a culinary journey around the world, also drawing on his Australian and Filipino roots. At lunchtime, options include a small set menu ("Business Lunch") and the "Quicktray" comprising four dishes on one plate. In the evening, guests can choose from the "Domingo Pur Menu Surprise" and "Tavolata" – also available in a large portion to share. The small selection of bowls is available at both mealtimes.;Air conditioning;[]
10843;Roter Bären;Switzerland;Basel;Ochsengasse 17, Basel, 4058, Switzerland;47.5616838;7.5915757;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This pretty restaurant in the red-light district has a rather original concept that is popular with diners: in an open kitchen, the chefs conjure up ambitious appetiser-sized dishes that draw inspiration from modern culinary trends – three are recommended, then maybe a dessert to round things off. Great bar.;;[]
10844;Restaurant LA;Switzerland;Basel;St. Johanns-Vorstadt 13, Basel, 4056, Switzerland;47.562886;7.5848343;25;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;If you're not careful, you might end up walking right past the narrow façade of this mid-terrace restaurant. Here, an intriguing modern dining experience is proposed – and that goes for both the minimalist interior and the seasonal cuisine. Available either à la carte or as a surprise menu comprising four or six courses, the dishes are well-thought-out, with harmoniously balanced flavours. The staff are more than happy to cater to special dietary needs – please mention these when making your reservation. From some tables it is possible to see into the kitchen. In summer, there is terrace seating on the pavement overlooking the tram line.;Terrace;[]
10845;Le Guillaume Tell;Switzerland;Aran;Route de la Petite Corniche 5, Aran, 1091, Switzerland;46.4979041;6.7104549;25;false;false;Creative;A charming pink house in the heart of this wine-producing village overlooking Lake Geneva. In this traditional setting, chef Denis Velen conjures up creative gastronomic cuisine that combines originality with delicious flavours as witnessed in dishes such as crispy spiced sea bass with choucroute.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10846;La Fontana;Switzerland;Locarno;Via ai Monti della Trinità 44, Locarno, 6600, Switzerland;46.1728458;8.7954249;88;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Splendidly located inside the Hotel Belvedere, at an altitude of approximately 240m, this elegant south-facing restaurant boasts a splendid terrace and a lounge space. Depending on where you sit, watch the chef at work in the kitchen or enjoy the impressive views through La Fontana’s ground floor picture windows overlooking its verdant surroundings. The culinary focus here is on modern and seasonal Mediterranean cuisine without neglecting the region’s gastronomic roots. In addition to the classic menu, you can also choose the 4- or 5-course tasting option as well as the restaurant’s signature dishes such as the La Fontana tartare, the Chateaubriand, and the Raviolini del Plin. The extensive glass-fronted wine cabinets at the entrance provide an impressive backdrop.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10847;Schmitte;Switzerland;Grindelwald;Swiss Alp Resort 1, Grindelwald, 3818, Switzerland;46.6252656;8.0313822;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This is the fine dining restaurant of the long-established Hotel Schweizerhof. The small space is inviting, with an elegant and cosy feel, and the service team is friendly and attentive. The dishes are rooted in classic cuisine and draw on modern influences. The tasting menus "Fauna" and "Flora" (vegetarian) can be ordered in a four- to six-course format. The hotel garden has a sun terrace and there is also a bar.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10848;Hide & Seek;Switzerland;Ascona;via del Segnale 10, Ascona, 6612, Switzerland;46.1503589;8.7903035;47;false;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Ayurvedic philosophy inspires part of the menu at this restaurant, where Mediterranean culinary techniques and ingredients result in colourful, playful dishes. In fine weather, don’t miss the magnificent terrace overlooking the garden with its small lake and abundance of flowers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10849;PRISMA Expérience;Switzerland;Vitznau;Seestrasse 18, Vitznau, 6354, Switzerland;47.0152316;8.4774529;82;false;true;Asian and Western;Housed in the exclusive Park Hotel Vitznau, which dates back to 1903, this elegant yet casual restaurant whisks you away on a culinary voyage. Japanese fusion cuisine is the name of the game here. There is an omakase menu (for two or more diners), as well as an à la carte selection including sushi, sashimi, Wagyu dishes and ramen. The location overlooking the lake is a draw in itself, and it goes without saying that tables on the terrace are highly coveted.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10850;Chez Be;Switzerland;Sursee;Mühleplatz 11, Sursee, 6210, Switzerland;47.1714921;8.1102391;68;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;Following on from their successful restaurant, Amrein's, the amiable couple at the helm has embarked on a new culinary adventure. Romy takes good care of customers, while Beat cooks up fresh Mediterranean dishes. Shorter menu at lunchtime. The charming modern bistro-style interior with its open kitchen and the terrace giving onto the little square (Mühleplatz) are both lovely places to sit and eat.;Terrace;[]
10851;Lumières;Switzerland;Lucerne;Kanonenstrasse, Lucerne, 6003, Switzerland;47.0516043;8.2948508;37;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The location is simply divine! The restaurant of Hotel Château Gütsch affords a breathtaking view over the city and the lake surrounded by mountains, especially from the large terrace – the perfect setting for a romantic dinner! Inspired by the hotel's 140-year history, the interior design draws on Belle Époque design elements but also incorporates nods to the natural surroundings. Fresh, modern accents successfully bridge the gap to the present day. The cuisine is influenced by the culinary traditions of France and the Mediterranean. Opt for the "Chef's Choice" set menu or order à la carte. At midday, the shorter "Time for Lunch" set menu is available, along with other dishes.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10852;Sonne Seuzach;Switzerland;Seuzach;Ohringerstrasse 2, Seuzach, 8472, Switzerland;47.5363323;8.7296927;85;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Located in the town centre, Sonne is an inviting restaurant. The interior is tastefully sleek, the atmosphere warm and welcoming, and there is a gorgeous terrace out in front of the glass-paned façade. The cuisine is seasonal, and showcases a range of regional produce. Reduced menu at lunchtime. Friendly and professional front-of-house team. There is also a bar. Modern guestrooms available for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10853;Restaurant Olivo;Switzerland;Lucerne;Haldenstrasse 6, Lucerne, 6006, Switzerland;47.0550306;8.3168543;54;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic French;Its Belle Epoque style lends this restaurant on the first floor of the Grand Casino a distinct elegance and charm that hark back to a bygone era. Under a high ceiling with moulding and chandeliers, Mediterranean-inspired cuisine is served in the form of a set menu or à la carte. The "Dinner & Casino" packages are also worth mentioning. Fabulous balcony terrace with lake and mountain views. Tip: Park in the casino garage.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10854;Ahaan Thai;Switzerland;Arosa;Innere Poststrasse 269, Arosa, 7050, Switzerland;46.7747809;9.6648262;54;false;false;Thai;A slice of Thailand in Graubünden! As well as dim sum and the usual range of curries, the menu features specialities such as Goong Hom Pha (shrimp in a blanket) – deep-fried king prawns with a sweet chilli sauce. Diners can also look forward to friendly service in a comfortable setting with elegant Thai-inspired decor. The restaurant is housed in the attractive Arosa Kulm Hotel, which dates back to 1882.;Car park;[]
10855;Potato-FINE FOOD RESTAURANT;Switzerland;Zermatt;Bahnhofstrasse 10, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0230515;7.7476945;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This pleasant little restaurant in a lively street (Bahnhofstrasse) has a down-to-earth and friendly atmosphere, where the cordial service is in invitation to sit back and enjoy your evening, while. Tasty modern dishes are served in the form of a set menu made from top-notch regional ingredients sourced from within a 50km radius whenever possible.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10856;Belle Vue;Switzerland;Adelboden;Bellevuestrasse 15, Adelboden, 3715, Switzerland;46.4918082;7.5561949;88;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;To make the most of the simply stunning mountain views, opt for a table near the large glass-planed front – or on the delightful terrace! Complementing the wonderful scenery, the interior of the Bellevue Parkhotel & Spa restaurant boasts a sleek design that provides the backdrop for the fine dining menu: classic dishes such as roast duck breast with potato galettes are served in the evening, and a simpler à la carte selection is available at lunchtime. Choose an accompaniment from the exquisite wine list.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10857;Osteria del Centenario;Switzerland;Muralto;viale Verbano 17, Muralto, 6600, Switzerland;46.1717205;8.8031524;49;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A restaurant that has been renovated in contemporary style, in complete harmony with its attractive setting overlooking the scenic lakeside promenade. Talented chef Egon Bajardi conjures up interesting Mediterranean cuisine with a focus on creative technique and the occasional exotic touch. Don’t miss his selection of desserts, including Crema Catalana with pumpkin, orange and bay leaf gelato.;Terrace;[]
10858;Zum See;Switzerland;Zermatt;Zum See 24, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0060638;7.7321852;37;false;false;Swiss, International;A pleasant walk in the mountains leads to this charming restaurant with a romantic terrace. Simple, good cuisine is served.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10859;Sonnenhof;Switzerland;Saanen;Sonnenhofweg 33, Saanen, 3792, Switzerland;46.4927662;7.2462367;66;true;true;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;Set above the valley, this cosy, rustic restaurant boasts a wonderfully sunny terrace and fabulous views of the mountains.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10860;Kronenhalle;Switzerland;Zurich;Rämistrasse 4, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3675657;8.5455505;43;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This building, constructed in 1862, is a Zurich institution, and is located on Bellevue Square. Be sure to take a look at the art collection put together over a period of decades. The atmosphere is traditional, as is the cooking.;Air conditioning;[]
10861;Accademia del Gusto;Switzerland;Zurich;Rotwandstrasse 48, Zurich, 8004, Switzerland;47.3753225;8.5285941;83;false;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant is a smash hit with its many regulars, which is hardly surprising considering the terrific food and lively and buzzing atmosphere. Over time, various dishes have achieved classic status. While Stefano Piscopo conjures up delectable creations such as home-made pasta (eg veal ravioli with sage butter) or marinated tuna tartare, his charming wife presides front-of-house. The handful of tables on the pavement tend to get snapped up quickly.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10863;Landhaus Liebefeld;Switzerland;Liebefeld;Schwarzenburgstrasse 134, Liebefeld, 3097, Switzerland;46.9323759;7.421783;74;false;false;Classic French;Diners at this restaurant in a converted bailiwick (1671) choose between the Gaststube and the more elegant – but no less cosy – Rôtisserie. The cuisine is regional and seasonal, eg beef entrecôte with a herb butter foam. In summer, you can tuck into barbecue dishes in the small garden. On Thursday, Friday and Saturday evenings, le caveau serves a vegan set menu. For guests wishing to stay overnight, there are also tasteful guestrooms.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10864;Le Café Suisse;Switzerland;Bex;Rue Centrale 41, Bex, 1880, Switzerland;46.2503337;7.0155428;15;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This former village café has morphed into a buzzy, friendly eatery decked in colourful cartoon murals. Youthful Marie Robert, assisted by an almost woman only team, wholeheartedly regales diners with creative, light-hearted dishes that are in tune with the seasons to be washed down with excellent local tipples. Robert has a flair for spontaneously showcasing seasonal ingredients. Examples include a mousseline of seabream enhanced by a whipped beurre blanc or an incredibly powerful and heady duo of blueberry and chocolate. Be bold and opt for her surprise menu – a hit with regulars, it is as playful as it is indulgent.;;[]
10867;Auberge d'Onex;Switzerland;Onex;Route de Loëx 18, Onex, 1213, Switzerland;46.1837966;6.0969451;83;true;false;Italian, Traditional Cuisine;Since 1977, this inn has been nestled in verdant surroundings in the former clubhouse of Geneva's first golf course. It serves traditional Italian cuisine, including the chef's specialities of penne with vodka and penne alla Norma (a Sicilian dish that pays tribute to the composer Vincenzo Bellini, who was from the island), but also classics such as vitello tonnato. The dessert trolley features Italian specialities and a choice of fresh fruit.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10868;Landgasthof Wartegg;Switzerland;Wigoltingen / Hasli;Müllheimerstrasse 3, Wigoltingen / Hasli, 8554, Switzerland;47.588804;9.0140047;41;false;true;Classic French;In this historical inn – run by the Frei family since 1982 – they serve fresh, flavoursome seasonal cuisine with classical foundations, made using excellent produce. The lunch menu is also popular. The ambience ranges from rustic to elegant, with a beautiful outdoor terrace shaded by trees. There are comfortable guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10869;Brücke;Switzerland;Niedergösgen;Hauptstrasse 2, Niedergösgen, 5013, Switzerland;47.372832;7.9976117;65;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;The superb location on the River Aare is a big draw here, and it goes without saying that the terrace is in high demand! As for the food: a modern spin is put on fresh, traditional cuisine. The emphasis is laid squarely on the quality and seasonality of the produce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10870;La Table du Palafitte;Switzerland;Neuchâtel;Route des Gouttes-d'Or 2, Neuchâtel, 2000, Switzerland;47.00472;6.964792;82;false;true;Classic Cuisine;The “Menu Découverte” carries guests away on a journey inspired by the time-honoured culinary traditions of the Mediterranean coast. Choose between the dining room or the large waterfront terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10872;Sala of Tokyo;Switzerland;Zurich;Schützengasse 5, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.376217;8.5401828;22;false;true;Japanese;Classic Japanese cuisine made from top-notch ingredients is the name of the game here. The sushi and sashimi, tempura, and robata grill specialities, as well as the sukiyaki and shabu shabu stews all come highly recommended. Another draw of this place is its inviting interior, which is sleek and simple, yet cosy at the same time. You can watch the sushi master at work at a small counter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
10873;Hide & Seek;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Maistra 3, Saint Moritz, 7512, Switzerland;46.4777473;9.8110408;21;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;If you like to dine in a lively, modern atmosphere, the restaurant of Hotel Giardino Mountain is for you. The decor features a combination of trendy, chic features and rustic wood. Attentive front-of-house team and Mediterranean and Swiss dishes that are aromatic and flavoursome, made with fresh, often regional produce. Lunch is served in the bar-lounge.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10874;Thai Garden;Switzerland;Lucerne;Pilatusstrasse 29, Lucerne, 6002, Switzerland;47.0480749;8.3052017;44;false;false;Thai, Asian;You could almost fancy you are in Thailand: with dim lighting, Far Eastern background music, Thai decoration, large ceiling fans and a babbling fountain, the setting alone transports you to an exotic world. Complementing this is exceptionally friendly service and authentic Thai cuisine – the spiciness can be adjusted to suit diners' individual preferences. Tip: The appealing lunch deal is available in two variations: the "Thai Box" and the "Vegi Box".;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10875;MEGU;Switzerland;Gstaad;Alpinastrasse 23, Gstaad, 3780, Switzerland;46.4760534;7.2888129;24;true;true;Japanese;This stylish offshoot of the New York flagship restaurant brings a modern and cosmopolitan take on Japanese cuisine, serving up sushi, sashimi and rolls, as well as Wagyu beef and chicken teriyaki. Fittingly, star designer Noé Duchafour-Lawrence drew inspiration from the Far East to create the sophisticated and distinctive interior. There is also a sushi counter, where – as you might expect in an establishment of this calibre – sushi master Tsutomu Kugota works his magic. In summer, the terrace is a delightful spot.;Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
10876;Oliveiras;Switzerland;Lachen;Sagenriet 1, Lachen, 8853, Switzerland;47.1902063;8.8498668;93;true;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;The friendly Oliveira family runs this establishment, making sure guests feel at home in the harmonious and deliberately informal atmosphere. They are attentively looked after as they tuck into Mediterranean cuisine made from excellent produce. All of this is accompanied by a fantastic selection of wines from the owner's Portuguese homeland.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10878;Löwen - Gaststube;Switzerland;Bubikon;Wolfhauserstrasse 2, Bubikon, 8608, Switzerland;47.2684531;8.818702;51;false;true;Farm to table, International;Run by Rita and Domenico Miggiano-Köferli, Gasthof Löwen's second eatery is a delightful and more down-to-earth alternative to the fine dining restaurant. The atmosphere is inviting, not least because of the warm hospitality provided by the waitstaff. The freshly prepared, flavoursome dishes include pan-fried Lötschberg perch fillet with lemon thyme and almond butter, and Zurich veal ragout with glazed vegetables and butter rösti. Vegetarian options available. Popular lunch deal.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
10879;Auberge aux 3 Tilleuls;Switzerland;Genolier;Place du Village 7, Genolier, 1272, Switzerland;46.4352559;6.217496;98;true;false;Contemporary, French;If you're passing through Genolier, be sure to stop off at this charming Auberge! Filipe, the young chef here, serves fresh, tasty cuisine infused with contemporary flair: think fillet of turbot grilled skin on, with pesto and crunchy vegetables. An enjoyable mealtime.;Terrace;[]
10880;Le 1424, La Fabrique Cornu;Switzerland;Champagne;Chemin de Praz 2, Champagne, 1424, Switzerland;46.8277048;6.6611974;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;"La Fabrique" has many strings to its bow: it is a biscuit-maker, an interactive museum and, on the third floor, it houses this chic, contemporary restaurant with a panoramic view of the Vaud Alps. The ambitious and tasty dishes are made with a wide range of regional and national ingredients and given an international spin. Good value for money.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10881;Wirtschaft zur Rosenburg;Switzerland;Stans;Alter Postplatz 3, Stans, 6370, Switzerland;46.9578888;8.3653962;16;true;true;Country cooking;Wherever you look, there's history – the old fortified tower is magnificent! After 33 years, the business has changed hands, but new owners Lukas and Evelyn Christen are committed to keeping the tradition alive. The menu continues to feature both regional and international dishes. Look out for the label "Guets vo hie" on the menu, which indicates the local specialities such as topside beef carpaccio with horseradish, red onions and fried mushrooms. The courtyard terrace is especially pleasant. Tip: This pretty restaurant also makes an ideal venue for weddings and other celebrations.;Terrace;[]
10882;La Maison du Village;Switzerland;Sauges;Rue de la Fontanette 41, Sauges, 2024, Switzerland;46.8871524;6.7634007;55;true;true;Creative;With its resolutely relaxed ambience, this auberge is far from the traditional image of a high temple of gastronomy. Here, Marc Strebel, a young chef from the Valais, conjures up dishes very much inspired by a return to nature. Superb view of the lake from the terrace.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10885;Wirtschaft zum Frieden;Switzerland;Schaffhausen;Herrenacker 13, Schaffhausen, 8200, Switzerland;47.69529;8.63279;67;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This centuries-old inn enjoys a prime location right on Marktplatz, and its charming ambiance, redolent of a bygone era, will have you yearning to return. The dedication of your hosts is also infectious. While maître d' Heidi Bischoff graciously attends to diners in the cosy wood-panelled dining areas, chef-patron Fabrice Bischoff cooks up classic, home-style fare using fresh, high-quality ingredients. Some dishes also incorporate a Mediterranean twist. On the menu you will find beef fillet Stroganoff, as well as Swiss salmon steak with accras. A simpler set menu of the day is also available at lunchtime. The verdant terrace is a delightful spot in the summertime!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10886;Donatz;Switzerland;Samedan;Plazzet 15, Samedan, 7503, Switzerland;46.53506;9.87175;27;true;false;Country cooking;Cornelia and René A Donatz run their business with great dedication. In an elegant rustic-style decor, they serve good fresh cuisine, including classic veal dishes, Angus beef "bestsellers", vegetarian fare and fish such as Graubünden salmon from Lostallo. They stock some 550 wines (20 available by the glass) – a passion of the owner. Donatz Wine Bar proposes a smaller menu. Hotel Donatz has appealingly modern and comfortable guestrooms.;Interesting wine list;[]
10887;t3e terre;Switzerland;Ponte Brolla;via Vecchia Stazione 2, Ponte Brolla, 6652, Switzerland;46.1871126;8.7534313;95;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Owned by the Meneganti family, this beautiful house is home to a restaurant with an attractive dining room and stunning terrace that provide the backdrop for delicious Mediterranean cuisine. A charming hotel with welcoming guestrooms (additional rooms are under construction) adds to the appeal.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10888;Centovalli;Switzerland;Ponte Brolla;Via Alla Stazione 5, Ponte Brolla, 6652, Switzerland;46.1872015;8.7532814;43;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This attractive restaurant boasting rustic yet modern dining rooms and a beautiful terrace shaded by a pergola has offered the same format for over 20 years – a single risotto-based dish (the house speciality) served with a delicious meat option, nearly always lamb fillet, and very few fish dishes. Reasonably priced, with everything of an excellent quality.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10889;Windows;Switzerland;Geneva;Quai du Mont-Blanc 17, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2095877;6.150388;23;false;true;Creative French, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant of Hôtel D'Angleterre commands a panoramic view of Lake Geneva and its emblematic Jet d'Eau, with the mountains and Mont Blanc in the distance. Fresh, seasonal produce takes the limelight in well-crafted French cuisine that mixes classical and traditional influences and which is quite the equal of its splendid setting! Pop into the Leopard Bar for evening cocktails in a buzzy, jazzy vibe, (there is a cigar lounge in the basement). Afternoon tea is very popular.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
10891;Scalottas - Terroir;Switzerland;Lenzerheide;Voa Principala 29, Lenzerheide, 7078, Switzerland;46.7256622;9.5576171;18;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;At this trendy Alpine-style restaurant, the kitchen works exclusively with regional produce, much of it their own. Seasonality and sustainability are a central tenet – the staff will be happy to tell you more about their concept. To order, simply mix and match the dishes on the menu that pique your interest. The wines are also sourced from the region and surrounding areas – astute recommendations come courtesy of the friendly service team.;Car park;[]
10892;Osteria Cyrano Cibo e Vino;Switzerland;Lugano;corso Enrico Pestalozzi 27, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;46.00587;8.954809;71;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Enjoy personalised cuisine full of flavour and prepared with excellent ingredients at this restaurant, which offers a simple menu at lunchtime and a wider choice of dishes in the evening. Delicious recipes and a good balance of meat and fish options.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10893;Stiefels Hopfenkranz;Switzerland;Lucerne;Zürichstrasse 34, Lucerne, 6004, Switzerland;47.058843;8.3095593;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This attractive, personally managed restaurant boasts beautiful pictures on the walls, a relaxed atmosphere, and warm, friendly service from the female owner, who also offers good wine recommendations. In the partly open kitchen, guests can watch the chefs at work. Seasonal produce takes pride of place on the menu.;;[]
10894;Auberge Les Platanes;Switzerland;Chéserex;Rue du Vieux Collège 2, Chéserex, 1275, Switzerland;46.4006032;6.1748177;28;false;false;Classic French;An elegant 17C patrician manor house with smart dining rooms furnished in Regency-style. The fine, classic cuisine is in keeping with its surroundings and changes with the seasons, ensuring that only the freshest ingredients are served.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10895;Vecchia Osteria Seseglio;Switzerland;Chiasso-Seseglio;via Campora 11, Chiasso-Seseglio, 6832, Switzerland;45.82496;8.99888;27;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Traditional local dishes, excellent regional produce, plus a few fish and seafood options, all served in warm dining rooms with low wooden ceilings and exposed brick vaults or outdoors in the garden in summer. Friendly service and a good selection of wines accompany the delicious cuisine.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10896;Villa Honegg;Switzerland;Ennetbürgen;Honegg, Ennetbürgen, 6373, Switzerland;46.9949996;8.4028348;37;true;true;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;Set 914m above the ground, Villa Honegg offers a truly grandiose view from its terrace. Inside, enjoy the classic, regional cuisine with a modern twist, which includes the Honegg meatloaf and a six-course set menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10897;Sauvage;Switzerland;Lucerne;Bahnhofstrasse 30, Lucerne, 6003, Switzerland;47.050344;8.303077;74;true;false;International, Classic Cuisine;This place has been dedicated to hospitality for over 500 years. Not only does the long-standing Hotel Wilden Mann have charming, individually styled guestrooms, it is also a bastion of fine dining. Sascha Behrendt has been the head chef at the upscale and elegant fine dining restaurant since April 2022. He incorporates Japanese elements into his classic cuisine, as well as nods to the region and the season. The four- to six-course set menu is available in both an omnivore and a vegetarian version. There are à la carte options too. In addition, the tempting caviar menu showcases different varieties – quail egg, blini, toast and butter are excellent accompaniments. Tip for motorists: the Kesselturm multi-storey car park is just a short walk away. Alternatively, you can park on the other side of the river, stroll through the beautiful old town and then cross the bridge (Reussbrücke).;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
10898;Chasellas;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Suvretta 22, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.4875534;9.8169369;55;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This charming restaurant in the Suvretta House hotel at the entrance to the skiing and hiking area has found a winning formula, offering rustic specialities for lunch and more sophisticated dishes in the evening, such as herb-crusted rack of lamb, mashed potatoes, chanterelle-asparagus ragout and baby carrots.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10899;Les Touristes;Switzerland;Martigny;Rue de l'Hôpital 2, Martigny, 1920, Switzerland;46.0999272;7.0707804;35;false;false;French Contemporary;This restaurant has been a culinary landmark for decades, thanks to well-crafted cuisine and inspired recipes. Two young local lads are now at the helm. Their culinary creations, which exhibit a particularly minimalist approach and are refreshingly succinct, star carefully selected ingredients, often sourced locally. There are three set menus to choose from, one of which is vegetarian. In addition to outstanding food, there is a strong emphasis on creating an enjoyable dining experience. The buzzy vibe, stylish interior and attentive and friendly service all play their part, including excellent wine tips (the white Metphusus goes down a treat with the poultry breast stuffed in morels). In summer, the terrace is heavenly.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10900;Corso;Switzerland;Sankt Gallen;Brühlgasse 37, Sankt Gallen, 9000, Switzerland;47.4250425;9.3788108;36;false;false;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;This modern, urban restaurant on the edge of the old town is dedicated to the Alpine region, serving good, seasonal produce and game dishes in the autumn. The ambience here is minimalist, with an open kitchen which allows guests to watch chef Franz Ackermann creating his culinary works of art. Simpler lunch menu. The bistro “Unikatessen am Corso” next door also sells regional produce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10901;da Frappa;Switzerland;Richterswil;Dorfstrasse 1, Richterswil, 8805, Switzerland;47.2055784;8.7070702;49;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Childhood friends Fabio Imparato and Alfonso Petti, both from the Italian province of Salerno, have joined forces at this restaurant not far from the lake. The two chefs have adopted a culinary style that draws heavily on their roots, serving up Italian and Mediterranean dishes (eg roasted pulpo on chicory, or braised veal cheek with polenta) in the form of a surprise set menu – at lunchtime a two- or three-course "Business Lunch", and in the evening a four- or five-course tasting menu. The wine list, too, revolves around their homeland. Plus: friendly, proficient service and an appealingly refined, upscale decor. There is a public car park just a stone's throw away.;;[]
10902;De la Cigogne;Switzerland;Geneva;Place Longemalle 17, Geneva, 1204, Switzerland;46.2028091;6.1501133;17;false;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;Trained in some of the world’s leading restaurants, the chef at De la Cigogne creates fine French cuisine which is full of flavour and always beautifully presented. Choose between the “old school” interior decor of mahogany panelling and padded chairs or the pleasant terrace in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10903;Brasserie Les Trois Rois;Switzerland;Basel;Blumenrain 8, Basel, 4001, Switzerland;47.5604072;7.587584;32;false;true;Classic French, International;This attractive brasserie with its classic, elegant design and a fantastic view of the Rhine is located in the left wing of the hotel Les Trois Rois. The French-Swiss cuisine also has international influences: The menu includes a good selection of classic and seasonal dishes, which are presented at your table by the attentive waitstaff. Brunch is served on Sundays. Tip: You can look into the kitchen through a window in the passageway leading to reception.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
10905;L'Artichaut;Switzerland;Carouge;Quai du Cheval-Blanc 9, Carouge, 1227, Switzerland;46.190001;6.1401531;31;false;true;Modern French, Farm to table;Only the street separates this appealing restaurant from the River Arve. You will feel completely at home here, thanks to both the pleasant bistro atmosphere, including decorative paintings and posters of vintage advertisements, and the French cuisine reinterpreted with seasonal influences. Excellent wine list.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10906;La Cantine des Commerçants;Switzerland;Geneva;Boulevard Carl-Vogt 29, Geneva, 1205, Switzerland;46.1998206;6.1328924;86;true;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;A neo-bistro in the old abattoir district of the city, characterised by white and bright green walls, retro decor and a large counter where you can sit and eat. The varied menu is very much in keeping with the times: risotto with prawns and wild herbs, grilled fish and pan-fried fillet of beef.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10907;Le Vallon;Switzerland;Conches;Route de Florissant 182, Conches, 1231, Switzerland;46.1838741;6.1747921;53;false;false;French, Classic Cuisine;With its pink façade and green shutters, this elegant and classically styled inn is an inviting proposition. The tastefully luxurious interior is adorned with bouquets of fresh flowers and floral wallpaper. In his open kitchen, Julien Poulain concocts classic dishes with a sprinkling of extremely subtle modern touches (roasted langoustine, celeriac risotto, bisque emulsion, tarragon, chopped hazelnuts). Friendly, attentive service and a very appealing wine list (a noteworthy selection of red wines, also available in magnums). In fine weather, make the most of the terrace and the verdant garden.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10908;Kakinuma;Switzerland;Geneva;3 rue Henri-Blanvalet, Geneva, 1207, Switzerland;46.202833;6.157784;99;true;false;Japanese;This small restaurant in the lively Eaux-Vives district is definitely worthy of its current success. The couple that run it create fresh and elegant dishes that include the most exquisitely sliced fish, tempuras that are as light as a feather, and silky chawanmushi (an egg flan). A feast for the senses!;Air conditioning;[]
10909;Auberge de la Gare;Switzerland;Grandvaux;Rue de la Gare 1, Grandvaux, 1091, Switzerland;46.4967335;6.7212996;24;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The first thing that impresses guests here is the stunning panoramic view of Lake Geneva. The dishes are simple and fresh – house classics include tartare and fillets of perch from the lake served with fries. Family atmosphere and a lovely terrace. Comfortable guestrooms are available for guests wishing to stay the night.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10910;moment;Switzerland;Berne;Postgasse 49, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.9486666;7.4536355;49;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Set in the historical heart of Bern, this trendy, modern restaurant spread over two floors serves creative cuisine with a focus on regional and seasonal produce. The "Carte Blanche" menu offers a choice of two four- to five course set menus, – one completely plant based. A laid-back front-of-house team takes care of the service. There are entrances on both Postgasse and Gerechtigkeitsgasse.;Terrace;[]
10911;Casa Novo;Switzerland;Berne;Läuferplatz 6, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.949455;7.4577398;41;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Swiss;This place is now under new management, although the name has not changed. Since chef-patron Dirk Wagner took over the restaurant, the cooking has a more international flavour, but has retained a Mediterranean side – for example, beef tongue carpaccio or French guinea fowl in a wild garlic sauce. In addition, tapas are served from 5-7pm, and the "Casa Novo beef tenderloin tartare" is a house classic. At lunchtime, the menu is significantly slimmed down. The location on the River Aare is as idyllic as ever, and the terrace is wonderful! La Vinoteca also remains in operation. The Klösterlistutz car park on the other side of the river is conveniently close.;Terrace;[]
10912;Heugümper;Switzerland;Zurich;Waaggasse 4, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.370238;8.5401296;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This venerable townhouse enjoys a fantastic location in the heart of Zurich – the small terrace is a lovely spot in the summer. With its elegant contemporary decor, the interior is also inviting, and the charming hostess provides attentive service. Prepared using select ingredients, the dishes draw on Mediterranean and Asian influences. Options on the menu range from veal cordon bleu with truffle Brie to tuna with sesame and a ginger and mango sauce. Shorter, simpler menu at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10913;Bistrot du Boeuf Rouge;Switzerland;Geneva;Rue Dr. Alfred-Vincent 17, Geneva, 1201, Switzerland;46.2100947;6.1481679;64;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Lyonnaise;This restaurant is well known in the local area for its simple yet gourmet Lyonnaise specialities: rosette sausage, hot saucisson, pike quenelles, etc. The Farina family's culinary skill is demonstrated on a daily basis, to a backdrop of attractive old-fashioned decor.;;[]
10914;Sternen;Switzerland;Walchwil;Dorfstrasse 1, Walchwil, 6318, Switzerland;47.0997359;8.5130206;25;true;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;In this gorgeous inn, a winning father-and-daughter team conjures up modern takes on classic dishes. They propose a surprise menu – slightly cheaper at lunchtime than in the evening. Incidentally, they smoke the salmon themselves. If you would like a vegetarian menu, please indicate this when making your reservation. Well-stocked wine list. Tip: Across the road, there is a terrace shaded by plane trees, right by Lake Zug and with a view of the Rigi – in fine weather the sunsets are magical!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10915;Porto Pojana Ristorante Terminus;Switzerland;Riva San Vitale;Via Poiana 53, Riva San Vitale, 6826, Switzerland;45.931217;8.958444;33;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A modern, elegant restaurant with an open-view kitchen, a wine cellar built into the rock, a cigar room, a winter garden and – the highlight – a beautiful terrace overlooking the lake with private mooring. The chef creates excellent Mediterranean-inspired cuisine and fish dishes, including recipes that make full use of fish from the lake.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10917;Krone;Switzerland;Regensberg;Oberburg 1, Regensberg, 8158, Switzerland;47.4828278;8.4387993;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant in the hotel of the same name is located in a medieval castle complex on top of the mountain – the view couldn't be more beautiful! The stylish decor is a winning combination of modern design and historical charm. Drawing on contemporary influences, the cuisine takes its cue from the changing seasons and is made with produce sourced from Switzerland and the region. There is a gourmet menu on Fri. and Sat. NB: Due to the location, in a reduced-traffic zone, parking is available a few minutes' walk away – the hotel also provides a shuttle service (to be booked in advance).;Great view,Terrace;[]
10918;Casa Tödi;Switzerland;Trun;Via Principala 78, Trun, 7166, Switzerland;46.7425054;8.9851158;52;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, International;Manuel Reichenbach represents the third generation of his family to run the kitchen here. The cuisine showcases regional and seasonal ingredients of the finest quality. Sustainability is also a core value at this restaurant. Take a punt on the surprise menu, which comprises four to seven courses, or go à la carte. The friendly and adept front-of-house team is managed by the proprietress.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10919;Landgasthof Bären;Switzerland;Madiswil;Kirchgässli 1, Madiswil, 4934, Switzerland;47.1674558;7.7964426;76;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The inviting exterior of this 17C half-timbered house gives a taste of the traditional dining rooms inside, which are lovingly decorated with high-quality furnishings. It is the garden terrace, however, that is the real highlight! In the evening, you can order an ambitious set menu, the appealing vegetarian alternative, or regional classics and modern dishes à la carte. More limited options at lunchtime. Decent wine list. Contemporary-style guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
10920;Eder's Eichmühle;Switzerland;Wädenswil;Eichmühle 2, Wädenswil, 8820, Switzerland;47.2142963;8.6814569;88;false;false;Farm to table, International;A terrific place that is understandably popular! The picturesque location on a hill with a wonderful garden and view of the lake is its calling card – needless to say, the terrace is a big hit in summer! Dining inside the Eder family's traditional inn is also an excellent option, whether in the more cosy dining area or in the airy, modern extension. The service is friendly and professional with a personal touch. As for the sophisticated dishes, choose à la carte or opt for one of three set menus – omnivore, vegetarian or fish and shellfish. Another stand-out feature is the extensive, top-notch wine list. Their lunch menu is also an appealing option.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10921;Tenne;Switzerland;Gluringen Goms;Furkastrasse 320, Gluringen Goms, 3998, Switzerland;46.46251;8.23276;44;false;true;Swiss;Your welcoming hosts run this long-standing family business with great dedication. Done out in a contemporary take on Alpine style, the cosy interior is very pleasing. The menu takes its cue from the seasons and includes some exquisite game dishes – the chef himself is a hunter! In the evening, you can choose between two set menus – one of which is vegetarian – or order à la carte. At lunchtime, the selection is a little smaller, but there is also a set menu. The appealing wine list showcases the best of the Valais region. For overnight stays, there are well-kept, modern guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10922;AURA;Switzerland;Zurich;Bleicherweg 5, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3687208;8.5376022;89;false;true;Meats and Grills, Grills;A stylishly urban restaurant, a top-flight events venue, a lounge or a club? AURA is a little bit of each, but above all the place to be for lovers of modern crossover cuisine with a weakness for grilled food – just watch the chefs at work! Located near Paradeplatz in the old stock exchange building.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10923;Zum Zähringer;Switzerland;Berne;Badgasse 1, Berne, 3011, Switzerland;46.9463339;7.4528702;32;true;true;Classic French;In the Matten neighbourhood, just a block away from the River Aare, this restaurant is run by Gaston Zeiter. He is originally from the Valais canton, but settled here in the lower part of Bern's old town some time ago. In the stately old building that is the Zähringerhaus, he cooks up classic French cuisine, but also dishes with Swiss influences – for example, there is fried sea bass with risotto, as well as a terrific cordon bleu. Top tip: the bargain-price menu of the day! In addition to the charming restaurant, there is a wonderful garden terrace with venerable old trees and a covered outdoor area. The wine list is also well stocked, including with numerous Valais wines.;Terrace;[]
10924;Bodega Noi;Switzerland;Lichtensteig;Loretostrasse 19, Lichtensteig, 9620, Switzerland;47.3257941;9.0855295;77;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Swiss;A really attractive restaurant: sleek, modern, spacious and – thanks to the large glass frontage – pleasingly bright, not to mention the view of the beautiful countryside. The leafy terrace with its shady chestnut tree is also very inviting. On the menu: flavourful cuisine prepared using excellent ingredients and drawing on Mediterranean and regional influences. Lunchtime options are more limited and more moderately priced.;Car park,Terrace;[]
10925;Groven;Switzerland;Lostallo;Via Cantonale 3, Lostallo, 6558, Switzerland;46.3172181;9.1984377;69;false;true;Classic Cuisine;A small restaurant with a focus on simple local dishes. If you stop here for lunch on the terrace, you’ll find a different menu every day inspired by whatever ingredients are in season. There’s also a tempting selection of cheeses and game such as venison and wild boar during the hunting season, plus an interesting wine list.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10926;Chez Meyer's;Switzerland;Wengen;Dorf, Wengen, 3823, Switzerland;46.6045883;7.9229369;67;false;true;Classic French;This elegant little restaurant charms its guests with piano music and a lovely mountain view. The classic fare comes in the form of a surprise menu that is accompanied by a reasonably priced wine list.;Great view,Terrace;[]
10927;L'Accadémia;Switzerland;Lausanne;Place du Port 11, Lausanne, 1006, Switzerland;46.5072486;6.6283994;98;false;true;Italian;This ‘academy’ offers a good lesson in taste and delicious flavours. As such, it is the ideal place to discover top quality Italian cuisine that is fresh and tasty. This is enhanced by an ambience that is relaxed and friendly. In summer, make sure you sit out on the terrace to enjoy the view of the lake.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10928;La Cène;Switzerland;Fribourg;Rue du Criblet 6, Fribourg, 1700, Switzerland;46.8048495;7.1536829;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This establishment draws the eye with its refined decor as much as it appeals with its two mouth-watering set menus: the weekly lunch menu ("Inspiration de la Semaine" – three to five courses) and the evening menu ("Éclosion des Sens" – three to seven courses), which is changed every month. Diners enjoy modern seasonal cuisine with a dash of creative flair, which keeps them coming back for more. A food and wine pairing event is also organised one evening a month.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10929;Le Patio;Switzerland;Geneva;Boulevard Helvétique 19, Geneva, 1207, Switzerland;46.2007905;6.1541696;42;true;false;Creative French, Traditional Cuisine;Philippe Chevrier (chef at the Domaine de Châteauvieux in Satigny) has opted for an original twin-pronged culinary concept here based around beef and lobster, alongside a selection of traditional French bistro dishes, such as pan-fried frogs’ legs with sweet garlic, and crispy snails with mushrooms. A highly enjoyable dining experience!;;[]
10930;Kronenstübli;Switzerland;Pontresina;Via Maistra 130, Pontresina, 7504, Switzerland;46.4934789;9.9019021;18;false;true;Classic French;Premium materials, tasteful fabrics and attractive pinewood panelling make for a cosy yet elegant atmosphere – just the right backdrop for the sophisticated cuisine served here, which is classic French with Italian influences. Tip: Try the canard à la presse – pressed duck – (available if ordered by at least two of your party). The restaurant is housed in the traditional and stylishly luxurious Grand Hotel Kronenhof.;Interesting wine list;[]
10931;Haus zum Rüden;Switzerland;Zurich;Limmatquai 42, Zurich, 8001, Switzerland;47.3706709;8.5430709;21;true;false;International, Modern Cuisine;This beautiful guild house on the Münsterbrücke bridge, only a stone’s throw from the town hall, dates back to 1348, as does the unique 11m-wide wooden barrel-vaulted ceiling in the Gothic Room. Dishes are based on seasonal ingredients and include classics such as Zurich-style veal and mushroom ragout in a cream sauce. Less expensive menu at lunchtime, plus a selection of dishes available in the modern bar with a terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10932;Salmen;Switzerland;Olten;Ringstrasse 39, Olten, 4600, Switzerland;47.3508005;7.8992712;16;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A delightful place with a lively atmosphere! This elegant 19C townhouse opposite the Church of St Martin houses a charming brasserie with decorative details such as old photos, a striking chandelier and attractive parquet flooring. There is also a heritage-protected dining room with stuccoed ceilings. Chef-patron Daniel Bitterli cooks classic, traditional dishes that take their cue from the seasons and draw on Mediterranean influences. Dishes such as the sole fillets with two kinds of asparagus and hollandaise sauce exemplify the restaurant's commitment to fresh, high-quality ingredients and flavoursome cuisine. The waitstaff are very attentive, friendly and adept.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
10933;Relais du Mont d'Orge;Switzerland;Sion;Route du Sanetsch 99, Sion, 1950, Switzerland;46.2348004;7.3401463;27;true;true;Classic French;Originally from Auvergne, chef Bernard Ricou was a pupil of Paul Bocuse. He extends a warm welcome at this charming, friendly place with a timeless atmosphere and a terrace commanding one of the best views of Sion. Three different classic and seasonal set menus are served. Lobster playing an important role year round and is almost always to be found on the menu.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10934;Taverne zur Krone;Switzerland;Dietikon;Kronenplatz 1, Dietikon, 8953, Switzerland;47.4056588;8.4006619;63;true;false;International;This stately, beautifully restored historical building proposes two dining options: an elegant wood-panelled restaurant as well as a modern-style brasserie. In summer the terrace is particularly delightful. You'll find a great selection of traditional and classic dishes on the menu.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10935;Adler;Switzerland;Fläsch;Krüzgass 2, Fläsch, 7306, Switzerland;47.0265842;9.5133168;98;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern French;A little off the beaten track, this inn is delightfully cosy with its wood-panelled interior. The chef, who hails from South Tyrol, serves up classic cuisine with a modern twist, making a point of working with regional produce. The attentive front-of-house team includes his partner, a trained sommelier – the wine cellar boasts over 600 labels. There are a few attractive guestrooms available for overnight stays.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10936;Namun;Switzerland;Bad Ragaz;Bernhard-Simon-Strasse 2, Bad Ragaz, 7310, Switzerland;47.0007975;9.503637;59;true;true;Thai-Chinese;For fans of Thai food, this restaurant in the luxurious Grand Resort Bad Ragaz is the place to be! The focus is on Thai cuisine, but there are also Chinese dishes. Elegant and minimalist, the Far Eastern-style decor makes for the perfect setting. Tip: Ask about the Thai curry – even if it's not on the menu. In case you were wondering, the name Namuntranslates as "lukewarm water" and is a reference to the local thermal spring.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10937;Seven Lugano - the restaurant;Switzerland;Lugano;via Stauffacher 1, Lugano, 6900, Switzerland;46.0040015;8.9550424;66;false;true;Grills;Situated on the rooftop of the casino and accessible via a glass-sided lift, this restaurant boasts fine views of the lake. In summer, the popular seats on the terrace need to be booked well in advance, while the lounge bar on the ground floor is perfect for a post-dinner cocktail. The cuisine here is varied and wide-ranging, both on the set menus and the à la carte, plus there’s an excellent choice of wines featuring labels from around the world.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10938;La Parenthèse;Switzerland;La Chaux-de-Fonds;Rue de l'Hôtel-de-Ville 114, La Chaux-de-Fonds, 2300, Switzerland;47.0944673;6.8420895;23;false;true;Regional Cuisine;On the road into town, enjoy a gourmet interlude in this spruce, yet unpretentious restaurant depicted by a cosy, contemporary interior and a warm welcome. The culinary score is the work of chef Gennaro Rotella, hence the Italian twang of dishes such as cappellacci stuffed with greater amberjack (fish), confit of yellow tomatoes and smoked provola. Delicately crafted, the chef’s cuisine stars regional produce like raw and cooked Seeland vegetables and beef from the Franches Montagnes district. Head to the cellar to choose your cheese, which you can wash down with a 10- or 20-year-old Tawny port. A most charming front-of-house team.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10939;Tout un Monde;Switzerland;Grandvaux;Place du Village 7, Grandvaux, 1091, Switzerland;46.4932537;6.7166651;35;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the village, this restaurant occupies an old 13C church that enjoys a stunning location overlooking the lake and the vineyards. Regional produce such as locally sourced meat and fish from the lake are transformed into elegant dishes, which are accompanied by equally impressive wines from the region.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10940;Du Théâtre;Switzerland;Monthey;Avenue du Théâtre 7, Monthey, 1870, Switzerland;46.25412;6.94882;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This bistro, depicted by a stripped-back minimalist decor is conveniently located for a meal before or after a show at the Crochetan theatre. The chef conjures up creative, well-crafted dishes made from top-notch produce with regular nods to his native Italy. Dishes include specialities such as a ‘gargouillou’ of asparagus, fresh morels and spring veggies. The talented sommelier is a font of wine knowledge and fully worthy of our applause!;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
10941;La Muña;Switzerland;Zurich;Utoquai 45, Zurich, 8008, Switzerland;47.3628045;8.5472952;33;false;true;Peruvian, Japanese Contemporary;Do you fancy Peruvian-Japanese cuisine? This restaurant on the sixth floor of hotel La Réserve Eden au Lac, on the shores of Lake Zurich, serves interesting and unfussy dishes made from top-notch ingredients. Up here you can dine in a cosy atmosphere beneath the exposed roof beams or out on the fantastic rooftop terrace – the view over the lake and the old town is magnificent! Exclusive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
10942;Weisses Rössli;Switzerland;Zurich;Bederstrasse 96, Zurich, 8002, Switzerland;47.3619305;8.5262798;87;true;false;Classic French, Mediterranean Cuisine;At the Weisses Rössli, good-quality ingredients are used to create dishes inspired by French cuisine with Mediterranean and seasonal influences, including options such as monkfish with gnocchi, beetroot, radicchio and cassis. In the rear courtyard away from the street, there is a quiet terrace that can be covered by an awning. We recommend parking in the nearby car park on the Hürlimann site.;Terrace;[]
10943;KCC by Mauro Colagreco;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Maistra 41, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.5002815;9.843345;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;KCC stands for Kulm Country Club. The handsome L-shaped building is located right next to the ice rink and has a garden for summer days. Local produce takes centre stage in the dishes, which often draw on Mediterranean influences. As well as an appealing selection of starters and pasta dishes, the menu includes dishes for two, such as beef cutlets and lamb shoulder. Much of the food is flame-grilled or roasted over embers. The atmosphere is relaxed and the decor tasteful – the vintage sledges adorning the ceiling are bound to draw the eye! There is also a fabulous terrace. Live music and vinyl sessions provide the acoustic backdrop.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10944;Balm - La Pistache;Switzerland;Meggen;Balmstrasse 3, Meggen, 6045, Switzerland;47.0445153;8.3679902;43;true;true;Classic French;The elegant restaurant of Hotel Balm has a classical feel when it comes to both the service and Beat Stofer's cuisine – this is unpretentious fare made with excellent ingredients. Diners can opt for a tasting menu with four to five courses or order à la carte. There is also a well-curated wine list. In good weather, the terrace is a fabulous spot from which to enjoy the mountain views. This place is always busy, so be sure to book well in advance! Cheerful guestrooms are available for overnight stays.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10945;CAAA by Pietro Catalano;Switzerland;Lucerne;Haldenstrasse 19, Lucerne, 6006, Switzerland;47.0549879;8.3145202;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The location right next to an art gallery (from which you also have direct access to the restaurant) could not be more fitting, as the theme of creativity is omnipresent here in the restaurant, too. The chic, modern interior is all curved lines, with the relief of the original ceiling as its centrepiece! Pale tones and the sleek design of the tables and chairs lend a Nordic feel. All of the activity in the open kitchen can be followed by diners – in the evening, a tasting menu comprising three, five or seven courses is created here. Served at lunchtime, the three-course "Chef's Mood Menu" changes on a weekly basis. The proprietor, who happens to be the chef's sister, manages the service in concert with the chefs, and ensures a pleasant atmosphere. She is happy to provide information about the regional ingredients and the restaurant's nature-based philosophy. The cocktails and mocktails served at the bar are an integral part of the culinary experience here.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10946;Le Soleil de Dugny;Switzerland;Leytron;Route d'Ovronnaz 556, Leytron, 1912, Switzerland;46.1885054;7.1799481;37;true;false;Classic French;In this restaurant standing at an altitude of 1 000m, the friendly and dedicated family at the helm offers guests a seasonal menu that can also be ordered as a half-portion, on which numerous local products are used to create tasty classic dishes such as the speciality “local veal with Valais gnocchi”. Spectacular views of the valley and mountains, plus a stunning terrace in summer!;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10947;National da Sergio;Switzerland;Olten;Klosterplatz 17, Olten, 4600, Switzerland;47.3503541;7.9037968;84;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;A pleasant and down-to-earth restaurant in the historic old town, right next to Klosterplatz square. The former “Felsenburg” team offers classic Italian cuisine made from top-quality ingredients, including dishes such as Spaghetti Scampi and the classic Piccata Milanese. As you’d expect, Italian wines feature on the wine list.;Terrace;[]
10948;Nouvo Bourg;Switzerland;Saillon;Rue du Bourg 25, Saillon, 1913, Switzerland;46.1720755;7.1853931;50;false;false;French Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the historical village of Saillon, this laid-back little restaurant oozes modern bistro charm. It also boasts a very pleasant terrace. They serve three ambitious set menus (including a vegetarian one) based on the French classics and accented with modern and creative details. At lunchtime they also serve a short "business menu".;Car park,Terrace;[]
10949;Lusi Brasserie;Switzerland;Zermatt;Bahnhofstrasse 55, Zermatt, 3920, Switzerland;46.0199257;7.7465518;18;false;true;French, International;A tip before we get started: In fine weather, be sure to nab a table on the terrace in front of the building, from which you can take in stunning views of the Matterhorn! But the brasserie of the long-established Grand Hotel Zermatterhof also provides a delightful, classically elegant setting with its lovely walnut panelling and partially glass-paned vaulted ceiling. The cuisine is French and draws on international influences. The menu includes "Lusi Classics" such as calf's head, and traditional dishes such as Wiener schnitzel, steak tartare, burgers and flammkuchen – and there is always an evening special.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
10950;Langosteria;Switzerland;Saint Moritz;Via Salastrains 10, Saint Moritz, 7500, Switzerland;46.5017315;9.8334101;88;true;true;Italian Contemporary;This is the new place to see and be seen on the ski slopes overlooking St Moritz. The terrace affords magnificent views, making it a delightful spot in which to savour freshly prepared Italian cuisine. Langoustine, lobster and fish, truffle pizza and pasta are the specialities of this restaurant, which also has locations in Milan, Paris and Paraggi. If you're not skiing, the best way to get here is by taxi.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
10952;Les deux;Japan;Tokyo;2-7-2 Kamimeguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0051, Japan;35.642776;139.699494;15;false;true;French;The chef mixes his own sensibilities into cuisine rooted in French bistro fare. The blackboard menu is a medley of authentic dishes and à la carte items made with seasonal ingredients. Generally, an appetiser and a main course is the perfect amount, but some items can be ordered as half portions, so ask your server.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10953;KIBUN;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 4-11-28 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.659416;139.722558;70;false;true;Contemporary;The chef came from France to study Japanese cuisine, and the tale of his journey is told in his prix fixe menus, which interweave French and Japanese culinary traditions. Japanese knife techniques shine in preparing squid and pike conger, finely sliced to cut up the bones, with sauces that raise the ingredients’ taste to a higher level. Fruit and herb flavours interlace to form a cuisine that knows no borders. The ‘ki’ in the name of the restaurant is the same as the Chinese ‘qi’. The essential taste of each ingredient, expressed with consummate sensitivity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10954;Shirokane Shin;Japan;Tokyo;3-2-3 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.646732;139.731203;79;false;false;Japanese;The chef queues up the first few items with a narrative arc in mind. Guests then order whatever they like from the menu, creating a programme of their own. That is to say, the chef decides the start of the meal, then guests freely request portions and flavours according to their whims on that day. With omakase seemingly everywhere these days, this show of mutual respect testifies to the thoughtfulness of the chef.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10956;SUKIYAKI ASAI;Japan;Tokyo;3-11-15 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.665312;139.74701;60;false;true;Sukiyaki;Experience sukiyaki hospitality at a counter. Standing right across from you, the server expertly prepares alternating slices of beef and vegetables. Sourced from a distinguished butcher in Shiga Prefecture, the choice beef is served in a variety of thicknesses. On the side are the signature dipping sauces: meringue-like beaten egg and rich egg yolk mixed with Tosa vinegar. The meal culminates with a final dish of shirataki noodles, stir-fried in warishita sauce and beef fat. Each dish will enchant both your eyes and taste buds.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10957;l'Odorante par Minoru Nakijin;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 7-7-19 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669736;139.76222;41;true;true;French;The chef sharpened his gastronomical senses in Grasse, a city in the south of France known as the ‘capital of perfumes’. Recalling his apprentice days, the chef named his restaurant ‘l’Odorante’, meaning ‘the pungent’ or ‘the aromatic’. Refined fragrance is the name of the culinary game here. Matching classic French techniques with Japanese ingredients, he fuses the two into a Franco-Japanese esprit, ensuring each dish is unique and brimming with flavour. He revels in explaining the background to his cuisine, leaving the memories of the culinary journey in all five senses.;Air conditioning;[]
10959;LE PRISTINE TOKYO;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Toranomon Hills Station Tower, 2-6-4 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.667515;139.746319;71;true;false;Contemporary, Italian Contemporary;This is the Tokyo outpost of Le Pristine of Belgium. Directing the kitchen is Sergio Herman, a standard-bearer in the world of Dutch cuisine. The restaurant introduces ‘New Italian’, which combines pure Italian flavours and the culinary traditions of Herman’s native region of Zeeland, in the Netherlands. The orecchiette is a true Le Pristine classic bearing Sergio Herman’s signature and is now available in Tokyo. The art and background music combine to help create a modern dining experience.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10960;Keichitsu;Japan;Tokyo;2-13-12 Shoto, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0046, Japan;35.659191;139.691891;44;true;true;French, French Contemporary;‘Keichitsu’ is the traditional name for the ‘solar term’ micro-season in early March when insects emerge from winter hiding – an evocation of spring, when animals awake from hibernation. The chef applies his passion to the green shoots of the natural world to conjure a cuisine bursting with imagination. Focusing on a few main ingredients, he prepares these in a variety of ways and serves them on a single plate. Vegetables, for example, may be roasted, pureed or served as a sauce, deepening their flavour. Fragrances such as yuzu citrus and Japanese pepper complement the seasons.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10961;bonélan;Japan;Tokyo;4F, GYRE, 5-10-1 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.667538;139.70695;20;false;true;French;Tucked adjacent to its sister restaurant l’élan, Bonélan offers a relaxed dining experience, where the theme is ‘classic cuisine, casual style’. Prix fixe offerings centre on modern preparations such as vegetable terrine, seafood poêle and duck confit. Offcuts are used to make consommé, sending a message about food loss. The allure of traditional cuisine, passed through a modern filter.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
10962;Quatre Vingt Douze;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-9-5 Funabashi, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 156-0055, Japan;35.647493;139.622802;23;true;false;French, French Contemporary;French cuisine overlays ingredients of varying flavours and textures to express a medley of tastes. That defining characteristic, says the chef, is the wellspring of his creative drive and the key to his approach in assembling his menu. Fruits, herbs and spices are all deployed to good effect and with a light touch to create his flavours. Fish and meat dishes always come with sauces, paying homage to the classics. The proprietress is in charge of the desserts. An intimate eatery from a couple who support each other like a synchronized team.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10963;DepTH brianza;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Azabudai Hills Residence A, 1-2-3 Azabudai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0041, Japan;35.662017;139.74026;17;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;DepTH brianza explores concepts that broaden the possibilities of Italian cuisine. Chef Okuno’s latest culinary adventure is a taste test that takes Italian cuisine a little outside its comfort zone. While firmly grounded in tradition, Okuno enjoys reframing Japanese ingredients in creative ways. ‘DepTH’ is a play on his name: ‘okuyuki’ is ‘depth’ in Japanese. Like a wizard reworking ancient spells, Okuno dreams up imaginative cuisine you won’t find anywhere else.;Air conditioning;[]
10964;Sushiya Hajime;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 4-3 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.701694;139.740107;26;true;true;Sushi;The character for ‘sushi’ in Sushiya Hajime refers specifically to fermented sushi, harking back to the beginnings of sushi culture. ‘Hajime’ means ‘beginning’, expressing the chef’s desire to see the sushi world with a newcomer’s eyes, as when he used to be sent to select fish at the market. Fish is prepared according to ancient practices such as salting and simmering. Omakase set meals consist of numerous pieces of sushi formed small, affording rich variety and commitment to quality is uncompromising, which is deeply satisfying. Finely honed skills shine in attentive service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10965;YAKITORI Moe es;Japan;Tokyo;7-13-10 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.663713;139.730292;93;true;false;Yakitori;The chef’s pedigree in both yakitori and French cuisine shines in this restaurant’s omakase set meal. The magic begins with appetisers such as smoked chicken or terrine de foie gras. The chicken soup is like a clear consommé. The restaurant sources whole chickens of a variety that requires a long breeding period, and rests the meat for several days to concentrate the flavour. To bring out the flavour of the meat, salt is used liberally, sauce sparingly. Simple chicken soba noodles end the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10966;Gendaisaryo Ginza Fugetsudo;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 6-6-1 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671166;139.762704;74;false;true;French;A former teahouse is now a French restaurant. Displaying their respective talents, chef and sommelier pair cuisine with wine or cocktails. Prix fixe menus are based on the 52 weeks of the year, with ingredients changing weekly, and a motif of ‘seasons.’ Fare is classic yet modern, with a focus on sauces. A full selection of Japanese and Western desserts round out this iconic Ginza confectionary.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10967;AMOUR;Japan;Tokyo;1-6-13 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.648728;139.714137;77;false;false;French;The restaurant’s name declares respect for people, ingredients and tools alike. A sealed letter brought to your table contains a message from Chef Yusuke Goto, thanking you for visiting, explaining his approach to cuisine, and detailing the menu du jour. ‘Japanese French’ cuisine, specialising in domestic ingredients, is delicate and light and cuisine that reflects the seasons is a delight.;Air conditioning;[]
10968;Tokyo Chinese Ichirin;Japan;Tokyo;1-5-8 Tsukiji, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0045, Japan;35.669873;139.771525;53;false;true;Chinese;Sichuan cuisine that strives for a mellow spiciness. The evening prix fixe offering, which combines steamed spicy chicken with liver paté, is highly original. We recommend adding some of the distinctive à la carte items, such as shrimp chili sauce made with whole large shrimp, or fried egg and crab as airy as a soufflé. Weekday lunches are a set menu of twice-cooked pork and dandan noodles. A popular place, so queues form at times.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10969;La Rochelle Minami Aoyama;Japan;Tokyo;3-14-23 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.665171;139.714349;83;true;true;French;The restaurant of Hiroyuki Sakai, the famed ‘Iron Chef’ of French cuisine. On the show, resplendent in red chef’s uniform and with a pear in one hand, Sakai brought excitement to living rooms. At one time Sakai dazzled the port town of Rochelle with his ‘French cuisine à la kaiseki’. Japanese elements such as water shield and pike conger are served on artisanal plates and garnished with seasonal leaves. Bread made with rice flour is the perfect complement to sake.;Air conditioning;[]
10970;Ne Quittez pas;Japan;Tokyo;3-15-19 Higashigotanda, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 141-0022, Japan;35.626015;139.729612;94;true;true;French;Toshio Tanabe was an Olympic gymnast candidate and a professional boxer before he became a chef, steering his ambitions for the wider world towards French cuisine. His billboard reads, ‘French cuisine with seasonal seafood and vegetables’. The secret stories behind the restaurant’s name, the fish soup and the grilled clams lay bare Tanabe’s mode of living. The ‘soil course’ and the watermelon prix fixe offerings are ideas from a unique imagination. Enjoy the flavours and share in the secrets.;Air conditioning;[]
10971;Miyake Akira;Japan;Tokyo;3-8-12 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.663262;139.734469;99;false;true;Japanese;The Gifu Prefecture–born owner-chef uses his restaurant to showcase the crafts and foodstuffs of his native region. Born to a family that runs a pottery studio in Tajimi, he serves his dishes on Mino-ware vessels he made himself. Eels are beloved by the locals as they are thought to provide the stamina to overcome the famously sweltering heat of Tajimi. A bowl of fragrant grilled unagi on a bed of rice makes a fine end to the meal. A menu replete with delicacies, such as small bowls of caviar and other seafood on rice, crab served in small pots and char-grilled wagyu beef, lifts the spirits.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10973;Canton Meisai Akasaka Rikyu;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Akasaka Biz Tower, 5-3-1 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-6302, Japan;35.673036;139.73606;95;false;true;Chinese;This Chinese restaurant has been preaching the gospel of Cantonese cuisine for years. The richly-varied bill of fare centres around seafood, grilled items and dim sum, with whole-steamed grouper being worthy of note. Don’t pass up the steamed gyoza dumplings and siu mai dumplings. Salt stir-fry of seafood and veggies, dried abalone and stewed sea cucumber are all excellent choices as well. The goal here is to serve orthodox Cantonese cuisine. Cooking that can stand with the best Hong Kong can offer testifies to the passion of chef Hikoaki Tan.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
10974;KOTARO Hasegawa DOWNTOWN CUISINE;Japan;Tokyo;4-2-11 Taito, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 110-0016, Japan;35.705731;139.781121;50;false;true;French;DOWNTOWN CUISINE is located in the chef’s local Satake Shopping Street. The chef arrays each table with Japanese vessels that recall memories of the working-class neighbourhood. The inspiration for the restaurant came from a world cooking contest, in which the chef competed with a concept designed to showcase the culture of Japan. Each plate is imbued with the passion to aim ever higher and the desire to thank and give back to the chef’s hometown.;Air conditioning;[]
10975;Hei Fung Terrace;Japan;Tokyo;2F, The Peninsula Tokyo, 1-8-1 Yurakucho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0006, Japan;35.67458;139.76074;82;true;false;Chinese;The exotic atmosphere is suggestive of a Chinese garden. Being part of a Hong Kong group, the focus is on Cantonese cuisine. The dim sum master creates xiaolongbao and gyoza, while the grill master serves up chicken and pork baked in iron pots. From the cornucopia of ingredients, guests can decide the seasoning and cooking style, including stewed items in oyster sauce and stir-fried items with XO or black bean sauce. Ask to sit overlooking the outer garden of the Imperial Palace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
10976;JULIA;Japan;Tokyo;3-1-25 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.669816;139.714034;70;false;true;Contemporary;The wife is the chef, the husband the sommelier in this couple-run restaurant. The omakase set menu consists of pairings only. An evangelist to the world for Japan as a terroire, JULIA specialises in Japanese foodstuffs and Japanese wines. Most ingredients come from Ibaraki Prefecture, where the husband was born and the restaurant originated. Uniquely, the couple favours pairings of vegetables and fish with fruit. Self-taught and freewheeling, the cuisine is colourful and light.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10977;Sushi Satoru;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-17-16 Ebisuminami, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0022, Japan;35.644668;139.710292;68;false;false;Sushi;Retired pro boxer Satoru Araki is testing his mettle in a new arena. The backbone he developed from keeping his weight under the cut-off helped him overcome the struggles he faced moving from boxing ring to sushi counter. He excels in firing up the crowd. Straight from the bell, he offers eggplant sushi with a jaunty ‘oide nasu!’, a pun on the words ‘welcome’ and ‘eggplant’. Focusing on tuna, he forms the vinegared rice reverently in his fist. You’ll be knocked out by his charm and passion.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10978;L’éclaireur;Japan;Tokyo;6-6 Daikanyamacho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0034, Japan;35.651853;139.705717;70;false;false;French;Ichiei Taguma was taught that a great chef is one who creates a new culinary culture. He tinkered and tested throughout his apprenticeship, honing his creativity, an experience that led him to where he is today. When he became independent, Taguma decided to focus on wood-fired cooking. Smoking by skilful tending of flame is the key to his presentation of creative French cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
10979;HYÈNE;Japan;Tokyo;5-13-14 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.666257;139.706907;21;true;false;Contemporary;Expect creative fare fusing Japanese, Korean and French culinary culture. A perfect reflection of Chef Yoko Kimoto’s life, as she carries both Japanese and Korean DNA and is schooled in French cuisine. Her speciality, potato fondant au chocolat, overlays a French dessert onto a Korean rice-cake snack her mother used to make her when she was little. Imbuing Japanese ingredients with Korean flavours using French techniques, Kimoto conjures a gastronomy that is all her own.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10980;Bouquet de France;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 7-10-3 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.664655;139.729082;71;false;true;French;“The countryside is the foundation of French cuisine”, says Hidetoshi Imoto. He pours his labours into the flavours of rural France, such as cassoulet, a stew from Languedoc, and baeckeoffe, an Alsatian casserole. The charcuterie of pork pâtés and sausages is indispensable in expressing its home culture. Proprietress Yoko Harada’s amiable service relaxes guests with a cheerful, homelike atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
10981;Yakitori Honda;Japan;Tokyo;3-5-1 Minato, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0043, Japan;35.669847;139.778187;86;true;true;Yakitori;The boundless curiosity of Chef Takuya Honda shines in his yakitori. The Hinai chicken he uses is aged to bring out the umami. Honda constantly tinkers with his fare through trial and error to elicit the best flavour from each cut. Unimpressed by the usual, narrow choice of salt or sauce, he broadens the selection to include condiments like condensed soy sauce, balsamic soy sauce, and rice vinegar with herbs. The chef similarly puts effort into recommending the best wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10982;HASUO;Japan;Tokyo;5-10-3 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.649529;139.720946;64;true;true;Korean;The fare here is New Korean: traditional Korean cooking with a modern interpretation. The chef applies the techniques and sensibilities he learned studying Western cooking. Banchan with 16 side dishes is a revelation. The Imperial Crepe adhering to the five flavours and five colours, is a brightly coloured treat. Ganjang-gejang, sauce-marinated blue crab, is marinated lightly to suit modern tastes. Hasuo proclaims a new Korean cuisine, raising the food of the chef’s Korean homeland to a new level.;Air conditioning;[]
10984;IBAIA;Japan;Tokyo;3-12-5 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670829;139.769195;57;false;true;French;This bistro is sure to satisfy the cravings of carnivores, with French flame techniques that bring out the sizzle in meat dishes. Beef, pork, lamb and duck are cooked as hearty slabs. Their famous cutlet of beef tenderloin looks like a standard Japanese take on Western cuisine, but with a French twist: parsley and garlic are mixed in, a la lamb grilled in breadcrumbs. Here, you’ll find the thrill of savouring thick cuts of meat and the joy of opening a bottle of wine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10985;Kappo Ryu;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 4-26-12 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.662071;139.718199;96;true;true;Japanese;Aiming to conjure dishes that leave an impression, the chef creates through a process of addition, umami upon umami, flavour upon flavour. Tsukuri is combined with grated onion and Tosa vinegar jelly. Boiled-down sake used in grilled items is mixed with dried sardine dashi to bring out its grain flavour. The menu eschews soups and appetiser platters in favour of wagyu beef dishes. Beef tongue in dashi vinegar and cutlets wrapped in bread are the chef’s pride and joy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10987;DA PEPI;Japan;Tokyo;4-25-6 Sengoku, Bunkyo-ku, Tokyo, 112-0011, Japan;35.730294;139.73945;54;true;false;Italian;The ivy-draped façade arrests the eye. On the menu, one item after another professes the chef’s admiration for the cuisine of Tuscany. ‘Fumo’ is a dish of pasta in tomato sauce, learnt by the chef on his Tuscan sojourn. Aromas of olive oil and garlic wafting from the kitchen, tables set to encourage sharing from a single dish: it all recalls everyday life in Italy. Set menus are always an improvised surprise. DA PEPI is fun, like an invitation to dinner at a friend’s home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10989;Yuan Yamori;Japan;Tokyo;3-9-7 Tsukishima, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0052, Japan;35.663125;139.781472;15;false;true;Soba;Omakase set meals showcase the appeal of soba in all its glory. An assortment of stone mortars used to make different types of soba flour attest to the chef’s attention to detail. Buckwheat dumplings are kneaded from freshly ground flour. To keep an eye on the flour and ensure that no heat is added, buckwheat is slowly and carefully ground. Soba topped with nori seaweed is rich with the aroma of broth and nori, while mori soba is placed in the hands rather than on the table so you don’t miss any of the pure fragrance of buckwheat. Through the aroma and act of slurping rediscover the essence of soba noodles.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Shoes must be removed;[]
10991;Tamawarai;Japan;Tokyo;5-23-3 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.664462;139.70467;79;true;false;Soba;The chef is of the view that soba’s deliciousness is determined by its flour. He grinds husked buckwheat both from his garden and from farmers in Ibaraki Prefecture, catching every iota of the fresh-ground aroma. Coarse ground seiro (soba served on bamboo wicker) is full of wild flavour. Tofu soba, inspired by staff meals, and hot seiro with hot tsuyu sauce and beaten egg, are unique taste experiences. Evening service is prix fixe only, with treats such as buckwheat mash and rolled omelettes included.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
10992;Sense;Japan;Tokyo;37F, Mandarin Oriental Tokyo, 2-1-1 Nihombashimuromachi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-8328, Japan;35.68683;139.77299;23;true;true;Chinese;The chef is thoroughly versed in Cantonese cuisine and his credo is to faithfully reproduce traditional cuisine. Specialities include deep-fried whole pigeon, double-boiled premium soup with dried mushrooms and quickly-steamed star grouper. We also recommend the dim sum. Enjoy orthodox Cantonese cuisine while taking in some of the best scenery in Tokyo – there’s nothing quite like a dinner in subdued lighting against a night cityscape.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
10994;Shizuru;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 1-3-12 Tomigaya, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0063, Japan;35.669363;139.68909;59;false;true;Japanese;A kappo with service by a couple in chef’s whites. Having both studied Kyoto cuisine, this husband-and-wife divide cooking duties between them. The husband prefers subtler seasoning, always to be accompanied by local sake from Yamagata. The rice, Koshihikari from Uonuma, is delivered from the proprietress’ hometown, cooked in a broad-rimmed cooking pot and patiently transferred to a wooden container. The aroma of incense wreathes the shop in a gentle, quietly soothing Japanese ambience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10995;LE BOURGUIGNON;Japan;Tokyo;3-3-1 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.658299;139.727402;47;false;true;French;Evoking Burgundy, the name of the restaurant comes from the owner-chef being inspired by the passion of the restauranteur and wine producer where he trained, an influence also evident in the rich selection of wines from Burgundy. His specialities include boudin noir with apple salad and purée, and millefeuille-style horse crab, eggplant and avocado. He also does wild game and offal well.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10996;ARMANI / RISTORANTE;Japan;Tokyo;10F, 5-5-4 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671589;139.763989;59;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;Creative cuisine, a fusion of Japanese and Italian food cultures, graces the tables of this contemporary interior. Pasta in the shape of rice and risotto using domestically grown saffron attest to a culinary sense bursting with imagination. Carbonara and tiramisu prepared with updated techniques offer fascinating glimpses of a modern cuisine evolved from time-honoured tradition. The refinement for which the Armani brand is famed provides a fitting venue.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
10997;Tsunokamizaka Koshiba;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 15 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.691072;139.724738;24;true;false;Japanese;The owner-chef learned his trade from a master of the Kansai school, and that experience shines in his dashi stock enriched with kombu kelp and his amuse-bouche of rod-shaped pressed sushi of chub mackerel. Appetisers are indispensable to the menu out of respect for time-honoured craftsmanship, but also to delight guests with a cornucopia of drinking snacks. A wide variety of grilled items and rice dishes offers plenty of choice. Diner satisfaction is the top priority here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10998;Tokihami;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-11-6 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670853;139.768819;98;false;false;Izakaya;A kappo izakaya bursting with creativity. The extensive menu captures your attention with its blend of Japanese and Western styles. Sansho pepper simmered in oil becomes ajillo à la Japonaise with seafood and unripe pepper. Popular items are lavished with delicacies: monaka wafers stuffed with foie gras, for example, or truffle omelette. Tsufuhan (‘Gout Rice’) is an ensemble of salmon roe, salted and dried grey mullet roe, sea urchin and caviar. Opulence that piques one’s curiosity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
10999;nerisa;Japan;Tokyo;6-7-6 Koyama, Shinagawa-ku, Tokyo, 142-0062, Japan;35.614612;139.699997;56;true;false;Italian;Tonnato of veal, hand-rolled tajarin pasta, agnolotti: Chef's experience with the cuisine of Piedmont is everywhere on display. He stays faithful to the recipes he learned, because he wants guests to know the taste of true Piemontese cuisine, but he links Italy to Japan by incorporating local ingredients. The accent in cooking is on simplicity and his personality shines in his line-up of ingredient-focused fare.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11000;Takumi;Japan;Tokyo;1-11-10 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.660377;139.724214;35;false;true;French;Each dish arrives with a card explaining it. The Chef was inspired to adopt this approach by the way art galleries convey the concepts behind their artworks. Exploring unusual combinations of ingredients, he uses spices and herbs to assemble layers of flavour and fragrance. From temperature to texture, everything is calculated to create a cuisine that is by turns simple and complex. All five senses are satisfied, leaving a lasting impression.;Air conditioning;[]
11001;Le Coq;Japan;Tokyo;2-7-2 Ebisunishi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0021, Japan;35.650355;139.707281;89;false;false;French;Simple cuisine that emphasises ingredients leaves a lasting impression of flavours and arrangements. Thick-cut smoked salmon is one example. A veteran chef, Mitsuhiro Hiruma focuses his skills on delicious preparations with nothing extraneous. The restaurant’s name is French for ‘rooster’, the symbol and national bird of France. Having honed his technique in local restaurants, Hiruma expresses this precious experience in his cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
11002;Asagaya BIRD LAND;Japan;Tokyo;3-37-9 Asagayaminami, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 166-0004, Japan;35.704383;139.6347;37;false;false;Yakitori;Piped jazz fills the air at this little counter wrapped around a grill. When his mentor let him open up his own branch, the chef put down roots in Asagaya. Emulating his mentor, he grills Okukuji Shamo chicken, pairing it with wines. Prix fixe menus alternate between chicken and vegetables. The value of the rare chicken cut known as the ‘oyster’ was revealed in this area as well, leading to its popularity. Free-range chicken as you’ve never tasted it.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11003;Arakicho Tatsuya;Japan;Tokyo;10 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.68968;139.722413;40;false;true;Japanese;The owner-chef prides himself on being the link between diner and food producer. He visits not only the producers of the ingredients he uses, but also the potters who make his crockery, sake breweries and wineries, building strong and trusting relationships. To convey that background to his guests, the chef goes the extra mile to make the dining experience fun. Meals conclude with risotto-like rice soup made with broth from takiawase. The chef is determined to waste nothing, using every morsel of food—a commitment he delivers on with flavours that warm the soul.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11004;BIRD LAND;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 4-2-15 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.672747;139.763894;63;true;false;Yakitori;BIRD LAND enchants guests with its wonderfully distinctive yakitori. With supple imagination and a wealth of experience, Toshihiro Wada crafts a new world of possibilities for the humble skewer.  Included among the skewers in his set menus are liver paté, chicken grilled in pepper and oyakodon (chicken and egg on rice). Always attentive to customers’ voices, he reveals the value of rare cuts such as chicken oyster. Determined to pass on his skills, he often works the grill with apprentices at his side.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
11005;THE UPPER;Japan;Tokyo;10F, MARUNOUCHI TERRACE, 1-3-4 Marunouchi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0005, Japan;35.684379;139.764073;86;true;false;French;Dining on the top floor of a tall building surrounded by other high-rises, the view from the spacious rooftop terrace will leave you spellbound. The chatter of guests and the unpretentious service mirror the day-to-day vibrancy of the metropolis below. Regional dishes such as escargot, quenelle and cassoulet are fine companions for wine. Experience a typical day in France in a contemporary Tokyo setting.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11007;Oryori Katsushi;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 8-7-19 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.668507;139.760927;60;true;true;Japanese;The owner-chef’s obsession with dashi soup stock was learnt from his mentor, a Kansai native. He mixes dashi of dried bonito flakes, kombu kelp and clams to impart depth and richness. This dashi is found throughout: in savoury egg custard, soup dishes, hot pots and other Japanese favourites. The chef’s choice of career is down to the influence of his brother, a sushi chef, and this brotherly bond is shown in his vinegared rice, simmered abalone liver sauce and pressed chub mackerel sushi. The menu is a stage on a fascinating journey that we’re going to keep watching.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11008;Äta;Japan;Tokyo;2-5 Sarugakucho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0033, Japan;35.652917;139.704849;34;true;true;French;The appetiser is a seafood charcuterie: squid and mussels dressed in aioli, finely minced raw horse mackerel, and dried chub mackerel. Be sure to try the speciality, bouillabaisse with a rich seafood flavour, and mix it rice with the leftover soup to make risotto. This is a bistro for enjoying seafood to your heart’s content, although the mains include meat dishes as well.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11009;Kagurazaka Marutomi;Japan;Tokyo;3-4 Fukuromachi, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0828, Japan;35.701149;139.738628;19;true;false;Japanese;Wagyu beef is the tie that binds the family of Kenichi Onodera. He named his restaurant ‘Marutomi’ after his grandfather’s cattle farm, and his parents ran a butcher’s shop in Ichinoseki. For that reason, he focuses on wagyu from Iwate Prefecture. Char-grilled and fried items are on the menu, as is sukiyaki with edible wild plants and matsutake mushrooms. The menu changes twice monthly, so a wide range of ingredients are sourced. The combination of traditional multi-course meals with beef dishes is pure Onodera.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11010;Benoit;Japan;Tokyo;10F, La Porte Aoyama, 5-51-8 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.662686;139.709605;36;true;false;French;The Tokyo outpost of Benoit, which was founded in Paris in 1912. The cuisine of this bistro that co-stars French and Japanese influences is overseen by Alain Ducasse. The menu is prix fixe, but diners can choose items to their liking. Dishes bequeathed by the Paris flagship, such as oven-baked escargot and terrine, stand alongside regional fare made with ingredients from across Japan. Antique-accented décor and attentive service convey an unmistakeably French esprit.;Air conditioning;[]
11011;bistro simba;Japan;Tokyo;1-27-8 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.672828;139.772058;96;true;false;French;Visiting France in the 2000s, chef Kikuchi was deeply impressed with the ‘bistronomy’ that was sweeping Paris at the time. He made up his mind to focus on this fusion of casual bistro fare with refined gastronomy. Bouillabaisse rich in the flavour of shrimp and Paris-Brest, a pastry, are prepared with loving memory of Kikuchi’s mentor. Committed to “simple, aromatic food with friendly service”, Kikuchi is moving forward.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11012;Tempura Asanuma;Japan;Tokyo;6F, 2-10-11 Nihombashi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0027, Japan;35.680982;139.774542;84;true;false;Tempura;Fascination with Edo culinary culture led this chef to open a restaurant in Nihombashi. Knowing that Edokko (natives of Tokyo) would eat thick-battered tempura soaked in sauce, the chef uses the technique completely opposite to the thin coating he learned as an apprentice. But the thicker coating traps air bubbles, imparting a fragrant nose and light texture. In an homage to the port of call where tempura arrived from Portugal, the fried feast begins with shrimp toast, a speciality of Nagasaki.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11013;Sushi Matsumoto;Japan;Tokyo;1-49-14 Itabashi, Itabashi-ku, Tokyo, 173-0004, Japan;35.747692;139.719196;27;false;false;Sushi;The atmosphere is relaxed, with jazz playing in the background. To ensure the most enjoyable sake experience, the chef alternates between snacks and nigiri. This is a great place to try a variety of sakes, served in glasses and accompanied by an extensive selection of snacks and sushi. Toro (fatty tuna) is served first, so that the heat of the freshly cooked vinegared rice melts the fat.  Fresh-toasted nori and tea served in Nambu ironware teapots show commitment without compromise.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
11014;commedia;Japan;Tokyo;1-11-3 Toyo, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0016, Japan;35.668418;139.810436;62;true;false;Italian;Seating is counter only, and everyone begins at the same time. After starting with cured ham and cheese, a succession of homemade pasta dishes follows. Meat is char-grilled wagyu sirloin. To wrap up the evening, dishes from dried noodles bring joy to pasta lovers. Mr and Mrs Yamaguchi recreate the cheerful fun of a typical day in Italy, as befits the name commedia, ‘the comedy’. Their desire to bring joy to customers comes through naturally from their cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11015;Arva;Japan;Tokyo;33F, Aman Tokyo, The Otemachi Tower, 1-5-6 Otemachi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0004, Japan;35.685414;139.765432;59;true;true;Italian;Chef Masakazu Hiraki’s aim is to create Italian dishes showcasing the appeal of Japanese ingredients. His work is a cross-fertilization of the knowledge of Japanese farmers with his own experience in Italy, particularly in the Veneto region. Vegetables and fruit bring lively colour to simple, modern fare. His devotion to the good things of the earth manifests in his restaurant’s name, which means ‘harvest’. The stunning view from his dining room atop a 33-floor building adds to the feeling of spaciousness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11016;LA BONNE TABLE;Japan;Tokyo;1F, Coredo Muromachi2, 2-3-1 Nihombashimuromachi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0022, Japan;35.686647;139.774821;35;true;true;French;LA BONNE TABLE lives by the motto ‘farm to table’. Chef Kazunari Nakamura builds strong relationships of trust with food producers, who ship ingredients to him directly from their farms. An amuse-bouche, appropriately named ‘Farm to Table’, is a colourful assortment of vegetables prepared in a variety of ways. Roast shiitake wastes no part of the mushroom, not even the stem. The chef’s ingenuity and creativity bring out the value of his ingredients.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11017;O2;Japan;Tokyo;2-15-12 Miyoshi, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0022, Japan;35.680288;139.802687;45;false;true;Chinese;‘O2’ (‘oh-two’) is a play on Chef Otsu’s name. Like his bow tie and denim apron, the pun is an Otsu trademark. Presented as Chinese cuisine, the fare at O2 really defies easy categories, making use of both Western and Japanese ingredients. The chef’s code is to use Chinese elements in both technique and seasoning. The playful interior also expresses Otsu’s unique vision.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11019;JINBO MINAMI AOYAMA;Japan;Tokyo;4-11-13 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.665668;139.717559;93;false;false;Italian;Modern Italian fare that makes abundant use of vegetables. Chef Yoshinaga Jimbo visits farmers throughout Japan to paint scenes of pastoral life through his cooking. The bagna càuda theme is the breath of the seasons. Brilliantly multicoloured platters and light flavours are the strong points here. As a proud supporter of his home region, Jimbo sources many ingredients from Ibaraki Prefecture, fulfilling hometown expectations as an Ibaraki Food Ambassador.;Air conditioning;[]
11020;BON CHEMIN;Japan;Tokyo;2-40-5 Gohongi, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0053, Japan;35.634677;139.686785;74;true;false;French;The name, which means ‘good road’, reflects Ryo Hanazawa’s determination to tread the path of the culinary artist with sincerity.  His theme is universal flavour and his methods are based on the recipes of the legendary restaurateur Auguste Escoffier. Sardine and vegetable soup, and pigeon and duck roti with offal sauce are long-time favourites in which he takes special pride. Japanese ingredients give a unique twist to his dishes as they bring back the aroma of the good old days of French cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
11021;Asakusa Nagami;Japan;Tokyo;4-43-6 Asakusa, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0032, Japan;35.718952;139.796775;99;true;true;Japanese;Asakusa is the stage on which chef Takumi Nagami performs. Staying faithful to the native flavours of his ingredients, he brings to bear the seasonal elegance he learned in Kyoto. Soup stock is lightly seasoned so as not to overpower the main ingredients. Two options are available for appetiser platters: drinking snacks adorned with leaves or served in hollowed-out yuzu fruits. The kaminari-okoshi sweet rice puff snack is used as batter for fried items, in a tip of the hat to the chef’s beloved Asakusa.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11022;Pont d'Or Inno;Japan;Tokyo;1F, YUITO, 2-4-3 Nihombashimuromachi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0022, Japan;35.687207;139.774153;90;false;true;French;The name ‘Pont d’Or’, literally ‘Golden Bridge’, is a wish that French cuisine and the district of Nihombashi will both prosper. Tasteful décor, reminiscent of a European house, oozes panache. Chef Ken Yuhara incorporates Japanese elements into classic French cuisine taught to him by Noboru Inoue. Manager Toru Ozaki regales guests with explanations of each dish, his attentive service adding to the meal like a floral bouquet. A golden bridge anchored by three talented partners.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11023;sio;Japan;Tokyo;1-35-3 Uehara, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0064, Japan;35.669588;139.68218;88;false;false;Contemporary;Remixed music plays in the background of a dining room which has the feel of a vintage café. The venue is popular for its simple, casual style. The young, close-knit team puts guests at ease with their friendly service. Cuisine is based on French fare but interweaves influences from Italian and Japanese cooking. This is genre-free cuisine born of multinational creativity.;Air conditioning;[]
11024;Sushi Taichi;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 6-4-13 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.671212;139.761328;78;true;true;Sushi;This restaurant loves the chic style of Edo culture and values the human touch. Many sushi shops these days offer two time-limited seatings, serving only omakase set meals. However, Sushi Taichi shows the mettle of an old-fashioned sushi chef. The owner-chef’s agreeable disposition ensures him many regular customers. Above the counter is a shop curtain, while the walls feature woodblock prints depicting street stalls. If you like old-school sushi shops, Sushi Taichi is for you.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11025;MASIA;Japan;Tokyo;8F, 2-4-6 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.673982;139.766492;66;false;false;Spanish;Masía is Spanish for ‘farmhouse’. The chef, Mateu Villaret, created the restaurant from his roots, the dining table of his family back in Catalonia. Inspired by the Mediterranean Sea and the Pyrenees, the hometown fare combines ingredients from both sea and mountain – and proves that Japanese seafood and Spanish ham and chorizo go very nicely together.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11026;Hikarimono;Japan;Tokyo;7-5-11 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.664867;139.727917;85;false;false;Sushi;Kan Sato, known affectionately as ‘Satokan-san’, loves hikarimono (literally ‘shining thing’: fish with silver skin, sliced with the skin left on), hence the shop’s name. The menu is composed with drinkers in mind, so this hikarimono is never left off. Sato’s offering of three courses—sushi and bar snacks, mainly nigiri, and bar snacks—as well as à la carte is pleasing. Hikarimaki of pilchard, shredded dried plum and bettarazuke (daikon pickled in salted rice malt) is famous. Sato’s aim is to offer a sushi shop where people drop in casually. The value for money truly shines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11028;GINZA HABSBURG VEILCHEN;Japan;Tokyo;7F, 7-8-7 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.668979;139.762503;74;true;false;Austrian;Shingo Kanda is spreading Austrian culinary culture. Giving top billing to the cuisine of Vienna, Kanda serves traditional fare from each state of Austria. Wiener schnitzel and boiled ham are typical Viennese specialities. Kanda happily explains where he gets his recipes and tells anecdotes, explaining a cuisine unfamiliar to many of his diners. This dining experience is sure to spark your desire to visit Austria.;Air conditioning;[]
11029;Sushi Kagura;Japan;Tokyo;3-2-3 Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0004, Japan;35.66656;139.754605;20;false;true;Sushi;The chef was drawn to sushi by the simplicity of a dish that is complete with only vinegared rice, wasabi, and a topping. Labouring as an apprentice from dawn to dusk, Kagura’s chef gained a thorough grounding in work that was faithful to the basics. As he moulds his sushi, the chef adds a unique interpretation to the techniques he learned.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11030;Takahashi;Japan;Tokyo;1-7-6 Morishita, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0004, Japan;35.686919;139.797627;27;false;false;Japanese;After studying kaiseki cuisine, the chef moved to Singapore to spread awareness of Japanese cuisine. He returned out of renewed appreciation for the quality of Japanese ingredients. Exceptionally particular about his ingredients, the chef refuses to trust them unless he inspects them at market himself. He learned the basics at famous restaurants in Japan, then acquired hospitality skills from his experience overseas. Both qualities reveal themselves in his fare and service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11031;Chiso Koryu;Japan;Tokyo;5F, 5-14-14 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.668557;139.766796;69;true;false;Japanese;The restaurant’s name declares that its food is created, not merely prepared, and indeed the cuisine here is infused with imagination. Kazuki Takagi spares no effort to furnish a delightfully creative bill of fare, casting his magic on ingredients from around the country. Puffer fish spring rolls, monaka wafer cake filled with monkfish liver and smoked daikon pickles testify to his inventive spirit. Sesame tofu and sea bream on rice with Japanese tea poured over it follow tradition.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11032;Sanwa;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 5-13-14 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.637765;139.722837;28;true;true;Italian;‘Sanwa’ means ‘three-part harmony’: harmony between producers, chefs and guests. Descending the stairs, your eye is caught by the three-ring logo, which is both the Watanabe family crest and the restaurant’s symbol. The menu lists producers by name, neatly linking them to guests through the chef. The name would not suggest an Italian restaurant, nor does its offering of char-grilled meats, but these speak to its unique character. The strength of three brings mutual prosperity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11033;Arakicho Kintsugi;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-3-6 Yotsuya, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0004, Japan;35.688496;139.72185;89;true;false;Japanese;An intimate Japanese restaurant that fits well among the string of watering holes in the Arakicho area of Shinjuku. The two who run it are experts in cuisine and sake. Set menus are plotted with the tastes of sake drinkers in mind. One piece at a time, in small quantities, is an enjoyable way to dine. As the sake flows, boiled greens, sushi, fried items and other items are served with varying degrees of preparation and temperature. A seasonal selection of steamed items on rice ends the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11034;Jimbocho Gokita;Japan;Tokyo;2-4-9 Nishikanda, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 101-0065, Japan;35.698396;139.754346;95;true;false;Yakitori, French;Yuto Gokita is pioneering yakitori eaten with French sauces. In place of yakitori dipping sauce, Gokita favours Madeira and red-wine sauces prepared from chicken bones and calf broth. Skewers of chicken breast and shrimp are smothered in sauces of crustaceans. Skewers of chicken meatballs are accented with herb butter for a Bourgogne flavour. Reservations are required for the set menu which includes wood-grilled lamb and pigeon.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11035;Nebuka;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 6-8-28 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.659973;139.732128;50;false;true;Contemporary;Nebuka was opened by the proprietor of a wine bar. It is said that the best grapevines are those with the deepest roots (‘ne-buka’), and deep are the connections Nebuka cultivates with producers and in ingredients and cuisine. Omakase set menus focus on vegetables and game. Experienced in both French and Japanese cuisine, the chef applies expertise in both schools, and even creates pasta dishes. Each dish is arranged simply, placing the ingredients centre stage. A young team provides bright and pleasant service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11036;Tasogare;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 2-6-2 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.656261;139.733094;21;true;true;French;Tasogare means ‘twilight’, and that’s when the doors open, to ensure guests an enjoyable visit. Fun is on the blackboard menu, with combinations that make visions of deliciousness dance before the eyes - foie gras with Danish pastry, for example, or asparagus with zabaglione. Vinegared fish and stew are the very essence of Japanese cuisine. Tasogare entices with layers of nuanced technique and a spirit of playfulness. Free-spirited cooking, to be enjoyed with a free spirit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11037;Oryori Kokoroba;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 2-10-11 Nihombashiningyocho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0013, Japan;35.685584;139.784063;38;false;true;Japanese;The name incorporates a character from the chef’s name while professing sincere devotion to gastronomy. That sincerity is on full display in the hassun appetisers. To convey the mood of the passing seasons, the chef incorporates meticulously chosen items fresh from the market. Oyakodon (chicken and egg on rice) made with freshly cooked rice is a sentimental favourite of the chef, one he’s made continuously since his apprenticeship. His dedication shines through in his painstaking attention to his work.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11038;Chugokusai KAKYU-BOU;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-1-62, Takanawa, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0074, Japan;35.640708;139.73776;92;false;false;Chinese;Huaqiu (read as Kakyu in Japanese) is the name of a holy mountain, mentioned in a Chinese book of philosophy, where many fruits grow. The name Kakyu-bou, ‘Kitchen of Mount Huaqiu’, captures the joy of cooking in a spirit of thanksgiving for the foods granted by the gods. As an apprentice, the chef learned that without the basics there can be no application. Accordingly, he searches for innovation while staying within the boundaries of orthodox Chinese cuisine. The appetiser assortment consists of bounty from sea and soil prepared with Chinese techniques. The joy of cooking creates the joy of eating.;Counter dining;[]
11040;Alternative;Japan;Tokyo;5-12-24 Shirokane, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0072, Japan;35.645258;139.72364;94;false;false;French;Alt-rock is rock music that doesn’t fit any particular category or is born of a spirit of breaking down established concepts. Noting the free rein Gallic cuisine enjoyed during his sojourn in France, the chef named his restaurant ‘Alternative’ to signal his determination to create new value. He lays the foundations of classic French theory and technique before adding elements from Japanese and Chinese culinary traditions. The venue, the former premises of a neighbourhood workshop, also expresses the chef’s individualism.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11041;Chugokusai HINA;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 2-16-12 Kamimeguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0051, Japan;35.642093;139.697751;69;false;true;Chinese;Counter-style Chinese committed to natural deliciousness. The husband, schooled in the kitchens of Yokohama and Shanghai, focuses on the cooking, while his wife serves guests. The inherent flavours of the ingredients are held paramount, interpreting the seasons of Japan through Chinese cuisine. Each dish is seasoned with restraint and elegance. In a novel twist, instead of Shaoxing wine, items are paired with well-aged Japanese sake or organic wine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11042;Kabukizaura Masashi;Japan;Tokyo;4-11-9 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669836;139.768574;94;true;true;Japanese;Diners are greeted by the open owner-chef and the graceful proprietress. The playful riot of colours on the wall is a tableau on the theme of people’s relationship with food. In this vision stretching from the past to the future, faces are drawn in kumadori, the shaded kabuki makeup fitting for a restaurant ‘behind the kabuki theatre’ (kabukiza-ura). The omakase set meal abounds in changes in inflection: two pieces of nigiri and two types of fried items (tempura and deep-fried) highlight contrasting textures. The chef’s experience with Chinese cooking bursts from his baked gyoza. For the best drink pairings, let the proprietress choose.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11043;DAN;Japan;Tokyo;4-34-10 Daizawa, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 155-0032, Japan;35.653543;139.672301;70;true;true;French;Casual French dining by a chef with deep experience in gastronomy. The counter forms an arc around the kitchen, dissolving the barrier between host and guest. Traditional recipes cooked with Japanese ingredients highlight the affinity between the two. Risotto, for example, is a perennial favourite, being a rice dish. The intimate establishment and cheerful circle of guests make Dan a step up.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11044;Toriyaki Ohana;Japan;Tokyo;3-28-2 Ebisu, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0013, Japan;35.643771;139.715599;50;false;true;Chicken Specialities;A menu that is all about chicken in the traditional kaiseki multi-course meal style, from a chef accomplished in Japanese cuisine. Start with an appetiser of chicken breast wrapped with nori seaweed or spring roll of minced chicken with miso. Soup dishes are stocked with chicken wonton. Grilled chicken and duck are not skewered but char-grilled on a wire net, pungently scorched on the surface by broiling close to a hot flame. Chicken bone soup over rice brings down the curtain. Nothing is wasted, proving that every part is delicious.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11045;Orchestra;Japan;Tokyo;4-1-7 Yoyogi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0053, Japan;35.679255;139.693608;70;false;true;Italian;Imola, the city in Italy’s Emilia-Romagna where the chef apprenticed, has a famous music academy. The restaurant’s name derives from the passion for classical music he learned from the students he befriended there. In Imola, the chef developed his belief that a restaurant resembles an orchestra, in that a wide range of players work in harmony to create a greater whole. Cuisine on plates decorated with musical instrument motifs and classical music piped into the dining room deliver a performance worthy of any conservatory.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11047;124. KAGURAZAKA;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 12-4 Wakamiyacho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0827, Japan;35.700304;139.739357;93;false;false;Yakitori;The numbers in the name are both the address of the shop and the birthday of a member of staff. The first skewer is chicken heart, because the deep, rich flavour of this cut makes a strong impression. norimaki (bite-size chunks wrapped in nori seaweed) of chicken tenderloin, cooked vegetable salads and deep-fried tofu intersperse the omakase set meal, varying the tone and providing items that pair agreeably with sake. Ramen in chicken broth closes out the presentation. Served in dragon-pattern bowls with nori to evoke a certain sense of nostalgia.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11048;hatsune;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-11-6 Meguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0063, Japan;35.63198;139.70651;62;false;true;Chinese;The chef works alone in this tiny restaurant. At lunchtime the predominant theme is noodle dishes, such as dandan noodles and hot-and-sour ramen. In the evening, both à la carte and set menu dining are available. Be sure to order the appetiser platter, as it’s packed with variety and the time and effort taken to prepare it are apparent. The spring rolls, a finger food, are also recommended. The ‘Yellow Mapo Tofu with Seafood’ intrigues with its unusual name and distinctive yellow colour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11049;Chez Inno;Japan;Tokyo;2-4-16 Kyobashi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0031, Japan;35.676831;139.768703;97;true;true;French;Chez Inno is a creation of Noboru Inoue, a name engraved in the history of French cuisine in Japan. Responsible for the kitchen, Koga and Teshima carry on his ambitions. This restaurant raises the bar in gourmet dining, as witnessed in the lamb à la Maria Callas, the founder’s reframe of a venerable recipe. The sense of what must be preserved and what should be tinkered with is astute. It will be a joy to see how the new Chez Inno changes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11050;Valinor;Japan;Tokyo;4-32-7 Ogikubo, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0051, Japan;35.704279;139.623899;49;true;true;French;The chef aims for nothing less than unforgettable cuisine. His ingredients are the stars of his show, and to place them at centre stage, each dish uses as few as possible. While adding twists to texture and flavour, he leaves a vivid impression of each ingredient. Only those dishes that keep being made, keep being eaten, can be called classics. He puts his stamp on his food through simplifying the complexities of French cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
11051;KOKYU;Japan;Tokyo;2-13-9 Yokokawa, Sumida-ku, Tokyo, 130-0003, Japan;35.704836;139.812039;83;false;true;Contemporary;A ‘food laboratory’ housed in a small, renovated warehouse. Only creative cuisine, fragrant with spices and suffused with the umami of tea, for pairing with cocktails is offered. Recipes take their inspiration from French cuisine and the restaurant’s name, which means ‘wither and decay’, is from the desire to breathe deeply of love for old cuisine before creating the new. Enjoy the fruits of experimentation in cooking and beverages.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11052;Wakiya Ichiemicharo;Japan;Tokyo;6-11-10 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.6696361;139.7348462;26;true;false;Chinese;The flagship restaurant of Yuji Wakiya, renowned pioneer of nouvelle chinois cuisine. With “tradition and creativity” as his motto, Wakiya professes a new style of Chinese cooking. The starter, ‘Nine Joys Assorted Appetiser’, is so named because nine is a number believed to bring good luck in China. The restaurant name means ‘once a day, let’s relax, laugh and have tea’. Cuisine and hospitality to bring a smile to your face.;Air conditioning;[]
11053;Tanakada Nishiazabuten;Japan;Tokyo;2-2-2 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.664171;139.720271;33;true;false;Izakaya;From the Rosanjin crockery to the retro Showa-era coasters, Tadaaki Tanaka’s restaurant is an interplay between authenticity and playfulness. The comments on the menu are easy to understand, enticing with delicious descriptions. When the chef exclaims “Tabetenshai!” meaning “let’s eat” in the Hakata dialect, it makes you want to eat what you like, as much as you like. The courteous staff of this high-grade izakaya, a step above a kappo but not quite a ryotei, ensure you’ll enjoy your visit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
11054;Kappo Yuichi;Japan;Tokyo;1-6-10 Kamiogi, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0043, Japan;35.705104;139.621378;49;true;true;Japanese;This counter-style restaurant hangs out its shingle in a corner of the roundabout in front of the north entrance to Ogikubo Station. Chef Kotaro Tachibana bases the menu around vegetables, showcasing the depth of Japanese cuisine. Takiawase highlight the ever-changing faces of nature, with colourful vegetables that cool you in summer and warm you in winter. Appetiser platters arrayed with salad with mashed tofu dressing, seasoned boiled greens and vegetables dressed with sesame sauce calm the soul still further with their savoury flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11055;Uisane;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 4-2 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.70207;139.739727;92;true;false;Japanese;What Kohei Ikeda tries to do is mix freewheeling imagination into traditional fare, an approach taught by the head of Kikunoi during his apprenticeship there. Fine examples include sea urchin wrapped in sea bream and spring rolls of glass shrimp. He focuses on ingredients from his native Ehime, the better to share its wonders with the world. Born and raised in Uwajima, Ikeda dreamed of becoming a chef in his youth. He never forgets to carry out this ‘original intention’, a phrase reflected in the name of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11056;Sushi Kanesho;Japan;Tokyo;3-33-9 Asakusa, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0032, Japan;35.717715;139.796983;50;false;true;Sushi;Akira Watanabe inherited old-school sushi traditions but learned from his mentor the spirit of adding his own novel spin. Vinegared sushi rice is regarded as the most important component of great sushi, and Watanabe’s evolved over time through trial and error. The chef displays judgment and skill as he serves gizzard shad first, and his simmered conger eel and kurakake egg (egg straddling the rice like a saddle) reflect his personality. He confides that he tries to ‘investigate the old and understand the new’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11057;UDATSU SUSHI;Japan;Tokyo;2-48-10 Kamimeguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0051, Japan;35.64197;139.6953;56;true;false;Sushi;A fresh intersection between sushi and art. The walls of this modern space are hung with paintings by artists, giving the feeling of dining in a gallery. Bright and colourful side dishes include herb rolls, smoked tuna and veggie rolls. Nigiri technique hews close to the basics, but with some tempura-inspired creative touches, such as sea urchin and fried nori. A sushi restaurant for a new age.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11058;Maeshiba Ryoriten;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 4-7-5 Tamagawa, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 158-0094, Japan;35.61678;139.625753;45;false;false;French;The speciality is charcoal-grilled beef and sauce only. On this, the French cuisine of Taira Maeshiba is focused. Ingredients whose producers are listed by name, finely disciplined flame-tending techniques, and traditional yet distinctive sauces combine to form menus only Chef Maeshiba could compose. The fare is simple, the work meticulous.;Air conditioning;[]
11060;Shunka Nakamura;Japan;Tokyo;2-11-7 Higashinihombashi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0004, Japan;35.692857;139.787149;38;true;true;Chinese;Relentless curiosity is the driving force of this chef. After going to Hong Kong to study Cantonese cuisine, he then worked at a kappo to learn about Japanese food. He calls the marriage of these two shunka, which roughly translates as ‘Chinese food with a seasonal sensibility’. Spring rolls of pike conger or conger eel are one example. The steamed chicken is a secret recipe passed on from his Hong Kong mentor. He presents the home-cooked flavours that Hongkongers love.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11061;Nœud. TOKYO;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-5-7 Hirakawacho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 102-0093, Japan;35.67969;139.738705;95;false;true;French, Contemporary;The focus of the cuisine is aroma above all. Dishes are built around vegetables, with parts such as leaves, stalks and peels transformed through a variety of cooking methods. Presentation is modern, a layering of flavours and textures. The restaurant’s approach of ‘All Sustainable French’, using everything, wasting nothing, is its way of discovering new facets of familiar ingredients. Recycled materials in the décor reflect the same conviction.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11063;Akasaka Watanabe;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-17-59 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.670705;139.738022;59;true;false;Japanese;Dressed in white and sporting a bow tie, Yujiro Watanabe greets his guests with a smile. His spirit of graceful service is ‘delicious, fun and welcoming’. Sesame ground in a large bowl, karasumi (salted and dried grey mullet roe) shaved before customers’ eyes and the staging of the kitchen are three shared moments. Rice from Niigata, produced by his sister and her husband, is used. Sea bream chazuke (green tea poured over rice) is a legacy from his mentor. The gratitude is palpable, the conversation lively.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11064;caillou;Japan;Tokyo;1-7-9 Haramachi, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 152-0011, Japan;35.616065;139.698561;35;true;false;French;The carefully selected fare borrows ideas from the local markets of France. The style here is to confer with the chef before you order, perusing the showcase full of ingredients in front of the kitchen. Simple French items dominate, such as smoked salmon, pâté en croûte, fish du jour, pig’s feet, cured beef and vanilla ice cream. Pointing and choosing adds to the fun, and dishes are prepared in the quantity you prefer.;Air conditioning;[]
11065;IL GiOTTO;Japan;Tokyo;5-21-9 Komazawa, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 154-0012, Japan;35.6287706;139.6525879;35;false;false;Italian;In this white-walled detached house facing Komazawa-Koen Avenue, with its cosy, wood-lined interior, sounds of food preparation from the open kitchen, and the atmosphere of a shop run by a couple, guests feel invited into a home. Chef Naofumi Takahashi specializes in meat dishes, such as bruschetta with home-cured ham and simmered tripe. He takes special pride in his slow-aged, char-grilled meats. Beef, aged to enhance umami, is seasoned with salt and pepper.;Air conditioning;[]
11066;sio AOYAMA;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Nonoaoyama, 3-4-3 Kitaaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0061, Japan;35.667647;139.713086;71;true;false;Contemporary;The Aoyama branch of sio fairly bubbles with imaginative power. The foundation is French, but the direction is creative, paying no attention to genre. Meats are grilled over a wood fire to draw out the full strength of their inherent flavours. If you sit at the counter, you can gaze into the flickering flames and enjoy the aroma of meat sizzling on the grill. The restaurant’s name, ‘sio’, is Japanese for ‘salt’, affirming the importance of this vital seasoning. The restaurant prides itself on salting with just the right touch to highlight flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
11068;UNE PINCÉE;Japan;Tokyo;2-19-2 Higashiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0044, Japan;35.656709;139.742547;46;true;true;French;Gelée of vegetable mousse and consommé is a much-requested dish. The ingredients vary with the season—white asparagus in spring, corn in summer, butternut squash in autumn, Jerusalem artichoke in winter—and are prepared with a light touch. Vegetables arrive from the chef’s parents in Ibaraki Prefecture. For the main course, pastry-wrapped pigeon or quail is a longstanding favourite. The number of dishes, arranged in a modern style, and the portions are adjusted to preference.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11069;Tempura Shimomura;Japan;Tokyo;1-11-13 Misuji, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0055, Japan;35.704205;139.785405;62;true;false;Tempura;The menu is extensive to cater to diners’ tastes but has strong regional roots. Fish and vegetables are fried in alternation, with the accent on shrimp, sillago and conger eel. Recently, few tempura places offer tendon only, but here, tendon of vegetable tempura and kakiage (all-in-one seafood and vegetable tempura blend) are available at lunchtime. Feel free to add seafood items to the vegetable set menu. Woodblock prints and an icebox vaguely recreate the atmosphere of working-class Edo.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11070;BVLGARI IL RISTORANTE LUCA FANTIN;Japan;Tokyo;9F, 2-7-12 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.672858;139.767133;71;true;true;Italian;Luca Fantin is a seeker after Japanese ingredients. He finds ones that bring forth his creativity and interprets them according to his Italian roots. Sea urchin pasta, entwined in a seafood sauce, expresses the bounty of the ocean. The panache of the service staff as they ladle out sauces and soups, desserts arriving on wagons: all are exuberant in presentation. Refined cuisine, gracious service and harmonious interior are all steeped in the elegance of BVLGARI.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11073;ÉTAPE;Japan;Tokyo;2-21-6 Higashikomagata, Sumida-ku, Tokyo, 130-0005, Japan;35.707483;139.799983;85;true;true;French;A casual French affair near Komagata Bridge over the Sumida River. Keen to develop a rapport with the surrounding old neighbourhoods, Chef Shinji Kawamura installed a counter so that he could converse with his guests. Focus is on à la carte dishes that can be ordered without fuss. The Uni Pain Perdu is sea urchin with French toast. Bouillabaisse is paired with chorizo. On weekends and holidays, lunch is limited to set menus only.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11074;LUGDUNUM Bouchon Lyonnais;Japan;Tokyo;4-3-7 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.701746;139.740121;24;false;true;French;This ‘Little Lyons’ down a Kagurazaka alley entertains guests with the regional cuisine chef Christophe Paucod remembers from his hometown. The famed quenelle is paired with buttered rice in the style of a doria. Homemade sausages are used in miniature hamburgers. The interior, a faithful recreation of Bouchon, a Lyons restaurant, wraps guests in the warm feeling of travelling in France.;Air conditioning;[]
11075;MIMOSA;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-10-40 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.666438;139.714327;79;false;false;Chinese;The counter seats are a uniform white, creating a sense of presence, and the sight of cooking right in front of you is reassuring. Amid the sounds and aromas of stir-frying in woks, the chef sometimes makes conversation with guests while plating their meals. Based on Shanghai cuisine, the dishes are set in front of you as soon as they are cooked. The restaurant’s name was chosen for the chef’s grandmother’s favourite flower. This is food created with loving thoughts of Grandma.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11076;Tempura Otsuka;Japan;Tokyo;2-12-11 Iriya, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 110-0013, Japan;35.719715;139.789306;23;true;true;Tempura;The owner-chef, born and raised in Iriya, is an artisan through and through. Proceedings are by the book, starting with milder flavours like tiger prawn, squid and sillago before proceeding to bolder tastes. Edomae toppings are favoured, such as tidepool gunnel and big-eyed flathead. Decorating the walls are senshagaku, wooden tablets typically posted on the pillars of shrines, inscribed with local supporters’ names. The characters suffuse the restaurant with the atmosphere of old neighbourhoods.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11077;REQUINQUER;Japan;Tokyo;5-17-11 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.637594;139.723284;34;false;true;French;Soichi Furuya seeks out the attractions and possibilities of French cuisine while staying in touch with current trends. Terrine de foie gras is a speciality that keeps customers coming back. Soups and crepes made using vegetables that don’t meet JA size regulations support farmers. The various set menus focused on the unique traits of Japanese-French fusion cuisine excite diners. The restaurant’s name means ‘be of good cheer’, and indeed REQUINQUER invigorates diners and food producers alike.;Air conditioning;[]
11080;Tsurutokame;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 6-7-15 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670611;139.762574;79;false;true;Japanese;The name means ‘crane and turtle’ and derives from a Japanese folktale in which a crane from the wider world (the guest) befriends a turtle in a pond (the chefs). It reflects the ladies’ desire to spread Japanese culture through Japanese cuisine, so appetiser platters are arranged like the decorations of traditional events. The gracious service puts you immediately at ease. The crane and turtle are a symbol of good fortune. At birthday parties, happiness is sure to descend on your table.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11081;eman;Japan;Tokyo;1-3-6 Shirakawa, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0021, Japan;35.681538;139.799395;19;true;false;Spanish;Satoru Kobayashi expresses his connections with the seasons and food producers of Japan through the medium of Spanish hometown cooking. A speciality is rice cuisine. Clams on rice, a Basque dish, is done in a Fukagawa-meshi style (asari clam miso soup over rice). For the squid-ink paella, firefly squid are used. Familiar Japanese rice is harmonized with the styles of each region. The sheer variety of the menu, encompassing tapas, char-grilled dishes and more, testifies to the depth and richness of Spanish cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11082;MATSUKI;Japan;Tokyo;2-23-3 Nakano, Nakano-ku, Tokyo, 164-0001, Japan;35.705373;139.667722;82;false;true;French;The husband-and-wife team of chefs make you feel at home. Inspired by life in the south of France, the couple strive to recreate the unpretentious flavours of the countryside. Vegetable soup, fragrant with basil, encapsulates the memories of both chefs. With onion tarts, stewed beef à la Provençal and couscous, visions of everyday life in France float before your eyes. Accompany your meal with one of their select organic wines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11083;Ginza Adachi Naoto;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 7-6-5 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669698;139.761992;68;true;false;Japanese;This restaurant values traditional techniques honed at a ryotei. The painstakingly prepared appetisers are a must-try. Seasonal iimushi, mochi rice topped with fish and steamed, is served as an amuse-bouche, paired with seasonal tastes such as sea urchin, salmon roe and chestnut. Instead of rice, the meal closes with konnyaku soba (devil’s-tongue noodles), to relieve uncomfortable fullness after the meal. Meticulous food preparation eloquently conveys the spirit and feeling of the owner-chef.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11084;Akebonobashi Kazu;Japan;Tokyo;16 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.691283;139.724753;17;false;true;Japanese;In search of cuisine that only his native country could conceive, the chef devoted himself to the path of Japanese cuisine. The menu observes the basics of kaiseki while imparting creative flourishes. Wanmono include items with fishcake that complements the broth. Fish in season is salted and grilled over charcoal. Takikomi-gohan, served at the end of the meal, is attuned to the seasons as well. He prizes simplicity yet spares neither ingenuity nor attention to detail.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11085;Oryori Ichiho;Japan;Tokyo;3F, 1-23-10 Ebisu, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0013, Japan;35.646112;139.715927;33;true;true;Japanese;The name is a play on ‘ho’, which could mean ‘step’, as in ‘stepping forward’ or ‘bounty, prosperity’, reflecting chef Ryusuke Yamazaki’s desire that his restaurant blossom and prosper. The soup stock gets its umami from kombu, with a light flavour reflecting his Kyoto experience. Dishes such as fish steamed with grated turnip on top and dumplings made from bamboo-shoot derive from ages past, recounting the culinary culture of the ancient capital. Pike conger in summer and eddoes in winter are eagerly awaited.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11086;RISTORANTE Al Porto;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-24-9 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.658807;139.724294;74;true;false;Italian;Mamoru Kataoka is a pioneer who has broadened the appeal of Italian gastronomy in Japan. His passion for seafood stems was inspired by the seafood restaurants he encountered on a visit to Milan in the 1960s. Al Porto’s famous pasta is a seafood ragù prepared with lashings of clams and shrimp. Kataoka manages the kitchen and restaurant with his son. When time allows, father and son circulate among the tables, ever mindful of the importance of graceful service.;Air conditioning;[]
11087;COMME À LA MAISON;Japan;Tokyo;6-4-15 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.670221;139.734375;70;false;false;French;Yuji Wakui faithfully recreates the cuisine of southwestern France, taught to him by a chef from Landes. From pâté de campagne to terrine de foie gras and duck confit, all are prepared with heartfelt affection. But Wakui reserves a special fondness for soupe de garbure, a simmered mélange of ham, duck, white kidney beans and other ingredients that spreads the flavours of Landes to a ready audience in Tokyo. Unwavering faithfulness to tradition wordlessly expresses Wakui’s gratitude to his mentor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11088;Shokudo Uyuki;Japan;Tokyo;4-11-9 Asakusa, Taito-ku, Tokyo, 111-0032, Japan;35.718337;139.796784;56;false;true;Japanese;The characters for dining hall can be read as ‘jikido’ in Buddhist terminology – a hall where monks take their meals. Yuki Kanazawa chose the name because he aspires to offer respite that soothes people’s souls through cuisine. He eschews luxurious ingredients and sprinkles his menu with simple fare such as o-hitashi (a boiled vegetable side dish) and aemono (a salad of cooked vegetables). Running his restaurant alone, the chef is never far from his customers. Good-humoured service stimulates lively conversation.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11089;L'allium;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 4-9-23 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.638314;139.72337;46;false;false;French;The basement dining room has the air of a concert hall. The conductor, on stage in his brightly lit kitchen, is chef Yoshiaki Shindo. Modern French is the cuisine here, composed of both Japanese and French ingredients. Teppanyaki foie gras is an imaginative variation, while Japanese parsley and Okinawan spinach add a gentle bitterness to fruits and root vegetables, bringing a fresh face to old favourites.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11090;songbook;Japan;Tokyo;5-10-7 Daita, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 155-0033, Japan;35.659368;139.66027;73;true;false;French;The fire used for cooking is a flickering flame of kindling inside a stove. The chef focuses on the heating power and convection heat of the embers to elicit the desired flavours. Vegetables sent direct from farm and chicken and beef are grilled uncut to cover them with smoky aroma. Western music piped through the chic interior is selected by the chef, a former musician. Artful arrangement of cuisine, interior and music creates a welcoming time and space.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11091;Hibinoryori Viola;Japan;Tokyo;4-12-4 Minamiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0047, Japan;35.647457;139.724216;64;true;true;Japanese;A mother-daughter team opened this restaurant out of a desire to spread Japanese culinary culture. The chef and author of the menu is the mother, herself the daughter of the head of a tea ceremony school. The guiding principle is to base the fare on daily Japanese home cooking. Soup stock is drawn with painstaking care from select seasonal ingredients. The salad of cooked vegetables in season is generously portioned, while steaming fresh-cooked rice is served with Japanese comfort food. Home-style fare infused with the spirit of kaiseki.;Air conditioning;[]
11092;APICIUS;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-9-4 Yurakucho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0006, Japan;35.674942;139.761009;76;true;true;French;The name is a tribute to an epicure of ancient Rome. Masterpieces by Maurice Utrillo and Bernard Buffet decorate the art nouveau interior, creating the atmosphere of a salon. A particularly recommended menu item is the mousse of sea urchin, caviar and vegetables, a speciality handed down from the restaurant’s first chef. Interior, cuisine, wine, service: the quintessential elements of a great restaurant are here in abundance.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11093;Tinc gana;Japan;Tokyo;4-3 Rokubancho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 102-0085, Japan;35.689171;139.735318;82;false;true;Spanish, Contemporary;To convey the gastronomy of contemporary Spain, the chef adopted the concept of Barcelona's local cuisine with a modern sensibility. Pan con tomate is just one Catalan tradition. All ingredients are painstakingly selected to whet the appetite with their lightness. The restaurant’s name means ‘I’m hungry’ in Catalan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11096;Clos Des Gourmets;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-18-4 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.635275;139.720819;56;false;true;French;In his primary school graduation yearbook, the future chef wrote, “I want to be a chef”. He studied gastronomy in Paris, developing his most intimate relationships with a restaurant in the 7th arrondissement. The chef’s culinary philosophy, his restaurant’s name and his signature cuisine are all inherited from his mentor. One representative dish is tête de cochon, grilled cuts from a pig’s head. In this intimate eatery, guests are in close proximity with the chef, as if invited by a friend.;Air conditioning;[]
11097;PATH;Japan;Tokyo;1-44-2 Tomigaya, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0063, Japan;35.668478;139.689938;74;true;true;French, Contemporary;This casual restaurant is the brainchild of a chef and a pâtissier. Dinner is mostly prix fixe, fusing Japanese ingredients with fermented foods as well as spices from various countries. Catering to the local lifestyle, Path offers a selection of organic wines and is open from morning onwards. Music of no particular genre streams through the vintage interior themed on street culture.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining;[]
11098;PONTE DEL PIATTO;Japan;Tokyo;5-19-7 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.649071;139.720288;32;true;false;Italian;Originality of approach is Hidenori Tadauchi’s strong suit. After being raised by parents who ran a sushi shop, he majored in Japanese cuisine, but his passion for Italian cooking and football persuaded him to travel to Italy, where he honed his modern creativity at restaurants there. Cold pasta with white-flesh fish is braced with kombu kelp, the influence of his father. Risotto of young ayu, served in early summer, imparts a Japanese sense of the seasons.;Air conditioning;[]
11099;Kiyosumi Takahara;Japan;Tokyo;2-15-4 Kiyosumi, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0024, Japan;35.683152;139.796707;72;false;true;Japanese;Kyoto cuisine has left its mark on chef Shimon Takahara. Like his father before him, he apprenticed as a chef in Kyoto, devoting himself to his gastronomical studies. Guided by the teachings of his mentor, Takahara dedicates his heart and soul to creating dishes that offer a sense of the seasons and reverberate in the senses. Each day’s appetiser, prepared from what is most seasonal, shows this devotion. In spring, expect dishes laden with the colours and aromas of daily variations such as bamboo shoots and asparagus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11100;Sushi Kobayashi;Japan;Tokyo;8-2-10 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669349;139.759504;97;false;true;Sushi;Guests are greeted in Edo dialect with a hearty “Irasshaimashi”. A short shop curtain hangs under a market-stall roof, lending the shop an Edo-era food-stall ambience. Expect steaming hot towels, piping hot tea and gracious service. Influenced by two mentors, the owner-chef prepares fish patiently in the time-honoured way and uses red vinegar to form rice portions. His aim is to be his patrons’ every-day sushi stop. An old-school, no-nonsense sushi shop in both appearance and demeanour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11102;Shintomicho Yuasa;Japan;Tokyo;2-7-4 Shintomi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0041, Japan;35.670861;139.773717;32;false;true;Chinese;The character for ‘food’ (食) is composed of the components for ‘person’ (人) and ‘good’ (良), signifying the power of food to make a person good. Daisuke Yuasa, who puts great store by the principles of a balanced diet and good food for good health, creates dishes he hopes will support his patrons’ health in both body and soul. Another of his wishes is that food should be fun, so he gained a sommelier qualification to help customers expand their enjoyment.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11103;Sushi Marufuku;Japan;Tokyo;3-17-4 Nishiogiminami, Suginami-ku, Tokyo, 167-0053, Japan;35.70367;139.602345;80;true;false;Sushi;Aged sushi prepared with originality and passion. Yutaka Isayama ages fish to bring out aroma, tenderness and flavour, favouring dry-ageing to impart a certain wildness of taste. Snacks are interspersed so as not to jade the palate with a succession of intensely flavoured sushi toppings. Aged sushi pairs well with sake, so ask the proprietress, an accomplished sake sommelier, for suggestions.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11104;Ristorante ACQUA PAZZA;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Passage Aoyama, 2-27-18 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.669067;139.716577;88;false;false;Italian;Chef Yoshimi Hidaka has broadened the horizons of Neapolitan hometown cooking. Acqua pazza, the poached white fish dish that so thrilled him in Naples, is both the restaurant’s name and its signature dish. Prepared by fishermen, it began as fish and tomatoes simmered in seawater but here freshwater is used and Manila clams are added for saltiness. The synergy of umami from inosinic acid in the fish, glutamic acid in the tomato and succinic acid in the Manila clams is classic Yoshimi Hidaka ingenuity.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
11106;unique;Japan;Tokyo;3-12-3 Meguro, Meguro-ku, Tokyo, 153-0063, Japan;35.631832;139.705803;94;false;true;French;Fine dining in a casual setting and price range is the concept. Masaaki Nakai interprets the classics to conjure a cuisine that is unique, hence the restaurant’s name. Stately presentations such as smoked terrine of foie gras and orange-fleshed yam or Asian black bear grilled in pie crust argue the case persuasively. Game such as fowl and rabbit are a seasonal speciality. Enjoy à la carte with a well-aged wine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11108;Sakuragi;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-7-2 Tsukiji, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0045, Japan;35.667948;139.773784;92;true;false;Japanese;What Izuru Sakuragi prizes is the deliciousness born of freshness. Soup stock is made with dried bonito flakes shaved in front of the guests. Some items are toasted over straw, others grilled over charcoal, at the chef’s discretion. Freshly cooked rice is served steaming, with accompaniments chosen for contrast in flavour. The thoughtful timeliness with which Sakuragi asks if guests would like seconds is a welcome touch. The chef’s character and passion shine in his cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11109;Oryori Horiuchi;Japan;Tokyo;9-15 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.690053;139.72219;80;false;false;Japanese;The starting point for Mrs. Sayaka Horiuchi is her early life lived amid natural beauty. Considering that ‘the mountains water the village and feed the ocean,’ the dishes are prepared with a spirit of gratitude for ingredients from land and sea. Horiuchi nurtures relations with food producers nationwide who share her vision. Local vegetables are from farmers in Nerima, clams from fishermen in Kyoto. Her famous chicken offal stew is home cooking from her native Yamanashi Prefecture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11110;ETHICA;Japan;Tokyo;1-3-3 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.675388;139.766344;93;false;true;Mexican;The chef studied in Mexico to learn about a culture that had been evolving for millennia. Based on the natural and spiritual features he sensed there, he created recipes to bring to mind local ingredients and culinary methods. The ‘three jewels’ of Mexican cuisine are maize, beans and chilli peppers. Combining this trio with Japanese ingredients is Ethica’s speciality. Out of concern for the environment and society, the chef aims to minimize food loss at his restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11111;Sushidokoro Yamato;Japan;Tokyo;3-7-2 Tsukiji, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0045, Japan;35.667948;139.773784;33;true;false;Sushi;Growing up immersed in the rhythm of his father's sushi restaurant, the chef nurtured a childhood dream of becoming a sushi chef. After apprenticing in Tokyo, in gratitude he gave his shop the same name as his father’s restaurant. Omakase set menus lean towards nigiri, fulfilling the duty of a true sushi restaurant. Rice is seasoned with a mixture of red vinegar and rice vinegar to accommodate a wide range of sushi toppings. The first item is gizzard shad, an ingredient that taxes the skill of any sushi artist. Generous portions of rice lend presence to each item.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11112;malca;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-27-16 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.668536;139.71702;87;true;true;Italian;The painting of a wave and the ornamental terra cotta plates are blue like the sea. Awaji Island, where Chef Tsukasa Kitano grew up, is never far from his mind. He named his restaurant after his grandfather’s old fishmonger’s shop and takes pride in the seafood and Awaji beef that arrives regularly from his home region. All items are served à la carte, as Kitano wants guests to be able to enjoy exactly the food they like. Non-Italian is also available, reinforcing this message of freedom.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11113;ESPRIT C. KEI GINZA;Japan;Tokyo;11F, 7-8-17 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669273;139.762323;55;true;true;French, Contemporary;Chef Kei Kobayashi, renowned for his 3 Michelin Stars in Paris, moves onto the next stage with this harmonious blend of tradition and modernity in Ginza. Based on the concept of a ‘gourmet laboratory’, he offers à la carte dishes bursting with creativity. The C. in the restaurant name stands for both ‘cuisine’ and ‘creation’. The spirit of KEI breathes new life into French cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
11114;Haruka Murooka;Japan;Tokyo;1-21-9 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.667231;139.724668;47;false;false;Creative;Dessert prix fixe by a restaurant pâtissière. Named after the owner, ‘Haruka’ comes from ‘fragrance of spring’, expressing her desire to move guests’ souls. Generous portions of fresh fruits from producers throughout Japan brighten the palate, with a vegetable dish served between the dessert courses. Each item is a work of delicate beauty, honouring the aesthetic heritage of the chef’s sculptor father and art lecturer mother.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11115;joujouka;Japan;Tokyo;3-22-7 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0001, Japan;35.661439;139.747586;75;false;true;French;The restaurant’s name comes from an album recorded by a former guitarist of The Rolling Stones in the 1960s. The chef is not one to be swayed by fads, as his cooking attests. He pursues his own ideals in flavour, yet never strays far from the foundations of French cuisine. In roasting meats, vegetables and fish the chef prizes heat and aroma. No-nonsense, simple preparations make the results all the more impressive.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11116;KEI Collection PARIS;Japan;Tokyo;49F, Toranomon Hills Station Tower, 2-6-2 Toranomon, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-5549, Japan;35.667573;139.746882;40;false;false;French, Contemporary;A project by Kei Kobayashi – the chef who charmed the Paris culinary community. Billing his restaurant as a ‘grill with gastronomy’, he sends out his new wave in cuisine from the top of a skyscraper. In a first for him, KEI Collection PARIS focuses on à la carte items. Appetisers boast a spirit of playful creativity. Wagyu beef is grilled with grass over a traditional charcoal stove. The stylish interior and lights glittering like jewels create a real sense of being in the heart of the big city.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
11117;TRATTORIA SICILIANA Don Ciccio;Japan;Tokyo;1-2-6 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.672179;139.725466;22;false;true;Italian;‘Don Ciccio’ is the nickname of a Sicilian Cosa Nostra boss in The Godfather. Used by those close to the Don, ‘Ciccio’ means ‘broad-shouldered gentleman’. The restaurant's name reflects the chef's aspiration of becoming a beloved ‘Don’ or culinary figure. He is a pioneer, dedicated to spreading the joy of Sicilian cuisine. This ‘Don Corleone of Sicilian cuisine’ conveys the flavours of the Mediterranean with lemons and herbs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11118;Ginza Nominokoji Yamagishi;Japan;Tokyo;10F, 7-3-6 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.6703;139.760706;35;false;false;Izakaya;This izakaya was opened by one of Kyoto’s most popular kappo. Ingredients are sourced from Nishiki Market, ‘Kyoto’s kitchen’, and even the water is famed water from the ancient capital. Service begins with a set of four items, such as decoratively arranged sashimi and soup dishes, followed by à la carte items to the customer’s taste such as oden, baked gyoza dumplings and squid fried noodles. Curry rice and ramen are typical ending dishes. The shop stays open late, so drop in without worrying too much about the time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11119;Sushi Yuki;Japan;Tokyo;5-17-4 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.649819;139.720394;54;false;false;Sushi;This sushi restaurant moved to Hiroo from its original location in Yokohama’s central Kannai district. When Yuki Hayashinouchi became the shop’s third-generation owner-chef, he named it after himself. He continues the distinctive long, narrow, streamlined sushi pieces that he learned from a sushi shop in Ginza. Devotees of Hayashinouchi’s mentor can see from the chef’s comportment that the two have much in common. He infuses his individuality and character into every sushi piece he forms. The model temperament of a sushi chef.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11120;ABBESSES;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-26-17 Ebisu, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0013, Japan;35.647173;139.71557;26;false;true;French;‘Abbesses’ is the name of a train station in the Montmartre district of Paris. The damask patterns on the walls, red bench seating and antique furnishings conjure the atmosphere of a bistro from the good old days. À la carte menu items are meant for sharing. Popular items include mackerel marinated in vinegar and roast wagyu. The freshly cooked truffle soufflé omelette shares its fresh-cooked scent.;Air conditioning;[]
11122;Margotto e Baciare;Japan;Tokyo;4-2-6 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.658091;139.723452;36;false;true;Contemporary;Whole truffles are on offer here, and indeed ‘Margotto’ is a creative spelling of marugoto, ‘the whole thing’. The concept is revolutionary: guests can choose a single bead of the truffle of their liking. The chef brings his Japanese cuisine experience to bear on a base of French cuisine. Consommé of kombu dashi is poured into wine glasses, the better to enjoy its fragrance. Truffles are even paired with fried eggs on toast and raw egg on rice. Enjoy this moment of mellowness to its fullest.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11123;UNE IMMERSION;Japan;Tokyo;1-28-8 Hommachi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0071, Japan;35.680202;139.680159;15;true;true;French;The chef runs UNE IMMERSION all by himself. To control all aspects of the restaurant, from cooking to service, the lunch and dinner shifts are limited to two parties each. Prix fixe starts with carp soup. Appetiser of turnip and squid, sculpted into the shape of a white rose, is an elegantly plated homage to the restaurant where he apprenticed. A modern tapestry weaving French gastronomy with the chef’s hometown roots.;Air conditioning;[]
11125;YAUMAY;Japan;Tokyo;2F, Nijubashi Square, 3-2-3 Marunouchi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-0005, Japan;35.677693;139.761662;100;true;false;Chinese, Dim Sum;A specialist in dim sum, popular in cities around the world. The red exterior belies the classic dining experience within, which is lively on every visit. Enjoy the culture of dim sum with Chinese tea to your heart’s content. The full complement of authentic dishes includes jasmine-smoked pork, steamed scallop siu mai dumplings, steamed shrimp gyoza dumplings and rice-noodle rolls wrapped in fried tofu skin. If the weather’s nice, taking in the local ambience on the terrace is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11127;Aoyama Ototo;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 3-1-28 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.669894;139.714473;94;false;true;Japanese;Char-grilled fish and rice cooked in an iron pot are the mainstays here. Set lunches of salt-grilled mackerel and sablefish saikyo-yaki (fish marinated in white miso and grilled) are popular. In the evening, guests can choose from a selection of meats and vegetables to grill. Pickled dried Nanko-ume apricots from the chef’s native Wakayama are the perfect companion to rice. À la carte offerings are plentiful, so pairing various fish and bar snacks with sake and wine is a fun way to dine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11129;Sushi Miura;Japan;Tokyo;6-19-46 Akasaka, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0052, Japan;35.667722;139.733563;28;true;false;Sushi;The wall hanging, calligraphy by the chef’s mentor in Kyoto cuisine, says ‘forthrightness’, recalling the Buddhist exhortation to remember a sincere and honest heart at all times. Kenta Miura opened his sushi restaurant to bring his studies of Japanese cuisine to life in every sushi piece. A master of the basics, he interposes them with seasonal delicacies such as young pepper leaves with bamboo shoot and sweetfish smoked in pine needles. The career of a talented chef unfolds before you.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11130;La Lune;Japan;Tokyo;2-26-16 Higashiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0044, Japan;35.656414;139.739919;95;false;true;French;The restaurant name ‘La Lune’ is a juxtaposition: the house is the moon, and the customer is the sun. The restaurant’s glow, its proprietor says, is no more than a reflection of guests’ approval. As celestial bodies move, the seasons wheel. Flowers and herbs that garnish each plate join the ingredients in imparting a sense of season. Idiosyncratic items abound, including shrimp with carrot fondant and foie gras with grilled watermelon. Earnest perfectionism shines in every morsel.;Air conditioning;[]
11131;Watanabe Ryouri-mise;Japan;Tokyo;1-2-9 Tomioka, Koto-ku, Tokyo, 135-0047, Japan;35.671116;139.796208;25;false;true;French;A chef who is a disciple of gastronomy opened this bistro. Keen on making French cuisine accessible to a general audience, Watanabe Ryouri-mise fosters a casual atmosphere, greeting guests with à la carte offerings. French techniques are on display in the charcuterie of pâtés and hams, and in the beef cheek stewed in red wine. Seafood offerings make full use of Japan’s advantages as a country surrounded by oceans. The chef draws on his experiences and lessons from working at Toyosu Market.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11132;Jfree;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-11-7 Kagurazaka, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0825, Japan;35.701175;139.741948;40;true;true;French;French cuisine with a healthy dollop of Japanese influence, by a chef well versed in Japanese cuisine. Soup of locally raised chicken uses chicken dashi stock with char-grilled chicken thigh meat, prepared with Japanese techniques and scented with vermouth for a French sensibility. ‘Jfree’ means ‘free’ as in ‘free expression’. Prix fixe offerings centre on the bounty of Miyazaki Prefecture, dovetailing the chef’s love of good ingredients with his love of his homeland.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11133;Washoku Ebihara;Japan;Tokyo;19 Iwatocho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 162-0832, Japan;35.701574;139.737552;68;false;false;Japanese;The shopfront lettering sums up this couple’s approach: ‘Enjoy the season’. The proof is in the earnest cooking of the owner-chef and the cheerful disposition of the welcoming proprietress, his wife. Taking a page from his experience as a caterer of chakaiseki (tea ceremony cuisine with its roots in Kyoto), seasonings are both delicious and nutritious. Garnishes and pickled vegetables are inventive, teaching us that true flavour is found in the subtler notes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11134;Merachi;Japan;Tokyo;1-4-23 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661483;139.724031;79;true;true;Italian;The name means ‘creation of an artisan, pouring in heart and soul’. It was chosen to express thanks to his food producers, who grow his ingredients with care and effort. Preparations are no-nonsense, respecting the sanctity of domestic foodstuffs. Tokyo tomatoes are used to prepare sauces and mozzarella cheese from Chiba is paired with cured ham. Pastas express the joys of each season, such as pasta Genovese in summer and brown-mushroom pasta in autumn.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11136;gentil H;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 5-18-17 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.637152;139.723332;70;true;true;French;The culinary philosophy of Joël Robuchon forms the cornerstone of Keisuke Hirano’s work as a chef. In his student days, he came to appreciate the sophisticated artisanal techniques behind the most eye-catching cuisines. The velvety smoothness of the foie gras fondant is the product of painstaking research into the subtleties of texture. Eel pie is a unique creation, evolved with a French touch from a beloved confection of his native Shizuoka.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11137;Ginza Yondaime TAKAHASHIYA;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 4-12-1 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670174;139.767908;80;false;false;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;This restaurant was founded in Sugito, Saitama Prefecture, in 1873, at the dawn of the Meiji period. Charmed by the allure of Tokyo, Akihiro Takahashi, the fourth proprietor, fulfilled a dream by hanging out his shingle in Ginza. As his main store’s concept was to be an ‘eel kappo’ he serves soup dishes and decoratively arranged sashimi in the kaiseki style. Eel is freshly cut, steamed and grilled to achieve a tender texture, in the Kanto style. Dipping in egg yolks, à la sukiyaki, is one of his creative ideas.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11138;Sushi Miyuki;Japan;Tokyo;1-15-11 Shintomi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0041, Japan;35.672295;139.775016;48;false;true;Sushi;The owner-chef of Sushi Hashimoto opened this restaurant for young people to showcase the spirit and skills they learned from him. Sushi is cut thick and portioned generously. At lunchtime, only nigiri is served, but both nigiri and side dishes are offered in the evening. Hiroyuki Hashimoto keeps a watchful eye over his young charges, to see that they grow to become chefs in their own right. The name is an amalgam of one Chinese character each from Hashimoto’s parents’ names. Graceful service by artisans devoted to their craft.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11140;Courage;Japan;Tokyo;2-7-14 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.655866;139.733373;90;false;true;French;Modern French cuisine, served by the amiable owner and his chef. The chef frequently visits her producers in gratitude for their foodstuffs they provide her. She arranges her recipes according to the Japanese ingredients she obtains. Tartare of fresh fish with smoked daikon pickles and sauce accentuated with rice malt fuse Japanese and French influences. Each dish is an interplay of French culinary culture and Japanese terroir.;Air conditioning;[]
11142;Daikanyama Issai Kassai;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-5 Sarugakucho, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0033, Japan;35.652969;139.704847;56;true;true;Izakaya;The warmly lit counter catches the eye through the glass walls – so Japanese in style, yet Western in mood. Having honed his craft in New York, the chef opened this izakaya to offer Japanese fare in a casual setting. The proprietress greets guests in kimono. Sashimi is served as a mixed platter. Potato salad and steamed shrimp siu mai dumplings are perennial favourites, as is the finisher of takikomi-gohan (rice dish with soy sauce and boiled with various ingredients). Every dish bursts with playful creativity.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11143;Raisan;Japan;Tokyo;5-9-9 Yoyogi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0053, Japan;35.670912;139.687986;75;false;false;Japanese;The name derives from the masterwork of French epicure Jean Anthelme Brillat-Savarin, The Physiology of Taste, translated as Bimi Raisan. Raisan’s owner was deeply impressed by how timeless gastronomy is. His guiding purpose is to serve dishes light on salt that diners won’t weary of eating. Each dish uses a particular type of dashi stock, including shrimp, dried fish and shellfish. Raisan means ‘praise’, and we praise the warm spirit pervades the service here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11144;Noyashichi;Japan;Tokyo;2-9 Arakicho, Shinjuku-ku, Tokyo, 160-0007, Japan;35.68856;139.722445;67;true;false;Chinese;Chinese cuisine overlaid with Japanese ingredients and techniques, such as kombu kelp and dried bonito flakes, is the theme here, with Shinya Yamamoto treading an original path that blends the two. The technique of steamed chicken with spicy sauce, for example, is applied to fish sashimi, which is spiced with chilli oil. Rice cooked in clay pots is topped with Sichuan-style bean curd or stir-fried beef. Kombu kelp in clear soup is an homage to Japanese preparation. Dishes are served on Japanese serving plates, highlighting the affinity between the cuisines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11145;Noto Kanazawanosachi Ginza Furuta;Japan;Tokyo;5-10-11 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.669887;139.765457;42;true;true;Japanese;The couple in charge of this restaurant want to tell the world about the wealth of food from Ishikawa Prefecture. Fish arriving from Nanao, the proprietress’ place of birth, is prepared by her husband, the owner-chef. In addition to vinegared mozuku seaweed and rosy sea perch cooked whole, the restaurant serves mountain treats such as vegetables from Kaga and edible wild plants from the Noto Peninsula. The couple tour farms and sake breweries, building warm relations with producers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11146;Chez Olivier;Japan;Tokyo;4-1-10 Kudanminami, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 102-0074, Japan;35.691517;139.741246;81;true;true;French, Contemporary;The French-born chef named this restaurant, which means ‘Olivier’s House’. He personally selects the wines and brings out the food, treating customers like guests in his own home. He uses ingredients from both France and Japan out of his wish to be a bridge between the two countries. In autumn, diners can enjoy fusion cuisine of French escargot ravioli and Japanese awabi and mushrooms. The dishes, rich with French esprit, are also a feast for the eyes.;Air conditioning;[]
11147;SIGNATURE;Japan;Tokyo;37F, Mandarin Oriental Tokyo, 2-1-1 Nihombashimuromachi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-8328, Japan;35.687;139.773157;98;false;true;French;Pâté en croûte, fish bouillabaisse, lamb baked in pie crust: SIGNATURE breathes modern elements into recipes interwoven with French history. The chef reveres French sauces, while using herbs and vinegar for a light finish. From the dining room, decorated in blue throughout, the view is exhilarating. The service team’s pleasant demeanour also puts the mind at ease.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11148;YŌSHOKU BISTRO TŌYAMA;Japan;Tokyo;1-11-13 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.660707;139.72407;96;true;true;Yoshoku;The symbol of YŌSHOKU BISTRO TŌYAMA is a mural of Chef Tadayoshi Toyama at work in the kitchen. The interior is enfolded in warm wood panelling, the blackboard menu a touch of bistro charm. Yoshoku in ‘Yoshoku bistro’ means Western-influenced cooking, and the name references Toyama’s longstanding love affair with Western dishes and his experience studying French cuisine. The accent here is on dishes that pair well with wine. From yoshoku to French, the chef’s time and effort are rewarded with the depth of his menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11149;Le Bouton;Japan;Tokyo;2-15-1 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.661667;139.720974;86;false;true;French;‘Le Bouton’ is French for ‘the button’, and the chef loves to match dishes to wishes like buttons to buttonholes. Macaron de foie gras and pike conger pie are popular appetisers. Guests can choose salad or French fries to accompany their main dishes. Napolitan (Japanese ketchup spaghetti) and curry are not on the menu but may be available if you ask. A genuine desire to please makes this bistro a pleasure to visit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11150;CIRPAS;Japan;Tokyo;4-2-7 Shirokanedai, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 108-0071, Japan;35.639301;139.728182;91;false;true;French, Contemporary;Exploring the new path of the culinarian, chef Takashi Yoshida started using social media and has now attracted an impressive subscriber base on YouTube. The name of the restaurant is an amalgam of the ‘circulation’ of guests, producers and food culture, and the ‘passion’ that drives him. Using top-grade ingredients without compromise, Yoshida arranges traditional fare that is delightfully light on the palate.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11151;The Pizza Bar on 38th;Japan;Tokyo;38F, Mandarin Oriental Tokyo, 2-1-1 Nihombashimuromachi, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-8328, Japan;35.687041;139.773232;39;true;true;Pizza;As the name suggests, food is served at a counter, which seats just eight. Prix fixe is made possible by starting each seating at the same time. A succession of different pizzas are baked, then cut into eight, allowing diners to enjoy a slice of each type. The dough is kneaded from organic Italian wheat and rested for hours, creating a moist crust with a light texture. This is a popular place, so make your reservations early.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11152;ALTER EGO;Japan;Tokyo;2-2-32 Kandajimbocho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 101-0051, Japan;35.696305;139.757121;30;true;true;Italian;ALTER EGO is the Tokyo outpost of Yoji Tokuyoshi, who runs the main location in Milan. The walls are the same shade of green as the original, and the concept is ‘Italian food with Japanese ingredients’. Examples of their approach include frit of shiitake mushrooms coated with salted and dried grey mullet roe, and bamboo shoots brushed with fish sauce and grilled. Ingredients such as firefly squid, sakura shrimp and Yezo deer are paired with either handmade or dried pasta, depending on the texture desired.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11153;recte;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-17-5 Ebisunishi, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0021, Japan;35.648877;139.705947;16;true;true;French;‘Recte’ embodies the spirit of embracing things as they are. The chef uses hand-picked ingredients, prepared simply to showcase their vibrant flavours. The star of the show is the kamado cuisine, cooked over charcoal or wood in a traditional stone oven, or kamado. This method draws out the full potential of the ingredients with the power of far-infrared rays. Respect for nature, producers, and diners fuels the passion behind every dish.;Air conditioning;[]
11155;Waki Shun;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-4-15 Nihombashihoncho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0023, Japan;35.685984;139.775798;61;false;false;Japanese;What Shun Miyahara wants is to convey is the power and vigour of ingredients in season. His determination comes from his mentor. Pride of place on the menu goes to char-grilled items. Grilling fresh-caught fish and wagyu beef, Miyahara works the flame with constant minute adjustments, aiming for the precise moment when the flavour is fully revealed. His experiences in Paris come out in an interior blending Western design with Japanese influences, and in sparking conversations with his guests.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11156;La maison finistère;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 3-1-1 Ebisu, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0013, Japan;35.645461;139.716696;45;false;true;French;Finistère is the westernmost department  of Bretagne. Chef Tomomitsu Oki named his restaurant after this region, where he and his friends burnished their culinary skills in their youth. Duck, lamb and lobster flown in from France are prepared in classic style. Ingredients are judiciously salted, while sauces are suffused with butter and cream for depth and richness. An homage to the traditional flavours of French cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
11157;TEMPURA & WINE SHINO;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 4-2-15 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.658657;139.723552;89;true;true;Tempura;Diners enter from the ground-floor café. Ascending the staircase beside the piano takes you to a space like the darkness lit by the full moon. ‘Tempura with wine’ is the concept here, with the focus on à la carte dining, with food presentation accompanied by descriptions of the day’s tempura. Among the natural wines are those based on agricultural methods that track the movements of celestial bodies. The atmosphere is mystical, as if tilting a glass of wine in the company of the moon.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11158;LA BOTTEGAIA;Japan;Tokyo;3-12-15 Ginza, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 104-0061, Japan;35.670628;139.768806;76;true;false;Italian;Seasonal cooking and organic wine heighten the appeal of this Italian fare. Japanese ingredients enliven dishes such as ravioli of clam and bamboo shoot and spaghetti of milt and dried mullet roe. From his experience in French cuisine, the chef favours sauces suffused with vermouth and port, serving as perfect complements to the wines. Many wines are available by the glass, and the owner-sommelier, a disciple of Italian cuisine, takes care to suggest the best pairings.;Air conditioning;[]
11159;OLD NEPAL;Japan;Tokyo;1-42-11 Gotokuji, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 154-0021, Japan;35.654689;139.647786;67;false;true;Nepali;The restaurant’s name is a shout-out to the culinary culture of Nepal in the good old days. Street scenes of the capital Kathmandu adorn the walls. Keen to convey the mood of old Nepal, the chef uses his own experiences to spin tales on the theme of journeys. Of particular note in his set menu is the creative flair of appetisers. They’re followed by Dal bhat, a dish enjoyed by mixing the flavours of lentil soup, rice and curries – a Nepalese journey of the palate.;Air conditioning;[]
11160;Ăn Ði;Japan;Tokyo;3-42-12 Jingumae, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0001, Japan;35.671901;139.713897;70;true;true;Vietnamese;Modern Vietnamese food from a chef trained in French cuisine. Ăn Ði combines seasonal Japanese ingredients with bánh xèo, raw spring rolls and phở to express the four seasons of Japan with Vietnamese cuisine. With a skilled sommelier at the helm, you can also expect perfect pairings that elevate each dish. The emphasis is on natural wines, but the restaurant also showcases a modern approach to pairing sake and shochu. The restaurant name means '’Bon appétit!’ in Vietnamese.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
11161;MAISON MARUNOUCHI;Japan;Tokyo;7F, Four Seasons Hotel Tokyo at Marunouchi, 1-11-1 Marunouchi, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo, 100-6277, Japan;35.678083;139.767155;23;false;true;French;Casual French dining overseen by Chef Daniel Calvert of SÉZANNE. Both prix fixe and à la carte offerings are served at lunch as well as dinner, so guests are spoiled for choice. Everyday bistro fare such as chicken-liver pâté, confit of pork belly and beef steak are raised to the height of elegance. Floor-to-ceiling windows afford sweeping views of the shinkansen bullet trains passing through Tokyo Station and the office towers of Marunouchi.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
11162;L'EAU;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 2-14-14 Minamiaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0062, Japan;35.670162;139.720212;56;true;true;French;The whole restaurant is a canvas on which Takamitsu Shimizu expresses his love of nature. Driftwood and charcoal adorn the stone walls and the cuisine celebrates the seasons, stirring the senses. ‘Water, Leaf, Soil, Tree,’ an amuse bouche, drives this concept home. On dishes moulded in the shapes of mosses and plants are served bite-sized pieces of the bounty of mountain and sea. The appeal of each producing region and producer is on display here, appreciated through the chef’s own filter.;Air conditioning;[]
11163;Tomidokoro;Japan;Tokyo;6-13-3 Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0004, Japan;35.661905;139.754083;77;false;false;Sushi;A place to feed on sushi to your heart’s content. The owner-chef, a man of few words, focuses strictly on sushi to maintain the proper tempo. True to his Obihiro roots, he cooks ancient varieties of Hokkaido rice in a broad-brimmed hagama pot. Fish is cut thick, so guests can enjoy the flavour to the fullest, and vinegared rice servings are generous to match. Standard lunchtime items are a bargain. The chef is generous both in sushi and in spirit.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
11164;Ristorante HONDA;Japan;Tokyo;2-12-35 Kitaaoyama, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 107-0061, Japan;35.670285;139.714502;86;true;false;Italian;Seasonal foodstuffs are the theme at this modern Italian restaurant. Tetsuya Honda’s culinary creations link the traditional cuisine of Italy with the seasons of Japan. The speciality, ‘Sea Urchin Tagliolini’, uses no cream, relying instead on lashings of sea urchin to achieve a rich, satisfying flavour. Honda strives to elicit the flavour of each ingredient.;Air conditioning;[]
11166;Soan Mitate;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 2-8-12 Azabujuban, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0045, Japan;35.65539;139.73423;25;true;true;Soba;Mitate means ‘the three freshes’: freshly ground, freshly kneaded and freshly boiled. Like the chef, most of the ingredients come from Toyama, and his experience with Japanese cuisine is evident. The set menu includes buckwheat-flour galettes of tuna and caviar as well as an assortment of delicacies served before the soba, which is are slender, cleanly cut 100% buckwheat noodles. Watching his practiced movements as he prepares the soba is an added entertainment. An impressive list of champagnes is also offered.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11168;Ji-Cube;Japan;Tokyo;3-18-10 Nishiazabu, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0031, Japan;35.659126;139.726065;43;false;false;Chinese;Ji-Cube aspires to create Chinese cuisine that could only be made in Japan, using Japanese ingredients. For example, dim sum is dressed with sauces of sudachi and yuzu, two characteristically Japanese citrus fruits. Jellyfish salad paired with daikon smoked like iburigakko (smoked daikon pickles from Akita) is an intriguing innovation. The chef’s devotion to polishing his skills in Sichuan cooking shines in his mastery of cooking with Sichuan pepper and chilli pepper. Milt in mapo sauce is a dish to enjoy in winter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11169;Shiomachi;Japan;Tokyo;2F, 1-34-10 Uehara, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0064, Japan;35.669414;139.681984;68;false;false;Izakaya;‘Shiomachi’ means waiting for the right tide to push out to sea. The name expresses the owner-chef’s wish to create a shop where people congregate, just as fishermen gather to await favourable conditions. Yearning for the sea, the chef was drawn to a job where he handles fish. He visits Toyosu Market daily, ever on the lookout for that once-in-a-lifetime catch. He chats with brokers as he makes purchases and drains fish of blood to preserve freshness. Gather here to enjoy your fill of high-quality fish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11170;SŌWADŌ;Japan;Tokyo;1-12-15 Hiro, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 150-0012, Japan;35.647992;139.715191;15;false;true;Izakaya;SŌWADŌ is just past Ebisu Bridge, which crosses the Shibuya River, but there is no sign. Pass through a cheerless grey corridor, then be greeted by cooks in crisp whites working in a lively interior. The eye is drawn to the ‘Genshiyaki’, skewers of fish and meat grilled slowly over a charcoal brazier as in ancient times. We recommend the dishes with which the chef feels a special connection: Unzen ham cutlet, nanbanzuke and steamed squid dumpling, for example. All are from Kyushu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11171;Sushi Ikki;Japan;Tokyo;2-29-21 Sakuragaoka, Setagaya-ku, Tokyo, 156-0054, Japan;35.646766;139.624571;28;false;true;Sushi;The menu is a judicious balance of sushi and other Japanese dishes. The meal begins with meticulously refined sesame tofu and bowls of basic soup stock. To vary the tone, the sushi is interspersed with savoury egg custard and flame-broiled offerings. For the first piece, Chef Takafumi Kiyonaga likes to serve young Pacific sea bream, demonstrating the marination, knife techniques and other aspects that make up his craft. Red-fleshed fish is paired with mustard and conger eel with pepper, testifying to the influence of other types of Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11172;à table;Japan;Tokyo;3-1-1 Yushima, Bunkyo-ku, Tokyo, 113-0034, Japan;35.703002;139.767999;17;true;true;French;Owner-chef Yoichi Nakaaki pours his heart into creating cuisine that would win the approval of a person from France, the land of epicures. His classic dishes such as pâté en croûte, roast lamb and tarte Tatin are the result of painstaking research. He is especially adept at preparations of fillings, such as pigeon, foie gras and game, wrapped in pastry and dressed in sauces. Dishes here are meant for two, so reservations are for two people or more.;Air conditioning;[]
11173;farsi largo!;Japan;Tokyo;B1F, 1-4-3 Nihombashihoncho, Chuo-ku, Tokyo, 103-0023, Japan;35.686248;139.775637;19;true;false;Italian;The Italian-trained chef runs this restaurant with his wife. A chance encounter with a fishmonger in Shizuoka Prefecture made the seafood of Suruga Bay the star of this show. One fish dish after another is served, from fried fish to soup and carpaccio. Panna cotta of black truffle comes from the chef’s experiences in Piedmont. The name of the restaurant means ‘blaze your own trail’, and the cuisine wordlessly conveys the chef’s single-minded passion.;Air conditioning;[]
11174;Kyoryori Aun;Japan;Tokyo;1-33-6 Tomigaya, Shibuya-ku, Tokyo, 151-0063, Japan;35.666613;139.688158;56;false;true;Japanese;Seasonal menus are supported by dashi broth drawn from ripened Rishiri kombu. Chef Eiji Onoyama uses dashi in everything, from appetizers to the final takikomi-gohan, rice seasoned with various ingredients. sashimi dishes are prepared in a jellied dashi broth style. They may be complemented with ume or nori seaweed, depending on the type of fish. Egg-yolk soy sauce is the secret ingredient that brings out the umami in tuna sushi. While the soup and takiawase add inflection, the focus is on the power of dashi broth to accentuate the flavour of the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11175;ROPPONGI RIAN;Japan;Tokyo;4F, 6-2-6 Roppongi, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 106-0032, Japan;35.66194;139.730759;73;false;true;Japanese;The concept of this kappo is ‘as much as you want of what you want’. Seasonal fruits and vegetables are lined up on the counter, ready to be cooked by your preferred method. The head chef honed his craft in Kyoto, so he uses rice and water from Kyotango. Pike conger and oysters are sourced from Nagasaki, reflecting his Amakusa roots. The champon served to close out the meal is a recipe from his mother, who runs a shop specialising in this noodle dish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11176;Edomae Shibahama;Japan;Tokyo;2-22-23 Shiba, Minato-ku, Tokyo, 105-0014, Japan;35.651428;139.750523;86;false;false;Japanese;A stylish eatery serving the popular fare of Edo. To discover the original dishes of the city, Hiroshi Kaibara dived deep into the literature. ‘Mukimi-kiriboshi’ (dried daikon strips in clam soup stock), a staple of the restaurant, was widely enjoyed during the late Edo period as a favourite to pair with rice. Shiba shrimp, so named because it was originally caught in Shiba inlet, is served in soup as a fishcake. Soup stock brewed from dried bonito flakes, without using kombu, is another traditional taste of Edo cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11177;Qiao Dong Bei;China Mainland;Beijing;No. 01-03, Office Tower C2, Podium, The Malls At Oriental Plaza, 1 East Chang'an Avenue, Dongcheng, Beijing, 100738, China Mainland;39.88985;116.36171;85;true;true;Dongbei;This place stands out from the crowd of typical Dongbei restaurants with its modern decor done out in red and white, and servers in tailored suits. That said, the food is unmistakably Dongbei, covering recipes from Heilongjiang, Liaoning and Jilin, albeit in smaller portions and finer presentations. In addition to classics such as fried pork loin in sweet and sour sauce, and pork stew with pickled cabbage, try rare culinary gems such as crayfish "tofu".;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
11178;Fujian Restaurant;China Mainland;Beijing;6F, Xiamenair Jianianhua Hotel, 16 Lize Road, Fengtai, Beijing, 100073, China Mainland;39.871317;116.341943;90;true;true;Fujian;From the décor to the food, this restaurant celebrates Fujian culture. In the absence of a main dining area, diners need to book one of the 13 private rooms and pre-order a set menu. To ensure authenticity, the all-Fujianese kitchen team insists on most ingredients being flown in daily from their home province. Signatures include braised eel with red mushrooms, pork cheek braised with dried squid, and sliced clam blanched in chicken stock.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11179;Rong Pao;China Mainland;Beijing;2F, The Ritz-Carlton Hotel, 83A Jianguo Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9093239;116.4746892;24;false;true;Sichuan;This brand under the Xin Rong Ji group specialises in Sichuan fare, in particular cuisine from Yibin, the home city of the chef. He doesn't hold back on the use of fiery chillies and even makes his own cured bacon in-house. River fish and quick-fried dishes are the biggest draw. With its deep fiery heat, the plateau loach hot pot with green Sichuan peppercorns on the vine is a hit. The quick-fried pork liver and kidney is another must-try.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11180;Xin Ming Yuen;China Mainland;Beijing;Unit L1-12, 1F, Tower C, Parkview Green Fangcaodi, 9 Dongdaqiao Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.918261;116.441901;77;true;true;Cantonese;The spacious room in a large-scale shopping mall blends contrasting modern details and oriental motifs. The veteran chef is keen to craft refined, authentic Cantonese dishes using traditional techniques. The concise menu offers a wide range of Cantonese classics, such as roast meat, stir-fries, seafood and double-boiled soups. Crispy skin chicken, and osmanthus scrambled egg with conpoy stand out in particular. Warm, thoughtful service.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11181;Horizon;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Kerry Hotel, 1 Guanghua Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.912572;116.452606;94;false;false;Cantonese;The head chef here has been working in Beijing’s prestigious hotels and boasts over 30 years of experience. His signature date-wood roast duck speaks volumes about his exceptional culinary acumen. Other timeless classics, novelty creations and the stellar array of appetisers paint a colourful tapestry of Cantonese food. Experience the authentic ‘yum cha’ culture down south with dim sum made by Cantonese chefs at lunch.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11182;Meng Du Hui;China Mainland;Beijing;Block B, Wan Shou Hotel, 12A Wanshou Road, Haidian, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9107582;116.2879479;26;false;true;Hui Cuisine;Run by a team from Anhui, this restaurant opened its doors in 2023. The two-storey architecture seamlessly melds classical Anhui style and modern touches. The kitchen team imports most ingredients from Anhui for maximum authenticity. The signature dish, braised Huizhou smelly mandarin fish, is fermented in a wooden barrel for one month and boasts firm flesh and unique briny umami. In addition to the á la carte menu, check out the seasonal offerings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
11184;Chao Shang Chao (Xicheng);China Mainland;Beijing;Basement Level, Winland IFC, 7 Jinrong Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9191004;116.351839;27;false;true;Chao Zhou;This upmarket Chaozhou restaurant is another gem in the F&B chain. Hailing from Chaozhou, Chef Gu has been cooking professionally for over 30 years. His menu is based on tradition but pervaded by a sense of creativity. The boneless pigeon stuffed with bird's nest in matsutake broth delivers amazing layers of textures. Shaobing flatbread baked in a clay oven and stuffed with pig's trotter meat, coriander, pickles and green pepper is a solid backup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11185;The Tasty House;China Mainland;Beijing;Block 21, 4 Gongrentiyuchang North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9305253;116.4524691;45;true;false;Jiangzhe;Set in Jing Yard, a tree-lined recreational complex in a converted heritage factory site, this elegant restaurant is a subtle nod to the building's industrial past. Thanks to a skylight on the gable wall and glass doors, the space is flooded with natural light. The large menu is dominated by Jiangnan cuisine, with signature dishes from Guangdong, Chaozhou and Sichuan. Try the crispy Peking duck roasted over jujube wood. There are five private rooms. Be sure to book ahead.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11186;Yue Jie (Qi Yang Road);China Mainland;Beijing;Shop 204, 2F, Radiance Edifice, 2 Qiyang Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;40.0016645;116.4828328;24;false;true;Cantonese;With stints in top establishments, the executive chef from Guangdong leads the kitchen team as it rolls out a lineup of Cantonese classics. Items like double-boiled soup and Cantonese barbecue need pre-ordering. Dried tangerine peel is a recurring theme on the menu – try deep-fried pork spareribs with Xinhui dried tangerine peel for rounded citrus warmth. Whelk slices and fish maw soup, slow-cooked for six hours, seduces with depth and umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
11187;Yu De Fu (Dongzhimennei Street);China Mainland;Beijing;264 Dongzhimennei Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.93938;116.41201;31;true;false;Hotpot;This owner was once responsible for some of the nation’s most acclaimed banquets and now his protégés run this tiny gem with only six tables. It prides itself on the four special cuts of Mongolian sheep, to be blanched in a copper steamboat heated by red-hot charcoal. Hand-sliced lamb is tender and flavourful, while those averse to mutton may order such rare cuts of beef as the aorta. In addition to hotpot, the menu also flaunts other worthy options.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11188;Rive Gauche;China Mainland;Beijing;2F, The Puxuan Hotel, 1 Wangfujing Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.904713;116.407258;81;false;true;French Contemporary;Inspired by the arty Left Bank of Paris, this dining room is modern and chic. Gallic techniques and recipes hold no secrets for the seasoned head chef from Hong Kong and the six-course tasting menu is a great way to experience his culinary vision. Deceptively simple at first glance, each dish features complex flavours and textures, as well as bold Chinese twists – such as butter flavoured fermented bean curd or longjing tea panna cotta.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11189;Jia (Chaoyang);China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Nuo Hotel, 2A Jiangtai Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.975138;116.474095;56;true;false;Cantonese;Chandeliers add visual appeal to the high-ceilinged room with ink murals and carved wood windows. The menu is predominantly Cantonese, borrowing occasionally from other provinces. The Cantonese kitchen team delivers authentic flavours in signatures such as sautéed grouper fillet with green chilli and wild rice stems. The slow-boiled soup menu on daily rotation is also worth checking out. At lunchtime, try the tofu skin roll with shrimp filling.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11191;Qu Lang Yuan;China Mainland;Beijing;25 Dongsi 11th Alley, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.933086;116.418056;38;false;true;Innovative;You'll find this chic and charmingly run sanctuary in an award-winning remodelled courtyard house amid a bustling neighbourhood. The architecture effortlessly blends history with modernism, encompassing motifs from the north and south. Its food is equally striking. To realise her vision, the young chef uses local ingredients for an original dining experience. The wine list offers interesting Chinese choices by the glass, while by-the-bottle options from around the world abound.;Air conditioning;[]
11192;Wolfgang's Steakhouse (Gongrentiyuchang North Road);China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Space 8, Pacific Century Place, 2A Gongrentiyuchang North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.930849;116.452189;18;false;false;Steakhouse;This outpost of the namesake institution in New York City is furnished in classic American-style with burgundy leather chairs and dim, warm lighting. The menu and recipes are essentially the same as its Manhattan flagship, where the chefs and manager were trained to ensure the same standard of service across the board. USDA prime Angus steaks are dry-aged for at least 28 days and its signature crab cake will send your palate into overdrive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11193;Héritage East;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Block 66, 1 Zhongguancun South Street, Haidian, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9651564;116.3147777;18;true;true;Chinese Contemporary;Exquisite artwork and elaborate wainscoting set the scene for a dining experience that is the epitome of stylish, even down to the hand-painted tableware. The restaurant prefers to customise menus to diners’ tastes ahead of time, but à la carte choices also abound. Top notch ingredients are deftly crafted with spot-on seasoning and outstanding wok hei. During the mushroom season, try the sautéed lurid bolete with wrinkly chillies.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11194;Maison Flo;China Mainland;Beijing;18 Xiaoyun Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.964309;116.470555;77;false;false;French;It’s out of the way and you need a taxi to get here. But when you see the vast patio and grand dining room styled after the archetypal Parisian brasserie circa 1900s, its suburban address will make sense instantly. On the menu, French classics take precedence – escargots, steak tartare, confit de canard, baba au rhum – though their seafood platter is also popular. Charming table service makes dishes like côte de bœuf and crêpes Suzette stand out.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11195;Mio;China Mainland;Beijing;3F, Four Seasons Hotel, 48 Liangmaqiao Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.95071;116.4672;77;false;true;Italian;Despite its discreet entrance, the lavish dining room will take your breath away: strings of glass beads draped from the mirrored ceiling form a dazzling sculpture that spans the room’s length. The head chef champions a seasonally driven menu complete with modern techniques and aesthetics, but with a nod to Italian traditions. Boston lobster paccheri, for instance, is cooked to perfection, complemented by dried cherry tomatoes and basil pesto.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11196;Fortune Long Beijing Bean Sauce Noodles (East Xinglong Street);China Mainland;Beijing;56 East Xinglong Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.895633;116.408905;45;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;Since 1994, this restaurant has been synonymous with authentic zhajiangmian. It moved to this three-storey location over ten years ago and is always jam-packed. Once you step in the shop, you can’t miss the two caldrons of rich and flavoursome soybean sauce made fresh every day, to be served on the side with house-made noodles. Beijing snacks such as fried pork balls, and blanched ox tripe in sesame sauce are other solid options.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11197;Nishiki;China Mainland;Beijing;L303, 3F, CP Center, 20 Jinhe East Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9116034;116.4618984;83;true;false;Japanese;After the success of Andō in Hong Kong, Argentinian chef Agustin Balbi took up the role of consultant for Nishiki. The season-driven menu is essentially Japanese with hints of European influences. The four set menus feature 10-plus courses made with the freshest catch and top-tier produce from around the world. Wine pairings are available, sometimes with rare finds. Besides private rooms of various sizes, the six counter seats are much sought after.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11198;San Qing Tan (Sanlitun Road);China Mainland;Beijing;NLG-09A, B1 Level, Taikoo Li Sanlitun North, Sanlitun Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.93694;116.44928;67;true;true;Cantonese;No trip to Beijing is complete without trying the iconic roast duck. Cantonese roast goose, albeit harder to come by, is actually a nice alternative. Geese, chilled not frozen, are shipped to this spot from Guangdong and you may specify fattier or leaner cuts. Honey goose liver, and marinated goose head, web and wings are also worth a try. Don’t miss the Cantonese classics like double-boiled soups and dim sum. The goose and soups must be pre-ordered.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11199;1949 - Duck de Chine;China Mainland;Beijing;98 Jinbao Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9109245;116.4133837;39;false;true;Cantonese;As you set foot in this courtyard house-turned-restaurant, it’s hard to miss the life-size terracotta soldiers, painted beams and red pillars . All of these decorative elements impart a majestic feel befitting its imperial speciality – Peking duck – served to the banging of a gong. While a crossbreed between Cherry Valley and local white duck is roasting over date wood, tease your appetite with deep-fried king oyster mushrooms and mustard duck web.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11200;Café Zi;China Mainland;Beijing;5F, Mandarin Oriental Wangfujing, 269 Wangfujing Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.91231;116.405045;68;false;false;Cantonese;This stylish cafe tells a narrative that is less to do with pushing boundaries and more focused on celebrating traditions. Its concise menu stars all of Canton’s culinary hits – seafood, stir fries, soups… you name it! Each dish rustled up by the veteran kitchen team showcases their shrewd judgment. Also try the refreshing cocktails, interestingly infused with Chinese tea. The views of the Forbidden City from the roof-terrace are also a plus!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11201;Chef 1996;China Mainland;Beijing;4A Jiangtaiwa, Xinghuo East Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.958147;116.517802;75;false;false;Sichuan;Slightly out of the way, this private rooms-only restaurant sits amid bamboo lined alleys and boasts an alfresco lounge, whose outdoor misting system creates an otherworldly aura. The menu features painstakingly prepared gems like camphor wood-smoked duck with crispy skin and smoky depth, as well as dishes that intelligently include house-made pickles and sauces. Exquisitely plated Kung Pao prawns burst with fruity spices and a hint of sweetness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11202;La Roba;China Mainland;Beijing;Building 7, Zaojun West Lane, Zaojunmiao Road, Haidian, Beijing, China Mainland;39.96485;116.341314;62;true;false;Yunnanese;The owner has paid tribute to his ethnic roots by naming his restaurant, La Roba, after a subgroup of the Nuosu tribe in Yunnan. The exotic ethnic flair is manifest on every level from the decor and artwork to the waiters’ outfits and background music. The menu features all Yunnan’s classic dishes, such as the deliciously chewy millefeuille pea flour pancake. The Dali-style fish braised in pickled papaya is tart, fruity and appetising. Expect to queue at peak periods.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11203;Country Kitchen;China Mainland;Beijing;3F, Rosewood Hotel, Jing Guang Centre, Hujialou, 1 Chaoyangmenwai Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.918808;116.454181;91;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;Reclaimed bricks, vintage ceramics and wood stoves impart rustic flair. Despite the panoramic views, your attention may be drawn to the spectacle of the chefs at work in the open kitchen. Rows of chestnut-fed Huairou ducks, prized for their unique nutty sweetness, are grilled in a display oven. Well versed in Beijing and Shandong cooking, the chef presents a menu rife with distinctive Northern charm. Try the Beijing classic of crispy pork belly, too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11204;Hong 0871;China Mainland;Beijing;Building 6, E9 Zone Innovation Works, Shuangshu North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.909;116.3892;44;true;false;Yunnanese;Nestled in an industrial park, Hong 0871 is a bit out of the way. But that doesn’t stop gastronomes from making a trip there for their refined Yunnanese food deeply rooted in traditions but updated with creative twists. Most ingredients are shipped from Yunnan and the menu changes regularly. But try stewed pig skin with red bean and preserved vegetable when it’s available: gelatinous pig skin soaking up the flavourful sauces is truly decadent.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11205;Mansion Xún;China Mainland;Beijing;85 Beilucaoyuan Hutong, Qianmen Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.8937823;116.3985319;61;false;false;Jiangzhe;Inside this seemingly typical courtyard house in an old town back street, the sleek, modern and well-appointed private rooms come as a pleasant surprise. Mansion Xún prides itself on meticulous one-on-one service and set menus that showcase the season's best seafood, like stir-fried white crabmeat. Their signature steamed chicken in scallion oil has gelatinous skin and umami-loaded meat. The couches in the courtyard are the best spot for afternoon tea.;Valet parking;[]
11206;Bad Ass Lamb Hot Pot (Maizidian West Street);China Mainland;Beijing;39 Maizidian West Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9535491;116.473461;78;true;false;Hotpot;The restaurant offers a smorgasbord of 15 cuts of lamb, and despite its name, dishes offered here are anything but "bad". While you may see hand-sliced lamb on almost every table, lamb shin tastes less greasy and more velvety after being swished for seconds in a broth of your choice. The blanched head is also a nice surprise with thin slices of juicy meat seasoned with cumin. Malabar spinach and kelp are delicious and provide a healthy dose of dietary fibre.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
11207;Exquisite Bocuse;China Mainland;Beijing;4F, Sanxing Tower, 31 Jinghui Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.91037;116.468615;96;true;true;Cantonese;The modern room sports muted neutral tones and wood with occasional splashes of red and motifs depicting the Great Wall of China. The menu is basically Cantonese with the odd Jiangzhe accents. Try braised Iberico pork in Shanghainese wine-infused soy sauce or poached free-range chicken boasting springy skin and silky flesh. Both are sourced from an organic farm on Chongming Island owned by the restaurant group.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11208;Top Feast (East Chang'an Street);China Mainland;Beijing;UG Level, Grand Hyatt Beijing, 1 East Chang'an Street, Dongcheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.90845;116.408443;87;true;false;Cantonese;With abalone as its self-proclaimed theme, Top Feast not only serves a variety of dishes made with the treasured shellfish, but also displays an impressive collection of dried abalones from around the world. The butler will customise the menu to diners' liking. Try the chargrilled abalone with goose liver, flambéed tableside. Those without deep pockets can opt for the set menus of regional flavours or the Cantonese à la carte. Extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11209;Ji Chuan;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Atour Hotel, 2A West Dawang Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9138604;116.4721293;56;true;true;Sichuan;The chef champions a novel Sichuan cuisine based heavily on Chongqing cooking. Expect an intense tingly numbness in the mouth from signatures such as mapo tofu with marbled beef or the appetiser of pickled chillies with peach kernels. To quench the burn, round off the meal with bingfen – an iced dessert made with shoofly seed jelly, seasonal fruits, distillers' grains and red beans. The array of alcoholic drinks will also put out the flames.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
11210;Bistro Strong (Chaoyanggongyuan Road);China Mainland;Beijing;M175, SOLANA, 6 Chaoyanggongyuan Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9489357;116.4705617;66;false;false;Meats and Grills;This bistro specialising in lamb dishes has a small menu featuring different cuts from Mongolia, all aged in the house. Here, lamb is prepared in a myriad of ways: mini lamb pie is made with porcini, truffle oil and parmesan in a vol-au-vent, while lamb skewer uses dry-aged hind leg meat alternated with fat. You may even order a lamb chop on the barbecue. Signature cocktails that call for air-dried lamb or lamb ricotta are also ingenious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
11211;Qian Li;China Mainland;Beijing;D5202, 5F, SKP Beijing, 87 Jianguo Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.909316;116.473274;91;false;false;Taizhou;Qian Li opened in a shopping mall in 2021 to serve various Taizhou dishes at wallet-friendly prices. Fresh seafood is shipped from Taizhou daily to ensure freshness and a good variety. The must-tries include yellow croaker and fish maw thick soup that tastes briny-sweet, rich and deep. Seasonal offerings such as promfet, Bombay duck and white crab are also keenly sought after. Booth seating offers some privacy, or book one of the two private rooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
11214;Fu Man Yuan (Xinyuanli);China Mainland;Beijing;No. 102, 1F, Block 2, Kunsha Center, 16 Xinyuanli, Xindong Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.94049;116.44426;68;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;A household name for traditional Beijing home cooking since 1994, this branch is directly opposite the flagship. Its glass façade and sleek architecture set a contemporary tone. The dishes may not be attention-grabbing, but are skillfully made with fresh ingredients and are very reasonably priced. Try braised Zhoushan hairtail for its extra-fine flesh in a mildly sweet sauce, or the silky, flavourful braised tofu with fish roe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
11215;Les Morilles;China Mainland;Beijing;1F, Sunflower Tower, 37 Maizidian Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.947469;116.465147;82;false;true;French Contemporary;The pared-back, uncluttered interior of this little gem tucked away on the ground-floor of an apartment block by Liangma River provides the perfect foil to modern French cuisine, characterised by top-notch ingredients, precise techniques and bold flavours. Dishes are exquisitely plated and reflect the dedication of the entire team. There are two set dinner menus to choose from with optional wine pairings. Save room for the decadent Galette des Rois dessert.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11217;L. Bodhi (Guanghua Road);China Mainland;Beijing;No. 202, Building F, Sunshine 100 International Department, 2 Guanghua Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9119421;116.4696544;65;true;true;Vegetarian;This branch of the chain restaurant serves three different nine-course vegan sets at various price points. Emphasising holistic well-being, both physical and emotional, the mindfully designed sets cover amuse-bouches, appetisers, hot mains, hot pot, salad, staple starch and dessert. No sign of greasy or heavily processed food here! Instead, organic produce is treated with a light touch so the natural flavours shine.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11218;Char (South Sanlitun Road);China Mainland;Beijing;3F, InterContinental Sanlitun Hotel, Topwin Mall, 1 South Sanlitun Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.933357;116.445098;30;false;true;Steakhouse;After passing through a red neon tunnel, diners are greeted by a copper cow sculpture that sets the scene for a beef-focused feast against panoramic views of the bustling Sanlitun area. Larger steak cuts for sharing, such as David Blackmore’s Australian Wagyu, Porterhouse and Tomahawk steaks, are portioned on individual plates tableside. The signature array of salt and mustard is equally impressive. Ask for a table on the terrace for the ultimate alfresco experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11219;Amico BJ;China Mainland;Beijing;Shop 109, 1F, Pacific Century Place, 2A Gongrentiyuchang North Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9311888;116.4532782;100;true;false;European Contemporary;Exposed, unfinished flakeboard in an upmarket restaurant? The passionate owner-chef has used the construction material to great effects in this intimate and stylish dining room. Omakase menus offer six to eight creative courses firmly rooted in Italian traditions, but with Japanese twists. The chef’s highly original recipes fare well with precise judgment and astute handling. The eight counter seats are the most prized spots to watch the alchemy unfold.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
11220;Everlasting Happiness;China Mainland;Beijing;F101-111, No.39 Capital Xindadu, 21 Chegongzhuang Street, Xicheng, Beijing, China Mainland;39.9318522;116.3302795;80;false;false;Hunanese;For over 20 years, the brand has been a celebrated institution, both within and beyond Hunan. Its first outpost in Beijing greets diners with a bright red entrance, a visual clue to its hot fiery food. The must-try fried pork loin with crackling delivers fascinating textures and rich flavours. Rice paddy eel flown in from Hunan is slaughtered the same day before being stewed in shiso leaves and pickled mustard greens. The in-house preserved meat is also worth trying.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11221;Beef & Dumplings;China Mainland;Beijing;5 Shunyuan Street, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.951851;116.451772;90;false;true;Dumplings;The shop’s name is quite self-explanatory. Different cuts of beef such as shin, tripe and tendon are braised in a spiced soy marinade for over ten hours resulting in robust flavours and tenderness, but without being too mushy. Beef and pork dumplings are made on the spot with house-made wrapping. Feel free to choose your favourite toppings and vinegar dips from the self-serve condiment station. Braised beef is also available for take-out.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11222;Xiang Shang Xiang (Jinhe East Road);China Mainland;Beijing;L301A-L302A, 3F, CP Center, 20 Jinhe East Road, Chaoyang, Beijing, China Mainland;39.910992;116.461892;87;false;false;Hunanese;The chain now runs a few establishments in Beijing and Chengdu, but the story started in 2021 at this very first outlet. A veteran with 20-plus years of experience under his belt, Chef Peng revamps the menu every now and then to keep it fresh. He presents a good-value set menu featuring 24 different chilli peppers – heaven for spicy food lovers. The butler, tea master and sommelier go the extra mile to deliver thoughtful, meticulous service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
11224;Ratatouille;Netherlands;Harderwijk;Vischmarkt 6, Harderwijk, 3841 BG, Netherlands;52.3516407;5.6181997;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Ratatouille is cosy and convivial, and its spacious terrace on the historical Vischmarkt is understandably very popular. Hostess Cindy and chef Gerwin have gained a loyal following in a short period of time, and that is more than deserved. Whether you order à la carte or take a punt on the surprise menu, the value for money is second to none. The versatile chef is just as likely to serve up an oven-baked fillet of red mullet with a rich white wine sauce and a zingy antiboise as a vegetarian pie with sweet and sour nuances. His cuisine is sophisticated and very much on trend, and he puts a lot of thought into his vegetable accoutrements and his choice of suppliers.;Terrace;[]
11225;Bar Beurre;Netherlands;Maastricht;Sint Pieterstraat 54, Maastricht, 6211 JP, Netherlands;50.844998;5.6918228;44;true;true;French;Once a traditional café, this place is now a no-nonsense bistro, complete with upbeat background music. Bar Beurre certainly lives up to its name. Just like in traditional French cooking, butter (beurre) is a key ingredient here, but this cuisine is not at all lacking in sophistication. For example, the chef uses it to prepare megrim à la meunière, which he serves with anchovies, broad beans and an exquisite beurre blanc finished with a dash of sherry. The short menu features dishes that are bold and playful. Le beurre, c'est la vie!;Terrace;[]
11226;On Cru;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Haringvliet 92B, Rotterdam, 3011 TH, Netherlands;51.9193385;4.4943376;18;true;true;Farm to table;Housed in a listed building, this restaurant with its exposed brick walls is reminiscent of old England. Think Chesterfield chairs, a striking semi-circular counter and dimmed lighting. Kelvin de Pijper's classic market-fresh cuisine lets the ingredients take centre stage, for example, pairing freshly caught cod with a velvety creamed sauce made with fish fumet. Crispy sweetbreads are given a glossy finish with a veal reduction infused with cardamom, lovage and pink peppercorns. This chef honours the natural flavours of the produce while adding subtle, measured nuances. A real gem at the picturesque old port.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11228;River Bar;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Westerkade 8, Rotterdam, 3016 CL, Netherlands;51.9059096;4.4776105;57;true;true;Modern French;The maritime decor inside this striking oval pavilion is indeed enchanting, yet one of its main draws is the view of the Nieuwe Maas River. As you soak up the vibrant atmosphere and watch the cruise ships dock, you can choose from a fine selection of wines by the glass and the European-inspired menu. Eschewing any unnecessary frills, the chef comes up with some truly original dishes. His repertoire includes perfectly cooked Mediterranean-style turbot, foie gras as rich as anywhere in France – and even beef Wellington! The wide selection promises a delightful culinary journey along Europe's rivers.;Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
11229;De Vijverhoeve;Netherlands;Sint Anna ter Muiden;Greveningseweg 2, Sint Anna ter Muiden, 4524 JK, Netherlands;51.3132112;3.3652258;55;false;true;Classic Cuisine;The rustic charm of this little farmhouse and the beautiful French garden demonstrate the passion with which chef Bart Grahame runs his family restaurant. This ambitious chef serves generous dishes made from top-quality ingredients and home produce, accompanied by delicious sauces that show off his classical expertise. A good place to eat after a visit to nearby Sluis.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11230;Kasteel Elsloo;Netherlands;Elsloo;Maasberg 1, Elsloo, 6181 GV, Netherlands;50.9475569;5.7576131;24;true;true;Country cooking;Dining in a castle makes for a special experience. The surrounding natural beauty and centuries-old arcades beneath which guests take their seats cannot fail to impress. This fabulous setting inspires the chef to work with respect for the region, the seasons and sustainability. French and Mediterranean flavours dominate the appealingly updated menu, which now features occasionally innovative dishes. Wine lovers will delight in the enticing selection of wines sold by the glass.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11231;Onglet;Netherlands;Maastricht;Wycker Brugstraat 27, Maastricht, 6221 EB, Netherlands;50.8492801;5.699464;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;To get to this restaurant, you first enter the butcher’s shop, then open the door to the cold storage room – and suddenly there you are in a fashionable, chic and cosy dining room! The attractive menu offers a choice of traditional dishes, such as cold meat platters, vegetarian options and steak, all of which are easily shared.;Counter dining;[]
11232;Portfolio;Netherlands;The Hague;Prinsestraat 36, The Hague, 2513 CD, Netherlands;52.0786675;4.3059486;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Asian Contemporary;The expertise of chef Kasper Verlinden and maître d'/sommelier Remco van Antwerpen is palpable at Portfolio and testament to their combined wealth of experience. Meticulously prepared and ambitious, their original creations live up to high expectations. Fish, seafood and Asian flavour nuances are the name of the game here. Expressive, technically sophisticated, captivating. All that deliciousness is also enhanced by a magnificent selection of natural wines and some very appealing non-alcoholic options.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
11233;Goyvaerts;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Kanaalstraat 6, Eindhoven, 5611 CT, Netherlands;51.437915;5.4842;95;false;true;Modern French, International;Jip, Yelle and Jesse Goyvaerts have set up shop in the heart of Eindhoven, in Domusdela, a converted church that has retained its serenity. Inside, the modern decor with Scandinavian touches works well – the wine cabinet is sure to draw the eye. The brothers conjure up creative dishes incorporating international influences, the finesse of French cuisine and Japanese seasonings. Think celeriac glazed with soy sauce in a vegetarian concoction with delicate sweet/salty/spicy nuances. Goyvaerts is a name that is synonymous with culinary excellence!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11234;Lastage;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Geldersekade 29, Amsterdam, 1011 EJ, Netherlands;52.3753865;4.9022565;22;true;false;Creative;Hospitality and conviviality are the bedrock of this cosy little restaurant in the heart of Amsterdam, where you can enjoy good food in a relaxed atmosphere. Rogier van Dam's dishes are full of character, and nothing on the plate is superfluous. If he serves up a fillet of venison, the whole dish revolves around that ingredient. Naturally, there is also a focus on sauces and creative garnishes. The dessert of brioche stuffed with creamy Époisses is a classic of the house, and rightly so!;Air conditioning;[]
11235;SAAM restaurant;Netherlands;Amstelveen;Amstelzijde 59, Amstelveen, 1184 TZ, Netherlands;52.2977823;4.8994285;100;true;true;South African, Modern Cuisine;South Africa comes to the Netherlands in this cosy establishment, which resembles a glass conservatory from the outside. Here on the Amstelzijde strip, some big names in the hospitality industry, including chefs and sommeliers, have joined forces in an endeavour to marry the two culinary cultures. Ingredients such as granadilla, suurvygie and goat meat are incorporated into modern creations with distinct flavours. Those not familiar with South African ingredients can rest assured that the waitstaff are always on hand to offer guidance.;Interesting wine list;[]
11236;Restaurant 273;Netherlands;Utrecht;Oudegracht 273, Utrecht, 3511 NN, Netherlands;52.0864901;5.1217764;31;false;false;International;Choose a table near the open kitchen in Tommy den Hartog’s chic, modern restaurant situated on the outskirts of the city centre. Here, the chef prepares modern cuisine with ingredients from around the world, resulting in dishes with occasionally playful and surprising combinations, but above all full of such intense flavours that you’re sure to want more!;Counter dining;[]
11237;Bleue Bar Bistro;Netherlands;Breda;Grote Markt 5, Breda, 4811 XL, Netherlands;51.5875278;4.7764362;71;false;true;French, Modern Cuisine;Rather inconspicuously located on Grote Markt, there is a distinctly Parisian feel to this bistro with a predominantly green colour scheme. The long bar with ceramic tiles and open kitchen with green panelling make for an inviting setting. As you might expect, the menu features French bistro fare with the odd fresh twist – for instance, the chef incorporates kumquat into the rich duck jus that accompanies pan-fried duck breast and orange compote, without compromising the dish's signature flavours. The house-made pâté en croûte is certainly tempting. Full flavours guaranteed!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11238;Aroma;Netherlands;Vaassen;Kerkweg 1, Vaassen, 8171 VT, Netherlands;52.2882939;5.9673523;36;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in a stately villa, this restaurant feels rather like a living room. It is here that Pasquale Carfora and Elisa Leune showcase their vision of Italian fine dining. The elegant luxury of the decor perfectly complements the refined cuisine, which is a celebration of fresh seasonal ingredients, traditional Italian techniques and innovative ideas. Think fresh pasta filled with lamb ragout, accompanied by a flavoursome pea cream, cream of pecorino for some bite and a smoked lamb jus full of finesse. This chef elevates tradition to new heights. A vibrant and stylish place to dine.;;[]
11239;Restaurant 1397;Netherlands;Bergen op Zoom;Grote Markt 38, Bergen op Zoom, 4611 NT, Netherlands;51.4945529;4.2866636;37;false;false;French Contemporary;Hotel de Draak's restaurant takes you on a journey back to 1397, taking in the Dutch Golden Age before looking to the future. The decor subtly incorporates all manner of dragons, ubiquitous touches of gold, high ceilings and large windows – this is a 21C take on historical grandeur! Treat yourself to a drink in the chic aperitif lounge before chef Torben Bouterse starts working his magic. Classic dishes are enhanced by a predilection for vegetables, nods to Zeeland cuisine and inspirations from around the globe. Take, for example, his teppanyaki scallops with a velvety Jerusalem artichoke cream, lent a hit of umami by a delicate white wine jus infused with koji. Diners delight in such a masterful and spontaneous approach to textures and flavour pairings.;Terrace;[]
11240;Orangerie De Pol;Netherlands;Doetinchem;Hulleweg 2, Doetinchem, 7004 GG, Netherlands;51.9389905;6.3330649;40;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Talented chef Mark and his charming partner Marjolein are in their element in this restaurant in the Achterhoek region. Excellent local ingredients, produce from their own kitchen garden, and intensely flavoured sauces all feature on the trendy surprise menu which combines international variety and local quality. In this bright setting, guests will definitely feel at one with nature.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11241;Watergang;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Weteringstraat 41, Amsterdam, 1017 SM, Netherlands;52.3611056;4.8887572;58;false;false;European Contemporary;This lovely little restaurant with space for just 30 guests boasts a genuine warmth and intimacy. The chefs here create a surprise five-course menu that changes each month and is particularly inspired by French and Italian cuisine. The classic comfort food on offer here, featuring the occasional original twist, is highly satisfying!;;[]
11242;Diga;Netherlands;Haarlem;Damstraat 10, Haarlem, 2011 HA, Netherlands;52.3805224;4.6385543;71;false;false;Italian;Diga is a trendy and intimate restaurant where colourful details brighten up the dark interior – it’s worth asking for a place at the back of the restaurant where you can see the kitchen and the impressive wine cabinet. Subtle influences from all over the world give the delicate antipasti and traditional Italian dishes a contemporary twist.;Terrace;[]
11243;Huisje James;Netherlands;Ugchelen;Van Golsteinlaan 20, Ugchelen, 7339 GT, Netherlands;52.1787512;5.9115179;82;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Start your meal with an aperitif by the fireplace of this former workshop, after which you will be guided to the villa. The thatched roof, the intimate ambience and beautiful art give this restaurant a cosy feel. The surprise menu features classic favourites alongside contemporary surprises, all made from regional ingredients, including home-grown produce.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
11244;Héroine;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Kipstraat 12, Rotterdam, 3011 RT, Netherlands;51.9237089;4.4917248;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed in an industrial building, this restaurant has a unique feel on account of its decor incorporating retro features and modern design, as well as striking artwork on the walls. The surprise menu showcases exciting combinations, international influences and vegetables. The chef serves crispy breaded scallops, for instance, on a delicate passion fruit cream, finishing the dish with a butter sauce enhanced with coconut and dill. His bold and innovative creations will leave you craving more.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
11245;de Wanne;Netherlands;Ootmarsum;Winhofflaan 2, Ootmarsum, 7631 HX, Netherlands;52.4080608;6.9118329;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It is no surprise that German guests feel at home in de Wanne, with its good choice of German wines and recommendations offered by the experienced maître. Original, contemporary dishes full of flavour prepared by a classically trained chef, plus a beautiful terrace overlooking the hotel gardens.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11246;LIMES aan den Rijn;Netherlands;Valkenburg;Voorschoterweg 23G, Valkenburg, 2235 SE, Netherlands;52.1682396;4.4447008;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Daan Reijngoudt is a chef who knows the importance of sauces. Think a delicate foie gras cream sauce with a hint of Calvados to add depth to fried duck liver with sweet fruit garnishes and a brioche roll. His cuisine is beautifully in step with the times, without resorting to any unnecessary frills. Inside, you can watch the chef at work in the attractive open plan kitchen. However, a spot on the terrace, nestled right next to a business complex and overlooking the river, might be your best bet.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11247;Vive La Vie;Netherlands;Groningen;Oosterstraat 39, Groningen, 9711 NP, Netherlands;53.2171832;6.5697009;19;true;true;Modern French;This retro-style building with a warm ambience is the perfect place for a special meal. Chef Jeroen Sportel prepares complex and creative dishes, regularly taking inspiration from Asian cuisine and offering just one surprise menu which is highly influenced by the passing seasons.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11248;OH30;Netherlands;Weert;Oude Hushoverweg 30, Weert, 6003 AN, Netherlands;51.259407;5.7018657;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Although its interior design is stylishly modern, OH30 fully embraces the rustic charm of the 1904 windmill in which it is housed. The surrounding terrace is an oasis of calm. Chef Emile Maessen gives you two options: you can order delicious no-nonsense classics such as entrecôte Rossini à la carte, or opt for the more elaborate and creative set menu. Think steamed cod and lobster lasagne, topped with lightly browned Gruyère cheese and encircled by a delicate bisque. This dedicated and inspired chef possesses all the necessary attributes to delight the most discerning of foodies.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11249;La Trinité;Netherlands;Sluis;Kaai 11, Sluis, 4524 CL, Netherlands;51.3086265;3.384405;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The lounge-style interior of La Trinité, in its beautiful waterfront location, is particularly inviting. Here, you can settle into your seat and enjoy the unique finger food on offer, in which the chef enjoys using Asian influences to add a trendy and international touch. His many years of experience is also evident in his classic cooking styles.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11250;JanZen;Netherlands;Woerden;Rietveld 130, Woerden, 3443 XE, Netherlands;52.0797638;4.8281956;28;false;false;Farm to table;Cosiness reigns supreme in this beautiful Art Deco building surrounded by tranquil polders, where you will be spoilt by your hosts Jeroen and Natasja van Hensbergen. The tasting menus are a must for those keen to experience the chef’s surprising creations. Attentive service, beautifully presented dishes and flavours to match!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
11251;Danyel;Netherlands;Maastricht;Observantenweg 3, Maastricht, 6212 EN, Netherlands;50.8387531;5.6870785;92;true;true;French, Modern French;Danyel van den Bongard is a veteran of the Maastricht food scene who knows his classics well. Experience his cuisine for yourself in this pleasant restaurant with its French bistro feel, and enjoy delicious dishes that are rich, unctuous, succulent… In short, you can eat like a king here! House specialities such as the foie gras and sweetbreads are simply exquisite.;Terrace;[]
11252;Vanille;Netherlands;Eijsden;Diepstraat 1, Eijsden, 6245 BJ, Netherlands;50.7756096;5.7024854;81;true;false;Farm to table;The locals (Belgian and Dutch) flock to this snug restaurant, whose vintage floor tiles immediately catch the eye. The menu is carefully crafted, subtle and deliciously in tune with the zeitgeist. The inspired chef bends over backwards to rustle up fine fare to the delight of his patrons.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11253;Restaurant Chocolat;Netherlands;Breda;Torenstraat 9A, Breda, 4811 XV, Netherlands;51.5886377;4.7749226;44;false;false;World Cuisine, Creative French;Beneath the gaze of elegant women on pictures adorning the walls to the trendy chocolate-coloured furniture, Chocolat exudes a “sexy” ambience. The overall feel is enhanced by Dorus Clement’s equally exciting creativity in the kitchen where he toys with a palette of varied flavours and is never frightened of introducing delicacies such as vadouvan and yuzu in his French-inspired recipes, showcasing his willingness to experiment.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11254;Fabuleux;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Verwersstraat 23, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5211 HT, Netherlands;51.6872;5.30485;36;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Fabuleux is a trendy restaurant with a classic decor in its front dining room and a more intimate ambience to the rear. On arrival, your gaze is immediately drawn to the striking wine “library”, from which host Paul van Gestel selects the best bottles. Chef Busio creates updated and beautifully presented dishes which are full of classic flavour.;Interesting wine list;[]
11255;Landgoed Groenendaal;Netherlands;Heemstede;Groenendaal 3, Heemstede, 2104 WP, Netherlands;52.3382057;4.6135853;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;What a magnificent location! Set in the beautiful Groenendaal forest, this former coach house exudes luxury and boasts a terrace that is among the loveliest in the region. The chef likes to draw on the finest ingredients when devising his set menus (one of which is vegetarian). Diners can therefore indulge in a rich terrine of foie gras as well as a carrot dish prepared with miso, pumpkin and yellow curry. This fresh and unfussy take on authentic flavours never disappoints.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11256;De Herberg van Smallingerland;Netherlands;Rottevalle;Muldersplein 2, Rottevalle, 9221 SP, Netherlands;53.1455916;6.1022743;83;true;true;Modern French;Dating back to 1791, this charming inn is full of character and extremely popular. Tables in the gorgeous courtyard garden are in high demand, as are the guestrooms. With a special emphasis on vegetables, Chef Freddy and son Jurmen showcase Frisian cuisine at its best. For instance, they will draw on the distinct flavours of beetroot, cherries and capers to give a fillet of red mullet a special twist. The menu at de Herberg is full of surprises!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11258;TOV;Netherlands;Schagen;Loet 8, Schagen, 1741 BP, Netherlands;52.7857284;4.7949339;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;TOV stands for Team Onvergetelijk Verrassend (literally, an unforgettably surprising team), giving an indication of what is in store at this trendy restaurant. The young staff are full of enthusiasm and everything is organised just as it should be. Resolutely contemporary-style cuisine created by an imaginative chef.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11259;In den Doofpot;Netherlands;Leiden;Turfmarkt 9, Leiden, 2312 CE, Netherlands;52.1619251;4.4857075;80;true;false;Creative;Enjoy an aperitif on the restaurant’s boat or on the terrace overlooking the water before sampling cuisine which pays real tribute to the history of Leiden. In this trendy restaurant, a highly imaginative chef serves subtle and precise reinterpretations of classic dishes, while the extensive wine list is a veritable Bible!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11260;'t Pakhuus;Netherlands;Oudeschild;Haven 8, Oudeschild, 1792 AE, Netherlands;53.0393675;4.8496039;60;false;true;Seafood;This restaurant's designer decor is delightful, with a moss-clad wall that brings a touch of nature into the dining room. However, the ultimate appeal of this historical warehouse is its view of the harbour and the shrimp boats. Fish and seafood are the speciality of the house – the centrepiece is the fish tank, which is replenished daily. Think fresh Wadden oysters or scallops, enhanced by Asian flavours such as ponzu, ginger and pimento. Of course, the menu also features other local delicacies, such as Texel lamb. To cap it all off, why not spend the night in one of the designer suites?;Great view,Terrace;[]
11261;Amused Food & Wine;Netherlands;Hardenberg;Voorstraat 39, Hardenberg, 7772 AB, Netherlands;52.5755998;6.6169701;24;true;true;Modern French;On one side is Next wine bar, which is a stylish and trendy spot in which to sample vinologist Corine Vink's latest finds, served with freshly prepared bar snacks. Then there is the elegant restaurant with its chic decor, where Chiel de Groot incorporates his creative ideas into a surprise menu and beautifully presented plates of food. He likes to use produce from his own vegetable garden to bring his creations to life. Intensity is his guiding principle: a grilled sandwich filled with game stew, for instance, makes for an original accompaniment to a medium-rare roe fillet, an exquisite game jus and a cream sauce with chanterelles. Prepare to be surprised with every bite!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11262;Fris;Netherlands;Haarlem;Twijnderslaan 7, Haarlem, 2012 BG, Netherlands;52.3722241;4.6339847;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Meticulously prepared sea bass terrine, perfectly fried veal sweetbreads, koji butter (fermented on site) and a penchant for exotic flavours such as coconut milk and kombu – the culinary worlds of France and Asia meet at Fris. Classic techniques, top-of-the-range ingredients and playful originality bring the dishes to life. The non-alcoholic beverage accompaniments include delicious kombuchas made using kitchen scraps, among other things.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11263;Catch by Simonis;Netherlands;The Hague;Dr. Lelykade 43, The Hague, 2583 CL, Netherlands;52.0946381;4.2651506;75;false;true;Seafood;No, you are not in New York, although this impressive restaurant in the Scheveningen marina would not look out of place there with its highly fashionable decor, prestigious bottles adorning the wine walls, and luxury terrace on which to soak up the trendy atmosphere… Talk about a hip hangout! Fish and seafood steal the show in traditional dishes, seafood specialities, sushi etc. Whether classically prepared by frying in butter or drawn into original creations, the flavours of the sea take pride of place here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11264;Den Burgh;Netherlands;Hoofddorp;Rijnlanderweg 878, Hoofddorp, 2132 ML, Netherlands;52.286768;4.7070905;26;false;true;Farm to table;This impressive farmhouse dating from 1859 has retained its original charm and gained in elegance since its refurbishment. Inlaid with golden coins, the main bar is sure to draw the eye, as is the terrace. This bustling establishment is popular with business people, not only due to its proximity to a business park and the airport. The extensive menu includes appetisers, salads, steak tartare and bouillabaisse. The succulent pan-fried halibut accompanied by an exquisite fish sauce shows that, although the dishes may have a modern look, they are rooted in beautiful classic flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11266;Hofstede Meerzigt;Netherlands;Zoetermeer;Zonnenberg 10, Zoetermeer, 2716 PG, Netherlands;52.0620932;4.4595121;36;true;true;Farm to table, French;Zoetermeer harbours a secret oasis that is waiting to be discovered. This enchanting estate boasts a chef’s table in a wine barn, a wedding venue in a converted stable, a terrace overlooking a lush garden, not to mention a stylish restaurant in a converted 17C farmhouse. The hospitality here is genuine, as is the kitchen team's appreciation of their ingredients. Alain Adriaanse shares his passion by delivering dishes that give familiar flavours the odd twist. With an Asian touch and fresh flavours, he elevates the sea bass tartare to new heights. He also puts a unique spin on steak tartare by adding playful textures. The extensive wine list is the icing on the cake.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11267;Hoog Holten;Netherlands;Holten;Forthaarsweg 7, Holten, 7451 JS, Netherlands;52.2902861;6.4241389;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Your experience at Hoog Holten begins with the drive there: the charm of the surrounding Salland countryside is captivating in itself. The terrace of this romantic establishment, housed in an old hunting lodge, happens to be one of the most beautiful in the country! Brasserie Birds keeps things traditional – go to the restaurant for more varied, contemporary cuisine. The set menu changes daily, but always seeks inspiration abroad for its sometimes truly innovative dishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11268;Oostergoo;Netherlands;Grou;Nieuwe Kade 1, Grou, 9001 AE, Netherlands;53.0972897;5.8388368;96;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Oostergoo is an ideal base from which to explore the picturesque town of Grou and, for that matter, the lovely province of Friesland – starting with a visit to this beautiful marina terrace. It's quite an experience! The old Dutch interior, with its Delftware and lovely parquet flooring, is no less enchanting. They serve up an authentic brand of traditional cuisine. The locally caught smoked eel is a real treat!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11269;Wilhelminapark;Netherlands;Utrecht;Wilhelminapark 65, Utrecht, 3581 NP, Netherlands;52.0871349;5.14125;100;true;true;Farm to table;Utrecht's city park is an ideal spot to unwind, and where better to do that than in this stylish restaurant with its authentic thatched roof and idyllic terrace overlooking the magnificent lake? Wilhelminapark has been a fixture since 1926, and you'll notice that right away. The chef wins diners over with both a rather classic fish dish accompanied by a rich beurre blanc and a steak tartare with an Asian twist. The wine pairings are equally impressive. Or just drop in to enjoy a drink and some delicious oysters.;Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11270;Red Chilli;Netherlands;Nieuwe-Niedorp;Oude Provincialeweg 2, Nieuwe-Niedorp, 1733 NG, Netherlands;52.7434825;4.9123414;45;true;true;Asian, Fusion;Asia is a world away from the peaceful polders but this intimate restaurant creates a real Eastern ambience. Its fusion Asian cuisine is authentic yet modern in style. Red Chilli will definitely spice up your evening!;Car park,Terrace;[]
11271;Dell'arte;Netherlands;Cadzand;Mariastraat 34, Cadzand, 4506 AE, Netherlands;51.3671538;3.4103136;19;true;false;Modern French;Robbert Dellaert has transformed his childhood home, dating from 1878, into a restaurant with a romantic feel. This is an intimate space with a beautiful garden. Thanks to Julie's excellent service, you can just relax and delight in the love that the chef expresses for his terroir – Zeelandic Flanders. He treats local produce with reverence, and his well-thought-out combinations create a sense of depth. For instance, he enhances ultra-fresh soused herring with avocado ice cream, yuzu gel and sweet and sour daikon. A unique culinary adventure!;Car park,Terrace;[]
11272;Kaagman & Kortekaas;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Sint Nicolaasstraat 43, Amsterdam, 1012 NJ, Netherlands;52.374813;4.892399;29;true;true;Farm to table;Giel Kaagman and Bram Kortekaas have clearly chosen to focus on quality in their lively bistro, where the chef enjoys working with vegetables, wild game and fish, transforming these ingredients into exciting dishes which are striking for their contrasting flavours. Both the menu, which changes regularly, and the wine list are full of surprises!;Counter dining;[]
11273;Café Caron;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Frans Halsstraat 28, Amsterdam, 1072 BS, Netherlands;52.3574102;4.8887114;53;false;false;Classic French;This cosy bistro is run by Alain Caron (a well-known TV personality and chef) and his family. The ambience here is typically French, as is the menu which features traditional, generous bistro-style dishes which are a work of art in their own right. Trying out the à la carte here is a real joy.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11274;De Kluizenaer;Netherlands;Goes;Grote Markt 12, Goes, 4461 AJ, Netherlands;51.5049553;3.8905051;70;true;false;Modern French;This former savings bank has been converted into a restaurant with a touch of industrial decor, with large drawings providing a bit of fun. The internationally seasoned chef brings punchy flavours to the plate to present his own vision of gastronomy. His cuisine is resolutely contemporary, involving robust taste combinations.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11275;De Koetsier;Netherlands;Boxtel;Eindhovenseweg 41, Boxtel, 5283 RA, Netherlands;51.57669;5.3399116;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A romantic atmosphere reigns supreme at De Koetsier. Shades of blue and pink provide the colourful modernised decor at this auberge without taking anything away from its authenticity. An old wardrobe has even been converted into a cheese store! Martijn will be delighted to share his passion for wine, while Ayesta brings elegance and a subtle modernity to the kitchen.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11276;Trattoria Da Giulio;Netherlands;Arnhem;Markt 37, Arnhem, 6811 CJ, Netherlands;51.9782675;5.9097714;84;false;false;Italian;Giulio keeps the traditions of his native Sardinia alive in this cheerful trattoria. He makes his own pasta and bread every day, and the orata (gilt-head bream) in a salt crust is even filleted at the table. Here the Italian art of simplicity is at its most exuberant. House-made pappardelle with a creamy duck sauce, an aromatic panna cotta topped with a subtly flavoured juniper jam... Da Giulio is undeniably the best Italian in Arnhem!;Air conditioning;[]
11277;THE DUCHESS;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Spuistraat 172, Amsterdam, 1012 VT, Netherlands;52.3728921;4.8894578;65;true;true;French, Mediterranean Cuisine;This upscale brasserie in what was once a waiting room of KAS Bank exudes the captivating charm of the Belle Époque. Features such as dark marble, impressive chandeliers, antique clocks and stunning stained-glass windows create an intimate setting. The extensive menu is inspired by Mediterranean culinary tradition, with a particular emphasis on southern France and Italy. Classics such as beef Wellington and tagliolini cacio e pepe are served in generous portions, without any unnecessary frills. The weekend afternoon tea is a real treat.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11278;Nassau;Netherlands;Groningen;Martinikerkhof 23, Groningen, 9712 JH, Netherlands;53.2206768;6.5688507;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A centuries-old beamed ceiling, glossy parquet flooring, sleek furniture design and views of the beautiful Prinsentuin walled garden – you really dine in style at Groningen's Nassau. The chef knows the importance of an intense sauce and loves working with top-notch produce such as langoustine and Anjou pigeon, which he showcases in elaborate dishes. For instance, he elevates hamachi, along with a medley of vegetables and seasonings, with a Thai-style sauce made with miso, coconut and lemongrass. His plant-based creations are equally remarkable. A beautifully curated wine list featuring an interesting range of German wines has the perfect accompaniment in store. Sophistication is in Nassau's very DNA.;;[]
11279;Sizzles at the Park;Netherlands;Apeldoorn;Kerklaan 17, Apeldoorn, 7311 AA, Netherlands;52.2175338;5.9612906;44;false;false;International;The monumental building that provides the setting for Sizzles is truly impressive – the contemporary elegance, trendy ambience and terrace almost whisk you away to Ibiza! You can eat here morning, noon and night, enjoying Leon Habers’ family-inspired and highly original dishes that include a dynamic twist, a hint of Asia and an acidic touch. Fascinating!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11280;Le Nord;Netherlands;Bilthoven;Soestdijkseweg Noord 492, Bilthoven, 3723 HM, Netherlands;52.1507106;5.2239578;55;false;true;Classic French;This authentic farmhouse dating from 1885 combines rural charm and modern design – the ideal setting in which to experience Grégory Nicole's cuisine. The finesse with which this French chef pays tribute to his homeland is a testament to his expertise. More modern inspirations add a dash of excitement without overcomplicating things. He surprises diners with, for instance, his own take on Poire Williams, or a beautiful cod fillet infused with zesty notes. Be sure to try the tuna pizza, a tribute to master chef Joop Braakhekke. Le Nod is also a sure bet at lunchtime!;Car park,Terrace;[]
11281;Tante Blanche;Netherlands;Brummen;Arnhemsestraat 22, Brummen, 6971 AR, Netherlands;52.0861907;6.1555928;59;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;In this contemporary restaurant Charles Ek honours the memory of his aunt’s fine cooking. Enjoy delicious, fresh dishes that are simple, copious, full of flavour and exciting without being overstated.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11282;De Goede Gooier;Netherlands;Blaricum;Crailoseweg 151, Blaricum, 1261 AA, Netherlands;52.2774317;5.2112326;65;true;true;French, Modern Cuisine;The thatched roof and trendy yet welcoming interior are a draw in their own right. However, it's the pergola and the gorgeous terrace overlooking the heathland that steals the show. The kitchen is run by a highly skilled chef who produces French cuisine with the utmost respect. The sole meunière and pan-fried foie gras do not disappoint with their robust flavours, but the chef also has some surprises up his sleeve, such as a swordfish carpaccio finished with a spicy harissa vinaigrette. There is an appealing lunch menu, an extensive dinner menu, and they are open every day for both lunch and dinner: a firm favourite!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11283;De Hemel;Netherlands;Bergen op Zoom;Moeregrebstraat 35, Bergen op Zoom, 4611 JB, Netherlands;51.4956051;4.2825454;99;false;false;Modern French, Home Cooking;Enjoy an intimate dinner in a romantic dining room, or on the rear terrace in fine weather, and choose from a selection of tasty dishes prepared in French style, with a nod to modern cuisine. A delightful dining experience.;Terrace;[]
11284;De Steenen Tafel;Netherlands;Arnhem;Weg achter het Bos 1, Arnhem, 6822 LV, Netherlands;52.0017236;5.9239232;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fans of fine food put on their Sunday best to dine at this elegant conservatory restaurant on the edge of the pretty Klarenbeek park (what a view!). They come here for the traditionally prepared lobster or the wild game from the Veluwe region, although the chef also prepares more original fare such as the occasional oriental dish with foie gras. Rich, authentic cuisine is to the fore here.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11285;Dorset;Netherlands;Borne;Grotestraat 167, Borne, 7622 GE, Netherlands;52.2998235;6.757634;24;false;true;Farm to table, Modern French;Dorset is intimate and trendy, with a pleasant lounge atmosphere. Chef Davy Roord will delight you with his modern fusion of local ingredients and Asian flavours. This enthusiastic cuisine is occasionally innovative and always fresh. Guest satisfaction is the priority here, both on the plate and in the wine glass!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11286;Lagrange;Netherlands;Buren;Buitenhuizenpoort 11, Buren, 4116 CA, Netherlands;51.9116165;5.3323479;24;false;false;French, Modern Cuisine;Picture the scene: You are in the lovely town of Buren, and step into an elegantly converted barn in anticipation of an intimate dinner. The dishes served embody a modern take on French cuisine. The chef knows how to cook a fillet of wild duck to perfection, for example, but also makes his mark by seasoning leg rillettes with hoisin. At Lagrange, flavours from the local area and around the globe go hand in hand.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11287;Bij Brons;Netherlands;Almere-Haven;Sluis 3, Almere-Haven, 1357 NZ, Netherlands;52.3339342;5.221305;99;true;true;Classic Cuisine, French;At John and Yvonne Brons’ restaurant you can enjoy good food in a cosy pavilion, right in the harbour area of Almere-Haven, where fresh fish is served in season (outside the spawning period) straight from the sea onto your plate. The meat dishes are also a fine example of chef Brons’ focus on quality. Generous classic cuisine offering a delightful dining experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11288;Restaurant Bakboord;Netherlands;Almere-Haven;Veerkade 10, Almere-Haven, 1357 PK, Netherlands;52.3323;5.22128;52;true;false;Modern French, Classic French;The view you have here of Almere's marina as the boats sail away is quite something to behold. The lounge terrace is a great place to sit, but equally charming is the contemporary decor indoors. The dishes, which showcase vegetables, are brimming with creative enthusiasm. They are elaborate, even daring at times, and always display technical mastery. There are plenty of delicious vegetarian options on the à la carte menu should you wish to avoid meat and fish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11289;Rue de la Plume;Netherlands;Alkmaar;Veerstraat 22, Alkmaar, 1811 LB, Netherlands;52.63244;4.7478456;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Everything about this inviting restaurant makes it clear that Luella and Madelene are passionate about what they do. Luella likes nothing better than to amaze her guests with her contemporary surprise menu. Her dishes revolve around a main ingredient of the finest quality, elaborate garnishes and velvety sauces that bring it all together. The wines recommended by Madelene complement the intense flavours beautifully. This duo's enthusiasm is infectious!;Air conditioning;[]
11290;Bridges;Netherlands;Amsterdam;O.Z. Voorburgwal 197, Amsterdam, 1012 EX, Netherlands;52.3709766;4.8966078;84;true;false;Seafood;Fish reigns supreme at this sleek restaurant, which also offers a beautiful view of the canals. Salted delicacies take centre stage in dishes that are distinctly contemporary in style. The chef combines classic sauces with the occasional Asian twist to showcase the fresh flavours of his ingredients.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11291;De Saffraan;Netherlands;Amersfoort;Kleine Koppel 3, Amersfoort, 3812 PG, Netherlands;52.1617128;5.3796392;28;true;false;Creative;This old clipper moored in the canal has been converted into an elegant and intimate restaurant with a terrace on the deck where you can while away the hours. De Saffraan really is an exceptional restaurant with great service provided by charming waitstaff. Chef van Wechem has a penchant for punchy flavours and innovative techniques, handling top-notch ingredients with finesse. For instance, he elevates fried turbot with a wonderfully robust beach crab jus and adds coconut for depth. This place has real personality!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11292;Gaar;Netherlands;Meerssen;Klinkenberg 173, Meerssen, 6321 BC, Netherlands;50.8765057;5.7354752;55;true;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;The world is Joachim Müller's culinary playground. Generous dishes such as Limburg pork terrine or crispy tortilla with Asian-style marinated tuna and wasabi give expression to the chef's sense of fun. The extensive and varied menu never disappoints, and diners will enjoy the interesting wine pairings. Chef Joachim and front-of-house manager Myrthe make it their mission to show guests a good time. The pops of turquoise in the decor are in keeping with the convivial spirit of this place.;Terrace;[]
11293;Oan Tafel;Netherlands;Wergea;Kerkbuurt 3, Wergea, 9005 NZ, Netherlands;53.1519621;5.8445263;16;false;true;International, Country cooking;80% homegrown produce and vegetables, the remaining meat and fish comes from further afield. Such is the concept of this natural restaurant, whose interior sports raw materials, a handsome counter and a casual vibe. Eastern exuberance meets Frisian temperance. Fermentations, sweet and sour touches, surprising flavours… Intriguing!;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11294;Bar BAUT;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Stadionweg 320, Amsterdam, 1076 PK, Netherlands;52.3457043;4.8598138;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;With its Banksy-style frescoes, trendy, intimate interior and delightfully relaxed ambience, Bar BAUT is a must in Amsterdam, where guests can choose from the enticing à la carte featuring international ingredients cooked in contemporary style. Enjoy intense flavours, well-prepared produce and original ideas – plus excellent value for money!;;[]
11296;In de Oude Stempel;Netherlands;Steenbergen;Kaaistraat 19, Steenbergen, 4651 BL, Netherlands;51.5863293;4.3159684;16;false;false;Country cooking, Creative;In this former post office, stamps and letters have made way for the on-trend cuisine of Mark van Loon. This is a chef who doesn't hesitate to play with textures or bring bold combinations to the table. His creativity is complemented by his prowess in the art of making sauces – think a rich game jus to accompany the venison fillet. For something more low key, head to Puur, the brasserie next door.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11297;Witlof;Netherlands;Nijmegen;Lage Markt 79, Nijmegen, 6511 VK, Netherlands;51.8496807;5.8633481;76;false;false;Farm to table;With the view of the River Waal, the jovial hostess and the chef who you see cooking as you make your way to use the facilities, at the Witlof, you will immediately feel at home. Jurgen Eikholt lovingly prepares classic cuisine with his trademark sophisticated, often oriental touches. Each dish on the menu can be ordered as a large or small portion.;Air conditioning;[]
11298;Sukerieje;Netherlands;Zwolle;Rodetorenplein 16, Zwolle, 8011 MJ, Netherlands;52.5140276;6.0897528;83;false;true;Farm to table;Sukerieje has now relocated to Hopmanshuis, a tastefully converted warehouse brimming with character. The menu has also been revamped. Chef Yannick Roodhof likes to focus on vegetables and enjoys expressing his creative side – his creamy cashew nut 'pâté with melon and chilli causes quite a stir. Through his expertise in using exotic ingredients and his patience in imbuing his sauces with depth, he creates an exceptional intensity of flavours. This restaurant is going places!;Terrace;[]
11299;Ni Hao;Netherlands;Nunspeet;Harderwijkerweg 85, Nunspeet, 8071 EN, Netherlands;52.3752693;5.7743914;24;false;false;Chinese, Cantonese;This restaurant with an intimate Eastern feel introduces its guests to “chistro” dishes, a combination of bistro and Chinese cuisine. Chef Chen creates delicious contemporary dishes, which are made to share and which include specialities from Sichuan, Guangdong, Beijing and Wenzhou. An innovative approach to authentic Chinese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11300;Ron Gastrobar Indonesia;Netherlands;Amstelveen;Amstelzijde 51, Amstelveen, 1184 TZ, Netherlands;52.297463;4.8997836;87;true;false;Indonesian;Top chef Ron Blaauw has a nose for a winning concept, as proven by this typical Indonesian restaurant with its bustling terrace by the River Amstel. The flavours are distinctively Asian, but he and his colleague Agus Hermawan also add their own twists for that extra fragrance and depth. The rijsttafel options "Agus" (15 dishes) and "Tim" (12 dishes) provide the perfect opportunity to share all kinds of delicious treats, such as satay kambing and udang peteh.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11301;NY Basement;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Koninginnenhoofd 1, Rotterdam, 3072 AD, Netherlands;51.9041375;4.4842617;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;A jazzy vibe reigns supreme in the cellar of the New York hotel, which is reminiscent of the Big Apple of the 1920s and 1930s. After a delicious cocktail at the 11m-long bar, guests can enjoy the modern cuisine on offer here. Choose from a delicious fish or meat dish, vegetables prepared on the charcoal grill and an array of trendy suggestions.;Air conditioning;[]
11302;Amber Garden;Netherlands;Amstelveen;Van Heuven Goedhartlaan 15, Amstelveen, 1181 LE, Netherlands;52.3021698;4.868516;30;false;true;Chinese;Amber Garden is a lavish, swanky Chinese restaurant, whose guiding line is authenticity, as the house specialty, roast duck, demonstrates. The chef enjoys adding the occasional western touch and cannot be rivalled for his ability to subtly blend texture, taste and fresh produce. A tantalising insight into Chinese cooking.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11303;YANO;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Straatweg 114, Rotterdam, 3051 BM, Netherlands;51.9466603;4.4843528;45;false;false;Creative French, Fusion;Scandinavian minimalist design, a Japanese Zen vibe and a convivial atmosphere are the defining features of YANO. You will be welcomed by the charming Britta before the highly experienced chef Yuri lets his cooking do the talking. His dishes are vibrant and skilfully seasoned. His culinary style has French foundations, yet he also draws on his Moluccan roots and other influences from far-flung places. Whether he is combining pigeon with pumpkin and coffee or langoustine with pipián verde and huacatay, his creativity knows no bounds and never fails to impress.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11304;De Monnikendam;Netherlands;Amersfoort;Plantsoen-Oost 2, Amersfoort, 3811 HH, Netherlands;52.1536841;5.3923176;18;false;false;French Contemporary, International;Originally part of Amersfoort's second city wall, Monnickendam is a watergate dating back to the early 15C. Today, this piece of history has been repurposed to create a unique culinary destination. There are intimate dining spaces within the towers and a waterside terrace affording wonderful views. Thanks to the enthusiasm of hostess Kristel and chef Richard, this establishment has made a name for itself. With each course, the tasting menu seamlessly navigates between the familiar and the exotic: Think hamachi accompanied by a tangy ponzu, or lamb saddle with a crispy crust and a lamb jus infused with rosemary, thyme and wild garlic oil. A memorable dining experience!;Terrace;[]
11305;Neder;Netherlands;Alkmaar;Laat 85, Alkmaar, 1811 EC, Netherlands;52.6292992;4.7501576;22;true;false;Country cooking;At Neder, they are committed to working with local produce. From Eastern Scheldt salt and wild-harvested herbs to Veluwe red deer and Texel mustard seeds, everything, including the drinks, comes from within a 223km radius. What they don't grow themselves is sourced from responsible suppliers. This approach presents numerous challenges, but it also inspires chefs to be more creative. They bring each season to life with a new set menu, building on a foundation of ingredients preserved using a variety of methods. Marinated hogweed flowers and a chamomile beurre blanc lend the steamed pike-perch a fresh, floral lift. Summer venison is rubbed with wheat koji for that umami flavour – this is sophisticated, aromatic and innovative cuisine. The fact that Neder is an ambassador for the Dutch terroir is also expressed in the interior design, with its landscape paintings, visible fermentation room and a combination of rusticity and soothing natural materials.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11306;Bistro Pinot;Netherlands;Grou;Wijdesteeg 10, Grou, 9001 AK, Netherlands;53.09693;5.8406;54;false;false;French;Are you in Friesland and dreaming of a getaway to Paris? Then make your way through the lovely streets of Grou to this delightful bistro. The nostalgic wall tiles, the marble counter and wooden stools, the French music pouring out of the speakers… This place has real character! Bistro classics are prepared in time-honoured tradition here: succulent foie gras on brioche, zesty canard à l'orange, a crispy and wonderfully fresh macaroon tart. The dishes for sharing (choose at least four) transport you to those iconic bistros of the Parisian Left Bank.;Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11307;Het Sluishuys;Netherlands;Nijkerk;Arkersluisweg 31, Nijkerk, 3861 NG, Netherlands;52.2550522;5.4653018;80;true;false;Farm to table;Hand-cut steak tartare with fine acidity, turbot à la meunière with a beurre blanc cooked in time-honoured tradition and ravioli stuffed with oxtail: these are the kind of classic dishes for which Erik Hendriksen is renowned. At this warm and welcoming restaurant, in an idyllic location by an old lock and close to a small harbour, familiar flavours are given the attention they deserve.;Car park;[]
11308;Troef;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Schollenbrugstraat 8, Amsterdam, 1091 EX, Netherlands;52.3491461;4.9135577;43;true;false;Modern French;This bistro exudes an endlessly appealing nostalgic charm, as well as a fully à la carte menu and a chef who is able to impart his infectious enthusiasm to his team and to diners. In short, it has enough aces up its sleeve to convince any self-respecting foodie. First and foremost among them is the creative spin the chef puts on classic French dishes. Take, for instance, his perfectly cooked langoustines, topped with slivers of lardo di Colonnata and served with a delicate butter sauce infused with vin jaune and vanilla. Troef epitomises the laid-back vibe of Amsterdam!;Counter dining;[]
11309;CouCou;Netherlands;Vught;Taalstraat 57, Vught, 5261 BB, Netherlands;51.6656774;5.2950119;59;false;true;Contemporary, Sharing;With the mixologist doing their thing behind the imposing bar, the hip CouCou is reminiscent of a London cocktail bar. Whether you prefer to watch the chefs work their magic or enjoy a more intimate meal, this chic establishment has the perfect table for you. The wide range of sharing options on the menu is equally appealing and on trend. These are inspired by French and Mediterranean cuisines and given an original twist. Take the beautifully crispy fried lobster and prawn roulade finished with a lobster bisque gel and velvety pine nut cream. Délicieux !;Car park,Counter dining;[]
11310;The Church;Netherlands;Arnhem;Ir J.P. Van Muijlwijkstraat 19A, Arnhem, 6828 BP, Netherlands;51.984296;5.9137562;58;false;true;Creative;With its stained-glass windows, sculptures, murals and old pews, this Lutheran church has been beautifully preserved. The juxtaposition of modern opulence with the venue's rich past is truly inspired. Take in the spectacle of the open kitchen while enjoying a meal prepared right before your eyes. Nestled in the church's rafters, there are a few cosy guestrooms. But first, it's time to let yourself be spoiled by Bart Leussink, a chef who embraces creativity and boldness in his cooking. For instance, he elevates lamb neck with a crispy herb crust and lamb fillet with a vibrant sweet-and-sour cucumber garnish and a rich lamb jus. The chef has a penchant for fish and seafood dishes, into which he likes weave zesty flavours. An extraordinary experience!;;[]
11312;De Salentein;Netherlands;Nijkerk;Putterstraatweg 7, Nijkerk, 3862 RA, Netherlands;52.2356893;5.4966563;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Argentina and Uruguay are the main sources of inspiration for the elegant De Salentein. Not only does the menu feature the traditional cuisines of those countries, with dishes such as chimichurri and empanadas, but the restaurant even raises its own beef cattle and has its own winery in Argentina. Led by chef Rik Jansma, the kitchen team elevates robust South American flavours with a touch of sophistication. The distinctive aromas of a sea bass ceviche, for instance, are enhanced with a leche del tigre vinaigrette. Cooked to perfection over flames, the picanha is paired with a rich brown sauce. For something a little more down-to-earth, head to Bodega Portillo, housed in the same building. A Latin American adventure awaits!;Car park;[]
11313;Restaurant Uijttewaal;Netherlands;Breda;Ulvenhoutselaan 96, Breda, 4834 MH, Netherlands;51.5575471;4.792141;33;true;false;French Contemporary;Chef Sven and his brother, sommelier Lars Uijttewaal, warmly welcome you into their chic and stylish establishment. A timeless interior design and a tasteful blend of warm tones combine to create a pleasant atmosphere. Their fresh cuisine follows current trends, as demonstrated by their signature amuse-bouche – an ode to their grandfather, who owned a pickle company: a refreshing sweet-and-sour piccalilli sorbet served with sweet-and-sour pickle creams and a carrot coulis finished with dill oil. The menu intrigues from start to finish (they also serve lunch), with dishes such as steak tartare with ponzu or a delicate pairing of sole and morels. The excellent wine list, with plenty of options by the glass, is also worthy of your attention.;;[]
11314;Holsterhof;Netherlands;Posterholt;Paalderweg 2, Posterholt, 6061 NV, Netherlands;51.1370816;6.039228;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;With the hard work of hostess Lissa and chef Kaj, the restaurant at Holsterhof camping farm has gradually evolved into a sought-after culinary destination, set in a modern, light-filled space surrounded by lush greenery. The service is relaxed and friendly. The chef is an expert sauce maker who creates daring combinations on the plate, without making things overly complicated. His exquisite red curry with coconut milk adds depth of flavour to the tender quail leg with black lentils. Working with two set menus, he consistently surprises with subtle nuances.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11317;Novaela;Netherlands;Delft;Bagijnhof 118, Delft, 2611 AS, Netherlands;52.0139309;4.3535645;28;false;true;Creative French;Novaela encapsulates the magic of the Bagijnhof, a historical beguinage. The blend of upscale contemporary design and old architectural features is unique – as, for example, in the oval stone counter and the wooden beams. Daniel Duijster Gomero's cuisine is all about creativity, excitement and beautiful presentation. His surprise menu features some daring ideas such as the unexpectedly harmonious combination of razor clams and beetroot, but also familiar dishes like succulent quail fillet with an exquisite jus. You only have the choice of a six-course set menu and lunch, but you are definitely in safe hands with this chef.;;[]
11318;Brasserie Mijn Streek;Netherlands;Heerlen;Bongerd 18, Heerlen, 6411 JM, Netherlands;50.8879351;5.9791434;38;true;false;Contemporary;Cold or hot dishes, whether to share with your dining companions or go solo, to opt for one of the many vegetarian options or plump for fish or meat… In this convivial brasserie on the fifth floor of the Glaspaleis, there are plenty of choices to be made. Brace yourself for an international culinary adventure that takes in ceviche, ravioli, strawberry Romanoff and many other mouth-watering treats. A visit to the Schunck Museum in the same building is a must if you visit the area.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11319;Villa Coucou-La cuisine d'Alexandre;Netherlands;The Hague;Laan Van Meerdervoort 6, The Hague, 2517 AJ, Netherlands;52.0865073;4.3001918;35;false;true;French;With its parquet floors, marble tables and walls adorned with works of art, the luxurious Villa Coucou, one of The Hague’s shining culinary lights, is not short on style! Enjoy a cocktail at the bar or in the wine cellar (which even has space for a game of boules!) before savouring the revisited classics of French cuisine. The chef here is passionate about top-quality ingredients and enjoys toying with intense aromas and light textures.;Terrace;[]
11320;Restaurant De Olliemölle;Netherlands;Borculo;Lange Molenstraat 17, Borculo, 7271 BJ, Netherlands;52.1149541;6.5212415;21;false;true;Farm to table;Picture the scene: a table by the water, with water lilies floating nearby and an old-fashioned water wheel turning occasionally. Could it be more romantic? Rest assured that De Olliemölle is every bit as enchanting inside. Roel Sieverink has a soft spot for French cuisine and loves serving lobster straight from his lobster tank. The bisque here is full-bodied and spicy, the foie gras terrine is juicy and the veal jus with crispy sweetbreads is deliciously intense. The chef adds the odd modern twist to his classic dishes, introducing brighter flavours while maintaining the rich, hearty taste that his cuisine is known for.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11321;MANO Restaurant;Netherlands;Haarlem;Bakenessergracht 109, Haarlem, 2011 JV, Netherlands;52.3804328;4.6414548;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Hermanos Daniël and Kevin have been best friends since childhood. In their elegant little establishment, which has preserved the charm of this corner building, they showcase their combined experience. The food is contemporary, featuring intense sauces, an interplay of fresh and zingy flavours, and multiple international influences. Here, technically crafted creations and vigorous creativity go mano a mano.;;[]
11322;Sinck;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Prinsengracht 422, Amsterdam, 1016 JC, Netherlands;52.36624;4.88222;94;false;true;Modern French;Locals and tourists alike love to meet up at this bustling place. This old building on the Prinsengracht boasts a charming waterfront terrace and a lovely bistro-style interior. The renowned wine list (there is a wine bar at basement level) and modern culinary creations complement each other perfectly. The chef has a no-nonsense approach to cooking – a few elements that are full of flavour plus sauces for a fine accompaniment. This is Amsterdam at its coolest!;Terrace;[]
11323;Le Sable;Netherlands;Veldhoven;Zandoerle 5, Veldhoven, 5507 RJ, Netherlands;51.4140055;5.3584872;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This old farmhouse radiates all the charm of the peaceful hamlet of Zandoerle – diners will particularly enjoy the welcome given by the ducks. Inside, the hushed and intimate ambience combines rusticity with modern elegance. They may be young, but chef Chiel and maître d' Laura bring a wealth of talent and experience to the table, delivering cuisine that reflects their youthful enthusiasm. Although he draws primarily on French cuisine tradition, the chef likes to add his own twist, serving dishes in a series of small plates. Think candied lamb, alongside a lamb shoulder stew (with a wonderfully intense jus!) and a medium-rare rack of lamb. The palpable sense of ambition at Le Sable makes it all the more appealing.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11324;Domenica;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Noordermarkt 7, Amsterdam, 1015 MV, Netherlands;52.3801212;4.887348;45;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;Domenica is the place to come to experience the bustling Jordaan neighbourhood. Whether you are dining outside on the terrace or inside at the bar of this modern bistro, there is always a lively atmosphere here. Authentic Italian seasonal dishes are served up with great skill and a proper sense of generosity. Think octopus with crispy skin and tender meat served alongside robust bell pepper and broccoletti. Owner Flavio pays tribute to his heritage with every vibrant plate. Be sure to check out his French and Italian wine selections too.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11326;Morille;Netherlands;Koudekerke;Biggekerksestraat 3, Koudekerke, 4371 EW, Netherlands;51.4835059;3.5516384;79;true;false;Regional Cuisine;At Morille, they strive to source all their produce from within a 15km radius of the restaurant. It feels like nature has taken root in this cosy place – and with good reason. Floris Vriens has taken over the reins and is maintaining the restaurant's commitment to sustainability: ingredients harvested from his own kitchen garden, foraged in the wild or purchased from producers in the vicinity are presented in a 14-course set menu accompanied by drinks sourced solely from the Netherlands and Belgium. This inspired, modern culinary approach – with its respect for micro-seasons – is an ode to Zeeland's (mostly vegetable-based) riches.;;[]
11327;Suzie's en Van Aken;Netherlands;Oegstgeest;Geversstraat 63a, Oegstgeest, 2341 GC, Netherlands;52.1768631;4.468193;37;false;false;French, Modern Cuisine;Chef Tom is no stranger to the concepts of nose-to-tail eating and zero waste. With a keen sense of the zeitgeist, this is a creative chef who draws inspiration from his extensive travels, especially to Asia. For example, a beurre blanc sauce with dashi that adds depth to a salty dish based on oyster and samphire. The jovial Suzanne plays her part, serving up excellent wine and dessert recommendations. The natural vibe of this cosy establishment will make your dinner that little bit more enjoyable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11328;Rozewied;Netherlands;Kortgene;Hoofdstraat 35, Kortgene, 4484 CB, Netherlands;51.5568836;3.80195;99;false;false;Farm to table;Rozewied, "poppy" in Zeelandic, is the joint venture of Ferdy and Noëmie. The two of them do everything themselves in this centuries-old building, into which they have breathed new life, while taking care to preserve its historical character. In the kitchen, classical combinations are given a modern twist. Lamb, for example, is paired with garlic, but with the lightness and playfulness expected by today's diners. The chefs give pride of place to European produce, and have a penchant for fish dishes and delicate sauces.;Terrace;[]
11330;Lime;Netherlands;Malden;Kerkplein 2, Malden, 6581 AC, Netherlands;51.7807563;5.8502149;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The open kitchen immediately catches the eye at the contemporary Lime, which also has a charming veranda. A table by the kitchen is a must if you want to see accomplished chef Ysbrandt Wermenbol at work. He gives traditional dishes a carefully considered personal twist, often taking inspiration from Mediterranean and Asian cuisine. His surprising ideas dare to be complex, while retaining a sense of generosity and balance.;Terrace;[]
11331;Katseveer;Netherlands;Wilhelminadorp;Katseveerweg 2, Wilhelminadorp, 4475 PB, Netherlands;51.5400135;3.8703319;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Having taken over Katseveer, chef Leon Vermaire and maître d' and sommelier Paul Labruijere are steadily finding their feet. For many years, they have been working at this restaurant that showcases the best of what Eastern Scheldt has to offer. This former ferry waiting room commands stunning views of passing ships and the surrounding countryside.Zeeland produce reigns supreme in chef Vermaire's culinary world. Whether Zeeland venison or North Sea crab, top-notch, locally sourced ingredients play the starring role. His dishes – often really creative – are beautifully crafted and frequently use acidic Asian flavours for that fresh twist.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11332;Harry's;Netherlands;Maastricht;Wycker Brugstraat 2, Maastricht, 6221 EC, Netherlands;50.8495878;5.7005616;22;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;This luxury brasserie is as cosmopolitan as it is vibrant. French flair characterises both the ambience and the cuisine. On the menu, international flavours and vegetarian options show that the chefs are keeping up with the times, but not at the expense of the golden rules of superior brasserie cuisine. The kitchen garden is a manifestation of their sustainable approach (more details on the website). Creative, local, seasonal: Harry's ticks all the boxes!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11333;Kruiden & Jasmijn;Netherlands;Woudrichem;Kerkstraat 43, Woudrichem, 4285 BA, Netherlands;51.8160768;5.0029868;79;true;true;Farm to table, French Contemporary;Located just inside the historical city walls, this is an elegantly appointed restaurant featuring modern art and imposing chandeliers. The terrace exudes tranquillity, and the attentive service creates a warm and welcoming atmosphere. A passionate advocate for local produce, chef Patrick de Rade especially loves Eastern Scheldt lobster when it is in season. He also regularly harvests fruit and vegetables from his garden. Sourced from a friendly local farmer, red cabbage adds a touch of sweetness to his venison fillet, perfectly complementing the sweet-and-sour pickled red beets. His rich sauces are testament to his culinary expertise and generosity.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11334;Nolet's Vistro;Netherlands;Yerseke;Burgemeester Sinkelaan 6, Yerseke, 4401 AL, Netherlands;51.4955027;4.0508932;43;false;false;Seafood;Zeeland oysters, grilled lobster and smoked eel from the Eastern Scheldt are just a few of the reasons why you’ll want to book a table in this charming bistro. Here, you won’t find any unnecessary fuss, just pure cuisine based around superb ingredients of the freshest quality. A generous spirit is also part of the Nolet’s Vistro DNA!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11335;La Mère Anne;Netherlands;Oudendijk;Dorpsweg 110, Oudendijk, 1631 DJ, Netherlands;52.6017575;5.0033263;19;false;true;Regional Cuisine;La Mère Anne is a huge business encompassing a range of activities. You can hire the venue for parties, spend the night in modern guestrooms, but above all, enjoy good food! The chef favours regional produce, which he showcases in contemporary dishes. These steer clear of frills, focusing instead on straightforward, delicious flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11336;Salon de Provence;Netherlands;Breda;Ginnekenweg 172, Breda, 4835 NH, Netherlands;51.5730665;4.7830921;66;true;false;Creative, Modern French;An ambitious duo has taken over this cosy restaurant in which distinguished service, meticulously selected wines and creative, lovingly prepared cuisine are to the fore. Vegetables play a predominant (and playful) role here, while inspirations from around the globe, with a small focus on South Africa, are also evident on the menu and wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11337;De Voetangel;Netherlands;Ouderkerk aan de Amstel;Rondehoep Oost 3, Ouderkerk aan de Amstel, 1191 KA, Netherlands;52.2795523;4.9258563;69;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This cosy family restaurant rises up out of the Ronde Hoep polder, from where it enjoys magnificent views across pastureland and streams. The chefs here veer more towards the traditional, although modern dishes are starting to creep into their cuisine. Organic, vegetarian and international options give the menu extra appeal.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11338;Joia;Netherlands;Oudewater;Havenstraat 2, Oudewater, 3421 BS, Netherlands;52.0221895;4.8722365;85;false;false;World Cuisine;To share or not to share, that's the dilemma awaiting you at this charming brasserie. Once a café, it enjoys a picturesque location beside the canal and boasts a delightful waterside terrace. The enticing menu features international cuisine – deciding will not be easy. Will it be the creamy risotto with mushrooms, a venison dish with a rich cognac-based sauce and green peppercorns, or the yellowtail kingfish with Tomasu soy sauce and passion fruit? Joia has something for everyone. N.B. Simpler lunch menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11339;Elea;Netherlands;The Hague;Noordeinde 142, The Hague, 2514 GP, Netherlands;52.0825984;4.3055209;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Greek;Located in a grand building in the heart of The Hague, Elea is a modern restaurant with a Greek soul. This idea finds expression in a fabulous Mediterranean-style setting that incorporates natural materials. Takis Panagakis is an inventive chef who draws on Greek tradition, using ingredients such as smoked yoghurt, caper leaf and fava beans to lend his original creations an individual touch. Vegetables play an important role here, with top-notch vegetarian options, such as a celeriac Wellington. The charming Bibi is on hand to suggest some excellent wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11340;Oxalis;Netherlands;Wervershoof;Dorpstraat 9, Wervershoof, 1693 AB, Netherlands;52.7274387;5.151762;31;false;false;Creative, Modern French;Prepare yourself to be blown away as you drive past fields full of red and white cabbages en route to this cosy little establishment housed in a former post office. Geoffrey van Melick cut his teeth at top-flight restaurants such as The Fat Duck and 't Nonnetje, and it shows in his selection of quality ingredients, the depth of his sauces and his meticulous garnishes. Take, for example, the perfectly pitched and beautifully reduced veal jus that accompanies the rich fillet of veal Rossini, with fine vegetable accompaniments that add their distinctive nuances. This chef proves that creativity need not be at odds with respect for tradition!;Terrace;[]
11341;Noble;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Wilhelminaplein 1, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5211 CG, Netherlands;51.6828128;5.2948973;23;false;true;Contemporary;Noble pays tribute to the rich history of this building, which once housed Chalet Royal. Having undergone a drastic makeover, the decor features a blend of sleek design and warm materials. Wine is a serious business here, which becomes clear when you see the imposing cabinet. Thanks to the small portions, you can explore how global influences and attention to freshness create tantalising flavours. We were delighted by the chocolate mousse with peanuts, unctuous ice cream with bay leaf, crunchy caramel and a citrus cream. The bold combinations on the extensive menu never fail to impress!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11342;Landgoed de Wilmersberg;Netherlands;De Lutte;Rhododendronlaan 7, De Lutte, 7587 NL, Netherlands;52.3094692;6.95988;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Organic;At Landgoed de Wilmersberg nature takes centre stage, beginning with a wonderful view of the landscape of Twente, both on the terrace and in the charming dining room. The chef makes vegetables the focus in his modern dishes. He is bold enough to present the occasional challenging combination, always applying the correct techniques.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11343;Citrus;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Lange Putstraat 7a, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5211 KN, Netherlands;51.68702;5.305577;77;false;true;Farm to table;Paul Hermes and Jill van Orsouw treat their guests like friends in their intimate, convivial restaurant. The chef, who can be seen at work on his “podium” to the rear of the dining room, likes to bring his carefully prepared dishes to the table himself. He prepares dishes which are full of different textures and flavours, showcasing exciting ideas and delighting guests with his rich cuisine.;;[]
11344;Het Roode Koper;Netherlands;Leuvenum;Jhr. Dr. C.J. Sandbergweg 82, Leuvenum, 3852 PV, Netherlands;52.306608;5.7131023;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At Het Roode Koper, diners are immersed in the fairytale setting of a romantic decor that exudes luxury and sophistication, set against fabulous English gardens and the forests of the Veluwe all around. Dennis van den Beld's cuisine is rather classical but in keeping with the times. This translates into fabulous sauces, an emphasis on the produce and creative garnishes. The excellent wine list offers both prestigious bottles and finds from small wineries.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11345;Japans restaurant Shiro;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Uilenburg 4, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5211 EV, Netherlands;51.688;5.29967;55;true;false;Japanese;Shiro has been famed for serving traditional Japanese cuisine since 1989. In this intimate restaurant you will discover all the delights of kaiseki-ryori cuisine – a traditional interplay of intense flavours and subtle textures. Sushi made with the finest rice and ultra-fresh fish (it's best to order sushi when you make your reservation), beautifully crispy shrimp tempura, a deeply aromatic teriyaki sauce... Accompanied by exciting sake recommendations courtesy of your hostess.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11346;Hof van Herstal;Netherlands;Peij;Pepinusbrug 8, Peij, 6102 RJ, Netherlands;51.08775;5.921277;96;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;What used to be the guesthouse of Lilbosch Abbey is now a classic fine dining restaurant with bags of character. Martin Bruggeman takes great pride in his work, presenting his suggestions to guests and proving every day that he is a master of traditional cuisine. Try the game dishes, especially the venison – the chef slaughters the game himself and showcases the distinctive intense flavour of the meat. His generous sauces are the best evidence of his culinary skill. You can trust his judicious wine recommendations too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11347;Aan Sjuuteeänjd;Netherlands;Schinnen;Dorpsstraat 74, Schinnen, 6365 BH, Netherlands;50.943868;5.881862;22;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Sustainability takes centre stage at this cosy farmhouse restaurant with its eye-catching designer lighting. Even before it was trendy, chef Thoma was working with organic produce, mostly from his own vegetable garden. He has now even planted a food forest for the future. This ambassador of local Limburg produce proposes only a surprise menu, demonstrating his close ties with small-scale suppliers. Think rosefish from the North Sea, a beautifully grainy spelt risotto and a spicy/tangy beurre blanc sauce with nettles.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11348;Allemansgeest;Netherlands;Voorschoten;Hofweg 55, Voorschoten, 2251 LP, Netherlands;52.1331416;4.4685066;71;false;false;Modern French;The Vliet canal provides the stunning backdrop to this former farmhouse with an elegant decor. The waterfront terrace (with mooring facilities) will take your breath away. This is the perfect setting in which to savour a modern approach to French cuisine that is replete with subtle exotic nuances. How about tuna with foie gras, foie gras ice cream and a spicy vinaigrette? A surprising culinary delight!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11349;Stiel Oriental;Netherlands;Schagen;Markt 23, Schagen, 1741 BS, Netherlands;52.7862471;4.7963607;49;false;false;Indonesian, Fusion;Stiel exudes an Oriental vibe – with bright Eastern motifs, warm tones and wicker furnishings, this is as cosy as it gets and you immediately feel at home. The front-of-house team is beautifully in sync with the enthusiastic kitchen brigade, who you can see at work in the open kitchen. Often inspired by Indonesia, their wide range of dishes to share (a regular menu is also available) pack the spicy punch you would expect. House-made dim sum with veal and five spices, a rich curry with prawns, juicy satay kambing – this is a veritable feast for the taste buds!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11350;DIELS;Netherlands;Wageningen;Vijzelstraat 2, Wageningen, 6701 DC, Netherlands;51.9649945;5.6640115;65;true;true;Modern French;Dietmar and Elsko's restobar is a friendly, relaxed spot where diners can come for a full dinner or a pleasant drink. The chef draws inspiration from across the borders and serves modern dishes prepared with an eye for detail.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11351;'t Golfje;Netherlands;Midsland;Heereweg 22a, Midsland, 8891 HS, Netherlands;53.3875385;5.285946;30;true;false;Modern French;Housed in a quintessential Terschelling farmhouse just outside Midsland, this is a charming restaurant where diners are made to feel right at home. The gorgeous natural surroundings not only foster a mood of tranquillity, but they also determine what ends up on your plate. Many of the ingredients are picked by the staff themselves or sourced from the restaurant's own vegetable garden. These then feature in modern dishes which also draw on Mediterranean and Asian influences. This is no-nonsense cuisine. Think a perfectly fried quail fillet, a robust chicken stock and Jerusalem artichoke in cream and deep-fried. Divine!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11352;Lokaal;Netherlands;Doetinchem;Ruimzichtlaan 150, Doetinchem, 7001 KG, Netherlands;51.972502;6.2886379;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Nowadays, Villa Ruimzicht is both a hotel and home to this elegant and chic yet warm and welcoming restaurant. The name Lokaal can be translated as "classroom" and is a nod to the building's past as a school. But it is also much more than that: it reflects the commitment of Bjorn Massop and his team to sustainability. They source everything from vegetables to meat and fish from local small-scale suppliers who share their values. This dining experience is a real education. For instance, you will learn that coffee grounds are used to lend earthy notes to a medlar and sherry dessert. Embracing a zero-waste philosophy fuels the chef's innovation. For example, by fermenting spruce in a vegetable broth, he creates a harmonious accompaniment to trout from De Smallert fish farm. The set menu is a celebration of the riches of the Achterhoek terroir.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11353;Villa de Duinen;Netherlands;Noordwijk aan Zee;Oude Zeeweg 74, Noordwijk aan Zee, 2202 CE, Netherlands;52.239571;4.4335738;89;true;true;Modern French, Mediterranean Cuisine;Arriving at this Anglo-Norman-style villa (1902) feels like coming home. The cosy interior, reminiscent of a cottage, and the endearing personality of the hostess are irresistible. The youthful kitchen team favours a resolutely modern approach to cooking. They play with textures, allow the main ingredient to shine and sometimes come up with surprisingly imaginative ideas. Hand them a butternut squash, and they will turn it into something amazing, with great technical skill and subtle influences from around the globe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11354;Plantage 87;Netherlands;Oude-Wetering;Plantage 87, Oude-Wetering, 2377 AE, Netherlands;52.2037838;4.6447028;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Cuisine from the Marches;The first thing that strikes you at Plantage 87 is the phenomenal view of the surrounding marina. Stephan Möllers's biggest source of inspiration, however, lies a little further away, in his generously sized vegetable garden. He likes to express his creativity by working with vegetables so that they yield the right acidity or spiciness to bring out the best of the main ingredient – letting it speak for itself.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11355;Pirandello;Netherlands;Landgraaf;Tunnelweg 99, Landgraaf, 6372 XH, Netherlands;50.8729639;6.0281011;69;false;true;Italian;A trendy restaurant with charming views of vines and a stork’s nest, as well as one of the most attractive outdoor terraces in the Netherlands! Both the cuisine and the wine list have a strong Italian focus, the former offering authentic flavours with the occasional daring twist. The option of overnight accommodation completes the picture.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11356;Restaurant De Lage Vuursche;Netherlands;Lage Vuursche;Dorpsstraat 2, Lage Vuursche, 3749 AD, Netherlands;52.1793559;5.2223508;81;false;false;Classic Cuisine, French;This restaurant was opened by Willem van Oosterom in 1865 and is now run by the fifth generation of his family. Authentic details, such as a fireplace and wooden tables, add to the charm of this quintessential Dutch café and restaurant, which also boasts a delightful terrace. The kitchen team takes pride in serving up traditional French cuisine. Perfectly pan-seared scallops with blood sausage and a rich bisque, crispy sweetbreads and succulent veal tongue with a Bordelaise sauce, and a delectable Eton Mess to finish: a symphony of flavours awaits! The nearby woods are ideal for a tranquil post-prandial stroll.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11357;Marque;Netherlands;Hoorn;Bierkade 2, Hoorn, 1621 BE, Netherlands;52.638397;5.061109;48;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The open kitchen and spacious bar (which you can eat at) will grab your attention as soon as you walk into this former cheese warehouse (1618). The character of this property is enhanced by the elegant decor. Marque is proud of its Mediterranean soul, and the experienced head chef wins diners over with modern textures, delicate acidic touches, and all the panache and exuberance of the South.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11358;MARIO;Netherlands;Wijdewormer;Neck 15, Wijdewormer, 1456 AA, Netherlands;52.5083062;4.9197846;33;true;true;Italian;A former inn on a dyke across from a canal. Italian cuisine featured on the single menu. Elaborate Italian wine list and excellent advice from the sommelier-owner. A handful of well-kept rooms with good bedding.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11359;De Beejekurf;Netherlands;Venray;Paterslaan 15, Venray, 5801 AS, Netherlands;51.5221283;5.9735796;54;true;true;Modern French;De Beejekurf manages to blend a cosy, inviting atmosphere with sophisticated elegance. Hostess Hanneke's warm welcome and attentive service make dinners feel at ease right away. Chef Mathijs Jacobs allows his local suppliers to dictate what goes into his set menu. His creativity knows no bounds, yet his dishes, although made with an eye for detail, are remarkably straightforward. For example, he transforms poached veal tenderloin with its exquisite jus and sweetbreads into an interesting concoction with aubergine, a hollandaise sauce espuma, potato mousseline and truffle. This is cuisine that packs a punch!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11360;Zheng;Netherlands;The Hague;Prinsestraat 33, The Hague, 2513 CA, Netherlands;52.0787457;4.3060036;56;true;false;Fusion;Zheng takes you back to the banquets of Imperial China. Through a parade of small dishes, often served on three plates, you will discover the traditions of the four main branches of Chinese cuisine. The succulent Peking duck, with its crispy skin, is deservedly a signature dish – it is heavenly when paired with hoisin sauce and the house-made sambal! The typical tableware and objets d'art (also for sale) add to this unique dining experience. Subtle cuisine which nonetheless offers a wealth of flavours.;Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11361;Soigné;Netherlands;Bussum;Kapelstraat 16, Bussum, 1404 HX, Netherlands;52.2745479;5.1646119;17;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;At Soigné, which might be described as cosy and charming, you are in the right place to discover the contemporary culinary aspirations of Dennis Jong. He makes an impression by complementing familiar flavours with exotic ingredients and rich sauces. The adjoining room can be booked for private dinners.;Terrace;[]
11362;Sequenza;Netherlands;The Hague;Spui 224, The Hague, 2511 BX, Netherlands;52.0756248;4.3190071;67;true;false;Farm to table;The intimate Sequenza has conquered a place in the hearts of its many regulars, who keep coming back for the French-influenced market menu, offering a selection from a limited number of dishes. The choice is small and the flavours are big. The high quality produced by the chef bears witness to real knowledge of his craft.;Terrace;[]
11363;'t Havenmantsje;Netherlands;Harlingen;Havenplein 1, Harlingen, 8861 XA, Netherlands;53.1751355;5.4124627;20;true;false;Modern French;A spot in the conservatory is an absolute must when you come to this restaurant in a converted courthouse – the view of the water and the passing boats is magnificent! The restaurant is open throughout the day, so you can come for lunch, high tea or dinner. The chef skilfully navigates his way between classic and modern culinary traditions. For instance, he won't do too much to a steak tartare, but then he will conjure up a vegetarian dish based on roasted fennel and an apple jus. Be sure to check out the Asian-inspired appetisers.;Great view,Terrace;[]
11364;Wox;Netherlands;The Hague;Lange Voorhout 51, The Hague, 2514 EC, Netherlands;52.0820646;4.3140405;33;true;false;Asian Influences, Modern Cuisine;The name gives you an inkling of the ambience here and the interior confirms it: this flashy brasserie is an ultra trendy venue. Fashionable Franco-Asian dishes feature on the menu, as well as phenomenal wines with a good selection available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11365;'t Pestengasthuys;Netherlands;Zwolle;Weversgildeplein 1, Zwolle, 8011 XN, Netherlands;52.5133575;6.0970068;20;false;false;Farm to table;The red-brick façade, mezzanine floor and modern dining area with a high ceiling and timber beams lend this location (1450) plenty of character. A spot under the tree is perfect for a romantic dinner of a summer's evening. The hostess wins diners over with her jovial manner, as does her husband with his generous contemporary cuisine with a preference for local, organic ingredients. He does not shy away from more down-to-earth produce such as rabbit, and he respects traditions.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11366;Pollevie;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Hofvijver 2b, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5223 MC, Netherlands;51.6849898;5.2886395;86;true;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Martin Berkelmans has a passion for vegetables. He sources them from a food forest and a local farm and likes to experiment with them in his fermentation lab. The versatility of vegetables makes his dishes both playful and intriguing – they dictate the culinary direction, although meat and fish are also incorporated into his cooking. The succulent partridge breast and the rich stew are elevated to new heights with parsley root, a vegetable and walnut purée and a robust sauce featuring cassis for a sweet-and-sour note. The slightly industrial feel and organic vibe lend this inviting restaurant a unique character.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11367;Tante Kee;Netherlands;Kaag;Julianalaan 14, Kaag, 2159 LA, Netherlands;52.2172069;4.5584448;36;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Asian Contemporary;The back and forth of the ferry bringing guests to this magnificent establishment makes for a wonderful spectacle in the evenings. Inside, the decor has been given a makeover and creates a modern yet intimate atmosphere, with the surrounding water playing an integral part in the overall look. The intriguing flavour combinations in the modern, occasionally oriental dishes provide the basis for an exciting culinary experience. Think an exotic/fresh/zesty combination of mango, passion fruit, coconut and fried rice noodles. Dinner at Tante Kee is quite an adventure!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11368;Faulk;Netherlands;Bussum;Herenstraat 26, Bussum, 1406 PE, Netherlands;52.2733977;5.1583446;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Menno and Monique ensure that everything is to your liking in their cosy neighbourhood bistro. The ambitious, contemporary-style dishes are presented in a thoughtful, balanced way. The friendly enthusiastic service is also an indicator that this couple have a bright future ahead of them.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11369;Choux;Netherlands;Amsterdam;De Ruyterkade 128, Amsterdam, 1011 AC, Netherlands;52.3776924;4.9066171;23;false;false;Modern French, Vegetarian;Cabbage in winter, peas in spring, tomatoes in summer, kale in autumn: in this trendy, industrial-style restaurant, seasonal produce takes centre stage. Embracing sustainable practices, this restaurant places the emphasis on vegetables and boasts an extensive selection of organic and natural wines. Merijn van Berlo uses his creativity to bring intensity to the plate. For instance, he infuses spelt risotto with chlorophyll in a smoked eel broth and combines it with an emulsion of horseradish and pike-perch gravlax. This cuisine bursts with floral and spicy notes and just the right amount of kick to bring the seasons to life. A captivating ode to nature's rich bounty!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11370;Lyf's;Netherlands;Beetsterzwaag;Hoofdstraat 73, Beetsterzwaag, 9244 CM, Netherlands;53.0592735;6.0801538;30;true;true;Farm to table;One of this neighbourhood restaurant's main assets is its convivial atmosphere. The commitment to quality is palpable on every plate that is brought to your table. Martijn Stroosma serves up beautifully presented dishes that showcase his creativity. This astute chef never goes over the top. For instance, he will mellow the combination of langoustine tail tempura and confit bacon with touches of mango and celeriac. He always strikes the right balance, including in the mouth-watering à la carte and lunch options.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11371;Gebr. Hartering;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Peperstraat 10hs, Amsterdam, 1011 TL, Netherlands;52.3716619;4.9075126;78;false;false;French, Fusion;Niek and Paul Hartering share a love of ingredients. This cheerful venue proposes a short menu, which changes regularly, as the fusion cuisine depends on the ingredients at their best on the day. Flavours don't lie.;;[]
11372;Buitenplaats Slangevegt;Netherlands;Breukelen;Straatweg 40, Breukelen, 3621 BN, Netherlands;52.1580967;5.0183297;88;true;true;Farm to table, Creative;The River Vecht is the star of the show at this warm and welcoming restaurant – the riverside terrace alone is reason enough to book a table! Another draw of this place is the extremely attentive service. The cuisine here is playful and creative. Classic combinations are elevated with original ideas and exquisite textures. The chef also enjoys adding a touch of spice to his sauces for that extra kick.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11373;Beulings;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Beulingstraat 9, Amsterdam, 1017 BA, Netherlands;52.36808;4.8877497;44;true;true;Contemporary;Beulings is a little gem full of atmosphere. Lisja offers guests a warm welcome, and is also in charge of the excellent wines, while Bas and his team create delicious meals in the open kitchen. They put a lot of effort into the preparation of their dishes, which are full of versatile textures and carefully thought-out flavours. A delightful experience!;;[]
11374;EN;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Dusartstraat 53, Amsterdam, 1072 HP, Netherlands;52.3511279;4.8894807;69;true;true;Japanese;Whether you opt for one of the seven seats up at the counter or for a regular table, there is no escaping EN's vibrancy. This energy is also reflected in the food. The set menus introduce you to creative Japanese dishes including an original take on tuna sashimi. The à la carte options, on the other hand, are more traditional. Whatever you choose, you can count on the characteristic finesse and richness for which this cuisine is world-renowned. The extensive sake selection is terrific.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11375;Brasserie van Baerle;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Van Baerlestraat 158, Amsterdam, 1071 BG, Netherlands;52.3539359;4.881296;43;false;false;Classic Cuisine;There is no getting around it: wine is part of the core business of this elegant, ever-inviting luxury brasserie. The impressive selection of wines by the glass and extensive drinks menu will impress even the most seasoned connoisseur. Classics from the brasserie repertoire are served up here with great attention to detail and a sense of generosity. The steak tartare is a real crowd pleaser.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11376;Ledeboer;Netherlands;Almelo;Wierdensestraat 2, Almelo, 7607 GH, Netherlands;52.3553643;6.6636456;50;true;false;Farm to table;Until 1994 this stately building housed a bank. Today retro and industrial features complement one another beautifully at this trendy restaurant offering quick snacks as well as larger meals, with the top choices on the set menu. The chef produces modern combinations with a sophisticated twist. At Ledeboer, taste reigns supreme.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11377;De Jonge Dikkert;Netherlands;Amstelveen;Amsterdamseweg 104a, Amstelveen, 1182 HG, Netherlands;52.3082149;4.8472484;89;false;false;Creative French, Regional Cuisine;De Jonge Dikkert has given a new lease of life to this windmill dating from 1672, with its chic decor, intimate atmosphere and attractive dining room with wooden beams. This is the epitome of Dutch charm! The chef has a penchant for Dutch produce and Asian seasonings. His dishes are meticulously prepared with a nod to classic culinary tradition, and always likes to delight diners with something unexpected. For example, he complements pink-roasted lamb saddle with a puttanesca garnish and an aromatic lamb jus, and he combines crispy lamb neck with a goat's cheese cream. This chef has a passion for bold flavours and creates dishes that pack a punch.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11378;Tollius;Netherlands;Amersfoort;Utrechtseweg 42, Amersfoort, 3818 EM, Netherlands;52.1506497;5.3800761;49;false;true;Modern French;With its sleek decor done out in burgundy and white and contemporary artwork on the walls, Tollius has an inviting feel. This is also down to chef Barry's expertise in producing hearty classics such as his wonderfully crispy pithivier filled with a rich combination of quail, foie gras and morels. But he is just as adept at whipping up a surprisingly zesty modern dessert involving wasabi and a lemon gel. If the extensive wine list is anything to go by, this place is certainly run by people with excellent taste.;Terrace;[]
11379;LIZ Restobar;Netherlands;Amerongen;Drostestraat 12, Amerongen, 3958 BK, Netherlands;51.9956799;5.4598834;76;true;true;Creative;The wooden horse heads on the walls, the impressive chandeliers that call to mind the wheels of a horse-drawn carriage, the partitions between the tables: you can't help but notice that you're dining in the former stables of Amerongen Castle. The terrace overlooking the castle and gardens is breathtaking! The cuisine is characterised by its use of locally sourced ingredients, French cooking techniques and a global outlook. The duck gyoza in a rich game broth with marinated mushrooms and crispy scallions says it all!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11380;Bergpaviljoen;Netherlands;Amersfoort;Utrechtseweg 180, Amersfoort, 3818 ES, Netherlands;52.1431616;5.3653789;77;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Choose your fish from the counter, treat yourself to one of the classics such as steak tartare or just opt for some tasty bar food accompanied by a good glass of wine. In this light-filled pavilion, with its Art Deco design features and spacious terrace by the beehives, you are spoilt for choice. But rest assured that, thanks to the quality of the produce that the chef has to work with, you simply cannot go wrong here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11381;Vermeer;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Prins Hendrikkade 59, Amsterdam, 1012 AD, Netherlands;52.3764859;4.9003448;17;true;false;French Contemporary;Sebastian Baquero Garces has taken over the reins at this intimate designer restaurant, which is every bit as upmarket as the NH Collection Amsterdam Barbizon Palace, where it is located. A champion of the farm-to-table movement, the chef is passionate about using the freshest locally sourced ingredients, and his creativity shines through in every dish. Think thinly sliced ​​hamachi and zolderspek (aged smoky bacon) with a subtly smoky bacon jus infused with dashi and soy. His cooking is intricate and sometimes complex. And if you would rather not commit to the set menu, you can simply dine à la carte.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11382;Bistro LOF;Netherlands;Leersum;Broekhuizerlaan 2, Leersum, 3956 NS, Netherlands;52.0082149;5.4017794;62;false;false;Modern French;The essence of nature permeates the ambience in this former farmhouse in Parc Broekhuizen, which is now a restaurant with a splendid timber framework. This is a laid-back restaurant with a modern yet rustic feel, where the experienced chef draws inspiration from Dutch produce, including from the surrounding kitchen garden. He showcases premium vegetables in a vibrant appetiser, for example, or elevates farmhouse chicken with a celeriac cream infused with curry and a rich jus. Despite their unassuming descriptions, the dishes – underpinned by modern ideas – pack a punch with their deep flavours. Cleverly devised, sophisticated and indulgent.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11383;Oud-Zuid;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Johannes Verhulststraat 64, Amsterdam, 1071 NH, Netherlands;52.3550566;4.8738725;46;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Oud-Zuid is a restaurant that is full of character. Take a seat inside to admire the trendy brasserie-style decor or sit out on the pleasant pavement terrace where you can enjoy the vibe of this neighbourhood. The chef puts a modern spin on tradition in his tempting and no-nonsense menu that has a focus on fish, seafood and organic produce. There is something for everyone in the impressive wine selection. Less than 10 minutes' walk from the renowned Concertgebouw.;Terrace;[]
11384;Karel V;Netherlands;Goes;Turfkade 11, Goes, 4461 AP, Netherlands;51.5058134;3.8888557;84;true;false;French;Oozing with character, this 1555 historic edifice on the embankment of the port of Goes leaves no one indifferent. An open fire, harbour terrace and artwork set the inviting scene in the Karel V. The youthful chef blends the intensity of classical recipes with refreshing modernity. Flavoursome, authentic food stamped with the chef’s signature.;Terrace;[]
11385;Les Salons;Netherlands;Valkenburg;Joseph Corneli Allée 1, Valkenburg, 6301 KK, Netherlands;50.8697501;5.7983963;48;true;true;Farm to table, Modern French;The Belle-Époque elegance of Les Salons is a sight to behold. The character of this historical chÂteau, the art and murals, the modern furnishings and the terrace set in the meticulously tended gardens give it that "wow" factor. The chefs put a contemporary twist on French tradition and understand the importance of precise cooking and rich sauces. Playful garnishes and fresh nuances bring their dishes to life.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11386;IJssel Restobar;Netherlands;Deventer;Worp 2, Deventer, 7419 AD, Netherlands;52.2500079;6.1511264;78;false;false;Modern French, French Contemporary;Part of the Pillows hotel, this stylish restaurant encapsulates the best of Deventer. Seating options include a lovely conservatory and a terrace overlooking the River IJssel – the perfect place from which to take in the city's skyline. Wouter van Leeuwen creates a menu that's simply irresistible. Timeless classics such as steak tartare are accompanied by contemporary creations that draw on international influences and feature playful textures. For instance, he serves a combination of North Sea crab, leek and carrot with an espuma and powdered tomato. Foodies are sure to be delighted by the wide range of options.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11387;Bisque;Netherlands;Groningen;Verlengde Hereweg 46, Groningen, 9722 AE, Netherlands;53.1987907;6.5797873;70;true;true;Modern French;Chef Niels Schievink and charming hostess Sabrina Mans's experience shines through in their inviting, intimate restaurant. Their expertise is evident in every aspect of a meal here, from the welcome to the wine pairings to the delicious dishes. The "less-is-more" approach to French cuisine relies on technical skill and a sense of balance. The chocolate and hazelnut soufflé is truly an ode to this classic dessert – not to be missed! This celebration of wonderful produce, underpinned by exquisite sauces, is captivating.;Air conditioning;[]
11388;Hof aan Zee;Netherlands;Koudekerke;Strandweg 15, Koudekerke, 4371 PJ, Netherlands;51.4788955;3.5194759;72;true;true;Scandinavian, Country cooking;Only 500m from the North Sea, this historic Scandinavian farmstead stands in the heart of the countryside. The stripped-back interior weaves a rustic spell, while the menu shines the spotlight on the rich produce of Zeeland. Seaweed, fish from the Oosterschelde, fermented vegetables, smoky flavours – superlative purity!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11389;De Keuken van Arragon;Netherlands;Fluitenberg;Hoogeveenseweg 27, Fluitenberg, 7931 TD, Netherlands;52.7504973;6.4659165;71;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Herco van Arragon’s unashamedly contemporary cuisine is based around modern techniques, a variety of menu options and home-grown vegetables. He has a good eye for quality, which he uses in his subtle garnishes to emphasise the main ingredient of a dish. The hospitality of friendly sommelier Cynthia accentuates the warmth of this rural property.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11390;De Boet;Netherlands;Urk;Wijk 1 nr 61, Urk, 8321 EM, Netherlands;52.6608559;5.5966273;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Occupying a beautifully renovated traditional carpentry house, De Boet blends in perfectly with the picturesque harbour of Urk. Here, chef Cees Kramer demonstrates his clear appreciation of top-quality ingredients through his beautifully prepared modern dishes with the occasional Oriental twist. Reasonably priced wines add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11391;Restaurant Calva;Netherlands;Nootdorp;Dorpsstraat 30, Nootdorp, 2631 CT, Netherlands;52.0429994;4.3946123;52;true;true;Modern French;This intimate restaurant is a love story in itself, where chef Tom enjoys explaining his dishes at the table and is always happy to recommend the best wine to accompany his well-constructed culinary creations. As an example, his traditional savoir-faire shines through in the way he cooks pigeon to perfection as well as his intensely flavoured sauces. His exquisite and more modern side dishes provide the perfect harmony.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11392;De Haan;Netherlands;Groningen;Aweg 4, Groningen, 9718 CS, Netherlands;53.21632;6.55699;98;true;false;Creative;Three friends have come up with an original concept: they prepare a single set menu in their open kitchen, serve the dishes themselves thus dispensing with the services of any additional waitstaff. Diners are responsible for getting their own bread and beverages. The chefs enthusiastically explain in detail how they creatively combine complex flavours. They do not shy away from contrasts, but always maintain the right balance. With a vegetarian Stroganoff – intensified by a sophisticated sauce based on Madeira, port and red wine – the chefs showcase their prowess.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
11393;Mei Wah;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Leenderweg 86, Eindhoven, 5615 AB, Netherlands;51.425871;5.4895028;85;false;true;Chinese, Cantonese;Mei Wah has been a household name since 1965. The third generation now at the helm has returned to authentic Chinese cuisine with a focus on finesse and purity, not adapting to Western taste. The result is a contemporary look with flavours from overseas, accompanied by a choice of wine or sake.;;[]
11395;Locals;Netherlands;Arnhem;Stationsplein 1, Arnhem, 6811 KG, Netherlands;51.9832755;5.9021346;27;false;false;Farm to table;Housed in the same building as Hotel Haarhuis, just across from Arnhem Central train station, Locals boasts a cosmopolitan atmosphere. Ingredients are sourced as locally as possible, according to the principles of Dutch Cuisine. The abundance of plants and warm colours reflects that philosophy. Upstairs, there is even a vertical farm. The chef delights in working with vegetables, eg incorporating lentils from the Netherlands into a curry with herbs from the farm, seasonal vegetables and briny seaweed, and most of the fish and meat are locally sourced. . This place really lives up to its name!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11396;Green;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Beethovenstraat 305, Amsterdam, 1083 HK, Netherlands;52.3379219;4.8771475;77;true;false;Creative;The sustainable Valley building, which houses Green, is a visually impressive piece of architecture. To get to this sleek, luxurious restaurant, walk through the Moltenifurniture shop, to the top floor, from where the view is stunning! Plant-based creations showcase the power of nature here, with the occasional addition of fish or meat. It is fresh, original and with surprising contrasts. Using every part of the vegetables from the seed to the leaf, this cuisine is a celebration of the produce.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11397;Ambrozijn;Netherlands;Valkenburg;Plenkertstraat 45, Valkenburg, 6301 GL, Netherlands;50.8646459;5.8268325;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative French;Previously a church, Irenekerk (1891) is now a restaurant where design reigns supreme. The organ has been converted into a bar, dark brick walls surround you, and the new roof truss is magnificent. You can also see the impressive Sven Nijenhuis in action in the completely open kitchen. This place is all the more exceptional because of the way the talented chef draws on French cooking styles and innovative techniques. He really makes his mark with his exquisite sauces and meticulous seasonings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11399;Reverie;Netherlands;Veldhoven;Dorpstraat 1, Veldhoven, 5504 HA, Netherlands;51.4022322;5.3972246;19;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Indonesian;United by a shared passion, Stuart and Luca, who met at hotel school, have turned their dream into reality with this sleek, intimate and rather minimalist restaurant. The bonsai tree in the middle of the dining space is a nod to the Far Eastern-inspired cuisine they serve. In the evening, they propose two set menus: "Taste of Reverie" and "Indonesian Menu". Drawing on classic French foundations, they add the sweetness and piquancy of Asian seasonings. The perfectly pan-seared duck fillet is accompanied, for instance, by an intense duck jus infused with the heat and slight sweetness of finely chopped chilli. A pumpkin cream married with ginger brings out the umami flavours. A vibrant and ambitious place.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11400;De Kromme Bistro;Netherlands;Hoofdplaat;Slijkplaat 6, Hoofdplaat, 4513 KK, Netherlands;51.3774129;3.6028704;23;true;true;Grills, Meats and Seafood;Walk through the wine cellar to discover this charming bistro, an extension of the renowned De Kromme Watergang. The lush garden and open kitchen, complete with a sturdy charcoal grill instantly catch the eye. With every bite, you will sense the chefs' deep-rooted passion for the seafood of Zeeland, which is showcased here in all its briny glory. Think cockles with finely chopped chives and a rich beurre blanc infused with the cockles' juices and a hint of lemongrass. But rest assured, they can just as easily barbecue a bavette steak or whip up a vegetarian creation. Brasserie cuisine with a unique twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
11401;Mearkas;Netherlands;Eastermar;Skûlenboargerwei 5, Eastermar, 9261 XA, Netherlands;53.1902945;6.0677196;94;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking;It is an 11-minute drive from the highway to Mearkas. The short journey through the stunning Frisian countryside serves as a prelude to the sense of tranquillity that awaits you in this glass-walled restaurant flooded with light. The surrounding vegetable gardens, fields, and glamping tents form the backdrop to this ode to Friesland. Chef Kees and gardener Christiaan have joined forces to showcase the finest local produce. Everything is either homegrown or sourced from nearby suppliers. In his set menu, the chef skillfully marries the hearty flavours of Friesland with a touch of sophistication, in dishes characterised by vitality and freshness. Think North Sea sole, delicately marinated in lemon, enhanced with local bacon and expressive garnishes of sour cream, fennel, lemon, puffed quinoa and paprika sorbet. A digestif by the campfire makes for the perfect ending to a uniquely serene experience.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11403;De Mark;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Durgerdammerdijk 73, Amsterdam, 1026 CB, Netherlands;52.3775497;4.9886776;99;false;true;Creative French;Leave your car outside Durgerdam and embrace the charm of this dike village as you walk to De Mark. From the terrace, you have an exceptional view over the water – simply breathtaking! The attractive interior is done out in natural tones and makes the most of the character of the building. Dinner here is a cosy affair. Each dish revolves around three main ingredients, cooked over the wood fire. Think textures of onion – from crisp and crunchy to sweet and grilled – elevated with a Zaandam mustard ice cream. The experienced chefs offer a fresh perspective on natural flavours. If you really want to explore the extensive wine list, luxurious guestrooms are available on the first floor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
11404;Il Gattopardo;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Delistraat 2, Rotterdam, 3072 ZK, Netherlands;51.9014458;4.4865796;40;true;false;Italian;Il Gattopardo is a charismatic Italian restaurant that possesses a certain je-ne-sais-quoi. The chef personally comes to your table to present his signature Sicilian dishes, which he continuously revamps with exciting new takes – for instance, crème brûlée made with butter-soft octopus alongside an exquisite potato cream enhanced with seaweed. He is meticulous both when crafting intricate sauces and filling home-made ravioli with gorgonzola. Be sure to peruse the wine list, which features a tempting array of fine Italian wines.;;[]
11405;Rosie;Netherlands;Utrecht;Lucasbolwerk 21, Utrecht, 3512 EJ, Netherlands;52.0944196;5.1258574;65;true;false;Modern French, International;Rosie is a bustling yet cosy establishment where foodies can indulge uninterrupted from noon. A love of wine pervades the place and music fills the air – the record player spins nostalgic tunes regularly. From shrimp croquettes to Jerusalem artichoke with labneh or a no-nonsense meat or fish dish: the international menu has something for everyone. This straightforward cuisine makes the most of the versatility of vegetables. Reservations are recommended!;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11406;Mont Blanc;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Govert Flinckstraat 308, Amsterdam, 1073 CJ, Netherlands;52.3563725;4.8988606;41;false;false;Savoyard, Creative;From the chalet vibe to the cowbells in the toilets, the space is an ode to French chef Thibault's native Savoie, as are the food and the selection of wines. He skilfully combines authentic flavours and creative inspirations. He likes, for instance, to work with cheese (the cheese trolley is excellent), using Bleu des Aravis to give a dish based on various mushrooms extra punch. This is Alpine cuisine with natural undertones and a focus on preparation techniques.;;[]
11407;BAK;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Van Diemenstraat 408, Amsterdam, 1013 CR, Netherlands;52.390205;4.887137;76;true;false;Farm to table;Take the stairs to the third floor of this unobtrusive warehouse (you'll need to ring the bell in the evening) to discover this rather rugged yet inviting restaurant with its splendid view over the IJ River. Benny Blisto sets great store by the origin of his ingredients, be it a carrot or ray wing. Locally sourced, seasonal produce is the inspiration behind his creativity. For instance, with slightly tart rhubarb and an exquisite beetroot sauce, he elevates a venison fillet to new heights. An exciting dining experience is guaranteed!;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11408;Het Arsenaal 1309;Netherlands;Doesburg;Kloostertuin 10, Doesburg, 6981 CC, Netherlands;52.013176;6.1338184;36;true;true;Creative;Björn de Waal has a special relationship with fruit and vegetables, which he sources as locally as possible and gives pride of place in his creative cuisine. Think mandarin orange combined with candied kumquat, a light corn foam, crispy potato chips and black truffle. The chef is also fond of cooking with game, but the vegetable accompaniments play a prominent role in those dishes, too. No visit to the picturesque Hanseatic city of Doesburg would be complete without a meal at this former monastery, a stunning blend of old and new.;Terrace;[]
11409;Arca;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Martelaarsgracht 5, Amsterdam, 1012 TM, Netherlands;52.3778475;4.8967362;38;true;true;Portuguese, Asian Influences;Top Portuguese chef Henrique Sá Pessoa is the creator of the enticing sharing menu at this trendy, cosmopolitan establishment. Traditional, home-style dishes such as gambas ao alhinho are expertly given a modern twist, perhaps even a little Asian finesse. But the portions remain typically generous. The bespoke cocktails are fabulous, as is the lunch menu in the cool bar!;Air conditioning;[]
11411;Moustique;Netherlands;Haarlem;Oude Groenmarkt 8, Haarlem, 2011 HL, Netherlands;52.3807435;4.6368529;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This highly modern restaurant in the centre of Haarlem is open almost every day. Here, you’ll find an extensive menu on which the chef showcases his experience through cuisine with an Asian inspiration and modern presentation, including a choice of vegetarian dishes and plenty of intense and authentic flavours. An impressive new arrival on the city’s food scene!;Terrace;[]
11413;Robuust;Netherlands;Vollenhove;Kerkplein 12, Vollenhove, 8325 BN, Netherlands;52.6820558;5.9479002;25;true;true;Farm to table;This warm and welcoming restaurant is run by two larger-than-life brothers: chef Raimon and maître d' Peter Ian. You can look forward to dishes brimming with distinctive flavours, as in the finely spiced beurre blanc that lends a touch of indulgence to a perfectly fried slice of cod. Such culinary excellence characterises their classic fare as well as the more creative set menu. Be sure to ask your expert host for his beer recommendations – he has some real gems up his sleeve!;Terrace;[]
11414;HFSLG Bar & Bistro;Netherlands;Zeist;Vossenlaan 28, Zeist, 3735 KN, Netherlands;52.1242646;5.2466928;20;true;false;Creative, Classic French;The cosy atmosphere at this bistro envelopes you in its warm embrace. Views of the garden, where vegetables and vines grow, contributes to this, as do the attentive service and the pared-down cuisine. The menu features both classic dishes and more sophisticated options. Whether it's the game jus to accompany the venison fillet or the beurre blanc to go with the catch of the day, this chef knows the importance of a good sauce and takes care to present visually appealing plates.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
11415;6&24;Netherlands;The Hague;Nobelstraat 13, The Hague, 2513 BC, Netherlands;52.0782292;4.305909;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;This appealing restaurant with its bright interior has an atmosphere that is welcoming and cosy, while at the same time natural and contemporary. With a wealth of experience at top-flight establishments, chef Rik and hostess/sommelier Saskia serve creative cuisine that draws inspiration from around the globe. The dishes consist of just a few ingredients that enhance each other's intensity.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11416;Concours;Netherlands;Utrecht;Biltstraat 20, Utrecht, 3572 BB, Netherlands;52.0952344;5.1275373;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located on Utrecht's Biltstraat, this stylish restaurant is in keeping with its lively and inviting surroundings. Alex Zeelenberg likes to keep the courses of his set menu a secret right up until they are served, and they never fail to impress. Whether he is spicing up a pan-fried pink duck breast with a harissa-infused poultry stock, seasoning a lentil beignet with Middle Eastern spices or incorporating the sweet earthiness of beetroot into a dessert, his creativity will take your taste buds on a voyage. Their commitment to sustainability, both in the dishes and the overall dining experience, is an added bonus.;Air conditioning;[]
11418;Aji;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Pannekoekstraat 40A, Rotterdam, 3011 LH, Netherlands;51.9236184;4.4875954;36;false;true;South American, Asian;Immerse yourself in the tropical world of Aji. The vintage, lounge-style decor exudes an adventurous spirit, a quality that Pelle Swinkels's cuisine also possesses. His technique is rooted in French culinary tradition, and he draws on experience gained in Asia and South America. He combines tuna tartare, for instance, with a spicy emulsion and leche del tigre vinaigrette, lime and crispy corn. With a sure touch, he uses flavour enhancers, such as sambai and aji amarillo, in original ways to add depth and complexity with umami, fruity and sweet notes. Intriguing!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11419;DOYY;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Hoogstraat 50, Eindhoven, 5615 PR, Netherlands;51.4338881;5.471733;96;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;DOYY offers an intimate and relaxed atmosphere with a touch of Middle Eastern elegance, reflecting the Azerbaijani-Turkish heritage of owner Yavuz. Chef Daan van Lieshout knows his French classics, as evidenced in the à la carte selection, which includes dishes such as steak tartare and tournedos Rossini. However, he also likes to incorporate Asian and Middle Eastern influences into his cooking – it is his set menu that really showcases his creativity. Think salty-sweet langoustine tartare with citrus chiboust, confit tomatoes, crispy chicken skin and a frothy bisque jus. Brace yourself for bold flavours with a spicy kick!;Terrace;[]
11420;Kale & de Bril;Netherlands;Goes;Piet Heinstraat 3A, Goes, 4461 GL, Netherlands;51.5010064;3.8881896;51;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;It would be a shame to pass up a visit to this discreet property where chefs Marc (the bald one or “Kale” in Dutch!) and Niek (the one with glasses – “de Bril” in Dutch!) certainly know how to please their guests. In their pleasant restaurant, savour Zeeland products (in particular from the “homarium”), generous flavours and subtle culinary creations that are always fascinating.;;[]
11421;Bistro Bord'o;Netherlands;Leiden;Apothekersdijk 2, Leiden, 2312 DC, Netherlands;52.1611727;4.4855062;46;false;false;Contemporary;European wines take centre stage in this casual establishment – hence the name (a pun on Bordeaux)! Start with an aperitif before digging into fine French classical fare. Rather than prissy frills, the focus is on quality ingredients, spot-on cooking and wholesome flavours! In summertime, you can even hire a rowing boat!;Terrace;[]
11422;Het Oude Gemeentehuis;Netherlands;Rhenen;Herenstraat 47, Rhenen, 3911 JB, Netherlands;51.9572122;5.5692673;86;true;false;Modern French;Once the town hall, this is the ideal place for convivial dining. Original features provide a striking contrast with the modern design and warm colours. Indulgence is the name of the game when it comes to the food. Whether you opt for the rich lobster bisque, the sea bass with the rich beurre blanc or their contemporary take on tiramisu, you will be bowled over by the skill and charm of hosts Niels Minkman and Janneke Eerbeek.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11423;Cèpes;Netherlands;Otterlo;Houtkampweg 1, Otterlo, 6731 AV, Netherlands;52.1023627;5.7785508;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Hotel de Sterrenberg's restaurant draws on its natural surroundings. The interior is sleek yet warm, combining lots of wood with concrete, and a large wooden stag's head that draws the eye. The chef believes in sourcing his produce locally, using local suppliers such as Gert van Eldik and the Veluwe asparagus farm. Diners are served a surprise menu composed of intricate and beautifully presented dishes. Think venison from the region with carefully considered vegetable accompaniments and a game jus enhanced with vermouth. A proud ambassador for the Veluwe!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11424;Auberge des Moules;Netherlands;Philippine;Visserslaan 3, Philippine, 4553 BE, Netherlands;51.281481;3.760617;42;false;false;Seafood;Mussels, lobster and other seafood from Zeeland are the stars on the menu at this atmospheric inn. Here, these delicacies have for decades been prepared according to old family recipes. The black and white pictures on the walls demonstrate the rich history.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11425;De Mandemaaker;Netherlands;Spakenburg;Kerkstraat 103, Spakenburg, 3751 AT, Netherlands;52.2535404;5.3781999;43;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;The Mandemaker has a lot of trumps up its sleeve, such as its terrace on the inner harbour, cheerful flowers, the winning combination of hip design and a cosy atmosphere, as well as the guestrooms. Excellent seasonal produce, with a focus on fish, is beautifully showcased in contemporary creations such as pickled mackerel with crispy asparagus and lime leaf cream. Fans of classics like fried sole are also catered for with appropriate generosity.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11426;Kasteel Ter Worm;Netherlands;Heerlen;Terworm 5, Heerlen, 6411 RV, Netherlands;50.8906725;5.9524449;18;true;false;French Contemporary, Asian Influences;This 14C castle is brimming with character, and a meal here promises an experience beyond compare. With its wooden floors, medieval paintings and old stone walls, the setting couldn't be more enchanting. The waterside terrace overlooking the verdant surroundings is an absolute delight! Dave Beckers's approach is refreshingly modern and his sophisticated creations frequently feature flavour profiles based on koji, yuzu and koshi. For instance, he adds extra depth to his lamb fillet and crispy braised lamb neck by incorporating powdered seaweed into the potato mousseline and kombu into the rich lamb jus. This is easy-to-enjoy cuisine that also pushes boundaries. An overnight stay in the castle makes for the ultimate grand finale.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11427;Restaurant 55;Netherlands;Maastricht;Heggenstraat 3a, Maastricht, 6211 GW, Netherlands;50.8487526;5.6908352;27;false;false;Modern French;Set in the Heggenstraat, a cosy spot in the old city centre, is this pleasant restaurant with an atmospheric, baroque-style interior. It is immediately apparent that the kitchen is run by a young team – even if they do keep the flavours classic. The prices are very reasonable too!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11428;Damianz;Netherlands;Roermond;Pollartstraat 7, Roermond, 6041 GC, Netherlands;51.1944367;5.9895739;94;true;true;French Contemporary, Asian Influences;In what was once Roermond's prison, you will be served bread and water first of all. But fear not: any culinary nods to the past vocation of the premises end there. At this restaurant, which is part of Het Arresthuis hotel, historical details and contemporary design elegantly intertwine. Chef Jeroen van Gansewinkel masterfully incorporates international influences and rich sauces into his dishes. From lamb with typically Middle Eastern seasonings such as za'atar and smoked paprika to langoustine with a tangy beurre blanc infused with basil oil, the food is complex and brimming with flavour. As they say themselves – it's criminally delicious!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11429;Red Orchids;Netherlands;Heemstede;Zandvoortselaan 139, Heemstede, 2106 CM, Netherlands;52.35929;4.609;65;true;false;Asian, Fusion;If you have a hard time making decisions, we suggest you head to this intimate, trendy restaurant where the menu brings together Japanese, Chinese, Thai and Indonesian specialities. The chef always manages to add just the right dose of spices, creating dishes full of rich flavours and crisp textures. Subtle Asian cuisine at reasonable prices.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11430;De Luytervelde;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Jo Goudkuillaan 11, Eindhoven, 5626 GC, Netherlands;51.4764517;5.4375836;59;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Karin Smits is the heart and soul of De Luytervelde. She has been welcoming guests at this converted farmhouse (1912) just outside the city centre since 1992. Diners are smitten with the stylish decor and delightful garden terrace, but the main focus remains, of course, the modern interpretation of classic flavours and the well-curated wine list. The chef will expertly fry a veal sweetbread until golden brown and knock up a robust sauce Périgueux, but he is just as adept at giving venison an exotic twist with five-spice powder. A perennial favourite!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11431;Nastrium;Netherlands;Helmond;Mierloseweg 130, Helmond, 5707 AR, Netherlands;51.47492;5.636487;54;true;true;Asian Influences, World Cuisine;(Temporary move to Paradijslaan 2-8 in Eindhoven) Two very different culinary traditions come together in this elegant villa, which is also home to the private Gani dining room. Here, chef Djailany’s Indian origins add spice to traditional French cuisine, with foie gras and langoustines served alongside ingredients such as soya and kombu, resulting in harmonious dishes full of subtle and exotic flavours.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11432;Auberge de Veste;Netherlands;s-Hertogenbosch;Uilenburg 2, 's-Hertogenbosch, 5211 EV, Netherlands;51.6889272;5.299926;35;false;false;Farm to table;Dating from 1849, this restaurant right by the river is the perfect setting in which to enjoy complex and beautifully presented cuisine. The chef prepares contemporary influenced dishes with bold flavour combinations. The owner’s passion for wine is a bonus, as are the extra dishes which can be added to the interesting set menu.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11433;Zuid by Adrian Zarzo;Netherlands;Eindhoven;Geldropseweg 5, Eindhoven, 5611 SB, Netherlands;51.4346977;5.4840851;95;true;true;World Cuisine, Modern French;Adrian Zarzo brings the world to your plate in this trendy, chic establishment. For example, you start with dim sum, then move on to an intense bouillabaisse and continue your journey with a Mediterranean take on sea bass. Zuid advocates a relaxed approach to gastronomy and is run by a chef who knows how to win over the modern diner. Be sure to drop by the bodega next door for some delicious snacks and a good glass of wine.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11434;Bistro T-bone;Netherlands;Enter;Dorpsstraat 154, Enter, 7468 CS, Netherlands;52.2905782;6.5753056;98;true;true;Meats and Grills;Everything revolves around the charcoal grill in this atmospheric establishment pleasantly situated in a quintessential old Dutch building. Whether he's barbecuing T-bone steak, a rack of lamb or sole, the chef bends the flames to his will with a sure touch. The results are dishes that are generous and brimming with typically robust flavours and character. The jovial owner will be happy to guide you through the menu, which also includes classics such as snails and onion soup – there are plenty of mouth-watering options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
11435;Het Weeshuys;Netherlands;Geertruidenberg;Markt 52, Geertruidenberg, 4931 BT, Netherlands;51.7008737;4.8597188;55;true;true;Country cooking;Striking murals with a culinary theme give this orphanage chapel (1310) real individuality. The vibrant decor indoors is certainly a sight to behold, but there is also a courtyard terrace that is idyllic in fine weather. Opt for the lunch set menu or simply let the chef surprise you with inspired and delicate creations such as choucroute and prawns with an Asian twist, or a new take on wild boar terrine – a feast for the senses is guaranteed!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11436;Infini;Netherlands;Wahlwiller;Botterweck 3, Wahlwiller, 6286 DA, Netherlands;50.81211;5.939325;70;true;false;Modern French;The interplay of modern art and rustic features make this elegant villa a lovely setting for a fine dining experience, the terrace is the prettiest of South Limburg! The ambitious chef strongly favours modern cuisine, resulting in elaborate dishes. House specialities include the highly recommended soufflé.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11437;De Knip;Netherlands;Voorschoten;Kniplaan 22, Voorschoten, 2251 AK, Netherlands;52.1067579;4.4349494;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;Tables on the sunny terrace and in the conservatory are much in demand at this long-established restaurant. The view of the shimmering Vliet canal is breathtaking! Marcel van Teijlingen's culinary creations are a testament to his attention to detail and refined palate, both in their presentation and their flavour profiles. He likes to add playful touches to his dishes, which are classic in their foundations. Think celeriac mousse finished with onion and a ponzu oil, adding vibrancy to a rich millefeuille of celeriac and oxtail. The old and the new join forces at De Knip.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11438;de Molenaar;Netherlands;Onderdendam;Uiterdijk 4, Onderdendam, 9959 PK, Netherlands;53.3351378;6.5907934;56;true;true;Creative;The charm of the converted Hunsingo windmill (1855) is as captivating as this picturesque village, and it houses a really special restaurant. Chef Kooijker works only with a surprise menu in which he brings to bear all his creativity, paying special attention to the presentation, creating elaborate garnishes and giving a new perspective on familiar flavours. Rest assured, you are in good hands here. And why not treat yourself to an overnight stay in the mill or granary?;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11439;DYLANS;Netherlands;Noordwijk aan Zee;Oude Zeeweg 63, Noordwijk aan Zee, 2202 CJ, Netherlands;52.2412166;4.4311384;28;false;true;Meats and Grills, Creative;The founder of Alexander Hotel was born a butcher's son and can be proud of this restaurant for meat lovers. The trendy intimacy of the decor, the gold elements, the hip lounge and cocktail bar all make for a magnificent venue. Many of the modern dishes are prepared on the Josper charcoal oven, resulting in robust, pure flavours. A fine côte de boeuf, a salt-crusted tenderloin to share, a choice cut of Japanese Wagyu beef: a feast for carnivores!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11440;Villa la Ruche;Netherlands;Voorburg;Prinses Mariannelaan 71, Voorburg, 2275 BB, Netherlands;52.064065;4.3525152;72;true;true;Modern French;This 19C villa is alluring, chic and inviting. The classic cuisine is the real standout feature here. The chef has a good command of his techniques and cooks with wonderful subtlety. He also regularly ventures into more modern dishes to treat his guests to a whirlwind of flavours.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11441;De Zeeuw;Netherlands;Haarlem;Nassaulaan 1, Haarlem, 2011 PB, Netherlands;52.3827889;4.6321609;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Janine and Jeroen De Zeeuw are a power couple who know exactly what they want – and their vision has been further honed by moving into this listed building. A pleasingly intimate and smart atmosphere prevails here, with art from their personal collection adding a touch of individuality. They will be happy to tell you about the sustainable concept behind their restaurant, which extends to the tableware and the close proximity of their chosen suppliers. With respect for the terroir, Chef Jeroen delivers exciting dishes rife with fresh and earthy flavours. His white asparagus, for example, is prepared with coconut and given a subtle twist in the form of a jus of clear tomato stock, vin jaune and elderflower. Meanwhile Janine wins diners over with wines she has discovered, as well as amazing mocktails and kombuchas.;;[]
11442;Bosq;Netherlands;Den Hoorn;Bakkenweg 16, Den Hoorn, 1797 RJ, Netherlands;53.0533615;4.7471282;30;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Bosq is a cosy establishment on the outskirts of the National Park, overlooking beautiful surroundings – the sunny terrace is particularly attractive – and offering the many delicacies that Texel has to offer. The chef here cooks with real Mediterranean finesse, serving a selection of smaller-sized portions. An appealing concept for a restaurant with real character.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11443;Breakers Beach House;Netherlands;Noordwijk aan Zee;Koningin Astrid Boulevard 5, Noordwijk aan Zee, 2202 BK, Netherlands;52.2418549;4.4268207;24;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Welcome to the "Dutch Riviera", where dining with your toes in the sand is sure to give you that holiday feeling. The relaxed terrace affords a wonderful view of the sea, or you can enjoy the trendy brasserie ambience inside. This is the place to come for a plate of ultra-fresh oysters and seafood, followed by classically prepared dishes in which the produce (mainly fish, of course) steals the show. Simple and delicious!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
11444;The Bishop;Netherlands;Leiden;Middelweg 7, Leiden, 2312 KE, Netherlands;52.157715;4.4945927;98;false;true;World Cuisine;The Bishop is where the bustling centre of Leiden truly comes alive. The wooden beams and supporting columns are a reminder of the building's past, yet the trendy decor and lively atmosphere give it a contemporary feel. Take a punt on the surprise menu or order from the small à la carte selection – the chef's creations include subtle nods to his Indonesian heritage. He draws inspiration from all over the world, dabbling in international flavours to create exciting dishes: serundeng and Asian spices are added to the rendang, kimchi and gochujang to the veal tartare, hot and spicy aji amarillo to the kingfish. This place is a surefire hit, especially because of the terrific wine list. Be sure to make a reservation!;Air conditioning;[]
11445;Old Skool;Netherlands;Druten;Hooistraat 22, Druten, 6651 AD, Netherlands;51.8933622;5.6105239;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Druten's old school has been converted into a restaurant with a charming retro-modern location and a menu offering a choice of modern, traditional and vegetarian dishes. Although the chef will readily produce a game dish based on pheasant, he tends towards the contemporary end of the spectrum. This manifests itself in his use of seasonings from around the globe and the presentation of the dishes. A delicious lesson for any foodie!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11446;DeliCees;Netherlands;Dordrecht;Lange Geldersekade 8, Dordrecht, 3311 CJ, Netherlands;51.8141772;4.6593483;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;You could certainly call Cees Timmerman's cuisine delicate and delectable. He scours his region for the finest produce, and likes to incorporate Mediterranean influences. For instance, he has no qualms about combining beetroot with burrata and anchovies. He proposes only a surprise menu that lives up to its name, with combinations such as pluma iberico and corn. At this elegant establishment, whose decor incorporates vintage and modern design, you are in for a full evening's entertainment.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11447;Oogst;Netherlands;The Hague;Denneweg 10B, The Hague, 2514 CG, Netherlands;52.0845678;4.3130981;37;false;true;Modern French;With its warm and welcoming atmosphere, Oogst is right at home in the cosy Buurtschap Centrum 2005 neighbourhood. There is something of the lively Parisian bistro about this place, which makes it all the more enjoyable to dine here. The set menus are always determined by what the Laantje Voorham vegetable garden has to offer. The versatility of vegetables and herbs provides subtle nuances. By incorporating herbs into ice cream and broths, chef Van Bommel gives dishes a new twist. His modern and always generous creations are fragrant with punchy flavours.;;[]
11448;Bøg;Netherlands;The Hague;Prinsestraat 130, The Hague, 2513 CH, Netherlands;52.0801043;4.3038734;89;false;false;Creative, Scandinavian;Slick Scandinavian design is beautifully executed at Bøg. You have the choice between a vegetarian menu and a meat/fish menu, both as creative as they are appealing. The pure flavours drawn from local ingredients are truly delicious.;;[]
11449;'t Arsenaal;Netherlands;Deventer;Nieuwe Markt 33, Deventer, 7411 PC, Netherlands;52.2520105;6.1539796;67;false;false;Farm to table;This traditional building next to the Lebuïnus church is now a modern, bright, no-frills restaurant. Attractive bar, patio garden with terrace amongst the church buttresses, tempting menus and attentive service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11450;Woods;Netherlands;Leiden;Haagweg 81, Leiden, 2321 AA, Netherlands;52.156873;4.4723021;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;From the magnificent sawmill next door to the wonderful waterside summer terrace to the rear, this modern restaurant enjoys a fantastic location. The chef reveals his fresh, tasty cooking style in a selection of small dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11451;Bistro de Holterberg;Netherlands;Holten;Forthaarsweg 1, Holten, 7451 JS, Netherlands;52.2912364;6.4213424;31;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Experience the charms of each season in this cosy bistro, whether it's winter by the large open fireplace or summer on the stunning terrace, offering an awe-inspiring vista of the Salland Ridge National Park. The extensive set menu features authentic French dishes that each showcase one or two bold flavours. Crispy fried sea bass fillet, langoustine sauce and boiled fresh vegetables: unadulterated flavours at their best.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11452;Mezger;Netherlands;Domburg;Domburgseweg 26, Domburg, 4357 NH, Netherlands;51.5647012;3.5059014;27;false;true;Modern French;Mezger is the dream of Jeroen and Sanne Tanis who found the perfect setting in this orangerie which they have redecorated with wood and trendy furniture. His cuisine highlights his own experience, which respects the seasons and products from the Zeeland region. He adds to this mix perfect cooking techniques and ingredients that work together to create a dream that is now a pleasurable reality!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11453;In Den Rustwat;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Honingerdijk 96, Rotterdam, 3062 NX, Netherlands;51.9182665;4.5184874;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In den Rustwat adds an exotic touch to metropolitan Rotterdam with its thatched roof, history dating back to the 16C and an idyllic setting close to an arboretum. The food here is anything but traditional, offering contemporary-style dishes with an abundance of ingredients and cooking methods.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11454;De Gaffel;Netherlands;Valthe;Odoornerweg 1, Valthe, 7872 PA, Netherlands;52.84266;6.87689;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine;De Gaffel creates a wonderful dining experience under the old Saxon farm's thatched roof and around the open hearth, which fills the rustic interior with a homely feel. Outside, the chef grows his own vegetables, working with top-quality ingredients, accentuated with contemporary techniques.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11455;Brasserie Goeie Louisa;Netherlands;Utrecht;Geertebolwerk 1, Utrecht, 3511 XA, Netherlands;52.0876191;5.1177659;57;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This brasserie shares the medieval charm of the upscale hotel, Karel V, to which it belongs. Once a monastery, the property has been elegantly decorated but has retained its original character. The chefs here like to put their own unique spin on classic recipes. They understand the value of a decent béarnaise sauce with a succulent cut of meat, but they also enjoy playing with the tartness of orange to elevate a dish based on lobster and fennel. This cuisine presents familiar flavours with an exciting twist.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11456;Dudockx Bar & Kitchen;Netherlands;Hilversum;Vreelandseweg 50, Hilversum, 1216 CH, Netherlands;52.2210718;5.1415944;63;false;false;Farm to table;Architect Dudok is the designer behind this trendy 1930s pavilion. Each table overlooks the Hilversumse kanaal, which really is something to behold as you sit on the gorgeous terrace. The resolutely modern cuisine shows a preference for organic and local produce, yet remains down to earth. This is the place to come if you want an original take on wonton or a perfectly cooked cut of meat with an elegant sauce. The restaurant also rents out boats!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11457;Restaurant Eindeloos;Netherlands;Leeuwarden;Korfmakersstraat 17, Leeuwarden, 8911 LA, Netherlands;53.201854;5.8002598;87;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;The biggest draws of this warm and welcoming restaurant are Willem Schaafsma's culinary prowess and the exquisite pairings dreamt up by his sommelier. Here, you can savour dishes made with top-quality ingredients that are sourced as locally and sustainably as possible – and all at excellent value for money. A firm favourite!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11458;Hanasato;Netherlands;Groningen;Gedempte Zuiderdiep 55, Groningen, 9711 HB, Netherlands;53.2148781;6.5670706;97;true;false;Japanese;In this atmospheric restaurant diners will discover authentic Japanese cuisine in all its glory. The chef cooks with respect for tradition and unites subtlety of flavour with precise preparation methods. The smoked sashimi and the Shabu Shabu menu are particularly popular.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11460;Hendrik van Maurick;Netherlands;Vught;Maurick 3, Vught, 5261 NA, Netherlands;51.658478;5.306266;21;false;true;Creative French;A visit to this medieval castle (1257) is an experience in itself. The wooded surroundings, the drawbridge, the courtyard... What a magnificent place this is! Inside, all that historical character meets with modern comfort. The portrait of the knight Van Maurick holding a smartphone is certainly a talking point. The menu may seem classical at first glance, but it features inventive dishes in which Dutch produce is given a French twist. This cuisine is sophisticated, vibrant and ambitious!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
11461;De Hinde;Netherlands;Hindeloopen;'t Oost 4, Hindeloopen, 8713 JP, Netherlands;52.9440185;5.4019782;61;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Harmen Ligthart has converted his grandfather's café into a cosy restaurant with an endearing and authentic soul. The view over the IJsselmeer (also from the two luxury guestrooms) is truly stunning! A stroll through the village and down by the boats is a must. Whether you opt for fish or game, you can rest assured that the ingredients are locally sourced and that the classic sense of generosity is adhered to. The pâté and fine Riesling wines are firm favourites here.;Great view,Terrace;[]
11462;Oesterbeurs;Netherlands;Yerseke;Wijngaardstraat 2, Yerseke, 4401 CS, Netherlands;51.4928246;4.0499774;86;true;false;Seafood;Lobster, oysters, sea lavender and mussels are just some of the Zeeland delicacies served in this restaurant which is decorated in warmly gilded tones. More than 80% of the dishes served here are fish based, with a richly flavoured classic bouillabaisse featuring on the menu alongside more creative fare. A true ode to Zeeland.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11463;Sillyfox;Netherlands;Veghel;Verlengde Noordkade 10, Veghel, 5462 EC, Netherlands;51.6148946;5.5292207;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences;Located at the top of a converted grain-processing plant, this delightful space combines a raw, industrial aesthetic with modern design elements. It also boasts a roof terrace affording panoramic views of the surrounding landscape. With years of experience, Joppe Sprinkhuizen meticulously crafts each dish, blending timeless French cooking techniques with international influences. For example, the entrecôte, cooked rare, is served with a bitterbal (Dutch meatball) filled with rendang, alongside beans cooked in red curry and lemongrass, plus a peanut cream and a red berry cream providing sweet and fruity nuances. The set menus are fantastic, although an appealing à la carte selection is also available in the evening.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11464;Scherp;Netherlands;Middelburg;Wijngaardstraat 1, Middelburg, 4331 PM, Netherlands;51.4991415;3.6095662;37;false;true;World Cuisine;Mart Scherp's restaurant, which also offers accommodation, merges the historical charm of Middelburg's town centre with a trendy vibe. The talented chef likes to work with Zeeland's local produce and Asian seasonings. Enticing flavours and subtle spiciness are common features, so it's no surprise that he has gathered a loyal following.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11465;Restaurant MANNA;Netherlands;Nijmegen;Oranjesingel 2c, Nijmegen, 6511 NS, Netherlands;51.8421529;5.862548;56;false;true;International;Fashionable restaurant in a beautiful old building, which acts as a backdrop for cosmopolitan, modern cuisine with a focus on fish. Attractively priced 4-course menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11466;Bistro Madeleine;Netherlands;Utrecht;Wed 3A, Utrecht, 3512 JH, Netherlands;52.0898987;5.1216438;97;false;true;Classic French;As typical as the name sounds, this place is far from being your average bistro. Rather than a stuffy decor, you can expect a 21C take on the standard bistro setting. The chef conjures up the same impression on the plate. Upon entering, you are greeted by the delicious aroma of fresh bread. Here, simplicity is synonymous with robust flavours. The modern touches he brings to the dishes add a surprising twist. Think ray wing with a roasted pepper sauce vierge, creamed celeriac and a frothy tarragon sauce. The carefully curated wine list is second to none. An atypical bistro!;;[]
11467;Wolf Atelier;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Westerdoksplein 20, Amsterdam, 1013 AZ, Netherlands;52.3830958;4.8922574;63;false;true;Modern French;Michael Wolf likes to experiment with sophisticated flavours and surprising ideas, giving diners the opportunity to test them out and then refining them to retain their best features. He is just as happy to cook up a turnip-based vegetarian take on Beef Wellington as he is to concoct surf and turf combinations that put a new spin on familiar flavours. The name Atelier is therefore particularly appropriate in this trendy, industrial-style restaurant, which is located on an old railway bridge with a beautiful view of the IJ.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11468;De Ertepeller;Netherlands;Papendrecht;Slobbengorsweg 149, Papendrecht, 3351 LH, Netherlands;51.8228187;4.6764503;23;true;true;Creative;The steady stream of boats passing by provides a captivating backdrop for this bright and airy restaurant located at a point where three rivers meet. Large windows afford uninterrupted views. During the week, Arjan Kuipers serves up an appealing selection of simple dishes, including crispy battered fish and freshly cut chips. Alternatively, you can opt for a more ambitious and adventurous set menu. A variety of textures and international flavours are expertly combined, and the dishes are beautifully presented. With an accomplished chef at the helm, De Ertepeller offers the best of both worlds, and the quality is second to none.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
11469;De Silveren Spiegel;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Kattengat 4, Amsterdam, 1012 SZ, Netherlands;52.3776519;4.8941858;17;true;false;Creative French;These two step-gabled houses from 1614 take you back in time . From the open fireplace with matching tiles to the romantic candlelit setting, silver cutlery and beautiful porcelain plates, everything here exudes Dutch charm at its best. The menu features exquisite, intricate dishes that showcase Dutch produce. The young chef has a keen eye for freshness, as demonstrated by the foamy mussel sauce he uses to elevate the salty symphony of mussels and seaweed. With its good selection of natural wines and a penchant for French labels, the wine list is definitely worth a look.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11470;Le Moulin;Netherlands;Castricum;Dorpsstraat 96, Castricum, 1901 EN, Netherlands;52.5476986;4.6669097;25;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;At the warm and cosy Le Moulin, they have been paying their respects to classic French-Flemish cuisine for more than 35 years. Frans Glas knows the importance of a sauce, like the amazing beurre blanc that he serves with the flawless sole meunière. They steer clear of unnecessary frills and everything revolves around flavour. Salmon is still smoked according to an old family recipe. His sister Yvonne provides charming service and astute wine recommendations.;Terrace;[]
11471;La nouvelle Auberge;Netherlands;Tilburg;Bredaseweg 441, Tilburg, 5036 NA, Netherlands;51.56246;5.0132;51;true;true;Farm to table;Ask for a table in the elegant glass conservatory at this intimate restaurant with its modern auberge feel and enjoy the view of the greenery outdoors. The chef here delights fans of rich cuisine with dishes which are influenced by French and international culinary traditions and made from locally sourced ingredients.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11472;Etablissement 1880;Netherlands;Groede;Markt 9, Groede, 4503 AG, Netherlands;51.3789922;3.5071193;75;false;true;Modern French;Etablissement 1880 is much more nuanced than the black and white that dominate its colour scheme. The charm of the decor and the location on Groede's historic market square make for a cosy setting. For her surprise menu, chef Mariëlla draws on flavours from around the globe and Zeeland produce. With an eye for detail, the creative chef focuses on subtle touches such as zesty garnishes and rich sauces that bind her dishes together. If you wish to extend your stay, book one of the two guestrooms upstairs.;Terrace;[]
11474;Carelshaven;Netherlands;Delden;Hengelosestraat 30, Delden, 7491 BR, Netherlands;52.2637;6.73107;60;false;false;Modern French;Carelshaven has been providing comfortable overnight accommodation since 1772, in a stunning location near Twickel Castle. Here, the chef prepares fine French cuisine using produce from his own vegetable garden, giving classic flavours a fresh twist without the need for excessive flourish.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11475;Restaurant Kasteel Engelenburg;Netherlands;Brummen;Eerbeekseweg 6, Brummen, 6971 LB, Netherlands;52.0904387;6.1348431;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this restaurant, occupying a 19C conservatory, the cooking style is modern and the wines South African. Lounge featuring an impressive whisky collection to round off the evening.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11476;Arles;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Govert Flinckstraat 251, Amsterdam, 1073 BX, Netherlands;52.3563139;4.8981164;34;false;true;Modern French;Arles brings Provence to Amsterdam. The prints on the walls of this bustling little bistro hark back to the hometown of the chef, who also shares his love of jazz music here (get a table in the dining room at the front if you prefer a quieter space). His culinary style is neo-bistro – a fresh take on the familiar flavours of French cuisine. Think the earthy flavour of beef cheeks cooked in red wine with buttery carrots or a new take on rice pudding. The set menu changes monthly and offers unbeatable value for money!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11478;Hemel & Aarde;Netherlands;Utrecht;Keistraat 8, Utrecht, 3512 HV, Netherlands;52.0922448;5.122971;33;false;false;Modern French, Creative French;Rene van der Weijden and his team move heaven and earth (Hemel & Aarde) to showcase the seasons in their cuisine. It's hard to miss the majestic building on a corner plot that houses both this restaurant and the Nox Hotel. Done out in blue, gold and white, the stylish interior makes for an opulent setting. Rich flavours derived from garums and time-honoured techniques, such as fermentation, are incorporated into modern, sophisticated creations. This dynamic chef takes a bold and creative approach to highlighting the wealth of delicious produce the earth has to offer.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11479;Oesterput 14;Netherlands;Yerseke;Havendijk 21, Yerseke, 4401 NS, Netherlands;51.494244;4.05314;65;false;true;Seafood;The oyster tanks and the Eastern Scheldt reveal all their secrets in this sparkling establishment, which is the height of contemporary cuisine. Fish-lovers are well placed here for mouthwatering sea delicacies delivered fresh and unadulterated to the plate. Those who opt for a delicious piece of meat will also find tailored dishes on offer.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11480;Puur Sanh;Netherlands;Berg en Dal;Zevenheuvelenweg 87, Berg en Dal, 6571 CJ, Netherlands;51.8197472;5.9212564;63;true;false;Creative;Puur Sanh's cuisine is captivating with its creative, daring, and exciting flavours. Chef Witte focuses on plant-based dishes and likes to think outside the box. For instance, he combines textures of pineapple with a sweet potato beignet, coconut and curry cream, spicy fennel and sesame seeds, and a potato crème brûlée. Daring, but it absolutely works! Treat yourself to a seat on the terrace and sample the wonderful selection of whiskies and wines. A feast for the senses!;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11481;Het Bosch;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Jollenpad 10, Amsterdam, 1081 KC, Netherlands;52.3355485;4.8480042;43;false;false;Modern French;From this contemporary restaurant diners enjoy a breathtaking view of the Nieuwe Meer marina. In this dream location the chef entertains diners with lavish, up-to-date dishes prepared with real know-how.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11482;Senses;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Vijzelstraat 45, Amsterdam, 1017 HE, Netherlands;52.365905;4.8932476;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Indulge your palate at Senses, where the cuisine brims with vibrant Asian flavours, invigorating acidity, and showcases a mastery of both classic and new techniques. Prepare to be captivated by the imaginative and daring flavours. The enthusiastic team behind this graceful restaurant leaves nothing to chance. The sophisticated atmosphere and fine wines are the icing on the cake.;Air conditioning;[]
11483;Visaandeschelde;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Scheldeplein 4, Amsterdam, 1078 GR, Netherlands;52.3446185;4.8903184;70;true;false;Seafood;Visaandeschelde has been a haven for seafood enthusiasts since 1999. The maritime theme of this brasserie is emphasised by details such as anchors and fish drawings on the tiles, scale patterns on the windows and the blue and white colour scheme. In this lively establishment, you can savour briny oysters, sumptuous seafood platters and the freshest fish. The dishes are rather traditional in style – it is the quality of the produce that counts. When you order lobster, expect it to be perfectly cooked and served with a subtly sweet olive oil vinaigrette with parsley and a crisp salad. The lunchtime menu comes highly recommended!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
11484;Kook Atelier op Oost;Netherlands;Oosterend;Oost 76, Oosterend, 1794 GR, Netherlands;53.0968229;4.8903551;34;true;false;Organic, Country cooking;Nature takes centre stage at this tastefully converted farmhouse, which also has splendid guestrooms. The restaurant's Nordic-inspired design and large windows that make you feel connected to the outdoors reflect the house's commitment to sustainability. The menu is centred on ingredients from the Wadden Sea and Texel, which they have either grown themselves or sourced from friendly local purveyors. Produce such as peas, algae and lamb are showcased in vibrant creations, in which techniques such as fermentation and koji add intensity and depth. This exploration of Texel's ecosystems is truly fascinating.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
11486;Reblochon;Netherlands;Haaren;Kerkstraat 45, Haaren, 5076 AT, Netherlands;51.6013766;5.2268227;83;true;true;Modern French, Asian Influences;Elise and Jurgen have transformed a charming cottage into a cosy living room-style restaurant, welcoming diners with genuine hospitality. The chef only serves a surprise menu, which he executes masterfully. Expect no gimmicks, but rather carefully crafted dishes with occasional influences from far-flung places. For instance, he combines pickled salmon with the earthy sweetness of beetroot and the umami of miso. Be sure to try the cheese board – a delicious way to discover the inspiration behind the restaurant's name.;Terrace;[]
11487;Valuas;Netherlands;Venlo;St. Urbanusweg 11, Venlo, 5914 CA, Netherlands;51.3853664;6.1680553;42;false;true;Modern French;The stunning view of the Maas River from the terrace here is something you won't soon forget. The same goes for the warm welcome you will receive and the genuine hospitality that is so characteristic of the Limburg region. At this restaurant, they aim to please, as you will see from Eric Swaghoven's extensive menu. The range of delectable options includes a rich North Sea crab remoulade with textures of potato and an exquisite shrimp bisque, a guinea fowl and rabbit paté en croûte, mackerel sashimi, as well as a Mediterranean-style risotto. The experienced chef's versatility shines through, and the value for money is exceptional. Oenophiles will delight in the extraordinarily extensive wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11488;De Rozario;Netherlands;Helmond;Markt 213, Helmond, 5701 RJ, Netherlands;51.4808446;5.6570656;86;false;false;Creative, Asian Contemporary;With its street art-inspired decor and laid-back atmosphere, this restaurant couldn't be more hip. The quirky and creative self-taught chef fuses French culinary tradition with Indonesian influences. His wonderfully hot and spicy hot-and-cold rendang is a signature dish. But he just as deftly elevates sea bass fillet with grated Belper Knolle cheese and a rich jus seasoned with tom kha kai herbs. Jermain de Rozario is always on the hunt for unconventional flavours and is accompanied on his quest by an expert sommelier with a rock 'n' roll edge.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11489;Prix de Rome;Netherlands;Maastricht;Susserweg 1, Maastricht, 6213 NE, Netherlands;50.8372626;5.6719421;45;true;true;Contemporary, Modern French;As far as Maastricht foodies are concerned, all roads lead to Prix de Rome. Inside this impressive building just outside the city centre a cosy interior awaits, in which exposed beams work well as part of the otherwise modern design of the place. The open kitchen at the back is a nice added touch. Here, chef Wouter alternates sophisticated, original creations with dishes that focus mainly on the produce. Among the favourites on the menu are the salmon ceviche and house special crispy fried veal sweetbreads. A winning combination!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11490;Broederenklooster;Netherlands;Zutphen;Rozengracht 3, Zutphen, 7201 JL, Netherlands;52.1428627;6.1954195;82;false;false;Modern French;The authenticity of this former monastery (1293) has been preserved in every detail. Where once the friars used to take their meals, you can now enjoy a luxurious dining experience in a historical setting. The ultra-modern open kitchen immediately catches the eye. Niels van Dooijeweert prepares French dishes using contemporary techniques. Turbot fried À la minute, a robust jus enriched with butter and juicy veal cheeks. For fans of such delicacies, this is the place to be. Top-notch produce takes pride of place at Broederenklooster. The beautiful guestrooms are perfect for a good night's rest.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11491;MEI;Netherlands;Amersfoort;Krommestraat 49, Amersfoort, 3811 CB, Netherlands;52.156634;5.3882072;85;false;true;Organic;Marco Blok is an enthusiastic champion of sustainable development. His menu and restaurant have been treated to a makeover, in particular the splendid counter. This seasoned chef crafts subtle dishes in which the wide diversity offered by vegetables is exploited to its full. He plays with fermentation, acidity, fruity flavours and slow cooking… Subtly balanced guest star appearances of local meat and fish.;Interesting wine list;[]
11492;Céline;Netherlands;Nieuwegein;Fort Jutphaas 3, Nieuwegein, 3439 LX, Netherlands;52.0373738;5.0999349;74;false;false;Creative;The austere appearance of Fort Jutphaas is in marked contrast to the restaurant it houses, which boasts an intimate atmosphere with subdued lighting and cosy terrace. Chef Rick works principally with Dutch produce, such as Dutch yellowtail, which he likes to season with subtle Asian flavours. This is original and modern cuisine, in which vegetables take pride of place. In fact, why not opt for the appealing vegetarian set menu?;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11493;Graphite by Peter Gast;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Paardenstraat 11, Amsterdam, 1017 CX, Netherlands;52.366685;4.8982799;72;false;false;Creative;A scanner next to an unassuming façade on Paardenstraat marks the beginning of your adventure. Scan the QR code you received when you reserved and enter this speakeasy restaurant, an intimate, nightclub-like space with trendy music playing in the background. Peter Gast's cuisine is detailed and inventive, at times even complex. This chef likes to play with tangy and sweet-and-sour nuances. For example, he combines melon and red/yellow beetroot with a zesty herb vinaigrette and various edible flowers. The mysterious Graphite is a world unto itself.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11494;Barres;Netherlands;Middelburg;Plein 1940 nr 10, Middelburg, 4331 LH, Netherlands;51.4978314;3.610351;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Edwin Dingemanse and Sjoerd Dooge's bar/restaurant exudes youthful elegance – everything here is impeccable without being stiff. Their sincere commitment to guests manifests itself in the cuisine. Diners are bowled over by the complex interplay of local delicacies – Zeeland shellfish, for instance – with influences from all around the globe. The sauces are rich and the garnishes playful, yet it is always the core ingredient that steals the show.;;[]
11495;Nazka;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Van Ostadestraat 352, Amsterdam, 1073 TZ, Netherlands;52.3539259;4.9018303;30;true;true;Peruvian, World Cuisine;You might, for a moment, feel as if you have stumbled across a wine cellar, but you will soon see that this hip South American eatery is very much at home in this cosmopolitan city. Nazka unleashes a whirlwind of bold flavours on your palate, from pisco cocktails to ceviche and other Peruvian specialities. This is exhilarating cuisine featuring a captivating interplay of spicy and sweet chilli peppers, Asian umami and the zing of leche del tigre. The well-curated selection of wines from around the globe adds extra character to this unique dining experience.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11496;Bistrobar Beaune;Netherlands;Rozendaal;Beekhuizenseweg 1, Rozendaal, 6891 CZ, Netherlands;52.0091583;5.9667484;20;false;true;French;The magnificent Rosendael Castle houses this fashionable upscale bistro that affords views over the delightful surrounding grounds. This is a seriously cool bistro bar! The wide-ranging menu proposes a range of appealing entrées served in modest portions that diners will find hard to resist. Vegetarian options, a classic cod dish, meat specialities, the house version of an eclair for dessert… You'll be spoilt for choice!;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11497;Tres;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Vijf Werelddelen 75, Rotterdam, 3071 PS, Netherlands;51.9104902;4.4986381;84;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Walking down the steps to Michael and Emy's intriguing basement restaurant is akin to embarking on an extraordinary adventure. At Tres, the vintage-style decor is pared down and somewhat rugged yet inviting. The best of what local producers have to offer is showcased here. At the expansive dining counter, you will discover the fascinating work of the inventive self-taught chef: his tangy fermentations, rich garums, complex ageing processes, state-of-the-art preparation techniques. Every season brings with it a new set menu, and it is always full of surprises.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11498;Foer;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Cruquiusweg 9, Amsterdam, 1019 AT, Netherlands;52.3686323;4.9353863;55;true;true;Vegetarian;Foer certainly has character both in terms of the stylish decor – nab a place at the dining counter if you can – and the food. The focus here is on vegetables and herbs, perhaps complemented by a fish or meat dish. Using inventive preparation techniques, Steven Broere succeeds in elevating vegetables in original combinations. For instance, he marries intense beetroot cooked in a salt crust and an emulsion of egg yolk with subtle acidity to create a remarkable flavour sensation. The select wines add to this unique sense of harmony.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11499;Bij Hammingh;Netherlands;Garnwerd;Hunzeweg 32, Garnwerd, 9893 PC, Netherlands;53.3051373;6.4943068;32;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It is impossible to resist the authentic charm of this former ferry house, from the terrace of which you can fully appreciate the lovely views across the canal and drawbridge. Inside, you can sense the building’s rich heritage, where the chef focuses on regional delicacies that showcase modern techniques and natural finesse.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11500;The Green Rose;Netherlands;Arnhem;Koningstraat 50, Arnhem, 6811 DH, Netherlands;51.9800558;5.9104888;29;true;true;Organic;Vegetables, fish or meat – the wonderful produce that the Netherlands has to offer is the biggest source of inspiration for Jin Hu and his team of artisans. He takes his cue from the micro seasons and lets nature dictate what goes into his French-Asian fusion dishes. Sustainability is at the heart of this cuisine, which is characterised by the intense authentic flavours of ultra fresh ingredients, as well as an element of surprise. Be sure to sample the extraordinary range of natural wines and special beers.;Terrace;[]
11501;Puur Zee;Netherlands;Wijk aan Zee;Van Ogtropweg 2, Wijk aan Zee, 1949 BA, Netherlands;52.49066;4.59129;24;true;true;Classic French;Master chef Imko Binnerts knows how to bring out pure seafood flavours, and how to combine them into a delicious meal. His interesting cuisine is cleverly presented, while the modern combination of flavours is as elegant as the decor.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11502;De Harmonie 23;Netherlands;Rotterdam;Westersingel 95, Rotterdam, 3015 LC, Netherlands;51.9147776;4.474545;21;true;true;Creative;Whether you opt for the 23-course tasting menu or something from the enticing à la carte selection, creativity is the hallmark of this restaurant. Marco Sommer uses his own house-made ingredients as much as possible in his ambitious cuisine. His dishes are finely balanced and unpretentious. For example, he brings together juicy chicken with a crispy crust, fried morels, Cévennes onion with a surprising pine nut stuffing, as well as a rich poulette sauce, creating a glorious ensemble. This stylish establishment, with its tranquil terrace at the back, pushes boundaries while maintaining a sense of harmony.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11503;'t Nieuwe Diekhuus;Netherlands;Terwolde;Bandijk 2, Terwolde, 7396 NB, Netherlands;52.2609595;6.1259145;62;true;false;Modern French;This old thatch-roofed farm on the banks of the Yssel provides a charming setting (including a terrace with a stunning view of the river) in which you’ll feel immediately at ease. To this splendid backdrop, enjoy international delicacies (often with an Asian influence) prepared with top-quality ingredients and well-crafted garnishes that provide the perfect accompaniment. Generous cuisine that is well thought out yet gentle on the pocket!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11504;Flores;Netherlands;Nijmegen;Kelfkensbos 43, Nijmegen, 6511 TB, Netherlands;51.846282;5.8704667;69;false;false;Country cooking, Contemporary;Owner and sommelier Elroy Slijkhuis has transformed this family-run business into a cosy gastro bistro – the tables on the patio by the wine store are much in demand! He has a clear vision for this enterprise: The emphasis is on plant-forward cuisine, with a commitment to using home-grown/local produce and ensuring the welfare of all parties. Natural wines dominate the wine list. Chef Luuk Freriks's dishes tend to be daring – even unsettling at times. He painstakingly transforms vegetables such as carrots and beetroot into a remarkable "charcuterie" platter. Koji is a tool he frequently uses to create depth, for example drying beef heart in it and then shaving it over a cut of meat to imbue it with profound intensity. At Flores, nature's bounty is showcased in the most innovative of ways.;Terrace;[]
11506;Restaurant Vannu;Netherlands;Bavel;Gilzeweg 24, Bavel, 4854 SG, Netherlands;51.5581248;4.8385449;69;false;true;Farm to table, Vegan;Today's culinary landscape is characterised by a shift towards plant-based, zero-waste dishes underpinned by long-established techniques such as fermentation and pickling. At Restaurant Vannu, Gijs Kemmeren gives his creativity free rein, incorporating all those sustainable elements into a multi-course set menu. With seaweed, for example, he adds nuance to the earthiness of beetroot and fresh celery. He also whisks up an intensely flavoursome chanterelle sauce to tie together al dente vegetables and a millet polenta cake. His cuisine is sophisticated, playful and certainly intriguing. The accompanying natural wines and juices underscore the ethos of this establishment. A memorable dining experience is guaranteed.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11507;R21;Netherlands;Amsterdam;Peperstraat 23, Amsterdam, 1011 TJ, Netherlands;52.3716408;4.9077542;55;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Start off with an aperitif at the marble counter, before being greeted by the chefs in the kitchen on your way to one of the dining areas, all of which exude a certain Scandinavian elegance. Having long worked with Sergio Herman, Orlando David has developed a vibrant style of cooking. Take, for example, his asparagus, briefly seared to lend it extra flavour, pepped up with wild garlic flowers, and served with a beurre blanc made from fermented asparagus and wild garlic oil to round off the dish with refinement. Sommelier Mattia has a keen understanding of the cuisine and complements it with judicious wine pairings. R21 delivers an exciting and creative culinary experience!;Interesting wine list;[]
11509;De Etalage;Netherlands;Geleen;Raadhuisstraat 11, Geleen, 6161 GA, Netherlands;50.9691003;5.8278447;67;false;true;Modern French;What was once a menswear shop is now a cosy bistro with a touch of Parisian charm. The fact that the young chefs have experience at top-flight establishments under their belts is evident in the dishes they create. They put an original spin on the classic combination of veal sweetbreads and onion – the beurre blanc with a hint of caramelised onion is the perfect finishing touch. These chefs have mastered the art of using flavours from around the globe to add nuance to their dishes. So, if you happen to be in Geleen one afternoon, be sure to stop by for a drink and a bite to eat.;Terrace;[]
11510;SEAson - Arsenaal;Netherlands;Naarden;Kooltjesbuurt 1, Naarden, 1411 RZ, Netherlands;52.2972289;5.1614472;71;true;true;Seafood, Seasonal Cuisine;Originally erected in 1688 as a military barracks, this building was converted many years later by renowned interior designer Jan des Bouverie. Today, the place is chic and inviting, and the terrace is a real draw on sunny days. Dennis Koopmans specialises in seafood, but does cater to meat eaters as well. If you're looking for a plateau de fruits de mer or the freshest of seasonal fish, it doesn't get much better than this. Think pan-fried red mullet and a rich shellfish bisque, with finely chopped fennel providing a hint of zesty flavour, complemented by salty samphire and crispy croutons. As the name suggests, this restaurant is a celebration of the finest and freshest seasonal produce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
11511;Savour;Netherlands;Haren;Rijksstraatweg 143, Haren, 9752 BD, Netherlands;53.1734798;6.6023886;39;true;false;Modern French;Trijntje and Jaap are making waves in this vibrant little town just outside Groningen. They go the extra mile to make their diners feel welcome, and they are always on hand to provide help or advice. Chef Jaap works with a young and enthusiastic kitchen team, and it shows: their culinary creations are well-thought-out, sophisticated and technically accomplished. For instance, they give a perfectly medium-rare venison fillet extra nuances by pairing it with beetroot and elderflower in various guises. There are some great ideas behind the set menus – prepare to be blown away!;Air conditioning;[]
11512;Restaurant Markant;Netherlands;Breda;Prins Hendrikstraat 69, Breda, 4835 PL, Netherlands;51.5725931;4.7867531;79;true;true;French, Classic Cuisine;This cosy little establishment outside Breda city centre bears its name well. The fact that the staff take great pleasure in spoiling their diners is palpable. Decorative features such as wine crates show that Markant is driven by a passion for wine as well as food. Be sure to take a look at the wine list, which features all sorts of great finds, before perusing the extensive à la carte menu. The young chef's repertoire includes classics such as œuf en gelée, as well as vegetarian options and the occasional Asian-influenced creation. His attention to quality is evident in the generosity of flavours and depth of the sauces. Some dishes are prepared right at your table, which is a nice touch.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11513;Wijnhuis De Blauwe Camer;Netherlands;Oosterhout;Kloosterdreef 3, Oosterhout, 4901 PH, Netherlands;51.6413786;4.8749943;39;false;true;French Contemporary, Creative French;The medieval site of St Catherine's Valley convent is an oasis of charm. The coach house has been turned into a modern restaurant, bathed in natural light and with a rustic vibe. There is also a kitchen garden and several hectares of vineyards (hence the wine barrels at the entrance). The food has just as much character as the site. Home-grown vegetables, influences from around the globe and spicy/subtly acidic details skilfully combined to create expressive dishes. Highly impressive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
11514;Wildlight Kitchen + Bar;Canada;Vancouver;5380 University Blvd., Ste. 107, Vancouver, V6T 0C9, Canada;49.2664456;-123.2376108;89;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Wildlight Kitchen + Bar is at the center of the quickly growing community of leləm̓ Village. This light-filled space is enhanced with natural and organic decorative elements, but the relaxed sophistication belies the serious nature of Chef Warren Chow's kitchen, where sourcing is paramount. Begin with a stunning charcuterie board that substitutes seafood for the ubiquitous meat to snack on everything from house-made salmon pastrami, marinated Salt Spring Island mussels, and pickled sea asparagus to tataki of smoked albacore tuna and cod rillette topped with cured ikura. A thick fillet of Gindara sablefish rests over soba noodles with baby bok choy for a main dish that is deeply satisfying. Finally, go for broke and order both the caramelized honey cheesecake with cardamom granola crust and the lemon tart.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11516;Bravo;Canada;Vancouver;4194 Fraser St., Vancouver, V5V 4E8, Canada;49.2477529;-123.0903323;23;false;true;Contemporary, Seafood;This buzzy neighborhood spot has no shortage of admirers, and it's not hard to see why, between the friendly, down-to-earth service, thoughtful bar program, and satisfying, lively cooking. The small menu of seafood-centric offerings changes frequently, but bold, punchy flavors are a consistent element. Guests are liable to start with raw items like oysters on the half shell, paired with fermented hot sauce made from red jalapeño, or hiramasa, dry aged in house and served with a passionfruit aguachile and cantaloupe. More substantial options might include seared Hokkaido scallops with coconut, fregola, and kuri squash, or house-made pasta like tagliolini with a Humboldt squid "bolognese," herbed ricotta, and Taggiasca olives.;;[]
11517;Nammos Estiatorio;Canada;Vancouver;3980 Fraser St., Vancouver, V5V 4E4, Canada;49.2495066;-123.0899986;28;false;false;Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine;Escape to Greece via Nammos Estiatorio, where white-washed walls, bare wood tables and loads of blue set a lovely, laidback tone. Greek fare may be plentiful in Vancouver, but the menu at Nammos is impossible to resist. Seafood figures prominently along with many influences from the Aegean and Mediterranean seas.Begin with the sardines, house-cured and served with taramosalata and carob bread, then tuck in to the dolmathes, those classic grape vine leaves wrapped around well-seasoned rice. Traditional dishes reign here, and avgolemono, with its lemony broth bobbing with braised chicken and orzo, warms you on the coldest nights. Finish with bougatsa, a round of beautifully fried phyllo layered with a luscious warm semolina custard.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11518;The Lobby Lounge & RawBar;Canada;Vancouver;1038 Canada Pl., Vancouver, V6C 0B9, Canada;49.2881932;-123.115683;49;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;In one of the city's top hotels (Fairmont Pacific Rim), find one of its hottest hangouts, The Lobby Lounge and RawBar. It makes a big impression, and not just because of its expansive space. Snuggle up by the two-sided fireplace, nab a seat by the stage, where nightly live music is performed, or pull up a chair at the marble bar—it's all on offer. The best part? It's not just about good looks and sensational sips. Snack on a variety of sushi, including salmon motoyaki, a signature roll with chopped wild sockeye, steelhead trout, avocado, cucumber and warm motoyaki sauce. Miso soup is a good bet for a cold night, and braised local octopus is a simple delight. Local salmon and steelhead figure largely on the menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11519;acquafarina;Canada;Vancouver;425 W. Georgia St., Vancouver, V6B 5A1, Canada;49.2811684;-123.1154658;92;true;false;Italian, Contemporary;With lofty ceilings and a business casual dress code, this downtown Italian restaurant has equally lofty ambitions. This wasn’t always the plan: it originally meant to open as a pizzeria, which explains the large wood-burning ovens perched up above the room. But this pivot to fine dining is less severe than it seems. Friendly, uniformed servers hardly enforce the rules, and diners can still order a la carte, including pizzas at lunch. The kitchen shines brightest at more straightforward preparations, like a wonderful, chilled tomato soup with Spanish ham or delicate pasta dressed simply. The enclosed patio offers the best mix of formality and fun.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11520;Octopus Garden;Canada;Vancouver;1995 Cornwall Ave., Vancouver, V6J 1C9, Canada;49.2724488;-123.1496845;62;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Decades in, and Octopus Garden is still going strong. There is a reason why it's still difficult to score a reservation at this quirky charmer: quality fish at a very palatable price. The namesake cephalopod decorates every nook and cranny, but kitsch aside, it's a welcoming place that makes regulars out of first-timers. Guests feast well on supremely fresh fish, and specials, like jellyfish strips tossed in garlic ponzu and peanut tofu with brown sugar, are attention-worthy. Maki can stray from tradition, as in the lobster roll on vacation, a roll with tempura Canadian lobster and creamy avocado. Nigiri, whether it's moist saba or crunchy-delicious spot prawn, are ever-changing but always spot on. There is an impressive collection of premium spirits and sake to boot.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
11521;Boulevard Kitchen & Oyster Bar;Canada;Vancouver;845 Burrard St., Vancouver, V6Z 2K6, Canada;49.2829569;-123.1236811;89;false;true;Seafood, Contemporary;It's large, with several dining spaces bearing distinctive styles, but Boulevard Kitchen & Oyster Bar ties it all together with chic, modern ease. Whether it's the imported hand-painted tile floors and marble-topped bars, the romantic lighting or the buttery leather seating, luxurious details abound. The versatile menu is as instantly likeable as the setting. Discover classics like baked oysters with creamed spinach, garlic bread crumbs and wild oregano. House-made pasta is tucked with a bevy of seafood, including Pacific white prawns, Humboldt squid, clams and mussels, while Calabrian chili bread crumbs deliver an enjoyable kick of heat. Whole cauliflower, roasted in curry leaves with green chutney and coconut turmeric sauce, is a veritable celebration of the vegetable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11522;Bacaro;Canada;Vancouver;1029 W. Cordova St., Vancouver, V6C 0B9, Canada;49.2879723;-123.1171839;21;true;true;Italian, Venetian;From its marble-clad entrance to its modern furnishings and bright colors, bacaro bridges cool elegance and simplicity, and blends right in with the upscale lobby of the Fairmont Pacific Rim. The address may be Vancouver, but this spot is decidedly Venetian with its menu leaning toward the art of cicchetti, or small bites enjoyed on the go while quaffing a glass of wine. Some of the best  include sardines in saor, and fusilloni, enrobed in a veal and pork ragu with chanterelles and red wine-braised snails, is nothing short of divine. Capesante, or seared scallops in a cannellini bean stew crowned by fish-stuffed cabbage and a baci-baci sauce, is a Venetian kiss.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11523;Café Medina;Canada;Vancouver;780 Richards St., Vancouver, V6B 3A4, Canada;49.2803152;-123.1172375;31;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The clink of glasses, the hissing steam of the cappuccino maker, even the shuffling back and forth to the counter by loyal patrons...Café Medina hums with activity all day long. This casual spot attracts locals who flock here for hearty Mediterranean-style fare. Mornings are especially great here—it's when egg dishes take center stage. The heady smell of freshly made Belgian waffles may have you trying to jump the (long) line outside, but ask nicely and they'll share a few of the hand-sized waffles while you wait. Once seated, don't waste any time deciding, as the paella is a must order. Inspired by the Spanish classic, their version is made with orzo flecked with cubes of smoky, spicy chorizo, roasted vegetables, avocado and a textbook-perfect fried egg.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11524;Sushi Jin;Canada;Vancouver;750 Nelson St., Vancouver, V6Z 1A8, Canada;49.2798331;-123.1237384;35;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;A nondescript facade and a location tucked amidst forgettable neighbors mean you could miss Sushi Jin, but don't. This place is tiny but mighty, with room for just six at the bar, plus two additional tables. It is something of a local secret, but those in the know come here for traditional Japanese served with a distinctive voice. Begin with otsumami like live lobster sashimi topped with osetra caviar in an olive oil and thick, savory soy sauce finished with fresh satsuma rind.Ankimo in a ponzu bath is brilliantly simple yet luxurious, followed up by miso soup in lobster broth that is far from humdrum. Nigiri, from hirame to anago, balance sweet and salty, but the otoro with Hokkaido uni and white baby prawn is as pretty as it is pleasing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11525;Carlino;Canada;Vancouver;1115 Alberni St., Vancouver, V6E 1A5, Canada;49.285737;-123.124405;15;false;true;Italian, Regional Cuisine;It’s only fitting that this verdant sanctuary should be tucked away on a terrace of the Shangri-La Hotel, offering a sense of placid elegance. The cuisine is inspired by Friuli, in Northern Italy (as well as neighboring Trentino-Alto Adige and Veneto) and reflects the area’s Slavic and Germanic influences—think braised cabbage agrodolce with pork cutlet Milanese. The menu displays a typically Italian devotion to simplicity, celebrating seasonal produce from local farms. Freshly made pastas are a feature, in particular regional specialties like cjarsons, a half-moon shape that might be filled with creamy beet puree and gilded with poppy seed butter. At dinner, a family-style tasting option (dubbed “fai tu” or “you pick”) puts the kitchen in charge.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11526;per se Social Corner;Canada;Vancouver;891 Homer St., Vancouver, V6B 2W2, Canada;49.2785598;-123.118276;42;false;true;Italian, Spanish Contemporary;They may occupy a corner location, but this well-run establishment deserves center stage. It's the sort of place where you might pop in for a tapa or two one night, then return a few nights later to tuck into a heartier pasta. Service is accommodating and friendly, and the menu is loaded with items that will please many diners.Nestle in to one of the side booths for an enjoyable meal. Hummus is sized generously and served with warm, freshly made flatbread. Salads, such as the heritage greens with crispy goat cheese and candied walnuts, are lovingly made. Lobster & crab ravioli in a chipotle coconut milk reduction is a top pick, while come dessert, you'll be debating between the tiramisu or pizza di Nutella.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
11528;Fanny Bay Oyster Bar;Canada;Vancouver;762 Cambie St., Vancouver, V6B 2P2, Canada;49.2787225;-123.1147629;100;false;true;Seafood, North American;It doesn't get much more tide to table than Fanny Bay Oyster Bar. Tucked on a quiet street within walking distance from the city's stadiums, this hot spot gets crowded, especially on game days, and for good reason. This menu features some of the best shellfish and seafood-driven entrees around. Should your shucking skills be slightly rusty, they'll gladly offer a primer. Whether perched at the bar or settled in at a table, raw bar items should be top of mind. Prefer cooked items? The grilled oysters, served hot and bubbly, shellacked with Creole butter and a fresh herb-flavored gremolata, will float your boat. Then, tuck in to intensely rich sablefish collar, served crisped alongside with hot-sweet peppadew puree and grilled shishito peppers.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11529;Suyo;Canada;Vancouver;3475 Main St., Vancouver, V5V 3M9, Canada;49.2540693;-123.1011891;78;false;false;Peruvian, Regional Cuisine;The façade may be simple (think white-washed cement with a black framed door) but inside, this place is one-of-a-kind. Filled with greenery and stunning tall plants, plush seating and elegant lighting, Suyo is sophisticated without a trace of fuss. Word is out, so make a reservation, unless you care to take the chance of finding a seat at the always bustling bar. Hamachi tiradito, with its supple slices and bright yellow sauce, impresses at the first bite. White asparagus is grilled, then topped with a vibrant huancaína and tart salsa verde atop a purple potato puree. Arroz con pato delivers that beloved, rustic taste while riffing with the addition of duck confit. Conclude with the chocolate tres leches cake with berries and whipped toasted honey.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11530;Chef's Choice Chinese Cuisine;Canada;Vancouver;955 W. Broadway, Vancouver, V5Z 1K3, Canada;49.2634916;-123.1253562;96;false;true;Cantonese, Chinese;Copper and wood panels lend a handsome appeal to the dining room, but make no mistake: Chef's Choice Chinese Cuisine deals in spectacular food. The kitchen offers dishes that are unique and classic, including many not often seen on other menus. Peruse the "kitchen specialties" to discover dishes like Chinese wine-marinated crispy duck tongues and kidneys. Few things beat a warm bowl of congee with dried oyster, salty pork and preserved egg. Minced pork and seafood soup dumplings are steamed pockets of soul-soothing and savory broth, but it's the signature marinated chicken with thick and fragrant black truffle sauce that lives up to the hype.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11531;Homer St. Cafe;Canada;Vancouver;898 Homer St., Vancouver, V6B 2W5, Canada;49.2789974;-123.1178894;78;false;true;Contemporary, French;Nestled within a hip neighborhood, Homer St. Cafe entices with its inviting patio, but step inside and and you'll quickly see that this contemporary bistro is no slouch indoors, either. Equal parts trendy and quirky, with chairs doubling as wall hangings, Homer St. Cafe delivers on its promise of comfort food done really well. The rotisserie chicken is the draw, brined in their signature sauce overnight to render tender, flavorful meat. Order it half or whole and then tuck in to the crispy skin doused in gravy or buttermilk ranch. Sided by fluffy, buttery biscuits, it's a stick-to-your-ribs satisfying meal. If you have room, order the cheesecake with white chocolate-almond crumble resting over quince preserve.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
11532;Chang'An;Canada;Vancouver;1661 Granville St., Vancouver, V6Z 1N3, Canada;49.2735847;-123.1316969;16;true;false;Chinese, Shaanxi;Diners flock here to indulge in the waterfront views and the sometimes-fiery culinary specialties from Shaanxi, but the signature theatricality is what gilds the lily. Peking duck is given a prima donna treatment: it must be ordered beforehand on the phone, later to appear tableside with a fanfare of flambéed rum. After the choice morsels of crisp golden skin and tender meat have been artfully carved and served, you’ll even get an encore, where the last bits of the duck are transformed into a soup or a rustic peppery stir-fry. Those unwilling to make an advance commitment will find no shortage of other diversions, from pricy seafood delicacies to hearty dishes of roast lamb, not to mention satisfyingly chewy hand-pulled biang biang noodles.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11535;Osteria Savio Volpe;Canada;Vancouver;615 Kingsway, Vancouver, V5T 3K5, Canada;49.2574339;-123.0911178;85;false;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;Clean and contemporary, with white marble and modern light fixtures, Osteria Savio Volpe could easily fit right in on a street in Milan, Naples or Rome. Simple materials, including red-and-brown tiles and a muted palette, set a modern tone for cuisine that takes inspiration from the regions of Italy while balancing authenticity and expectations. Dig in to warm and tender garlic knots studded with black pepper and a thatch of grated pecorino. Sop up every last dot of the piquant marinara—it's worth the additional charge. Thinly sliced beef carpaccio is plated in traditional fashion, then topped with a flavorful leek-accented aioli, and creste di gallo is an ideal pasta for the richly flavored lamb ragu with zippy sage and pecorino.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11538;¿CóMO? Taperia;Canada;Vancouver;201 E. 7th Ave., Vancouver, V5T 0B4, Canada;49.2646409;-123.100697;46;true;false;Spanish, Small eats;Prepare for a trip to Spain sans passport when pulling up a seat at ¿CóMO? Taperia—that is if you can score one at this perpetually packed spot. Equal parts tapas bar and despensa/bodega, it boasts all the warmth, authenticity and conviviality of similar spots in Spain.From the fritos and the raciones to a whole world of spectacular conservas, there's plenty to whet your appetite. Start with the tart and fleshy boquerones accompanied by a side of pan con tomate. If the silky berenjenas con miel are on the menu, go for it—you won't be disappointed. Daily specials show the kitchen's flair for bridging classic Spanish fare with local product.Rare Spanish wines are a special treat here, so have the server guide you through a wine pairing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11541;Bao Bei;Canada;Vancouver;163 Keefer St., Vancouver, V6A 1X3, Canada;49.279556;-123.1007331;32;true;true;Chinese, Taiwanese;Bao Bei may mean "precious," but there's nothing twee about this brasserie located at the edge of Vancouver's old Chinatown. Instead, Chef Joël Watanabe shows off his playful, creative cooking style, delivering food that's inventive and fun. Far from traditional, these unique takes on classic Chinese cuisine are crafted from top-notch ingredients. Take the "kick ass fried rice," their savory and a tad sweet version of the ubiquitous standard. This dish punches above its weight with an ingenious blend of prawns, bitter melon, masala-preserved mushrooms and papadam. Mantou buns filled with braised pork, hoisin, pickled ginger and miso-serrano aioli are positively irresistible, and even seemingly simple plates, like braised pea shoots with garlic, bring the flavor.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11542;Folke;Canada;Vancouver;2585 W. Broadway, Vancouver, V6K 2E9, Canada;49.2639443;-123.1641491;74;true;true;Vegan, North American;Friends Colin Uyeda and Pricilla Deo have brought bright, delicious plant-based fare to Kitsilano with Folke. A wall of wine greets guests at the entrance to this small-but-sophisticated spot where deep blue walls are adorned with original seaweed pressings and dried grasses complement the tranquil, coastal ambience. The fully open kitchen turns out impressive items. Don't skip the irresistible bread served with kale "butter" sprinkled with sesame seeds. A main dish of tender yet crunchy cabbage resting in a silky mole made from potatoes has terrifically tangy and smoky notes. In addition to the selection on display, the Folke team features a small selection of natural wine and locally produced ciders, as well as non-alcoholic libations to pair with your meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11546;Sushi Bar Maumi;Canada;Vancouver;1668 Robson St., Vancouver, V6G 1C7, Canada;49.2900816;-123.1334063;29;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Sushi omakases can be serious affairs that cost as much as a ticket to Tokyo, but this counter by Chef Maumi Ozaki is a refreshingly affordable alternative. Once seated at the counter with room for just under 20 guests, Ozaki gets right to business. His movements are practiced and confident and the quality ingredients are fresh and enticing. Expect around a dozen or more nigiri, with several standouts, including the botan ebi draped over rice and seasoned with a shake of salt. Sweet and creamy, it's a definite highlight. Gently smoked skipjack topped with grated ginger and green onion is a good bet, and Murasaki uni delivers on texture and taste. A wide variety of sake, champagne, shochu, and Japanese whisky serves as a nice accompaniment to the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11547;Archer;Canada;Vancouver;1152 Alberni St., Vancouver, V6E 1A5, Canada;49.2862552;-123.1249967;84;true;false;Contemporary, North American;Nestled alongside high-end retailers in the posh shopping district, Archer fits right in. It's sexy and sultry here, where natural materials are abundant, white-washed walls are adorned with contemporary art, and dark wood tables are set with leather-covered chairs. Dining solo? The bar in back is the perfect perch.The kitchen gives local and seasonal ingredients the royal treatment in classic preparations like seared sablefish served with snow crab yuzu butter and crab chowder. In addition to offering a prix fixe, à la carte offerings include lush items such as creamy uni and ribbons of lardo atop toasted brioche, and a tenderloin cooked to perfection accompanied by pomme paillasson. Go for broke and add Hokkaido scallop for a luxe touch. Chocolate semifreddo makes a nice ending.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11550;Zab Bite - Thai E-Sarn Cuisine;Canada;Vancouver;4197 Fraser St., Vancouver, V5V 4E9, Canada;49.2476612;-123.0901991;23;true;true;Thai, Regional Cuisine;Focusing on the cuisine of northeastern Thailand, this cheery operation has quickly become one of Vancouver's favorites for casual Thai. The sizable menu makes the typical concessions to crowd-pleasing mainstays like pad Thai and pad see ew, which are prepared diligently, but it's the regional specialties on offer that will leave the strongest impression. Think boat noodles, featuring funky, aromatic beef broth loaded with bouncy meatballs and tripe, or crunchy, succulent grilled pork jowl with toasted rice and a punchy nam jaew dipping sauce. Although there are options for all tastes, diners seeking to break a sweat are not likely to be disappointed when requesting spice.;;[]
11552;Ophelía;Canada;Vancouver;165 W. 2nd Ave., Vancouver, V5Y 1B8, Canada;49.2694746;-123.1083363;97;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Stunning murals, colorful carvings...Ophelía is quite literally a bright spot in Vancouver's Olympic Village. It's always packed, so make a reservation. Of course, if you didn't plan ahead, a bevy of special margaritas will help you pass the time. Chef/co-owner Francisco Higareda prepares traditional pan-regional Mexican fare just as his mother, Ophelia, did. Corn-crusted octopus sided by cilantro rice, braised kale and zucchini is bested with a Oaxacan mole blanco that's rich and creamy. A trio of tacos rewards diners with delectable ingredients piled high atop locally made tortillas. End things with that ultimate classic—tres leches cake.Weather permitting, the outdoor patio is the spot to while away the night.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11553;Neptune Palace Seafood Restaurant;Canada;Vancouver;470 S.W. Marine Dr., Vancouver, V5X 0C7, Canada;49.2104026;-123.1162365;19;false;true;Cantonese, Seafood;Ensconced on the second floor of the Marine Gate shopping mall, this expansive banquet hall-cum-restaurant is no secret to locals in search of excellent dim sum and Cantonese specialties. The spacious room readily accommodates large groups, the better to sample a wide range of mouthwatering options—though at peak hours, you may face wait times. During the day, the menu offers the traditional array of carefully prepared dumplings, many featuring exceptionally plump, juicy shrimp, as well as warming bowls of congee. At dinner, expect a broader variety of seafood, including pricier delicacies like lobster, abalone and sea cucumber, as well as a wide selection of meaty options, from crisp-skinned roasted duck to sweet and sour pork with pineapple.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11554;Hawksworth Restaurant;Canada;Vancouver;801 W. Georgia St., Vancouver, V6C 1P7, Canada;49.2838104;-123.1191613;87;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;Respected native son Chef David Hawksworth helms this eponymous restaurant nestled inside the posh Rosewood Hotel Georgia. Enter through the lobby or directly from Georgia Street into an elegant bar where guests who look as if they just stepped off a fashion shoot sip well-crafted drinks. In the dining room, a shimmering chandelier and an eye-catching wall of wine set an elegant tone.Simple luxuries never disappoint, as in the caviar and oysters. Then, savor the light and elegant mushroom consommé stocked with meaty matsutake and foie gras. Agnolotti with hazelnut & celery foam is almost too pretty to eat, but then you'd miss the earthy umami of the roasted king oyster mushrooms. Finally, it's difficult to pick just one, so order the macaron sampling.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11555;PiDGiN;Canada;Vancouver;350 Carrall St., Vancouver, V6B 2J3, Canada;49.2818661;-123.1041584;29;true;true;Contemporary, North American;There are many reasons why Vancouver is considered a culinary destination, and PiDGin certainly has something to do with that. Inside, stirring artwork from local artists, soft industrial lighting and wood banquettes set a city-chic tone. Chef Wesley Young has been running the show here for a handful of years, and his menu is distinctive. Playful, even irreverent, he is clearly having fun surprising diners with unusual combinations that not only work, but they wow. Signature dishes, like the Korean rice cakes cooked in an umami-rich gochujang "bolognese" with crunchy, spiced hazelnuts, make a nightly appearance. Other dishes include refreshing tuna tartare with nori puree and salty ikura, accompanied by taro root crisps.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11556;Bonjour Vietnam Bistro;Canada;Vancouver;3944 Fraser St., Vancouver, V5V 4E4, Canada;49.2497775;-123.0898923;94;true;true;Vietnamese, Vegetarian;With looks somewhere between a tropical greenhouse and a nightclub, plus a cool, clubby atmosphere, this lively, colorful boîte could just as well be in West Hollywood as Vancouver. Some of the plant life is artificial, but rest assured the homey Vietnamese fare is the real deal. A hip, fashion-forward clientele is drawn in by the cooking, but the energetic vibe and disarmingly sweet service can’t hurt. You might start with grilled skewers, like a pork sausage shaped around a lemongrass stalk, or a pepper-crusted beef carpaccio topped with fragrant herbs, crispy garlic and shallot—but save room for the soul-warming bowls of pho (a short rib version is noteworthy) and bun bo hue. Each item has a vegetarian counterpart, so there’s no shortage of options.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11557;The Mackenzie Room;Canada;Vancouver;415 Powell St., Vancouver, V6A 1G7, Canada;49.2832157;-123.0948702;41;false;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;The Mackenzie Room rightly describes itself as a “hidden gem,” as it really is waving the flag for culinary ambition in an area not overly encumbered with competitors. It boasts a laid-back vibe, a strong urban look and a blackboard menu listing dishes that focus on local, seasonal ingredients. If you can get past the puns—names like ‘Prince Char-ming’ featuring Arctic char, or ‘Collar by Your Name’ which involves succulent braised pork collar with sauce à la Royale— you’ll find yourself enjoying generously sized and creatively conceived dishes that don’t skimp on flavor.If you come as a table or four or more, you can have the whole menu at a set price. Be sure to start with one of their cocktails (Werewolf in Vancouver, anyone?).;Air conditioning;[]
11559;Moltaqa;Canada;Vancouver;1002 Mainland St., Vancouver, V6B 2T4, Canada;49.2765492;-123.1191154;74;true;true;Moroccan, Regional Cuisine;Located in one of Vancouver's hippest dining areas, Moltaqa is where Moroccan hospitality shines. The space has several nooks and crannies for seating, so even when the house is full, it still feels intimate, and warm service encourages lingering. The menu brims with tempting options. Bite into a flaky chicken pastilla, a dome-shaped phyllo pastry stuffed with shredded chicken and blanched almonds. Dusted with powdered sugar and cinnamon, it's the perfect balance of sweet and savory. The vegetarian platter delivers everything from tomato and pepper salad and eggplant filled with walnuts to a hearty, thick split pea soup and harira soup with lentils and chickpeas in a tomato base. To finish, you'll never go wrong with a square of crisp baklava.;;[]
11560;Maenam;Canada;Vancouver;1938 W. 4th Ave., Vancouver, V6J 1M5, Canada;49.2679673;-123.1489653;31;true;true;Thai, Regional Cuisine;The standard-bearer for exceptional Thai cuisine in Vancouver, Maenam has been a local favorite since opening in 2009. This kitchen delivers vibrant, heady cooking with bold flavors and an eye toward authenticity. Traditional dishes are given a local accent with top-tier local ingredients, from in-season produce to pristine fish caught in local waters. Dishes may be rustic in their presentation, but they reveal abundant refinement when it comes to their laser-focused flavors. Familiar items like hot and sour soup or panang curry achieve breathtaking heights thanks to a masterful use of aromatics and artfully balanced tastes. Plates are ideal for sharing in groups, but a family-style tasting menu features the menu's highlights for smaller parties.;Air conditioning;[]
11563;Nightingale;Canada;Vancouver;1017 W. Hastings St., Vancouver, V6E 0C4, Canada;49.2872485;-123.1177062;19;true;true;Contemporary, Farm to table;A lofty, stylish room and downtown locale attract no shortage of business lunches, but this songbird is also a pitch-perfect fit for relaxed meals among friends. The name references a fable that gives us the proverb “a bird in the hand is worth two in the bush,” and an approachable menu of rustic fare aims to make the most of the season with a bounty of shareable plates. A wood-fired oven leaves its mark on beautifully blistered Roman-style pizzas, as well as imparting a trace of smoke to impeccably sourced local produce, as in roasted carrots with spiced honey, or cauliflower with sunflower seeds and caper raisin vinaigrette. Desserts like a lime bar topped with chewy coconut and accompanied by mango sorbet skillfully reimagine childhood indulgences.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11564;ro.bo;France;Montignac-Lascaux;Hôtel de Bouilhac, 6 avenue Professeur-Faurel, Montignac-Lascaux, 24290, France;45.0657687;1.1604383;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the Périgord Noir area of the Dordogne, the Hôtel de Bouilhac is housed in a 17C mansion. Its restaurant welcomes guests in a magnificent courtyard or in one of two salons with stone walls that bear the marks of their long history. Diners will be happy to discover that chef Nick Honeyman, of the MICHELIN-starred Le Petit Léon, just 10km away, is also at the helm here. His creative cuisine is already renowned for its freshness and pronounced flavours, particularly those of citrus fruits, which he uses to excellent effect. A case in point is his take on île flottante: elderflower-infused blancmange, citrus foam, on a bed of Périgord strawberries, served with a peaty whisky cream.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11566;Saison;France;Dijon;17 rue Lamonnoye, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3228137;5.043886;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In Dijon's Antiquaires neighbourhood, this French-Italian restaurant welcomes diners in a pleasant space decorated in a palette of light colours. Milanese chef Riccardo Maiello, who trained in MICHELIN-starred establishments, is at the helm: he delights diners with modern cuisine that alternates French recipes with nods to local produce, such as a starter of slow-cooked egg, broad beans from nearby Arc-sur-Tille, shiitake, emulsion with garlic and farmhouse Cancoillotte cheese, and 100% Italian dishes, eg al dente paccheri alla carbonara, home-made pasta straight from Italy made with Pecorino and guanciale.;Terrace;[]
11567;Madame B;France;Bordeaux;Hôtel Burdigala, 115 rue Georges-Bonnac, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.83985;-0.58668;18;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At this chic brasserie in the Hotel Burdigala, particular care has gone into the decor, which plumps for a slightly old-fashioned feel: oak parquet flooring, banquettes and armchairs, black tables and a pale wood console covered with black marble. The chef does an authentic job of cooking up an absolute storm here, with dishes inspired by tradition (veal blanquette, braised chuck, stuffed cabbage) – punctuated by contemporary touches and accompanied by irresistible sauces. And the patisserie doesn't disappoint, with desserts such as biscuit sablé, strawberries, fromage blanc and lime, herb sorbet.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11568;La Maison de Mézos;France;Mézos;Place de l'Église, au bourg, Mézos, 40170, France;44.0767318;-1.1684454;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a village set deep within the Landes forest, this restaurant boasts a façade with the red shutters that are so emblematic of the region. A fragrant pergola covered in jasmine leads to a charming covered terrace with mismatched furniture. Inside, the atmosphere is that of a rustic-style country house. The chef, who has gained a wealth of experience from his travels, rustles up cuisine that very much captures the zeitgeist, infused with creative details such as a lemon and caper ice cream to accompany the veal confit with tonnato sauce, or a mussel and red curry mayonnaise on the trout and peas.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11570;L'Obélias;France;Naucelle;7 boulevard Eugène-Viala, Naucelle, 12800, France;44.197906;2.3408344;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the Ségala region, nestling in a village that is famous for its Cistercian church, this recently renovated little restaurant is accommodated in a half-timbered house. A well-travelled couple of industry professionals, Gilhem and Léonie, chef and pastry chef respectively, put a skilful spin on traditional fare such as shredded shoulder of lamb served tajine-style or, for dessert, citrus millefeuille with caramel and blood orange sorbet. The well-balanced and appealing menu they have come up with abounds with fresh and colourful dishes – plus it's excellent value for money. In short, they've got it all figured out. Delightful terrace laid out in the shade of an albizia and a magnolia.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11572;Le Lodge;France;Samoëns;20 route de Sixt, Samoëns, 74340, France;46.0826908;6.72898;87;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is run by a young couple who are passionate about what they do: chef Flavio Ricco and Lola Goudenove. In the heart of the village it has a cosy dining area done out in the style of a lodge. The blend of wood and stone makes for a relaxing feel. The chef prepares traditional cuisine with a measure of creativity, highlighting local ingredients on a set menu (with options). This lunchtime, the chef demonstrated his finesse when revisiting soupe châtrée – a rather hearty Samoëns speciality made with bread, Tomme de Savoie cheese and onion soup, that was followed by a fillet of sea bass with celery and beurre blanc with Génépi. For dessert, there was candied apple, vanilla cream and vanilla ice cream. The welcome and service are charming: in fact, the chef comes out of his kitchen from time to time to serve his guests.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11573;L'Inattendu - Domaine de Locguénolé;France;Kervignac;Route de Port-Louis, Le Hingair, Kervignac, 56700, France;47.7735735;-3.2761308;54;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The decadently revamped Locguénolé Estate features a 19C château and an 18C Brittany manor house set in several hundred acres of wooded grounds that are also home to a “farmyard” (chickens, goats, ducks and geese) together with a kitchen garden, orchard and beehives that supply the restaurant. The dining area, reminiscent of the heyday of the East India Company, unfolds beneath an industrial-vibe conservatory structure dotted in greenery. In this classy setting, you will taste the spot-on, delicate handiwork of youthful chef Yann Maget (MOF 2023 with stints in top establishments under his belt). Produce from Brittany takes pride of place and kari gosse curry spice, black pudding, razor clams and andouille often feature in his cooking. Top-drawer ingredients crafted with talent and flair in a constant quest for taste, depicted by gutsy sauces rich in depth, illustrated by his virtuoso squid and pork recipe, jazzed up with a punchy sauce or John Dory garnished with girolles and fresh almonds.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11576;L'Argence;France;Sainte-Geneviève-sur-Argence;Rue du Riols, Sainte-Geneviève-sur-Argence, 12210, France;44.8015746;2.7593948;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Aubrac, a couple of industry professionals have taken over this old inn dating from the early 1900s that has been completely renovated to sport a refined contemporary style. Chef Jonathan Riboulet, who has a wealth of MICHELIN-starred experience (Guérard, Pic, Lameloise and, above all, 12 years with Bras at Laguiole), serves up a cuisine in which he skilfully allies produce from the terroir (trout from the Monts d'Aubrac, escargots from Aveyron, entrecôte from Aubrac) with local herbs (meadowsweet, wild garlic, salad burnet). The result is playful, fresh and colourful – but also creative, a rare thing in these parts. The bright, modern dining area looks out onto a delightful terrace surrounded by a garden that bursts with blooms in season. Six guestrooms and two spacious, comfortable apartments provide a base from which to explore this pretty part of France.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11577;Almacita;France;Valence;51 Grande-Rue, Valence, 26000, France;44.93216;4.89082;77;true;false;Latin American;It can get very hot in Valence! Designed by Louis Chabran, this restaurant, which serves South American cuisine prepared by bona fide Latin-American chefs, is just the ticket. As you might expect, the menu proposes tapas (pimientos, tacos de pollo, croquetas de chorizo) to whet the appetite, followed by sea bass ceviche with roasted apricot, red onion and dill, then octopus accompanied by chimichurri sauce and aubergine caviar infused with coconut milk. Diners delight in the exotic spices and aromas in a laid-back atmosphere that has plenty of soul (which translates to almacita in Spanish).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11578;Bistrot 1936 - Domaine du Limonay;France;Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes;Lieu-dit Le Limonay, Saint-Méloir-des-Ondes, 35350, France;48.6151282;-1.9052688;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The latest addition to the Maison Tirel-Guérin stable (established back in 1936) is this bistro firmly rooted in the current century, with its lovely choice of materials (light-coloured wood and exposed beams) and its bay windows that invite the light to flood in. The menu, overseen by the chef of the fine dining restaurant, features mouthwatering top-quality ingredients, such as poularde, foie gras and spider crab. The delicious farm-reared pork – grilled belly and a wafer-thin slice of andouille – was a particular hit with its delicious Roscoff onion jus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11579;La Table du Grapiot;France;Pupillin;3 rue Bagier, Pupillin, 39600, France;46.8834044;5.760462;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of a Jura wine-growing village, this restaurant featuring wood, concrete and sheet metal is reminiscent of a warehouse standing out in the landscape of peaceful vineyards. Headed up by chef Vivien Sonzogni and his partner, sommelier Noémie Paris, a new team is now at the helm of this fine dining institution. He draws on his experience to deliver his take on contemporary cuisine, often showcasing local produce (pike soufflé, trout etc) and throwing in the odd creative flourish or Japanese influence.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11581;Breizh Café Rennes;France;Rennes;1 place de la Trinité, Rennes, 35000, France;48.1123311;-1.6832891;86;false;false;Breton;Why change a formula that works? Bertrand Larcher, the man who introduced the Breton crêpe to Japan, has set up shop in Rennes, a stone's throw from the city's Marché des Lices. The setting is a modern, industrial-style space with an open kitchen. The ingredients for success are still the same: high-quality produce that is predominantly organic (stone-ground wheat grown in Brittany, buckwheat flour milled in Vitré, organic eggs, artisanal Basque charcuterie from Pierre Oteiza). Alongside the classic galettes (buckwheat pancakes), there are more original iterations, some with a Japanese twist, such as the kinako crêpe with Okinawa black sugar and matcha ice cream. There is a short menu of nibbles and oysters.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11582;The Counter by Robin Read;United Kingdom;Royal Tunbridge Wells;77 Calverley Road, Royal Tunbridge Wells, TN1 2UY, United Kingdom;51.133004;0.2681572;66;true;false;Modern British;Considering its name, it may come as a surprise to learn that there are actually only four counter seats at this dark and moody restaurant on a leafy street. Those spots are very much the prized tickets here however, as not only do they give you a great view of the action, but they also allow you to order two exclusive extra courses. The eponymous chef roots his cooking in local producers, crafting dishes that shine a spotlight on the top-quality central ingredients like succulent Sussex chicken – even the wine list features some nearby growers. The service is personable and pleasingly relaxed.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11583;Puro by Tommy Thorn;United Kingdom;Clevedon;Rear of 32-34 Hill Road, Clevedon, BS21 7PH, United Kingdom;51.44325;-2.8582;75;true;false;Modern British;Tucked away beneath the Vintage & Vine wine shop and bar, you’ll find ‘Masterchef: The Professionals’ finalist Tommy Thorn and his team hard at work in this subterranean restaurant. Diners can choose between a concise seasonal à la carte and a tasting menu of elaborate dishes, but ensure you always begin with the delicious brioche and Marmite butter. Sensible pricing, a carefully curated wine selection and the occasional guest chef evening all add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11584;Plates London;United Kingdom;London;320 Old Street, Hoxton, London, EC1V 9DR, United Kingdom;51.5265904;-0.0819587;76;false;true;Vegan, Vegetarian;There’s an appropriately earthy, natural vibe to this elegant restaurant dedicated to promoting plant-based cuisine. The slate floor, warm hues and rustic plastering help it feel stripped-back yet stylish, with some counter seating providing another on-trend touch. Chef Kirk Haworth – who founded Plates with his sister Keeley – brings his strong classical technique to bear on inventive and inviting vegan dishes that give vegetables the respect they deserve. The maitake mushroom with black bean mole is superb, while the raw cocoa gateau is a real treat to finish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11585;Miga;United Kingdom;London;1 Mare Street, Hackney, London, E8 4RP, United Kingdom;51.5345354;-0.0576208;17;false;false;Korean;There’s always a certain joyfulness to family owned and run restaurants – and Miga is truly a family affair, with dad running things in the open kitchen and the younger generation looking after guests in the bright, airy room. If you want to find out more about them, check out the family history as described on the wall outside. ‘A modern take on Korean cuisine’ is their tagline and this is borne out by fresh-tasting dishes like delicious soy-braised short ribs – already a fans’ favourite – and spicy noodles with crispy beef jeon. The generous prices, especially at lunch, allow for enthusiastic ordering – which you won’t regret.;;[]
11586;Whyte's;United Kingdom;London;Unit 3, 143 Mare Street, Hackney, London, E8 3RH, United Kingdom;51.5392555;-0.0568599;38;true;true;World Cuisine;With a reputation forged in pop-ups and supper clubs, the self-styled rock ‘n’ roll chef known as 'Whyte Rushen' has success on his hands with his first permanent restaurant, which he opened here in London Fields in 2024. His menu is made up of sharing plates big and small but is also something of a movable feast: it may be Basque-influenced one month, Italian the next – but if there's a whole turbot to share or BBQ ‘finger burners’ on the menu, don’t hesitate to order them. It’s loud, fun and furious – ask for counter seats and join the party.;Counter dining;[]
11587;Holy Carrot;United Kingdom;London;156 Portobello Road, Notting Hill, London, W11 2EB, United Kingdom;51.5151688;-0.2044226;78;false;false;Vegan;London’s constantly expanding vegan food scene received another boost when this former pop-up and supper club opened up permanently on Portobello Road. It’s the ideal place for convincing your carnivorous friends of the virtues of plant-based cuisine, as each dish bursts with colour and creativity. The ‘small’ and ‘large’ plates are best shared to sample the broad range of cooking techniques, from barbecued carrot to coal-roasted leeks. The dining room itself – filled with polished concrete and light Mediterranean colours – provides a soothing backdrop that enhances the experience.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11588;Chef's Table by Josh Barnes;United Kingdom;Swinton;Swinton Park, Masham, Swinton, HG4 4JH, United Kingdom;54.2133951;-1.6759994;88;false;false;Modern British;In a bright, airy former stable that doubles as a cookery school within the sprawling Swinton Estate, this restaurant delivers what it promises: an intimate counter dining experience where Chef Josh Barnes and his team cook in front of you and serve their dishes with pride. The place has a country kitchen feel befitting of this grand domain – which also houses a hotel – while the Estate itself provides much of the seasonal produce. The cooking comes with some creative twists, such as using locally foraged mushrooms to add richness to a chocolate mousse. The wine flight, too, contains unusual and intriguing touches.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
11589;July;United Kingdom;London;10 Charlotte Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 2LT, United Kingdom;51.5183735;-0.1344704;52;true;false;Modern French, Alsatian;Bright, modish and hugely enjoyable, July is a spot-on bistro driven by the passion of its team. Located on Fitzrovia’s ever-popular Charlotte Street, it’s a lovely neighbourhood restaurant that just so happens to be in the heart of the city. Sit in the narrow front area if you like to be on-view, or the spacious, more peaceful room to the rear. The cooking is stripped-back but full of flavour, with an Alsatian backbone to the menu. Look out for the seasonal terrine and, when available, the baeckeoffe to share. Owner Solynka Dumas leads the warm, chatty service which provides genuine hospitality.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11590;Tare Bistro;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;Unit 25, Cargo 2, Museum Street, Wapping Wharf, City of Bristol, BS1 6ZA, United Kingdom;51.447344;-2.598205;49;true;false;Modern British;You could easily miss this terrific little restaurant housed in a shipping container on the trendy foodie haven of Wapping Wharf. What a shame that would be, as Chef-Owner Matt Hampshire has crafted a relaxed, stripped-back eatery where the cooking is uncomplicatedly delicious and provides brilliant value for money – especially on the set lunch menu. Dishes such as a bowl of expertly cooked Fowey mussels with cider marinière sauce are a perfect demonstration of Matt’s unfussy, technically adept sharing plates.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11591;Native;United Kingdom;Tenbury Wells;Pensons Yard, Netherwood Estate, Tenbury Wells, WR15 8RT, United Kingdom;52.25096;-2.52956;49;true;false;Modern British;Having had stints in Mersea, London and now moving all the way over to Worcestershire, you have to say that the team at Native are a well-travelled bunch. Their latest incarnation is at Netherwood Estate, where the delightful kitchen gardens are a perfect match for the restaurant’s sustainable ethos. The dining room is housed in a glorious 16th-century barn, where diners can enjoy a hyper-seasonal menu celebrating produce from the Estate including tomatoes from the greenhouse and apples from the orchard. A walk round the enviable gardens will enhance your visit.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11592;The Fuji Grill;United Kingdom;London;115 Sloane Street, Belgravia, London, SW1X 9PJ, United Kingdom;51.4947198;-0.1584907;21;true;true;Japanese;The discreetly stylish Beaverbrook Town House is home to this warm, elegant restaurant that’s something of a hidden gem. The framed Japanese prints on the walls and lacquered furniture help make it a lovely place to dine, while there’s plenty to entice on the wide choice of menus, from a full omakase – which should naturally be enjoyed at the counter – to bento box deals and an extensive à la carte featuring skilfully made nigiri. A good sake selection adds to the authentic Japanese appeal – albeit inside an English townhouse.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
11593;Bucks Head;United Kingdom;Dundrum;77-79 Main Street, Dundrum, BT33 0LU, United Kingdom;54.2588912;-5.8416067;37;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Alex Greene’s first job was at this historic pub and now he has returned to his hometown to run the lovely village inn with his partner Bronagh McCormick. He arrives back in Dundrum with plenty of experience, borne out in pared-back, accessible and hugely enjoyable dishes based on a bounty of Northern Irish produce, from Kilkeel crab to Mourne Spring lamb – the seafood chowder is a particular highlight. The pub itself is charming, as is the service led by Bronagh.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11595;Botanical Rooms;United Kingdom;Bruton;The Newt in Somerset, Bruton, BA7 7NG, United Kingdom;51.0779571;-2.4863776;89;false;false;Modern British;Set within the grounds of The Newt in Somerset, a striking Georgian estate that houses a number of mini-hotels, sits a beautiful mellow stone building. Within it is a stunning oak-panelled dining room, with a glass-covered courtyard and a laid-back feel. Inside a semi-open kitchen, the chefs skilfully handle seasonal local produce, be it lamb from the estate or seafood from the Dorset coast, with the wood-fired grill often used to good effect. The polite and efficient service ensures everything runs smoothly within this eminently elegant setting.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
11597;Grande Étoile;Germany;Düsseldorf;Bastionstraße 16, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.221634;6.775079;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French;This restaurant in the Carlstadt district is a masterclass in chic: shimmering gold, velvet, striking chandeliers and stylish Art Deco features create a trendy, elegant atmosphere. It serves up flavourful, well-executed dishes from a menu featuring French brasserie classics as well as Italian influences: beef bourguignon, beef tartare, pasta, vitello al limone... Service is professional and friendly. Head there in the evening for the cocktail bar and DJs, who underscore the Parisian club vibe.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11598;Richard Bistro;Germany;Berlin;Köpenicker Straße 174, Berlin, 10997, Germany;52.504212;13.435281;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Hans Richard made a name for himself with his restaurant Richard, housed here in the former Köpenicker Hof, which dates back to 1892. He and his team have now turned their attention to a pleasingly down-to-earth bistro concept. Drawing inspiration from the Mediterranean, they rustle up modern dishes, such as baked monkfish with fennel and a tarragon and caper sauce, using select ingredients. The interior is a beautiful blend of old and new, featuring a stunning high wooden ceiling and contemporary artwork.;;[]
11600;Celia;Germany;Düsseldorf;Gladbacherstraße 15, Düsseldorf, 40219, Germany;51.2118734;6.7616208;75;false;true;Mexican;For an authentic taste of Mexico in Düsseldorf, head to Celia in the bustling Bilker Kirche area. Rene Brauchle, of Mexican-German heritage and born in Venezuela, and Florentina Assis, a native Chilean, have been sharing their passion for Latin American cuisine here since summer 2024. The joy and enthusiasm of your cordial hosts is palpable, and they clearly love what they do: he is in charge of the kitchen, and she presides front-of-house. Once you have tried his mouthwatering dishes such as the taco pescado, the ceviche or the cochinita, you'll be hooked and eager to return. Fun fact: this friendly, modern restaurant is named after Rene's grandmother, who inspired his love of cooking.;;[]
11601;Otto;Germany;Cologne;Am Hof 48, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.939852;6.9594174;65;false;true;Italian;Conveniently located in the city centre, a stone's throw from the cathedral and the Rhine River, this is the second maiBeck restaurant. In a trendy and chic setting, Jan C Maier and Tobias Becker serve up modern Italian cuisine with a focus on fish and seafood, although vegetarian options are also available. The pasta dishes are highly recommended. In addition to the excellent à la carte selection, the six-course "La Sera" set menu is available in the evening. The wine list is exclusively Italian. The front-of-house team are dedicated and attentive – the chefs also help to serve the food.;Air conditioning;[]
11602;Bratwursthäusle;Germany;Nuremberg;Rathaus-Platz 1, Nuremberg, 90403, Germany;49.4550064;11.0767363;75;true;false;Bavarian, Grills;A trip to Nuremberg wouldn't be complete without trying the city's famous Rostbratwürste! Look no further than this little old stone house on Marktplatz next to Sebalduskirche. Sausages have been sold here since 1312. The interior is rustic and charming, the beechwood barbecue being the centrepiece. Their wonderful sausages are made fresh every morning in their on-site butchery. They are served with sauerkraut and/or potato salad – simply delicious! For the full experience, wash it down with a draught beer. If you're not in the mood for sausages, the menu includes alternatives such as pork shoulder, offal dishes and other snacks. In the summer, the delightful terrace is a popular spot.;Terrace;[]
11603;La Boucherie;Germany;Kreuzwertheim;Hauptstraße 18, Kreuzwertheim, 97892, Germany;49.7649722;9.5160361;50;false;false;Contemporary;Daniel Schröder has made a name for himself in the region. Previously head chef at Kuno 140 in Würzburg, he now runs the small fine dining restaurant at this charming inn and together with Marcel Meining forms the double helm in the kitchen. Drawing inspiration from French cuisine, their culinary creations are full of finesse and made from excellent ingredients. A standout dish is the Norway lobster: a symphony of flavours, cooked to perfection and delicately seasoned, accompanied by a beautifully intense shellfish bisque, which is poured at your table. There is a set menu comprising five or six courses, complemented by a well-curated wine list dominated by regional labels. The decor is inviting and tastefully modern in style. The friendly service also makes for a delightful dining experience. Run by the same family for two generations, Landgasthof zum Kaffelstein has well-appointed guestrooms.;;[]
11604;Down Home;Canada;Markdale;1355299 9 Line, Markdale, N0C 1H0, Canada;44.4026662;-80.6101532;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Known for their time at Sumac & Salt, Chef Joel Gray and Hannah Harradine apply a heartfelt approach by welcoming diners into their own home in Grey County for a charming, intimate experience. Here, an interior kitchen and a barbecue are used to create a meal that spotlights excellent local products. Everything is lovingly presented by the team, with the chef offering explanations of many of the courses. Standouts include pieces of coal-roasted beets arranged with pickled pumpkin and dabs of creamy pumpkin seed purée. Trout brined with spruce tips is slow-smoked then quick-seared and presented with Ontario potatoes, fiddlehead ferns, and trout roe. Braised lamb neck stuffs a wild leek raviolo dressed with a preserved green tomato jus, giving a subtle hint of spice.;;[]
11605;Famiglia Baldassarre;Canada;Toronto;122 Geary Ave., Toronto, M6H 4H1, Canada;43.6704401;-79.4346806;95;true;false;Italian;If you want pasta for lunch, you’ll have to plan accordingly. Chef Leandro Baldassarre started out as an underground pasta maven and quickly matured into a bona fide, city-wide wholesaler and retailer. He opens his doors for lunch for just a few hours each day, and on an industrial strip of Dovercourt Village, diners line the sidewalk waiting to get in. Be advised: Tables are in scarce supply, as most of the space is an industrial kitchen busy filling orders for other restaurants and grocers. The menu is even more limited, confined to two or so pastas that change daily, plus prosciutto and mozzarella. The likes of cavatelli with asparagus, ravioli with ricotta and spinach, and tagliolini with wild chanterelles are honest and satisfying.;Terrace;[]
11606;Parquet;Canada;Toronto;97 Harbord St., Toronto, M5S 1G4, Canada;43.6626972;-79.4038014;47;false;true;French;French bistros can be predictable, but this neighborhood corner in Harbord Village takes a wonderfully refreshing approach. One could spend all day taking in the design: The marble bar is a worthy perch for admiring the gorgeous, patterned floors, forest-green ceiling and stylish, wood-paneled walls. And that patio – it’s a summer oasis. The cooking, meanwhile, hits all the right marks, and feels unquestionably French in its richness and satisfaction. Who knew that mushroom beignets could be so light and pair so well with lime and pepper sauce? One could make a meal out of the roasted cauliflower with cumin vinaigrette and puffed chickpeas. Cassoulet with duck confit and steak frites with béarnaise are proper classics.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11607;Madrina Bar y Tapas;Canada;Toronto;2 Trinity St., Toronto, M5A 3C4, Canada;43.6496021;-79.3593146;81;true;false;Spanish;Located in the center of the historic Distillery District in a space that seamlessly blends old and new, this lively spot impresses with its style and swagger. Madrina translates to godmother, though their interpretation has a whimsical bent.Chef Ramon Simarro pens a tribute to his native Catalan region with a lengthy tapas menu balancing classic and modern bites for a dynamic experience. Classics like pan con tomate hold their own, while the creative, modern twists are bold, yet grounded by solid techniques and quality ingredients. Sweet tapas, such as rice pudding croquetas, round out the meal.From a Spanish-focused wine list to an interesting cocktail menu with a designated gin and tonic section, the sips are equally compelling.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11608;Som Tum Jinda;Canada;Toronto;76 Gerrard St. E., Toronto, M5G 2A7, Canada;43.6599343;-79.3781648;84;true;true;Thai;As the name suggests, somtum is the specialty here and it’s made Isan-style with fermented fish paste for that extra tang. Tom Puu Nam Pla is classic Isan somtum, with the addition of salted crab along with the papaya, garlic, chili and tomato. You can stipulate your desired heat, but be aware that the scale here goes up to 11. Kor Moo Yang – grilled, succulent pork jowl – is another house specialty that’s fast become one of its biggest sellers and is well worth ordering. What this simple basement restaurant may lack in comfort, it more than makes up for in color. There’s a family connection to the original Som Tum Jinda in Thailand and, while it doesn’t serve any alcohol, it offers a wide variety of drinks from the next-door café.;;[]
11609;Tamarind Modern Indian Bistro;Canada;Mississauga;33 City Centre Dr., Mississauga, L5B 2N5, Canada;43.5944148;-79.639399;72;true;false;Indian;There’s a lot to take in at this colorful Indian restaurant, located in the frenzy of a Mississauga shopping district. For one, the menu covers extensive ground and features the familiar dishes you’d expect to see, alongside more curious creations like Chettinad chicken tacos and panipuri shots. Special weekend events get rowdy with live music and dancing. But for all the flash and the noise, there’s substance here too. Curries like the lamb Roganjosh are rich and hearty, and vegetable specialties like paneer cooked in a serious onion and tomato sauce pack volumes of flavor. Even those Chetinnad chicken tacos are surprisingly convincing. Servers might ask how comfortable you are with spice levels. Ask for spicy – and a side of raita for insurance.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11610;Dil Se;Canada;Toronto;335 Roncesvalles Ave., Toronto, M6R 2M8, Canada;43.6491505;-79.4501167;56;true;false;Indian;Dil Se is set along the village's main thoroughfare in Toronto's "Roncy" neighborhood. Effort has gone into the decor here, with linen-draped tables and walls accented by colorful fabrics.Chef/owner Mani Panwar offers highly enjoyable, well-prepared northern Indian cuisine.Paneer lababdar, a "Chef's special," is a Mughlai-style specialty featuring soft cubes of fresh cow's milk cheese simmered in a creamy, highly flavorful, orange-hued sauce enriched with cashews. Neatly presented in a metal bowl, vegetable biryani is fluffy and hot with a bright flavor courtesy of chilies, herbs and dried spices. Among the tandoor offerings, choose the lamb seek kebab, which comes with a zesty red chutney that leans tart.;Air conditioning;[]
11611;Henry's;Canada;Toronto;922 Queen St. W., Toronto, M6J 1G6, Canada;43.6449145;-79.4158126;54;false;false;Contemporary;Of the city’s many, many wine bars, Henry’s is both the newest and one of the most accomplished. Globe lighting, forest green cushions and gold-trim tables lend a certain mid-century modern sleekness to this inviting, airy space, which includes a backyard patio and a retail wine shop just next door.The menu makes no commitments to any one cuisine, beyond working exceptionally well with the wines on hand. You could assemble dinner solely out of appetizers like beef tartare with smoked crème fraiche, shrimp toast and fried zucchini blossoms. But then you’d miss that superb skate wing set in a fiery curry. Some might choose wine for their dessert, but a recent ancho-chili and chocolate mousse made a compelling case for never skipping sweets here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11612;Ardo;Canada;Toronto;243 King St. E., Toronto, M5A 1J9, Canada;43.65104;-79.36843;15;false;true;Italian, Sicilian;Inspiration comes from the sunny flavors of Southern Italy in this easygoing Old Town favorite, but the cooking isn’t overly preoccupied with tradition. For instance, nonna might not countenance the amount of butter that goes into a dish of orecchiette with sausage and rapini—but the indulgent results are unlikely to elicit any complaints. Scrupulously fresh seafood is a highlight, whether it be an albacore tuna carpaccio with celery and capers, or tender grilled octopus with marinated artichoke. It’s only fitting to end a meal with a spot-on rendition of cannoli with creamy ricotta filling. Those who are particularly smitten can take a bit of flavor home: the imported Sicilian olive oil, tomato sauce and pasta lining the walls are available for purchase.;Air conditioning;[]
11613;Bar Chica;Canada;Toronto;75 Portland St., Toronto, M5V 2M9, Canada;43.6437876;-79.3997157;44;false;true;Spanish;Bar or not? It's debatable, but what's safe to say is Bar Chica is bursting with vitality in every way. This is a cool place for cool people and it's quietly making its mark on the city. Foodies in the know  come for their unique take on tapas and a sherry or two. The servers' beaming smiles light the place up, and that passion follows through to the kitchen where they put their all into every plate. Expect a colorful plate of heirloom tomatoes & ajo blanco in the ensalada and fluffy grated truffle on their version of croqueta de jamon. Save room for the delectable torta de chocolate.Chica is easy to miss with its minimal exterior so keep a look out for the glowing lantern above the door, then settle in for a great night out.;Air conditioning;[]
11614;Koh Lipe Thai Kitchen;Canada;Toronto;35 Baldwin St., Toronto, M5T 1L1, Canada;43.6559493;-79.3935171;40;true;true;Thai, Southern Thai;Koh Lipe stands out among its Chinatown neighbors for its lively atmosphere and its authentic southern Thai cooking. Set over two floors and boasting a popular terrace, this place just feels fun, a mood buoyed by the friendly young staff.The kitchen dishes out regional specialties that deliver heat and flavor in spades. Coconut green curry beef with plantain and stink bean is a classic bowl of piping hot, delicious comfort. The chef's specials are always a sure bet, but for those diners who may be less familiar with Thai food, the noodle dishes are a perfect introduction. Don’t worry if there is a line—they turn around tables swiftly, so you won’t be waiting long to bite into those meaty prawn tails served with a kicky lime-chili dip.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11616;Vela;Canada;Toronto;90 Portland St., Toronto, M5V 2N2, Canada;43.6449086;-79.4003644;97;true;false;American, Asian;With exposed brick, a bar that goes on and on, and lights swirled into a sloped ceiling, this cool-kids restaurant has wide appeal. There is certainly seating for all occasions: white banquettes in the back, an up-close chef’s counter and plenty of tables in between. By design, the menu has faint Asian touches but is otherwise broad in its selection of seafood, pastas, steaks and vegetables. The results? Surprisingly dialed-in, largely thanks to a kitchen that makes as much as it can in-house. Highlights include cod with beurre blanc and chili crisp and, for dessert, a sugar-crusted profiterole filled with miso dulce de leche mousse and mascarpone cremeaux. Live music throughout the week will either attract or deter, depending on your mood.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11618;Alder;Canada;Toronto;51 Camden St., Toronto, M5V 1V2, Canada;43.6467951;-79.398156;79;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The stylish Ace hotel scored big when the industrious Chef Patrick Kriss moved into the ground level. The restaurant is a cool mix of dark brick floors, sleek wood finishes and large windows that usher in radiant beams of sunlight. And true to everything that the Alo Food Group does, expect a serious kitchen brigade and equally serious cooking. There’s a lot to like on this Mediterranean menu. Beef carpaccio is a crowd-pleaser, while the cucumber salad is a sleeper hit festooned with shaved fennel, dukkah, and hazelnuts. Stacks of firewood in the dining room is a clue to hone-in on proteins like roast chicken, Australian lamb, and a bone-in strip loin. Dessert is a must, especially if the astoundingly light coconut cream pie is still around.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
11619;Musoshin Ramen;Canada;Toronto;9 Boustead Ave., Toronto, M6R 1Y7, Canada;43.6533655;-79.4523554;34;true;false;Japanese, Ramen;Hiding just off the main drag in Roncesvalles, this restaurant is not like other ramen-yas. For starters, none of them can bake like Chef Aoi Yoshida, who turns out trays of perfectly formed Japanese milk bread and other sweet treats. Her house-made noodles, bundled into every bowl, are also a cut above most. But perhaps the most fascinating part of this restaurant hides in the broths. Whereas a typical tonkotsu ramen favors heart-stopping, porky richness, the style here is a vegetable base that is both lighter and leaner and yet equally savory. In a testament to both her own talents and to modern technology, Yoshida learned both noodle and ramen craft by video chatting with an old friend who runs this restaurant’s original location in Kyoto.;Air conditioning;[]
11621;Scaramouche;Canada;Toronto;1 Benvenuto Pl., Toronto, M4V 2L1, Canada;43.6817366;-79.4001638;33;true;true;French;Set in the affluent northern suburb of South Hill, Scaramouche has been a Toronto mainstay for decades, with Chef Keith Froggett at the helm since 1983. Don’t be alarmed when you arrive and head downstairs to the restaurant thinking you are off to a basement—you're not, as the superb city skyline view soon proves.Guests come for the views and stay for the traditional French cuisine. Don't expect modern twists, as dishes such as foie gras terrine with a sour cherry reduction and rabbit loin wrapped with bacon sided by a fricassee of sweet peas and fava beans, are as classic as they come. Savor the dark chocolate mousse with cherries for dessert, or take home one of their signature coconut cream pies.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11623;Yukashi;Canada;Toronto;643 Mount Pleasant Rd., Toronto, M4S 2M9, Canada;43.7050219;-79.3888979;78;true;true;Japanese;Chef Daisuke Izutsu is the quiet force behind this highly personal, kaiseki-style experience. While the room verges on cluttered, the menu takes seasonal ingredients and turns them into ornate works of art. The otsukuri is a colorful signature, featuring cuts of toro and hay-smoked hamachi stylishly arranged on a white marble base with the likes of pickled turnips, radishes, and daikon. Another signature combines wagyu beef, Hokkaido uni, and foie gras – all blowtorched and wrapped with shiso leaf. Dinner ends with simple, unadorned slices of Japanese crown melon from the chef’s hometown. These presentations come at considerable expense, but for those looking for artistry, intimacy, and subtlety, this restaurant is one to consider.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11624;Azura;Canada;Toronto;162 Danforth Ave., Toronto, M4K 1N1, Canada;43.6765755;-79.3575129;26;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;At last, Danforth Avenue scores big with an ambitious restaurant that sets a new standard for the neighborhood. Just across from the favored music hall, enjoy a generous, leisurely tasting menu that plays with Mediterranean flavors and rolls with the seasons. Start to finish, Chef Adam Ryan has a fine hand with presentation. From the striking tomato tart with rose harissa to a very soigné wagyu beef with wild ginger and morels, ingredients are often locally foraged and always arranged with style. The space itself is one of ease, featuring a busy bar anchoring the center, warm honeyed lighting, and a comfy tufted banquette. Esoteric wines and cocktails, like the gin-based Olive Branch, tell their own thoughtful stories and should be explored liberally.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11625;Union;Canada;Toronto;72 Ossington Ave., Toronto, M6J 2Y7, Canada;43.6457996;-79.4195261;78;false;true;French;Butchers, artisan bakers, antique shops and coffee shops define this stretch of Ossington Avenue where the appealingly worn Union awaits. There is a horseshoe-shaped bar at the entrance, but head back to the rustic brick-faced dining room. If you're up for a bit of theater, nab a seat at the counter to catch the action.Chef/owner Teo Paul once worked on a farm and his menu is a love letter to the region's seasons and its local suppliers. Lunch is perfect for a quick bite, while dinner is more of an event. Dishes are rustic with a refined edge and pack a flavorful punch.. The same effort and care goes into an omelette as steak frites, and if servers are busy, expect the chef himself to serve your plate, along with an explanation of what's on it.;Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11626;Gia;Canada;Toronto;1214 Dundas St. W., Toronto, M6J1X5, Canada;43.6495248;-79.4230795;33;false;false;Italian, Vegetarian;Panko-crusted meatballs, crab cakes with bagna cauda, pappardelle Bolognese. You could have a full dinner at this narrow hotspot in Trinity Bellwoods and not even realize that everything is meatless. Such is the charm of Jenny Coburn’s latest, plant-forward restaurant, which replaces her previous spot, Ufficio. High ceilings, exposed white brick, herringbone floors and a constantly packed dining room make for a stylish night out. House-made pasta is the prime order here, with one dish that has carried over from the previous restaurant: porcini agnolotti glossed in a sauce of butter and Parmigiano Reggiano, which can be made with vegan butter upon request. Unable to land a reservation? Walk-ins can snag a seat at the cozy, walnut-topped bar.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11627;Prime Seafood Palace;Canada;Toronto;944 Queen St. W., Toronto, M6J 1G8, Canada;43.6447281;-79.4166009;51;false;false;Steakhouse, Seafood;To find the front door, you’ll have to follow your nose. The scent of barbecue wafts down an alleyway fitted with stacks of firewood. Inside, find a dazzling space lined with maple slats, a domed ceiling and salmon-pink booths and walls. There is nothing like it around, and no surprise that Chef Matty Matheson is the mastermind here behind the city’s newest and most ambitious steakhouse. The menu is tightly curated balancing fantastic seafood, big meats cooked on the grill and serious vegetable preparations. Sicilian crudo and delicate ricotta dumplings are proper preludes to a bone-in dry-aged strip loin. Supplements like palace potatoes, cacio e pepe-inspired cauliflower and steamed carrots with pink shrimp aim to be more than sideshows.;Air conditioning;[]
11628;Bar Vendetta;Canada;Toronto;928 Dundas St. W., Toronto, M6J 1W3, Canada;43.6509085;-79.4131974;58;false;false;Italian;Anyone with a kitchen no bigger than a hotel closet should look to this narrow nook for inspiration. Truly, it is a wonder how restaurateur Jen Agg and her team manage to turn out so many from-scratch breads and pastas. Rosemary focaccia, tagliatelle alfredo and pappardelle twirled around oxtail ragu are just some of the hearty offerings at this favored wine bar in Dundas West. The signature dish is a cacio e pepe-inspired coil of ricotta-stuffed pasta. White-and-orange tile flooring, vintage posters and wood tones, along with welcoming servers, create a come-as-you-are, retro vibe. Some guests aren’t even here to eat. Instead, they’ve come to sidle up to the long bar and dig into the surprisingly lengthy, Italian-leaning wine list.;Air conditioning;[]
11629;Chubby's Jamaican Kitchen;Canada;Toronto;104 Portland St., Toronto, M5V 2N2, Canada;43.6455859;-79.4006722;92;true;true;Jamaican;The warm breezes of the Caribbean might be far away, but even in the dead of winter, stepping into this lively haven will bring a bit of island sunshine. Warm, easygoing hospitality is matched by homey, unpretentious cooking, with traditional dishes whose humble appearances belie surprising depth of flavor. "Likkle bites" like saltfish fritters are a fine starter, but don't let them distract you from exemplary versions of comforting classics like curry goat or oxtail stew (and take urgent note that the gravy from either can be ordered as a side). Perhaps best of all is the succulent jerk chicken, expertly cooked over a wood-burning grill to achieve an ethereal marriage of smoke, sweetness and spice—as good as any you’re likely to find this far from a beach.;;[]
11632;The Wood Owl;Canada;Toronto;1380 Danforth Ave., Toronto, M4J 1M9, Canada;43.6824441;-79.3280874;79;false;true;Contemporary;This quaint, wooden shoebox is a welcome retreat in Danforth. Wine bottles line the perimeter of a room that has a pleasant sepia tint. In fact, there’s no pretense at all here, which in part is what makes this restaurant so appealing. The menu is small, nothing extravagant or overly complicated, and offers far more vegetables than one might expect from a wine bar (adobo- roasted carrots with green goddess, anyone?). Beef, though, is still very much welcome at the table, highlighted as a weekly special, usually paired with a superb tangle of shoestring French fries. With or without a reservation, you should take a seat, order the fried polenta cakes with romesco and boquerones, and relish in the ease of a place that gets all the little details right.;Air conditioning;[]
11634;Mother's Dumplings;Canada;Toronto;421 Spadina Ave., Toronto, M5T 2G6, Canada;43.6569825;-79.399299;95;true;false;Chinese, Dumplings;Chef-owner Zhen Feng has folded so many dumplings for Toronto that she might as well be the city’s honorary mother. In 2005 she opened a small, eight-table nook on Huron Street. Five years later, she relocated to a much larger space and by then had boiled, steamed and pan-fried her way to becoming a city institution in the heart of Chinatown. The menu boasts all manner of Chinese dishes, but stick to the namesake specialty, which are rolled out and folded at all hours by a dedicated team in the back. One could make a meal out of just the boiled pork and dill dumplings, but other types are also worth dipping into. On the way out, bags of frozen dumplings are available for take-home when the craving hits and Feng’s kitchen is closed for the day.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
11635;PAI;Canada;Toronto;18 Duncan St., Toronto, M5H 3G8, Canada;43.6479556;-79.3886124;70;true;true;Northern Thai;Named for the Thai village where Nuit Regular and her husband opened their first restaurant, PAI is perpetually busy. A former nurse, Nuit now soothes by cooking her family recipes and street food favorites for hungry patrons. The mod bohemian look is appealing, but it's the extensive menu that you'll spend all of your time admiring. It's full of fresh, tasty dishes and vibrant curries. While they traipse across Thailand for inspiration, zero in on the North Thai plates and chef favorites, including khao soi, a noodle and coconut milk dish, or kanom jin nham ngeaw, a pork rib and tomato soup with rice vermicelli. Kung tawt, a plate of fried shrimp sided by a piquant tamarind sauce, is delicious but gaeng panang, a sweet-and-sour red curry, hits all the right notes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11636;Aanch;Canada;Toronto;259 Wellington St. W., Toronto, M5V 3P9, Canada;43.6450991;-79.3907092;65;true;false;Indian;Some things never change, like the stylish, tranquil setting of this restaurant, which opened under a different name (and chef) over a decade ago. The menu is lengthy and covers a wide swath of familiar, regional dishes, from the famous deep-fried chicken 65 of Chennai to the sharp, fiery vindaloos of Goa. Efforts to gussy up the plating with swirls and dots of sauce can come across as superfluous, but the end result is still a delicious one. Fried cones of paneer dusted in mango powder showcase the kitchen’s modern sensibilities, while the butter-rich dal bukhari seasoned with garam masala is a trusted classic. Heat levels across the board are on the mild side so chili hounds will have to request for extra kick, if so inclined.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11637;FK;Canada;Toronto;770 St. Clair Ave. W., Toronto, M6C 1B5, Canada;43.6811739;-79.4287876;53;true;false;Contemporary;In a sun-drenched space that could pass for a precious tearoom, this neighborhood gem is a reliable crowd-pleaser. Colorful, market-driven cooking starts with excellent, crusty house bread made with garlic scapes, sundried tomatoes, olives or whatever else the chef has in mind. Are soft shell crabs in season? Is it time for morels? Such questions are front of mind for this honest kitchen, which doesn’t get too fussy with the cooking. Familiar flavors ring true in hearty entrees like the meltingly tender Cornish hen brushed in a smoky-sweet barbecue sauce. Fresh pasta, like the braised oxtail tortellini, conveniently comes in appetizer portions. The pacing here can be a bit leisurely, but when the food is this satisfying, what’s the hurry?;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11638;Trius Winery & Restaurant;Canada;Niagara-on-the-Lake;1249 Niagara Stone Rd., Niagara-on-the-Lake, L0S 1J0, Canada;43.2128256;-79.133572;56;false;false;Contemporary;You could spend the afternoon at this expansive winery in Niagara wandering the vineyards and hanging by the outdoor sparkling bar. Or, you could make a beeline for a table with Chef Frank Dodd. Since 2006, he has spearheaded the property’s culinary arm, sourcing from nearby farms and paying close attention to the seasons. The menu offers a two and three course prix-fixe and has wide appeal: Gin-cured smoked salmon with warm potato pancakes is an elegant start before digging into heartier entrees like maple-brined grilled pork chops, corn and chorizo stuffed quail, and scallops with sweet pea and mascarpone ravioli. Lunch is the best time to drop by so you can sit on the patio, look out across the vines, and take in the setting.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11639;Mama Fatma;Canada;Vaughan;10385 Weston Rd., Unit 7B, Vaughan, L4H 3T4, Canada;43.85482;-79.56207;54;true;false;Turkish;On name alone, you can bet that nobody leaves this restaurant hungry. Kebabs charred over glowing coals, meats spinning on a spit, and fluffy, dome-like rounds of pita cooked in a wood-burning oven are served here in abundance. Such is the appeal of this Vaughan favorite that has fed local families well for years. In fact, it’s not uncommon to see large groups huddled around a feast that covers every corner of the table. Tiny poached beef dumplings coated in a garlicky yogurt sauce (kayseri mantısı) could be a meal of their own. Flatbreads topped with everything from tomatoes to ground beef add to the carb-loading. The menu is lengthy, but servers are quick to make suggestions. There’s rarely room for dessert, but there’s always a place for hot tea.;Air conditioning;[]
11640;Buca;Canada;Toronto;604 King St. W., Toronto, M5V 1M6, Canada;43.6445257;-79.4002881;99;false;false;Italian;Note: Temporarily closed Tucked underground through an alleyway entrance, this hideout is nonetheless a very poorly kept secret, drawing acclaim from all quarters with its hearty, meat-centric Italian fare. For starters, a notable selection of salumi is artfully cured and aged in house, showcasing carefully sourced heritage breed pork in exemplary versions of coppa or prosciuttini (sliced wafer-thin, naturally). Handmade pastas and crisp Roman-style pizzas both vie for attention, with intriguing accoutrements like wild boar soppressata and Calabrese-style braised pork—a dilemma best resolved by covering more ground with a group. Note that a second location on Scollard shifts focus to the fruits of the ocean, as in buttery Nova Scotia lobster matched with fresh angel hair pasta.;Air conditioning;[]
11641;Fat Rabbit;Canada;Saint Catharines;34 Geneva St., Saint Catharines, L2R 4M4, Canada;43.1617051;-79.2398662;63;false;true;Steakhouse;Every city needs a restaurant that’s easy for walk-ins, doesn’t take itself too seriously, and cooks with gusto. Focusing on house-made charcuterie and excellent steaks grilled over charcoal, this casual butcher delivers flavors in spades. One could make a meal out of superb slices of bresaola tinged with warm Christmas spices, melting sheets of mortadella studded with pistachios, and spicy salami lifted with orange zest. Steaks are sizeable, best shared with friends, and thrive with sauces like au poivre and piri piri. There are vegetables, too, like a cold green bean salad dressed with anchovy vinaigrette and toasted pine nuts. On the way out, check the surrounding fridges for take-home goodies like pork ragu, guanciale, and prime steaks.;Air conditioning;[]
11642;Lucie;Canada;Toronto;100 Yonge St., Toronto, M5C 2W1, Canada;43.6500269;-79.3783147;81;true;true;French;Owner Yannick Bigourdan named his French restaurant after his grandmother who clearly inspired his journey into the world of hospitality. No doubt she would approve of the warm, inclusive atmosphere and the attentive service. It’s a sizeable space, whose quasi-industrial looks are tempered with an abundance of hanging pendant lights, while shaded glass in front of the kitchen allows hints of the activity within. While the food is recognizably Gallic, there’s a discernible contemporary edge to the dishes, whether that’s the rewarding vichyssoise or the quail with sweetbreads. Lunch is a relatively simple affair but things go up a gear at dinner, with a six-course tasting menu offered alongside the prix fixe. Even the cocktails have something of a French accent.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11643;Quatrefoil;Canada;Hamilton;16 Sydenham St., Hamilton, L9H 2T4, Canada;43.2673579;-79.9567612;87;false;false;Contemporary;This Victorian house in charming Dundas has been a fixture of the city’s dining scene since 2010. No doubt, countless birthdays and anniversaries have been celebrated under the talented wings of chef-owner Fraser Macfarlane, who offers a short but poignant menu that stays well within the boundaries of familiar, upscale dining. Beautifully seared sea scallops arrive in a pool of corn puree with bacon butter sauce. There’s duck breast from Quebec, glazed in lavender and thoughtfully paired with kale, pear chutney, and scallion pancakes. There’s also grilled tenderloin, halibut with tarragon vin blanc, and lemon tarts lined with red currant jam. It’s all very friendly and delightful, in a space carefully managed by a team that’s much of the same.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11644;CÀ PHÊ RANG;Canada;Toronto;147 Spadina Ave., Toronto, M5V 2L7, Canada;43.6480551;-79.395861;30;false;false;Vietnamese;This collaboration between Chef Matty Matherson and his mentor Rang Nguyen has established itself as a firm favorite on Spadina for lovers of Vietnamese food. One bite of the banh mi with succulent roasted pork and you’ll be transported back to Ho Chi Minh City on that backpacker’s trip you once took. The bowls of pho will warm the bones and gladden the heart – the sliced rare beef is well worth ordering – and the chicken wings are cooked to order in a kitchen that appears to be almost the same size as the dining area. The prices are fair, the service helpful and efficient and the room has a colorful, bright, laid-back vibe. For a quick refuel or a bite with friends, this little place might just hit the spot.;Air conditioning;[]
11645;156 Cumberland;Canada;Toronto;156 Cumberland St., Toronto, M5R 1A8, Canada;43.6699298;-79.3932967;22;true;false;Korean, Fusion;Note: This restaurant is temporarily closed.Pockets of fried tofu skin stuffed with gochujang beef tartare topped with fried onions. Hand-torn noodles with seared baby scallops, zucchini puree and parmesan. On a packed street squished among a jigsaw puzzle of stores, this quirky Yorkville restaurant doesn’t fit neatly in a box, but that’s the point. A young team has designed a small menu grounded in Korean cooking with global inspiration. Guests looking for something a little more familiar but nonetheless refined should swing for the beef short ribs, marinated in a sweet kalbi soy and paired with grilled maitake and spinach namool. The space is minimally designed with strawberry-pink walls and white kitchen tile on the ground floor and a darker, more business-friendly setting upstairs.;Air conditioning;[]
11647;Northern Smokes;Canada;Scarborough;371 Old Kingston Rd., Unit 12, Scarborough, M1C 1B7, Canada;43.7837048;-79.1696098;99;true;true;Barbecue, American;It's a ride from downtown to get to this spot in Scarborough tucked inside a simple strip mall, but the smoky aroma will beckon you inside. Imran Ali opened Northern Smokes in 2019 with the simple promise of traditional barbecued meats and sides. A custom reverse-flow wood stick-burning smoker and seasoned split hard wood infuse the fully halal meat with delicious flavor. Order as a multi-meat plate, as a sandwich, or by the pound, and with everything from tender, Montreal-style brisket and Korean-style short ribs in a sweet marinade to chicken, there's plenty to be had. Sides are a terrific complement to the meaty delights, and just in case you forgot that you weren't in the American South, maple-smoked beans will remind you exactly where you are.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11648;Adrak Yorkville;Canada;Toronto;138 Avenue Rd., Toronto, M5R 2H6, Canada;43.674535;-79.3965475;54;false;true;Indian, Regional Cuisine;How many dining rooms could you describe as regal? This is surely one of them. No expense was spared in the design, with hand-carved furniture, cushy, turmeric-colored booths lining the walls and striking archways all basking in a golden aura. But good looks can only take you so far, and this kitchen rises to the occasion with precisely seasoned, carefully cooked dishes inspired from regions all across India. A fiery thecha paneer tikka showcases creativity while crisp garlic naan and meaty kebabs roasted in clay tandoor ovens are a nod to familiar favorites. One very fragrant chicken biryani baked under puff pastry and served with a sauce of peanuts, chilies and yogurt stands as a refreshing change of pace from the standard preparation.;Air conditioning;[]
11649;Amal;Canada;Toronto;131 Bloor St. W., Toronto, M5S 1R1, Canada;43.6689039;-79.3925909;15;true;true;Lebanese;Looking for a bite to eat in between shopping and sightseeing? Amal, with a sexy, sleek, mod Middle Eastern look and ambient vibe, is just the place. Tables are always in demand here, but the smartly dressed service team handles it all seamlessly. Weekends are especially buzzy thanks to a DJ spinning tunes.Expect modern presentations of classic Lebanese and Middle Eastern dishes prepared with authenticity, heart and refinement. Order a few mezze to start—perhaps the seared halloumi or truffle rakakat, a plate of crisp pastry rolls dipped in pistachios and filled with truffle-infused cream. Then, a delicious skewer or char-grilled chicken Tawok are worthy orders. Baklava, that classic dessert, is always a good idea.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
11650;George;Canada;Toronto;111C Queen St. E., Toronto, M5C 1S2, Canada;43.653462;-79.3742882;34;true;true;Contemporary;Set in a red brick building that echoes the historic vibe of its surroundings, George has been one of Toronto's most popular restaurants since opening in 2003. Inside, the room exudes charm with its industrial bones mixed with an upscale bistro look and feel. A display kitchen turning out enjoyable cooking for the amiable crowd.Diners keep returning for always pleasing cuisine that features the likes of seared high-quality halibut nestled in potato puree dressed with finely diced, crispy lardons and sweet peas. In addition to à la carte, there is the choice of a 5-, 7- or 10-course tasting which the chef composes spontaneously.Half-pour cocktails and 3- or 5-oz glasses of wine are just right for those who prefer to imbibe with restraint.;Terrace;[]
11651;Aloette;Canada;Toronto;163 Spadina Ave., Toronto, M5V 2A5, Canada;43.6484508;-79.3960828;86;true;true;Contemporary;Open since 2017, this stylish bistro remains one of the coolest reservations in town. Chef Patrick Kriss and his well-oiled restaurant group again demonstrate that they have the Midas touch. With the tasting menu-only ALO just upstairs, the team here is impressively polished in this diner setting. No wider than a train car, the cozy space offers satisfying, approachable dishes that look and taste far better than imagined. Iceberg wedges dressed in chive cream arrive under a mountain of puffed wild rice. A complimentary loaf of cheddar brioche wouldn’t be out of place on white tablecloth. Everyone wants the burger. And for dessert, there must be pie. The signature lemon meringue is a towering finale that will have you rolling out the door.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11652;La Banane;Canada;Toronto;227 Ossington Ave., Toronto, M6J 2Z8, Canada;43.6490359;-79.420529;83;true;true;French, Steakhouse;It may have something to do with the crowd of artists, movie stars and sophisticates who have made this their perch. Or, it could be the ambience defined by rich, seductive colors and loud, high-energy music. Either way, it's all very hip and very cool at La Banane. The cooking is equally lavish, featuring a well-stocked raw bar, wagyu steaks and plenty of truffle and foie gras in between. Start your evening at the elegant bar with a perfectly chilled shrimp cocktail before digging into Salt Spring mussels with Normandy cider and crème fraiche. Beef flatiron set in a delicious sauce au poivre is a classic done right. And to finish, don’t miss the Gâteau à la banane, a sweet cake accompanied by salted caramel ice cream and caramelized bananas.;Air conditioning;[]
11653;Bar Isabel;Canada;Toronto;797 College St., Toronto, M6G 1C7, Canada;43.6547095;-79.4207874;45;true;false;Spanish;Right on bustling College Street, Bar Isabel charms diners with its old-world tavern vibe and broad appeal. Perfect for groups, it's also just right for solo diners, as some some dishes may be prepared in half portions, inviting exploration. Chef Grant van Gameren's cooking is heartfelt and there is never anything frilly or overwrought on his Spanish tapas menu. Dishes are rustic and straightforward and there is a clear focus on quality flavors married with strong product. Case in point? The pork secreto, which takes a flavorful grilled pork cheek and ratchets it up a notch with a honey and apple cider reduction. The craft beer list is interesting, and there are plenty of ciders, Spanish wine and cocktails, particularly those employing Sherry, on offer.;Air conditioning;[]
11654;Langdon Hall Country House & Spa;Canada;Cambridge;1 Langdon Dr., Cambridge, N3H 4R8, Canada;43.38248;-80.37843;99;true;true;Contemporary;Located a mere hour away from Toronto, this historic 19th-century Cambridge estate has long been something of a special retreat in Ontario. The mansion sits on 75 acres with a spa, walking trails, culinary gardens, and, of course, its signature restaurant. A stately interior with white tablecloths and a well-heeled staff fit the aesthetic. Chef Jason Bangerter has led this kitchen since 2013 and cooks with a kind of familiar French classicism. Think warm lobster with English peas and Champagne velouté or an indulgent foie gras parfait paired with a superb slice of warm, buttery brioche. A lengthier chef’s tasting offers a comprehensive look at the day’s menu. To drink, the wine list is an impressive collection of top producers and older vintages.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
11655;Kiin;Canada;Toronto;326 Adelaide St. W., Toronto, M5V 1R3, Canada;43.64767;-79.39217;79;true;true;Thai;Chef Nuit Regular impresses with her elaborate, one-of-a-kind vision of royal Thai cuisine. The elegant space is a prime setting for equally elegant dishes, which are presented with flair. Colorful mounds of rice, pineapple and dumplings shaped like flowers, and so much more arrive in petite forms in small bowls and on large platters. The dishes themselves will ring familiar, from Isan-style sausage and larb, to hot and sour beef soup and the famed khao soi, all of it seasoned and spiced in a measured manner. The tender Boombai short rib glossed in a dark curry is a particular standout. First-timers should start with the signature chef’s tasting, which nearly covers the entire menu alongside a few bonus dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11656;SARA;Canada;Toronto;98 Portland St., Toronto, M5V 2N2, Canada;43.6450607;-79.4003576;94;true;true;Contemporary;Sara, with its cool, almost monastic modernity, is a place to keep the outside world at bay—the tables are even designed with center compartments for storing phones. Reconnection and shared experiences seem to be the theme here, where a globally inspired, contemporary shared plates menu takes center stage. Fret not if you've arrived solo, as many dishes are available in half-portions for a deeper survey of the kitchen's ability. And able they are. Standouts include ikura latkes, featuring two butternut squash latkes topped with a lemon chive crème fraîche, smoked ikura and finished with a maple kombu drizzle. Alaskan king crab is served with a nuoc cham sauce and topped with crispy fried rice finished with avocado, curls of scallion and cilantro.;Air conditioning;[]
11657;Viaggio;Canada;Toronto;1727 Dundas St. W., Toronto, M6K 1V4, Canada;43.6500725;-79.4389529;70;true;true;Italian;You might consider dropping by even if it means you can only order dessert. A novel effort that feels part soufflé, part pancake, the signature tiramisu finished with espresso maple syrup and whipped mascarpone may very well be one of the best desserts in the city. Many dishes, in fact, feel unique to this neighborhood charmer, which could have very easily played it safe with standard Italian dishes. However, this is a kitchen that chooses to top pizzas with smoked pastrami and sauerkraut and chooses to toss tagliolini with charred octopus glossed in smoked dashi butter. Refreshingly creative, such moves pay off in delicious ways.The historic building boasts a handsome dining room as well as an inviting deck lit with strung garden lights.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11658;Antler;Canada;Toronto;1454 Dundas St. W., Toronto, M6J 1Y6, Canada;43.6494976;-79.4305813;55;true;true;Contemporary;This small chef-run restaurant in quaint Little Portugal is cozy and rustic with a welcoming bar, walls of exposed brick and forest scenes and, yes, a mounted deer with antlers (naturally). Chef/co-owner Michael Hunter lives and breathes by the locally sourced and grown ethos, and takes it up a notch by focusing on game. First up, a carrot and smoked ricotta salad. Sound boring? It's anything but, with roasted heirloom carrots and ribbons of yellow and red raw carrots over a pool of creamy, smoked ricotta. Then, pan-seared and roasted Ontario venison, bathed in a green peppercorn sauce and served with a wedge of hot Boulangère potatoes, hits all the right notes. For dessert, pear tart Tatin is a wedge of pure bliss.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11659;Dreyfus;Canada;Toronto;96 Harbord St., Toronto, M5S 1G6, Canada;43.6629067;-79.4032098;37;true;false;French;No obvious signage, curtains drawn and the front door frosted top to bottom. What could this cozy French bistro be hiding? The answer is indulgence. Situated on the first floor of a narrow townhouse, Dreyfus is the kind of dinner you have before hibernation and after an annual physical. Rare (and sadly empty) trophy wines line the room’s perimeter, while servers explain that the fries are for the pâté and that the doughnuts are for the smoked trout dip garnished with roe. That Zach Kolomeir cooks with maximum impact shouldn’t be a shock given his tenure at Montreal’s famed Joe Beef. Sitting elbow to elbow, oenophiles looking for primo vino will have to ask for off-menu bottles, some of which sit in plain sight above the bar.;Air conditioning;[]
11661;Alobar Yorkville;Canada;Toronto;57A-162 Cumberland St., Toronto, M5R 1A8, Canada;43.6699762;-79.3934727;64;false;false;French, Seafood;The warm and flattering lighting, the low ceiling, and the curved banquettes all make you think you’ve walked into a cocktail bar rather than a destination restaurant. But that noisy buzz of contentment you hear on arrival is a testament to the food, which hits the spot just as well as the skillfully made cocktails. Seafood is a big deal here, whether scallops or bream, but meats too, such as Creekstone striploin and Iberico pork chop, demonstrate that the kitchen knows its way around a charcoal grill. Those familiar with the Alo Food Group’s other restaurants will recognize classics like the wedge salad, Dover sole, and the banana cream pie holding court in this dining room as well. A second location downtown offers a near identical menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11662;Lapinou;Canada;Toronto;642 King St. W., Toronto, M5V 1M7, Canada;43.6441495;-79.4018599;29;false;true;French, Contemporary;Chilly Toronto nights call for cozy spaces, and Lapinou delivers in spades with its beamed ceiling, vintage-style oil lamps, forest green booths and an eye-catching green-veined marble bar. Just west of the Theater District in an area teeming with standout spots, Lapinou pulls its weight with a fresh spin on classic bistro fare. Don't confuse tried and true with ho-hum though, as Chef Jamie Ullrich carefully balances tradition with intrigue. Shrimp cocktail is a simple but elegant starter, as is the perfect disc of beef tartare topped with an egg yolk and sided by sourdough toast. Duck confit is comfort in a casserole dish with buttery white flageolet beans and garlicky andouille sausage. The delightful tarte au cafe rounds out the enjoyable experience.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
11663;Mimi Chinese;Canada;Toronto;265 Davenport Rd., Toronto, M5R 1J9, Canada;43.6743358;-79.3984679;89;false;false;Chinese;Lipstick red banquettes and servers fitted in sharp suits make for a different kind of Chinese restaurant. Unlike the homestyle comforts and flavors of its sibling Sunnys, this Yorkville looker pulls in an equally gussied-up crowd out for an upscale evening. The kitchen takes regional classics and spins them with just enough style. The shrimp toast, brilliantly made with fried bread and a hot mustard mayo, is worth a visit alone, but don't miss out on the scallop crudo with fried donut and that soulful soy broth. Spice-hounds will be all over the Hunan chili sea bass, and someone should probably order the picturesque “four-foot belt noodle.” There’s plenty to drink too, with sharp cocktails and a thorough selection of baijiu.;Air conditioning;[]
11664;Giulietta;Canada;Toronto;972 College St., Toronto, M6H 1A5, Canada;43.6533974;-79.4276823;71;false;true;Italian, Pizza;Every neighborhood deserves a reliable hotspot that cooks, pours and serves with remarkable ease. Dufferin Grove has this in Giulietta, a stylish (but not too stylish) Italian looker by Chef Rob Rossi. Even if you don’t live nearby, this talented team treats every guest like a long-time VIP. And the food? This is cooking that comforts, thanks to a kitchen that makes the most out of every dish on the menu. Yellowfin tuna crudo with bergamot marmalade is a vibrant way to begin before moving into heartier dishes. A diner might attempt ordering both the ricotta agnolotti with morels as well as the mafalde with veal cheek ragu, but don't forget pizza. Charred, puffy and dressed with smart ingredients, the savory pie is greedily delicious.;Air conditioning;[]
11665;Katamachi Kawaguchi;Japan;Osaka;1-3-11 Katamachi, Miyakojima-ku, Osaka, 534-0025, Japan;34.693005;135.526253;21;true;false;Japanese;The low-profile exterior, small billboard and stripped-down accoutrements express an understated Japanese architecture aesthetic. The goal here is cuisine of which one never tires. Rishiri kombu kelp is selected for the dashi stock drawn for soups, reassuring with its light flavour. Fermented seasonings are handmade fish sauces, provide the subtle seasoning that enhances other flavours. Relying on patient craftsmanship rather than fancy ingredients, Katamachi Kawaguchi impresses with technique and singular character.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11667;Kamado;Japan;Osaka;4-1-11 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696269;135.505298;81;true;true;Contemporary;A wood fire blazes in a kamado, or traditional wood-fired stove. Echoing the shop’s name, the meal begins with a bowl of freshly cooked rice straight from the kamado. The style is fusion of Italian and Japanese cuisine, with wood-fired cooking the unifying concept. The hearth is a primaeval scene of meat roasting over glowing embers, yet the flavours are distinctly contemporary. A dish of pasta wraps up the evening. Continuing the theme, the pottery on which the fare is displayed was also fired in a wood-fuelled kiln.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11669;Germoglio;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 172 Higashisakaicho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8217, Japan;34.989348;135.758377;71;false;true;Italian;The name is Italian for ‘bud’, expressing the desire to sprout, blossom and grow, restaurant and chef alike. The chef learned his craft in the Piedmont region, so northern Italian techniques are his speciality. Handmade pastas such as tajarin and tagliolini showcase his experience. Garlic is used sparingly so as not to mask the native flavours of ingredients. Vegetables from Ohara and duck from Kameoka are expressions of thanks for the bounty of Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11670;Gion Senryu;Japan;Kyoto;227-3 Nishinocho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0088, Japan;35.006397;135.77373;54;true;true;Tempura;Service consists of tempura and decoratively arranged sashimi in season, with guests’ favoured tempura items added as desired – the relaxation of leaving the menu to the chef combined with the joy of choosing. The head chef is a vegetable expert, so the list of vegetables is extensive. As with wine pairings, sauces are sometimes chosen to suit particular tempura items. Rice is freshly cooked in an earthenware pot. Tendon (rice topped with tempura) and Tencha (rice served in a tea broth often with tempura) can both be enjoyed a little at a time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11671;PRESTAU;Japan;Osaka;2-17-17 Shimmachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0013, Japan;34.677398;135.491043;47;false;false;Italian;The restaurant’s name is a portmanteau of ‘impress’ combined with ‘restaurant’. The concept is a ‘restaurant that touches the heartstrings’, and PRESTAU aims to do just that. His experience in Kobe leads the chef to favour ingredients from Hyogo Prefecture, served on Tambayaki flatware. Preparing each item to its best advantage is his top priority. This is Italian cuisine in a modern style.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11672;Takezaki;Japan;Kyoto;150 Takeyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0823, Japan;35.012295;135.762624;57;true;false;Japanese;Seating consists of tatami mats around a sunken kotatsu counter. The intimate space closes the distance with the owner-chef, fostering a welcoming atmosphere. Fare is prepared from few ingredients, the better to draw out the flavour of each. Unusual fish species, indicative of the chef’s curiosity, are crafted as decorative sashimi and grilled items, in a search for novel flavours. All steps, from kitchen preparation to service at the table, are handled matter-of-factly by the chef alone.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
11674;Hozan;Japan;Osaka;3-13 Higashikozucho, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0021, Japan;34.667767;135.522602;98;false;false;Japanese;Hozan’s allure lies in its menu’s exhaustive range of fish dishes. Having apprenticed at a seafood restaurant, the owner-chef is a master of fish preparation. Fresh and aged fish are handled differently, conveying all the depth and subtlety of their flavours. The meal begins with a seafood iimushi (mochi rice steamed with toppings). For soups, the dashi stock is drawn from the seafood, modulating the flavour. Keen that every guest should enjoy to their heart’s content, Hozan offers rice in earthenware pots as a choice of white rice or fish takikomi-gohan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11675;Yamaji Yosuke;Japan;Kyoto;570-151 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002646;135.775698;96;true;false;French;Yamaji Yosuke prizes originality, paying homage to French cuisine while blazing his own trail in gastronomy. Yamaji named his shop after himself to assert that individuality. His apprenticeship in France gave him a precious opportunity to build relationships with chefs from all over the world, learning about the cuisines of Italy, the Middle East, China and more. The squid carbonara recalls a co-creation with a chef in Paris.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11676;Chikuyuan Taro no Atsumori;Japan;Kyoto;242-12 Yoancho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8022, Japan;35.018511;135.758853;26;true;true;Soba;‘Soba is medicine’, says the signboard. The restaurant feels soba is so crammed with nutrients that they tout it as yakuzen, ‘medicinal cooking’, and hope that it brings good health. When ground with its husk, buckwheat acquires a dark brown cast and mysterious flavour. Don’t pass up the “Atsumori-soba”, soba boiled fresh and served hot from the pot. Soba water is poured under the bamboo steamer to keep the noodles warm. Hot dipping sauce with lashings of chopped Kujo green onion, egg and wasabi is a distinctive touch.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Shoes must be removed;[]
11677;Bramble & Hare;USA;Boulder;1970 13th St., Boulder, 80302, USA;40.018145;-105.2785678;50;false;true;American;It's a farmhouse-meets-lodge vibe at Jill and Chef Eric Skokan's Bramble & Hare, where wood paneled walls and wood floors keep things rustic, and chairs and loveseats are draped with fur throws for an extra dose of charm. The couple's own farm supplies most of the inspiration for the dishes on this American menu—even down to the prosciutto they age in-house from their own pigs. Those impressive ingredients aren't gussied up in this kitchen, where a smart but straightforward cooking style allows them to truly shine. Many items are married in new and creative ways. Case in point? The salted turnips served with a pistachio purée, pickled onions and that fantastic house-cured prosciutto, delivering a fantastic surprise in a well-balanced, bright dish.;Air conditioning;[]
11678;Fruition;USA;Denver;1313 E. 6th Ave., Denver, 80218, USA;39.7257;-104.97144;70;false;true;American, Contemporary;Although the space itself isn’t exactly ritzy, top-flight service and indulgent cooking combine to make guests here feel like royalty despite the lack of luxury trimmings. Chef Alex Seidel is one of the Denver dining scene’s leading lights, at the vanguard of ingredient-centered eco-conscious cuisine. Whether it's a crisp golden-brown latke served with sweet onion creme fraiche and smoked trout roe, or impeccably seared scallops with creamy farro, the dishes here impress with their strong technique, pristine products and rich flavors, but an element of playfulness is also apparent, as in a fried maitake slider in the style of Nashville hot chicken. For an unfussy finale, chewy, crispy chocolate chip cookies, served warm and melty, are sure to satisfy.;;[]
11679;Element 47;USA;Aspen;675 E. Durant Ave, Aspen, 81611, USA;39.18644;-106.81765;65;false;true;Contemporary;The name is a nod to Aspen’s origins as a silver mining town, and its location inside the luxurious Little Nell Hotel, mere steps away from the slopes, is certainly glitzy. Enter the sleek, modern dining room through the lounge (with a crackling fireplace in season) and settle in for Chef Matt Zubrod's approachable contemporary menu that highlights top-notch ingredients, from seasonal produce like wild mushrooms, to meats like locally raised lamb and wagyu-breed beef. Lighter dishes like salads are thoughtfully composed, and house-made pastas like hazelnut cavatelli with rabbit ragu and fennel will satisfy heartier appetites. Diners will make note of the array of bottles displayed behind glass in the bar area, a telltale sign of the restaurant’s impressive wine program.;Interesting wine list;[]
11680;Smok;USA;Denver;3330 Brighton Blvd., #202, Denver, 80216, USA;39.76857;-104.98041;19;true;false;Barbecue, American;This counter service fast-casual concept in the Source Hotel may have an approachable, no-frills ambiance, but Chef Bill Espiricueta, an Austin native, is clearly serious about barbecue. From succulent brisket to jalapeño sausage links studded with oozing cheddar cheese, the restaurant's namesake is deployed skillfully, pervading the food with a subtle, savory aroma that doesn't overpower. Typical sides like slaw and mac & cheese are passable, but shouldn't distract from the meaty main event—fried fare like sweet potato tots and French fries might tempt those with truly outsize appetites, and the Nashville hot chicken sandwich has its crowd of devotees.;;[]
11681;Mercantile Dining and Provision;USA;Denver;1701 Wynkoop St., Denver, 80202, USA;39.7535403;-104.9997319;75;false;true;American;They may have their own entrance, but it's worth the walk through Union Station to arrive at Mercantile Dining & Provisions. Chef/owner Alex Seidel presides over this handsome spot complete with wood floors and tables, tufted leather banquettes and a soothing palette of brown and blue. The elevated take on American comfort food wins over guests who dine on starters, pastas and meat-forward entrees like venison and Tomahawk steak. Portions are large, but expect spot-on flavors and executions. Tuck in to a half confit Miller farms chicken with gorgeous golden-brown crispy skin for a dish that feels at once classic and unexpected. To conclude, a flaky galette-style apple pie with roughly chopped, skin-on apples is bested by vanilla ice cream, a Vin Santo sauce and smoked cinnamon.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
11682;Mawa's Kitchen;USA;Aspen;305 Aspen Airport Business Center, Ste. F, Aspen, 81611, USA;39.2205223;-106.860941;71;true;false;Contemporary, American;Mawa's Kitchen may not be the easiest to find with its tucked-away entrance, but stay the course because it's worth visiting this welcoming spot. Light colors, tasteful artwork and bare tables set with wildflower-filled vases create a mood-boosting vibe inside, while the outdoor terrace is a breezy perch. The food is equally appealing (think new-world meets old-world). Owner Mawa McQueen, who hails from the Côte d’Ivoire, delivers extraordinary quality with everyday value, such as black-eyed pea hummus served with pickled, charred and smoked vegetables and bread. The African chicken and seafood gumbo is boldly spiced and finger-licking good, but don't fill up because you'll want dessert—especially a wedge of that dreamy cheesecake.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11683;Blackbelly Market;USA;Boulder;1606 Conestoga St., Boulder, 80301, USA;40.0148356;-105.2279535;51;true;false;American, Steakhouse;Chef/owner Hosea Rosenberg is a familiar name in these parts, and Blackbelly Market is just one of the reasons why. There are plenty of spots to sip and snack here, whether at the counter facing the open kitchen, the well-stocked bar area, or the polished, dark wood tables. Take a peek at the refrigerated, glassed-in butchery room, where you may see Head Butcher Kelly Kawachi holding court. You'll taste her handiwork across the menu, and in the charcuterie boards showcasing duck rillette, pork terrine, headcheese and saucisson. Koji-cured pork is supremely flavorful, while agnolotti made of caramelized onion dough in a fragrant mushroom "brodo" is an inventive twist. For the win, order the donuts, especially the chocolate hazelnut cream with hazelnut caramel and milk chocolate-hazelnut topping.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11684;Zoe Ma Ma;USA;Boulder;919 Pearl St., Boulder, 80302, USA;40.01752;-105.283304;99;true;true;Chinese;This humble operation wears its charms on its sleeves: a mother-and-son collaboration between businessman Edwin Zoe and Chef Anna Zoe, who cooks up her take on traditional from-scratch recipes using high quality ingredients, resulting in soul-satisfying, homey dishes—the appeal is not hard to find. The pint-sized space is counter service only—you’ll seat yourself and bus your own table—but the exceedingly reasonable prices make this an easy value proposition. Staples like dan dan noodles and potstickers are top-notch, but look out for rotating daily specials like Sichuan braised beef soup noodles. A second location, in Denver's Union Station, is just as popular.;;[]
11685;Olivia;USA;Denver;290 S. Downing St., Denver, 80209, USA;39.7112681;-104.9732617;76;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;Partners Ty Leon, Austin Carson and Heather Morrison bring their talents to bear at one of the city's hottest tables, respectively overseeing cooking, beverages and hospitality (Morrison's daughter is also the restaurant's namesake). House-made pasta occupies the bulk of the menu, from bronze-die extruded gemelli with Umbrian sausage and pecorino cream, or hand-shaped tortellini filled with braised duck. The offerings range from fairly traditional, like the tagliatelle Bolognese, to inventively globe-trotting, as in ricotta gnocchi paired coconut lobster bisque and black garlic, but assertive flavors are a constant throughout. Inventive cocktails serve well as aperitifs, or to sip while lingering in the relaxed, comfortable atmosphere.;;[]
11686;Splendido at the Chateau;USA;Beaver Creek;17 Chateau Ln., Beaver Creek, 81620, USA;39.6054;-106.5213;64;true;true;Contemporary;You might think the name lays things on a bit thick, but the setting is as grand and as comfortable as could be hoped for, and the warm, attentive service is sure to make you feel like royalty. Looking beyond the glamorous environs, you'll find a thoughtful menu overseen by longtime chef Brian Ackerman, which straddles the line between creative and classic, seen in a pomegranate-marinated rack of Colorado lamb. Dover sole, pan-seared before being adroitly filleted tableside and served with brown butter beurre blanc, is a menu staple for good reason. End with an airy soufflé, or opt for something a bit more nostalgic, like a chocolate and peanut butter pave.;;[]
11687;Safta;USA;Denver;3330 Brighton Blvd., Denver, 80216, USA;39.7687444;-104.9802092;97;true;true;Israeli;Safta may mean "grandmother" in Hebrew, but there's nothing old school about this restaurant, Chef Alon Shaya's first outside Louisiana. Instead, this hot spot is located in the trendy Source Hotel. At first glance, it looks like you’re walking toward a coffee counter (and you are), but it wraps around to the restaurant and the kitchen. It's all airy and upbeat, just like the Israeli menu that lists many favorites but feels original and interesting. There must be hummus, of course, but here it's given a fresh take with roasted chanterelle mushrooms and chermoula butter served with freshly baked pita. Next up is a selection of salatim, or pickles and spreads, followed by a panoply of dishes ranging from harissa chicken, duck matzo ball soup, and short rib-stuffed cabbage to pomegranate lamb shank.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11688;Prospect;USA;Aspen;330 E. Main St., Aspen, 81611, USA;39.19088;-106.81944;45;true;false;Contemporary;Located in the swanky, thoroughly photogenic Hotel Jerome, Prospect offers its own bespoke take on Aspen dining. The colorful, eclectic space provides the setting for contemporary cuisine that celebrates ingredients from local producers. Diners select between a three-course “Taste of the Land” prix fixe, or a longer “Colorado Journey” tasting menu. A well-appointed bar provides an assortment of libations.;;[]
11690;Noisette;USA;Denver;3254 Navajo St., Ste. 100, Denver, 80211, USA;39.7633456;-105.0042659;45;true;true;French, Contemporary;Chefs Tim Lu and Lillian Cho earned their chops in some of New York's top restaurants but thankfully chose Denver to open their own place. Sophisticated and spacious with a separate patisserie up front, the dining room is elegant, but the real draw is the precisely crafted dishes bound by tradition while reflecting a creative approach. Foie gras au torchon with a light coating of Björn's lavender honey and a Port reduction is served with a buttery brioche for a classic take. Next, a lush beef entrecôte enthralls with tender meat topped with petals of sweet roasted pearl onions and a Bordelaise sauce that offers indulgence in every last bite. End on a sweet note with tarte tropézienne aux fraises, a light-as-air brioche filled with diplomat cream and strawberry jam.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11691;Barolo Grill;USA;Denver;3030 E. 6th Ave., Denver, 80206, USA;39.7255061;-104.9515215;50;false;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;Here you'll find one of Denver's most esteemed and longstanding fine dining establishments, which keeps a loyal stable of regulars thanks to its singular hospitality and finely tuned, flavorful take on Northern Italian cuisine. The service is among the warmest and most knowledgeable you'll find anywhere, a fact that surely owes something to annual staff trips to Europe. The team is only too glad to provide expert assistance plumbing the depths of one of Colorado's most impressive wine lists—which encompasses a nearly biblical amount of the restaurant's namesake—to match a menu that might include delicate, soufflé-like spinach and parmesan sformato, handmade tortellini filled with roasted squash and taleggio, and a signature braised duck with kalamata olives.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
11693;Santo;USA;Boulder;1265 Alpine Ave., Boulder, 80304, USA;40.02566;-105.28103;40;true;true;American, Mexican;Chef Hosea Rosenberg draws inspiration from his hometown of Taos, in northern New Mexico, to deliver a menu of satisfying, rustic cooking. Guests can stop in at all times of day to satisfy a craving for southwestern fare. In the morning, grab-and-go breakfast burritos are the mainstay, while at lunch, casual counter service encompasses a broader array of options from pozole to tortas. Finally, at dinner, full table service accommodates a livelier crowd where margaritas flow with the full menu in play, featuring specialties like roasted chicken mole with red pepper polenta.;;[]
11694;Oak at Fourteenth;USA;Boulder;1400 Pearl St., Boulder, 80302, USA;40.0184038;-105.2772661;82;true;true;Contemporary;Smack dab in the heart of charming downtown Boulder, Oak at Fourteenth invites guests to settle in to a space where light wood floors, white walls and a minimalist design aesthetic set a modern tone. The kitchen echoes the contemporary mindset with a hearty menu focused on meat, but with equal care shown to vegetarian dishes. To begin, a vibrant disc of beet tartare is served with mustard ice cream and a beet-colored rice cracker for a dramatic start. Rotisserie chicken with a green apple and celery root slaw is a go-to, but save room for a slice of their peanut butter tart. With its thick cookie crust, thin layer of cherry gelee and a quenelle of celery sorbet balanced on chopped peanuts, it's a nod to that childhood classic: ants on a log.;Air conditioning;[]
11695;Q House;USA;Denver;3421 E. Colfax Ave., Denver, 80206, USA;39.7402495;-104.9466287;72;false;true;Chinese;Wood floors, exposed ducts and garage-style doors keep things casual at Q House, where eager diners dig in to family-style dishes. Chef Christopher Lin shares his Taiwanese heritage on this broad Chinese menu with modern Sichuan leanings. Pick and choose from small and large dishes, all designed for sharing. A plate of chicken and shrimp wontons made with chicken schmaltz and dressed in a sweet soy with rice vinegar and chili oil is a crowd-pleaser. Chong Qing chicken, with cubes of dark meat chicken tossed in potato and rice starch and fried crispy with chilies and Sichuan pepper, is subtle at first, but the heat builds and delivers fantastic flavor.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11696;WYLD;USA;Avon;130 Daybreak Ridge Rd., Avon, 81620, USA;39.6297933;-106.5643368;81;false;true;American, Contemporary;Nestled inside The Ritz-Carlton, Bachelor Gulch, this sophisticated restaurant is far from wild. Instead, it's the very picture of rustic refinement right down to the large windows framing postcard-perfect views of Beaver Creek. Settle in to this laid-back luxe spot and share stories of the day's alpine adventures over likeable dishes like salsa macha atop a crisp tostada with avocado aioli and slices of albacore. Earthy red and yellow beets rest over a creamy, tart tzatziki sprinkled with toasted pumpernickel breadcrumbs in a refreshing first course. Heartier entrees, like chicken under a brick with roasted carrots, parsnips and celery root puree, are especially satisfying after epic days filled with skiing or hiking.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11697;Boulder Dushanbe Tea House;USA;Boulder;1770 13th St., Boulder, 80302, USA;40.0154701;-105.2773137;69;false;true;Eastern European;This hand-built gift from Dushanbe, Boulder's sister city in Tajikistan, offers a respite from quotidian life. Walk through the front garden and you'll be instantly transported to a zen-filled, magical space. If the bucolic setting doesn't lower your blood pressure, the stunning interior that transports you to a faraway culture will. As the name suggests, tea is the raison d'être here, and the selection is comprehensive. From apple strudel and samosas to feijoada and plov (a buttery rice dish studded with chickpeas, dried fruit and grilled beef), the menu reads like a world explorer's diary. Naturally, tea time and afternoon tea are reason alone to visit, and the dessert selection is particularly tempting.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11699;Sweet Basil;USA;Vail;193 Gore Creek Dr., Vail, 81657, USA;39.6407175;-106.374848;33;true;false;Fusion;Opened in 1977, this legendary local establishment has a long and storied history, and it remains as popular now as ever, whether for lunch, après-ski drinks at the bar or dinner. The menu is eclectic, freely borrowing and blending flavors from across the globe, as in tempura-fried mahi mahi tacos with peanut salsa macha, bone marrow pho with scallop, or a miso black garlic-glazed halibut with fondant potatoes. Desserts are whimsical, but seriously good, for example the indulgently named “if you like piña coladas,” which features caramelized pineapple compote, passion fruit pâte de fruit and a crunchy coconut crumble. Carefully mixed cocktails and a compelling wine list round out the abundant appeal of this approachable yet elevated favorite.;Interesting wine list;[]
11700;A5 Steakhouse;USA;Denver;1600 15th St., Denver, 80202, USA;39.7504512;-105.0011928;39;true;false;Steakhouse, American;With its prime corner location, large picture windows and beautifully framed doors, A5 Steakhouse beckons diners with an instant warmth. Inside, an attractive bar is particularly welcoming, especially at happy hour, while the dining room shares a retro vibe complete with kitschy artwork. The kitchen is headed by Partner/Chef Max MacKissock who doles out classic steakhouse favorites with slight variations, as in a wedge salad with cubes of avocado, tomato confit, pickled red onion and crisp guanciale doused in Roquefort dressing. The Denver steak does its namesake proud, with anterior chuck from Blackhawk Farms, KY, flawless technique and taste that warrant a return visit. To finish, choose the banana creme brûlée with spiced sour cherry preserves.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11701;Marco's Coal-Fired;USA;Denver;2129 Larimer St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7544518;-104.9909661;15;true;false;Pizza;Set in the shadow of Coors Field, Marco's takes pride in being the only spot in Colorado to be certified by the Associazione Verace Pizza Napoletana—a stamp of approval from the Italian birthplace of this beloved foodstuff. The crust alone makes a strong case, made with flavorful, hand-stretched dough, expertly fired in a traditional oven, with beautifully blistered, flame-kissed edges, but the quality of the toppings impresses as well, from San Marzano tomatoes, to prosciutto di parma, to aged pecorino. No substitutions are allowed on the Neapolitan pies, but non-traditional offerings will give guests plenty of room to play. Though the menu does have other offerings, as in salad and lasagna, pizza should rightfully hold the center of attention.;;[]
11702;Dio Mio;USA;Denver;3264 Larimer St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7649409;-104.9770313;25;false;true;Italian, Contemporary;Chefs/owners Spencer White and Alex Figura have a background in fine dining, but this popular fast-casual concept thrives on an accessible, laid-back format. Creativity and a clear understanding of flavor go hand in hand on a small, seasonal menu, with house-made forming the centerpiece of the operation (both literally and figuratively—a pasta production table is visible at the heart of the kitchen), from tradition-adjacent mafaldine cacio e pepe, boosted with pink peppercorn, to totally iconoclastic combinations like casarecce with shrimp, dill and toasted parmesan.;;[]
11703;Stella's Cucina;USA;Boulder;1123 Walnut St., Boulder, 80302, USA;40.0166594;-105.2806496;87;true;false;Italian, Contemporary;The entrance flies a bit under the radar (hint: look for the "S" on the door), but once inside owner Stella Spanu's Italian gem, nothing is held back. The place is utterly stunning with a discernible 1930s sexy speakeasy ambience. Chef Filippo Piccini impresses with a focused menu of pan-regional Italian dishes. If comfort is what you need, start with ribollita, that traditional, thick Tuscan soup brimming with vegetables, beans and silky bread. Limone e uova di mare offers a dramatic presentation with a nest of spaghettone alla chitarra, while Milanese di vitello, with a properly thick chop of satiny Limousin veal, is a special for good reason. Finally, babà al rum is an elegant ode to one of Naples' best-known desserts.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11704;Guard and Grace;USA;Denver;1801 California St., Denver, 80202, USA;39.7473205;-104.9897761;40;true;false;Steakhouse, American Contemporary;Guard and Grace occupies an enviable location at the base of the 56-floor Brookfield Building in downtown Denver. Expectations at this restaurant in one of the city's tallest skyscrapers are deservedly high, as this ultra-sleek space delivers day and night. The vast space is stunning, with an oak fire roaring in the open kitchen, a floor-to ceiling wine room and a sophisticated blend of modernity and rusticity. Steaks are the obvious draw but a full seafood bar is a close second. Artichoke and spinach dip is a rich and flavorful starter before tucking in to filet mignon with lime smashed potatoes and chili butter. Chocolate Luxardo cherry cheesecake sided by a scoop of honey Bourbon ice cream is nothing short of indulgent.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11705;Hey Kiddo;USA;Denver;4337 Tennyson St., Ste. 300, Denver, 80212, USA;39.776174;-105.0438293;74;true;true;Contemporary, Fusion;High above Tennyson Street, Hey Kiddo is one of Denver's trendiest restaurants. From the third floor location to the eclectic menu, there is nothing typical about this hot spot. Chef Kelly Whitaker mans the stoves, taking full liberties with an ever-changing menu. There's something for everyone, with oysters, caviar, K-town fried chicken, shrimp toast, crudo and pasta dishes among the tempting options. Flavors and inspiration come from around the world, as in shaken beef that's as much fun as it is delicious. Tonnarelli tossed with asparagus, mushrooms and parmesan is hit with an Asian sauce for a winning dish, and the quirkiness continues through dessert, where rice cream with burnt banana can be topped with sancho, broken cone, lingonberry or caramel.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11706;Brasserie Brixton;USA;Denver;3701 N. Williams St., Denver, 80205, USA;39.7682182;-104.9660289;57;true;true;French;The owners of this cozy spot in North Denver drew its inspiration from their love of the casual bistros and wine bars of Montreal, resulting in a certain approachable charm that makes it a neighborhood restaurant par excellence. It also comes through both in the rustic aesthetic, and moreover in the small menu of staples like steak frites with creamy pepper sauce, rib-sticking chicken fricassee with Boursin pomme purée, and comforting French onion soup, alongside more inventive items like blood sausage fried wontons with tamari vinaigrette. There's also an excellent burger. Well-crafted cocktails and a compact but thoughtful list of thirst-quenching natural wines round out the roster.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11707;Temaki Den;USA;Denver;3350 Brighton Blvd., Denver, 80216, USA;39.7690964;-104.979923;73;true;true;Japanese;Temaki Den is nestled within The Source Hotel + Market Hall. It's an open space, tucked among other vendors, and a dark color palette lends a modern, if moody, feel to this spot. As the name suggests, it is all about temaki, or handrolls, though they do feature aburi (flame-seared) nigiri as well. Begin with broccolini goma-ae, a nicely balanced dish of blanched bright green broccolini dressed in a sesame dressing, before moving on to temaki, available à la carte or as a set. Rolled for guests, one at a time, the Scottish salmon belly with yuzu kosho and crispy shallots is a standout. Don't skip the eggplant nigiri, seared and caramelized with miso to deliver a buttery, rich and slightly sweet knockout flavor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11708;LAVA - Cuisine & Vin;France;Paris;9 rue de la Montagne-Sainte-Geneviève, Paris, 75005, France;48.8490731;2.3487718;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;How do you combine a chef's passion for volcanoes and fire with a sommelier's passion for his craft? This restaurant unites the talents of two hospitality professionals who cut their teeth in renowned establishments. As for the food: the chef serves up his particularly tempting brand of cuisine based on flames and hot coals. French produce is meticulously combined with ingredients that are full of character – often spices – brought back by the chef from his many travels. A case in point: poultry from the Perche area grilled over binchotan, early courgettes and calçots (green onions), poultry jus with juniper. A lively, colourful feast, enhanced by a wide-ranging wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11709;Sienne;France;Saint-Cloud;46 boulevard de la République, Saint-Cloud, 92210, France;48.844411;2.210214;84;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Baptiste Renouard is at the helm of this contemporary bistro, which is open all day long and serves brunch on Sundays. This talented chef is all about culinary indulgence, in the form of dishes peppered with references to the French classics such as œuf meurette (egg in red wine sauce), whiting Colbert, pot-au-feu or pike quenelle. It's concise and flawless! Opt for the upstairs dining area, which has tables close to the large bay windows, or the terrace in fine weather.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11711;Hakuba;France;Paris;Cheval Blanc Paris, 8 quai du Louvre, Paris, 75001, France;48.8587333;2.3422408;32;true;false;Japanese;What might one expect from a Japanese restaurant featuring an all-star line-up of chef Takuya Watanabe (previously at Jin) and Arnaud Donckele and his pastry chef partner Maxime Frédéric? Nothing but the best, of course! Takuya Watanabe belongs to the inner circle of the capital's grand masters, channelling all his passion and expertise into his sushi, shaping each and every piece to perfection in view of diners. For his part, Arnaud Donckele brings to the table his talent for sauces, jus and broths, in creations such as shellfish dashi, sweet garlic purée and green shiso coulis, or the clear and potent accompaniment to the ramen. A rarity in Japanese restaurants, dessert is a must here, masterfully orchestrated by Plénitude's pastry chef. The decor and service, just like the meal, elevate the silence and purity of the materials used.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11715;Adami;France;Paris;19 bis rue Pierre-Fontaine, Paris, 75009, France;48.8815609;2.3341354;67;true;true;Italian;This small Italian pasta restaurant breaks away from traditional trattoria fare, embracing a more contemporary approach – an inspired idea reflected in the sleek, modern decor and the long counter from which diners watch the kitchen team at work. Dishes to share and a warm, convivial atmosphere are all part of the experience here. The Italian chef, who has an impressive track record, delivers fresh cuisine that abounds in bold flavours. A case in point is his vitello tonnato-style veal, artichoke and black garlic, or his incredibly indulgent ricotta gnocchi in a creamy courgette sauce. The lunch menu is appealing, as are the mouthwatering à la carte options.;Counter dining;[]
11716;Le 21;France;Pornic;21 rue de la Plage-de-la-Birochère, Pornic, 44210, France;47.1053547;-2.0916328;80;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Although a little out of the way, this restaurant enjoys an enviable location overlooking Plage de la Birochère, whose sandy cove surrounded by rocks is visible from the restaurant. Chef Sylvain Belouin and oenologist and sommelier Valérie Belouin are the brilliant couple behind this Pornic institution. The experienced chef (for a decade, Sylvain headed up the kitchens at Le Pigeon Blanc in Vern-d'Anjou, where his efforts were crowned with a Bib Gourmand) certainly knows his stuff. His simple way of treating guests to dishes centred on local ingredients, meat (pigeon, pig) and fish, eg his beautifully crispy sole meunière, is testament to this. The wine list features 500 wines (mainly biodynamic). Laid-back and friendly service.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11717;Le Charlie;France;Porticcio;Bella Vista Hôtel, Porticcio, 20166, France;41.8950702;8.8105225;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine;After many years as a MICHELIN-starred chef in his restaurant near Poitiers, Richard Toix has found in the heights of Porticcio an ideal setting for his delicate, flavoursome cuisine. With a sure hand and impeccable taste, he delivers cosmopolitan cuisine, blending influences from Corsica and the French mainland, as well as from stints in Asia, which have nourished his imagination and his palette. His cuisine is particularly attuned to flavours, a case in point being the apricot, tomato, anchovy starter, or the delicious dessert of honey and Brocciu cheese, an ode to the "Island of Beauty". The terrace commands a superb view of the Gulf of Ajaccio and the Îles Sanguinaires.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11718;L'Auberge de la Vallée;France;Nassandres-sur-Risle;7 route de Brionne, Nassandres-sur-Risle, 27300, France;49.1470662;0.7318733;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This charming half-timbered house set in a bucolic location is extremely pleasant. In this setting you can tuck into simple, seasonal cuisine concocted with the finest ingredients, such as a charlotte of andouille sausage with cabbage.;Terrace;[]
11719;Amicis;France;Bordeaux;19 rue Mably, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8436643;-0.5772326;72;true;true;Creative;In the chic part of Bordeaux, between the Allées de Tourny and the Place des Grands-Hommes, chef Alexandre Baumard (previously at Logis de la Cadène in Saint-Émilion and L'Observatoire du Gabriel) has set up this elegant two-storey restaurant. Served in the form of a tasting menu (at dinnertime only), the refined and clear cuisine showcases quality ingredients – not least fish and seafood – that are precisely and creatively prepared, eg delicately cooked prawn placed on a flavoursome reduction of the heads and dressed with a shell bisque vinaigrette. Damien Amilien's desserts, as delicious as they are technical, continue in this subtle vein – with the likes of his cooked and raw cherries with fresh herbs. The food goes into a more accessible bistronomy mode at lunchtime. Attentive service and a terrific wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11722;Mareluna;France;Théoule-sur-Mer;55 avenue de Lérins, Théoule-sur-Mer, 06590, France;43.5080143;6.9395889;64;true;true;Creative;This former 17C soap factory is now a luxury hotel with a superb terrace affording panoramic views over the Bay of Cannes, Théoule-sur-Mer, Cap d'Antibes and the Îles de Lérins. Decorated in the Mediterranean style with rattan furniture, its elegant fine dining restaurant is open for dinner only. Having trained at Le Meurice Alain Ducasse restaurant and with Ryuji Teshima at Pages, Italian chef Francesco Fezza cooks up a number of Italian and local ingredients with spirit and creativity. This modern cuisine may be unabashedly Mediterranean, but the recipes are enhanced by little Asian touches: asparagus yuzukosho with ikejime-killed matured yellowtail or Thai consommé with osso buco pasta.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11723;Erroa;France;Saint-Jean-de-Luz;32 boulevard Thiers, Saint-Jean-de-Luz, 64500, France;43.3916752;-1.6593074;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Coupled with his Basque heritage (erroa means "root"), chef Mathieu Moity has honed his skills in the restaurants of Michel Bras, Iñaki Aizpitarte and René Redzepi. Now he has set up shop in Paris, in a hybrid space comprising a bar area serving tapas and a restaurant in which to take your pick from the concise menu. With their judicious flavour combinations, his generously portioned dishes will bring a smile to your face – think flame-smoked mackerel, Chartreuse-infused fennel, smoked dashi gel, leek and rhubarb. The chef's American partner heads up the relaxed front-of-house team.;Terrace;[]
11725;Masama;France;Saumur;5 place de la Bilange, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2606375;-0.0774073;35;true;true;Fusion;Experience a slice of South America behind this resplendent pistachio-green shopfront in the heart of Saumur. Colombian chef Marlon Medina made headlines in the local press when he coached his country's team for the Bocuse d'Or cooking contest in 2023. His cuisine may be multicultural, but it nevertheless shows clear South American leanings, which are sometimes allied with local ingredients (such as asparagus or mushrooms). For dinner, by means of a short and to-the-point menu, the chef proposes indulgent dishes such as an excellent picanha accompanied by an impeccable chimichurri condiment. Another signature dish is the ceviche, made with fish from the market. At lunchtime, there's a more typically French single set menu without options.;;[]
11726;Chengdu Restaurant;China Mainland;Chengdu;2F, North Building, Shangshan International, No. 46-1, Section 4, Renmin South Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.618011;104.064047;92;false;true;Cantonese, Sichuan;The hanging lamps are a nod to the Golden Sun Bird, an ancient artefact unearthed in Chengdu, while the back-lit, perforated brass wall is evocative of basket weaving. The head chef from Guangdong built the menu on traditional Cantonese lines, spicing it up with Sichuanese touches and deftly incorporating produce from all over the world. Some seafood dishes require pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11727;Silver Cottage;China Mainland;Chengdu;Luke Island, Section 1, South Tianfu Avenue, Shuangliu, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.458252;104.065353;19;false;false;Sichuan;From its lake-side location and lush garden, to private rooms with spaces for chess playing, flower watching and incense burning, every nook and cranny of Silver Cottage exudes an elegant aura à la Song Dynasty. The menu features Sichuan classics, like the painstakingly prepared dish snowflake minced chicken, all prepared with the freshest produce. Diners must book a private room and live Chinese zither recitals make the experience unforgettable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11728;Pairedd;China Mainland;Chengdu;Shop 703, 7F, UFun, 300 Jiaozi Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.585596;104.055164;86;true;true;European Contemporary;With only 12 counter seats framing the open kitchen, Pairedd offers an intimate dining experience and close interaction with the young chefs. As its name suggests, wine is at the core of its brand DNA and the set 10-course tasting menu is designed to complement the seven-glass wine flight. Dishes change with the seasons, but meat and seafood form the backbone of the menu: expect Fujian seafood in summer and local produce from Sichuan in winter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11730;Member;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 26, 100 Qinglongzheng Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.647509;104.086381;52;true;false;Noodles;Open only from 10am to 2pm, this neighbourhood joint on a quiet street is inspired by the 1980s with ceiling fans, a mint green fridge, wooden benches and other knick-knacks that open the floodgates of nostalgia. Similarly, the concise menu stars old-time local favourites, such as steamed rice dressed in lard and spiced soy. String bean noodles are another must-try – al dente noodles tossed in a spicy sauce, topped with ground pork and string beans.;Cash only;[]
11731;Xiang Shang Xiang;China Mainland;Chengdu;E2003, 2F, East Pavilion, SKP, 2001 North Section of Tianfu Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5714635;104.0683597;21;false;false;Hunanese;The Hunanese brand manager and kitchen team strive to re-create specialities from their home province as authentically as possible. The must-try fish head steamed with five different chillies flown in from Hunan mesmerises with a complex depth of spiciness, remarkable umami and punchy tartness. The 18-second stir-fried Xiangxi yellow beef uses the clod cut, rife with meaty flavour, in conjunction with chillies and aromatics for a real kick.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11732;Brustin;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 301, 3F, Building 21, Art Park, No.111, Section 1, North Third Ring Road, Jinniu, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.717554;104.031173;84;true;true;Innovative;Chefs Bruce and his partner Justin opened Brustin in 2023 in a design-forward space in line with the artistic flair of the Tianfu Art Park complex that houses it. The dinner prix-fixes have 12 to 15 courses, re-interpreting Sichuan cuisine with Western techniques and an emphasis on seasonality. Diners can take home the paper menu, which features illustrations by local artists. Exquisite food is matched by the professional service of the servers and sommelier.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11734;Co-;China Mainland;Chengdu;XZ32-1-19, Eastern Suburb Memory Music Park, 4 South Jianshe Road, Chenghua, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6710899;104.1220589;69;true;false;Innovative;Informed by the chef's extensive travel and gastronomic experiences, the multicourse tasting menu features novel creations with seasonal ingredients. Quality produce from all over China is prepared deftly using modern techniques. For instance, the game bird egret duck is marinated in Cantonese seasoning and dry-aged for a week, then chargrilled to perfection for crispy skin and juicy flesh. There are only five tables, so booking is a must.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
11735;Long Sen Yuan (Qingyang);China Mainland;Chengdu;60 Qintai Road, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.661221;104.042962;96;true;false;Hotpot;For over 20 years, this no-frills restaurant has had just one thing on the menu – authentic Chengdu hotpot. But diners won’t get bored because of the 18 soup bases and the stunning variety of dipping sauces, meat, offal, and sea and river fish on offer. Lamb is the preferred soup base available in winter, while the signature red spiced oil base and tomato base are also popular. Beef lovers should try cuts like aorta, tenderloin and leaf tripe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
11737;Chuanpu;China Mainland;Chengdu;1F, Huangcheng Jewelry Exchange Center, 39-1 Lihua Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6568657;104.0652355;76;false;true;Fujian;The entrance may be rather obscure, but it is well worth seeking out Chuanpu for its authentic Fujian cooking. There is no menu – take your pick from the live fish tank near the kitchen. Eel, whelks and razor clams are among the most popular choices. Servers recommend having the eel steamed in black bean sauce to accentuate its fattiness. Other Fujian specialities such as layered pork intestine, and lor mee also live up to their reputation.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11738;Nan's Gourmet;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 101, Block B, UPARK+, 666 Fuhua North Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5576344;104.0372497;84;false;false;Cantonese;In 2021, the Hongkong owner opened Nan’s Gourmet at this dining hub. In the F&B business for over 40 years, he convened a kitchen team of mostly Guangdong natives to capture the essence of Cantonese cooking. The menu features classics like dim sum, Cantonese barbecues, double-boiled soups and sizzling claypot dishes. Try the steamed pork patty with sweet dried cabbage – the springy half-fatty pork in a briny-sweet seasoning is simply addictive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
11739;Tivano;China Mainland;Chengdu;B1 Level, The Temple House, 81 Bitieshi Street, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.65409;104.081971;47;false;false;Italian;With a floor-to-ceiling wine wall as the centrepiece, the room is elegantly furnished but without feeling too formal. Diners’ eyes are also drawn to the glitzy bar by the entrance and the semi-open kitchen where pizzas are baked and food is prepared. Apart from the traditional Italian varieties, pizzas also come in Sichaunese twists and in smaller portions. House-made pasta dishes are not to be missed. Round out the meal with torrone semifreddo.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11742;The River House;China Mainland;Chengdu;21F, Minshan Hotel, No. 55, Section 2, Renmin South Road, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.651129;104.06408;44;true;true;European;Knockout nightscapes, romantic live music and thoughtful touches make this restaurant a popular spot for marriage proposals. The food is classic European, but features unmistakably local ingredients. The velvety steamed wild-caught yellow croaker is steeped in a rich fish stock seasoned with Puning bean sauce. Also try the peach iron Buddha tea sorbet for a floral-fruity treat. In addition to the á la carte selection, the set menus offer great value.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
11743;Sichuan Folk (Wuhou);China Mainland;Chengdu;2-3F, 63 Shenxianshu South Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.609531;104.04755;54;true;false;Sichuan;The entrance, which is framed by two memorial arches with a pond in its centre, leads into a traditionally appointed dining room. It stages a show of Sichuan ‘face changing’ opera every evening at 7pm for a cultural-culinary experience. The menu is mostly Sichuanese, with an emphasis on Chongqing snacks and nibbles. Try stewed yellowhead catfish in peppery stock with scallion which is silky and flavoursome. Portions are big enough for sharing, so bring your mates!;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
11744;Cloud Arise (Chenghua);China Mainland;Chengdu;3-4F, Building Raidy Boer, 222 Shanbanqiao Road, Chenghua, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6667;104.0667;21;true;true;Sichuan;Although there are only six tables in the main dining room, there are private rooms with solariums, balconies and tea brewing rooms spread over two floors. A stylish, peaceful vibe reigns throughout the spacious, comfortable interior. The kitchen team crafts a menu of traditional Sichuanese fare such as fuqi feipian – sliced beef brisket and tripe in Sichuan pepper sauce. Their signature spicy pork belly, slow-cooked in an earthen jar over a wood fire, is rich and flavoursome.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11746;Xue Tao · In the Yard;China Mainland;Chengdu;Xingfu West Road, Xingfu Mei Lin, Sanshengxiang, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.589531;104.126535;59;true;false;Sichuan;Named after a poet from the Tang Dynasty, this branch of the chain opened in 2018 in a scenic area famous for its flowering plum trees. Two rustically styled buildings are connected by lush greenery. The menu features Sichuan home cooking and river fish, such as yellowhead catfish prepared in a myriad of ways. But most diners prefer it simmered in a spicy, tangy broth perfumed with green Sichuan pepper and Chinese patchouli. Reservations recommended at weekends.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
11747;The Bridge;China Mainland;Chengdu;66 Binjiang East Road, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.644532;104.083533;15;false;true;Sichuan;Perched on Anshun Bridge that Marco Polo wrote about in the 13th Century, The Bridge is celebrity chef André Chiang’s debut dining concept in mainland China. The food reveals his modern take on Sichuan cooking, delivering refined touches and mindful plating. Marble goby in stone pot, and almond tofu dessert are the highlights. The pickle trolley presents over 10 choices for diners to choose from, including cherry belle radish, bitter melon and lotus shoot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11748;New Peking Cuisine;China Mainland;Chengdu;Shop 328-329, 3F, Yintai IN 99, 1199 North Section of Tianfu Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5874831;104.0671055;29;false;true;Beijing Cuisine;The brand is created by a kitchen team from Beijing aims to re-create royal recipes and street food with modern techniques. Some dishes are tweaked to cater to the Sichuanese palate. Try their low-fat Peking duck that is grilled twice to drain excessive fat, yet remarkably, the flesh remains juicy and tender. The Beijingese sugar fritter is fluffy and golden, and a surprising drizzle of balsamic vinegar cuts the richness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11749;Datenbank;China Mainland;Chengdu;28 East Zijing Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6149774;104.0539851;67;true;true;Innovative;Its name conjures up images of rows of servers with flickering lights, but the room is designed like a cavern with raw, handmade stoneware to match. The “data” here refers to the deconstruction and re-assembly of taste memories for an original experience. It opens for dinner only with one set menu that blends the heat in Sichuanese and Mexican food seamlessly to a surprisingly good effect. Also try the house-brewed kombucha in seasonal flavours.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
11750;Nantang Wang;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 301-303, 3F, Chinese Financial Center, 33 Jiaozi Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5836826;104.060726;27;true;true;Sichuan;Established in the Chinese Financial Centre, this stylish restaurant aptly sports a textured wall inspired by Jiaozi, the first paper money in Chinese history unearthed in Chengdu. A pre-dinner carbonated Sichuan pepper drink teases the palate, before the novel Sichuan menu unfolds with refined dishes, some of which in individual portions. The rice paddy eel with chillies tastes fatty and authentic, while liangfen noodles dressed in a spicy sauce whet the appetite.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11751;Nan Tang (Tianshun Road);China Mainland;Chengdu;2F, North Tower, Interaxx Plaza, 151 Tianshun Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.59555;104.068276;40;false;true;Sichuan;This cultural dining concept spreads across several elegant rooms dotted with pierced carvings and calligraphy reliefs. The Chinese stacking food box motif symbolises culinary heritage. Various ingredients are prepared in traditional Sichuanese ways to great effect, examples being the crispy-skinned pigeon enhanced by Sichuan pepper, or the velvety fish tofu shaped like a crescent moon, with a veil of bamboo fungus and covered in a consommé.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
11752;Art Yinba;China Mainland;Chengdu;Building 1, Luxetown, No.18, Section 2, Lushan Avenue, Shuangliu, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.487019;104.086201;89;true;false;Sichuan;Since graduating from culinary school, the owner-chef always wanted to open a one-of-a-kind establishment like this. The room is furnished in a rustic country style and is divided into zones, while food-related artefacts add interest to the experience. Traditional Sichuanese flavours are re-invented with Western techniques, witty word play and arty presentations. Standouts include fish head with artisan gluten noodles in a golden pea soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
11753;Tan Jia;China Mainland;Chengdu;70-1 Yulin South Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6259265;104.0551056;56;true;false;Small eats;If you fancy authentic Chengdu small plates, this tiny, no-frills shop is just the place. Regulars can't get enough of the rabbit head and duck head in mala marinade, but the less adventurous can fix their cravings with items such as pork trotter soup, chicken soup rice, and assorted cold skewers (eg chicken, beef tripe, celtuce) steeped in a flavourful stock generously seasoned with chilli oil and Sichuan pepper.;Cash only;[]
11754;Chaimen Gong Guan;China Mainland;Chengdu;10 Tongzilin East Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.61714;104.060279;36;false;true;Sichuan;In 2012, this restaurant opened its doors on a main drag teeming with dining options. In the modern space, the four-person booths are the tables of choice. The predominantly Sichuanese menu features an array of sea and freshwater fish, such as spicy and sour braised marble goby with pickled string beans and radish. Plump for the starter of seared beef strips with dried tangerine peel – a mild, sweet aftertaste balances the heat of chilli and red oil.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
11755;Rongle Garden;China Mainland;Chengdu;29 Wenshuyuan Street, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.6763762;104.0704511;34;true;true;Sichuan;Right next to Wenshu Yuan Monastery, this restaurant with almost 200 years of history is especially popular among tourists. Diners can see the manicured garden from most tables. On the menu, you can find almost all Sichuanese classics, alongside some refined creations. Try their braised swamp eel with Korean mint and pickled chillies for a combination of sour, sweet, salty and umami flavours. Sichuan pepper free-range chicken is silky and juicy.;;[]
11756;Yanyu;China Mainland;Chengdu;E2005, 2F, East Pavilion, SKP, 2001 North Section of Tianfu Avenue, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5729482;104.068305;64;true;false;Fujian;This restaurant in an upmarket shopping mall serves an array of Fujian dishes with a Sichuanese twist. Most produce and seafood is shipped from Fujian, including squid from Zhangzhou, which is cooked in typical Sichuanese shuizhu style. The nourishing soup "Buddha jumps over the wall" is made with gourmet dried seafood for briny-sweet richness. For dessert, panna cotta with dai hong pao oolong tea melds velvety texture with floral earthiness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11757;Shu Mansion;China Mainland;Chengdu;No. 301-304, 3F, Building 7, Tiexiang Temple Riverfront, 116 Shenghua North Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.5588575;104.050141;86;false;true;Sichuan;The modern room boasts a water screen that veils the lush green exterior. The glazed showcase housing gourmet dried seafood like fish maw and sea cucumber is also eye-catching. Of course, wine buffs won’t miss the glass wine cellar boasting a fine collection. Polished Sichuanese defines the menu, with a fondness for seafood. Try the twice-cooked eel that boasts fatty meat, while chillies, garlic leaves and black beans impart deep flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11758;#8;China Mainland;Chengdu;16F, Grand Hyatt Hotel, 8 South Chunxi Road, Jinjiang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.656425;104.074246;18;true;true;Hotpot;You can find almost any seafood, mushrooms, meats and leafy greens at this hotpot restaurant but it's the crispy textured hand-torn beef tripe and the yellowhead catfish with fine silky meat that deserve tip billing. Each diner has their own mini hotpot and chooses from eight different soup bases – try the old Chengdu-style mala butter base. The snacks such as golden pork strips or ice jelly in fruit syrup are also a delight.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11760;Wu Yue Gong;China Mainland;Chengdu;Inside CD Courtyard, 28 Wuyuegong Street, Qingyang, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.676454;104.071681;60;false;false;Chinese Contemporary;Inside a historic courtyard house-turned hotel, this private dining concept opened its doors in 2018. It only accepts reservations for parties of 2 to 10 diners and menus are tailor-made according to guests’ preferences. Novel Sichuanese fusion dishes are underpinned by solid skills and exquisite plating, complemented by Cantonese, Guanfu, Huaiyang and even Western items. Try kung pao prawns and chargrilled beef ribs in black pepper sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
11761;Hidden Place;China Mainland;Chengdu;1F, Hidden Place Hotel, 57 Shengxing Road, Wuhou, Chengdu, China Mainland;30.564121;104.048377;96;false;true;Sichuan;Once a protégé of the Sichuan culinary master, the young owner chose to open her first venture in a secluded, serene hotel. She aims to re-create ancient Sichuan recipes, using precise techniques and premium ingredients from around the world. Braised mandarin fish topped with chillies boasts tender flesh in an aromatic, spicy sauce. Guaiwei chicken is dressed in a blend of over 20 condiments for layered, complex flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11763;Albatross Death Cult;United Kingdom;Birmingham;Newhall Square, Jewellery Quarter, Birmingham, B3 1RU, United Kingdom;52.4829409;-1.9070853;23;false;true;Seafood;It is key, when structuring your restaurant around a kitchen counter, that you provide an engaging, relaxing experience for your guests. This is something that is perfectly understood by the team at this eye-catchingly named restaurant, inspired by the albatross in Coleridge's 'The Rime of the Ancient Mariner'. Everyone, from the chefs to the sommelier, is full of enthusiasm and confidently chats away with diners throughout the experience. The food itself carries a heavy Japanese influence, with the tasting menu consisting almost entirely of pared-back preparations spotlighting top-notch seafood, with plenty of raw and cured dishes among them.;Counter dining;[]
11764;Julie's;United Kingdom;London;135 Portland Road, Holland Park, London, W11 4LW, United Kingdom;51.5101581;-0.2105141;52;true;false;Modern British;Judging by the amount of diners flooding through its doors, the residents of Notting Hill are glad to have this bright bistro de-luxe among their roster of neighbourhood haunts. Inside, it’s an eye-catching place with rich, warming colours and booths that are perfect for date night. The menu offers an appealing range of dishes, from the light (chopped salad of the day) to the luxurious (lobster soufflé). The extensive wine list and cocktails from the trolley will ensure you’re well-refreshed, while the service team are friendly and engaging.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
11765;The Coach House;Ireland;Roundwood;Main Street, Roundwood, A98 P635, Ireland;53.06445;-6.2245459;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A complete top-to-toe refurbishment has left this former Victorian coaching inn looking fabulous, with an aesthetic that could be best described as shabby-chic meets Irish country house. The front bar has been retained, making this still feel very much like a pub, while the large, airy dining room provides a great setting for dishes that come free of gimmicks or over-elaboration, instead showing off the natural flavours of the produce, such as quality cod from the Irish Sea. There is a welcome originality too, as when offering beef cheeks in a bun instead of the classic pub burger.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11766;Volta Do Mar;United Kingdom;London;100 Draycott Avenue, Chelsea, London, SW3 3AD, United Kingdom;51.4934879;-0.1674032;19;true;true;Portuguese, Classic Cuisine;Volta Do Mar may have relocated to a new premises, but as the team here will tell you, its soul is very much unchanged. The cooking remains a tribute to the cuisine not just of Portugal, but of the countries it established trade routes with centuries ago, hence the restaurant's name meaning 'to return from the sea'. So expect to find Goan curry sitting alongside piri piri chicken from Mozambique, as well as dishes from Brazil and Macau. The intimate room is decorated with colourful modern artwork, mirroring the vibrancy of the cooking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11767;Roe;United Kingdom;London;5 Park Drive, Canary Wharf, London, E14 9GG, United Kingdom;51.5025121;-0.0147162;70;false;false;Modern British;Launched by the team behind Fallow, this vast restaurant can house up to 500 diners in the heart of Canary Wharf, all while being run with impressive slickness. Guests are spread across several dining rooms, some with counter seating, plus a lovely wrap-around terrace that boasts commanding views of South Dock. The wide-ranging menu offers something for everyone, including playful takes on British classics like maitake Cornish pasty or market fish served with parsley liquor, that's reminiscent of an East End pie and mash.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11768;Camille;United Kingdom;London;2-3 Stoney Street, Borough Market, Southwark, London, SE1 9AA, United Kingdom;51.5049892;-0.0908046;74;true;true;French;Situated at the entrance to the foodie wonderland that is Borough Market, this intimate French bistro is rooted in an ethos of unpretentious, pared-back cooking that perfectly suits its rustic interior design. The blackboard-written menu is regularly changing, and you can expect straightforward yet eminently satisfying dishes like pâté-en-croûte or whole mackerel with café de Paris butter. A friendly welcome and cheery service ensure you’ll be dining with a smile on your face.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11769;daróg;Ireland;Galway;56 Lower Dominick Street, Galway, H91 K225, Ireland;53.271021;-9.0569245;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s a huge amount of passion channelled into this welcoming little wine bar. Hungarian-born Zsolt Lukács has an infectious enthusiasm for wine, which comes across in his carefully curated list that gravitates towards small artisan producers using organic and biodynamic methods. Accompanying the wine is a selection of sharing plates – like kingfish crudo – that are exactingly executed, deliver on flavour and provide brilliant value for money. The regularly changing artwork from local artists is on sale and is curated by co-owner Edel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
11770;Bistro Air du Temps;Belgium;Liernu;Rue de la Croix Monet 2, Liernu, 5310, Belgium;50.5926188;4.8345491;94;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;The square farmstead, in which chef Sang Hoon Degeimbre works his magic in the kitchen of the high-flying L’Air du Temps (evenings only), is also home to a country chic bistro (open for lunch only). Meals are served beneath a canopy of greenery or alfresco in fine weather. Chef Denis has adapted the house DNA into bistro recipes. The result is a cornucopia of bold associations and an abundance of veggies, Asian influences and innovative techniques. For example, the chef may pair pork belly with a frothy espuma of potatoes and coffee, salty caviar and spinach leaves with a subtle olive vinaigrette. Ideal for a bistro meal with a difference!;Car park,Terrace;[]
11771;Cella;Belgium;Antwerpen;Kattendijkdok-Oostkaai 21b, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2335861;4.4086773;23;false;false;French Contemporary, International;One half of the restaurant commands a view of the kitchen team crafting all sorts delicacies, while the other overlooks the Antwerp docks and skyline. There is never a dull moment at Cella, starting with the industrial cachet of this stylishly repurposed warehouse by the team that used to run Het Pomphuis. The menu features a tempting lineup of pedigree Belgian fare with matured meat grilled over charcoal embers, fresh fries and a last-minute sauce, together with a smattering of ubiquitous international dishes of the likes of ceviche and sushi. Flawless technique and aromatic sauces are the hallmark of the gifted chef.;Great view,Terrace;[]
11772;'t Gasthuis by InstroomArt;Belgium;Mechelen;Keizerstraat 7, Mechelen, 2800, Belgium;51.0291561;4.48683;39;true;true;Farm to table, International;Seppe Nobels, Charuwan Pauwels and Nico Dockx make no bones about the fact that they source the majority of their produce from sustainable farms in the Mechelen region, in line with an ethos that naturally encompasses their HR policy. The result is international cuisine by a youthful generation of Europeans, keen to tell their story at your table. Examples of dishes you may sample include a Ukrainian borscht of red beetroot or al dente asparagus with Palestinian moussaka made with mushrooms and sumac with a lemon thyme mousse and parsley root fries. The stories are fascinating, as is the artwork that adorns the different areas of this former inn. This restaurant demonstrates that there is more to a sustainable future than just ingredients.;;[]
11773;Compagnique;Belgium;Lovendegem;Vellare 93, Lovendegem, 9920, Belgium;51.099486;3.5962814;54;false;false;Modern French;Ideal for a romantic date night, this charming farmstead is the quintessence of poised and intimate and only offers tables for two (but there is a private room that caters to groups). Working hand in hand, Angélique manages the front-of-house while Tim runs the kitchen, in a bid to provide a personalised experience. Luxury ingredients enjoy the leading role on the menu and the chef might sign a high-flying combination of oysters and seaweed, caviar and a distinctive beurre blanc made out of curds. He has a soft spot for fresh, tangy notes, illustrated by the subtle sauce vierge that contrasts so wonderfully with the mild yet sweet flesh of turbot. A mouthwatering prospect…;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11774;Jean-Philippe;Belgium;Ingelmunster;Bruggestraat 97, Ingelmunster, 8770, Belgium;50.9253269;3.253624;82;true;false;Modern French;Jean-Philippe and Sara-Sofia have crafted a cosy cocoon in this townhouse. Artwork by Isidoor Goddeeris underscores the restaurant’s classy interior and reflects the chef’s love of seafood. The couple’s experience shines through in every detail. Sara-Sofia seamlessly manages the front of house, while presenting her latest cocktails. Jean-Philippe draws on his flawless technical background as he works with outstanding ingredients. Examples include wild seabass, grilled to keep the skin crispy and flanked by different textures of fennel, a baby artichoke and characterful crab bisque. This consummate chef, a master of delicacy, has a way with flavour and gutsy sauces that is second to none.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11775;Sardis;Belgium;Brasschaat;Kapelsesteenweg 406, Brasschaat, 2930, Belgium;51.2935072;4.4432924;73;true;true;Italian;Tiziano Cappai welcomes diners warmly into this stylish red-brick terraced house, which boasts a cosy interior, sensual artwork on the walls and a blissfully peaceful patio at the rear. Chef Eveline Cappai deftly updates a pure-bred lineup of Italian classics. For example, she might pair bigoli pasta with a subtle stock, to which she adds white wine, parsley, savoury vongole and a hint of umami thanks to kombu. The tiramisu manages to underscore authentic flavours with an amusing new spin thanks to a play on textures. Attention to detail is the watchword here.;Terrace;[]
11776;Qin;Belgium;Antwerpen;De Keyserlei 66, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.2171424;4.419496;44;false;true;Cantonese, Chinese Contemporary;Emperor Qin provided the inspiration for the team at the helm of the restaurant of Hotel Keiser, hence the dark wood furnishings, soft red fabrics and oriental details like Chinese lanterns and paintings. The Cantonese culinary lineup is the quintessence of authentic, albeit subtly updated to suit today’s palates. The varied range of home-made dim sum dishes are characteristic of this ethos. Stuffed with chopped wagyu beef and a black pepper Chinese sauce, or with ginger and taro - piping hot delicacies that embody the generous character of this aromatic cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
11777;Flamme;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;Rue de Roumanie 56, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8271697;4.3497763;56;false;false;Country cooking;Flames and fire are central to this buzzy gourmet bistro. Entirely open, the kitchen provides a fascinating insight into how the food is smoked, roasted and grilled. The menu may be concise, but making your choice remains a challenge. Veggies take the star role in big-boned recipes. Slices of celeriac are roasted like shawarma, rubbed with pitta spices and flanked by a garlic sauce. Or would you prefer pleurote mushrooms cooked over the open fire with a tempura of enoki mushrooms and marinated vegetables? You can trust the wine tips of the smiling, spontaneous lady of the house with your eyes closed.;;[]
11778;Nova;Belgium;Sint-Niklaas;Collegestraat 11, Sint-Niklaas, 9100, Belgium;51.1659099;4.1401549;55;true;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;Tineke and Guy have left their stamp on this stylish townhouse steeped in serenity and tucked away in a working-class district near the Grand Place. We warrant that Tineke’s natural charm and Guy’s creative way with seasonal produce will win you over. Take a seat at the counter or at a table with a view of the chef and get ready to be bowled over by the surprise (or à la carte) menu, depending on availability. The chef works closely with local producers and rolls out an ethical zero waste farm-to-table concept. While barbecue flavours take the limelight in his culinary score, he might also make a ‘loaf’ out of old bread and a bisque of shrimp heads, jazzed up with fennel and a cream of veggies, or just with brown shrimp and wild fennel. Most definitely a restaurant with a soul.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11779;De la terre à l'assiette;Belgium;Arlon;Rue de la Poste 13, Arlon, 6700, Belgium;49.6827457;5.8145558;80;true;true;Modern French;Magali and Guillaume Lempens’ colourful venue is the quintessence of comfortable and steeped in feelgood vibes, a large proportion of which are courtesy of their bistronomic cuisine. The latter includes fried cod flanked by a subtle bouillabaisse, white asparagus, homemade gnocchi and a knockout aioli mayonnaise. Big-boned, punchy sauces and impeccable technique bear witness to the experience of seasoned chef Guillaume. Rather than fussy frills, you can expect wholehearted authenticity and no-nonsense rustic fare.;;[]
11780;Yakitori Kiyu;South Korea;Seoul;31 Dohwa 4-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04169, South Korea;37.54059;126.95149;15;true;false;Yakitori;The chefs’ busy hands deftly grill the chicken as the enticing aroma of Korean tojongdak chicken yakitori fills the entire space. The experienced chefs who grill each cut of tojongdak to perfection add extra charm to each dish. The restaurant uses chickens that are naturally raised on various medicinal herbs so diners can experience healthy, quality cuts of chicken. The menu features unlaid chicken eggs, or chochin, (which means lantern in Japanese), that can only be obtained when an egg-laying hen is slaughtered, highlighting the freshness of the ingredients. Kiyu's goal is to study the attributes of tojongdak to take the flavors of yakitori to the next level, is the place to enjoy delicious yakitori.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11781;ALT.a;South Korea;Seoul;109 Bogwang-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04391, South Korea;37.53245;126.99446;48;false;true;Vegan, Chinese;This is a Korean-Chinese restaurant that uses all plant-based ingredients including plant-based alternative meats. That’s right. It’s a vegan Chinese restaurant. Chinese food made without any meat piqued my curiosity. They create incredible flavors that are sure to entice even diners who aren’t familiar with vegan food. The food is also low-fat so it’s easy on the stomach. They serve vegan jjamppong and fried dishes like tangsuyuk and yurinyuk that are so delightfully bouncy and chewy that no one will notice that they aren’t made from real meat. It is both a great vegan and a great Chinese restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
11782;Okdol Heyonok;South Korea;Seoul;26-1 Ogeum-ro  36-gil, Songpa-gu, Seoul, 05700, South Korea;37.50153;127.12408;77;false;true;Naengmyeon;Taste the deeply savory broth and the nutty flavor of the noodles made from 100% buckwheat that intensifies the more you chew at Okdol Hyeonok. The restaurant is fairly new, but it has gained a solid following among Pyongyang naengmyeon connoisseurs. Some of their most popular dishes are mandu with a nuttiness that comes from plenty of tofu in the filling, eobok jaengban, and gajami shikhye. You can also have your favorite wine with your meal for a corkage fee. Enjoy the mild flavors with incredible depth.;Air conditioning;[]
11783;RMW Carne;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 12 Daesagwan-ro 5-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04400, South Korea;37.53483;127.00085;27;false;true;Barbecue;RMW Carne, which is located on the second floor of a renovated old house, isn’t particularly spacious, but you can enjoy your food in a comfortably petite, cozy venue. The restaurant which is named after the first letters of steak doneness - rare, medium, and well-done - dry ages various cuts of beef of a variety of different cattle breeds. Salami, chorizo, pastrami, sausages and other charcuterie, all cured in-house, are available for purchase at the store inside the restaurant. They also serve simpler dishes like grilled vegetables and pasta that can be enjoyed as a light meal or refreshment.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11784;Neungdong Minari;South Korea;Seoul;28 Hangang-daero 40-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04386, South Korea;37.53008;126.97078;51;true;false;Gomtang;The gomtang at Neungdong Minari is topped with a pile of minari so tall that at a glance, it doesn’t look like a tang at all. The clear, clean broth is made from fresh hanwoo beef that was slaughtered on the day, which is topped with piquant minari that was grown in clear freshwater for added freshness. You should expect a wait, but you will think it is well worth it once you take your first bite.;Air conditioning;[]
11785;Manao;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 18 Hannam-daero 21-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04401, South Korea;37.53411;127.00613;29;true;true;Thai;Enter Manao, and you will be greeted with exotic vibes bolstered by seek décor and an array of art objects brought directly from Thailand. Its prix-fixe menus consist of multiple dishes in small portions, allowing guests to enjoy a variety of plates in one meal. The kitchen does an excellent job of presenting authentic Thai cuisine with its characteristic spiciness. Another appeal of this spot is that the meat and seafood are grilled to order over charcoal. Manao means “lime” in Thai, and its fare is as refreshing as its name.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
11786;Kirameki;South Korea;Seoul;18 Dosan-daero 28-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06040, South Korea;37.51808;127.02822;97;true;true;Japanese;Kirameki is a Japanese restaurant that serves a tasting menu centered on rice. I expected rice to be the primary focus of the meal, but after experiencing the meal, but it consisted as a wide array of dishes. The menu is designed around the Japanese washoku, and showcases kaiseki cuisine prepared with seasonal ingredients. Once the ceramic pot rice is served, small morsels of food were served over scoops of aromatic white rice. Each savory bite lingered pleasantly on the palate.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
11787;Gomtang Lab;South Korea;Seoul;153 Dosan-daero, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06037, South Korea;37.51883;127.02521;65;true;true;Gomtang;True to its name, Gomtang Lab is dedicated to studying gomtang (beef bone soup) and developing diverse new recipes. Chef Yim Jung-sik has relentlessly pursued this culinary journey since the days when he helmed Pyeonghwaok. His signature dish is collagen beef bone soup, made by simmering beef leg bones, tendons, feet and oxtail for more than 10 hours until thick. Once you finish the bowl brimming with chewy, tender meat and savory broth that make a perfect meal, you’ll find your lips sticky with gelatinous collagen. To cater to different tastes, the menu offers several variations of gomtang, including a clear, meat-only version and a spicy version with added beef tripe. One last note: The signature soup is limited to only 20 bowls per day, so be sure to visit when the eatery opens.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11789;Aleisha;Taiwan;Taipei;16, Alley 4, Lane 217, Section 3, Zhongxiao East Road, Da’an District, Taipei, 106080, Taiwan;25.0427734;121.540615;26;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The Argentinian-Irish owner-chef Nico Gellon crafts a new take on pan-Mediterranean cuisine with eclectic influences. The tasting menu, cooked in purebred Italian or French style and seasoned with Middle Eastern spices, alongside Greek staples such as olives and eggplant. The dishes satisfy both the eye and the tastebud. Choose the counter seats to stay close to the action or book a room for more privacy.;Air conditioning;[]
11790;Kohaku;Taiwan;Taipei;15, Lane 32, Yixian Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0465752;121.5633992;75;true;false;Japanese;The serene Japanese garden is matched by the minimalist wood-clad room and exquisite tableware. Celebrating a career that spans over 20 years, the Japanese chef serves a single season-driven tasting menu dominated by the freshest catch from Kyushu, Japan. Seasoning is intentionally light-handed and nuanced for diners to appreciate the natural flavours. The soy-free seared sesame tofu appetiser is heavenly. The sake list is short but sweet.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11791;Xiantaosu;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;496 Minglun Road, Gushan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6625831;120.2979468;82;false;false;Vegetarian;After a long stint in a Taipei vegetarian restaurant, the chef returned to his hometown, piquing curiosity with his refined plant-based cuisine. He serves three set menus with artfully plated courses that layer rich flavours. Varied techniques, such as fermenting, pickling, grilling, braising and searing, are deftly used to great effect. The vegan braised pork rice uses diced monkey head mushrooms instead of pork, creating light, briny umami.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
11792;Hsin Hsin;Taiwan;Tainan;245, Section 2, Minzu Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9960366;120.2044247;47;true;true;Taiwanese;He may be in his 70s, but founder Chef Ah Tu is still hands-on in the kitchen and his restaurant is a veritable institution of vintage Taiwanese cooking. Symbols of joy and good fortune are deeply ingrained in the décor – from the red shop sign to the red tablecloths. There are only 18 items on the menu, including specialities such as fried shrimp with egg, and traditional fried pork liver. Some dishes require pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11793;Da-Wan;Taiwan;Taipei;5F, 199 Jingye 2nd Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0843789;121.5541471;45;false;false;Barbecue;Da-Wan moved to the shopping streets of Dazhi in late 2021. The dining room adopts a hip, faux-industrial style, with dramatic lighting while at night, the full-height windows let in the electric glow of the department stores nearby. As always, the signature remains Wagyu beef, mostly from Miyazaki prefecture – oyster blade, chuck eye roll, flat iron… grilled to perfection by skilful servers. Thick-cut ox tongue is divinely springy and beefy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
11794;Crab's House;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;93 Minsheng 1st Road, Sinsing District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6277122;120.3118177;40;true;true;Seafood;Founded in 1976, this household name was the first restaurant in town specialising in live seafood shipped daily from the island county of Penghu. As you can tell from its name and the giant crab sign, crab is the signature dish, especially the spiced salt and pepper variety. Besides the eponymous crustacean, ask the friendly servers about the catch of the day. Try also the shrimp rolls wrapped in pork caul fat before being deep-fried.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11795;A Ming Zhu Xing (Baoan Road);Taiwan;Tainan;72 Baoan Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9905684;120.196022;86;false;true;Small eats;Don’t be surprised if you see a queue even before this shop’s opening at 5pm – after all, its cellophane noodle soup with pork offal is one of the must-try Tainan delicacies for many travellers. Chef A Ming still cooks the offal like his father did almost 70 years ago – in a bain-marie to prevent overcooking. As well as the signature pork heart soup, try pork ribs or duck feet and wings braised in a garlicky herbal stock.;Cash only;[]
11796;Moment in Beijing;Taiwan;Taichung;57 Wuquan 7th Street, West District, Taichung, 403, Taiwan;24.135059;120.663236;17;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;Named after Lin Yutang's novel and channelling the style of northern China's grand mansions with its gable roof and grey tiles, this well-known restaurant has been building a loyal following since 2002. The menu revolves around northern Chinese classics such as stir-fried shredded pork and vegetables in an omelette "hat" or sautéed lamb loin with a sweet soybean glaze that marries well with rice. There are also Jiangzhe and Taiwanese choices.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11797;Iron Chef Teppanyaki;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, 215 Zhifu Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.0830941;121.5607867;79;true;true;Teppanyaki;Along with impressive skills, founder Chef Hsieh with almost 50 years of experience on the griddle is also passionate about Chinese medicine. That’s why the food here is lightly seasoned and cooked in tea seed oil instead of butter. The prix-fixe menus emphasize dietary needs according to the time of the year, without sacrificing gastronomic pleasure. Signatures include U.S. beef sirloin roll, popcorn and soufflé made on the spot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
11798;Fresh & Aged;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, 128 Minshan Street, Neihu District, Taipei, 114, Taiwan;25.0613439;121.5748536;34;true;true;Steakhouse;Owned by the largest meat importer in Taiwan, Fresh & Aged specialises in premium beef cuts from Nebraska, U.S.A, typically dry-aged for 28 days in a custom-made chamber. Diners can even pre-order steaks dry-aged up to 128 days. Non-beef choices are also ample and include Cherry Valley duck breast and SRF Kurobuta pork dry-aged for 21 days. The annexed supermarket selling a smorgasbord of raw meats is worth checking out. Pre-ordering is recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11799;Papillon;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;26F, TAi Urban Resort, 189 Linsen 4th Road, Qianzhen District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6110326;120.3040085;21;true;true;French Contemporary;Named after the French word for butterfly, the French chef strives to transform quality ingredients into radically different culinary gems. The spacious room, in muted wood tones, is dotted by butterfly motifs with a tree-like centrepiece being the focal point. Only one tasting menu is served and it’s inspired by the chef’s travel across three continents. Exotic elements come through subtly in his refined French cooking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11800;Yu Yue Lou;Taiwan;Taichung;783, Section 2, Gongyi Road, Nantun District, Taichung, 408, Taiwan;24.150939;120.629279;79;false;false;Cantonese;The high-ceilinged dining room imparts an imposing sense of space while the gold-and-black colours and dew-like strings of pendant lamps exude drama. The kitchen team from Hong Kong reinvents Cantonese cooking with creativity. Grouper fillet poached in lobster bisque over crisp rice uses live seafood from Penghu. Cherry Valley duck is roasted in a longan wood oven and needs pre-ordering. Dim sum is served at lunch and private rooms are available.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11802;Yuan Huan Pien Oyster Egg Omelette;Taiwan;Taipei;Ningxia Night Market, 46 Ningxia Road, Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0563308;121.5152488;22;false;false;Street Food;Has been making its tasty omelettes, with oysters from Tainan drizzled in homemade sweet hot sauce, since 1965.;Cash only;[]
11803;Gi Yuan;Taiwan;Taipei;324, Section 1, Dunhua South Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0353132;121.5484324;16;false;false;Sichuan;Regulars come for the signature chicken soup casserole – it takes 10 hours to make the milky rich chicken stock before free-range chicken, ham, dried scallops and pork trotters are added and cooked for two more hours. Other famed Sichuan dishes are also on the menu, such as dry-fried French beans and Kungpao chicken. Some dishes can be customised with condiments of your choice. It’s always busy so early reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11804;Paul's Canteen;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;162 Sihwei 3rd Road, Linya District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6197004;120.3080244;92;false;false;Taiwanese;The Macanese owner-chef, who has been cooking professionally for over 30 years, opened this bustling spot in 2022. The menu is based on Taiwanese fare, with occasional Cantonese twists, and he seasons his food lightly allowing the natural flavours to shout their name. His deft hand is best sampled in simple dishes like scrambled egg with spinach and tomato – the mild peppery heat, bright colours and light seasonings work together seamlessly. BYOB.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Cash only;[]
11806;Xiang Se;Taiwan;Taipei;1-2 Hukou Street, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0328173;121.5149464;64;true;true;European Contemporary;That the owner is also an antique dealer explains the abundance of exquisite pieces dotting the room. The terrazzo and reclaimed wood flooring also echo with the overall vintage feel. The young chef creates only one fixed price menu based on European traditions, but heavily influenced by South Asian and Tibetian cultures. The intimate ambiance makes it perfect for date nights or casual get-togethers.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11807;Ukai-tei;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;3F, Silks Club, 199 Zhongshan 2nd Road, Cianjhen District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6104003;120.3055122;61;false;false;Teppanyaki;The first overseas venture of Japan’s Ukai group greets diners with a circular staircase and a warm-hued interior that exudes understated elegance. On top of witnessing quality ingredients being cooked skilfully on the iron plate right before your eyes, the experience is completed by attentive service. The signature Wagyu menu includes a rump cut for optimal marbling, while Kaohsiung Ukai-tei course predominantly features local seafood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11809;Plum Chang;Taiwan;Tainan;1-5, Wanqiu, Nanxi District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.1752354;120.4979801;40;false;true;Taiwanese;The owner’s family used to run a plum farm in the neighbourhood. In the 1990s, they opened this restaurant, incorporating the tangy stone fruit into their recipes. Diners’ favourites include plum-scented pork, egg tofu in plum sauce, and stir-fried pork intestines with sour plums. There is a shop selling plums next door and the Meiling Scenic Area nearby is a famous viewing spot for plum blossom in winter. It’s best to book at the weekend.;Cash only;[]
11810;Principe;Taiwan;Tainan;34 Xihua Street, North District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9993779;120.210727;37;true;true;French Contemporary;The wood-rich interior is homely and understated, matching the elegant food with its meticulous attention to detail. The chef honed his skills in Japan and his prix-fixe menu recounts Tainan’s culinary stories with classic French techniques, Japanese influences and ethereal touches. The amuse-bouche is always inspired by a Tainanese snack, while produce from small local farms, such as local beef, takes centre stage in many courses.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11811;Zan;Taiwan;Taipei;B1, 192-1, Section 4, Chengde Road, Shilin District, Taipei, 111, Taiwan;25.087711;121.522072;49;false;true;Teppanyaki;A mishmash of different styles seems to work miraculously here – Italian stained glass window and a marble counter are juxtaposed with Chinese wooden furniture and silver cutlery. The chef was trained in one of most prestigious teppanyaki restaurants in Japan and has over 40 years of experience under his belt. Signatures include U. S. SRF Wagyu, braised abalone in kombu salt, and prawn with French sauce. Hida beef is also available for pre-ordering.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
11812;Shan Nay Chicken;Taiwan;Taipei;Nanjichang Night Market, Stall 3, 20-3, Lane 307, Section 2, Zhonghua Road, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.029061;121.5058198;85;true;false;Street Food;Good-value steamed chicken is feted for its springy skin and juicy flesh. Come before 8 pm for chicken legs.;Cash only;[]
11813;Shing-Peng-Lai (Zhongshan North Road);Taiwan;Taipei;55, Section 7, Zhongshan North Road, Shilin District, Taipei, 111, Taiwan;25.120419;121.53094;27;true;false;Taiwanese;Since 1987, this joint has been popular for get-togethers among family and friends on account of its remarkable traditional Taiwanese fare. With an array of both home-style dishes and banquet classics, the menu features sharing plates and comforting staples that deliver big flavours. Try signatures such as boiled free-range chicken, and Buddha Jumps Over The Wall. Taiwan-style ice lollies at the end of the meal are the icing on the cake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11814;Set.;Taiwan;Taipei;110, Section 2, Chengde Road, Datong District, Taipei, 103, Taiwan;25.0587162;121.5180001;20;false;false;Creative;Far from being stuffy or overly formal, this fine dining spot boasts a friendly, laid-back vibe. Inspired by personal experiences, nature and the seasons, the dishes are underpinned by solid Western technique and packed with Asian flavours. The chef couple gives kitchen scraps a new lease of life as house-made condiments, such as mushroom chilli paste with pumpkin skin, in a bid for zero waste. The wine list comprises natural choices only.;Air conditioning;[]
11815;AKIN;Taiwan;Taipei;8, Lane 92, Section 1, Jianguo North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.06868;121.53061;45;true;false;Creative;Chef Ah-kin hails from Hong Kong and Akin is a love letter to his homeland. The single tasting menu changes with the seasons, but the distinctive Hong Kong influence remains. His deep-fried sea urchin and purple shiso puff pastry is a nod to Hong Kong’s dim sum radish puff. Next to the Yitong Park, the understated elegant interior exudes natural earthy tones around an open kitchen. Concise wine list - ask the sommelier for pairing tips.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11817;Capstone Steakhouse;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;1F, H2O Hotel, 366 Minghua Road, Gushan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6636112;120.3021023;28;false;false;Steakhouse;The first outpost of Danny’s Steakhouse outside of Taipei shares the same design motifs with its flagship – a high-ceilinged, spacious dining room with a mezzanine glass cellar and a show kitchen behind a glass wall. The set menu follows suit and is also the same as its Taipei sister, offering multiple choices for each course. The dry- or wet-aged U.S. beef steaks remain the culinary highlight. Private rooms are available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11818;Tainan Wang;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;187 Liouhe 2nd Road, Cianjin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6302612;120.2936053;25;false;true;Taiwanese;The Tainanese founder started selling fried noodles with eel over 60 years ago. The second-generation owner is a passionate foodie and has been adding new items to the menu. That said, the speciality is still the eel, either fried with scallion or braised in sesame oil, boasting tasty, springy flesh. House-made meat balls, cuttlefish balls and taro balls are also addictive. Those interested in trying virgin crabs should pre-order when booking.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11819;Marc L³;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;231 Renyi Street, Cianjin District, Kaohsiung, 80145, Taiwan;22.6205944;120.3009909;64;true;false;European Contemporary;After living abroad for 10-plus years, the chef opened a pop-up kitchen at Yancheng Market to much acclaim. In memory of his childhood friends, he opened Marc L³ in 2021 to serve fine dining food in a relaxed atmosphere. His 9-course menu comprises modern, Western dishes made with local seasonable produce, weaving layered flavours with his witty descriptions. The soundtrack of English and Taiwanese oldies adds to the experience. The cocktail designed in-house is worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11821;Cheng Jia;Taiwan;Taipei;6, Lane 92, Section 2, Minquan East Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0610613;121.5316422;41;false;true;Taiwanese;After honing his skills in an establishment of classic Taiwanese cooking for over 20 years, the head chef opened his own restaurant with only three tables in an alleyway hectic with street food stalls. Taiwanese all-time favourites are given a new spin here and his chicken soups are hugely popular. Try also sautéed shrimps with scrambled eggs in lettuce wraps. Book a table on social media and discuss the menu with the owner in advance.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11822;Mochi Baby;Taiwan;Taipei;111 Raohe Street, Songshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.050415;121.574025;69;true;true;Street Food;The transparent case houses gooey mochi – they’re freshly made every day and have a strong sticky rice fragrance.;Cash only;[]
11823;Muji Beef Noodles;Taiwan;Taipei;239 Wuxing Street, Xinyi District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.0274656;121.5634637;54;false;true;Noodles;The three sisters who run the place are very specific about their cooking. The flavoursome broth is made with beef bones and meat, Chinese herbs, scallion, garlic and a secret fruit that lends a subtle sweetness. The signature beef noodle soup uses only local beef for its unrivalled meaty flavour. Equally addictive is their jinbing – a fluffy pancake made to order with beef or pork wrapped inside. Don’t miss their marinated food either.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11824;FIRNS;Taiwan;Taichung;19, Lane 50, Jingcheng Road, Xitun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1565402;120.6561637;80;false;false;French Contemporary;Chef Ricky from Hong Kong honed his skills in some prestigious kitchens in Europe and his home city. From his unique vantage point, he champions a modern French-Asian cuisine featuring locally sourced produce. His love for Taiwan also manifests itself in the papier mâché lamp, cutlery and tableware crafted by local artisans. The incredibly fresh catch of the day and the beautifully plated seasonal dessert are the highlights on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
11825;Baho (Da'an);Taiwan;Taipei;4, Lane 102, Section 1, Anhe Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0342117;121.5519352;63;true;false;Barbecue;This Japanese barbecue restaurant buys whole Omi Sawai hime cows, offering over 30 Shimofuri and Akami wagyu cuts to be enjoyed in eight different ways, including tartare, sushi, soup, and seared steak. Rare cuts like top round and inside skirt tend to run out but you can pre-order them. The very flavoursome beef lard rice in lotus leaf is not to be missed. The dimly-lit room is cosy, service impeccable and presentation dramatic.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
11826;Duck Zhen (Wufu 4th Road);Taiwan;Kaohsiung;258 Wufu 4th Road, Yancheng District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6249514;120.2811377;90;false;true;Small eats;After opening its doors over 60 years ago, Duck Zhen now takes up two retail space, but still has barely enough room to seat the hordes of diners lining up for its duck dishes day and night. Its smoked duck platter is the must-try item, with juicy, flavourful meat to be dipped into the house-made garlic sauce, and best enjoyed with a bowl of braised pork rice. Portion sizes of assorted duck offal or duck soup can be tailored to your party size.;Cash only;[]
11827;The Ukai;Taiwan;Taipei;46F, Breeze Nan Shan, 17 Songzhi Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.034418;121.567301;15;false;false;Teppanyaki;This is the second Taiwanese outpost of its namesake in Japan, famous for its Western-style table experience delivered with teppanyaki techniques. There is no à la carte and the two set menus change with the seasons. Signatures include steamed abalone with rock salt, garlic fried rice, and Wagyu steak or tenderloin from Tamura farm. Finish in style with a choice of dessert made with seasonal fruit and served in the cosy lounge.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
11828;A-Yu Beef Shabu Shabu (Kunlun Road);Taiwan;Tainan;733-1 Kunlun Road, Rende District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9410754;120.2613675;41;true;false;Hotpot;It took the founder’s wife and son three years to build A-Yu’s second outlet that spans over 3,000 square metres. Just like the original branch, this restaurant uses only the freshest beef from Shanhua district and serves it in beef stock hotpot to let its natural flavours shine. Order different bovine cuts on a form, but help yourself to the sides, veggies, drinks or the famous braised beef rice. Reservations aren’t accepted so expect long queues.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11829;Yuan;Taiwan;Taichung;35 Dadun 12th Street, West District, Taichung, 408, Taiwan;24.1498848;120.6539851;55;false;true;Taiwanese contemporary;After stints at some top restaurants in Japan, chef-owner Yuan opened this dining concept in 2013. In 2024, it moved to this spot with a compact dining room gracefully decorated with floral arrangements. The single menu with three main course options is inspired by Taiwan's culinary history. Banquet classics such as eel rolls with salted egg yolk and ham are given a fresh spin. House-grown herbs and edible flowers add colour to the attractive plating.;Air conditioning;[]
11830;Sushi Nanami;Taiwan;Taipei;6, Lane 452, Section 4, Ren'ai Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.037111;121.559124;79;false;false;Sushi;This place feels like a secluded Japanese home – the kimono-clad hostess walks you through the garden to the dining room with 12 seats at a cypress counter. The Japanese chef serves an omakase menu that draws on both tradition and innovation with dishes such as octopus with house-made ricotta. The sashimi shows intricate knife skills and the sushi rice is dressed in a special vinegar blend. The panna cotta with honey rounds off the meal nicely.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11831;L'herbe;Taiwan;Tainan;950, Section 2, Yonghua Road, Anping District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9920043;120.1651164;28;false;true;European Contemporary;The head chef trained in France and worked in some top-tier establishments in Taipei. She opened L’herbe in 2019, recruiting an all-women kitchen team to imbue traditional Gallic cuisine with distinctive local flavours. Expect to see angled loofah, basella, pork offal and the like on the table. Her tasting menu changes every season, with a choice of several main courses – Lumina lamb chop from New Zealand is especially worth trying.;Air conditioning;[]
11832;Mao Su;Taiwan;Tainan;43 Fudong Street, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9861941;120.2229702;63;false;false;Vegetarian;Light wood furnishings, arched windows and a crackle effect wall combine to create a relaxed, modern space. Run by a Tainanese catering group, this restaurant is aimed at omnivorous diners who wish to reduce their carbon footprint by forgoing meat once in a while. The lacto-ovo-vegetarian dishes are loaded with Asian spices and condiments, such as satay, Sichuan pepper and kimchi. Try the classic stir-fried king oyster mushroom with basil.;Air conditioning;[]
11833;Komboi;Taiwan;Taipei;28, Lane 270, Section 1, Dunhua South Road, Da’an District, Taipei, 10685, Taiwan;25.03892;121.54678;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Komboi is the homophone of the Taiwanese phrase for ‘empty plates’, as the chef hopes his guests enjoy their meals down to the last bite. Modern dishes embody his novel ideas, finessed by techniques acquired when travelling in France. While a shorter set menu is offered at lunch, we recommend the unabridged ‘experience’ menu to best appreciate his vision. The minimalist room boasts warm hues, dark wood furniture and ribbed glass pendant lamps.;Air conditioning;[]
11835;Fu Yuan;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;9F, Grand Hi-Lai Hotel, 266 Chenggong 1st Road, Cianjin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.62042;120.29532;34;false;true;Taiwanese;This restaurant in a luxury hotel is the group’s only F&B outlet serving Taiwanese cooking. With crystal chandeliers and oil paintings, the classically furnished room can feel a bit dated, but the friendly service, homely dishes and seafood sourced daily from neighbouring ports more than compensate. Deep-fried chicken nuggets offer a hint of camellia oil aroma that works well with the crispy sliced ginger.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11836;Thomas Chien;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;11 Chenggong 2nd Road, Cianjhen District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6043997;120.3008295;30;true;false;French Contemporary;Not only has Chef Chien got culinary acumen and all the classic French techniques, but he also cares for his carbon footprint and sustainability of food sources. By eating here, you’ll be supporting small local farms and fishing communities. His set menus use mostly local, seasonal ingredients and his lunch menus change monthly to keep them fresh. From time to time, top guest chefs are invited from overseas to broaden diners’ gastronomic horizons.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11837;Chope Chope Eatery;Taiwan;Taipei;4F, Shin Kong Mitsukoshi Xinyi Place A4, 19 Songgao Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.0394728;121.5668751;15;true;true;South East Asian;While ‘chope’ means to reserve a seat by putting a tissue pack on it in ‘Singlish’, you can call to book a table here. The Singaporean chef helming JL Studio in Taichung opened this Kopitiam concept to celebrate casual Singaporean dining. Try har cheong gai (fried wings in fermented shrimp sauce), kopi pai kut (coffee ribs) and house-made murtabak bread. Asian-inspired cocktails such as Tan herbal tea in a plastic bag are both fun and delicious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11838;The Tavernist;Taiwan;Taipei;12F, Kimpton Da An Hotel, 25, Lane 27, Section 4, Ren'ai Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0403733;121.545489;51;true;false;European Contemporary;With globe light fixtures connected like an oversized pearl bracelet, the bamboo-clad room has a whimsical feel. In addition to European classics such as fish and chips, thyme-roasted chicken and beef Wellington, the Taiwanese chef also caters to the local palate by using Western techniques to cook local produce. Try his dried radish chicken soup with squid, and kelp popcorn chicken. It's also a pet-friendly space, so book ahead for your furry friend.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11839;Hibiki Seafood;Taiwan;Taichung;356 Shizheng North 2nd Road, Xitun District, Taichung, 407, Taiwan;24.1652034;120.6344988;95;false;false;Seafood;It's hard to guess from the façade what cuisine is served here, but then the live fish tanks by the entrance give it away. There is no menu: guests make their selection and specify how they would like it cooked. Seafood from Yilan, Penghu, Japan and other places are prepared in traditionally Taiwanese ways, namely steamed or shallow-fried, to highlight their natural flavours. Go alone or with friends – portions are adjusted according to party size.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11840;The Temple-front Eatery;Taiwan;Tainan;86, Section 2, Simen Road, Central West District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9923374;120.1985955;47;false;true;Taiwanese;Formerly in front of Shatao Temple, this 60-year-old bolthole is barely more than a seafood cart in a no-frills space. It serves rustic, traditional Taiwanese cooking at frugal prices until late. Rice omelette is filled with tangy-sweet shredded pork and fried rice in ketchup. The Taiwanese fried pork chop is crispy and golden and ideally paired with potato salad. Oden is served in an amber broth without MSG, alongside house-made dips.;Cash only;[]
11841;Tao Luan Ting Roast Peking Duck Palace;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, 86 Fuxing North Road, Songshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.051288;121.543761;42;false;false;Beijing Cuisine;The third-generation owner still makes Peking duck the way his grandpa did over 50 years ago. Antibiotic-free Muscovy ducks from Yilan County are kept 100 days more than their counterparts for extra fattiness. Delivered daily and air-dried for a day to crisp up the skin before roasting in a wood oven, each duck is carved into 36 pieces and served with flatbread. Don’t miss the made-to-order pan-fried shredded radish dumplings with a soupy filling.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11842;Meidz Seafood;Taiwan;Taichung;473-2 Zhongshan Road, Shalu District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.24439;120.56179;91;true;false;Seafood;Before the owning couple opened this restaurant in 1989, they had been fishers and fishmongers. Now a household name and managed by the second generation, Meidz still prides itself on quality seafood mostly imported from Penghu. Oval squid in soy, three-cup grouper, rice vermicelli soup with pomfret, and catch of the day such as dusky stingfish are all excellent choices. Reservations are recommended at weekends.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11843;Page;Taiwan;Taipei;4, Alley 20, Lane 595, Bei'an Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.08184;121.547774;86;false;false;International;This laid-back bistro dotted with music memorabilia speaks loudly of the passions of one of its owners – food and music. The blue and white dining room with its open kitchen sets the mood for a food and music journey. The chef reinterprets Taiwanese classics with western techniques, as pickled glueberries and barrel broiled chicken find their way into the menu. Oo-peh-tshiat, or assorted offal and meat platter, is jazzed up with western spices.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11844;Tajimaya Shabu Shabu;Taiwan;Taipei;5F, THE ARCADE, 166 Dunhua North Road, Songshan District, Taipei, 105, Taiwan;25.055637;121.548475;95;true;true;Shabu-shabu;The owner believes hot pot dinner is the perfect occasion for diners to chat and have a good time. That’s why the servers here cook the food for them so that they won’t be distracted from their conversations. Apart from local seafood and veggies, he also imports wagyu and Tajima beef directly from Japan to ensure the quality. If you feel like splurging a little, order a whole fish or a Filipino lobster to share.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11845;Sushi Nomura;Taiwan;Taipei;4, Alley 19, Lane 300, Section 4, Ren'ai Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.036207;121.554783;97;false;false;Sushi;Renovated in 2023, the room now features clean, simple lines and muted hues. Chef Nomura, who moved to Taiwan years ago, still serves several set menus, with Edomae sushi being the main event. A mix of Koshihikari and Nanatsuboshi rice is cooked in Mount Fuji spring water and dressed in a blend of akazu and regular sushi vinegar. To sample a greater variety of sashimi, opt for the menus at higher prices.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11846;CRATAIN;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;306 Changsheng Road, Gushan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.66398;120.29867;66;true;false;European Contemporary;Cratain is a portmanteau of Tasmania’s Cradle Mountain, which the owner once climbed. He draws a parallel between his restaurant and mountaineering, using the pristine white space as a blank canvas for dishes finessed with well-honed European techniques. The 5-course set menu offers flexible choices, together with á la carte options at dinner. Meat, chargrilled or pan-seared, is the main event, but the pasta is also a highlight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11847;Lin Ju;Taiwan;Taipei;100 Dunhua North Road, Shongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0534541;121.547928;21;true;false;Cantonese;This restaurant at Illume Taipei exudes understated elegance. It serves fittingly refined Cantonese food that showcases premium ingredients and the chef's well-honed skills. The veteran Hong Kong chef, in his 70s, specialises in season-driven dishes and dried seafood. The baked crab shell is stuffed with crabmeat, roe and cheese, and boasts deep umami. There are two customisable menus. Book at least three days ahead.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11848;Gyu Go Zou;Taiwan;Tainan;577 Jianping Road, Anping District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9947887;120.1834751;78;false;false;Hotpot;This spacious restaurant with high ceilings and a black colour scheme is a sub-brand of the beef hotpot legend Liu Jia Zhuang. Freshly slaughtered local beef and offal are the specialities, to be blanched in an array of soup bases, such as the classic Tainan beef bone broth or mala broth. The popular Motsunabe with beef intestines needs pre-ordering. Alongside Japanese hotpot, it also serves Taiwanese stir-fries like beef heart with scallion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
11849;Syan Syang;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;75-1 Wenhua Road, Jiaxian District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;23.0815488;120.5878598;94;true;true;Taiwanese;Adjacent to a water park in an area famous for taro and bamboo shoots, this restaurant has been serving game meats and wild greens since 1971. Signatures include wild boar, muntjac, spotted dove, giant mottled eel, wild fish and shrimps. Braised pork belly with taro and shredded bamboo shoot, and turmeric chicken are also worth trying. Round it out with deep-fried taro balls, and the complimentary taro ice cubes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
11850;Master of Mushroom (Xinshe);Taiwan;Taichung;287 Xiezhong Street, Xinshe District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.2007861;120.7992768;67;true;true;Taiwanese;In 2006, a mushroom farmer opened this mushroom-themed restaurant in Xinshe, the mushroom capital of Taiwan. Free-range chicken soup with shiitake tastes rich and flavoursome, while dried day lily flowers and assorted mushrooms add to the complex taste profile. Try also three-cup monkey-head mushrooms, and mushroom minced pork rice. Adjacent to the Sea of Flowers and Dakeng, it makes a great stop to recharge your body after a day out.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11852;16 by Flo;Taiwan;Taipei;4-1, Lane 118, Section 2, Heping East Road, Da’an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.02394;121.542709;99;false;false;French Contemporary;Look for the blue house in this quiet alley for the atmospheric 16-seat eatery specialising in traditional Burgundy fare. A Robuchon alumna opened this tiny gem in 2023 to showcase her brand of French cooking with a feminine touch. The appetiser of ossetra caviar with scampi tartare, elegantly presented on an antique embossed silver plate, has a buttery, briny sweetness. Don't miss the cheese course before dessert – a must in any French meal.;Air conditioning;[]
11853;85TD;Taiwan;Taipei;85F, Taipei 101, 7, Section 5, Xinyi Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0339324;121.5644667;59;true;true;Cantonese;The group that owns Taïrroir opened this fashionably retro restaurant in the iconic skyscraper in 2021. The sweeping view is a given, and the room in brass and olive green is quite charming. The head chef from Hong Kong has over 50 years of experience under his belt and is well-versed in both contemporary and classic dishes like the juicy barbecue pork, and his take on Buddha’s Temptation, a cross between the Hong Kong and Taiwanese versions of the soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11854;Cheng's Noodles;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;5, Lane 201, Sinle Street, Yancheng District, Kaohsiung, 803, Taiwan;22.625;120.28273;39;true;false;Noodles;In Yancheng district famous for street snacks stands this 80-plus-year-old noodle shop. The third generation owner insists on using top-quality ingredients and keeping the room spotless. All food is served in porcelain tableware with vintage floral prints. The signature noodles swim in a flavourful broth made with pork bones, chicken and veggies, to be enjoyed with an array of side dishes such as blanched pork offal or sliced chicken.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11855;Hai Guang;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;4 Nanda Road, Zuoying District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6744488;120.2871402;24;false;true;Jiangzhe;Formerly an army club for entertaining the U.S. army and assorted VIPs, this is now a popular restaurant serving mostly Jiangzhe cuisine with a few Beijing and Sichuan items. Though the décor is nothing to write home about, signatures like pork ribs in orange glaze, and sea perch in chilli bean sauce are impeccably made. Don’t miss their scallion pancakes loaded with flavours and aromas. Reservations are recommended, especially at weekends.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11857;Good Crab House;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;696 Jiangong Road, Sanmin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.64873;120.32092;41;false;false;Seafood;For over three decades, the owner-chef has been flying in the best ingredients from his home island of Penghu twice a day to serve his customers. The famous salt-baked virgin crab burst with buttery roe, while the baby octopus in dark brown sugar sauce boast tender flesh and deep caramel flavour. Fried fish tail tossed in salt and pepper is also hard to resist. Don’t miss the Feng-ju tea made with an herb native to Penghu.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11858;EMBERS;Taiwan;Taipei;24, Lane 122, Section 4, Ren-Ai Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.03582;121.55014;94;false;false;Taiwanese contemporary;The owner-chef revives the embers of Taiwan’s culinary past with a seasonal 12-course menu that subverts the preconceptions about Western dining. The food displays influences of indigenous cultures, featuring native ingredients such as mock betel nut and paper mulberry leaf. The room is furnished generously with wood and the nest-like centrepiece above the bar made with steam-bent cedar is styled after hunting huts of the old days. Vegan flavor menu is available for reservation.;Air conditioning;[]
11859;Le Côté LM;Taiwan;Taichung;59 Cunzhong Street, West District, Taichung, 403, Taiwan;24.1411594;120.6589121;40;false;false;French Contemporary;Nestled in a quiet alley, this classical modern-style place with an opulent chandelier as its centrepiece seamlessly combines wood textures and metallic accents. The open kitchen is visible from all seats, but sitting at the counter offers a more intimate and interactive experience. The tasting menu features contemporary French dishes enlivened by spices and seasonal vegetables. Wine and non-alcoholic beverage pairings are served at lunch only.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11860;Tsuki Yo Iwa;Taiwan;Taipei;9, Lane 25, Shuangcheng Street, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0662965;121.5248202;62;false;false;Japanese;Taiwan’s first crab-themed kaiseki restaurant ships live matsuba and taraba crabs from Japan every week. Kegani crabs and puffer fish are also offered when in season. Four set menus showcase the crustaceans in all their glory using different preparations and techniques. Even the claypot rice is nothing short of stunning. Ask for counter seats to be close to the action or a room for more privacy. Book at least one week ahead.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11861;A Cun Beef Soup (Baoan Road);Taiwan;Tainan;41 Baoan Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.990219;120.1965471;79;true;false;Small eats;This renowned shop has been around since 1968, serving hand-sliced beef half-cooked in a scalding broth made with beef bones and veggies, to be enjoyed after being dipped in a special blend of sweet and thick soy sauce accompanied by shredded ginger. Do also try their stir-fried beef with cabbage. The shop closes once the ingredients have sold out.;Cash only;[]
11863;Opus One Yin Yue;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;215 Wunci Road, Zuoying District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6745873;120.3092914;47;true;true;European Contemporary;The dimly lit dining room is sleek and minimal, and the kitchen and service teams are small but efficient. Only one seasonal omakase menu is offered, with a choice of main from pork, beef and lobster, followed by a small portion of Japanese curry rice. The chef cleverly incorporates Asian influences in European-style dishes using ingredients like turmeric, lemongrass, huangjiu and kombu. Reservations are mandatory via social media.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11864;MeatGQ;Taiwan;Taichung;699, Section 4, Yifeng Road, Nantun District, Taichung, 408, Taiwan;24.15085;120.62848;40;false;false;Steakhouse;A Taichung-based brand opened MeatGQ in 2014 and the steaks surpass mere good quality (or "GQ"). The glass room for aging occupies a prominent position in the restaurant, complementing the lofty ceiling and elegant decor. The menu features various prime cuts from the US, Australia and Japan – those that are dry-aged in-house are especially prized. Stay tuned for the creative appetisers that are added to the menu now and then.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11865;Orient Dragon;Taiwan;Taichung;271-1, Section 2, Gongyi Road, Nantun District, Taichung, 408, Taiwan;24.150829;120.6429518;31;false;false;Taiwanese;This restaurant changed hands in 2022, but the festive interior with its red and black colour scheme stayed the same – as did the kitchen team. Rest assured that their signature Taiwanese home-style cooking, along with some novelty Sichuanese dishes, still taste as good as always. Popular choices include three-cup “springy” pork trotter, steamed fourfinger threadfin with pickled bamboo shoot, and sakura ebi fried rice.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11867;Really Good Seafood;Taiwan;Taipei;222, Section 1, Fuxing South Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.039168;121.54344;73;false;true;Seafood;As its name suggests, seafood is big on the menu – and it’s good! Diners can pick from the live fish tanks and the staff is more than happy to recommend cooking methods. Salt-baked virgin mud crab, salad of bamboo shoots and bottarga from wild-caught mullet are among the highlights. Solo diners are also pampered – a number of menus for one lets them sample an array of specialities. Its convenient location next to a metro station is a further bonus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11868;Shun Te Beef Soup;Taiwan;Tainan;59 Mincyuan Road, Syuejia District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.2317947;120.1805228;85;false;true;Small eats;Its sign could use a new coat of paint and the room is nothing to write home about, but the regulars have been returning for its hearty beef soup for nearly three decades. The broth is made from beef bones and tendons, slow cooked for up to eight hours. Fresh local beef is shipped from the slaughterhouse three times a day to ensure freshness. Besides the soup, beef stir-fry and braised pork rice are also popular. Avoid peak hours if you don’t want to wait.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11869;Cho;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;2F, YUIMOM Residence, 815 Jiouru 1st Road, Sanmin District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6397001;120.3202191;39;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The pristine space in a serviced apartment tower is done out in brick-red hues and has trendy pendant lamps. Helmed by a Taiwanese head chef, the kitchen delivers a tasting menu that effortlessly unites local produce with influences from around the world. A dietician by training, the chef advocates healthy eating and a balanced diet, while keeping prices affordable. In addition to the main room, there are private rooms for parties and banquets.;Air conditioning;[]
11870;Como En Casa Gourmet;Taiwan;Tainan;590 Anbei Road, Anping District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9984552;120.1488159;80;true;false;Spanish;The chef, who hails from Pamplona in Spain, was originally a trader of Spanish food. He married his Tainanese wife and decided to use his knowledge by opening a restaurant, on a quiet street that resembles the European countryside. Both set menus and à la carte choices abound, all made with quality ingredients, such as live seafood from Anping Port. Check out the Spanish wines at bargain prices. On balmy nights, ask for a table on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11871;Wamaki;Taiwan;Taipei;22, Lane 119, Linsen North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0504962;121.5259584;26;false;false;Japanese;The head chef of Amis descent hailing from Taitung has over 20 years of experience in Japanese cuisine. At Wamaki, he creates kappo dishes over charcoal fire, using mostly Taiwanese produce and native herbs such as prickly ash seeds and Maqaw pepper. The chef even travels to his hometown on weekends to pick his own herbs. For lunch and dinner, there is only one set menu, but the chef can tailor the menu for you with advance notice.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11872;Kanshi;Taiwan;Tainan;58 Chongren Street, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.98432;120.22278;33;true;true;Japanese;The Hongkong head chef worked in Japan and Macau for over 20 years before opening Umami in 2015 as he got hooked on the charm and slower pace of Tainan City upon his first visit. The cosy, wood-clad room is furnished in traditional Japanese style, with meticulous attention to detail. Diners can choose between the omakase menu and the nigiri sushi set: the former comprises multiple courses with sashimi, kappo dishes, tempura and sushi.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11873;Orchid;Taiwan;Taipei;83, Section 2, Anhe Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0300658;121.5521914;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Perfect for a date, this restaurant has gold chain curtains hanging mid-air, theatrically lit against a dark ceiling. The young Japanese chef has worked and travelled extensively in Japan, Australia, Singapore and Taiwan, gaining culinary insights along the way. His season-driven menu sees eclectic influences through a global lens, providing diners with a choice of three mains. The meticulously plated food has a distinctly modern look.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11875;Cha Cha Thé Cuisine;Taiwan;Taipei;23, Lane 219, Section 1, Fuxing South Road, Da’an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.039092;121.5455407;72;true;false;French Contemporary;A tea salon started by the founder of a local high fashion brand became a full-blown dining concept in 2022. The room boasts a wall of Pu-er tea bricks as a nod to its past. The 3- to 5-course lunch set offers good value, with only one season-driven tasting menu at dinner. The head chefs excel in preparing local and Asian produce using classic French techniques. Petit fours are served with your choice of Chinese tea, such as Taitung red oolong.;Air conditioning;[]
11876;Antico Forno;Taiwan;Taipei;141 Rui'an Street, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0267194;121.5397453;86;true;false;Italian;Young crowds have been coming here in droves since 2013 for its famous thin-crust pizzas – from simple classics like Margherita to crowd-pleasers such as Tartufata. The chef learned his craft in Italy and his respect for tradition is evidenced by dishes like Ginocchio di Agnello alla Milanese, tender in texture and robust in flavour. The room feels homely and cosy, and many items are for sharing. The Italian wines represent excellent value.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11877;Jin Xia;Taiwan;Tainan;2F, T.S. Mall, 366, Section 1, Zhonghua East Road, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9916433;120.2330771;88;true;false;Taiwanese;A spin-off from long-standing institution Asha Restaurant, this sub-branch was started by a third generation of the family in 2015 after graduating from culinary school. As a tribute to their great aunt, Asha’s founder, Jin Xia carries most items from Asha’s menu, but with new creations on top. Start your meal with an appetiser platter – chargrilled bottarga, shrimp rolls, and crab balls are especially divine. Then order red crab on sticky rice as a main.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11878;Le Plein;Taiwan;Taichung;3, Alley 39, Cunzhong Street, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1409408;120.6597656;37;true;true;Innovative;Le Plein moved to a remodelled heritage building in 2021. The room now spreads across two floors, complete with vaulted ceiling and a courtyard. Bare concrete and exposed brick walls work nicely with the wood-rich interior. The à la carte menu has been replaced by a 4- to 5-course tasting menu that celebrates Taiwanese produce and culinary culture with ingenious, artfully plated creations. Cold-brewed tea pairings are also worth checking out.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
11879;Sushi Masuda;Taiwan;Taipei;5F, THE ARCADE, 166 Dunhua North Road, Songshan District, Taipei, 105, Taiwan;25.0556369;121.548475;92;true;true;Sushi;Mosaic tiles, mirrors and a chandelier with hundreds of floating glass balls make this dining room hipper than most sushi spots. This joint venture by its Tokyo namesake and the Arcade is helmed by Chef Kosugi and supervised by Chef Masuda, the head chef at the Tokyo flagship who also sources ingredients for this outpost, mostly from Toyosu Market. Don’t miss the maguro from Aomori prefecture with its silky texture and lovely sheen. Omakase only.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11880;Kuca Seafood;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;55 Dewei Street, Zuoying District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6622365;120.3063119;68;false;false;Seafood;Unlike many seafood joint, the room with blue-green walls and lots of greenery feels relaxed but also chic. The family business, run by a father and son, also stands out with a unique sense of humour in dish naming and the incorporation of Western produce in recipes like squid ink fried rice, which impresses with its strong, earthy aromas of truffle oil. Another popular dish, silky scrambled egg with sea urchin roe bursts with briny sweetness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11881;Rong Cuisine;Taiwan;Taichung;10-2, Lane 17, Section 4, Fuxing Road, East District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1357195;120.6837919;30;true;false;Asian;Chef Rong opened this little gem tucked away in an alley in 2021. The room is reminiscent of a Japanese diner, with its wooden counter enclosing an open kitchen. The eclectic menu covers Taiwanese, Japanese and Western dishes in smaller portions so that guests can sample more variety. Signature items include braised pork rice with sakura shrimps – the hand-diced pork is fatty and melty, Job’s tears and rice that’s rich and creamy. Reservations are mandatory.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
11883;Wen Tao;Taiwan;Taichung;191, Section 3, Taiyuan Road, Beitun District, Taichung, 406, Taiwan;24.1654322;120.6915378;21;true;false;Taiwanese;Meaning ‘my home’, this single-storey courtyard house circa 1950s set amid tall residential buildings will instantly teleport guests back to grandma’s home in the countryside. The menu is mostly Taiwanese from a bygone era, with occasional Hunan and Xinjiang offerings. Old-time steamed river perch with fermented chillies has complex savoury umami with a mild kick. Barrel chicken is chargrilled in the courtyard and needs pre-ordering.;Car park,Cash only;[]
11884;ÉCRU;Taiwan;Taipei;19, Lane 177, Section 1, Dunhua South Road, Da’an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.04315;121.55039;52;false;true;Creative;A Fukuoka native, Chef Tobimatsu honed his skills in Tokyo and Taipei. At Écru, he rolls out pedigree Gallic cuisine with subtle Japanese and Taiwanese influences. Not only are most of the seasonal ingredients sourced from Japan, the crockery and dinnerware are also made by Japanese artisans, in a perfect match with the elegant interior. Only one set menu. Wine and sake pairing is available.;Air conditioning;[]
11885;Torien Yakitori;Taiwan;Taichung;48 Zhongming South Road, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1554371;120.6583189;95;false;true;Japanese;The owner-chef used to run an izakaya and honed his yakitori skills in Japan. After walking through a mini Japanese garden, diners are ushered to their seats at a U-shaped counter to witness the chefs' grilling tricks. Only local Gui Ding chickens are used and not a single part goes to waste. Diners are expected to opt for a set menu, to which other rare cuts can be added. Call ahead to pre-order chicken sashimi, squab or Silkie chicken.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11886;Shi;Taiwan;Taipei;39-1, Section 3, Jinan Rd, Da’an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.04027;121.53607;71;false;true;Japanese;The miniature Japanese garden at the entrance aptly sets the mood for a cosy, tranquil dining experience. The two head chefs prepare dishes in the kappo tradition, with occasional sushi courses and some minor adjustments to cater to the Taiwanese palate. Most of the ingredients are sourced in Japan, but super fresh seafood from Taiwan’s northeastern coast also makes it to the dining table. The menu changes daily depending on the availability of top-notch ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11887;Taiwan Rice Dining Hall;Taiwan;Taipei;12, Lane 175, Section 2, Heping East Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0262836;121.5420492;35;true;true;Taiwanese;An advocate of healthy and sustainable gastronomy, this eatery sources its produce from small local farms and serves only organic food. The 14-seater offers one set menu with a drink, a main, two sides, soup and dessert each day. Rice is at the core of its ethos – from the dazzling varieties of steamed Taiwanese rice, to amazake and desserts made with the treasured grain. Local condiments and snacks are available for purchase. Reservations mandatory.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11890;Uosho;Taiwan;Taipei;24, Lane 83, Section 1, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0499609;121.5238215;61;false;true;Japanese;Uosho was founded in Japan’s Saitama Prefecture in 1883. This restaurant is the century-old unagi-ya’s only outpost outside of Japan. The room juxtaposes light and dark woods with neutrals in a modern Japanese style. The signature una-jyu uses Taiwanese eel that is steamed before grilling to order à la Kanto style, and served in a lacquered box over a bed of rice, drizzled with a sweet-savoury glaze. Try also the fluffy unagi tamagoyaki while you wait.;Air conditioning;[]
11892;CEO 1950;Taiwan;Taipei;24, Lane 62, Section 3, Xinsheng North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0656859;121.5265823;67;false;true;European Contemporary;The restored mansion of Taiwan Central Bank’s first CEO circa 1950s is now home to a European restaurant on the ground floor and an exhibition space upstairs. The airy room is lavishly furnished, with modern light fixtures that set nicely against the exposed wooden beams. The food also matches its tranquil, lush surrounding – the seasonal 8-course prix-fixe menu is thoughtfully designed by the Taiwanese head chef who used to work abroad.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11893;Uke;Taiwan;Taipei;37, Lane 78,  Section 1, Anhe Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0351541;121.5501646;85;false;true;Japanese;The understated room behind a Zen garden is tucked deep in a residential area. Behind the 600-year-old solid fir counter, Chef Uke – with over 20 years of experience – marries fish from Kyushu, Tokyo and Hokkaido with sushi rice dressed in white or red vinegar according to their taste profiles. If you let him know prior to your visit, he can serve more sushi and sashimi instead of cooked Kappo dishes, or you can pay extra for an all-sushi meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11895;Temperature Studio;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;50 Gongyuan East Road, Gangshan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.7995122;120.292222;92;false;true;Innovative;The owner-chef has over 10 years of experience in haute cuisine. He opened this 6-seater in 2021 because he believes temperature is at the core of all good food. The down-to-earth multi-course omakase menu uses European, Japanese and Taiwanese techniques to create dishes that are homely but layered with flavours and textures. Highlights include stuffed Portobello mushroom, and marinated milkfish on koshihikari rice.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
11896;PASTi;Taiwan;Taipei;30 Zhongnan Street, Nangang District, Taipei, 115, Taiwan;25.05456;121.61516;91;false;false;Italian;The chef couple have a passion for Italy and have covered every wall with photos and maps of their favourite country. Seafood is big on the menu which changes every couple days to reflect availability. The no-frills food may not always be photogenic, but the quality and flavours more than make up for that. Try their grilled silverfish rolls stuffed with smoked cheese and pork scallopini. The zesty lemon jelly will transport you instantly to the Amalfi coast.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11897;Lin's Vegetable Lamb Hotpot;Taiwan;Taipei;327 Jilin Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.063854;121.530475;85;true;false;Hotpot;Lamb hotpot here differs from others thanks to its special soup base which is fragrant and nourishing – it’s made with shellfish, lamb bones, goji berries and ginger, plus mustard cabbage stems in winter or white radish in summer. Order an extra portion of sliced lamb belly or loin to be blanched in the soup. Lamb trotters braised in spiced marinade are also worth trying. Choose between the wood-clad dining room and al fresco seating.;Cash only,Valet parking;[]
11900;Bo Home;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;183-1, Cingnian 1st Road, Lingya District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6219103;120.3082843;76;false;false;Taiwanese;The founder opened Bo Home in 1969 to feed hungry workers away from home with nutritious comfort food – braised pork rice, and giant grouper soup. Over time the menu grew bigger, but the drool-worthy signature rice topped with amber, luscious diced pork remains the key draw. On top of that, order stir-fried squid in salted egg yolk sauce, or stir-fried whelks if you want variety. Open till midnight, so it’s perfect for late night snacks.;Air conditioning;[]
11901;Artbrosia;Taiwan;Taipei;6F, Palais de Chine Hotel, 3, Section 1, Chengde Road, Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0493305;121.5169633;87;true;false;Italian Contemporary;A fine dining concept from celebrated chef Massimiliano Musso, Artbrosia is helmed by his most-trusted aides who execute his culinary vision faithfully. The Piedmontese-inspired tasting menu pays homage to his granny’s comforting dishes, jazzed up by artful plating and the ingenious use of local ingredients. The dimly-lit room imparts understated luxury with a glass-clad wine cellar that houses a well-curated Italian collection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
11904;Eastern Castle Noodles;Taiwan;Tainan;235, Section 1, Dongmen Road, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9874208;120.2171727;19;true;false;Small eats;On the bustling Dongmen Traffic Circle, this simple shop has been serving stir-fried eel since opening its doors in 1970. Diners can specify if they want their eel in a glaze or not. The ‘dry’ version highlights the natural flavour of the fish with smoky wok hei and sweet and sour seasoning. E-fu noodles with stir-fried eel is a must for most regulars. Other specialities include stir-fried cuttlefish, and pork kidney cooked in sesame oil. Dishes are cooked-to-order.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11905;Isagi;Taiwan;Taichung;29 Cunzhong Street, West District, Taichung, 403, Taiwan;24.14109;120.66031;57;true;false;Japanese;No matter where you sit in this glass-clad space occupying two floors, a good view onto the lush Japanese garden is guaranteed. Three Japanese chefs, specialising in sashimi, hot dishes and desserts respectively, strive to recreate authentic Fukuoka flavours. The niigata rice steamed in a rustic claypot with assorted seasonal ingredients is the highlight of a meal here. Pre-order the itamae or chef's menu if you have a big appetite.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
11907;Shin Yeh Taiwanese Cuisine;Taiwan;Taipei;34-1 Shuangcheng Street, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.066534;121.524189;77;true;true;Taiwanese;A household name in Taiwanese cuisine since 1977, it specialises in authentic home-style cooking that seems simple, but requires scrupulous care – just try the egg omelette with dried radish, pan-seared pork liver and flatbread rolls. Even their almond tofu dessert is made by three chefs from scratch. This branch boasts 110 tables and is ideal for banquets and parties of all sizes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11908;A Fung's Harmony Cuisine;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;63 Jiangdu Street, Lingya District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6280689;120.3196909;81;true;false;Taiwanese;After more than 20 years away from home, Chef Lin is back in Kaohsiung, where he has opened this tiny gem with only four tables. His seasonal tasting menu champions a farm-to-table concept, showcasing produce from small local farms. Chef Lin declares his love of Taiwan, taking diners on a culinary voyage of the island as he highlights ethnic diversity in every dish. His wife, in charge of the front of house, explains the dishes in detail. Check social media for opening hours.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11909;LA Vie by thomas bühner;Taiwan;Taipei;1F, Noke Mall, 200 Lequn 3rd Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.08254;121.55429;75;true;true;European Contemporary;With muted greens, stone greys and gold accents, the high-ceilinged room in a recently built shopping mall is a masterclass of understated modern elegance. LA Vie is managed by German chef Bühner and local investors, while the kitchen is helmed by a Hongkong chef. The single prix-fixe menu showcases refined dishes underscored by European technique but showing strong Japanese influences. Diners can watch the chefs at work through the picture window.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11910;Bistro Alley;Taiwan;Tainan;47, Lane 115, Dungrung Street, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.989052;120.2157538;75;false;false;European Contemporary;The owner-chef used to work in Taipei and Australia but chose to settle down in his wife’s hometown, where he opened this cosy bistro that boasts a relaxed vibe. There is no paper menu – the day’s offerings are written on a blackboard. Signatures like fish carpaccio, and scrambled eggs with truffles are underpinned by Italian and Mediterranean techniques. Ask the maître d’ (owner’s wife) about the wine selection and catch of the day.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
11911;PI;Taiwan;Taichung;2F, 373 Dajin Street, Nantun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1495497;120.6512652;69;false;false;European Contemporary;The room exudes a relaxed vibe with its faux-industrial décor, semi-open kitchen and full-length windows. The owner named it Pi as a circle with no beginning or end is a good metaphor for the boundless possibilities in cooking. The head chef has worked in some prestigious kitchens in Taiwan, and his 6-course prix-fixe menu offers excellent value, featuring novel creations in European traditions, and one speciality from the charcoal grill.;Air conditioning;[]
11912;Hello VietNam;Taiwan;Taichung;92 Chenggong Road, Central District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1399064;120.6840852;54;false;true;Vietnamese;This cheerful restaurant is run by its Vietnamese owner. The menu tips towards the Northern end of her home country, and cilantro is used sparingly to cater to local taste. The speciality bun dau mam tom consists of rice noodle squares, pork intestines, pork feet, blood sausage, deep-fried tofu and leafy greens, alongside fermented shrimp paste, or a fish sauce dip. Nem ran (fried spring rolls) and pork skewers are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11913;Silks House;Taiwan;Taipei;3F, Regent Hotel, 3, Lane 39, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.054231;121.524194;66;true;false;Cantonese;Chinese calligraphy etched on glass screens is the perfect foil to the elegant cuisine. The Hong Kong head chef has over 30 years of Cantonese cooking under his belt. In addition to his specialty barbecue meats, seafood also features prominently. Xishi soup rice sees king crab blanched in a golden lobster stock tableside before crispy deep-fried rice is sprinkled on top. For dim sum, try the flaky puff pastry with a savoury radish filling.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11914;Longtail;Taiwan;Taipei;174, Section 2, Dunhua South Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0239343;121.5483519;56;false;false;Innovative;The menu changes every three months and features local seasonal produce alongside the finest ingredients from around the world. Specialities include uni on crispy rice, pork chop in sukiyaki sauce, and Kaya French toast with espresso ice cream. Opt for the seasonal Experience menu to experience the complete vision of the chef. Cocktail pairings are also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11915;Inflorescence;Taiwan;Taichung;111, Section 1, Zhongxingling Street, Xinshe District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.2092675;120.7851268;63;false;false;Japanese;On a mountainside nearly 500 metres above sea level, this Zen-inspired establishment was founded 10 years ago and opened by a renowned restaurant group. The elegant room is nestled on meticulously manicured ground that spans over 3,000 square metres. Only one 10-course omakase menu is offered, featuring tea tasting rituals and novel creations based on kaiseki traditions. Seasoning is precise and restrained for natural flavours to come through.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
11916;le beaujour;Taiwan;Taipei;118, Section 2, Nanjing East Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.0518229;121.5327167;77;true;true;French Contemporary;Picture a sleek, stylish dining room decked in white and light grey and a relaxing, eclectic soundtrack that rather defies classification. Consultant celebrity chef Lanshu Chen worked closely with Chef Pili Chiang, an alumnus of the Joël Robuchon Group, on the à la carte weekday dishes, as well as the weekend tasting menu. The culinary focus offers a new spin on French classics, with a lighter taste and a deft, ethereal touch.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11917;Feng No Seafood;Taiwan;Tainan;146-10 Changshali, Jiangjyun District, Tainan, Taiwan;23.2137062;120.1051764;20;true;false;Seafood;In the past 10 or so years, nearly every car on the way to Jiangjun Fishing Harbour stops here to try its fresh catch at great prices. Pick your critters from the fridge and ask the server for the best way to prepare them. The sizzling three-cup marbled eel is its speciality, exuding heady aromas and savoury umami. A great spot for lunch on your trip to Qinkunshen Salt Fields or Mashagou 3D Mural Village. Reservations on holidays are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
11918;Robin's Teppanyaki;Taiwan;Taipei;2F, Regent Hotel, 3, Lane 39, Section 2, Zhongshan North Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.054231;121.524194;31;false;true;Teppanyaki;One of the best known teppanyaki places in town, named after a long-serving maître d’, enjoys an enthusiastic local following. The show-stopping teppan tricks are something to behold, but they don’t outshine the perfectly cooked seafood, premium steaks from the U. S. , or the Wagyu from Japan and Australia. The six-course dinner unfolds according to your pace as experienced chefs time things just right. An excellent wine list also features.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
11919;Thai & Thai;Taiwan;Taipei;5F, THE ARCADE, 158 Dunhua North Road, Songshan District, Taipei, 105, Taiwan;25.055589;121.548152;38;false;false;Thai;Situated in the elegant mall behind the Mandarin Oriental, this restaurant have served authentic Thai food in Taipei for many years. It matches its surroundings by having a beautifully appointed interior complete with an impressive sculpture. The experienced Thai chef delivers what Thai food is renowned for on all fronts, alongside charming service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11920;Wenpapa Goose;Taiwan;Tainan;274, Section 3, Simen Road, North District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.99162;120.18503;83;false;false;Small eats;The goose-themed menu is the handiwork of an owner-chef who has over 20 years of experience with the bird. He opened his own joint in 2008 and moved to this location in 2018. His signature saltwater goose uses 90- to 100-day-old birds, precisely blanched in brine, left to cool and boasting juicy flesh. Classic goose meat rice is paired with braised bamboo shoots and scallion goose oil sauce for a lovely crispy crunch and deep aromas.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11922;Chef Ah-Hsi's Old Time Restaurant;Taiwan;Taichung;706, Section 2, Zhongqing Road, Beitun District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1847432;120.6649726;53;true;false;Taiwanese;Chef Ah Hsi's career in Taiwanese cooking spans more than 30 years. His family used to farm geese, which explains his skills in butchering and cooking geese. As opposed to poaching the birds in brine as most Taiwanese do, he slow roasts them in a barrel before smoking them with cane sugar. His signature roast goose boasts juicy flesh and smoky aromas. The duck sausage is meaty and tender without the greasiness of its pork counterpart.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11923;enPure;Taiwan;Taichung;33, Alley 7, Lane 86, Jiangxing Road, North District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1606258;120.687517;93;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Another venture by the owner of a famous tea parlour, enPure is tucked away in a quiet alley. Diners are escorted through the lush garden into the minimalist space done out in muted tones of brick red and cool grey. The head chef was once an interior designer and her tasting menu seduces with delicate elegance, finessed by modern techniques. Both oenophiles and teetotallers are catered to, with astute wine/tea pairings to complement the food.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11924;Jarana;Taiwan;Taipei;8, Alley 46, Lane 553, Section 4, Zhongxiao East Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0441409;121.5632126;26;false;true;Spanish;Nestled in serene grounds near Songshan Cultural and Creative Park, this bustling joint is the brainchild of a Madrilenian chef. The small menu is heavy on Spanish classics, encompassing the essence of the cuisine and the chef’s experience spanning over two decades. Try oreja a la plancha, and fideuà with foie gras. The chef can tailor a paella or fideuà to your liking if you pre-order a week ahead. Round it out with his signature 5-cheese cheesecake.;Air conditioning;[]
11925;Tain Chu;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;174 Jhong Dong Street, Sinsing District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6332227;120.3140796;81;true;false;Sichuan, Taiwanese;Since 1971, the same couple has owned this nostalgic, elegant space clad in warm walnut wood. The wife helms the kitchen, and her Sichuanese and Taiwanese dishes, as well as original creations inspired by her travels have attracted a loyal following. Apart from the main menu, check out the daily specials – they never disappoint. Certain painstakingly prepared items need to be pre-ordered, and are big enough for a few people to share.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11926;Sushi Touryuumon;Taiwan;Taipei;16, Alley 27, Lane 216, Zhongxiao East Road, Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.04067;121.55211;32;true;true;Sushi;When Sushi Amamoto became off-limits for non-members, Chef Amamoto opened this offshoot in 2022 so that all food lovers could experience his culinary vision. Run by his protégés, Sushi Touryuumon uses the freshest catch mostly from Fukuoka, Japan, alongside sushi rice from Hualian, Taiwan. The chef’s signatures like crispy deep-fried eel, kombu saba nigiri, and soufflé tamagoyaki made with free-range chicken eggs are also available. Book ahead online.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
11927;MU;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;128 Fuheng 1st Road, Sinsing District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6293776;120.3094313;90;true;true;Innovative;The same owner couple has been running this snug, homely restaurant for 10 years, but the muted, monochromatic room doesn’t feel a bit dated. The 10-course tasting menu changes every 6 weeks, inspired by Taiwanese, Hakka and aboriginal recipes and demonstrates a flair for local Chinese herbs and spices. Most dishes are cooked over charcoal and the reduced sauces are free of starch. Try the chargrilled, smoked beef short ribs as a main dish.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11928;White Gourd and Fat Person;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;12, Lane 784, Yingde Street, Cianjhen District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6146747;120.3188634;84;false;true;Taiwanese;Short, plus-sized people are affectionately called winter melon (a.k.a. white gourd) in Chinese. The humorous owner-chef named his restaurant after his nicknames and decorated it like someone’s home straight out of 1970s sitcoms. The homely feel works perfectly with the family-style dishes. There is no menu – solo diners can only order the braised pork belly set, while parties of two or more are served 4 or 5 courses omakase-style.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
11931;Lao Tseng Lamb;Taiwan;Tainan;131, Section 2, Minzu Road, West Central District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.99487;120.20782;28;false;false;Small eats;Within walking distance from Tainan train station, Lao Tseng has been serving simple lamb dishes at frugal prices for half a century and, for that, they use Australian lamb. The menu is easy to navigate – either sliced lamb or lamb ribs in one of the three broths, namely sesame oil soup, clear broth or herbal stock. Try also their stir-fried lamb with kale in a light bean sauce with a sweet aftertaste – perfect with steamed rice.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11933;Peng Lai;Taiwan;Taipei;238 Zhonghe Street, Beitou District, Taipei, 112, Taiwan;25.139451;121.501449;56;true;true;Taiwanese;This simple shop is famous for its pork ribs that are marinated for 20 hours before being deep-fried until crispy on the outside and tender on the inside. Another favourite is ‘Jadeite tofu’ – shrimp, ham, coriander and tofu wrapped up in fried tofu skin. Crabmeat and baby oyster thick soup, and whelk and squid soup with leeks are the other recipes from a bygone era that are now seldom found elsewhere.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11934;Ephernité;Taiwan;Taipei;233, Section 2, Anhe Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.0251526;121.5503531;72;false;true;French Contemporary;The décor seamlessly blends faux-industrial style with minimalist chic. Owned and run by a couple who once lived in France, it champions a farm-to-table concept using fresh produce grown on the fringes of the city. The owner-chef honed her skills at world famous L’Astrance so classic French techniques underpin all her ambitious creations – the vegetable terrine made daily stands out. You can also pre-order the 9-course seasonal menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
11936;Three Wheels;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;25, Alley 296, Bade Road, Fengshan District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6396024;120.35531;16;false;false;Small eats;From a tricycle food cart in 1961, the third-generation family business has transformed itself into a no-frills booth, open from noon till dusk. This popular venue for Taiwan-style afternoon snacks is a stickler for tradition. The best-selling chargrilled pork sausage in intestine skin is mildly laced with five spices and sorghum wine. Fried shallot and peanuts give sticky rice sausage extra aromas, best enjoyed with the hearty sparerib soup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
11937;the FRONT HOUSE;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;132 Sianjheng Road, Lingya District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.6363896;120.3236163;20;false;true;Innovative;A palette of warm wood and soft neutral shades, soothing curves and rich textures set the scene. The veteran chef-manager has over 20 years of fine dining experience and his tasting menu relates his life and travels in Europe, Asia and the Americas. His clever use of local produce like starfruit, pickled cabbage and betel leaves adds a unique twist. A few private upstairs’ rooms overlooking a green balcony are ideal for small parties.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11938;Hosu;Taiwan;Taipei;17, Alley 20, Lane 300, Section 4, Ren’ai Road, Da’an District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0439036;121.5500623;80;false;false;Taiwanese contemporary;The rustic chic room is adorned by dried flowers, antiques and cast iron furniture, paying homage to Taiwan’s country life of yesteryear. The owner-chef pledges his love to his homeland on the menu, making reference to the seasonal changes in Taiwan’s mountains, seas, rivers and plains. Dishes pivot around his childhood memories using mostly produce from sustainable sources. Chargrilling techniques are deployed prominently and to great effect.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11939;Chinese Cuisine;Taiwan;Taipei;Grand View Resort Beitou, 30 Youya Road, Beitou District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.1376962;121.5150766;90;false;true;Taiwanese;Breath-taking mountain views and hot spring baths aside, the food alone is reason enough to visit this resort. The head chef has been honing his skills for over 10 years and his set menus and à la carte choices are nothing short of impressive, such as his abalone and pork tendon in a three-cup sauce steeped in deep savoury flavours. The complimentary Taiwanese tea is a nice touch. Check out the day-trip hot spring deals with meal options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
11940;Clover;Taiwan;Taipei;4F, Bellavita, 28 Songren Road, Xinyi District, Taipei, 110, Taiwan;25.0395299;121.5674925;75;true;false;French Contemporary;Renowned chef Jean-François Piège’s first venture outside of France is a collaborative effort with the upmarket department store Bellavita. The greatest hits from Chef Piège’s four restaurants in France are available à la carte and on the season-driven tasting menu. Local ingredients are deftly crafted in signature dishes like carbonara of wild squid where shredded squid is used in place of pasta, or lobster stewed in whole pumpkin with a seashell jus.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11941;Wang Jia Smoked Lamb;Taiwan;Tainan;34 Wushulin, Longci District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9588834;120.3692938;59;true;true;Taiwanese;On the outskirts of the city lies this rustic open-air restaurant on a mountain. Expansive views of green rolling hills complement the intoxicating smell of meat cooked in the wild. The signature smoked lamb is slow-cooked with rice wine and Chinese herbs in cooking pits for 24 hours, boasting a dark rich broth that is considered a health tonic. Wild greens and game meats, such as stir-fried wild boar, are also recommended. Book ahead on weekends.;Car park,Cash only;[]
11942;The Dragon;Taiwan;Taipei;B1, Sheraton Grand Hotel, 12, Section 1, Zhongxiao East Road, Zhongzheng District, Taipei, 100, Taiwan;25.044601;121.521862;73;false;false;Cantonese;Pre-booking is recommended at this spacious restaurant boasting a contemporary décor, with Chinese details, tan wood finishes and comfy chairs, which add to the feeling of serenity. The kitchen is run by experienced chefs specialising in Cantonese cuisine. Signature dishes include stir-fried pork tendons in XO sauce, crispy barbecued pork, roasted baby duck (pre-order needed) and Cantonese-style Peking duck (in strictly limited quantities).;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11944;Danny's Steakhouse;Taiwan;Taipei;58 Lequn 3rd Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.0824839;121.552909;74;true;true;Steakhouse;Known as Taiwan's "Godfather of Steaks", owner Danny has been cooking meat for over 40 years. He no longer helms the kitchen, but the young head chef is following in his footsteps. The set menus featuring US prime cuts and Japanese and Australian Wagyu beef are good value. The meat is grilled to perfection over lychee wood and rested properly before being served. The USDA prime rib eye is dry-aged in-house for 14 days for intense flavour and tenderness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
11946;Hara Peko;Taiwan;Tainan;13, Lane 81, Section 2, Yongfu Road, West Central, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9936144;120.2004718;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The owner-chef received classic French training and worked for a time in Japan. With this joint in the artsy enclave known as Snail Alley, he champions a unique take on "French-influenced Nippon cuisine". The single set menu changes once a month, with a choice of main from two or three options. Instead of red and white, the wine list features an array of sake from Kyushu, which the owner-chef finds matching his culinary style to a tee.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
11947;Chuan Mu Yuan;Taiwan;Taipei;120, Section 2, Chengde Road, Datong District, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0588662;121.5179744;70;false;false;Dim Sum;Tucked down a little alley, this shop always attracts a long queue of office workers and shoppers at peak hours. Behind the glass wall by the entrance, chefs are busy making dim sum, dumplings and noodles to keep pace with the piling orders. Regulars adore their beef pancake roll and red bean paste pancake that are golden and crispy. Moo-shu fried noodles made with freshly made knife-cut noodles are also popular.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11948;Di Yi Ding;Taiwan;Tainan;1, Lane 161, Section 2, Dongmen Road, East District, Tainan, Taiwan;22.9854433;120.2232979;72;false;false;Seafood;This mansion, dating from the 1960s, has been restored to its former glory. The chef served Taiwanese seafood classics, with omakase menus offered at three price points, typically starting with sashimi and ending with starch like bi tai bak in pumpkin sauce. For mains, first-timers usually get crab or lobster, but the chef is happy to entertain requests. BYOB if you fancy drinks other than beer. Reservations are mandatory and it’s cash only.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
11950;N°168 Prime Steakhouse (Zhongshan);Taiwan;Taipei;4F, Grand Victoria Hotel, 168 Jingye 4th Road, Zhongshan District, Taipei, 104, Taiwan;25.0841413;121.5588621;25;true;true;Steakhouse;The dining room boasts an ultramarine colour scheme dotted by oak logs and panels. Top-quality U.S. Kobe ribeye, Australian grade 9+ and Japanese Miyazaki A5 Wagyu are grilled to perfection in an oak wood-fired oven imbuing steaks with a lovely smokiness. The set menu with starter, soup, main and dessert represents good value. Service is smooth, prompt and friendly and the open kitchen keeps your eyes entertained.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11951;Mume;Taiwan;Taipei;28 Siwei Road, Da'an District, Taipei, 106, Taiwan;25.036278;121.548015;86;true;true;European Contemporary;In line with its name (the Latin word for ‘plum blossom’), the relaxed and friendly MUME generously garnishes dishes with fresh herbs and flowers – in somewhat stark contrast to the dimly-lit faux-industrial interior of the restaurant itself. On the menu, seasonal Taiwanese ingredients are melded with Nordic influences and modern techniques are used effectively to create dishes that provide contrasts in tastes and textures.;Air conditioning;[]
11952;3927;Taiwan;Taipei;14, Lane 101, Section 4, Zhongxiao East Road, Taipei, Taiwan;25.0422466;121.5479555;66;true;true;Taiwanese;3927 reimagines traditional Taiwanese food in a bold, modern and unconventional way. The head chef has extensive experience in Taiwanese cooking and has worked overseas. He draws on globally sourced produce and techniques from various cuisines to create new flavours that tap into diners' collective memories. The mixologists are more than happy to stir up a concoction to your liking.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11953;Zai Lai;Taiwan;Taichung;231, Section 1, Xiang Shang Road, West District, Taichung, Taiwan;24.1466038;120.6597164;33;true;true;Small eats;Just a stone's throw from the hipster neighbourhood known as Shen Ji New Village, this shop is named after the variety of rice used to make wa gui, or steamed bowl rice cake. White wa gui (as opposed to Tainan's black version) is served at room temperature to accentuate the rice aromas and springy texture. Feel free to top with spicy dried radish or garlic sauce for extra flavours. Round off your meal with brown sugar wa gui and milkette.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Terrace;[]
11955;Chang Sheng 29;Taiwan;Kaohsiung;3 Hexi Road, Yancheng District, Kaohsiung, Taiwan;22.621486;120.2897959;56;true;false;Taiwanese;This restaurant, renowned for its home-style Taiwanese cooking, moved shop in 2024. The dining room is now spread over two levels and features a wood-rich space adorned in the owner’s collection of vintage crockery. The upper level commands unobstructed views of Love River. Two omakase menus are on offer and the dishes change daily depending on availability. Best sellers include deep-fried pork belly marinated in red rice wine lees and fish soup in a claypot.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
11956;Trattoria Felino;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 3&4, GF, Pao Yip Building, 1-7 Ship Street, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.276755;114.1708063;22;true;false;Italian;The chef hails from Naples and his trattoria serves culinary gems from the Italian city, including his grandma's recipes. Start with the carbonara egg, aerated egg yolk with guanciale and pecorino in an eggcup on a bed of corn kernels. Then move on to the house-made pasta, which embodies the ethos of the trattoria. The tagliatelle with Wagyu beef ragout strikes the perfect balance between meaty and tangy. Book well ahead to secure a table.;Air conditioning;[]
11957;Zuicho;;Macau;Shop 302, 3F, The Karl Lagerfeld, Grand Lisboa Palace Resort, Rua do Tiro, Cotai, Macau;22.1442132;113.5753495;51;true;true;Japanese;Just like its namesake in Hong Kong, Zuicho specialises in kappo cuisine. With an illustrious career spanning over 30 years, chef Kinomoto rolls out three omakase menus that show attention to detail, meticulous care and exceptional skill. All the ingredients are flown in from Japan, like Hokkaido bafun uni and tuna belly in the hand roll, as well as Satsuma A5 Wagyu from Kagoshima – the tenderloin is deep-fried and sirloin is used in sukiyaki.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
11958;Prince and the Peacock;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;2F, The Magistracy, Tai Kwun, 1 Arbuthnot Road, Central, Hong Kong;22.2812647;114.1545079;88;true;true;Indian;Chef Palash Mitra opened this lavish restaurant in a prison and police station-turned arts complex. Fit for royalty, the interior is matched by a menu inspired by the royal kitchens dotted around India. The chef collects lost recipes as he travels, recreating them as sharing plates for Hong Kong audience. Try his nalli gosht biryani – aged basmati with lamb shank and short ribs, plus minty raita to cut through the richness.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11959;Carna by Dario Cecchini;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;39F, Mondrian, 8A Hart Avenue, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.297653;114.174571;16;true;false;Steakhouse;The swanky room creates a Tuscan vibe with gracious arches and exquisite stained glass. It also commands breathtaking harbour views visible from almost every table. The Italian steakhouse, brainchild of the famous butcher Dario Cecchini, champions a nose-to-tail concept with a focus on beef from Italy, Australia, the U.S., Japan and Ireland. Premium U.S. Wagyu steaks stand out in particular. The Italian wine list practically covers the entire country.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11960;Lulu Baobao;;Hong Kong;Shop 102, 1F, Metro South Tower 2, 39 Wong Chuk Hang Road, Wong Chuk Hang, Hong Kong;22.2488838;114.1663974;86;false;true;Dim Sum;With custom-made crockery and retro marquetry on the walls and tables, the space feels stylish and spacious. Noodles and buns are handmade à la minute in the glass-clad kitchen, so expect a wait during peak hours. Try their noodles in "gentle" scallion oil – bouncy noodles dressed in the perfect amount of infused oil. The xiao long bao are also exquisitely made with beautiful pleats and soupy pork filling. The combo sets are great value.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
11961;Bánh Mì Nếm;;Hong Kong;GF, 247-249 Queen's Road East, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2743698;114.1740595;99;false;true;Street Food;This takeout-only shop specialises in Vietnamese sandwiches, alongside rice noodles and coffee. The signature bánh mì dặc biệt features Vietnamese char siu, sausage and pâté in a baguette. Pickled radish and chilli add extra zing.;;[]
11963;Freia;France;Nantes;22 boulevard de Berlin, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2166676;-1.5361316;82;false;false;Creative;This greenhouse with timber arches devoted to the goddess Freia is perched on top of a contemporary building. It is the perfect place to grow a garden of aromatic herbs and berries and to admire the panoramic view of Nantes. After the success of Vacarme, Sarah Mainguy crafts poetic and creative cuisine, mainly plant based and scattered with Scandinavian and Asian touches. Each dish is a treasure trove of brainwaves and delicious sauces – cases in point being the white asparagus with a vegetable seaweed XO sauce, or periwinkles with crisp green peas, topped with a glazed gwell snow.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
11965;Nuance;France;Bayonne;23 rue des Cordeliers, Bayonne, 64100, France;43.4892875;-1.4731919;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Having worked at Choko Ona in Espelette, Brice Goeuriot and Margaux Le Baillif have a taste for nuance, as reflected in their refined interior decorated with natural materials by Basque artisans. The result is on point – an upscale and comfortable setting with a warm and friendly vibe. A lot of work has gone into sourcing produce from small-scale organic farmers and producers from the Landes and Basque regions, and the chef's blind menu is stacked with complex dishes, in which ingredients are often prepared in several guises (eg lamb leg, chop and shoulder confit). Aromatic plants and herbs are skilfully used in a variety of ways: oxalis flower and sea fennel sorbet, wild garlic sabayon, nasturtium extraction. Infinitely delicate cuisine.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11966;Chez Jeannette;France;Flassans-sur-Issole;1204 chemin de la Commanderie de Peyrassol, Flassans-sur-Issole, 83340, France;43.37893;6.26346;40;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This highly sought-after restaurant is set amid a Provençal vineyard, a former Knights Templar commandery and a thousand-year-old site where Roman amphorae have been unearthed. The owner also has his collection of contemporary sculptures on display. The kitchen is the domain of Vivien Rouleaud (formerly at Restaurant Anne-Sophie Pic) and pastry chef Victor Lorente (who has worked with Thierry Marx). John Dory, braised sucrine lettuce tartlet, bouillabaisse jus made with olive oil from the estate and, for dessert, a duo of rhubarb and strawberry, showcase a refined take on Mediterranean cuisine that also makes use of vegetables from their kitchen garden. Looking out over the ancient vines, the idyllic terrace is shaded by a lime tree and a holm oak.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
11967;L'Instinct;France;Saumur;42 rue du Maréchal-Leclerc, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2562812;-0.0825544;57;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In his aptly named contemporary restaurant, chef Romain Bersan shows a distinct talent for cooking up modern cuisine. Spices make a welcome appearance, perfectly dosed with a sure hand (a case in point being the poultry jus elevated with smoked paprika and sake). Vegetarians can rest assured that the chef also caters to their dietary requirements. His delicious starter of vitello tonnato was nothing short of an escapade to Italy.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11970;Arbane;France;Reims;7 rue Noël, Reims, 51100, France;49.2573961;4.0272938;22;true;true;Creative;After many years at Le Parc des Crayères, ‘Meilleur Ouvrier de France’ Philippe Mille has opened his own restaurant in this elegant abode dating back to 1874. In a contemporary interior done out in natural shades and strewn with references to the vineyards of Champagne, the chef from Sarthe pursues a culinary vision that is rooted in the Champagne terroir in his open kitchen. He cooks over vine branches, draws inspiration from the seven grape varieties (including Arbane), adding the odd fine seafood ingredient (monkfish, turbot, lobster etc). The champagne list is naturally of interest, and the plush lounge upstairs is adorned with a sculpture by a famous Reims-based master glassmaker.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11971;La Ferme Ilharregui Baita;France;Urrugne;70 chemin de Apezerreka, Urrugne, 64122, France;43.3611849;-1.7225314;18;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This 17C former farmhouse has been tastefully renovated both inside and out and now accommodates a contemporary Basque inn. Three set menus that focus on the Basque terroir set the tone: the first revolves around pulses, the second is based on seafood and the third showcases local ingredients. The colourful dishes taste as good as they look, a case in point being the lamb with Tarbais beans and smoked aubergine caviar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11973;Monique;France;Calvisson;1 ter impasse du Charron, Calvisson, 30420, France;43.7845468;4.1927965;98;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Julien Caligo, previously co-executive chef at Duende (Nîmes), has returned to his natural environment – namely his native Vaunage, a plain surrounded by hills, between Nîmes and Montpellier. The premises, originally a farm building, now accommodate this beautiful interior with white walls, exposed stonework and refined light wood furniture – perfect for a restaurant that is a homage to the chef's grandmother, who taught him the fundamentals of cooking. The carte blanche menu is a masterclass in technical skill, a shining example of which is the daring fusion of calf intestine and red mullet, while the Baron des Cévennes pork is showcased by a spicy black pudding sauce. The culinary innovation at work here is propelled by the finest local ingredients, fresh from the land (or sea).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
11976;Le Boïdicou;France;Thonac;27 route des Eyzies, Thonac, 24290, France;45.0224237;1.1169032;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the "Périgord Noir" area of the Dordogne, this boïdicou (Occitan for the basket you take to market) embodies authentic, seasonal cuisine in all its simplicity. Run by two enthusiastic young chefs, the restaurant favours fresh, top-notch local ingredients, most of which are sourced within a 50km radius. The lunch menu changes every week, adapting to what local suppliers have to offer. In the evening, there's a more elaborate surprise set menu. Relaxed atmosphere and efficient service.;;[]
11978;JU - Maison de Cuisine;France;Bonnieux;2 rue Lucien-Blanc, Bonnieux, 84480, France;43.8231711;5.3065565;71;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Julien Allano (La Mirande, Le Clair de la Plume) chose to go it alone and set up shop in this beautiful traditional building in the heart of the village. In an interior with exposed stonework, the chef can be seen at work behind a wooden counter. Meanwhile, guests are seated on handcrafted furnishings made of untreated walnut wood – a decor that oozes style. The carte blanche menu, which is divided into several sections, reflects the season from day to day. Heirloom varieties of wheat, peanuts from Malataverne, green beans from a neighbouring farm and pigeon from Sarrians are just some of the carefully sourced local ingredients used to create harmonious, delicate cuisine, rife with the flavours of the South of France, about which the chef is genuinely passionate. The "Cheese Experience" is held in a huge, superb vaulted cellar dating back to the 13C.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
11979;L'Auberge d'Allex;France;Allex;Montée de l'Ancien-Hôpital, Allex, 26400, France;44.7644513;4.9159041;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Between Valence and Montélimar, this erstwhile village inn is continuing its vocation as an eatery thanks to a young couple who have turned it into a cosy and inviting bistro-style restaurant with a smattering of contemporary decorative touches. The food, too, is in a bistro vein – think simple, contemporary cuisine designed for the modern palate. The fillet of hake with citrus sauce, red cabbage and butternut takes no prisoners.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11981;Animae;USA;San Diego;969 Pacific Hwy., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7155757;-117.1708845;75;true;false;Asian;It's smack dab in the heart of San Diego's power scene, located on the ground floor of the Pacific Gate by Bosa in the Embarcadero Marina, so it comes as no surprise that Animae is sexy and scene-y. This bastion of glamour attracts a who's who of trendy diners who come here largely to be seen—attention seekers should ask for the cushy round booths in the center of it all. Luxe details abound, with thick velvet curtains and art deco elegance, but the Asian fusion plates are on pace with the setting and most dishes are meant to be shared. The coal-fired octopus skewer with shishito peppers, basil aïoli and bacon is a reliable pick, while the chef's rendition of glazed black cod with tatsoi , sunflower dashi and shimeji mushrooms is a total crowd-pleaser.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11982;Solare;USA;San Diego;2820 Roosevelt Rd., San Diego, 92106, USA;32.737253;-117.213925;94;true;true;Italian, Tuscan;It’s just steps from the Liberty Public Market in the NTC Promenade, while inside, the vibe is homey, welcoming and relaxed, splashed with plenty of colorful fabrics and wood fixtures. The cooking is rustic and hearty, drawing on Italian-American and Southern Italian traditions. House-made pasta is a specialty, as in a lasagna al forno made with tender veal and beef meatballs and vibrant marinara, or spinach and ricotta ravioli with a sauce of sage, butter and Grana Padano. Pizzas, like pear and gorgonzola or fennel sausage with roasted peppers, emerge from a 900° wood-fired oven with blistered crusts. Weekly specials highlight fish such as branzino sauteed in a lemon garlic sauce with arugula salad and seared long-stemmed Italian artichokes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11985;Stella;USA;West Hollywood;8899 Beverly Blvd., West Hollywood, 90048, USA;34.0774;-118.38606;59;false;false;Italian;Italian food with local California products is the promise at Stella, where a two-story dining room has an Art Deco flair, and the chef's counter offers a mesmerizing look at live-fire cooking.Don't miss the lardo di Colonanta, a dish of thinly sliced and meltingly soft lardo paired with strawberries, razor-thin caciocavello cheese, and a balsamic amaro. Su Filindeu is an impressive pasta dish with hand-stretched noodles cooked in bone broth accompanied by braised lamb neck and pecorino dolce. Other sure bets include Iberico pork pluma with porchetta spices, saba lacquer, and hens yolk cooked over the live fire, or opt for a hand-made pizza. Finally, cassata Sicilliana is a delicious dessert to cap off the meal.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
11986;La Costanera;USA;Half Moon Bay;260 Capistrano Rd., Half Moon Bay, 94019, USA;37.5042731;-122.4825404;67;false;true;Peruvian, Latin American;Where else can you stroll in after a day at the beach and get a delicious Peruvian meal? La Costanera, nestled within the darling coastal town of Half Moon Bay, of course! Traditional and modern art abound, but it's the boldly flavored plates from Chef Carlos Altamirano and his team that garner attention. Palta rellena, which fills half an avocado with roasted chicken chicharrones and lime-infused mayonnaise, is a fun and light-hearted interpretation of the dish. Cebice pescado marinated in aji rocoto leche de tigre is both tangy and kicky, while arroz con mariscos is a savory and satisfying dish tucked with plenty of seafood. Be sure to sample the creative cocktails. Alternatively, try a delicious and refreshing chicha morada.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11988;Troubadour;USA;Healdsburg;381 Healdsburg Ave., Healdsburg, 95448, USA;38.6116465;-122.8710511;54;false;true;French, Californian;Owners Melissa Yanc and Sean McGaughey worked together at SingleThread (as a baker and sous-chef, respectively), but the married couple left fine dining to forge their own path—though they haven’t strayed too far. This winsome little spot is a sandwich shop and bakery by day (the pair also run popular nearby Quail and Condor), but the creative itch led them to offer an intriguing prix fixe menu at night, interpreting classic French cuisine through a contemporary California lens. Served on gorgeous antique plates that look as though they might have been pillaged from the tomb of Escoffier, the likes of asparagus chartreuse with trout roe and halibut à la Normande with lobster mousseline are especially becoming, and the charming service doesn’t hurt either.;;[]
11990;Diavola;USA;Geyserville;21021 Geyserville Ave., Geyserville, 95441, USA;38.7063619;-122.9041561;93;true;true;Italian, Pizza;Its home in downtown Geyserville has a Wild West appeal, and the interior, styled with vintage film posters and antique tools, has a playful yet smart vibe. Diavola is certainly one of the most popular spots for miles—within minutes of opening, it's always a full house.The crowds are here for pizzas, like the signature combo of spicy meatballs, red peppers, provolone, pine nuts and raisins or the smoked pork belly, goat cheese and scallion, perhaps. Top-notch house ingredients include salumi, lardo and cured olives. But, that’s not to count out their pastas, including linguine tossed with baby octopus, bone marrow, zucchini and bottarga. Finish with their chocolate pistachio semifreddo paired with a Blue Bottle espresso.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11991;Tiya;USA;San Francisco;3213 Scott St., San Francisco, 94123, USA;37.7994785;-122.4411872;49;true;false;Indian, Contemporary;Brothers Sujan and Pujan Sarkar combine their talents as co-chefs at this boutique space at the edge of Cow Hollow. Their cooking deploys seasonal produce like squash blossoms, artichokes, and ramps to lend a Californian edge to an intriguing contemporary take on Indian cuisine. Both a la carte and tasting options give equal billing to vegetarian dishes and feature lively textures, whether it’s tender, keema-style jackfruit with crunchy potato, or an eggless take on a bhurji roll, made with paneer and crispy kataifi. The elegant room adds an additional layer of sophistication, down to a well-appointed bar, which offers unique cocktails named in honor of San Francisco neighborhoods.;;[]
11992;Burdell;USA;Oakland;4640 Telegraph Ave., Oakland, 94609, USA;37.8341828;-122.2630921;40;false;false;American, Contemporary;Chef Geoff Davis named this nostalgic, homy Temescal spot after his grandmother, whose cooking informs his own fresh personal take on soul food. The small menu is a blend of staples like collard greens and fried chicken (though these are tweaked with the addition of berbere and pickle brine, respectively), novelties like an appetizer of chicken liver mousse with cornmeal waffle, and more broadly contemporary, Southern-inflected fare like a halibut crudo with buttermilk and grapefruit, or dry-aged duck with cherry "drippings" and dirty rice. Desserts follow a similar style, like strawberry shortcake with strawberry rhubarb jam and sorghum whipped cream. A particularly thoughtful wine list offers a wealth of options for afficionados, and who doesn’t love fried chicken with champagne?;Interesting wine list;[]
11993;Danbi;USA;Los Angeles;3465 W. 6th St., Ste. 90-100, Los Angeles, 90020, USA;34.063778;-118.297274;76;true;true;Korean;Danbi sports a sleek, modern dining room with an industrial feel (think concrete floors, hanging plants, and dark wood tables) as well as a large bar for bites and sips like their "kimchi mule." Chef Lareine Ko's streamlined menu pops with large, shareable plates. The hit list includes  mushroom bibimbap with fresh vegetables, as well as a crispy scallop pancake accompanied by a creamy mentaiko sauce. Wagyu Zabuton, cooked over charcoal and served on a hot cast iron skillet over a bed of grilled onions, is a solid winner. End the meal with one of Chef Isabell Manibusan's pastries—perhaps the almost-nostalgic banana milk cloud with brûléed meringue and banana milk crème anglaise, or the Mont Halla, a Korean twist on a Mont Blanc.;Air conditioning;[]
11994;MARKET Restaurant + Bar;USA;Del Mar;3702 Via De La Valle, Del Mar, 92014, USA;32.982616;-117.23147;89;true;false;International;Chef/owner Carl Schroeder is a La Jolla native with an encyclopedic knowledge of the region’s bounty. He’s been celebrating every locally sourced ingredient for over a decade now in this kitchen, and his repertoire of creative cooking continues to draw patrons for both special occasions as well as date night. The dark and seductive décor manages to be elegant without a hint of pretense, but one glance at the parking lot and you know that this spot is favored by a moneyed lot.Sushi is well-loved here, but it would be a shame to miss the chef’s creative and internationally influenced dishes. For instance, blue cheese soufflé with anise-orange marmalade shows off a European bent, while miso-glazed cod with shrimp dumplings is resoundingly Asian.;Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11995;Herb & Wood;USA;San Diego;2210 Kettner Blvd., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7271564;-117.1709448;67;true;false;Californian;It’s relatively new to restaurant-rich Little Italy, but this establishment has gained a loyal following since opening in 2016. The multi-level former warehouse could lean cavernous but its barrel-vaulted ceilings and funky artwork exude a distinct Parisian bohemian warmth. The whole place is set aglow and everyone, including the staff, wants to be here.Its wide-ranging menu runs the gamut—from rustic, wood-fired dishes including grilled trumpet mushrooms and pizzas, to more refined plates like venison over buttermilk polenta. The PB&C, a chocolate-whiskey cake with peanut butter mousse and rich milk chocolate gelato, absolutely hits the spot.If on the run, head to their connected all-day eatery—a good bet for lunch and Wednesday trivia nights.;Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11996;Alderwood;USA;Santa Cruz;155 Walnut Ave., Santa Cruz, 95060, USA;36.9733903;-122.0273871;84;false;false;American, Contemporary;Thanks to its promise of serving delicious cuisine with local and sustainably sourced ingredients, this lively spot stands tall. Set upon a busy downtown corner, it virtually screams easy breezy, despite being nowhere near the coast. But due to the vision of Jeffrey Wall (forager and photographer extraordinaire), the entire aesthetic feels natural, chic, and contemporary.The menu stars responsibly sourced oysters, other bivalves, and choice cuts of aged beef. Get going with a crispy crab sandwich offered with cool tartar sauce and piping-hot fries. Then tuck into wood-roasted shrimp with leeks and pancetta, before calling it a night with the raspberry dream sundae. Offered with pineapple compote and chocolate sauce, it's a treat to beat all sweet dreams.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
11997;Beijing Duck House;USA;Cupertino;10883 S. Blaney Ave., Cupertino, 95014, USA;37.3101319;-122.0234064;86;false;true;Chinese, Duck Specialities;This "duck house" is no new kid on the block. In fact, it's been a local fixture for a while now, and this is perhaps in large part due to its well-known Chinese classics. Donning a clean space imbued with splashes of red and gold, wood carvings, and dark wood furniture, there is nothing on the menu that pays particular homage to Beijing. However, the eponymous duck specialty is prepared impeccably and deserves every bit of praise. Presented tableside by a well-suited server, the glistening bird boasts a crisp, fragrant, and succulent skin. It is then carved with unflinching precision and presented with ultra-thin pancakes for wrapping.Vegetables, like Napa cabbage with vinegar, chunky duck sauce, and other accompanying sides complete this decadent meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
11998;Luce;USA;San Francisco;888 Howard St., San Francisco, 94103, USA;37.7818638;-122.404765;63;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Reservations are easy to come by at this longstanding downtown standard, though getting inside can be a bit trickier—enter through the lobby of the InterContinental hotel. Once inside, you’ll be met with a striking space with stylish modern design, comfortable accommodations, and a tasting menu featuring broadly Mediterranean influences peppered with notes of inventive originality. Examples include a kampachi crudo dressed with a tangy sauce of yuzu and white chocolate, as well as a deconstructed “lasagna” with roasted octopus, which boasts striking pasta striped with squid ink. A dessert combining various textures of chocolate and sesame halva offers a happily indulgent finale.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
11999;CUT;USA;Beverly Hills;9500 Wilshire Blvd., Beverly Hills, 90212, USA;34.067036;-118.401024;67;false;false;Steakhouse, American;Tucked inside the sleek Four Seasons Hotel, this steakhouse from Wolfgang Puck isn't pulling any punches when it comes to luxury. Offering the finest cuts of beef from Australia and America to Japan, this is a place for a deep-pocketed crowd, and the elegant dining room with banquette seating is the ideal setting for a power meal. Chilled prawns or oysters on the half shell are classic openers, and it may prove difficult to stop nibbling on the sundried tomato Parker house rolls and the house-knotted pretzels, served with roasted pepper and walnut dip. Creekstone filet mignon with Armagnac green peppercorn bearnaise sauce is a sure bet, but it's those wagyu tallow French fries that you'll be thinking about later.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12001;Alta Adams;USA;Los Angeles;5359 W. Adams Blvd., Los Angeles, 90016, USA;34.032516;-118.35998;27;false;false;Southern;This is the kind of homey and comforting spot that anyone would be glad to have in their neighborhood, but would just as happily drive to find. Generous portions make it a favorite for family-style and group dining. The lovely back patio is draped with string lights and vines, fashioning a perfect backdrop for evenings alfresco. The cooking is soulful and comforting, starting with a plate of golden-fried black-eyed pea fritters with a garlicky green herb sauce for dipping. Their fried chicken is decadent, served juicy with a wickedly spicy hot sauce and caramelized sweet potatoes. Buttery coconut cake for dessert is pure, old-fashioned bliss.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12003;wonderful;USA;Millbrae;270 Broadway, Millbrae, 94030, USA;37.600597;-122.391426;60;false;false;Chinese, Hunanese and Sichuan;Hunanese cuisine may have once taken a backseat to the Bay Area's roster of Chinese spots, so it’s no wonder that this snug gem has attracted many a local and curious palate. Try to snag one of the beautifully carved booths in the back—then you'll be privy to the goings-on in the kitchen. Settle in and begin to peruse the menu of specialties.Boldly flavored dishes incorporate oodles of smoked, cured and fermented ingredients—from the bacon-like pork wok-tossed with leeks, garlic and soy, to the pungent pork, black bean and pickled chili mixture that tops a mound of spicy, hand-cut godfather’s noodles. That whole chili-braised fish, bright and flaky in its bath of red chili sauce flecked with scallions and garlic, is an absolute must.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12004;Sierra Mar;USA;Big Sur;47900 CA-1, Big Sur, 93920, USA;36.229935;-121.7717;40;true;true;Californian, Contemporary;Poised on the brink of a rocky seaside bluff in Big Sur, the vantage point here gives unbeatable sweeping views of the Pacific coast, thanks to a panoply of floor-to-ceiling windows. Housed inside the exclusive Post Ranch Inn resort, the breathtaking location certainly seems to call out for romantic celebrations like honeymoons or anniversaries, while the rustic modern décor and friendly service promote comfort and calm.Stunning vistas aside, the approachable four-course dinner menu (and simpler three-course lunch) offers a bounty of California seasonality, from Monterey abalone with garden lettuce to homemade cavatelli with summer squash. Desserts, like a peanut pavé with caramel and Valrhona chocolate ganache, are both satisfying and easy on the eyes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12007;Fia;USA;Santa Monica;2454 Wilshire Blvd., Santa Monica, 90403, USA;34.0351233;-118.4785237;43;true;true;Contemporary;A Santa Monica landmark dating back to the 20s, the onetime Wilshire has been reimagined with an Italian streak. It’s hard to imagine a more exquisitely Angeleno locale than this sprawling courtyard, encased by massive pine trees and illuminated by twinkling string lights. Fia's menu features organic produce from local farmers from no further than 50 miles away, and though it appears routine on the surface, it's full of inventive twists, as seen in the spicy tuna on crispy arancini, or the porcini tortellini with asparagus, spinach and pearl onion. Save room for the Amalfi lemon mousse cake with Limoncello granita and meringue.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12009;Friends Only;USA;San Francisco;1501 California St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.7906694;-122.4191545;57;true;true;Sushi, Contemporary;Although reservations are now open to the public, an air of exclusivity still pervades this hot-ticket counter, not least of all because of the Olympian price point. What that pretty penny buys, however, is one of the most engaging and indulgent omakase experiences in town, replete with enough luxury to sate even the most committed of sybarites. Sip on delightfully unique cocktails with the likes of black truffle amaro or sesame orgeat, and enjoy a parade of bites highlighting seafood of impeccable quality, much of it painstakingly dry-aged in house. Traditional nigiri and sashimi are served alongside cooked dishes, as in cherrywood-smoked unagi brightened with the prickle of sansho pepper, or binchotan-grilled spot prawn with ramp butter.;;[]
12010;Tasty Place;USA;Millbrae;1625 El Camino Real, Millbrae, 94030, USA;37.612988;-122.40426;36;false;true;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;If you like dumplings and noodles—and plenty of them—Tasty Place is your kind of place. Hot or cold, steamed or pan-fried, solo or in soup, this cornucopia of carbs is made entirely by hand, a process diners can watch unfold in a glassed-in room adjacent to the kitchen. It’s likely you’ll find yourself with some time to do so, as waits can get long at peak hours.As with many Chinese eateries, the menu is overly vast, spanning from Sichuan to Cantonese. The happiest diners stick to dough-based items, like tender chicken dumplings with sweet corn, or chewy handmade cold noodles topped with ground pork, mung bean sprouts, green onion and chilies. Pork dumplings with fermented cabbage are ferociously good—equal parts juicy, tangy and toothsome.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12011;Funky Elephant;USA;Berkeley;1313 9th St., Berkeley, 94710, USA;37.879658;-122.29792;98;false;false;Thai;Look completely past the strip mall location and head into this storefront for some of the more nuanced Thai cooking around. Pop music and colorful plastic tablecloths create a leisurely, relaxed mood. This kitchen is helmed by an ex-Hawker Fare chef, so expect spice blends and house-made curry pastes at the base of each dish.The menu is small but mighty, with items that exude a playful spirit. Nowhere is this clearer than in the “party wings,” which sound like a good time but in fact have great depth of flavor. Nam kao todd is coated in a house-made red curry paste, fried until crispy, hit with fish sauce and layered with tendrils of pork skin and crumbles of fermented pork for a vibrant taste with just the right amount of heat.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12013;Sabio on Main;USA;Pleasanton;501 Main St., Pleasanton, 94566, USA;37.6605365;-121.8758887;29;false;false;Californian, Contemporary;This far-from-sterile space might even be described as dramatic, given its arched wood panels, dark charcoal tiles, soft pendant lights, and backlit wall of wine. A ladder running across completes the effect.  Locally sourced produce, meat from regenerative ranches and responsibly caught seafood are the foundation of the impressive, hyper-seasonal cuisine produced here. Menus dance to the seasons, unveiling such passionate and ingenious dishes as a spring garlic velouté with Livermore olive oil, and half a head of za'atar-roasted romanesco with green tahini and pine nuts. An Irish take on coffee and donuts is executed perfectly and will leave you wanting for more.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12014;Navio;USA;Half Moon Bay;1 Miramontes Point Rd., Half Moon Bay, 94019, USA;37.43336;-122.44099;22;false;true;Contemporary;Nestled inside the luxe Ritz-Carlton, Half Moon Bay, Navio is blessed with a classic northern California setting. Golden sunsets are ripe for romantics, but you’re almost as likely to find families with young children here. The real draw, however, is the thoughtful globally inflected cuisine, overseen by Chef Francisco Simón. Plates offer an easygoing sense of luxury with classic underpinnings, as in cured Mt. Lassen trout with ponzu gelée and a smoked crème fraîche sauce, or beef tenderloin with morel mushrooms, sunchokes, and nutty Palo Cortado sherry. Desserts present a bolder, more inventive face, like a striking construction of Brazilian chocolate fermented with passionfruit and paired with fresh mango and Thai tea-flavored ice cream.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12016;Dama;USA;Los Angeles;612 E. 11th St., Los Angeles, 90015, USA;34.035213;-118.25298;78;true;false;Latin American, American Contemporary;Sultry, colorful and complete with a breezy Caribbean vibe, folks flock here to tuck into satisfying food. While starters like whipped white beans with crispy pork, cotija and pickled pearl onions are captivating, delve deeper into such unlikely items as a Latin take on panzanella, featuring tomatoes and garlic confit. And while a dry-aged ribeye is hard to beat on its own, it’s especially good in build-your-own tacos with pickled sweet peppers and salsa verde.Dama's feisty flavors play well off its chic old-Havana-style dining room, with plush leather sofas, massive wicker fans spinning overhead and colorful tile underfoot. The jaunty front patio is filled with plenty of greenery, while the glam central bar busily blends tropical cocktails to order.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12017;Mar'sel;USA;Rancho Palos Verdes;100 Terranea Way, Rancho Palos Verdes, 90275, USA;33.73889;-118.39618;26;false;true;American;At the end of the Palos Verdes Peninsula, find a windy road that meanders through the plush grounds of the Terranea Resort. Beautiful herb gardens are planted along the sidewalk leading you to Mar’sel’s main entrance. Inside, breathtaking ocean views and a roaring fireplace in the dining room take the chill off the evening breeze.A sense of opulence pervades everything here, including the superb service.Meals commence with a warm homemade English muffin that may have its own cult following. Every dish looks beautiful and well made, especially those cubes of supremely tender Wagyu beef short ribs, with celery prepared four different ways. For dessert, caramel pot de crème is the house specialty, with ganache, cocoa nibs and flecks of sea salt.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12018;ASA South;USA;Los Gatos;57 Los Gatos-Saratoga Rd., Los Gatos, 95032, USA;37.2260847;-121.9721498;46;true;true;Californian, Mediterranean Cuisine;ASA South is like your good looking friend, who also just so happens to be the perfect dining companion. The space is plain likable, featuring a chic dining room set with sleek furnishings, silver bark-like wallpaper and black-and-white photos. And then there's the kitchen, which doesn't take itself too seriously and manages to infuse a bit of fun into its repertoire of serious food. Case in point? The signature rigatoni with mushrooms, described as having too many ingredients to list. But, rest assured as they do a bang-up job. There's something for everyone on this wide-reaching carte, especially if you're a lover of fish—sustainably harvested, of course.The horseshoe-shaped bar out front is an ideal perch for a sip or solo meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12019;Milo + Olive;USA;Santa Monica;2723 Wilshire Blvd., Santa Monica, 90403, USA;34.0373984;-118.4758441;49;true;false;Farm to table, Italian;The name is as cute as a button, but the wood-fired pizzas turned out of this kitchen are serious business. This cheery establishment shines the spotlight perfectly blistered pies, homemade pastas and an outstanding pound cake that may just end up being the highlight of your meal—also wood-fired and finished with honey and whipped cream.A seat at the counter offers a bird’s eye view as the chefs roll out paper-thin pizza crusts, lacing them with tomato sauce, creamy mozzarella and a flutter of sea salt. Tender gnocchi made with brown butter and dyed orange from garnet yam may then arrive tossed with charred radicchio, hazelnuts, and cranberries (most of the organic fruits, vegetables and herbs are from the Santa Monica Farmers’ Market). Weekend brunch is a hit.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12020;Sushi Note;USA;Sherman Oaks;13447 Ventura Blvd., Sherman Oaks, 91423, USA;34.147365;-118.4265586;36;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Nota bene: Sushi Note is far from a postscript. Whether you're here for the supreme fish or distinctly focused wine selection, it hits all the marks. The sleek dining room is defined by soft fabrics, moody colors and provocative artwork, including framed letters and photos.  Chef Kiminobu Saito showcases serious craftsmanship, ace textures and rare flavors in his seasonal plates, available in half-note or full-note omakase menus or à la carte. The attention to detail is remarkable, with every piece of nigiri and sashimi cut to order. Meaty and sweet scallop with truffle salt and citrus, perfectly aged king salmon from New Zealand, kochi with a subtle note of "char," and Japanese halibut fin with a brush of soy are among the best.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12021;The Ranch;USA;Anaheim;1025 E. Ball Rd., Anaheim, 92805, USA;33.81892;-117.897194;77;false;true;Steakhouse, Regional Cuisine;There may not be many cowboys in these parts, but there are plenty of decorative elements and music they’d covet at this urban steakhouse with farm to table touches. The menu is meat-centric, but also focuses on seasonal vegetables grown on their own farm. Pay close attention to daily specials and you might just be rewarded with an heirloom tomato salad bursting with ripeness. Unless you have the appetite of a rancher, these dishes are best shared. Crisp popovers served with sweet homemade tomato jam are a can't miss, and the prime rib is ultra-tender with jus, horseradish sauce and a cast-iron skillet bubbling with cheese-topped scalloped potatoes. Top it all off with their PB&J milk chocolate bar, an upscale take on a familiar favorite.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12022;Gary Danko;USA;San Francisco;800 North Point St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.8058115;-122.4206863;35;true;false;Contemporary;Opened in 1999, Chef Gary Danko's eponymous dining room is a San Francisco institution. Located in Fisherman's Wharf, the restaurant continues to be a busy beacon for business types, celebratory couples, and well-heeled families. The cooking is rooted in classic French cuisine with a wandering sense of global inspiration. Diners select from a prix-fixe of three to five courses, with ample options in each category of appetizer, seafood, meat, and dessert. Those who aren’t in the mood to decide can hand over the reins to the chef’s tasting menu. An extensive wine list, servers dressed in dark suits, and an impressively large cheese trolley round out the vintage experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12023;Vik's Chaat;USA;Berkeley;2390 4th St., Berkeley, 94710, USA;37.8614273;-122.2979676;68;true;false;Indian;This bright orange and yellow building looks big enough to be a warehouse, which makes sense as the inside is not only a counter-service restaurant but also a market. Its namesake chaat may be the star here, but lunch specials are a fantastic bargain. For $15, you can get perfectly tender tandoori chicken with a mouthwatering smoky char, served alongside basmati rice, dal, raita and papadum. Family-friendly and casual, this Indo canteen seems to attract everyone with its excellent chaat, authentic flavors and breads—especially the fried and puffy bhature ideal for sopping up spicy chole. A glass case filled with colorful sweets reminds everyone to save room for dessert.The kitchen closes early at dinner, so unless you’re an early bird, go for lunch.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12024;Bavel;USA;Los Angeles;500 Mateo St., Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.041275;-118.233055;51;false;true;Middle Eastern, Californian;Everyone wants a piece of this Middle Eastern spot, exuding all the downtown feels thanks to an open-air setting. It's definitely a place to see and be seen and getting a table here isn't easy, but the kitchen continues to push Levantine cuisine to ever-higher levels. Bread, in all its wonderful variations, gets a starring role here—from fresh pita to savory black sesame and buckwheat loaves. Dinner standouts include the slow-roasted lamb neck shawarma, smothered in earthy spices and roasted over wood-fired flames. You'll be soaking up every last bit of its fantastic juices with laffa, served on the side. If you can exercise some restraint at dinner—and it certainly won’t be easy—save room for the rose clove chocolate donuts or Persian mulberry ice cream.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12025;Frances;USA;San Francisco;3870 17th St., San Francisco, 94114, USA;37.76293;-122.43239;92;false;false;Californian, American Contemporary;Stylish and always packed, this disarmingly personal restaurant from Chef/owner Melissa Perello remains a neighborhood favorite. It’s as perfect for a low-key date night as it is for dinner with the kids, and while reservations are difficult to score, its cozy setting and gracious staff justify planning ahead.The ultra-seasonal tasting menu, served family style, combines fantastic Californian produce with a Mediterranean bent, eschewing trendy powders and foams for appealingly rustic fare like roasted beets with chickpea dukkah and chèvre. House-made pastas, like a chewy whole wheat casarecce with ramp pesto, are eminently satisfying. The meal ends with a homey dessert like ricotta lemon cake serve with pear, gooseberry and a cloud of Chantilly cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12026;Fort Oak;USA;San Diego;1011 Fort Stockton Dr., San Diego, 92103, USA;32.7507849;-117.1723897;70;false;true;Steakhouse, American;It's named for the majestic oaks of nearby Presidio Park, but this Mission Hills eatery is no friend to trees—at least, not the ones that fuel its beast of a wood-burning hearth, through which nearly every item passes. Yet the arboreal sacrifice is a worthy one as Chef Brad Wise puts the flames to good use in his fresh and uncomplicated preparations. Think: French-style halibut with squash blossoms or Southern chicken-fried quail with redeye gravy.Just don't let the fire fool you—Fort Oak is no log cabin. This historic, former car dealership space is bright and airy, complete with a glamorous horseshoe-shaped bar and sleek, mid-century vibe. Drop in for a casual brunch or happy-hour drink, before splurging on an intimate “chef’s experience” tasting.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
12027;Luv 2 Eat Thai Bistro;USA;Los Angeles;6660 Sunset Blvd. P, Los Angeles, 90028, USA;34.09794;-118.33596;49;false;false;Thai;If you crave authentic Southern Thai food, you’ll love this homey restaurant, which draws crowds to an otherwise unremarkable setting on Sunset. Chefs Noree Pla and Fern Kaewtathip spare no detail in rendering the cuisine of their native Phuket, concocting dishes rarely seen on American menus, including tai pla (a fish organ curry) or jungle curry with chicken feet.Even if you’re not ready for such adventurous food, there’s still a lot to enjoy here. Noodle soups are a specialty, with zeed (featuring a pho-like clear broth with three kinds of pork) being a standout. There’s also the Southern Thai fried chicken with sticky rice as well as a yellow fish curry. Cool down the spice with a homemade pudding in flavors like Thai tea, durian or Ovaltine.;Air conditioning;[]
12029;Kazan;USA;Beverly Hills;111 N. La Cienega Blvd., Beverly Hills, 90211, USA;34.0676223;-118.376527;43;true;true;Japanese, Ramen;Noodle spots may be all the rage, but few prepare such a memorable handmade version of the delicious soba as Chef Ryu Isobe. His brick-lined structure, marked by a bright yellow sign, certainly seems at odds with the ritzy locale, but rest easy as the interior design is chic to the core—imagine brick walls lined with gold-tinted patterns and an inviting open kitchen.The name is Japanese for "volcanic" and conveniently this soba-focused spot blows the lid off its competitors. Highlights include fried shishito peppers with a sweet miso dressing and edamame with a chili yuzu sauce and fried onions. All eyes are on the lei ramen, a spicy broth with their in-house made thin noodles and your choice pork, chicken or tofu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12031;Omakase by Gino;USA;Santa Ana;304 N. Main St., Santa Ana, 92701, USA;33.7473976;-117.8677951;69;false;false;Japanese, Contemporary;Omakase by Gino is nestled amid a sleepy section of downtown Santa Ana but inside, this sushi den is firing on all cylinders. Distressed wood and exposed brick lend a tavern feel while decorative touches are decidedly Japanese. Chef Choi Jin-ho (the restaurant's name is a play on his name) brings palpable joy to this spot with his friendly but focused manner, and the food is just as smile-inducing. Imagine the likes of yuzu cream tucked with a ribbon of crisp Asian pear filled with house-cured ikura or a beautiful fillet of tuna sliced, hit with a flame and set atop an elegant swoosh of garlic and shishito pepper miso. Thick udon noodles are tucked with lobes of creamy uni and a thatch of Italian black summer truffles for a supremely enjoyable (woodsy) bite.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12033;Selanne Steak Tavern;USA;Laguna Beach;1464 S. Coast Hwy., Laguna Beach, 92651, USA;33.5312062;-117.7743716;33;false;true;Steakhouse, American Contemporary;Once a home, this historic setting on Pacific Coast Highway now houses a winning steakhouse. Inside, a variety of settings welcome guests, ranging from the upstairs Loft, the bistro-style Wine Library, the handsome Tavern, or outside on the Veranda or Sunset Terrace. The buzzy bar is also a favorite perch for a crowd that's both relaxed and regulars. Steak is revered in this place and it lives up to its promise with tender, well marbled meat, but the kitchen ratchets it up with expert cooking (and dousing it in butter never hurts). Thick seared mushrooms in a Madeira reduction are a nice touch, and creamy, buttery mashed potatoes are a must, but don't monkey around when it comes to dessert—Selanne's monkey bread can't be missed.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12034;Zhengyalov Hatz;USA;Glendale;318 E. Broadway, Glendale, 91205, USA;34.1462609;-118.2516092;68;true;false;Armenian;How many leafy greens and herbs can you name? At this minimally embellished Armenian bakery, watch as two seasoned chefs knead, roll out, and griddle a specialty flatbread stuffed with more than a dozen chopped varietals. It’s as if they’ve been doing this their entire lives, working with the likes of sorrel, spinach, scallions, and beet leaves to make a tight, forest-green lining that is at once sweet, sour, sharp, and refreshing.It’s easy enough to eat one for a snack and several for a meal. Conveniently, there’s no need to guess what else to order here: The namesake dish is the only thing on the menu, besides a tangy yogurt drink chock-full of dill and cucumber, okroshka, and a simple square of paklava made with flaky phyllo and ground nuts.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12035;Anomaly SF;USA;San Francisco;2600 Sutter St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7849679;-122.4433492;59;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;After several pop-up locations, this covert operation has finally found a permanent home, but its sub rosa supper club vibe is still in force. The entrance, on an unremarkable residential block, is marked only by the numbers of its address, and once inside, the space has a feeling of intimate seclusion. Chef Mike Lanham impresses with beautifully presented dishes that display both creativity and a keen sense of texture, drawing upon a modernist toolkit without going overboard with foams and gels. The frequently changing tasting showcases a wealth of seasonal produce alongside a playful sensibility, as in an emoji-inspired egg bite, or a sophisticated trio of fennel preparations, a winking response to a previous complaint that the ingredient was over-used.;;[]
12036;Chiang Rai;USA;Long Beach;3832 E. Anaheim St., Long Beach, 90804, USA;33.782478;-118.1490324;41;false;true;Thai;Chiang Rai is exactly why you don't judge a book by its cover. You could easily walk by its generic-looking facade, but that would be such a shame indeed. Inside, it's delightfully quirky and colorful with a contemporary vibe. And then there's the food.There is a lengthy Thai menu spotlighting Northern specialties and street food, but skip straight to the Chiang Rai Local Food portion and order away. The kitchen caters to the American palate, so if you're a heat seeker don't be shy about speaking up. Khao soi, a classic northern Thai curry, is given a twist here with thin slices of raw ribeye over thin egg noodles. Hot soup is then ladled over it to gently cook the tender meat while delivering a depth of flavor for a supremely satisfying meal.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12037;La Toque;USA;Napa;1314 McKinstry St., Napa, 94559, USA;38.30351;-122.28349;32;true;true;Contemporary;Chef Ken Frank has been a Napa Valley mainstay ever since he opened this fine-dining lair in the Westin Verasa hotel in 2008. Walk under an oversized inflatable chef’s hat hanging above the entrance and into the elegant room, where you can first glimpse into the gleaming open kitchen and see a brigade of chefs running about. Leather-topped tables, a fireplace and an extensive wine list offer creature comforts to a crowd that’s usually here to celebrate. Though pricey and at times diminutive, the signature tasting menu takes broad culinary cues. Highlights include roasted rack of lamb with Red Hawk aligot potatoes as well as a dry-aged Liberty Duck breast with za'atar cherry coulis. A full vegetarian tasting menu is also available.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12038;Boozehounds;USA;Palm Springs;2080 N. Palm Canyon Dr., Palm Springs, 92262, USA;33.8482;-116.5469;84;true;false;International;What's in a name? In this case, at least, there’s a tongue-in-cheek précis: a dog-friendly cocktail bar. Diners and their canine confrères can enter a spacious enclosed patio area through a separate "doggy door," which offers access to an additional menu of bowls and treats for Fido and Spot. The stylish indoor space remains a humans-only domain, where the focus shifts to a top shelf drinks menu (replete with dog-themed nomenclature, naturally), as well as an appealingly eclectic bar menu that spans both snacks and more substantial fare. Standbys like truffled parmesan fried and blistered shishitos are nothing to sniff at, but less expected items like Japanese-inflected tuna tataki, Filipino adobo or Korean rice cakes offer an exciting change of pace.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12039;Zola;USA;Palo Alto;565 Bryant St., Palo Alto, 94301, USA;37.445244;-122.160576;50;false;true;French, Californian;A Palo Alto sparkler, Zola charms its way into diners’ hearts via a seductive French bistro menu with Californian flair. Whether you’re spreading smoky salmon rillettes on toasted artisan levain, twirling pillowy caramelized ricotta gnocchi into the yolk of a soft-cooked egg in brown butter or tucking into tender filet de boeuf with creamy sauce béarnaise and golden-brown fingerling potatoes, you’re sure to fall hard for the food.The stylish space updates a few classics (wood tables, bistro chairs, pressed ceilings) with a dark teal color scheme and enticingly low lighting, and the well-chosen wine list is equal parts Gallic and Golden State. Crème caramel for dessert may be traditional, but it’s also perfectly executed and decadently rich.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12040;4 Saints;USA;Palm Springs;100 W. Tahquitz Canyon Way, Palm Springs, 92262, USA;33.8233852;-116.5476173;52;true;false;American;Set on the seventh-floor rooftop of the posh Rowan Hotel, this is the highest perch in all of downtown. A stylishly modern room features leather banquettes and a handsome central bar, but it’s the sweeping views of the San Jacinto Mountains that will really make you swoon—and that’s before a few rounds of signature date-infused Old Fashioneds. Chef Ysaac Ramirez lends a Southern twang to a shareable menu replete with seasonal produce, as in grilled purple sweet potatoes with creamy Alabama white barbecue sauce and pickled red chiles. Larger appetites will be satisfied by an assortment of grilled steaks, like a ribeye with smoked onion, charred tomato and rosemary salsa verde. It’s true that the prices are lofty, but after all, so are the views.;Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12041;Destroyer;USA;Culver City;3578 Hayden Ave., Culver City, 90232, USA;34.024647;-118.381424;99;true;false;Contemporary;The architecturally intriguing Hayden Tract district is the perfect backdrop for Jordan Kahn's adventurous Destroyer, located just across the street from sister restaurant, Vespertine. The minimalist interior keeps your attention on the food, where each plate is a complex composition of flavors that are bound to delight and surprise. Begin with such harmonious starters as avocado confit, a half avocado dusted with their onion ash and served with confit tomatoes and dressed arugula that is simple but impressive. Koshikari rice porridge delivers depth and a riot of textures, while the milk chocolate crémeux finished with almond streusel, praline and a dusting of frozen cucumber cream is a striking closer.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12042;Guisados;USA;Los Angeles;2100 E. Cesar E. Chavez Ave., Los Angeles, 90033, USA;34.048306;-118.21142;56;false;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Set on a busy corner with an unassuming façade, this may be a humble storefront, but it’s all heart with an inimitable taste of home. This clean, airy and family-owned spot is open all day, so pop in when the mood strikes to sample their daily specials. Consult the chalkboards for the latest update, then snag a seat at one of the few tables with a view of the grill.It's all about their skillfully prepared tacos and expect to make a mess, as the sauce and juice drip while you're eating. Steak picado tacos with stewed flank steak served over black beans, or their cochinita pibil, with shredded pork braised with achiote and topped with pickled onions, are two favorites.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12043;Petit Trois;USA;Los Angeles;718 N. Highland Ave., Los Angeles, 90038, USA;34.0839644;-118.3382499;94;true;false;French;Open and operating non-stop from noon until late night, this bijou is the casual sibling of Trois Mec next door. The narrow room is always full and the counter cramped, as the chefs display their skills before you, assembling such lovely dishes as pâté de campagne. And while the setting may not sound overly comfortable, there is a focus on service, which makes every meal here a pleasant experience from start to finish.The French hip-hop in the background eschews tradition, but the cooking does the exact opposite. This menu is a canon of bistro favorites, like garlicky escargots de Bourgogne, steak frites with mustard sauce and what may be the city’s best omelet. Try their "Big Mec," a double cheeseburger with bordelaise and house sauce and fries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12045;Campfire;USA;Carlsbad;2725 State St., Carlsbad, 92008, USA;33.1621181;-117.3508896;66;true;false;Contemporary;Located in a midcentury Quonset hut enlivened with eclectic outdoorsy decorations, this rough-and-tumble counterpart to more glamorous nearby Jeune et Jolie has plenty of fun with its theme, down to the teepee on the patio. The centerpiece is a custom-built 12-foot wood-burning hearth, which lends an appropriate note of smoke to many of the kitchen’s offerings, from vegetables like crispy roasted broccoli with a tangy chermoula sauce, or grilled octopus with Jimmy Nardello peppers. Meatier options like slow-cooked brisket or a hefty tomahawk steak for two will sate even the burliest appetites. A nearly obligatory end to this glamping experience is the DIY s’mores, served with a small pile of red-hot coals for toasting fluffy house-made marshmallows.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12046;Adega;USA;San Jose;1614 Alum Rock Ave., San Jose, 95116, USA;37.35131;-121.85845;25;false;true;Portuguese, Californian;Adega is Portuguese for “wine cellar,” and following suit, this dining room stocks over 200 vintages that are rarely seen on these Western shores. It's the ethos here, where Chef David Costa and Pastry Chef Jessica Carreira create an appetizing menu with a perfect blend of pristine local produce and top-notch, imported ingredients.Seafood is a focus, and diners shouldn't miss the likes of a dressed-up take on Portugal's culinary backbone—bacalhau. In this rendition, it is moist and flavorful, and arranged over crisp potatoes. Succulent carabineros are marinated in lemongrass and seaweed, then topped with caviar.  Chef Carreira’s desserts, like flan, layered with caramelized sugar and gilded with a quenelle of vanilla ice cream, are equally notable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12047;Cafe Reyes;USA;Point Reyes Station;11101 Hwy. 1, Point Reyes Station, 94956, USA;38.066696;-122.80451;82;true;true;Pizza;This unassuming charmer in quaint Point Reyes Station is a perfect stop for day-trippers who are sure to enjoy the many delicious dishes that emerge from its duo of wood-fired ovens. Pizza is the focus, with ten varieties ranging from a classic Margherita to meaty staples like fennel sausage and mushroom. The deliciously crusty pies are named after local destinations, like the Limantour and Bodega, as well as the Farallon, with its slivers of roasted garlic, mini pepperoni with crisped edges and a pile of mozzarella.Given its cooking method, it’s no surprise that Cafe Reyes is stacked high with wood, both against the walls and under the counter. The big, spacious, barn-like dining room is rustic, unfussy and perfect for groups.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12048;Madera;USA;Menlo Park;2825 Sand Hill Rd., Menlo Park, 94025, USA;37.42014;-122.21151;45;true;true;Contemporary, Californian;Enveloped in the luxury of the Rosewood Sand Hill hotel, this elegant retreat boasts vaulted ceilings, a crackling fireplace, and a stunning backdrop of the Santa Cruz Mountains—think Silicon Valley meets Swiss chalet. Affluent techies clad in Patagonia vests flock here for the tranquil, sophisticated ambience and uncomplicated, ingredient-driven dishes that emerge from a grand open kitchen. An efficient power lunch might consist of a lobster and avocado tartine, whereas a three-course prix-fixe dinner calls for a bit more involvement. In both cases, simplicity reigns, with local products placed front and center. A wood-fired grill is used liberally to lend a primal, smoky savor.Beignets matched with single malt caramel provide a comforting finale.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12050;Nightbird;USA;San Francisco;330 Gough St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.776485;-122.42288;100;false;true;Californian, Contemporary;Located just behind a beautiful wooden door with a carved owl and in a prime Hayes Valley location, Nightbird invites you into its nest with a small and sleek dining room. If you arrive early, don’t miss a delicious craft cocktail at their adjacent bar, Linden Room, as it’s the perfect lead-up to Chef/owner Kim Alter’s multicourse tasting menu.Though the menu changes often to follow the changing seasons, Alter’s presentations are consistently artful. For example, a composition of roasted duck breast and tender confit might be arranged with summer squash and a bright compote of gooseberries, plus a chaser of spiced duck broth. House-made breads like a crusty farro loaf or fluffy Parker House rolls arrive at separate points of the meal to gild the lily.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12051;Bacon & Butter;USA;Sacramento;5913 Broadway, Sacramento, 95820, USA;38.54683;-121.43599;67;false;false;American;If the name doesn’t have you salivating yet, the dishes being ferried to and fro by the bustling staff certainly will. Bacon & Butter lures diners and lots of them—you’ll see lasting queues late into the morning—thanks to its promise of good old-fashioned American breakfast and brunch.From flapjacks and crisped potatoes to super-sized cinnamon rolls, this kitchen’s goods taste like Sunday morning at your Mom’s, including all the noise and nagging. The absolute don’t miss however is the biscuit sandwich, featuring egg, cheese, bacon and caramelized onion layered atop fluffy, flaky biscuits and then smothered with bacon gravy for a “wet,” messy and all-out delicious dish. Everything here is big enough for two, but who wants to share when it’s this good?;Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12053;Himitsu;USA;La Jolla;1030 Torrey Pines Rd. G, La Jolla, 92037, USA;32.8430208;-117.2724495;98;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;"Irasshaimase!" is the greeting commonly heard upon entering this cozy little sushiya. You’ll want to plan ahead to snag one of the eight coveted seats at the pristine counter, but it’s well worth the forethought, as these friendly chefs take great pride in discussing the quality of their fish and the techniques used to prepare your meal. It’s also a front row seat to their admirable knife skills.Such affability extends to the dining room, where servers flash big smiles and loads of greenery as well as natural wood come together to create a truly serene effect. Omakase is the way to go, but there are à la carte options as well—from appetizers, soups, sashimi and maki (sporting soft, well-seasoned rice) to specialty plates and daily fish specials.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
12054;Ayara Thai Cuisine;USA;Los Angeles;6245 W. 87th St., Los Angeles, 90045, USA;33.95861;-118.39456;100;false;false;Thai;A family owned and operated restaurant, having opened in 2004, now with Vanda Asapahu has taken on the role of chef in this family-owned and operated restaurant started by her parents. Wood tables and chairs decorate the interior, and a patio also welcomes diners.The menu is packed with everything from tried-and-true pleasures to more inventive items, and the kitchen caters to your spice preferences. Start with their classic papaya salad with a bold and flavorful kick and make sure to get a curry, perhaps the green curry that's made with a fresh chili curry paste and coconut and your choice of protein. Don't ignore their pastries, which incorporate a bit of French technique. The Thai tea flan with bitter caramel and ripe, fresh berries on top is a perfect choice.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12056;Paprika Café;USA;Monterey;309 Lighthouse Ave., Monterey, 93940, USA;36.610821;-121.8995455;100;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Greek;This tiny spot is the perfect sojourn before or after a visit to the Monterey Bay Aquarium, thanks to its delectable and affordable Mediterranean food and friendly service. A diminutive and humble place, it has only six tables, but the chef/owner provides a warm welcome, recommending favorite items before he goes to work in the tiny back kitchen.Vegans and vegetarians will delight in the ample menu featuring flaky spanakopita, smoky baba ghanoush and vibrant tabbouleh with a perfect zip from fresh lemon. The tahini that accompanies the crisp, golden falafel is luscious, and a classic Greek salad is refreshingly satisfying. Don’t fill up completely though, as the homemade baklava, which just so happens to be vegan, is sure to sate and is available packaged to go.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12057;Los Agaves;USA;Santa Barbara;600 N. Milpas St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.427376;-119.6866;79;false;true;Mexican, Californian;Serving generous portions of hearty south-of-the-border favorites by way of California, along with a relaxed, family-friendly vibe, this place deserves every bit of praise lavished upon it. The staff may bring chips immediately to your table, but salsa and drinks are both self-service. Remember to order at the counter and collect a number before taking a seat. Start with the likes of lime-marinated halibut ceviche tostada with cilantro and avocado. Then pick from a variety of sizeable burritos or go for the satisfyingly cheesy and crispy costra taco al pastor, with pineapple, marinated pork, and chipotle—enlivened with pickled onions.There may be four locations, but this one is the original. The room can get crowded, so takeaway is a popular option.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12058;The Lark;USA;Santa Barbara;131 Anacapa St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.414574;-119.68986;23;true;false;Californian;This former fish market is located in the Funk Zone arts district, just a stone’s throw from the oceanfront. The vibrant dining room has become one of the trendiest places in town, largely thanks to the urban scene it fashions through an edgy décor and vintage lighting. Service remains cool and laid-back as ever, while also taking very good care of each guest.Meals are served as large, family-style portions that are meant to be shared and spotlight the central coast’s finest ingredients. Well-mastered original creations may unveil blistered shishito peppers and roasted eggplant with cilantro yogurt, sweet and sour pickles as well as duck-fat breadcrumbs.The wine selection is a smart representation of the best of Santa Barbara’s producers.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12059;First & Oak;USA;Solvang;409 1st St., Solvang, 93463, USA;34.593758;-120.14039;98;false;true;Contemporary;In a small, romantic boutique hotel, this is a deliciously old-school restaurant that is coming into its own with ambitious cuisine. This should be no surprise, as the chef boasts a background in some esteemed and globally acclaimed kitchens. Guests are invited to create their own prix-fixe menu by selecting four to five dishes from a variety of categories, such as garden, ocean or farm (some beef comes from a northern California ranch). This might yield a meal that begins with a refreshing gazpacho made from delicately spiced melon with basil blossom and a bit of smoky fried shrimp. Masterful desserts have included a brown-butter sponge cake with dense clotted cream and marinated strawberries. Be sure to sample the owner’s own wine label, Coqueliquot, available in a range of styles.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12060;Sol Food;USA;San Rafael;903 Lincoln Ave., San Rafael, 94901, USA;37.97187;-122.5241;22;true;false;Puerto Rican;You won’t be able to miss this Puerto Rican favorite, recognizable by its grasshopper-green exterior and overflowing crowds of festive diners. In fact, their comida criolla is so popular that it’s taken over the block: a sister bodega does a booming takeout business, while gift store Conchita sells wares from San Juan and beyond.Sol Food’s soul food is hearty and abundant, from tamale-like pasteles of mashed plantain and taro stuffed with garlicky pork to fragrant sautéed shrimp loaded with tomato, onion and spices. Outstanding daily specials, like arroz con pollo and pernil, are also big draws. Wash it all down with a delicious mango iced tea, and don’t skip the decadent pineapple bread pudding, soaked in warm, buttery mango sauce, for dessert.;Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12061;Pearl 6101;USA;San Francisco;6101 California St., San Francisco, 94121, USA;37.783943;-122.48298;23;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Californian;This recruit in a retro drugstore is already the toast of town, with crowds young and old packing in—not unlike neighboring sister, Pizzetta 211. The big and airy space is designed for all-day dining —whether that may be coffee and wood-fired bagels during the day, or a substantial dinner (and cocktail) later.Co-chefs Mel Lopez and Joyce Conway turn out a Cal-Mediterranean menu heavy on seafood and pastas, like rustic handkerchiefs in a velvety white Bolognese sauce. Carnivores can get down on a grilled bone-in pork chop, accompanied by gently charred broccolini and nectarines. And that San Francisco must—brunch—is brilliantly executed here, with enticing eggs in purgatory or Dutch baby pancakes with fresh fruit and whipped crème fraîche.;Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12062;Kusakabe;USA;San Francisco;584 Washington St., San Francisco, 94111, USA;37.7956831;-122.4030806;48;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Serene with warm lighting and clean lines, distinctive creativity is the motto of this sushi-focused operation. Inside, a stunning counter crafted from a piece of live-edge elm, oyster-hued leather chairs and a ceiling of wood slats complete the Japanese-chic look.While the preparation of their nightly omakase might seem like a production line by employing myriad cooking techniques, the kitchen ensures that every bite is memorable. Begin with warm kelp tea, before embarking on a sashimi parade of bluefin slices served with a yuzu-onion-sesame sauce. Then, savor softshell crab soup in a corn and sweet miso broth before a top rendition of sushi yields Santa Barbara sea urchin atop Hokkaido scallop and snapper with cured egg yolk shavings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
12063;Cotogna;USA;San Francisco;490 Pacific Ave., San Francisco, 94133, USA;37.7974268;-122.4034608;92;true;false;Italian;Though rustic compared to high-end sibling Quince just next door, Michael and Lindsay Tusk’s casual offshoot would be elegant by any other standard. It's quintessentially Italian with exposed brickwork, a gleaming copper counter and bar, and wooden tables. The space is designed around a display kitchen, from which crispy pizzas and savory roasted meats emerge. The menu highlights Chef Tusk's flawless pastas, like agnolotti del plin, stuffed with tender rabbit, veal, and pork, or the rigatoni with guanciale, chanterelle mushrooms, and pistachio. Seasonal appetizers like kale and radicchio salad in a tangy vinaigrette are equally delicious, as is the antipasti platter. The plum and ginger torta is moist and delicious, but those sweet, ripe plums steal the show.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12064;Rustic Canyon;USA;Santa Monica;1119 Wilshire Blvd., Santa Monica, 90401, USA;34.024952;-118.49118;19;false;true;Californian;A sense of community and warm hospitality pervade this beloved Santa Monica institution—it feels like your favorite neighborhood spot, even if you’ve traveled miles to dine here. The menu of shareable plates overseen by Chef/owner Jeremy Fox is market-driven even by California standards, a fact that’s proudly advertised with the inclusion of a bevy of local farmers’ names. A prime example is Zuckerman's delta asparagus, plating the vibrant green stalks in alternating layers over a sauce gribiche with grated lemon zest and chicken skin crackling. The quality of the produce is exceptional, and the cooking is simple and hearty, as in poached Mt. Lassen trout atop a bed of sauerkraut in a Riesling wine sauce mixed with smoked trout roe and finely cut chives.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12065;El Mercado Modern Cuisine;USA;Santa Ana;301 N. Spurgeon St., Santa Ana, 92701, USA;33.7473569;-117.8654136;52;false;true;Mexican, Californian;El Mercado sits in downtown Santa Ana tucked between art house theaters, modern-day galleries and much of the town's storied and Latino past. The welcoming dining room echoes its setting with well-chosen artwork, with many pieces crafted by local artists. Serving a "modern" take on Mexican food in Santa Ana is no small feat, but this kitchen delivers on flavor, composition and quality. Paper-thin slices of cucumber with chili powder and salt are shingled to create a thatch over lime-cured fresh shrimp with chopped red onion and cubes of creamy ripe avocado. Tylayuda takes a large, toasted flour tortilla, topping it with black beans, avocado puree, Oaxaca cheese and jocoque, plus a selection of meat—spicy chorizo is the perfect complement.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12066;Blackbird;USA;Santa Barbara;36 State St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.4132948;-119.6900705;70;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;Located at the waterfront Hotel Californian, Blackbird is as attractive as its surroundings. Inside, its décor blends art deco and mid-century styles, with an “air kiss” to the private clubs of yesteryear. Striking arched doors seem to let the sea breeze wash over the room and an inviting bar runs the length of the space with plenty of creative cocktails.The kitchen keeps the nearby Pacific in mind with first courses like Dungeness crab puffs with Manchego cheese and Urfa pepper-spiked honey. Spaghetti with local sea urchin, Calabrese pepper and smoked seaweed, or a whole roasted branzino with ramps, beets and grilled onion jam keep the theme going. Expect a creative finish, such as a fig pavlova with a drizzle of savory olive oil.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12067;Connie & Ted’s;USA;West Hollywood;8171 Santa Monica Blvd., West Hollywood, 90046, USA;34.0909948;-118.3672928;95;false;false;Seafood;It's set in the West Coast, but this new-school shack still has serious East Coast vibes—even if it does indeed source its sustainable, wild-caught seafood from both the Atlantic and Pacific. With an extensive raw bar, parking lot strewn with shells and a funky interior plastered with seafaring knickknacks, it’s a fitting tribute to Chef Michael Cimarusti’s New England origins.Chowder is a must for a seafood spot and this particular one offers a tempting flight of three: creamy New England, tomato-based Manhattan and buttery Rhode Island. The lobster roll, packed with tail and claw meat, is a gem among solo diners, while chilled seafood platters and the oak-grilled fish are great for crowds. Don’t forget to grab a bit of saltwater taffy on your way out.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12068;Hamano Sushi;USA;San Francisco;1332 Castro St., San Francisco, 94114, USA;37.7510261;-122.4341135;51;false;false;Japanese;Those who think that all sushi counters are stiff and unapologetically expensive should take a hard look at this easy-going iteration in Noe Valley. While the dining room is ideal for larger groups looking for casual à la carte items like maki, tempura, and sashimi, the well-tread counter is a favorite among Chef Jiro Lin’s loyal fan base, each of whom enjoy quality nigiri at remarkably reasonable prices.Chef Lin flexes his creative muscles by complementing the likes of salt-cured tile fish, aged hamachi, and sea-perch with a potent dose of wasabi, Japanese chili pepper, and fish liver. First timers should call ahead for reservations, as this counter boasts weekly regulars, including wine geeks particularly besotted by their tightly curated list.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list;[]
12069;Chi Spacca;USA;Los Angeles;6610 Melrose Ave., Los Angeles, 90038, USA;34.08342;-118.339096;50;true;false;Italian, Steakhouse;The carnivorous heart of Nancy Silverton’s “Mozzaplex” is as strong as ever. A modern Italian take on the old-school steakhouse, the restaurant boasts a steady menu of classics that seem to have only gotten better with age. Is there a better beginning than the indulgently cheesy focaccia di recco? Is there a chicken more compelling than the 24-hour brined and marinated pollo alla diavola? The team makes the most of smoke and live fire, as big proteins pass through the wood-burning oven. Indeed, this is hearty cooking that is seasoned boldly and keenly seasonal, served in a space that is intimate and energized all at once. A superb wine list celebrates the vast talents of Italy, and an astute, welcoming staff keeps everything flowing with ease.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12070;Badmaash;USA;Los Angeles;108 W. 2nd St., Ste. 104, Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.05115;-118.24476;83;false;true;Indian, Gastropub;Now boasting two locations, this Indian gastropub helmed by a father and his two sons is as popular as ever, and with good reason. The skilled kitchen delivers each dish with flavor and fun, employing authentic ingredients with global inspiration. Find the clearest expression of their philosophy in the poutine, accompanied by masala-spiced potatoes with gravy, mozzarella and chicken tikka. Try one of their butter chicken samosas or tuck into Mother's recipe of saag paneer  with sauteed spinach and tomato with garam masala and paneer, then chase it with a mango lassi. The setting, complete with blasts of color, vintage Bollywood posters and a pop-art Gandhi mural, is as vibrant as the food.;Air conditioning;[]
12071;Flea St. Cafe;USA;Menlo Park;3607 Alameda de las Pulgas, Menlo Park, 94025, USA;37.4317;-122.20127;89;false;true;Contemporary, Californian;This classic “café” retains the feeling of being in a house, with dining areas distributed throughout. Interesting artwork adorns each of these rooms, simply adding to the sense of intimacy, not unlike the warm and inviting front bar area, filled with friendly banter and soft tunes.The team ensures that each item from this kitchen is well conceived and adheres to California’s farm-to-table ethos. Everything on this seasonally driven menu strives to emphasize freshness, starting with the warm and buttery biscuits that welcome you to your table. Don't miss the shell bean soup featuring a braised tomato broth complete with summery flavors.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12072;Vina Enoteca;USA;Palo Alto;700 Welch Rd., Unit 110, Palo Alto, 94304, USA;37.437077;-122.17345;38;false;true;Italian, Contemporary;It has been made more than apparent by now that this owner, Rocco Scordella who is a native of Italy, succeeded in bringing a delicious taste of his homeland to Palo Alto. Look around and note that pasta tops everyone’s table for good reason. If offered, be sure to try the toothsome spinach tagliatelle in a meaty ragù that's composed with local pork and naturally raised beef. This kitchen clearly prioritizes sourcing—a majority of the greens and vegetables are grown at Stanford Education Farm—and pastas, pizzas and bread are all crafted in-house.The industrial-chic décor features high ceilings, arches and soft leather chairs. Whether you pop in for snacks and cocktails at the bar or plan on savoring a full meal, service is always friendly and quick.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12073;Café Jacqueline;USA;San Francisco;1454 Grant Ave., San Francisco, 94133, USA;37.80056;-122.40738;89;true;true;French;Note: This restaurant is temporarily closed.Café Jacqueline is a restaurant from another time, but for those who appreciate its eccentricities, it’s a total treasure. Savory and sweet soufflés big enough for two make up the entirety of the menu, but getting one requires endurance.Reservations are by phone only, though the staff rarely answers, and tuxedo-clad servers don’t so much serve as they do command—handling tables in a direct but never offensive manner. They are also unapologetic about just how long this candlelight dinner will take: three hours, for most, as every towering soufflé is made by the grand dame herself, who’s been whipping egg whites for nearly 40 years. From broccoli and brie to Grand Marnier and chocolate, dinner here is a special affair unmatched in its romanticism.;Air conditioning;[]
12074;Ella;USA;Sacramento;1131 K St., Sacramento, 95814, USA;38.5786358;-121.4914258;16;false;false;Contemporary, American;This upscale beaut in downtown Sacramento is equal parts rustic and refined, with floor-to-ceiling curtains, thick linens and a colorful overhang comprised of antique wood. You’re likely to be seated among regulars, who can be found chatting with the attentive staff and sampling their wine pairing suggestions (there are plenty of half-glass options for the lunchtime Capitol crowd). The menu offers creative takes on global dishes, including a salad of vine-ripened, handpicked, heirloom tomatoes with shaved radish, avocado purée, and a dill dressing enriched with ricotta salata. Perfectly crispy Southern fried chicken is a staple and rightfully so.The bar is a great place to linger—with an expertly prepared cocktail, like the house gin and tonic.;Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12075;The Hatch;USA;Paso Robles;835 13th St., Paso Robles, 93446, USA;35.6278739;-120.6892269;87;false;true;American;It's all hail to the bird at The Hatch. This downtown Paso Robles restaurant reveres the rotisserie and roasted chicken is indeed the must order. Brined and smoky, the half Mary's organic chicken is sided by a vanilla-maple slaw, buttermilk dip and Hatch hot sauce, and its perfectly salty skin coupled with flavorful meat gives an expensive steak a run for its money. The skillet cornbread, finished with brown butter, flaky salt and honey, is a worthy sidekick. With down-home style cooking, it may come as no surprise that cream pies are the focus come dessert. Order the chocolate cream pie, an individually-sized treat served in a metal pie tin. How could you ever go wrong with chocolate pudding and salted caramel in a coconut graham crust?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12076;Yasu;USA;Beverly Hills;265 S. Robertson Blvd., Beverly Hills, 90211, USA;34.0632305;-118.3836501;82;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;The first stateside branch of the acclaimed Yasu Toronto, this outpost is akin to a jewel in the crown of area sushiyas. It's a minimalist, wonderfully lit, and rather Zen den, with an L-shaped counter seating some ten lucky guests as well as a few tables lining one side of the room. A mingling of dark and light colors along with a "metallic" backdrop help things along nicely.This omakase opens with a parade of sashimi, like cherry trout, sea bream, and scallop—each slice carefully arranged on an ornate tray with a dab of wasabi, ginger, and soy. Nigiri follows next—think snappy striped jack over perfectly formed shari, golden eye snapper with yuzu kosho, and snow crab dipped in warm dashi. Tuna served three ways is a signature way to seal the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12078;Doppio Zero Pizzeria Napoletana;USA;Mountain View;160 Castro St., Mountain View, 94041, USA;37.394318;-122.0787;84;true;false;Pizza, Italian;It’s easy to overlook pizza as a way to quell hunger pangs, but sink your teeth into the selections here and you’re quickly reminded that it’s an art form unto itself. The pies are, well, epic (and certified by the Associazione Verace Pizza Napoletana, one of just a few in the state), and well-seasoned—topped with a zesty tomato sauce and bold ingredients. Then there is that crust—chewy and blistered with just the right amount of char. You could come just for pizza, but that would mean missing out on such delicious dishes as polpo—smoky octopus dressed with anchovy vinaigrette and set atop tomatoes. It’s so much more than just a “salad.”The bustling interior doesn’t distract from the goods. On a nice day, grab a seat on the sidewalk to imbibe the bliss.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12079;Elf Cafe;USA;Los Angeles;2135 W. Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.077515;-118.2646683;31;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;There are no elves running the show at this intimate spot but with just three people staffing the kitchen throughout service, they're certainly working like Santa's helpers. It's a wine bar, so expect a nice selection of bottles, but there's also cider and beer, as well as non-alcoholic offerings. Originally fully vegetarian, Elf Cafe has tweaked its Mediterranean-minded menu to now include animal proteins. Case in point? The lamb skewers, marinated and seared to a crisp crust. Paired with a refreshing yogurt sauce and onions hit with sumac, it's skillfull and satisfying. For a vegetable-focused plate, consider the maitake, grilled over a wood fire, topped with chimichurri, and served over a smashed potato with a ramekin of ají verde for dipping. Craving something sweet? Warm date cake with rich caramel sauce and pomegranate seeds does the trick.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12080;Oma San Francisco Station;USA;San Francisco;1737 Post St., #337, San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7850342;-122.4309219;76;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;This simple wood counter serves some of the area’s better nigiri, right from the corner of a mall in Japantown. Blink and you’ll miss it—Oma is about the size of a kiosk near the Webster Street exit.Behind the counter, find Chef Wilson Chan deftly slicing each morsel before your eyes, artfully placing it before every guest, piece by piece. Choose from five- eight- or twelve-piece prix-fixe menus to match your appetite and budget, though prices are reasonable for such quality. Clean flavors and rich, silky fish are the hallmarks of dining here. Highlights include a lightly torched wild star butterfish that melts in the mouth, and a delicious handroll combining chopped bluefin tuna balanced with pickled yellow daikon wrapped in crisp nori.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12083;Hed 11;USA;San Francisco;1800 Sutter St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7865983;-122.4301349;91;false;false;Thai, Contemporary;Perched in a swanky space at the corner of the Kimpton Hotel Enso, this ambitious Thai project from Chef Piriya "Saint" Boonprasan and owner Naruephon "Billie" Wannajaro gives a hint to its concept right in the name: an 11-course menu that celebrates regional Thai flavors with a contemporary style. The price point doesn’t lend itself to dining on a budget, but despite its variety, the meal won’t over-tax your schedule, with most of the courses arriving together as a sort of miniature banquet for the main. Sweet and savory are blended throughout the menu, whether in bites like a coconut pancake with lime and caviar, a take on khanom jeen sao nam with seared scallop paired with chilled rice noodles, tangy pineapple, and garlic, or even a Thai-style cheesecake with crispy fried onions and passionfruit syrup.;;[]
12084;Azalina’s;USA;San Francisco;499 Ellis St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.7846459;-122.414331;98;true;false;Malaysian, Californian;Chef Azalina Eusope continues to make her mark as an ambassador for Malaysian cuisine in this cleverly designed space that calls to mind a tropical hideaway ensconced in the rough-and-tumble Tenderloin.The menu is a frequently changing seasonal prix fixe with dishes that offer her own interpretation of flavors she grew up with— think California meets Penang. Quality ingredients and creativity are hallmarks, seen in a dish of "economy noodles" with fermented chili paste, topped with barbecued quail and toasted hazelnuts, or steelhead trout baked in banana leaves. Her pastry training is evident in a complex dessert of pandan custard with water chestnut and coconut granita, served with a take on kuih kasturi, a mung bean fritter filled with jackfruit and sweet red bean.;;[]
12085;Amour;USA;West Hollywood;8715 Beverly Blvd., West Hollywood, 90048, USA;34.0771943;-118.381192;70;false;false;French Contemporary;Indoors or out? It's the eternal question in Los Angeles, but even more difficult to decide at Amour. Banquettes and booths beckon on the patio, while the dining room, accessed through a library stacked with vintage books, is loaded with charm down to the very last candlestick. Multicourse tasting menus are on offer or order à la carte from a menu that blends French and Asian influences, as in chawanmushi with Perigord truffles and trout roe. New Caledonia blue prawn carpaccio and a French-style omelet with a quenelle of caviar and Comté foam are just two of the well-executed dishes. Wagyu sided by crispy matchstick potatoes is given a hint of sweetness courtesy of a swirl of beet puree, while millefeuille with dulce de leche brings it all home.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
12087;LSXO;USA;Huntington Beach;21010 Pacific Coast Hwy., Huntington Beach, 92648, USA;33.6553551;-117.9985791;42;true;false;Vietnamese, Contemporary;Across from beautiful Huntington Beach, find this not-so-secret speakeasy tucked inside its parent restaurant, Bluegold, where it's difficult to avoid staring at the Pacific views. But the difference is palpable—LSXO is a bit cooler, louder and has a more defined personality. There are so many terrific dishes on offer that it's hard to go wrong and helpful servers will always steer you in the right direction. Don't miss the savory pork, shrimp and crab dumplings served alongside an incendiary, peanut-loaded black vinegar dressing. Then, a big steaming bowl of cháo loaded with crab, salted cod, white fish and egg whites, is silky and delicious.Getting a seat here can be tough, but good food makes this so much more than just a scene.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
12088;Medina;USA;San Diego;2850 El Cajon Blvd., San Diego, 92104, USA;32.7555336;-117.1323169;34;true;false;Moroccan, Mexican;This self-described “Moroccan-Baja kitchen” might sound unusual, but it’s full of bold, enticing flavors. Inspired by both her local environs and family heritage, Chef Alia Jaziri turn outs a fascinating fast-casual menu. Delicacies include Moroccan-spiced chicken tacos dressed with preserved lemon and tzatziki-inspired crema, or couscous bowls layered with merguez, black beans, queso fresco and toasted pepitas. For those less inclined to fusion fare, the shakshuka (poached eggs in a spicy North African tomato sauce) is a faithful rendition.Though simple, this space has a coastal feel from skylights, a roll-up door, and relaxing color scheme of white, cyan and teal. Linger in the calm with a serving of baklava and rosewater-topped Greek fro-yo.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12089;Tempura Endo;USA;Beverly Hills;9777 S. Santa Monica Blvd., Beverly Hills, 90210, USA;34.0675967;-118.4089392;86;true;false;Japanese, Tempura;There are few restaurants in the country dedicated solely to tempura, a Japanese style of cooking that is so much more than just “frying.” Tempura Endo in Beverly Hills is one such rare breed. Though there are tables woven throughout the restaurant, aim for a seat at the counter in front of the handmade copper cauldron. The tasting menus are on the pricey side, but such is the cost for a parade of vegetables and seafood dipped and fried delicately and served one at a time by the chef himself. Ribs of sweet corn, scallops from Hokkaido, broccolini, and snapper wrapped in shiso are all carefully placed in hot cottonseed oil and emerge with a lacy, almost transparent coating. At the meal’s end, opt for the tempura rice bowl over the soba noodles.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
12090;Asanebo;USA;Studio City;11941 Ventura Blvd., Studio City, 91604, USA;34.1433318;-118.3919412;67;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;With its spare design, fire-glazed stone pottery and even Hello Kitty dolls doubling as décor, everything about Asanebo’s look is appealing. There is certainly no dearth of sushi restaurants in this city, but this well-regarded favorite has been at it for more than two decades. Three omakase options open the menu, which then expands to an impressive, if somewhat dizzying five pages filled with everything from maki, house signature dishes and an entire page dedicated to desserts. With so many decisions, it’s best to stick to the daily specials, though do keep a close watch on the prices, which climb slowly but steadily.While the items may pander a bit to the Western palate and aren't known for razzle-dazzle, they remain a standby for good reason.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12091;kodō;USA;Los Angeles;710 S. Santa Fe Ave., Los Angeles, 90021, USA;34.0343252;-118.2299181;90;false;true;Izakaya, Sushi;It may be tucked inside a former firehouse, but kodō is more calm and cool than fiery. It's the kind of place where a boulder doubles as a desk and the abundant use of natural materials sets a serene tone. Choose from breezy, outdoor dining on the patio or come indoors for a menu that celebrates Kyoto cuisine, from robata to sushi, albeit with a California influence. The sushi and nigiri are so good that you won't even notice the trendy crowd snapping photos for their Instagram feed. Off-menu specials, such as the Japanese sea snail, are especially memorable, while sea bream and octopus are impeccable. A steaming bowl of little neck clams garlic and butter is dreamy. Up for something sweet? Cheesecake with passion fruit sauce and kinako crumble is a favorite.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12093;Juliet;USA;Culver City;8888 Washington Blvd., Culver City, 90232, USA;34.0267154;-118.3888379;98;false;true;French, Contemporary;Chic and French go hand in hand, especially at Juliet in Culver City. This gorgeous space has a contemporary French aesthetic with as much seating outdoors on the posh patio as indoors. The open kitchen buzzes all day, but dinner is where this team shines. Oysters, tartare or tuna carpaccio could kick off the meal, but the mousse au foie de volaille, with its delicate tart filled with chicken liver mousse, toasted hazelnuts and an apple gelee, is an auspicious beginning. Sea bream with ratatouille and pistou is simple but well executed, and pairs well with one of their many wines available by the glass. Don't skip dessert—whether you choose the éclair or the crème fraiche cheesecake with passion fruit gelee, it's a perfect ending to a delightful meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12094;Gusto Handcrafted Pasta & Pizza;USA;Seaside;1901 Fremont Blvd., Seaside, 93955, USA;36.6167466;-121.8418416;49;false;true;Italian-American;The surroundings may not be glamorous (Monterey airport is just a skip away), but this family-run establishment is a popular venue for large groups—and the proof is in the pasta. Gauging from the sizable menu of saucy, generously portioned Italian-American staples, no one is likely to leave their table hungry. Delightfully al dente house-made pastas are sure to banish any associations with mushy chain restaurant versions, and even hearty, rustic dishes like eggplant parmigiana get an extra touch of care. The from-scratch approach extends to the mozzarella, which is certainly worth sampling, whether as an antipasto or a topping for an array of thin-crust pizzas.Desserts, like cannoli with sweet mascarpone and ricotta, will tick the nostalgia box.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12095;San Laurel;USA;Los Angeles;100 S. Grand Ave., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.0557521;-118.2480445;22;true;true;Spanish, Contemporary;San Laurel is at the top of its game—quite literally, since this tenth-floor dazzler affords unobstructed views of Walt Disney Concert Hall from its polished perch. With soothing earth tones, lush greenery, a bustling bar and a breezy vibe courtesy of a fully opened facade, it looks and feels like an urban oasis. Expect modern Californian dishes with Spanish leanings from a talented team put together by visionary chef, José Andrés. A tartare turns tradition on its head when "beefsteak" is actually tomatoes in a perfect disc, topped with a "yolk" made of gelatinous tomato water. A rack of lamb, cut into four, is plated around a circle of red mole sauce and a half baby eggplant, roasted and topped with pea tendrils and puffed rice. Desserts really shine, as in an ethereal pistachio cake with fragrant lime zest and sweet strawberries matched by a tart mascarpone sorbet.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12097;Cento Pasta Bar;USA;Los Angeles;4921 W. Adams Blvd., Los Angeles, 90016, USA;34.0327104;-118.3476019;87;true;false;Italian;Tucked away in West Adams, this one-time pop-up gone brick-and-mortar from Chef Avner Levi feels timely but has a great laidback vibe. The courtyard, capped off by a large tree set with twinkling lights, is an absolute stunner.  The menu leans Italian-contemporary, with selections including antipasti, mole-braised ossobuco made with yogurt-marinated lamb, but as the name suggests, pasta takes center stage. A gorgeous twirl of beet pasta in a beet and brown butter sauce with poppy seeds is finished with a quenelle of whipped ricotta for a dish that is both beautiful and delicious. Desserts are equally tempting. Try the Key lime pavlova, with a round meringue of lime curd and lime sorbet, for a refreshingly sweet-tart finish.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12100;Silvers Omakase;USA;Santa Barbara;224 Helena Ave., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.415283;-119.6920226;59;true;true;Sushi;With just a handful of seats and a small staff, this omakase from Chef Lennon Silvers Lee is ever-changing. Some things change daily, while others change weekly, but one thing you can always expect is well-executed dishes made with rice from Japan that is milled in house, and fish that is sourced both locally and from Japan and then dry aged.Arrive early and enjoy a glass of sparkling wine before being called in, as all guests are seated and served at the same time. Enjoy one or two small dishes before a parade of nigiri, which may include hamachi, shima aji, as well as bluefin tuna. Their uni rice is deliciously mixed with wasabi and topped with masago arare for a bit of crunch, marking the end of the savory dishes before a dessert of sorbet made in house.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
12101;Fishing with Dynamite;USA;Manhattan Beach;1148 Manhattan Ave., Manhattan Beach, 90266, USA;33.8853648;-118.4110518;86;false;false;Seafood;This tight and warm seafood spot is located just down the block from the ocean. Inside, it has a decidedly beachy vibe, flooded with sunlight and colors that make it feel cozy even when it's loud and busy. Raw bar dishes comprise half the menu, and if the list of first-class oysters, clams, and lobsters seems overwhelming, the friendly staff will help make sense of it all. Dishes such as wild New Caledonian prawns with garlic butter and fragrant lemon jasmine rice or seared diver scallops with Japanese curry sweet potato coulis are indicative of the delicious, decidedly uncomplicated cooking available here.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12102;Phởholic;USA;Westminster;14932 Bushard St., Westminster, 92683, USA;33.7458787;-117.9633123;27;true;true;Vietnamese, Regional Cuisine;We'll give you one guess as to what makes Phởholic a much-talked-about spot. Yes, it is the pho, and it's the reason why everyone flocks to this Westminster original (two other locations also lure slurpers). It's a classic shop that attracts everyone from grandparents to Gen Z'ers, all here to partake in the beef-focused pho. Though the prices are gentle, the kitchen never skimps, using only high quality products. Diners take their pick of noodle style and meat from the beginners and adventurers menus, then wait for the large metal bowls of steaming comfort to arrive. The scent of anise fills the air, while the sweet broth soothes the soul. If ordering from the Holic menu, prepare to leave stuffed beyond expectation.;Car park;[]
12103;Kajiken;USA;San Mateo;112 S. B St., San Mateo, 94401, USA;37.5667007;-122.3239319;33;true;true;Noodles, Asian;Originally from Nagoya, Japan, Kajiken has landed on the West Coast with the promise of shaking up your noodle routine with abura soba. This noodle dish is similar to ramen but eschews the broth, instead punching up the flavor courtesy of a special blend of oils and sauces. The springy noodles are made in house (score a seat facing the windowed noodle-making area) and are satisfying enough to eat plain, but with nine varieties, why? Toppings range from ajitama and chives to kimchi, ume or spicy mentaiko. Tables are topped with a well-chosen selection of vinegar, hot sauces and powdered nori for adjusting to your liking. The menu is rounded out with a small selection of karaage, takoyaki, edamame (in three variations), gyoza and sides.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12104;Catania;USA;La Jolla;7863 Girard Ave., Ste. 301, La Jolla, 92037, USA;32.846547;-117.27404;43;true;true;Italian;In the historic heart of La Jolla, find this cool and hip retreat on the top floor of the Plaza Center. The artfully designed dining room features sunny Mediterranean colors and ceramic tiles. A large, elegant terrace offers panoramic coastline views.Come early for their aperitivo (cocktails and snacks), but make sure you stay to explore this kitchen’s modern twists. Start with a daily salad special, featuring lovely flavors like beet chips and butternut squash, crowned by ahi tuna crudo with poppy seeds and basil leaves. Then dive into a Neapolitan-style pizza from the wood-burning oven, or decadent pastas such as orecchiette mingled with slow-braised duck ragù accented by tomato coulis, porcini mushrooms and freshly grated parmesan.;Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12105;Shunji.;USA;Santa Monica;3003 Ocean Park Blvd., Santa Monica, 90405, USA;34.0202154;-118.4537626;97;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Freshly relocated, Shunji lives on as a notable Japanese counter manned by a chef whose experience runs deep. Inside, a sliding wood partition divides the space into two sections—both standard minimalist in décor, starring beige walls, a dark brown ceiling and that beloved blonde matte wood counter. While the two counters both offer an excellent omakase, the smaller counter run by LA sushi veteran, Chef Shunji Nakao, is the one to beat. Begin with a handful of bites, like sesame tofu or smoked King mackerel with dots of green onion and ginger sauce. Then move on to the nigiri, of which sea perch and sea eel are both exemplary. Finish with soup tailed by dessert. The quality of product and flavor combinations are anything but standard (as are the prices).;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12106;Café Romanat;USA;Oakland;462 Santa Clara Ave., Oakland, 94610, USA;37.811855;-122.248276;79;true;false;Ethiopian;In a stretch of Oakland that teems with Ethiopian restaurants, Café Romanat is a standout, thanks to its deliciously spiced dishes served in generous portions. Locals (including some Ethiopian families) fill the small room that is set with traditional low stools, woven tables and features colorful fabric curtains and artwork.Order up a homegrown beer, honey wine or a nutty ground flax or sesame seed juice to pair with the sambusas, triangular pastries stuffed with piquant jalapeño-spiked lentils. All the combination platters, served on spongy, slightly sour injera, are perfect for sharing. And the veggie combo, with dishes like sautéed collard greens, lentils in smoky berbere and split peas with turmeric and ginger, will delight any crowd.;Air conditioning;[]
12107;Burmatown;USA;Corte Madera;18 Tamalpais Dr., Corte Madera, 94925, USA;37.9261343;-122.5290448;94;false;false;Burmese;Bypass the tired Asian-fusion offerings and head straight for the authentic Burmese dishes at this out-of-the-way cutie. A nutty, crunchy and flavorful tea leaf salad is the perfect answer to a hot summer day, while hearty spiced potato-stuffed samosas and fresh, springy egg noodles tossed with barbecue pork and fried garlic chips will warm your soul in the cooler months.Given the high quality of its food, it’s no surprise that Burmatown is Corte Madera’s most popular neighbor: it’s big with local families from the surrounding residences who pack every single table, attended to by warm servers. If you’re willing to make a special trip to this charming bright-orange bungalow, the laid-back vibe will have you feeling right at home.;;[]
12109;Bistro Na’s;USA;Temple City;9055 Las Tunas Dr., Ste. 105, Temple City, 91780, USA;34.1048803;-118.0712093;100;true;true;Chinese, Beijing Cuisine;The shopping block exterior off Rosemead Boulevard might be unremarkable, but the expansive interior, splashed with red, gold and blue, is as comfortable as it is eye-catching. The culinary offerings are no less opulent, deriving from royal Manchu cuisine, first established in the imperial courts of the Qing dynasty, and boasting no shortage of luxury ingredients. The menu has a plentitude of options, but you’re likely to see many neighboring tables enjoying a signature lightly battered shrimp, fried together with their tender shells to an airy crispness, and diced black pepper Angus beef is similarly popular (and indulgent). Perhaps the wisest course is to come with a large group, the better to sample as many of the enticing dishes as possible.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12110;Hidden Fish;USA;San Diego;4764 Convoy St., San Diego, 92111, USA;32.8283394;-117.1536932;75;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;You’ll be on the clock at this tiny sushi spot, where the omakase is priced at a straightforward dollar per minute—50 for 12 nigiri, or 90 for 18. But despite such punctuality, you will savor every bite here. In fact, you’ll find yourself slowing down to savor each and every creation from the talented chefs. However, seats here are hard to come by so be sure to reserve ahead of time or risk serious FOMO.Like other top-tier sushiyas, this one sources from across the globe: Peruvian scallops, Santa Barbara uni, and of course, plenty of Japanese species. A chalkboard menu keeps diners apprised of the current lineup, and for those who are still peckish after their tasting, there’s a bonus menu of handrolls and special seasonal nigiri for further sampling.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12111;The Lobster;USA;Santa Monica;1602 Ocean Ave., Santa Monica, 90401, USA;34.011154;-118.49501;56;true;false;Seafood;True to its name, this lovely perch overlooking the Santa Monica pier has earned its reputation for great American seafood, thanks to its focus on Maine lobsters and much more. Don’t let its beachy location lure you into thinking that this is a tourist trap. Tightly spaced tables don’t leave much room for privacy and the service seems focused on efficiency, but those expansive views and steaming seafood more than compensate.Lobsters arrive at the height of temptation—find them beautifully steamed until the meat is so incredibly tender, rendering that side of melted butter all but superfluous. Hearty seared crab cakes have a crisp exterior and are generously filled with meat, served alongside peppery arugula, fennel salad and remoulade.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12112;Parks BBQ;USA;Los Angeles;955 S. Vermont Ave., Ste.G, Los Angeles, 90006, USA;34.053967;-118.29194;23;true;true;Korean, Barbecue;Lauded as one of the city's most cherished destinations for Korean barbecue, Park's has been luring patrons for well over an age. This is evidenced by the photo wall of famous chefs, actors and politicians right by the front door. The interior is simple, as efficient, friendly servers do most of the work managing the grills and flipping and slicing meat. From bulgogi to galbi, the meat is prime quality and often lightly marinated. Pricier American Wagyu will appeal to bigger spenders, and the acclaimed garlic-soy-brown sugar marinade is ace with short ribs. Crisp kimchi pancakes served hot on cast-iron skillets as well as cold noodles are proper foils for the protein. Lunch specials are particularly popular and offer both good value and variety.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12113;Siamo Napoli;USA;San Diego;3959 30th St., San Diego, 92104, USA;32.749668;-117.1299206;63;true;true;Italian;Flavio Piromallo has another hit on his hands with this hip North Park District spot. In keeping with its trendy surrounds, the décor sports an industrial-chic look with concrete floors, exposed pipes and a massive photographic elegy to Sophia Loren. Laid-back, cool service completes the experience. The modern affect belies its classic Southern Italian cooking. Neapolitan-style pizza is a favorite, and the homemade pastas have terrific flavor—ravioli con manzana is a delicious signature. Mandorle al Caffé, a spongy almond cake with a layer of espresso custard surrounded by a duo of white and black chocolate sauce, is a decadent way to end a satisfying meal. Lunchtime leans quiet, but come for dinner for a lively and entertaining scene.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12114;Le Comptoir;USA;Los Angeles;3606 W. 6th St., Los Angeles, 90020, USA;34.0634658;-118.300451;23;true;true;Californian, Vegetarian;Find this hidden dining room tucked inside the historic Hotel Normandie and helmed by Chef Gary Menes along with a passionate crew. The name, French for “counter,” is a literal description of the space, which seats no more than ten guests before the stainless-steel kitchen.Dining here is a personal experience, emphasized by the fact that the chef is cooking and plating everything right before your eyes. Dishes are handled with care, with the chef focused almost entirely on vegetables—protein plays a subsidiary role. Keeping that in mind, anticipate the likes of a savory carrot velouté or morsel of cured squash, both of which are as satisfying as the supplemental grass-fed beef. Much of the produce arrives fresh from the chef’s Long Beach garden.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12115;La Bicyclette;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;29 Dolores St., Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93921, USA;36.5539364;-121.9225771;18;false;false;European;This is a quintessential bistro and relaxed neighborhood spot in the heart of charming Carmel-by-the-Sea. The quirky corner space offers petite but comfortable wooden chairs and tables, set beneath hanging copper pots and, of course, a bicycle or two.First and foremost, the kitchen focuses on comforting seasonal cuisine with a California-Mediterranean slant, plus a handful of pizzas and fantastic breads fired in their wood-burning oven. At the same time, they are dedicated to beloved French classics: picture fork-tender duck confit, set on a bed of earthy Puy lentils with halved Brussels sprouts. At the end, a golden, flaky and buttery-sweet tarte Tatin filled with caramelized apples and finished with a tuft of whipped cream is absolutely delicious.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12116;Craft & Commerce;USA;San Diego;675 W. Beech St., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.72086;-117.16902;53;true;true;American;Channel your best Ernest Hemingway before entering this place, designed to the hilt and a feast for the eyes with its library-meets-hunting lodge look. From its mounted trophies to the taxidermy specimens on loan from the Natural History Museum, this may not be the wisest pick for your PETA-supporting pal, but it definitely appeals to the trendy set.The kitchen dishes out contemporary comfort food with glimmers of Asian influences. The menu is packed with hearty selections. Dig in to a dish of plump mussels in a thick red Thai coconut curry studded with pan-seared fennel slices, roasted garlic slivers and fried spicy chorizo. Bone marrow with Fresno chili relish and toasted milk bread or confit duck leg tacos up the ante.;Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12117;Barra Santos;USA;Los Angeles;1215 Cypress Ave., Los Angeles, 90065, USA;34.0955433;-118.2281252;16;false;false;Portuguese;Snag a seat outside or in at this small, no reservations restaurant in Cypress Park. Inside, the best seats are at the bar with a view into the kitchen. The focused menu is Portuguese and even features some family recipes. Plenty of items are designed for sharing, including their crispy and tender bacalhau fritters with salt cod, potato, and caramelized onion, or charred cabbage over a bed of white beans studded with Iberico pork and garlic butter sauce. Their whole branzino with a flavorful green sauce made with pumpkin seeds, roasted serranos, and tomatillos is an absolute must. Finally, spiced almond cake with whipped crème fraîche is a nice ending.;;[]
12118;Anajak Thai;USA;Sherman Oaks;14704 Ventura Blvd., Sherman Oaks, 91403, USA;34.1517478;-118.4535952;47;false;true;Thai, Contemporary;Now in its fifth decade of operation, this beloved family-owned fixture has never been more in-demand. Much of its current acclaim owes, no doubt, to second-generation Chef Justin Pichetrungsi, whose approach hits a sweet spot between minding tradition and walking his own boldly idiosyncratic path. This is amply demonstrated on freewheeling “Thai Taco Tuesdays,” a no-reservations event that draws lines around the block. For additional excitement, one weekend per month, a unique omakase experience is surely one of the city’s most coveted reservations. Whether sampling spot-on versions of Thai classics, or delving into more rarified fare, the warm service, memorable wine list and singularly buzzy atmosphere make for a one-of-a-kind experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12119;Mägo;USA;Oakland;3762 Piedmont Ave., Oakland, 94611, USA;37.8233782;-122.2561959;51;true;true;Californian;Chef Mark Liberman may draw his culinary inspiration from some of the greatest kitchens in the world, but rest assured that his food isn't about fireworks. Instead, this kitchen team is focused on the unpretentious charms of great seasonal produce and a well-handled wood grill.Mägo's carte is heavy on casual small plates, such as ratatouille on toasted zucchini bread or crispy soft-shell crab with peaches and plums. And yet, there are fun surprises, too, like the kimchi-style sungold tomatoes that crown a pile of pasta alla chitarra. The nightly “for the table” meat option, like rabbit saddle or grilled tri-tip, is a surefire winner. Save room for such deliciously rustic desserts as corn pudding with blueberries and lime granita.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
12121;Pomet;USA;Oakland;4029 Piedmont Ave., Oakland, 94611, USA;37.8259318;-122.2530358;86;true;true;Californian;The phrase "farm-to-table" is by now undoubtedly well-worn, but here the cliché takes on a literal dimension. Proprietor Aomboon Deasy is also a farmer, best known as the owner of K&J Orchards, a longtime darling of Bay Area farmers' markets thanks to its top-notch tree fruit. At Pomet, the menu is unsurprisingly ingredient-driven, proudly proclaiming the myriad local farms that supply it (in addition to Deasy's own). Whether it’s oysters with Niitaka pear and cider mignonette, or pasta filled with a puree of “ugly mushrooms” and sauced with a celery root miso butter, simplicity is a virtue when ingredients are this good. Case in point: the meal ends with a complimentary slice of whatever seasonal fruit is currently at its peak.;Wheelchair access;[]
12122;Killer Noodle;USA;Los Angeles;2030 Sawtelle Blvd., Los Angeles, 90025, USA;34.0404507;-118.4430102;84;false;false;Japanese, Ramen;This sister spot to ramen palace Tsujita specializes in tan tan ramen, a Japanese favorite that’s equal parts tantanmen (dipping ramen) and spicy Sichuan dan dan noodles. The original bowl is light and gently herbaceous, with bold notes of peanut and garlic accenting the ground pork and tofu, while the “downtown” version is tangier and nuttier. If you’d rather slurp sans soup, either bowl can be ordered “dry” as well.The “killer” in the restaurant's moniker comes from the range of spice levels offered to diners—opt for the six out of six, and you’ll be supremely grateful for the pitcher of water provided to each table. All those heaping portions of chili oil are matched by the casual, cheerful dining room, which is dressed in shades of screaming red.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12123;Pizzetta 211;USA;San Francisco;211 23rd Ave., San Francisco, 94121, USA;37.7837368;-122.4829596;48;true;false;Pizza;This shoebox-sized pizzeria may reside in the far reaches of the Richmond, but it’s easily identifiable by the crowds hovering on the sidewalk to score a table. Once inside, you’ll be greeted by pizzaiolos throwing pies in the tiny exhibition kitchen—ask for a counter seat to get a better view.The thin, chewy, blistered pizzettas each serve one, making it easy to share several varieties. Weekly specials utilize ingredients like seasonal produce, house-made sausage and fresh farm eggs, while standbys include a pie topped with wild arugula, creamy mascarpone and San Marzano tomato sauce. Whatever you do, arrive early: once the kitchen’s out of dough they close for the day, and the omnipresent lines mean the goods never last too long.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12124;The Fishery;USA;San Diego;5040 Cass St., San Diego, 92109, USA;32.8066725;-117.2547654;20;true;false;Seafood;Nestled within a restored mid-century warehouse in North Pacific Beach, The Fishery is exactly what it claims. As if you needed further proof, there’s even a premier seafood market housed at its center.You would be hard-pressed to find fish fresher than the selection offered here and the open kitchen does wonders with this market-driven menu overseen by these talented chefs, who let the quality product shine bright. Think—ahi tuna poke prepped with just a hint of soy sauce, sesame seeds and chili. Stuffed with crisp-fried cod fillets, rice, beans, guacamole and served with homemade chips, the cod burrito makes a hearty and hefty meal—just right for the many surfers who come here after tackling the waves at nearby Tourmaline Canyon Surfing Park.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12125;Quarters BBQ;USA;Los Angeles;3465 W. 6th St., Los Angeles, 90020, USA;34.063614;-118.29773;23;true;false;Korean, Barbecue;LA's barbecue scene is forever brimming with options, so it can be hard to ferret out the more desirable spots. However, the lines wrapping around this upscale, longstanding gem are a sure sign you’ve chosen well. Make sure to make a reservation, or try to sneak in for lunch or an early dinner to avoid a wait.Its name reflects how the menu is organized—offering meats in quarter-pound portions, thereby allowing diners to sample an ample array of marinated cuts. Come hungry or bring a friend, as solo diners are required to order at least a couple orders of meats. Kick things off with the sizzling pork skin, loaded with rich collagen and excellent seasoning. Four strips of beautifully marbled boneless short rib are then presented on a platter, judiciously seasoned and cooked to pink perfection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12126;SPQR;USA;San Francisco;1911 Fillmore St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7873703;-122.4336712;94;false;true;Italian, Contemporary;Kitschy and boisterous with modern cooking, this dining room is always packed. The space is slender while a soaring ceiling, skylights and open kitchen brighten the mood.Chef Matthew Accarrino's mingling of Italian and Californian elements makes for satisfying cooking, and the best of the season's produce is highlighted in the five-course prix-fixe menu. The meal might begin with a crespelle with pork belly, fennel and persimmon, or a chicken liver terrina with rhubarb and wood sorrel.  Of course, choosing between house-made pastas like squid ink perciatelli with octopus cream and chili pequin or spinach pappardelle with mushroom and fried egg might seem challenging, but it's difficult to go wrong.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12129;Charcoal Venice;USA;Los Angeles;425 Washington Blvd., Los Angeles, 90292, USA;33.981514;-118.462845;56;true;false;American, Steakhouse;Chef/owner Josiah Citrin works his magic at this casually upscale grill, where nearly everything is cooked over the fire. Wafts of aromatic charred meat greet guests before they’ve even made it through the door. The menu may be inspired by a backyard barbecue, but the décor is a contemporary mix of concrete walls, beige booths and modern artwork.Steaks come with ramekins of sauce like creamy and smoky choron, in addition to the trio of signature condiments on the table. However, this meat is too flavorful to really need anything. Diners may be here for the steaks, but those in the know also order the cabbage baked in embers, served with lemon-sumac yogurt.The bar area is bustling and loud, thanks to the list of happy hour specials.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12130;Beast + Bounty;USA;Sacramento;1701 R St., Sacramento, 95811, USA;38.5689202;-121.4870595;18;true;false;Californian;With its good looks and regal food, this bright haunt is already a hot spot. Its hip, industrial-chic interior is modern and plain gorgeous, with hanging green plants, white painted pipes and exposed brick. Incredibly fresh, creative Californian fare reigns supreme on this menu, and the dishes turned out are well-balanced and neatly executed. Try the delicate pickled fritto misto, a crispy tempura mix of rotating, seasonal vegetables (think sweet potatoes, okra, or cauliflower) paired with a vibrant pink beet “aïoli” made from aquafaba. Another crowd favorite is the juicy half chicken from the hearth, served with zucchini purée, roasted baby squash and basil oil.The Tobacco Road, infused with white oak smoke, is their updated take on the Old Fashioned.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12131;Picco;USA;Larkspur;320 Magnolia Ave., Larkspur, 94939, USA;37.9339075;-122.5357174;72;true;true;Contemporary;Picco is Italian for “summit,” and this charming Larkspur hilltop home has long been a beacon among Marin County diners. Chef/owner Bruce Hill is a true local-food devotee: his Italian-influenced fare heaps on Marin ingredients like the fresh turnips that dot his silky-smooth duck tortelli, or the Meyer lemon yogurt and beets that sit atop a nourishing kale salad. The “Marin Mondays” menu is a particular steal.The precise staff moves ably through the busy dining room, carrying bowls of creamy risotto made on the half-hour. With a high ceiling and exposed brick walls, the vibe is graceful but never fussy, making this the perfect setting for couples and groups of friends who congregate here.Also check out Pizzeria Picco next door.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12132;Tūmbi;USA;Santa Monica;115 Santa Monica Blvd., Santa Monica, 90401, USA;34.014547;-118.4976517;60;false;true;Indian, Contemporary;Just a block from the bustle of the Santa Monica Promenade, Tumbi feels worlds away, offering Indian cooking in an industrial-chic setting. All of their proteins benefit from being prepared in a clay tandoor, which adds to their complexity, and of course there's butter chicken and palak paneer to satisfy Western palates. Make sure to get a dosa, also available stuffed, as in the masala dosa with a filling of mashed potatoes that are spiced and mixed with onion and cashew nuts. Desserts are especially unique—envision deconstructed carrot halwa and a "dessert dosa" served with creamy Nutella.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12133;Ronan;USA;Los Angeles;7315 Melrose Ave., Los Angeles, 90046, USA;34.08361;-118.34922;54;true;false;Italian;Aim for the two-story floral mural to find this Italian favorite with a dive bar-feel and plenty of LA style. Sit in the lovely patio, or head inside to the black marble bar. Other options include booths as well as an attractive communal table crafted from a varnished wood slab. Diners can expect to see pizza dough stretched, blenders whirring and the wood-fired oven crackling, all of which contribute to Ronan's swank allure.Come for their hand-stretched Neopolitan pizza, as well as their shared plates using seasonal produce and ingredients, with appetizers like their spring arancini with pastrami-spiced maitake with English peas and garlic, or their charred broccolini with their house blend of za'atar, fresh mint, and a Meyer lemon aïoli.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12134;Yoichi’s;USA;Santa Barbara;230 E. Victoria St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.426804;-119.70299;79;false;true;Japanese;This quaint little house run by a husband-wife team just happens to be one of the area's favorite spots for traditional Japanese dining. This should be no surprise, as Chef Yoichi Kawabata’s background includes cooking at Nobu Tokyo. The dining room is quiet and serene, filled with white walls and dark wood tables—there is no sushi counter. Service is both friendly and informative.The seven-course menu respects all the rules of kaiseki dining, using top seasonal ingredients and pristine, top-class fish. Meals begin with an array of four appetizers (zenzai) including delectable Wagyu beef that has been grilled and glazed in a sansho pepper sauce. Then grilled duck breast may be prepared with perfect tenderness in sweet soy sauce with green peppers.;Air conditioning;[]
12135;Leopardo;USA;Los Angeles;460 S. La Brea Ave., Los Angeles, 90036, USA;34.0649997;-118.3439494;16;true;true;Californian, Seafood;Chef Joshua Skenes is back on the scene with Leopardo, a likeable spot with a laidback feel where the menu leans on seafood with a few pizzas thrown in for good measure. Come with a group to sample a variety, beginning with crispy red flint waffles with bordier butter and maple syrup, and splurge by adding Ossetra caviar aged for six months with country bacon salt. Then, tuck into a raw bar offering, perhaps the live prawn crudo with a kumquat and habanero sauce. A classic margherita pizza is never a bad idea or opt for their Hello Satan pizza with wild honey, chili, salumi, and herbs. End on a sweet note with tiramisu or a wild blackberry hand pie, made even better by adding soft serve. Cocktails like "Rhubarb like a Negroni" or a "Barbeque Old Fashioned" are impressive.;Air conditioning;[]
12136;Fish & Bird Sousaku Izakaya;USA;Berkeley;2451 Shattuck Ave., Berkeley, 94704, USA;37.8648544;-122.2673266;81;false;true;Japanese, Izakaya;On Shattuck Avenue, this stylish gem from Chef Asuka Uchida brings it with a bang. The building is painted blue with dark tiles along the bottom, silver-framed windows, and a red neon sign. If that doesn't sound on trend, the modern izakaya menu does the trick with a panoply of dishes. It's a modest space, with a shimmering open kitchen, bar featuring floating shelves of bottles, and charcoal is the dominant palette.On the menu, diners are privy to a myriad of staples like hot pot, skewers, rice boxes, and sandos. While the karaage is prize-worthy, the team's skill runs across the board. From tempura to tofu, they are clearly doing something special. To wit: green bean fritters with sansho curry, followed by creamy tofu enriched with ginger and scallion.;;[]
12137;Angelini Osteria;USA;Los Angeles;7313 Beverly Blvd., Los Angeles, 90036, USA;34.076214;-118.34914;64;true;false;Italian;The delicious cooking at this humble osteria has been drawing crowds for more than two decades—and in a city that rolls out the red carpet for the hottest new thing, that’s no small feat. This simple, authentic charmer is the real deal, right down to the red scarf-bedecked chef in the kitchen as well as those regulars sipping and supping on Italian wines and fresh pasta in the dining room.Though the service brigade leans old school, their generous spirit defies the gruff stereotype. Menu favorites include expertly grilled calamari, linguini with sea urchin and a perfectly authentic tiramisu for dessert. On your way out, be sure to pop into the café next door for a jar or two of Chef Gino Angelini’s sauce and bring the goodness home.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12139;Vaca;USA;Costa Mesa;695 Town Center Dr., Ste. 170, Costa Mesa, 92626, USA;33.692516;-117.8851;64;true;false;Spanish, Contemporary;Courtesy of Chef Amar Santana, this cool and rustic tapas bar offers consistently pleasing food and an extensive list of sherries and Spanish wines amid a quirky setting (the banquettes are decorated with jokes). In addition to the beautiful bar area, guests may sit in two outdoor areas or the main dining room with views into the semi-open kitchen. The lunchtime prix fixe is a great deal, though it would mean skipping their wonderful array of tapas and paellas. Standouts include the bikini sandwich, layering cured Jamón Ibérico, Manchego cheese, and a bit of truffle oil into pretty little piping-hot grilled sandwiches. Croquettas de pollo tucked with shredded white meat are perfectly seasoned and fried to a golden crisp.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12140;Chosun Galbee;USA;Los Angeles;3330 W. Olympic Blvd., Los Angeles, 90019, USA;34.0526;-118.310326;62;false;true;Korean, Barbecue;There are elements of reverence and seriousness to dining here, which is an asset for anyone seeking authentic Korean food. The warm servers all wear traditional garments to heighten the classic feel, while also donning earpieces in the upscale modern setting. The wait may seem long, but the food is worth it.The menu, too, can seem extensive with familiar classics from the barbecue lineup, but these are then elevated by the kitchen’s distinct care and skill. The sheer variety of banchan is a feat here. This is also the perfect place for large groups on the hunt for superbly tender meat to grill on the spot. Galbee junullk is a standout, presenting short ribs prepared with the house’s own “secret” soy sauce, then seared before your eyes with onions and mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12142;Mensho;USA;San Francisco;672 Geary St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.7867072;-122.4143032;92;false;true;Japanese, Ramen;This little ramen shop from the chef behind the highly popular Tokyo outposts isn't new, but even after years of operation, lines still form before the doors open to snag one of the 28 communal seats in the small, no-frills room. Only true aficionados can say if the ramen is worth it, but the tori paitan is one undeniably spectacular bowl, packed with springy, chewy noodles and outstanding duck chashu in a luxuriously creamy and umami-rich broth. Just know you’ll be asked to slurp it down quickly: you're allotted one hour and the hungry, huddled masses outside are anxious to take your seat.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12143;jū-ni;USA;San Francisco;1335 Fulton St., San Francisco, 94117, USA;37.77672;-122.43886;89;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;The word "jūni” is Japanese for “twelve,” which also happens to be the number of seats available in this petite, omakase-only spot, housed just off the busy Divisadero corridor. They’re a young, lively crew, often led by Chef/owner Geoffrey Lee, and they’ve designed this space with a crowd of similarly young, moneyed professionals in mind. A meal may begin with a tasting of seasonal vegetables—think tomatoes over edamame hummus—before proceeding to an array of nigiri. Standouts include sakura masu with a salt-cured cherry blossom leaf, buttery Hokkaido scallop and the signature ikura—cured, then finished with a grating of velvety frozen monkfish liver. The meal finishes with a surprisingly gentle send-off: sweet, tender mochi dabbed with adzuki bean paste.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
12144;Utzutzu;USA;Alameda;1428 Park St., Alameda, 94501, USA;37.7649366;-122.2420257;38;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;It may take a little digging to find this place, since there are no signs and you must ascend a steep flight of stairs, but once inside, you'll discover an ambitious Japanese restaurant where the kitchen deserves as much praise as the eight-seat sushi counter. The okimari menu begins with a clean and simple dish of ohitashi, or blanched romesco in a dashi broth, then continues with nanbanzuke, a lightly fried and intensely flavorful fish. Skillful sashimi and a selection of sushi follow, including horse mackerel brushed with sweet soy and a dot of yuzu, seared Japanese whitefish, okra  topped with bonito flakes and fried Japanese eggplant, which takes a humble ingredient and steals the show. Black sesame ice cream rounds out the meal.;Counter dining;[]
12147;Belotti Ristorante e Bottega;USA;Oakland;5403 College Ave., Oakland, 94618, USA;37.840256;-122.25138;17;false;false;Italian;Pasta aficionados will find paradiso in this petite and casual restaurant-turned-enoteca, set on a busy but bucolic stretch of Rockridge’s main artery. Boasting an impressive passel of regulars who frequently park at the bar to chat with the owner in Italian between bites, Belotti dabbles in the traditional cuisine of Piemonte.Envision such hearty dishes as brasato—braised beef with mushrooms served over polenta and finished with a nebbiolo reduction. House-made pastas are also a major attraction here, including the heirloom grain spaghettini in a tomato sauce with creamy burrata. But more unexpected dishes excel as well: try the delicious butter lettuce salad with lemon and pine nuts, or the decadent tortino, a spinach flan with egg yolk and truffle.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12148;Pèppoli;USA;Pebble Beach;2700 17 Mile Dr., Pebble Beach, 93953, USA;36.6124137;-121.9418838;29;true;true;Italian, American;The ocean and golf course views may be pure California, but a meal here is all about Tuscany. Named for the Pèppoli Vineyard in Italy and owned by the legendary Antinori family of winemakers, this restaurant strives to deliver rustic cooking to their discerning Pebble Beach clientele. Many of their own labels are featured here, as a perfect complement to the cuisine.The dining room transports guests back to the homeland with rooms styled to resemble an exclusive Italian estate serving a menu of wood-fired Tuscan food. Expect hearty but skillfully prepared dishes like hand-crafted orecchiette tossed in vibrant green pesto, mixing puréed kale and broccoli with house-made sausages. Save room for excellent desserts like tiramisu and other traditional treats.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12149;République;USA;Hollywood;624 S. La Brea Ave., Hollywood, 90036, USA;34.0641162;-118.3438101;63;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, American;In some ways, this all-day hit feels like a city of its own. With soaring ceilings, beautiful brickwork and sunny skylights, the cavernous space is a beehive of activity. In the morning, freshly baked pastries and breads draw long lines. Come evening, the open kitchen is in full swing, working quickly to serve wave after wave of diners. The tightly curated menu explores the cuisine of Southern Europe through exceptional ingredients, many of them local. Trays loaded with warm potato and leek beignets or toast points stacked with eggs and uni land on almost every table. Baguettes with superb French butter inevitably follow. Dungeness crab risotto, braised wagyu beef cheek and duck with baby beets round out an experience that never fails to satisfy.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12150;Yong Su San;USA;Los Angeles;950 S. Vermont Ave., Los Angeles, 90006, USA;34.053997;-118.29128;61;true;true;Korean, Regional Cuisine;Specializing in the storied dishes that were once served to Korea’s royals, this mini Seoul-based chain stands out from the K-town crowd. This is largely thanks to its hanbok-attired servers and warren of private rooms, featuring an expansive foyer with a counter and carved wooden seats with plush cushions. Most diners arrive in large groups to sample set menus that are available at various price levels. However, dining à la carte is a great option as well.Staples like bibimbap and colorful japchae noodles hit their marks, as does the galbijjim—sweet and savory braised short ribs—and all come with a generous assortment of banchan, including several types of kimchi. As a grace note, you might be given a bowl of sujeonggwa, a chilled cinnamon-flavored punch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12152;Casanova;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;95 5th Ave., Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93921, USA;36.5568435;-121.921233;97;false;true;European, Californian;This historic 1920s cottage—once owned by Charlie Chaplin’s personal chef—is marked by a bike parked out front with lavender flowing from the basket. Before opening in 1987, the family remodeled the building after their Belgian farmhouse and even dug down to replicate their wine cellar, which today houses a notable collection. Its setting, just a block off quaint Carmel’s main drag, makes dining here seem all the more relaxing and charming. A private room invites 2-8 people to enjoy the chef’s prix-fixe on Vincent Van Gogh’s very own dining table.The rustic French and Italian cooking features deliciously simple dishes, ranging from the likes of hearty cannelloni to a peak-season grilled peach topped with pickled onion, toasted almonds and torn basil.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12153;Akaoni;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;Mission St., Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93921, USA;36.5559718;-121.9210771;66;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;With few seats, limited hours and a two-person staff, snagging a table at this no-frills sushiya can be a real challenge. But those willing to make the effort will be rewarded, because Akaoni offers some of the region’s most pristine sushi—at surprisingly down-to-earth prices.A 12-piece chef’s choice platter is offered for those who’d like to put their fate in the kitchen’s hands, but savvy diners know to go straight for the options on the daily specials board—like buttery local spot prawns served to order from a tank right behind the omnipresent counter. Simply plated and nicely cut, the nigiri far outshines most of the cooked dishes. But if you’re looking to supplement your sushi, the light and crispy vegetable tempura is a worthy option.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12154;Fiorella;USA;San Francisco;2339 Clement St., San Francisco, 94121, USA;37.78197;-122.48453;15;true;false;Italian;In the foggy Outer Richmond, this casual neighborhood pizzeria is as hot as its wood-fired oven. Local families come in droves to share a pie or plate of pasta in the compact dining room, set amidst funky wallpaper depicting a bevy of Bay Area landmarks and legendary locals. The chewy, blistered crusts are loaded with flavor, whether in a classic Margherita or salami pie with provolone and red chili. Throw in a seasonal salad, a pile of chicken wings tossed in a Calabrian chili-honey glaze, and a glass of Italian wine from the compact list. Save room for the warm almond and Meyer lemon ricotta cake, which gets toasted alongside other pies in the oven.Two other locations, in Russian Hill and The Sunset District, are just as popular as the original.;Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12155;Élephante;USA;Santa Monica;1332 2nd St., Santa Monica, 90401, USA;34.0153998;-118.4978304;77;true;true;Contemporary;It would be easy to write off this rooftop haunt as just another trendy spot, but that would be a shame as the gorgeous space comes with some serious kitchen talent. The cactus garden is a lush perch, but ocean views from the sunset room, replete with natural word and stone, are unbeatable.Contemporary small plates infused with Southern Mediterranean influences is what this team does best, and diners would do well to share. Dishes deliver deliciously surprising flavors, as in a rich whipped eggplant spread served with olive oil in the center and fresh-baked puccia bread on the side. Rigatoni verde with mushroom ragù is best bookended by such textbook treats as a pavlova, topped with white chocolate mousse, vanilla bean ice cream, and fresh passion fruit.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Terrace;[]
12156;Dear Jane's;USA;Marina del Rey;13950 Panay Way, Marina del Rey, 90292, USA;33.9788903;-118.4532242;86;true;false;American, Seafood;In case this Marina del Rey restaurant's glass wall with views of the boats outside didn't give it away, Dear Jane's celebrates the life aquatic with its focus on old school seafood and Continental cuisine. This spot pours it on with large portions and over-the-top flourishes (caviar makes a regular appearance) while keeping things grounded with strong cooking. Shrimp Louie, done tableside, is sized to share, as is the wedge, which brilliantly subs in vinaigrette in place of creamy dressing. Blackened salmon with a rich parsley and caper sauce is perfectly cooked, and lemony potatoes are a nice accompaniment. Signature cocktails riff on the famous Janes but will you choose Jetson, Goodall or Austen?;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12157;Girl & the Goat Los Angeles;USA;Los Angeles;555-3 Mateo St., Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.0403787;-118.2330441;68;false;false;Contemporary, American;Chef Stephanie Izard's West Coast offshoot of her wildly popular Chicago original has made its home in downtown LA's Arts District among Spotify's podcast production campus. It's boho chic to a tee with an airy look, soothing linen-color design palette and loads of natural light and potted greenery.Perpetually full and lively, everyone comes here for a good time. Patrons at the bar sip colorful drinks decorated with marigold blossoms while perusing the eclectic menu with the chef's trademark style (read: free-roaming with global inspiration and gutsy flavors). Savory dishes, like roasted oysters and goat curry, feed the evening crowds while über-popular Sunday brunch lures diners with items like the potato crepe, a whimsical riff on the Vietnamese banh xeo.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12158;Rossoblu;USA;Los Angeles;1124 San Julian St., Los Angeles, 90015, USA;34.035248;-118.25355;90;true;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;This standout from Chef/owner Steve Samson is a favorite among local shoppers and visitors alike. While the area teems with restaurants aplenty, cutting-edge Rossoblu won't disappoint. There’s nothing avant-garde about its food however, and thankfully so. In fact, due to delicious summers spent in Emilia-Romagna, the chef's creations are a veritable ode to the region and promise to make Italian palates proud.Quality ingredients and simple execution come to life in redeye tuna tartare with shallots, capers, and preserved lemon over an avocado puree, served with lavash bread. Pastas, like Olimpia's tagliatelle, with house-made pasta with a pork and beef ragu, are just right. Close on the heels is an irresistible brick of tiramisu crowned with candied cocoa nib cream.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12159;Sushi Takeda;USA;Los Angeles;123 Astronaut Ellison S. Onizuka St., Ste. 307, Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.0503344;-118.2419274;64;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Located on the third floor of Weller Court in Little Tokyo, Sushi Takeda is fairly new to the scene but already has a loyal following. The fans are here for Chef Hide Takeda, who has worked at some of the city's top sushi dens. There are two nightly seatings for omakase (one helmed by Chef Takeda), or skip the splurge-worthy dinner and opt for the reasonably priced lunch omakase. The counter is certainly the best place to pull up a seat to savor such items as the signature iwashi, a sardine roll wrapped in pickled daikon and filled with ginger and shiso. Lean tuna from Japan is simply delicious while spear squid with fermented tuna intestine is an enjoyable bite. Discover a perfect morsel of striped jack or the sweet and creamy kelp-cured spotted prawns.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12160;Robin;USA;San Francisco;620 Gough St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.77919;-122.42336;91;true;false;Japanese, Californian;Trust is the name of the game at Robin, a hip sushi-focused destination, where no menu is ever presented. Instead, guests happily submit themselves to the very capable skills of Chef Adam Tortosa and eagerly await his modern take on omakase. This kitchen’s decadent vision includes lots of elite ingredients like A5 Wagyu beef and caviar, though the staff will kindly ask what your budget is (or if you have allergies). The upscale space is a mix of posh and street cool—think graffiti-esque bathrooms and hip-hop beats. Young sushi chefs are the focal point of the room, working fastidiously with tweezers, torches and gel in front of a bright backdrop.A small, carefully curated list of beer, sake and wine pairs nicely with the food.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12162;Jeong Yuk Jeom;USA;Los Angeles;621 S. Western Ave., Ste. 100, Los Angeles, 90005, USA;34.0626623;-118.3088186;53;true;true;Korean, Beef;There are many Korean barbecue options in this section of town, so what sets this one apart, you might ask? It could be anything from the ample banchan and exceptional meats to the and attentive service. Courtesy of brothers Andrew and Jaeyong Son, this cavernous spot is perennially popular, thanks in part to the comfortable setting and sleek design.With a name that translates to "butcher shop," it's no surprise they proffer only the most premium beef. While the tomahawk steak costs a pretty penny, it will feed an army with leftovers aplenty. Other items—like top quality prime dry-aged prime rib or buttery marinated boneless short rib—arrive on a tray to be grilled tableside. Minimal embellishments, like soy and salt, ensure maximum enjoyment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12165;asterid by Ray Garcia;USA;Los Angeles;141 S. Grand Ave., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.0549354;-118.249647;30;true;false;Californian, Contemporary;Tucked within Frank Gehry’s iconic Walt Disney Concert Hall, asterid by Ray Garcia has an enviable location, but the restaurant is as stunning as its surroundings, with floor-to-ceiling windows bringing the outdoors in. The evolving menu draws from seasonal local produce and Latin American, Asian and European influences with Chef Garcia's distinctive Angeleño point of view. Begin with a refreshing aguachile, where firm cubes of hiramasa are paired perfectly with melon, cucumber and fiery serrano chili. Then, a terra-cotta pot arrives brimming with shredded braised oxtail and beans atop a masa-based "spaetzle." The deconstructed strawberry shortcake with hibiscus-flavored angel food cake and strawberry ice cream ends things on a sweet note.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12166;Barndiva;USA;Healdsburg;231 Center St., Healdsburg, 95448, USA;38.60977;-122.86942;75;false;false;Californian;Healdsburg has no shortage of eye-catching spots, but Barndiva captures the attention of many. It's perpetually packed with a stylish crowd. Now located in an annexed location, the service is attentive without a hint of pretense. Nothing feels contrived here, where farm-to-table is the dictum. Chef Erik Anderson's cooking is laser-focused on prime local produce. Come in spring and you may be treated to first of the season Zuckerman Farms green asparagus with a rich Hollandaise sauce. Roasted Mt Lassen trout is simple but delicious, as is a scoop of seasonal sorbet to complete the meal.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12167;Prik Hom;USA;San Francisco;3226 Geary Blvd., San Francisco, 94118, USA;37.7817894;-122.4534544;69;true;true;Thai, Californian;The mood is relaxed at this quiet neighborhood newcomer, but the compact menu offers an excitingly fresh, vibrant take on Thai cuisine. It is owned by siblings Tanya and Jim Suwanpanya, the latter of whom runs the kitchen and applies finesse learned in fine-dining kitchens in Bangkok to approachable versions of both familiar and lesser-known dishes. The name translates to fragrant chili, and aroma is part and parcel of the cooking, from complex hand-pounded curry pastes, to a bright, herbaceous salad of crunchy lotus stem. Even a signature dessert of coconut ice cream topped with candied palm seeds and pandan-flavored rice crisps is finished with a plume of fragrant smoke from a traditional Thai incense candle.;;[]
12170;RYLA;USA;Hermosa Beach;1220 Hermosa Ave., Hermosa Beach, 90254, USA;33.8624242;-118.3999149;86;false;true;Contemporary, Japanese;Husband and wife chefs Ray Hayashi and Cynthia Hetlinger run the show at this splashy and sophisticated spot in Hermosa Beach.Expect contemporary cooking with a Japanese focus and broad Asian elements. The menu offers a panoply of small plates—ideal for sharing but you may not want to. After sharing a few plates (or not), pick a main like ox tongue curry rice. This Japanese curry with a touch of sweetness is chock full of vegetables and cubes of buttery tender ox tongue, while rice finished with sweet corn and pickled green strawberries cuts the richness.End with matcha tiramisu or soy milk pudding, topped with a brown sugar gelee, fresh strawberries and a scoop of strawberry shiso sorbet with a spicy ginger-sugared churro.-;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
12171;Stokes Adobe;USA;Monterey;500 Hartnell St., Monterey, 93940, USA;36.5967104;-121.8961384;34;true;false;Contemporary;Named after a former owner with a checkered reputation, today this graceful historical residence wards off any hint of reproach with ample charm and warm hospitality. Beyond the accommodating service and handsome setting (which includes outdoor firepits ideal for enjoying well-made cocktails), diners here will be disarmed by the flavorful cooking that opts for substance over style.The small, ingredient-driven menu draws upon French and Italian elements, seen in hearty, satisfying dishes like the maltagliati pasta in prosciutto-parmesan broth, or duck confit with roasted apples and quince agrodolce. Comforting desserts, like an apple-pear crumble with vanilla ice cream, are a great excuse to linger—while sipping from a tempting array of after-dinner drinks.;Wheelchair access;[]
12173;Ernest;USA;San Francisco;1890 Bryant St., Ste. 100, San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.7630762;-122.4111166;27;false;false;Contemporary;Once you’ve managed to make your way inside (the entrance is around the block from the address, at the corner of Florida & Mariposa), you’ll meet no additional difficulty in finding fun at this unorthodox Mission hotspot. Chef Brandon Rice’s hip, irreverent cooking style sets the vibe, exemplified in fancy-meets-comforting combos like kaluga caviar with crème fraîche and tater tots. A small, eclectic menu spans raw bar items like crudos and oysters, plus a handful of snacks and more substantial mains, all featuring top-notch seasonal products. To try nearly everything, let the kitchen take the reins in the form of a family-style fixed menu. Reservations are snapped up quickly, but the bar is open for walk-ins—the better to sample a terrific cocktail program.;Air conditioning;[]
12175;Noodle in a Haystack;USA;San Francisco;4601 Geary Blvd., San Francisco, 94118, USA;37.780737;-122.4686149;60;false;false;Japanese, Californian;This humble counter, located in a nondescript corner building in the Inner Richmond, is one of the city’s hardest-to-snag reservations, with a singular ramen-centered tasting menu that is hotly in-demand. Married couple Yoko and Clint Tan returned from living in Japan with a passion for ramen, which they translated into a homespun business after learning the craft. The results are a testament to their dedication, offering some of the most memorable ramen in the Bay Area. The particular bowl on offer at any given time is subject to the season and the creative impulses of the kitchen, unbound by strict tradition, as in a Szechuan-inflected version straddling the line between tantanmen and mazemen, enriched with peanuts and enlivened with spice.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
12176;Funke;USA;Beverly Hills;9388 S. Santa Monica Blvd., Beverly Hills, 90210, USA;34.0717835;-118.4016441;38;true;true;Italian;Chef Evan Funke, who also runs Felix and Mother Wolf, is at it again with this eponymous restaurant. Set in a three-story 1930s art deco building, it's a stunning tribute to Italian cooking, with handmade pasta taking center stage (there's even a glassed-in room to watch them at work). Tall ceilings, red leather booths, and stone tables with brown leather/suede chairs set a stunning tone for a menu that pulls from their sister restaurants while remaining true to itself. Start with their pillowy focaccia, then savor a plate of tender South Pacific blue prawns in a garlicky salsa verde. Handmade agnolotti is delightful with a creamy filling of taleggio fonduta, finished with a meaty, buttery sugo di arrosto and parmigiano reggiano. Finally, torta di cioccolato is a wonderful finish.;;[]
12178;Felix;USA;Venice;1023 Abbot Kinney Blvd., Venice, 90291, USA;33.99208;-118.47177;63;false;false;Italian;This Venice Beach trattoria is run by Chef Evan Funke, who studied pasta-making at the celebrated La Vecchia Scuola Bolognese. There may be other delicious and well-prepared menu items, but diners come here for the pastas, listed regionally and made in-house behind a glass-walled laboratorio. The proof lies in the rigatoni all’Amatriciana, a “del Centro” specialty of large, finely ridged tubes in a tomato sauce enriched by delicious guanciale and finished with Pecorino Romano. Wonderful pizzas hail from the wood-burning oven and their dessert crostata is made with equal care and talent.The space is chic and homey with multiple dining sections that add to the overall sense of intimacy. Crowds can arrive early, making this something of a hot spot.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12179;Yuji;USA;San Francisco;1700 Post St., Unit K, San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7856487;-122.4299838;27;true;true;Japanese;Tucked away in an inconspicuous space in the heart of Japantown, this nine-seat counter feels miles away from the bustling outside world—though be punctual, or the meal will begin without you. Specializing in kappo cuisine, the less-formal counterpart to Kaiseki, the 12-course menu similarly reflects the seasons, featuring a progression of dishes spanning a series of delicate bites, both hot and cold, and culminating in a hearty dish of steamed rice (which might be enriched with hairy crab), paired with pickled vegetables and savory miso soup. In between, you’ll find various other preparations of pristinely fresh seafood, whether impeccably sliced sashimi or ultra-crunchy fried tilefish. At the end, a silky matcha custard is a final note of refinement.;;[]
12180;Boulevard;USA;San Francisco;1 Mission St., San Francisco, 94105, USA;37.79335;-122.39273;89;true;false;Californian;Housed in one of the city’s most historic buildings, this Belle Époque stunner is still breathtaking after more than 20 years, with glamorous mosaic floors, colorful glass and polished bronze at every turn. The Embarcadero-adjacent location offers lovely views of the Bay Bridge and the water, and business lunchers as well as evening romance-seekers adore its transporting vibe—there's not a bad seat in this restaurant.Chef/owner Nancy Oakes is known as a pioneer of Californian cooking, with comforting takes on standards like silky-smooth lobster bisque and a tweaked Cobb salad that eschews chicken for roasted white prawns and comes tossed with crispy bacon bits, feta cubes, cucumbers and tomato slices in different, visually appealing shapes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12181;Pasta Moon;USA;Half Moon Bay;845 Main St., Half Moon Bay, 94019, USA;37.46544;-122.42864;67;true;false;Italian, Californian;One of Half Moon Bay’s most popular restaurants, Pasta Moon is always packed to the gills with locals and tourists filling up on massive portions of hearty Italian-American fare. With its vaulted ceilings, open kitchen and multiple dining rooms, including one with views of the Pilarcitos Creek and lush garden, it's a hit among all ages.Recognized by Slow Food U.S.A., expect artisanal products like the house-made pastas that steal the show, with tempting options like the spaghetti with a luscious puttanesca sauce brimming with seafood and just a hint of heat. Thin-crust pizza Margherita with its garlic-kissed tomato sauce is a delight, but oh that mascarpone cheese cake with a chocolate cookie crust. It's bound to send you over the moon.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12182;Newport Seafood;USA;San Gabriel;518 W. Las Tunas Dr., San Gabriel, 91776, USA;34.1023916;-118.1068473;63;true;true;Seafood;This San Gabriel Valley spot is not of the salty old fisherman and oyster crackers ilk, but it's still a seafood fave, albeit one that imbues Chinese, Thai, Cambodian and Vietnamese flavors and cooking styles.Begin with a hot and sour soup before moving on to seafood-studded chewy rice noodles. Salt and pepper crab drowned with sliced chilies, chopped scallions and golden fried garlic is a delicious deep-fried mess, but don’t ignore the elephant—er, lobster—in the room, though. It’s why everyone is here. This Newport special is wok-fried and tossed with spicy jalapeño, green onions and clarified butter. The plucky creature, served at a minimum four pounds and dripping with juices, is an undertaking worth ruining your best shirt.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12183;Sushi by Scratch Restaurants: Montecito;USA;Santa Barbara;1295 Coast Village Rd., Santa Barbara, 93108, USA;34.4214368;-119.6400634;43;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;In sun-kissed Santa Barbara right by the tony Montecito Inn, this convivial counter is out to make sushi on its own terms. Though the group counts at least six other locations in the US and Canada, the setup is largely the same: Guests start with a cocktail in the lobby before finding their names written in chalk at their seats. The chefs, always talkative and ready to have a good time, work in tandem to deliver creative combinations that go beyond the realm of traditional nigiri. The likes of brown sugar, pineapples, chili ponzu, olive oil and fried onions find their way onto frequently blowtorched slices of A5 wagyu, Japanese tuna and New Zealand salmon. Those who book the last seating of the day can stay longer and request more pieces.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12184;Saru;USA;San Francisco;3856 24th St., San Francisco, 94114, USA;37.7516715;-122.4287658;76;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Hilly Noe Valley is the perfect setting for this jewel of a sushi restaurant, so make your way inside to discover a bustling (read: energetic) vibe. The menu is thoroughly Japanese with a few Californian touches—think grilled shishito peppers tossed with crunchy daikon in a ponzu dressing.Begin with the signature tempura-fried seaweed cracker topped with spicy tuna and avocado. Then, perfectly sized tasting spoons of seared ankimo with scallions, as well as halibut tartare with yuzu make for delightful quick bites. Though rolls are available, regulars opt for the nigiri, which might include kampachi, baby snapper and snow crab. Several omakase (including an all-salmon variation) are also on offer. Since Saru doesn't take reservations, arrive early to avoid a line.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
12185;Mulvaney’s B&L;USA;Sacramento;1215 19th St., Sacramento, 95811, USA;38.574375;-121.48236;51;false;false;Californian;A firehouse in its previous life, this Sacramento gem features food that will have you returning time and again, but sentimentalists beware, as the menu changes daily. While you can’t be sure what’s on offer here, fresh, seasonal and satisfying cooking is a guarantee. Imagine the likes oftortellini stuffed with winter squash, followed by a “beggar’s purse” filled with pumpkin pie, and you’ll be in no doubt as to the time of year.The waitstaff is well versed in the carte and ingredients—watch them name drop local farms like a celebrity stylist on the rise.If the heirloom tomato and mozzarella is available, don’t hesitate. It’s the most popular dish for a reason, starring ripe Ray Yeung Farms heirloom tomatoes and hand-pulled, still-warm cheese.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12186;Q Sushi;USA;Los Angeles;521 W. 7th St., Los Angeles, 90014, USA;34.046883;-118.255844;100;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Authenticity and tradition are paramount in this little sushiya. From the moment you walk in, to the rapid succession of courses that follow, everything in this dining room seems steeped in a sense of calm. Chef Hiroyuki Naruke prepares every item and thoughtfully serves each diner. Edomae-style sushi arrives as an omakase of fish, while other courses may commence with sashimi and nigiri. Case in point—amberjack sashimi with onions and soy, where each morsel is sliced, seasoned and set before your eye. This may be tailed by nigiri such as Hokkaido scallops, kohada, and fatty tuna. The pleasure of dining here extends right to end with the simple, spongy, and fluffy block of tamago.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
12187;Lucia Restaurant & Bar;USA;Carmel Valley;415 W. Carmel Valley Rd., Carmel Valley, 93924, USA;36.5007123;-121.7540509;63;true;true;Californian, Seasonal Cuisine;This dining room in the luxe Bernardus Lodge & Spa boasts its own garden, which provides many of the superb ingredients, and is proof of the kitchen’s dedication to local and seasonal food. It might show a talent and focus on vegetables, but highlights from the nightly menu as well as à la carte may include brilliantly tender lamb, served as medallions of deboned ribeye with rosemary jus on a bed of sautéed greens.There is a casual feel to the upscale lodge-like interior, with its large fireplace and muted colors. It's located just off the lobby but draws diners from well beyond mere hotel guests. The view alone, overlooking the Carmel Valley and Bernardus vineyards, may be worth a visit. Better yet, come on a sunny day and dine alfresco on the patio.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12188;Cultura;USA;Carmel-by-the-Sea;Dolores St. btw 5th and 6th Ave. Su Vecino Courtyard, Carmel-by-the-Sea, 93921, USA;36.556052;-121.9229063;92;false;true;Mexican, Californian;Cultura’s cooking is inspired by the cuisine of Mexico, with particular attention paid to the region of Oaxaca. It might not be the right place to take abuela for an authentic taste of home, but the food is very good. Tucked among shops in a courtyard away from the street, this dining room resembles a sort of Mexican taberna, lined with deep red booths, coffered ceilings and wrought-iron accents. On fair nights, dine alfresco around the courtyard’s fire pits.Try the house-made Cultura mole with smoked pork, which arrives as a feast of freshly made tortillas and lightly pickled vegetable slaw for assemble-your-own tacos. Save room for desserts like the dense and dark Oaxacan chocolate brownie with a touch of chili and cinnamon cloaked in ganache.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12190;Ember;USA;Arroyo Grande;1200 E. Grand Ave., Arroyo Grande, 93420, USA;35.1207805;-120.599957;93;true;true;Californian;Ember was at the forefront of open fire cooking in the Central Coast when they opened, and this Arroyo Grande charmer hasn't lost any of its spark. Its inviting industrial-rustic interior is the perfect setting for their heartfelt and down-to-earth cooking. You'll likely never tire of the contemporary menu filled with comforting favorites like bruschetta, made here with slices of house-made country sourdough with burrata atop an English pea purée & walnut pesto. There are plenty of mains, with staples like the grilled under-a-brick chicken, as well as not-to-miss features like the 50-layer lasagna. A blueberry cream puff filled with a honey chèvre mousse and sided by lemon buttermilk gelato is creative, yet classic.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12191;Ox + Anchor;USA;San Luis Obispo;877 Palm St., San Luis Obispo, 93401, USA;35.2816181;-120.6637893;46;false;false;Steakhouse;Chef Ryan Fancher's modern steakhouse is on the grounds of Hotel San Luis Obispo, in a separate building connected by a walkway. The hotel's contemporary Southwest vibe lives on in the restaurant. Design details, like butterscotch leather banquettes, a stacked brick wall divider, and teal-blue tiles, enhance the X factor. Staff are well-informed, so let them steer you through the menu. Start with such comfort fare as savory goat cheese croquettes with sweet lavender honey before embarking on the main event—charred steaks and sides of creamed spinach topped with onion rings.On the same property and from the same chef, Piadina is worth a visit—for its Cal-Ital menu and that hotel classic club sandwich turned on its head with fried chicken and B&B pickles.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12192;Oliver's Osteria;USA;Laguna Beach;853 Laguna Canyon Rd., Laguna Beach, 92651, USA;33.550877;-117.7781668;90;true;false;Italian, Regional Cuisine;Set just minutes from the Pacific Coast Highway near Laguna College of Art + Design, this Italian gem makes a delightful sight. Inside, the dining room oozes warmth, thanks to sleek banquettes, artwork-lined walls and an inviting bar—perfect for solo diners. It paints the very picture of Italian hospitality and that's even before you've had your first bite.Chef Erik De Marchi's menu has something for everyone. He takes a range of familiar dishes and enhances them with an authentic flair. Start with fiori di zucca, a zucchini blossom stuffed with ricotta cheese, anchovies and capers. Pasta is a natural choice, and while it's difficult to pick just one, tuck into a dreamy plate of bucatini all'amatriciana. Tempting desserts are all made in house.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12193;Abacá;USA;San Francisco;2700 Jones St., San Francisco, 94133, USA;37.806718;-122.4170585;20;false;false;Filipino, Californian;Chef Francis Ang, together with wife and co-owner Dian, sowed the seeds for this ode to Filipino cooking when they founded acclaimed pop-up, Pinoy Heritage. Born of a desire to more deeply connect with their culinary roots, their delicious explorations now have a permanent home in the lush Kimpton Alton Hotel.The sunny space pales next to the vibrant cuisine, which uses traditional flavors and techniques as a jumping-off point for creative, colorful dishes. Pork features heavily, as in juicy skewers of longganisa with cane vinegar and puffed rice, but a bounty of NorCal produce gets its due as well. Chef Ang gets to show off his pastry chops with one-of-a-kind desserts, not to mention the baked goods, available in the morning at the in-house panaderia.;Wheelchair access;[]
12194;Breakwater Barbecue;USA;El Granada;30 Ave. Portola, Ste. 1B, El Granada, 94018, USA;37.5049706;-122.4684833;75;false;false;Barbecue, American;Just about ten minutes north of Half Moon Bay in the charming seaside town of El Granada, Breakwater Barbecue is an all-American spot tucked at the base of a blue shingled house. Walk in and you may be greeted by the butcher slicing and prepping slabs of meat. This is the kind of place where you'll want to grab a beer immediately upon entering before tucking into the likes of chili made with house-ground brisket, smoked short rib and house-made sausage. Braised in smoked pork stock with roasted poblano, smoked tomato and garlic, it's packed with smoky, spicy flavors and best sided with a slice of corn bread. But wait, there's more, specifically the Texas Trinity. It's an impressive heap of brisket, ribs and links, plus two sides (Merle's potato salad and beans and greens are good choices) and bread. Come hungry.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12195;North Block;USA;Yountville;6757 Washington St., Yountville, 94599, USA;38.4061027;-122.366906;95;false;false;Californian;The space, at the edge of the villa-like expanse of the luxury hotel of the same name, is relaxed and airy. It is an ideal wine country retreat.Seafood specialties, like mussels with chardonnay butter sauce and grilled bread, or oysters on the half shell with house-made hot sauce, are a highlight. Slow-fermented wood-fired pizzas are always a good idea, and pastas, like a traditional tagliatelle bolognese, show equal care. For dessert, a caramel budino made with Macallan Scotch, paired with pistachio and chantilly cream, strikes a sophisticated and satisfying note.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12197;Spoon & Pork;USA;Los Angeles;3131 W. Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, 90026, USA;34.0852694;-118.2745864;97;true;false;Filipino, Fusion;Keep an eye out for the neon pig above the door of this modern Filipino comfort food spot—think of it as a porcine portent of things to come. Inside, the vibe is family-friendly and casual with a mix of aluminum and wooden tables set with bamboo and metal chairs.It may be tough to make a decision after reviewing the mouthwatering menu loaded with—you guessed it—pork. Adobo pork belly nigiri, a chorizo burger and a belly banh mi dabble with fusion, while dishes like lechon kawali stay in line with Filipino tradition. Come hungry for the patita—a hefty pork shank braised, then deep fried and smothered with a chili- vinegar- and garlic-sauce. Not a fan of pork? Order the staff favorite beef tapa with sirloin, garlic rice, eggs and pickled papaya.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12198;Luyu Dumplings;USA;City of Industry;17980 Castleton St., City of Industry, 91748, USA;33.9916484;-117.9124425;80;false;false;Chinese, Dumplings;This bare-bones operation hides in the back of a shopping center in City of Industry. The space is Spartan and deadly quiet, except for the sound of the refrigerators that hum constantly and the steady chop-chop of a chef’s knife in the nearby kitchen. If you want anything to drink, including water, you have to ask, and if you have questions about the menu, you’re better off looking at the poster of dishes on the wall. All to say, this humble restaurant is short on creature comforts but delivers admirably in the realm of excellent, handmade dumplings and bowls of chewy noodles glossed in scallion oil. From lamb with fennel to chicken with celery, dumplings come with a multitude of fillings, but the tender ground pork with lotus root win.;Terrace;[]
12200;Nate's on Marsh;USA;San Luis Obispo;450 Marsh St., San Luis Obispo, 93401, USA;35.2762985;-120.667298;94;true;true;American, Italian;This affable spot is just outside of downtown San Luis Obispo. It's no surprise that Nate's on Marsh feels very welcoming—it's set within a converted residence. Inside is just as darling with palm-printed wallpaper and a Western/equestrian theme. Nate Long is the consummate host and the service is exceptionally warm, though it certainly doesn't hurt that the menu is loaded with classics and riffs on favorites that will have you coming back for more. Try the La Scala salad, a blend of shredded iceberg, salami, artichoke hearts, sun-dried tomatoes, and crispy chickpeas, all tossed in a red wine vinaigrette, before tucking into hearty mains. Hand-cut pappardelle with Tablas Creek lamb ragu and walnut gremolata isn't fussy but it's fantastic.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
12201;Sushi Shin;USA;Redwood City;312 Arguello St., Redwood City, 94063, USA;37.4871305;-122.2323102;35;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;This discreet nook offers an elegant refuge from the quaint bustle of downtown Redwood City, and in turn offers some of the best sushi in town. Chef Jason Zhan manages the counter with aplomb and no shortage of charm, skillfully assembling a distinctive omakase featuring carefully sourced, seasonal seafood. At dinner, guests can select either a standard menu, or a pricier “premium” version that gilds the lily with rarer delicacies, while at lunch a single abbreviated menu is offered. The meal begins with a procession of small plates, which might include unique offerings like tempura-fried greeneye dusted with matcha, or soy-marinated Japanese sea snail, before proceeding to flavor-forward nigiri topped with the likes of horse mackerel and hairy crab.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12202;Parche;USA;Oakland;2295 Broadway, Oakland, 94612, USA;37.81222;-122.26653;98;false;false;Colombian, Contemporary;A festival atmosphere, advertised by a lively playlist of Latin music and colorful décor, may draw you in off the street, but the charming service and soulful, satisfying cooking seal the deal. Alongside an assortment of ceviches and empanadas, the menu proudly announces its Colombian bona fides with dishes like patacones (smashed fried plantains) and arepas, but isn’t shy about departing from tradition. The cooking embraces the country’s multicultural influences, including African and Lebanese, spotted in items like a labneh dipping sauce served with cheese-filled yuca buñuelos, or a leche de tigre with tahini. This isn’t a spot for a quiet, pensive night out, but if the volume is elevated, so too is the sense of fun.;;[]
12203;sawa;USA;Los Angeles;111 S. San Pedro St., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.050302;-118.24094;54;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;It's tucked in the basement of an office building in Downtown LA and isn't easy to find (they even send a video with directions) but this sleek, edomae-style omakase with a sprinkling of seats at the counter is worthy of a visit. Fish is sourced from Japan, with bluefin tuna hailing from Mexico and Spain, and the cocktail pairing is a nice complement. Nigiri is left to shine with a stroke of nikiri and simple toppings of yuzu kosho or ginger, but items like the shredded sous vide scallop roll prove that they're willing to be playful, too. Shrimp cake with panko-battered, deep-fried lotus root is spot on, while minced spearhead squid topped with Hokkaido bafun uni tucked in nori hits all the right notes. Soy sauce cheesecake is a smooth and rich ending.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12204;Kingfisher;USA;San Diego;2469 Broadway, San Diego, 92102, USA;32.7158;-117.140958;76;true;true;Vietnamese, Contemporary;This pretty bird makes a splash in its stunning Golden Hill location, which offers no shortage of charm. A striking central bar provides the perfect perch for thirsty guests to wet their beaks with a terrific assortment of inventive cocktails, which serve as excellent complements to the mouth-watering menu of inspired Vietnamese cooking. The shareable dishes are bursting with vibrant, herbaceous flavors typical of the cuisine, treated with a modern sensibility and careful technique. Expect creative, ingredient-driven takes on classic dishes, as in raw scallops prepared with the flavors of canh chua, a sweet-and-sour soup with tamarind and pineapple. Vegetarian offerings, like a hearty bowl of congee topped with wild mushrooms, are no slouch, either.;;[]
12205;Workshop Kitchen & Bar;USA;Palm Springs;800 N. Palm Canyon Dr., Ste. G, Palm Springs, 92262, USA;33.8340852;-116.5466923;84;true;false;Californian;Farm-to-table food may seem like an impossibility in the middle of the desert, but nearby Coachella Valley is actually one of the nation’s most productive regions. Here you’ll find that bounty on full display. A dedicated garden in Rancho Mirage, along with a sizeable herb planter behind the kitchen, furnishes peak-season produce for wood-fired dishes like a flat iron au poivre, and even a simple yuzu tart is prettied up with farm-fresh raspberries and wood sorrel. The setting is a Spanish-style building from the 1920s, while the interior is a modernist temple of polished concrete—a mist-cooled courtyard provides additional seating. Special touches like house-made ginger beer distinguish an exemplary bar program, with cocktails both classic and creative.;Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12206;Guelaguetza;USA;Los Angeles;3014 W. Olympic Blvd., Los Angeles, 90006, USA;34.0525532;-118.3008979;59;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;This distinct Oaxacan eatery knows exactly what its culinary mission is—so much so that it is made abundantly clear in everything from its website address (ilovemole.com) to the orange façade that announces its presence from blocks away. Inside, pops of green, vinyl-covered tables and happy faces brighten the whimsical setting. A grill station fills the room with the scent of blistering peppers and more.The tlayudas, enchiladas and pozole are all delightful, but it is their negro and rojo moles that are absolute favorites. Mole estofado is so complex that it is nearly impossible to pick out the ingredients creating such a rich and dark sauce, slathered onto chicken or pork. Everyone gets a taste of mole coloradito, drizzled over gratis chips.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12207;Bestia;USA;Los Angeles;2121 E. 7th Pl., Los Angeles, 90021, USA;34.0334815;-118.228991;98;false;true;Italian, Californian;As cool and convivial as ever, this is the kind of place where both diners and staff seem perpetually at bliss. Inside, it all feels like a labor of love, thanks to the husband-and-wife team who make it their mission to bring fresh, rib-sticking food to this neighborhood. The space itself is warehouse-sized and rustic, with a copper bar, tulip-shaped pendant lights, booths that appear virtually suspended, and a flaming red-domed oven.However, it is the cooking that lures these crowds. To wit: a justifiably popular deboned and properly grilled whole fish stuffed with pea tendrils, fried herbs, and charred citrus. Desserts though are equally enticing, so save room for a rich and creamy chocolate budina tucked into a crisp tart with salted caramel.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12208;Marché Moderne;USA;Newport Beach;7862 E. Pacific Coast Hwy., Newport Beach, 92657, USA;33.57024;-117.834656;61;true;false;French, French Contemporary;Chefs/owners Florent and Amelia Marneau deliver modern dishes with hints of French classics. This is a stunning, elegant and sumptuous establishment that feels and tastes familiar yet original. The cooking follows suit from the glassed-in kitchen with soft globe lighting to the fire engine-red Berkel that's ready to slice their superb charcuterie. The classics, from coq au vin to the poached Maine lobster tail flambéed in Courvoisier and paired with a quenelle of scallop, are perfectly on point. End with a cheese plate or a traditional baba au rum. Handcrafted cocktails mirror the bounty of the seasons and may feature a host of aged spirits or enjoy the well-priced wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12209;Hippo;USA;Los Angeles;5916 1/2 Figueroa St., Los Angeles, 90042, USA;34.1106258;-118.1903181;63;false;true;Italian;The name comes from the building’s former life as the Highland Park Post Office, but everything else here is Cal-Ital in spirit. The dining space is convivial and airy, with beamed ceilings and an open kitchen as its focal point. The vibe is as good for dates as it is for groups.Complimentary bread is rarely as satisfying as their focaccia, with its crispy, salty crust and soft interior. Begin with a sampling of small plates, like hamachi crudo topped with dollops of Meyer lemon relish. Then move on to freshly made pasta, like tender purses of cappellacci filled with sweet corn and dressed in a sauce of butter, mushrooms and thyme. While a meal could end there, you’d be remiss not to order the wood-grilled game or cedar-smoked ocean trout.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12211;Dio Deka;USA;Los Gatos;210 E. Main St., Los Gatos, 95030, USA;37.22089;-121.9769;51;false;true;Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine;Dio Deka may specialize in Greek food, but this is no typical taverna, as the stylish dining room (complete with a roaring fireplace) ably demonstrates. A wealthy, well-dressed Los Gatos crowd flocks to the front patio on warm evenings, dining and people-watching within the vine-covered walls of the Hotel Los Gatos. The bar also draws a brace of cheery regulars.Skip the dull mesquite-grilled steaks and keep your order Greek: think stuffed grape leaves with tender braised beef cheek, or a bright pan-seared local salmon with roasted yellow peppers, potatoes and artichokes. The adventurous shouldn’t miss out on the fun offering of Greek wines, and sweet buffs should allow space for the crema me meli, a fantastic burnt-honey mousse with almond and lemon.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12212;Sushi Tadokoro;USA;San Diego;2244 San Diego Ave., San Diego, 92110, USA;32.7483809;-117.1913167;55;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Guests are in good hands at this mini sushi counter that's off the beaten path in a modest strip mall. Chef/owner Takeaki Tadokoro along with young chef, Tatsuro Tsuchiya, take great pleasure in providing an enjoyable experience. Their style is approachable, and while an à la carte menu is offered in the dining room, the omakase is a more popular option. Whether it includes those creamy and meaty oysters from British Columbia or succulent scallops from Hokkaido, they use only the finest ingredients. To wit: a mix of sea urchin from California and Hokkaido topped with ikura hits all the right notes. Goldeneye snapper with yuzu zest and ponzu-marinated bluefin tuna are two more highlights.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12213;Gjelina;USA;Venice;1429 Abbot Kinney Blvd., Venice, 90291, USA;33.99045;-118.465034;29;false;true;Contemporary;In more than a decade, this buzzy restaurant has spawned a to-go counter, highly popular bakery and cookbook. The ambience is ceaselessly upbeat, resulting in a scene that is a major draw among pretty young things.Brick floors and creeping vines fashion a picturesque, garden-like setting that is an idyllic match for their simply prepared Mediterranean menu of pizzas and shared plates like saffron spaghetti with bottarga, confit tomato, and garlic or grilled hanger steak with a rhubarb chimichurri. Vegetables, many sourced locally, are an absolute must with winning options like Japanese sweet potato with jalapeno yogurt and scallion, or the umami-rich grilled oyster mushroom with tarragon butter.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12214;Carlitos Gardel;USA;Los Angeles;7963 Melrose Ave., Los Angeles, 90046, USA;34.083855;-118.36319;15;false;true;Argentinian;This may be the land of big, glitzy steakhouses, but Carlitos Gardel offers guests something more refined and quiet, with juicy meats and empanadas that have people coming back again and again. The evening mood here is romantic, and often accompanied by live piano music. There are larger seating options for groups, but those tiny, close-knit tables are often occupied by celebrities, without the paparazzi in tow.That said, big red wines, sharp knives and cutting boards laden with bone-in ribeye are sure to cover every available space. Start with a salad or crispy empanada with a side of chimichurri that’s so good it’s even available online for purchase. Sweet lovers rave about desserts, like a fluffy wedge of mascarpone tart with strawberry drizzle.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12215;Guesthouse;USA;Kentfield;850 College Ave., Kentfield, 94904, USA;37.9545644;-122.5483542;85;true;false;Contemporary;After a decade cooking at Larkspur’s beloved Picco, Chef Jared Rogers has grown well-attuned to the tastes of the polished Marin crowd. His Kentfield eatery is a neighborhood gem, but for residents with million-dollar homes. The menu is appropriately packed with dressed-up crowd-pleasers—from grilled king salmon with chimichurri and summery succotash to decadent flourless chocolate cake piled with chocolate ice cream.Donning soft leather booths, eye-catching wallpaper and a tiled central bar, the room has the feel of a cavernous old barn transformed into a luxe vacation hideaway. This holiday vibe continues through Co-owner Dustin Sullivan’s hand-crafted cocktails, like the Royal Bermuda Yacht Club—a tropical rum concoction with lime and grapefruit.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12216;The Morris;USA;San Francisco;2501 Mariposa St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.76314;-122.40833;31;true;true;Contemporary, Californian;After working at a number of SF’s top restaurants, veteran sommelier Paul Einbund has settled down at this neighborhood charmer in the Mission, named for his father. Unsurprisingly, The Morris boasts a selection of wine, top-notch cocktails and a sophisticated, craveable comfort-food menu.Quell your hunger with slices of Tartine country loaf—baked just down the street—as you peruse the menu with appealing bites both small (pork cracklins with honey and Aleppo pepper) and large (charred broccolini with succulent grilled squid in chili-lime dressing). They have an extensive list of housemade charcuterie and the pâte de Campagne is a can't miss. Their signature smoked duck, brined for two days and aged for four, is a smoky, tender and meaty marvel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12218;The Sardine Factory;USA;Monterey;701 Wave St., Monterey, 93940, USA;36.6155569;-121.9013993;96;false;true;Seafood, American;The name and exterior of this "factory” can be deceptive as it is pretty damn elegant, if even a bit stodgy on the inside. Imagine silk curtains, monogrammed seatbacks and other ornate touches, including a glassed-in greenhouse “conservatory.” If that’s not enough, white tablecloths, silver chargers and a menu listing “favorite” and “famous” dishes showcase decades of approval from tourists and elders.The menu is well executed but far from trendy, featuring a mix of classics like crispy sand dabs alongside ‘80s-glamour revivals like lobster ravioli in cream sauce. For those more open-minded however, the throwback theatricality can also be a lot of fun—from the ample bread basket with tomato-white bean dip to an engaging staff with fine-dining panache.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12220;Merchant Roots;USA;San Francisco;1148 Mission St., San Francisco, 94103, USA;37.778609;-122.412406;37;true;false;Creative;Plan ahead to secure tickets to this intimate den, where there are just a handful of seats and dinner is served only four nights a week. Dining here is a singular experience—though simple, the room flaunts an impressive fiber piece from a local artisan, custom-made tableware, and other hand-hewn furnishings.Chef Ryan Shelton arranges each of his meticulously-planned menus (which change seasonally) around a central theme, as in spring flowers or fall mushrooms. You might be enchanted by an alpine cauliflower meadow, featuring tiny crunchy florets with date hummus, before entering a fungi-laden forest. The latter is laden with canapés, including an oyster mushroom jambalaya encased in a maltose sphere--it's a feast for the eyes as well as the palate.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12221;Allora;USA;Sacramento;5215 Folsom Blvd., Sacramento, 95819, USA;38.560177;-121.44248;42;false;true;Italian, Seafood;Clean, modern and convivial, Allora is filled with the neighborhood feels, largely thanks to the owners’ passion and dedication. Tastefully decorated in shades of white, wood and deep green, this Cal-Ital kitchen is focused on fresh and sustainable ingredients. Seafood is supremely enticing and consistently woven through their menu of fresh pasta, local fish and Italian wines. The cavatelli, for instance, is made from scratch before being napped in a garlic-and-tomato sauce bobbing with chunks of sausage and summer squash.Come dessert, stick with a straightforward gelato, or just indulge in another glass from Sommelier/co-owner Elizabeth-Rose Mandalou’s large and reasonably priced selection that's displayed through the glass-enclosed cellar.;Brunch,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12222;Yangban Society;USA;Los Angeles;712 S. Santa Fe Ave., Los Angeles, 90021, USA;34.0340941;-118.2298677;44;false;false;Asian, American;Katianna and John Hong are behind Yangban Society, where black walls and dim lighting lend an industrial chicness to the space. It's softened by flowing paper shades covering the lights and plenty of greenery, including against the walls and grafted to tree stumps. Modern Korean-American cooking is given the spotlight here, with dishes like lush golden Hokkaido scallop toast that's indulgent thanks to a liberal slathering of brown butter and a surprising touch of grated egg. Then, delicate ocean trout in a terrific beurre blanc balanced with white kimchi is offset by hand-torn dumplings for a dish that delights. Yangban wings are double fried for an exquisitely crispy crust that's boosted with a sweet glaze.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12223;Lumière;USA;Los Angeles;2025 Avenue Of The Stars, Los Angeles, 90067, USA;34.0576053;-118.4153219;61;false;false;French, Farm to table;Nestled inside the Fairmont Century Plaza, Lumière is a relaxed brasserie-styled spot for French-inspired cooking. Friendly staff are on hand to offer guidance and share their favorite selections, but you'll certainly want to indulge in a variety of classics like fruits de mer and steak frites, if only for the delicious fries. Start things off right by ordering the velvety chicken liver mousse served with an olive jam, or sample the Bayonne, Fermin Iberico or five year-aged Iberico hams from the charcuterie menu. Seared sea bass is plated with a delicious onion soubise for a pleasing main dish. Then for dessert, you'll never go wrong with crème brûlée with its pure vanilla flavor and nutty caramelized crust.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12224;Bird & Buffalo;USA;Oakland;4659 Telegraph Ave., Oakland, 94609, USA;37.8339965;-122.2633711;34;false;false;Thai, Regional Cuisine;Picnic tables gift-wrapped with colorful plastic tablecloths and unhurried, nonchalant service readily evoke the casual roadside restaurants scattered throughout Thailand—and happily, so do the multifaceted, punchy flavors. The menu encompasses Northeastern specialties like redolent grilled meats and zingy, crunchy green papaya somtum (pick from Thai or Lao style, with the addition of fish paste and salted crab), but you’ll also find more cosmopolitan staples like drunken noodles and a variety of curries. When it comes to spice level, ask and ye shall receive—you won’t regret having an ice-cold Singha on hand. After a meal of boldly seasoned dishes, lusciously ripe mango over sweet-salty coconut sticky rice makes for a pleasingly gentle finish.;;[]
12226;Baroo;USA;Los Angeles;905 E. 2nd St., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.047286;-118.2348094;93;true;true;Korean Contemporary;Married couple Kwang Uh and Mina Park are behind this modern Korean dining room in DTLA. The look is sleek (think concrete floors and black-and-white walls) and the seats to be had are at the chef's counter, where you can watch the team at work.The format is tasting menu only, with options for wine and non-alcoholic pairings. Items may include a nicely seared Hokkaido scallop in a pool of watercress sauce with cubed seaweed jelly and puffed rice. Silky, soy-braised wild black cod is served in the center of a wide-rimmed bowl that is filled with a creamy buttermilk sauce that's poured tableside. Finally, wood sorrel bingsu, shaved to order, is refreshingly tart and a nice contrast to the creamy panna cotta tucked beneath.;Air conditioning;[]
12227;Copra;USA;San Francisco;1700 Fillmore St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.78535;-122.43284;73;false;false;Indian, Contemporary;Chef Srijith Gopinathan’s return to San Francisco’s dining scene is a love letter to the cuisine of his home state of Kerala, on the southwestern coast of India—even the name refers to the dried coconut meat common in the cooking there. The swanky space is lush and well-lit, seemingly tailor-made to draw in influencers, though certain rustic dishes, like a shell-on Konkan crab curry featuring a sticky sauce made with tamarind, dried chiles and shallot, make dressy attire a risky, albeit delicious, proposition. The sizable menu is geared towards sharing, though the modest portions encourage enthusiastic ordering, from a “palette” of assorted brightly flavored chutneys with pappadom, to a seriously aromatic fried chicken dish inspired by a favorite street food.;;[]
12228;Marugame Monzo;USA;Los Angeles;329 E. 1st St., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.050018;-118.2397919;30;true;false;Japanese, Udon;This LA spot is appropriately named, as Marugame is a Japanese town where udon is revered. Here, diners are even privy to these large discs of dough being rolled out, stretched, and cut into deliciously chewy strands. The space is simple, clean, and welcoming, as evident by the groups of friends and families with tots in tow. Come early to put your name down, especially on the weekends, because everyone is here to indulge in these savory and slurp-worthy bowls. One fine example is the mushroom udon infused with miso for an umami-rich base. Other items include the uni and miso "carbonara" and the crispy-and-creamy agedashi eggplant, along with hot and cold udon choices, bonus toppings, and cold Asahi on tap.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12229;Aziza;USA;San Francisco;5800 Geary Blvd., San Francisco, 94121, USA;37.78056;-122.48179;48;true;true;Moroccan, Middle Eastern;After shuttering his beloved Aziza in 2016, Chef Mourad Lahlou has finally made a triumphant return with this freshly minted spot. Dressed up with pale hues and a colorful bar, this remarkable menu offers a fresh take on the chef's signature Moroccan fare. As for the staff? They are (as always) gracious and well-informed. Chef Lahlou is famous for weaving California staples into dishes with stunning results. Loyalists will be happy to know the iconic specialty, Basteeya, remains—with golden phyllo wrapped around a delicious mix of shredded chicken and spiced almonds. Other staples include the slow-roasted, bone-in chicken thigh, served with crisped potato, olives, and house-made curry. Match it with buttery couscous for an utterly memorable meal.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12233;Donaji;USA;San Francisco;3161 24th St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.75232;-122.4154709;54;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Chef Isai Cuevas, who earned a reputation selling his excellent tamales at farmer's markets across the city, now has a cheerful, neighborhood brick-and-mortar. Named after a Zapotec princess of yore in a nod to his roots, he lets masa take center stage while showcasing his exemplary command of Oaxacan flavors. The tamales, of course, are a highlight, but you won’t be let down by well-crafted antojitos, like taquitos or sopes, either. The kitchen team's care and attention to detail are apparent in every dish, but a deep, complex mole negro makes a plate of enchiladas (featuring handmade tortillas, naturally) particularly memorable.Thirst-quenching, house-made agua fresca makes an ideal accompaniment to the savory and earthy fare.;Wheelchair access;[]
12234;Colony Club;USA;Palm Springs;572 N. Indian Canyon Dr., Palm Springs, 92262, USA;33.8316752;-116.5448581;87;false;true;American;This Moroccan-style oasis at the plush Colony Palms Hotel has history and charm to spare, having once been the stomping ground of stars like Clark Gable and Humphrey Bogart. Whether you’re indoors admiring its elaborate floor tiles and wallpaper, or poolside watching guests take a dip in the turquoise waters, the glamour factor is undeniable and infectious. You might even spot a famous face on a jaunt from LA—perhaps with some post-partying bedhead at weekend brunch or catching a cocktail as the sun sets. In keeping with the pool-party vibe, the menu is laid-back, from snacks like edamame hummus, to heftier fare like a grilled pork chop with cheesy polenta. To finish, a frosted carrot layer cake with pineapple and toasted pecans is just right.;Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12235;Evvia;USA;Palo Alto;420 Emerson St., Palo Alto, 94301, USA;37.44513;-122.1638;45;true;false;Greek, Californian;Inviting with its rustic wood beams, hanging copper pots and roaring wood-burning fireplace, this central Palo Alto spot is a draw for Maserati-driving tech billionaires by day and couples in the evening. Dress to impress here, where the scene dictates high prices (though lunch features lighter dishes and more palatable pricing).Much of the menu emerges from the wood-fired grill, including smoky, tender artichoke and eggplant skewers drizzled in olive oil and paired with garlicky Greek yogurt. The rustic, impossibly moist lamb souvlaki is nicely contrasted by a refreshing tomato, cucumber and red onion salad. For dessert, pumpkin cheesecake is subtle, sweet and accented with syrup-poached chunks of pumpkin.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12236;La Marcha;USA;Berkeley;2026 San Pablo Ave., Berkeley, 94702, USA;37.86863;-122.29215;74;true;false;Spanish;This Spanish delight from the team behind acclaimed caterer Ñora Cocina Española does double duty as a mecca for both tapas and paella, offered in varieties from the traditional mixta (prawns, chicken, chorizo, garlic, peppers) to the inventive “tres cerditos” (three little pigs) featuring pork chorizo, shoulder and belly. The classic tapas are also out in full force—from grilled head-on garlic shrimp and salt cod croquettes with nutty romesco, to tortilla Española.Located on busy San Pablo Avenue, the lively space offers enticements for groups of all sizes: foursomes can make the most of the sizable paellas, while a duo of happy hours offer discounts on wine at the L-shaped bar and a selection of free tapas, perfect for solo diners or couples.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12237;Mourad;USA;San Francisco;140 New Montgomery St., Ste. 1, San Francisco, 94105, USA;37.78695;-122.39987;35;false;false;Moroccan, Contemporary;Chef/owner Mourad Lahlou’s eponymous restaurant boasts a boldly designed space replete with soaring ceilings, glowing central columns and a superb (suspended) wine cellar. Chef Lahlou's expression of Moroccan cuisine is peppered with local and contemporary influences like maple and brown butter, as well as more traditional inflections such as charmoula and preserved lemon. Dinners may commence with the likes of basteeya, a Moroccan pastry made modern with finely shredded duck and enhanced with verjus crème fraîche, compressed pear, edible flowers and a rich cocoa paste. Couscous may then be presented with savory brown butter and a parade of vegetables, before it is hit with spicy harissa for a slight kick.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12238;Kokkari Estiatorio;USA;San Francisco;200 Jackson St., San Francisco, 94111, USA;37.79702;-122.3997061;21;true;false;Greek;Zeus himself would be satisfied after a soul-warming meal at this Greek favorite, which serves up San Francisco-chic with a side of old-world taverna hospitality. Once you’re seated at the bar or settled near one of its toasty fireplaces, the thoughtful staff will cater to your every whim.The intoxicating scent of caramelizing meats and lemon will certainly whet your appetite for what's to come. Kokkari's menu leans heavily on the wood grill and rotisserie, which turns out such simple delights as bizelosalata—spring peas topped with olive oil, feta, and scallions—followed by the eternally classic chicken souvlaki. For dessert, go for the galaktoboureko, or semolina custard, rolled in crisp filo and matched with pistachio ice cream.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12240;Redbird;USA;Los Angeles;114 E. 2nd St., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.05062;-118.24392;31;false;true;Contemporary, Californian;This airy stunner, which occupies a former church in the heart of Downtown, flaunts an impressive open ceiling allowing diners to stargaze—and that’s not even counting the occasional celebrity sighting. The boisterous atmosphere is beloved by the trendy patrons, who can be seen swapping small plates from perches at the two circular bars and eclectic sofa-stuffed lounge. On the global menu, creative dishes sit side-by-side with more traditional treats like John Dory in a leek fondue strewn with pan-seared gnocchi and mushrooms. Save room for clever desserts like their Meyer lemon tart with blueberry frozen yogurt or opt for another cocktail from the extensive list.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12241;Shizen;USA;San Francisco;370 14th St., San Francisco, 94103, USA;37.7682494;-122.4216544;83;true;true;Vegan, Asian;At first glance, this stylish izakaya and sushi bar could be another in a line of similar places that dot the San Francisco landscape were it not for a major twist: everything on the menu is vegan. Purists and die-hard carnivores may scoff, but the food is exceptional, skillfully manipulating vegetables and starches to recreate seafood-centric Japanese favorites.Spicy tuna gets a run for its money from the impressive tofuna rolls, with chili-inflected minced tofu and cucumber, crowned with creamy avocado and dusted in chili “tobiko.” A yuba salad with miso dressing and tempura-battered shiitake mushrooms stuffed with faux-crab is equally compelling. Throw in a sleek, contemporary setting, and Shizen is a winner for eaters of all stripes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12242;Kan Kiin;USA;Daly City;201 Southgate Ave., Daly City, 94015, USA;37.6972823;-122.4847186;36;true;false;Thai, American;An unremarkable Daly City strip mall might not be the most obvious spot to find well-crafted Thai cuisine, but putting appearances aside, this cheery little spot delivers on flavor. During the daytime, you’ll find an assortment of fusion brunch items (for example, a take on chicken and waffles that features hat yai, fragrant Southern Thai-style fried chicken) alongside a variety of more typical Thai restaurant fare. The menu includes the usual suspects of stir-fried noodles and curries, as well as less ubiquitous items like spicy clay pot catfish, and across the board special care and bold seasoning sets the cooking apart. For a case in point, try the hand-made curry puffs, which boast an impeccably delicate, flaky crust.;;[]
12243;Prospect;USA;San Francisco;300 Spear St., San Francisco, 94105, USA;37.7898387;-122.3909077;40;false;false;Californian;For a polished and contemporary experience that doesn’t sacrifice approachability, area denizens turn to Prospect, a crowd-pleaser for the full-pocketbook folk. Set on the ground floor of a soaring high-rise, this lofty, airy space offers attractive, roomy tables, adept service and a popular, well-stocked cocktail bar.Simple, well-constructed American cooking is the name of their game, as evidenced by olive oil-dunked burrata accompanied by roasted cherry tomatoes, thyme and golden crostini. Heartier appetites will relish the bavette steak served with a rich, peppery creamed corn, crispy smashed purple potatoes, and bright arugula salad. Desserts like house-made caramel corn balanced by sweet cacao nibs and a pinch of sea salt are a thrill to behold.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12244;Pasjoli;USA;Santa Monica;2732 Main St., Santa Monica, 90405, USA;34.0005122;-118.4821085;88;false;false;French, Contemporary;Chef Dave Beran’s Santa Monica bistro is irresistibly charming, a breezy space buzzing with activity and accented with wood beams, exposed brick and gleaming white kitchen tile. Brioche with chicken liver mousse and shallot truffle jam or bay scallops with green garlic beurre blanc reflect an unapologetically French approach. There are a number of dishes intended for two, and the pressed duck is the pinnacle of luxury. Should there be room to spare, chocolate soufflé paired with vanilla ice cream or a strawberry tart with whipped cream make for a sweet sendoff. No time for a full meal? Take to the elegant marble bar for Champagne, Osetra caviar and blinis.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12245;Serẽa Coastal Cuisine;USA;Coronado;1500 Orange Ave., Coronado, 92118, USA;32.6812848;-117.1785815;21;true;true;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;If the historic “Hotel Del” is the jewel of Coronado Island, then snagging a seat on Serẽa’s sprawling patio is like nestling into said jewel box. Thanks to its stunning views of the hotel's landscaped grounds and the ocean beyond, this is one of the prettiest perches in all of California. Just be sure to snag a reservation, because you’ll have competition from plenty of wedding parties and conference-goers.Deep-pocketed pescatarians will be delighted by the freshness and sustainability of the fish on offer—from inviting platters of raw oysters and cracked Maine lobster to flash-fried red snapper from Baja, offered by the pound for sharing. And even after the sun finally fades on the million-dollar view, the outdoor fireplace sets an exquisite mood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12246;Montrio Bistro;USA;Monterey;414 Calle Principal, Monterey, 93940, USA;36.599761;-121.8953049;84;true;false;Contemporary;This vast space is actually a 1910 firehouse replete with curving architecture, a beautiful bar and stairs that lead up to private rooms. The environment may seem upscale and contemporary, but don’t be afraid to bring the kids—crayons and paper cover the tablecloths, and they just might score a balloon on the way out. The kitchen prides itself on being green, sourcing many ingredients from local farmers, using sustainable seafood, prime meats and doing their part for responsible waste management. Expect tasty renditions of familiar favorites, like big, crisp pieces of golden-fried calamari with zesty charmoula. Happy hour brings deals in the lounge but come on Tuesday night for half-price bottles of California wines, with plenty of pinots to choose from.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12247;Saltwater;USA;Inverness;12781 Sir Francis Drake Blvd., Inverness, 94937, USA;38.094555;-122.849525;92;false;true;Seafood;If you love oysters, this coastal-chic spot will have you as happy as a clam. Nearly half its menu features these ultra-fresh bivalves plucked straight from nearby Tomales Bay—whether raw, broiled with chili-garlic butter or simmered in a creamy leek stew. If oysters aren't your thing, there’s also plenty of other local seafood to choose from, including crisp-skinned steelhead trout or risotto with clams and uni. Carnivores can opt for a roasted pork chop with collard greens.Set in a country-style house, Saltwater is a small town hot spot that attracts casual couples of all ages for local beer and wine on tap. The menu changes often to reflect the best of its markets, so be sure to pounce on such dishes as spicy gingerbread cake before they vanish.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12248;Zuni Café;USA;San Francisco;1658 Market St., San Francisco, 94102, USA;37.7737194;-122.4212575;17;true;true;Californian, French;Zuni has been at it for more than forty years, and locals and visitors remain drawn to this San Francisco institution. Famous for its laid-back California vibe and great, locally sourced eats, this iconic space embraces its unique shape, and is styled with bold artwork-covered walls, a copper bar and wood-burning oven sending out delightful pizzas that fill the room with mouthwatering aromas.Given its ace location, Zuni makes for a divine lunch destination—and proof is in the many business folk, trendy ladies-who-lunch and tourists who fill its tables midday. Menu treasures include Caesar salad and oysters to start, plus chicken for two roasted in the wood-fired brick oven.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12249;Barbareño;USA;Santa Barbara;205 W. Canon Perdido St., Santa Barbara, 93101, USA;34.422848;-119.69819;95;false;false;Californian;Smoke lures guests to the covered patio or casually cool dining room, set just steps from downtown Santa Barbara's hustle and bustle. Start with a local craft beer or wine to accompany any one of their diverse small plates. Dishes are bold and flavorful, and the kitchen showcases their distinct vision with attention to detail and a touch of whimsy. Grilled avocado is unapologetically Californian, balancing creamy with a subtle, smoky char. Eggamuffins, or cornmeal blini with a piped whipped seascape cheese foam, speck and grated, cured egg yolk, are as adorable as they are tasty. Five different single chocolates from different climates and a non-dairy panna cotta with a mead granita and fresh fruit are among the desserts.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12250;Otoño;USA;Los Angeles;5715 N. Figueroa St., Los Angeles, 90042, USA;34.109833;-118.19239;75;true;false;Spanish;Whether you want tapas and cocktails to share with friends or prefer to lean traditional with a Spanish classic (paella), this place offers something for everyone in a relaxed, trendy atmosphere. Croquetas, especially the organic chicken poached in goats milk and umeboshi membrillo, are always a good idea.Modern California touches influence the tapas turned out of this kitchen, while larger dishes like braised octopus, smoked chicken thighs and paella options offer heartier fare if you're game. Don't miss the boquerones y mantequilla, a delicious little plate of fresh anchovies paired with roasted radishes and a terrific tuna and anchovy goat butter. Crema Catalana with wine-soaked blackberries is a light, boozy delight.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12252;Cloak & Petal;USA;San Diego;1953 India St., San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7252952;-117.1688122;47;false;false;Japanese;It’s in the heart of Little Italy, but you won’t hear any old crooners at this temple of Japanese haute cuisine. Instead, you'll find old-school rap on the soundtrack and graffiti art installations on the walls. And then there’s the bar, flanked by two faux-cherry trees in full bloom.The fresh-spirited menu brims with shareable plates such as blistered shishito peppers and crispy chicken karaage. Entrées include duck breast with golden tomato confit, miso-glazed black cod or even Wagyu grilled tableside on a yakitori. The sashimi is straight-up sublime, but it’s the envelope-pushing items that make the most impact. Contemporary maki are a hit among the hungry hordes, and include the Tokyo Gangster, with shrimp and beef in a spicy black garlic sauce.;Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12254;Masa's Sushi;USA;Novato;813 Grant Ave., Novato, 94945, USA;38.10692;-122.56675;35;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Respected veteran Chef Takatoshi Toshi has returned to his roots and taken over the reins to bring Novato locals hearty and affordable sushi. Don’t be surprised to see him behind the counter here, breaking down a whole salmon while making small talk with his neighbors. The space is simple, understated and quiet, which seems to match its quaint downtown location, set amid boutiques and restaurants.Lunch combinations are an excellent deal, offering chirashi bowls as well as sushi and nigiri with miso soup. Come dinner, the affordable omakase selection unveils nigiri, salmon and tuna tastings. Bigger platters might arrive as lovely amalgamations of avocado and albacore rolls alongside ebi, yellowtail and cherry wood-smoked goldeneye snapper (kinmedai).;Air conditioning;[]
12255;La Taqueria;USA;San Francisco;2889 Mission St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.750828;-122.41827;57;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;This local favorite always has a queue because everyone loves it—from tech bros in hoodies to families out for Sunday lunch. The jovial Miguel Jara runs this show—you may find him working the register or handing out roses to customers. Counter service makes it feel no-frills, but this is the kind of place that relishes in its simplicity.Everything here is supremely fresh, as exhibited in the open kitchen with its mountains of char-grilled steak alongside vibrant tomato, cilantro and onion. The carne asada super burrito is everything you dream it should be. It may not be on the menu, but order your taco “Dorado-style,” which begins as a corn tortilla crisped on the plancha, layered with cheese and another tortilla before getting loaded with toppings.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
12256;El Buen Comer;USA;San Francisco;3435 Mission St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.74184;-122.42225;97;false;false;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;“Good eats” are promised right in the name of this approachable neighborhood restaurant on the outskirts of the Mission, and La Cocina alum Isabel Caudillo delivers in full. Her menu highlights the cooking of her native Mexico City, featuring homestyle dishes like her signature guisados, as in tender, pork ribs slowly simmered in salsa verde, served with nopales and plenty of warm, handmade corn tortillas to mop up every last drop of the delectable sauce. The focused menu is rounded out with other classics: pambazos, chiles rellenos and fresh-fried tortilla chips accompanied by a hefty scoop of guacamole and zippy house-made salsas. Save room for Caudillo’s desserts, like a chocoflan that combines silky caramelized custard and rich chocolate cake.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12257;Valette;USA;Healdsburg;344 Center St., Healdsburg, 95448, USA;38.6120896;-122.8697182;27;true;true;Californian;Housed in the former Zin space, this contemporary darling is actually a full-circle comeback for Chef Dustin Valette and his brother/General Manager Aaron Garzini, whose grandfather owned the building in the 1940s. Its current look offers plenty of charm, thanks to dandelion-like light fixtures, concrete walls and horseshoe-shaped banquettes. The bill of fare is modern American with a few French twists. Scallops arrive beneath squid ink puff pastry, into which a server pours caviar-flecked champagne-beurre blanc. Then, Peking-spiced duck breast set atop hearty forbidden rice is taken to the next level with a touch of tamarind sauce. For an appetizing end, dig into the smooth block of chocolate mousse with a luscious salted caramel center.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12258;Mattei's Tavern;USA;Los Olivos;2350 Railway Ave., Los Olivos, 93441, USA;34.6675349;-120.1173756;70;false;false;American;Once a popular stagecoach stop in the late 1880s, then an infamous hangout during Prohibition, Mattei's Tavern has now been reimagined courtesy of Auberge Resorts. Nestled just outside the charming town of Los Olivos, this place simultaneously reeks of history while feeling decidedly modern. Chef Rhoda Magbitang oversees a shared plates, Californian menu that benefits from an on-site garden and live fire cooking. Begin with the braised abalone finished with abalone liver mousse over mushroom confit in white miso butter. Main dishes are large, but be sure to sample wood-fired sides like grilled wedges of cabbage over a tomato stew with spiced chickpea and salsa macha. Finally, a dark chocolate soufflé with crème anglaise and butterscotch is never a bad idea.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12259;All Spice;USA;San Mateo;1602 El Camino Real, San Mateo, 94402, USA;37.553135;-122.315445;99;true;false;International, American Contemporary;Like a bracelet glittering with different jewels, All Spice is home to a bevy of vibrant dining rooms, made extra colorful with artwork and sparkling chandeliers. It’s a delightful blend of old-school charm and contemporary verve that appeals to a sophisticated crowd. They’re usually here to catch up with friends or celebrate a birthday.This kitchen offers a variety of creative selections on both the three- and five-course tasting menus, which spin to highlight the seasons. Chilled butternut squash soup in a shot glass makes a soigné amuse-bouche and is a delicious way to start a meal. Then a brick-shaped, perfectly cooked strip loin is accompanied by baby zucchini, pearl onions, confit mushrooms and smoked kale sauce for added enrichment.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace;[]
12260;Damian;USA;Los Angeles;2132 E. 7th Pl., Los Angeles, 90021, USA;34.0334339;-118.2289049;58;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Housed within a repurposed warehouse with polished concrete, exposed brick and pendant lighting, Damian has that industrial chic look down pat, but add plush leather-covered chairs and loads of leafy green plants, plus an ever-popular terrace, and this Arts District denizen is a notch above. The menu speaks to a kitchen that is rooted in the nuances of Mexican cooking. While there may not be a right way to start a meal here, a delicious tamal de elote paired with a thirst-quenching cocktail is always a good idea. The uni tostada with a blue corn base topped with a generous pile of uni petals and a "Caesar salad" represents the kitchen's modern, subtle layering technique. Even the ever-traditional fish taco punches above its weight with precision and surprise.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12262;Mijoté;USA;San Francisco;2400 Harrison St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.7589774;-122.4125819;23;false;true;French, Contemporary;Chef Kosuke Tada’s culinary career began in Japan, but French cuisine is where he elected to earn his stripes, and diners at this casual neighborhood bistro are all the luckier for it. The name translates to “simmered,” which might serve as a metaphor for the careful yet uncomplicated style of the cooking, seen in a seasonal prix fixe menu that endeavors to avoid obscuring the quality of excellent locally sourced ingredients. In line with Chef Tada’s low intervention approach, the beverage program is dedicated to food-friendly natural wines, which feels especially fitting, given that the space’s relaxed wine bar aesthetic would not be at all out of place in Paris—though don’t expect even a whiff of hauteur. A winning combination, sans doute.;;[]
12266;Taira Sushi & Sake;USA;Garden Grove;8851 Garden Grove Blvd., Ste.113, Garden Grove, 92844, USA;33.7741725;-117.9770598;30;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Taira Sushi & Sake isn't knocking anyone off their feet with its nondescript mall location, but it's what's inside this tiny spot that makes it special. Young duo Chef Ben and Ayako Sato have penned a love letter to Japan here, where great care is paid to details (the menu is written by hand nightly) and warm hospitality makes everyone feel welcome. Guests are invited to enjoy omakase or order à la carte. Standouts include kanpachi slightly seared and served with a sprinkle of rock salt, lemon and yuzu, or tender firefly squid topped with scallions and laced with nori. Seared spicy cod roe and hearty stewed fish cheeks are inventive starters, and a smattering of "rolls" are on offer (think ume shiso roll).;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12267;Artifact at Mingei;USA;San Diego;1439 El Prado, San Diego, 92101, USA;32.7314293;-117.1509782;24;true;true;International, Contemporary;Visitors to scenic Balboa Park's trove of museums are well-advised to stop in for the unique collection of folk art, craft and design on display here, but this unassuming restaurant, just across from the gift shop, is worth a visit in its own right. Like the museum itself, the culinary offerings are proudly eclectic and international, ranging from carefully pleated rock shrimp gyoza with a yuzu-flavored dashi, to lamb kibbeh with quinoa tabbouleh. Plant-based options, like Thai green curry with sweet potato and crispy noodles, are clearly no afterthought, and desserts like cardamom tapioca with saffron granita hold their own. As if to drive home the kitchen’s far-ranging sensibilities, an exclusive dinner series highlights a different global cuisine every month.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
12268;Sushi Kisen;USA;Arcadia;1108 S. Baldwin Ave., #B6, Arcadia, 91007, USA;34.1273449;-118.0545406;76;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Sushi restaurants can be as expensive as a mortgage and as quiet as a library, but this casual Arcadia hotspot is a wonderfully refreshing change of pace. The setting is more like Tokyo’s Shibuya Crossing, a frenetic intersection of customers lined up at the door, servers scurrying about, and chefs working like they are on a tight deadline. Counter seating or a table farther back? Omakase or a la carte? It doesn’t matter. The rice for the nigiri is reliably generous and lush in texture, and fish flies in from Japan on Monday and on Thursday. For this reason, Friday is often packed, as regulars look to catch the freshest shipment. Efficient, fairly priced and friendly, Sushi Kisen meets all expectations in the most approachable of ways.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12269;Chef Tony;USA;Arcadia;1108 S. Baldwin Ave., Arcadia, 91007, USA;34.1271832;-118.0543464;60;false;true;Chinese, Dim Sum;Tony He may not be a household name, but dim sum enthusiasts know him from his work at Sea Harbour, which he opened in Vancouver in 1999, and then later in Rosemead.Just a few miles down the road in Arcadia, Chef He offers a similar experience, albeit in a more casual setting with nary a fish tank in sight and a large window offering views into the kitchen.Indeed, steam rises at all hours as chefs diligently prepare delicate bites, like steamed shrimp and scallop dumplings crowned with roe, or rice noodle rolls lined with chicken and bitter melon. Everything is ordered à la carte, so those hoping for roving carts should look elsewhere. Still, dishes arrives hot and fast, and you could easily be fed and out the door in record time.;Air conditioning;[]
12272;Liholiho Yacht Club;USA;San Francisco;871 Sutter St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.7884286;-122.4146384;73;false;false;Asian, American;There are no yachts to be found at its current Mission residence, but hordes of locals and enthusiasts remain quite eager to book passage on Liholiho's love boat. Fusing Californian technique with the flavors of Chef/owner Ravi Kapur’s native Hawaii, this earthy, bustling, and airy space is known for strong cocktails, shareable plates, and near-impossible reservations. Walk-ins are welcome, but make sure you arrive in time to beat the crowds.Pivoted around a large, open kitchen, the dining room hums with groups savoring the likes of short rib bao or whole fried fish marinated with coconut and turmeric. If you turn your nose up at Spam try the house-made version. It just might convert you.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12273;Flour + Water;USA;San Francisco;2401 Harrison St., San Francisco, 94110, USA;37.7589299;-122.4123569;19;false;true;Italian, Californian;As the name implies, two ingredients create a world of possibilities at this always-packed Mission stalwart. Affable service, plus a space that’s both buzzy and approachable, partly explain the evergreen appeal of this humble space, but it’s really the kitchen’s vibrant blend of Californian and Italian cuisines that draws the crowds. An ever-changing array of expertly handmade pastas is the main event, with creative offerings like squid ink bucatini sauced with octopus ragu and Calabrian chili crunch, plus lesser-known regional shapes, like a plate of lusciously taleggio-filled scarpinocc. The option of half portions helps to ease the difficulty of choosing only one, but for those seeking even more variety, a multicourse pasta tasting is a real treat.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12274;Zócalo;USA;Sacramento;1801 Capitol Ave., Sacramento, 95801, USA;38.574226;-121.4837515;93;false;false;Mexican;Set right in the Capitol Mall, this upscale stunner (which also has outposts in University Village and Roseville) dons an elegant demeanor by way of heavy wooden doors, dark metal chandeliers and plenty of lush greenery. The sprawling outdoor patio boasts terrific people-watching. And though it’s named for Mexico City’s central plaza, this kitchen's menu offers regional highlights from around the country.Puebla-style chicken enchiladas, for instance, smothered in handmade mole poblano burst with flavor, while crispy tostadas contrast rich Michoacan-style carnitas against a zesty and bright salsa. Tequila nerds will thrill to the extensive selection, but there’s no shame in just ordering a margarita—the “Mango Fresco” with a tajín salt rim is a winner.;Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12275;Miller & Lux;USA;San Francisco;700 Terry A Francois Blvd., San Francisco, 94158, USA;37.7678384;-122.3863769;61;false;false;Steakhouse, American;Fine dining may seem an unlikely find in the shadow of the hulking Chase Center arena, but this stunning harborage from Chef Tyler Florence is worth a splurge.The elegant vintage-meets-modern design is an ideal setting to dress up and dine in comfort on a menu of steakhouse classics. Begin with a spot-on martini and superlatively fresh oysters (pulled from a saltwater "estuary" located in the kitchen). The Caesar salad and Dover sole meunière get an extra dose of charm, thanks to tableside service. Excellent dry-aged steaks (finished with barley, a healthier alternative for the animals and the planet), are seared to a deep mahogany and are the main event for good reason. Sides like creamed kale with crispy shallots also don't disappoint.;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12276;Manuela;USA;Los Angeles;907 E. 3rd St., Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.04608;-118.23489;87;false;true;American, Californian;Tucked inside the multi-use Hauser & Wirth Arts Complex with an open-plan kitchen and conceptual art, Manuela has a creative, contemporary look and feel. The cooking is strong, with a Southern leaning, and features a menu with a heavy leaning toward local ingredients (including from their own garden). Choose a cocktail from their classic list, all elevated with house-made bitters and tonics. Warm, flaky biscuits with aged country ham and whipped butter are a must before a main course like their roasted duck breast with nicely rendered, crispy skin served over a bed of smoked soubise and paired with sliced yellow peaches. End the meal with one of their desserts, like their take on s'mores or their Harry's Berries and genmaicha shortbread ice cream.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12277;Be.Stéak.Ă;USA;Campbell;1887 S. Bascom Ave., Campbell, 95008, USA;37.287535;-121.9322084;47;true;true;Steakhouse, Contemporary;An elegant ambience complements an elevated menu of exceptional steaks and an array of dishes at Chef Jeffrey Stout's newest restaurant, BE.STÉAK.Ӑ, located a minute's walk from his other very popular spot, Orchard City Kitchen. Here, the menu meanders through the Mediterranean before focusing on high-quality and well-prepared steaks and sides. Kicky clams casino substitutes pepperoni for bacon, while rigatoni all'amatriciana delivers another spicy hit, but really, you're here for the meat. Good thing too, since bacon-wrapped filet in a horseradish crema with king oyster mushrooms and finished with a "meaty" demi-glaze is first rate.  The Sunday Supper menu, featuring four courses for the whole table, is a draw for families and groups.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12278;Horses;USA;Los Angeles;7617 Sunset Blvd., Los Angeles, 90046, USA;34.0981132;-118.3555764;98;false;true;Contemporary;Best of luck to anyone hoping to score a coveted seat at the buzziest restaurant in town. Online reservations disappear in a flash, and early birds line up just before doors open. Once home to a storied pub, this veritable hit exudes a members-only charm in a vintage space where banquettes, side rooms and a long bar up front hum with energy.The food offers broad appeal. Endive dressed in a creamy Caesar is one of the best salads in the city, while blood sausage with fried hen’s egg or an off-menu shell pasta tossed in vodka sauce offer hearty satisfaction. Keeping this crowd moving is a talented bar that manages to stay on track against a rush that never lets up. Is it time for dessert yet? The sheep’s milk cheesecake is as light as air.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
12279;Dela Curo;USA;Oakland;907 Washington St., Oakland, 94607, USA;37.8017344;-122.2748232;63;true;false;Japanese, Curry;Located in Swan's Market in downtown Oakland, this order-at-the-counter style of spot is brought to diners by Chikara Ono. Decked with glass and bamboo accents, as well as—you guessed it—a counter with partial views of the kitchen, your eyes will be solely focused on the plates in front of you. They are massive in portion and bold in presentation.The menu specializes in Japanese curry, but this version is nearly black in color and thicker in texture, thanks largely to a dark roux-sauce typically seen in Northwestern Japan. These curries may be prepared with fried chicken, tonkatsu or even with a tender omelet in the case of omu. All arrive with rice, which is a perfect vehicle for the sauce. Pickled vegetables add yet another layer of flavor and texture.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12280;Gintei;USA;San Bruno;235 El Camino Real, San Bruno, 94066, USA;37.61866;-122.409615;98;false;true;Japanese, Sushi;Set back in an ordinary strip mall, the vibe and service at this sushi jewel are anything but. Wonderful, warm, and gracious, diners here are in for a treat. The interior is sleek and stylish, with dramatic pressed-tin ceilings and a coveted eight-seat counter. Naturally, reservations are a must, especially for the omakase, complete with items that can hang with the best in San Fran.Fans of nigiri should make a beeline for the chef's selection, but the more discerning palate will revel in market specials, like silky Hokkaido scallops, sweet and succulent live spot prawns (with the traditional deep-fried heads alongside), as well as firm yet delectable octopus. Everything is minimally dressed—all the better to accentuate the product's supreme quality.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
12281;Rooh;USA;San Francisco;333 Brannan St., San Francisco, 94107, USA;37.7813216;-122.3925983;44;true;true;Indian, Contemporary;Amidst a slew of upscale Indian restaurants descending upon San Francisco, Rooh rises to the top, thanks to an innovative menu that fuses the subcontinent’s myriad flavors with modern restaurant staples (oysters, pork belly, burrata). The bold India-goes-industrial décor is a bit paint-by-numbers, with vivid jewel tones and an oversized mural, but the vibe is engaging and the cocktails quite unique.Rooh's cuisine is approachable, but an extra degree of care and punched-up ingredient quality are reflected in the pricing. Opt for a meal of delicious small plates, like redolent bites of spice-marinated chicken under a colorful disc of crisp shreds of kataifi. Wrap up with unique desserts like a cashew praline cake paired with phirni mousse and thaindai ice cream.;Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12282;Grange;USA;Sacramento;926 J St., Sacramento, 95814, USA;38.5802489;-121.4937062;31;false;false;American;The Citizen Hotel is primo for those with business on their minds, but that doesn’t mean it’s all just corporate here downtown. In fact, Grange, tucked inside the hotel, is proof positive that business and pleasure mix with fine results. High ceilings and an arched shelf stacked with liquor instantly draw the eye, while wood tables lined with orange leather banquettes balance style and comfort. If visiting midday, opt for the Power Lunch and enjoy three courses for a palatable price.The menu shares a farm-focused sensibility with rustic creations. Mojo pork loin spread with calabrese bomba on toasted bread is simple and tasty, not unlike the dependably creamy broccoli-arugula soup. Hazelnut cake with strawberry and chocolate ends things on a sweet note.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12283;Oriel;USA;Los Angeles;1135 N. Alameda St., Los Angeles, 90012, USA;34.0624425;-118.2357866;48;false;true;French, American;This breezy, classic bistro may just be your next choice neighborhood haunt. Nestled amid the shops in Chinatown, the window-flanked space offers a full bar and dining room along with an inviting foyer and terrace. Clean, white walls are richly adorned with artwork and rows of wine bottles. The bar is of course beloved by solo diners, while groups should go for a table by the windows. Then get nibbling on a variety of cheese and charcuterie, before savoring such piquant mains as bouillabaisse Marseillaise with seafood aplenty, tomato, garlic, and herbs. A hunk of sourdough is great for sopping up its fragrant broth. If that sounds heavenly, just wait for the decadent pot de crème.A brief wine list, dominated by French labels, amplifies the experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12284;Found Oyster;USA;Los Angeles;4880 Fountain Ave., Los Angeles, 90029, USA;34.0953376;-118.2958733;21;true;true;Seafood;There is no ocean in sight from this busy corner of East Hollywood, and yet, a single Santa Barbara spot prawn dressed with yuzu ponzu arrives so pristine and plump you'll wonder if it swam to your table when you weren’t looking. Then meaty, freshly harvested scallops from Maine are presented atop a tostada finished with yuzu kosho.Such is the beauty of this breezy hangout, which is so narrow that blink and you'll miss it. Minimally decorated with a long bar, wee kitchen and antiques, diners here can be sure of one thing—delicious success is easy to come by. This is in large part because the kitchen sources impeccably and prepares everything from sea urchin to razor clams so adeptly and simply, often with just a drizzle of olive oil or squeeze of lemon.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12285;Manhattan Beach Post;USA;Manhattan Beach;1142 Manhattan Ave., Manhattan Beach, 90266, USA;33.885162;-118.410934;94;true;true;International;Just a stone's throw from Manhattan Beach Pier, this restaurant is big and buzzing. It's almost always packed, especially with plenty of young families, and they're all here for a taste of Chef/co-owner David LeFevre’s globally minded creations with a clear California point of view. Head-on Caledonian blue prawns ajillo atop diced potatoes with saffron mayonnaise. Beeler's Farm pork porterhouse is grilled and accompanied by Asian pear kimchi and a black mustard sauce. Everything revolves around gathering, conversing and sharing, and portions lean small, so plan your ordering as a group to explore a majority of the menu.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12287;Rory's Place;USA;Ojai;139 E. Ojai Ave., Ojai, 93023, USA;34.4476677;-119.2461823;56;true;true;Californian;Sisters Rory and Meave McAuliffe run this charming Ojai spot with rustic, feel-good vibes. Wide plank wood floors lend warmth while exposed ducts keep things trendy. There is a little bit of everything here, from a local produce-driven menu and terrific raw bar offerings to a natural wine list and a provisions counter up front. Some dishes seem simple but deliver in spades. A stunning salad of avocado, baby beets and citrus served on a wide, oval plate is a riot of colors. Then, an herb-laced broth bobbing with Aleppo sausage, spring garlic, potatoes and steamed countneck clams offers a refined take on stew. Then, a classic Pavlova is topped with a citrus custard and fresh blood and cara cara oranges, grapefruit and kumquat for a bright finish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12288;AMA Sushi;USA;Montecito;1759 S. Jameson Ln., Montecito, 93108, USA;34.4205379;-119.6257621;47;false;true;Sushi, Japanese;Located at the Rosewood Miramar, AMA Sushi is straight out of Japan. The name is a nod to the famed female divers and the space resembles a typical Japanese house with a moody nautical appeal (think dark wood walls with lantern-like light fixtures and a scalloped sushi bar). Then there is the edomae-style sushi, available à la carte or as an omakase. It's worth going all in on the omakase to sample the chef's artistry, which begins with a trinity of bites from soba noodles and fried eggplant to sesame tofu. A seared scallop with wasabi vinaigrette paves the way for nigiri, with standouts including rich New Zealand king salmon and kamasu, a Japanese barracuda finished with a red chili paste. Black sesame cheesecake is a solid finish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12289;Pizzeria Sei;USA;Los Angeles;8781 W. Pico Blvd., Los Angeles, 90035, USA;34.0548356;-118.3835826;34;false;true;Pizza, Contemporary;Thick or thin. Sauced or left bare. Traditional or irreverent. Pizza is the shape-shifter of the culinary world, with seemingly endless variations and an insatiable appetite for the newest iteration. Enter Pizzeria Sei, where individual pies are made with a Japan-meets-Italy flair. A handful of diners perch at the counter to watch the chefs hard at work prepping these savory treats. Wondering where the Japanese comes into play? It's the cornicione—with its trademark puffy pinch with a mochi-like chew. White pies are more offbeat, as in the Bismarck topped with a poached egg, while red pies lean more Italian. The Margherita is a go-to, topped with simple tomato, basil, fior di latte and olive oil, then cooked in a gas- and wood-fired oven.;Air conditioning;[]
12291;Routier;USA;San Francisco;2801 California St., San Francisco, 94115, USA;37.7879899;-122.4405741;91;false;true;French, Californian;Routier is a welcoming neighborhood spot serving French bistro fare with a distinct Californian accent. Chef/owner JP Carmona’s seemingly casual approach belies serious culinary sophistication in dishes like a hot-and-cold composition of crisp, buttery potato pavé topped with sweet Dungeness crab in an herby, lemony mayonnaise. Fantastic seasonal produce and bold flavors are hallmarks year-round. Sweets are furnished by celebrated next-door neighbor, B. Patisserie, so it should go without saying, save room for dessert.;Wheelchair access;[]
12292;Dalida;USA;San Francisco;101 Montgomery St., Ste. 100, San Francisco, 94129, USA;37.7999028;-122.4596299;88;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Turkish;The lush seclusion of the Presidio seems at first an unlikely locale for a restaurant hotspot, but once the charisma and talent of married couple and co-chefs Laura and Sayat Ozyilmaz are factored in, the popularity here is a foregone conclusion. The menu is broadly Eastern Mediterranean, drawing inspiration from the melting pot of Istanbul, with a bounty of dishes—from flaky, cheesy borek to juicy short rib kebabs with sweetbreads—that are well-suited to sharing with a group.Whatever else you opt for, consider it all but mandatory to start your meal with “breaking bread,” an assortment of spreads, olives, and pickles, served with superlatively pillowy, toasty pita that is rolled and hearth-baked to order—you’re unlikely to find better in the Bay Area.;;[]
12293;The Dutchess;USA;Ojai;457 E. Ojai Ave., Ojai, 93023, USA;34.4479891;-119.2421256;40;false;false;Burmese;Smack in the center of Ojai, The Dutchess reigns from its perch inside a charming 1920s building. It may be the queen of cool, but prim and proper it's not. Instead, this quirky concept features a bakery/cafe by day and a trendy Burmese restaurant by night. Come hungry, as this heartfelt menu is brimming with snacks, salads, curries and large plates designed for sharing. Begin with a tea leaf salad, piled high with slightly bitter tea leaves balanced by napa cabbage and sungold tomatoes with crispy-crunchy peanuts, fried garlic and shallots. Chickpea tofu is perfectly golden-brown and sided by a sweet and sour tamarind sauce. The contemporary, rustic dishes are bested by the skillfully prepared desserts, like a decadent chocolate-caramel ganache tart.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12295;Shalizaar;USA;Belmont;300 El Camino Real, Belmont, 94002, USA;37.52775;-122.285416;50;false;true;Persian, Grills;A perennial favorite for Persian flavors, Shalizaar is friendly, charming and authentic. Lunchtime draws a large business crowd, while dinners cater to couples on dates. The upscale space features chandeliers, linen-topped tables, Persian carpets and walls of framed windows that flood everything with light.Meals here are always a pleasure, thanks to the high quality of every ingredient. Try the signature koobideh, smoky ground beef and chicken kebabs served with char-broiled whole tomatoes and rice. Or, tuck into baghali polo, fork-tender lamb shank over bright green rice studded with dill and young fava beans. For dessert, take the friendly servers’ advice and order the zoolbia bamieh, sticky-crisp squiggles of fried cake soaked in rosewater syrup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12296;Terrapin Creek;USA;Bodega Bay;1580 Eastshore Rd., Bodega Bay, 94923, USA;38.3391;-123.04818;27;false;true;Californian;Whether it’s the ochre walls, the bold artwork or the fireplace, Terrapin Creek emits palpable warmth. Liya Lin and Andrew Truong, partners and co-chefs, have created an alluring sanctum where everyone feels like a regular, whether you’re a resident or simply here to spot the migrating whales.The menu is concise, so expect a spectrum of bites that may include grilled Monterey sardines set over shaved radishes and cabbage dressed in a refreshing lime-curry vinaigrette. Pasta is made in house, so dig your fork into those torch-shaped curls with crumbled merguez, chopped spinach, feta cheese, mint and sweet English peas in a spicy tomato-based broth. For dessert, a chocolate cake with cream cheese frosting is bested with a heavenly caramel sauce.;Air conditioning;[]
12297;Tac/Quila;USA;Palm Springs;415 N. Palm Canyon Dr., Palm Springs, 92262, USA;33.8290158;-116.5469796;80;true;false;Mexican;Amidst the hacienda-inspired elegance of this popular venue, you may find yourself flanked by suit-clad business types quaffing top-shelf tequila on one side, and on the other, poolside-tanned tourists with clothes thrown over their bathing suits as they sip from margarita flights— and everyone seems perfectly at ease. Likewise, the sizeable menu offers room for both street tacos with typical fillings like carne asada or al pastor, as well as more upscale options like lobster and seared ahi tuna. In all cases, the tortillas are made in house, the flavors are lively and the portions are generous. Cheery service will help you select from a bountiful list of agave spirits, and a nudge to finish with a churro ice cream sandwich is wisely heeded.;Wheelchair access;[]
12298;Ardor;USA;West Hollywood;9040 Sunset Blvd., West Hollywood, 90069, USA;34.0904261;-118.3890649;82;true;false;Californian, Mediterranean Cuisine;If a luxury spa ran a restaurant, it would probably look something like Ardor. Cushy white velvet and leather booths, white and beige staff uniforms, and enough verdant greenery to rival a small forest match the equally chic aesthetic at its parent venue, the West Hollywood EDITION hotel. The prices are high too, not that any hotel guests would even notice. But know that there is plenty of substance and care packed onto this vegetable-forward menu. Tandoor carrots with hummus and paprika vinaigrette or grilled dukkah-crusted ahi tuna with yogurt make for satisfying, clean eating. Dry-aged lamb and steaks cater to heavier appetites, and no meal is complete without a tower of tempura onion rings and at least one dessert (try the mojito pie).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12299;Hatchet Hall;USA;Los Angeles;12517 Washington Blvd., Los Angeles, 90066, USA;33.996941;-118.4314275;90;false;false;American, Contemporary;This lively Culver West spot is always in full swing, starting with the sprawling, pergola-shaded patio that rallies groups when the weather is right. Beyond lies an equally ample dining room with vintage accents like tufted leather banquettes and an L-shaped bar. The lengthy menu highlights a broad range of classics from across the South and, rightly so, biscuits, seasonal vegetables and plenty of pork are given due billing. Deviled eggs, pimento cheese and fried green tomatoes channel all the comfort of an old-fashioned picnic. Entrees, which are often easy to share, cover land and sea, though you could assemble a feast from the vegetable section, starting with collard greens with smoked turkey or blistered snap peas with buttermilk.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12300;Henry's Cuisine;USA;Alhambra;301 E. Valley Blvd., Alhambra, 91801, USA;34.0788401;-118.1196496;74;false;false;Chinese, Cantonese;In an unremarkable building that nearly blends in with the rest of the street, Henry’s has quietly but confidently satisfied an ever-dwindling demand for homestyle Cantonese cooking since 2015. With a scarlet-red lobster as their logo, shells painted silver and gold and hung on the wall, and large groups huddled around platters of it, there isn’t much guessing as to what the signature is here. Come for dinner to unlock the menu’s full breadth of specialties. Highlights include delicately fried shrimp with salted egg as well as a striking deep-fried salted pig’s feet, its skin as crisp and crunchy as a chip. Vegetables are a must but ask what’s in season. We’re partial to the soothing, quiet bitterness of mustard greens with garlic.;Air conditioning;[]
12301;Koi Japanese Cuisine;USA;Seal Beach;600 Pacific Coast Hwy., Unit 100, Seal Beach, 90740, USA;33.7464271;-118.1054577;38;false;false;Japanese, Contemporary;Helmed by chefs have a century of experience under their collective belts, Koi Japanese Cuisine may have a familiar name, but this spot stands firmly on its own. It's not hip or trendy, but it is beloved by regulars who are known by their first names and have a clear rapport with the chefs. Though it has history and heart, these regulars are here for more than just a warm welcome. From orange clam and kampachi to Kumamoto and Kusshi oysters, the sashimi lineup is impressive. A tempura of zucchini flowers stuffed with scallops serves as a culinary intermission between the sashimi and nigiri, which presents eight selections with a variety of flourishes ranging from seabass with a dab of yuzu kosho to scallop topped with uni.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12302;Juanita & Maude;USA;Albany;825 San Pablo Ave., Albany, 94706, USA;37.89059;-122.29897;61;false;true;Contemporary;Downtown Albany is abuzz about this chic arrival named for the mother and grandmother of Chef/co-owner Scott Eastman. It has all the accoutrements of a fancy local joint—think unique sculptures from an area artist, rustic plates and fun craft cocktails like the rum- and coconut-based White Picket Fence. And yet, this rookie eschews the tragically hip crowds for an easier, more communal feel.The roving menu is heavy on odes to seasonal produce, like a succotash of summer squash, corn and cherry tomatoes topped with flaky halibut. You'll also be able to taste the chef’s nine years of cooking at Berkeley favorite—Corso—in his perfect veal Bolognese sauce. Creative, well-balanced desserts like a creamy banana custard with coconut granita are menu musts.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12303;Octavia;USA;San Francisco;1701 Octavia St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.7880138;-122.4270235;55;false;false;Californian;Tucked among the Victorians that line its picture-perfect street in Lower Pac Heights, locals count themselves lucky to claim this charming, elegant dame as their neighborhood spot—though they may still need to plan ahead to score a table.Executive Chef Nico Pena adds his own creative touch to Chef/owner Melissa Perello’s signature brand of simple-yet elevated cooking. A meal might progress from impeccably crispy fried artichokes to silky hand-made fettucine with morels, followed by juicy quail with grapefruit and spinach, each showcasing spectacular local products in their best light. Don’t skip the baked goods: house-made levain is excellent, as are seasonal desserts like a bay leaf panna cotta with rhubarb granita and tarragon crumble.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
12304;Yunomi Handroll;USA;Los Angeles;806 E. 3rd St., Los Angeles, 90013, USA;34.0457338;-118.2353754;60;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Chef David Movsisian's Yunomi Handroll is located on a stretch of East 3rd Street that has become a hotbed of terrific restaurants and nightlife, and this cool, inviting spot is certainly keeping up with its neighbors. Inside, it's moody and dark with a pared-down design while the counter is the heartbeat of the operation. It's always buzzing—likely due to its unique offerings. There's nothing cookie cutter about this experience where you'll savor the likes of crispy Brussel sprouts with sweet soy sauce, sesame seeds and Ichimi pepper or rock shrimp tempura tossed in spicy mayo seasoned with shichimi togarashi. A signature for a reason, the Yunomi special handroll marries spicy albacore, shrimp tempura, crunchy onions and truffle soy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12305;Les Petites Canailles;USA;Paso Robles;1215 Spring St., Paso Robles, 93446, USA;35.6269947;-120.6916397;33;true;true;French;Courtney and Julien Asseo have named this Paso Robles restaurant in honor of their three children (the name translates to "the little rascals") but this welcoming spot with a spot-on kitchen is more head of the class than detention bound. Set smack in the heart of downtown, the space's pressed concrete floors, simple furnishings and Edison lights read contemporary. Meals begin with a warm gougère before moving on to a selection of hearty appetizers. The menu features several entrées, though most eyes land on the perfectly cooked steaks. Leeks à la plancha, served on an oversized platter, are grilled, covered with an herb vinaigrette and finished with flaky salt, Espelette pepper and toasted pine nuts for a simple, yet refined dish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12306;Agnes;USA;Pasadena;40 W. Green St., Pasadena, 91105, USA;34.1444438;-118.1513515;56;false;false;American, Californian;Say hello to the coolest cat in Pasadena. This breezy, A-frame hangout exudes all the feels with serious beats bouncing off exposed brick that stretches from the cheese shop and bar up front, past the open kitchen, and down to the handsome patio out back. All day, guests lounge in the parlor nibbling on cheese and charcuterie. Come night, the kitchen grill roars with life. Cornbread eclair with chicken liver mousse is an easy decision, but choosing between the cavatelli with braised lamb and lamb fat gremolata or the half chicken with smoked jus is no small thing. The latter is brined, steamed, and charred over open flames until the skin is crisp as a chip.You probably won’t have room for dessert, but order the tres leches with corn pudding, anyway.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12307;matū;USA;Beverly Hills;239 S. Beverly Dr.,  Ste. 100, Beverly Hills, 90212, USA;34.0635158;-118.3991829;52;false;true;Steakhouse, Californian;Matū may have wood panels, exposed brick walls and plenty of gleaming brass, but this isn't your typical temple of masculinity. Instead, this Beverly Hills steakhouse adds a little romance to its chic digs. The inviting ambience is elevated by an open kitchen with views of the action, and the warm, courteous wait staff rounds out the experience. Steaks hail from New Zealand (matū is a Māori word) and their wood-fired preparation delivers on the promise of tender and juicy meat. Wagyu is usually a budget buster, but here it's offered at an accessible price. Its delicate, exceptional flavor will have you remembering its for weeks to come. Steaks may be the heart of the menu, but fazzoletti with a slow-braised beef ragu are a fine choice.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12308;Cafe La Haye;USA;Sonoma;140 E. Napa St., Sonoma, 95476, USA;38.29197;-122.45584;51;true;false;Californian;For years, Cafe La Haye has been a standby off the square in downtown Sonoma. One bite of its luscious burrata, surrounded by Early Girl tomatoes and crispy squash blossoms in the summer, or vinaigrette-dressed pea shoots in spring, proves it hasn’t aged a day. The small, modern space is still charming, with large windows and lots of mirrors. Stunning local artwork for sale decorates the walls.The food spans cultural influences, including a delicate risotto with pine nuts in a cauliflower broth, or soy-sesame glazed halibut atop whipped potatoes and braised kale. A postage stamp-sized bar pours glasses of Sonoma chardonnay and cabernet, perfect with rich strozzapreti tossed with braised pork ragù, Grana Padano and toasted breadcrumbs.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12310;Sorella;USA;San Francisco;1760 Polk St., San Francisco, 94109, USA;37.7931112;-122.4210529;37;false;false;Italian, Californian;The spirited younger sister to grande dame Acquerello, this hot spot trades in an air of stately luxury for a more hip, lively vibe. The family resemblance is nonetheless apparent in the thoughtful cuisine, which runs Californian by way of Northern Italy. You can snack on a collection of cicchetti at the well-equipped bar while sipping excellent cocktails, but you'll need to nab a table for a more substantial repast.When in season, a gem lettuce salad with sweet Dungeness crab, fine herbs and anchovy dressing might just be the best possible spin on a classic Caesar, but top-notch ingredients are assured at any time of year. House-made pastas naturally meet the grade, as in a multi-layered baked timballo with dry-aged beef and Comté cheese.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12311;Ken;USA;San Francisco;252 Divisadero St., San Francisco, 94117, USA;37.7714702;-122.4369312;29;false;false;Sushi, Japanese;The city has its share of intimate omakase counters, but few offer quite as much cozy charm as this six-seat gem in the Lower Haight. Walking through the unmarked door on Divisadero puts diners in the experienced hands of Chef Ken Ngai, a native of Hong Kong who mastered his craft at respected sushi spots here in the Bay Area. The menu’s approach straddles tradition and creativity, spanning a moderate selection of skillfully prepared nigiri, featuring unconventional toppings like cured egg yolk and preserved plum. Apart from the sushi, a variety of small composed plates shine especially bright, as in a silky chawanmushi luxuriously flavored with crab and dried scallop, or an intriguingly sweet-savory dish of poached ikura in a refreshing ume broth.;Wheelchair access;[]
12312;Saffy's;USA;Los Angeles;4845 Fountain Ave., Los Angeles, 90029, USA;34.0954746;-118.2951512;52;false;false;Middle Eastern;Crackling flames, heat radiating from the coals, the constant kneading and stretching of dough— the visceral nature of Ori Menashe and Genevieve Gergis’s latest restaurant is impossible to ignore. Clearly, as snagging a reservation at this hot spot isn't an easy feat.Lamb and pork kebabs cooked on long metal skewers are the main event, but grilled lobster marinated in green harissa is a luxurious feast that would dazzle in fine dining temples. Turmeric mussels are a delight, as is the golden-brown falafel with creamy tahini. Bread is a constant source of pleasure, from the delicate challah to the soft laffa, but dessert is far from an afterthought. Avocado honey butter soft serve ice cream with a tableside pour of sherry is a real treat.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12313;Fia Steak;USA;Santa Monica;2454 Wilshire Blvd., Santa Monica, 90403, USA;34.0351143;-118.4785275;64;true;false;Steakhouse;Some places are just right for stopping in on a regular weeknight, and then there's Fia Steak. This no expense-spared spot is just right for getting dressed up and feeling festive, even if all you're celebrating is the end of the week.It has the classic masculine steakhouse look down pat, complete with dry-aged steaks on full display. The menu is a classic paean to meat with opulent touches (spy the separate sections for caviar and Champagne). Seafood-focused starters kick things off—keep an eye out for specials like the Dungeness crab salad topped with a seafood panna cotta. Of course, steak is the reason you're here, but the decadence continues through dessert, with either a soufflé or a seasonal strawberry trifle with basil ice cream.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12315;Chulita;USA;Venice;533 Rose Ave., Venice, 90291, USA;33.9987622;-118.4729134;55;false;true;Mexican;With its mod Mexican good looks and its Venice location not far from the beach, Chulita is primed for sunny SoCal days. Tacos are served all day at this spot where Oaxacan-style, California-influenced fare rules. Slake your thirst with a tequila or mezcal, then tuck into a starter, such as the quesadilla de calabaza, made from dark masa, filled with Oaxacan queso and garnished with pipián de calabaza. Tender barbacoa takes it up a notch. Tortillas are made in house, and tacos are always a good idea. Order the tinga de pollo, filled with juicy chicken, or go straight for the steak taco with its slight char. You'll be satiated but go for the vegan churros with dulce de leche-style dipping sauce anyway.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
12316;The Barn Kitchen at Sparrows Lodge;USA;Palm Springs;1330 E. Palm Canyon Dr., Palm Springs, 92264, USA;33.801619;-116.532384;60;false;true;Californian;Once an exclusive getaway for Hollywood elites, the privileged serenity of this quaint refuge no longer requires a SAG card to gain entrance (though you will need a reservation if you’re not staying at the property). With open-air communal seating in an idyllic poolside setting, this is hardly a typical restaurant, but embrace the relaxation and allow yourself to be pampered by the effortlessly disarming service. Matching with the general wellness retreat aesthetic, the ingredient-driven cooking tends towards wholesome Cali-style simplicity—think fresh salads, grilled cauliflower steak with sauce vierge and the requisite avocado toast at lunch. The menu is small (especially during the day), but dietary restrictions are readily accommodated.;Wheelchair access;[]
12317;Birdie G's;USA;Santa Monica;2421 Michigan Ave., Santa Monica, 90404, USA;34.0270128;-118.468556;98;true;true;American;Named for Chef Jeremy Fox's young daughter, this homespun delight serves up square meals with satisfying swerves. Soothe your ails with matzo ball soup made from a family recipe, then tuck into marinated Badger Flame beets with smoked trout roe, mustard cream and sprinkled with an “everything” spice & seed mix. Try one of the steaks (Flatiron with fries is a good choice) or order some of the smaller plates to share. For dessert, Jell-O pie makes a comeback, infused here with strawberry, hibiscus and garnished with candied rose petals.While the menu is diner-inspired, its interior skews modern-trendy. A thoughtful kids’ menu keeps tots happy, allowing the grown-ups to luxuriate in hand-picked wines that go with each special.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
12318;Antico Nuovo;USA;Los Angeles;4653 Beverly Blvd., Los Angeles, 90004, USA;34.0765417;-118.3110212;20;false;true;Italian;For those who’ve been following chef/owner Chad Colby in East Larchmont Village, the revamp of this Italian looker will not feel so unfamiliar. The space remains a hive of activity, boasting all the coolness of an underground speakeasy, now fitted with comfy, backlit booths lining the room. A hand-cranked rotisserie grill is the centerpiece of this handsome kitchen, which turns out hearty pastas and big proteins. Focaccia with whipped ricotta and hazelnut pesto is a must, while a broccoli chicory Caesar scratches any itch for greenery. Pasta stuffed with rabbit is a signature, but don’t sleep on the veggies like the potato tart served with whole garlic cloves or the fire-roasted sweet potato. Freshly churned ice cream is the ultimate finale.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12320;Tony's Seafood;USA;Marshall;18863 Shoreline Hwy., Marshall, 94940, USA;38.1468731;-122.8830959;61;false;false;Seafood;You’ll be hard pressed to find more picturesque views than the ones at this charming, sun-lit nook perched right on the edge of Tomales Bay. Under the ownership of Hog Island Oyster Co., the restaurant offers a casual foray into ace seafood that's often been caught or harvested in local waters. Regulars swing by for trays and trays of freshly shucked oysters sourced from California to Washington. Grilled oysters dressed in a smoky-sweet barbecue sauce or a simple garlic butter also tempt. Other highlights include mussels steamed in a spicy tomato broth, as well as a signature clam chowder. Seats fill up fast on weekends so consider making a reservation before taking the trek through rolling hills and along the edge of the California coastline.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12322;Poppy & Seed;USA;Anaheim;350 S. Anaheim Blvd., Anaheim, 92805, USA;33.8328395;-117.9127088;22;false;true;Southern, American;Chef/co-owner Michael Reed and co-owner Kwini Reed are behind this gorgeous perch in the Anaheim Packing District. Poppy & Seed epitomizes the SoCal lifestyle with a lounge and bar nestled inside a greenhouse, and outdoor dining surrounded by citrus trees, herbs and flowers. As the setting hints, the focus is on organic, sustainable and locally grown (as well as raised or caught) ingredients. Settle in at sunset or under the stars to enjoy dishes such as creamy Anson Mills grits topped with gravy and plump tail-on shrimp. Charred eggplant puree and pickled sea beans lend a bite to steak tartare, while fried Brussels sprouts are sweet and salty thanks to bacon jam and pomegranate. Juicy strawberries and roasted beets make an earthy-sweet combination that could pull double duty as dessert.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12325;Sushi Sonagi;USA;Gardena;1425 W. Artesia Blvd., Unit 27, Gardena, 90248, USA;33.8734669;-118.3009826;97;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Don't expect to drop by Sushi Sonagi when the mood strikes, as this eight-seat sushi counter is only open on the weekends and hosts just two seatings nightly. Those who have planned ahead will be rewarded with an enticing multicourse omakase prepared by Chef Daniel Son, a second-generation sushi chef. Chawanmushi, an ankimo tart and minimally dressed nigiri are all part of the experience, though it's the dolsot sekogani, or female snow crab stone pot rice, that makes a big impression. Presented to guests in the pot, then heated to produce a crispy crust, it's then portioned to eager diners who delight in the richly seasoned meat. End with a charcoal-roasted sweet potato topped with house-made white sesame ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12326;Coast Range;USA;Solvang;1635 Mission Dr., Solvang, 93463, USA;34.5961541;-120.1403036;98;false;false;Steakhouse, American;Solvang's charms are not lost on Coast Range, which ups the ante with vintage details inside its  multi-concept space. Brunch spot by day, it's a steakhouse tavern by night with a winsome cocktail bar through a separate entrance. The menu leans heavily on the seasons and dishes will change often, but there is plenty to choose from when it comes to mains like wood-grilled seafood and steaks. Potato pierogi with sour cream and peach butter or a fantastic Dungeness crab cake are must-order appetizers. Grilled items are always a sure bet, but don't overlook the entrées like Wagyu stroganoff with homemade tagliatelle noodles or tapioca-encrusted snapper served on a crispy sushi rice cake with a bright ponzu sauce.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12327;Cheeky's;USA;Palm Springs;622 N. Palm Canyon Dr., Palm Springs, 92262, USA;33.8323479;-116.5466303;86;false;false;American, Californian;Bacon is in the air at this perpetually packed daytime-only hotspot. After checking in, you’ll rub elbows with sunglass-clad locals while waiting for a text saying you’ve nabbed a seat on the ever-popular (covered) patio. There is a small dining area inside, and house-made pastries like tempting cinnamon rolls are available at the counter for those on the run, but the bulk of the action is outdoors. This kitchen taps into the area’s bounty, with most of the produce hailing from within 100 miles. The quirky menu, divided between breakfast and lunch options, changes weekly, offering dishes like birria hash with poached eggs. Don’t miss the “bacon flight,” a selection of five strips of various flavors, ranging from apple cinnamon to jalapeño.;Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12329;hibi;USA;Los Angeles;3121 W. Olympic Blvd., Ste. 103, Los Angeles, 90006, USA;34.0529853;-118.3038025;20;false;true;Japanese Contemporary, Korean;hibi may have started life as a casual concept but it's shifted gears and is firmly planted in the fine dining scene. The intimate space shares a sleek, minimalist design with gray walls, tables and chairs fitted with black leather.While this restaurant has changed concept to now feature a new chef and menu every season, expect to see some underlying Korean and Japanese influence with dishes like sliced red abalone grilled over binchotan, served with barley "risotto," fermented scallions, and gamtae seaweed or their Korean-influenced tiramisu with ssuk mascarpone cream and crumble with azuki beans.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12331;The Matheson;USA;Healdsburg;106 Matheson St., Healdsburg, 95448, USA;38.6103905;-122.8700559;93;true;true;Contemporary;Chef Dustin Valette's latest venture is no shrinking violet. Located in a soaring complex, the über-cool space never takes the focus away from the menu that weaves seasonal products with California flair and Mediterranean elements. The results are thrilling, largely thanks to the Executive Chef Matt Brimer's ingenuity. Behold a golden paupiette of petrale sole, served with a typically French accoutrement like braised endive, elevated to unexpected heights with the addition of a rich and savory mushroom dashi. All-too-familiar luxuries like foie gras and caviar have an edge of excitement when given counterpoints like kiwi or shiitake XO sauce.These unique stylings are matched by the wine program, which uses a high-tech system to dispense over 100 wines by the glass.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12332;Olivia;USA;Los Angeles;205 S. Vermont Ave., Los Angeles, 90004, USA;34.0707832;-118.2923502;27;false;true;Vegetarian, Contemporary;This restaurant and wine bar in Koreatown charms from its intimate dining room where marble tables are topped with candles and flowers. The vegetarian menu displays both Korean and Mexican influences in dishes like breaded, deep-fried oyster mushrooms with a gochujang dipping sauce and fried squash blossoms filled with fully vegan macadamia ricotta, served on a bed of a pumpkin seed sauce. Nut-based white sauce and slow-roasted tomatoes add terrific flavor to the crispy and airy pizza. Finally, marjoram olive oil cake, served warm with a smooth and creamy passionfruit curd and stewed strawberries, brings it all home. The wine selection is curated by the chef/owner and is available by the glass or bottle.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12333;Paradisaea;USA;San Diego;5680 La Jolla Blvd., San Diego, 92037, USA;32.81545;-117.2707313;33;false;false;Californian, Contemporary;Just look to its name to get a sense of what Paradisaea is all about. This La Jolla spot has an upscale tropical theme, where bar chairs are enlivened with a floral pattern and everything feels sunny and warm, especially outside on the patio.  As might be expected, the mood extends to the bar, where tiki drinks take center stage. The kitchen turns out simple, contemporary cooking featuring local ingredients with Asian and tropical inflections. Case in point? A classic coconut shrimp, though here it's grilled over a robata and served with a coconut-lime dipping sauce. Northern halibut is fried to a crispy, golden brown and served over a thin slice of watermelon radish and lettuce with green curry aioli and a sweet chili sauce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12337;OMA;United Kingdom;London;3 Bedale Street, Borough Market, London, SE1 9AL, United Kingdom;51.5053331;-0.0897239;35;true;true;Greek;Find the subtle little sign and then head upstairs to this lively, hugely fun restaurant serving thrilling cooking from Greece and beyond. This is the spot that the capital’s Hellenic food enthusiasts have been crying out for, with utterly delicious sharing dishes that include spreads and breads, tuna in various forms, plenty from the charcoal grill and standouts like spanakopita and giouvetsi. The covered terrace overlooks Borough Market, the pacing from the kitchen is spot on and the young service team are both warm and helpful. The list of coastal wines is great too.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12338;Jean-Georges at The Leinster;Ireland;Dublin City;7 Mount Street Lower, Dublin City, A94, Ireland;53.3392061;-6.2456518;98;true;false;Contemporary;The famed French chef Jean-Georges Vongerichten, who owns restaurants all over the world, has now expanded his empire to the Emerald Isle with this top-floor restaurant inside The Leinster hotel. It’s a cosy and comfortable place, with floor-to-ceiling windows and an awning-covered terrace allowing for prime city views. The extensive menu includes Jean-Georges signatures like egg toast with caviar, alongside a range of international influences from rigatoni with meatballs to spiced chicken samosas.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12339;Kolae;United Kingdom;London;6 Park Street, Borough Market, London, SE1 9AB, United Kingdom;51.5054308;-0.091596;30;true;false;Thai;The cuisine of southern Thailand provides the inspiration for this bustling restaurant in the equally bustling Borough Market. It’s an extremely popular place and rightly so, with attractive pricing, efficient service and downright delicious cooking. The menu lends itself to sharing and each dish is packed with flavour, including the terrific grilled mussel skewers and some lip-tingling curries. If you can’t decide, opt for the set menu to share – which is also available in a vegan form.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12341;Caladh;Ireland;Greystones;Church Road, Greystones, A63 TW18, Ireland;53.1452478;-6.0641344;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A welcome addition to this residential seaside town just south of Dublin, Caladh sits inside a double-fronted Georgian property painted in a fresh light green colour that permeates inside, giving a cool, calming vibe to the brasserie-style dining room. The chefs aren’t trying to reinvent the wheel here, and therein lies the appeal. Classic dishes like confit duck leg and grilled pork chop are ingredient-led and lean on the abundant natural flavours of the produce. A sensibly priced wine list adds to the already considerable attraction.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12342;Riviera by Jean Imbert;;Dubai;The Lana, Marasi Drive, Business Bay, Dubai;25.1888818;55.2890885;44;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Be transported to the iconic French Riviera in the heart of Business Bay. Ideally located on the fourth floor of The Lana hotel, overlooking a small marina of luxury yachts, this restaurant exudes chic, French allure from its style to its flavours. Ratatouille cake, signature tuna tartare (made at your table) to green risotto and Carabineros spaghetti, allow you to travel from the South of France to Italy in just a few bites. Its bright terrace is perfect for alfresco dining during cooler weather.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
12343;Siraj;;Dubai;Souk Al Bahar, Dubai;25.1949403;55.277198;20;false;true;Middle Eastern;Siraj has a stylish, modern look enhanced by numerous references to Arabic culture, and its comfortable terrace is a great place from which to enjoy the nightly fountain show. The wide-ranging menu respects the traditions of Emirati and Levantine cuisines, whilst incorporating subtle modern influences, such as the lobster kebbe and shrimp kunafa.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12345;Rhodes w1;;Dubai;Mezzanine Florr, Grosvenor House Hotel, Al Emreef Street, Dubai Marina, Dubai;25.0859416;55.1440124;15;true;true;British Contemporary;The most recent redecoration resulted in a brighter, airier look for this restaurant in the Grosvenor House hotel. The culinary legacy of the late, great Gary Rhodes is reflected in the appealing menu of European and British dishes. The kitchen handles classics like smoked haddock with Welsh rarebit, salmon fishcake, and bread and butter pudding so well they’re sure to hit the spot. Be sure to also try the chocolate Jaffa fondant with orange jelly.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12346;Maya Bay;;Dubai;Jumeirah Al Naseem Hotel, 906 Jumeirah Street, Umm Suqeim 3, Dubai;25.1366389;55.1869276;36;false;false;Asian;Glamorous sister to the original in Monte Carlo, this restaurant’s unmistakeable Asian vibe comes courtesy of wood panelling, carvings and a cool red palette, while a resident DJ keeps things jumping until the wee small hours. The menu covers Japan, Thailand and China, so you can start with sushi or dim sum and then head for their signature pad thai or something from the robata grill. Grab some mochi buns from the counter on the way home.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
12348;Akira Back;;Dubai;5th Floor, W Dubai Hotel, West Crescent Road, The Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.1067914;55.1117003;64;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;Set on the fifth floor of the colourful W Hotel, this bright, modern restaurant features raised alcoves and a magical terrace with breathtaking views of the city skyline. The professional staff are happy to make recommendations and the creative Japanese cuisine comes with Korean and international flavours.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12350;Fi'lia;;Dubai;70th Floor, SLS Dubai Hotel & Residences, Marasi Drive, Business Bay, Dubai;25.1850567;55.2924909;72;false;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Its name means ‘daughter’, highlighting the women leading the way in the kitchen, as well as the culinary knowledge passed down through the generations. Set on the 70th floor, it offers impressive views, while menus list everything from artisan pizza and traditional pastas, like spaghetti carbonara, to sea bass crudo. Save room for their desserts – the pavlova and limone in particular.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12351;L'Atelier de Joël Robuchon;;Dubai;Gate Village 11, DIFC, Dubai;25.2150153;55.2830011;45;true;false;French Contemporary;Robuchon’s Dubai outpost is set in the heart of the DIFC and features the trademark open kitchen and red and black colour scheme. Sophisticated small plates are underpinned by a strong classical base, revisited in a contemporary key. Desserts are a highlight with an impressive choice of soufflés – for the ultimate experience, go for the 7-course tasting menu. Eat directly on the counter or on the panoramic, outdoor terrace.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12352;Coya;;Dubai;Restaurant Village Four Seasons Resort Jumeirah Beach Road, Jumeirah 2, Dubai;25.2026388;55.2405258;16;true;false;Peruvian;Part of the popular 'Restaurant Village' at the Four Seasons resort, this stylish restaurant brings all the intoxicating atmosphere and vibrant flavours of Latin America to Dubai. Contemporary Peruvian dishes feature intense contrasts of texture and flavour. The beautiful pisco bar adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12353;Trèsind;;Dubai;One&Only Royal Mirage, Arabian Court, Dubai Marina, Dubai;25.0990942;55.1542869;62;false;true;Indian;Expect exciting and imaginative Indian cuisine that isn’t afraid to push the boundaries, but also a kitchen which knows quality ingredients and how to get the best out of them. The spacious restaurant relocated here to the luxury One&Only Royal Mirage hotel at the end of 2022. There are lots of large tables for bigger parties and even larger windows providing views over the gardens.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12354;French Riviera;;Dubai;Jumeirah Al Qasr Hotel - King Salman Bin Abdulaziz Al Saud Street, Dubai;25.133465;55.1832647;99;false;false;French;Whilst the restaurant may overlook the Persian Gulf, the menu transports you to the Mediterranean and, as the name suggests, the cuisine of the Côte d'Azur. The Dégustation menu is the best way to sample the specialities, like onion tart and bouillabaisse. It’s a charming space on a private beach and is divided into a series of elegant rooms with an open kitchen at its hub. It’s best to approach from the Jumeirah Al Qasr hotel and walk through the gardens.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12355;Rüya;;Dubai;The St. Regis Dubai, The Palm, Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.113989;55.1404915;19;false;true;Turkish;On the 3rd floor of the St. Regis Dubai sits this boldly decorated restaurant, with its striking chandeliers, picture windows and an open kitchen down one side. The Anatolian cuisine takes traditional recipes and updates them, to create dishes that are as vibrant as they are satisfying – this is the sort of food that you feel is doing you good. There’s plenty of choice and a great value lunch menu too – just leave room for fırın sütlaç, a traditional baked rice pudding.;Air conditioning;[]
12357;Bombay Bungalow;;Dubai;The Beach Mall, Unit 2301, JBR Walk,, Dubai;25.0780481;55.1328043;46;false;true;Indian;This fun, modern Indian restaurant is open from breakfast onwards and is set right by the beach, so you can sit on the terrace and watch the world go by. Choose from street food, kebabs and classic curries: cooking is fresh, authentic and well-priced, and the caring service adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12359;Cipriani;;Dubai;Gate Village 10, DIFC, Dubai;25.2126877;55.2827172;20;true;false;Italian;In the centre of the Financial District you’ll find this lively, popular Italian restaurant, which comes with classical styling and old-school service from well-organised staff, smartly dressed in white jackets. Expect pizza, pasta and risotto, alongside all the celebrated Cipriani signatures and classics from Venice’s iconic Harry’s Bar. The fixed price lunch menu is a steal.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12360;TERO - The Experience by Reif Othman;;Dubai;Building 3, Dubai Hills Estate Business Park, Dubai Hills, Dubai;25.1065943;55.2404162;82;false;true;Creative;Accessible through an entrance inside Reif's Kushiyaki Japanese Restaurant, in Dubai Hills Business Park, TERO is an intimate and immersive dining experience. A wooden, U-shaped table seats 12 guests in front of an open kitchen, where Chef Noor Ibrahim showcases his skills with an 8 or 12 course omakase of modern Japanese creations with some international influence, depending on the menu’s monthly theme. Diners can directly interact with the chef and service team, creating a warm, conversational and communal atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12362;L’Olivo at Al Mahara;;Dubai;Burj Al Arab Jumeirah - Jumeirah Street, Dubai;25.1412296;55.1855351;80;false;false;Italian;The restaurant may be on the ground floor of Burj Al Arab, but thanks to the aquarium around which the tables are wrapped, one is soon transported to another world. The base of the cooking is Italian and the menu includes some of the signature dishes from their mothership in Capri, but the kitchen also puts its own spin on many of the creations. The set menu offers an all-round experience and represents the best value. Service is attentive and charming.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
12363;99 Sushi Bar;;Dubai;Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Boulevard, Dubai;25.1949842;55.2780878;88;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;Its prime, raised position and smart outdoor terrace lend an element of glamour to this Spanish-owned Japanese restaurant. The wide-ranging menu covers all the bases, with plenty of sushi – both modern and traditional – on offer. The robata grill is used to particularly good effect and there’s also a well-priced set lunch for those short on time. The service team are helpful and attentive.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
12365;Il Borro Tuscan Bistro Dubai;;Dubai;Jumeirah Al Naseem Hotel, 906 Jumeirah Street, Umm Suqeim 3, Dubai;25.1373392;55.1873157;100;false;true;Italian;Set by the lovely Turtle Lagoon on the Jumeirah Al Naseem resort, this chic, well-dressed restaurant is understandably popular. Colourfully presented, traditional Italian dishes transport diners to the rolling Tuscan hills, and the friendly yet formal service comes with an old-fashioned Italian charm.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12366;City Social;;Dubai;43rd Floor, Tower 2, Grosvenor House Hotel,  Al Emreef Street, Dubai Marina, Dubai;25.0861018;55.1435568;19;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Commanding views from its perch on the 43rd floor of the Grosvenor House hotel are not the only attraction of this branch of the Jason Atherton empire.  The extensive menu offers something for everyone, including pasta dishes and a wide choice of dry-aged steaks which are cooked over charcoal. Kick off your experience with a cocktail on the intimate and elegant outside terrace.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12367;Demon Duck by Alvin Leung;;Dubai;Banyan Tree Dubai, Bluewaters Island, Dubai;25.0813059;55.1201059;86;true;true;Chinese Contemporary;The eponymous celebrity chef brings his fun, bold style of cooking to Banyan Tree Hotel, where service is sweet and attentive, and the generous dishes are ideal for sharing. The fun, extensive menu offers Chinese classics with an original twist. We suggest starting with their salt and pepper tofu, then try out their lobster with green onions and ginger and finish off with a chocolate matcha fondant with brown rice ice cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12368;La Petite Maison (LPM);;Dubai;Gate Village 8, DIFC, Dubai;25.2138472;55.2830487;98;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, French;A popular and bright French brasserie with high ceilings, an open kitchen and a buzzing atmosphere. The menu offers tried-and-tested French classics with some Mediterranean influences and dishes are fresh, well-crafted and very tasty. End on a sweet note with desserts mostly complemented by homemade ice cream. The friendly service team put their guests at the centre of the dining experience. Be sure to book in advance to secure your spot in this busy restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12369;Avli BY TASHAS;;Dubai;Unit C01, Gate Village 9, DIFC, Dubai;25.213057;55.2821754;66;true;false;Greek;Expectations are exceeded at this bright, dapper-looking restaurant in the DIFC. Its owner is of Greek heritage, and the extensive menu offers authentic, carefully cooked Greek dishes made from quality ingredients. Enjoy mezze, salads and seafood alongside classics such as feta saganaki and lamb youvetsi.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12370;Armani Hashi;;Dubai;Burj Khalifa, 1 Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Boulevard, Dubai;25.1970278;55.2746057;25;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Sleek, modern and minimalistic, with impressive views of the fountains, as well as plenty of culinary theatrics at the sushi, robatayaki and teppanyaki counters. Contemporary Japanese dishes use first class ingredients flown in from Japan, with desserts a particular highlight. Go for one of the omakase menus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12372;Shang Palace;;Dubai;Shangri-La Dubai Hotel, 1st Floor, Sheikh Zayed Road, Dubai;25.2100338;55.2732758;52;true;true;Chinese, Contemporary;Set on the first floor of the Shangri-La Hotel, this restaurant features traditional Chinese décor and offers friendly, professional service. Their menu is extensive, where good quality ingredients are used to create tasty, authentic dishes, with Cantonese specialities, assorted and colourful dim sum – and a signature dish of Peking duck in generous portions. The business lunch menu is full of favourites at a good price.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
12375;StreetXO;;Dubai;4th Floor, One&Only One Za’abeel, Za'abeel 1, Dubai;25.2282916;55.2906261;48;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant was borne from the mind of acclaimed Spanish chef, Dabiz Muñoz of DiverXO in Madrid. The lively and open-plan space has graffiti-covered walls, a neon-lit cocktail bar serving creative drinks, and large open kitchen with a counter (the best place to sit). The menu boasts a mix of modern, globally inspired street food originating from Europe, Asia, South America and beyond. Start with some croquetas, then the beautifully crisp soft-shell crab, and be sure to end with the 'Fluido', a molten white chocolate and egg yolk 'lava' cake. Staff are dressed in punk-inspired jackets, with a super-friendly, attentive yet relaxed attitude.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12376;Zuma;;Dubai;Gate Village 6, DIFC, Dubai;25.2143067;55.2837797;97;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;The Dubai outpost of this global brand is set over three floors and comes with trendy, contemporary styling, several sushi counters and a lively atmosphere. Super-fresh, high quality ingredients are prepared with dexterity. Flavours are superb and the charming staff provide friendly, efficient service.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12377;Jaleo by José Andrés;;Dubai;Atlantis The Royal, Crescent Road, The Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.1391107;55.1287225;44;true;false;Spanish;Don’t be put off by learning that this restaurant is found in the basement of the Atlantis The Royal hotel, because it’s full of colour and always fun. Under the aegis of chef José Andrés, it offers a mouth-watering mix of great paellas from the wood-burning fire, fine Galician seafood and other prime Spanish produce – the tasting menu offers a great all-round experience. Be sure to take a table by the long waterfall on the lovely terrace, fringed by ancient Spanish olive trees.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12378;Mina Brasserie;;Dubai;Four Seasons, Dubai International Financial Center, Dubai;25.2140189;55.2837836;15;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Michael Mina is a chef best-known in the USA and here at the Four Seasons he now has this brightly decorated and impeccably run brasserie de-luxe as the backdrop for his menu of equally sunny French and Mediterranean classics. From a host of fresh salads to seafood and wood-grilled steaks, there’s something for everyone and all occasions. Look out too for the good value mid-week menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12379;La Mar by Gastón Acurio;;Dubai;Atlantis The Royal, Crescent Road, The Palm Jumeriah, Dubai;25.1387601;55.1275229;38;true;false;Peruvian;Enthusiastic staff are here to greet you at this first-floor restaurant at the Atlantis The Royal hotel – the views are impressive and the DJ ensures the atmosphere never lets up. The large fish counter is busting with prime seafood and the menu is full of classic Peruvian dishes, from ceviche and tiraditos to anticuchos. A pisco sour will help you make your choices.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12381;Indego by Vineet;;Dubai;Tower 1, Grosvenor House Hotel,  Al Emreef Street, Dubai Marina, Dubai;25.0860929;55.1439412;57;true;false;Indian;This brightly decorated, intimate Indian restaurant offers everything from street food inspired snacks to dishes from the griddle, tandoor, grill and stew pot, with plenty of options perfect for sharing. Spicing is delicate and presentation can be playful. Sit on the terrace overlooking the marina.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12382;Masti;;Dubai;The Dubai Edition Hotel, Floor 1, Downtown, Dubai;25.1922715;55.2808803;18;false;true;Indian;In 2023 this colourful and creative restaurant moved to a new berth within The Dubai Edition hotel – and it’s a good fit. There’s more than a hint of whimsy to the vibrant decoration and equal amounts of imagination are shown in the menu. The kitchen isn’t afraid of incorporating global influences alongside the Indian flavours, which results in intriguing but always enjoyable dishes that are meant for sharing. Fun and mischievous indeed.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12383;Brasserie Boulud;;Dubai;Wafi City, Sheikh Rashid Road, Dubai;25.2313051;55.3184046;42;false;true;French, Classic Cuisine;Creating a little piece of France in Sofitel Dubai The Obelisk is this classically styled brasserie deluxe with its marble flooring, red leather banquettes and art deco touches. In a spacious setting inspired by acclaimed chef Daniel Boulud, the restaurant’s appealing menu offers all the French classics from escargots and canard rôti to tarte Tatin and île flottante. It also has a good value business lunch.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12384;Mimi Kakushi;;Dubai;Restaurant Village Four Seasons Resort, Jumeirah Beach Road, Jumeirah 2, Dubai;25.202733;55.2406678;79;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;With its exotic décor and sultry soundtrack, this trendy spot evokes 1920s Osaka, and offers a lively atmosphere as well as plenty of intimate corners. Good quality ingredients are used to create classic Japanese dishes with a contemporary twist. Well-structured service comes from an enthusiastic young team.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
12385;CÉ LA VI;;Dubai;The Address Sky View Tower 2, Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Boulevard, Dubai;25.2019048;55.2704192;100;false;true;Contemporary;The Dubai outpost of this fashionable restaurant group is set on the 54th floor of the Address Sky View Hotel. It comes with a party atmosphere and a bird’s eye view over the city from its super terrace, and service is friendly and professional. Contemporary dishes have influences ranging from a mix of Mediterranean, such as fried calamari and spinach rigatoni, to Japanese classics, such as nigiri and beef kushiyaki.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12387;Cinque;;Dubai;FIVE Palm Jumeirah - No 1 Palm Jumeirah, Dubai;25.1041759;55.1485486;24;false;false;Italian, International;Fashionable, glamorous and full of energy, this buzzing Italian restaurant overlooks the trendy FIVE Palm Jumeirah’s swimming pool. Arched ceilings are complemented by warm lighting and a self-playing piano keeps everyone entertained. The menu offers up a mix of classic Italian favourites, such as parmigiana di melanzane and fassona tartare with white truffle, along with more modern interpretations, like their dessert version of a Bellini cocktail. The terrace is a great spot for alfresco dining during Dubai’s cooler weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12389;Chic Nonna;;Dubai;DIFC, Gate Avenue, South Zone, Dubai;25.2070824;55.2766019;45;false;true;Italian;Set over two levels within DIFC, this Dubai outpost of the Florentine original is a handsome creation – to find it just look out for the bright green door. The main dining room is set around an open kitchen, while upstairs hosts a stylish and comfortable lounge. Meanwhile, the menu boasts all the Italian classics, including chef’s signature ‘calamarata 2.0’ and ricciola e melone.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12391;RSVP;;Dubai;Al Wasl Road, Jumeriah 2, Dubai;25.2045773;55.2524842;55;false;false;French;The good-looking terrace and comfortable interior are not the only things that set this restaurant apart from its Boxpark neighbours – there’s the attentive service and the flattering lighting to consider too. The appealing menu and skill of the kitchen also make this a good choice for dinner. There’s no better representation of the cuisine – which is French, with hints of Japanese – than the delicious charcoal-smoked lamb chops with teriyaki sauce.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12393;Clap;;Dubai;Gate Village 11, DIFC, Dubai;25.2144782;55.2828953;45;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;Private lifts whisk you up to the 9th floor, where you enter this chic, modern restaurant with a sizeable cocktail bar and a buzzy vibe. The menu is a roll-call of Japanese classics, from sushi, sashimi and shrimp tempura to mains like miso cod. The rooftop terrace with its city views is the place to be.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12394;Al-Fanar;;Dubai;Al Seef unit P3-07-02, Dubai;25.2642514;55.3052805;53;true;false;Emirati Cuisine;The newest restaurant from the Al-Fanar stable is on the banks of the Dubai Creek and, like the others, showcases the owners’ passion for Emirati cuisine. The interior has a rustic feel, while, out on the terrace, diners can watch the fish stalls float by, underlining the freshness of the seafood on their plate.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12396;Atrangi by Ritu Dalmia;;Dubai;207, Jumeirah Al Qasr Hotel, Al Safouh First, Dubai;25.129476;55.183856;54;false;true;Indian;Situated in a charming spot by a canal at Jumeirah Al Qasr resort is this pretty, spacious house presenting Indian creations from the mind of chef Ritu Dalmia. Inside, the bright and open dining room benefits from the large bay windows that provide views out over the water and lush gardens. The menu offers a good choice of traditional specialities from many different regions of India, prepared in a contemporary way, along with other dishes that are more fusion in their makeup. Guests are greeted by smiling staff and service is always friendly and efficient.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12397;Fouquet's;;Dubai;Burj Plaza, Sheikh Mohammed Bin Rashid Boulevard, Dubai;25.1912742;55.2759316;32;false;true;French;After launching at Louvre Abu Dhabi, in 2023 it was the turn of Downtown Dubai to welcome its own branch of this famous Parisian restaurant. The plaques by the red carpeted entrance advertise all the famous faces who have passed through its various doors – so if you want a souvenir of your own glamorous experience there’s even a photo-booth downstairs. As expected, the menu celebrates classic French cooking.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12398;Mott 32;;Dubai;Address Beach Resort, The Walk, Jumeriah Beach Residence, Dubai;25.0724501;55.1267553;99;true;true;Cantonese;The 73rd floor of Address Beach Resort was the chosen venue for Dubai’s branch of this ever-expanding chain and the views are predictably stunning. As with all their restaurants, the owners didn’t spare any expense when it came to the decoration – this is a sumptuously furnished spot. The carefully prepared food is largely Cantonese, but applewood roasted Peking duck is a speciality and there are also some Sichuan dishes on offer.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12400;Netsu by Ross Shonhan;;Dubai;Mandarin Oriental Jumeira Hotel, Jumeirah Beach Road, Jumeirah 1, Dubai;25.2169226;55.2510563;40;true;true;Japanese Contemporary;This Japanese steakhouse delivers a theatrical culinary experience thanks to the large open kitchen which takes centre stage. The cavernous room is light and airy, and menu highlights include dishes cooked over rice straw on the Warayaki grill. Start with the tuna tataki, followed by a Wagyu steak.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12402;Boca;;Dubai;Gate Village Building 6, Dubai International Financial Centre, Dubai, 506772, United Arab Emirates, Dubai;25.2140452;55.2829438;98;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The bright, sunny look of the room is reflected in the extensive menu which careers joyfully around the Mediterranean, offering something for everyone – be sure to bring some friends so you can order with abandon. The Spanish dishes particularly stand out, such as the good-looking green herb gazpacho – the perfect refresher on a hot day.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12403;Ariana's Persian Kitchen;;Dubai;Atlantis The Royal, Crescent Road, The Palm Jumeriah, Dubai;25.1385087;55.1277911;87;false;true;Persian;From celebrity chef Ariana Bundy comes this fragrant, pastel-coloured restaurant on the ground floor of Atlantis The Royal, with its almost tent-like feel and a fine covered terrace with views of the gardens. The appealing menu offers a host of Persian foods and flavours, from vibrant salads to charred meats and kababs, all designed for sharing, along with a great selection of teas. You’ll leave feeling good about life.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12404;Ninive;;Dubai;Emirates Towers Hotel, Sheikh Zayed Road, Dubai;25.2178336;55.2834042;48;false;false;Middle Eastern;Set in a bustling area of the city, in the midst of grand towers, this charming restaurant exists in another world: a relaxing oasis, a step back in time. The design of this outdoor-only restaurant reflects a Bedouin tent, with rugs and lanterns, low tables and cosy sofas and lush greenery, representative of the ancient Mesopotamian city, Ninawa. Tasty and made-to-share dishes boast flavours from all over the Middle East and North Africa.;Air conditioning;[]
12406;Sucre;;Dubai;Gate Village 5, DIFC, Dubai;25.2143957;55.2835532;30;true;false;Latin American;You're guaranteed a lively night out at this fashionable spot with its buzzy bar and huge open kitchen. Sharing plates combine Latin American and global influences and the open fire is used to good effect, so expect some bold and punchy flavours. The engaging team further enhance the experience.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12409;Pirouette;France;Nice;34 rue Bonaparte, Nice, 06300, France;43.7005196;7.2850063;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This intimate bistro was a grocery shop in a former life. Opened by the team behind Nice restaurant Les Agitateurs, this place serves up seasonal and fresh dishes playfully drawing inspiration from both classic and more exotic dishes: lamb in lettuce-leaf "tacos", "River Kwai" ravioli or, a classic if ever there was one, pigeon pithiviers and foie gras… On this short menu, most dishes are designed for sharing (for two people), to a background of trendy music. The "living" wine list also embraces the orange wine craze. Sunday brunch.;Air conditioning;[]
12410;Naissain;France;Le Teich;10 rue des Castaings, Le Teich, 33470, France;44.635595;-1.0246331;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Naissain means "spat" – or oyster larvae. This modern bistro was opened by Thomas Iglesias, a chef who has sailed the seven seas. He always has one dish devoted to this mollusc, with supplies from his brother's oyster farm in La Teste de Buch. As for the rest, this chef who loves to travel admits to having a soft spot for vegetables (there is a vegetarian starter and main course on the menu at every service). Imagination goes into teasing out each vegetable's flavour, in dishes such as the slice of baked celeriac brushed with a tasty vegetable jus and topped with roasted pistachios and cubes of feta. There is a short à la carte menu comprising three dishes that change each month, plus a great value lunch set menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12412;Halo Paris;France;Paris;12 rue Saint-Sauveur, Paris, 75002, France;48.8660245;2.3489295;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is tucked away at the back of a fashion and design concept store showcasing young designers. Behind the wooden door, light flows through the glass roof into a space with an open kitchen and a bare concrete floor. A veritable cultural hub, the basement includes a small exhibition room, a cocktail bar and a table d'hôte. In the kitchen, chef Victor Blanchet (who was a contestant on French TV's Top Chef in 2023 and has also worked at L'Arpège and Neso) is inspired by the Mediterranean and the Basque Country – serving dishes that are colourful, light and well composed, such as sea bass tataki flambéed with pastis, beetroot mousseline and preserved lemon. Online bookings only.;;[]
12413;Mắm From Hanoï;France;Paris;39 rue de Cléry, Paris, 75002, France;48.868479;2.3480425;16;false;false;Vietnamese;In a corner of the Sentier neighbourhood, this authentic Vietnamese restaurant is a hit, and rightly so (book several days in advance). The Hanoi-born couple at the helm prepare bona fide Northern Vietnamese cuisine – the word mắm refers to a fish-based condiment that is very popular there. The vegetables and meats are of French origin and rigorously selected. Focusing on the essentials, the menu includes the not-to-be-missed pork nems, served with their famous mắm sauce, plus an excellent phở: typical of the North, the soup is slightly salty and all the more easily digestible for it – the quintessence of this aromatic food, which effortlessly fuses simplicity of execution with complexity of flavour.;Air conditioning;[]
12417;Le Pétrocore;France;Périgueux;15 rue Éguillerie, Périgueux, 24000, France;45.1851007;0.7211365;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Petrocorri were a Gallic people who settled in the Dordogne – a sign that the chef is proud of his roots. This pleasant venue in the historical heart of Périgueux, beneath century-old arcades, is the chef’s brainchild. He rolls out a two-pronged concept, with a bargain bistro-style lunch, and a more elevated fine dining menu with several courses in the evening. The contemporary, meticulously plated food takes local ingredients and tweaks them ever so slightly, like his black pork of Périgord with black beans and garlic condiment.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12419;Le Florida;France;Castéra-Verduzan;2 rue du Lac, Castéra-Verduzan, 32410, France;43.8044123;0.4328314;32;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;While regional delicacies remain firm fixtures on the menu of this welcoming traditional establishment (in business since the 1930s), a few discreet nods to the Mexican roots of the new owner have found their way into the culinary score. Examples include crispy crackling chicharron appetisers or a smoked, spicy tomato sauce that adds a kick to a starter of thinly sliced carpaccio of stuffed duck neck, apples and mayonnaise made from Gascony mustard. Healthful, fresh, throbbing with flavour and top-drawer quality. On sunny days, the shaded alfresco patio is blissful.;Terrace;[]
12423;Little Bear;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;36 Nguyen Ba Huan Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.804291;106.729192;80;true;true;Vietnamese Contemporary;This newcomer to HCMC’s bistro scene greets diners with a cosy dining room that offers both counter and table seating. The theatrical open kitchen is where the alchemy takes place. The menu consists of modern dishes inspired by the chef’s childhood memories and Vietnamese food culture, including cheese and noodles made from scratch in-house. The wine list features a wide range of wines by the glass, covering organic, biodynamic and natural tipples.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12424;Phở Bò Phú Gia;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;146E Ly Chinh Thang Street, Ward 14, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, 722700, Vietnam;10.786433;106.684542;97;false;false;Noodles;This shop specialises in beef noodle soup – choose between sliced beef, brisket, or both. As opposed to raw beef instantly blanched in the hot broth, its signature phở tái lăn is topped with wok-seared garlic beef, alongside heaps of chopped scallion, onion and coriander that impart rich aromas. If you fancy the brisket, we recommend the phở dặc biệt. For a different texture, dip the fried dough sticks into the broth before sampling.;Cash only;[]
12425;Le Beaulieu;Vietnam;Hanoi;Sofitel Legend Metropole, 15 Ngo Quyen Street, Trang Tien Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.02418;105.85581;26;true;true;French;Le Beaulieu has been operating at the same spot since 1901. The interior has been entirely refurbished and remodelled with mod cons and a chic décor, while retaining its French DNA courtesy of details such as blue velvet banquettes and crystal chandeliers. Century-old classics like the lobster bisque and house-cured kingfish or salmon come with gueridon service, just like in the good old days. Subtle Vietnamese notes depict the tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12426;Mỳ Quảng Cô Sáu;Vietnam;Da Nang;397 Tran Hung Dao Street, An Hai Tay Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0664166;108.2296495;17;false;true;Vietnamese;Perched on the bank of Han River, the room with yellow walls and greenery feels relaxed and cheerful. The owner hails from Quảng Nam and naturally, he chose to sell mi quảng noodles, a speciality from his homeland. The intense broth is coloured yellow by turmeric and available toppings include chicken, fish and shrimp. Another must-try is thịt heo bánh tráng – thinly sliced pork belly rolled in rice paper with herbs and veggies.;Car park;[]
12428;Kobe Bistro;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;23C Ton Duc Thang Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 710000, Vietnam;10.782601;106.705549;17;true;true;French Contemporary;Owner-chef David Thai spent time in France, together with stints in Dubai, Spain and various Asian countries. Formerly a Japanese produce trader and culinary consultant, he makes the most of his connections and expertise in this bistro. On top of French classics such as bouillabaisse and duck leg confit, the menu also features a line-up of marbled Kobe Wagyu steaks, including Bushu Oguma A4 and Satsuma A5+, served with a range of sauces.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
12429;Cau Go;Vietnam;Hanoi;6-7F, 9 Dinh Tien Hoang Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0321366;105.8519429;79;false;true;Vietnamese;Enter the building from Dinh Tien Hoang or Cau Go Street and ride the lift to the restaurant. You can expect authentic, immaculately seasoned Central Vietnamese cuisine. Don't miss the deep-fried traditional Vietnamese spring rolls. If you go as a group, definitely order their popular hot pot – either chicken with basil leaves or beef and a wide range of other ingredients. The window seats and 7th-floor terrace command scenic lake views.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12430;Ốc Vi Saigon;Vietnam;Hanoi;21 Gia Ngu Street, Hang Bac Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, 100000, Vietnam;21.0329841;105.8527937;41;true;false;Seafood;The extensive, reasonably priced menu is mainly composed of seafood dishes with a wide array of shellfish from oysters to white clams, snails, cockles and scallops. Snails are the specialty here, cooked in a variety of ways and sauces. The stir-fried white clams in garlic butter exude a strong aroma, while an irresistible umami flavour pervades the stir-fried cockles with tamarind. Order a mini baguette so you can mop up the delicious sauce!;Air conditioning;[]
12431;Bờm;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;24 Nguyen Thi Nghia Street, Ben Thanh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.770666;106.69366;42;true;true;Vietnamese Contemporary;Bờm's ambience and cuisine conjure up a fairy tale-like nostalgia for Vietnamese diners. In a chic, low-lit venue combining traditional bamboo with minimalist cement elements, the modern, refined Vietnamese cuisine ticks all the boxes. Try the bò kho tart – tender braised beef encased in flaky puff pastry – and the signature Bờm Set, comprising bite-size shrimp fritters, snail cakes and fishcakes. Mè đen, a mochi with a black sesame filling, provides a sweet finale.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12432;Hemispheres Steak & Seafood Grill;Vietnam;Hanoi;2F, Sheraton Hotel, K5 Nghi Tam, 11 Xuan Dieu Road, Quang An Ward, Tay Ho District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.02828;105.85388;90;true;true;Steakhouse;Embark on a culinary journey around the world with the freshest ingredients from the northern and southern hemispheres, as well as the east and the west. Tailor your itinerary across the continent, possibly with house marinated Atlantic salmon from the north/west, or grilled New Zealand rack of lamb from the south/east. Fine range of worldclass premium beef steaks. The views over West Lake offer a slice of tranquillity amidst the urban turmoil.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12433;A Bản Mountain Dew;Vietnam;Hanoi;76 Tran Phu Street, Dien Bien Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.03254;105.8321;67;false;false;Vietnamese;The lush garden complete with water features and a dining room decked out in colourful fabric are inspired by the nature and culture of northwestern Vietnam, Chef Phạm Việt’s birthplace. In the same vein, authentic Mông, Tày, Muong and Tai cuisine from the region dominates the menu resulting in a fascinating ethnic mix hard to find elsewhere. Rare ingredients such as snake, horse, buffalo and carp add to the exotic and eclectic experience.;Air conditioning;[]
12434;La Badiane;Vietnam;Hanoi;10 Nam Ngu Street, Cua Nam Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.02652;105.84243;83;false;true;Fusion;Badiane is French for star anise and a glass jar of this spice adorns every table. The experienced and well-travelled French chef delivers an impressive selection of vibrant and adventurous fusion dishes with bold flavours and appealing textural contrasts. A black and white tiled floor and a friendly vibe set the scene downstairs, while the rooms upstairs are more intimate. The set lunch menu is deliciously affordable.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12435;Mì Quảng 1A;Vietnam;Da Nang;1A Hai Phong Street, Hai Chau I Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0722697;108.2191652;17;false;true;Noodles;Mì quảng is a dish from Central Vietnam, popular throughout the country. So, unsurprisingly, this simple shop specialises in ribbon rice noodles in a yellow broth seasoned with fish sauce and turmeric and topped with peanuts and bean sprouts. There are two versions here, pork and shrimp or chicken, with or without hardboiled egg. Order the ‘special’ to try them all. Lettuce, cilantro, and banana flower on the side add aromas and a crispy texture.;Cash only;[]
12436;Coco Dining;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;143 Nam Ky Khoi Nghia Street, Vo Thi Sau Ward, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7808709;106.6932479;36;true;false;Innovative;This chic establishment, part of CoCo Saigon, boasts a whisky bar, a private party villa and a stylish dining room with a kitchen counter and black granite tables. Chef Vo Thanh Vuong presents contemporary cuisine that blends Vietnamese recipes with modern techniques and fermentation. The 12-course tasting menu echoes five distinct philosophies and each course is expertly crafted to balance the complex flavours. À la carte menu available too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
12437;Lửa;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;2 Street No. 11, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, 7000000, Vietnam;10.8051347;106.7466608;27;false;false;European Contemporary;The al fresco wine bar, whose tables are set in a courtyard surrounded by lush greenery, is perfect for a drink and nibbles. There are about 100 wine references to choose from with a substantial by-the-glass selection. The wine list changes every month, but the home-brewed sake, a firm fixture, is worth trying. The menu, which features only organic produce from small local farms, combines European dishes with a twist of Japanese elements as both the manager and head chef hail from Japan.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12438;Phở Việt Nam (District 1);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;14 Pham Hong Thai Street, Ben Thanh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.771283;106.696128;81;true;true;Noodles;This is one of the more recent outlets of the phở chain, which prides itself on its rice ribbon noodles made from scratch. Besides the habitual raw beef and beef balls, specific cuts such as beef shank, flank, oxtail and ribs render different textures and flavours. Every noodle soup comes with herbs, bean sprouts, onion and lime wedges. If you prefer your food piping hot right down to the last mouthful, order phở thố đá (phở in a hot rock bowl).;Air conditioning;[]
12439;3G Trois Gourmands;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;39 Tran Ngoc Dien Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.806161;106.740628;57;false;true;French;Since it opened in 2004, this establishment, a household name in Saigon, has been synonymous with classic French dining. The lavish interior sports ornate chandeliers and stained-glass windows. Most of the ingredients on the extensive menu are flown in from France, but the owner insists on making his own cheeses. All the fish dishes and the classic duck leg confit are excellent main courses. Welcoming yet formal, the service is suitably starched.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12440;Quán Ăn Ngon (Hoan Kiem);Vietnam;Hanoi;18 Phan Boi Chau Street, Cua Nam Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0264787;105.8435552;77;true;true;Vietnamese;Set in a charming colonial villa with bucketloads of character, Quán Ăn Ngon is spread over two storeys. Our favourite spot is the spacious garden-courtyard and its buzzy vibe. The extensive menu, which covers all the bases, takes you on a tour of Vietnam with colourful photographs of each dish to help you make your selection. The cooking is fresh, flavourful and authentic. Even better, the prices won't break the bank.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12441;Olivia's Prime;Vietnam;Da Nang;Lot G1-G4, GF, Indochina Mall, 74 Bach Dang Street, Hai Chau 1 Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0701482;108.2242387;87;true;false;Steakhouse;The family-owned restaurant is known for its quality food and service, as well as its friendly vibe. The menu focuses on beef steaks, including some top notch imported choices such as Japanese Hitachi A5 Wagyu, Aussie Sanchoku MB5 and Black Angus, and USDA Prime. Chargrilled to perfection and flawlessly seasoned, the steaks are tender, juicy and flavourful. Round off your meal with New York style cheesecake.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12443;Bánh Cuốn Bà Xuân;Vietnam;Hanoi;16 Hoe Nhai Street, Nguyen Trung Truc Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0423129;105.8476837;79;false;false;Street Food;The chef crafts delectable bánh cuốn, Vietnamese steamed rolls with minced pork and black fungus. She also serves an option with a soft poached egg. Order the pork meatloaf and sausage, and season with fresh herbs, chilli, lime or garlic at will for a great breakfast or snack.;Cash only;[]
12444;Ốc Oanh;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;534 Vinh Khanh Street, Ward 8, District 4, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.5983;106.74513;36;true;false;Street Food;This joint on a busy street serves a range of seafood cooked in countless ways. Whelks, tiger prawns, lobster, octopus, crab… the choice is yours. The authentic outdoor vibe more than makes up for the lack of air conditioning.;Cash only;[]
12445;Highway4 (Hang Tre Street);Vietnam;Hanoi;5 Hang Tre Street, Ly Thai To Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, 100000, Vietnam;21.0336338;105.8550549;84;false;true;Vietnamese;This Vietnamese tửu quán (tavern) has always been popular with the locals and tourists alike. Most diners take their time, enjoying the food and drink in good company. The inn serves Northern Vietnamese fare and we recommend the subtly flavoured appetisers, such as salads or spring rolls. The catfish spring roll is the tasty signature dish. The heart-warming main courses come in earthen pots. The deliciously tender oxtail stew with herbs is to die for!;Air conditioning;[]
12446;Nu Đồ Kitchen;Vietnam;Da Nang;11/1 Luu Quang Thuan Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.041299;108.245252;47;false;false;Noodles;The owner’s parents used to sell mì quảng, noodle soup from Central Vietnam. The shop is named ‘Nu Đồ’, a transliteration of the word ‘noodle’. The menu boasts four versions of mì quảng served in traditional bamboo baskets like in the old days, each with a special broth to highlight the key ingredient. The snakehead fish variety with pronounced turmeric aromas is not to be missed. Tables are laid in the covered patio, surrounded by greenery.;Cash only;[]
12447;Bánh Xèo Bà Dưỡng;Vietnam;Da Nang;280/23 Hoang Dieu Street, Nam Duong Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.058836;108.216052;87;true;true;Vietnamese;This 30+-year-old no-frills shop at the very end of an alley serves a concise menu of crispy pancakes known as bánh xèo, alongside skewered pork, grilled meat and noodles. Everything comes with fresh herbs, pickled papaya, cucumber and strips of eggplant. Feel free to customise your own rice paper pancake with meat to order and condiments on the table. The minced pork peanut sauce dip is a must.;Cash only;[]
12448;The Temptation;Vietnam;Da Nang;125 Ho Nghinh Street, Phuoc My Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0735611;108.2433229;58;false;false;French Contemporary;This modern villa with a beautiful courtyard and an opulent dining room is home to an upmarket eatery helmed by Vietnamese chef La Thua An. Brought up in France, he opened The Temptation in 2019, wowing diners with ingenious creations, layers of flavours and often whimsical plating. His signature dessert The Sweet Egg Nest of Han River, for instance, features numerous ingredients encased in a spun-sugar egg-shaped shell in a bamboo cage.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12449;MaSa French Eatery by Hervé;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;204/20 Nguyen Van Huong Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7797546;106.7186274;72;false;true;French Contemporary;Abutting the swanky upmarket Hervé Dining Room, MaSa (Manipulator of Savours) is the same chef’s more accessible sibling eatery. As opposed to a multi-course experience, the menu focuses on French tapas to share. The food shows a hint of Asian accents, paired with a well curated wine list. Try Black Angus hanger steak from Korea, and the signature snickers dessert. Al fresco dining with a pond and a charcoal grill dripping in unique charm.;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12450;Bún Thịt Nướng Hoàng Văn;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;137 Chan Hung Street, Ward 6, Tan Binh District, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7851694;106.6623288;38;false;false;Street Food;There is only one item on the menu – rice noodles in a tangy sweet dressing with a spring roll, grilled pork, lettuce, bean sprouts, cucumber, carrot, peanuts and scallion. The contrasting textures and flavours are magical.;Cash only;[]
12451;Oryz;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;51 Tran Nhat Duat Street, Tan Dinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.793999;106.689591;67;true;true;Asian Contemporary;Rice is the staple ingredient that links all Asian culinary cultures, so the chef named the restaurant after the Latin word for rice. Naturally, he endeavours to present the grain in various forms, from puffed rice and deep-fried rice noodles to koji and sparkling sake. Familiar Asian recipes are reimagined with a flourish. Try his version of cơm lam, or glutinous rice in a bamboo tube with shrimp and 18-day home-cured pork and sausage.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12452;Olivia;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;31A Le Van Mien Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.80536;106.73358;82;true;true;European Contemporary;Named after Chef David Green’s daughter, Olivia is another highlight of his glorious culinary career. The serene oasis amid the hustle and bustle of Thao Dien ward features a white colour scheme, pale wood and European-style furnishings. The kitchen behind a glazed wall showcases the chefs working their magic. Food-wise, Asian ingredients are precisely prepared with sensuous flavours and underpinned by modern European techniques.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12453;Chapter;Vietnam;Hanoi;12C Chan Cam Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0303781;105.8482559;83;false;false;Vietnamese Contemporary;Chapter’s façade of Corten steel slats leads into an open kitchen that produces unique flavours and textures over a charcoal grill. The single tasting menu features 10+ courses anchored in Vietnamese heritage, all artfully plated. A small clay house is set on each table and each course comes with a postcard in which the chef shares his memories. Globally sourced produce is combined with Vietnamese culinary heritage to great effect.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
12454;Bún Bò Huế Cô Như;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;274/29 Vo Van Tan Street, Ward 5, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, 722700, Vietnam;10.772525;106.68554;79;false;true;Noodles;This family-run shop is tucked away in a narrow alley. It takes a little effort to find, but you’ll well be rewarded by tasty beef noodle soups. First-timers may go for bún bò thập cẩm (mixed beef noodle soup), a great way to sample all four toppings of beef and pork, boasting robust meaty flavours. The sweet broth with great depth is made from beef meat and bones alongside herbs like lemongrass. Add a dollop of chilli sauce for added whoomph.;Cash only;[]
12455;Lai;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;28F, Sedona Suites, 92-94 Nam Ky Khoi Nghia Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7721749;106.7008896;15;false;true;Cantonese;Bringing 30 years' experience to the table, the Malaysian-born chef has worked in six major cities across Asia. The interior is done out in traditional Chinese décor featuring modern paintings and flowers. The menu combines classical Cantonese with contemporary elements and a twist of southern Asian in a creative presentation. Be sure to try the há cảo thủy tinh (crystal shrimp dumpling) and the xá xíu ướp thao được quay kieu 'truyền thống' (traditional roasted pork belly with herbs).;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12456;Duong's;Vietnam;Hanoi;27 Ngo Huyen Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0295015;105.8486102;97;false;true;Vietnamese;Doung's is low profile yet easy to find. Over two storeys, the setting is cosy with comfortable wooden furniture and intimate, soft lighting. The set menu is suitable for smaller parties, while the à la carte presents a selection of more substantial signature dishes from Hanoi. The traditional grilled La Vong-style fish is a treat for the eye, while the consommé of beef soup has a clear broth with layers of spices. The chef also offers cooking classes.;;[]
12457;Hoa Túc (District 1);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;74/7 Hai Ba Trung Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.77852;106.70362;73;false;false;Vietnamese;Remodelled from an old opium refinery, Hoa Túc boasts an al fresco dining area steeped in an early 1900s circa Parisian vibe, while the Colonial-style interior pays homage to Vietnam’s history. On the menu, traditional Vietnamese dishes are updated thanks to fancy presentations. Start with refreshing pink pomelo salad with crabmeat and shrimps, followed by bò lá lốt bánh hỏi (grilled beef wrapped in betel leaves on a rice noodle nest).;Car park,Terrace;[]
12458;Bánh Canh Yến;Vietnam;Da Nang;253 Nguyen Hoang Street, Binh Hien Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0578177;108.2132186;89;true;false;Street Food;Come here for bánh canh – thick, chewy noodles made with tapioca starch and rice flour in a snakehead fish and pork broth. Choose toppings like fishcake, quail egg or crabcake. Order fried dough sticks for added crunch.;Cash only;[]
12459;An's Saigon;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;5A Tong Huu Dinh Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.8061063;106.732415;75;false;false;Innovative;Nestling in a stately 20C villa, An's Saigon is fairly out of the way, so you’ll need a cab to get there. The restaurant is divided into three zones: the garden and the lounge serve breakfast, lunch and a dinner tasting menu, while the L-shaped eight-seat Chef’s Table offers an intimate experience and a more personalised menu inspired by Vietnamese culture and nature. Artful plating and creative twists add a new spin to familiar flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
12460;Fashionista Café;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;22B Phung Khac Khoan Street, Da Kao Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7856249;106.6969767;66;true;true;European Contemporary;Food and fashion are the passions of many tastemakers. This café annexed to a two-storey clothing store seamlessly melds the two under one roof. With only two tables indoors, most seating is al fresco. The food is essentially Gallic with Vietnamese twists. Local tropical fruits and nuts are generously used in the sauces and seasoning, while soigné plating pays tribute to fine French dining. Lunch set menus offer great value.;Terrace;[]
12461;Stoker (District 1);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;44 Mac Thi Buoi Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7754922;106.7047851;47;false;true;Steakhouse;The three-storey restaurant has a bar and counter seats around an open kitchen on the ground floor, while upstairs, heavy leather chairs, dark wood wainscoting and antler chandeliers evoke classic steakhouse vibes. Grass-fed and grain-fed beef steaks are the house specialities, especially those dry-aged for over 21 days. The creamy mashed potato cooked over a wood fire is rich in smoky flavour. Round it off with your favourite whisky.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12462;Nén Light;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;122/2 Tran Dinh Xu Street, Nguyen Cu Trinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.762612;106.6883681;97;true;false;Innovative;After walking down a narrow street, diners are invariably enchanted by the pretty lights that set the scene in the tranquil bamboo garden. The interior is equally atmospheric. Championing a cuisine without boundaries, the young chef curates a tasting menu of 7 or 9 courses that tells a story. She uses mostly local ingredients in her ingenious creations and changes the menu every four months to keep it fresh. Ask about the wine pairing option.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12463;Phở Hùng (District 1);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;241-243 Nguyen Trai Street, Nguyen Cu Trinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7650032;106.6876257;62;true;true;Noodles;This venue may not offer much in terms of ambience, but can’t be beaten for tasty beef noodles at affordable prices. Besides the usual raw beef, or medium-rare brisket, their springy and flavoursome beef balls are also a must. If you can’t make up your mind, order the house special with everything in the bowl. Basil, bean sprouts, onion and lime wedges are served on the side. Feel free to customise your phở according to your whim.;Car park,Cash only,Valet parking;[]
12464;Square One;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;2 Lam Son Square, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7775862;106.7034062;28;false;true;International;With stints all over Europe, including prestigious establishments in France, chef Arnaud delivers a unique dining experience by seamlessly switching between Vietnamese and French recipes. Dishes boast balanced flavours and artful plating, befitting the stylish dining room clad in wood and brick. Generous portion sizes are intended to share and ideal for get-togethers. The dramatically visible kitchens make a meal here entertaining and engaging.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12465;Vietnam House;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;93-97 Dong Khoi Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7748944;106.7041683;70;false;true;Vietnamese;This elegant French Colonial-style building stands in the middle of a well-heeled district in the vibrant city centre. The menu is devised by Vietnamese-Australian celebrity chef Luke Nguyen. The team elevate traditional Vietnamese cooking with modern twists, in tasty dishes such as duck noodle soup, juicy chicken breast, and truly delicious silken bean curd dessert. A glass of local flavour infused cocktail adds to the experience.;Air conditioning;[]
12466;Bếp Prime;Vietnam;Hanoi;12 Hang Dieu Street, Cua Dong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.03345;105.84689;40;true;true;Vietnamese;Tucked away in a quaint historic edifice, c. 1932, Bếp Prime specialises in traditional delicacies from Hanoi and the rest of Vietnam. For a Hanoian classic, order pigeon and mushroom hot pot – veggies, pigeon meat and offal are served in a bird cage to be blanched in a herbal broth or glutinous rice porridge. The crispy rice dish with the chef’s dip, made from pork jus, dried shrimps, chilli and pepper that packs umami and a spicy kick, is also recommended.;;[]
12467;Bún Chả Đắc Kim (Hang Manh Street);Vietnam;Hanoi;1 Hang Manh Street, Hang Gai Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0323506;105.848169;29;false;false;Street Food;Nước chấm – sweet chilli fish sauce with finely sliced pickled green mango – is the perfect condiment for the vermicelli noodles which come with shredded smoky pork and plump pork patties. It’s a win-win combination of meat with sweetness and refreshing acidity.;Cash only;[]
12468;Lüne;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;17/14 Le Thanh Ton Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.779904;106.704168;32;true;true;French;With offerings such as duck pâté parfait, escargot and pithiviers, the menu seems traditionally French… But the French chef (from Lyon) aims to re-interpret the classics in line with modern forms and aesthetics. The à la carte menu may not be long, but it covers all bases. For those wanting to experience the chef's vision in all its glory, opt for the tasting menu. Again, the wine list isn't overwhelming, being well curated with some solid choices.;Air conditioning;[]
12469;Maison 1929;Vietnam;Hanoi;2 Cua Dong Street, Cua Dong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.034592;105.846879;51;true;true;Vietnamese;The restaurant, which is established in a historic circa 1929 edifice, is a sister establishment of Chào Bạn. The dining room, spread over two floors and a balcony, features a vibrant colour scheme. The menu is 80% identical to that of Chào Bạn, emphasising a modern approach to Vietnamese cooking. One of the highlights is their array of spring rolls, served hot or cold. Minced beef in lolot leaves boasts a unique aroma and juicy, tender meat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12470;My Hanh Seafood;Vietnam;Da Nang;3-5 Vo Nguyen Giap Street, Phuoc My Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0654849;108.2457453;82;false;true;Seafood;The terrace with panoramic ocean views is one of the biggest draws of this beach-front restaurant. But the well-crafted seafood is more than equal to the setting. The live fish tank heralds a feast of fresh shellfish and fish, to be cooked in various ways. But the stellar attraction is definitely mantis shrimp, boasting firm, flavoursome flesh and rich, buttery roe. Mud crab from Hoi An is another exclusive speciality not found elsewhere in Da Nang.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12471;Béo Ơi;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;15/20 Nguyen Thi Minh Khai Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.785178;106.700997;51;false;false;Vietnamese;Off from the main drag, this simple shop is run by the owner-chef, affectionately known as béo ơi or "fat boy" by regulars, who come in droves during lunch hours. The menu features generous portions of Hanoian home-style cooking, including bún riêu cua, a flavoursome tomato crab soup topped with crispy deep-fried tofu. Order a couple of sides for a complete meal. Or go with friends and opt for a hot pot dinner with the tasty soup as a base.;Cash only;[]
12472;Miên Saigon;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;50A Dang Dung Street, Tan Dinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.792498;106.688896;37;false;true;European Contemporary;Soft lighting and buckets of atmosphere set the scene in the ground-floor dining room which sports an open kitchen with counter seats for those who want to stay close to the action. The 18-seat private room upstairs is perfect for parties. European dishes are spruced up and given local twists – the beef soup pot au pho melds classic pot au feu with Vietnamese noodles. To sample all the highlights, opt for the tasting menu, but à la carte options abound.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12473;Senté (Nguyen Quang Bich Street);Vietnam;Hanoi;20 Nguyen Quang Bich Street, Cua Dong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, 100000, Vietnam;21.0321095;105.8457201;77;false;true;Vietnamese Contemporary;Step away from the bustling streets of the Old Quarter, down a discreet alley and into this cosy dining venue, which is strewn with green plants and champions healthy food. The artistically presented, modern Vietnamese dishes use flowers, leaves, seeds, stems and roots of the humble lotus plant to create unique, flavourful inventions. As a starter, the shrimp, pomelo and lotus root salad is refreshing and appetising. Advance reservations recommended.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
12474;Tanh Tách;Vietnam;Hanoi;3 Yet Kieu Street, Nguyen Du Ward, Hai Ba Trung District, Hanoi, 112605, Vietnam;21.0201154;105.8427666;69;false;true;Seafood;Nestled in a historic French colonial villa, the restaurant occupies two storeys. The chef team exhibits a knack for seafood dishes based on textbook European techniques, thus explaining their prominence on the à la carte menu. Before trying the deftly crafted fish or shellfish, kick off your meal with nori or kimchi rice crackers and tom yum mayo dip. Black chicken consommé is another smash hit.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12475;Ốc Đào (District 1);Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;212B/D48 Nguyen Trai Street, Nguyen Cu Trinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.76523;106.68463;38;true;false;Seafood;In addition to regular fish and crustaceans dishes, this legendary restaurant is especially famous for bivalves and sea snails – a plethora of different species are on the menu, many of which are rarely seen elsewhere. The live critters are cooked in traditional Vietnamese condiments with enough seasoning to complement the natural umami without being overpowering. The bustling vibe makes it great for casual gatherings.;Cash only;[]
12476;Esta;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;27 Tran Quy Khoach Street, Tan Dinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7933721;106.6882191;31;true;true;Asian Contemporary;The menu is depicted by spot-on fusion Asian cuisine, influenced by trips to Japan, Korea and China and the chef’s Vietnamese roots. The theatrically visible kitchen showcases his culinary wizardry, founded on high-quality ingredients. Esta believes in sourcing vegetables from independent farmers and fish caught by small boats.;Counter dining;[]
12477;Hanoi Garden;Vietnam;Hanoi;36 Hang Manh Street, Hang Gai Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, 100000, Vietnam;21.031516;105.848364;68;true;true;Vietnamese;The Indochine-style villa with an elegant courtyard has been home to this establishment since 1998. Expect to find all the greatest hits of Vietnamese cooking on the menu, from appetisers like spring rolls to meat and seafood dishes. Hot pot choices also abound. With over 20 years' experience, the Vietnamese chef reinvents his home country's classics with a modern twist. The food is meticulously prepared and astutely seasoned.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12478;La Fontaine;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;2F, Trade Center, River Garden, 170 Nguyen Van Huong Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.81505;106.72718;87;true;true;French;This bistro with a vintage Parisian vibe is a spin-off of La Villa, operated by the same French owner-chef. Open for breakfast, lunch and dinner, it serves classic, no-frills Gallic fare ranging from pastries and baguette sandwiches to pork terrine and pâté en croûte. Inspired by the chef’s childhood souvenirs, the rustic Provence-style lamb ragout is unbelievably rich and flavoursome. Also check out the wine list leaning towards French labels.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12479;Bếp Người Hội An;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;22 Tran Quoc Toan Street, Ward 8, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7885475;106.68881;68;false;true;Vietnamese;The decor is unmistakably Hội An in style – yellow walls, lanterns and wooden furniture. The menu is easy to navigate, with mì quảng noodles and cơm gà chicken rice being the main events. Trouble choosing? Try the mì quảng đặc biệt topped with shrimp, pork, quail egg, ham, fermented pork roll and peanut spring roll. Cơm gà xé comprises silky shredded chicken, onion and laksa leaves on a bed of chicken fat rice, with chicken offal sauce on the side.;Cash only,Valet parking;[]
12480;Izakaya by Koki;Vietnam;Hanoi;Basement 2, Capella, 11 Le Phung Hieu Street, Trang Tien Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0259082;105.8550521;76;true;false;Japanese;Tucked away in the basement of Capella hotel, Izakaya is a modern and chic setting, with various seating areas, including more intimate sofa areas. Guests are welcomed with a complimentary sake with aromatic notes of tropical fruit. Sourcing 70% of its ingredients from Japan, this restaurant has an extensive menu including a specialty of grilled dishes: the grilled black cod with Saikyo sauce is particularly impressive. Be sure to save room for the signature dessert: housemade yame matcha or black truffle ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12481;Hervé Dining Room;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;204/20 Nguyen Van Huong Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.814789;106.7319;89;false;true;French Contemporary;Set in a residential building, Hervé Rodriguez's restaurant has an open kitchen, and an intimate atmosphere that makes it just the place for a romantic dinner or low-key social gathering. The tasting menu, which changes every three weeks, sees various cooking techniques (e.g. molecular, dry aging and preserving) applied to the best of Vietnamese produce. To cleanse the palette between dishes, diners are served a series of small bites that range from acidic to fruity and icy.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
12482;French Grill;Vietnam;Hanoi;Lobby Level, JW Marriott, 8 Do Duc Duc Road, Me Tri Ward, South Tu Liem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.00714;105.78236;22;false;true;French Contemporary;This elegant hotel restaurant boasts a sleek, spacious dining room oozing with special occasion indulgence. Counter seats offer a view of the huge open kitchen and create a connection between the chefs at work and the diners. The contemporary French culinary score is consummately executed with subtle Asian twists, flanked by equally immaculate, spot-on, courteous service. Private dining rooms are available for everything from date nights to business dinners.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
12483;El Gaucho (Hoan Kiem);Vietnam;Hanoi;11 Trang Tien Street, Trang Tien Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.02442;105.85636;44;false;false;Steakhouse;This is an outpost of a global chain that specialises in steakhouse classics, specifically premium beef steaks. Certified organic, corn-fed beef from the U.S. and grass-fed cattle from Australia are grilled to perfection Argentinian style – sparingly seasoned and free of sauce to further highlight their natural flavours. Visit the adjoining butcher’s shop to take some quality meat home. Start or end your evening with cocktails at the bar. Reservations recommended.;;[]
12484;Le Comptoir;Vietnam;Da Nang;16 Che Lan Vien Street, My An Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0435407;108.2455154;77;true;true;French;Run by a chef from Lyon, France, this restaurant is the epitome of Gallic authenticity. The á la carte and set menus roll out bistro classics made with premium local and globally sourced ingredients, cherry-picked by the chef. Expect items like roasted beef bone marrow and hand-chopped Wagyu tartare with Melba toast and smoked aioli. The interesting wine list offers a wide range of boutique wineries. Pop into the deli after your meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12485;Nén Danang;Vietnam;Da Nang;16 My Da Tay 2 Street, Khue My Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.03466;108.24062;43;false;false;Vietnamese Contemporary;Reopened in 2022, the first venture of owner-chef Summer Le is tucked away from the main road. The interior is modern and minimalistic, with theatrical lighting to set the mood. To keep it fresh and exciting, the single set menu is tweaked every few months and revamped entirely every 6 months. Each creative Vietnamese dish comes with a hand-drawn card explaining the inspiration and ingredients. Check out the wine- and sake-food pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12486;Bếp Hên;Vietnam;Da Nang;47 Le Hong Phong Street, Phuoc Ninh Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0641288;108.2209519;56;true;true;Vietnamese;Step back in time and immerse yourself in the room’s vintage circa 1990s decor and memorabilia. The family business has been in operation since 2015 and the kitchen is helmed by mum. The extensive menu, which covers all of Vietnam, might seem overwhelming, but rest assured that all the sharing plates are authentic, hearty and comforting. When unsure, check out the section known as ‘mum’s favourites’, for items like fried garlic prawn, or stir-fried morning glory with garlic.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only;[]
12487;Tre Dining;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;2F, 35 Xuan Thuy Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.80336;106.73061;80;true;true;Vietnamese Contemporary;Down a path lined in bamboo trees, diners are led into a bamboo-clad room. The chef team cook up a storm over the charcoal grills in the open kitchen and complement the grilled food with east-meets-west condiments and artful plating. Think octopus tentacles in a spicy, buttery tom yum sauce, or Hokkaido scallops in a brown butter hollandise. Choose counter seats to stay close to the action, or the al fresco dining area for the city’s skyline.;Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12488;La Villa;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;14 Ngo Quang Huy Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.804002;106.7324648;56;false;true;French;The culinary Gallic line-up whisks you back to the 1960s with duck foie gras, pâté en croûte, lobster à l'américaine and Grand Marnier soufflé. Decorated with artwork, red velvet curtains and a stunning chandelier, La Villa also offers al fresco dining in the garden. Attentive, suitably formal service, a fine wine list and cheese selection. The starched classical vibe of this restaurant will appeal to those who appreciate vintage charm and nostalgia.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12489;Phở Gà Châm (Yen Ninh Street);Vietnam;Hanoi;64-68 Yen Ninh Street, Truc Bach Ward, Ba Dinh District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0423348;105.8439803;81;false;false;Noodles;The phở gà at this small stall might be more expensive than the average, but the chicken is premium quality and the natural chicken flavour of the soup base is impeccably seasoned. Choose from white or dark meat, or a mixture of both, and add chilli sauce, garlic, lime and chilli to taste. Arrive early to ensure the best selection of chicken cuts. This stall, perfect for an authentic breakfast experience in Hanoi, is open until 1:30pm.;Cash only;[]
12490;Etēsia;Vietnam;Hanoi;14B Lo Su Street, Ly Thai To Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0313938;105.8556968;36;false;true;European Contemporary;An 18-seat kitchen counter is the focal point of this snug buzzy wine bar. Shelves of empty wine bottles adorn the walls, and the wine list showcases over 350 vintages from the Old World. They offer a vast array of wines by the glass and from a Coravin. The neatly presented, modern dishes are Mediterranean at heart with an Asian twist and deliver accurate, well-judged flavours. Don't miss the homemade pasta: the pride and joy of Etēsia.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
12491;T.U.N.G dining;Vietnam;Hanoi;2C Quang Trung Street, Hang Trong Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0267108;105.8500595;99;true;true;Innovative;The TUNG-in-cheek acronym – twisted, unique, natural, gastronomic – encapsulates the philosophy of Chef Hoang Tung's culinary style. His tasting menu, which keeps pace with the seasons and uses local produce, boasts colourful, minimalist dishes, each of which features just 3 or 4 ingredients, whose complexity explodes with every bite. The flavours are balanced and well-judged, with contrasts of texture and temperature, and acidity often playing a key role.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
12492;Azabu;Vietnam;Hanoi;2F, Hôtel du Parc, 84 Tran Nhan Tong Street, Nguyen Du Ward, Hai Ba Trung District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0177948;105.8423073;71;true;false;Japanese;Located on the 2nd floor of Hôtel du Parc, bask in the elegant main dining room or watch the sushi chefs at work from the blonde wooden counter. The menu covers all the bases and is great value for money at lunchtime. The extensive à la carte menu offers a fine range of Kaiseki options. Don't overlook the house specialities, including the knockout sushi and sashimi. A smooth, professional operation run by a smart, friendly team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12493;Bún Chả Cá Bà Hoa;Vietnam;Da Nang;27 Le Hong Phong Street, Phuoc Ninh Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.06389;108.22159;54;true;true;Noodles;Since 2009, this simple shop has attracted a loyal fan base with only one item on the menu – bún chả cá – rice noodles in a tangy tomato and pumpkin broth with fresh fishcakes, made in house daily using a variety of fish. Almost 300 bowls are sold every day and customised to order with fishcake only or a combo of fishcake and a chunk of mackerel or tuna. Try it with pickles or a dab of shrimp paste for extra flavour.;Cash only;[]
12494;Bé Mặn;Vietnam;Da Nang;Lot 8, Vo Nguyen Giap Street, Man Thai Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0817651;108.2472366;32;true;false;Seafood;One of the most famous seafood restaurants on My Khe Beach, Bé Mặn knows how to bring out the best in every ingredient. Start by picking your own live seafood from the rows of tanks and then specify how you want it cooked. From crabs and lobsters to geoduck and snails, whether deep-fried, stir-fried or steamed, everything tastes as good as it looks. Try the steamed squid with ginger and onion, dipping it in the spicy sour sauce for an extra zing.;Great view;[]
12495;Rice Field;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;2F, 75-77 Ho Tung Mau Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7723695;106.7036408;64;true;false;Vietnamese;Spread over three storeys, this delightful venue with an open-air rooftop boasts a rustic décor inspired by local villages and rice fields and serves Vietnamese dishes from the north to the south. The stuffed snails with meat cooked with lemongrass and paired with ginger fish sauce, are succulent, while La Vong fishcakes strike the perfect balance combining vermicelli, marinated fish, fresh Vietnamese vegetables and herbs, shrimp paste sauce and rice paper sheets.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12496;Labri;Vietnam;Hanoi;2F, 113 Bui Thi Xuan Street, Hai Ba Trung District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0148368;105.8499876;95;false;false;European Contemporary;A neon sign in the upstairs window is the clue to finding this modern-day bistro, tucked away on the 2nd floor of a nondescript building. Abri is French for shelter and the restaurant imbues a sense of cosy luxury. The open kitchen takes centre stage and four huge crystal chandeliers hang from the ceiling. The chef delivers virtuoso cuisine using French techniques and Vietnamese ingredients. For the full experience, opt for the 7-course menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12497;Vị An;Vietnam;Hanoi;145 Hoang Cau Street, Trung Liet Ward, Dong Da District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.01663;105.821145;56;false;false;Vietnamese;The owner couple strives to replicate the authentic taste of Northern Vietnam for their Hanoian audience. Unlike the sweet flavours cherished in other parts of Vietnam, here they emphasise umami and saltiness. Chả ốc is one of the most popular dishes. The pork sausage with periwinkle snails is perfumed with herbs and fried until crispy. The pork is juicy and bouncy in texture. Gà xáo gừng is chicken cooked in turmeric and ginger. Simply irresistible.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
12498;Mía Dining;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;12G2 Nguyen Thi Minh Khai Street, Da Kao Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7885676;106.7022256;100;true;false;European Contemporary;The soft lighting, minimalist interior and romantic soundtrack make this venue the perfect spot for date nights. The most prized seats are at the counter offering intimate views of the kitchen. Three set menus star modern European recipes jazzed up by a scattering of local produce and seasonings. The must-try duck breast is velvety and juicy, clad in crackling skin as crisp as peanut brittle. Expect sound wine tips from the sommelier.;Car park,Valet parking;[]
12499;Năm Đảnh;Vietnam;Da Nang;139/59/38 Tran Quang Khai Street, Tho Quang Ward, Son Tra District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.1021138;108.2528756;22;false;false;Seafood;Tucked away in a residential neighbourhood, Năm Đảnh provides a golf cart shuttle service from Phan Vinh Street. Seafood is the strong suit of this sprawling restaurant, which boasts a huge number of tables. There is even a hut clad in live fish tanks from which diners can make their pick. Lobster, whether steamed, tossed in cheese sauce, or fried with garlic and chilli, is always tasty. Sea whelks in garlic butter exude spellbinding aromas. Early birds get the most choice...;;[]
12500;Du Yên;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;26B Street 10, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, 71000, Vietnam;10.77653;106.70098;46;true;true;Vegetarian;Nestled in a quiet neighbourhood in town, this place occupies two levels with its room exuding rustic chic. The eclectic menu presents Vietnamese dishes plus Western and Thai options. Gỏi cuốn hoa bướm are the photogenic rice paper rolls adorned with edible pansies. The sweet peanut dip works well with the crisp vegetables. Męt bánh Huế is the vegetarian version of the famous steamed rice cake wrapped in banana leaves with fish sauce on the side.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12501;Luk Lak;Vietnam;Da Nang;28 Bach Dang Street, Thach Thang Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0788486;108.2236448;67;true;false;Vietnamese;Perched on the banks of the Han River, this outpost of its Hanoian namesake boasts a dining room dripping in lush greenery. This branch shares the same culinary ethos as its flagship – creative Vietnamese fare packed with bold flavours. Grilled ground beef skewer with herbs and lemongrass seduces with aromas. Wrap in rice paper with veg and fruit for a hunger-quenching kick or pair with sticky rice and cassava root in a claypot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12502;Cồ Đàm;Vietnam;Hanoi;68 Tran Hung Dao Street, Tran Hung Dao Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0224737;105.8477632;18;false;false;Vegetarian;Named after the Buddha, Cồ Đàm’s eye-catching architecture boasts an ornate exterior inspired by Buddhist and Champa culture and a striking arched entrance of terracotta bricks. Four floors are open for dining, but the ground floor stands out for its tranquil pond and terracotta Buddha. The vegetarian tasting menu comprises creative, modern twists on exquisitely presented Vietnamese classics, rich in flavour combinations.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12503;Elgin;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;27 Mac Dinh Chi Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.784774;106.69932;55;false;false;European;Orange banquettes and soft lighting enhance and offset the dark green wall tiles. Run by an energetic and passionate young team, Elgin can be relied upon to pamper its patrons. The menu, which changes regularly, showcases deftly prepared European dishes made mostly with local produce. Try the pork belly with fried brussels sprouts or gnocchi with lamb sugo, both of which are rich in flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
12504;Quince Eatery;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;37 Bis Ky Con Street, Nguyen Thai Binh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7661947;106.6992335;73;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Set in a refurbished colonial-style house with a vibrant décor, bistro-style furniture and soft lighting, this culinary hotspot adds a modern twist to Mediterranean fare. A copper counter with 6 seats faces the open kitchen. Guests can pick from a wide range of charcoal-grilled, wood-fired and oven-baked delights. Our favourites: hummus and merguez, and tasty golden berry with burnt sourdough mousse dessert. The 2nd floor bar is ideal for drinks before or after your meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12505;Bánh Cuốn Bà Hoành;Vietnam;Hanoi;66 To Hien Thanh Street, Bui Thi Xuan Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0135667;105.8496851;37;true;false;Street Food;This is among the busiest shops in the area because of its steamed rice rolls known as bánh cuốn. Rice noodle sheets are steamed to order and then wrapped around minced shiitake and pork. They also sell bún chả, or grilled pork noodles.;Cash only;[]
12506;Cơm Gà Lan;Vietnam;Da Nang;520 Trung Nu Vuong Street, Hoa Thuan Tay Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, 550000, Vietnam;16.0488832;108.2130368;71;false;true;Rice Dishes;As the name suggests, there's only one thing on the menu – cơm gà, or chicken rice, but you can opt for the poultry roasted, steamed or shredded. Served with soup and pickles, the cơm gà xé bóp (shredded version), is especially popular. The lemongrass, coriander and onion lend the juicy chicken extra zing. Given the quality of the food and bargain prices, it's no surprise that this place is always jam-packed. Avoid peak hours.;Cash only;[]
12507;Backstage;Vietnam;Hanoi;Capella, 11 Le Phung Hieu Street, Trang Tien Ward, Hoan Kiem District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0258498;105.8565574;73;true;false;Vietnamese Contemporary;Your inner celebrity will revel in this opera-themed restaurant, whose open kitchen takes front stage. Signature dishes like Capella Pho and Bun Cha Hanoi respect their northern heritage, whilst featuring modern techniques with European touches that will leave your tastebuds singing an aria of delight. The impressive cocktail list offers some intriguing mixes. The theatrical setting showcases stunning costumes from the world’s greatest operas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12508;The Monkey Gallery Dining;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;3F, 91 Mac Thi Buoi Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.774419;106.70401;24;false;false;European Contemporary;Three wise founders, all born in the year of the monkey, have thoughtfully designed this relaxed "gallery" with a minimalist, Japanese-influenced decor, in which the food takes centre stage. The result is a lovely ambience that is perfect for social gatherings. A concrete dining counter faces the open kitchen where the young kitchen team uses modern European cooking techniques. Pick from a selection of dishes for each of the four courses, then choose your drink pairing from the creative list of cocktails and mocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
12509;Madame Lam;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;10 Tran Ngoc Dien Street, Thao Dien Ward, Thu Duc City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.8031685;106.7398833;37;false;true;Vietnamese Contemporary;Indochine-Art Deco design fosters a laid-back ambience in this restaurant where the chef showcases modern Vietnamese cuisine from the central region of the country, where he grew up. The traditional dishes are presented with a refined yet creative touch. Be sure to try the delicious bao ngư nướng mỡ hành (grilled abalone with spring onion oil and fish sauce). The kem chuối nước cốt dừa (banana ice cream with coconut rice and crushed peanuts) is a satisfying and traditional dessert to round off your meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12510;Ngon Garden;Vietnam;Hanoi;70 Nguyen Du Street, Nguyen Du Ward, Hai Ba Trung District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.01975;105.84519;22;true;true;Vietnamese;On the banks of Thien Quang Lake, this restaurant, reminiscent of an Indochinese-style villa, boasts a patio surrounded by lush greenery. The menu features specialities from all over Vietnam, alongside Asian delicacies of Chinese and Thai origins. From the century-old Bat Dan phở recipe from Hanoi and bún bò huế grilled beef from Nha Trang to fresh veggies from Dalat and live seafood from all over the world, every dish is deftly crafted and delicately seasoned.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12511;Si Dining;Vietnam;Da Nang;1 Giang Chau 2 Street, Khue My Ward, Ngu Hanh Son District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0395;108.24686;87;true;false;Italian Contemporary;The Italian owner-chef opened this al fresco dining spot to showcase authentic Italian fare, adding a subtle local spin. The menu changes daily to keep it fresh and hyper-seasonal, but beef carpaccio is a firm fixture – thinly sliced raw Aussie beef dressed in anchovy sauce and olive oil, topped with croutons and shaved parmesan. Fish remains his passion and the catch of the day always hits the spot. House-made limoncello is perfect to sip after dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12512;Cô Liêng;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;321 Vo Van Tan Street, Ward 5, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7735478;106.6871417;36;false;true;Street Food;Established in 1995, Cô Liêng serves up a modest take on Southern Vietnamese cuisine. The main draw is the charcoal-grilled bò lá lốt (minced beef wrapped in betel leaves) that features perfect savoury-sweet flavour. They also serve rice vermicelli bundles (bánh hỏi with grilled meat).;Cash only;[]
12513;Bún Chả Hương Liên (Hai Ba Trung);Vietnam;Hanoi;24 Le Van Huu Street, Phan Chu Trinh Ward, Hai Ba Trung District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0180886;105.8538623;60;true;false;Street Food;Playing on their claim to fame, this joint displays photos of its celebrity guests and offers a Combo Obama, which includes a fried seafood roll, a bowl of the special bún chả and a bia hà nội. The bún chả itself delivers a satisfying blend of rustic flavours, with smoky pork, meat patties, fragrant herbs and fresh salad leaves. They also serve a tasty pork skewer.;Cash only;[]
12514;Thúy 94 Cũ;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;84 Dinh Tien Hoang Street, Da Kao Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 710000, Vietnam;10.790191;106.69786;93;false;false;Seafood;This popular restaurant specialises in crab, with a menu that shines the spotlight on the crustacean – crab spring rolls, fried rice, salt-baked crab, steamed crab… the list goes on. Crab vermicelli soup brims with umami-loaded crabmeat and roe. The broth features deep, slightly sweet flavours. Soft-shelled crab is fried to order, boasting a crispy crust and firm flesh. What’s more, crab can be replaced by shrimp in most dishes.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
12516;Chả Cá Anh Vũ (Dong Da);Vietnam;Hanoi;120-K1 Giang Vo Street, O Cho Dua Ward, Dong Da District, Hanoi, Vietnam;21.0269484;105.8241614;90;true;false;Vietnamese;One of four branches in the city, this bouncy family-run operation offers slick service. The homely vibe is depicted by chequered tablecloths, patterned wallpaper and brightly painted murals. Chả cá, grilled catfish seasoned with turmeric, is the name of the game here, although you can add nem cá, fish spring rolls, canh cá, fish soup, and lòng cá, fish stomach, as extras. The fresh, tasty food delivers an explosion of flavours and textures.;Air conditioning;[]
12517;Madame Lân;Vietnam;Da Nang;4 Bach Dang Street, Thach Thang Ward, Hai Chau District, Da Nang, Vietnam;16.0812954;108.2232854;90;false;false;Vietnamese;Named after the owner’s late mother, Madame Lân exudes Hoi An flair with its decor and lanterns. The sprawling yellow house is surrounded by water features, boasting both indoor and outdoor seating. The chef rolls out an extensive culinary lineup that covers every facet of Vietnamese cuisine, including the signature dish of Da Nang: fried fish summer roll. Sautéed beef with pepper elder is also a popular salad dish to tickle your tastebuds.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12518;Đông Phố;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;57 Ho Xuan Huong Street, Ward 6, District 3, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7764018;106.6874161;30;false;true;Vietnamese;Popular among the locals and tourists alike, this unpretentious eatery shares a bungalow with an ice cream parlour and specialises in traditional Vietnamese dishes and French snacks. If you find the vast menu a bit daunting, the tasting menu is a great way to sample all the signature dishes. The five-salad assortment includes banana blossom salad, pomelo salad, and baby clams sautéed in angel hair – all of which are refreshing and appetising.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12519;Octo;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;2F, 75 Ho Tung Mau Street, Ben Nghe Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam;10.7720814;106.7037588;65;false;false;Spanish;With bare brick walls, a wood-clad high ceiling and black metal accents, the interior is the epitome of faux-industrial. Drenched in sunlight during the day, it is moodily lit at night. Either way, it has a real buzz that makes for a fun visit. Octo, which bills itself as a tapas restobar, is ideal for Spanish tapas, like their famous traditional croquettes, gazpacho and 48-month Iberico ham, washed down with a round of drinks.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12520;Truffle;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;73F, Landmark 81, Vinhomes Central Park, Binh Thanh District, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.805325;106.58814;52;true;false;French Contemporary;Towering more than 300 metres above Saigon in Landmark 81, Truffle offers knockout views. As you’d expect, this French restaurant specialises in truffles and offers several tasting menus, all of which feature the seasonally sourced fungi from different countries. The large dining area is surrounded by floor-to-ceiling windows that frame exceptional views of the city below – truly breath taking!;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking;[]
12521;Å by T.U.N.G;Vietnam;Ho Chi Minh City;31-33 Dang Dung Street, Tan Dinh Ward, District 1, Ho Chi Minh City, 700000, Vietnam;10.7924372;106.6895287;15;true;true;Innovative;With a ceiling mural of the Northern Lights, the airy dining space is a nod to chef Tung’s stint in Finland. On entering, diners first catch sight of the open kitchen before they are greeted by the chefs. Only one multi-course tasting menu is offered, and it changes every three months in line with the seasons. Chef Tung’s small plates are creative and original, paying tribute to Vietnamese food culture in terms of ingredients, flavours and techniques.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12522;Otok;Croatia;Supetar;Vlačica 3, Supetar, 21400, Croatia;43.3846158;16.553267;32;false;true;Croatian;Located just a minute's walk away from the pretty harbour on the picturesque island of Brač, this lovely modern restaurant sits on the ground floor of the Osam hotel. The terrace is covered with mature olive trees and makes a great spot from which to enjoy the rustic Croatian cooking. Dishes have an honest island feel, with the fish soup particularly delicious. Fresh Adriatic seafood is a feature, accompanied by Croatian wines - and all at a sensible price. Comfortable bedrooms are attached, and the ferry terminal is just two minutes away.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12523;Luciano;Croatia;Buje;Mužolini Donji 7, Buje, 52460, Croatia;45.387602;13.6865005;91;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Meats and Grills;Situated just outside the typical medieval village of Buje, this beautiful hotel complex with typical Istrian architecture provides a peaceful oasis for its guests. The Luciano restaurant (named after its main supplier of fresh vegetables) has a welcoming ambience with fine views of the surrounding countryside from its outdoor terrace. Prepared using carefully chosen, top-quality ingredients, the dishes served here are available via an à la carte or on tasting menus of varying lengths. Contemporary meat and fish options with a regional focus take centre stage, accompanied by an extensive selection of local wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12524;Matsunoki;Croatia;Mali Lošinj;Čikat 9, Mali Lošinj, 51550, Croatia;44.53217;14.45527;70;false;true;Japanese Contemporary, Fusion;Situated in the luxurious Hotel Bellevue, this Japanese restaurant boasts a terrace and an elegant dining room with an open-view kitchen and sushi bar. The cuisine here includes excellent sashimi in traditionally prepared and more imaginative recipes, plus ramen dishes, Kobe beef and sea bass carpaccio. The wine list includes options by the glass, as well as the proverbial sake and Japanese whisky.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12525;Dvor;Croatia;Split;Put Firula 14, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5010598;16.4541051;26;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The shaded garden with its open grill and fine views is the main attraction at this beautiful restaurant on the coast overlooking the sea. The catch of the day takes pride of place on the buffet, where guests can also choose their cut of meat. An excellent selection of wine, including by the glass, completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12526;Nav;Croatia;Zagreb;Masarykova Ulica 11a, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.810604;15.9728635;51;false;false;Creative;You ring the doorbell to gain access to this restaurant, where just five tables and an open-view kitchen create an intimate and welcoming ambience that deliberately gives the impression of dining in chef Tvrtko Šakota’s own home. The seasonal ingredients in the dishes here are sourced from the restaurant’s own farm, situated 40km from Zagreb. The chef chooses the dishes and Croatian wines served on his surprise tasting menu, where the focus is on small-scale producers who farm in accordance with traditional biodynamic methods. The cuisine takes guests on a creative and personalised journey through Croatia, with an emphasis on dishes cooked in the oven, from the carefully prepared bread to the traditional Salenjaci dessert. Booking ahead and prior payment required.;Air conditioning;[]
12527;Theatrium by Filho;Croatia;Zagreb;Teslina 7, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8111548;15.9761396;24;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a small courtyard belonging to Zagreb’s youth theatre (ZKM), this young, lively restaurant boasts a bold colour scheme and retro furnishings, with an open-view kitchen and a veranda (the best seats are here). The extensive menu features classic French and Italian dishes alongside more creative options that pay tribute to local cuisine. Starters include fresh fish from the Adriatic, while the Beef Wellington is considered to be one of the chef’s specialities. The excellent wine list includes labels from all over Croatia – make sure you ask for recommendations. Don’t miss the charming outdoor space in summer.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12528;Le Bistro Esplanade;Croatia;Zagreb;Mihanoviceva Ulica 1, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8054583;15.9756389;98;true;true;French;Housed in one of the best hotels in the city, this elegant yet informal all-day bistro has become one of Zagreb’s most popular meeting places and is ideal for a simple snack and aperitif, as well as a full meal. The menu features meat, fish and plenty of vegetables, with a focus on local ingredients and the occasional French influence. Make sure you try the iconic Esplanade Štrukli, pasta filled with cheese and cooked au gratin, a house speciality since 1951. An excellent selection of wines by the glass completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12529;Takenoko;Croatia;Zagreb;Masarykova 22, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8107595;15.9722421;20;false;false;Japanese, Fusion;Transferred in Preradovićeva 22. This restaurant’s modern appearance provides a striking contrast with its surrounding buildings. Although the menu is described as Nikkei, the Japanese influence is more noticeable here than the Peruvian. Meals start with ceviche and continue with sushi, the latter ranging from classic Japanese to the restaurant’s more creative “American” style. A well-stocked bar and attractive cocktails add to the appeal, while the restaurant’s location makes it convenient for the National Theatre (HNK).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12530;Mon Ami;Croatia;Velika Gorica;Trg Kralja Tomislava, 26, Velika Gorica, 10410, Croatia;45.7112127;16.0801126;88;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The many regular guests at this often-crowded restaurant seem to have no doubts about the quality of the meat and fish dishes served here and with good reason! Fish, served in simple, traditional recipes that allow the full flavour to shine through, is the real star of the show. Among the desserts, make sure you try the Skradinska cake, a chocolate speciality with chopped walnuts and orange, in which the three different flavours are balanced to perfection.;Air conditioning;[]
12531;Nicolo Polo;Croatia;Gradac;Obala 15, Gradac, 21330, Croatia;43.1042265;17.3441724;39;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;You’ll find the small, intimate and privately owned Marco Polo hotel set right on the waterfront of the Makarska Rivijera. Its restaurant, Nicolo Polo, is a light, airy spot and the service is incredibly warm and welcoming. The food is a mix of classical and modern Mediterranean: start with ‘DIY prawns’, before moving on to bold main courses and contrastingly delicate desserts – the rožata is a must-try. There’s also a terrace over the road where they serve simpler dishes during the day.;Great view,Terrace;[]
12532;Boban;Croatia;Zagreb;Gajeva 9, Zagreb, 10 000, Croatia;45.8115292;15.9764446;71;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the pedestrianised area of the historic centre, Boban is a delightful, recently renovated restaurant which serves Mediterranean-style Italian cuisine. The starters are particularly delicious, while the main courses include fish, seafood and meat dishes. There’s also a good wine selection, with an emphasis on champagnes.;Terrace;[]
12533;Bugenvila;Croatia;Cavtat;Put dr. Ante Starčevića 9, Cavtat, 20210, Croatia;42.5823895;18.2166585;75;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This long-established restaurant situated in the charming village of Cavtat stands on the seafront promenade facing the harbour. Its delightful terrace adorned with sweetly scented bougainvillea, geraniums and jasmine has a truly romantic feel, while the cuisine served here focuses on authentic, unfussy Mediterranean dishes made from high-quality meat and fish. Booking ahead is recommended.;Great view,Terrace;[]
12535;Gallo;Croatia;Zagreb;Hebrangova 34, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8090898;15.97329;89;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;Located in the basement of the “Castellum Centar”, this elegantly decorated restaurant serves cuisine based around Mediterranean- and Italian-inspired fish dishes, alongside homemade pasta and highly enticing desserts. Very friendly service, an impressive wine selection and outdoor dining in summer add to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12536;Johnson;Croatia;Mošćenička Draga;Majčevo 29b, Mošćenička Draga, 51417, Croatia;45.2389541;14.2488125;60;false;false;Seafood;Just a stone’s throw from one of the most beautiful beaches in the region, this restaurant serves fresh fish, scampi and shellfish caught that very day and prepared in simple, traditional dishes that allow the full flavour of the fish and seafood to shine through (dishes are announced at your table). In summer, don’t miss the relaxing and sunny panoramic terrace. The Jurdan family have been running this restaurant since 1996 – almost thirty years of enthusiastic and reliable service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12537;Foša;Croatia;Zadar;Kralja Dmitra Zvonimira 2, Zadar, 23000, Croatia;44.1113852;15.2282888;47;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Seafood;Fish and seafood specialities take pride of place at this restaurant situated just behind the town’s 16C walls overlooking the port at Foša. The Dalmatian-inspired cuisine is Mediterranean and contemporary in style, while in summer, the delightful terrace overlooking the sea is an absolute must.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12539;BÒME;Croatia;Split;Ul. Dinka Šimunovića 14a, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5056955;16.4738468;77;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The exterior of this surprising “socialist-style” Modernist building decorated in bright colours is in sharp contrast with the more contemporary interior. Warmly run by owner-chef Mario himself (who has returned to the area where he grew up) and by his fiancée Franciska, the restaurant has just seven tables arranged in front of an L-shaped kitchen. Specialities here follow a modern Mediterranean approach in dishes where flavours are highly balanced and textures play an important role. The bread and pasta are made on the premises with ingredients purchased by the chef himself in the local market.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12540;Tekka by Lone;Croatia;Rovinj;Ul. Luje Adamovića 31, Rovinj, 52210, Croatia;45.0731609;13.6392588;35;false;true;Japanese, International;Whether you take a seat in its delightful summer garden or beautiful minimalist-style dining room, the Japanese restaurant at the extremely modern Lone hotel provides an interesting blend of Istrian and Japanese cuisine. The techniques and recipes are Japanese, while the ingredients and personalised reinterpretations are from the region. We particularly enjoyed the duck breast with chicory, which was cooked to perfection with crispy skin and accompanied by a creamy umeboshi plum and pomegranate sauce – the perfect balance of sweet and savoury flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
12541;Vapor;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Hotel Bellevue, Pera Čingrije 7, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.6468469;18.0922684;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;One of the main attractions of this restaurant in the luxurious Bellevue Hotel is the superb sea view that can be enjoyed from its terrace and through the large windows in its dining room. Another is the fresh Mediterranean cuisine on offer here, which includes a delicious sea bream ceviche served with marinated citrus fruit, salmon roe and crispy quinoa chips.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12542;Mala Hiza;Croatia;Mačkovec;Balogovec, 1, Mačkovec, 40000, Croatia;46.4229626;16.4279019;31;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Occupying a late-19C house surrounded by a beautiful garden with a fountain and small stream, this friendly restaurant run by its owner-chef and his family boasts a romantic ambience. The cuisine is regional in style, with a focus on local ingredients and dishes accompanied by local wines. Appetisers include stuffed pasta, while meat options (especially beef and lamb) dominate the main courses. To finish your meal in style, why not try the gibanica, a popular local dessert made with layers of shortcrust pastry, fresh cheese, eggs and pumpkin.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12543;Nautika;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Brsalje 3, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.641525;18.10585;99;true;false;Classic Cuisine;One of the busiest restaurants in the city (so booking well in advance is recommended), Nautika serves carefully prepared, traditional cuisine that is full of flavour. The dishes here are rooted in a respect for local traditions and enhanced with French and Italian influences, while avoiding the latest culinary trends and exotic twists. The service is impeccable and the wine list highly impressive. Make sure you try the prawns with semolina gnocchi, beurre blanc, parsley cream and toasted almonds, a dish full of delicious and enticing flavours. There’s a magnificent view of the two fortresses lit up at night from the front terrace.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12544;Morgan;Croatia;Brtonigla;Bracanija 1, Brtonigla, 52474, Croatia;45.385498;13.642433;42;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Situated in the green heart of Istria, this long-established, family-run hotel-restaurant boasts a welcoming dining room plus an attractive summer terrace looking out at the countryside. The regional cuisine served here closely follows the seasons, with game, mushrooms and truffles making an appearance in autumn, and vegetables and fresh cheeses in spring. Throughout the year, you can enjoy delicious Istrian hams and homemade pasta, including the tasty asparagus-filled ravioli served with grilled asparagus.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12545;San Rocco;Croatia;Brtonigla;Srednja ulica 2, Brtonigla, 52474, Croatia;45.3776783;13.6242143;97;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;This romantic hotel-restaurant occupies an elegant stone building in a typical small Istrian village just a few kilometres from the sea. Take a seat in what was once the wine cellar or outdoors on the summer terrace, where you’ll enjoy well-crafted, creative dishes that are full of flavour and made from top-quality local, seasonal ingredients, with a choice of meat and fish dishes, as well as a 5-course vegetarian menu. In autumn, the menu is enhanced by delicacies such as truffles, mushrooms and game. Guided tastings of the restaurant’s own extra-virgin olive oil can be enjoyed in the oil boutique.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12546;Bistro Tavulin;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Cvijete Zuzorić 1, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.640564;18.110249;35;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Although this restaurant is admittedly aimed at tourists given its central location in the heart of Dubrovnik, the cuisine here is prepared using fresh, local ingredients which result in pleasing, elegantly presented dishes that are full of flavour. The superb agnolotti pasta stuffed with Adriatic prawns, accompanied by a beurre blanc and parsley-flavoured oil, is delicious and beautifully prepared.;Terrace;[]
12547;Balon;Croatia;Zagreb;Prisavlje 2a, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.7901058;15.9617033;87;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Croatian;In a verdant setting not far from the banks of the River Sava, this charmingly elegant bistro-style restaurant, which has stood on the same square for many years but has been recently refurbished, is surrounded by glass on three sides and boasts a spacious terrace for summer dining. The classic cuisine served here is inspired by the Mediterranean and features some original touches by the chef.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12548;The Restaurant at Maslina Resort;Croatia;Stari Grad;Uvala Maslinica 11, Stari Grad, 21460, Croatia;43.1797966;16.5711841;24;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Housed in the luxurious Maslina Resort directly facing the sea, this elegant, minimalist-style restaurant is in perfect harmony with its surroundings. The cuisine combines French techniques with local and Mediterranean ingredients, such as the herbs and vegetables grown in the property’s own kitchen garden. The à la carte menu features meat and fish dishes which are served in the dining room or on the terrace alongside the pool.;;[]
12549;Restaurant Mare;Croatia;Trogir;Lučica 11, Trogir, 21220, Croatia;43.51388;16.25082;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated on the island of Čiovo, just a 5-minute walk from the historic centre of Trogir, this restaurant is part of the Hotel Bifora Heritage, a 14C building that was restored in 2016. Here, chef Robert Predag Zmire uses modern techniques to create delicious cuisine from fine ingredients. Although fish takes centre stage, there’s also a choice of meat dishes and a few vegan options. The dishes are carefully prepared and full of flavour, including options such as cuttlefish tagliatelle with a wild herb pesto, sea asparagus, lemon pearls and prawn chips, and the extremely fresh sea bass ikejime served with celery and a parsley sauce. Although the wine list is not particularly extensive, it offers good value for money and includes many Croatian wines available by the glass. A welcoming restaurant a little off the tourist track, with a charming, intimate stone patio that is perfect for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12550;Zinfandel Food & Wine bar;Croatia;Split;Marulićeva ul. 2, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5084024;16.4390742;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated in a narrow street in the old town, this busy, welcoming restaurant is open from breakfast to dinner, when live music adds to the atmosphere. The young Croatian chef serves eclectic cuisine which includes Dalmatian recipes alongside more internationally influenced fare. Some of the dishes are designed for sharing, such as the platters of local hams and cheeses, while the homemade tonnarelli pasta with a Prošek wine sauce, onions, garlic and prawns is excellent. The well-curated wine list covers the whole of Croatia, with around 15 wines also available by the glass.;;[]
12551;El Toro;Croatia;Zagreb;Ul. fra Filipa Grabovca 1, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8114;15.99454;73;true;false;Asian Influences, Asian and Western;A new option among the capital’s cosmopolitan restaurants, El Toro offers a Taco menu (we recommend the langoustine), as well as sushi and sashimi, with an excellent tuna hamachi served with Oscietra caviar proving one of the most popular choices at the sushi bar. The main dishes have a South American influence and are cooked over the grill, with large Rib Eye and T-bone steaks available for two or more people to share. Arranged over two floors, the restaurant is modern and trendy in style despite its location at the base of an old-fashioned building. The wine list includes top-quality labels from Croatia and further afield, many available by the glass – ask the young staff for pairing recommendations.;Terrace;[]
12552;Waldinger;Croatia;Osijek;Županijska ulica 8, Osijek, 31000, Croatia;45.5584962;18.675891;92;false;true;Regional Cuisine;The name of this restaurant situated in the Art Nouveau-style hotel of the same name pays tribute to the painter Adolf Waldinger, who was born in Osijek in 1843. In bright, modern dining rooms adorned with contemporary paintings, enjoy a selection of traditional dishes, with something for all tastes on the menu. If you like strong flavours, try the Slavonian black pork cheeks, while guests with a sweet tooth will be tempted by delicious desserts from the Gold pastry shop on the other side of the street, including Krempite tart (a puff pastry speciality with custard cream). The wine list includes labels from local, small-scale wineries. Comfortable, well-appointed guestrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12553;Ribarska Koliba;Croatia;Pula;Verudela 3, Pula, 52100, Croatia;44.8448106;13.8421107;50;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;This century-old restaurant in the modern resort of Ribarska Koliba (the name translates as Fisherman’s Hut) stands near the Marina Veruda, which can be admired through its large picture windows or from its attractive summer terrace. Delicious Mediterranean cuisine takes pride of place on the menu, ranging from pasta-based starters to fish and seafood dishes made from the freshest ingredients (the bouillabaisse is superb), although a few meat specialities also feature. Vintage car enthusiasts can also admire the Triumph Spitfire convertible that is “parked” inside the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
12554;Konoba TRS;Croatia;Trogir;Matije Gupca 14, Trogir, 21220, Croatia;43.5169071;16.2499863;67;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in an alleyway in the busy historic centre, this restaurant boasts an elegant dining room with exposed stonework and an attractive outdoor patio. The traditional Mediterranean cuisine with a modern touch is showcased on an à la carte and a tasting menu. The house specialities include a delicious brodetto with langoustine, monkfish and octopus, which is served with creamy mashed potatoes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12555;Konoba Tri Piruna;Croatia;Vodice;Ul. Roca Pave 5, Vodice, 22211, Croatia;43.759354;15.777178;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Meats and Grills;Mature, large and aged steaks are at the heart of the business here-carved in the room with skill (the steaks are all Croatian and of upmost quality) they are modern in presentation and accompanied by a good choice of wines. The simple dining room has a rustic and relaxed feel, while the cool, shaded outdoor terrace comes into its own in summer.;Terrace;[]
12556;Konoba Fetivi;Croatia;Split;Tomića Stine 4, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5083839;16.4344042;42;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A very popular restaurant in the city, which is well worth a visit for its traditional cuisine served in a simple yet beautifully kept dining room. The menu features unpretentious Mediterranean fish dishes and traditional meat specialities, with ingredients purchased fresh from the local market every day. Don’t miss the delicious apple strudel, which is made from an old family recipe. The friendly welcome from all the staff is an added attraction!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12557;Tekka;Croatia;Zagreb;Radnička cesta 37b, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.80283;16.00258;57;true;true;Japanese, Asian;A small Japanese restaurant with a modern feel and an open-view kitchen that allows guests to watch the chefs at work. Traditional Japanese specialities such as nigiri, uramaki, hosomaki and sashimi are to the fore, as well as tempura and teppanyaki and other Asian options including stir-fries.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12558;Pod Zidom;Croatia;Zagreb;Pod zidom 5, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8139203;15.978409;19;false;true;Farm to table;A modern-style bistro with a wine bar and small attractive outdoor space in the city centre, just behind the main square with fine views of the cathedral. The chef, who describes his cuisine as “market-fresh”, makes daily visits to the nearby Dolac market for his ingredients, which include seasonal vegetables and meat reared on local farms. The owner is passionate about wine, and includes several Croatian wines made from native grape varieties on the wine list, which also pays close attention to organic labels.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12559;Villa Ariston;Croatia;Opatija;Ulica Maršala Tita 179, Opatija, 51410, Croatia;45.3199952;14.2966503;62;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in a beautiful 19C residence with a garden offering stunning sea views, Villa Ariston is one of the region’s unmissable gastronomic experiences. The cuisine maintains a subtle balance between tradition, classic flavours and the creativity which has given the restaurant its fine reputation. The menu features numerous fish dishes (the scampi-filled ravioli served with a scampi and mussel bisque are delicious), as well as local specialities such as lamb from nearby Cres island.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12560;Zlatne Gorice;Croatia;Varaždin Breg;Ul. Banjščina 104, Varaždin Breg, 42204, Croatia;46.2363848;16.4022305;85;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Situated in a picturesque and relaxing setting of rolling hills, vineyards and charming villas, this restaurant is part of a wine estate. The cuisine focuses on regional specialities with an emphasis on meat, including a wide array of grilled dishes.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12561;Konoba Buščina;Croatia;Umag;Buščina 18, Umag, 52470, Croatia;45.4469238;13.5998626;93;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This beautiful rustic-style inn occupying a country house just outside Umag has been in business for 30 years. Here, traditional meat and fish ingredients such as scallops, langoustine, Boscarin beef, Istrian ham and truffles inspire simple, generous dishes which showcase the best of the region. Friendly service and pleasantly informal atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12562;ZOI;Croatia;Split;Obala Hrvatskog Narodnog Preporoda 23, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.50736;16.439678;38;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant boasts what is arguably the best location in the centre of Split, with a long panoramic terrace that runs alongside the southern section of the Palace of Diocletian and offers fine views of the port. The young chef reinterprets traditional Dalmatian cuisine inspired by old recipes and offer three menus: Obala (focuses on fish and seafood), Zagora (ingredients from inland areas), and a long menu that combines the two. The delicious carrot cake with cashew nuts and orange juice offers a snapshot of Split’s commercial history, combining the port’s exports (carrots and oranges) with other ingredients that were imported (cashews). We recommend booking a table on the top floor to make the most of the beautiful view.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12563;Šug;Croatia;Split;Tolstojeva 1a, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5094919;16.4432943;27;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Šug is the Croatian word for sauce, an important feature of this chef’s cuisine. Situated away from the busy tourist centre of Split, this informal, attractive and relaxing restaurant serves generous portions of traditional meat and fish dishes from Dalmatia, with the occasional influence from nearby Italy. In summer, the small outdoor space in an inner courtyard adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12564;Spinnaker;Croatia;Porec;Obala Maršala Tita 15, Porec, 52440, Croatia;45.2272298;13.5924544;23;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Creative;It was at Heinz Beck’s La Pergola that chef Goran Hrastovčak learned how to make an ingredient the centrepiece of a dish. In his two tasting menus, “Istrian Fables” and “Modern Tales” (as the names suggest, the first is more traditional and the second more innovative), the cuisine showcases the region and its iconic ingredients, such as scampi, squid, sea bass and Istrian beef. The ravioli filled with lobster and served with Jerusalem artichoke and a scampi bisque is highly recommended. The view of Poreč harbour plus a wine list that features excellent Istrian labels as well as an extensive selection of Croatian wines and renowned bottles from elsewhere in Europe add to the appeal. Among the local wines, we suggest the Primo Fakin, an Istrian Teran-based red with spicy aromas and a pleasant roundness.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12565;Konoba Boba;Croatia;Murter;Ulica Butina 22, Murter, 22243, Croatia;43.82326;15.594688;56;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A gastronomic landmark on the island of Murter, the gateway to the Kornati archipelago, which is linked to the mainland by a small bridge. Although the restaurant is a “konoba” (tavern) in name, it is decidedly elegant in feel, with an intimate dining room and outdoor space for the summer months. The cuisine has a Mediterranean focus with just a few meat dishes, while raw fish options (especially tuna) are the house speciality. The property’s kitchen garden provides the fruit and vegetables used in the dishes here, as well as herbs such as marjoram, oregano, basil, rosemary, mint and parsley. There’s also a good choice of wine with an emphasis on Dalmatia and elsewhere in Croatia. The young, dynamic staff add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Garden or park;[]
12566;Meneghetti;Croatia;Bale;Stancija Meneghetti 1, Bale, 52211, Croatia;45.007668;13.744981;33;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This rustic yet elegant hotel restaurant occupies a charming stone building idyllically situated among vineyards and olive trees in tranquil countryside. The cuisine, which is traditionally Mediterranean with personalised touches, is accompanied by the property’s own excellent wines and olive oils, with a wide selection of the latter that includes whites, reds and classic sparkling options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
12567;Marina;Croatia;Novigrad;Ulica Sv. Antona 38, Novigrad, 52466, Croatia;45.319618;13.56541;84;false;false;Creative;This tiny yet elegant restaurant with a terrace overlooking the port is situated just above street level. At the helm in the kitchen (visible through a large window from the dining room), the female owner serves modern, Mediterranean fish and seafood dishes on tasting menus which vary according to market availability.;Air conditioning;[]
12568;Stara Loza;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Prijeko Palace Hotel, Prijeko 22, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.641818;18.1087915;32;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in the Old Town of this UNESCO World Heritage city is the intimate and luxurious Prijeko Palace Hotel. Its restaurant, Stara Loza, is almost three in one – there’s a street level terrace, a formal restaurant on the third floor and a delightful open terrace right at the top which affords great views. Cooking is Mediterranean in heart, with plenty of depth and flavour. The veal risotto is a must-try and be sure to save room for dessert, which is always a highlight.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
12569;ManO2;Croatia;Zagreb;Radnička cesta 50, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8026606;16.0021755;36;true;false;Croatian, Contemporary;Situated just outside the old town, this elegant restaurant with contemporary furnishings also boasts an attractive outdoor space near the entrance. The meat and fish dishes served here combine creative touches with a solid foundation in traditional Croatian cuisine, as well as a focus on top-quality grilled meats. There are two tasting menus (five or eight courses), plus a fairly extensive à la carte. Among the appetisers, try the prawn and crab salad with miso and toasted almond cream, salicornia, seaweed and buckwheat “pops”.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12570;Cap Aureo;Croatia;Rovinj;Smareglijeva ulica 1A, Rovinj, 52210, Croatia;45.0754807;13.6369528;82;false;true;Creative, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the fifth floor of the elegant and stylish Grand Park Hotel Rovinj by Maistra Collection, this restaurant offers spectacular views of Rovinj’s old town and marina from its glass-enclosed terrace. Chef Jeffrey Vella’s seasonal tasting menu showcases modern, Mediterranean cuisine made from local ingredients, with a particular focus on Istrian flavours and traditions. In addition to meat and fish dishes, careful attention is paid to vegetarian options.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
12571;Kadena;Croatia;Split;Ivana pl. Zajca 4, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5015874;16.4595869;90;false;false;International;The main attraction of this restaurant, one of the most elegant addresses in the city, is its stunning location overlooking the sea and the delightful views from its outdoor terrace. On the menu, the undisputed star of the show is the fresh fish displayed in a chilled cabinet, although a few meat dishes are also available. Highlights include the saffron ravioli with blue crabmeat and leeks, and the sea bass fillet with baby beets, pine nuts, a white wine reduction and caper sauce. The wine list features an interesting choice of wines, champagnes and sparkling wines from Croatia and further afield, as well as top-quality gins and whiskies.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12572;Damir & Ornella;Croatia;Novigrad;Zidine 5, Novigrad, 52466, Croatia;45.316772;13.559227;63;false;false;Seafood, Mediterranean Cuisine;The welcoming ambience and the quality of the ingredients used are the trump cards of this family-run restaurant, which serves delicious fish and seafood. Raw marinated fish is the house speciality, including scampi, prawns, squid, cuttlefish, marinated sole and a few pasta dishes. The concise menu is announced at your table, a sure guarantee of fresh ingredients.;;[]
12573;Zinfandel's;Croatia;Zagreb;Mihanovićeva Ulica 1, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8054747;15.9759303;68;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated in the Hotel Esplanade, which dates back to 1925 and is one of the most luxurious hotels in Zagreb, Zifandel's cuisine has been overseen by chef Ana Grgić for the past ten years. She reinterprets Mediterranean traditions in a creative and personalised style, with a focus on local, seasonal ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12574;Il Ponte;Croatia;Trogir;Kardinala Alojza Stepinca 15a, Trogir, 21220, Croatia;43.5190802;16.2502609;20;true;false;Contemporary;Located just a stone’s throw from the centre, this elegant restaurant named after Trogir’s iconic wooden bridge boasts a beautiful dining room with a veranda and stylish furnishings with a blue-and-yellow colour scheme. The cuisine is inspired by the flavours and traditions of the Mediterranean and prepared using modern techniques and creative twists – in summer, there’s a barbecue grill where the chef can be observed at work. Guests with a sweet tooth will enjoy the delicious desserts.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12575;Dunav;Croatia;Ilok;Julija Benešića, 62, Ilok, 32236, Croatia;45.2302782;19.3798675;29;true;true;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;Situated on the banks of the Danube (known as Dunav in Croatian), this restaurant boasts an excellent location which can be enjoyed from its outdoor terrace in summer. The menu features fish from the river, including grilled zander and catfish fillets in white wine. Guests with a sweet tooth will enjoy rounding off their meal with a taške (a kind of jam-filled pastry) or a šnenokle, the Croatian version of the French île flottante.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12576;Bedem;Croatia;Varazdin;Vladirmira Nazora 9, Varazdin, 42000, Croatia;46.311234;16.333961;64;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;“Bedem” is the Croatian word for “bastion” – a highly appropriate name for this restaurant which overlooks Varaždin’s historic castle and surrounding park. The cuisine here is classically French in style, with a contemporary touch and the use of local, seasonal ingredients such as vegetables from nearby Vidovce, pumpkin oil, turkey from Zagorie and local trout. The strukli (dumplings) stuffed with fresh cheese and served as an appetiser are delicious and the local wines offer excellent value for money. In winter, take a seat near the fireplace, while in summer the outdoor terrace is a must.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12577;Jeny;Croatia;Tucepi;D512, Tucepi, 21325, Croatia;43.277737;17.061975;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The first thing you’ll notice when you get here is the spectacular view: the restaurant is actually perched over the coastal village. Jeny is the tangible manifestation of a real family business whose key players are two brothers: Milenko in the dining room and Vladomir in the kitchen. In high season (1 July - 15 August) there are three tasting menus of 7, 5 and 3 courses: modern and sometimes articulated dishes, with an indisputable aesthetic appeal. The table on the patio is a great plus!;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Terrace;[]
12579;Konoba Zijavica;Croatia;Mošćenička Draga;Šetalište 25. travnja 2, Mošćenička Draga, 51417, Croatia;45.2366041;14.2544333;52;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The sea takes centre stage at this welcoming restaurant in a delightful fishing village, both on the plate and in its location just a stone’s throw from the water. In the dining room, guests can admire the chef at work in the tiny open-view kitchen, while the restaurant’s veranda overlooking the sea with the waves lapping the shore is a real gem. The focus here is personalised fish cuisine, where the main ingredient is the star of the show. Be patient if something is missing from the menu – the fish on offer here depends very much on the season and local fishermen’s catch of the day. Simple yet delicious recipes are to the fore, including raw fish dishes, pasta, and fish and shellfish priced by weight – a real paradise for fresh fish enthusiasts. As for Mošćenička Draga itself, this is the perfect location for lazing on the beach or cycling in the surrounding hills.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12580;PiNKU fish & wine;Croatia;Split;Obrov ulica 4, Split, 21000, Croatia;43.5092213;16.4376232;79;false;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant, once a butcher’s shop, is located next to the Peškarija fish market, where the chef chooses the best local fish for his creative cuisine. Dishes, showcased on an à la carte (lunchtime only) and a 6-course tasting menu, can be enjoyed in the dining room or outdoors on the terrace, and are often prepared using modern techniques such as sous-vide cooking. Try delicious recipes such as poached hake with cuttlefish noodles accompanied by poached egg, a beetroot coulis and citrus fruit foam.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12581;Konoba Kala;Croatia;Supetar;Kala 7, Supetar, 21400, Croatia;43.3841;16.55529;55;false;true;Croatian;Hidden away close to the main harbour lies this intimate and beautifully designed restaurant. Take a seat on the delightful terrace with large wooden benches if you fancy enjoying the quality cooking al fresco. Two menus are available, which both reflect the island well, with seasonally influenced cooking including Adriatic fish and some lovely lamb. Some dishes are cooked over the wood-burning fire for a natural smoky flavour. Desserts are a real highlight, with those featuring figs particularly worth choosing. Top off your visit by trying one of the local island wines - a glass or two of Senjković Bosso is called for.;Terrace;[]
12582;Filippi;Croatia;Korcula;Šetalište Petra Kanavelića, Korcula, 20260, Croatia;42.9615394;17.136996;56;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant along the seafront promenade in the old town boasts an outdoor space overlooking the sea, the Pelješac channel and the islands of the Korčula archipelago. The cuisine here is classic, unpretentious and decidedly Mediterranean, with a focus on fish on 3-or 4-course set menus, as well as on a tasting menu. The concise wine list showcases wines from Korčula, Hvar and Pelješac, with particular attention paid to lesser-known producers. The sea bass served with green peas, courgettes and gregada, a typical Croatian seafood soup, is delicious.;Great view,Terrace;[]
12583;Dubrovnik;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Marojice Kaboge 5, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.640522;18.109539;93;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;In this elegant, stylish restaurant in the heart of the historic centre, the chef uses local ingredients to create fresh, delicious dishes such as scallops with soft polenta, goat’s cheese, hazelnuts and porcini mushrooms, and a mouthwatering puff pastry dessert filled with figs cooked in the local sweet Prošek wine and served with vanilla cream, cinnamon and almonds. Don’t miss the enchanting outdoor terrace in summer.;Terrace;[]
12584;Zuzori;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Cvijete Zuzoric 2, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.6407;18.1098;46;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This small restaurant within the city’s medieval walls has a welcoming and informal atmosphere. The menu is imaginative and includes fresh seafood from the Adriatic, pasta dishes, light salads and vegetarian options with a pleasing contemporary touch. The attractive outdoor dining area in an alleyway in the historic centre allows guests to experience all the magic of Dubrovnik.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12585;Proto Fish;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Široka ul 1, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.641304;18.108404;54;true;false;Seafood;Choose between the terrace out on the street, the dining room and (easily the best option) the first-floor terrace at this restaurant in the heart of the old town. The restaurant’s name hints at the menu, which focuses on fresh local fish served in tempting dishes such as the superb fresh sea bass, king prawns and delicious barbecue-grilled octopus. Make sure you leave space for dessert: the rožata (crème caramel) is the perfect conclusion to your meal.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12586;Wine Vault Restaurant - Levante Edition;Croatia;Rovinj;Ul. Antonia Smareglie 3, Rovinj, 52210, Croatia;45.0726767;13.6368122;63;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated within the luxurious “adult only” Monte Mulini hotel, this restaurant with a beautiful terrace serves local cuisine prepared using regional produce alongside a few Asian ingredients – guests choose the number of courses they want from the menu. Careful attention is paid to wine pairing, with an impressive selection of local labels, including sparkling wines and a good choice of champagnes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12587;Badi;Croatia;Lovrečica;Umaška Ulica 12, Lovrečica, 52470, Croatia;45.3849458;13.5377703;52;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Although a few meat dishes feature on the menu, it is fish and seafood that has cemented this restaurant’s reputation. Its dishes are traditionally prepared with an emphasis on simplicity in order to allow the quality of the fish to shine through. Scampi features widely, while the “Badi” soup, breaded sea bass and various “na buzaru” dishes (stewed in white wine with parsley, garlic and breadcrumbs) are among the house specialities.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12588;Kaštel;Croatia;Zadar;Bedemi Zadarskih Pobuna 13, Zadar, 23000, Croatia;44.11785;15.224;56;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;This restaurant is housed within the luxurious Hotel Bastion, which occupies the remains of a corner tower of the town walls. In this intimate and elegant setting, enjoy Mediterranean cuisine with its roots in Dalmatian traditions yet with an intriguing Italian influence. In summer, booking a table on the terrace with its fine panoramic views is highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12589;Torero;Croatia;Zagreb;Ivana Tkalčića 84, Zagreb, 10000, Croatia;45.8186374;15.9765136;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated in the oldest, most visited part of Zagreb, this quiet, well-run restaurant welcomes guests with an entire wall covered with plants and flowers that symbolise the Medvednica, the mountain chain to the north of the capital that inspires the cuisine served here. With a focus on local, mostly organic ingredients, dishes are colourful and creative, aiming to awaken the senses by introducing a range of different flavours (sweet, acidic, bitter etc). The sommelier will happily recommend Croatian wines to accompany your meal, while the service is enthusiastic, friendly and attentive. Make sure you taste the risotto made with Acquerello rice, as well as the Torero’s own delicious cheesecake.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12590;Pjerin;Croatia;Dubrovnik;Villa Dubrovnik, Vlaha Bukovca 6, Dubrovnik, 20000, Croatia;42.6384188;18.1272478;93;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated outside the city centre, the Villa Dubrovnik hotel provides a tranquil and relaxing setting. Enjoy an aperitif at the roof-top bar and admire stunning views of the coast, which are also visible from the Pjerin restaurant terrace. The excellent cuisine here is regional and seasonal, with fish and seafood from the Adriatic taking centre stage. The home-made appetisers are truly delicious, with the lobster spaghetti now justly considered to be a house speciality. The discreet and elegant service includes recommendations on the best Croatian wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12591;Ouzeria;Germany;Cologne;Brüsseler Str. 68, Cologne, 50674, Germany;50.9380575;6.9347365;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Maria Karpathiotaki and her partner Nikos Kasotakis have taken over her parents' Greek restaurant in the Belgian Quarter and turned it into a trendy, vibrant fine dining spot. While she cordially welcomes guests front of house in the well-kept rustic-style bistro space, the chef is to be found at work in the kitchen, cooking up modern, creative dishes with Mediterranean and Asian influences. The menu includes a lovely selection of starters, plated in slightly smaller portions that are good for sharing and for trying out several – examples include "baby calamari, red pepper, pine nut pesto" and "half a corn-fed poulard breast, fermented celery, baby pak choi, ponzu, miso-samos-nectar espuma". Naturally, the menu also features ouzo. There is a small terrace laid out on the pavement.;Terrace;[]
12592;Berghotel Wiedener Eck;Germany;Wieden;Oberwieden 15, Wieden, 79695, Germany;47.8449189;7.8672651;92;false;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;Marie and Lorenz Wissler represent the fourth generation of their family to run Berghotel Wiedener Eck, which enjoys an idyllic location at over 1 000m above sea level – the view of the valley is stunning! For overnight stays, there are attractive, cosy guestrooms, and the restaurant is brimming with traditional Black Forest charm, interspersed with modern touches. In the restaurant, you can look forward to friendly and courteous service, as well as regional cuisine and dishes that draw on the culinary traditions of France and the Mediterranean, all made from fresh high-quality ingredients – the chef even hunts his own game. In the evenings, there is a set menu that changes every day, plus the seasonal "Wiedener Eck Menü". You can also order the individual courses of both à la carte. Tip: The surrounding forests and meadows make this hotel a perfect starting point for hikes!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12594;Frau Specht;Germany;Duisburg;Hohe Straße 19, Duisburg, 47051, Germany;51.4312984;6.7710054;27;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine;"Dinner is ready" is the slogan here. You ring the doorbell before being escorted into this somewhat hidden little restaurant with a modern, minimalist decor. You are shown to your table in a pleasantly intimate living room-style interior – with a small open kitchen and just a handful of tables, it makes for a private atmosphere. The service comes with a personal touch: your cordial hostess, Yvonne Specht, after whom the restaurant is named, will also recommend just the right wines from the extensive list of top-draw international labels. In the kitchen, head chef Dirk Brendel cooks up an ambitious seven-course surprise menu in the evening, further embellishing it with a variety of additional small dishes. The menu is devised based on the season and the availability of the ingredients. The cuisine is classic and Mediterranean, but also includes international flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12595;Morchella;United Kingdom;London;84-86 Rosebery Avenue, Islington, London, EC1R 4QY, United Kingdom;51.5266576;-0.1085719;40;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Set in a converted former bank, Morchella sports a small but well-stocked wine bar to one side, offering largely natural and biodynamic options that the wine list describes as either ‘Classic’, ‘Coastal’ or ‘Funky’. On the food side of things, the menu has a Mediterranean slant and is designed for sharing – although if the spaghetti alle vongole is available, you’ll be loath to give any up. Service is bright and breezy, while the great value lunch menu means you can dine without breaking the bank, so to speak.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12596;1919;United Kingdom;Malvern Wells;Cottage in the Wood Hotel,  Holywell Road, Malvern Wells, WR14 4LG, United Kingdom;52.0819;-2.33519;42;false;false;Modern British;In finer weather, you must aim for a table on the terrace at this restaurant set within the famous The Cottage in the Wood hotel. Built – funnily enough – in 1919, it boasts one of the best panoramic views of the English countryside that you will find. The restaurant itself is a bright, stylish place serving both a tasting menu and an à la carte. A proudly British spirit shines through in the cooking, from the use of Exmoor caviar and Evesham asparagus to a butter sauce flavoured with English sparkling wine. The service is well-paced and the whole experience comes at a sensible price tag.;Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12597;Hansom;United Kingdom;Bedale;7-9 North End, Bedale, DL8 1AF, United Kingdom;54.2906208;-1.5938002;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A stone-faced 16th-century house in the pretty market town of Bedale provides a fine home for this friendly restaurant. A drinks terrace sits on the cobbled street out front, while small plates are served in the interior wine bar. The main dining room, where the tasting menu is the focus, stylishly contrasts rustic beams and an old fireplace with modern décor. Eponymous Chef-Owner Ruth Hansom is a local and it shows in her cooking, which skilfully spotlights wonderful produce from the surrounding area – be it Swaledale lamb or the famous Yorkshire rhubarb.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12598;The Shed;United Kingdom;Swansea;Unit 1&2 J-Shed, Kings Road, Swansea, SA1 8PL, United Kingdom;51.62317;-3.94144;16;true;true;Traditional British;Experienced Chef-Owner Jonathan Woolway worked in London for many years before returning home to his beloved Wales to open this industrial-style restaurant by the former docks. His patriotic side comes out in the use of terrific local produce, along with a none-more-Welsh lamb, leek and laverbread pie to share. The other dishes too, from Mangalitsa brawn to a Welsh rarebit on the side, are hearty, traditional and decidedly unfussy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12599;Josephine Bouchon;United Kingdom;London;315 Fulham Road, Chelsea, London, SW10 9QH, United Kingdom;51.4866083;-0.1795928;21;false;true;Lyonnaise, French;Chef Claude Bosi returns to his Lyonnaise roots with this buzzy ‘bouchon’, where the tables are tightly packed and the walls are adorned with colourful posters. The menu could scarcely be more French if it was emblazoned with the tricolore: vol-au-vent, andouillete, frog’s legs… take your pick. It’s all executed with great skill and packs in plenty of flavour, while the service is delivered with a certain ‘bonne humeur’. The set menu is remarkably good value and the well-chosen wine list contains some notable French producers.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12600;Ballyfin;Ireland;Ballyfin;Ballyfin Demesne, Ballyfin, R32 X5X8, Ireland;53.0576118;-7.431594;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It takes some doing for a restaurant to stand out when it’s in a hotel as beautiful as this. Ballyfin Demesne is a spectacular, lovingly restored Regency-era manor house that screams luxury at every turn. The opulence continues into the dining room, where the chefs serve fittingly impressive dishes. Broths, purées and sauces are a real highlight and underline the technical skill of the kitchen team, be it a rich, glossy reduction or a roasted onion consommé with bags of flavour. Charming and attentive service completes the rather special picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
12601;Sète;United Kingdom;Margate;238 Northdown Road,  Cliftonville, Margate, CT9 2QD, United Kingdom;51.3874279;1.3988254;89;false;true;Modern British;A characterful, bow-windowed former sweet shop is the home for this lovingly run restaurant located on the road between Margate and Broadstairs. In a fairly small space, the passionate team have managed to combine a restaurant, a wine bar and a bottle shop. The kitchen fuses some classical French techniques with a distinctly British, produce-driven approach, where nothing is overworked and the natural flavours of a few key ingredients are the driving force. The blackboard-written menu is ever-changing, but expect the likes of curried lamb mince or braised squid and peas.;Terrace;[]
12602;The Owl;United Kingdom;Hawnby;Hill Top, Hawnby, YO62 5QS, United Kingdom;54.3010645;-1.1674678;54;true;false;British Contemporary;The team from the former Bantam in Helmsley are behind this characterful rural pub, which benefits from an enviable location perched above a pretty valley in the North York Moors National Park. A former drover’s inn dating back to the 19th century, there’s a vintage style to the décor and a lovely, welcoming vibe thanks to the friendly team. Hearty, unfussy and downright tasty dishes are the order of the day, with old favourites like devilled kidneys and toad in the hole sure to satisfy. Bedrooms are available for those looking to explore the surroundings in more detail.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12603;Primitif;Belgium;Gedinne;Rue de Charleville 15A, Gedinne, 5575, Belgium;49.9795417;4.936571;19;false;false;Creative French;Augustin Massinon and Darius Van Hoef have returned to their roots as they roll out their nature-inspired gourmet concept. First of all, they tastefully refurbished this Ardennes edifice whilst maintaining its authentic character. We recommend booking a table downstairs to make the most of the view of the open kitchen. The chefs, who are committed to using locally sourced produce as much as possible, pool their creative talents to craft beautifully plated dishes. Impeccable handiwork underscored by local ingredients, exotic seasonings and fermented flavours, examples of which include a tartare of langoustine with fermented radish, green apples, poached and foamy oyster and a hint of blackcurrant. The menu, which changes every five weeks, both surprises and enchants.;;[]
12604;Paulette;Belgium;Ename;Enameplein 12, Ename, 9700, Belgium;50.8555244;3.6313146;30;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;True, the pretty square is picturesque, but the cute interior is something else again and often love at first sight! Timber rafters, a fireplace, floral-patterned ceiling lights and a lovely sheltered alfresco patio – simply glorious! The chef shines the spotlight on local, seasonal produce with the odd international twist. He might underscore lamb from the Vande Walle butchers with cooking juices and asparagus, while his moist, fudgy chocolate cake, which borders on perfection, is paired with vanilla ice cream in a match made in heaven. Generosity is the byword here.;Terrace;[]
12605;Vicomté;Belgium;Roucourt;Rue d'Arondeau 29, Roucourt, 7601, Belgium;50.5243991;3.5731458;55;false;false;Modern French;Vicomté castle, part of the Arrondeau Estate, is the epitome of date-night romanticism. The wrought-iron conservatory, stylish fixtures and fittings and view over the pond are fully worthy of an Impressionist work of art. This unique setting provides the perfect foil for Quentin Gallopyn’s ode to top-drawer produce. Knife-edged precision and rich, fruity flavours set the culinary stage. He might coat delicately crispy scallops in balsamic vinegar, before adding a subtly sweet red apple and soy sauce jelly. Don’t forget to take the time to peruse the wine list of mainly French vintages, before finally heading upstairs to spend a restful night in one of the swish guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
12606;Sébastian;Belgium;Liège;Rue de la Cathédrale 25, Liège, 400, Belgium;50.642942;5.576279;39;false;true;Farm to table, Creative French;Sébastien Cassart is forging his own path. He works alone in his open kitchen, sometimes even serving the food himself as he embarks you on a culinary adventure. The untreated interior, adorned with art photos, is emblematic of the buzzy venue’s ethos. The chef crafts intuitive dishes that bear witness to his passion for outstanding, mainly local ingredients. Breast and leg of Malines poultry are served with a crispy skin and underscored by a mind-blowing blend of a gutsy gravy, truffles, sherry vinegar and the distinctive flavours of satay and peanut. Wholehearted, playful cuisine presented in a concise menu.;;[]
12607;LOF;Belgium;Gent;Hoogstraat 36, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0546726;3.7145446;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The Ghent Pillows Hotel sports a regal Louis XIV vibe, whose plush opulence also extends to the LOF restaurant, albeit in a less extravagant vein. A mouthwatering range of outstanding produce sets the sophisticated culinary scene with the odd Asian twist. The chef might cook monkfish on the bone to preserve the taste and juicy flesh, while a delicately sweet cream of carrots, a stock of lapsang souchong tea and a velvety emulsion of olives and carrot juice further underscore this subtle fish. Heaven for lovers of spot-on, up-to-the-minute French fare.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12608;Bar Raket;Belgium;Antwerpen;Bresstraat 10, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2069393;4.3979388;83;false;false;Sharing, International;Convivial and buzzing Bar Raket provides a chic industrial-style setting in which to share a variety of delectable dishes. Flavours from all over the globe are represented here in cuisine that is all about enjoying the simple things: from Catalan bread to the umami of tonkatsu with North Sea crab to super-fresh clams with fried diced guanciale and a delectable hot sauce. The bread is simply divine! With a selection of smaller dishes and three main courses, the menu shows that good food can also be a delightfully laid-back affair.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
12609;Blanc by Aytems;Belgium;Antwerpen;De Burburestraat 4a, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2093675;4.391099;81;false;false;Turkish, Modern Cuisine;Ayt Ems and family invite you to sample the distinctive ambiance of their terraced house in Antwerp’s hip Zuid district. Before admiring one of the Quartier Sud suites, sip a knockout cocktail and nibble an appetiser or two in the Bar Bleu. Next make your way into the snug dining area whose buzzy vibe and baroque curves provide the perfect backdrop to the talented chef’s subtle culinary score which rolls out Ottoman and French influences. Home-made spice blends and delicacies such as Baharat and chermoula enhance and underscore the food. The halibut is rubbed in spices (cumin and curcuma) and cooked in a fermented lime mousse that imparts refreshing acidity. The little buns that the lady of the house prepares in front of you are simply divine!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12610;545 Whampoa Prawn Noodles;;Singapore;Tekka Centre, #01-326, 665 Buffalo Road, 210665, Singapore;1.3059012;103.8504528;94;true;false;Street Food;The stall dates back to 1920s. Dry noodles dressed in sambal sauce are topped with bean sprouts, prawns and pork, and served with umami-laden prawn soup. Or opt for the noodle soup version. Add fried shallots and lard on top.;Cash only;[]
12611;Olivia;;Singapore;#01-03, 55 Keong Saik Road, Singapore;1.2807626;103.8416376;89;false;true;Spanish;Come to this lively Catalan spot for tapas and small plates packed with flavour, made with finesse and plated with modern aesthetics. Don’t miss the iconic creamy cheesecake and “spherical olives,” a tribute to the legendary el Bulli. The chic interior by Barcelona-based designer Rosa-Violán embodies the Mediterranean soul and takes diners to Spain instantly. Service is very friendly and attentive, and the maître d is always up for a chat.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
12612;Shi Le Yuan;;Singapore;Redhill Market, #01-82, 85 Redhill Lane, 150085, Singapore;1.2873967;103.818244;67;false;true;Street Food;Richly-flavoured braised pork and organs are a good match with the kway chap, which is served separately.;Cash only;[]
12613;Podi & Poriyal;;Singapore;486 Serangoon Road, 218151, Singapore;1.3150249;103.8572419;78;false;false;Indian Vegetarian;The name says it all – this vegetarian joint prides itself on the spicy ground lentil condiment known as podi, and sautéed vegetables, or poriyal. Replicating South Indian grandmas' cooking, the menu covers all plant-based dietary desires, with gluten-free, allium-free and vegan options. "Which Podi? Idli" – steamed rice cake tossed in podi – is served with a cashew and coconut chutney. Their podi dosai with poriyal filling is also excellent.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12614;Vue;;Singapore;OUE Bayfront, Level 19, 50 Collyer Quay, 049321, Singapore;1.2830712;103.85301;99;true;false;European Contemporary;Aptly named after the French word for ‘view’, this romantic restaurant boasts one of the most stunning vistas of Marina Bay. Even the ceiling is designed to emanate light without casting reflections on the glass panes. The menu shows the culinary vision of the young head chef, with the four-course chef’s tasting menu being the most popular choice where diners may choose from a number of interesting options. Steaks and risotto are great for sharing. Executive set lunch is popular.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12615;Toa Payoh 93 Soon Kueh;;Singapore;Geylang Bahru Market & Food Centre, #01-68, 69 Geylang Bahru, 330069, Singapore;1.32144;103.870173;95;true;true;Street Food;The stall carries three kinds of dumplings – soon kueh stuffed with bamboo shoot, rice kueh and kuchai kueh with chives. All varieties boast elastic skin and generous filling. Try also the limited offer Hakka yam abacus seeds.;Cash only;[]
12616;Maison Boulud;;Singapore;The Shoppes at Marina Bay Sands, #B1-15 & L1-83, 10 Bayfront Avenue, 018956, Singapore;1.2852929;103.8607;37;true;true;French;With executive chef Rémy Carmignani on board, Maison Boulud is located in the shopping mall at Marina Bay Sands. The patio on the upper level boasts stunning views – perfect for al fresco dining. The elegant main dining room (lower level) has an oversize wine cellar displaying impressive vintages. The menu is defined by classic French cuisine, with more sophisticated plating, as opposed to bistro-style fare. There is also their signature seafood platter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12617;The 1950's Coffee;;Singapore;Chinatown Complex Market & Food Centre, #02-048, 335 Smith Street, 050335, Singapore;1.2821578;103.8432905;25;true;false;Street Food;Come here for the quintessential Singaporean teatime classics – kaya toast with kopi kosong (black coffee). This popular stall opened its doors in the 1950s and locals have been lining up to get their caffeine fix ever since.;;[]
12618;Feng Zhen Lor Mee;;Singapore;Taman Jurong Market & Food Centre, #03-146, 3 Yung Sheng Road, Jurong West, 618499, Singapore;1.3349205;103.7213881;97;true;true;Street Food;This popular stall offers lor mee with generous toppings like meatballs and fish flakes. The noodles are springy and the broth is tasty and flavoursome. Also, try their deep-fried prawn rolls with a crispy skin and juicy filling.;Cash only;[]
12619;Lao Jie Fang;;Singapore;Mei Ling Market & Food Centre, #02-15, 159 Mei Chin Road, 140159, Singapore;1.2932654;103.8028365;70;false;false;Street Food;Cantonese-style noodles topped with beef brisket, pork ribs, pork knuckles or beef tendon are the name of the game here. The noodles are springy, and the pork knuckles are braised until gelatinous in a secret soy sauce.;Cash only;[]
12620;Roia;;Singapore;Singapore Botanic Gardens (Nassim Gate entrance), E.J.H Corner House, 1 Cluny Road, 259569, Singapore;1.3150816;103.8154772;92;false;false;French Contemporary;Not only can you feast your eyes on the lush greenery, you can also taste the herbs and edible flowers grown in the garden and picked minutes before serving. In a refurbished historic edifice, chef-owner Priyam Chatterjee serves two tasting menus that are updated quarterly and feature modern French fare rooted in tradition and exquisitely plated. The top-notch produce comes from around the world and each course tells a story about its source.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12621;Khiri;;Singapore;15 Hamilton Road, 209185, Singapore;1.31152;103.86083;62;false;false;Thai contemporary;Formerly known as Chedi, this Thai restaurant rechristened itself Khiri in 2023. Other than that, nothing has changed – the food still strikes a balance of sweet, sour, spicy and salty flavours. The 8-course tasting menu is inspired by Northern, Northeastern, Southern and Central Thai recipes, creatively melding traditions and modern techniques. Khao pad kid terng, the signature fried rice packed with smoky aromas, is still a firm fixture on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12622;Food Street Fried Kway Teow Mee;;Singapore;Chinatown Complex Market & Food Centre, #02-173, 335 Smith Street, 050335, Singapore;1.2821551;103.8432905;72;true;true;Street Food;Loaded with wok hei, their kway teow mee is ribbon rice noodles, egg noodles, bean sprouts and scrambled egg tossed in a secret sauce. For toppings, choose clams only, or a mix of seafood with fish, squid, shrimps and clams.;Cash only;[]
12623;Guan Kee Fried Carrot Cake;;Singapore;Albert Centre, #01-59, 270 Queen Street, 180270, Singapore;1.3009493;103.8543342;92;false;true;Street Food;Kind of a misnomer, fried carrot cake is made with radish and not a dessert. It comes in two varieties – black and white. The black one has a caramel-like sweetness while the white one is eggy and salty. Order a mix of both.;;[]
12624;Fiz;;Singapore;#01-01/02, 21 Tanjong Pagar Road, 088444, Singapore;1.279692;103.844015;87;false;false;Malaysian, Contemporary;Malaysian owner-chef Hafizzul Hashim opened Fiz in 2023 in a bid to showcase his native food culture. His experience menus are an ode to his childhood memories and family recipes, emphasising bold flavours and Malaysian produce. Each course is intricately crafted and composed of numerous ingredients. Expect to spend up to 3 hours over your meal. Speciality cocktails and wine pairings complete the experience.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12625;Imbue;;Singapore;32 Keong Saik Road, 089137, Singapore;1.2804955;103.8417162;100;true;true;Innovative;In this heritage shophouse updated with an open kitchen, the dishes are essentially European – but Asian ingredients and taste profiles lend a unique twist. The five- or eight-course dinner menu features Shaoxing-infused abalone from Jeju island, wrapped in kelp and ginger and steamed, served with ginkgo chawanmushi and accompanied by a shiitake reduction and ham jus. The sticky-sweet Malai bread with ginseng honey butter also delivers layers of flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12627;Mag's Wine Kitchen;;Singapore;Kesa House, #01-06, ​55 Keong Saik Road, 089158, Singapore;1.2806561;103.8416323;41;true;false;European Contemporary;Two things catch your attention when you set foot in this long-standing household name – the small walk-in cellar and the bustling open kitchen, where chef-owner Mag can be seen working with her team. Octopus with tomato and chorizo coulis is a decadent start to the meal, followed by classics such as risotto with Boston lobster: for years a staple on the menu, it keeps regulars coming back. The perfect wine-and-dine spot for a Friday night out.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
12628;Hong Wen Mutton Soup;;Singapore;Beauty World Food Centre #04-20, 144 Upper Bukit Timah Road, 588177, Singapore;1.3423709;103.7762553;35;true;false;Street Food;In operation for over half a century, this stall is now run by the second-generation owner and his wife. Their signature soup comprises mutton, tripe or tendon in a garlicky and peppery broth with strong herbal accents.;Cash only;[]
12629;Hup Hong Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Yuhua Village Market and Food Centre, #01-51, Blk 254, Jurong East Street 24, 600254, Singapore;1.3436675;103.7376637;81;true;false;Street Food;The queue to get your roasted or boiled chicken rice may be long, but the wait is worthwhile for the silky-fleshed meat and the heady aromas of rice cooked in chicken stock and fat. Enjoy with char siew or roast pork.;Cash only;[]
12630;Garibaldi;;Singapore;#01-02, 36 Purvis Street, 188613, Singapore;1.296564;103.855;37;false;true;Italian;Ossobuco, costoletta alla Milanese and tiramisu are some of the signature dishes here, at one of the city’s best known Italian restaurants. The affable owner, though, wants everyone to be able to find their favourite dish which is why he offers such a large, all-encompassing menu. The impressive wine list, featuring around 7000 labels, is another feature for which this cosy and contemporary-styled restaurant is celebrated.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12631;Da Po;;Singapore;Golden Mile Food Centre, #B1-53, 505 Beach Road, 199583, Singapore;1.3029969;103.8639417;87;true;false;Street Food;This stall serves only curry chicken noodles and Hainanese chicken rice. The latter comes in three portion sizes. Choose between roast or steamed chicken. The steamed one boasts meaty flavour, springy skin and silky flesh.;;[]
12632;Ann Chin Handmade Popiah;;Singapore;Chinatown Complex Market & Food Centre, #02-112, 335 Smith Street, 050335, Singapore;1.2821926;103.8432986;79;false;true;Street Food;Popiah packed with ingredients including eggs, shrimp, carrot, peanuts etc. provide a rich and varied taste.;;[]
12633;Fatty Ox HK Kitchen;;Singapore;Chinatown Complex Market & Food Centre, #02-84, 335 Smith Street, 050335, Singapore;1.2822034;103.8432932;83;true;true;Street Food;Offers a wide array of noodles, including pork trotter and barbecue meats. The fresh yam noodles are handmade and available for take away only.;;[]
12634;Rojak‧Popiah & Cockle;;Singapore;Maxwell Food Centre, #01-56, 1 Kadayanallur Street, 069184, Singapore;1.2802066;103.844857;28;false;false;Street Food;This clean, tidy stall is named after the three items on its menu. The rojak features pineapple, yam bean, cucumber and fried dough stick dressed in a sweet, tangy and spicy sauce. Try their made-to-order popiah, too.;;[]
12635;Traditional Hakka Lui Cha;;Singapore;Jurong West 505 Market & Food Centre, #01-12, Blk 505, Jurong West Street 52, 640505, Singapore;1.347649;103.717921;64;false;true;Street Food;Hakkanese Lui Cha is a soupy rice dish in which chicken, cabbage and pickles meet the nuttiness of sesame and peanuts plus a hint of herbs. Order the fish cake, stuffed tofu or fried egg toppings.;Cash only;[]
12636;Zi Jing Cheng Hainanese Boneless Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Alexandra Village Food Centre, #01-15, Blk 120 Bukit Merah Lane 1, 150120, Singapore;1.2862958;103.8045586;84;false;false;Street Food;There is only one thing on the menu – Hainanese boneless chicken rice. Set menus are available for one to three guests, all served with steamed chicken, rice and soup. The bird is tender and flavoursome. Expect to queue any time.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
12637;New World Mutton Soup;;Singapore;Bedok Interchange Hawker Centre, #01-23, 208 New Upper Changi Road, 460208, Singapore;1.324706;103.9306438;15;false;true;Street Food;The speciality here – mutton soup – is briny-sweet with plenty of umami, and finely shredded ginger to add zing. Other lamb specialities such as rib soup, kway teow, meatballs, lamb tendon and offal are also worth trying.;;[]
12638;Ah Ter Authentic Teochew Fish Ball Noodles;;Singapore;Amoy Street Food Centre, #01-14, 7 Maxwell Road, 069111, Singapore;1.2794786;103.8466829;40;false;false;Street Food;Now run by the third generation, this family-run stall is famous for its fish ball noodle soup topped with ground pork, pork liver, seaweed and pork rinds. Pork ribs are simmered for hours resulting in a broth rich in gutsy flavours.;;[]
12639;C.M.Y. Satay;;Singapore;Chinatown Complex Market & Food Centre, #02-168, 335 Smith Street, 050335, Singapore;1.2821685;103.8432959;98;true;true;Street Food;Two shops share the same venue, so be sure you order from the right one. The grilled-to-order satay comes in pork, chicken and lamb varieties (or an assortment). The nutty, tangy sauce is tasty and you can order rice on top.;;[]
12640;People's Park Hainanese Chicken Rice;;Singapore;People's Park Complex Food Centre, #01-1098, 32 New Market Road, 050032, Singapore;1.2851661;103.8425425;89;false;false;Street Food;Cantonese barbecue like roast pork and duck aside, the main draws are Hainanese chicken rice and double-boiled soups. The rice is richly perfumed with garlic and the flavourful chicken with a gelatinous skin is not to be missed.;;[]
12641;Loong Kee Yong Tau Fu;;Singapore;Jurong West 505 Market & Food Centre, #01-31, Blk 505, Jurong West Street 52, 640505, Singapore;1.3495894;103.7182191;17;false;true;Street Food;Serve yourself with the stuffed tofu or vegetables. You may also add soup, chee cheong fun, laksa, mee or rice.;Cash only;[]
12642;Hua Xing Bak Kut Teh;;Singapore;Yuhua Market & Hawker Centre, #01-171, Blk 347, Jurong East Avenue 1, Jurong East, 600347, Singapore;1.3452792;103.7313194;55;false;false;Street Food;(The hawker center it locates is temporarily closed.) Bak kut teh with a strong, peppery flavour and aromatic pork ribs. Add rice, pork organs, pork trotter, or vegetable soup for a complete meal.;;[]
12644;Ah Hock Fried Hokkien Noodles;;Singapore;Chomp Chomp Food Centre, #01-27, 20 Kensington Park Road, 557269, Singapore;1.3642542;103.8665402;56;true;false;Street Food;Serves fried Hokkien noodles with shrimp and squid.;;[]
12645;Heng Gi Goose and Duck Rice;;Singapore;Tekka Centre, #01-335, 665 Buffalo Road, 210665, Singapore;1.3056875;103.8505645;71;true;false;Street Food;The soya sauce duck is very popular.;;[]
12646;Singapore Famous Rojak;;Singapore;Albert Centre, #01-45, 270 Queen Street, 180270, Singapore;1.3008879;103.8543306;90;true;false;Street Food;Here, the second generation of the family sells local-style salad with pineapple, cucumber and deep-fried dough stick, tossed in a special home-made sauce and sprinkled with ground peanuts. Chilli is optional.;;[]
12647;Chomp Chomp Satay;;Singapore;Chomp Chomp Food Centre, #01-34, 20 Kensington Park Road, 557269, Singapore;1.3642842;103.8664665;74;true;true;Street Food;Opt for pork, chicken, mutton or ketupat served with pineapple sauce.;;[]
12648;Gordon Grill;;Singapore;Goodwood Park Hotel, 22 Scotts Road, 228221, Singapore;1.3088935;103.8343348;76;true;true;European Contemporary;A feature of Goodwood Park hotel since 1963, the restaurant is famed for its meat trolley service which is wheeled over to each table. Along with the meat and plentiful supplies of seafood from the grill, you can expect French-inspired classic dishes like lobster bisque, braised beef cheek, or Crêpes Suzette flambéed tableside. It’s a good choice for a quiet business lunch, a romantic dinner or weekend family outings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12649;Jade Palace;;Singapore;Forum The Shopping Mall, #B1-13, 583 Orchard Road, 238884, Singapore;1.3059609;103.828514;41;true;false;Seafood;Both the décor and the menu show strong Hong Kong influences, all the more so as super-fresh seafood and veggies are shipped from the city twice a week. The must-tries (sautéed white eel with chives in black bean sauce and braised lobster with ginger and scallion in a claypot) boast exceptional wok hei and craftsmanship. You can also specify how you want your live seafood cooked – ask the friendly front-of-house staff for advice.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12650;Ji Ji Noodle House;;Singapore;Hong Lim Market and Food Centre, #02-48/49, Blk 531A, Upper Cross Street, 051531, Singapore;1.2851692;103.8457399;44;false;false;Street Food;Local wonton and noodle dishes like chicken feet noodle and Ipoh sar hor fun.;;[]
12651;Ibid;;Singapore;18 North Canal Road, 048834, Singapore;1.2863152;103.848305;66;true;false;Innovative;After winning a popular TV cooking contest, lawyer-turned-chef Woo opened Ibid in a remodelled shophouse. The passionate chef gets hands-on in every part of his venture, overlooking the kitchen, greeting guests warmly and serving dishes himself. French techniques and Asian twists are manifested in every course of the varied and exciting set menu. Prized counter seats are the best spots to interact with the chefs and watch the alchemy unfold.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12652;Nasi Lemak Ayam Taliwang;;Singapore;Yishun Park Hawker Centre, #01-33, 51 Yishun Avenue 11, 768867, Singapore;1.4249952;103.8447273;54;false;false;Street Food;Traditional coconut milk rice with Indonesian spicy chicken and sambal sauce.;Cash only;[]
12653;91 Fried Kway Teow Mee;;Singapore;Golden Mile Food Centre, #01-91, 505 Beach Road, 199583, Singapore;1.3029121;103.8638813;92;true;true;Street Food;Their fried kway teow boasts exceptional wok hei and is pork free. Topped with leafy greens, cockles, egg, bean sprouts, deep-fried anchovies and a prawn, the noodles are perfectly seasoned. It closes when sold out.;;[]
12654;Bam!;;Singapore;38-40 Tras Street, 078977, Singapore;1.2784476;103.8444;66;false;false;Innovative;Gone are the days when European dishes had to be paired with wine. Sake can complement any food when chosen wisely. Bam! champions a revolutionary way of appreciating the Japanese rice wine with exquisite modern culinary creations. The sommelier can also help you pick a wine. Though it proclaims itself as an omakase restaurant, you can also order à la carte. Ask for a counter seat to stay close to the action in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12655;Foc (Clarke Quay);;Singapore;40 HongKong Street, 059679, Singapore;1.287412;103.8475;62;false;true;Spanish;You can’t miss the huge papier mâché caricatures of the owner and chef hanging from the ceiling. The food is equally fun as the chef melds Catalonian flavours with modern techniques to create original and exciting tapas-style dishes such as smoked Cantabrian anchovies on charcoal brioche, and patatas bravas FOC style. Always busy and buzzing with a cheerful vibe. Ask for a seat at the counter to enjoy the experience to the full.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12656;Ivy's Hainanese Herbal Mutton Soup;;Singapore;Pasir Panjang Food Centre, #14, 121 Pasir Panjang Road, 118543, Singapore;1.2759467;103.7914178;21;true;false;Street Food;Herbal mutton soup, herbal tendon soup and herbal tulang soup are delicious.;;[]
12657;Tien Lai Rice Stall;;Singapore;Taman Jurong Market & Food Centre, #02-66, 3 Yung Sheng Road, Jurong West, 618499, Singapore;1.3347274;103.7214058;49;true;true;Street Food;Roast duck, roast meat and char siew are available at reasonable prices. Come early before the meat is sold out.;Cash only;[]
12658;Open Farm Community;;Singapore;130E Minden Road, Singapore;1.305662;103.8161;51;false;false;International;Adjacent to the Botanic Garden, this verdantly set glasshouse combines an urban farm and dining concept. The founder-chef advocates an eco-friendly philosophy and therefore designed a mostly plant-based menu. Produce may be sourced from local artisan farms as well as Malaysia, but the food shows eclectic technique and flavours from around the world. The menu offers vegan, vegetarian and gluten-free options to cater to different dietary needs.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12660;National Kitchen;;Singapore;National Gallery Singapore, #02-01, (Coleman Street entrance), 1 St. Andrew's Road, 178957, Singapore;1.2896;103.85155;23;false;false;Singaporean;Art and sculptures aren’t the only treasures found in the National Gallery – on the 2nd floor is this restaurant from Violet Oon, Singapore’s own national treasure and one of its greatest ambassadors. The handsome, panelled 1920s-style dining room is an ideal backdrop to the cooking which, through its spicing, contrasting textures and enticing aromas, showcases Singapore’s unique culinary heritage. This is a restaurant with genuine charm.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12661;Luke's (Gemmill Lane);;Singapore;22 Gemmill Lane, 069257, Singapore;1.282271;103.8472284;96;true;false;Steakhouse;A favourite with local office workers, this steakhouse and oyster bar, run by a U.S. national, bustles with patrons all day long and is ideal for power lunches or after-work cocktails. It has acquired a faithful crowd of regulars thanks to high-quality food and friendly, slick service. Expect to see U.S. classics on the menu, such as New England clam chowder and Maryland crab cake. The generous portions make it a great venue for get-togethers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12662;Mustard;;Singapore;32 Race Course Road, 218552, Singapore;1.307995;103.850682;27;true;true;Indian;This halal restaurant specialising in Bengali and Punjabi cuisines is christened Mustard because the spice is used extensively in both cuisines. For instance, mustard oil is often used in place of coconut oil in Bengali cooking. Try their maacher cutlet – deep-fried fish croquettes served with a house-made fermented mustard sauce called Kashundi, which tastes strong and spicy. All food is made to order, but is so worth the wait.;Air conditioning;[]
12663;Path;;Singapore;Marina Bay Financial Centre, Tower 3, #01–05/06, 12 Marina Boulevard, 018982, Singapore;1.27944;103.854436;78;true;false;Asian Contemporary;The place is popular with a business lunch clientele craving creative Asian fare underpinned by classic French techniques. Come evening, it turns into a romantic spot, serving a six- or eight-course dinner menu. The mildly hot crabmeat and tofu spread is the perfect accompaniment for the bread baked in the charcoal oven. The pork trotter wrapped in caul fat is doused in a sauce inspired by the Chinese classic of braised pork with pickled mustard greens.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12664;Huat Heng Fried Oyster;;Singapore;Whampoa Makan Place, #01-26, 90/91 Whampoa Drive 90, 320091, Singapore;1.3231563;103.8549835;29;true;false;Street Food;The oyster omelette is fried to order until the crust is nicely browned, while the oysters remain plump and juicy. The house-made chilli sauce elevates the dish considerably. Various portion sizes are available.;;[]
12665;Lor 9 Beef Kway Teow;;Singapore;237 Lorong 9 Geylang, 389296, Singapore;1.312193;103.8767;34;false;false;Street Food;Cantonese and Fujian dishes prepared with local ingredients are tweaked to cater to local tastes. The beef kway teow is the main event. Comfort-food classics such as coffee pork ribs and sambal sweet potato leaves are also excellent.;;[]
12666;Osteria Mozza;;Singapore;Hilton Orchard, Level 5, 333 Orchard Road, 238867, Singapore;1.3022687;103.8359587;20;true;true;Italian;After a hiatus, the first Asian outpost of celebrity chef Nancy Silverton’s famed establishment Osteria Mozza reopened, now in a modern, rustic setting with a lively and inviting vibe. The small lunch menu features antipasti, salads, pizza and house-made pasta. The dinner menu steps up a gear to include her signature mozzarella dishes and other Italian specialties. The impressive wine list covers 280 labels from different regions of Italy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12667;Putien (Kitchener Road);;Singapore;127 Kitchener Road, 208514, Singapore;1.3095414;103.8574032;55;true;false;Fujian;This first branch of the chain known for its friendly service opened in 2000. The menu showcases Fujian classics, with small plates and noodles being the highlights. Try the bian rou (Fujian wonton soup) – the translucent skin is made with pork pounded over 10,000 times into a paste. The lor mee, topped with an impressive array of seafood, is also popular. Don't miss the seasonal offerings, some using rare ingredients from the city of Putian.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
12668;Birds Of Paradise (Katong);;Singapore;#01-05, 63 East Coast Road, 428776, Singapore;1.3052429;103.9035725;66;true;false;Street Food;A mesmerising array of top-quality gelato and sorbet is served in house-made thyme-scented waffle cones. Sea salt hojicha, white chrysanthemum, and raspberry lychee are some of its outstanding offerings.;Air conditioning;[]
12669;San Shu Gong;;Singapore;#01-01,135 Geylang Road, 389226, Singapore;1.3111829;103.8739285;49;true;true;Teochew, Cantonese;The owner named the restaurant after her late father and serves Cantonese and Teochew cuisines – her father's favourites. The two chefs, each with over 30 years of professional experience, excel at seafood dishes that accentuate the natural umami of seasonal produce. Some specialities have to be pre-ordered, such as the steamed and chilled fourfinger threadfin with tender flesh and generous fish oil.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12670;Hock Lye Noodles House & Fishii Tales;;Singapore;20 Ghim Moh Road Market & Food Centre, #01-35, Blk 20, Ghim Moh Road, 270020, Singapore;1.3110846;103.7884261;76;false;true;Street Food;Popular dishes include Hock Lye's noodle soup and "dry" noodles with meatballs, fish balls, prawns or pork ribs. The hand-made fish balls and fish cakes are springy and flavoursome. Come early, as the meatballs tend to sell out.;;[]
12671;Zhang Ji Shanghai La Mian Xiao Long Bao;;Singapore;Alexandra Village Food Centre, #01-56, Blk 120 Bukit Merah Lane 1, 150120, Singapore;1.2859524;103.8042849;40;false;true;Street Food;Besides xiao long bao, this busy stall offers an array of Shanghainese food, such as pan fried dumplings, sour and spicy soup. Their pork and chives potstickers are filled to the brim and nicely browned on the bottom.;;[]
12672;Sushi Katori;;Singapore;#01-03, 21 Tanjong Pagar Road, 088444, Singapore;1.2795296;103.8441068;96;false;false;Sushi;Chef Katori has years of experience working in kaiseki and sushi restaurants in Japan and Singapore. His first venture focuses on Edomae sushi and features the freshest catch from Toyosu Market on sushi rice from Miyagi prefecture dressed in either of the two vinegar blends according to the variety of the fish. The signature abalone is cooked in liver sauce in a sizzling stone bowl which imparts appealing aroma. Nothing ends the meal better than well-made tamagoyaki.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12673;Fiamma;;Singapore;Capella Hotel, 1 The Knolls, Sentosa Island, 098297, Singapore;1.2494097;103.8242699;32;false;false;Italian;Eagerly anticipated by gourmets, this dining concept by the celebrated chef Mauro Colagreco opened in the ultra-luxury beach resort. The rustic chic room comes complete with an open kitchen, wood-fired oven and a terrace overlooking the pool and garden. The menu sees a good range of Italian classics, especially those from the South of the country. Start your meal with seabream carpaccio, followed by house-made pasta, and tiramisu for two to share.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12674;Yong Xiang Xing Tou Fu;;Singapore;People's Park Complex Food Centre, #01-1084, 32 New Market Road, 050032, Singapore;1.2851661;103.8425425;31;true;true;Street Food;There is only one thing on the menu – assorted tofu stew. Fish balls, tofu skin rolls, silken tofu and deep-fried tofu stuffed with minced fish are ladled into your bowl alongside a clear broth seasoned by scallion. Simply delicious.;Cash only;[]
12675;Sushi Sato;;Singapore;6B Dempsey Road, 247662, Singapore;1.304985;103.808433;79;false;false;Sushi;The duo of chefs chose to open this sushi-ya in serene surroundings away from the busy CBD. In the same vein, the wood-rich interior is minimal and Zen-inspired. All the ingredients are shipped from Japan four times a week for peak freshness. Three seasonal menus are available and attention to detail is visible at every level – Yamagata rice is dressed in a blend of three red vinegars for the perfect tartness that complements oily fish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12677;Gemma;;Singapore;National Gallery, #05-03, 1 St. Andrew's Road, 178957, Singapore;1.28966;103.85171;58;false;true;Steakhouse;The bold decor with a bright red couch, marble wall panels and gold columns doesn't outshine the smoky aromas from the charcoal grill. The kitchen is helmed by an Italian chef, so while most of the beef is imported from Australia, Italian influences abound in every course – the house-made pasta in particular is worth trying. The steaks and accompaniments are cooked to perfection. Have a nightcap on the rooftop patio commanding gorgeous views.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12678;Redhill Pork Porridge;;Singapore;Redhill Market, #01-90, 85 Redhill Lane, 150085, Singapore;1.2872772;103.8180805;27;false;true;Street Food;The porridge may not look exciting but the creamy base is loaded with meaty flavour. Pad it out with sliced pork, pork meatballs, pork liver or deep-fried dough sticks. Crack in a raw egg and stir it into wispy ribbons. Open from 6am while stocks lasts.;Cash only;[]
12679;Ye Tang;;Singapore;Beauty World Food Centre #04-26, 144 Upper Bukit Timah Road, 588177, Singapore;1.3424073;103.776255;22;true;true;Street Food;The owner learned to make cendol in Malacca, and his rice flour jelly worms – made on the spot – are softer than most. On top of the classic cendol shaved ice, add red kidney beans, palm seeds, corn kernels or durian.;Cash only;[]
12680;Yong Kee Claypot Bak Kut Teh;;Singapore;Taman Jurong Market & Food Centre, #02-78, 3 Yung Sheng Road, Jurong West, 618499, Singapore;1.3345193;103.7214706;69;true;false;Street Food;Pork rib soup is served in a claypot alongside other condiments, such as peppercorns. The Chinese herbal version strikes a fine balance, with distinctive yet not overpowering herbal flavours. Other claypot soups are also available.;Cash only;[]
12681;Sushi Yuki;;Singapore;Wilkie Edge, #01-23/24, 8 Wilkie Road, 228095, Singapore;1.30206;103.84908;60;false;true;Sushi;After helming a renowned sushiya in Singapore for 10 years, Chef Yukinori Kawakami brings the experience to this new venture in 2023. Three omakase menus are offered at lunch and dinner, featuring fish flown in from Japan four times a week. Sushi rice from Yamagata Prefecture is dressed in a blend of two vinegars for a delicate taste that accentuates the fish’s natural flavours. With only 13 counter seats and two private rooms, reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12682;Ron Sheng Fish Head Bee Hoon;;Singapore;Yuhua Village Market and Food Centre, #01-44, Blk 254, Jurong East Street 24, 600254, Singapore;1.3435581;103.7374158;15;true;true;Street Food;Crispy fried fish head and fish meat with bee hoon. The broth infused with milk is smooth and sweet.;Cash only;[]
12683;Lor Mee 178;;Singapore;Tiong Bahru Market, #02-23, 30 Seng Poh Road, 168898, Singapore;1.2846377;103.8326;88;true;false;Street Food;Lor mee in robust stock offers a rich taste with garlic and chillies. You should also try the fish nuggets.;;[]
12684;Jiang-Nan Chun;;Singapore;Four Seasons Hotel, Level 2, 190 Orchard Boulevard, 248646, Singapore;1.304937;103.8288;67;true;false;Cantonese;This exquisite space, reached via a marble staircase, is warm and welcoming, with heavy leather chairs that are especially comfortable. The kitchen team excels in barbecue meats, double-boiled soups and seafood dishes that use the freshest ingredients of the best quality. Try wok-fried Australian beef tenderloin with portobello mushrooms. Set menus are a great way to sample the popular hits all at once.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12685;Bedok Chwee Kueh;;Singapore;Bedok Interchange Hawker Centre, #01-19, 208 New Upper Changi Road, 460208, Singapore;1.3247792;103.9305925;68;false;false;Street Food;The freshly steamed chwee kueh rice cakes are soft and velvety and the sauce on top made with preserved radish, scallion, dried shrimps and chilli is simply irresistible. May be closed without prior notice.;;[]
12686;Hoe Kee Kitchen;;Singapore;Jurong West 505 Market & Food Centre, #01-39, Blk 505, Jurong West Street 52, 640505, Singapore;1.3499648;103.7184122;64;false;false;Street Food;Steamed chicken rice with tender meat and flavourful rice is popular. Other options include reasonably priced char siew and roasted pork rice.;Cash only;[]
12687;Xing Yun Hainanese Boneless Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Yuhua Market & Hawker Centre, #01-202, Blk 347, Jurong East Avenue 1, Jurong East, 600347, Singapore;1.3452585;103.7313252;48;false;true;Street Food;(The hawker center it locates is temporarily closed.) Its signature Hainanese boneless chicken rice is garnished with pineapple, tomato and cucumber. Dip the juicy, silky chicken in the briny-sweet chilli and ginger sauce before savouring it with the aromatic rice.;;[]
12689;Yuan Chun Famous Lor Mee;;Singapore;Amoy Street Food Centre, #02-80, 7 Maxwell Road, 069111, Singapore;1.279623;103.8466196;24;false;false;Street Food;Lor mee here can be topped with fried fish cake, fried chicken, sliced fish or braised pork belly. The dark gravy boasts depth thanks to spices and prolonged simmering. Jazz it up further with chilli and cilantro.;Cash only;[]
12690;Sheng Seng Fried Prawn Noodle;;Singapore;Pek Kio Market & Food Centre, #01-40, 41 Cambridge Road, 210041, Singapore;1.3162872;103.8499262;47;true;true;Street Food;It's all about rice vermicelli and egg noodles stir-fried with eggs and seafood. Homemade chili sauce enriches the flavour.;;[]
12693;Gaig;;Singapore;#01-01, 16 Stanley Street, 068735, Singapore;1.2807179;103.8482116;27;true;false;Spanish;After renovation, this relaxed and friendly restaurant run by the same family as its namesake in Barcelona has doubled in size. Catalan classics like the cannelloni are prepared the same way as they were back in the 19th century, and their tapas portion sizes allow diners to sample a wider variety. Recommendations include lamb shoulder with trinxat and mint pesto. The wine list has a great Spanish selection that’s available at a reasonable price.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12694;Claudine;;Singapore;39C Harding Road, 249541, Singapore;1.3048538;103.8134286;16;true;false;French;From chef Julien Royer of Odette fame comes a classic French brasserie, which he named after his mother. It’s housed in a lovely 1930s converted chapel, with an open kitchen at one end and a bar at the other. Those with a fondness for comforting French classics will find the rollcall of favourites very appealing, from onion soup to vol-au-vents and baba au rhum. If you’re willing to share, then go for the bouillabaisse or the pepper steak flambéed at your table.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
12695;Min Jiang at Dempsey;;Singapore;7A & 7B Dempsey Road, 249684, Singapore;1.3049401;103.8083222;32;true;false;Cantonese, Sichuan;Amidst lush greenery, the one-storey colonial structure houses an airy dining room done up in a yellow, gold and green palette, boasting floor-to-ceiling windows, wood details and rattan furniture. The menu is Cantonese and Sichuanese with a touch of finesse and subtlety. Must-try items include turbot fish two ways, Beijing duck grilled in a wood-fire oven and various dim sum. There are also many good choices for vegetarians.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12696;Bar-Roque Grill;;Singapore;165 Tanjong Pagar Road, 088539, Singapore;1.2755732;103.843511;63;true;true;European;The Alsace-born chef takes diners on a culinary journey to his homeland with authentic regional specialties such as choucroute garnie and tarte flambée aux escargots. International dishes are also popular, like Malaysian rotisserie free-range chicken and a selection of beefsteaks dry aged in-house and chargrilled to perfection. Service is attentive and helpful. Start or end the night with a drink on the terrace or at the bar.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12698;Cure;;Singapore;21 Keong Saik Road, 089128, Singapore;1.2798686;103.841484;50;false;false;European Contemporary;Inspired by bistro culture, chef-owner Walsh has devised a Nua Irish tasting menu that riffs on his Celtic roots and draws on local influences. The menu ranges from absolutely purist takes on the classics to small plates with playful touches. To a soundtrack of Irish rock, learn about exceptional homegrown ingredients from the map on the table, as you indulge in dishes informed by the history and wisdom of the Emerald Isle.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12700;Tiong Bahru Lien Fa Shui Jing Pau;;Singapore;Alexandra Village Food Centre, #01-10, Blk 120 Bukit Merah Lane 1, 150120, Singapore;1.284671;103.8326;35;false;true;Street Food;The teochew dumplings are stuffed with jicama for a lovely crunch, while chopped dried shrimps lend briny umami. Try them with the home-made chilli sauce. Dumplings with red bean or taro paste filling are available after 1pm.;;[]
12701;Chung Cheng;;Singapore;Golden Mile Food Centre, #01-59, 505 Beach Road, 199583, Singapore;1.3033256;103.8639165;77;true;false;Street Food;Three options feature on the menu of this stall – chilli mee, prawn mee and laksa. Go for chilli mee: yellow egg noodles topped with tangy chilli sauce, pork ribs, prawns, hard-boiled egg, fish cake and tofu puffs.;;[]
12702;Hokkien Street Bak Kut Teh;;Singapore;Hong Lim Market and Food Centre, #01-66, Blk 531A, Upper Cross Street, 051531, Singapore;1.2854726;103.84592;15;false;false;Street Food;The dark amber coloured bak kut teh from this stall is loaded in herbal goodness. Pair with pork knuckle, pork intestines, steamed fish, pork tail, pork kidney or pork liver on the side, as you prefer.;;[]
12703;Boon Tong Kee Kway Chap‧Braised Duck;;Singapore;Zion Riverside Food Centre, #024, 70 Zion Road, 247792, Singapore;1.2924249;103.8311181;23;false;false;Street Food;Boon Tong Kee prides itself on its spiced soy marinade made with aromatic Chinese herbs. With its springy skin and tasty meat, the signature braised duck is a hit. The braised pork trotter and taro rice are also popular.;;[]
12704;Ushidoki Wagyu Kaiseki;;Singapore;#01-01, 57 Tras Street, 078996, Singapore;1.2780323;103.8444829;99;true;false;Japanese;This chef puts a new spin on classic kaiseki with two Wagyu set menus that honour a head-to-tail concept. He chooses Ozaki beef from Miyazaki, otherwise unavailable in Singapore, for its gutsy flavour. Various cuts from 32- to 36-month-old cattle are prepared in a myriad of ways to highlight their textures and umami. Most of the other ingredients are flown in from Japan to ensure authenticity. There is also an á la carte menu for add-on courses.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
12706;Hock Seng Choon Fish Ball Kway Teow Mee;;Singapore;Pasar 16@Bedok (Bedok South Food Centre), #01-50, 16 Bedok South Road, 460016, Singapore;1.3203827;103.9351611;79;true;true;Street Food;Fish balls are tender and rich. The al dente noodles marry well with the fresh broth.;;[]
12707;Gunther's;;Singapore;#01-03, 36 Purvis Street, 188613, Singapore;1.296602;103.8549;57;true;false;French Contemporary;This owner-chef worked in some famous restaurants in his native Belgium and France before coming to Singapore. He describes his cooking as "simple, honest and down-to-earth", though a number of sumptuous dishes are to be had. Try his cold angel hair with a 6g quenelle of Oscietra caviar – one of his proudest creations, served since 2005. In addition to the timeless classics, check out seasonal offerings such as white asparagus.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12708;Fleur de Sel;;Singapore;#01-01, 64 Tras Street, 079003, Singapore;1.2777778;103.84417;75;false;false;French;In this stylish eatery with a bar and an open kitchen, you’ll find the eponymous artisanal French salt on each table – but you won’t need it thanks to the owner-chef’s spot-on sense of seasoning. At this ‘bistro de luxe’ he delivers classical French cuisine with a light, modern spin – making it easy to save room for his signature Baba. Two set menus - we recommend the tasting menu for a global experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12709;Fu He Turtle Soup;;Singapore;Berseh Food Centre, #02-40, 166 Jalan Besar, 208877, Singapore;1.3075565;103.8568638;67;true;false;Street Food;There is an array of Cantonese soups to choose from here. The eponymous soft-shelled turtle soup emits rich herbal aromas, served with plain steamed rice or taro rice.;Cash only;[]
12710;Come Daily Fried Hokkien Prawn Mee;;Singapore;127 Toa Payoh West Market & Food Centre, #02-27, Blk 127, Lorong 1 Toa Payoh, 310127, Singapore;1.3381846;103.8447186;58;false;false;Street Food;The signature Hokkien prawn mee is made with yellow egg noodles, rice vermicelli and squid, topped with fried crispy lard that adds an extra layer of texture and flavours.;;[]
12711;Nyonya Chendol;;Singapore;Chong Pang Market and Food Centre, #01-162, 105 Yishun Ring Road, 760105, Singapore;1.4318534;103.8279828;100;true;false;Street Food;The stall specialises in the classic iced dessert chendol. Pandan-flavoured flour jelly, coconut milk and palm sugar syrup impart the right level of sweetness. Extra toppings like red beans or durian are available.;;[]
12712;Jiao Cai Seafood;;Singapore;Yishun Park Hawker Centre, #01-39, 51 Yishun Avenue 11, 768867, Singapore;1.4251958;103.8446508;91;false;true;Street Food;Cooked-to-order seafood dishes. Signature sambal stingray is spicy and delicious.;Cash only;[]
12713;Zheng Zhi Wen Ji Pig's Organ Soup;;Singapore;Clementi 448 Food Centre, #01-26, 448 Clementi Ave 3, 120448, Singapore;1.313468;103.76461;82;false;true;Street Food;As well as pork offal, the menu features marinated pork trotter, kway chap and bak kut teh. But the noodle soup with pork liver and kidney stands out – the offal is cooked perfectly and the broth loaded with herbal aromas.;Cash only;[]
12714;Shang Palace;;Singapore;Shangri-La Hotel, Lobby Level, 22 Orange Grove Road, 258350, Singapore;1.310968;103.8264;44;false;true;Cantonese;With a graceful dining room reminiscent of a Chinese garden, Shang Palace serves an extensive menu dominated by old-time Cantonese classics that are hard to find elsewhere, such as grilled chicken liver and pork fat skewers, and deep-fried pork fat medallions stuffed with crabmeat. Order the deep-fried whole boneless chicken stuffed with glutinous rice one day ahead and ask the servers about the slow-boiled soups that exude rich deep flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12715;Ce Soir;;Singapore;#01-03, 5B Portsdown Road, 139311, Singapore;1.2942933;103.7960641;85;true;true;European Contemporary;Ce Soir wins kudos not only for its impossibly romantic floral theme and everything botanical, but also because of its deftly crafted French fare with strong Asian notes. Every course of both the lunch set and dinner tasting menus is visually stunning: like a garden on a plate, even the flowers are edible. The seafood stands out in particular. Everything down to the bread and the mignardises are made from scratch in-house.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12716;Heng Long BBQ Chicken Rice;;Singapore;Mei Ling Market & Food Centre, #02-42, 159 Mei Chin Road, 140159, Singapore;1.2932654;103.8028365;18;true;false;Street Food;The BBQ chicken rice is an absolute must, but the honey-glazed char siew and roast pork are also popular. Or opt for their brine-poached chicken – succulent, perfectly seasoned and with a wonderful velvety texture.;Cash only;[]
12717;Rempapa;;Singapore;Park Place Residences at PLQ, #01-01/02/03, 2 Paya Lebar Road, 409053, Singapore;1.3169118;103.8932424;45;false;false;Singaporean;In a smart, casual room with tan banquettes, powder blue chairs and terrazzo tiled floor, Damian D’Silva, a respected judge from the Singaporean edition of a popular cooking show, champions a novel cuisine that crosses boundaries among Chinese, Peranakan, Eurasian, Indian and Malay cooking. Hearty dishes sit comfortably next to century-old recipes, all prepared with shrewd judgment, and the right amount of oomph. Baca Assam (beef cheek) is unmissable.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12718;R&B Express;;Singapore;Newton Food Centre, #01-76, 500 Clemenceau Avenue North, 229495, Singapore;1.3122041;103.8396372;47;false;true;Street Food;Chicken wings grilled with charcoal are crispy and juicy while the spicy sauce adds to the flavour. Also try satay, traditional popiah and kueh pie tee.;;[]
12719;Cheng Heng Kway Chap and Braised Duck Rice;;Singapore;Holland Drive Market & Food Centre, #02-05, 44 Holland Drive, 270044, Singapore;1.3081707;103.7924893;21;true;true;Street Food;The name reveals the two signature dishes – the braised duck is tender, has robust flavours and is accompanied by a perfectly seasoned, spiced soy marinade. The kway (rice noodles) are silky smooth and the soup is moreish.;;[]
12720;Tambuah Mas (Orchard);;Singapore;Paragon, #B1-44, 290 Orchard Road, 238859, Singapore;1.3036065;103.8349852;36;false;false;Indonesian;Since 1981, the Indonesian chefs at Tambuah Mas have been making authentic home-style dishes from Padang, Sulawesi and Java. Family recipes with delicate blends of spices and precise preparations are closely guarded secrets, passed down over generations. The signature tahu telor (deep-fried egg-coated tofu cubes in a dark sweet sauce) boasts crispy skin and perfect briny-sweetness. Always round off a meal here with a cendol.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12721;Hokkien Man Hokkien Mee;;Singapore;Blk 19, Toa Payoh 7, #01-264, Kim Keat Palm, 310019, Singapore;1.3352503;103.8565087;84;false;false;Street Food;As its name suggests, this stall specialises in Hokkien fried noodles in a garlicky broth made with prawn heads. Besides the typical toppings of prawns and squid, you may order others, like egg or abalone, at an additional cost.;Cash only;[]
12722;Unforgettable Carrot Cake;;Singapore;115 Bukit Merah View Market & Hawker Centre, #01-30, Blk 115 Bukit Merah View, 151115, Singapore;1.2856834;103.8222026;95;false;false;Street Food;Not to be confused with the western sweet of the same name, carrot cake here is savoury, made with radish and stir-fried in seasoning. Opt for the dark version coated in egg, and tossed in sticky, caramelised dark soy sauce.;Cash only;[]
12723;La D'Oro;;Singapore;Mandarin Gallery, #01-16/17, 333A Orchard Road, 238897, Singapore;1.30216;103.83648;49;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Rebranded in 2023, La D’oro now offers a single season-driven omakase menu that changes every two months. Hailing from Tokyo, Japan, the owner-chef Sasaki honed his skills in Italy. His ambitious, kappo-style cooking effortlessly blends Italian traditions with Japanese influences, delivering complex, original creations underpinned by modern techniques. Fresh ingredients flown in from Japan and Italy impart distinctive flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12724;Wakuda;;Singapore;Marina Bay Sands Hotel, Tower 2, Lobby, 10 Bayfront Avenue, 018972, Singapore;1.283879;103.8606805;83;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;This more accessible spinoff of its upscale sister Waku Ghin is the brainchild of the eponymous chef Tetsuya Wakuda. All rooms feature the traditional Japanese craft of wood joinery prominently, alongside soft lighting, tan leather chairs and banquettes. The menu offers an array of modern Japanese classics made with quality ingredients sourced globally. Adding original cocktails and a buzzy vibe to the equation, Wakuda guarantees a fun night out.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12725;Lolla;;Singapore;22 Ann Siang Road, 069702, Singapore;1.2809936;103.845712;34;true;false;European Contemporary;The turquoise tiled façade sets nicely against the faux-industrial interior. Seasonal Mediterranean dishes in generous portions for sharing are served by the chefs themselves. Flavours are bold and hearty, with occasional Asian touches. Ask for counter seats to see the chefs in action, or sit at the communal table in the basement which can be reserved for private parties. Only seven- or nine-course tasting menus are served on Friday and Saturday nights.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12726;Springleaf Prata Place (Spring Leaf Garden);;Singapore;1 Thong Soon Avenue, 787431, Singapore;1.3971;103.81896;47;false;true;Street Food;The birthplace of Singapore’s popular prata chain serves 20 different variations with sweet or savoury fillings. But even the basic egg prata tastes great with a crisp crust and fluffy centre - perfect for any curry in any meal.;;[]
12727;Spago Dining Room;;Singapore;Marina Bay Sands Hotel, Tower 2, Sands SkyPark, Level 57, 10 Bayfront Avenue, 018956, Singapore;1.2834229;103.8604919;17;true;false;Californian, Asian Contemporary;Wolfgang Puck’s fresh, revitalising cuisine may have been born in Beverly Hills, but its second home atop Marina Bay Sands has proven an equally good fit. The menu is an appealing blend of American, Asian and European influences, with dishes ranging from honey miso broiled black cod to a falafel burger with roasted capsicum. The poolside terrace may provide great views, but the elegant dining room comes with a cooling serenity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12728;Jian Bo Shui Kueh;;Singapore;Tiong Bahru Market, #02-05, 30 Seng Poh Road, 168898, Singapore;1.2846506;103.83259;30;true;true;Street Food;Shui kueh is quintessential local street food: white rice cake with salted diced radish and a secret tung tsai sauce, packed with oomph. The house-made sambal, oozing in dried shrimp flavour, is perfect with the rice cake.;;[]
12729;Hong Peng La Mian Xiao Long Bao;;Singapore;People's Park Complex Food Centre, #01-1064, 32 New Market Road, 050032, Singapore;1.2852868;103.8425969;34;false;true;Street Food;Offers xiao long bao, dumplings and hand-pulled noodles.;;[]
12730;Yan Ting;;Singapore;The St. Regis Hotel, Level 1U, 29 Tanglin Road, 247911, Singapore;1.305914;103.8259;50;false;false;Cantonese;Since the name translates as ‘Banquet Court’, it's no surprise to find a very comfortable space, ideal for impressing visitors and friends. The head chef has extensive experience when it comes to traditional dishes, especially Cantonese barbecue and double-boiled soups. Try his crispy roast pork belly for the ultimate indulgence. He's also an expert at preparing live fish – choose from 11 cooking styles. At lunch, don't miss his Hong Kong-style dim sum.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12731;Mustard Seed;;Singapore;75 Brighton Crescent, 559216, Singapore;1.3630824;103.8711608;80;true;false;Singaporean;Before you can experience the head chef’s unique take on Singaporean-Japanese fusion cooking, you have to book a table online months ahead. Punctuality is key as the food is only served after all the guests are seated at 7.30pm sharp. The 8-course omakase-style menu changes every two months, reinventing national dishes like rojak and laksa with clever Japanese twists. Counter seats overlooking the open kitchen let diners see the magic first hand.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
12732;Buko Nero;;Singapore;126 Tanjong Pagar Road, 088534, Singapore;1.277667;103.84357;27;true;false;Italian;Diners flock to this small neighbourhood joint and it’s easy to understand why: the bubbly, charming hostess works seamlessly with her husband chef from Veneto, who in turn delivers simple, delicious Italian fare with subtle Asian twists. Try his tau kwa tower – an appetising mix of sautéed Italian-style greens and Singaporean dried tofu salad in a tangy Asian dressing. Hand-made pasta is another highlight, as are the weekly specials.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12733;Chilli Padi (Joo Chiat);;Singapore;#01-03, 11 Joo Chiat Place, 427744, Singapore;1.3133199;103.9001;27;true;false;Peranakan;A stroll around Joo Chiat is made all the more enjoyable by making a pitstop here, as it’s a great place to share a host of authentic Peranakan dishes. The Nonya specialities include popiah, kueh pai ti, creamy and delicious curry chicken, and chap chye. Many of the dishes come in three sizes but prices are so good that over-ordering is easy and excusable. The batik fabric covering the tables adds some colour to this simple restaurant.;Air conditioning;[]
12734;Yì By Jereme Leung;;Singapore;Raffles Arcade, #03-02, 328 North Bridge Road, 188719, Singapore;1.295585;103.8540095;45;false;false;Chinese Contemporary;The chef honed his remarkable skills while working in China for many years. He returned to Singapore and opened Yi – the Chinese word for art and craftsmanship, hence the fancy dining room adorned in exquisite paper art and the food that reflects eclectic influences from all over China. Steamed free range chicken in herbal broth impresses by its umami and mild herbal aftertaste. Also check out the seasonal menu bursting with creative twists.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12736;Tunglok Heen;;Singapore;Hotel Michael, #02-142/143, Resorts World Sentosa, 26 Sentosa Gateway, 098138, Singapore;1.2548974;103.820172;45;false;true;Cantonese;Clever lighting, dark wood and shades of red lend this modern Chinese restaurant a slick, stylish feel. Amidst traditional recipes, novel dishes also feature on the menu. Either way, the food is always meticulously plated. Don’t miss the fish bone and fish maw soup, double-boiled with chicken and pork for six hours. Chilli crab served in a casserole boasts firm, flavoursome meat. Order deep-fried buns to mop up the knockout sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12737;Straits Chinese (Cecil Street);;Singapore;Keck Seng Tower, #B1-01, 133 Cecil Street, 069535, Singapore;1.2804274;103.8488583;24;true;false;Peranakan;The owner’s family opened Singapore’s first Peranakan restaurant in 1953 – this branch has been in the CBD since 2011. Ornaments and wooden furniture lend a Chinese aesthetic. The versatile menu features dishes made with local produce and lots of spices and herbs, all prepared using traditional Chinese cooking methods. Dishes to try include ayam buah keluak (chicken with local nuts) and ikan assam nanas pedas (sweet and sour fish).;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12738;Wah Lok;;Singapore;Carlton Hotel, Level 2, 76 Bras Basah Road, 189558, Singapore;1.295806;103.8523;82;false;false;Cantonese;A loyal clientele has made this comfortable, classically decorated Cantonese restaurant their own. The chef was born in Guangzhou but really developed his culinary skills and honed his craft in Hong Kong. His Cantonese dishes range from banquet delicacies like abalone and bird’s nest soup to seafood dishes such as steamed fish. There are also Cantonese roast meats, claypot dishes and home-style items like steamed minced pork with salted fish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12739;Ghim Moh Chwee Kueh;;Singapore;20 Ghim Moh Road Market & Food Centre, #01-54, Blk 20, Ghim Moh Road, 270020, Singapore;1.3110349;103.7882915;54;true;true;Street Food;This stall founded in 1959 is a household name! Its lovingly hand-made chwee kueh – toothsome rice cakes topped with dried radish and mildly spicy sambal – are hugely popular among locals. Minimum order of four pieces.;;[]
12740;Koka Wanton Noodles;;Singapore;North Bridge Road Market & Food Centre, #01-99, 861 North Bridge Road, 198783, Singapore;1.3058048;103.8636367;92;false;true;Street Food;Barbecue pork with wonton noodles is the signature. Deep-fried pork skin and chillies enrich the flavour.;;[]
12741;Ah Heng Duck Rice;;Singapore;Hong Lim Market and Food Centre, #02-64, Blk 531A, Upper Cross Street, 051531, Singapore;1.2851653;103.8457572;90;false;false;Street Food;The taste of duck meat blends with the spice marinade, each boasting a rich flavour. Snacks like duck liver and dried tofu are also offered.;;[]
12742;Mellben Seafood (Ang Mo Kio);;Singapore;Block 232, #01-1222, Ang Mo Kio Avenue 3, 560232, Singapore;1.36839;103.83717;23;true;false;Seafood;It may not be in the most convenient location but that doesn’t deter the crowds from descending on this open-air space. Nearly everyone is here for one thing: crab. The chef has 15 different ways to cook them, from black pepper crab to creamy butter crab and that, of course, includes the classic chilli crab. There’s also live seafood available, along with cze char dishes – and the claypot bee hoon soup is delicious.;;[]
12743;Maxwell Fuzhou Oyster Cake;;Singapore;Maxwell Food Centre, #01-05, 1 Kadayanallur Street, 069184, Singapore;1.28033;103.84473;44;false;true;Street Food;The second-generation owner still fries oyster cakes à la minute as her mother did in the 1960s. They may be darker than usual, but the minced pork, oysters, prawns and coriander are still soft and juicy under the crispy crust.;;[]
12744;Hill Street Fried Kway Teow;;Singapore;Pasar 16@Bedok (Bedok South Food Centre), #01-41, 16 Bedok South Road, 460016, Singapore;1.3203783;103.9355949;91;true;false;Street Food;This stall serves a single dish that is drop-dead perfect every time. Full-bodied wok hei, irresistible aromas and generous toppings like cockles, Chinese sausage, chives and bean sprouts justify the often hour-long wait.;;[]
12745;Keng Eng Kee (Bukit Merah);;Singapore;Blk 124, #01-136, Bukit Merah Lane 1, 150124, Singapore;1.2857642;103.8037043;77;true;true;Singaporean;This popular cze char restaurant may not be the most conveniently placed, but it does some great dishes, like fried salted egg crab, coffee pork ribs and claypot duck with sea cucumber. The setting and environment are not unlike a hawker centre, although there is a smaller inside area that’s air-conditioned. It provides mostly Hainanese cuisine, along with some Cantonese dishes – the stir-fries are particularly delicious.;Wheelchair access;[]
12746;Boon Tong Kee (Balestier Road);;Singapore;399, 401, 403 Balestier Road, 329801, Singapore;1.3255796;103.8495;53;false;false;Singaporean;You won’t have any trouble finding this enduringly popular restaurant – its colourful neon sign will guide you in from afar. The group may have expanded over the years but this is the original branch, opened in 1983. Their signature boiled chicken is still the biggest draw and can be ordered in three different sizes, but those looking for a full zi char feast won’t be disappointed. Avoid peak times if you’re not prepared to queue.;Air conditioning;[]
12747;Nicolas;;Singapore;10 Teck Lim Road, 088386, Singapore;1.280254;103.8420413;24;false;false;French;The eponymous French chef has been quietly going about his business in this comfy and intimate little gem for some years now. Choose the Tasting menu to best experience his cooking, underpinned by classical French techniques and made with top-quality ingredients, like langoustines from New Zealand and pigeon from Brittany. Diners can watch the chefs at work in the kitchen through the glass wall. Don’t forget to check out the wine collection in the small walk-in cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
12748;Tambi;;Singapore;47 Amoy Street, 069873, Singapore;1.280424;103.846898;66;true;false;Innovative;Tambi is a collaborative effort by chef-owners Sun Kim, of Meta fame, and Mano Thevar, who helms Thevar, an innovative restaurant featuring the rare mix of Korean and Indian food. The menu is short but sweet, with creative combinations such as oxtail bone marrow murtabak with kimchi, and a fusion take on Korean cold spicy noodles known as "Tambi's Bibimmyeon". The young kitchen team melds Indian spices and Korean produce to great effect.;Air conditioning;[]
12749;Torno Subito;;Singapore;#01-02, 26 Dempsey Road, 249686, Singapore;1.305934;103.8113126;87;true;true;Italian;A nod to the heyday of Italian cinema, the interior takes you back to the Adriatic Riviera circa 1960s. The red-yellow-blue colour scheme is carried through from the walls to the tableware. The concept by celebrity chef Massimo Bottura involves whimsically and creatively harnessing Italian produce in signature dishes like artisan tortellini in a silky sauce made with parmigiano reggiano aged for 36 months. Stone-baked pizzas are delicious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12750;Béni;;Singapore;Mandarin Gallery, #02-37, 333A Orchard Road, 238897, Singapore;1.301757;103.83692;26;false;false;French Contemporary;The small, elegant restaurant boasts a minimalist décor, so as to keep the spotlight on its exquisite French cooking with a Japanese twist. Top-quality ingredients from France and Japan are transformed here, thanks to well-honed skills and meticulous attention to detail. The set menus change according to the availability of ingredients, such as seafood dishes are adapted to the catch of the day. Check with the sommelier for unusual choices not shown on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12751;Shanyuan Teochew Kway Teow Mian;;Singapore;North Bridge Road Market & Food Centre, #01-95, 861 North Bridge Road, 198783, Singapore;1.3058048;103.8636367;40;false;true;Street Food;Get your noodle fix 24/7 at this popular stall. With myriad made-to-order options on the menu – from fish dumplings and minced pork noodles to mee tai mak and kway teow noodle soup – you're spoiled for choice.;Cash only;[]
12752;Butcher's Block;;Singapore;Raffles Arcade, #02-02, 328 North Bridge Road, 188719, Singapore;1.2953284;103.8538526;77;true;false;Meats and Grills;Wood-fire cooking is the speciality of this dark and handsome restaurant within Raffles hotel. Head straight to the tasting menu if you want to experience a variety of top-quality fish and meat dishes, all expertly prepared using American wood and supplemented with Asian flavours. The moodily lit room ensures your gaze never wanders too far from the open kitchen. A restaurant to appeal to the hunter-gatherer in all of us.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
12753;Sushi Masaaki;;Singapore;South Beach Avenue, #B1-17, 26 Beach Road, 189768, Singapore;1.2939051;103.855084;84;true;false;Sushi;This omakase sushiya with only 12 seats boasts a counter crafted from a 250-year-old hinoki tree. In stark contrast, the lively lounge for tea and dessert is clad in wallpaper with dancing cranes on a pink background. The freshest fish is creatively combined with other ingredients to great effects while the well thought-out, sometimes unorthodox, seasoning on the sushi makes the experience unique. Friendly chefs are happy to interact with diners.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12754;Majestic;;Singapore;Marina One, The Heart (East Tower) #04-01, 5 Straits View, 018935, Singapore;1.2780668;103.8528577;95;true;true;Cantonese;Laid out beneath a glass roof, the airy dining area overlooks a garden. The food, which draws on modern techniques and time-honoured traditions, is exquisite in both taste and appearance. The claypot chicken with glutinous rice wine, ginger and wood ear fungus boasts silky, free-range meat and spellbinding aromas. The business clientele can opt for items in individual servings. Booking a week ahead recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12755;Revolver;;Singapore;56 Tras Street, 078997, Singapore;1.2781226;103.8442476;85;false;true;Indian;Its name is a pun on how cooking revolves around the charcoal grill, brazier and tandoor. Whether you sit at the counter or in a booth, the chefs put on a show that is visible from all seats. Three tasting menus and a vegetarian menu are offered.  Dishes are rooted in different regions of India, but are reimagined and reborn over coals and fire. The distinctive smoky flavour  and layering of spices works magic, resulting in a delicate balance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12756;Hup Kee Teochew Fishball Mee;;Singapore;Mei Ling Market & Food Centre, #02-38, 159 Mei Chin Road, 140159, Singapore;1.2932654;103.8028365;21;true;true;Street Food;This popular stall is always busy, even at off-peak times. There are different noodles to choose from, and these are topped with tasty fish balls, pork balls and fried fish cakes. A little of the hot sauce goes a long way!;Cash only;[]
12757;Kang's Wanton Noodle;;Singapore;Zion Riverside Food Centre, #06, 70 Zion Road, 247792, Singapore;1.29236;103.83122;83;false;false;Street Food;Alongside wanton or dumpling noodle soup, this stall serves deep-fried wanton and char siew. The springy noodles are best enjoyed with a dollop of chilli sauce, while the wantons encase a tasty filling in their paper-thin skin.;Cash only;[]
12758;Whampoa Soya Bean & Grass Jelly Drinks;;Singapore;Whampoa Makan Place, #01-52, 90/91 Whampoa Drive 91, 320091, Singapore;1.3228091;103.8551585;38;false;true;Street Food;Tofu pudding is freshly made on the spot – just add toppings such as grass jelly, red beans or lotus seeds. Or try their drinkable versions, in which the soybean flavour is complemented by the velvety texture of a smoothie.;;[]
12759;Tow Kwar Pop;;Singapore;Tiong Bahru Market, #02-06, 30 Seng Poh Road, 168898, Singapore;1.2846506;103.83259;33;true;true;Street Food;Here, the rojak is made with sliced cucumber, apple and bean sprouts, topped with either crispy tofu puffs or fried dough sticks. The syrupy dressing is rich and tangy, and the ground peanuts give the salad a lovely crunch.;Cash only;[]
12760;Brasserie Astoria;;Singapore;Victoria Concert Hall, #01-01, 11 Empress Place, 179558, Singapore;1.28801;103.85171;38;true;false;European Contemporary;An outpost of its namesake in Stockholm, this is the brainchild of the Swedish owner-chef Björn Frantzén. Nestled in the historical Victoria Concert Hall (1800s), its retro glamour complements the chef's new spin on brasserie classics, some with trolley or tableside service. Try the råraka, a Swedish potato cake topped with vendace roe, crème fraîche, chives and red onion. Toast Astoria with prawn, king crab and wasabi aioli is also unmissable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
12762;Hana Sushi;Poland;Krakow;ul. Kupa 12, Krakow, 31 057, Poland;50.0518487;19.9461693;58;false;true;Japanese, Korean;Thanks to its quality produce prepared with precision, this simple Japanese-inspired restaurant has made a real impact in Krakow. It's a professionally run place, offering colourful dishes that are fragrant and full of flavour. The lunch menu revolves largely around set bento box options that include sushi, salad and gyoza. Korean cuisine is also represented on the menu with dishes like bibimbap and kimchi jjigae.;;[]
12763;Kropka.;Poland;Krakow;Rynek Podgórski 4, Krakow, 30-533, Poland;50.0442478;19.9499028;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Cool, casual and a little grungy, there is a rustic, welcoming vibe to this neighbourhood spot that’s very much in the bistro mould. The simply furnished dining room is enlivened by modern art on the walls and a corner bar that’s well-stocked with natural wines. The cooking mixes a Polish base with influences from over the world, such as the Korean-style chilli sauce that smothers the pierogi. The generous portions are indicative of the restaurant’s spirit.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
12764;Filipa 18;Poland;Krakow;ul. Św. Filipa 18, Krakow, 31 150, Poland;50.06772;19.9419556;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This intimate, modern restaurant blends a small open kitchen with powder blue banquettes and walls decorated with bright artwork from The Polish Poster School. The modernised versions of classic Polish dishes deliver an appealing blend of textures, alongside a careful balancing of complementary flavours. Breads are baked in-house and local ingredients are sourced from the nearby Stary Kleparz market.;Wheelchair access;[]
12765;Papavero;Poland;Poznan;ul. 3 Maja 46, Poznan, 61 728, Poland;52.4087793;16.9251971;39;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This long-established little restaurant serves a mixture of Polish and Mediterranean-inspired cooking in a stylish setting. The generous and well-executed dishes include their signature roast duck with red cabbage, alongside homemade pastas and classic desserts like tiramisu and crème brûlée. Sit overlooking the street or in the smaller, more intimate room to the rear.;Air conditioning;[]
12766;Mazi;Poland;Krakow;Rynek Podgórski 9, Krakow, 30-518, Poland;50.0442222;19.9483848;82;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Close to the city’s famous cathedral, you’ll find this charming neighbourhood restaurant with a distinctly Mediterranean vibe. From the bright, airy décor to cooking that is fresh, pared-back and abundant in olive oil, the pleasant warmth of the Greek and Italian coasts feel within touching distance. The great value dishes range from delicious, just-baked pitta with salt and herbs to tuna steak with a classic salmoriglio sauce. Chatty, welcoming service adds to the positive atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12767;Fiorentina;Poland;Krakow;ul. Grodzka 63, Krakow, 31 044, Poland;50.0558983;19.9381788;59;false;true;Creative;The beautiful vaulted, red-brick ceiling is a key attraction at this well-run and deservedly busy restaurant. An experienced chef takes traditional dishes and gives them a modern update, while using the best of the local larder and delivering plenty of flavour. Their house specialities include Siberian sturgeon caviar, Dover sole cooked over a wood-fired grill and, as the name would suggest, Fiorentina steak, which is dry-aged for 30 days before being chargrilled.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12768;Albertina;Poland;Krakow;ul. Dominikańska 3, Krakow, 31 043, Poland;50.05903;19.93954;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This sophisticated modern restaurant features a basement wine bar and boasts 32 wines available by the glass thanks to the Enomatic wine system. The cooking showcases the chef’s passion for hunting and fishing, with ingredients like venison and wild boar likely to make an appearance. The restaurant has its own lobster tank too, resulting in a range of lobster dishes on offer. Across the menu, the eye-catching cooking captures the ingredients’ true flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
12769;elixir by Dom Wódki;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Wierzbowa 9-11, Warsaw, 00 094, Poland;52.2435462;21.0083437;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;It’s all about vodka at this fashionable bistro that forms part of the ‘Vodka House’, which also includes a museum and cocktail bar. There are over 750 versions of the spirit to choose from, accompanied by well-cooked dishes prepared with care. The menu prioritises classic flavours in dishes like beef tartare, chicken broth and dumplings. Friendly service enhances the experience and there is, of course, always a vodka recommendation at the ready.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12770;A nóż widelec;Poland;Poznan;ul. Czechosłowacka 133, Poznan, 61 425, Poland;52.3766954;16.8903251;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located some way out of the city, ‘Knife and Fork’ is a modern, understated restaurant that’s run well by an engaging team. The small space has a relaxed atmosphere, while the menu is underpinned by modern interpretations of traditional Polish recipes. Seasonal produce informs the cooking too, with a tasting menu available at dinner. 'Podążaj za tym co Cię uszczęśliwia' written across the wall means ‘follow what makes you happy’ – and here you will be!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12771;Szara;Poland;Krakow;Rynek Główny 6, Krakow, 31  042, Poland;50.0611703;19.9384198;91;true;true;International;In the city's Grand Square, you’ll find this family-run, brasserie-style restaurant which boasts a hand-painted Gothic ceiling and a lovely terrace. The charming, vaulted dining room plays host to traditional cooking that draws on classic dishes from Polish, French and Swedish cuisine – accompanied by a largely French wine list. The well-executed, hearty dishes are brought to the table by an efficient service team.;Terrace;[]
12772;Bez Gwiazdek;Poland;Warsaw;Wiślana 8, Warsaw, 00 317, Poland;52.241913;21.0218748;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Located just minutes from The Royal Castle in Warsaw, this cosy restaurant has a real neighbourhood feel. The menu changes monthly, with each version focusing on cooking inspired by one of Poland's 16 regions. The chefs take traditional recipes and modernise them using contemporary techniques and sometimes a creative edge. Service comes from a wonderfully enthusiastic team who show considerable pride in their work. The great wine recommendations favour biodynamic choices from smaller producers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12773;Nolita;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Wilcza 46, Warsaw, 00 679, Poland;52.2243724;21.0127877;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences;A glass-fronted kitchen is the focal point of this smart monochrome restaurant that takes on a multitude of influences. The cooking exhibits flavours from a range of global cuisines, be that Polish, Mediterranean or Southeast Asian. Check the daily specials too, for luxurious produce like whole Alaskan king crab to share. Dishes have assured flavours, often accompanied by vibrant colours, and the excellent bread is a real highlight. Friendly service and spot-on wine recommendations complete the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
12774;Oberża 86;Poland;Gdynia;ul. Starowiejska 30, Gdynia, 81-356, Poland;54.5212682;18.5375345;56;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, French;Tucked away amongst some more utilitarian buildings, sits this pretty red-brick cottage with a cobbled terrace out front. With a long history that includes stints as a shop, a shoemaker’s and a museum, it now feels like a perfect fit for this cosy, welcoming restaurant. Seasonal Polish produce is the bedrock of the cooking, which is allowed to shine with a lightness of touch and a French flourish, showcased in technically adept elements like a piquant butter sauce accompanying the sea trout.;Terrace;[]
12775;L’Entre Villes;Poland;Sopot;Aleja Niepodległości 737, Sopot, 81-838, Poland;54.4372406;18.5613222;74;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, French;This beautifully elegant villa dates back to the turn of the 20th Century and sports interior décor that mixes the traditional with the contemporary, chandeliers with modern art – while its bright orangery is the most in-demand dining area come the summer. The neatly laid tables hint at the formality of the place, with dishes arriving under cloches and the smartly aproned team occasionally donning white gloves to serve. The French-inflected cooking demonstrates sound classical skill from the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12777;Muzealna;Poland;Warsaw;The National Museum, al. Jerozolimskie 3, Warsaw, 00 495, Poland;52.2317922;21.0247548;19;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Within the impressive main building of the National Museum of Poland sits this younger sibling to alewino, which serves unfussy bistro-style food. A broad menu includes both hot and cold starters, with hearty dishes like trout paprikash a feature. There is a refined finish to the cooking, but it’s the punchy flavours that really stand out. The friendly team make everyone feel welcome and always serve with a smile.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12778;Eliksir;Poland;Gdansk;ul. Hemara 1, Gdansk, 80-280, Poland;54.3837902;18.588553;95;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An ideal spot for cocktail lovers, Eliksir reputedly has the longest bar in the region and holds over 400 bottles ready and waiting to be used in a mixture of classic and bespoke drinks. A cocktail pairing is also offered with the tasting menu, as an alternative to the usual wine flight. Both the tasting option and the à la carte showcase quality local produce like Masurian beef, which is given the platform to shine in an excellent tartare. Smooth, friendly service adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12779;Mercato;Poland;Gdansk;Hilton Gdańsk, Targ Rybny 1, Gdansk, 80-838, Poland;54.35367;18.65796;28;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Offering tasting menus named after nearby streets, this restaurant on the ground floor of the Hilton takes its inspiration from the markets of Gdańsk. Its history as a port city means this could include global influences alongside local produce such as fine Pomeranian lamb. The technical skill of the kitchen comes through in elements like sous vide and blow-torched salmon. An à la carte is available too, and the charming staff explain the dishes with pride.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12780;Café Xander;Poland;Sopot;Jana Jerzego Haffnera 59, Sopot, 81-715, Poland;54.4509112;18.5614153;54;true;true;International;Housed inside a hotel but with a separate entrance and a feel all its own, this elegant restaurant is worth the short walk out from the city centre. Start with a cocktail while you study the concise à la carte, where the Polish cooking comes with a Mediterranean influence that's noticeable in the occasional pasta or risotto. Top produce is clearly a priority, with super ingredients from black tiger prawns to glistening cod on offer. Attractive presentation and a touch of formality in the service enhance the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12781;ZaKładka;Poland;Krakow;ul. Józefińska 2, Krakow, 30 529, Poland;50.0457883;19.9483291;19;false;false;French;Just a few steps from a footbridge over the Vistula, you'll find this riverside restaurant with a striking orange façade. With their chequered floors and red banquettes, the characterful rooms have a classic bistro feel – and the French cooking also offers a traditional edge. Dishes are hearty and founded on high quality ingredients, and warm, professional service completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
12784;Noriko Omakase;Poland;Warsaw;Mińska 45, lok 204u, Warsaw, 03-808, Poland;52.2498867;21.0641879;54;false;false;Japanese;An engaging husband-and-wife team bring their natural charm to this intimate Japanese restaurant that relocated from Wrocław towards the end of 2022. The L-shaped counter seats just eight guests, who are encouraged to interact as the omakase menu unfolds. Largely imported produce is utilised in familiar dishes such as tuna temaki, chawanmushi and an array of nigiri. Japanese whiskies and a choice of sakes complete the memorable experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
12785;Port Sołacz;Poland;Poznan;Litewska 22, Poznan, 60-605, Poland;52.42108;16.9027596;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The gorgeous Sołacki Park provides a wonderful setting for this restaurant housed inside a fine lakeside building that’s over 110 years old. The recently refurbished interior is suitably bright, but it’s the lovely terrace that steals the show. The extensive menu caters for a range of appetites, featuring soup, salads and pizzas alongside more substantial dishes like confit duck leg – which shows off the technical skill of the kitchen. Their bedrooms provide the perfect base for exploring the park.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12786;NOTA_RESTO by Tomasz Leśniak;Poland;Krakow;ul. Św. Krzyża 17, Krakow, 31 023, Poland;50.0623966;19.9427542;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The chef to the Polish national football team is behind this brightly decorated restaurant, and also owns the more informal bistro next door. The wide-ranging menu includes both a variety of steaks – served with a choice of sides and sauces – and a 'flour and water' section that includes homemade pasta alongside classic pierogi. Everything comes in generous portions and delivers bold, gutsy flavours. The professional service team run the place well.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12787;Cucina;Poland;Poznan;ul. Wyspiańskiego 26a, Poznan, 60 748, Poland;52.4002704;16.8934951;99;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed inside a historic building that was once a military barracks, the ever-developing Cucina now forms part of the City Park Hotel. The Mediterranean-influenced menu caters to a range of tastes, from pizzas and pastas to beef tartare and fine roast duck. A large, on-view wine wall is an indicator of the serious list, which features some excellent vintages and is enhanced by charming, knowledgeable service. A covered terrace comes into its own in the summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12789;Amarylis;Poland;Krakow;ul. Józefa Dietla 60, Krakow, 31 039, Poland;50.0542957;19.9432882;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Global and Polish influences are effectively integrated at this basement restaurant inside the Queen Hotel, close to Krakow Old Town. Choose to sit in either a traditional brick-built room or a more modern space furnished in black and white, then sit back and enjoy the attractively presented modern dishes. There’s a good degree of detail in the cooking, which showcases precision and effective flavour contrasts throughout.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12791;Farina;Poland;Krakow;ul. Św. Marka 16, Krakow, 31 018, Poland;50.063989;19.9394017;17;false;false;Seafood;A pretty little restaurant in the heart of the Old Town, the dining area here is divided across three cosy rooms, each with their own character and blending original features with more modern furnishings. The simple cooking eschews fussiness in favour of reliably enjoyable dishes that allow the core flavours to shine. Seafood is the speciality, with fish arriving from France several times a week and then cooked whole over salt and herbs. Dishes to share are a feature.;Air conditioning;[]
12792;Fisherman;Poland;Sopot;Grunwaldzka 89, Sopot, 81-771, Poland;54.4387165;18.5743861;58;false;true;Seafood;Just 300m from the beach and with a name like Fisherman, it’s no surprise that seafood is the focus of this cosy, candlelit restaurant, which also boasts an attractive terrace if you prefer to dine alfresco. Produce from trout to catfish is used in unfussy, flavoursome dishes – including a knockout paprikash – that are often adorned with sea herbs and hedgerow flowers foraged by the team. It sits within Villa Sentoza, so there’s rooms available if you want to stay the night.;Terrace;[]
12793;True;Poland;Gdansk;Chmielna 10, Gdansk, 80-748, Poland;54.3483745;18.6571738;37;true;false;Meats and Grills;Quality primary ingredients and skilled treatment of them form the basis of the cooking at this stylishly understated restaurant. Although multiple cuts of beef form a chunk of the menu, this is far more than a steakhouse. Seafood plays a big role too, with surf and turf platters catching the eye, while the quality of the kitchen shines through even in the smaller details – like a terrific side dish of girolles. The wine list contains some hidden gems and the service team will be happy to recommend a glass or two.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12795;Dyletanci;Poland;Warsaw;Koszykowa 47, Warsaw, 00 659, Poland;52.2217359;21.0141011;72;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away in a quiet city centre mews since its relocation towards the end of 2023, this smart restaurant is the brainchild of an experienced chef and wine importer. This background shines through in an impressive wine list with over 1,500 choices, and a particular focus on biodynamic and organic options. The cooking is pared-back and vibrant, utilising ingredients from their own farm and local producers. The friendly team enhance your visit with relaxed yet professional service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12797;Ritz;Poland;Gdansk;ul. Szafarnia 6/U6, Gdansk, 80-755, Poland;54.3502389;18.6602444;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef-Owner Basia Ritz was the first winner of MasterChef Poland and used this as a springboard to fulfil her ambition of running her own restaurant. Her dream has been realised at this quayside spot nestled amongst numerous other eateries. Locally sourced produce provides many of the menu’s highlights, with the likes of in-season chanterelles laying a strong foundation for the unfussy modern cooking. The personable team provide keen and friendly service.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12800;Epoka;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Ossolińskich 3, Warsaw, 00 072, Poland;52.2421045;21.0139848;17;true;false;Innovative;Spread across two stylish, colourful rooms conceived by a Polish theatre designer – one bright blue, one in warmer hues – this restaurant inside the Raffles Europejski hotel takes its inspiration from the Polish cookbooks of yesteryear. Classic recipes like roasted goose are listed on the menu next to their dates of origin, but given a modern spin in their execution. Local produce plays a big role too, with the ingredients presented to diners at the start of the meal.;Air conditioning;[]
12801;PASODOBRE;Poland;Poznan;Poznań Congress Centre, Śniadeckich 25, Poznan, 60-773, Poland;52.4021539;16.9044997;36;true;true;Spanish;Just to the side of the Poznan Congress Centre, you’ll find this spacious Spanish restaurant serving up the usual tapas suspects. You’ll find Padrón peppers and patatas bravas all present and correct, alongside more filling main dishes and a selection of pintxos. Strong, satisfying flavours run throughout, while the flan is a terrific incarnation of a classic dessert. A small fridge is filled with Spanish goodies to buy and take home, including olive oil and almonds.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12802;Zazie;Poland;Krakow;ul. Józefa 34, Krakow, 32 056, Poland;50.0512398;19.9469489;44;false;false;French;In the city's historic Jewish quarter of Kazimierz, you’ll find this busy little bistro with a bustling atmosphere that belies its residential location. Ask for a table in the characterful cellar, which mixes French memorabilia with brick and stone walls. The Gallic influence continues into the cooking, with dishes like beef Bourguignon and classic onion soup with Gruyère cheese among the gutsy and generously sized options on the menu.;Air conditioning;[]
12803;Kogel Mogel;Poland;Krakow;ul. Sienna 12, Krakow, 31 041, Poland;50.0606185;19.940715;95;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;There’s a chic, retro quality to this lively brasserie in Krakow’s Old Town, which sports several dining rooms – including one with a vaulted brick ceiling – plus an enclosed garden terrace. It's a smart place, with the menu bringing modern updates to classic Krakovian dishes, as well as those from wider Poland. This is simple, satisfying cooking with a generous touch that no doubt pleases their regulars. For dessert, the hot apple pie made with Polish Szara Reneta apples is not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12804;Karakter;Poland;Krakow;Brzozowa 17, Krakow, 31 050, Poland;50.0532758;19.9460344;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;There's a lively atmosphere when eating at Karakter thanks to its loud music, cocktails and pared-back décor. The charming young team serve an extensive menu with a focus on offal, so be prepared for sweetbreads, brains and horse meat tartare, the last of which is one of their signature dishes. The cooking of these less-common ingredients is original and refined, blending many different flavours together. The set lunch menu is a steal.;Air conditioning;[]
12805;Piwna47;Poland;Gdansk;ul. Piwna 47, Gdansk, 80-831, Poland;54.3500945;18.6518512;16;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;An unpretentious, friendly vibe is key to the charms of this modern café-brasserie found down a cobbled street in the shadow of the impressive St. Mary's Church. With a bright conservatory extension on the ground floor and a more rustic feel upstairs, it offers a pleasant environment for breakfast, a light lunch or something more substantial. The menu takes local produce and applies influences from other areas of Europe, often promoting the unfussy cooking style of the Mediterranean.;Terrace;[]
12806;Tygle;Poland;Gdansk;Chmielna 10, Gdansk, 80-748, Poland;54.3483743;18.6571868;83;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located on one of the city’s busiest waterside boulevards, Tygle is made all the more appealing by its enthusiastic service team and enclosed terrace that’s ideal for alfresco dining. Inside, you'll find a minimalist-meets-industrial style, with exposed pipes and Edison bulbs. The satisfying and well-executed dishes come in hearty portions – exemplified by the pork schnitzel – and there’s a sense of fun about options like the honey cheesecake dessert. They also offer a popular breakfast menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12807;Niesztuka;Poland;Gdansk;ul. Mariacka 2/3, Gdansk, 80-833, Poland;54.3497507;18.6541974;88;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s a mysterious, secretive feel to this restaurant tucked away inside a historic house, which sits surrounded by amber jewellers in the heart of the Old Town. Its ground floor has long high-topped tables that lend themselves to communal dining, while the first floor offers a bit more privacy. A concise menu uses excellent daily produce, with a distinct South American influence running through the dishes – from classic ceviche to delicious corn husk ice cream and meringue for dessert.;;[]
12808;The Farm;Poland;Warsaw;Mokotowska 8, Warsaw, 00 641, Poland;52.2184153;21.0171602;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A farm in Masuria, around 190km north of this appropriately named restaurant, provides produce for the chefs’ wholesome dishes that showcase big, gutsy flavours. Not all of the ingredients are local however, with the speciality in-house butchered steaks coming from Japan, Australia and beyond – the delicious beef dripping chips are the ideal accompaniment. The wine list is concise yet varied, while the bottles are stored on copper racks that suit the simple, rustic aesthetic of the room.;Air conditioning;[]
12809;Delicja;Poland;Poznan;Pl. Wolności 5, Poznan, 61 738, Poland;52.4076787;16.9272011;29;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Dine in the shade of one of the oldest trees in the Wielkopolska region in the small enclosed garden of this romantic restaurant. The elegant dining room is filled with antiques and polished silver, bringing an old-fashioned feel to proceedings. The formal and personable service is a good match for the surroundings, as is the roster of classic yet ambitious dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12810;Pod Różą;Poland;Krakow;ul. Floriańska 14, Krakow, 31 021, Poland;50.0629811;19.9398439;24;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the centre of the 300 year old hotel of the same name, within a glass-covered atrium, you'll find this spacious restaurant boasting a lounge bar and a dining area overlooking the kitchen. Quality Polish ingredients power modern dishes underpinned by a strong classical base, with confident and assured presentation, bold flavours and an Italian influence. The well-chosen wine list features over 300 Italian wines.;Air conditioning;[]
12811;Marino Bistrot;Poland;Poznan;Poznańska 50/2, Poznan, 62-851, Poland;52.4140064;16.9103226;18;true;false;Italian;Hidden away in a residential area, this basement restaurant sports rustic exposed brickwork and simple bistro furnishings. It’s named after Chef-Owner Livio Marino, who has a passion for authentic Italian dishes that manifests itself here in an extensive menu that includes a selection of homemade pastas. Look out for the gnocchi, which could come with the delicious combination of gorgonzola, pear and walnuts. For dessert, it’s very hard to resist tiramisu in a place like this.;Air conditioning;[]
12812;hub.praga;Poland;Warsaw;Jagiellońska 22/LU1, Warsaw, 03 719, Poland;52.2512002;21.035961;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the eastern side of the Vistula River lies this small, modern restaurant. Dishes offer distinct, recognisably Polish flavours and have a refined touch, with each one appearing as a work of art on the plate. The menu is made up of 14 courses: enjoy them all as the full tasting menu, choose 10 for the shorter version or simply pick four or five per person to share. A chef’s table is on offer inside the kitchen if you really want to get in on the action.;Air conditioning;[]
12813;Tuna;Poland;Warsaw;ul. Elektryczna 2, Warsaw, 00 346, Poland;52.2395727;21.0303246;51;false;false;Seafood;Wearing its fishy heart on its sleeve, this restaurant sports hundreds of tiny metal scales on its walls and a counter near the entrance displaying a bounty of seafood produce. These ingredients, ranging from skrei cod to scallops, are treated in a variety of ways, including raw preparations like tiraditos, tartares and ceviches. The titular ‘king of the sea’ does of course make an appearance too. The same team is behind Ceviche Bar on the other side of the city.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12814;Zen On;Poland;Poznan;Święty Marcin 21, Poznan, 61-804, Poland;52.4060118;16.9268825;76;true;true;Ramen, Japanese;It’s easy to see why this restaurant styled on Japanese izakaya is one of the city’s hotspots. Simple, fresh and fun, it boasts bright décor and a buzzing atmosphere that reverberates around the split-level dining room. The menu offers all manner of delights, from dim sum and bao buns to daily made udon noodles and stand-out ramen crafted using flour delivered direct from Japan. The 2 course lunch menu is a steal and the sake list is worth checking out.;Air conditioning;[]
12815;Dvor Jezeršek;Slovenia;Cerklje na Gorenjskem;Zgornji Brnik 63, Cerklje na Gorenjskem, 4207, Slovenia;46.2359784;14.4867892;85;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Situated in the quiet, bucolic village of Cerklje na Gorenjskem in the heart of the Kamnik and Savinja Alps around 40km from the Austrian border, these traditional old buildings have been converted by the Jezeršek family into a hotel with large rooms and a gourmet restaurant. The outdoor tables are particularly attractive, while the dining room has small windows allowing guests to observe the chefs at work in the kitchen. Among the desserts, don’t miss the Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake), which is served in a traditional steel pan. The restaurant also organises cookery courses and workshops on themes such as bread-making and finger food.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
12816;B-Restaurant;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Slovenska Cesta 59, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0571776;14.5054436;42;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;This rooftop restaurant at the InterContinental hotel boasts stunning 180° views of the historic centre and castle through its floor-to-ceiling windows, especially at night when the illuminated castle is surrounded by the lights of the city. Inside the restaurant, the contemporary design and open-view kitchen provide the setting for a choice of dishes which is as extensive as the views. As a result, the restaurant has built a well-deserved reputation for its international cuisine, alongside Slovenian specialities. We particularly enjoyed the fresh red prawn ceviche served with a mango sorbet that enhanced the freshness of the prawns, and an excellent tapioca quail with green asparagus and a delicate jus. Before dinner, we recommend a cocktail in the adjacent bar to admire the views of the other half of the city!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12817;Restavracija Grad Otočec;Slovenia;Otočec na Krki;Grajska cesta 2, Otočec na Krki, 8222, Slovenia;45.8381531;15.2350579;81;false;false;Regional Cuisine;This luxury hotel and restaurant in a spectacular and tranquil location in the middle of the Krka river occupies a charming 13C castle that was demolished and then rebuilt for the purpose. Antiques, a delightful bar with a fireplace and soft comfortable sofas all combine to create the feel of bygone days in the attractive dining room. The cuisine is regional and traditional, featuring carefully prepared dishes (the chicken with fregola pasta is delicious) and fresh vegetables sourced from the restaurant’s organic kitchen garden. Both the à la carte and the tasting menus follow the seasons. To round off your visit in truly aristocratic style, stay in one of the hotel’s luxurious guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
12818;Kendov Dvorec;Slovenia;Spodnja Idrija;Na Griču 2, Spodnja Idrija, 5281, Slovenia;46.0332986;14.0249171;42;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Organic;The history of this magnificent country mansion overlooking the Idrijca river valley dates back to the 14C. Today, the building houses a warm and elegant restaurant, with stylish rooms for winter dining and a beautiful terrace for the summer. The cuisine is traditional and full of authentic flavours, featuring two tasting menus – Katarina (fish) and Jakob (meat). We recommend the latter, especially if it includes the delicious “bati and bakalca” (steamed bread dough and lamb goulash). The entire wine list is dedicated to Slovenia, with all wines available by the glass – the Štemberger Malvazija is particularly good. Charming guestrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
12819;A3;Slovenia;Brestanica;Grad Rajhenburg, Cesta izgnancev 3, Brestanica, 8280, Slovenia;45.98894;15.46642;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, housed in the superbly restored 12C Rajhenburg castle overlooking the Sava river, takes its name from the huge inner courtyard that provides the perfect setting for an aperitif chosen from the many Slovenian sparkling wines served here. In the elegant and stylishly furnished dining room, enjoy a surprise tasting menu (4, 5, 6 or 7 courses) of modern dishes that are full of flavour – the zander with celeriac and the beef with Jerusalem artichoke are particularly delicious. The friendly staff are happy to offer tours of the castle, while the views from the outdoor terrace are truly delightful.;Car park;[]
12820;City Terasa;Slovenia;Maribor;Ulica kneza Koclja 22, Maribor, 2000, Slovenia;46.5567921;15.6505023;61;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Grills;If you’re exploring Maribor, this restaurant is a great place to stop and take a break and has a real holiday feel with its spacious terrace boasting views of the town, the Drava river and the Pohorje mountains in the distance. The menu focuses on fish from the Adriatic (including shellfish and plenty of grilled options), as well as meat recipes that include grass-fed Slovenian beef. There’s a more concise menu at lunchtime, plus a café and the sky lounge, both of which are perfect settings in which to relax.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12821;Julijana;Slovenia;Bled;Cesta Svobode 12, Bled, 4260, Slovenia;46.3664639;14.1079637;44;false;false;International;Housed in the Grand Hotel Toplice which stands amid some of the most popular landscapes in Slovenia, this restaurant boasts truly breathtaking views of Lake Bled from its dining room and its outdoor terrace. Here, the chef offers tasting menus of various lengths featuring meat and fish specialities with the occasional international influence, as well as a 4-course option (the Gorenjska selection menu) with a stronger regional focus. On the latter, the array of local ingredients is showcased via a delicious hazelnut crème brûlée served with ice-cream made from cherries soaked in Terrano liqueur.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12822;Etna;Slovenia;Divača;Kolodvorska ulica 3/a, Divača, 6215, Slovenia;45.6822074;13.9671424;15;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Pizza;On its website, this modern restaurant describes itself as “the home of different flavours from the Karst region”. Its cuisine is generous and exciting, with a focus on top-quality ingredients that the chef skilfully transforms into delicious dishes. The pizzas are excellent, as are the highly recommended desserts.;Air conditioning;[]
12823;Špacapanova Hiša;Slovenia;Komen;Komen 85, Komen, 6223, Slovenia;45.8173515;13.7470004;42;true;false;Contemporary;For more than 50 years, Špacapanova Hiša has been a bastion of Karst cuisine. The restaurant has been run by the Špacapan family since 1973, while its current success is largely due to son and brilliant manager Ago, who has taken the quality of the cuisine to a new level. The regional cuisine is prepared from local ingredients – staff are happy to provide information on the provenance of the ingredients and the human stories involved in their production. Depending on the time of year, don’t miss the lamb and kid, both of which are raised in the Karst and cooked in the oven, then served with cow’s milk curd ravioli. The traditions of the Karst are also alive and well in the wine cellar (the venue for tastings of wine, ham and cheese matured on site). If you’d like to prolong your stay here, the restaurant also offers a few guestrooms, some of which have been recently renovated with period furnishings.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12824;Sushimama;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Wolfova ulica 12, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0506271;14.5051044;65;false;true;Japanese;Situated not far from the castle and the riverside, in the city lively and pedestrianised tourist district, Sushimama serves elegant and precisely prepared Japanese dishes: sushi and sashimi, of course, in different combinations, but also soups (miso and others), tempura dishes, and cooked meat and fish options. In a simple furnished setting, the service is attentive and courteous.;Air conditioning;[]
12825;PEN KLUB Restavracija;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Tomšičeva ulica 12, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.05285;14.49966;63;false;false;European, Mediterranean Cuisine;Head up to the first floor to this retro-style restaurant, where you pass a welcoming lounge bar before moving into the main dining room adorned with an attractive fresco. The current managers and chef have brought the restaurant back into vogue thanks to a menu which includes some of the restaurant’s historic dishes (such as foie gras) alongside new meat and fish (both salt- and freshwater) dishes, such as the excellent trout marinated with oil and lemon and served with a dried egg yolk and green tea gel. The tiny summer terrace has just a few tables (book in advance), while the wine list features a selection of mainly regional labels.;Terrace;[]
12826;Miza za štiri;Slovenia;Zgornja Polskava;Mariborska ulica 17, Zgornja Polskava, 2314, Slovenia;46.42382;15.60557;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of this restaurant (Table for 4) says it all. The business began a few years ago as a type of “table d’hôte” for just four guests, then in 2020, Jure and Mia Brložnik followed their dreams and moved from the city to the countryside. Their restaurant is divided into three rooms, each with just one table – the perfect setting for an intimate dinner! The chef offers a fixed menu of 5, 7 or 9 courses (to be ordered ahead of time) which showcases modern cuisine with its roots in the region and a focus on vegetables and features dishes such as beetroot with horseradish, trout with mushrooms and delicious desserts. For a unique bespoke experience, we recommend the pairing with local wines.;Car park;[]
12827;MAK;Slovenia;Maribor;Osojnikova ulica 20, Maribor, 2000, Slovenia;46.5544414;15.6660942;26;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Situated on the outskirts of Maribor, this restaurant with a slightly eccentric and very individual feel is home to owner-chef David Vračko. The two dining rooms here are decorated with a curious mix of furnishings and tables with attractively simple settings. There’s no à la carte, but instead a long tasting menu created by the chef that features colourful, playful dishes with unusual and occasionally contrasting textures. The theme here is creative, interesting cuisine, including a carefully prepared selection of appetisers, delicious salmon tartare with exotic fruit, superb prawns with cauliflower, and mouth-watering duck. Everything is served with a cheerful smile and a real sense of performance.;;[]
12828;Peti 181;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Dvorni trg 1, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0492539;14.5048986;34;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;Although this restaurant’s excellent location is best appreciated in summer, with tables overlooking the river and charming views of the castle lit up at night, the attractive dining room also has an elegant and welcoming ambience influenced by the chef’s interior design skills. The cuisine is Mediterranean in style, with a focus on fish and seafood – the shellfish is excellent, as is the delicious grilled sea bass with buttered mashed potatoes, and the mouthwatering scampi soup with fried scampi tempura. The wines available by the glass are mainly Slovenian, although there’s also an interesting Riesling Gruss from Alsace that makes an excellent pairing with fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12829;Altrokè;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Stari trg 19, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0471406;14.5065572;33;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Inspired by Istria and the Mediterranean, the meat and fish dishes served at Altrokè are enhanced by the use of ingredients such as fruit, aromatic herbs and olive oil which are grown or produced on the restaurant’s own property in Plavje near Koper. The ambience here is pleasantly rustic, with exposed stonework and a brick-vaulted ceiling which blend in well with this old district of the city.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12830;Restavracija Hotela Marina;Slovenia;Izola;Veliki Trg 11, Izola, 6310, Slovenia;45.5390805;13.6569735;83;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Seafood;Although its immediate setting may lack charm, the position of this restaurant facing the marina is delightful, with its superb sea views through its picture windows. The delicious, authentic and carefully prepared cuisine focuses on fish and seafood “straight from the sea to your plate”. Although there is an à la carte, ingredients are often subject to availability. Seafood, rock fish and pasta served with an array of original sauces are just some of the delicious classic dishes on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12831;Gostilna Krištof;Slovenia;Kranj;Predoslje 22, Kranj, 4000, Slovenia;46.2680267;14.385542;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The Bolka family continues with their long-established tradition of hospitality in this authentic and welcoming restaurant that immediately warms the heart. The skilfully updated cuisine combines local recipes with a contemporary twist, as demonstrated by dishes such as trout tartare served with sweet and sour ginger, trout roe and a Bernese foam sauce. The menu changes with the seasons and showcases local ingredients such as Krškopolje pork, Carnolian sausage and locally farmed trout. The wine list has the same regional focus, with almost every Slovenian wine available by the glass.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12832;Landerik;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Stari Trg 11, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0478623;14.5062553;42;false;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This small restaurant on one of Ljubljana’s typical pedestrianised streets boasts a modern, minimalist-style dining room, as well as an attractive outdoor terrace from which to enjoy the views of this picturesque district in the heart of the city. To appreciate the cuisine to the full, we recommend choosing one of the tasting menus. The desserts include a lighter version of the traditional Kaiserschmarrn, featuring small portions of pancake, apricots and a truly mouthwatering vanilla cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12833;Hiša Krasna;Slovenia;Sežana;Lokev 78, Sežana, 6129, Slovenia;45.66302;13.92615;100;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;Run by owners Dajana and Boris Škibin and situated just a few kilometres from the Italian border, Casa Krasna is a pleasant boutique hotel where the traditions and character of Istria and the Karst meet (she is from Istria, while he is from the Karst). The ambience and cuisine at the restaurant combine to provide one of the most interesting dining experiences in the area, with a menu that features a careful selection of the region’s gastronomic specialities, as well as home-made bread and pasta. Tasting evenings organised in conjunction with local wineries are held in the old wine cellar carved out of the rock.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12834;Stara Gostilna;Slovenia;Piran;Savudrijska ulica 2, Piran, 6330, Slovenia;45.5286573;13.5668019;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Situated just off the seafront in lovely Piran, this elegant, stylish restaurant greets guests with the aromas of fresh herbs planted in large vases. The pleasant, intimate dining room serves as a backdrop for two tasting menus and a concise à la carte, all of which feature local, Mediterranean cuisine with a modern touch. Try the lobster ravioli or local sea bass cooked to perfection, followed by a selection of delicious desserts. The wine list offers over 400 labels, all chosen for their excellent pairing potential, plus a fine selection of rums and brandies.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12835;Rizibizi;Slovenia;Portorož;Obala 20, Portorož, 6320, Slovenia;45.5127743;13.5946853;64;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in an attractive location on the seafront promenade in Portorož, this restaurant boasts a classic-style interior and a pleasant summer terrace facing the beach and the sea. Most of the fish on the menu is local, and is served in simple, unfussy dishes that are full of flavour. Truffles make an appearance on the menu in season, adding their unique flavour to various dishes – don’t miss the delicious sea bass options (carpaccio and pan-fried). An impressive wine list completes the picture.;Terrace;[]
12836;Restavracija Calypso;Slovenia;Nova Gorica;Kidričeva ulica 7, Nova Gorica, 5000, Slovenia;45.95539;13.64734;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Housed within the Perla Resort and Entertainment Centre on the Slovenian side of Gorizia, this renowned restaurant has an excellent reputation in the region for its fish and seafood cuisine. The classically prepared dishes are announced at your table, with options such as raw and baked fish taking pride of place here and a particular focus on fresh fish from the Adriatic.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12837;Gostilna AS;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Čopova ulica 5a, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0517191;14.5046716;54;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;At this restaurant located in the centre of Ljubljana, choose between a dining room with a typical vaulted ceiling and, in summer, a delightful outdoor area surrounded by greenery with views of the castle. The traditional menu here features Slovenian meat dishes, with a particular focus on grilled options (such as the Cowboy steak of local beef which we particularly enjoyed), fish from the Adriatic, and home-made pasta.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12838;JB Restavracija;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Miklošičeva cesta 19, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0573549;14.5083198;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant, named after owner-chef Janez Bratovž, the father of modern Slovenian cuisine, occupies a Secessionist building dating from the 1920s and designed by architect Jože Plečnik. The building provides an intriguing setting for Bratovž’s cuisine, where the chef, assisted by his son Tomaž in the kitchen and the rest of his family front of house, combines regional ingredients and flavours with classic influences. Don’t miss the iconic JB ravioli (a permanent feature on the menu), which are stuffed with cheese and pistachio and served with goose liver and a veal jus. Bratovž has also published a book detailing his philosophy, his ingredients and forty of his most popular recipes.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12839;Restavracija Sedem;Slovenia;Maribor;Cafova 7, Maribor, 2000, Slovenia;46.56147;15.65516;89;true;true;Contemporary;In Slovenian, the word for “seven” (Sedem) also means sitting down at the table. An interesting option for either lunch or dinner, this restaurant is where students from a local tourism and catering college are trained under the watchful eye of their mentors and teachers. The original dishes on offer here are full of flavour and reflect the region and changing seasons and are presented on various tasting menus (including a vegan option) and an à la carte. You can also take a peek at the open kitchen, where a future culinary star may well be cooking your meal for you!;Air conditioning;[]
12840;Gostilna Vovko;Slovenia;Brusnice;Ratež 48, Brusnice, 8321, Slovenia;45.8223779;15.2432106;39;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Comprising a bar, wine bar, restaurant and hotel, the Gostilna Vovko is a family-run business with more than 50 years of history behind it, where the traditionally furnished dining room includes a charming wood-fired stove. The cuisine is just as you would expect – authentic and regional, including dishes such as delicious local trout tartare served with horseradish and herbs, and thick, meaty pork chops which are perfect accompanied by a glass of velvety and intensely flavoured 2019 Modra Frankinja wine. The wine list pays tribute to regional labels.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12841;Sophia;Slovenia;Portorož;Obala 45, Portorož, 6320, Slovenia;45.5148583;13.5916193;21;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Open in the evening, the gourmet restaurant at the exclusive Kempinski hotel offers an elegant tribute to the famous Italian actress Sophia Loren, whose unique beauty was as Mediterranean in style as the flavours that inspire the cuisine served here. Influences from Istria, Italy and even France combine harmoniously on a menu that focuses mainly on fish and seafood from the Adriatic (don’t miss the shellfish), although a few carefully selected, top-quality meat dishes and truffle specialities also feature. The turbot steak with prawns, leek and chive-flavoured extra-virgin olive oil is superb.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12842;Gredič;Slovenia;Dobrovo v Brdih;Ceglo 9, Dobrovo v Brdih, 5212, Slovenia;45.9763412;13.522168;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine;To get to this imposing 17C castle, home to an elegant boutique hotel as well as this restaurant, you make your way through the delightful rolling hills of the Collio wine-producing region. The cuisine here reflects the multicultural character of the country, combining Mediterranean traditions and ingredients such as sea bass, cuttlefish and crayfish with other ingredients from Central Europe such as trout, carp and venison in imaginative dishes with a personalised touch. As this is one of Slovenia’s most important wine-producing regions, make sure you visit the vinotheque here.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12843;Danilo;Slovenia;Škofja Loka;Reteče 48, Škofja Loka, 4220, Slovenia;46.1582777;14.3688129;70;false;true;Contemporary;Now run by the third generation of the Čarman family (opened by grandfather Danilo), this restaurant continues to offer cuisine that is much appreciated by its guests, with Nina at the helm in the kitchen and her brother Gašper front of house. The menu includes traditional dishes such as Loška smojka, Loška medla and Loška mešta (old peasant recipes from Škofja Loka – hence the adjective Loška – which are based on semolina and served with turnips, pork or potatoes), as well as a few more creative options that also have a regional flavour. Although meat takes centre stage, a few fish specialities from the Adriatic also feature on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12844;AFTR;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Nazorjeva ulica 2, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0524212;14.5057886;48;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated in the heart of the city, AFTR is a trendy bistro with colourful, modern dining rooms and a charming outdoor space which is perfect for a slightly cooler dining experience away from the busy riverside promenade. The cuisine here, which includes Mediterranean dishes such as taramasalata and Central European options such as suckling pig with kiwi and fennel, is fresh and tasty, skilfully combining delicate ingredients with more intense flavours. Instead of the usual division of courses, the menu has sections dedicated to cold dishes, hot dishes and desserts. The small wine selection includes a number of wines also available by the glass. Our inspector recommends the Vitvoska di Kukanja, an organic white from the Karst which both fresh and mineral.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12845;Ošterija Debeluh;Slovenia;Brezice;Trg izgnancev 7, Brezice, 8250, Slovenia;45.9078197;15.5910199;55;true;false;Contemporary;Situated in inland Slovenia just a few miles from the border with Croatia, this is one of the most interesting restaurants in the region. Here, highly experienced owner-chef Jure Tomič has created an excellent network of suppliers from all over Slovenia. His meat and fish dishes are prepared with a modern, precise and technical touch that is unfussy and focuses on bringing out the full flavour of his ingredients. Traditional recipes and ingredients are reinterpreted with a personal twist: examples are the plum extract served with duck and the sweet “butter, honey and milk” dish that takes the ingredients of a typical local dessert and creates something new and original. You’ll have no problem finding the right wine to accompany your meal from the extensive wine list.;Interesting wine list;[]
12846;Kogo;Slovenia;Koper;Šmarska cesta 1, Koper, 6000, Slovenia;45.53518;13.73658;77;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Situated away from the busy tourist centre yet easily accessible by car, this restaurant is home to an elegant wine bar (on the right when you enter the building) and a modern dining room with a few designer-style features (on the left). Despite the contemporary ambience, the food at Kogo (the name is the Slovenian word for “cook”) is traditional and includes a huge selection of cheese and charcuterie (from Slovenia and further afield), followed by main courses that focus on meat (although fish dishes also feature). There’s also an impressive wine list with detailed descriptions on a tablet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12847;Restavracija 1906;Slovenia;Bled;Hotel Triglav, Kolodvorska cesta 33, Bled, 4260, Slovenia;46.3693625;14.0833677;63;true;true;Contemporary, Traditional Cuisine;Housed in the Triglav hotel in a superb location in the foothills around beautiful Lake Bled, this restaurant offers fine views from its brightly lit dining room and delightful summer terrace. The hotel opened in 1906 and the restaurant reflects over a century of culinary tradition, serving reinterpretations of typical Slovenian specialities, often adding typical French sauces and jus to its dishes. A small vegan menu is also available.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12848;Gostilna Repovž;Slovenia;Šentjanž;Šentjanž 14, Šentjanž, 8297, Slovenia;46.0111224;15.1692284;74;true;true;Farm to table, Regional European;The Repovž family who run this restaurant are continuing a long family tradition that dates back centuries – it’s thought that the property has been in their hands for over 500 years, while there’s been a restaurant here for 300 years! Although it’s impossible to list the different generations that have worked here, one thing’s for sure – the current management has really made its mark. Both the dining room and kitchen staff work hard to ensure that guests enjoy the best regional ingredients and dishes (for example, there’s no fish on the menu), which feature on tasting menus of various lengths, with a careful balance of traditional recipes and more contemporary-style fare. The choice of delicious appetisers showcases an array of local traditional specialities, including locally bred trout, vegetables from the restaurant’s own kitchen garden, rabbit with plum cream, and diced pork with a horseradish mousse. The impressive wine list focuses on Slovenian labels – make sure you try the Laški Riesling from Slovenian Styria, a natural wine, or perhaps the Frelih St. Rupert, a lightly macerated and elegant Sylvaner produced nearby.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12849;Vila Planinka;Slovenia;Zgornje Jezersko;Zgornje Jezersko 67, Zgornje Jezersko, 4206, Slovenia;46.3950998;14.5006545;33;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Innovative;Although it takes a while to get to this restaurant, following the magical Jezersko valley to a setting just a few kilometres from the Austrian border, once you’ve reached your destination you realise that the journey was well worth it! Surrounded by splendid mountain peaks, this boutique Alpine hotel and its excellent gourmet restaurant of the same name provide a warm, welcoming haven for guests. The chefs here create elegant, refined dishes that showcase the best Slovenian ingredients, paying careful attention to local recipes. Specialities include bear prosciutto served with bread crackers, hazelnut cream and pear, and smoked trout with camomile-flavoured frothed milk, carrot reduction and pickled celery. The menu always features a few vegetarian options, such as fried celeriac with pinenut butter, poached egg and hollandaise sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12850;Gostilna Francl;Slovenia;Celje;Zagrad 77, Celje, 3000, Slovenia;46.21183;15.26504;22;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Situated at the entrance to a tranquil valley, this restaurant dating back centuries now has young new managers at the helm with a focus on cuisine that has its roots in local traditions yet with a slightly modern twist. The portions are decidedly generous, with real attention paid to presentation and colour as well as substance and quality. Meat takes centre stage here, although fish dishes also feature on the menu. In summer, dine outdoors under the trees or the delightful pergola.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12851;Hiša Torkla;Slovenia;Izola;Korte 44b, Izola, 6310, Slovenia;45.488769;13.6565981;34;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Grills;The view of the surrounding hills is one of the main attractions of this restaurant, along with the traditional open grill in the dining room. Although grilled meat dishes (Tomahawk and picanha steak, chops, fillets etc) naturally take centre stage, the menu also features first courses such as fuzi (a type of Istrian pasta) with various sauces, as well as some good raw fish options. An excellent setting in which to enjoy gourmet dining surrounded by unspoilt natural scenery.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12852;Breg;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Breg 20, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0465506;14.5051062;99;false;true;Contemporary;Overlooking Ljubljana’s riverfront, this restaurant boasts one of the most famous and picturesque views of the city from its terrace in the summer months, while in the winter the historic building’s indoor dining rooms are equally attractive. The cuisine brings a breath of international creativity to the city, with influences from Italy, France and the Middle East in its dishes. A perfect example is the hummus served with lamb ragu, pita bread, pesto and pine nuts – a real culinary voyage around the Mediterranean!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12853;Vila Podvin;Slovenia;Radovljica;Mošnje 1, Radovljica, 4240, Slovenia;46.3398753;14.2092027;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Nestled in the countryside around Radovljica, Vila Podvin is both a restaurant and a hotel. The beautiful garden is one of its attractions, along with its fresh, strongly flavoured cuisine which showcases local, seasonal ingredients from the Upper Carniola, a region influenced by Italian, Slavic and Germanic traditions – good examples are the open ravioli with Kosec cheese and sweet chestnuts, and the turbot with mussels and apples. The dining room is classic in style, plus there’s a niche with a few tables which is perfect for a romantic dinner. A good selection of Slovenian and international wines, including some excellent vintages, completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
12854;Restavracija CUBO;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Šmartinska cesta 55, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0639702;14.5275151;85;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated on the edge of the city in a district little visited by tourists, this modern restaurant dominated by a dark colour scheme serves Mediterranean-influenced yet eclectic cuisine with the occasional international flavour. The maize-crusted tuna fillet with fine vegetables and avocado is cooked to perfection – the tuna is pink and succulent and a green curry sauce adds an extra touch of character to the dish. An extensive wine list (with wines also available by the glass) adds to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12855;Georgie Bistro;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Čufarjeva ulica 5, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.05531;14.50868;24;true;true;Contemporary;Just a stone’s throw from the heart of the historic centre, this relaxed, informal restaurant serves beautifully prepared contemporary-style dishes. Although there’s a focus on Slovenian ingredients here, the chef’s imagination is also inspired by influences from outside the country. Choose between an à la carte and tasting menus of varying lengths (three to nine courses). The pairing options include organic wines, as well as craft beers and home-made syrups. Popular for work lunches, and so very busy at lunchtime.;Air conditioning;[]
12856;Galerija okusov;Slovenia;Petrovče;Novo Celje 9, Petrovče, 3301, Slovenia;46.2457883;15.1784594;28;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This excellent restaurant, whose name translates as a “gallery of flavours”, boasts an attractive setting surrounded by a park with an 18C Baroque palace (formerly Novo Celje castle) at its centre. The welcoming dining room is decidedly more contemporary in style than its surroundings, as is the cuisine served here, which is prepared from local ingredients using imaginative techniques and presented on a single tasting menu (usually 10 courses) from which guests can choose individual dishes as they please. Careful attention is paid to reducing food waste: the trout served with asparagus is also accompanied by chips made from fish skin, while the jus uses butter and other leftovers. Most of the wines on the impressive wine list are also available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12857;Restavracija Shambala;Slovenia;Ljubljana;Križevniška ulica 12, Ljubljana, 1000, Slovenia;46.0464199;14.5044235;37;false;false;Asian;A “hidden oasis of peace, tranquillity and joy” right in the centre of Ljubljana, just a stone’s throw from the city’s bustling riverside promenade, Shambala serves Asian cuisine amid an Asian-influenced decor that is attractive without being overly decorative. The dishes on the menu (meat, fish and seafood, and vegetarian) are inspired by countries all over Asia, from Japan to Thailand and Vietnam. The desserts feature more European options such as panna cotta, which is served with a mango and date sauce that gives it a more exotic flavour.;Terrace;[]
12858;Protėviai;Lithuania;Vilnius;Odminių Gatvė 3, Vilnius, 01122, Lithuania;54.6857274;25.2848718;52;false;false;Barbecue;The name Protėviai translates as ‘ancestor’ and their tagline is “The legend of fire and steaks, inspired by the ancestors of the world”. As you may have guessed, this restaurant is all about the primeval method of cooking steaks over fire and smoke. The striking interior takes in huge wooden sculptures and a fire-effect central counter hewn out of a huge piece of wood. The steaks – some dry-aged for 60 days – are a mix of Lithuanian, USDA Prime rib-eye, Koji tenderloin and Wagyu from Japan and Australia, and are served by weight, cooked over glowing embers and rested with care.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12859;Augustin;Lithuania;Vilnius;Didžioji Gatvė 18, Vilnius, 01128, Lithuania;54.6793223;25.2884742;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Sister to Momo Grill and monai, this informal restaurant has a sleek modern style. Parquet floors sit below two striking circular faux-candle chandeliers hanging from a concrete ceiling, while shelves of wine fill vintage sideboards. Punchy, colourful dishes blend Mediterranean and Middle Eastern flavours and are offered in two different formats. The majority of the menu comprises modern plant-led small plates – three per person plus a dessert is about right – but there are also three main courses on offer which are based around fish or meat. Service is warm and friendly, and the courtyard terrace is a real boon in warmer months.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12860;HeJi;Lithuania;Vilnius;Lukiškių Gatvė 3, Vilnius, 01108, Lithuania;54.6927259;25.2688788;27;true;true;Asian Influences;Having been five years in the making, this impressively opulent restaurant seems like it might be more at home in Dubai or Macau than Vilnius! The cavernous glass-roofed main dining room is overlooked by two ‘caged’ balconies and a champagne bar – and there’s an intimate, dimly lit cocktail bar serving innovative Asian creations. A wood-framed open kitchen takes centre stage, and captivating and intriguing design details abound. The original menu fuses East and West, with the dim sum a hit and the signature beef dishes cooked over charcoal a real highlight. The wine list features some fine growers and the whole place makes for a glamorous night out.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
12861;Apvalaus Stalo Klubo;Lithuania;Trakai;Karaimų g. 53A, Trakai, 21104, Lithuania;54.64948;24.93048;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the shores of Lake Galve, in the heart of a national park, you’ll find this intimate, modern restaurant, which affords incredible views over the water to the 14th-century Trakai Island Castle from its floor-to-ceiling windows. When the sun's shining, the lovely terrace is the place to be. Complex modern cooking is a reflection of the locale, exemplified by the likes of beetroot with goat’s cheese and flavour-packed lamb cutlets. Desserts are a highlight, with the ‘raspberries with raspberries’ always a surefire winner. Cheery service brings a smile to everyone’s face, and cosy bedrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12862;DIA;Lithuania;Kaunas;Maironio Street 9, Kaunas, 44298, Lithuania;54.8965678;23.9093753;42;false;true;International, Creative;You’ll be surprised how busy this formally laid restaurant in a residential spot can get, but the experienced team cope well with the numbers – among which there are many returning guests. It sits within a tardis-like building, which also houses meeting rooms, and is smartly decked out with fine glassware and crockery. The menu is one of the most eclectic around and offers everything from a burger to fine steaks, with the popular daily specials including the likes of freshly caught fish. There really is something for everyone here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12863;elven;Lithuania;Vilnius;L. Stuokos-Gucevičiaus Gatvė 7, Vilnius, 01122, Lithuania;54.6843712;25.2843156;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Sister to Nüman in Kaunas, the name of this restaurant means ‘river’ in Norwegian, with the language being a clue both to the design of the room and the style of the food here. The traditional creamwashed façade of the heritage building is certainly in complete contrast to the sleek interior, which is an elegant space with a design-led style. The menu delivers a good range of creative, pared-back dishes with bold flavours, a blend of textures and eye-catching presentation, with sharing dishes for two also a feature. In summer, head for the rear terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12864;Arrivée;Lithuania;Kaunas;Vilniaus Street 29, Kaunas, 44285, Lithuania;54.89692;23.89485;23;false;true;French;This special occasion restaurant sits in the heart of the city, in a unique setting in a 17th Century former Dominican monastery. Modern art decorates the garden, and a good-sized terrace really comes into its own in the summer months, while inside it’s intimate and relaxed, with lovely original fittings and just nine tables. The cooking is unashamedly French, with modern overtones and flavour to the fore. Desserts are a highlight, and at weekends they sell homemade bread and delicious croissants. The evening lasts for around 4 hours, so settle in and make the most of the experience.;Terrace;[]
12865;Stikliai;Lithuania;Vilnius;Gaono Gatvė 7, Vilnius, 01131, Lithuania;54.6804973;25.2859912;26;true;false;Classic French;For a comfortingly classical experience in the city, head to Stikliai, set within a hotel in the heart of the Old Town. Here, photos of famous faces who have visited over the years line the walls – including celebrities and Heads of State – and the glass-roofed room filled with greenery has an elegant feel. Matching the atmosphere, the food has a classical French base, with the sauces in particular being a strength. You might find lamb shoulder confit with bulgur wheat, tomato concasse and aubergine caviar or haddock fillet served with sweet potatoes, fennel, pak choi and beurre blanc.;;[]
12866;Stebuklai;Lithuania;Vilnius;L. Stuokos-Gucevičiaus Gatvė 1, Vilnius, 01122, Lithuania;54.6852129;25.2849952;61;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Set in a hotel beside the Cathedral Square, you can expect an idyllic ambience here, complete with twinkling water fountains. When the weather’s good, the terrace is the place to be, as it faces the Square and the Cathedral, but the restaurant itself is also a beautiful place with a chic, modern ambience. The ambitious kitchen produce cosmopolitan dishes such as hamachi ceviche with strawberries, hibiscus, avocado and shiso or duck breast with carrot gratin, cherries, pickled onions and Pedro Ximenez sauce, which all arrive in attractive arrangements.;Terrace;[]
12867;Ertlio Namas;Lithuania;Vilnius;Šv. Jono Gatvé 7, Vilnius, 01123, Lithuania;54.6819148;25.2874623;61;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Set over three floors of a historic townhouse in the city centre, this is a charming restaurant with wonderful wooden floors, fine period art on the walls and a historical menu to match. Choose either a 4 or 6 course set menu to experience interesting dishes from a bygone era – dating as far back as the 16th Century – which could include sorrel soup, salted and cured veal pekenfleišas or beef tart with beef broth sauce. Following each dish comes an explanation of its origins, providing sustenance for your brain as well as your body.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12869;Farmer & The Ocean;Lithuania;Vilnius;Vilniaus Gatvė 25-33, Vilnius, 01402, Lithuania;54.68551;25.27948;95;false;true;Meats and Seafood;Located in a busy spot amongst many other eateries, it’s worth seeking out this basement restaurant. Inside it’s bright and colourful, with orange walls, designer touches and a large octopus hanging from the ceiling. The name says it all, with meat and seafood centric dishes including delicious beef, lamb shank, herring and a wonderful seafood stew. The snails on toast is a popular choice and the classical desserts – like crème brûlée – are always a hit. Be sure to book ahead though, as they do get busy.;Air conditioning;[]
12872;Uoksas;Lithuania;Kaunas;Maironio g. 28, Kaunas, 44249, Lithuania;54.8982332;23.9099511;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this chic, smartly furnished restaurant, things are both relaxed and lively at the same time. The team are pursuing their vision of redesigning Lithuanian cuisine and work with modern techniques following a Nordic style. Ingredients come mainly from the Baltic region, although there are some exceptions, resulting in dishes like beetroot taco with seabass ceviche, pickled onion and coriander or grilled veal chop with chive butter, grilled tomatoes, potato and ghee butter mash. Choose from the concise à la carte or order the tasting menu in advance to sample the full range of the kitchen’s talents.;;[]
12873;Monte Pacis;Lithuania;Kaunas;T. Masiulio Street 31, Kaunas, 52436, Lithuania;54.8762375;24.0204057;62;false;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Set within a historical property in a large park just outside of the city, Monte Pacis sees Lithuanian cuisine reinterpreted in a modern and visually appealing way. Carefully prepared native, Baltic and international ingredients feature in flavoursome dishes such as lamb sirloin with ricotta tortellini, Swiss chard, shiitake mushrooms, courgette, parsnip cream and pepper sauce. The owner is a passionate wine-lover and a qualified sommelier, so wine is naturally a highlight, with more than 200 bottles individually and lovingly described.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12874;Dine;Lithuania;Vilnius;Gedimino prospektas 35, Vilnius, 01109, Lithuania;54.68909;25.26836;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Dine is one of those places which simply provides great enjoyment. The kitchen is rooted in the classical camp but has modern overtones – and keeps things simple by using fresh ingredients which are cleanly cooked and refrain from unnecessary adornment, as exemplified by the likes of cod with wild garlic purée, peas and mint oil in the summer. That being said, there’s some skill on display in elements like of the two-coloured ravioli dough. The regularly evolving wine list offers a good selection by the glass, as well as a strong selection of champagnes. They also offer themed tasting dinners.;Wheelchair access;[]
12875;Telegrafas;Lithuania;Vilnius;Universiteto Gatvė 14, Vilnius, 01122, Lithuania;54.6848275;25.2857353;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Built in 1900, this rather magnificent building – now home to a smart hotel – sits in a prime position overlooking Vilnius Cathedral and was once the city Telegraph office, hence the restaurant’s name. The contemporary ground floor space comes complete with a decked terrace and the personable service team cater for your every need. Modern menus offer plenty of appeal, with the Business Lunch representing great value for money. Dishes take on a straightforward approach and are carefully executed, with harmonious flavour combinations found in dishes such as salmon tartare with buttermilk panna cotta, compressed cucumber, bread & beer chips and dill emulsion.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12876;monai;Lithuania;Klaipeda;Liepų Gatvė 4, Klaipeda, 92114, Lithuania;55.7119701;21.1329864;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The busy port city of Klaipėda plays host to this cosy restaurant where, once you’ve located the discreet entrance – a very warm welcome awaits. As you step over the threshold, a feeling of calm engulfs you, and you can drift away from the world outside. Lunch is a simple affair and represents great value, while at dinner, honest flavours shine through in modern dishes where fish is a highlight, such as in the roasted cod with coco beans, chorizo and cauliflower. This will quickly become one of your favourite new places to eat.;;[]
12878;Somm;Lithuania;Vilnius;Pylimo Gatvė 21, Vilnius, 01141, Lithuania;54.6790271;25.2781069;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name Somm is an abbreviation of sommelier, giving a strong clue as to where Owner Narimantas Miežys’ passion lies. He is one of the top sommeliers in the Baltic region and, with over 500 bottles making up a truly global selection, this really is an oenophile’s paradise. Set opposite the MO modern art museum, it’s decorated with wine bottles and related memorabilia, and has a pleasingly unfussy, neighbourhood feel. This is a place where the sommeliers choose your wines for you – after discussing your preferences, of course – matching them with simple yet interesting dishes, some of which are prepared in the wood-burning oven;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12882;Clover Saint-Germain;France;Paris;5 rue Perronet, Paris, 75007, France;48.8551986;2.3304041;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In keeping with the trend of great chefs opening modest restaurants, Jean-François Piège serves generous starters for sharing (oysters, cold meats etc) and home-made pasta dishes (the laboratory is right next door). Penne, ravioli and tortellini are combined with humble ingredients such as ox cheek, premium ingredients such as langoustine, and even exotic elements – see his green curry on tortellini, Mediterranean crab, piquillos and cauliflower. The desserts, such as an "invisible apple cake", are simply delicious. The small space is long and narrow, encompassing both the kitchen and dining area.;;[]
12883;La Bastide des Magnans;France;Vidauban;32 avenue du Général-Gallieni, Vidauban, 83550, France;43.4240832;6.4311224;46;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This former silkworm farm near the road serves an appetising score that changes daily in a bid to shine the spotlight on fresh regional produce, crafted by a local Vidauban lad, Christian Bœuf. The culinary score reflects the attentive, meticulous personality of the chef: scrambled eggs with truffles, fillet of bream, leeks, Swiss chard, green peas and a lobster emulsion with a tempting citrus fruit tart and a vanilla and lime mousse to finish by pastry chef Benjamin Mozzone. Intelligent selection of well-priced regional tipples and attentive service, whether on the terrace shaded by plane trees or in one of two dining rooms done up in a chic, contemporary Provençal vein.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12885;Là-Haut;France;Annecy;8 rue du Baronnet, Annecy, 74000, France;45.9107435;6.1387917;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the top floor of the Parc des Artisans, this contemporary restaurant affords a view over the rooftops and the mountains beyond. The chef homes in on the essentials with his tasty, no-nonsense cuisine. Top-notch ingredients, generous dishes, intense sauces – it all conspires to ensure a pleasant time is had by all. At lunchtime, in particular, there is an affordable set menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12886;Freya;France;Biarritz;1 rue du Lycée, Biarritz, 64200, France;43.4864413;-1.5495264;56;false;true;Creative, Vegetarian;Freya, the goddess of nature in Norse mythology, presides over the very vegetable-forward feast served at this compact restaurant in the Saint-Charles neighbourhood. At the helm is a couple with a wealth of professional experience and many trips around the globe under their belt. Chef Guillaume Chatillon doesn't shy away from using meat or fish (particularly the top-notch fish from Saint-Jean-de-Luz fish market), but focuses on vegetables, which are elevated in the same way as any other premium ingredient, with a host of indulgent preparations and occasionally daring combinations, such as his beautifully balanced cauliflower with seaweed. N.B. Guests at the same table are invited to share the same plate. Wine recommendations come, with a smile, from Margot – most are organic or natural, and all are available by the glass.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12887;Azerole;France;Dijon;86 rue Berbisey, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3181794;5.0358102;51;false;false;Fusion;Originally from Northern China, Xin Gan, who happens to be married to the chef of Parapluie, runs this delightful French-Asian fusion place with a simple neo-bistro decor (stone walls, dark wood tables and chairs). Single-handed in the kitchen, the chef skilfully combines spices, tofu and kimchi with high-quality seasonal French ingredients, to compose dishes such as rack of pork, chimichurri, courgette cream and green curry, accompanied by a dash of creamy hummus and multi-coloured carrot ribbons tossed in an orange vinaigrette – delicious!;Terrace;[]
12888;Amâlia;France;Paris;32 rue de la Fontaine-au-Roi, Paris, 75011, France;48.8681622;2.371705;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Unlike many of the other restaurants in the east of Paris, this one has gone for classic elegance: a refined decor, tablecloths, stylish service. Perhaps this is the mark of the good taste of Italian couple Cecilia Spurio (pastry) and Eugenio Anfuso (cooking), who are familiar with Michelin-starred restaurants. Prepared with small pieces of citrus fruit and cashew nuts, the smoked Galician veal tartare is served in a sea urchin shell, topped with a quenelle of sea urchin ice cream. For his red mullet à la bourguignonne, the chef arranges the fish on shredded beef and cabbage leaves, the whole of which is then doused with a superb sauce. This is a modern iteration of the French repertoire, punctuated by a few Italian touches or other influences from further afield, executed with precision and a clear penchant for acidic notes.;;[]
12889;Relais de la Vallée;France;Ambialet;75 route de la Vallée, Ambialet, 81430, France;43.9442737;2.3770971;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Caroline Blau and Tommy Medalle have set up shop in Ambialet, the village where Tommy is from, in a photogenic bend in the Tarn. They have transformed an old café nestling close to the riverbank and sporting a slightly old-fashioned brand of rustic charm. The menu, devised by the chef, may consist of simple dishes, but the results are exacting and exciting, ranging from classics such as marrow bone and soup of the day to more original creations like pork belly with daikon marinated and braised in mirin and sake, in a nod to Japan. The ingredients are fresh and high quality, and the service is down-to-earth and extremely pleasant. Very reasonable prices!;Terrace;[]
12892;Fujiyama 55;France;Lyon;40 avenue Jean-Jaurès, Lyon, 69007, France;45.7509758;4.845175;60;false;true;Ramen;A Japanese DJ based in Lyon wanted to replicate a Japanese ramen institution in France. In this utilitarian-style space in the Guillotière neighbourhood, he has joined forces with his compatriot, originally a musician, trained in the exacting art of ramen. Everything is made in house, including gyoza and desserts, and the ingredients are local if not Asian (such as farmhouse pork). Fine sake selection.;;[]
12894;The Attic;China Mainland;Guangzhou;A3-103, T.I.T Smart Zone, Yuan Cun, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1196094;113.3513135;88;false;false;European Contemporary;At The Attic, located in a historical cotton mill turned science park, they believe it takes time for flavours to develop in food. The young kitchen team excels in lengthy and painstaking processes such as meat aging and sauce fermentation. Most items are made from scratch in-house, including hand-spun ice cream, charcuterie, bread and butter. The menu changes according to the season and features mostly produce from China. The desserts are worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12897;Emmelyn;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Unit 101, Kingold Century, 62 Jinsui Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.124816;113.316765;48;false;false;French Contemporary;The head chef honed his skills in New Zealand and Australia before joining Emmelyn. It serves business sets at lunch and a dinner tasting menu that respects the seasons. All of which showcase dishes underscored by French tradition with fresh, modern twists. You can expect top-notch local and imported produce like Qiandao Lake caviar, French oysters and Iberian ham. The sourdough is made with homemade wild yeast that the restaurant has been fermenting since it opened.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
12898;Chao Yue;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 36-1, West Gate, The Canton Place, Qingfeng Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1172373;113.3335288;16;true;false;Innovative;Chao Yue means jumping waves, echoing the sculptural wave form on the ceiling of the spacious dining room. Three fixed price menus put the fun back into fine dining and globally sourced produce is used in impeccably presented, playful and pleasantly surprising dishes, such as eel maw disguised as sticky lychee rice balls. Chaozhou traditions and innovative techniques are melded seamlessly in dishes like boneless crispy skinned pigeon in bean sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12900;Aroma;China Mainland;Guangzhou;5F, Conrad Hotel, 222 Xingmin Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.118088;113.326814;44;true;false;European;Prior to helming the kitchen of Aroma, this chef had done time in Paris and Shanghai. His short but sweet menu features well-judged European dishes made with quality ingredients from around the world. Culinary highlights include pan-seared foie gras served with fig jam and a tangy berry-port sauce that cuts through the richness. The lunch set offers exceptional value. Ask for a table by the full-height windows for panoramic city views.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
12902;Li Château;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Basement 1 level, 228 Tianhe Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.135443;113.320744;33;true;false;European;The romantic and dimly lit dining space is done out in European style, but Lingnan motifs and old-time Guanxi scenes are featured for an eclectic effect. Popular items on the menu include beef tenderloin Wellington with a red wine sauce and the black truffle risotto with pan-seared foie gras. The monthly changing tasting menu keeps things fresh for regulars.;Air conditioning;[]
12905;Deli Boutique・Uncle De Abalone;China Mainland;Guangzhou;909 Xingye Avenue, Nancun Town, Panyu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.005011;113.377458;61;false;true;Cantonese;It’s a bit out of the way, but the ample parking, privacy in individual rooms and tasty abalone dishes make this trip worthwhile. The menu features abalone from South Africa, Middle East, Australia, Japan and Lienchiang in varying sizes—from 22 to 1.5 heads. The chefs cook the gastropod perfectly, rendering them flavourful and tender, but with a lovely chew. Other Cantonese dishes, especially those served in a claypot, also stand out. Reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
12906;The Eminent;China Mainland;Guangzhou;L4, Four Seas Bay, Four Seas City, 388 Hanxi East Avenue, Panyu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.0085265;113.3452494;31;true;true;Cantonese;This dining concept consists of 19 generously sized private rooms, all tastefully furnished in Southeast-Asian style. Based on the theme of Moutai, it has a gallery where a rare collection of the national liquor is displayed. The food is mostly Chaozhou and Cantonese, with an emphasis on seasonal ingredients. Certain items such as double-boiled silkie chicken soup with fresh ginseng and deer sinew have to be pre-ordered.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
12907;Chao Ji Claypot Rice (Liwan);China Mainland;Guangzhou;723 Longjin East Road, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1251758;113.2438596;82;false;false;Cantonese;Time is of the essence when it comes to cooking claypot rice. In this popular two-storey joint, both the rice and soups are made to order, so expect to wait for at least 15-20 minutes, longer at peak hours. The rice is perfectly cooked, soft but toothsome with a crispy golden crust. Choose from an array of toppings: pork liver, chicken, pork patty, preserved pork and sausage, raw or fried eggs…;Air conditioning;[]
12908;Guo Fan Jia Yan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, 123 TangAn Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.135231;113.370587;63;false;false;Hunanese;A must-try for spicy food lovers. Named after famous statesman Zeng Guofan of Qing Dynasty, the room pays tribute to him with his literary and calligraphic works. The menu also focusses on dishes and seasonal ingredients from Hunan province, where Zeng hailed from. The signature softshell turtle is either braised in sauces or blanched in stock, best ordered ahead of time. Also try the braised pork belly, a recipe from Shuangfeng County.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
12909;Cheers (Kaichuang Avenue);China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, A4 Building, Zhitai Plaza, Kaichuang Avenue, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1769656;113.4774464;16;true;false;Hunanese;The main dining room on the bottom floor evokes relaxed vibes with sheer curtains and rattan chairs while the upper level houses private rooms exclusively. The private rooms serve a special menu with keenly sought-after Hunanese ingredients in limited quantity. Try ice-chilled crisp lotus root from Dongting Lake, or Cantonese-style braised sea cucumber with premium chilies from Zhangshu Port. Pre-order these dishes to avoid disappointment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
12910;He Yuan (Tianhe);China Mainland;Guangzhou;Level 3 and 3M, IMP, 68 Huacheng Avenue, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.120747;113.321807;49;false;false;Cantonese;This kitchen serves well-executed Cantonese dishes with an emphasis on various breeds of abalone – Japanese, South African, Australian and Middle Eastern. All dim sum is made on the spot, but for those seeking more heat in their food, there are Sichuanese chefs to satisfy your cravings. The palatial dining room houses 60 tables for banquets. For smaller parties, 17 private rooms are available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
12911;The Legend;China Mainland;Guangzhou;3F, Star River Bay Center, 168 Pazhou Avenue, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1032123;113.341158;74;true;true;Cantonese;Adjacent to a convention centre, the restaurant is spread over two floors with both a main dining area and many private rooms. Bird and flower murals and marble with exquisite veining add to the contemporary Chinese chic. In addition to Cantonese barbecue and dim sum, Chef Fei and his team excel in Chaoshan favourites such as marinated raw seafood and soy-marinated meats. Must-try items include the baby pigeon with its crispy skin and juicy meat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12912;Yushan Soup (Liede Xipu Street);China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 103, 10 Liede Xipu Street, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1175085;113.32698;60;true;true;Cantonese;This quaint restaurant stands in a restored 900-year-old village. It says “soup” on the sign and its double-boiled soups that take six hours to prepare are must-tries. However, the season-driven menu offers much more than soups. Scrambled egg with brisket deckle and wild chilli imparts big flavours and mild heat. Diners in private rooms may try the chef’s secret menu. Make sure you book your table and pre-order your favourite seafood.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12913;BingSheng Pin Wei (Dongxiao Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;33 Dongxiao Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.108049;113.281028;41;false;false;Cantonese;The group first made its name with sashimi and, at this branch, diners may choose from sea perch, grass carp, amberjack and a myriad of live prawns. It also prides itself highly on the unmissable 'four beauties' – crispy char siu (pork belly crusted with breadcrumbs and sugar), soy-marinated pork trotters, pork tripe and goose intestines. Large parties may also try their jumbo-sized pineapple buns, to be ordered by the half dozen.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12914;Yue Jing Xuan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;68F, Park Hyatt Hotel, 16 Huaxia Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.121317;113.316264;35;true;false;Cantonese;Diners get to take in lovely city views, as well as the action in the open kitchen – the chefs, flames, aromas and dynamic energy of the team. The chef has nearly 20 years' experience and his sand ginger chicken is famed for its thick, tender flesh: he uses only 225-day-old free-range birds from Zhanjiang. Try also the crispy roast pork belly or honey-glazed sleeper goby. Besides the main menu, ask the servers about seasonal dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
12915;Taozui Guan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Building 10, Zone B, Zhujiang Party Pier Beer Culture & Art Zone, 118 Modisha Street, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.109345;113.334612;97;false;false;Chinese Contemporary;Showcasing a ceramic theme, this restaurant doubles as a cultural hub for art making and exhibitions. The interior resembles an elegant tea house, whereas the food shows international influences and creative touches—emphasising MSG-free, healthful recipes. The signature surfer fish with pickled cabbage is cooked tableside, as the server pours scalding broth onto the raw fish. Tofu and sea urchin in claypot melds and balances all the great flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
12916;Famous Cuisine (Tianhe North Road);China Mainland;Guangzhou;2-3F, China Mayors Plaza, 189 Tianhe North Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.14103;113.30969;82;true;false;Cantonese;The founder has been in the business for over 40 years. Besides traditional Cantonese fare, his group also excels in novelty creations and seafood prepared in myriad ways. Opened in 2006, this location has its own speciality menu. Soy-marinated chicken is seasoned with luo han guo instead of sugar for extra depth. Steamed grouper fillet with pepper and salted potherb mustard is another standout. Popular dishes such as roast pigeon have to be pre-ordered.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12917;Thai Alley (Yuexiu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 219, 2F, Man Lap Fong, 9 Qingbo Road, Ersha Island, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.110372;113.29703;61;false;true;Thai;This Thai restaurant on Ersha Island affords views of the city’s skyline from afar. Yet, the interior is a world apart from the cityscape – elephant motifs, triangular seat cushions and lanterns instantly whisk diners to Thailand. If you like your food hot, go for the larb lettuce wrap with ground pork or beef, perfumed by Thai basil. Yellow curry beef uses Angus cuts for tenderness, while the tom yum goong boasts balanced flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
12918;Sing Wan Loi Noodle;China Mainland;Guangzhou;181 Middle Guangzhou Avenue, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1221959;113.3090888;22;false;true;Noodles;Unlike your typical wonton noodle joint, this one sports blue and white porcelain patterns and exquisite millwork. The menu is similarly off-kilter: expect eclectic ingredients ranging from black truffle and sea urchin to hairy crab and dried abalone. The wontons made with Iberico pork are the epitome of juicy while duck eggs give the noodles a springy texture. Various beef cuts and pork liver blanched in shrimp roe stock are also worth sampling.;Cash only;[]
12919;The Peach Blossom (Yuexiu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;3F, LN Garden Hotel, 368 Huanshi East Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.137908;113.280891;45;true;true;Cantonese;Those familiar with the classic novel ‘Romance of the Three Kingdoms’ should be able to tell what inspired the name here. The interior is also decorated heavily with portraits of the protagonists and scenes from the ‘Oath of the Peach Garden’ episode. The food is home-style Cantonese with seasonal specialities, and everything is made from scratch in-house. Try the famous barbecue meat and dim sum. Private rooms are available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
12921;Yong Zuo;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 105, No.20, Li Fu Garden, Baoye North Street, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.094977;113.259022;68;false;true;Congee;The owner opened this shop with a mission to replicate the fish congee that his grandpa used to make. As opposed to the creamy type, the Chaoshan-style congee here is more like steamed rice in that flavorsome pork bone broth simmered for three hours. Besides seafood and fish, those adventurous may order offal like fish liver and maw with the congee. Don’t miss dim sum, like fried taro roll, shrimp rolls, Puning dried tofu and pan-fried chive dumpling.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12922;Wing Lee Restaurant (Yuexiu);China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, Xianjian Building, 259 Yanjiang Zhonglu, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1183637;113.2667025;86;false;true;Cantonese;The room, furnished in classic Cantonese style, affords lovely river views. Born to a family of chefs, the owner aims to pass on the art of Cantonese cooking by reviving nostalgic recipes, like crispy skinned chicken stuffed with minced shrimp, that are rarely found elsewhere. Top marks for the dim sum breakfast or lunch and the eggy doughnuts in icing sugar. The restaurant is hugely popular, so expect to share a table with strangers at peak hours.;Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12923;Cicada;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop D1, South Gate, The Canton Place, Haifeng Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1167057;113.3341299;50;false;false;Hunanese;From the outside, this stylish restaurant looks like a piece of avant-garde art. On the inside, the theatrically lit interior exudes understated luxe. Here, classic Hunanese dishes are given a new spin with haute cuisine precision and artistic plating. Highlights include stir-fried Hunanese dried pork with garlic sprouts and bamboo shoot, and braised goose web and Sri Lankan crab in ginger chili sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
12924;Beiyuan Cuisine;China Mainland;Guangzhou;202 Xiaobei Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.139095;113.267105;93;true;true;Cantonese;The national historical site in the heart of the city faithfully replicates details of a Lingnan-style Chinese garden. Inside, diners are wowed by 14 gilded redwood vases with elaborate carvings on all sides. Opened in 1928, it is famed not only for its palatial decor but also for such Cantonese home-style dishes as Huadiao drunken chicken and its exquisitely made dim sum – try char siu puff pastry, and steamed chicken with fish maw.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12925;Ebony;China Mainland;Guangzhou;4F, Mandarin Oriental Hotel, 389 Tianhe Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.137162;113.327751;99;true;true;European;In addition to devising an à la carte menu featuring excellent grilled meats and steakhouse classics, the Spanish head chef creates themed prix-fixes using seasonal produce. The char-grilled, 28-day dry-aged Australian Wagyu beef is the standout dish – perfect for pairing with one of the many wine options available by the glass. To round things off, try one of the exclusive house-infused gins at the adjoining gin bar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12926;Flavors of China;China Mainland;Guangzhou;3F, White Swan Hotel, 1 Shamian South Street, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.108321;113.237649;46;true;false;Huaiyang, Sichuan;Generously adorned with glass work and art, this graceful restaurant befits the famous hotel in which it is nestled. All tables have gorgeous river views that jazz up the dining experience. The menu features the best from all over China, with an emphasis on Huaiyang and Sichuan specialities, such as sunflower seed-fed chicken in rice wine sauce and scalded shredded eel in oil. Oenophiles are bound to be thrilled by the varied wine selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12927;Dr. Xu's Wellbeing Branch (Tianhe);China Mainland;Guangzhou;7F, Concord Center, 57 Linjiang Avenue, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.116705;113.323545;38;true;true;Cantonese;Founder Dr. Xu is a postdoc in Chinese medicine who advocates therapeutic diets. This restaurant doubles as a museum showcasing his collection of antiques and rare medicinal herbs. Diners here appreciate the tonic effects of double-boiled soups and there is a vast array on the menu. Most dishes combine seasonal ingredients from Japan and Taiwan with natural health-boosters. Ask the friendly team about the availability of wild-caught seafood.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
12928;Four Seasons Pavilion · Rùn;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, 9 South Door, Hall 3, Liu Hua Exhibition and Trade Center, 117 Liuhua Road, Yuexiu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.144071;113.254091;55;false;false;Chinese Contemporary;The dining room had a facelift in 2022 and now boasts modern décor with Beijingese motifs. For more privacy, consider booking one of their well-appointed individual rooms. Helmed by a Beijingese kitchen team, it prides itself on Peking duck — sliced tableside and served with an array of condiments and toppings. Besides traditional Beijingese cooking, novelty dishes that reinvent Cantonese flavours in unexpected manners are also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
12929;Zen Tea;China Mainland;Guangzhou;on the side of main entrance of Xiaogang Park, 146 Qianjin Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.100977;113.276901;99;true;true;Vegetarian;Styled after a Zen theme, this space provides only private rooms to ensure a serene dining experience. Soybean products made with spring water are exceptional, as are specialities such as faux sea cucumber made with agar-agar and yam starch in a creamy cashew pumpkin sauce. For ovo-vegetarians, stir-fried lily bulbs with olive nuts and egg white is the must-try – the half-set egg white works magic with the crunchy lily bulbs and olive nuts.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12931;Yun Pavilion;China Mainland;Guangzhou;5F, Conrad Hotel, 222 Xingmin Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.118215;113.326635;53;false;false;Cantonese;This lavish interior is inspired by the eight categories of Chinese musical instruments, while the Longquan celadon teacups add a touch of refinement. The experienced kitchen team focuses on traditional Cantonese fare, spiced up by the clever use of gourmet ingredients, such as the signature deep-fried honeycomb taro puff stuffed with seared scallop. In addition, the menu includes regional specialties that cater to all tastes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12932;The Penthouse;China Mainland;Guangzhou;23 & 25F, South Tower, Grand Hyatt Hotel, 12 Zhujiang West Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.124859;113.318041;30;true;false;Cantonese;The executive chef has years of experience in hotel kitchens and his short but sweet menu embodies the quintessence of Cantonese cooking. Think barbecue meats, seafood, stir-fries and dim sum at lunch. Certain dishes, such as honey-glazed char siu, are available in limited quantity and should be pre-ordered. Round it out with the silky egg custard in walnut milk. Ask for a table by the windows for the lovely cityscape. Reservations recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
12933;Chōwa;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop C04-1, South Gate, The Canton Place, 46 Haifeng Road, Zhujiang New Town, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1166386;113.3347349;50;true;true;Innovative;TV may well have changed the life of Hongkong chef, Louis Tam, who helms Chōwa. Despite his extensive experience of Western cuisine and stints in Asia, he actually started exploring Franco-Japanese fusion cooking because of a Japanese drama series on TV. The seasonal 6- and 8-course tasting menus embody his vision and everything is made from scratch: the sauces, pickles and bread, even the plum wine. Ask about wine and sake pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
12934;Tao Ran Xuan (Liwan);China Mainland;Guangzhou;50 Shamian South Street, Liwan, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.108924;113.238898;82;false;true;Cantonese;The ubiquitous Chinese interior and live zither music playing at night may seem incongruous given the European exterior, but the authentic Cantonese food with regional offerings is so good you will probably choose to gloss over the oxymoron. Early risers come for an authentic dim sum brekky – don’t miss their shrimp dumplings, and thousand-year egg puff pastry with young ginger. Baked No.1 chicken with sand ginger boasts springy skin and silky meat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12935;Summer Palace;China Mainland;Guangzhou;2F, Shangri-La Hotel, 1 Huizhan East Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.10479;113.364695;82;false;false;Cantonese;The majestic red and gold colour scheme is a fitting lead-in to the Cantonese classics reimagined by Chef Chan with a refined touch. Try his juicy and tender char siu or the Peking duck with its dark and crispy caramelised skin. The array of dim sum on offer, such as apple sauce char siu puff pastry, is also a highlight. With vivid colour and varied textures, the steamed red yeast rice roll stuffed with minced shrimp in a crispy crust is enticing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
12936;Xin Cuo;China Mainland;Guangzhou;Shop 801, 8F, K11 Art Mall, 6 Zhujiang East Road, Tianhe, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1209651;113.3207375;48;false;false;Chao Zhou;The restaurant opened its doors in 2021 in an art-themed shopping mall. It serves ten set menus at a range of prices, featuring ingredients from around the world prepared in Chaozhou style. Dishes are traditional, yet bold and creative. The cold pigeon appetiser is steeped in a herbal broth for a whole day, exuding deep herbal aromas. The simple room is elegant and the terrace is ideal for alfresco dining.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12937;Liang Jia Cai Guan;China Mainland;Guangzhou;683 Nanhua East Road, Haizhu, Guangzhou, China Mainland;23.1142607;113.2668785;81;true;true;Cantonese;Its facade may not be grand, but regulars don’t come for the glitz.. Originally a food stall in Changdi Road over 40 years ago, it has moved to a three-story building in the old town of Haizhu district, but the chefs, the menu and the affordable food haven’t changed one bit. Specialities include deep-fried marinated pork intestine served with a homemade tomato dip, and plain steamed Qingyuan chicken.;Cash only;[]
12938;Cuubo;United Kingdom;Birmingham;49 High Street, Harborne, Birmingham, B17 9NT, United Kingdom;52.4606671;-1.9441865;30;true;true;Modern British;Adding to the growing food scene in the Birmingham suburb of Harborne is this Kickstarter-funded spot from a local chef. The space is small and stylish, with the feel of a contemporary bistro, while the contented diners and lively soundtrack combine to bring a pleasant buzz to the atmosphere. The menu is proudly British and fiercely seasonal, coming across in well-crafted dishes like a wonderful frozen rhubarb dessert with peanut brittle and vanilla ice cream. The cooking is all the better for its absence of unnecessary frippery.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12939;MAYA;United Kingdom;Manchester;40 Chorlton Street, Manchester, M1 3HW, United Kingdom;53.4775258;-2.2362009;47;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Manchester, close to the famous Canal Street, sits this impressively renovated basement restaurant. It’s an elegant, beautifully appointed place, with an art deco feel and a large cocktail bar that feels appropriate for an area of the city known for its party scene. The dishes often have a modern make-up but the kitchen’s classical skillset is evident in finely executed elements like a well-made sauce bonne femme to accompany top quality turbot.;Air conditioning;[]
12941;The Duck on the Pond;United Kingdom;South Newington;South Newington, OX15 4JE, United Kingdom;51.9977103;-1.4086608;45;false;true;Traditional British;Parts of this attractive roadside inn reputedly date back to the 16th Century, providing a lovely setting for cooking based around local ingredients. Several of them come from the owners’ own smallholding and others from nearby producers who are named on the menu – sometimes alongside their distance from the restaurant. These ingredients are fashioned into dishes that burst with flavour and don’t overcomplicate matters, like bright, fresh-tasting roasted cod with mussel sauce.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12943;NORD;United Kingdom;Liverpool;100 Old Hall Street, Liverpool, L3 9QJ, United Kingdom;53.4105667;-2.9953124;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city, this spacious restaurant sports modern décor with an almost futuristic edge thanks to the pod-like booth seating. The menu offers plenty of variety, with a mix of international influences resulting in dishes ranging from tandoori beetroot to cod Kiev and asparagus tagliatelle to a traditional Sunday roast. It’s all carefully executed by the kitchen and doesn’t lack for flavour thanks to judicious seasoning. The cheery and chatty service team add to the appeal.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12944;dario&;Germany;Aachen;Promenadenstr. 36, Aachen, 52062, Germany;50.7763186;6.0934302;75;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The chef behind the name is Dario Breuer. He serves modern, creative dishes that are pleasingly minimalist and clearly structured. The "&" in the name deliberately leaves plenty of room for interpretation, because everyone should feel at home here – whether you like laid-back or ambitious cuisine, whether you are here for a meal with friends or colleagues, whether you want to push the boat out or perhaps just drop in for a glass of wine. True, indeed, to its byline: "casual fine dining". The monthly changing dishes are available à la carte or as a tasting menu. The wine list is also impressive, with around 260 items, including big names as well as new finds and a champagne section.;;[]
12946;Roussel's Restaurant La Bonne Adresse;Germany;Bernkastel-Kues;Am Ring 37, Bernkastel-Kues, 54470, Germany;49.904334;7.0476597;100;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Thierry Roussel and Jane Kölchens run this place with dedication. The elegant restaurant exudes cosiness, and the extremely friendly service, directed by your hostess, also contributes to the pleasant atmosphere. At beautifully laid tables, upscale classic cuisine is served in the form of set menus (one vegetarian) or à la carte. They are also happy to share their wine recommendations, including some from their own production. Plus: guestrooms where you will feel right at home.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12947;NaNum;Germany;Berlin;Lindenstraße 90, Berlin, 10969, Germany;52.5025182;13.393981;82;false;true;Korean Contemporary;As soon as you enter the restaurant, you can see into the open kitchen, where chef Jinok Kim puts a modern spin on the culinary traditions of her Korean homeland. Using regional ingredients, some from the restaurant's own garden in Brandenburg, she shows a particular interest in fermented foods. The ingredient-led dishes are beautifully precise. Natural wines accompany the five-course set menu (vegetarian or with meat) served on Wednesdays and Thursdays, and the seven-course set menu (vegetarian or with fish) available on Fridays and Saturdays. The space is pleasantly pared back and the service is very friendly. Jinok Kim is also a ceramicist and makes the crockery on which the dishes are served – the studio is also located in the building. The restaurant is located not far from Checkpoint Charlie, on a small square (with a lovely terrace) opposite the Jewish Museum.;Terrace;[]
12948;Macionga;Germany;Berlin;Xantener Straße 9, Berlin, 10707, Germany;52.4990506;13.3109617;36;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Not far from Ku'damm (Kurfürstendamm), this attractive, sleek restaurant is named after its owner – sommelier and winemaker André Macionga. In keeping with his passion for wine, the wine list is very nicely curated, and the restaurant also has its own wine shop. The kitchen turns out tasty dishes with a regional and seasonal bent – fine, well-rounded compositions that combine classic and modern elements. The portions are somewhat smaller, meaning you can try several dishes. The beef tartare is a classic.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12949;Schneider Stube;Germany;Görlitz;Peterstraße 8, Görlitz, 02826, Germany;51.1580896;14.9913108;37;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Hotel Tuchmacher, ensconced in a pretty Renaissance town house with this delightfully cosy restaurant, is an institution here in Görlitz. The classic regional menu includes dishes such as Wiener schnitzel, stewed rabbit leg on Leipziger Allerlei vegetables, and stewed brook trout roll on pickled vegetables. Almost all of the wines are also available by the glass. In summer, the courtyard with its terrace is absolutely idyllic! "Bleicherstube" and "Zunftsaal" are their attractive salons. The location in the heart of the old town is charming – it is next to the church (Pfarrkirche St Peter and Paul) and not far from the Lausatian Neiße River that borders Germany, Poland and the Czech Republic.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12950;Le Schloss Halberg;Germany;Saarbrücken;Franz-Mai-Straße 1, Saarbrücken, 66121, Germany;49.2235448;7.0300896;49;false;false;Classic French;This restaurant set up in one wing of the castle, which was built between 1877 and 1880, has rightly proved to be a hit with diners. Its popularity is due both to the beautiful historical estate with its delightful terrace, and to the classic French cuisine, which ranges from Iberico pork chop with white bean stew and sauce pistou to œuf à la neige on a vanilla crème anglaise with caramel and almonds. The food is made with fresh top-notch ingredients, eschewing unnecessary frills in favour of full-bodied flavour. The penchant for France extends to the sophisticated wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
12951;Zum Simonbräu;Germany;Bitburg;Am Markt 7, Bitburg, 54634, Germany;49.9738897;6.5223181;47;false;false;German;A down-to-earth pub, just the way we like them! Part of the Bitburger Brewery, this place has an attractive decor of solid wooden tables (no tablecloths here!), walls decorated with pictures, and modern details that foster a pleasantly lively atmosphere. The charming team serves home-style regional dishes, as well as more sophisticated options. Cordon bleu with Eifelschwein pork and "Ōra King salmon – tartare & fried" whet the appetite. The inexpensive dish of the day is popular with the lunchtime crowd. You can also spend the night in one of the spruce guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
12953;Nishimuramen;South Korea;Seoul;4F, 265 Donggyo-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03983, South Korea;37.56337;126.92526;58;false;true;Ramen;Nishimuramen, a famed restaurant in Fukuoka known for its unique marriage of Japanese ramen and French cooking, has finally opened its doors in Seoul. The culinary offspring of Chef Takahito Nishimura born out of his unparalleled enthusiasm for ramen, this noodle joint flaunts his distinctive style by bringing out the rich, multifaceted flavors of ramen through an intriguing union of toppings, sauces and oils. While maintaining the authenticity of ramen, the kitchen has successfully localized its fare, for instance, by using laver oil, Cheongyang chili pepper, and tsukemono (Japanese pickles) in the style of white kimchi. Freshly cooked pot rice mixed with cheese and ramen broth (like risotto) is another standout dish that asserts this eatery’s unique role in the gastronomic universe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12954;Gaggen;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 19-1 Apgujeong-ro 80-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06015, South Korea;37.52451;127.04523;66;true;false;Japanese;Gaggen is a portmanteau of the Chinese characters ”雅” (a) and “元” (won) pronounced Japanese-style (ga, gen). Each character is a syllable from the names of the chef couple Choi Hyun-a and Won Jin-hui, who received culinary training in Japan at the noted Tokyo restaurants Kanda and Kurogi, respectively. Seasonality, a core characteristic of Japanese cuisine, is what clearly defines Gaggen’s menu. Rare gems, including Kurogi-style somen noodles, aromatic dishes featuring freshly roasted and ground sesame seeds, and warabi mochi made with bracken starch, are a treat to the senses. Accompanied by detailed informative explanations by the chefs and their hospitality, dining here is a pure delight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12955;Rialto;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 13 Samseong-ro 149-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06063, South Korea;37.52318;127.04655;69;false;true;Italian;Over the past few years, a streamlined selection of antipasti, paired with a focus on primi dishes, has been an overarching trend across Seoul’s Italian dining landscape. In line with the trend, this fine diner offers a simple menu while remaining true to its northern Italian roots, as highlighted by the name “Rialto,” and to the chef’s unique culinary philosophy, sensibilities and style. Winning dishes include tajarin and cacio e pepe, deeply flavored with a beguiling harmony of butter and cheese. The kitchen’s other pastas flaunt an equally excellent balance of sauce flavors. Pickled ponytail radish is yet another standout that evokes the endearing flavors of our memories.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12956;Sool052;South Korea;Seoul;26 Gosanja-ro 14-gil, Seongdong-gu, Seoul, 04750, South Korea;37.56344;127.03766;80;false;false;Korean;Sool052 is a portmanteau of “sool” (alcohol) and “052,” the area code of the region the chefs live in. It’s a Korean gastropub brimming with culinary ideas as playful as the restaurant’s name. Employing diverse fermented pastes and fermentation techniques, the basis of most Korean cuisine, the chef duo offers unique dishes that are household names yet prepared with exceptional care and attention to detail to draw out unforgettable flavors. On top of this, the varied menu selections tend to go well together, making it easy to enjoy multiple items at once. These allures make Sool052 a perfect place to experience the exquisite harmony between Korean food and Korean alcohol.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
12957;Escondido;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 61-7 Hannam-daero 20-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04419, South Korea;37.53517;127.01046;98;true;false;Mexican;Escondido is a space replete with Chef Jin Woo-bum’s passion for Mexican food. His infatuation with the cuisine led him to Mexico, where he steadily learned and improved his culinary skills while engrossed in Mexican culture. The restaurant offers bona fide Mexican cuisine with the chef’s unique twists. He conjures up finely nuanced flavors by making particularly nuanced use of tortilla and mole, the staples of Mexican cuisine. One last tip: pairing your dish with tequila, mezcal or a cocktail will take your gourmet experience at Escondido to a whole new level.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
12958;Sanro;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 518 Dosan-daero, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06070, South Korea;37.52417;127.04978;73;true;false;Japanese;Chef Yoo Sung-yup’s culinary mastery and dedication to washoku, or traditional Japanese cuisine, shine through at Sanro. The entrance greets diners with a hanging scroll that reads “三露,” the name of this spot that expresses the Japanese practice of sprinkling the entrance with water three times after welcoming customers into an establishment. The nuanced and chic objets d’art adorning every corner are in sync with the vibes and sensibilities the chef seeks to convey through his menu and dining space. When refreshing seasonal ingredients meet his ardor for culinary art and sophisticated skills, what’s born is a smorgasbord of subtle flavors that invariably soothes the palate throughout the meal. To top it off, the service here is as impeccable as the clean and refined flavors of the chef’s washoku cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
12959;Mipildam;South Korea;Seoul;22 Seongji 3-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04083, South Korea;37.54658;126.91419;61;true;false;Mandu;Tucked in a quiet yet youthfully vibrant alley in Hapjeong-dong, Mipildam is an unpretentious little spot specializing in handmade mandutguk (dumpling soup) in northern Korean style. The recipe for this lightly flavored dish is based on the home recipe of the young owner couple’s grandmother, who was born and raised in Hwanghae Province, now in North Korea. The perfect combination of plump dumplings packed with juicy filling and the broth infused with subtle flavors (and without any additional artificial flavors) is not something a diner can easily resist. In addition to the signature soup, the menu offers seasonally updated traditional dishes that reflect the couple’s passion for serving good food. The seating layout accommodates solo diners as well as couples and friend groups.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
12960;Trio;Denmark;Copenhagen;Axel Towers, Jernbanegade 11, Copenhagen, 1608 V, Denmark;55.6757459;12.5656841;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The highest restaurant in the city is located on floors 9 and 10 of the striking Axel Towers building, making it an ideal place to enjoy a cocktail while taking in the view. The menu – available in either a tasting or à la carte format – brings together a range of global influences, from Japanese (yuzu kosho) to South American (hamachi ceviche), with fabulous results. The wine pairings are particularly well-chosen.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
12963;OTO;Iceland;Reykjavík;Hverfisgata 44, Reykjavík, 101, Iceland;64.1461331;-21.9278614;80;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Fun, lively and offering something fresh and exciting to the Reykjavik dining scene, OTO is one of the hottest tickets in town thanks to its bustling atmosphere and Italian-Japanese fusion cuisine. The uncommon pairing works a treat, with their shared ingredient-led approach resulting in dishes that showcase clever cross-cuisine combinations and deliver pure, natural flavours – like a take on scallops Florentine enhanced by the piquancy of ponzu and the warming spice of shichimi. If you can’t decide, go for their version of a kaiseki menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12964;Leijontornet;Sweden;Stockholm;Lilla Nygatan 5, Stockholm, 111 28, Sweden;59.324333;18.0678748;50;false;true;European;After a few years as Djuret, this long-established restaurant has returned to its original guise and provides heaps of old-school charm. The dining room is full of character, with armchairs, vaulted brick ceilings and candlelit tables all adding to the appeal. The cooking has heavy French and other European influences, providing bold flavours across a wide selection of generous dishes. Expect plenty of premium produce, from lobster to turbot, and an extensive, similarly luxurious wine list.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12965;Minh Mat;Sweden;Stockholm;Odengatan 94, Stockholm, 113 22, Sweden;59.3406147;18.041789;87;false;false;Vietnamese;There is a wonderfully personal touch to this well-run Vietnamese restaurant, with posters and old photos adorning the walls, and an array of objects decorating the room. It’s an enjoyably relaxed setting for the cooking, which uses impressive ingredients – some of them from local producers – and mines plenty of flavour from simple-looking compositions. A light, smooth cream of corn sauce, for example, is a skilful and delicious accompaniment to quality grilled prawns.;;[]
12966;Molskroen;Denmark;Ebeltoft;Hovedgaden 16, Femmøller Strand, Ebeltoft, 8400, Denmark;56.229523;10.604763;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A table on the charming terrace of this relaxed and stylish seaside inn is the perfect spot to enjoy traditional French cuisine, as well as more modern interpretations of the classics. The chef collaborates with a local organic farmer and the restaurant’s comprehensive sustainability programme includes staff welfare.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
12967;Gaijin;Finland;Helsinki;Bulevardi 6, Helsinki, 00120, Finland;60.1659101;24.9419414;47;false;true;Asian;Gaijin comes with dark, contemporary décor, a buzzing atmosphere, attentive service and an emphasis on sharing. Its experienced owners offer boldly flavoured, skilfully presented modern takes on Japanese, Korean and Northern Chinese recipes. The tasting menus are a great way to sample the different cuisines.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12968;Le Ankka;Finland;Helsinki;Huvilakatu 28, Helsinki, 00150, Finland;60.1577296;24.9426967;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This tiny little restaurant's natural buzz is enhanced by the presence of an open kitchen that feels like it's fully part of the room, while a racing green and matt black colour scheme contribute to the décor’s moody feel. Throughout the cooking, there is a desire to pair Finnish produce with classical French techniques and flavours – exemplified by the use of ‘almond potatoes’ from Lapland to make a vichyssoise. The wine list is made up of mostly natural and organic choices.;;[]
12970;Bistro Bardot;Finland;Helsinki;Kluuvikatu 1, Helsinki, 00100, Finland;60.1680778;24.9477284;88;true;true;French;Exposed brick and pipework give this two-roomed brasserie a rustic, slightly retro feel that chimes perfectly with its buoyant atmosphere. It’s a deservedly busy place, named after actress Brigitte Bardot and taking a similarly French outlook on culinary matters too. The extensive à la carte offers all manner of classic brasserie staples, from steak au poivre to tarte Tatin, while the 'menu du jour' provides a simpler, good value selection. The wine list has some appealing French favourites and the friendly team serve the large numbers with ease.;Air conditioning;[]
12972;Kockeriet;Sweden;Malmo;Norra Vallgatan 28, Malmo, 211 25, Sweden;55.6082408;13.00533;56;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a characterful 17C former grain warehouse, owned by Malmö-born TV chef Tareq Taylor, a young and talented team prepare well-balanced contemporary dishes with great precision. Scandinavian produce is at its heart, with some coming from the kitchen garden. The timbered dining room is relaxed and inviting, the service friendly, and the drinks pairings well-conceived.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
12975;Hillenberg;Sweden;Stockholm;Humlegårdsgatan 14, Stockholm, 114 46, Sweden;59.336674;18.0759101;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Perfectly pitched for busy Humlegårdsgatan is this stylish take on a classic brasserie. It has a smart, elegant feel and a hugely impressive wine cellar. Appealing Swedish classics are immensely satisfying yet exhibit a subtle modern touch and sense of finesse.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
12977;Statholderens Mat og Vinkjeller;Norway;Oslo;Rådhusgate 11, Oslo, 0151, Norway;59.9094876;10.7431522;74;true;false;Classic Cuisine;The informal sister of Statholdergaarden is set over three rooms in the old vaults of the same 17C house. One wall of the large entranceway is filled with wine bottles. Choose from a huge array of small plates or go for the 10 course tasting menu.;;[]
12983;Aamanns 1921;Denmark;Copenhagen;Niels Hemmingsens Gade 19-21, Copenhagen, 1153 K, Denmark;55.6802762;12.5758817;96;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A visit to this appealing city centre restaurant is made all the more enjoyable thanks to its original stone arches and friendly, attentive service. Lunch and dinner both focus on excellent traditional smørrebrød made from quality produce. A homemade, sustainable approach is taken as they grind and mill their own flours, marinate their herring for 6-12 months and gather the herbs for their snaps.;Air conditioning;[]
12984;Alimentum;Denmark;Aalborg;Løkkegade 23, Aalborg, 9000, Denmark;57.0457734;9.9292863;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The foliage-covered walls should be an immediate clue as to this restaurant’s nature-focused ethos. Plant and animal produce both come from their farm, Lille Østergaard, and are used with a seasonal approach – meaning winter menus feature a host of preserved ingredients. There’s a no-waste policy too, so don’t be surprised if you find both tongue and tail in your pork dish. If it’s a special occasion and you enjoy watching chefs in action, book the ‘Foodlab’ counter for a menu of around 30 courses.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
12985;Høst;Denmark;Copenhagen;Nørre Farimagsgade 41, Copenhagen, 1364 K, Denmark;55.6832973;12.565939;21;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Not far from Nørreport station, Høst is a busy neighbourhood restaurant that offers an enjoyable atmosphere and good value cooking. Dishes are modern, boldly flavoured and visually impressive, and the set menus come with lots of extra surprises. Nordic fish and shellfish feature largely, while the vegetarian dishes – like celeriac with truffle and ´Vesterhavsost’ – are some of the highlights of the menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12986;Radio;Denmark;Copenhagen;Julius Thomsens Gade 12, Copenhagen, 1632 V, Denmark;55.6820619;12.5543448;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s an unfussy style to this informal restaurant, with its wood-clad walls and cool anglepoise lighting. The regularly changing menu is solidly Nordic in base, but there’s the odd international influence like yuzu kosho or vadouvan curry too. The full-flavoured dishes use organic ingredients grown in the restaurant’s nearby fields and showcase well thought-through combinations.;;[]
12987;Sankt Annæ;Denmark;Copenhagen;Sankt Annæ Plads 12, Copenhagen, 1250 K, Denmark;55.6814191;12.5912007;26;true;true;Smørrebrød;An attractive terraced building with a traditional, rather quaint interior. There's a seasonal à la carte and a daily blackboard menu: prices can vary so check before ordering. The lobster and shrimp – fresh from local fjords – are a hit.;Terrace;[]
12988;Kødbyens Fiskebar;Denmark;Copenhagen;Flæsketorvet 100, Copenhagen, 1711 V, Denmark;55.6679589;12.5594649;77;false;false;Seafood;This buzzy, industrial-style restaurant is set – somewhat incongruously – in a former butcher’s shop in the old meatpacking district, and was one of the pioneers in transforming the area into a leisure destination. Menus feature freshly prepared seafood dishes which are based around the latest catch, with oysters being a speciality. The terrace is a popular spot come summer.;Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
12989;Tèrra;Denmark;Copenhagen;Ryesgade 65, Copenhagen, 2100, Denmark;55.694735;12.5708358;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Organic;A zero waste restaurant with an impressive open kitchen sunk below ground level. Set menus offer creative, modern dishes inspired by the chef’s global travels. These come with original combinations, purity of flavour and a lightness of touch. Wines have a natural, organic and biodynamic focus.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12990;Petri;Sweden;Stockholm;Kommendörsgatan 16, Stockholm, 11448, Sweden;59.33856;18.07944;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The name is a diminutive version of ‘petrichor’, which refers to the lovely scent that accompanies rain after a warm period. There is a similarly pleasant cosiness to the restaurant itself, with its intimate and charming atmosphere. Dishes like white pepper ice cream with porcini are well thought out in their creativity, showcasing a good understanding of balance and flavour. Wine pairings and homemade non-alcoholic options complete the package.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
12993;ROKS;Denmark;Tórshavn;Gongin 5, Tórshavn, 100, Denmark;62.0091465;-6.7697262;64;true;true;Seafood;This sister to Ræst is set in an ancient, turf-roofed building and has a rustic inner, a laid-back ambience and chatty staff. The set menus reflect the bounty from the surrounding waters, from local sea-urchins to langoustines and Greenlandic snow crab. All these dishes are cooked with great precision to unlock their natural flavours.;;[]
12994;Varemottaket;Norway;Oslo;Dronning Eufemias gate 37, Oslo, 0194, Norway;59.9072761;10.7590168;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Pumping music and a relaxed, friendly team ensure there’s always a fun vibe at this tiny restaurant situated behind the Annis Pølsemakeri butchery and farm shop. You enter via the shop’s deliveries door, hence the name ‘Varemottaket’, which translates as ‘The Goods Reception’. The narrow, intimate space is filled with high tables and stools, where diners can enjoy a tasting menu with a strong element of charcoal grilling. Unsurprisingly, the fabulous dry-aged meats from the butcher’s make an appearance, such as entrecôte of Norwegian beef.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
12996;Ræst;Denmark;Tórshavn;Gongin 8, Tórshavn, 100, Denmark;62.0091389;-6.7698154;46;false;false;Creative;Take a seat at the shared table at this traditional turf-roofed house with characterful, low-ceilinged dining rooms. Its name means ‘fermented’, and the set menu is indeed centred around fermentation and ageing, with an insight into the heritage of Faroese food and flavours. Dishes are bold, creative and well-balanced.;Interesting wine list;[]
12998;Human;Sweden;Gothenburg;Risåsgatan 8, Gothenburg, 41307, Sweden;57.6944348;11.9559239;98;true;false;Creative;In a quiet residential street behind the 17C Skansen Kronan fortress, you'll find this stylishly decorated restaurant decked out with neutral tones and vintage furniture. The first solo project for Martin Moses, it focuses on New Nordic cooking, which is executed with a skilful touch. In the evening you can sample the quality dishes from either a small or large tasting menu, with a 4 course set menu available at lunch.;;[]
12999;Hærværk;Denmark;Aarhus;Frederiks Allé 105, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.1478296;10.1963525;30;true;true;Danish;Run by a group of friends, this restaurant’s ersatz industrial feel comes from a concrete floor, stark white décor and a glass-fronted fridge of hanging meats. The menu focuses on organic produce in dishes that are earthy and natural. Their ingredient options initially made them think more about sustainability, which now underpins all their actions.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13000;Smör;Finland;Turku;Läntinen Rantakatu 3, Turku, 20100, Finland;60.4501368;22.2720816;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There is a well-executed fusion of the old and the new at this city centre restaurant. Stylish, contemporary décor is brought into the vaulted cellar of a 19C riverside merchant's house,  whilst the cooking combines traditional techniques with modern presentation. The finest Nordic ingredients run through the creative dishes, with the combinations offering memorable contrasts of flavours and textures.;;[]
13001;Brasserie Blanche;Norway;Oslo;Josefinesgate 23, Oslo, 0351, Norway;59.9232136;10.7260967;84;true;false;French;A cosy French restaurant housed in an 18C building which was originally a stable and later spent time as a garage and an interior furnishings store. It has a small front terrace, a bar decorated with wine boxes and a wall made of corks. The chef is a Francophile and creates flavoursome classic French dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13003;Nokka;Finland;Helsinki;Kanavaranta 7f, Helsinki, 00160, Finland;60.169035;24.960124;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Finnish;A huge anchor and propeller mark out this harbourside warehouse and, inside, three high-ceilinged rooms juxtapose brick with varnished wood. An on-view kitchen allows you to watch wonderful, sustainably sourced ingredients being prepared in a rustic style. There is a strongly Finnish heart to the cooking, which includes classic dishes like freshly made blini topped with crème fraîche, pickled red onions and vendace roe. Friendly, professional service adds to the experience.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13005;Ulla Winbladh;Sweden;Stockholm;Rosendalsvägen 8, Stockholm, 115 21, Sweden;59.3281207;18.100003;71;true;true;Swedish;Ulla Winbladh was originally built as a steam bakery for the 1897 Stockholm World Fair and is set in charming parkland beside the Skansen open-air museum. Sit on the terrace or in the older, more characterful part of the building. Typical Swedish dishes include the likes of fish roe and sweet and sour herring.;Terrace;[]
13007;Bravo;Norway;Stavanger;Pedersgata 71, Stavanger, 4013, Norway;58.9697952;5.7464651;55;false;true;Norwegian, Modern Cuisine;Bravo was opened at the end of 2022 by a young couple on their first venture – and their enthusiasm and friendliness infuse this sweet little restaurant in a converted house. The menu is refreshingly concise and chef-owner Daniel, from his open kitchen, concentrates on clean, seasonal flavours using local ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13008;Voisine;Sweden;Stockholm;Erstagatan 21, Stockholm, 116 36, Sweden;59.3140798;18.0903578;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Homely and cosy, there is a wonderful lack of pretension to this French-inspired bistro. Flavourful dishes from the small open kitchen include classical French desserts like blueberry clafoutis and Paris-Brest. The restaurant has a lived-in feel, with stripped wooden flooring and leather banquettes. The owners have a wine bar next door and it shows in the excellent wine list and shelves stacked full of bottles.;Interesting wine list;[]
13009;aster;Sweden;Malmo;Jagaregatan 6, Malmo, 211 19, Sweden;55.6112313;12.9894423;45;true;false;Contemporary;The faux industrial décor feels like an appropriate fit for this restaurant housed in a former warehouse, in an area once home to the city's shipyards. The kitchen forms part of the room, bringing a certain energy to proceedings, and the friendly team also help to create an enjoyable atmosphere. The short menu offers dishes with a rustic edge, where distinct flavours are nicely balanced – such as minty salsa verde with grilled lamb loin, or sharp apple cutting through a rich chocolate dessert.;Terrace;[]
13010;Farang;Sweden;Stockholm;Tulegatan 7, Stockholm, 111 53, Sweden;59.3417041;18.0625801;67;false;false;South East Asian;The flavours of Southeast Asia are the inspiration behind this stylish restaurant and bar that occupies the building once home to the Stockholm Electric Company. The unusual front door harks back to its former occupation, but once inside it's a chic space with soft lighting and a large open kitchen. The colorful, zingy cooking includes Thai dishes like laab and crying tiger beef, along with Vietnamese-style sashimi and other influences from the wider region. Strong service, sensible prices and a fun atmosphere complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13011;Cru;Norway;Oslo;Ingelbrecht, Knudssøns gate 1, Oslo, 0365, Norway;59.9272824;10.7227645;87;false;true;Norwegian;This friendly neighbourhood restaurant offers guests a choice of dining experiences. Upstairs, in the rustic dining room, they serve a 5 course set menu with inventive British touches and 2 optional extra courses. Downstairs, in the wine bar, you can enjoy everything from snacks to a full meal from an à la carte that includes dishes like bone marrow with beef tartare, chimichurri and toast.;Interesting wine list;[]
13012;Arakataka;Norway;Oslo;Mariboes gate 7, Oslo, 0183, Norway;59.9164457;10.7505162;79;true;true;Norwegian;A smart glass-fronted restaurant with a central food bar, an open kitchen and a buzzy atmosphere. Choose from a concise menu of seasonal Norwegian small plates – they recommend 3 savoury dishes plus a dessert per person.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13013;Plah;Norway;Oslo;Sommerrogata 1, Oslo, 0255, Norway;59.91523;10.7196336;33;false;false;Thai;Norwegian ingredients blended with Thai flavours is the core concept behind this well-run restaurant centred around an open kitchen. The cooking comes in the form of a seafood-focused tasting menu that takes you on a real journey through Thai cuisine and features eye-catching, imaginative dishes that are full of flavour. Adding to the experience are the lively atmosphere and attentive service. Sister restaurant Ahaan offers a simpler take on Bangkok street food, with both eateries housed inside the Sommerro Hotel but independently run.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13014;B.A.R.;Sweden;Stockholm;Blasieholmsgatan 4a, Stockholm, 111 48, Sweden;59.3300196;18.0769372;25;false;true;Seafood;This bright, buzzy restaurant is just a cast away from the waterfront and has a semi-industrial fish-market look. Choose your seafood from the fridge or the tank, along with a cooking style, a sauce and one of their interesting sides.;Air conditioning;[]
13015;Kolonialen Bislett;Norway;Oslo;Sofies gate 16, Oslo, 0170, Norway;59.9229189;10.7352867;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Close to the stadium you’ll find this popular neighbourhood bistro, which was previously a grocer’s shop for nearly 80 years. The concise, keenly priced menu includes oysters, cured meats and wholesome Norwegian classics that have been brought up-to-date. There’s a diverse selection of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13016;Trattoria La Strega;Sweden;Gothenburg;Aschebergsgatan 23B, Gothenburg, 411 27, Sweden;57.6962089;11.9709436;16;true;true;Italian;Run by passionate, charming owners, this lively little trattoria is nestled within a quiet residential area, and serves the kind of authentic Northern Italian food that you would find in a good trattoria in Piemonte or Triveneto. Boldly flavoured dishes are best enjoyed from the 'Menu Degustazione', accompanied by a candlelit table and a glass of wine from the extensive Italian selection.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13018;Bryghuset Vendia - Gourmet;Denmark;Hjørring;Markedsgade 9, Hjørring, 9800, Denmark;57.4569967;9.9930341;54;true;false;Creative;A microbrewery plays host to a stylish brasserie and this tiny gourmet restaurant, which consists of just three tables. It serves an 11 course themed surprise menu of creative, elaborately presented dishes designed to stimulate the taste buds.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13019;Moment;Denmark;Rønde;Ravnen 1, Rønde, 8410, Denmark;56.2814408;10.5877073;96;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A welcoming glow draws you towards this restaurant, as you navigate the dark streets of the small hamlet of Rønde. It’s clear that sustainability runs through Moment’s veins: its permaculture garden guides the menus, the chefs explain the philosophy behind every dish and there’s a remarkable selection of natural wines. Depending on the day, you can choose between a short and a long version of the tasting menu, where well-presented plant-led recipes give prominence to vegetables with dishes such as ‘greens’ or ‘corn, tomatillo and tomato’. Fully vegan and vegetarian menus are available too.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13020;Ghrelin;Denmark;Aarhus;Dagmar Petersensgade 111, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.1665519;10.2275241;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;An elegant, modern restaurant with an open kitchen at its centre, set in the up-and-coming dockland area. Set menus showcase good quality produce and the skilful cooking has a classic French base and some complex, creative touches. Attentive, professional service completes the picture.;;[]
13021;Møf;Denmark;Aarhus;Vesterport 10, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.1582567;10.1998478;39;true;false;Danish;Ask for a seat at the counter to watch the young chef-owners cook in the open kitchen at this cosy, relaxed restaurant. The cooking is Danish at heart and based on local produce, providing great value in dishes that accentuate the central ingredient, like pumpkin gnocchi with smoked and pickled pumpkin. An impressive selection of organic and natural wines are available, as well as a wide range of orange wines.;Counter dining;[]
13022;Shelter;Finland;Helsinki;Kanavaranta 7, Helsinki, 00160, Finland;60.1689876;24.9592984;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Finnish;A fun night out is guaranteed at this converted warehouse in a corner of Katajanokka Harbour, close to Uspenskin Cathedral. The serving team are enthusiastic, the atmosphere is contagious, and from the open kitchen come meticulously prepared and appealingly presented dishes that deliver on flavour.;Terrace;[]
13024;Hotell Borgholm;Sweden;Borgholm;Trädgårdsgatan 15, Borgholm, 387 31, Sweden;56.8788038;16.6575365;73;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The beautiful island of Öland is famous for its wild herbs, and that’s reflected in the cooking at this historic hotel’s restaurant, where the chefs enhance their elaborate dishes with thyme, basil and a host of other flavours from their garden. The cooking comes in a tasting menu format, either short or long, and marries classical techniques with subtle modern ones – all while delivering bold flavours and original combinations The wine list is a real treasure trove for oenophiles.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13027;Restaurant Saga;Norway;Trondheim;Fjordgata 1, Trondheim, 7010, Norway;63.4344185;10.4035181;48;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There is some eclectic, striking art adorning the walls of this relaxed and trendy restaurant with an adjoining wine bar. The array of bottles to choose from is as impressive as you’d expect, with real depth to the list and numerous vintages from heavy hitting producers. The 8 course tasting menu offers modern, restrained cooking and original touches – like a deconstructed XO sauce – that enhance the dishes.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13029;Kappo Andō;Denmark;Copenhagen;Øster Farimagsgade 93, Copenhagen, 2100, Denmark;55.6953732;12.5794116;33;false;true;Japanese Contemporary;Contemporary Japanese cooking and an extensive sake selection are on offer at this chic restaurant just outside the city centre. The décor suits the Japanese theme, with dark wood furnishings and a pure, minimalist feel. Flavourful dishes are underpinned by quality ingredients, with the sashimi proving a highlight and a 'yakitori of the day' option allowing you to enjoy the smoky flavours of meat cooked over binchotan charcoal. Choose between an à la carte or a 7 course tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
13030;Kiin Kiin;Denmark;Copenhagen;Guldbergsgade 21, Copenhagen, 2200 N, Denmark;55.6918598;12.557336;84;true;false;Thai, Contemporary;A charming restaurant, whose name means ‘come and eat’. Start with refined versions of street food in the moody lounge, then head for the tasteful dining room decorated with golden Buddhas and fresh flowers. Menus offer modern, personal interpretations of Thai dishes, which have vibrant flavour combinations.;Air conditioning;[]
13031;JORD;Sweden;Linkoping;Johannesborgparken 1A, Linkoping, 582 49, Sweden;58.4073604;15.6022776;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;‘Forest to plate’ is the message here, with wild and hyper-seasonal ingredients at the fore. Some of the produce is foraged, whilst meat is often hunted by the owner in the surrounding area. The surprise tasting menu delivers a large array of creative dishes with intriguing blends of flavours and textures. Preserving, pickling, smoking and curing are all done in-house, giving new life to the local ingredients.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13033;TIDES;Iceland;Reykjavík;Austurbakki 2, Reykjavík, 101, Iceland;64.1502916;-21.9318558;63;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Surrounded by the sea, mountains and the old harbour, this stylish restaurant benefits from an enviable location nestled inside The Reykjavík EDITION hotel. Quality Icelandic produce forms the core of the menu, which includes carefully cooked dishes like baked arctic char with celeriac, apples and smoked almonds. The warm colours and tasteful décor help make a visit here all the more enjoyable.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13034;Restaurant Palægade;Denmark;Copenhagen;Palægade 8, Copenhagen, 1261 K, Denmark;55.6823359;12.5863548;54;true;true;Smørrebrød, Danish;It’s easy to see why this cosy, classic eatery is so popular: from the professional, friendly service to the good value, well-crafted cooking, the team here get everything spot on. Lunch sees smørrebrød brought up-to-date, with seasonal European dishes on offer in the evening.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13036;Det Røde Pakhus;Denmark;Rønne;Snellemark 30, Rønne, Rønne, 3700, Denmark;55.1014268;14.6966327;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Two experienced owners bring their knowledge together at this modern, wood-furnished restaurant set in the centre of Bornholm’s capital. The chef is passionate about good produce and skilfully prepares local ingredients to create refined, imaginative dishes. Desserts are a highlight.;Terrace;[]
13037;The Pescatarian;Denmark;Copenhagen;Amaliegade 49, Copenhagen, 1256 K, Denmark;55.6880348;12.5965081;29;true;false;Creative, Contemporary;Dine in one of three rooms at this buzzing, minimalist restaurant that, unsurprisingly, features plenty of freshly caught seafood. Choose from the fish-based tasting menu or a vegetarian version, both offered in either 4 or 6 courses. The chef prepares modern dishes with all the typical Danish hallmarks, including preservation techniques and a lightness of touch.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13039;NISCH;Sweden;Stockholm;Dalagatan 42, Stockholm, 113 24, Sweden;59.3408266;18.0468559;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This pleasantly relaxed little neighbourhood restaurant is sleekly and stylishly decorated with a monochrome colour scheme. For its part, the kitchen produces accomplished dishes and boasts some good eco-credentials. The modern, understated Nordic set menu is inspired by global flavours and changes every few weeks. The interesting wine list is mainly organic and biodynamic in nature.;;[]
13040;Atelier 33;Denmark;Aarhus;M.P. Bruuns Gade 33, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.1479366;10.203654;29;false;false;French;Bouillabaisse, Paris-Brest and a great selection of burgundies… with a menu like this, it’s hard to believe you’re not in France. Classic bistros and brasseries are the inspiration behind this charming place with a warm, friendly atmosphere. Danish produce is nevertheless at the heart of the cooking, which provides well-executed and satisfying versions of these traditional dishes. The lunch menu includes lighter bites like a croque madame, while at dinner you can pick between the à la carte and a surprise 4 course seasonal menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
13041;Washoku TOMO;Sweden;Stockholm;Timmermansgatan 15, Stockholm, 118 25, Sweden;59.3187561;18.059922;38;true;true;Japanese;In the western half of Södermalm, Chef-Owner Tomoko Hayashi is bolstering Stockholm’s Japanese dining scene by offering an omakase experience that doesn’t break the bank. While this is Japanese cooking that’s not entirely focussed on sushi, seafood nevertheless plays a central role in the menu. The produce comes from all over the world, be it Spanish sea bass, Argentinian prawns or Canadian black cod. Tomoko leads the smooth service herself with personality and professionalism.;Notable sake list;[]
13042;Madonna;Norway;Oslo;Operagata 17, Oslo, 0194, Norway;59.9073835;10.7560374;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Named in part after the painting by Edvard Munch, it is appropriate that this restaurant sits just a few long strides away from Oslo’s Munch Museum. The dining room is small here and so are the plates, which work well for sharing and provide an appealing range of flavours. The influences are global, so don’t be surprised to see tacos sitting next to chawanmushi on the menu, along with some more typically Norwegian fare. There’s a fun, relaxed vibe in the air, and a pleasing eclecticism to the wine list.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13044;Brút;Iceland;Reykjavík;Radisson Blu 1919 Hotel, Pósthússtræti 2, Reykjavík, 101, Iceland;64.1482483;-21.9364626;43;false;false;Contemporary, Seafood;Seafood lovers will feel right at home at this celebration of wonderful fish and shellfish. The likes of marinated scallops and Icelandic whelks join a roll call of prime quality fish, cooked well by an able kitchen in pleasingly uncomplicated dishes that let the central ingredient shine. Stone floors, upholstered benches and open pipework give the dining room a simple, casual feel – and this is accompanied by a lively atmosphere.;Brunch;[]
13045;xef;Norway;Oslo;Bryggegangen 8, Oslo, 0252, Norway;59.9085991;10.7216599;20;false;false;Spanish Contemporary;A little slice of Spain has landed in the Oslo restaurant scene thanks to this lively spot that sits overlooking the harbour in a modern waterside development. Elaborate and visually striking, dishes are creative but grounded in the influence of northern Spain in particular, including the Chef’s native Galicia. The appearance of components like romesco sauce typify cooking that is as bold in colour as it is in flavour. An excellent Basque cheesecake will ensure your visit ends on a high.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13047;Forma;Sweden;Stockholm;Hornsbruksgatan 28, Stockholm, 117 34, Sweden;59.3160693;18.0346215;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Asian;Chic and sultry, this Södermalm spot delivers the look and vibe of a bar, with the added bonus of flavoursome small plates. The cooking is bang on-trend, blending Nordic and French influences with pan-Asian elements including Korean kimchi, Chinese wontons and a daily selection of Japanese mochi for dessert. If you’re an indecisive diner, go for the keenly priced tasting menu to appreciate the full breadth of the kitchen's talents. Well-versed, professional service is the icing on the cake.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
13049;Brutalisten;Sweden;Stockholm;Regeringsgatan 71, Stockholm, 111 56, Sweden;59.3357902;18.0674683;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Owned and created by German artist Carsten Höller, this intriguing concept restaurant abides by the ‘Brutalist Kitchen Manifesto’. Dishes are labelled as either 'Orthodox Brutalist', 'Brutalist' or 'Semi Brutalist', depending on how far they take the ethos of unadulterated prime ingredients presented with minimal accompaniments, freed from the shackles of unnecessary frippery. The first-rate produce is skilfully cooked with a refreshing emphasis on purity of flavour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13050;Mark;Denmark;Copenhagen;Axeltorv 3, Copenhagen, 1609, Denmark;55.6757346;12.563746;52;true;false;Danish, Country cooking;The produce of the Danish countryside is the inspiration behind this stylish city centre bistro that also features some classical French methods in the kitchen. There is a wonderful feeling of spaciousness to the dining room, with its central counter, high ceilings and modern décor. Top quality Danish ingredients are seasoned and cooked with real skill, resulting in a roster of refined and well-balanced dishes.;;[]
13051;Natura;Finland;Helsinki;Iso Roobertinkatu 11, Helsinki, 00120, Finland;60.1636375;24.9423269;17;true;false;Finnish;Well-chosen Finnish ingredients are used to good effect at this intimate restaurant and techniques like fermenting, pickling, salting, chargrilling and smoking all play their part. Choose from a range of colourful modern small plates or opt for the 'All Out' menu – the full range of dishes in miniature!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13052;Muru;Finland;Helsinki;Fredrikinkatu 41, Helsinki, 00120, Finland;60.1652927;24.9358497;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You’d be hard pushed to find a restaurant with a greater focus on wine than Muru. This cosy little bistro is home to quirky touches such as a wine bottle chandelier, a bar made from old wine boxes and a raised ‘cellar’ – and that’s not to mention the nearby wine bar they run. Simple, tasty dishes are on-hand to accompany the excellent wine list, and the sommelier’s pairing suggestions are spot-on.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13055;Vinkkeli;Finland;Helsinki;Pieni Roobertinkatu 8, Helsinki, 00130, Finland;60.1641504;24.9462501;53;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This charming, deservedly popular restaurant is smartly laid out and run by a delightful team, whose attentive and personable service will make you want to become a regular. The honest, well-judged cooking is a pleasing mix of the modern and the traditional.;Air conditioning;[]
13056;Matur og Drykkur;Iceland;Reykjavík;Grandagarður 2, Reykjavík, 101, Iceland;64.15246;-21.951603;44;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This simple little eatery is named after an Icelandic cookbook and shares its premises with the Saga Museum. Old recipes are given modern twists, resulting in delicious dishes with a creative edge. The finest seasonal produce is used throughout the tasting menu, and transformed into refined, well-balanced dishes by the kitchen team. Friendly, professional service completes the picture.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13057;Pasfall;Denmark;Odense;Brandts Passage 31, Odense, 5000, Denmark;55.3954216;10.3815365;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Watch the eponymous chef at work in the open kitchen of this bright, contemporary restaurant. Top seasonal ingredients are used to create robustly flavoured dishes which are classic in their foundation but modern in delivery.;Air conditioning;[]
13058;Restaurant vRÅ;Sweden;Gothenburg;Clarion Hotel Post, Drottningtorget 10, Gothenburg, 411 03, Sweden;57.7078716;11.974785;59;true;true;Fusion;The imposing 1920s city post office is now a hotel, and this glamorous restaurant sits within what was the central hall – the listed cashier booths still on display. A Nordic-Japanese approach sees fine Scandinavian produce meet Asian techniques, and there’s an impressive range of sake by the glass.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
13060;Falsled Kro;Denmark;Millinge;Assensvej 513, Millinge, 5642, Denmark;55.1529987;10.1483635;17;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This charming whitewashed, thatched inn will draw you in with its enticing fireplace and lovely conservatory dining room overlooking the garden. The kitchen takes its cue from the French gastronomy of old, producing rich and indulgent dishes based on quality produce, be it rabbit or langoustine. Many of the ingredients are local, with fruit and vegetables often coming from the estate itself. Watch the chefs in the open kitchen to feel closer to the action.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
13062;Savoy;Finland;Helsinki;Eteläesplanadi 14, Helsinki, 00130, Finland;60.1670625;24.9470648;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This local institution’s refurbishment has restored much of its original charm and its 8th floor setting boasts superb views over Esplanade Park. Sophisticated classic dishes have a Finnish-French slant and a modern edge, with the occasional Russian touch. The wine matches are first class.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13063;Vækst;Denmark;Copenhagen;Sankt Peders Stræde 34, Copenhagen, 1453 K, Denmark;55.6788195;12.5672291;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Dining outside ‘inside’ is the theme here, and you’ll find plants, garden furniture and a full-sized greenhouse at the centre of the room. Interesting Danish cooking follows the seasons and is light, stimulating and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13064;Admiralgade 26;Denmark;Copenhagen;Admiralgade 26, Copenhagen, 1066 K, Denmark;55.677584;12.5821663;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This historic house dates from 1796 and sits in one of the oldest parts of the city. It’s a relaxed place: a mix of wine bar, café and bistro, with minimalist décor. From oyster mushrooms to actual oysters, the à la carte comprises a selection of vegetable and fish-led dishes. Wednesday nights are reserved for communal dining and movie nights, while Saturday lunch sees a set, Japanese-style 'choushoku' served. Owner Christian is always eager to let you taste some of the 4,000 wines from the cellar.;Interesting wine list;[]
13065;tabu;Denmark;Aalborg;Vesterå 5, Aalborg, 9000, Denmark;57.0499796;9.9178712;65;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Hidden within a handsome townhouse near the harbour, this contemporary restaurant serves a 5 or 10 course tasting menu, with an à la carte option also available. High quality local and international produce, be it seasonal vegetables or Jutland seafood, is one of the restaurant's greatest strengths – along with the satisfying desserts. Dishes are brought to the table by the chefs themselves and, with notice, can be adapted for vegetarian or vegan diets.;Air conditioning;[]
13067;Mielcke & Hurtigkarl;Denmark;Copenhagen;Runddel 1, Copenhagen, 2000 C, Denmark;55.6747592;12.5305057;47;true;false;Creative;Set in a delightful spot in Frederiksberg Gardens, its walls painted with garden scenes, is this charming 1744 orangery with a fire-lit terrace. Dishes come from around the globe, with Asian influences to the fore – and an amazing array of herbs from the gardens.;;[]
13068;Restaurant ET;Denmark;Aarhus;Mindegade 8, Aarhus, 8000, Denmark;56.15374;10.21116;45;false;true;French;When this smoothly run brasserie moved location to an elegant 19C house near Aarhus Harbour, the team took the original spirit with them. Familiar Gallic dishes like fish soup are generous in size and robust in flavour, whilst the seasonal dishes have some more modern Danish touches. All the food can be accompanied by wine from their exclusively French and highly impressive cellar.;Air conditioning;[]
13069;L' Enoteca di Mr. Brunello;Denmark;Copenhagen;Rysensteensgade 16, Copenhagen, 1564 K, Denmark;55.6711346;12.5740962;19;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Tucked away near the Tivoli Gardens is this restaurant and wine shop run by passionate, experienced owners. Refined, classic Italian cooking uses good quality produce imported from Italy. As you'd hope, the good value Italian wine list offers over 150 different Brunello di Montalcinos.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13070;Young Hearts;Finland;Helsinki;Runeberginkatu 55, Helsinki, 00260, Finland;60.1795084;24.9238467;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There is a comfortable and contemporary feel to this restaurant in the neighbourhood of Töölö. The cooking is inspired by the seasons and the well-constructed dishes deliver layers of intense flavours, with texture and acidity also playing a key role. There is generosity in the tasting menu offer, including some servings split across multiple complementary dishes – as with scallop presented both raw and as a dried powder to add flavour to a cabbage salad. Wine pairings are available to enhance the experience.;Air conditioning;[]
13071;à terre;Denmark;Copenhagen;Tordenskjoldsgade 11, Copenhagen, 1055 K, Denmark;55.6786792;12.5875713;27;false;false;French;Tucked behind the Royal Danish Theatre, there is a proud French heart to this cosy bistro created in homage to Jean-Louis le Lay, the Chef-Owner's father, who passed on his love of gastronomy to his son. The tasting menu incorporates global influences including – Caribbean and North African – alongside the classical French base, with good quality ingredients underpinning pared-back and boldly flavoured dishes. A shorter version of the menu is available on Wednesday and Thursday evenings, as well as Saturday lunch.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13072;Söl;Norway;Stavanger;Hetlandsgata 6, Stavanger, 4013, Norway;58.9693137;5.7355783;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Overlooking the 12th Century Stavanger Cathedral, this cosy restaurant has a friendly touch and offers guests a seasonal set menu. Expect an abundance of vegetables in summer and more meat and fish in winter, but with maximum flavour all year round. The Røros butter and freshly baked sourdough bread are a reason to come alone. They are equally passionate about wine, with one of the biggest natural wine lists in Norway.;Interesting wine list;[]
13074;Woodstockholm;Sweden;Stockholm;Mosebacke Torg 9, Stockholm, 116 46, Sweden;59.3177443;18.075003;17;true;false;Contemporary, International;A compact bistro owned by a group of friends, who set up a furniture making business and now use the bistro to showcase their products. Cooking follows a theme which changes every two months – perhaps a country, a style of food or a famous chef – and the rustic small plates are simple yet full of flavour.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13075;Koefoed;Denmark;Copenhagen;Landgreven 3, Copenhagen, 1301 K, Denmark;55.6830114;12.5851704;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine;An intimate collection of rooms in an old coal cellar, where everything from the produce to the glassware celebrates Bornholm island. Modern cooking is accompanied by an impressive range of bordeaux wines. Lunch sees reinvented smørrebrød.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13076;Tollbua;Norway;Trondheim;Brattørkaia 13B, Trondheim, 7010, Norway;63.4393;10.40263;32;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the Brattøra waterside development, this large eatery provides the crackling atmosphere you want from a brasserie like this. Banquettes and a central bar fit the bill décor-wise, while visible ducting and terrazzo flooring lend an industrial edge. Choose from a 4 or 6 course set menu, with a signature dish of scallops, sea buckthorn, XO and celeriac available as an extra. It’s beautiful Norwegian seafood like this, and skrei cod of course, that will be among the highlights of the meal.;;[]
13077;Bon Lio;Norway;Oslo;Storgata 41, Oslo, 0182, Norway;59.9152837;10.7551321;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Kitty and Cato will warmly welcome you into their bright neighbourhood restaurant, which offers a friendly experience that’s more relaxed than most. The ground floor Gastrobar is for drinks and bistro-style small plates, while upstairs it’s all about a multi-course tasting menu. Local, seasonal produce is the bedrock of Cato's cooking, which brings together elements from both his Majorcan and Norwegian heritage in a sophisticated manner. You’ll find the likes of perfectly seared turbot with almond, soya and carrot purée, accompanied by some excellent Spanish wine recommendations.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13078;Lola;Denmark;Copenhagen;Christianshavns Voldgade 50, Copenhagen, 1424, Denmark;55.6713725;12.5962831;80;true;false;World Cuisine;This laid-back restaurant is set within a 17C former windmill on the old city ramparts and comes complete with gardens, a terrace and even a pétanque pitch! The original, globally inspired dishes make use of quality local ingredients and are bursting with freshness and packed with flavour. At lunch, choose from a simpler smørrebrød menu.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13079;Levi;Denmark;Copenhagen;Ny Østergade 24, Copenhagen, 1101, Denmark;55.6817794;12.5822821;27;false;false;Italian and Japanese;Japanese and Italian cuisine join forces at this stylish restaurant near Rosenborg Castle Gardens. Expect to find Italian ingredients mixed into recognisable Japanese dishes and vice versa, such as salsiccia gyozas or spaghettoni with yuzu miso. The ambitious, high quality dishes are served by the friendly, attentive team in a strikingly designed room with high ceilings, bare tables and a large glass front.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13080;STUD!O;Denmark;Copenhagen;Paulas Passage 5, Carlsberg Byen, Copenhagen, 1799, Denmark;55.6665827;12.5308582;25;false;true;Creative;Part of the redevelopment around the former Carlsberg Brewery, this is a spacious, stylish restaurant with an open kitchen that lets you observe the chefs as they work. Vegetables from local farms, game in season and top quality seafood – like squid, langoustine and Pacific oysters – underpin original, creative dishes that showcase the ambition of the young team. In a demonstration of their zero-waste ethos, the leftovers from their freshly baked bread are sometimes used as the basis for the dessert.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13081;Café Savoy;Finland;Helsinki;Eteläesplanadi 14, Helsinki, 00 130, Finland;60.1670666;24.9469973;72;false;true;French;Located in the same building as the iconic Restaurant Savoy, on the city’s central esplanade, this well-run brasserie is spacious, airy and deservedly busy. The cooking is classical with a southern French influence, so expect to find the likes of salade Niçoise and ratatouille on the menu. The chefs prepare their good quality ingredients with care, resulting in authentic and flavoursome dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
13082;Eero;Norway;Oslo;Henrik Ibsens gate 48, Oslo, 0255, Norway;59.9150362;10.723516;61;false;false;Seafood;Perched on the top floor of the former American Embassy and named after its architect Eero Saarinen, this restaurant and cocktail bar features a wrap-around terrace with views of the Oslofjord on one side and The Royal Palace gardens on the other. A wood-fired oven is at the heart of the cooking, which is fish-centric and takes a ‘fin to gill’ approach. So you might get cod tongue as a snack, then later its belly on the bone, enhanced by the richness of its liver and roe. Everyone is served at once from a tasting menu, and some of the dishes are presented ‘family style’.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13083;Black Milk Gastro Bar;Sweden;Stockholm;Engelbrektsgatan 3, Stockholm, 114 32, Sweden;59.3380976;18.0697376;80;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;A younger sibling of Aloë, this intimate restaurant offers more great cooking with a fun and lively night out thrown into the bargain. Influenced by South America, Asia and Europe, the creative dishes deliver vibrant flavours and well-judged spicing, whilst using plenty of modern techniques. Expect to see some luxury ingredients, like Oscietra caviar and Périgord truffles, alongside an enjoyable dose of theatricality.;Counter dining;[]
13084;Ego;Finland;Helsinki;Korkeavuorenkatu 27, Helsinki, 00140, Finland;60.16393;24.9462644;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Simplicity runs through the team’s ethos at this relaxed neighbourhood spot, from the minimalist Nordic décor to the straightforward cooking that eschews overcomplication. On the ground floor you’ll find the brighter of the two dining rooms, which also has plants dotted around, whilst the cellar offers moodier lighting and exposed brickwork. There are Finnish elements to the menu, along with some seasonal French ingredients and classic dishes like steak tartare.;;[]
13086;Symbios;Sweden;Stockholm;Skånegatan 80, Stockholm, 116 37, Sweden;59.3122531;18.0800548;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There’s a wonderfully unpretentious feel to this relaxed, friendly restaurant perfectly suited to the trendy suburb of Södermalm. Watch the world go by as you relax with an aperitif on the pavement terrace, before enjoying classic Swedish and southern European dishes that are simple, fresh and full of flavour. The midweek lunch menu represents great value for money, and the place is informally yet professionally run by a friendly team.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13087;Frank;Denmark;Copenhagen;Ny Adelgade 3, Copenhagen, 1104 K, Denmark;55.6811404;12.5840769;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;The open kitchen takes centre stage at this relaxed, contemporary restaurant, with its soft lighting, flickering candles, comfy sofas and designer wooden furnishings. Choose between an à la carte and a tasting menu – both of which offer flavour-packed, original and understated modern dishes.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13088;Sushi Anaba;Denmark;Copenhagen;Sandkaj 39, Copenhagen, 2150, Denmark;55.7068801;12.5987021;28;true;true;Japanese;A Japanese staple through a Nordic lens is what you can expect at this compact quayside sushi restaurant that seats just eight diners round its counter. The Danish Chef-Owner trained in Tokyo and brings a passionate approach to the cooking, which is underpinned by superb produce from Nordic waters, be it Norwegian scallop or lobster from Jutland. An excellent sake selection highlights some lesser-known choices.;Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
13090;Theo;Denmark;Copenhagen;Skindergade 29, Copenhagen, 1050, Denmark;55.67934;12.57437;40;true;true;Contemporary, European Contemporary;Located in the heart of Copenhagen, this is the sort of restaurant we’d all love to have in our neighbourhood. The team here have dedicated themselves to serving uncomplicated, appealing dishes that offer good value for money. Charming service and an unpretentious approach to both the décor and food strengthens their mission, as does the simple yet consistently high quality cooking.;;[]
13092;BELLIES;Norway;Stavanger;Støperigata 6, Stavanger, 4014, Norway;58.971336;5.7519404;95;false;false;Vegan, Vegetarian;Vegetable lovers will find paradise at this plant-powered restaurant that celebrates fabulous, yet often overlooked, ingredients. Whether it's beetroot, pumpkin or Jerusalem artichoke, quality vegetables are given a starring role that they are rarely afforded. A range of Asian elements, from Sichuan pepper to ssamjang, are used to embellish the natural flavours of the produce, as are fermented and preserved components made in-house. There’s a lovely atmosphere and all dishes are served with a smile.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13093;Boulevard;Finland;Helsinki;Bulevardi 6, Helsinki, 00120, Finland;60.1660338;24.942305;36;true;true;Seafood;The welcome is warm, the room elegant, and the food heartening and eminently satisfying. The passion and experience of the two chef-owners is evident in all areas of this likeable restaurant. The quality of the fish and shellfish really comes through, thanks to the classic techniques used by the kitchen.;;[]
13094;Bulot;Sweden;Gothenburg;Norra Hamngatan 8, Gothenburg, 411 14, Sweden;57.7063993;11.961487;84;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There’s a real buzz about this neighbourhood wine-bar-cum-bistro, which makes it so appealing as soon as you set foot through the door. The personable team keep things relaxed as they serve a seasonal tasting menu which comes with a subtle French slant and plenty of seafood – the restaurant’s name is French for whelk, so expect to find one somewhere on the menu. The simple, well-cooked dishes are also available from the à la carte as small plates.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13095;freyja.;Sweden;Stockholm;Hornsgatan 18, Stockholm, 118 20, Sweden;59.319803;18.0688904;61;true;true;Swedish, Modern Cuisine;Head straight for the roof terrace to kick off your visit with a cocktail and 360° views of Stockholm and, once inside, opt for a seat by the curved window to capitalise on the 13th floor location. The menu includes modernised yet comforting Swedish classics like Kroppkaka, executed with care and confidence, yielding well-balanced flavours. This is a place where you'll feel equally at home dining in a couple or as a group, as it delivers something for everyone.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13097;Pull;Estonia;Tallinn;Rotermanni 2, Tallinn, 10111, Estonia;59.4395107;24.75881;37;false;false;Meats and Grills;Within the rejuvenated, pre-war industrial area of the ‘Rotermann Factories’ sits an impressive 19C grain elevator and, inside that, this fittingly rustic restaurant with exposed stone walls and concrete pillars. Generously proportioned Estonian dishes focus on meats and charcoal-grilled steaks.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13098;Wicca;Estonia;Laulasmaa;Puhkekodu tee 4, Laulasmaa, 76702, Estonia;59.3744849;24.2377328;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Angelica Udeküll is not only a TV chef but a torchbearer for Estonian food. Her elegant restaurant at the LaSpa hotel sits in a beautifully tranquil spot overlooking the pine trees and the sea – and is the perfect location to showcase her ethical cooking. Dishes are creative, with some Nordic touches.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13099;Hõlm;Estonia;Tartu;Ülikooli 14, Tartu, 51003, Estonia;58.3795843;26.7217518;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant is named ‘Hõlm’ and the hotel within which it sits, ‘Lydia’ – after Lydia Grünmann Hõlm, on whose recipes the dishes here are based. Full-length windows flood the elegant dining room with light and the attractively presented dishes exhibit appealing combinations of both texture and flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13100;Art Priori;Estonia;Tallinn;Olevimägi 7, Tallinn, 10123, Estonia;59.4400349;24.7479121;27;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in the heart of the Old Town, this is a wonderfully elegant, romantic spot, where two striking rooms ooze period charm and an eclectic mix of artwork fills the walls. In contrast, the food is modern and understated. Well-formed dishes give each core ingredient the space to shine, with unadulterated flavours fitting together seamlessly. You might find earthy yellow beetroot paired with soft goat’s cheese or wonderfully mature venison with a silky celeriac purée. Friendly service and a great choice of cocktails and wines by the glass finishes things off perfectly.;;[]
13101;38;Estonia;Tallinn;Olevimägi 9, Tallinn, 10123, Estonia;59.4402166;24.7481048;50;false;false;Creative;This pop-up turned permanent is sister to Mere 38 in Võsu. It exudes a cool, fashionable vibe, courtesy of a modern interior with striking murals which contrast with its historic exterior and quaint Old Town setting. Well-judged, creative dishes have subtle Asian influences and are attractively presented.;;[]
13102;Tchaikovsky;Estonia;Tallinn;Vene 9, Tallinn, 10123, Estonia;59.4377615;24.7473496;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Russian;Set within the well-known Hotel Telegraaf, in the heart of the Old Town, this glass-roofed, restaurant has something of a celebratory feel, courtesy of a beautiful chandelier and battleship-grey walls hung with gilt-framed pictures. Cooking has a classical French base with Russian influences and modern overtones.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13103;Lee;Estonia;Tallinn;Uus 31, Tallinn, 10111, Estonia;59.441047;24.7494223;37;true;false;Asian Influences, Modern Cuisine;A ‘Lee’ is the ancient communal fireplace around which families would sit together to prepare a meal – and this powder blue restaurant with ornate columns and a charming courtyard setting certainly has a historic feel. The cooking ranges in style from the traditional to the modern, with the chef’s background showing through in dishes with distinct Asian influences, like Liivimaa dry-aged beef short rib with cauliflower cream and wasabi or cherry mille-feuille with green tea and tofu cream.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13106;Joyce;Estonia;Tartu;Riia 2, Tartu, 51004, Estonia;58.3766297;26.7282274;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A modern shopping centre in the heart of the city plays host to this large, split-level brasserie with bold décor, a popular cocktail bar and a buzzy vibe. Attractively presented dishes mix local and Baltic influences: the kitchen adds creative twists and flavours pack a punch.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13107;ÂME;Estonia;Tallinn;Nunne 14, Tallinn, 10133, Estonia;59.4388227;24.7423634;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Housed within a small boutique hotel on the edge of the Old Town is this elegant restaurant where the old and the new combine: part of the Medieval city wall runs down one side of the room, yet it also has a contemporary, design-led style. Âme is French for ‘soul’ and, while the appealingly understated dishes certainly have a French heart, flavours are also drawn from around the globe and, as such, are described as ‘dishes that feed the soul’. Opt for one of the two tasting menus to sample a range of these dishes, such as goose breast à l'orange or roasted cauliflower à la Marrakech.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13109;RADIO;Estonia;Tallinn;Terase 16, Tallinn, 10125, Estonia;59.4349406;24.7720244;97;true;false;International;Part wine shop, part café-cum-bistro, this neighbourhood establishment is all things to all people. You enter via a shop packed full of interesting wines, before heading through the restaurant where a glass wine cave takes centre stage. The room has a bistro feel – there are even a few sofas available for those who like it super laid-back – and dishes come in the form of medium-sized plates that are designed for sharing. From sausage soup to cured trout or onion pie, each dish comes with the perfect wine recommendation.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13110;Kolm Sõsarat;Estonia;Lüllemäe;Kirikumõisa tee 9, Lüllemäe, 68116, Estonia;57.75131;26.37397;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Three Sisters run this small, remotely set restaurant and each has their role to play: Kerti does the cooking, Triin looks after the service and Kadri tends to the kitchen garden. The playful set menu is a showcase of the area, featuring top quality produce from their garden and farm – such as in the country-style mushroom, potato and sauerkraut – while superb honey from their father’s long-established hives is celebrated in desserts such as honey, apple and milk with sea buckthorn. This is a truly special place where the passion of the team is palpable, as they go above and beyond to care for every guest.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park;[]
13113;SOO;Estonia;Maidla;Maidla Mõis 1, Maidla, 79408, Estonia;59.051638;24.8971753;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Visionary owner Ragnar Sass purchased the Maidla Estate and manor house back in 2019, then added some rather smart eco-lodges in the woods and wetlands – as well as this intimate 5-table restaurant. Sustainability and ecological considerations are key, and the set dinner menu looks to the seasons and the region for its inspiration. Dishes are rich in flavour but come with a welcome lightness, and foraging, pickling and preserving all play their part. Wines are organic and natural.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
13115;Mon Repos;Estonia;Tallinn;Narva mnt. 92, Tallinn, 10127, Estonia;59.4409706;24.7868407;72;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This former imperial summer residence comes with a charming interior which blends original stained glass windows and panelled ceilings with sleek, modern furnishings. The modern menu reflects the locale and extends across to the Mediterranean, with colourfully presented dishes exhibiting flavours and textures which have been well thought through. The gravlax with beets, horseradish and blinis is a must to start, and to finish the tiramisu is a winner. The lovely terrace looking out over Kadriorg Park is a popular spot.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13116;Nok Nok;Estonia;Tallinn;Vana-Posti 7, Tallinn, 10146, Estonia;59.4354781;24.745177;95;true;false;Thai;Nok means ‘bird’ in Thai, which makes sense when you spot the two stone owls set into the stonework. With its central location and two spacious, colourfully decorated dining rooms, this is a popular place to eat both amongst locals and visitors. Authentic Thai flavours are sure to warm you up on colder days and you’ll find all your Thai favourites, from a wonderful chicken satay with sweet and sour pickles to rich curries, such as a Massaman made using braised short ribs. Be sure to save room for dessert though, as the sticky rice with mango is superb.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13117;Moon;Estonia;Tallinn;Võrgu 3, Tallinn, 10415, Estonia;59.4451977;24.7477385;23;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The word ‘Moon’ refers to the poppy seed, which is an apt name, as it’s hard not to eat too much of the delicious poppy seed bread here! Split into three rooms, this intimate bistro comes with bright décor, a lovely teacup chandelier and a seasonally changing menu comprising flavoursome Slavic dishes. The sweet team greet both locals and visitors as if they are regulars.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13119;Barbarea;Estonia;Tallinn;Marati 5, Tallinn, 11713, Estonia;59.4559963;24.6749609;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A former rubber boot factory in an up-and-coming area plays host to this city hotspot, which starts the day as a bakery and then morphs into a stylish, laid-back bistro in the evening. Family-style dining is at the heart of their ethos and the vibrant, flavour-packed sharing plates follow the seasons, with 50-75% of the ingredients (depending on the month) having been produced organically. The wine list comprises a good selection of natural, organic and biodynamic wines, and they have a wine bar next door where you can continue your night.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13121;Rado;Estonia;Haapsalu;Posti 7, Haapsalu, 90502, Estonia;58.9446465;23.538496;66;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Sister to the restaurant of the same name in Tallinn – and also with their signature bicycle parked outside – is this bright, modern bistro run by a sweet, friendly team. The small menu is chalked up on the blackboard and the fresh, unfussy cooking represents great value. In summer, head for the terrace at the back.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13122;Mere 38;Estonia;Võsu;Mere 38, Võsu, 45501, Estonia;59.5763779;25.9607297;31;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in a quiet village, this green-painted wooden house boasts both a fashionable New England style restaurant and smart apartments. It has a cosy dining room with fleece-covered chairs, as well as a lovely summer terrace. Dishes are largely Mediterranean influenced and are vibrant and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13124;Casa Rios;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Itapura, 1327, São Paulo, 03310-000, Brazil;-23.5502289;-46.5651316;91;true;false;Brazilian, Contemporary;Chef Rodrigo Aguiar, originally from Rio de Janeiro, combined his skills with owner Giovanna Perrone to realise her dream here. This charming restaurant features an open kitchen where guests can view the wood oven and churrasco grill, both of which exude the smoky flavours for which Casa Rios is famous. If you sit at the bar counter, you can watch the preparation process in full flow as well as appreciate the aromas emanating from the kitchen. The cuisine here is based around typical Brazilian cooking with a focus on the south-east of the country, using ingredients from small-scale producers and a constant nod to seasonality. Whether you opt for the tasting menu or à la carte, make sure you try the wood oven-baked pizzeta of merguez sausage made with cornbread – an absolute must!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13125;Borgo Mooca;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Barão De Tatuí, 302, São Paulo, 01226-030, Brazil;-23.5383601;-46.6540355;80;false;true;Italian;Fried gnocchi, egg pasta, langoustine, octopus and black rice with squid ink are just some of the dishes and ingredients you’ll find here, a list enhanced by the slow-fermented and Maraschino cherry babá with a smooth crème anglaise. This gastronomic refuge is located in the Santa Cecília district and features a modern-retro style and uncluttered atmosphere. It includes a bar counter overlooking the kitchen, decoration that is teeming with details on the walls and ceiling, plus a basement bar called Bargo offering an array of superb cocktails. Chef Matheus Zanchini conjures up creative cuisine with Italian nuances, including homemade pasta, all of which is prepared with top-quality ingredients. The menu is updated weekly in line with the availability of ingredients sourced by the chef.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
13126;Bicol Korean Cuisine;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua José Getúlio 422, São Paulo, 01509-000, Brazil;-23.5691791;-46.6340311;78;true;true;Korean;Bicol is a must if you’re keen to try Korean barbecue-style cuisine. This classic address in the Liberdade district of the city has been run by a South Korean family for three generations. In this spacious restaurant, the tables have their own grills so that guests can cook meat (usually cut super-fine) to their individual taste. Dishes for sharing are the mainstay here, including the Burgogui, Garbi and Samguiopsar combos, always accompanied by Banchan (small side dishes of the day). The Bibimbap (a typical rice dish) and the soups are other interesting options on the menu, not forgetting the delicious kimchi, of course. Why not pair your food with the traditional soju, a typical Korean beverage with differing strengths of alcohol?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13127;Corrientes 348 - Marina da Glória;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Infante Dom Henrique, Rio de Janeiro, 20021-140, Brazil;-22.9198977;-43.1696199;45;false;false;Meats and Grills;The name of this restaurant is a reference to the famous Argentinian tango “A Media Luz”, while the number 348 corresponds to the number of the street where the first of the brand’s ventures opened in Greater São Paulo. It overlooks the Marina da Glória, hence the spectacular views from tables on the terrace, and features several spacious dining rooms and an extensive glass-fronted wine cellar. The culinary focus is of course on Argentina and choice cuts of meats cooked on the grill, including specialities such as ribeye, centre cut ribeye, filet mignon with garlic, chorizo sausage and top sirloin, all accompanied by sides designed for sharing. To finish, the “dulce de leche” pancake served with sorbet is an authentic Argentinian dessert that is truly irresistible.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13128;Mäska;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Joana Angélica, 159, Rio de Janeiro, 22420-030, Brazil;-22.9828833;-43.2050012;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;It's worth braving the frenetic traffic along Ipanema’s narrow streets to eat at this modern but relaxed restaurant with a contemporary bistro feel and a kitchen that opens on to the dining room in which you can savour chef Danilo Parah’s “innovative and emotional” cuisine. Here, the chef showcases Asian ingredients in contemporary dishes that are generous, colourful and pleasing on the palate. The impressively varied menu is complemented by dishes inspired by ingredients available in the market, such as the highly popular spaghetti with beurre blanc and braised prawns. The dining experience and atmosphere are enhanced by Mäska’s array of refreshing cocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
13129;NOTIÊ;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Formosa 157, São Paulo, 01049-000, Brazil;-23.5463026;-46.6388915;98;false;true;Brazilian, Modern Cuisine;Although only recently opened, this restaurant is already being talked about by the city’s foodie community. Located on the rooftop of the Shopping Light building, its design comes as a pleasant surprise as soon as you walk through the door thanks to its decor of yellow tones, glass-fronted kitchen enabling guests to watch the chefs hard at work and, first and foremost, the 18m panel on the ceiling depicting images of nature. At the helm in the kitchen is Paraíba-born chef Onildo Rocha who impresses with his use of typical Brazilian ingredients and combinations that result in intense and striking dishes. His recipes are based around his journeys to different Brazilian regions every season, and are showcased on 5-, 7- and 11-course tasting menus. The name of the restaurant is a fusion between one of the country’s most colourful birds, the tanager (tiê in Portuguese) and the Portuguese word for night (noite).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13130;Tiara;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Ataulfo De Paiva, 270 loja 111, Rio de Janeiro, 22440-900, Brazil;-22.9834173;-43.2184219;63;false;false;Contemporary;The name Tiara refers to the district (Itacoatiara) in which chef Rafa Gomes was born. Nowadays, he owns two restaurants called Itacoa and, to complete the full name, Tiara. This famous chef is known for his appearance on reality cooking shows and his impressive career thus far, including stints in leading restaurants in New York. Housed in the Rio Design Leblon complex, the restaurant boasts an elegant backdrop of soothing tones for innovative cuisine that relies on modern techniques and the use of seasonal ingredients where possible. Here, the chef elevates duck meat (a key ingredient in his story) to another level. An example of this is the aged duck lacquered with honey and spices served with pumpkin, miso and a “gastrique” sauce – a quite surreal combination!;Air conditioning;[]
13132;Naga;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Bandeira Paulista 385, São Paulo, 04532-011, Brazil;-23.5826917;-46.6760698;59;true;true;Japanese;A legendary Japanese restaurant in the city that has for a long time been a favourite address for aficionados of the country’s cuisine. It’s no surprise that the Nagayama group does not just have a single restaurant – in fact, in this area they own almost an entire block that includes the Bar do Naga, the Café do Naga etc. It is split between two floors, with access to the floor above via an attractive steep staircase. In the latter you’ll find two rooms: a waiting area with just a few tables, and a second more spacious room with a direct view of the pleasantly and subtly illuminated sushi bar. The extensive menu features a wide array of carpaccios, sushi, sashimi, uramaki, temaki, tartares and teppanyaki, and if there are several of you, you may want to try combination options such as the popular Naga Case 2 or the enticing Omakase-style tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
13133;Kosushi;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Viradouro 139, São Paulo, 04538-110, Brazil;-23.5853793;-46.6808999;76;true;true;Japanese;The name of the restaurant has a direct link with Japanese philosophy as the word “ko” (which translates as “turtle”) is associated with long life and the symbolism of the number 1. Opened in 1988 by chef George Yuji Koshoji, it is now located at a different address (in the Itaim Bibi district), where it has become a popular meeting place for locals. It boasts a welcoming, contemporary ambience, soft lighting and a decor of bright colours, plus an impressive large balcony from where guests can watch their dishes being prepared. The extensive menu offers a variety of options such as gyosas, tartares, ussuzukuri, uramaki, sushi and sashimi, as well as hot dishes that include yakisoba, octopus yaki and Wagyu medallions. It also features a superb selection of sakis and innovative cocktails.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13134;Loup;Brazil;São Paulo;Dr. Mário Ferraz 528, São Paulo, 01453-011, Brazil;-23.5849874;-46.6853155;85;false;false;International;Loup’s unique decor and atmosphere, featuring several dining spaces, designer details, lofty glass ceilings and an impressive vertical garden, have been very carefully curated, and provide the backdrop for an enticing fusion of cuisine from different parts of the world, prepared with top-quality ingredients and enhanced by a Raw Bar section serving an array of tartares, carpaccios, ceviches etc. If you prefer to be seated at a more traditional table, the menu includes delicious mini palm heart pastries with prawns, appetising dishes such as arroz de pato (rice with duck) that take you back to Portugal, and for dessert, the irresistible cannoli with a light yet crunchy dulce de leche and red berries, which transports you to the shores of Italy. It’s also worth taking time out to enjoy a cocktail in the lounge.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13135;Charco;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Peixoto Gomide 1492, São Paulo, 01409-002, Brazil;-23.5651497;-46.6616177;57;true;false;Brazilian, Grills;In this restaurant inspired by the typical cuisine of the Rio Grande do Sul region, chef Tuca Mezzomo leads his team alongside Nathalia Gonçalves – masters in the art of preparing grilled and flame-cooked dishes with a continual focus on the best and freshest ingredients. Dishes that you won’t want to miss include the toasted mushrooms with smoked pumpkin and parmesan, and the succulent grilled Wagyu short rib, served with a wild tomato salad and a Bordelaise sauce. In addition, the restaurant also produces its own delicious sausages, butter and fresh goat’s cheese. The backdrop to the dining experience is a rustic, welcoming mix of exposed brickwork, wooden tables and subdued lighting that adds to the pleasant ambience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13136;Pobre Juan;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Comendador Miguel Calfat 525, São Paulo, 04537-082, Brazil;-23.5936444;-46.6776858;47;true;false;Meats and Grills;The first Pobre Juan outlet opened in the Vila Olímpia in 2004 and nowadays you’ll find the brand all across the country. Inspired by traditional Argentinian steakhouses, Pobre Juan serves top-quality grilled meats in an informal and rustic setting. Each of its restaurants features a wide array of carefully selected meats, a process that extends from their provenance to the maturing process. Whether you order classic options such as short ribs, ribeye or flank, or the more exclusive centre cut ribeye, porterhouse or Wagyu, every dish here is perfectly cooked. If you’re eating out with friends, you may want to order the Gran Tabla, which serves three people and comes with delicious sides. Fish, seafood and chicken, all cooked on the open grill, are also available, as well as sublime desserts such as the exquisite churros with dulce de leche.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13137;Cepa;Brazil;São Paulo;Praça Dos Omaguás, 110, São Paulo, 05419-020, Brazil;-23.5618174;-46.6922842;84;false;false;Farm to table, Home Cooking;Cepa is one of those restaurants that always features in food-related conversations in the city, and now it has a new home in the Pinheiros neighborhood! Here, chef Lucas Dante presents creative, seasonal cuisine that prioritises the freshness of ingredients and champions small-scale producers. By his side is sommelier and front-of-house manager Gabrielli Fleming, who is in charge of sourcing biodynamic and organic wines for the cellar that are always the perfect pairing for your choice of dish. We can highly recommend the simply incredible starter of Wagyu tongue with chicken broth, okra and mint.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13138;Lilia;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua do Senado 45, Rio de Janeiro, 20231-005, Brazil;-22.9091605;-43.1840026;33;false;false;Brazilian;This unique restaurant, with an unremarkable façade that could easily pass unnoticed among the historic colonial-style houses in the Lapa district, is located just a few metres from the conical São Sebastião cathedral. As you walk up a long, narrow staircase, you come to this two-storey restaurant featuring brick walls and corrugated iron panelling which endow it with a spacious, uncluttered and industrial feel. Here, chef Rafael Scatolin heads up a kitchen characterised by its creativity, where the cuisine is updated daily in line with the availability of ingredients. A three-course set menu is available at lunchtime, while at dinner you can choose between options on the à la carte or an eleven-course tasting menu. And make sure you save space for the Chocolate ganache, cupuaçu caramel and cocoa crunch, which it is an absolute must!;Air conditioning;[]
13139;Mesa do Lado;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Conde Bernadotte 26, Rio de Janeiro, 22430-200, Brazil;-22.9809883;-43.2227589;44;true;false;Creative;A recent innovation from the Troisgros Group and one with a completely different concept that ensures a unique dining experience. Here, inside the renowned Chez Claude restaurant in Leblon, chef Claude Troisgros offers a sensory gastronomic experience that aims to awaken all five senses. The small dining room, with seating for just 12 guests per sitting, provides the setting for a tasting menu that evolves in line with lighting effects and the projection of images that varies according to the background music. The contemporary cuisine has a strong French influence and somewhat nostalgic feel thanks to family recipes handed down through the generations. Timings are strict here so you’ll need to arrive and depart at your appointed times!;Air conditioning;[]
13140;L'Etoile;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Niemeyer 121, Rio de Janeiro, 22450-220, Brazil;-22.9915044;-43.2329427;76;true;true;International;L'Etoile is the perfect option if you’re planning a romantic dinner with breathtaking views. Located on the 26th floor of the imposing Sheraton Grand Rio Hotel & Resort on Leblon Beach, the restaurant boasts a sophisticated and romantic atmosphere and a menu that bears the signature of renowned chef Jean-Paul Bondoux, who reinterprets classic French techniques and combines these with Brazilian ingredients. The kitchen is under the daily charge of chef Juan Garcia Molina, who brings his own personality touch to dishes, which are available on an à la carte and a seven-course tasting menu. The creative desserts are the domain of pastry chef Mariana Ribeirinha, who conjures up delicate dishes with sublime flavours!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13141;Térèze;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Felicio dos Santos 15, Rio de Janeiro, 20241-260, Brazil;-22.9216463;-43.1879377;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Térèze is the perfect choice if you’re on the lookout for a quiet setting for a romantic supper. It is part of the Santa Teresa Mgalley hotel, a delightful historic property built in 1850 with a sophisticated atmosphere and breathtaking views. The menu is based around a contemporary theme that uses seasonal ingredients, plus a mix of Brazilian and international recipes. Chefs Jérôme Dardillac and Luanna Malheiros conjure up surprising combinations such as the perfectly grilled octopus with a chickpea purée, ratatouille and a delicious rougail sauce. After lunch or dinner, why not prolong the enjoyment with a drink in the delightful surroundings of the charming bar?;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
13142;Mr. Lam;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Maria Angélica 21, Rio de Janeiro, 22470-201, Brazil;-22.9627448;-43.2077344;44;false;false;Asian Influences;Mr. Lam gained renowned for his culinary prowess in restaurants in New York and London, however he has run this modern, sophisticated eatery on the edge of the Rodrigo de Freitas lagoon for almost two decades. In contrast with other gastronomic restaurants these days, the majority of dishes on the menu have been mainstays since it first opened, in so doing keeping with the tradition of offering the best Chinese cuisine. Featuring a hint of cutting-edge innovation as well as a focus on top-quality ingredients, the menu boasts memorable dishes such as the lightly battered and crispy Senhor Batista prawns, with a delicious sweet and sour sauce. The restaurant is laid out on three floors, with an attractive dining room and welcoming bar on the top floor that includes picture windows and a glass roof that provide lots of natural light and stunning views.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13143;Sud, O Pássaro Verde;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Visconde de Carandaí 35, Rio de Janeiro, 22460-020, Brazil;-22.9658198;-43.2203784;89;false;true;Brazilian;Walking into this restaurant is like entering the home of a friend, as you’ll need to knock on the door or announce your presence in order to be let in. Occupying a house in the quiet Jardim Botânico district, this is the domain of chef Roberta Sudbrack who describes it as a space in which to “tell and eat stories”. Inside, the decor is modest yet welcoming, with an impressive wood-fired oven next to the main dining room, plus a charming open kitchen, from which comforting home-style dishes emerge prepared with ingredients from small-scale local producers. As a result, the menu changes daily in line with market availability and freshness. However, one mainstay that is always on the menu is the superbly textured and irresistibly flavoured chocolate cake (“bolo de chocolate molhadinho”).;Air conditioning;[]
13144;Giuseppe Grill Leblon;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Bartolomeu Mitre 370, Rio de Janeiro, 22431-001, Brazil;-22.9805137;-43.224215;44;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;As the name clearly states, all the dishes (fish and meat) at this restaurant are cooked on the charcoal grill. The menu here includes dry-aged meat options (T-bone, prime rib, bone-in tenderloin etc). Other standout dishes include the Maminha (sirloin trip-tip), the Picanha supra sumo (supra sumo rump cap), the brand’s registered trademark, as well as the slow-cooked Uruguayan lamb shoulder served with its own jus. A number of fish and seafood options are also on display, which vary according to availability on the day. The decor here features exposed stone walls, wooden chairs and leather sofas, all of which combine to add a rustic-elegant touch. Not forgetting the extensive wine cellar in the basement, featuring over 400 labels from different countries.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
13145;Fasano;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Vitório Fasano 88, São Paulo, 01414-020, Brazil;-23.5645122;-46.6695865;55;false;true;Italian;The grand piano at the entrance and the lounge with its high ceiling and skylight take us right back to the New York of the 1940s. A symbol of quality, glamour and fine dining, the Fasano is renowned across Brazil for its classic Italian cuisine, albeit with a modern touch. The menu, designed by chef Luca Gozzani, showcases an extensive array of copious and surprising dishes on which pasta plays a starring role. We can recommend starting with the creamy burrata with Parma ham, followed by a succulent lamb fillet with gnocchi, with a delicious panna cotta as a final flourish – a combination of dishes that will take you on a gastronomic adventure back to Italy. The exceptional service from the front-of-house team makes the experience even more special!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13146;Casa Santo Antônio;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida João Carlos da Silva Borges 764, São Paulo, 04726-001, Brazil;-23.6384337;-46.7116546;79;true;false;Italian;This extraordinary partnership is the result of a bond of friendship, the fruits of which are clearly visible in this superb gastronomic restaurant. Located somewhat off the beaten track in the southern section of São Paulo, it occupies a property built in the 1960s. It features a charming and elegant space with various dining rooms, a stunning bar and an outdoor terrace when the weather allows (a section of the glass-fronted kitchen is also visible to guests). The menu showcases an Italian influence with fresh homemade pastas, generous portions and moderate prices. An “executive” menu is also available during the week. Standout dishes here include the authentic and extremely delicious spaghetti alla carbonara, and the classic tiramisu, with its perfect creamy texture.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13147;Território Aprazível;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Aprazível 62, Rio de Janeiro, 20241-270, Brazil;-22.9247815;-43.1873557;51;true;true;Brazilian;Aprazível is a must for those who love delicious food inspired by nature. This family-run restaurant, located inside an exuberant tropical garden and furnished in rustic style, boasts a superb view of the city. Here, chef Ana Castilho conjures up typical Brazilian dishes teeming with flavour and created using organic and biodynamic ingredients, yet without neglecting either elegance or delicacy. One of her signature dishes is the free-range “galinhada caipira”, served with a delicious free-range chicken-flavoured rice, plantains, sausage from Minas Gerais, braised cabbage, and a tasty pepper jelly and beans. Enjoy Aprazível’s pleasant atmosphere and charming setting in the company of a relaxing drink!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13148;Aconchego Carioca;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Barão de Iguatemi 245, Rio de Janeiro, 20270-060, Brazil;-22.9127851;-43.2139701;26;false;false;Brazilian;A whole host of traditional dishes such as the rice-based “arroz de rabada”, “baião de dois” (black-eyed peas with rice) and the unmissable Bolinho de feijoada (fried feijoada dumplings) are just some of the dishes served in this restaurant, which has become a popular culinary focal point in the northern part of Rio de Janeiro. Here, well-known chef Kátia Barbosa creates cooking with a focus on typical Brazilian dishes with influences from the north-east of the country, all of which are prepared with meticulous detail and lots of flavour. In this completely relaxed and informal setting, decorated with hammocks hanging from the ceilings, the pleasant garden and friendly staff make you feel very much at home. Make sure you also try the innovative and amazing cocktails!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13149;Aiô;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Áurea 307, São Paulo, 04015-070, Brazil;-23.5870733;-46.6454652;70;false;false;Taiwanese;If you’re keen to enjoy a different type of dining experience, make sure you book a table at Aiô, where the menu is based around Taiwanese cooking with an international touch that will take you on a journey to some surprising flavours. Located in the same street as its sister restaurant Mapu, Aiô features a distinctive glass façade, behind which you’ll find a bar by the entrance offering an array of delightful and inventive cocktails. The menu is uncomplicated and does not differentiate between starters and mains, enabling guests to share and order individual tasting menus. Standout options include the pork char siu, consisting of mini pancakes served as tacos, accompanied by a delicious dish of meat, red rice and honey, and featuring an explosion of mouthwatering and stunning flavours.;Counter dining;[]
13150;Chez Claude;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Conde de Bernadotte 26, Rio de Janeiro, 22430-200, Brazil;-22.9807869;-43.2226213;86;false;true;Modern French;Run by the famous French chef Claude Troisgros, this dining space has plenty of detail to pique your interest. Firstly, the completely open kitchen in the centre of the room, enabling diners to watch dishes being prepared at close quarters, which are based around French cuisine with the addition of some Brazilian elements. And secondly, the fact that food is served in bowls for sharing, to add to the sense of home-style cooking. The staff here recommend four dishes for two people including delicacies such as the fillet steak au poivre with a sauce that will make your mouth water, accompanied by cassava puff pastry and broccoli with Grana Padano cheese. To finish your meal, don’t miss the impressively textured melted chocolate Carola cake.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13152;Maza;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Manuel Guedes, 243, São Paulo, 04536-070, Brazil;-23.5825651;-46.6794071;56;true;true;Japanese;As well as a highly enjoyable dining experience, Maza boasts a relaxing and welcoming setting, where the combination of wood and soft tones is clearly evident as soon as you walk through the door – a decor embellished by the beautiful cherry tree. The cuisine here is based around classic Japanese fare with a modern and personalised touch, including some Korean dishes. The different types of menus on offer include a seven-course option called Shinrai (served exclusively at table), the Omakase (only available at the bar counter), an à la carte. Exquisite dishes include karasumi, ussuzukuri, Wagyu tataki, “shake butter”, as well as sushi, sashimi, temaki. An impressive choice of sakes and cocktails completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
13153;Paparoto Cucina;Brazil;São Paulo;Av. Pres. Juscelino Kubitschek, 2041 - Térreo, São Paulo, 04543-011, Brazil;-23.5920518;-46.6915164;33;false;true;Italian, Brazilian;Part of the luxury JK Iguatemi complex, this restaurant has a spacious and modern setting with a decor that includes plants and subdued lighting that accentuates the illuminated Italian phrase “Se non ora quando?” (“If not now, when”). Famous chef Dayse Paparoto, who won the first edition of Brazil’s Professional Masterchef, showcases his Italian-inspired menu with an authentic and innovative touch that is based around fresh, top-quality ingredients. The menu features an array of options, such as the excellent egg yolk ravioli with ricotta and spinach, served with a soft egg yolk. Other options include fresh pastas and risottos, although the desserts steal the show here, highlighting the extreme creativity of the chef in dishes such as tiramisu, served with a candy floss tree, which comes as a complete surprise.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13154;Metzi;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua João Moura, 861, São Paulo, 05412-002, Brazil;-23.5579746;-46.6795487;17;true;true;Mexican;Although the fusion of Brazilian and Mexican cuisine is not an immediately obvious one, the end result at Metzi is really impressive, thanks to the skill of chefs Luana Sabino and Eduardo Nava Ortiz, who met while working in a restaurant in New York and decided to combine their respective culinary talents for the benefit of their guests. Their cooking is a combination of Mexican techniques and traditions and Brazilian ingredients, with careful attention always paid to seasonality. Start, perhaps, with an exquisite tostada (crab, fish or Campechana), followed by barbecued lamb cooked according to pre-Hispanic techniques, then round things off with a refined Buñuelo doughnut served with camomile ice cream and drizzled with Jataí honey. Several vegan options are also available.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13155;Rudä;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Garcia D'Ávila, 118, Rio de Janeiro, 22421-010, Brazil;-22.9834208;-43.2090335;51;false;false;Brazilian, Contemporary;One of the most talked about restaurants in Ipanema. Here, chef Danilo Parah champions what he calls “emotional and creative cuisine” in a contemporary bistro-style setting featuring different ambiences and a private room on the first floor. Brazilian cuisine is very much to the fore and is showcased on a varied à la carte (plus an ”executive” menu) with a focus on local ingredients and in colourful, generous and highly flavourful dishes with little fear when it comes to combining lots of ingredients. It’s hard to forget the octopus with jambu fruit (a dish with a profusion of colours and textures that includes pasta cooked in a moqueca sauce) or the delicious cheesecake that takes on its own personality! The hospitality is on a par with the food here!;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
13156;Jiquitaia;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Coronel Oscar Porto 808, São Paulo, 04003-004, Brazil;-23.5761535;-46.6458013;77;true;false;Brazilian;If you're looking for typical homemade Brazilian cuisine prepared with quality ingredients, then this is the perfect place! Jiquitaia occupies a charming 1950s house surrounded by greenery, with a large, elegantly decorated dining room, where a plethora of wood and beautiful photos on the walls provide the decorative backdrop. Here, chef Marcelo Corrêa Bastos conjures up comforting traditional cuisine that feeds body and soul. During the working week, the playful “executive” menu is complemented by a concise menu featuring delicacies such as “coxinhas de frango caipira” (deep-fried dough filled with chicken), fish “moqueca” with shrimp, and grilled fish of the day served with a tasty pirão porridge. It's also worth noting that Jiquitaia also has a superb array of cachaças from across Brazil which have been carefully selected by the owner.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13157;Ama.zo - Cozinha Peruana;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Guaianases 1149, São Paulo, 01204-001, Brazil;-23.53255;-46.6467795;34;false;true;Peruvian, Farm to table;This restaurant occupies the charming garden of an old property known as the Casa da Don'Anna, a 20C house with a strong coffee legacy. The ambience here is delightful, protected by the vagaries of the weather by an almost invisible roof, and features large jabuticabeira trees, tables laid out in the garden, and a semi-open kitchen to the rear. Here, Peruvian chef Enrique Paredes conjures up Andean cuisine that is reinterpreted through the use of local ingredients, strong flavours, pleasant textures and subtle nuances from the Amazon region. Among the starters, the fresh oysters with a Japanese ponzu sauce, physalis and black massago stands out, followed, perhaps, by a main of ossobuco cooked at low temperature with an Arequipeño sauce, and accompanied by a cassava millefeuille. Lovers of cacao will adore the intense and absolutely delicious chocolate x 4!;Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13159;Clan BBQ;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Dias Ferreira, 233 Loja B, Rio de Janeiro, 22431 050, Brazil;-22.9841101;-43.2274659;68;false;true;Meats and Grills;To the backdrop of a neon sign “Não apague o meu fogo” (“Don’t put out my fire”) clearly visible above the door, chefs Pepo Figueiredo and Newton Rique showcase cuisine in which fire plays a key role here, enabling them to prepare fresh ingredients imbued with a special flavour. In this industrial-style ambience with a predominance of raw concrete, a sturdy tree takes centre stage in the middle of the dining room. There’s also the option of sitting at the counter by the grill to watch dishes and cocktails being prepared at close quarters. The menu is of course heavily focused on barbecued meats, although you’ll also find other options such as vegetables, fish and burgers. Dishes you won’t want to miss include the creamy oxtail croquettes and cubes of smoked tongue with aioli. The succulent French rack of lamb, served with chimichurri, is cooked to perfection.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13160;Henriqueta;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Aristides Espínola, Rio de Janeiro, 22440-050, Brazil;-22.985072;-43.2276381;30;false;true;Portuguese;This “tasca” style restaurant in the southern part of Rio de Janeiro showcases the best of Portuguese cuisine in a bright environment with a glass façade, open kitchen and Portuguese ceramic decoration. The cuisine on offer dispenses with unnecessary frills, focusing on the quality of the ingredients and dishes designed for sharing, among which the “biff-anas açorianas”, a crispy bread sandwich filled with pork escalope marinated in wine and garlic, stands out. As a main course, we recommend the tender octopus “a lagareiro” roasted in oil, served with onion confit and mashed potatoes, followed by the “toucinho do céu” made with egg yolks, almonds and cinnamon, an authentic Portuguese dish if ever there was one!;Terrace;[]
13161;Izär;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Barão Da Torre, 538, Rio de Janeiro, 22411-002, Brazil;-22.9827015;-43.209944;56;true;false;Spanish, Rice Dishes;Located in the heart of Ipanema, a district teeming with dining options, this Spanish-inspired restaurant stands out from the crowd. Here, is presented a menu on which paella is the undoubted star of the show and is available via a range of options. The variety of fish- and seafood-based dishes is also impressive, enhanced by the freshness and quality of the ingredients he uses. The menu spans traditional tapas to generous portions of paella perfect for sharing. The main distinction that sets Izär apart is the completely open kitchen with a bar counter enabling guests to watch as many as seven paellas being prepared at the same time. Alternatively, take a seat at one of the wood tables in the charming dining room crowned by a vaulted ceiling and lighting that recreates the feel of a starlit sky.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13162;Les Présidents;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Da Consolação 3527, São Paulo, 01416-001, Brazil;-23.5625625;-46.6700946;38;false;true;French;Under the helm of a famous chef who needs no introduction and who is widely known as a result of his participation in Masterchef, this bistro-style eatery offers refined cuisine inspired by Érick Jacquin’s French roots. Occupying a striking building with a completely black façade and red doors, the interior is no less impressive with its red walls and myriad paintings and embellishments that add to the typically French ambience. To enjoy the experience to the full, we recommend the flavoursome, traditional and hearty rabbit cassoulet and duck foie gras. A seven-course surprise tasting menu created by the chef is also available, alongside the à la carte and a midweek “executive” menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
13163;Spicy Fish;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Maria Quitéria, 99, Rio de Janeiro, 22410-040, Brazil;-22.9831796;-43.2071981;28;false;false;Asian Contemporary;A restaurant that is the talk of the town when it comes to Asian cuisine, a reputation enhanced by the magnificent building in which it is situated – a four-storey property featuring a decor of neutral tones, soft lighting and lots of plants which add a touch of freshness to the space. The cuisine created by chef Emerson Kim is a fusion of Japanese and Korean cooking, showcased via well-presented dishes with a unique flavour. The menu is extensive and for those unsure what to order, the chef’s selection includes two portions of nigiri, sashimi and the “house special”. Hot dishes include the reinterpretation of the Bibimbap, the finishing touches to which are always added at the table, and the delicious Kagoshima wagyu beef, known as Hot Stone.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13164;Piselli;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Padre João Manuel 1253, São Paulo, 01411-001, Brazil;-23.5672576;-46.667715;57;false;false;Italian;Piselli is the Italian word for “pea” and this vegetable is highly significant for the owner Juscelino Pereira who still maintains his custom of decorating every plate with three peas. Nowadays, the brand has three restaurants in São Paulo and one in Brasilia, and the cuisine is the same in each of them: namely, high-quality Italian cooking inspired by the Piedmont region. Dishes here are well prepared and full of flavour. Among them, we recommend the incredible “burrata calda al tartufo”, baked in delicious focaccia. Follow this, perhaps, with the homemade tortelloni filled with mozzarella di bufala and served with a fresh tomato and basil sauce, and the classic ossobuco alla milanese with saffron rice. In summary, a simply wonderful culinary experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13165;Jamile;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Treze de Maio 647, São Paulo, 01327-000, Brazil;-23.5586242;-46.6463018;86;false;false;Brazilian;The nostalgic Bixiga district of the city was the place chosen by famous chef Henrique Fogaça, a judge on Masterchef Brazil, to open this restaurant almost a decade ago. Now completely remodelled with exposed brick walls and a rustic-contemporary decor, Jamile features a large dining room, an open kitchen plus a bar counter for guests keen to watch the culinary action unfold, as well as an inner terrace. Traditional Brazilian cuisine is the mainstay here, showcased via a harmonious combination of ingredients and flavours from different regions. Options on the menu include crispy cupim dumplings with a pepper jelly, “cupim do sal” with yellow cassava and plantain farofa, as well as a delicious “moqueca baiana” of white fish with prawns and cassava farofa.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13166;Marine Restô;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Avenida Atlântica 4240, Rio de Janeiro, 22070-900, Brazil;-22.9858939;-43.1892062;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Enjoy one of the most breathtaking views of Copacabana beach at this restaurant on the sixth floor of the luxurious Fairmont Rio de Janeiro Copacabana hotel, where the panoramic terrace and swimming pool come as a highly scenic surprise! In this large, contemporary space with an open-view kitchen, choose from a mix of Brazilian and international cuisine which showcases top-quality ingredients and has a strong focus on quality and grilled dishes. As a result, some of the standout dishes on the menu are cooked on the Josper grill, such as the tender Carioca-roasted chicken, the mouthwatering Angus skirt steak with a guaraná demi-glace, and vegetarian options that include grilled heart of palm with smoked “bottled butter”.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13167;Rubaiyat Rio;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Jardim Botânico 971, Rio de Janeiro, 22470-051, Brazil;-22.97013;-43.22207;88;false;true;Meats and Grills;Located in the Jockey Club Brasileiro within the boundaries of the city’s botanical gardens, this restaurant boasts breathtaking views where you can enjoy a meal on the terrace to a picture-postcard backdrop that features the horse-racing track as well as the statue of Christ the Redeemer. Inside, there is a large dining room with a counter that is home to the kitchen, where a large glass window provides views of the churrasco grill. Renowned for its array of premium meats and for managing its own production, the restaurant offers more than ten different cuts, although fish, seafood, rice and a variety of sides also feature on the menu. On Saturdays, don't miss the chance to try the traditional feijoada stew, made with prime cuts of meat, along with milkshakes and an incredible dessert buffet!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13168;Oia Cozinha - Mediterrânea;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Barão da Torre 340, Rio de Janeiro, 22411-002, Brazil;-22.9831284;-43.2051081;83;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;If the prospect of a voyage to explore the flavours and charming ambience of the Aegean islands sounds appealing, this restaurant will fit the bill with its fresh and bright decor typical of a restaurant on the delightful island of Santorini, thanks to its attractive plants and relaxed blue and white colour scheme. The menu includes classic Greek dishes, the personality of which are enhanced by flavours from other Mediterranean countries. Start, perhaps with the truffle egg with a potato foam, mushroom ragu and Grana Padano tuile, followed by a choice of dishes from the land or sea, such as the traditional moussaka or the tender octopus served with a fantastic roast cauliflower cream, macadamia vinaigrette and broccoli.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13169;Huto Campo Belo;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Dr. Jesuíno Maciel 682, São Paulo, 04615-001, Brazil;-23.61822;-46.67361;50;true;false;Japanese;The star of the show here is the charcoal grill, providing a different emphasis to other restaurants in the Huto group. Taking a step back from the usual nigiri and sashimi, the menu includes a variety of seafood, fish, meat and vegetables, all of which are imbued with the smoky flavours of charcoal, alongside signature dishes from the renowned flagship eatery in Moema. The most attractive option is the Omakase, a tasting menu chosen by the chef, although you’ll also find a sushi bar serving fresh fish, roes and an array of top-quality seafood. The wood decor and soft lighting are the key features of the sophisticated yet welcoming ambience. If you have the chance, take a seat at the bar counter to feed off the energy from the kitchen as part of a unique dining experience.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13170;Cantaloup;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Manuel Guedes 474, São Paulo, 04536-070, Brazil;-23.58481;-46.67903;45;false;false;International;A real oasis of elegance that is immediately evident the moment you step through the door. Occupying a former bread factory, Cantaloup features high ceilings and a spacious and stylish dining room complemented by a classic-style bar in the corner. Next to it is an attractive waiting area protected by a retractable roof that provides plenty of light, which combines pleasantly with a charming green space and a fountain that adds a hint of freshness to the overall feel. Chef Valdir Oliveira offers an attractive menu based around international recipes that he creates via strong technique and well-defined combinations. Starters include delicious options such as foie gras, burrata and carpaccio, followed by mains such as duck magret, veal shank and “bobó de lagostim” (a type of crayfish stew). The wine list, which includes a selection of wines from 13 different countries, is the most comprehensive in the city.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13171;Vista;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Pedro Álvares Cabral 1301, São Paulo, 04094-050, Brazil;-23.58737;-46.652378;22;false;false;Brazilian;Occupying the top floor of the MAC USP (Museu de Arte Contemporânea da Universidade de São Paulo), this restaurant boasts spectacular views of Ibirapuera and a 360° panorama of the city. The kitchen is run by chef Pedro Oliveira, who offers guests a traditional Brazilian dining experience featuring typical ingredients from the country’s five regions, which he prepares in a harmonious and balanced way and is showcased on an “executive”-style format at lunchtime. On Saturdays, pumpkin shrimp with rice and sweet potato chips is the highlight, with crispy pururuca pork making an appearance on Sundays. The star of the show on the dessert menu is Vista’s own irresistible version of the traditional Portuguese dish “toucinho do Céu”, made with pumpkin, egg yolk and almonds. A special menu of starters and appetisers, plus an impressive selection of cocktails, is available on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13172;Dinho's;Brazil;São Paulo;Alameda Santos 86, São Paulo, 01418-000, Brazil;-23.5712927;-46.6462835;73;false;true;Meats and Grills;Dinho's was opened by Fuad Zegaib (the creator of the strip steak) six decades ago. Nowadays, the restaurant is run by chef Paulo Zegaib, the founder’s son. Occupying a new home on the ground floor of the Hotel Qoya, in the Paraíso section of the city (there’s also a Dinho’s in the Jardins district), it features a spacious, classically furnished main dining room, which is entirely glass-fronted and enclosed by a beautiful vertical garden plus a colourful open kitchen to one side. Renowned for its longevity in this bustling capital city, the restaurant offers superb cuts of beef, as well as feijoada on Thursdays and Saturdays, a buffet of salads and desserts, plus a copious seafood buffet on Fridays.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13173;Tanit;Brazil;São Paulo;Oscar Freire 145, São Paulo, 01426-001, Brazil;-23.5679568;-46.6636877;51;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This charming restaurant has become a reference for excellent Spanish cuisine in the city. In this bright, modern setting with high ceilings, polished cement floors and wood-clad walls, chef Oscar Bosch, who arrived in Brazil in 2009 having worked in leading restaurants in his native Spain such as El Bulli and El Celler de Can Roca, offers Mediterranean cuisine which he adapts to Brazilian tastes via refined technique and elaborate presentation. While tapas and a variety of rice dishes are an integral part of his identity, you can also enjoy other delicious options such as croquetas, patatas bravas and, as a main course, the classic roast suckling pig, cooked at low temperature and served with a velvety roasted carrot purée.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
13174;Chef Rouge;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Bela Cintra 2238, São Paulo, 01415-002, Brazil;-23.5636372;-46.6697676;65;true;true;French;An authentic French bistro, both in terms of its black façade and red awning and its elegant, welcoming interior. The main dining space is complemented by a charming terrace at the entrance, adorned with two impressive trees and with candlelight in the evening. Some of the tables are also occupied by adorable, large red teddy bears that add to the delightful atmosphere. Understandably, the culinary focus and star of the show is classic French cooking with a contemporary touch that is showcased by top-quality ingredients and delicately prepared dishes. These include the grilled foie gras with figs, served with bitter chocolate, and the classic roast duck breast with orange sauce accompanied by gaufrettes potatoes. The incredible Eclair XXL provides the perfect finale!;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
13175;Fasano Trattoria;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Iguatemi s/n, São Paulo, 01451-010, Brazil;-23.5865974;-46.6813744;21;false;true;Italian;This unique section of the city is home to the super-modern Pátio Malzoni alongside the Casa Bandeirista, an example of 17C Brazilian colonial architecture. Amid these contrasts, you’ll also find this exquisite trattoria paying homage to Southern Italy with its decor combining wood, leather and the flags of Italian football teams, plus a pleasant outdoor terrace. Here, the chef has created a menu featuring traditional recipes and dishes inspired by the region around Naples, including the island of Capri. The extensive choice includes the memorable linguine alle vongole with cherry tomatoes, the classic spaghetti alla carbonara, and the polpettone al forno (baked meatloaf), another excellent choice. Service is also a strong point here, so don’t hesitate to ask for a personal recommendation or choose one of the daily specials.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13176;Fogo de Chão;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Augusta 2077, São Paulo, 01413-000, Brazil;-23.56042;-46.66246;95;false;false;Meats and Grills;The Fogo de Chão restaurant is much more than just a place to eat as it represents Brazil’s churrasco tradition that has won admirers in different parts of the world. The origins of this method for cooking meat date back to the gauchos who discovered that skewering pieces of meat on wooden sticks and placing them around a fire transformed a simple cut of meat into a true delicacy. Served as part of “rodizio” all-you-can-eat format, the extensive selection includes beef, lamb and pork, as well as the famous prime rib and dry-aged meats (only available on the à la carte). To accompany the superb choice of meat, there’s also an extensive buffet of salads, rice dishes, carpaccios, cheeses and sausages. In total, there are five Fogo de Chão restaurants in São Paulo, all of which boast a comprehensive wine list. The new addition at the Jardins restaurant is a space dedicated to cigar-lovers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13177;A Figueira Rubaiyat;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Haddock Lobo 1738, São Paulo, 01414-002, Brazil;-23.5652766;-46.6697787;71;true;true;Meats and Grills;The backdrop here is definitely a surprise, thanks to the majestic Bengal fig, a century-old tree that attracts admiring glances inside this restaurant. The glass roof adds a special touch, enabling guests to admire the immensity of its crown and branches to the full. In keeping with its sister property in the famous Faria Lima, the cuisine is based around the "fork to plate” concept. Both the beef and pork are produced at the group’s own farms and distributed throughout its franchises. Dishes include baby beef, Denver steak, filet mignon, master beef and “tirita de picanha”, all of which are cooked to perfection, although the menu also features a variety of fish, rice and pasta options. Enhance your dining experience with the superb array of labels available on the wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13179;Aya Japanese Cuisine;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Pedroso de Morais 141, São Paulo, 05419-000, Brazil;-23.5684255;-46.688308;18;true;true;Japanese;This attractive property with a contemporary ambience and minimalist decor has a good location in a busy part of the city, just a few metres from the famous Avenida Rebouças. It is under the baton of sushi chef Juraci Pereira (better known as “Jura”) who, after working as Jun Sakamoto’s right-hand man for 11 years, decided to open his own venture in collaboration with his business partner Beto Ganme. Downstairs, where guests can sit at the counter to watch the expert hands of the chefs in action, the atmosphere is more intimate, while the upstairs is more modern and cosy. The cuisine includes a special Aya omakase menu, various types of sashimi, sushi (à la carte and combos), makimonos and hot dish options.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
13180;Amadeus;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Haddock Lobo 807, São Paulo, 01414-001, Brazil;-23.5592361;-46.6629717;25;true;true;Seafood;No description of Amadeus can be made without mentioning the Masano family, along with their passion, enthusiasm and dreams. Thanks to rave reviews of their cooking from friends, they decided to open a restaurant known as “fish corner” in São Paulo. Today, the kitchen is overseen by chef Bella Masano, the owners’ daughter, who embellishes the menu with her innovative culinary creations alongside classic dishes which have been given a contemporary makeover. Her cooking is showcased on an à la carte and tasting menu which includes options such as fresh oysters from the family’s own beds in Florianópolis. Amadeus’ signature dishes include the shrimp “à paulista”, prepared with olive oil and garlic, which is full of flavour and perfect for sharing, and the “moqueca Amadeus”, a stew with fish and shrimp, served with plantain and onion farofa – an exquisite combination!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13181;Cais;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Fidalga 314, São Paulo, 05432-000, Brazil;-23.5567144;-46.6895266;85;false;true;Seafood;A relaxed restaurant with a lively atmosphere and good food, so it’s not surprising that it’s always full. Occupying a charming small house in the Vila Madalena neighbourhood of the city, Cais features tables outdoors next to the window, seats at the counter by the kitchen, as well more traditional tables. Run by Adriano de Laurentiis in the kitchen and his business partner Guilherme Giraldi, sommelier and front of house manager, its cuisine is centred around fresh fish and seafood. The concise menu is constantly updated in line with the availability and freshness of seasonal ingredients. Having savoured the delicious appetisers on offer here, we particularly recommend the week’s selection of fish and seafood, followed by the creamy and delicate cheesecake served with a milk sorbet.;Air conditioning;[]
13182;De Segunda;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Prof. Tamandaré Toledo, 160, São Paulo, 04532-020, Brazil;-23.5834874;-46.6752488;57;true;true;Brazilian;Young chefs Júlia Tricate and Gabriel Coelho already have impressive CVs, having won TV food competitions and worked in Michelin-starred restaurants such as Noma (Copenhagen) and Oro (Rio de Janeiro). Following on from these incredible experiences, they decided to open their own restaurant, with an open kitchen and simple decor that helps to channel the complete focus onto their cuisine. Their modern culinary vision is showcased on a creative menu that champions fresh, seasonal ingredients. Start with the “katsu sando”, consisting of breaded pork belly in toasted milk bread and a sweet and sour Asian-inspired sauce. As a main, we recommend the “arroz caldoso” rice dish with cod served with a delicate beurre blanc, followed by the strawberry with yoghurt and jabuticaba, accompanied by an irresistible white chocolate ganache.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13183;Nôa;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Garcia D'Ávila, 135, Rio de Janeiro, 22421-010, Brazil;-22.9830825;-43.2093341;96;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Occupying a house from the 1930s with a well-preserved façade in one of the most renowned parts of Ipanema. The decor here has been meticulously designed, from the unusual fabrics hanging from the ceiling to the Hebrew-inspired paintings on the walls. The cuisine is inspired by the coasts of the Mediterranean, and includes fish, seafood and fresh pasta with a Brazilian and international flavour. The extensive menu features options such as burrata di bufala with beetroot pesto and Grana Padano. Mains range from the vegan “moqueca” stew to the excellent fresh pasta served with shrimp and an oyster foam. The charming veranda is perfect for one of Nôa’s refreshing cocktails.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13184;Nelita;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Ferreira De Araújo, 330, São Paulo, 05428-000, Brazil;-23.5605315;-46.6980906;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A recently opened restaurant that has already made a name for itself in the city’s Baixo Pinheiros district. Under the baton of chef Tássia Magalhães, an exclusively female team is in charge of the kitchen, conjuring up innovative dishes with an Italian influence. The wine list, which includes natural and organic wines, has been carefully curated by Danyel Steinle. To a modern decorative backdrop of exposed brick walls and different ambiences, guests can choose between tables at the entrance, the marble counter in front of the kitchen, or a private room which can be reserved for groups. The menu includes delicious fresh pastas such as Linguini with carrots and roe, alongside the appetizing Pork with pear and toasted bread. Absolutely perfect!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13185;Animus;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Vupabussu 347, São Paulo, 05429-040, Brazil;-23.5599769;-46.7000769;78;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The kitchen here is under the baton of young chef Giovanna Grossi, who has had an impressive career thus far. Having worked in renowned restaurants in France and Spain, she decided to open his own business where she offers creative cuisine that champions local and seasonal ingredients. Occupying a corner location in the charming Pinheiros district, Animus features a decor of warm tones combined with wood, and features an open kitchen where guests can observe the chefs in action. The menu comprises à la carte options and a six courses tasting menu, in addition to an “executive” menu available during the week.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13186;OCYÁ Leblon;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Aristides Espínola, 88, Rio de Janeiro, 22440-050, Brazil;-22.9855906;-43.2274811;91;true;true;Seafood;Fisherman, diver and chef Gerônimo Athuel is a font of knowledge when it comes to seafood, and is keen to highlight the importance of conscious, selective and artisanal fishing. He is also strongly committed to research into preserving and maturing techniques, as well as the use of all fish and seafood species, prioritising those that are often discarded. With one restaurant in Ilha Primeira already behind him, he has now brought his cuisine to this exclusive space in the Zona Sul. Here, the decor is modern with plenty of natural light and a glass-fronted fish maturing cabinet that highlights his culinary concept. Fabulous options on the menu range from seafood charcuterie to grilled, fried and raw fish dishes which will delight guests’ tastebuds with their surprising flavours and skilful technique and presentation.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13187;Blaise;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Itapeva, 435, São Paulo, 01332-000, Brazil;-23.5599768;-46.6527573;75;true;false;French Contemporary, South American;Occupying the historic Maternidade Filomena Matarazzo building, this restaurant takes its inspiration from the Franco-Swiss writer Braise Cendrars. The interior is similar to a wood cabin (similar to where he is said to have lived) and includes Brazilian volcanic stone crystals between the woodwork, rustic decor and subtle lighting provided by the lampshades that illuminate the room. Here, chef Fernando Bouzan, conjures up French cuisine with a Brazilian touch. Our suggestions include the succulent and incredibly tender braised beef tongue, served with potato salad and a refined red wine sauce. The jabuticaba sorbet with jam, jelly and jabuticaba pearls in a delicate “crème diplomate” is an absolute must!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13188;Haru Sushi;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Raimuindo Corrêa, 10, Rio de Janeiro, 22040-042, Brazil;-22.9722576;-43.1880595;68;true;false;Japanese;Owner-chef Menandro Rodrigues’ passion for Japanese cuisine provides the impetus for everything that goes on at this welcoming restaurant in Copacabana. On the ground floor, enjoy relaxed serviced at the pavement tables, while on the first floor you’ll find a dining room decorated in Japanese style with an impressive bar counter overlooking the kitchen, as well as tables and chairs laid out in different sections. The chef follows the Japanese “Kaisen” philosophy (which translates as “continuous improvement”) and devotes special attention to its techniques as well as to ingredients sourced directly from local fishermen. His cuisine is served as part of an Omakase menu, and includes options such as sushi, sashimi, and special and traditional “combos”. These are complemented by an extensive array of sakis that can be enjoyed in “tasting” measures.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
13189;Osso;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Bandeira Paulista, 520, São Paulo, 04532-001, Brazil;-23.5842326;-46.6759119;64;false;true;Meats and Grills;An address that is much prized by meat-lovers in the Greater São Paulo area. Here, chef Renzo Garibaldi, who is known as the “Master Butcher” in his native Peru, has opened his first culinary venture in Brazil. His cuisine is based around meat sourced from sustainable producers, with the option of dry aged and different maturing times covering an array of different cuts. Beef is the star of the show here, available as ribeye, fillet mignon, picanha and short ribs, alongside special dry-aged pure Wagyu, Vaca Velha and Angus. Dishes such as ceviche, salad, Josper-grilled fish and the rice-based “arroz de costela” also feature on the menu in a modern, elegant space with an extensive and superb wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13190;TARAZ;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Itapeva, 435, São Paulo, 01332-000, Brazil;-23.5601045;-46.6527894;21;false;true;South American;Part of the historic and former Condessa Filomena Matarazzo Maternity hospital complex, now converted into the luxury Rosewood São Paulo hotel, where the menu bears the signature of famous chef Felipe Bronze. In this charming space, the cooking is based around that of South America as a whole, with the open grill featuring prominently in a variety of harmonious dishes prepared with ingredients of the highest quality. Why not start with an authentic South American dish such as the excellent combination of tuna ceviche with caramelised peanuts, shiso, sesame, peanut milk and crispy tapioca? Follow this with a Brazilian classic – duck with tucupi (fermented manioc juice), sheep curd and toasted pineapple. For those who prefer to eat alfresco, the terrace is simply charming!;Terrace;[]
13191;Escama;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Visconde de Carandaí, 5, Rio de Janeiro, 22460 020, Brazil;-22.965067;-43.2196922;20;false;false;Seafood;After visiting a French restaurant with a similar outlook, inspiration struck to open this restaurant serving the best fish and seafood in a relaxed ambience. The focus at Escama is one that showcases the best maritime ingredients, which he always sources fresh from local fishermen. For your main, you can choose how you want to have your fish prepared (grilled, baked or poached), such as the sea bass, which is accompanied by a delicious champagne sauce and roasted onions. The menu also features options such as squid, shrimp, scallops and oysters, plus a splendid seafood feijoada on Fridays. The restaurant is located close to the city’s botanical garden, in a charming two-floor property with an extremely relaxed ambience enhanced by a decor of muted colours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13192;Kubo Zushi;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Das Tabocas 158, São Paulo, 05445-020, Brazil;-23.5511409;-46.6978653;65;false;true;Japanese;If you’re looking for a classic Japanese dining experience that is truly authentic and steers clear of any form of contemporary influence, especially when it comes to sushi and sashimi, this is the perfect restaurant for you. Here, to a backdrop of simple decor in the residential Vila Madalena district, chef Sergio Kubo prepare edomae sushi, a culinary tradition mastered over many years. The high quality of ingredients is clearly evident in dishes such tuna tartare, tartare with salmon roe, and tobiko and quail egg yolk, as well as an array of combinations. The restaurant is divided into three sections, although it is obvious that the sushi bar is the heart and soul of the property, where guests will enjoy watching and admiring the skill of Kubo Zushi’s chefs. There’s even an attractive play area for kids!;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
13193;Mondo;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Oscar Freire 30, São Paulo, 01426-000, Brazil;-23.5685022;-46.6627895;66;true;true;Italian;If you’re looking for a restaurant where you can enjoy excellent Italian cuisine, this is definitely the right place! Located at the end of the famous Rua Oscar Freire, it boasts an elegant glass façade and a spacious interior, with an open kitchen to the rear. The cooking revolves around classic Italian recipes, including pasta, but without neglecting generous dishes of fish and meat. The menu is teeming with amazing options, including “ravioli al tuorlo”, stuffed with ricotta, spinach and melted parmesan and served with a creamy egg yolk, and “pappardele con ragù d'ossobuco”. If you still have an appetite, we also recommend the majestic “filetto alla rossini”, served with black truffle and potato millefeuille. A midday “mezzogiorno” menu option is also available midweek.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
13195;Lassù;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Conselheiro Saraiva 207, São Paulo, 02037-020, Brazil;-23.4989496;-46.6251009;49;true;true;Italian Contemporary;If the idea of an incredible dining experience coupled with breathtaking views appeals to you, Lassù is able to combine both at the same time. With a location on the 28th floor of the lofty Edifício K1 in the Zona Norte district, this restaurant boasts one of the most impressive views of the city, with some tables enjoying a 270° perspective. The ambience here is both refined and elegant, enhanced by subtle lighting and a charming bar on one side of the dining room. The cuisine is a mix of Italian influences and ingredients from Brazil’s different regions. Standout dishes include the unmissable cod brandade served with black olive farofa, and the exquisite “lasagna ristorantino” with black truffle. The space also has the Lassù Rooftop Club, which makes it possible to celebrate exclusive events, besides a feijoada buffet with live music on Saturdays!;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13196;Sushi Leblon;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Dias Ferreira 256, Rio de Janeiro, 22431-050, Brazil;-22.9841634;-43.2272514;58;true;true;Japanese;An exclusive space with a trendy (and renowned) atmosphere in the southern part of Rio de Janeiro, where it has become a popular choice for those who enjoy high-quality Japanese cuisine. Open for almost four decades, the place is always on the up as it maintains its sense of tradition without turning its back on emerging food trends. In an intimate space decorated with a mix of dark tones and wood, the most sought-after spot is the bar counter by the kitchen where incredible dishes such as cubes of salmon with chilli pepper and truffle oil are served. Other options include the unmissable tuna tartare with free-range egg yolk and black roe, “combinados”, sushi, sashimi etc. At lunchtime, there’s more flexibility if you don’t have a reservation, but we recommend booking ahead for dinner.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13197;La Villa - Bistrô Francês;Brazil;Rio de Janeiro;Rua Alvaro Ramos 408, Rio de Janeiro, 22280-110, Brazil;-22.9574121;-43.1839668;43;false;true;French;This French brasserie occupies a unique property in Botafogo dating back to 1884 and has established itself as a trusted option for those who enjoy authentic Gallic cuisine. Under the management of French owner Gregoire Fortat, La Villa features a simple decor, high ceilings, outdoor tables and a pleasant and hospitable ambience. The menu here is centred around traditional French bistro fare with an added Brazilian touch. The experience begins with a delicious pâté de champagne served with bread baked on the premises, followed by the classic onion soup, and an authentic duck cassoulet. On Sundays, there’s also a French-Brazilian barbecue including an impressive array of fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13198;El Tranvia - Itaim Bibi;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Leopoldo Couto de Magalhães 1372, São Paulo, 03178-200, Brazil;-23.58936;-46.68544;29;false;false;Meats and Grills;Those who head to this restaurant should be in no doubt as to its reputation as a culinary institution showcasing the very best flavours of traditional Uruguayan cooking. The beef served here is of exceptional quality and includes numerous choice cuts (beef short ribs, strip loin, sirloin etc) and matured meat options that are enhanced to the full over the flames of the parrilla. You’ll also find fillets of meat of all types and sizes to cater to the many families from every generation who flock here, with the quantity of side dishes depending on the number of guests at the table. The fries and the delicious Uruguayan flan with “dulce de leche” are a must.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13199;Emiliano;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Oscar Freire 384, São Paulo, 01426-000, Brazil;-23.5657988;-46.6658133;82;false;false;International;Part of the majestic Hotel Emiliano, along the city’s iconic Rua Oscar Freire, with its array of luxury shops and boutiques, this eponymous restaurant is under the baton of chef Viviane Gonçalves (known as Chef Vivi), who focuses on classic cuisine that combines Brazilian flavours and Italian influences. Her concise menu includes dishes ranging from seared scallops with cauliflower cream and leeks to slow-roasted lamb served with yam purée and lamb stock. For dessert, centre stage is taken by the sweet and crunchy combination of banana, peanut and dulce de leche with vanilla sorbet. The classical decor, enhanced by extensive windows and views of a vertical garden, provides the perfect setting for a delightful meal.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Valet parking;[]
13200;Varanda;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Prudente Correia 432, São Paulo, 01450-030, Brazil;-23.5768616;-46.6866363;61;false;false;Meats and Grills;This renowned group, with three outlets in São Paulo, not only serves the best and most perfectly cooked meat, it also exclusively uses products from the renowned Intermezzo brand, whose quality is strictly controlled and certified to ensure excellence across the board. The kitchen, under the baton of chef Fabio Lazzarini, offers a wide selection of beef cuts cooked in the Brazilian, Argentinian and American styles, which are considered the best grilling methods worldwide. The menu ranges from the famous Kobe-style beef (considered a global delicacy), rump heart, rib flank, sirloin and porterhouse to the Varanda al Mare, a menu specialising in seafood and fish which, in keeping with the meat on the menu, showcases maximum quality and freshness. Vegetarian and vegan options are also available.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13201;Vinheria Percussi;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Bianchi Bertoldi 109, São Paulo, 05422-070, Brazil;-23.56877;-46.69108;15;true;false;Italian;A family-run Italian restaurant that was a trailblazer for enogastronomy (the pairing of food and wine) in Brazil. It first opened as a wine shop in 1985 with the aim of offering good wine and food to go with it. However, with the arrival of chef Silvia Percussi and her brother Lamberto Percussi (restaurant manager and sommelier) the concept was taken to the next level. In this classic, welcoming setting, enjoy excellent cuisine including fresh pasta, which is a particular highlight. Classic dishes that you’ll want to try include the perfectly creamy tonnarelli alla carbonara, the beef ossobuco, served with a divine sauce, and the tiramisu, which is brought to your table on a platter. Why not pair these delicacies with one of the fines wines on the 300-strong wine list and in the award-winning cellar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13202;A Casa do Porco;Brazil;São Paulo;Rua Araujo 124, São Paulo, 01220-020, Brazil;-23.5448671;-46.6447421;80;false;false;Brazilian, Pork;If you’re keen to try pork that you won’t find anywhere else, then this (as the name would suggest!) is the perfect place. Here, chefs Jefferson Rueda and Janaína Torres, who are responsible for rearing their pigs and for growing most of the vegetables used in their restaurant, have rekindled and revisited the flavours from their childhood through dishes showcasing sophisticated technique. In this informal and relaxed space, with an open kitchen and a small grocery store, their cuisine comes courtesy of an à la carte and a tasting menu entitled “We are all Meat and Bone”, which also comes in a vegetarian format. Dishes that you won’t want to miss include the pork tartare with its slightly creamy texture and served with crunchy root vegetables of the day, the Ossobuco accompanied by an aromatic onion soup, and the typical Porco San Zé, slow roasted for 6-9 hours, which explains its sublime texture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13203;KANOE;Brazil;São Paulo;Alameda Itu 1578, São Paulo, 01421-004, Brazil;-23.5578032;-46.6660508;69;true;false;Japanese;An unusual and exclusive restaurant that is more akin to a secret dining club. In the bright interior, with its minimalist decor and impressive dining counter with just nine seats, the aim is to resurrect classic and authentic Japanese cuisine using ancestral techniques that make full use of the best market ingredients (scallops with sea salt, sea bream with yozu, yellowtail with sesame, horse mackerel etc). Chef and master of ceremonies Tadashi Shiraishi explains each dish on the single Omakase menu and how his maternal grandmother encouraged him to rediscover the culinary knowledge of his ancestors. The chef also enjoys organising unique food tours to Japan for his guests to introduce them to the country’s unique gastronomic culture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13204;Ama.zo - Pátio Higienópolis;Brazil;São Paulo;Avenida Higienópolis 618, São Paulo, 01238-001, Brazil;-23.5423921;-46.657901;81;false;true;Peruvian;Located outside of the Pátio Higienópolis shopping mall, it features an attractive room with lots of natural light and an open-air terrace decorated with plants and Peruvian works of art. Here, the Lima-born chef Enrique Paredes, whose philosophy is “Cooking with freedom”, is at the helm of his second venture, where he combines Peruvian flavours and techniques with local ingredients to showcase the flavours of the Amazon, without losing sight of the region’s roots. On the menu you’ll find dishes such as langoustine carpaccio, the traditional Lima dish “causa limeña”, along with various types of ceviche, rice dishes and vegetarian and vegan options. One dessert that you won’t want to pass up is the “Suspiro Limeño” made with delicious Peruvian “dulce de leche”, a dehydrated quinoa and togarashi meringue, praline and chocolate sorbet – a true delight for the tastebuds!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13205;FOGO;France;Paris;8 rue Meissonier, Paris, 75017, France;48.8835431;2.3045801;94;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In his open kitchen – part of a meticulously appointed decor composed principally of premium and natural materials (such as veined marble, wood and stone) – the chef joyously sets about cooking on a charcoal grill, in a tribute to the gauchos, Brazil's traditional cowboys. The resulting dishes are generous, spicy and vibrant.;;[]
13206;Bairoz;France;Nantes;40 bis rue Fouré, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2115848;-1.5469661;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Just a stone's throw from the River Loire, this charming, modern restaurant sports a striking decor: pendant lights, wood panelling and exposed stonework. At the helm are chef Estelle Méheust and pastry chef Jérôme Berdelou, both of whom are active in the kitchen as well as the dining room: one starts the service while the starters and main courses are being served, the other taking over when it comes to the desserts. This charming, discreet couple won us over with their market-fresh fare at lunchtime, and their more high-level cuisine at dinner. The jus are particularly tasty, eg the mushroom emulsion on the raviolo filled with brousse soft cheese, or the creamy bisque on the hake, saffron purple top turnips and fondant potatoes.;;[]
13209;Mouffu;France;Clermont-Ferrand;4 rue Ribeyre-Jaffeux, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7785633;3.0792648;19;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;After Le Saint Eutrope, here's a second convivial restaurant where diners come to feast on down-to-earth fare such as pâté en croûte, vol-au-vent or pork filet mignon with a mustard sauce – served with a good selection of natural wines. The chef-patron, the son of a baker, changed course to become a chef. His succinct menu with clear headings is a veritable ode to family and humble cuisine. The simple bistro decor is a touch vintage, with antiques and mismatched furniture. Friendly and festive atmosphere.;Air conditioning;[]
13210;Ondine;France;Strasbourg;10 petite rue des Dentelles, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5815124;7.742881;46;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the picturesque little streets of the Petite France neighbourhood, this tiny restaurant attracts those looking for a lively, meaningful culinary experience. At the helm are Noémie D'hooge, an art graduate turned chef, and her partner Marin Rémy, whose path has been more conventional. Their modern, predominantly plant-based set menu is full of finesse, featuring seasonal ingredients that have been carefully selected from small local producers. You'll be pleasantly struck by the variety of dishes, which are never repeated twice. The pair work in front of the customer in a pleasant, laid-back atmosphere. As for drinks, the Salvadoran sommelier serves a range of wines, often natural, as well as home-made kombuchas and other non-alcoholic concoctions.;;[]
13214;Mijoba;France;Marseille;79 boulevard Vauban, Marseille, 13006, France;43.2832653;5.3748917;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Venezuelan-born chef David Mijoba, well known on Marseille's restaurant scene, has opened his own bistro in the Vauban neighbourhood, with Notre-Dame-de-la-Garde as a backdrop. With fruit and vegetables from the region, fish (some caught locally), and spices from all over the world, his passion for ingredients is evident, with practically every dish featuring produce with a protected geographical indication. This flavoursome cosmopolitan cuisine taps into one continent after another, with lunch tending towards vegetables and dinner being more fish and seafood-based. On this occasion, lunch was a feast of raw and cooked purple artichokes from Le Garlaban, raw and marinated scallops from Deauville, served with chop suey and a beef broth with Hanoi spices and, to finish, a flaky tarte fine with caramelised apples and home-made ice cream. A fine selection of "living" wines, particularly from the Jura.;Air conditioning;[]
13215;Le Boréal;France;Paris;39 rue Montcalm, Paris, 75018, France;48.8938017;2.3389877;72;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Come in from the cold of rue du Pôle-Nord ("North Pole Street") – a warm welcome awaits you, courtesy of chef Philippine Jaillet and her partner Charles Neyers. Their restaurant with an open kitchen, brass counter and Thonet chairs has all the trappings of a typical Parisian bistro. When it comes to food, they use good fresh ingredients in keeping with the seasons to fashion contemporary creations with an innovative and quirky touch, as seen in the mushroom chawanmushi (a Japanese egg custard dish without milk or sugar, normally prepared with dashi), cep praline, pickles and grilled mushrooms, or vegetarian pithiviers with celeriac. Very reasonably priced lunch menu.;;[]
13217;Castacán;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Calle Puebla 387, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4201541;-99.1744549;87;false;false;Mexican;There are two reasons to make a beeline to this Roma Norte restaurant and they're both focused on pork. This spot's large staff welcomes diners at both lunch and dinner, but everyone is focused on the food. Cochinita pibil and lechon tacos compete for your attention, so get both. Good quality tortillas get things off to a good start. The slow-roasted, marinated pork that's shredded and enhanced with pickled red onions is top notch, while the lechon tacos plate tender, roast suckling pig with pieces of crispy skin for a standout bite. A wide range of salsas is on offer, from spicy habanero and a sesame aioli to mild yogurt sauce.;;[]
13218;Cariñito Tacos;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Guanajuato 53, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4174489;-99.156818;72;true;true;Mexican;This is certainly not your tia's taqueria. Instead, this spot doles out tacos with a Southeast-Asian bent. Order at the white tiled counter and take a peek at the highly efficient kitchen where everything is prepared to order, then grab a seat outside. Tacos like the Cantonese, with confit porkbelly, a mix of spices, plus hoisin, sriracha and pickled cucumber in a flour tortilla, are served on dried corn husks instead of plates. The siu yuk wraps crispy roast pork with nam jim jaew sauce and encurtidos in a flour tortilla for a successful marriage of flavor and texture.;;[]
13219;Tacos Hola El Güero;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Ámsterdam 135, Hipódromo, Cuauhtémoc, 06100, Mexico;19.4116887;-99.1714972;29;true;false;Mexican;This longstanding taqueria in Condesa has been open since 1968 and features a large selection of guisado (stewed) tacos with hearty meat and vegetarian fillings, all kept warm in large ceramic pots. It's an order at the counter-style spot with just a few small tables outside. Choose between one or two tortillas and various toppings. Standouts include the picadillo, with well-seasoned ground meat and potatoes topped with creamy green salsa with avocado and cotija cheese, and the chorizo con papa, with two larger corn tortillas topped with a chorizo and potato mixture, black beans, cotija cheese, and a semi-spicy salsa.;;[]
13220;Guzina Oaxaca;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Avenida Presidente Masaryk 465, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11560, Mexico;19.4325514;-99.2036507;98;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Mexican;Set on a street lined with luxury shops in the Polanco neighborhood, Guzina Oaxaca shines a spotlight on the gastronomy of this southern Mexican region. The cuisine, based on corn and chile, is known for its moles and its inclusion of insects, including grasshoppers. Chef Álex Ruiz, who designed the menu, and Chef Carlos Galán, who executes the dishes, hail from Oaxaca, and Chef Galán credits his grandmothers for sharing their passion for the cuisine. Arrive in the morning for a full breakfast menu or come later in the day to savor classic dishes such as memelitas tradicionales, tlayuda, tamaliza de mole negro con pollo, and of course, a cup of chocolate.;Terrace;[]
13221;Mari Gold;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Gob. Protasio Pérez de Tagle 66, San Miguel Chapultepec, Miguel Hildalgo, 11850, Mexico;19.412971;-99.1836384;79;true;true;Fusion, Indian;From its dining room to the kitchen turning out plates with an India-meets-Mexico slant, Mari Gold comes with a dose of fun. Pop by for lunch or brunch for tasty dishes, as in the freshly made picadas with flaky fish that are livened up with flecks of soft tomato, slices of green olive and a tart chutney. Servers are quick to offer suggestions if you're stumped but whatever you do, be sure to order a jugo verde for a refreshing start and finish with the very satisfying falooda dessert with plenty of rich and tangy marmalade, creamy-smooth ice cream, and rice flour noodles.;Air conditioning;[]
13222;Martínez;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Puebla 90, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4231363;-99.1586301;56;true;false;Contemporary;Chef/owner Lucho Martinez was inspired to open this eponymous restaurant by his daughter, Emilia, who once shared that her favorite thing to do in Paris was eat in the bistros with him. It sparked an idea—why not recreate that feeling right here in Mexico City—and Martinez is just that: a small restaurant with good food and wine.The ambience is young and bustling. Order at the bar and you'll get a sneak peek into the kitchen. The concise menu features a list of tasty dishes with nods to Mexican, French and even Japanese cuisine. Pollo a la parrilla is a main course hit, while chocolate cake with vanilla ice cream is spot on.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13223;Limosneros;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Ignacio Allende 3, Centro, Cuauhtémoc, 06010, Mexico;19.4360971;-99.1379026;63;false;false;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;Taking its name from the "limosneros walls" built in ancient times, this centrally located spot is perfectly poised for downtown dwellers and visitors. From the remnants of an old fountain in the entrance hall to the walls hung with mirrors from Tlayacapan, Puebla talavera, and Huichol embroidery, this place is loaded with charm. This kitchen has a clear respect for tradition, even reviving old recipes, but it's all done with an infusion of contemporary flair. Opt for the tasting menu and you'll be rewarded with a tour of their flavorful, well-prepared cuisine, or choose the unusual-but-intriguing taco tasting, which also includes a sweet offering.;Terrace;[]
13224;Aúna;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Anatole France 139, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11550, Mexico;19.4331786;-99.1973857;90;true;false;Contemporary;Chef Jorge Vallejo delivers the best of both worlds at this two-in-one space where Aúna Café welcomes guests with breakfast and lunch, and Aúna Restaurant invites more serious diners. Enter through a separate door to access the light-filled restaurant where abundant greenery sets a natural tone, and exposed brick and natural elements create a cozy and enticing space. Of course, it's the flavorful, contemporary cooking that takes center stage. Every detail is given the highest regard, and seasonal produce shines in dishes like such as jitomates rostizados and lobina rayada with salsa romesco. Everything is light and delicious to the very end, with a refreshing dessert of piña-coco sealing the deal.;;[]
13225;Carmela y Sal;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Pedregal, 24, Col Molino del Rey, Lomas de Chapultepec, Miguel Hildalgo, 11040, Mexico;19.4254133;-99.2033424;22;false;false;Mexican;Carmela y Sal is Chef Gabriela Ruiz Lugo's love letter to her Tabasco roots. She shares so much of her personality in this welcoming, modern restaurant where a kind staff ensures an enjoyable experience. This isn't food that you'll find on every corner. Its distinct personality is memorable, and you'll be back in no time for another terrific meal. Don't miss dishes like the broccoli with spicy sauces, cheese and black piquin chili. Short rib con chirmol is packed with flavor, thanks to the generous sauce, and is a hearty dish intended for big appetites. Mostachón is a simple dessert to round things out.;Air conditioning;[]
13226;Contramar;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Durango 200, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4195779;-99.1671515;42;true;true;Seafood, Mexican;Contramar, with its beautiful terrace and its huge windows framing views of the outside, will enchant you from start to finish. Inside, the music and the hustle and bustle of the open kitchen help liven up the atmosphere. Chef Gabriela Cámara has other restaurants in Mexico City but this one has been open since 1998. The house specialty, with a focus on fish and seafood, is the tuna tostada, and it's the dish that everyone comes to savor. Although it is not a taqueria, it offers a series of tacos as delicious as shrimp, octopus carnitas, or al pastor made with fish and a touch of pineapple, cilantro, and chives. Remember to leave room for dessert: the meringue with strawberries is the most requested.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13227;Nicos;Mexico;Azcapotzalco;Cuitláhuac, 3102, Claveria, Azcapotzalco, 02080, Mexico;19.4650343;-99.1776703;43;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Mexican;Nicos was once a humble stand selling sodas and snacks until one day a customer saw employees eating something delicious and the restaurant was born. The son of the founder now serves as chef, overseeing a tasting menu of classic Mexican cuisine features such standouts as taco de cecina crujiente on a corn tortilla that delivers characteristic intensity. and a flavor-packed, bright dish of camarones al tamarindo. An enchilada stuffed with tasado and beans and bathed in a pixtle sauce from Oaxaca is an aromatic, tasty crowd-pleasing dish, while the aguachile comes with a feisty kick thanks to fiery chili peppers.;;[]
13228;Taqueria El Paisa;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Joaquin Garcia Icazbalceta 36, San Rafael, Cuauhtémoc, 06470, Mexico;19.4408204;-99.1610057;20;true;false;Mexican;On a corner in San Rafael, this bustling taqueria is a well-oiled machine. Everyone comes for the suadero, which is best ordered late in the evening when the meat has had hours to braise in its own fat. The al pastor is worth a try too. Whatever the order, tacos are on the small side so aim for three or four per person. Once through the queue, people eat wherever they can: sitting on the curb, leaning against a building, or on the hoods of their cars.;;[]
13229;Entremar;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Hegel 307, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11560, Mexico;19.4331717;-99.1881925;22;false;true;Seafood, Mexican;There are plenty of enviable seats at Entremar, though certainly those on the terrace under the awnings and surrounded by plants are first on the list. Inside, try to book on the first floor, with the best tables resting in a row at the back overlooking the Plaza Uruguay.Of course, Entremar is about so much more than a good seat, and some of the best dishes to order include fresh tuna tostadas with chipotle sauce, a little avocado and fried leek, giving them a crunchy touch. Choose wisely when it comes to the aguachile, as the red is spicy, while pescado a la talla is the restaurant's signature dish. The boneless grilled fish is a feast for the eyes with its two sides sharing a red and green sauce. Finish with the tarta de higos or merengue con fresas.;;[]
13230;Botánico;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Alfonso Reyes 217, Condesa, Cuauhtémoc, 06100, Mexico;19.4071091;-99.1739583;74;true;true;Contemporary;Upon first glance, it may not look like much, but the exterior belies the oasis found within. Tall cacti, a lake stocked with fish and a convivial atmosphere make this a natural choice for date night, but this laidback spot is equally well suited to families and groups too. Everyone enjoys being here as they connect over plates like homemade ravioli with blue crab and a pumpkin cream base, or a simple grilled fish with al dente vegetables. Crème brûlée delivers a strange-sounding surprise with the addition of Kalamata olive, but it's a convincing finale.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13231;Los Danzantes Mexico City;Mexico;Coyoacán;Parque Centenario 12, Jardín Centenario, Coyoacán, 04000, Mexico;19.3487834;-99.1636504;50;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Located in downtown Coyoacan, Los Danzantes is often busy with a mix of locals and foreigners. Set in a historic building, this restaurant shines a spotlight on contemporary Mexican cuisine, and the menu is packed with a wide variety of dishes. Chef Alejandro Piñom knows what works--the hoja santa with a base of goat cheese and a miltomate sauce with chile, has been on the menu for more than two decades. Filete de res en chichilo has a hint of smoke from the grill but it's the mole that stands out. Empanada de membrillo pairs quince and cheese for a pleasant taste. Their sister spot in Oaxaca shares the same name but offers a different style and menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13232;Lorea;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Sinaloa, 141, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4202321;-99.1700682;94;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Named after the Basque word for flower, this Roma Norte restaurant is Chef Oswaldo Oliva’s way of evoking memories of his life back in Spain. The multilevel space has handsome wood tables and smooth finishes all over, but perhaps the best seat in the house is right at the chef’s counter, where guests can watch all of the action. This quiet, perpetually clean kitchen prepares only a single, seasonal tasting menu that is loosely based on Mexican cooking but more widely takes culinary inspiration from all over: a buttery lobster brioche roll with ikura emulsion, shrimp tostada with smoked chili aioli, and crudo with strawberry. Not all of the team’s ambitious ideas come together clearly but the effort and style are commendable.;Air conditioning;[]
13233;Sarde;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Puebla 109, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4231292;-99.1598157;39;false;true;Contemporary;Set in the Roma Norte neighborhood in a charming three-story townhouse, Sarde makes no bones about its specialty—the name says it all. Sarde, which means "sardine" in French and Italian, is focused on the sea, and their contemporary dishes are rooted in the freshest seasonally appropriate product possible from the Mexican coasts. Cold dishes of Japanese cuts like kampachi and macarela stand out alongside modern reinterpretations of familiar favorites like fish and chips.Attention to detail, especially when it comes to presentation, is appreciated in this warm and welcoming spot with exposed brick and wood details. The cozy bar entices with interesting cocktails and is a nice perch for solo diners.;Counter dining;[]
13234;El Tigre Silencioso;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Colima 159 1A, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.420399;-99.1597464;30;false;false;Creative, Mexican;This cool Roma Norte spot has a front courtyard laid with stone blocks, set with tables, and enhanced by old growth trees. The interior dining area is set a few steps above and is fronted by ivy-wrapped columns and a wrap-around terrace for additional al fresco dining. Inside, the space features wood plank flooring, stucco walls, a bar, and open kitchen in back.The menu offers an abundant array of choices, and the creative items are sparked by an intriguing combination of ingredients. Empanadas norteños is a golden-crisped half-moon stuffed with chicharrón prensado and smoked fish. The zesty octopus stew is topped with bits of crunchy menudo and accompanied by freshly made tortillas.;;[]
13235;Migrante;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Chiapas, 186, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.41184;-99.1649269;15;true;true;International;Modern, with a stylish flair and an impressive set-up, Migrante benefits from a young team with a warm and welcoming attitude. An open kitchen is always busy sending out contemporary, internationally minded plates like crispy prawns with homemade mandarin kosho and radish salad or homemade churros with charred mamey sided by butternut squash purée and seared foie gras. The mini grilled artichoke sandwich with cured kampachi is a delicious snack before a main dish like striped Bass cooked in charcoal, mussels and yuzu beurre blanc.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13236;Barbacoa Gonzalitos;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Calle Colima 76, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4206541;-99.1564096;99;true;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;This taqueria in Roma Norte specializes in northern-style tacos. The short list starts with their signature barbacoa de res which can be tucked into a corn or flour tortilla and is a juicy and flavorful morsel, particularly when done "dorado-style," or shallow fried to produce a crisped tortilla. Any option is worthwhile, and the range includes a tempura-fried chile relleno or the machacado con huevo (shredded beef with scrambled eggs).The food is adeptly prepared in the small kitchen and guests grab a seat at the few tables or counter arrangement on the sidewalk.;;[]
13238;Cana;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Liverpool 9, Juárez, Cuauhtémoc, 06600, Mexico;19.4282159;-99.1563375;52;false;true;Contemporary, International;Light-filled with a classically elegant look, Cana is at once cozy and bustling with a bistro atmosphere that is inviting yet informal. Just right for date night, it's also a perfect pick for a night out with friends. No matter what you settle on, you're sure to have a pleasant experience here.The small menu of contemporary Mexican cuisine is based on seasonal and local produce with well-presented dishes ranging from croquetas de bacalao and arroz meloso con calamar y almejas to magret de pato, zanahorias y farro and cheesecake de camembert y compota de guayaba.;Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13241;Ruba's Bakery;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Morelos 8, San José del Cabo, 23406, Mexico;23.0632278;-109.6963233;67;true;true;Mexican, Bakery;There's sure to be a crowd at this Arts District charmer, housed in a casita dating back to the 1940s. The space is fronted by umbrella-shaded tables facing a papel picado-strewn street. Inside and out back, it's all quite comfortable.This casual bistro serves throughout the day, and there is a coffee counter and display case of conchas, croissants and donuts, among other treats. More substantial offerings include cheese and charcuterie, salads, sandwiches and wood-fired pizza. At brunch, order the chilaquiles (available only Friday-Sunday), served in a skillet with crisp yellow corn tortilla chips soaked in a morita chile sauce, accompanied by diced bits of roasted lamb and a Valle de Guadalupe-style consommé. The freshly baked bolillo is great for dipping in the broth.;Brunch;[]
13242;Almoraduz;Mexico;Puerto Escondido;Benito Juárez 11 & 12, Rinconada, Puerto Escondido, 71983, Mexico;15.861743;-97.0776367;55;true;true;Mexican;This ambitious restaurant has for years set the standard for serious cooking in sunny Puerto Escondido. Open since 2013 by a husband-and-wife team, Almoraduz is Oaxacan at its core but pulls inspiration from all over. Think slices of raw Baja tuna set in a fennel, shallot, and vanilla emulsion and paired with warm pita. Or, consider a traditional pescadilla stuffed with fish and brown sugar and garnished with purple cabbage. Whether you order a la carte or trust the kitchen with the signature tasting menu, expect attractive presentations and bold flavors. The space is equally inviting with its handsome wood tables, comfy dining chairs, and pleasant greenery. Service is ace as well thanks to friendly servers with a strong attention to detail.;;[]
13243;CARBÓNCABRÓN;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Boulevard Cerro Colorado, México 1 Kilómetro 24.5, 23400, San José del Cabo, 23400, Mexico;23.0015099;-109.7340161;91;false;false;Contemporary;Chef Poncho Cadena is in charge at this moody space where it will take your eyes a minute to adjust to the darkness. Library-style stacks of mesquite wood serve as a dramatic design theme but also as a not-so-subtle hint at the live fire concept. The menu is divided into vegetables, seafood and "black market" meats including tongue, sweetbread and more. These plates are ideal for sharing, though a chef's tasting menu is on hand for those who want to sample it all. Nuanced cooking is seen in dishes like the onion petals filled with habanero aïoli, coated in charcoal tempura batter, and fried. Served simply in a bowl, guests are encouraged to use their hands to scoop up these delights. Tail-on shrimp over a thick slice of pork belly leans sweet but satisfying.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13244;Ancestral Cocina Tradicional;Mexico;Oaxaca;José López Alavéz 1347, Oaxaca, 68040, Mexico;17.074822;-96.7237426;37;true;false;Mexican;Nestled in a grove of trees under a thatched roof, this spacious, outdoor restaurant in the Barrio de Xochimilco neighborhood has been something of a hidden oasis since 2017. The flavors are fairly classical, as Chef Miguel Mijangos takes inspiration from his grandmother, his childhood, and beyond. An opening volley of local cheese compressed with tomato and herbs, a jar of pickled vegetables, and warm, crispy tostadas is a treat all on its own. The cooking gets creative in dishes like plantains stuffed and garnished with queso and crema and finished with mole coloradito. With a flair for attractive presentations, the restaurant serves a more classic breakfast with the likes of memelas, quesadillas, and tetelas made on the comal by the entrance.;Terrace;[]
13245;Maizajo;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Fernando Montes De Oca 113, Condesa, Cuauhtémoc, 06140, Mexico;19.4148588;-99.1781367;44;false;false;Mexican;While their downstairs taqueria is standing room only, upstairs at Maizajo, diners are encouraged to pull up a chair. There is a clear industrial chic aesthetic to this dining room, where I-beams stand in for legs at metal tables and chairs are made from heavy rebar.You'll be greeted with some tostadas and a spicy habanero and pepita salsa at your table as you peruse Chef Santiago Muñoz Moctezuma's menu. Top picks include an oven-roasted blue corn tostada topped with avocado puree and sliced raw yellowfin tuna in a black sesame oil and soy dressing, as well as the tamal de boda. This vegetarian corn tamal filled with stewed poblano chile, leeks, and chard in an achiote, tomato and habanero salsa is topped with thinly sliced tubers for a dish that is equal parts sweet and earthy.;;[]
13246;Ricos Tacos Toluca;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;López 103, Centro, Cuauhtémoc, 06000, Mexico;19.4293577;-99.1427626;52;false;false;Mexican;In more than two decades, this taqueria has moved three times. It's now situated in the Centro Histórico of Mexico City near the Mercado De San Juan. There are just a few red stools, so come early or you'll eat standing up. This taqueria specializes in handmade Toluca-style chorizo and sausages. Sample individually to appreciate the flavors and unique characters of each chorizo or mix them for an equally satisfying experience. Top with grilled or fresh onions, French fries, cilantro and various salsas. Obispo is a large pork-based sausage, seared ever so slightly for a delicate crisp, while chorizo tamarindo is diced then grilled and delivers a subtle sweetness and terrific flavor.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
13247;Campobaja;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Colima 124, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4201946;-99.1583255;72;true;true;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;Chef Alejandro Zarate brings the cuisine of Ensenada to Mexico City with Campobaja. Set on two floors, the restaurant's upper level is reminiscent of a warehouse with high ceilings, iron beams, and recycled wood materials used for towing boats that have been reborn as tables, seating and accents.The kitchen is inspired by the honest and simple cuisine of a Mexican fish camp. The quality of the seafood is paramount, and the menu is designed for sharing, with dishes ranging from ceviches and aguachiles to burritos, tostadas, and fish tacos, of course. Fried spiny red lobster and grilled octopus are two highlights not to miss.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13248;MeroToro;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Avenida Ámsterdam 204, Hipódromo, Cuauhtémoc, 06100, Mexico;19.409639;-99.16986;54;false;true;Contemporary, Mexican;Located on a tree-lined street surrounded by restaurants in the Condesa neighborhood, MeroToro delights guests with its cozy environs. The terrace is a nice spot, while indoors, the contemporary styling is particularly inviting. Chef Jair Téllez plates simple, straightforward, and flavorful dishes based on the cuisine of Baja, California. The menu balances meat and seafood, and a tasting menu is also on offer. Dishes that never fail to impress include the tostada de ceviche de pescado, jaiba suave rebozada, and arroz cremoso con camarón, while meat eaters will be delighted by rabo de res braseado. Desserts such as pastel de chocolate, crema de téjate, and helado de yogurt seal the deal.;Terrace;[]
13249;Sartoria;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Orizaba, 42, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.42194;-99.1605399;89;true;false;Italian, Italian Contemporary;Sartoria, with its terrace outside and its industrial-chic interior, is always buzzing with a crowd of young diners and couples, here to enjoy a night out. The kitchen turns out typical Italian offerings, ranging from antipasti and pasta to entrees. The menu may not be large, but there's something for everyone. Great care is taken with the presentation in dishes like tortellacci with a creamy burrata that tastes as good as it looks, and entrees highlight quality products. To finish, you'll never go wrong with a classic tiramisu.;Terrace;[]
13250;La Barra de Fran;Mexico;Miguel Hildalgo;Emilio Castelar, 185, Polanco, Miguel Hildalgo, 11560, Mexico;19.4306954;-99.2003001;83;false;false;Spanish;Just in case you're unsure of the offerings inside La Barra de Fran, a bull's head is posted right at the entrance as a good reminder that the soul of this place, and its flavors, are decidedly Spanish. It's fashioned after Spain's famed tapas bars, and it's a perfect place to go for a fun night out. Taste the likes of patatas bravas, anchovies on lightly toasted bread with a little oil and tomato, gambas al ajillo, flan, and other classic Spanish food that is all sized for sharing, so be sure to bring a friend—or make a new one.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13251;Taqueria Los Parados;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Av. Monterrey 333, Roma Sur, Cuauhtémoc, 06760, Mexico;19.406206;-99.1612084;67;false;true;Mexican;Don't expect a sit-down experience at this taqueria that has been open since 1965, as there are no chairs, but metal shelving subbing in for tables does the trick. Charcoal grilled meats are their specialty, and everything is cooked to order. Finished to a medium-well, the bistec enjoys a subtle smokiness from the grill, while the costilla is equally delicious in all of its razor-thin, well-done glory. Al pastor tacos are also a sure bet.;;[]
13252;Máximo;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Álvaro Obregón, 65 Bis, Roma Norte, Cuauhtémoc, 06700, Mexico;19.4188657;-99.1579904;57;true;true;International, Mexican;Once an auto repair shop, then a pool hall, the bones of its industrial past are ever-present at this chic restaurant in Roma Norte. Though Maximo has only been here for a handful of years, they're making a mark, both for the chef and his fascinating life story and for his internationally influenced Mexican cuisine, offered as a tasting menu and à la carte. Bread with roasted eggplant with a pleasant charcoal essence arrives after you take a seat, then slices of kampachi with avocado cream have just a hint of spice. French leanings are evident in the duck breast with crispy skin and jus with a touch of sherry, while the goat cheese ice cream with a drizzle of oil and a guava sauce with sprinkles of pumpkin and nuts is a very pleasant finale.;;[]
13253;Bajel;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Paseo De La Reforma, 297, Centro, Cuauhtémoc, 06500, Mexico;19.4286674;-99.1659082;32;false;true;Contemporary;Nestled on the ground floor of the Sofitel, Bajel boasts a prime location with stunning views. It's a French brand so they may whisper bonsoir, but one look at the menu and it's clear they're firmly planted here. Inside this sophisticated setting, the fully open kitchen demands your attention. Both a la carte and the tasting menu highlight contemporary Mexican-leaning cuisine with many nods to smoked meats and Spanish influences. Dishes like enchilada de pato confitado, tortilla de epazote and abodo de guajillo are as traditional (and enjoyable) as they come. Barbacoa is tender and plentiful, while dessert is a Basque-style tart with peach ice cream.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13257;Ostrería 109;Mexico;Cuauhtémoc;Avenida Nuevo León 109, Hipódromo, Cuauhtémoc, 06100, Mexico;19.4109192;-99.1728082;84;true;false;Seafood, Contemporary;Come sip a cocktail and listen to vinyl music at this trendy restaurant that is equal parts warm and cozy and industrial chic. Tables at the back of the room are the best, as they front an open window, while the table located just in front of the kitchen is exactly where many want to be. Take a seat and you'll be greeted by four jars of homemade sauces of different intensities and spiciness to accent this cuisine based on the sea. Begin with oysters and chocolate clams, as well as black shrimp aguachile or the winsome tosta de pulpo enamorado, before moving on to main dishes like shrimp with chintextle or arroz a la tumbada. For dessert, strawberries with cream and Pernod ice cream is the perfect finish.;;[]
13258;Vernáculo;Mexico;San Pedro Garza García;Av. Cto. Frida Kahlo 303, Valle Oriente, San Pedro Garza García, 66260, Mexico;25.6450656;-100.3213767;74;false;true;Mexican;Chef Hugo Guajardo showcases Noreste Mexican cuisine here, with local ingredients bolstering traditional recipes cooked over a live fire. Tortillas are made in-house, so take a seat and have some freshly made tostadas and salsa brought to your table as you peruse the seasonally minded menu. Tacos filled with adobo-marinated and fire-roasted pork belly are a sure thing, especially when accompanied by the spicy red salsa and a kicky piquin chile. Carne zaraza is a dry-brined skirt steak that is enlivened with charred onion atop fresh corn tortillas. The accompanying watercress and cilantro salad is as refreshing as the steak is juicy. End the meal with a pastry, like their tarta de nuez, that's served warm with a scoop of piñón ice cream on top.;Air conditioning;[]
13259;Bu’ul;Mexico;Playa del Carmen;Carretera Federal Cancún - Tulum, Punta Maroma Km. 51, Playa del Carmen, 77710, Mexico;20.7291459;-86.9683709;44;false;true;Mexican, Creative;A journey through the jungle, past the private villas that make up the Chablé Maroma, will bring you to this enclave, serving singular cuisine that celebrates native ingredients and flavors. To that effect, sophisticated permutations of corn, beans, and chiles are threaded through the menu, as in a salbute made from puffed fried masa, filled with chunks of spiny lobster and crunchy green apple, dressed with an earthy, complex recado rojo sauce. A main course of luxurious creamy rice—enriched with Ocosingo cheese and accented with nutty, herbaceous pipián verde alongside earthy venison longaniza—offers an unapologetically Mexican answer to risotto. Finish with a wonderfully intense molten cake of Oaxacan chocolate—ideally paired with a sip of mezcal.;Interesting wine list;[]
13260;Latitud 32;Mexico;El Porvenir;Carretera Guadalupe-El Tigre Parcela Km. 118, El Porvenir, 22755, Mexico;32.0616841;-116.647751;70;false;true;Mexican;Latitud 32 is located outside of Ensenada on the Valle de Guadalupe wine route. This dining room neighbors the El Cielo resort and is set within a working vineyard, commanding a prized view of the valley's landscape. The grounds are stunning, while the restaurant has a rustic elegance with a high ceiling, stone and brick-lined walls and floor-to-ceiling glass.The menu is a fusion of Baja and Yucatan specialties. Highlights include salbute de pato, comprised of fried masa tortillas topped with shredded greens and a generous amount of slow-cooked, shredded duck pibil. Slow-cooked lamb atop mashed potatoes liberally sauced with birria broth shines in borrego tatemado. House wines are poured to enhance the experience, and the menu offers recommendations for each course.;Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
13262;Madre;Mexico;Ensenada;C. Octava 444, Zona Centro, Ensenada, 22800, Mexico;31.8704277;-116.6237217;46;true;true;Mexican;Comfortable and amiable, Madre is from chefs and partners Miguel Bahena and Carolina Verdugo. Found in a white stucco home with a terra-cotta tiled roof, the dining area's layout features two small rooms and a bar area with the kitchen on display at the back. Decorative elements include polished wood plank floors, tables dressed in cloth runners and light walls accented with artwork.The concise menu offers seafood starters, such as the pepita and-sesame crusted shrimp plated with a chileatole sauce made from shrimp stock and slivers of nopal and onion. Pasta and roasted meats round out the menu, such as the duck breast presented with a crisped skin and sauced with a house-made mole coloradito.;;[]
13263;Tacos Mi Ranchito El Fenix;Mexico;Ensenada;C Sexta y Espinoza 603, Zona Centro, Ensenada, 22830, Mexico;31.8654307;-116.615657;19;false;false;Mexican;Tacos Mi Ranchito El Fenix is a streetside kiosk done up in white and red tile. This perch offers a handful of counter seats, as well as two tables off to the side. The counter surrounds the prep area where one corner is devoted to the frying of the fish fillets for the signature taco here, the taco pescado. This crispy, delicious treat is served unadorned and invites dressing up from the various garnishes.;;[]
13264;Ophelia;Mexico;El Sauzal de Rodríguez;Carr. Tijuana-Ensenada 103, El Sauzal de Rodríguez, 22760, Mexico;31.8870027;-116.6891618;70;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;El Sauzal de Rodríguez's restaurants are typically laser-focused on seafood, but Ophelia offers something a little different. This spot with light walls, wood ceiling, and dark tiled floor, features a Mediterranean-themed menu with items ranging from salads, pastas, and pizza to entrees like roasted octopus, fish in mole, roasted quail, and lamb shank. Lasana de Susana, named for the chef's mother, is presented in a cast iron skillet. Its layers of fresh pasta are loaded with a coarsely ground meat ragu studded with diced mushrooms, and a rich cheese for a deliciously comforting dish that is accompanied by a refreshing green salad with sliced cucumber and cherry tomatoes in a creamy cilantro dressing.;;[]
13265;Itanoní;Mexico;Oaxaca;Av. Belisario Domínguez 513, Col. Reforma, Oaxaca, 68050, Mexico;17.0753;-96.71464;15;true;true;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;There are few addresses better than this one that offer such an up-close view of tortilla-making excellence. Chef-owner Gabriela Fernandez Orantes has been celebrating heirloom varietals of corn since opening back in 2001. The menu is chock full of memelitas, tetelas, quesadillas and more, and everyone is welcome to stand close, right by the kitchen, and watch as chefs work with fresh masa that’s been nixtamalized and stone-ground in house. Pressed, shaped and slowly cooked on a hot comal, tortillas of all kinds arrive garnished and stuffed with melted cheese and paired with the likes of squash blossoms, pork lard and hot salsas. While you wait, sip on a cool glass of the corn and chocolate-infused tascalate.;;[]
13266;Teocintle-Tika'aya;Mexico;Oaxaca;Av. de la Independencia 12, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0597148;-96.7154558;17;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Just south of the Mercado de La Merced, this tiny little nook of a restaurant is a surprise in every way. With just a handful of tables and no menu in sight, the tasting pulls inspiration from Oaxaca’s Mixteca region. The young chef Toño García cooks with the maturity of someone much older, as he brings refined flair to indigenous preparations. His colorful, accomplished dishes wouldn’t be out of place in far ritzier settings, starting with the avocado croquette crowned with nopales. Mole amarillo with fish rolled in hoja santa as well as a vibrant beet salad pull flavors from Mexico and beyond. The signature dish is surely the taco, made with three colors of corn and paired with tender tongue, roasted pineapple and pickled red onions.;;[]
13267;Deckman's En El Mogor;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Carretera Tecate Km 85.5, Valle de Guadalupe, 22766, Mexico;32.0360195;-116.6029495;21;false;true;Mexican;It's a short drive off the main road to the Cavas del Mogor property, home of this flagship restaurant. As is common in this region, the dining space is outdoors, built on a platform with tables shaded by trees and a roof lit with cafe lights. In the middle, a live fire kitchen takes center stage. Drew Deckman's cooking is contemporary Mexican, as in a tempura fried soft shell crab on a bed of dressed arugula and sorrel leaves with avocado purée and a Pilsner foam. Main dishes, like the short rib or smoked chicken with potatoes and sauerkraut, lean hearty. Ingredients are top notch and there is a strong commitment to sustainability. Just up the hill is Baja Omakase, Deckman's ode to local sourced fish with Mexican sake.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13268;Manta;Mexico;Cabo San Lucas;Carretera Federal 1 Km. 5, Fracc. A, L-21, Cabo San Lucas, 23456, Mexico;22.8988802;-109.8698544;91;false;false;Mexican, Fusion;Set within the Cape Hotel in a stunning space that frames picture-perfect views of Cabo's famed Lands End, this modern dining room under Enrique Olvera's umbrella isn't just impressing with its good looks. The contemporary Mexican cuisine is punctuated by clear Peruvian and Japanese influences. Offered as a tasting menu and à la carte, expect bold dishes from a kitchen that's unafraid of bringing the heat. Begin with sashimi or a Peruvian ceviche before savoring a refreshing melon salad with diced honeydew and cantaloupe in a leche de tigre fueled by yuzu. Next, a sweet potato with a tamarind and soy crust in an almond mole is at once simple and elegant. From Korean fried chicken and tempura fish tacos to cochinita served in bao buns, Asian accents run from beginning to end on the à la carte menu.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
13269;Primitivo;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Carretera Tecate-Ensenada Km. 89, Valle de Guadalupe, 22760, Mexico;32.0122712;-116.6276842;38;true;false;Contemporary;Indeed, the name says it all at this rugged space that's down a dirt road, past a fence draped with wine bottles. and situated under a sprawling oak tree that is three centuries old. The kitchen is anchored by a large fire pit where ingredients are cooked in cast-iron dishes or directly on the flame. Chef Carolina Jimenéz brings a unique approach to this rustic menu rooted in local sourcing. There are oysters to start before guests pick a protein, then savor multiple courses sized for sharing and utilizing every part of the fish or animal. The cooking is earnest, focused, and clever. Dessert is a must, especially that fudgy, flourless chocolate cake with candied orange peel and a quenelle of smoked lavender ice cream.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13270;Arca;Mexico;Tulum;Boca Paila Km. 7.6, Tulum Beach, Tulum, 77780, Mexico;20.149471;-87.4594377;28;true;false;Contemporary, Mexican;Don't let its location along a very busy road in the touristy part of town fool you: Arca is every bit a can't-miss spot. This inviting open-air venue welcomes guests to three seatings each night. The menu changes frequently, as it's all based on what's freshest from their long list of farmers and trusted suppliers. Everything is cooked over the live fire, and dishes are complex in their mix of ingredients, with compelling presentation and flavor. Everything has been considered in this highly personalized, au courant cuisine. Some dishes, like the expertly seared octopus paired with a lively xcatic-based salsa, lentils, pickled radish and epazote, will linger long in your memory. Finally, mamey brûlée with caramel, pixtle ice cream and amaranth granola, is a worthy conclusion.;Terrace;[]
13271;Asador Bacanora Oaxaca;Mexico;Oaxaca;5 De Mayo 519, Oaxaca, 68080, Mexico;17.068347;-96.7167677;18;false;false;Mexican;As you approach this charming spot tucked away on a small but colorful side street, the smell of the grill is the first clue you’ve arrived. Chef José Manuel Baños presides over a large Mexican menu with a few European touches and a focus on steaks. Dialed-in executions and nuanced flavors are seen from start to finish in dishes like tostones rellenos, a savory-sweet plate of plantain dumplings in a deep, rich mole negro sauce. Steaks steal the spotlight, though main dishes still shine, as in the impossibly tender short ribs with a beer and piloncillo reduction glaze. End on a lighter note with the airy chocolate mousse with a layer of chocolate cookie crumble and fresh mint ice cream.;Terrace;[]
13272;María Dolores;Mexico;Isla Mujeres;Condominio Playa Mujeres, Interior resort ATELIER Playa Mujeres, Isla Mujeres, 77400, Mexico;21.2532723;-86.8121965;43;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Expect to be pampered like royalty from the second you step into this luxurious enclave within the sprawling Atelier Playa Mujeres hotel. Apart from hyper-attentive hospitality (including top-notch beverage service), the grand space features a balcony from which diners are serenaded with live music. The menu of contemporary Mexican cuisine, curated by celebrated chef Edgar Nuñez, is similarly ornate, featuring a multitude of à la carte offerings and specials, in addition to a signature tasting menu. The flavorful, original cooking draws upon the breadth of Mexico’s culinary landscape, reimagining familiar regional dishes with a refined modern style, whether it’s a tempura-fried shrimp taco in honor of Sonora, or a complex Oaxacan mole coloradito paired with roasted quail.;Interesting wine list;[]
13273;Lumbre;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Jose Maria Morelos 162, San José del Cabo, 23400, Mexico;23.0615425;-109.6960783;97;true;false;Mexican;Located just off the art walk in San Jose del Cabo, Lumbre is a contemporary, stylish space from César Pita. It's a Mexican and live fire concept with global influences where creativity and originality reign supreme. Case in point? The grilled bread that kicks off the meal that's served with a bone marrow butter, served in the bone with hibiscus salt. And that's just the beginning. Compressed watermelon is a riot of colors and flavor, then a classic chile relleno is revamped with a Pasilla chile, stuffed with a "scallop chorizo" with gooey cheese, and fried until crispy. Pork belly in a Recaudo Negro sauce sided by carrot puree and a croquette of plantain puree is highly original. The friendly, welcoming staff caps off the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13274;Posada Margherita;Mexico;Tulum;Tulum Boca Paila Km 4.5, Tulum Beach, Tulum, 77760, Mexico;20.1649581;-87.4524655;34;true;true;Italian;When it comes to beachside dining in Tulum, Italian may not be the first thing that springs to mind, but this shabby chic local favorite is popular for good reason. The compact menu, which draws upon the cuisine of Genoa, features a small selection of handmade pastas, fresh seafood, and pizzas, all dutifully prepared with quality ingredients (both local and imported) and a faithful sense of rustic simplicity that will be pleasing to purists. Although certainly not a traditional pairing, an enticing variety of fresh-pressed juices and unique cocktails fits the setting to a T (and might be just the thing after a night of carousing). End your meal with the house-spun gelato, which, in keeping with the rest of the food, is straightforwardly delicious.;;[]
13275;Omakai;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Ignacio Zaragoza 1311, San José del Cabo, 23400, Mexico;23.0618444;-109.6975999;64;true;false;Japanese;Located near the heart of San Jose del Cabo, Omakai sports a serene Mexican minimalist design while putting Japanese cuisine front and center. There are three menus to choose from, but whether you choose the teppanyaki tasting menu, the omakase, or select from the a la carte offerings, you can't go wrong. Those who opt for the omakase will find good quality, with many of the fish sourced from the local waters of La Paz and Ensenada. House-made pork belly gyoza are executed flawlessly, while the nigiri leans traditional at first, becoming more complex as the meal progresses. Seared salmon topped with a truffle sauce is decadently delicious. The meal concludes with a charming vanilla ice cream on squares of coffee jelly.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13276;Nao;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Miguel Hidalgo 100 y Manuel Doblado, Centro, San José del Cabo, 23400, Mexico;23.0014381;-109.7341207;95;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;One look at Nao, with whitewashed brick and pops of blue, and you won't be surprised that it's Mediterranean-minded. What will come as a welcome surprise, however, is the high level of service and the exemplary dishes. Local chef Alex Branch has created a winning menu, and from the bread and pasta to the gelato, everything is made in house. Don't skip the starters, especially the roasted beets with pomegranate molasses. From there, tuck into house-made tortellini with flavors of cacio e pepe with shrimp, small tobiko, and pea tendrils. Main dishes, like lechón, are sized for sharing, which leaves plenty of room for yogurt gelato with crumbled baklava and macerated strawberries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13277;Tacos Marco Antonio;Mexico;Ensenada;Av. Rayón 351, Obrera, Ensenada, 22830, Mexico;31.86049;-116.6108631;88;true;true;Mexican;Partially open-air with concrete flooring and a metal roof, the industrial bones of this taqueria harken back to this setting's roots as a fish canning warehouse started by Marco Antonio's father in 1965. Order at the rear station, then pull up a metal chair at one of the simple tables. The extensive menu of seafood tacos includes chicharrón de pescado, carnitas de atún and camarón al chipotle. Taco pescado empanizado offers a tender, warm and golden tortilla topped with a breaded fish fillet that is dressed with onions and a squirt of spiced crema. Shredded cabbage and a host of salsas are arranged on a table for your embellishment.;;[]
13278;El Paisa;Mexico;Ensenada;Av. 20 De Noviembre 1043, Ensenada, 22800, Mexico;31.8753534;-116.627964;36;true;true;Mexican;Serving tacos and tortas, and focused on adobada or asada, El Paisa is a tasty taco recommendation. The crew is always busy grilling beef and green onions, and roasting spice-rubbed pork in a vertical rotisserie at this tidy spot with a few tables. It's all supremely fresh, as everything is hot off the grill here. You can even watch as staff members slice the roasting meat right into your tortilla. Dress with your choice of salsas, then add chopped onion, cilantro and other flourishes to taste.;;[]
13279;Woodend;Mexico;Playa del Carmen;Carr. Cancún - Tulum Km. 51, Playa del Carmen, 77720, Mexico;20.741699;-86.9653711;64;true;true;Contemporary;Acclaimed Chef Curtis Stone lends his name and refined culinary sensibilities to this seaside retreat, and though he’s unlikely to be present in the flesh, rest assured that you are in good hands regardless. As the first step into the smoke-perfumed room will give away, the cooking here centers around live fire, with a charcoal oven and wood-fired grill lending their aroma to a small menu that leans to bold simplicity. Local seafood and well-marbled steaks from Oklahoma make up the mains, while sides like crunchy potato pavé with jocoque and buttery Parisian gnocchi with endive and poblano are tasty enough to stand on their own. For dessert, a twist on tarte tatin with pineapple, mezcal-tinged caramel, and toasted vanilla ice cream hits just the right mark.;Interesting wine list;[]
13280;Atarraya;Mexico;Brisas de Zicatela;Guerrero 633 Brisas de Zicatela, La Punta, Brisas de Zicatela, 70934, Mexico;15.8357857;-97.0422176;74;false;true;Mexican;Is there a cooler restaurant in Puerto Escondido? Channeling the sleekness of a Japanese zen garden, the outdoor space is picture-perfect and built out with handsome wood beams, a backlit bar, and an old tree that stretches across the dining room. The cooking is familiar fare, seasoned and presented with the right amount of care: Crisp tostadas stacked with pan-fried ribeye, squares of tuna rolled in sesame seeds, and vibrant salsas that upgrade everything they touch. You could make a meal out of the appetizers alone or press on with a chile relleno stuffed with vegetables and blanketed in a smooth manzano pepper sauce. Though the cocktail offerings are succinct and stick largely to the classics, the bartenders shake and stir with notable skill.;Terrace;[]
13281;Oryx;Mexico;Tijuana;Blvd. Agua Caliente 10750, Int 84, Tijuana, 22015, Mexico;32.5136859;-117.0082533;95;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;This Tijuana favorite is the domain of Chef Ruffo Ibarra. The dining room boasts a dressed-up industrial look with dark earthy colors, exposed red brick walls, wood and tiled flooring, metal beams and warm lighting.The menu is a contemporary take on Mexican cuisine and lists an extensive selection of items including chilled seafood starters and grilled steaks. Consomé de camarón con hongas is presented with chopped raw shrimp, then filled tableside with a hot, deeply flavorful shrimp broth which gently poaches the shrimp. Golden-brown, crisped striped bass shares the plate with creamy onion puree, bits of fried kale and some salsa verde. The stack of churros, served warm and accompanied by bourbon ice cream, make for a fine ending.;;[]
13282;Mision 19;Mexico;Tijuana;Mision de San Javier 10643, Zona Urbana Rio, Tijuana, 22010, Mexico;32.5212331;-117.0078243;42;false;false;Mexican;The name is a reference to the 18 Catholic missions that exist in Baja California. Their mission is a bit more down-to-earth: To celebrate the area's food. Located on the second floor of Vía Corporativo, Mexico's second self-sustainable building, the restaurant strives for sustainability by utilizing products that do not travel more than 200km from farm to table. Noteworthy dishes include aguachile, featuring slivers of local rockot dressed with salsa verde and avocado puree. Lechon prensado is an enticing roasted pork plated with a zesty roasted tomatillo salsa as well as reduced pork jus. It is a feast in itself, perhaps best accompanied by a rich tinta from one of the Valle de Guadalupe labels on offer.;;[]
13283;Zandunga;Mexico;Oaxaca;Manuel García Vigil 512 E., Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.06635;-96.7246;95;false;true;Mexican, Regional Cuisine;Sunlight beams down through an open roof and into this colorful, spacious courtyard set with handsome wooden tables. Pottery, textiles and paintings by local artists adorn every wall in sight. Truly, this restaurant captures the vibrant spirit of downtown Oaxaca. It’s a lovely scene to take in while exploring a curated menu focused on traditional regional flavors. Start with the garnachas, the masa carefully fried and topped with tender, shredded beef and pickled cabbage, before moving on to the crispy plantains stuffed with queso and crema that are both tropical and savory. Tamales come prepared with mole negro, sweet corn or raisins. A generous platter featuring many of these standout dishes offers diners an efficient way to sample everything.;;[]
13284;El Fogón;Mexico;Playa del Carmen;Av. Constituyentes, Playa del Carmen, 77720, Mexico;20.6328577;-87.07393;68;true;true;Mexican;It's not just about classic tortillas stuffed with various types of meat here. Instead, this taqueria also offers more complex dishes that are always worth considering. The fogoncito bistec is a house specialty heaped with beef, bacon, chorizo and melted cheese.Frequented by both locals and tourists alike, this place is typically crowded but the service is prompt, so you won't be waiting too long. Paddle fans up above keep things cool while you work up an appetite.;;[]
13285;Casa Oaxaca El Restaurante;Mexico;Oaxaca;Constitución 104, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0652641;-96.722276;72;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;In the shadow of the Templo de Santo Domingo de Guzmán, Chef Alejandro Ruiz’s two-story restaurant buzzes with all the energy of a new opening. And yet, the stoves have been firing for more than two decades and have drawn attention from all corners of the world. Stylishly dressed, guests opt for the spacious rooftop patio where attentive servers are quick to make salsa tableside. The menu spins local ingredients and Oaxacan flavors with international touches, and nothing comes out of the kitchen looking anything less than beautiful. Desserts, like the platano Colorado with banana cream and mezcal caramel, show delicious refinement. All the while, as the sun sets and the church bell rings, the party goes on to the sound of cocktail shakers.;Terrace;[]
13286;Criollo;Mexico;Oaxaca;Av. Francisco I. Madero 129, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0642526;-96.7338307;92;false;true;Mexican, Traditional Cuisine;Chefs Enrique Olvera and Luis Arellano are the culinary forces behind this magical oasis that is also part of a guest house listed as a UNESCO heritage. Entirely outdoors, the dining room is a straight-edged work of smooth concrete and a canopy of trees and Edison bulbs stretched over handsome wood tables set with flickering candles. Chirping birds and burning incense add to the romance. Serving only a tasting menu, the kitchen leans on traditional Oaxacan recipes and local ingredients. A warm cheese croquette starts the meal with total fireworks, followed by a smooth tamal set in a bold shrimp-infused mole coloradito and, later, excellent tempura fish tacos. Desserts are refreshing, as in the pineapple nicuatole with passionfruit and mango sorbet.;Terrace;[]
13287;Taqueria La Principal;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Principal, Valle de Guadalupe, Valle de Guadalupe, 22750, Mexico;32.0974031;-116.5690283;32;true;false;Mexican;Situated in a warehouse space with plastic furniture, this quintessential no-frills roadside taqueria doesn’t get a lot of points for ambience, but happily the simple, satisfying fare speaks for itself. The compact menu doesn’t call for extensive decision-making: diners choose between three meats (thinly sliced beef asada, spice-marinated pork adobada, and, for the more adventurous, tender tripa), and their vehicle of choice (corn or flour tortilla, burrito, torta, etc.) and then watch the magic come together before their eyes. Lively, well-balanced salsas and perfectly fresh toppings combine with flavorful grill-kissed meats for love at first bite, and the late nighttime hours of operation might be a lifesaver after a busy day of wine tasting.;;[]
13288;Kous Kous;Mexico;Valle de Guadalupe;Carretera Tecate Ensenada, Km 73.30, Valle de Guadalupe, 22758, Mexico;32.1214336;-116.5402002;20;false;false;Moroccan;This stunning restaurant with dramatic views may seem like other outdoor spots in the area but keep down the path and a lively space draped with curtains and Moroccan lamps soon appears, revealing the singular experience. Come for an unexpected yet memorable meal spotlighting Moroccan cuisine. There is plenty of heart and loads of flavor in this family-style selection where guests take their pick of protein for the tagine. Kick the meal off with flatbread, made in-house, along with a refreshing cucumber salad. From the chicken with olives to the honey lamb, the tagine offerings are exceptional, but their namesake couscous, with caramelized onions, garbanzo beans and golden raisins, almost steals the show.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13289;Crudo;Mexico;Oaxaca;Av. Benito Juárez 309, Oaxaca, 68000, Mexico;17.0638256;-96.7211778;26;true;true;Fusion, Mexican;There is nothing quite like this intimate counter, certainly in Oaxaca and possibly beyond. Chef Ricardo Arellano has crafted a creative omakase that fuses Japanese flavors with local ingredients and preparations. What does that look like? It means nixtamalized papaya might come with your kampachi. Or maybe tuna will arrive seared with binchotan and set in a chicory leaf brushed in charred onion puree. An eel handroll is dressed in a smoky-sweet puree made from the pulp of agave. The menu is on the lighter side but the lasting impression and ingenuity is nonetheless impressive and at no point feels forced or generic. Locals have yet to warm to the place, so visitors shouldn’t be surprised when they’re seated with fellow travelers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13290;DŪM;Mexico;Todos Santos;Calle Centenario S/N, Colonia Centro, Todos Santos, 23300, Mexico;23.4543156;-110.2220432;40;true;true;Mexican;Look for the carved wood sign, then walk along the path through what looks a bit like a jungle to this oasis-like space. Husband and wife, Chef Aurelien Legeay and Paulina Noble, are at the helm of this kitchen where the menu changes every new moon and offers both à la carte and tasting menu options cleverly dubbed "new moon" and "full moon." The cooking is playful and delights in the unexpected, as in oxtail with a red wine reduction and a smoked carrot purée with roasted baby carrots and long carrot chips. Steamed potato ravioli covered in a creamy potato Dauphinoise-inspired sauce with crispy matchsticks, diced smoked mackerel and a sweet candy tuile is a perfect example of their out-of-the-box style that comes with plenty of heart.;Terrace;[]
13291;Acre;Mexico;San José del Cabo;Calle Rincón de las Animas S/N, San José del Cabo, 23407, Mexico;23.0790926;-109.6811316;44;false;false;Mexican;Up a dusty road is this jungle resort where you'll discover an animal sanctuary, villas and treehouses, and this chic, open-air restaurant where fans swirl overhead and misters keep the abundant greenery at its peak. The casual, contemporary Mexican cooking is punched up with Asian influences, and the simple-but-stylish dishes are as gorgeous as the delightful setting. Guacamole is a perfect opener, with a bowl that's pitch-perfect in flavor but equally impressive with its looks (think flower petals as a flourish). Ceviche in a fresh, sweet mango sauce with leche de tigre is a riot of color before moving on to main dishes like grilled octopus, al Pastor suckling pig, and even ramen on certain days. To finish, their riff on key lime pie is just right.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13292;Manzanilla;Mexico;Ensenada;Teniente Azueta 139 Recinto Portuario, Zona Centro, Ensenada, 22800, Mexico;31.8596705;-116.6324544;93;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Manzanilla offers a truly worthwhile dining experience brought to you by chefs and partners Benito Molina and Solange Muris. A local favorite, the establishment feels like a world unto itself, located within a gated area and unwinding into a prettily arranged courtyard area and spaciously arranged dining rooms anchored by an ornate, carved wood bar. Speaking of drinks, an extensive selection of classic cocktails is on offer, as well as wines from the Valle de Guadalupe.The dishes lean simple but remain elevated and refined, showcasing a mastery of flavor and impeccable quality with dishes like their arroz de mar with guajillo chili and a myriad of seafood. The meal is not complete without their daily rotating crème brûlée, perhaps adorned with fig leaves from their garden.;;[]
13293;Oystera;Mexico;Todos Santos;Calle Benito Juárez, Todos Santos, 23300, Mexico;23.4475064;-110.2270928;33;true;true;Seafood, Mexican;Oystera is located in the heart of Todos Santos, in a massive and rather grand building that is built on the former site of a sugar mill. The oyster bar takes center stage, with the dining space surrounding the bar. A patio out back takes advantage of the view. Chef Poncho Cadena, a Sonoran native, oversees a seafood-focused, Mexican menu spotlighting contemporary, even ambitious, cooking. As might be expected, oysters are a must. Try the half-dozen selection, with all six sourced from Baja waters and served with their version of cocktail sauce, a mignonette and Baja-style ponzu sauce. If raw isn't to your liking, try the plump, fried oysters with habanero aïoli. Beyond the bi-valves, a marinated tuna tostada or the catch of the day would round out your meal nicely.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
13294;Wild;Mexico;Tulum;Boca Paila Carretera Tulum Km. 10, Boca Paila, Tulum, 77780, Mexico;20.1351475;-87.4642546;32;true;false;Contemporary, Mexican;In a world where uniformity is seemingly around every corner, Wild stands out from the pack. Nestled within the jungle of Tulum, this setting blends striking modern and rustic elements with lush nature. American Chef Norman Fenton is the brains behind the contemporary dishes, offered à la carte or as tasting menus. Begin with an appetizing vegetarian dish such as the crispy avocado with sikil pak, pico de gallo and oxalis before moving on to main dishes where quality ingredients shine. Excellent fish is seen in seafood plates like Campeche prawns or sea bass wrapped in hoja santa leaf. For dessert, a coconut granita with passionfruit, almond coco-crunch, lime and fresh mango is as refreshing as the open-air setting.;;[]
13295;Olivea Farm to Table;Mexico;Ensenada;Carretera Federal 3, KM 92.5 San Antonio de las Minas, Ruta de Vino, Ensenada, 22766, Mexico;31.9914653;-116.6419181;99;false;true;Contemporary;Located inside a boutique hotel fittingly dotted with olive trees, this charming newcomer is a promising addition to the local restaurant scene. The frequently changing seasonal menu displays a confident simplicity and purity of flavor, wearing its farm-to-table bona fides on its sleeve thanks to pristine produce that arrives daily from nearby acreage. Guests select between multicourse vegetarian or seafood-forward menus, with a handful of à la carte offerings, and will find equal satisfaction in main dishes like their daily catch fish with a celeriac puree or grilled octopus atop mole blanco. Desserts, like caramelized plums with a purple basil sorbet or a squash-filled eclair with kohlrabi ice cream, are particularly intriguing.;Interesting wine list;[]
13296;Casa Banana;Mexico;Tulum;Tulum-Boca Paila Km. 7.5, Tulum Beach, Tulum, 77780, Mexico;20.1507211;-87.4589474;43;true;false;Argentinian;Long a favorite of the Zona Hotelera dining scene, this boisterous spot offers more than just a hip, lively atmosphere—the crowds flock here to indulge in a menu of rustic, satisfying Argentine cooking. Centered around a traditional wood-fired oven and parrillada, the menu presents a bevy of options to suit diverse tastes. Signature appetizers like juicy empanadas or roasted artichokes with smoked labne and fried capers are a cut above. For mains, carnivores will find satisfaction with the requisite hearty steaks, which share space with fresh seafood and vegetarian options, as in whole roasted fish, or vegetarian offerings like a gratin of spinach gnocchi. Finish with a sweetly satisfying warm dulce de leche-filled crepe, paired with banana ice cream.;;[]
13297;NÜ Tulum;Mexico;Tulum;Tulum-Boca Paila Km. 8.7, Tulum Beach, Tulum, 77780, Mexico;20.1405807;-87.4617385;81;true;false;Mexican, Contemporary;Although the outdoor jungle-chic setting here fits right in with the numerous restaurants of this heavily trafficked strip, the cooking offers plenty of personality to set it apart from the pack. Chef Luis Aguilar has composed a menu that utilizes a plethora of local ingredients (many from Mestiza de Indias, a regenerative farm in the Yucatan Peninsula), blending tradition with novelty for memorable results. Vegetables play a key role, whether in meat-free dishes like an “agrodolce” of sweet potato and squash enriched with peanuts or in more substantial items like xcatic chiles filled with boudin blanc. A delicious finale of barbecued pineapple and almond cake boasts an elegant simplicity.;;[]
13298;TENOCH by Paradero Todos Santos;Mexico;Todos Santos;La Mesa KM 59 +3100, Degollado, Todos Santos, 23300, Mexico;23.3899243;-110.1961656;18;true;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Travel down a long dirt road past fields of peppers to find Tenoch. Located within Paradero Todos Santos, the restaurant's open-air setting is breezy and laidback and belies the serious food coming from this kitchen. The contemporary Mexican menu focuses on locally sourced seafood and produce from their own farm, and dishes feel timely. The soft-shell crab taco is as deceiving as it is delicious, appearing simple but coming alive on the palate. Slow-roasted beef tongue is loaded with flavor and incredibly tender while the manchamantel mole offers the perfect blend of spicy, sweet and fruity. For dessert, order the chocolate taco with black garlic panna cotta, or the dessert take on French Toast that is both decadent and dramatic.;Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13299;Bruma Wine Garden;Mexico;Ensenada;Bruma Winery, Valle de Guadalupe, Ensenada, 22760, Mexico;32.128037;-116.5310902;51;true;false;Contemporary;Run by Chef David Castro Hussong, this spot is located on the Bruma winery property. Entirely outside, the lovely tree-covered space welcomes guests to take a seat at the oversized communal table or a few smaller tables flanking the sides. A contemporary menu echoes the casual setting. Starters like ceviche or cauliflower with mole are followed up by hearty main dishes like short rib with shiitake and noodles. The pizzas are a popular choice, and though far from traditional Italian, the Mexican spin (think tender beef birria with chile morita) are very successful. Don't sleep on dessert, especially the flaky banana tart that delivers on flavor and, like many other dishes, is sized for sharing.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13300;Malva;Mexico;Villa de Juárez;3 Km. 96, Villa de Juárez, 22755, Mexico;31.9650245;-116.6560426;69;false;false;Mexican, Contemporary;From its idyllic location on the Mina Penélope vineyard to its talented chef, Roberto Alcocer, who is also the chef/owner of San Diego's Valle, Malva is a hard one to beat. This open-air restaurant's setting is certainly a scene stealer, but the season-driven, Mexican cooking commands equal attention. Two menus of four or eight courses are on offer, and the kitchen delivers elegant, original dishes. Served in a shell, paper-thin slices of scallop layered with thinly sliced cucumber on top of a classic aguachile simply shines. As Malva is the Latin name name for the mallow plant, the namesake mallow coulant is a must, and the green-tinted, molten cake accompanied by goat cheese ice cream certainly doesn't disappoint with its subtle vegetal and floral notes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13302;Envero en el Valle;Mexico;El Porvenir;Callejon Emiliano Zapata, Carretera Tecate, El Porvenir, 22750, Mexico;32.0812399;-116.6525401;74;true;false;Mexican;Add this gorgeous outdoor restaurant to your must-visit list. Located at the Las Nubes winery, you'll enjoy dramatic, sweeping views of The Valley from your table, while overhead, sun shades and café lights add to the ambience.The kitchen team makes good use of local produce and seafood while also favoring grilled meats for this contemporary Mexican cuisine, available both à la carte and as a tasting menu. Polenta finished on the plancha has a nice, crispy exterior before being topped with shredded braised beef and stewed cherry tomatoes. Local crab shines in a house-made taco served with a bright orange salsa, then thick slices of grilled New York strip steak with an excellent char is served with peanut Jalisco-style mole, a nod to the chef's heritage.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13304;Autor;Mexico;Tulum;Carretera Cancun Tulum 307, Tulkal Chemuyil, Tulum, 77775, Mexico;20.3587118;-87.3372659;52;false;false;Contemporary, Mexican;Autor is quickly writing itself into Riviera Maya's history from its relaxed perch at the luxurious Conrad Tulum Riviera Maya. Chef Jersaí Miranda Sánchez is at the helm, delivering two tasting menus focused on contemporary Mexican cuisine. One is entirely vegetarian, while the other draws on ancient local traditions while simultaneously modernizing and elevating the dishes. Tuna is impeccably presented on a lovely plate with raised edges, and the exquisite pieces, paired with avocado and caviar, as well as fermented daikon, make for an excellent beginning to the meal. Pork belly al pastor is popular in this part of Mexico, but here it's a notch above.The wine list features bottles from Mexico and the United States, as well as Champagnes and European varieties.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13305;Fonda San Francisco;Mexico;Monterrey;Manuel González 115, Casco Urbano, Monterrey, 66230, Mexico;25.6611909;-100.4009463;45;true;false;Mexican;As the name indicates, this is a humble establishment, with an under-the-radar vibe that’s a bit at odds with Chef/owner Adrián Herrera’s outsized personal brand. But though it certainly isn’t the sort of place to expect fancy trappings or hoity-toity service, it’s just right for satisfying a hunger for hearty food and good drinks in a relaxed, friendly atmosphere. Accordingly, the cooking is rustic, celebrating the kind of homey dishes whose charms are irresistible even without elegant plating, from earthy, nutty encacahuatadas to empalmes filled with a supremely tender, juicy stewed goat.;;[]
13306;Hartwood;Mexico;Tulum;Carr. Tulum-Boca Paila 7-6 km, Tulum Beach, Tulum, 77780, Mexico;20.1499647;-87.4594405;29;false;false;Mexican;Hartwood has plenty of allure. This Tulum hot spot was launched in 2010 by New Yorkers and husband and wife, Eric Werner and Mya Henry. Since then, the place has earned a loyal following, and it's packed nightly with eager diners who come here as much for the ambience as the food. In high season, you'll need to book well in advance, though solo diners can almost always find a perch at the bar. It's the essence of beach dining here in this jungle-like setting where the menu is everchanging. Consult the blackboard for the day's offerings, all based on what's freshest at the market, though ceviche and grilled local fish are likely candidates.;;[]
13307;Comal;Mexico;Cabo San Lucas;Carretera Transpeninsular Km. 15, Cabo San Lucas, 23410, Mexico;22.9477912;-109.8077004;32;false;true;Mexican, Contemporary;Walk through the lobby of the posh Chileno Bay Resort, down a small hill and along a dramatic walkway with swings and lounge furniture to arrive at this open-air restaurant with beautiful views of the water. The contemporary Mexican menu is inventive with a clear personality that spans the country's distinct regions while also pulling in influences from South America. Octopus kastakan is a ceviche-style dish made with thin coins of octopus tossed with crispy cubes of pork belly and crispy pork skin. Served with warm plantain tortillas with slightly sweet notes, it's a brightly flavored dish. Their variation on a Pavlova with strawberry-basil sorbet employs a variety of pastry techniques and is noteworthy.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13308;Kiosco Verde;Mexico;Cancún;Av. López Portillo SM. 84 Lote 14, Cancún, 77520, Mexico;21.1868293;-86.8078601;81;false;false;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;Octavio Santiago continues a longstanding family tradition at Kiosco Verde. This simple but welcoming kiosk was founded by his father in 1974 and is located along the road that crosses Puerto Juarez. The detailed menu is complemented by specials written on the blackboard, but all focus on seafood from the local market and highlight the regional style. The dishes are as tasty as they are colorful, as in the Argentine-style empanadas stuffed with lobster meat and chimichurri sided by baked potatoes, fried leek julienne and aguacate, along with chile hummus. Pulpo zarandeado is another winning dish, and with generous portions you'll be hard-pressed to order dessert—but don't skip it. The specials, like the dreamy panna cotta, are worth it.;Car park;[]
13309;La Casa De Las Mayoras;Mexico;Cancún;Calle Guadalupe Victoria y Calle Miguel Hidalgo Donceles 28, Cancún, 77524, Mexico;21.1768163;-86.8182436;47;false;true;Mexican, Vegetarian;Finding a dedicated vegetarian restaurant in a city that aims to please all manner of tastes can be expected, but it’s still a pleasant surprise to find one with this much homey charm and hospitality, not to mention such flavorful, satisfying cooking, regardless of your dietary predilections. Breakfast is the order of business here, with a menu featuring an assortment of chilaquiles, quesadillas and tostadas, boasting hand-made tortillas and astutely seasoned salsas. Tame the spice with “superfood” batidos blended with the likes of organic honey, tropical fruits and chia seeds. To add to the ambience, lucky visitors may have the pleasure of encountering Guato, a local celebrity in the guise of a chihuahua-beagle mix, who sometimes holds court here.;;[]
13310;Tacos El Franc;Mexico;Tijuana;Blvd. Gral Rodolfo Sánchez Taboada 9257, Zona Este, Tijuana, 22010, Mexico;32.5288952;-117.0276643;36;true;true;Mexican;This taqueria boasts a bustling corner setting with a covered roof and bright blue open walls. There is plenty of seating at anchored white tables as well as at the counter. Grab a table, then place your order from one of the pleasant apron-clad ladies circulating throughout the room. There are different stations cooking specific items, and the sounds of sizzling and chopping rise above the cacophony. The menu is wide-ranging, with tacos, tostadas and vampiros, all with a meat focus.;;[]
13311;Los Tres Gallos;Mexico;Cabo San Lucas;Leona Vicaria Esquina 20 de Noviembre, Cabo San Lucas, 23469, Mexico;22.8895263;-109.9117195;44;true;true;Mexican;This popular operation commands a corner of downtown Cabo San Lucas. The sprawling space is centered around a grand courtyard, and the setting, with its brick structure, paver stone patio, and wood furnishings, is brightened by pink and red painted stucco. A roof terrace is open during the evening.Los Tres Gallos serves a crowd-pleasing menu of generously portioned traditional Mexican cuisine like chile rellenos, enchiladas, and mole con pollo. The pozole is a vivid broth enriched with roasted chiles and tomatoes. Stocked with plump kernels of toothsome hominy alongside chunks of braised pork, it is served with a host of embellishments. The flan de casa is as big as a house, so plan on sharing dessert.;Terrace;[]
13312;Corazón D'Petra;Mexico;El Porvenir;Rancho San Marcos, El Porvenir, 22755, Mexico;32.0084379;-116.679907;44;true;true;Mexican;Casa Frida is part of a sprawling complex in the Valle de Guadalupe with several outlets on offer, including a tasting room for wine and agave spirits, and a patio bar overlooking the vineyards. The dining room at this formal restaurant is spacious with an airy feeling, attractively arranged with an encaustic tiled floor in shades of grey, rows of tables and a grey stone bar fronting a colorful tile wall with insets for bottles.The menu is an extensive offering of Chef Carlos Esquivel's cuisine. There are cold and hot starters, like an aguachile negro or tuna tostada. Entrees present the elegant tlacoyo filled with black beans and topped with diced octopus and pico de gallo. For groups, there are platters of grilled meats.;;[]
13313;Arbol;Mexico;Cabo San Lucas;Transpeninsular Km. 19.5, Cabo San Lucas, 23400, Mexico;22.9788092;-109.7694061;41;false;true;Indian, Asian;Located within Rosewood's Las Ventanas al Paraiso, this beguiling setting hosts diners in an indoor/outdoor space arranged with chunky blond wood tables on a polished stone patio. Lantern-hung branches cast a rosy glow.The large menu is impressively prepared and is founded on Indian specialties. However, the range of offerings is further enhanced by charcoal-grilled meats and seafood, as well as an abundance of Asian specialties. The Punjabi fish masala features the catch of the day, which is gently cooked in a zesty, moderately spiced tomato-based sauce enriched with ground cashews and flecked with herbs and spices. It comes served with spice-tinted basmati pilaf and Indian-style pickled vegetables and is best paired with butter-brushed naan hot off the tandoor.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13314;Shikinosushi KROUTO;Japan;Nara;6-9-2 Omiyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8115, Japan;34.684907;135.810919;31;true;true;Sushi;Yutaka Shimonaka uses over 200 different kinds of seafood throughout the year and expresses the season in his sushi. He visits fishing ports in each area and orders seasonal fish. The wide variety of snacks includes sashimi, tempura and assorted shuko. Sushi toppings are prepared in such ways as maturing or pickling them. The rice is made with akazu and rice vinegar, combining the traditions of Edomae and Kansai.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13315;La Cachette;Japan;Nara;5-3-5 Nishitomigaoka, Nara, Nara, 631-0006, Japan;34.713275;135.738516;76;false;true;French;During the 1980s, when classics were making a comeback, the owner-chefhoned his skills by going from restaurant to restaurant in Paris. Based on that experience, he seasons the dishes with salt and provides them with balance using tartness and fattiness. He emphasises uniqueness and this includes making soup with uncured ham and melon and using duck in potato dishes. He also uses sour pickled ume in putting both his French and Japanese sensibilities to work.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13316;ocu;Japan;Nara;38-6 Takamacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8241, Japan;34.683895;135.825976;22;true;false;Italian;An Italian restaurant famed for its wood-fired cuisine. The chef’s experiences in Tuscany made him fall in love with cooking over firewood. Grilled vegetable dishes, such as shiitake mushrooms with anchovy butter and broccoli with karasumi (salted and dried grey mullet roe), are served one at a time, fresh from the kitchen. At lunchtime, prix fixe courses focus on pizzas, made using home-cultured yeast and noted for their high rims. Evening offerings include duck, beef and pasta.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
13317;LA PIE;Japan;Nara;15-3 Kasasagicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8391, Japan;34.677247;135.83207;24;true;false;French;Longing to recreate the bustling mood of a Paris bistro, the chef made his dream come true in his native Nara with a restaurant that seems to blend in with the daily life of France. Seafood bouillabaisse, inspired by memories of student days in Montpellier, brings the flavours of the Mediterranean to his hometown. ‘La Pie’ is French for ‘magpie’, a bird said to be a bringer of happiness. The name is also a shout-out to the restaurant’s location, Kasasagi-cho, whose name means ‘Magpie Town’. Happiness brought by delicious cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13319;AWA Naramachiten;Japan;Nara;1 Shonamicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8363, Japan;34.678613;135.830542;80;true;true;Japanese;Enjoy the locally cultivated bounty of historic Nara, in an area with many elegant townhouses. As at the head restaurant, Kiyosumi no Sato Awa, the key ingredients on the menu are traditional homegrown vegetables. The offerings include a basket of assorted colourful appetisers, tempura of Yamato vegetables, and nimono thickened with Yoshino kudzu. The culinary delights of Nara are also highlighted, such as Yamato beef with local sake.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
13320;nakamuraya;Japan;Nara;8-1 Minamiichicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8373, Japan;34.679927;135.830065;20;true;false;Italian;In Italy, chef Nakamura learned the importance of traditional food appropriate to the land and climate. He reflects the season with vegetables that come from the Soni Plateau, and in autumn and winter, he procures wild game such as deer and boar from Tsuge. With the set menu, he serves both handmade and dried noodles so you can enjoy the variety. The Genovese made with fresh basil in the summer is a dish that showcases his experience of training in Genoa.;Air conditioning;[]
13321;Bon appétit Meshiagare;Japan;Nara;1 Juriincho, Nara, Nara, 630-8312, Japan;34.676015;135.833308;64;false;true;French;The chef honed his skills in Paris and other parts of France and uses Nara ingredients to prepare local dishes using traditional techniques he learned there. Seasonal vegetables and fruits come from Gojo City and Soni Village, and he also uses wild game caught in Tsuge. The main appetisers are homemade-style charcuterie, and the main meat dishes are roast and stew. He also incorporates ingredients like ayu and tilefish, sometimes giving the dishes a Japanese touch.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
13322;La Terrasse;Japan;Nara;98-1 Kasuganocho, Nara, Nara, 630-8212, Japan;34.684605;135.84574;25;true;true;French;This restaurant is at the base of Mt. Wakakusa, with scenery that could include cherry blossoms, green leaves and autumn colours. The set menu features Nara ingredients on the theme of ‘a feel of nature on each plate’. Yamato vegetables, as well as vegetables pickled in sake lees are also used. The chef goes easy on oils and fats and seasons food lightly, creating harmony with the fragrance of herbs and citrus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
13323;Soba Saishoku Ichinyoan;Japan;Nara;1362 Haibara Jimyo, Uda, Nara, 633-0217, Japan;34.519943;135.982177;68;false;false;Soba;This old house built at the end of the Edo period is Issei Oketani’s family home. The antiques, chest of drawers and hearth make for a nostalgic air. He serves a set menu featuring soba and vegetables. The appetiser is an assortment of more than a dozen vegetable dishes and is pleasing to the eye as well as the palate. He mills mostly Hitachiaki buckwheat from Ibaraki to make the soba. The quiet location and atmospheric setting will completely refresh you.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Shoes must be removed;[]
13324;LE UN;Japan;Nara;NIPPONIA HOTEL Nara Naramachi, 4 Nishijodocho, Nara, Nara, 630-8345, Japan;34.679569;135.826365;24;false;false;French;The elegant space was once a sake brewery founded in the 19th century, in the Meiji period. Enjoy French cuisine featuring Nara ingredients and various creative touches. Vegetables delivered from nearby farms are used in salads and soups. Also unique are the desserts made using sake lees and sweet sake. After the meal, a special Japanese tea, Yamatocha, is brewed, extending the magic to the last moment. Pairings with sake sourced directly from the brewery accentuate the cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13325;FAON;Japan;Nara;1122-12 Takabatakecho, Nara, Nara, 630-8301, Japan;34.681886;135.832014;32;false;false;French;‘Faon’ is the French word for fawn. The chef opened this restaurant in his hometown, choosing the name because of how everyone finds fawns irresistible. The cuisine is French, but with ume vinegar, salted rice malt and white miso added to the mix. Terrace seating is available, so you can enjoy your meal while admiring the five-storey pagoda of Kofukuji Temple, a National Treasure.;Air conditioning;[]
13326;Kiyosuminosato AWA;Japan;Nara;861 Takahicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8411, Japan;34.632427;135.854843;50;true;true;Japanese;Seasonal crops are lined up on the zataku. Yamato vegetables and vegetables from various countries spruce up the plates. The Miuras visit farms and grow the seeds they collect. The harvested vegetables are used in local dishes they learned how to prepare in each area. You’ll enjoy items grilled on a ceramic plate in spring and summer and soy milk nabe in autumn and winter together with colourful takiawase. The menu makes you feel like you’re strolling around a market garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Shoes must be removed;[]
13327;Chez Kurahashi;Japan;Nara;3406-1 Kamimachi, Ikoma, Nara, 630-0131, Japan;34.726921;135.720219;56;false;false;French;The chef sharpened his creative focus after travelling to Paris and meeting local chefs to discuss all things culinary. In search of cuisine that his customers will remember, the chef limits his dishes to combinations of just three ingredients. Pairings of seafood appetisers with fruit is his signature styling. Butter and cream are used with restraint for a lighter taste. Descriptions are provided by the chef himself. You’ll feel like an invited guest in the Kurahashi family home—chez Kurahashi.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13328;Nidaime Izumosoba Dandan;Japan;Nara;2-2-34 Omiyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8115, Japan;34.68244;135.816705;48;false;false;Soba;Izumo soba is a local cuisine of Shimane. The family moved to this location from Shimane and opened this restaurant to introduce the taste of their hometown. Nana Nitta, who took over the restaurant from the father, mills the unpolished buckwheat. This is what gives Izumo soba its blackish colour. The thin juwari soba is served with broth poured over it. Another cultural tradition of Izumo is the three-tiered vermilion-lacquered serving dish called a ‘warigo’.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13329;KOHYAMA;Japan;Nara;2-1 Isono Minamimachi, Yamatotakada, Nara, 635-0062, Japan;34.506772;135.741874;92;true;false;Japanese;The friendly welcome by the Koyamas will make you feel at home at this restaurant with no sign outside. The wife is the chef and her husband is the sommelier. Wine and sake are paired with the set menus. The dishes are based on dashi from kombu and katsuo, and Western elements are incorporated for a touch of creativity. Not only is there synergy between the dish and the sake, but the husband-and-wife team makes for a sense of easy-going togetherness.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13331;GENMAIAN;Japan;Nara;1-3-24 Horyuji Higashi, Ikarugacho, Ikoma-gun, Nara, 636-0112, Japan;34.614487;135.743431;63;true;false;Japanese;The meals here are all based on unpolished rice. Vegetable dishes with no meat or fish are served in small pots with unpolished rice that’s been cooked in a wood-fired oven. The owner-chef calls himself a master of unpolished rice cake, his speciality being rice cake made with a mortar and pestle. He wants his customers to get to know tastes that are being lost in an age of plenty, so he seasons his dishes with soy sauce, miso and mirin made using traditional processes.;Car park,Cash only,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13333;Le Bois;Japan;Nara;NOBORIOJI HOTEL NARA, 40-1 Noboriojicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8213, Japan;34.684136;135.829924;100;true;true;French;Nara and Hokkaido are co-stars in this drama of gastronomy. Hokkaido ingredients are used because of the collaboration with French restaurant in Sapporo. Through this interplay of two backgrounds, the charms of Japan's natural bounty come to the fore. Ingredients from Nara take the stage in plates garnished with vegetables and cuisine of amago trout. Seafood and potatoes arrive from the north. As the play unfolds, the diner’s knowledge of food producers and producing regions deepens.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13334;Sushidokoro WASABI;Japan;Nara;39 Hayashikojicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8227, Japan;34.682764;135.825754;59;true;false;Sushi;Born into a family that owned a sushi restaurant, the owner-chef helped her father out from a young age. The father noticed how drawn she was to sushi artisanry and provided a guiding hand. She was in her element when training and learned the techniques of those who came before. She starts with white-fleshed fish as it has a lighter taste. The restaurant is named after wasabi grown in a clean environment. Likening herself to wasabi, she put down her roots in Yamato.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13338;Camino;Japan;Nara;29-1 Fukuchiincho, Nara, Nara, 630-8381, Japan;34.677008;135.834792;87;true;true;Italian;Chef Takeshi Kamiji presents his guests with the hometown cooking of regions throughout Italy, from north to south. He is especially fascinated by pasta, pouring his efforts into handmade dishes such as Apulian orecchiette and Ligurian trofie. The array of dishes from each area are complemented by wines from every region of Italy. The warmth of the cheerful service in a machiya (merchant’s house) over a century old brings joy to the soul.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
13339;Sanjuhachi;Japan;Nara;12-11 Katashiocho, Yamatotakada, Nara, 635-0085, Japan;34.508629;135.743501;87;true;false;Italian;Toshikazu Kamei is a ‘chef of the soil and water’ who researched vegetable growing and water quality at university. He grows the vegetables himself and uses water that goes well with the dishes. Having prepared data on the water that goes best with each ingredient, he blends different kinds to achieve the right hardness and pH. The formula in the name is the deadline, set by his wife, for his becoming independent by age 37, and the plus one is his apology for missing it by a year.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13340;Kuramoto Ryori Maruto Shoyu;Japan;Nara;170 Iyodo, Tawaramotocho, Shiki-gun, Nara, 636-0243, Japan;34.549966;135.816381;27;true;false;Japanese;This Japanese restaurant is located in Nara’s oldest soy brewery. The head chef works together with the 18th generation owner and prepares a menu focused on soy sauce and vegetables. Soy sauce is used with everything from the appetisers to the sweets, such as the Miwa somen with soy sauce espuma and takikomi-gohan with unrefined soy powder. The theme is modern Japanese, and some of the dishes draw inspiration from Chinese and French cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Shoes must be removed;[]
13341;Wa Asuka;Japan;Nara;4-3-15-2 Tomio Motomachi, Nara, Nara, 631-0078, Japan;34.692248;135.733713;96;true;false;Japanese;Mitsuru Sakamoto opened his restaurant in Tomio, which appears in the ancient Nihon Shoki (Chronicles of Japan) . Incorporating traditional events such as the five seasonal festivals into the menu and decorating the dishes with seasonal leaves further celebrates the Japanese spirit. Yamato round eggplant is made into takiawase with herring. Yamato beef is grilled slowly over charcoal. The rice is Hinohikari from Asuka Village, from where Sakamoto hails.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
13342;cucina regionale YANAGAWA;Japan;Nara;12 Shibatsukinukecho, Nara, Nara, 630-8385, Japan;34.677237;135.83132;92;false;false;Italian;Mami Yanagawa has followed the path of Italian cuisine. She enjoyed her cooking classes so much that she became a chef herself. To study Italian gastronomy in its home, Yanagawa travelled to Italy, where she learned the depth and richness of regional variation. Her choice of name for her restaurant, ‘cucina regionale’ (‘hometown cooking’) proclaims the importance she attaches to the network of local and regional producers she has cultivated. Yanagawa links Italy and Nara to showcase the appeal of hometown traditions.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13343;Araki;Japan;Nara;B1F, 1-15-26 Gakuen Kita, Nara, Nara, 631-0036, Japan;34.700416;135.750256;87;true;false;Japanese;The Chinese character for ‘food’ comprises two radicals, one for ‘people’ and one for ‘good’, which could be interpreted as ‘making people better’. The owner-chef makes a credo of this interpretation and talks with customers about how to best enjoy the seasons. The hamo comes directly from Awaji, and longtooth grouper from Wakayama. Standard items to end with include Kyoto-style dashi chazuke and chirimen sansho on rice. The steamy hot dishes speak to the kind of training he had.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
13344;Gen;Japan;Nara;23-2 Fukuchiincho, Nara, Nara, 630-8381, Japan;34.676787;135.833865;73;true;false;Soba;A soba shop on the premises of a sake brewery. The location is Shimizu-cho, meaning ‘pure water town’, named for the clear streams that flow down from Mt. Kasuga and gush out in springs. Using water fetched for sake brewing, the owner-chef prepares exceptionally fine 100% buckwheat noodles. Soba grains carefully selected for their aroma are ground by hand in a stone mortar. Pure flavour is best conveyed in the ‘mizusoba’, soba dipped in nothing but cold water – the same way farmers would gauge the quality of their harvests.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Notable sake list,Shoes must be removed;[]
13345;Kawanami;Japan;Nara;4-6-14 Shibatsujicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8114, Japan;34.685979;135.810155;98;true;true;Japanese;The phrase ‘cook of the soil’ on the curtain expresses how much the founder prized vegetables. He tilled the field and grew his vegetables with care. That passion was passed on to his son, the second-generation owner-chef. His ingenuity is on display in how, for example, early harvest onions simmered in dashi are served in bowls made out of wax gourd. The ceramic serving dishes, which he made himself, also come from the soil.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
13346;KOMFORTA;Japan;Nara;1524-1 Nakayamacho, Nara, Nara, 631-0012, Japan;34.711486;135.773203;83;false;false;Italian;‘Komforta’ is Esperanto for ‘comfortable’ or ‘cosy’. It is an apt description for this restaurant in the style of a mountain hut, located in a slightly elevated part of town, as the wood accents feel warm and inviting. The cuisine bursts with creativity, crafted by a chef who gives his imagination free rein. Nara ingredients reflect the tempo of the seasons. The appetiser platter, piled with the flavours of a rich variety of ingredients, is served only at lunch. In the evenings KOMFORTA offers prix fixe menus with several courses.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13348;Pinot Noir;Japan;Nara;1-5-12 Imaicho, Kashihara, Nara, 634-0812, Japan;34.507122;135.788938;80;true;true;French;The Pinot Noir grape, produced in Burgundy, is used by vintners to make unique wines. Ikuo Komatsu chose this name for his restaurant because he wants to be a one-of-a-kind chef, just like the one-of-a-kind grape. He brings together numerous ingredients, including vegetables, to create dishes based on traditional French cuisine. He and his daughter prepare the food and serve the customers as a tag team. Their friendly competition provides a glimpse of the family bond.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13350;BANCHETTI;Japan;Nara;4-6-14 Shibatsujicho, Nara, Nara, 630-8114, Japan;34.685952;135.810077;29;false;false;Italian;The name of the restaurant is the imperative “Feast!” , which the chef chose to reflect the hospitality he offers, replete with the Japanese sense of season. Seating is at the counter, where customers can watch as the food is prepared: an idea he took from kappo restaurants. The acqua pazza, stewed with hanasansho in the spring and mushrooms in the autumn, is a speciality that brings together Japanese and Italian cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13351;Nikutoieba Matsuda;Japan;Nara;2F, 5-2-40 Naizencho, Kashihara, Nara, 634-0804, Japan;34.513889;135.791868;86;false;false;Beef;The owner-chef, a butcher, prepares wagyu. The set menu meal begins with a bold, hearty meat dish. He uses mostly Yamato beef for his customers to get a feel for Nara ingredients. His creative touches include slicing it thin and pressing it between sheets of kombu and making minced meat into gyoza dumpling. Even the last dish features wagyu, and includes chopped beef and curry. Creative dishes and attractive presentations make this a popular spot.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13352;Kappo Risuke;Japan;Nara;498-5 Kuzumotocho, Kashihara, Nara, 634-0007, Japan;34.524241;135.797382;50;false;false;Japanese;The colourful Japanese paintings and fusuma paintings are by owner-chef Toshiyuki Fukui himself. He likes fish, thus the paintings of tai, tilefish and other varieties. Most of the seating is in private rooms, so he puts much effort into kaiseki. The first highlight is the hassun and he includes more than 10 shuko for a good match with the sake. In summer, he catches the ayu himself. Having trained in Kyoto and Osaka, he also specialises in hamo dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
13353;Tama;Japan;Nara;4-5-14 Imaicho, Kashihara, Nara, 634-0812, Japan;34.506748;135.78597;76;false;true;French;This restaurant brings a little Edo era charm to the town of Imai. The interior of an old townhouse has been renovated and features both the nostalgia of old materials and a modern touch. Chef Reiichiro Nambu seeks to convey the flavours of the ingredients in a natural way. He exercises restraint with the seasoning and oil to prepare light dishes and puts much effort into a single set menu that brings out the very best of the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13354;Yakitori Mochizuki;Japan;Nara;32-14 Surugamachi, Nara, Nara, 630-8357, Japan;34.678305;135.820395;78;false;false;Yakitori;Hirokazu Bandofollows the teachings of where he trained and uses and cooks at high heat directly over the flame. He fills the roaster with bincho charcoal, leaving no spaces in between. Only a set menu is offered so that customers can enjoy a variety of skewers. He dresses whole chickens himself, so also offers rare parts such as chicken oysters and arteries. The meal starts with shuko, such as liver pâté, and proceeds to yakitori chosen to provide gradual changes in taste.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13355;Ristorante L'incontro;Japan;Nara;9 Yakushidocho, Nara, Nara, 630-8321, Japan;34.675882;135.832054;95;true;false;Italian;The chef was inspired by Italian food culture, especially local cuisines. He gathers ingredients from producers in Nara and goes to the mountains to pick wild vegetables and mushrooms himself. He processes meats like uncured ham and salami himself because he wants his customers to experience the homemade taste. The linguini and tagliolini pastas are also made from scratch. He uses simple seasonings to emphasise the natural fragrance of the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13356;Gojo GENBEI;Japan;Nara;2-5-17 Hommachi, Gojo, Nara, 637-0041, Japan;34.349032;135.693532;80;true;false;Japanese;Gojo vegetables are the main ingredient here – Akihito Nakatani has built relationships with nearby farmers and carries a wide variety, from traditional to Western. He picks the vegetables together with the producers and comes up with his ideas while talking with them. He also incorporates items of local culture such as local soy sauce, miso and sake. The fried konnyaku was inspired by southern Nara home cooking. His passion comes through when he explains the dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13357;Kaiseki Kakomura;Japan;Nara;2F, 10 Tsunofurishinyacho, Nara, Nara, 630-8223, Japan;34.681356;135.827648;59;false;false;Japanese;Inspired by the spirit of chakaiseki, Toshihiko Kakomura set out on the path of Japanese cuisine. He serves traditional kaiseki that pleases both eyes and tastebuds. The hassun always incorporates something seasonally festive and shows off his experience working at a ryotei. The chef is from Hiroshima, so prefers seafood from Setouchi, such as tai and stonefish. Holding dear the spirit of the tea ceremony, he puts care into hospitality, including setting out flowers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13359;Yan Zhu Chao;China Mainland;Hangzhou;2-3F, Block C, Zhongying Xinghai, 30 Zhongchuang Road, Binjiang, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.195333;120.2051635;18;true;false;Chao Zhou;The room sports a mix of cultural motifs from the Chaoshan region, including a miniature replica of Guangji Bridge, an icon of Chaozhou. Rather than a main dining room, guests are ushered into private rooms and menus must be customised in advance. The signature marinated “gelato” raw mud crab boasts creamy orange roe that melts in the mouth. The double-boiled silkie chicken soup with deer tendon and ginseng is ideal to warm you up on cold days.;Air conditioning,Car park,Foreign credit cards not accepted,Valet parking;[]
13360;A Bing Bao Shan Mian;China Mainland;Hangzhou;21 Zhonghe Middle Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2419024;120.1672762;24;true;false;Noodles;Experienced chef-owner A Bing honed his skills in a famous noodle shop in town before opening this joint over 40 years ago. Having moved to the current address in recent years, it remains a firm favourite with many locals. Its signature fried eel noodle soup has impressively springy noodles and crispy, meaty eel chunks. Try his "semi" noodle soup, too – noodles dressed sparingly in a thick broth, for a flavour-forward experience.;Cash only;[]
13361;28 Hubin Road;China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, Grand Hyatt, 28 Hubin Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2570318;120.1572255;77;false;false;Zhejiang;Perched on the shore of West Lake, this hotel restaurant is led by a local chef with over 20 years of experience under his belt. Traditional Zhejiang recipes are given a new spin – to great effect. The braised pork belly pagoda comes in two portion sizes: a mini version served with pumpkin flatbread and a regular one with chestnut pancakes. The wine list features a plethora of Chinese labels from Hebei, Shandong, Shanxi, Xinjiang and Ningxia.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13362;Li' An;China Mainland;Hangzhou;50F, Conrad Hotel, 228 Xinye Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2513646;120.2092093;23;false;true;Cantonese;Atop a skyscraper hotel, this elegant place commands breath-taking views of the Qiantang River. The decor is inspired by the East-meets-West Art Deco style of China around the 1920s. Cantonese classics are broadly covered – from soups and barbecue meats, to stir-fries with plenty of wok hei, plus a few innovative Zhejiang dishes. Don’t miss the crispy skin chicken. The sautéed fish bladder with pickled mustard greens goes well with an alcoholic drink.;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13363;Hu Qing Yu Tang Yao Shan;China Mainland;Hangzhou;98 Zhongshan South Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2306897;120.1653541;40;false;false;Hang Zhou;Hu Qing Yu Tang is a renowned Chinese medicine shop and this restaurant is its culinary venture, specialising in medicinal cooking. The chef complements ingredients with the therapeutic properties of herbs to derive maximum benefits. Huang qi river shrimps, steamed fu ling dumplings, and black sticky rice cake with ginseng are all unique creations you won't find anywhere else. For optimum results, pair your food with medicinal wines or healthy drinks.;;[]
13364;Ming Kitchen;China Mainland;Hangzhou;23F, Zhejiang Culture Building, 370 Tiyuchang Road, Gongshu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2733309;120.1563029;16;false;false;Zhejiang;This is the upmarket flagship of an F&B group that has been active on Hangzhou’s dining scene for over two decades. It specialises in refined cuisine that encompasses all the representative flavours of Zhejiang province. Their house-made dim sum is hugely popular, including deep-fried stinky tofu stuffed with radish and Chinese celery from Shaoxing, tofu buns from Jiande, bamboo shoot shao mai from Suichang and tofu pancake from Changshan.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13365;De Ming Fan Dian;China Mainland;Hangzhou;36 Huyu Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2090369;120.1457101;73;true;true;Hang Zhou;The down-to-earth joint is nestled in a residential neighbourhood. At the entrance of the dining room, dishes are neatly displayed – leafy greens, meat stews in clay pots and of course, the river fish that the restaurant is most famous for. Fried eel in bean sauce is loaded with scallion and garlic aromas. Braised pork intestine is tender and flavoursome, even better with their secret dip. Try also their house-made wines infused with herbs or fruits.;Cash only;[]
13367;Grand Dragon;China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, The Dragon, 120 Shuguang Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2691111;120.1383329;73;true;true;Zhejiang;This long-established hotel restaurant is famous for its gorgeous garden views, elegant ambiance and upmarket dishes. Authentic Hangzhou cooking takes centre stage, alongside some Cantonese and regional options. Classics such as sautéed river shrimps with Longjing tea, and crispy eel with shrimps are revisited, the latter as fried eel pieces stuffed with minced shrimp in a sweet and sour glaze. Private dining rooms of various sizes are available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
13368;Wu Ming Mian Guan;China Mainland;Hangzhou;17-1 Youdian Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2517039;120.176408;20;false;true;Noodles;The shop has no name because the owner believes his noodles are good enough to keep guests coming back regardless. In over 30 years, the place has not changed – with just six tables set up in the tiny space. But the huge portions of tasty noodles at bargain prices have amassed a loyal fan base. The fall-off-the-bone pork ribs with strong scallion aromas in particular tend to sell out early. The pork liver and kidney are also popular.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
13369;1913;China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, The New Hotel, 58 Beishan Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.258298;120.139151;80;true;false;Hang Zhou;This century-old restaurant opened its doors in 1913 along with the hotel where it is located. Memorabilia such as a typewriter and rotary phone are perfect details in the plush, nostalgic interior. The menu is also based on last-century Hangzhou favourites, updated with creative touches. The classic Xihu sweet vinegar fish is made with marble goby for its velvety texture. Ask for a table by the windows so you can take in the sweeping views of the lake.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13370;Zi Wei Hall;China Mainland;Hangzhou;Building 8, West Lake State Guesthouse, 18 Yanggong Causeway, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.237448;120.1282835;78;false;true;Zhejiang;Set in a manicured Chinese garden by the lake, the traditionally furnished restaurant makes an impression with its grand and airy space. The smart Chinese attire of the service team is also part of the appeal. On the menu: nicely made Jiangzhe and Hangzhou fare. Try the fried shrimp cake with crunchy water chestnut and diced Chinese celery. The Hangzhou crisp fish is a cold appetiser of deep-fried fish braised in sweet soy – delicious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13371;Xi Xi Liang Chen;China Mainland;Hangzhou;8 Wujiawan Street, Xixi National Wetland Park, Fangxi Road, Yuhang, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2709586;120.0427761;62;false;true;Chao Zhou;A serene place in a wetland park with a manicured Chinese garden. With just eight private rooms, privacy is guaranteed. Menus are tailor-made to diners' liking in advance, without à la carte options. The kitchen puts a sophisticated spin on authentic Chaozhou and Swatow dishes, with produce such as pickled mustard greens and baby mussels from Chaozhou. Try the soy-marinated goose webs and liver, and sticky rice balls in peanut sesame sugar.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13372;La Lune;China Mainland;Hangzhou;L628, 6F, The Mixc, 701 Fuchun Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2542195;120.211048;75;true;true;Chinese Contemporary;The high-ceilinged room is lavishly furnished with elegant chandeliers, ceiling fans and elaborate trims. The kitchen team excels in fusion Chinese cooking that creatively mixes and matches influences and techniques from various regional cuisines. Thinly sliced air-dried mackerel steeped in a special briny-sweet sauce is loaded with umami. The slow-cooked veal in a truffle sauce literally melts in your mouth. The curated tea list is intriguing!;Car park,Terrace;[]
13373;Shuiyang;China Mainland;Hangzhou;Xianghu Xiaoyao Manor, 256 Yuewang Road, Xiaoshan, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.25582;120.1645;85;true;false;Zhejiang;Xiaoyao Manor hotel opened in Xianghu Lake Resort in 2020. This F&B outlet is set in an idyllic landscape, boasts gorgeous views and serves authentic Hangzhou, Zhejiang dishes, as well as Xiaoshan farmhouse cooking. Made-to-order fish head à la Qiandao Lake can be prepared in various ways and is great for sharing. The peasant-style steamed stinky duo is quite unique and worth trying. The perfect spot to eat as part of your Xianghu Lake itinerary.;Air conditioning;[]
13374;Pu Zhu;China Mainland;Hangzhou;122 Dadou Road, Gongshu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.3004268;120.141863;57;true;true;Vegetarian;Adjacent to Xiangji Temple, this Jiangnan-style villa stands in a manicured garden with bamboo trees, rock works and water features. In the absence of à la carte options, diners pre-order the classic or seasonal set menu. Quality globally sourced produce is finessed by both Chinese and Western techniques into neat creations with potential health benefits. Tree tomato soup with seaweed from the waters of Xiapu kicks off the meal on a refreshing note.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13377;The Yue Hall;China Mainland;Hangzhou;58F, Sky Habitat, T1 Raffles City, 228 Xinye Road,  Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2509814;120.2080104;54;true;false;Cantonese;On the 58th floor of a skyscraper, this tiny gem with just eight tables affords lovely views of the bustling financial centre. Modernised Chinese motifs are juxtaposed with a futuristic electric glow. Under the supervision of an experienced chef from Hong Kong, the kitchen turns out umami-packed double-boiled soups, such as the whelk and dried scallop soup with matsutake mushrooms. The live seafood, such as fish and crab, tastes divine even when simply steamed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13380;Tian Lun Inn (Xihu);China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, Building No. 7, Ecological Cluster, 550 Xixi Road, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.26091;120.117185;87;false;false;Hang Zhou;Synonymous with delicious crab dishes, Tian Lun Inn serves different species of this crustacean depending on the season, with its multicourse all-crab meals being the most renowned. With firm, plump flesh and rich, creamy roe, hairy crabs from Taihu Lake are extremely popular year round. The crab roe pastry takes 45 minutes to prepare, but it's well worth the wait. Try local specialities such as West Lake beef soup or West Lake vinegar fish, too.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13381;Zhi Wei Guan • Wei Zhuang (Xihu);China Mainland;Hangzhou;10-12 Yanggong Causeway, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2327461;120.1326612;90;true;false;Hang Zhou;Nestled in the lakeside Hongli Villa complex in a picturesque setting, this restaurant is the city's pioneer in garden dining. The kitchen team excels in the new Hangzhou cuisine – rooted in tradition but updated with Western techniques. The signature gold medal braised pork has a melt-in-the-mouth texture, its fine slices modelled into a pagoda. Lotus flower pastries are exquisitely crafted, with purple sweet potato filling in a flaky crust.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13382;Pan Fang Chun (Zhongshan South Road);China Mainland;Hangzhou;479-481 Zhongshan South Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2395723;120.1663899;80;true;true;Dim Sum;A favourite spot for breakfast among locals, Fang Chun specialises in potstickers – with a nicely charred, paper-thin crust and juicy pork filling, they taste even better dipped in chilli sauce and vinegar. Cut through the richness with a bowl of sweet soymilk. For a lighter option, try the bite-size wonton soup with laver and scallions. Expect to queue at the door for service, and they close before 1pm, so come early to avoid disappointment.;Cash only;[]
13383;Dining Room;China Mainland;Hangzhou;37F, Park Hyatt Hotel, 1366 Qianjiang Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2562462;120.2104945;94;true;true;Zhejiang;With exquisite glass lanterns, glass screens and panoramic windows that welcome in river views, the high-ceilinged room is perfect for banquets and business dinners. The menu is dominated by Zhejiang classics, alongside some Cantonese dishes. The poetically named "Sinking Fish, Falling Geese" consists of white fish balls stuffed with bird's nest. The classic braised pork belly is thinly sliced and styled into a pagoda. Reservations recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
13386;Jiang Nan Yu Ge;China Mainland;Hangzhou;49-53 Shiwukui Alley, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2396235;120.1652199;92;false;true;Ningbo;Tucked away in a historical back street, this place teleports diners to a bygone era. The rustic-style interior is quirky, with bottles of yellow wine, including its own brand, placed on the floor. The kitchen team tailors menus to diners' budgets and the fish-heavy Ningbo fare is rife with bold flavours and umami. Try the steamed crab on pork ribs with distillers grains. With only two tables for two in the main room, it makes sense to book a private room.;Air conditioning,Foreign credit cards not accepted;[]
13388;Hotwoods;China Mainland;Hangzhou;1F, Building 27, Xixi Yihao, Ziyun Street, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.3134625;120.1415967;64;true;false;Latin American;This bustling spot serves barbecue in Texan, Brazilian and Argentinian styles. With a wood-fired smokery and ovens on site, the place exudes intoxicating smells. Try slow-smoked beef brisket, either grain-fed from the U.S. or grass-fed from New Zealand: the former is richer, the latter leaner. Pronounced smoky notes complement the beef perfectly. Grilled pineapple in banana walnut sauce for dessert cuts through the richness. The wine list is worth exploring.;Car park,Cash only,Wheelchair access;[]
13389;Hangzhou House;China Mainland;Hangzhou;Building EX4, Amandayun, 22 Fayun Lane, Xihu Street, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2376598;120.092537;61;false;false;Zhejiang;Within walking distance of Lingyin Temple and right next to the Amanfayun resort, this rustic-style restaurant exudes otherworldly serenity. On the menu, classic Jiangzhe dishes get a refined makeover with some creative combinations proving to be a pleasant surprise. The signature rice cake in chopped crab sauce, for instance, showcases the mild grassy note of perilla leaves. Ask about the dishes that need to be pre-ordered when making your reservation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13391;Fortune Garden;China Mainland;Hangzhou;504-506, 5F, Phase 2, Star Avenue, 1766 Wentao Road, Binjiang, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2146497;120.2011587;91;false;false;Cantonese;This modern, cosy restaurant sits on the top floor of a shopping mall. The menu showcases the best of Cantonese cooking with sophistication, astuteness and precision. Their dim sum lunch is a must, as are the barbecued meats. The honey-glazed cha siu pork, for instance, boasts the perfect ratio of fat and lean meat, as well as smoky and crispy charred edges. Plum sauce on the side cuts through the richness. Book ahead for private rooms.;Car park;[]
13392;Chic 1699;China Mainland;Hangzhou;L698, 6F, The Mixc, 701 Fuchun Road, Shangcheng, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2542195;120.211048;97;false;false;Fujian;The dimly lit space on two levels feels modern and chic, with its mix of bare concrete, glass, and metal structures. The food, meanwhile, is very much in keeping with Fujian tradition. Seafood from the province features heavily on the menu, alongside other Fujian produce. Signatures include honey-glazed grilled river eel with crispy skin and oily, velvety flesh. The raw oysters from Xiamen Harbour dressed in speciality sauce are zesty and summery.;Car park;[]
13394;Gui Yu Jia Mian;China Mainland;Hangzhou;74 Lower Manjuelong, Xihu, Hangzhou, China Mainland;30.2216743;120.122983;86;false;false;Noodles;The space may not be huge, but the minimalist Zen-inspired decor is soothing. In contrast to traditional Hangzhou-style noodles with their firm texture, these are handmade to a softer consistency – all the better for soaking up the soup. The spring water beef shin noodles deliver plenty of umami and a hint of spiciness. Sides such as braised bamboo shoot are also worth trying. Round off your meal with ding sheng cake with red bean filling.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
13396;Bavette;United Kingdom;Horsforth;4-6 Town Street, Horsforth, LS18 4RJ, United Kingdom;53.8367894;-1.6422927;45;true;true;French;From baguettes to bavettes, there’s something so overtly French about this terrific neighbourhood bistro that it’s a wonder they don’t have the tricolore flag hanging outside. Its unlikely location in the Leeds suburb of Horsforth is a result of the relationship between Leeds native Sandy Jarvis and Frenchman Clément Cousin, who met while working in some of London’s top restaurants. Clément runs the chatty service, while Sandy is in the kitchen working on keenly priced Gallic classics – expect to spot delicious renditions of the likes of pâté en croute and shellfish bisque.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13397;Six;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;Baltic Centre for Contemporary Art, South Shore Road, Gateshead, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE8 3BA, United Kingdom;54.969158;-1.5984701;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name refers to this restaurant’s location – perched on the sixth floor of the Baltic Centre for Contemporary Arts and affording brilliant views of the River Tyne. Formerly the Rank Hovis flour silo, before being transformed into a gallery in the 1990s, the building is an imposing and eye-catching presence in the city. A set menu comes in ‘Land and Sea’ and ‘Plant’ formats, delivering colourful dishes that are generous in both size and flavour, using fine produce like Portland crab and Dexter beef.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13398;1 York Place;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;1 York Place, Clifton, City of Bristol, BS8 1AH, United Kingdom;51.4544512;-2.6133507;51;false;true;European;Deep within the Georgian lanes of Clifton, lies this neighbourhood bistro with an uncluttered feel. Sit on the ground floor to make the most of the natural light flooding in the large windows, or head down the spiral staircase for a more intimate setting. The date-stamped menu takes a pan-European approach, be it ricotta gnudi from Italy, squid ink bomba rice from Spain or veal schnitzel from Austria. The relaxed service is delivered with a smile and sharing dishes like whole roast chicken add to the conviviality.;Air conditioning;[]
13399;Montrose;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;1 Montrose Terrace, Edinburgh, EH7 5DJ, United Kingdom;55.9566869;-3.1720143;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Located close to The Palace of Holyroodhouse, this 19th Century former inn has been converted into a wine bar and restaurant by the owners of Timberyard. The upstairs dining room has an intimate atmosphere courtesy of its soft lighting, rustic décor and small capacity. The cooking – which comes in the form of a set menu – is characterised by big, bold flavours, demonstrated in the likes of game tortellini or piquant green tomatoes. In the bar, oysters, charcuterie and other small plates are offered alongside an excellent wine list that champions lesser-known regions.;Interesting wine list;[]
13400;Osters;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;125 High Street, Gosforth, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE3 1HA, United Kingdom;55.0044566;-1.620273;98;false;true;Seafood;The team behind Lovage in Jesmond have turned their attention to the fruits of the sea at this restaurant on the bustling Gosforth High Street. Despite not quite being the restaurant’s namesake, oysters are available in multiple guises to kick off proceedings, before a choice of prime fish and shellfish. The chefs are aware of the quality of their ingredients, eschewing overcomplication in favour of simple combinations – like Pink Fir potatoes, tenderstem and beurre blanc accompanying a generous helping of sea trout.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
13401;Kinkally;United Kingdom;London;43 Charlotte Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 1RS, United Kingdom;51.5192114;-0.1356432;55;false;false;Eastern European;Offering something original to the Charlotte Street dining scene, this trendy restaurant takes its name from the Georgian dish khinkali. These dumplings come with a ‘handle’ at the top and fillings could include langoustines, pumpkin or beef. Accompanying the khinkali are a selection of Georgian-influenced small and large plates, from chkmeruli to pkhali. Keep the night going with a trip to Kinky, their basement bar serving a selection of creative cocktails, accompanied by a techno soundtrack and the same fabulous buzz as the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13403;Lasdun;United Kingdom;London;National Theatre, Upper Ground, Southwark, London, SE1 9PX, United Kingdom;51.50687;-0.11409;46;false;true;Modern British;Inside the Brutalist blocks of the National Theatre, lies this buzzy brasserie named after the building’s architect, Denys Lasdun. The sparse modern décor is accompanied by an abundance of exposed concrete, while the cooking has the same seasonal British ethos as the Marksman pub, which comes from the same owners. A good dose of flavour is extracted from the quality produce, while sharing dishes – like chicken, leek and girolles pie – are also on offer.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13404;Shin Jung;USA;Orlando;1638 E. Colonial Dr., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5529122;-81.3587859;15;true;false;Korean;Established in 1993 but redone following a fire, this local fixture is beloved for its highly enjoyable Korean dining. The interior is adorned with dark tile floors, wooden booths and white walls. Tables feature a center console for grilling meats, and a mounted television broadcasts a stream of K-Pop videos.This menu covers plenty of ground, from stews and noodles to an array of beef and pork barbecue dishes. As a starting point, know that the kitchen does right by the classics. Kimchi pancake is both substantial and properly crispy, and the banchan are all made in-house. Sharing is ideal here, but solo diners can take heart in the dolsot bibimbap or a kimchi stew, which arrives bubbling hard in a cauldron and packed with delicate, soft tofu.;Air conditioning;[]
13406;Pao by Paul Qui;USA;Miami Beach;3201 Collins Ave., Miami Beach, 33140, USA;25.8072484;-80.1237473;38;true;true;Asian;Damien Hirst's giant sculpture of a gilded woolly mammoth resides famously behind the lavish Faena Hotel. Such scale and grandeur is also the norm in this restaurant, overlooking the iconic attraction. Pao’s oval room is capped with a gold-dome ceiling that's centered around yet another statue by Hirst—a golden unicorn perched on a platform looming large over the stylish guests.To be clear, this spot is more than just good looks and its short menu knits together a range of influences. Many of them are Asian, as in dishes like scallop aguachile with pineapple and black lime or a bao with smoked Wagyu short rib with XO aïoli. Roasted black bass with chili patis and ginger-garlic rice swings from sweet to savory to spicy, and comforts at every turn.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13407;Estiatorio Milos;USA;Miami Beach;730 1st St., Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.7698852;-80.1355092;98;false;true;Greek;This "Greek God" has been a beacon of seafood excellence for the glamorous diners of South Beach since opening its doors in 2012. Some don’t even need a menu and prefer to order based on a guided tour to the back, where all manner of fish and crustaceans gleam on packed ice.With fresh seafood arriving multiple times a week, the kitchen tends to keep preparations simple. Sashimi of any type is a good first step, though we’re partial to the bigeye tuna with yuzu kosho and dill. Thin slices of fried zucchini and eggplant mounded around creamy tzatziki are also worth an order. Grilled whole fish baked in salt, and large lobsters round out the feast, though big spenders should inquire about deep-sea prawns for a pricey but precious seafood luxury.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13410;Mister O1 Extraordinary Pizza;USA;Miami Beach;1680 Michigan Ave., Ste. 101, Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.7915713;-80.1389949;79;true;false;Pizza;This boldly named pizzeria comes from Italian-born Chef and co-owner Renato Viola. Located steps from Lincoln Road Mall, this South Beach original is hidden away on the ground floor of an office building. Work your way towards the back to find a small space fronted by a wall of glass and offering seating for 16.There are choices to be had on this menu—from the thin-crust, 13-inch pizzas available plain or with toppings and the smaller 8-inch pies, to "Extraordinary" signatures like the Star Luca made distinct by its shape (the edges of the crust are folded to form a series of points). Topped with tomato, mozzarella and Calabrese salami, it reflects the chef's passion for pizza dough, made from imported Italian flour and slow-proofed for 72 hours.;Air conditioning;[]
13413;Cítricos;USA;Orlando;4401 Floridian Way, Orlando, 32830, USA;28.410967;-81.5873008;92;true;true;American, Regional Cuisine;Set on the second floor of the Grand Floridian Hotel, Citricos brings to life a gloriously contemporary vibe and décor elements that are a subtle nod to Mary Poppins. The menu is coastal American, as evidenced by the use of seafood, citrus and tropical fruit. The team has a refined cooking style, replete with balanced flavors and technical prowess.While the carte is seasonal, expect the likes of corn bisque whimsically arranged with pickled fennel and popcorn. Crispy smoked duck is finished with salt and gently set atop a tangle of tagliatelle with celeriac purée. Up next might be guava-braised short ribs with cheddar grits and poblano sauce, leaving you full to the brim. Save room for at least one exquisite dessert—like an orange blossom flan.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13414;Predalina;USA;Tampa;1001 E. Cumberland Ave., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9449249;-82.4497488;43;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Located in the Channelside District of downtown Tampa, siblings Blake Casper and Allison Casper Adams founded Predalina as an homage to their great-grandmother's coastal heritage (she was born in Brazil, raised in Portugal and finally settled in Rhode Island).The large menu is a nod to the Mediterranean, beginning with a wide variety of mezzes (the blistered cauliflower surrounded by whipped tahini is a winner). Lunch offers a nice mix of sandwiches and salads, while dinner is squarely focused on entrées and pastas. The tomato calamarata looks every bit the calamari it's named for, and dressed with a chunky, herb-laced tomato sauce and delicious kefalograviera, or Greek sheep's milk cheese, it's a satisfying dish.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13415;The Pearl;USA;Tampa;823 Water St., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9433027;-82.4501376;68;true;false;American;Located in the Channelside district of downtown Tampa, The Pearl rests within a mixed-use building with plenty of outdoor seating for warm days and nights. Inside, the space is contemporary with maritime and nostalgic touches throughout. The large American menu with shareable options aplenty sports a seafood focus, but don't sleep on dessert, as the in-house pastry chef oversees the pie-only menu. Come with friends for a fun time and to snack on treats such as fried pickles with a creamy dipping sauce or raw, baked or fried oysters. Go for broke with a seafood tower or enjoy a humbler entree, like the fish and chips. Their brown sugar pie with oatmeal cookie crust is a house classic that you'll definitely want.;Air conditioning;[]
13417;Ulele;USA;Tampa;1810 N. Highland Ave., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9594956;-82.462424;92;true;true;American;With a scenic location at the edge of a restored natural spring and a name that references a legendary Native American princess, there's clearly no shortage of charm on offer here. Although the "Native-inspired" cooking has only a tenuous connection to Florida's original inhabitants, the menu is a nod to Tampa's history and draws upon the various influences that have shaped the city's current culinary landscape. A bounty of seafood is featured, much of it sourced from local waters, with conventional delicacies like oysters and scallops alongside the less commonplace alligator (flash-fried or incorporated into hush puppies).Diners can soak up views of Hillsborough River amid an outdoor sculpture garden while sipping suds from the restaurant’s own brewery.;Wheelchair access;[]
13418;Prato;USA;Winter Park;124 N. Park Ave., Winter Park, 32789, USA;28.5983654;-81.3509796;45;false;true;Italian, Pizza;This seasonal delight arrives courtesy of Park Lights Hospitality and Chef Brandon McGlamery. Set along a tree-lined street, an overhead sign and tables out front signal the entry to this vast retreat. Inside, the room is rustic-chic, with vaulted ceilings, exposed brick and Edison bulbs that illuminate a central bar as well as caramel-leather booths.Flavorful Italian-American fare with a focus on wood-fired pizzas is what this kitchen does best. Start with crispy pumpkin arancini, enriched by celery root and apple mostardo. Then savor one of their ever-rotating pies with delectable toppings, like crab béchamel, sliced potatoes and artichoke-pepper conserva. End with a bit of sweet—there's no going wrong with a classic tiramisu, gelato or sorbet.;Air conditioning;[]
13419;Twenty Pho Hour;USA;Orlando;11951 International Dr., Unit B2, Orlando, 32821, USA;28.3913977;-81.4673621;58;false;true;Asian;It's not just pho, and they're not open 24 hours, but no matter, since this place is popular all the same. Expect to line up outside during busy hours, though the staff is very efficient and soon enough you'll be inside the black-and-white dining space. Peruse the broad noodle-based Asian menu that includes a stir-fried section in addition to appetizers and more. As the name suggests, there is indeed pho, and the broth is impressive. Go for the short rib pho to get a side of drama—the bone sticks out of the bowl—and falling-off-the-bone tender meat. From there, your meal might take a Korean turn with kimchi noodles or the Korean fire noodles, which despite their name, don't require a heat warning.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
13420;Juju;USA;Orlando;700 Maguire Blvd., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5536062;-81.3448901;70;false;true;Japanese;Juju is from the same folks behind Susuru, and it shares the same quirky dining room with an izakaya menu, but here they take it to another level with a seven-seat kappo bar that features something similar to kaiseki yet original. Seasonality reigns and diners choose from a wide menu of snacks and soup before selecting from the fried, grilled and dry-aged sashimi courses. Slices could include Japanese rock fish with citrus zest and skin-on goldeneye snapper, both aged a few days. Two-week-aged king salmon and four-week-aged otoro finished with Kaluga caviar are loaded with depth and prove that this spot is putting a different spin on sashimi. Steamed chawanmushi made with spiny lobster and mushroom is hit with a supremely creative lobster head dashi that packs on the flavor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
13421;Hiyakawa Miami;USA;Miami;2700 N. Miami Ave., Miami, 33127, USA;25.8026213;-80.1952187;57;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Is there a dining room cooler than Hiyakawa Miami? Probably not. Modern art hangs throughout the space that is art itself, with the counter and tables under an arch of backlit, undulating wood slats. This intimate stage glows at the bottom of an apartment building in trendy Wynwood.Top-quality seafood flown in from Japan and beyond meets creative flourishes like cured egg yolk and Okinawa salt. The menu is flexible and in addition to nigiri, sashimi and maki (also available by the platter) there are a range of items such as soups, tempura, and grilled meats.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13422;The Gibson Room;USA;Miami;2224 S.W. 22nd St., Miami, 33145, USA;25.7504714;-80.2304388;96;false;false;American;A stage for live music and a long, backlit bar do not usually signal serious cooking, but this moody and groovy Coral Way restaurant is the rare exception. Candlelight bounces off the tables in a room painted entirely black, as Chef Michael Beltran again expands his already-significant footprint across the city. His penchant for creative, bold flavors and his refusal to cut corners serve him well. For that matter, the menu does not fit into a tidy box: Croutons in the Caesar are filled with a mousse of anchovies. Agnolotti are handmade, packed with a clever venison bolognese. Wide as a dinner plate, the chicken schnitzel gets dolled up with salsa verde, a fried egg, and boquerones. There are no limits to what you’ll find or how long you’ll stay.;Air conditioning;[]
13423;Supernatural Food & Wine;USA;Tampa;305 E. Polk St., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9507312;-82.4587371;82;false;false;American;Located in downtown Tampa in a tiny space with some seating outside and a small counter inside, this casual concept is all about sandwiches—at breakfast and lunch—as well as a few sides and salads. It's a bright, mood-elevating kind of place where diners come in the morning for the olive and feta sandwich, served on a toasted focaccia bun with a black olive tapenade, fluffy egg, feta, thinly sliced red onion, and roasted peppers. Craving sweet instead of savory? Fresh cinnamon sugar sour doughnuts are a hit (and often sell out). Middays are met with the likes of turkey and cheddar melts with sweet bacon jam that are equal parts hearty and impressive.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13424;Ossobuco;USA;Miami;62 N.W. 27th St., Miami, 33127, USA;25.8021227;-80.19638;33;true;true;Contemporary, Steakhouse;Wynwood’s newest tenant is making some noise in an already-bustling zip code. From the glossy wood tables to the handsome bar, everything seems to shine under the spotlights. The dining room is anchored by a roaring, wood-burning grill, which turns out big proteins like smoked lamb chops with pistachio dukkah and charred, dry-aged steaks. Indeed, the steakhouse portion of the menu offers obvious appeal but so too do the lighter courses. Smoked baby beets with ricotta mousse is right on target, while the ossobuco empanada and sweetbreads with wagyu potato purée are the makings of a meal of their own. A stylish patio with a vibe of its own, a thoughtful cocktail list worth digging into, and a weekend DJ who knows how to work a room seal the deal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13425;Maty's;USA;Miami;3255 N.E. 1st Ave., Miami, 33137, USA;25.807409;-80.1929;76;false;false;Peruvian, Seafood;With the beloved Itamae now closed, Chef Valerie Chang strikes out on her own with this full-service follow-up in Midtown. Pulling inspiration from her childhood and from her grandmother, after whom the restaurant is named, Chang uses quality seafood to deliver bright, citrus-forward Peruvian flavors. Those who’ve eaten with Chang before will recognize some of the dishes: Black grouper, kanpachi and ocean trout arrive dressed with the likes of aji dulce, kiwiberries, finger limes and passionfruit. Meaty entrees like chicken milanesa and oxtail saltado strike heavier chords, but we’re quite happy to stick with seafood in the grilled dorade with aji amarillo beurre blanc. The bar, meanwhile, offers an appealing roster of pisco-based cocktails.;Air conditioning;[]
13426;MILA;USA;Miami Beach;1636 Meridian Ave., Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.7900371;-80.1365933;29;true;false;Asian, Mediterranean Cuisine;It's hard to ignore the sensory overload that greets diners as they exit the elevator and enter this titanic-sized establishment. There are two full bars—one indoors and a second out on the terrace—both beloved by the city's hip and trendy. Wood-carved artwork, natural materials and a plethora of foliage blend seamlessly to ensure a unique setting. From the light starters and ceviches to maki and substantial entrées, this menu may best be described as "MediterrAsian-inspired." Plates are best when shared among friends, as in the robata-grilled lamb kofte with herbed yogurt or a soba noodle salad with artichoke and pesto.If you can snag a seat at brunch, don't miss the eggs Benedict, starring a brioche bun, Bellota ham and blood orange hollandaise.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13427;Maxine's on Shine;USA;Orlando;337 N. Shine Ave., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5472456;-81.3621309;81;true;false;American;In operation for more than a decade, Maxine and Kirt Earhart's Colonialtown charmer is everyone's favorite neighborhood hangout. Crowds spill out in front during the weekend for brunch, thanks to a host of comforting dishes that soothe and satisfy. Think plates of fried green tomatoes, flaky crab cakes and of course, chicken and waffles. Dinner follows suit with such familiar yet flavorful dishes as a half-pound burger, or skillet lasagna, which is available with roasted vegetables instead of beef.There are good vibes all round. The décor is eclectic and bears a whimsical slant by way of bold colors, lots of artwork, a dark, sultry bar, as well as tightly packed tables. Interior accommodations are supplemented by ample outdoor seating.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park;[]
13428;Macchialina;USA;Miami Beach;820 Alton Rd., Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.7785114;-80.1409833;75;false;true;Italian;Locals and residents are devout fans of this cozy spot, filling the space nightly. The setting features tufted leather banquettes tailed by a charming covered patio area. The bar is graciously attended to and pours an almost all-Italian wine list that's bolstered by house-infused grappa in flavors like chai tea and chamomile.The menu is concise, so it's easy for diners to focus on the best attributes of this kitchen team—that largely being the house-made pasta. Think of supple strands of spaghetti slicked with pomodoro sauce or cacio e pepe. Other highlights include the hearty veal parmigiana. But make sure you save room for the tiramisu—given a distinct Miami accent with dulce de leche-sweetened cream and a sea salt-sprinkled cap of espresso granita.;Air conditioning;[]
13429;Taquiza;USA;Miami Beach;7450 Ocean Terrace, Miami Beach, 33141, USA;25.8605169;-80.1199036;26;false;false;Mexican;When Steve Santana launched his humble taco stall in 2014, he probably didn’t imagine just how popular it would get. The web developer-turned-chef was one of the first in the city to nixtamalize, grind, press and griddle his tortillas in-house, and now look—the breezy location in North Beach is central command for a recognized brand that sources corn from small farms in the Midwest and supplies restaurants across the city. Signature blue corn tortillas wrap around a host of fillings, like melting lengua or fried mahi, all garnished with radish, onion and served with sharp salsas (ask for the charred jalapeño).With palm trees swaying throughout and the lure of the ocean just one block away, this beachside favorite is a Miami mainstay for good reason.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13430;Mignonette;USA;Miami;210 N.E. 18th St., Miami, 33132, USA;25.793416;-80.1906106;29;true;false;Seafood;You could wander in solo wearing flip-flops or pull up with a date in a dinner jacket. Nobody minds either way at Chef Danny Serfer’s oyster bar, which has lit up this corner of Edgewood since 2014 and sits directly across from the city cemetery.Once a 1930s gas station, this refitted space is retro-cool, thanks to warehouse floors, comfy booths and floor-to-ceiling windows. Standing under a vintage marquee that lists the day’s bivalves, chefs may be found shucking for a crowd that gets louder as the night moves on. Guests can make an entire meal out of oysters, but fantastic small plates, like the smoked fish dip served with buttered saltines or mussels cooked in a spicy tomato sauce, are entirely worth an order. Key lime pie is a sweet send-off.;Air conditioning;[]
13432;Fiola Miami;USA;Coral Gables;1500 San Ignacio Ave., Coral Gables, 33146, USA;25.7052813;-80.2823328;96;false;false;Italian, Seafood;Everything seems to sparkle inside Chef Fabio Trabocchi’s Italian looker in Coral Gables. White tablecloths, dark hardwood floors, glass at every turn and a gleaming open kitchen set the stage in a restaurant that is busy any day and time of the week. Seafood, naturally, is the calling card here, and raw bar items like shrimp cocktail with tomato compote highlight quality sourcing. Caviar and truffles can find their way to any dish, if you ask, and housemade pastas like spaghetti alla vongole are portioned to share. From there, the grill does most of the heavy lifting for any whole fish and high-end steaks offered. Even though this is a prime destination for business meetings, the setting is far from stuffy, in part thanks to a suave service team.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13433;Lung Yai Thai Tapas;USA;Miami;1731 S.W. 8th St., Miami, 33135, USA;25.7658469;-80.2230997;51;false;false;Thai;You could drive down the street a dozen times and still overlook this intimate little nook that hides in plain sight. Little Havana is certainly an unexpected place to find one of the city’s hottest Thai kitchens, but the long waits are an indication (no reservations) that Chef/owner Veenuthri Trisransri knows what he’s doing. On a menu that mixes typical standbys with Northern specialties, begin with an order of homemade dumplings with a pork or shrimp filling, served steamed or fried. Khao Soi, a coconut-based curry with your choice of protein, bobs with egg noodles and has a rich, creamy profile without too much heat. Tables, plates and even the place itself is small, so order ambitiously and be prepared for a kitchen that sends out dishes faster than you can finish them.;Air conditioning;[]
13436;La Mar by Gastón Acurio;USA;Miami;500 Brickell Key Dr., Miami, 33131, USA;25.765803;-80.1851609;40;false;false;Peruvian;Gastón Acurio and Executive Chef Diego Oka opened this Peruvian hangout on Brickell Key back in 2014, and yet, in a city that prides itself on staying young and looking good, there is still no restaurant that can match these views.At the base of the Mandarin Oriental hotel, the space's expansive terrace sits right on Biscayne Bay in full view of the Miami skyline. It is a sight to savor—and the reason why nobody books a table indoors. All the while, friendly servers usher out a broad menu of familiar favorites. Start with seafood. Ceviche loaded with grouper, shrimp and octopus arrives dressed in a tangy leche de tigre, while meaty, jumbo scallops come grilled with parmesan foam. The classic, umami-packed lomo saltado and a piquant pisco sour round out any good meal here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13437;The Pinery;USA;Orlando;295 N.E. Ivanhoe Blvd., Orlando, 32804, USA;28.5655889;-81.3735524;81;false;false;American;This trendy first-floor restaurant overlooking Lake Ivanhoe has the substance to support its hype. The name, referring to a "hothouse" or "field" where pineapples are grown, is an homage to the area's history—it was once the center of the nation's pineapple industry. A fire pit outside is set beside an array of tables that offer spectacular sunset views and are a great spot for a seasonal cocktail.Beyond the front door (which dons a brass handle of a pineapple, of course) lies the dining room—warm with earthy hues, plush booths and a tufted leather banquette. The cuisine is similarly inviting, replete with local produce. The smoked peanut soup and a bread board (with pimento cheese and cinnamon sugar butter) are hearty, unfussy and flavorful favorites.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13439;The Den at Azabu Miami Beach;USA;Miami Beach;161 Ocean Dr., Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.7704634;-80.1326776;44;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Tucked away in the Stanton Hotel through Sushi Azabu’s dining room and behind a sliding door is this intimate sushi spot. Everything about the space is sleek, from the smooth blonde counter made from a Hinoki cypress tree to the meticulous chef who slices and serves with effortless precision.Most of the fish is handpicked at the market in Japan and flown in a few times a week. And whereas some counters can come off a little too earnest, the itamae here are a friendly bunch who are happy to answer questions and accommodate special requests. The menu alternates between hot and cold dishes, and few twists, as in uni soy sauce, are to be expected. Recent highlights have included thinly sliced octopus dotted with a sunny orange miso as well as soy-marinated akami nigiri.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
13440;Walrus Rodeo;USA;Miami;5143 N.E. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33137, USA;25.8235437;-80.1914786;39;false;false;American, Italian;With no proper stove or gas oven on site, the team behind Boia De in Buena Vista brings wood-fire cooking to this rambunctious corner spot just a few doors down. And in an unexpected turn, it’s vegetables, not meat, that seem to get top billing on this finely honed menu. Carrot tartare with carrot top salsa or schmaltz-roasted maitake mushrooms with heirloom beans exemplify delicious sophistication. Even the lamb ragù lasagna is a light-hearted, garden marvel: The pasta sheets are made from mustard greens. There is, of course, some meat, as well as pizza, but it's the charred quail which recalls the best of backyard barbecues. All of it is very easy to take in and enjoy in a casual space that welcomes families and couples alike.;Air conditioning;[]
13441;Toledo;USA;Orlando;1000 W. Buena Vista Dr., Orlando, 32830, USA;28.3636313;-81.5715048;68;true;true;Spanish;Situated on the 16th floor of Disney's Coronado Springs Resort, Toledo is quite the looker with lofty ceilings in bold colors and geometric tiled floors. Nab a table by the glass wall and you'll have a bird's eye view of the Epcot fireworks. Meanwhile, on the tables Spanish cuisine takes center stage. Tapas kick things off, and pan con tomate is a natural choice. Meat-forward mains include several steak options, as well as a ribeye for two, but the Rioja-braised chicken makes a compelling argument for choosing a different route. End on a sweet note with café con leche, a chocolate choux pastry filled with chocolate and coffee cream.Though certainly not inexpensive, Toledo packs less of a punch to the wallet than other Disney restaurants. -;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
13442;On Swann;USA;Tampa;1501 W. Swann Ave., Tampa, 33606, USA;27.9374088;-82.4750772;43;true;true;Contemporary, Southern;This lofty, stylish space draws in crowds, thanks to its relaxed, hip vibe and flavorful, unpretentious cooking. Chef and owner Chris Ponte, a heavy-hitter in the local dining scene, has assembled a menu that’s as charmingly eclectic as the restaurant’s design. You’ll find nods to Spain and France, but Italian and Southern flavors predominate, so you’re as likely to encounter ricotta salata as pimento cheese, and both grits and risotto find equal footing. Combinations of sweet and savory seem to be a specialty, as in a tomato-date sauce paired with lamb meatballs, or a fig tart with gorgonzola and caramelized onions.Brunch is particularly popular, owing, no doubt, to the airy, well-lit room and ample list of tempting seasonal cocktails.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
13443;Kaya;USA;Orlando;618 N. Thornton Ave., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5520757;-81.365581;61;true;true;Filipino;Kaya occupies a small bungalow-style building in the Mills 50 district. Inside, there's a quirky charm along with views of the open kitchen. Diners enjoy a tasting menu served in multiple courses, some with more than one element. Expect a modern spin on classic Filipino dishes with local seafood and central Florida produce taking center stage. Kinilaw na isda, a ceviche-style dish with madai and finely diced fruit in a vinegar sauce is a stunning dish that wakes up the palate for a strong start. Then, the menu changes often, but you may enjoy kare, a rectangle of braised fork-tender oxtail resting in the classic and flavorful peanut stew/sauce, along with various vegetables. It's served with their pitch-perfect garlic rice, served classic or with a luxe update with King crab.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13444;AVA MediterrAegean;USA;Orlando;290 S. Park Ave., Orlando, 32789, USA;28.5959186;-81.3509356;87;false;true;Greek;This sleek modern Mediterranean dazzler is smack in the center of the ever-charming Winter Park. It's a bit of a scene, so dress up for shared plates and a family-style menu with a focus on the Cycladic region. It's best enjoyed as a duo or a group, especially with their tempting selection of  mezze, appetizers, salads and raw options—and that's just to start. Don't skip the crispy eggplant zucchini with its alternating stack of paper-thin slices. Move on to seafood-focused main dishes but save plenty of room for their baklava. It's a knockout modernized rendition of the traditional phyllo and spiced nut mixture, served here with walnuts and pistachios dressed in honey with ample spice and a round of pistachio ice cream.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13445;Flaming Mountain;USA;Tampa;13520 University Plaza St., Tampa, 33613, USA;28.0705177;-82.4297298;22;true;false;Chinese, Regional Cuisine;Flaming Mountain's strip mall environs may be less than exciting but they save their sizzle for the food. The owners, husband-and-wife Hongfeng Li and Ling Wu, are originally from  Shenyang in China's northeast, and the menu proudly displays their regional heritage alongside classic Sichuan cuisine and grilled skewers. Chef Wei Zhang sources quality ingredients for dishes that deliver bold flavor across the board. Portions are hearty, so arrive armed with an appetite for meals like Chungking spicy chicken, with a plate piled high with classic dry fried chicken studded with chilies and peppercorns. Cucumber salad tossed in a vinegar sauce balances the heady spice. Cumin-scented lamb done in a stir fry style is another standout.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13446;Swine & Sons;USA;Orlando;201 N. Bumby Ave., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5448964;-81.3518036;100;false;false;American, Southern;Alexia Gawlak is behind this sandwich concept nestled within the Winter Park Social House, a collaborative, multi-concept space that buzzes with an industrial farmhouse chic. There are tables indoor and out, but you'll need to order at the counter. The menu is compact but plenty enticing with a line-up of comfort food classics. Tuck into the the likes of a fried chicken sandwich done Thai-style, as well as other sandwiches such as pastrami melts and Cubans, as well as burgers. Finish the meal with a soft chocolate chip cookie that has a hearty amount of flaky salt for good measure.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13447;Kabooki Sushi;USA;Orlando;3122 E. Colonial Dr., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5531215;-81.341509;38;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;This freshly minted space wears all the contemporary touches that pepper our Instagram feeds. There are hexagonal tiles and a green "living" accent wall donning a neon sign that reads "Good Vibes Only." The marble bar hums with activity, not unlike the booths situated along the center.It may be billed as updated Japanese fare fused with inventive Pan-Asian elements, but make no mistake—this is not an average strip mall spot. This cooking is unbound by tradition. Sushi is de rigueur, but splurge on the omakase for a worthy venture with the likes of torched salmon with truffle pâté, smoked trout roe and aji amarillo. Other oceanic delights include a bluefin sashimi flight, hamachi nigiri with truffled caviar and uni rice with seared lobster.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
13448;Lido;USA;Miami;9011 Collins Ave., Miami, 33154, USA;25.8777849;-80.1214556;82;false;true;Italian, Seafood;Lido brings breezy, Italian coastal cooking to the Four Seasons Hotel at The Surf Club. There is nothing better than a seat than on the terrace, which overlooks the pool and off to the ocean through a line of palm trees. Against this dazzling backdrop, his team delivers politely seasoned, well-sourced seafood. Crudo is an easy start, like bluefin tuna tartare with pickled seaweed and puffed wild rice. Plenty will be content with just a king crab salad, but don’t ignore housemade pastas like seafood risotto or spaghetti with clams. Larger plates include branzino with rainbow chard or tagliata with beef jus. An oasis that radiates tranquility, the restaurant is a pricey, albeit luxurious, retreat from the rest of the city.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13449;Brasserie Laurel;USA;Miami;698 N.E. 1st Ave., Miami, 33132, USA;25.7810533;-80.1920482;18;false;false;French;It’s early days for this clean-cut brasserie, located in the construction-clogged Miami Worldcenter. An expansive patio, high ceilings and plenty of seating all around set the stage for a tight menu of French classics that most kitchens have long since forgotten. On sparkling Bernardaud porcelain, Chef Michael Beltran delivers a hefty dose of nostalgia with escargot drenched in garlic butter, foie gras with berry gastrique and lobster with veal sweetbreads. Though rich, the cooking – and the environment, for that matter – manage to feel decidedly of the times. Know that these luxuries come with a price and are meant to be enjoyed, so anyone hoping to grab an easy omelet or burger with fries in between shopping will be disappointed.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13450;YH Seafood Clubhouse;USA;Orlando;8081 Turkey Lake Rd., Orlando, 32819, USA;28.4474652;-81.4759932;98;false;false;Chinese, Cantonese;The strip mall environs belie the sweeping elegance of YH Seafood Clubhouse, where several dining spaces beckon guests with a refined tone. There is a full menu from the kitchen, along with an entire page devoted to Cantonese dishes, but the comprehensive selection of dim sum is of particular note. Rather than roaming carts, dishes are ordered, then arrive piping hot. From siu mai and egg tarts to pineapple pork buns, all of the classics are excellent. Sticky pork dumplings are a surprising delight with their crispy-sweet exterior and mochi-like, savory ground pork interior. Served warm, they're a memorable bite. Of course, the best way to enjoy this spot is to come with a group and order with abandon.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13451;Four Flamingos, A Richard Blais Florida Kitchen;USA;Orlando;1 Grand Cypress Blvd., Orlando, 32836, USA;28.3821588;-81.5097444;25;true;true;Contemporary;This exciting concept from Chef Richard Blais is nestled in the Hyatt Regency Grand Cypress property. Follow the footpath that leads over a bridge and towards the bright pink entrance, fronted by a waterfall. This retreat radiates a calming, coastal vibe with design details like plentiful windows, warm wood and pops of color. Fittingly, the menu is contemporary Americana meets the tropics. The chef's focus is on seasonal, bold and creative flavors, as in a tuna tostada crowned by an egg yolk that is, in reality, a bright passion fruit sauce. Big eaters know to save room for mains like swordfish, lobster and deliciously spiced mojo chicken.Couples rejoice, as this is a perfect place to splurge, celebrate and eat to your heart's content.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
13452;Havana Harry's;USA;Coral Gables;4612 S. Le Jeune Rd., Coral Gables, 33146, USA;25.7291466;-80.2618992;89;false;true;Cuban, Regional Cuisine;A couple of refrigerated showcases filled with eats and treats welcome diners to this tropical haven. But for those who don't wish to grab and go, a vast and contemporary room lies beyond, furnished with tasteful artwork, a central bar, splashes of color and lush banquettes.The dominantly Latin menu flaunts all the classics, from tostones in various forms and flavors to guayaberos (fried plantains eclipsed with shredded pork, grilled onions and a guava-infused barbecue sauce). Mixed seafood with beans and yellow rice is ideal for groups, especially when you consider its ingredients—shrimp, clams, chicken, chorizo and peppers galore. Forget about your waistline for a moment and indulge in a sweet finale from their well-edited selection.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
13454;Niu Kitchen;USA;Miami;104 N.E. 2nd Ave., Miami, 33132, USA;25.7753022;-80.1903736;49;false;false;Spanish;If anybody is going to blast Snoop Dogg over the speakers, it might as well be this restaurant in downtown Miami. With glossy concrete floors, a dark, dim interior and a handful of come-as-you-are servers, it's an effortlessly cool spot. The cooking speaks volumes, designed for groups and based around Spanish tapas. Follow the hype and start with the much-talked-about charbroiled oyster, branded tableside with a hot coal and paired with ponzu and rice vinegar-mayo. Branzino tartare with white garlic cold soup, hearty paellas and other seafood-forward dishes showcase big flavors and quality product enlivened with smart, creative flourishes.For a similar vibe, head next door where the team runs a bar and retail shop focused on natural wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13457;Los Fuegos by Francis Mallmann;USA;Miami Beach;3201 Collins Ave., Miami Beach, 33140, USA;25.807485;-80.1235918;89;false;true;Argentinian, Steakhouse;“Theatrical” barely begins to describe the scale and style of Francis Mallman’s restaurant set inside the FAENA Hotel. Much like the hotel itself, the director of Moulin Rouge is responsible for such décor elements as leopard-print booths, striking red-cushioned seats and flashes of gold that appear on everything from the bar to the carpet.Known for open-fire cooking, Chef Mallman is not outmatched by the room’s design, delivering an asado experience that rivals the city’s best steakhouses. Beets buried under coals for eight hours and festooned with pistachio yogurt and garlic chips are a must, followed by big proteins like Australian filet that's grilled, coated in breadcrumbs and fried.The bustling bar at the end of the room draws a stylish crowd.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
13459;Oak & Ola;USA;Tampa;1910 N. Ola Ave., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.9612386;-82.4643945;20;true;true;European;Under the aegis of celebrated chef, Anne Kearny, this boisterous scene forms one of the keystone culinary destinations for the massive Armature Works development in which it is housed.The menu relies heavily on prominent wood-fired ovens and casts a wide net for European flavors, turning to Iberian ingredients—as in the roasted octopus with chorizo, white beans and kale. Then, Germany might be the inspiration behind a plate of bregenwurst with caraway-pickled cabbage and apple chutney. Other offerings, like yellowtail snapper with amandine sauce, have their roots in New Orleans, where the chef first earned her reputation. Regardless of this particular reference point, the common thread here is assertive flavors prepared with an assured lack of fuss.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13460;Chuan Fu;USA;Winter Park;1035 N. Orlando Ave., Ste. 105, Winter Park, 32789, USA;28.606839;-81.365562;81;true;true;Chinese, Sichuan;This sleek Winter Park spot is elegant and polished but never feels stuffy thanks to warm service that shows genuine consideration for each guest. The large Szechuan menu features many of the classics served in a traditional family-style manner, and the solid cooking shows its skill with layered flavors and bold takes. First, tuck into the cucumber salad, with its punch of soy and garlic, before settling into the Chongqing chicken with its chili and peanut garnish. A bowl of flaky white fish in a savory broth loaded with vegetables, pickled cabbage and glass noodles is further proof that heat and spice are balanced nicely here.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13461;Cafe La Trova;USA;Miami;971 S.W. 8th St., Miami, 33130, USA;25.7662072;-80.2102565;50;true;false;Cuban, Latin American;Of Jewish and Latin descent but born and raised in Miami, Chef Michelle Bernstein is intrinsic to the city's culinary scene. For this concept in Little Havana, she teams up with cocktail guru, Julio Cabrera, and the result is extraordinary. It's a vivacious place that hums with live music and a décor that transports guests through decades of history—from Cuba to the Cuban experience in Southern Florida.The menu features such classics as lechon with steamed yuca and tangerine mojo. Specials may deviate from the norm but are exquisite in their sweet and savory blend—think seared foie gras paired with Spanish French toast, maduros and maple syrup. Digestifs, like the Hotel Nacional with pineapple rum and apricot liqueur, are a fine way to quench the affair.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
13464;Doce Provisions;USA;Miami;541 S.W. 12th Ave., Miami, 33130, USA;25.7679401;-80.2142528;28;false;false;Cuban;You could drive by this spot in Little Havana a dozen times and still not realize what’s behind the blackout windows. And if you walked in and didn’t notice the back door, you’ve again missed the point. That door leads down a narrow path that opens up on to a backyard oasis like no other. With garden lights and greenery all around, this patio feels like a private party that nobody else knows about. True to the area, the menu is fundamentally Cuban with hearty flourishes. Golden chorizo croquetas, crispy lechon asado buns and tostones piled high with shredded beef make for a meal, but this is hardly the place to rush. Come with a group, order a round of drinks and see where the night takes you.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13465;Ponte;USA;Tampa;1010 Gramercy Ln., Tampa, 33607, USA;27.9522981;-82.5029771;55;false;false;Contemporary, American;Chef Christopher Ponte oversees the very grand eponymous restaurant located in midtown Tampa where a cream-and-white palette sets an elegant tone. This is a linen tablecloth kind of place where a comprehensive menu lists dishes with a contemporary and creative American flair.Kick off this memorable meal with Champagne and pearls—oysters finished with a pink peppercorn mignonette foam—or opt for the salmon Wagyu set over crispy sushi rice. Discover an entire section of the menu devoted to steaks with different sauces, toppers and butters. It may read a bit showy, but it's exciting nonetheless and feels worthy of the price tag. Cocktails are quite literally split down the middle, offering both a classic version of the usual suspects alongside modern takes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13466;Knife & Spoon;USA;Orlando;4012 Central Florida Pkwy., Orlando, 32837, USA;28.4056024;-81.4293671;79;true;false;Steakhouse;Located within the Ritz-Carlton, Grande Lakes, this restaurant from Chef John Tesar cuts an impressive figure. It is a vast, modern space sporting beachy hues, weathered wood, and a well-stocked bar. The dimly-lit dining room is front and center, while an open kitchen resides in the back. In-house, dry-aged steaks from 44 Farms, inventive pastas like cacio e pepe made with ube noodles, and top-shelf seafood give diners plenty to choose from. The kitchen is quick to highlight local farmers who supply a range of produce and even offers a “green” tasting menu that solely celebrates this bounty. Luxury imports such as sea urchin and scallops from Japan punctuate the menu. An adventurous cocktail list and an attentive service team round out the experience.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13467;Bern’s Steak House;USA;Tampa;1208 S. Howard Ave., Tampa, 33606, USA;27.93162;-82.48282;99;false;true;Steakhouse;For decades, this stately steakhouse has been a local favorite for special occasions of all stripes, and its popularity shows no signs of shrinking. Diners dress to impress amid the garish vintage opulence, which is matched by a slickly ceremonious suit-clad service team and colossal wine collection.A meal might start with oysters, or one of the many caviar options, but savvy diners save ample space for a curated selection of prime steaks, many dry-aged extensively in house before getting a char treatment on the kitchen’s massive grill. Don’t fill up on the assorted sides—at the end of the meal, guests are whisked to the posh upstairs dessert room, where bananas Foster or baked Alaska can be enjoyed with house-roasted coffee and live piano music.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
13468;Steelbach;USA;Tampa;1902 N. Ola Ave., Tampa, 33602, USA;27.96083;-82.46376;61;true;true;Southern, Steakhouse;Set in a space that once housed the Tampa Electrical Company's main offices, the stripped-down, industrial-chic aesthetic mirrors an air of studied nonchalance. Essentially a steakhouse with a Southern drawl, the menu here focuses on meats cooked over a blazing grill fueled by mesquite and oak.Composed plates, like a brick chicken served with hominy, tasso ham and green tomato chowchow, have their merit, but most diners direct their attention to an assortment of exceptional steaks. The meat's provenance is what sets the offerings apart: a partnership with a local rancher provides grass-fed, grain-finished cattle specifically for the restaurant's use, minimizing waste and maximizing flavor—and few would dispute the caliber of the end product.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
13470;Restaurant BT;USA;Tampa;2507 S. Macdill Ave., Tampa, 33629, USA;27.9228185;-82.4937336;61;false;true;Vietnamese, French;Both intimate and serene, this romantic retreat is restaurateur and Chef BT Nguyen's flagship. Its motto "eat local, think global" accurately captures both her genre-defying, eclectic cuisine as well as her dedication to high quality, local ingredients. Although the presentation may lean a bit fussy and old-fashioned (think tomato roses and other such twee garnishes), there's plenty of substance behind the fluff. This is cooking that's assiduously seasoned and bursting with flavor.Many of the dishes draw upon the chef's Vietnamese heritage, seen in the telltale use of bright, aromatic flavors, but items like a sophisticated vichyssoise and Basque-inspired pink prawns are a testament to her classic French training and time spent abroad.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
13472;Beauty & the Butcher;USA;Miami;6915 Red Rd., Miami, 33143, USA;25.7049125;-80.2852761;43;true;true;Contemporary, American;Away from his Miami Beach flagship, Chef Jeremy Ford brings his bold style to Coral Gables. A gleaming, square bar anchors the center of this attractive, sizeable restaurant styled with a floor-to-ceiling glass wine cellar and personalized wine lockers placed throughout the room. The menu is broad in its reach, swinging from jalapeno fritters to aged Japanese yellowtail with winter citrus and then right back to Florida with local snapper paired with Colombian chorizo. As expected, everything is made in-house, and no corners are cut. This is especially true of the Caesar salad, a triumphant tower of gem lettuce, snow peas, garlic sourdough and aged Parmesan. Much like the restaurant itself, it walks a fine line of comfort, creativity and class.;Air conditioning;[]
13473;Yummy House;USA;Tampa;2620 E. Hillsborough Ave., Tampa, 33610, USA;27.996141;-82.429634;34;true;false;Chinese, Dim Sum;Crowds still clamber to fill the seats at this spacious, no-frills eatery, whose sizable menu presents ample options for a range of tastes. Diners can find contentment with familiar American-Chinese staples, like orange chicken and salt-and-pepper fried calamari (or tofu). However, dishes like clay pot-braised fish have their own unique, earthy appeal. During lunch hours you’d be well-advised to select from the separate dim sum menu, which features typical bites like dumplings and turnip cakes, as well as sweet regional specialties like pineapple buns and Hong Kong-style egg tarts.Thanks to the popularity of the original, a number of offshoots can be found throughout southern Florida, including a more upscale one in South Tampa.;;[]
13475;Black Rooster Taqueria;USA;Orlando;1323 N. Mills Ave., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.562959;-81.3643146;18;true;true;Mexican;This Mills area dining den is brought to you by husband and wife team, John and Juliana Calloway. The space is compact and industrial with a smattering of local artwork and refurbished furniture, including sleek tables crafted by the chef himself. Colorful booths and a striking black rooster painted on the wall put patrons in the mood for correspondingly vibrant and eclectic taqueria food.Farm to taco is their ethos, and every item packs a wallop of flavor peppered with creativity. A recent favorite included the slow-roasted pork achiote taco, crowned with pickled onion, cilantro and spicy habanero salsa. The smoked greens taco—with ricotta, shiitake mushrooms and crispy onions—has vegetarians coming in droves.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
13477;Tori Tori;USA;Orlando;720 N. Mills Ave., Orlando, 32803, USA;28.5539463;-81.3646633;48;false;false;Japanese;Founded by Sean “Sonny” Nguyen, this Mills District concept is a classic izakaya offering bar bites, yakitori, as well as sake and creative libations. Unlike its sibling (Domu), this menu is varied and the trendy space is especially cutting-edge. Its name is painted on the side of the building and there's parking behind the restaurant. If that doesn't draw crowds from afar, the eclectic vibe and focused dishes certainly will. Start with skewers before moving on to grilled lamb chops, elevated with a mint-yogurt sauce, cherry tomatoes and diced cucumbers. A mound of fragrant fried rice may then show up mixed with sweet crab, notes of savory garlic and lemon essence.Reservations are not accepted, so arrive early or risk waiting in line.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
13480;Pizza Bruno;USA;Orlando;3990 Curry Ford Rd., Orlando, 32806, USA;28.5241442;-81.3353562;27;false;true;Pizza;Nestled into a strip mall, this mini spot flaunts big know-how on the art of pizza. Thanks to an A-frame ceiling, it doesn't feel cramped—inside find a small bar as well as a kitchen with a massive oven. Bright walls and plenty of windows give it all the neighborhood feels.This team appears to focus on turning out pizzas with creativity and flair, but bites like meatballs and garlic knobs make for a hearty start. Then move on to those wood-fired, Neapolitan-style pies, which are a sight for sore eyes—as in the Blanca with lemon ricotta, garlic, rosemary and mozz. While that age-old question of whether to add pineapple to pizza still remains, the 5-0 with speck, jalapeños and roasted pineapple sauce might just present the resounding answer—yes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13481;Sushi Yasu Tanaka;USA;Miami;140 N.E. 39th St., Ste. 241, Miami, 33137, USA;25.8124631;-80.192069;70;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;Advanced bookings, high price tags and dinner-only appear to be the usual foundations for sushiyas these days. Thank goodness then for Chef Yasu Tanaka, who brings his celebrated skills to this casual corner inside the MIA Market in the heart of the Design District. Nigiri is the sole focus of his carte, offered in multiple sets, made with top-quality fish flown in several times a week and adorned with clever garnishes. Exquisite bites, such as hotate with chimichurri and ebi dusted with lime zest, arrive in a flash so that speedy diners can be out the door in under 20 minutes.There is no ceremony or show inside this unassuming food hall, but the quality speaks for itself. With neighbors like Bulgari and Armani, perhaps we shouldn’t be too surprised.;Air conditioning;[]
13482;Kai Asian Street Fare;USA;Orlando;1555 State Rd. 436, Orlando, 32792, USA;28.6235582;-81.3152205;23;false;true;Asian;Opened in 2018, this restaurant is the brainchild of Thai-born Isra Sunhachawi and his Vietnamese brother-in-law, Quan Van. Found in a Winter Park shopping center, the space is tiny and simple, offering seating for a handful at a dark granite counter as well as at a few tables. Everything is freshly prepared, and the room quickly fills with the sounds and scents of the crew at work.The concise menu never loses focus, and regulars are well aware that it's all about stir-fried noodles and spicy Korean-style chicken wings. Ramen is also a treat, like the tonkotsu shio, featuring a richly flavored, slow-simmered pork bone broth, stocked with toothsome, thin and wavy noodles, slices of tender, lean pork belly, a shoyu egg and a host of other tasty additions.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13483;Joe's Stone Crab;USA;Miami Beach;11 Washington Ave., Miami Beach, 33139, USA;25.769113;-80.1351466;57;true;true;Seafood;When Joe Weiss opened his lunch counter in 1913, Miami Beach didn’t even have paved roads, and customers had to take the ferry to cross over. One century later, as high-rises and shopping districts blossomed all around, this restaurant has endured as one of the city’s prime attractions. Celebrities, politicians and locals alike make a beeline to this crustacean hot spot, now open year-round. And if the dedicated parking lot across the street is any clue, waits for a table here can get lengthy.Boiled, chilled and served with a signature mustard sauce, this seasonal specialty is also sustainable since crabs can regenerate their claws in around two years. End the meal with a refreshing, tart slice of key lime pie.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13484;Kaori;USA;Miami;871 S. Miami Ave., Miami, 33130, USA;25.7658958;-80.1932142;68;false;true;Asian, Japanese;Upscale Asian fusion menus are a dime a dozen in Magic City, but this attractive Brickell restaurant is a cut above the rest. Yes, there’s a DJ booth and yes, some entrees fly far north of $30 but there is style and substance to back it all up. The design features two stories of sleek concrete, wood furnishings and splashes of greenery with a handsome bar on the ground floor and the kitchen and dining room up top. The space is sized on the more intimate side and, fittingly so, the menu is equally well measured. Indulgent wagyu and foie gras gyoza arrive with picture-perfect searing, and bluefin tuna comes dressed in a sharp coconut-lime sauce. Entrees include Miyazaki A5 beef, Kurobuta pork, and local fish served in an electric curry.;Air conditioning;[]
13485;Krüs Kitchen;USA;Miami;3413 Main Hwy., Miami, 33133, USA;25.7276394;-80.2426489;75;true;true;Contemporary, Deli;This airy, glass-fronted restaurant blends in with the rest of its cool neighbors in the heart of bustling Coconut Grove. But take a closer look: At night, the space is a double-threat operation. On the ground floor, Chef Sebastián Vargas’s dinner-only Los Felix is in full swing. Up the winding staircase, you’ll discover a sunny space with a separate kitchen and retail offering that sources from small farms and takes aim at market-driven flavors and organic wines. Seafood is a frequent highlight, like grilled prawns with saffron sabayon or the reliably satisfying smoked coconut rice with wild caught crab and cilantro aioli. As an added bonus, a percentage of sales benefits the group’s nonprofit arm that aims to serve future community needs.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13486;Mise en Place;USA;Tampa;442 W. Kennedy Blvd., Tampa, 33606, USA;27.944789;-82.4652014;34;false;true;International, Contemporary;Originally a small-scale catering business founded in 1986 by partners Maryann Ferenc and Chef Marty Blitz, this riverfront enclave has gone on to become a local culinary fixture. The sleek, comfortable space and assured service are as suitable for romantic duos as business groups—and either set would be well advised to sample from their list of carefully poured classic cocktails.The menu features a freewheeling selection of international flavors—from squash blossoms filled with creamy ricotta and spicy 'nduja, to mole-crusted scallops with a masa and squash purée. Desserts in particular are noteworthy. A warm pistachio polenta cake paired with olive oil gelato and basil blackberry jam, for instance, manages to be both comforting and au courant.;Air conditioning;[]
13487;and/or;Belgium;Antwerpen;Haantjeslei 1, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.2039003;4.3975959;69;false;false;Vegan, Farm to table;Karen Shu's welcoming neighbourhood eatery has a stylish urban vibe reminiscent of New York City. Her plant-based cuisine is perfectly in tune with the times: crisp, light and bursting with exciting flavours. She has a taste for spiciness and umami, which she skilfully balances with herbs and acidity. Take the feta toast, for example, a popular choice from the à la carte menu: creamy vegan feta, a mildly spicy tomato salsa and young daikon sprouts for extra zing are served on toasted pain de mie with a subtle honey flavour. Every bite of this captivating cuisine leaves you craving more. The "/or" could really dropped from the name altogether!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13488;Soixante;Belgium;Berchem;Guldenvliesstraat 60, Berchem, 2600, Belgium;51.2018453;4.4331073;23;false;true;Creative;The window of this hip eatery extends an enticing invitation to step inside and the interior lives up to its promises with tightly packed tables and lashings of distinctive character. The chef has a weakness for veggies and seafood and enjoys surprising us with unexpected pairings and intriguing blends of earthy and acidic textures. He might flank a generous piece of brill with fermented tomatoes and salsifies or an exquisite sauce made out of brill bones and a meaty jus. Big-boned food in tune with the seasons.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13489;Feast;Belgium;Genk;Hoefstadstraat 23a, Genk, 3600, Belgium;50.9783518;5.4909803;91;true;true;Creative French;With Feast, Donaat and Guy have created a vintage-style haven where you come to relax and enjoy yourself. The presence of record players makes it clear that music is central to the experience here and you can even customise the background music with your own records. The menu features a variety of international dishes presented in tapas-sized portions. Think smörrebröd topped with scallops and kohlrabi, or oven-baked leek with a satay sauce – playful and packed with flavour, without a hint of pretentiousness. With a wide range of natural wines and well-known favourites, the wine list has plenty of gems in store.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13490;Ander;Belgium;Nieuwpoort;Potterstraat 15, Nieuwpoort, 8620, Belgium;51.1298126;2.7524236;90;false;false;Creative French;Fire is central to everything at this cosy home restaurant run by hostess Hermien and chef Arno. They have devised a set menu comprising four to six courses, showcasing local produce from the land and the sea. The chef imbues venison fillet with a distinct smoky flavour and serves it with a colourful red cabbage accompaniment. Fillet of Steenvoorde pigeon comes with a rich jus and a confit leg. Rest assured: this young couple knows how to show their diners a good time.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13491;POLLEN;Belgium;Wanze;Rue Naxhelet 1, Wanze, 4520, Belgium;50.5476938;5.2036777;71;false;true;Modern French;Surrounded by the gorgeous Meuse Valley, the Naxhelet estate boasts a golf course, a luxury hotel and this cosy restaurant. The natural beauty of the area is best appreciated from the terrace. Chef François Durand strives to maximise the use of local produce, often sourced from the sustainable projects of Terres du Val. His cuisine celebrates vegetables in all their glory. For example, he roasts pumpkin, crisps up the seeds and makes oil from the leaves. The dish is finished off perfectly with a subtly spicy Brillat-Savarin cheese sauce. At POLLEN, the flavours of the seasons come alive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13492;Cobra;Belgium;Antwerpen;Leopoldplaats 3, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2127609;4.4070588;22;true;false;Sharing, International;With its casual yet chic vibe, this lively establishment draws inspiration from the CoBrA art movement. A number of colourful pop art paintings command attention the moment you walk in. Behind the bar, the mixologist is at the ready. All manner of delicious dishes for sharing are served here from noon onwards. For example, you could start off with a lobster roll or pâté en croûte, then have Oedslach beef entrecôte as a main course and round off your meal with tarte Tatin. It's all possible here. No messing around, just simple, delicious flavours that will keep you coming back for more.;Terrace;[]
13493;De Gouden Muts;Belgium;Zoerle-Parwijs;Gevaertlaan 64, Zoerle-Parwijs, 2260, Belgium;51.0884111;4.8624;55;true;true;French Contemporary;This elegant villa is so cosy and inviting, and with the warm welcome extended by Evi, your charming maître d', you are sure to feel right at home. In the open kitchen, chef Rudy puts his own spin on French and Belgian recipes, adding in the requisite zing and occasional Japanese nuances. For instance, he uses miso to enhance flavours, but he also stays true to tradition with dishes such as pigeon cooked on the bone and served with beetroot and foie gras. He takes a detailed approach to his cooking, and his rich sauces are a key part of his dishes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13494;Basta!;Belgium;Wanze;chaussée de Tirlemont 118, Wanze, 4520, Belgium;50.540469;5.2214156;15;true;true;Italian, Modern French;The bright, contemporary dining room is the quintessence of Italian warmth and the garden terrace is ideal for alfresco dining when the weather is fine. Gianni Caruso allows his Sicilian heritage to run riot in dishes packed with exuberant flavours. He might season tartare of tuna with a delicate blend of ricotta, capers and lemon oil, unless you wouldn’t prefer a generous plate of risotto followed by Taglioni al tartufo… One thing is certain: the chef’s immaculate knowhow and craftsmanship do full justice to Mediterranean produce (the wine list is of the same ilk). Unadulterated pleasure is the name of the game at Basta!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13497;Kanzan;Japan;Kyoto;465-2 Senshojicho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8076, Japan;35.000002;135.762813;60;false;true;Japanese;Kazuma Yagi learned the spirit of devoted customer service at a succession of high-profile ryotei and ryokan. He thinks about his menus as he visits the fields of Shugakuin Imperial Villa in Kyoto. His vegetable takiawase impart the flavours of the season using the rich aroma of freshly harvested ingredients. The son of an antique store owner in Gion, Yagi also expresses the seasons through the elegant antique vessels on which he presents his dishes. Appetiser platters are served on rafts and baskets made by his own hands. Sincere devotion to details unseen by the eye underpins the cuisine here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13498;Sushi Kawano;Japan;Kyoto;72-8 Shimogamo Higashihangicho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-0824, Japan;35.044146;135.766825;96;false;true;Sushi;As a young man, Mitsutaka Kawano was a hurdler. Sushi preparation is much like hurdling, he says, as in both cases you try to deliver the best performance in the shortest possible time. Nigiri, a product of countless hours of forming practice, are relatively small, formed from relatively warm vinegared rice of just the right saltiness. The chef’s pet saying is that each day a sushi chef must improve his technique from the day before. In his quest for excellence, Mitsutaka Kawano will never stop hurdling.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13500;Le progrès;Japan;Osaka;2-1-13 Dojimahama, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0004, Japan;34.694683;135.494268;78;false;false;French;This restaurant was opened by a chef and a sommelier who had experienced the joys and sorrows of apprenticeship together. Valuing the pulse of the seasons, the chef composes his menu using seasonal ingredients, with the accent on seafood and vegetables. The kaiseki-style menu reflects the fusion of Japanese and French cultural influences, as do Japanese ingredients such as pike conger, milt and sudachi citrus. Le Progrès is a restaurant that ‘progresses’ through the passion of its two partners.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13503;Oku;Japan;Osaka;2-1-37 Katamachi, Miyakojima-ku, Osaka, 534-0025, Japan;34.694294;135.530018;94;false;false;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;The owner-chef opened a counter restaurant specialising in unagi after studying Japanese cuisine. The theme is ‘unagi and sake’, so the fare consists of the unagi set menu only. The menu uses fresh vegetables to impart seasonal moods. Ingredients are boiled, fried or straw-smoked for a unique sensibility. Unagi on rice brings the meal to a close, delighting the palate with rice freshly steamed in clay pots. The owner-chef’s experience also shines in the endless variety of vessels.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
13504;Benoit;Japan;Kyoto;The Hotel Seiryu Kyoto Kiyomizu, 2-204-2 Kiyomizu, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0862, Japan;34.997112;135.779255;28;true;true;French;Benoit opened as a bistro in Paris in 1912. Later Alain Ducasse took over the reins and brought the spirit of ‘good old Benoit’ to Kyoto. The fare consists of familiar favourites such as pâté en croûte, duck confit and millefeuille. Though the walls are glass, the roof is tiled for a touch of Kyoto style and the dining room has a certain Parisian charm. Along with its views of Yasaka Pagoda, it creates a pleasing blend of French and Japanese in the ancient capital.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13505;UPSTAIRZ;Japan;Osaka;2F, Zentis Osaka, 1-4-26 Dojimahama, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0004, Japan;34.695666;135.496368;96;true;true;French;All-day dining supervised by the chef of Craftale in Tokyo. The extensive menu is based on French cuisine. For lunch, Western-style curries, vegan salads and other casual fare are served. At dinnertime the menu switches to snacks, à la carte items and an authentic, modern French prix fixe. With each dish, the chef aims to raise the bar a notch or two, hence the name ‘Upstairz’.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13507;Shunten Shin;Japan;Osaka;3-8-10 Ueshio, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0002, Japan;34.665574;135.516878;46;true;true;Tempura;For this owner-chef, the tempura must have a refined aroma and not be oily, so the batter is applied thinly and the cooking oil used is mainly sesame and corn oil. Red aubergine is not soaked with oil all the way through, to preserve its vibrant juiciness. Asparagus tips and stalks are served at different times, calculated to ensure the right firmness for each. The most famous among them is the bowl of rice topped with tempura made from egg yolk, and raw uni.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13508;Le Caneton;Japan;Osaka;2-6-23 Uehommachinishi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0062, Japan;34.674065;135.518023;48;true;true;French;The name is French for ‘duckling’, reflecting the chef’s passionate pursuit of duck and foie gras cuisine. He places the accent on prix fixe, the better to ensure perfection in each dish. Playful amuse-bouche are dramatically presented on a high-tea stand. For the main course, Osaka duck is naturally de rigueur. His wife, the pâtissière of the establishment, flexes her talents in the dessert department.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13509;Kasane;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 1-2-14 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.696386;135.498674;38;true;false;Izakaya;The dish Toyama native chef offers as his speciality is oden. Typically for Osaka, his is salty, to make a fitting companion for sake. Ma-kombu and katsuo-bushi exude a rich umami. The sardine dumplings look like they belong in a kaiseki soup. The items are abundantly varied: potatoes are seasoned with soy sauce flavour, for example. To wrap up the meal, udon in oden dashi is served. Etchu sake is brought in from his native prefecture, showing his love for his hometown.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13510;Hachiraku;Japan;Kyoto;428-5 Kamibentencho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0822, Japan;35.000196;135.778449;59;false;false;Chinese;‘Urban Chinese’ that uses no garlic or lard. The starting point for Hachiraku is the spirit of graceful service as only the ancient capital can offer, so these ingredients are banned to prevent odours from transferring to the kimono of gentlemen, geishas and maikos. The chef applies the richness of top-grade soup stock to his cuisine to good effect. Stir-fries are paired with wasabi, fried rice with Kyoto pickled vegetables. Spice use is restrained, as befits the urbane refinement of Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13511;Pontocho Masuda;Japan;Kyoto;200 Shimokorikicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8016, Japan;35.005793;135.771054;77;true;false;Obanzai;The mood is the Showa era, when Pontocho was a much sleepier place. Two generations, father and son, man the kitchen, displaying their talents in ryotei cooking. ‘Obanzai’, a style of cooking beloved by Kyoto families, exudes the warmth and familiarity of the good old days. Side dishes are simply simmered and unadorned: okara (soy pulp), hijiki (black seaweed), nishin-nasu (Pacific herring with eggplant). Grilled seafood and seasonal stews are popular. ‘Daimyotaki’, dried daikon pickled and simmered in dashi, was born of the wisdom of previous generations.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13512;Kitashinchi Okurano;Japan;Osaka;3F, 1-3-23 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697836;135.496137;54;true;true;Japanese;The menu, incorporating seasonal ingredients when available, changes each month. The head chef, whose passion is cuisine that sparks conversation, respects tradition while sneaking a little playfulness into his menus. Even familiar items are presented with ingenuity. The crab croquettes, for example, are suffused with the aroma of toasted crab shells to add the flavour of baked crab to the creamy fillings. The counter sports a stylish, modern design. Five private rooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13514;Yakitori Matsuri;Japan;Osaka;2-2-33 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.69735;135.494939;27;false;false;Yakitori;The restaurant stands on the site of Yakitori Ichimatsu, the restaurant where the chef apprenticed, hence the name – a word formed by taking one character from Ichimatsu and one from the word meaning ‘hometown’. The omakase menu begins with flavour-rich chicken ham. Seasoning shifts from salty to sweet dipping sauce, offering a variation from light to rich flavours. Yakitori chicken is delicate, gauged according to the size of the chunks when bitten and the texture on the teeth.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13515;Nonkiya Mune;Japan;Kyoto;127-5 Kinuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0804, Japan;35.015181;135.76339;24;true;false;Izakaya;In picture-perfect Kyoto style, Nonkiya Mune is tucked away at the end of a long blind alley. As you enter, the friendly owner-chef and his mother greet you. The heart and soul of the menu is fish and shellfish in season. The preparation of the fish as sashimi, grilled, sakamushi or other style is tailored to each type. Friendly service makes this restaurant easy to love, so naturally many of the customers are locals. Enjoy the harmonious atmosphere that enfolds you in this izakaya.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13517;Hirosawa;Japan;Kyoto;183 Fudocho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8215, Japan;35.006192;135.756155;91;false;false;Chinese;Creative Chinese cuisine with the ambience of a Japanese villa. The cheerful sound of woks being tossed around reverberates in the interior. Fearful of wearing out guests’ tastebuds, the chef seasons with a light touch, drawing on his experience in Cantonese cooking. Oven-roasted pork fillet is a case in point. Ingredients suffused with premium shang tang Chinese soup stock to create soups and ankake served in hot clay pots are a Hirosawa trademark. The restaurant is a forum for his self-expression, so the chef named it after himself.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13518;Raiz;Japan;Kyoto;21-4 Murasakino Kamimonzencho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8217, Japan;35.044526;135.748535;19;false;false;Contemporary;The cuisine inherits a modern Spanish pedigree. The message is the delicious flavour of freshly picked vegetables. Raiz partners with local farmers to deliver the aroma and vibrancy of freshly harvested produce. Dishes are arranged with a simple, modern sensibility that puts the ingredients in the spotlight. The restaurant’s name means ‘roots’ in Spanish, and it is putting down roots in the Murasakino region and showcasing the appeal of the area’s produce.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13520;Asador ROCA;Japan;Osaka;2-6-4 Hiranomachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0046, Japan;34.687559;135.503711;93;true;true;Spanish;Asador ROCA offers a pairing prix fixe menu, showcasing Spanish food culture in all its delightful variety. Cuisine drawing on the uniqueness of the Basque region makes effective use of paprika and chilli. Combining the bounty of land and sea, asado of mushrooms and shrimp works its magic by forming a connection with the chef’s native Itoshima, hemmed between mountain and ocean. Hometown memories, nature, people he’s met – the chef’s life experiences are understood on a deeper level through his flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13521;Yassan;Japan;Kyoto;347 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0073, Japan;35.004776;135.775782;15;false;true;Beef;This restaurant is currently operating in a temporary location for renovation. Address: 271-2-5 Giommachi Kitagawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto.Yassan is a meat kappo of long renown. The shop is busy night after night, filling up as soon as the shop curtain is posted outside. Staff use German as a sort of code, calling tongue ‘Zunge’, heart ‘Herz’, stomach ‘Magen’ and so on. The practice began at a time when many of its regulars were German physicians. ‘Yassan’ is an affectionate contraction of the restaurant’s original owner-chef’s name, ‘Yasuo-san’. Calabashes hang from the rafters around the counter, recalling that Yasuo-san liked sake in these gourds.;Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13523;Shintaro;Japan;Osaka;2-5-5 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.695136;135.501828;16;true;true;Tempura;The eye is drawn to the two cooks frying tempura, standing side-by-side in front of their pot. The owner-chef skilfully wreathes each piece in batter and slips it into the oil. The fry cook focuses exclusively on adjusting the flame. Working in sync, the two cooks produce tempura wrapped in a thin yet flavoursome coating. Seasoning with salt further highlights the item’s flavour. Shintaro jealously preserves the methods of its founder, striving to maintain a flavour unchanged in decades.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13524;Tempura Mizuki;Japan;Kyoto;B1F, The Ritz-Carlton, Kyoto, 543 Hokodencho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0902, Japan;35.013704;135.770876;71;false;true;Tempura;Ingredients are presented before frying begins: vegetables from Takagamine and Shūgakuin, seafood from Awaji and Shizuoka. Safflower oil is used to achieve a light tempura coating. While some items, such as shrimp and conger eel, are fried on their own, other items are ingeniously paired, such as sesame tofu with sea urchin, wagyu with perilla leaf, and egg yolk with caviar. Gracious hospitality accompanies.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
13525;Okuniya Mambei;Japan;Kyoto;534 Kikuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8127, Japan;35.005215;135.763337;31;true;false;Unagi / Freshwater Eel;The chef opened Okuniya Mambei as the third-generation owner-chef of a river-fish restaurant in Nishiki Market. He realised his dream with the help of architects, calligraphers and potters. Décor of rustic simplicity, bold and vigorous calligraphy and tricolour earthenware pots exude a unique personality. The menu consists only of large kabayaki on rice. Eel is grilled with the fat intact and served with rice freshly cooked in an earthenware pot. In true Kyoto style, the leftover rice is topped with eel tsukudani (a preserve using sweetened soy sauce) and hojicha (roasted green tea) is poured over it.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
13526;Ryo Kawashima;Japan;Kyoto;333-2 Nushiyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0843, Japan;35.011805;135.760271;92;true;false;Japanese;As the stage for his culinary performances, Ryo Kawashima refurbished an old row house. Envisaging his eatery as an intimate gathering with a host and guests, he laid it out with no boundary between counter seating and kitchen. Drawing of dashi stock and arrangement of foodstuffs are done directly in front of customers, by Kawashima alone. His concept is to trust intuition while constantly inventing and improving. The restaurant’s name means (roughly) ‘food’ and is homonymous with Kawashima’s given name: Ryo no ryori, ‘Ryo’s cooking’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13527;Senda;Japan;Kyoto;1038-16 Kamiyagawacho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-8384, Japan;35.027645;135.733747;77;true;false;Japanese;Ryuji Senda’s parents ran an eel restaurant in Fukui. Having helped with the family business from a young age, the path of a chef came naturally to him, and he made his way to Kyoto as his father and elder brother had apprenticed there. At dinner the pièce de resistance is the elegant appetiser. Senda learned from his mentors such points as how to use fresh ingredients in season and the origins and meanings of arrangements. The eel kabayaki, basted with sauce from the family recipe before broiling, is not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13529;Miyawaki;Japan;Kyoto;122-1 Shikiamicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8261, Japan;35.010035;135.753714;48;true;true;Japanese;Japanese decor with Scandinavian chairs creates a harmonious modern Japanese interior. The chef respects the boundaries of Japanese cuisine while overlaying some creative touches. Tsukuri are dressed with salted kombu, enhancing umami. Tofu skin is grated and incorporated into pureed soup, coaxing out its sweetness. Pairing of fish and vegetables with fruit adds a lightness for a modern sensibility. Ingenious, yet true to the native flavours of the ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13531;Le Nez;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-3-29 Higashishinsaibashi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0083, Japan;34.674317;135.505795;76;false;true;French;Hideyo Dezaki draws seasonal scenes using finger foods. His set menu, themed around a given aroma, begin with an amuse-gueule called ‘Hakoniwa’ or ‘miniature garden.’ Dezaki uses ingredients from his native Wakayama Prefecture, conveying his memories of home through scent. One example is the consommé, which combines foie gras, symbolic of French cuisine, with plums from his native Minabe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13534;Le cadeau;Japan;Kyoto;541-25 Suemarucho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0901, Japan;35.016611;135.770219;25;false;true;French;Shinji Imoto apprenticed in Italian cuisine, but his desire to study sauces led him to French cooking. Fascinated by its depth and subtlety, Chef Imoto soon switched fully to French cuisine. He prizes combinations of familiar fare, such as apples paired with boudin noir sausages, navy beans with bacon, and oysters with spinach. The restaurant’s name means ‘The Gift’, and each dish brings to guests the chef’s devotion to his craft.;Air conditioning;[]
13536;Niomon MUI;Japan;Kyoto;41-1 Shimmarutacho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-8386, Japan;35.011862;135.773193;27;false;false;Japanese;Recalling the words of his mentor, ‘a chef must have a gentle spirit’, the chef devotes himself to his craft. To encourage patrons to trust him, he taught himself to be attentive to their needs and run a customer-first restaurant, in true kappo style. The menu is crammed with items, from reimagined dishes to simple preparations. ‘Mui’ in the shop’s name means ‘no contrivances, everything natural’. It’s fun to leave everything to the master and go with the flow.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13537;Tosara;Japan;Osaka;2-7-26 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.69597;135.502149;54;false;true;Contemporary, Italian;The name means ‘ten-plate cuisine,’ derived from a book that became the chef’s guiding principle. He expresses insights drawn from Italian cuisine, his hometown roots in Awajishima and the appeal of his producers in the form of a ten-plate prix fixe. The plate of straw-grilled wagyu with fermented onions incorporates memories of his farmer parents. A local potter supplies pots and dishes. Cuisine born of solidarity with family and region tells the story of this chef’s life.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13538;Takocho;Japan;Kyoto;1-237 Miyakawasuji, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0801, Japan;35.00201;135.771618;21;true;false;Oden;This oden speciality shop has been in business for four generations, since the Meiji period (1880s-90s). The owner-chef in his bow tie and proprietress in her apron greet guests as they enter. Oden is seasoned with light dashi soup stock tinged with kombu kelp. Octopus (the ‘Tako’ in ‘Takocho’ means ‘octopus’), tofu skin and daikon radish are popular items. Ask about items not on the menu and start a conversation. A grilled octopus onigiri rice ball and chazuke in oden soup draws the meal to a close. Dashi drawn from a wide variety of sources adds depth to the flavour.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13539;Jikiba Ono;Japan;Kyoto;2-267 Miyagawasuji, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0801, Japan;35.00108;135.771418;100;true;false;Japanese;‘Jikiba’ is the name of the region in Amakusa, Kumamoto, where the chef was born. Attesting to the richness of the seas of Kyūshū, seafood is sourced from local waters and from the Bungo Channel. To bring out the goodness, seasoning is minimal. Appetisers, decoratively arranged sashimi and soup dishes are all decided by the chef, out of a determination to impart the flavours of the season. After these, grilled and stewed items can be selected from the menu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13540;Être à l'aise;Japan;Osaka;1-26-2 Uemachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0005, Japan;34.675969;135.521654;83;true;true;French;The intimate dining space wraps you in the warmth exuded by the couple at its heart. The chef’s cuisine and the wine pairings of his sommelier wife are a perfect match. French duck and lamb are dressed in rich sauces, their flavours supported by patiently prepared consommé and soup stock. The couple work in tandem like a well-oiled machine to put their guests at ease.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13541;Claro;Japan;Osaka;4-18 Matsuyamachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0067, Japan;34.674214;135.512341;51;true;true;Spanish;The chef creates modern Spanish fare with Japanese ingredients. Uniting two cultures, the chef combines foodstuffs like tortillas with seaweed, while other dishes feature elements such as sherry sauce and Daitokuji natto. Paella made with Japanese rice is another example: ingredients such as firefly squid, eel and crab tell of each season. The all-black interior is stylishly appointed with modern art. While lacking a bright mood during the daytime, it is nicely relaxing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13542;Nominokoji Yamagishi;Japan;Kyoto;293-1 Shimohakusancho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8085, Japan;35.009717;135.7657;56;false;true;Izakaya;The chef borrows the good points of both kappo and izakaya places. Typical appetisers, soup dishes, shiizakana (kaiseki drinking snacks) and vegetables are offered along with whatever guests choose from the menu. Choices range widely from Japanese fare such as potato salad with smoked daikon pickles and stir-fried noodles with squid to Chinese items like crispy pork and gyoza dumplings. The name Nominokoji, ‘drinker’s alley’, is a play on Tominokoji, the pub that is this eatery’s parent. Cuisine with a playful spirit, accompanied by delicious spirits.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13543;Oryori Maeshiro;Japan;Kyoto;234 Owaricho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0934, Japan;35.01254;135.765853;97;false;false;Japanese;In the Kyoto dialect, ‘monmona-ryori’ means ‘as it is’. As with ‘kinari-ryori’ in Osaka, fussy over-preparation is avoided. The Osaka-apprenticed chef takes to heart the words of his mentor: ‘light, sweet and deep’, and let the ingredients do the talking. Though the custom at a Kyoto kappo is to do the cooking in the back, here the chef displays all his skills for guests to see.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13544;Tsuroku;Japan;Kyoto;51 Matsuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0831, Japan;35.013703;135.761845;73;false;true;Japanese;The name derives from an old Kyoto word meaning ‘balance’ or ‘harmony’. Simple arrangements and friendly service make for a pleasant experience. The decision to make all menu items à la carte was taken so customers could drop in casually. The head chef excels in wanmono (dishes served in small bowls) using shinjo, as well as fried foods. Guji knife-scored to look pinecone-like and grilled and bowls of white miso soup are standard fare and quintessentially Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13545;Kitashinchi Shien;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-7-19 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.69736;135.499911;73;false;true;Yakitori;Only prix fixe menus using chicken from Kyushu, prized for its quality, richness and texture, are available. Appetisers and stews, served first, are meticulously prepared, worthy of a much more formal restaurant. Zucchini smothered in Italian cheese suggests snow-clad landscapes of purest white. Chicken wings are lightly scored to make them easier to eat. A serving of white rice brings the meal to a close.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13546;Jizakeya Iwatsuki;Japan;Osaka;4-6-19 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0041, Japan;34.703483;135.511771;50;true;true;Izakaya;In a restaurant lined with local sakes from every part of Japan, owner-chef Hiroki Iwatsuki pursues a concept he calls ‘cooking that makes you want to have a drink’. Potato salad with octopus, braised burdock root with squid, finely minced fish with takuan: this is reworked home cooking to tickle the palate of tipplers. The fish is simmered in the sake of the diner’s choice to enhance its umami. To close, the gentleness of congee steamed in grated daikon soothes the stomach.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
13547;Kappo Shinatomi;Japan;Kyoto;315-4 Shintomicho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-0875, Japan;35.017725;135.767823;87;true;false;Japanese;Keen to earn the affection of locals, the chef named his restaurant after the ancient word for this part of Kyoto. Offerings are determined by customers’ à la carte preferences, the chef’s omakase menus, and how he feels that day. The quality of the seafood Kappo Shinatomi sources is top-notch, so we recommend the sashimi assortment. Boiled greens redolent with bonito stock and stewed dishes warm the soul. The meal ends with sweets prepared by the lady of the house. The couple’s personality is stamped on the ambience of this kappo restaurant.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13548;Masaki;Japan;Kyoto;15-20 Mibu Bambacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8805, Japan;35.008013;135.744641;47;true;false;Japanese;As an apprentice, Shunsuke Masaki learned about the kaleidoscope of flavours that could be generated by combining ingredients. Today, Masaki uses those skills to pursue a cuisine all his own. Many dishes in small bowls, are soups of pureed vegetables. Multiple soup stocks, such as basic soup stock, clam stock and chicken stock, are combined to produce richly layered umami. Accompanied by rice, dried fish fry is mainly seasoned with pepper, but shredded dried plum is sometimes used for a twist.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13549;middle;Japan;Kyoto;5-3 Shimogamo Kamigawaracho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-0812, Japan;35.0441;135.763488;77;false;true;Contemporary;The Kamo River provides a serene backdrop to this house near Kitaoji Bridge. Inspired to become a chef in Paris, the chef studied French cooking in Osaka and Japanese cuisine in Kyoto. This life story is evident in his prix fixe menus, which blur the boundaries between Western and Japanese gastronomy. Sauces are lovingly prepared, fish and meat grilled over charcoal flame. The style is freely expressive, with hints of Middle Eastern and South American influences scattered here and there.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13550;TAVERNETTA da KITAYAMA;Japan;Osaka;1-6 Ishigatsujicho, Tennoji-ku, Osaka, 543-0031, Japan;34.664805;135.523061;75;true;true;Italian;In Italian, ‘tavernetta’ denotes a casual eatery, so the atmosphere here is informal and relaxing. Traditional Italian fare is listed on a blackboard. Tripe stewed in tomato, marlin baked in herb-seasoned breadcrumbs and mushroom pappardelle offer the flavours of a village in the north of Italy. The signature dish is beef, pork or lamb grilled in slabs. The menu changes based on supply. Servings are big enough for two, making them nice to share.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13551;Shuhaku;Japan;Kyoto;392 Kinencho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0828, Japan;34.99862;135.778717;66;true;false;Japanese;In his early days as a cook, Nobuhisa Yoshida learned a freewheeling approach not beholden to any particular format, so the sensibilities of both French and Japanese cuisine play their parts in his menus. Steamed fish with grated turnip, chub mackerel sushi and rice cooked on a traditional stove called an okudosan (or kamado) are Kyoto to the hilt. French ideas are evidenced in abalone foie gras and black soybean Mont Blanc. This conversation between two food cultures results in an eclectic blend.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13552;Kosai Fukumimi;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-1-8 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.696528;135.500302;48;true;false;Chinese;The enduring appeal of Cantonese cuisine stems from its breadth, in terms of both ingredients used and how it is prepared. The chef’s forte is seafood. Hong Kong grouper and filefish are steamed or stir-fried. The stewing of ‘ham yui’, fish pickled in salt and dried in the sun, together with chicken and tofu is trademark Guangdong. In a unique touch, mapo tofu is combined with shirako and oysters. Eager to reproduce the flavours of Hong Kong, the owner-chef uses jasmine rice.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13553;Kappo Takohachi;Japan;Kyoto;498 Higashigawacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8046, Japan;35.006216;135.767048;96;true;true;Japanese;The ambience of mid-20th-century Japan remains along Takoyakushi Street. The cooking is as nostalgic as the shop, both a legacy from the chef’s father. Customers sit shoulder to shoulder while the owner couple work in perfect sync. The intimate space shortens the distance between people, enfolding all present in a harmonious mood. On the menu, only ingredients are listed: sea bream, squid, octopus. Ask the chef for that day’s recommendation—all part of the fun.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13554;Shoroku;Japan;Osaka;1-16-18 Utsubohommachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0004, Japan;34.684744;135.494629;86;true;true;Japanese;It’s said that “Kyoto flavours are natural, but Osaka flavours are deep”. Masato Shimoda’s menu expresses the goodness in both. Crab cream croquettes stuffed in abalone shells combine the ingenuity of both cities, using the creative flair of Osaka as a base while bringing native flavours to the fore in true Kyoto style. Working in the kitchen alongside his father, Masato pours the skills and spirit he inherits into his dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13556;YOSHOKU OGATA;Japan;Kyoto;32-1 Tojijicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0956, Japan;35.012454;135.764055;18;false;false;Yoshoku;‘A kappo-style yoshoku restaurant to satisfy the heart as well as the stomach’ is the concept here. The chef converses with guests at the counter while pouring all his skills into his food preparation. Determined to satisfy, he never compromises on quality, sourcing ingredients from a butcher in Shiga, a fishmonger in Shizuoka, and a farmer in Kyoto. Old yoshoku favourites such as deep-fried horse mackerel, sautéed pork and hamburger steak are popular. Flame technique and sauces draw on the chef’s experience with French cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13557;Kamekichi;Japan;Osaka;1-3-13 Yariyamachi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 540-0027, Japan;34.682689;135.515553;65;false;false;French;The chef wanted his guests to feel comfortable around him, so he named his restaurant after his own nickname. French country favourites fill the menu, including quiche Lorraine, cassoulet and beef cheek simmered in red wine. Game in season, such as mallard and Daurian partridge, are a delight. À la carte items at dinner are generously portioned for sharing. Sauces prepared with liberal amounts of butter and cream are the true pleasure of French cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13558;Gion Yamagishi;Japan;Kyoto;570-154 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002518;135.775697;81;false;false;Japanese;The air of a tea arbour lingers in this kappo. Amid the spare furnishings, the staff take care to provide a comfortable dining experience. In a bid to make Japanese cuisine approachable, in addition to an omakase set meal, à la carte ordering is also available. In the evening, a prix fixe assortment is provided to which à la carte items can be added. At lunch, eager to acquaint guests with its dashi soup stock, the restaurant serves udon using Kujo leek or tofu skin. Appetisers and Kyoto sushi are also included in a welcome addition.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
13560;Kinari;Japan;Osaka;4-17-15 Temma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0043, Japan;34.695875;135.513968;33;true;false;Japanese;Kinari means ‘simple, unvarnished, in its natural state’. The owner-chef strives as far as possible not to season his dishes, letting the ingredients do the talking. Takiawase and ohitashi boiled greens, prepared with minimal seasoning and the lightest of dashi soup stock, are prime examples. Decoratively arranged sashimi is prepared not with rigid insistence on dipping in soy sauce but by pairing with complementary items. The bounty of nature, enhanced with a few subtle twists.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13561;Nikuryori Shibuya;Japan;Kyoto;193-1 Nishikodocho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0904, Japan;35.014866;135.768535;80;true;true;Beef;Chef has been in the wagyu business for over half a century. He does not favour any particular region, prizing quality over brand. The menu starts with items that take full advantage of the freshness of their ingredients, such as tongue and heart. Parboiled tripe is followed by Yanagawa-style sirloin. It’s omakase, but customers can add items from the menu. The old-fashioned townhouse seems the perfect ambience for immersing in the world of wagyu. The banter between the kitchen craftsman father and the amiable hostess daughter is heartwarming.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
13562;Kyochuka Makisada;Japan;Kyoto;565-5 Kawaracho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0827, Japan;35.012305;135.762202;51;true;true;Chinese;The brothers who run Kyochuka Makisada are following in the footsteps of their father, who was a chef at a Chinese restaurant. The sign beside the shop curtain was written by their father, a gift to celebrate their start of a new life. The “sada” part is common to both brothers’ names. The elder brother runs the kitchen, while the younger brother handles service. The counter is the place to sit to watch the spectacle of dishes being prepared, such as sizzling Peking duck. The brothers’ passion is driven by the family tie that binds them.;Air conditioning,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13563;Chugokusai S.Sawada;Japan;Osaka;4-6-28 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.696264;135.505146;31;true;true;Chinese;The omakase is a feast of cuisine learned in Hong Kong but with Japanese and Western elements mixed in. For example, the chef learned to prepare crispy chicken in Hong Kong but now adds grated daikon radish with red vinegar, wasabi and other twists for a unique character. Burger of foie gras caramelised in Shaoxing wine is a unique menu item that applies French techniques. Old friends such as dim sum, mapo tofu and dandan noodles are offered, so there is plenty of variety.;Air conditioning;[]
13564;Sushisho Nehachi;Japan;Osaka;4-1-70 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.691096;135.483948;80;false;false;Sushi;The delightfully varied omakase menu begins with a snack. Bright perilla spikes and grilled soy marinated fish show the chef’s experience. Nigiri is painstakingly crafted, sparing neither effort nor inventiveness. Clams are broiled to a pungent fragrance, sweet shrimp comes with roe marinated in soy sauce. The vinegar for the rice is coupled with roasted sesame seeds for an inviting aroma. The name means ‘sushi smile’, conveying the chef’s desire that patrons enjoy the restaurant in a relaxed mood.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13567;Kitashinchi Kushikatsu Bon;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 1-3-16 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.696599;135.497094;81;true;true;Kushiage;Kitashinchi Kushikatsu Bon serves skewers of unstinting luxury, including chateaubriand and foie gras. Creative combinations of delicacies, such as ‘pregnant kombu’ (kombu kelp with Pacific herring roe attached) with sea urchin and caviar or name-brand pork with truffles, are especially fun. To ensure a light palate, items are coated in powder-fine breadcrumbs and deep-fried in cottonseed oil. Osaka soul food, enriched with uniquely conceived ingredients.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13568;OSTERIA IL CANTO DEL MAGGIO;Japan;Kyoto;512-2 Kikuyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8127, Japan;35.005889;135.763225;39;false;false;Italian;An Italian eatery specialising in the flavours of Tuscan cuisine. The name and menu alike are an heirloom from the chef’s apprentice days. Located in the mountains outside Florence, the restaurant where Takashi Tamura learned his trade did not offer fish dishes, so nor does Tamura. Crostini of chicken liver, pappardelle of duck broth, steak à la Florentine: his dishes convey the flavours of Tuscany in homage to where he trained.;Air conditioning;[]
13569;Nijo Aritsune;Japan;Kyoto;694-3 Chojiyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0935, Japan;35.013675;135.766674;43;false;false;Izakaya;Billing itself as ‘a kappo for grown-ups’, Nijo Aritsune maintains a dignified tenor while offering a broad range of à la carte items. While elaborate dishes are the establishment’s forte, familiar friends such as chargrilled chicken meatballs and croquettes are on offer too. In a fresh take on rice topped with raw egg, only the whites of the eggs are whipped. ‘Aritsune’ means ‘changing so that things will not change’. An evolution of Japanese cuisine through a modern sensibility.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13571;Gion Rakumi;Japan;Kyoto;570-206 Giommachi Minamigawa, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0074, Japan;35.002699;135.776619;49;false;false;Japanese;‘Delicious, fun flavours’ is Gion Rakumi’s motto. The bustling of the amiable young cooks in the kitchen is a pleasing sight. Items are à la carte but no set formula is followed, so there’s no menu. Instead, guests choose ingredients from a wooden box and consult with the chef on preferred ways of preparation. Being a Gion Sasaki-run place, the quality of ingredients is uncompromising. The playfulness of presentation and pub-like joviality make the mood cheerful and lively.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13575;Yiwanshui;Japan;Osaka;2-6-13 Utsubohommachi, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0004, Japan;34.68322;135.48991;25;true;true;Chinese;The characters on the sign read ‘tàocān’, meaning ‘set menu’ in Chinese. Keen to become their customers’ habitual haunt, Yiwanshui serves Chinese home cooking. Jiǔ cǎi pén on the prix fixe menu is influenced by Chinese imperial court cuisine. The approach here is to use familiar ingredients and take the time and effort to bring their native goodness to the fore. A light touch on the oil and seasonings makes the fare easy on the constitution and places natural flavours front and centre.;Air conditioning;[]
13576;Doshincho Washoku Zui;Japan;Osaka;2-4-13 Doshin, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0035, Japan;34.702368;135.513967;66;true;true;Japanese;‘Zui’ means ‘fresh and lively’, which applies equally well to both fare and chef. His cheerful personality and energetic expression reflect his passion for cuisine and service. As a restaurateur who studied in Kyoto, the chef makes Rishiri kombu and light-coloured dried bonito flakes the foundation on which he works. Each dish is restricted to just two ingredients, so each component leaves a strong impression. He is especially adept at pairing ingredients with their own dashi, as seen in the sea bream sashimi accompanied by a jellied broth of sea bream dashi.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13577;Jikon Hiratate;Japan;Kyoto;352-1 Shoshoiotabicho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0873, Japan;35.015593;135.760216;43;false;true;Japanese;The fare here isn’t omakase but it isn’t really à la carte either. Instead, in a trend that seems to be growing, a few de rigueur items are supplemented by dishes of the guest’s choice. We recommend the shiraae (salad dressed with white sesame, miso and tofu) in season. Jikon in the restaurant’s name means ‘live with all your heart in this moment’. This is a restaurant that focuses single-mindedly on cuisine, heart and soul.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13579;Yakitori Matsuoka;Japan;Osaka;1-4-17 Tohei, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0063, Japan;34.669882;135.51834;82;true;true;Yakitori;Cuisine rich with the fertile imagination of Hiroki Matsuoka expresses a spirit of relentless curiosity. Free-range chickens from Kagoshima are aged to draw out their flavour. In addition to the usual salt and sauce, the chef brushes yakitori with a fragrant oil he prepares himself. The menu intersperses skewers with chicken items such as stews and soups. Meals wrap up with rice served in earthenware pots or ramen in chicken broth. Admiring the chef’s skill and forwards-looking imagination is part of the fun.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13580;WASHOKU TOKU;Japan;Kyoto;45-1 Murasakino Kamimonzencho, Kita-ku, Kyoto, 603-8217, Japan;35.04509;135.748545;23;true;false;Japanese;À la carte is the focus, so guests can freely sample the cuisine of the season. The menu ranges widely, beguiling diners with items from appetisers to more creative offerings. The sashimi plate is garnished with green peppercorns. Refreshing flavours draw out the sweetness of seafood. ‘Kamo Wasa’, quick-boiled duck tenderloin, draws inspiration from the yakitori technique. The wide range of items includes rice dishes, donburi, rice soup and fried rice. The flexibility to make portions larger or smaller is much appreciated.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13581;Kyoryori Hachisei;Japan;Kyoto;15-2 Chudoji Maedacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8804, Japan;34.9950648;135.7474885;60;false;true;Japanese;Akiyuki Hasegawa learned from his mentor that good cooking comes from sincerity. His devotion to great dining is what sends him to the market every morning to check the ingredients. He constantly tinkers with his menu to ensure that guests can enjoy his fare no matter how many times they come. The appetisers are just as how his mentor prepared them. Meals end with takikomi-gohan (rice cooked together with other ingredients) because he loves its colourful appearance when he lifts the lid.;Air conditioning;[]
13582;Yakitori Kyoto Tachibana;Japan;Kyoto;B1F, 612 Tachibanacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0944, Japan;35.012102;135.76593;42;false;false;Yakitori;Tomonori Sakata turned his attention from Japanese cuisine to yakitori when he fell in love with Kyotamba chicken. Many dishes are served wrapped in skin, because of its tenderness and to bring out the flavour of the fat. Unique inspirations from Japanese cuisine include chicken meat marinated in kombu broth and chicken meatballs mixed with takikomi-gohan. In a clever twist, yakitori is served atop vegetables, which absorb flavour from the many types of skewer placed on top of them, then are grilled last.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13583;OIMATSU Tempura Suzuki;Japan;Osaka;4-4-2 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697364;135.505291;89;true;false;Tempura;The tempura here shows an awareness of the start and end of each ingredient’s season, reflecting the chef’s experience in Japanese cuisine. Thinly battered items are lightly fried in safflower oil to convey their flavour plainly and honestly. Tiger prawn and cod milt are wrapped in perilla leaves for added fragrance. Wagyu fillet is grilled to a rosy pink with consummate skill. Red pickled ginger added to kakiage (all-in-one seafood and vegetable tempura blend) is a unique touch that is pure Osaka.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13584;Luca;Japan;Kyoto;2F, 585 Takamiyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8056, Japan;35.005554;135.764965;30;false;true;French;The restaurant name comes from lucas, ‘bringer of light’ in Latin, out of chef’s desire to make it a place of bright smiles. He strives to create fare based on the classic French cuisine which so impressed him during his apprenticeship, while keeping the flavours light. Food is served colourfully garnished with vegetables of Kyoto in season. The fare is both creative and richly expressive.;Air conditioning;[]
13585;Pontocho Sushi Ishiya;Japan;Kyoto;210 Nabeyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8015, Japan;35.005051;135.771069;98;false;true;Sushi;This restaurant is tucked away at the end of Lane 24, Pontocho-dori, a narrow alley stretching to the west. It caters to customers’ desires by offering sushi and dishes that can be enjoyed à la carte. Unusually for a sushi restaurant, it serves beef dishes, including char-grilled wagyu beef and rolls of beef and sea urchin. Tuna, served at the perfect time to ensure the flavour is at its best, is a joy. The extensive menu amply fulfils the shop’s role as a counter-style restaurant serving traditional cuisine. Naturally, the omakase (daily changing set menu) set meal is recommended.;Counter dining;[]
13586;anu;Japan;Osaka;2-4-25 Doshin, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0035, Japan;34.702468;135.514957;44;false;true;Italian;The open kitchen is a blur of motion. Chef and kitchen team are united in creating dishes that fulfil the potential of their ingredients. To dispel preconceptions, the menu lists ingredients only. Their speciality onions are a lucky happenstance, a flavour created when onions got burnt by mistake. The appeal of each dish is enhanced with stories about their producing regions and encounters with their producers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13587;Shokudo Tanoshi;Japan;Osaka;2F, Shin Daibiru, 1-2-1 Dojimahama, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0004, Japan;34.695629;135.499255;72;false;true;Izakaya;The down-to-earth name, ‘Shokudo’ or ‘cafeteria’, was chosen because the restaurant aims to be one where people can drop in casually, while ‘Tanoshi’ (from tanoshii, ‘fun’) reflects the fun atmosphere created by Hirata, who handles service, and the chef. Indeed, it’s fun just to peruse the extensive menu. The inventive items, which weave together Japanese, Western and Chinese influences, offer no end of variety. Abalone-like shrimp croquettes and Chinese-style fried chicken-wing tips amply exemplify the spirit of Shokudo Tanoshi.;Air conditioning;[]
13588;Kitashinchi Yumiba Shinnosuke;Japan;Osaka;7F, 1-5-21 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697998;135.497245;58;true;true;Japanese;The owner-chef prizes nothing more than the temperature and aroma of his cooking. All dishes are prepared and served fresh, so counter seating is arranged around the preparation surface. In a twist, the sashimi is served with unconventional dressings such as nori seaweed soy sauce and monkfish liver with ponzu. Char-grilled beef and, in winter, shabu-shabu of bear and boar are prepared in front of customers. To finish, a selection of takikomi-gohan, rice seasoned with various ingredients, allows diners to enjoy comparing flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13589;L'aparté;Japan;Kyoto;247-3 Nishiwakamatsucho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8334, Japan;34.992707;135.75387;43;true;false;French;L’aparté serves modern French cuisine by Anthony Bâcle, who has travelled the world. Using Japanese ingredients and French methods, Bâcle conjures an eclectic blend of both cuisines, creating harmony with numerous ingredients such as bean-curd skin, miso and nori seaweed. The XO soy sauce reflects his experience in Macao just as the Manhattan Cheesecake reflects his in New York., Loire wines are stocked in homage to his native region.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13590;Kyo Ajiwa;Japan;Kyoto;455-2 Nishigomoncho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0816, Japan;34.998069;135.770659;40;true;false;Japanese;Amid the teahouses lining the streets of Miyagawacho stands this counter-style restaurant. The chef leavens his traditional kaiseki with an imaginative touch learned from his father. Seasoned broth used in soup dishes is prepared with an emphasis on aroma. One of the pleasures here is the dried bonito flakes, shaved in front of the customer and presented fresh. Parboiled pike conger is dressed with unripe apricot instead of shredded dried apricot for an original twist. The entrance is decorated with the uchiwa fans from geisha and maiko, expressing the charm and brilliant colour of the geisha quarter.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Shoes must be removed;[]
13591;Kassen Iritani;Japan;Osaka;1-8-6 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697383;135.500111;99;true;false;Japanese;Genki Iritani apprenticed at a number of kappo in Osaka. He flexes the skills and ingenuity he developed there, responding nimbly to customers’ preferences. He focuses on live seafood dishes, as the restaurant name ‘Kassen’ (‘sliced fresh’) suggests. Being able to select drinking snacks such as squid cut into thin strips like noodles with caviar or oysters simmered with pepper is fun. Crumbed beef fillet and beef tongue simmered to tender perfection are flavours neither Western nor Japanese, yet quintessentially Osaka.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13594;Koryu Keishin;Japan;Osaka;1-5-1 Dojima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0003, Japan;34.695948;135.497136;94;false;false;Japanese;In classic Naniwa (Osaka) kappo style, Koryu Keishin offers an extensive à la carte menu, prepared from Kansai ingredients. The pride of the house is its clear soup made with makombu kelp stock. Vegetables are used in generous measure: summer dishes include vinegared eel and Kema cucumber, while in winter yam from Tondabayashi is deep-fried in a batter made from powdered rice crackers.Char-grilled seafood from Osaka Bay and Kawachi duck are a delight. This sister shop of Koryu is on a quest for ‘the new flavours of Naniwa’.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13595;Ryoriya Otaya;Japan;Kyoto;456-2 Temmacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8024, Japan;34.999953;135.768649;22;true;false;Japanese;A charming kappo on the banks of the Takase River. The chef’s aim is to create a restaurant that he himself would frequent, so let’s peruse the menu and gauge his tastes. His strong points are the inventiveness and patience he pours into his creations, such as salad dressed with heshiko (mackerel pickled in rice-bran paste). A native of Toyama, the chef serves seafood from Toyama Bay. Items such as firefly squid, glass shrimp and buri arrive in season. And don’t forget the regional sakes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13596;L'angolo;Japan;Osaka;1-12-1 Tenjimbashi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0041, Japan;34.694201;135.511815;99;true;true;European;L'angolo is Italian for ‘corner’, and a corner site is where you’ll find this European eatery. The name is also an homage to a restaurant once run by the chef’s grandmother, Kadoya, ‘Corner Place’. The husband trained in Nice, the wife in Tuscany, so this is the place to tuck into simple, honest flavours from those regions. The only fare offered is a pairing course with organic wines. Though currently raising a child, the wife still prepares the ingredients, guarding the flavours of the couple.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13598;Kitashinchi Fukutatei;Japan;Osaka;B1F, 1-11-19 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.698021;135.499116;90;true;false;Steakhouse;The steaks at Kitashinchi Fukutatei are grilled by the double action of Bincho charcoal flame stoked in a furnace and far-infrared photothermal heat. Beef is Japanese Black wagyu, heifer only. Tasting and comparing different cuts, such as tenderloin, rump and aitchbone, is part of the fun. To ensure you fully enjoy the fragrant, delicate quality of the meat, seasoning is limited to salt and pepper. While the meat is being patiently grilled, tuck into wagyu consommé soup and appetisers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13599;MOTOÏ;Japan;Kyoto;186 Tawarayacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0952, Japan;35.012727;135.764903;61;true;false;French;Housed in a remodeled Taisho-era residence, with a dining room looking out on a courtyard, MOTOÏ is suffused with the atmosphere of Old Japan. Kyoto native Motoi Maeda boasts careers in both Chinese and French cuisine, so he assembles prix fixe menus applying Kyoto customs to Chinese and French techniques. Sichuan-style tofu mousse is a chilled hors d’oeuvre. During seasonal festivals, Motoi cheerfully mixes elements of traditional events into his dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13600;COPPIE;Japan;Kyoto;367 Takatsuji Inokumacho, Shimogyo-ku, Kyoto, 600-8353, Japan;34.999219;135.750532;73;false;true;Contemporary;The aproned staff greet arriving guests as if welcoming friends into their home. The nostalgic interior of this old Japanese-style house oozes serenity. The concept is fare that complements sake and wine. The chef, not binding himself to any genre, serves up an imaginative medley of Japanese, Chinese, Western and ethnic influences. Using fermentation to impart flavour and tartness is the chef’s forte. Enjoy pairing innovative cuisine with compatible sakes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
13601;Mescita Pane e Vino;Japan;Kyoto;277 Tenjinyamacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-8221, Japan;35.004882;135.75709;60;false;true;Italian;‘Mescita’ is an old Tuscan word for a bar or tavern. Come here to try the steak of aged beef and organic wine. The chef sources rump, aitchbone and rib roast, which he chargrills in the Florentine style. Seasoning is restricted to salt and pepper and portions start at 200g. Order appetisers to tide you over while the beef is grilled slowly. If you still have room, the pastas are recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13602;Yoshoku Izumi;Japan;Osaka;4-9-20 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697115;135.503772;59;false;false;Yoshoku;During the Meiji era (1868 -1912), Western-influenced cuisine spread amid Japan’s rapid modernization, developing in tandem with the native food culture. Yoshoku Izumi’s offerings form a wide assortment, from hamburger steak and cream croquettes to terrine and rillettes. The specialities of the house are omurice (rice-stuffed omelettes) and beef cutlet sandwiches. The latter offers a pleasing contrast between the aroma of the grilled bread and the tenderness of the beef tenderloin. The well-balanced prix fixe menu is recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13603;DuKKAh;Japan;Osaka;4-3-13 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.697535;135.505479;90;false;false;Spanish;A counter restaurant serving the cuisine of northern Spain. After spending considerable time in Galicia and the Basque Country, the chef drew inspiration from the guardians of those regions’ culture and food. Both regions face the Bay of Biscay, so their cuisines, blessed with bounties of sea and land, are delightfully varied. Overlaying these traditions with Japanese foods such as kudzu, soba and green pepper flower creates expressions of unique character. A marriage of Spanish local cuisine with Japanese ingredients.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
13605;TEMPURA HANAGATAMI;Japan;Osaka;5F, The Ritz-Carlton, Osaka, 2-5-25 Umeda, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0001, Japan;34.698397;135.492641;80;true;false;Tempura;Boxed sea urchins, foods from both land and sea, and tempura to start. The tempura, fried in blended oil, is light and airy. The secret is in the batter: to reduce gluten, wheat flour is chilled to below freezing before frying. One inventive dish is tempura of sea urchin and nori seaweed. Combinations are delightful, including eel grilled without seasoning then brushed with wasabi, and Orient clams dressed with pepper flowers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13606;Le Logis h;Japan;Osaka;1-2-3 Higashitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0044, Japan;34.696457;135.517436;94;true;false;French;The chef’s attention focuses on spices, herbs and fruit. These are used freely in everything from appetisers to dessert. Foie gras offerings drive home the concept with creative use of fruits and spices. Millefeuille and tarte Tatin are prepared with a playful spirit. Only a chef who apprenticed in Périgord, famous for its foie gras, could imagine dishes that are this much fun.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13607;Varier;Japan;Osaka;2F, Nakanoshima Daibiru, 3-3-23 Nakanoshima, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-6102, Japan;34.6964033;135.490811;78;true;true;French;‘Varier’ is French for ‘change’. The restaurant’s name echoes Minoru Takai’s creed of continually moving forwards. Prix fixe menus change monthly, matching step with the shifting seasons. Takai weaves a story with ingredients that speak of their native lands, such as chicken and ume from Wakayama, or pork and sweet potatoes from Kagoshima. To cultivate the talents of the next generation of chefs, recipes are conceived as a team. ‘Modest spirit, humble heart’ is the driving force at Varier.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13608;LOUISE;Japan;Osaka;1-1-5 Itachibori, Nishi-ku, Osaka, 550-0012, Japan;34.680074;135.497594;17;true;true;French;The Cameroon-born chef co-stars with the hospitable sommelier. What prompted a chef who pursued gastronomy in Paris to set up shop in Osaka. Simply put, a fascination with the foodstuffs of Japan. Layered ingredients, effectively seasoned with herbs and spices, bring out a distinctive character. The counter, where you can chat with staff and enjoy the delicious aromas wafting from the kitchen, offers the best seats in the house.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
13609;Aoikonshin Yamada;Japan;Kyoto;12-1 Shimogamo Nishihommachi, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto, 606-0826, Japan;35.043664;135.767608;51;true;true;Japanese;The owner-chef makes the extra effort to offer gorgeous presentations of elaborately prepared cuisine. The menu, which begins with a hassun appetiser, conveys a joyous love for the seasons. In sweetfish season, come for the rock garden platter. A clear stream and waterfall are drawn in salt on a black lacquer panel. The sweetfish on the platter is posed as if swimming upstream as mist rises from the spray of the waterfall, recalling the natural beauty of the valleys surrounding Kyoto. The scene imparts cooling thoughts as you dine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13610;Tokumaru;Japan;Kyoto;406 Kameyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0941, Japan;35.0120423;135.7668528;43;true;true;406 Kameyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0941, Japan;Though he apprenticed in kaiseki, the chef became captivated by the freedom à la carte dishes gave him. To create a restaurant where the customer comes first, he crafted a menu with a full range of options. Potato salad combines beef with pickled turnip, the better to serve as a drinking snack. Sweetfish sushi uses roasted sweetfish paired with vinegared rice seasoned with Japanese pepper. The rice ball with eel tempura filling is an idiosyncratic touch. As the conversation flows with the amiable owner-chef, time flows by in a comfortable mood.;;[]
13611;Kawahara;Japan;Osaka;2-4-21 Toyosaki, Kita-ku, Osaka, 531-0072, Japan;34.709936;135.500804;46;true;true;Japanese;The interior of the restaurant, an old family home, exudes warmth. The affable owner-chef, Koji Kawahara, is creative too, as his menu abounds with ingenuity. Rishiri kombu kelp is used only for soup dishes, ensuring an elegantly flavoursome broth. In cooked items, however, ma-kombu is favoured, to bring out flavour. In an innovative touch, fish is marinated in miso before frying. An assortment of items come together in a single dish, creating a unique expression that adds variety to the meal.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13612;ortensia;Japan;Kyoto;274 Demizucho, Kamigyo-ku, Kyoto, 602-0862, Japan;35.018832;135.769454;92;true;false;Italian;The chef has gained experience in many parts of Italy, but Sicily remains closest to his heart. Pasta made with dried tuna roe, and ‘matalotta’, a stew of whitefish and vegetables, are traditional flavours. To grow a clientele that drops in casually, ortensia is decorated in a burnt-orange tone, recalling the blood oranges of the Mezzogiorno. Familiar items such as clam sauce pasta and spaghetti peperoncino grace the menu as well.;Air conditioning,Cash only - lunch,Counter dining;[]
13613;Gion Rohan;Japan;Kyoto;232 Nijuikkencho, Higashiyama-ku, Kyoto, 605-0077, Japan;35.004179;135.772986;19;true;false;Japanese;Gion Rohan runs the gamut from seasonal favourites to creative Japanese cuisine. Potato salad is paired with fermented crucian carp sushi as a drinking snack. Sandwiches of mackerel pickled in vinegar pique the interest. Fish of the day is served salt-grilled or stewed. A good choice is to choose one of the rice dishes in clay pots and supplement it with ginger-fried pork or sukiyaki. Quantities can be adjusted according to taste, so you’ll want to try a range of offerings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13614;Oryori Matsumura;Japan;Osaka;4-20-11 Gamo, Joto-ku, Osaka, 536-0016, Japan;34.699733;135.544429;56;true;false;Japanese;A menu only a chef who honed his craft in Kyoto, Osaka and Paris could conjure. He calibrates his flavours by gathering ingredients in Kansai and drawing his dashi soup stock from ma-kombu kelp and dried tuna flakes. The spirit of frugality espoused at Oryori Matsumura decrees that each ingredient should be used completely. For example, the bony parts of fish left over are used up making sea-bream miso and dashi. By bringing together the aesthetic senses of disparate locations, Oryori Matsumura has created a cuisine that is refreshingly original.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13615;PONTE VECCHIO;Japan;Osaka;1-8-16 Kitahama, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 541-0041, Japan;34.691443;135.507296;73;false;true;Italian;Daisuke Yamane insists on originality in everything about his restaurant. Leather seating, show plates of Venetian glass and silverware are all designed by the chef. One intriguing offering, inspired by Yamane’s days in Italy, is ‘the world’s most luxurious pauper food’, a dish made with potatoes and caviar. Each ingredient complements the other, converging in a harmonious whole.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13617;Washun Taiki;Japan;Osaka;6F, 1-3-30 Sonezakishinchi, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0002, Japan;34.697324;135.496691;15;true;false;Japanese;The name ‘Washun’ means ‘complementing the seasons’. The purport here is to bring together ingredients that draw out each other’s goodness, using proper techniques but with splashes of creativity. Noting bread’s affinity with fats and oils, Washun Taiki created baguette sandwiches, breaking new ground with fillings such as grilled seafood and deep-fried items. With orthodox techniques as the baseline and smiling guests as the goal, Washun Taiki is not afraid to break a few rules.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13619;Tempura Urakami;Japan;Osaka;1-2-4 Fukushima, Fukushima-ku, Osaka, 553-0003, Japan;34.69473;135.488646;40;true;true;Tempura;In his tempura creations, Dai Urakami prizes lightness above all. Frying in light safflower oil brings the flavour of each piece to the fore. The meal begins with two tiger prawns. To ensure that the sweetness of the flesh makes an impression, fragrant prawn legs are served afterward. Tempura items such as abalone and milt are imaginatively paired with vinegared rice stuffed with sea urchin. The painting of Mount Fuji on the wall reminds Urakami always to seek greater heights.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13621;Sosakukappo Otani;Japan;Kyoto;145 Takeyacho, Nakagyo-ku, Kyoto, 604-0823, Japan;35.01222;135.762464;72;true;false;Japanese;The blending of Japanese and Western styles is the appeal of creative kappo cuisine here. With its pivot foot firmly in Japanese gastronomy, the restaurant moves imaginatively to incorporate Western elements. For example, the dashi is based on kombu and katsuo but, influenced by French chefs, mixes in fish fumet, the stock from the bones of white fish. To broaden its culinary range, the restaurant added an oven. Roasts and gratins now widen the scope of Otani’s Japanese cooking.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13623;Yoshitaka;Japan;Osaka;2F, 2-8-5 Higashishinsaibashi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0083, Japan;34.671482;135.503279;25;true;false;Oden;Oden fashioned in the manner of a simmered dish in kaiseki fare. Toppings such as dried kombu shavings for tofu and ground sesame for soft-boiled eggs are served one piece at a time to offer a twist on familiar flavours. Each serving-dish is different, an influence from the chef’s experience in other cuisines. The meal ends with ramen flavoured with dashi or, taking a page from Edo cooking, peppered rice. Osaka has been a port of call for kombu merchants since the Edo period, and this is a place to savour stewed items from that rich dashi culture.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13624;xiang hua;Japan;Osaka;1-13-8 Nishitemma, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0047, Japan;34.694394;135.505768;29;false;true;Chinese;True to its name, which means ‘serving the cuisine of every region of China’, the menu features a rich variety of regional dishes. The background to the recipes is a tale worth telling. As the chef used to teach at a cooking school, he is well-versed in his craft. He follows Confucius’s teaching of ‘Bù shí bù shí’, that people should eat foods in season. Tour the regional cuisines of China and taste its many fascinating flavours.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13625;Sui Okazaki;Japan;Osaka;2F, 1-16-20 Higashishinsaibashi, Chuo-ku, Osaka, 542-0083, Japan;34.672239;135.50246;34;true;false;Japanese;When he took over the restaurant, the chef inherited its teachings, preserving the forms of traditional multi-course meals while expressing his own imagination. Experience in Kyoto cuisine shines in soup stock of ma-kombu and Rishiri kombu. Pickled mackerel is paired with fruit, highlighting the tartness in both. His inspiration for pursuing the gastronomic life came, he says, from the way appetiser platters express the shifting seasons. To celebrate those seasons, dishes are cheerfully garnished.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13626;LACERBA;Japan;Osaka;2F, Shin Daibiru, 1-2-1 Dojimahama, Kita-ku, Osaka, 530-0004, Japan;34.695635;135.499291;77;false;false;Italian;Masaaki Fujita reaches deep into the character and history of Japan and Italy to conjure his cuisine. Eel, Chinese yam and red rice on a single plate fuse the gustatory senses of the two countries, both rooted deeply in cultures of river fish and rice. Zest of Japanese pepper married with the bittersweet of red wine sauce is somehow nostalgic. Fujita’s motto is ‘to be master of one is to be master of all’. His long study of hometown cooking followed by his own innovations proves the point.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
13627;Sushidokoro Hirokawa;Japan;Osaka;1-8-39 Gamo, Joto-ku, Osaka, 536-0016, Japan;34.698339;135.537082;83;true;true;Sushi;When you order sake, the chef presents a box of paulownia wood containing Satsuma and Tenma kiriko cut-glass drinking cups. These craft traditions of Kagoshima and Osaka tell of where the chef was born, and where he apprenticed. Fish is selected at Tsuruhashi Market. The meal starts with snacks before proceeding to more creative preparations, attesting to his experience. Nigiri are formed small, in the hope you will sample as many different items as possible. The chef’s ready smile is another factor that keeps diners coming back.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13629;Matsu;Japan;Kyoto;21-26 Umezu Onawabacho, Ukyo-ku, Kyoto, 615-0925, Japan;35.004;135.69052;88;true;true;Japanese;Always take on challenges – that was the teaching of Toshio Matsuno’s tempura chef father – which is why Matsuno travelled to the USA to broaden his perspective. The experience prompted his recent changing of the family restaurant from tempura only to a general Japanese restaurant. Tilefish fried with its scales still on and served with egg yolk vinaigrette sauce and shaved black truffle on top testifies to his broad-minded approach. The one dish Matsuno never omits is his tempura, in respect for his father. ‘Matsuno cuisine’ is an evergreen that never fades.;Air conditioning,Car park,Cash only,Counter dining;[]
13630;The Golden Fork;Malta;Rabat;31 Triq L-Isptar, Rabat, RBT 1040, Malta;35.882215;14.401365;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Situated along one of Rabat’s typical narrow alleyways, this elegant restaurant’s new venue boasts a courtyard setting in a historic building dating from the 16C. The chef Letizia Vella here creates surprisingly creative and technically skillful cuisine full of distinctive Mediterranean flavours. Careful attention is paid to using seasonal and locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
13631;Terroir;Malta;Attard;13 Triq Il-Kbira, Attard, ATD 1027, Malta;35.8903675;14.4425168;77;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated in a charming square with an old fountain, this 16C building boasts original brick walls and a rustic, romantic ambience – the intimate dining room is on the first floor, where there is even a small table on the balcony (make sure you book this in advance). The cuisine focuses on local and Mediterranean ingredients and includes highlights such as ricotta gnocchi with a Maltese sausage ragù, while the wine list also features a few international labels.;Terrace;[]
13635;One80 St.Christopher Street;Malta;Valletta;45A St. Christopher's Street, Valletta, VLT 1464, Malta;35.8994817;14.5149611;64;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;From the various options on the menu, we recommend starting with one of the excellent snacks such as crab croquette, Joselito chorizo and black garlic and then continuing with pistachio carbonara, a delicious pasta made with traditional guanciale and roasted pistachios. Main courses include excellent meat options, such as chateaubriand for two served with gravy. The restaurant has a chic, bistro-style decor and a lively atmosphere typical of the restaurants in La Valletta’s historic centre.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13636;The Fork and Cork;Malta;Mdina;20 Saqqajja Hill, Mdina, MDN 1400, Malta;35.883115;14.4037651;45;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Behind the stone walls of a historic building sits this charming restaurant. Chef-owner Carl Zahra seems to be everywhere at once: you’ll find him not only in the kitchen but also out front recommending regional wines to go with the tasty pastas and other Mediterranean-inspired dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13637;Kaiseki;Malta;Valletta;77, Merchants Street, Valletta, VLT 1174, Malta;35.8988146;14.515441;78;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Asian Influences;If you find yourself on one of the most beautiful islands in the Mediterranean Sea and hungering for Mediterranean-Asian fusion cuisine, then head for Noel Azzopardi's Kaiseki. There's a cosy vibe to this basement restaurant and the Chef-Owner's kitchen produces interesting creations like soy-marinated tuna belly carpaccio, goat's cheese and grapefruit crostino, BBQ pork dumplings with teriyaki, sesame seeds and spicy mayo or roasted duck breast with pickled beetroot, pak choi and crispy duck & mozzarella roll. The different cooking styles are combined well, and the informal, casual atmosphere makes the experience all the more enjoyable.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13638;Aaron´s Kitchen;Malta;Valletta;107 Archbishop Street, Valletta, VLT 1446, Malta;35.8997592;14.5136909;58;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This bistro in the town centre with a welcoming ambience and an attractive, colourful decor is the setting for Mediterranean fish dishes and typical island fare. Very popular with locals and tourists alike, the restaurant also offers a few outdoor tables which need to be booked well in advance.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13639;Giuseppi's;Malta;Naxxar;Salini Resort, Salina Bay, Naxxar, NXR 9030, Malta;35.9483589;14.4289128;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Situated within the attractive Salini Resort hotel overlooking the bay of the same name, this exquisite restaurant uses top-quality ingredients to create Mediterranean-style dishes, although modern trends are starting to make a fleeting appearance in some recipes. Lunchtime options are slightly simpler than those served in the evening.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13640;Root 81;Malta;Rabat;22A Saqqajja Hill, Rabat, MDN 1400, Malta;35.8831608;14.4038731;51;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This pleasant restaurant serves Mediterranean-style cuisine skilfully prepared by the talented chef with a focus on local ingredients. The outdoor space has an attractive and relaxing vibe, plus there’s an excellent selection of wines and cocktails.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
13641;Tmun;Malta;Għajnsielem;Martino Garces Street, Mġarr Harbour, Gozo, Għajnsielem, GSM 2413, Malta;36.0257325;14.2968455;99;true;true;Seafood;This restaurant serves delicious Mediterranean cuisine which is often inspired by the fresh fish caught that day. The atmosphere here is informal, with friendly, welcoming staff, plus there’s an attractive sunny terrace for summer dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13642;Tartarun;Malta;Marsaxlokk;20 Fisherman's Wharf, Marsaxlokk, MXK 1301, Malta;35.8414467;14.5454023;41;false;true;Seafood;This elegant restaurant on the harbourside of a small fishing village has been run by the Schiavone family for over 10 years. Son James treats diners to a daily changing selection of simply cooked whole fish and other, more modern, imaginative seafood dishes. Apart from fishermen they support the local baker that provides daily bread for the village and a hydroponic farmer which is a few kilometers from the restaurant. Their 150+ bin wine list is renowned locally.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13643;Grotto Tavern;Malta;Rabat;9/10/12 St Pauls Square, Rabat, RBT 1232, Malta;35.8821211;14.3987874;74;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Boasting an excellent location in the historic centre of Rabat, this restaurant full of character has a bar, a garden room and a “cave room”, the latter a grotto which has been excavated out of the limestone rock and is available for private dining (book in advance). The cuisine bears the signature of the new chef Nikolai Abela, who uses local and seasonal ingredients. Professional service completes the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
13644;LOA;Malta;St Paul's Bay;Saint Geraldu, St Paul's Bay, SPB 3310, Malta;35.9493734;14.4043557;52;true;false;South American, Fusion;Facing the sea on Malta’s Sirens coast, this modern restaurant named after the ancient Loa river (the longest river in Chile) serves South American fusion cuisine which is both varied and delicious. The atmosphere here is relaxed and inviting with a contemporary vibe. A good choice of pre-dinner cocktails is also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13646;Briju;Malta;Gzira;Triq l-Imsida, Gzira, GZR 1405, Malta;35.9017;14.49324;86;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The chef at Briju has a passion for all things local and sustainable. 90% of his ingredients are sourced from nearby farms and he even uses regional salt and olive oil. Cooking blends Maltese and Mediterranean flavours and the place has a pleasingly relaxed, neighbourhood feel.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13647;The Medina;Malta;Mdina;7 Holy Cross Street, Mdina, MDN 1231, Malta;35.8864486;14.4027391;76;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Hidden away in the enchantingly narrow streets of Mdina is this equally characterful 500 year old restaurant. Dine beneath a vaulted stone ceiling or in the internal courtyard beside an ancient vine. Local ingredients underpin well-executed dishes which exhibit subtle modern twists.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13648;Level Nine at The Grand;Malta;Għajnsielem;58 Triq Sant Antnin, Mġarr Harbour, Gozo, Għajnsielem, GSM 9026, Malta;36.03149;14.29719;47;false;true;Italian Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The menu at this restaurant has been designed by German chef Oliver Glowig, now an ambassador for the type of Italian cuisine showcased here. We highly recommend the tasting menu, which will give you a delicious overview of the chef’s different dishes, but if you do decide to order from the à la carte, the tournedos Rossini with foie gras and spinach is an excellent choice. Various local labels stand out on the wine list, including a remarkable Marsovin Antonin 2021 which is full and round yet retains a fruity character. From the charming terrace, the stunning views of the small harbour at Mgarr add to the appeal in summer.;Great view,Terrace;[]
13649;Al Sale;Malta;Xagħra;32 Victory Square, Xagħra, XRA 2205, Malta;36.05123;14.26922;30;true;true;Meats and Seafood;In the middle of Xaghra lies this outwardly inconspicuous restaurant that extends over two floors and boasts a small terrace out front. The Chef-Owner hails from Toronto and forged his independent business here in the middle of the pandemic, showing just how much heart and soul is behind his cooking! If you love simple cuisine based on fresh produce – especially when it comes to meat and seafood – try the prawn & scallop-filled ravioli with prawn bisque, or the delicious veal rack with salsa verde. Everything is uncomplicated, ingredient-led and freshly prepared. An international wine list and the friendly, attentive yet unstuffy service round off the overall experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13650;KuYa;Malta;St Julian's;20 St. George's Road, St Julian's, STJ 3209, Malta;35.9202567;14.4905542;70;true;false;Asian, International;Head up the spiral staircase and past the kitchen to this modern, light-filled room, where they offer an appealing blackboard menu of Asian classics. Cooking is fresh and authentic, with bold, vibrant flavours. Choose one of the craft beers from their wide-ranging list.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
13651;Guzé;Malta;Valletta;22 Old Bakery Street, Valletta, VLT 1454, Malta;35.8986685;14.5110933;57;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A striking 17C palazzo houses this cosy cellar bistro. Glance into the kitchens from street level, then head down the narrow staircase at the side to reach the two rustic, romantic dining rooms adorned with knick-knacks. Traditional Maltese dishes are generously proportioned.;Air conditioning;[]
13652;Chophouse;Malta;Sliema;Censu Xerri, Tigné Point, Sliema, SLM 3190, Malta;35.9059998;14.5127628;79;false;true;Grills, Classic Cuisine;Its superb location on Tigné Point means that The Chophouse affords wonderful views across the harbour to Valletta, both from its modern dining room and heated terrace. The cuisine served here is influenced by culinary trends from across the globe and includes top-quality cuts of meat such as Scottona, Angus and Wagyu. These are hung and matured in an ageing cabinet in the dining room, and then grilled on one of the largest barbecue grills in Malta!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
13653;Legligin;Malta;Valletta;Triq Santa Lucia 116-119, Valletta, VLT 1183, Malta;35.8992238;14.5118558;64;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This small, rustic restaurant in the historic centre has limited space and a vaguely bohemian feel thanks to its informal tables, ceramics and candles. Delicious, simple, home-made cuisine full of Mediterranean and Maltese flavours takes pride of place here, with just one tasting menu that changes almost every day. There’s a shorter menu at lunchtime, while dessert can be chosen separately from a mini dessert menu. Excellent bread baked in a wood-fired oven, olives, extra-virgin olive oil from Gozo, pasta, and slow-cooked meat are just some of the attractions here. Booking in advance is recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
13654;Caviar & Bull;Malta;St Julian's;St George's Bay, St Julian's, STJ 3301, Malta;35.9286726;14.4913568;32;false;true;Beef;The name says it all, as the menu at this restaurant is based on a selection of different caviars and aged beef, the latter on display in a glass cabinet near the entrance. Although fish also makes an appearance on the menu, we recommend the excellent beef tartare or Argentine ribs, grilled and served with roast potatoes and sautéed onions. The location is delightful and includes a cocktail bar, where chef Gauci’s recipes are listed in a personalised book, alongside a selection of Cuban cigars. The service is elegant and attentive, akin to dining in a private club.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13655;59 Republic;Malta;Valletta;St George's Square, Valletta, VLT 1190, Malta;35.8990289;14.5133987;65;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This basement restaurant is cosy and characterful but, if it’s sunny, the terrace overlooking the Grandmaster's Palace is the place to be. Generously sized dishes blend classical French techniques with Mediterranean flavours. The 'bites to share' are imaginative, and Beef Wellington is the house speciality.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13657;Marea;Malta;Kalkara;Marina street, Kalkara waterfront, Kalkara, KKR 1521, Malta;35.8917236;14.5240799;99;false;false;Asian, Mediterranean Cuisine;This chic, contemporary-style lounge bar-cum-restaurant near the Grand Harbour boasts fine views of the marina. The menu features Mediterranean cuisine alongside more Asian-influenced options, while the excellent wine list includes sparkling wines and a good choice of cocktails. Perfect for a relaxing meal, with an extensive outdoor space that adds to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13658;Ponyhof Stammhaus by Tobias Wussler;Germany;Gengenbach;Mattenhofweg 6, Gengenbach, 77723, Germany;48.412094;8.025932;19;false;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The sort of restaurant you would love to have in your own neighbourhood, thanks to its excellent cuisine. The next generation has now taken over the management of this long-standing family business. The kitchen serves modern dishes, but also classics such as cordon bleu and “dry aged” beef from the charcoal grill.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13660;Hirschen;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Breisgauer Straße 47, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79110, Germany;48.015873;7.8020835;33;false;true;Farm to table;Hirschen boasts two restaurants. One is in the traditional Baden-style with lots of wood and small alcoves, and the other is light, bright and friendly with a small winter garden. The food is fresh and uncomplicated and includes dishes such as Wiener Schnitzel with spring vegetables, and pork loin medallions with spinach. The roast duck is also a speciality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13662;Traube;Germany;Heidelberg;Rathausstraße 75, Heidelberg, 69126, Germany;49.3783967;8.6932115;32;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Run with great dedication in the heart of the old Rohrbach district, this lovely traditional restaurant has a cosy interior featuring a blend of traditional and modern elements. Chef Ole Hake's ambitious dishes are made with carefully selected regional ingredients, for example excellent game. His commitment to sustainability is palpable. The seasonal seven-course set menu comes in an omnivore or vegan version. There is also a well-curated wine list with an emphasis on German labels. These can also be enjoyed in the wine bar with snacks or a light meal. Tip for motorists: the public car park at the nearby Thorax Clinic is convenient.;;[]
13663;Weisser Bock;Germany;Heidelberg;Große Mantelgasse 24, Heidelberg, 69117, Germany;49.4121233;8.7060755;81;false;true;International;Pretty details such as wood panelling and historical photos contribute to the cosy atmosphere in this traditional establishment. The kitchen serves up a fine selection of dishes made from regional and international ingredients, from which you can choose a three- to six-course menu. The à la carte menu includes appetising dishes such as "beef tartare, anchovies, brioche, caviar" and "turbot, wild cauliflower, capers". The hotel of the same name has comfortable and tastefully decorated guestrooms. The central location is another trump card.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13664;Hofgut Hohenkarpfen;Germany;Hausen ob Verena;Hohenkarpfen 1, Hausen ob Verena, 78595, Germany;48.0390014;8.719446;57;true;true;International, Farm to table;This restaurant enjoys a wonderful location in the middle Baden-Württemberg's oldest nature reserve and boasts stunning views – it's well worth booking a table on the terrace. In what was once the dairy of the over 300-year-old farmstead, diners are pampered with delicious food and attentive service. The modern cuisine incorporates classic and regional influences, as well as international, sometimes Asian touches. The former barn of the heritage-protected estate has been transformed into a hotel with attractive and cosy minimalist-style guestrooms. Tip: Take the time to look around the art museum.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13665;Bachmaier;Germany;Heilbronn;Untere Neckarstraße 40, Heilbronn, 74072, Germany;49.1445345;9.2172862;48;true;true;Farm to table;Ulrike and Otto Bachmaier have been running their restaurant for many years. The modern decor is delightful and you can watch the river traffic on the Neckar through the floor-to-ceiling windows, as well as from the terrace. Friendly and adept service comes courtesy of the lady of the house while the chef-patron delivers seasonal dishes such as Obsiblue prawn soup with ginger, or braised shoulder of locally hunted venison, glazed in the pan, with Swede, palm tree kale and celeriac. A vegetarian set menu is available by prior arrangement. Good wine pairings. Tip: Book well in advance.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13666;Das Ballenberger;Germany;Erfurt;Gotthardtstraße 25, Erfurt, 99084, Germany;50.9795683;11.0313762;92;false;true;Farm to table, International;A friendly, modern restaurant in the centre of the old town close to the historic Krämerbrücke bridge, Das Ballenberger serves seasonal, international cuisine including scallops with two kinds of asparagus and orange. You’ll also find some mouthwatering home-made cakes and a delicious breakfast from 9 am after a stay in one of the five charming overnight apartments.;Terrace;[]
13667;Zenzakan;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Taunusanlage 15, Frankfurt on the Main, 60325, Germany;50.1145767;8.669115;83;false;false;Asian;Somewhat hidden away, this elegant and stylish restaurant is accessible via a rear courtyard. The interior is done out in dark tones with dimmed lighting, and it smacks of the Far East (the terracotta warriors are eye-catching). The atmosphere is lively, and contemporary beats provide the acoustic backdrop. The menu includes a wide selection of pan-Asian dishes ranging from sushi and sashimi to classic curries and robata grill specialities – the braised beef short ribs are a real classic.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13668;Il Cortile;Germany;Erfurt;Johannesstraße 150, Erfurt, 99084, Germany;50.9817462;11.0324634;98;false;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;You get to this restaurant, which is located in Erfurt's old town in a pretty little courtyard, via Johannesstraße. In a cosy atmosphere, diners tuck into fresh, Mediterranean-inspired cuisine – either in the form of the set menu or à la carte. The dishes adhere to the seasons, and there is a new menu every three weeks.;Terrace;[]
13669;Hebelstube;Germany;Müllheim;Posthalterweg, Müllheim, 79379, Germany;47.8124646;7.6101049;86;true;true;Farm to table;This establishment has been a familiar and beloved landmark for decades. The long-established Hotel Alte Post offers contemporary-style guestrooms, and the restaurant serves a modern take on classic and regional dishes, such as salmon trout ceviche or dry-aged saddle of back, prepared by new chef duo Nicolas Volk and Christoph Dees and team. The wine list predominantly features labels from the region. Diners can also look forward to a friendly and charming atmosphere, as well as attentive service. The terrace is delightful in summer.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13670;HIO;Germany;Pilsach;Hilzhofen 18, Pilsach, 92367, Germany;49.3014683;11.5954556;60;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;"HIO" is the nickname of the small village that is home to this restaurant. In the seven-course tasting menu proposed here, vegetables take centre stage. Much of the produce comes from the restaurant's own garden, which is right by the house, or from local farmers. The chic and modern interior incorporates a smattering of rustic touches, with the open kitchen being a focal point. With just 16 places, the restaurant has something akin to a family atmosphere, and the service is friendly, pleasingly laid-back and professional. Upon arrival, guests are taken outside to enjoy hors-d'oeuvres by the charcoal grill and hear about the sustainable philosophy in place here. In addition to HIO, HILZHOF also houses another restaurant – MEIER – plus a handful of guestrooms.;Garden or park;[]
13671;Hohenhaus Grill;Germany;Herleshausen;Hohenhaus 1, Herleshausen, 37293, Germany;51.0410072;10.0801261;97;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;This is the second restaurant of the idyllically situated Hohenhaus hotel, a magnificent property laden with history. The eatery has a classic-meets-rustic-style interior and a warm atmosphere – plus a lovely 18C tiled stove. The cuisine is seasonal and based on premium ingredients, which are for the most part sourced from the region. It is a treat to sit on the terrace and take in the view of the surrounding countryside.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13672;Hirschen;Germany;Glottertal;Rathausweg 2, Glottertal, 79286, Germany;48.0491232;7.9405598;66;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This restaurant and hotel of the same name are among the stand-out addresses in this valley, with a friendly team taking care of guests in the rustic yet elegant dining rooms. The chef prepares dishes based on Baden cuisine, with the occasional French touch. The menu includes a range of tasty dishes from local game to sea bass, chanterelle risotto and saffron sauce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13673;Bastian's Restaurant;Germany;Friedberg (Hessen);Erbsengasse 16, Friedberg (Hessen), 61169, Germany;50.3501256;8.7882524;91;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;This country inn with a tasteful bright interior and beautiful partly covered terrace focuses on culinary classics that evolve with the seasons. You can choose from the à la carte menu or try a surprise menu. Dishes served include, for example, pigeon with savoy cabbage, parsnip and truffle. The service is very friendly and charming.;Terrace;[]
13674;Lemabri;Germany;Boppard;Alte Römerstraße 3a, Boppard, 56154, Germany;50.2059725;7.5596349;68;false;true;World Cuisine;Despite its somewhat unusual location in an industrial estate, this restaurant run by Sarah Henke and Christian Eckhardt has diners coming in droves. Building on successful stints in Andernach ( at YOSO and PURS respectively), the duo set up shop here with a casual and varied concept. In a spacious setting with chic modern interior design, the kitchen team serves up a wide-ranging selection of plates that are perfect for sharing. The extensive menu includes Asian and regional dishes, as well as pasta and fantastic pizzas from the large Morello Forni pizza oven. Children are also welcome – they will love the children's menu and play area.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13675;Kupferpfanne;Germany;Fürth;Königstraße 85, Fürth, 90762, Germany;49.4772555;10.9898033;30;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Erwin Weidenhiller's restaurant, in a central location opposite the town hall, has been a classic on Fürth's food scene for decades. In the comfortable and elegant interior, they serve classic cuisine with seasonal and international-Mediterranean influences, made with good-quality produce. Tip: the reasonably priced lunch menu.;;[]
13676;[maki:'dan] im Ritter;Germany;Durbach;Tal 1, Durbach, 77770, Germany;48.4942285;8.0168471;28;false;false;Contemporary, Creative;Housed in the historical part of the Hotel Ritter, this exceedingly cosy and tastefully decorated restaurant serves modern cuisine in the evenings. The "Signature Menu" comprises four or five courses, and wine pairings are available on request. Alternatively, you can choose à la carte. Tip: the delicious sourdough bread from the Müller Bäckerei in Durbach! If you are wondering about the name, makidan comes from the Persian and encompasses the notion of delicacies, conviviality and hospitality. Consider the option of staying overnight – it's worth it!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13677;Landgasthaus Schuster;Germany;Freyung;Ort 19, Freyung, 94078, Germany;48.8090385;13.5324005;96;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The Schuster family's country inn is thoroughly charming! This is primarily down to the warm hospitality extended by the lady of the house, and the tasteful interior design. And then there are the chef-patron's seasonally influenced classic dishes such as pike-perch sausage accompanied by creamed sauerkraut with dates, or venison with nuts, black walnut sauce, cranberries and Savoy cabbage. Individual courses from each of the two set menus ("Tradition" and "Genusswerk") can be ordered à la carte. Decent wine selection with good options available by the glass.;Car park;[]
13678;Stüble;Germany;Freudenstadt;Amselweg 5, Freudenstadt, 72250, Germany;48.4439627;8.4346835;80;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Stüble is the tasteful, rustic-style à la carte restaurant of the chic wellness Hotel Lauterbad! In this wood-panelled parlour, you can soak up the cosy atmosphere while the friendly staff take care of you, serving fresh traditional, but also more modern, dishes. The hanging spit is a speciality here.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13679;Weinstube Sibylla;Germany;Ettlingen;Rheinstraße 1, Ettlingen, 76275, Germany;48.9413033;8.4046797;39;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;A good place to come for unpretentious cuisine. The menu ranges from classics such as Wiener schnitzel or Berlin-style calf's liver to a "Gourmet Tradition" section featuring dishes such as saddle and shoulder of venison in pasta sheets, with tenderstem broccoli and an elderberry jus. There is also a selection of vegetarian dishes and a range of delicious desserts. Lovely old wooden floors, wood-panelled walls and pretty decorations make for a charming atmosphere. The verdant terrace is also inviting. Guestrooms are available in the adjoining Erbprinz hotel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13681;Bistro Fatal;Germany;Düsseldorf;Hermannstraße 29, Düsseldorf, 40233, Germany;51.2294558;6.807572;58;true;false;French;It would be a shame to not to get to know Alexandre and Sarah Bourgeuil's pleasantly unpretentious bistro, because the food is excellent. Why not start with a pastis as an aperitif, accompanied by some house-baked baguette with butter? You could follow that with skate à la grenobloise served with mashed potatoes and mesclun salad, and then finish off with crêpes Suzette for dessert. Delightful terrace in front of the building. NB: Finding a parking space nearby is not easy.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13682;Kronenschlösschen;Germany;Eltville am Rhein;Rheinallee, Eltville am Rhein, 65347, Germany;50.0136968;8.0623029;63;true;true;International, French Contemporary;Here, diners can sit beneath a stylishly painted historical ceiling or out on the pretty terrace with adjoining garden. The kitchen draws on traditional French cuisine to propose creative dishes in the form of a four- to six-course menu. Plus the wine list is one of the best in Germany. Alternatively, try the bistro. Guests can also stay overnight in the hotel of the same name in cosy, well-appointed guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13683;Villa Feer;Germany;Lörrach;Beim Haagensteg 1, Lörrach, 79541, Germany;47.6324644;7.6819148;48;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;Owner Kathrin Bucher has been running this restaurant in an attractive old villa near Lörrach exhibition centre since 2012. Dine in the cosy, bright interior or, in summer, out on the wonderful terrace. They serve lunch only: until 3pm you can order the set menu or from a small menu compiled from favourite dishes of the last decade. After that, there are desserts and ice creams/sorbets until 5pm.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13684;schuberts;Germany;Lauterbach;Kanalstraße 12, Lauterbach, 36341, Germany;50.63557;9.3966573;56;false;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in the centre of town, right by the Lauter River, this popular restaurant has a casual brasserie feel and serves flavoursome regional and seasonal cuisine that draws on Mediterranean influences. The daily special, "Schuberts Schneller Teller" ("Schubert's Quick Plate"), is a hit at lunchtime. Entennest is a cosy and charming wine tavern that makes for a more rustic alternative – the menu is the same here in the evening. If you would like to stay overnight, the hotel of the same name has attractive individually furnished guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13685;Gasthaus Stappen;Germany;Korschenbroich;Steinhausen 39, Korschenbroich, 41352, Germany;51.1659892;6.5330557;20;false;false;International, Seasonal Cuisine;Steeped in tradition, this establishment is run with great dedication. Diners are drawn by the attentive service provided by the friendly and adept staff, as well as the excellent food. The regional cuisine is replete with international influences. The leafy terrace is delightful in summer. Ask about the wine tastings held in the wine shop. Tip: There are chic, modern guestrooms should you wish to stay overnight. N.B. card payment only.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13686;VIDA;Germany;Dortmund;Hagener Straße 231, Dortmund, 44229, Germany;51.4614812;7.4567693;45;false;true;Creative, International;This place has it all: a stylish, upscale decor, enthusiastic, professional and friendly service, and creative international cuisine incorporating both Asian and Mediterranean influences. Diners are offered a choice between the "VIDA" set menu – with meat or vegetarian – and a range of à la carte dishes. The attentive and well-drilled service team is also on hand to offer expert wine recommendations – there is an attractive selection to choose from. Wine pairings to complement the set menu are also available. Tip: Enjoy an aperitif or digestif at the VIDA bar.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13687;SCALA - Das Turm Restaurant;Germany;Jena;Leutragraben 1, Jena, 07743, Germany;50.9285717;11.5838915;74;true;true;International, Modern Cuisine;Take in the fantastic view of the city and surrounding area from the striking JenTower from 128m above street level! The cuisine is modern and international: dinner takes the form of a sharing menu (vegetarian also possible), and there is a good-value lunch. Tip: from the Neue Mitte multi-storey car park, take the lifts up to the restaurant (there is a sign). Hotel on the floors below the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13688;TISK;Germany;Berlin;Neckarstraße 12, Berlin, 12053, Germany;52.4801477;13.4323088;84;true;true;German, Modern Cuisine;Situated in a quiet side street of Neukölln, TISK (old German for table) calls itself a Speisekneipe (food pub) – and the description works well. It offers a young, urban ambience and modern German cuisine with pepped-up flavours. Options include set menus (e. g. with meatballs or knuckle of lamb) and roast chicken for two people.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13689;Zur Mühle;Germany;Kürten;Wipperfürther Straße 391, Kürten, 51515, Germany;51.0536634;7.2691606;46;false;false;International;In their well-established restaurant – it’s been in the same family since 1895 – Hermann and Kerstin Berger prepare internationally inspired cuisine such as sliced salmon in a rocket and pesto crust with teriyaki beans, mashed potato and sweet mustard. The interior is cosy with a modern note.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13690;Sonne;Germany;Lautenbach;Hauptstraße 51, Lautenbach, 77794, Germany;48.5204145;8.1157604;66;true;true;International, Country cooking;The luxurious Wellness Hotel Sonnenhof welcomes you to its upscale yet cosy restaurant. The menu is dominated by regional cuisine but includes the odd Asian dish. The attractively priced lunch deal is especially popular. Look down through the glass pane in the floor and you'll see some excellent wines stored below – the selection is extensive. On days when the restaurant is closed, Sonnenstüble stands in as a somewhat simpler alternative.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13691;Locanda Grappolo d'Oro;Germany;Lebach;Mottener Straße 94, Lebach, 66822, Germany;49.4139462;6.8943883;70;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;It really is a joy to dine at this restaurant, which has been run by the same family with great dedication for years. The decor is bright and cheerful, and warm hospitality and service come courtesy of the lady of the house. The Mediterranean-inspired cuisine is fresh and delicious. The pasta, the gnocchi, the bread… It's all house-made. No wonder this place draws so many regulars from the region.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13692;Gasthaus;Germany;Lahr;Reichenbacher Hauptstraße 18, Lahr, 77933, Germany;48.3299999;7.924922;35;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;Like the gourmet restaurant, Gasthaus also combines modernity and tradition, from the decor down to the menu. While things are a bit more casual here, the cooking is also really good – the quality of the sauces alone will convince you of that! You can put together your own menu – and even make it vegetarian. Friendly service.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13693;ZEN Japanese Restaurant;Germany;Cologne;Bachemer Straße 233, Cologne, 50935, Germany;50.924924;6.90729;61;false;true;Japanese;Located in a residential area, this restaurant is a firm favourite with fans of Japanese cuisine. In a pared-back Far Eastern-style setting, diners can look forward to a pleasantly lively atmosphere, as well as friendly and professional service with an authentic Japanese touch. It is clear that a well-coordinated team is at work here. Your options include gyoza, tempura, grilled and pan-fried dishes, udon, sushi and sashimi, plus a large omakase set menu. Wine, sake and Japanese whisky to go with it.;;[]
13694;Brasserie Colette Tim Raue;Germany;Berlin;Passauer Straße 5, Berlin, 10789, Germany;52.5009665;13.3394824;89;true;false;French;A big name on the fine dining scene, Tim Raue has created a pleasantly down-to-earth brasserie of the sort you might be more inclined to expect to find in Paris. This place has a modern feel tempered by a slight touch of nostalgia. The food is excellent, and the intriguing menu changes every three months. Along with the à la carte selection, there are always three set menus to choose from: "Colette Classics", the "Tim Raue Menü" and a vegan one.;Wheelchair access;[]
13695;Nagels Kranz;Germany;Karlsruhe;Neureuter Hauptstraße 210, Karlsruhe, 76149, Germany;49.0513204;8.3770637;66;false;false;Country cooking;This restaurant sets great store by the first-class ingredients it uses to create dishes such as confit Arctic char with sautéed asparagus, peas & hollandaise. The good food is more than matched by the friendly atmosphere, whether you eat in the cosy dining room or on the secluded terrace in the courtyard.;Terrace;[]
13697;Gasthof zum Kranz;Germany;Lottstetten;Dorfstraße 23, Lottstetten, 79807, Germany;47.6061825;8.5770144;20;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Built in 1769 and run by the same family for seven generations, the interior at Zum Kranz is modern and elegant in the minimalist style. The kitchens produce flavoursome, classic, international fare. If you come in the autumn, make sure you try the game!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13698;Hirsch Genusshandwerk;Germany;Bad Liebenzell;Monbachstraße 47, Bad Liebenzell, 75378, Germany;48.7898064;8.7500984;32;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;This lovely village inn serves dishes with classical foundations and modern inspirations. The seasons call the shots, and there is a preference for quality produce sourced locally or even grown in the restaurant's own garden. The friendly and dedicated front-of-house team helps create the welcoming atmosphere. Delightful terrace.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13699;VEN;Germany;Dresden;Rampische Straße 9, Dresden, 01067, Germany;51.0515939;13.7429373;61;false;true;International, Modern Cuisine;This place sets itself apart with its loft vibe and a streamlined urban chic design. International cuisine inspired by the region and the seasons. Then there is the extremely friendly service. The sheltered terrace in the inner courtyard also beckons. VEN is located in the Innside by Meliá hotel, which proposes stylish guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13700;Zum Krug;Germany;Eltville am Rhein;Hauptstraße 34, Eltville am Rhein, 65347, Germany;50.0138071;8.0605839;55;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;This place has a long history that stretches back to 1720, and the Laufer family has now been at the helm for three generations. Behind the gorgeous historical façade, the cosy dining spaces exude traditional charm. Theregional and international cuisine takes its cue from the seasons, and the menu includes dishes such as a Sauerbraten (marinated pot roast) of organic pasture-fed beef with potato dumplings and cranberries. The friendly and professional waitstaff will be happy to recommend fine Rheingau wines from the estate to accompany your meal. Delightful courtyard terrace. Smart guestrooms – some are especially modern.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13701;Planerts;Germany;Leipzig;Ritterstraße 23, Leipzig, 04109, Germany;51.3416212;12.3794542;90;false;false;International, Asian Influences;Casual fine dining near the church (Nikolaikirche) and opera house (Leipzig Oper). The high ceilings, exposed ventilation shafts, urban design and open kitchen create an on-trend industrial-style interior in which to savour cuisine with Asian influences. The dishes can be combined to compose a set menu or chosen à la carte. Friendly service and good wine recommendations. Thu-Sat, lunch takes the form of a dish of the day or a three-course set menu.;Terrace;[]
13702;Grüne Gans;Germany;Kronberg im Taunus;Pferdstraße 20, Kronberg im Taunus, 61476, Germany;50.1793391;8.507493;55;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Housed in a former locksmith's shop in a building dating from 1825, this restaurant has been a culinary favourite since opening in 2007. Here in the heart of the old town, diners can look forward to French-international cuisine with seasonal influences and a cosy, modern feel. Lovers of Flammkuchen are also in for a treat. Tip for fine summer days: Head to the secluded terrace in the courtyard.;Terrace;[]
13703;Rebstock;Germany;Durbach;Halbgütle 30, Durbach, 77770, Germany;48.4905844;8.0349378;81;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Rebstock offers comfortable, country-style dining rooms, attentive service and good regional fare including snail soup, pike dumplings and venison ragout. In summer the idyllic terrace offers views of the surrounding parkland and the Black Forest, while another attraction is the large selection of home-made cakes and pastries.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13704;handicap.;Germany;Künzelsau;Hauptstraße 22, Künzelsau, 74653, Germany;49.2783931;9.6892869;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;As its name suggests, this tastefully decorated restaurant employs differently abled, and the success of this initiative is clear to see in the great team! Diners choose between two set menus: "Einerseits" (vegetarian) and "Andererseits" (with meat and fish) – one standout dish features perfectly cooked and wonderfully spicy Norway lobster, tender tête de veau, aromatic and delicately acidic sauerkraut and expertly prepared pappardelle. The stylish interior combines clean lines with artwork and features a celestial painting by Markus Schmidgall on the high ceiling. The small terrace in the courtyard is delightful on a fine summer's day.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13705;Hinterding;Germany;Lengerich;Bahnhofstraße 72, Lengerich, 49525, Germany;52.185572;7.860008;58;true;false;Classic French, Farm to table;Dating back to 1904, this spruce urban villa has been known as a stylish culinary destination for aeons. Owners Klaus Weingartz (kitchen) and Elke Zeitner (front of house) have been running this establishment with great dedication since 2011. Ambitious classic cuisine made with select ingredients is served by charming waitstaff in comfortable and elegant dining rooms with high ceilings, or out on the gorgeous terrace. Set menus can even be pre-ordered to take home. Cookery classes and overnight accommodation are also available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13706;Caro's;Germany;Tübingen;Haaggasse 10, Tübingen, 72070, Germany;48.5204512;9.05213;71;true;true;Contemporary;Once a student pub, Caro's is just a stone's throw from the beautiful Marktplatz and Rathaus. The restaurant is laid out over two floors and boasts a cosy interior featuring wood panelling and furnishings. In summer, tables are set up outside on the pavement. The menu comprises fresh contemporary cuisine, from ceviche to Iberico pork chop and sea bream, but there are also vegetarian options. Across the street, Speisekammer is a delicatessen under the same management, which sells high-quality foods and spirits.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13707;Weingärtnerhaus;Germany;Kaisheim;Schlossstraße 1, Kaisheim, 86687, Germany;48.7421623;10.8834434;46;true;true;International, Farm to table;Not only does this place promise good food, but the setting is also inviting: the restaurant is located in a lovely winegrower's house (named after the vineyards below). Built in 1542, it stands directly on the historical estate of Schloss Leitheim. Season-driven cuisine is served in a lovely, cosy interior. On Sundays and Mondays there is a more limited offering in the form of the Azubi-Menü devised by the trainee chefs. Tip: The wine list includes a number of South African vintages. Should you wish to stay overnight, the Schloss Leitheim hotel has inviting guestrooms.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13708;Alfredo;Germany;Cologne;Tunisstraße 3, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.9386146;6.9529926;77;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;If you are looking for authentic Italian cuisine in Cologne, Roberto Carturan is your man. His father, Alfredo, laid the foundations for upscale Italian cuisine in 1973, and the second generation of the Carturan family has cultivated a straightforward and minimalist style of cooking. The chef himself is responsible for the friendly, informal and elegant atmosphere: he likes to spend time with his guests and talk them through the dishes. Besides cooking, Roberto Carturan has another talent: he is a trained singer – on Friday evenings there's the "musical culinary soirée": a five-course menu with a bout of singing as the finale! One practical tip: Parking is available in the Opern Passagen shopping centre located behind the restaurant. You might also take the opportunity to see the original 4711 store with its famous carillon.;Air conditioning;[]
13709;Alte Mühle Thomas Höreth;Germany;Kobern-Gondorf;Mühlental 17, Kobern-Gondorf, 56330, Germany;50.3121654;7.4543688;88;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;With this individual and thoroughly charming establishment the Höreth family have created a wonderful retreat. The guest lounges are lovingly decorated and the inner courtyard is idyllic. This is a real gem of a place, which also has its own wine estate. Slightly higher up, charming rooms are available for guests to stay the night.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13710;Ambiente Italiano - Alte Oberförsterei - Ristorante & Trattoria;Germany;Kelsterbach;Staufenstraße 16, Kelsterbach, 65451, Germany;50.0655703;8.5298652;51;true;false;Italian, Traditional Cuisine;Dating from 1902, this inviting villa entices guests with its scenic location and excellent cuisine that caters to all tastes. In the trattoria, the menu features Italian classics, pasta made in-house or freshly caught fish, as well as a selection of pizzas. Ristorante Ambiente Italiano, meanwhile, serves more sophisticated dishes that draw on Italian influences. The terrace with its stunning views of the Main River is a summer highlight! The service is friendly and attentive. Good to know: There is a car park directly in front of the building.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13711;Gruber's Restaurant;Germany;Cologne;Clever Straße 32, Cologne, 50668, Germany;50.953173;6.9655314;43;true;false;Austrian, Modern Cuisine;Austrian cuisine is served in this charming restaurant with its various tastefully decorated rooms and pretty terrace. Whether traditional (such as the excellent schnitzels and memorable Kaiserschmarrn – shredded pancakes) or modern (Carinthian cheese noodles, pointed cabbage and blueberries), the dishes are always made from carefully chosen ingredients. More limited options, plus a schnitzel menu at lunchtime.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13712;Landgrafen;Germany;Jena;Landgrafenstieg 25, Jena, 07743, Germany;50.9366335;11.5794832;24;true;true;Country cooking, International;The restaurant close to the observation tower, also known as the Balcony of Jena, serves regional cuisine and offers a fantastic view over the city. Three individual rooms are available: country, Art Deco or honeymoon.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13713;Chambao;Germany;Heidelberg;Dreikönigstraße 1, Heidelberg, 69117, Germany;49.4132335;8.7077668;88;false;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Sharing is the focus of this appealing restaurant. Good-quality ingredients go into imaginative dishes that you can combine as you see fit to create your own set menu. Some tables afford a view into the glass-fronted kitchen. The staff are friendly and professional, and you can confidently follow the wine recommendations. Chambino bar and bistro is located diagonally opposite. Gorgeous lively terrace overlooking the Alte Brücke (Old Bridge).;Terrace;[]
13714;Die Kurfürstenstube;Germany;Heidelberg;Friedrich-Ebert-Anlage 1, Heidelberg, 69117, Germany;49.4080309;8.69533;67;false;true;Classic French, Modern Cuisine;A classic in the city! The mighty coffered ceiling and wall panelling with beautiful inlays preserve a piece of history. The cooking is classic with modern influences. Summer restaurant in season.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
13715;Heritage;Germany;Hamburg;An der Alster 52, Hamburg, 20099, Germany;53.5584787;10.0075862;60;false;true;International, Meats and Grills;Heritage offers a fantastic view of the River Alster and appetising cuisine to boot. Menu options include international dishes such as the North Sea turbot with black beluga lentils and lime Hollandaise sauce, as well some delicious smelling (thanks to the 800° US Southbend Broiler) prime mature steaks.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13716;NIKKEI NINE;Germany;Hamburg;Neuer Jungfernstieg 9, Hamburg, 20354, Germany;53.5557705;9.9917573;53;true;true;Japanese, Peruvian;You should not hesitate to make a reservation at this culinary hotspot in Hamburg. Located in the luxurious Fairmont Hotel Vier Jahreszeiten, the restaurant has a stylish and elegant ambience, courtesy of an interior done out in dark wood, cream and gold tones. On the menu: Japanese-international fusion cuisine. The service is very friendly and attentive. They also have a cool bar.;;[]
13717;CARALEON;Germany;Wasserburg am Bodensee;Halbinselstraße 70, Wasserburg am Bodensee, 88142, Germany;47.5686765;9.6314751;87;true;true;Classic Cuisine, International;This tastefully designed restaurant is housed in the small boutique hotel of the same name, which enjoys a fabulous location in the Wasserburger Bucht and boasts stunning lake views. It specialises in modern European cuisine infused with authentic Peruvian influences. There is a small selection of à la carte options as well as a five-course set menu (by advance booking only) – the chefs themselves serve the dishes, adding a distinctive personal touch. The 300 labels on offer showcase wines from Bordeaux to Slovakia. Alternatively, there is a good range of non-alcoholic drinks to accompany your food. Every Sunday from 12pm to 6.30pm is "Family & Friends", when à la carte classics are served, such as parihuela (Peruvian bouillabaisse), Wiener schnitzel or Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancakes). Tip: Head to the Sunset Lounge for a nightcap by the lake.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13718;Zum Adler;Germany;Bünde;Moltkestrasse 1, Bünde, 32257, Germany;52.1958268;8.5870207;21;true;true;Contemporary, Meats and Grills;Bearing its name of old, this modern restaurant carries on the tradition of the original 19C Zum Adler inn. Today it is lovely and light inside, with a smart and minimalist decor. The focus lies squarely on high-quality meat, such as Wagyu beef steak. Fish and vegan options also available. At lunchtime there is a smaller offer with a reasonably priced lunch menu - but you can also choose from the steak menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13719;Brechtmanns Bistro;Germany;Hamburg;Erikastraße 43, Hamburg, 20251, Germany;53.593061;9.9871201;98;false;true;Asian Influences;Brechtmanns is an extremely popular, friendly minimalist-style modern bistro serving Asian-inspired dishes as well as regional cuisine. We recommend trying the dishes prepared from the Oldenburg duck. In summer, meals are also served outside.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13720;Eiden Restaurant;Germany;Bad Zwischenahn;Eiden 9, Bad Zwischenahn, 26160, Germany;53.1887383;8.0331347;54;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;The location of this hunting lodge, set amid almost 25 acres of parkland, is superb. The lovely restaurant includes a conservatory and a wonderful garden terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13721;Kamino;Germany;Häusern;Sankt-Fridolin-Straße 1, Häusern, 79837, Germany;47.7536248;8.1686661;78;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Country cooking;The Zumkeller family have transformed what was once Chämi-Hüsli into this cosy restaurant and tapas bar – the striking fireplace with extended flue after which Kamino is named presides in the middle of the dining area, which has a high ceiling and a round floor plan. The classic and Mediterranean cuisine always has a modern touch and a certain pizazz. Dishes such as roasted sea bass fillet with home-made tagliarini and lobster cream give the tasty tapas a run for their money. The icing on the cake is the charming service provided by owner Stefanie Zumkeller and her team. For an overnight stay, there are three pretty and cosy guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13722;Puricelli;Germany;Trechtingshausen;Burgweg 24, Trechtingshausen, 55413, Germany;50.0058373;7.8535208;34;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Here you can enjoy seasonal, regional and Mediterranean cuisine in a wonderful location. On the menu, for instance, supreme of Eifeler Prachthahn (cockerel), tagliatelle, basil sauce, sautéed green vegetables. Inside, a friendly, pared-down ambience, modern with rustic touches, from the terrace you have a view of the Rhine. The wine list showcases the surrounding region.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13723;Weinbistro "George";Germany;Schwerin;Schusterstraße 13, Schwerin, 19053, Germany;53.6281702;11.4139904;93;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This bistro is definitely worth a visit. The second dining option in the Weinhaus Uhle hotel is a wine shop and appealing restaurant that is open all day in one. Seated at bare wooden tables in an attractive space, you are served tasty dishes made from regional produce, such as "Der Pilzgarten" (The Mushroom Garden) – mushrooms from the Helvesiek mushroom garden in cream with bread dumplings. And of course, Müritz zander is also on the menu. Decent wine list. In summer, there are tables laid out front on the street.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13724;Wolfs Junge;Germany;Hamburg;Zimmerstraße 30, Hamburg, 22085, Germany;53.5747264;10.017785;21;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;The accent here is on sustainable, regional cuisine, the very epitome of “nose to tail” eating. The ingredients are sourced from selected producers with some of the vegetables and herbs grown by the restaurant itself. Serves simple midday fare such as home-made bratwurst and an ambitious, creative set menu including Angeln Saddleback, kimchi and fermented onion in the evenings.;Terrace;[]
13725;east;Germany;Hamburg;Simon-von-Utrecht-Straße 31, Hamburg, 20359, Germany;53.5510846;9.9652099;79;true;true;Fusion;This restaurant, housed in the stylish hotel of the same name, is quite striking on account of the fantastic industrial architecture of the former iron foundry and the slick, chic interior. The centrepiece here in what was once the factory hall is the sushi counter. The menu features modern international dishes. A tip for meat lovers: fine steaks from the Southbend Grill.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13726;Zipang;Germany;Hamburg;Eppendorfer Weg 171, Hamburg, 20253, Germany;53.5796608;9.9663367;38;true;true;Japanese;The minimalist interior at Zipang has clean lines, muted colours and a smart silver sheen. This makes a perfect match for chef Toshiharu Minami’s mix of traditional and modern Japanese cooking styles. The restaurant is popular with Japanese diners – always a good sign.;Notable sake list;[]
13727;Meet & Eat by Sandro;Germany;Tuttlingen;Donaustraße 30, Tuttlingen, 78532, Germany;47.9855817;8.8180215;33;false;true;Meats and Grills, International;Hotel Stadt Tuttlingen is located on the Rathaussteg across the Danube, and on the ground floor you will find this pared-back, modern restaurant. The star of the ambitious cuisine is dry-aged beef. But on the menu you will also find dishes such as roast turbot and potato, kohlrabi, red wine butter. To the front of the house is the covered terrace facing the pedestrian area.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13728;Gänsweid;Germany;Wertingen;Gänsweid 1, Wertingen, 86637, Germany;48.5603083;10.6833391;19;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;In this carefully restored former garage, it is a case of ‘olive oil not engine oil’! Enjoy your meal in a relaxed atmosphere where you can watch the cooks preparing their fresh mixture of Swabian and Mediterranean dishes in the kitchen. Simple, good value menu only at lunchtimes.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13730;Lammershof Stuben;Germany;Birkenau;Absteinacher Straße 2, Birkenau, 69488, Germany;49.5507141;8.737863;63;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;To start with, the location on a 45ha estate is terrific. The cosy space with a tiled stove that draws the eye exudes rustic charm and a certain chic. Specialities include various dishes featuring meat from bison they have reared on their own farm. Note: On Mondays only bison burgers, or veggie burgers, are served. Tip: the marvellous terrace with a view of the countryside! The small Lammershof hotel, the main building of which dates from 1709, has cosy guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13731;Jagdhaus Waldfrieden;Germany;Bilsen;Kieler Straße 1, Bilsen, 25485, Germany;53.7551635;9.8812269;38;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Choose whether to enjoy your meal in the cosy dining room with its open fireplace, in the airy conservatory or on the lovely terrace shaded by trees… This restaurant is a charming location in which to sample good regional food: the menu includes dishes such as Glückstädter Matjes (PDO preserved herring) or fillet of wild boar, cooked rare in a juniper berry jus. Tip: The lunch set menu is an excellent deal. Should you wish to stay overnight, the pretty guestrooms are very inviting and all individually decorated.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13732;Alois-Anton Kaminrestaurant;Germany;Rottach-Egern;Aribostraße 19, Rottach-Egern, 83700, Germany;47.6943171;11.7539287;35;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;A good alternative to the fine dining restaurant of the Park-Hotel Egerner Höfe. The choice is yours: dine in the cosy Bavarian-style dining rooms dubbed "Alois" and "Anton" or in the more upmarket Kaminrestaurant. Just as charming is the terrace, which is sheltered from the wind and has a view of the pastures and mountains. Either way, you can enjoy cordial service and regional and seasonal dishes in a pleasantly laid-back atmosphere.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13733;Pierburg - Erika Bergheim;Germany;Essen;Schmachtenbergstraße 184, Essen, 45219, Germany;51.3803839;6.9519292;73;true;false;Farm to table, International;Located in the rural outskirts of Essen, Pierburg has been welcoming diners since 1901. With many years of experience in the top league of gastronomy under her belt, Erika Bergheim is now at the helm, cooking up internationally and seasonally inspired dishes. You can choose from the à la carte selection, named "Pierburg Karte", or opt for the "Selection E.B." set menu – the individual courses can be ordered à la carte, too. There is also an extensive, well-curated wine list. Friendly service and a tasteful contemporary setting, with certain tables affording a glimpse into the kitchen. Gorgeous terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13734;Redüttchen;Germany;Bonn;Kurfürstenallee 1, Bonn, 53117, Germany;50.6818185;7.1526005;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;What was once the gardener's cottage at the 18C La Redoute ballroom and concert hall is a feel-good place that has won over more than its fair share of regulars. The restaurant's appeal lies not only in its extremely charming ambience, but also in Matthias Pietsch's innovative take on modern cuisine and the experienced, courteous and cordial service. The pleasant dining area is laid out over two levels, and the terrace to the rear of the building is also a lovely spot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13735;CARLS Brasserie an der Elbphilharmonie;Germany;Hamburg;Am Kaiserkai 69, Hamburg, 20457, Germany;53.540996;9.9858449;26;false;false;German;As you take in the view of the Elbe River and the Elbphilharmonie concert hall, you can soak up the lively and casual yet elegant brasserie atmosphere and enjoy sophisticated North German cuisine such as fish stew or whole sole. The unique location means that window seats are in demand. And in summer, diners make a beeline for the terrace. The bistro next door serves bowls and tartines. A wine bar is also part of the premises.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13736;Caroussel Nouvelle;Germany;Dresden;Königstraße 14, Dresden, 01097, Germany;51.0610555;13.741642;78;true;true;Contemporary;In the attractive Hotel Bülow Palais in Dresden's Baroque quarter, the bistro and winter garden have been combined in the Caroussel Nouvelle, with a stylish interior by star designer Carlo Rampazzi. The "Classics" menu is available for lunch and dinner, along with two "Gourmet" set menus (one is vegetarian) in the evening – also with à la carte options. Palais Bar and Cigar Lounge for aperitif or digestif.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13737;Puricelli;Germany;Lieser;Moselstraße 33, Lieser, 54470, Germany;49.91729;7.01963;66;false;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;In keeping with the historical setting of the lavishly renovated 19C Schloss Lieser (the striking faÇade of which is quite something), Puricelli has a high cross-vaulted ceiling, lovely old wooden flooring, crystal chandeliers and stylish furniture. The view through the picture windows takes in the garden and the Moselle. Contemporary classic cuisine is offered. The wine list includes bottles from the hotel's own vineyard. Pretty guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
13738;20zwanzig;Germany;Südharz;Thyrahöhe 24, Südharz, 06536, Germany;51.5654722;10.9614739;15;false;false;Farm to table, International;Nestled in a quiet location on the outskirts of town, Hotel Freiwerk's core building is a spruce half-timbered villa dating from 1894. Its restaurant, 20zwanzig, is housed in the modern extension, built in 2020. The chic, trendy interior has a large window front that affords a splendid view of the surrounding greenery. You can order the contemporary seasonal cuisine à la carte or opt for a surprise menu comprising a variable number of courses. Friendly and well-trained waitstaff.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13739;Chang Bistro;Germany;Munich;Wolfratshauser Straße 268, Munich, 81479, Germany;48.0719453;11.5193181;20;false;false;Asian;This smart and trendy bistro version of the main restaurant, Chang, in Grünwald features mostly Thai cuisine and dishes with influences from Japan. Here, too, the emphasis is on high-quality ingredients. The Thai curries as well as the sushi can be highly recommended. At lunchtime there is also a daily changing lunch menu. Lovely terrace, as well as covered winter garden-style dining space.;Terrace;[]
13740;Hartmaier's Villa;Germany;Ettlingen;Pforzheimer Straße 67, Ettlingen, 76275, Germany;48.9394284;8.4166417;75;false;true;International, Farm to table;This modern restaurant is housed in a pretty villa dating back to 1816. The Hartmaier family and their team have been serving up good food here for many years. The menu is wide-ranging, characterised by seasonal, regional and international influences – from Zwiebelrostbraten (steak with onion rings), beans with bacon and roast potatoes to wild-caught Icelandic redfish fillet with pak choi and spinach and ricotta ravioli. At lunchtime, people flock here for the bargain set menu with a choice of starters and mains. The feel of the place is both elegant and more casual, with a lovely leafy terrace in front of the building. Tip: You can buy wines to take home at their Vinothek.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13743;Adler;Germany;Wangen im Allgäu;Obere Dorfstraße 4, Wangen im Allgäu, 88239, Germany;47.6925896;9.8537702;71;false;false;Country cooking, International;Ambitious, fresh and unfussy are the terms that best describe the mixture of regional and international cuisine offered by Uwe Zöller at this slightly out-of-town restaurant. Front of house, friendly Anne-Kathrin Zöller serves a range of dishes including scallops with Thai curry, and duo of lamb on a bed of wild garlic pesto with Barolo jus.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13744;Alte Feuerwache;Germany;Würselen;Oppener Straße 115, Würselen, 52146, Germany;50.811896;6.1410692;90;true;true;Country cooking;Linear design, a relaxed atmosphere, as well as competent service and good food make this restaurant so popular. See into the kitchen and watch the tasty seasonal, regional and international dishes being prepared.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13746;Strandhaus;Germany;Bonn;Georgstraße 28, Bonn, 53111, Germany;50.7422977;7.0915618;81;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A beach house (Strandhaus) right in the heart of Bonn – who would have thought? The delightful maritime decor and laid-back atmosphere transport you to a seaside retreat. Not forgetting the cosy secluded terrace. This is the perfect setting for a Mediterranean-influenced cuisine, with fish at the heart of it all. Using only the finest ingredients, the chef creates flavoursome dishes with a unique twist, available both à la carte and as a tasting menu. As well as fish, there are meat options and a dedicated vegetarian set menu.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13747;PIER 6;Germany;Bremerhaven;Barkhausenstraße 6, Bremerhaven, 27568, Germany;53.5475404;8.5724056;44;true;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;In this stylish restaurant located in the Havenwelten quarter, a friendly front-of-house team serves modern international cuisine. This is made with produce from the region and the menu is determined by the seasons. In addition, there is an inexpensive lunch menu. The window seats and terrace are especially coveted – the view of the New Harbour is beautiful. Given the popularity of this place, it's definitely best to book in advance.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13748;Pfälzer Stube;Germany;Herxheim;Hauptstraße 62, Herxheim, 76863, Germany;49.1237502;8.2045296;16;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Pfälzer Stube is as important for the gorgeous Krone hotel as the hotel is for the town of Herxheim-Hayna. Centrally located, this is a traditional, family-run business. The space has ample charm, with diners comfortably seated at attractively set tables inside, or, in summer, out on the leafy terrace. On the menu: regional and seasonal food with Italian influences – in keeping with the chef's roots, although he also puts a distinctly modern spin on proceedings. Dishes such as "roasted Venetian calf's liver, tagliolini, Blutwurst, apple, shallot" can be selected à la carte or you can combine three or four courses to create your own set menu.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13749;Landhaus Halferschenke;Germany;Dieblich;Hauptstraße 63, Dieblich, 56332, Germany;50.3156792;7.4723406;31;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;In this beautiful quarry-stone building dating from 1832, the Schmah family serve ambitious cuisine that revolves around top-notch ingredients and the seasons – from sole meunière and Aubrac beef to oysters and turbot from Brittany. You can opt to dine à la carte or go for a set menu. In addition to the food, diners can look forward to attentive service in a tasteful setting with a country-house feel. In summer, the gorgeous terrace beckons. In addition, MA PETITE CHAMBRE is a small gourmet haven serving a set menu. They have four well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
13750;Sawito;Germany;Falkensee;Spandauer Straße 14, Falkensee, 14612, Germany;52.5645708;13.112693;66;false;true;Farm to table, International;In this pleasant restaurant done out in a timeless, refined style, chef Marco Wahl injects quality, flavour and personality into seasonal dishes – this is where the Palatinate-born chef's experience in some prestigious establishments comes into play. You can dine à la carte or opt for the set menu. Tuesday to Thursday (except public holidays) they also offer a surprise menu with three to four courses. The fact that you feel in good hands here is also down to the very friendly service team under the management of Patrik Schwabe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13751;Kantiners;Germany;Delbrück;Graf-Sporck-Straße 34, Delbrück, 33129, Germany;51.7700459;8.5570797;75;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, French;Hotel Waldkrug is a traditional family business in a green and leafy location, and its restaurant is tastefully designed with modern touches. The menu includes good modern bistro dishes in a French vein – think beef carpaccio, Caesar salad or grilled steaks – but also traditional regional dishes, such as beef consommé with marrow dumplings, or schnitzel. In addition, they have pretty terraces at the front and to the rear of the building. The cosy Barstube in the front area is another really lovely option.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13752;Das Alte Haus;Germany;Brunswick;Alte Knochenhauerstraße 11, Brunswick, 38100, Germany;52.2605145;10.5164179;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this attractive, cosy yet modern restaurant, the cooking is ambitious and creative with international influences. You can put together dishes from the menu to create a set meal with the number of courses of your choice, to be accompanied by an extensive selection of fine German wines. There is also a pairing menu. Delightful terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13753;bistronauten;Germany;Weinheim;Kopernikusstraße 43, Weinheim, 69469, Germany;49.5489714;8.6653164;85;true;false;Farm to table;A word to the wise: make sure you book, as this really appealing restaurant is always busy! Housed in an old railway station dating from 1903, the atmosphere is laid-back, the decor modern with industrial charm and the food excellent. On the blackboard there is a seasonal set menu – choose between meat, fish and vegetarian for the main course. They also have a selection of German wines. Dine at the counter to watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13754;Gasthof Kreuz;Germany;Bad Waldsee;Gut-Betha-Platz 1, Bad Waldsee, 88339, Germany;47.9213167;9.7520982;97;false;false;Country cooking, Home Cooking;This traditional hotel and restaurant located at the edge of the pedestrian area has a gorgeous terrace overlooking the Gut Betha Fountain. On the menu: regional and seasonal cuisine, including locally hunted game. In addition to à la carte dishes, there is an inexpensive three-course set menu ("Regiomenü"), to be relished in a pleasant atmosphere. The wine list has some surprising rarities in store, and the service is cordial and attentive. They offer several immaculate guestrooms in the building itself, plus holiday apartments within walking distance. You can park free of charge just a few minutes' walk away (Parkplatz Bleiche).;Terrace;[]
13755;79 °;Germany;Wuppertal;Luisenstraße 61, Wuppertal, 42103, Germany;51.2566359;7.1377784;56;false;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant is located in the Elberfeld district in a narrow street full of eateries, bars and small shops. With its unpretentious, trendy decor, the friendly and laid-back service, as well as its ambitious cuisine, this place is a hit! The dishes are modern and seasonal, drawing on Mediterranean and classical influences, from pickled Arctic char, elderflower tomato stock and tarragon oil to wild mushrooms, mashed potatoes, chives and nut butter foam. You have the option to create your own set menu – conventional or vegetarian. Lovely courtyard.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13756;Taverna & Trattoria Palio;Germany;Celle;Hannoversche Straße 55, Celle, 29221, Germany;52.6205673;10.0757669;90;true;true;Italian;Palio offers fresh Italian fare from the open kitchen in a relaxed trattoria-style atmosphere – you simply have to try one of the pasta dishes! The seasonal set menus are also interesting. There’s also a lovely terrace in the shade of some old chestnut trees.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13758;Adler;Germany;Brackenheim;Hindenburgstraße 4, Brackenheim, 74336, Germany;49.0649146;9.065938;25;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Here, traditional Swabian cuisine meets global influences, blending local and international flavours. Enjoy cordial service in the comfort of either the main dining room steeped in history or the charming inner courtyard. The kitchen serves up seasonally influenced dishes. One of the most tempting dishes is the house classic: Swabian Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) with maultaschen, spaetzle and salad. Chic guestrooms are available for overnight stays. On Tuesday evenings, the restaurant is only open to hotel patrons.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13759;Al Pappagallo;Germany;Bremen;Außer der Schleifmühle 73, Bremen, 28203, Germany;53.0789562;8.8240668;69;false;false;Italian;You will feel at ease in this elegant restaurant with a lovely bright winter garden and also wonderful outdoor garden. The kitchen serves classic Italian dishes, prepared with very good produce – a particular highlight is the pasta. Friendly service.;Terrace;[]
13760;Asam Schlössl;Germany;Munich;Maria-Einsiedel-Straße 45, Munich, 81379, Germany;48.0954111;11.542264;52;false;true;Bavarian, International;Shane McMahon is no stranger to Munich's gastronomy scene. In his charming restaurant just outside the city centre, the Irish-born chef serves tasty Bavarian cuisine into which he skilfully weaves his personal touch. Here you will find pub classics, but also modern dishes, as well as steaks barbecued in the Big Green Egg.;Terrace;[]
13761;Johann Grill;Germany;Berchtesgaden;Hintereck 1, Berchtesgaden, 83471, Germany;47.63407;13.0468268;23;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Overlooking Berchtesgaden, surrounded by stunning natural beauty and with a magnificent mountain backdrop, the location is to die for! At the restaurant of the luxurious Kempinski Hotel Berchtesgaden, you can enjoy delicious seasonal cuisine made with fresh, local ingredients. For dessert, we highly recommend the Eckerbichl-Haustorte! The sleek, modern interior design is a draw in itself. Incidentally, the restaurant is named after the first person to climb the east face of the Watzmann and Germany's first official mountain guide. Hotel guests can even take in the panoramic view here at breakfast.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13762;Genussschmiede;Germany;Pirk;Rathausplatz 6, Pirk, 92712, Germany;49.6344545;12.1638926;57;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This blacksmith's shop dating back to 1682 is now devoted to modern cuisine that follows the seasons and draws on fresh, mainly regional ingredients. The interior is pleasingly trendy and minimalist, with a dining area laid out beneath a high steel ceiling. Diners choose between a 5-course set menu and à la carte dishes. Vegetarians are also well catered for on the menu.;Terrace;[]
13763;Staudi's;Germany;Düsseldorf;Münsterstraße 115, Düsseldorf, 40476, Germany;51.245184;6.7891653;16;true;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Once a butcher's, now a pretty little restaurant with a bistro feel. Decorative relics of the past such as tiled floors and stained glass in the ceiling make for a charming interior. Diners also enjoy cordial service and seasonal dishes with a modern twist – order à la carte or opt for the five-course set menu complete with wine pairings. A vegetarian alternative is available, too. From earlyNovember to early December, only the goose set menu is served on Wednesdays. "Fondue Chinoise" in winter has to be booked one day in advance. Tip: Stube can be booked as a separate room for private events (Nov-Mar).;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13765;Café GUPI;Germany;Weil am Rhein;Römerstraße 1, Weil am Rhein, 79576, Germany;47.5948316;7.6290732;58;false;false;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Set up in what was the gardener's house on a historical country estate, this is the trendy restaurant-bar concept of the Düster and Schneider restaurateur and winemaking families. Their tasty modern dishes made with seasonal ingredients are served à la carte or as a set menu. In summer, the terrace shaded by the large trees of the lovely Läublin Park is highly inviting. The name of the restaurant is derived from the regional "GuPi" wines (Gutedel and Pinot Noir). Tip: Booking advisable.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13766;riva;Germany;Deidesheim;Weinstraße 12, Deidesheim, 67146, Germany;49.4103944;8.1864567;21;false;true;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Housed in Kaisergarten Hotel – the sister establishment of Ketschauer Hof, also located in central Deidesheim – this restaurant has a sleek interior done out in light natural tones. In this setting, pleasingly laid-back, friendly and professional waitstaff serve up delicious international and Mediterranean cuisine. The menu also features barbecued meats prepared on the Big Green Egg, along with options for fans of pizza. The selection of wines from the hotel group's own vineyards is excellent. RIVA Bar-Lounge is the perfect spot for a cocktail. The terrace overlooking the garden is delightful in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13767;Landhaus Rössle;Germany;Bretzfeld;Mainhardter Straße 26, Bretzfeld, 74626, Germany;49.1191957;9.5207516;74;false;true;Classic French, International;Expect ambitious cuisine is in a classic/French vein with regional and seasonal influences – dishes include the likes of seared scallops on orange fennel, and the classic Zwiebelrostbraten (beef and onions in gravy). You can dine à la carte or opt for the set menu – available in an omnivore or vegetarian version. Attentive and charming service is the forte of the lady of the house. The interior is modern and elegant, and in winter tables by the fireplace are very much in demand. In summer, the garden terrace is a boon. There are attractive rooms for overnight guests.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13768;Tomatissimo;Germany;Bielefeld;Am Tie 15, Bielefeld, 33619, Germany;52.044776;8.4398812;67;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;This popular restaurant with a friendly atmosphere lies slightly outside the city, in a small village. In summer you can make the most of the wonderful terrace by the village fountain, in the shade of the chestnut trees. Bernhard Grubmüller and his kitchen team serve up various set menus and à la carte dishes, including dry-aged beef from their own maturing cabinet, plus delicious offerings such as braised veal cheek, morels & peas, potato waffle & wild garlic. Tip: Bernhard's Küchentisch, the chef's table, for smaller groups (on prior reservation).;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13769;Bocca di Bacco;Germany;Berlin;Friedrichstraße 167, Berlin, 10117, Germany;52.5152094;13.3890234;57;true;false;Italian;On the outside, a smart historical façade, on the inside an attractively modern and elegant restaurant complete with bar and lounge. Visible through its glass panes, the kitchen turns out Italian cooking. Needless to say, the pasta is home-made. To be paired with one of their great Tuscan wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
13770;136;Germany;Berlin;Linienstraße 136, Berlin, 10115, Germany;52.5263173;13.3887518;28;true;false;Fusion, Creative;The name of the game here is a culinary fusion of Peru and Italy. Drawing on his Peruvian heritage and inspired by life in Italy, head chef Matias Diaz weaves together produce from both countries in his "136 Experience Menü", a set menu that changes every two months. The restaurant's trendy vintage decor brims with charm. In summer, there are also tables outside.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13771;Restaurant 1463;Germany;Karlsruhe;Friedrichstraße 10, Karlsruhe, 76229, Germany;49.0087227;8.4974951;75;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This building, dating from 1463, exudes rustic charm both inside and out. Dark wood finishings and low ceilings add to the cosy feel of the two small dining spaces on the first floor. The secluded terrace in the quiet courtyard is also delightful. Verena and Henning Weick, your cordial hosts, run the establishment as a team – she handles service, he is in charge of the kitchen. Diners can choose between two set menus (with optional wine pairings), and each course can also be found in the tempting à la carte selection. There are six lovely comfortable apartments for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
13772;Villa Rothschild Grill & Health;Germany;Königstein im Taunus;Im Rothschildpark 1, Königstein im Taunus, 61462, Germany;50.1837413;8.473785;54;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in a park, this smart bankers' villa dating from 1894 is home to a stylish boutique hotel as well as this chic, modern and elegant restaurant. Patrick Bittner, who previously made a name for himself at Frankfurt's Français, where he was head chef for many years, is now at the helm here. The classic cuisine has international influences, and the dishes are served à la carte. Good news for oyster enthusiasts: There are always three varieties to choose from. The modern and elegant interior is tastefully decorated, with a striking open fireplace in the centre of the room serving as the focal point and creating a wonderful atmosphere in winter. In summer, the lovely terrace beckons. Tip: Head to Titian's Bar for a digestif. Lunch is also available on Sundays – ideal for day trippers.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13773;Die Reichsstadt;Germany;Gengenbach;Engelgasse 33, Gengenbach, 77723, Germany;48.4049209;8.0152034;16;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;This is the restaurant of the chic hotel of the same name, which provides the historical backdrop for your meal. The tasteful dining area is done out with high-end furnishings and a modern touch. Staff are friendly and professional as they set about serving you with fine Baden classics, modernised French dishes and various set menus, including a vegetarian one. In summer, the garden is magical!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13774;The Wild Duck;Germany;Hanover;Podbielskistraße 167, Hanover, 30177, Germany;52.3982545;9.7737357;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This young and fresh addition to Hanover's fine dining scene is proving to be a hit – and with good reason. Part of the appeal is the upscale and tastefully trendy decor. Diners are also drawn by the modern and pleasingly pared-down dishes (eg cucumber and cherry or duck and parsnip), from which you can create your own three- to five-course dinner menu. Vegetarian and vegan options are available, too. The friendly waitstaff will gladly recommend the perfect wine accompaniment.;;[]
13775;Mühlenhof;Germany;Friesenheim;Oberweierer Hauptstraße 33, Friesenheim, 77948, Germany;48.376981;7.8996992;57;true;false;Country cooking, Home Cooking;It is little wonder that Anette and Stefan Rottler's hotel is so popular: Their restaurant serves classic Baden dishes made with top-quality ingredients – from snail soup to pork fillet in cream of mushroom sauce to Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy). The smaller dishes and reasonably priced set menu of the day are also much in demand. The wine list is dedicated to local labels. Friendly and attentive service. Food is served in various dining rooms, some with a cosy, regional feel, others with a fresh and modern look. Delightful covered terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13776;Phaedra;Germany;Cologne;Elsaßstraße 30, Cologne, 50677, Germany;50.920468;6.9579396;55;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Are you in the mood for Mediterranean cuisine with Greek influences? Then try, for example, the fried halibut with a chive beurre blanc and trout caviar or the house-made mezze – to share or as a starter. Good produce is used, including meat from Franz Keller and wild-caught prawns. The place has an appealingly trendy bistro look and a pleasantly relaxed atmosphere. Diners take their seats at regular tables or high tables – the latter offer partial views into the open kitchen. Tip for motorists: public multi-storey car park opposite.;;[]
13777;Medici;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Weißadlergasse 2, Frankfurt on the Main, 60311, Germany;50.1117384;8.6790019;90;false;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Two brothers are your hosts in this city centre restaurant. International dishes with a Mediterranean influence are served in a modern atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13779;Bistro Villa Merton;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Am Leonhardsbrunn 12, Frankfurt on the Main, 60487, Germany;50.1271537;8.6534917;79;true;true;Country cooking, International;Located just outside Frankfurt, north of the Palmengarten, Bistro Villa Merton is a lovely alternative to the fine dining restaurant. While the latter welcomes diners in the evening, the bistro is only open at lunchtime. In the spruce villa built in neo-Baroque style, you can take a seat in an inviting decor done out with an elegant touch to enjoy high-quality regional and international cuisine infused with seasonal influences. An appealing lunchtime set menu is on offer, as well as several à la carte options. The appetising dishes include breast and leg of guinea fowl and classics such as Wiener schnitzel made with veal. Excellent wine recommendations are to be had from the friendly and knowledgeable front-of-house team. Tip: There is a fantastic selection of champagnes. The terrace is also a pleasant place to sit. Good to know: Regular events are also held here.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13780;Brasserie;Germany;Glücksburg;Uferstraße 1, Glücksburg, 24960, Germany;54.8225633;9.4998586;98;true;true;International;Temporarily closed for renovation.If you don’t fancy the gourmet cuisine on offer at Meierei, you can enjoy fresh, international fare or just a slice of home-made cake in the less formal atmosphere of the Brasserie.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13781;Schlossberg;Germany;Homburg;Schloßberg-Höhen-Straße, Homburg, 66424, Germany;49.3206047;7.3435852;19;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;The location on the Schlossberg (castle hill) is fantastic in its own right: located right beside the Vauban fortress, the business hotel that houses this restaurant overlooks the city and affords a one-of-a-kind view – best enjoyed from the terrace. However, the interior is also delightful with its sleek contemporary design, coupled with panoramic vistas through the expansive windows. The seasonal cuisine can be enjoyed as a set menu or ordered à la carte.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13783;Die Pfarrwirtschaft;Germany;Endingen am Kaiserstuhl;Hauptstraße 2, Endingen am Kaiserstuhl, 79346, Germany;48.1415903;7.7074253;82;false;false;Country cooking, International;This is not just Thomas Merkle's second restaurant, but a hotspot in its own right. The tasty food is wonderfully unpretentious and based on very good ingredients. Tip: Try one of the Black Forest beef dishes. The burgers are also very popular. In addition, the restaurant proposes an interesting weekly menu. Your meal here is enhanced by friendly and attentive service, a pleasingly informal vibe and a really modern aesthetic with a rustic edge. Needless to say, guests find themselves drawn to the beautiful garden in summer. In short, a place that fosters a feeling of well-being!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13784;Haus Bosen;Germany;Erftstadt;Herriger Straße 2, Erftstadt, 50374, Germany;50.8002567;6.7645585;46;true;false;Classic Cuisine, International;This cosy half-timbered house, a restaurant for more than 120 years, now offers Mediterranean, regional and classic fare including squid Mallorcan style, vintage sardines with sourdough bread, Königsberger Klopse (meatballs in white sauce with capers) and braised pigs’ cheeks.;;[]
13785;Mon Amie Maxi;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Bockenheimer Landstraße 31, Frankfurt on the Main, 60325, Germany;50.1163306;8.6671502;49;true;false;French, Traditional Cuisine;Housed in a villa dating from 1925, this restaurant is chic, almost opulent – the wonderfully lively atmosphere is complemented by friendly, attentive and adept service. To the side is Raw Bar, and there is an open kitchen. The menu features French cuisine, including oysters, lobster cocktail, offal dishes and high-quality barbecued steak. Good, exclusive wine selection.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13786;XO Seafoodbar;Germany;Hamburg;Paul-Roosen-Straße 22, Hamburg, 20038, Germany;53.5531921;9.9583347;29;false;true;Seafood, Vegetarian;As well as haebel, just across the street, Fabio Haebel runs this trendy, laid-back establishment in the heart of St Pauli. Spread over two floors, the restaurant has an agreeably lively atmosphere. Upstairs there are also a few seats at a counter facing the open kitchen. The cuisine is modern with seafood specialties and vegetarian dishes. Options include daily specials and classics such as tinned sardines in oil with new potatoes, quark and dill. Alternatively, you could opt for "Chef's Choice" – a selection of items to be shared, picked from the menu by the kitchen team. There is also a small cocktail bar and a lovely terrace where you can enjoy the hustle and bustle.;Terrace;[]
13787;Landhaus am See;Germany;Garbsen;Seeweg 27, Garbsen, 30827, Germany;52.4337814;9.5870768;78;false;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;A pleasant dining experience: a lovely country-style interior, great terrace and views of the garden and lake. The food is seasonal and regional. You can also get hold of your own copy of their recipe book. For overnight guests, there are really pretty, individually decorated rooms available.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13788;Zum Goldenen Engel;Germany;Glottertal;Friedhofweg 2, Glottertal, 79286, Germany;48.0497322;7.94065;83;true;true;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;This traditional 16C inn right next to the church has been rebuilt in a way that is absolutely true to the original. You will feel completely at home in the lovingly decorated restaurant, thanks not only to the atmosphere and the competent, charming front-of-house team, but also of course to the high-quality food. Many ingredients come from the region. Plus they have cosy guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13789;Gasthaus Landbrecht;Germany;Freising;Freisinger Straße 1, Freising, 85354, Germany;48.440592;11.7234713;37;true;false;Farm to table;A typical Bavarian country house, home to this rustic restaurant serving tasty, locally grown produce.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13790;Eiflers Zeiten;Germany;Euskirchen;Burg Flamersheim, Euskirchen, 53881, Germany;50.6224572;6.850706;24;true;true;Country cooking, International;The pleasant, rustic-style alternative to Bembergs Häuschen has a distinctly cosy feel. The menu features mouthwatering regional classics such as roast Eifel beef with roast potatoes, as well as internationally influenced dishes such as cod with a lemon crunch topping and Chinese cabbage. There are also daily changing specials. The two chandeliers fashioned from bottles are sure to draw the eye! The view through the windowed façade onto the pond is also lovely.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13791;Weinhaus Tante Anna;Germany;Düsseldorf;Andreasstraße 2, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.2270195;6.7736603;99;false;true;Country cooking;This traditional family business is now in its seventh generation. Here you dine in the impressive historical setting of a 16C former chapel – the 1 000-year-old granite column by the counter is well worth seeing! The menu features sophisticated regional dishes, which can be accompanied by your choice from a large selection of German wines.;Interesting wine list;[]
13792;Rôtisserie Jagdhof Stuben;Germany;Bad Laasphe;Glashütter Straße 20, Bad Laasphe, 57334, Germany;50.9207825;8.2799771;55;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Meats and Grills;The cosiness and rustic charm of the Rôtisserie at the upscale Jagdhof Glashütte hotel are almost unparalleled – a wealth of wood panelling and beams, a roaring fireplace and the decorative remnants of what was perhaps the original kitchen all play their part. Factor in the amiable owner, Edmund Dornhöfer, and the attentive front-of-house team, too. Chef Petar Popovic delivers a wide range of classics. Excellent recommendations include "Petar's bouillabaisse" and the char-grilled veal chop with fresh chanterelles.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13793;Schwanen;Germany;Köngen;Schwanenstraße 1, Köngen, 73257, Germany;48.6847652;9.3637585;43;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;This family business has been going for three generations. The dishes served in this chic, modern restaurant are made with preference for regional produce and sing with freshness and flavour. For a bistro alternative, Karl Benz Stube has a short menu featuring traditional Swabian fare. There are also suitable spaces for special occasions available and practical guestrooms with contemporary decor. Tip: the "Kultur & Genuss" events.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13794;MIZU Sushi-Bar;Germany;Kreuth;Wiesseer Straße 1, Kreuth, 83700, Germany;47.6862885;11.7582897;71;true;false;Japanese, Sushi;Located in the Spa & Resort Bachmair Weissach, not far from Lake Tegernsee, this restaurant boasts an understated Far-Eastern design. It serves a combination of classic and modern Japanese cuisine. Traditional sashimi and nigiri or tempura dishes feature on the menu alongside Nikkei-style dishes that are a fusion of South American and Japanese elements.;Car park,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13795;Zehntkeller;Germany;Iphofen;Bahnhofstraße 12, Iphofen, 97346, Germany;49.70234;10.258749;67;false;false;Country cooking, International;Located in the middle of the village, this traditional establishment serves good regional and seasonal cuisine. The menu features mouth-watering dishes such as braised beef cheek in a Pinot noir sauce. Opt for a four-course set menu or order à la carte. The house proposes its own organic wines. Very friendly and well-drilled service, a cosy interior, and a lovely terrace laid out under the wisteria. The hotel of the same name has stylish, classic guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13796;Danzer's;Germany;Juist;Wilhelmstraße 36, Juist, 26571, Germany;53.6773217;7.0008599;33;true;false;International, Country cooking;The contemporary ambience in a sleek and at the same time homely style makes for an appealing start – not to mention the terrace with a view of the dike. The food is international and regional, such as fillet of sea bass in bacon butter with wok-fried savoy cabbage. Short lunch menu.;Terrace;[]
13797;Zur Iphöfer Kammer;Germany;Iphofen;Marktplatz 24, Iphofen, 97346, Germany;49.704578;10.2606603;87;false;true;Farm to table, International;This small historic restaurant is located on the market square at Iphofen, a pretty wine-growing town. The delicious fare, which includes dishes such as red mullet with ratatouille and breast of guinea fowl with risotto and girolles, can be sampled in the cosy dining room or outside on the lovely terrace. Excellent wines from the Wirsching vineyard.;Terrace;[]
13798;Brasserie Stadthaus;Germany;Düsseldorf;Mühlenstraße 31, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.2275303;6.7742461;32;false;true;Classic French;This attractive brasserie with its striking high coffered ceiling and pretty interior courtyard promises a genuine French dining experience. Try the tourte de queue de boeuf (oxtail pie) or the seafood platter followed by the tarte au citron. All the wines are French.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13799;The Duchy;Germany;Düsseldorf;Königsallee 11, Düsseldorf, 40212, Germany;51.2252194;6.7772471;22;true;true;Contemporary;On the first floor of the luxurious Breidenbacher Hof, overlooking Heinrich-Heine-Allee, this is an elegant brasserie. The cuisine is a broad mix, from sashimi and ceviche to beef tartare or ravioli, not to mention the steaks. They set great store by the origin of their ingredients, working with regional producers – and they keep their own chickens and cows. Decent wine selection.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13800;Setzkasten;Germany;Düsseldorf;Berliner Allee 52, Düsseldorf, 40212, Germany;51.2195261;6.782331;46;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;A fine dining restaurant in a supermarket? You can experience this novel culinary concept in the basement of The Crown, one of the largest food markets in Europe. It is not only the location that is worth mentioning: in addition to the smart decor and the partially open kitchen, the dedicated kitchen team turns out creative, modern and pleasingly pared-down dishes made using select produce. Chef Egor Hopp also successfully brings in influences from his Kazakhstan homeland, such as Smetana sauce or raschenka cream. There is a set menu comprising six courses in the evening and four at lunchtime. For a corkage fee, you can also consume wine brought from Zurheide Feine Kost. Top tip: If you really want to see what the kitchen can do, make a reservation at the chef's table. Those who arrive by car can make use of The Crown's multi-storey car park.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13801;Schweizer Wirt;Germany;Lenggries;Schlegldorf 83, Lenggries, 83661, Germany;47.7077629;11.5558762;55;true;true;Country cooking, German;This place has been synonymous with tasty cuisine for years. The fresh, regional dishes are made with excellent ingredients. Stripped back to the essentials, they eschew any frills. The atmosphere in the restaurant is charming and the waitstaff are friendly. This beautifully situated traditional inn also has a fabulous terrace. You can park directly in front of the building.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13802;Saittavini;Germany;Düsseldorf;Luegallee 79, Düsseldorf, 40545, Germany;51.2313526;6.7516882;37;false;true;Italian;Combining a bistro, wine bar and delicatessen, this friendly restaurant serves Italian food (including a lovely small antipasto counter). They also sell over a 1 000 different wines in the wine shop and a range of Italian specialities in the delicatessen.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13804;RIVA;Germany;Constance;Seestraße 25, Constance, 78464, Germany;47.6674911;9.1876285;48;true;true;International, Classic Cuisine;The fantastic location on the lake is a draw in itself – a spot on the lovely terrace with a view of the water is of course particularly sought after! But the interior of this bright, elegant restaurant inside the hotel of the same name is also appealing – the floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the lake can be opened up. The cuisine is based on classical and international influences, here and there with an Asian touch, and often on regional products. Chic bar and relaxed outdoor lounge.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13805;Michaelis;Germany;Leipzig;Paul-Gruner-Straße 44, Leipzig, 04107, Germany;51.3284567;12.3742568;22;true;false;International, Seasonal Cuisine;Tasty and fresh food is served in this refined restaurant in a restored building from the Wilhelminian period, which also houses the comfortable hotel of the same name. The menu is seasonal – there are various set menus (one of which is vegetarian) and a sophisticated à la carte selection. Friendly and attentive service. In summer, the terrace behind the house is very appealing.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13806;Schuppen 13;Germany;Langenargen;Argenweg 60, Langenargen, 88085, Germany;47.5906158;9.5535496;31;true;false;Italian, Farm to table;The Pusceddu family’s restaurant is located right on the marina and from the outside looks a little like a boathouse. The food within is classic Italian cuisine meticulously prepared using fresh produce. Try the delicious baby squid braised in tomato stock with pan-fried polenta.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13807;Wettsteins Restaurant;Germany;Langerwehe;Schlossstraße 66, Langerwehe, 52379, Germany;50.7951272;6.3885755;33;false;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;This beautiful property is a little out of the way – on summer days, diners can enjoy sitting out on the terrace. The restaurant has been around for many years. In addition to cordial hosts and friendly service, the programme here includes regionally influenced cuisine, which you can choose to sample as a set menu or à la carte. The menu also features barbecued meat, such as rump steak, and classics like schnitzel and roast joint.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13808;Tafelhaus;Germany;Köngen;Bahnhofstraße 19, Köngen, 73257, Germany;48.6781336;9.3668629;99;true;true;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;The tastefully modern restaurant of Neckartal business hotel is run with dedication. The regional cuisine draws on international influences and is made using top-notch seasonal produce. In addition to the menu, there are also daily specials presented verbally. Owner Bernd Nödinger brings not only professional competence but also a friendly and personal touch to the service. The beverage recommendations are also spot on – thanks to the Coravin system, you can even enjoy high-quality wines by the glass. There is a delightful terrace in summer, and that space gives way to the Tafelhütte event venue in winter. The restaurant is open for lunch on Wednesdays and Thursdays – please book in advance. Reservations for Sundays and Mondays are possible by prior arrangement.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13809;Restaurant 1687;Germany;Berlin;Mittelstraße 30, Berlin, 10117, Germany;52.5181125;13.3844441;81;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This stylish, tastefully designed restaurant is tucked away in a narrow side street just off Unter den Linden. The cuisine is predominantly Mediterranean with hints of a few other international influences. Friendly and attentive service. Breakfast is also served here. In summer, you can make the most of the delightful terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13810;Christoph Pauls Restaurant;Germany;Cologne;Brüsseler Straße 26, Cologne, 50674, Germany;50.9349015;6.9348954;49;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;No stranger to the Rhineland's restaurant scene, Christoph Paul runs this trendy modern restaurant with his wife Juliane. The striking religious imagery on the wall is a reminder of the site's former vocation as a chapel. A seasonal three- or four-course set menu with a choice of dishes is served. The terrace laid out beneath venerable old trees is delightful. A parking space can be reserved upon request.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13812;AL FORNO;Germany;Schirgiswalde-Kirschau;Bautzener Straße 74, Schirgiswalde-Kirschau, 02681, Germany;51.0960149;14.4294966;60;false;false;Italian, Pizza;For fans of authentic Italian food, this ristorante makes for a pleasing alternative to JUWEL and WEBERSTUBE, the other two restaurants to be found here in the Hotel BEI SCHUMANN. Soak up the atmosphere in the wonderfully cosy dining area, in which Italian background music brings that feel-good factor, while the team in the open kitchen conjure up delicious fish and meat dishes, as well as classics such as antipasti, pasta and pizza cooked in the brick oven – the pizzas are available in smaller sizes, too. Desserts such as the zabaione di Marsala are also delicious. Speciality in winter: spaghetti from the parmesan cheese wheel. In summer, head for the pleasant terrace overlooking the SEEWUNDERBAR.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13813;Landgasthof Hirschen;Germany;Hüfingen;Wutachstraße 19, Hüfingen, 78183, Germany;47.8704872;8.464392;54;false;false;Country cooking;The dedication of chef Verena Martin and her team is palpable. In a charming setting diners enjoy cordial service and good food that is made primarily with produce from the region and draws inspiration from the seasons. The kitchen staff put their heart and soul into their work – the motto here is ä weng eppis Feins, or "a little something fine" in the local dialect. Tip: "Unser badisches Menü" or "Unser großes Menü" (for two or more people).;Car park,Terrace;[]
13814;Wieland-Stuben;Germany;Hamm;Wielandstraße 84, Hamm, 59077, Germany;51.6443739;7.7676568;94;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;This restaurant has become something of an institution in the region. The Wieland-Stuben has been a byword for classic cuisine since 1965. The elegant, tastefully decorated dining area makes for a really appealing setting, as does the gorgeous garden terrace. In their classic French cuisine, Lukas Erfurth and his team use only selected ingredients that impress with their freshness and quality. You can opt for the set menu or dine à la carte. The excellent service comes courtesy of a team headed up by sommelier Ronja. On Sundays, there is a three-course set menu (no à la carte dishes).;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13815;Henriks;Germany;Hamburg;Tesdorpfstraße 8, Hamburg, 20148, Germany;53.5635124;9.9922295;83;true;true;International;Some ambitious cooking goes on in this elegantly designed restaurant, where the menu includes Asian, Mediterranean and regional cuisine with dishes ranging from Wiener Schnitzel to lobster. There’s a good selection of wines to accompany the food, plus a popular spacious terrace and lounge.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13816;Scala;Germany;Bad Waldsee;Wurzacher Straße 55, Bad Waldsee, 88339, Germany;47.9199544;9.7594064;24;true;true;Regional Cuisine, International;This modern restaurant boasts beautiful views across the lake and a delightful terrace. It also serves seasonal dishes with an emphasis on regional ingredients, and the vegetable and animal produce are used in their entirety. A smaller selection of dishes is served at lunchtime. Friendly service and fine wines.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13817;Schmidt's;Germany;Dresden;Moritzburger Weg 67, Dresden, 01109, Germany;51.1073877;13.7592368;50;false;true;Farm to table, Creative;This restaurant is housed in the Hellerauer Werkstätten für Handwerkskunst (a workshop founded in 1909 by Karl Schmidt). Served in a modern bistro atmosphere, the classically based food has seasonal and regional influences, and is made with carefully selected ingredients, which are prepared for maximum flavour and minimum fuss. Having difficulty deciding? Then go for the surprise menu ("Schmidt's Karte rauf und runter"). The affordable lunch deal goes down a treat, and the terrace is also lovely.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13818;Baron.ess;Germany;Sonderhofen;Am Mühläcker, Sonderhofen, 97255, Germany;49.5946961;10.0125345;22;true;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;This trendy and stylish restaurant occupies an old bridge structure on the premises of the Brückenkbaron event venue. When you enter, you can take a peek into the glass-walled kitchen before being seated in the airy dining space. The large windows look out onto the landscaped grounds, complete with a pond and fountain. Gorgeous terrace. They propose a creative seasonal set menu with an emphasis on sustainability. Expect pleasingly straightforward and remarkably tasty dishes, such as Swiss chard roulade filled with mild goat's cheese, which is lent a fruity note by a serving of aromatic plums. The chefs are on hand to talk you through the dishes. On the wine list: organic, ecological and natural Franconian wineries.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13819;C'est la vie;Germany;Leipzig;Zentralstraße 7, Leipzig, 04109, Germany;51.3390595;12.3687323;60;false;false;French, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is dedicated to the French way of life. As you sit comfortably at your table in the stylish modern interior, looking out through the floor-to-ceiling windows, the dedicated team busy themselves in the open kitchen, cooking up modern interpretations of dishes such as sea bass with root vegetables and potato croissant or Bresse chicken with morels, shimeji mushrooms and vin jaune. The creations are organised into two set menus – one vegetarian, one with meat – and accompanied by exclusively French wine, which are charmingly and skilfully presented at your table with the aid of a map. The wines can also be purchased in the shop. Tip: There is parking in the garage right next door.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13820;La Mer;Germany;Norderney;Bülowallee 5, Norderney, 26548, Germany;53.703901;7.1475981;82;false;false;Classic French, French Contemporary;Having earned his spurs at some award-winning restaurants, most recently at Seesteg, owner and head chef Hilko Uphoffis, together with his partner Giulia Casto, is now at the helm of this smart restaurant located right next to the Michels Thalasso Hotel Nordseehaus, on the edge of the pedestrian/shopping zone. His classically French cuisine also demonstrates the odd modern flourish, as in the flambéed Chilean sea bass marinated in miso and cider. The restaurant itself is also inviting, with its beautifully bright, pared-down and modern interior, as well as its appealing terrace laid out in front of the large window façade.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13821;La Cantina by Catalana;Germany;Erfurt;Allerheiligenstraße 19, Erfurt, 99084, Germany;50.9786294;11.0272201;20;false;false;Spanish;Located in the city centre, in an old townhouse accessible via a small courtyard, this restaurant is owned by Jan-Hendrik Feldner, who also runs the nearby ESTIMA by Catalana. As a connoisseur of Spanish cuisine, the chef proposes a down-to-earth tapas concept in his convivial, simple little establishment. The menu features authentically prepared small dishes mainly inspired by Catalan cuisine – it's best to order four or five. The chef also serves and talks you through the dishes.;;[]
13822;Dröppelminna;Germany;Bergisch Gladbach;Herrenstrunden 3, Bergisch Gladbach, 51465, Germany;51.0051723;7.1780666;40;true;false;German, Home Cooking;The atmosphere in this pretty half-timbered house is rustic and cosy. The decoration is charming, with its antique pieces and all manner of ornaments, including the eponymous three-legged pewter coffee pots. The open kitchen sends out a varying array of classic dishes. Accompanied by fine wines, including a good selection from Alsace – the owner is a sommelier. Snug terrace.;Car park,Cash only,Terrace;[]
13823;Ressmann's Residence;Germany;Kirkel;Kaiserstraße 87, Kirkel, 66459, Germany;49.2860957;7.229851;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The modern decor, with its sleek design and light, warm tones, is a hit with diners, as are the ambitious, international, seasonal cuisine and fine wines. Tip: At lunchtime, you can put together your own inexpensive three-course menu or simply order à la carte. For those hot summer days, one of the dining rooms is air-conditioned, but if you would rather sit outside, there is a lovely garden terrace tucked away behind the building. Overnight accommodation is also available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13824;Vinothek im Weingut am Nil;Germany;Kallstadt;Neugasse 21, Kallstadt, 67169, Germany;49.4927029;8.177185;69;false;true;International, Regional Cuisine;Set in a lovely period building, this combination of restaurant and wine shop works beautifully well. The upscale, chic interior is characterised by a blend of rustic and modern design features. In summer, make a beeline for the enchanting courtyard. The cuisine draws on global influences and is served alongside a selection of excellent wines from their own production. Tip: there are tastefully furnished guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13825;Wappen-Saal;Germany;Hohen Demzin;Burg Schlitz 2, Hohen Demzin, 17166, Germany;53.7011537;12.5425502;48;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This imposing castle estate provides a truly unique setting for dining. Before taking a seat in the stately Wappensaal in the Schlosshotel at Burg Schlitz, take a leisurely stroll along the Goetheweg. Experience the historical ambiance of this restaurant as you savour a four- to six-course menu of ambitious classic cuisine beneath an impressive high ceiling. The charming and experienced staff will be happy to help you choose the perfect accompaniment to your meal from the well-curated wine list.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
13826;Hubertushof;Germany;Ilbesheim bei Landau in der Pfalz;Arzheimer Straße 5, Ilbesheim bei Landau in der Pfalz, 76831, Germany;49.1831279;8.0541413;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Remaining true to the Südliche Weinstraße, Sandra Bernhard and Jochen Sitter moved from Birkweiler to this 300 year-old former coaching house, which they run with great dedication and charm. The chef cooks traditional and modern, but above all, flavoursome fare. Dishes include classics such as pan-friend black pudding and Saumagen (stuffed pig’s stomach). The interior courtyard is gorgeous.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13827;Westphalenhof;Germany;Hoyerswerda;Dorfaue 43, Hoyerswerda, 02977, Germany;51.4234791;14.2762774;36;false;false;International, Classic Cuisine;This stylish and sophisticated restaurant is somewhat tucked away in a residential area. Here, the Westphal brothers – one is the chef, the other the sommelier – delight diners with delicious food and excellent wine recommendations. The menu features international dishes that take their cue from the seasons, such as confit halibut fillet in nut butter, potato scales, cauliflower cream, dried tomatoes and Sardinian pasta. The walk-in wine cellar accommodates 120 different labels. The restaurant is also open for lunch on Saturdays and Sundays.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13828;Fischereihafen Restaurant;Germany;Hamburg;Große Elbstraße 143, Hamburg, 22767, Germany;53.5447513;9.9360057;72;true;true;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;This is and remains an institution – something of a home from home for Hamburg's fish lovers, young and old! A constant stream of international customers comes and goes from lunchtime to evening. In an elegant setting boasting traditional Hanseatic decor and a view of the harbour, quality fish from the fish market is served at the height of freshness. Classic dishes include turbot or lobster in different variations, but the menu also includes Asian and Mediterranean-influenced options.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13829;Alter Wirt;Germany;Grünwald;Marktplatz 1, Grünwald, 82031, Germany;48.0398327;11.5228961;48;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;This inn has a long-standing tradition of hospitality. A relaxed atmosphere reigns in the delightful interior, which combines modern elements with rustic charm. Outside, the lovely terrace is shaded by chestnut trees. With an emphasis on organic and locally sourced ingredients, the menu features regional fare and takes its cue from the seasons. Daily specials are also available. For overnight stays, there are well-appointed guestrooms furnished with natural materials and designed with sustainability in mind.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13830;Cox;Germany;Hamburg;Lange Reihe 68, Hamburg, 20099, Germany;53.557535;10.0115776;39;false;false;International;Pleasant and laid-back – a bistro in the best sense of the word. A diverse cohort of diners enjoys dishes such as lamb fillets with pesto fried in brik pastry with ratatouille and fried capers. The service is friendly and attentive. Popular and inexpensive lunch offer.;;[]
13831;Villa Busch;Germany;Haiger;Westerwaldstraße 4, Haiger, 35708, Germany;50.7411925;8.2017152;70;true;true;International;This beautiful, lavishly refurbished villa in an elevated location not only boasts a lovely terrace for summer, but the interior of the restaurant is also tasteful with its stuccoed ceilings, wooden floorboards and modern designer chairs. The chef-patron's kitchen team creates dishes with Mediterranean and Asian influences, including many fish specialities. Plus, you are waited on by a warm and charming front-of-house team.;Terrace;[]
13833;EssensArt;Germany;Haan;Bachstraße 141, Haan, 42781, Germany;51.1879715;6.9830438;50;true;true;International, Modern Cuisine;A bright, friendly restaurant fronted by a leafy secluded terrace with a lovely pergola. The cuisine is international with a few truly classic dishes. Great value for money.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13834;Butcher's american steakhouse;Germany;Hamburg;Milchstraße 19, Hamburg, 20148, Germany;53.5705928;9.9973129;40;true;true;Meats and Grills, American;At Butcher's american steakhouse you can enjoy fine Nebraska beef that the chef presents to the table personally. The cosy restaurant is dominated by dark wood and warm colours.;;[]
13835;Heimatjuwel;Germany;Hamburg;Stellinger Weg 47, Hamburg, 20255, Germany;53.5801378;9.9476808;53;true;false;Creative, Country cooking;Marcel Görke, no stranger to Hamburg's culinary scene, runs this minimalist, rustic-style and pleasingly informal little restaurant. Creative seasonal cuisine made from regional produce is served in the form of a vegetarian set menu comprising four or six courses – there is also an alternative main course of fish or meat. You have the option of dining at one of the tables on the small terrace lining the pavement.;Terrace;[]
13836;Witwenball;Germany;Hamburg;Weidenallee 20, Hamburg, 20357, Germany;53.5671427;9.9651716;37;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This former dancing bar is now a trendy, modern deluxe bistro with pale green chairs and azure blue bench seats, shining marble tables, a striking white marble counter and decorative wine shelving. The themed menu changes every few weeks. There are over 300 wines to choose from as pairings to the delicious dishes – the emphasis here is on organic viticulture. The desserts are highly recommended.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13837;Brook;Germany;Hamburg;Bei den Mühren 91, Hamburg, 20457, Germany;53.5453627;9.9936828;58;true;false;International;International, German and classical influences are at play here, e.g. loin of lamb with string beans and Parmesan potatoes or venison with Brussels sprouts and chestnuts. In the evening, the beautifully illuminated Speicherstadt opposite is a sight to behold!;Terrace;[]
13838;Tschebull;Germany;Hamburg;Mönckebergstraße 7, Hamburg, 20095, Germany;53.5513722;10.0028066;20;false;true;Austrian, International;On the first floor of this exclusive shopping arcade the nods to Austria are everywhere: in the decoration -cowbells and edelweiss motifs on the ceiling, mountain panorama mural - and in the dishes, in the guise of classics such as Carinthian Kasnudeln, Wiener Schnitzel and apricot strudel. Beisl, serving Austrian tapas is more casual.;;[]
13839;LENZ;Germany;Hamburg;Poppenbütteler Chaussee 3, Hamburg, 22397, Germany;53.708252;10.1053;49;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Here you can enjoy regional cuisine in a friendly and modern atmosphere. Try the labskaus (a traditional northern German meat dish), braised veal cheeks, or red berry compote. There is also a simpler, more moderately priced lunch menu. The food is complemented by an appealing wine list, service is attentive, and the bright conservatory can be opened up in summer!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13840;Farmerhaus;Germany;Groß-Umstadt;Am Farmerhaus 1, Groß-Umstadt, 64823, Germany;49.8671409;8.9444486;70;false;false;African;African produce enriches the cuisine, which is international in character. Wood carvings and trophies from the country where the dishes originated are interesting to look at.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13841;Bahnhöfle;Germany;Gundelfingen;Bahnhofstraße 16, Gundelfingen, 79194, Germany;48.0434689;7.8734138;80;true;true;Classic French, Mediterranean Cuisine;The friendly host cooks French and international dishes. Prettily decorated by his wife, the restaurant radiates country charm. Lovely terrace at the front.;Terrace;[]
13842;Bistro oma & enkel;Germany;Wirsberg;Marktplatz 11, Wirsberg, 95339, Germany;50.1072743;11.6068249;16;true;true;Country cooking;oma & enkel ("grandma & grandchild") is the culinary concept at this bistro in the long-established Posthotel. The name symbolises a bridging of the gap between the generations, from the traditional to the modern. Recipes of yesteryear are brought up to date and classics of Franconian cuisine are given a contemporary twist. In a pleasingly laid-back atmosphere, choose between "Franconian tapas", the "Signature Menu" or the "Duck Menu". Don't miss out on the Franconian bouillabaisse or the apricot dumplings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13843;martino KITCHEN;Germany;Wiesbaden;Webergasse 6, Wiesbaden, 65183, Germany;50.0844366;8.2422731;56;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;A charming bistro where friendly and attentive staff serve Mediterranean-inspired cuisine made using regional and seasonal ingredients. A choice of two set menus is available in the evening: one vegetarian and one omnivore. The restaurant is located in the Citta Trüffel hotel, which boasts chic guestrooms, as well as a delicatessen.;Air conditioning;[]
13844;Thuns Dorfkrug;Germany;Werdohl;Brauck 7, Werdohl, 58791, Germany;51.2370629;7.7627727;64;true;false;International, French;This restaurant offers beautifully laid tables, attentive service and good cuisine offering a mix of regional and international elements. The simple and elegant style of the decor features attractive contemporary pictures and parquet flooring. The guestrooms are in a clean-lined, modern style.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13845;Köllner's Landhaus;Germany;Celle;Im Dorfe 1, Celle, 29223, Germany;52.639225;10.0270311;22;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, International;Set in grounds covering 11 000m² this charming half-timbered house dating from 1589 is a picture-book property with a country house-style interior that certainly does it justice. Then there is the excellent regional and international cuisine. You might also choose to spend the night in one of the comfortable and modern guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13846;WILD X BERG;Germany;Birkenau;Absteinacher Straße 2, Birkenau, 69488, Germany;49.5507474;8.7378012;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This chic little fine dining restaurant on the first floor of the tasteful Lammershof hotel serves modern cuisine that is ambitious and extremely technically precise. It takes the form of a set menu comprising a variable number of courses – a vegetarian version is also available if you order in advance. Select ingredients, including meat from bison reared on site. A few tables offer a view into the kitchen. Tip: Bison Bar in the rustic-style cellar.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13847;Reussenstein;Germany;Böblingen;Kalkofenstraße 20, Böblingen, 71032, Germany;48.6824272;9.0192833;39;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The motto here is "100% Swabian". All the ingredients come from Württemberg, and the menu is entirely dedicated to regional cuisine. If you are ordering à la carte, you pick your main dish by its key ingredient (beef, game, freshwater fish…) and it comes served on a special ash wood tiered platter that was custom-made for the restaurant. Alternatively, you can opt for the "Fein-Wild-Dining" set menu, which changes every season and exclusively features game. The glass-paned wall into the kitchen provides interesting glimpses behind the scenes, plus the service is really friendly. There is a cookery school in the vaults. Their rather novel "Spätzle Drive-in" is open throughout the day. This long-standing family business also offers cosy modern guestrooms.;Air conditioning;[]
13848;St. Urban;Germany;Deidesheim;Am Marktplatz 1, Deidesheim, 67146, Germany;49.4080041;8.1873988;83;false;true;Country cooking;Along with the fine dining restaurant Schwarzer Hahn, St. Urban is part of the appealing culinary microcosm of the lovely Deidesheimer Hof hotel, which is located right on the historical market square. The cosy interior exudes the traditional charm of a Palatinate inn. Good regional and seasonal cuisine is served, à la carte or as a set menu. The menu also includes the classic "Palatinate Favourite – Saumagen (stuffed pig's stomach), Bratwurst and liver dumplings with sauerkraut and mashed potatoes".;Car park,Terrace;[]
13849;Zucker;Germany;Brunswick;Frankfurter Straße 2, Brunswick, 38122, Germany;52.2562019;10.5149382;29;true;false;Farm to table, Contemporary;The name sort of gives it away if you have any German: This attractive modern brasserie is housed in a former sugar factory, now a listed building. Exposed red brick walls and high ceilings give the setting an appealing industrial feel. In summer, the terrace is shaded by awnings. Flavoursome seasonally inspired dishes are served à la carte, with an additional set menu available. The waitstaff are pleasantly down-to-earth, very friendly and well organised.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
13850;Atable im Amtshaus;Germany;Freinsheim;Hauptstraße 29, Freinsheim, 67251, Germany;49.5069254;8.211317;59;true;false;Farm to table, International;Surrounded by the town wall, the Amtshaus boasts a lovely location in Freinsheim's old town, which is well worth a visit. The courtyard with its idyllic terrace leads to this chic restaurant, where you will notice a white cross vault supported by columns. Chef Swen Bultmann cooks classic French dishes that are made from fine ingredients and inspired by the seasons. The food is accompanied by an appealing and extensive selection of wines. There is also accommodation – in the tasteful guestrooms, as in the restaurant itself, the decor harmoniously incorporates modern design into the historical setting.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13851;Kö59 masterminded by Björn Freitag;Germany;Düsseldorf;Königsallee 59, Düsseldorf, 40215, Germany;51.2204384;6.7776756;76;true;false;German, Contemporary;Björn Freitag, familiar from Goldener Anker in Dorsten, set up this interesting restaurant right on Königsallee, the shopping street known as "Kö". The chic brasserie in Hotel Kö59 serves up seasonally inspired Rhenish cuisine, but international influences can also be detected on the menu. Shining examples include tartare of Simmental beef fillet with lentils, mustard, lettuce and crunchy celeriac, or confit salmon with carrot, quince, curry and couscous.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13852;esszimmer das Restaurant;Germany;Weinheim;Alte Postgasse 53, Weinheim, 69469, Germany;49.5542838;8.6700458;70;false;true;Modern Cuisine, International;Old floorboards, beautiful bare wooden tables and eclectic decoration make for a really comfortable atmosphere, almost as if you were in your own dining room. The cuisine is creative and made with high-quality and carefully sourced ingredients, many from the region - top for example Hamachi from Völklingen. There is a set menu comprising four to seven courses – including appetisers, a breadboard and salad, plus a petit four to finish.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13853;Bootshaus;Germany;Weissenhaus;Strandstraße 4, Weissenhaus, 23758, Germany;54.30624;10.765205;98;true;true;International;The beachside location is simply idyllic – you can't get much closer to the Baltic Sea! In this restaurant at the Weissenhaus Private Nature Luxury Resort, diners are shown to their tables in a modern interior with a glazed façade that affords fantastic views. But it is of course the terrace that is the top attraction! The food is a fresh blend of Mediterranean fare – somewhat simpler at lunchtime, more sophisticated in the evening, from classic dishes to elegant culinary compositions. Service runs from 1pm-4.30pm, reservation times in the evening are 6pm and 8.30pm.;Great view,Terrace;[]
13854;Ratsstube;Germany;Wildemann;Bohlweg 37, Wildemann, 38709, Germany;51.8260954;10.2838501;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;In the former town hall, you can now dine in a stylish and inviting space that combines contemporary design with the warmth of wood and natural tones. The cuisine is ambitious, creative and modern, but at the same time pleasantly down-to-earth. The names of the dishes are original, such as "H2O" (cold watermelon and cucumber soup, trout ceviche) or "Haarscharf" ("Razor-sharp") (medium-rare wild boar, spring onion and beetroot ragout, garden herbs, horseradish pasta). The presentation is colourful and very visually appealing. In summer, there is pleasant terrace seating in the shade of lime trees. Good overnight accommodation available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13855;Schapers;Germany;Celle;Heese 6, Celle, 29225, Germany;52.6178469;10.0600954;31;true;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;A family-run place where you will be treated to friendly and cordial service. As for the food, you can look forward to ambitious classic cuisine brimming with regional influences. Choose from the à la carte offering or the set menus drawn from it, which include a vegetarian set menu. The terrace is lovely. Should you wish to stay overnight, there are comfortable and convenient guestrooms available, distributed over two buildings.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13856;der allerKrug;Germany;Celle;Alte Dorfstraße 14, Celle, 29227, Germany;52.604938;10.1203084;27;false;true;Country cooking, International;Here at der allerKrug with its friendly hosts Sven Hütten and Petra Tiecke-Hütten, you can look forward to carefully and skilfully prepared dishes. The dishes are based on country cuisine with international influences, plus there’s an attractive terrace to the rear of the restaurant.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13857;Leopold;Germany;Deidesheim;Weinstraße 10, Deidesheim, 67146, Germany;49.4105783;8.1865464;19;false;false;International, Country cooking;This lavishly converted stable of the Von Winning winery (part of the Bassermann-Jordan empire) is an impressively modern and extremely popular restaurant that serves excellent food. The menu includes a selection of international and Palatinate dishes. Lovely terrace. It can also be booked as a fantastic location for events. The restaurant was named after Leopold von Winning, founder of the winery.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13858;Hanse Stube;Germany;Cologne;Trankgasse 1, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.9424592;6.9565392;38;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The exclusive Excelsior Hotel Ernst, right opposite the cathedral, is home to the dignified and extremely elegant Hanse Stube. With its dark wood panelling, it is an absolute classic and you might say the "second home" of Cologne society. It serves ambitious classic cuisine with modern influences, as a menu or à la carte. At lunchtime there is an additional small menu. Excellent wines and friendly, trained service accompany your meal, and the terrace is beautiful.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13859;Restaurant 1718;Germany;Deidesheim;Ketschauerhofstraße 1, Deidesheim, 67146, Germany;49.4079621;8.1851482;41;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;At 1718, elegant period architectural elements blend beautifully with modern design. Part of Ketschauer Hof hotel, the restaurant sits across from the fine dining restaurant L.A. Jordan – separating them is a lovely terrace in the peaceful, verdant courtyard. On the menu, French and international cuisine are the order of the day, accompanied by a superb selection of wines from the Palatinate and beyond. Tip: The establishment runs a wine shop around the corner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13860;Nose & Belly;Germany;Augsburg;Heilig-Kreuz-Straße 10, Augsburg, 86152, Germany;48.3716097;10.892181;44;false;true;Innovative, Regional Cuisine;"Follow your nose – listen to your belly" – that's the idea behind the name of this small restaurant. Located in the centre of Augsburg, it is well worth a visit, primarily on account of the cleverly thought-out seasonal cuisine, for which Hendrik Ketter and his team use regional produce wherever possible. On Wednesdays and Thursdays, there is the à la carte offering "NO.BEL LEGER" as well as the "Chef's Choice Menu", which comprises five or seven courses. On Fridays and Saturdays, a set menu with four to seven courses is available – also in a vegetarian version. In addition, you can expect proficient and friendly service along with a pleasantly minimalist and modern setting. Ask about the dates for Sunday lunch openings.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13861;Behl's Restaurant;Germany;Blankenbach;Krombacher Straße 2, Blankenbach, 63825, Germany;50.0657755;9.2302406;39;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;The dedication of the Behl family is palpable whether you're staying in their Genusshotel with its cheerful and cosy guestrooms or dining in the restaurant, complete with charming shaded courtyard terrace. You can look forward to a welcoming atmosphere and delicious dishes made with locally sourced produce such as Blankenbach brook trout or Spessart pasture-raised beef. They also host regular Brennabende ("spirit evenings") in the distillery, including a set menu with spirit pairings and a demonstration.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13862;Kucher's Weinwirtschaft;Germany;Darscheid;Karl-Kaufmann-Straße 2, Darscheid, 54552, Germany;50.2108509;6.8832272;78;true;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;The mismatched antique tables and chairs, the pretty decoration and the almost familial atmosphere lend this place a charming feel. The Swabian-style sour kidneys with sautéed potatoes have been on the menu here forever – a classic with its own loyal following. In addition, the menu includes contemporary dishes such as braised Ellscheid lemon chicken with Mediterranean vegetables. Most of the meat used by Florian Kucher and his team to create their seasonal regional fare comes from the Eifel area. Be sure to peruse the wine list – wine is a passion of senior chef Martin Kucher and he will be happy to advise you.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13863;KOI;Germany;Munich;Wittelsbacherplatz 1, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1432046;11.5755902;42;true;false;Japanese Contemporary, Fusion;Head here for modern Japanese cuisine. The trendy decor and lively ambience extend over two floors, with diners able to choose from a wide range of sushi options, as well as meat dishes and light bites. Some dishes are cooked on the open charcoal grill.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13865;GRACE;Germany;Berlin;Kurfürstendamm 25, Berlin, 10719, Germany;52.5036007;13.3290711;78;true;true;International, Modern Cuisine;"The place to be" in Berlin! A really appealing and stylish restaurant that oozes glamour and counts Hollywood stars among its patrons. Dishes with Asian-Californian and European flavours are served. A must: after the meal, a cocktail in the rooftop bar lounge! The restaurant is located in the tasteful, high-quality designed "Hotel Zoo" in a great location directly on Kurfürstendamm.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13866;Der Schwarze Adler;Germany;Nuremberg;Kraftshofer Hauptstraße 166, Nuremberg, 90427, Germany;49.511686;11.0497791;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Even from the outside, this beautifully restored, centuries-old building will grab your attention, while inside you can expect a cosy and comfortable decor with a touch of romance to it. Quality is of major importance for owner and chef Christian Brieske: he creates modern and ambitious dishes built on classical foundations. Very attentive and friendly service.;Terrace;[]
13868;Otto;Germany;Berlin;Oderberger Straße 56, Berlin, 10435, Germany;52.5382029;13.4102304;99;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This compact restaurant has an appealingly lively atmosphere. The friendly vibe is due in no small part to the fantastic, well-drilled team, who have a personalised touch when it comes to looking after diners. The open kitchen – overlooking which there are also a few seats at the bar – sends out seasonal, modern, pared-down dishes with Nordic influences, all made using locally sourced ingredients. You can choose between the sharing menu and à la carte dishes. Vegetarians are also catered for. There is a rather short but carefully curated wine list with a predilection for natural and orange wines. Small terrace in front of the restaurant. This very popular restaurant has limited seating, so be sure to book in advance!;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13869;Daniels;Germany;Kusel;Marktplatz 6, Kusel, 66869, Germany;49.5374668;7.4007843;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in Kusel's old town centre, right on the market square, this renovated townhouse is certainly charming. Out front, there are a few trees and a fountain – the terrace seating here is delightful in summer. The place has a modern feel and a laid-back, friendly atmosphere. Wooden ceiling beams and exposed old sandstone masonry hark back to a bygone era. Ulrike und Daniel Bößhar delight diners with attentive service and ambitious cuisine in the form of a modern inspired set menu with three to seven courses.;Terrace;[]
13871;Gasthaus Adler;Germany;Glottertal;Talstraße 11, Glottertal, 79286, Germany;48.05126;7.93315;19;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;Savour classic Baden fare with French and international influences in these cosy, quintessentially "Black Forest" dining rooms. In winter, for example, the game and goose dishes are popular. In summer, there is outside seating in the Adler Gärtle. The service is friendly and there are comfortable guestrooms, some simpler than others.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13872;Wirtshaus zur Sonne;Germany;Glottertal;Talstraße 103, Glottertal, 79286, Germany;48.0483979;7.9610555;89;true;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant has been in the same family for over 300 years. Diners can sit inside in the wonderful, wood-panelled dining room or outside on the pretty garden terrace to enjoy the flavoursome fare. This includes tafelspitz (boiled topside of beef) galantine with radish carpaccio or pan-fried skrei cod with tomatoes and herbs.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13873;Moosleitner;Germany;Freilassing;Wasserburger Straße 52, Freilassing, 83395, Germany;47.8435935;12.9542752;36;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;The tradition of this restaurant has been cultivated for centuries. With their rural charm, the attractive dining rooms are cosy and inviting, and make an ideal setting in which to enjoy the Bavarian cuisine that is served here – fresh, seasonal and with a penchant for locally sourced produce. This is also a nice place to spend the night: There are well-kept guestrooms, plus a small sauna and gym facilities.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13874;Posthörnle;Germany;Esslingen am Neckar;Pliensaustraße 56, Esslingen am Neckar, 73728, Germany;48.7380538;9.3038955;31;true;true;International;This casual, minimalist-style little restaurant is housed in one of the oldest taverns in the town. It serves fresh, seasonal cuisine with dishes ranging from venison rissoles with black mustard to pan-fried zander with oranges and chicory.;Terrace;[]
13875;LUISE;Germany;Horben;Luisenhöhestraße 14, Horben, 79289, Germany;47.9456143;7.8550446;84;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The beautiful landscape here is perfectly complemented by the elliptical shape of Luisenhöhe hotel, which gracefully blends into its surroundings. Inside, too, modern design and high-quality natural materials make for an attractive decor that pays homage to the region – both in the guestrooms and the restaurant. The latter has a pleasantly laid-back feel, and a large glass façade looks out onto the terrace and beyond to the Black Forest and the Schauinsland mountain. Prepared in the open kitchen, the vegetarian set menu comprises four courses such as ancient grains salad with chard and sweet potato, or carrot with physalis and madras curry – meat, fish and even shellfish are available as add-ons. The excellent wine list features a good selection of German and international labels. The futuristic design of the passage that leads from the multi-storey car park to the hotel is also impressive.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13876;Jennerwein;Germany;Gmund am Tegernsee;Münchner Straße 127, Gmund am Tegernsee, 83703, Germany;47.7592484;11.7347823;26;true;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;A truly delightful establishment with a charmingly rustic inn atmosphere – it's genuinely cosy here. The menu includes freshly prepared seasonal Bavarian cuisine such as braised shoulder of lamb with root vegetables, or beef tenderloin on a bed of fried mushrooms and potatoes, as well as parmesan risotto with king prawns. More limited options at lunchtime.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13877;Schillingshof;Germany;Friedland;Lappstraße 14, Friedland, 37133, Germany;51.4372085;9.9321733;29;true;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;This elegant restaurant is set in a timber-framed house built in 1648. It serves ambitious, classically based international cuisine with creative elements made using high-quality produce. Overnight guests will appreciate the attractive modern rooms and the quiet location.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13878;Alte Mühle;Germany;Rödental;Mühlgarten 5, Rödental, 96472, Germany;50.3124471;11.022707;62;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;This friendly restaurant with its appealingly pared-back decor adjoins the historical building of a grain mill, which has been converted into guest accommodation. The cuisine is Mediterranean, regional and seasonal, and there will be something on the menu for those looking for vegetarian/vegan options. Lunch is also served Thu-Sat.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13880;Wirtshaus zum Herrmannsdorfer Schweinsbräu;Germany;Glonn;Herrmannsdorf 7, Glonn, 85625, Germany;47.9933545;11.8976544;15;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;"Dishes that can't be pigeonholed" – such is the name of the game for chef Olimpia Cario. In her surprise set menu, she gives free rein to her creativity, cooking up unusual combinations such as chicken, trout, egg, cucumber, corn and redcurrants. She uses seasonal produce and high-quality ingredients, often grown on her own farm. The interior itself has an eye-catching design, with a large, high-ceilinged space reminiscent of a modern rustic barn on account of the beam construction climbing up into the roof.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13881;Zur Krone;Germany;Gottenheim;Hauptstraße 57, Gottenheim, 79288, Germany;48.0483443;7.7246956;96;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;The Isele family has been cultivating the art of hospitality in this traditional building since 1854. The interior boasts a pleasant atmosphere in which to enjoy classic German cuisine that is seasonal, carefully prepared and based on a range of regional ingredients. The home-made terrines and desserts are definitely worth trying – the diet will have to wait! The wine list also has a very regional slant. In addition, there are comfortable, tastefully decorated guestrooms in which you will be tempted to stay for more than one night!;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13882;Les Deux Dienstbach;Germany;Hochheim am Main;Geheimrat-Hummel-Platz 1A, Hochheim am Main, 65239, Germany;50.0108688;8.3471099;83;true;true;French Contemporary, Farm to table;"Les Deux Dienstbach" refers to the two siblings who founded this restaurant at the renowned Weingut Künstler winery and whose French roots define the cuisine. Maitre d' Jennifer Dienstbach heads up the very friendly and adept waitstaff. Her sister, who is now based in her native Normandy, supports the kitchen team by providing culinary ideas. They propose a set menu comprising three to six courses made with select ingredients. Diners choose from a selection of wines from both France and Weingut Künstler. The setting is also appealing with its colour palette of muted tones, and smart, modern interior design features make for a tasteful interior in the heart of this historical building. Once a month you can dine à la carte on Sunday lunchtime.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13884;Kölbl;Germany;Enkenbach-Alsenborn;Hauptstraße 3, Enkenbach-Alsenborn, 67677, Germany;49.4884244;7.8996906;44;true;true;International, Country cooking;Plenty of regulars come here to enjoy the regional and international cuisine served à la carte or in the form of a four-course set menu – a vegetarian version is also available. Diners can sit in one of the cosy dining rooms or on the courtyard terrace to enjoy the seasonal dishes. The guestrooms are ideal for overnight stays.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13887;Sette Feinbistro;Germany;Elmshorn;Marktstraße 7, Elmshorn, 25335, Germany;53.7532128;9.6514047;73;true;false;International, Farm to table;This pleasant place is somewhat tucked away in the pedestrian precinct. Behind the name "Feinbistro", it comprises both a delicatessen and a restaurant. They are open in the morning to serve breakfast, and at lunchtime there is a small Mediterranean-influenced menu. Don't forget to purchase delicacies such as jam, cheese and wine etc from the shop to enjoy at home.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13888;Spessarttor;Germany;Lohr am Main;Wombacher Straße 140, Lohr am Main, 97816, Germany;49.9770593;9.5725783;74;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;This long-established family business is a well-run affair, with diners settling into the cosy dining rooms to enjoy regional fare. On the menu, tasty dishes such as roast venison with red cabbage and dumplings will whet your appetite. You can stay overnight in the inn or in the guesthouse located 300m away.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13889;Grüner Baum;Germany;Lahr;Burgheimer Straße 105, Lahr, 77933, Germany;48.3470923;7.8812777;29;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;It is delightful to sit in the shade of the large chestnut tree on the terrace to the rear of this inn, which dates back over 300 years, but the interior is also cosy. Either way, your dedicated hosts are always on hand. They serve Baden cuisine such as Sauerbraten (marinated pot roast) with red cabbage, or pikeperch on a bed of creamed sauerkraut.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13890;La Cuisine Mario Kalweit;Germany;Dortmund;Lübkestraße 21, Dortmund, 44141, Germany;51.5053488;7.5080818;86;true;true;Classic French;A nicely restored building from the late 19th century houses this stylish, modern, elegant restaurant serving creative cuisine. Pleasant terrace.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13891;Piccolo;Germany;Cologne;Rheinbergstraße 49, Cologne, 51143, Germany;50.8520729;7.0085988;47;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;You may not see the cathedral here in Porz-Langel, but you do pretty much have front row seats onto the Rhine! This restaurant serves classic cuisine with seasonal and Mediterranean influences, prepared using decent ingredients, most of which are sourced from the region. You can choose à la carte or put together your own three-course menu for a set price. The friendly staff also have plenty of good wine recommendations up their sleeve, drawing on the decent selection with a focus on Austria and Germany.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13892;Hardthaus;Germany;Kraiburg am Inn;Marktplatz 31, Kraiburg am Inn, 84559, Germany;48.1817743;12.4290236;62;false;true;International;The charming ambience of a former colonial shop surrounds you in this listed property, which boasts an inviting cosy vaulted wine cellar and a beautiful terrace opening onto the Marktplatz. The cuisine is both international and creative. Modern, high-quality guestrooms are available in the building opposite.;Terrace;[]
13893;Im Gütchen;Germany;Bad Kreuznach;Hüffelsheimer Straße 1, Bad Kreuznach, 55545, Germany;49.8469435;7.8482996;71;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, International;This elegant modern restaurant is accommodated in a charming Baroque mansion within the historical Schlosspark. In an airy, high-ceilinged space, diners are served classic cuisine with regional and Mediterranean sides, for you to pick à la carte or as a set menu. The proprietor himself runs the kitchen, using good-quality ingredients to cook up tasty dishes, while the lady of the house takes care of diners in a cordial manner. On hot summer days, make a beeline for the marvellous terrace.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13895;Zum Ochsen;Germany;Kernen im Remstal;Kirchstraße 15, Kernen im Remstal, 71394, Germany;48.7894727;9.3418075;93;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;It is not without good reason that this 300-year-old restaurant has so many regulars. Here, they honour tradition while managing to keep up with the times – and that goes for both the decor and the food, which is not only beautifully presented but also of the highest quality. The Swabian cuisine follows the seasons and draws on international influences. The emphasis is on regional ingredients, including meat and sausage products made on site in their own butcher's shop. As well as à la carte dishes, a three- or four-course set menu is available.;Terrace;[]
13896;Die Scheuer;Germany;Hofheim am Taunus;Burgstraße 12, Hofheim am Taunus, 65719, Germany;50.0871908;8.445019;43;true;false;Country cooking;Once known as the Hammelsche Scheune, this 17C barn converted into a pretty half-timbered building has bags of charm. This family business a stone's throw from the market square is run with great dedication, and attracts many regulars. In summer, there is a lovely terrace out front. The interior makes for a cosy setting in which to savour delicious food such as locally hunted game. The restaurant endeavours to source ingredients locally and knows its suppliers personally.;Terrace;[]
13897;Bootshaus Bar & Grill;Germany;Hamburg;Am Kaiserkai 19, Hamburg, 20457, Germany;53.5411563;9.9916523;58;true;false;Meats and Grills;The Bootshaus is situated right in the heart of Hamburg’s HafenCity district. Sit in the comfortable “Boot” (boat) dining room with a view of the open-plan kitchen or, if you prefer, look out over the Grasbrookhafen marina from the light and airy bar area. The Josper meat grill is the focus here, serving “New York Strip” and “Rib Eye” just how you like it! Good choice of side-orders and delicious sauces.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13898;Daniel;Germany;Dresden;Gluckstraße 3, Dresden, 01309, Germany;51.0509163;13.7775375;47;false;true;Classic Cuisine;In this pleasingly bright, convivial and refined restaurant, you can look forward to sampling rather classical, seasonally influenced cuisine. There are set menus to choose from, as well as à la carte dishes drawn from these. Or perhaps you will plump for the surprise menu. The front-of-house team are attentive. In summer, diners can enjoy sitting out on the pretty terrace. Tip: Browse the "Genusskalender" for themed evenings based on different produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13899;L'arte in cucina;Germany;Düsseldorf;Gerricusplatz 6, Düsseldorf, 40625, Germany;51.237138;6.8621294;60;false;false;Italian, Tuscan;This attractive restaurant opposite the Basilika St. Margareta is a rare example of an authentic Italian ristorante, where the cuisine of Tuscany is served with love and culinary flair. Specialities from the chef's Tuscan homeland such as gnudi (a kind of gnocchi) or "Il Coniglio" (rabbit). The pasta is house-made.;Terrace;[]
13900;Waldgasthof am Letten;Germany;Lauf an der Pegnitz;Letten 13, Lauf an der Pegnitz, 91207, Germany;49.4886024;11.2803455;54;true;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;This restaurant has various dining spaces with a charming rustic feel – including lovely cosy alcoves – where diners tuck into seasonal cuisine that is regional but also draws on international influences. Served by friendly and attentive waitstaff, the food is prepared with fresh, good-quality ingredients. Affording views of the verdant surroundings, the terraces in front and to the rear of the building are delightful in summer. This family-run establishment is also ideal for an overnight stay – on the edge of the forest, yet with good transport connections.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13901;Brasserie Colette Tim Raue;Germany;Constance;Brotlaube 2A, Constance, 78462, Germany;47.660811;9.1765899;53;false;true;French, Classic Cuisine;This is MICHELIN-starred chef Tim Raue's take on a French brasserie.As at the Colette brasseries in Berlin and Munich, there is a small à la carte selection, as well as three set menus: one comprising Colette classics, one devised by Tim Raue himself and a vegan menu. The highlight here is the first-floor terrace overlooking the pedestrian area – but seating is limited, so you'd be well advised to book!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13902;Golden Phoenix;Germany;Berlin;Brandenburgische Straße 21, Berlin, 10707, Germany;52.4957976;13.3086734;25;true;false;Chinese, French;This restaurant belonging to The Duc Ngo, owner of multiple restaurants, is located in the stylish Provocateur hotel. Expect a personable welcome and an informal atmosphere in this chic space with a visible kitchen. The French-influenced Chinese cuisine includes everything from interesting dim sum to sea bass, spinach, beurre blanc. Alternatively, you can eat in the adjoining bar. There are also outdoor tables: on the hotel terrace or on the pavement out front.;Terrace;[]
13903;EigenArt;Germany;Karlsruhe;Hebelstraße 17, Karlsruhe, 76133, Germany;49.0083148;8.4026804;24;false;true;International, Farm to table;This restaurant is set in a spruce townhouse centrally located close to Marktplatz. It is hardly surprising that there are so many regulars, given the very pleasant atmosphere and friendly service. The cuisine is seasonal and can be enjoyed as a set menu or ordered à la carte. By prior arrangement, you can also make reservations for lunch and at weekends.;Terrace;[]
13904;Nigrum;Germany;Baden-Baden;Schloßstraße 20, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7642671;8.2399669;65;true;false;International, Modern Cuisine;An impressive cross vault, elegant dark tones, designer elements, works of art – these former stables overlooking the city and a stone's throw from the New Castle have been stylishly converted. Drawing on modern influences, a three- to eight-course set menu is served – Beef tartare (classically prepared at the table) is available as an optional extra course. There is also a chic bar for an aperitif or digestif. Tip: You can reach the restaurant from the pedestrian area via the Burgstaffeln steps. There are several car parking spaces in front of the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
13905;Diergardts Kühler Grund;Germany;Hattingen;Am Büchsenschütz 15, Hattingen, 45527, Germany;51.4051276;7.2049366;58;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Established in 1904, this family-run restaurant is now in its fourth generation, with Philipp Diergardt now at the helm. He is passionate about cooking up traditional, seasonal cuisine that draws on locally sourced ingredients. The extensive menu is extremely appealing, making it difficult to choose. In addition to the fairly priced set menu ("Heimatmenü"), there are also classics such as bouillabaisse or Wiener schnitzel, as well as weekly specials that change with the seasons and dishes for two or more people. Wine connoisseurs will find plenty to enjoy here, and all reasonably priced. The fine selection of high-end German wines and French vintages is of particular note. Then there is the tasteful country house ambience, gorgeous terrace and attentive service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13906;Portomarin;Germany;Hamburg;Dorotheenstraße 180, Hamburg, 22299, Germany;53.5913302;10.0023221;40;false;true;Spanish;Red-painted walls and light wooden flooring sets the mood for dishes from the Iberian peninsula. From tapas to dessert, the menu is Spanish.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13907;esskunst;Germany;Schwarzenfeld;Hauptstraße 24, Schwarzenfeld, 92521, Germany;49.38906;12.1388095;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;The former hall of a bank is now a smart and sophisticated restaurant serving ambitious cuisine. Here, culinary tradition is tastefully combined with modern trends. On the menu, for example: char fillet, strudel dough, celery, turnips, kohlrabi. Tip: try the home-made pralines with your coffee. Charming, attentive and experienced service.;Terrace;[]
13908;Stüffel;Germany;Hamburg;Isekai 1, Hamburg, 20249, Germany;53.5854449;9.9886972;25;true;false;Farm to table, Mediterranean Cuisine;The riverside location here is every bit as appealing as the seasonal cuisine with Mediterranean and regional influences in which top-quality produce combines to create dishes such as fillet of spined loach with tomato, bread and basil salad. You can eat in the stylish modern bistro or outside on the waterfront. The wine list is well chosen and if you’re lucky the owner himself will advise you on your choice.;Interesting wine list;[]
13909;GRILL;Germany;Hamburg;Neuer Jungfernstieg 9, Hamburg, 20354, Germany;53.5554455;9.991496;68;false;false;Classic French, Meats and Grills;In this restaurant housed in Hotel Vier Jahreszeiten by Hamburg's Inner Alster lake, Caucasian walnut wood, warm colours such as olive green and pigeon blue, along with a log fire create an elegant yet cosy setting that harmoniously blends traditional and modern elements. On the menu: seafood specialities such as oysters and lobster, along with classics such as steak tartare and special cuts of meat cooked in the Southbend infrared broiler.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13910;ESSLIBRIS;Germany;Zweibrücken;Fasanerie 1, Zweibrücken, 66482, Germany;49.2449335;7.3927992;27;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Country cooking;ESSLIBRIS offers a relaxed, elegant atmosphere with a fine view of the garden. The food on offer is a mix of Mediterranean and regional. Try the suckling calf fillet and ravioli with carrots, parsley root and shallots. The kitchen is pleased to meet personal requests.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13911;Porte Neuf;Germany;Detmold;Woldemarstraße 9, Detmold, 32756, Germany;51.9361269;8.8836889;75;false;true;French;A good tip if you are looking for a place to eat in Detmold is this restaurant on the edge of the old town. Chef-patron Daniel C. Fischer awaits you in his compact, smartly designed establishment with a modern, feel-good atmosphere. In this setting, he serves up predominantly French-inspired classic cuisine with a modern twist. You can dine à la carte or opt for the set menu.;Terrace;[]
13912;Torschänke;Germany;Dudeldorf;Philippsheimer Straße 1, Dudeldorf, 54647, Germany;49.97374;6.6362885;17;true;true;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;Right next to the Obertor (the historical city gate), Torschänke is a really inviting restaurant. The atmosphere inside is cosy and pleasingly down to earth, and outside there is a lovely, leafy terrace. Dishes with French and Mediterranean influences are prepared using top-notch fresh produce and served by a friendly, attentive and proficient front-of-house team.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13913;Backmulde;Germany;Ladenburg;Hauptstraße 61, Ladenburg, 68526, Germany;49.47263;8.611793;76;false;false;Modern French;This is just the sort of restaurant you would like to have at home. Great food and select wines with good recommendations. All are served in the friendly surroundings of a charming, centuries-old, half-timbered building. Wine shop just over the road.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13914;Elefanten;Germany;Lauffen am Neckar;Bahnhofstraße 12, Lauffen am Neckar, 74348, Germany;49.0761065;9.1503916;18;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of this charming town is this welcoming inn, which is run with great dedication by the Glässing family – now in its fourth generation at the helm. The classic, regional cuisine makes full use of what each season has to offer, often drawing on regional produce to conjure up flavoursome dishes. You might choose to pair your food with one of the locally produced wines on offer.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13915;Schaarschmidt's;Germany;Leipzig;Coppistraße 32, Leipzig, 04157, Germany;51.3667341;12.3771544;26;true;false;Farm to table;This building on a corner plot with a gorgeous leafy façade is home to a cosy restaurant that is run with great dedication. Its many regulars come in droves to enjoy specialities of Saxon cuisine – the beef roulade is a firm favourite! The friendly waitstaff will gladly talk you through the options on the menu. Head for the lovely small terrace planted with trees.;Terrace;[]
13916;Münsters;Germany;Leipzig;Platnerstraße 13, Leipzig, 04159, Germany;51.3585245;12.3602928;61;true;true;Farm to table;This extremely popular place boasts fresh and flavoursome cuisine in the form of a short menu that changes with the seasons. Tables without tablecloths, wooden floorboards and partly exposed brick walls, as well as appealing wine-themed decorative details make for a cosy bistro feel with a rustic touch. The service is laid-back, friendly and attentive. The chef also gets in on the action front of house, providing charming service and excellent wine recommendations. There's also a great beer garden!;Car park,Terrace;[]
13917;alto;Germany;Bremen;Bredenstraße 2, Bremen, 28195, Germany;53.075509;8.8050647;94;false;true;Contemporary, Farm to table;This restaurant in the Atlantic Grand Hotel has a tastefully sleek interior, with dark wood panelling, large modern fixtures, as well as designer upholstered chairs in red and brown. The conservatory extension is also a lovely spot, as is the courtyard garden in fine weather – an Alpine-style hut is erected here every winter. The menu features classic dishes with a modern twist, plus classics such as schnitzel and burgers. Incidentally, the crockery is custom-made in Bremen. The location in the old town is ideal, with all the main attractions – the Weser River, Schnoor, Rathaus, Kunsthalle – just a short walk away.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13918;Crackers;Germany;Berlin;Friedrichstraße 158, Berlin, 10117, Germany;52.5164289;13.3886924;66;false;false;International;You’ll find this trendy eatery one floor below Cookies Cream. Ring the bell and the staff will lead you through the kitchen into a large and lively restaurant with a high ceiling and dim lights. The menu offers a range of ambitious meat and fish dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
13919;WEBERSTUBE;Germany;Schirgiswalde-Kirschau;Bautzener Straße 74, Schirgiswalde-Kirschau, 02681, Germany;51.095971;14.429233;49;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;Wood panelling, a tiled stove, pretty decor... The cosy, rustic-style restaurant in the Hotel BEI SCHUMANN has bags of regional charm. The same goes for the selection of ingredients used in the seasonal cuisine. The menu includes dishes such as spicy beef consommé, fried skrei with asparagus ragout and Saxony pancakes with apple sauce. Then of course there is the speciality: "Schuhmann's Currywurst", which comes in various degrees of spiciness. The cordial and professional service doesn't go unappreciated. Tip: Why not book yourself in for a fondue evening? Next door is the BEI CHURCHILL smoking lounge. There is a terrace at the front of the establishment.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13920;Schlegelhof;Germany;Kirchzarten;Höfener Straße 92, Kirchzarten, 79199, Germany;47.96171;7.974529;46;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;The ambience is friendly, the service cordial (the chefs, too, are always present) and the food really good. In addition to regional dishes such as the Rostbraten Schlegelhof Art, there are ambitious dishes exuding finesse, such as the Arctic char with chanterelles and black mountain lentils. Interesting wine selection. It is a pleasure to sit on the terrace or in the spacious meadow to the rear.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13921;Zum Riesen;Germany;Kandel;Rheinstraße 54, Kandel, 76870, Germany;49.0837233;8.2033744;69;true;true;International, Farm to table;The Wenz family put their heart and soul into running this place, and quality is also a top priority in the kitchen. Good-quality regional and seasonal ingredients are used to rustle up modern-inspired dishes, which are also served in the form of a set menu. Choose a regional wine to go with your food. In summer, the terrace in the courtyard is a secluded spot. There are lovely individually decorated guestrooms too.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13922;Schloss Loersfeld;Germany;Kerpen;Schloss Loersfeld 1, Kerpen, 50171, Germany;50.8894616;6.6956731;69;false;true;Classic French, International;The centuries-old castle set in extensive grounds really is a magnificent property. Behind the massive stone walls, stylish rooms and lounges with period details await. This stately backdrop makes for a fabulous setting in which to relish the modern cuisine with classic foundations, served à la carte or as a menu comprising three to six courses. Caviar or oysters are also popular appetisers. Friendly and attentive service. An adjacent building accommodates overnight guests in three pretty apartments.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13923;Inzlinger Wasserschloss;Germany;Inzlingen;Riehenstraße 5, Inzlingen, 79594, Germany;47.5870277;7.6973192;59;false;false;Classic Cuisine;With over 500 years of history to its name, plus a stylish interior, this moated castle near the Swiss border has for years been synonymous with classic French cuisine made from top-notch produce. You can dine à la carte or choose the set menu – there is also a vegetarian or vegan option. Accompany your food with one of the great wine recommendations. Our tip: The guesthouse 150m away has terrific rooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13924;Henrich HÖER's Speisezimmer;Germany;Idstein;Obergasse 26, Idstein, 65510, Germany;50.219769;8.2713257;22;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This 400-year-old half-timbered building, which houses Hotel Höerhof and its charming restaurant, is a place where you feel at home. The combination of the historical setting and modern touches makes for a special atmosphere – in summer, make a beeline for the gorgeous terrace in the secluded courtyard! Morish dishes from the region are served here, as well as a gourmet set menu (Wed-Sat).;Car park,Terrace;[]
13926;philipps restaurant;Germany;Hamburg;Turnerstraße 9, Hamburg, 20357, Germany;53.5581119;9.970912;74;false;true;International;A really appealing restaurant in the Schanzenviertel neighbourhood. A few steps lead down to this lively, modern establishment on the lower ground floor, where friendly and dedicated waitstaff serve fresh international cuisine. Tip: Be sure to make a reservation – this place is small and extremely popular!;Terrace;[]
13927;STRAUCHS FALCO;Germany;Hamburg;Koreastraße 2, Hamburg, 20457, Germany;53.5429318;10.0002884;55;true;false;International, Meats and Grills;This smart and stylish restaurant is next to the Maritime Museum. Situated in the Elbarkaden in the middle of HafenCity, it also boasts an appealing terrace. The menu features a variety of cuisines from around the globe, including specialities from the barbecue, Mediterranean dishes, such as fish and shellfish soup, German classics like Labskaus (meat stew) and Wiener schnitzel, as well as pasta. Additionally, there is the Bar & Deli.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13928;Rive Fish & Faible;Germany;Hamburg;Van-der-Smissen-Straße 1, Hamburg, 22767, Germany;53.5434867;9.9421049;64;false;false;Seafood, Meats and Grills;Sitting right on the port, this bistro is run by the same team as Tschebull. It serves good quality, flavoursome seafood and grilled meats alongside classic dishes such as Hamburger Pannfisch and Wiener Schnitzel. In summer the wonderful terrace is a must! Hot food served throughout the day.;Great view,Terrace;[]
13929;Kaltwassers Wohnzimmer;Germany;Zwingenberg;Obergasse 15, Zwingenberg, 64673, Germany;49.7235332;8.6137046;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;Wohnzimmer offers a cosy "living room" feel with some charming nostalgic touches inside and a designer atrium with view of the glazed kitchens in the interior courtyard. The modern regional cuisine uses fresh quality produce and includes dishes such as Wels catfish served with mashed potatoes and apples, kohlrabi and Ahle Worscht sausage.;Terrace;[]
13930;James Farmhouse;Germany;Flensburg;Fördepromenade 30, Flensburg, 24944, Germany;54.8120501;9.4555599;79;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Fresh and tasty cuisine is served here, and the menu is strongly influenced by the restaurant's own farm. For example, they raise their own Husum red pied pigs, chickens and German Angus cattle – exceptionally tender rump steaks guaranteed. The decor is a blend of industrial chic and charming retro style. Very friendly service. There is a smaller menu at lunchtime. Alongside the restaurants Das Grace and Minato, this is another dining option at the Hotel Das James, which enjoys a charming location on the harbour.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13931;Ente-Bistro;Germany;Wiesbaden;Kaiser-Friedrich-Platz 3, Wiesbaden, 65183, Germany;50.0850888;8.2441582;24;true;true;Classic French, Farm to table;This little offshoot of the famous Ente restaurant is also firmly established in the city. The ambience is typical of a bistro: narrow, cosy, lots of photos on the walls testifying to well-known patrons. Floor to ceiling windows make the premises nice and light. The cuisine is classically French and imbued with seasonal and Mediterranean influences.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13932;Schimmel's;Germany;Wustrow;Parkstraße 1, Wustrow, 18347, Germany;54.3462631;12.3969029;86;true;false;Country cooking;This restaurant's striking red façade draws the eye. The smart interior is modern and stylish, and the atmosphere is welcoming – the wooden tables are a nice touch. In the open kitchen, regional dishes are prepared, occasionally incorporating influences from around the globe. Diners can choose between the two set menus or order à la carte. The soups, for example, are delicious, but so is the fresh fish! The proprietress ensures cordial and attentive service. They also offer pretty guestrooms and holiday flats.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13933;Atlantik;Germany;Munich;Zenettistraße 12, Munich, 80337, Germany;48.1238482;11.5574605;15;true;true;Seafood, Contemporary;Located in the Dreimühlenviertel, this charming old brick building was a fish market back when it was set amid an abattoir and wholesale butchers. Now it has evolved into this attractive restaurant, which has been designed with an individual touch. Although seafood dominates the menu, it is far from being the only option. Those who prefer meat can indulge in a fillet of beef, to name but one example. Highly recommended for groups: a whole fish to share, eg. turbot, char or Atlantic lobster. Be sure to leave room for dessert – the chocolate cake is a tempting proposition! To accompany your meal, there is an extensive selection of fine wines to choose from.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13934;Oktopussy;Germany;Norderney;Luisenstraße 13, Norderney, 26548, Germany;53.706157;7.1408169;92;true;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;At the restaurant of the New Wave hotel, the food is down-to-earth and delicious, with a regional focus and an international twist. The menu features dishes such as braised ox cheek and Japanese-style halibut. Characterised by sleek, modern interior design with a maritime touch, the setting is appealing. There is also an open kitchen and a custom-built table for larger groups. The friendly, laid-back service is another draw. In summer, make a beeline for the secluded courtyard terrace. From May, the rooftop bar is open for delicious cocktails in a relaxed atmosphere.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13935;MAXIME de Guy Graessel;Germany;Bretten;Melanchthonstraße 35, Bretten, 75015, Germany;49.0374672;8.7043624;36;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;An appealing modern restaurant with an intimate atmosphere. Chef-patron Guy Graessel, who hails from Alsace, specialises in classic fare from Alsace and Baden. Diner choose between the five-course surprise menu (for two or more people) and à la carte dishes. For al fresco dining, there are tables in the charming verdant garden courtyard. Drinks are also served on the terrace in the pedestrian precinct Tip: Located in the entrance area, Café Hesselbacher has house-made cakes, tarts and pastries for sale at the weekend, over the counter or pre-ordered. For motorists, there is a car park – Parkhaus Löwenhof – not far from the restaurant.;Terrace;[]
13936;Zum Goldenen Pflug;Germany;Chieming;Kirchberg 3, Chieming, 83339, Germany;47.9242345;12.5067095;89;true;false;Country cooking, International;In one of the oldest inns in the region, tradition is celebrated, but not at the expense of progress. There are a number of charming dining areas in which to enjoy dishes such as Rindertafelspitz aus dem Kupferpfandl (boiled beef fillet from the copper pot), apple horseradish, chive sauce, creamed spinach and sautéed potatoes and, for dessert, Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake) with plum compote and whipped cream. Order à la carte or opt for the "Signature Menu" for two or more diners.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13937;ESSperiment;Germany;Delbrück;Schöninger Straße 74, Delbrück, 33129, Germany;51.788155;8.497642;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This relaxed modern restaurant with its lovely terrace offers a bistro menu at lunchtimes and fine dining in the evenings. The food is fresh and flavoursome. Try the saddle of venison with muesli, black salsify, pear and layered potato cake.;Terrace;[]
13938;Orania.Berlin;Germany;Berlin;Oranienplatz 17, Berlin, 10999, Germany;52.5021772;13.4168046;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant belonging to the lovely hotel that shares its name has a stylish, warm and relaxed ambience. The lobby and bar (with its interesting cocktail menu) are directly adjacent. Modern, creative dishes are sent out of the large open kitchen that draws the eye. Attentive and accomplished service. Try the four-course "Xberg Duck" set menu (min. two people).;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13939;Kitchen Library;Germany;Berlin;Bleibtreustraße 55, Berlin, 10623, Germany;52.5073556;13.3204234;88;true;false;Modern French;A great team of two, Daniela and Udo Knörlein run this place together - she looks after the guests cordially, while he cooks up the international "Kleine Dinger" set menu. Available with either four or five courses, an eight-course version for sharing is also possible. The characterful decor is reminiscent of a library: rustic-style charm and over 600 collector's items related to cookery.;Terrace;[]
13940;Wilde Klosterküche;Germany;Neuzelle;Bahnhofstraße 18, Neuzelle, 15898, Germany;52.0917869;14.6489556;44;false;true;Farm to table, Creative;This restaurant is located near the 13C Cistercian monastery with its Baroque church. The ambience is chic and modern, the kitchen partly visible. The food is carefully cooked and replete with flavour, and dishes reflect seasonal produce and ingredients that are mainly sourced from the region. A vegan option is also available by prior booking. Tip: They serve gin that they produce themselves. Guestrooms for an overnight stay in the separately run Klosterhotel.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13941;Julius;Germany;Berlin;Gerichtstraße 31, Berlin, 13347, Germany;52.5449031;13.3682985;50;true;false;Creative;This restaurant is in a sense the younger sibling of ernst, Dylan Watson-Brawn and Spencer Christenson's restaurant. Its interior is minimalist and sleek, the atmosphere youthful and laid-back. The kitchen, which is visible behind the counter, sends out creative dishes, which are also available in the form of a tasting menu in the evening, if booked in advance. A shorter lunch menu is served at weekends. You can also come for breakfast and brunch, as well as coffee, pastries and snacks during the day.;Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13942;Lucente;Germany;Essen;Rüttenscheider Str. 212, Essen, 45131, Germany;51.4266395;7.0023707;65;false;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;If you are on the lookout for good Italian cuisine in Rüttenscheid then this ristorante is the place for you. The menu includes classics such as vitello tonnato and house-made ravioli. The daily specials on the blackboard and recommendations announced by waitstaff are also interesting. The atmosphere is young, fresh, friendly - Italian joie de vivre is in the air here!;Terrace;[]
13943;Terra;Germany;Wolfsburg;Parkstraße 1, Wolfsburg, 38440, Germany;52.4329745;10.7897662;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This restaurant in the attractive Ritz-Carlton hotel boasts a bright and elegantly modern interior with captivating views of the VW works and the harbour basin afforded by floor-to-ceiling windows. The cuisine takes its cue from the seasons and showcases quality produce from the region and elsewhere in the country. One of their signature dishes is braised veal cheek with mustard jus. Good vegetarian options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
13944;Saxlers Restaurant;Germany;Zeltingen;Uferallee 9, Zeltingen, 54492, Germany;49.95226;7.017;44;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in the inviting Weinhotel St. Stephanus on the riverside promenade and not far from the old market square. In a refined setting, the friendly and committed hosts serve delicious food made with top-notch ingredients, vegetarian options included. The menu features classic dishes and regional specialities. Tip: Leave room for the delicious desserts! In the basement, the Braukeller serves Kloster Machern beer.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
13945;Zur Schlupp;Germany;Walluf;Hauptstraße 25, Walluf, 65396, Germany;50.0342407;8.1593026;32;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;The Ehrhardt family are passionate about their charming little restaurant, in a building dating back to 1608. The atmosphere is cosy, the cuisine fresh and in tune with the seasons – why not sample one of the fine wines from the region? Just don't forget to reserve. Our tip: the interior courtyard is a romantic spot in summer.;Terrace;[]
13947;Henssler Henssler;Germany;Hamburg;Große Elbstraße 160, Hamburg, 22767, Germany;53.5445706;9.9419014;78;true;false;Asian Influences;Set in a typical Hamburg location between the Holzhafen and Altona fish market, the restaurant of well-known TV chef Steffen Henssler stands amid a plethora of seafood and fishmongers. The interior is slick and smart, with a nice and lively laid-back atmosphere. The 20m-wide kitchen serves modern interpretations of sushi in many variations, as well as dishes such as teriyaki-style Faroe salmon or rump steak from the lava grill. Senior chef Werner Henssler also gets involved in the service. It is advisable to make a reservation, whether for lunch or dinner.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13948;Die Alte Schule;Germany;Herford;Holland 39, Herford, 32052, Germany;52.1179012;8.6731838;52;true;false;International;Torben Tönsing, scion of a well-known family of restaurateurs in Herford, took over this restaurant from his parents in 2017. He focuses on contemporary cuisine that draws on both regional and international influences. The 17C half-timbered building has a charming atmosphere – food is served on different levels, and in summer the secluded terrace comes into its own. Excellent wine selection – they even have their own wine shop.;Terrace;[]
13950;Oliveto;Germany;Bonn;Adenauerallee 9, Bonn, 53111, Germany;50.7335758;7.1080458;42;false;false;Italian;In the tastefully elegant restaurant on the ground floor of Ameron Bonn Hotel Königshof, the tables by the window or on the Rhine terrace come highly recommended. The attentive front-of-house team serves fresh, flavoursome Italian/Mediterranean cuisine. Decent selection of wines. Popular with business people at lunchtime. Some of the comfortable contemporary-style guestrooms boast a view of the Rhine.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13951;Warias Am Markt;Germany;Braunsbedra;Markt 14, Braunsbedra, 06242, Germany;51.2845748;11.8844145;93;true;false;Farm to table;Diners can expect regional and seasonal cuisine that makes use of excellent produce – the daily specials are always a good option. The menu features timeless favourites such as beef carpaccio with pesto and Belper Knolle cheese, or pan-seared fish-of-the-day with potato and cucumber salad. The single five- or nine-course surprise menu served on Friday and Saturday evenings available only by reservation. The restaurant has a convivial atmosphere, and the outdoor terrace is a delightful spot. Conveniently, the establishment has well-kept, light and airy guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13952;Salon 1900;Germany;Keitum;Keitumer Süderstr. 40, Keitum, 25980, Germany;54.8906008;8.368144;91;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This inviting thatched-roof cottage, somewhat off the beaten track in Keitum, is just as pretty inside. Low ceilings and decorative details such as pictures, old sewing machines, coffee grinders and various other features create a cosy and charming ambience with a nostalgic feel. The friendly team serves up classic regional cuisine with a modern twist.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13953;Brasserie Lamazère;Germany;Berlin;Stuttgarter Platz 18, Berlin, 10627, Germany;52.5051456;13.300745;87;false;false;French;Ready for a dose of French savoir-vivre in Berlin? You almost feel like you are in France here in the heart of Charlottenburg at Brasserie Lamazère thanks to its charming, down-to-earth and lively atmosphere. The regularly changing seasonal dishes are chalked up on the blackboard. You can put together your menu (starter, main, dessert) from a fine selection. They will be happy to recommend a good French wine pairing to accompany your food – the appealing and reasonably priced wine list is proprietor Régis Lamazère's passion.;;[]
13955;Landgasthaus zum Kreuz;Germany;Biberach;Untertal 7, Biberach, 77781, Germany;48.328019;8.0110798;88;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;Everything about this place is an appealing mix of regional and modern influences – from the cosy dining area to the food and the attractive, comfortable rooms in the Speicher guesthouse next door. The menu features classics and seasonal dishes – the "Mini-Versucherle", for instance, are intriguing. In summer, make the most of this delightful countryside location by dining on the fabulous terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13956;AnnA;Germany;Weimar;Markt 19, Weimar, 99423, Germany;50.9790747;11.3301215;84;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;This restaurant inside the luxury Hotel Elephant is flooded with beautiful light thanks to its enormous windows. Seated beneath the high ceiling, diners can take in the exclusive ambience – the pictures in the entrance area are particularly decorative. The regional cuisine is modern and creative. Be sure to take a stroll through the pretty old town.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13957;KINK Bar & Restaurant;Germany;Berlin;Schönhauser Allee 176, Berlin, 10119, Germany;52.5318902;13.4117557;75;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Head to Pfefferberg – former brewery compound, now cultural venue – for this trendy and urban restaurant. The modern and creative dishes showcase a certain flair and sense of individuality. Perhaps you'll go for one of the interesting concoctions on offer at the adjoining bar? The pleasantly relaxed service makes for a friendly, down-to-earth atmosphere. Beautiful terrace.;;[]
13958;Rutz - Zollhaus;Germany;Berlin;Carl-Herz-Ufer 30, Berlin, 10961, Germany;52.4966971;13.401064;48;false;true;Modern Cuisine, German;This restaurant's location on the Landwehrkanal truly lends it something special. In summer you can make the most of the covered terrace but the interior of this former customs house is also appealing, with its tasteful furnishings and relaxed atmosphere. The menu puts a modern spin on classic German fare. Note the selection of high-grade cold meats, to be ordered as a starter or side dish.;Terrace;[]
13959;ITO;Germany;Cologne;Antwerpener Straße 15, Cologne, 50672, Germany;50.9402484;6.9366162;20;false;true;Japanese, Modern Cuisine;In this trendy Japanese restaurant in the Belgian Quarter, Kengo Nishimi uses top-notch ingredients to create clearly structured dishes in which traditional Japanese cuisine is laced with modern European influences. In the evening, Japanese classics such as tempura, sashimi and sushi can be ordered à la carte, plus there is an extensive omakase menu. At lunchtime, a moderately priced set menu is available. In the front part of the restaurant, you can watch the chef at work at the sushi counter.;Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
13960;Marktwirtschaft Besigheim;Germany;Besigheim;Marktplatz 2, Besigheim, 74354, Germany;48.9996979;9.1416711;52;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;This charmingly laid-back restaurant serves dishes made with regional and seasonal ingredients, drawing on influences from the Mediterranean and beyond. The best way to experience the culinary artistry is through the six-course set menu. There is also a popular lunch deal that changes weekly. In the summer, the terrace on the charming little market square beckons, whether for a meal, a glass of wine or a coffee. The service is friendly and attentive. Across the street is the Marktkeller brasserie and wine bar. They also put on regular themed evenings. Tip: Take a stroll through the enchanting little half-timbered town!;Terrace;[]
13962;Restaurant Quack in der Villa Weismüller;Germany;Saarbrücken;Gersweilerstraße 43A, Saarbrücken, 66117, Germany;49.2320478;6.9634376;72;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;You can dine either out on the lovely terrace overlooking the city or inside – in a tastefully decorated dining area blending old-time elegance and more modern details. The ambitious seasonal menu proposes Mediterranean as well as regional dishes. The Chef's Table is an interesting affair: counter seating with a view into the kitchen, and a surprise menu. Good wine list. Be aware that the restaurant is accessed via a narrow private road.;Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13963;Fleher Hof;Germany;Düsseldorf;Fleher Straße 254, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.1911375;6.7707888;58;true;true;Regional Cuisine;A little out of the way, this traditional restaurant has a cosy interior, with all the charm of wood-panelled walls, old floorboards and wooden tables. Then there is the tasty cuisine, which includes flavoursome classics with a modern touch. Choose from the à la carte selection, or opt for one of the set menus ("Hof Menü", "Bistro Menü" or vegetarian). This pleasant restaurant is popular, so be sure to book in good time! N.B. Although finding a parking space may not be easy, it's definitely worth coming.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13964;Hofgut Albführen;Germany;Dettighofen;Albführen 5, Dettighofen, 79802, Germany;47.6414675;8.4869161;87;true;false;Classic Cuisine, International;This farmhouse set against a verdant backdrop of paddocks, woods and fields makes for a wonderful location. On top of that, you will eat well: seated in a tasteful interior, enjoy classical cuisine that draws on different international culinary traditions and makes full use of regional produce. Pretty and comfortable guestrooms, should you wish to stay the night.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13965;alexxanders;Germany;Chemnitz;Ludwig-Kirsch-Straße 9, Chemnitz, 09130, Germany;50.8374591;12.9356713;45;false;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Located in a residential area, this restaurant boasts a stylish interior and a courtyard terrace with a beautifully landscaped little garden. The flavoursome dishes draw inspiration from around the globe and incorporate Mediterranean and seasonal influences. Why not enjoy an aperitif at the bar before your meal? The wine list is also worth a look. Tip: The appealing and reasonably priced lunch deal draws in a lot of customers during the week. Guestrooms with modern interior design are available in the hotel of the same name.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13966;Poisson;Germany;Cologne;Wolfsstraße 6, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.9378549;6.9467827;67;false;true;Seafood;Top quality products are deliciously prepared at this modern bistro with a fish orientated menu. The chef allows Asian, as well as Mediterranean and classic components to influence his food.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13967;Kuro Mori;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Grünwälderstraße 2, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79098, Germany;47.9942154;7.8496256;90;true;false;Asian Influences, Contemporary;"The Black Forest meets Asia" is the motto of this cool, stylish restaurant located in Freiburg's beautiful old town. Kuro mori is Japanese for "black forest". Here, modern dishes are conjured up from high-quality ingredients in an open kitchen. As well as an à la carte selection, a small set menu is proposed at lunchtime and a more sophisticated one in the evening. There are also two special offers available on Tue to Thu evenings: "Dinner for two" and "Twenü" (for foodies under the age of 30). Tip: Owner Steffen Disch, who some will know from Gasthaus zum Raben in Horben, also offers cookery courses.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
13968;GUI;Germany;Bielefeld;Gehrenberg 8, Bielefeld, 33602, Germany;52.0199052;8.5323604;73;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;It's a good idea to book, because this lively bistro in the middle of town has more than its fair share of regulars! The Mediterranean-inspired cuisine also has regional influences. The quality of the ingredients is first rate, from the fresh pasta with porcini to the cod and the tender venison fillet. The modern interior decor is pleasant – the floor-to-ceiling shelf with decorative wine bottles draws the eye, as does the open kitchen with one striking red wall. In summer, the terrace in the pedestrian area is very inviting. Incidentally, ĝui means "enjoy" in the international language of Esperanto.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13969;ESTIMA by Catalana;Germany;Erfurt;Allerheiligenstraße 3, Erfurt, 99084, Germany;50.9781375;11.0265937;59;false;false;Spanish Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;Set in the heart of the old town, not far from the cathedral, this compact restaurant with an open kitchen serves flavoursome Catalan-inspired dishes. At the helm in the kitchen is Jürgen Birth, who skilfully weaves both Spanish and French elements into his modern set menu. His penchant for patisserie is also evident. The set menu (also available in a vegetarian or pescetarian version) can be accompanied by select Spanish wines, enthusiastically presented by owner Jan-Hendrik Feldner – his personalised style of service is highly attentive. They also run a tapas restaurant about 100m away.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13970;Intuu;Germany;Göttingen;Berliner Straße 30, Göttingen, 37073, Germany;51.533758;9.9259671;33;false;false;Japanese Contemporary, South American;Ensconced in the Freigeist hotel is this appealingly modern and lively restaurant. Diners have the option of sitting at the counter with views of the action in the open kitchen, as the team prepares a broad offering of Japanese and South American cuisine: dishes range from sushi and sashimi, tempura and yakitori to meats grilled in the Josper oven. These are also perfect plates for sharing.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13971;Rubens;Germany;Düsseldorf;Kaiserstraße 5, Düsseldorf, 40479, Germany;51.2344727;6.7782144;17;false;false;Austrian, Traditional Cuisine;This pretty restaurant owned by friendly hosts Cornelia Stolzer and Ruben Baumgart – she is Austrian and he is German-Austrian – is something of an Alpine hot spot. Accordingly, classics such as Backhendl (breaded fried chicken), Alt-Wiener Tafelspitz (prime boiled beef) or Kaiserschmarrn (shredded pancake), as well as modern dishes feature on the menu. Charming, well-trained waitstaff and a decent selection of Austrian wines. Incidentally, the pumpkin seed oil comes from the proprietress's village.;Terrace;[]
13972;Goldmund;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Schöne Aussicht 2, Frankfurt on the Main, 60311, Germany;50.1093495;8.6930611;77;false;false;Classic French;The restaurant in the Literaturhaus, set on the banks of the Main, has an extremely stylish and upscale interior. The large bar area and the striking portraits of international figures from the arts draw the eye as you savour food that tends towards the classical. The adjoining Kaminzimmer ("fireplace room") is also very pleasant. Plenty of places to park behind the restaurant. This address is also ideal as an event location.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13973;Salt & Silver -  Lateinamerika;Germany;Hamburg;Hafenstraße 136, Hamburg, 20359, Germany;53.5465299;9.9585587;27;false;true;Latin American;A slice of Latin America in St. Pauli. With a view of the Elbe, you can enjoy a set menu (with fish and meat or vegetarian) that is inspired by the travels of the two owners. The cuisines of Mexico and Peru in particular are reflected in the piquancy and interplay of spiciness and acidity. Far Eastern touches also feature. Flavours from far-flung places are combined with local ingredients, with an emphasis on sustainability. The charming front-of-house team is professional and caters to diners' needs with a confidence that contributes to the enjoyably lively ambience.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13974;Freisinger Hof;Germany;Munich;Oberföhringer Straße 189, Munich, 81925, Germany;48.1745958;11.6297813;52;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, International;It is easy to see why this charming inn dating from 1875 is always busy. It boasts a stylish interior, a lively atmosphere and delicious food. There are classics from Bavaria and Austria – the focus is on beef but there is also Backhendl (breaded fried chicken). If you're lucky, you'll be able to try the fabulous creamy veal goulash at lunchtime. Quick and helpful service. You can have a comfortable stay in one of the well-maintained guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13975;BEES Restaurant;Germany;Rüdesheim am Rhein;Am Rottland 6, Rüdesheim am Rhein, 65385, Germany;49.9774499;7.9156229;74;true;false;Farm to table;This attractive restaurant serving appealing seasonal cuisine is housed in the premises of a former Asbach Uralt brandy distillery. The set menu includes a minimum of four courses, but you can also order à la carte. Sit back to savour your meal and enjoy friendly service in this chic setting with a partially visible kitchen. Tables are set up to create a pleasant terrace in summer. Tip for motorists: there is also a public car park near the train station and the Rhine.;;[]
13976;Lindenhof-Kasteel;Germany;Munchengladbach;Vorster Straße 535, Munchengladbach, 41169, Germany;51.2057238;6.3417062;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Volker and Susanne Kasteel have been playing host to their guests with great dedication for many years. In a tasteful interior (featuring ceiling beams from the original building, which dates back to 1682), tuck into ingredient-focused, seasonally inspired cuisine that draws on both classic and modern influences. Should you wish to spend the night, the hotel of the same name has well-kept guestrooms.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
13977;[w]einklang;Germany;Nuremberg;Johannisstraße 130, Nuremberg, 90402, Germany;49.4610098;11.0540419;28;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;In the northwest of Nuremberg, this chic little restaurant boasts a wonderfully cosy atmosphere. Here, owner and chef de cuisine Tomas Spanu, who has Sardinian-French heritage, serves a set menu comprising four or five courses – pleasingly streamlined and ingredient focused. Also available as a vegetarian menu option. The friendly and attentive service is the icing on the cake. You will want to keep coming back for more!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
13978;Springbrunnen SKLENAR;Germany;Oberkirch;Springstraße 11, Oberkirch, 77704, Germany;48.5535761;8.0687485;76;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Spanish;After almost 30 years in Mallorca, Czech-born Martin Sklenar and his wife Lucie swapped the Balearic island for the vineyards of Oberkirch. Here, they propose an interesting blend of regional (Baden), Mallorcan and Bohemian-inspired cuisine. This is served in a cosy interior with a slightly rustic feel, or out on the wonderful terrace known as the Weinberggarten. The ingredient-led dishes can be accompanied by your choice of wine from a predominantly regional selection.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13980;STUBN in der Frasdorfer Hütte;Germany;Frasdorf;Zellboden, Frasdorf, 83112, Germany;47.77559;12.28774;79;false;true;Alpine, Modern Cuisine;This exclusive mountain-top location, surrounded by woods and meadows, really is the stuff of dreams. What was once a hiking lodge is now a cosy restaurant serving modern Alpine cuisine that can only be reached on foot (50 minutes from the Lederstube car park) or by booking a shuttle bus. Diners seated at the front can see the chefs at work in the open kitchen, grilling top-quality produce over an open fire. A shining example is the super-fresh Chiemsee pike-perch with bold roasted aromas, accompanied by an intensely flavoursome Jerusalem artichoke puree and crunchy rapini – a delightfully accessible combination. You can choose à la carte from a short list of options or have a surprise menu put together for you. The evening menu is also available at lunchtime, if requested in advance. The wine list is very well curated and the waitstaff are highly adept. The terrace is wonderful in summer! Simple guestrooms can be booked for overnight stays.;Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
13981;Lovis;Germany;Berlin;Kantstraße 79, Berlin, 10627, Germany;52.5073295;13.2972357;60;false;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;An impressive architectural feat – a former prison has been transformed into an attractive restaurant. High ceilings and exposed brick walls, sleek interior design and soft lighting make for a special atmosphere. Diners take their seats in the former lock yard, now covered and fitted with large windows – the "Aquarium" room is truly original. The modern vegetable-oriented cuisine is available as a set menu or à la carte – regular, vegetarian or also vegan upon request. Food intolerances can be accommodated too. A selection of wines from around the globe. Tip: Enjoy an aperitif in the lovely bar, which also boasts a terrace. You can enjoy a night in Wilmina, the adjacent hotel.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
13982;PULS;Germany;Cologne;Bürgerstraße 2, Cologne, 50667, Germany;50.9386572;6.9593568;29;true;true;Contemporary, International;With this culinary hotspot located in the chic boutique hotel Legend, Daniel Gottschlich (known from Ox & Klee) has another restaurant concept to his name in the cathedral city. The vibe here is lively, modern and urban. You can dine at the bar, at one of the high tables or at a regular table. In summer, there is the gorgeous terrace. Johannes Langenstück's kitchen team serves up bar food as well as dishes for sharing – also available in individual portions. Or would you prefer the surprise menu "Chefs Choice"? Decent wine list and an appealing cocktail selection including their "Signature" drinks.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
13983;Zum Wendl;Germany;Freyung;Stadtplatz 2, Freyung, 94078, Germany;48.8091193;13.5475049;100;false;false;Bavarian, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant dating back to 1889 has a long history to its name. Today, Bavarian-style cuisine is the name of the game, presented in both traditional and modern guises. Fine examples include Bavarian Forest venison roulade stuffed with smoked meat, cranberries and pickled vegetables, mashed parsnip and potato, and a red cabbage roll, or pan-fried Breitenberg char with wild broccoli, spicy curry carrot puree, aniseed crust and lime foam. Alternatively, "Signature Dishes" such as Wiener schnitzel, cordon bleu and roast onion are available. We also recommend the two three- to four-course menus. The restaurant is housed in the hotel of the same name, which has a small spa area. This a great place to spend the night – then you can take full advantage of the excellent wine list. It features a good 180 items and is mostly devoted to German wines, especially Riesling.;Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
13985;vierzehn 85;Germany;Leiwen;Euchariusstraße 10, Leiwen, 54340, Germany;49.8227481;6.8828163;30;true;false;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;The former tithe farm from 1485 - still with a beautiful half-timbered façade - offers homely, modern guest rooms and a very nice, tasteful and casual restaurant on two floors with smaller and larger rooms and charming niches. The kitchen serves really good contemporary dishes from many regional and always seasonal products. Wines from the own vineyard. In summer, the terrace is inviting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
13987;Oukan;Germany;Berlin;Ackerstraße 144, Berlin, 10115, Germany;52.5322024;13.3957924;45;false;true;Vegan, Japanese;It's worth seeking out this restaurant, which is tucked away in a side street. The Japanese-inspired cuisine is completely vegan, with fermented food playing a major role – hence the "Fermentation Lab" having been built in the cellar. There is a creative menu with six to eight courses. The dishes are pleasantly stripped back, but no less complex for it. A shining example is the delicately cooked, finely sliced and grilled king oyster mushrooms seasoned with a squeeze of lime, sprinkled with a yeast/brioche crumble and served with a mushroom broth with thyme and apple cider, which adds a subtle spiciness. The intriguing tea pairing is a must! The icing on the cake is the decor. Drawing on Far Eastern influences, the aptly clean-lined, minimalist-style interior is done out in soothing dark tones. Extremely friendly service is the final flourish.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13988;Brasserie Cocotte;Germany;Ravensburg;Grüner-Turm-Straße 16, Ravensburg, 88212, Germany;47.7841915;9.613072;63;true;false;French;Not only does this place have a really charming brasserie vibe (decorative pictures of cooking legends such as Paul Bocuse and Marco Pierre White), but they also serve good food. French cuisine is the order of the day. Be sure to check out the inviting terrace laid out beneath shady trees.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
13989;Ursprung;Germany;Friedrichstadt;Am Mittelburgwall 4, Friedrichstadt, 25840, Germany;54.376572;9.0910673;45;true;false;Contemporary;This smart restaurant is set in the family-run Hotel Aquarium, which is located in the heart of the beautiful city centre. With Jan Boddenberg, the third generation is now at the helm. As head chef, he curates a modern set menu and delivers classic, regional dishes, attaching importance to good produce and seasonality. Friendly service.;Car park;[]
13990;Restaurant zum Bären;Germany;Balduinstein;Bahnhofstraße 24, Balduinstein, 65558, Germany;50.3462368;7.9690269;56;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;The Buggle family has been running this traditional restaurant in the idyllic Lahn Valley since 1827. With chef Joachim Buggle, the eighth generation is now at the helm and his concept is impressive. He has dedicated himself to culinary classics, serving flavour-intensive, pleasantly pared-back dishes prepared without fuss or frills. Examples from the menu include dishes such as braised veal shank with root vegetables, leek, and potato and cheese purée, or fillet of line-caught sea bass with stuffed courgette, wild garlic risotto and a crustacean foam. The restaurant, with its delightful country-house style interior, has a pleasant and cosy atmosphere, while the Weinstube exudes a slightly more rustic feel. And then they have another ace up their sleeve in the form of a wonderful terrace in the shade of the lime trees! The front-of-house team provides charming and friendly service. The Landhotel zum Bären is also an excellent option, should you wish to spend the night here.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13991;Kaminstube;Germany;Baiersbronn;Hermine-Bareiss-Weg 1, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5205998;8.3269829;72;false;false;Classic French, International;The stylish and elegant dining area boasts the fireplace after which this restaurant is named. Classic and traditional cuisine with international influences is served – small portions are also possible. The terrace with a view of the Ellbachtal is popular in summer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13992;Heiligenstein;Germany;Baden-Baden;Heiligensteinstraße 19a, Baden-Baden, 76534, Germany;48.7189251;8.1875123;82;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Come here to enjoy classic seasonal cuisine in a tasteful, modern setting. High-quality, fresh ingredients are prepared in an agreeably straightforward way that brings out their flavour. Then there's the excellent wine list featuring over 400 different bottles. Pretty terrace. The hotel boasts a peaceful location and lovely, cosy guestrooms.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
13993;moriki;Germany;Baden-Baden;Lange Straße 100, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7688617;8.2309896;53;true;false;Asian, Japanese;Situated very close to the Festspielhaus (opera and concert house), the restaurant of Roomers hotel serves pan-Asian cuisine and a wide range of sushi. The menu reads, for example, "sake teriyaki – Scottish salmon, teriyaki glaze, sweet cucumber, rice". In a setting that is upscale and very much on trend, a young and enthusiastic front-of-house team provides competent service while maintaining a laid-back atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
13994;Penz Am Dom;Germany;Altenberge;Kirchstraße 13, Altenberge, 48341, Germany;52.0464588;7.467081;42;true;true;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;In this attractive old townhouse opposite the cathedral, history meets modernity, to create a lovely harmonious setting in which to savour seasonally influenced cuisine. There are two four-course set menus, from which you can also choose à la carte. Tip: Come for the "After Work Dinner" on Mondays, when there is a three-course set menu for €28. At lunchtime during the week, only the "Business Lunch" set menu is served. Great terrace!;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
13995;plaisir by Hamid Heidarzadeh;Germany;Aachen;Schlossstraße 16, Aachen, 52066, Germany;50.7690425;6.1009725;48;false;false;Contemporary;The minimalist, elegant look immediately catches the eye, with its gorgeous terrazzo flooring, clean-lined, pared-back design in black and white, and high ceilings with stunning mouldings. Chef Hamid Heidarzadeh blends classic foundations and modern elements to interesting effect, incorporating subtle Asian and Mediterranean influences. Two set menus are available in a three- or five-course format – one vegetarian ("Pflanzenfresser/-innen"), one with meat ("Fleischfresser/-innen"). The names belie finely tuned and precisely crafted dishes with full-bodied taste profiles, such as the boldly seasoned tartare of Balfego tuna with hints of spiciness courtesy of jalapeno cream, and beautiful layers of acidity thanks to the vinegar mayonnaise, as well as the freshness of subtly sweet grapefruit ice cream, plated on an aromatic salad of finely diced tomatoes. The laid-back yet discreet service is pleasant, and the chefs also join in with the service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
13997;Hasenpfeffer;Germany;Rathenow;Ferchesarer Straße 8B, Rathenow, 14712, Germany;52.6445361;12.4005319;80;false;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;This elegant restaurant in the idyllically situated Golf Resort Semlin is something of a culinary beacon in the region. They serve contemporary creations that are in touch with the seasons and draw on regional influences. Prepared from very good ingredients, these dishes can be sampled as a set menu or à la carte. The beautiful view of the golf course – through the floor-to-ceiling windows – also deserves a mention.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
13998;Eulenstein;Germany;Idstein;Friedrich-Ebert-Straße 9, Idstein, 65510, Germany;50.2151296;8.2647109;83;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Taking its cue from the seasons and made with select ingredients, the food here is meticulously prepared, flavoursome and fresh – it is clear that chef Steve Eulenstein has worked at some top-flight establishments in his time. He proposes two set menus as well as classics such as rump steak. The dining space is attractive and minimalist in style, and the service is friendly and professional. The location in a residential area just a few minutes' drive from the BAB 3 motorway is also convenient.;Terrace;[]
14000;Rocus;Germany;Baunach;Bahnhofstraße 16, Baunach, 96148, Germany;49.9890721;10.8539428;20;true;true;International, Classic Cuisine;Housed in an attractively converted railway building dating from 1904, this restaurant proposes ambitious cuisine that takes its cue from the seasons – available à la carte or as a set menu. Dine al fresco in the courtyard or on the terrace facing the railway line. A table in the wine cellar, surrounded by Spanish red wines, comes highly recommended.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14001;Landhaus Hadrys;Germany;Magdeburg;An der Halberstädter Chaussee 1, Magdeburg, 39116, Germany;52.0981133;11.5753079;18;false;true;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;Since 2003, Sebastian Hadrys has been synonymous with sophisticated cuisine! The food is seasonal and has an international edge. There is a set menu that you can put together yourself by choosing three to seven courses. The prices are very reasonable and the wine list is also very good. As for the setting, the pleasantly bright, modern space has a casual feel, plus a large terrace. Experienced staff provide friendly service. Tip: Cookery courses are also organised here.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14002;Engelwirts-Stube;Germany;Baiersbronn;Rechtmurgstraße 28, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5316683;8.2834842;18;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;This lovely restaurant with its delightful terrace overlooking the garden serves regional and seasonal cuisine with the odd nod to international culinary traditions. A friendly and well-drilled front-of-house team help to create an inviting atmosphere. Tip: If you want to be close to the action, book the Chef's Table in the kitchen ( minimum 6 people). And if you wish to spend a little longer here, Hotel Engel Obertal offers comfortable, stylish guestrooms and fantastic facilities to help make your stay a relaxing one.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14003;Menge;Germany;Arnsberg;Ruhrstraße 60, Arnsberg, 59821, Germany;51.4011388;8.0643033;70;true;true;Farm to table, French Contemporary;Christoph Menge cooks ambitious, flavoursome food that is both contemporary and classic. Dishes include sweet and sour schnitzel and Bavarian cream dessert with a duo of rhubarb, which is bound to set your taste buds tingling. Depending on the season, the menu also includes local Galloway beef, game and lamb.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14004;PURS;Germany;Andernach;Steinweg 30, Andernach, 56626, Germany;50.4389346;7.3973765;82;false;false;Modern French, Fusion;Peter Fridén, of YOSO fame, has brought his "New Nordic Japanese Cuisine" to the 17C Alte Kanzlei, the interior of which has been tastefully designed by Axel Vervoordt. In a small side street adjacent to the boutique hotel PURS, this beautiful building houses a chic restaurant decorated in muted tones. Inside, the eye is drawn to the artwork on the walls and the open kitchen, visible through a glass sliding door, where Fridén brings together three different cuisines. Born in South Korea, he grew up in Sweden, and is schooled in the French culinary arts. His six-course tasting menu (vegetarian version also available) reflects his personality with an intriguing fusion of Asian-Japanese, Scandinavian and French elements. An appealing case in point is his combination of dashi chawanmushi, delicately smoked Oscietra caviar, Mangalitza bacon broth with a subtle smoky flavour and a hint of lemon salt. Accompanied by a carefully curated selection of wines by the glass (over 1 000 labels). The sake and kombucha selections are also impressive.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14005;Rössle;Germany;Alpirsbach;Aischbachstraße 5, Alpirsbach, 72275, Germany;48.3444584;8.404488;99;false;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;This family-run business is now in its fourth generation. Behind a smart half-timbered façade, diners can choose from seasonal cuisine with some international influences and classics with a connection to the region. There are guestrooms done out in a modern Black Forest style. If you fancy a little excursion, the monastery complex and brewery are both within easy walking distance.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14006;Wintergarten;Germany;Baden-Baden;Schillerstraße 4, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7561164;8.2400955;27;true;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;The tastefully designed conservatory restaurant of the long-established Brenners Park-Hotel & Spa is a light and airy space with floor-to-ceiling glazing that affords a splendid view of the leafy gardens – and the terrace is, of course, especially inviting. In the evening, the classic and seasonal dishes can be enjoyed as a set menu or ordered à la carte. Vegetarian options are also available. A three-course set menu is served at lunchtime from Monday to Friday.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
14007;Müllers auf der Burg;Germany;Geisenheim;Rosengasse 32, Geisenheim, 65366, Germany;50.0080143;7.9777168;49;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;With his chic brasserie in the glass-paned extension at Schwarzenstein Castle, Nelson Müller has brought his gastronomical philosophy to the Rheingau. Diners can take in stunning views – especially delightful from the terrace – and savour freshly prepared classic Mediterranean cuisine with a hint of rustic simplicity. Options range from Breton turbot to veal currywurst. For overnight stays, there are wonderful individually styled guestrooms and suites available at the Burghotel, Burgresidenz and Gästehaus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14008;Bar Mural;Germany;Munich;Theresienstraße 1, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1469093;11.5788632;55;false;true;Contemporary, International;This hip bar is loud, lively and trendy – and therein lies its charm! The short menu features various cold cut platters, as well as a selection of tasty and carefully thought-out dishes, which are also served as a set menu – a vegetarian version is also available. A few options can also be ordered to share. For advice on what to drink, just ask the laid-back, well-drilled service team. The wine list is moderately priced and includes a decent selection of wines by the glass. Terrace seating is offered in the inner courtyard behind the restaurant and on the pavement in front of the house.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14009;Sonne;Germany;Vörstetten;Freiburger Straße 4, Vörstetten, 79279, Germany;48.0645939;7.8500348;87;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Contemporary;In this historic inn with a lovely half-timbered façade and a cosy rural-style feel inside, the young owner serves up dishes such as braised knuckle of pasture-raised lamb with Madeira, or pike-perch fillet with chanterelles. The terrace lies under a big old chestnut tree. There are also guestrooms for an overnight stay.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14010;Weinhaus Anker;Germany;Marktheidenfeld;Obertorstraße 13, Marktheidenfeld, 97828, Germany;49.8456206;9.6003008;76;false;true;French, Country cooking;A restaurant that is steeped in tradition and run with great commitment. The lovely interior exudes a historical charm in which to enjoy French and regional dishes, and the service is friendly – hostess Elisabeth Deppisch is also a sommelière. In the winter, on Thu-Sat evenings, a short Franconian menu is served in the rustic vaulted Schöpple. You can also stay overnight in well-kept guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14011;Oberländer Weinstube;Germany;Karlsruhe;Akademiestraße 7, Karlsruhe, 76133, Germany;49.0117334;8.3981052;34;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This townhouse, built in 1826, is full of charm: inside you sit in a cosy, traditional wood-panelled decor, while the charming courtyard beckons outside. And in addition they take really friendly care of you. The kitchen turns out dishes that are adapted to the seasons and really tasty. At lunchtime you choose from a smaller menu.;Terrace;[]
14012;Renoir;Germany;Auerbach;Schönheider Straße 235, Auerbach, 08209, Germany;50.509373;12.46294;23;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;This restaurant has been building on a solid reputation for over 30 years, serving classic cuisine and a sophisticated yet pleasantly down-to-earth atmosphere. Delicious dishes are served as a seasonal menu comprising three to five courses or à la carte. Astute wine recommendations come courtesy of the maître d', who happens to be a trained sommelier. Tip: The small gallery in the building is definitely worth a visit.;Car park;[]
14013;Landgasthof zum Adler;Germany;Überlingen;Hauptstraße 44, Überlingen, 88662, Germany;47.8044515;9.2380514;79;true;false;Country cooking, Home Cooking;This is a charming family-run establishment. The cosy restaurant is housed in an old half-timbered building, and there are attractive and comfortable cottage-style guestrooms in both the main building and the guesthouse. The menu is dominated by home-style regional dishes, but there are also more sophisticated options. Apart from traditional fare (eg Zwiebelrostbraten – fried beef with onions), a well-devised set menu of the day is proposed, including dishes such as Arctic char, Riesling, julienne vegetables and pasta.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14014;Überland;Germany;Brunswick;Willy-Brandt-Platz 18, Brunswick, 38102, Germany;52.2558748;10.5405541;55;true;false;Contemporary, International;In less than a minute, the lift takes you up to the 18th floor of the BraWoPark building near Hauptbahnhof. People come here to enjoy modern cuisine in a trendy, chic setting – not to mention the view. Try the choice cuts of the excellent beef aged in-house. Incidentally, the concept is the brainchild of TV chef and food professional Tim Mälzer. NB: two sittings per evening. On the floor above, rooftop bar and terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14015;Brasserie Ehrlich;Germany;Freital;Wiesenweg 1, Freital, 01705, Germany;51.028285;13.6250451;61;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;A French-style brasserie par excellence. Stephan Fröhlich and his wife Nadine run their small restaurant with a personal touch – he is the head chef and she is the sommelier. In this cosy setting, diners can look forward to friendly service and good seasonal cuisine in the form of two set menus. Given the popularity of the place, it is advisable to book in advance. In summer the gorgeous terrace beckons. Tip: Delicatessen goods can be purchased to take home. Overnight accommodation available.;Terrace;[]
14016;am kai;Germany;Hamburg;Große Elbstraße 145 b, Hamburg, 22767, Germany;53.544672;9.9342709;51;false;true;Seafood, International;Trendy, hip and relaxed is how you might describe this pleasant restaurant right on the waterfront. Great view of the container port – especially from the terrace in summer. The kitchen serves modern seafood, e.g. Tristan Rock Lobster, Bisque, Papaya, Mousseline. Some dishes are also ideal for sharing. Vegetarian and vegan dishes are also available. In addition to the a la carte selection, the restaurant offers a tasting menu with six or seven courses.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14017;Museum;Germany;Munich;Prinzregentenstraße 3, Munich, 80538, Germany;48.1433181;11.5898402;94;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;A hip address in the Bavarian National Museum. The best thing is to sit outside on the cosy terrace, otherwise beneath the cross vaults and high ceilings in the chic modern brasserie ambience. Shorter, simpler menu at lunchtime, more ambitious seasonal Mediterranean cuisine in the evening. Wine list with specialities, but also wines for any time.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14018;erasmus;Germany;Karlsruhe;Nürnberger Straße 1, Karlsruhe, 76199, Germany;48.9848686;8.4033911;59;false;false;Italian, Farm to table;In a listed building dating from 1928, Marcello Gallotti provides charming service and excellent recommendations from the well-stocked wine list to accompany his ambitious Italian-Mediterranean cuisine. This is served in form of the four- to six-course set menus "Terra e Mare" (meat and fish) and "Flora e Prato" (vegetarian), from which you can also choose à la carte. There is also a short oyster menu and organic Riofrío caviar. The terrace overlooking the garden with its old trees is marvellous! Thu. to Sat. wine bar on the roof terrace. They run a delicatessen next door. A commitment to sustainability underpins their work, and the restaurant is certified organic.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14019;893 Ryotei;Germany;Berlin;Kantstraße 135, Berlin, 10623, Germany;52.5059322;13.3167205;89;false;true;Japanese Contemporary, Creative;The mirrored, graffiti-covered façade gives no hint of the restaurant that lies behind it. But despite appearances, this restaurant is a hit, drawing in diners in their droves. The trendy interior is done out in black and furnished with small tables. Guests bask in a lively atmosphere that centres around the open kitchen. Here, The Duc Ngu serves up a wide range of Japanese cuisine, infused with other Asian, South American and European influences, incorporating a wealth of spices. The menu includes traditional favourites such as sushi, sashimi, tempura and tataki, as well as more creative options like "sashimi taquitos", "tai yuzu truffle" and "unagi royal".;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
14020;Kräutergarten;Germany;Wachtberg;Töpferstraße 30, Wachtberg, 53343, Germany;50.6134266;7.0571836;35;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The friendly and dedicated hosts have been running this restaurant with an appealing elegant interior since 1983. It is with good reason that they have won over their many regulars: their classically oriented cuisine is seasonal and focuses on the quality and freshness of the ingredients. The service comes courtesy of attentive waitstaff. You'll certainly want to come back again!;Terrace;[]
14021;Forsthaus Ilkahöhe;Germany;Tutzing;Oberzeismering 2, Tutzing, 82327, Germany;47.89937;11.255;26;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine;The idyllic hilltop location with its fantastic view across Tutzing to the lake is a huge draw of this restaurant – the terrace is fabulous! This converted forester's lodge has an attractive, upscale interior that combines modern style and regional touches. The menu features seasonal dishes made with select ingredients. Mediterranean and international influences are as prominent as the regional classics. While only a small selection of simpler dishes is served at lunchtime, things take a more ambitious turn in the evening. There is also a self-service beer garden.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14022;Königshafen;Germany;List;Alte Dorfstraße 1, List, 25992, Germany;55.0200546;8.4353115;71;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;The journey up to the north of the island is well worth it! Here, family tradition dates back to 1881, with the fifth generation currently looking after this spruce house with a white-brick façade, serving good regional and seasonal cuisine. Nice garden terrace behind the house. Tip: They are always well booked, so you should book early!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14023;Christophorus;Germany;Stuttgart;Porscheplatz 5, Stuttgart, 70435, Germany;48.8345812;9.1521304;49;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, International;For car enthusiasts who are fans of quality cuisine: here you can take in views of the Porsche Museum or Porscheplatz as you tuck into Mediterranean and international fare such as confit turbot fillet, pancetta foam, black trumpets, pumpkin quiche and Amalfi lemon or barbecued US prime beef. The open kitchen offers some fascinating insights. Impressive wine list comprising over 500 items. Located on the third floor, the restaurant can be accessed directly from the car park via a lift.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14024;Krone;Germany;Steinenbronn;Stuttgarter Straße 45, Steinenbronn, 71144, Germany;48.6636584;9.1202761;89;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;Nestled in the heart of Steinenbronn, this family-run establishment has been welcoming diners for many years. Here, modernity meets tradition in both the decor and the cuisine. The menu features timeless classics such as pork fillet in a creamy sauce, alongside more ambitious dishes, some made with game that they hunt themselves. For a pleasant, laid-back alternative, head to Krönle – the options written up on the board are very reasonably priced. Some house-made food items such as greaves lard spread, tripe, spaetzle, sauces and maultaschen can be purchased to take home. Decent guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14025;Cube;Germany;Stuttgart;Kleiner Schlossplatz 1, Stuttgart, 70173, Germany;48.7782165;9.1776887;51;true;false;International, Modern Cuisine;The absolutely fabulous location is as much of a draw as the glass architecture, the design and the ambitious international cuisine. There is a simpler lunch menu, too. The o.T. Bar serves breakfast, cake and after-work drinks. The lovely terrace is positioned on Schlossplatz, a square in front of the art museum. Tip for theatre- and concert-goers: Ask about their "late-night" dining slot.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14026;Habbel's;Germany;Sprockhövel;Gevelsberger Straße 127, Sprockhövel, 45549, Germany;51.3216969;7.2918817;62;false;true;International, Farm to table;Habbel’s offers a fine-dining experience beyond compare. International dishes such as tuna carpaccio coated in wasabi-sesame seeds and saddle of lamb in thyme foam with grilled vegetables feature on the menu, while the wine list offers around 1, 000 wines and spirits from the Habbel in-house distillery, including a 1977-vintage whisky!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14027;Schweizers Restaurant;Germany;Stuttgart;Olgastraße 133 B, Stuttgart, 70180, Germany;48.7656452;9.1771577;94;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Originally opened in 1903 as Schweizer Hof, this restaurant is housed in a painstakingly restored listed building. In the aesthetically pleasing Jugendstil setting of this neighbourhood restaurant, the atmosphere is welcoming, which is in no small part down to the charming service team. Savour the five- to seven-course set menu, which also comes in a vegetarian version. The kitchen serves up ambitious, flavoursome dishes, showcasing precise technique and high-quality ingredients. There is a well-curated wine list, as well as pairings by the glass. The quiet shady courtyard terrace is delightful in summer.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14028;Zur Sonne;Germany;Sankt Peter;Zähringerstraße 2, Sankt Peter, 79271, Germany;48.0157533;8.0319312;35;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Hanspeter Rombach attaches great importance to organic ingredients in his inviting, friendly restaurant. The cuisine is regional and classical: on the menu, for example, local venison ragout in Spätburgunder sauce or filet of organic salmon and wild gambas in pumpkin juice sauce. There are also cosy guestrooms and a pretty sauna area.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14029;Bistro;Germany;Pulheim;Hahnenstraße, Pulheim, 50259, Germany;51.0362139;6.7865947;16;true;true;Farm to table;The bistro at the exclusive Gut Lärchenhof golf club on the outskirts of Cologne offers a somewhat simpler alternative to the eponymous fine dining restaurant, but you are just as assured of flavour and freshness – at both lunch and dinner. They serve dishes ranging from Currywurst to Königsberger Klopse (meatballs) and caviar. Needless to say, the terrace overlooking the green is delightful!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14030;Ganter Restaurant Mohren;Germany;Reichenau Insel;Pirminstraße 141, Reichenau Insel, 78479, Germany;47.696495;9.0630725;70;false;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Whether you opt for a cosy-rustic or a chic-modern interior, the food on offer here is fresh and regional with international influences. Try the char with pearl barley, herbs, almonds and madras curry spices.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14031;Heim's Restaurant;Germany;Reil an der Mosel;Moselstraße 27, Reil an der Mosel, 56861, Germany;50.0209389;7.1181193;67;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;The food served in this 300-year-old restaurant is honest, fresh and full of flavour. Classic and regional cuisine is served throughout the day (kitchen opening hours: 12-8.30pm), taking the form of dishes such as cod à la grenobloise with spinach and mashed potatoes or "Original Wiener Schnitzel" with fried potatoes, salad and cranberries. You will be able to find just the right Moselle wine to accompany your meal. Service comes courtesy of a friendly and proficient team, the atmosphere is pleasant, and in summer, the wonderful terrace with a view of the vineyards and Moselle beckons. The Reiler Hof hotel has lovely guestrooms.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14032;Wilde Triebe;Germany;Osnabrück;Am Sutthauser Bahnhof 5, Osnabrück, 49082, Germany;52.2321932;8.0210815;47;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Set in refurbished former railway buildings dating back over 150 years, Wilde Triebe offers a minimalist, imaginative and fashionable mix of art and food. The flavoursome, seasonal, regional fare is served in an upmarket brick, concrete, steel and wood interior on the restaurant’s own tableware. Great garden.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14033;Schloss Restaurant Venus;Germany;Nordkirchen;Schloss 1, Nordkirchen, 59394, Germany;51.7347001;7.5330703;61;true;true;International;Set in the "Versailles of Westphalia", this classic, distinguished restaurant has vaulted ceilings and numerous paintings by owner Franz L Lauter, an avid painter. A seasonal set menu is available in the evening (from 5pm). At lunchtime on Thursday to Saturday, there are set menus. Tip: Either before or after dinner, why not take a walk around the castle and park?;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park;[]
14034;ZweiSinn Meiers | Bistro;Germany;Nuremberg;Äußere Sulzbacher Straße 118, Nuremberg, 90491, Germany;49.4643067;11.1183197;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;If you are looking for a really nice bistro in Nuremberg, this is the place! A pleasant, cultivated atmosphere, friendly service and good food await you here. At lunchtime, the reasonably priced daily special is always in demand. The fine dining restaurant located to the rear is very popular.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14035;Imperial by Alexander Herrmann;Germany;Nuremberg;Königstraße 70, Nuremberg, 90402, Germany;49.4484745;11.0800647;94;true;false;International, Sharing;The location that houses this restaurant is interesting in the way it blends the architectural details of the old building, such as high ceilings and large arched windows, into the modern, chic-meets-urban look. In this stylish yet relaxed setting, diners are treated to warm hospitality and can watch Michael Seitz at work in the open kitchen, as he cooks up international dishes with a Franconian twist. For groups of two or more people, the sharing menus "Celebration Mood" and "Glamour Mood" are highly recommended. "Dinner Mood" is a set menu comprising four or six courses, which you compile yourself. Tip: The "OpenHausBrunch" takes place on certain Sundays, and there are other regular events.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14036;Atelier Gourmet;Germany;Munich;Rablstraße 37, Munich, 81667, Germany;48.1272571;11.5926659;49;false;false;Classic French;Small, intimate, lively and popular, Atelier Gourmet is quite simply a great little restaurant. The food is fresh, delicious and good value for money thanks to chef Bousquet. It is served in a casual, friendly atmosphere with efficient service and good wine recommendations from the female owner. Try the capon and duck crépinette.;Terrace;[]
14037;Waldrestaurant Maxlmühle;Germany;Valley;Maxlmühle, Valley, 83626, Germany;47.8783769;11.7839448;78;true;false;Country cooking;If you like trout, you can eat them home-smoked here at Maxlmühle alongside home-made brawn and pastry bakes or perhaps a delicious dish of breaded veal sweetbread sausage or braised shoulder of venison. The restaurant lies in a secluded location at the end of a street on the water, so the beer garden is also a particular favourite.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14038;Rindenmühle;Germany;Villingen-Schwenningen;Am Kneippbad 9, Villingen-Schwenningen, 78052, Germany;48.0676921;8.435997;48;false;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Take a seat in the elegant yet cosy, country-style interior – or, in summer, out on the beautiful garden terrace – and choose from a seasonal menu. Vegetarians are also catered for. For overnight guests there are cosy contemporary guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14040;Die Traube;Germany;Vallendar;Rathausplatz 12, Vallendar, 56179, Germany;50.4009755;7.6161389;95;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This gorgeous half-timbered house dating back to 1647 boasts a cosy interior with banquette seats and ambitious seasonal Mediterranean cuisine made from excellent ingredients. The terrace in front of the old barn with its glockenspiel clock is also very appealing. Tip: There is a public car park just around the corner.;Terrace;[]
14041;Landgasthof Backers;Germany;Twist;Kirchstraße 25, Twist, 49767, Germany;52.6376948;7.0612283;90;true;false;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;The Backers family business has a long tradition to its name, stretching back to 1843. Today, the sixth and seventh generations are running the show with great dedication. The fresh and flavoursome food draws on the region and the seasons, and ingredients are sourced locally wherever possible, including the venison and Diepholz geese. The restaurant is a long-standing member of the Slow Food community. There are also a few comfortable guestrooms. Try the "Backers zum Kennenlernen" deal: four-course regional set menu with drinks, plus overnight accommodation.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14042;Gasthof Hirsch;Germany;Schramberg;Hauptstraße 11, Schramberg, 78144, Germany;48.2266547;8.3848739;98;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Set in the centre of this Black Forest village, this attractive restaurant dating back to 1748 is popular for its robust cuisine with classic foundations and plenty of flavour – the sauces are also fantastic! This is all testament to the skill of owner Thomas Zimmermann, who uses select ingredients in his dishes. The atmosphere, too, is just right, thanks to the lovely decor and the exceedingly friendly, attentive hostess. Tip: There are also some individually designed, upscale guestrooms for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
14043;Gasthaus Cervus;Germany;Plochingen;Bergstraße 1, Plochingen, 73207, Germany;48.7118464;9.4150693;64;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Centrally located, just a stone's throw from the train station, this lovely inn has also proved to be a hit with locals. A simple and fuss-free setting in which to enjoy the decidedly fresh and tasty food prepared in the open kitchen. In addition to more ambitious fare, classics such as schnitzel or roast beef also go down well with diners. Simpler and shorter lunchtime menu. Charming inner courtyard.;Terrace;[]
14044;Domschenke;Germany;Rietberg;Lippstädter Straße 1, Rietberg, 33397, Germany;51.7570759;8.3899232;58;true;false;Country cooking, International;This family-run restaurant is now in its third generation. Whether you sit in the rustic-style dining area with its regulars' table or in the pleasant conservatory, you are assured of friendly service. The menu features home-style, regional and more sophisticated dishes. Order à la carte or opt for one of the daily specials on the blackboard. In summer, make a beeline for the outdoor seating area, which is shaded by old trees.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14045;Landhaus Drei Raben;Germany;Rees am Rhein;Reeserward 5, Rees am Rhein, 46459, Germany;51.7706551;6.3492504;53;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;The Koep family has been synonymous with excellent cuisine since 1995… and you can expect just that when you come to eat here on this property on the 18C Landgut Jaquetrois. This former agricultural estate is planted with beautiful old trees. The restaurant has a cosy dining area (warming fireplace in winter) and a fabulous terrace with views over the Mahnensee – especially charming at sunset! The food is international, regional and seasonal. Tip: Coffee and cake are served on Sundays.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14046;Pades Restaurant;Germany;Verden (Aller);Grüne Straße 15, Verden (Aller), 27283, Germany;52.9169388;9.2299413;69;false;false;Country cooking, International;Wolfgang Pade offers a constantly changing menu, which is based on the availability of produce and relies on regional producers. Please note that there are only two service times: 5.45pm and 8.15pm – so make your reservation in good time! The garden terrace behind the pretty patrician house is magnificent.;Terrace;[]
14047;Die Achkarrer Krone;Germany;Vogtsburg im Kaiserstuhl;Schlossbergstraße 15, Vogtsburg im Kaiserstuhl, 79235, Germany;48.0683036;7.6254105;68;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;The culinary tradition at Zur Krone dates back to 1561. Today you can look forward to a plate of calf’s kidney, tripe or oxtail stew, and in summer, a delicious sausage salad. The Baden cuisine and wines can be enjoyed in the cosy dining room or on the terrace. Comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14048;BECKER'S Weinhaus;Germany;Trier;Olewiger Straße 206, Trier, 54295, Germany;49.7421208;6.6678823;43;false;true;Classic Cuisine, International;The original building, which houses the wine bar, stands in contrast to the modern new hotel building. The abundance of pale wood makes it nice and cosy. Choose between a set menu, classic favourites and seasonal à la carte dishes. Pretty terrace.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14049;La Maison Eric;Germany;Sulzburg;Im Brühl 7, Sulzburg, 79295, Germany;47.8406013;7.7060857;42;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This absolute gem of an old half-timbered house is somewhat tucked away in a side street. The interior is tastefully decorated, while outside a gorgeous terrace gives onto the wonderful garden. A set menu of classic dishes is served at lunchtime from Thursday to Sunday.;Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14050;Nannina;Germany;Stuttgart;Gaishämmerstraße 14, Stuttgart, 70186, Germany;48.7783415;9.2083252;96;true;false;Italian;In her tiny restaurant, host Giovanna Di Tommaso (known as Nannina) devotes herself tirelessly to her passion: Italian cuisine. Prepared with fresh high-quality ingredients, her dishes are ambitious and packed with flavour. As well as an extensive à la carte menu, there are three different set menus – one for two or more people and another for four. Delightful terrace to the rear of the building. Practical: The restaurant has its own car park.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14051;Hugenhof;Germany;Simonswald;Am Neuenberg 14, Simonswald, 79263, Germany;48.0970997;8.0663323;49;true;true;International;Inside Hugenhof is every bit as attractive as its exterior suggests with its lovely high ceilings, cosy old beams and a roaring open fire in winter. Every evening brings a different 4-course menu, which chef Klaus Ditz will announce at your table. This is accompanied by expert wine selections from his fellow chef and sommelier. The rooms are simple but smart.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
14052;Genießer Wirtshaus;Germany;Simmerath;Hövel 15, Simmerath, 52152, Germany;50.6157353;6.3803964;31;false;false;Country cooking;This historical half-timbered house in the middle of the town is an idyllic address. Regional dishes are served in its cosy ambience. Pretty, individually styled rooms are available. There is a garden with fruit trees behind the house.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14053;mundart Restaurant;Germany;Saulheim;Weedengasse 8, Saulheim, 55291, Germany;49.8758822;8.1504159;25;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Swabian-born Markus Hebestreit’s restaurant has an attractive, modern, country-style decor and charming interior courtyard. It is located in a pretty, old village house in this little wine-growing town. The fresh and tasty food includes dishes such as braised ox cheeks and tuna fish carpaccio.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14054;Hofgut Ruppertsberg;Germany;Ruppertsberg;Obergasse 2, Ruppertsberg, 67152, Germany;49.401599;8.1914336;74;true;true;Country cooking, French;This estate on the outskirts of town is steeped in history. One of the cornerstones of the Bürklin-Wolf winery, it is now also a charming restaurant with a wonderful courtyard. The cuisine is French, regional and seasonal, with a penchant for organic produce. The teahouse can be booked for exclusive celebrations. The farm shop sells delicious food to take home.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14055;Zum Hirschen & Gasthaus beim Stöckeler;Germany;Scheidegg;Kirchstraße 1, Scheidegg, 88175, Germany;47.581608;9.849408;97;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;This family-run restaurant is firmly established in the village and surrounding area. The cosy, rustic dining rooms and pretty terrace in the shadow of the church making an ideal setting for its seasonal, regional cuisine. Overnight guests can look forward to pretty, modern Alpine rooms and a good breakfast – taken on the balcony terrace perhaps?;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14056;Ballebäuschen;Germany;Reichshof;Hasseler Straße 10, Reichshof, 51580, Germany;50.9693252;7.7306981;17;false;false;Classic French;The Allmann family has been running this friendly restaurant for over 30 years, staying true to tradition without standing still. The cuisine is flavoursome, fresh and authentic and ranges from regional to classic, including locally caught game in season. Small lunchtime menu. Pretty terrace to the rear.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14057;Kirschner Stuben;Germany;Rottach-Egern;Seestraße 23, Rottach-Egern, 83700, Germany;47.6945415;11.7673353;21;true;true;Country cooking, Regional European;This warm and welcoming place exudes a charming liveliness. The terrace overlooking the lake is an absolute delight. Complementing the inviting ambiance is a delectable selection of regional cuisine. An appealing array of fresh, flavoursome dishes awaits, ranging from braised veal cheeks to game and fish from Tegernsee. Most of the ingredients are sourced locally. At lunchtime there is a speciality menu. Maier zum Kirschner Hotel proposes pretty guestrooms imbued with Alpine charm.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14058;Juliette;Germany;Potsdam;Jägerstraße 39, Potsdam, 14467, Germany;52.4023765;13.0555473;75;true;true;Classic French;Are you looking for a slice of the French way of life in the middle of Potsdam? In the Holländisches Viertel (Dutch Quarter), you will find this beautifully designed restaurant, which is housed in a charming 17C half-timbered house. The dining space comprises three different levels, where you can enjoy ambitious classic cuisine accompanied by just the right wine, as a discreet soundtrack plays in the background. In addition to the menu, you can also choose a few dishes à la carte. If the weather is nice, would you like an aperitif at one of the small tables on the pavement before your meal?;;[]
14059;MINNECI;Germany;Nuremberg;Zirkelschmiedsgasse 28, Nuremberg, 90402, Germany;49.4481396;11.0709709;44;true;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;The historical character of this town house dating back to 1560 makes it the perfect setting for an Italian restaurant. Here, diners can either opt for a four- to six-course set menu or order à la carte – think flavoursome Mediterranean dishes such as ravioli with wild mushrooms, sage and balsamic vinegar. At lunchtime, there is a smaller, more budget-friendly set menu. Friendly service comes courtesy of charming waitstaff. Delightful terrace in front of the building. For those coming by car: there is a public car park next door.;Terrace;[]
14060;Acetaia;Germany;Munich;Nymphenburger Straße 215, Munich, 80639, Germany;48.1580543;11.5271034;68;false;false;Italian;Serving Italian cuisine in a comfortable Art Nouveau setting, Acetaia takes its name from the aged balsamic vinegar you will find on sale here. Walkers will enjoy a stroll along the Nymphenburger Canal to the palace with its lovely grounds.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14061;Historisches Gasthaus Sanct Peter Restaurant Weinkirche;Germany;Bad Neuenahr-Ahrweiler;Walporzheimer Straße 134, Bad Neuenahr-Ahrweiler, 53474, Germany;50.5306759;7.0780227;57;true;true;International, Classic Cuisine;Having been renovated following the disastrous floods of 2021, this restaurant gives off an impression of classical elegance. A 13C church with a gallery forms the core of the establishment. There are also two other attractive dining spaces (called Alte Lay and Walporzheimer Himmelchen). The delightful terrace to the rear of the building offers a view of the greenery. The menu features dishes with regional, seasonal and international influences. Classics include braised ox cheeks in Ahr valley Burgundy sauce, and turbot in Ahr valley blanc de noir sauce. The selection of Broggsitter wines is impressive, and there is a well-stocked wine shop on site, too. From 2-6pm, you can order from the smaller menu, with options such as the platter of cold meats and cheeses. They also run Hotel Sanct Peter in the town.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14062;Spielweg;Germany;Münstertal;Spielweg 61, Münstertal, 79244, Germany;47.8775192;7.8375246;66;false;false;Asian Influences, Regional Cuisine;First mentioned in records in 1705, the original Spielweg building, managed by the Fuchs family, makes for a wonderfully cosy setting. The charming dining rooms are done out in traditional Black Forest style and the service is extremely friendly and attentive. Diners can expect classic regional cuisine that is ambitious and full of flavour, as in the warm smoked char from the Wutach in a cold potato and leek broth. It also draws on Asian influences, cf. their wild boar dim sum with soy sauce – Asian cuisine is one of the young chef's passions. The lunchtime menu proposes somewhat simpler fare, making this place an ideal stop-off for a light meal during a hike. You can stay overnight in well-kept, individually furnished guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14063;Weinhaus Neuner;Germany;Munich;Herzogspitalstraße 8, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1377386;11.5684504;81;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;With its cross-vaulted ceiling, herringbone parquet and wood panelling, this old restaurant has lost nothing of its traditional charm. The food is just what you would expect from an upmarket Munich inn – try the flaky pastry crust chicken fricassee pie. The Kaiserschmarrn for two is also a firm favourite! Nice wine list with a good selection of champagnes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14064;Huber;Germany;Munich;Newtonstraße 13, Munich, 81679, Germany;48.1496737;11.6100156;97;true;false;Contemporary;Sandra and Michael Huber run their sleek, minimalist-style restaurant In an attractive residential area of Bogenhausen. Here, they serve flavoursome and ambitious contemporary cuisine that makes a pleasingly down-to-earth impression. There is a choice of two set menus (one of which is vegetarian), each comprising four or six courses, with dishes such as spinach with organic egg and Perigord truffle or skrei, beans and 'nduja. The wine list has a few gems in store, with plenty of appealing options for every budget.;Terrace;[]
14065;IU & ON;Germany;Nuremberg;Roritzerstraße 10, Nuremberg, 90419, Germany;49.460352;11.0703224;61;false;false;Thai;This family business in the heart of Nuremberg has been around since 1972! Many regulars keep coming back, having been won over by the aromatic dishes, which include classics like laab and tom yum. Add to that a clean-lined, minimalist-style interior and friendly service. By the way, the restaurant takes its name from the sisters Iu and On who cook here.;Terrace;[]
14066;Schloss Niederweis;Germany;Niederweis;Hauptstraße 9, Niederweis, 54668, Germany;49.8702187;6.4649596;83;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This tasteful restaurant is housed in the converted corn barn of a magnificent Baroque castle dating from 1751. The decor is a fascinating blend of rustic cachet and modern design – the open truss roof is striking and the two historical carriages on the wall are certainly eye-catching! Sample the flavoursome dishes à la carte or as a set menu, washed down by your choice from the terrific wine list that includes rare finds, including by the glass. Charming garden, a banquet hall and a registry office. On a practical note: easy parking.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14067;Christians Restaurant;Germany;Neckargemünd;Neckarstraße 40, Neckargemünd, 69151, Germany;49.3950904;8.7983587;85;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;Run by Sandy and Christian Heß, this is an appealing restaurant – and that goes for the atmosphere as well as the cuisine. The interior is sleek, bright and welcoming, with beautiful arched windows affording a view of the Neckar River. And then there's the terrace overlooking the water – a truly idyllic spot in which to dine in fine weather! The cuisine is contemporary with a Mediterranean touch – opt for a set menu or order à la carte. This lovely space can also be used for private functions.;Great view,Terrace;[]
14068;HerR;Germany;Rothenburg ob der Tauber;Herrngasse 20, Rothenburg ob der Tauber, 91541, Germany;49.376904;10.176474;81;true;false;International, Seasonal Cuisine;Located in the old town, the pretty Hotel herrnschlösschen is home to a delightful little restaurant, whose stylish modern interior design seamlessly incorporates the building's historical architectural features – note the huge wooden beam dating back to 1526! Named "INNOVATIVE KLASSIK By Sascha Bungeroth", the set menu comprises five courses and a few added extras. The chef takes his cue from the seasons, with dishes such as pickled Canadian scallops with beetroot, apple and shiso or raw Taubertal Wagyu beef, marinated and served with horseradish, mustard and smoked eel. The charming waitstaff will recommend the perfect wine to accompany your meal. Fabulous terrace in the baroque garden!;Terrace;[]
14069;Turmstube;Germany;Neunburg vorm Wald;Hofenstetten 55, Neunburg vorm Wald, 92431, Germany;49.3383982;12.2619678;39;false;false;Country cooking, International;In the friendly atmosphere of this elegant space, diners are served delicious and seasonally inspired cuisine that is based on select produce. Rest assured, Wiener schnitzel is also a mainstay of the menu. Tip: Take in the view from the terrace. For those who would like to stay a little longer, Der Birkenhof hotel promises patrons a comfortable stay complete with spa facilities.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14070;Steinheuers Landgasthof Poststuben;Germany;Bad Neuenahr-Ahrweiler;Landskroner Straße 110, Bad Neuenahr-Ahrweiler, 53474, Germany;50.5509501;7.1640392;64;true;true;Country cooking, Classic Cuisine;By no means a lesser version of Steinheuer, this is a restaurant in its own right where everything is cooked fresh. Taking its cue from the seasons, the menu features regional classics and international dishes. The same well-stocked wine list is presented here as in the fine dining restaurant. Dine in the cosy interior, or head out to the delightful leafy terrace. For overnight stays, there are double rooms available in the main building, as well as a comfortable guesthouse.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14071;Brasserie Colette Tim Raue;Germany;Munich;Klenzestraße 72, Munich, 80469, Germany;48.126953;11.5699476;43;true;false;French, Classic Cuisine;Tim Raue has his finger on the pulse with the concept behind this place: you could almost imagine you are in a French brasserie, what with the stylish, cosy and pleasantly informal atmosphere, and the flavoursome food made with good-quality ingredients. The menu changes every three months and along with the à la carte selection, there are always three set menus to choose from: "Colette Classics", the "Tim Raue Menü" and a vegan one.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14074;Alemannenhof;Germany;Hinterzarten;Bruderhalde 21, Hinterzarten, 79856, Germany;47.8927154;8.1391193;59;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This historical Black Forest establishment in an idyllic location is thoroughly inviting. Inside, an attractive upscale dining space exuding bags of regional charm awaits. Affording magnificent views of the lake, the terrace beckons in summer. The menu takes its cue from the seasons and includes dishes such as Black Forest trout fillets with pickled cherry tomatoes, courgettes and parsley mashed potatoes or French corn-fed poularde breast, tender young beans and thyme pasta. There is also a "Gourmetmenü" comprising five or eight courses with wine pairings. Options are more limited at lunchtime. For overnight stays, the boutique hotel of the same name has guestrooms that seamlessly blend modern and traditional elements.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14075;Johanna Berger;Germany;Lübeck;Doktor-Julius-Leber-Straße 69, Lübeck, 23552, Germany;53.867271;10.6921439;47;false;true;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Tucked away in a fine 19C building in the centre of Lübeck, this restaurant has a charming interior with wooden flooring, chandeliers and an elegant feel. The pretty terrace enjoys an appealing location to the rear of the building. On the menu: a modern take on Mediterranean cuisine, available as a surprise menu or à la carte. Nice selection of German and international wines, also available by the glass.;Terrace;[]
14076;Gasthaus Spieker;Germany;Hövelhof;Detmolder Straße 86, Hövelhof, 33161, Germany;51.8500725;8.623596;32;false;false;Country cooking, Mediterranean Cuisine;Gasthaus Spieker serves regional cuisine with a Mediterranean touch including "Spieker’s Tasty Tapas" and ragout of lamb with bulgur wheat, green asparagus and crème fraîche served in its tasteful, beautifully decorated dining rooms. For those who fancy an extra glass of wine there are also a number of well-kept guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14077;Helbigs Gasthaus;Germany;Johannesberg;Hauptstraße 2, Johannesberg, 63867, Germany;50.0292927;9.1377749;41;true;true;Farm to table;Helbigs promises "casual fine dining" in a pleasantly relaxed atmosphere with attentive, friendly and professional service. In the kitchen, top-quality produce and skill are the order of the day with offerings ranging from traditional inn-style dishes to a set gourmet menu, the latter available in the evenings and at Saturday lunchtime only.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14078;Bayerischer Hof;Germany;Heiligenberg;Röhrenbacherstraße 1, Heiligenberg, 88633, Germany;47.8213203;9.3128894;55;true;false;Country cooking, Home Cooking;In this well-kept restaurant run by the Leykauf family, you can expect a relaxed atmosphere and flavoursome, fresh cuisine prepared by the chef-patron, as well as friendly and attentive service overseen by the lady of the house – this is hospitality as it should be! The wine list predominantly features local produce. There are also reasonably priced guestrooms, varying in style from simple to modern.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14079;Stilbruch;Germany;Karlsruhe;Scheffelstraße 58, Karlsruhe, 76135, Germany;49.0067811;8.3817194;98;true;true;Contemporary;This smart restaurant proposes a surprise menu comprising four to seven courses, in which good use is made not only of regional but also international ingredients. Diners are treated to dishes such as Atlantic cod with spinach cream, wild broccoli, king oyster mushrooms, walnuts and a Parmesan beurre blanc. A vegan set menu is also available. The friendly and courteous front-of-house team will also be able to help you choose the perfect bottle of wine. In summer, secure yourself a spot on the cosy terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14080;Schupps;Germany;Deisenhofen;Bahnhofstraße 30, Deisenhofen, 82041, Germany;48.0193883;11.5868062;19;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Regina and Markus Schupp, after whom this restaurant is named, are both professionally trained chefs. Here they rustle up seasonal dishes inspired by the cuisines of France and Germany. Delicious examples include scallops au gratin with green asparagus, Jerusalem artichoke and almond, or venison ragout with cranberries, Brussels sprout leaves and sour cream. Those who wish to savour a more extensive meal can put together their own set menu comprising three to five courses for a fixed price. At lunchtime, the inexpensive daily specials are ideal for a quick meal. This friendly little restaurant also has a terrace for sunny days. Tip: free parking available along the street.;Terrace;[]
14081;VINOTHEK by Geisel;Germany;Munich;Schützenstraße 11, Munich, 80335, Germany;48.1398631;11.5621221;94;true;false;International;Housed in the luxurious EXCELSIOR by Geisel hotel in the centre of Munich, not far from Stachus, Vinothek is a relaxed establishment done out in a cosy rustic style. The high cross-vaulted ceiling certainly has the wow factor, as does the array of decorative wine bottles. As you might expect from the name of this restaurant, delicious dishes that are inspired by the region and the Mediterranean – such as octopus carpaccio with fennel salad, potato, tomato and basil, or glazed veal cheek with truffle sauce, celeriac and mashed potato – are accompanied by a terrific selection of international wines. Comprising around 800 items, the list is dominated by German, French and Austrian labels. Tip: Check out their reasonably priced lunchtime set menu, which includes coffee and water. Cookery courses and "kitchen parties" are also organised.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14083;Limbourg;Germany;Cologne;Limburger Straße 35, Cologne, 50668, Germany;50.9403037;6.9381622;76;true;false;French Contemporary, International;A wonderful addition to the Belgian Quarter's fine dining scene. The atmosphere is pleasantly laid-back and the vibe tasteful, whether you dine in the ground-floor space or at BelEtage. Chef-patron Alen Radic showcases his cosmopolitan cuisine, which draws on French influences and is made with fresh, good-quality ingredients – served as a set menu (vegetarian version available) or à la carte. The slightly shorter set menu served at lunchtime is also popular. The sheltered courtyard terrace is particularly inviting in summer.;Terrace;[]
14084;Magnifico da Umberto;Germany;Heilbronn;Im Zukunftspark 10, Heilbronn, 74076, Germany;49.1545428;9.2083169;84;true;false;Italian;Umberto Scuccia is a well-known figure in Heilbronn. Here on the 12th floor of the WTZ Tower he runs an upmarket, minimalist-style restaurant offering both pleasantly pared-down Italian cuisine with the accent on top-quality produce and a wonderful view of the city.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14085;Tischlein Deck Dich by Lilly;Germany;Siebeldingen;Bismarckstraße 1, Siebeldingen, 76833, Germany;49.2103881;8.0540468;66;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Having worked at Lilly in Neupotz, Stefan Echle (service) and Matthis Nowak (kitchen) have found their new vocation – in the vaulted cellar of the separately run Villa Königsgarten hotel (formerly Diehl winery). A few steps lead down from the courtyard, home to a leafy terrace in summer, to the restaurant. As you make your way to the dining area, you can take a peek into the glass-fronted kitchen to see the chefs creating their modern seasonal set menu, which offers a choice of options for each course. Named after a fairy tale by the Brothers Grimm (The Lying Goat), the restaurant has a modern, elegant interior with a historical touch. Great service comes courtesy of a friendly and well-trained front-of-house team. The idyllic location in a village surrounded by vineyards, at the foothills of the Palatinate Forest, offers endless possibilities for excursions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14086;möbius - das restaurant;Germany;Schwetzingen;Kurfürstenstraße 22, Schwetzingen, 68723, Germany;49.3854144;8.5818304;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;What used to be möbius lebensmittel.punkt, the delicatessen and bistro, has now been reimagined as a chic little restaurant by Tommy R. Möbius and his wife, Elli. In this modern and tastefully designed space, she runs the service with warmth and professionalism. In the evenings, her husband serves up bold and ambitious cuisine based on classical foundations. Simpler menu at lunchtime Tue-Sat (also available to take away). Delicatessen goods can still be bought here to enjoy at home. In addition, there are regular themed dinner menus and cookery courses.;;[]
14087;Tante Fichte;Germany;Berlin;Fichtestraße 31, Berlin, 10967, Germany;52.4908347;13.4132767;43;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Walk across the small terrace and down a few steps to reach this friendly and pleasingly down-to-earth neighbourhood restaurant. The decor embodies a winning combination of rusticity, elegance and modern design. The cuisine marries classic techniques with regional produce and influences from Croatia (where the chef's family has its roots). The set menu is also available in a vegetarian version. Featuring around 650 labels, the wine list is definitely worth a look. Friendly and attentive service.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14088;Jacobs Restaurant;Germany;Hamburg;Elbchaussee 401, Hamburg, 22609, Germany;53.5504952;9.8441853;80;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Accommodated in Hotel Louis C. Jacob, which boasts a prime location, this restaurant serves modern cuisine with classic touches in an elegant setting. Diners can order à la carte or opt for one of the set menus (conventional or vegetarian). Among the standout dishes are the lobster foam soup and the braised ox shoulder. The Vierland duck served in four courses is a classic option for two. Well-curated wine list. The seating out on Lindenterrasse, overlooking the Elbe River, is undoubtedly the highlight in summer.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
14089;1804 Hirschau;Germany;Munich;Gyßlingstraße 15, Munich, 80805, Germany;48.161743;11.602656;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;"Sustainable - seasonal - regional" is the motto of chef Lukas Adebahr and his team. The restaurant is housed in a historical building that enjoys an idyllic location in Munich's Englischer Garten – be sure to factor in a walk before or after dinner. He and his team adhere to the farm-to-table principle, using the finest ingredients sourced from regional producers or grown on site for dishes such as "rooster, green asparagus & morels". The cuisine often draws on imaginatively integrated Bavarian influences. Desserts such as "baba, rhubarb & sour cream" are tempting, too. There are two tasting menus: the omnivore "Vom Hof" and vegetarian "Vom Garten". The stylish interior has an Alpine feel, tastefully incorporating sleek design, wood, glass and attractive decorative details.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14090;20° RESTOBAR;Germany;Düsseldorf;Mutter-Ey-Platz 3, Neubrückstraße, Düsseldorf, 40213, Germany;51.2282122;6.7750735;74;false;true;Spanish Contemporary;This modern, unpretentious restaurant with a terrace, bar and lovely inner courtyard is located in the centre of town. In a pleasantly lively atmosphere, you can enjoy Spanish-Mediterranean cuisine: in addition to fish, meat, rice and potato dishes, you will of course also find tapas, croquetas and the like. In keeping with the Mediterranean concept, the name refers to the average water temperature around the island of Mallorca.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
14091;Oechsle;Germany;Hamburg;Bundesstraße 15, Hamburg, 20146, Germany;53.5650805;9.9803278;84;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Serving flavoursome dishes made from fresh, high-quality ingredients in a pleasant contemporary atmosphere, this restaurant on the corner is a real gem. Its short menu draws on both Mediterranean and classical influences. This place also doubles as a wine bar, so you can look forward to a well-curated wine list. Experienced and charming waitstaff provide great service with a personal touch. In summer, the tables out front, facing the street, are in high demand.;Terrace;[]
14093;Roku - Japanese Dining & Wine;Germany;Düsseldorf;Schwerinstraße 34, Düsseldorf, 40477, Germany;51.2400579;6.7781527;53;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;This is the third restaurant to be opened by Yoshizumi Nagaya in the state capital. The atmosphere is trendy, modern and relaxed and dishes range from sushi and sashimi to tempura and Japanese fish and meat dishes. There is a good, predominantly German wine selection to go with the food.;;[]
14094;KOSTBAR;Germany;Weingarten;Ravensburger Straße 56, Weingarten, 88250, Germany;47.7978485;9.627574;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Following Marco Akuzun's departure, Daniele di Fabio is the new head chef. As well as a good à la carte selection, a five-course set menu is served in the evening (vegetarian version available on request) and there is an attractive "business lunch" formula comprising two or three courses. The mouthwatering options include ricotta gnocchi with summer truffle and Parmesan, or guinea fowl saltimbocca with olive marinara sauce and basil purée. Furthermore, a creative tasting menu can be ordered in the evening. The upscale interior is both stylish and cosy, featuring warm wood and a minimalist design that creates a welcoming atmosphere. Lovely covered terrace with a working water wheel as the standout feature!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14096;Ristorante Engel;Germany;Wittnau;Weinbergstraße 2, Wittnau, 79299, Germany;47.9403052;7.8174627;90;true;false;Italian;With almost 200 years of gastronomic history to its name, this place has been in Italian hands for over 40 years. Following in his parents' footsteps, Franco Iaia now runs this ristorante with his wife Yvonne. With a tiled stove and warm wood, the inviting dining space is vibrant and charming. "La Piazza" is their lovely terrace shaded by mulberry trees. Highlights of the "cucina italiana strettamente classica" include homemade pasta, brasato and osso buco.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14097;Inspektorenhaus;Germany;Brandenburg City;Altstädtischer Markt 9, Brandenburg City, 14770, Germany;52.4137637;12.5538665;59;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, International;In the city centre, opposite the brick-built Gothic town hall, is the Inspektorenhaus, from which the inspector used to keep an eye on the market and the activity it harboured. Nowadays it is a restaurant with a cosy ambience and distinct charm, thanks to old wooden beams and pretty decorations. In summer, you can sit outside in the courtyard garden. Two seasonal set menus are served, one with fish, one with meat. Friendly service.;Terrace;[]
14098;Diekmann;Germany;Berlin;Meinekestraße 7, Berlin, 10719, Germany;52.5012397;13.328717;60;false;false;French, German;In the mood for the charm of a typical bistro setting? At the front, amid decorative wine racks from an old colonial goods shop, is a casual dining area with high tables positioned around a free-standing oyster bar. Alternatively, nab one of the small tables in the charming minimalist-style space at the back of the premises. In the evening, ambitious French and German dishes are served à la carte or as a tasting menu. Lunchtime options are more limited but moderately priced – water, bread and espresso are included. The impressive oyster menu is available at both mealtimes.;Terrace;[]
14099;Sorriso;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Oppenheimer Landstr. 49, Frankfurt on the Main, 60596, Germany;50.0995166;8.6803418;41;false;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;In a smart building occupying a corner plot in the Sachsenhausen district, this tastefully designed restaurant serves modern Mediterranean-inspired cuisine made with top-notch ingredients. There are two set menus, one of which is 100% vegan. The owner has some great wine recommendations up his sleeve. Pleasant terrace for summer.;Terrace;[]
14100;Portun Restaurant;Germany;Munich;Leopoldstraße 150, Munich, 80805, Germany;48.1696865;11.5864118;75;false;true;Contemporary, Fusion;Former co-chef at Les Deux, Gregor Goncharov, is now at the helm of this restaurant in Schwabing's Leopoldstraße. His surprising cuisine is rooted in Alpine-Adriatic culinary tradition, drawing on influences from Istria, Slovenia, Italy and Austria. On the menu, there are intriguing options such as Adriatic lobster served with peas, sweetcorn, tomato consommé and almonds, or Mangalica pork for two. The interior design is modern and stylish, with outdoor seating available in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14101;INDIA CLUB;Germany;Berlin;Behrenstraße 72, Berlin, 10117, Germany;52.5149399;13.3798063;24;false;true;Indian;Truly authentic Indian cuisine is to be found in Berlin! The self-styled "rustic cuisine" from the north of India includes delicious curries as well as original tandoori dishes. Many ingredients are sourced from the restaurant's own organic farm (Gut Vorder Bollhagen) on the Baltic Sea. The elegant restaurant with an interior of dark wood and typical Indian colours and patterns is located not far from the Brandenburg Gate, at the back of the exclusive Hotel Adlon.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14102;Park-Restaurant Vogelherd;Germany;Zerbst;Lindauer Straße 78, Zerbst, 39264, Germany;51.995772;12.086178;78;false;true;Farm to table;Quality restaurant in a former manor house famous for its good seasonal cuisine. You can also dine on the attractive terrace alongside a small pond.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14103;MANUELIS;Germany;Miesbach;Kolpingstraße 2, Miesbach, 83714, Germany;47.7904388;11.8338934;58;false;false;Creative, Regional Cuisine;Very centrally located, this restaurant is really charming with its cosy atmosphere and cordial service. Championing regional and seasonal produce with a deep respect for the ingredients, the chef adheres to the nose-to-tail and leaf-to-root principles. The six- or eight-course set menu culminates in a delightful finale named Eine kleine Schweinerei (house-made Alpine pork specialities). Alternatively, there is a small à la carte selection. The beverage pairings are also intriguing, showcasing a selection of German wines alongside house-made kombuchas, sparkling wines, and beers. Tip: You can also book themed menus on certain dates.;Terrace;[]
14105;sansaro;Germany;Munich;Amalienpassage 89, Munich, 80799, Germany;48.1518557;11.5779699;56;true;false;Japanese;The minimalist Japanese-style interior of the restaurant is inviting, as is the lovely verdant inner courtyard terrace. As well as sushi and sashimi (which you can also order omakase), the menu offers a five-course set menu with drink pairings, dubbed "Journey to Japan", and a small à la carte selection of Japanese dishes. The short explanations on the menu are a nice idea. There is also a terrific selection of sake and Japanese whiskies.;Notable sake list,Terrace;[]
14106;nagare;Germany;Stuttgart;Feuerbacher-Tal-Straße 34, Stuttgart, 70469, Germany;48.8062161;9.1561029;80;false;true;Japanese, Creative;Don't be fooled by the rather unspectacular exterior of this corner-plot building! Once inside, you will be immersed in a Far Eastern-style minimalist setting and have the chance to savour Nakagawa's Japanese creative cuisine, which draws on contemporary and French influences. Choose from set menus and à la carte options – sushi and vegetarian dishes are also present and correct. Only fish of the finest quality makes the cut. Professional service comes courtesy of polite, friendly waitstaff, who will gladly provide sake recommendations.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14107;Zur Schwane;Germany;Metzingen;Bei der Martinskirche 10, Metzingen, 72555, Germany;48.5362892;9.285834;65;true;false;Farm to table, Country cooking;Here, the Swabian Jura theme is writ large. The menu changes with the seasons and puts the emphasis on top-quality ingredients, most of which are sourced from the surrounding area. A huge panorama of the Swabian Jura landscape is the most striking feature of the modern yet cosy dining area – it couldn't be more apt. Tip: Given the restaurant's proximity to OUTLETCITY, keen shoppers might consider an overnight stay in one of the hotel's stylish guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14109;AIMY;Germany;Munich;Brienner Straße 10, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1434321;11.5752212;61;true;false;Thai;Fans of Thai cuisine are in good hands at this restaurant with an attractive decor, where diners can enjoy flavoursome dishes made from high-quality produce – authentic Thai flavours are guaranteed here. Tip: The cocktail menu is also worth a look. There is also a delightful bar at the back of the restaurant. In summer, the seats in the inner courtyard are especially inviting.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14110;Landhotel Donner;Germany;Meschede;Zur Alten Schmiede 4, Meschede, 59872, Germany;51.3044294;8.3030167;85;true;false;Country cooking, International;Here you can enjoy classic regional cuisine – for example the menu features braised wild boar in a juniper jus. The decor is warm and welcoming, the pretty country-style dining rooms boast classy soft furnishings and warm wood. Don't miss the home-made cakes served in the afternoons on the pretty garden terrace. You can also stay overnight in well-kept accommodation.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14112;Bernhardhof;Germany;Andechs;Andechser Straße 32, Andechs, 82346, Germany;47.9715205;11.1846708;37;true;false;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;At the foot of the hill on which Andechs's famous abbey stands, you will find this charming, chic, modern restaurant. The Holzinger family used to run a farm here, but nowadays they welcome diners with warmth and dedication. It is the son who is at the helm, serving up excellent, fresh cuisine that draws on regional and international influences. Incidentally, you can also enjoy a really comfortable overnight stay here, in one of the spacious maisonettes or suites.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14113;Restaurant Max'es;Germany;Langenhagen;Walsroder Straße 39, Langenhagen, 30851, Germany;52.4316826;9.7317676;29;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;A chic bistro vibe, friendly service and good food are the hallmarks of the restaurant of the Hotel Wegner, a family-run business since 1957. The cuisine is modern and takes its cue from the changing seasons. The menu includes dishes such as beef tartare with black garlic, anchovies and caper berries, or cod, beetroot done in two different ways and black salsify. At lunchtime, there is a selection from the evening menu. Tip: Head for the quiet leafy terrace! You can also come for breakfast.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14114;Salt & Silver am Meer;Germany;Sankt Peter-Ording;Zum Böhler Strand, Sankt Peter-Ording, 25826, Germany;54.2692515;8.6505304;41;true;true;Grills, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in an 8m-high building on stilts right by the beach, within spitting distance of the sea – an impressive location in which to enjoy fresh cuisine featuring produce from the region. The tempting menu includes grilled fish and meat, and their must-try signature dish: ceviche. The atmosphere is nice and lively both inside and out on the fabulous terrace. A welcome addition to the two other Salt & Silver restaurants in Hamburg.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14115;von Euch;Germany;Meppen;Kuhstraße 21, Meppen, 49716, Germany;52.6892629;7.2913239;20;false;false;International;Located in the city centre, Hotel von Euch not only offers modern guestrooms, it has now also made a name for itself as a destination for foodies! In the elegant restaurant – or on the gorgeous terrace in summer – owner and head chef Johannes Schute delights diners with delicious cuisine that won't break the bank. Consisting of Livar cloister pork with potato, apple, onion and a wonderful jus, the dish "Himmel & Erde" ("Heaven & Earth") is a perfect example of how to combine superior and more down-to-earth elements to create something that is both refined and intensely flavoursome.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14116;Atelier Tian;Germany;Ravensburg;Veitsburgstraße 2, Ravensburg, 88212, Germany;47.7782279;9.6162588;48;true;true;International, Modern Cuisine;The location in Veitsburg castle is indeed something special. Once you reach the top, not only does a magnificent view of Ravensburg await you, but also Christian Ott's ambitious, flavoursome cuisine. You can put together your own set menu from the dishes on offer – flexibility is the name of the game! You can also look forward to professional and friendly service. Tip: Make your reservation in good time – this location is not only popular with locals.;Car park,Great view;[]
14117;Momo Ramen;Germany;Hamburg;Margaretenstraße 58, Hamburg, 20357, Germany;53.566273;9.9633915;37;false;false;Ramen;Fancy some Japanese ramen? Then look no further! This hip and laid-back spot serves fresh house-made noodles. The aromatic dishes draw on regional ingredients and dispense with any additives. Reduced menu at lunchtime. An amusing detail: the toilets are wallpapered with Japanese newspapers.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14119;Löwengrube;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Konviktstraße 12, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79098, Germany;47.9940801;7.8545331;77;true;true;International, Farm to table;This former wine tavern in the heart of the old town has been given a new lease of life. The traditional character of this historic building has been successfully mixed with modern elements. The food offering takes the form of internationally inspired cuisine made with regional produce. It is a real treat to sit on the sheltered terrace.;Terrace;[]
14120;Lindenhof 1887;Germany;Lunden;Friedrichstraße 39, Lunden, 25774, Germany;54.3298094;9.0240219;96;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;This North German family-run establishment is pretty as a picture! After being welcomed into the attractive inn built in 1887 with a lively local greeting ("moin"), you can expect good, attentive service in a modern and thoroughly chic ambience. Chef Tjark-Peter Maaß cooks tasty dishes of a regional bent. For example, the fried North Sea plaice, fried potatoes, cucumber salad, Tönning shrimps is a tasty and fresh option – one of the classics. There are also some appealing and cosy guestrooms for an overnight stay.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14121;Il Teatro²;Germany;Karlsruhe;Ettlingerstraße 2c, Karlsruhe, 76137, Germany;49.0041057;8.4026047;43;true;true;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Founded in 1984, this family-run establishment located close to the Staatstheater (hence the name) is now run by the second generation, with Daniele di Sario taking the helm several years ago. He delivers classic Italian and French-style cuisine that is in keeping with the zeitgeist: The spaghetti carbonara, turbot with Champagne sauce or lemon dessert ("Kreation von der Zitrone") are shining examples. In keeping with the name of the restaurant, the menu is divided into different sections: Act 1, Intermezzo, Act 2 and Epilogue. Veteran chef Giovanni likes to get in on the action front of house, joining forces with the enthusiastic and attentive service team. In summer, the terrace seating out on the wide pavement is especially appealing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14122;Meilenstein;Germany;Lübeck;Königstraße 5, Lübeck, 23552, Germany;53.8707261;10.689658;47;true;true;Contemporary;A listed building steeped in history is the attractive location that houses this chic restaurant with its bar and lovely terrace. Here, they propose a set menu that you can put together yourself and that draws on modern influences. The front-of-house team is friendly and accomplished. There is also an appealing selection of cocktails at this stylish venue with a variety of spaces you can hire for private events.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14123;bellasLOKAL;Germany;Bad Soden am Taunus;Langstraße 15, Bad Soden am Taunus, 65812, Germany;50.1576971;8.4708219;56;true;true;Creative, Farm to table;Located in a narrow village lane in Altenhain, Isabelle Pering's restaurant has a pleasantly bright interior done out in a tasteful, minimalist style. With her menu, which you can also choose vegetarian, the chef shows her knack for creating harmonious flavour combinations – this is where her experience gained at top-flight establishments shines through. Most of the ingredients and wines are from the region and certified organic. Delightful terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14124;Krone;Germany;Bempflingen;Brunnenweg 40, Bempflingen, 72658, Germany;48.5766029;9.2725229;22;false;false;Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine;This long-standing family business is run with real dedication. No compromises are made when it comes to the quality of the produce, and the dishes taste great! No wonder the restaurant is widely known and popular – this also means it is better to make a reservation. Tip: the very reasonably priced lunch menu.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14125;Forellenhof;Germany;Baiersbronn;Schliffkopfstraße 64, Baiersbronn, 72270, Germany;48.5244129;8.2559237;61;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;The diversity of the Bareiss culinary empire knows no bounds! The historic and idyllically located Forellenhof has been transformed into a charming restaurant open to all-comers from 11. 30am-5. 30pm. The emphasis here is on freshwater fish – from their own fish farm – but they also serve snacks. Tip: you can buy fresh fish in the Forellenlädle (9am-noon).;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14126;Zauberberg;Germany;Munich;Hedwigstr. 14, Munich, 80636, Germany;48.1531028;11.5408064;74;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;"Zauberberg" translates as magic mountain, and the name is fitting for a number of reasons. For one, dedicated host Claudia Kimbacher, who adds a pleasantly personal touch to the service with her remarkably warm manner and is also happy to assist you in choosing your wines. Then there is Sven Gerlach's cuisine, which comes in the form of a surprise menu comprising five to six modern and creative courses. For example, he combines crispy pork neck with a Korean spicy glaze and kale kimchi or fresh, aromatic mushrooms with a creamy sauce seasoned with Shoyu soy sauce as well as Taleggio cheese dumplings. Vegetarian options are available on request. This friendly restaurant with elegant decor also has a terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14127;Madame Ngo - Une Brasserie Hanoi;Germany;Berlin;Kantstraße 30, Berlin, 10623, Germany;52.5062238;13.31818;23;false;true;South East Asian, Vietnamese;It is definitely worth waiting for one of the coveted tables here! This charmingly informal restaurant is very popular due to its simple but excellent Vietnamese cuisine, which is also inexpensive. There is an enticing aroma from the bubbling pots in the open kitchen – a large bowl of authentic “pho” (noodle soup) is practically a must!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14129;Stubersheimer Hof;Germany;Amtstetten;Bräunisheimer Straße 1, Amtstetten, 73340, Germany;48.5949476;9.9176569;23;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;The tasteful decor of this lovingly restored old farmhouse exudes rural charm. In the pleasant dining area with its attractive wooden flooring, diners are treated to a friendly welcome and delicious regional fare prepared by the junior chef. In summer, there's no better place to dine than in the charming courtyard. And if you're looking for a place to stay overnight, the family-run business also has lovely guestrooms available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14131;Johanniter-Kreuz;Germany;Überlingen;Johanniterweg 11, Überlingen, 88662, Germany;47.7797116;9.1870066;75;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;This former farmhouse, which is over 350 years old, has been turned into the lovely Johanniter-Kreuz Romantik Hotel, complete with a tasteful, rustic-style restaurant in what was once the stable. Old beams and a central fireplace lend the space a cosy atmosphere. The food is rooted in classical culinary tradition, with regional influences and close ties to the seasons. Vegetarians are also catered for, and there is a decent wine selection.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14132;959;Germany;Heidelberg;Friedrich-Ebert-Anlage 2, Heidelberg, 69117, Germany;49.4070942;8.6948087;18;false;true;Contemporary, Classic Cuisine;The Stadtgarten Pavilion (1936) has been given a new lease of life with a trendy-chic feel, plus a good dose of glamour! Food is served throughout the day: a modern, ingredient-led take on classic cuisine à la carte at both lunch and dinnertime (somewhat reduced menu at lunchtime). There are also classics such as Wiener schnitzel and beef goulash, plus a small selection of pizzas. In addition, in the evening, a set menu made up of dishes from the à la carte selection is available. Short snack menu served 3-5pm. Lovely terrace overlooking a small park. Very good, wide-ranging wine list. Pino's Bar has a classic vibe and an outdoor lounge.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14133;Dae Mon;Germany;Berlin;Monbijouplatz 11, Berlin, 10178, Germany;52.5230337;13.3994235;36;false;true;Fusion, Asian Influences;This chic and rather stylish restaurant is an interesting option. The food is dubbed "open-minded cuisine": modern dishes that combine the techniques and flavours of Japanese and Korean cuisine in a variety of ways – for example, street food influences make their presence felt. There is also a creative vegetarian version of the set menu. Tip: As an alternative to wine, they propose a beautifully curated cold Asian tea pairing – a real treat for all those who like to go alcohol-free.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14134;Scarpati;Germany;Wuppertal;Scheffelstraße 41, Wuppertal, 42327, Germany;51.2389479;7.0854661;62;true;true;Italian;The Scarpati family have been running this inviting restaurant since 1982. In this beautifully kept Art Nouveau villa, you take a seat at your table in the classically elegant interior and let the attentive waitstaff serve you Italian cuisine. The garden terrace is also really lovely (and sheltered by an awning). Tip: On Wednesdays, come and try the reasonably priced set menu – the "Amuse Bouche Menü".;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14135;Freilinger Wirt;Germany;Mitterskirchen;Hofmarkstraße 5, Mitterskirchen, 84335, Germany;48.3489847;12.7329689;74;true;true;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This traditional Bavarian inn has been around since 1870 and today it boasts a lovely blend of clean, modern design and warm wood. The patron and chef is a master butcher and his experience working at renowned restaurants can be seen in his good seasonal dishes. The large terrace is popular.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14136;Küppersmühle Restaurant;Germany;Duisburg;Philosophenweg 49, Duisburg, 47051, Germany;51.4409975;6.7736277;40;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;A fantastic location with an old industrial atmosphere, view of the inner harbour, and terrace right next to the water. This urban-style interior is the backdrop for modern cuisine with classic and international influences, served as fresh and precisely cooked dishes. Slightly simpler menu at lunchtime. Küppersmühle Museum of Modern Art next door is worth a visit.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14137;Broeding;Germany;Munich;Schulstraße 9, Munich, 80636, Germany;48.151496;11.5344111;50;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This lively restaurant is an institution in Neuhausen. In an outwardly unassuming building on a residential street, diners can look forward to a five- or six-course set menu comprising flavourful pared-down dishes such as lake trout with oxheart tomato and porcini mushrooms. The top-quality ingredients (mostly organic or Demeter produce) are sourced in the Alpine and pre-Alpine regions. The pleasingly laid- back atmosphere is in no small part down to the friendly, attentive and unpretentious service, which also includes expert advice when it comes to the fabulous wine list (with a focus on Austrian wine-growing regions). In summer, the secluded inner courtyard terrace beckons. Tip: Try out the shorter three-course early evening menu (until 7.30pm).;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14138;Landhaus Mönchenwerth;Germany;Meerbusch;Niederlöricker Straße 56, Meerbusch, 40667, Germany;51.2564389;6.7202129;51;false;true;Classic Cuisine, International;Good products form the basis of the ambitious contemporary cuisine of Guy de Vries, who also includes elements of molecular gastronomy. Wonderful Rhine terrace and beer garden.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14139;Zur Waage M.E.B.;Germany;Leer;Neue Straße 1, Leer, 26789, Germany;53.2263202;7.4508648;77;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Farm to table;This long-established restaurant enjoys a charming location in the town centre, directly on the Leda River – in summer, the lovely terrace with a view of the museum harbour beckons! Inside, you can expect all the trappings of a traditional inn with the odd rustic maritime touch. Mario E. Brüggemann (who completed his apprenticeship as a chef here) proposes high-quality cuisine at reasonable prices with a strong focus on sustainability. Regional produce goes into dishes such as young herring tartare, plum, tomato – tasty, fresh and pleasingly straightforward! The simpler lunch menu includes a few of the evening options.;Terrace;[]
14140;Berchtesgadener Esszimmer;Germany;Berchtesgaden;Nonntal 7, Berchtesgaden, 83471, Germany;47.6358238;13.0048551;18;false;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;This long-established inn run by Maximilian and Roxana Kühbeck with great dedication and a commitment to sustainability has bags of charm and atmosphere. Made with select ingredients sourced from the local area, the food is flavoursome and ambitious. There are two set menus, one of which is vegetarian, plus an à la carte selection. In addition to the cosy little dining space with its vaulted ceiling, there are two very popular "kitchen tables" for those who wish to see the chefs at work.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14141;Le comptoir 17;Germany;Mannheim;Lameystraße 17, Mannheim, 68165, Germany;49.486836;8.4789656;100;true;true;French, Farm to table;The addition of "Bistrot Parisien" to the name tells diners exactly what to expect. If you like a friendly, down-to-earth bistro atmosphere and classic French cuisine, then this is the place for you! Here, the emphasis is on the excellent ingredients that are used to make their house specialities such as blood sausage, beef tartare, mussels or fish soup. As well as the regular menu, there are specials written up on the blackboard.;Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14143;Weinstube Baldreit;Germany;Baden-Baden;Küferstraße 3, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7625203;8.2397638;55;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Home Cooking;This lovely wine tavern may be somewhat hidden away in its pleasantly quiet location, but it is well worth seeking out – especially in summer, when the charming secluded courtyard terrace comes into its own. Along with a relaxed atmosphere with rustic charm and friendly service, diners can look forward to an array of different flammkuchen, speciality mussel dishes and regional classics. The seasonal specials of the day are written up on a wooden board or presented verbally. The restaurant has plenty of regulars and is always busy, so it's advisable to make a reservation!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14144;Ebanat;Germany;Sinzheim;Ebenunger Straße 23, Sinzheim, 76547, Germany;48.7460797;8.1806533;80;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, International;Surrounded by vineyards, this modern restaurant boasts a beautiful location on the premises of Weingut Kopp, a Demeter winery complete with its own wine shop. As you savour classic seasonal cuisine that draws on international influences, you can take in the view of the vines and the plain, to which the name makes reference (the village of Ebenung used to be called "Ebanat", a derivation of the Old High German word for "plain"). Made with locally sourced ingredients wherever possible, the excellent food can be accompanied by the restaurant's own wines. Friendly and professional service.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14145;Goldene Sonne;Germany;Neuenstein;Vorstadt 2, Neuenstein, 74632, Germany;49.2053959;9.5828192;34;false;true;Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;A quaint historical half-timbered building provides the setting where Heiner Bohnet and Constanza Piccolo welcome diners into their inviting dining space, which has retained its traditional charm. The pair approach their work with tremendous dedication and enthusiasm – she provides friendly and attentive service, and he creates a new vegetable-forward set menu every week, always guided by what is in season. Ingredients are sourced almost entirely from the local area (except for the sustainably line-caught fish from the coast of Brittany). The chef-patron is a member of a farming collective and grows his own vegetables. A great deal of fermenting, pickling and preserving is done in-house, plus they bake their own bread. Tip: They offer three lovely double rooms for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
14147;Kurpfalz Weinstuben;Germany;Berlin;Wilmersdorfer Straße 93, Berlin, 10629, Germany;52.5009112;13.3080932;36;false;true;Regional Cuisine;A typical Palatinate wine tavern in the middle of Berlin? At Adenauerplatz near Ku'damm, you will find this traditional bar tucked away in a courtyard. In cosy, rustic rooms you can enjoy home-style cooking and regional classics, along with 50 wines served by the glass and 800 on the wine list. Short menu of the day at lunchtime.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14148;Landgang;Germany;Koblenz;An der Fähre 3, Koblenz, 56072, Germany;50.3582869;7.5599647;39;false;false;French, Mediterranean Cuisine;The modern restaurant on the first floor of the Hotel Fährhaus is already a magnet for diners on account of its wonderful location. Take in the view of the Moselle as you tuck into French-Mediterranean cuisine with regional influences. There is also a vinotheque boasting very good wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14149;Franziska;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Hainer Weg 72, Frankfurt on the Main, 60599, Germany;50.0973481;8.6937021;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;It takes 40 seconds in the lift up to the top of the Henninger Turm. As well as its magnificent views over the Frankfurt skyline, this restaurant proposes "Progressive German Vintage Cuisine". The name is a tribute to the great-aunt of the Mook Group founder. Cocktails in the Barrel Bar. Terrace one floor down. Online bookings only.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14150;Krone;Germany;Höchst im Odenwald;Rondellstraße 20, Höchst im Odenwald, 64739, Germany;49.8108278;8.9810734;69;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;You will feel at home here for a number of reasons. Not only can you enjoy the modern, classic and seasonal cuisine showcasing local produce, but there is also the friendly, attentive service that comes courtesy of the owner and her team, who also know their way around the wine list. The elegantly pared-down interior is equally inviting, not to mention the beautiful garden with shaded seating that draws diners in summer. Well-kept guestrooms are available should you wish to stay the night.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14151;Genießer Stube - Daniel Raub;Germany;Friedland;Weghausstraße 20, Friedland, 37133, Germany;51.4189041;9.9186842;83;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Daniel Raub represents the third generation at the helm of this family-run business. At Genießer Stube, one of the restaurants of Romantik Hotel Landhaus Biewald, he serves up classic French-based cuisine with a seasonal focus, eschewing any frills and putting his ingredients centre stage. In the evening there is the set menu ("Genießer Menü") that comes in four, six or eight courses. You can also opt for fine wine pairings. The wine list is also worth a look. In winter, food is served in the cosy dining room with its old wooden beamed ceiling. In summer, you can also dine in the conservatory or on the terrace. Professional service is provided by a charming front-of-house team. The second restaurant, Zur Tränke, is housed in the newly constructed modern hotel building. In addition to comfortable accommodation, overnight guests can look forward to a fantastic breakfast. Tip: Museum Friedland is just round the corner.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14152;Drexlers;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;Rosastraße 9, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79098, Germany;47.9980793;7.8463693;51;true;true;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Since 2007, this bright, modern restaurant right next to Colombipark has been something of an institution in Freiburg. Service is friendly and adept and the atmosphere warm and welcoming. Showcasing regional produce and sustainable practices, the ambitious seasonally inspired cuisine draws on French and Italian influences. The four- to six-course set menu comes in a "classic" or vegetarian version. On Mondays and Thursdays you can also order individual courses à la carte. Great selection of reasonably priced wines – courtesy of their own wine shop. Tip for motorists: Rotteck underground car park is within walking distance.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14153;Rittersturz;Germany;Veldenz;Veldenzer Hammer 1a, Veldenz, 54472, Germany;49.8857659;7.0291963;91;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This place has no shortage of charm: a lovely, cosy interior, friendly and attentive service and an idyllic location in the countryside! It's especially pleasant to take your meal on the terrace, from where you can enjoy the view of the castle ruins and the rocky Rittersturz Felsen. The classic seasonal cuisine – in set menu form or à la carte – is made with wild herbs, fruit, vegetables etc sourced from the surrounding area.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14154;Steinbuck Stube;Germany;Vogtsburg im Kaiserstuhl;Talstraße 2, Vogtsburg im Kaiserstuhl, 79235, Germany;48.1047845;7.6282282;29;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;In the centre of town is this pretty, lavishly restored 400-year-old house. You can sit in the cosy, tastefully decorated restaurant, in the modern wine bar or on the terrace that adjoins the two. There, you will be served seasonal and Mediterranean-influenced classic dishes, accompanied exclusively by regional wines. There are also guestrooms for a pleasant overnight stay.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14155;Uwe & Uli - Zuhause bei uns;Germany;Usingen im Taunus;Marktplatz 21, Usingen im Taunus, 61250, Germany;50.3358603;8.5334016;98;true;true;International, Classic Cuisine;A listed building standing directly on the market square, the 17C Liefrink House has an appealing exterior. Behind the pretty half-timbered façade is a charming, modern restaurant (formerly “essWebers - Küche am Markt” but now with a new name) which serves seasonal, international cuisine. The chef's set menu is complemented by a number of à-la-carte options.;Terrace;[]
14156;Seehalde;Germany;Uhldingen-Mühlhofen;Birnau-Maurach 1, Uhldingen-Mühlhofen, 88690, Germany;47.7412714;9.2228172;76;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Run by the Gruler brothers, this restaurant boasts a stunning lakeside location – tables on the terrace are much coveted in summer! The fresh and ambitious cuisine is also a major draw. The menu takes its cue from the region and the seasons with a classic bent. Fish from Lake Constance is also served and is even the focus of a three- or four-course set menu for two people. There is also a set menu based on regional classics. Alternatively, take your pick from the appealing à la carte selection. The well-curated wine list includes some gems, too. Well-drilled front-of house team. Tip: Take some homemade bouillabaisse in a jar with you to enjoy at home. There are well-kept guestrooms as well - most of them look out to the lake.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14157;Zur Tanne;Germany;Tunau;Alter Weg 4, Tunau, 79677, Germany;47.7853266;7.9223701;78;true;true;Country cooking;Housed in a charming old farmhouse, this restaurant is inviting from the outside, and the interior is rustic-looking and cosy. In this setting, top-notch ingredients that take their cue from the region and the seasons go into flavoursome dishes. For overnight stays, there are well-kept guestrooms – with no TV, but you'd rather enjoy the peace and quiet here anyway!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14158;Meister Lampe;Germany;Stuttgart;Solitudestraße 261, Stuttgart, 70499, Germany;48.8163322;9.1142101;73;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;It's a real pleasure to eat here, and there's a good reason for that: chef-patron Daniel Stübler clearly puts his heart and soul into running his cosy little restaurant. He cooks up excellent regional and international dishes, and also does the serving himself – not only is he highly accomplished at what he does, he is also an extremely cordial host and single-handedly creates a fantastic atmosphere! The carefully curated wine list is also remarkable, featuring wines from Baden-Württemberg, Baden and the Palatinate only.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14159;La Bouche et El Pato;Germany;Schwerin;Buschstraße 9, Schwerin, 19053, Germany;53.628613;11.413325;38;true;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;This bistro with a friendly, cosy atmosphere is located in the middle of the city – the cathedral is just a stone's throw away. La Bouche is on the ground floor and El Pato is on the first floor, but diners enjoy the same international and Mediterranean dishes and friendly service on both levels. Lovely terrace in the pedestrian zone.;Terrace;[]
14160;Kugelmühle;Germany;Schweinfurt;Georg-Schäfer-Straße 30, Schweinfurt, 97421, Germany;50.0393239;10.2166961;80;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;Max Matreux has been at the helm of this minimalist-style restaurant in the side wing of a factory since 2001. He is a strong advocate for sustainability, as is apparent in his classic cuisine, which features seasonal and regional ingredients. A three- to five-course set menu is proposed, as well as an à la carte selection. Tip: Ask about the "Bib Gourmand" set menu. Friendly and well-trained waitstaff.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
14161;Die Alte Brauerei;Germany;Sankt Ingbert;Kaiserstraße 101, Sankt Ingbert, 66386, Germany;49.2812104;7.1185216;61;true;true;French, European Contemporary;Florian Dauphin, son of friendly owners Eric and Isabelle Dauphin, is now at the helm of this restaurant, where you can look forward to cordial service. Diners are seated in a cosy setting to enjoy seasonal dishes that draw on French tradition . You can order à la carte or opt for a set menu. During the week, they propose a reasonably priced "Business Menü" at lunchtime. Access to the restaurant in the former brewery is via the inner courtyard. You also have the option of staying overnight: the six guestrooms have been individually designed by artist Margret Lafontaine.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14162;Krietsch;Germany;Schwäbisch Gmünd;Münstergasse 2, Schwäbisch Gmünd, 73525, Germany;48.7982076;9.7967534;90;false;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;This place used to be called Fuggerei – its name may have changed but it continues to be a great restaurant. At Krietsch, the cuisine is seasonal with a connection to the region, but it also draws on international influences. At lunchtime there are daily specials. Diners can sit inside, beneath the period vaulted ceiling, or out on the gorgeous terrace. Great location for a visit to the cathedral, which is just to the rear of the restaurant.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14164;Heldmann & Herzhaft;Germany;Remscheid;Brüderstraße 56, Remscheid, 42853, Germany;51.1803094;7.1815479;51;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Originally the home of an industrialist, this smart 19C villa now houses this splendid restaurant, with its high ceilings, fine parquet flooring and elegant table settings – the perfect setting to enjoy Ulrich Heldmann's ambitious cuisine. Whether you opt for the seasonal set menu or order à la carte, you will be served meticulously prepared, flavoursome dishes made with fresh ingredients. The terrace is of course the place to go in summer. Wednesdays and Thursdays also open at lunchtime.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14165;Adler;Germany;Ratshausen;Hohnerstraße 3, Ratshausen, 72365, Germany;48.1939626;8.7965146;47;false;true;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;The atmosphere in this historical inn is cosy and rustic. The cordial and welcoming service staff is led by the charming Styrian manager, who herself is a fantastic host! In the kitchen, a father-and-son team prepares flavoursome dishes using high-quality ingredients. The menu is divided into two sections: classic Swabian dishes such as Kutteln in Lemberger (a tripe speciality) or house-made maultaschen, and sophisticated dishes like Japanese ramen soup or Breton monkfish with cauliflower and almond puree. An old jukebox provides the background music. Tip: The restaurant produces its own range of schnapps.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14166;Kraftwerk;Germany;Oberursel;Zimmersmühlenweg 2, Oberursel, 61440, Germany;50.194255;8.5920853;71;true;true;Contemporary, International;This converted power station is not only a chic location – it is also a place for extremely good food. The cuisine combines classic and Mediterranean influences, in the form of modern set menus, including "Around the World", "Pescetarian" or – if ordered 48hr in advance – the "Grand Classique" (for the whole table, minimum two people). Alternatively there is the large "Culinary Experience" set menu. They can recommend just the right wine pairing, should you wish. The high-ceilinged space channels industrial charm. Friendly service.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14167;Villa Medici;Germany;Münster;Prozessionsweg 402, Münster, 48155, Germany;51.9684648;7.6777191;44;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This spruce villa enjoys a delightful location in a quiet residential area on the outskirts of the city. Diners here are pampered with friendly service, Mediterranean flavours and Italian wines in a chic and inviting atmosphere. In addition to à la carte options, there are daily specials and a tasting menu. A charming terrace is laid out to the side. Plus, there are five attractive guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14168;Gastraum;Germany;Trier;Bernhardstraße 14, Trier, 54295, Germany;49.7450068;6.6418236;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This modern extension of the attractive Villa Hügel (1914) has a sleek and elegant feel. The ceiling-to-floor windows afford an impressive view of Trier, and the terrace is a particularly sought-after spot in this regard! Savour fresh, contemporary dishes made from good-quality ingredients and washed down with regional wines. The young team in charge of serving you are charming and professional. Cosy guestrooms and a lovely relaxation suite await overnight guests.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14169;Brunnenstuben;Germany;Waiblingen;Quellenstraße 14, Waiblingen, 71334, Germany;48.8192344;9.3497605;76;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Don’t be put off by the somewhat unprepossessing exterior at Brunnenstuben because the food is excellent! Petra and Thorsten Beyer – she running the kitchen, he managing the friendly and professional front-of-house team – serve flavoursome Swabian fare including an excellent Zwiebelrostbraten (roast beef with onions).;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14170;Fässle le Restaurant;Germany;Stuttgart;Löwenstraße 51, Stuttgart, 70597, Germany;48.7476434;9.1706567;82;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;Patrick Giboin prepares his own particular take on classic French cuisine in this cosy restaurant, where the mouthwatering menu includes dishes such as braised veal cheeks with king oyster mushrooms, risotto and wild broccoli. Vegetarian options and children’s menus also available.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14171;Ambiente;Germany;Staufen im Breisgau;Ballrechterstraße 8, Staufen im Breisgau, 79219, Germany;47.8721187;7.7139569;87;true;true;Farm to table;Mathias and Melanie Luiz’s restaurant is in a small industrial area. He cooks with a Mediterranean note, which is also reflected in the bright, warm colours of the interior.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14172;Dorfstube;Germany;Sonnenbühl;Im Dorf 12, Sonnenbühl, 72820, Germany;48.3505257;9.1943389;55;true;false;Swabian, Farm to table;It's no wonder people that love to eat here! In addition to its fine dining restaurant, Hotel Hirsch has its Dorfstube, which is a great option for fans of Swabian cuisine. In the cosy old dining space, completely done out in wood, you can tuck into specialities such as tripe, maultaschen and Zwiebelrostbraten (roast beef with onions). Vegetarian options are also on the menu. The delicious dishes are all made using regional produce. Friendly service. We highly recommend staying overnight. The guestrooms are really lovely and inviting.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14173;Zum Hirsch;Germany;Remchingen;Hauptstraße 23, Remchingen, 75196, Germany;48.9463759;8.5747277;76;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;This charming half-timbered inn dates back to 1688. In winter you can sit in the pretty room dominated by the fireplace, in summer on the attractive terrace. On the menu, for example, roasted & braised venison from local hunting in venison pepper jus with celery, mole & apricot. At lunchtime there is reasonably priced three-course "Eat & Talk" set menu. Guestrooms for a pleasant overnight stay.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14174;Gasthof zum Maurerwirt;Germany;Reichertshausen;Scheyerer Straße 3, Reichertshausen, 85293, Germany;48.4601268;11.4484275;46;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Georg Grimm represents the fourth generation of the family to run this tastefully designed, rustic-style inn. It serves carefully prepared contemporary dishes based on fresh produce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14175;Hermannshof;Germany;Bad Sobernheim;Felkestraße 100, Bad Sobernheim, 55566, Germany;49.7773178;7.6585776;25;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Country cooking;This is the second restaurant of the tasteful BollAnts Spa im Park hotel. Like the first, it has a fine vaulted ceiling and an exceptionally beautiful interior done out in an attractive vintage look. The terrace in the courtyard is also inviting. Mediterranean cuisine with regional influences is served in two set menus that change daily and with courses that can be mixed and matched.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14176;Der Engel;Germany;Sasbachwalden;Talstraße 14, Sasbachwalden, 77887, Germany;48.6197585;8.1231943;51;false;false;Country cooking;The perfect example of a traditional Baden inn! This family-run establishment has been welcoming guests since 1764, offering a consistently enjoyable experience. Behind its old half-timbered walls, there are charming dining areas – some more traditional, others more modern. In a warm and welcoming atmosphere, diners tuck into delicious regional fare. Options include classic dishes, daily specials and set menus. Tip: There is a fantastic selection of digestifs. Overnight accommodation available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14177;Kings and Queens;Germany;Schweinfurt;Bauerngasse 101, Schweinfurt, 97421, Germany;50.0471334;10.2314188;27;false;false;International, Farm to table;This small restaurant has plenty of regulars, who are drawn by the modern and elegant decor, the friendly and professional service and the seasonal international cuisine. A choice of three menus, one of which is vegetarian, is proposed. You can also swap out courses or order à la carte. The wine list is sure to please, with an especially well-curated selection of labels from the region.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14178;Weinstube am Brühl;Germany;Quedlinburg;Billungstraße 11, Quedlinburg, 06484, Germany;51.7842276;11.137494;62;true;true;International, Farm to table;These former stables have been converted into a delightful restaurant, in which terracotta tiles, warm colours and an old brick ceiling lend a real country feel. The international cuisine on offer follows the seasons closely. The six-course "Weinstuben-Menü" (with vegan/vegetarian alternatives) comes with optional wine pairings. À la carte dining is also possible. Attentive service comes courtesy of a friendly and adept front-of-house team. Tip: Summer barbecue evenings (Jun-Aug) – booking recommended. Charming and elegant guestrooms are available in the Hotel Am Brühl.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14179;Berghotel Schlossanger Alp;Germany;Pfronten;Am Schlossanger 1, Pfronten, 87459, Germany;47.5701162;10.5862904;96;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;Set against the backdrop of the Allgäu Alps, this beautiful building houses both a hotel with tasteful and comfortable guestrooms, and a cosy and stylishly furnished restaurant. Affording stunning views, the terrace is naturally a wonderful spot in summer! The food is excellent and made with ingredients that are sourced exclusively from the region. Dishes such as Arctic char confit served with morels and peas are complemented by your choice from the excellent wine list.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14180;Fährhütte 14;Germany;Rottach-Egern;Weißachdamm 50, Rottach-Egern, 83700, Germany;47.6958438;11.7398383;31;false;true;International, Farm to table;This restaurant, an offshoot of Überfahrt, enjoys an idyllic lakeside location. The modern decor has a touch of rustic maritime flair while the service is friendly and accomplished. International and seasonal dishes. You will also have the opportunity to rent a deckchair on the beach! N.B. the restaurant is not accessible by car – getting there involves a 300m walk.;Great view,Terrace;[]
14181;Gastwirtschaft Ferdinand Reuter;Germany;Rheda-Wiedenbrück;Bleichstraße 3, Rheda-Wiedenbrück, 33378, Germany;51.8540576;8.2910084;48;true;true;Farm to table;This traditional family-run establishment serves good-quality regional cuisine that takes its cue from the seasons. Classic fare and more sophisticated dishes both feature on the menu. The atmosphere is friendly and cosy – in the more modern section, diners take their seats at long wooden tables. Hotel Reuter, which houses this restaurant, has comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14182;Hoppe's;Germany;Pforzheim;Weiherstraße 15, Pforzheim, 75173, Germany;48.8886167;8.6971441;49;true;false;French;The atmosphere is welcoming and lively, and the food is great – it's no wonder that people come back again and again. The menu features dishes from Alsace and Baden, with mouthwatering options such as "coq au vin à la chef", beef sirloin served with roasted onions and spaetzle, or Baden-style pike dumplings. They also do Flammkuchen. There is outdoor seating to the front of the building.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14183;Weingut;Germany;Passau;Theresienstraße 28, Passau, 94032, Germany;48.5734125;13.4618329;21;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;After a stroll through the city, how about dinner at a chic restaurant with a trendy modern decor? There are plenty of options to choose from here at Weingut, including house specialities, steaks, plus a selection of dishes that changes every week (see the "Wochenkarte"). Alternatively, you could simply opt for tapas or a glass of wine – you can also buy bottles to take home. The service is very friendly and attentive. Decorative wine racks and high tables contribute to the pleasant wine bar atmosphere of the place. There are two reservation times: 17:30 - 20:00 and from 20:15.;Terrace;[]
14184;Ondersch Genusswirtschaft;Germany;Oberstdorf;Ludwigstraße 7, Oberstdorf, 87561, Germany;47.4057896;10.2789481;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Going by the name "Ondersch" (a dialect word meaning different), this establishment located in the multipurpose "LOFT" building offers a cinema, a street-food bar and a gourmet restaurant. On the upper floor, a lively, urban atmosphere provides the setting for tasty modern cuisine made from seasonal and regional produce.;Wheelchair access;[]
14185;Alpenkönig - Esslust;Germany;Oberstaufen;Kalzhofer Straße 25, Oberstaufen, 87534, Germany;47.55773;10.02608;65;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Diners take their seats in a lovely, upscale dining space comprising areas that range in style from traditional charm to modern chic. A cordial and professional front-of-house team serves fresh regional cuisine that draws on the seasons and Mediterranean influences. You can go à la carte or choose dishes for the three or four courses of your own set menu. There is also an appealing wine list. The restaurant is located in the attractive Alpenkönig hotel, which has inviting guestrooms and modern wellness facilities, set in the gorgeous Allgäu landscape.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
14186;Löwen Genuss Wirtschaft;Germany;Oberstdorf;Kirchstraße 1, Oberstdorf, 87561, Germany;47.4084453;10.278386;87;false;true;Country cooking, Bavarian;The "Alpine lifestyle hotel" Löwen & Strauss proposes this really appealing eatery as an alternative to its fine dining restaurant. The rustic yet modern decor (complete with lovely little touches like old skis, cow bells etc) goes down just as well as the friendly service and the mouth-watering cuisine, which takes its cue from the region and the seasons. Top tip: Have a drink at Berggold, the adjacent bar.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14187;Würzhaus;Germany;Nuremberg;Kirchenweg 3a, Nuremberg, 90419, Germany;49.4623209;11.0699166;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This really is an appealing restaurant. At lunchtime, things are toned down a little, with reasonably priced options (à la carte or a small set menu). In the evening, there is an ambitious set menu that comes in four to six flavourful courses. Head chef Diana Burkel is committed to using locally sourced ingredients. The dedication to sustainability extends to the wine selection – the list is dominated by organic, biodynamic and natural wines. The service is friendly and attentive, and the atmosphere is welcoming.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14188;Zum Rössl;Germany;Neckargemünd;Heidelberger Straße 15, Neckargemünd, 69151, Germany;49.3730653;8.7702096;33;false;true;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;This long-standing family-run place is in a former post station dating from 1642. It is a pretty, traditional-style restaurant that offers a choice of regional classics as well as Mediterranean and seasonally influenced daily specials. A surprise menu is also available on reservation. Tip: the idyllic terrace!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14189;Il Borgo;Germany;Munich;Georgenstraße 144, Munich, 80797, Germany;48.1575717;11.5608352;38;true;true;Italian;This Italian restaurant has been a mainstay of Schwabing's culinary scene since 1989. The interior is modern and elegant yet cosy, with the current decor successfully incorporating the old wall tiles and original bar. The menu sticks close to the seasons. In addition to the five-course tasting menu, there is an à la carte selection – from delicious pasta dishes to branzino al sale (salt-baked sea bass) for two.;Terrace;[]
14190;Villa Hammerschmiede;Germany;Pfinztal;Hauptstraße 162, Pfinztal, 76327, Germany;48.9704756;8.5488317;83;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Whether seated in one of the comfortable dining areas or the light and airy pavilion, you can look forward to cuisine that is ambitious, classic and regional, ranging from the intriguing "Villa Lunch" set menu to the "Feinschmecker-Menü" in the evenings. Options include turbot fillet fried in olive oil accompanied by Hokkaido pumpkin and dried apricot relish with walnut. Delightful terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14191;Stephans Stuben by Marco Langer;Germany;Neu-Ulm;Bahnhofstraße 65, Neu-Ulm, 89231, Germany;48.3969664;10.0088519;70;false;false;Creative, Farm to table;This restaurant is run by Marco Langer, a well-known chef in the region. His dishes are meticulously prepared, creatively modern, and made with the finest ingredients. Plus he is not afraid to create bold flavour combinations. A prime example is the tomato, onion, and basil, each presented in different variations and paired with an incredibly flavoursome blend of mascarpone and parmesan. Comprising four or six courses, there are two set menus, one of which is vegetarian. The restaurant's clean, tasteful design is very inviting. Friendly, professional service creates a welcoming atmosphere, and the chef himself often interacts with diners. Wine recommendations come courtesy of the enthusiastic sommelier. Alongside wine pairings, non-alcoholic alternatives are available to go with the set menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14192;Little London;Germany;Munich;Tal 31, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1356681;11.5808989;82;false;true;Grills, Meats and Grills;This lively steakhouse not far from the Isartor is fronted by a classic bar of impressive dimensions – there are over 320 types of gin to choose from here! The attractive interior design successfully brings together a certain rusticity and a touch of English elegance. Meat eaters can look forward to high-quality cuts cooked on the Montague grill – tantalising examples include US Black Angus Prime Beef and Wagyu Kagoshima A5. There are over 250 wines on the wine list. Tip: Why not sign up for one of their beef-tasting sessions? With its various lounges, the restaurant also caters to private parties.;Terrace;[]
14193;Chalet am Kiental;Germany;Herrsching am Ammersee;Andechsstraße 4, Herrsching am Ammersee, 82211, Germany;47.9978785;11.178146;54;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Set in an old farmhouse, this lovely modern restaurant embodies a charming blend of old and new, which makes for a cosy atmosphere. There is also an attractive terrace. The cuisine is modern, seasonal and regional. Diners have a choice of two set menus: "Kiental", which comprises four or five courses and the three- or four-course vegan "Chalet". An à la carte selection is also available. For overnight stays, they have individually designed guestrooms – all done out tastefully and with great attention to detail.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14194;Galleria;Germany;Munich;Sparkassenstraße 11, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1373693;11.5781018;78;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;A cosy little restaurant in the city centre. It uses fresh, top quality produce in its ambitious Italian cuisine. The brightly coloured pictures on the walls change frequently.;Air conditioning;[]
14195;Johannas;Germany;Munich;Heiglhofstraße 18, Munich, 81377, Germany;48.1127257;11.4779971;76;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;With its pleasant, upscale decor, gorgeous courtyard terrace and excellent food, the restaurant in the family-run Hotel Neumayr is certainly inviting. Ambitious cuisine is served as a set menu or à la carte comprising sophisticated, meticulously crafted dishes made from the finest ingredients. Take, for example, the saddle of chamois with juneberry, purple curry, wild mushroom, red cabbage and celeriac. Game and offal specialities are a firm fixture on the menu. The owner's œnophilia is given away by the impressive wine list, which comprises over 2 000 labels. The selection is international, but Chardonnay and Pinot Noir from Burgundy take pride of place. Such a range of small bottles is also something one does not often see. The waitstaff are highly professional yet friendly and approachable.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14197;Blauer Bock;Germany;Munich;Sebastiansplatz 9, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1343618;11.5739034;32;false;false;Classic Cuisine;A cornerstone of the fine dining scene for years, this restaurant is housed in the spruce hotel of the same name, nestled in the centre of Munich – a stone's throw from the Viktualienmarkt and the city museum. The decor is tasteful, sleek and contemporary in style, with striking pictures adorning the walls. The cuisine is classic with a modern twist, and the menu includes mouthwatering options such as braised veal shoulder or sole for two. Outside, the tables overlooking the pedestrian area are in high demand.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14198;Sängerheim - Das Restaurant;Germany;Hennef;Teichstraße 9, Hennef, 53773, Germany;50.805487;7.315749;36;true;true;Farm to table;This pleasant restaurant in an attractive neighbourly village environment offers flavoursome seasonal cuisine. Regional produce often features in the dishes and the service is warm and welcoming. There is a beautiful terrace behind the restaurant.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14200;Hirschkönig;Germany;Parsberg;Marktstraße 1a, Parsberg, 92331, Germany;49.1600111;11.718611;65;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Here, rural charm combines with elegant and contemporary interior design to create a welcoming setting – that goes for both the Hirschen hotel and its small fine dining restaurant with its upscale, sleek and stylish dining space. The modern and seasonal set menu, "Feld & Flur" ("Field & Fell"), is composed of six or seven courses imbued with a hint of the Mediterranean, such as wild garlic ravioli with tomato. Wine pairings are available upon request. Head to the delicatessen for house-made specialities such as chutneys, pickles and cured meats.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
14201;Höfli;Germany;Staufen im Breisgau;Hauptstraße 56, Staufen im Breisgau, 79219, Germany;47.8817338;7.7312063;19;false;true;Farm to table;The charming Höfli blends seamlessly into the picturesque old town setting. The enchanting cobblestone courtyard invites you to dine under the summer sky, surrounded by historical walls and half-timbered buildings. The interior is just as pleasant with its sleek, contemporary feel. While maître d' Alexandra Killy ensures a warm welcome, her husband, Marco, prepares delicious and neatly crafted dishes. His classical training shines through in dishes such as the Breton skate wing with buckwheat and saffron risotto, capers and shellfish stock.;Terrace;[]
14202;von Rhemen;Germany;Münster;Steinfurter Straße 374, Münster, 48159, Germany;51.987784;7.5851685;29;true;true;Classic French;The restaurant of the stylish Schloss Wilkinghege hotel is set in an elegant, high-ceilinged room with fine mouldings and bags of historical charm. The classical cuisine makes the most of seasonal ingredients, with diners able to choose between à la carte dishes, the "Schlossmenü" and vegetarian set menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14203;Jin;Germany;Munich;Kanalstraße 14, Munich, 80538, Germany;48.1359299;11.5841857;79;true;true;Asian, Chinese;Highlights at Jin include the upscale, minimalist-style interior inspired by the Far East and the flavoursome pan-Asian cuisine with a distinct Chinese edge, as well as Japanese and European influences. Tip: In addition to the à la carte selection, there are the set menus "Jin's Flavours" and "Jin's Degustation", which provide the best impression of the chef's skills.;Terrace;[]
14204;Pungshaus;Germany;Hilden;Grünstraße 22, Hilden, 40723, Germany;51.1659842;6.9503522;21;false;true;Farm to table, Classic French;This pretty little half-timbered house serves good food in a cosy setting. The market-fresh cuisine includes dishes such as veal tenderloin with purple potato mash and pan-fried green asparagus.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14205;AUVIGU;Germany;Bad Salzuflen;Wenkenstraße 21, Bad Salzuflen, 32105, Germany;52.084932;8.747979;57;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Nestled in the old town, a stone's throw from the renowned saltworks, this restaurant is a haven of pure comfort run by Gianluca Fleer, who has set up shop with his wife Inga. "High Dining" is what they call their concept of modern, creative yet down-to-earth cuisine – served as a set menu or à la carte. In dishes such as creamy risotto with Aquerello rice, nashi pear, scallop, lardo, saffron, yuzu and parsnip, the chef-patron draws on his Sardinian roots as well as French and international accents – simple yet captivating. The setting is also inviting: well-appointed, modern and with a touch of elegance.;;[]
14206;Matsuhisa Munich;Germany;Munich;Neuturmstraße 1, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1373365;11.580929;75;false;false;Japanese Contemporary, Peruvian;The high quality evident throughout the luxury Mandarin Oriental is also reflected in the minimalist-style restaurant run by Nobu Matsuhisa, who runs restaurants around the world. The cuisine is modern Japanese and interesting, refined with Peruvian flavours and techniques – an exciting mix. Don’t miss the sushi and sashimi or the classic Black Cod Miso dish!;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining;[]
14207;KIKU Restaurant by Jan Fribus;Germany;Quedlinburg;Pölle 8, Quedlinburg, 06484, Germany;51.7887691;11.1429829;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Asian;Kiku means chrysanthemum – the Japanese national flower – and, indeed, the cuisine here is strongly marked by Japanese elements. Influences from other Asian countries, as well as the odd subtle touch of classic French cookery, can also be detected. The menu features dishes such as bluefin tuna with misato rose radish and tomato ponzu, and hibachi steak with pumpkin and hoisin. The restaurant is located in a tastefully restored historical building in a small street lined with half-timbered façades, not far from the city centre. Inside, the atmosphere is laid back and elegant, and there is a secluded terrace in the courtyard. The service is friendly and informal – the charming chefs also come to your table to talk you through their dishes. The best way to get to know the food is to opt for the nine-course set menu, but there is also an appealing à la carte menu. The short yet carefully curated wine list complements the food perfectly, and most wines are available by the glass. Tip: Just upstairs from the restaurant, Anno 1560 offers cosy and stylish apartments.;Terrace;[]
14208;IL Sommelier;Germany;Munich;Kreillerstraße 194, Munich, 81825, Germany;48.1225923;11.6609953;51;true;false;Italian;Behind the unassuming façade of a modern building in the Trudering district, this is a real gem of a restaurant. In the chic, contemporary space, diners are served authentic, flavoursome, down-to-earth cucina italiana. The dishes on the menu are sophisticated but not pretentious, and include tortelli with a cheese and aubergine filling or beef cheek braised with sweet potato mash. The wine list features Italian wines exclusively. In summer, the quiet terrace to the rear of the property beckons.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14209;Kulinarium;Germany;Röthenbach an der Pegnitz;Friedrichsplatz 4, Röthenbach an der Pegnitz, 90552, Germany;49.4818921;11.2375911;21;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Creative;This delightful restaurant is nestled in a spruce half-timbered building in the heart of Röthenbach an der Pegnitz, just outside Nuremberg. Modern interior design incorporating a rustic wooden beam ceiling creates a cosy atmosphere. You can feel commitment and passion here. Gerald Hoffmann, a well-known chef in the region and most recently head chef at Koch und Kellner, is in charge in the kitchen. His wife presides over the service, adding a soupçon of heartfelt charm to every interaction. There is a seasonally orientated set menu that is prepared using mainly regional ingredients. In summer you can sit on the terrace in the front garden. There is also a small hotel in the building.;Terrace;[]
14210;Knipsers Halbstück - Brasserie;Germany;Bissersheim;Hollergasse 2, Bissersheim, 67281, Germany;49.5364084;8.2013192;17;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;The Knipsers, a well-known family of winemakers from Laumersheim, opened Halbstück as a wine tavern back in 2014. Christian Rubert, who is also known for his work at the restaurant Karlbacher in Großkarlbach, has now taken over as head chef here. His roots in Alsace are evident in his dishes, which pair beautifully with the finest wines from the Knisper winegrowing estate. Laura Rubert provides warm hospitality in a cosy setting. Delightful courtyard. They also offer guided wine tastings (for 10 people or more) and accept bookings for weddings and conferences. A holiday flat is available to rent out, too.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14211;Schreiberei;Germany;Munich;Dienerstraße 20, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1377709;11.577008;35;false;false;International;In the heart of the city, just a stone's throw from Marienplatz, this restaurant is on the ground floor of Munich's heritage-protected chancery, where the city's history was first recorded in 1552. The attractive interior has a brasserie feel and, in good weather, the quiet sheltered courtyard terrace is especially inviting. The dishes on the menu are bursting with flavour and made with select ingredients, such as the veal cheeks with truffle polenta.;Terrace;[]
14212;Waldhorn;Germany;Stuttgart;Krehlstraße 111, Stuttgart, 70565, Germany;48.7185034;9.1022375;89;true;false;Contemporary, Regional European;This restaurant in Stuttgart's Rohr neighbourhood serves an intriguing take on classic French cuisine that draws on Spanish and Swabian influences. This concept wasn't simply plucked out of thin air: the two chefs – José María González Sampedro, who hails from Mallorca, and Caroline Autenrieth from Swabia – met while working in a restaurant in Marseille. The six courses on their surprise menu include deliciously aromatic lamb and braised shallot with a filling of blood sausage ragout with Mediterranean spices. In the attractive seating area, old wood panelling and modern furnishings add to the charm.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14213;Joseph's Fine Dining;Germany;Bad Sachsa;Bismarckstraße 23, Bad Sachsa, 37441, Germany;51.600267;10.5450555;29;false;false;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;An intimate atmosphere reigns in Hotel Romantischer Winkel's small restaurant. The open kitchen contributes significantly to the vibe – diners can see, hear and smell everything that's happening. You're practically sitting in the thick of the action and communication with the team is encouraged. Primarily local and seasonal ingredients are combined with international spices and aromatics to conjure up creative cosmopolitan dishes with poetic names. For their "Großer Gourmetabend" (Thu-Sat), they devise an eight-course set menu, and a six-course version for the "Kleiner Gourmetabend" on Wednesdays : Each course is served to every table at the same time, with the chef and sous-chef guiding you through the evening. To finish off, coffee is brewed at your table. The pleasingly modern interior is complemented by floor-to-ceiling windows that look out onto Lake Schmelzteich.;Car park;[]
14214;Lou im Cavalierhaus;Germany;Cottbus;Zum Kavalierhaus 9, Cottbus, 03042, Germany;51.7414615;14.36975;65;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The estate is worth a visit in its own right. Along with the palace, there is the 620ha Branitz Park, landscaped by Prince Hermann von Pückler in the 19C. Lou (a nickname given to Prince Pückler) is an elegant restaurant housed in the smart Kavaliersbau (squire's lodge). Here, chef-patron Tim Sillack serves up a modern and seasonal take on classic cuisine, drawing on international influences, cf. his saddle of venison with chanterelles, Lieblingsbrot and wild berries. The chef also refers to the prince's own recipes, creating a link between past and present. The Pücklereis (Neapolitan ice cream) – something of a signature dessert – is a permanent feature of the menu. There are also three tastefully furnished guestrooms for overnight stays.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14215;Chicha;Germany;Berlin;Friedelstraße 34, Berlin, 12047, Germany;52.4932823;13.4278887;73;false;false;Peruvian;Bustling, loud, rustic, and just a touch “shabby”... Chicha has succeeded in creating an informal authentically South American atmosphere to complement its modern Peruvian cooking. Quality fresh products are ambitiously blended to mouthwatering effect, with dishes such as ceviche of meagre fish and Thüringer Duroc belly of pork with smoked banana featuring on the menu.;Terrace;[]
14216;Konrad's;Germany;Bonn;Platz der Vereinten Nationen 4, Bonn, 53113, Germany;50.7195382;7.1221448;16;true;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;This restaurant on the 17th floor of the Marriott Hotel has the "wow" factor of a great view over Bonn through its floor-to-ceiling windows. In the open kitchens they cook up modern dishes with Mediterranean influences. Pre- or after-dinner drinks are served in the bar right next door. Parking is available in the underground garage, and the lift leads directly to the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14217;mural farmhouse - À LA CARTE;Germany;Munich;Gmunder Straße 27, Munich, 81379, Germany;48.0973132;11.5284664;69;true;true;Regional Cuisine;The second part of mural farmhouse is a modern, casual bistro that places just as much emphasis on sustainability and regionality as FINE DINE. Ingredients are sourced locally and harvested from the restaurant's own raised garden beds on the roof of its affiliated hotel, WunderLocke. Delicious dishes such as einkorn risotto with mountain cheese, herbs (from the rooftop garden), piment d'Espelette and cabbage crisps are served à la carte. You can also have lunch here – the range is slightly smaller and includes some options from the evening menu, as well as a reasonably priced bento box. The selection of organic and biodynamic wines is the same as in the fine dining restaurant.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14218;Marie;Germany;Hanover;Wedekindplatz 1, Hanover, 30161, Germany;52.3855784;9.7493772;72;false;true;French, Creative;Marie is located in the Oststadt district of the city, surrounded by historical buildings. The modern yet warm and inviting atmosphere sets the scene for French cuisine with creative and Far Eastern influences. Chef-patron Sven Holthaus serves two set menus (one vegetarian) with up to five courses, plus oysters as an optional course. Choose your accompaniment from the wine list, which may be short but covers all bases when it comes to German and French labels – there are also wines by the glass. Attentive service. The pleasant terrace in front of the house opens in summer. Be sure to reserve.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14219;Beetle;Germany;Munich;Schumannstraße 9, Munich, 80538, Germany;48.141707;11.6029205;57;false;false;Vegetarian, Modern Cuisine;Environmental awareness and sustainability have always been key in every aspect of this restaurant certified as organic – from the tasteful interior design to the staff uniform and not least the food. Following a change of concept, meat and fish dishes are now offered in addition to the tried and tested vegetarian and vegan dishes. The exceptionally friendly and attentive front-of-house team will happily recommend wines from their almost exclusively organic or biodynamic selection. Lovely covered terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14220;Alte Schule;Germany;Bad Berleburg;Goetheplatz 1, Bad Berleburg, 57319, Germany;51.0503386;8.3893006;77;true;true;Classic Cuisine, International;In this former school building done out with a cosy modern decor, enjoy the friendly attentive service. Here, they serve seasonal dishes prepared using regional ingredients, such as Wittgenstein venison goulash with Serviettenknödel (sliced bread dumpling cooked in a napkin) and apple compote.;;[]
14221;Clinton's;Germany;Hoppegarten;Neuer Hönower Weg 7, Hoppegarten, 15366, Germany;52.5095869;13.650439;16;false;true;Farm to table, International;Near the outskirts of Berlin, this restaurant is housed on the first floor of the European headquarters of the fashion company Clinton. The decor is up to the minute, as is the seasonally influenced cuisine – choose between a four- or six-course set menu and their à la carte "Signature" dishes, from "Berlin Blutwurst, sauerkraut, green back bacon, cassis, mustard" to "300g beef – roast beef, fillet, 16hr-cooked ox shoulder, truffle purée, teriyaki, vegetables from the farm". Fans of dry-aged steaks are also in for a treat. The service is attentive and the waitstaff professional. From some tables you can sneak a peek into the Clinton outlet.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
14222;Kuhlemann;Germany;Neustadt an der Waldnaab;Freyung 39, Neustadt an der Waldnaab, 92660, Germany;49.73223;12.17514;33;true;false;Creative;You can tell from the food that the chef has worked in some top establishments. Here in the restaurant of the family-run Grader hotel, his interesting cooking style translates into a creative set menu. This is accompanied by an appealing and concise wine list. The attractive setting blends rustic and modern features.;Car park;[]
14223;Belvedere;Germany;Heringsdorf;Delbrückstraße 10, Heringsdorf, 17419, Germany;53.953949;14.1699806;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The culinary flagship of the Travel Charme Strandidyll hotel. From your table in the fourth-floor dining area, which with its glass dome has an elegant modern feel , you can take in the wonderful view over the hotel grounds all the way to the Baltic Sea. The cuisine is classic in its foundations and partly based on regional produce. You are free to put together your own set menu. Friendly and well-drilled waitstaff. Tip: Your aperitif is best enjoyed on the gorgeous terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14224;POTS;Germany;Berlin;Potsdamer Platz 3, Berlin, 10785, Germany;52.5101659;13.3753068;72;true;true;German, Modern Cuisine;Relaxed, chic and stylish! The eye-catching features of the Ritz-Carlton's restaurant are its striking decor and large open kitchen. The chefs put a modern spin on traditional German cuisine in dishes such as Königsberger Klopse (meatballs in a white wine sauce) with capers and yellow beetroot. There are also options for sharing. Alternatively, take a punt on the surprise menu. The lunch deal is also popular. Friendly and adept service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14225;Restaurant Mühle;Germany;Binzen;Mühlenstraße 26, Binzen, 79589, Germany;47.6347203;7.6257354;78;true;true;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;The kitchen crew from Krone in Weil am Rhein has joined forces with the local team behind the stove here. Their cuisine – based on a contemporary blend of regional, seasonal and Mediterranean influences – is made with good, fresh produce. The elegant, rustic-style interior is inviting, plus there is a lovely terrace. Cosy, comfortable guestrooms await you in the hotel. On the practical side: it is only about 15 minutes by car to Basel, the airport and the trade fair.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14227;Berta;Germany;Berlin;Stresemannstraße 99, Berlin, 10963, Germany;52.505803;13.3803159;27;false;false;Israeli, Contemporary;Berta would be very proud of her grandson, chef Assaf Granit, who has named this appealing restaurant after her. The energy of the chefs in the open kitchen, nestled behind the counter, is infectious, as they fill the colourful dining space with a vibrant and convivial atmosphere. A lively scenario, for which the menu is a perfect match: it is a veritable celebration of family recipes from Jerusalem infused with the modern spirit of Berlin. The "Frenavon" bread with tahini and tomatoes served beforehand is downright addictive. It is practically impossible to resist the charm of this restaurant!;Air conditioning;[]
14228;KOS fine dining;Germany;Kiel;Hamburger Chaussee 183, Kiel, 24113, Germany;54.2993596;10.1068319;33;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant is a little off the tourist trail, but it's well worth the journey. Expect chic and trendy interior design, attentive service and, last but not least, a cuisine based on well-chosen seasonal ingredients. There are two seatings and two set menus every evening: the 3-course ‘Jungfernfahrt’ menu at 6 pm and the 5-course ‘Kreuzfahrt’ menu at 8 pm. Both are also available as vegetarian options (please order one day in advance).;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14229;Restaurant 1831;Germany;Essen;August-Thyssen-Straße 51, Essen, 45219, Germany;51.3617978;6.9173244;20;true;true;French Contemporary, Modern French;Even the route to the magnificent moated castle, a 17C architectural gem, is an experience – you get to this stunning estate through a wooded area, then a bridge over the moat leads into the beautiful inner courtyard. The restaurant allies the character of this site steeped in history with modern comfort and winter garden-style. The view through the large glazed front is fabulous, not to mention the terrace! They serve two 4- or 6-course set menus of modern inspiration – one with meat and its vegetarian counterpart. You can choose the matching wine or non-alcoholic pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14230;Fritz's Frau Franzi;Germany;Düsseldorf;Adersstraße 8, Düsseldorf, 40215, Germany;51.2182494;6.7775864;91;false;false;Creative, International;This restaurant is located in stylish boutique hotel The Fritz, and you can have an aperitif at the bar in the lobby . The upscale interior is tasteful, and has a cool and trendy feel. Tobias Rocholl refers to his cosmopolitan, modern and creative culinary concept as "Gourmet in Action". Instead of butter, he uses high-quality oils, any dairy products are lactose-free, and he avoids industrial sugar altogether. Dishes such as Ijsselmeer pike-perch, lemon pointed cabbage, sauerkraut, leek vinaigrette can be ordered à la carte or as part of a set menu that you put together yourself. Vegetarian and vegan options are also available. Tip: From some tables you get a good view of the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14231;Ontra;Germany;Regensburg;Franz-Mayer-Straße 5a, Regensburg, 93053, Germany;49.0016611;12.1022688;67;true;true;Farm to table, Contemporary;This restaurant with a tastefully designed modern interior is located in TechSquare, the new centre for digitalisation south of the city centre. A friendly and professional team serves up seasonal cuisine that also includes vegetarian dishes. The shorter lunchtime menu proposes some cheaper options. The neighbouring Ontra's Gourmetstube serves a fixed set menu made up of seven courses in the evening.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14232;l'Ecume;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Friedberger Landstraße 62, Frankfurt on the Main, 60316, Germany;50.122521;8.6915254;38;true;true;Modern French, French Contemporary;L'Ecume means "foam" and makes reference to the lightness of the cuisine here as well as to French chef Alexandre Sadowczyk's native region of Champagne and its famous sparkling wine. In a friendly, casual atmosphere, diners tuck into modern French dishes that incorporate regional accents. The length of the set menu is variable.;Air conditioning;[]
14233;Margaux;Germany;Limburg an der Lahn;Kornmarkt 7, Limburg an der Lahn, 65549, Germany;50.3880334;8.0647968;43;true;false;Farm to table, Creative;Fabian Sollbach has struck out on his own and opened this tastefully modern restaurant housed in a fully renovated 14C building in the heart of the old town. In this setting, he serves up a modern take on French cuisine, in which select ingredients take centre stage. The menu includes ambitious dishes such as beef carpaccio with onion, truffle and oxtail praline. At lunchtime, the options are somewhat more limited and simpler. There are a handful of places to be had on the small gallery level and, in summer, tables are set up on a lovely terrace on the Kornmarkt.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14234;Feinschliff;Germany;Sinzig;Kirchplatz 8, Sinzig, 53489, Germany;50.5452526;7.2521643;68;false;false;Modern Cuisine, European Contemporary;This town-centre restaurant has a trendy, chic interior and a window through which you can see the chefs at work in the centrally positioned kitchen. The large floor-to-ceiling windows look out onto the church square of Pfarrkirche St Peter. In the evening, there is a modern set menu which incorporates subtle Asian influences and service starts for everyone at 6.30pm (by reservation only). Decent, reasonably priced wine pairings. At lunchtime, only a dish of the day is served.;Air conditioning;[]
14235;Hof Grothues-Potthoff - Hasenklee;Germany;Senden;Hof Grothues-Potthoff 4, Senden, 48308, Germany;51.8582427;7.4993127;58;false;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;A charming modern restaurant serving seasonal cuisine that often incorporates home-grown fruit and vegetables. Choose from two set menus of either four or five courses (with a three-course version on Wednesdays), one of which is vegetarian. Two additional dishes are available as optional extras. The service is friendly and the chef offers helpful wine recommendations. This beautiful farm also boasts a bakery, farm shop and hotel. Alternatively, Hasenpfeffer is open in the evenings – it serves traditional cuisine and dishes drawing on modern influences.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14236;Ivy;Germany;Karlsruhe;Karlstraße 34, Karlsruhe, 76133, Germany;49.006737;8.394522;98;true;false;Contemporary, International;The restaurant on the ground floor of the very centrally located 133 Boutique Hotel Karlsruhe provides a stylish bistro-style setting in which to enjoy modern, trendy cuisine either à la carte or in the form of a sharing menu for upwards of two people. You can also order various steak cuts served with a side dish and sauce of your choice – you even get to choose your own knife! The appetisers for sharing beforehand are fun, too. Why not finish off with a cocktail in the adjoining bar?;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14237;Ahlmanns;Germany;Kiel;Niemannsweg 102, Kiel, 24105, Germany;54.3387107;10.1513168;92;false;true;Creative, Seasonal Cuisine;The fine dining restaurant of Romantik Hotel Kieler Kaufmann lies in a quiet location in a smart residential neighbourhood. Here, Lasse Knickrehm and his team create innovative dishes that incorporate striking contrasts while maintaining a delicate balance – an interesting example is the Danish salmon with red cabbage, winter cress and black radish. In keeping with the modern thinking behind the three- to seven-course set menu, intriguing alcohol-free drink pairings are also offered as an alternative to wine. A vegetarian version of the omnivore set menu is available (please specify when booking). The historical space, a former banker's mansion, has been tastefully enhanced by a contemporary minimalist design and warm tones. Tip: On summer evenings, make a beeline for the gorgeous terrace overlooking the park. Kaufmannsladen is a laid-back alternative.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14238;Fangfrisch;Germany;Lübeck;An der Untertrave 51, Lübeck, 23552, Germany;53.8722931;10.6836572;90;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Seafood;A friendly, laid-back restaurant located on the edge of the city centre, only five minutes from the Holstentor. Trendy industrial-style design, very friendly and relaxed young service team and, last but not least, tasty modern cuisine. The emphasis is on regional ingredients – for example, organically farmed catfish from Brandenburg. Hot meals are served all day, but there are also sandwiches and fish rolls to go.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14239;Zwo20;Germany;Passau;Schrottgasse 12, Passau, 94032, Germany;48.5743103;13.4680915;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;The name of this restaurant refers to the year 2020, in which Andrea von Csiszer (head chef) and Sophie Herzog (the cordial and highly adept maître d') set up shop. Diners are drawn here not only by the somewhat unusual setting in a historical chapel with striking features such as vaults and ceiling paintings, but also the trendy and laid-back atmosphere, as well as the intriguing culinary concept: Asian sharing cuisine with a European twist. You can put together an assortment of several small, cleverly devised dishes to share, such as "Peking pork 24hr sous vide" with fried onion, soya and honey, or cauliflower wings with red cabbage, sweet chilli, fennel and potato. The location in the centre of the old town, caught between the Danube and the Inn, near the Dreiflüsseeck (three-river confluence), is also delightful. Tip: Römerplatz multi-storey car park just a few minutes' walk away.;Terrace;[]
14240;JAPATAPA TOSHIBAR;Germany;Munich;Marschallstraße 2, Munich, 80802, Germany;48.1635859;11.5881727;70;true;true;Japanese;Japatapa Toshibar is tucked away in a side street near Münchner Freiheit in the Schwabing district. Having formerly run the restaurant Toshi for a long time, owners Toshio and Tamiko Kobatake are no strangers to Munich's gastronomy scene. The small space, in which you sit at the counter or a small table, is done out in a minimalist style. Kobatake's cuisine is authentically Japanese: you should definitely try the tasty sushi, but dishes such as onsen egg with caviar and dashi broth or black cod grilled with saikyo miso are also tempting. The proprietress provides discreet and friendly service, and there is a good selection of wines as well as an impressive number of sakes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
14241;Eatrenalin;Germany;Rust;Roland-Mack-Ring 5, Rust, 77977, Germany;48.2617631;7.7377402;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;An almost futuristic spin on the fine dining experience! Using the online ticket system, you choose one of the set menus – "Red Dimensions" with fish and meat, or the vegetarian-vegan "Green Dimensions" – and your drink accompaniments in advance. Those who want extras can choose both menus in the variants "Exclusive Dinner", "Champagne Dinner" or "Sommelier Dinner". During the 2hr "Eatrenalin Experience", you are guided through different themed worlds and rooms on ultra-modern "floating chairs" and treated to corresponding appetisers and dishes in each space. This is an ambitious take on modern and creative cuisine that draws on international as well as classical influences. The evening is clearly structured and seamlessly organised, starting in the lounge and ending in the bar with music courtesy of a DJ, champagne and cocktails.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14242;Landgasthof Adler;Germany;Rosenberg;Ellwanger Straße 15, Rosenberg, 73494, Germany;49.0198683;10.0363909;85;true;false;Farm to table, Regional Cuisine;This centuries-old inn has long been known in the region for serving good food. Since February 2022, chef Michael Vogel has been perpetuating this tradition: he worked at the Adler years before and took over the reins after a stint working under top chef Andreas Caminada. The style of the decor is charming with its mix of tradition and modernity. Tip: The shop (Lädle) selling regional produce. Pretty guestrooms.;Car park;[]
14243;Von Korff;Germany;Meschede;Le-Puy-Straße 19, Meschede, 59872, Germany;51.3490406;8.2797025;45;true;false;International, Contemporary;This patrician house, successfully remodelled and extended, has an appealing feel of modernity with its clean, simple forms and abundant light. Good selection of Bordeaux wines.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14244;In Vino Veritas;Germany;Haslach im Kinzigtal;Steinacher Straße 9, Haslach im Kinzigtal, 77716, Germany;48.2782824;8.0841633;92;false;false;Farm to table, International;Inga and Ralf Müller have made a name for themselves with this friendly restaurant. This is due in no small part to the international and regional cuisine, which is made with very good, often local ingredients. The service is attentive and charming. In summer, you can dine on simpler fare in the charming courtyard with its vine arbour. There are chic, modern guestrooms and apartments for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
14246;Ratsstube;Germany;Limbach-Oberfrohna;Rathausplatz 1, Limbach-Oberfrohna, 09212, Germany;50.8584661;12.7679344;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Antje and Ronny Pester's lovely restaurant is located in the town centre, in the wing of the town hall. In the cosy, tastefully decorated interior, they serve ambitious modern cuisine aligned with the seasons – the tuna tartare, for example, is delicious. There is a set menu on Fridays and Saturdays – a vegetarian version can be pre-ordered. The service is attentive and friendly - the owner's wine suggestions are spot on. Lovely terrace to the rear of the building.;Terrace;[]
14247;Gutsschenke;Germany;Ludwigsburg;Monrepos 22, Ludwigsburg, 71634, Germany;48.921323;9.1674247;36;false;true;Country cooking, Contemporary;This restaurant's tasteful modern interior design has been beautifully integrated into the historical setting of the 150-year-old Monrepos estate. Outside, there is a delightful terrace under the shade of chestnut trees. The seasonally influenced cuisine is served in the form of a set menu (vegetarian version available) and à la carte. Options include classics such as Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) with champagne sauerkraut, as well as modern dishes such as wild garlic risotto with red prawns marinated in rosemary and burrata. Tip: Take a walk through the beautiful park and take in the view of the lake and golf course.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14248;WEINrestaurant Ayler Kupp;Germany;Ayl;Trierer Straße 49a, Ayl, 54441, Germany;49.62913;6.553654;66;false;false;Farm to table;While you tuck into the fresh seasonal dishes, which the chefs here like to cook up with produce from the region, you can take in the vineyards and the lovely garden. The wine list includes Riesling from the neighbouring wine estate. They also offer accommodation for overnight guests: the hotel has inviting, well-kept guestrooms ready for you.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14249;Berghofstüble;Germany;Bad Bellingen;Markus-Ruf-Straße, Bad Bellingen, 79415, Germany;47.7337074;7.5684094;16;true;true;Farm to table, International;This restaurant enjoys a stunning location up above the town. The interior has a pleasing design and there is an attractive conservatory with a pretty terrace outside offering impressive views. The cuisine is based on good, fresh produce with appetising dishes such as Skrei cod on leaf spinach in beurre blanc.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14250;Schwarzmatt;Germany;Badenweiler;Schwarzmattstraße 6a, Badenweiler, 79410, Germany;47.8036044;7.6789303;79;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Served à la carte or as a set menu, classic cuisine made with seasonal produce is the order of the day here. The upscale interior is very comfortable, with harmonious, lovingly arranged decorative objects – it certainly does full justice to the luxurious setting of the traditional holiday hotel of the same name in which this restaurant is housed. For overnight stays, there are elegant country-house-style guestrooms – this is after all the sister hotel of Baiersbronn's Hotel Bareiss. Make a beeline for the gorgeous garden terrace in summer. A must in the afternoon: cakes made to Hermine Bareiss's old recipes!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14252;Heiderand;Germany;Dresden;Ullersdorfer Platz 4, Dresden, 01324, Germany;51.0623119;13.855478;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Located close to the Dresdner Heide woodland, after which the restaurant is named, Heiderand now has Martin Walther at the helm – representing the fourth generation of the family to run the place (his parents are still involved). In this grand building dating back to 1905, diners can enjoy modern cuisine with an international slant. There are two set menus: wasser & weide ("water & pasture") and the vegetarian acker & beet ("field and beet"), each with three or five courses on offer, as well as seasonal dishes à la carte. Wine pairings are available upon request. Friendly and dedicated service.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14253;Villa's Wine & Dine;Germany;Reil an der Mosel;Moselstraße 5, Reil an der Mosel, 56861, Germany;50.0188703;7.1191245;16;false;true;Contemporary;In the fine dining restaurant of Villa Melsheimer, you can look forward to imaginative and creative modern dishes that are made from very good fresh ingredients. In summer, the gorgeous terrace overlooking the Moselle beckons! Should the weather not cooperate, you can also enjoy the view from the bright winter garden. The boutique hotel has comfortable guest rooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14254;Vinophil;Germany;Gaggenau;Max-Roth-Straße 16, Gaggenau, 76571, Germany;48.7875461;8.33773;32;false;true;Contemporary, Regional Cuisine;The name is a clue to the fact that wine plays a major role here. The restaurant with its pleasantly informal atmosphere also has a Vinothek. You can look forward to sound wine advice to help you find the right pairing for the delicious modern dishes with a regional touch. Interesting cocktails are also available.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14255;Genusswerkstatt Lodner;Germany;Lauingen;Imhofstraße 6, Lauingen, 89415, Germany;48.5702318;10.4313508;79;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Creative;You'll find this chic restaurant in the Hotel Lodner, a building that is a good 500 years old. Beneath the fine cross vault, they offer ambitious cuisine in the evening in set menu form or à la carte. At lunchtime, there is a simpler menu. Produce from their own spice manufactory is seamlessly incorporated. Friendly and well trained service. Specialities to take away in the adjoining delicatessen.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14256;PUR;Germany;Lütjenburg;Neuwerkstraße 9, Lütjenburg, 24321, Germany;54.29379;10.5880712;69;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;This pleasant, minimalist-style little bistro near the town centre serves seasonal cuisine with a penchant for regional produce – every effort is made to ensure that the ingredients are of the highest quality. In summer, make a beeline for the terrace in the garden at the rear of the building. They also sell their own house-made sauces, fruit spreads, ready meals in jars and the like.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14257;Brauereigasthof Aying;Germany;Aying;Zornedinger Straße 2, Aying, 85653, Germany;47.9707646;11.7805504;87;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;The restaurant is part of the picture-perfect Brauereigasthof Hotel Aying is a family-run establishment steeped in tradition and now run by the seventh generation. Diners are treated to warm hospitality in an upscale yet cosy setting. The terrace to the rear of the building is delightful in summer. The menu features exquisite regional and seasonal dishes, crafted from carefully selected produce of the highest quality – the restaurant has its own herd of Pinzgau beef cattle, as well as a hunter, who provides the game. In addition to the selection of fine wines, there are of course Ayinger beer specialities. Good event facilities. Comfortable and tastefully decorated guestrooms available for overnight stays.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14258;Gasthof Widmann;Germany;Maisach;Bergstraße 4, Maisach, 82216, Germany;48.2423572;11.2739916;41;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;You can clearly taste the enthusiasm that goes into preparing the food here. Seasonal and international dishes are served alongside regional fare, in a six-course set menu. A friendly front-of-house team presides over the two cosy dining rooms. Wed. - Sat. you are welcome from 6 pm.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted;[]
14259;Die Klosterschänke;Germany;Baden-Baden;Klosterschänke 1, Baden-Baden, 76530, Germany;48.7452103;8.1978966;78;true;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;Idyllically set a few kilometres from the city centre, this warm and welcoming family-run restaurant boasts a magnificent terrace affording splendid views of the Rhine plain. The chef cooks up regional and seasonal cuisine along with a selection of Italian dishes. The mouthwatering options include a classic cordon bleu with Black Forest ham and Alpine cheese, and saltimbocca alla romana from the chef's homeland.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14260;Mine;Germany;Berlin;Meinekestraße 10, Berlin, 10719, Germany;52.5007603;13.3286263;23;true;true;Italian, Contemporary;Very close to Ku'damm, this chic and laid-back establishment is run by a family that already has restaurants in St Petersburg and Moscow. The premises actually used to be home to Berlin's smallest bar. A charming pavement terrace beckons in front of the restaurant. Their Italian cuisine (including classics such as vitello tonnato or pasta) also draws on international and seasonal influences. Opt for the "Greatest Hits" set menu (two or more people) for a tempting selection of dishes. Nicely curated wine list. The wine cellar can also be booked for private dinners or chef's table events.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14261;Appare;Germany;Cologne;Balduinstraße 10, Cologne, 50676, Germany;50.9344748;6.9414601;86;true;false;Japanese, Traditional Cuisine;Here, traditional Japanese food – washoku – is skilfully combined with modern influences, blending Far Eastern spices and cooking methods with European food. There is a short lunch menu and a more elaborate dinner menu. In Japanese "appare" is an exclamation of enthusiasm.;;[]
14262;Schlosskeller;Germany;Aerzen;Schwöbber 9, Aerzen, 31855, Germany;52.0694668;9.251853;62;true;true;Farm to table, International;When it comes to the setting, the lovingly decorated vaulted cellar is really cosy, and the terrace by the castle pond is fantastic! The seasonal cuisine is in a regional vein, ranging from classic Wiener schnitzel to roasted fillet of sea bass with a rosehip foam. They are also open at lunchtime, which is excellent news.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14263;Le Comptoir;Germany;Saarbrücken;Försterstraße 15, Saarbrücken, 66111, Germany;49.2359075;6.9989004;21;true;true;Creative, Farm to table;Located in the Nauwieser Viertel, this restaurant is housed in an old sandstone and brick building, incidentally the birthplace of director Max Ophüls. An attractive modern interior and a friendly atmosphere await you here. The seats at the counter ("le comptoir" in French – hence the name of this establishment) are very popular. In the evenings, a modern seasonal set menu comprising four or five courses is served.;Counter dining;[]
14264;DAS GOLDSTEIN BY GOLLNER'S;Germany;Wiesbaden;Goldsteintal 50, Wiesbaden, 65207, Germany;50.1174633;8.255769;27;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;It's quite unexpected to come across such a chic restaurant in a remote wooded area like this. But the journey is absolutely worth making. Set in the former rifle club house about 5km from the city centre, this establishment boasts a tastefully sleek and upscale interior. It serves freshly prepared, predominantly Austrian cuisine, but the menu also features international dishes, some with Asian influences. The walk-in wine cellar and extensive wine list are a draw in themselves.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14265;The Sakai;Germany;Frankfurt on the Main;Hedderichstraße 69, Frankfurt on the Main, 60596, Germany;50.0983;8.6823;35;false;true;Japanese Contemporary, European;With Hiroshi Sakai at the helm here, you're in the hands of a real sushi master. This basement restaurant is done out in authentic Japanese style: sleek and minimalist. From the seats at the counter, you can watch the food being prepared. They serve an omakase menu, which also comes in a vegan version. The service comes courtesy of a very friendly and professional front-of-house team. Great sake selection.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
14266;Fine Dining by Phillip Probst;Germany;Bremerhaven;Columbusstraße 67, Bremerhaven, 27568, Germany;53.5461882;8.5738941;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Located in The Liberty hotel, this is a tastefully modern fine dining restaurant with floor-to-ceiling windows affording a view of the small harbour. There is also a gorgeous terrace. Four evenings a week, chef Phillip Probst and his team use excellent ingredients to create an interesting set menu comprising four to eight courses. The dishes are modern, yet classical in their foundations – the wonderfully intense sauces deserve a mention. The fjord trout served lukewarm with cauliflower, caviar and a brown butter sauce, for example, is a highlight. The well-drilled front-of-house team are friendly and attentive – they really pull out all the stops!;Air conditioning;[]
14267;Regional;Germany;Freiburg im Breisgau;St.-Erentrudis-Straße 12, Freiburg im Breisgau, 79112, Germany;47.9688739;7.6987756;29;false;false;Regional Cuisine;After being refurbished and rejuvenated, Regional has moved into the former Herrehus of Schloss Reinach. The name says it all: to create their tasty, punchy dishes, almost exclusively Baden and Black Forest produce is used, and the majority of it is also organic. It's a joy to sit on the patio terrace!;Brunch,Car park,Terrace;[]
14268;Das Bootshaus;Germany;Bingen am Rhein;Hafenstraße 47a, Bingen am Rhein, 55411, Germany;49.970363;7.91207;60;true;true;Contemporary, Farm to table;The restaurant of the Papa Rhein lifestyle hotel combines a tasteful maritime vintage look with good, fresh cuisine, offering dishes such as cod in a potato crust with balsamic mixed vegetables and lentils and pesto. There is a wonderful view of the Rhine and the surrounding vineyards – in summer guests can enjoy sitting out on the delightful terrace!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14270;Der Dantler;Germany;Munich;Werinherstraße 15, Munich, 81541, Germany;48.1153822;11.5829932;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;A tip to start with: reserve well in advance! Given the great value for money and the relaxed atmosphere, it's no surprise that they tend to get booked up. They call themselves the "Bavarian Deli". In the interior done out in a slick Alpine/country-style style, the service is personable and relaxed. At lunchtime you can order pasta, a pastrami sandwich, ramen or the fish dish of the day à la carte, or the three-course "business lunch". In the evening, creative modern cuisine is served in the form of a set menu – a vegetarian or pescetarian version is also available (request this when you book). On Thursdays and Fridays, the wine bar next door serves as a pop-up location.;;[]
14271;Lamm;Germany;Maselheim;Baltringer Straße 14, Maselheim, 88437, Germany;48.1534478;9.8699692;51;true;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;The impeccable façade is inviting for a start. Cross the threshold and an exceedingly friendly welcome awaits you. Take a seat in the charming dining area, where you will eat extremely well! The chef's cooking is classic, pared back and made with select seasonal ingredients. There is a choice of à la carte dishes and a set menu, which is also available in a vegetarian version.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14272;Lockstein 1;Germany;Berchtesgaden;Locksteinstraße 1, Berchtesgaden, 83471, Germany;47.6370931;13.0061278;52;true;false;Vegetarian, Farm to table;This really is a special place: you enter the charming kitchen through the 500-year-old farmhouse, which is run by an established mother-and-daughter team. They inject love and skill into their cooking, which takes the form of a vegetarian set menu comprising fresh dishes made using regional produce. The two pretty holiday flats are also popular.;Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14273;Fleur de Sel;Germany;Maintal;Florscheidstraße 19, Maintal, 63477, Germany;50.1354702;8.8330512;47;false;false;Classic French, Farm to table;This restaurant in a residential area in Maintal-Dörnigheim brings a slice of France to the Rhine-Main area. You can look forward to experiencing French-Mediterranean flair, both in terms of the feel of the place and Patrick Theumer's seasonally influenced cuisine. The three set menus, one of which is vegetarian, are particularly appealing. Friendly service. It is also pleasant to dine on the beautifully verdant terrace.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14274;Schwitzer's PUR;Germany;Waldbronn;Etzenroter Straße 4, Waldbronn, 76337, Germany;48.9206899;8.4754317;76;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, International;There have been some developments at Schwitzer's. In the newly refurbished rooms of the former fine dining restaurant with floor-to-ceiling windows affording views of the park grounds, diners are invited to embark on a culinary adventure that takes its cue from the seasons. Depending on the time of year, varying styles of cuisine are proposed – à la carte or as a three-course surprise set menu. Schwitzer's Hotel am Park has upscale guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14275;Gasthaus Assenmacher;Germany;Altenahr;Brückenstraße 12, Altenahr, 53505, Germany;50.5168466;6.991215;84;false;false;International;It's clear that Christian and Christa Storch put their heart and soul into running this place. The chef-patron wins over diners with his modern take on classic cuisine. Eschewing any gimmickry, he lays the focus squarely on quality produce and flavour. The lady of the house manages the friendly and attentive waitstaff. Pleasant little terrace to the rear of the building. Decent accommodation options at the hotel.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14277;Abt- und Schäferstube;Germany;Amorbach;Schafhof 1, Amorbach, 63916, Germany;49.6400568;9.1951067;31;true;true;Classic French, Farm to table;This restaurant is housed in a centuries-old monastery manor set in lovely, peaceful countryside. The food is classical with seasonal influences – the house speciality is lamb – and can be enjoyed in the historical, rustic-style interior or on the pleasant terrace overlooking the Odenwald. The very well-stocked vaulted wine cellar dating from 1524 is also worth seeing. Well-kept guestrooms in Der Schafhof hotel.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14278;Papageno zur Schweizer Grenze;Germany;Constance;Gottlieber Straße 64, Constance, 78462, Germany;47.6633136;9.1606485;23;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;A stone's throw away from the small border crossing at Tägerwilen, Patrick Stier (previously of Papageno at the old location) serves up classic cuisine with Mediterranean influences. Cosy interior with wood panelling and modern details. The vine-clad terrace beneath the pergola is delightful.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14279;Trichards;Germany;Munich;Reitmorstraße 21, Munich, 80538, Germany;48.1405196;11.5925859;31;false;false;Classic French, Seasonal Cuisine;This chic and modern restaurant-cum-wine bar is located in Munich's Lehel neighbourhood. The owner comes from France, which is reflected in the cooking style. Tip: The "Bouillabaisse-style noble fish and gamba with rouille" is a year-round speciality. The seasonal dishes can be accompanied by your choice from the comprehensive wine list. Ideal for those who like to eat al fresco – the terrace and garden are covered and as such protected from the elements.;Terrace;[]
14280;Wildfrisch Gutsküche;Germany;Wolfsburg;Schulenburgstraße 16, Wolfsburg, 38446, Germany;52.3995693;10.8282308;30;true;true;Regional Cuisine, Country cooking;Situated in the former gatehouse of the Schulenburg family manor house just outside Wolfsburg, this modern restaurant is simple yet elegant, with a completely open kitchen acting as the focal point in the dining room. The cuisine here is uncomplicated and seasonal, with an emphasis on regional products.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14282;Luis Dias - Das Restaurant;Germany;Cologne;Wilhelmstr. 35a, Cologne, 50996, Germany;50.8937031;6.9919154;68;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Luis Dias, who gave the restaurant his name, cooks flavoursome Mediterranean dishes, and quality ingredients are par for the course in his kitchen. In the pleasant and exceedingly elegant space, he serves dishes such as "sea bass, gnocchi fritto, spinach, lobster foam". The three-course lunch set menu is reasonably priced. There is also a small shop where you can buy spices – the menu tells you which spice is used in which dish. Tip for motorists: parking available at Parkhaus Maternusplatz.;Terrace;[]
14283;Valentin;Germany;Lindau;In der Grub 28A, Lindau, 88131, Germany;47.5473404;9.6847977;24;true;true;Contemporary, International;In a small side street in the island's old town, you will find this restaurant in a lovely vaulted cellar. In a stylish and modern setting, you can enjoy seasonal cuisine made with fresh, locally sourced ingredients. Opt for a set menu comprising four or seven courses, or choose from the small à la carte selection. At lunchtime, the options are more limited. Friendly front-of-house team. The secluded terrace in the courtyard is a pleasant spot. There is also a wine bar.;Terrace;[]
14285;Schranners Waldhorn;Germany;Tübingen;Schönbuchstraße 49, Tübingen, 72074, Germany;48.5606015;9.0625281;41;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Maximilian and Marie-Luise Schranner's establishment is a haven of comfort and calm. They have lovingly transformed this traditional inn with a tasteful interior design concept. At the helm, Maximilian Schranner specialises in classic cuisine and proposes three set menus: the "Menü Gourmet", the "Menü vegetarisch" and the "Wirthaus-Menü" – but you can also order dishes from these à la carte. There is also a very reasonably priced set menu at lunchtime. On warm days, the gorgeous terrace on the Seebach with its views of the castle is a particular highlight.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14286;Bistro;Germany;Aachen;Monheimsallee 52, Aachen, 52062, Germany;50.7813724;6.0908623;71;true;false;Classic French, Mediterranean Cuisine;Bistro is housed in Parkhotel Quellenhof, the flagship of Aachen's hotel scene – the marble lobby and the fireplace and tearoom with its exquisite wood panelling are well worth seeing. Classic cuisine with Mediterranean influences is served in a stylish, minimalist-style dining space. The appealing evening menu features dishes such as Black Angus beef tartare with brioche, lobster foam soup with lobster ravioli and tarragon, and Wiener schnitzel with potato and cucumber salad, as well as vegetarian options. There is a smaller selection of dishes available at lunchtime and a snack menu in the afternoon. The terrace overlooking the park is a delightful spot.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14287;Gocklwirt;Germany;Stephanskirchen;Weinbergstraße 9, Stephanskirchen, 83071, Germany;47.8591966;12.2043484;69;true;false;Home Cooking, International;What is it that draws regulars and day trippers here in equal numbers? The richly decorated rooms are wonderfully rustic and the remarkable collection of farm machinery is well worth seeing. Classic international as well as regional cuisine, from spicy salmon tartare to "Böfflamott" (beef in red wine) to the four-course set menu. Double guestroom in the house next door, should you wish to stay over.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14288;CLYNe - Das Restaurant;Germany;Speyer;Große Greifengasse 5, Speyer, 67346, Germany;49.3183951;8.434615;94;true;true;Country cooking, Regional Cuisine;On the edge of the old town and just a stone's throw from the pedestrian area is this cosy restaurant run with a personal touch. The name "CLYNe" (a play on the German word "klein") refers to the small number of seats – it is advisable to book. The seasonal cuisine draws on regional produce to create dishes bursting with flavour. There are three set menus: "Menü vom Land" (meat), "Menü aus dem Wasser" (fish) and "Menü nich' Fisch, nich' Fleisch" (vegetarian).;Credit cards not accepted;[]
14289;Lazarus Stube im Oberschwäbischen Hof;Germany;Schwendi;Hauptstraße 9, Schwendi, 88477, Germany;48.1759407;9.975697;30;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;Do you fancy some really tasty seasonal regional cuisine, including classics such as Zwiebelrostbraten (fried beef and onions in gravy) or house-made Maultaschen (Swabian dumplings)? Here at Lazarus Stube, good, fresh, often locally sourced ingredients go into appealing à la carte dishes and specials that change with the seasons. Friendly, attentive service. For more ambitious cooking, look to the tasting menu (vegetarian or omnivore) of the second restaurant, Esszimmer. The excellent, wide-ranging selection of wines is the same in both establishments. Modern and functional guestrooms available next door at Oberschwäbischer Hof.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14290;Pure Wine & Food;Germany;Munich;Neureutherstraße 15, Munich, 80799, Germany;48.1546335;11.5724335;88;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Farm to table;The atmosphere here is pleasingly laid-back and trendy – in summer, the lovely terrace in front of the building gives you that holiday feeling. Using the freshest ingredients, the kitchen team serves up pared-back, modern Mediterranean cuisine. Diners choose between the "Chef's Choice" set menu, a vegetarian set menu and à la carte dishes. Given the restaurant's name, it is no surprise that wine plays an important role. The friendly and adept waitstaff will gladly recommend a suitable pairing for any dish. The terrific wine list comprises over 250 (organic) labels – also available to take away. Tip: Book a wine tasting.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14291;Gutshaus Kubbelkow;Germany;Klein Kubbelkow;Im Dorfe 8, Klein Kubbelkow, 18528, Germany;54.4046211;13.3818576;80;true;true;International;With its smart façade and stylish dining rooms, this listed manor house set in wonderfully peaceful grounds has lost nothing of its 1908 charm. It serves fresh, ambitious cuisine including lagoon-fished zander with jellied bouillabaisse broth and pan-fried asparagus. The idyllic location makes the tasteful upmarket guestrooms dotted with antique furniture all the more inviting, as does the excellent breakfast.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14292;Rolin;Germany;Pinneberg;Fahltskamp 48, Pinneberg, 25421, Germany;53.6579397;9.8069029;36;false;false;International, Classic Cuisine;Elegant ambience, friendly service, tasty and ambitious international, classic and seasonal cuisine – on the menu e. g. fillet of North Sea cod with a horseradish, honey and rosemary crust. Incidentally, "Rolin" is the name of a ship's captain. Hotel Cap Polonio has well-kept rooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14293;Hackbarth's Restaurant;Germany;Oberhausen;Im Lipperfeld 44, Oberhausen, 46047, Germany;51.4870236;6.8673137;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Behind its red front door, this restaurant has a trendy, chic interior. A welcoming and attentive service team also awaits you. The modern cuisine combines local and international elements, Mediterranean and Far Eastern influences, and an emphasis on seasonal produce. Options are slightly more limited at lunchtime, but in the evening there is an additional six-course set menu. Nicely curated wine list. Lovely terrace. Tip: It is advisable to make a reservation for the weekend (Fri and Sat).;Car park,Terrace;[]
14294;DAS BERNHARDS;Germany;Oberaudorf;Marienplatz 2, Oberaudorf, 83080, Germany;47.6474076;12.1737002;95;false;false;Farm to table;The very centrally located Bernhard family restaurant is inviting in its country-traditional style and attracts many regulars as well as tourists. Tip: Try the Swiss-inspired dishes – the owner is a native of the Grisons canton. The menu also includes delicious classics such as Café de Paris rump steak. It is exceptionally pleasant to dine on the terrace. Should you wish to stay overnight, there are well-kept guestrooms available here or at Seebacher Haus, the hotel under the same management.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14295;Zirbelstube;Germany;Nuremberg;Friedrich-Overbeck-Straße 1, Nuremberg, 90455, Germany;49.3730097;11.0989573;24;false;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;The journey to this friendly family-run establishment on the outskirts of Nuremberg is well worthwhile. Set in a smart sandstone building (1860), Zirbelstube boasts an attractive main dining space and a separate room with a vaulted ceiling. They serve good regional and seasonal cuisine with classical and international influences in the form of two set menus featuring dishes you can mix and match, such as pan-fried octopus with fennel and beans, labneh and olive tapenade, or Franconian Sauerbraten (marinated pot roast), red cabbage and cranberry salad, dried fruit and bread dumplings. Delightful terrace. Attractive guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14296;Hermannshöhle;Germany;Niederhausen;Hermannshöhle 1, Niederhausen, 55585, Germany;49.7910422;7.7646243;82;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Set in a former ferry house dating back to 1517, this establishment has been run by Wigbert Weck since 2007 and has a loyal following of regulars. The dishes created by the chef-patron are skillfully prepared from fresh ingredients with no unnecessary embellishments, and they are delicious! Tip: the surprise menu (only for the whole table). Complete with a glass-fronted wine refrigerator full of regional wines, the interior has the feel of a modern wine bar. Outside, the lovely terrace overlooks the Nahe River, which is just across the road. Two holiday flats can be booked for overnight stays.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14297;Am Kamin;Germany;Neumünster;Propstenstraße 13, Neumünster, 24534, Germany;54.0677653;9.9864595;100;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;The atmosphere in this lovingly decorated restaurant is charming and welcoming. Over the service counter you can take a look into the partly open kitchen and watch chef-patron Karl Ress at work. He is a master of his craft and works meticulously to bring out the full flavour of his ingredients. The dishes on the menu are classical and seasonal – you can opt for the surprise menu or order à la carte.;;[]
14298;H'manns;Germany;Neuleiningen;Am Goldberg 2, Neuleiningen, 67271, Germany;49.5434241;8.1406129;87;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The Hegmanns run this genuinely charming restaurant that is a hit with diners. Only the best produce makes its way into the dishes, which are meticulously prepared to bring out the full flavour of the ingredients. You can opt for a set menu or order à la carte. On Thursdays, only tapas are served. Excellent wine list. Extremely friendly waitstaff. Tip: the chef's table is very close to the kitchen, but sheltered from the thick of the action.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14299;Jagstmühle;Germany;Mulfingen;Jagstmühlenweg 10, Mulfingen, 74673, Germany;49.3139977;9.8061246;78;false;true;Classic French, Farm to table;With its cosy yet elegant interior and charming terrace, the restaurant blends wonderfully into the picture-perfect scene of the estate, which stands against the romantic backdrop of the River Jagst. The light hues of the wood panelling, the tiled stove and pretty fabrics all contribute to the inviting atmosphere. The food draws on international influences, with subtle Asian touches here and there. Dine à la carte or opt for the set menu (omnivore or vegetarian). Alternatively, the pleasant Mühlenscheune serves regional cuisine. There are also lovely guestrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14301;Gaststube Zum Klosterbräu;Germany;Neuburg an der Donau;Kirchplatz 1, Neuburg an der Donau, 86633, Germany;48.7832727;11.1423405;93;false;false;Bavarian, Seasonal Cuisine;This is how you imagine a historical Bavarian restaurant: wooden beams on the ceiling, floorboards, tiled stove – rustic, inviting and wonderfully cosy (or "zünftig" as they say in these parts). There is also a wonderful terrace. The cuisine is classic, regional and seasonal – served à la carte or in three set menus, one of which is vegetarian. There is a good selection of wines to choose from. Tip: well-priced lunch menu with two or three courses (Tues. to Fri., except public holidays). You can also visit the Baroque Münster Heilig Kreuz in Bergen.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14302;Bavarie;Germany;Munich;Am Olympiapark 1, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1781547;11.556206;24;false;true;Farm to table, French;Regionality and sustainability are two principles that underpin Bavarie, here at BMW Welt. This translates into combining elements of Bavarian and French cuisine with a focus on high-quality produce. You can dine à la carte or take the set menu – there is also a vegan option, plus a three-course business lunch deal. The atmosphere in the spacious, airy, high-ceilinged room is pleasant. Nice terrace with a view of the Olympic Park and Tower.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14303;Garden-Restaurant;Germany;Munich;Promenadeplatz 2, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1402445;11.5735276;38;true;false;Contemporary, International;Belgian designer Axel Vervoordt has given this restaurant a very particular look. The industrial-style conservatory design creates a setting reminiscent of an artist’s studio.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14304;Novalis;Germany;Nörten-Hardenberg;Hinterhaus 11a, Nörten-Hardenberg, 37176, Germany;51.6286538;9.9492496;64;true;false;Classic Cuisine, International;Diners can opt to eat inside, in the stylish, elegant restaurant, or outside with a view of the historical castle grounds. The seasonal food is positively packed with flavours and aromas, and made with top-notch produce – regional wherever possible – such as game that they have hunted themselves or smoked fish from Leinetal. There is also a vegetarian set menu. The service is cordial and professional. Tip: The wine list comprises a broad selection of French red wines, alongside gin, korn schnapps, vodka and whiskey from the restaurant's own Hardenberg Distillery. "Novalis" comes from an ancestor of the owners – it is the pseudonym of writer Georg Philipp Friedrich Freiherr von Hardenberg. Hardenberg BurgHotel promises an overnight stay in tasteful accommodation.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14305;Kaisers Eck;Germany;Ahlbeck;Kaiserstraße 1, Ahlbeck, 17419, Germany;53.939882;14.189415;61;false;true;Regional European, Country cooking;Situated by Ahlbeck's main church, this cosy restaurant with its pleasantly down-to-earth atmosphere is run by a husband-and-wife team – she manages the waitstaff in her friendly and relaxed manner while he does the cooking. The cuisine is predominantly regional, and the "Lieblingsmenü" is a hit. However, there are plenty of other options that whet the appetite – the decision won't be easy.;Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14306;Klebers;Germany;Bad Saulgau;Poststraße 1, Bad Saulgau, 88348, Germany;48.0151409;9.5011325;38;true;false;International, Farm to table;Whether you are seated in the pleasantly bright interior or on the delightful terrace in summer, you can look forward to friendly and charming service as well as international and regional cuisine made from excellent produce. There are various set menus (including a vegetarian one) to choose from, plus a selection of dishes à la carte. The restaurant is housed in the tasteful Kleber Post hotel.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14307;Gengs Linde;Germany;Stühlingen;St.-Gallus-Straße 37, Stühlingen, 79780, Germany;47.7415054;8.3895602;66;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Christian Geng offers fresh and flavoursome cuisine that is traditional with international influences. His fashionable restaurant combines clean, modern lines with warm wood. Try the veal cordon bleu or the rack of lamb baked in a herb crust with peperonata and homemade gnocchi.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14308;Gasthof Schütte;Germany;Schmallenberg;Eggeweg 2, Schmallenberg, 57392, Germany;51.1583551;8.3735128;81;false;true;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This region, which is a popular destination for hiking and cycling enthusiasts, is home to this traditional family-run country hotel with its own spa facilities and lovely restaurant. There are regional, classic and international dishes on the menu, which is somewhat more limited at lunchtime. In winter, an open fireplace adds to the charming atmosphere.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14309;Zum Ochsen;Germany;Schönwald im Schwarzwald;Ludwig-Uhland-Straße 18, Schönwald im Schwarzwald, 78141, Germany;48.1018786;8.2062829;38;false;true;Country cooking;The atmosphere is really cosy in this restaurant, which is charmingly done out in the traditional style typical of the region. The kitchen serves up flavoursome, ambitious dishes with a regional and seasonal focus, as well as the occasional international twist. For overnight guests, this long-standing family-run establishment offers comfortable guestrooms and a spa with a range of facilities and treatments and a swimming pool.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14310;Gourmetrestaurant 1751;Germany;Schwerin;Schusterstraße 15, Schwerin, 19055, Germany;53.6279798;11.4138737;58;false;false;International, Mediterranean Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city, in a wine merchant's house that is over 250 years old, this restaurant is considered one of the finest in the region. A delightful historical setting, it boasts a beautifully restored barrel-vaulted ceiling. They serve a five- or seven-course set menu comprising dishes that are meticulously prepared using predominantly regional produce. The wine list includes a few rare finds! Tastefully designed guestrooms are available in the Weinhaus Uhle hotel.;Interesting wine list;[]
14311;Beesten;Germany;Rheine;Eichenstraße 3, Rheine, 48431, Germany;52.2828443;7.4282786;18;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Since 1906, over four generations, the Beesten family has put its heart and soul into running this traditional inn in the heart of Rheine. The owner himself is at the helm in the kitchen, preparing classic French and German cuisine peppered with seasonal influences. The interior is elegant and tasteful, while the service is charming. Take a seat on the terrace under the lovely old chestnut trees.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14312;Kreutzer's;Germany;Regensburg;Prinz-Ludwig-Straße 15a, Regensburg, 93055, Germany;49.0165603;12.1211883;82;false;true;International, Meats and Grills;Though the location on business premises in the Westhafen port is a little out of the way, this smart, modern restaurant is fashionable and popular. It serves business lunches in the middle of the day and delicious meat and fish from the charcoal grill in the evenings.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14313;Lumperhof;Germany;Ravensburg;Lumper 1, Ravensburg, 88212, Germany;47.772555;9.6299325;51;true;false;Country cooking, Farm to table;This family-run inn is a lovely spot in the countryside and has a charming terrace shaded by a majestic old lime tree. The menu is varied and full of delicious options. Made with regional and seasonal produce, the dishes draw on Mediterranean, Middle Eastern and Asian influences. Options such as the cream of sweetcorn soup with deep-fried mussels and purple curry, or the Allgäu cheese spaetzle with melted onions and a green salad are sure to whet the appetite. In the evening, you can dine à la carte or opt for a set menu comprising three or five courses. Cash payments only.;Car park,Cash only,Terrace;[]
14314;Sansibar;Germany;Rantum;Hörnumer Straße 80, Rantum, 25980, Germany;54.8144874;8.285324;22;false;true;International, Seasonal Cuisine;A restaurant with cult status! This smart beach cabin is a much sought-after place to eat. It takes five minutes to reach it on foot through the dunes – or you can use the shuttle service. Fancy a Sansibar classic such as rice pudding with red fruit jelly? Or perhaps you'd prefer something more sophisticated? Superb wine list. No reservations taken at lunchtime. There is a playground for children next to the restaurant.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14315;Schloss Monaise;Germany;Trier;Schloss Monaise 7, Trier, 54294, Germany;49.7172235;6.5998745;48;false;true;Classic French;With Hubert Scheid's cuisine, this place is nothing short of a culinary institution in the region. His signature style comprises pleasantly straightforward dishes made from excellent ingredients – served à la carte or as a set menu. The restaurant occupies stylish, high-ceilinged rooms that channel the stately flair of these premises dating back to 1783 – once a summer residence. Or you can dine on the wonderful terrace with a view of the surrounding nature and the Moselle. It's also worth taking a look at the wine list, which features many a big name.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14316;freistil.;Germany;Ofterschwang;Schweineberg 20, Ofterschwang, 87527, Germany;47.4953154;10.2595888;53;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;In addition to an appealing modern decor featuring sleek design and warm wooden fittings, diners can look forward to a selection of regional and seasonal dishes (including vegetarian and vegan options) that can be put together to create a set menu or ordered à la carte. For overnight stays, the boutique hotel has attractive, comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14317;Forsthaus Hessenstein;Germany;Panker;Hessenstein 1, Panker, 24321, Germany;54.328214;10.546505;99;true;true;Farm to table, Country cooking;Once a forester's lodge, this restaurant in a stunning location is very popular on account of the cosy and charming dining area, friendly service and, last but not least, the good cuisine, in the form of classics such as Wiener schnitzel, Zwiebelrostbraten or crème brûlée. Tip: It is worth taking the time to climb the lookout tower. In addition, the many tracks all around are conducive to walks in the surrounding countryside.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14318;Postschänke;Germany;Odenthal;Altenberger-Dom-Straße 23, Odenthal, 51519, Germany;51.0323821;7.1149717;85;true;false;Farm to table;With its cosy and lively atmosphere, Postschänke is a fantastic alternative to Zur Post, the fine-dining restaurant. Here, the delicious seasonal cuisine made with select, fresh ingredients goes down a treat. They serve a daily set menu with options, as well as daily specials. The service is exceedingly friendly and attentive.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14319;Sülbecker Krug;Germany;Nienstädt;Mindener Straße 6, Nienstädt, 31688, Germany;52.2889268;9.1520453;36;false;false;Meats and Grills, International;If you fancy prime beef cooked in an oven heated to 800°C, then this restaurant renowned for its meat is a good choice. The menu includes classics such as rib-eye, rump or flank steak served on a wooden board with superb sauces. They also have a wine bar. Various promotions are also offered throughout the year – don't hesitate to enquire!;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
14320;Kaiserblick;Germany;Nideggen;Kirchgasse 10 a, Nideggen, 52385, Germany;50.6892515;6.4797331;45;false;true;Farm to table;This eatery is a good alternative to the Brockel Schlimbach restaurant at Nideggen's centuries-old castle, Burg Nideggen. They serve market-based cuisine in the form of regional dishes, prepared from fresh seasonal ingredients mainly sourced from suppliers and producers in the region. The interior decor is modern and the front-of-house team is very friendly and obliging. Weather permitting, you can dine on the pretty terrace in the castle courtyard.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14321;Spinne;Germany;Neustadt an der Weinstraße;Eichkehle 58, Neustadt an der Weinstraße, 67433, Germany;49.3715256;8.1425625;90;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;This restaurant situated on the forest's edge sticks to a simple winning formula, with a focus on regional and seasonal cuisine prepared using the finest ingredients. Perhaps you'd like to try the surprise menu? Take a seat out on the lovely terrace. Welcoming and modern guestrooms for an overnight stay.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14322;Das Esszimmer;Germany;Neustadt an der Weinstraße;Hintergasse 38, Neustadt an der Weinstraße, 67433, Germany;49.3550637;8.1381553;59;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A lovely restaurant in the Old Town: the welcoming, sleek and modern setting is bound to appeal, and the atmosphere is pleasantly intimate, the service is attentive and well trained. You can watch Italian/Mediterranean dishes being prepared in the open kitchen. Look out for the "speciality days". On Thursdays: tasting menu only. The terrace in front of the house is also a pleasant place to sit.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14323;Spitzweg;Germany;Neuss;Glockhammer 43a, Neuss, 41460, Germany;51.2000702;6.6928002;67;false;false;Farm to table, International;This place has been serving up consistently good food for years – there's a reason why it attracts so many regulars. On the menu: seasonal, regional and international dishes. The sleek, modern decor boasting a bold red colour scheme and paintings on the walls is stylish. Friendly and professional service. The lively terrace set up on the pavement is a lovely place to sit. There is also an annexe for private events.;Terrace;[]
14324;Ostaria da Gino;Germany;Nagold;Querstraße 3, Nagold, 72202, Germany;48.5509829;8.7254793;29;true;true;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;This delightful family-run restaurant's enduring popularity among regulars is a testament to the unwavering dedication and passion that have been poured into its operations for the past 40 years. Authentic Italian cuisine is served in a laid-back setting with bags of charm! Staff will be happy to guide you through the options written up on the board and recommend the right wine. Tip: the moderately priced lunch deal. Delicatessen goods can be purchased to take home.;Terrace;[]
14325;Gute Stube im Parkhotel;Germany;Herne;Schäferstraße 109, Herne, 44623, Germany;51.5439598;7.2355292;16;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The modern and elegant restaurant complete with conservatory and roof terrace is housed in a pretty palace building near Herne's Stadtgarten. The contemporary cuisine takes the form of seasonal set menus and à la carte dishes, including vegetarian options. The chefs try to use regional produce as much as possible. Friendly service. For a simpler alternative in the evening, head to Das Stübchen for classic fare or to the beer garden. Parkhotel offers cosy guestrooms. Tip: Enjoy a short walk through the beautiful Stadtgarten. A longer route takes you to the debris field of the (closed) Mont Cenis colliery – right next to it is the viewing platform at the Mont Cenis Academy, which affords fantastic views.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14326;Vinaiolo;Germany;Munich;Steinstraße 42, Munich, 81667, Germany;48.1312236;11.5960025;23;true;false;Italian;Even after more than 25 years since its opening, Vinaiolo continues to bring a delightful taste of la dolce vita to Haidhausen. Attentive service comes courtesy of a charming, well-drilled team, embodying a spirit that is tipicamente italiano. Although the Italian cuisine served here is not focused on any particular region, it is unfailingly authentic. Mouthwatering options such as the Sardinian fregola with lamb ragout and the Nebrodi pork chop are testament to this. Excellent selection of Italian wines. The cosy, authentic atmosphere is accentuated by furnishings salvaged from a Trieste grocer's shop dating back to 1904!;;[]
14327;Käfer-Schänke;Germany;Munich;Prinzregentenstraße 73, Munich, 81675, Germany;48.1404683;11.6020537;41;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine;The name "Käfer" has become synonymous with Munich's gastronomy scene. The ace up the sleeve of this Munich institution: the restaurant and delicatessen being under one roof means you can be sure that you are dealing with top-drawer ingredients. These are used in classics such as beef tartare, lobster stew or roast duck for two, served in two courses. The atmosphere is cosy, the service professional and friendly. An additional feature is that they have a number of individually designed function rooms available for special occasions.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14328;Nymphenburger Hof;Germany;Munich;Nymphenburger Straße 24, Munich, 80335, Germany;48.1489563;11.5523732;29;true;true;International, Classic Cuisine;Steeped in tradition, this charming establishment is the epitome of a classic restaurant, both in terms of its decor and cuisine, which draws on regional, Austrian, Mediterranean and French influences. The long-serving chef hails from Styria, which explains why the wine list is exclusively dedicated to Austrian labels. Delightful secluded terrace.;Terrace;[]
14329;Culinarium;Germany;Nittel;Weinstraße 5, Nittel, 54453, Germany;49.6536225;6.443146;53;true;false;Farm to table;This chic, pared-back restaurant with a lovely terrace area is located in the Weingut Matthias Dostert, a winery that also offers cosy guestrooms. Chef Walter Curman draws on his considerable craftsmanship to meticulously create flavoursome dishes. The classics on the menu hint at his Austrian origins – try the appetising Kaspressknödel (pressed cheese dumplings) orAlt Wiener Kaiserschmarrn (Viennese pancake)!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14330;Brasserie Nodhausen;Germany;Neuwied;Nodhausen 1, Neuwied, 56567, Germany;50.4543977;7.4629197;60;false;false;Farm to table, French Contemporary;The brasserie at this charming historical property serves international, regional and seasonal cuisine. On the menu, you'll find mouth-watering options such as mascarpone ravioli with truffle and parmesan or saddle of venison with wild broccoli, pearl barley and celeriac cream. This appealing restaurant has the feel of a conservatory – large windows look out onto the beautiful grounds planted with old trees. Tip: Edible oils are available for purchase at the restaurant's own delicatessen – ideal for the home or as a little gift.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14331;Herzog von Burgund;Germany;Neuss;Erftstraße 88, Neuss, 41460, Germany;51.1963766;6.6903176;51;false;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;First you admire the attractive exterior of this stylish townhouse. Then, inside, the impressive, heritage-protected staircase. The two dining spaces (Erftzimmer and Gartenzimmer) form a classically elegant setting – the paintings by Düsseldorf artist Markus Tollmann draw the eye. The menu has a seasonal focus, and Wiener schnitzel is a house speciality. Friendly and experienced waitstaff. Delightful outdoor seating: The terrace is a verdant oasis in the heart of the city!;Terrace;[]
14332;Martinelli;Germany;Munich;Wilhelm-Dieß-Weg 2, Munich, 81927, Germany;48.156136;11.6369142;19;false;true;Italian, Italian Contemporary;If you’re looking for Italian hospitality and the food that goes with it, Martinelli offers seasonal, modern cuisine including dishes such as pecorino ravioli with walnut and balsamic vinegar or saddle of venison with quince. And to whet your appetite, there’s always a plate of air-dried ham and some delicious bread.;Terrace;[]
14333;Torkel;Germany;Nonnenhorn;Seehalde 14, Nonnenhorn, 88149, Germany;47.5755272;9.6114549;37;true;true;Farm to table;The Stoppel family serve not only cuisine underpinned by Mediterranean and classic influences, but also plenty of regional dishes. If you are having trouble choosing, a failsafe option is the short "Fine Dining Menü". It's also well worth perusing the wine list. Sit back and enjoy your meal in the inviting dining space or out on the pretty terrace. The hotel of the same name has lovely cosy guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14334;Rocca Riviera;Germany;Munich;Wittelsbacherplatz 2, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1438581;11.5758705;51;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Italian;A stone's throw from Odeonsplatz, this is a stylish and elegant restaurant with a retro-style bar as its focal point. The menu features Mediterranean cuisine for sharing, fantastic charcoal-grilled meat and fish options, as well as Italian classics and dishes that draw on North African and French influences. At lunchtime, options are more limited but include some items from the evening menu. In summer, the terrace on Wittelsbacherplatz beckons.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14336;Gasthof Ochsen;Germany;Müllheim;Bürgelnstraße 32, Müllheim, 79379, Germany;47.7726941;7.6434311;51;false;false;Country cooking;This welcoming inn that is run with great dedication has been in the family since it was founded in 1763. This place is really inviting with its charming dining areas, gorgeous terrace and courtyard. Taking its cue from the changing seasons and Baden culinary tradition, the menu includes specialities of the house such as saddle of veal and offal. Comfortable overnight accommodation available.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14337;Pfistermühle;Germany;Munich;Pfisterstraße 4, Munich, 80331, Germany;48.1379992;11.5799081;76;false;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Once a ducal mill dating from 1573, Pfistermühle delights diners with its stylish Bavarian setting (including a lovely vaulted ceiling). The "Pfistermühlen Brettl" lunchtime set menu (Mon-Fri) with its four small courses (including vegetarian options) is great value. Good location only a stone's throw from the famous Platzl.;Terrace;[]
14338;Kurlbaum;Germany;Moers;Burgstraße 7, Moers, 47441, Germany;51.4505954;6.6269259;22;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Farm to table;Michael Kurlbaum has run his restaurant with great dedication for 35 years. Spread over two floors, this place exudes a timeless elegance – in summer, a few additional tables are set up out front in the pedestrian zone. There are plenty of regulars who come for the classic cuisine. Lunch in the bistro area on the ground floor is popular too – they serve a moderately priced two-course set menu that changes weekly. This includes a bottle of water, and dessert is available as an optional extra. If you order in advance, you can also choose from the evening menu at lunchtime. Convenient for motorists: Kastell car park in Haagstraße close by.;Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14339;Stern's Restaurant;Germany;Bad Hersfeld;Linggplatz 11, Bad Hersfeld, 36251, Germany;50.8677434;9.7061864;87;true;true;Country cooking, International;Housed in the long-established Zum Stern hotel, this restaurant has a charming rustic feel with its wood panelling and lovely white tiled stove. The cuisine is regional but draws on international influences. There are two set menus to choose from (one of which is vegetarian), as well as an à la carte selection including barbecued steaks. The options are a little more limited at lunchtime.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14340;La Bohème;Germany;Munich;Leopoldstraße 180, Munich, 80804, Germany;48.173077;11.5866625;53;false;true;Meats and Grills, Seasonal Cuisine;A pleasingly convivial and relaxed place to eat. If you appreciate high-quality steak cuts, then this restaurant with a trendy urban atmosphere is just the ticket. But the menu also whets your appetite with a host of other dishes and delicious desserts. The sharing options (vegetarian versions available) will give you a good impression of the cuisine here. Popular brunch on Saturdays and Sundays. Tip for car drivers: Public car park ‘Schwabinger Tor’.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
14341;Brasserie Les Deux;Germany;Munich;Maffeistraße 3a, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.1393129;11.5746986;92;true;true;International, Contemporary;If you like a lively, modern bistro, you’ll enjoy the seasonal, international dishes (such as gnocchi with asparagus and black tiger prawns) served here on the ground floor of Les Deux. Alternatively, try one of the “old” or “new” classics such as mini burgers or beef tartare with imperial caviar.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14342;Le Stollberg;Germany;Munich;Stollbergstraße 2, Munich, 80539, Germany;48.13619;11.58263;69;false;false;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;This charming little restaurant is run with a very personal touch by chef-patron Anette Huber. She serves up good-quality, fresh cuisine that takes its cue from the seasons and draws on French and Mediterranean influences. The front-of-house team is friendly and well drilled, providing astute wine recommendations. Tip: The appealing lunch menu is great value for money! Plus light bites are served in the daytime bistro Le Petit Stollberg opposite.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14343;Altes Brauhaus;Germany;Heinsberg;Wurmstraße 4, Heinsberg, 52525, Germany;51.0731132;6.1248508;39;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;The date 1779 is marked above the entrance to Altes Brauhaus, a brewery where beer was never in fact brewed. Now it serves up a tasty mix of regional and classic dishes (including vegetarian options) prepared by chef Ute Weishaupt who runs this lovely old restaurant with her sister Elke. The elegant, traditional style dining rooms alone with their sumptuous wood panelling and ornate carving are worth a visit. Charming interior courtyard terrace.;Terrace;[]
14344;Altes Rathaus by What the Food;Germany;Winnenden;Marktstraße 47, Winnenden, 71364, Germany;48.8762127;9.3990693;77;false;false;Creative, Farm to table;A truly delightful example of casual, down-to-earth dining that brings pleasure and joy! This restaurant is housed in a picturesque half-timbered house in the pedestrian area. The interior is modern and minimalist, and outside there is a charming terrace overlooking the forecourt. Chef-patron Patrick Schubert cooks up dishes that are creative and full of flavour – opt for his ambitious signature set menu ("Da kommsch rum") or choose from the somewhat simpler à la carte selection. Options are more limited at lunchtime. Friendly and competent service comes courtesy of maître d' Anne Henrichs. Good to know: they have a food truck that can be booked for special occasions.;Terrace;[]
14345;sushi Lounge;Germany;Mainz;Karl-Weiser-Straße 1, Mainz, 55131, Germany;49.9899484;8.2895679;49;true;true;Sushi;The latest culinary hotspot at FAVORITE Parkhotel is a restaurant within a restaurant! Sushi lounge is located inside the hotel's Weinbar. Only sushi and sashimi are on the menu in this compact space, and everything is made with the finest produce – something for which FAVORITE Restaurant also has a reputation. Must-try nigiri: otoro for melt-in-your-mouth richness, scallops for pristine freshness or unagi for bold umami.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
14346;Müllers auf Norderney;Germany;Norderney;Am Weststrand 3, Norderney, 26548, Germany;53.70299;7.14138;43;true;false;Contemporary, Fusion;Affording unobstructed views of the sea, 1884's exclusive location alone is a major draw. The charming little boutique hotel is a spa-style building complex composed of Villa Mathilde and the adjoining Villa Olga. It is also home to a chic restaurant with modern and minimalist interior design and a fabulous terrace. In the kitchen, Nelson Müller's team prepares flavoursome and pleasingly uncomplicated dishes from fresh, good-quality ingredients. Soul food would be an apt label for this cuisine.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14347;Pageou;Germany;Munich;Kardinal-Faulhaber-Straße 10, Munich, 80333, Germany;48.140755;11.5746251;65;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Located in the CityQuartier Fünf Höfe shopping centre, the chic restaurant of renowned TV chef Ali Güngörmüs is named after his hometown in the Turkish province of Tunceli. Here, his team serves Middle Eastern cuisine that draws on classic French influences and is available as a four-course vegetarian "Levante Menu" and as a five- or six-course "Chef Menu". A starter dubbed "Meze", for example, is a great option comprising various small dishes. A number of noteworthy Turkish labels are included in the extensive wine list. The lovely sheltered terrace is delightful on summer days.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
14348;Schorn;Germany;Düsseldorf;Martinstraße 46a, Düsseldorf, 40223, Germany;51.208618;6.7636413;42;false;false;Contemporary;With Franz-Josef Schorn as maitre d' and Lukas Schild as chef, this restaurant in the Bilk neighbourhood boasts two big names in the Düsseldorf fine dining scene. Ambitious and flavourful dishes such as braised tri-tip of Wagyu beef from the Eifel region, with a balsamic jus, mashed potatoes, Brussels sprouts and watercress are served as part of the set menu and à la carte. The appealing wine list comprises mostly German and French labels. Friendly service. The dining space has a charming, intimate feel, with decorative features including an old stove, a wine barrel serving as a digestif table and modern paintings.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14349;Müllers auf der Rü;Germany;Essen;Rüttenscheider Straße 62, Essen, 45130, Germany;51.4377929;7.005258;55;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Nelson Müller's fine dining restaurant, Schote, may have moved to Bergisch Gladbach, but this cherished Essen-based establishment at Rüttenscheider Stern U-Bahn station has stayed put. This is a market hall-style brasserie integrated into a shopping arcade. Sitting at high tables, diners tuck into delicious dishes ranging from currywurst to turbot, prepared in the centrally positioned open kitchen. Friendly service. Tip for motorists: public multi-storey car park around the corner.;Terrace;[]
14350;Hirsch;Germany;Kehl;Gerbereistraße 20, Kehl, 77694, Germany;48.569164;7.8740597;44;true;false;Country cooking, International;This upscale restaurant serves classic cuisine that draws on Baden's culinary tradition and is made predominantly with regional ingredients. Options such as braised veal cheeks or a tasty fish medley in beurre blanc are sure to whet the appetite. Abundant wood and decorative features provide a cosy backdrop. In summer, head for the lovely verdant terrace. Very friendly service. Given the proximity to Strasbourg, the Black Forest and Europa-Park, it is also worth considering staying in one of Hirsch's well-kept guestrooms or apartments.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14351;Der Kaiserhof;Germany;Guldental;Hauptstraße 4, Guldental, 55452, Germany;49.8913984;7.844836;78;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Run by the same family for four generations, Kaiserhof hides a surprisingly chic and fresh interior behind its deceptively traditional façade. The tastefully designed dining space is accessed via the open kitchen – diners can also watch the chefs at work. A seasonal menu comprising seven courses is proposed. The chefs are involved in serving and talk you through the dishes. In summer, head for the terrace in the small courtyard. There are well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14352;Benders;Germany;Birkenfeld;Silcherstraße 1, Birkenfeld, 75217, Germany;48.8710277;8.6400613;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This remarkably chic and modern restaurant is housed in the pretty half-timbered building of the long-established Birkenfelder Hof. It is an ideal setting for casual dining, which is the name of the game here. The atmosphere is also suitably relaxed, and the waitstaff are experienced and friendly. The ambitious modern cuisine draws on French, Mediterranean and regional influences, and incorporates the odd Asian touch. The menu includes dishes such as Kikok rooster breast with a Madeira jus, pumpkin curry cream and pak choi, plus classics such as roast beef or burgers (only on certain days). Smart guestrooms available for overnight stays.;;[]
14353;DAS MAXI - GENUSSREICH;Germany;Oberstdorf;Freibergstraße 21, Oberstdorf, 87561, Germany;47.4053349;10.2707141;80;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, International;Das Maxi has proven to be a successful addition to Das Freiberg hotel and is an appealing dining option – and not only for hotel guests. The kitchen specialises in contemporary, mostly Mediterranean dishes with seasonal influences. In addition to the set menu, which changes daily, there is also a small à la carte selection. Food is served in tastefully designed dining areas, and there is additional garden seating available for the summer months. The wine list, featuring international labels, is second to none. The gorgeous guestrooms have magnificent views of the mountains.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14354;La Citadelle;France;Châteaubriant;9 place de la Motte, Châteaubriant, 44110, France;47.7179537;-1.3774407;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant occupies a prime position in the heart of this medieval town packed with old stone buildings and half-timbered houses. Chef Maxime, a local, and his wife Patricia, who hails from Lima, have created a delightful space in which you can sit back and lap up their hospitality. The dishes are made with fresh ingredients treated respectfully so as to bring out their intrinsic flavours, and are sometimes spiced up with a few South American touches (ceviche with tigre de leche, coconut milk etc) and dishes to share (platters of cold meats or cheeses), in a nod to Patricia's Peruvian origins.;;[]
14356;Au Marquis de Terme;France;Margaux;3 route de Rauzan, Margaux, 33460, France;45.0385925;-0.6774396;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Surrounded by the Médoc vineyards, this contemporary restaurant is nestled in an outbuilding of the Château Marquis de Terme (a Grand Cru classified in 1855). It boasts a terrace that opens out onto the estate's pretty garden courtyard. Under the stewardship of Grégory Coutanceau, who devised the menu, chef Thibaud Guena welcomes his guests with fresh, modern cuisine that is very much of its time and shuns unnecessary frills. The appealing wine list features almost 600 labels, including a selection of Bordeaux reds and prestige wines available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14357;Partage;France;Andlau;19 rue du Docteur-Stoltz, Andlau, 67140, France;48.3871065;7.4168166;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Julie and Hugo first met at Lameloise, later setting up shop in the house where Alexis Kreyder (1839-1912) – renowned for his still-life paintings of flowers and fruit – was born. The location, a traditional half-timbered inn painted pomegranate red on the outside and done out in contemporary style inside, wins diners over. As for the food, the talented chef creates nicely fragrant and balanced dishes that taste as good as they look, for example marinated and subtly smoked sea bream, bibalakas-style cream with herbs and beetroot shavings.;Terrace;[]
14358;Penati al Baretto;France;Paris;94 boulevard de la Tour-Maubourg, Paris, 75007, France;48.8542331;2.30954;31;false;true;Italian;It is no secret that Italians have great taste. Milanese chef Alberico Penati has set up shop in this chic bistro with honey-coloured wood panelling, and bay windows overlooking the garden of the Invalides – a highly prized location indeed! Tradition is the chef's passion. With no concessions to passing fashions, his menu features a selection of Italian classics made out of carefully selected ingredients. Home-made pasta remains the forte of this place, eg ravioli del plin piemontesi with a very good roast beef jus. The 100% Italian wine list highlights Piedmontese wines, particularly Barolo and Barbaresco.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14359;Akabeko;France;Paris;40 rue de l'Université, Paris, 75007, France;48.8575543;2.3282805;56;false;false;Fusion;This restaurant, which is home to Japanese chef Yasuo Nanaumi, who trained in star establishments, sports a ground-floor space with just a counter and a more upmarket, romantic dining room upstairs. At lunch and dinner, the chef crafts a surprise omakase (which literally means “I leave it up to you”) menu, reflecting his Japanese culture and his passion for French gastronomy, depicted by dishes such as foie gras with teriyaki sauce or sole goujonnettes with dashi. The entire team bends over backwards to ensure the wellbeing of their diners.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
14360;La Grange de Pépé;France;Vignieu;Domaine de Suzel, 267 route de Suzel, Vignieu, 38890, France;45.6344776;5.4335195;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;In the peaceful northern Isère countryside, a family has revived the farming estate of its forebears and turned it into a hotel resort. In a picturesque, revamped stone barn, guests are invited to sample dishes overflowing in flavour rustled up by Argentinian chef Agustín Mercado Murua and inspired by the seasons and the region (Dombes duckling, farm-reared veal and locally bred trout), as well as herbs and veggies from the kitchen garden. Lovely alfresco patio in fine weather.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14362;L'Atelier du Nord;France;Concarneau;Dock 2, Quai Carnot Bâtiment Ouest Criée, Concarneau, 29900, France;47.875222;-3.9149262;38;true;true;Fusion, Modern Cuisine;Res nostra mare (or "the sea is our law") is the motto featured on chef Romain Paillet's website and, indeed, his modern, Japanese-inspired cuisine relies solely on what the sea has to offer. The ingredients, such as tuna belly, are impeccably fresh. Thanks to well-balanced condiments and preparations, each plate has plenty of pep… as does the chef, who, passionate about what he does, spends a lot of time in the dining area mingling with his customers. In line with the chef's cooking, the decor has blue walls and more than the odd nod to Japan. The kitchen, literally in the centre of the space, is the beating heart of the restaurant.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14363;Flaveurs - Domaine Mont-Riant;France;Jurançon;1 avenue des Frères-Barthélémy, Jurançon, 64110, France;43.2838644;-0.4130548;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the Jurançon hillsides, this handsome 19C white mansion with a slate roof and set in wooded grounds is enjoying a new lease of life in the hands of a locally-born couple, Basque chef Patxi and his Béarn wife, Marilyn. The couple has tastefully revamped the bourgeois interior, whose windows command knockout views of Pau below. The decor provides the perfect foil for the veteran chef’s talented craftsmanship which slaloms between tradition and modernity. All of which is anchored in a commitment to sustainable fishing and local producers, illustrated by cèpe ravioles served with a mouthwatering slab of premium foie gras.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14364;Base Kamp by Aïnata;France;Courchevel;Le K2 Altitude, 356 route de l'Altiport, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4024897;6.6380402;46;false;true;Lebanese;Zaatar, freekeh, sumac, pomegranate, bulgur, hummus, tahini, mograbieh: French-Lebanese chef Alan Geaam made sure he packed his rucksack full of produce and spices from his homeland before heading up to Courchevel. Mezze and food for sharing, to be enjoyed – at lunchtime only – beneath the rafters in the spacious dining room, or on the terrace with views of the ski slopes.;Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14365;L'Attanum;France;Saint-Yrieix-la-Perche;64 place de la Nation, Saint-Yrieix-la-Perche, 87500, France;45.5090743;1.2026841;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;The ground floor of this 19C sous-préfecture is now home to a restaurant that welcomes you with contemporary interior design and smiling service. At the helm is a seasoned chef with stints at some prestigious establishments to his name. A fan of local seasonal produce, his cooking demonstrates his stellar technique (illustrated by his venison terrine), spot-on cooking and reductions (see his duck fillet served with spelt and beetroot) and delicately balanced flavours. The attentive staff and excellent wine cellar add the final flourishes to this gourmet experience.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14367;Jupi;France;Paris;25 rue des Dames, Paris, 75017, France;48.8845239;2.324428;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At the helm of this modern bistro (polished concrete floor, trendy light fittings, wooden tables), with electronic music playing in the background, young chef Alice Roger shows she has experience (three years in London) and good taste (she worked with Michelin-starred chef Ryuji Teshima at Pages). Her cuisine is full of pep (thanks to elements such as the Noilly Prat sabayon, the gribiche sauce with violet mustard and the horseradish sauce) and decidedly exciting. The lunch menu is a steal. In the evening, plates for sharing are the name of the game.;;[]
14368;Maison Pavlov;France;Le Bouscat;199 avenue de la Libération-Charles-de-Gaulle, Le Bouscat, 33110, France;44.8625361;-0.6015408;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Nowadays, this 17C Carthusian monastery is home to a small boutique hotel and its restaurant. Opt for a table out on the terrace, which overlooks the swimming pool, or in an atmosphere reminiscent of an elegant boudoir (velvet banquettes, cane chairs and salvaged objects). In keeping with this setting, the cuisine is meticulous and comforting, promoting subtle, delicate flavours. Short menu at lunchtime, more expansive in the evening.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14369;L'Intangible;France;Lempaut;Château de la Bousquétarié, Lempaut, 81700, France;43.5332973;2.0769507;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This 1850 family château was tastefully restored in 2022 by a young couple raised in the world of Alain Ducasse and used to high-flying establishments (Palais de l’Élysée and Plaza Athénée for her, Meurice for him). Their single set menu aims to showcase vegetables from the local terroir and their own kitchen garden, albeit scattered with globetrotting touches. Grilled white asparagus accompanied by a garlic sabayon, shiitake and oyster mushroom ravioli with egg confit, pigeon breast and leg wrapped in chard leaves. For dessert, the pastry chef steps in with fruity delights, such as a strawberry and Espelette pepper pavlova. Five exquisitely appointed guestrooms are available should you wish to prolong your stay in style.;Garden or park;[]
14371;Rond de Carotte;France;Saint-Gervais-les-Bains;50 rue de la Vignette, Saint-Gervais-les-Bains, 74170, France;45.8938363;6.7116384;55;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the resort, this eatery shines the spotlight on seasonal, sometimes local ingredients, such as Magland snails. The chef conjures up well-crafted dishes, like free-range poached egg flanked by sweet chestnuts and creamy squash, or melt-in-the-mouth chuck beef stew that is eaten with a spoon. The chalet-inspired dining room, divided in two by a small open-plan kitchen, is the quintessence of alpine charm, in particular due to the shelves loaded in bottles (the establishment is also a wine merchant). Daily brunch from 9am-2pm.;Terrace;[]
14372;Sao;France;Quimper;1 quai Neuf, Quimper, 29000, France;47.9901667;-4.1124614;71;false;true;Creative;On the quayside of the River Odet in Quimper city centre, this restaurant is the brainchild of Kevin Gourret, who was previously chef at Le Goyen restaurant in Audierne. In an inviting contemporary setting, he serves original recipes inspired by local ingredients (langoustine, local fish, seaweed, buckwheat, buttermilk) and Asian influences (such as yuzu, ponzu, gomasio, sesame and ginger).;Wheelchair access;[]
14374;Mieux;France;Paris;21 rue Saint-Lazare, Paris, 75009, France;48.8767047;2.3369895;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Three long-standing partners have opened this friendly address, the archetype of unapologetic bistronomie that satisfies the taste buds without breaking the bank. The food pays tribute to the market and quality produce, with dishes always in tune with the season. Friendly, unpretentious vibe and great value for money at lunchtime.;;[]
14377;Il Ristorante - Niko Romito;France;Paris;Hôtel Bulgari, 30 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.8683712;2.3015041;30;true;false;Italian;Niko Romito, a chef from Abruzzo with three Michelin stars to his name, updates the classics of Italian cooking in a menu that really homes in on the produce and dares to go light (easy on the fat, limited sauces, steamed ingredients, rice starch for the breadcrumb coating etc). The saffron risotto with parmesan is subtle and does not weigh on the stomach, as is the magnificent veal cutlet alla Milanese, to be savoured in this elegantly sleek dining area that opens onto the interior garden.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14378;Terra;France;Chartres;65 avenue du Maréchal-Maunoury, Chartres, 28000, France;48.4392089;1.4818595;40;false;false;Italian;A short walk from the city centre, in the suburbs of Chartres, the husband-and-wife team behind Terra (he is an Italian chef and she is a South African pastry chef) extend an invitation to join them on a culinary journey. The excellent and quintessentially Italian cuisine is served in a friendly atmosphere – the fiorentina-style cannelloni stuffed with veal and spinach and the house parmesan sauce is delicious!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14379;Parcelles;France;Paris;13 rue Chapon, Paris, 75003, France;48.8632515;2.3565199;100;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The quintessence of retro Paris! In a side street between Arts et Métiers and the Centre Pompidou, this 1936 bistro would not have been out of place on the set of Woody Allen's Midnight in Paris: authentic bistro furniture, bare or beige walls, vintage tiled flooring, gilded ceiling, and a copper and wooden counter. The food is all that you'd expect: pressed pork shank, line-caught sea bass with spelt risotto and smoked eel sauce, and, of course, the dark chocolate and caramelised pecan tart. Ten out of ten for this restaurant that fully deserves its success. (Book if you can.);Interesting wine list;[]
14380;Le Sens 7367;France;Vaux-sur-Mer;141 boulevard de la Côte-de-Beauté, Vaux-sur-Mer, 17640, France;45.6352744;-1.0681036;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a small village near Royan, this contemporary eatery is the haunt of Frédéric Loivel. The chef is a craftsman with a creative bent, whose modern score highlights the seasons through intelligent associations and numerous nods to Japan (panko, yuzu, matcha, Kagoshima beef…). The interior tastefully blends mismatched decorative objects picked up here and there.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14381;Le Comptoir Kokagué;France;Mouchard;8 rue Léopold-Alixant, Mouchard, 39330, France;46.9755031;5.7975458;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in the unlikely location of a tiny village in the Jura, this restaurant serving French-Japanese cuisine based on regional produce has a local following among the people of Mouchard and from the surrounding areas! In an interior that is largely unadorned but for a few plants, diners first make the acquaintance of this French-Japanese couple (she cooks, he manages the restaurant floor). Then the food is served: ingredients from the local terroir are woven into Japanese dishes, as in the celeriac purée with a wasabi kick, the trout marinated with kombu seaweed (on the kawamatsu kobujimè), or the Bresse chicken fillet worked into a tofu and shiitake patty flavoured with ginger (tori daikon). There is a good selection of wines organised by grape variety, mainly showcasing natural wines.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14382;Les Capucines;France;Le Petit-Quevilly;16 rue Jean-Macé, Le Petit-Quevilly, 76140, France;49.42406;1.06405;53;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The Demoget family has been perfecting the art of hospitality in this Rouen institution for three generations. In a stylish, classical interior, the focus is on generous French staples (thick juicy steaks served with Anna potatoes or salmon gravlax with a beetroot emulsion).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14384;Maison Grandclaude;France;Chaumousey;37 rue d'Épinal, Chaumousey, 88390, France;48.1736769;6.3355702;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in a handsome bourgeois house, fashionably done up in a contemporary vibe with untreated materials such as oak, this inviting venue, a ten-minute drive from Epinal, is the brainchild of Nicolas Grandclaude and his wife. The modern, soul-warming culinary slant, backed up by exquisite plating, is illustrated in the likes of butterflied and seared wild prawns with coconut milk, ginger and lemongrass, or pan-fried whiting filets with courgettes, almonds and basil. Delightful.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14386;La Traboule;France;Paris;27 rue de Penthièvre, Paris, 75008, France;48.8726824;2.3152579;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Italian;Just a few hundred metres from the Élysée Palace, this establishment sports a fashionable bistro interior and a buzzy vibe. The food errs towards well-crafted bistronomic courtesy of simple recipes that focus on big-boned, legible flavours.;;[]
14387;L'Hippi'curien;France;Toulouse;62 chemin des Courses, Toulouse, 31100, France;43.59094;1.40239;52;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;At this small restaurant in an old building with exposed brick and pebble interior walls, diners have two options: excellent value for money at lunchtime or more elaborate cuisine in the evening with the single set menu. The new chef, who has a particular fondness for France's South-West, makes the best seasonal ingredients the focus of his set menus: grilled green asparagus, roast fillet of duckling, bluefin tuna from Saint-Jean-de-Luz etc. Attentive service.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14389;Le Patte Noire;France;Cholet;17 avenue de Nantes, Cholet, 49300, France;47.0609399;-0.8922222;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Presiding over its grounds, this charming 19C château houses a lovely restaurant on the first floor. Done out with carpeting, beige walls, colourful wallpaper, mouldings, mirrors on the ceiling and a large fireplace, the space is modern and inviting. Chef Adrien Roux expertly selects top-quality seasonal ingredients for his set menus: trout roe, hand-dived scallops, lobster from Brittany and rabbit from the Vendée… And how could we forget the famous pata negra bellota, which not only gives the restaurant its name, but also lends an indulgent touch to a number of dishes. Generosity, colour and bold flavours characterise every dish prepared by this chef who means business.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
14392;Aux Crieurs de Vin;France;Troyes;4 place Jean-Jaurès, Troyes, 10000, France;48.2951489;4.0715178;100;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The decor is trendy with bare bricks, polished concrete floors and bistro furniture, as is the concept... Choose a bottle of wine from the cellar, before pairing it with a good, simple dish with a focus on ingredients (artisan produced charcuterie, free - range meat, cheeses from Bordier etc). A tasty and friendly place.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14393;Le Réverbère;France;Vic-en-Bigorre;29 boulevard d'Alsace, Vic-en-Bigorre, 65500, France;43.3846327;0.0554159;56;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Come and bask in the light of the very pleasant Réverbère, whose entirely redesigned interior is modern and light. Enjoy the chef’s creations, which rely heavily on local produce. He works with several local farmers to serve up generous and tasty dishes that are full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14394;La Mercerie;France;Marseille;9 cours Saint-Louis, Marseille, 13001, France;43.2958736;5.3783657;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;An avalanche of quality local ingredients, undeniable know-how and gourmet delicacies... You can count on the young team to take care of your appetite in the best possible way. As for wine, the menu is lovingly put together with an emphasis on natural wines, with a promising turnover: all the ingredients are in place for you to have a great time.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14396;Bistro S;France;Paris;7 rue Saint-Nicolas, Paris, 75012, France;48.8507621;2.3741688;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;S like secret, savoury, sapid or Spinoza, not the philosopher but the owner who lovingly watches over this discreet Parisian establishment, and who is also a numismatist specialising in antique Greek coins and a genuine wine connoisseur. The talented Japanese chef Shimpei Oié crafts a fresh, healthy, balanced set menu backed up by his flawless culinary technique. Don’t miss the gilthead seabream: expertly fire-roasted and accompanied by white grapes and a kiwi juice. S like Super!;;[]
14398;Caffé César L'initial;France;Opio;2 route de Nice, Opio, 06650, France;43.6680384;6.9874766;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Provençal;A large patio and a spacious, modern interior with an open-plan kitchen set the scene for spot-on, bistronomic cuisine, steeped in the aromas and flavours of Provence and the Mediterranean. Delicious chard-flavoured gnocchi (“Merda de Can” - a delicacy of Nice), caponata-style fillet of dentex in red wine and rose-scented rum baba… A cheerful, friendly vibe with wines by the glass from a magnum bottle…;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14399;Le Braque;France;Lille;45 rue de la Monnaie, Lille, 59000, France;50.6410447;3.0626904;95;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Sous-chef to Florent Ladeyn and a TV cooking show contestant, Damien Laforce and dog, Marcel (a pointer or ‘braque’), have opened this eatery, depicted by brick and light wood. He crafts tasty regional fare, scattered with bold touches. Concise organic wine list, smiling service and 20 or so wall counter seats for customers without a booking.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14400;Omnivore;France;Pau;1 place Gramont, Pau, 64000, France;43.2964825;-0.3739743;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Two minutes from Pau Château, on the picturesque Place Gramont, imagine a nostalgic bistro with a zinc-topped counter, wood panelling and upholstered seating. Pau's foodies flock here, sharing good vibes as they tuck into fish fresh from the fish auction or 24hr shoulder of pork. The slate menu features traditional nosh served generously and sometimes enhanced by touches of citrus fruit or well-balanced smoky notes. The jovial front-of-house staff are an added bonus.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14401;Là DN;France;Plescop;11 rue Blaise-Pascal, Plescop, 56890, France;47.6796356;-2.8002347;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Open only on weekday lunchtimes, this small restaurant with an experienced chef at the helm serves an indulgent but wallet-friendly menu-carte. His pleasant bistronomy cooking is inspired by the market, and includes dishes such as gurnard with Jerusalem artichokes and vegetable colombo, or caramelised veal breast, crispy polenta and parsley mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14403;Le Clos d'Émile;France;Mornay-sur-Allier;1 Bel-Air, Mornay-sur-Allier, 18600, France;46.8204352;3.0309948;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This farmhouse is home to a charming restaurant, where Madame takes care of the cooking and Monsieur provides attentive and high-quality service. They propose straightforward and healthy cuisine, with a strong emphasis on produce from farms located within a 30km radius – as well as their own beef and pork. A welcoming place.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14404;La Cuisine de la Fontaignotte;France;Semur-en-Auxois;4 rue de la Fontaignotte, Semur-en-Auxois, 21140, France;47.4903161;4.3318671;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This exquisite 17C mansion, whose conservatory and large terrace command a matchless view over the town’s ramparts and the River Armançon, enjoys a premium location in this picture postcard medieval town. The town and its walls may be rich in heritage, but the incisive, fresh cuisine of chef Martin is light years from old school, as the brook trout smoked over vine shoots and beetroot in a salt crust demonstrates. The chef faithfully keeps pace with the seasons, working with farmers from Auxois and Burgundy.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14405;Ferme de la Besse;France;Usclades-et-Rieutord;La Besse, Usclades-et-Rieutord, 07510, France;44.7624423;4.1664654;99;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The poultry, calves and ewes that are reared on the family farm are the starting point for this pleasant, hard-working young chef, who has energy to spare. Fresh and appetising dishes served in an informal and friendly ambience. Quite delightful!;Car park;[]
14406;L'Informel;France;Saint-Céré;Les Prés-de-Montal, Saint-Jean-Lespinasse, Saint-Céré, 46400, France;44.8630131;1.8627884;72;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The gourmet annexe of the Michelin - starred restaurant Les Trois Soleils de Montal. The chef proposes generous and tasty traditional cuisine, made with fresh seasonal ingredients, such as the top - notch leg of lamb roasted with thyme. Friendly and informal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14407;La Table d'Élise;France;Monaco;2 rue du Portier, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7421478;7.4294841;21;true;true;Provençal;This swish, fashionable brasserie, located a stone's throw from Monaco’s Japanese Garden and the Grimaldi Forum, welcomes diners in a modern, spacious interior with pop music playing in the background. The Provençal cuisine, prepared with fine seasonal ingredients, is spot on, unfussy, generous and tasty. It is always a pleasure to watch the action in the open-plan kitchen. Excellent lunch deal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14408;Les Caudalies;France;Vichy;7 rue Besse, Vichy, 03200, France;46.1220106;3.4233205;37;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Les Caudalies in Vichy has it all: a stylishly elegant dining room strewn with contemporary details, an appealing wine list with over 900 labels selected by Lucie, chef Emmanuel Basset’s wife, and a culinary line-up of tasty and generous dishes that tread a fine line between tradition and modernity. NB: check out the “cadole” dining area, between the wine cellar and the kitchen, which sports a vintner's lodge vibe.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
14409;Hôtel des Deux Rocs;France;Seillans;1 place Font-d'Amont, Seillans, 83440, France;43.6367715;6.6428313;48;false;false;Farm to table;This beautiful 12C bastide overlooks a picture postcard medieval village… The chef crafts Provençal cuisine that navigates between gutsy classical recipes, such as snails, and more contemporary preparations, e.g. tandoori curried octopus. Good food in an authentic, rural setting, which can be extended by booking one of the guestrooms – what more could we want?;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14410;Auberge de Sainte-Maure;France;Sainte-Maure;99 route de Méry, Sainte-Maure, 10150, France;48.3451222;4.060857;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The young owner, Victor Martin, and his chef Julien Drapier are now a well-established duo. The dishes tend towards an undeniable finesse, such as the roasted langoustine, fennel confit and shell jus. Add to that smiling service, good value for money, and a pleasant terrace by the water.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14411;L'Alchimiste;France;Saumur;6 rue de Lorraine, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2605311;-0.0832207;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Despite the name you won’t find any molecular cuisine here. Instead, enjoy good, no - nonsense dishes such as courgette and goat’s cheese flan, and poached pears. It is often full so it is best to book.;Terrace;[]
14412;Le Cèdre;France;Port-Vendres;29 route de Banyuls, Port-Vendres, 66660, France;42.5130376;3.1095939;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The food shows off the undeniable richness of the Catalan terroir, and varies freely with the passing seasons, so it is impossible to tire of it! As for the setting, it is an invitation to daydream. The picture window gives onto the fine terrace and, beyond, the port and the sea. Le Cèdre has it all.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14414;La Petite Plage;France;Saint-Tropez;9 quai Jean-Jaurès, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2727045;6.6388987;59;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;In this restaurant in the village port, Eric Frechon devises the menu, and the sea does the rest. Enjoy a new take on flavoursome Mediterranean cuisine, as you bury your feet in the sand overlooking the yachts, ever a subject of conversation. On summer evenings, a DJ provides the soundtrack, as is the norm in Saint-Tropez! Attentive service despite the bustle.;;[]
14415;Nobuki;France;Tours;3 rue Buffon, Tours, 37000, France;47.393463;0.6905458;56;false;true;Japanese;A zen and minimalist interior all done out in pale wood sets the scene for traditional, seasonal Japanese cuisine that stands out for its fresh, unusual flavours: assortment of cold starters and tempura of the day, chirashi (traditional dish of raw fish), a hot dish of the day and miso soup. Booking essential.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
14416;Bistrot des Hauts de Loire;France;Onzain;79 rue Gilbert-Navard, Onzain, 41150, France;47.5088869;1.1433334;39;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the outbuildings of the estate, a picturesque Sologne building with exposed timber beams and oak floorboards sets the scene. On the terrace, facing the kitchen garden, you can tuck into simple bistro dishes (matured meat, spit-roasts) or the chef’s more imaginative creations. Scrumptious!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14419;Domaine de Baulieu;France;Auch;822 chemin de Lussan, Auch, 32000, France;43.6437642;0.6174979;76;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In an elegant and modern interior with large bay windows overlooking the terrace and the surrounding nature, you can enjoy food cooked up by Maxime Deschamps. Their dishes are well crafted and make the most of local produce. A super dining experience.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14422;La Cassolette;France;Vence;10b place Georges-Clemenceau, Vence, 06140, France;43.72258;7.11359;22;true;true;Provençal;In the heart of the exquisite historic town, facing the town hall, this institution continues to remain a landmark of Vence’s culinary scene. It is a pleasure to take a seat indoors or on the terrace to tuck into flavoursome, market fresh dishes of Mediterranean inspiration.;Terrace;[]
14424;La Tour;France;Sancerre;31 Nouvelle-Place, Sancerre, 18300, France;47.3320182;2.8400766;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Nestling at the foot of a 14C tower in the heart of the famous wine-growing village, this traditional townhouse boasts an elegant, contemporary dining room offset by a scattering of period details (beams, ceiling and mouldings). Simplicity, authenticity and bags of character are the hallmarks of the food characterised by premium ingredients that keep pace with the seasons presented in an enticing lunchtime menu (that is also a steal!) and a surprise menu available in different versions in the evening. There is also an entirely vegetarian menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14425;La Table de Catusseau;France;Pomerol;86 rue de Catusseau, Pomerol, 33500, France;44.9234713;-0.2065061;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Kendji Wongsodikromo, owner - chef of New Caledonian extraction, fell in love with southwest France and his wife, Nadège, whom you will meet in the dining room. The enthusiastic, young couple does not lack experience as the first taste of their market - fresh, carefully crafted dishes made with tasty, regional ingredients will confirm.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14426;Le Château de Sable;France;Porspoder;38 rue de l'Europe, Porspoder, 29840, France;48.5167139;-4.7628871;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Time seems to have stopped here, in this tranquil spot on the coast overlooking the Saint Laurent peninsula, which can be seen from the plush, cosy interior of this smart seaside establishment. The chef uses local Breton produce in traditional recipes, together with more high-flying creations.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14427;Le Sens Unique;France;Aix-les-Bains;Hôtel Gallia, 24 boulevard-Berthollet, Aix-les-Bains, 73100, France;45.6902807;5.9173371;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This friendly bistronomy restaurant is part of a small hotel in the upper reaches of the town centre. Behind a façade still reminiscent of Aix-les-Bains's heyday as a spa resort, this stylish eatery, complete with a wine bar, has lost none of its period cachet. It is run by a vital chef who often puts in an appearance on the restaurant floor. His down-to-earth bistro-style cuisine with a twist uses seasonal and sometimes premium produce (Angus beef, Corsican meagre etc). Attentive service. The enclosed tree-lined terrace to the rear is charming.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14429;L'Arborescence;France;Cruseilles;175 route du Lac, Cruseilles, 74350, France;46.0371584;6.1212198;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Between Annecy and Geneva, a chef, who trained with the greats (Lionel Giraud, Christian Constant, Laurent Petit), crafts a range of surprise menus using fresh and often local ingredients. Charming service courtesy of the chef’s spouse.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14430;Leptine;France;Lyon;16 rue Hippolyte-Flandrin, Lyon, 69001, France;45.768076;4.8305695;48;false;true;Creative;The sound system is an integral part of this place with its long corridor bathed in red light, its open kitchen behind a counter and its tables lining the wall. The name ("leptin" in English) refers to the hormone that signals to your brain when you are satiated – no question of leaving here on an empty stomach! The chef deftly draws on the culinary traditions of France, Asia and beyond, treating diners to siu mai, an array of fermented foods and Japanese seasonings. It's brilliantly done, and the seasoned team is more than happy to tell you how. Two to three savoury dishes plus one sweet should do the trick. Natural wine list, an interesting selection of wines by the glass and savvy recommendations.;Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14431;Odorico;France;Angers;2 place de Lorraine, Angers, 49100, France;47.4698187;-0.5481127;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Isidore Odorico is the name of the Italian-born mosaic artist from Rennes who decorated the dining room of this restaurant in 1928. The blue and gold tiles of his Art Deco fresco unfurl majestically over the walls, arches and columns. In the kitchen, the repertoire of chef Armand Lallart – who worked in some prestigious establishments before settling in his hometown – pays tribute to the fish and seafood of Brittany and the sun of the Mediterranean with a short, modern menu at lunchtime, and a single set menu in the evening. The ingredients are carefully sourced, the sauces and jus are well made and the dish as a whole is very fresh.;;[]
14432;Charbonnel;France;Brantôme;57 rue Gambetta, Brantôme, 24310, France;45.3652307;0.649903;67;false;true;Creative;This emblematic inn stands in the heart of the picturesque village of Brantôme. Enticing seasonal cuisine made from painstakingly sourced produce and scattered with Asian notes is served in a cosily comfortable dining room, which leads onto an enchanting terrace overlooking the River Dronne.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14433;Les Belles Canailles;France;Cassis;Les Roches Blanches, 9 avenue des Calanques, Cassis, 13260, France;43.2118058;5.529995;72;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The view from the terrace of this luxury hotel restaurant (popular with celebrities), which looks out over Cap Canaille, is quite simply sublime. Chef Nicolas Sintes, who grew up in Cannes, serves his guests Mediterranean-inspired cuisine that has a focus on fish, but also features, for example, local lamb and seasonal vegetables. However, you may prefer to opt for the chef's down-to-earth speciality of bouillabaisse borgne, followed by a wild bass and its broth of pistou soup… All accompanied by a Cassis or Bandol wine, as you would expect.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14434;Taggat;France;Lyon;110 rue Vendôme, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7671385;4.8453444;78;false;false;Creative;In this contemporary-style bistro with an industrial vibe, the chef showcases his culinary skills. These tend towards the creative, and he is not afraid to lace his dishes with bold flavours: burrata and cucumber, mojo verde, bread crisps, garlic confit and black olive powder… or John Dory, caponata, olive oil puff pastry and a red pepper jus. Set menu at lunchtime and à la carte in the evening in a similar vein, but with more upmarket ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14435;Restaurant Côté Marais;France;Beauvoir-sur-Mer;Le Grand Pont, Beauvoir-sur-Mer, 85230, France;46.8953486;-2.0648735;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A starter of ceviche of white mullet (a fish rarely found on restaurant menus) with rhubarb for a hint of tartness, followed by a savoury/sweet main course of pollack fished by small boats, French peas al dente and a smattering of sweet cherry condiment. The young chef applies his own personal culinary style to local ingredients, while his partner works the restaurant floor in this outlying establishment surrounded by marshland (and with a lovely terrace).;Car park,Terrace;[]
14437;Le Serghi;France;Saint-Martin-de-Ré;15 quai Georges-Clemenceau, Saint-Martin-de-Ré, 17410, France;46.2061591;-1.3661906;20;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;On the old port, this restaurant (with its pleasant terrace at the front) belongs to the island's select club of restaurants that are open all year round. In the kitchen, a great chef, Philippe Tredgeu (previously at Entredgeu and Les Cocottes in Paris), crafts cuisine that calls to mind Parisian bistronomy. Fine ingredients, seasonal produce and indulgent dishes are the order of the day: green asparagus, egg mimosa, sauce parisienne or grilled and glazed confit pork belly with market-fresh vegetables. A joy from start to finish.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14440;La Taula;France;Périgueux;3 rue Denfert-Rochereau, Périgueux, 24000, France;45.18371;0.72205;73;false;false;Regional Cuisine;At La Taula (which means "table" in Occitan), Christine Maurence concocts no-nonsense family-style cuisine. Among her specialities, the veal kidney cooked whole with mustard seeds, the home-made stuffed duck's neck, and the semi-cooked foie gras are the signature dishes. An authentic restaurant just next to the cathedral, where traditions are not something to be trifled with!;Air conditioning;[]
14441;La Maison des Toqués;France;Noirmoutier-en-l'Île;26 rue de la Prée-aux-Ducs, Noirmoutier-en-l'Île, 85330, France;47.0008515;-2.248864;26;true;false;Farm to table;Aurore and Sébastien Duchenne share the same passion for top-quality regional produce, often organic, which they transform into delicious recipes that capture the zeitgeist and are inspired by market availability. As you enter, you are greeted by a colourful, modern interior whose blue and white walls are adorned with artwork, providing the perfect foil to elegantly plated ingredients such as lobster, local oysters, John Dory or royal Charmilles pigeon. Booking highly advisable.;;[]
14443;Armada;France;Lyon;16 rue du Bœuf, Lyon, 69005, France;45.7628723;4.8271176;51;true;false;Creative;This bolthole in historic Lyon ticks all the boxes: a trendy chummy vibe and a ubiquitous decor of exposed beams and stonework. The food demonstrates a clever, creative slant with uninhibited dishes to share depicted by mussels, curry and dried lime, an exuberant new take on blanquette of veal or stuffed cabbage. Beware: it may well become your new HQ.;Air conditioning;[]
14444;Céna;France;Montpellier;2 place Pétrarque, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6107056;3.8783932;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Clément Briand-Seurat has left the Pic Saint-Loup restaurant to open his own establishment (Cena means supper or dinner in Latin) beneath the ribbed vaults of a medieval edifice in the heart of historic Montpellier. A snug, romantic vibe, enhanced by centuries-old stonework and candle-lit rough oak tables, sets the scene. The chef signs a creative single set menu in which he endeavours to enhance the produce of local growers and breeders thanks to flawless craftsmanship (chutneys, oils, crumbles, crackers and whipped siphon concoctions). His knockout mushroom consommé and ‘stroll in the woods’ embodies this ethos.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14448;La Cantine Urbaine - Artchives;France;Lille;74 rue Jacquemars-Giélée, Lille, 59000, France;50.634591;3.0539257;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Previously an annexe of the local archives, this urban canteen now houses a venue dedicated to art and to good food. On the top floor, light streams in from the atrium, setting the scene in the trendy interior.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14450;La R'mize;France;Les Gets;160 rue du Vieux-Village, Les Gets, 74260, France;46.159935;6.6718197;58;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Located in the historic village, near the church, this eatery serves traditional toothsome nosh. A veteran chef regales diners with well-crafted dishes like cream of pumpkin soup served with shavings of Abondance cheese and whipped cream lightly flavoured with passion fruit or a carpaccio of scallops with a jus of lobster shells. His gourmet repertoire also includes timeless Savoyard specialities ranging from gratinée gourmande to fondue Savoyard made with champagne!;Wheelchair access;[]
14452;Chez Mosse;France;Cornier;58 place du Tilleul, Cornier, 74800, France;46.0932585;6.2999584;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The boss here is Mattéo Mosse, a youthful chef from Haute Savoie who decided to settle in this village to be as close as possible to the countryside and to small local producers. Fish and meat from sustainable breeders, as local as possible and a vegetarian score depict the ethos of this eco-responsible eatery. The chef’s modern repertory unsurprisingly revolves around seasonal produce, with a distinct weakness for organic veggies. A simple, no-fuss bistro interior in a colourful village house that is flanked by a refreshingly shady terrace.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14453;Léonor;France;Strasbourg;11 rue de la Nuée-Bleue, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5859505;7.7473384;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Behind a 19C façade and within 18C walls, this contemporary hotel designed by Jean-Philippe Nuel has its own lounge-style restaurant adjoining the bar. The menu is in keeping with the culinary zeitgeist: for example, tuna sashimi, mango, avocado, with soy and sesame sauce, or sautéed calf’s sweetbreads, celery and lovage. For tables of friends, there are large dishes designed to share (whole seabass, rib steak etc). For those with a sweet tooth, there’s a choice of plated desserts or pretty pastries laid out in the display cabinet.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14454;Peixes Bonaparte;France;Nice;5 rue Bonaparte, Nice, 06300, France;43.7007122;7.2818862;76;true;true;Seafood;Between Place Garibaldi and the Old Town of Nice, this restaurant is run by the team behind Peixes Opéra. Here, too, they deploy their winning formula, starting with a large terrace that is a very popular spot on sunny days, followed by a range of seafood dishes (fish, tataki, sashimi, accras, oysters) and ceviche specialities. The contemporary blue and white "marine bistro" setting calls to mind Portugal or Greece. Behind the bar, a mixologist creates your cocktails. The lunch menu is really good value. This place is open all day, with a reduced menu until 7pm.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14455;Le Bistrot de Madeleine;France;Lucinges;67 place de l'Église, Lucinges, 74380, France;46.190457;6.318321;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This village inn is a real boon for lovers of the finer (and healthier) things in life. It would not be out of place to talk about programmatic cuisine in this bistro with a slightly rustic feel: whole carcass approach, local market gardening, fish sourced directly from the fish markets, a menu that changes every week… The end result? Tasty, generous and delicious cuisine.;Terrace;[]
14456;Origines Restaurant;France;Paris;6 rue de Ponthieu, Paris, 75008, France;48.8702343;2.3111842;82;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this contemporary restaurant, Aveyron-born chef Julien Boscus finetunes bold, crisp cuisine thanks to a solid classical background. His genuine à la carte lineup (something of a rarity these days…) showcases intelligently crafted, flavoursome dishes made with first-class seasonal produce. Examples include a delicious crispy tartlet filled with morel mushrooms creamed in sous-voile wine, or sautéed calf sweetbreads with green asparagus from Vaucluse steamed in citron, while his amazing hare à la royale, reworked in a more modern vein, deserves a special mention. The wine list stars an impressive selection from France's vineyards, served by a slick, professional team. Friendly and endearing!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14457;La Table Cachée par Michel Roth;France;Paris;BHV, 33 rue de la Verrerie, Paris, 75004, France;48.8573225;2.3534354;41;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the 5th floor of the BHV department store, this “hidden table” lies behind a mysterious green curtain - at the rear of the lingerie department! The cosy setting (all the “props” are sold in the store) is the lair of Michel Roth who crafts an enticing seasonal score (tartlet of haddock, magret of Gers duck with bigarade sauce, millefeuille pastry with Corsican clementines) and a reasonably priced first-class market-fresh menu at lunchtime. The panoramic terrace commands a fantastic view of the townhall of Paris.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14458;CoDa;France;Paris;15 rue de la Tour-des-Dames, Paris, 75009, France;48.8777461;2.3323468;49;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set back from the boisterous Rue Blanche, this pocket-handkerchief bolthole is the epitome of an authentic Parisian café. The tables are so tightly packed, it may feel like you are dining with rather than next to your neighbours. Irrepressibly cheerful, Pauline and Vincent Da Costa (former second chef of Bruno Doucet’s Régalade) pamper their guests with nosh that hits the spot every time: field to fork market-fresh seasonal ingredients. Fine food without the fuss. The lunchtime menu is a steal.;;[]
14459;Ambos;France;Paris;38 rue de Vaugirard, Paris, 75006, France;48.8492387;2.3350789;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Overlooking the grandiose seat of the Senate (upper house of the French parliament) and the Luxembourg gardens, this friendly bistro in tune with its era sports untreated materials (exposed stone, brickwork and rafters), an open kitchen and a small counter. ‘Ambos’ (‘both’ in Spanish) refers to Pierre Chomet and his Venezuelan wife, Cristina. Their culinary adventures have taken them from Bangkok to London and Paris, and a Top Chef TV season for Pierre. Together they concoct a light-hearted, personal and vibrant tapestry of flavours which aims to please as it draws on a variety of influences – European (Castilian beef and Paimpol beans) and Thai (pad thai-style langoustine tartar,) as well as South American (stuffed arepa cornbread).;Air conditioning;[]
14460;Baud;France;Bonne;181 avenue du Léman, Bonne, 74380, France;46.1680826;6.3195438;20;true;false;Creative;This family-run hotel-restaurant is always a safe bet. The decor is contemporary, with black and white striped carpets and crimson walls and ceiling. The cuisine, meanwhile, carves out a niche between traditional and modern, with a multi-course surprise set menu. The terrace nestles beneath a pergola by the river, and there are cosy guestrooms for overnight guests.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14461;La Cour des Sens;France;Ceintrey;9 rue de Benney, Ceintrey, 54134, France;48.5233037;6.1628705;33;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant installed in an old farmhouse boasts an intimate atmosphere and a decor in which wooden floors meet exposed stonework. Head chef Benjamin Royer creates dishes that show off an undeniable savoir-faire: scallops cooked on stones, flambéed with saffron gin, smoked aubergine caviar and beurre blanc, and pan-roasted turbot, poached heirloom turnip with parmesan and a truffle sauce.;Wheelchair access;[]
14462;Le Sauvage;France;Besançon;6 rue du Chapitre, Besançon, 25000, France;47.2316093;6.0278644;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;At the foot of the Vauban Citadel, this smart hotel occupies the former convent of the Poor Clares. The restaurant provides a cosy setting, with old parquet floors and tablecloths, and – a major asset – its terrace overlooking the park! Chef Hugo Mathieu (trained in Lyon's top restaurants) is no novice, judging by his polished dishes: glazed pea velouté, cod loin fillet cooked at 50C, crispy pistachio tartlet.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14463;Cave et Cuisine;France;Demigny;1 cour du Wauxhall, Demigny, 71150, France;46.9312328;4.8371271;94;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A town house with blue shutters next to the church, a wine cellar with over 1 000 labels, a chef who is following in her parents' footsteps. An undeniable talent in the kitchen, she combines classics (eggs in a red wine sauce, ham terrine with parsley etc), contemporary dishes (salmon gravlax) and specialities such as roast pigeon and sweetbreads. To be savoured in a refined bistro decor, where smiling service is the order of the day and the wine recommendations are on point.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14465;Passionné;France;Paris;17 rue Bergère, Paris, 75009, France;48.8723409;2.3451574;31;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set back from Grands Boulevards, this restaurant plays the minimalist card: a bar with midnight blue mosaics, dark walls and floor and refined lighting. A very Japanese brand of elegance, designed for this location officiated by chef Satoshi Horiuchi, originally from Hokkaido island, a few kilometres from Sapporo, a prefecture with a high concentration of small-scale producers, especially market gardeners. Horiuchi is as passionate as ever about creating a modern French cuisine characterised by his quest to find quality ingredients and cook them perfectly.;Air conditioning;[]
14467;Lafayette;France;Versailles;10 boulevard du Roi, Versailles, 78000, France;48.8105186;2.1263564;100;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Abutting his first restaurant, chef Xavier Pincemin has opened this trendy bistro that sports a series of adjoining Art deco rooms. He is enjoying himself and, in the process, delights us with a menu of varied influences (tacos, ceviche, tiger beef) and a selection of outstanding matured beef displayed in an ageing cabinet, such as the knockout black Baltic rib steak. Casual vibe.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14468;Les Quatre Saisons;France;Le Frenz;3 route du Frenz, Le Frenz, 68820, France;47.9255981;6.9506039;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This cosy chalet is set in a landscape of forests and mountains. Christelle proposes her own personal brand of cuisine (savoury éclair filled with porcini mousse, chanterelles in vinegar and cured ham, duck pot au feu with autumn vegetables cooked in broth), while Frédéric carefully selects the wines.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14469;Frenchie Pigalle;France;Paris;29 rue Victor-Massé, Paris, 75009, France;48.8808736;2.337594;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Grégory Marchand has brought a tongue-in-cheek vibe to the ground-floor restaurant of this hotel in Paris’ sleazy yet romantic Pigalle. Dishes to share in a joyful canteen ambience that err between regional comfort food, bang-on Gallic classics and world food, including a splendid cheeseboard and a wine list with natural inclinations…;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14470;Sens;France;Bordeaux;93 rue de Soissons, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8420746;-0.599071;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Off the bustling tourist track of Bordeaux, this cosy, modern bistro is run by chef Alexandre Bru and his wife, Loren, pastry chef. Their precise, deftly crafted, bistronomic score is particularly sensibly priced at lunchtime. Examples include gently steamed line-caught cod in a vin jaune sabayon or chocolate mousse flavoured with pecan nut praline and fleur de sel.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14471;Félicie;France;Loos;78 rue du Maréchal-Foch, Loos, 59120, France;50.61515;3.01662;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a rather industrial-style decor (waxed concrete, bricks, square tables made of frosted iron and wood), a young and dynamic team runs this address in the suburbs of Lille. The prices are simply fantastic for market-based cuisine of this quality – Félicie's is an absolute treat, make no mistake!;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
14473;Impressions;France;La Rochelle;7 rue Saint-Michel, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1598353;-1.1500437;75;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After 18 years at Le Saison near Rennes, David Etcheverry has moved to this restaurant in the centre of La Rochelle. It is a small place with a sleek modern loft design, where they serve refined, unfailingly delicious dishes. A real treat for the taste buds.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14476;Disciples;France;Paris;136 boulevard Murat, Paris, 75016, France;48.8370018;2.2619086;62;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Chef Jean-Pierre Vigato has lost nothing of his passion for passing on his knowledge. Indeed, in this bright, contemporary dining space that is in keeping with the chic neighbourhood, he has dubbed Romain Dubuisson his "disciple". On the agenda, a short menu of generous and tasty cuisine, specials and fine pieces of meat for sharing (e.g. veal chop, farmhouse pork loin).;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
14478;Chardon;France;Arles;37 rue des Arènes, Arles, 13200, France;43.6777282;4.6280836;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At Chardon, Julia Mitton, Laura Vidal and Harry Cummins, the trio behind "The Paris Pop Up" concept, host different chefs-in-residence, who temporarily take the reins in the kitchen. The one thing they all have in common: they use locally sourced ingredients. The result is fresh, delicious food served in a lovely bistro setting along with a fine selection of living wines. Spot on!;;[]
14479;Le Bateleur;France;Vaison-la-Romaine;1 place Théodore-Aubanel, Vaison-la-Romaine, 84110, France;44.23933;5.0745463;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A stone's throw from the Roman bridge, at the foot of the medieval town, the chef cooks up market-fresh cuisine. In tune with the seasons, it is often Provençal, and occasionally peppered with Italian or Mexican influences. To be enjoyed on the terrace when the weather is mild. A lovely place to sample dishes that are rich in flavours!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14480;La Sérafine;France;Veynes;8 hameau Les Paroirs, Veynes, 05400, France;44.5425359;5.8506493;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The Vietnamese-born chef produces modern and instinctive cuisine. Elegant and refined interior, savvy wine list (the wine cellar is visible as you enter) and the conservatory extends onto a pleasant terrace.;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14483;La Canopée;France;Villevieille;2 allée du Pigeonnier, Villevieille, 30250, France;43.8072975;4.0903345;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this vaulted Renaissance former weapons room (5m high! ), diners sample cuisine that fetes the Cévennes and Camargue regions. It is accompanied by a nice selection of minor wines from the region.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14486;Café Compagnon;France;Paris;22-26 rue Léopold-Bellan, Paris, 75002, France;48.8666817;2.3453241;40;false;false;Modern Cuisine;After Richer and 52 Faubourg, Charles Compagnon, restaurant owner, sommelier and coffee roaster, strikes again! This cafe offers an extensive menu ranging from nibbles to share to home-made ices. The original, deftly crafted recipes feature a modern bistro slant, depicted by market-fresh starters and succulent loin of pork. Heart-warming, authentic comfort food.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14487;Le Repère;France;Mandelieu-La Napoule;Port de la Rague, Mandelieu-La Napoule, 06210, France;43.5179223;6.9403775;25;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This well-established hideaway enjoys a knock-out location, boasting a terrace right on the beach and a panoramic view over the Bay of Cannes and the Lérins Islands. It is a delight to meet up with Nicolas Decherchi, a gifted chef who trained with the best (from Bruno Oger to Alain Ducasse), once again. He has been given carte blanche to devise a Mediterranean-focused menu with a special mention for dishes to share. Flawlessly fresh fish take front stage, although juicy cuts of meat also vie for pride of place. Open all day long, you can expect a pleasure-loving, casual vibe.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
14488;Le Grill Alpin;France;Courchevel;Cheval Blanc, Le Jardin Alpin, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4094884;6.6338614;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Under the leadership of Yannick Alléno, the chic Alpine brasserie of the upscale Cheval Blanc hotel has brilliantly reinvented high-altitude dining, serving up a contemporary and uninhibited fine dining offering. Your taste buds won't know what hit them! A sublime list of top-of-the-range wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14489;Imperial Treasure;France;Paris;44 rue de Bassano, Paris, 75008, France;48.8705493;2.2992482;33;false;false;Chinese, Shanghainese;If you are in the market for some authentic Chinese cuisine served in a luxurious and elegant setting close to the Champs Elysées, then this is the place for you. Dishes such as imperial shrimp carabinero with sticky rice, Peking duck, and smoked eel with green tea are all prepared according to time-honoured tradition by an outstanding chef from Shanghai. Fine ingredients, subtle flavours and flawless service. Don't miss the dim sum at lunch.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14491;Maison de Bacon;France;Antibes;664 boulevard de Bacon, Antibes, 06600, France;43.5696424;7.1391312;100;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Le Bâcon, an Antibes institution since 1948, has been transformed into the Maison de Bâcon. In the kitchens, Nicolas Davouze, formerly of Bocuse and Le Bristol, celebrates the house's signature dishes (such as rockfish soup, bouillabaisse, millefeuille), alongside a fine selection of fish grilled over a wood fire. Splendid view of the sea.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14492;Les Mérovingiens;France;Noisy-le-Grand;32 avenue Émile-Cossonneau, Noisy-le-Grand, 93160, France;48.848775;2.5567725;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Jacky Ribault (L'Ours in Vincennes, Qui Plume la Lune in the 11th arrondissement in Paris) opened this brasserie on the ground floor of a residential building in the centre of Noisy-le-Grand. It pays homage to the history of the town, which was built on a Merovingian and Carolingian necropolis. The menu proposes good classic dishes – slightly revamped – made from impeccable produce. Pleasant contemporary setting.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14493;Les Pieds Dans l'Eau;France;Saint-Langis-lès-Mortagne;28 chemin de la Folle-Entreprise, Saint-Langis-lès-Mortagne, 61400, France;48.5181909;0.5285387;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Built at the far end of the village and surrounded by fields, this old mill is also close to a lake: it is hard to imagine a more bucolic sight! A hard-working chef serves up modern bistro cuisine comprising generous mains (eg beef confit with turnips and lentils) and mouth-watering desserts (coffee panna cotta, ladyfinger sponges and mascarpone). Soak up the warm, laid-back atmosphere as you gaze out over the meadows from the pleasant terrace.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14495;Len'K - La Maison Bonnet;France;Grane;2 place du Champ-de-Mars, Grane, 26400, France;44.7314714;4.9234129;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Len'K is the bistronomic wing of the Bonnet establishment. Seated on the terrace shaded by plane trees or in the dining room, diners are in for a treat as they tuck into guinea fowl and olive terrine, or stuffed red mullet paired with a velvety shellfish emulsion. Laid-back service.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14496;L'Aparté;France;Limoges;39 boulevard Carnot, Limoges, 87000, France;45.8328394;1.2590322;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine;When Arthur Buisson, formerly second of the previous chef, took over the helm here, the transition was naturally smooth and seamless. While the interior remains unchanged, the culinary score is now more modern in spirit thanks to an abundant use of aromatic herbs and spices of all sorts. The chef’s globetrotting past can be tasted in the manifold flavours of his fresh, distinctive craftsmanship. Even better, he also turns out to be a dab pastry chef!;;[]
14500;Caffè Cosi - La trattoria de Bruno Caironi;France;Troyes;5 rue Marie-Pascale-Ragueneau, Troyes, 10000, France;48.2943755;4.0685415;84;true;true;Italian;Of Italian and Mediterranean inspiration, this colourful contemporary trattoria, housed in a former art gallery, overlooks a cobbled courtyard. We fell in love with the risotto with French green peas and different textures of guanciale – to die for! Before leaving, pop into the gourmet grocery store and stock up on first-rate Italian goodies.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14501;Chez Mon Jules;France;Vesc;5 rue Étienne-de-Vesc, Vesc, 26220, France;44.521423;5.151026;97;false;true;Country cooking;In the deliciously homely dining room decked in miscellaneous paraphernalia, you will be treated to tasty regional fare presented in two season-driven menus. Examples include homemade rennet with foie gras or lacquered pork belly from Dieulefit with regional veggies. In fine weather, take a seat on the shaded terrace and savour the knockout view.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14502;La Grangée;France;Alluy;Le Bourg, Alluy, 58110, France;47.0338345;3.6405428;56;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Jean-Baptiste Girard, a local lad and enthusiastic champion of his region, and his Japanese born wife, Maiko, have turned this village inn around. Local produce (Bourbonnais Charolais beef, organic veg from Rouy, Vandenesse poultry) and what the chef picks at the weekends take centre stage on the menu. The bread with wild garlic is out of this world. Attentive service, lovely tableware by a local artisan. Heavenly!;Terrace;[]
14503;La Table du Château Gratien;France;Saumur;94 route de Montsoreau, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2489139;-0.0504435;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the landscaped grounds of the Gratien and Meyer wine estate, this adorable late 19C château oozes character and cachet – herringbone parquet, glittering chandeliers and a fireplace. The cuisine deftly showcases the region's fine produce – white asparagus, black truffle and Val de Loire potatoes. Herbs from the garden, excellent home-made bread, warm madeleines served with coffee. A taste of the good life.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
14504;Monsieur P;France;Lyon;8 place des Célestins, Lyon, 69002, France;45.759541;4.8317011;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;On Place des Célestins, Monsieur P is the stomping ground of good food lovers. In the kitchen, Florent Poulard, who trained at the Paul Bocuse Institute and honed his skills in top houses, deftly prepares tasty modern cuisine. He loves to work with vegetables (after a stint with Alain Passard) and whole fish and cuts of meat. Love at first bite!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14505;La Petite École;France;Vergongheon;Rilhac, Vergongheon, 43360, France;45.3596976;3.3497956;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant moved into the premises of the former village school a few years ago. The delicate, flavoursome cuisine is definitely worth an A. Ten out of ten, too, for the chef, a lover of fine produce, who concocts precise, succulent recipes. Even better, it is excellent value for money - if only our school canteen had been like this!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14506;Bistrot Loiseau du Morvan;France;Saulieu;Hostellerie de la Tour d’Auxois, 5 avenue Bernard-Loiseau, Saulieu, 21210, France;47.2801283;4.2313936;57;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Opposite the Loiseau family’s legendary Côte d’Or restaurant, this handsome 17C edifice is both a supremely comfortable traditional hostelry and a bistro, offering an appetising more casual alternative to its fine dining parent establishment. Here, local and regional recipes take pride of place, such as eggs in a red wine sauce or chicken à la Gaston Gérard. The rotunda dining room, which leads onto a terrace, is the epitome of country chic with old terracotta tiled flooring and a glorious timber ceiling, all of which in an unabashed, full-on Burgundy style.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14507;La Côte des Monts Damnés;France;Chavignol;Place de l'Orme, Chavignol, 18300, France;47.3376267;2.7975372;55;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Developed entirely around the wines of this family-owned estate, the bistronomic menu is flanked by some of the house signature dishes: tagliatelle with Chavignol goat's cheese, hot soufflé… Damnably delicious! Comfortable rooms for longer stays.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14508;L'Orangerie des Trois Roys;France;Rambouillet;4 rue Raymond-Poincaré, Rambouillet, 78120, France;48.646023;1.818882;20;false;true;Seafood;L'Orangerie is a gorgeous setting with sculptures and verdant plants beneath the glass roof, club armchairs in the dining area and a charming shaded terrace. Here you will be received like a king. Fish and seafood are given pride of place: monkfish with green curry and coconut milk, perfectly cooked sole meunière. Pastries from Chez Francis (a well-known local artisan).;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14509;La Bourdasso;France;Pradelles-en-Val;La Bourdasse, Pradelles-en-Val, 11220, France;43.149837;2.497174;46;true;false;Italian;This lovely traditional building tucked away in Les Corbières has been infused with the energy of an Italian family who fell in love with the region. Authentic Italian cuisine: divine homemade mozzarella (with milk from their own buffaloes, brought over from Italy!), pasta and bread made with ancient wheat, also home grown. The spacious terrace is ideal to appreciate the lovely countryside.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14510;Olhabidea;France;Sare;270 Olhako bidea, Sare, 64310, France;43.31556;-1.5556;86;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In this 16C Basque farmhouse you can enjoy simple and unpretentious dishes prepared using ingredients fresh from the vegetable garden. Opt to eat in the hushed atmosphere of either the salon or the library. The guestrooms are overflowing with interesting objects and keepsakes. Outside, you can wander around 4ha of parkland planted with maples, conifers and camellias. Quite charming!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14511;Le Chai;France;Sainte-Marie-de-Ré;5 place d'Antioche, Sainte-Marie-de-Ré, 17740, France;46.1526199;-1.3158921;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Beautifully located on Sainte-Marie-de-Ré market square, this laidback eatery offers bistronomic fare with a distinct preference for local veg from mainly organic small market gardeners. The frequently changing concise menu stars seasonal ingredients, together with local fish and offal. Everything is fresh, well executed and good value for money, illustrated by a tender slab of pearlescent haddock or a 64°C poached egg in a creamy mushroom sauce topped with crispy bacon pieces.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14513;Les Lilas;France;Vagney;12 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Vagney, 88120, France;48.0124369;6.7156753;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the village at the foot of the Vosges, this large salmon - pink building by the roadside is impossible to miss! Diners are warmly welcomed by Armelle, in the handsome Art deco conservatory, while Lionel, in the kitchens, turns out tasty, contemporary dishes with a sprinkling of creative touches. Pleasant terrace.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14514;Soces;France;Paris;32 rue de la Villette, Paris, 75019, France;48.8763595;2.3876991;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A gem of a Parisian brasserie, where Marius de Ponfilly, formerly chef at Clamato, has teamed up with Kevin Deulio. Previously at Bar Vendôme in The Ritz, the latter has taken to the restaurant floor like a duck to water. The pair have found a formula that is as irreverent as it is on point: choice cuts of meat and plates to be shared between friends (aka soces in Parisian slang), not forgetting their trademark fish and seafood… We recommend the Pyrenean trout and its indulgent basil sauce, or the delicious wedge clams from Le Guilvinec in a spicy parsley sauce.;;[]
14516;AGA;France;Cadillac;7 rue Porte-de-la-Mer, Cadillac, 33410, France;44.6365674;-0.320726;47;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Alexandre Goniak and Gerie Jenner met in Australia but opened their first venture in a small country town on the banks of the Garonne just two minutes from a medieval gateway. The contemporary bistro menu illustrates the chef’s spot-on craftsmanship and flair for devising intelligent recipes based on seasonal availability, illustrated by loin of pork with Paimpol cranberry beans, bacon cream, fluffy mashed potato and roast cauliflower. Casual, smiling welcome and a genuine desire to share and inform, in particular regarding the wines.;Air conditioning;[]
14517;L'Alto;France;Villemur-sur-Tarn;980 chemin de Pellausy, Villemur-sur-Tarn, 31340, France;43.8551296;1.4561004;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this pretty pink-brick château tucked away in the countryside, the kitchen uses only high-quality ingredients with a renewed look at local produce. Highly contrasted flavours, like this fillet of wild seabass with shellfish and a rhubarb emulsion… L’Alto orchestrates a fine-tuned culinary score and an equally musical interior, with a sculpture of a saxophone and a swimming pool in the shape of a violin!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14518;Riviera;France;Cannes;Carlton Cannes, 58 boulevard de la Croisette, Cannes, 06400, France;43.5492958;7.0272085;69;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The legendary luxury hotel, which celebrated its 110th anniversary in 2023, now has its own marble-clad restaurant with a superb terrace overlooking the Croisette. In an opulent-feeling dining room where white meets black, the tables set with Gien porcelain are in line with time-honoured tradition of French table arts. The chef's table opposite the open kitchen also draws the eye. Everything else meets the standard set by your surroundings: Mediterranean cuisine made from top-quality local and seasonal ingredients, the calibre of service, with meat and fish cut at your table. You'll enjoy an excellent rack of Alpilles lamb with vegetables and jus, and a remarkable St Honoré cake with vanilla caramel and walnut pieces.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14519;Hinoki;France;Brest;6 rue des 11-Martyrs, Brest, 29200, France;48.39088;-4.483675;56;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;A real Japanese restaurant in Brest! Hinoki is run by a Breton chef who is deeply passionate about Japanese cuisine. Locally caught fish are selected with minute attention to detail. A word to the wise: opt for a place at the counter (ten covers) for an experience that goes beyond mere dining, as the chef creates his sushi and maki in full view of diners seated here. You will definitely feel a sense of privilege!;Counter dining;[]
14520;Nonos par Paul Pairet;France;Paris;Le Crillon, 10 place de la Concorde, Paris, 75008, France;48.8673;2.32114;27;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In addition to L'Écrin, Hotel Crillon on the Place de la Concorde has this smart brasserie with an Art Deco interior in its portfolio. The chef entrusted with devising its menu is Paul Pairet, well known to the French at this point in time. He pays homage to the grills of his childhood (in the form of a fine selection of matured meats) and brasserie classics (oysters, tartare, Caesar salad, sole meunière etc). And, it must be said, the bill is affordable for such a place. Their sole objective is to create good food out of good ingredients.;Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14521;Le Madeleine par Cyril Coutin;France;Verneuil-d'Avre-et-d'Iton;206 rue de la Madeleine, Verneuil-d'Avre-et-d'Iton, 27130, France;48.7400545;0.9260967;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This charming little restaurant has been completely restored by its new owners, chef Cyril Coutin and his wife. Behind the shopfront, you'll find a delightful space in which old – stonework, exposed beams – meets new (contemporary emerald green feature wall). In his cuisine, the chef channels all his skills into preparing seasonal produce (eg courgette, fennel, peach, verbena) into dishes that are sure to appeal, such as the beautiful slice of turbot with fennel confit and a pesto of capers, lemon and shallots. Friendly, smiling service.;Wheelchair access;[]
14522;Soul Kitchen;France;Beaune;1 rue Rousseau-Deslandes, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0249576;4.8390055;78;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;“Let me sleep all night in your soul kitchen” hauntingly sang Jim Morrison on the Doors’ first album and you can always ask Mathieu Guennal, the owner-chef who works alone in this dinky (12 seats only) downtown eatery in Beaune, if he’s willing to put you up! Mathieu works with local producers (chalked up on the blackboard) and cheerfully dishes up soul-warming, heartfelt nosh, as good as it is unfussy (such as slow-cooked pork belly, a ginger reduction and gratin of helianthus) in two gloriously priced €30 menus (one of which changes weekly). Take a seat and soak up the friendly, casual vibe of this small eatery with wooden floors and a raftered ceiling in the company of a generous chef.;Air conditioning;[]
14523;Le Lys;France;Courchevel;Lys Martagon, 464 route de Bellecôte, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.4119533;6.6374142;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in a luxury boutique hotel, this restaurant with its panoramic window boasts an Art deco-inspired decor: vintage light fittings, glass roof panels and a superb collection of Lalique vases. Comfortably seated in a chic yet cosy dining room, diners can sample a lineup of dishes in the zeitgeist lovingly crafted from first-class ingredients. Highly appealing wine list.;Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14524;Le P'tit Roseau;France;Issoire;2 avenue de la Gare, Issoire, 63500, France;45.5438087;3.2534589;98;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Between the railway station and the picturesque René Cassin Square, Jérémy Bonhivers crafts an inspired culinary score. Delicate, tasty recipes, subtly perfumed with flowers, herbs and young shoots set the scene for colourful, exquisitely plated dishes. To be sampled either in the minimalist dining room or, weather permitting, on the covered terrace and patio abutting the square.;Terrace;[]
14525;Bloom;France;Paris;99 rue Jouffroy-d'Abbans, Paris, 75017, France;48.882068;2.3017157;72;false;true;Vegan, Japanese;"Bloom" is an apt name for a restaurant that serves plant-based sushi! Crispy breaded rice delicately dressed in vinegar, brunoise of shiitake, oyster mushroom and avocado, futo maki and pesto sauce, vegetable gyoza with kimchi sauce: Mexican chef Christian Ventura is committed to protecting natural resources and has risen to the challenge thanks to an array of delicious and dynamic dishes. Ingredients selected from small producers, including for the cocktails, a natural wine list and a fine range of sake. The serene interior plays on different textures of wood.;;[]
14528;L'Épicurien;France;Périgueux;1 rue du Conseil, Périgueux, 24000, France;45.1857827;0.7221377;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This quaint old house in the heart of Périgueux provides the perfect foil for Gilles Labbé's assuredly epicurean cooking. It is clear that careful work goes into the precisely crafted recipes including the inspired vegetable dishes. The menu features quality Aubrac and Salers meats matured for six weeks on site. A master class of delicate craftsmanship and delicious food. Particularly attentive and enthusiastic front-of-house team.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14529;Le Saint-Nicolas - Au Coin du Feu;France;Megève;252 route de Rochebrune, Megève, 74120, France;45.8534432;6.6153107;77;true;false;Creative;Snail ravioli from Magland, guinea fowl from the Ain, cheese trolley (100% Savoyard), baba in hay: young chef Marvin Lance, previously Julien Gatillon's sous-chef at Le 1920, is bringing a breath of fresh air to this pleasant chalet in Megève in the form of his technical skills and ambition. A restaurant whose star is in the ascendant in this ski resort!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14533;Étude;France;Aix-en-Provence;24 rue de l'Aumône-Vieille, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.5283527;5.446453;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Non-conformist chef Loïc Pétri cut his teeth in leading Parisian establishments (Jean-François Piège, Joël Robuchon) before going back to his roots in the south of France. In the heart of the historical part of Aix, in his intimate, contemporary-style restaurant with just 12 covers, he lets his inspiration run riot with a single set menu guided by the seasons. With bold associations and a savvy use of oils, spices and chillies, his free-spirited cooking elevates the finest ingredients, such as bass, lobster and sweetbreads, which are treated with care and dexterity. You can sense the commitment to a job well done and spoiling guests, as reflected in both the dishes and the service!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14534;Le Pastel;France;Toulon;20 rue Victor Micholet - Square Léon Vérane, Toulon, 83000, France;43.121433;5.930486;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Just a stone's throw from the harbour, this restaurant is a great success. With dishes such as semi-salted skrei with mussels, spinach, a shellfish jus with curry and lemon leaf, the chef's cuisine is very much in tune with the times. A cordial welcome and professional service from the owner.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14536;Schorre;France;Saint-Valery-sur-Somme;2 quai Lejoille, Saint-Valery-sur-Somme, 80230, France;50.180726;1.6439855;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The top floor of this entirely revamped 18C salt barn is home to a contemporary, ‘unfinished’, stripped-back restaurant which commands a panoramic view over the Somme Bay. According to the dictionary, a schorre (or a salt marsh) refers to an “upper coastal intertidal zone of thick mud, covered by grass and regularly flooded by high tides”. Our poached turbot was flanked by a crisp, salty salad of salt marsh plants (samphire, maritime asters, halimione). Chef François-Xavier Sailly regularly renews his creative gourmet score, illustrated by white asparagus and a tarragon-flavoured hollandaise sauce or a pear and Jerusalem artichoke dessert.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14537;Augustine - La Table du Château;France;Maffliers;Allée des Marronniers, Maffliers, 95560, France;49.0746056;2.3027906;22;false;true;Classic Cuisine;In a handsome 19C abode near Montmorency Forest, this restaurant aims to uphold French art de vivre: period tableware and furniture, gleaming silverware and copper and high ceilings – all of which in a plush muted interior dominated by wood. The food is suitably classical and generous, whilst traversing the annals of French cookery: pâté en croûte, rabbit cooked in mustard and rice pudding. A few rooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
14538;Le Refuge;France;Megève;2615 route du Leutaz, Megève, 74120, France;45.8236042;6.5999476;22;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;After a hike to Le Leutaz, enjoy smiling service at this charming wood-panelled restaurant extended by a veranda as well as a terrace in fine weather. Tuck into generous and indulgent dishes taken from a menu that includes some of the absolute classics (egg with green lentils, morels and shavings of foie gras), without forgetting the perennial Savoie specialties.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14539;Signature;France;Combloux;62 chemin de la Promenade, Combloux, 74920, France;45.8951561;6.6451094;32;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;From the threshold of this listed 19C farmhouse, you can see Mont Blanc on the horizon. With its mountain-style interior (wood panelling, whitewashed walls, parquet flooring) and traditional cuisine by Florent Meyer (who has worked with Flocons de Sel chef Emmanuel Renaut), the restaurant is an instant hit… This is thanks, in particular, to the vin jaune sauce that envelops the delicious free-range chicken supreme, or the moreish tartiflette with a nod to the village's terroir – a signature starter. Plus a warm welcome awaits you!;;[]
14540;Inari;France;Arles;16 place Voltaire, Arles, 13200, France;43.67989;4.6314;24;false;true;Fusion, Creative;Having worked in some emblematic Parisian restaurants (Ze Kitchen Galerie, Saturne, Septime), chef Céline Pham, an adept of pop-up restaurants, has set up shop in the heart of Arles in a former chapel done up in a vintage vein. It is a pleasure to resample her spot-on, tasty French-Vietnamese fusion cuisine, in which vegetables, as one might imagine, often reign supreme. Examples include a fillet of red mullet, spelt bread, confit of tomatoes, stock of red mullet with garrigue oil, yellow courgettes and chrysanthemums. Concise natural wine list.;Terrace;[]
14542;Perception;France;Paris;53 rue Blanche, Paris, 75009, France;48.8811877;2.3315174;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A friendly and contemporary bistro, with exposed stone and dark green walls, mirrors and velvet banquettes. A Korean chef, who is passionate about French gastronomy, creates modern cuisine with occasional nods to his home country, and it proves to be a winning formula: for example, his starter of burrata, duck breast, basil/arugula pesto and sesame. In the evening, he pulls out all the stops, with premium ingredients and more sophisticated dishes (and a tasting menu).;;[]
14543;L'Osmose;France;Pleudihen-sur-Rance;7 place de l'Église, Pleudihen-sur-Rance, 22690, France;48.5106055;-1.9517519;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Whiting-pout marinated in Kerala curry spice, white radish glazed in soy and samphire or pistachio-flavoured kouign-amann with halva ice cream… Former Michelin-star chef, Ludovic Dirscherl, celebrates the osmosis between Brittany and more exotic flavours from further afield, particularly in his tasting menu. The small dining room sports rough wood panelling, bare stone and a fireplace.;;[]
14544;Liquide;France;Paris;39 rue de l'Arbre-Sec, Paris, 75001, France;48.8610009;2.3424224;64;false;false;Creative;The quirky decor is delightfully amusing: a horn chandelier and mismatched armchairs, chairs or sofas, plus a 12m-long marble table d'hôte by Philippe Starck. Trendy, but friendly and ideal for hanging out with the mates, sharing dishes, sampling cocktails and a fine bottle (or two). The brainchild of Matthias Marc, variety and creativity set the culinary scene at Liquide.;Terrace;[]
14545;Pétrelle;France;Paris;34 rue Pétrelle, Paris, 75009, France;48.88087;2.34643;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Chef Lucie Boursier-Mougenot and sommelier Luca Danti, formerly at Caves Legrand, have revamped this restaurant once frequented by celebrities. In a romantic and intimate boudoir setting that is decorated with flea-market pieces, the chef serves lovely, delicate and healthy market-fresh cuisine with strong Mediterranean influences. Good wine cellar with over 150 references, for all budgets.;;[]
14546;brut.;France;Guérande;16 rue des Prés-Garniers, à Saillé, Guérande, 44350, France;47.2952613;-2.430927;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a traditional salt workers' village in the heart of the salt marshes, this picturesque white house with snug, cosy dining rooms is open for business. Japanese chef Takashi Aoki crafts a creatively subdued Gallic line-up that showcases the season. The wine list is extremely well curated and the vast majority of the wines are available by the glass.;Wheelchair access;[]
14547;MatCha;France;Cucuron;Montée du Château-Vieux, Cucuron, 84160, France;43.7736714;5.4396988;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Everything is fresh and made from scratch: the veg comes from small, local growers and the meat and poultry is free range. An enticing menu tailored to modern appetites. Smiling service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14548;Pilgrim;France;Paris;8 rue Nicolas-Charlet, Paris, 75015, France;48.8425254;2.313917;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Hideki Nishi (owner of Neige d'Été in Paris) has entrusted Yurika Kitano with the cuisine of this restaurant near Montparnasse. In a central and slightly raised kitchen, the chef crafts her elegant, delicate dishes, like tiny masterpieces influenced by France and Japan. This paradise for our tastebuds looks all set to become a place of pilgrimage for foodies.;Air conditioning;[]
14549;Le Landemer;France;Urville-Nacqueville;2 rue des Douanes, Urville-Nacqueville, 50460, France;49.67799;-1.7601;40;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This fine stone house with a shale roof has an undeniable charm. Inside, a pleasant young Dutch chef cooks up modern cuisine with a dose of creativity, out of which he devises several courses according to his whims. The ingredients are exclusively from Normandy – not least fish, vegetables, wild herbs and flowers. The dishes are precise and on point, as are the food and drink pairings (the drinks, too, are local). The restaurant has a breathtaking view of the sea and coastline, as do the delightful guestrooms – it would be a shame not to book an overnight stay!;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14552;La Fine Bouche;France;Bordeaux;30 rue du Hâ, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.83612;-0.57696;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The chef's interest in regional traditions and his creative spirit are reflected in his use of the capuchin, an ancient utensil with a cast iron cone attached to a long rod, in which pieces of bacon are melted and used to flambée his scallops, lending them a slight grilled and smoked taste. With its hardwood floors, mouldings and exposed stonework, the tastefully refurbished dining room makes for an intimate dinner setting.;Terrace;[]
14553;Sushi Shunei;France;Paris;3 rue Audran, Paris, 75018, France;48.8851108;2.3357826;42;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Located on Montmartre’s hill, this joint sports an elegant, minimalist interior that celebrates the aesthetic codes of Japanese restaurants: light wooden furnishings, a long counter and an amazing origami-inspired ceiling by an interior design firm. Chizuko Kimura and the Sushi master Takeshi Morooka pursue the legacy of Shunei Kimura, who made this eatery such a success. The omakase menu comes in two versions, which must be chosen when you book. Both embark the diner on a genuine sensorial experience courtesy of razor-sharp nigiris, a truly exceptional selection of fish, expert handiwork and a range of subtle seasonings, without forgetting Japan’s unique vision of hospitality that is both unobtrusive and highly attentive.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
14554;Les Têtes d'Ail;France;Toulouse;6 rue de la Fonderie, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.5946982;1.4435657;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This is the place for wholesome bistronomic fare from southwest France! Market-fresh, flavoursome dishes that keep pace with the seasons, well-selected local produce, excellent value for money (particularly at lunchtime), all of which in a busy shopping high street near Place des Carmes. Invariably packed, which is always a good sign!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14555;Kaito;France;Megève;Four Seasons Megève, 373 chemin des Follières, Megève, 74120, France;45.8468823;6.6443034;43;true;true;Japanese, Fusion;At the Four Seasons Hotel, flawlessly fresh sashimi, tataki and sushi rub shoulders with delicately crafted alpine specialties. Fusion cuisine to be enjoyed on the terrace commanding a splendid view of the slopes or in the softly lit interior.;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14556;Le Lion et l’Agneau;France;Nantes;40 rue Fouré, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2115244;-1.5469286;26;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A lion and a lamb adorn the coat of arms of Auch, which is the birthplace of chef Thierry Lebé. His bistronomic score is founded on top-drawer produce: Janzé chicken, cuttlefish, Pénestin mussels… The lunchtime menu is a steal.;Terrace;[]
14557;Lume;France;Bordeaux;3 rue des Faussets, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8407101;-0.5704749;48;false;false;Italian;A 14-seater restaurant with an intimate atmosphere that is due in part to the candlelight (lume in Italian). Venetian chef Riccardo Suppa regales guests with an appetising single set menu that gives pride of place to seafood and organic vegetables. Everything is made in-house, from the pasta to the bread prepared using heirloom wheat flour. Alice, the chef's partner, is an accomplished hostess who knows her way around a wine list featuring carefully selected Italian labels. On the menu: cicchetti (Venetian canapés), scallop crudo, paccheri with chanterelles, vanilla panna cotta etc.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
14558;Le 1825 - La Table;France;Gesté;Domaine de la Brûlaire - 404 La Brûlaire - Gesté, Gesté, 49600, France;47.1841917;-1.094786;91;false;true;Creative;Hidden deep in the countryside, this small 19C château is home to an elegant restaurant and a number of guestrooms. Housed in the converted orangery, the vast space boasts high ceilings, exposed stonework, trendy furnishings and picture windows overlooking the courtyard. The chef's refreshing creativity makes itself felt in dishes that contain aromatic herbs from the garden – for instance, the pollack with shiso leaves and a sauce evoking the flavours of Thailand.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
14559;Halle aux Grains;France;Paris;Bourse de Commerce, 2 rue de Viarmes, Paris, 75001, France;48.8629409;2.3424271;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Not only is the old corn exchange home to part of the Pinault Collection, it also houses a highly creative restaurant. In homage to the history of the building, Michel and Sébastien Bras take seeds, cereals and legumes as their starting point and cook up healthy and contemporary cuisine. Be sure to sample a tasty dessert, such as their take on the Paris-Brest: choux pastry meets pumpkin seed cream in a crunchy praline affair. Unbeatable view of the rooftops of Paris.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14560;La Table du Marquis au Château de Maubreuil;France;Carquefou;Allée de Maubreuil, Carquefou, 44470, France;47.2972481;-1.4651414;36;false;true;Contemporary;The illustrious history and pageantry of this romantic castle dating from the 19C can be felt both in the grounds, dotted with works of art, and in the plush, stylish interior (huge mirrors, carved fireplaces, parquet floors and Napoleon III-style furnishings). All that remains is to enjoy the well-crafted food, fully in tune with today’s tastes and palates.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14561;Kaiseki;France;Aix-en-Provence;Château de la Gaude, 3959 route des Pinchinats, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.568895;5.4785435;50;false;false;Japanese, Fusion;In the magical setting of an 18C bastide, the Kaiseki upholds Japanese gourmet dining traditions with its “Omakase – The Great Journey” tasting menu that gives the chefs carte blanche. Chefs Matthieu Dupuis Baumal and Kazunari Noda have pooled their skill and talent to create a genuine culinary voyage poised between France and Japan. The next-door brasserie, Le K, offers a varied, more affordable score.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14562;La Canourgue;France;Montpellier;Place de la Canourgue, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6118097;3.8747902;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Established in the lavish inner courtyard of Hotel Richer de Belleval under a glass roof, this bistro of the Pourcel brothers is the quintessence of stylish: cornices, mouldings, crystal chandeliers… The food is equally first rate: beautifully crafted, rich in flavour and just the right dose of creativity. A genuine pleasure.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14565;Roscanvec;France;Vannes;19 rue des Halles, Vannes, 56000, France;47.6572181;-2.7579707;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is set in the historical surroundings of a 17C mansion built by the Lord of Roscanvec, royal council. The pared-back dining area is furnished in a contemporary style. The chef cooks up dishes that cater to modern tastes, while the two Kaczorowski sisters provide professional, smiling and attentive service. Pleasant guestrooms are available, should you wish to prolong the experience.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14566;Biscotte;France;Paris;22 rue Desnouettes, Paris, 75015, France;48.8361274;2.2913415;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Pauline and Maximilien, two alumni of the most prestigious establishments (Le Bristol, Lasserre, Arpège), have set up their own place near Porte de Versailles. Convivial bistro interior, large atelier windows separating the kitchen, tasty and studied dishes: all the ingredients are in place for an enjoyable experience.;;[]
14567;Le Boeuf Noisette;France;Saumur;29 rue Molière, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2608413;-0.0770189;89;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Take a seat in this vintage - style bistro, dotted with benches, marble tables and mirrors to sample a brief, well - designed menu focused on regional produce (particularly “Rouge des prés” beef). Ideally located behind the theatre, parallel with the Loir embankment and close to a large carpark. First - class, short food supply chain produce.;;[]
14569;Château du Bost;France;Bellerive-sur-Allier;27 rue de Beauséjour, Bellerive-sur-Allier, 03700, France;46.1121115;3.3937857;80;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A few minutes from Vichy, in peaceful grounds, this château with towers and a water-filled moat (15C-19C) offers a contemporary and cosy decor, complemented by a beautiful terrace and some comfortable guestrooms. The restaurant has a refined setting and serves tasty seasonal cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14571;La Ferme Auberge - Domaine de La Font des Pères;France;Le Beausset;1306 chemin de Pontillaou, Le Beausset, 83330, France;43.1784115;5.8199983;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Provence’s hilly terraces, the terrace of this Farm Inn commands a staggering view over the valley and the Sainte-Baume range. Produce from the estate takes pride of place on the menu (the chickens have the run of the pinewood, orchard, olive grove, herb and vegetable garden), which is healthily and creatively crafted by the chef and paired with estate wines. Pretty rooms and cottages also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14573;Maison Chabran - Le 45ème;France;Pont-de-l'Isère;26 avenue du 45ème-Parallèle, Pont-de-l'Isère, 26600, France;45.0041135;4.8711217;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;As you motor south down the iconic N7 highway, why not stop off in this verdant spot that boasts a shaded terrace overlooking the garden, which is blissful in fine weather? This bistronomic eatery is a pleasant alternative to the parent establishment, a renowned temple of regional gastronomy. In its younger sibling, you will sample light, unstuffy dishes presented in a series of set menus. A few guestrooms are available should you wish to relax for longer.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14574;Côté Sud;France;Uchaux;3395 route d'Orange, Uchaux, 84100, France;44.20862;4.80087;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You are bound to enjoy your visit to this stone house with a garden and pleasant terrace. The chef whips up intelligent recipes packed with regional tributes. Examples include a 64°C poached egg, mushrooms and foie gras, or a breast of guinea fowl marinated in garden thyme and garnished with sweet potatoes and an olive oil sauce. The wine list focuses on organic and biodynamic wines. Charming service.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14575;La Tête au Loup;France;Le Pin-au-Haras;Lieu-dit la Tête-au-Loup, Le Pin-au-Haras, 61310, France;48.7390573;0.1581694;79;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Stéphane and Agnès Mabille greet guests warmly in their spruce, traditional inn, appointed in a rustic vein. The seasoned chef concocts homemade terrines and assorted Normandy delicacies. In fine weather, make a beeline for the garden and terrace, which overlook the horses grazing in the next-door world-famous Haras du Pin stud farm. Unstarched, friendly vibe.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14576;La Bodega;France;Melun;18 quai Hippolyte-Rossignol, Melun, 77000, France;48.5354351;2.6557384;53;true;false;Spanish;Diners come here for the atmosphere and tastes of Spain, especially Asturias, where the family who own the place hail from. On the menu, you'll find top-notch ingredients, succulent Iberian recipes – Iberian pork pluma, paella bodega (chicken, chorizo, cuttlefish, mussels and prawns), salt cod with aïoli, delicious turrón for dessert – as well as some daily specials. You won't be disappointed!;Wheelchair access;[]
14580;Le Soufflot;France;Meursault;8 route Nationale 74, Meursault, 21190, France;46.9740789;4.7846431;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Jérémy Pèze rustles up delicate, appetising, gourmet fare in a former winegrower’s house, which, unsurprisingly, also boasts a stunning wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
14581;Cécile;France;Toulouse;43 place des Carmes, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.5974291;1.4444186;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the lively, bustling Carmes neighbourhood, a close-knit young team welcomes you to this modern bistro with a wood-decked veranda, large open kitchen and contemporary decor. The short menu is inspired by a real mix of cultures: exotic touches are incorporated into dishes such as Thai duck tartare and farm-reared pork loin with mango and pomegranate.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14582;La Mère Hamard;France;Semblançay;2 rue du Petit-Bercy, Semblançay, 37360, France;47.4986487;0.5792682;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;This stone-built inn, which opened in 1903, is a genuine institution. The delightful dining room is flanked by a welcoming terrace shaded by wisteria, ideal to sample delicate, generous dishes, tinged with the occasional exotic influence. Attentive welcome and a few guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14583;La Terrasse;France;Saugues;11 cours du Docteur-Gervais, Saugues, 43170, France;44.9596909;3.5475282;80;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Do not worry, the Beast of Gévaudan is no more! However, if you are as hungry as the wolf, this place is for you. The chef, Cyril Tardy, cooks a contemporary interpretation of cuisine du terroir using good, very fresh, locally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
14584;Maison Chabran - La Grande Table;France;Pont-de-l'Isère;26 avenue du 45ème-Parallèle, Pont-de-l'Isère, 26600, France;45.0040651;4.8710209;82;false;true;Modern Cuisine;By the side of the legendary N7 holiday road of France, this family business has come a long way after its debut as a small bistro in the 1930s to what is now a culinary landmark. It continues to champion its own distinctive brand of tradition and modernity.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
14585;Auberge de Clochemerle;France;Vaux-en-Beaujolais;173 rue Gabriel-Chevallier, Vaux-en-Beaujolais, 69460, France;46.056396;4.594033;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You will feel right at home in the understated Auberge de Clochemerle in the heart of a picturesque winegrowing village. The "surprise menu" (only the ingredients are listed) stars seasonal ingredients. The cooking is spot on and tasty, apparently classical at first glance, but often scattered with unorthodox notes (spicy Japanese seasoning), Maury-chocolate sauce, etc.). Rather than restrict itself to a single region, the menu pays tribute to French cuisine in all its glory and diversity, illustrated by a Brittany starter of scallops and Guémené andouille sausage. A long-standing favourite with the locals, the establishment is equally popular with passing tourists and visitors. A few comfortable guestrooms available for overnight stays.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14586;Le Mermoz;France;Paris;16 rue Jean-Mermoz, Paris, 75008, France;48.8706592;2.3114589;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It is easy to see why this convivial neo-bistro located close to the Champs Elysées is always busy! Diners are won over by bistronomy-style cuisine that strikes a balance between tradition and modernity: impeccable produce, punchy, indulgent dishes and distinctive flavours. The reasonably priced wine list features an interesting selection of organic and natural wines.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14587;La Côte Vermeille;France;Port-Vendres;Quai du Fanal, Port-Vendres, 66660, France;42.519846;3.1109202;98;true;true;Seafood;This local institution boasts a breathtaking view of the port, especially from the stunning, first-floor terrace. The chef crafts light, colourful seafood cuisine with Mediterranean influences, cleverly underscored by spices and citrus fruits in a bid to showcase the catch of local fishing boats.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14588;Le Gentiane;France;Pinsaguel;7 rue du Cagire, Pinsaguel, 31120, France;43.493523;1.3965667;21;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Gentian root is lauded for various properties, one of which stimulates the appetite – true to its name, this place does just that! Nicolas Bachon and his father work in tandem in the kitchen, cooking up traditional dishes with a modern twist (such as the sautéed beef mignon). Service with a smile from their respective wives. During the week, the lunch menu is a real bargain!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14589;La Table de mon Père - Castel Beau Site;France;Ploumanach;Plage de Saint-Guirec, Ploumanach, 22700, France;48.8324607;-3.4862152;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Comfortably ensconced in this sleek, elegant interior, soak up the glow of the magnificent sunsets over Plage St Guirec. As you feast your eyes on the view, tuck into carefully presented, contemporary cuisine featuring ingredients of indisputably high quality, such as pigeon from Le Ménez Bré, monkfish, spider crab and white asparagus.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14590;Plume;France;Paris;24 rue Pierre-Leroux, Paris, 75007, France;48.8486942;2.3194714;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Born in Tunis, the chef brings a touch of diversity and plenty of talent to this small street near Le Bon Marché. Diners squeeze into this tiny bistro to tuck in to seamless cuisine that is perfectly in tune with the seasons, such as a silky cream of celeriac soup with an intense and slightly spicy taste! Reasonably priced lunch menu and ambitious tasting menu in the evening.;;[]
14591;Le Cheval d'Or;France;Paris;21 rue de la Villette, Paris, 75019, France;48.8757697;2.3873686;40;true;true;Asian;In the sleepy Jourdain neighbourhood in Upper Belleville, a brand-new team has taken over the reins of this golden horse, without changing the scenery (oriental red façade, polished concrete, whitewashed walls and open-plan kitchen). The eclectic Asian-inspired menu is jazzed up with nods to Gallic traditions, or is it the other way round? Examples: tofu and caviar consommé à la royale, barbajuan raviolis in sweet pepper sauce, tofu and shitake tortellini, stuffed duck à l’orange, vegetable cassoulet (100% vegetarian).;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
14592;Omija;France;Nantes;54 rue Fouré, Nantes, 44000, France;47.210365;-1.5472623;86;true;true;Creative;At the helm of his own restaurant since 2019 and with a splendid starred experience under his belt, Romain Bonnet crafts a creative surprise menu of Asian inspiration: the ‘omija’ is a Korean berry known to feature the five ‘flavours’ in perfect harmony. Romain is unswerving in his dedication to taste: radish and seaweed gnocchi brilliantly play on acidic notes as shrimp adds a well-judged spicy edge. Flawlessly cooked, gutsy stocks and irresistible big-boned sauces. The produce, mostly organic, is painstakingly sourced (common shrimp from la Cotinière, Oléron Island, line-caught pollack, Vendée squab). An infectiously cosy eatery with unstarched, yet seamless service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14593;Petrossian;France;Paris;13 boulevard de la Tour-Maubourg, Paris, 75007, France;48.8611745;2.3102282;88;true;true;Seafood;A legendary name in the hearts of caviar lovers since 1920, when the Petrossian brothers, of Armenian origin, began importing it. The restaurant honours the history of the house with "classic" caviar tasting, but also with well - thought - out dishes in which this delicacy appears in other forms (pressed, dried, matured, liquid).;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
14594;Le Bistrot du Paradou;France;Paradou;57 avenue de la Vallée-des-Baux, Paradou, 13520, France;43.72024;4.784601;20;false;true;Provençal;This inviting restaurant with blue shutters is a genuine local landmark. Telephone (only) bookings compulsory. The dish of the day changes daily, but comes back every week – e.g. cassoulet on Wednesdays, in the single set menu. On top of that, Provence's culinary repertory is celebrated with generous wholesome dishes, of the likes of aioli, spit-roast Bresse chicken and calf's head with ravigote sauce, to be devoured in a lively and laid-back vibe cultivated by the bubbly, unstarched front-of-house team. Wine and a generous cheeseboard are included in the price of the single set menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14595;Rhizome;France;Compiègne;6 rue des Pâtissiers, Compiègne, 60200, France;49.4182861;2.8263593;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The rhizome is an underground shoot full of energy resources that is the equivalent to a root for some plants. A name that cleverly references the return of this young Soissons couple to their Picardy roots, after stints in top establishments (Mère Brazier, Parisian Saturne, Auberge du Vert Mont). The name also depicts their lively and instinctive, market-fresh cuisine and regularly changing menu, together with the couple’s clear preference for local produce and organic and natural wines. A firm fixture on the local culinary scene and not only because of its (single) lunch set menu. We recommend booking.;;[]
14596;L'Intimiste - Auberge de Buellas;France;Buellas;10 route de Buesle, Buellas, 01310, France;46.2093534;5.1330035;70;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Buellas village, take a seat in the snug, plush dining room to sample polished, thoughtfully curated dishes presented in a single set menu that shines the spotlight on a seasonal ingredient: lobster, Bresse poultry, celery, etc. The Auberge Bressane de Buellas is more traditional in style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
14597;La Petite Ferme;France;Aix-en-Provence;7 avenue Victor-Hugo, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.52536;5.44621;69;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This chic contemporary brasserie run by Ronan Kernen, the chef-owner of Côté Cour, showcases dishes from all over the world as well as serving a wide choice of meat cooked over embers, spit-roasted or in a wood-fired oven.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14598;L'ArtYsan;France;Quissac;35 plan de la Gare, Quissac, 30260, France;43.9106936;4.0034535;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Yohann Boucard has turned the old station of Quissac into a fine establishment, sporting minimalist lines and iron work by local artisans… The food is equally enthralling, thanks to painstakingly selected ingredients and unusual, flavoursome combinations. Professional service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14599;Vista;France;La Croix-Valmer;Lily of the Valley, colline Saint-Michel, quartier de Gigaro, La Croix-Valmer, 83420, France;43.1880282;6.5948009;71;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The hotel, perched on an unspoilt hillside overlooking the sea, is divine, and the swish, yet funky restaurant is equally fantastic! Take a seat by the pool and bask in the exclusive vibe as you sample recipes by chef Vincent Maillard (shoulder of Sisteron lamb braised in savory or a chocolate and Piedmont hazelnut eclair). Valet parking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14600;Le Garde Champêtre;France;Gyé-sur-Seine;50 route des Riceys, Gyé-sur-Seine, 10250, France;48.0275466;4.4238131;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This former railway warehouse has been turned into a sustainable farm restaurant with greenhouses and an organic vegetable garden by a group of four partners judiciously teamed up with two local winegrowers. They serve fresh and fortifying cuisine, based on ingredients sourced locally or from the garden. A very pleasant locavore and ecological approach. A pleasant place.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14601;Les Chants d'Avril;France;Nantes;2 rue Laennec, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2124934;-1.5481385;17;false;false;Farm to table;The enthusiasm of chef Christophe François is infectious. Every day brings his own appealing and confident bistronomy-style take on market-fresh cuisine. Fine ingredients from the region are showcased in surprise set menus (without options), served in a pleasant bistro setting. As for the wine, try some of the surprising picks in their selection, to be tasted blind. A sociable experience!;Terrace;[]
14602;Le Bouchon;France;Nantes;7 rue Bossuet, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2171368;-1.5551009;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Appetising, up - to - the - minute food, reinvented daily, a prettily appointed interior (terracotta tile floors, old beams and mirrors) and the wonderful terrace, which is a haven of greenery in the town centre. It isn’t difficult to understand why this establishment is so popular with Nantes’ inhabitants!;Terrace;[]
14603;L'Art de Vivre;France;Narbonne;Château de L'Hospitalet, route de Narbonne-Plage, Narbonne, 11100, France;43.1679774;3.1145084;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At this vineyard nestled in the La Clape mountains, chef Laurent Chabert sources some of his ingredients (including aromatic herbs) from his own kitchen garden, and also uses fine local produce (organic for the most part). He creates colourful, fragrant dishes, such as grouper cooked over the embers of a barbecue, braised aubergine glazed with tomato juices… The food and wine pairings draw on a selection of bottles from the estate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14604;Culina Hortus;France;Lyon;38 rue de l'Arbre-Sec, Lyon, 69001, France;45.7667005;4.8374054;67;true;true;Vegetarian;This vegetarian restaurant offers beautifully crafted dishes that are unabashedly creative in a tasting set menu made with seasonal ingredients. The food is paired with a concise organic and biodynamic wine list, to enjoy in a snug, modern decor of wood, concrete, adobe.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14605;L'Essentiel;France;Saint-Jean-de-Luz;3 rue Vincent-Barjonnet, Saint-Jean-de-Luz, 64500, France;43.3916704;-1.6600074;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Off the beaten tourist track, chef Morgan Ortéga goes straight to the essentials: industrial loft interior, open kitchen, huge bay window, glazed wine cellar and leather bench seats. His talent and skill metamorphose market-fresh produce, enabling each ingredient to shout its name, to the delight of diners.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14606;Le Parvis;France;Saintes;12 quai de l'Yser, Saintes, 17100, France;45.7486653;-0.6314083;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This picturesque house on the banks of the Charente in downtown Saintes is where Pascal Yenk rustles up mouth - watering regional dishes using ingredients fresh from the market. Everything is homemade, including the sauces, to the delight of diners’ taste buds. Sheltered terrace in fine weather.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14607;L'Auberge de la Poule d'Or;France;Puymirol;52 rue Royale, Puymirol, 47270, France;44.1870331;0.7973294;26;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Part and parcel of its flagship, Michel Trama’s iconic gourmet restaurant, this Golden Hen (Poule d’Or) is a smart inn sporting old stone walls, a long central wooden table, the legs of which are adorned with lion’s heads, chandeliers and still-lifes... Michel’s son is in charge of the impeccable service. The menu reads like a culinary textbook of bistro classics: ox tail pie, calf’s head in poulette sauce, giant cream puffs with a dribble of caramel. Spot-on, confident cooking, flavoursome ingredients and heart-warming dishes in an authentic setting. A foodies’ gold mine!;;[]
14608;LAZU;France;Paris;47 rue Marguerite-de-Rochechouart, Paris, 75009, France;48.8790417;2.345426;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The chef was second in command to Bruno Doucet for three years at La Régalade St-Honoré – so he knows the ropes! Here, he serves up well-crafted bistronomy fare with inspired associations of high-quality seasonal ingredients. The menu changes weekly, but specialities such as caramelised veal sweetbreads and pâté with a potato crust have been permanent fixtures since the restaurant opened. Inviting atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14609;Chez Monsieur;France;Paris;11 rue du Chevalier-de-Saint-George, Paris, 75008, France;48.8686785;2.3250523;46;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The Parisian bistro in all its splendour (zinc countertop, velvet-upholstered wall seats, patterned tiles), with the immutable – and delicious! – cuisine that goes with it: Burgundy snails with white butter sauce, veal blanquette served in a casserole dish, not to mention a wide selection of wines from all over France.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
14610;Au Fil du Temps;France;Pernes-les-Fontaines;51 place Louis-Giraud, Pernes-les-Fontaines, 84210, France;43.9974611;5.0590418;30;false;true;Farm to table;In a pedestrian area, just opposite the old church, which has been turned into a cultural centre, this former grocery store is now a charming little restaurant. Sustainable agriculture is favoured, with well - packed dishes: for example, the beef carpaccio, slipper lobster jus, marinated seaweed and oyster fritters.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14614;La Deuvalière;France;Tours;18 rue de la Monnaie, Tours, 37000, France;47.3942317;0.6824887;36;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Julien and Alexandra have poured every ounce of their enthusiasm into successfully wooing local and visiting gourmets. Their seasonal cuisine is a treasure trove of culinary gems. The charm of their old country house, appointed with bare beams, terracotta tiled floors and a fireplace, together with the odd contemporary detail, further adds to the experience!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14615;L'Arche de Meslay;France;Parçay-Meslay;14 rue des Ailes, Parçay-Meslay, 37210, France;47.4385922;0.7138055;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The surroundings are quickly forgotten (a business estate), as you concentrate on the fine and fresh food, truly bursting with flavours. One case in point is the speciality of the Breton chef: Tours - style bouillabaisse – packed with red mullet, scorpion fish, pork rillons and andouillette.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14616;La Réserve à la Plage;France;Ramatuelle;Chemin de l'Épi, Ramatuelle, 83350, France;43.2213528;6.6619433;91;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The Pampelonne beach version of the Réserve Ramatuelle casts its magical seaside spell in a smart, casual interior signed by Philippe Starck. Normandy-born chef Nicolas Cantrel has bewitched the clientele with his Riviera-inspired cuisine, which features carefully sourced meat, the local catch of the day and an array of top-notch produce.;Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
14618;Villa Morelia;France;Jausiers;Avenue des Mexicains, Jausiers, 04850, France;44.4187094;6.733555;24;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Villa Morelia exudes a certain discreet charm. The setting offsets the refined, tasty and inventive market - based cuisine. You can really taste the freshness and savour the flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14619;Petit Boutary;France;Paris;16 rue Jacquemont, Paris, 75017, France;48.8879155;2.3223691;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Petit Boutary is certainly living up to the standard set for it by Boutary, its Left Bank counterpart. In this refined bistro, with its chequered floor, zinc-topped bar, leather-clad banquette seating and hanging light bulbs, modern, creative cuisine is served in the form of a single menu with several courses.;Wheelchair access;[]
14620;Bistrot 1954;France;Plougonvelin;7 place Saint-Tanguy, Plougonvelin, 29217, France;48.330871;-4.7710337;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Overlooking the grandiose scenery of Pointe Saint-Mathieu, this bistro makes your mouth water: a terrace in the fresh sea air, contemporary decor combining untreated wood and rattan furniture, and dishes from the chef, who lovingly showcases Brittany's fresh produce in his dishes: from shellfish and fish to buckwheat and seaweed.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14621;Le Quai de Champagne;France;Troyes;1 bis quai des Comtes-de-Champagne, Troyes, 10000, France;48.3011402;4.0758742;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;On the banks of the Cordé, this 19C mansion, tastefully refurbished in a modern vibe with two large dining rooms whose windows overlook the leafy, tree-lined garden, provides the perfect foil to chef Jean-Paul Braga’s spot-on, seasonal cuisine. Recipes which also feature the occasional nostalgic tribute (braised calf sweetbreads with morels, Rossini tournedos) or even a sprinkling of mouth-watering Portuguese delicacies from the chef’s homeland.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14622;Bo-tannique;France;Bordeaux;2 rue Tustal, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8384731;-0.5743791;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;These attractive premises (with a contemporary interior and exposed Bordeaux stonework) are located on a charming cobbled pedestrian square. The fresh cuisine is full of contrasts and draws on influences from far and wide: grilled sardines with burnt miso and Lebanese-style tomato tabbouleh. The fine wine list features mostly organic and natural wines. Friendly service... A recipe for success!;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14624;Le Paris-Brest by Christian Le Squer;France;Rennes;Gare de Rennes, Rennes, 35000, France;48.1034946;-1.6721476;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Christian Le Squer has reinvented the railway station buffet concept whilst teasingly jazzing up traditional Breton fare. A trendy interior, a bistronomic menu and a wine list by Eric Beaumard: you’re in for a treat in Rennes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14625;La Rissole;France;Tours;51 place du Grand-Marché, Tours, 37000, France;47.3930094;0.6805832;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of this bistro pays tribute to a great chef of the last century and celebrates the joys of cooking. The concise menu highlights the changing seasons and regional produce (asparagus, snails, freshwater fish). A flair for seasoning makes for simple and tasty food, such as white asparagus mimosa, broccoli and vadouvan. There are only a few tables, so be sure to book!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14626;L'Expression;France;Beaune;11 rue Maufoux, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0231735;4.8352526;56;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This city-centre establishment serves top-drawer ingredients, many of which are to share (whole fish from the market, rib of Galice beef, butterflied, plump fattened Bresse Miéral chicken), in two trendily appointed dining rooms (open kitchen, glazed wine cellar and high tables). The food is cooked in a wood-fired oven. Extroverted, friendly atmosphere. Beautifully curated wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14627;Brasserie du Louvre - Bocuse;France;Paris;Place André-Malraux, Paris, 75001, France;48.8627544;2.3362334;55;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Lyonnaise;Take a seat in the sleek, spacious dining hall framed by bay windows and marvel at the quintessential view over Paris: Comédie-Française, Conseil d’Etat, Louvre… The enticing menu cleverly navigates between iconic Lyons classics (hot pistachio sausage in a soft bread roll, pike quenelle and nantua sauce) and timeless brasserie staples (foie gras salad, sole meunière, etc. ). Splendid terrace beneath the arcades of this emblematic Haussmannian edifice.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14628;L'Hostellerie d'Acquigny;France;Acquigny;1 rue d'Évreux, Acquigny, 27400, France;49.1719372;1.1756287;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This small village inn with a lively contemporary vibe has been run by the same couple for many years. As keen as ever, chef Éric Georget rustles up generous and indulgent modern cuisine to make your mouth water, organising it into a set menu and an à la carte menu. Carefully selected produce goes into dishes that are packed with flavour: fillet of John Dory and poached oyster with seaweed butter and, for dessert, Calvados and apple hot soufflé. Pleasant guestrooms available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14629;Ébullition;France;Montpellier;10 rue du Pila-Saint-Gély, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6132891;3.8797575;36;false;true;Creative;In this lovely restaurant steeped in character in the heart of historic Montpellier, Boris Caillol (formerly Le Petit Nice and La Maison Troisgros) signs a bold creative modern score and the inventive, no-holds barred chef continues to set our tastebuds tingling! He scours Montpellier’s organic market himself, hunting out the best seasonal ingredients. The resulting subtle dishes are admirably paired with an enticing wine list that demonstrates a weakness for biodynamic wines from the region. The old stone walls are offset by soft lighting and contemporary fixtures, all of which is further enhanced by the graceful greeting of Coralie Semery, who elegantly supervises the front of house.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
14630;Du Bruit en Cuisine;France;Montauban;12 allée Mortarieu, Montauban, 82000, France;44.0147655;1.3557372;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A chef who trained in several Ducasse establishments is at work in this genuine gourmet bolthole. Mathieu Lévèque creates up-to-the-minute, deceptively spontaneous cuisine in the shape of small, tapas-inspired dishes. This veteran chef has a knack with jus, sauces and spot-on cooking, illustrated by his confit of ox cheeks garnished with mushroom and celeriac gnocchis. The venue sometimes hosts musical evenings, adding a festive dimension to the venue. As it goes from strength to strength, we are likely to hear more from this boisterous kitchen.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14631;Le Petit Comptoir;France;Narbonne;4 boulevard du Maréchal-Joffre, Narbonne, 11100, France;43.1845917;2.9996214;100;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This gastronomic eatery with a 1930s character serves bistro cuisine with fine ingredients. If you fancy buying a bottle of one of the wines served here – there are 350 on the list, most of them local – pay a visit to the cellar!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14632;Nomade;France;Labarde;3 route des Châteaux, Labarde, 33460, France;45.0220786;-0.6381299;64;false;false;Creative;This restaurant, opened in the middle of the Médoc region by a local young couple, is a pleasant surprise. The chef serves up French cuisine with exotic touches, using local produce as much as possible: the results are tasty. Pleasant decor and a friendly welcome.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14633;Pinson;France;Chambéry;22 place Monge, Chambéry, 73000, France;45.5635471;5.9225601;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This enticing city-centre establishment overflows with the infectious enthusiasm of its youthful owners, who, like its namesake chaffinch, adore travelling… After stints in London and Paris, the chef rustles up a melting-pot menu, while his partner brings her experience in the luxury trade to bear in the dining room. Gracious, warm welcome and vibe.;Terrace;[]
14636;Le 26-28;France;Lorient;26-28 rue Poissonnière, Lorient, 56100, France;47.7473559;-3.3584491;42;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Contemporary design, open kitchens, a chef – Arthur Friess (with a fine Michelin-starred career) – and, managing the restaurant floor, Charlotte Le Gall: these are the ingredients that make this place a success. Lovely contemporary cuisine made from impeccable ingredients – such as pigeon, spelt au gratin and roots. Menu renewed every month.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14637;L'Arlatan;France;Arles;26 rue du Sauvage, Arles, 13200, France;43.6783939;4.6272876;56;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;The flamboyant, Instagram-worthy interior designed by Cuban artist Jorge Pardo makes an immediate impression. Your attention is then drawn to the seasonal, Mediterranean-inspired menu. Delicious, well-crafted dishes that make the most of local produce to conjure up bold and appealing flavours: think Camargue oysters, beef marinated à la provençale, Camargue red rice, pistachio millefeuille to share.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14638;Au Cheval Blanc;France;Niedersteinbach;11 rue Principale, Niedersteinbach, 67510, France;49.0317082;7.7108224;23;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Alsatian;"The soul of a winstub... and all the flavours of the region lovingly presented: blue trout, venison steak with sauce grand veneur, kirsch mousse etc. The same spirit is mirrored in the decor: lots of wood panelling and two ""stuben"": rustic rooms that are typical of the region. Finally, a special mention for the absolutely exemplary service. ";Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14639;Les Bouteilles;France;Nantes;11 rue de Bel-Air, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2210766;-1.5591182;47;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Next to the Marché de Talensac, an impressive wine bar/bistro: appealing wine - inspired decoration, excellent food based on quality products (Italian cold cuts, rough - and - readycanaille dishes, fresh fish) not forgetting – the clue is in the name – a memorable wine list (1,500 types), with a particular penchant for Burgundy.;Interesting wine list;[]
14640;Jean-Michel Couron;France;Nevers;21 rue Saint-Étienne, Nevers, 58000, France;46.9913119;3.1635605;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Over more than 30 years, this chef has built up a loyal clientele of happy diners courtesy of his contemporary cuisine featuring nods to the Mediterranean, in dishes such as bouillabaisse jus and carpaccio of large wild prawns. The yakitori sauce on the duck fillet is one of his more exotic marriages. You can choose to dine in either the contemporary space or the former 14C cloister.;Interesting wine list;[]
14641;L'Adress...;France;Bessines;1 rue des Iris, Bessines, 79000, France;46.3007591;-0.490421;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A glazed parallelepiped extended by decking and framed by greenery: such is the modern, stylish setting! David Seguin’s inventive menu is devised around high-calibre produce. The cooking is flawless, the plating exquisite and the flavours ideally balanced, such as crab and avocado ravioles with buckwheat and a tangy shellfish stock. Splendid cheese platter.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14642;L'Instinct Gourmand;France;Nantes;14 rue Saint-Léonard, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2171843;-1.5555155;100;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Two young men, who met in Oxford, have teamed up in this ‘no label’ bistro, determined to forge a name for themselves without the usual traditional trappings. Simple, fresh food is their goal, illustrated by the enticing slate menu that changes daily depending on market produce. Trust your own instincts and book a table!;Air conditioning;[]
14643;Ô Dissay;France;Dissay;111 place Pierre-d'Amboise, Dissay, 86130, France;46.6989735;0.4284568;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The Château de Dissay, a 15C stately home with an elegant and refined interior, serves modern, visually exciting cuisine, created by two young chefs, Henri Dupont and Stanislas Simonet. A trained pastry chef, Simonet has not lost his touch, as his work with blackberries in season amply illustrates. In autumn, the duo harness their talents to revealing the big-boned flavours of game. Pleasant terrace in the castle courtyard.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14645;Âma Terra;France;Aix-en-Provence;7 traverse Saint-Pierre, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.5229685;5.457781;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Diners are faced with a dilemma in the restaurant of this magnificent hotel. You can opt to dine in the inside space, with its Second Empire glass roof, crystal chandeliers and imposing china cabinet, or on the gorgeous terrace, with the gentle sound of water tinkling in the pools and fountains and the scent of typical Mediterranean fragrances hanging in the air. The Chef cooks up gourmet cuisine with Provençal overtones and a backdrop of original and striking associations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14646;Yam;France;Saint-Louis;4 rue d'Altkirch, Saint-Louis, 68300, France;47.5786411;7.5463139;51;true;true;Thai;You can rely on chef Chatchai Klanklong (chef/patron of L'Orchidée, 1 star at Altkirch) and his brother Kriankai to concoct flavoursome Thai cuisine, such as Tom Yam (prawn and coconut milk soup), or 30-day aged Iberico pork chop with cauliflower and spiced tamarind jus... Premium ingredients, distinctive, well-balanced flavours, precise culinary technique and careful presentation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14647;La Golmotte;France;Le Mont-Dore;Le Barbier, Le Mont-Dore, 63240, France;45.5845839;2.8213643;34;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Not far from Le Mont-Dore, authenticity is guaranteed in this inn, where the dining area was originally a cowshed! Fresh ingredients and copious portions of tasty traditional cuisine, such as tender pork cheeks, home-made potato purÉe and Saint-PourÇain white wine sauce… even if the chef allows himself a few incursions into more contemporary territory, with dishes such as salmon gravlax.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14648;Le Pré Fillet;France;Les Molunes;Route du Pré Fillet aux Molunes, Les Molunes, 39310, France;46.3341506;5.8997221;33;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This former farmstead, turned into a restaurant three generations ago, stands in a landscape of meadows and woodland at an altitude of 1200 metres. Simplicity and generosity are the bywords of this establishment which shines the spotlight on the region’s knockout produce. The chef crafts wholesome, hearty fare: calf sweetbread flambéed in Jura marc and asparagus in flaky pastry or melt-in-the-mouth knuckle of lamb braised in assorted veggies. To be sampled and enjoyed in a dining area overlooking the unspoiled countryside. Diners are pampered by attentive staff.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14649;Auberge du Moulinel;France;St-Josse;116 chaussée de l'Avant-Pays, Le Moulinel, St-Josse, 62170, France;50.4788599;1.6814185;39;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This peaceful inn between Le Touquet and Montreuil-sur-Mer sports a smart rural vibe. The chef painstakingly selects his ingredients to carefully craft flavoursome traditional fare. House specialties include lobster salad, pigeon cooked two ways and a decadent millefeuille smothered in a light frothy cream. Everything is prepared in house, including the bread and ice creams!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14650;Le Saint-Martin;France;Montbéliard;1 rue du Général-Leclerc, Montbéliard, 25200, France;47.510847;6.7979742;53;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Olivier Prevot - Carme's flavoursome cuisine is all about the ingredients. He uses each one in a straightforward way but the apparent simplicity is misleading, as the recipes, cooking and seasoning bring out all of the flavour within. Nothing pretentious, nothing complicated, nothing but pleasure!;;[]
14651;Auberge du Cellier;France;Montner;1 rue de Sainte-Eugénie, Montner, 66720, France;42.7490993;2.6785143;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Typical of the region, this charming house is the setting for a chef – with roots in the district who has returned home – to create delicate fare. It is from locally sourced ingredients, authentic and bursting with flavour. A feast for the eyes and the taste buds! The accommodation is simple yet agreeable.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14652;Le Carré d'Ange;France;Montauroux;2169 quartier Narbonne, Montauroux, 83440, France;43.6004266;6.7867807;21;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This updated, airy Provençal inn outside town provides the perfect foil for generous, throbbingly good Mediterranean food. Examples include a mouthwatering breast of guinea fowl and truffles with girolles and a millefeuille of potatoes. Served on a pretty patio in fine weather.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14653;Yushin;France;Neuilly-sur-Seine;77 rue Chauveau, Neuilly-sur-Seine, 92200, France;48.8936084;2.2702676;17;false;false;Japanese;Between Île de la Jatte and the American Hospital of Neuilly, this traditional Japanese restaurant offers a variety of menus: sushis, bento, omakase and a tasting menu. The fish is of the freshest quality and meticulously prepared as one would expect. The traditional Japanese desserts are exquisitely presented. The interior is unsurprisingly pared down with light wooden fixtures and white walls and the 100% Japanese staff is dutifully attentive. The tea service is carried out with full ceremony and each diner is walked out to the street and thanked on leaving.;Air conditioning;[]
14654;L'Altiplano;France;Val-d'Isère;Le K2 Chogori, 143 avenue du Prariond, Val-d'Isère, 73150, France;45.4486253;6.9810989;17;true;false;Peruvian;We may be in the Alps, but this place fêtes an entirely different mountain range – the Andes! The culinary offering here is inspired by Peruvian history and cuisine: think barbecued specialities, condiments, dishes for sharing etc. Be transported to Peru, without even leaving this chic, intimate and friendly setting.;Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14655;Au Cœur d'Artichaut;France;Morbecque;8 avenue des Flandres, Morbecque, 59190, France;50.6940764;2.5176531;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary restaurant, run by an enthusiastic young couple from the village, is depicted by dishes that keep pace with current tastes, while remaining true to the ingredients and seasons. The lovely dining room is in a conservatory. Attentive service.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
14657;Le 7 Restaurant Panoramique;France;Bordeaux;4 esplanade de Pontac, Bordeaux, 33300, France;44.8624169;-0.5500702;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;As the name implies, this restaurant is located on the seventh floor of the Cité du Vin, commanding a matchless view over the Garonne River and historic Bordeaux. The food is pleasantly up - to - date and well - prepared, accompanied by a fine choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14658;La Cantinetta;France;Marseille;24 cours Julien, Marseille, 13006, France;43.295387;5.382512;60;false;true;Italian;Since childhood, Pierre-Antoine Denis has been passionate about Italian food and regularly pops over the border to scour the country for premium produce. Chalked up on a slate, the menu spans antipasti, fresh house-made pasta and the chef’s signature dish: scaloppine di vitello. Tightly-packed tables, a buzzy vibe and a patio to the rear set the scene.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14659;Jean des Sables;France;Hossegor;121 boulevard de la Dune, à Soorts, Hossegor, 40150, France;43.6583533;-1.4436989;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This beach front restaurant sports a fashionably stark interior: polished concrete, a light colour scheme, a live lobster tank and an ocean view… The modern cuisine is presented in a brief, well-crafted menu. Special lobster menu. Attentive welcome and service.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14660;L'Étier;France;Noirmoutier-en-l'Île;Route de l'Épine, Noirmoutier-en-l'Île, 85330, France;46.9935631;-2.2490301;29;true;false;Seafood;Between the road and the étier (a seawater channel) onto which the conservatory backs, this characteristic island house showcases splendid local seafood: grilled lobster, wild turbot cooked on the bone, sole meunière, marsh eels in garden herbs, without forgetting the desserts, soufflé au Grand Marnier or Paris-Brest pastry – to die for! The food of a genuine craftsman – fresh and oozing with flavour.;Car park;[]
14661;Le Gentil;France;Paris;26 rue Surcouf, Paris, 75007, France;48.8602472;2.3095678;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant on the rue Surcouf, a street strewn with eateries, is the work of a Japanese pair, chef Fumitoshi Kumagai in the kitchen and his wife front of house. They propose contemporary French cuisine with the occasional Asian influence, such as pig's trotters stuffed with pak choi and beef faux-filet with a Japanese sauce.;;[]
14663;Lacaille;France;Marseille;42 rue des Trois-Mages, Marseille, 13006, France;43.29441;5.38499;73;true;true;Farm to table;This neighbourhood bistro offers no-fuss market cuisine that keeps pace with the seasons. Service with a smile.;Air conditioning;[]
14664;La Côte Bleue;France;Bouzigues;Avenue Louis-Tudesq, Bouzigues, 34140, France;43.4474049;3.6576895;68;false;false;Seafood;The Étang de Thau, a major shellfish farming site and lake in Languedoc, famous for its mussels and the legendary oysters of Bouzigues, is also well-known for its biodiversity on land, in the sea and in the airs. So, taking a seat on the terrace overlooking the lagoon is an opportunity not to be missed. Expect to tuck into delicious, ultra-fresh seafood, including oysters, mini squid in garlic and parsley or mussels broiled in garlic butter.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14665;Le 80;France;Méribel;88 rue des Jeux-Olympiques, Méribel, 73550, France;45.3939988;6.5673542;70;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Adorned in colourful hot-air balloons, Le 80 presents a patriotic culinary line-up of French traditions in well-crafted dishes: Richelieu pâté en croûte (porkpie), free-range pork chop smoked in hay or rose-scented praline meringues in a vanilla custard cream. More festive in the evenings. Follow in the footsteps of Jules Verne!;;[]
14666;La Table de la Réserve;France;Beaulieu-sur-Mer;5 boulevard du Maréchal-Leclerc, Beaulieu-sur-Mer, 06310, France;43.7059754;7.3350726;50;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Supervised by chef Julien Roucheteau, this restaurant is a welcome gourmet addition to the dining options at this superb establishment. The contemporary Mediterranean-inspired menu takes inspiration from the local terroir – note the textures of pissaladière with house-marinated anchovy and a sweet onion espuma, or the tartlet showcasing figs from the Var, with its melting brambleberry centre. You might also like to sample their bouillabaisse (Fri and Sat), traditional octopus dishes from the South of France, or rockfish soup. Diners take their seats in a bistro-style setting that is suitably cordial and laid back.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14667;Le Grand Chaume;France;Chaumont-sur-Loire;Route de Queneau, Chaumont-sur-Loire, 41150, France;47.472951;1.1827316;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Architects Patrick Bouchain and Loïc Julienne designed this unique venue with a traditional thatched roof and an exposed timber frame that calls to mind a star-studded night sky. The pared-back, minimalist interior seems to be open to the elements, courtesy of floor-to-ceiling windows, some of which command a view of the small terrace and its water feature. The entire project is truly jaw dropping! The seasonal menu stars produce from the Val de Loire region.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
14670;83 Restaurant;France;Metz;83 rue Mazelle, Metz, 57000, France;49.1152032;6.1839228;64;false;true;Italian, Provençal;A ten - minute walk from the Centre Pompidou - Metz, this pleasant restaurant showcases Italian food, through carefully selected ingredients (charcuterie, burrata, pasta, wild fish, purebred meats). And to accompany it all, a fine selection of Italin wines!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
14671;Le Bénaton;France;Beaune;25 rue du Faubourg-Bretonnière, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0211819;4.8323645;23;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Burgundy, Beaune is known the world over for its annual charity wine auction held in the iconic Hospices edifice, famous for its glazed tile roof. A steadfast champion of fine French food and wine, Japanese chef Keishi Sugimura, couldn’t have found a town that suits him better. Trained in Japan, the chef excels in the art of the porkpie, which earned him the title of vice world champion in 2013. Flavoursome seasonal dishes sprinkled with creative touches.;Terrace;[]
14672;Le Sirocco;France;Paris;8 bis rue des Gobelins, Paris, 75013, France;48.8358767;2.351666;78;false;true;Moroccan;The warm air of the Sirocco has reached Les Gobelins, bringing its fragrances of tajines, couscous and hariras into the old stables of the Château de la Reine Blanche, where this Moroccan restaurant with typical decor is located. The owner himself imports the argan oil that flavours his traditional dishes. Of course the couscous itself is home-made, and very fine, just as it should be.;;[]
14673;Bistro de l'Hôtel;France;Beaune;5 rue Samuel-Legay, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0228701;4.8395348;64;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The elegant, chic bistro - style interior is the setting for cuisine that honours tradition and first - rate ingredients. The house speciality is roasted Bresse chicken. As for the wine list, it is quite simply impressive.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14675;Piero TT;France;Paris;44 rue du Bac, Paris, 75007, France;48.8566037;2.3265494;91;false;false;Italian;Welcome to Pierre Gagnaire's Italian restaurant, where the great chef proposes his personal and creative take on cucina italiana, beautifully made with rigorously selected produce. The dishes are punctuated with subtle contrasts created, for example, by bitter salad leaves, spices and condiments. You can look forward to a chic and opulent but nonetheless relaxed atmosphere, a warm welcome and expert recommendations on the best Italian wines from the sommelier. Booking strongly advised.;Air conditioning;[]
14676;Wistub Brenner;France;Colmar;1 rue de Turenne, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0738805;7.3577843;26;true;true;Alsatian;In this authentic winstub in the heart of Little Venice, the cuisine is – of course – regional: salad with Comté cheese and cervelas, "Papi Lucien's onion tart", sauerkraut and braised pork knuckle, Pinot Noir sauce. Local produce, a friendly atmosphere and a pleasant terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14678;La Ruche;France;Saint-Péray;13 quai du Docteur-Jules-Bouvat, Saint-Péray, 07130, France;44.9436083;4.8413832;80;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the wine country where Marsanne and Roussanne grapes are grown (the two varieties used to make white Saint-Péray), a modern bistro done right! On the menu: tasty, carefully prepared neo-bistro cuisine in tune with the seasons, and an excellent list of wines from the northern Côtes du Rhône region. Reservation required.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14679;Tabi - Ippei Uemura;France;Marseille;165 corniche du Président-John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2858871;5.3510494;78;true;false;Japanese Contemporary;Tabi, which means journey in Japanese, says it all! Born in Kyoto, the chef has adopted the city of Marseilles as his own. He incorporates locally caught fish into traditional Japanese recipes, prepared in front of customers. Food-saké pairings for aficionados. One of a kind!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Wheelchair access;[]
14680;Parapluie;France;Dijon;74 rue Monge, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3188424;5.0338897;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This lilliputian restaurant serves globetrotting food in the zeitgeist, with a sprinkling of spices and based on seasonal, mostly local, ingredients. The culinary offer is rolled out in a single set "mystery" menu comprised of several courses at dinner, and a reasonably priced lunchtime menu with options. Fine selection of wine, beer and spirits (whiskies, eaux de vie etc).;Terrace;[]
14681;Le Bélouga;France;Perros-Guirec;L'Agapa, 12 rue des Bons-Enfants, Perros-Guirec, 22700, France;48.81415;-3.45035;42;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This granite, glass and steel structure commands a breath-taking panoramic view over the coast and the bay of the Sept-Îles archipelago from its chic black-and-white interior. The subtle, meticulous cuisine oscillates between classicism and creativity, with the occasional more exotic note, such as raviole of duck foie gras and tonka bean cream or Breton lobster rubbed in saté and served with a red lentil houmous. From Tuesday to Saturday, the evening menu errs towards ambitious, with a more bistronomic streak the rest of the time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14682;Mantesino;France;Toulouse;8 rue Maury, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6050452;1.4535606;95;false;false;Italian, Campanian;The Naples-born chef, who used to be an engineer, has enthusiastically donned an apron (mantesino in Italian) and opened this small bistro in a street near the Église Saint-Aubin. He gives pride of place to his roots by tapping into the culinary traditions of Southern Italy, from Campania to Puglia. A far cry from stereotypical Italian fare, his no-nonsense bistro cuisine wins diners over by drawing solely on flavoursome, meticulously selected ingredients: mortadella from Bologna, hazelnuts from Piedmont, Ibaïama pork, as well as meat from Aveyron and vegetables from local growers. Uplifting!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14683;Auberge de la Roche;France;Valdeblore;La Roche, Valdeblore, 06420, France;44.0702973;7.1751076;53;false;true;Creative, Contemporary;In the heart of the Mercantour National Park, between the valleys of the Tinée River and Vésubie River, a duo with a longing for nature set their sights on this traditional stone-built inn. The calm beauty of the surrounding countryside won them over, as it will you, too. Our hosts serve a single set menu of natural, creative cuisine with a strong vegetable component, as well as local produce (including from their kitchen garden). There is a good selection of natural beers and wines.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14684;Bohème;France;Mougins;47 avenue du Moulin de la Croix, Mougins, 06250, France;43.6012074;6.9968076;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this smart, trendy establishment with a decor of premium and untreated materials, the food is an ode to the very best breeds of beef cattle, aged and prepared by the famous butcher Alexandre Polmard in his unique way. Peruvian chef Manuel Rondan is in a class of his own when it comes to cooking over hot coals and wild-fish ceviche, as well as some lovely Mediterranean dishes. There is a drop-dead view from the terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14685;La Bulle d'Air;France;Moulins;22 place d'Allier, Moulins, 03000, France;46.5646366;3.3294015;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;From his open kitchen, the chef consummately crafts dishes such as low-temperature arctic char, flanked with a velvety gribiche sauce and a crunchy salad of fennel. The single set lunchtime menu is a steal – all the better when leisurely sampled on the delightful, cobbled patio in summertime.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14686;Au G'Retz des Saisons;France;La Bernerie-en-Retz;17 rue Jean-Duplessis, La Bernerie-en-Retz, 44760, France;47.080975;-2.0363838;56;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Well-travelled young chef Samuel Duchêne aligns his cooking with the seasons. His short menu, which changes every month, showcases first and foremost local Pays de Retz farmers and artisans – fish, free-range eggs, sea salt. Beetroot marinated in cider, confit egg yolk, watercress coulis or fillet of sea bass, carrot, coconut emulsion, turmeric: hard work, audacity and flavour. The house-made bread is very good, too. Limited capacity, so it's best to book in advance.;;[]
14687;Le Clos de la Prairie;France;Gouy-Saint-André;17 rue de Saint-Rémy, Gouy-Saint-André, 62870, France;50.37091;1.89458;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in the countryside, this charming restaurant is peaceful and bucolic. Behind his stove, the chef masterfully prepares dishes in tune with the zeitgeist and the seasons. In summer, enjoy the quiet terrace overlooking the meadow. Accessible only by reservation.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14688;Peron;France;Marseille;56 corniche John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2877469;5.3522299;21;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;On the coast road, this building clinging to the rocks offers a breathtaking view of the bay of Marseille and its islands and the château d’If. A brisk sea breeze has shaken up the menu which features dishes such as local and wild fish of the day, stuffed vegetables, duck breast and beef fillet, without forgetting the ubiquitous bouillabaisse, all of which served on the splendid terrace. A genuine institution since 1855!;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14689;Chez Fonfon;France;Marseille;140 rue du Vallon-des-Auffes, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2855277;5.351348;42;true;false;Seafood;This family restaurant (1952) is pleasing in terms both of its contemporary interior and its seafood, freshly fished in the wooden pointu boats that can be seen bobbing about in the little port.;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
14690;Epiro;France;Nice;53 boulevard Stalingrad, Nice, 06000, France;43.69478;7.286565;75;true;true;Italian;After a stint in Rome, where they ran a highly sought-after bistro, Alessandra and Marco are giving it another go near the port in Nice. Appetising Roman delicacies, heart-warming home-made pasta, lashings of generosity and tingling tastebuds, without forgetting the splendid Italian wine list – bang on every time!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
14691;Auberge de l'Abbaye;France;Beaumont-en-Auge;2 rue de la Libération, Beaumont-en-Auge, 14950, France;49.2784849;0.1097106;61;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Local produce, meticulous plating, generous helpings and a taste for fresh herbs, all in tune with the seasons: the scene is set. And let’s not forget the rustic interior of this inn in the heart of a Normandy village that is the epitome of French rural charm.;;[]
14692;Emotions;France;Plappeville;50 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Plappeville, 57050, France;49.1299791;6.1254769;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the village, this former winegrower's house has been turned into a restaurant (previously La Vigne d'Adam) with a pared-back interior design that blends wood, fabrics and natural materials. The cuisine follows the seasons to create marriages of premium ingredients: hare à la royale in autumn, truffle menu in winter, asparagus in spring and lobster in summer! Over 400 wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14693;Lazare;France;Paris;Parvis de la gare Saint-Lazare, rue Intérieure, Paris, 75008, France;48.8759051;2.3252325;20;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of the famous Gare St - Lazare is this elegant railway brasserie, version 2013. It is the brainchild of Éric Frechon, who respects the canons of the genre: French - style devilled eggs, pike quenelles or mackerel in a white wine sauce. Fine French tradition is right on track! Pleasant and very lively.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14694;Le Relais de Saulx;France;Beaune;6 rue Louis-Véry, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0223962;4.835609;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This characterful establishment (1673) in the town centre, not far from the Hospices de Beaune, is in the capable hands of Charles Danet (previously of Le Timbre in Paris) and it would be an understatement to say that he has settled in quickly! His unmistakable signature style errs towards wholesome market-fresh cuisine, which he describes as "artisanal seasonal" cooking.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14695;L'Agastache;France;Volnay;1 rue de la Cave, Volnay, 21190, France;47.0012103;4.7808684;68;false;true;Farm to table;This restaurant, whose reputation has grown by word of mouth, is fully deserving of its success. The chef is very attentive to the quality of his ingredients and his creative cuisine, in which vegetables and plants play a pivotal role, is as tasty as it is balanced. Examples include houmous of winter veggies with curcuma and egg parfait or a purée of celery with finely diced Granny Smith apples. Bargain priced menu at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14697;Eclipses;France;Paris;27-29 rue de Beaune, Paris, 75007, France;48.857898;2.3293282;91;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, by a chef who has carved out a career in Michelin-starred kitchens (Ledoyen, Apicius, Le Grand Véfour), serves contemporary cuisine that is heedful of ingredients and the seasons. Enjoy your meal in the tastefully decorated neo-Classical setting. Lovely vaulted cellar.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14698;Le Pré de la Cure;France;Yvoire;1 place de la Mairie, Yvoire, 74140, France;46.3693777;6.3277324;69;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Fancy diving into Lake Geneva! The view is as stunning as the food is mouth - watering. Fish and produce from the lake take pride of place in the menu, as do succulent local specialties. Depending on availability, you will taste pike, perch or trout. A treat for the taste buds!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14699;Le Bout du Quai;France;Cancale;Route de la Corniche, Cancale, 35260, France;48.6680043;-1.8627114;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Aptly located at the end of the quayside (hence the name), the fashionable slate grey glazed front of this restaurant overlooks the Atlantic and Mont St Michel. Chef Romain Roland, after a stint at a star restaurant in Corsica, crafts ambitious, creative cuisine, dotted with subtle Mediterranean notes.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14700;Les Ronins;France;Praz-sur-Arly;9 route de Megève, Praz-sur-Arly, 74120, France;45.8385594;6.5729767;74;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In Japanese culture, ronins are samurai without a master, which is Anthony and Émilie’s metaphor for their unfettered approach to cooking and, of course, their exquisitely presented Franco-Asian cuisine, such as Angus beef hanger steak served with crying tiger sauce and a hearty gratin dauphinois. Trendy Alpine-inspired decor, friendly service and good vibes!;Terrace;[]
14701;Le Goût du Large;France;Le Tréport;4 place Notre-Dame, Le Tréport, 76470, France;50.0613573;1.3705394;18;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Sheltered from the bustling port, take a seat in this cosy, modern eatery and dig into the contemporary, generous nosh of youthful Jonathan Selliez (assisted by his mum for pastries) who plays on textures and flavours. The fish is from sustainable fishing boats, such as the superb fillet of mackerel, flanked with a maki of leeks rolled in nori seaweed leaves and a medley of carrots, jelly and pickled. All the more reason not to set sail straight away…;;[]
14703;Côté Toqués;France;Néris-les-Bains;21 rue Hoche, Néris-les-Bains, 03310, France;46.2876763;2.6611676;95;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Julien Chabozy's aromatic, tasty food showcases the best of local produce, with lashings of personality to boot. Friendly and endearing depict the front of house vibe, supervised by his wife Marie. The establishment also boasts a delicatessen and a wine shop, La Cave des Toqués, next door… It was love at first bite.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14704;La Table du Chef;France;Cannes;5 rue Jean-Daumas, Cannes, 06400, France;43.5525706;7.0252399;63;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Only open in the evenings, this small bistro just two minutes from Rue d’Antibes never disappoints. In an open kitchen, a youthful chef works with local, seasonal produce, crafting subtle, tasty dishes, such as his knockout velvety carrot soup with star anise and lightly seared shrimp. Market availability dictates the contents of the “Surprise” menu which is great value for money… Booking recommended.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14705;La Table de Marie-Ange;France;Manigod;4910 route du Col-de-la-Croix-Fry, Manigod, 74230, France;45.872314;6.38931;37;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The terrace overlooking the Aravis range is so mesmerising, it is difficult to tear oneself away. Marie-Ange aims to serve fine regional dishes oozing with authentic flavour: pan-seared cèpes, fillets of wild perch from Lake Geneva, fillet of beef simmered in mushrooms and grandma’s potato gratin, without forgetting the wickedly lavish dessert trolley. The interior sports old wood and farming tools – charming welcome.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14706;LiLi;France;Paris;19 avenue Kléber, Paris, 75116, France;48.8707359;2.2932972;84;false;false;Chinese;Opened by the Hong Kong luxury hotel group of the same name, the already famous Peninsula Hotel is a fitting home for this Asian restaurant. In a strikingly theatrical decor, the long menu, prepared by the Chinese chef, unveils a wide range of the country's specialities (some adapted to European tastes). A culinary ambassador for China.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14707;Capitaine;France;Paris;4 impasse Guéménée, Paris, 75004, France;48.854091;2.3659234;58;false;false;Farm to table;After working in the kitchens of some restaurants with a great pedigree (L'Ambroisie, L'Arpège, L'Astrance), Baptiste Day decided to open this pleasant bistro. Diners are treated to lovely market-fresh dishes that are inspired by his Breton origins and enhanced by exotic flavours. The popular starter of pork croquettes (ginger, garlic and chilli mayonnaise) will certainly whet your appetite! Selection of organic and natural wines.;;[]
14710;Rooster;France;Paris;137 rue Cardinet, Paris, 75017, France;48.886701;2.3130776;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;After training in prestigious houses (from Passedat to Darroze), Frédéric Duca has set up shop in the more working-class part of the 17th arrondissement. In a former street corner cafe, the Marseille-born chef signs dishes which pay numerous tributes to his Mediterranean and Provençal roots. The lunchtime menu is at delicious eater-friendly prices. More ambitious in the evenings.;;[]
14711;Tadam;France;Paris;14 rue du Jura, Paris, 75013, France;48.8369518;2.3560424;74;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This delightful little eatery proposes a brief, seasonal and mouth-watering menu, underscored by a commitment to sustainable development. The food hits the spot every time thanks to tip-top ingredients stripped of unnecessary frills, illustrated by the scrumptious hot mushroom pie. A casual vibe and brunch on Sundays. A welcome addition to the Gobelins culinary scene.;;[]
14712;Auberge du Cheval Blanc;France;Bayonne;68 rue Bourgneuf, Bayonne, 64100, France;43.4909228;-1.4725488;45;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This 18C coaching inn has been run by the same family since 1959. Chef Jean-Claude Tellechea adds a new spin to the traditional regional line-up: crispy hake, black pudding, Ibaïama ham, Bayonne chocolate. The interior is patriotically decked in red and white Basque Country colours. The range of menus is such that there is something for every budget.;Air conditioning;[]
14713;Marso & Co;France;Paris;16 rue Vulpian, Paris, 75013, France;48.83171;2.34635;74;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Tomy Gousset (Tomy & Co, near Les Invalides) runs this restaurant that sets out to take diners on a culinary journey: the food tours the entire Mediterranean basin from Greece to Portugal via Italy and Lebanon (but also Latin America). Examples of the Colombian born chef’s handiwork include an aguachile of seabream and shrimp, pink grapefruit, cucumber and coriander. The octopus-themed artwork on the walls is by street artist Kraken. Soul-warming recipes, spot-on flavours, fantastically fresh ingredients – a felicitous feast awaits you!;;[]
14715;Kodawari Ramen - Yokochō;France;Paris;29 rue Mazarine, Paris, 75006, France;48.8547351;2.3380215;20;true;true;Japanese;The bustling vibe and cramped dimensions of this eatery instantly conjure up pictures of historic Tokyo. The ramen, made on site and served in delicious broths of Loiret poultry, attract gourmets from every horizon. The house speciality is kurugoma ramen made with a secret black sesame seed sauce and pata negra pork. Avoid peak times, as the place is very popular. Fully deserving of its success.;;[]
14717;Les Trois Forts;France;Marseille;36 boulevard Charles-Livon, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2927422;5.3606543;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;From the seventh floor, the panoramic view over the port is simply sublime! The contemporary dishes with a delicious Southern flavour make for a wonderful gourmet interlude.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
14718;L'inaTTendu;France;Reyrieux;311 chemin de Port-Bernalin, Reyrieux, 01600, France;45.9221271;4.8093239;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The inaTTendu, which first opened in Lyon, has opted for a radical change of venue in this attractive sand-coloured stone house idyllically set on the banks of the Saône. The chef continues to craft modern, generous fare, inspired by regional traditions with the odd Asian twist. Smart interior and a knockout view of the river from the lush green terrace.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14719;Le Comptoir de la Mère Germaine;France;Châteauneuf-du-Pape;7 place Jean-Moulin, Châteauneuf-du-Pape, 84230, France;44.0567306;4.8325033;51;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This offshoot of the star establishment doesn’t do things by halves: wood prevails in the contemporary interior and an imposing counter-cum-kitchen with a gleaming spit-roast oven and a shaded terrace. A bistronomic lineup strewn with South American notes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14720;L'Escargot;France;Saumur;30 rue du Maréchal-Leclerc, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2563803;-0.0824101;82;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant contemporary setting for traditional cuisine and emblematic dishes, such as snails in butter, garlic and parsley. Chef-owner Dominique Dubert jazzes up a traditional repertory with the odd dash of modernity (combava, ginger, curry, etc). It is a pleasure to linger over a meal on the terrace of this Snail in summer.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14722;Les Épicuriens;France;Sainte-Preuve;Domaine de Barive, Sainte-Preuve, 02350, France;49.6156563;3.8822523;60;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant set in a period castle concocts delicate, up-to-date food whose exquisite plating will find favour with even the most discerning connoisseurs, illustrated by carpaccio of langoustines in citrus fruit, fennel and caviar. The enticing wine list naturally showcases champagnes and the stylish terrace overlooks the estate’s gardens. Pleasant rooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14724;Le Panoramique;France;La Pernelle;1 village de l'Église, La Pernelle, 50630, France;49.6186005;-1.2984783;74;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, run by the same family since 1966, stands next to the village church on a hill overlooking the sea and the island of Tatihou. Initially a bar, then a crêperie, it is now an upmarket eatery that seeks to showcase produce from Normandy.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14725;Racines des Prés;France;Paris;1 rue de Gribeauval, Paris, 75007, France;48.8561982;2.327099;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in Saint-Germain-des-Prés is always bustling! Open kitchen counter, laid-back but chic "vintage" atmosphere, and delicate cuisine that is beautifully presented on the plate. The menu features refined dishes such as cod cooked with ash, burnt leek and smoked grenaille potatoes, plus delicious desserts, eg Manjari chocolate soufflé tart and cocoa ice cream… You'll be coming back for more!;;[]
14726;Les Botanistes;France;Paris;11 bis rue Chomel, Paris, 75007, France;48.8520317;2.3255075;94;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Not far from Le Bon Marché, this pleasant bistro is in the hands of a chef who does not cut corners when it comes to ingredients or taste! Take a seat on the characteristic bistro benches and dig into mouth-watering beef and shallots or a decadent rum baba smothered in whipped cream. The well-stocked wine cellar offers ample choice to pair with your meal. Friendly, tasty and casual – a winning formula!;;[]
14727;Sinabro;France;Lyon;126 rue de Sèze, Lyon, 69006, France;45.769051;4.8567063;57;true;true;Korean;In the mood for bibimbap and authentic Korean cuisine? Then this bistro is the right place for you! On the programme: a concise menu, splendid meat, meticulously sourced by a MOF, slick, smiling service, and, of course, healthy, flavoursome food – right down to the desserts and all made from scratch.;Air conditioning;[]
14728;Le Castellane - Château Le Prieuré;France;Chênehutte-Trèves-Cunault;Route du Comte-de-Castellane, Chênehutte-Trèves-Cunault, 49350, France;47.3110158;-0.1603885;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Le Castellane, part of the Château du Prieuré, serves modern fare that keeps tabs on the seasons and is predominantly local. You can choose between the Empire-inspired dining room or the terrace overlooking the Loire. Each of the guestrooms is individually appointed and fully in keeping with the historic character of the valley of kings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14729;Le Florimond;France;Paris;19 avenue de La Motte-Picquet, Paris, 75007, France;48.8558969;2.3078709;67;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Florimond – named after Monet's gardener at Giverny – has a convivial bistro atmosphere. The chef makes sure to use plenty of vegetables in his traditional local cooking, featuring many ingredients from his native Corrèze. And like his father before him, who was a pork butcher, he makes all his sausages, black pudding and conserves himself!;Air conditioning;[]
14730;La Roche Le Roy;France;Tours;55 route de Saint-Avertin, Tours, 37200, France;47.365242;0.713004;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This pretty little manor house on the outskirts of town has recently been refurbished and modernised, all the way from the decoration to the kitchens, the domain of chef Maximilien Bridier. Taking an enthusiastic approach to high-quality ingredients, he presents elegant, precise dishes with no frills. Without fail, the menu features a vegetarian option. There is a fine selection of wines by the glass, and the service is attentive. Sit out on the terrace on warm days.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14731;Le Bougainvillier;France;Saint-Raphaël;1792 route de la Corniche, Saint-Raphaël, 83700, France;43.4145312;6.8034012;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Le Bougainvillier is set in La Villa Mauresque, a five-star oasis of comfort and luxury, and boasts a waterside terrace overlooking an exotic garden and commanding jaw-dropping sea views. It is an idyllic spot to sample Mediterranean-inspired cuisine rich in frank, legible flavours, knife-edge cooking techniques and first-rate local produce, in particular fish and vegetables. The menus come in several courses, including a visually appealing 100% vegetarian tasting menu.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14732;Folie Cuisine d'Émotions;France;Chambéry;23 rue Bonivard, Chambéry, 73000, France;45.5656741;5.9177624;35;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a heritage edifice in the heart of historic Chambéry, not far from the Château des Ducs de Savoie, indulge yourself(ves) in this establishment, set in the former courtyard of what is now a luxury hotel. In a suitably classy yet cosy setting, the chef crafts a “carte blanche” menu inspired by the seasons and travel.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14733;Belvédère;France;Fontvieille;Hôtel Belesso, 34 avenue des Baux, Fontvieille, 13990, France;43.72876;4.71738;91;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Japanese chef Kohei Ohata skilfully harnesses the flavours of the Mediterranean fare that abounds in the surrounding markets to produce really appealing dishes. His talented wife brings her skills to bear on the pastry section. It is all fresh, fragrant and charged at a fair price. This excellent establishment is a little hidden away in the Hotel Belesso – reserved for those in the know, and all the better for it.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14734;L'Écluse;France;Amboise;Rue Racine, Amboise, 37400, France;47.4117932;0.9874856;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A step away from the royal castle of Amboise and the Clos Lucé, chef Mélanie Popineau can be relied upon for joyful bistronomic cuisine, rich in flavour, in the form of brief seasonal menus. Diners are simply and warmly welcomed by her partner. In fine weather, the leafy terrace shaded by willows is heaven-sent.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14735;Les Planeurs;France;Toulouse;56 boulevard des Minimes, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6163202;1.4395142;61;true;true;Farm to table;A Japanese chef and his partner have opened this unusual establishment in a deliberately bohemian and offbeat setting. The French cuisine is precise, original, balanced and flavoursome, illustrated by a risotto of poultry and shellfish, rich in seafaring aromas or roast apricots in rosemary served with homemade yoghurt ice cream. Good value for money.;Terrace;[]
14736;Auberge du Forgeron;France;Seclin;17 rue Roger-Bouvry, Seclin, 59113, France;50.5489686;3.0291586;84;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A traditional inn packed with charm. In the fine dining Table du Forgeron restaurant, the menu is in tune with the seasons and the zeitgeist, and the creative chef's dishes go down a treat every time (the "Mosaic of Artois Trout" is a feast for the eyes). For more traditional nosh, head to L'Estaminet for regional specialities of northern France. Comfortable, well-kept guestrooms for overnight stays.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14737;Au Bon Pichet;France;Sélestat;10 place du Marché-aux-Choux, Sélestat, 67600, France;48.2586085;7.4567673;15;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;It is a delight to eat at this restaurant that has been run by the same family for four generations! Like his forefathers before him, the chef concocts good traditional recipes: smoked pork shank with potato sauerkraut, pike perch quenelles and matelote sauce... The convivial service and winstub decor confirm that the rules of good living never go out of fashion!;Terrace;[]
14738;Le Vivarais;France;Vals-les-Bains;Hôtel Helvie, 5 avenue Claude-Expilly, Vals-les-Bains, 07600, France;44.65555;4.36702;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the city, right next to the casino, this Belle Époque grand hotel stands out from its surroundings. Its classic and elegant restaurant serves seasonal French cuisine made with good fresh produce, often locally sourced. Impeccable, friendly service. Spacious terrace shaded by plane trees at the side of the hotel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14740;La Pomme d'Or;France;Sancerre;1 rue de la Panneterie, Sancerre, 18300, France;47.3297762;2.8391881;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of a famous wine-growing village, a young couple from Brittany has opted to shine the spotlight on seafood to such an extent that you can almost smell the sea air. Their single set menu, whose dishes are intriguingly and poetically named, offers a choice of flawlessly fresh fish and shellfish, all of which are consummately cooked. The chef, who clearly knows his stuff, has his sights clearly focused on a single goal: taste. The wine list unsurprisingly gives the floor to Sancerre wines, and you'll hear no complaints from us. Cheerful, smiling service in an uncluttered, elegant interior.;Wheelchair access;[]
14741;Arraditz;France;Lescar;2 rue Cachau, Lescar, 64230, France;43.3324344;-0.4367985;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This 19C house near Pau is the haunt of a couple, chef Olivier Nicolau from Lescar, and his partner Karine, in charge of the service, both of whom learnt the ropes in star establishments. The subtle, niftily crafted repertory showcases regional produce: Projan squab, Lucq-de-Béarn mushrooms, Bahus-Soubiran lemon, Poey-de-Lescar pepper… Intelligent surf and turf combinations and generous helpings add the final touch to this epicurean portrait.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14742;L'Amphitryon;France;Castillon-du-Gard;Place du 8-Mai-1945, Castillon-du-Gard, 30210, France;43.9704825;4.5545225;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Stéphane Goudet has been valiantly regaling his guests in a style worthy of Molière’s Amphitryon since 1997 in this immense vaulted dining room whose stone walls are offset by the odd modern detail and soft lighting. A polished culinary lineup that stars fresh local produce and a reverence for the seasons: truffle in winter, lobster in summer (served on the patio), and whole hare in autumn. Slick, smiling service.;Wheelchair access;[]
14743;Le Vivier;France;Ploemeur;9 rue de Beg-Er-Vir, Lomener, Ploemeur, 56270, France;47.70076;-3.431827;73;true;true;Seafood;In this restaurant facing the open sea, the cuisine showcases fish and seafood (of course!). With the island of Groix as a backdrop, guests could almost dip their toes in the water while the chef serves up extremely fresh fish dishes, from a menu interspersed with a few modern touches.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14744;L'Ami Jean;France;Paris;27 rue Malar, Paris, 75007, France;48.8603113;2.3059323;38;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Passionate about fine seasonal produce, Stéphane Jégo serves cuisine that is bursting with generosity and flavours. Dishes with quite some character! Be sure to book.;;[]
14745;Claire et Hugo;France;Troyes;77 avenue du Général-Galliéni, à Sainte-Savine, Troyes, 10300, France;48.2936931;4.0526735;23;false;false;Farm to table;An enthusiastic self-taught young couple runs this restaurant with a subdued decor composed of raw materials. The premises also house a bakery and delicatessen leading onto a lovely terrace and indoor garden (including a citrus tree greenhouse). The ingredients, which are 95% organic, make for healthy, tasty and balanced dishes.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14746;Auberge de Port Vallières;France;Fondettes;195 quai des Bateliers, Fondettes, 37230, France;47.3871058;0.6115117;51;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;On the banks of the Loire, this slate-roofed, white stone country inn is a temple to fine produce and traditional cooking. The score ranges from a carpaccio of veal’s head, truffles and a ravigote sauce to scallops lacquered in a BBQ sauce flavoured with instant coffee for a more contemporary edge. Elegant and welcoming, the restaurant also stands out by its slick, seamless service and a stonking wine bin, rich in regional tipples. An establishment that continues to delight a loyal crowd of discerning foodies.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14747;Le Mas des Aigras - Table du Verger;France;Orange;Chemin des Aigras, Orange, 84100, France;44.160072;4.784744;53;false;true;Provençal;Pleasant stone farmhouse set amid vineyards and fields. The chef rustles up, partly in front of diners, tasty recipes based on organic produce. Tasteful decor and attractive terrace. An ideal spot for stopovers, this hotel’s rooms are enlivened with Provençal colours.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14748;Manger & Dormir sur la Plage;France;Marennes;61 avenue William Bertrand, Marennes, 17320, France;45.817033;-1.1357578;32;false;false;Seafood;It sounds like the title of a song from the 1980s. This young and relaxed restaurant facing the sea offers marine-inspired cuisine, with a mouthwatering choice of shellfish, fish, and of course oysters: the establishment belongs to the Gillardeau family, the famous oyster farmers. The large terrace offers a lovely view, with the Île d'Oléron on the horizon. As for accommodation, "Dormir sur la Plage" has four large very well-appointed junior suites.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14749;À l’Épi d’Or;France;Paris;25 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau, Paris, 75001, France;48.8629035;2.341121;49;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This quintessential Parisian bistro of the former Baltard market is the latest acquisition of Elodie and Jean-François Piège. The authentic vintage interior (old tiles and mirrors and stained walls) provides the setting for traditional fare that changes daily during the week. Also available: pork pie, croque madame, foie gras, steak tartare and chips.;;[]
14752;Le Jardin;France;Haguenau;16 rue de la Redoute, Haguenau, 67500, France;48.8107246;7.7916833;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the family for three decades, this restaurant with its trompe l'œil façade and Renaissance ceiling is virtually an institution. Running the kitchen today is young Romain Meyer, who worked alongside his father for eight years and continues to serve the house classics (fish soup, tuna carpaccio, Chateaubriand with Béarnaise sauce), albeit with a nod to more modern tastes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14753;Arcada;France;Bordeaux;13 rue de la Rousselle, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.83762;-0.56906;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away between Place Camille-Jullian and Saint-Michel, a contemporary vibe sets the scene in the vaulted dining room whose bistronomic menu is ingredient-centred: in fact, some 90% of the fruit and veg comes from small, local producers. At lunchtime, you might sample a deliciously priced tataki of marinated watermelon in soy and citrus fruit or confit of loin of hake baked in olive oil. The culinary score becomes more high-flying in the evenings as do the ingredients. The menu changes regularly. Outstanding warm welcome and service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14754;Les Bords de Mer;France;Marseille;52 corniche du Président-John-Fitzgerald-Kennedy, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2892959;5.3547228;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Subtle cuisine and a stunning sea view: what more could we ask for? Chef Camille Gandolfo, who hails from Marseille, adds a fresh (occasionally Asian) spin to her original Mediterranean recipes in a bid to showcase seasonal produce. The savvy wine list gives top billing to the organic production of the Domaine de Fontenille wine estate (AOP Luberon), which owns this elegant establishment. An impressive restaurant that takes its food seriously.;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14755;Cédrat;France;Marseille;81 rue Breteuil, Marseille, 13006, France;43.2885822;5.3765713;35;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;A couple, two chefs, two different culinary formulas: at lunchtime, chef Maëlyss Vultaggio chalks up her menu on the blackboard, assisted in the kitchen by Éric Maillet, a young chef who earned his stripes working for the likes of Gérald Passedat. In the evening, the roles are reversed: he takes the lead, creating more of a fine dining menu with his partner supporting him. Dishes such as farmhouse chicken on the barbecue, celeriac confit, sorrel, ginger/lemongrass sauce and XO reduction exemplify this modern Mediterranean-style cuisine. Using organic vegetables, locally caught fish and well-reared meats, the food certainly packs a punch. Contemporary setting.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14756;Epona;France;Lyon;InterContinental Lyon - Hotel Dieu, 20 quai Jules-Courmont, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7588365;4.8369302;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A hospital for eight centuries, the former Hôtel-Dieu has preserved all the building's historical character. The Epona restaurant serves regional specialities with a modern twist, which you can enjoy in a lovely setting that calls to mind a high-end brasserie. And in fine weather, the team welcomes you in a superb courtyard garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14757;La Réserve de Nice;France;Nice;62 boulevard Franck-Pilatte, Nice, 06300, France;43.6918769;7.2916025;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Elegant, Art Deco cruise liner - inspired decor. Enjoy refined cuisine and superb views of the Bay of Angels and the Estérel mountains.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14759;Bar des Oiseaux;France;Nice;5 rue Saint-Vincent, Nice, 06300, France;43.6973424;7.2751574;76;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In this small corner house, Armand Crespo's "Bird Bar" won't fail to have foodies flapping with delight. Fine traditional French dishes (brandade, bourride) feature alongside delicious artisanal pasta: ravioli and stuffed chicken, seafood linguine etc. All at reasonable prices, in a decor inspired by pop art.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14761;Le 27 Gambetta;France;Nancy;27 rue Gambetta, Nancy, 54000, France;48.692191;6.1806362;42;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Cod simmered in olive oil, butternut purée and bacon powder, or young pigeon with creamy sweet potatoes and foamy mashed potatoes: the chef crafts delicate bistro fare to which he adds his own personal signature, two minutes from Place Stanislas.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14762;Pleine Terre;France;Paris;15 rue de Bassano, Paris, 75116, France;48.8689401;2.2970938;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Behind a discreet façade, down the few steps leading to the basement, you will find a chef who is passionate about citrus fruits, spices and pepper: he has developed a cuisine that closely follows the seasons and showcases the work of handpicked small-scale producers. An inventive array of dishes, served by a friendly and enthusiastic front-of-house team: a great find.;Air conditioning;[]
14763;Ducasse sur Seine;France;Paris;Port Debilly, Paris, 75016, France;48.8611804;2.2928294;83;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Well, no one can say that Alain Ducasse lacks for boldness or ideas, as the Ducasse sur Seine once again proves. An electric boat, moored on the quayside of Port Debilly in the swanky 16th arrondissement, offers a gastronomic cruise that is both ecological and silent. At the same time as you discover Parisian monuments, you will taste up - to - the - minute cuisine, masterfully crafted by a kitchen team worthy of the best restaurants. Well done, mon capitaine!;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking;[]
14765;Le Divil;France;Perpignan;9 rue Fabriques-d'en-Nabot, Perpignan, 66000, France;42.7000921;2.8938634;81;true;true;Meats and Grills;Between Le Castillet and the prefecture, a specialist of fine matured meats: customers choose their piece (rib steak, entrecote, sirloin), which is then weighed, grilled and accompanied by tasty home - made fries. There are 300 types of wine to wash it down.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14766;Le Café des Artistes;France;Ville-d'Avray;53 rue de Versailles, Ville-d'Avray, 92410, France;48.8220971;2.1832201;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This bistro is the ideal complement to the Michelin-starred restaurant of this oh-so-bucolic establishment on the outskirts of Paris. It serves contemporary, tasty and inspired cuisine made with top-notch produce – delicious cod, Coco de Paimpol beans, chorizo and lobster cream – that you can enjoy on the terrace as you take in the view of the charming garden. Idyllic.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14767;L'Inconnu;France;Paris;4 rue Pierre-Leroux, Paris, 75007, France;48.8502565;2.3186047;90;true;true;Italian, Creative;The chef, who for a long time was second-in-command at Passage 53, concocts Italian-inspired cuisine with influences from France, as well as his native Japan. He only works with the finest ingredients, using them to produce original and creative dishes, such as Breton langoustine tails topped with a cider and confit lemon emulsion.;;[]
14768;Arnaud Nicolas;France;Paris;46 avenue de la Bourdonnais, Paris, 75007, France;48.8570631;2.3010077;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Pork butchers who can cook don't grow on trees, especially not in this residential part of the 7th arrondissement (a stone's throw from the Eiffel Tower, no less). The chef-patron appropriates pâté en croûte and terrine to create his "haute couture charcuterie". The interior is unadorned and elegant. The small shop at the restaurant entrance means you can take a piece of this culinary experience home.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14769;Brasserie Lutetia;France;Paris;45 boulevard Raspail, Paris, 75006, France;48.8514122;2.3269755;15;true;false;Seafood;Tartare of wild sea bass, sole meunière, Burgundy snails with parsley butter: the famous Brasserie Lutetia proudly serves the classics that have made its reputation, as well as some more contemporary creations. Purists and regulars alike can't get enough of the easy-going refined Art Deco atmosphere. Conservatory, mezzanine or patio: take your pick!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14770;L'Atelier d'Olivier Arlot;France;Saint-Cyr-sur-Loire;55 quai des Maisons-Blanches, Saint-Cyr-sur-Loire, 37540, France;47.3954855;0.6562458;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set up by Olivier Arlot on the banks of the Loire, L'Atelier is modern both in terms of the decor and the menu. They serve up tasty and savvy creations, such as oxtail terrine and foie gras – a happy combination that melts in the mouth! This is bistronomy at its best, with intriguing and punchy dishes, plus a menu that is renewed very regularly.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14771;Le Clos de la Fontaine;France;Guingamp;9 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Guingamp, 22200, France;48.5632059;-3.1503283;85;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A welcoming rustic-style interior (tablecloths, English crockery), friendly service and skilfully executed cuisine: Stéphane Ollivier and his wife Corinne certainly know how to receive guests. The generous dishes are made with plenty of good local ingredients (eg scallops, oysters, Breton cheeses) and include tasty local specialties, such as roast duck breast strips with cider and tarragon sauce.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14772;L'Épicurieux;France;Illies;5 rue Mermoz, Illies, 59480, France;50.5616626;2.8312173;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This cosy modern bistro with an immaculate white façade is run by former Top Chef contestant Christophe Pirotais and his partner Julie Dieudonné. Food lovers should take this as an invitation to come and taste delicious dishes made with local produce such as dog cockles, mushrooms, olives and black radish, or pollack, pumpkin, yacón and Jerusalem artichoke.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14773;Bistro Gaby;France;Château-Arnoux-Saint-Auban;14 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Château-Arnoux-Saint-Auban, 04160, France;44.0937917;6.0097634;83;true;true;Provençal;The restaurant’s name and wholesome French country cooking are a tribute to Gaby, who was the chef’s grandmother. Market- and garden-fresh ingredients take pride of place in this attractive homely interior, adorned in soft provençal colours.;Air conditioning;[]
14776;Le Relais du Castelet;France;Fontvieille;Mas le Castelet, quartier Montmajour, Fontvieille, 13990, France;43.7137044;4.6807987;30;true;true;Provençal;This former hunting lodge surrounded by hilly olive groves is a genuine haven of tranquillity. You can expect deftly crafted, local Provençal recipes, served generously with a distinct preference for veggies and herbs from the garden, supplemented by ingredients from local producers. Ten out of ten for Jean-Baptiste Bert who has added a contemporary chapter to the family property where he was born.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14777;Les Hortensias du Lac;France;Hossegor;1578 avenue du Tour-du-Lac, Hossegor, 40150, France;43.6752982;-1.432603;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This local institution boasting an idyllic location on the shore of Lake Hossegor extends a charming welcome to its guests. Chef Philippe Moreno, a protégé of Gérald Passedat, serves carefully prepared, high-quality cuisine, with well-executed dishes organised into a seasonal menu and a tasting menu. Fish from Capbreton's fish market and excellent poultry from the Landes area take pride of place. Enjoy your meal in the bright bistro interior, or on the pleasant terrace, in a chic, laid-back atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14778;Emporium;France;Lecci;32 boulevard Napoléon, à San Ciprianu, Lecci, 20137, France;41.6382534;9.3465165;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;Before setting up shop in San Ciprianu, Italian-born chef Sébastien Salamon clocked up stints in some top establishments (Guy Savoy, Le V). The technical brilliance and precise seasoning on display in his spider crab cappelletti, in particular, are testament to this experience. The grilled escalope of foie gras with flaky brioche and cherry tartare is a real treat. With direct links to the terroir (local fish, Bonifacio market gardens, Corsican veal), the short menu features absolutely top-notch contemporary cuisine – to be savoured in the magnificent setting of a spacious, light-filled veranda.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14779;La Table de Romain;France;Renescure;1 rue Gaston-Robbe, Renescure, 59173, France;50.7279114;2.3706243;83;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This village restaurant with typical local architecture is located in the heart of this market town. It is the HQ of a chef who proposes a set menu at an unbeatable price during the week, and more elaborate dishes at the weekend, when some premium ingredients are deployed. Menu and produce regularly adapted. To enjoy in a chic and convivial interior.;Terrace;[]
14781;La Rotonde;France;Nice;Le Negresco, 37 promenade des Anglais, Nice, 06000, France;43.6942999;7.2579981;74;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The rotunda-shaped brasserie of the legendary luxury hotel has resolutely entered the modern world. In this light-filled space (with a terrace), you choose from a menu (designed by Michelin-starred chef Virginie Basselot) that celebrates a flavoursome and colourful cuisine full of Mediterranean flair, with nods to Nice's traditions.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14782;L'alouette;France;Toulouse;24 place Victor-Hugo, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.60681;1.4469557;79;true;true;Farm to table;Nicolas Servant, former chef of the Bon Servant, is at the helm of this friendly eatery acclaimed by good food lovers. Splendid range of aged meat and offal (pig’s ears, calf’s liver and sweetbread), spring veggies from the nearby market (white asparagus and chorizo) and desserts to die for (clafouti of seasonal fruit)! A wholesome, casual vibe is perfectly suited to a drink and meal with the mates…;Terrace;[]
14783;Sources;France;Nantes;22 rue de Verdun, Nantes, 44000, France;47.21685;-1.55256;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The meat, fish and vegetables are all meticulously sourced at Sources. You can expect fresh, bold bistro cuisine with a vegetarian and seafood slant. The front-of-house team aims to please, offering excellent natural wine tips along the way.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14784;Brasserie Chavant;France;Voiron;72 avenue Léon-et-Joanny-Tardy, Voiron, 38500, France;45.3633179;5.5970043;87;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Located in a handsome mansion, not far from the Chartreuse cellars, this tastefully redecorated brasserie, which boasts a fine wooden staircase leading up to the guestrooms, offers a patriotic line-up of Gallic fare, in which delicacies from Voiron feature prominently, such as cabbage stuffed with venison, free-range poultry with a Chartreuse-flavoured jus or the iced parfait, also perfumed with Chartreuse. Very pleasant welcome and service.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14785;Bec;France;Paradou;55 avenue de la Vallée-des-Baux, Paradou, 13520, France;43.7205992;4.786917;62;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Set up in an old Provençal farmhouse standing in the shadow of a small church and boasting a pretty courtyard, this restaurant run by a young couple serves fresh modern cuisine with international influences. Lovers of fine food will appreciate the monkfish marinated in satay served with watercress purée – to be savoured in the inviting rustic-style interior or on the delightful terrace clad in laurel trees and Virginia creeper.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14786;Auberge de Crussol;France;Saint-Péray;Chemin de Beauregard, Saint-Péray, 07130, France;44.9411897;4.8484458;60;false;true;Grills;Perched on the heights of Saint-Péray, a stone’s throw from the ruins of Crussol castle, this former sheepfold is now the venue for regional country cooking. The meat, fish and vegetables are baked in a wood-fired oven or roasted on a spit. The chef showcases local produce, farm-reared veal and pork and organic eggs and veggies... Warm, welcoming vibe and a suitably rustic interior.;Car park,Terrace;[]
14787;Peixes Opéra;France;Nice;4 rue Jacques-Médecin, Nice, 06000, France;43.69589;7.27104;47;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Near the town hall and the opera house is Peixes – pronounced "pesh" (i.e. "fish" in Portuguese). In its small bistro interior with white and blue tiles and a very Mediterranean feel, fish and seafood cuisine is served in the form of tapas-style dishes (ceviche, carpaccio, fried fish, cod accras). This is a popular place, and spots on the terrace are hotly contested (no reservations!).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14788;Le Séjour Café;France;Nice;11 rue Grimaldi, Nice, 06000, France;43.6988011;7.2650424;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Shelves filled with books, trinkets and plants, paintings and photos on the walls set the scene for what feels like the inviting sitting room of a lovely private mansion. Now let’s add the appeal of market-fresh cuisine, an abundance of culinary delights and a commitment to respecting the seasons, without forgetting the gracious welcome and service.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14789;Vincent Croizard;France;Nîmes;17 rue des Chassaintes, Nîmes, 30000, France;43.83719;4.352915;92;true;false;Creative;You will need to ring the bell at this discreet townhouse in a narrow street near the Carré d'Art in order to gain access. The self - taught chef composes lovely creative cuisine, striking out and experimenting with at times surprising combinations. His wife is behind the superb selection of wines, which showcases the Languedoc - Roussillon.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14790;Auberge de la Roussille;France;Niort;30 impasse de la Roussille, St-Liguaire, Niort, 79000, France;46.3325307;-0.5081476;67;true;true;Modern Cuisine;One can't help but fall under the spell of this fine lock - keeper's house, which stands in the bucolic setting on the banks of the Sèvre. An enchanting environment, but that doesn't eclipse the main focus, which is the chef's meticulous and well - calibrated cooking. Ingredients are top notch and enhanced without frills. A real pleasure.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14792;Relais Chantovent;France;Minerve;17 Grand-Rue, Minerve, 34210, France;43.3543297;2.7467212;91;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A charming country inn in Cathar, where diners and pilgrims alike arrive on foot, eager to do justice to meat dishes that simmer for hours, illustrated by 24-hour low-temperature roast pork, or 20-hour leg of lamb roasted at 70°C. All the ingredients come solely from the surrounding local markets. The terrace with its view over the Briant valley is sumptuous.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14793;Disini;France;Castries;1 rue des Carrières, Castries, 34160, France;43.6842912;3.9912929;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Established in a hotel surrounded by oak trees, this fine dining venue boasts a bright airy dining room and an alfresco area sheltered by foliage. After a dip in the pool, treat yourself to a meal underscored by Asian influences, crafted by a chef who’s something of a fan of molecular gastronomy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14794;Marcelle - Domaine de Verchant;France;Castelnau-le-Lez;1 boulevard Philippe-Lamour, Castelnau-le-Lez, 34170, France;43.6252365;3.9215376;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;(Temporarily closed, reopening planned for spring) A few minutes outside Montpellier, amid fields and vineyards, a major surprise awaits. This superb hotel and wine estate boasts enchanting surroundings to be contemplated through the bay windows of the dining area. Favouring seasonal produce from the southernmost reaches of France, the chef composes elegant, meticulous dishes that steer clear of bells and whistles. His creations abound with personality and flavour, eg roast saddle of Lozère lamb with artichoke and Collioure anchovies – best enjoyed with one of the estate's wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14795;Au Bon Accueil;France;Attin;52 route Nationale 39, Attin, 62170, France;50.4872148;1.7447965;76;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;There are countless examples of these former inns that have been given a facelift by young business partners. In this case the gamble has paid off! A modern bistro interior is the setting for good homemade fare that showcases ingredients fresh from the market. And at such reasonable prices, who could ask for more?;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14796;Magma;France;Caen;24 rue Saint-Manvieu, Caen, 14000, France;49.1829122;-0.3713232;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This town house, outside the centre of Caen, is almost on the doorstep of the Abbaye-aux-Hommes. Olivier Barbarin, an experienced chef who is no stranger to fine dining, concocts food that resembles his character – uninhibited and appetising, including a nod to his native Auvergne – the purple walls evoke volcanic rock like pozzolan. Bargain priced lunch deal, and the dinner tasting menu changes depending on the market and the chef’s mood.;;[]
14797;Au Koning Van Peene;France;Zuytpeene;8 contour de l'Église, Zuytpeene, 59670, France;50.7932857;2.4306606;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the centre of an out-of-the-way village in the Flanders region, this place is an unexpected foodie haven: chef Kevin Barata and Lucile Prevost (partners in business and in life) welcome travellers into their inviting restaurant with an interior in which brick and wood predominate. The chef, who knows his stuff, whips up good simple dishes, such as lamb kofta, thyme-lemon hummus, barbecue sauce and kataifi, or farmhouse pork chop, cauliflower, horseradish, asparagus and a reduction of cooking juices. Lunch is excellent value.;Terrace;[]
14798;Dyades au Domaine des Étangs;France;Massignac;Domaine des Étangs, Massignac, 16310, France;45.7761702;0.6439324;57;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Picture a sprawling estate (almost 2,500 acres) of woodland, forest, meadows, fields, farms and ponds and now add a 13C castle equipped with every modern comfort one would expect from a top-of-the-range luxury establishment. The former stables have been converted into a dining area that adroitly blends antique and trendy details. At its helm, chef Matthieu Pasgrimaud (Saint Tropez’ La Vague d’Or and Manhattan’s Daniel Boulud) can be relied upon to make the most of the first-class produce grown on the estate, scattered with aromatic herbs and garden veggies. Kitchen garden dishes (Camus artichoke flowers and plum amandon oil) vie for pride of place with dishes to share, more classical recipes and the chef’s signatures (like sturgeon loaf and Neuvic caviar) in a culinary repertory that is as eclectic as it is high-flying. Chloé Tardivel, the chef’s partner, elegantly and seamlessly manages the welcome and service.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14799;Maison Kieny;France;Riedisheim;7 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Riedisheim, 68400, France;47.749585;7.3682191;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This inviting coaching inn (from 1850) not far from Mulhouse occupies an imposing traditional Alsatian building in the centre of the village. In an elegant dining room, the chef serves seasonal cuisine with a contemporary bent, such as slow-cooked egg with peas and a creamy sauce made with their pods, or lamb cooked two ways, accompanied by chick peas in a French curry. Simpler bistro fare on weekday lunches.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14800;Michel - Brasserie des Catalans;France;Marseille;6 rue des Catalans, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2907259;5.3560159;15;true;false;Seafood;Soak up the atmosphere of Marseille in this popular restaurant on the Plage des Catalans. Here they take their bouillabaisse very seriously... and it tastes phenomenal! As you would expect, the menu proposes an exceptionally fresh catch of the day: you will see the fish in the tanks as you come in.;Air conditioning;[]
14801;Aroma;France;Les Herbiers;7 rue du Brandon, Les Herbiers, 85500, France;46.8709308;-1.0159927;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This modern and colourful restaurant in the town centre is run by a young couple who have plenty of drive. They have created an evolving menu, never departing from the sacrosanct trio of freshness, tastiness and Vendée ingredients.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14802;TO;France;Paris;34 rue Beaurepaire, Paris, 75010, France;48.8715161;2.3644176;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Just a stone's throw from Canal Saint-Martin, enter this TO – "door" in Japanese – to discover the French-Japanese fusion cuisine of chef Ryo Miyazaki (who previously worked at Saturne). Inside: a series of three modern spaces, each with a distinct atmosphere. Inspired and meticulously presented dishes, in different "omakase" formats.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14806;La Lanterne;France;Metz;17 place de la Chambre, Metz, 57000, France;49.1206207;6.1743435;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine;La Lanterne is inspired by "La Lanterne du Bon Dieu", the nickname given to Metz Cathedral, which looms over the restaurant. It is run by a young couple who really give it their all: chef Célia Bertrand, originally from Metz, and Romain Bouchesèche, from the Jura, who takes care of matters in the dining room and in the wine cellar. They propose modern cuisine (pollack, morels, vin jaune) that draws inspiration from the Jura, where they met.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14807;Alleudium;France;Paris;24 rue Rodier, Paris, 75009, France;48.878431;2.3428312;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Keiichi Shinohara, a Japanese chef with solid credentials (including a stint at Le Violon d'Ingres during the Christian Constant era), is at the helm of this restaurant with refined contemporary decor. Customer satisfaction is the goal here, in particular when it comes to the food, which is modern and inspired, with the odd nod to Japan.;Air conditioning;[]
14808;Au Vieux Pressoir;France;Mesnil-Saint-Père;5 rue du 28-août-1944, Mesnil-Saint-Père, 10140, France;48.2482249;4.3328404;39;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;On the Lac d'Orient road, this half-timbered house, typical of the Champagne Humide region, offers house specialities that juggle with tradition: salad of prawns with fennel and baby spinach, brill and beurre blanc sauce with champagne, chocolate sphere packed with berries. There are also comfortable guestrooms, a pleasant spa area and a bistro in an adjoining building. "Maison Gublin" is doing well.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14809;Le Parc;France;Besançon;Place de la 1ère-Armée-Française, Besançon, 25000, France;47.242146;6.0296086;74;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the Parc Micaud, on the banks of the River Doubs, this glass, concrete and steel pavilion is the Modernist work of Besançon architect Michel Demenge. The chic, contemporary interior, with its open-plan kitchen, also offers a view of the river. Dishes are in a contemporary vein, the menu under the supervision of the chef of nearby Château de Germigney.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14810;L'Entre-Roches;France;Ville-du-Pont;1 rue Principale, Ville-du-Pont, 25650, France;47.0030297;6.4788589;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the self-proclaimed "Republic of Saugeais" on the Swiss border, the proprietors are as meticulous about their spruce and contemporary premises as they are about the food they serve. The chef proposes delicious, indulgent and flavourful cuisine, and it’s worth mentioning the exceptionally warm and friendly service.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14811;Le Clos des Oliviers;France;Saint-Gély-du-Fesc;53 rue de l'Aven, Saint-Gély-du-Fesc, 34980, France;43.6782203;3.8154505;16;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Taste, simplicity, skilful use of quality ingredients: here, you can enjoy good food without unnecessary complications – and what a real pleasure! The wine list is put together with the neighbouring cellarman. In summer, make the most of the terrace in the shade of the reed screening.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14813;Le Cèpe;France;Méribel;1827 Résidence Les Merisiers, Méribel, 73550, France;45.39894;6.57439;54;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;It all starts with fine produce from the local land, mountain porcini or fish from the neighbouring lakes, which the chef comes out and proudly present to diners. He then turns it into delightful, fresh dishes, all the tastier for the unbeatable prices. A place that is quite simply comfortable in its own skin.;Terrace;[]
14814;Gusto Caffe;France;Martigues;4 quai Paul-Doumer, Martigues, 13500, France;43.4073824;5.0531367;37;true;false;Italian;In front of the Canal Baussengue marina, a picturesque trattoria where waiters and clients call to each other in a cheerful and distinctly Italian atmosphere! Homemade fare (spaghetti, gnocchi etc), Parma prosciutto cut with the slicer, and the great Italian classics. The terrace is taken by storm in fine weather, as is the lunchtime chalkboard menu, excellent value for money.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14816;Chai nous comme Chai vous;France;La Flotte;1 rue de la Garde, La Flotte, 17630, France;46.187037;-1.323898;66;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Friendly and attractive, this pocket handkerchief restaurant instantly makes you feel at home. The concise, appetising menu showcases island produce with a weakness for seafood, illustrated by the flawlessly cooked monkfish, flanked by a chardonnay-flavoured sabayon and white asparagus. Intelligently curated wine list, the occasional inventive note and a scattering of thoughtful attentions.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14817;Le 703;France;Paris;9 rue Fourcroy, Paris, 75017, France;48.8803999;2.2961791;74;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Navigating between France and Japan, chef Naomi Ogaki trained in Alsace and Provence, under the tutelage of Antoine Westermann and Christian Étienne respectively. In his lovely bistro complete with a long counter, he serves high-quality traditional French cuisine that draws on influences of Alsace in autumn and winter, and of the South of France in spring and summer. House classics include pâté en croûte, game, spaetzle, home-made boudin, fish aioli – not to mention some first-rate classic desserts.;;[]
14818;Ardent;France;Esvres-sur-Indre;Loire Valley Lodges, 1 allée de la Duporterie, Esvres-sur-Indre, 37320, France;47.32186;0.79232;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the midst of sprawling private woodland, where lodges on stilts and contemporary art blend in with the trees, a restored farmstead gradually comes into view, appointed in a full-blown arty and sylvan theme. Serenity is the watchword of this establishment, which uses only top-quality ingredients in carefully crafted recipes that scrupulously respect the seasons in a single set menu that can be ordered in a choice of courses. The establishment’s kitchen garden and the harvest of wild plant foraging forays feature prominently in the gastronomic lineup.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14819;Nolinski;France;Paris;16 avenue de l'Opéra, Paris, 75001, France;48.8657607;2.3344799;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;On Avenue de l'Opéra, near the Comédie Française, a chic brasserie whose vintage interior mixes Art Deco and the 1970s, with mirrors, gilding, yellow marble and corduroy upholstering. The culinary lineup by Philip Chronopoulos is big-boned and Gallic down to its core (pot au feu, poultry and sweetbread vol au vent, veal cutlet with morels).;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14820;Bistrot du Bac;France;Combrit;19 rue du Bac, à Sainte-Marine, Combrit, 29120, France;47.873912;-4.1190301;42;true;true;Seafood;This Breton restaurant is located on the quayside of Sainte-Marine's little port, facing Bénodet – to which there is a ferry link in season. The terrace affords picturesque views over the River Odet estuary, the dining area is painted blue and white (as are the guestrooms) and, most importantly, the food celebrates the sea, with fresh and simple dishes (special mention for the sole). A very pleasant port of call.;Great view,Terrace;[]
14821;Osmossi - Maison Mavrommatis;France;Paris;70 avenue Paul-Doumer, Paris, 75016, France;48.8598676;2.2790358;52;true;true;Greek, Mediterranean Cuisine;One of the restaurants of Andreas Mavrommatis, maestro of Mediterranean food in Paris. In a contemporary bistro-style interior, decorated with photos from Nikos Aliagas' collection, diners enjoy meze, pan-fried octopus with fava from Santorini or soudjoukakia (beef meatballs with tomato and cumin). It's fresh and tasty. Delicatessen and wine shop.;Air conditioning;[]
14822;Ermitage de Corton;France;Chorey-lès-Beaune;D974, Chorey-lès-Beaune, 21200, France;47.0523061;4.8576708;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this house set in vineyards opposite Corton “mountain”, the chef aims to shine the spotlight on local producers. His modern meticulous cuisine draws upon his classical training and features a traditional Gallic line-up, including snails and œufs en meurette (poached eggs in red wine) crafted with text-book precision. Stylish interior, inviting patio and spacious guestrooms to prolong your stay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14823;Coretta;France;Paris;151 bis rue Cardinet, Paris, 75017, France;48.890823;2.3176746;17;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the Clichy-Batignolles district, opposite Martin Luther King Park (King's wife was called Coretta), Mexican-born chef Beatriz Gonzalez, with stints in star-rated eateries of the likes of Senderens and La Grande Cascade, consummately curates a season-driven menu rich in big-boned generous flavours. Youthful, buzzy front-of-house team and a bright airy designer interior overlooking the trees in the park from the second floor.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14824;Le Bistrot du Bord de l'Eau;France;Levernois;Hostellerie de Levernois, 15 rue du Golf, Levernois, 21200, France;46.992768;4.8776647;22;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A delightful rustic dining room with exposed stonework, beams and a fireplace serves as the setting for the traditional, regional cuisine served in this restaurant. Enjoy mouthwatering dishes such as Meurette - style eggs (in a red wine sauce), belly of pork and blanquette of veal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14826;Pouliche;France;Paris;11 rue d'Enghien, Paris, 75010, France;48.8717113;2.3524058;39;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this friendly neo-bistro, Amandine Chaignot fetes market produce, spontaneity and creativity, without ever betraying the flavours of her carefully selected ingredients. Indeed, that is the approach that has informed her single set menu: only the main course is chosen by the guest – meat, fish or vegetarian – with the rest of the meal left to the chef's discretion. On Wednesdays, the set menu is entirely vegetarian. On Sundays, you can enjoy traditional family-style chicken dishes. Good value for money at lunchtime. Pouliche will steal your heart.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14827;Le Saint-Sébastien;France;Paris;42 rue Saint-Sébastien, Paris, 75011, France;48.8616215;2.3712039;54;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It's an enticing offer in this neighbourhood bar turned into a hub of bistronomie cooking: a short menu that respects the seasons, very vegetable oriented, a judicious choice of seasonings, masterful use of herbs and spices to add character to the dishes… not to mention good natural wines. Spot on.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
14828;La Yole de Chris;France;La Rochelle;Plage de la Concurrence, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1553007;-1.1598394;96;false;true;Seafood;This dazzling place by Christopher Coutanceau offers two incomparable pleasures: for the eyes and for the taste buds. A long counter in the shape of a skiff (light, long and narrow boat), houses the open kitchen, where the cooks can be seen in action. Seafood (oysters and shellfish) and fish of the day enjoy pride of place on the menu here... to be enjoyed on the terrace that overlooks the sea, in fine weather. Booking recommended.;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14830;Fleur de Neige;France;Châtel;564 route de Vonnes, Châtel, 74390, France;46.26213;6.84085;20;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Duck pâté en croûte with foie gras, calf's head with ravigote, pavlova with bilberries: this tasty and hearty traditional cuisine is served in a family atmosphere and – in summer – on the lovely panoramic terrace, with a view of the Chablais mountains.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14833;Ore;France;Versailles;Place d'Armes, Versailles, 78000, France;48.8041792;2.1219968;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Ore means "mouth" in Latin. A disarmingly simple name for this place that is quite simply exceptional – a 17C pavilion within the Palace of Versailles. Alain Ducasse is the Sun King of the premises, enforcing the culinary law for which he is known. That of naturality and a constantly renewed homage to fine ingredients.;Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
14834;Cap de Castel;France;Puylaurens;36 rue Cap-de-Castel, Puylaurens, 81700, France;43.5708898;2.0157119;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Take a seat on the splendid terrace with the Pyrenees in the distance and the Montagne Noire in the foreground and get ready to sample modern cuisine with traditional touches. The food highlights local produce, such as veal raised in Puylaurens, lightly seared and served rare with Veggie Wellington and a coffee-flavoured veal gravy. Lovely guestrooms to prolong your stay in style.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14837;Le Bœuf en Écailles;France;Magné;24 avenue du Marais-Poitevin, Magné, 79460, France;46.3111315;-0.5276731;25;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Authenticity is a word so often used as to be almost meaningless, but it is nonetheless the right term for the gutsy, flavoursome food of this establishment. The meat and fish recipes are steeped in generous mouth-watering flavours, such as 16-hour roast pork with mashed potato in olive oil. The lovely patio on the banks of the Sèvre Niortaise is also authentic.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14839;L'Hippocampe;France;Vichy;3 boulevard de Russie, Vichy, 03200, France;46.121414;3.4197958;84;true;false;Seafood;In his restaurant near the Parc des Sources, chef Gilles Ruyet prepares seafood dishes in a traditional vein: sole meunière, seared halibut with a beurre blanc sauce, not forgetting the crystallised orange soufflé with Grand Marnier – prepared by his daughter Marianne, who is also to be seen on the restaurant floor. Attractive contemporary decor, plus a view of the kitchen and the lobster tank.;Air conditioning;[]
14840;La Maison Tourangelle;France;Savonnières;9 route des Grottes-Pétrifiantes, Savonnières, 37510, France;47.3474002;0.5416983;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Rustic meets modern in this 18C Touraine building. It boasts a delightful terrace on the Cher and fine cuisine using quality ingredients.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14842;Le M - Château de Massillan;France;Uchaux;730 chemin de Massillan, Uchaux, 84100, France;44.2332145;4.7932319;77;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This beautiful 16C castle stands in extensive grounds surrounded by vineyards. The food aims to enhance the estate’s organic cottage garden and orchard produce. You can wash down your meal with a biodynamic wine from the Domaine de la Guicharde, which also produces the olive oil used in the kitchen. Slick, smiling service. In summer, take a seat in the courtyard adorned with a fountain, overlooking the garden.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14843;Campagne, Vignes et Gourmandises;France;Sainte-Cécile-les-Vignes;629 chemin des Terres, Sainte-Cécile-les-Vignes, 84290, France;44.2525673;4.8842377;92;true;false;Provençal;With its atmosphere blending rustic charm (exposed stones, painted wooden furniture) and modern touches (contemporary paintings), this restaurant has bags of character. In the kitchen, chef Sylvain Fernandes prepares fresh ingredients in a subtle celebration of the flavours of the South of France. Extremely courteous service provided by Sylvia, the chef's wife!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14844;Le Montrachet;France;Puligny-Montrachet;10 place du Pasquier-de-la-Fontaine, Puligny-Montrachet, 21190, France;46.9445744;4.7537454;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Classic refinement: the description is equally applicable to the restaurant – all exposed stonework and beams – and the seasonal cuisine. This is prepared by a chef who has cut his teeth in some leading restaurants and displays his skills with care and elegance.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14847;Òliba;France;Molitg-les-Bains;Château de Riell, Molitg-les-Bains, 66500, France;42.647541;2.3869296;51;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set deep in the Catalan Pyrenees, this refined restaurant in a romantic hotel serves flavoursome cuisine inspired by the surrounding countryside and locally picked produce: the local version of chimichurri sauce with mountain herbs exudes aromas of wild dill and burnet flowers. To be enjoyed on the terrace or in front of the picture windows, as you contemplate the snow-capped summit of Mount Canigou in the distance.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14848;Sépia;France;Marseille;2 rue Vauvenargues, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2890614;5.3686499;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This guinguette perched on the Colline Puget promises an incredible view of the city and the sea as well as a colourful dining experience. In the kitchen, the chef's go-to ingredient is seafood, but he also likes to combine fish with a meat sauce (or vice versa), in dishes such as yellowtail with Albufera-style sauce. Next door is Julis – their offshoot wine and tapas bar, which is very popular with locals from the Saint-Victor and Endoume neighbourhoods for after-work drinks.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14849;La Superb;France;Beaune;15 rue d'Alsace, Beaune, 21200, France;47.02256;4.83935;81;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the heart of the old town, this contemporary "dining bar" serves market-fresh dishes that are in tune with the seasons. Take a seat at the counter for views of the chef cooking fine mature meats or his tuna Rossini a la plancha, or alternatively in the small dining room with stone walls and glassed-in wine cellar, and prepare to enjoy tasty, no-frills cuisine. Bargain-price set menu at lunchtime!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14850;MAJU;France;La Turballe;18 quai Saint-Paul, La Turballe, 44420, France;47.3484242;-2.5125711;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;MAJU is a portmanteau of MArine and JUlien, who are at the helm of this elegant contemporary bistro, overlooking the port. From his open kitchen, the chef rustles up an ambitious, modern score in the shape of a single menu rolled out in several courses. Bliss from the first to the last bite thanks to a devotion to detail in terms of plating combined with a focus on premium local country produce, including from the local fish auction, seaweed, samphire and Mesquer pigeon…;Wheelchair access;[]
14851;Auberge Sundgovienne;France;Carspach;1 route de Belfort, Carspach, 68130, France;47.630006;7.2007713;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This hotel restaurant is very pleasant: everything is attractive, contemporary and cosy. The cuisine is of a modern slant, concocted by a chef who is eager to please (dressed crab with avocado and grapefruit, pan-fried scallops with sweet potato mousseline). Fine wine list and comfortable rooms for a stopover.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14852;Maison;France;Paris;3 rue Saint-Hubert, Paris, 75011, France;48.8637612;2.3793456;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Sota Atsumi, whose CV boasts lofty establishments such as Le Clown, Toyo, Michel Troisgros in Roanne, etc., transports diners with his Gallic cuisine imbued with modernity, served as a set menu composed of the best market-fresh ingredients. The fashionable dining area calls to mind a post-industrial loft with its gabled ceiling, huge central table d'hôte and open-plan kitchen (with a wood-fired oven), extended by a bar. Dishes include Mediterranean red tuna, grilled white asparagus and garlic sabayon or grilled scorpion fish and turnips… Pleasantly casual vibe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
14853;Korus;France;Paris;73 rue Amelot, Paris, 75011, France;48.8592917;2.3681901;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This fashionable dinky bistro tucked away between Bastille and République is run by an enthusiastic duo who works closely with a talented chef. Creativity, premium ingredients and unexpected associations result in forthright flavours that hit the spot every time.;Counter dining;[]
14854;Petit Gris;France;Paris;67 rue Rennequin, Paris, 75017, France;48.8843513;2.2944482;75;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Jean-Baptiste Ascione, a former Top Chef contestant, dreamed of opening his own restaurant. Now he has done so in this cosy space (oak floorboards, sanded wooden tables, bistro chairs etc), which celebrates the joys of breaking bread together, by drawing on fine terroir produce and the traditional culinary repertoire.;Air conditioning;[]
14855;La Table des Bauges;France;La Biolle;1821 route d'Annecy, La Biolle, 73410, France;45.7583888;5.9322746;75;true;false;Farm to table;This is the brainchild of chef Clément Girod (formerly with Emmanuel Renaut), who has returned to his birthplace between two lakes. The result ticks all the boxes: local ingredients, homemade bread and ices, an organic wine list and spot-on market-fresh fare, illustrated by rainbow trout, medley of carrots and a carrot and ginger reduction.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14857;La Table d'Armante;France;Saint-Gervais-les-Bains;L'Armancette, 4088 route de Saint-Nicolas, Saint-Gervais-les-Bains, 74170, France;45.8526056;6.7237661;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Inside a luxuriously understated hotel, this chic contemporary mountain restaurant (think wood, stone, velvet and an open kitchen) is run by chef Fabien Laprée. Trained in top establishments and a Meilleur Ouvrier de France finalist in 2018, he crafts modern fare that keeps pace with the seasons, showcasing a lineup of fine alpine and also Mediterranean ingredients. The summer terrace commands a view of the Dômes de Miage mountains.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14858;Caves Pétrissans;France;Paris;30 bis avenue Niel, Paris, 75017, France;48.8813056;2.2955969;33;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This splendid family business has seen successive generations of the Allemoz dynasty at the helm since 1895. Treat yourself to a chicken liver pâté with onion jam, grilled hanger steak or calf’s head with a ravigote sauce. Bistro classics also depict the dessert lineup, with regressive dishes like rum baba or île flottante. An enticing wine list adds the final cherry to this appetising programme.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
14859;Scratch Restaurant;France;Bourg-en-Bresse;2 bis rue Gustave-Doré, Bourg-en-Bresse, 01000, France;46.2034164;5.2252789;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Ardent slow-food disciples, Estelle and Andréas Baehr enthusiastically showcase premium, fresh, organic, local ingredients and shine the spotlight on producers, as well as seeking to share their culinary vision thanks to the chatty lady of the house. Intelligently devised and flawlessly crafted, the lunch and dinner surprise menus are a masterclass of hunger obliterating perfection, illustrated by grilled white and green asparagus, served with a delicate citrus-flavoured cream further enhanced by egg yolk, confit of black garlic and puffed buckwheat. Friendly casual welcome and service. Bookings essential.;;[]
14860;Le Temps Suspendu - Château de Fonscolombe;France;Le Puy-Sainte-Réparade;Route de Saint-Canadet, Le Puy-Sainte-Réparade, 13610, France;43.6395497;5.4682076;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a modern wing of Fonscolombe Castle, Le Temps Suspendu is depicted by a smart, understated interior with exposed timber beams and bay windows opening onto the terrace and grounds. The chef’s elegant, well-crafted cuisine is rich in passing nods to the Mediterranean.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14861;Canaima;France;Lyon;24 rue René-Leynaud, Lyon, 69001, France;45.7699114;4.8342927;58;false;false;Latin American;This tiny restaurant sports a modish interior. Only open in the evening, it is run by a delightful couple and serves Latin American cuisine with a sea focus, peppered with French influences. The Venezuelan chef, formerly of the Paul Bocuse Institute, whips up flavoursome dishes rich in surprise and colour. Smiling service, Chilean and Argentinean wines. A new ethnic establishment on the Lyon culinary scene.;Air conditioning;[]
14862;L'Étape Louis 13;France;Beaumesnil;2 route de la Barre-en-Ouche, Beaumesnil, 27410, France;49.0107216;0.7057674;28;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This 17C presbytery located near the Château de Beaumesnil has a superb Louis XIII - style and exudes a timeless atmosphere. Under the direction of its young owners, it is the ideal place to discover some of Normandy's culinary traditions such as hot oysters with Camembert and light Calvados soufflé. Freshness and flavours are on the agenda.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14863;Ishikawa;France;Bordeaux;22 rue du Hâ, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.836137;-0.5767159;92;true;false;Japanese;In a busy pedestrian street in the city centre, chef Yugo Ishikawa has set up shop in this elongated, minimalist-style restaurant. He throws himself body and soul into his painstakingly crafted dishes from the traditional Japanese cuisine he so loves. On the daily specials board: tonkatsu shoulder of pork in breadcrumbs, tuna tataki with ponzu oroshi, tsukemono pickled vegetables. Simpler delicious options at lunchtime. You almost feel like you are in an izakaya in Tokyo. A hit.;Terrace;[]
14864;Okuda;France;Paris;7 rue de la Trémoille, Paris, 75008, France;48.866806;2.3023321;61;true;true;Japanese;A sober and elegant decor, 23 seats, hostesses in traditional kimonos and golden silence. It is in this setting that since 2013 diners have been tasting the ‘kaiseki’ creations of the famous Japanese chef Toru Okuda, crowned with Michelin stars back in Tokyo. Harmonious flavours, subtle sauces, delicate textures – this is great art.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14865;Les Coqs;France;Milly-la-Forêt;24 place du Marché, Milly-la-Forêt, 91490, France;48.402218;2.4701356;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, located in an old antique shop in the centre of the village, cannot fail but delight: a contemporary, elegant interior, a patio-terrace ideal in fine weather, and at the helm, a young couple who offer market-inspired dishes like this grilled octopus with black garlic and fregola sarda pasta, or rump of veal with polenta and cardamom.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14867;L'Arazur;France;Antibes;8 rue des Palmiers, Antibes, 06600, France;43.5819212;7.1274607;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;At the helm of this pocket - sized restaurant tucked away in historic Antibes, the owner - chef celebrates the seasons with fresh, colourful and simply prepared dishes. Vegetables are particularly pampered. A delicious moment in store for your taste buds.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14868;Le Julianon;France;Senlis;5 place Gérard-de-Nerval, Senlis, 60300, France;49.2063896;2.5797926;79;false;true;Creative;The contemporary bistro decor of this charming 17C house sets the scene for the chef’s inventive dishes that tactfully play on combinations of texture and flavour, such as cuttlefish, kohlrabi, romaine lettuce and coppa ham, or raspberries, organic polenta from Piedmont and Columbian coffee. The menu changes daily, depending on market availability.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14869;Auberge des Ris;France;Vallon-en-Sully;Lieu-dit Les Ris, Vallon-en-Sully, 03190, France;46.5539415;2.6193686;77;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Here, barrels and a winepress are part of the decor. At the stove, the chef concocts tasty cuisine, bringing together tradition and contemporary dishes, made using select ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14870;Le Musigny;France;Valenciennes;90 avenue de Liège, Valenciennes, 59300, France;50.3636253;3.5359954;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The chef, after stints at some prestigious establishments, opted to set up shop on these discreet premises, with spare, refined decoration, in Valenciennes – and his delicate cooking has quickly won over the city. Choice ingredients, and recipes inspired by the seasons.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14874;Le Morvan;France;Quarré-les-Tombes;6 rue des Écoles, Quarré-les-Tombes, 89630, France;47.3681268;3.9983576;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine;How one imagines Sunday lunch in rural France: traditional, expertly crafted food that keeps pace with the seasons. In summer, relax in the flower-decked garden and soak up the sunshine. Beautifully located at the gate to the Morvan regional park.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14876;Les Clos de Paulilles;France;Port-Vendres;Baie de Paulilles, Port-Vendres, 66660, France;42.5058697;3.1219842;31;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Set between vineyards and the sea, just a few minutes from the beach, the location is idyllic. Maison Cazes – a major wine producer in the region – acquired the 90ha estate and runs this restaurant that promises to treat your taste buds. Only local produce is used in bringing the regional recipes to life: capon with green crab bisque and squid ink tagliatelle. A superb terrace overlooking the vineyards... and a friendly tapas bar!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
14877;Les Archives;France;Poitiers;14 rue Édouard-Grimaux, Poitiers, 86000, France;46.5830346;0.3398048;48;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of historic Poitiers, this 19C Jesuit chapel was for many years home to the region’s archives. Now its columns and arches have been transfigured thanks to a contemporary makeover, resulting in a lavish brasserie boasting a ceiling of cathedral-height proportions and an open-plan kitchen. The modern score by chef Fabien Boinot demonstrates a weakness for vegetables and there is an entirely vegetarian menu. Dishes you may sample include cod in fresh ginger, orange-flavoured carrots and a Thai basil emulsion which illustrates the exotic tinge of the chef’s culinary lineup. The lunchtime menu is a steal – hence the crowds…;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14878;La Racine et la Moelle;France;Figeac;6 rue du Consulat, Figeac, 46100, France;44.6090832;2.0345371;82;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Julie and her Irish partner have already won the hearts of Figeac with their flavoursome, modern recipes. Simple, unprissy dishes and flawless execution, the food is served in a friendly, welcoming setting that is as natural as the fine wine list (the establishment also sells wine). Bingo!;Terrace;[]
14882;Les Hospitaliers;France;Le Poët-Laval;Vieux village, Le Poët-Laval, 26160, France;44.5368827;5.0149133;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of a stunning village of Drôme provençale at the foot of the Commandery of the Order of Malta, these hospitallers provide a gourmet interlude, together with stylish accommodation should you wish to stay longer. The immense rooftop terrace of this ancient edifice affords 360° views.;Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14883;Maynats;France;Pau;24 avenue Gaston-Lacoste, Pau, 64000, France;43.2923046;-0.3687262;64;false;false;Creative;In their new premises, the Maynats (meaning "boys" or "kids" in the Béarn dialect) continue to win us over with their instinctive and playful cuisine – their surf and turf combinations are particularly on point. The vibe is cool and friendly in the octagonal glass-paned dining room. Thanks to the mixture of ambitious food and relaxed service, it has earned a place in the hearts of the locals. Surprise menu with several courses in the evening. The wine list specialises in organic labels.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14885;L'Envol;France;Cavaillon;35 rue Gustave-Flaubert, Cavaillon, 84300, France;43.8371102;5.0394748;77;true;false;Farm to table;In a small street in the city centre, this restaurant is as charming as it is discreet. At the stove, Laurent Renoult fetes produce such as vegetables from Vert'Tige, in Cabannes, Sisteron lamb or the pigeon of Costières. It's full-flavoured, tasty, and Sarah Hotten's welcome is fuss-free and charming. Don't hesitate to try this place out!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14886;Baie;France;Saint-Valery-sur-Somme;30 rue de la Ferté, Saint-Valery-sur-Somme, 80230, France;50.1853852;1.6425015;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This tiny restaurant, which has only two tables for guests, proposes a short menu and sources its produce from suppliers who lie within a strict 100km radius. The natural ingredients are prepared without gimmicks, as in the monkfish roasted on the bone. Add to that the friendly welcome and you have one of the best places to eat in town. Given all that, you should really book!;;[]
14887;Le Pincemin;France;Versailles;10 boulevard du Roi, Versailles, 78000, France;48.8106063;2.1264131;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A bona fide star of social media who rubs shoulders with rappers and celebrities, Xavier Pincemin (the runaway winner of Top Chef 2016) almost overshadows the Sun King here in his Versailles restaurant. He brings together all generations and nationalities – if you are lucky enough to get a table. His up-to-the-minute cuisine showcases the finest produce without bells and whistles and demonstrates his sense of ambition as well as his undiminished passion for high-end gastronomy, as exemplified by his dish of hake, verbena, peach and courgettes.;;[]
14888;8 Clos;France;Beaune;8 rue d'Alsace, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0225606;4.8391957;45;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In a long, narrow interior, where black leatherette benches meet exposed stone, Stéphane Léger, former Michelin-starred chef, regales us with his Burgundian cuisine and traditional dishes with a Mediterranean edge. Poached eggs in red wine sauce, braised ox cheek, ham and parsley terrine, snails, but also roast langoustine tails, baby potatoes and girolles mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14890;Le Chicoula, bistrot d'Art;France;Bordeaux;22 rue de Cursol, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8348402;-0.5768595;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This tiny bistro opened without fanfare, yet there is plenty to write home about. The chef is a dab hand, as demonstrated by the single set menu that changes every month with its original flavours and harmonious presentations. The decoration is just as noteworthy, including work by local artists. Opening nights are occasionally held – the chef himself paints in his spare time…;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14891;La Maison Rouge;France;Colmar;9 rue des Écoles, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0747604;7.3589771;39;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Chef Jean Kuentz (dubbed Petit Jean), who learned the ropes in top Parisian establishments, runs this iconic establishment in Colmar's historic centre, a stone's throw from the Petite Venise quarter. In an 11C edifice, he crafts gourmet fare, navigating between regional and more modern dishes, accompanied by well-chosen wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14894;Song, Saveurs & Sens;France;Nantes;5 rue Santeuil, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2132855;-1.5603502;74;true;false;Asian Contemporary;Self-taught chef Nhung Phung was born in Vietnam, but grew up in Laos, Cambodia and Thailand. The aromas and perfumes of her childhood have forged her culinary identity: sensitive, intelligent, balanced cuisine, poised between Southeast Asia and France, delicately spicy and crafted with premium produce. The interior sports a striking blend of turquoise, black and wrought iron – a fine setting for a sensibly priced meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14895;Brioude;France;Neyrac-les-Bains;7 rue Mazade, Neyrac-les-Bains, 07380, France;44.6728297;4.2543667;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This endearing family inn has been serving well-crafted food, in which local producers take pride of place, since 1887! The elegant dining room which overlooks the countryside of southern Ardèche provides the perfect foil to sample Claude Brioude’s “Discovery” menu: a new spin on the omelette with Ardèche watercress, gravlax of trout and leeks, trilogy of lamb with a veggie pie…;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14896;Mathieu Kergourlay - Château de Boisgelin;France;Pléhédel;Domaine de Boisgelin, Pléhédel, 22290, France;48.6807486;-3.0242695;21;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Mathieu Kergourlay welcomes diners to this 450-hectare property and small castle, tastefully restored and decorated by his companion and himself. The tasty, generous and consummately crafted food is full of surprises, such as the mini pissaladière reworked by the chef, which is served with a marinated fillet of mackerel, perfectly grilled over the BBQ.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14897;Gram's;France;Toulouse;64 rue de la Colombette, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6047759;1.4547091;56;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Bang in the centre of Saint Aubin, chef Laura Pelou adds a new twist to country recipes from Aveyron and her grandmothers’ cooking – hence the name! The spruce dining room, depicted by elegant oak parquet floors and lots of room between tables, believes in serving wholesome, simple fare such as leeks in vinaigrette, sprinkled with hard-boiled egg and croutons or a hummus of lentils, risotto of spelt and mushrooms – there is often a vegetarian starter and main course. Regularly renewed menu.;;[]
14898;L'Auberge du Château;France;Muret-le-Château;Le Bourg, Muret-le-Château, 12330, France;44.494186;2.574457;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant opposite the town hall in an Aveyron village is well known to food lovers, who come here to enjoy contemporary cuisine which places the onus on herbs and vegetables. The dishes are colourful and flavoursome. Lovely flower - filled terrace.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14900;Clovis;France;Tourrettes-sur-Loup;21 Grande-Rue, Tourrettes-sur-Loup, 06140, France;43.7154;7.05873;15;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this bistro in the heart of a medieval village, kick off your meal with a drink and nibbles, before sampling the chef’s unusual concept which involves several variations (starter & main course), all of which are based on one main ingredient (vegetable, meat or fish). Warm welcome and small private room.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14901;Le Relais d'Ozenay;France;Ozenay;1244 route de Brancion (Le Bourg), Ozenay, 71700, France;46.54288;4.84691;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the picturesque medieval village of Ozenay, you cannot miss this colourful fronted inn. The contemporary interior provides the perfect foil to well-crafted cuisine by a chef who boasts a fine CV. His plating is particularly precise and flowery. Examples include velvety green peas, poached egg and an emulsion of smoked bacon. Fine view of the castle from one of the venue’s two terraces.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14903;Transparence - La Table de Patrick Fréchin;France;Nancy;28 rue Stanislas, Nancy, 54000, France;48.6930712;6.1814478;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A short walk from Place Stanislas in a busy pedestrian street, transparency is more than just a name and you can actually see chef Patrick Fréchin working his magic in the theatrically visible kitchen. His enticing dishes showcase premium seasonal ingredients, such as loin of skrei cod, roasted in bay leaf oil with mead-flavoured yoghurt.;Terrace;[]
14904;La Table du Relais du Bois Saint-Georges;France;Saintes;132 cours Genet, Saintes, 17100, France;45.7505133;-0.6623787;42;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Fall under the spell of this restaurant housed in an old farmhouse, where the chef has a penchant for beautiful seasonal ingredients (sourced from local producers or the aromatic plant garden located in the grounds). Drink in the view of the terrace, fountain and small lake through the bay windows, as you savour calf sweetbread, spatchcock, elderberry – the soft juicy meat makes for a taste sensation!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14905;Les Jardins de Kerstéphanie;France;Sarzeau;Route du Roaliguen, Sarzeau, 56370, France;47.5157478;-2.7736134;41;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This old stone farmstead smothered in Virginia creeper and set in wooded grounds is home to the new headquarters of Emmanuel Kouri, previously encountered at Les Climats (Paris). Mindful of the provenance of his produce (line-caught fish, organic market gardeners, local dairy produce), he conjures up seafood dishes, like little tunny in kari-gosse, marinated cucumber and iced coriander soup or ikejime pollock, violin courgette in basil and a pistachio and lime sabayon. To be enjoyed on the shaded terrace in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14906;La Cigale Égarée;France;Quimperlé;8 rue d'Athenry - ZA Villeneuve-Braouic, Quimperlé, 29300, France;47.8644382;-3.530296;17;false;true;Farm to table;This cricket has taken up abode in Brittany, in a quirky antique shop-style décor, flanked by a lush green patio. The menu is depicted by seasonal market produce, fish of the day and garden veggies, grown by the inspired chef. Flavoursome, no-frills recipes (roast hake, spring vegetables and gravy), cooked to perfection.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14909;L'Esberit;France;Bizanos;34 boulevard du Commandant-René-Mouchotte, Bizanos, 64320, France;43.3022862;-0.3186803;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This handsome 19C listed stone house, located by a road and just a few minutes from downtown Pau, deploys all its charms to the rear of the property thanks to the peaceful garden patio, shaded by a hundred-year-old oak tree. Inside, the stylish dining room sports herringbone parquet flooring and high ceilings. Chef Nicolas Lormeau has been thriving in this plush setting for some years now. His inventive recipes are a treasure trove of plays on texture and harmonious or surprising flavours (such as the multiple textures of marinated scallops with passion fruit and sweetcorn or the semolina milk with truffles from Lot, kiwi and yuzu-flavoured white chocolate ice cream). Béarn produce takes the limelight in creative, skilfully plated dishes, served professionally and seamlessly. Book (well) in advance!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14910;L'Entre Pots;France;Pézenas;8 avenue Louis-Montagne, Pézenas, 34120, France;43.4591107;3.4266728;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This former warehouse is now dedicated to the pleasures of the palate. The cuisine combines regional flavours with creative touches, and the wine list features a good selection of local wines. Small delicatessen.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14911;La Passerelle;France;Perpignan;1 cours François-Palmarole, Perpignan, 66000, France;42.7022361;2.8945473;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The chef now at the helm of this maritime-inspired restaurant, where she once trained with her father, is giving us her own modern take on family tradition. She likes to add good concentrated jus to her dishes (octopus with pork jus) as well as sweet-and-sour flavours (langoustine, turnip, almonds). She is also a sommelier, and puts her heart and soul into coming up with optimal food and wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14913;Le Pré du Moulin;France;Sérignan-du-Comtat;29 cours Joël-Estève, Sérignan-du-Comtat, 84830, France;44.1899314;4.8464208;60;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Originally a mill, then a primary school, this stone-built village house draws you in with its lovely bucolic atmosphere... and traditional Provençal-inspired cuisine. The terrace, shaded by old plane trees, exudes the essence of Provence.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14914;Nancy Bourguignon;France;Paradou;Lieu-dit de Bourgeac, 1 chemin de l'Ancienne-Voie-Ferrée, Paradou, 13520, France;43.7243182;4.7954347;82;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;What a pleasure it is to take a seat in this establishment where you are welcomed naturally and simply by a Burgundian family. In this charming restaurant, the chef concocts subtle and delicate dishes, sprinkled with Provençal innuendo. The patio, next to the swimming pool and surrounded by Mediterranean vegetation, invites you to slow down and take things easy. An oasis of peace and charm.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14916;Flocon;France;Paris;75 rue Mouffetard, Paris, 75005, France;48.842049;2.3498081;59;true;false;Farm to table;In a lively neighbourhood, this is the first business venture of the Flocon brothers, Alexis and Josselin: one is dedicated to the running of the establishment and the other to the cooking. In a bright interior, tuck into surprising, well-thought-out dishes made from carefully sourced products. On top of that, they keep the prices low, wine included.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
14917;Ô Gayot;France;Bagnoles-de-l'Orne;2 avenue de la Ferté-Macé, Bagnoles-de-l'Orne, 61140, France;48.5571756;-0.4129207;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This chic bistro in a pretty stone house certainly has its finger on the pulse. On the menu find good bistro recipes that change on a weekly basis. These include, soft - boiled egg with cream of mushroom soup and Calvados baba. A taste sensation!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14918;La Ferme du Chozal;France;Hauteluce;361 route des Combes, Hauteluce, 73620, France;45.7554173;6.5800253;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant may sport a characteristic rustic Alpine vibe, but the appetising cuisine is no less modern. It is made with fine local ingredients illustrated by Leman fera in grilled leeks and a herby butter or a haunch of tender veal, poivrade artichokes and gnocchis. And let's not forget the remarkable list of Alpine wines.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14919;Empreinte;France;Vannes;15 place Valencia, Vannes, 56000, France;47.6568734;-2.7574306;68;true;false;Farm to table;Make a stop at this establishment on a small square in the city centre. The interior is inviting, with its warm decor of untreated wooden floorboards, fabrics and vintage porcelain. Marine and Baptiste Fournier put their hearts into serving particularly polished cuisine, showcasing fish sourced from the market and vegetables from farmers. Menu-carte at lunch, "surprise" menus at dinner. Natural wines.;;[]
14920;SouKa;France;Aniane;36 boulevard Saint-Jean, Aniane, 34150, France;43.6854998;3.5857173;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;In this tiny village in the heart of the Terrasses du Larzac vineyards, SouKa (root in Occitan) focuses on market ingredients and local producers. The playful chef enjoys conjuring up surprises, such as the mystery lunch and evening menu, whose ingredients you’re asked to guess! The fine local tipples can be purchased from the wine shop on the premises.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14921;Chapeau de Paille - Bistrot Provençal;France;Saint-Rémy-de-Provence;29 boulevard Mirabeau, Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, 13210, France;43.7895304;4.8334558;64;false;false;Provençal;Bourvil and Piaf play in the background, while straw hats adorn the walls in this cheerful flea market vibe! This rustic, Provençal bistro, located on the town’s ring road, concocts a seasonal menu with an emphasis on market-fresh ingredients: pork terrine, anchovy purée, aïoli, Alpilles lamb, quail flambéed in pastis at your table, baba à la provençal…;Terrace;[]
14922;Le Bastion;France;Lagrasse;50 boulevard de la Promenade, Lagrasse, 11220, France;43.0891229;2.6196977;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Take a seat in one of two pretty rustic dining spaces to sample "avant-garde country fare", inspired by Auguste Escoffier but with a modern twist. Great produce from the region is used – tomatoes from the Estarac Gardens, vinegar by Cyril Codigna, fish fresh from the market at Port la Nouvelle… Concise tapas menu and spacious terrace.;Terrace;[]
14923;Le 428;France;Savigny-lès-Beaune;54 rue de Bourgogne, Savigny-lès-Beaune, 21420, France;47.0654162;4.8125419;31;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The term ouvrée refers to the area of vineyard - 428m² - that could be dug by a winegrower in one day. Chef Christophe Ledru welcomes diners in a sleek, contemporary interior and serves up modern, well-prepared cuisine ("surprise" menus only), accompanied by a good selection of wines from the village (and beyond).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14924;Restaurant Bohrer;France;Rouffach;Rue Raymond-Poincaré, Rouffach, 68250, France;47.9615733;7.2978898;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;This handsome regional abode is steeped in bourgeois, countrified elegance. It is ideal to sample gourmet cuisine accompanied by fine, mainly local, vintages. The chef takes pleasure in surprising us with goose fillet tataki and pistachio-teriyaki sauce, or a lobster bao with passion fruit and parmesan. Alternatively, the lively, friendly Brasserie Chez Julien is housed in a former cinema.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14925;Restaurant de l'Écluse 16;France;Altwiller;Lieu-dit Bonnefontaine, Altwiller, 67260, France;48.90302;7.0054294;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant standing beside the Canal de la Sarre towpath was once a coaching inn, along which horses used to tow coal from the mines. The chef, from Morbihan in Brittany, cooks up delicious and meticulous cuisine, such as saffron risotto with chorizo served alongside premium quality poultry with wild prawns, or his truly unforgettable take on tarte Tatin. He occasionally uses ingredients from the local terroir, enhanced with condiments or home-made aromatic oils.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
14926;L'Écrin;France;Ajaccio;16 cours du Général-Leclerc, Ajaccio, 20000, France;41.9171964;8.7273927;80;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This endearing restaurant, slightly off the historic town’s crowded tourist track, offers fresh, seasonal, expertly crafted Mediterranean cuisine, such as brandade of forkbeard fish, bottarga and a peppery piquillo cream. The dinky terrace is invariably taken by storm in summertime. Infectiously cosy welcome. A genuine bijou of an eatery.;Terrace;[]
14927;Le Grand Réfectoire;France;Lyon;3 cour Saint-Henri, Grand Hôtel-Dieu, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7580619;4.8359156;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the grandiose Hôtel Dieu, beneath the hundred-year-old vaults of the nuns’ former refectory, the menu of this huge brasserie is signed by Marcel Ravin (2*-chef of Monaco’s Blue Bay). The modern food is sprinkled with exotic West Indian influences. The swish rooftop bar (L’Officine) draws city slickers like bees to honey, as does the exquisite patio in the inner courtyard.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14928;L'Abélia;France;Nantes;125 boulevard des Poilus, Nantes, 44300, France;47.2331697;-1.5332064;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Vincent Berthomeau and his spouse Pascale have set up shop in an edifice dating from 1900 that is slightly outside the city centre of Nantes. Their handsome mansion is further enhanced by a conservatory, a terrace and a garden. The regulars return for the chef’s generous seasonal score and his menus vary depending on what he finds on his frequent forays to Talensac market. Enticing dishes such as a cassolette of langoustines and pleurote mushrooms in a flavoursome seafood stock or an exquisite chocolate, butterscotch and caramelised peanut tartlet, further jazzed up by a carrot sorbet and carrot coulis.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14929;Comptoir du Marché;France;Nice;8 rue du Marché, Nice, 06300, France;43.697469;7.2749116;41;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of bustling historic Nice, casual and friendly are the watchwords of this vintage-inspired market counter, whose name is equal to the chef’s colourful, flavoursome dishes. Concise menu, unfailingly fresh and reasonable rates: it is always a pleasure to spend time here.;Terrace;[]
14930;L'A Cheda;France;Bonifacio;Route de Cavallo-Morto, Bonifacio, 20169, France;41.4062638;9.1699026;81;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Take a seat on the terrace overlooking the pool in a setting, steeped in romanticism. The chef has a preference for local ingredients and rigorously selects his suppliers. You will enjoy wild fish, organic Corsican meat and vegetables fresh from the permaculture garden. Attentive service and a wine list rich in pleasant surprises.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
14931;Relais du Teulet;France;Goulles;Lieu-dit Le Teulet, Goulles, 19430, France;44.9968629;2.1365735;67;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Contemporary;This former coaching inn, run by the same family for five generations, is a pleasant surprise! The chef devises simple and accessible contemporary cuisine, based on a short menu that highlights the region's great produce – Corrèze meats, Aurillac fruit and vegetables.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
14934;Le François II;France;Couëron;5 place Aristide-Briand, Couëron, 44220, France;47.21085;-1.7278;96;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;For the last ten years, Breton chef Jérôme Evain has been paying tribute to his region as he crafts primarily local produce of flawless quality. An endearing venue, a tempting score and a bargain-priced lunchtime menu, illustrated by 65°C free-range egg, green lentils, emulsion of Ossau Iraty cheese, melt-in-the-mouth cod cooked at a low temperature and an iconic gâteau nantais with banana confit and butterscotch to finish. The professional, friendly front-of-house service is courtesy of Solenn.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14936;Bonnotte;France;Boulogne-Billancourt;1 rue de Billancourt, Boulogne-Billancourt, 92100, France;48.8446306;2.2345513;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A 10-minute walk from the Albert Kahn Museum, the restaurant of Antoine Guichard (David Bizet's former sous-chef) and Manon Negretti pays homage to the Île de Noirmoutier, the island where the bonnotte potato is cultivated. In a low-key contemporary bistro setting, the dishes, concocted with fresh produce, are in step with the latest in bistronomy cuisine. Set menu at lunchtime and à la carte menu in the evening.;;[]
14937;Ar Maen Hir;France;Locronan;15 bis rue du Prieuré, Locronan, 29180, France;48.0977773;-4.2114968;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;For his first restaurant, youthful Thibaud Érard chose the picturesque, medieval village of Locronan, near Quimper, where he is clearly flourishing. His traditional, wholesome cuisine quietly feeds you well. Pleasant, casual service.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14939;Le Capu;France;Nancy;31 rue Gambetta, Nancy, 54000, France;48.6921069;6.1803695;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In an ideal location 300m from Place Stanislas, this restaurant boasts an elegant decor in a bold, contemporary vein, enhanced by baroque notes (rich hues and crushed velvet). The cuisine is suitably generous – for example, filet mignon of veal, with aubergine caviar, grilled courgettes and a tarragon sauce.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14940;Ourea;France;Marseille;72 rue de la Paix-Marcel-Paul, Marseille, 13006, France;43.2906647;5.3734441;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Provençal;Matthieu Roche moved from Paris (where he worked at Semilla) to open this tiny bistro with his partner Camille. The space, located between the port and the courthouse, reflects the colours and flavours of Provence. The chef is attentive to the seasons, buying locally (Mediterranean fish directly from the port, vegetables from Mallemort's market gardens, citrus fruits from the Domaine du Jasson).;Air conditioning;[]
14941;Chabrol;France;Nice;12 rue Bavastro, Nice, 06300, France;43.699549;7.2852132;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;“Faire Chabrol” is an ancient custom in rural southern France, which consists in adding a little wine to the dregs of soup to further dilute the stock, before gulping it down. In the restaurant of the same name, two childhood buddies seek to enhance simple (but high-quality) ingredients, thanks to modern recipes, strewn with a sprinkling of intelligent inventiveness – to the delight of diners.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14942;Terminal #1;France;Montpellier;1408 avenue de la Mer, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.5928;3.90737;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The Pourcel brothers have upcycled this former wine storehouse into a vast space where stone, steel and wood are blended in a smart neo-industrial vein. The dishes, which draw on locally sourced ingredients at their height of their maturity, are infused with inspirations from far and wide. As you peruse the menu ranging from super-fresh seabream, red mullet and seabass to fried potato cakes, rockfish soup or roast squid with tempura of squid head, houmous cream and lemon confit dressing, you will get an excellent foretaste of the “gastronomic bistro” spirit of this terminal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14946;La Table du Château;France;Montreuil;4 chaussée des Capucins, Montreuil, 62170, France;50.4659476;1.7613212;50;true;true;Creative;In the hushed, elegant decor of this Montreuil-sur-Mer institution, a young chef from Lille serves creative, eco-responsible cuisine (fermentation, decoction). He puts the emphasis firmly on plants and vegetables and showcases small-scale local producers. The yellow pollack, courgette from the market gardener, fish roe and elderflowers is a surprising, hearty dish with wonderful marriages of flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14947;Jérôme Brochot;France;Montceau-les-Mines;7 place Beaubernard, Montceau-les-Mines, 71300, France;46.6693188;4.3652537;51;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Jérôme Brochot concocts a set menu made with market-fresh produce that changes on a weekly basis and comprises several courses. He works with excellent produce: green asparagus, lobster, turbot etc. They offer a cookery class on Sunday mornings.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14948;Émile Job;France;Montmerle-sur-Saône;12 rue du Pont, Montmerle-sur-Saône, 01090, France;46.0810449;4.7560759;79;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This restaurant extends a cordial invitation to sample the popular classics that showcase the terroir: Bresse poultry, frogs' legs in parsley sauce, lake fish, cherries jubilee and vanilla ice cream. The chef sticks to tradition, much to the delight of his guests. Dine on the lovely terrace, in the shade of the hundred-year-old lime trees and overlooking the river.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14949;Anecdote;France;Montreuil;1 rue des Juifs, Montreuil, 62170, France;50.4646639;1.7635884;15;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the words of Anecdote's owner Alexandre Gauthier, who is also chef at La Grenouillère, Samuel Pesquet creates a "cuisine of memory" – in it, he pays homage to the dishes his father used to make in the 1980s. This is generous and mouth-watering cuisine made from fine ingredients – goujonnettes with gribiche sauce, braised rib steak, crêpes Suzette or tarte Tatin – that you won't be forgetting any time soon.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14950;Le Petit Jardin;France;Montpellier;20 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.61223;3.8732502;19;true;false;Modern Cuisine;As its name ("The Little Garden") suggests, this traditional fine dining restaurant has one of the prettiest terraces in the city, nestled in a lush, quiet garden. There is a subdued and bucolic atmosphere in the dining area with its large glass-paned façade, where the beautifully presented seasonal dishes are served. Those with a sweet tooth won't be disappointed by the delicious desserts, such as the remarkable trompe l'œil lemon, fleur de sel sablé biscuit and lemon sorbet. There is also a bistro serving international cuisine.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
14951;Le Lucullus;France;Montmorillon;4 boulevard de Strasbourg, Montmorillon, 86500, France;46.4236623;0.8699088;81;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a modern interior, this restaurant puts local ingredients centre stage. On sunny days, on the peaceful patio, you will make the connection between the name of this place and its namesake, the Roman general Lucullus, renowned for his lavish dining table. The flavoursome dishes, such as Anjou quail roasted whole, with confit legs, burnt corn purée and royal sauce, are beautifully presented.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14953;La Baratte;France;Tourcoing;395 rue du Clinquet, Tourcoing, 59200, France;50.7256987;3.1298385;66;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A small brick house in a residential neighbourhood has been home to this family-run eatery for four generations. The stylish, contemporary dining room opens onto a pretty garden and teak decked terrace. The chef impressively crafts enticing dishes, such as sautéed snails in a light frothy garlic and parsley emulsion and a bacon-flavoured cake. The after-dinner marshmallow treats are almost too pretty to eat!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14954;Annette;France;La Rochelle;14 rue Bletterie, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1591752;-1.1508748;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This pair – she is from Ile de Ré, he hails from Bristol – met in a restaurant in Amsterdam and went on to open this modern bistro in La Rochelle. The space comprises pale wood tables and furniture, a glassed-in kitchen at the back, a zellige-tiled wall and a small terrace overlooking a pedestrian street. They propose French cuisine that is packed with freshness and flavour! The chef shows he has technique and talent, eg with his wild sea bass, white wine sauce, cockles, broccoli purée and lightly grilled green cabbage. As for dessert, Audrey delights diners with her "gâteau au chocolat d'Annette" (her grandmother's recipe), served with chestnut cream ice cream – potent and delicious.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14955;Le Relais Plaza;France;Paris;25 avenue Montaigne, Paris, 75008, France;48.8660855;2.3039834;54;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Ensconced within the Hotel Plaza Athénée, it is impossible to resist the charm of the lovely 1930s decor inspired by the liner SS Normandie. A unique atmosphere in which to sample cuisine with a pronounced sense of tradition, ranging from the "granny's cooking" dear to Jean Imbert (sea bream gratin, stuffed tomato and pilaf rice) to the classics that have sealed the reputation of this famous Art Deco spot.;Air conditioning;[]
14956;Aux Trois Rois;France;Moosch;35 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Moosch, 68690, France;47.8596215;7.0496555;45;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The bistro classics reign supreme (meat pie, calf's head) but there is still room for seafood dishes. The slate board features constantly changing dishes and the wines are real finds. A restaurant where taste, quality and conviviality are the order of the day!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14957;Le Jarrousset;France;Murat;RN 122, Murat, 15300, France;45.1158485;2.9151985;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a lush green setting, this recently restored inn is a champion of local produce, illustrated by the chef’s painstakingly selected network of nearby farms and producers. Meals are served in a pared-down, modern interior, whose furniture and tableware is the work of local artisans. Let yourself be guided by the expert tips of the knowledgeable sommelière.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14958;Le Petit Banc;France;Noirmoutier-en-l'Île;7 rue des Douves, Noirmoutier-en-l'Île, 85330, France;47.00021;-2.24281;53;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Originally from the Lyon area, Véronique and Gilles have been at the helm of this pretty regional building at the foot of the Château de Noirmoutier for some 10 years. The quaintly quirky interior sports red Skai banquettes, bistro furniture, mirrors and old wooden floorboards. The menu stars charcuterie from Lyon and Vendée delicacies in a reasonably priced set menu that changes frequently. The vibe is suitably buzzy and casual and reminiscent of a “bouchon lyonnais” that has been uprooted to the island of Noirmoutier, much to our delight!;Wheelchair access;[]
14959;Maison Castet;France;Martres-Tolosane;44 avenue de la Gare, Martres-Tolosane, 31220, France;43.1967078;1.0162721;28;true;false;Creative;This contemporary eatery at a remove from the town centre used to be the station café. The chef here employs premium ingredients and his considerable technical skill to conjure up his creative cuisine, transporting diners to Brazil, for example, with a wild pollack moqueca, herb salad and farofa. His impressive desserts, such as beef heart tomato in puffed sugar and sage cream, deserve a special mention. Terrific wine list.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14961;Au Fil des Saisons;France;Luçon;55 route de la Roche-sur-Yon, Luçon, 85400, France;46.475255;-1.177178;67;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This engaging roadside inn provides an opportunity to sample stripped-back, seasonal fare that relies on fresh ingredients of traditional and regional inspiration (duck foie gras with juniper berries, breast of roast guinea fowl in herbs, etc.). A small cottage garden supplies the kitchen with some veggies and herbs. Take a seat in the conservatory or in the garden, depending on the season.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14962;L'Endroit;France;Honfleur;3 rue Charles-et-Paul-Bréard, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.4182337;0.2332445;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Not the kind of place you would expect to find here! Innovative loft - style interior and kitchens that open right onto the dining area. Hamburger with foie gras, rognons revisités (kidneys), superb desserts. This is the place to be.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
14963;Le Vallon de Chérisy;France;Cherisy;12 route de Paris, Cherisy, 28500, France;48.746774;1.4162886;46;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The name is a passing nod to an ode composed by Victor Hugo in this very inn back in 1821. The food has remained voluntarily rustic and hearty and faithfully keeps pace with the seasons, in particular the veggies and aromatic herbs. Save room for the wickedly decadent house dessert: a hot vanilla and butterscotch soufflé – to die for!;Car park,Terrace;[]
14964;Le Petit Mézériat;France;Mézériat;250 Grande-Rue, Mézériat, 01660, France;46.2349562;5.047839;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a small village near Vonnas, the owner chef serves a bargain priced lunchtime menu and a surprise menu (in several stages) which varies according to the season and market availability, with a distinct fondness for locally sourced ingredients. All of which is served by cheerful Amandine, the chef’s spouse, in their spruce, tastefully appointed venue.;Wheelchair access;[]
14965;Le Clos Perché;France;Montarcher;Le Bourg, Montarcher, 42380, France;45.4592074;3.9963032;20;true;false;Creative;Once upon a time, there was an inn on the high plateaux of the Monts du Forez, set at an altitude of 1 150m. It is here, on the edge of this tiny village, that Julien Magne has set up shop. In the kitchen, this chef creates colourful, inventive cuisine with a playful approach that brings a smile to your face!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14966;Le Jardin de Bellevue;France;Metz;58 rue Claude-Bernard, Metz, 57070, France;49.1121218;6.216453;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The comfortable and elegant setting of this century-old building has been rejuvenated by the recent arrival of Élise and Paul Fabuel. He is the young chef who appeared on French TV's Objectif Top Chef, as well as completing stints at À Table in Metz and À l'Échevin in Colmar. Here, he serves up an attractive seasonal menu, eg a medley of pumpkin, roast chestnuts, Iberian ham and porcini, or turbot a la plancha, radishes, courgettes with mint and sauce vierge.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
14967;La Place de Mougins;France;Mougins;41 place du Commandant-Lamy, Mougins, 06250, France;43.600391;6.9944637;82;false;false;Creative;On the village square as the name suggests! Chic and pleasing are adjectives equally applicable to this charming restaurant and its cuisine, thanks to a passionate and creative chef. Month by month he gives pride of place to a succession of seasonal ingredients... celebrating the truffle, the asparagus and so on.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14968;Amour Blanc;France;Blois;Hôtel Fleur de Loire, 24 quai Villebois-Mareuil, Blois, 41000, France;47.582948;1.3375171;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Christophe Hay's second restaurant is named after a species of carp. It is located on the first floor of a modern extension slightly set back from the original building. This inviting wood-panelled and light-filled interior, with its large bay windows looking out over the Loire, immediately works its magic. The chef of Fleur de Loire gives free rein to his passion for Loire ingredients (local cheeses, géline de Touraine heirloom poultry, fried small fish and mullet from the River Loire, lamb and caviar from the Sologne), but also Wagyu beef from his own farm. In short, fine ingredients treated with care to create dishes that tend towards the classical.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
14969;Au Cheval Blanc;France;Hochstatt;55 Grande-Rue, Hochstatt, 68720, France;47.7037608;7.2763053;40;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this small village on the doorstep of the Sundgau, you can taste carefully-prepared, flavoursome dishes, devised by a chef who draws his inspiration from market produce – green asparagus with poached egg and Gascon bacon, gently-cooked veal fillet, etc. An appetising establishment.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14970;Le Cammissar;France;Ribeauvillé;81 Grand'Rue, Ribeauvillé, 68150, France;48.1958252;7.3174499;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This youthful chef isn’t lacking in ambition. In this half-timbered red-painted 15C edifice, restored at great cost, he produces modern dishes using painstakingly selected produce – pearlescent wild turbot with baby artichokes à la barigoule, or Breton lobster tail, with white asparagus and morels.;Terrace;[]
14971;La Colline du Colombier;France;Iguerande;Lieu-dit le Colombier, Iguerande, 71340, France;46.1888494;4.067558;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Deep in the countryside, overlooking the Loire, this restored farmhouse has a style that is rustic but also chic and minimalist! It allies nature and design and serves refined dishes made from local ingredients, combined with modern touches.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14972;Boat aux Saveurs;France;Marmande;36-38 avenue Jean-Jaurès, Marmande, 47200, France;44.503338;0.154712;31;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary villa set away from the bustle of the town centre is run by a mother and daughter team. Foodies adore the lovingly prepared dishes fully in tune with the times. The chef makes a point of honour of sourcing ingredients from local producers and most of the veggies come from their own vegetable garden.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14973;Huître Brûlée;France;Honfleur;8 rue Brûlée, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.420648;0.2322818;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Don’t worry, the oysters aren’t burnt - despite the establishment’s name! Updated recipes, quality ingredients, locally sourced whenever possible (organic veggies, fish from small boats), concise, seasonal menu. This friendly bolthole is run by an enthusiastic couple: local lad Paul Lacheray, in the kitchen and his partner, Chloé Woestelandt, who runs the dining room with considerable brio…;;[]
14975;Maison Cluny;France;Paris;3 rue de Cluny, Paris, 75005, France;48.8506914;2.344945;64;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Much to our delight, the gourmet duet, formerly of the Cornichon in the Daguerre district, has teamed up again in this stylish bistro opposite the Cluny Museum garden in the heart of the Latin Quarter. The slate menu reads like an old-school cookbook: chicken liver pâté, veal kidneys, game in season, rice pudding… Warm interior and casual, upbeat vibe.;;[]
14976;Racine;France;Lectoure;6 rue Fontélie, Lectoure, 32700, France;43.9337585;0.6230352;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;She is Canadian and he’s Belgian and they have set up shop in Lectoure in a narrow street near the cathedral. They regale diners with healthy, unpretentious food in the zeitgeist that shines the spotlight on regional producers and on aromatic herbs, fermented seasonings and citrus fruits, all of which washed down with a fine lineup of natural wines. Meals are served in a workshop-inspired interior, whose high ceiling, timber rafters and old stone walls are cleverly paired with stylish modern furnishings. Now add eater friendly prices and you will understand that a meal in this establishment often requires forward planning.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
14977;Le Binôme;France;Annecy;32A avenue des Carrés - à Annecy-le-Vieux, Annecy, 74940, France;45.9132353;6.1432351;55;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Mathilde and Remi work together like clockwork. He is in charge of savoury dishes, she crafts the desserts and together they cheerfully wait at table. Market-fresh, throbbingly simple, deftly executed cuisine, illustrated by melt-in-the-mouth chuck beef stew with fluffy mashed potatoes. A few seats at the bar offer an insight into the chefs’ handiwork.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14978;Symbiose;France;Bordeaux;4 quai des Chartrons, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8491003;-0.5706489;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Run by four young partners, Symbiose makes it all look easy: the bold and efficiently prepared dishes, the friendly, relaxed service, the mostly young, if not trendy, clientele. Then there is the little bistro - style dining area – and unbeatable value for money at lunchtime. Highly recommended.;Terrace;[]
14979;Sébastopol;France;Lille;1 place Sébastopol, Lille, 59000, France;50.6289783;3.0589891;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This engaging small eatery, something of a landmark in Lille, is the haunt of a chef who concocts a regularly renewed, concise menu strewn with personal touches and a fondness for surf and turf combinations (scallops from Boulogne, roast artichokes, puree of Camus artichokes and Noir de Bigorre pork belly). Fine wine list and attentive yet unstarched service.;Air conditioning;[]
14981;Le Saint-Martial;France;Saint-Martial-de-Nabirat;Le Bourg, Saint-Martial-de-Nabirat, 24250, France;44.74468;1.25899;61;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Valérie and Jean-Marc Réal have been at the helm of this delightful restaurant in a peaceful Black Périgord village for over twenty years. The chef enhances seasonal produce, cleverly blending tradition and modernity, in particular courtesy of punchy gravies and carefully balanced combinations of ingredients. Examples include sautéed snails and calf’s head wrapped in green leaves, garnished with a watercress-flavoured crème of cep mushrooms. A warm welcome and an extensive wine cellar add the final flourish to a slap-up meal.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14982;Maison Soubeiran;France;Lunel;129 cours Gabriel-Péri, Lunel, 34400, France;43.6749283;4.1326815;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;We fell in love with this family-run establishment whose chef whips up spontaneous regional fare made with fresh, seasonal ingredients from local organic market gardeners. Scents and flavours from the garrigue, Camargue and Mediterranean, jazzed up with spicy notes and flanked by homemade sourdough bread made with heritage wheat. Authentic warm welcome and an exquisite patio shaded by a natural trellis.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14983;À Table ! Chez Éric Léautey;France;Thoiry;28 rue Porte-Saint-Martin, Thoiry, 78770, France;48.86573;1.7889999;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Being at Chez Eric Léautey is a pleasure. The small porch prepares you for the tasting to come, and your taste buds stand to attention as you read the menu. The suggestions are deliberately down - to - earth, drawing on the seasons and local terroir, such as the veal chop, as tender and juicy as can be. So, what are you waiting for?;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14984;Le Cénacle;France;Toulouse;La Cour des Consuls, 46 rue des Couteliers, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.59936;1.44156;88;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Le Cénacle has a plush, elegant atmosphere (superb 16C sculpted fireplace, a Caravaggio print, exposed beams). The chef takes pride in forging long-lasting partnerships with good regional producers: organic vegetables from Gers, lamb from Béarn, line-caught fish. Inventive cuisine with a Mediterranean flavour, and good value for money at lunchtime.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
14985;Le Séran - Château d'Audrieu;France;Audrieu;Château d'Audrieu, Audrieu, 14250, France;49.2040517;-0.5944419;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A listed 18C stately house, the epitome of special occasion indulgence, provides the perfect foil to polished French cuisine. Forthright recipes inspired by the classics which star local and seasonal produce that hit the spot every time, illustrated by saddle of lamb in marjoram garnished with potatoes and seaweed. First-class sauces and craftsmanship courtesy of a virtuoso chef.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14986;Aux Poulbots Gourmets;France;Thionville;9 place aux Fleurs, Thionville, 57100, France;49.3620135;6.1496214;26;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The rascally, iconic poulbots (street urchins) of Montmartre have now been joined by those of Thionville! Large bay windows, Lloyd Loom chairs and modern light fixtures add to the timeless elegance. The menu features recipes such as lobster salad and seasonal vegetables or pan-fried frogs’ legs…;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
14987;Mas de Dardagna;France;Toulouse;1 chemin de Dardagna, Rangueil, Toulouse, 31400, France;43.5575282;1.4557939;95;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Now, this is simple, well-made fare that does justice to its ingredients (the chef uses short supply chains as much as possible): guinea fowl and black Gascon pork charlotte, artichoke cream, full-bodied gravy and fresh mushrooms. No doubt about it, this typical Toulouse farmhouse is a haven for foodies! On sunny days, make the most of the terrace beneath the wisteria.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
14988;L'Instant...;France;Montrabé;13-14 chemin du Logis-Vieux, Montrabé, 31850, France;43.6436558;1.5221149;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Take an instant to savour a gourmet interlude not far from Toulouse! Diners eat cheek to jowl at immaculate white tables. In the kitchen the chef creates contemporary cuisine with a few Southern French and Asian touches. Don't miss the "L'instant gourmet" set menu!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14989;La Table d'Auzeville;France;Auzeville-Tolosane;35 chemin de l'Église, Auzeville-Tolosane, 31320, France;43.5285427;1.4807838;73;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In this white house in the heart of a village in the suburbs of Toulouse, the chef serves up generous traditional cuisine, including dishes such as fillet of duck with a spicy reduction or tournedos of beef with morel mushrooms. For dessert, a crunchy strawberry tartlet with home-made pistachio ice cream. In fine weather, enjoy your meal on the shady terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
14990;La Table de Monrecour;France;Saint-Vincent-de-Cosse;Lieu-dit Monrecour, Saint-Vincent-de-Cosse, 24220, France;44.8388373;1.1186609;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This gourmet restaurant is housed in a contemporary extension at the heart of this estate overlooking the Périgord countryside. It is furnished in a resolutely classical style and reflects modern culinary tendencies with the skilfully prepared and flavoursome dishes. Perfect for hotel residents, and anyone else.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14991;Auberge de Groisy;France;Groisy;34 route du Chef-Lieu, Groisy, 74570, France;46.0147113;6.1708556;17;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This engaging 19C farmstead has been renovated in keeping with today’s tastes: stylish bare beams and stonework and contemporary comforts adorned in beige and linen. Perfect to sample up - to - the - minute cuisine, which focuses on local produce. All the bread and ice cream is homemade.;Terrace;[]
14992;La Brucelière;France;Issigeac;54 place de la Capelle, Issigeac, 24560, France;44.7299607;0.6091185;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This authentic country inn restored by the owner couple is the epitome of charm. Star-studded chef Anthony Hardy has built up a network he can rely on, starting with his wife Marie for the front of house, and including a handful of local producers for the ingredients. The resulting cuisine combines consummately crafted seasonal produce, spot-on seasonings and flawless cooking. Start with mackerel cooked over a direct flame and organic marinated celery, followed by exquisitely plated French duckling roasted whole and served with glazed carrots, finishing with a chou pastry stuffed with hazelnut cream, both minimalist and comforting at the same time. Pretty terrace overlooking the garden to the rear is heaven when the weather permits.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14993;La Table des Merville;France;Castanet-Tolosan;3 place Pierre-Richard, Castanet-Tolosan, 31320, France;43.5151273;1.4983052;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This glass extension on a pretty square with a terrace has kitchens that open onto the dining area, giving the impression that the chef is working among the guests. Claudie and Thierry Merville have succeeded in creating an original space in which to serve their nicely contemporary and lovingly prepared dishes!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14994;Au Pois Gourmand;France;Toulouse;3 rue Émile-Heybrard, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6090756;1.4096529;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Extended and refurbished, the terrace of the Pois Gourmand, which commands a matchless view of the Garonne, offers a rural setting in the heart of town. The food is equally uplifting from semi-cooked duck foie gras in apricots to grilled Mediterranean croaker with fennel and orange confit. Simply delicious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14996;La Coquerie;France;Sète;1 chemin du Cimetière-Marin, Sète, 34200, France;43.3951885;3.6928937;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Close to the famous naval cemetery, this chic, contemporary little place boasts the Mediterranean as its backdrop and a panoramic terrace for fine weather. The restaurant serves exceedingly fresh cuisine focused on market produce and local producers, with a single six-course set menu served at both lunch and dinner. Chef Guilhem Blanc-Brude juggles Mediterranean inspirations and more inventive dishes, such as sea bass cooked scales on, potatoes confit with saffron, hollandaise sauce with wild fennel and dill, and chanterelle pickles. They also have a terrific list of natural wines.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
14997;Le Quai;France;Tain-l'Hermitage;17 rue Joseph-Peala, Tain-l'Hermitage, 26600, France;45.0695415;4.8358064;73;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;You could stay on this quayside for hours admiring the Rhône and the vineyards. On the terrace or in the bright dining area, you could almost be on an ocean liner! A modern-day bistro in which to enjoy generous dishes.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
14999;Shu;France;Paris;8 rue Suger, Paris, 75006, France;48.853083;2.3423562;85;false;true;Japanese;You have to stoop to get through the doorway that leads to this 17C cellar. In a minimalist decor, discover authentic and finely executed Japanese cuisine, in which the freshness of the ingredients works its magic in kushiage, sushi and sashimi.;Notable sake list;[]
15000;Les Tamaris - Chez Raymond;France;Le Lavandou;Boulevard de la Baleine, Le Lavandou, 83980, France;43.1417712;6.3813171;19;true;false;Seafood;Bourride, stuffed capon, grilled Mediterranean langouste, and, above all, the iconic bouillabaisse cooked over a wood fire. Under the watchful eye of its colourful boss, Raymond, the local catch of the day takes pride of place in this iconic institution on Saint-Clair beach. The terrace overlooking the sea is exquisite – so remember to ask for a seat here when you book (compulsory).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15001;Aux Prés;France;Paris;27 rue du Dragon, Paris, 75006, France;48.85274;2.33059;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine;An openly vintage bistro (red banquette seating, smoked - glass mirrors, floral wallpaper) in St Germain and international cuisine by Cyril Lignac, whose creativity never strays entirely from its French country roots.;Air conditioning;[]
15002;Le 39V;France;Paris;39 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.86979;2.30081;45;false;true;Modern Cuisine;International customers flock to the sixth floor of 39 Avenue George V... and for good reason! Overlooking the rooftops of Paris, you will enjoy consummately crafted, polished French food. After a major makeover, every detail, from the wooden parquet floor to the made-to-measure seating and the haute couture crockery, has been preened and pondered over. The epitome of understated luxury!;Air conditioning;[]
15003;SOlange;France;Lille;59 rue d'Isly, Lille, 59000, France;50.6234522;3.0375963;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Slightly out of the lively city centre, you can expect creative, heart-warming dishes made with local ingredients (most sourced from small local producers) and a menu that changes weekly. Daring combinations and inventive, tasty recipes such as cuttlefish, peppers and black pudding or Iberic pluma ham, chickpeas and chorizo…;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15005;Nodaïwa;France;Paris;272 rue Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75001, France;48.8644088;2.3331572;21;false;false;Japanese;This little restaurant, an off - shoot of a Tokyo - based eatery, boasts an unusual speciality: eel! The unagi is meticulously crafted and seasoned with soy sauce, or sanshô, an Asian pepper. The vast majority of diners who come here are Japanese, which gives an idea of the quality of the cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
15006;Mori Venice Bar;France;Paris;27 rue Vivienne, Paris, 75002, France;48.8690618;2.3400215;85;false;false;Italian;Take a seat here, in front of the former stock exchange, to savour the great specialities of Venice and northeast Italy in an interior by Philippe Starck that evokes the refinement of Venice. Painstakingly chosen ingredients: the veggies come straight from a “respectful cottage garden” and the fish from sustainable sources, like the turbot cooked in butter and prosecco with spinach leaf and cream of celery. Let’s not forget the cicchetti (small snacks) or the delicious ice cream topped with hazelnuts from Piedmont.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15008;Émile;France;Toulouse;13 place Saint-Georges, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6022225;1.4473025;93;false;false;Country cooking;An appealing wine list, 100% house-made traditional cuisine that focuses on fresh produce and local producers and – the icing on the cake – a pretty terrace overlooking a lovely square. The star of the show is obviously the cassoulet, but the menu proposes plenty of delicious alternatives, all at reasonable prices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15009;Auberge de Grilly;France;Grilly;34 ruelle de l'Église, Grilly, 01220, France;46.33059;6.11404;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a charming village between Gex and Divonne, Auberge de Grilly stands close to the church. While the interior decor tends toward the rustic, the cuisine is modern, with dishes based on fine ingredients cleverly curated into just one generous tasting menu. Service with a smile, plus a pleasant terrace.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15011;Le Terminus;France;Tournus;21 avenue Gambetta, Tournus, 71700, France;46.566862;4.9073429;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The menu of this former 1900s station buffet features modern cuisine that places freshness above all other virtues! You can have lunch or dinner in the brasserie, in an intimate and cosy room, to enjoy the regional classics that have made the house so successful (pâté en croûte, quenelle de brochet, frogs' legs). There are a few guestrooms on the first floor.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
15013;Lavandin - Château Les Oliviers de Salettes;France;Charols;1205 route du Château, Charols, 26450, France;44.5873188;4.9700561;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This peaceful 16C château, restored to the highest standards, is the quintessence of Drôme provençale. From the terrace overlooking the grounds and lavender fields or in the cosy dining room with its vaulted ceiling and a fire crackling in the hearth, get ready to embark on a poetic culinary voyage inspired by regional delicacies. Thanks to chefs Kévin Vaubourg and Lucille Routin, the castle boasts a knockout fine dining option. Each dish is carefully thought out and crafted to allow the ingredients to shout their name, depicted by an incredibly delicate tomato or locally reared lamb prepared in two ways and underscored by a chervil jus and olive seasoning. Delightful welcome. Book one of the lovely rooms and stay longer.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15014;Le Panoramic;France;Tignes;Glacier de la Grande Motte, Tignes, 73320, France;45.4281;6.8735;38;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Grills;Accessed by a funicular railway, this high-altitude restaurant (elevation: 3 032m!) promises a breath of fresh air as well as fine dining. In an inviting interior that is done out in wood, staff in traditional costume serve up authentic and delicious wood-fired dishes, including choice cuts of meat and fish to share (eg rib steak, pork shoulder and whole turbot). A delightful change of scene.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15016;Amarante;France;Paris;4 rue Biscornet, Paris, 75012, France;48.8496031;2.370009;89;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This bistro wedged between Bastille and Lyon railway station serves a bighearted, no-nonsense score rich in nostalgic flavours. The ingredients, such as ‘triple zero’ jumbo shrimps from Nantes, Kintoa pork or monkfish caught by small fishing boats, are allowed to shout their name. The interior is equally simple and authentic: tiled floor, red imitation leather benches and wooden tables. Bags of substance and atmosphere!;Air conditioning;[]
15017;Towa;France;Paris;75 rue Crozatier, Paris, 75012, France;48.8495686;2.3794117;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Japanese chef Shin Okusa is at the helm of the Towa, close to the bustling Aligre market. A champion of old-school French culinary traditions and a true disciple of Escoffier, he not only whisks up the great classics (French lamb stew, breast of duck in flaky pastry), but also sauces, hot terrines and pies, with superlative skill and flair.;;[]
15018;Montée;France;Paris;9 rue Léopold-Robert, Paris, 75014, France;48.8406781;2.3303885;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This is what you get when a talented Japanese chef decides to share his love of French cuisine: graphic presentation of the food and solid technical skill. The stripped-back designer decor adds to the experience.;;[]
15019;Le Bistro du Clos;France;Le Rouret;9 route d'Opio, Le Rouret, 06650, France;43.6731822;7.005074;97;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Provençal;Whether outdoors, in the shade of hackberry trees or indoors, in the bistro dotted with old knickknacks, you will inevitably find yourself surrounded by an enthusiastic crowd of faithful regulars. The chef ticks all the boxes in his open kitchen. A talented craftsman, he curates generous, seasonal dishes from fresh, premium ingredients in a Provençal register that hits the spot every time: chuck beef stew, braised vegetables, fresh tomato vinaigrette or red fruit pannacotta. The establishment is located in the left wing of the Maison des Terroirs, aptly devoted to promoting regional produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15020;Bistrotters;France;Paris;9 rue Decrès, Paris, 75014, France;48.8330076;2.3149935;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A lovely place in the southern reaches of the 14th arrondissement near Métro Plaisance. The Spanish chef carefully selects his ingredients, with a preference for small-scale producers in the Paris region, and instils them with various influences (Asian, Mediterranean etc). Laid-back service.;Air conditioning;[]
15021;Au Fil des Saisons;France;Étupes;3 rue de la Libération, Étupes, 25460, France;47.5058772;6.8644355;19;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Stéphane and Fabienne Robinne’s establishment is home to a cleverly refurbished interior, depicted by untreated wooden tables and velvet upholstered chairs… A refreshing modern vibe that provides the backdrop to the chef’s signature recipes oozing in traditional accents.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15022;Auberge des Ruines;France;Jumièges;17 place de la Mairie, Jumièges, 76480, France;49.4327185;0.8189002;16;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this pretty half-timbered house just opposite the ruins of the abbey, a friendly green-fingered chef showcases his passion for the riches of Normandy's terroir. Following the seasons, he fêtes ingredients such as trout, beef and lamb, ciders and Calvados, goat's and cow's cheeses. Everything comes from Normandy, not least the fruit and vegetables picked in the restaurant's kitchen garden – the chef does his own planting. With the greens and pastures of Normandy on his doorstep, he composes the magnificent cheese trolley using produce from neighbouring farms. Savour in an inviting and chic contemporary interior, or in the glass-paned extension giving onto the terrace.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15023;L'Arpège;France;Tarbes;22 place de Verdun, Tarbes, 65000, France;43.2335046;0.0743525;99;false;false;Creative;This pair of Japanese chefs cook lovely creative, Japanese - inflected cuisine, in which broths, seaweed and seasonings show off good - quality ingredients. The interior, in keeping with the presentation on the plates, is elegant and contemporary.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15024;L'Agrume;France;Paris;15 rue des Fossés-Saint-Marcel, Paris, 75005, France;48.8386064;2.3560938;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the open kitchen of this bistro, the chef delicately crafts refreshingly wholesome dishes, such as poultry in vin jaune paired with asparagus or a piece of roast turbot with mashed potatoes and poultry jus. Flawlessly fresh produce is the name of the game (the fish comes from Brittany and the fruit and vegetables from the very best suppliers). Tasting menu in the evening.;Air conditioning;[]
15025;Liza;France;Paris;14 rue de la Banque, Paris, 75002, France;48.8676451;2.3408562;66;false;true;Lebanese;Originally from Beirut, Liza Asseily gives pride of place to the food of her homeland. In a bright interior strewn with Middle Eastern touches, you can expect mezze to share, grilled meats or fattet batinjan (aubergine, minced lamb and yoghurt). Numerous vegetarian dishes and a fine selection of Lebanese wines.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15027;L'Initial;France;Paris;9 rue de Bièvre, Paris, 75005, France;48.850875;2.35052;16;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This Japanese chef with a brilliant track record proposes French cuisine that demonstrates remarkable precision and is made with fine produce (sea bass, scallops, langoustine, morel mushrooms) and represents good value for money. The roast rack of Lozère lamb, celeriac purée, lemon condiment and reduced lamb jus was a stand-out dish. Highly attentive service and a refined and light-filled setting.;Air conditioning;[]
15028;Le Mazenay;France;Paris;46 rue de Montmorency, Paris, 75003, France;48.8635214;2.3533471;96;false;true;Farm to table;The emphasis here is on good cooking technique, the right jus and fine produce. There is no unnecessary fuss when you feast on wild snails with herbs or a poached farm-reared chicken. But the chef hankers after just one thing – the start of game season! Roasted Scottish grouse, hare à la royale. A place for bon viveurs.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15031;Étude;France;Paris;14 rue du Bouquet-de-Longchamp, Paris, 75016, France;48.86591;2.29091;100;false;true;Creative;Inspired by his encounters with small-scale producers, chef Keisuke Yamagishi, who hails from the rural province of Nagano, Japan, serves surprise menus based on seasonal ingredients. In a minimalist setting (the overhead lighting is by Serge Mouille), the chef treats us to his creative outlook, his refined vision of plating and his passion for Burgundy wines, in particular.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15032;La Laiterie;France;Lille;138 avenue de l'Hippodrome, à Lambersart, Lille, 59000, France;50.6398564;3.0329022;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Grandson of dairy farmers and son of restaurant owners, chef Édouard Chouteau, who trained with the likes of Pierre Gagnaire, Alain Passard and Christophe Pelé, has settled in this historic cottage, a former dairy farm (yes, really!), next-door to Citadelle Park and a stone’s throw from the banks of the Deûle. The tastefully appointed dining rooms open onto a huge garden and a patio. The perfect foil for the chef’s creative score, which delves freely into produce from Northern France with a fondness for surf and turf recipes.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15033;GrandCœur;France;Paris;41 rue du Temple, Paris, 75004, France;48.8595675;2.3538933;37;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Take a seat in the warm, welcoming interior (with exposed beams and stonework, marble table tops and velvet upholstery), or on the pleasant terrace in the picturesque, cobbled courtyard of the Marais Dance Centre. The brainchild of Mauro Colagreco, the pedigree Gallic recipes come with an international, often Italian twist… Examples include stuffed confit of lamb in a provençal sauce, Taggiasche olives and a gutsy gravy – high-flying culinary art!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15034;24 - Le Restaurant;France;Paris;24 rue Jean-Mermoz, Paris, 75008, France;48.87125;2.3118615;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a quiet street just a stone's throw from the Champs-Elysées, this establishment offers well-crafted, pedigree Gallic cuisine with an occasional personal spin, such as breast of Dombes duckling, chutney of yellow peaches, pine nuts and duckling jus underscored by mulled wine. Cheerful and professional welcome in a stylish setting.;Air conditioning;[]
15035;Méson Chalut;France;Saint-Malo;8 rue de la Corne-de-Cerf, Saint-Malo, 35400, France;48.6503902;-2.0247934;16;true;true;Seafood;In his "méson" (which means "house" in Gallo, the language of Upper Brittany), the chef-owner goes all out Breton, showcasing seafood and other regional ingredients (buckwheat, lait ribot (Breton buttermilk), Coco de Paimpol beans, salted butter) that he sources locally. Freshness, flavour and a respect for nature.;Air conditioning;[]
15036;Atelier Maître Albert;France;Paris;1 rue Maître-Albert, Paris, 75005, France;48.8511482;2.3501854;79;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;An attractive medieval fireplace and roasting spits take pride of place in this handsome interior designed by J.-M. Wilmotte. Guy Savoy signs the menu which boasts a knockout cast of first-class ingredients. T-bone steak, free-range poultry, spit-roasted suckling lamb chops and leg – all that remains is to choose your side dish, for example, gratin dauphinois or purée, both crafted with text-book precision.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
15037;Kitchen Ter(re);France;Paris;26 boulevard Saint-Germain, Paris, 75005, France;48.8495431;2.3526214;61;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In his third establishment devoted to pasta, William Ledeuil crafts a kaleidoscope of pared-back tastes and flavours, starring high-flying creations from spelt, durum wheat, einkorn or tender Roussillon wheat by artisan Roland Feuillas. Chef Julien Jéquier (with stints at Le V and L’Écrin) orchestrates a balanced score in which Asian notes and fresh herbs play major supporting roles. From the exquisitely laid tables to the plating, balance is the key word, as is illustrated by his dish of coquillettes (small pasta shells) made out of fresh milled khorasan wheat flour with chicken wings, Taggiasche olives, spinach and Thai broth! Vibrant, lively and the epitome of charming!;Air conditioning;[]
15038;Elmer;France;Paris;30 rue Notre-Dame-de-Nazareth, Paris, 75003, France;48.8673447;2.359184;89;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Close to République, this terribly chic bistro is officiated by a chef with an impressive career (including L'Oustau de Baumanière, Pierre Gagnaire, travels in Asia and Latin America). He composes a flavoursome menu that packs a punch, with fine meats cooked on embers or on the rotisserie.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
15039;À La Biche au Bois;France;Paris;45 avenue Ledru-Rollin, Paris, 75012, France;48.8478758;2.3711407;31;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In an atmospheric interior reminiscent of historic Parisian bistros and two minutes from Lyon railway station, regulars and travellers rub shoulders as they dig into traditional no-nonsense nosh. Country terrines, Burgundy snails and Royan ravioles star alongside duck breast in honey, fillet of beef served with cèpes and foie gras or coq au vin (the house specialty), without forgetting game in season (venison and even Scottish grouse!). The crème caramel to finish is wickedly addictive…;;[]
15040;Mamagoto;France;Paris;5 rue des Petits-Hôtels, Paris, 75010, France;48.8772959;2.3547006;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Mamagoto is Japanese for tea party. Seasoned chef Koji Tsuchiya serves an appealing selection of dishes you can share (or not!), combining Japanese and Basque influences – for example, sea urchin with parsley sayon or grilled squid with pesto. The wine list includes some unusual natural wines. A simpler set menu at lunchtime.;Air conditioning;[]
15044;Winstub Arnold;France;Itterswiller;98 route des Vins, Itterswiller, 67140, France;48.3639658;7.4277058;57;true;false;Alsatian, Traditional Cuisine;Dive headlong into Alsace traditions at this winstub featuring numerous elsässische Spezialitäten, including kougelhopf, sauerkraut, black pudding, apple purée, baeckeoffe hotpot or specials such as "Marie Leczinsca vol-au-vent"… Choose a wine from the family estate to accompany your food, then sit back and enjoy in a setting that couldn't be more characteristic of the region.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15045;Les Flots;France;Châtelaillon-Plage;52 boulevard de la Mer, Châtelaillon-Plage, 17340, France;46.0750236;-1.0934672;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This picturesque 19C blue and white house stands on the boulevard that skirts the immense beach. Take a seat in a contemporary dining room overlooking the sea and dig into beautifully presented super-fresh fish and shellfish platters, the establishment’s pride and joy. Guaranteed to find favour with seafood lovers!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15046;Les Terrasses de Clairefontaine;France;Clairefontaine-en-Yvelines;1 rue de Rambouillet, Clairefontaine-en-Yvelines, 78120, France;48.613185;1.907527;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the Chevreuse Valley and Rambouillet forest, this restaurant on the edge of Clairefontaine pond serves heart - warming, up - to - date food, with a weakness for truffles and game (in season). Fine view of the pond (all year long).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15047;Le Pierre Scize;France;Châtillon-sur-Chalaronne;Place de la République, Châtillon-sur-Chalaronne, 01400, France;46.12042;4.9566493;44;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Behind a handsome half-timbered façade in the centre of this picturesque medieval town, this restaurant has a charming interior. Like any self-respecting disciple of Escoffier, the chef prepares delicious regional-style dishes, such as pike quenelles with "Geoffroy sauce", Bresse chicken pot-au-feu, sabodet (pig's head sausage) à la beaujolaise, Dombes carp. Pleasant guestrooms available.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15049;Les Gourmands Disent;France;Chalon-sur-Saône;59 rue de Strasbourg, Chalon-sur-Saône, 71100, France;46.7793009;4.8625321;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In Île St-Laurent's "restaurant street", an enthusiastic double act (Laurent is in charge of savoury dishes, while Nadine handles the desserts) has breathed new life into this engaging eatery. Bare stone walls and high coffered French ceilings set the scene for well-crafted dishes, before perusing the knockout selection of trompe-l’œil desserts, such as the chocolate Montecristo. Do as the regulars do: book well in advance.;Terrace;[]
15050;Hostellerie de l'Abbaye de la Celle;France;La Celle;10 place du Général-de-Gaulle, La Celle, 83170, France;43.3938151;6.0405673;53;false;true;Provençal, Mediterranean Cuisine;Near Celle Abbey, this remote fine dining inn occupies a stunning 18C edifice. Part of the Ducasse Group, the restaurant boasts all the facilities one would expect of a luxury establishment, including a finely crafted Mediterranean score with a soft spot for veg, illustrated by stuffed Provençal vegetables overflowing with herbs and garlic. Unostentatious tradition.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15051;Auberge du Prunelli;France;Bastelicaccia;Pont de Pisciatello, Bastelicaccia, 20129, France;41.91265;8.83617;78;true;true;Country cooking;A cosy, inviting atmosphere reigns in this restaurant that first welcomed guests in 1860 in its former life as a coaching inn. It's been a family affair since 1997, when father André Orlandazzi bought the place – today his sons have taken over the reins. Charcuterie, cheeses and honey from the valley, vegetables from the garden, simple dishes simmered for hours on the stove, tarts made with fruit from the orchard, over 200 Corsican wines... Timeless! In fine weather, you might like to take advantage of the large terrace surrounded by greenery overlooking the Prunelli.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15052;La Garenne;France;Dracy-le-Fort;Le Dracy, 4 rue du Pressoir, Dracy-le-Fort, 71640, France;46.7989;4.78163;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An appealing place where you can enjoy, for example, melt-in-the-mouth salmon gravelax with a creamy carrot purée and potato espuma, and, for dessert, chou au craquelin, lemon yuzu mousse and citrus fruit flavours. The low-key decor incorporates some pretty prints of artwork by Alain Thomas, and the veranda overlooks the terrace and grounds. The hotel, meanwhile, boasts pleasant guestrooms, a swimming pool and a spa.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15053;Le Quai 21;France;Colmar;15 quai de la Poissonnerie, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0742591;7.3600599;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Head down to the docks of Little Venice for a fine dining experience, courtesy of Le Quai 21 and its expertly prepared contemporary cuisine, eg fillet of German sashi beef accompanied by chanterelles, onions, cherry tomatoes and parmesan. The inviting dining area on the first floor is complemented by a pleasant patio terrace. Chic bistro vibe on the ground floor.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15054;Auberge du Pont de Rethondes;France;Rethondes;21 rue du Maréchal-Foch, Rethondes, 60153, France;49.4162518;2.9388529;27;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The pretty traditional façade epitomises the charm of this village on the banks of the Aisne. Inside is a modern and refined dining room, perfect for enjoying a meal put together by an imaginative chef with good seasonal ingredients at his disposal. Garden terrace.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15055;La Corniche;France;San-Martino-di-Lota;1 chemin di u Fornu (Hameau de Castagneto), San-Martino-di-Lota, 20200, France;42.7347741;9.4347259;74;false;true;Corsican;A family business clinging to the mountain with a splendid terrace shaded by plane trees overlooking the sea... Exquisite plating, delicious flavours with notes of Corsican saffron and confit of citron, twice-cooked mouth-watering veal or the decadent vacherin dessert perfumed with the one and only Madagascan vanilla, all of which washed down with locally grown vintages.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15056;Les Oliviers;France;Bandol;Hôtel Île Rousse, 25 boulevard Louis-Lumière, Bandol, 83150, France;43.1332056;5.7511869;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In Renécros Bay, this posh, stylish, fashionable restaurant commands a breathtaking view of the Mediterranean. Open for dinner (only!), Martin and Fleur craft colourful, flavoursome Mediterranean and Provençal cuisine, presented in several tasting menus, starring ingredients such as green asparagus from Mallemort, line-caught fish direct from local boats, strawberries from Hyères… As you might expect, the vision of the sun gently setting over the glittering horizon is truly spectacular!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15058;Kapara;France;Paris;9 rue d'Alger, Paris, 75001, France;48.8653808;2.3297932;58;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;In their new venue, Kapara, whose interior is almost identical to that of the former Balagan, Assaf Granit and his partner Tomer Lanzman have called upon chef Zohar Sasson. In a setting depicted by groovy background music and hoots of laughter from the ebullient kitchen brigade, Ms Sasson cheerfully conjures up dishes loosely inspired by Sephardic culinary traditions. The menu rolls out a colourful culinary anthology, boosted by spices, seasonings and chickpeas. Some of the emblematic dishes of the former Balagan remain on the menu, such as “deconstructed” kebab. Festive, friendly and (very) buzzy vibe.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15059;Les Alisiers;France;Lapoutroie;Lieu-dit Faudé, Lapoutroie, 68650, France;48.1443335;7.1674265;43;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This lovely panoramic restaurant has a minimalist decor. The food showcases local ingredients but stands out from local dishes by mixing influences and flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15060;Côté Vigne;France;Kientzheim;30 Grand-Rue, Kientzheim, 68240, France;48.1365361;7.2875045;84;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this charming village, an imposing 16C half-timbered house. The chef crafts modern dishes, scattered with exotic flavours, such as beef terrine with grated egg and wasabi cream, or grilled squid with leeks, pumpkin gnocchi, mussels and red curry. On the wine side, you will be treated to the organic vintages from the family estate. The terrace is very popular in summertime. Simpler lunch menu.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15061;La Vieille Fontaine - Le Club de Cavalière & Spa;France;Cavalière;820 avenue du Cap-Nègre, Cavalière, 83980, France;43.150784;6.423567;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant offers fine seafood, as well as some meat dishes, cooked with great skill. Try ravioli with langoustine and coriander, curry bisque, sea bass roasted in its skin, and crunchy escabeche with condiments. Sea views while you eat!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15062;Auberge de la Vieille Ferme;France;Le Meux;58 rue de la République, Le Meux, 60880, France;49.3647475;2.7458724;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this little village not far from Compiègne, a former farmstead is now a very popular hotel and restaurant. The chef signs a culinary score that is both delicate and appetising, dotted with personal touches such as a starter of razor clams, cuttlefish and potatoes, or the peanut, caramel and vanilla millefeuille dessert – to die for! Highly recommended.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15063;Bistro Saint-Jean;France;Bar-le-Duc;132 boulevard de la Rochelle, Bar-le-Duc, 55000, France;48.7706065;5.1657039;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This ex-grocer’s shop is now a contemporary bistro, rich in flavour and colour, that hits the spot every time. The owner, son of a pastry chef, rustles up market-fresh cuisine in tune with the seasons, like this slow-cooked pork belly with baby onions and braising juices. Respect for the ingredients is the motto. Efficient, unobtrusive staff.;Air conditioning;[]
15064;Le Pirate;France;Erbalunga;au port, Erbalunga, 20222, France;42.7743572;9.4762846;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This well-known Cap Corse establishment stands on the pretty port of Erbalunga. Fish soup, tiger veal, suckling pig, barbecued fish: the quintessence of Corsican food, with the odd, unexpected note, such as a new take on vitello tonnato. The setting is idyllic with a few tables on a small balcony and a large waterside terrace.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15065;L'Espérance;France;Bandol;21 rue du Docteur-Louis-Marçon, Bandol, 83150, France;43.136773;5.7572062;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine;If you're lucky enough to be in Bandol, leave the harbour area and make a beeline for the refreshing establishment of Maria and Gilles Pradines, a treasure trove of culinary talent and delight. Born in the Basque country, the chef has retained his love of the south of France, from stuffed piquillo peppers to black cherries and pata negra. Each ingredient is fastidiously sourced and prepared with great care: wild sea bass marinated in fennel seeds, grilled special oyster no. 2, apricots from Provence, olive oil and lemons… The presentation of the dishes is beautiful, and the service is charming!;Air conditioning;[]
15067;Le Millésime;France;Chambolle-Musigny;1 rue Traversière, Chambolle-Musigny, 21220, France;47.18578;4.95028;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of a winegrowers’ village, this spruce building is home to a contemporary restaurant. The chef cleverly, even daringly, juggles with a range of culinary scores, illustrated by a tartare of whelks flanked by a foie gras emulsion. Examples of the bargain-priced lunchtime menu include a chicken liver cake with a shellfish sauce or a Black Angus steak, pinot noir jus and autumn pickles. The menu slaloms between pure-bred Gallic classics and more elaborate recipes: poached eggs in red wine rub shoulders with Brittany lobster in a chorizo crust flanked by girolle mushrooms and vin jaune sauce. You can taste the wine before purchasing at the Musigny wine shop, abutting the establishment and which also belongs to the owner.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15068;Le Relais du Çatey;France;L'Isle-d'Abeau;10 rue du Didier, L'Isle-d'Abeau, 38080, France;45.6231685;5.2355615;55;false;true;Classic Cuisine;A contemporary decor and lighting enhance the authentic character of this regional house from 1774. Arctic char with meadowsweet, roast saddle of venison with juniper and mushrooms or Williams pear on a wafer-thin millefeuille. Pedigree classics and inventive flourishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15069;Michel Béjeannin - Auberge de Chavannes;France;Courlans;1890 avenue de Châlon, Courlans, 39570, France;46.67481;5.48255;59;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In winter, an open fire burns brightly in this welcoming and contemporary inn. The food sings an ode to the Mediterranean with bouillabaisse (the chef lived in Marseille for some 26 years), and also the local countryside with Bresse hen in vin jaune and morels, a whimsical nod to his Jura roots. Fine wine list with a fondness for organic and biodynamic produce. Spacious rooms for overnight stays.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15070;L'Océanic;France;Chinon;13 rue Rabelais, Chinon, 37500, France;47.1659776;0.2407273;57;true;false;Seafood;The ocean breeze blows as far inland as Chinon! As its name suggests, this restaurant gives seafood pride of place. The chef prepares very fresh fish, adding a dash of originality, with a pinch of spice here and a hint of sweet and sour there. Good value for money.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15072;La Botte d'Asperges;France;Contres;52 rue Pierre-Henri-Mauger, Contres, 41700, France;47.4196538;1.428599;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With a name that conjures up springtime (it means "bunch of asparagus"), this restaurant delivers delicious cuisine, showcasing local producers and winegrowers as well as herbs from its pretty garden in aesthetically pleasing dishes. At the helm is a professional couple and a chef with a solid track record, Stéphane Bureau – he loves to pop out into the dining area and share his enthusiasm with diners. The comfortable interior is done out in a contemporary bistro style.;Air conditioning;[]
15073;L'Instantané;France;Clermont-Ferrand;2 rue de l'Abbé-Girard, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7774503;3.0869313;57;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary bistro located in the art gallery district proposes moments of pure culinary bliss, dreamt up by a seasoned chef (Ritz, Lasserre, Plaza). Veal, poultry and pork “porkpie”, 12-hour melt-in-the-mouth beef, roast loin of hake with hazelnut butter, crème brûlée… Finger licking good from start to finish!;;[]
15074;L'Auberge Bressane;France;Bourg-en-Bresse;166 boulevard de Brou, Bourg-en-Bresse, 01000, France;46.1974614;5.2355625;77;true;true;Classic Cuisine;A firm favourite: justice is done to regional specialities (Bresse chicken, frogs' legs, crayfish and its legendary pike quenelles) and the wine list is packed with vintage bottles. Terrace with a view onto the church of the Royal Monastery of Brou.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15075;Les Cordois Autrement;France;Avallon;15 rue Bocquillot, Avallon, 89200, France;47.4859102;3.9074984;40;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, run by the same family since 1910, now abuts a 12C church. Take a seat and admire the bright colourful interior or relax on the shaded terrace, as you sample a cleverly updated version of regional country nosh: Burgundy snails, eggs in red wine, veal kidneys in mustard sauce without forgetting the odd intriguing creation such as an escalope of salmon with Morteau sausage and a creamy sauce of runny cheese…;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15076;Le Fanal;France;Banyuls-sur-Mer;18 avenue Pierre-Fabre, Banyuls-sur-Mer, 66650, France;42.4799784;3.1356336;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The lights of Le Fanal (“The Lantern”) will guide you to this idyllic spot overlooking Banyuls marina. Catalan-born Pascal Borrell has decided to drop anchor here after stints in several top Paris restaurants and running the Chapon Fin at Perpignan. The main attraction here is fish: hake, monkfish, sole, turbot, cod and anchovy pickles delicately marinated in Banyuls vinegar.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
15077;Le Bistrot du Quai;France;Charolles;1 avenue de la Libération, Charolles, 71120, France;46.433527;4.2752307;68;true;true;Burgundian;In this new place, standing opposite the parent restaurant on the other side of the road, the chef proposes traditional cuisine and spit - roast meats. Menu du Jour in harmony with the seasons, and Menu Charolais, showcasing produce from Burgundy. Terrace overlooking the river.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15078;Auberge du Bon Laboureur;France;Chenonceaux;6 rue du Docteur-Bretonneau, Chenonceaux, 37150, France;47.3321782;1.0658093;93;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Housed in a converted coaching inn built in 1786, this 100-year-old family-run restaurant sticks to the well-trodden path of cooking with a focus on seasonal ingredients. Chef Antoine Jeudi, now assisted by Julien Perrodin, certainly knows his stuff, and his flavoursome dishes go down a treat with your choice from an appealing wine selection. Thanks to the small kitchen garden, there is also a vegetable-forward set menu that includes, most notably, tomato stuffed with Touraine vegetables, fresh herb coulis and chickpea cream. Along with a charming setting, it all makes for a pleasant meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15079;La Suite;France;Bourges;50 rue Bourbonnoux, Bourges, 18000, France;47.08398;2.3993096;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A fashionably stylish modern interior sets the scene in this warm, friendly eatery. The regularly renewed seasonal menu will make your mouth water... before the flavours and aromas satisfy your tastebuds and obliterate your hunger pangs. Let's not forget the pretty patio terrace or the wine list that leaves nothing to chance – the owner is a trained sommelier, while his brother is in charge of the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15080;Les Chênes;France;Augerolles;Route de Courpière, Augerolles, 63930, France;45.7225667;3.6110023;90;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A wind of change is blowing through this family establishment (open since 1975), since the son Léo, who learned the ropes in top houses, has taken over the helm. Still surrounded by woodland and the Monts du Forez, the interior has been revamped as has the intelligently updated traditional lineup which showcases regional produce (meat, mushrooms, cheese).;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15083;La Tupina;France;Bordeaux;6 rue Porte-de-la-Monnaie, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8329101;-0.5620775;98;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A genuine institution, this country inn champions dishes of yesteryear... Sanguette (blood pudding), macaronade (pasta with beef and tomato sauce), chips fried in duck fat: local produce is promoted with conviction in hearty dishes from South-West France, but also seasonal vegetables and meat roasted in the hearth. The fine produce on the counter certainly whets the appetite.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15084;L'As de Trèfle;France;Bernières-sur-Mer;420 rue Léopold-Hettier, Bernières-sur-Mer, 14990, France;49.3291482;-0.4308544;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Slightly set back from the D-Day landing beaches on the Côte de Nacre, here we are in the very pleasant restaurant of Anthony Vallette, an energetic chef from Normandy, born in Condé-sur-Vire. Over the course of the seasons, he draws on the flavours of the local terroir – fish from the Channel, andouille de Vire, De Bayeux pork – and composes meticulous dishes with just the right amount of daring! His modern cuisine takes its cue from the market and follows his heart… and his personal favourites are reflected in the menu!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15085;Les Impressionnistes - La Ferme Saint-Siméon;France;Honfleur;20 rue Adolphe-Marais, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.4236963;0.2249564;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Established in the luxury Ferme Saint Siméon Hotel, a historic hamlet in the upper reaches of Honfleur, this property is the quintessence of stylish. The plush elegant Normandy-style interior, the wooded grounds and the terrace with a superb view of the Seine Estuary may be absolutely enchanting, but not enough to distract us from the matter at hand! The chef creates seasonal contemporary cuisine that draws on top-notch Normandy produce. The estate is also home to the half-timbered, thatched roof La Boucane bistro, which serves equally tasty, but more traditional cuisine.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15086;Lore Ttipia - Auberge Ostape;France;Bidarray;Domaine de Chahatoenia, Bidarray, 64780, France;43.2895753;-1.3619713;68;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A sprawling country estate on the heights of Bidarray and Itxassou is home to this inn that occupies a 17C farmstead. A panoramic terrace commands a jaw-dropping view of the grandiose rolling countryside. Chef John Argaud, who trained with the best of the Basque Country (La Table des Frères Ibarboure, Ithurria) as well as at Le Meurice with Alain Ducasse in Paris, shines the spotlight on outstanding local produce. Some ingredients are cooked over embers or finished on a hot stone for an added distinctive edge. The food is crisp, legible and delicate, like the stuffed courgette flowers with grilled cuttlefish. From Monday to Wednesday, the restaurant only offers a bistronomic menu, which is simpler but just as appetising as that available later in the week.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15088;Le Pavé d'Auge;France;Beuvron-en-Auge;Le Bourg, Beuvron-en-Auge, 14430, France;49.1881765;-0.0460846;72;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated between Caen and Lisieux in the heart of the Pays d’Auge, Beuvron-en-Auge is picture postcard perfect with its 17-18C half-timbered houses, its manors and its gardens decked in flowers come summertime. The restaurant, which occupies the village’s former covered market, is fully in keeping with this olde worlde character. Chef Adrien Haye champions local producers in a bid to work with the best seasonal produce. The enticing culinary lineup allows diners to choose from oysters from Saint-Vaast, lobster from Carteret or John Dory, as well as foie gras, veal sweetbread, tripe and andouille sausage. The quintessence of Normandy!;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15089;Le Castel Marie-Louise;France;La Baule;1 avenue Andrieu, La Baule, 44500, France;47.28132;-2.4079697;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A prime example of La Baule’s early-20C seaside architecture, this manor house is home to a hotel and a restaurant appointed in a classical bourgeois style whose windows overlook the grounds and pretty terrace. Local lad Jérémy Coirier draws his inspiration from the region (fish, shellfish, Croisic seaweed, Guérande saffron, Mesquer pigeon) to compose a menu that changes with the seasons.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15090;L'Entre Deux;France;Biarritz;5 avenue du Maréchal-Foch, Biarritz, 64200, France;43.4810077;-1.5588191;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Young chef Rémy Escale is at the helm of this trendy bistro, which is inviting and tastefully decorated. Food - wise, the objective has been set to stick close to the ingredients and bring out their natural flavour. He weaves flavours together with panache, demonstrating faultless technical know - how: an enjoyable experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
15091;Gavroche;France;Strasbourg;4 rue Klein, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5785761;7.7528562;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a quiet side street in the Krutenau quarter, this restaurant has an intimate feel. Chef Alexy Fuchs serves contemporary cuisine (langoustine, apple salad and mustard ice, or scallops, sweet potato, crispy ravioli and bisque emulsion) with the odd nod to Alsace, as in the foie gras terrine with fruit chutney and dampfnudel. Service is particularly charming.;Air conditioning;[]
15092;Au Vieux Moulin;France;Graufthal;7 rue du Vieux-Moulin, Graufthal, 67320, France;48.8212776;7.2813631;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Take a seat in the luminous dining room overlooking the countryside of this family - run house tucked away in the Graufthal valley and dig into the sparkling cuisine of Guillaum Kessel. The menus are dictated by seasonal availability, a principle adhered to by the entire community. For example, hen’s egg from Moulin farm and Steilberg snails, breast of duckling, fried girolles and cherries. The wine list boasts over 200 references.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15093;Le M;France;Ambert;1 place du Livradois, Ambert, 63600, France;45.5485419;3.7453734;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;We love this trendy contemporary bistro as much for its charming hospitality as for its tasty, up-to-the-minute cooking, such as a thick loin of cod, fregola sarda and poultry jus. The concise menu-carte, which ensures the freshness and quality of seasonal ingredients, is a steal at lunchtime! Don't miss the excellent cannelé, a nod to the couple's Bordeaux roots. There is a fine selection of wines on the blackboard.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15094;Anthon;France;Obersteinbach;40 rue Principale, Obersteinbach, 67510, France;49.0361543;7.6875967;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Georges Flaig represents the fourth generation at the helm of this gorgeous half - timbered house, dating from 1860. No nostalgia on his watch. His cooking is modern and tasty, and readily promotes producers from the surrounding area. For instance, Windstein Highland beef and Wingen trout.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15095;Auberge Ramstein;France;Scherwiller;1 rue du Riesling, Scherwiller, 67750, France;48.2915546;7.4241757;69;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The tradition of hospitality continues from one generation to the next at this family affair, surrounded by vineyards. The son, Lucas, who honed his craft in several prestigious restaurants, creates contemporary dishes with a nod to the Alsace terroir : barbecued beets with salmon trout from Sparsbach, or saddle of venison with celeriac, cocoa nibs and spaetzle. The welcome is warm, the service attentive and guestrooms prolong the pleasure.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15097;Ail des Ours;France;Amiens;11 rue Sire-Firmin-Leroux, Amiens, 80000, France;49.8930033;2.2992049;97;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This pleasant, trendy restaurant close to the cathedral is run by young chef Stéphane Bruyer. In a renovated dining space decorated in natural tones (with lots of plants), he serves simple, seasonal cuisine, using market produce to devise a single set menu (with a choice of fish or meat). This is a very popular spot in Amiens... and it's easy to see why.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15098;Akira Back Paris;France;Paris;Prince de Galles, 33 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.86911;2.3008;82;false;true;Japanese, Fusion;In the Prince de Galles hotel, this is the first European restaurant of American-Korean chef Akira Back. After a career as a professional snowboarder (he grew up in Aspen, home to the legendary ski resort), he turned his hand to cooking. He was recruited by Nobuyuki Matsuhisa and later became the executive chef at the renowned chef's restaurant. Diners are given the opportunity to taste this new take on Japanese cuisine, a real melting pot of cultures and flavours, including Back's speciality: AB Tuna Pizza. Meanwhile, feast your eyes on the sumptuous decor of this large modern restaurant with Art Deco light fixtures emitting subdued lighting, while the kitchen team busy themselves at the marble counter.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15099;L'Ambassade;France;Béziers;22 boulevard de Verdun, Béziers, 34500, France;43.3369314;3.219751;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fresh ingredients, balanced dishes: chef Patrick Olry, well known in the region, demonstrates his know - how and consistency. In particular, be sure to try the tasting menus based on truffles, scallops or lobster, which are in no small part responsible for the establishment's reputation.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15100;Le Senso;France;Beauvais;25 rue d'Agincourt, Beauvais, 60000, France;49.429753;2.0847508;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the market square, this spruce, well-kept restaurant provides the perfect foil for simple, unfussy cuisine in which local produce takes pride of place. Chef Allan Castellote cannot be faulted for his artistic presentations, while his brother Tristan masterfully attends to the wine-food pairing suggestions. The house speciality, kouign amann, is to die for!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15101;Ma Cuisine;France;Beaune;Passage Sainte-Hélène, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0218626;4.8386238;49;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Wine takes pride of place in this friendly bistro with an outstanding selection of some 800 different bottles. The chef certainly knows his way around them, and is equally at ease in the kitchen. Diners delight in his homemade jellied ham with parsley, veal chop in jus and crème caramel. The dishes will have you coming back for more.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15102;Sormani;France;Paris;4 rue du Général-Lanrezac, Paris, 75017, France;48.8758923;2.2937235;63;false;true;Italian;This Italian restaurant has an opulent feel, with its Murano glass chandeliers, mouldings and mirrors, and is popular with Paris's celebrities. The cooking pays tribute to Italian specialities, with spaghetti alle vongole and Calabrian chilli, for example, or iconic desserts such as the gigantesco – Italian-style vanilla ice cream frozen to order on site, served with meringue, nougatine and liquid caramel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
15103;Le Pergolèse;France;Paris;40 rue Pergolèse, Paris, 75116, France;48.87433;2.28259;36;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;While the interior is adorned in contemporary art, the food continues to celebrate classicism, in the style of a plush bourgeois home in which each guest is pampered as if they were a VIP. Unsurprisingly, the menu features a patriotic lineup of French classics: lobster, pressed leeks, quince dressing or whole roast pigeon garnished with beetroot chutney and basted in offal gravy.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
15104;Racines;France;Paris;8 passage des Panoramas, Paris, 75002, France;48.8712766;2.3417661;17;false;true;Italian;Simone Tondo, a chef of Sardinian origin, runs this charming bistro-cum-wine cellar, having made the excellent decision to turn it into a traditionally styled osteria. The chef's cooking is firmly rooted in Italian produce and he gives free rein to his creativity with a carte blanche menu and daily specials. These present a choice of down-to-earth Italian dishes that are rife with distinct flavours and carefully prepared from well-chosen ingredients: vitello tonnato, polpette al sugo, ricotta ravioli, spinach and squid.;;[]
15106;La Table de Colette;France;Paris;17 rue Laplace, Paris, 75005, France;48.8473182;2.3471519;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;With green electricity, energy-efficient appliances, seed saving and the carbon footprint of the dishes shown on the menu – everything has been thought out with eco-responsibility in mind. Vegetables and pulses, prepared in all manner of ways, take pride of place, eg the medley of lentils – stewed, emulsified and fried. And there is the odd nod to the chef's native Brittany, in the form of the cauliflower surf and turf, Guéméné andouille sausage and abalone.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15107;L'Enoteca;France;Hyères;3 rue des Porches, Hyères, 83400, France;43.1205545;6.1288929;19;true;false;Modern Cuisine;(Temporarily closed) This enoteca is the first restaurant of a young couple overflowing with culinary talent and ambition. In the kitchen, the chef sources premium ingredients to create flavoursome, enticing dishes poised between southwest France and Provence, while his partner warmly and professionally welcomes diners.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15108;Ogata;France;Paris;16 rue Debelleyme, Paris, 75003, France;48.861118;2.3633746;56;false;false;Japanese;Ogata, a temple dedicated to Japanese art de vivre, is located in a private mansion in the Marais and masterminded by Shinichiro Ogata, world-famous designer and connoisseur. The (mainly) traditional Japanese food sports an omakase spirit, through a tasting menu comprised of immaculate seasonal produce (first-class sashimi). The best seats are at the counter. Pop into the shop or art gallery on your way out…;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
15109;Cucina Mutualité;France;Paris;20 rue Saint-Victor, Paris, 75005, France;48.8484632;2.3508114;88;true;false;Italian;The colourful modern bistro decor and extremely cordial staff make for an appealing atmosphere. As for the food, the wonderful seasonal Italian menu is a pageant of authentic, flavourful and truly generous dishes: you won't be disappointed by the melt-in-the-mouth braised ox cheek paccheri... al dente, obviously! You may even be allowed a second helping.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15111;Chez Mathilde;France;Maxilly-sur-Léman;97 route de Lugrin, Maxilly-sur-Léman, 74500, France;46.3993735;6.6345198;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Mathilde is the daughter of the famous fisherman of Lake Geneva, Eric Jacquier. She is now established in this cheerful eatery in the heart of the village with a concrete counter, off-kilter lighting and light wood bistro furnishings. Her slate menu resembles her spontaneous, playful and intuitive personality!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15114;La Table de Michèle;France;Mulhouse;16 rue de Metz, Mulhouse, 68100, France;47.7480293;7.3430197;57;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Michèle Brouet is a figure on the local gastronomy scene. Her restaurant is the reflection of her generosity and cheer, as is the atmosphere, which is welcoming with its various random objects and bouquets of flowers. Good food and good times are on the menu!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15115;Le Goût du Jour;France;Avignon;20 rue Saint-Étienne, Avignon, 84000, France;43.950539;4.8043087;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Good ideas, know - how... Julien Chazal, a young chef from Avignon, shows us how it's done! Furthermore, his seasonal cooking is visually meticulous, with presentations that leave nothing to chance. And let's not forget the down - to - earth, smiling service.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15116;Les Sales Gosses;France;Toulouse;81 rue Riquet, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6061;1.45401;51;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Les Sales Gosses (naughty kids) chalks up its creative version of heart-warming bistro classics on large blackboards. The food is the work of chef Bruno, who is definitely top of the class! A great meal every time. And if it’s fully booked, there is now a Plan B: Le Bistrot, not far away, on Rue de l'Industrie.;Air conditioning;[]
15117;L'Ancolie;France;Rochefort-en-Terre;12 rue Saint-Michel, Rochefort-en-Terre, 56220, France;47.699175;-2.3352034;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Named after a pretty flower, this appealing restaurant successfully blends old stone with contemporary elegance. The fine cuisine errs towards traditional fare, eg crayfish tartare or scallops with vanilla-infused orange.;Wheelchair access;[]
15119;À la Maison;France;Plouguerneau;21 place de l'Europe, Plouguerneau, 29880, France;48.6068427;-4.5077886;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This house rustles up wholesome bistro fare that shines the limelight on regional produce. The chef particularly likes devising dishes around a single ingredient, such as pork or lamb. House specialties include black pudding, a 64° egg and Guéméné andouille. Well worth discovering.;Wheelchair access;[]
15120;Buerehiesel;France;Strasbourg;4 parc de l'Orangerie, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5914793;7.7753964;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This picturesque, half-timbered 17C farmhouse was reconstructed stone by stone in the Orangerie Park, next-door to the Council of Europe. The conservatory dining room and patio command a bucolic view of this leafy haven. The menu features some of the house signature dishes, such as frog’s legs sautéed in chervil or free-range pullet roasted in a casserole dish (backeoffe), together with more contemporary seasonal recipes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15122;Solides;France;Toulouse;38 rue des Polinaires, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.597942;1.444046;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant opposite the market stands out on account of its fine bistro food, delivered by a chef who is a proponent of short supply chains. It also boasts an excellent (and coherent) natural wine list. In a bohemian atmosphere, sample the house speciality: vol-au-vent with calf sweetbreads, cockerel combs and chicken sauce, as well as terrific cheeses from the region.;Air conditioning;[]
15123;Le Bistrot du Port;France;Golfe-Juan;53 avenue des Frères-Roustan, Golfe-Juan, 06220, France;43.56624;7.07552;92;false;true;Seafood;Opposite the old port, the chef-patron gives free rein to his abundant creativity and his passion for fish and seafood: the tasting menu ("Plongée en plusieurs paliers") is a veritable ode to the sea, with dishes such as sea urchins with grapefruit and spirulina served as a dessert. The produce is remarkably fresh, the cooking is skilful and the risk-taking is constant: this is a restaurant that stands out from the crowd!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15125;L'Empreinte;France;Tarbes;2 rue Gaston-Manent, Tarbes, 65000, France;43.2324664;0.070654;90;false;true;Creative;Solid oak tables, custom-made tableware and a warm welcome… This snug restaurant is the stomping ground of Manuel Godet, who harnesses his impeccable textbook skills to crafting creative recipes that shine the spotlight on local produce, sometimes with surprising twists. Examples include Pyrenean gravlax trout and whipped cream flavoured with locally brewed gin, or a kiwi from Adour with cocoa, buckwheat and truffles. Simple lunchtime menu, more ambitious in the evening.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15126;La Contre Allée;France;Paris;83 avenue Denfert-Rochereau, Paris, 75014, France;48.83595;2.3341897;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In an unassuming side road running parallel to Avenue Denfert-Rochereau, you can expect simple, deftly crafted market-fresh fare. Smart, pared-back interior with a casual vibe. Spot on every time.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15127;L'Instant Z;France;Le Thou;1 bis rue du Château-de-Cigogne, Le Thou, 17290, France;46.08486;-0.9244;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Z for Zanchetta, the chef's surname. Working with top-notch ingredients fresh from the market and small-scale, local organic farmers, he conjures up dishes with a mixture of influences and a weakness for game in season. Even better, the bread is baked on the premises! The recently revamped interior is casual and friendly with service to match: a real pleasure.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15128;Nous;France;Montauban;7 rue Bessières, Montauban, 82000, France;44.0169666;1.3578815;70;false;true;Contemporary;In this modern bistro overflowing in feel-good vibes, Raphaël and Elise Campas treat the foodies of Montauban to a culinary festival, all made in-house, from the bread to the ice cream. Taking their cue from the seasons, the experienced couple conscientiously selects regional ingredients (vegetables from independent market gardeners and farmstead cheeses), which the chef crafts into colourful, appetising dishes. Élise professionally and seamlessly manages the front of house, while Raphaël pops out from time to time to lend a hand and wax lyrical about his cooking. This excellent establishment, only open for lunch, offers a concise menu that changes monthly, giving you the perfect excuse to return again and again.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15129;Fleurs d'Olargues;France;Olargues;au Pont-du-Diable, Olargues, 34390, France;43.5569086;2.9108125;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Danish;It's a real family affair here at this attractive restaurant run by Danish chef Kasper and his wife Fé. The culinary programme comprises local ingredients, vegetables from the garden, foie gras and home-made bread (eg smørrebrød) and a scattering of subtle Nordic touches (salmon marinated in beetroot juice, hasselback potatoes). The bucolic terrace overlooks the 12C Pont du Diable ("Devil's Bridge") and the village, officially designated as one of the Plus Beaux Villages de France.;Great view,Terrace;[]
15130;Les Affranchis;France;Paris;5 rue Henri-Monnier, Paris, 75009, France;48.8794774;2.337034;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This young duo happily ignore the classics to create tasty cuisine, such as the œuf parfait façon carbonara ("perfect egg" with carbonara) or pollock with cauliflower, orange and botargo. An (excellent) place that is right at home in the bourgeois - bohemian 9th arrondissement.;;[]
15131;La Tour des Sens;France;Tencin;Route de Theys, Tencin, 38570, France;45.3135642;5.9660664;40;false;true;Creative;On the upper reaches of Tencin, this Tower is a treat for the five senses! Run by the same chef since 2016 (2017 Top Chef winner), his creative, natural menus aim to stimulate the taste buds of diners and thus call upon their emotions. When the weather’s fine, why not enjoy the fabulous view of the Chartreuse range from the terrace?;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15132;Charbon Kunitoraya;France;Paris;5 rue Villedo, Paris, 75001, France;48.86616;2.3362928;46;false;false;Yakitori, Japanese;Outside, the attractive timber façade has a Japanese feel. Inside, you'll find an old zinc counter, Paris Métro-style tiling, mirrors, wood panelling and mouldings, and two large bar tables built of solid wood. In this chic setting with a vintage feel, chef Nomoto – a pioneer of udon restaurants in France – serves up a range of top-notch yakitori, particularly chicken. Cordial, well-paced service.;Air conditioning;[]
15133;La Condesa;France;Paris;13 rue Rodier, Paris, 75009, France;48.8784538;2.3427703;100;false;false;Creative;La Condesa, a district of Mexico City, has lent its name to this restaurant run by Indra Carrillo. The Mexican-born chef came to study at the Lyfe (formerly Paul Bocuse) Institute, before working in top establishments such as Le Bristol and L'Astrance. Trained by MOF chefs, notably in fishmongery and bakery, he has also worked in Japan. Although his techniques are purebred Gallic, his inspiration is more multicultural than simply Mexican. A chic, pared-back vein depicts the interior.;Air conditioning;[]
15135;Les Résistants;France;Paris;16 rue du Château-d'Eau, Paris, 75010, France;48.8699714;2.3607033;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;These résistants believe that taste and traceability should be the backbone of all food. Indeed, the credo of owner, Florent Piard, is none other than "good food that respects natural cycles! " and he amply proves his case in this cheerful establishment. The concise menu changes daily in keeping with market availability and the prices are never outlandish. Natural wines bien sûr!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15136;Rouge Barre;France;Lille;50 rue de la Halle, Lille, 59000, France;50.6443571;3.0594017;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Vieux Lille, local man Steven Ramon confirms – after his Top Chef adventure in 2014 – that we should be counting on him in the future. A Ch'ti to the core, he concocts inspired and lively dishes that make the most of fine ingredients. The restaurant has a "rouge barre" interior (red brick and white stone). Irresistible!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15137;Drouant;France;Paris;16-18 place Gaillon, Paris, 75002, France;48.8687869;2.3343779;23;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;This iconic, yet resolutely sprightly restaurant provides the smart, elegant stage where the Goncourt and Renaudot Book Prizes have been awarded respectively since 1914 and 1926! After learning the ropes with legends such as Cyril Lignac and Yannick Alléno, gifted chef Romain Van Thienen rolls out a pedigree lineup of French classics, from vol-au-vent and sole meunière to last-minute steak tartare and the famous "madeleine de Proust". As you take a seat in the plush interior you can expect to taste beautifully crafted, flavoursome dishes whose ingredients are nothing if not fresh, served by a front-of-house team that is both on the ball and cheerful. The wine cellar boasts nearly 2000 references and a very respectable range of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
15138;L'Alexandrin;France;Lyon;83 rue Moncey, Lyon, 69003, France;45.7608621;4.8491809;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;L'Alexandrin combines originality with generosity, serving dishes made using fine, locally sourced produce. Each menu (vegetarian, revisited Lyon classics or pure creation) proposes a different take on the art of fine dining in an exclusive atmosphere. One novelty is the table d'hôte with four guests seated in the kitchen at the heart of the action!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15140;L'Écume Gourmande;France;Cercié;35 Grande-Rue, Cercié, 69220, France;46.1195957;4.6711828;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is the brainchild of a young chef with an enviable CV. His classical training shines through, albeit with an intelligent inventive twist, illustrated by his organic 64°C egg, duxelles of (minced) mushrooms, grated Beaufort, pecan nuts and an emulsion of cep oil, or a cappuccino of snails from Gilles Nesme. The glazed wine cellar is a treasure trove of affordable tipples.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15142;Éléonore;France;Monpazier;5 rue Saint-Pierre, Monpazier, 24540, France;44.6790879;0.8933932;23;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This elegant restaurant is housed in a pretty little château, which has the art of hospitality down to a T. The globetrotting chef welcomes you with a menu presented in two sections: one “classical” which features a traditional lineup, while the other is more “unusual” with creative twists.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15143;Le Paris;France;Le Touquet-Paris-Plage;88 rue de Metz, Le Touquet-Paris-Plage, 62520, France;50.5226584;1.5842982;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A few streets away from the seafront, this restaurant is in sync with the markets and seasons and very much appreciated by local gourmets! They know how to pull off happy marriages of flavours, as in the asparagus, egg, morels and pancetta, or the meagre with capers and spinach. Friendly welcome.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15144;Confins des Sens;France;Le Grand-Bornand;341 Le Villavit, Le Grand-Bornand, 74450, France;45.9391399;6.4216852;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The house speciality is a delicious muscat-flavoured foie gras soup with a confit of red onions and ‘cromesquis’. The chefs pay tribute to the region whilst respecting the seasons, illustrated by a velvety soup of green peas and an ice cream of fresh cow’s cheese flavoured with wild garlic. Other highlights include pork cheeks braised in a local red wine or free-range chicken wings stuffed with morels and flanked by “pressed” potatoes (finely sliced and stacked before being roasted). The terrace is glorious in the sunshine.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15146;La Table du Rouan;France;Gérardmer;2 boulevard de la Jamagne, Gérardmer, 88400, France;48.0729273;6.8703306;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;"Julien Jeanselme, a committed and welcoming chef, creates fresh and straightforward cuisine, whose regional roots do not preclude nods to other influences, especially Provence (he's a fan of fish soup), or tributes – here, to his great - grandfather, who was awarded a Michelin star... in 1936! – with the ""Ernest Jeanselme"" mountain terrine. A reliably good option. ";Wheelchair access;[]
15147;Les Pipelettes;France;Pau;3 rue Valéry-Meunier, Pau, 64000, France;43.2960392;-0.3663516;46;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Here, the delicious dishes are prepared according to the produce available at the market stalls and the harvests of some 30 farmers based near Pau. The chef does her job well, and her dishes are both sophisticated and delicious: beef ravioli with squash and yarrow, line-caught hake from Saint-Jean-de-Luz, or the goat's milk cream with vanilla and Landes raspberry. Set menus (without options) at lunch and dinner, but the value for money at this pleasant little bistro is excellent.;;[]
15148;Passerini;France;Paris;65 rue Traversière, Paris, 75012, France;48.8492204;2.3747359;54;false;false;Italian;In his convivial restaurant, Giovanni Passerini treats us to tasty, carefully prepared Italian dishes, such as his trippa alla romana, which could hardly be bettered. Here, it's all about the produce and authenticity: sharing plates are a house speciality, as is Black-Headed Manech suckling lamb or whole pigeon in two courses. This place is very popular, so be sure to book!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15149;Kigawa;France;Paris;186 rue du Château, Paris, 75014, France;48.8330662;2.3245251;74;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Kigawa is named after Michihiro Kigawa, the chef at this refreshingly simple restaurant. Buoyed by his experience in a French restaurant in Osaka, he now finds himself in Paris, delighting guests with classic French dishes such as pâté en croûte and roast pigeon.;Air conditioning;[]
15150;Le Pavillon Bleu;France;Olivet;315 rue de la Reine-Blanche, Olivet, 45160, France;47.8693;1.89302;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A "guinguette" atmosphere pervades this 1903 building on the bank of the Loiret, where you can sit on the terrace in the shade of old plane trees, right by the water's edge. Fun fact: the dining area is actually an old boathouse. As for the food, the techniques are deft and the seasonings balanced, making for tasty dishes.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15151;Ciasa Mia;France;Paris;19 rue Laplace, Paris, 75005, France;48.8474318;2.3469012;71;true;true;Italian;Originally from northern Italy (the Dolomites, to be precise), Francesca and Samuel Mocci like to highlight their culinary heritage, which proves to be as delicious as it is surprising. The dishes exude authenticity, as does the space, designed in a cosy little chalet spirit. An appealing place.;Interesting wine list;[]
15152;Aux Lyonnais;France;Paris;32 rue Saint-Marc, Paris, 75002, France;48.87076;2.33868;86;true;false;Lyonnaise;This bistro established in 1890 has a delightfully retro decor and serves delicious cuisine that explores Lyon's gastronomy in all its riches. The terrines, pike-perch quenelles with crayfish, and the chicken liver terrine vie with the specials chalked up on the slate, and the desserts are enough to awaken anyone's sweet tooth.;Air conditioning;[]
15153;Le Quincy;France;Paris;28 avenue Ledru-Rollin, Paris, 75012, France;48.8471183;2.3700395;66;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A cosy ambience prevails in this utterly timeless establishment, which was dominated by its larger-than-life boss, “Bobosse”, for so many years. Even though he doesn’t pop in quite so often anymore, his personality continues to underscore the DNA of this haunt of foodies. For fifty odd years, fine food lovers have been digging into wholehearted, rustic dishes from Berry or Ardèche. The chef scrimps neither on quality nor quantity when it comes to the house terrine of cabbage and garlic, poultry in cream or the rum-flavoured ice cream! An establishment whose existence is almost anachronistic in today’s restaurant universe.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
15154;L'Atelier de Joël Robuchon - St-Germain;France;Paris;5 rue de Montalembert, Paris, 75007, France;48.85681;2.3278568;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Bathed in a studied semi-darkness, two bars face each other around a central kitchen where the dishes are prepared under the gaze of the guests, seated on high stools at the counter. This "chic canteen" is a Western version of Japanese teppanyaki and sushi bars, with a menu that can be “tailored” into small portions and plates that boast superlative ingredients. Caviar on a soft-boiled hen’s egg and smoked salmon in puff pastry and the house staples, king crab ravioli, suckling lamb chops, Joël Robuchon's famous mashed potatoes...;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
15155;Le Domaine de Saint-Géry;France;Lascabanes;Le Domaine de Saint-Géry, Lascabanes, 46800, France;44.34349;1.30317;82;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Self - proclaimed ‘farmer - chef’, Patrick Duler does not mess around with the origin of his ingredients. Much of what is on your plate – ham from black pigs, truffles, foie gras – comes straight from his own fields! His simple, meticulous dishes reveal the soul of a truly passionate chef.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15156;Clover Grill;France;Paris;6 rue Bailleul, Paris, 75001, France;48.8610034;2.3417836;96;false;true;Grills;Mouthwatering dry - aged meats – Baltic black beef, Bavarian beef, Blonde d'Aquitaine, Black Angus – take pride of place in the window, drawing in diners keen to try them for themselves. From the starters to the desserts, everything is cooked over coals or roasted on a spit, giving the dining experience its own particular flavour. A great success.;Air conditioning;[]
15157;Néva Cuisine;France;Paris;2 rue de Berne, Paris, 75008, France;48.8800727;2.3240722;94;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The Neva is not only a river in Russia, but also the name of this restaurant, headed by Mexican chef Beatriz González, after completing stints in top establishments including Lucas Carton and La Grande Cascade. In a friendly, modern Parisian bistro setting, she conjures up modern, multi-facetted cuisine, illustrated by blow torch-seared foie gras, smoked eel and dashi stock, or skate meunière with spring vegetables and a gutsy aïoli. Everything tastes of something here.;Air conditioning;[]
15158;Le Duc;France;Paris;243 boulevard Raspail, Paris, 75014, France;48.8386602;2.3308865;77;true;true;Seafood;Despite being in the heart of the Left Bank, you would be forgiven for thinking you were in the cabin of a yacht packed with seafaring acolytes… The chef works with first-rate fish and seafood and is a consummate craftsman: tartare of langoustine with black lemon, sole meunière, lobster sautéed with orange, grilled John Dory… All aboard!;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
15159;Maison Daniel et Julia;France;La Seyne-sur-Mer;Route de Fabrégas, plage de Fabrégas, La Seyne-sur-Mer, 83500, France;43.0694233;5.871426;57;false;false;Seafood;Julia is the soul of this hundred-year-old institution nestling in a charming cove. On the patio shaded by tamarisk trees, you can enjoy bouillabaisse and grilled wild fish. On Sundays during the summer, their authentic whole fish barbecues are a hit!;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15161;Le Cornichon;France;Paris;34 rue Gassendi, Paris, 75014, France;48.8341702;2.3261818;47;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Armed with a CV that pulls no punches (Atelier Guy Martin, Lucas Carton, Grand Véfour), Sébastien Dagoneau has been working wonders since taking over Le Cornichon in January 2020. True to his word, he cooks up a fresh and tasty take on ingredient-led cuisine. This is as neo-bistro as it gets, with game in season and a fantastic list of organic and natural wines. Enjoy dishes such as beef chuck lasagne with sauce diable and a crunchy choux bun filled with a Bourbon vanilla cream.;;[]
15162;Le Petit Lucas;France;Paris;9 place de la Madeleine, Paris, 75008, France;48.86977;2.32346;62;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The bistro counterpart of Lucas Carton is accommodated on the first floor of the fine dining restaurant, in a space with a more low-key vibe (but with a view of the Église de la Madeleine). Chef Hugo Bourny's cuisine follows in the footsteps of fine French tradition (sole meunière, pâté en croute, chocolate mousse etc), thanks in particular to the quality of the ingredients used. The business menu, albeit without options, is a notable bargain in this upscale neighbourhood.;Air conditioning;[]
15163;La Régalade Saint-Honoré;France;Paris;106 rue Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75001, France;48.8616261;2.3417802;59;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Bruno Doucet regales foodies in the Halles neighbourhood with dishes that sing an ode to fresh market and country produce. After titillating your tastebuds with the chef's delicious terrine, dig into pan-fried snails, mushrooms and chorizo, followed by braised chuck steak with a bourguignon garnish or the “famous” rice pudding with a dairy caramel. Fine wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15164;Les Délices d'Aphrodite;France;Paris;4 rue de Candolle, Paris, 75005, France;48.8402584;2.3509393;67;true;true;Greek;In this charming tavern-style restaurant, you could be forgiven for thinking you are in Greece! Freshly made, sun-drenched dishes such as marinated peppers, spit-roasted leg of lamb on a skewer, etc., all prepared with top-notch ingredients.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15165;Amphitryon;France;Limoges;26 rue de la Boucherie, Limoges, 87000, France;45.8286771;1.257625;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This pretty half - timbered house in the heart of the picturesque "village" around rue de la Boucherie is now the fief of chef Olivier Polla. He proposes modern cuisine that lets the ingredients do the talking, such as langoustine and angel hair pasta, lièvre à la royale, raspberry croquant and milk bastilla. A treat for the taste buds.;Terrace;[]
15166;Château de Rochecotte;France;Saint-Patrice;43 rue Dorothée-de-Dino, Saint-Patrice, Saint-Patrice, 37130, France;47.2871745;0.3067195;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;Not far from the Bourgueil vineyards, this elegant château dating back to the Enlightenment is set in sumptuous grounds. In La Verrière with its contemporary decor and huge windows with views onto the greenery, or in the more classical dining area, enjoy fine dining-style cuisine, for instance, a fricassee of smoked eel in a Thai jus with lemongrass and coriander.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15167;Le Petit Saint Thomas;France;La Garnache;25 rue de Lattre de Tassigny, La Garnache, 85710, France;46.889416;-1.8336135;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This endearing family-run restaurant is popular with a crowd of locals. The chef, at the helm for over twenty years, painstakingly rustles up French staples, albeit with a tasty new twist and the odd hint of exoticism (curry, sobrassada, nori, mafé, coconut).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15168;Atmosphère;France;Chamonix-Mont-Blanc;123 place Balmat, Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, 74400, France;45.9231828;6.8698599;54;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Go up the splendid granite staircase, dripping with flowers and plants, to the entrance of this establishment with atmosphere by the bucketload. The pared-down, alpine interior sports a friendly, casual vibe. Should you be given the choice, ask for a table in the conservatory, which commands a knock-out view of the Arve River and the peaks of Chamonix in the distance! Recipes as Gallic as La Marseillaise, regional specialities and game in season take pride of place on the menu. Splendid wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15169;Au Carillon Gourmand;France;Châlons-en-Champagne;15 bis place Monseigneur-Tissier, Châlons-en-Champagne, 51000, France;48.9571947;4.3648401;89;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this smart, elegant restaurant, dotted with designer touches and a subtle industrial loft vibe, diners can expect finely crafted, exquisitely presented modern dishes (carpaccio of gilthead seabream and medley of carrots). Warm welcome, swish service and fine tableware.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15170;Le Collet;France;Col de la Schlucht;9937 route de Colmar, Col de la Schlucht, 88400, France;48.0541926;7.0050189;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;“Instinctive, last-minute” regional dishes, rustled up by a seasoned veteran who has trained many a local chef. In a picture postcard swish Alpine chalet décor, each dish celebrates and pays tribute to authentic regional produce.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15171;L'Atelier des Saveurs by Stéphane Garcia;France;La Colle-sur-Loup;51 rue Georges-Clemenceau, La Colle-sur-Loup, 06480, France;43.6870911;7.1015674;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Fruit and veg from local producers, fish from local fishermen, meat from Southwest France and a knockout selection of Basque cheeses: the “flavour workshop” is fully equal to its name! Examples include a ballotine of Gers poultry stuffed with truffles and hazelnuts with green asparagus from St-Paul-de-Vence… A 100% Basque menu is available to order, in tribute to the youthful chef’s roots.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15173;L'Astrolabe;France;La Rochelle;35 rue Gambetta, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1618497;-1.147941;58;true;false;Fusion;An astrolabe is a disc-shaped astronomical instrument that was used to calculate longitudes and latitudes, and this restaurant transports you from one country to another (from Finland to Guatemala) and from one cuisine to another. Each dish is depicted by a fusion of world culinary traditions, as is exemplified by the mohinga of line-caught whiting. A journey to be savoured in a bright, pleasant interior with a buzzy chic bistro vibe.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15174;Le Vioben;France;Landéda;30 Ar Palud, Landéda, 29870, France;48.5959192;-4.560557;64;true;false;Seafood;Fish from small fishing boats, lobster and seafood, and, more generally, gourmet cuisine which highlights the fine local produce. It is not difficult to see why this establishment is such a hit with the locals, who also appreciate its warm contemporary décor, trendy light fixtures and the friendly, casual vibe.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15175;Maison de Laveline;France;Ban-de-Laveline;5 rue du 8-Mai, Ban-de-Laveline, 88520, France;48.24272;7.06545;99;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This rustic Vosges inn, depicted by a spruce yellow facade, is run by a youthful couple. The accent is clearly on wholesome French country fare and theme dinners based on a seasonal ingredient are organised throughout the year. Heart-warming dishes, such as melt-in-the-mouth veal chop and asparagus risotto. Meals are served in the recently refurbished dining room or on the patio in fine weather.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15176;La Table by La Villa;France;Calvi;Chemin Notre-Dame-de-la-Serra, Calvi, 20260, France;42.5555312;8.7454817;16;false;false;Modern Cuisine;La Table is part of La Villa, the luxurious decor of which is subjugated by the majesty of the panoramic view – the bay, the citadel, the mountains. It cultivates the beauties of the island, and quality regional produce… to sample on the superb panoramic terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15177;L'Arbre;France;Gruson;1 pavé Jean-Marie-Leblanc, Gruson, 59152, France;50.5899122;3.2299859;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This red-brick restaurant is located along the route of the legendary Paris-Roubaix cycling race and serves flavoursome food that makes perfect sense. The committed young chef prepares a surprise set menu featuring seasonal and local ingredients in well-crafted dishes, such as line-caught sea bass with broccoli and a creamed fish fumet – delicious and impressive! A pleasant terrace for fine weather.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15179;La Fleur de Sel;France;Cevins;15 route du Portelin, Cevins, 73730, France;45.5895069;6.4527942;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This modern building en route to the ski resorts serves appetising seasonal cuisine made with quality ingredients comprising regularly changing menus. The interior is modern and cosy, with as a focal point the lovely fireplace crackling in the middle of the room. Delightful.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15180;Le Bistrot;France;Chalon-sur-Saône;31 rue de Strasbourg, Chalon-sur-Saône, 71100, France;46.7797087;4.860917;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On Île St Laurent, a contemporary restaurant offering a well-crafted lunchtime menu at prices that make sense. For example, warm mushroom mousse with vin jaune and a creamy Mont d’Or cheese topping. The evening menu is more elaborate (foie gras, turbot, lobster). Some of the super fresh vegetables and fruit come from the kitchen garden.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15181;Restaurant du Port;France;Locquirec;5 place du Port, Locquirec, 29241, France;48.69118;-3.647035;52;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;After a walk around the headland, where the pretty beaches are too many to count, head to the little port. At the restaurant, tuck into the catch of the day, turbot fillet, oysters from Sterec, or the lovely sole meunière, which the chef, a pro who has worked under chefs Michel Trama and Stéphane Carrade, complements with a bowl of new potatoes, fine green asparagus, snow peas and confit red pepper. Pleasantly informal atmosphere.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15182;Marnage - Hôtel La Marine;France;Barneville-Carteret;11 rue de Paris, Barneville-Carteret, 50270, France;49.3773468;-1.7859611;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With its panoramic view of the sea and the port, this local institution on the Cotentin peninsula faces the Channel Islands of Jersey and Guernsey. In a pleasant contemporary interior, you will sample modern, elegant cuisine that shines the limelight on Normandy produce, with a weakness for local seafood, illustrated by pollock, fennel (confit and roasted) and a lemon-flavoured butter emulsion.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15184;La Table du Marché;France;Bergerac;21 place Louis-de-la-Bardonnie, Bergerac, 24100, France;44.8521501;0.4840139;75;true;false;Creative;Owner-chef Stéphane Cuzin has been at the helm of this street corner bistro with a distinctive red façade and a snazzy, modish interior for many years now. It faces Bergerac’s covered market, where Stéphane sources the majority of his ingredients. Creative recipes and unusual seasonings set the tone: tonka, nutmeg, cumin and coffee may underscore veal, spinach or asparagus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15187;Auberge de Cassagne & Spa;France;Le Pontet;450 allée de Cassagne, Le Pontet, 84130, France;43.9608889;4.8742537;25;true;true;Provençal, Classic Cuisine;This old Provençal bastide on the outskirts of Avignon upholds the traditions of Gallic bourgeois establishments devoted to good food. Noble produce and classical recipes are the name of the game, albeit with the occasional more modern creation, such as tataki of house smoked salmon on a pannacotta of green vegetables. Southern Côte du Rhône wines take pride of place in the cellar. Lovely terrace in fine weather and polished service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15188;La Bastide;France;Barbotan-les-Thermes;Avenue des Thermes, Barbotan-les-Thermes, 32150, France;43.9519064;-0.0442725;55;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the small spa village of Cazaubon, this swanky 5-star Relais & Chateaux hotel, owned by the Guérard family, has been refurbished in a tasteful chic country house vein. The chef crafts a score founded on the classical, dietary recipes invented by the late Michel Guérard: the food is light, healthy, modern and overwhelmingly mouthwatering and each dish is generously laden in first-class, locally sourced seasonal produce, all of which is consummately crafted. Spot-on service and a swish, tasteful setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15189;Blisss;France;Mérignac;98 avenue de Magudas, Mérignac, 33700, France;44.8568699;-0.6584981;62;false;false;Creative;In the suburbs just outside Bordeaux, this modern restaurant proves to be a wonderful surprise. It has an intimate and immaculate decor featuring made-to-measure furniture and crockery that matches the ethos expressed in the food. Let Anthony Aycaguer transport you with his interactive menus, presented as a series of riddles based on seasonal produce (diners have to guess the ingredients). An unusual experience! Booking is essential.;Air conditioning;[]
15190;Le Coq d'Or;France;Chénérailles;7 place du Champ-de-Foire, Chénérailles, 23130, France;46.1116433;2.1771463;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;‘The Golden Cockerel’ is aptly named: the interior is full of the birds – brought back by customers from their travels! As for the food, expect an array of fine, well - crafted dishes that offer a creative take on local specialities.;Wheelchair access;[]
15191;Les Années 30;France;Chinon;73 rue Haute Saint-Maurice, Chinon, 37500, France;47.1671306;0.2358278;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant may be named after the 1930s but that's where the connection to that period ends. The decor is chic and trendy, with walls in hues of terracotta and verdigris and retro dining chairs. Diners will love the appetising cuisine based on fresh ingredients. Tables on the terrace in fine weather.;Terrace;[]
15192;Le Vieux Moulin;France;Chabanais;Étang du Bouchaud, Chabanais, 16150, France;45.8798019;0.7409922;42;true;true;Farm to table;This restaurant housed in an old mill sports a cheerful interior and a splendid fireplace for cosy winter moments. In summer, the riverside terrace is the perfect spot to dig into appetising, market-fresh food, whose original and well-crafted recipes focus on locally sourced produce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15193;Le 5ème Péché;France;Collioure;16 rue de la Fraternité, Collioure, 66190, France;42.5273486;3.0832819;72;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant in Collioure's old town is run by a chef from Tokyo, who is passionate about French food and wine. Here, Japan meets Catalonia in fusion cuisine that stars ultra-fresh fish. A prime example is the rockfish soup with coconut milk, braised ox cheek with banyuls and prawns. Remember to book well in advance.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15194;A Nepita;France;Ajaccio;4 rue San-Lazaro, Ajaccio, 20000, France;41.9250662;8.7373676;75;true;false;Farm to table;English born chef Simon Andrews, a former Michelin star holder, fell head over heels with Corsica. He goes to the market every day to painstakingly select local ingredients, which he then meticulously crafts: red tuna, denti, seabass, brocciu, veal, etc. Some of his signature dishes are always on the menu, such as grilled squid or his medley of local fish, to the delight of regulars and tourists alike. The chef also enjoys scattering his dishes with wild marjoram (“nepita”, after which the restaurant is named). The cheerful front-of-house service is managed by Simon’s wife, Corsican born Roberta.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15195;L'Estellan;France;Lorgues;1000 route de Saint-Antonin, Lorgues, 83510, France;43.49784;6.34034;78;true;true;Farm to table;Amid vineyards and olive groves, it is difficult not to fall in love with this inviting country house. The staff bends over backwards to make sure your stay is relaxing and that you really take your time. Run by a couple with an extensive catering career already under their belt, they know what they want and how to get there: first-class, regional produce, modern, flavoursome recipes and a concise, mouth-watering slate menu, illustrated by rack of farm-reared pork and butter of cèpe mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15196;Le Martin Pêcheur;France;Ay-sur-Moselle;1 route d'Hagondange, Ay-sur-Moselle, 57300, France;49.2496028;6.1834297;46;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Between the Canal des Mines de Fer de la Moselle and the Moselle, this former fisherman's house (1928) exudes the appealing spirit of a country inn and is embellished with a pretty summer garden. Here, tradition mingles with modern trends, and the cellar is well stocked.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15197;1217;France;Bagnols;Château de Bagnols, Le Bourg, Bagnols, 69620, France;45.9165715;4.6083417;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This superb medieval château seems bent on upholding the opulent traditions of banquets of yore… Take a seat by the imposing, delicately carved Gothic fireplace and dig into a feast of infinite refinement. The strawberry-rhubarb dessert is to die for: crunchy strawberry topping, savory-flavoured pannacotta and fresh strawberry purée with a rhubarb sorbet. Wickedly tempting!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15198;Le San Felice;France;Le Castellet;3001 route des Hauts-du-Camp, au Circuit Paul Ricard, Le Castellet, 83330, France;43.2502745;5.7834947;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine;San Felice is not only a Dumas novel: at the Hôtel du Castellet, it is also a swish, imaginative bistro! The menu is deliberately concise, with a seasonal line-up and a mouth-watering focus on matured meats and fish cooked over hot embers. The terrace by the swimming pool commands a drop-dead view of the golf course and greenery. Treat yourself to the lunchtime ‘Gourmand’ menu (Mon to Sat).;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15199;Au Lavoir;France;Colombiers;Rue du Lavoir, Colombiers, 34440, France;43.3153568;3.1380897;32;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Adjacent to the Canal du Midi, this lovely yellow building seems to shine, especially when the lush green garden (with terrace) is bathed in sunlight. Fully inspired by the Mediterranean, the cooking lets the ingredients enjoy the limelight and exudes the flavours of the South of France. Do not hesitate to book one of the elegant guestrooms upstairs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
15200;Le Lancelot;France;Chilleurs-aux-Bois;12 rue des Déportés, Chilleurs-aux-Bois, 45170, France;48.0711488;2.1349334;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the centre of the village, this welcoming flower-decked place with a garden and terrace is a real oasis of calm. Cosy setting and cuisine that navigates between tradition and modernity (notably the melt-in-the-mouth pithivier pie, rum crème brûlée, pistachio ice cream), not forgetting Sologne game in season.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15202;Ko-sometsuke 2K;France;Arcachon;156 boulevard de la Plage, Arcachon, 33120, France;44.662095;-1.1587375;40;true;false;Asian;Originally from Cambodia, the Khong family settled in Arcachon, and now they are the ones inviting diners on a journey: from China and Japan to Southeast Asia, using regional ingredients. Don't miss the dim sum, the real stars of the show, wrapped in a remarkably fine dough.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15203;La Table du Lavoir - Les Sources de Caudalie;France;Martillac;Chemin de Smith-Haut-Lafitte, Martillac, 33650, France;44.7310722;-0.5569478;56;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;When you take a seat in this unabashedly rustic, yet plush establishment, you are reminded of the region’s rich heritage – the winegrowers’ wives used to wash their clothes in the old stone sink that stands in the centre of this reconstructed 18C hall. The menu is accordingly traditional and wholesome: grilled free-range breast of chicken, crunchy potatoes, trompette mushrooms and bearnaise sauce. The epitome of a spruce, country inn of yesteryear, with the bonus of cheerful waiting staff. Even better, it is possible to taste the wines of the property, which is none other than Château Smith Haut Lafitte (also available by the glass)!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15204;L'Aspérule;France;Auxerre;34 rue du Pont, Auxerre, 89000, France;47.7944642;3.574239;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Sited in an old house in historic Auxerre, the dining room sports a minimalist look with a polished concrete floor and beige walls. The Japanese chef crafts cuisine that pairs local produce with the millimetric accuracy of his homeland, depicted by perfectly rare duckling fillet, duxelles of shiitake mushrooms, balsamic sauce. Sensibly priced lunchtime market menu, more ambitious in the evening.;Air conditioning;[]
15205;Loiseau des Vignes;France;Beaune;31 rue Maufoux, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0226424;4.8345945;39;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A Bernard Loiseau stamped score and a chic bistro vibe (stone, wood and velvet-upholstered banquettes) paint this culinary portrait. The menu includes classics such as eggs in a red wine sauce, pâté en croûte, Charolais ox cheek and Saône catfish, without forgetting beautifully fresh Burgundy veal tartare with smoked eel. The splendid wine list also unveils a wide range of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15206;Le Pérou;France;Saint-Béron;341 rue Jules-Ferry, Saint-Béron, 73520, France;45.5003128;5.7293386;96;true;true;Peruvian;Pulpo anticuchero, lomo saltado, tiradito, arroz cremoso, and, of course, the indispensable ceviches: all the classics of Peruvian cooking are on the menu here in the Alps, thanks to a chef and her team, who all hail from Peru. Much of the produce is imported direct from the Andes, via Spain. Anyone who has been lucky enough to taste authentic South American food will be delighted by the incredible range of flavours and tastes of this cuisine rich in seasoning and unexpected ingredients on offer.;;[]
15207;Le 180°;France;Port-Goulphar;Castel Clara, Port-Goulphar, 56360, France;47.306673;-3.2247159;54;true;true;Creative;The name is an expression used in Belle - Isle - en - Mer to refer to the indefinable colour of the sea... Indeed this would be just the spot to discuss its nuances: the dining area affords breathtaking views over Goulphar cove! At the helm, the chef concocts original recipes using the best ingredients the island has to offer. Enjoy the crossing!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15208;Le Chardenoux;France;Paris;1 rue Jules-Vallès, Paris, 75011, France;48.8527452;2.3850308;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;In this Parisian bistro founded by the Chardenoux family and a listed historic monument, the eye wanders from the beautiful painted ceiling to the Art nouveau details, before it is drawn back to the business at hand, the enticing menu in front of us. Fish and seafood are the name of the game here, including Lignac’s iconic signature dishes: lobster roll, salt-crusted sea bass, tuna tartar, avocado, ponzu, wasabi, without forgetting the decadent millefeuille or the rum baba! We fell in love with the crunchy savoury pancake of curry-flavoured crab and avocado: a masterpiece of balanced flavours.;;[]
15209;Le Bistrot Flaubert;France;Paris;10 rue Gustave-Flaubert, Paris, 75017, France;48.8814358;2.2986644;43;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Abutting its parent establishment, Maison Rostang, this Parisian eatery has been an iconic feature of its neighbourhood for several decades, rolling out well-crafted, big-boned dishes. This authentic bistro, which is as popular with politicians as with businesspeople, sports rows of wooden shelves lined with bottles of wine and a few vintage Michelin guides! Formerly of Contraste, chef Erwan Ledru signs a modern score in tune with the seasons, adding a new twist to satisfying Gallic staples, such as a spicy jus that adds a kick to corn-fed duck from Landes, cooked whole.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15210;Auberge de l'Abbaye;France;Villemagne-l'Argentière;4 place de l'Abbaye, Villemagne-l'Argentière, 34600, France;43.6178;3.1187024;95;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A small medieval village. Tucked away from view, a 12C tower casts a shadow onto a stone wall, and behind this wall you come across this charming inn, which is certainly worth getting to know! Here they serve good traditional food that is at one with the monastic atmosphere of the place, all vaulted ceilings and stone walls.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15212;La Ferme Saint-Sébastien;France;Charroux;Chemin de Bourion, Charroux, 03140, France;46.186364;3.1580868;87;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This authentic mid-19C Bourbon farmhouse, next to the fortified city of Charroux, is a pleasant spot to sit down and enjoy the simple dishes concocted by the owner, especially on sunny days on the terrace. Diners appreciate the contemporary cuisine, palpably influenced by the terroir, such as the zucchini fritters with chives sauce. A good place.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15213;L'Îlot Vert;France;Boulogne-sur-Mer;36 rue de Lille, Boulogne-sur-Mer, 62200, France;50.72517;1.61436;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, which feels like a smart bistro, ticks all the boxes. Here, Tony Regnier, who trained at some prestigious establishments, conjures up really modern cuisine with creative touches, flawlessly executed and flavoursome, to be savoured in a tastefully decorated room, or on the pretty flower-filled terrace. The guinea fowl and pistachio terrine served with apple chutney left a lasting impression!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15214;Le Voilier;France;Bonifacio;81 quai Comparetti, Bonifacio, 20169, France;41.3880853;9.162304;65;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Drop anchor in the marina and climb on board this elegant yacht to sample fresh Mediterranean cuisine (fish soup and carpaccio, ceviche, courgette blossoms) in which the local catch (whole or in portions) takes pride of place. Meat lovers are, however, not forgotten and the menu also offers dishes such as a thick juicy veal cutlet or stuffed saddle of lamb.;Terrace;[]
15215;Le Cromesquis;France;Aurillac;1 rue du Salut, Aurillac, 15000, France;44.9294;2.44591;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;After an impressive career working in Michelin - starred restaurants in Switzerland, the chef has returned home, to his wife's region. In an unusual setting – a former forge that has been refurbished with a lot of wood, concrete and picture windows –, he proposes modern and delicious dishes with, of course, a cromesquis (croquette) featuring every day among the starters.;Terrace;[]
15216;Fouquet's;France;La Baule;Le Royal La Baule, 6 avenue Pierre-Loti, La Baule, 44500, France;47.2819003;-2.4052282;40;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A restaurant in the Royal Hotel, typical of the large seaside hotels of the early 20C. The cosy wood panelling and the photos of actors by Studio Harcourt recall the atmosphere of the Parisian Fouquet's. The menu is inspired by brasserie fare (seafood, sole meunière, fillet of beef with Béarnaise sauce, andouillette, profiteroles), but there are also light dishes – as you would expect at a seawater therapy resort.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15217;La Source des Sens;France;Morsbronn-les-Bains;19 route d'Haguenau, Morsbronn-les-Bains, 67360, France;48.9036;7.74702;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The setting is strikingly contemporary, with black walls and carpeting and atmospheric lighting. The food is equally up-to-date, thanks to the commitment of chef Pierre Weller, who slips in the odd tribute to Japan’s culinary culture, while excelling in the art of precise plating, demonstrated by his arctic char makis with green asparagus, orange foam and pistou. The Source also proposes guestrooms for overnight stays, together with a luxurious spa to pamper your senses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15218;La Marmite du Pêcheur;France;Les Mées;Boulevard des Tilleuls, Les Mées, 04190, France;44.0304661;5.9796881;98;false;false;Seafood;This restaurant, a former mill, stands at the foot of the village’s iconic pointed rock formation. It serves fish and seafood specialities (bouillabaisse to order). The interior sports a modern vibe, offset by an old mill wheel that adds a characterful note to the décor.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15219;Influences;France;Bordeaux;36 rue Saint-Sernin, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8406341;-0.5823087;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A wind of revival is blowing through this venerable institution, which has changed hands but not name and is still located in a quiet street near Place Gambetta. The handsome sandstone façade now ushers guests into the lair of a youthful couple, cheerful Kéveena, in the front of house and Ismaël who gives free rein to his solid background in the kitchen. Modern, tasty dishes which mainly star ingredients from southwest France, jazzed up with the odd creative twist, like a grilled duck magret, punchy gravy and Japanese-style lacquered aubergine sprinkled in puffed rice. Seamless, smiling service.;Air conditioning;[]
15220;La Charrette Bleue;France;Condorcet;5 chemin Barjavel, Condorcet, 26110, France;44.3859981;5.195536;70;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;You can't miss this 18C coaching inn with its blue cart on the roof, in a nod to René Barjavel's eponymous book in which he recounts his childhood in this part of the world. The spirit of the region is everywhere, from the terrace shaded by a reed canopy to the generous regional cuisine, examples of which are a terrine of marbled ham, warm potato salad with a spicy ravigote sauce and a decadent île flottante (egg whites in custard) in a culinary lineup as patriotic as the Marseillaise!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
15222;Pianovins;France;Paris;46 rue Trousseau, Paris, 75011, France;48.8525915;2.379178;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Both formerly of the Guy Savoy, Michel Roncière and Éric Mancio have joined forces: the first in the kitchen, the second in the wine cellar. The menu is well designed and prepared according to market availability. Meals are served in a small dining room (20 seats at tightly packed tables) with an open kitchen and counter dining.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15223;L'Assaggio;France;Paris;Castille Paris, 37 rue Cambon, Paris, 75001, France;48.8685903;2.3270701;72;true;true;Italian;Assaggio is all about taste! Chef Ugo Alciati (of Guido Ristorante, in Piedmont) devised the menu for this elegant restaurant in the Hôtel Castille. As expected, Northern Italy takes pride of place in the dishes – house-made agnolotti, risotto minute... The pastas are quite something: the spaghettone with lobster, lemon zest, confit tomatoes and trout roe is absolutely delicious. Tables are laid out in the delightful interior patio adorned with a fountain and frescoes.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15225;Nestou;France;Marseille;43 rue de Suez, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2912438;5.356693;58;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Just a few strokes from Catalans beach, this restaurant pays homage to Ernest (Nestou), the young son of Jean-Philippe and Jeanne Garbin, who are the joint chefs of this endearing family establishment. He supervises the hot dishes, while she is in charge of the starters and desserts and together, they devise unusual recipes that surf between Mediterranean influences and more globetrotting inspirations. A great place for a meal with the mates!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15227;Symbiose;France;Epernay;5 rue de Reims, Epernay, 51200, France;49.0448366;3.9600871;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Modern and skilfully balanced cuisine, with creative touches and a predilection for spices, not to mention neat presentations: this is what Symbiose has in store for you. The couple who run the show know where they're going and are delighting in the journey.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15228;Juste à Côté;France;Saint-Romain-de-Colbosc;18 avenue du Maréchal-de-Lattre-de-Tassigny, Saint-Romain-de-Colbosc, 76430, France;49.5313832;0.3495294;69;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Simplicity is a central tenet of this former roadside eatery transformed into a bistro by chef Olivier Foulon, assisted on the restaurant floor by his wife Amandine and a team of efficient, smiling servers. Though classic, the menu – pâté en croûte, monkfish à l'armoricaine and riz au lait – changes daily to cater to a large clientele of lunchtime regulars.;;[]
15231;Le Doyenné;France;Saint-Vrain;5 rue Saint-Antoine, Saint-Vrain, 91770, France;48.5375413;2.3259764;98;true;true;Modern Cuisine;What are two Australian chefs (with stints at Yard, Spring, Bones and Au Passage) doing in the heart of the grounds of Saint Vrain Castle, more precisely in the tastefully refurbished former stables? Well, they are knocking up spot-on food that is sourced directly from the estate’s huge cottage garden, which actually existed before the restaurant, using fruit and vegetables that are only harvested when perfectly ripe. A fine dining experience that mingles rural charm and gourmet delights, overlooking the surrounding countryside. Booking compulsory.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
15232;Jardin Secret;France;Cotignac;13 rue de l'Araignée, Cotignac, 83570, France;43.5271329;6.1488922;53;true;false;Provençal;Back from the rock of Monaco, Benoît Witz has hung his hat in a pretty estate in Provence. In the shade of olive groves and released from gastronomic codes, he crafts 100% authentic dishes in a style that he himself joyfully describes as “grandma’s country cooking”! Garden-fresh beefsteak tomatoes, fish of the day with summer veggies, melt-in-the-mouth chocolate cake. Scrumptious and generous – yummy!;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15233;L'Hermine;France;Morlaix;35 rue Ange-de-Guernisac, Morlaix, 29600, France;48.5787172;-3.827863;27;false;true;Breton;This very pleasant crêperie in a picturesque pedestrian area has wooden beams, polished wooden tables and rustic objects. Choose from some 50 savoury buckwheat and sweet pancakes.;Terrace;[]
15234;Le Manoir des Impressionnistes;France;Honfleur;23 route de Trouville, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.4242524;0.214308;26;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Settle in at your table, in the bright dining room or on sunny days head for the terrace to enjoy the lovely view of the estuary. Savour the modern cuisine, centred on a short and appetising seasonal menu that gives top billing to Normandy's produce from land and sea.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15235;Entre Terre et Mer;France;Honfleur;12/14 place Hamelin, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.4216041;0.2331065;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;On Place Hamelin, in Honfleur's historical quarter, this restaurant is accommodated in the house that is said to be the 1768 birthplace of JFE Hamelin, a rear admiral in Napoleon Bonaparte's navy. The space – typical of Normandy, with its half-timbered walls and exposed stonework – is the perfect place in which to sample seasonal dishes that embrace both meat and fish (as the name suggests). The roast sea bream, herb jus, beans and redcurrants are steamed to perfection and beautifully presented. Small terrace for fine weather.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15236;Bistrot Instinct;France;Paris;19 rue de Picardie, Paris, 75003, France;48.8637583;2.3626181;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This pocket handkerchief contemporary bistro is in the hands of chef Maximilian Wollek and his enthusiastic youthful team. A market-fresh culinary score and updated classics with bistronomic overtones. Everything is homemade, even the cordials used in the unusual cocktails.;Terrace;[]
15238;Le Turenne;France;Beaulieu-sur-Dordogne;1 boulevard Saint-Rodolphe-de-Turenne, Beaulieu-sur-Dordogne, 19120, France;44.9787356;1.8383361;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Modern cuisine is served in this restaurant that combines original stone walls with contemporary design. On fine days the gorgeous terrace adds to the gourmet experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15239;L'Écusson;France;Beaune;2 rue du Lieutenant-Dupuis, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0196976;4.8442702;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Proudly flying the fine dining flag, the chef, who trained in prestigious establishments (La Côte Saint-Jacques, Lameloise and La Pyramide), crafts a fresh, colourful score that is often jazzed up with citrus fruits. The result is often inspired, illustrated by langoustine and tourteau crab, leeks, buckwheat, watercress and smoked yoghurt or scallops, Belgian endive, salsify and clementines… Meals are served in a bright, contemporary interior.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15240;Jòia par Hélène Darroze;France;Paris;39 rue des Jeûneurs, Paris, 75002, France;48.869805;2.34329;80;true;true;Cuisine from South West France;Hélène Darroze's restaurant draws on her memories of her native southwestern corner of France, with nods to the Basque Country, Landes and Béarn. Strong flavours and emblematic dishes (chipirones from Saint-Jean de Luz fried with chorizo, Carnaroli rice with squid ink, parsley and parmesan emulsion), to be enjoyed alone or to share, and desserts that awaken your sweet tooth (chocolate chou with Espelette chilli, peanut praline).;Brunch,Counter dining;[]
15241;Gaya - Cuisine de Bords de Mer par Pierre Gagnaire;France;Châtelaillon-Plage;Avenue de la Falaise, Châtelaillon-Plage, 17340, France;46.0581127;-1.0878834;41;true;true;Creative;Part of La Grande Terrasse Hotel and not far from Les Boucholeurs, chef Pierre Gagnaire’s free-spirited culinary vision, which is local and comprised of surf and turf ingredients, combines blessed familiarity with flawless execution. Elegant recipes and consummately crafted jus, sauces and cremes, embodied by a pearlescent acidic orange and curcuma jus that adds a kick to flawlessly fresh wild turbot. The stonking wine bin boasts some 700 labels. Swish service and a cosy interior that commands a knockout view of the ocean.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15243;La Table du Centenaire;France;Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil;2 avenue du Cingle, Les Eyzies-de-Tayac-Sireuil, 24620, France;44.9344866;1.0156594;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Previously an oyster farmer working in the Bassin d'Arcachon, chef Mathieu Métifet draws his inspiration from the Périgord terroir, weaving in fish and seafood elements to create generous, personal cuisine, of which his signature dish is a good example: "Le Centenaire's unmissable razor clams with a morel cream and home-smoked magret de canard". Hand-picked small-scale local producers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15244;Le Dallaison;France;Saintes;30 rue du Bois-Taillis, Saintes, 17100, France;45.7405948;-0.6121804;33;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The beautiful exterior of this 18C manor house set in grounds gives little away. Inside, the 21C makes itself felt throughout the various dining nooks: designer furniture, original lights, white walls, wine cabinets. A place like this can only inspire Jérôme Dallet, a chef who has worked with Emmanuel Renaut (Megève) and Anne-Sophie Pic (Valence). Local produce is given pride of place (mogette beans, snails, Confolens lamb…) and the chef uses it to create wonderfully indulgent compositions. In fine weather, you can enjoy the terrace surrounded by greenery.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15245;Dante;France;Paris;14 rue de Paradis, Paris, 75010, France;48.8747273;2.3541018;84;false;true;Modern Cuisine;After a period of purgatory, this hip establishment in Rue de Paradis is back in favour thanks to an enthusiastic young chef who fell in love with haute cuisine after an internship with Alain Passard. Rébecca Beaufour consummately crafts fiendishly flavoursome bistronomic dishes, such as lobster and king prawn ravioles or crisp sweetbread served with squash and apple caramel. The house also offers a range of dishes to share, like pigeon or whole seabream cooked in salt.;Wheelchair access;[]
15246;Bord'eau;France;Colmar;17 rue de la Poissonnerie, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0740962;7.3587483;18;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This spinoff by two-star chef Jean-Yves Schillinger is located next to the Lauch River in the heart of Little Venice. The menu allows the chef to express his creativity in recipes that blend Asian traditions with local Alsace produce. Carrots roasted in hay, herby snail fritters and salted kumquats, or pollock with pumpkin purée, maki of vegetables and yuzu gel. Contemporary decor.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15247;Martin Comptoir;France;Limoges;13 rue Lansecot, Limoges, 87000, France;45.8291425;1.2571973;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A stone’s throw from the market (ideal for fresh produce), the clientele is drawn by the work of youthful chef, Martin Dumas, also a local lad. His culinary score, perfectly in tune with today’s tastes, features a brief seasonal menu, generous hunks of meat to be shared and the house speciality, “thickly sliced calf’s liver”, which he learnt from Jean-Paul Arabian in Paris. Small, quiet terrace.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
15248;Jeff envoie du bois !!!;France;Auch;12 place de la Libération, Auch, 32000, France;43.6469229;0.5842626;45;false;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Fresh ingredients sourced from the market where the Chef goes twice a week, a spacious terrace on Place de la Libération, a tasteful, elegant exterior, a black and white interior décor and up-to-the-minute market-fresh cuisine. The overwhelming popularity of this canteen-cum-bistro is further reinforced by a fine selection of local vintages.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15249;Les Magnolias;France;Le Perreux-sur-Marne;48 avenue de Bry, Le Perreux-sur-Marne, 94170, France;48.8352952;2.497831;34;true;true;Creative;A young chef is now at the helm of this pleasant restaurant. He pays particular attention to the presentation of his dishes, which are full of flavour and strewn with Asian influences. In the kitchen and the elegant dining room, his young team pulls out all the stops to please.;Air conditioning;[]
15251;Monsieur Bleu;France;Paris;20 avenue de New-York, Paris, 75016, France;48.863834;2.296578;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;For a location in Paris, it would be hard to do better than this address... Nestled in the Palais de Tokyo, it is superb with its Art Deco interior in a palette of grey, green and gold, and its terrace looking out over the Seine and the Eiffel Tower. Not to be outdone by the setting, the food is sophisticated and tasty. A very high - profile place!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15252;La Poule au Pot;France;Paris;9 rue Vauvilliers, Paris, 75001, France;48.8616966;2.3432641;43;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The great classics of the French culinary repertoire are given an overhaul here by Jean-François Piège. Service on a silver tray, old-fashioned bistro decor, zinc counter: it has all the trappings. It's Audiard's Paris down to a T... right down to the food: onion gratinée, quenelle of arctic char, beef chuck hash, Colbert fried whiting with tartar sauce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15253;La Fourchette du Printemps;France;Paris;30 rue du Printemps, Paris, 75017, France;48.8877235;2.3102526;42;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this elegant little neighbourhood bistro, the young chef has come through some top establishments. He hones the taste of quality ingredients (the menu evolves according to the market), and takes pleasure in revisiting the classics. A good place.;Air conditioning;[]
15254;L'Agapé Bistrot;France;Guérande;11 faubourg Saint-Michel, Guérande, 44350, France;47.326952;-2.426238;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Just a stone's throw from Guérande's famous fortified wall, this family-run bistro with a sober contemporary decor serves appetising cuisine that combines regional ingredients (catch of the day, seaweed, pork, butter milk, buckwheat) with more exotic touches (spices, ginger, lemongrass, coconut etc). The resulting dishes are hearty, meticulous and balanced: quite a feast!;;[]
15255;La Table d'Émilie;France;Viuz-en-Sallaz;1069 avenue de Savoie, Viuz-en-Sallaz, 74250, France;46.1480606;6.4103996;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At the helm of this friendly restaurant, Émilie and Yoann showcase first-rate produce in the form of a market-fresh set menu that offers excellent value for money at lunchtime and sets its sights higher in the evening. The chef has a sure touch, especially when it comes to desserts. In fine weather, head for the pleasant garden terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15256;Café des Ministères;France;Paris;83 rue de l'Université, Paris, 75007, France;48.8606833;2.3191495;97;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The name of this bistro that is reminiscent of a neighbourhood café is on the lips of every fan of wonderfully rich sauces and authentic French cuisine (especially South-Western fare). The vol-au-vent with sweetbreads, poultry and truffle jus, as well as the stuffed Pontoise cabbage (French champion in 2022) have put this place on the map: book in advance!;Air conditioning;[]
15257;La Table du Caviste Bio;France;Paris;55 rue de Prony, Paris, 75017, France;48.8824081;2.303991;67;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A few well - polished, leather footfalls from Parc Monceau and you are in this stylish restaurant combining a modern dining room and food that is in tune with current tastes, fresh and subtle, concocted by Japanese culinary artist, Junko Kawasaki. The matching wines are naturally organic.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15258;La Passerelle;France;Bricqueville-sur-Mer;113 route du Havre-de-la-Vanlée, Bricqueville-sur-Mer, 50290, France;48.9139737;-1.5443565;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It was love at first sight when the chef, who hails from Orléans, saw this restaurant located on the edge of Le Havre de la Vanlée, which offers an ideal landscape for walks among the salt meadow sheep. Now well established, it serves contemporary market cuisine that is fresh and tasty, for example the monkfish, chorizo and leek. A pleasant place.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
15259;Bouche B;France;Bezannes;9 rue Jean-Dausset, Bezannes, 51430, France;49.2144;4.0033959;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The Bouche B on the "Place Gourmande" of this village near Reims is the HQ of chef Thibault Laplaige (previously Michelin starred in Reims). His modern, well-crafted dishes rely on top-drawer produce such as tartare of scallops and fennel with soy vinaigrette or braised Black Angus in a sort of “applejack” jus with buttered green cabbage. Bouche B for "Bon"!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15260;Blanc;France;Marigny-Saint-Marcel;90 avenue Sindeldorf, Marigny-Saint-Marcel, 74150, France;45.82931;5.98463;20;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This family inn features two enticing options: an elegant, contemporary restaurant, with a well-designed menu based on fine ingredients, or the chalet-inspired wooden interior of the brasserie, where Savoie cheese specialities take pride of place (alongside frogs' legs and pike). Comfortable guestrooms, for those who wish to stay longer the region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15262;Amapola Kitchen;France;Albi;100 rue Porta, Albi, 81000, France;43.93202;2.14407;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The superlative location, at the foot of Pont Vieux overlooking the historic town and its stunning cathedral, is definitely Instagram worthy. This cleverly revamped pocket handkerchief bistro is in the hands of a former art historian, whose healthy, colourful, well-crafted dishes to be shared hit the spot every time. This unorthodox, fine food DJ mixes South American, Italian and Comorian influences, with a generous scattering of lacto fermented ingredients and a definite preference for organic sources, such as the Comorian-style minced beef flanked by red onion and chervil pickles and the delicious house houmous. Fine selection of organic and natural wines.;Terrace;[]
15263;Olivier Leflaive;France;Puligny-Montrachet;10 place du Monument, Puligny-Montrachet, 21190, France;46.9464333;4.7538105;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A plush house in the centre of the village, a glass-paned wine cellar, a bar with an Art Deco look, a chic and inviting dining room: welcome to Olivier Leflaive's place! The famous Côte de Beaune winegrower has created two eateries. Le Bistro d'Olivier offers a seasonal menu inspired by local produce, and the restaurant Klima has more fine dining ambitions. Great wine list, needless to say, thanks to the estate's 80 appellations.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15266;La Corniche - Sainte-Barbe;France;Le Conquet;Pointe Sainte-Barbe, Le Conquet, 29217, France;48.3587203;-4.7800138;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Sainte Barbe Hotel offers a choice of Instagrammable views looking out to sea or of the harbour. La Corniche sports and elegant contemporary vibe. Finely crafted cuisine, recipes of bistronomic inspiration with a distinct preference for local fish and seafood. The rooftop bar is heaven for a drink before or after dinner.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15267;La Gare;France;Guewenheim;2 rue Soppe, Guewenheim, 68116, France;47.7492648;7.0923371;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A very contemporary local institution (since 1874)! It has a perfect combination of elegance, vitality and conviviality, offering a brasserie for those in a hurry or carefully-prepared modern cuisine in a conservatory setting... Goat’s cheese and vegetable terrine, or thick veal chop with morel mushrooms and gnocchi, all accompanied by one of the finest wine lists in the country.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15268;Au Déjeuner de Sousceyrac;France;Sousceyrac-en-Quercy;2 allée Gaston-Monnerville, Sousceyrac-en-Quercy, 46190, France;44.8727764;2.0360174;21;true;false;Classic Cuisine;A chef dedicated to his craft, Patrick Lagnès draws on solid classical foundations and fine produce to deliver high-quality cuisine. He even tries out a few more contemporary dishes when the inspiration takes him, while desserts are the work of his daughter. Diners are served in the intimate setting of a small dining area done out in traditional style with wainscoting and period furnishings.;;[]
15269;Umami - La Cinquième Saveur;France;Montpellier;15 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.61193;3.87361;37;false;true;Korean;Not even a stone’s throw from Place de la Canourgue, this small bistro with a minimalist interior invites you to sample the chef’s French-Korean cuisine, dotted with Japanese notes. This talented chef works exclusively with fresh produce, changes the menu every couple of months (except for classics such as the bibimbap) and, of course, shines the spotlight on umami flavours, illustrated by chawanmushi, an egg and shrimp flan with edamame and a dashi stock. Bookings essential.;;[]
15270;Le Christine;France;Paris;1 rue Christine, Paris, 75006, France;48.8544233;2.3400955;72;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In a quiet little street, you will spot the inviting façade of this restaurant, where the conviviality and generosity are first apparent on the (short and appetising) menu, then in the nicely crafted dishes, which always include a vegetarian option. Thank you, Christine, and see you soon.;Air conditioning;[]
15271;Le Bon Saint-Pourçain;France;Paris;10 bis rue Servandoni, Paris, 75006, France;48.850192;2.3347169;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away behind St Sulpice church in the heart of the high - brow Saint Germain des Prés district, this former 'bougnat' restaurant reopened in the spring of 2015. Bistro traditions with a modern twist depict the delicious food – doubtless due to the high quality fresh produce. Booking advisable!;Terrace;[]
15272;ASPIC;France;Paris;24 rue Louise-Émilie-de-la-Tour-d'Auvergne, Paris, 75009, France;48.8791753;2.3436245;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;After ditching the world of finance to enrol in the Ferrandi Culinary School, the chef went on to hone his skills in a variety of establishments (including the French Ministry of Foreign Affairs and L'Épi Dupin). He then went it alone and opened this restaurant. With its vintage vibe and open kitchen, the chef devises a surprise set menu that is unabashedly creative and showcases carefully selected ingredients: free-range meat and poultry, line-caught fish from small boat fishing, citrus fruits, herbs and spices, all sourced as locally as possible.;Air conditioning;[]
15273;Shirvan Café Métisse;France;Paris;5 place de l'Alma, Paris, 75008, France;48.8650379;2.3013985;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant near Pont de l'Alma is the brainchild of Akrame Benallal. Starched white linen has given way to designer cutlery and, first and foremost, a menu inspired by the Silk Road from Morocco to India via Azerbaijan. A delicious melting pot seasoned with a wealth of spices, as in the vegetarian tikki or the confit lamb chops with home-made harissa... Efficient service and you can eat at almost any time of the day.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15274;La Cuisine d'Amélie;France;Lauris;Domaine de Fontenille, route de Roquefraiche, Lauris, 84360, France;43.7627568;5.301305;22;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The Domaine de Fontenille's restaurant serves pleasant Mediterranean cuisine from a menu that changes with the seasons, as well as an appealing lunch set menu. As you sit on the superb terrace overlooking the grounds, be sure to try the estate's organic wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15275;La Cuisine du Cloître;France;Limoges;6 rue des Allois, Limoges, 87000, France;45.8295093;1.2657419;31;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At the foot of the cathedral, this former 17C cloister is the quintessence of characterful! The chef’s market-fresh cuisine varies with his mood (surprise menus) and the season. His consummate technique and the quality of the ingredients hit the spot every time for a fine dining experience.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15276;Odette;France;Paris;25 rue du Pont-Neuf, Paris, 75001, France;48.8607301;2.3445353;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Two steps from Les Halles, in the luxurious Albar Hotel, the Rostang family demonstrates that they haven’t lost their touch in this urban inn. Odette regales us with dishes to be shared: sea bass in a pastry crust, one of the house’s signature dishes, veal chops, roast guinea fowl. Each dish showcases the chef’s hallmark talent.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15277;Le Petit Kembs;France;Kembs;49 rue du Maréchal-Foch, Kembs, 68680, France;47.686775;7.503926;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This pretty half-timbered village house is home to a 5-table only dining room, with colourful walls and an open kitchen. Here, the chef is in charge of everything, from the food (modern, carefully-prepared, tasty) to…the service ! The approach is heartfelt and demands respect. On the plate, seasonal, local, often organic produce, with delicious bread from a local baker.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15278;Au Sourd;France;Toulon;10 rue Molière, Toulon, 83000, France;43.1244087;5.9328858;62;false;false;Seafood;A true Toulon institution, created by an artilleryman of Napoleon III, who went deaf while fighting, as referenced in the name. You can't really argue with what the chef offers: his cooking draws whole shoals of fish-lovers (bouillabaisse and bourride made to order, fried red mullet, rainbow wrasse, sole etc, depending on the catch) in a chic and contemporary atmosphere.;Terrace;[]
15280;Les P'tits Fayots;France;Toulouse;8 rue de l'Esquile, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.6063633;1.4418642;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A cosy, stylish restaurant on two levels serving modern and creative dishes, in which organic produce, particularly vegetables, from the Gers takes pride of place. The owner - chef is committed heart and soul to his culinary creations and business.;Air conditioning;[]
15281;La Table du Clos;France;Thiers;49 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Thiers, 63300, France;45.84207;3.5097;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the way out of town, this eatery combines a peaceful, secluded setting with a modern, brasserie score. The dessert of green apple on a vanilla ganache with apples in a butterscotch sauce, for example, is heavenly! Pleasant terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15282;La Table d'Emilie;France;Marseillan;8 place Carnot, Marseillan, 34340, France;43.35598;3.528355;84;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The house where the poet Achille Maffre de Baugé was born is home to this very popular restaurant: the delicious and meticulous cuisine is anchored in French tradition (the pâté en croûte is excellent!). Made using fresh produce, this is particularly artfully plated food. To be enjoyed in a dining space with a vaulted ceiling or out on the pleasant patio.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15283;Le Cotte Rôti;France;Paris;1 rue de Cotte, Paris, 75012, France;48.8482152;2.3767504;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant made very much in the image of the friendly, exuberant chef , who brings a touch of finesse to bistro tradition: depending on the market and the mood of the day, he composes delicious, indulgent dishes that hit the mark! Memories of the slow-cooked egg with leek, Morteau sausage and hollandaise sauce. And there's nothing like a few Rhône Valley wines to accompany the food.;;[]
15285;Le Petit Gourmand;France;Tarbes;62 avenue Bertrand-Barère, Tarbes, 65000, France;43.23785;0.07112;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Near the city centre, this vintage bistro is now the lair of Mathieu Espagnacq, who has taken over from his father, who opened the establishment back in the eighties. Mathieu, a seasoned chef with stints in Paris working with top chefs under his belt, crafts food in the zeitgeist that respects tradition and stars premium country produce (farm-reared pork cheeks braised in red wine, vegetables confit in thyme and gnocchi in a smoky cream sauce). A treat for your tastebuds from start to finish – remember to book!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15287;L'Apibo;France;Paris;31 rue Tiquetonne, Paris, 75002, France;48.8647345;2.3475169;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In his small bistro in the Montorgueil neighbourhood (hushed atmosphere, oak floorboards, exposed stone), Antony Boucher, a chef with a strong track record, creates beautifully original and delicate cuisine that fêtes ingredients. He is renowned for his two classics: filet of sea bass, black rice and paprika sauce and the eight-hour confit pork with sweet potato mousseline. The laid-back (and very professional) service evokes the rough and ready spirit that used to characterise Les Halles.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15288;Boutary;France;Paris;25 rue Mazarine, Paris, 75006, France;48.8549073;2.3379513;49;true;true;Creative;The ideal place to discover or brush up on your caviar know-how (osetra, sterlet and baeri), as the owners have been raising sturgeon in southern Bulgaria for several generations. The plush smart interior and the chef’s “carte blanche” menus, with a traditional tasting session served on the back of the hand, are very popular.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15289;Sagan;France;Paris;8 rue Casimir-Delavigne, Paris, 75006, France;48.8501505;2.3390856;47;false;true;Japanese;A stone’s throw from the historic Odéon Theatre, this pocket handkerchief restaurant serves inventive, razor-sharp Japanese food: sashimi of semi-cooked salmon and caviar, miso soup with sake marinated clams. The wine list is a treasure trove of Bordeaux and Burgundies. Served with a smile in a hushed, cosy interior.;Interesting wine list;[]
15290;Bistrot Marloe;France;Paris;12 rue du Commandant-Rivière, Paris, 75008, France;48.8727045;2.3083732;97;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this upscale neighbourhood, on the corner of two pretty streets, Marloe has a chic and cosy bistro vibe and its popularity reaches beyond the neighbourhood. Indeed, the food, made with high-quality ingredients, is deft and unfussy. It is delicious, especially the "black truffle" menu (in season).;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
15291;Chante Bise;France;Seychalles;Lieu-dit Courcourt, Seychalles, 63190, France;45.8059866;3.317799;58;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Despite the whimsical reference to one of La Fontaine’s parables (The ant and the grasshopper), this restaurant is the antithesis of scarcity in terms of fine produce! Discerning local food lovers flock here to sample big-boned Gallic staples (7-hour shoulder of lamb, served with gravy, mashed potatoes and olives and a gutsy ratatouille garnish). The pedigree lineup of French family favourites is occasionally jazzed up with the odd more contemporary note. Friendly vibe and a lunch set menu at unbeatable value.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15292;Tosca;France;Paris;18 rue du Cirque, Paris, 75008, France;48.8710947;2.3155562;35;false;false;Italian;Italy seems to have converged on this small-capacity, smartly furnished restaurant. The food is an ode to Italian gastronomy, showcasing its meat, olive oil, cheese… Classical at lunchtime, more elaborate, and often inspired, at dinner. The Splendide Royal Hotel (formerly Pierre Cardin’s home) offers swish, elegant suites.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15293;Le Quai des Saveurs;France;Les Sables-d'Olonne;8 place de Strasbourg, Les Sables-d'Olonne, 85100, France;46.4908383;-1.772796;24;false;true;Creative;You can expect a warm welcome with the bonus of a sea view from Estelle and Maxime Dourdin. The chef, formerly of establishments of the calibre of the Four Seasons George V in Paris, signs a single set menu that changes frequently depending on market availability. Unusual, well-crafted dishes in the zeitgeist, such as mussels in white wine, jalapeno sauce, fermented milk and herb-flavoured tapioca.;Air conditioning;[]
15294;La Charrue;France;Sand;4 rue du 1er-Décembre, Sand, 67230, France;48.3817611;7.6145041;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of a two-centuries-old edifice, Nicolas Laurent (who trained in places such as the Chambard, the Auberge de l’Ill and the Vieux Couvent) offers contemporary cooking highlighting the region (eel from the Rhine, local game), along with “noble” produce (Cotentin lobster, wild turbot etc.). Regulars will be happy to note that the carp fillets, with fries and Alsatian horseradish cream, remain on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15295;La Table de Pierre;France;Saint-Paul-de-Vence;2320 route des Serres, Saint-Paul-de-Vence, 06570, France;43.6829022;7.1244509;66;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Le Mas de Pierre has morphed into a sublime, intimate and luxurious resort... and La Table has followed suit. The pair of chefs cooks up modern and locavore Mediterranean cuisine, with subtle international influences. Perfectly cooked and seasoned, there is an overarching harmony to it all: very nicely done.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15296;La Courtille de Solutré;France;Solutré-Pouilly;Route de la Roche, Solutré-Pouilly, 71960, France;46.2965326;4.7243008;40;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A pretty country house, its charming terrace in the shade of an old chestnut tree... and a dynamic Basque chef, who puts passion and good - quality ingredients into his cooking, nicely accompanied by a fine selection of Pouilly - Fuissé wines! There is a handful of guestrooms.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15297;La Ponche;France;Saint-Tropez;5 rue des Remparts, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2733601;6.6410327;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Thomas Danigo (formerly of the Galanga in Paris) signs the menu of this emblematic Saint-Tropez restaurant, located in the eponymous district facing the sea. The cuisine is Mediterranean, giving pride of place to the catch of the day and vegetables from the region, alongside premium joints of meat. The memory of his ceviche of seabream, citrus fruits and coriander-basil sorbet and the dessert of roasted figs with apple and myrtle balsamic, almond crumble and pistachio ice cream lingers with us still.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15299;Les 110 de Taillevent;France;Paris;195 rue du Faubourg-Saint-Honoré, Paris, 75008, France;48.8759171;2.3030348;46;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Under the aegis of the prestigious Taillevent name, this ultra - chic brasserie puts the onus on food and wine pairings. The concept is a success, with its remarkable choice of 110 wines by the glass, and nicely done traditional food (pâté en croûte, bavette steak with a peppercorn sauce etc). Elegant and inviting decor.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15300;Chez Michel;France;Paris;10 rue de Belzunce, Paris, 75010, France;48.8795815;2.3522586;94;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Since 2015, Japanese chef Masahiro Kawai has been in charge of the kitchens at this restaurant steeped in history. He draws on his experience in Japan, Spain and France (working with Yves Camdeborde and Christian Etchebest) to create traditional yet cheerful bistro cuisine, in which seafood ingredients play a key role. The classics are present and correct – roast foie gras, game in season – the flavours are delicious and the cooking is precise, particularly in the case of the grilled mackerel, ratatouille and pistou.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15301;Court La Vigne;France;Lavaudieu;Le Bourg, Lavaudieu, 43100, France;45.2620661;3.4540549;62;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Head for the medieval cloister: this charming 15C sheepfold is just a stone's throw away. The bar and its fireplace, the art gallery and the courtyard are all very pleasant features. Local organic wines are served with the unpretentious local cuisine.;;[]
15302;Zen;France;Paris;8 rue de l'Échelle, Paris, 75001, France;48.8641048;2.3346748;36;true;true;Japanese;This enticing restaurant combines a refreshing contemporary interior design and authentic Japanese cooking. The menu is well - rounded and faithful to the classic sushi, grilled dishes and tempura, with house specialities of gyoza and chirashi. Ideal for a quick lunch or a relaxing ‘zen’ dinner.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15303;Le Val d'Auge;France;Bondues;805 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Bondues, 59910, France;50.7003027;3.0944903;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;It may have an exterior that is typical of northern France, with its white bricks and eaves, small window panes and black surrounds, but this restaurant actually has a smart contemporary interior. Chef Christophe Hagnerelle is a true craftsman, who creates unfussy seasonal cuisine. The menu features excellent fish and shellfish from the North Sea, including turbot, sea bass or John Dory, depending on the catch of the day, but also scallops, as well as grouse and hare à la royale in season, veal sweetbreads and pigeon – from Flanders, of course.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
15305;Bloempot;France;Lille;22 rue des Bouchers, Lille, 59000, France;50.6381816;3.0582578;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Florent Ladeyn, a great defender of his region's terroir, is at the helm of this self-professed "Flemish canteen". An atypical setting (once a carpentry workshop), good natural ingredients and original recipes – refreshing! There is no telephone here: reservations are made through the website or in person.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15306;Restaurant Le Dalí;France;Paris;Le Meurice, 228 rue de Rivoli, Paris, 75001, France;48.8652168;2.3279642;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The second restaurant of Le Meurice, located at the centre of the action at the luxury hotel, is a place to meet and to enjoy appealing seasonal cuisine peppered with understated Mediterranean touches, as well as the great classics associated with luxury hotel dining. The beautiful decor – pilasters and mirrors – pays tribute to Dalí, who was a regular patron.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15307;Baffo;France;Paris;12 rue Pecquay, Paris, 75004, France;48.8602089;2.3562719;95;true;true;Italian;Originally from southern Tuscany, cooking enthusiast Fabien Zannier pays tribute to the flavours of his childhood in this small, colourful Italian restaurant that packs a tasty punch. Fresh organic ingredients, often sourced directly from the producer (arborio rice, Colonnata bacon, artisanal pasta from Pitigliano). Unusual antipasti, set menus for sharing (on seafood or truffle themes) and a cellar stocked in great Italian wines – just the place for a "pranzo con i baffi" – a meal so good, you’ll want to lick your whiskers!;Air conditioning;[]
15309;Au Fil du Zinc;France;Chablis;18 rue des Moulins, Chablis, 89800, France;47.81624;3.8008264;98;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Mathieu Sagardoytho, the new owner-chef of the Zinc, signs a creative menu that pays tribute to painstakingly sourced ingredients (mackerel from Trinité-sur-Mer marinated in mirin, lamb from Clavisy farm, plums from Yonne). Remarkable list of Chablis (and other Burgundies).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15310;Le Petit Henri;France;L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue;Grand Hôtel Henri, 1 cours René-Char, L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue, 84800, France;43.9191882;5.0560516;21;true;true;Provençal;The restaurant of the Grand Hôtel Henri is in the extension just off the main hotel building. It has a beautiful decor with a fireplace dating back a century and sparkling chandeliers. There is a terrace shaded by mulberry plane trees with a fountain, as well as lovely seasonal cuisine with a focus on regional flavours. Very good value for money at lunch;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15312;Villa Saint-Antoine;France;Clisson;8 rue Saint-Antoine, Clisson, 44190, France;47.0870879;-1.2787088;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a former textile mill on the banks of the Sèvre Nantaise, diners can enjoy a smart brasserie interior (red velvour banquette seating, bay windows) and the chef's delicious repertoire of dishes, which are full of flavour and lovingly prepared. Last but not least, service courtesy of a young and dynamic team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15314;Auberge de la Diligence;France;Loiré;4 rue de la Libération, Loiré, 49440, France;47.6145334;-0.9804741;23;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Something of a local culinary landmark, this delightful inn marries old stones with a tasteful makeover. Tania Cudraz cheerfully escorts you to your seat where you will sample the handiwork of her hubbie, Michel. The veteran chef’s varied, individual repertory is scattered with herbs from their kitchen garden and spices discovered on their numerous trips to distant lands, Asia in particular. The stonking wine bin boasts over 400 references. The enchanting terrace is set in the inner courtyard of this former post house.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15315;Les Servages;France;Les Carroz-d'Arâches;841 route des Servages, Les Carroz-d'Arâches, 74300, France;46.02073;6.64361;80;false;false;Modern Cuisine;One thing is sure, the chef loves what he does, and this passion is contagious. He creates food that is contemporary, meticulous and generous with superb quality ingredients such as fresh fish and seafood. His John Dory fillets and squid cooked à la plancha are just one delicious example of his dishes.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15316;L'An Faim;France;Bonifacio;7 montée Rastello, Bonifacio, 20169, France;41.3878684;9.1615592;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant is located at the end of the marina, by the stairs that go up to the citadel. Boasting a terrace, it is a favourite with regulars, attracted by the menu bursting with colourful, flavoursome market-fresh cuisine, including Corsican veal and prawns, pastilla of suckling lamb from Bonifacio, and blanquette-style dentex and vegetables. At lunchtime there is a simpler set menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15317;Allard;France;Paris;41 rue Saint-André-des-Arts, Paris, 75006, France;48.85331;2.34096;76;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of bustling Saint Germain des Près, this authentic Parisian bistro, dripping in charm and now part of the Ducasse empire, has changed very little since it opened in 1932. The culinary score wavers between bistro fare and heroic brasserie staples: snails in parsley, butter and garlic, pâté en croûte, sole meunière, profiteroles. Attractive lunchtime menu.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
15318;Tavline;France;Paris;25 rue du Roi-de-Sicile, Paris, 75004, France;48.8564098;2.3575124;33;true;false;Israeli;Between Saint-Paul and Hôtel de Ville, a slice of Tel Aviv, a taste of Morocco, a hint of Lebanon – such is the formula of Tavline. Spices supplied by Shuk Ha'Carmel, the largest market in Tel Aviv, adorn the fine cuisine served here, including ksitsot daguim – grilled fish balls with herbs and spices on a bed of lentils with yoghurt and candied lemon, or the memorable memoulam (onions stuffed with lamb), a recipe passed down to the chef from his mother.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15319;La Balade des Saveurs;France;L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue;3 quai Jean-Jaurès, L'Isle-sur-la-Sorgue, 84800, France;43.919797;5.054997;44;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant young couple – Benjamin and Sophie Fabre – run this spruce and stylish restaurant, which boasts a terrace running alongside the picturesque River Sorgue. The dishes manage to encapsulate and convey both the character and the sweetness of Provence.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15320;Yen;France;Paris;22 rue Saint-Benoît, Paris, 75006, France;48.85457;2.33272;80;false;true;Japanese;The highly refined Japanese decor in this restaurant will appeal to fans of the minimalist look. The menu showcases the chef’s speciality, soba – buckwheat noodles served hot or cold and prepared in front of you.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15321;La Table du Mas;France;Joucas;Lieu-dit-Toron (route de Murs), Joucas, 84220, France;43.9347215;5.2426319;72;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Grilled sea bass, artichoke barigoule and summer truffle: the cuisine here puts a clever spin on the classics of Provence. The Mediterranean soul expresses itself as much in the dishes as on the large terrace overlooking the countryside.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15322;Restaurant Bonnet;France;Itxassou;Place du Fronton, Itxassou, 64250, France;43.332422;-1.41105;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Beñat Bonnet represents the third generation at the helm of this family-run restaurant, whose reputation is well established in the region. Local ingredients are celebrated in contemporary-style cuisine, with dishes such as Baigorry trout gravlax and braised veal with cep and chorizo viennoise sauce. For dessert, try the coconut finger sorbet, as crisp as it is refreshing!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15323;Chai l'amère Kolette;France;Kervignac;Parc d'activités de Kernours, Kervignac, 56700, France;47.7568166;-3.2859187;39;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Between Hennebont and Port-Louis, this house, set in a small commercial district, is definitely worth a visit. In the kitchen, visible from the airy, tastefully appointed dining room, the chef concocts market-fresh recipes, whilst adding distinctive personal touches.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15324;Le Saint Lazare;France;L'Abergement-Clémenciat;19 route de la Fontaine, L'Abergement-Clémenciat, 01400, France;46.1515267;4.920207;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;On the high street of a Dombes village, this establishment has been in the family since 1899! Nowadays, father and son cook together, crafting an inventive "carte blanche" mystery menu of elaborate dishes based on good, fresh ingredients. Meals are served in the low-key, stylish dining room or on the summer patio.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15325;La Grange;France;Cholet;64 rue de Saint-Antoine, Cholet, 49300, France;47.05023;-0.90803;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Wood sets the scene, including in the imposing feeding trough - this isolated old farmstead is proud of its rural vibe. A few modern details do however contrast with the initial portrait, starting with stylised photos, a glazed wine cellar and the smoked black glass service area. In the same vein, Christian Gingreau rolls out a modern score founded on tradition. The menu is concise and enticing: beef tartare, 30-day aged on the bone rib of beef, whole sole meunière, wild seabass and a new take on paella.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15326;Le Café de la Fontaine;France;Joucas;Le Phébus, route de Murs, Joucas, 84220, France;43.9290776;5.2560407;83;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;The menu of this Café features a seasonal repertory with Mediterranean influences (Roussillon asparagus, Ventoux pork chop, aïoli of salted whiting) and recipes that are reminiscent of the summer holidays (salade niçoise, club sandwich). Simple, no-nonsense nosh served by a fountain overlooking the swimming pool.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15327;Le Bistrot;France;Chambéry;6 rue du Théâtre, Chambéry, 73000, France;45.565573;5.9241142;100;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;On the menu of this bistro near the theatre and the cathedral, you will find hearty Gallic seasonal recipes, starring fine ingredients that shout their name. The Savoie-born chef worked for a long time in Ducasse establishments. In fine weather, meals are served on a shaded terrace, which further increases the pleasure.;Terrace;[]
15328;ME.;France;Limoux;1 place du Général-Leclerc, Limoux, 11300, France;43.0533672;2.2161365;46;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is ensconced in the Grand Hôtel Moderne et Pigeon, a former monastery dating back to the early 16C. With a superb 17C stained-glass window, the place has undeniable cachet. With its elegant patio, it has the feel of a bohemian bistro. Chef Stéphane Castaing is as creative as ever: salmon gravlax on tomato panna cotta, fillet of beef with black garlic and vegetable condiment... Laid-back friendly service.;Terrace;[]
15329;Auberge de la Fontaine du Berger;France;Orcines;167 route de Limoges, Orcines, 63870, France;45.7997168;2.991897;33;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;On a minor road linking Clermont to the motorway, this red-shuttered country inn built out of volcanic stone overlooks the authentic, preserved countryside of the Puy de Dôme and Pariou. Tuck into a tasty, traditional Gallic lineup, assembled with top-drawer ingredients such as seared scallops from Erquy, Belgian endive and pleurote mushrooms in vin jaune, or ham stuffed with free-range chicken. Don’t even try to resist the wickedly tempting home-made Paris-Brest pastry for dessert. A friendly greeting and lovely rustic interior set the scene in this warm, inviting establishment.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15330;L'En-but;France;Clermont-Ferrand;107 avenue de la République, Clermont-Ferrand, 63000, France;45.7887179;3.1059478;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The set menus, which are modern and shine the spotlight on local ingredients from the Massif Central, of this restaurant inside the Marcel Michelin rugby stadium, are named after the game's terminology (forward pass, grand slam and backhand spin). Designed in the spirit of a contemporary brasserie, the dining area commands a breathtaking view over the stadium and, from the terrace, over the Puys mountains.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15332;I Salti;France;Speloncato;au golf du Reginu - Moulin de Salti, Speloncato, 20226, France;42.6038961;8.9773613;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;In the Reginu valley, next to the golf course, this pretty little restaurant housed in a converted mill enjoys a bucolic setting and outdoor café garden vibe. The delicious menu is the culmination of the finest ingredients of the Balagne region (local fish, organic vegetables). The prawn arancini, cold bisque and snow peas is a particularly fond memory. A warm welcome and a really charming setting, far from all the hustle and bustle: a firm favourite.;Terrace;[]
15333;Le Jardin;France;Bormes-les-Mimosas;1 ruelle du Moulin, Bormes-les-Mimosas, 83230, France;43.1514365;6.3424702;19;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in a picturesque little street in the old part of the village, this small restaurant initially charms you with its rustic appeal and delightful terrace, complete with fountain and pergola, and surrounded by greenery and flowers. In the kitchen, Riccardo Berto sprinkles his colourful Mediterranean dishes with Peruvian touches, informed by his experience as chef at L'Altiplano in Val d'Isère. One example would be the amberjack ceviche enhanced by an invigorating leche de tigre with peach and crispy corn. A truly enjoyable experience.;Terrace;[]
15334;Auberge de l'Espérance;France;Le Buisson-de-Cadouin;3 avenue des Sycomores, Le Buisson-de-Cadouin, 24480, France;44.8465544;0.9126812;83;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Desperate souls should rush to this restaurant that offers hope! The owner extends a warm and smiling welcome, and there is lots of attention to detail in the food, which combines freshness and taste. A reminder that it can be the simple pleasures that leave the deepest impression.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15335;Le Yachtman;France;Lorient;14 rue Poissonnière, Lorient, 56100, France;47.7463281;-3.3589898;34;false;false;Seafood;Unsurprisingly, seafood – in particular fish from the local auction – takes pride of place in this pretty restaurant located close to the marina. Simplicity and accuracy reign on the plate, while the dining area has a minimalist and intimate decor.;Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15336;Da Passano;France;Bonifacio;53 quai Comparetti, Bonifacio, 20169, France;41.3879569;9.1637204;39;false;true;Corsican;Overlooking the port, this restaurant and wine bar revisits traditional Corsican fare in a modern, designer interior. Live guitar music on summer evenings on the shaded terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15338;La Grange des Agapes;France;Cogolin;7 rue du 11-Novembre, Cogolin, 83310, France;43.2515982;6.5320097;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Like every true enthusiast, Thierry Barot is a master of multi - tasking. Not content to offer tasty and appetising theme - based menus (vegetables, Provence, asparagus, truffles etc), he regularly runs cookery classes and is the author of a book of chocolate recipes. What a feast!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15339;L'Aigle d'Or;France;Azay-le-Rideau;10 avenue Adélaïde-Riche, Azay-le-Rideau, 37190, France;47.2619857;0.4628505;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Just a few hundred metres from the château you will come across this lovely spot. The restaurant is set in a country house where you can tuck into delicious food at a table near the fireplace or out on the shady terrace. The chef revisits tradition with his tasty fare.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15341;A Pignata;France;Levie;Route de Pianu, Levie, 20170, France;41.7125555;9.1016821;42;true;true;Corsican, Country cooking;This farm-inn, the quintessence of rural charm, specialises in hearty, wholesome dishes that pay tribute to regional traditions through a set menu and top-notch produce. The Corsican cured meats are made from pigs raised on the family farm and the roasted caramelised lamb is exquisite, while the iconic stuffed seabream pays a highly fitting tribute to Corsica’s culinary heritage. Take a seat in the shade of the arbour and admire the knockout view over the mountains and the estate’s vegetable garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15342;B2K6;France;Lempdes;6 rue du Caire, Lempdes, 63370, France;45.7695859;3.197085;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This friendly village bistro dishes up food that is in harmony with the seasons and uses local ingredients (free-range eggs and poultry from nearby farms, lamb, mushrooms, etc.), flanked by a splendid mainly organic and natural wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15343;L'Imparfait;France;Bergerac;8 rue des Fontaines, Bergerac, 24100, France;44.8506567;0.4836836;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this medieval edifice in historic Bergerac, the chef has been crafting seasonal cuisine of regional inspiration that packs a punch for over 15 years. In summer on the terrace or in winter by a huge fireplace, you will sample elegant, deftly curated dishes, such as panacotta of white asparagus, crab meat and aïoli or a chou craquelin (half chou – half macaroon) with Timut-flavoured stewed strawberries and basil ganache: the antithesis of imperfect in fact!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15344;Le Clos Monteils;France;Monteils;7 chemin du Moulin, Monteils, 82300, France;44.1737162;1.5659788;43;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Françoise and Bernard Bordaries turned this 1771 presbytery into an intimate restaurant that feels like a family home. She extends a genial welcome, while he cracks on with the cooking. He builds dishes on simple foundations to highlight seasonal ingredients in well-crafted recipes.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15345;Le Chamagnon;France;Chamagne;236 rue Claude-Gellée, Chamagne, 88130, France;48.4083301;6.2773378;97;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in the village where artist Claude Lorrain was born, this snug bistro serves bang-on French country cooking (a juicy fillet of Hereford beef and home-made béarnaise sauce, sweetbread with morels and a crème brûlée worthy of Amélie Poulain), dotted with modern touches (red tuna and seasonings). Top-notch produce and a savvy wine list.;Air conditioning;[]
15346;Place Bernard;France;Bourg-en-Bresse;19 place Bernard, Bourg-en-Bresse, 01000, France;46.2065008;5.2283975;42;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In the hands of Georges Blanc, this handsome 1900 edifice is home to a splendid brasserie adorned with a fresco of the Blanc clan. The culinary score showcases a regional line-up of classics: Bresse poultry in cream, frog’s legs in garlic and parsley and traditional Nantua-style quenelle of pike. Lovely conservatory-cum-patio.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15347;Restaurant de la Plage;France;Boulogne-sur-Mer;124 boulevard Sainte-Beuve, Boulogne-sur-Mer, 62200, France;50.7336636;1.5951085;27;false;true;Seafood;After taking a dip, what could be better than a good meal to recharge your batteries? This restaurant across from the beach is an ode to the sea and its bounty – from perfectly cooked and carefully prepared turbot with beetroot and chorizo, to scallops, in season… And, for dessert, crêpes Suzette flambéed in the dining room in front of the customer. Delicious!;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15348;La Matelote;France;Boulogne-sur-Mer;80 boulevard Sainte-Beuve, Boulogne-sur-Mer, 62200, France;50.7309128;1.5959422;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;A family-run business that pays tribute to women must be a good sign! A “matelote” is the fisherman’s wife, whose talent cannot be equalled when it comes to preparing fish, just like that of this establishment devoted body and soul to seafood (but not to the exclusion of other ingredients). Fish and shellfish are crafted in keeping with culinary tradition and with the firm intention of encouraging sustainable fishing. Save room for the patriotic line-up of Gallic desserts, such as soufflé, the house signature dish.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15349;La Cabro d'Or;France;Les Baux-de-Provence;Mas de Baumanière, Les Baux-de-Provence, 13520, France;43.740567;4.7877368;93;true;false;Provençal;Chef Michel Hulin crafts generous provençal fare using first-rate ingredients from Alpilles and Camargue, illustrated by hot-cold Mediterranean squid cooked like a bouillabaisse or the incredible roast lamb, confit then smoked in AOP Crau hay, courgette flower and parsnips from Moulin de Daudet… The site is jaw-dropping with a terrace shaded by mulberry plane trees and a view over the jagged skyline that has made this enchanting village and its countryside so famous. Thoroughly enchanting.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15350;Saint-Christophe;France;La Baule;1 avenue des Alcyons, La Baule, 44500, France;47.2837054;-2.3962636;90;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Established in a genteel early 20C villa, the large windows of this cosy, colourful restaurant overlook a lush green garden. Amidst treelined flowerbeds and shaded by parasols, the spacious alfresco area is bliss in summertime. Appetising traditional cuisine strewn with contemporary touches. Don’t miss their signature dessert: lemon and passion fruit soufflé with a sorbet made out of fermented milk!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15351;La Ferme Sainte-Cécile;France;Moustiers-Sainte-Marie;Route des Gorges-du-Verdon, Moustiers-Sainte-Marie, 04360, France;43.8345597;6.2206216;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Once through the gate, follow the lovely cobbled driveway, at the end of which is this 18C farmhouse that has been turned into a go-to place for foodies! At the kitchen stove, the chef concocts delicate and subtle cuisine that draws on the South of France: royal sea bream, vegetable pistou and roasted garlic ice cream. One of the best restaurants in Moustiers.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15352;Le Clos d'Augusta;France;Bordeaux;339 rue Georges-Bonnac, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8367656;-0.5974833;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine;With its inviting bottle-green façade and pleasant terrace in the garden to the rear, this restaurant is run by a couple whose genuine dedication inspires confidence. The deft and creative dishes lay the emphasis on local ingredients. One example of their fresh, flavourful and seasonal starters is the generous carpaccio of Zebra tomatoes, smoked scamorza, fresh peas, leeks, basil and a green apple sorbet. Diners can expect a very warm welcome. At lunchtime, the set menu du jour is a bargain.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15354;Montcalm;France;Paris;21 rue Montcalm, Paris, 75018, France;48.89279;2.337155;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This is a pleasant neighbourhood bistro, where the tattooed chef sporting a hipster look uses selected market - fresh ingredients. It's well put together, with bold flavours finely teased out. The menu evolves depending on the consignment from Rungis Market.;;[]
15355;L'Accolade;France;Paris;208 rue de la Croix-Nivert, Paris, 75015, France;48.8372658;2.289303;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a downright convivial atmosphere, the chef – a former sports teacher who has chosen to branch out – prepares tasty cuisine that he changes up every day. He makes ample use of produce from South-West France (pork belly, pointed cabbage and green lentils), but also borrows a smattering of Asian ingredients (carpaccio of Tokyo turnip, crab meat, coriander and black garlic). An appealing place.;;[]
15356;La Fine Fourchette;France;Belley;2500 avenue du Bugey, à Virignin, Belley, 01300, France;45.7358533;5.7079944;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A jaw-dropping view over the Canal du Rhône and an elegant interior set the scene in this renowned regional temple of good food. Generous portions of Ain produce take the limelight in the chef’s well-crafted score, depicted by fascinating flavour combinations and impeccable plating. Special mention for the strawberry-themed dessert that will knock the tastebuds off fans of fine French fare!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15357;Arraya;France;Sare;30 place du Village, Sare, 64310, France;43.3124904;-1.5801775;48;true;false;Creative;This restaurant is accommodated in a traditional setting in a former coaching inn en route to the Camino de Santiago, in one of the most beautiful villages in the Basque hinterland. The chef, originally from La Réunion, draws inspiration not only from her home island but also from her travels in Asia (Thailand, Indonesia) and Africa (Madagascar, Mauritius and South Africa). She uses local ingredients such as Banka trout and duck breast, to which she adds spices and more exotic flavours. A delightful terrace shaded by plane trees.;Terrace;[]
15358;George's;France;Saint-Martin-de-Ré;Hôtel de Toiras, 1 quai Job-Foran, Saint-Martin-de-Ré, 17410, France;46.205244;-1.3663957;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Boasting an ideal location in the port of Saint-Martin-de-Ré, this chic brasserie has a seaside-inspired interior decor. Featuring alongside the unfussy dishes made with precisely prepared regional produce (freshly caught fish, Challans poultry) are some great French classics (pan-fried foie gras, baked snails). The pleasant terrace lounge and cocktail bar are popular. Attentive service.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15359;Nosso;France;Paris;22 promenade Claude-Lévi-Strauss, Paris, 75013, France;48.8308644;2.3749114;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Brazilian-born chef Alessandra Montagne is delighted to be in her new restaurant, which has an inviting contemporary interior featuring a preponderance of concrete and wood as well as floor-to-ceiling windows. Her recipe for success (and pleasure) comprises meticulous plating, seasonal, locally sourced ingredients, a whirlwind of flavours and a patchwork of influences (from Brazil to Asia). Zero waste and 100% natural. Tasting menus in the evening.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15360;Fleur de Sureau;France;Gambsheim;22 rue du Chemin-de-Fer, Gambsheim, 67760, France;48.6947882;7.8797797;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This “Elderflower” has taken root opposite the train station! Its gardener is a chef who trained under Jean-Georges Klein at the Arnsbourg and who rustles up food for today’s palate, based on fine seasonal produce : tuna tartare, smoked herring roe, green pepper and blackberry gel, or gently cooked suckling pork, pan-fried cauliflower and plum compote…;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15361;La Table des Délices;France;Grignan;Chemin de Bessas, Grignan, 26230, France;44.4201284;4.896597;40;false;false;Provençal;This 1980’s house stands on the road to the grotto where Mme de Sévigné used to seek refuge. The chef concocts hearty regional dishes, such as a terrine of baby rabbit with walnuts and confit of spring onions wrapped in smoked bacon. Fine wine cellar.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15363;Les Jardins du Moulin;France;Gundershoffen;7 rue du Moulin, Gundershoffen, 67110, France;48.90328;7.65983;68;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant blends perfectly into the setting of the mill. Through the bay windows, one can admire the garden and magnificent terrace. Diners can look forward to well - crafted creations from the carpaccio of sea bream with citrus olive oil to the fillet of Simmental beef, béarnaise au siphon and buewespaetzle.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15365;L'Essentiel;France;Saumur;11 rue Raspail, Saumur, 49400, France;47.2576583;-0.0714453;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Nestled at the foot of the castle, this beautiful tuffeau-stone house sports charming dining rooms (parquet floors, exposed rafters and bare stone walls) and peaceful little patios. Chef Anthony Vaillant crafts food in the zeitgeist, jazzed up by a scattering of deft creative touches: start with a medley of asparagus and green peas, enhanced by a citrus fruit flavoured dressing followed by fabulously fresh cod flanked by a curry sauce and velvety mashed potato. Extremely attentive service. Regional tipples take pride of place on the wine list. An enjoyable culinary experience!;Terrace;[]
15366;Agastache;France;Issoire;95 rue de Brioude, Issoire, 63500, France;45.537254;3.2516313;21;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A bistronomic establishment opened by the star chef of the Atelier Yssoirien. An extensive menu, updated, seasonal recipes, expertly prepared and artistically presented, in a Scandinavian-style décor.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15367;Le Cairn - Hôtel le Celtique;France;Carnac;82 avenue des Druides, Carnac, 56340, France;47.5731192;-3.0716535;29;false;true;Contemporary;In the heart of Carnac-Plage, just a pebble stone's throw from the sandy beach and the sea, Hôtel Le Celtique has been treated to a magnificent Art deco-inspired refurbishment. The menu features a happy marriage of traditional foundations and modern trends, with the occasional exotic spice, such as on the lobster with ajo blanco, squash and goji berries.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15368;L & Luy - Château d'Ygrande;France;Ygrande;Le Mont, Ygrande, 03160, France;46.54767;2.980203;93;true;false;Creative;Chef Cédric Denaux works his magic in this elegant Directoire château (1835), whose terrace overlooks the Bourbon countryside. His creative and seasonal cooking prominently features plant-based and of course seasonal ingredients. He uses home-grown aromatic herbs, plants and vegetables from the château garden, paired with top-drawer ingredients. The memory of his Roscoff monkfish, dashi stock, marigold petals and purple basil lingers with us still.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15369;Beam !;France;Toulon;2 rue Hippolyte-Duprat, Toulon, 83000, France;43.1245324;5.9318362;82;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Beaming and buzzing! The kitchens of the Télégraphe, a high spot of Toulon’s cultural life, are all go! Energetic Arnaud Tabarec, born in Burgundy, honed his skills in prestigious establishments and was the star chef of the Five Hotel’s Roof in Cannes. Today he is acclaimed for his delicate, predominantly vegetarian cuisine, whose ingredients are of course sourced locally and combined boldly.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15370;Yka bar & ceviche;France;Lyon;112 boulevard des Belges, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7684028;4.8584876;26;false;true;Peruvian;The casual sibling of the Franco-Peruvian star-rated gastronomic Miraflores, Yka is the perfect venue for afterwork socialising in the Brotteaux district. Relax in the warm contemporary vibe (the colourful mural depicts Peruvians from the Cusco region), while sipping a pisco cocktail and nibbling on warm flaky pastry empanadas stuffed with beef and green peas or a ceviche from the wide range on the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15371;La Réserve du Presbytère;France;Montagne;22 Grand-Rue, Montagne, 33570, France;44.9307342;-0.1291704;38;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Opposite the Romanesque church of a wine-growing village is this eatery serving bistronomy dishes. Diners savour traditional flavours in a decor comprising bistro tables and industrial chairs set up against a backdrop of exposed stone walls. The delicious desserts deserve a special mention: amandine tartlet with figs, raspberry confit and sorbet. Pleasant terrace to the rear.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15372;Chartron;France;Saint-Donat-sur-l'Herbasse;1 avenue Gambetta, Saint-Donat-sur-l'Herbasse, 26260, France;45.1238619;4.9835121;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated between the Drôme and Ardèche areas in southeastern France, this local family-run establishment dates back to 1946, when Paulette Chartron and her brother René bought the inn in this village famous for its Jean-Sébastien Bach Festival (held every summer). The key to their success? The cuisine, made from quality ingredients, reveals a definite savoir-faire: duck foie gras, sea bream, pike-perch fillet, Provençal lamb… plus there are dishes starring truffles in season. They have a handful of cosy guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15373;La Casserole;France;Strasbourg;24 rue des Juifs, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5835892;7.7527033;33;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Formerly maître d' at Au Crocodile, the owner of this place officiates in a contemporary and elegant setting that beautifully sets off the refined cuisine made with first-rate ingredients. The surf and turf-inspired "choco-beef" tartare with Kristal caviar and quail egg may be one of his most original dishes, but that's no reason to pass over the crêpes Suzette prepared in time-honoured tradition at your table, accompanied by vanilla ice cream made to order – delicious.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15374;Château Hochberg;France;Wingen-sur-Moder;2 rue de Château-Teutsch, Wingen-sur-Moder, 67290, France;48.9268363;7.3636558;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Within this majestic 19C residence, chef Arnaud Barberis serves up delicious seasonal cuisine with a few French classics: bouchée à la reine royale, heart sweetbreads with chanterelles. The contemporary decor is dotted with creations by master glassmaker René Lalique, whose work is celebrated in the museum just opposite. Gorgeous terrace to the rear of the château, overlooking the grounds.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15376;Garum;France;Beaune;10 rue de l'Hôtel-Dieu, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0213532;4.837327;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The chef has turned his Jardin des Remparts into a “living table”. This fashionable, classy bistro uses premium ingredients in a menu ranging from pre-dinner snacks to share with friends (Gillardeau oysters, charcuterie and French fries) to a selection of mouth-watering, well-crafted seasonal dishes. The bistro’s namesake (garum) is a fermented sauce, popular with the Romans, that Christophe Bocquillon uses to season beef tartare, in particular.;Terrace;[]
15377;La Vieille Enseigne;France;Strasbourg;9 rue des Tonneliers, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5800141;7.74922;100;false;false;Alsatian;Despite the name, this is a brand new winstub! The magnificent traditional wainscoting is the work of a cabinetmaker, lithographs by Tomi Ungerer adorn the walls, while copious helpings, local ingredients and traditional regional recipes (presskopf, choucroute, game) depict the gourmet tribute to Alsace, down to the splendid selection of mainly organic wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15378;Iod'in;France;Allauch;602 avenue du 7e-Régiment-de-Tirailleurs-Algériens, Allauch, 13190, France;43.3382139;5.4738281;94;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Contemporary;On the outskirts of the pretty village of Allauch, this modern and spacious, maritime-inspired brasserie comes highly recommended. Youthful chef Anthony de Filippo (stints with Lionel Levy at Alcyone and Dominique Frérard at Les Trois Forts in Marseilles) takes his crew of foodies on an appetising, no-holds barred voyage, in which fish and shellfish take pride of place. Bouillabaisse on the menu (without prior reservation).;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15380;Auberge des Matfeux;France;Arnage;289 avenue Nationale, Arnage, 72230, France;47.9154685;0.1784837;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Close to the famous motor racing track, Circuit des 24 Heures du Mans, this family-run restaurant is decorated with abstract patterns and uses crockery made by a local artist. It was established in 1962 by the current chef's parents, and holds the Sarthe region close to its heart. Bringing to bear solid technical skills, chef Xavier Souffront composes flavoursome dishes that are in tune with the times, without shunning tradition, and highlight ingredients from his beloved terroir. Don't miss the langoustine ravioli, one of the restaurant's classics. The fine wine list is sure to be a hit with wine lovers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15381;À l'Étoile;France;Klingenthal;7 place de l'Étoile, Klingenthal, 67530, France;48.4688839;7.4071454;98;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Tucked away in a small Alsace village on the Mont Sainte Odile road, this traditional hostelry, opened in 1920, is today run by the fourth generation. A warm welcome and honest, homely recipes, starring market-fresh produce and a slate menu. For example, start with a waffle piled high with smoked salmon and citrus fruit, while offal fans won’t be able to resist the fried kidneys and sweetbread.;Terrace;[]
15383;Le Baratin;France;Paris;3 rue Jouye-Rouve, Paris, 75020, France;48.87321;2.3828;66;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Argentine chef Raquel Carena pretty much invented bistronomy, as many young chefs acknowledge. This stripped-down, retro bistro serves food that is delicate or hearty, but always personal. The blackboard menu makes pleasant reading, the prices are restrained and the wines appealing. Reservations strongly recommended.;;[]
15384;Goustut;France;Capbreton;Quai de la Pêcherie, Capbreton, 40130, France;43.6521444;-1.4332857;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;On the lookout for a friendly restaurant delivering good food with a rich variety of flavours? Sit back in the relaxed atmosphere and enjoy the mezze menus – a host of local dishes served in small portions for sharing. The house specialty, they feature Capbreton fish and vegetables from the Bastelica family market gardeners. Highlights include the excellent cuttlefish and foie gras pâté en croûte, the fried blue whiting ravioli with pil pil sauce and the crispy bonito roll with Asian spinach and courgette purée.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15385;Auberge Sauvage;France;Servon;3 place Saint-Martin, Servon, 50170, France;48.6007516;-1.4196972;17;true;false;Creative;This former 16C presbytery in the heart of a photogenic country village on the road to Mont Saint Michel is home to a restaurant flanked by a cottage garden, which provides chef Thomas Benady with plenty of produce (veggies, fruit, aromatic herbs, flowers…), as well as inspiration for his single set surprise menu. The chef also frequently works with small local producers and independent fishermen. You can expect a vegetable-focused, seafood slant presented and plated in a modern, minimalist manner and above all steeped in the distinctive personality and character of its author. Examples include his work with beetroot or a vegetable sausage stuffed with celery and garden herbs. The chef’s partner, Jessica, elegantly manages the front of house. A few stylish guestrooms also available. Seating is limited so reservations are recommended.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15386;Le Café de Paris;France;Biarritz;5 place Bellevue, Biarritz, 64200, France;43.4825063;-1.5610758;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The legendary Café de Paris boasts a prime location in the heart of town, just above the Grande Plage. Diners choose dishes from an intelligently updated brasserie repertoire, inspired by the local terroir and peppered with nods to the Iberian peninsula. Think supreme of free-range poultry browned in a sauté pan, piperade spiced up with chorizo and confit grenaille potatoes. Pleasant terrace.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15387;Hito;France;Toulouse;26 rue de la Fonderie, Toulouse, 31000, France;43.5952419;1.4432416;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Hitoshi Araki's restaurant is near Place des Salins. Working alone in the kitchen, the chef cooks up creative French cuisine enriched with passing references to Japan. His indisputably precise execution, remarkable cooking technique and bold flavours come through in dishes such as melt-in-the-mouth pork belly preserved in its own juices and lightly caramelised on the outside – delicious! The lunch menu is a steal.;Air conditioning;[]
15388;L'Hommage;France;Paris;36 avenue de Choisy, Paris, 75013, France;48.8223735;2.3629364;36;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a neighbourhood swarming with Chinese eateries, this establishment stands out from the crowd by courtesy of a bistronomic purebred Gallic lineup and minimalist Scandinavian-style loft interior. The high-flying culinary score boasts quality ingredients and bang-on cooking and seasoning: ravioles of Ossau-Iraty cheese, smoked pimiento sauce, dusting of chorizo, poached rhubarb and roquette oil, or loin of croaker with asparagus, miso and capers in a gutsy red wine sauce…;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15389;Caves Madeleine;France;Beaune;8 rue du Faubourg-Madeleine, Beaune, 21200, France;47.0214283;4.8407778;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A stone's throw from the town centre, this wine bar-restaurant is a little gem. Chef Martial has hooked up with the best local producers, including some top wine growers, to create wholesome, punchy cuisine that is rife with flavour, eg warm potatoes, haddock, and tarragon sabayon. Relaxed, no-fuss service – the focus is firmly on the contents of your glass and your plate. In fine weather, make the most of the pleasant terrace in the shade of a fig tree.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15390;Le Jardin de l'Abbaye;France;Le Tronchet;L'Abbatiale, Le Tronchet, 35540, France;48.4902657;-1.8373707;95;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away in the countryside of Saint-Malo's hinterland, between Mont Saint-Michel, Saint-Malo and Dinan, this hotel was once an abbey (12C). The premises are also home to a quality restaurant serving cuisine inspired by the market and the season, with dishes such as saithe, carrot, potato and gingerbread. Enjoy your meal in the sober interior with views over the countryside and lake, before returning to your nice comfortable guestroom – peace and quiet guaranteed!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
15392;Song Qi;France;Monaco;7 avenue Princesse-Grace, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7429923;7.4304206;84;false;true;Asian, Chinese;Opposite Grimaldi Forum, this swanky, gourmet Chinese restaurant has opted for premium materials and a serene atmosphere. The appetising menu offers a vast array of Chinese cuisine from Peking soup with smoked chicken to crispy dragon prawns with Chinese mustard or the classic dim sum. Bookings advisable!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15393;L'Auberge d'Anthy;France;Anthy-sur-Léman;2 rue des Écoles, Anthy-sur-Léman, 74200, France;46.3555228;6.4271969;78;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This traditional small hotel-restaurant-café is all about the simple pleasures in life! It is perfect to enjoy fish from Lake Geneva (perch, fera and Arctic char), supplied by local fishermen. The chef also likes to showcase the charcuterie and cheese from the Chablais region!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15394;La Maréa;France;Théoule-sur-Mer;16 avenue du Trayas, Théoule-sur-Mer, 06590, France;43.484841;6.9326172;25;true;false;Seafood;Opposite the sea and the ochre-coloured rocks of Esterel and looking down on the beach and port of La Figueirette, this restaurant was founded in the 1950s by a local fisherman. It has been happily taken over by Jérôme Cervera, former fishmonger. The chef whips up à la carte flawlessly fresh seafood and carefully crafted dishes, illustrated by roast loin of gilt-head bream with shrimps, paella-style stock and chorizo. The lunch and evening menus feature à la carte dishes, served alfresco or in the pretty dining room with a sea view.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15395;La Table du Tillau;France;Verrières-de-Joux;Le Mont des Verrières, Verrières-de-Joux, 25300, France;46.8836025;6.4577108;100;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A few metres from the Swiss border, this Franche-Comté farmhouse built out of stone and old wood exudes serenity, just like its elegant guestrooms appointed in chalet style. On the menu, modern cuisine that highlights often regional produce, like lemon cream with beetroot-marinated trout gravadlax, or filet of beef, red wine reduction and celeriac puree.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15398;Le Berlot;France;Montlouis-sur-Loire;2 place François-Mitterrand, Montlouis-sur-Loire, 37270, France;47.3884112;0.8267215;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Hervé and Patricia Chardonneau, a couple of foodies formerly of Casse-Cailloux in Tours, have set up shop in the heart of a wine-growing village. Hervé crafts a hearty, wholesome lineup of traditional French nosh, together with game in season: hare à la royale (a sort of jugged hare), a game pie (oreiller de la belle Aurore), lamb’s brains... His bistronomic approach draws its inspiration from the seasons. Fine wine list with a focus on organic and natural wines. Separate wine bar.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15399;29;France;Saintes;9 place Blair, Saintes, 17100, France;45.7432069;-0.6357023;74;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Michael Durkin is a tattooed Englishman and rugby fan who has worked in some of the best restaurants in the world. He whips up creative modern bistro cuisine, for example seared cod, celeriac and capers – a well-presented and harmonious dish. Not only is the four-course set lunch menu unbeatable value, the small terrace is a real draw in fine weather.;Terrace;[]
15401;La Table de Léa;France;Villeneuve-de-Berg;Le Petit Tournon, Villeneuve-de-Berg, 07170, France;44.5472039;4.490029;70;false;false;Farm to table;In this former farm the female chef creates seasonal dishes with a personal touch. In fine weather take advantage of the attractive terrace beneath the shade of the chestnut trees.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15402;Momento;France;Bué;5 rue de la Cure, Bué, 18300, France;47.3108911;2.7921817;90;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Here you really are guaranteed a delightful "momento", complete with a view of the vineyards. A very professional couple in their thirties runs the show: Mexican chef Mariana Mateos cooks up seasonal cuisine that demonstrates finesse and generosity, alongside her husband, Thomas Jacquet, a local man (service, sommelier). A real treat.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15403;La Maison Badine;France;La Tronche;2 rue du Pont-Prouiller, La Tronche, 38700, France;45.2067909;5.7455783;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This welcoming modern establishment, named after one of the chef’s forebears, is depicted by a trendy, casual vibe that mirrors its tattooed maestro. From his open-plan kitchen, Florian Poyet crafts a legible bistronomic score with a strong focus on the seasons: squid in parsley and garlic and white asparagus, Trièves lamb with wild garlic and black limes, slow-baked rhubarb and strawberries in Kampot white pepper…;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15404;Les Ombres;France;Paris;27 quai Jacques-Chirac, Paris, 75007, France;48.8616912;2.299329;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the roof terrace of the Musée Quai Branly – Jacques Chirac, this entirely glass-sided restaurant boasting interior and exterior architecture designed by Jean Nouvel overlooks the nearby Eiffel Tower. The menu, supervised by Alain Ducasse, is skilfully executed by talented chef Alexandre Sempere, a trusted collaborator. The modern seasonal cuisine is made with fine ingredients and smacks of the Mediterranean influences beloved of its mentor.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15405;Café de l'Ardèche;France;Montélimar;19 avenue Charles-de-Gaulle, Montélimar, 26200, France;44.5580744;4.7476993;88;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Grey leather banquettes, contemporary furniture, Pop art and a fine collection of works by artist Ricardo Santamaria set the scene in the modern interior. The food is expertly crafted, seasonal and starring local produce, such as farm-range guinea fowl and a gutsy girolles gravy.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15406;AOR La Table, le Goût et Nous;France;Riquewihr;2 rue de la Piscine, Riquewihr, 68340, France;48.1670377;7.300378;67;false;false;Creative;Something of a UFO in the gastronomic universe of Alsace, globetrotting cook, Serge Burckel, is also part poet, part rock star – check out the old LPs and CDs recycled as place mats! He works with his family in a bohemian, laid-back ambience, with a choice of surprise menus.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15407;La Serre;France;Paimpol;4 rue de Poulgoic, Paimpol, 22500, France;48.7845982;-3.0486461;99;false;false;Modern Cuisine;An explosion of greenery sets the scene for a splendid lineup of dishes, scattered with the odd creative touch. The spot-on result stars punchy flavours and meticulous plating. Meals are served in a magnificent greenhouse or on the alfresco patio that is bliss in fine weather.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15411;Auberge du Sombral - Les Bonnes Choses;France;Saint-Cirq-Lapopie;Place du Sombral, Saint-Cirq-Lapopie, 46330, France;44.4645135;1.6689546;92;false;false;Country cooking, Traditional Cuisine;In this house at the foot of the Château des Lapopie, you can be sure that good things – Les Bonnes Choses – are to come! Enjoy the pleasant cuisine du terroir, in which local ingredients are the star (lamb, foie gras, cheese... ). There are a handful of pretty guestrooms, if you wish to stay on in this village overlooking the Lot.;Terrace;[]
15412;Le Théophile - Château d’Orfeuillette;France;Albaret-Sainte-Marie;La Garde, Albaret-Sainte-Marie, 48200, France;44.8733147;3.2558612;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The muted, romantic and château-like atmosphere of this restaurant combines the elegance of a historic edifice with a striking modern decor. Drawing upon premium local produce, the chef whisks up modern, delicate dishes. Poised between the Aubrac and Margeride, the 19C hotel surrounded by grounds is theatrically contemporary and glamorous.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15413;Biondi;France;Paris;118 rue Amelot, Paris, 75011, France;48.8638284;2.3669976;20;false;true;Argentinian;Near the Cirque d’Hiver, this gifted chef named his buzzy restaurant after a famous Argentine clown, Pepe Biondi. South America also takes pride of place on the menu: ceviche of tuna, empanadas of meat, churrasco de las Pampas cooked over embers, or a dessert of a caramel flan with a dulce de leche mousse – to die for! Fine selection of Argentine wines.;;[]
15414;Saperlipopette !;France;Puteaux;9 place du Théâtre, Puteaux, 92800, France;48.8805111;2.2393177;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This former brewery has had a major facelift, to become an inviting, trendy restaurant, under expert direction. The generous food is in a chic bistro style and neatly presented.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15415;La Passerelle;France;Issy-les-Moulineaux;172 quai de Stalingrad, Issy-les-Moulineaux, 92130, France;48.8251892;2.2577531;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is presided over by a talented and motivated chef who knows how to take you on a culinary journey of taste and flavours! Enjoy rigorously selected ingredients in the fine and colourful cuisine that is peppered with Mediterranean influences. The best restaurant in town.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15416;Prunier par Yannick Alléno;France;Paris;16 avenue Victor-Hugo, Paris, 75116, France;48.8725474;2.2917735;58;false;true;Seafood;Adorned with the work of some of the greatest mosaicists, engravers and sculptors of the Art deco period, the lavish interior of Prunier is well worth a trip in its own right. The menu, signed Yannick Alléno, gives pride of place to seafood and Prunier’s legendary caviar, of course.We recommend house signature dishes, such as the Christian Dior Egg (poached and sprinkled with caviar) or fish to be shared.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Valet parking;[]
15417;La Flamiche;France;Roye;20 place de l'Hôtel-de-Ville, Roye, 80700, France;49.6982153;2.7893145;68;false;true;Classic Cuisine;A classical interior lies behind the large windows of La Flamiche. Here, cuisine with robust traditional foundations is enhanced by a touch of modernity: one example would be the duck foie gras and smoked trout in a Granny Smith jelly, cucumber pickles and apple chutney – a beautifully crafted starter. Then there are the medallions of monkfish with lime, carrot and rocket, perfectly cooked in butter, the good old-fashioned way.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15418;La Table de Marc Turpin – Hostellerie Saint-Germain;France;Saint-Germain-lès-Arlay;635 Grande-Rue, Saint-Germain-lès-Arlay, 39210, France;46.759277;5.5589576;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Opposite the church, this engaging 17C coaching inn has been entirely refurbished in a low-key, contemporary vein. The chef sources fine local produce, often organic, to craft appetising dishes, occasionally peppered with creative touches, such as pink trout and nori seaweed. All of which is washed down with fine Jura wines. The cosy rooms are pleasant, and quieter overlooking the terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15419;L'Essensiel - Domaine de Champlong;France;Villerest;100 chemin de la Chapelle, Villerest, 42300, France;45.9996432;4.0201241;40;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Flavour and special occasion indulgence depict this 18C property nestled in greenery. Diners are treated to contemporary cuisine in the "salle des peintures" hung with period paintings, or in the conservatory overlooking the park. The chef scours the countryside for premium produce like Chérier pigeon, matured seabass or high-quality blue lobster. Warm welcome and seamless service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15420;La Ferme de Voisins;France;Voisins-le-Bretonneux;4 rue de Port-Royal, Voisins-le-Bretonneux, 78960, France;48.7578116;2.0497388;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You reach this lovely 19C farmhouse via a flower-decked courtyard, which serves as a patio in summertime. The relatively concise menu shines the spotlight on the house classics, which are prawns on sticks, the ‘irreplaceable’ calf’s head and signature desserts such as the rum and orange punch baba, together with a range of tasty and creative dishes. A fine establishment to try out post-haste!;Terrace;[]
15421;Inima;France;Bordeaux;48 rue du Palais-Gallien, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8433442;-0.5814434;44;false;true;Creative;In her small restaurant that sports an uncluttered interior (formerly the Cromagnon), young Moldavian-born chef Oxana Cretu gives free rein to her culinary imagination in a surprise menu. This perfectionist rolls out colourful dishes packed with aromas: crayfish, bouchot mussels and roses or imperial prawns, sweetcorn and lavender. Her dessert of meringue with strawberries from the Lot, Namelaka cream, lemon marmalade and jasmine sorbet is an unqualified hit.;Wheelchair access;[]
15422;Une Table à la Campagne - La Fenière;France;Cadenet;1680 route de Lourmarin, Cadenet, 84160, France;43.7487272;5.3643004;40;false;false;Provençal;Nadia Sammut crafts seasonal Provençal cuisine that is gluten free and strongly anchored in the region (partnerships with local producers, home-made flours, home-grown vegetables). In fine weather, you can bask on the terrace beneath the reed canopy. A vibrant experience close to nature.;Brunch,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15423;Aho Fina;France;Saint-Jean-de-Luz;43 boulevard Thiers, Saint-Jean-de-Luz, 64500, France;43.3926083;-1.6596853;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Bang on the beach opposite the sea, the Empire-style Grand Hôtel is certainly a local landmark! Aho Fina treats diners to cuisine that is inspired and driven by the ocean and the Basque country. Examples include coffee praline finger with vanilla custard and chocolate ice cream and then topped with coffee mousse – to die for! Bistronomic set lunch menu.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15424;Autour de la Table;France;Huningue;17A rue de Village-Neuf, Huningue, 68330, France;47.596607;7.5786524;92;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This place calls to mind a hotel training school, with its classic menu (paupiette of sole, beef fillet, pancakes with quetsch brandy), serious and applied service – the forgotten art of cutting and preparing in the dining room is still practiced. Here, tradition and classicism are present and correct, both around and especially on the table.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15425;Zest;France;Cesson-Sévigné;32 cours de la Vilaine, Cesson-Sévigné, 35510, France;48.1155977;-1.6072798;77;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The secret behind the Zest’s success is market-fresh cooking, original recipes dusted with exotic notes, spices and seasonings, a delightfully friendly vibe and in summertime, a riverside patio on the banks of the Vilaine. Slick service with a smile.;Terrace;[]
15426;Le Mange-Grenouille;France;Saint-Aignan;10 rue Paul-Boncour, Saint-Aignan, 41110, France;47.2702867;1.3751328;68;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This former coaching inn located in a lane just a stone's throw from the banks of the Cher has a pleasant patio in the courtyard, delightfully rustic dining areas with bare stonework and terracotta tiled floors... but above all ambitious cuisine whose roots are firmly embedded in tradition. At lunchtime, a simpler, great-value set menu is served. Don't miss the house speciality: frog's legs sautéed in parsley!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15427;Le Rocher Blanc;France;La Garde;Route du Gévaudan, La Garde, 48200, France;44.881235;3.2469389;16;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A country inn with a refreshingly trendy vibe! The chef, who is into interior design, likes to shake things up, both on the decor front – you'll notice the eclectic style – and when it comes to the food. As for the menu, terroir meets more modern touches (eg crayfish ravioli on a pepper velouté, pork mignon with a Cantal crust, carrot purée with vanilla). A success!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15428;Le Karelian;France;Dommartin-lès-Remiremont;36 rue du Cuchot, Dommartin-lès-Remiremont, 88200, France;47.9982392;6.6439325;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;An understated, stripped-back dining room is the perfect foil for the chef’s modern, creative recipes, illustrated by flawlessly cooked arctic char served with grilled sarrazin wheat and crisp baby leeks in a saté sauce. The chef’s welcoming, professional spouse oversees the front of house. Those with a sweet tooth will be in seventh heaven thanks to the decadent dessert trolley.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
15430;La Ferme du Vert;France;Wierre-Effroy;Rue du Vert, Wierre-Effroy, 62720, France;50.77801;1.751499;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Homemade and regional produce: this farm is still a going concern and the owners – two brothers – divide their time between agriculture and the restaurant. Be sure to try the delicious cheese from their dairy herd!;Car park,Garden or park;[]
15431;Le Relais de Sillery;France;Sillery;3 rue de la Gare, Sillery, 51500, France;49.2001011;4.142508;96;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This elegant inn, a post house in a former life, sports a terrace overlooking the River Vesle. The setting is bucolic, the food classical: sea bass meunière, baby artichokes and confit tomatoes, and a Grand Marnier soufflé. The impressive wine cellar is very competitively priced!;Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15432;Le Crypto;France;Reims;14 place du Forum, Reims, 51100, France;49.2564625;4.0343073;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Opposite Reims’ famous crypto portico (an underground gallery dating from Roman times), this bistro is run by chef Frédéric Dupont, whose CV speaks for itself. Generous helpings of wholesome seasonal fare, a judicious wine list, well-stocked in champagnes, and slick service. The establishment’s success is fully deserved.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15434;La Croix Blanche;France;Saint-Brieuc;61 rue de Genève, Cesson, Saint-Brieuc, 22000, France;48.5181166;-2.7345924;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Two brothers: one in the kitchen, the other serving in the dining room... It is a family affair in this pleasant restaurant overlooking a pretty garden. The cuisine is gourmet and refined, for instance the excellent Dubarry pannacotta with crumbled crab and a shellfish emulsion. You get plenty of enjoyment for the price.;Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
15435;Ô Saveurs;France;Saint-Brieuc;10 rue Jules-Ferry, Saint-Brieuc, 22000, France;48.5058435;-2.7663882;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chances are it won't be the charm of the location near the train station that draws you here, but the restaurant has more than enough of its own merits. Where shall we begin? Scallops from St Brieuc Bay in a Quessoy saffron sauce and seaweed-flavoured conchiglioni or duckling breast roasted in honey and sage with a pear poached in blueberries and shiitakes, and a delicious encounter between cherries and pear with a white chocolate topping to finish…;Wheelchair access;[]
15436;Bistro'Quai;France;Les Sables-d'Olonne;17 quai René-Guiné, Les Sables-d'Olonne, 85100, France;46.4962998;-1.7930291;85;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;On the busy docks of the port, this cosy, colourful eatery in tune with the era serves a seafood menu that varies depending on the catch of the day. You may also be tempted by chef François Gauthier’s specialties, such as squid and cuttlefish flanked by an Espelette pepper sauce or pig’s trotters and ears in a mustard seed sauce. Discerning foodies should save room for the île flottante (egg whites floating on vanilla custard) and pink pralines (candied almonds) à la Alain Chapel – to die for!;;[]
15437;L'Auberge d'Antan;France;Saint-Girons;Avenue de la Résistance, Saint-Girons, 09200, France;42.9773859;1.1464525;19;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In what used to be the barn belonging to the château, this restaurant boasts an impressively high ceiling. Hams suspended from the ceiling, stonework and beams make for a lovely country atmosphere. No - nonsense cooking at its best, with traditional dishes such as grilled meats and suckling pig prepared right in front of you at the huge fireplace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15438;Au Fulcosa;France;Saint-Germain-en-Laye;2 rue du Maréchal-Foch, à Fourqueux, Saint-Germain-en-Laye, 78112, France;48.886338;2.0634202;97;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Fulcosa means "fern" in Latin, a reference to the plant that once carpeted the surrounding forests, suggesting that the young proprietors have a sense of history as well as flavours! In the inviting decor of their "culinary bistro", they treat us to tasty seasonal cuisine in which tradition meets innovation: for example, mushroom ravioli in a chicken broth, with bacon and hazelnut.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15439;Comme Chez Maman;France;Paris;5 rue des Moines, Paris, 75017, France;48.8876647;2.3182189;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary bistro near a green square in the heart of the Batignolles neighbourhood is a real home from home. The Belgian chef, Wim Van Gorp, makes lovely contemporary dishes that he peppers with creative touches, and some of which pay delicious tribute to his Flemish roots.;;[]
15440;Pierre Sang on Gambey;France;Paris;6 rue Gambey, Paris, 75011, France;48.8650736;2.3720763;49;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;This is Pierre Sang's second restaurant, the first being in nearby Oberkampf. Both locations are run with the same ethos and have the same concept. The famous chef's commitment to quality ingredients is also present and correct. Care and creativity go into turning produce into innovative, cosmopolitan dishes, with the occasional nod to Korea. The originality does not stop at the food: diners are invited to guess what they have just eaten! An inviting setting in which to indulge in a moment of sharing.;Counter dining;[]
15441;Mensae;France;Paris;23 rue Melingue, Paris, 75019, France;48.8758985;2.3856352;56;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Cuisine of the moment, full of freshness and with spot-on flavours. Among the classics, on the menu all year round, the frogs' legs, garlic and parsley or the mousse au chocolat praliné are good enough to spark a riot. The decor has the good taste to make itself discreet. The small sidewalk terrace is welcome in summer.;Air conditioning;[]
15442;Les 3 Cépages;France;Reuilly;17 rue de la Gare, Reuilly, 36260, France;47.0861442;2.046317;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of rural Berry and in the famous wine - growing village of Reuilly, this white - fronted ex - hotel is enjoying a new lease of life in the capable hands of a committed Japanese couple crazy about French food. Fine, flavoursome and flawlessly cooked, with a focus on fine quality produce.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15443;Les Tourelles - Château d'Apigné;France;Le Rheu;Route de Chavagne, Le Rheu, 35650, France;48.0926193;-1.7639023;36;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Relax in the blatantly romantic ambiance of this stylish neo-Renaissance castle dating from 1833 set in sprawling grounds. Its exquisite living rooms provide the perfect foil for appetising cuisine made with local produce in tune with modern sensibilities. Rooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15444;Etsi;France;Paris;23 rue Eugène-Carrière, Paris, 75018, France;48.89025;2.333;32;true;false;Greek;Mikaela Liaroutsos, a young chef of Greek origin, has returned to the cuisine of her childhood, after learning the ropes in prestigious establishments. At étsi, she rolls out strikingly fresh mezze with bold touches such as roast cauliflower, anchovies and Serifos capers or scallops in a pistachio butter of mizithra and tarragon – to die for and the antithesis of clichéd! The feta, olives, capers, charcuterie, cheese and olive oil are all imported straight from Greece. Don’t even try to resist the warm, friendly vibe!;Terrace;[]
15445;Le Chiquito;France;Méry-sur-Oise;3 rue de l'Oise, Méry-sur-Oise, 95540, France;49.0597697;2.1646949;92;true;true;Classic Cuisine;In a handsome 17C edifice, this restaurant continues to fly the flag of gourmet hospitality and upholds a distinctly bourgeois brand of elegance. Chef Anne-Sophie Godry has remained true to the establishment’s traditional Gallic ethos and its signature dishes, among which calf’s sweetbread with a frothy butter, sole meunière and Paris-Brest praliné à l'ancienne with a chicory custard. The front-of-house team is cheerful, competent and slick. Terrific wine list, with more than 400 references.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15446;Eels;France;Paris;27 rue d'Hauteville, Paris, 75010, France;48.8732716;2.3503038;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At Eels, the dishes flirt with "bistronomie", and some of them focus on eel (the clue is in the name). The young chef, Adrien Ferrand, already has considerable experience under his belt (six years for William Ledeuil, first at Ze Kitchen Galerie, then KGB). And now he has a place of his own. A success!;Interesting wine list;[]
15447;Thomas;France;Lyon;6 rue Laurencin, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7529153;4.83216;28;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Owner-chef Thomas Ponson is not one to twiddle his thumbs, to the point that the street could almost be named after him, given the quantity of thriving businesses (bistro, café, bouchon, fish and seafood restaurant) he has opened here. In the parent bistro, he crafts enticing lunchtime menus, while the evening score shines the spotlight on his high-flying technical skills, revolving around ingredients such as scallops, pigeon, lamb sweetbread, etc). A must…;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15448;Les Pyrénées;France;Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port;19 place Charles-de-Gaulle, Saint-Jean-Pied-de-Port, 64220, France;43.1633082;-1.2376505;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;An institution in St Jean Pied de Port, passed down from father to son. Both the decor and the cuisine pay homage to the classicism and taste of the Basque country, all of which with good quality produce.;Air conditioning;[]
15449;Sterenn;France;Penmarc'h;432 rue de la Joie, Penmarc'h, 29760, France;47.8117037;-4.3721567;23;true;true;Seafood, Regional Cuisine;This pleasant restaurant perched on the Pointe de Penmarch serves cuisine that is rooted in the local area and made using top-notch ingredients. The chef puts a lot of effort into meticulously plating his dishes, particularly when it comes to the fish. For dessert, it's all about tradition and savoir-faire, eg the buttery kouign amann, served warm, is nicely caramelised, and soft and crispy at the same time. Lovely views over the bay and Eckmühl Lighthouse.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15450;Lauryvan;France;Saint-Junien;200 allée du Bois-au-Bœuf, Saint-Junien, 87200, France;45.87109;0.9017;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this verdant setting in a small wood close to the Vienne River, tuck into meticulous cuisine attuned to the seasons. The inspector was a fan of the organic confit egg, creamy parsnip purée, Cantal cheese shavings and ham crisps, as well as the lovely terrace with a view of the lake. Two spaces: restaurant and bistro.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15451;Hostellerie du Prieuré;France;Saint-Quirin;163 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Saint-Quirin, 57560, France;48.6100898;7.0646491;34;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This 18C sandstone former convent chants a pure-bred Gallic culinary litany based on regional produce (rack of lamb from the Moselle meadows, fillet of Lorraine beef) and seafood (brill, line-caught whiting, scallops). The portions are generous and the desserts by Maeva (the owners’ daughter) are divinely decadent, illustrated by her Grand Marnier-flavoured strawberry soup. Charming welcome.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15452;Au Cœur de la Forêt;France;Montmorency;Avenue du Repos-de-Diane, Montmorency, 95160, France;49.0019384;2.3408621;23;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A welcoming decor in two rustic rooms, one of which is very spacious with rafters and a fireplace. Shaded summer terrace. Simple, traditional menu in tune with the seasons.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15453;Café Bras;France;Rodez;Jardin du Foirail, Rodez, 12000, France;44.35207;2.56687;87;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The Café Bras, established in the heart of the Soulages Museum, pays tribute to Averyron produce. Two possibilities: order a snack or picnic basket from the counter or take a seat in the restaurant… The kitchen team crafts crisp, aromatic, light dishes, rich in generosity, colour and scents, like a tartare of tuna marinated in calamansi and Greek-style cucurbits or breast of roast duckling, acidic jus, new potatoes, cone cabbage and tiger courgettes with a sauce vierge. The attention lavished on flavour is second to none, as are the welcome and interior décor. Fully worthy of its ongoing success.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15454;L'Escargot 1903 par Yannick Tranchant;France;Puteaux;18 rue Charles-Lorilleux, Puteaux, 92800, France;48.88538;2.23429;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;L'Escargot 1903 is enjoying a new lease of life and welcomes a chef with a proven track record (Ritz, L'Abeille). His market - centred cooking sends sparks flying: meticulous presentations, underpinning finesse, harmonious marriages of flavours. The "must" is to get a look in on the terrace, weather permitting. The lunch set menu is a bargain.;Terrace;[]
15455;Sourire Le Restaurant;France;Paris;15 rue de la Santé, Paris, 75013, France;48.8371287;2.341983;35;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Blue velours banquette seating, old-school bistro tables, trusted farmers (Galician pink veal, Clavisy Farm lamb): the tried-and-tested formula hits the spot, a case in point being the Bay of Morlaix scallops, medley of cabbage, candied lemon. The lunchtime set menu provides two options for every course. A second restaurant in the 5th arrondissement serves tapas in the evening and brunch at the weekend.;Air conditioning;[]
15456;Lao Lane Xang 2;France;Paris;102 avenue d'Ivry, Paris, 75013, France;48.8256;2.3613799;76;true;false;South East Asian;The Parisian chapter of the history of the Siackhasones, originally from Laos, began in the 1990s with the creation of the Lao Lane Xang 1. In 2007, Do and Ken – worthy heirs of the family know - how – opened this second restaurant. The dishes are Laotian, Thai and Vietnamese specialities. Simplicity and flavour are on the menu!;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15459;Vantre;France;Paris;19 rue de la Fontaine-au-Roi, Paris, 75011, France;48.8684469;2.37016;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In France in the Middle Ages, a vantre was a "place of enjoyment", and indeed that's certainly still the case here today. In a neo-bistro interior, a former sommelier (Le Bristol, Le Taillevent) and his chef serve fine dining cuisine prepared using carefully selected ingredients. Every dish looks and tastes terrific, a case in point being the roast sea bass with marinière sauce and samphire, presented vertically. Over 3 000 wines… and well-deserved success.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15460;L'Institut Restaurant;France;Lyon;Le Royal, 20 place Bellecour, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7563785;4.8332565;52;false;true;Modern Cuisine;On Place Bellecour, this training restaurant feels nothing like a school! In a contemporary decor designed by Pierre - Yves Rochon, with open kitchens giving onto the restaurant, the students deliver a high standard of service. The dishes are extremely well made and deserve a high mark.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15461;Osteria Ferrara;France;Paris;7 rue du Dahomey, Paris, 75011, France;48.8511996;2.38303;28;false;false;Italian;Foodies can come here safe in the knowledge that they have found sanctuary in this elegant interior where the culinary magic happens. Sicilian chef Fabrizio Ferrara builds a menu of tasty and well-crafted ingredient-led Italian recipes, such as carpaccio of lean meat, puntarelle and Sicilian citron, or ravioli stuffed with Castelmagno cheese and potatoes. This bistro has soul, and an appealing wine list to boot.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15462;Le Clos du Vigneron;France;Ousson-sur-Loire;18 route Nationale 7, Ousson-sur-Loire, 45250, France;47.5965419;2.793103;70;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;The hillside vineyards of the Coteaux du Giennois lie adjacent to Le Clos du Vigneron. Here you can enjoy hearty, fresh and seasonal cuisine, with an emphasis on fish: the chef works like a true craftsman and is passionate about his profession. Handy guestrooms should you wish to stay overnight.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15463;Les Bas-Rupts;France;Gérardmer;181 route de la Bresse, les Bas-Rupts, Gérardmer, 88400, France;48.0512097;6.865635;99;true;true;Classic Cuisine;In the upper reaches of Gérardmer, this imposing chalet-hostelry has been in the same family for five generations. The culinary focus is on classical dishes with a regional slant and crafted with top-notch ingredients, like duck foie gras, snails, game, fresh-water fish... The wine list is out of this world.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15464;Le Suprême;France;Lyon;106 cours Gambetta, Lyon, 69007, France;45.7513213;4.8541033;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The brainchild of a Franco-Korean couple of chefs who met in New York, the ubiquitous chicken is the star of this vintage bistro oozing with charm. The chef, former right-arm man of Daniel Boulud, consummately signs a gourmet gateau of sautéed chicken livers and a chicken in “half-mourning” that has already become a signature dish. This virtuoso technician has also invented a wafer-thin tart of Nashi pear, scallops and Brussels sprouts. Local game in season. Knockout wine list.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15465;Fuumi;France;Fontainebleau;39 rue de France, Fontainebleau, 77300, France;48.405014;2.6974241;54;false;true;Japanese;This young Japanese restaurant, located in the centre of Fontainebleau, is none other than the outpost of L'Axel, the Michelin - starred restaurant of chef - patron, Kunihisa Goto, and his wife, Vanessa. In this convivial setting, sample aromatic and generous traditional Japanese dishes, as well as gyoza and ramen. Booking strongly recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
15467;Chez Flo;France;Parentis-en-Born;9 rue Saint-Barthélémy, Parentis-en-Born, 40160, France;44.3493261;-1.0715526;61;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Guests are greeted with a smile in this friendly eatery… The same sunny disposition characterises the food, which is in the competent hands of an enthusiastic chef who changes his menu monthly. Uplifting, modern bistro fare composed with carefully selected ingredients: mild pepper from the Landes, Chalosse duck, Gastes saffron, Aquitaine peanuts… A first-rate dining experience, cheerful, seamless service and a lunchtime menu that won’t break the bank – what’s not to like?;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15468;Le Lénigo;France;Le Croisic;11 quai du Lénigo, Le Croisic, 44490, France;47.2979354;-2.5149114;32;true;false;Seafood;This restaurant located opposite the fish market is run by a very pleasant family. Seaside atmosphere (varnished wood, portholes) and fresh, carefully prepared seafood dishes.;Terrace;[]
15469;Le Garet;France;Lyon;7 rue du Garet, Lyon, 69001, France;45.7668431;4.8368812;41;false;false;Lyonnaise, Traditional Cuisine;This veritable institution is well known among aficionados of Lyonnais cuisine. Calf’s head, tripe, dumplings and andouillette sausages are served in a convivial atmosphere and in a typical setting.;Air conditioning;[]
15470;L'Estérel;France;Mulhouse;83 avenue de la 1ère-Division-Blindée, Mulhouse, 68100, France;47.7332137;7.3438307;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Mulhouse's Estérel serves 100% homemade dishes made with market - fresh ingredients that are tasty and very contemporary. The shady terrace is taken by storm in summer.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15472;Restaurant Fond Rose;France;Caluire-et-Cuire;23 chemin de Fond-Rose, Caluire-et-Cuire, 69300, France;45.7909924;4.8263415;50;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;A 1920s mansion transformed into a chic brasserie by the Bocuse group. With its terrace surrounded by 100 year - old trees, it is the epitome of peace and quiet. The food is tasty and generous and squarely in the tradition of the areas around the River Saône, with frogs' legs and quenelles etc.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15473;L'Argot;France;Lyon;132 rue Bugeaud, Lyon, 69006, France;45.767069;4.856083;63;true;false;Meats and Grills;This restaurant doubles as a butcher’s shop in the Brotteaux district. Customers first choose their cut of meat from the refrigerated display counter: beef from Limousin, Galicia, Aubrac and lamb and veal from Auvergne, served with a tasty side dish of the day. Good, wholesome, no-nonsense food.;Air conditioning;[]
15474;Les Remparts;France;Èze;Rue du Barri, Èze, 06360, France;43.727378;7.3620777;52;false;false;Provençal;If you would like to taste the high-flying cuisine of chef Arnaud Faye, this little sister of the Chèvre d’or is just the ticket. In addition to the jaw-dropping view from the terrace overlooking the Mediterranean, St-Jean-Cap-Ferrat and the Bay of Angels, you will sample consummate, Mediterranean dishes, followed by a trolley of ices and pastries to die for! Heavenly!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
15475;Restaurant du Musée;France;Fréland;2 rue de la Rochette, Fréland, 68240, France;48.1697123;7.1935728;30;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this former mill on the Ure, next to the museum of the Welche country, Alain Schmitt’s cooking finds varied inspiration, close to home in “terroir” dishes (fleischschnaka of local trout) and further afield (line-caught grouper in a yosenabe style dashi broth).;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15476;Avelan;France;Gargas;Hôtel Coquillade Provence, Hameau Le Perrotet, Gargas, 84400, France;43.8805486;5.3165338;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Part of a luxury resort in the midst of the sweet-scented Luberon gorse land, this restaurant sports a Provençal-style interior and a patio shaded by a pergola overlooking the surrounding hillsides. Chef Pierre Marty crafts distinctive cuisine, packed with rugged flavours (chilli, ginger, etc.) and strong Mediterranean influences, yet his consummate signature dish is a textbook pithiviers of poultry and foie gras. Vegetarian menu, trolleys brimming with home-made bread and splendid cheeses, plus a remarkable wine list, in which the estate’s wines figure prominently. A bistronomic alternative is available at Les Vignes restaurant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15477;Ty Mad;France;Tréboul;3 rue Saint-Jean, Tréboul, 29100, France;48.1003179;-4.3470707;23;false;false;Seafood;On the heights of Tréboul in a quiet residential district, sample fresh dishes in which market availability and organic produce are much more than a fashionable concept. Dig into a buckwheat pie of aubergines and sheep’s cheese or black Guengat pork rich in local aromas, before making your way down the coastal path to the beach below for a nap! Vegan menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15478;Auberge des Vieilles Pierres;France;Flers;169 Le Buisson Corblin, Flers, 61100, France;48.755074;-0.530764;100;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This inn run by a couple of industry professionals is located on the outskirts of Flers. Behind an inviting frontage, it boasts a modern space with contemporary bistro-style furnishings, where you can tuck into the chef's up-to-the-minute dishes. Fast service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15479;Les Bories;France;Gordes;Route de l'Abbaye-de-Sénanque, Gordes, 84220, France;43.9223102;5.1938699;28;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In Luberon, “bories” are dry-stone huts built by and for shepherds and they inspired the architecture of this farmstead on the road to Sénanque Abbey. Overlooking sweet-scented scrubland, the grounds and gardens provide the foundation of the scrumptious provençal-focused cuisine, which showcases regional produce such as Sisteron lamb and Mediterranean fish without forgetting fruit and veg from Luberon.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15480;Le Moulin des Quatre Saisons;France;La Flèche;14 rue Gallieni, La Flèche, 72200, France;47.6968742;-0.0758236;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This delightful 16C building set in the town centre on the banks of the River Loir offers an absolutely enchanting setting whatever the season! The contemporary cuisine follows the seasons and is accompanied by a fine selection of wines (including some from Austria, the proprietor's home country). On sunny days, you can sit out on the terrace and soak up the enchanting setting.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15481;14 Avenue;France;La Baule;14 avenue Pavie, La Baule, 44500, France;47.2826254;-2.4053562;18;false;true;Seafood;Simplicity and quality are the watchwords here. Seafood ingredients are treated with the utmost respect: appetising when presented on the plate, then nicely prepared by chef Antoine Le Moal. The starter of crab, prawn and lobster is fresh and well seasoned, the skate wing carefully cooked, and the rum baba adds the final flourish of deliciousness. The modern interior is elegant, and the friendly service comes with a smile.;Terrace;[]
15483;Chez Éric;France;Montfuron;Place Daniel-Viguier, Montfuron, 04110, France;43.8354514;5.6937108;33;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;On the square of a charming village, this dry-stone building has everything you could wish for, from a shaded terrace to a bistro-style interior. To top it all off, the Provençal fare is full of flavour. For instance, the courgette flower stuffed with Brousse cheese and basil, Mediterranean meagre, rockfish stock with saffron and tarte Tatin with apricots from Provence go down a treat!;Terrace;[]
15484;Les Semailles;France;La Wantzenau;10 rue du Petit-Magmod, La Wantzenau, 67610, France;48.6571914;7.8372632;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This spruce Alsace house stands in a quiet side street. On the menu: top-notch ingredients, perfectly cooked, intelligently seasoned and paired and a catering tradition that upholds the practice of tableside service (a rack of veal is carved and langoustine is seared on hot stones right in front of the diner). We were particularly taken with the langoustines, asparagus and caviar – a masterpiece of scrumptious delicacy. When the weather is fine, make a beeline for the terrace shaded by a hundred-year-old wisteria.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15485;La Table du 6717;France;Ottrott;17 route de Klingenthal, Ottrott, 67530, France;48.4638775;7.422975;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Looking out onto the woods and decorated in harmony with nature, La Table offers a gourmet menu and a longer “discovery” option highlighting the day’s produce. The cuisine is modern and some of the vegetables come straight from the garden. Herdshire sirloin steak served with a variation of artichokes, onions and intense jus gives an indication of the style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15486;Abacus;France;Montpellier;26 rue Terral, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.60949;3.87294;16;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This couple from Rouen and Paris were drawn to the South of France, and landed here in the heart of Montpellier's Écusson neighbourhood, in their tiny restaurant with an intimate and warm atmosphere. Meticulous preparations, interplay of textures, seasonal dishes, smiling service and a savvy choice of wines: what more could you ask for?;;[]
15488;La Fourchette;France;Avignon;17 rue Racine, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9502603;4.8048699;45;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Collections of cutlery, cicadas, photos, greetings cards and knick - knacks: this bistro – with decor that is cluttered yet charming – is often full. Tasty cuisine of southern inspiration.;Air conditioning;[]
15489;Les 16 Clochers;France;Monthion;91 chemin des 16-Clochers, Monthion, 73200, France;45.6321704;6.3597897;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The terrace of this restaurant boasts a superb panoramic view over the valley's 16 church towers. The new, young and energetic team swear by local and organic producers (for their mushrooms, eggs and vegetables in particular) to create their well-crafted and market-fresh cuisine. The menu changes regularly and the terrace is popular in summer.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15491;Le Verre à Soie;France;Nyons;12 place des Arcades, Nyons, 26110, France;44.3604536;5.1404562;52;false;true;Fusion;After a career at Christian Têtedoie’s restaurant (Lyon), Fei - Hsin and Jérôme Lamy decided to take over this place. He still works as a sommelier, offering appetising food and wine pairings that showcase his wife’s lovely cooking, which is inspired by her Taiwanese origins. A wonderful marriage of French and Asian.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15492;C'Yusha;France;Bordeaux;12 rue Ausone, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.838173;-0.5683508;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Modern cuisine that makes full use of herbs and spices, created by a chef who works single - handedly in full view of the diners. Minimalist and intimately scaled (numbers are deliberately limited) in a resolutely contemporary setting.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15493;À l'Agneau;France;Pfaffenhoffen;3 rue de Saverne, Pfaffenhoffen, 67350, France;48.8440165;7.6082566;36;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In this Alsace inn dating from 1769, catering has been a family affair for seven generations. The two sisters now at the helm serve traditional cuisine that is in lockstep with the seasons and which they vary with the odd modern touch (we recommend the knuckle end of lamb confit for three nights, accompanied by bulgur wheat with sultanas and aromatic coriander).;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15494;Le Clos Y;France;Paris;27 avenue du Maine, Paris, 75015, France;48.8429138;2.3207894;77;false;false;Creative;Elegantly arranged next to each other, French cutlery and Japanese chopsticks symbolise the spirit of Le Clos Y. Quality ingredients, attentive execution, pursuit of subtlety: Yoshitaka Ikeda underscores once again all the well - established affinities of French and Japanese food. Simpler fare at lunchtime, "surprise menu" at dinner.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15495;Au Pont M;France;Wissembourg;3 rue de la République, Wissembourg, 67160, France;49.0354682;7.9443217;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Little Venice, this former local butcher's now draws crowds of diners keen to tuck into the creations of the chef – truly passionate about ingredients, he pays tribute to his suppliers by displaying their names. Here, the ultimate experience is to dine on the terrace on the banks of the Lauter, or inside with a view of the Église St-Pierre-et-St-Paul.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15496;Au Grès du Marché;France;La Petite-Pierre;19 rue du Château, La Petite-Pierre, 67290, France;48.8567051;7.3161437;54;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A warm welcome awaits you at this cosy restaurant in the old part of the village! The chef rustles up traditional cuisine made with seasonal ingredients and remarkably fresh meats, such as locally hunted venison, cooked in a stew at a low temperature and accompanied by ceps and spaetzle. He does also cook more contemporary dishes, such as duck tataki served with sauerkraut salad.;Terrace;[]
15497;À l'Agneau d'Or;France;Obernai;99 rue Général-Gouraud, Obernai, 67210, France;48.4618843;7.4789875;27;true;true;Alsatian;Head cheese with vinaigrette sauce, fillet of pikeperch on sauerkraut with Riesling sauce, a different kind of home-made tart every day. These are examples of the delights this Alsace establishment, typical both in appearance and philosophy, has in store for you. The decor is eminently inviting and the dishes exude the great flavour of the region's recipes.;Wheelchair access;[]
15498;La Maison Despouès;France;Puylausic;911 route de Montadet, Puylausic, 32220, France;43.4403003;0.9288137;74;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The former home of French pop singer, Pierre Vassiliu, who was N°1 in the hit parade in 1973, is now devoted to singing the praises of amberjack, sautéed girolles and a woody-scented sabayon or figs and fig leaves, served raw, in a chutney and in a sorbet. The culinary score is the work of chef Julien Razemon from les Landes, who honed his skills with the Coussau family. Julien plays a refined, gourmet melody, with the bonus of a view of the Gers hillsides or the Pyrenees (in fine weather) for some tables. Consummate technique, lashings of creativity and a knockout lineup of ingredients, all of which at eater friendly prices: what more could we want?;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
15499;Mademoiselle 10;France;Strasbourg;10 quai des Pêcheurs, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5830421;7.7579215;57;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the banks of the Ill, this charming restaurant delights its regulars with very reasonable prices, especially at lunchtime. Salmon and leek mosaic wrapped in nori, scallops with sweet potato and coconut cream, or fillet of duck, home-made cep gnocchi and “spicy cocoa” jus...;Air conditioning;[]
15500;La Suite;France;Alençon;19 place Auguste-Poulet-Malassis, Alençon, 61000, France;48.432503;0.0888481;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Slightly out of the town centre, you will sample seasonal family favourites tailored to today’s palates and entirely made from scratch. The chef is single-minded in his goal for flavour before all else. Examples include ravioles of prawns, creamy cauliflower and a velvety bisque. A concise menu, seasonal produce, generous helpings and incisive, legible flavours. All of which in a smart, buzzy vibe in the company of numerous locals.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15501;Zuem Ysehuet;France;Strasbourg;21 quai Mullenheim, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5900458;7.7635922;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a neighbourhood on the bank of the Ill, this inn clad in Virginia creeper also has a quiet picturesque terrace. In the tasty dishes, seasonal ingredients take pride of place: vegetables grown by the chef's father and intelligently cooked by his son. The lamb fillet, osso buco-style vegetables and date condiment is a good example. Terrific wine list, with a particularly good choice of wines by the glass.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15503;Chez Delagare;France;Montpellier;21 rue Jules-Ferry, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6047382;3.8791477;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;A delightful surprise awaits you opposite Saint-Roch station, in the Belaroïa complex. Chef is visible in the open kitchen concocting a concise, punchy menu, poised between bistronomy and street food. Appetising, colourful and aromatic: what more can we add?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15504;La Femme du Boucher;France;Marseille;10 rue de Village, Marseille, 13006, France;43.2878575;5.3833251;89;true;true;Meats and Grills;Established in a former butcher’s, energetic Laëtitia Visse, who trained at the Paris Ferrandi School before stints in star restaurants and renowned bistros (Guy Savoy, Alain Dutournier, Cyril Lignac, Olivier Nasti at Kaysersberg) has, unsurprisingly given the name, decided to focus on meat: homemade pâté, fried black pudding, sausages, pig’s trotters, etc… Equally in tune with the zeitgeist, her wine list is strongly focused towards natural and biodynamic wines. Casual service and vibe. In the finest traditions of a Gallic bistro!;Air conditioning;[]
15505;Les Jardins du Léman;France;Yvoire;30 Grande-Rue, Yvoire, 74140, France;46.3703254;6.3256417;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the pedestrianised medieval city, this appealing restaurant is laid out over several levels and furnished in a contemporary style. It proposes modern, impeccably crafted and generous dishes, all washed down with the best Savoie wines. Attentive welcome and service. Be sure to book if you wish to enjoy the splendid panoramic terrace overlooking the château and Lake Geneva.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15506;Dorangeville;France;Ainay-le-Château;3 rue du Vieux-Château, Ainay-le-Château, 03360, France;46.711996;2.6924642;64;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A picturesque medieval village provides the backdrop for this attractive 14C building, which now houses a restaurant boasting an elegant contemporary interior and a terrace overlooking the garden. Chef Quentin Dorangeville, who hails from France's Sarthe département, cooks up seasonal cuisine that is as meticulous as it is ambitious. Using fine ingredients, he creates striking combinations, such as confit egg, fragola sarda, chanterelles and chorizo. Good food and service with a smile!;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
15509;À l'Ami Fritz;France;Ottrott;8 rue des Châteaux, Ottrott, 67530, France;48.4569001;7.4228254;84;false;true;Alsatian;Mr Fritz is the chef - patron but the restaurant name also refers to the novel by Erckmann and Chatrian (1854), in which the hero sacrifices everything for good food. Quite a patronage for well - made Alsace cuisine, served in an interior that also showcases all the charm of the region.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15510;Côté Lac;France;Schiltigheim;2 place de Paris, Schiltigheim, 67300, France;48.6106587;7.7115734;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This raw concrete and glass parallelepiped looks slightly incongrouous standing on the banks of a small lake in an industrial area in the north of the city. The interior has a distinct modern loft feel with its modern lighting and contemporary paintings. Enjoy the current and carefully prepared dishes from a menu that changes regularly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15511;Zum Loejelgucker;France;Traenheim;17 rue Principale, Traenheim, 67310, France;48.5945792;7.4668003;50;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Alsatian;In a wine-growing village at the foot of the Vosges, this 18C Alsace farmhouse has bags of charm: tasty regional dishes, plus some more modern options, dark wood panelling, frescoes and a flower-decked courtyard in summer. Warm, friendly service and a family vibe.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15512;Auberge de la Chèvrerie;France;Griesheim-près-Molsheim;1 rue des Puits, Griesheim-près-Molsheim, 67870, France;48.499068;7.5345621;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away in the countryside, this tastefully appointed contemporary inn draws foodies likes bees to honey. The menu adds a tasty new twist to Alsace classics thanks to meticulously selected seasonal ingredients. For example, the goat’s cheese comes from the next-door cheese dairy run by the chef’s brother. The egg parfait ensconced in a crunchy nest and served with a frothy truffle-flavoured celery sauce is a culinary masterpiece and the nostalgic banana split is to die for!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15514;L'Établi;France;Lyon;22 rue des Remparts d'Ainay, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7528907;4.8301945;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant run by an alumnus of Christian Têtedoie is a real favourite. The lunch menu is good value for money, the dishes are in keeping with the times and seasonal (hake, asparagus, fennel, smoked raspberry): from start to finish it's a treat. Not to spoil anything, the service is also attentive.;Air conditioning;[]
15515;Les Bartavelles;France;Tours;33 rue Colbert, Tours, 37000, France;47.3956194;0.6882425;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Devoted to pleasure! First-rate, often local produce: smoked trout from the Moulin des Couvent or Touraine asparagus. Ingredients with crisp, legible flavours, such as rack of roast lamb, cocoa flavouring, roast fennel, potatoes and mushrooms. Chef Ghislain Damaye and his sister Véronique, who tends to the wellbeing of the front of house, pay tribute to the memory of French novelist Marcel Pagnol, in their smart, city centre bistro, courtesy of an ethos that seeks to share their love of good food.;Air conditioning;[]
15516;La Petite Table;France;Capbreton;7 quai de la Pêcherie, Capbreton, 40130, France;43.6521068;-1.4334549;78;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Whether seated on the terrace or inside, you are promised an enticing culinary interlude at this really inviting compact restaurant on Capbreton harbour. Generous and colourful dishes enhanced by citrus fruit and spices get to the heart of the matter, showcasing the local catch, lamb from the Pyrenees and vegetables from a market gardener in nearby Tosse. Don't miss the chocolate tart – a proper showstopper!;Terrace;[]
15517;Le Rouergat;France;Casteculier;4 place de la Mairie, Casteculier, 47240, France;44.1745381;0.6903872;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary bistro is bistronomic at lunchtime and gastronomic in the evenings. In the hands of a veteran chef from Aveyron, overflowing with contagious enthusiasm, this friendly, invariably-packed eatery focuses on local, seasonal produce, jazzed up with the occasional globetrotting souvenir. We tasted duck foie gras terrine with pineapple and ginger chutney followed by roast guinea fowl, cream of green peas and a samosa of pleurote mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15518;L'Auberge - Les Sources de Cheverny;France;Cheverny;23 route de Fougère, Cheverny, 41700, France;47.4835706;1.4269137;61;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Set in sprawling wooded grounds, the chic bistro of the hotel Les Sources de Cheverny serves fine and meticulous seasonal dishes that constitute something of a whistle-stop tour of the Loire Valley, as well as a tribute to local producers: vegetables from a market gardener in Mont-Près-Chambord, Sologne strawberries, Roi Rose pork loin from Touraine roasted in the fireplace… which takes pride of place in the dining area: here, cooking over a wood fire is a speciality!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15519;La Brasserie des Haras;France;Strasbourg;23 rue des Glacières, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5776061;7.74274;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A buzzing atmosphere at this large-capacity restaurant run by the great chef Marc Haeberlin, set in the former royal stables and stud farm, constructed during the reign of Louis XV. On the menu, modern cuisine, brasserie classics and a handful of local specialities. The superb contemporary décor with the original exposed roof structure is well worth a look !;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15520;La Table du Prieuré;France;Le Louroux;2 rue du Château, Le Louroux, 37240, France;47.1603294;0.7868118;95;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Pierre Drouineau, who hails from Sarthe (near Le Mans), runs this restaurant at the entrance to an attractive fortified priory, the jewel in the crown of this charming country village. Both the setting and the food are a delight, thanks in particular to the wealth of local ingredients: Touraine lentils, spelt from Manthelan, strawberries from Chouzé-sur-Loire. Think modern bistro cuisine, simple and flavoursome, in the form of dishes such as fillet of duck, roasted crisps, new potatoes from Louans and carrot ketchup – a creation that is packed with distinct flavours. Look out for the affordable lunch set menu!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15521;Le Poème de Grignan;France;Grignan;Rue Saint-Louis, Grignan, 26230, France;44.4200264;4.9090596;15;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This village restaurant is a poem indeed, with its old china, its flowers and flavours of Provence. Everything is carefully prepared, tasty and made on site. An invitation to revel in the best of the region.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15522;Le Piquebaure;France;Roussillon;166 avenue Dame-Sirmonde, Roussillon, 84220, France;43.9036786;5.2906515;92;true;false;Provençal;At the foot of Roussillon village, this picturesque dry-stone house proposes Provençal-inspired food in an enticing menu in which fresh produce is a major component. The restaurant’s pride and joy is its second terrace overlooking the wonderful Luberon countryside.;Great view,Terrace;[]
15523;L'Éternel;France;Vézelay;Hôtel de la Poste et du Lion d'Or, 9 place du Champ-de-Foire, Vézelay, 89450, France;47.4632669;3.7413976;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At the foot of the hill leading to Vézelay basilica, a major pilgrimage site, L'Eternel caters to more earthly needs, in a bright interior. The dishes are of a modern ilk, and contain a few nods to the region (pressed gambas with Morvan ham, mango and celery). The perfect prelude to a visit to the remarkable Musée Zervos (modern art museum). Comfortable guestrooms for a stopover.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15524;Le Capella;France;Vignieu;312 rue de la Garenne, Vignieu, 38890, France;45.6364721;5.4042472;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Soigné plating, interplay of textures, top-drawer ingredients: such are the winning arguments of Le Capella. The décor holds its own: two stone vaulted dining rooms, and a terrace facing the pool and garden. The high-flying wine list boasts 450 vintages (mainly from the Rhône Valley). Chapeau Cornu castle and its outbuildings also offer deliciously romantic guestrooms and a wellness centre.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15525;Beefbar;France;Saint-Tropez;Chemin du Pinet, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2590695;6.6585502;22;true;true;Meats and Grills;This is Saint Tropez’ delightful take on the beef bar concept that is gaining traction around the world. A stunning terrace overlooking the hotel pool allows red meat lovers and fans of exotic flavours to sample outstanding cuts of meat (wagyu and Black Angus beef), as well as dishes of South American and Asian origin.;Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15526;Le Galie;France;Prades;3 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Prades, 66500, France;42.618313;2.4291591;32;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Don’t bother lingering on the ground-floor, but make a beeline for the upstairs, modern, comfy dining room where a sweet young couple rustles up market-fresh fare in keeping with today’s tastes. The chef’s signature dish is fricassee of lobster with a lobster sauce and rice vermicelli.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15527;Suzanne;France;Lille;4 place Philippe-Lebon, Lille, 59000, France;50.6281833;3.0610758;48;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In his global hit, Leonard Cohen sang about Suzanne… At this place near the Palais des Beaux-Arts, tribute is paid to the cooking talents of a different Suzanne, pastry chef Elisa Rodriguez's grandmother. The chef demonstrates a clear preference for working with vegetables and aromatic herbs, and he also knows how to elevate his creative "bistronomy" dishes with tasty sauces (as did Elisa's grandmother), whether classically French, such as his beurre blanc, or of the more far-flung variety, as in his soya sauce, smoked eel and verjuice which accompanies his toasted bread pudding, ice cream with porcini mushrooms and mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15528;Le Tertre;France;Saint-Emilion;5 rue du Tertre-de-la-Tente, Saint-Emilion, 33330, France;44.89358;-0.15602;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;In a small cobbled street in the village, this restaurant has been given a new lease of life by an accomplished professional couple, who took over in 2020. Building on classical foundations, the creative dishes are inspired and harmonious. They showcase produce from the region: Landes duck, Basque country trout, fish from the ports of Aquitaine. In an extension to the dining room, the wine cellar hewn out of the monolithic stone has a table for four that is in great demand in the evening.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15529;Le Bonheur dans Le Pré;France;Lucinges;2011 route de Bellevue, Lucinges, 74380, France;46.1941114;6.3297239;90;true;false;Farm to table;In this 19C farmhouse deep in the countryside, authenticity is the name of the game. The chef creates a single menu (vegetarian version available) using top-notch local ingredients. The food is perfectly paired with wines from the splendid cellar (over 300 references) that abuts the dining room. The restaurant’s name is a playful reference to a well-loved French movie (1995) starring a plethora of Gallic movie stars.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15530;Le Saint Marc;France;Aups;7 rue Jean-Pierre-Aloisi, Aups, 83630, France;43.6274673;6.2244199;89;false;false;Provençal;The scenic village of Aups, south of the Verdon Gorges, invites you to make a bistronomic halt. Chef Alexandre Dimitch and his small team play a local, bistronomic score, rich in generous flavours, with truffles in summertime and bouillabaisse and bourride by the fireside in winter. Wine lovers may like to know that the next-door wine cellar becomes a wine bar in the evenings.;Terrace;[]
15534;Simone, Le Resto...;France;Paris;33 boulevard Arago, Paris, 75013, France;48.8355712;2.348067;40;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;A two-in-one establishment for twice the culinary pleasure: the wine cellar with a focus on biodynamic wines (a hundred or so metres away) and this lovely, little restaurant-cum-neighbourhood hangout, in which friends dine cheek by jowl in a bistro-style interior. The menu focuses on contemporary, locally sourced cuisine that's both healthy and flavoursome (enticing seasonal menu and an excellent value-for-money lunch set menu), eg white asparagus with mousseline sauce and onion pickles, or boudin basque with piment d'Espelette, beetroot and a red wine and beetroot sauce.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15535;À la Table des Lys;France;Saint-Etienne;58 rue Saint-Simon, Saint-Etienne, 42000, France;45.4548002;4.368955;78;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Recently taken over by its owner/chef, this small restaurant has been turned into a beautiful, contemporary eatery serving tasty and light modern cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15536;La Baratte;France;Saint-Denis-le-Vêtu;Le Bourg, Saint-Denis-le-Vêtu, 50210, France;48.9862703;-1.4040991;67;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Country cooking;Tasty wholesome food crafted from top-notch local produce at eater-friendly prices: such is the pledge of the Lefèvre couple who runs this welcoming inn built out of local stone – formerly the village bar and grocery shop. A bright, trendy interior with a pleasant alfresco space for sunny days and a rotisserie in the hall that fills the dining room with the enticing aromas of dishes of the day such as chicken colombo.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15537;Restaurant Arcé;France;Saint-Étienne-de-Baïgorry;630 Mixeleneko Bidea, Saint-Étienne-de-Baïgorry, 64430, France;43.1753362;-1.3487206;86;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;A delicious place to eat in a verdant spot at the foot of the Ispéguy Pass. The authentic Basque house has an attractive narrow dining area, the bright white of which echoes the immaculate garb of the Basque pelota players pictured on the walls. The market-fresh cuisine is seasonal and gives pride of place to local produce. Be sure to try the trout with blue cheese – straight from the restaurant's tank, the fish couldn't be fresher. In summer, tables are set up on the terrace, which is lined with plane trees. After your meal, stroll along the ivy-clad metal footbridge spanning the River Nive.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15538;La Table de Jean;France;Saint-Affrique;7 boulevard Émile-Trémoulet, Saint-Affrique, 12400, France;43.9570521;2.8842454;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It's no secret: when the food is good, it's a real hit! The cuisine is delicious and oscillates between traditional brasserie dishes (fillet of beef, knife-cut steak tartare, roast loin of veal etc) and Mediterranean touches such as pasta risotto with baby squid, chorizo and a shellfish jus. Reservations strongly recommended.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15539;La Ferme de l'Hospital;France;Bossey;272 rue de la Mollard, Bossey, 74160, France;46.1536315;6.1620771;22;true;false;Classic Cuisine;The years pass, but this well-known establishment on the Franco-Swiss border continues to uphold time-honoured traditions, as the warm, elegant interior, gleaming silverware and polished service bear witness. The chef concocts impeccably presented, pedigree French cuisine overflowing in flavour: duck ravioli and foie gras, venison in bacon and a pepper sauce…;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
15540;Pierre Sang in Oberkampf;France;Paris;55 rue Oberkampf, Paris, 75011, France;48.8647084;2.3723679;87;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Pierre Sang was a finalist in the 2011 Top Chef French TV show. As amiable as ever, we find him here deftly crafting delicate food designed to be shared and often dotted with Korean influences. The sensibly priced menus change regularly. We recommend taking a seat at the counter overlooking the open kitchen to make the most of the show!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
15541;L'Accent du Soleil;France;Saint-Martin-de-Londres;19 route des Cévennes, Saint-Martin-de-Londres, 34380, France;43.78678;3.73034;64;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Previously chef at Château de Mercuès, in the Lot, Philippe Combet serves up good seasonal cuisine, highlighting the region's produce. Truffle or asparagus menu, Quercy lamb... served by his pleasant and professional wife.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15542;Le Grand Bain;France;Paris;14 rue Dénoyez, Paris, 75020, France;48.8716343;2.3787074;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the bustling heart of Belleville, we love this hip bistro and its authentic industrial workshop vibe, complete with a central island counter, glazed partitions, untreated materials (brick and concrete) and numbered tables. Tuck into tasty small dishes – chalked up on the blackboard. The funky playlist reflects the tastes of the hipster night owls and discerning foodies who flock here.;;[]
15543;Les Saisons Gourmandes;France;Saint-Pierre-de-Jards;Place des Tilleuls, Saint-Pierre-de-Jards, 36260, France;47.0978048;1.9666647;69;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;With its beams painted "Berrichon blue", this is an extremely appealing spot. You are in for a culinary treat, safe in the hands of a chef who draws inspiration from tradition and premium ingredients, producing dishes such as foie gras poached in Reuilly or hay-steamed pigeon. In fine weather, be sure to reserve a table on the terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15544;Le BanH Hoï;France;Saint-Tropez;12 rue Petit-Saint-Jean, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2729654;6.6405713;20;false;false;Asian;Top marks for the decor. Subdued lighting, romantic atmosphere, black lacquered walls and ceilings, stylised buddhas serve as a backdrop to a friendly Vietnamese and Thai cuisine. Despite there now being a number terraces extending down the winding lane as far as the picturesque cobbled square, it is imperative to book: the tables are snapped up very fast.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15545;L'Air du Temps;France;Saint-Brieuc;6 rue Sainte-Barbe, Saint-Brieuc, 22000, France;48.5121936;-2.7605436;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This attractive old building with a grey granite façade is located in the town centre. Inside, contemporary features are woven into the original decor to great effect, and there is also a patio terrace for quiet dining. A successful transition to its new premises! As for the food, the chef continues to cook traditional dishes, mostly served in casserole dishes, such as the slow-cooked pork loin. Excellent cuisine at reasonable prices;Terrace;[]
15546;La Grappe d'Or;France;Riquewihr;1 rue des Écuries-Seigneuriales, Riquewihr, 68340, France;48.1666498;7.2988408;69;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Alsatian;This flower - decked house built in 1554 could not be more inviting and the characteristic regional interior has lost none of its yesteryear appeal. Classic regional delicacies on the menu: choucroute, baeckeofe, knuckle of ham, stuffed trout, etc.;Air conditioning;[]
15547;La Maison des Bois;France;Plaisir;1467 avenue d'Armorique, Sainte-Apolline, Plaisir, 78370, France;48.79769;1.95139;96;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the same family since 1926, this thatched-roof inn, clad in Virginia creeper has retained its character after a tasteful restoration. The same spirit prevails on the menu, with traditional fare and dishes inspired by market availability. Terrace in the shade of an old plane tree.;Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15549;Auberge du Parc Carola;France;Ribeauvillé;48 route de Bergheim, Ribeauvillé, 68150, France;48.197392;7.3344365;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In this charming pavilion-style setting, a stone’s throw from the Carola spring, chef Michaela Peters continues to delight a gourmet clientèle. Along with her pastry-chef partner, she creates authentic, inspired food, such as her organic Alsace egg cooked at 64° with summer truffles and new-potato mousseline, or her grilled ribs of wild boar with Kampot pepper, braised kale and lardo di Colonnata. Pretty terrace in the shade of the trees.;Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15550;La Machine à Coudes;France;Boulogne-Billancourt;57 rue Yves-Kermen, Boulogne-Billancourt, 92100, France;48.8275877;2.2407419;37;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Welcoming and bubbly owner Marlène has a knack for always surrounding herself with a motivated team. They are happy to work with the seasonal produce – scallops and squash – that goes into creating a single set menu at lunchtime, and a more creative and ambitious dinner menu. Good food and wine pairings. An enjoyable moment of bistronomy.;Air conditioning;[]
15551;Istr;France;Paris;41 rue Notre-Dame-de-Nazareth, Paris, 75003, France;48.867525;2.3577281;30;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This cocktail and oyster bar, inspired by New York but also influenced by Brittany, draws a youthful crowd to its packed terrace, plays loud music, and has a trendy atmosphere and decor (technical ducts on the ceiling, high tables, counter-bar). The menu features seafood and contemporary touches – all made from fresh produce.;;[]
15552;Langosteria;France;Paris;Cheval Blanc Paris, 8 quai du Louvre, Paris, 75001, France;48.8587844;2.342029;47;false;false;Italian, Seafood;On the seventh floor of La Samaritaine, in the heart of the Hotel Cheval Blanc, is this Italian-style seafood brasserie, a "branch" of Langosteria Milano. Lively atmosphere, cocktail bar, remarkable wine list, fresh fish and shellfish, pasta, delicious desserts... and one of the best expressos in Paris.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15553;La Table Saint-Martin;France;Sauxillanges;17 place Saint-Martin, Sauxillanges, 63490, France;45.5503376;3.3706355;87;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Table Saint-Martin specialises in spot-on, tasty food that keeps pace with the seasons. Top-notch quality, consummate culinary skill and distinctive flavours – the stage is set for a fine dining experience. Patio in the inner courtyard.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15556;L'Auberge - Maisons Glenn Anna;France;Sainte-Anne-d'Auray;56 rue de Vannes, Sainte-Anne-d'Auray, 56400, France;47.7038353;-2.9487441;18;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Ste-Anne-d'Auray is known for its sanctuary and pilgrimages, and Pope John Paul II is said to have stopped off at this restaurant in 1996. But it is by no means stuck in the past: the new generation concocts delicious fare, in which premium seafood takes pride of place, as in the half-cooked tuna with a medley of tomatoes and béarnaise sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15557;Au Roman du Vercors;France;Beauvoir-en-Royans;1 ancienne route de Presles, Beauvoir-en-Royans, 38160, France;45.1208517;5.33918;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The chef and his wife now welcome guests on the slopes of the Vercors in the listed medieval site of a former Carmelite convent (flanked by a museum, garden and conservatory orchard with fruit varieties native to South Grésivaudan, which can be visited after your meal). The menu showcases market-fresh seasonal and regional produce, racks reminiscent of walnut drying sheds adorn the interior, outdoors is a pleasant, shaded patio.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15558;Le V;France;Saint-Rémy-de-Provence;9 chemin Canto-Cigalo, Saint-Rémy-de-Provence, 13210, France;43.7850582;4.8410388;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A chef with a fine CV to his name (including Lucas Carton and Anne - Sophie Pic) has taken over the kitchen of this restaurant, and quickly made his mark! With a motivated team supporting him, he cooks classic cuisine, adding modern touches, and the result is a hit.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15559;Le Wauthier by Cagna;France;Saint-Germain-en-Laye;31 rue Wauthier, Saint-Germain-en-Laye, 78100, France;48.8958991;2.0882;87;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This lovely restaurant located in Saint - Germain - en - Laye also boasts a chic bistro interior and attentive service. Dishes are prepared using quality market ingredients and will please a modern palate. Try dishes like: Piedmont risotto with lobster and beurre blanc, braised sweetbread escalopes, celeric mousseline and Albufera sauce.;;[]
15560;Le Sérac;France;Saint-Gervais-les-Bains;22 rue de la Comtesse, Saint-Gervais-les-Bains, 74170, France;45.891935;6.711612;87;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The discreet entrance opens into a large, bright and elegant room. The chef's cuisine is inspired by the seasons. The sharing menu allows you to indulge in fine cuts of meat or fish. In short, a fresh and colourful selection of carefully prepared dishes, such as calf's head and pan-fried foie gras or a tartlet filled with raw and cooked seasonal vegetables, and, for dessert, a delicious warm soufflé flavoured with passion fruit. Enjoy your meal in a pleasingly modern interior that offers views of the mountains. Attentive service. A lovely place.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15561;La Table d'Aimé;France;Rivesaltes;4 rue Francisco-Ferrer, Rivesaltes, 66600, France;42.7700821;2.8776854;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Established within a winery and appointed in a style that blends Provençal and industrial elements (wrought iron, barrels of wine, bare brick walls), the restaurant offers inspired market-fresh food, organic whenever possible, washed down with wines from the estate. In summertime, the leafy patio is irresistible.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
15562;Bistrot Paul Bert;France;Paris;18 rue Paul-Bert, Paris, 75011, France;48.8522609;2.3848213;61;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The façade of this pleasant bistro promises "cuisine familiale". Translate this as: feuilleté of calf sweetbreads with mushrooms, and roast venison with cranberries and celeriac purée. Generous, tasty dishes are prepared without frills. You will be asking for more but be sure to save some room for the rum baba!;Interesting wine list;[]
15563;Auberge du Poids Public;France;Saint-Félix-Lauragais;Route de Toulouse, Saint-Félix-Lauragais, 31540, France;43.4497309;1.8851368;62;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Following in her parents' footsteps, Céline Taffarello continues to showcase the best of the terroir, with produce such as magret of black mountain duck with sarawak pepper and delicious, perfectly seasoned roasted peach with verbena. The cassoulet, which has won several awards, is particularly popular. The panoramic terrace, with its pretty view of the Lauragais plain is delightful. Comfortable guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15564;Mazette !;France;Annecy;15 faubourg Sainte-Claire, Annecy, 74000, France;45.8973637;6.1231283;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Mazette is on point! When Laura, the pastry chef, and Maximilien, the chef, opened this small traditional bistro decked out in brick and wood, we followed its cohort of loyal regulars there for a meal. On the menu: French bistro classics (pâté en croûte, pie with comté cheese and truffle ham, grilled pork belly), nods to the proprietors' roots in Alsace (spaetzle, poultry vol-au-vent with morels, apple pie, rhubarb compote) and, on the blackboard, a short list of dishes for sharing.;Air conditioning;[]
15565;Le Clos de Chevreuse;France;Chevreuse;33 rue de Rambouillet, Chevreuse, 78460, France;48.7062289;2.0379563;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There's no doubt about it: chef Laurent Gasnier, whose CV speaks volumes (stints at Le Bristol, George V and with the Troisgros), knows how to choose good, mature ingredients, both vegetables and fish. He transforms them into generous dishes, impeccably cooked and seasoned, such as the courgette ball, organic Brousse cheese and basil pistou, or indeed the sea bass, coconut, young broad beans and a butter sauce. In summer, you'll want to sit out on the charming flower-decked terrace in the quiet courtyard. The restaurant is located in the pretty village of Chevreuse – all the more reason to make the trip.;Terrace;[]
15566;Gare au Gorille;France;Paris;68 rue des Dames, Paris, 75017, France;48.8836067;2.3200069;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Marc Cordonnier has now found his niche in the Batignolles neighbourhood. He knows how to prepare ingredients without subverting their essence, and devises bold, unfussy and original cooking with more personality than posturing. Meanwhile, his acolyte, Louis Langevin, is a benevolent mine of information on a fine array of natural wines.;;[]
15567;Daniel et Denise Créqui;France;Lyon;156 rue de Créqui, Lyon, 69003, France;45.7622588;4.8472142;32;true;false;Lyonnaise;Joseph Viola, Best Craftsman of France, reigns over this dyed-in-the-wool, patina-aged bolthole, oozing in authenticity. Patriotic line-up of Gallic recipes, high-flying technique (calf’s head, quenelle of pike) founded on superlative ingredients with an eye on the seasons. His signature dish is a “porkpie” of sweetbread and foie gras – to die for!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15568;Le Canut et les Gones;France;Lyon;29 rue Belfort, Lyon, 69004, France;45.7785703;4.8346198;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A unique atmosphere, somewhere between bistro and secondhand shop – formica bar, wooden floorboards, vintage tapestry, collection of old clocks on the walls –, modern cuisine in tune with the seasons, a wine list boasting over 300 types... In a little - frequented area of La Croix - Rousse, this is definitely one to try out.;Interesting wine list;[]
15569;La Trinquette;France;Grandcamp-Maisy;7 rue du Joncal, Grandcamp-Maisy, 14450, France;49.3871513;-1.0500271;51;false;false;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;The exuberant young chef of this historic establishment, both warm and welcoming, invites you to taste food of incomparable freshness. So fresh that the mussels, scallops, sole and turbot seem to have come straight from the fishing boat! Lovely veranda - lounge next to the house and a terrace on the other side.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15571;La Table du Royal;France;Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat;Royal Riviera, 3 avenue Jean-Monnet, Saint-Jean-Cap-Ferrat, 06230, France;43.70229;7.32912;75;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Geoffroy Szamburski skilfully crafts a modern score, in tune with the seasons and the environment that showcases produce from the Riviera and the Nice hinterland (Gamberoni of San Remo oxalis, Menton lemons). On the dessert side, head pastry chef Lucas Simoncini is equally on the ball with a Piedmont hazelnut soufflé and ice cream. Picture yourself sitting on the terrace with the sea as far as the eye can see…;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15572;Éclosion;France;Saint-Paul-en-Jarez;40 avenue du Château, Saint-Paul-en-Jarez, 42740, France;45.4922948;4.5665188;42;true;false;Creative;Having set up shop in this handsome early 20C château, whose interior sports a cosy, contemporary vibe, youthful Pierre Carducci rolls out cuisine that is as creative as it is bold, in which organic produce, notably from his father's market garden, takes pride of place. Pink trout, lemon and green Sichuan pepper paste reveal their full depth when paired with steamed and fermented garden cabbage. Everything is served in tableware made by the chef’s mother in another detail that is emblematic of the house ethos. Hats off too, to the eclectic wine list, with a preponderance of organic tipples. Uncluttered guestrooms, named after plants growing in the grounds, are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15574;Ricordeau;France;Loué;13 rue de la Libération, Loué, 72540, France;47.9933079;-0.1526003;92;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Sit out on the pleasant terrace set up in the garden, on the banks of the River Vègre, and treat yourself to a fine dining interlude courtesy of the chef's cooking, which is always in touch with the seasons. The contemporary dishes, which are deliberate and meticulous, make use of the finest local ingredients, including supreme of Loué chicken stuffed with onions and morel mushrooms, first-harvest vegetables and a creamy poultry jus. La Table du Coq, the hotel's second restaurant, serves simpler fare.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15575;La Table de Cybèle;France;Boulogne-Billancourt;38 rue de Meudon, Boulogne-Billancourt, 92100, France;48.8281492;2.2422127;41;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A Franco-American couple is at the helm of this neo bistro. San Francisco-born Cybèle rustles up original recipes in the kitchen, using premium produce: warm lentil salad with a poached egg and button mushrooms or canederli and minestrone of winter veggies… Fine dining and sustainable development go hand in hand here.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15576;Le Moulin à Vent;France;Saint-Germain-des-Vaux;10 route de Port-Racine, Saint-Germain-des-Vaux, 50440, France;49.712844;-1.9026822;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;By the coastal road leading to the headlands, this old country inn is a lovely refuge from the elements. A short menu showcases inventive cuisine made from local produce (such as pigeon, lamb, fish, abalone) by a chef with a clear interest in Japanese culinary tradition. The interior has a pared-back decor and a view of the sea and the cove, Anse Saint-Martin.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15577;Le Bistrot des Bonnes Femmes;France;La Rochelle;5 rue des Bonnes-Femmes, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1625035;-1.1490777;70;false;false;Modern Cuisine;"Bistronomie" all round in this trendy and convivial place! Distinct and precise dishes with no fuss or frills are created from top - notch ingredients, such as fish sourced from the fish market and vegetables from the nearby covered market. In fine weather, enjoy your meal on the pleasant patio.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15578;Le Clos Heurtebise;France;Remiremont;13 chemin des Capucins, Remiremont, 88200, France;48.0077248;6.6034088;46;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Away from the hustle and bustle, this traditional house run by a friendly couple serves contemporary cuisine. Sample dishes such as marinated Arctic char with pea mousse, or pavlova with gariguette strawberries. The summer terrace boasts a lovely view of the Vosges mountains.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15579;L'Assiette Roannaise;France;Saint-Forgeux-Lespinasse;97 place de Verdun, Saint-Forgeux-Lespinasse, 42640, France;46.1232361;3.930811;22;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Now here is a restaurant that has a sense of the original! The interior design is very contemporary and, similarly, the chef keeps his ear to the ground for the latest trends and techniques. His dishes are aesthetically pleasing, with the onus on creativity and freshness.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15580;La Ferme de Cupelin;France;Saint-Gervais-les-Bains;198 route du Château, Saint-Gervais-les-Bains, 74170, France;45.88904;6.7000265;89;false;true;Regional Cuisine;Recently taken over by Florian and Lauriane Langellier, a young couple with a jaw-dropping CV (Megève’s Four Seasons under Gatillon, Megève’s Flocons de Sel with Emmanuel Renaut, L'Armancette and finally Père Bise with Jean Sulpice where he worked as a pastry chef and she was in the front-of-house), this hotel complex in the upper reaches of the resort has changed hands smoothly as the former owner-chef, Romain Desgranges, continues to helm the kitchen. The set menu showcases local produce from the lakes (arctic char), rivers (crayfish) and forests (game in season), without forgetting forays to Italy (Piedmont hazelnut gnocchi and Colonnata bacon). A fine dining experience featuring tasty modern cuisine with a knockout view of Mont Blanc as a bonus. What’s not to like?;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15581;Le Central;France;Roanne;20 cours de la République, Roanne, 42300, France;46.0395894;4.0636404;45;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Michel and Marie-Pierre Troisgros are behind the family's other gourmet establishment set in a former 1920s hotel. The vibe is smart yet casual and the warm, vintage decor is inspired by the brasseries of yesteryear. You will sample a concise menu that changes daily, flanked by à la carte suggestions in a traditional register, although often reworked with creative twists, illustrated by a profiterole with mustard-flavoured ice cream. The place is always busy, bearing witness to its well-deserved success.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Wheelchair access;[]
15583;O'Plaisir des Sens;France;La Roque-Gageac;sous la Grande-Vigne, La Roque-Gageac, 24250, France;44.81262;1.21018;24;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This spruce stone house has earned a fine reputation for itself in Périgord. Bruno enthusiastically whips up dishes tailored to modern appetites featuring premium regional delicacies: free-range geese, partridges, a nose-to-tail ethos and fruit and veg from local growers. Bistro/roast spit menu at lunchtime, gastronomic in the evening. The shaded patio by a fountain is bliss come summertime.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15584;La Fabrique;France;Brie-Comte-Robert;1 bis rue du Coq-Gaulois, Brie-Comte-Robert, 77170, France;48.696689;2.6124819;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This industrial - style loft is well hidden at the end of a small alley. Guests enjoy the warm, convivial atmosphere at this contemporary restaurant, which offers delicious, bistro - style gourmet cuisine.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15585;Aux Armes de France;France;Corbeil-Essonnes;1 boulevard Jean-Jaurès, Corbeil-Essonnes, 91100, France;48.6053994;2.4665788;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This former coaching inn run by Yohann Giraud, a chef who has worked in several Michelin-starred restaurants, has a pleasantly hushed atmosphere. On the menu: dishes bursting with flavour, such as the signature macaroni stuffed with foie gras, celeriac and tartufata au gratin with parmesan, cream and a veal jus, or the oh-so-delicate millefeuille with a caramel sauce. The charming service completes the picture.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
15586;L'Amélyss;France;Grenoble;3 boulevard Gambetta, Grenoble, 38000, France;45.1914164;5.7211473;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A young couple have turned this establishment into an endearing eatery with an offbeat tongue-in-cheek sense of humour. The modern fare of chef Héloïse Pelletier is sparkling and vibrant, the ingredients flawlessly fresh, the seasonings precise, and the flavours subtly blended. Well-thought out wine list by monsieur who’s in charge of the service. One of the best in town!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15587;Le Bistrot des Voraces;France;Lyon;13 rue d'Austerlitz, Lyon, 69004, France;45.7755351;4.8346761;33;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Do you just have a healthy appetite or are you downright starving? Either way, this bistro in the Croix-Rousse district will sate you. Youthful Cédric Blin honed his skills in top establishments like Les Crayères (Reims), before going solo here. Genuinely eater-friendly, almost bargain prices – not to be missed!;Terrace;[]
15588;Cinq Mains;France;Lyon;12 rue Monseigneur-Lavarenne, Lyon, 69005, France;45.75886;4.82674;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this very touristy area alongside the Saône, this house with exposed stone walls is now the HQ of Grégory Cuilleron, with his brother and a friend at his side. The cuisine has a distinctly gastro - bistro and modern tendency, and is accompanied by a selection of well - chosen minor wines – the three partners are oenophiles.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15589;Le Grenier à Sel;France;Le Mans;26 place de l'Éperon, Le Mans, 72000, France;48.005617;0.1955079;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At the entrance to medieval Le Mans, the team of this former salt loft has one goal in life: to please themselves and their customers! A contemporary vibe and top-quality ingredients (lobster, turbot, foie gras) with bold, authentic flavours, all of which washed down with a fine selection of Rhône, Loire and Bordeaux tipples.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15590;L'Atelier;France;Nice;17 rue Gioffredo, Nice, 06000, France;43.7016302;7.2761729;27;true;true;Regional Cuisine;Originally from Vendée, chef Stéphane Chenneveau must have been a little crazy – or "fada" in the Nice dialect, to dare to revisit the city’s ubiquitous socca, flatbread made with chickpea flour... And yet it remains a firm fixture of the menu. The chef has never ceased to evolve, crafting flavoursome regional recipes, together with a more ambitious carte blanche menu which is seasonal and reflects his mood of the moment. Splendid biodynamic wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15591;La Maison;France;Gaujac;1 rue du Presbytère, Gaujac, 30330, France;44.0789058;4.5774945;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;You are made to feel right at home here at La Maison, once a winegrowers' home, with a magnificent stone interior. Creative cuisine is served in the form of dishes in which a number of different elements are juxtaposed. Ludovic Davouze always makes sure to showcase local producers, and enjoys adding an element of surprise, with original combinations of flavours such as just-seared little tuna marinated with chives, with smoked aubergine and miso sauce. The patio is a joy in fine weather.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15592;Danton;France;Lyon;8 rue Danton, Lyon, 69003, France;45.7560642;4.8573024;51;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this friendly neo-bistro, the menu gets straight down to business - it is concise, to the point and stars dishes that are as hearty and unpretentious as they are delicious, while the wine list showcases regional (but not only) producers. The chef’s consummate technical know-how shines through in his perfect mastery of cooking times and techniques, while the desserts are fully equal to those of any high-flying pastry chef. A warm welcome and slick, smiling service. If they are full, try L'Escapade Danton next-door.;Air conditioning;[]
15593;La Croix Blanche;France;Donnemarie-Dontilly;2 place du Marché, Donnemarie-Dontilly, 77520, France;48.4776942;3.1345904;27;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Hard at work in the kitchens, the chef makes it a point of honour to use great seasonal ingredients. The dishes are a taste sensation, for example, the chicken supreme with mixed vegetables. Definitely a place you will want to tick off.;Wheelchair access;[]
15594;Le Chateaubriand;France;Paris;129 avenue Parmentier, Paris, 75011, France;48.869354;2.3714371;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Basque chef Iñaki Aizpitarte attracts an international clientele of food lovers with his unadulterated French bistro in this institution that wholeheartedly embraces the bistronomy movement, of which he was one of the initiators. The place has retained its original interior decor, the likes of which you would have come across in the 1930s, which it juxtaposes with a neo-retro mix of zinc, slate, high ceilings and narrow tables. Their winning formula is a single set menu with original marriages of flavours. Ingredients and wines are carefully selected from independent producers. Reservations are essential.;Interesting wine list;[]
15595;Le Restaurant;France;Saint-Priest;9 bis avenue de la Gare, Saint-Priest, 69800, France;45.6894516;4.936687;21;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Le Restaurant is 10 minutes from Lyon Saint-Priest Parc Technologique. Sit at your table surrounded by artwork by young artists and enjoy well-crafted traditional cuisine, with a few exotic twists. The menu is rooted in the terroir: lentils and runny poached egg flavoured with bacon, or artisan-made hot sausage poached in wine and cut into good generous slices!;Air conditioning;[]
15596;Marius et Janette;France;Paris;4 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.86539;2.30156;18;false;true;Seafood;This elegant yacht-style décor, replete with fishing rods, nets and copper portholes, caters to discerning food lovers. The chef highlights fish and seafood, with a menu that is renewed daily, according to the catch. Carpaccio of salmon and basil, grilled seabass to share or linguine with lobster (a house speciality): a festival of flavours!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
15597;Auberge de la Rivière;France;Velluire;Rue du Port-de-la-Fouarne, Velluire, 85770, France;46.4064515;-0.893102;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A riverside location and ivy-clad façade set the charming rural scene for this Vendée inn overlooking the old stone bridge – ideal for a gourmet get-away! The chef works with top produce, aromatic herbs and subtle seasonings and each dish reveals the hallmark of his enthusiastic culinary quest. Make sure you save room for the desserts – to die for! The menu changes fortnightly. A few attractive rooms overlooking the River Vendée are available, together with boats and mountain bikes for rent should you feel more energetic. Perfectly idyllic!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15600;Le Sully;France;Lyon;20 rue Sully, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7706095;4.8437919;75;true;true;Lyonnaise;A small bistro, opened by Julien Gautier (owner of neighbouring M Restaurant) in a modernised bouchon vein, tantalises diners with dishes such as chicken liver gâteau, veal liver en persillade (with parsley and garlic) and calf's head with sauce ravigote. It is tasty, well made and you will be going back for more!;Air conditioning;[]
15601;Le Restaurant du Château;France;Saint-Sernin-du-Bois;2120 route de Saint-Sernin, Saint-Sernin-du-Bois, 71200, France;46.8407358;4.4327596;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At the foot of the 11C château and facing the lake, the tastefully revamped interior of this restaurant is depicted by two vibes: historic vaults on one side and industrial overlooking a water feature on the other. The food features the same contrast between tradition and modernity. A genuine fine dining experience.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15602;La Table de la Mainaz;France;Gex;Route du Col-de-la-Faucille, lieu-dit La Mainaz, Gex, 01170, France;46.3626315;6.0258533;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At the Faucille Pass, between the Geneva Basin and the Haut-Jura, this regional landmark, decked out in contemporary fashion, commands a stunning view of Mont Blanc and Lake Geneva. Attractive dishes in the zeitgeist are presented in surprise menus starring premium ingredients: Arctic char, turbot, calf’s sweetbread. Its sibling, Le Panorama, is more affordable.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15604;Le M des Avenières;France;Cruseilles;Les Avenières, lieu-dit Chenaz, Cruseilles, 74350, France;46.0577584;6.0995509;96;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;On the banks of the Salève, this early 20C stately home set in over 150 acres of grounds, houses a welcoming hotel-restaurant. The period interior (wainscoting, stone fireplace, coffered ceiling, mirrors, chandeliers and old banquettes) provides the perfect foil to sample a modern lineup tinged with tradition, illustrated by veal cutlet served in a casserole dish and paired with garlicy gratin dauphinois. Other examples include conchiglie stuffed with goat’s cheese, walnuts and a hint of honey. A portion of the produce is sourced locally: cheese, honey, veggies, as are the wines, most of which are organic. Splendid sweeping view over the Alps that extends from Mont Blanc as far as Lake Annecy!;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15605;Mouton-Benoit;France;Loire-sur-Rhône;1167 route de Beaucaire, Loire-sur-Rhône, 69700, France;45.5604959;4.8084888;46;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This roadside establishment founded in 1822 was once home to the "Mères" Dumas' stoves. In winter you can enjoy the chef's speciality: lièvre à la royale, prepared according to the recipe immortalised by Senator Couteaux more than a century ago! Round off your meal with one of the delicious desserts.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15606;La Ferme aux Grives;France;Eugénie-les-Bains;Place de l'Impératrice, Eugénie-les-Bains, 40320, France;43.6976714;-0.3783839;84;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A village inn that has rediscovered its colours of old. It has a vegetable garden, old beams and terracotta floor tiles. An ideal setting in which to relish a nicely revamped version of the local cuisine. The exquisite suites and rooms promise a perfect night’s sleep.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15608;Le Saltimbanque - Auberge du Moulin;France;Eaucourt-sur-Somme;1500 lieu-dit du Moulin, Eaucourt-sur-Somme, 80580, France;50.07127;1.88764;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This endearing establishment gazing down over the Somme Valley is in the hands of a local lad in love with his region’s produce. The several-course surprise menu showcases ingredients from sustainable farms and small-scale fishing. Suave subtle flavours for a slap-up meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15610;Le Saint-Pierre;France;Besançon;104 rue Battant, Besançon, 25000, France;47.2435348;6.0222311;93;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Savour fine dining with a predominance of fish dishes and quality produce in an elegant setting of open stonework and modern touches. The St - Pierre makes for an idyllic experience!;Air conditioning;[]
15611;Le Manège;France;Besançon;2 faubourg Rivotte, Besançon, 25000, France;47.2332896;6.0339346;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At the foot of the citadel, this former military riding arena specialises in delicate, flavoursome fare rich in regional twists (such as a mushroom crust cooked in vin jaune or their amazing sliced black pudding). The self-taught chef is a stickler for perfection – as the first and last bite will confirm.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15612;Numéro 75;France;Avignon;75 rue Guillaume-Puy, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9449431;4.8142025;68;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This friendly restaurant is decorated in vibrant colours and is set in a 19C townhouse. It serves seasonal cuisine based on fresh local produce, which can be enjoyed in the courtyard when the weather is fine.;Terrace;[]
15613;Racine;France;Nancy;9 rue Stanislas, Nancy, 54000, France;48.6931351;6.1822747;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located just a stone's throw from Place Stanislas, the restaurant of the young chef Martin Debuiche (formerly Pierre Vigato's second-in-command, at Apicius) and his partner, butcher and restaurateur Alexandre Polmard, offers market cuisine through a short and appetising menu. The ingredients are good quality, the recipes are well put together. Tasty.;Terrace;[]
15614;Le Bistrot;France;Bonnétage;5 chemin de l'Étang-du-Moulin, Bonnétage, 25210, France;47.1975217;6.7214189;59;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Croûte forestière, veal entrecôte, fillet of trout, Morteau sausage: traditional produce and recipes are on the menu at the pleasant Le Bistrot. It is the perfect complement to the Étang du Moulin's restaurant. Simple and well - made food – you will be coming back for more!;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15615;La Table du Lion;France;Bayeux;71 rue Saint-Jean, Bayeux, 14400, France;49.2760088;-0.69846;65;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At Le Lion d'Or, the chef works his magic with produce sourced in Normandy that he embellishes with Asian flavours. An unexpected culinary marriage inspired by his travels in Asia, particularly Japan and Thailand. Add to this, flawless culinary technique and seasoning and you will be roaring with pleasure!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15617;Au Bistronome;France;La Ferté-Bernard;11 rue Bourgneuf, La Ferté-Bernard, 72400, France;48.1852215;0.6545734;49;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Grills;The luminous, high - ceilinged interior is decorated in the manner of a contemporary bistro. The same concept extends to the menu, without forgetting tradition and a distinct fondness for charcoal - fired preparations – rib of beef, steak, andouillette, tuna and sole, all of which are cooked directly in the dining room. Simple and generous.;Wheelchair access;[]
15618;Auberge de la Poutre;France;Bonlieu;25 Grande-Rue, Bonlieu, 39130, France;46.6003467;5.8550159;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the hub of a pretty village in the Jura lakes area, this family-run inn dating from 1740 plays on its rustic charm. Chef François Moureaux works with fine ingredients to create delicate and tasty contemporary cuisine, but doesn't neglect to revisit local specialities. As for the decor, the establishment is named after one notable feature: its 17m-long ceiling beam that comes from a 3m3 fir log!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15620;Au Bœuf Rouge;France;Niederschaeffolsheim;39 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Niederschaeffolsheim, 67500, France;48.772397;7.7343951;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Run by the same family since 1880, this restaurant is quite the local institution. Chef François Golla serves modern cuisine without turning his back on tradition: take, for example, his carpaccio of langoustine royale served with crispy vermicelli. His genial wife takes charge of the restaurant floor, and his sister serves wines, including some by the glass, often from magnums – a really nice touch! An appealing place, in no small part due to the smart interior in which wood features heavily.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15621;André;France;Valence;Pic, 285 avenue Victor-Hugo, Valence, 26000, France;44.9177696;4.8854912;50;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This bistro replete with history celebrates the signature dishes of each generation of the Pic family. These include, most memorably: Jacques's mosaic of red mullet and foie gras, a surf and turf creation as audacious as it is aesthetically pleasing, to which his daughter Anne-Sophie added the bouillabaisse jelly, or the vol au vent filled with crayfish, calf sweetbreads and Nantua sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15623;Le Banquet des Sophistes;France;Strasbourg;5 rue d'Austerlitz, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5788917;7.7518956;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It’s no mean feat to get a table at this bistrot in the Krutenau neighbourhood. A well-deserved success for this address that offers an unbeatable set menu at lunchtime and a more elaborate menu in the evenings: scallop tempura with ginger, avocado and pomegranate-lemon dressing, or Basque pork chop with stuffed cabbage and polenta. Well-crafted, fresh and aromatic dishes, prepared in a spirit of eclecticism that pushes gently into fusion cuisine. Stimulating for the tastebuds and a friendly atmosphere to boot, what’s not to like ?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15624;Bassas;France;Pamiers;Place des Trois-Pigeons, Pamiers, 09100, France;43.1165476;1.6103036;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Bassas couple, whom we first encountered at Deymier (also in Pamiers), has renovated this old town centre building from top to toe. The striking result is both understated and smart and provides the perfect foil to the food which shines the spotlight on local producers. Inspired selection of local wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15625;L'Arbre;France;Montpellier;10 parvis Oscar-Niemeyer, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.6059736;3.8980582;18;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;On the ground floor of a building whose tree-inspired avant-garde design is by architect Sou Fujimoto, this restaurant serves a patriotic line-up of gourmet cuisine as its delicious veal liver, Madeira sauce and mashed potato amply demonstrate! White predominates in the 2.0 brasserie interior. Near the canal, the lush green patio draws the crowds like bees to honey, but many are also lured to the swish rooftop bar perched on the 17th floor, which commands a panoramic view over the city that stretches as far as the Mediterranean!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15626;Le Saint Jean;France;Saint-Jean-d'Arvey;2496 route des Bauges, Saint-Jean-d'Arvey, 73230, France;45.5858959;5.9963813;39;false;true;Modern Cuisine;You will be as impressed by the scenery as by your food. By a winding road through the Bauges mountains, this ancient village inn commands a view of Chambéry below. Romain honed his culinary craft in top establishments, and Anaïs, a wine lover, suggests pairings that stimulate and awaken our tastebuds. The food is a bona fide catalogue of local produce (fish from the lake, locally reared lamb), whose flavour and character the chef enhances in modern, seasonal dishes. Surprise menus invite the diner to “let go”…;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15627;L'Hibiscus by Jérémy Lasserre;France;Sauveterre-de-Comminges;Hameau de Gesset, Sauveterre-de-Comminges, 31510, France;43.0210599;0.6777627;75;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In his stronghold in the Hôtel du Barry, at the foot of the Pyrenees, is a chef who knows his stuff: his intelligent, technically sound cuisine (eg low-temperature cooking, espumas and dashi stock) also hints at the 14 years he spent in Asia. The onsen-style slow-cooked egg served with a trilogy of Tarbais beans and mushrooms is one of his specialities. Attentive service and comfortable guestrooms mean there's no reason not to prolong the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
15629;Fischhutte;France;Mollkirch;30 route de la Fischhutte, Mollkirch, 67190, France;48.4895682;7.3666638;77;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A hostel with an inviting atmosphere, well-made and tasty traditional cuisine, a dynamic team: the recipe for success at this pleasant restaurant, which has a following of regulars.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
15632;Les Tilleuls;France;Autrans-Méaudre en Vercors;111 rue de Puilboreau, Autrans-Méaudre en Vercors, 38880, France;45.1757;5.545886;20;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The fifth generation, embodied by the owners’ daughter and her husband, is continuing the family saga. The chef signs traditional recipes that call upon fine local produce – caillette (pâté), Vercors trout and a dessert based on Grenoble walnuts and green Chartreuse. The flavoursome food is served in a bright, contemporary interior with an Alpine twist.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15633;Les Jardins Sothys;France;Auriac;Route de Darazac, Auriac, 19220, France;45.2014894;2.1420925;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Plots of aromatic herbs, Japanese enclosure, rose garden etc. These gardens (entry fee charged), by the famous cosmetic brand, mix poetry and the cult of the virtues of nature. In the restaurant, the chef elevates the Corrèze terroir by using lots of spices – he worked in Asia and the West Indies for a long time – for an aromatic and confident result.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15634;Le 1544;France;Bordeaux;10 place de la Bourse, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8413804;-0.5705072;49;false;true;Farm to table;On the first floor of the central edifice of Bordeaux’ iconic Place de la Bourse, this entirely revamped bistro (vintage armchairs, interlocking parquet floor and coffered ceilings) commands drop-dead views over a masterpiece of 18C architecture and the city’s emblematic "water mirror". Succulent, up-to-date bistro fare poised between tradition and modernity.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Wheelchair access;[]
15635;Sevin;France;Avignon;10 rue de Mons, Avignon, 84000, France;43.9501821;4.8067173;16;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Right next to the Palais des Papes, this medieval residence is steeped in history. Inside, cooking up a storm with the support of a motivated young team, chef Guilhem Sevin has devised a modern culinary repertoire. If possible, take advantage of the terrace overlooking the square. Nice wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15636;Gaztelur;France;Arcangues;Chemin de Gastelhur, Arcangues, 64200, France;43.4428384;-1.5334324;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This magnificent abode dating from 1401 – antique furniture and an exquisite lush green patio – shouldn’t divert your attention from the matter at hand: market-fresh food with high-end Basque and Spanish ingredients. All of which is crafted by a star chef, Fabrice Idiart, who composes a culinary score rich in nostalgic recipes (duck foie gras, mimosa poached egg, Basque Kintoa pork). Superlative setting.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15638;Le Sin;France;Biarritz;1 avenue de la Plage, Biarritz, 64200, France;43.46232;-1.5722297;47;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Within the Cité de l'Océan, Le Sin’s eye-catching wave-shaped architecture commands drop-dead views of the sea and Château d'Ilbarritz. The ingenious chef-craftsman selects first-rate ingredients which he incorporates into an elaborate bistro menu that changes regularly. An example: farm-reared pigeon, gutsy garlic-flavoured jus and mashed potato.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15639;Le Parc;France;Obernai;169 route d'Ottrott, Obernai, 67210, France;48.4624597;7.4715155;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the outskirts of the town, this imposing Alsatian hotel/restaurant has been in the family since 1954. The elegant dining room features honey-coloured panelling, a coffered ceiling and a crystal chandelier. Dishes are up-to-date and carefully prepared.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15640;Hostellerie des Châteaux;France;Ottrott;11 rue des Châteaux, Ottrott, 67530, France;48.4568389;7.4226428;46;false;false;Modern Cuisine;An elegant and intimate backdrop for modern cooking with good classical foundations : millefeuille of Rosheim snails with wild garlic and parsley, or fillet of turbot, champagne beurre blanc and black bean cream. Comfortable guestrooms that combine the contemporary with traditional Alsatian style.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15641;Ferme Lizarraga;France;Urrugne;550 Chemin de Lizarraga, Urrugne, 64122, France;43.36928;-1.6921201;43;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In lovely natural surroundings (lizarragameans "ash forest" in Basque), Véronique and Stéphane Poulin's restaurant is set in a converted 17C farmhouse with its character very much intact – it tastefully blends original rustic and pastoral cachet with more contemporary details. The chef serves up a sincere and skilful take on market-fresh cuisine that is infused with bold, distinctive flavours, such as the semi-cooked Landes duck foie gras, the line-caught hake served with excellent gnocchi and toasted sesame espuma, not forgetting the melt-in-the-mouth biscuit with almonds, strawberries and basil ice cream. Opt for the terrace in the shade of a century-old walnut tree and enjoy the efficient service of the lady of the house while taking in the view of the Rhune. A real gem!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15643;L'ID;France;Lingolsheim;11 rue du Château, Lingolsheim, 67380, France;48.55553;7.6820993;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Named ID in tribute to its charismatic owners, Isabelle and Denis Vetter, this restaurant is tucked away in a plush 18C edifice that boasts a grandiose original staircase. A muted contemporary interior sets the stage for seasonal dishes that alternate between daring creations (seafood casserole dish with black garlic aïoli) and comforting, wholesome family favourites, such as juicy tender beef tournedos with aligot (a sort of mashed potato made with Alsace tomme in this case).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15645;Le Mangevins;France;Tain-l'Hermitage;7 rue des Herbes, Tain-l'Hermitage, 26600, France;45.0700084;4.8365177;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Here, bistro spirit and modernity are skilfully allied in the decoration. The food, created by a young couple of self-taught chefs, fêtes the market and proves to be meticulously prepared. The single set menu changes every day and for lunch on this occasion we sampled the Bigorre black pork shoulder, mustard seed juice and a Breton buckwheat shortbread, chocolate cream and praline emulsion. The dishes are explained in a friendly atmosphere, and, as is fitting in such a place, the menu is accompanied by a fine selection of regional wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15646;La Musardière;France;Giverny;123 rue Claude-Monet, Giverny, 27620, France;49.075219;1.5359297;93;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the heart of the village, close to Claude Monet's house and the Musée des Impressionnismes Giverny, La Musardière serves a bistronomy lunch menu at Le M and more ambitious dining options in the evening at Révélations. The convivial, contemporary bistro setting is complemented by a pleasant terrace that receives plenty of sun in summer. A number of guestrooms are available, should you wish to extend your stay.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15647;La Table - Sébastien Gravé;France;Bayonne;21 quai Amiral-Dubourdieu, Bayonne, 64100, France;43.4917996;-1.4744764;69;true;false;Farm to table, Cuisine from South West France;After the success of Pottoka in Paris, the chef, a key figure on the Bayonne bistronomy scene, is back on his home turf. All smiles behind the stove, he prepares dishes inspired by the best produce South-West France has to offer, including natural hake from Saint-Jean-de-Luz, marinated and charred mackerel and Ibaïma pork shoulder. You can eat at the zinc-topped counter, at the large table d'hôtes with friends or in the kitchen (there is a table for two, for a more immersive experience). An inviting restaurant with a convivial atmosphere!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15648;La Grande Georgette;France;Reims;18 rue Tronsson-Ducoudray, Reims, 51100, France;49.253549;4.0317044;46;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name is a nod to an amusing tradition, which involved naming the fire engine’s ladder after the captain's wife. In this 1900’s industrial-style building next to the former Chanzy fire station, chef Julien Raphanel rustles up a high-flying score: line-caught cod, seagrapes and shellfish in champagne, braised sweetbread and girolles in vin jaune with a chocolate extravaganza to finish. The terrace with its breathtaking view commands a priceless view of Notre Dame Cathedral. Little Georgette next-door offers a tasty lineup of French family favourites at reasonable prices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15649;Auberge Le Bouc Bleu;France;Beblenheim;2 rue du 5-Décembre, Beblenheim, 68980, France;48.1579865;7.3244519;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Romain Hertrich and sommelier Romain Lambert, after stints in top establishments in France and abroad, are at the helm of this pretty half-timbered inn. Pan-fried girolles with pak choy, pumpkin seeds and pine nuts, or seared beef chuck steak with onion and beetroot pickles... All produce are from organic or small producers. Thoughtful food-wine pairings.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15650;Chantoiseau;France;Paris;63 rue Lepic, Paris, 75018, France;48.88777;2.33471;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In 1765, Mathurin Roze de Chantoiseau opened the first modern restaurant (individual tables and dishes to choose from on a menu) in the Louvre area. In homage to him, brothers Nicolas and Julien Durand work in tandem to create lovely modern cuisine, which is also inspired by the French classics and occasionally makes use of noble products, as in the delicious puff pastry pigeon pie.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15651;Signature Montmartre;France;Paris;12 rue des Trois-Frères, Paris, 75018, France;48.8844432;2.3412778;33;false;true;Fusion;Located in touristy Montmartre, this Lilliputian restaurant sports a minimalist interior and a buzzy vibe. At the helm of the restaurant, that is fully deserving of its success, is a Franco-Korean couple (bookings highly recommended). He warmly welcomes diners, proffering insightful wine tips along the way, while she deploys her pastry talents in the kitchen. The Franco-Asian repertory quietly feeds you well, courtesy of intelligent recipes scattered in subtle aromas, illustrated by a tataki of bonito with cucumber pickles, a watercress crepe and a vitello tonnato sauce jazzed up with mint – flavoursome and surprising! Consider us smitten!;;[]
15652;Le Bistrot du Maquis;France;Paris;69 rue Caulaincourt, Paris, 75018, France;48.8895388;2.3362549;49;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;André Le Letty, formerly of the Anacréon, has set up shop in the renowned Rue de Caulaincourt and specialises in bistro classics. Try pressed ox cheek in crystallised lemon, veal kidneys in mustard, roast hake, and not forgetting the house specialty, pressed duck served in two stages.;;[]
15653;Le 1903;France;Talloires-Montmin;Auberge du Père Bise, 303 route du Port, Talloires-Montmin, 74290, France;45.8394313;6.2106522;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At the 1903 (the year the Auberge du Père Bise was established), Jean Sulpice rolls out the house signature dishes and new takes on regional classics, like this gratin of crayfish tails "new style". The particularly attentive waiting staff will guide you through the treasures of the cheese cellar. The superb rotunda with floor to ceiling windows overlooks the mythical bay of Talloires.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15654;Au Cheval Noir;France;Kilstett;1 rue du Sous-Lieutenant-Maussire, Kilstett, 67840, France;48.6749778;7.855847;78;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Food lovers come galloping to the Cheval Noir – the Black Horse! Behind the façade of this 18C half-timbered house, a team of two brothers works with fine ingredients to create traditional cuisine that is served in a stylish, bourgeois interior.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15655;La Table de Maïna;France;Montrouge;18 rue Perier, Montrouge, 92120, France;48.813636;2.317862;55;false;true;Fusion;This fine establishment is tucked away in the heart of Montrouge. The globetrotting chef, who trained in top establishments such as Nobu Matsuhisa, lets her creativity run riot in flavoursome, fusion-inspired recipes. The ingredients, spices and produce, which come from all over the world, are exquisitely blended. The garden terrace is a hit in fine weather.;;[]
15656;La Table de Jeanne;France;Tignes;14 avenue de la Grande-Motte, au Val-Claret, Tignes, 73320, France;45.4575361;6.8990226;52;true;false;Savoyard;This mountainside restaurant, the brainchild of the Bouvier family (of Les Suites, Ursus, Panoramic), is depicted by generous dishes in which country produce takes pride of place. Warm, welcoming and a fine selection of reasonably - priced wines.;;[]
15657;Le Bistro Urbain;France;Montpellier;5 rue Alexandre-Cabanel, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.608369;3.8733614;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At the helm of this spacious, light-filled bistro in the heart of Montpellier is Cédric Sangenito, a chef with a seamless CV and a firm grasp of classic techniques. His modern, somewhat inventive cuisine features Japanese barbecue cooking and lacto-fermentation. He highlights good fresh produce, especially seasonal vegetables from market gardeners, to which he devotes a surprise menu at lunchtime and in the evening. The menu is updated every week – although the rum baba, the emblematic dish of the house, is a mainstay (in various guises). A diligent and professional team is at your service.;Terrace;[]
15658;La Poste;France;Urmatt;74 rue du Général-de-Gaulle, Urmatt, 67280, France;48.5266053;7.3241305;52;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Fans of tradition will be happy to discover this family - run inn installed opposite the former town hall. Game in season, truite au bleu ("blue trout"), Rossini beef tournedos, goose foie gras and country terrines... The food is generous and the atmosphere pleasant.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
15659;L'Auberge de la Pomme;France;Les Damps;44 route de l'Eure, Les Damps, 27340, France;49.3031618;1.1781719;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The name may evoke Normandy and its apples, and it may have a half-timbered façade that is typical of the region, but that's where the cliché ends! Inside you will encounter a very contemporary decor, with a bright dining area with large picture windows affording views out over the garden. The dishes, which showcase local producers, include carpaccio of scallops from Normandy, poached monkfish with a coulis of watercress from Cailly-sur-Eure, and farm-raised veal chop casserole.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15661;Sadarnac;France;Paris;17 rue Saint-Blaise, Paris, 75020, France;48.8593481;2.4053637;39;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This tiny restaurant is located in a semi-pedestrian street with a village feel in the heart of the 20th arrondissement. In the spruce little dining room, tuck into "surprise" menus concocted with market ingredients by youthful Lise Deveix. Welcoming, well-run establishment.;Terrace;[]
15662;À l'Aigle d'Or;France;Osthouse;14 rue de Gerstheim, Osthouse, 67150, France;48.4019756;7.641886;83;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;At one corner of this imposing village house, the wrought-iron eagle seems to herald your arrival. Inside, tuck into classic dishes (home-made goose foie gras terrine with port jelly, Paul Haeberlin's mousseline of frogs’ legs, sole meunière prepared tableside…) in a traditional and inviting setting. Less formal atmosphere in the winstub.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15663;In Vino Veritas;France;Strasbourg;25 place de la Cathédrale, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5822823;7.7506033;40;false;true;Italian;This Italian restaurant is in an ideal location at the foot of the magnificent cathedral.The concise menu offers dishes that are generous and tasty, with a focus on the produce : foie gras agnolotti, zucca al forna, costolette di vitello con burro e salvia, affogato... Pleasant terrace in fine weather and a splendid wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15664;Monique, boire et manger;France;Dijon;33 rue Amiral-Roussin, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3199593;5.0399227;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;What would Monique, the grandmother of chef Clara Reydet, have made of this charming bistro where seasonal vegetables are the star attraction? Only positive things, for sure! Clara cooks without inhibitions, draws on various influences and wins everyone over with her lamb kefta, creamy raw red cabbage or garam masala roasted carrots, toum (Middle Eastern garlic sauce) and reduced carrot jus. This fusion cuisine with vegetarian leanings is to be enjoyed in the simple, spruce space with lots of wood. Small terrace on the pedestrianised street.;Terrace;[]
15665;D'une Île;France;Rémalard-en-Perche;Domaine de l'Aunay, lieu-dit l'Aunay, Rémalard-en-Perche, 61110, France;48.4627754;0.7914779;54;true;true;Country cooking;The country annexe of Paris's Septime. Come to enjoy enduring, seasonal and rustic cuisine that is rooted in its surroundings, drawing solely on quality produce from the nearby markets (in Sarthe and Normandy) and, to a lesser extent, what is harvested in the farm's vegetable garden. The tastefully decorated dining room exudes rustic chic. In the same spirit, a few guestrooms extend an invitation to linger a little on this wooded hill in the Perche region, with its fruit trees, hives, and even a sauna overlooking the natural surroundings. A laudable initiative.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15666;L'Antiquaire;France;Laval;64 rue de Vaufleury, Laval, 53000, France;48.0647437;-0.7785364;30;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The name may suggest an antique dealer's, but despite the absence of old tomes, 19C paintings and 1930s objets d'art, you won't be disappointed! Set outside of the town centre, L'Antiquaire is a very pleasant and welcoming restaurant, with a façade completely smothered by foliage. Chef Jérôme Lebreton's generous cuisine with flashes of creativity is sure to delight the palate with its distinctive flavours, not least his combination of veal sweetbreads and kumquats. Worth noting: There is a completely vegetarian set menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15667;Le Bistro du Grand Cerf;France;Lyons-la-Forêt;31-32 place Isaac-Bensarade, Lyons-la-Forêt, 27480, France;49.3987701;1.4770116;81;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This rustic - style neo - bistro has bags of character, with its exposed beams, brickwork and a pretty terrace in the cobbled courtyard. It serves bistro - style food squarely focused on the terroir: what are you waiting for?;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15668;La Vieille Tour;France;Strasbourg;1 rue Adolphe-Seyboth, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5812902;7.739377;54;false;false;Classic Cuisine;We could not but fall in love with this authentic inn, run by a couple of professionals. Their generous restaurant, close to the “Petite France”, nurtures traditional flavours (breast of chicken with jus, cod fillet with vegetables and mushrooms, game in season) depending on market availability. The simple décor is embellished with humorous posters on Alsace by the renowned Tomi Ungerer.;Air conditioning;[]
15669;Auberge Baechel-Brunn;France;Merkwiller-Pechelbronn;3 route de Soultz, Merkwiller-Pechelbronn, 67250, France;48.9384615;7.8287879;68;true;false;Modern Cuisine;With Thomas in the kitchen and Esther in the dining room, the Limmacher’s restaurant is a family business! The chef favours premium ingredients, local whenever possible and concocts primarily traditional recipes with a welcome hint of creative modernity. For example, he proposes a new take of the familiar flammkuchen or adds a puff pastry Wellington-inspired spin to local venison, flanked by a gloriously velvety game sauce. The menu changes frequently, to the delight of the (numerous) regulars.;Air conditioning;[]
15671;Casse-Cailloux;France;Tours;26 rue Jehan-Fouquet, Tours, 37000, France;47.3878418;0.6835971;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This gourmet bistro, so popular that it is often taken by storm (bookings advisable), is established in a residential neighbourhood near Prébendes garden and flanked by a summer patio. Sincerity depicts the seasonal dishes chalked up on a slate, all of which washed down with delicious Loire wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15672;Beefbar;France;Monaco;42 quai Jean-Charles-Rey, port de Fontvieille, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7277253;7.4217471;39;true;true;Meats and Grills;On the docks of Fontvieille Marina, this trendy "meat bar" serves quality beef (Wagyu, Black Angus and some from France) but also street food, gourmet salads and a few fish dishes. It has a trendy decor and is very popular with local diners. Check out the impressive meat maturation display cases.;Air conditioning,Great view,Valet parking;[]
15673;L'Eau d'Oust;France;Rohan;6 rue du Lac, Rohan, 56580, France;48.0728366;-2.7524339;58;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;An old farmstead on the way out of the village near a pond paints the inviting picture. In a contemporary, welcoming décor, the owners focus on genuinely wholesome food with the occasional whimsical touch of creativity. The ingredients are fresh and first - rate, and the service is with a smile. A pleasant meal every time.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15674;L'Âtre;France;Honfleur;25 cours des Fossés, Honfleur, 14600, France;49.4188835;0.2346274;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;After stints at some prestigious Michelin-starred establishments in Paris, then at Château Cordeillan-Bages in Pauillac, chef Julien Lefebvre, who hails from Normandy, set up shop a few years ago in this charming medieval town. His cooking is both in step with the seasons and very much in the spirit of the times. Open kitchens giving onto a dining space with contemporary decor or a terrace for sunny days.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15675;La Dînée du Viguier;France;Figeac;4 rue Boutaric, Figeac, 46100, France;44.6097674;2.035057;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this long-established restaurant in the city centre, chef Grégory Tavan serves up seasonal cuisine with a hint of creativity. The setting is the castle's elegant guardroom, which has been treated to a contemporary makeover.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15676;Auberge de Montpoupon;France;Céré-la-Ronde;Le Moulin Bailly, Céré-la-Ronde, 37460, France;47.2518052;1.1395442;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A friendly inviting inn established at the foot of the castle of Montpoupon. The interior sports a fashionable patchwork of rustic (bare stone and beams) and contemporary details, while the menu takes you on a gourmet tour of the Val de Loire’s succulent produce. Prices that make sense and a terrace with a view of the castle.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15677;Auberge à l'Agneau;France;Roppenheim;11 rue Principale, Roppenheim, 67480, France;48.8424921;8.0537046;19;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This family-run institution dating from 1902 is located in a handsome 17C half-timbered building. It is a great place to indulge in hearty food: in the kitchen, dishes simmer under the watchful eye of the chef, who loves his region. Stand-out dishes include local and meat specialties. Expect unpretentious, generous and authentic fare, served in an inviting setting… plus a warm welcome!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15678;La Petite France;France;Montélimar;34 impasse Raymond-Daujat, Montélimar, 26200, France;44.55843;4.74901;80;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;It is worth seeking out this little place up a cul - de - sac in the heart of the old town. It features a lemon yellow decor and traditional cuisine based on the freshest produce.;Air conditioning;[]
15679;Lao Siam;France;Paris;49 rue de Belleville, Paris, 75019, France;48.8730687;2.3807795;22;false;true;Asian;Lao Siam stands out from the crowd of Asian eateries in Belleville. Founded in 1985 by the current owner's parents, who were originally from Thailand and Laos, this neighbourhood restaurant is an institution that celebrates the cuisines of these two countries. Everything is made on site by the three Souksavanh brothers for fine, flavoursome food that is full of flavour: crying tiger and its spicy sauce, thadeua nem (Lao crispy rice salad), tom kha soup, red ruby dessert with coconut milk. If the place is full, head to the adjoining Ama Siam, which has a short menu of specials.;;[]
15680;Bistrot de la Place;France;Trémolat;Le Bourg, Trémolat, 24510, France;44.8755904;0.8305268;58;false;false;Regional Cuisine;In the heart of the village where Chabrol filmed Le Boucher (1970). Old stonework, beams and tasty country cuisine including andouillette and confit de canard.;Terrace;[]
15682;Les Terrasses - Le Cottage Bise;France;Talloires-Montmin;390 route du Port, Talloires-Montmin, 74290, France;45.8399093;6.2113706;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A luxurious and smart restaurant, a lovely terrace shaded by chestnut trees with the lake as its horizon, and modern cooking seasoned to a T mean you will enjoy your dining experience here. The chef prepares trout gravlax with asparagus, monkfish glazed with carrot and turmeric jus, and picanha of Black Angus beef with crunchy vegetables.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15684;La Pie qui Couette;France;Nîmes;1 rue Guizot, Nîmes, 30000, France;43.8389664;4.3582738;25;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Bang in the heart of Nîmes’ bustling food market, this eatery, run by a seasoned chef, will knock the socks off your tastebuds. Market fare crafted with fresher than fresh produce from the neighbouring market stalls. House specialties include matured meat, cod brandade, chopped beef tartare and île flottante (vanilla custard and meringue). Hearty helpings, an intelligent wine list, tightly packed tables and a good-natured, jovial vibe. No bookings possible, open from 11.30am to 3pm and always packed (try and come off peak at the weekend).;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
15685;Les Trente Pas;France;Villard-de-Lans;16 avenue des Francs-Tireurs, Villard-de-Lans, 38250, France;45.0693598;5.5497908;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A short stroll from Villard church will take you to the site of this portrait - sized restaurant in the heart of the village. Local artwork adorns the dining room, while the chef pays homage to market - fresh produce with a soft spot for the Vercors, assembled according to his inspiration. Fine handiwork!;;[]
15686;La Forge;France;Le Subdray;1 rue de la Brosse, Le Subdray, 18570, France;47.010211;2.2934566;44;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a small village about 15km from Bourges, this restaurant run by a young couple is definitely one to recommend. Everything is home-made, most of the vegetables come from the garden, and freshness is the order of the day. Simple menu at lunchtime during the week, more elaborate options on the dinner menu and at weekends.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15687;Bistrot de l'Oustalet;France;Gigondas;5 place du Rouvis, Gigondas, 84190, France;44.1633382;5.0051838;81;true;false;Provençal;Fronted by an exquisite patio that is taken by storm in fine weather, this bistro occupies the site of the old village bakery, whose lovely stone wood-fired oven brings a promise of gourmet delights. The chef crafts dishes steeped in Mediterranean aromas in a concise menu that showcases market-fresh produce. Fine choice of wines by the glass: we are in Gigondas, after all!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15688;La Table de Kamiya;France;Cagnes-sur-Mer;52 promenade de la Plage, Cagnes-sur-Mer, 06800, France;43.6560898;7.1622151;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Japanese chef Takayuki Kamiya and pastry chef Claire, his French-Japanese wife, have set up shop on the seafront of Cagnes-sur-Mer. The food is inspired by their adopted homeland (Provence) and their family backgrounds. Their set menus feature dishes inspired by France and Provence (sea bass in an almond crust, courgettes and pistou) and elevated by discreet Japanese touches (wakame, oloshi sauce, yuzu). Both the delicious peach dessert with verbena jelly and the rum baba, a house classic, are out of this world.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15690;Getaria;France;Guéthary;360 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Guéthary, 64210, France;43.4233837;-1.6087991;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You would be well inspired to make a halt in one of the Basque Coast’s most beautiful villages. In addition to a small room decked in white wainscoting, this inn boasts an exquisite patio shaded by plane trees tucked away to the rear. The chef, former vice-champion of pâté en croûte (pork pie) which he changes each season, also has a knack with fresh fish straight from the local fish auction (illustrated by a tataki of tuna or a ttoro – shellfish soup), as with Hispanic-Basque produce. The lunchtime menu is a bargain.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15691;Moris;France;Vendôme;77 rue du Change, Vendôme, 41100, France;47.7942084;1.0677768;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the banks of the Loir, this bistro adjoins the bridge that leads to the old town. The chef swears by short supply chains and puts the seasons firmly in the spotlight in his cooking, which is accompanied by carefully chosen natural wines. When the weather is fine, head for the two terraces, one of which is on the first floor, overlooking the river. Delightful.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15692;Les Jardins du Cloître;France;Marseille;20 boulevard Madeleine-Rémusat, Marseille, 13013, France;43.3356374;5.4234637;25;true;false;Farm to table;Set in a former monastery, this training centre run by the Auteuil Apprentices charity, has a restaurant that is open to the public. Supervised by a professional chef, the brigade of young trainee cooks enthusiastically prepares fine meals in a bistronomic spirit that keeps pace with the seasons, all of which sourced with regional, preferably organic produce. A laudable ethical approach which aims to forge the next generation of restaurateurs.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15693;Roza;France;Nantes;3 place de la Monnaie, Nantes, 44000, France;47.21321;-1.56527;46;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative;In his restaurant in the centre of Nantes, chef Jean-François Pantaléon expresses his passion for the produce of the Pays de Loire terroir. The wine list gives pride of place to hand-picked small-scale wine producers. The cosy interior and inviting, laid-back atmosphere further add to this delightful dining experience.;Terrace;[]
15694;L'Arôme;France;Dijon;2 rue Jean-Jacques-Rousseau, Dijon, 21000, France;47.325864;5.0453091;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This gourmet bolthole offers a taste of happiness. Chef Kadoguchi delivers well-executed and beautifully presented dishes, alternating between Japanese specialties (gyozas) and French recipes (pollack, Provençal sauce) or mixing the two, as he does in his excellent picanha with Asian sauce. Harmonious textures and flavours, spot-on cooking techniques, a fine selection of wines and a perfect welcome – what's not to like?;Air conditioning;[]
15695;La Tulipe Noire;France;Fleury;1 rue du Ramonétage, Fleury, 11560, France;43.2299441;3.1329202;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a tastefully converted wine barn, the chef and his wife are in tune with the seasons, in particular thanks to their cottage garden that supplies the majority of veggies here. Do not be misled by the apparently simple names of the dishes, each one is a compendium of consummate technique and happily reinterprets the classics (onion soup, tarte tatin).;Terrace;[]
15696;La Forge;France;Fontaine-Daniel;8 place de l'Ondine, Fontaine-Daniel, 53100, France;48.27828;-0.67424;46;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fontaine Daniel is the epitome of a French country village steeped in history and the birthplace of the famous toiles de Mayenne fabrics. Overlooking a pond and the forest, this restaurant is housed in a former outbuilding of a Cistercian abbey, which became the hub of this textile manufacturing enterprise in the 19C. Chef William Blondel, who has worked as far afield as New Zealand, cooks primarily with local produce that he doesn’t hesitate to enhance with modern and creative twists of his own creation. It’s unique, sometimes unsettling, but always hits the spot, depicted by dishes like mackerel, cauliflower and a coffee-based sauce!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15699;L'Auberge Saint Jean;France;Saint-Jean-de-Blaignac;8 rue du Pont, Saint-Jean-de-Blaignac, 33420, France;44.8134329;-0.1389675;51;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A couple of industry professionals is at the helm of this contemporary-style restaurant nestling on the banks of the River Dordogne, which is visible just outside the picture windows. The menu includes a number of dishes in which chef Thomas L'Hérisson accurately combines ingredients in a modern and somewhat creative style. The salmon confit with dill yoghurt, green aniseed baby turnips and vinegar-preserved mushrooms, or the veal sweetbreads marinated in miso, floured and fried, soy sauce beetroot and artichokes are the perfect reflection of the chef's personality. The fine wine list – with some 550 labels – has something for everyone. Manuela, the obliging hostess, lavishes diners with attentive service.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15701;Le Pré Gourmand;France;Eyragues;175 avenue Max-Dormoy, Eyragues, 13630, France;43.8446289;4.842528;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This inviting establishment on the way out of the village specialises in seasonal Mediterranean cuisine: courgettes, aubergines, olive oil and lemon accompany local fish and lamb from La Crau. The sublime south-facing terrace overlooks the leafy, well-tended garden. At the end of a flower-decked meadow, a handful of authentic guestrooms done up in Mediterranean colours await you.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15702;La Grange des Halles;France;Rungis;28 rue Notre-Dame, Rungis, 94150, France;48.74803;2.35059;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Rungis is more than just the famous food market known to every chef, it is also an old town and home to a this somewhat idiosyncratic bistro. The venue provides the setting for the chef to concoct market-fresh (what did you expect?) cuisine that combines visual appeal with crisp flavours. Very pleasant shaded terrace to the rear.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15703;L'Ortensia;France;Saint-Gervais-sur-Mare;Domaine de la Pièce, Saint-Gervais-sur-Mare, 34610, France;43.650547;3.04086;21;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Ortensia means hydrangea in Occitan and this is how it is spelt in the local lingo! Run by a sister-brother team, Lise and Mathieu, this restaurant is in a picturesque village miles from anywhere. The veteran chef is equally at home with gnocchi in gorgonzola and lobster as with duck from Landes, croaker from Corsica or apricots from Provence. Only the veggies and aromatic herbs are local, like mimosa-style celtuce (stem lettuce) from Pezènes-les-Mines and poutargue (fish roe). Super fresh produce and spot-on pairings depict the culinary scene, served in a bright, airy dining room-cum-conservatory which leads onto a panoramic terrace. Five comfortable very spacious guestrooms overlooking the blissfully peaceful countryside.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15704;La Table du Moulin;France;La Roche-l'Abeille;1 route des Aurières, La Roche-l'Abeille, 87800, France;45.5818538;1.2494478;25;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;The bistro of hotel-restaurant Moulin de la Gorce is now within the same walls as the gourmet restaurant, but with its own separate dining area and terrace. Rest assured, the chef of Moulin de la Gorce still treats his guests to traditional hearty dishes that are replete with produce from the local terroir. No doubt about it, this is tasty fare!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15705;La Cuisine de Bertrand;France;Les Sables-d'Olonne;22 quai de Franqueville, Les Sables-d'Olonne, 85100, France;46.49658;-1.78855;93;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Opposite the fishing harbour, it is well worth keeping an eye open for this low-profile restaurant. The chef unashamedly crafts textbook French recipes with the objective of showcasing first-rate ingredients in dishes that hit the spot every time. Diligent service.;Wheelchair access;[]
15707;La Suite S'il Vous Plaît;France;Les Sables-d'Olonne;20 boulevard Franklin-Roosevelt, Les Sables-d'Olonne, 85100, France;46.49509;-1.7928095;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located behind the casino and the beaches, this establishment is a breath of fresh air on the local restaurant scene. In a trendy bistro decor, to a soundtrack of jazz and R&B, chef Mélanie Sire serves up dishes that echo market availability of ingredients. Skilfully playing on textures and flavours, she prepares simple but delicious plates, including creations such as the beautifully presented trilogy of oysters, or the perfectly cooked pluma ibérica pork. We will be coming back for more... s'il vous plaît!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15709;La Table du Balthazar;France;Rennes;28 rue Vasselot, Rennes, 35000, France;48.1085757;-1.6776722;85;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You can expect a meal in a smart, stylish brasserie vibe whipped up by talented chef Benjamin Jourdren, former second who became head chef in 2020. Located in what must be Rennes’ most elegant hotel, the cooking shines the spotlight on essentially Brittany produce of top-notch quality. The recipes have been reworked, illustrated by the buckwheat-flavoured butter that flanks white poppy seed bread, quickly seared scallops cooked in soured milk, ravioles of kale cabbage with citron, or hay-flavoured creamy quenelle paired with apple. The tables are elegantly laid with fine crockery and the eye is often drawn to the outdoor patio which can be seen through the handsome conservatory.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15710;Le Saint Cerf;France;Besançon;1 rue Mégevand, Besançon, 25000, France;47.2364281;6.0229271;66;false;true;Modern Cuisine;"This contemporary bistro with a pleasant interior proposes tasty food rife with various influences, including Asian touches, skilfully handled from start to finish, without ostentation. Add to that a distinct tendency towards the ""natural"" (seasonality, ingredients) and a handful of vegetarian dishes and you get an ambassador of the Besançon's revival. ";Air conditioning;[]
15713;Les 3 Faisans;France;Saint-Savin;100 rue des Auberges, Saint-Savin, 38300, France;45.6278589;5.3093284;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Madame is in charge of the savoury dishes, while Monsieur takes care of desserts: this enthusiastic couple lovingly crafts seasonal fare. Served in one of two dining rooms or alfresco on the shaded terrace. After your meal, why not go for a stroll over the hillsides, possibly humming Jacques Brel’s famous song, Les Bourgeois, which mentions a “Hôtel des Trois Faisans”?;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15714;Au Bœuf Noir;France;Hésingue;2 rue Folgensbourg, Hésingue, 68220, France;47.5762465;7.5181712;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Quality produce sets the tone here, in the form of flavourful dishes like skate wing à la grenobloise with baby potatoes, fricassee of calf’s sweetbreads and frogs’ legs in the spirit of a carbonara, or hare à la royale in the game season…There is a pretty little terrace to the rear, which is ideal for fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15715;Le Clos Saint-Pierre;France;Le Rouret;Place de la Mairie, Le Rouret, 06650, France;43.67438;7.00679;93;false;false;Provençal;Opposite the church of this village dedicated to perfume manufacture, a charming inn where set menus (diners have one choice only) are devised using the lovely market-sourced ingredients. Pleasant terrace, fast and efficient service.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15716;L'Auberge Bretonne;France;La Roche-Bernard;2 place Duguesclin, La Roche-Bernard, 56130, France;47.5195065;-2.2992262;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This gastronomic restaurant was taken over by a young couple in 2010 and has a good local reputation. It occupies an old stone house overlooking a small square in the heart of a charming, small town.;;[]
15717;La Pierrevue;France;Saint-Rogatien;2 place de la Mairie, Saint-Rogatien, 17220, France;46.1509739;-1.0740595;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;"There are six seasons in the year": with this saying in mind, chef Cécile Richard adapts her recipes to the times, with a drive for creativity that can be sensed in her fresh and precise cuisine. Locally caught fish, fruit and vegetables from organic market gardeners, aromatic herbs and flowers from the garden can be enjoyed in this farmhouse, converted in a pleasant rustic style. Attractive glass-paned wine cellar with 120 types. New menu every two months.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15718;Auberge des Saints Pères;France;Aulnay-sous-Bois;212 avenue Nonneville, Aulnay-sous-Bois, 93600, France;48.92;2.48955;54;false;true;Creative;In an elegant, pared-back setting, you can enjoy cuisine made with top-notch produce by chef Jean-Claude Cahagnet, whose experience can't be argued with and who leaves us in no doubt about his penchant for herbs and spices. Regular diners keep coming back for the high-quality matured purebred meats, presented in a tempting window display. The hostess provides a warm welcome and impeccable service.;Air conditioning;[]
15719;Le Servan;France;Paris;32 rue Saint-Maur, Paris, 75011, France;48.86105;2.38131;77;false;true;Modern Cuisine;On the watch of Katia and Tatiana Levha, two Filipino sisters, this place has blossomed into one of the most popular bistros in Paris (booking essential). The interior puts its best foot forward, showing off its period frescoes. Tatiana put her English studies on hold in order to indulge her twin passions of eating and cooking! Trained in the establishments of Alain Passard and Pascal Barbot, she creates lively and cheerful cuisine, French but with a good measure of Asian influences. Indeed, just the right amount of chilli is used to spice up a number of recipes. Particular care goes into the sauces and jus, such as the soy and chilli butter on the pork and langoustine ravioli, and the saffron bisque and rouille served with sea bass, fennel and kale.;Counter dining;[]
15721;Bon Kushikatsu;France;Paris;24 rue Jean-Pierre-Timbaud, Paris, 75011, France;48.8655073;2.3691162;76;false;true;Japanese;This restaurant is an express trip to Osaka to discover the city's culinary speciality of kushikatsu (meat, vegetables or seafood skewers coated with breadcrumbs and deep - fried). Dish after dish reveals fine flavours, such as: beef sancho, peppered foie gras, and shiitake mushrooms. The courteous service transports you to Japan.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
15722;Dessirier;France;Paris;9 place du Maréchal-Juin, Paris, 75017, France;48.8849879;2.2966208;95;false;true;Seafood;Contemporary, arty and chic: Dessirier is the Rostang family's flagship restaurant. It attaches a great deal of importance to the fish selection: bouillabaisse and sole meunière are among the signature dishes.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15723;Daniel et Denise Saint-Jean;France;Lyon;36 rue Tramassac, Lyon, 69005, France;45.7603529;4.8254821;23;true;true;Lyonnaise;A stone's throw from Cathédrale St - Jean, this Old Town bouchon is run by chef Joseph Viola (Meilleur Ouvrier de France in 2004), already known for Daniel and Denise in the 3rd arrondissement. On the menu, traditional Lyon cuisine to delight fans.;Air conditioning;[]
15724;Café Terroir;France;Lyon;14 rue d'Amboise, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7592207;4.8318169;30;false;false;Country cooking;Established near the Célestins Theatre, under the auspices of Jean-François Têtedoie (son of legendary Christian!), this house upholds the art of good food. The menu reads like a culinary bible of Lyon’s specialties: signature dishes like homemade terrine and gâteau lyonnais rub shoulders with rotisserie joints, to be shared and carved in front of you (Bresse poultry, rib of beef, lobster), without forgetting a lineup of bistro classics such as calf’s sweetbread vol-au-vent or Monts du Lyonnais snails with girolle mushrooms and cress. The wine cellar boasts over 1,500 references at temptingly reasonable prices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15725;La Bastide Saint-Antoine;France;Grasse;48 avenue Henri-Dunant, Grasse, 06130, France;43.6454752;6.9257262;29;false;true;Provençal;To celebrate the 20th anniversary of his Provençal haven, Jacques Chibois – a leading proponent of "cuisine du soleil" – has updated all of the restaurant's key posts (head sommelier, chief account manager etc). A dynamic team working to create dishes that fête pell mell citrus fruits, herbs, olive oil and other delicacies of the region... A real treat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15726;Eugène;France;Orléans;24 rue Sainte-Anne, Orléans, 45000, France;47.9039395;1.905464;49;false;true;Modern Cuisine;If you are passing through the Loiret, département, this cosy establishment is recommended for chef Alain Gérard's subtle seasonal cuisine: his dishes are meticulous, tasty and fine, and he composes his mouth-watering surprise set menus as the inspiration takes him.;Air conditioning;[]
15727;Cent33;France;Bordeaux;133 rue du Jardin-Public, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8550026;-0.573945;74;true;true;Creative;A chic, cosy bistro atmosphere reigns in the restaurant of Grenoble-born chef Fabien Beaufour. He has worked in some of the finest Michelin-starred restaurants in France (eg Anne-Sophie Pic in Valence and Patrick Henriroux in Vienne), as well as in New York and London. So it's hardly surprising that his cooking is unconventional, globe-trotting and eco-responsible. Intense, contrasting flavours and spot-on cooking and seasonings. Signature dishes include delicious miso-glazed black cod slow-cooked on the robatayaki, warm octopus salad, Piedmont hazelnuts with salted butter caramel.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15728;L'Envers du Décor;France;Saint-Emilion;9 rue du Clocher, Saint-Emilion, 33330, France;44.8938046;-0.1562106;89;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of this iconic wine village, a few steps from the bell tower, the picturesque red façade of this bistro catches the eye. Inside lies an elegant vintage décor with a zinc counter and leather bench seating. The menu runs the gamut of classic French staples from calf’s liver to rum baba. Fine selection of reasonably priced wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15729;Le Chazal;France;Le Monêtier-les-Bains;Les Guibertes, Le Monêtier-les-Bains, 05220, France;44.9651429;6.5288612;76;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At the highest point of a charming hamlet, this converted stable, which has retained its authentic feeders and hooks for smoking meat and fish, sports a vaulted dining room oozing in stylish appeal. Chef Fabien Ferdinand lovingly crafts regional, even super local produce: such as Arctic char, rainbow trout from Châteauroux-les-Alpes, ewe's milk cheese and duck foie gras from the village. An address worth keeping…;;[]
15731;Château Grand Barrail;France;Saint-Emilion;Route de Libourne D243, Saint-Emilion, 33330, France;44.909139;-0.1922461;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This romantic-looking château built in 1902 lies in the heart of the Saint-Émilion vineyards. It blends a time-honoured setting with contemporary design and diners sit either in the Art Nouveau-inspired lounges or on the beautiful terrace that looks out over the grounds and a sea of vines. Bistronomy dishes are served at lunch: eg roast aubergine and smoked caviar with tomato and fig balsamic condiment. The dinner menu features more ambitious cuisine (Charolais beef tenderloin, "pain-jus" with red wine, potato espuma with truffle oil).;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15732;Chez Mattin;France;Ciboure;63 rue Evariste-Baignol, Ciboure, 64500, France;43.3826626;-1.6692846;15;false;false;Basque;This building, characteristic of the local area, is delightfully rustic, with its wooden tables and exposed beams, and has a real family atmosphere. Basque specialities and market-based daily specials make for lively cuisine that never fails to surprise: txangurro (specialities based on spider crab meat), ttoro (fish soup), txipirones (baby squid). Fish takes pride of place and it is exceptionally good!;Air conditioning;[]
15733;La Plage;France;Plonévez-Porzay;Lieu-dit Sainte-Anne-la-Palud, Plonévez-Porzay, 29550, France;48.1335769;-4.2691048;73;true;true;Seafood;This beachfront restaurant has looked out onto the ebbing and flowing tides since 1924. An idyllic setting in which to enjoy dishes that showcase fine ingredients, in particular fish and seafood, such as line-caught pollock, shallots, potatoes, mushrooms in a seafood emulsion…;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15734;O'Rabasse;France;Richerenches;5 place de la Pompe, Richerenches, 84600, France;44.35953;4.91292;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the “truffle capital”, O’Rabasse sings an ode to good food that respects traditions. Everything is made from scratch by the chef, with the help of local suppliers and in line with the seasons. A truly pleasant meal, further enhanced by smiling, professional service.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15735;Le Patio;France;Saint-Tropez;1 boulevard d'Aumale, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2725478;6.6410866;24;true;true;Italian;Le Patio is part of the hotel Le Yaca and is a stone's throw from the hustle and bustle of the port. It proposes flavoursome and refined Italian cuisine that is much indebted to excellent ingredients imported directly from Italy. The meal is even more pleasant when you are seated on the shady terrace alongside the pool.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
15736;Auberge Quintessence;France;Roubion;Route du Col-de-la-Couillole, Roubion, 06420, France;44.0996599;7.0229406;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine;At the Col de la Couillole, a pass in the Mercantour National Park, this former refuge run by Pauline and Christophe Billau is a top destination for foodies. These two serve up a warm welcome and a single set menu that draws inspiration from the mountains and changes with the seasons. Diners can indulge in creamy local mountain nettle cappuccino, superb roasted white asparagus, whether tangy with candied citrus fruit or in a sabayon sauce, or lightly smoked Mediterranean tuna served confit-style and subtly counterbalanced by the herbal notes of oxalis. Dishes such as veal from the Plateau de Longon accompanied by confit shallots and a courgette flower filled with pine nuts and a herb cream are brimming with skilfully mastered flavours, while the cheeses are carefully matured. There's nothing superfluous or artificial about this place! A few prettily decorated guestrooms are up for grabs for overnight stays.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15737;Le Musée;France;Lyon;2 rue des Forces, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7645768;4.8346115;97;false;true;Lyonnaise;A sincere and authentic bouchon replete with checked tablecloths, closely packed tables and a buzzy vibe. The colourful young chef, Luc, frequently pops out to chat with guests, when he’s not conjuring up textbook recipes with consummate flair, such as pistachio sausage in brioche pastry or tablier de sapeur (offal)… 100% patriotic line-up.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15738;Bistro Là-Haut;France;Suresnes;70 avenue Franklin-Roosevelt, Suresnes, 92150, France;48.8753144;2.2193744;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Thanks to the hilltop location on Mont Valérien, this loft-style restaurant commands a superb view of Paris. The à la carte menu boasts a tempting range of contemporary dishes, such as confit farmhouse pork belly grilled on the barbecue, sweet potato mousseline, roast pointed cabbage, grapes with verjuice. For dinnertime, booking is strongly recommended.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15740;Bistrot Pas Parisien;France;Colombes;3 place du Général-Leclerc, Colombes, 92700, France;48.9223442;2.2525916;86;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of Colombes, close to the imposing church designed by Jean Hébrard, this place started out as a brasserie in 1907. With its zinc counter, mirrors, ceiling mouldings and chandelier with white globes, the decor is truly eye-catching and makes for a chic setting in which to enjoy traditional cuisine prepared with care and made with quality produce. The menu includes a number of signature dishes, such as veal chop and rib steak to share.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15741;La Lozerette;France;Cocurès;Route du Pont-de-Montvert, Cocurès, 48400, France;44.3477325;3.6201083;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the Cévennes, this charming inn is the domain of a chef who specialises in cleverly crafted dishes using regionally sourced produce. On the wine side, Pierrette, a talented sommelier, will help you choose from the 300 references available… Let’s not forget the splendid cheeseboard!;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15742;Cercle Rouge;France;Lyon;36 rue de l'Arbre-Sec, Lyon, 69001, France;45.766709;4.8372373;69;false;true;Fusion;This young bistro nestles behind a small, glass - paned façade on a bustling street close to Opéra. On the menu, fusion cuisine with influences ranging across Asian, South American and British, and a fine technical command. Really friendly atmosphere.;;[]
15743;Le Spinaker;France;Le Grau-du-Roi;Voie de la Pointe-du-Môle, Le Grau-du-Roi, 30240, France;43.5193705;4.1360636;40;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Asian Influences;Mediterranean cuisine in the zeitgeist (ceviche of sea bream and red onion pickles, for example), served in a pleasant contemporary interior or on the splendid terrace overlooking the marina, dotted with pleasure craft. Delightful guestrooms to make the most of the seaside holiday vibe.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15744;Auberge du Château de Vaite;France;Champlive;17 Grande Rue, Champlive, 25360, France;47.2883374;6.2467325;91;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In the family since the 1960s, this inn proposes traditional cuisine that showcases regional produce. Morels take pride of place, as do pike-perch and chicken in vin jaune, without forgetting frogs’ legs, fresh from the restaurant’s pond in season. The self-service distributor of home-made dishes next-door is something of a curiosity.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15745;La Table 101;France;Lyon;101 rue Moncey, Lyon, 69003, France;45.7617729;4.8502238;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the Part-Dieu neighbourhood, near Paul Bocuse Market, Olivier and Maryline Delbergues’ establishment rolls out market-fresh recipes with the odd creative twist: tataki of sea trout, sweet-sour red meat radishes, mashed squash, green apple and pecan nuts… Intelligent wine list.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15746;La Maison Carrier;France;Chamonix-Mont-Blanc;44 route du Bouchet, Chamonix-Mont-Blanc, 74400, France;45.9251353;6.8736882;56;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Part of the luxurious Hameau Albert I hotel, this typical farmhouse is home to a friendly restaurant. They serve a beautifully devised seasonal menu – sample the charcuterie that they smoke and dry on site, and take your pick from the legendary and lavish buffet of desserts ("vré de toutes les tartes de la Grand-Mère"), including biscuit de Savoie and blueberry tart. Pleasant terrace.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15747;Le Mas - Alexis Osmont;France;Gordes;Chemin de Saint-Blaise (Les Imberts), Gordes, 84220, France;43.8881522;5.1853525;24;false;true;Farm to table;Alexis Osmont’s market-inspired cuisine is as spontaneous as the old farmhouse seems timeless. Let yourself be transported into Alexis’ creative and culinary universe – he cannot be rivalled for his knack for enhancing the treasures of the Vaucluse: asparagus, girolle mushrooms, artichoke…;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15748;Auberge de Vigny;France;Digoin;Lieu-dit Vigny, Digoin, 71160, France;46.5034563;4.0820536;66;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Up - to - the - minute cuisine served in a former classroom that is a treat for the eyes. The lady of the house is also an accomplished pastry chef. Lovely south - facing garden - terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15749;Daniel et Denise Croix-Rousse;France;Lyon;8 rue de Cuire, Lyon, 69004, France;45.7753916;4.8308651;24;true;true;Lyonnaise;Daniel and Denise Croix - Rousse – the third in the series, after locations on rue de Créqui and in the St Jean quarter – is enjoying the same success as its older siblings. Fill up on hearty Lyon cuisine in a traditional bouchon (tavern) setting.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15750;Philip;France;Fontaine-de-Vaucluse;Chemin de la Fontaine, Fontaine-de-Vaucluse, 84800, France;43.9191746;5.1318709;60;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant has an incredible location at the foot of the famous fountain from which the Sorgue river springs, and it certainly knows how to play on its bucolic charms. Father and daughter (the house has been in the family since 1926) offer a cuisine that plays the traditional card. Smiling and efficient service. Booking is obligatory in season.;Great view,Terrace;[]
15752;Anga - Beaulieu;France;Montpellier;10 rue Saint-Firmin, Montpellier, 34000, France;43.610551;3.8752187;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A narrow street of historic Montpellier is home to the characteristic old traditional stone-built edifice that houses chef Cyril Garcia's new restaurant. His aim is clear: to showcase top-notch Mediterranean produce in a pared-back, fuss-free style. Diners have a choice between two set menus, one vegetable-based, the other featuring fish and seafood, and each with three courses at lunchtime and six courses in the evening – and the components change every month. For example, try wild Mediterranean prawn with kale, satay condiment and a gutsy prawn jus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15753;Les Boulistes;France;Lyon;9 place Tabareau, Lyon, 69004, France;45.7744815;4.8257497;90;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;On La Croix-Rousse plateau of Lyon, this restaurant, overlooking a square popular with boules’ players (hence the name), proposes authentic cuisine with a twist and, more recently, jazzed up with a few inspired Mediterranean tributes: Moroccan harira, portokalopita (a Greek, orange-flavoured pastry), etc. Meals are served in the bistro interior or on the al fresco patio, which is taken by storm as soon as the temperatures begin to rise.;Terrace;[]
15754;La Cour d'Eymet;France;Eymet;32 boulevard National, Eymet, 24500, France;44.6679705;0.3990507;19;true;false;Classic Cuisine;In a style typical of the region, this house on the town’s main street is flanked by a little courtyard where tables are laid on fine days. Impressive cuisine based on excellent produce. Local wines. A few spacious, smart guestrooms.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15755;Comptoir à Huîtres;France;Dieppe;12 cours de Dakar, Dieppe, 76200, France;49.9210212;1.086369;33;false;true;Seafood;Far from the bustle of the seafront, along the quays, this Comptoir is a popular new spot in Dieppe. After you have been presented the catch of the day, with no frills, it is time to make your choice. Which fish? Whole, cut? À la plancha? Unless, that is, you prefer the oyster menu... All as fresh as can be!;;[]
15756;La Cuisine du Marché;France;Figeac;15 rue de Clermont, Figeac, 46100, France;44.6085535;2.0342439;91;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;The old town is a lovely setting for this pleasant restaurant, the name of which sets the tone. Indeed, quality market produce goes into cooking simple and tasty food, peppered with a few Spanish touches. After all, that is where the chef’s origins lie.;Air conditioning;[]
15757;La Tour;France;Dunières;7 ter route du Fraisse, Dunières, 43220, France;45.2141516;4.3412381;44;false;true;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Local ingredients (Puy green lentils, Grazac snails, free - range guinea fowl etc) are transformed into appetising meals by the chef. The food is good and hearty, as well as carefully prepared. The cheese trolley, which includes lots of cheeses from Auvergne, is an added bonus. It is all very appealing, not least the very well - appointed rooms.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15759;Les Arômes;France;Gémenos;230 avenue du 2ème-Cuirassier, Gémenos, 13420, France;43.3030826;5.6158577;88;false;true;Farm to table;In this 1930s house basking in the aromas of Provence, unflappable hostess Françoise Besset and her husband Yannick officiate. His innkeeper's soul has not changed and he continues to regale guests with fresh and inventive regional cuisine. Enjoy in one of the charming little dining spaces or, in fine weather, on the terrace on the veranda overlooking the garden planted with olive trees. An exemplary place.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15760;La Table de Jérôme;France;Luzy;26 rue de la République, Luzy, 58170, France;46.78931;3.97171;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the walls of the Hôtel du Morvan, chef Jérôme Raymond plays a modern, culinary score based on regional produce. A single set menu, with more upmarket ingredients at the weekend (Charolais beef is a firm favourite). Whopping 400-bin wine list of mainly Burgundy origins. Comfortable rooms should you wish to stay longer.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15761;L'Edulis - Jonathan Datin;France;Granville;8 rue de l'Abreuvoir, Granville, 50400, France;48.8373809;-1.5972741;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant's tasteful interior nicely offsets the food, which is devised by an enthusiastic and talented chef, the grandson of a baker. Meticulous cuisine, fine regional produce and culinary delights: quite simply, the best restaurant in Granville.;Wheelchair access;[]
15762;Cazenove;France;Lyon;75 rue Boileau, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7696971;4.8489424;20;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Bronze sculptures and Chesterfield leather seating sets the turn-of-the-19C vibe. In this snug, yet plush ambiance, Best Craftsman of France Pierre Orsi masterfully rustles up smart bistro dishes of classical inspiration. Regularly packed to the seams, so bookings are advisable.;Air conditioning;[]
15763;La Maison Haute;France;Crolles;Place de l'Église, Crolles, 38920, France;45.2876751;5.8856157;81;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Veteran chef Thomas Chegaray (in Basque, the “maison haute” (upper house) is called an “etchegaray”), rustles up modern dishes based on seasonal produce presented in a concise menu. The food is fresh and colourful, with a focus on taste and texture: thick, juicy, tender, farm - reared pork chops, cooked on the bone. Terrace in fine weather and service with a smile.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15764;La Pointe du Cap Coz;France;Fouesnant;153 avenue de la Pointe, au Cap Coz, Fouesnant, 29170, France;47.8910288;-3.9730052;98;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;This white cottage seems to sit right on the ocean. The chef has chosen this isolated location to craft delicious cuisine in line with his commitment to local surf and turf produce. The result is beautifully presented dishes, such as slow-cooked pork cheeks in cider vinegar served with cabbage and apples baked in salted butter.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15767;Les Vignes et son Jardin;France;Gargas;Hôtel Coquillade Provence, Hameau Le Perrotet, Gargas, 84400, France;43.8806472;5.3164481;43;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This bistro serves tasty food that is infused with local flair and made with seasonal ingredients. Dine in the wine - tasting cellar in winter and in the garden, among the vines, in summer. All in a hotel that is in itself worth a look!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15768;Le P'tit Bouchon;France;Gien;66 rue Bernard-Palissy, Gien, 45500, France;47.6864573;2.6248798;23;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This small restaurant located between the town centre and the Faïencerie de Gien ceramics museum is a real hub of bistronomy. Tradition is somewhat revisited in a short set menu dictated by the seasons, but the crispy duck confit with its coteaux-du-layon sauce and the chocolate fondant are among the must-tries. Tuck in!;;[]
15769;Le Périgord;France;Donzenac;9 avenue de Paris, Donzenac, 19270, France;45.2282518;1.5235444;69;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;If you pay a visit to this restaurant covered in Virginia creeper, be sure to try the calf's brains in gribiche sauce. This is one of the house specialities and highly renowned! This place is rustic in the best sense of the word.;Wheelchair access;[]
15770;Cook'in;France;Epernay;18 rue Porte-Lucas, Epernay, 51200, France;49.0449982;3.9540074;15;false;false;Thai;This restaurant is where France (the chef) meets Thailand (front of house). The result is fusion cuisine (pan-fried scallops, lentil salad with ginger, red curry shellfish bisque) with a few “unmissables” (“tom yum talay” soup, or wok-fried Dublin Bay prawns with panang curry…). Reasonable prices.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15771;La Sassa;France;Nonza;à la tour de Nonza, Nonza, 20217, France;42.7850848;9.3436339;81;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;This unusual restaurant, without an inside dining room, nestles at the foot of the watchtower built by Paoli (18C), a veritable crow's nest, perched 160m up, offering an exceptional view over the coast of Cap Corse and Saint Florent bay. The terraces with their many nooks and crannies mean you can enjoy the good, Corsican - accented Mediterranean cuisine with a certain amount of intimacy.;Great view,Terrace;[]
15772;Terra Cotta;France;Propriano;29 avenue Napoléon-III, Propriano, 20110, France;41.6753514;8.8999366;28;false;false;Seafood;This enchanting little restaurant boasts an amazing terrace that unfolds along the quayside of the port. Chef Thomas Duval works with the catch supplied by his fisherman brother, which he brilliantly combines with other ingredients to create dishes throbbing with contrasting flavours. Examples include crunchy wild prawns, panko breadcrumbs, fregola of veggies, herbs, sweet-sour sauce or low-temperature fillet of umbrine in a lemony sauce of capers and parsley with courgette fritters. Consider us smitten!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15773;Au Chamois d'Or;France;Alpe-d'Huez;169 rue Fontbelle, Alpe-d'Huez, 38750, France;45.09723;6.0720186;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This elegant restaurant is one of the many highlights of the Hotel Chamois d'Or, thanks to its classy, cocooned dining area decked out in wood, and its well-crafted up-to-the-minute cuisine. Inviting lunchtime terrace and a romantic vibe in the evenings.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15774;Le Bistrot à la Mer;France;Argelès-sur-Mer;3638 route de Collioure, Argelès-sur-Mer, 66700, France;42.5338767;3.064289;48;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In a hotel overlooking the coastal road to Collioure, you will taste tip-top regional produce, assembled in recipes drenched in Mediterranean aromas. The lovely terrace overlooking the sea provides the perfect foil to the splendid menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15775;Auberge Le Cabaliros;France;Arcizans-Avant;16 rue de l'Église, Arcizans-Avant, 65400, France;42.9881984;-0.1048551;92;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This pleasant village "inn" halfway between two famous passes – Col d'Aubisque and Col du Tourmalet – stands surrounded by the peaks of the Pyrenees. The menu features wonderful traditional dishes that are big on flavour and nicely presented: noir de Bigorre black pork loin, braised sweetbreads, Pyrenean trout. Pretty little guestrooms available!;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15776;Le Viscos;France;Saint-Savin;1 rue Lamarque, Saint-Savin, 65400, France;42.9802862;-0.0909701;69;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Welcome to the village of Saint-Savin, which is a vantage point overlooking the Argelès valley and home to this family-run restaurant with a classic, elegant feel. In the kitchen, Alexis (representing the seventh generation of chefs in the family!) treats diners to dishes that are an ode to the terroir, courtesy of local produce enhanced with more modern touches. The desserts, in particular, are fantastic, eg the macaron and nougatine ice cream. Charming guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15777;Le Moulin de Poustagnacq;France;Saint-Paul-lès-Dax;Chemin de Poustagnacq, Saint-Paul-lès-Dax, 40990, France;43.7355845;-1.0681671;77;true;false;Classic Cuisine;If you like eating by the water, this old mill is the stuff of dreams! The chef prepares fresh ingredients and cooks up traditional cuisine with plenty of appealing regional flair: sole meunière, braised calf sweetbreads with morel sauce, fillet of beef, and chips cooked in goose fat. In fine weather, sit on the terrace overlooking the lake. Bucolic atmosphere guaranteed.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15778;Le Bistrot Gourmand;France;Cuiseaux;8 place Puvis-de-Chavannes, Cuiseaux, 71480, France;46.4936949;5.388737;19;false;false;Regional Cuisine;"Pleasure and tradition" is the motto of this former butchery, where Camille Maître has taken over the family business and is now alone at the helm. The menu is rich in Bresse and Jura ingredients, with distinctive flavours such as quenelle of pike in a creamy lobster bisque. Concise, attractive wine list. Fully deserving of its name!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15781;Le Dauphin;France;Caen;29 rue Gémare, Caen, 14000, France;49.1844861;-0.3648097;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This place is just the ticket for fans of Normandy's specialities: oysters from the bay of Isigny - sur - Mer, Swiss Normandy pigeon, and Vire andouille sausage. The onus is on ingredients from the region but the chef also knows how to compose more original recipes. Elegant and bright decor.;;[]
15784;Chocho;France;Paris;54 rue de Paradis, Paris, 75010, France;48.8757285;2.3489937;16;true;true;Creative;After forging his style for 15 years, Franco-American chef Thomas Chisholm has set up home at Chocho. The high-ceilinged, rectangular dining room is bright and buzzy – ideal to sample food devoted to sharing and sustainable gastronomy. Ikejime fish, rows of jars and fermentations and agroforestry ingredients add punch to his creative, even playful approach in a conscious bid to mix influences: roast carrots, garlic emulsion, egg yolk powder or red tuna, Corsican lemon and dashi of smoked beetroot…;Wheelchair access;[]
15785;La Chaumière;France;Aubigny-sur-Nère;2 rue Paul-Lasnier, Aubigny-sur-Nère, 18700, France;47.4881874;2.441789;69;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This family-run place, a 19C coaching inn, has been in the hands of chef-patron Philippe Arnault since 1992. He is ably assisted by his wife, daughter and, in the kitchen, his son-in-law, Sébastien Provendier (who has previously worked for the Meilleur family and Passedat). Tuck into delights such as trout gravlax with beetroot, buckwheat pancake and horseradish cream, in a pleasant dining room with large bay windows giving onto the inner courtyard. There is a shaded terrace to be enjoyed in fine weather and six guestrooms done out in a modern style inspired by the Sologne region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15786;Des Petits Pois Sont Rouges;France;Argelès-Gazost;44 avenue des Pyrénées, Argelès-Gazost, 65400, France;43.0042405;-0.0991257;69;true;false;Modern Cuisine;No need to be a guest at the Miramont Hotel to enjoy the chef's cuisine. He of course pays homage to Pyrenean culinary heritage but doesn't hesitate to make a few welcome innovations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15787;La Pinède;France;Lecci;à Cala-Rossa, Lecci, 20137, France;41.6214585;9.338574;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Whether for a relaxed lunch by the beach or dinner beneath the arbour, the intimate and romantic setting is utterly magnificent. The simple and delicious Mediterranean cuisine, courtesy of chefs Pascal Cayeux (for the savoury dishes) and Francis Péan (for desserts), is a celebration of local ingredients. Herbs and vegetables from the 3 000m2 organic kitchen garden are often incorporated. And let's not forget the maturing cellar for cheeses and the enticing wine list.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15788;U Santa Marina;France;Porto-Vecchio;Marina di Santa-Giulia, Porto-Vecchio, 20137, France;41.5309887;9.280439;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The view of the Gulf of Santa Giulia is superb, and, come evening, the sunset is jaw-dropping. The tasty, personal, inspired culinary score is the handiwork of chef Nikolaz Le Cheviller who oscillates between two proud, untamed lands: Brittany and Corsica, courtesy of handpicked, locally sourced (whenever possible), organic produce: kari gosse, kig-ha-farz, Roscoff onions and fermented milk are intelligently and masterfully blended with brocciu, Corsican olives or oysters from Diana’s lagoon. A flavoursome and delightfully romantic moment.;Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15789;La Saulire;France;Courchevel;16 place du Rocher, Courchevel 1850, Courchevel, 73120, France;45.41514;6.63599;68;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;An interior decked out in pale wood and decorated with old mountain objects is the authentic and inviting setting in which chef Benoît Redondo cooks up meticulous food: the famous Savoyard fondue rubs shoulders with the Périgord truffle. Please note that the restaurant is closed at lunchtime in good weather, to let skiers enjoy the snowy slopes of the resort.;Interesting wine list;[]
15790;Le Vieux Four;France;Châtel;55 route du Boude, Châtel, 74390, France;46.2677072;6.8419772;68;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This warm, rustic restaurant housed in an old farmhouse (1852) delights its guests with its authentic ambience. Admire the figurines nestling in the stable manger, while enjoying delicious cuisine from the Savoie region.;Terrace;[]
15792;La Vallée;France;Dinard;6 avenue George-V, Dinard, 35800, France;48.636265;-2.048447;91;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;With its large bay windows, the interior is pleasant, but it is outdone by the irresistible south-facing terrace just beyond the picturesque Bec de la Vallée dock. It's the perfect place to sample fine seafood (charred leeks, cockles from the bay with fresh herbs), as well as classics from Brittany's terroir, eg tranche de lard paysan du pays malouin (salted smoked bacon), far breton (traditional flan-style dessert).;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15794;Autour d'un Cep;France;Angers;9 rue Baudrière, Angers, 49100, France;47.472275;-0.5569159;31;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This little place, the origins of which date back to some time between the 15C and 16C, stands halfway between the cathedral and the Maine River. Chef Thony Pohu turns out generous and flavoursome cuisine that is in tune with the times and the seasons and has a strong emphasis on plants. The high-quality ingredients are sourced locally, and the suppliers are featured prominently on the menu. The wine list boasts over 300 labels, mostly organic and natural.;Interesting wine list;[]
15795;L'Essentiel;France;Attiches;19 rue de Neuville, Attiches, 59551, France;50.5139475;3.0619091;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This handsome redbrick edifice at a crossroads in the hamlet of Petit Attiches is run by an enthusiastic young couple. A stylish, modern interior, a terrace and a pretty garden to the rear set the inviting scene. Carefully crafted, up-to-the-minute dishes are paired with fine wines.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15796;L'Ambrosia;France;Pezens;Carrefour la Madeleine, sur D 6113, Pezens, 11170, France;43.2588551;2.2518613;72;true;false;Modern Cuisine;On the road to Toulouse, take a break in this modern house: the chef’s preparations are meticulous, coherent and crafted to suit modern tastes, all the more so as he uses premium ingredients: seabass, sweetbread, langoustine… Reasonably priced too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15797;Le Moulin de Trèbes;France;Trèbes;2 rue du Moulin-de-Trèbes, Trèbes, 11800, France;43.2074625;2.4492599;96;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This old mill is steeped in charm, illustrated by the terrace directly overlooking the Canal du Midi. The food is simple and modern, with a speciality of caramelised calf sweetbreads with sesame and stewed endives. A real pleasure to be sampled with one of the carefully selected local vintages.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15798;La Récréation;France;Les Arques;Le Bourg, Les Arques, 46250, France;44.6034341;1.24989;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;School’s out! In its place, this gently nostalgic establishment has a classroom - style dining room, courtyard terrace and kitchen garden in the old playground. Contemporary cuisine.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15800;Ruche;France;Gambais;Domaine les Bruyères, 251 avenue de Neuville, Gambais, 78950, France;48.7905592;1.6956604;79;false;true;Creative;On the outskirts of Rambouillet Forest, chef Cybèle, who also runs the Table de Cybèle in Boulogne Billancourt, fell in love with this estate dating from 1850, where she now grows practically everything she cooks according to permaculture methods… Fresh greens thus play a pivotal role, flanked by fermentation techniques and produce from local growers. The bread, butter and yoghurt are all homemade and the wine list is rich in biodynamic and natural vintages. The interior displays a Scandinavian slant and offers five pretty guestrooms for peaceful wellness retreats.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15803;Le Channel;France;Calais;3 boulevard de la Résistance, Calais, 62100, France;50.9604523;1.8478328;70;false;true;Seafood;This is a pleasant spot to eat before crossing the Channel. It has an elegant decor, classic cuisine, seafood, and a fine wine list (cellar opens onto restaurant).;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15804;Les Caudalies;France;Arbois;20 avenue Pasteur, Arbois, 39600, France;46.909387;5.7689756;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;At the helm of this stylish bourgeois establishment is an inspired sommelier, Best Craftsman of France, Philippe Troussard. His immense talent and the sheer scope of his wine list (over 1,000 references) raise the concept of food-wine pairing to an art form. The well-crafted recipes are the work of a skilful chef. The terrace enjoys a sweeping view of the grounds, the River Cuisance and the legendary Arbois vineyards.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15805;La Table de la Caillère;France;Candé-sur-Beuvron;36 route des Montils, Candé-sur-Beuvron, 41120, France;47.4941796;1.2704352;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Idyllically located for anyone touring the châteaux of the Loire, this inn, firmly in the zeitgeist, is run by an enterprising couple who work together in a bucolic setting of forests and meadows. The original 18C farmhouse has been replaced by a modern building, which reflects the chef's culinary ethos that favours local produce (girolle mushrooms, regional veggies, honey, Racan pigeon, Touraine pork, etc.), but also his homeland, Brittany, illustrated by a wafer-thin tart of spider crab covered in a warm mayonnaise flavoured with sea urchin roe. Each legible dish is a masterclass of exquisite plating and crisp forthright flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15806;Domaine du Châtelard;France;Dirac;1079 route du Châtelard, Dirac, 16410, France;45.6179919;0.2289223;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In this lovely "country house" the chef chooses his ingredients well. He cooks fresh and fine cuisine for the modern palate, and some dishes having interesting Italian influences. Lunch on the terrace with a view over the lake is not to be missed.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15807;Le Mas de Peint;France;Le Sambuc;Le Mas de Peint, route de Salin de Giraud (D36), Le Sambuc, 13200, France;43.5048052;4.7143596;30;true;false;Country cooking;Using good ingredients and vegetables from the kitchen garden, the chef creates lovely dishes that put a new spin on the old classics (bull beef gravlax, gazpacho made with old tomato varieties, etc). The ravishing terrace beneath the wisteria and the charm of the setting make this a great choice.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15808;L'Aubinière;France;Saint-Ouen-les-Vignes;29 rue Jules-Gautier, Saint-Ouen-les-Vignes, 37530, France;47.47049;0.99359;74;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This attractive, contemporary dining space basks in the light of the windows that open out onto the wooded parkland. The seasonal cuisine never compromises on the quality of the ingredients (Richelieu asparagus, Mouliherne escargots, line-cut meagre etc) and the cellar is packed with regional wines: L'Aubinière restaurant has it all. There are also a number of elegant guestrooms, plus a wellness area.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15809;La Table du Sommelier;France;Albi;20 rue Porta, Albi, 81000, France;43.934689;2.1457485;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A father-and-son team of trained sommeliers work in tandem in this pleasant contemporary bistro. The result is flavoursome, indulgent wine-based dishes that put a skilful new spin on the offerings of the local terroir, such as the fillet of blue ling with parsley, wild rice and sesame oil, or the raspberry and vanilla in sablé and mousse forms. The cellar boasts almost 500 wines, and in summer there are two terraces to choose from: beneath the pergola or in the open air. Highly recommended and excellent value for money.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15810;L'Atelier de Nicolas;France;Aigues-Mortes;28 rue Alsace-Lorraine, Aigues-Mortes, 30220, France;43.5674618;4.1912872;51;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant, bang in the historic heart with a wrought iron and glass front door, is where chef Nicolas rolls out a modern line-up, with the odd Asian twist picked up during his forays to Thailand. Examples include Tom Kha Kung (spicy soup) of shrimp and coconut milk or a Wellington-style Kushikatsu of Camargue bull. Each Asian-sounding, fresh, aromatic dish comes with lashings of reassuring explanations! The chef works with local organic producers and breeders whenever possible and the concise wine list demonstrates a distinct fondness for natural tipples.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15811;Le Bouchon du Vaugueux;France;Caen;12 rue Graindorge, Caen, 14000, France;49.1849313;-0.3596381;71;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Behind a simple exterior is this bistro with the soul of a true bouchon lyonnais (counter, cheek - to - jowl dining). That said, the chef does not limit himself to tradition and adorns his dishes with more modern ideas. Nice selection of wines from producers.;;[]
15812;Brasserie à 4 Temps;France;Carcassonne;2 boulevard Barbès, Carcassonne, 11000, France;43.2104421;2.3517654;37;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A modern brasserie complete with a shady terrace, where you can enjoy classics that have been given a new spin by Franck Putelat's former sous-chef. Devilled eggs and leek vinaigrette, beef tartare, cassoulet… absolutely delicious. Book ahead to secure your table.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15813;Le Pêché Gourmand;France;Briançon;2 route de Gap, Briançon, 05100, France;44.8912694;6.6283779;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant on the banks of the Guisane, run by a young French-Australian couple who are smitten with gastronomy. Sharon creates the lovely seasonal food including pastries, and Jimmy takes care of diners and the wine. Friendly, professional service.;Car park;[]
15814;Bvañ;France;Vannes;6 rue Alexandre-le-Pontois, Vannes, 56000, France;47.6547587;-2.7563145;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Romain Le Cordroch has travelled extensively, across continents (China, Australia, Brazil) and from one fine restaurant to another (Atelier de Rabanel, Atelier Robuchon, Violon d'Ingres). Now returning to his roots, he has established a natural style of plant- and fish-based cuisine. He lets nothing go to waste – everything is transformed. For instance, his gomasio is made from fish scales warmed in the oven! His dishes always demonstrate his know-how, eg mussels marinière, Armenian cucumber with verbena and a gwell (Breton fermented milk) foam.;;[]
15815;Chez Francis;France;Brive-la-Gaillarde;61 avenue de Paris, Brive-la-Gaillarde, 19100, France;45.1638727;1.5321185;26;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Chez Francis has the perfect family - run bistro atmosphere with its old - fashioned poster adverts, all manner of bric - a - brac and messages left by clients. You come here as a friend and are made to feel at ease as you sample the quality ingredients woven into lovely recipes: crab remoulade, Jerusalem artichoke and green apple, wok sautéed squid served with Languedoc wines!;Air conditioning;[]
15817;Aquar'aile;France;Calais;255 rue Jean-Moulin, Calais, 62100, France;50.9613896;1.8316405;73;false;true;Seafood;This pleasant top-floor restaurant boasts a peerless panoramic view over the Strait of Dover and the English coast… it is like something you would expect to see in a painting! The food showcases locally caught fish: lobster casserole, sea bass in a salt crust, sole meunière. To be washed down with a good wine chosen from a list carefully curated by the proprietor.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15818;Breizh Café Cancale;France;Cancale;7 quai Thomas, Cancale, 35260, France;48.67078;-1.85169;92;false;false;Breton;On the port of Cancale, Breizh Café has one motto: "A new take on crêpes." After all, the concept was originally born in Japan! The owner, Bertrand Larcher, was the first to export Brittany's galettes (buckwheat pancakes) to Tokyo, and several Japanese restaurants later, he has founded one back home. The produce is organic (eggs, cheese, meat) and first rate. The crispy flavoursome galettes and wafer-thin, soft pancakes are made entirely traditionally. The filling depends on your mood, ranging from classical to unusual: artichoke rolls, scrambled egg, Comté cheese or Saint Malo wakame seaweed. The upstairs window commands a splendid view of Cancale port. Something of a local landmark, it is often fully booked.;Air conditioning;[]
15819;Auberge de l'Île Enchantée;France;Fleury-sur-Orne;1 rue Saint-André, Fleury-sur-Orne, 14123, France;49.1506487;-0.3763021;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This former fishermen’s bar enjoys a verdant setting practically on the banks of the Orne. In keeping with the house traditions, the chef revamps hearty, wholesome recipes that keep pace with the seasons. Searingly good food!;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15820;Les Deux Canailles;France;Nice;6 rue Chauvain, Nice, 06000, France;43.6983952;7.2714469;65;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Les Deux Canailles are two energetic business partners who have brought together a young, disciplined and passionate Franco - Japanese team. Fresh modern French cuisine prepared with finesse and with a few Japanese touches.;Air conditioning;[]
15821;Le Grand Bleu;France;Calais;8 rue Jean-Pierre-Avron, Calais, 62100, France;50.962635;1.851295;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The chef, Matthieu Colin, puts the experience he gained in Michelin-starred establishments to good use. In a lovely contemporary interior, he continues to pay tribute to local fishing, but also brings local produce into creative dishes that thrive on originality: cod with seafood condiments, grapefruit, crozets, spiced fennel. Friendly and efficient service.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15823;Blue Flamingo;France;Strasbourg;Presqu'île André-Malraux, Strasbourg, 67000, France;48.5742494;7.759257;24;true;true;Modern Cuisine;All hands on deck! Made entirely out of glass, steel wood and aluminium, this floating restaurant, akin to a 21C barge, is anchored on the banks of André Malraux Presqu’île. Flooded in light, the waterside dining room commands a view of the kitchen to the rear. The rooftop terrace sports a delightful riverside café vibe. Chef Benoit Migeon, former sous-chef of the Crocodile, rustles up recipes rich in international flavours and steeped in fresh, vibrant ingredients, such as semi-cooked tuna, watermelon, chimichurri and feta.;Air conditioning;[]
15824;Vivant;France;Arradon;4 rue François-Jarlégan, Arradon, 56610, France;47.6270967;-2.8233793;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In a dining room as fresh as a spring morning, the former owners of the Moulin du Ponceau (Chartres), for whom sourcing locally is deep in their DNA, wanted to get closer to nature and to their producers. The chef crafts dishes in the zeitgeist with a weakness for seafood and veggies, depicted by hake from the coast and multiple versions of cabbage. Fermentation is a prominent feature of his cooking.;Wheelchair access;[]
15825;Vent Debout - Hôtel Les Hautes Mers;France;Port-Joinville;27 rue Pierre-Henry, Port-Joinville, 85350, France;46.7220579;-2.3431233;79;true;false;Seafood;Just imagine: the Île d'Yeu, a pretty little hotel overlooking the sea, a chic, laid-back restaurant, a terrace and a dining area decorated with models of old sailing ships... All in all, a truly charming spot for food lovers who can expect a deliciously fishy regional menu.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15826;Le Constance - Abbaye de Villeneuve;France;Les Sorinières;Lieu-dit Villeneuve, Les Sorinières, 44840, France;47.1234992;-1.533892;27;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The brasserie of this hotel that has been tastefully refurbished from top to bottom, is set up in a space that is flooded with light through a beautiful glass roof and bay windows overlooking the swimming pool and grounds. The chef presents a menu that combines traditional dishes (e.g. pâté en croûte, egg mayonnaise, fish with beurre blanc sauce, Loire fish quenelle with crayfish bisque) with more modern recipes. We also like the attractive wine list with (very) reasonable prices, especially for the wines from the region.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
15827;Auberge du Château;France;Bressieux;67 montée du Château, Bressieux, 38870, France;45.3237127;5.2776336;89;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Christèle and Xavier Vanheule are passionate about food and wine, and put their all into making this Auberge a wonderful establishment. The produce they source from surrounding farms is bursting with freshness. While contemplating the peaks of the Monts du Lyonnais, you can enjoy dishes with robust flavours, including filet of Dombes duckling, split pea purée, grilled pork belly etc.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15828;L'Espérance - Stéphane Carbone;France;Hérouville-Saint-Clair;512 rue Abbé-Alix, Hérouville-Saint-Clair, 14200, France;49.2004788;-0.319367;36;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Treat yourself to a bucolic gourmet getaway a stone's throw from Caen, in Stéphane Carbone's terracotta-coloured establishment. The chef, well known to locals, serves traditional dishes with a modern twist, for example knuckle end of lamb, bulgur risotto with turmeric and turnip roasted with sweet tonka pepper. Each table commands a lovely view of the canal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15829;Auberge de Bel Air;France;Brélès;1 Moulin de Bel-Air, Brélès, 29810, France;48.4759276;-4.7243298;50;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This granite-built farmhouse on the banks of the Aber Ildut cuts a picturesque figure with its large garden and lake. On the menu: the fish and seafood cuisine for which Brittany is so famed, eg fillet of pollack with lobster cream. A rustic setting in which to really unwind.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15830;Le Baligan;France;Cabourg;8 avenue Alfred-Piat, Cabourg, 14390, France;49.2906063;-0.1140702;92;false;true;Seafood;Fishing rods, lithographs, and frescoes set the maritime scene in this bistro. Flawlessly fresh fish from the local fish auction and knockout seafood platters (oysters and scallops) take the limelight on the table. The fish of the day, in our case sole and turbot, is sold by the kilogramme – to the delight of our appetites and wallets!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15831;Stéphane Carbone;France;Caen;14 rue de Courtonne, Caen, 14000, France;49.1843647;-0.354531;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Just a stone's throw from the marina, in the bustling hub of Caen life, chef Stéphane Carbone explores France's terroirs, from Normandy and the Lyonnais to Bresse (where he grew up and learned to cook) to his parents' and grandparents' native Calabria. Using the freshest ingredients, he serves modern cuisine with a dash of creativity, proceeding according to the mood on any given day. Signature dishes are available à la carte, including the heart sweetbread cooked in a sauté pan or the Caribbean chocolate shell with a hot chocolate velouté… To be enjoyed in the contemporary dining area, from which you can watch the activity in the kitchen from behind a large picture window. A lobster set menu and cookery class every Saturday morning.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15832;Hostellerie Les Gorges de Pennafort;France;Callas;8660 route Départementale 25, Callas, 83830, France;43.5869663;6.5426581;48;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The restaurant has an elegant, contemporary decor and a terrace beneath the plane trees. The setting is enticing, and the food even more so. Flowers, spices, herbs and the chef's personal touches bring together tradition and generosity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15833;La Maison des Blés - Le Bouche à Oreille;France;Boutervilliers;19 rue du Périgord, Boutervilliers, 91150, France;48.4564894;2.0552441;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A contemporary place with a modern interior, with two ears of wheat emblazoned on the walls in homage to the surrounding countryside, and two eateries where you can indulge yourself: Brasserie Louis (knuckle joint of lamb, seasonal vegetables etc) and the gourmet restaurant, Bouche à Oreille. Professionalism and dishes that showcase top-notch ingredients every time.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15834;Les Flots;France;La Rochelle;1 rue de la Chaîne, La Rochelle, 17000, France;46.1560623;-1.1542905;54;false;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in a converted 18C estaminet boasts an ideal location on the port of La Rochelle, and has a delightful terrace at the foot of the Tour de la Chaîne. They serve refined cuisine in which the flavours of the ocean enjoy the limelight, for example, "lobster stew with glazed seasonal vegetables, mushroom ravioli with lobster roe, a jus made from lobster juices and an inkling of ginger", chef Grégory Coutanceau's signature dish.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15835;La Vieille Auberge;France;Casteljaloux;13 avenue du 8-Mai-1945, Casteljaloux, 47700, France;44.3136795;0.0814637;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Splendid high vaulted timber ceilings and huge floor-to-ceiling windows reminiscent of a conservatory overlooking the garden: the scene is set in this well-known culinary landmark. Matthijs Bartman rolls out modern, enticing dishes illustrated by pastrami of bazadais beef, smoked beetroot and blueberries or a more classical choux pastry stuffed with tonka bean diplomat crème, yuzu caramel and mango sorbet… A traditional lineup with a modern twist, presented in two eater-friendly priced menus. Enthusiastic and delightful front of house team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15836;Kashiwa;France;Le Cannet;12 boulevard Gambetta, Le Cannet, 06110, France;43.5746894;7.0235559;17;false;false;Japanese;Don't be fooled by the sign: this small Japanese restaurant (kashiwa means "oak leaf") housed in a former tapestry - maker's workship, offers a lovely array of Japanese dishes (sushi, sashimi, soba etc). Small terrace, and prime location close to the Musée Pierre Bonnard. A pleasant place.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15838;Maison Nipa;France;Fillé;13 rue des Gesleries, Fillé, 72210, France;47.9000934;0.126273;32;true;false;Filipino, Creative;This restaurant, opened by an experienced Franco-Philippine couple (Jason is in charge of savoury dishes, while Sharon rustles up desserts), specialises in Gallic cuisine influenced by the flavours and aromas of the Philippine archipelago. The food takes you on a culinary tour from Sarthe to the Philippines, depicted by Croisic squid à la “Adobong Pusit”, stuffed with a sisig of bellota chorizo and coated in a subtle cuttlefish ink sauce or wild duck with coffee-flavoured ceps and an “Adobo” sauce, together with other delicately perfumed dishes that might feature sweet-savoury or surf-turf notes. The roof may not be covered in palm leaves (meaning of nipa), but the modern dining room which cleverly mixes materials, is delightful, as is the seamless service.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15839;Le Clos du Château;France;Pringy;70 route de Cuvat, Pringy, 74370, France;45.9545858;6.1125436;80;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Adjacent to the Château de Proméry, this imposing contemporary building has been run for 17 years by Pascal Avertis, who hails from the village. The chef is equally at ease with traditional recipes (braised chuck with an excellent Mondeuse sauce, potato croquettes to dip in a delicious home-made ketchup) as he is with more modern and creative creations, such as leek and nori maki with Thai vinaigrette and smoked caviar – absolutely delicious! To be savoured on the pleasant terrace, in the shade of the plane trees.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15840;Cavalieri;France;Paris;71 avenue Paul-Doumer, Paris, 75116, France;48.8595745;2.2787411;100;false;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Between Place du Trocadéro and la Muette, this smart, contemporary venue offers another spin on timeless Italian classics: aubergine parmigiana, fritto misto, a smoked version of vitello tonnato, linguine alle vongole... The interior sports Sicilian walnut furnishings, two-tone Italian marble and hand-painted tableware reminiscent of the Amalfi coast.;Valet parking;[]
15844;Jeanne-Aimée;France;Paris;3 rue Bourdaloue, Paris, 75009, France;48.8762273;2.3384668;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Bingo for this semi-industrial, semi-cosy bistro alongside Notre Dame de Lorette Church, where two mates tick all the boxes to regale us. On one side, Dan Humphris (who also runs a nearby bakery-grocery store where he sells organic produce from his father’s farm in the Yvelines) and on the other, youthful Sylvain Parisot, with stints in star-studded establishments (l’Astrance and La Marine with Alexandre Couillon) under his belt. Conclusion? First class ingredients (Gascony pork chops, Landes poultry), daring ideas (oysters and camembert ice cream), generosity, sensible prices and spot-on, friendly service.;Air conditioning;[]
15846;Le Comptoir du Relais;France;Paris;5 carrefour de l'Odéon, Paris, 75006, France;48.8518603;2.3388008;36;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Yves Camdeborde has entrusted the keys of his famous diminutive bistro to chef Bruno Doucet, whom he had already put in charge of La Régalade. Suffice to say, on his watch the place's bistronomy philosophy is scrupulously adhered to. In the tiny restaurant with tightly packed tables or on the heated terrace looking onto the Carrefour de l'Odéon, you can enjoy a menu (served right through from noon to 11pm, which is rare) that embraces local and market cuisine, and absolutely respects quality produce. They do not take reservations.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15847;Tekés;France;Paris;4 bis rue Saint-Sauveur, Paris, 75002, France;48.8659229;2.3495388;22;false;false;Israeli, Middle Eastern;One of the establishments owned by chef Assaf Granit, Tekés is summed up by its name, which is Hebrew for "ceremony". More than a restaurant, it's also a veritable musical extravaganza. The kitchen team puts on a thrilling show, cooking vegetables over an open fire, while the well-drilled waitstaff stand by, ready to spring into action. Flame-grilled leeks with potato and feta purée, fattoush salad with labneh and za'atar, fried gnocchi with yellow curry and yoghurt – just some of the delicious dishes on offer! This culinary journey taking in Levantine tradition and influences from the Middle East embraces intense flavours and carefully selected spices. The options on the mainly vegetarian (although not vegan) menu take the form of dishes to share – which is very much in keeping with the convivial atmosphere!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15848;Couvert de Vignes;France;Chigny-les-Roses;4 place Pommery, Chigny-les-Roses, 51500, France;49.1568458;4.0621731;70;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The village of Chigny-les-Roses in the heart of the Montagne de Reims is the site of this restaurant in a former classroom, which is, indeed, entirely hemmed in by vineyards. Chef Benjamin Gilles can be seen in the kitchen through a window in the dining room. Now his own boss, he signs modern dishes overflowing in fresh flavours and enhanced by a zest of creativity. Vegetables and fruit feature prominently in his culinary score through a variety of preparations (raw, cooked, pickled).;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15849;Sépia;France;Nantes;1 quai Turenne, Nantes, 44000, France;47.2131587;-1.553689;54;true;false;Creative;Lucie Berthier Gembara, riding high from her appearance on France's Top Chef TV competition, often has a full house at her trendy designer bistro on the ground floor of this fine 18C building. After stints working with Gérald Passedat and Alexandre Mazzia, she has retained a clear sense of creativity and an appetite for the Eastern influences of the Mediterranean basin. Her dishes, such as aubergines with charred baba ganoush, eggnog and feta crumble, are full of pleasant surprises. They are distinctly playful, going against the grain when it comes to the codes of gastronomy but no less tasty for it. The lighter lunchtime menu is expanded in the evening.;Terrace;[]
15850;Alebrije;France;Lyon;2 rue Belfort, Lyon, 69004, France;45.7759568;4.8349714;22;true;false;Mexican;After training at the Paul Bocuse Institute and a number of noteworthy spells in top establishments, such as Troisgros, youthful Carla Kirsch, who hails from Veracruz in Mexico, has settled in the Croix-Rousse district. The signature here is clearly Mexican from the décor, which features old rafters with splashes of colour, to the food, which Carla joyfully crafts using top-notch seasonal ingredients (sweet corn in the starter and chili peppers in the dessert). The menu changes monthly and the beverages include a few Mexican wines as well as tequilas and mezcals.;;[]
15852;Finestra by Italo Bassi;France;Bonifacio;51 quai Jérôme-Comparetti, Bonifacio, 20169, France;41.3879548;9.1637107;80;true;true;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;Among the traditional shopfronts, this elegant façade stands out from the crowd on Bonifacio harbour. On the first floor, this superb designer space mimicking the shape of the inverted hull of a ship, with a subtle maritime-inspired decor, features a large window (finestra in Italian) overlooking the port. Chef Italo Bassi, who presides also over the kitchens of his restaurant in Sardinia, has devised a menu that allies the cuisines of Italy and Corsica. The mainly local ingredients are handpicked in these masterfully prepared dishes – the double ravioli with two fillings, burrata, guinea fowl casserole and its reduction, light cream of parmesan and fresh thyme is a particularly appetising signature dish!;Air conditioning;[]
15853;Acte 2;France;Avignon;3 rue de la Petite-Calade, Avignon, 84000, France;43.947781;4.8039181;69;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the city of the famous arts festival, theatre is even part of the restaurant experience. Act I: a young couple of industry professionals set up shop in the historical centre. Act II: dishes that are packed with delicious, fresh local and seasonal ingredients. Act III: excellent value for money, whether you opt for the five-course dinner or the three-course lunch. The scene is set! Tuck into scallop carpaccio and turnip with lemon and juniper, or the veal fillet with truffle and Albufera sauce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15854;Petit Jacques;France;Grimaud;Place des Pénitents, Grimaud, 83310, France;43.2735626;6.5195118;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine;As you make your way up through the pretty paved streets of Grimaud to this enchanting leafy patio, you are already bewitched. Spread over two floors, the charm of this house is undeniable (light wooden floors, raftered ceilings, lime plastered walls, well-worn bench seating and soft lighting). The Quebec-born chef and his partner in charge of the front of house regale diners with spot-on market-fresh cuisine and a traditional culinary line-up, featuring family favourites like onion soup or French toast (of brioche) with a scoop of Madagascan vanilla ice cream to die for! Everything is made in house, including the bread!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15855;L'Argousier;France;Volmunster;1 rue de Sarreguemines, Volmunster, 57720, France;49.1211017;7.3566589;85;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In this pleasant contemporary restaurant, the young chef’s cuisine varies with the seasons. The food is cooked and seasoned to perfection, the presentation flawless, as in this duck fillet with confit vegetables and red wine jus. Friendly and attentive service and a fine selection of vintage rums.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
15856;Frédéric Carrion Cuisine Hôtel;France;Viré;Place André-Lagrange, Viré, 71260, France;46.4493509;4.8421716;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The elegant dining room combines the character of this former coaching inn (parquet, fireplace) with more plush and cosy touches. The chef uses fine regional produce to concoct wonderfully creative dishes. Your meal is accompanied by a delightful selection of wines, including a range of Viré - Clessé wines. The pleasant rooms and spa round off your stay in wine - growing country.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15857;L'Orangerie;France;Gordes;La Bastide de Gordes, 61 rue de la Combe, Gordes, 84220, France;43.9116427;5.1986086;42;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This famous village is one of the most prized in the Luberon Regional Nature Park. This stately home, which dominates the valley, now houses a luxury hotel – as well as this restaurant and its stunning terrace shaded by chestnut trees. In the style of a luxury brasserie, the menu gives some of the classics a Provençal twist: think gambero rosso with grapefruit, sole meunière and dauphinoise potatoes with lemon, or fillet of lamb with white asparagus.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15858;La Grange;France;Bayonne;26 quai Galuperie, Bayonne, 64100, France;43.4906531;-1.4739879;35;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In this city centre restaurant, old stones blend seamlessly with contemporary decoration. On the menu: market - fresh ingredients and a handful of bistro specialities with Basque overtones. In summer, make the most of the terrace beneath the arcades, on the banks of the Nive.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15860;Le Bistrot de la Caillère;France;Candé-sur-Beuvron;36 route des Montils, Candé-sur-Beuvron, 41120, France;47.494174;1.2704352;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Ideally located for anyone visiting the châteaux of the Loire, this inn is firmly rooted in its era. It is run by an enterprising couple, who work and live in harmony with the bucolic landscape of forests and meadows. The original 18C farmhouse has been replaced by a modern building – modern like chef Éric Rialland's cuisine. His well-thought-out bistronomy dishes follow the seasons and oscillate between creativity and tradition. Pleasant terrace for fine weather.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15862;L'Escudella;France;Paris;41 avenue de Ségur, Paris, 75007, France;48.8504724;2.3091433;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine;L'Escudella is, aptly enough, "plate" in Occitan! Paul-Arthur Berlan, the young chef, has worked in some prestigious establishments (Michel Sarran, Yannick Alléno). Here, he marries produce from the terroir of the Greater Paris area with the flavours of Languedoc. With fresh, high-quality ingredients and well-crafted dishes, he hits the mark.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15863;Le Lien;France;Belfort;32 faubourg de Montbéliard, Belfort, 90000, France;47.6348726;6.8573844;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The bond here (‘lien’ in French) is that which ties this young couple (he’s in the kitchen, she in the front of house) to the winegrowers and producers whose work is showcased in the plates and glasses of this friendly bistro. Modern food with a creative twist founded on first-class seasonal ingredients that are allowed to shout their name. Two lunchtime menus and a more elaborate offering in the evening. Highly recommended.;Air conditioning;[]
15864;Séquence;France;Caen;6 rue du 11-Novembre, Caen, 14000, France;49.17784;-0.35874;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Antoine Triquet may have an unusual career path (which led him from insurance to cooking), but the culinary fundamentals are present and correct! Ingredients are carefully selected to put the spotlight on local producers, nature and the seasons, and the cooking is always on point... This is modern, clear and uncluttered cuisine with a sincere, even generous approach! At dinnertime, the set menu is divided into three sequences, each featuring a given ingredient prepared in three different ways, which allows them to use the ingredient in its entirety. For example, veal: veal croquette, vitello sardinia, or standing rump served medium rare, accompanied by an onion purée and a delicious gravy. To be enjoyed in a contemporary decor with an open kitchen.;Wheelchair access;[]
15866;Cascade;France;Salles-la-Source;26 cour de la Filature, Salles-la-Source, 12330, France;44.4378842;2.5135244;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;What a pretty village clinging to a cliff and famous for its cooling waterfall! What a pleasant, convivial place, with its warm, colourful bistro decor, lovely old wooden floorboards, counter and arty posters on the walls (and let's not forget the terrace overlooking the courtyard in front of the town hall). In the kitchen, chef Marine Guichou cooks up a feast, using carefully selected local produce, which she skilfully prepares in a fresh, authentic bistro style. And with her almond pannacotta and chocolate mousse on a cocoa crumble, she has created the quintessential dessert for anyone with a sweet tooth!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15868;Goxoki;France;Bayonne;24 rue Marengo, Bayonne, 64100, France;43.4907577;-1.4724923;50;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Goxoki means an "inviting place" in Basque, which is perfectly suited to this restaurant run by the Hourcastagnou family in the Petit Bayonne neighbourhood. In a timelessly elegant setting, the food shines a spotlight on local seasonal produce, with a mouth-watering game menu including fillet of wood pigeon and pithiviers of the legs, hare à la royale and wild turbot with beurre blanc. Regulars come back often to tuck into the indulgent, generous dishes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15869;Choral;France;Annecy;33 avenue des Romains, Annecy, 74000, France;45.9097943;6.1202043;15;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the Romains district, 10 minutes from the centre, take a seat in this long, Scandinavian-inspired dining room opened by a chef who did a stint at Le Clos des Sens with Laurent Petit, before globe-trotting around the planet. The memory of his line-caught cod, tetragon, lemon and capers à la grenobloise lingers with us still. Alban’s instinctive, fine dining score (free of butter, cream and milk, except for desserts) is, for the most part, dictated by the availability of fresh market produce (such as baked apricots, honey and rhubarb sorbet), which are then given a deft professional spin. Mystery menu in several courses in the evening.;Air conditioning;[]
15870;Les Gueules Noires;France;Vouvray;66 rue de la Vallée-Coquette, Vouvray, 37210, France;47.4210532;0.7819161;100;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;The troglodyte dining room, wood burning fire in winter and the terrace shaded by a wisteria in fine weather are just a few of the discreet appeals of this charming establishment. The cuisine is tasty and wholesome, based on local produce and served with Loire wines. Booking advisable.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15871;Nous Restaurant;France;Quimper;17 rue Saint-Mathieu, Quimper, 29000, France;47.9954831;-4.107253;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine;With its discreet façade and small glass-paned front door, this restaurant is located in a pedestrianised cobbled street in the city centre. The light-filled interior has bay windows overlooking the street on one side and a pretty courtyard decorated with large window boxes on the other. The chef puts a lot of work into his dishes, which are made using local ingredients. The courgette flower, soufflé with fine pollack stuffing, shellfish sauce vierge, rocket cream and two-lemon fritter is a good illustration of his masterful dishes that are packed with flavour.;;[]
15872;Les Toits - Hôtel de Paris Saint-Tropez;France;Saint-Tropez;1 traverse de la Gendarmerie, Saint-Tropez, 83990, France;43.2695969;6.6359426;24;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Timeless Saint Tropez remains as legendary as ever – this outdoor restaurant perched on the roof terrace of the fabled hotel is further proof of that. Gazing out over the bay and the tiled roofs of the village, you can savour cuisine inspired by the Mediterranean and Provence, with a few Italian touches thrown in for good measure (Sicilian gambas, tiramisu etc) – after all, the new chef, whose CV includes Il Carpaccio, Le Grand Véfour and Pierro TT in Paris, is Italian. A simpler set menu is proposed at lunchtime.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
15876;Cadet;France;Nancy;3 rue du Sergent-Blandan, Nancy, 54000, France;48.68205;6.16604;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Between the Villa Majorelle and the Musée de l'École de Nancy, this restaurant is housed in a hundred-year-old former hairdressing salon. In a Scandinavian-style interior, brightened up by crates of vegetables, a few trendy cookery books and a vintage Faema coffee machine behind the counter, chef Theo Mareschal (previously encountered at La Maison dans le Parc in Nancy and Kontrast in Oslo) sticks to the brief and cooks up appealing contemporary cuisine that's simple and accessible, a case in point being the veal, mushrooms and baby potatoes or the surprising dessert of vanilla ice cream with squid ink, as black as a painting by Pierre Soulages!;;[]
15878;Le Bouillon;France;Annecy;9 rue de la Gare, Annecy, 74000, France;45.89916;6.12187;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In addition to meaning stock, a bouillon also refers to the first restaurants opened in Paris in the 18C. In a recently refurbished modern interior, the chef crafts tasty market-fresh recipes, with the odd Asian twist, such as a splendid loin of croaker in a chorizo crust underscored by a red curry and curcuma stock.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
15879;La Table du Château;France;Dampierre-en-Yvelines;1 Grande-Rue, Dampierre-en-Yvelines, 78720, France;48.7061239;1.9871812;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine, French;The lord of the manor, who now owns this beautiful 17C inn, has entrusted the kitchens to chef Élisabeth Passédat. She may have worked abroad for many years, but she hasn't forgotten her French classics – pan-fried foie gras, pâté en croûte with Houdan poultry, veal sweetbreads, tournedos Rossini-style Charolais beef. She puts a modern spin on these dishes, blending them with seasonal ingredients and drawing inspiration from France's terroirs. In this way, she comes up with creations such as monkfish and spaetzle, Normandy cider velouté, or ravioli with mushrooms, Morbier cheese and a vin jaune emulsion.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15880;Ekume;France;Marseille;139 rue Sainte, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2908092;5.367523;18;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;After clocking up some remarkable experiences, Panamanian chef Edgar Bosquez has dropped anchor in Marseille, not far from the abbey of St Victor. In a spruce, pared-back interior, he showcases fish, seafood and Provençal flavours in a lineup of deftly crafted, suave-tasting menus, including one devoted to bouillabaisse.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15881;L'effet Papilles;France;Laval;16 rue des Déportés, Laval, 53000, France;48.0697331;-0.7729361;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the town, almost within shouting distance of the castle, this small modern bistro, which sports a workshop vibe of wood and metal, is the brainchild of chef Adrien Barrier, who was born in Le Mans and knows Mayenne inside out. After stints with Yannick Alléno and Philippe Mille, this gifted craftsman curates feel-good, flavoursome food that hits the spot every time, be it his white asparagus with haddock, houmous and hazelnut crumble or the confit of pork belly, pressed aubergine and pork jus.;Wheelchair access;[]
15882;Lil'Home;France;Bordeaux;29 quai des Chartrons, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8505023;-0.5701;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This attractive restaurant on the Quai des Chartrons has a dining area with parquet flooring made up of repurposed wine crates, velvet-upholstered seats, wicker lampshades and hanging plants – think "chic bistro" style. The modern and creative cooking takes the form of multi-course surprise menus. Good selection of organic and biodynamic wines.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15883;Rouge;France;Nice;2 rue de Foresta, Nice, 06000, France;43.6973251;7.2828128;32;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sharing;Behind the port, in the antique dealer neighbourhood, a disciple of Yves Camdeborde is at the helm of this friendly wine bar. The chef prepares lovely Mediterranean sharing plates, concocted with ultra-fresh produce. It is delicious and hearty, and the wallet doesn't take too heavy a hit. A hundred or so lively wines feature on the list, also at reasonable prices. Open all day from noon (no reservations taken).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15884;Le Roc;France;Veyrier-du-Lac;13 vieille route des Pensières, Veyrier-du-Lac, 74290, France;45.8889;6.17208;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Tasting menus, an appetising à la carte lineup (perch from Lake Geneva with sorrel and pike roe, poached scallops in helianthus, pithiviers of duck and foie gras), a splendid wine list, a contemporary stylish interior in a chic alpine vein and a youthful team that is always spot on: chef Yoann Conte has covered all the bases in this, his second restaurant, also housed in the famous Maison Bleue. And, as always, the view of Lake Annecy is jaw dropping.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15885;Braise;France;Paris;19 rue d'Anjou, Paris, 75008, France;48.8706095;2.3212154;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The former second of Substance, Sylvain Courivaud, is determined to kindle our appetites in this contemporary venue entirely devoted to wood-fired cooking. Whatever the method from Japanese barbecue or Big Green Egg to a smoker, Sylvain combines consummate technique with a love of high-quality produce. The vibe of this trendy eatery is warm and welcoming.;Air conditioning;[]
15886;Auberge des Gorges;France;Servoz;81 route du Mont, Servoz, 74310, France;45.9316196;6.7686837;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;With its cosy mountain-style decor, this converted 18C coaching inn on the road to the Gorges de la Diosaz is home to a creative restaurant that piqued our curiosity. Over the course of a single multi-course set menu, the young chef cooks up dishes that draw ingredients both from the lakes and the mountains, such as Arctic char with beurre blanc, cooked to perfection, or crayfish ravioli enhanced by a beautifully emulsified bisque. On top of that, the welcome and service are the epitome of charm. Six guestrooms for an extended stay, and view of the summit of Mont Blanc.;;[]
15888;Auberge du Cheval Blanc;France;Westhalten;20 rue de Rouffach, Westhalten, 68250, France;47.956665;7.2603869;32;false;false;Modern Cuisine;An upscale restaurant, run by the same family since 1785. In the attractive contemporary dining area, meals are paired with fine wines from Alsace, including an interesting selection by the glass. The culinary style is refined, the products of high quality, often locally-sourced, and the presentations elegant. The ambition to treat diners well is clear: you're sure to come out with a spring in your step. Guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15889;Maison Renard;France;Béthune;15 place de la République, Béthune, 62400, France;50.532338;2.64074;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Sébastien Renard (Top Chef semi-finalist in 2022) has taken over the former premises of his mentor, the great chef Marc Meurin. This red-brick mansion oozes style, and its bar and elegant glass roof lend it undeniable flair. The chef, who hails from the region and made his solo debut here, turns out a carte blanche menu inspired by conversations with the growers who supply his kitchen with their produce. Dishes such as green asparagus, sheep's milk fromage frais and tarragon cream, or poached eggs in a red wine sauce with mushroom cream and walnut emulsion showcase all the savoir-faire of this chef with an impressive CV to his name.;Wheelchair access;[]
15895;Maison Zugno;France;Barretaine;Les Monts de Vaux, Barretaine, 39800, France;46.8174742;5.7392942;48;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Dating back to the late 18C, this former coaching inn has been turned into a charming hotel (nine guestrooms, a swimming pool and spa) and a restaurant with three small dining areas (wooden floors, walnut tables, exposed brick walls, floral wallpaper or a green wall). Chef Quentin Defert makes modern, entirely gluten-free cuisine from seasonal, often local produce (but that's not all). Starters include a pear brunoise paired with blue cheese from the nearby dairy in La Marre, creamed corn combined with hazelnuts, and melt-in-the-mouth Iberian pork belly served with romanesco and elevated by a flavoursome Thai emulsion.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15896;Mr Guss;France;Nérac;7 avenue Mondenard, Nérac, 47600, France;44.134672;0.3396856;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Augustin Guibert aka Guss, a chef with an impeccable track record, is going solo with this contemporary restaurant set at the foot of a beautiful 19C stone building. This inventive cook impresses with his substantial technical prowess, which allows him to play with flavours and textures, as he does with his violetta aubergine, roasted then glazed with honey and satay, potato fritters, hollandaise sauce with caramelised onions. Without fail, the arrival of the delicious dishes bursting with colour puts a smile on your face. Congratulations, too, for showcasing the finest local produce, most notably the vegetables.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15897;Le Bois Blanc;France;Romorantin-Lanthenay;11 rue de la Sirène, Romorantin-Lanthenay, 41200, France;47.3595391;1.7450851;73;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chambord asparagus and Sologne strawberries, freshwater fish like pike, catfish and carp, game in season: chef Maxime Valleye, with stints at Georges Blanc and in his parents’ establishment, sings an ode to his region. Even the restaurant’s name, which is evocative of a birch tree, is in tune with Sologne’s forests. Maxime carefully crafts seasonal dishes steeped in classical overtones: pork, confit of egg yolk, spinach and goat’s cheese crumble. The classy, stylish interior of this contemporary bistro sports varnished wooden tables and vintage incandescent light bulbs. Most of the tipples on the wine list are from the Val-de-Loire.;Wheelchair access;[]
15898;Emporio Armani Caffè;France;Paris;149 boulevard Saint-Germain, Paris, 75006, France;48.853693;2.3327031;24;true;false;Italian;Just across from the famous Les Deux Magots, this smart contemporary-style brasserie on the ground floor of the Michelin-starred Armani/Ristorante is run at a brisk pace by the same Italian team. From verdure alla griglia drizzled with Apulian olive oil, linguine alle vongole veraci – cooked al dente and served with a delicious helping of bottarga – to classic tiramisu with a light and full-flavoured mascarpone cream, as well as spaghetti al pomodoro, ravioli del plin, risotto, tortellini: all the classics of Italian cuisine are present and correct, executed in time-honoured tradition.;Air conditioning;[]
15901;Les Jardiniers;France;Ligré;1 La Gare, Ligré, 37500, France;47.1376164;0.2783905;91;true;true;Creative;Along the old railway line, which is now a greenway, this charming bistro occupies a restored winegrower's house with exposed stonework and beams, an open kitchen and a pewter-topped counter at the entrance. A large kitchen garden and a truffle farm supply the establishment with fruit and vegetables. Formerly sous-chef to Thibaut Ruggeri at Fontevraud le Restaurant, Belgian chef Martin Bolaers makes the most of the vegetable garden to create wholesome and creative cuisine in which plants play the starring role: a starter dubbed "L'Instant T", for example, is improvised using vegetables picked that very morning. Local ingredients – such as poultry and cheese – also feature in the credits.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15902;Monsieur B;France;Bourgoin-Jallieu;80 rue de la Liberté, Bourgoin-Jallieu, 38300, France;45.5886916;5.2782804;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The young chef cooks up fresh, tasty bistronomy cuisine without any showboating. The lunch set menu changes every week, while the evening menu evolves on a monthly basis in line with the market stalls and the seasons. An example might be his simple and tasty starter of peas, red tuna and kiwi. A convivial bistro in the heart of the town-centre pedestrian precinct.;Wheelchair access;[]
15903;La Table de l'Europe;France;Villeréal;1 place Jean-Moulin, Villeréal, 47210, France;44.6369184;0.7442802;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Opposite the country town’s covered market, this tastefully appointed guesthouse and restaurant invite diners to sit down, relax and enjoy a good meal. You will taste the fine cuisine of a veteran chef who deftly crafts appetising French-accented dishes, depicted by slow-cooked pork belly and fluffy mashed potato. The chef’s desserts (she originally trained as a pastry chef) are wickedly irresistible: a hazelnut extravaganza of praline, hazelnut mousse and butterscotch – to die for!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15907;La Bonne Auberge;France;Stiring-Wendel;15 rue Nationale, Stiring-Wendel, 57350, France;49.1932027;6.9150991;45;false;false;Creative;Lydia Egloff prepares inventive cuisine with complex flavours, while her sister gracefully welcomes diners. Unusual decor and a winter garden with bay windows. A fine wine list. The name says it all!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15908;La Grillade Gourmande;France;Epernay;16 rue de Reims, Epernay, 51200, France;49.0449565;3.9614171;61;true;false;Grills;This restaurant's specialities include boned squab with foie gras in puff pastry or traditional textbook calf sweetbread, all of which are the handiwork of a friendly chef of Lyon origins. The interior is the epitome of friendly and buzzy and the garden is bliss, come summertime!;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15909;Cheval Blanc;France;Feldbach;1 rue de Bisel, Feldbach, 68640, France;47.5356853;7.2650225;87;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;In this typical Sundgau house, food is a passion that has been handed down from generation to generation. Father and son cook lovely traditional dishes enhanced with a modern edge. Very good choice of wines. This White Horse really is a fine steed!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15910;L'Ô à la Bouche;France;Les Contamines-Montjoie;510 route Notre-Dame-de-la-Gorge, Les Contamines-Montjoie, 74170, France;45.8181918;6.7282744;81;false;true;Modern Cuisine;One site and two moods united by the same desire to make your mouth water! On the ground floor, a contemporary style of decor, and fresh, tasty gourmet cuisine, prepared by a chef with a distinct fondness for fresh produce and fish. Try the excellent home-made deli meats, too. Specials announced according to the market. Sit back and drink in the conviviality of the mountains.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15911;J'MCA;France;Coulanges-la-Vineuse;12 rue André-Vildieu, Coulanges-la-Vineuse, 89580, France;47.7007664;3.5819116;39;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Traditional, expertly crafted, market-fresh cuisine that lets the ingredient shout its name, such as lacquered sweetbread with peanuts and cauliflower. The à la carte lineup stars a range of pedigree Gallic classics such as homemade terrine, upside-down onion and chicory pie, calf’s head and even game in season. Cheerful service sets the tone in this handsome abode just a stone’s throw from the village church and square.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15913;Le Chou Rouge - Le Petit Chou;France;Entraygues-sur-Truyère;3 place de la République, Entraygues-sur-Truyère, 12140, France;44.64602;2.564945;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the town’s main square, the ground floor of a traditional edifice is the HQ of this ‘Parisian - style’ bistro. It is decorated with a jumble of old furniture and knick - knacks picked up by the owners, and it serves market - fresh cuisine, sourced only from local producers. Everything, or almost, is homemade. Four pretty rooms for overnight stays.;Terrace;[]
15914;Le Castellaras;France;Fayence;461 chemin de Peymeyan, Fayence, 83440, France;43.629682;6.6734312;25;false;false;Provençal;Quentin and Hermance Joplet are at the helm of this family business in a refurbished house, whose open kitchen backs onto a splendid terrace, which, in turn, commands a knockout view over the valley and the walled village of Fayence. The food is steeped in the colours and flavours of Provence and inspired by the market and the seasons, with dishes such as fillet of Mediterranean meagre, panisse and seasonal vegetables, or fig tart, almond cream and red berry sorbet. The attentive service is tailored to each guest. A handful of guestrooms should you wish to stay overnight.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15915;L'Essentiel;France;Dijon;12 rue Audra, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3256091;5.0343065;26;false;true;Modern Cuisine;At this restaurant just outside the city's touristy centre, a young owner-chef concocts a seasonal menu, underscored by distinctive, harmonious flavours and exquisitely presented. Those pressed for time will opt for the appetising lunch set menu. Best enjoyed on the patio, which is in great demand in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15916;La Bartavelle;France;Goult;29 rue du Cheval-Blanc, Goult, 84220, France;43.8637273;5.2426836;83;false;true;Provençal;Located in a picturesque Luberon village, this small but charming family business is run by an experienced couple. In a bid to ensure the dishes attain optimum quality, the chef offers a deliberately limited menu. You certainly can't argue with the results: meticulously prepared and fragrant recipes inspired by Provence and the finest seasonal ingredients. Considered a safe bet in the region, it has its fair share of regulars, which is always a good sign. It is wise to book a table.;Terrace;[]
15917;Taillard;France;Goumois;3 route de la Corniche, Goumois, 25470, France;47.2607439;6.9452705;74;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The stunning view of the valley is flanked by hearty, country cooking by a chef, who has a knack for flavoursome, delicate recipes. Pedigree French fare, illustrated by a fricassee of morel mushrooms in flaky pastry.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15918;Le Pélican;France;Geneston;13 place Georges-Gaudet, Geneston, 44140, France;47.0561382;-1.5131743;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Olivier Guenoun, chef of this family business since 2010, crafts recipes that appeal to modern tastebuds in a menu dotted with daily specials that vary with market availability. Just like the regulars to the Pelican, open your beak wide to sample a slice of Nantais cake, a ubiquitous regional classic, treated to a new twist with roast pineapple and a mojito sorbet!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15919;Chavant;France;Bresson;2 rue Émile-Chavant, Bresson, 38320, France;45.1381602;5.7502744;21;false;true;Classic Cuisine;It is so nice to come and enjoy summer days in this inn, run by the Chavant family since 1852. The food puts a smile on your face, and other assets include the wine cellar, swimming pool and spacious guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15922;Chez Parenti;France;Propriano;10 avenue Napoléon-III, Propriano, 20110, France;41.67571;8.902112;100;false;false;Seafood;Chez Parenti has been around since 1935, its kitchens successively manned by generation after generation of the same family! Those who love seafood are in for a treat – lobster and langoustines sold by weight, fish caught in the bay – but, to cater to all palates, there is also a small selection of Corsican meats, as well as an array of wonderful local cheeses. The cooking is technically on point and the dishes are nicely put together. Enjoy your meal in the comfort of the large shaded terrace that faces the Gulf of Valinco and the boats at anchor.;Great view,Terrace;[]
15924;Les Maisons  Rabanel;France;Arles;7 rue des Carmes, Arles, 13200, France;43.6760017;4.6269713;90;true;true;Creative;Jean-Luc Rabanel is a colourful character with a lilting accent, who perpetually reinvents his vegetable-based cuisine. Les Maisons Rabanel, a single place but two styles of cooking: Greeniotage, which tends towards bistro food, and Greenstronome for fine dining. Always going out on a limb, this engaging chef shakes things up at every service. A unique personality.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15925;Jiva;France;Crozet;Jiva Hill Resort, Route d'Harée, Crozet, 01170, France;46.2699359;6.0209591;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In Sanskrit, jiva means life, giving the visitor a foretaste of what to expect in this luxurious, understated resort. The restaurant specialises in exquisitely balanced French cuisine, using the best, fresh seasonal produce. Diners will enjoy a breathtaking view over Mont Blanc, whenever the weather permits, from the panoramic terrace.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15926;Restaurant de L'Île Benoist;France;Courseulles-sur-Mer;Route de Ver-sur-Mer, Courseulles-sur-Mer, 14470, France;49.3353925;-0.4663337;82;true;false;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;An oyster-farming family is behind this trendy, well-designed restaurant, which gives pride of place to locally fished seafood and, of course, oysters purified just opposite and other fine Normandy produce. The chef places particular importance on the careful presentation of the dishes, which are as attractive as they are flavoursome.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15927;Les Jardins Fleuris;France;Parcey;35 route Nationale 5, Parcey, 39100, France;47.02032;5.495;60;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In this well-kept traditional establishment, the chef creates generous and tasty dishes with nods to the local terroir: venison terrine with foie gras, tournedos of rabbit with mushroom duxelle and a beef gravy with morels, frozen soufflé with Marc d'Arbois. Pleasant terrace to the rear and a charming welcome.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15928;Chez Séraphin;France;Peri;au village, Peri, 20167, France;42.0051778;8.9213626;43;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A characteristic Corsican house in a charming mountainside village sets the splendid scene to sample wholesome country fare, prepared simply from painstakingly selected ingredients, among which Corsica’s famous cured meats and fruit, vegetables and herbs from the garden. Take a seat on the spacious terrace and drink in the jaw-dropping view of the mountains and ancient oak forest. Just a word of warning: bank cards are not accepted, so take cash!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15929;Le Belvédère;France;Porto-Vecchio;Route de Palombaggia, Porto-Vecchio, 20137, France;41.5864468;9.3000834;87;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Tuck into ravioli with preserved lemon and a Greek yoghurt cream with coriander, while comfortably seated on the large waterside terrace in the shade of umbrella pines and palm trees overlooking Porto Vecchio's old town... What more could you ask for? Modern cuisine, top-notch ingredients and true technical prowess: the fennel-roasted meagre is precisely cooked and served with a delicious sauce. In the peace and quiet of this enclave, expect a feast for the eyes and a treat for the taste buds.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15930;Don Cesar;France;Porto-Vecchio;Rue du Commandant-Quilici, Porto-Vecchio, 20137, France;41.5994632;9.2845968;36;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Mediterranean Cuisine;The restaurant of the Don Cesar Hotel is certainly not lacking in charm with its luxurious, refined interior and large bay windows giving onto the terrace. The meticulously prepared and flavoursome food lies at the crossroads of French and Italian cuisine, and gives seafood pride of place, but also serves a wide range of dishes based on pasta made on site!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15931;La Table de la Plage;France;Sartène;Domaine de Murtoli, Vallée de l'Ortolo, Sartène, 20100, France;41.5092038;8.9124287;50;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;By the prettiest beach in the Domaine de Murtoli, this restaurant with an exceptional decor inspired by fishermen's wooden huts is well worth a visit. Locally caught fish, grilled crayfish, veal, beef or lamb reared on the estate: diners can tuck into dishes such as John Dory à la meunière, courgettes stuffed with caponata and a rock fish jus. The pasta dishes make for a deliciously indulgent option. To access this highly exclusive property, it is necessary to book – you will then also be able to head for the beach with a deckchair and towel after your meal.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
15932;Hostellerie de la Mer;France;Crozon;11 quai du Fret, Crozon, 29160, France;48.2854481;-4.5079655;27;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;The chef crafts cuisine in tune with the zeitgeist, wonderfully blending fish from the local catch and ingredients from Brittany's terroir, such as house-smoked salmon, tangy herb cream and buckwheat blini, or the blanquette of monkfish and Molène sausage, vegetables and steamed potatoes. The cooking is precise and accentuates the well-chosen ingredients!;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
15933;La Calypso;France;Carnac;158 rue du Pô, Carnac, 56340, France;47.5803262;-3.1010912;81;true;false;Seafood, Grills;This charming maritime inspired bistro has a loyal band of regulars. They come here to savour the freshest fish and seafood prepared with great simplicity.;Wheelchair access;[]
15934;La Taverne Besson;France;Castelnau-de-Lévis;Rue Aubijoux, Castelnau-de-Lévis, 81150, France;43.9383933;2.0836081;50;true;false;Classic Cuisine;This is an original Taverne with its contemporary, elegant, light - filled decor – and a terrace giving onto the countryside. Enjoy the enticing food, blending good local ingredients and original touches. You can also stay the night in one of the cleverly designed guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15935;Le Vauban;France;Antibes;7 bis rue Thuret, Antibes, 06600, France;43.58199;7.12647;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In a bustling street in Antibes' old town, Le Vauban serves up good, contemporary, French cuisine that is in step with the seasons and technically impeccable. The restaurant's reputation is firmly established and the place is often full – be sure to book!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15936;Domaine d'Auriac;France;Carcassonne;2535 route de Saint-Hilaire, Carcassonne, 11000, France;43.1916124;2.335519;96;true;false;Classic Cuisine;A magnificent 19C property steeped in history sets the elegant scene and provides the perfect foil for classical recipes, enhanced by the odd modern twist. When the weather allows, make a beeline for the terrace overlooking the grounds. The epitome of good taste in a quintessentially French country estate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
15937;Côté Cour;France;Aix-en-Provence;19 cours Mirabeau, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.526745;5.447622;47;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Aix’s exclusive Cours Mirabeau is the place to see and be seen! A pared-back decor of natural materials, (very) soft lighting, a sliding roof, a glamorous edge and lounge music set the distinctive scene created by former Top Chef contestant, Ronan Kernen. The names of the dishes on the menu reflect his unorthodox approach: lamb cooked two ways/‘my version’ of stuffed cabbage, ‘my version’ of Saint-Honoré…;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15938;Le Vintrépide;France;Aix-en-Provence;48 rue du Puits-Neuf, Aix-en-Provence, 13100, France;43.5318254;5.4505362;54;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;One immediately falls under the charm of this contemporary and cosy decor (designer furniture, light wood and green-blue walls): a pleasant little place run by a pair who are eager to please. The chef prepares delicious seasonal dishes according to his inspiration. Meanwhile, the sommelier always has the right advice to guide you in your wine choice. A winning duo.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
15939;Auberge de la Vallée;France;Crozant;14 rue Armand-Guillaumin, Crozant, 23160, France;46.3913877;1.6212383;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Locally reared meat (lamb, veal, beef), regional cheeses (mainly goat’s) and veggies from his large market garden… The chef is a fan of the region as you will taste. The delicious food is served in a pleasantly rustic interior. The epitome of a French country inn!;Air conditioning;[]
15941;Fine Gueule;France;Nice;2 rue de l'Hôtel-de-Ville, Nice, 06300, France;43.6962694;7.2718323;30;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In Nice's old town, opposite the town hall, this restaurant's newly refurbished interior is organised around an open kitchen and a counter where customers can sit to eat. But the real pleasure is to be found in the food, with traditional dishes chalked up on the board each day, including for starters the home-made pissaladière, devilled eggs or calamari a la plancha.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
15942;L'Envolée - La Demeure Montaigne;France;Paris;18 rue Clément-Marot, Paris, 75008, France;48.8678426;2.3031238;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This exclusive venue established in a Haussmannian luxury hotel is a short walk from the Champs-Elysées and Avenue Montaigne. Set in an inner courtyard beneath a glass roof, it is reminiscent of a winter garden conservatory with its cane chairs. Sheltered from prying eyes, you will sample modern seasonal cuisine.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15944;L'Ormeau;France;Cancale;4 quai Thomas, Cancale, 35260, France;48.6708798;-1.8519726;62;false;true;Seafood;Who could turn down a platter of Cancale oysters, scallops and abalone (the restaurant’s namesake)? Even better when served with a splendid view of the fleet of fishing boats that guarantees their freshness! A stylish interior fronted by a pleasant terrace sets the scene for premium seafood dishes, such as razor clams stuffed with parsley, garlic and butter, home-made fish soup or local scallops roasted on the shell, white butter and vegetable risotto. Round off your meal on a sweet note with a pancaked stuffed with warm apples for example.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15945;La Villa Tartary;France;Aubenas;64 rue de Tartary, Aubenas, 07200, France;44.6226889;4.3972815;62;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Fine freestone vaulting, designer furniture, a delightful terrace... This converted water mill – previously used in the silk production process – has bags of charm. Lovely flavours on the menu.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15946;La Barbacane;France;Carcassonne;Place Auguste-Pierre-Pont, Carcassonne, 11000, France;43.2056386;2.3627119;71;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Set deep in historic Carcassonne, the Hôtel de la Cité is a superb example of neo-Gothic architecture, built in 1909 on the site of the former episcopal palace, whose magnificent gardens abut the ramparts. Inside, stained-glass windows, coats of arms and wainscoting lend it an ambience worthy of 19C French architect Viollet-le-Duc. Based on top quality ingredients, notably Mediterranean fish and seafood, as well as game and mushrooms in autumn, the menu champions the region’s terroir in dishes that add a new spin to classical recipes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
15947;Le Balbec - Grand Hôtel de Cabourg;France;Cabourg;Grand Hôtel de Cabourg, Les Jardins du Casino, Cabourg, 14390, France;49.2937355;-0.1155948;76;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The Grand Hôtel de Cabourg, once frequented by Marcel Proust, is one of the best-preserved seaside hotels from the Belle Époque and a gem of Art Deco architecture. Le Balbec – one of the hotel's restaurants – is located in the gallery, which overlooks the seafront, and where serving precise, refined dishes with an abundance of beautiful flavours is a matter of pride. For food lovers in search of lost time!;Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
15948;La Maison du Safran à l'Allée des Vignes;France;Cajarc;32 boulevard du Tour-de-Ville, Cajarc, 46160, France;44.4848731;1.8435349;82;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The Franco-Mexican chef, Claude-Emmanuel Robin, and his Russian wife, Evgenia, fell in love with this former presbytery in Carjac, an exquisite village in Quercy. They have tastefully turned it into an elegant, charming venue with a restaurant and a shop on the saffron theme. The bistronomic slant shines through in the creative, flavoursome cuisine, served alfresco on the lovely patio in fine weather.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15949;Million;France;Albertville;8 place de la Liberté, Albertville, 73200, France;45.6783417;6.3930066;31;false;false;Classic Cuisine;A family - run establishment that cultivates tradition, both in its restaurant, where the classics are served, and in the nicely old - fashioned guestrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15951;La Table de Beaurecueil;France;Beaurecueil;66 allée des Mûriers, Beaurecueil, 13100, France;43.512823;5.5434456;54;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant is housed in a former sheep barn and features a resolutely contemporary design (only a few of the original rustic features remain). It offers “cuisine du terroir” based on high quality produce. Wine by the glass.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15952;La Bonne Auberge;France;Dury;63 route Nationale, Dury, 80480, France;49.84617;2.27053;29;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In this pretty inn, you simply decide how many courses you would like and the chef will do the rest! The young chef is rather bold in his cooking, sometimes dreaming up original combinations of flavours (no bad thing in this region where tradition reigns supreme). Pleasant, efficient service and good value for money. It is worth noting that a new shop adjoining the restaurant has been opened for takeaway dishes, from starter to dessert, concocted by the chef.;Wheelchair access;[]
15954;Auberge de Briant;France;Briant;au bourg, Briant, 71110, France;46.3002561;4.1492916;93;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The spacious and light new dining room gives onto the water and surrounding greenery. Tuck into the delicious dishes made by Filipe, the chef – pressé of Charolais oxtail and crayfish with sauce ravigote, sea bass roasted in olive oil, dill and garlic cromesquis... – and the tasty desserts made by Angélique, his wife!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15955;Le Quatrième Mur;France;Bordeaux;2 place de la Comédie, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8426779;-0.5741434;69;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The quatrième mur (‘fourth wall’) of a theatre is the invisible one that separates the actors from the audience. An apt name for this restaurant set in Bordeaux’ iconic Grand Théâtre. Philippe Etchebest plays a gloriously simple, understated score focusing on first-rate ingredients, high-flying technique, a side dish and a jus. The terrace on one of the opera house’s outdoor side galleries is heavenly. Bookings essential – two sittings at lunchtime and in the evening. The menus change weekly.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15956;La Route d'Argent;France;Bozouls;1 route de Gabriac, Bozouls, 12340, France;44.46856;2.73242;68;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;On the ground floor of the hotel, this restaurant, which sports a bright, modern interior, has been taken over by a dynamic duo comprised of the former second and his wife. Tuck into heartwarming, bountiful fare made with regional produce: Aubrac beef and trout, persillade of lamb sweetbreads or squab breast. Traditional aligot (mashed potatoes and cheese) is served with the main course.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
15957;La Table de Haute-Serre;France;Cieurac;Château de Haute-Serre, Cieurac, 46230, France;44.3900727;1.4898894;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the wine storehouse of a château in the heart of the vineyards, this restaurant exudes the very particular charm of truly authentic places. Charcuterie rack, butcher's block, ham slicer and cases of wine herald a wonderful moment of gourmet delights, rounded off by wines from the estate. Rotisserie evening every Friday. Just delicious.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15959;Fleur de Sel;France;Cagnes-sur-Mer;85 montée de la Bourgade, Cagnes-sur-Mer, 06800, France;43.666145;7.145905;96;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Fleur de Sel, taken over by a couple of young industry professionals, Alexis Cachat and Chloé Feuillet, has the requisite crunch, freshness and flavour. The promising pair met while plying their trade at a MICHELIN-starred restaurant in the Massif de l'Estérel, and are now delighting their own guests with meticulous Mediterranean cuisine. Taking their cue from the seasons, they offer good value for money: courgette flower stuffed with ricotta, olives, anchovies, fresh herbs, gazpacho and crunchy local courgette. Chloé not only provides cordial service, she is also in charge of desserts: think brownie with roasted hazelnuts, vanilla cream and candied apricots with rosemary.;Air conditioning;[]
15960;La Poste et Hôtel La Reconce;France;Poisson;25 route des Michelets, Poisson, 71600, France;46.3849875;4.127896;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The Restaurant de la Poste is now run by a chef who hails from the village, ably assisted by his wife. His ambition is clear: to regale diners with modern dishes that celebrate good local produce – Charolais entrecote with seasonal vegetables is a good example. Stylish, well - kept rooms, should you wish to stay over.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
15961;Côté Mer;France;Cancale;4 rue Ernest-Lamort, Cancale, 35260, France;48.6681727;-1.8626259;55;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Inhale the salty sea air of the little port of Cancale, which makes for a picturesque sight with its fishermen's houses. In this restaurant overlooking the bay, you can sample cuisine that showcases first and foremost local coastal produce, but not to the exclusion of other ingredients: scallops, oysters, saltmarsh lamb, lobster, abalones… And all at eater-friendly prices.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
15963;Les Singuliers;France;Saint-Astier;6 rue Montaigne, Saint-Astier, 24110, France;45.1442997;0.5282938;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of Périgord Blanc, this traditional stone-built house, which sports a tasteful interior, bends over backwards to shine the spotlight on local artisans (the cutlery is exquisite) and local produce: aromatic herbs from the garden, Chantérac vegetables, Neuvic sturgeon, etc. From his gleaming open kitchen, Louis Festa, a young chef with a great track record, has devised a single surprise set menu (that can be tailored to suit your appetite) starring ambitious, spontaneous dishes that respect the seasons: Le Puy green lentils prepared three ways, Ribérac Limousin beef on the Japanese barbecue.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15964;Le Dauphin;France;Le Breuil-en-Auge;2 rue de L'Église, Le Breuil-en-Auge, 14130, France;49.2277429;0.225582;77;true;false;Modern Cuisine;With its half-timbering and quaint charm, this characteristic old inn is the quintessence of Normandy and is now the haunt of a young couple who pay tribute to Normandy’s produce. The Dutch-born chef crafts modern, inspired cuisine, such as monkfish with green peas, aubergine caviar and a floral emulsion, or an upside-down apple tarte Tatin with vanilla ice cream – that is wickedly tempting!;;[]
15965;Le Bistro 1911;France;Cahors;5 avenue Charles-de-Freycinet, Cahors, 46000, France;44.4505481;1.4342455;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The chef enthusiastically prepares up - to - date dishes, served in an elegant room adorned with stained glass. Magnificent wine list and a simpler lunchtime menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
15966;Le Lassey - Château Sainte-Sabine;France;Sainte-Sabine;8 route de Semur, Sainte-Sabine, 21320, France;47.1921572;4.6247008;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This elegant restaurant in the historical setting of the Renaissance Château Sainte-Sabine stands out on account of its refined cuisine. A simpler set menu is available at lunchtime. The guestrooms invite you to unwind as you take in the lake and bucolic grounds, where deer roam.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15967;Bro's;France;Blois;36 rue de la Foulerie, Blois, 41000, France;47.5873362;1.3370069;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This eatery in the historic town just a stone’s throw from the banks of the Loire, which has quickly been taken by storm by the locals, is the brainchild of two enthusiastic cooks and inseparable pals. The scene upstairs sports a stylish rustic interior with contemporary touches, providing the perfect foil to a bistronomic score that shines the spotlight on locally sourced, seasonal ingredients, naturally washed down with Loire wines. Tapas inspired by the produce of south-west France and Spain are also available (evenings only and without reservations) in the ground-floor room.;Terrace;[]
15968;Quelque Part;France;Paris;1 rue Ambroise-Thomas, Paris, 75009, France;48.8741211;2.3472572;27;true;true;Creative;This “somewhere” is the submarine wonderland of Top Chef contestant Florian Barbarot. Like Captain Nemo, he invites diners to explore his subtly creative cuisine in which seafood, seasonal veggies and scrupulously sourced ingredients are inspiringly assembled. Each menu features a different number of courses for an “abyssal immersion”.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
15969;Le Bel Ami;France;Etretat;25/27 rue Alphonse-Karr, Etretat, 76790, France;49.7071347;0.2032221;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A few hundred metres from the seafront, amid the crêperies and other taverns, don't hesitate to bag a table at this charming, colourful place run by the proprietor of Le Donjon – Domaine Saint-Clair, a Michelin-starred restaurant in the upper town. Here, you can enjoy Mediterranean-inspired cuisine, starting with mezze (hummus/beef tataki, bottarga/kefta, aubergine or even ceviche with citrus fruit and fennel), before tucking into a superb piece of meagre, served with a vegetable tian and rosemary hollandaise. There is also a (small) wine cellar where you can purchase a bottle to enjoy here or take away.;Wheelchair access;[]
15970;Café Brunet;France;Annecy;18 place Gabriel-Fauré - à Annecy-le-Vieux, Annecy, 74940, France;45.9193499;6.1423377;17;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This café dating back to 1875 is a real haven. It has managed to keep intact its soul of an authentic and convivial bistro (terrace, boules). As time meanders by, enjoy a good hearty meal or tasty little dishes.;Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15972;Loiseau du Temps;France;Besançon;27 rue des Boucheries, Besançon, 25000, France;47.2403637;6.0221827;19;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set in a former 18C grain store, this handsome dining room, with vaulted ceiling and contemporary details, is home to the Besançon outpost of the Bernard Loiseau Group. The menu focuses on produce and recipes from Bourgogne-Franche-Comté: hotpot of snails with cancoillotte and Morteau sausage, chicken fricassée Gaston Gérard style, Côte d’Or pork chop with Jura tomme gratin… Enticing dessert trolley and a decent selection of wines, particularly by the glass.;Wheelchair access;[]
15973;L'Auberge de Guillaume;France;Vandenesse-en-Auxois;4 place de la Mairie, Vandenesse-en-Auxois, 21320, France;47.2207822;4.6156135;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;After assisting Christophe Bacquié at Le Castellet, becoming a Meilleur Ouvrier de France in 2015 and then a Michelin-starred chef at La Bussière, local lad, Guillaume Royer, has at last opened his own place in his native village. In this charming inn, half a kilometre from the peaceful Canal de Bourgogne, he rolls out his talent in a contemporary bistronomic vein using knockout regional produce. Pleasant terrace and quiet garden to the rear.;Car park,Terrace;[]
15974;Otto;France;Paris;5 rue Mouffetard, Paris, 75005, France;48.8448803;2.3492193;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A welcome addition to the rue Mouffetard: this bistro with a minimalist decor comprising concrete floor and ceiling is modelled on the Japanese izakaya. Under the leadership of chef Eric Trochon, Otto proposes a cuisine for sharing based on a short menu that revolves around the produce, simply accompanied by a condiment or a sauce for that extra kick. Hence chimichurri, sauce vierge or diable, ponzu sauce or lemon condiment are served alongside meat and fish, often cooked over binchotan coals. Please note that they don't take bookings.;Air conditioning;[]
15975;Regain;France;Marseille;53 rue Saint-Pierre, Marseille, 13005, France;43.2931457;5.389379;28;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the trendy Le Camas neighbourhood, this friendly bistro is in the competent hands of experienced chef Sarah Chougnet-Strudel and sommelier Lucien Salomon, who deploys his flair and talent front of house. Whether seated at the traditional chestnut wood and zinc counter or in the leafy courtyard, which is open in fine weather, you'll love the flavoursome market-fresh cuisine, which highlights local produce, particularly vegetables and artisanal fish. Think rack of pork with kale, sorrel cream, lentils and limequat, or a delicious tartlet with maple syrup, coffee mousse and candied celery. To accompany your food, pick a bottle from the enticing selection of around 200 "living" wines. An energising harvest of flavours!;Terrace;[]
15976;VIVE, Maison Mer;France;Paris;62 avenue des Ternes, Paris, 75017, France;48.8792868;2.2916117;60;true;true;Seafood;Alsace-born restaurateur Adrien Rech opened this institution dedicated to seafood in 1925. After Ducasse, it is now the turn of David and Stéphanie Le Quellec, whose Breton name alone smacks of the ocean, to celebrate fish and shellfish cuisine. The decor is sumptuous, with its huge bar, dining area on the first floor and long banquette seating. David Le Quellec serves food that is good for sharing and made with excellent, ultra-fresh ingredients from fish markets spanning France, from the Atlantic to the Mediterranean. The ceviche of sea bream with coconut milk, lime and coriander is already a house classic – not to mention the dishes prepared from fish matured on site in the maturing cellar.;Air conditioning;[]
15978;Auberge de la Haute-Joux;France;Bonnevaux;2 rue du Jura, Bonnevaux, 25560, France;46.8084241;6.1840742;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;A former philosopher (and the epitome of courtesy and discernment when it comes to her wine recommendations) plus a globetrotting chef who grew up eating at Michelin-starred restaurants have taken over this family-run inn: just the ticket in the middle of this rural village. This pair promises diners a delightful dining experience that combines rustic surroundings and cuisine that nonchalantly switches between regional and more contemporary dishes, and is littered with nods to the chef's many travels: here you see vin jaune and saffron from Franche-Comté, peanut vinaigrette, seaweed emulsion alongside Thai-style mussels from Bouchot.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15979;Maison Bagarre;France;Nantes;6 rue Jean-Jacques Rousseau, Nantes, 44000, France;47.21244;-1.5601918;33;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant in the Graslin neighbourhood is often booked up, so it's best to reserve. The chef makes the most of the extensive network of producers (especially market gardeners) operating in Nantes to create an appealing bistronomy menu. The rather original contemporary setting (over two levels) is very attractive, especially the dining area on the large mezzanine overlooking the open kitchen.;;[]
15980;Cueillette;France;Cesson-Sévigné;54 route de Fougères, Cesson-Sévigné, 35510, France;48.1440268;-1.6099308;34;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A small establishment tucked away in the suburbs of Rennes, an attractive façade, a contemporary interior, a covered terrace overlooking the fields, and a charming welcome. As for the food, the chef has got it spot on: competent, pared-back dishes that are full of finesse, with judicious combinations and precise seasoning. Rich pickings at this lovely place outside of the centre.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15981;Brut maison de cuisine;France;Blois;14 quai Villebois-Mareuil, Blois, 41000, France;47.58348;1.33848;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This tasty bistro with a contemporary feel has an open kitchen, shelves filled with jars of fermented vegetables and books… and just a handful of tables, so it's best to book. The chef, who has a solid track record, devises a short menu that changes regularly. The three pillars of his cooking are seasonality, local ingredients (such as Racan poultry) and modern, often bold cuisine, for example his dessert that combines a naturally sweet Jerusalem artichoke cream and a coffee ice cream with a pronounced flavour. Short list of natural and organic wines.;Air conditioning;[]
15984;Ilô;France;Paris;6 rue Castex, Paris, 75004, France;48.8526313;2.3662485;100;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A marriage between a French gourmet bistro and a Japanese tavern is hidden behind a noren (a vertical fabric divider hung across the doorways of shops in Japan). Ilô is also the lair of a particularly inspired duet, both of whom worked at the star-rated Sola. On one side, Yuki Onuma supervises the service, suggesting perceptive, spot-on wine/saké-food pairings, while on the other, chef Seiya Kumabe conjures up a culinary patchwork of Gallic bistronomy with a smattering of Japanese allusions.;;[]
15985;Bulle;France;Lyon;9 place de Fourvière, Lyon, 69005, France;45.761892;4.8227205;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Guy Lassausaie masterminded the stylish top to toe refurbishment of this restaurant in a former Jesuit seminary (1853). You enter through a bar which boasts a jaw-dropping panoramic terrace, before heading downstairs into the restaurant, passing by the building’s Gallo-Roman foundations on the way! A swish, historic interior (crystal lighting, parquet floors and a view of the kitchen) sets the scene for colourful seasonal food, such as brook trout, fennel and seasonal mushrooms…;Air conditioning,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
15986;Apicius;France;Montbrison;29 rue Martin-Bernard, Montbrison, 42600, France;45.6079569;4.0651818;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This dinky city-centre eatery is run by a young couple with an enviable track record. In a recently refurbished chic trendy interior, you will sample market-fresh cuisine at unbeatable prices at lunchtime and a more elaborate menu on Friday evenings. The chef makes the most of local ingredients as well as wildflowers and plants. The epitome of generous!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15987;Auberge de l'Abbaye;France;Thiron-Gardais;15 rue du Commerce, Thiron-Gardais, 28480, France;48.31156;0.99234;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Treat yourself to a meal in the country, in the professional hands of this couple who have set up shop in a pretty stone house overlooking the abbey and Royal College of Thiron - Gardais. Seasonal dishes and a new subtle version of classical recipes. Flawlessly prepared with distinctive flavours. Lovely!;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
15988;Miro;France;Ostwald;Rue de la Nachtweid, Ostwald, 67540, France;48.5419158;7.7236234;78;true;true;Fusion;This restaurant stands in bucolic grounds on the banks of the River Ill. Familiar with South American, Japanese and French gastronomy, the chef regales diners with tasty and uninhibited cuisine inspired by his many travels, for example Thai-style sea bass ceviche and his superb Argentinian beef entrecote finished over burning embers. The lunch set menu is a steal.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15989;Itsasoa;France;Carnac;1 rue Ker Anna, Carnac, 56340, France;47.5827662;-3.0784671;27;true;false;Creative, Farm to table;The Basque overtones of this Brittany eatery are due to Erwann Le Pogam, a Breton who grew up in Southwest France and who worked in the film industry before turning to cooking. A great decision! This unfettered and unblinkered man has a single goal: fine, fresh, wholesome food that respects the produce, the producer and the customer. A few examples from the set menus (which change frequently in line with the seasons): monkfish tail, tempura of courgette flowers and smoked paprika emulsion or farm-reared pork with a mousseline of green peas and xipister Basque sauce.;;[]
15990;Les 5 Bouchons;France;Montauban;24 place Nationale, Montauban, 82000, France;44.0175165;1.3540203;30;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A pleasant restaurant for lunch beneath the arcades of Place Nationale, Montauban's architectural pride and joy. The name refers to the five members of the family of experienced chef David Soulier, who works with his wife Joan front of house. Every fortnight, a new seasonal menu showcases well-sourced local ingredients in straightforward, colourful and tasty dishes, for example roasted hazelnuts grown in Tarn-et-Garonne that accompany the beetroot hummus, or the sticks of celeriac and mustard seed pickles served with the pork loin cooked for five hours. Whether seated on the terrace or in the long room with its vaulted ceiling overlooking the kitchen, you'll have an enjoyable meal without breaking the bank.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15991;Gemellus;France;Paris;37 avenue Duquesne, Paris, 75007, France;48.8516862;2.31021;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This spruce, modern eatery done up in oatmeal shades features a square dining room with painted mouldings, a coffered ceiling, an imposing chandelier and upholstered velvet seats. Chef Maxime Le Meur, who trained with some of the greats, leaves nothing to chance as he crafts cuisine inspired as much by seasonal ingredients as by his Breton (check out the surf ‘n turf dish of Breton squab with lobster) and Grenoble roots (Chartreuse liqueur is never far from the culinary score). A festival of forthright, meticulous flavours overflowing in creative ideas. Affordable lunchtime menu.;Air conditioning;[]
15992;Auberge d’Aillon et d’Ailleurs;France;Aillon-le-Jeune;795 route de la Correrie, Aillon-le-Jeune, 73340, France;45.6101384;6.1094681;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the Bauges Mountains, an unspoilt natural haven, this contemporary hotel has a lovely restaurant run by a young chef who has both technique and ideas. He throws himself into his work to get the best out of the Val d'Aillon terroir: vegetable garden, cooperative cheese, farm lamb, wild herbs... The menu changes regularly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
15993;La Bòria;France;Veyras;105 avenue du Ruissol, Veyras, 07000, France;44.7292683;4.5651805;68;true;true;Creative;The view over the valley and the surrounding Ardèche hillsides, a beautiful timber structure, chestnut wood tables, an indoor aromatic herb garden and the etymology of the name bòria ("small Cévennes farm" in Ardèche dialect) - the stage is set! Assisted by a high-flying team whose wholehearted commitment to the house ethos is beyond doubt, chef Florian Descours pays tribute to his rural roots with fresh, local produce: beef from Privas, pork from Beaulieu, snails from the Eyrieux valley and trout from Labatie-d'Andaure). A treat from beginning to end, from the grilled baby gem lettuce and Villevocance pigeon with watermelon and sorel to the millefeuille of garden fruit and a delicate verbena-flavoured cream, without forgetting the fantastic cheese board. Hard to beat!;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
15994;La Récréation Gourmande;France;Villegenon;3 rue de l'Ancienne-École, Villegenon, 18260, France;47.4272632;2.6058455;100;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;In this former schoolhouse, an old stove presides, with a dunce's hat perched on top! Whatever the standard of the class, everyone can tuck into the generous and tasty cooking, which makes the ingredients the star of the class. A Récréation Gourmande indeed!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
15995;Chenapan;France;Paris;28 rue Louise-Émilie-de-la-Tour-d'Auvergne, Paris, 75009, France;48.8792669;2.3433338;37;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The pair at the helm of this compact restaurant in Pigalle are chef Bruno Laporte and front-of-house manager and sommelier Florentin Fraillon, who have both graduated with honours from Ze Kitchen Galerie, William Ledeuil's "training ground"! Here, they are going from strength to strength, with dishes such as the plant-based starter (butter beans, fava beans, peas, leaves and fresh herbs) – given a boost by its rhubarb juice sauce spiced up with chilli in the style of a beurre blanc – or the delicious wheat dessert, oozing childhood nostalgia. An intimate, contemporary bistro setting with an open kitchen and pleasant service with a smile.;Air conditioning;[]
15997;Em Sherif;France;Monaco;Hôtel de Paris, place du Casino, Monaco, 98000, France;43.7389575;7.4275873;90;false;false;Lebanese;A welcome opportunity to celebrate the pleasures of Lebanese cuisine, the Mediterranean and, of course, the philosophy of sharing. In the kitchen, chef Yasmina Hayek (who has worked at the Institut Paul Bocuse and the restaurants of Mathieu Pacaud, Jean-François Piège and Rasmus Kofoed at Geranium in Copenhagen) skilfully juggles the traditional and the modern, in dishes such as her excellent lentil salad (addas) or her delicious aubergine fatteh with yoghurt. Aromas, colours, flavours – a culinary voyage of the senses out on the panoramic terrace or in a chic bistro-style dining area on the ground floor of the Hôtel de Paris.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16001;Epicentre;France;Bordeaux;15 rue des Piliers-de-Tutelle, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8413379;-0.5736719;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This eatery is located in a side street off the busy Rue Sainte Catherine. From his tiny kitchen at the rear of the dining room, which enables him to chat with customers, chef Benjamin Wavrant whips up a bargain-priced bistronomic lunchtime menu with a patriotic line-up of dishes, like potato soup followed by a slab of pollock seared in butter, flavoured in citrus fruit and underscored by a gutsy meaty gravy. More upmarket in the evening, premium ingredients such as foie gras, scallops and pigeon are crafted into a more gastro-leaning menu.;;[]
16002;La Table du Grand Large;France;Dolus-d'Oléron;2 avenue de l'Océan, Dolus-d'Oléron, 17550, France;45.894659;-1.2856493;69;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Just a stone's throw from Rémigeasse beach, amidst dunes and unspoilt countryside, Le Grand Large Hotel overlooks the ocean below. The restaurant faces both the indoor swimming pool and the sea, which is perfect for sunset portraits in the evenings. The menu by David Boyer (Meilleur Ouvrier de France) exalts the region’s first-rate produce. The crab with roasted rice and glazed lovage, or the two-course Racan pigeon with a raspberry reduction, bear witness to the chef’s meticulous handiwork.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
16004;L’Oyat;France;Paris;11 rue Notre-Dame-de-Nazareth, Paris, 75003, France;48.8669937;2.3611118;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Even in Paris, near the Place de la République, a Ch'ti chef from Dunkirk like Jérémy Sergeant continues to hark back to the beaches of his native region: marram grass – oyat – is a small plant capable of holding in place the sand of the dunes. In the kitchen, he brings to bear all his experience: the produce is fresh, the style modern and light, the jus tasty and the whole thing smacks of sincerity. In the evening, the menu is subtly embellished with premium ingredients. Cosy, contemporary atmosphere.;;[]
16005;Le Noyo;France;Auxerre;26 rue du 24-Août, Auxerre, 89000, France;47.7908578;3.5660891;90;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A few minutes’ walk from the covered market, this dinky eatery, refurbished in a tasteful modern vibe, is the brainchild of François Liebaert, a well-known local chef. His enticing seasonal menu is occasionally jazzed up with creative notes, such as line-caught hake served with a gutsy Spanish sauce, flanked by spot-on balanced seasonings and artistic plating. Estelle efficiently and cheerfully manages the front of house.;Air conditioning;[]
16006;Au Soleil;France;Soultz-sous-Forêts;34 rue des Barons-de-Fleckenstein, Soultz-sous-Forêts, 67250, France;48.9382294;7.8816728;27;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in the heart of a picturesque Alsace village, this establishment is the epitome of sunny, like its gregarious chef, Anthony Schauer, who trained in top houses in northern Alsace. He and his wife cheerfully welcome you to their tasteful, contemporary restaurant, which provides the perfect foil to fresh, gutsy, seasonal fare with a bistronomic slant, such as marbled parsley ham served with a tangy ravigote sauce or confit of pollock, tomatoes, basil and fennel.;Air conditioning;[]
16009;POPS;France;Pornichet;96 avenue du Général-de-Gaulle, Pornichet, 44380, France;47.2660641;-2.3408214;86;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Pops is the nest of two fledglings who have flown the snug Mare aux Oiseaux, a recognised talent hatcher helmed by Éric Guérin. In their eatery just off the seafront, Corentin Leverger and Océane Maisonneuve bend over backwards to regale diners with fresh premium, often organic produce such as girolles mushrooms or red mullet. Their creative bistronomic score rolls out a festival of textures and forthright flavours illustrated by a scrumptious tartlet of mushrooms, prepared in several ways (raw, cooked, in jelly, creamed and pickled).;Air conditioning;[]
16010;Le Quai;France;Tournus;20 quai de Verdun, Tournus, 71700, France;46.563122;4.9125615;80;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;On the banks of the Saône, this quayside brasserie boasts a very pleasant terrace right beside the river. In charge of proceedings is chef Valéry Meulien, who was trained by Jean Ducloux and Paul Bocuse, and later earned a Michelin star himself. His dishes focus on the region's classics, including pâté croûte, ham terrine with parsley, calf's head, and sweetbreads with morel cream. The flavoursome red wine sauce sprinkled with chopped parsley that accompanies the œufs en meurette is proof that the chef has by no means lost his touch.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16012;Alivetu;France;Marseille;145 rue Sainte, Marseille, 13007, France;43.2907769;5.3670981;85;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This little "olive grove" (alivetu in Corsican) is an oasis for foodies in the Saint Victor neighbourhood, abutting the Colline de la Garde. The restaurant is split into a dining area with a polished concrete floor and a mezzanine, where diners tuck into the chef's Mediterranean cuisine: think grilled octopus, sweet potato purée, corn and pepper sauce. A "Market Menu" on the board at lunchtime and a surprise set menu in the evening.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16013;Sublime;France;Dijon;24 rue Bannelier, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3244686;5.0386462;97;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A stone’s throw from the covered market, the modern cuisine of Sicilian chef Giovanni Spataro encompasses carefully executed French dishes such as turbot, asparagus, aioli and lemongrass emulsion, and emblematic Italian specialities including his take on vitello tonnato. He sources excellent ingredients – Charolais beef, carnaroli rice, Sicilian prawns etc, which he prepares and presents with impeccable taste.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16017;Thiou;France;Paris;Hôtel Norman, 9 rue Balzac, Paris, 75008, France;48.8736808;2.300417;59;false;true;Thai;Chef Apiradee Thirakomen, who goes by "Thiou", has set up shop on the Right Bank, in a small hotel just off the Champs Élysées. In a chic, intimate atmosphere, you can sample the Thai specialities that have made her reputation. Some have a French twist: prawn ravioli with coconut cream flavoured with lemongrass, pad thai, "Crying Tiger".;Air conditioning;[]
16019;Circle;France;Lyon;11 rue Chavanne, Lyon, 69001, France;45.7648991;4.8324022;41;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The name of this restaurant pays homage to American rapper Mac Miller, as well as to the circle of friends and co-workers running the show here! Chef Bastian Ruga has perfected his concept. Playing out to a soundtrack of American rap music, his youthful, no-holds-barred cuisine charts a course between bold creativity, North African and Asian influences, and a healthy dose of affection for traditional cuisine – this is Lyon, after all! The original food-and-drink pairings are an integral part of the experience, encompassing beer, herbal teas and a natural wine list. A shining example would be the wonderfully pearlescent cod with black garlic hollandaise sauce, served with a comforting ginger brandade. The style of service is professional and trendy.;Air conditioning;[]
16021;Osteria Matto;France;Lyon;23 rue de Sèze, Lyon, 69006, France;45.7681645;4.8455216;28;false;false;Italian;Chef Thomas Asti has Italian blood running through his veins. So, it made sense when he and his partner opened this bistro-styled trattoria. The duo draws on Italy’s glorious culinary heritage to the delight of their loyal regulars, who flock here to sample vitello tonnato, bagna cauda, veal with house-made potato gnocchi – and Sicilian lemon tart, just the way nonna used to make it. To be washed down with premium Italian wines. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16023;Auberge du Prieuré Normand;France;Gasny;1 place de la République, Gasny, 27620, France;49.0892144;1.6068482;81;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Near Giverny, the main square of Gasny is home to this full-blown Normandy-style, half-timbered family-run inn. The chef favours local produce in his inspired cooking, steeped in gutsy sauces and forthright flavours. His signature dish, risotto of langoustines, is to die for! The interior boasts a bar, a cellar, two contemporary dining rooms and a patio come fine weather.;Terrace;[]
16024;Maison Léa;France;Lyon;11 quai des Célestins, Lyon, 69002, France;45.7596843;4.8302253;86;true;true;Lyonnaise;A new start for La Mère Léa, a true local institution, which has expanded on a quayside location and now enjoys more space and a beautiful view of the Fourvière and St-Jean quarters. Lyon specialities still feature prominently, with two good value-for-money set menus and a well-crafted à la carte menu.;Air conditioning;[]
16026;Ma Table en Ville;France;Mâcon;50 rue de Strasbourg, Mâcon, 71000, France;46.307847;4.8360062;58;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This is perhaps the archetypal 21C bistro, with its colourful contemporary interior, naked light bulbs and exposed pipes… The chef, who expertly prepares traditional cuisine, is also to be seen in the dining area. He is committed to quality ingredients – a favourite of ours is the cauliflower soup with cashews and poached egg! Good choice of regional wines, and service with a smile.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16027;L'Instant du Sud;France;Générac;39 Grand-Rue, Générac, 30510, France;43.7292304;4.3489416;100;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A pretty stone house in the heart of a village near the Camargue Nature Reserve is the haunt of an endearing couple. Whether it is on the patio beneath a canopy of reeds or in the small cosy dining room, the vibe is welcoming and professional. The chef wins us over with a concise, contemporary score at eater-friendly prices and a generous hand when it comes to filling the plates. He has a clear fondness for sweet-sour Thai marinades and barbecue sauces. The almond-flavoured pannacotta adds a refreshing light flourish to the end of the meal.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16028;Le 1720 - Château de Sully;France;Bayeux;Route de Port-en-Bessin, Bayeux, 14400, France;49.2993518;-0.7316203;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Grandiose is the term that springs to mind when describing this 18C château, set in landscaped grounds planted with Lebanese cedars and sequoias. Take a seat in one of the plush dining rooms or in the bright conservatory to savour the chef’s predominantly Normandy-focused cuisine: vegetables, cheeses, foie gras and, of course, line-caught fish.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16029;L'Océan;France;Le Croisic;Port-Lin, Le Croisic, 44490, France;47.2843425;-2.5139452;61;false;true;Seafood;Founded in 1981 by Louis and Yolande André, who are now assisted by their daughter Dominique and son-in-law Gérard Samson, L’Océan is a treat for the eye and the palate thanks to the huge conservatory and a menu that stars supremely fresh first-class seafood and fish. The establishment’s timeless signature dishes never fail to deliver: seafood platters, scallops in season, sole meunière or whole seabass in a salt crust (to be shared). We also recommend the big-boned lobster bisque, rich in whole pieces of perfectly cooked lobster and deliciously crunchy croutons. Finish with a wickedly tempting rum and raisin baba – the epitome of comforting nostalgia as you watch the sun set over the waves.;Air conditioning,Great view,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16030;Maison Burgarella;France;Espalion;3 place Saint-Georges, Espalion, 12500, France;44.5206765;2.7620032;47;false;false;Creative;Between Causses and Aubrac, the Burgarella family ushers you into this tastefully refurbished house. Downstairs, the Table de Romane brasserie celebrates hearty regional fare (calf’s head, tripoux (sheep tripe), while upstairs the swanky gourmet La Tour establishment allows the creative chef, visible from the open kitchen, to give free rein to his inspiration without losing sight of his Aveyron roots. A delicious gourmet halt on the banks of the Lot River under the aegis of Château de Calmont.;Air conditioning;[]
16032;Belle de Mars;France;Marseille;56 rue de Forbin, Marseille, 13002, France;43.3048592;5.367658;73;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Behind wrought-iron railings, this handsome establishment ushers diners into a tastefully understated interior (white walls, parquet floors, wooden chairs and tables) and an open-plan kitchen helmed by Michel Marini and Kim-Mai Bui. This veteran duet (formerly of William Ledeuil, Christophe Moret, Gérald Passedat…) crafts a flavoursome, legible, delicate score with a Mediterranean spin and invariably dotted with herbs they pick themselves. Everything is steeped in crisp, expressive flavours, examples of which include lightly seared squid with a salmorejo sauce or wild seabass in fig leaves. The desserts are low on sugar yet highly addictive!;Air conditioning;[]
16040;Vaisseau;France;Paris;35 rue Faidherbe, Paris, 75011, France;48.8532272;2.3827958;30;true;false;Creative;Chef Adrien Cachot has been a familiar face since appearing on French TV's Top Chef in 2020. In a space with a minimalist decor and intimate atmosphere, the chef puts his creativity to the test, creating dishes that often feature unexpected pairings, such as the show-stopping "Cachot e pepe" mochi, prepared in the manner of a pepper and citrus risotto! He also has a penchant for less conventional ingredients, such as offal, which contribute unusual textures. Finally, another characteristic of his cuisine is the marriage of surf and turf, with dishes such as his superb black ruff, a fish from the Mediterranean seabed, judiciously combined with tripe and vin jaune. Over the course of a carte blanche menu that is unapologetically playful, a singular culinary personality emerges, shaking things up and winning diners over from start to finish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16041;Koji;France;Issy-les-Moulineaux;34 bis rue Ernest-Renan, Issy-les-Moulineaux, 92130, France;48.82841;2.28158;26;true;true;Teppanyaki;Japanese teppanyaki cooking is nothing short of theatrical with its spectacular flames, so be sure to bag a front-row seat at the counter. Before your eyes, chef Koji Hashimoto carefully prepares premium ingredients. His elegant brand of craftsmanship, honed by years of experience in prestigious kitchens, never overwhelms the produce with culinary gimmicks. Both fish and meat (a Normandy beef fillet, for example) are cooked just right, and enhanced by impeccable sauces (eg white miso and sherry vinegar sauce on an assortment of grilled fish). Traditional Japanese decor dominated by wood.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
16042;L'Unisens;France;Vagnas;250 route de Barjac, Vagnas, 07150, France;44.3441386;4.363725;38;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This modern building just outside the village of Vagnas harks back to traditional Provençal architecture. In its spacious interior, which is done out in a contemporary style and has an open kitchen, sample the cuisine of Tarik Mezri-Charmasson, who ticks all the boxes, remaining true to the seasons and letting the ingredients speak for themselves.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16044;TLALI;France;Bordeaux;6 rue du Cancera, Bordeaux, 33000, France;44.8395499;-0.5709126;89;true;false;Fusion, Mexican;This Franco-Mexican establishment run by a native of Guadalajara, chef Kristian de Anda who was at the helm of the kitchen of the Parisian Biondi, is a delightful surprise. Only open in the evenings, his establishment masterfully proves that there is more to Mexican cuisine than tacos and enchiladas! In fact, the score is more fusion as pedigree Gallic recipes are dotted with intelligent Mexican notes – you won’t find a single tastebud-burning pepper in sight! We do however recommend ordering his array of tacos, in tribute to different regions of Mexico, as the ideal appetiser to kick off your meal in style.;Air conditioning;[]
16045;Comptoir du Lac;France;Duingt;410 allée de la Plage, Duingt, 74410, France;45.8289297;6.191389;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant looks like a modern industrial greenhouse and is surrounded by greenery, the mountains and a lake. A really lovely place that serves up dishes that are equally appealing!;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16046;Auberge Bienvenue;France;Doué-la-Fontaine;104 rue de Cholet, Doué-la-Fontaine, 49700, France;47.1914369;-0.2970574;88;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This place may have celebrated its 30th birthday but it shows no sign of tiring. Comfortably ensconced beneath the beams and arcades of the large dining area, you have to admit that at times nothing beats tradition, especially when it comes to cooking.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16047;Au Vieux Porche;France;Eguisheim;16 rue des Trois-Châteaux, Eguisheim, 68420, France;48.042399;7.3037807;53;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This typical residence (1707) stands in the winegrowing estate of the manager's family. His partner cooks classic regional dishes, but he is also a winemaker. So it goes without saying that you can enjoy some fine vintages here too.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16048;La Verdoyante;France;Gassin;866 chemin vicinal Coste-Brigade, Gassin, 83580, France;43.2396948;6.5901868;35;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Standing among the vines, this former rustic farmhouse enjoys a fine panoramic view... But La Verdoyante would be nothing without the enthusiasm of the couple who hold the reins. In the stylish interior or on the charming terrace, diners savour delicious Provençal cuisine that smacks of the garigue.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16049;Le Chalet;France;Gresse-en-Vercors;Le village, Gresse-en-Vercors, 38650, France;44.9023427;5.5681005;72;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A fortified house during the Middle Ages, and a monastery until 1905, this "chalet" is now a hotel and restaurant run by the Prayer family. The tasty dishes, such as house - smoked salmon or seven - hour leg of lamb with gratin du Vercors, attest to the two primordial values of the establishment: tradition and generosity.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16051;Le Carillon;France;Goult;10 avenue du Luberon (place de la Libération), Goult, 84220, France;43.86303;5.243239;40;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Facing the church on Goult's main square, this restaurant offers excellent Provençal-inspired cuisine with the odd contemporary twist. Tables are set up in a small dining area with modern decor and out on the terrace, where you can soak up the village atmosphere. A charming welcome and a well-devised wine list that pays particular attention to organic options. A lovely spot.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16052;Les Jardins Sauvages - La Grée des Landes;France;La Gacilly;Cournon, La Gacilly, 56200, France;47.7604449;-2.1227339;72;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the restaurant of the Yves Rocher hotel, you can expect modern, healthy, niftily crafted, flavoursome food, made primarily out of organic produce from the garden and local growers in keeping with the eatery’s sustainable ethos. Bathed in light, the glazed dining room stretches out between the rows of veg in the cottage garden on one side and a conservatory that leads into the garden on the other, maintaining an organic link with nature as befits the establishment’s mindset.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16053;L'Un des Sens;France;Dijon;3 rue Jeannin, Dijon, 21000, France;47.3224482;5.0429223;57;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Near the antique dealers’ district, this restaurant serves scrumptious food, presented beautifully and rich in distinctive flavours, illustrated by a rack of Ségala veal, ravioles of green peas and pecorino cheese and spring onions. The vegetables and fruit come from the chef’s garden. Several-course surprise menu in the evening and simpler fare at lunchtime. Courtyard patio for alfresco dining.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16054;Les Santons;France;Grimaud;743 route Nationale, Grimaud, 83310, France;43.272547;6.5221217;97;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This lovely Provençal inn is full of character, with its exposed beams, flower arrangements and, of course, its collection of figurines (santons in French). The menu never gets boring, alternating between classic cuisine and contemporary dishes, such as rack of lamb with crispy new garlic, garnished with a millefeuille of candied peppers and chard. The traditional aged-rum baba with vanilla whipped cream deserves a special mention.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16055;Le Pavillon Gourmand;France;Eguisheim;101 rue du Rempart-Sud, Eguisheim, 68420, France;48.0430032;7.3045363;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Alsatian;This village house (1683) offers a setting bathed in light, tastefully combining the historical character of the building with more contemporary touches. Tuck into cuisine that includes Alsace recipes (onion tart, sauerkraut, wild boar stew) and more modern dishes. Wines from the Eguisheim vineyard are well represented, and the small terrace is popular in summer.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16056;Les Gentianettes;France;La Chapelle-d'Abondance;73 route de Chevenne, La Chapelle-d'Abondance, 74360, France;46.29482;6.78901;35;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A mountain chalet decor with exposed beams, a traditional dining room with a fireplace in the middle and decorated with a collection of bells – it doesn't get much more inviting than this! The kitchen serves both traditional dishes, including beef tenderloin with a morel mushroom sauce, and slightly more modern and creative recipes such as carpaccio of sea bass with passion fruit. For Savoyard specialties, guests can head to La Baratte, the restaurant's ground-floor eatery, to tuck into authentic cuisine in a friendly atmosphere.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16057;L'Arbousier;France;Porticcio;D55 - Boulevard Marie-Jeanne Bozzi, Porticcio, 20166, France;41.87779;8.78582;41;false;false;Classic Cuisine;A throwback to another time in this establishment with a slightly old-fashioned atmosphere, where Mediterranean cuisine with Corsican influences is served on the very pleasant terrace facing the sea. Lobster, fish from small-scale local fishermen… and fricassee of lobster with buttered capellini, the house speciality. The wine is served by the glass from magnums, which is a nice touch! More limited menu at lunchtime.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16059;La Bartavelle;France;Argelès-sur-Mer;24 rue de la République, Argelès-sur-Mer, 66700, France;42.5469187;3.0226404;54;false;false;Creative;This place is an open secret among food lovers – and with good reason! Chef Thibaut Lesage and Stéphanie, his pastry chef wife, put an inspired spin on the classics to produce dishes that diners delight in. You will need to book ahead if you want to try it for yourself!;Air conditioning;[]
16060;La Poya;France;Châtel;196 route de Vonnes, Châtel, 74390, France;46.2658929;6.8414093;87;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;In a mountain-inspired decor, the chef serves up good-quality traditional cuisine that often takes meat as its starting point… but does not exclude the odd Asian note (eg gravelax salmon tataki marinated in beetroot, served with mustard sorbet). The dishes are beautifully presented and service comes with a smile. A good place to recharge your batteries after hitting the slopes on your skis!;Terrace;[]
16061;À la 12;France;Delme;6 place de la République, Delme, 57590, France;48.8872259;6.3915604;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This has been the fiefdom of the François family since it was founded in 1954. After a worthwhile experience at the Bras family's Laguiole restaurant, Thomas (in the kitchen) and Laura, his charming partner (on the restaurant floor), have both returned to the fold in Delme. So it's now the third generation at the helm of this contemporary restaurant, which is popular with locals and visiting guests alike. The menu is both indulgent and delicate, oscillating between tradition and modernity, showcasing an appreciation for herbs and spices. Uplifting!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16062;La Gaffe;France;Saint-Florent;Promenade des Quais, Saint-Florent, 20217, France;42.6814847;9.2990122;94;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Yann Le Scavarec, who hails from Morbihan, is at the helm of this restaurant, which boasts an ideal location on the Saint-Florent harbour front. His well-crafted contemporary cooking showcases local produce, eg lamb and veal from Oletta, fish sourced directly from a local fisherman and barbecued crayfish. The grouper, courgette flower with spider crab and Vadouvan spices made an impression! The modern interior is in keeping with the menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16063;MaThy'S;France;Saint-Florent;Place Furnellu, Saint-Florent, 20217, France;42.68091;9.3003135;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Picture a red façade preceded by a delightful patio shaded by a mulberry tree. On a street corner of Saint Florent, this eatery aims for a friendly village restaurant vibe and serves Mediterranean and Corsican cuisine (carpaccio of langoustines, olive oil and dried caviar, tartare of red tuna or grilled squid with chorizo), without forgetting a few more exotic Asian notes (yuzu-flavoured gyoza or crunchy king prawns, nori and wasabi). Simpler lunchtime menu and a highly tempting wine list add the final touch to this inviting portrait.;Terrace;[]
16065;La Table de la Grotte;France;Sartène;Domaine de Murtoli, Vallée de l'Ortolo, Sartène, 20100, France;41.516722;8.9484095;85;false;true;Corsican;Above the Domaine de Murtoli golf course, set deep in the maquis, this restaurant charms diners with its absolutely unique location and its delicious and flavoursome cuisine, which features quality ingredients either from the estate itself or sourced from neighbouring producers. On wooden benches nestled among the rock formations, or on one of the superb little terraces with a splendid view, you dine by romantic candlelight, tucking into typical Corsican dishes that take the form of a single set menu: courgette à la Sartenaise, confit shoulder of lamb... and a tomato sauce with herbs from the maquis that in itself is worth the trip. Booking essential.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16066;Les Orfèvres;France;Amiens;14 rue des Orfèvres, Amiens, 80000, France;49.8958267;2.2991222;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Bang in the middle of town, this restaurant sports a modern, pared-down, workshop interior and a friendly vibe. The menu is no stranger to the classics, albeit with the odd more modern touch. The chef avows a weakness for fish, illustrated by his superlative low-temperature loin of cod, honey-flavoured fermented milk, leeks and celery.;Interesting wine list;[]
16067;Le 59 Restaurant;France;Aix-les-Bains;59 rue du Casino, Aix-les-Bains, 73100, France;45.6899;5.91338;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is a family affair for the Campanellas, with Cédric having taken over from his brother Boris at the reins of this converted grocer's shop. The cuisine demonstrates a sense of precision, and comprises modern, ever-inventive dishes. One of the best spots in town.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16068;La Cigogne;France;Soyaux;5 impasse de la Cabane-Bambou, Soyaux, 16800, France;45.6351734;0.180437;75;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Not far from Angoulême, La Cigogne is located at the foot of old stone quarries – a rather unusual location, to be sure. Elegant contemporary setting, verdant terrace, and fresh cuisine prepared with good local ingredients.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16069;L'Aubergade;France;Dury;78 route Nationale, Dury, 80480, France;49.8473601;2.2720562;24;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef Éric Boutté, a fine connoisseur of local Picardy produce and sometime globetrotter, makes classically inspired cuisine that is in tune with the seasons and made with the best the market has to offer. The elegant dining area has an appealingly restrained decor. Don't leave without tasting the house special of stuffed cabbage: over 20 000 have already been served!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16070;Grand Largue;France;Port-Navalo;1 rue du Phare, Port-Navalo, 56640, France;47.5487127;-2.9171996;58;true;false;Seafood;From the upper floor of this villa, diners enjoy fine views over the gulf of Morbihan and gastronomic seafood cuisine (lobster, sea bass, shellfish). On the ground floor, the P'tit Zeph is a bistro with a distinctly seafaring air.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16071;Tempi Fà;France;Propriano;11 avenue Napoléon-III, Propriano, 20110, France;41.6756732;8.9024482;95;true;true;Country cooking;Welcome to "bygone days" (tempi fà), in this grocer's-cum-bistro run by a passionate man who selects the island's finest ingredients! You enter via the shop, reminiscent of an actual village market (cold cuts, cheeses, myrtle liqueur etc). You'll enjoy tucking into the tender, flavoursome Abbatucci veal chop with a jus flavoured with herbs from the maquis... and a fine wine from the island!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16072;Les Cornettes;France;La Chapelle-d'Abondance;43 route des Frasses, La Chapelle-d'Abondance, 74360, France;46.2954164;6.7843452;33;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, listed in the Michelin Guide since 1933, is a real institution, renowned throughout the Chablais region. On the menu: game pie, lake trout fillet with wild garlic and morels, guinea fowl roasted on the bone. The cold cuts are matured and smoked on site in a typical mountain atmosphere. It's simple, tasty and rustic as can be.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16074;L'Attilio - Château de Noirieux;France;Briollay;Château de Noirieux, 26 route du Moulin, Briollay, 49125, France;47.5757671;-0.4692073;63;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This handsome little 17C château and charming 15C manor house are set in grounds on the banks of the River Loir. The restaurant has an elegant interior refurbished in a contemporary style, in a palette of light tones, and a pleasant terrace overlooking the valley. Italian chef Attilio Marrazzo chooses quality ingredients – including produce grown in his own vegetable garden – for his modern cuisine. His dishes (free-range poultry, fricassee of chanterelles with parsley, Caesar-style salad) show a good command of culinary techniques, and can be washed down with a wine from a list that focuses on regional tipples.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16075;Comte Roger;France;Carcassonne;14 rue Saint-Louis, Carcassonne, 11000, France;43.2064171;2.36334;94;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;This restaurant within the medieval city walls has a sleek contemporary design and tables set up on a lovely airy patio – Comte Roger knows how to welcome guests! Cassoulet (the house speciality) is of course given pride of place, along with seasonal and regional ingredients (asparagus and local lamb, Lauragais lentils, Belpech poultry etc), which are prepared with a keen sense of precision.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16077;Le 1131 - Abbaye de la Bussière;France;La Bussière-sur-Ouche;Route départementale 33, La Bussière-sur-Ouche, 21360, France;47.2157221;4.7241758;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Pouvait-on rêver lieu plus inspirant qu'une abbaye cistercienne du 12e s. ? Sous ces impressionnantes voûtes en croisées d’ogives, le terroir bourguignon est mis à l'honneur de belle manière : escargots, grenouilles, poissons de lac et de rivière, cassis et miel des fleurs du parc... Prolongez votre méditation dans le parc de 7 hectares ou dans l'une des luxueuses chambres. Au déjeuner, cuisine plus simple au Bistrot des Moines.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
16078;Le Shardana;France;Bandol;16 rue de la République, Bandol, 83150, France;43.1361405;5.754168;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Bang in the middle of the seaside resort, this spruce, modern edifice is reminiscent of Sardinia, both in terms of the décor and the succulent seasonal food. The menu, which changes monthly, is liberally strewn with local and Sardinian ingredients. Examples include gently steamed local croaker in a tomato and cognac sauce with crunchy vegetables and black garlic or panettone French toast with roast apples, salted butterscotch and a scoop of stracciatella ice cream. The chef’s radiant wife cheerfully and professionally manages the front of house. Concise wine list of mainly Italian and local vintages.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16079;La Brasserie du Corton;France;Cassis;Avenue du Revestel, Cassis, 13260, France;43.2107934;5.5451032;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The brasserie offshoot of Villa Madie continues to foster simplicity with its market-fresh ingredients and enticing surf and turf combinations. The set menus are different at lunch and dinner, as well as being changed on a weekly basis. Less expensive than at the original restaurant, the dishes here are just as tasty (beef tartare with Tamaris oysters, real Marseille sôcisse with fennel, lemon tart. When the weather is fine, head for the terrace, which commands a knockout view of the pretty bay.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16080;Le Bellevue;France;Cambo-les-Bains;29 rue des Terrasses, Cambo-les-Bains, 64250, France;43.3622613;-1.4016742;94;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The interior is light, and the menu is short. Two reasons to linger in this tastefully decorated restaurant. Traditional cuisine is revisited with enthusiasm and a keen sense of the pleasure of food. Try off - the - bone pig's trotter terrine or, for dessert, the hot soufflé with pear brandy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16081;Maison Demarcq;France;Cambrai;2 rue Saint-Pol, Cambrai, 59400, France;50.1776258;3.2306999;75;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This grand town house close to where the famous Treaty of Cambrai is said to have been signed (1529) has gone down in history for hosting Napoleon. The decor fosters classical elegance, and the food is contemporary and meticulous – a good option in the town renowned for its "Bêtises de Cambrai" sweets. The simpler traditional cuisine served at the brasserie L'Éphémère is an alternative option.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16082;La Sittelle;France;Aizenay;33 rue du Maréchal-Leclerc, Aizenay, 85190, France;46.7384692;-1.6045844;24;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This inviting late-1940’s villa is enjoying a new lease of life thanks to two associates, formerly of Locguénolé chateau. The chef enhances regional produce in recipes with a creative twist, displaying a preference for surf and turf dishes. Welcoming and attentive service.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16085;Notes de Saveurs;France;Aubenas;16 rue Nationale, Aubenas, 07200, France;44.6215931;4.3873103;28;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Sitting in the vaulted room with exposed stones, looking onto the ruins of the former Benedictine convent, you can enjoy food that places the onus on quality ingredients. The dishes are generous, delicious, flavoursome and original. A friendly and pleasant place, opened by a young couple in 2011.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16087;Chez Jules Le Don Juan;France;Antibes;17 rue Thuret, Antibes, 06600, France;43.582328;7.1266388;98;false;true;Provençal, Mediterranean Cuisine;The major appeal of this particular Don Juan is its enthusiastic, hardworking owner-chef, who tirelessly sources produce (vegetables from his family, veal from an Aveyron farm etc). His food is steeped in the flavours of Provence and Nice cuisine: house specialties are pissaladière, petits farcis niçois, gnocchi à la daube and aioli. The restaurant is part of a convivial little hub for gourmets, complete with café, grocery shop and bistro. Atmosphere guaranteed.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16088;L'Assierois;France;Assier;10 route Galiot-de-Genouillac, Assier, 46320, France;44.67536;1.87682;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the village centre, opposite the church, this former inn with a pleasant shady terrace now presents a sleek contemporary interior. The chef proposes fairly simple seasonal cooking on weekday lunchtimes, and much more ambitious dishes in the evening and at weekends, but he always takes care to maximise local ingredients.;Terrace;[]
16090;Château de Salettes;France;Cahuzac-sur-Vère;Château de Salettes, Cahuzac-sur-Vère, 81140, France;43.9627128;1.922778;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant enjoys a prime location: a 13C château in the heart of a Gaillac wine estate. The food, very much in tune with the zeitgeist, is based on fine ingredients and the attractive wine list proposes Château de Salettes wines. On fine days, the terrace oozes with charm, as do the contemporary-furnished guestrooms and suites established in the edifice’s historic towers and the surrounding wall.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16091;Ryoko - Comptoir à ramen;France;Vannes;14 rue de la Fontaine, Vannes, 56000, France;47.660074;-2.7544939;100;false;true;Ramen;The flavoursome codes of Japanese cuisine are now part and parcel of French dining habits. This pocket handkerchief bistro embodies this trend, depicted by a red, white and black façade. You will taste one of the best ramens in town, based on pork (tonkotsu) or chicken (Tori chintan) broth – it’s your choice! Made with first-class local ingredients (pigs fed on flax seed), each dish is a masterpiece of Japanese tradition. A word of warning: they don’t accept bookings and the place is often packed to the seams!;;[]
16092;Hyacinthe;France;Amiens;11 rue Dusevel, Amiens, 80000, France;49.894523;2.2998759;94;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Previously active in the humanitarian sector, this chef found a new calling while being trained by mentors such as Cyril Lignac and Hélène Darroze. Remaining true to his ethos here in his vintage restaurant, he is mindful of the relationship between his cooking, nature and people, sourcing vegetables from the Hortillonnages (cultivated islets in Amiens), saltmarsh lamb from the Baie de Somme estuary, line-caught fish from the Côte d'Opale etc. Filet mignon pie, vegetable pickles or monkfish, tomato, aubergine and sea herbs: his – at times creative – dishes draw on various preparation techniques, good ingredients and flavours.;Terrace;[]
16093;Jeu de Quilles;France;Cajarc;7 boulevard du Tour-de-Ville, Cajarc, 46160, France;44.4861684;1.8435784;71;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Iced courgette velouté with mint and burrata, or grilled Aubrac beef with smoked pepper: the chef of this tiny bistro proposes simple and appetising market-based cuisine. The very reasonably priced dishes are listed on the blackboard. Don't miss the pleasant terrace under the arbour.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16094;Prélude;France;Saint-Vit;5 place Simone-Veil, Saint-Vit, 25410, France;47.1817176;5.8099537;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Far more than a prelude, this is a full-blown symphony! Now established in a spruce traditional building, Élodie Ouchelli and Thibault Étienne practiced their scales in top star restaurants, among which that of Romuald Fassenet. The virtuoso chef, whose talent is a masterclass in culinary subtlety, composes harmonious dishes in which first-class local produce plays the leading role. Several tables of the contemporary dining room provide a view of the chef at work in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16096;Onaka;France;Nice;12 passage Masséna, Nice, 06000, France;43.69824;7.26752;73;false;true;Sushi, Japanese;Tucked away in a cul-de-sac, this sushi bar is invariably packed to the seams (booking highly recommended). The chef at the helm, sushi champion of France, trained in several of chef Nobu Matsuhisa’s establishments, no less. Impeccably cooked rice, moist tender chicken, melt-in-the-mouth salmon, juicy red tuna, firm seabass, spicy miso sauce dusted with fresh garden herbs, last-minute grated wasabi and a knockout selection of sakés (the sommelier and partner knows his business). The omakase menu features a festival of flavours for a fine dining experience that can be adapted to suit the appetites and wallets of everyone.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16099;Le M;France;Brest;22 rue du Commandant-Drogou, Brest, 29200, France;48.4041632;-4.4909818;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Plenty of originality in the design of the dishes and the marriages of flavours in this typically Breton granite house done out with a contemporary decor. Tuck into modern cuisine that sources its ingredients (fish, poultry, vegetables etc) from local producers. In summer, dine alfresco on the pleasant terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16100;16âme;France;Le Monêtier-les-Bains;32 rue des Glaciers, Le Monêtier-les-Bains, 05220, France;44.9760626;6.5067018;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Behind a discreet façade is this inviting restaurant with decor that calls to mind a trapper's hut – we are in the mountains, after all! Julien Momon, originally from Corsica, worked in the kitchens of Christophe Bacquié and Gérard Boyer (formerly chef at Les Crayères in Reims) before becoming head chef at a hotel here in Monêtier-les-Bains. His dishes contain nothing but seasonal and local ingredients from this rural and Alpine territory, such as lamb from the Hautes-Alpes, coriander, mint, a pearly jus with olive oil or his lovage-infused cream.;Terrace;[]
16101;Taokan;France;Paris;8 rue du Sabot, Paris, 75006, France;48.85263;2.33149;63;false;false;Chinese;Come inside this pretty restaurant in the heart of St-Germain-des-Prés to enjoy light and fragrant Cantonese cuisine, with a few detours to the territory of Southeast Asia: the obligatory dim sum, steamed fish, spicy beef or lok lak. Lovely presentation and good ingredients: a real ambassador for Chinese food.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16102;Prosper;France;Saint-Aubin;3 rue des Lavières, Saint-Aubin, 21190, France;46.9499175;4.709516;45;false;false;Modern Cuisine;When a winemaker from the Côte de Beaune meets a starred chef, you get Prosper! This lovely contemporary bistro in the Château St Aubin is the result of a collaboration between the Prosper Maufoux wine estate and the restaurateur Édouard Mignot (restaurant Ed.Em in Chassagne-Montrachet). The chef proposes a menu inspired by the Burgundy terroir. Pleasant terrace with a view of the vineyards.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16103;Les Parisiens;France;Paris;1 rue du Pré-aux-Clercs, Paris, 75007, France;48.8566675;2.3303963;89;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Inside a new luxury hotel located in Faubourg-Saint-Germain, this restaurant adopts all the codes of the luxury brasserie genre. Wood panelling, large mirrors, mosaic floors, velvet banquettes, gilding, black marble tables: it is elegant, slightly retro and very cosy – a winning formula. Curated by Thibault Sombardier, the menu represents a refreshed and updated take on tradition. A fine and eclectic wine list, complete with some great bottles.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16105;Magma;France;Paris;9 rue Jean-Pierre-Timbaud, Paris, 75011, France;48.865099;2.3672731;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Like magma, Japanese chef Ryuya Ono fusions French haute cuisine with his own constantly renewed inspiration and gourmet instincts in a tasting menu that shows the greatest respect for the seasons. Spot-on associations are the chef’s hallmark, illustrated by trout garnished with chanterelle mushrooms. The desserts, like the squash-flavoured creamy mont-blanc delight, are equally inventive. Crisp, elegant interior and slick service.;;[]
16111;Ezkia;France;Bidart;6 avenue de la Grande-Plage, Bidart, 64210, France;43.4392106;-1.5907114;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Whether beneath the lime trees (ezkia in Basque) on the terrace, or inside the small, inviting and intimate restaurant room with exposed stonework, floorboards, saffron-coloured velvet seats and banquettes, it is the same traditional Basque house. Standing in the heart of the delightful village of Bidart, it exudes a quiet, refined atmosphere. The couple who run the place, defectors from Michel Guérard's restaurant, serve nice seasonal precisely cooked dishes, full of good local Basque produce e.g. farm-reared pig, line-caught tuna, black cherry, mature farm cheeses.;Terrace;[]
16112;Patern;France;Nancy;60 rue Stanislas, Nancy, 54000, France;48.6923925;6.1791657;90;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This superlatively located eatery is only a 5-minute walk from Stanislas Square! In a smart, modern interior, Martin Debuiche, former deputy of Jean-Pierre Vigato of the Apicius in Paris, crafts surprise menus based on flawlessly sourced premium ingredients: fish from Brittany, Vosges pigeon, dairy produce from Meurthe-et-Moselle, saffron from Lorraine, etc. Examples include frothy potatoes, Oscietra caviar from Aquitaine and a bay leaf emulsion, or blowtorch-seared Brittany mackerel garnished with fish bone powder and sautéed girolles.;;[]
16113;Eunoé;France;Paris;6 rue Rochebrune, Paris, 75011, France;48.86082;2.37893;79;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Japanese chef Ryuji Sato and Félix Perotte (front of house) are two friends who are passionate about food and wine. They offer hospitality at this location near Square Maurice Gardette. In a modern, stylishly "unfinished" setting in sand and ochre tones, the chef delivers his fine, no-holds-barred take on the culinary zeitgeist, with an emphasis on flavour in every dish: pork loin soaked in its full-bodied jus with aged sherry vinegar and a hint of thyme, smoked potato mash and a small salad of fresh herbs, seasoned to perfection. At dinner, the elegance goes up a notch.;;[]
16115;Le France;France;Villers-le-Lac;8 place Maxime-Cupillard, Villers-le-Lac, 25130, France;47.0594855;6.6703586;21;true;true;Creative;Between Morteau and La Chaux-de-Fonds, not far from the French-Swiss border, this restaurant welcomes guests to the heart of the Haut-Doubs mountains. In this family-run place, chef Hugues Droz offers guests typical Franche-Comté hospitality, just as his father and grandfather did before him. With a keen eye on seasonal produce, he loves to ally terroir and innovation. He also enjoys creating themed meals, such as his morel-based menu, in which this mushroom features in every course.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16116;Alluma;France;Paris;151 rue Saint-Maur, Paris, 75011, France;48.8682744;2.3749645;87;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Israeli;Former Balagan chef Liran Tal has tastefully revamped this establishment with immaculate white walls. He crafts delicious Mediterranean cuisine with Israeli influences, served in the form of tasting menus that are very good value for money: delicious msabbaha hummus, yellowtail crudo with figs and spices, lamb sirloin and an apricot-miso condiment. Choice of organic and biodynamic wines, most notably from Italy, Spain and Armenia.;Air conditioning;[]
16117;La Dariole;France;Orléans;25 rue Étienne-Dolet, Orléans, 45000, France;47.90071;1.908112;96;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;In the heart of the old town and not far from the cathedral, this 15C half-timbered house showcases an easy alliance of old stonework and cosy touches. The chef, who even trained here when he was learning his trade, hits the mark with delicious cuisine that is in tune with the times. The seasonal menu changes regularly and features appealingly tasty dishes such as pork chop with potatoes and a caper jus.;Terrace;[]
16118;Kazumi;France;Angers;3 rue d'Anjou, Angers, 49100, France;47.46635;-0.55691;31;true;false;Teppanyaki, Japanese;Behind the discreet façade of this Japanese restaurant, chef Kazumi Hatakenaka is at the helm. Having first come to France to work in a traditional inn in the Beaujolais region, he is now serving cuisine that speaks to his dual culinary culture (French and Japanese). His tasting menu alternates classic French dishes with ingredients prepared on the teppanyaki – expertly infused with subtle Japanese flavours. Fresh produce (fish, meat and vegetables), mouth-watering dishes such as pan-fried foie gras, melt-in-the-mouth kohlrabi and veal jus, and on-point cooking and seasoning make this a delightful culinary escapade. For dinner, allow three hours at your table.;Counter dining;[]
16119;Castel Ac'h;France;Plouguerneau;Plage de Lilia, Plouguerneau, 29880, France;48.6216697;-4.5621919;50;true;true;Seafood, Modern Cuisine;Brittany is full of magical places and the Abers region is one such! Just a stone’s throw from the lighthouses of Ile Vierge and Ile de Wrac’h, this handsome neo-Brittany house enjoys a superb location opposite the picturesque Lilia Beach. The food is of regional inspiration with a range of tasty surf and turf ingredients and the lunchtime menu is a steal. In the evening, two set menus and one à la carte play a bistronomic Brittany score: oysters, abalone, fish of the day, veggies from the cottage garden, seaweed and sarrazin wheat...;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16120;Les Roseaux Pensants;France;Cormery;2 place du Mail, Cormery, 37320, France;47.2677982;0.8379508;27;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This quaint historic village is the lair of a self-taught couple, who sources their organic ingredients entirely locally thus enabling them to develop close ties with producers. The gutsy result demonstrates a weakness for veggies and fermentation illustrated by vegetarian black pudding paired with apple and black garlic pickles, although the menu also features a sprinkling of meat and fish dishes. A delightful patio shaded by linden trees in fine weather and swish, slick service complete the portrait.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16121;À l'Échevin;France;Colmar;4 place des Six-Montagnes-Noires, Colmar, 68000, France;48.0736081;7.3568819;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of “Little Venice”, the half-timbered Le Maréchal hotel is home to a comfortable and classically-decorated restaurant. The food is rather more adventurous and the chef deftly crafts modern recipes, putting a new spin on regional and gastronomic favourites, thanks to a sprinkling of creative touches. Delicious desserts, like this duo of figs and creamed rice in a crisp cinnamon-scented tuile. We recommend booking a seat in the blue dining room which overlooks the Lauch River.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16122;La Cotriade;France;Les Sables-d'Olonne;18 quai Emmanuel-Garnier, Les Sables-d'Olonne, 85100, France;46.4960645;-1.7903471;24;false;true;Seafood;On the quayside facing the fishing port, the seafood counter piled high with fish and shellfish sits proudly in front of the restaurant. This seafaring theme is naturally pursued indoors, where the chef is busy in his open-plan kitchen. The menu features seafood platters, fresh fish chalked up on the daily specials board, a few family favourites and a scattering of signature dishes like seabream cooked in a banana leaf, lime and coconut milk, whole sea bass roasted in fennel and flambéed with aniseed, or their famous cotriade – Brittany's answer to bouillabaisse. A few meat dishes are also available.;Terrace;[]
16126;L'Ancienne Auberge;France;Vonnas;Place du Marché, Vonnas, 01540, France;46.21997;4.99065;21;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This establishment is in a former lemonade factory. The nostalgic 1940s bistro decor pays tribute to the inn opened by the Blanc family in the late 19C (old photos and posters). Regional cuisine.;Terrace;[]
16128;Le P'tit Bateau;France;Beaugency;54 rue du Pont, Beaugency, 45190, France;47.7790175;1.6317778;70;true;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of the medieval city, Le P'tit Bateau sets out to tantalise our taste buds with fresh produce, including fish sourced directly from Brittany's fish markets, as well as game from Sologne in season. The dishes are generous, precise, carefully presented and tasty. It is worth noting there is a pleasant patio for a meal al fresco. An eatery committed to doing a good job.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16129;Le Restaurant 1451;France;Renaison;15 rue Robert-Barathon, Renaison, 42370, France;46.0520866;3.9268415;15;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In the heart of this market town near Roanne, imagine an old stone house lit up in blue at nighttime, whose tasteful elegant interior is flanked by a lovely alfresco courtyard terrace that is perfect for special occasions. The scene is set for a fine dining experience. Chef Jérémie Louis crafts fresh, modern recipes in which artistically displayed vegetables are often cast in the lead roles. The cheese trolley is truly in a class of its own. Océane, the chef’s partner, supervises the front-of house cheerfully and seamlessly. A family-run establishment depicted by a genuine “home from home” vibe!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16134;La fleur de Sel;France;Le Creusot;2 rue Albert-1er, Le Creusot, 71200, France;46.7949849;4.4250879;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The initiative by this pair, chef Willy Lardry and maître d' Edwin Smietanski, to open their restaurant here is most welcome. Both hail from Le Creusot but met while working for Yohann Chapuis in Tournus. The interior is inspired in part by nature (with, in particular, wallpaper depicting a forest in the mist). The chef, working alone in the kitchen, shows undeniable maturity. Delicacy and finesse are the order of the day, for example, the lovely courgette flower with cod stuffing and the olive oil sabayon accompanying the cod tournedos, or the mackerel and its marinated cucumber ravioli.;Wheelchair access;[]
16135;Le Bistrot de Cancale;France;Cancale;à Port-Mer, 5 rue Eugène-et-Auguste-Feyen, Cancale, 35260, France;48.7013126;-1.8499885;15;true;true;Seafood;Run by Hugo Roellinger, this restaurant is located opposite the beach at Port-Mer with its small boats bobbing at anchor and Mont-Saint-Michel visible in the distance. The menu features dishes such as oysters, shellfish, langoustines, sole with a caramelised jus, turbot cooked on the bone, lobster cooked over hot coals – excellent fish, distinguished by its remarkable freshness and often seasoned with Olivier Roellinger's famous spice mixes. There is a beautiful terrace with a sea view and, inside, knick-knacks related to Brittany and fishing create a chic and modernised seaside bistro vibe that is enhanced by a 1930s fresco depicting a scene from life in the port of Saint-Malo.;Great view,Terrace;[]
16136;L'Ouzeri;France;Paris;41 rue du Ruisseau, Paris, 75018, France;48.8933894;2.340284;91;true;false;Greek;Saganaki cheese, gyro merida, myzithropita (cheesecake), spanakopita – the menu gives it away: this is French-Greek chef Mikaela Liaroutsos's Greek taverna, and it's just a stone's throw from the original restaurant Etsi that made her name. The food is served as a series of mezes, to savour as you dream of Greek holidays, past or future. The traditional songs playing in the background might tempt you to pull out a sirtaki step after a glass of ouzo.;;[]
16138;La Colombe;France;Bedoin;3890 route du Mont-Ventoux, Bedoin, 84410, France;44.1203545;5.2245211;17;false;false;Modern Cuisine;At the foot of Mont Ventoux surrounded by vineyards, this gourmet dove coos a delicious melody. Chef Christophe Schuffenecker (formerly of the star-rated Château de Mazan) serves modern, spot-on dishes, blessedly free of superfluous extras, such as Sarrians pigeon with geranium-perfumed mashed carrots. When the weather is fine, make a beeline for the terrace shaded by awnings overlooking the vineyards. The stylish interior sports bare beams and a large Provençal fireplace, as well as a permanent art exhibition.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16139;L'Embarcadère;France;Jassans-Riottier;15 avenue de la Plage, Jassans-Riottier, 01480, France;45.9870915;4.7523828;64;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Georges Blanc's new restaurant, on the banks of the Saône, is a cross between a chic guinguette and a contemporary brasserie. The food is traditional but trendy with dishes like frogs' legs, poached free - range egg with whiting, and Bresse chicken.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16140;La Mère Germaine;France;Villefranche-sur-Mer;9 quai Amiral-Courbet, Villefranche-sur-Mer, 06230, France;43.7037184;7.3122149;32;false;true;Seafood;Jean Cocteau used to eat at this local institution, which has been serving fresh fish and seafood since 1938. It is lovely just to sit on the terrace and gaze out over the harbour!;Great view,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16141;Boccafine;France;Nonza;au village, Nonza, 20217, France;42.784847;9.3450241;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A small, listed village on the Cap Corse road is home to this demure restaurant, hidden by a curtain of Virginia Creeper and tall plane trees. The chef unveils his know-how as he crafts painstakingly sourced, local and seasonal ingredients, illustrated by ultra-fresh croaker, pancetta and pork jus in a surf and turf recipe of wondrous harmony. Love at first bite.;Terrace;[]
16142;L'Affable;France;Cannes;5 rue La Fontaine, Cannes, 06400, France;43.5518774;7.0249091;76;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;In the centre of Cannes, this contemporary bistro is always busy and, indeed, it has much to recommend it. First and foremost its menu: courgette flower fritters, cod aioli, rack of lamb roasted with thyme… and the classic Grand Marnier soufflé, the house speciality.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16143;L'Espace PH3;France;Vienne;14 boulevard Fernand-Point, Vienne, 38200, France;45.5168027;4.8668013;32;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This is the Henriroux family’s second venture, created directly inside La Pyramide. The tasteful interior displays a strong plant focus in line with the menu’s healthy, wellness leaning, without forgetting pedigree classics, like calf’s head and pink praline. Everything is in the energetic hands of a charismatic team. Bags of vitality and flavour!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16145;Premnord;France;Premeaux-Prissey;6 RD 974, Premeaux-Prissey, 21700, France;47.1121709;4.932033;75;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The restaurant of the Prieuré-Roch estate rises up to greet visitors with its distinctive wood and steel U-shaped architecture, whose centre is graced with a vast patio overlooking the vineyards. Indoors are a parquet-floored lounge, a bar decked in light wood and a spacious contemporary dining room with immense floor-to-ceiling windows. Chef Céline Dedinger (who boasts stints with Thomas Collomb at the Rôtisserie du Chambertin and the Maison des Cariatides) crafts a modern score based on mainly local ingredients (whose exact source is indicated on the menu) in line with the seasons.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16146;Campelli;France;Paris;36 rue Croix-des-Petits-Champs, Paris, 75001, France;48.86427;2.34031;46;true;false;Creative;This diminutive restaurant with a midnight-blue and gold façade boasts a chic yet understated decor (velvet banquettes, wooden chairs upholstered in matching velvet, exposed stone walls) – all the better to showcase the creative cuisine and multicultural culinary experience of chef Vartivar Jarkezian. Firmly rooted in French tradition, his cooking also draws discreetly on the influences and pantry of the Middle East (cumin, pistachio, turmeric, yoghurt sauce).;;[]
16153;Nananère;France;Antibes;13 rue Championnet, Antibes, 06600, France;43.5814725;7.1228526;30;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Sometimes it is fun to revisit your childhood! Run by the former owners of Le P'tit Cageot, this restaurant has a playful decor that draws on comic strips and action figures of characters such as Spiderman and Buzz Lightyear. Things get serious, however, when it comes to the delicious food. The menu abounds with French classics (leeks in vinaigrette, saucisson brioché, poire belle Hélène), as well as dishes catering to teenage diners (mac & cheese and burgers) and fresh house-made pasta – everything is professionally prepared using quality ingredients. Large terrace. No reservations for parties of fewer than six people.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16154;Kitchen by Madame Rêve;France;Paris;48 rue du Louvre, Paris, 75001, France;48.8645154;2.3429336;66;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Restored from head to toe, the iconic Haussmannian Louvre Post Office building is also home to a luxury hotel and a classy neo-brasserie, nestled under an impressive ceiling. The menu is divided into culinary themes in a tongue-in-cheek poke at your usual restaurant codes: healthy trendy, veg out, flashback, etc. The onus is definitely on unstuffy pleasure!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16155;Dame Augustine;France;Paris;32 avenue des Gobelins, Paris, 75013, France;48.8357267;2.3525018;75;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This is the other restaurant of chef Lilian Douchet, who hails from Bordeaux: you can expect a laid-back atmosphere and a veranda-style space with the feel of a small brasserie. He serves several set menus, including a good-value lunch deal. Diners savour dishes such as a selection of heirloom tomatoes, fresh herb pesto, parmesan buttercrumb biscuits and mizuna sorbet, or a fillet of whiting simmered with coco de Paimpol beans and a lemon thyme emulsion. A welcome address in this residential area.;;[]
16157;Pamparigouste - Le Couvent des Minimes;France;Mane;Chemin des Jeux-de-Maï, Mane, 04300, France;43.9395678;5.7723872;59;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In addition to his fine dining restaurant, chef Louis Gachet lovingly oversees this upscale bistro. The space is soothing and relaxing, plus there is a dining room-cum-terrace, whose picture windows are opened fully in fine weather. The menu is a skilful blend of traditional favourites and contemporary dishes with a smattering of Provençal touches.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16158;Gaua;France;Urrugne;210 D810, Urrugne, 64700, France;43.3748366;-1.6795223;96;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Benoit Sarthou (who held a Michelin star at Moulin d'Alotz) has chosen to make his restaurant a celebration of conviviality and the "night" (gaua in Basque). This former garage has been turned into a trendy industrial-style lounge with a central bar-counter and large open kitchen. Share an array of tapas in an ambience fostered by skilfully curated playlists. Think comfort and fusion food, with various ingredients matured or cooked over an open flame.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
16159;Colvert;France;Paris;30 rue des Grands-Augustins, Paris, 75006, France;48.8534862;2.3401623;25;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Revealed by the French Top Chef TV show, Arnaud Baptiste and his flamboyant moustache and numerous tattoos, is something of a media darling. He has set up shop in a vintage street corner bistro (banquettes, bistro chairs, tightly packed tables, bare stone walls, cement tiled floor and a counter which now serves standing customers) in the somewhat touristy, but nonetheless picturesque 6th district of Paris. Arnaud happily crafts market-fresh, bistronomic fare. The seasonal menu is suitably concise and hits the spot every time: confit of cod, hollandaise sauce, courgettes and absinthe gel or figs, served roasted, raw and in pickles with a fig sorbet and ice cream.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16161;La Table du 5;France;Barr;Hôtel 5 Terres, 11 place de l'Hôtel-de-Ville, Barr, 67140, France;48.4089577;7.4500053;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This contemporary restaurant located within the 5 Terres Hotel looks out over the magnificent Renaissance town hall (1640). In a light-filled space done out in premium materials, you can enjoy contemporary cuisine that brings the best out of carefully sourced local ingredients. The wine list is particularly impressive, featuring hundreds of organic and biodynamic labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16162;19.20 by Norbert Tarayre;France;Paris;Prince de Galles, 33 avenue George-V, Paris, 75008, France;48.8691365;2.3007968;19;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Built in 1928, the Prince de Galles is a legendary jewel of the Parisian Art Deco movement. It has chosen to democratise luxury hotel cuisine by entrusting its kitchens to Norbert Tarayre, the firebrand chef discovered on French TV show Top Chef in 2012. In a cosy setting that pays tribute to artistic life in Paris, the chef serves up traditional cuisine that channels the tasty regional cooking of yesteryear: grated carrot salad, leeks in vinaigrette, celeriac in remoulade dressing, pork shoulder and pommes Anna, salmon tournedos – not to mention the dessert trolley. It's all lovingly prepared and delivered. Incredibly reasonable price of the menu.;Air conditioning,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16164;Château Fage - La Maison des Vignes;France;Arveyres;Fage, Arveyres, 33500, France;44.8652034;-0.3052989;15;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Built in the white stone typical of the region, this 19C château standing proud amid the vineyards is now a hotel-restaurant. The contemporary cuisine, at once straightforward and bold, wins diners over. Every ingredient is carefully selected and expertly prepared, for dishes such as fillet of pink sea bream, shellfish sauce vierge and mussels with samphire, or the appetising dessert trolley. Accompanied by wines from the estate.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16165;Mansouria;France;Paris;11 rue Faidherbe, Paris, 75011, France;48.8512188;2.3839767;23;true;true;Moroccan;Just a stone's throw from the Bastille, this restaurant has proved popular with fans of Moroccan cuisine for over 40 years. You are instantly transported by the aromas of this venerable institution, which is now run by the daughter of the founder. In a discreetly North African decor, traditional tagines and couscous are served alongside a host of lesser-known dishes, such as pigeon pastilla and traditional spicy lamb mourouzia "Al-Andalus" with sweet notes supplied by honey and sultanas – the house speciality. Top-quality ingredients and attentive service make for a delicious culinary voyage.;Air conditioning;[]
16167;Abîme - L'Auberge du Pont;France;Gruffy;991 route du Pont-de-l'Abîme, Gruffy, 74540, France;45.7644301;6.057976;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This long-established inn stands by a bridge spanning the gorge – the Chéran River flows a few hundred metres below! A native of the area, the chef likes to work with regional ingredients he sources from local producers. Even amateur mushroom foragers are welcome to offer up their pick of the day. His squash risotto, fricassee of shiitake, polypore and oyster mushrooms is a prime example of his culinary style, which is geared toward plants and vegetables and the interplay of textures. A "discovery menu" made up of several courses is available in the evening and at weekends. Appealing lunchtime set menu.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16169;Twist & Buckle;;Hong Kong;29-31 Chatham Road South, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2979744;114.1753884;23;false;false;Street Food;Two young South Americans opened this shop specialising in churros. Besides the traditional version with cinnamon sugar, also try them glazed, in dips like dulce de leche and salted caramel, or even in sundaes with ice cream.;Air conditioning;[]
16170;Celestial Court;;Hong Kong;2F, Sheraton Hotel, 20 Nathan Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2952366;114.1725979;20;false;false;Cantonese;The astute chef has over 25 years of experience and was brought up in a family who owned a dried seafood business. His shrewd insights on sourcing and preparing those gourmet ingredients are reflected in the menu. The speciality roast whole suckling pig with pearl barley and black truffles needs pre-ordering. Scrambled egg with lobster and caviar is another highlight. The windowless dining room is nicely furnished with rich wood accents.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16171;Ippoh;;Hong Kong;39 Aberdeen Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.282784;114.15167;26;false;true;Tempura;Now run by the fifth generation, this family business rooted in Osaka still strictly follows the traditional rules of making tempura. The owner-chef insists on battering and frying every morsel himself without delegating his duty. Seafood is flown in daily from Osaka and Toyosu fish market and they use flavourless safflower oil, so as not to overpower the ingredients’ natural tastes. The sauce is made to a secret recipe. Omakase is the best way to go. Bookings are essential.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16172;Fong Kei;;Macau;14 Rua do Cunha, Taipa, Macau;22.153482;113.55707;25;true;false;Street Food;A longstanding shop offering Chinese cakes and biscuits. The almond cakes and egg rolls stand out.;;[]
16173;Fat Boy;;Hong Kong;3 Hau Fook Street, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2994809;114.1740176;66;false;true;Street Food;Hong Kong-style snacks including octopus, pork liver & turkey gizzard marinated in soy sauce. Sweet sauce and mustard add to the flavour. The combo set offers great value with three signature items.;Cash only;[]
16175;Tsui Hang Village (Tsim Sha Tsui);;Hong Kong;Shop 507, 5F, FoodLoft, Mira Place One, 132 Nathan Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.301006;114.1721;93;true;false;Cantonese;A staple of the Tsim Sha Tsui restaurant scene since 1970s, this place is famous for its authentic Cantonese and Shun Tak fare, namely its bestselling honey-glazed char siu pork, braised beef ribs and shredded chicken, alongside some original creations by the head chef, such as fried king prawns in mango sauce topped with caviar. The dim sum is also good. Watching the chefs work their magic through the large window is all part of the experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16176;Keung Kee;;Hong Kong;406 Lockhart Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.279594;114.180225;100;false;false;Street Food;After moving to this new spot, this simple shop boasts better comfort and a bigger menu. But signatures like glutinous rice with preserved meat, wok-fried rice rolls, and pork bone congee remain as tasty as ever.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
16177;Ngao Kei Ka Lei Chon (Macau);;Macau;GF, 1 Rua de Cinco de Outubro, Macau, Macau;22.2000023;113.5374411;52;true;false;Noodles and Congee;Don’t judge a book by its cover because the simple neon signs outside do not reflect the quality of food and service at this friendly, well-run noodle shop. The key draw is the swimmer crab congee – crabs are dressed à la minute and burst with seafood flavours, while the creamy congee imparts a rich aroma of rice. Other recommendations include braised E-fu noodles with crab roe, beef brisket in clear broth, and curry chicken with coconut milk.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
16178;Mak Kee (May Ka Mansion);;Hong Kong;Shop 1, May Ka Mansion, 21 Fort Street, North Point, Hong Kong;22.289684;114.19698;23;true;false;Street Food;This shop serves Shanghainese delicacies made fresh daily, such as pot-stickers, pan-fried pork buns and sour and hot noodle soup. Scallion pancakes are available from 3pm until they run out.;Cash only;[]
16179;Lord Stow's Bakery (Rua do Tassara);;Macau;1 Rua do Tassara, Coloane Town Square, Coloane, Macau;22.1181417;113.5513107;16;true;true;Street Food;For over 30 years, the store has prided itself on its Portuguese egg tarts that have a crisp shell and silky, smooth filling. Tarts are made from scratch, baked throughout the day and sold fresh from the oven. Takeout only.;Cash only;[]
16180;China Tang;;Hong Kong;Shop 411-413, 4F, Landmark Atrium, 15 Queen's Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.2804857;114.1579105;83;false;false;Cantonese;This handsome restaurant was conceived and designed by the late Sir David Tang as a sister to the London branch, and mixes traditional Chinese art with contemporary Western design. Tables are set closely together and there are several private rooms. Dishes from Beijing, Sichuan and Canton feature and dim sum is popular. The chef has introduced a more modern element to the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16181;Beanmountain;;Hong Kong;GF, 1 Canal Road East, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong;22.278842;114.181482;48;true;true;Street Food;For over 20 years, sugar fiends have been getting their fix of Chinese-style sweets here – from traditional crowd-pleasers such as put chai ko and Hakka tea cake made with stinkvine to novelty treats like mango sticky rice ball.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
16182;Plaisance by Mauro Colagreco;;Hong Kong;1F, 1 Duddell Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.280231;114.1572208;40;true;false;French Contemporary;Mother of pearl finishes, turquoise accents and a whirlpool of metal fish sculptures introduce the ocean theme. Begin the meal with Chef Mauro's grandma's recipe – house-made bread with his favourite olive oil. The seafood-led menu delivers spellbinding dishes that incorporate the best ingredients from around the world alongside local vegetables, all finessed by solid French skills. Ask the sommelier to pick a wine for you.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16183;Sabah;;Hong Kong;Shop 1, GF, Pao Woo Mansion, 177-179 Wan Chai Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2770257;114.1772111;62;false;false;Malaysian;Sabah, a staple of Wan Chai’s restaurant scene for 18 years, shuttered its doors in 2019 before reopening here with the same kitchen team. Both the room and the menu are downsized, but signatures like bak kut teh, beef rendang, and seafood laksa remain, tasting just like before. Boneless Hainan chicken rice boasts bouncy skin and velvety juicy flesh. Even the trio of dips and pearl rice are also hard to find fault with.;Air conditioning;[]
16184;The Steak House;;Hong Kong;GF, Regent, 18 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.29488;114.1757;100;true;false;Steakhouse;The iconic Regent Hong Kong has reopened with several new F&B outlets. One of them is The Steak House commanding sweeping harbour views through its tall windows. As its name suggests, the menu revolves around steak – from Italy, Spain, Korea, Japan, Australia, and the U.S. The Moroccan chef ages his own beef - ask the servers. Season your favourite cuts with rock salt, charcoal salt, yuzu salt or the array of sauces and mustards on offer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking;[]
16185;Cafe Bau;;Hong Kong;Shop 8, Podium 1F, J Residence, 60 Johnston Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.2763;114.1711;78;true;false;European Contemporary;Cafe Bau, a new dining concept by the self-proclaimed “Demon Chef” Alvin Leung, is styled like a vintage brasserie dripping in retro glam. Sit at the bar and watch the bartender concoct exquisite beverages. On to the food, order the 3-course menu for traditional European fare, or opt for  the 8-course tasting extravaganza for more innovative, adventurous dishes. Local produce like oysters and fish is used to good effect. Service is off-the-cuff and to-the-point.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16186;Ho Lee Fook;;Hong Kong;3-5 Elgin Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2830819;114.1524866;42;false;true;Cantonese;Walls covered in gilded maneki-neko, mahjong tiles, pop art and red Chinese floral motifs make this a bold, unorthodox spot for a fun night out. The 80s Canto-pop soundtrack is also a proud expression of its local DNA. The open kitchen on ground level is a spectacle to behold and its creative Cantonese cooking harnesses bold distinctive flavours and wok hei. Try the crispy three-yellow chicken with sand ginger dip, and other wok-fries. Check ahead for dishes that need pre-ordering.;Air conditioning;[]
16187;She Wong Hei;;Hong Kong;59 Percival Street, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong;22.27947;114.18289;56;false;true;Cantonese;The manager that ran the famous snake soup shop She Wong Yee opened this restaurant on the same street. The classic snake soup is reworked with a slightly altered consistency, alongside fish maw, chicken, hand-sliced pork, dried tangerine peel, wood ear fungus and shiitake mushroom. Of course, you can still order barbecue meats, and glutinous rice to go with the soup. Duck liver sausage with snappy casing is certainly worth trying.;Air conditioning;[]
16188;Yuè (Gold Coast);;Hong Kong;LG, Gold Coast Hotel, 1 Castle Peak Road, Gold Coast, Tuen Mun, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.41878;113.98285;41;true;true;Cantonese;It’s not often one can enjoy Cantonese food surrounded by verdant scenery but here on the ground floor of the Gold Coast hotel that’s exactly what you get as this comfortable restaurant looks out onto a delightful garden. The menu includes both traditional and more contemporary dishes and it’s worth seeking out the chef’s specialities such as barbecued pork and double boiled pork lung soup with almond milk and fish maw, and deep-fried chicken with shrimp paste.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16189;The Swiss Chalet;;Hong Kong;GF, 8 Hart Avenue, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2982098;114.1747682;40;false;true;Swiss;Despite moving next door, the room still retains the same quaint Alpine chalet ambiance with wood furniture and beams set nicely against whitewashed walls. The classic Swiss menu covers a variety of cured meats and sausages, over 20 cheeses, and of course the unmissable fondue made with five cheeses and kirsch, to be paired with their extensive selection of Swiss wines. Thinly sliced veal with white mushrooms in a cream sauce is also worth trying.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16190;Ki Tsui;;Hong Kong;135 Fa Yuen Street, Mong Kok, Hong Kong;22.3214779;114.1705838;73;true;true;Street Food;Despite the small size, this shop offers a wide array of Cantonese traditional puddings and pastries like Xiaofeng cake and walnut cookies.;Cash only;[]
16191;Kika;;Macau;GF, 11A Travessa da Sé, Macau, Macau;22.194235;113.54116;82;false;false;Street Food;Pop in for an artisan Japanese gelato. Customers are spoiled for exotic choices here – crown melon from Shizuoka, Hokkaido 3.6 milk, Hojicha, and, of course, their famous ultra-strong matcha green tea for die-hard tea lovers.;;[]
16192;Terrazza;;Macau;Shop 201, 2F, Galaxy Hotel, Galaxy, Estrada da Baía de Nossa Senhora da Esperança, Cotai, Macau;22.1502393;113.5534567;19;false;true;Italian;The menu covers the culinary traditions of every region in Italy and is updated every three months to keep it fresh. Guests get to see how the food is prepared through the glass wall. Pizza dough, tagliatelle, ravioli and tagliolini are made from scratch in-house and the extensive wine list is well worth exploring. Add in exceedingly comfy chairs and warm, welcoming service and you have a great place for a relaxing meal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16193;Joyful Dessert House;;Hong Kong;Shop 2-3, GF, Ngai Hing Mansion, 74 Hak Po Street, Mong Kok, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3177706;114.1727452;68;true;false;Street Food;Come for beautifully plated Western desserts, such as waffles, chocolate fondant and velvety shaved ice. Recommendations include mango Napoleon, caramelised pineapple sorbet, and green tea fondant à la mode.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
16194;Carbone;;Hong Kong;9F, 33 Wyndham Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2804202;114.1551384;28;true;false;Italian-American;A nod to Manhattan’s American-Italian diners circa 1950s, this colourful spot celebrates the era in everything from the floor tiles and chandeliers, to the cutlery and servers’ uniforms. In the same way, the menu embraces classics like pastas and steaks, such as the signature Tasmanian lamb tomahawk. Portion sizes are more American than Italian, enough for a few to share. House-made limoncello makes great apéritifs and digestifs.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16195;Fishball Man (To Kwa Wan);;Hong Kong;GF, 50 Tin Kwong Road, To Kwa Wan, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.320017;114.1873922;23;false;false;Street Food;Though local snacks like shaomai and cheong fun are offered, its eponymous speciality remains the most popular. Besides the spicy variety, the springy and flavourful white fish balls drizzled in chilli oil are unmissable.;Cash only;[]
16196;Cornerstone;;Hong Kong;49 Hollywood Road, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.282768;114.1531672;54;false;false;European Contemporary;Owner-chef Shane Osborn of Arcane fame calls it an ‘Australian café’ – in fact, it feels more like a hip bistro with its faux-industrial décor. The small menu is a tapestry of global culinary cultures, including Aussie, European and Asian favourites. Though it changes a few times each month to keep things fresh, dishes are always competitively priced and loaded with big flavours and pleasing textures. Online reservations only.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16197;Hung Hom Pancake;;Hong Kong;Shop 2, Polly Court, Taku Street, Hung Hom, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3066703;114.1863566;76;false;true;Street Food;For over 40 years, this neighbourhood shop has provided the childhood memories of many. Pancakes, waffles and egg waffles are all made to order. Tricolour egg waffles in plain, chocolate and matcha flavours particularly stand out.;Cash only;[]
16198;Giando;;Hong Kong;Shop 1, GF, Tower 1, Starcrest, 9 Star Street, Wan Chai, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.276463;114.16777;43;true;false;Italian;Italian chef Gianni Caprioli owns several restaurants in Hong Kong but this one, tucked away in a quiet corner between Wan Chai and Admiralty, is his jewel. Besides the booths along one side of the smart dining room, outdoor seating is also prized for an al-fresco Italian feast or just a glass of Italian wine pre- or post-dinner. Expect to see dishes from all over Italy, such as hand-rolled strozzapreti pasta, or Milanese-style veal chop.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16199;Owl's;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, 32 Mody Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2971442;114.1746721;44;false;false;Street Food;You’ll need to wait as the homemade choux pastries are filled on order with cream and custard of different flavours but, rest assured, the wait is worth it. Check out the occasional limited time offers. Take-out only.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
16200;Ving Kei (Macau);;Macau;GF, 47 Rua da Tercena, Macau, Macau;22.1973989;113.5392144;73;true;true;Street Food;Apart from the signature cold or hot tofu pudding and soy milk, it also provides tofu products, squid and noodles.;Cash only;[]
16201;Hop Yik Tai;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;121 Kweilin Street, Sham Shui Po, Hong Kong;22.330359;114.16127;62;true;false;Street Food;The menu at this always busy shop features Hong Kong-style snacks like fish balls, pork skin and braised radish. The hugely popular rice rolls are silky-smooth, with a hint of richness from the lard.;Cash only;[]
16202;Cuisine Cuisine at The Mira;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, The Mira Hotel, 118 Nathan Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.3001459;114.1723811;62;true;false;Cantonese;The striking chandelier with hundreds of glowing glass globes is set nicely against the calming green colour scheme and verdant views. Cantonese classics underpinned by solid, traditional techniques are revitalised by creative use of ingredients and modern twists. On top of special dim sum such as crispy frog legs with peppered salt, try also Mrs. Song’s fish soup made with fresh grouper fillet. Wine pairings are thoughtfully matched.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16203;Heimat;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;8F, 33 Wyndham Street, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2804483;114.1551346;75;false;true;German;Heimat translates as “homeland”. After working in some prestigious kitchens, the German owner-chef Peter Find reinterprets classics from his home country with quality ingredients, dexterous care and much sophistication. The 6-course tasting menu takes diners on a journey across Germany with flavours from his childhood memories. A shorter 3-course menu is available at lunch. And who can resist the gummy bear trolley at the end?;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16204;La Brasserie;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, Lyndhurst Building, 23-29 Lyndhurst Terrace, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.28271;114.15365;56;false;false;French;As its name suggests, this restaurant serves authentic French fare in a convivial atmosphere. Seafood choices abound – from smoked salmon and bouillabaisse to the seafood platter. Meat lovers should check out the pâtés in the charcuterie section. A visit to the pastry counter is a must for classics such as éclairs and opera cake as much as novel creations like genmaicha St Honoré. The wine list boasts a good range of by-the-glass options.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16205;Chiado;;Macau;Shop 2206, 2F, The Londoner, Estrada do lstmo, Cotai, Macau;22.1458609;113.5653553;29;true;true;Portuguese;As well as a neighbourhood of Lisbon, Chiado is celebrity chef Henrique Sá Pessoa’s first dining concept outside Portugal. The room is modern and cosy, setting the mood for a feast of Portuguese classics oozing with understated elegance and robust flavours. Choose the 6-course degustation menu to sample all the chef’s signature dishes. Don’t miss the boneless suckling pig that is slow-cooked then grilled, boasting crispy skin and silky meat.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16206;Ho Kee Dessert (To Kwa Wan);Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 111 & 122, GF, I-Feng Mansions, 237A To Kwa Wan Road, To Kwa Wan, Hong Kong;22.3167147;114.1901629;39;true;false;Street Food;The staple in Mong Kok for over 30 years moved to this location in 2020. Rest assured their traditional sweet soups like black sesame paste, and glutinous rice balls in ginger syrup taste as good as ever.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted;[]
16207;Clarence;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;25F, H Code, 45 Pottinger Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2822658;114.1546007;57;true;false;French Contemporary;After working and living in Asia for over a decade, chef Olivier Elzer founded this restaurant that aims to allow new ways of enjoying French cuisine. He minted an original concept known as “Yakifrenchy” – a menu that serves French classics like duck confit, frogs’ legs and escargots on skewers, like Japanese yakitori. Local family table culture is taken to another level with meat and fish cooked whole on the bone, perfect for sharing.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16208;Testina;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;3F, 8 Lyndhurst Terrace, Central, Hong Kong;22.282479;114.1548125;69;false;false;Italian;Aptly named after its signature pig’s head dish, Testina is the collaboration between the Milanese trattoria Trippa Milano and a local hospitality group. Championing a nose-to-tail philosophy, the kitchen team serves every part of an animal to great effect. Besides pig’s head, expect to see tripe, bone marrow and veal tongue on the menu. For an authentic taste of Trippa Milano’s cooking, try homemade tagliatelle with duck ragù.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16211;Toritama;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;GF, Greenville, 2 Glenealy, Central, Hong Kong;22.279633;114.155205;52;true;true;Yakitori;Tokyo restaurants keep opening branches in Hong Kong and this time it’s all about yakitori. Seats are limited so it’s worth booking ahead and asking for the counter to watch the expert preparation in the kitchen. 40-day-old chickens are used, and 28 different parts of the birds are offered – rare cuts such as sweetbread may need pre-ordering. Pickles made with different produce according to the season make the perfect side dish for the skewers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16212;Wing;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;29F, The Wellington, 198 Wellington Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2850124;114.1529182;78;true;true;Innovative;The second venture from owner-chef Vicky Cheng who runs the well-acclaimed Vea upstairs, Wing is named after his Chinese name, meaning eternity. The tasting menu features contemporary Chinese courses made with mostly local ingredients but underpinned by European techniques. He reinterprets classic recipes and familiar flavours with creative twists and playful food combinations. Online reservations open at midnight for up to 28 days ahead.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16213;The Ritz-Carlton Café;;Macau;GF, The Ritz-Carlton, Galaxy, Estrada da Baía de Nossa Senhora da Esperança, Cotai, Macau;22.1465273;113.5550943;78;true;true;French;Tiles, mirrors and marble are used to great effect in this bright, lively French brasserie with an all-day dining concept. It prides itself not only on its friendly service, but also the array of classic French food on offer. Besides the daily special, steak is big on the menu with many prime cuts to choose from. Seafood lovers should try freshly shucked oysters. Round out your dinner with the spectacular tableside Grand Marnier flambéed crepes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16214;Ami;Hong Kong SAR China;Hong Kong;Shop 302, 3F, Alexandra House, 18 Chater Road, Central, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2818112;114.1594529;58;true;false;French Contemporary;Ami, decorated on a forest theme, offers a fine dining experience in a casual setting. On top of tasting menus, all-day à la carte choices abound – Gallic classics, plates to share and bar snacks are all up for grabs. The enthusiastic, young chef from Southern France imbues the menu with novel ideas, such as yellow chicken cooked two ways: poached breast and grilled leg with morels and a vin jaune sauce. Made-to-order orange blossom soufflé is fluffy and custardy.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16216;Imperial Court;;Macau;GF, MGM Macau, Avenida Dr. Sun Yat Sen, NAPE, Macau, Macau;22.185957;113.548454;65;true;true;Cantonese;On the same floor as the hotel’s VIP lobby, this sleek, contemporary dining room wows guests with a vividly carved Chinese dragon entwined around a marble pillar. The head chef has over 20 years of experience and updates the menu regularly to star seasonal dishes. Try his crispy-skin fried baby pigeon, and dim sum with a creative twist – order as few or as many pieces as you like. The impressive wine list boasts over 2,000 labels.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16217;Mok Yee Kei;;Macau;9 Rua do Cunha, Taipa, Macau;22.153435;113.55706;52;false;false;Street Food;Offering Serradura pudding and ice cream. The signature durian ice cream comes with Musang King, D24 and Mon Tong choices.;Cash only;[]
16219;Palace Garden;;Macau;Shop 306, 3F, Grand Lisboa Palace, Grand Lisboa Palace Resort, Rua do Tiro, Cotai, Macau;22.1441848;113.5739728;29;true;false;Cantonese;The room is the epitome of lavish maximalism – one wall is covered in a 35-metre-long Suzhou silk embroidery with a chrysanthemum theme. On the menu, ingredients from around the world are used to make refined Cantonese dishes, including labour-intensive items from ancient recipes. Crispy skin squab with lemongrass uses 18-day birds from Shiqi, boasting juicy flesh and mild smokiness. The menu can appear overwhelming, so ask servers for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16220;Shum Shum Desserts;;Hong Kong;Shop C, GF, 46 Kweilin Street, Sham Shui Po, Hong Kong;22.3320311;114.1628929;25;false;false;Street Food;Classic Hongkongese and Taiwanese sweet soups on offer here include creamy coconut soup – a silky delight on its own but even better with chewy taro or sweet potato balls. Try also purple glutinous rice soup with elastic jelly cubes.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
16223;So Kee;;Hong Kong;Shop 15, GF, Block A, Ho Shun Yee Building, 9 Fung Yau Street East, Yuen Long, Hong Kong;22.44325;114.034966;95;true;true;Street Food;There’s just one item on the menu – double-steamed egg white custard with milk, boasting a silky runny centre under a firmer crust. Order the chilled ones if you’re in a rush, or wait patiently as the hot ones are made to order.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
16224;Man Kee Cart Noodle;;Hong Kong;121 Fuk Wing Street, Sham Shui Po, Hong Kong;22.3317749;114.1627388;88;false;false;Street Food;The number of topping choices can be overwhelming, but Chinese chive dumplings and Swiss chicken wings are especially good. Fancy a spicy kick? Try the house-made chilli sauce over your noodles.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
16225;Yi Shun (Macau);;Macau;381 Avenida de Almeida Ribeiro, Macau, Macau;22.1948463;113.538037;67;false;true;Street Food;A longstanding shop offering traditional desserts, such as pineapple with crushed ice and sweet lotus seed soup with egg. Milk custard and ginger milk pudding are house specialties, to which you can add lotus seeds or red beans for extra flavour.;Cash only;[]
16226;Lei Garden (Wan Chai);;Hong Kong;1F, CNT Tower, 338 Hennessy Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.278435;114.1787642;93;true;false;Cantonese;An inventory of restaurants in Wan Chai wouldn’t be complete without a Lei Garden. This branch is bigger than most and boasts a busy, bustling atmosphere, particularly at lunchtime. It follows the group’s tried-and-tested formula of offering an extensive menu with luxurious dishes alongside less elaborate but classic Cantonese specialities. Seafood enthusiasts should consider pre-ordering the Alaskan king crab or Brittany blue lobster.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16228;Farm House;;Hong Kong;1F, Phase 1, China Taiping Tower, 8 Sunning Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2779698;114.1854696;80;true;false;Cantonese;The aquarium running the entire length of one wall certainly catches the eye. But it’s the traditional dishes painstakingly crafted with quality ingredients and gourmet dried seafood that win the hearts of the regulars. You must try their famous fried chicken wing stuffed with sticky rice. Baked sea whelks stuffed with foie gras, steamed rice with chicken, abalone and dried scallops are also deftly prepared. Friendly, thoughtful service.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16229;Tai Tsai (Tsuen Wan);;Hong Kong;GF, 99 Hoi Pa Street, Tsuen Wan, Hong Kong;22.372084;114.11555;35;false;true;Taiwanese;"Tai Tsai" is a homophone of "Taiwanese cuisine" in Chinese. The owner missed his home island's classic braised pork rice so much that he opened his own shop. He cooks the signature rice dish in Taipei style, adding sugar in moderation, and with hand-diced pork belly slow-cooked in aromatics and soy for up to four hours. Top it with onsen tamago or soft-boiled egg. The pepper salt popcorn chicken and boba tea are also well made. Arrive early to beat the crowd.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16230;Lucale;;Hong Kong;Shop A, GF, 100 Third Street, Sai Ying Pun, Hong Kong;22.2855233;114.1404712;54;false;true;Italian;Named after a portmanteau of the two chefs’ first names, this neighbourhood joint uses fine artisanal ingredients from Italy to craft Italian favourites, ranging from homemade pasta to seafood and meat dishes, best enjoyed with their selection of Italian wines. Black truffle chitarrino with Pienza pecorino is guaranteed to melt your heart with its al dente texture and tantalising aroma. The eater-friendly prices also explain its popularity despite its hidden location down an alley.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
16231;Saffron;;Macau;31F, Banyan Tree, Galaxy, Estrada da Baía de Nossa Senhora da Esperança, Cotai, Macau;22.1493633;113.5526986;84;false;false;Thai;The hotel’s restaurant has been completely revamped and moved to the 31st floor, commanding breathtaking views. Now helmed by a native Thai chef with extensive experience, the kitchen specialises in refined Thai cuisine, such as chargrilled organic pork jowl from the royal farm in Thailand with a tamarind fish sauce that is out of this world. The signature curry king crab is also unmissable with a three-chilli blend adding heat and aroma.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16232;Portugália;;Macau;75 Rua dos Clerigos, Taipa, Macau;22.1532832;113.5569251;80;true;false;Portuguese;After a hiatus, Portugália has reopened in the historic town with the same kitchen and service teams. The blue-and-white interior, dotted in matching azulejo tiles from their previous address, is relaxed and cosy. The menu features authentic Portuguese family favourites in sharing portions, such as gambas a la guillo, and the signature steak ‘a Portugália’ in a secret gravy. Round off the meal with a fluffy, whipped serradura.;Air conditioning;[]
16233;The Mews;;Macau;1F, The Londoner, Estrada do lstmo, Cotai, Macau;22.1465478;113.5662619;24;false;true;Thai;Diners are bowled over by the high-ceilinged room adorned in colourful lanterns and wood carving, all of which on a mews (stabling for horses in historic London) theme. The native Thai kitchen team reinvents specialities from their homeland with a contemporary spin. Try the mouthwateringly juicy grilled Wagyu beef with red curry and chakram leaves, or the tangy sunflower chicken tom kha soup. Thai-inspired nibbles and cocktails are also highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16234;Pin Yue Xuan;;Macau;Shop 1016, 1F, The Venetian, Estrada da Baía de Nossa Senhora da Esperança, Cotai, Macau;22.152141;113.571976;24;false;true;Cantonese;The high-ceilinged room, which sports a smart modern Chinese vibe, is the quintessence of stylish flair. The Hong Kong head chef, who has been honing his skills in Macau for many a year, imbues the mostly Cantonese menu with creative touches and luxe delights, such as crispy quinoa on smoked tofu skin rolls, and steamed savoury custard made with Breton blue lobster and Japanese Ranou eggs. The exquisitely crafted petit fours are not to be missed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
16235;Sếp;;Hong Kong;19F, High Block, H Code, 45 Pottinger Street, Central, Hong Kong;22.2822575;114.1542215;17;false;false;Vietnamese;The executive chef spent seven years working in Vietnam where he fell in love with wood-fired cooking. He was keen to introduce the concept to Hong Kong audience when he returned home. His project Sếp specialises in modern Indochine Vietnamese fare using a wood-fired grill in the open kitchen. Menus with 8 or 10 courses feature must-tries like Hoi An poulet made with dry-aged local three-yellow chicken, and bún bò Huế with premium black angus beef.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16236;Mosu;;Hong Kong;3F, M+ Tower, West Kowloon Cultural District, 38 Museum Drive, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.30098;114.15938;56;true;true;Innovative;Nestled in an art museum with commanding panoramic harbour views, the spacious room imparts serenity with its concrete walls and scattered lights that resemble a starry sky. The head chef has years of experience in French cooking, working in some prestigious kitchens in Japan. A single tasting menu is served and it changes from time to time. The courses reflect the chef’s multicultural exposure with its creative combinations of globally sourced ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
16237;Temple Street Beef Offal;;Hong Kong;18 Arthur Street, Yau Ma Tei, Hong Kong;22.3114695;114.1704957;37;false;false;Street Food;This long-standing shop is popular with locals. Tripe, intestine, pancreas or lung can be ordered individually or as an assortment, on a skewer or in a bowl. The offal soaks up the broth nicely, with three sauces on the side.;Cash only;[]
16238;Jardin de Jade (Wan Chai);;Hong Kong;G3-4, GF, Sun Hung Kai Centre, 30 Harbour Road, Wan Chai, Hong Kong;22.280532;114.1769077;68;true;false;Shanghainese;The first Hong Kong venture of the renowned Shanghai restaurant group is certainly not lacking in grandeur, with its double-height ceiling and striking chandelier. Shanghainese classics and dim sum are made the traditional way but with updated presentation. The xiao long bao with beautifully pleated paper-thin skin, soupy filling and spot-on seasoning is the jewel in the crown. The seasonal menu covers regional specialities from beyond Shanghai.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16240;Yi;;Macau;21F, Morpheus, City of Dreams, Estrada do Istmo, Cotai, Macau;22.1499419;113.5665969;49;true;false;Chinese Contemporary;Established on the 21st floor of a sky bridge, Yi’s knockout location is matched by stunning views, impressive architecture and an exotic interior. The 9-course seasonal-driven tasting menu refers to the 24 solar terms of the Chinese calendar, incorporating quality produce from around the world. Rare, premium ingredients, such as nodoguro and A4 Wagyu from Miyazaki, Japan, are deftly and creatively crafted with artful plating.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16242;Leela;;Hong Kong;Shop 301-310, Lee Garden Three, 1 Sunning Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2779966;114.1850822;62;false;false;Indian;The room, furnished in a neoteric Indian style, sports a balcony for pre- or post-prandial drinks. The Indian head chef champions a menu starring specialities from all over India, with contemporary, creative twists. Every course tells a story and diners can truly experience India’s food culture from different perspectives. Try the tandoori dishes from the custom-made oven. With firm yet tender flesh, monkfish imported from France works a treat in the curry.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16243;Mrs. Fong Chinese Desserts;;Hong Kong;198 Temple Street, Jordan, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.3065675;114.1700013;89;true;false;Street Food;This busy family-run shop moved here in 2022. Over 10 Chinese sweets are made from scratch daily, such as red bean cake or put-chai cake. Black sesame roll is especially prized for its soft-springy texture and deep flavour.;Cash only;[]
16244;Above & Beyond;;Hong Kong;28F, Hotel Icon, 17 Science Museum Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.3009241;114.1796763;28;true;true;Cantonese;The stylish décor, sweeping harbour views and extensive menu make this restaurant a popular choice for Cantonese dining. The chef puts a new spin on the dim sum tradition by melding imported ingredients with authentic local flavours. Signatures such as steamed Alaskan king crab dumplings, and scallop rice flour rolls with cordyceps flowers are nothing short of ingenious. The set lunch can be ordered individually with a vegan option.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16245;Chesa;;Hong Kong;1F, The Peninsula Hotel, 22 Salisbury Road, Tsim Sha Tsui, Hong Kong;22.2952504;114.1718282;26;true;false;Swiss;Even since opening as a ‘pop-up’ restaurant created by the Swiss-born manager back in 1965, Chesa has been the go-to place in town for those wanting authentic Swiss cuisine. The Alpine chalet-style décor more than compensates for the room’s lack of windows, while the menu covers all bases, offering fondue, raclette and the famous Chemin de Fer wines. You can even specify how strong you want the brandy taste to be in your fondue.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16246;Involtini;;Hong Kong;11F, The L. Square, 459-461 Lockhart Road, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong;22.280235;114.1816;33;false;true;Italian;The young chef, an alumnus of Otto e Mezzo, attracts a loyal following with his fresh pasta, handmade in-house daily. Italian eggs and flour are used in the dough which is rested overnight to give it a lovely al dente texture. The signature tagliolini with springy carabineros red prawns boasts a rich sauce loaded with seafood flavours. The pasta menu is updated from time to time to keep it fresh and reflect what’s in season.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16247;Yuè (Causeway Bay);;Hong Kong;Shop 1301, Food Forum, Time Square, 1 Matheson Street, Causeway Bay, Hong Kong, Hong Kong SAR China;22.2783509;114.182082;53;false;false;Cantonese;Having worked in some prestigious kitchens in Japan and Macau for over 40 years, the chef designed a menu of refined Cantonese dishes using top-notch ingredients from around the world, such as Alaskan king crab, Japanese chillies and Taiwanese bird’s-nest fern. The classic sweet and sour pork is given a new spin with aged vinegar and dried plums, plus an option of plant-based ‘meat’. Private rooms in various sizes are perfect for parties.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16248;Manuel Cozinha Portuguesa;;Macau;90 Rua de Femão Mendes Pinto, Taipa, Macau;22.1561882;113.5595445;84;true;true;Portuguese;After a spot of renovation for cosier feel, authenticity and hospitality remain the establishment’s hallmark. The friendly owner-chef has revamped the traditional Portuguese menu, now arranged by key ingredient. Using only top-notch seasonal produce, most dishes are barbecued traditionally. Grilled codfish and fried rice with squid ink are the must-tries. Check out the daily specials on the blackboard before ordering.;Air conditioning;[]
16249;The Merchants;;Hong Kong;43-45F, Forty-Five, Gloucester Tower, Landmark, 15 Queen's Road Central, Central, Hong Kong;22.2815663;114.1577663;80;true;false;Shanghainese;The top three floors of a prestigious office tower in Central have been remodelled into a swanky restaurant with drop-dead harbour views. Green velvet is a prominent feature, with contrasting splashes of orange on the semi-circular banquettes. Well-crafted traditional Shanghainese and Jiangzhe classics like braised wheat gluten, sautéed “dragon beard” shredded mandarin fish, pan-fried eight-treasure rice, and braised Chinese ham in osmanthus honey.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
16251;Hong Kong Cuisine;;Hong Kong;1F, Elegance Court, 2-4 Tsoi Tak Street, Happy Valley, Hong Kong;22.2695463;114.1857129;31;false;true;Chinese Contemporary;This upstairs restaurant was rebranded and remodelled in 2022. Chef Li started cooking professionally in the UK at the age of 16 and his dishes are rooted in Chinese traditions, but underpinned by modern French techniques and novel food combinations. He has an affinity for perfumed oils and the use of fried tofu and pork rind in caramelised sweet and sour Iberico pork is ingenious. His aromatic smoked soy sauce chicken is also unmissable.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16252;Mâm Amis;;Hong Kong;Shop A & B, GF, Fu Fai Commercial Centre, 27 Hillier Street, Sheung Wan, Hong Kong;22.285118;114.1511841;76;false;true;Vietnamese;The smart wood panelled front contrasts sharply with the distressed walls, vintage lamps and hanging greenery inside. Vietnamese chefs are keen on bringing authentic Vietnamese food to Hong Kong, with chargrilled items and phở among the highlights. Try the chargrilled river prawns that boast bouncy, briny-sweet flesh and exceptional smokiness. Phở comes in generous portions with a flavour-packed soup base.;;[]
16253;Don Alfonso 1890;;Macau;Shop 307, 3F, Palazzo Versace, Grand Lisboa Palace Resort, Rua do Tiro, Cotai, Macau;22.1435736;113.5732844;62;false;false;Italian;This family-owned haute cuisine brand from Italy opened this high-end outpost in Macau. Versace may have taken care of the design, but the fashion house's signature glamour doesn't outshine the food. The kitchen excels at delivering vibrant flavours from the Amalfi Coast, using fresh produce from the family's own organic farm – try the handmade tagliolini with scampi and white truffle. Ask the sommelier for help navigating the long wine list.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16254;Blind;Portugal;Porto;Rua de Entreparedes 40, Porto, 4000-197, Portugal;41.1451049;-8.6060592;33;false;false;Creative;This is one of those places where you don’t just come to eat, but where you’ll find quality ingredients, impressive flavours and solid technique as part of a gastronomic experience that touches the emotions. This is showcased in its homage to José Saramago’s novel “Blindness” and a philosophy built around three concepts (to feel, to touch and to provoke) that play with the senses. Part of the Torel Palace Hotel but with its own separate entrance, this restaurant is overseen by chef Vítor Matos and impressively run day to day by young chef Rita Magro. Here, the cuisine is based around a serious, common sense yet fun approach (some of the dishes are served “blind” to guests), with a desire to demonstrate a high level of cooking and to create an element of surprise in terms of technique, with presentation and flavour always to the fore. This is showcased on a single surprise tasting menu entitled Blind Emotions, with a choice of two different options (10 or 12 “moments”).;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16255;Drogaria;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Joaquim Casimiro 8, Lisbon, 1200-696, Portugal;38.7052888;-9.1671892;74;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;This restaurant, with its small entrance, is located on the exact spot of the erstwhile Drogaria do Sr. Albino (hence the name) in the busy Lapa district. Its retro ambience, featuring marble tables, various mirrors dotted around the two dining rooms and a checkered floor (all of which provide added personality) is in perfect harmony with a modern and sophisticated decor. The menu here is based around classic Portuguese dishes, albeit with a contemporary flair. Iconic dishes such as cod croquettes, “bacalhau à bras”, roast suckling pig, and rice pudding are all attractively presented and full of surprising textures. The delightful atmosphere on the charming outdoor terrace comes into its own on a summer evening!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16256;Quinta do Tedo Familia Geadas;Portugal;Folgosa;Quinta do Tedo N222 M512, Folgosa, 5110 204, Portugal;41.1568493;-7.6404927;86;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;If you’re looking for somewhere with good food and stunning views, this is the perfect place. Part of the quinta of the same name, at the confluence of the Douro and Tagus rivers, the restaurant boasts a welcoming ambience and extensive windows to maximise views of the spectacular landscapes here. It is run by the Geadas brothers (chef Óscar Geadas and sommelier António Geadas), who are known for the success of their restaurant in the north of the country. The focus is on the culinary traditions of the Trás-os-Montes region, which is reflected in deliciously fresh fish dishes and perfectly prepared meats. Make sure you save space for the sublime desserts!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16257;Casa do Gadanha;Portugal;Estremoz;Rua da Vasco da Gama 4, Estremoz, 7100-559, Portugal;38.8418766;-7.588567;42;true;true;Contemporary;A restaurant with a cosy, intimate feel featuring warm, bright colours. It is located in the historic centre of Estremoz, better known as the “white town” as a result of its famous marble. The kitchen is visible from the dining room, enabling guests to watch the preparation process in full flow. The cuisine here is centred around dishes for sharing and two tasting menus (6 or 8 “moments”). An added bonus is the artisanal home-made dough used for the bread and pizzas.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16258;Romando;Portugal;Árvore;Rua da Fonte 221, Árvore, 4480-068, Portugal;41.33316;-8.722646;58;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located in a district on the outskirts of Areia, Romando has a single modern - style dining room. The emphasis is firmly on traditional Portuguese cuisine, including a good selection of savoury rice dishes and a few seafood options.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16259;Bomfim 1896 with Pedro Lemos;Portugal;Pinhão;Quinta do Bomfim, Pinhão, 5085-060, Portugal;41.189216;-7.5404832;23;true;false;Contemporary;At the Quinta do Bomfim, an estate run by the Symington family since 1896 (hence the name of the restaurant), this project is a partnership with renowned chef Pedro Lemos. Situated on the banks of the River Douro, it boasts a classic and sophisticated ambience, plus a completely open dining room with a view of the kitchen, and superb vistas through the large picture windows. The fireplace and wood-fired oven take centre stage here, alongside cuisine that revisits the flavours of the Douro Valley’s time-honoured kitchens, albeit with a more contemporary vision.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16260;Cisco - Cozinha Tradicional;Portugal;Almeirim;Rua De Coruche 121A, Almeirim, 2080-094, Portugal;39.2045313;-8.6290866;79;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Portuguese;This restaurant is located in Almeirim, in a region renowned for its famous “sopa da Pedra”, a soup which understandably makes an appearance on the menu. However, you’ll also find lots of other options here, such as the “cozido à portuguesa” stew, the mouthwatering rice with veal cheek, the traditional “bacalhau à brás” and, for dessert, the classic “leite-creme”, and grandma Mariazinha’s almond pudding, both of which provide a fitting end to your meal. If you enjoy high-quality traditional and home-style cooking this is definitely the place, thanks to chef Alexandre Albergaria Diniz use of fresh ingredients to create authentic dishes without unnecessary frills, as well as daily specials, in a welcoming, traditional space run by an excellent team.;Air conditioning;[]
16261;Raiva;Portugal;Raiva;Estrada Nacional 222, Km 41, Raiva, 4550-631, Portugal;41.0382903;-8.3511142;81;true;false;Modern Cuisine;(Temporarily closed for refurbishment) This restaurant takes its name from the parish in which it is located along the banks of the Douro, from where it enjoys superb views. Following his return to Portugal having worked in leading restaurants abroad, chef Dárcio Henriques embarked on this project, which sees him working with ingredients sourced from the length and breadth of the Douro. The cuisine here is showcased on à la carte and two tastings menus (one of which is vegetarian), and includes dishes such as Wild mushrooms and DOP terrincho tortellini or Arouquesa Vazia with smoked celery and soufflé potatoes. The perfect place to unwind, given its setting in a delightful hotel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16262;Essencial;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua da Rosa 176, Lisbon, 1200-390, Portugal;38.7138831;-9.1455979;17;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This small restaurant, located on a narrow street in the bustling Bairro Alto district, features a completely open-view kitchen in the centre of the dining room, plus a minimalist decor of neutral tones. Influenced by his experiences in international restaurants, chef André Lança Cordeiro combines French techniques with seasonal Portuguese ingredients. Dishes such as the famous pâté en croûte with different fillings, the vol-au-vent of lobster and sweetbreads, and the pistachio and yuzu Paris-Brest take guests on a gastronomic flight of fancy to France without having to leave Lisbon! Options here include the Bistrot menu, with one starter, a main course, and a dessert, and the Amuse-Bouches tasting menu, accompanied by an interesting wine pairing.;Air conditioning;[]
16263;Salão Nobre;Portugal;Vidago;Parque de Vidago, Vidago, 5425-307, Portugal;41.6328757;-7.575402;31;false;false;Contemporary;A spacious, elegant restaurant occupying the large ballroom of a former palace. Contemporary cuisine that features a few vegetarian dishes as well as tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Valet parking;[]
16264;Fogo;Portugal;Lisbon;Avenida Elias Garcia 57, Lisbon, 1049-017, Portugal;38.7393023;-9.145645;26;false;false;Grills;Those who are familiar with chef Alexandre Silva’s cuisine will know all about the excellence and quality that you’ll always find at Fogo. As soon as you walk through the door you’ll sense the true essence of its cooking aided, of course, by a name (“fogo” is the Portuguese word for “fire”) that speaks for itself, as well as the delicious aromas and intense energy from the open grill. Every dish is meticulously prepared on it, from the starters (such as the enticing grilled oysters) and the freshest of fish sourced directly from the auction to the mouthwatering beef sirloin – not forgetting the undoubted house speciality, the traditional baked rice. Make sure you also cast your eye over the truly spectacular cocktail list.;Air conditioning;[]
16265;Oficina;Portugal;Porto;Rua de Miguel Bombarda 282, Porto, 4050-377, Portugal;41.1497992;-8.6201416;72;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Oficina combines an industrial atmosphere with the world of the avant-garde, given its location in an area full of art galleries. Traditional cuisine with a modern twist.;Air conditioning;[]
16266;Pequeno Mundo;Portugal;Almancil;Caminho de Pereiras, Almancil, 8135-907, Portugal;37.0912102;-8.0505531;25;true;false;International;The perfect venue for an intimate supper. Its setting is in a typical Algarve - style house with romantic patios and warm and welcoming dining rooms. International menu showing clear French influence.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16267;Terroir;Portugal;Lisbon;Avenida Duque De Loulé 86A, Lisbon, 1050-090, Portugal;38.72732;-9.14645;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant with a contemporary and somewhat relaxed feel where the focus is on strong technique and seasonal Portuguese ingredients. Surprise tasting menus are also available.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16268;Sem Porta;Portugal;Comporta;EN 261-1, CCI 3954, Muda, Comporta, 7570-337, Portugal;38.2886746;-8.7121804;77;false;true;Contemporary;Sem Porta is located inside the main building of the superb Hotel Sublime Comporta, in a glass-fronted space boasting a decor of wood and neutral colours. The focus here is on Portuguese cooking that features fresh ingredients sourced daily from its own garden or from local producers. This is showcased on a single 5-“moment” tasting menu or the à la carte, which includes fish starters such as smoked eel on a delicate potato foam, and main courses such as sea turbot with creamy rice, and Iberian pork “presa” with a smooth smoked celery purée.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16269;Alambique;Portugal;Almancil;Estrada de Vale do Lobo a Quinta do Lago, Almancil, 8135-160, Portugal;37.0619977;-8.046278;42;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A fine exponent of traditional Portuguese cuisine, featuring delicious grilled fish and specialities such as fish cataplana. Idyllic terraces surrounded by vegetation add to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16270;Tasca do Zé Tuga;Portugal;Bragança;Rua da Igreja 66, Bragança, 5300-025, Portugal;41.8034835;-6.7485414;64;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A superb location within the walls of the old town, with a terrace boasting superb views of the castle. Traditionally inspired cuisine with plenty of personal touches.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16271;Turismo;Portugal;Barcelos;Rua Duques de Bragança, Barcelos, 4750-272, Portugal;41.52872;-8.6233;98;true;true;Regional Cuisine;This restaurant, with its impressive statue of a Barcelos cockerel by the entrance, stands out for its modern architecture in the heart of this historic town, a location close to all of Barcelos’ main tourist sights, and its impressive views of the river. It is divided into three elegantly decorated dining rooms with a glass-fronted wine cellar at the heart of everything, but it is the energy of the team here that is particularly impressive. The menu follows traditional lines with a few contemporary touches in dishes such as the sautéed alheira with apple purée, the grilled octopus with potato crumble, and the “priscos” pudding with tangerine and a citrus sorbet, none of which will disappoint.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16272;Taberna d'Adélia;Portugal;Nazaré;Rua das Traineras 12, Nazaré, 2450-196, Portugal;39.5978991;-9.071555;38;true;false;Seafood;A pleasantly colourful taberna with a rustic feel just a few steps from the beach. The high-quality fish and seafood on the traditionally inspired menu is particularly impressive.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16273;Grenache;Portugal;Lisbon;Pátio de Dom Fradique 12, Lisbon, 1100-624, Portugal;38.7124025;-9.13165;28;false;true;French Contemporary;If you’re keen to take your tastebuds on a gastronomic odyssey across France, this delightful, intimate restaurant with a charming outdoor terrace in the heart of the Alfama could be the place for you. It is run by chef Philippe Gelfi who, ever loyal to his origins, offers cuisine rooted in French tradition but with a contemporary touch and a focus on seasonal Portuguese ingredients on a choice of two tasting menus: Grenache and Experience. Unusual details include petits-fours served on a bed of coffee beans, with their enticing aromas from countries as diverse as Angola, Ethiopia, Brazil and Costa Rica.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16274;Terra;Portugal;Porto;Rua do Padrão 103, Porto, 4150-559, Portugal;41.1567373;-8.6796962;37;true;true;Asian Influences;Behind the somewhat surprising façade is a sushi bar, plus a neo-rustic-style dining room with a designer feel upstairs. Extensive à la carte menu with a nod to Asian cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16275;Herdade dos Grous;Portugal;Albernoa;Herdade dos Grous, Albernoa, 7800-601, Portugal;37.879376;-7.940977;99;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A good option for discovering the essence of the Alentejo, given its location on a charming quinta surrounded by trees and vineyards (it also has two dozen guestrooms), with access via a private road that is well signposted from the village. Here, the focus is on traditional cooking with plenty of personality thanks to the use of organic ingredients grown on the estate or from meat from its own livestock (Alentejo veal, merino lamb, Iberian pork etc). A choice of wine-tasting options is also available, ranging from three wines on the Basic package to six, including tapas, for those booking the Flight pairing.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16277;Mercearia Gadanha;Portugal;Estremoz;Largo dos Dragões de Olivença 84, Estremoz, 7100-457, Portugal;38.8442955;-7.5883013;95;false;false;Regional Cuisine;This centrally located restaurant with a welcoming feel comes as something of a surprise, as it is accessed via a bar- gourmet shop that has the feel of an authentic grocery store. In the rustic-contemporary dining room, featuring exposed wood beams and even a table for two in the fireplace, choose from an extensive menu combining regionally inspired dishes (crispy prawns, scrambled eggs, different black pork recipes) with those with a more international feel, all of which are prepared with a subtle, modern touch. Cheese, sausages and wine from the Estremoz area are available for purchase in the boutique.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16278;Casa da Dízima;Portugal;Paço de Arcos;Rua Costa Pinto 17, Paço de Arcos, 2770-046, Portugal;38.6956249;-9.2900245;22;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant owes its name to the history of the building, which was once used to collect taxes. There are several dining rooms, most of which are rustic yet contemporary in appearance. The modern cooking is based around traditional Portuguese and international fare.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16279;Aladin Grill;Portugal;Porches;Rua Anneliese Pohl, Porches, 8400-450, Portugal;37.10253;-8.38141;72;true;false;International, Grills;Part of the Vila Vita hotel, where the Moroccan-inspired decor is reminiscent of the Arabian Nights! Oriental flavours, aged Galician meats and Portuguese fish all feature on the menu, with many dishes cooked on the grill.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16280;Prado;Portugal;Lisbon;Travessa Das Pedras Negras 2, Lisbon, 1100-404, Portugal;38.7105326;-9.1349192;75;true;true;Farm to table;When a restaurant adopts the “farm-to-table” principle, it’s easy to imagine what this entails, namely fresh, seasonal dishes prepared with local ingredients. What is even better is that every time you visit you’ll find new suggestions on the menu that are always skilfully prepared and full of flavour. At the helm in this setting full of natural light and decorated with lots of plants that add a touch of freshness is chef Antonio Galapito, who emphasises the important of small-scale producers and allows the seasons to guide him in the creation of his dishes. In the evening, the attractive tasting menu (as well as the à la carte available at all sittings) showcases all of the chef’s culinary skill. We can also recommend the organic wines that are part of the wine-pairing option.;Air conditioning;[]
16281;BAHR;Portugal;Lisbon;Praça Luís De Camões 2, Lisbon, 1200-243, Portugal;38.7103906;-9.1432259;35;false;true;Portuguese;Located on the top floor of the Bairro Alto Hotel (hence the origin of its name) and featuring a kitchen that opens onto the dining room, BAHR describes itself as a “bohemian and irreverent space”. At lunchtime it offers a much more informal market-inspired “executive menu”, with more elaborate, exclusively à la carte dishes in the evening, but all featuring the very best ingredients.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16282;O Talho;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Carlos Testa 1, Lisbon, 1050-046, Portugal;38.7333598;-9.1527439;83;true;true;Meats and Grills;Entering a restaurant through a butcher’s shop (“talho” in Portuguese) provides a clue as to the focus here and is a guarantee that the meat quality will be high and that it comes directly from the source! And it is in this modern yet at the same time informal space that chef Kiko offers his unique cuisine to guests through superb dishes prepared in an exceptional way. Meat-lovers can savour irresistible choices such as picanha from Uruguay, Galician 60-day dry aged T-bone, and A5 Kobe flank, considered one of the world’s best cuts of meat. Meat can also be purchased to be cooked at home.;Air conditioning;[]
16283;Solar dos Nunes;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua dos Lusíadas 68-72, Lisbon, 1300-372, Portugal;38.7053894;-9.1805237;100;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A renowned family-run restaurant which opened its doors in 1988 and has retained the essence of an old-style eatery serving traditional Portuguese cooking. To a backdrop of typical decor, including photos of famous faces who have eaten here, you’ll find an extensive menu that showcases the flavours of the Alentejo region, including an impressive selection of sausages and cured meats (such as the Jamón Ibérico Joselito Gran Reserva), daily specials, and game dishes in season. Don’t miss the fish soup, the Alentejo-style garlic “açorda” with cod, or “grandma’s dogfish soup”.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16284;Tia Alice;Portugal;Fátima;Avenida Irmã Lúcia de Jesus 152, Fátima, 2495-557, Portugal;39.6178345;-8.653409;38;false;true;Portuguese;A family-run restaurant that has been tastefully brought up to date. The dining rooms are complemented by an attractive shop selling household items, as well as a delightful garden. Delicious traditional cuisine!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16286;NUMA;Portugal;Portimao;Av. Miguel Bombarda 17, Portimao, 8500 299, Portugal;37.1335725;-8.5415936;80;true;true;Contemporary;NUMA is a combination of the names of the two owners: Nuno Martins (chef) and Manuela João (front of house manager), who followed a "family dream" in opening their own dining space. Situated along a busy avenue in a residential district, it boasts a refined ambience, with plenty of wood decor and warm tones that combine to create a welcoming feel. The cuisine is centred around local and Portuguese ingredients and a contemporary vision which is showcased on two tasting menus (NUMA and Estação) and an à la carte. Make sure you order NUMA’s two signature dishes: the Carabineiro red prawns and the sirloin steak.;Air conditioning;[]
16287;Marlene,;Portugal;Lisbon;Avenida Infante D. Henrique. Doca do Jardim do Tabaco, Lisbon, 1100-651, Portugal;38.7120612;-9.1240727;40;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A contemporary gastronomic restaurant adjoining the Zunzum Gastrobar, both of which occupy a completely glass-fronted building. A standout feature here is the large central kitchen, surrounded by a counter from where guests can watch the chefs at work. Innovative cuisine from Portugal and further afield, which is only available on two unique tasting menus.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16288;O Palco;Portugal;Coimbra;Avenida Dom Afonso Henriques, Coimbra, 3000-011, Portugal;40.2100933;-8.4146586;100;false;true;Contemporary;The aim here is to bring to the stage (“palco” in Portuguese) all those involved in this culinary project, from producers and their ingredients to the owners themselves, namely chef Marco Almeida and front-of-house manager Ana Almeida. Everything here revolves around the freshness and local provenance of its ingredients. Thanks to the restaurant’s zero-miles philosophy, the majority of these are sourced from local suppliers within a radius of 100km of Coimbra, as is highlighted (the producer’s name and the distance) alongside each dish. Menus are divided into Acts I, II and III, on which you can choose five, seven or ten “scenes”, alongside a vegetarian menu.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16289;fago;Portugal;Marvão;Travessa da Praça 2A, Marvão, 7330-124, Portugal;39.3944099;-7.3760821;39;false;true;Contemporary;This restaurant is situated in Marvão, a village at the highest point of the Serra de São Mamede, just a few kilometres from the Spanish border. It occupies a small house that has been completely remodelled by Diogo Branco, a chef from Porto, and Daniel Boto, a native of this region. The concise à la carte here changes constantly according to the seasons and availability from local producers. Three main dishes are always available: one vegetarian, one meat, and one fish or seafood.;Air conditioning;[]
16292;Elemento;Portugal;Porto;Rua do Almada 51, Porto, 4050-036, Portugal;41.1465149;-8.6122347;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Grills;Chef Ricardo Dias Ferreira has unashamedly gone back to basics here, cooking exclusively over wood, to such an extent that he rarely uses the grill or oven. With his combination of traditional Portuguese cuisine, smoky flavours and modern touches, he offers à la carte options alongside an “8-moment” tasting menu, and his cuisine varies from day to day depending on the availability of ingredients from small-scale local producers. Allow yourself to be guided by recommendations from the interesting selection of Portuguese wines, and if you’re keen to enjoy the experience to the full, take a seat at the counter in front of the kitchen so you can watch the chefs in action at close quarters.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
16293;Sabores d'Itália;Portugal;Caldas da Rainha;Praça 5 de Outubro 40, Caldas da Rainha, 2500-111, Portugal;39.4035971;-9.1364633;29;false;true;Italian;A sober façade conceals this attractive restaurant with two modern dining rooms. The predominantly Italian menu is enhanced by a few Portuguese dishes.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16294;Dona Júlia;Portugal;Braga;Falperra, Braga, 4715-390, Portugal;41.5209801;-8.3892235;47;false;false;Regional Cuisine;A restaurant striking for its modern interior design, traditional cuisine with a strong Minho flavour and a pleasant ambience in which to enjoy its abundant dishes. These are centred on a vast selection of fully certified meats, many from the restaurant’s own estate, as well as fish and seafood direct from the auction.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16295;Boubou's;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua do Monte Olivete 32 A, Lisbon, 1200-280, Portugal;38.7171311;-9.1507607;76;false;false;Modern Cuisine, International;A welcoming restaurant next to the Museu Nacional de História Natural e da Ciência which became famous when its chef, Louise Bourrat, won the French version of Top Chef in 2022! The young international team (between them they speak seven languages) creates modern, globally inspired cuisine featuring delicate textures that exude femininity, and which is available (for dinner only) on two tasting menus: Omnivorus and the vegetarian Terra. One dish that we particularly enjoyed was the sweet potato ceviche with pomegranate, coconut and kaffir lime.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16296;Ferrugem;Portugal;Portela;Rua das Pedrinhas 32, Portela, 4770-379, Portugal;41.46184;-8.44801;99;true;false;Contemporary;A particularly attractive restaurant occupying an old barn. In the dining room, with its high ceilings and rustic - modern ambience, discover contemporary cooking with a creative flair.;Air conditioning;[]
16297;CHECKin by Leonel Pereira;Portugal;Faro;Rua do Castelo 7, Faro, 8000-243, Portugal;37.0123583;-7.9342854;84;true;false;Contemporary;This charming restaurant occupies a former cereal and wine storehouse which has been completely remodelled in Faro’s historic centre. The cooking of chef Leonel Pereira, a native of the Algarve, is based around seasonal ingredients with a strong focus on creativity and flavour. The menu is divided into different sections: Check-in, Cozinhados no Tacho, Momentos Especiais and Check-out. Make sure you try the cheesecake with strawberries, lime, meringue and tangerine peel ice-cream.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16298;Avenida;Portugal;Lagos;Avenida dos Descobrimentos 53, Lagos, 8600-645, Portugal;37.1075518;-8.6752408;27;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The old adage that talent runs in the family is particularly appropriate here! Dutch chef Roeland Klein’s passion for cooking came from his father, a chef in a one-Michelin-star restaurant in his native country. Located within the walls of the Hotel Avenida, opposite Lagos marina, the restaurant features an open kitchen where guests can sit at the counter to watch and interact with the chef as he prepares his dishes. Choose between the tasting menu and à la carte, both offering a variety of fish and seafood, although the aged meats sourced from the renowned El Capricho by José Gordón are worthy of special mention.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16299;Dos Artistas;Portugal;Lagos;Rua Cândido dos Reis 68, Lagos, 8600-681, Portugal;37.100882;-8.6731582;54;true;false;International;A restaurant with a pleasant terrace and a dining room with a classic-colonial-style decor. Internationally inspired cooking including à la carte and set menu options, with a more extensive choice on offer in the evening.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16300;2 Passos;Portugal;Almancil;Praia do Ancão, Almancil, 8135-170, Portugal;37.0348278;-8.0401648;85;true;false;Seafood;A modern construction with lots of charm located on Ancão beach, a beautiful setting with protected status. Traditional Portuguese cuisine specialising in fish and seafood.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16301;Alameda;Portugal;Faro;Rua da Polícia da Segurança Pública 10, Faro, 8000-151, Portugal;37.0158521;-7.9285322;81;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant pays a genuine homage to the Algarve region through its name (from the town’s famous park) and the dishes featuring on the menu. Chef Rui Sequeira, who has returned to his native area having worked in prestigious restaurants elsewhere, creates innovative cuisine that combine modern technique and traditional roots. The tasting menu, entitled “Love beyond time: A journey through the tales of the Algarve”, tells a story from the region in every dish, and is complemented by dishes from the à la carte. The sophisticated and contemporary ambience also includes a charming glass-enclosed terrace on the street.;Terrace;[]
16302;Salpoente;Portugal;Aveiro;Cais de São Roque 83, Aveiro, 3800-256, Portugal;40.6468366;-8.6514174;39;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This restaurant is located along the São Roque canal in a building once used as a salt warehouse. Contemporary cuisine with an innovative touch, to a backdrop that features designer details.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16304;Rei dos Leitões;Portugal;Mealhada;Avenida da Restauração 17, Mealhada, 3050 -382, Portugal;40.3900732;-8.4507087;37;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In a region renowned for its roast suckling pig (as well as the production of sparkling wine), this is one of many restaurants in the area specialising in this popular dish. Occupying a charming house along an avenue in town, this longstanding eatery definitely lives up to its name (The King of Suckling Pig)! The recipe and preparation of the pork follow tradition to the letter and we recommend that you accompany the dish with a glass of excellent local sparkling wine. Fish, matured meats and rice dishes also feature on the menu – all prepared with top-quality ingredients and lots of flavour. A superb wine selection completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16305;S. Gião;Portugal;Moreira de Cónegos;Rua Comendador Joaquim Almeida Freitas 56, Moreira de Cónegos, 4815-270, Portugal;41.3801444;-8.3553803;79;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A space that symbolises authentic Portuguese cuisine, enhanced by well-conceived dishes and excellent service. Occupying a house with plenty of charm on the outskirts of Guimarães, and more specifically in Moreira de Cónegos, it features surprising aspects such as the central fireplace and superb views towards the Moreirense stadium and the surrounding vineyards. The cuisine, which is influenced by the north of Portugal but with an added touch of international flair, features generous portions and dishes prepared with top-quality ingredients on a menu that is constantly updated.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16306;dop;Portugal;Porto;Largo de São Domingos 16, Porto, 4050-545, Portugal;41.142819;-8.6146931;48;true;true;Contemporary;Occupying an historic building, this restaurant boasts contemporary dining rooms on two floors where guests can enjoy high - quality traditional cooking. Superb cellar of Portuguese and international wines.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16307;Cantinho do Avillez;Portugal;Porto;Rua Mouzinho da Silveira 166, Porto, 4050-416, Portugal;41.1431315;-8.6135199;86;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This is media - friendly chef José Avillez’s first venture outside of Lisbon. The urban bistro look and reasonably priced contemporary menu ensure that it is always full.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16308;Cais da Villa;Portugal;Vila Real;Rua Monsenhor Jerónimo do Amaral, Vila Real, 5000-570, Portugal;41.2936688;-7.7399346;31;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Cais da Vila has added fresh impetus to the local restaurant scene. Traditional cooking is to the fore here, showcased by classic recipes such as the cataplana of grouper, squid and shrimp. Excellent meat from the Trás-os-Montes region also features heavily on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16309;Dom Joaquim;Portugal;Évora;Rua dos Penedos 6, Évora, 7000-531, Portugal;38.5708721;-7.9145034;87;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Dom Joaquim is located next to the Porta de Serpa Pinto, one of the access gates to the historic centre of Évora. The stylish, classic-contemporary ambience here features bare stone walls and a series of hanging sculptures that add a welcoming feel. Chef Joaquim Almeida bases his cuisine on traditional Alentejo cooking with a modern touch. On the menu you’ll find daily specials, traditional and local dishes, plus a selection of “convent”-style pastries and desserts. Make sure you try the “auga de prata” pudding, the recipe for which originates from the Convento de Santa Clara, just a few metres away.;Air conditioning;[]
16310;Go Juu;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Marquês Sá da Bandeira 46A, Lisbon, 1050-149, Portugal;38.7357227;-9.1522175;61;true;true;Japanese;Enjoy authentic Japanese cooking in this unique, almost minimalist space featuring a profusion of wood and a sushi bar in the dining room. There’s also an exclusive area for Go Juu’s club members.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
16311;O Leão de Porches;Portugal;Porches;Rua Padre António Gregório A Cabrita 8, Porches, 8400-473, Portugal;37.1259021;-8.3983335;15;true;false;International;A romantic, rural restaurant with plenty of charisma! Choose between the tasting menu and an internationally inspired à la carte with different influences (Portuguese, French, Italian, Asian etc).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16312;Horta;Portugal;Funchal;Rua De Leichlingen 11, Funchal, 9004-566, Portugal;32.6366714;-16.9337438;54;true;true;Vegetarian;This restaurant is more than just the gastronomic showcase of the renowned PortoBay group. Here, the stars of the show are the vegetables and plants used to create its healthy and well-balanced dishes. Ingredients are sourced from its own kitchen-garden (“horta” in Portuguese) or from growers around the island. On the menus, standout vegetable-based dishes include the delicious home-grown roast pepper and carrot hummus. Fish and meat options also feature, such as the tasty scabbard fillet with a mussel nage, plus a new, head-turning version of Crema Catalana served with fruit grown in Horta’s kitchen-garden.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16313;Gastro by Elemento;Portugal;Porto;Rua Maria Adelaide Freitas Gonçalves 13, Porto, 4350-109, Portugal;41.163955;-8.58823;16;false;false;Grills, Contemporary;Chef Ricardo Dias Ferreira focuses on time-honoured cuisine in which the wood fire takes on a starring role. Here, everything is cooked on a wood grill or in a wood-fired oven, hence the distinctive and special flavour evident in each dish. The restaurant has an industrial feel that includes an elegantly decorated and welcoming dining room, but why not sit at the bar-counter in front of the kitchen, where you’ll experience the full preparation process and the aromas emanating from the grill and oven. The offer is based around a single tasting menu, made up of ten moments and changes with the products available each season.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16314;Origens;Portugal;Évora;Rua de Burgos 10, Évora, 7000-863, Portugal;38.5714634;-7.9087398;31;true;false;Contemporary;Somewhat hidden down a narrow street, Origens is a worthwhile choice given its location in the heart of Évora’s historic centre, where you can savour contemporary Alentejo cuisine prepared with sophisticated modern techniques. The menu is updated several times a year to ensure that the ingredients used are as fresh and seasonal as possible. One dish has been a mainstay since the restaurant first opened: “brás à farinheira”, made with smoked sausage. There’s also a surprise wine pairing option.;Air conditioning;[]
16315;À Mesa;Portugal;Tavira;R. Álvaro de Campos 14, Tavira, 8800-320, Portugal;37.12859;-7.6497412;87;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;À Mesa is situated next to the charming 17C São Paulo church, on the ground floor of a small boutique hotel but with its own private entrance. The tasteful dining room features stone walls and a section of glass floor through which the wine cellar is visible as a reminder of the property’s history. The menu was created by chef João Dias, whose partner is chef Luís Brito (A Ver Tavira). Choose between the à la carte and three tasting menus (Viagem pelo Atlântico, Iguarias que rimam and Terra e mar). The charming terrace comes into its own in summer!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16316;Âmago;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua da Alegria 41C, Lisbon, 1250-182, Portugal;38.7176011;-9.1473944;64;false;true;Farm to table, Contemporary;A unique and intimate restaurant with an informal ambience where the single surprise menu is only served to a maximum of ten guests all seated at the same table. The highly technical cuisine here changes according to the seasons produce and ingredients available in the market. Booking ahead is essential.;Air conditioning;[]
16317;Downunder by Justin Jennings;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua Dos Industriais 21, Lisbon, 1200-685, Portugal;38.7104569;-9.1540085;96;true;true;Australian Contemporary;If you’ve never eaten crocodile or kangaroo, now is your chance in this unpretentious restaurant run by a young Australian chef who fell in love with Lisbon and set up his own business here. His somewhat unusual cuisine, available on an à la carte and two set menus, shines a light on Australian cuisine and its exotic meats.;Air conditioning;[]
16318;Noélia;Portugal;Cabanas;Rua da Fortaleza - Edifício Cabanas Mar Loja 6A, Cabanas, 8800-595, Portugal;37.1372121;-7.5948562;32;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Nicknamed the Queen of Ria Formosa, chef Noélia, whose restaurant bears her name, is a well-known celebrity across Portugal. This passionate, self-taught cook is always seeking to create new recipes and experiment with new combinations. Her recipes are based around locally caught fish and seafood that feature on a fixed menu, although there are always a variety of choices that focus on the day’s freshest ingredients. We recommended booking ahead as it is always full.;Air conditioning;[]
16319;MA;Portugal;Coimbra;Rua do Norte 13, Coimbra, 3000 295, Portugal;40.2087599;-8.426432;99;true;true;Japanese;You’ll find delicacies such as tuna with caviar, Azores squid, sea urchin, crab gunkan and John Dory, as well as mochis and macaroons to round off your meal in this intimate space just a few steps from the old cathedral (Sé Velha) in this city located along the banks of the Mondego. The wooden bar counter is where MA serves its Omakase menu, while the à la carte dining room boasts more subdued lighting and a romantic feel. The culinary experience here is overseen by chef Ricardo Casqueiro, who combines Japanese tradition with Western techniques and Portuguese ingredients. Open for dinner only.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16320;Vinha;Portugal;Vila Nova de Gaia;Rua Quinta Fonte da Vinha 383, Vila Nova de Gaia, 4430-487, Portugal;41.1318828;-8.5755239;28;true;false;Portuguese, Creative;This restaurant is part of the Vinha Boutique Hotel, a 16C manor house on the banks of the River Douro, where sophistication and elegance are key elements. Decorated with exquisite taste, it offers a menu that bears the signature of highly respected chef Henrique Sá Pessoa. The cuisine here is centred around seasonal Portuguese ingredients with an international influence which is showcased on an à la carte and a single tasting menu entitled “Identity”, on which dishes such as the “shore sea bass” and the “Alentejo pork presa” will linger long in the memory. An extraordinary experience and the perfect setting in which to relax and enjoy the hotel.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16321;Apego;Portugal;Porto;Rua de Santa Catarina 1198, Porto, 4000-457, Portugal;41.1568534;-8.6045141;53;false;false;Creative;A modest yet unique restaurant serving Franco-Portuguese cuisine which pays homage to the family roots of the female chef at the helm (her father was French and also worked as a cook). The somewhat concise à la carte is complemented by a tasting menu that is based around Apego’s signature dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
16322;Plano;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua da Bela Vista à Graça 126, Lisbon, 1170-075, Portugal;38.7196908;-9.1265564;91;false;true;Contemporary;Trás-os-Montes-born chef Vítor Adão’s roots are strongly anchored in tradition and the provenance of his ingredients. Having worked in several leading restaurants, he decided to open his own eatery where he showcases the heritage of his native region. His cooking is based around two surprise tasting menus (6 and 9 courses) that vary according to what is available from producers. Despite its simple decoration, enhanced by numerous jars of pickles to highlight the connection with the land, the overall feel here is elegant. The pleasant terrace is perfect for outdoor dining in warmer weather.;;[]
16323;A Carvalheira;Portugal;Ponte de Lima;Rua do Eido Velho 73, Ponte de Lima, 4990-620, Portugal;41.7390681;-8.561671;48;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Located at the Quinta do Eido Velho, where guests will fall in love with its beautiful rustic ambience and gardens. Traditional Portuguese cuisine including two standout dishes: cod with a cornbread crust and roasted kid.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
16324;Arkhe;Portugal;Lisbon;São Filipe Néri 14, Lisbon, 1250-227, Portugal;38.7208384;-9.1541161;30;true;false;Vegetarian, Vegan;Situated in the centre of the city, Arkhe features a discreet façade and an interior where the dominant decorative themes are open stonework and tasteful minimalism. The cuisine here is the realm of chef João Ricardo Alves who, having worked in various kitchens around the world, decided to open this new space with a focus on vegan/vegetarian cooking, accompanied by Alejandro Chávarro (sommelier and front-of-house manager), who also boasts extensive international experience. Alves’ cooking is showcased on three menus at lunchtime (but just one midweek) and two dinner menus, all of which are created using a combination of seasonal ingredients, plentiful flavour and impressive technical skill.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16325;Taberna do Lopes;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua De São Filipe Néri 23, Lisbon, 1250-225, Portugal;38.7208627;-9.1542884;58;true;false;Steakhouse;If you enjoy eating well-matured meat, this steakhouse occupying a two-storey building will definitely impress thanks to its superb-quality Portuguese meats and regionally inspired dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16326;Al Quimia;Portugal;Albufeira;Pinhal do Concelho, Albufeira, 8200-593, Portugal;37.0884795;-8.168184;86;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A restaurant in a large resort with an impeccable contemporary design and a focus on luxurious decorative detail. Painstakingly prepared cuisine showcasing high levels of technical ability.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16327;Malhadinha Nova;Portugal;Albernoa;Herdade da Malhadinha Nova, Albernoa, 7800-601, Portugal;37.8214769;-7.9769371;28;true;false;Country cooking;Despite its access via a long lane, this restaurant surrounded by stunning vineyards is clearly signposted. It occupies the ground floor of a small house which is glass-fronted throughout and boasts breathtaking views. The cuisine here bears the signature of chef Joachim Koerper and is based on Alentejo cooking with hints of international influence. We can highly recommend the local eggs, DOP-certified Malhadinha-reared merino lamb and the honey produced on the estate.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16328;Almeja;Portugal;Porto;Rua Fernandes Tomás 819, Porto, 4000-219, Portugal;41.1502618;-8.6081647;41;true;false;Contemporary;This centrally located, bistro-style eatery, impressively run by married couple João and Sofia, offers a different culinary experience in the city, showcased on a contemporary à la carte and extensive tasting menu. A relaxing terrace-garden adds to its appeal.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16329;Hool;Portugal;Guimaraes;Rua de Santa Maria, Largo da Oliveira, Guimaraes, 4800-443, Portugal;41.44309;-8.29276;92;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A visit to Guimarães offers a deep-dive into Portuguese history – a result of its historic relevance to the country and its title as “the cradle of the Portuguese nation”. Part of the Hotel da Oliveira, in the heart of the city, this dining space boasts a classic decor of stone walls and wood-beamed ceilings. The gourmet cuisine created here by head chef Vítor Matos and overseen daily by chef Liliana Moura is both innovative and focused on the country’s traditional culinary roots. This is presented on three tasting menus (À Descoberta, Raízes and Terra Mãe), alongside a choice of à la carte options.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16330;Don Sebastião;Portugal;Lagos;Rua 25 de Abril 20, Lagos, 8600-763, Portugal;37.1018513;-8.672254;54;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A pleasant and interesting option, where the cuisine is traditionally Portuguese, well presented and copious, with fresh fish presented at your table before being prepared. The impressive wine cellar features no fewer than 75 different ports.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16331;Grand Salon;Portugal;Vila Real de Santo António;Avenida da República 171, Vila Real de Santo António, 8900-203, Portugal;37.1965528;-7.4151326;20;true;false;Portuguese;A restaurant occupying one of the most emblematic buildings in town within the walls of the Grand House hotel, where you can enjoy a delightful view of the port of Vila Real de Santo António and the banks of the Guadiana river that acts as a border between Portugal and Spain. Here, a meal is akin to delving deeply into the sophisticated ambience of another era. The decor has been thoughtfully designed, with wicker tables and decorative detail in which wood is the primary resource. The cuisine here is based around ingredients from the Algarve and is showcased on a concise menu that values freshness, seasonality and minimum waste. As a fitting end to this unique experience, enjoy a classic cocktail in the elegant Grand Salon Bar, with its old-style service.;Air conditioning;[]
16332;Porto de Santa Maria;Portugal;Cascais;Praia do Guincho, Cascais, 2750-642, Portugal;38.7247414;-9.4749123;43;true;true;Seafood;This attractively renovated classic restaurant right by the beach has returned to its origins serving wild-caught fish and seafood that is as popular as ever!;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16333;A Velha;Portugal;Abrantes;Alameda De Santo António 18, Abrantes, 2200-297, Portugal;39.4636327;-8.2029976;90;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;A small yet highly authentic property with lots of mementoes of those who lived in this area in the past, a time when this restaurant was no more than a simple “tasca”. Entry is through a door reminiscent of days gone by, which gives an indication of what you’ll find inside –a space that showcases the simplicity of another era. The menu comes courtesy of award-winning chef Rodrigo Castelo, who is renowned for keeping the traditions of Portuguese cuisine alive, while always adding his own personal touch to proceedings. Dishes such as the oxtail croquettes, the “arroz de tomate” served with a fillet of sea bass, and the traditional fritter-like “velhoses” (here, they are served with salted caramel and ham), will live long in the memory.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16334;Kappo;Portugal;Cascais;Avenida Emídio Navarro 23A, Cascais, 2750-337, Portugal;38.6971584;-9.422948;83;true;true;Japanese;Named after the Japanese term “to cut and to cook”, Kappo is a restaurant with an elegance and intimate ambience that come as a pleasant surprise. At the helm here is chef Tiago Penão, who has extensive experience working in leading restaurants. His skill and his respect for his ingredients are clearly evident, as he expertly combines the traditional and contemporary in his cuisine, resulting in precise and extraordinary dishes. Alongside his team, he brings great passion to his Omakase menu, which is complemented by an array of à la carte options (nigiri, sashimi, temaki etc). The highlight of the space is the dining counter, where guests can appreciate the synchronised preparation of dishes to the full, although other dining tables are laid out around it. A unique dining experience!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
16335;Villa Cipriani;Portugal;Funchal;Estrada Monumental 139, Funchal, 9000-098, Portugal;32.6398023;-16.9252387;28;true;false;Italian;Occupying a villa at the Belmond Reid's Palace, the Villa Cipriani provides an elegant setting for Italian cuisine with superb views of the cliffs, particularly from the terrace. The professional team here is very much old school!;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16336;Cafeína;Portugal;Porto;Rua do Padrão 100, Porto, 4150-557, Portugal;41.1564893;-8.6799128;74;true;false;International;The unique azulejo covered façade leads to two elegantly contemporary dining rooms, one in the style of a library. Good menu of traditional Portuguese and international cuisine.;Air conditioning;[]
16337;34;Portugal;Guimaraes;Largo do Toural 23, Guimaraes, 4810 427, Portugal;41.4419617;-8.2953664;27;true;false;International;There are few places where you can enjoy a meal accompanied by a view teeming with history but this is definitely the case at 34. So, if you’re exploring the charming town of Guimarães, make sure you book a table on the third floor of this restaurant boasting a delightful view of Toural square and the historic São Pedro basilica. The ambience here is modern and relaxed, accompanied by a tasteful decor of different woods that are in harmony with the verdant backdrop. The menu features an array of international dishes from the fresh burrata to Japanese-inspired options such as the salmon belly, rounding off your meal, perhaps, with the refined “borrego” with chestnut purée – reasons galore to book a table here!;;[]
16338;Castas e Pratos;Portugal;Peso da Régua;Rua José Vasques Osório, Peso da Régua, 5050-280, Portugal;41.158179;-7.7838446;25;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A delightful restaurant occupying a former train station warehouse with a terrace overlooking the tracks, a wine bar and a dining room with high ceilings. Superb wine cellar!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16339;Armazém do Sal;Portugal;Funchal;Rua da Alfândega 135, Funchal, 9000-059, Portugal;32.64788;-16.9064;58;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A rustic - style property with lots of character and charm thanks to the combination of traditional wood and stone and modern art on display. A contemporary take on traditional cuisine.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16340;Suba;Portugal;Lisbon;Rua de Santa Catarina 1, Lisbon, 1200-401, Portugal;38.7097117;-9.1471823;61;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;The name (Suba translates as “climb up” in Portuguese) offers an invitation to dine at this restaurant on the top floor of the Verride Palácio Santa Catarina hotel, a palatial 18C property that has provided the aristocratic inspiration for the uniforms worn by the attentive team. Once you’ve savoured its modern and extensive Portuguese-style cuisine (á la carte, including vegetarian options, and as many as five menus), head up to the panoramic rooftop with its stunning 360° views of Lisbon. Children under 12 are not permitted in the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16341;Willie's;Portugal;Vilamoura;Rua do Brasil 2, Vilamoura, 8125-479, Portugal;37.0942395;-8.108369;15;false;true;International;Located in a popular tourist area where the focus is very much on golf! In the welcoming dining room, enjoy classic, attractively presented cuisine aimed at an international clientele.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16342;Marinheiro;Portugal;Póvoa de Varzim;Rua Gomes de Amorim 1842, Póvoa de Varzim, 4490-091, Portugal;41.3982949;-8.7665853;18;true;false;Seafood;A ship run aground is the setting of this imaginative restaurant on two levels. Charming nautical décor and a varied menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
16343;Petiscas;Portugal;Ponte de Lima;Largo da Alegria, Ponte de Lima, 4990-240, Portugal;41.7697636;-8.589269;99;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;An attractive and intimate restaurant with a good location next to the Ponte Velho. Impressive à la carte menu of traditional and regional Portuguese cooking, including the must - try cod with corn bread (bacalhau com broa).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16344;Casinha Velha;Portugal;Leiria;Rua Professores Portelas 23, Leiria, 2415-534, Portugal;39.7594215;-8.8102638;66;false;true;Portuguese;Casinha Velha occupies a charming two-storey house with a rustic decor and homely ambience where tradition and high-quality ingredients are key tenets. Starters include a platter of cheeses and Iberian black pork sausages, accompanied by a basket of different types of home-baked bread. These are followed by signature mains that include cod with cream and shrimp and “duck rice” with dried fruits, followed by an assortment of “convent”-style desserts and pastries – all prepared with great dedication and panache!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16345;DOC;Portugal;Folgosa;Estrada Nacional 222, Folgosa, 5110-214, Portugal;41.1515748;-7.6821759;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;(Temporarily closed for refurbishment) This restaurant in a contemporary - style is beside the Douro river and has an attractive terrace over the river. Enjoy the good views and taste its traditional cuisine with a creative flair.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16346;Fauno;Portugal;Porto;Rua Estreita de Lóios 5, Porto, 4050-244, Portugal;41.1455144;-8.6129793;53;false;true;Contemporary;Behind the green retro-style glass doors of this restaurant in one of the city’s narrow streets you’ll find a unique dining space run by brothers Pedro Amorim (sommelier) and Tiago Amorim (chef) who have embarked on their first project together here. The cuisine comes courtesy of a single tasting menu (including a vegetarian option) that constantly evolves with the seasons and the availability of ingredients from local producers, all characterised by faultless execution and good taste. For an even more impressive dining experience, pair each dish with different wines or a cocktail or mocktail. We can also highly recommend the chef’s daily specials!;Air conditioning;[]
16347;Nast;Belgium;Izegem;Hondekensmolenstraat 60, Izegem, 8870, Belgium;50.9076205;3.2306731;82;true;false;Modern French, French Contemporary;Dean Masschelein has added his inimitable stamp to a former chicory factory, retaining the original rough brick walls, but cleverly dotted with modern fixtures and fittings. The chef is a genuine West Flemish lad, as his exuberant personality and passion for regional produce quickly reveal. The food is succulent, straightforward and international and he might mix presa iberico with a sweet-sour baba ghanoush and Mediterranean fregola, all of which comes together thanks to an emulsion of bacon. Creative seasonal cooking, rendered even more flavoursome when paired with gueuze beers or organic wines.;Car park;[]
16348;Dah Makan;Belgium;Knokke;Dumortierlaan 64, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3517944;3.2921282;60;true;true;Fusion;Cod marinated in miso and grilled on a robata, served with crunchy veg and lashings of frothy beurre blanc spiked with yuzu… Dishes to share such as these explain the success of this snug eatery. The culinary score, depicted by Asian flavours and western influences, demonstrates a clear preference for superior produce such as wagyu beef or crab from the North Sea, which are often finished on a robata grill or teppanyaki griddle. The menu is almost impossibly varied!;Air conditioning;[]
16349;Dante;Belgium;Haacht;Jennekensstraat 75, Haacht, 3150, Belgium;50.9716584;4.6239269;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine;“Falling and getting back up” is how Sven Fonteyn describes his journey. He designed this charming friendly restaurant as his very own paradise, a feeling he endeavours to communicate through his cooking. Each dish is depicted by his open-minded outlook and commitment to quality. Exotic, often Asian twists add a refreshing dimension to his playful recipes, illustrated by his new take on the traditional rabbit with prunes recipe. The spot-on menu changes regularly, to the delight of the loyal crowd of patrons.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16350;Delphine Ronsyn;Belgium;Bierghes;Chaussée d'Enghien 61a, Bierghes, 1430, Belgium;50.6975366;4.1261567;36;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking;Delphine Ronsyn opened this cheerful spacious restaurant, whose floor-to-ceiling windows command fantastic views of the surrounding fields and meadows, less than a kilometre from the family farm. Naturally enough, Delphine is a champion of local produce and her region. Her bistronomic menu is deceptively simple and straightforward, as the delicate chervil sauce that flanks gilt-head bream consummately illustrates.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16351;la petite Madeleine;Belgium;Tournai;rue de la Madeleine 19, Tournai, 7500, Belgium;50.610498;3.3824819;25;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Behind the authentic historic façade lies a contemporary interior, adorned with arty photos and boasting a fine terrace to the rear. Chef Dufranne enjoys surprising diners with his original recipes and generous helpings. Each dish is a treasure trove of meticulously prepared ingredients and fascinating combinations.;Terrace;[]
16352;Guzzi;Belgium;Leuven;Frederik Lintsstraat 5, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8752064;4.7046179;85;true;true;Italian;This characteristic town house with a small garden is a stalwart champion of Italian simplicity. The chefs add a new, yet respectful spin to authentic flavours. The menu is devised according to the availability of fresh, preferably organic ingredients, occasionally jazzed up with a Mediterranean twist. We recommend their sourdough pizzas cooked in a clay oven – your tastebuds won’t know what has hit them!;Terrace;[]
16353;Brimer;Luxembourg;Grundhof;1 route de Beaufort, Grundhof, 6360, Luxembourg;49.8357178;6.3298416;35;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;Looking for a delicious but inexpensive meal? The Brimers do it with flair. Their magic formula? Fine ingredients cooked with originality, generosity and flavour. And Mrs Brimer knows where to find the tastiest mushrooms.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16354;Escabèche;Belgium;Knokke;Dumortierlaan 94, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.352447;3.2931962;75;true;false;Creative French;The trendy welcoming interior of Escabèche is a hit with the inhabitants of Knokke. They pop in to chat with the friendly hostess, Lisbeth, and to sample the delicacies rustled up by chef Verhasselt, a virtuoso in the art of enhancing first-class ingredients. Blessedly free of fancy frills, you can expect a wholesome lineup of pedigree Gallic nosh, flanked by subtle side dishes and occasionally jazzed up with Mediterranean or Oriental twists. The extensive appetising menu ranges from a hamachi-based festival of Asian flavours to a juicy fillet of turbot in a Dijon mustard sauce or the gamey earthiness of pheasant à la brabançonne during game season. The vast menu is heaven for foodies!;Air conditioning;[]
16355;De Steenen Haene;Belgium;Zillebeke;Komenseweg 21, Zillebeke, 8902, Belgium;50.8354532;2.9033988;99;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;An irresistible friendly vibe echoes throughout this pretty modernised cottage, whose terrace-garden is set amidst fields and pastures. The family-run restaurant serves classical delicacies such as grilled lobster and the spring chicken and croquettes exhibit the chef’s talent. Flavour and generosity epitomise this establishment.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16356;Roosenberg;Belgium;Waasmunster;Patotterijstraat 1, Waasmunster, 9250, Belgium;51.1214387;4.0819893;94;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Waasmunster’s discerning foodies make up the faithful clientele of this smart eatery. They come for the elegant interior, friendly vibe and top-quality produce, without forgetting the lure of the wine cellar, well stocked in Burgundy and Tuscan tipples. The à la carte lineup embodies the establishment’s devotion to quality. Chef-owner Bruno De Wilde errs towards flame-licked techniques and seasonal ingredients, together with signature dishes like vol-au-vent, tartare steak, asparagus à la flamande or local game in season. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16357;Lys d'Or;Belgium;Gent;Charles de Kerchovelaan 81, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0411007;3.7212272;88;true;false;French, Classic Cuisine;Black marble, a blue and gold colour scheme and a grand piano set the scene in this stylish, modern venue, providing the perfect foil to the elegant, classical cuisine by chef Wattenberge. The purity of the produce is enhanced by consummate technique. Star ingredients include turbot, sole from the North Sea and pigeon from Anjou.;;[]
16358;Resto 136;Belgium;Hoogstraten;Vrijheid 136, Hoogstraten, 2320, Belgium;51.4028648;4.761773;69;true;true;French, Asian Influences;Make a beeline for this peacock blue townhouse at number 136 where you will be pampered by Niels and Laura. Their elegant contemporary establishment upholds tradition and while the chef clearly enjoys mixing spicy Asian flavours with Mediterranean extravagance, he is equally capable of winning you over with a flawless piece of cod flanked by knockout beurre blanc and creamy mashed potato.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16359;Klost’r;Belgium;Vlijtingen;Kloosterstraat 10, Vlijtingen, 3770, Belgium;50.8347176;5.5874728;40;false;true;Creative French;As soon as you venture over the threshold into this stylishly restored farmstead, you are warmly greeted by sommelier Lennert Holstens. His pals in the kitchen, Marco Veraldi and Chiem Boijen, take your tastebuds hostage with their creative talent. Gourmet cuisine meets family favourites is the hallmark of their modern elegant score. Surprises abound, such as a dessert of Hesbaye cherries and white chocolate. Expertly chosen Limburg wines add the final flourish, without forgetting the B&B, wellbeing facilities and beauty parlour!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16361;Talloor d'Or;Belgium;Ledeberg;Ledebergplein 20, Ledeberg, 9050, Belgium;51.0368271;3.7420759;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You will immediately feel at home in the tasteful interior of the Talloor d’Or. Seated at the counter, you can admire the chef at work, rustling up contemporary dishes in keeping with the establishment’s vibe. Subtle vegetable dishes, fine sauces and a few citrus notes enhance and underscore the main ingredient. Seasoned Matthias and Nikki give free rein to their creative bent.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16362;Racines;Belgium;Floreffe;Rue Emile Lessire 1, Floreffe, 5150, Belgium;50.427211;4.7562593;97;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Contemporary;Enter this wine bar boutique, choose a bottle (€15 corkage fee if you drink it here) and take a seat in the conservatory overlooking a stream. Welcome to Racines, where Louise and Maxime are on hand to guide and advise you. They enjoy waxing lyrical about their sustainable development beliefs and their love of all things local, which the chefs transform into enticing dishes rich in youthful appeal. A “slow wine and food” concept oozing with genuine authenticity.;Air conditioning,Bring your own bottle,Car park,Interesting wine list;[]
16363;Yijiangnan;Belgium;Sint-Genesius-Rode;Zoniënwoudlaan 359, Sint-Genesius-Rode, 1640, Belgium;50.7575077;4.3802841;52;true;true;Chinese, Fusion;The patterned wallpaper and understated class of this posh establishment are obvious right from the first minute, but it is the alfresco patio that will win your heart. Every detail counts from the first hello to the last farewell. Yijiangnan specialises in straightforward, generous Chinese cuisine. Rather than a never-ending menu, you will find family favourites such as Peking duck, together with a few more modern creations. All the better when you know that the prices won’t break the bank.;Terrace;[]
16364;Pur Boeuf;Belgium;Berlare;Donklaan 93A, Berlare, 9290, Belgium;51.0403592;3.9814769;99;false;false;Meats and Grills;The remarkable maturing room and attractive open wine cellar set the scene for chef Hanselaer’s two overriding passions. Son of a cattle breeder, Blanc Bleu Belge beef takes pride of place on the menu, which also showcases the strength and flavour of other fine ingredients. The resourceful chef is never short of creativity, demonstrated by his modern take on Belgian endive baked in ham and cheese and while his carne cuisine occasionally reaches the realm of high-flying, it is never OTT. The cheese and dessert trolley in particular is spectacular! A must if you plan on touring the Lake Donk area.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16365;Julienne;Belgium;Noorderwijk;Servaas Daemsstraat 25, Noorderwijk, 2200, Belgium;51.1420149;4.8365054;75;true;false;Belgian, French;This upmarket establishment dripping in marble, which is bright and airy by day and cosy by night, extends a warm welcome typical of the Kempen region, before presenting an enticing menu and list of daily specials. Seasoned chef, Tim Moeskops, knows his classics and skilfully turns out dishes ranging from crispy, generously filled shrimp fritters and fresh, juicy sole to flavoursome eel in sorrel or a Poire belle Hélène, straight from his own pear orchard. Julienne celebrates heroic classics and does so with flair and know-how.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16366;DOOR73;Belgium;Gent;Hoogstraat 73, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0552472;3.7125127;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;OAK’s younger sibling is hip and friendly. The handsome mosaic tiled floor and open kitchen first draw the eye, before you sit down to sample the Greek-born chef’s Mediterranean fare. You can choose between three types of menu: Comfort, Trust and Discover, featuring a range of international, unusual and deftly crafted dishes to share, such as his fascinating Holstein tonnato 2.0! Expect to be surprised!;;[]
16367;Le Jardin de la Gaichel;Luxembourg;Eischen;Maison 5, Eischen, 8469, Luxembourg;49.6941102;5.8685979;97;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Le cosy Jardin de la Gaichel est en parfaite harmonie avec son environnement boisé (un cadre idéal pour passer une nuitée !). La cuisine d’inspiration bretonne va droit au but. Fruits de mer (sur réservation), foie gras, canard découpé en salle… Une vraie cuisine de produits classique.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16368;Lafarques;Belgium;Pepinster;chemin des Douys 20, Pepinster, 4860, Belgium;50.5666351;5.774495;84;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;This heritage country mansion, gleaming with classy elegance, will take your breath away. Both the surrounding countryside and the stylish guestrooms are exquisite. The cordon bleu chef allows the (preferably local) ingredients to shout their name, whilst seeking to generously and delicately enhance their traditional flavours. Don’t miss the game in season.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16369;Brasserie Latem;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Latem;Kortrijksesteenweg 9, Sint-Martens-Latem, 9830, Belgium;51.0141831;3.6491246;64;true;true;Classic French;There is more to this stylish brasserie on the busy Kortrijksesteenweg than you might expect. Chef Van den Bossche's love of Asia is evident throughout the restaurant, from the decor of the izakaya to the lounge-like terrace and the cigar lounge. Although you will find sashimi options and a bento box on the menu, it is dominated by classic fare. Think sumptuous vol-au-vent, onglet à l'échalote and pan-fried ray wing – prepared the way it should be: generously and using the finest ingredients. The extensive wine list is definitely worth exploring!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16370;De Huifkar;Belgium;Koksijde;Koninklijke Baan 142, Koksijde, 8670, Belgium;51.120357;2.6343753;51;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Fish and lobster are the specialties of this vintage-modern restaurant. Admire the quality and freshness of the produce in the lobster tank at the entrance. The chef is keen on classical recipes and generous flavours, depicted by timeless dishes such as monkfish with shrimp, local-style poached cod, without forgetting Belgium’s family favourite, veal kidneys in mustard sauce. Affordable gastronomy!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16371;Vinke;Belgium;Westouter;Poperingestraat 32, Westouter, 8954, Belgium;50.7985631;2.7454049;20;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;The understated modernity of Vinke, which verges on the mysterious, is enhanced by a huge brass counter. Each dish showcases chef Gilles Demeere’s talents, demonstrating a modern culinary repertory of undiluted purity. Classics like sole meunière rub shoulders with more creative inventions, such as pink Steenvoorde pigeon served with a jus of the bones and a mousse made out of the liver and heart for extra depth and flavour. The chef’s generosity is further underscored by velvety mashed potato and thyme-flavoured green peas.;Terrace;[]
16372;Graspoort;Belgium;Mechelen;Begijnenstraat 28, Mechelen, 2800, Belgium;51.027496;4.4767546;63;true;true;Creative French, Fusion;Graffiti on the walls and a homemade tropical tree hung with brightly coloured leaves set the scene in this fun, offbeat eatery. Thibault Van Stratum cooks instinctively and frequently finds his inspiration in Asia. Highly creative fusion cuisine brimming in influences, illustrated by croaker and marinated mussels jazzed up by smoked oil-perfumed dashi.;Terrace;[]
16373;Chez Flo;Belgium;Flémalle;Quai du Halage 266, Flémalle, 4400, Belgium;50.5861767;5.4162725;49;false;true;Modern French;Imagine crispy, yet tender pigeon breast, flanked by legs cooked in a foie gras preparation, all of which in a full-bodied jus overflowing in gutsy flavour. Such dishes are emblematic of Florence Porignon’s culinary flair. After honing her skills in top establishments, Ms Porignon’s distinctive signature shines through in a modern repertory, which hits the spot every time and is depicted by a delicate touch that enhances knockout flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16374;Vier;Belgium;Kortrijk;Groeningestraat 4, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.8294939;3.2677268;74;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Concrete, black and turquoise set the unusual scene in this imposing, yet nonetheless cosy venue. Fine produce such as cottage garden veggies and black chicken from Burgundy takes pride of place in the cooking of chef Bas. Natural, simple and seasonal sum up his ethos, all of which flanked by knockout sauces and at prices that make sense in the heart of Kortrijk!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16375;Amélys;;Luxembourg;12 boulevard Royal, 2449, Luxembourg;49.6136115;6.1265517;84;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This light, airy brasserie pleases everyone. It serves tasty, scrumptious food all day long. The varied menu features classical and more modern dishes, always with the chef’s surprising and distinctive hallmark. Delicious Sunday brunch.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16376;Les Abris;Belgium;Oombergen;Steenweg op Aalst 109, Oombergen, 9620, Belgium;50.8979067;3.8313504;40;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Ring the bell and enter this friendly eatery, taking a seat in the lovely sitting room for a drink as you admire the lush green garden. Chef Kristof Timmermans and sommelier Tijs Coessens have pooled their joint talents to create a customised experience. After the host’s insightful explanations, we immediately noticed that everything is cooked to order. The chef’s skill can be tasted in the spot-on cooking and fascinating side dishes, for example, as oxalis and a sweet-sour cream of chickpeas add whoomph to langoustine. Les Abris offers gourmet shelter to foodies in search of sustenance!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16377;De Koolputten;Belgium;Waasmunster;Koolputten 2, Waasmunster, 9250, Belgium;51.1052448;4.1402827;82;false;true;French Contemporary;These former coal shafts overlooking the Mirabrug bridge have been carefully restored and are now home to a comfortable B&B, an exhibition area, an events venue and this restaurant. A trendy, pleasant setting in which to sample contemporary fare with classical roots, with a very open feel. Up-to-date cuisine with gastronomic flair.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16378;Equilibrium;;Luxembourg;107 Rue de la Tour Jacob, 1831, Luxembourg;49.6111345;6.1403721;96;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Baptiste Heugens boldly steps outside the box to create unexpected, yet balanced dishes, pairing his consummate knowhow with unconventional associations. The chef likes to cook fish (from Brittany) simply and purely, adding a new dimension thanks to side dishes jazzed up with fresh, spicy or tangy notes for added depth and intensity. A fascinating quest for culinary balance. We advise choosing a table downstairs for a bird’s eye view of the zinc counter where the cold dishes are prepared.;Air conditioning;[]
16379;Béus;Belgium;Passendale;Molenstraat 66, Passendale, 8980, Belgium;50.9038146;3.0219264;87;true;false;Farm to table;Maria and Michel welcome guests to their gourmet establishment as if they were old friends of the family. Maria tends to your every need in the dining room, while Michel crafts what appears to be classical fare, yet with a subtle modern spin. Examples range from old-school grilled white pudding and traditional sole meunière with fresh fries to scallops served with curry-flavoured beurre blanc. Soul-warming food that has kept up with the times. At Béus, which loosely translates as “our home” in the local lingo, flavour is the overriding goal every time.;;[]
16380;Maurice;Belgium;Brasschaat;Bredabaan 662, Brasschaat, 2930, Belgium;51.3134803;4.5135274;100;false;true;French Contemporary, Modern French;The friendly eatery of delightful Kaatje De Blick and chef Karl Ave is in fact named after their cat! They aim for a home-from-home vibe and welcome guests like old friends: “Maurice is like coming home” in their own words. The sommelier can be relied on to ply you with insightful tips, whilst the veteran chef masterfully deploys his classical training to craft knockout dishes and sauces, albeit with the occasional more modern twist. For example, he often slips in Asian notes, illustrated by a ballotine of langoustine underscored by a sublime yuzu and dashi sauce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16381;Refter;Belgium;Brugge;Molenmeers 2, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2098811;3.2319631;62;false;false;Flemish, Regional Cuisine;Top notch ingredients, complex-free combinations and gutsy flavours. Don’t expect fancy frills in this casual bistro, adorned with a colourful eye-catching mosaic. The food is always first rate and flawlessly executed – skin-on cod and yummy dame blanche (vanilla ice cream and hot chocolate sauce) dessert.;Terrace;[]
16382;L'Espérance;Belgium;De Haan;Driftweg 1, De Haan, 8420, Belgium;51.272327;3.0336909;49;true;true;Farm to table;The experience starts with the lovely 1930 façade. Inside, historic details such as period windows set the stylish scene. In his open-plan kitchen, the chef crafts fresh bistronomic fare with the odd Mediterranean tang. He might pair fresh, briny turbot with a champagne-flavoured beurre blanc liberally garnished in garden herbs. The (mainly Gallic) wine list impresses both by the range and by its affordable prices.;;[]
16383;Lounge Roannay;Belgium;Francorchamps;Rue de Spa 155, Francorchamps, 4970, Belgium;50.4643575;5.9370986;70;true;false;Modern French;The contemporary brasserie of the luxury Le Roannay Hotel is more than a match for our expectations: pedigree French cuisine served in a relaxed ambience. How about the rich velvety flavour of a foie gras terrine is paired with apples to add a subtle acidic kick or a thick slice of cod flanked by a smoothly unctuous beurre blanc? Familiar flavours and stellar execution are the hallmarks of the Roannay Lounge.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16384;Côté Préféré;Belgium;Jabbeke;Dorpsstraat 47, Jabbeke, 8490, Belgium;51.1818578;3.0897247;51;false;false;Creative French;A delicious slab of turbot cooked on the bone with a beurre noisette, al dente asparagus and a creamy morel sauce. Such are some of Tim Versyck’s emblematic recipes. The ingredient rules in his mainly classical repertory, albeit with the occasional international spin. The chef sources his produce locally, particularly fish from the North Sea and veggies, meat and poultry from the polders of West Flanders. The bright contemporary interior aims to pay tribute to the earthy, wholesome terroir of Flanders.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16385;OX'E;Belgium;Lochristi;Dorp-West 89, Lochristi, 9080, Belgium;51.094609;3.8269047;97;false;false;Classic French;Take a seat by the open fire for a drink before your meal and admire the refurbished Art deco interior as you get ready to sample an ode to classicism in a cosmopolitan vibe. Chef Xavier Leys, who avows a weakness for matured meat, cannot be faulted for his textbook craftsmanship when it comes to recipes such as Rossini tournedos or seabass in a salt crust. The focus is on familiar, even regressive comfort food, which is perfectly paired with South-African, French or Italian wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16386;Otoro;Belgium;Hasselt;Luikersteenweg 366, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9004902;5.3562793;71;true;true;French Contemporary, Asian Influences;Pajtim Bajrami makes no bones about his love of produce, as the top-drawer scallops, wagyu beef and other delicacies quickly demonstrate. His Anjou pigeon is a perfect example: he first cooks the breasts rare before adding a high-flying felicitous blend of foie gras and truffles. Polished French classics are right up his street, enhanced by gutsy sauces and the odd Asian tang. A cosy interior depicts this eatery sodden with rippling ambition. A knock-out wine list and Ardita’s friendly, professional service add the final flourish.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16387;Decan;Belgium;Berchem;Prins Boudewijnlaan 20, Berchem, 2600, Belgium;51.180735;4.4234668;51;true;true;Modern French;Jan Decan is a pianist and a chef down to his very core, as his restaurant, an elegant harmony of ebony and ivory, musically reflects. You may even see him play if you’re lucky! Jan enjoys jazzing up classical recipes, adding contemporary notes with the greatest respect for the ingredient. He excels in orchestrating dishes such as sole meunière or saddle of lamb with morels and green asparagus. His subtle sauces, flavoursome acidic melodies and familiar tunes demonstrate his talent as an accomplished (culinary) conductor. Ah! Music to our ears!;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16388;L'Entretien;Belgium;Leuze;Chaussée de Namur 258, Leuze, 5310, Belgium;50.5489778;4.906388;94;false;true;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;On the first floor of a modern BMW dealership, this open-plan restaurant sports a huge, glazed facade. Chef Robin is a dab hand at looking after our inner well-being. Adding a modern spin to French recipes, he shines the spotlight on ingredients, among which foie gras and pork. He may have a playful approach to textures, but the attention he lavishes on the vegetables and rich flavours is second to none. Even better, the restaurant is open for breakfast.;;[]
16389;Bottega Vannini;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Pierre;Avenue Charles Thielemans 63, Woluwe-Saint-Pierre, 1150, Belgium;50.83707;4.4293;35;true;false;Italian;This lively bottega doubles as a delicatessen, so you tuck into your meal surrounded by shelves of Italian delicacies (be sure to stop by the counter afterwards). Expect no frills here, just unadulterated Mediterranean flavours. Their take on beloved classics like vitello tonnato and saltimbocca alla romana showcases the full potential of these dishes. Or how about perfectly al dente cavatelli pasta with succulent sausage meat and crunchy niebé beans? Accompanied by interesting wines (corkage fee €15). Irresistibly authentic!;;[]
16390;Hors-Champs;Belgium;Ernage;chaussée de Wavre 170, Ernage, 5030, Belgium;50.5926755;4.6783704;30;true;true;Organic, Modern Cuisine;Stefan Jacobs has metamorphosed the Ernage farmstead. This gifted chef has opened a B&B, a bakery and a tasteful restaurant that sports a rough, brutalist look. His sustainable ethos can be tasted in subtle dishes, rich in unexpected and playful combinations. He pays a sincere homage to his region as he showcases the produce of local market gardeners and from his own garden. Examples include lamb from the Censier farm (an earthy stew of lamb shoulder, a fritter of chopped lamb tripe and a succulent lamb fillet) flanked with different textures of sweet corn.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16391;Bar Bulot at Botanic;Belgium;Antwerpen;Lange Gasthuisstraat 41, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2138174;4.4055025;66;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;This hip, cosmopolitan brasserie, Antwerp’s outpost of Bruge’s Bar Bulot, has found refuge in the lavish Botanic Sanctuary Hotel. Timeless classics such as asparagus à la flamande, vol-au-vent of Bresse chicken, sweetbread and shrimp are revamped to tempt and tickle today’s tastebuds. Top-notch ingredients and contemporary flavours, by way of exotic spices, add character to each dish. Heaven for discerning foodies!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16392;Lin’eau;Belgium;Sint-Baafs-Vijve;Koen Lisardestraat 19, Sint-Baafs-Vijve, 8710, Belgium;50.9094925;3.3882019;49;false;true;Modern French;This former flax factory (1907) is steeped in history, as is illustrated by the bare stone walls, authentic details and photos. This heritage is cleverly set off by trendy influences and personal works of art. A young couple is behind the helm, rustling up modern, painstakingly devised, international recipes, flanked by infused sauces and varied textures. The epitome of culinary delicacy.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16393;Rôtisserie Ardennaise;;Luxembourg;1 Avenue du 10 Septembre, 2551, Luxembourg;49.6094882;6.11922;37;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Glittering light fixtures and colourful chairs set the scene in this buzzy brasserie, whose watchwords are tradition and emotion. The ingredient is the star of the chef’s distinctive cuisine. He modernises traditional classics, creating contrasts and playing on textures. Spit roasted chicken (also take-away) is one of the house specialties.;Counter dining;[]
16395;Casello;Belgium;Schilde;Turnhoutsebaan 180, Schilde, 2970, Belgium;51.2379417;4.575746;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Modern French;This former toll station on the Turnhout-Antwerp road has morphed into a sophisticated restaurant. The sleek annexe drips with designer luxury and gilt details, and the open kitchen is sure to draw the eye as soon as you arrive. The chef works with top-notch ingredients, elevating them with subtle Asian touches and the bold flavours of Italy. Whether in the form of langoustine with wawasai and enoki, or tagliatelle with truffle and horn of plenty, this modern approach to the principle of "less is more" is captivating.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16396;Linéa;Belgium;Spa;Avenue des Lanciers 9, Spa, 4900, Belgium;50.4890226;5.8583247;18;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Frederic Scavone made a name for himself at Le Pontecino in Liège, before setting up shop in this impressive edifice, flanked by a modern wing. His contemporary spin on Italian cooking does feature the occasional Gallic twang, but Mediterranean exuberance is probably its overriding characteristic. Rigatoni alla norma, homemade ravioli with fresh sausages and a personal interpretation of tiramisu… Flavour is the watchword of Linéa. Book a room and treat yourself to a truly relaxing weekend in style.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16397;Les Frères Louise;Belgium;Ellezelles;Rue de Renaix 162, Ellezelles, 7890, Belgium;50.7318245;3.6467;61;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Classic French;This beautifully renovated miller's house (1737) has retained its classic soul and rustic charm – open fireplaces, rotating art collection, selection of cigars and pipe tobacco, and a lovely courtyard terrace. The Mertens family invite you to their restaurant, where you will be treated like an old friend as you tuck into timeless classics made with the finest ingredients, such as partridge shot by a local hunter and soufflé generously infused with Grand Marnier. This restaurant is known for its freshly cooked fries, delicious sauces, masterful cooking on the charcoal grill and large à la carte menu. The sommelier has a penchant for German wines, and his passion is infectious!;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16398;Brasserie David;Belgium;Oostende;Christinastraat 45, Oostende, 8400, Belgium;51.2313503;2.9164587;92;true;false;Contemporary;The menu of David Dewaele’s friendly brasserie showcases all the traditional delicacies of this coastline. The entirely open-plan kitchen allows you to admire his work as he prepares sole, seabass and shrimp. The side dishes are creatively crafted and add an extra whoomph to each dish. Ideal to sample Belgian favourites with a sprinkling of originality.;Air conditioning;[]
16399;Le Grand Pré;Belgium;Hantes-Wihéries;Rue du Grand Pré 13A, Hantes-Wihéries, 6560, Belgium;50.2928918;4.1784848;39;false;false;French, Creative French;Sprawling meadows encircle this old riverside stone farmstead, so it isn’t surprising that the country vibe has wound its tendrils into the interior. This friendly eatery takes pride in sourcing local Walloon produce that is crafted into a lineup of pedigree seasonal Gallic fare, like saddle of lamb, cooked rare in a herby crust, garnished with a subtle rosemary gravy and potato salad. The splendid wine list boasts over 400 references and is definitely worth a gander. A meal at the Grand Pré makes the perfect ending to a tour of this beautiful rural region. Country life at its best!;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16400;L.E.S.S. Eatery;Belgium;Brugge;'t Zand 21, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2047697;3.2185412;66;false;false;Asian Influences;Love Eat Share Smile is the baseline of this hip urban eatery, which is equally suited to a hunger-obliterating snack at the bar as to a full-course feast with all the trimmings with all the family. You can expect an international culinary repertory with a definite Asian slant. From steak tartare with a Korean kick and ceviche scattered with distinctive fresh, spicy, tangy Peruvian notes to Hong-Kong-style young turbot, the extensive menu is a treasure trove of premium produce and creativity. A trendy, suitably casual vibe depicts one of Bruges’ most popular foodie hotspots!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16401;Cosma;Belgium;Mechelen;Befferstraat 24, Mechelen, 2800, Belgium;51.0285146;4.4827222;82;false;true;Sharing, Contemporary;The bright, hip, relaxed vibe of this restaurant immediately sets everyone at ease. This enthusiasm is further enhanced when you take a glance at the menu which sports a wide range of dishes to be shared, countless vegetarian suggestions and excellent side dishes – bravo! An unusual formula and heart-warming international influences.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16402;Les Tilleuls;Belgium;Céroux;place Communale 2, Céroux, 1341, Belgium;50.6608441;4.5136379;15;false;false;Home Cooking;The former village hall of Céroux-Mousty has been turned into a welcoming bistro. Marc Volkaerts has thrown all his experience and enthusiasm into his own individual version of classical cuisine, such as tartare steak or duck shepherd’s pie, adding a personal and distinctive spin to consummately bistronomic dishes. Masterful!;;[]
16403;Locàle by Kok au Vin;Belgium;Brugge;Ezelstraat 21, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.212055;3.2198033;70;true;true;Country cooking, Farm to table;Locally sourced ingredients and a deep respect for nature's rhythms are the cornerstones of this cosy establishment. Influences from around the globe and the occasional use of the Mibrasa charcoal oven take things up a notch. The menu features dishes for sharing, such as zingy ceviche made with earthy beetroot or Zeeland mussels cooked in Bruges wheat beer. Nothing overly complicated, just playful, on-trend delicious food.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16404;Bistrôt Le Ciel;Belgium;Neerharen;Paalsteenlaan 90, Neerharen, 3620, Belgium;50.91503;5.66814;36;true;false;Classic French, Italian Contemporary;The sky is visible through the glazed roof and tropical plants and contemporary artwork set the singular scene indoors, while the terrace is taken by storm in fine weather. The food features a pageant of polished French fare with the occasional Italian twist, illustrated by terrine of foie gras or venison in a Grand Veneur sauce. Consummate craftsmanship and a reverent respect for culinary tradition.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16405;Adagio & Gusto;Belgium;Mont-sur-Marchienne;Avenue Paul Pastur 378, Mont-sur-Marchienne, 6032, Belgium;50.396438;4.4183374;51;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Philippo Santangelo and his right-arm man John Oremans take their time to ensure that your culinary experience will be truly memorable. They invite you to step inside their tastefully appointed townhouse and lovely adjoining garden. Their modern version of Italian cuisine from the authentic flavours of minestrone soup, which are treated to a creative new twist, to the cannelloni of sole in a noisette butter sauce, has already acquired numerous fans.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16406;Clash;Belgium;Brussegem;Nieuwelaan 127, Brussegem, 1785, Belgium;50.9363915;4.2775216;16;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Clash is a hip and vibrant restaurant with posters of celebrities providing an extra touch of cool. The lighting even gives the place a bit of a disco feel (be sure to check out the regular DJ nights). Classic dishes reign supreme on the menu, with aged meat being a big feature. No unnecessary frills, just straightforward, bold flavours. You might start with some crispy shrimp croquettes, then, during the game season, move on to pheasant roasted on the bone à la brabançonne. Be sure to leave room for the Brussels waffle, prepared to a time-honoured recipe. The extensive menu will leave you spoilt for choice.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16407;Le Délice du Jour;Belgium;Chapelle-lez-Herlaimont;Rue du Chemin de Fer 57, Chapelle-lez-Herlaimont, 7160, Belgium;50.4665752;4.2701268;73;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Modern Cuisine;Fabrizzio Chirico, who needs no introduction in Wallonia, is back on the gastro scene. He has set up shop in this elegant villa adorned with tasteful decor in warm tones. The chef's passion for working with top-quality, local ingredients is evident in every dish, and the sauces are particularly impressive. Classically trained, he is nonetheless keen to embrace new techniques and likes to play with zingy and smoky flavours, as well as juxtaposing textures. Think raw scallop taken to the next level with a lacto-fermented sauce or black tea enriched with the scallop's coral. One thing is for sure: you won't leave hungry!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16408;RectoVerso;Belgium;Ciney;Avenue de Namur 29, Ciney, 5590, Belgium;50.2992612;5.1011419;25;true;true;French Contemporary, Seasonal Cuisine;Loïc Thirion and Robin Van Habost are fanatical about pedigree Gallic cuisine. They invariably wave a cheerful greeting to diners from the open-plan kitchen of their contemporary establishment. First class produce, such as local game and mushrooms, is crafted into comfortingly familiar dishes rich in enticing aromas, to which the youthful chefs add a distinctive, personal and sometimes surprising touch. Feelgood French fare by fervent foodies.;Car park;[]
16409;'t Pachthuis;Belgium;Zottegem;Gentsesteenweg 264, Zottegem, 9620, Belgium;50.88443;3.8293;35;false;true;Farm to table;Behind the walls of this characterful villa hides a romantic restaurant and a lovely garden patio – ideal for lunch or dinner in summertime! Chef De Keyser shares his fondness for classicism as you will quickly remark when you taste his sauces. However, he is not averse to a dash of originality thanks to subtle combinations of flavours and modern influences. Excellent value for pleasure!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16410;Akko;Belgium;Rijkhoven;Kasteelstraat 2, Rijkhoven, 3740, Belgium;50.8427946;5.5217905;61;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Akko’s lounge vibe never fails to appeal as you savour the panoramic view over the gardens from the bay windows. Ingredients take centre stage in the cuisine of a youthful chef who creates up-to-the-minute associations. Unexpected details, varied textures and distinctive sauces set the delicious culinary scene.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16411;Toit;Belgium;Braine-l'Alleud;Chaussée de Tubize 481, Braine-l'Alleud, 1420, Belgium;50.6935025;4.3316525;63;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine, Sardinian;The Boulemberg firm has opened this unusual restaurant on the roof of its manufacturing showroom. Floor to ceiling windows (their stock in trade!) and a terrace command splendid views of the lush green countryside, while a Mediterranean-inspired interior provides the perfect foil to extravagant, full-bodied Sardinian recipes underscored by French technique. Hence the contrast between steamed seabass and cooked sweetbread, paired with a lemon confit beurre blanc. The menu (renewed every six weeks) is rich in big-boned Mediterranean flavours and aromas.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16412;Nyde;Belgium;Borgloon;Tongersesteenweg 30, Borgloon, 3840, Belgium;50.8021489;5.350069;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The decision to call their restaurant Nyde, which means “to enjoy” in Danish, was far from ingenuous. Chef Céline, flanked by Martijn, your host, bend over backwards to make sure their guests enjoy their meal. The restaurant, whose vibe is serene and boasts a gorgeous patio to the rear, offers a set menu and a selection of cocktails and mocktails and insightful food-wine pairings. Céline underscores each ingredient’s purity as she seeks to sensitively enhance their flavours. She may garnish a lemon-flavoured mackerel tartare with a delicate concoction of diced cucumber and briny oysters, all of which is further offset by a lemon and cucumber dressing. Feelgood food that is guaranteed to lift your spirits.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16414;Schéiss;;Luxembourg;142 Val Sainte-Croix, 1370, Luxembourg;49.6124605;6.1044594;64;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The colourful "lounge" vibe of the Schéiss provides a perfect backdrop to its owners’ very personal vision of classicism. The meat is carved before diners at the table and the menu is essentially composed of traditional dishes, to which the chef adds his own modern flourish.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16415;Atelier Noun;Belgium;Leefdaal;Dorpstraat 252, Leefdaal, 3061, Belgium;50.8573576;4.6141911;69;false;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Bert and Sandra’s workshop sports a cosy, lounge vibe, underscored by Scandinavian accents and a splendid leafy al fresco area. The couple’s passion can be felt throughout the restaurant and Bert adores rustling up fascinating modern recipes, scattered with Asian nuances and incisive, acidic notes. Paradise for foodies!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16416;Roma;;Luxembourg;5 rue Louvigny, 1946, Luxembourg;49.6104538;6.1292415;84;true;false;Italian;Opened in 1950, Roma was the first Italian restaurant of Luxembourg, and it remains true to its founding authentic values. Seventy years on, little has changed and the venue, adorned with Venetian chandeliers, is still as vibrant and colourful as the food is wholesome. The pasta is homemade and oozes with crisp Mediterranean accents. Examples include pasta stuffed with seafood and a velvety vongole-type sauce or why not order a melt-in-the-mouth medallion of lamb, flanked by a gutsy gravy, mashed potatoes and scamorza? Themed festivals and a varied menu with something for everyone transform each meal into a feast.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16417;Tomo Ya;;Luxembourg;675 Rue de Neudorf, 2220, Luxembourg;49.6224433;6.18892;43;false;false;Sushi;Sushis are the speciality of this minimalist establishment. The extensive menu also offers a wide range of noodle dishes, but we particularly recommend you try the mind-blowing lineup of fresh fish dishes. Salmon maki, beef gyoza or wafer-thin sashimi: forthright, authentic flavours blessedly free of fancy frills.;Air conditioning,Cash only;[]
16418;De Jangeli;Luxembourg;Mondorf-les-Bains;impasse Emile Didderich, Mondorf-les-Bains, 5616, Luxembourg;49.50325;6.283437;63;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The focus in this airy, elegant restaurant is on fresh and varied bistronomic recipes. The menu (changed monthly) is deliciously appetising, as is the theme menu (also regularly renewed). Don’t hesitate to ask the experienced wine waiter for advice.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16419;Heritage;Belgium;Gent;Rodekoningstraat 12, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0584659;3.7231391;60;true;false;Vegetarian, Seafood;Behind a characteristic brick façade in the historic Patershol district lies a charming restaurant whose soul is clearly devoted to nature. Fish and vegetables top the bill in recipes oozing with Latin-American accents. Gutsy enchiladas and tortillas acquire gourmet status in this characterful establishment, which bills itself as a “Match made in heaven” – fascinating!;;[]
16420;De Pefferkär;Luxembourg;Huncherange;49 route d'Esch, Huncherange, 3340, Luxembourg;49.5175347;6.0635706;66;true;false;Modern French, Classic Cuisine;An elegant restaurant adorned with vibrant modern artwork. The boundless energy of the lady of the house and her son can be felt in their cuisine. Building on a classical repertory, they don’t hesitate to introduce modern textures and techniques and the owner-wine waiter will suggest fine local wines.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16421;Hostellerie Stafelter;Luxembourg;Walferdange;rue de Dommeldange 1, Walferdange, 7222, Luxembourg;49.6589605;6.134982;93;true;true;Farm to table;Tom Brosius is the culinary guardian of this modern, elegant hotel. He sources excellent market-fresh produce and locally grown ingredients which are assembled using modern techniques. Varied and delicious, with an appetising vegetarian menu. Comfortable guestrooms.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16422;Les Jardins d'Anaïs;;Luxembourg;2 place Sainte Cunégonde, 1367, Luxembourg;49.6149252;6.1428142;51;false;false;Creative French;These gardens are the epitome of posh elegance from the conservatory overlooking the lush greenery to the guestrooms, without forgetting the champagne trolley. All of which doesn’t prevent chef Parjouet from occasionally erring from the path of classicism and giving a free rein to his creative streak. Fillet of smoked sturgeon is paired with a striking gin and caviar sorbet and subtly offset by asparagus, foie gras and grapefruit. Bold, daring, spot-on cuisine!;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16423;Bistronome;Luxembourg;Strassen;373 route d'Arlon, Strassen, 8011, Luxembourg;49.6221429;6.0561726;29;true;false;Modern French;At this chic bistro, chef Hospital imparts a lesson in bistronomy every day, giving popular dishes and flavours a gourmet spin. The food is as exquisite to behold as it is to taste. Throw in the occasional creative twist and a fine dose of generosity and the scene is set. Along with dishes that have been revamped with seasonings from around the globe, the menu also features classics such as braised beef cheeks in a bold red wine sauce and al dente pappardelle.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16424;La Paulée Marie-Pierre;Belgium;Tournai;chaussée de Bruxelles 234, Tournai, 7500, Belgium;50.6042968;3.4150288;55;true;false;Classic French;This friendly establishment is named after an ancient Burgundy wine festival, which is far from a coincidence. It is even possible to buy a bottle to take home from the sensibly priced wine bin. The culinary score errs towards the traditional, albeit with a more contemporary lineup of suggestions. Examples include tender juicy veal garnished with a poultry sauce enriched in Comté cheese and a gratin of sliced potatoes and onions. The lunchtime menu embodies the big-hearted mindset of this culinary landmark of Tournai.;;[]
16425;L'Auberge;Belgium;Spa;place du Monument 3, Spa, 4900, Belgium;50.49217;5.8622565;37;true;true;French;The mix of leather, wood panelling, copper and glass gives L'Auberge the look and feel of an authentic brasserie. Located in Spa's bustling town centre, this restaurant has plenty of regulars, who come to savour traditional Belgian cuisine. The menu features hearty classics such as mussels in white wine (also available in half portions), veal kidneys à la liégeoise, crêpes mikado – the generous flavours will leave you feeling warm and satisfied. The guestrooms are worth a look if you're considering a longer stay.;;[]
16426;Manoir de Lébioles;Belgium;Spa;Domaine de Lébioles 1/5, Spa, 4900, Belgium;50.46498;5.83168;85;false;true;Creative;The chef working at this manor house creates his own personal style of up - to - the - minute cuisine using the highest quality ingredients. Chic, modern decor and lovely panoramic terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16427;La Cour de la Reine;Belgium;Spa;avenue Reine Astrid 86, Spa, 4900, Belgium;50.4917714;5.8584455;77;false;true;Modern French;The ‘Queen’s Courtyard’ aims to serve creative bistronomic dishes with strong classical overtones. The chef, a seasoned stalwart, has no qualms about letting creativity guide his inspiration and you will taste the chef’s personal version of a Belgian classic, shrimp fritters, together with a cutlet of venison with a heroically wondrous pepper sauce. A distinctive metal structure forms the centrepiece of the elegant establishment, which also offers swish guestrooms.;Terrace;[]
16428;Al Piccolo Mondo;Belgium;Liège;rue Grétry 24, Liège, 4020, Belgium;50.6362926;5.5797244;17;true;true;Italian;Chef Jonathan and wine waiter Rino have added a classy touch to their dad’s pizzeria and the result is both upbeat and appealing. Immaculately selected Italian wines are perfectly paired with flavoursome food, revealing a fine balance between intense and subtle flavours. The à la carte menu reveals the chef’s knack with traditional dishes such as vitello tonnato, while the set menu is more modern in inspiration.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16429;Nage;Belgium;Antwerpen;Reyndersstraat 17, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2193279;4.39882;47;true;false;French Contemporary, Creative;The character of this medieval mansion has been intelligently enhanced by the cosy, trendy revamp. Niki shares his know-how in terms of choice of excellent natural wines to pair with the modern French recipes crafted by Koen. The chef sprinkles his cooking with the occasional unexpected note in a bid to further highlight the ingredients’ authentic flavours. Examples include saddle of lamb cooked in butter with suave, flavoursome side dishes based on wild garlic. A word of warning: à la carte only at lunchtime and set menu only in the evening.;;[]
16430;Eddy Vraie;Belgium;Wanfercée-Baulet;route de Namur 64, Wanfercée-Baulet, 6224, Belgium;50.4614326;4.5815162;37;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Chef Eddy’s last name (True) is emblematic of his powerful, authentic cooking. No pointless frills or fuss. Generous helpings of good wholesome food await the hungry diner.;Air conditioning;[]
16431;La Barrière de Transinne;Belgium;Transinne;rue de la Barrière 4, Transinne, 6890, Belgium;50.0113849;5.199001;52;true;false;Modern French;There is no question as to the rich heritage of the Barrière de Transinne, but rather than the ubiquitous olde worlde clichés, this former hunting lodge is a picture of modernity and Ardennes hospitality. Enticing gastronomic nosh is served à la carte and in set menus (named after the owners’ sons). A fervent upholder of Gallic culinary traditions, the Barrière respects its region and the seasons.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16432;De Kruidenmolen;Belgium;Klemskerke;Dorpsstraat 1, Klemskerke, 8420, Belgium;51.2395396;3.0272932;93;false;true;Contemporary;Ostend-style shrimp fritters, rabbit stew in stout beer, a German jam doughnut filled with rosemary flavoured crème patissière: such are a few of the culinary gems that explain the success of this tastefully restored former miller’s house in the heart of the unspoiled polder countryside. Ask for a table on the terrace sheltered by panes of glass and admire the landscape. A fan of humble, often overlooked ingredients, the chef has no lack of creativity and his enticing menu appeals to all foodies. The establishment’s continuing popularity is borne out by the lively, bustling vibe that inevitably sets the scene at mealtimes.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16433;Bistro Mathilda;Belgium;Oostende;Leopold II-laan 1, Oostende, 8400, Belgium;51.2298838;2.9145864;31;true;false;Farm to table;This modern bistro is much more than a pleasant trendy interior. The chef’s influences are wide ranging with a focus on first class ingredients. Bistro Mathilda brings the promise of a fine meal!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16434;Table Rase;Belgium;Polleur;Avenue René Lange 18, Polleur, 4910, Belgium;50.5575487;5.898063;54;false;true;Modern French;Ludovic and Clarisse tick all the boxes when it comes to good food, starting with the eater-friendly prices of their welcoming eatery. Chef Ludovic enjoys shining the spotlight on his region, as he jazzes up immaculately crafted dishes with acidic, savoury or other subtle touches. He cleverly mixes smoked eel, foie gras and red beetroot in a punchy celery and wasabi jus. A “clean slate” for a fresh beginning with the distinctive signature of a veteran chef.;;[]
16435;La Manufacture;Luxembourg;Bertrange;5 Rue des Mérovingiens, Bertrange, 8070, Luxembourg;49.6104433;6.0762544;99;false;true;Fusion, Mediterranean Cuisine;This sprawling, industrial-inspired restaurant with a central, open-plan kitchen and a disco mirror ball amusingly hanging over the stoves lies behind the grocery store. Trendy and fashionable is the name of the game as the chefs’ open-minded, no-holds barred approach to Mediterranean fusion cuisine illustrates: creativity, top quality ingredients and consummate technique.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16436;Magnà;Belgium;Waterloo;Chaussée de Bruxelles 528, Waterloo, 1410, Belgium;50.7015513;4.4020514;94;true;false;Italian;“Magnà!” is what Steven Mirelli’s grandmother used to shout to summon the family at mealtimes. No need to shout now, as the eatery is packed with fans of its authentic Italian cucina. From the subtle hint of lemon peel in the osso bucco to the big-boned aromas of pasta alla carbonara, the ingredients are first-rate, the flavours authentic and familiar and the generosity second to none at Magnà!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16437;Il Trionfo;Belgium;Knokke;P. Parmentierlaan 203, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3488484;3.2861474;84;true;true;Italian;Il Trionfo is both an elegant restaurant and a family story. The father and daughter-in-law preside front-of-house, and their enthusiasm is infectious. He also has some fantastic wine recommendations up his sleeve. Upon entering the restaurant, you will catch a glimpse of the mother and son at work in the kitchen. You can opt for the more creative set menu or order à la carte from a selection of traditional robust Mediterranean classics like vitello tonnato and spaghetti vongole. Don't miss the osso buco – the meat is unbelievably tender, and that typically rich tomato sauce is simply divine. The quintessence of Italian generosity!;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16438;Le D'Arville;Belgium;Wierde;rue d'Arville 94, Wierde, 5100, Belgium;50.412418;4.9585107;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This inviting redbrick, 19C farmhouse features a clever mixture of rustic and modern, while its terrace, furnished with wooden tables, commands a fine view of the countryside. The creative cuisine is depicted by regional recipes and a large proportion of house - made preparations. The Barabas guest rooms offer modern comforts.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16439;La Ligne Rouge;Belgium;Hoeilaart;Terhulpsesteenweg 2, Hoeilaart, 1560, Belgium;50.7651432;4.4488785;52;false;true;Modern French;This stylish contemporary eatery depicted by crisp clean lines is the epitome of tranquil. On the edge of Soignes Forest, get ready to be pampered by a friendly waiting team. Guillaume Desart himself describes his style as “nouvelle classical cuisine”. Indeed, his passion for top-drawer ingredients and his flair for sauces are indicative of a desire to uphold tradition, albeit scattered with playful notes, such as crispy calf sweetbread flanked by a velvety béarnaise with nasturtium-flavoured vinegar.;Car park,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16440;Château du Mylord;Belgium;Ellezelles;Rue Saint-Mortier 35, Ellezelles, 7890, Belgium;50.7297077;3.6726257;86;false;false;Contemporary;Martin and Nuria Simonart have breathed a new lease of life into this English-looking manor house (1861), a landmark for foodies for many years. Rich in period charm, you can expect a log-burning fire to greet you in winter. The food is high-flying, with a quest for perfection that occasionally borders on daring. Cream of Jerusalem artichoke with coffee-flavoured mushrooms and scallops, all of which jazzed up by a tangy mandarin jelly. Delicacy is what best defines this establishment.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16441;Agnes;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Bodegem;Processiestraat 3, Sint-Martens-Bodegem, 1700, Belgium;50.8621519;4.2149344;71;false;false;Sharing;The restoration of this former presbytery in the picturesque lanes around Sint-Martens-Bodegem Church has preserved the edifice’s authentic character, oozing in subtle charm. Diners are invited to choose from a range of amusing and unusual dishes to share, such as open sushi of river eel, Szechuan pepper and wasabi and sesame seed mayonnaise or traditional sweetbread and mushroom vol-au-vent. The intelligently curated wine list and insightful tips from the sommelier add the final flourish.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16442;Robuust;Belgium;Waregem;Wortegemseweg 115, Waregem, 8790, Belgium;50.8733046;3.4523694;58;false;true;Modern French, French;The contemporary elegance of this delightful villa is more than worthy of a home decoration magazine. Even better, it is flanked by a lovely patio and boasts a small conservatory to the rear. The chef focuses on flavours which he crafts into his own versions of traditional recipes such as classic eels in green herbs and vol-au-vent. High-flying, inspired craftsmanship and lashings of flavour illustrate that Robuust is far from averse to showcasing its delicate facet.;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
16443;La Baita;Belgium;Neerpelt;Kloosterstraat 23, Neerpelt, 3910, Belgium;51.2298674;5.4336964;73;false;false;Italian Contemporary;Authentic aromas and flavours of linguine alla Genovese, thickly cut wagyu picanha, grilled rare or a modern take on cannoli: this enchanting restaurant celebrates all the facets of Italian cuisine. Chef Sandro gets a kick out of mixing techniques and textures, adding his own distinctive hallmark to each dish, whilst remaining true to his homeland’s culinary roots – the chef hails from Marche.;;[]
16444;RAS;Belgium;Antwerpen;Ernest Van Dijckkaai 37, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2191025;4.3942809;32;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The view of the Scheldt River and the docks makes this restaurant's terrace one of the finest in Antwerp! Thanks to all the windows, the water feels omnipresent, even if you are seated inside. Charcoal sketches by Rinus Van de Velde lend an arty feel to the sleek interior. The extensive menu is dominated by traditional favourites. The fried sole is an obvious classic, but for something truly special, try the crispy veal sweetbreads in a brown stock and port sauce. The generous portions certainly go down well. And for those in a hurry, a quick lunch is always available, too.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16446;Esmeralda;Belgium;Knokke;Jozef Nellenslaan 161, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3485924;3.2797893;95;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Stefan Verhasselt has been at the helm of this elegant edifice, next-door to Knokke casino, since 1975. His vast experience can be felt and tasted in every detail and particularly in the choice produce, which is mainly from the sea. He has a flair for transforming Zeebrugge shrimp into crispy fritters and his sole meunière garnished with fresh tartare sauce and piping hot fresh fries is second to none. Rather than complex or fussy preparations, you will be treated to a banquet of classical know-how, illustrated by the house specialty, seabass in a salt crust.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16447;La table du Royal Snail;Belgium;Namur;avenue de la Plante 23, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.4552381;4.862017;31;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This laid-back restaurant is appointed in the same trendy, glamorous vein as the Royal Snail Hotel in which it is housed. The welcoming, casual vibe provides the perfect foil to sample Carl Gillain’s bistronomic vision. The slate menu features a pageant of unconventional bistro dishes and sensibly priced wines. He might add depth to ravioli of turnip with a stock of roast onion and veal, imparting subtle umami, but then again, he may simply pair a juicy entrecote with a fresh, wonderfully light, silky bearnaise sauce. Most of the dishes are designed to be shared, although you may not always wish to do so…;Terrace;[]
16448;Les Potes au Feu;Belgium;Namur;avenue de la Plante 4, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.4562085;4.8621577;90;false;false;Modern French;A couple of pals, Damien Gorjanec and François Schepens, have added a new spin to the bistronomic concept with creativity as their baseline, depicted by locally grown veggies, unorthodox combinations and throbbing sauces. For example, they might mix black and Morello cherries with a cocoa crumble and vanilla ice cream made with unpasteurised milk. A casual, fun vibe bordering on rock ‘n roll with masses of taste in the plate.;Terrace;[]
16449;Barisdam;Belgium;Werken;Werkenstraat 82, Werken, 8610, Belgium;51.0292064;2.9683258;45;true;false;French Contemporary;As chef Puype casts his culinary spell with top-drawer produce such as asparagus or loin of veal, you know you’re in for a magical bistronomic treat. Examples include a ceviche of rockfish with creamy goat’s cheese to offset the acidity and a crunchy medley of finely diced celery and carrots. Recognisable food crafted with flair thanks to gutsy sauces and intelligently balanced generous flavours. A word of advice: Pieter and Virginie’s friendly eatery is ideal for family get togethers.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16450;Yirmi;Belgium;Malonne;Trieux-Scieurs 22, Malonne, 5020, Belgium;50.4377927;4.8075792;93;false;false;Creative French;A meal in this elegant villa starts with the solicitous welcome of Adrien, who will later be your host in the bespoke glazed wine cellar where you are invited to select your own bottle at fixed prices depending on your menu (watch out for bargains!). Jeremy Vandernoot has harnessed his creativity to devising a formula in which you are free to choose the number of courses. Our inspectors were particularly impressed by the chef’s apple brioche and croissant ice cream, served with butterscotch caramel and cider sabayon. The team’s enthusiasm can be tasted in each bite.;Car park;[]
16451;Aster;Belgium;Brussels;Rue Antoine Dansaert 202, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8528859;4.3417099;84;true;false;Creative;Veg, locally caught fish and fire are the raison d’être of this urban eatery at the end of Rue Dansaert. The menu sports a cornucopia of creative combinations and amusing textures that frequently astound. Examples include monkfish underscored by a fascinating butter and sake sauce, while fish liver, steamed in spinach leaf, further highlights the savoury notes and finely chopped lovage adds a powerful final flourish. Aster is well and truly in the zeitgeist thanks to wholehearted, big-boned flavours and perfectly judged nuances.;Counter dining;[]
16452;Pazzo;Belgium;Antwerpen;Oude Leeuwenrui 12, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.226831;4.4066191;66;true;true;Fusion, Italian Contemporary;Ingrid Neven’s jovial, casual eatery with a separate patio is well-known among foodies for its international score and superb wine list (wine bar above the restaurant). Ingrid avows a weakness for Italian recipes and truffles, without forgetting Asian and Middle Eastern notes. The extensive menu features dishes such as risotto al dente with black truffle, Korean-style gnocchi and seabass in mandarin and cardamon. A seasoned chef, Ingrid lures us back with her playful, unconventional approach to cooking.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16453;Cuisine & Nous;Belgium;Tilff;Avenue Joseph Wauters 2, Tilff, 4130, Belgium;50.5672316;5.5835107;88;true;true;French Contemporary;Cuisine & Nous is a no-nonsense eatery, known for its warm, welcoming vibe. Modern materials adorn the characterful walls of this Ardennes edifice. The enthusiastic chef enjoys reworking Gallic recipes, adding his own hallmark signature. Fancy a duck breast in a popcorn crust? His no-holds barred approach to cooking is underscored by his superlative culinary expertise. Exemplary value for money!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16454;The Chick;Belgium;Mechelen;Sint-Romboutskerkhof, 2, Mechelen, 2800, Belgium;51.0297054;4.4785995;63;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Ancient murals and untreated or designer materials paint the picture in this authentic 16C edifice, idyllically located at the foot of Saint Rumbold’s Tower. A glamorous vibe provides the perfect foil for the creative, international set menu. You can expect unusual dishes such as a barbecued slice of watermelon with crumbly feta, pieces of herring, pistachios and crunchy rice noodles. An apparently classical façade hides a treasure trove of surprises. While you’re there, take the time to explore The (wine) Cellar boutique and The Chapel, ideal for events and special occasions.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16455;Savage;Belgium;Ixelles;Rue de la Paix 22, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.835775;4.3651215;99;true;false;Organic, Vegetarian;The trendy natural interior of Savage is perfectly at home in the fashionable Saint-Boniface neighbourhood. The plant-based cuisine is depicted by fascinating combinations of herbs and vegetables, whose varied impressions and textures never fail to surprise. You can choose meat (from the refrigerated meat counter) or fish to accompany your meal, also selected according to sustainable development criteria.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16456;An der Villa;Luxembourg;Steinfort;15 rue de Hobscheid, Steinfort, 8422, Luxembourg;49.6617735;5.9150688;51;false;true;Modern French;Enthusiastic Thomas Murer has taken brasserie cuisine to dizzying new heights. His authentic soul-warming fare, sprinkled in subtle modern details has earned him a devoted crowd of regulars. Orange sorbet and vinaigrette spiked with passion fruit and saffron add a refreshing kick to smoked salmon. The reasonably priced lunchtime menu offers the perfect opportunity to pay a visit to this opulent, upmarket historic villa which tastefully marries old and new!;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16458;Controverse;Belgium;Aalst;Zandberg 6, Aalst, 9300, Belgium;50.932307;4.0834289;18;true;true;Farm to table;Crisp clean lines set the scene of the modern brasserie of De Kluizen Golf Club (overlooking the greens), which is as well suited to a date night as to a business lunch. It rightly defines its cuisine as authentically characterful, with a classical repertory starring vitello tonnato, asparagus à la flamande and sabayon. The ingredients are outstanding, the cooking bang on and the sauces subtly suave. In season, you will also find game dishes like saddle of hare. The lunchtime menu never disappoints!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16459;Au Moriane;Belgium;Liège;En Neuvice 55, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.6446229;5.5775097;48;true;true;Creative, Modern French;This 1693 edifice adds a contemporary touch to the historic character of En Neuvice lane by way of bare stone walls and modern comforts. The exquisitely presented food is the handiwork of a gifted chef who demonstrates his international eclecticism, delving freely into the establishment’s cottage garden for his fruit and veggies. The accent is on tradition first and foremost.;;[]
16460;Gastrobar Hop;Belgium;Leuven;Vaartkom 1a, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8878715;4.7007668;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Hop is a gastrobar that celebrates wine and craft beer. The head-spinning choice is fortunately accompanied by the owner’s knowledgeable insights. Whether you choose an unusual natural wine or a craft beer, the chefs will always find a playful combination to enhance your dish. Eschewing luxury ingredients, they have honed in on the flavours of yesteryear and subtly textured variations. Gourmet dining in a delightfully casual setting that hits the spot every time!;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16461;Antoine;Belgium;Eupen;Stendrich 21, Eupen, 4700, Belgium;50.6266476;6.0225046;80;false;false;Modern Cuisine, French Contemporary;Lisa’s old family home has lost none of its welcoming allure. Today it is a magnificent restaurant, where Lisa offers excellent, mainly German, wine-food pairings. Chef Mirko concocts elegant dishes whose distinctive flavours are jazzed up with a bold individual touch, all of which founded on modern techniques. Examples include a subtly sweet carpaccio of strawberries paired with a bergamot sherbet and a yoghurt ice cream. Whether you plump for a meat, fish or vegetarian score, you can be certain to taste a festival of flavours.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16463;Lily's;Belgium;Brussels;Avenue Emile de Mot 1, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8172272;4.3724589;71;true;false;Contemporary;Lily’s, which recreates the vibe of a Saint Tropez or Los Angeles club in Brussels with elegant, premium materials, a pretty green pergola in summer and dancing at the weekends, has become a hotspot of the Belgian capital. Indulge in a glass of wine or a signature cocktail as you cast your eye over the awesome menu. Familiar Belgian favourites, such as immaculately cooked veal chop with fresh béarnaise sauce, are prepared with the same flair and talent as a ceviche of seabass or truffle taglioni. Attracts A-listers like bees to honey for an unforgettable evening!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16464;Upton;Belgium;Antwerpen;Napelsstraat 42, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2335476;4.410888;78;false;true;Italian, Modern Cuisine;Upton is a hip eatery in a buzzy neighbourhood. Experienced chef, Gianfranco Van de Maele, invites you to sample his globe-trotting approach to food. Start with a cold glass of draught lager, before digging into his succulent fresh pasta, the recipes of which come from his “nonna”. Bisque-flavoured homemade spaghetti and super fresh seafood and shellfish – magnifico! A fascinating modern culinary melting pot that blends Italian authenticity with Asian influences gleaned from his travels.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16465;Un Max de Goût;Belgium;Comblain-au-Pont;quai de l'Ourthe 17, Comblain-au-Pont, 4170, Belgium;50.4767771;5.5785763;50;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The charm of the Ourthe running by the side of the restaurant enhances the contemporary elegance inside. The creative, subtle cuisine of talented Maxime Zimmer underscores flavoursome local specialties. His youthful take on text-book classics stimulates our tastebuds. A restaurant with ambitions!;Terrace;[]
16466;Le Bouton d'Or;Belgium;Casteau;chaussée de Bruxelles 135, Casteau, 7061, Belgium;50.5157846;4.0126838;71;false;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;The soul of this friendly restaurant bears the hallmark of a love of nature. The veggies come from a neighbouring farmer and the chef hunts the game himself. Generous, unfussy cooking at its best. Partridge is one of the chef’s iconic specialties. The lady of the house can be trusted to suggest flawless wine-food pairings.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16467;Deboeveries;Belgium;Deurle;Lijnstraat 2, Deurle, 9831, Belgium;50.9975975;3.6079435;100;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;The regulars to this characterful farmstead (awesome terrace!) know that on Fridays, sole, the house specialty, takes pride of place on chef Bert Deboeverie’s menu. The food is steeped in with flavour and rich in clever contemporary combinations. Choice of menus - the all-inclusive formula is highly recommended. Fine selection of mainly French tipples.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16468;Zicht;Belgium;Geraardsbergen;Guilleminlaan 151, Geraardsbergen, 9500, Belgium;50.7662101;3.8876686;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You can enjoy the knockout view over the Flemish Ardennes as much as you like thanks to Zicht’s immense window walls. The experience is even better on the terrace. A veteran couple pampers you from the start to finish of your meal. Efficient and gracious, Hélène supervises the dining room, while Kwinten concocts subtle Franco-Belgian dishes that reveal his talent and craftsmanship.;Car park,Great view;[]
16469;September.;Belgium;Antwerpen;Minderbroedersrui 7, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.223423;4.4035098;77;false;false;Farm to table, Vegetarian;As you step over the threshold of September, you will immediately find yourself immersed in its zenitude. A stripped-back, minimalist vibe depicts the spacious interior, which is dotted with plants and has soft music playing in the background. It’s as if nature has merged with inner city Antwerp. Every detail of this establishment has been puzzled over and preened from its respect for the produce and attention to the seasons down to the ‘farm to fork’ concept. Veggies are the stars of the show, sometimes served with meat or fish. Ann Van der Auwera’s inventive, expressive cuisine is bold and distinctive and occasionally sprinkled with the odd Italian or Japanese accent. Intense umami flavours are frequently paired with fresh Mediterranean ingredients. It is summertime at September all year round!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16470;CRKL;Belgium;Roeselare;Diksmuidsesteenweg 351a, Roeselare, 8800, Belgium;50.95146;3.09837;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Squares and circles set the scene both for the tableware and CRKL’s romantic interior, decked in white and pink, as in the food. The menu’s goal is clear – add a modern twist to seasonal produce. Subtle interactions between the ingredients, international expertise and sauces that create finely balanced flavours.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16471;Klei;Belgium;Ieper;Grote Markt 11, Ieper, 8900, Belgium;50.8513163;2.8876845;40;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seasonal Cuisine;Inconspicuously located on the historic Grand Place, this cosy restaurant has a somewhat mysterious feel to it. At the helm, an experienced duo showcase their talents. Sommelier Carl Couvreur bowls diners over with his astute recommendations, while chef Jonathan Devogel delivers haute cuisine in which intricate sauces and influences from around the globe bring the flavours to life. Though his creations can be elaborate, they are ultimately defined by their boldness. Think marinated weever as the main ingredient in an aromatic dish with fig and celery in various guises. The short menu never fails to intrigue!;;[]
16472;Pino;Belgium;Overijse;Brusselsesteenweg 505, Overijse, 3090, Belgium;50.7895777;4.4917278;65;true;true;Italian;As soon as you take a seat, you will be served with a few slices of parmesan to whet your appetite. Pino Rigante is the perfect host and an authentic character. With the help of his sons and family, the team bends over backwards to ensure that their flavoursome, generous Italian dishes are irresistible!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16474;De Victorie;Belgium;Linden;Kerkdreef 1, Linden, 3210, Belgium;50.8955759;4.763368;80;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative French;This imposing historic farmstead, opposite the vineyards of Chateau Vandeurzen winery, is depicted by a stylish interior, whose centre piece is a sculpted flock of birds in flight that is most eye catching. The estate’s excellent wines are paired with a Gallic lineup of contemporary leaning. The chef enjoys pairing sweetbread with truffles or pheasant with Fine champagne cognac, adding a personal twist along the way by playing with the tangy freshness of ingredients such as kalamansi, yuzu and wine vinegar. It has proved a hit with fans of familiar flavours who appreciate an added twist.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16475;Clairefontaine;;Luxembourg;9 place de Clairefontaine, 1341, Luxembourg;49.609734;6.1334169;28;false;false;Creative French;Whether it be Bresse chicken or sole, Arnaud Magnier can be relied upon to pamper the ingredients. His classical training shines through in spot-on cooking and intense sauces, although he doesn’t shy away from bolder, more inventive touches. Striking, designer-inspired interior.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16476;Umā;Belgium;Brussels;Rue de la Reinette 8, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8390072;4.3608629;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine, International;Umā stands on a quiet side street near the bustling Porte de Namur. Its white-washed brick outer facade and modern artwork inside are both inviting and attractive. Admire Aurélie Kluyskens at work in the open-plan kitchen, rustling up her own spin on Nikkei cuisine, which she rolls out in a spot-on blend of gutsy Japanese and powerful Peruvian flavours. She adds her signature with subtle spicy notes, imparting a spicy/sweet edge to scallops, courtesy of an espuma of smoked pork. Both the varied à la carte menu and the enticing set menu provide an insight into Ms Kluyskens’ distinctive culinary flair and talent.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16477;Bistrot Blaise;Belgium;Marche-en-Famenne;Rue Porte Haute 5, Marche-en-Famenne, 6900, Belgium;50.2265169;5.3451207;64;false;true;French Contemporary;A palette of ochre and pastels make for an inviting atmosphere in this cosy bistro. Dining here is fun. Hanna, who knows the wine list like the back of her hand, immediately makes you feel at home. Chef F-X confidently asserts his distinctive culinary style, which is characterised by Gallic indulgence, phenomenal technique and a wide range of contemporary notes. The chalkboard lists exquisitely seasoned dishes that feature combinations such as langoustine, pig's foot croquette and cauliflower. Occasionally playful, this is satisfying cuisine that celebrates the natural flavours of the produce. The team's enthusiasm is infectious!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16478;L'O à la Bouche;Belgium;Wépion;rue Armand de Wasseige 1, Wépion, 5100, Belgium;50.4141652;4.8802927;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine, French;Tightly packed tables, the characteristic hum of a busy brasserie and the smiling faces of satisfied diners bear witness to the flair and talent of this chef who customises characteristic brasserie dishes. Risotto is a staple of the menu, without forgetting the knockout marriage of a 64° egg, asparagus, eel, bacon and emulsion of haddock. The pain perdu is simply out of this world!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16479;Vintage;Belgium;Kontich;Rijkerooistraat 14, Kontich, 2550, Belgium;51.1156516;4.4380212;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Cyril Moulin and Florian Vanderhoeven craft intelligent cuisine that is both bold and polished. Big-boned sauces and playful fresh nuances set the culinary scene. For example, they may pair textbook perfect cod with seaweed, pistachios and a zest of lemon, while velvety green asparagus, a light frothy espuma of seaweed and a pistachio crumble conclude the dish. The chefs conjure up recipes in which outstanding ingredients are delicately and harmoniously assembled. Steven Wullaert suggests insightful food-wine pairings. The scene takes place in a tastefully revamped farmstead surrounded by meadows: huge windows, exposed beams and works of art. A gourmet getaway destination par excellence!;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
16480;La Cuisine du Côté Vert;Belgium;Waterloo;chaussée de Bruxelles 200g, Waterloo, 1410, Belgium;50.7194273;4.3973429;67;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Creative French;The restaurant of Le Côté Vert Hotel unsurprisingly bears the hallmark of nature. Natural materials adorn the interior, whose floor to ceiling windows command a splendid view of the garden. Vegetables are the stars of the show in the chefs’ updated recipes, without forgetting meat and fish. The focus is on allowing each natural ingredient to shout its name.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16481;Le Val d'Amblève;Belgium;Stavelot;route de Malmédy 7, Stavelot, 4970, Belgium;50.3976311;5.939267;50;false;true;French, Modern Cuisine;Le Val d’Amblève has had a very successful facelift! The terrace in the garden is exquisite. The chef illustrates his firm grasp of new trends whilst enhancing classical flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16482;Brasserie Côté Cour;Luxembourg;Bourglinster;8 rue du Château, Bourglinster, 6162, Luxembourg;49.7025368;6.2163284;91;false;false;Creative, Organic;This nostalgic brasserie enjoys an idyllic location in the courtyard of Bourglinster Castle. The terrace on the rampart affords stunning views! The food is mostly plant based, but there is also a separate menu including fish and meat. The cauliflower "risotto" combined with marinated tomatoes and crushed hazelnuts is a shining example of this cuisine, which is inspired by the local nature and is all about bold flavours.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16483;Le Petit Axhe;Belgium;Waremme;rue de Petit-Axhe 12, Waremme, 4300, Belgium;50.6858;5.2359757;87;true;true;Farm to table;A journey through the lovely Liège countryside, the owner’s delightful welcome and chef Claes’ scrumptious dishes: get ready to treat yourself from start to finish, safe in the knowledge you are in the hands of an experienced and accomplished chef. You may taste a flawlessly fresh fillet of whiting flanked by an elegant beurre blanc. No compromise on quality is ever tolerated, all the better because the prices make sense.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16484;La Cuisine d'un Gourmand;Belgium;Profondeville;avenue Général Gracia 8, Profondeville, 5170, Belgium;50.38606;4.877166;30;true;false;Creative, Creative French;Ambitious John Maes is a genuine good food lover. His mission in life is to source the best regional ingredients, to unfetter his creativity and to please or surprise his patrons with subtle fare. Outstanding quality at affordable prices. The tasteful, modern interior commands a fine view of the river Meuse.;Great view,Terrace;[]
16485;Découverte;Belgium;Ieper;Lange Torhoutstraat 22, Ieper, 8900, Belgium;50.853813;2.8900075;60;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Take a seat in this modern, elegant restaurant by the ramparts and you may hear the moving ‘Last Post’ ceremony that takes place at the nearby Menin Gate every evening at 8pm… Local Westhoek delicacies, cooked creatively and playfully, are rich in the distinctive, crisp flavours that depict the spontaneous, market-fresh cuisine of chef Jeroen. Gracious Séverine can be relied upon for her insightful wine-food pairing tips. Book a room at the B&B, ideal to explore the fascinating heritage of Ypres.;Terrace;[]
16486;L'Air de Rien;Belgium;Esneux;Place du Vieux Tilleul 14, Esneux, 4130, Belgium;50.5295679;5.5904606;17;true;false;Creative;A log-burning fire is the centrepiece of this stylishly converted 18C farmstead. In his splendid glass-fronted kitchen, chef Diffels can be seen barbecuing most of the main ingredients, which are largely locally sourced. These take centre stage in particularly creative dishes featuring rich sauces and complex flavours. Fermentation adds a vibrant twist. The chef has a gift for coaxing the best out of every ingredient. He celebrates the earthiness of celeriac, for instance, cooking it in a salt crust and combining it with Comté cheese and sherry. This chef has an artistic bent, and his dishes are truly original.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16487;L'O de Source;Belgium;Sart;Station 32, Sart, 4845, Belgium;50.5006455;5.9569288;41;true;true;Farm to table;The old railway line is visible from the well-tended garden, but this former station is now the venue of a pleasant restaurant. You will be pampered by an enthusiastic couple. Chef Fisset, a keen believer in sustainable farming, concocts food that features subtle technique with rich flavours. A fitting tribute to the outstanding produce of Liege.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16488;Stad 10;Belgium;Hamont;Stad 10, Hamont, 3930, Belgium;51.250824;5.543492;95;false;true;Modern French, Creative French;Bert Brouwers has set up shop in Stad 10 in Hamont, rolling out his considerable know-how to great effect. He trained with the top chefs of Limburg and this experience can be tasted in his personal takes on pure-bred French fare, jazzed up with the odd creative touch. Japanese and fresh acidic flavours frequently find their way onto the menu. For example, he might slip in a hint of grapefruit and daikon winter radishes to exalt a dish of Anjou pigeon. The natural zen vibe of Stad 10 is emblematic of both the interior decoration and the food.;;[]
16489;Nesta;Belgium;Sint-Pieters-Leeuw;Bergensesteenweg 500, Sint-Pieters-Leeuw, 1600, Belgium;50.7753731;4.2684555;42;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;As you enter the lifestyle boutique, you will notice the snug restaurant at the rear leading into a pretty garden, where, as you sit on the patio, you may even be forgiven for thinking you’re in Italy! Chef Kayes Ghourabi soaks his recipes in Italian sunshine as recognisable Mediterranean aromas and flavours unfold and captivate our tastebuds. Examples include a pedigree vitello tonnato or a breast of duck with a hazelnut crumble and a drizzling of subtle cooking juices. Bang on every time and always open to new twists.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16490;De drie ridders;Belgium;Gijverinkhove;Weegschede 1, Gijverinkhove, 8691, Belgium;50.9702736;2.6776956;68;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;As you cross the threshold and see the red and green colour scheme of the decor, the huge fireplace and period flooring, you will fancy yourself back in 18C West Flanders. So take a seat and soak up the splendour. Emily and Bart are passionate about their work. This manifests itself in their choice of mostly local ingredients, their reinterpretations of time-honoured recipes and the finesse of their creativity. They are committed to using traditional cooking techniques as evidenced in the medium-rare duck fillet with a fine crust, accompanied by glazed vegetables and a jus de canard that incorporates the subtle bitterness of Picon. The carefully curated wine list gives exposure to smaller producers. This is cuisine with soul, bundled into a single set menu.;;[]
16491;Couleur Rouge;Belgium;Eupen;Gospertstraße 22, Eupen, 4700, Belgium;50.6305717;6.0321484;38;false;false;Fusion, Asian Influences;Wonton, mashed potato with wasabi illustrate the happy marriage between Asian sophistication and French gastronomy. Save room for the splendid platter of Belgian cheeses. The delightful terrace will almost make you forget you are in the heart of Eupen!;Terrace;[]
16492;Wagyu;Belgium;Durbuy;Rue du Comte Théodule d'Ursel 14, Durbuy, 6940, Belgium;50.3518037;5.4550233;84;true;true;Meats and Grills, Grills;(Temporarily closed due to a fire) Wout Bru is at the helm of this chic BBQ restaurant. Vintage lighting sets the scene in the tasteful interior, creating an intimate vibe. The open grill, striking bar counter and the dry-ageing fridge all catch the eye. You can expect prime beef from breeds like Wagyu and Holstein, gutsy sauces and a host of meat-based recipes, concocted with consummate culinary know-how.;Terrace;[]
16493;Octopus;Belgium;De Panne;Walckierstraat 8, De Panne, 8660, Belgium;51.1037065;2.5917259;85;false;false;Farm to table;Claude and Sylvie bend over backwards to pamper guests in their seafood eatery near the seawall. Sylvie’s warm welcome and service are framed by distinctive artwork (of octopi), while Claude sensitively adds a new spin to a classical repertory, all of which in a playful vein. Grilled pork fritters, pedigree vol-au-vent, fish from the North Sea (his passion) or rice pudding with strawberries: it is always a pleasure to return to the Octopus.;Terrace;[]
16494;La Cravache;Belgium;Rekkem;Gentstraat 215, Rekkem, 8930, Belgium;50.7622;3.2128479;44;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The culinary classics have no secrets for Koen Devos, whose team can be relied on to add the odd contemporary touch to pedigree dishes. You can expect a repertory of premium produce such as lobster and partridge and recipes that show a reverence for authentic flavours, albeit with modern side dishes. Chef Devos is a horse lover, as you will quickly discover when you admire the elegant interior of this lavish villa. The B&B offers a view of the horses grazing from the windows.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16495;'t Notenhof;Belgium;Londerzeel;Meerstraat 113, Londerzeel, 1840, Belgium;51.0084041;4.3087944;96;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Everything works like clockwork in the lovely ‘t Notenhof establishment. The seasoned owner welcomes guests, sharing his insightful wine tips along the way, while the rich flavours of classical cuisine, albeit with a modern twist, have no secrets for his wife. Eels, Anjou pigeon and seabass are frequent guest stars on her deftly cooked and generously served menu. The lunchtime menu is a steal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16496;Chez Louis;Belgium;Glimes;chaussée de Jodoigne 7, Glimes, 1315, Belgium;50.6748783;4.8272052;86;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Traditional Cuisine;Chez Louis is a friendly eatery with something for everyone. The menu features Belgian family favourites such as sole meunière and veal kidneys in mustard, as well as chef Lekeu’s more sophisticated culinary score, all of which is depicted by classical generosity. From November to February, a seafood bar is available at weekends. The extensive range of choice is undeniably one of the trump cards of this establishment, as are mussels, in season.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16497;Hof Ter Doest;Belgium;Lissewege;Ter Doeststraat 4, Lissewege, 8380, Belgium;51.2822194;3.2018559;93;true;false;Grills, Traditional Cuisine;A 17C monastic farmstead and its 13C barn depicts the picturesque setting of this country restaurant, run by the Dendooven family. You will taste delicious local turf (beef and poultry in particular) and surf (oysters and lobsters from the tank) produce. Hearty, wholesome cooking such as crispy shrimp fritters or Belgian Blanc Bleu beef roasted in a wood-fired oven. Luxurious guestrooms for overnight stays.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16498;Ma Passion;Belgium;Roeselare;Diksmuidsesteenweg 159, Roeselare, 8800, Belgium;50.9466193;3.1147421;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Kris and elegant Sandra share a passion for fine food and fine wine! This handsome townhouse with a lovely patio tastefully blends old and new with an inimitable Belgian knack for colours and materials. The chef voluntarily tries his hand at different styles, mixing the classical flavours of foie gras and sweetbread with subtle sauces and fresh, acidic side dishes, demonstrating his playful side and virtuoso talent.;Terrace;[]
16499;Bulthaup;Belgium;Gosselies;route Nationale 5, 193, Gosselies, 6041, Belgium;50.4743088;4.442459;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef Philippe Stevens knows how to pamper his diners. All year long he can be found in this stylish kitchen shop, conjuring up market-fresh fare with a focus on taste and presentation. This modern chef, whose technique is matchless, delicately coaxes the flavour out of choice ingredients. Ask for a table near the kitchen range!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16500;La Brasserie Xavier;Belgium;Nalinnes;route de Philippeville 7, Nalinnes, 6120, Belgium;50.3419888;4.4736091;67;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;This vast brasserie (thankfully, with highly efficient service! ) is divided into several areas, including a fine terrace. The good brasserie food makes ample use of top quality produce.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16501;L'artiste;Belgium;Falaën;rue de la Gare 85, Falaën, 5522, Belgium;50.2914199;4.8022184;27;true;false;Creative;In the heart of the Ardennes forest, make a beeline for this old railway station decorated in modern style. Chef Depuydt’s creative and contrasted menu combines originality with subtlety and the dishes overflow with details that pay tribute to local produce and Asian influences. Culinary art at its best!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16502;d'Afspanning;Belgium;Beernem;Bloemendalestraat 2, Beernem, 8730, Belgium;51.1433263;3.3398125;31;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Dark floor tiles and bare brick walls set the scene in this historic edifice of Beernem, albeit elegantly paired with modern fixtures and fittings. Diners can choose between cosy nooks or the spacious glazed extension. The varied menu appeals both to fans of classical fare and to those keen to try out world cuisine. The veteran chef is equally at home with the ubiquitous shrimp fritter as with an Asian take on steak tartare. Honest, wholesome fare.;Terrace;[]
16503;D'Oude Pastorie;Belgium;Lochristi;Hijfte-Center 40, Lochristi, 9080, Belgium;51.1116079;3.8124102;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Jan Audenaert believes in simplicity before all else, mixing vegetables and exotic herbs to compose stunningly presented dishes. His creativity shines through in the detail he lavishes on the side dishes, illustrated by his upside-down pumpkin pie which is served with a gutsy breast of pheasant. Nothing leaves his kitchen that hasn’t been endlessly pondered and puzzled over. We recommend his lunchtime menus. The minimalist interior of this restored presbytery suits this culinary offering down to a T!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16504;a food affair;Belgium;Gent;Hoogstraat 58, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0548519;3.7136138;44;false;false;Asian;As soon as you set foot in this eatery of oriental inspiration, you will feel the serene vibe, further enhanced by the exquisite terrace to the rear. Chef Locquet shares his passion for Thailand and Vietnam. Traditional recipes made with first-class ingredients and dishes that shout the talent and deft touch of their chef. An Asian excursion steeped in subtlety and enthusiasm.;Terrace;[]
16505;Vos;Belgium;Lokeren;Groenstraat 29, Lokeren, 9160, Belgium;51.1096877;4.0209253;47;false;false;Modern French, Creative French;This trendy joint is unusually located in a tennis club. The Audenaert brothers have successfully taken up the challenge. The youthful chefs’ hallmark can be tasted in mouth - watering dishes. Tasty, creative and flawlessly crafted.;Terrace;[]
16506;Le Coriandre;Belgium;Watermael-Boitsfort;rue Middelbourg 21, Watermael-Boitsfort, 1170, Belgium;50.795808;4.4176648;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The name of this restaurant gives a hint as to the chef’s love of Asia, which inspires his subtle, contemporary cuisine. Intense flavours at good value for money. Cooking workshops on Saturday morning.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16507;Pegasus;Belgium;Poperinge;Guido Gezellestraat 7, Poperinge, 8970, Belgium;50.8556729;2.7286526;46;false;true;Modern French;Pegasus is poised to take wing at the entrance to this restaurant housed in a magnificent 18C abode. While you immerse yourself in the classical interior (woodwork, old tiles), run your eye over the menu. This will reveal a wide choice of balanced dishes, all of which are made with fine produce. Lovely terrace.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16508;Le Coq en Pâte;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Lambert;Tomberg 259, Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, 1200, Belgium;50.8442145;4.42034;27;false;false;Italian;The Bacchetta family has been regaling diners since 1972 in their stylish establishment. You will taste the best of fine Italian fare in the company of a loyal band of regulars. Chef Olivier delves into Mediterranean tradition, adding a creative spin that combines visual flair and a love of contrasts. His veal alla Milanese and his asparagus risotto are second to none. The lunchtime set menu is a firm favourite with the regulars.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16509;Les Petits Oignons;Belgium;Brussels;rue de la Régence 25, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8392201;4.3551061;49;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Country cooking;Outdoors, diners are sheltered from the bustling Rue de la Régence by wooden decking, while indoors, a luxurious brasserie décor provides the perfect foil to a lineup of Gallic classics and stellar Mediterranean fare. The extensive menu offers dishes that star time-honoured family favourites like calf’s brains in a zesty lemon sauce, tagliata of beef, veal kidneys in mustard and desserts such as French toast. Les Petits Oignons delivers spot-on cooking every time as it bends over backwards to pamper and spoil its regular customers and passers-by in the Sablon district.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16510;Maxens;Belgium;Saint-Symphorien;chaussée du Roi Baudouin 117, Saint-Symphorien, 7030, Belgium;50.4388781;4.0117248;53;false;true;Modern French;Stéphane Grulois is a man of many talents and the stylish, cosy interior of this arty restaurant is also his work. He is, however, first and foremost a gifted chef. His love of French cuisine shines through the distinctive flavours of his inspired recipes, to which he enjoys adding a new spin and also inviting fine Belgian delicacies.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16511;Le Cirque;Belgium;Belsele;Nieuwe Baan 88b, Belsele, 9111, Belgium;51.1448332;4.1035675;100;true;true;Creative;Come in, come in - take a seat and enjoy and the show! Do not be misled by the apparently low - key interior - the climax of the performance comes on the plate! The chef is a fervent disciple of modern culinary techniques and masterfully produces recipes whose texture, structure and colour are both stunning and delicious. A treat for your taste buds!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16512;Potiron;Belgium;Kasterlee;Geelsebaan 73, Kasterlee, 2460, Belgium;51.2360776;4.970554;35;true;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Friendly Dirk and Sophie aren’t shy of demonstrating their phenomenal know-how. They smoke their own salmon, the ice cream is homemade, and they are justly proud of their 3-acre vegetable garden (visits by appointment). Vegetables and aromatic herbs add a playful twist and authentic purity to updated recipes. Distinctive French cuisine that eschews jargon and fancy frills.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16513;Pip-Margraff;Belgium;Saint Vith;Hauptstraße 7, Saint Vith, 4780, Belgium;50.2793923;6.1269726;65;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This family - run hotel restaurant has been open for business since 1876. The customers come for its essentially classical menu. The chef keeps pace with the seasons and game is one of the house specialties. The rooms are flawlessly kept, as is the well - being centre.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16514;Greenroom;Belgium;Perk;Vilvoordsesteenweg 82, Perk, 1820, Belgium;50.9350626;4.4887077;76;true;true;Modern French;Make a beeline for the terrace to make the most of the lush green countryside. If the weather is fickle, never mind, the interior is equally attractive. The Green Room doesn’t distinguish between starters and main courses, which gives you more freedom to compose your menu. A classic seafood béarnaise or Flemish-style asparagus with a modern twist – sea lavender and guanciale. The bargain-priced wine list (available to take home) adds the final flourish.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16515;Salto!;Belgium;Lier;Rechtestraat 18, Lier, 2500, Belgium;51.1301574;4.5725554;77;true;true;Farm to table;At this hip urban bistro, ingredient quality is paramount. As far as chef Duys is concerned, that goes as much for the Brussels sprouts as for the sea bass. He is also not averse to working with traditionally overlooked produce, such as pig's head. Whether he is rustling up a vegetable dish based on winter leeks, or pan-searing pheasant to be paired with a fine champagne sauce: generosity is key. His creations are not unnecessarily complicated, but they are brimming with flavour. Diners can also look forward to an expertly curated selection of wines and beers.;Terrace;[]
16516;De l'Ogenblik;Belgium;Brussels;Galerie des Princes 1, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8483643;4.3545868;90;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Belgian;A loyal band of regulars add a warm, friendly vibe to this former café, which has lost none of its authentic charm since it first opened its doors back in 1969. Classical repertory, bistro dishes and a fine selection of seasonal suggestions.;Terrace;[]
16517;Het land aan de Overkant;Belgium;Heverlee;Léon Schreursvest 85, Heverlee, 3001, Belgium;50.8708691;4.7120192;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Leuven’s urbanites don’t hesitate to desert their city centre in favour of a seat in this smart edifice. Natural light, artwork and a lovely terrace all combine to paint a pleasing portrait. First run your eye over the beverage menu and start with a refreshing glass of Gueuze beer, before moving on to peruse the wine list. The exquisitely presented dishes reveal unexpected combinations of ingredients, such as al dente confit of celeriac with cream of goat’s cheese and foie gras, smoked eel and chilled consommé of celeriac, eels and verjuice. At lunchtime, there is only a single set menu.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16518;La Régalade;Belgium;Toernich;Burewee 26, Toernich, 6700, Belgium;49.6511752;5.7792332;68;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Peaceful, relaxed and friendly describe both the village of Toernich and the Régalade restaurant. The chef rustles up immaculately prepared contemporary fare whose value for money cannot be beaten.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16519;Epices et Nous;Belgium;Erpent;chaussée de Marche 561, Erpent, 5101, Belgium;50.4422171;4.9046931;49;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Modern French;Chef Delvigne regularly calls upon oriental spices to add subtlety to his recipes. For example, a saffron sauce adds depth to a stew of megrim and lobster. Spices form the backbone of his cooking, oozing in generosity and free of fatuitous frills. Everything is crafted from scratch and the extensive menu further adds to the appeal. Finally, the casual serene vibe is delightfully contagious.;Terrace;[]
16520;De Refugie;Belgium;Tienen;Kapucijnenstraat 75, Tienen, 3300, Belgium;50.8048062;4.9466545;89;false;true;Farm to table, French;Franco-Belgian foodies are in seventh heaven in this eatery in a friendly neighbourhood. You are first greeted by your gracious hostess, before you sample the manifold talents of chef Van Vlemmeren. He prepares the food to order each time and cannot be faulted for his exquisite sauces or impeccable technique. The sole is gently sautéed in butter, the butter sauce is sprinkled with parsley and the crispy fries are piping hot. Good food worth writing home about - the epitome of bistronomic dining!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16521;U Eat & Sleep Antwerp;Belgium;Antwerpen;Nassaustraat 42, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2299142;4.4053518;49;true;true;Modern Cuisine, French;U Eat & Sleep is one of the hotspots of the buzzy Eilandje district thanks to a phenomenal view over the MAS and marina and a glammed-up interior oozing in vibrant sensuality. After kicking off your meal with knockout cocktails and tapas, we recommend the extensive menu which features playful, light dishes as well as big-boned brasserie classics. Whether you opt for a sole meunière or a vegetarian dish of aubergine, sesame and miso, you can rely on the establishment’s funky ethos: affordable luxury!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16522;Appelsveer;Belgium;Appels;Hoofdstraat 175, Appels, 9200, Belgium;51.0293084;4.0422057;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;As you bicycle along the banks of the Scheldt, Appelsveer cannot fail to be a welcoming sight. This listed house is flanked by a fine terrace overlooking the countryside. The chef serves regional dishes, to which he adds his own creative flair, using modern techniques. You may also be tempted by the “ice house”.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16523;Dolce Amaro;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;chaussée de Charleroi 115, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8293017;4.3556609;95;false;true;Italian;As you admire the mural depicting Piazza del Campo in Sienna and the patio to the rear, you may almost forget you’re in Brussels’ Louise district. Dolce Amaro is a 100% authentic, bustling Italian trattoria. The food is equally genuine: orecchiette al dente in an aroma-packed tomato sauce and juicy chunks of pork or super-fresh seabass exquisitely paired with melt-in-the-mouth aubergine… Outstanding flavours that will knock the socks off your tastebuds. Let’s not forget the wine list, an Aladdin’s Cave of Italian tipples.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16524;Riva;Belgium;Liège;esplanade Albert Ier 7, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.63036;5.571552;51;false;true;French, Belgian;Bathed in natural light, this striking minimalist edifice boasts both a holiday vibe and a luxurious designer edge. All of which is further enhanced by the drop-dead view over the Meuse from the idyllically placed terrace. Live lobster, which can be seen in tanks as you enter, is prepared different ways ranging from a familiar pasta dish to a Thai-inspired recipe. Brasserie classics such as filet américain with fries and vol-au-vent are reworked to suit a contemporary palate without losing their original DNA. Riva upholds the best of brasserie traditions and all its trappings!;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
16525;Mardaga;Belgium;As;Stationsstraat 121, As, 3665, Belgium;51.0057989;5.6023267;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The oldest hotel of Limbourg gracefully marries period fixtures with modern details. This classical-contemporary patchwork extends to the elegant food, depicted by classical recipes, gutsy sauces and subtle nuances whose fresh, acidic notes add a final flourish to an intelligently crafted menu. Legible flavours which bear the hallmark of gifted chefs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16526;La Marée;Belgium;Brussels;rue de Flandre 99, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8527965;4.3457917;37;true;true;Seafood;Everything is traditional, big-boned and wholesome from the homemade shrimp fritters and cod cooked in butter with a fresh tartar sauce and piping hot fries to the velvety custard tart, with which the chef celebrates her Portuguese roots: such are the delicacies conjured up by Teresa Alves for her diners. An authentic Brussels’ bistro steeped in vintage nostalgia to the delight of a mixed crowd of regulars. A classic seafood restaurant in which time seems to have stood still.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16527;Le Vismet;Belgium;Brussels;place Sainte-Catherine 23, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8511041;4.349947;18;false;true;Seafood;The Vismet (Brussels’ fish market) is a stone’s throw from this traditional restaurant, as quickly becomes apparent. The ambience is relaxed, the service typical of Brussels and the food scrumptious. Fish and shellfish take pride of place in dishes with an emphasis on fresh, generous portions.;Terrace;[]
16528;Le 13;Belgium;Libramont;rue des Alliés 17, Libramont, 6800, Belgium;49.9176973;5.3842936;60;true;false;Farm to table;Fashionably revamped manor house: Panton chairs, designer lighting, fashionable colours and a large wall board that forms the menu. Contemporary cuisine and terrace facing the station.;Terrace;[]
16529;Cum Laude;Belgium;Leuven;Groot Begijnhof 14, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8714684;4.6968244;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The rich heritage of the Grand Béguinage provides the perfect foil for the bold contemporary interior of Cum Laude. The plating is exquisite, while contrasting textures, finely crafted ingredients and crisp flavours set the scene for suave dining tailored to today’s appetites. A word of advice: often fully booked at lunchtime.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16530;L'Angelo Rosso;Belgium;Sint-Truiden;Brustem-Dorp 154, Sint-Truiden, 3800, Belgium;50.8030113;5.2204995;63;true;false;Italian;Welcome to the lair of the Catania family. Filippo welcomes patrons to a smart restaurant flanked by a lovely garden terrace. Chef Roberta, his partner, conjures up a feast of pedigree Italian classics with a modern spin. She has a preference for simplicity, creating intense flavours steeped in Mediterranean exuberance, illustrated by taglioni al dente served with a peppery velvet parmesan sauce, crispy pancetta, a 63° boiled egg and a lavish grating of truffle. You may be interested to know that sgroppino sorbet (vodka, prosecco and lemon) is served before the main course. As for the titbits served with coffee – they are truly squisito!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16531;Culinair;Belgium;Lauwe;Dronckaertstraat 508, Lauwe, 8930, Belgium;50.7932037;3.2053376;65;true;false;Creative;The refined interior and gracious welcome are a foretaste of the exquisite culinary experience awaiting the diner. You will be able to observe the chef at work, wielding modern culinary techniques as he updates classical dishes. The same desire to pamper guests is palpable in the modern B&B of the Culinair.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16532;Les Amourettes;Belgium;Dinant;place Saint-Nicolas 11, Dinant, 5500, Belgium;50.2562063;4.9159584;66;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Fuchsia, turquoise blue and red paint the colourful picture that frames this endearing establishment. The classical, flavoursome cuisine is greatly appreciated, as is the pleasant terrace in fine weather. Delightful service.;Terrace;[]
16533;Table Vaccin;Belgium;Oostmalle;Herentalsebaan 26, Oostmalle, 2390, Belgium;51.2982395;4.7352139;56;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Veteran chef Ivan Daelemans is equally at home with classical Belgian, Gallic and Italian cuisine. His impressive culinary skill can be sampled in the magnificent former home of a doctor, done up in a modern vein. The dishes are intended to be shared, but you can order individual portions. As you dig into timeless classics such as vitello tonnato, tomatoes stuffed with shrimps or a perfect poached egg, served with a light mousseline, al dente asparagus and hand-shelled shrimps, you remember why such dishes remain so popular. Even better when washed down with a fine glass of wine – the perfect vaccine for foodies!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16534;Chou;Belgium;Ixelles;place de Londres 4, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8376088;4.3681598;100;false;false;Farm to table, Traditional Cuisine;Chef Abdelhakim Akandar has been the darling (chou in colloquial French) of the European civil servants who work in the area and also of a loyal crowd of locals for a decade now. His gastronomic bistro is the quintessence of Mediterranean extravagance and exuberance. He may underscore a ballotine of Malines poultry with subtle side dishes and a bisque sauce or pair a ravioli of gutsy oxtail with Emmental, and don’t get us started on the exquisite rack of lamb… The extensive menu is quite simply irresistible.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16535;Moretti;Belgium;Hasselt;Havermarkt 23, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9293749;5.3356981;17;true;false;Italian;Check out the goodies lined up in La Cantina delicatessen before taking a seat on the terrace or indoors, in the cosy dining room laid out around an open-plan kitchen. Moretti knows how to put on a show of mouthwatering dishes that illustrate the manifold facets of Italian cucina. Tiana and Alexander curate a concise menu at lunchtime with a wide range of pasta dishes and a more modern lineup in the evenings. Textbook perfect vitello tonnato, homemade pasta flanked by an aromatic sauce and painstakingly crafted desserts: if you’re hankering for an authentic escapade to sunny Italy, make a beeline to Moretti.;Counter dining;[]
16536;Restaurant Dirkjan Decock;Belgium;Kortrijk;Groeningelaan 22, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.8273133;3.2759463;53;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Dirkjan and Hilde warmly welcome guests to their stylish establishment depicted by a cosy, tranquil vibe and flanked by an exquisite patio. Chef Decock enthusiastically gets on with the job in his open-plan kitchen. He works with top-notch ingredients, creatively preparing vegetables and also adding the odd hint of exoticism to jazz up the dishes. Stripped-back, subtle and fascinating food.;Terrace;[]
16537;Maxime Colin;Belgium;Kraainem;Pastoorkesweg 1, Kraainem, 1950, Belgium;50.8627475;4.4684889;53;true;true;Creative French;Maxime Colin’s artistically appointed romantic establishment was made for a date night (or lunch), while the patio, tucked away in the garden of Jourdain castle, drips with alfresco charm come summertime. The menu quickly reveals the chef’s passion for stellar ingredients and international influences. His modern culinary style features subtlety, spot-on craftsmanship and a constant quest for innovation. For example, he may coat scallops wrapped in a cabbage leaf in a house-made XO sauce and pair them with a salad of green peas jazzed up by a zest of refreshing lemon juice.;Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16538;Schatteman;Belgium;Hertsberge;Kruisstraat 13, Hertsberge, 8020, Belgium;51.1072586;3.2825263;42;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This imposing villa tucked away in the woods is a real gem. Modern artwork, a log burning fire and a wine cellar depict the stylish scene. While Marieke attentively spoils guests in the dining room, Gregory demonstrates his inventive flair in the kitchen. His creativity frequently surprises diners, but always subtly and delicately.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16539;ROSS;Belgium;Hasselt;Dorpsstraat 34, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9324691;5.3352857;67;true;false;Creative French;Glenn Ross often waves a hi to guests from his kitchen opening onto the buzzy dining room. The trendy vibe is the perfect foil for creative Gallic cuisine, paired with exotic delicacies and modern techniques. Perennial favourites like bavette steak and chocolate tart are heart-warmingly nostalgic, albeit stamped with the chef’s subtle personal hallmark.;Terrace;[]
16540;InVINcible;Belgium;Antwerpen;Haarstraat 7, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2204851;4.397873;78;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Creative French;Take a seat at the counter and soak up the warm atmosphere of inVINcible. You can admire chef Burssens and his team crafting traditional Gallic bistro fare. Examples include seabream in a sea salt crust for two, veal kidneys with green peas, Holstein entrecote steak, rare and flanked with a bone marrow, mustard seed and anchovy butter… Big boned, heroic flavours overflowing in character are the hallmark here. The wine list is equally first-rate, particularly thanks to a splendid choice of wines by the glass. You can even ask to taste your tipple before choosing – further proof that inVINcible is determined to bend over backwards to pamper its guests.;Air conditioning;[]
16541;De Ceder;Belgium;Kruibeke;Molenstraat 1, Kruibeke, 9150, Belgium;51.1762334;4.3156731;85;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Vintage black and white photos, the father-in-law’s old bicycle and a Berkel meat slicer offset this restaurant’s elegant, fresh interior. De Ceder has been a blue-ribbon establishment in the area for some 40 years now. The chef knows all the classics of Franco-Belgian cuisine and often whips things up at the last minute, as is demonstrated by his steak with a subtle pepper sauce and fresh fries. He’s also keen on full-bodied oriental spices and Asian notes. We warrant you will adore the attractive wine list and, why not, even treat yourself to a night in the B&B…;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16542;Va et Vient;Belgium;Kortrijk;Handboogstraat 20, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.82977;3.2661128;83;false;true;Farm to table, Modern French;A sweeping view of the Lys River and the Broel Towers thanks to the establishment’s huge windows and riverside terrace awaits diners. A “rough and refined” (their words) décor provides the perfect foil to Matthias Speybrouck’s creativity, which shines through in recipes that star local veggies and fish from the North Sea, jazzed up with fresh acidic, even quirky (their words again) notes, while exotic ingredients are crafted into punchy sauces. Subtle cuisine throbbing with character.;Terrace;[]
16543;Toucan sur Mer;Belgium;Ixelles;avenue Louis Lepoutre 17, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8198588;4.3588061;36;false;false;Seafood;How about an impressive skate dish with capers, oysters opened behind the seafood counter or a sumptuous seafood platter? This lively bistro serves up wonderfully fresh delicacies from the sea. Despite its lack of pretensions Toucan sur Mer definitely holds its own against the grander restaurants on the coast.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16544;August Wijnbar;Belgium;Sint-Kwintens-Lennik;Alfred Algoetstraat 2b, Sint-Kwintens-Lennik, 1750, Belgium;50.805849;4.1560607;76;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Sam Verstuyf’s pleasantly hip eatery, August, is infectiously lively and gloriously unstuffy. Pajottenland produce takes pride of place in the youthful chef’s creations, to which he adds a dash of originality. Fascinating flavours, a passion for veggies and sophisticated side dishes, without forgetting finely balanced sauces. His creativity knows no bounds. Even better, the fascinating wine list is not only enticing but also at drinker-friendly prices.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16545;Bruut;Belgium;Brugge;Meestraat 9, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2089374;3.2292118;36;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The initial impression of romanticism conjured up by the historic edifice in which Bruut is located, quickly gives way to a pared-down, almost brutal interior that is emblematic of its colourful, rock ‘n roll chef, Bruno Timperman. He crafts a single surprise menu that elegantly showcases his unconventional streak and technical ingenuity. He may pair the breast and thighs of slow-cooked partridge in a winter recipe with cèpes, a gutsy jus of the carcass, thyme, marinated pine buds and capers marinated in garlic. “When food meets wine” is the baseline…;Counter dining;[]
16546;Brasserie Taste;Belgium;Vilvoorde;Leuvensesteenweg 331, Vilvoorde, 1800, Belgium;50.9233068;4.4517068;26;false;true;Classic Cuisine;The large windows, fireplace and marble counter are sure to draw your eye as you enter this sleek brasserie. Foodwise, things are rather traditional: savour timeless classics such as crispy shrimp croquettes with that typical full flavour, herby eel in a green sauce, and rich chocolate mousse. With so many tempting options on the menu, it's never easy to decide what to order. The expertise of the seasoned chef shines through in this exemplary establishment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16547;La Plage d'Amée;Belgium;Jambes;rue des Peupliers 2, Jambes, 5100, Belgium;50.4375904;4.8643861;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The terrace of this modern villa on the banks of the Meuse is one of the finest in the region. The knockout view through floor-to-ceiling windows gives the impression of almost floating on water. This watering hole is a favourite with regulars who appreciate its creative cuisine and superlative value for money. Examples include soufflé stuffed with a cream of gruyere and fresh tomato coulis. Well-crafted cuisine, subtle delicate sauces and the occasional surprising texture or flavour!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16548;Le Jardin des Senteurs;Belgium;Nassogne;rue de Masbourg 30, Nassogne, 6950, Belgium;50.1272812;5.3396849;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A modern restaurant the way we like them. Comfortable, pleasant interior and chefs loyal to the establishment for years. Grand classics rub shoulders with more creative dishes for the adventurous. "All inclusive" good value for money formula.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
16549;La Traverse;Belgium;Merelbeke;Hundelgemsesteenweg 580, Merelbeke, 9820, Belgium;50.9972573;3.7480819;46;true;true;Classic Cuisine;La Traverse is the quintessence of a contemporary brasserie, sporting a warm, welcoming interior and a menu that mingles Flemish classics with more up-to-date dishes, of which shrimp fritters and braised pork cheeks or dimsum and cauliflower steak are just a few examples. We recommend the matured beef, cooked to perfection in a Josper oven. On Saturday evenings, La Traverse offers a menu of varied dishes to share and a platter of cured meats to nibble on.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16550;L'homard Bizarre;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Latem;Kortrijksesteenweg 259, Sint-Martens-Latem, 9830, Belgium;51.0053487;3.6250064;100;true;false;Seafood, Classic French;L'Homard Bizarre translates as "the bizarre lobster", but there is nothing at all outlandish about this elegant, cosily decorated villa. The chef does, however, have a predilection for lobster! As he is a champion of classic cuisine, his menu features timeless dishes such as fried foie gras with diced apple, or ultra-fresh lobster Bellevue with house-made sauces and a crisp salad. As ever, seafood lovers and meat enthusiasts are treated to a host of full flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16551;Brasserie du Quai;Belgium;Namur;rue du Quai 9, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.4657167;4.879531;54;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Seafood;The Meuse River is the star of this contemporary establishment, as the splendid view reveals. Take a seat on the terrace and treat yourself to a traditional brasserie meal, safe in the knowledge that the ingredients are fresh and flavoursome. Fine seafood and oyster counter!;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
16552;Cul'eau;Belgium;Aalst;Gentsesteenweg 177, Aalst, 9300, Belgium;50.9401136;4.0147824;62;true;true;Modern French;Kick off the evening in style with an aperitif and nibbles, before sampling Master Karim’s excellent nosh. The extensive menu of this modern brasserie reads like a classical cookery book with vol-au-vent and sole meunière, together with aged meat and the plating is exquisite. Spot-on cooking, entirely from scratch and jazzed up with occasional inspired note. Connoisseurs will drool over the wine list!;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16553;Brasserie de la Patinoire;Belgium;Brussels;chemin du Gymnase 1, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8124024;4.371068;54;true;false;Classic French;A grandiose Normandy-inspired edifice sets the scene for this characterful luxurious brasserie at the entrance to Bois de la Cambre, which can be admired from the spacious terrace. The chef favours nostalgic recipes, with the occasional more modern touch. A patriotic line-up of Belgian brasserie classics takes the limelight on the menu, including shrimp fritters, sole meunière and vol-au-vent. The shellfish bar, open all year round, is heaven for seafood lovers.;Terrace;[]
16554;Verschil;Belgium;Gits;Bruggesteenweg 164, Gits, 8830, Belgium;50.9997602;3.11607;19;false;false;French Contemporary;A pleasant atmosphere reigns in this rustic looking restaurant, where the owner provides service with a smile. The refined dishes are made with quality ingredients.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16555;CucinaMarangon;Belgium;Turnhout;Patersstraat 9, Turnhout, 2300, Belgium;51.3239672;4.9495265;65;true;false;Italian;If you miss the warmth of Italy, make a beeline for this stylish Venetian eatery (with a splendid wine cellar) and take a seat on the charming patio. The bread, pasta and desserts are all the handiwork of the mistress of the house, who fusses over diners like a real Italian mamma! The chef’s northern Italy delicacies range from vitello alla Milanese to pheasant risotto and sign a declaration of love to all foodies!;Terrace;[]
16556;Franco Belge;Belgium;Brugge;Langestraat 109, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2112599;3.2365232;74;true;false;Modern French;The trendy, cutting-edge establishment of Dries and Tomas is a culinary treasure trove, enhanced by an alfresco dining space to the rear and a theatrically visible kitchen, where you can see the ingredients respectfully, generously and traditionally curated. The chef is a genuine craftsman with a keen eye for detail and a love of vegetables. Succulent breast of guinea fowl with crispy skin is served with al dente green asparagus, morel mushrooms and a subtle jus of guinea fowl and tarragon. Highly popular at lunchtime.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16557;Terroir;Belgium;Gierle;Turnhoutsebaan 72, Gierle, 2275, Belgium;51.2775631;4.8859906;69;true;false;Beef, Farm to table;From the rib of beef from the Ceursters butchery in the aging cabinet to the smoky aroma of charcoal embers, this modern bistro captures your attention right from the start. Take a seat at the counter and admire the kitchen team at work. Unsurprisingly, red meat takes pride of place on the menu of this bistro, but chef Ivan is equally at home with fish, so you can choose from bouchot mussels in cream or a juicy faux-filet of Jersey beef, both served with crispy fresh fries. Soul-warming, rustic fare, prepared order, defines this generous establishment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16558;'t Overhamme;Belgium;Aalst;Brusselsesteenweg 163, Aalst, 9300, Belgium;50.928478;4.0662034;26;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Patrick and Anne’s villa has been a magnet for foodies since 1991. Bold wall coverings and a designer edge add a quizzical spin to their impressive establishment, whose terrace overlooks a magnificent, landscaped garden. Chef Bogaert rolls out a classical lineup, such as quail with foie gras or hare à la royale but is not averse to playing a more modern tune, adding tangy fresh notes to his nattily crafted side dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16559;Toucan;Belgium;Ixelles;avenue Louis Lepoutre 1, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8201261;4.3592685;73;true;true;French, Classic Cuisine;The buzzy vibe of the Châtelain district sets the scene in this modern take on a traditional brasserie, embellished with a design twist. The locals flock here for its friendly, casual atmosphere and its wholesome no-nonsense nosh. Flawlessly fresh oysters, platters of seafood, melt-in-the-mouth steak, terrine or andouillette: the focus is on top-quality traditional fare served generously.;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16560;Le Brasero;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Lambert;avenue des Cerisiers 166, Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, 1200, Belgium;50.8462967;4.4150418;84;true;true;Grills, Meats and Grills;Photos of the Venice carnival adorn the walls of this modern restaurant, but the real masterpiece is in the plate. In addition to his mastery of Italian classics, the chef offers an attractive range of charcoal - grilled meat dishes. A blue - chip value since 1995!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16561;Le Mont-à-Gourmet;Belgium;Gouy-lez-Piéton;place Communale 12, Gouy-lez-Piéton, 6181, Belgium;50.4868168;4.3284204;29;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Foodies immediately feel at home in the welcoming interior of this updated restaurant. Nicolas Tournay conjures up recipes that are both creative and distinctive. He sources his ingredients from local farmers and finds his inspiration in both local traditions and in Mediterranean and Asian cuisines. A spontaneous chef full of tasty ideas!;Terrace;[]
16562;Auberge de Herborist;Belgium;Sint-Andries;De Watermolen 15, Sint-Andries, 8200, Belgium;51.1670423;3.1631717;75;false;true;Farm to table, Creative;Nothing is missing from the picturesque 11C country inn, not even the romantic open fireplace. Admire chef Hanbuckers’ flower-decked cottage garden from the patio and the orangerie. Exquisitely presented dishes that showcase the full diversity of vegetables, combined with first-class ingredients. Suave, sensitive cuisine.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16563;Restaurant Rollier;Belgium;Sint-Amands;Emile Verhaerenstraat 14a, Sint-Amands, 2890, Belgium;51.0575647;4.2020131;68;true;true;French, Asian Influences;Tucked away in a bend of the River Scheldt, this spacious venue overlooks a typically Flemish landscape of (often) cloudy skies, grassy meadows and water. Maurane is in charge of the attentive service, while Nicolas demonstrates his mastery of classical cuisine (à la carte) and contemporary fare (set menu). Examples include a juicy breast of black chicken, intelligently paired with a knockout poultry jus. International accents also crop up in the menus, demonstrated by a slow-cooked cutlet paired with spicy kimchi.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
16564;Auberge Napoleon;Belgium;Meise;Bouchoutlaan 1, Meise, 1860, Belgium;50.9331437;4.3298279;37;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;Auberge Napoleon has been a favourite with foodies for years. With high ceilings and charming old beams, the restaurant is entirely done out in white. The chandelier is a particularly impressive feature. On the terrace, you can take in the full beauty of the garden, a tranquil green escape. The extensive menu features classic cuisine – expertly done, down to the dishes finished table side. Think duck breast with an intensely flavoursome port sauce, sole meunière or hop shoots in hollandaise sauce. Many of the dishes can be shared, which ups the fun factor!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16565;Sanzaru;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Pierre;avenue de Tervueren 292, Woluwe-Saint-Pierre, 1150, Belgium;50.8353564;4.4258502;52;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Asian Influences;Behind the Cubist-inspired façade lies a pleasant establishment adorned in colourful murals, which provides the perfect setting to sample modern cuisine of Japanese and Peruvian inspiration. This whirlwind of subtle flavours, alternating between spicy and acidic, is combined harmoniously. Don’t miss the Mizaru cocktail bar upstairs.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16566;Le Buone Maniere;Belgium;Etterbeek;avenue de Tervueren 59, Etterbeek, 1040, Belgium;50.8382941;4.4017884;89;true;false;Italian;Maurizio Zizza’s hard work and dedication has firmly established his stylish restaurant, which boasts a splendid terrace to the rear, on the culinary scene of Brussels. Zizza, who is assisted by Martin Denis, enjoys serving the food himself. Together they subtly rework an authentic Italian lineup, adding a new spin, illustrated by vitello tonnato that is rich in characteristic flavours while sporting playful textures or by a ‘light’ tiramisu flavoured with marsala. Family favourites with the odd kick and ubiquitous elegance are the hallmark of this fine establishment.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16567;La Brasserie de la Gare;Belgium;Berchem-Sainte-Agathe;chaussée de Gand 1430, Berchem-Sainte-Agathe, 1082, Belgium;50.8722727;4.2896264;45;true;false;Belgian, Classic Cuisine;To get a real taste of authentic Brussels, head for this historic café, whose pores ooze vintage charm with a bustling, almost boisterous brouhaha to match. The chef pays tribute to tradition with a patriotic line-up of no-nonsense Belgian classics, such as shrimp fritters, steak and fries and dame blanche (vanilla ice cream and hot chocolate sauce). The Brasserie de la Gare provides conclusive evidence that some things never change!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16568;Frenchette;Belgium;Oostende;Madridstraat 12, Oostende, 8400, Belgium;51.2314594;2.9140739;65;true;false;Farm to table;A bistro, but not only. Market-fresh, Frenchie fare, but not only! Don’t be misled by appearances. Contemporary textures and trendy ingredients add a modern twist to a line-up of dishes to share. The bar is perfect for a drink and a snack. To sum up, this is the perfect place to finish a day in the likable town of Ostend.;Air conditioning;[]
16569;Origine;Belgium;Etterbeek;rue Général Leman 36, Etterbeek, 1040, Belgium;50.8367642;4.3831731;87;false;true;Modern French, World Cuisine;The whimsical décor of the Origine is depicted by colourful creatures and plants, setting the scene for a modern restaurant run by Xavier Lizen, who demonstrates great maturity despite his youth. The menu is renewed each month and illustrates the chef’s international and original approach, in which each flavour lives up to expectations.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16570;San Daniele;Belgium;Ganshoren;avenue Charles-Quint 6, Ganshoren, 1083, Belgium;50.8682699;4.3133929;38;true;false;Italian;In the Spinelli family since 1982, San Daniele enjoys a stellar reputation. Their unassuming restaurant in the shade of Koekelberg Basilica is the quintessence of Italian charm. Heart-warming dishes such as tagliolini with mushrooms, lamb and Taggiascha olives with a foie gras and lamb jus take pride of place. Chef Franco exalts traditional recipes by his skill and delicacy. The seabass in a salt crust filleted in front of you is guaranteed to lift your spirits. Stefano is near at hand with a wealth of insightful wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
16571;Cômo;Luxembourg;Esch-sur-Alzette;19 rue des Remparts, Esch-sur-Alzette, 4303, Luxembourg;49.4961063;5.9804148;85;true;false;Italian;It is no coincidence that charming Renato Favaro named his restaurant after his birthplace. Inspired by his roots and genuine Mediterranean trattoria traditions, his lasagne alla bolognese and fettucine l ragù are to die for! A talented chef who works only with the very best produce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16572;De Kruier;Belgium;Ramskapelle;Ramskapellestraat 66, Ramskapelle, 8301, Belgium;51.3128211;3.2519652;33;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Belgian;This picture postcard restaurant stands in the shade of an 1897 windmill in a manicured garden. You can count on the Callant brothers to rustle up a delicious line-up of authentic Belgian dishes, calling on flawlessly fresh, deftly cooked ingredients. The extensive à la carte menu traverses the annals of traditional cuisine to the delight of good food lovers. In summertime, the alfresco terrace is the place to be.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16573;Cinq;Belgium;Anderlecht;route de Lennik 361, Anderlecht, 1070, Belgium;50.8179218;4.2817593;29;true;false;Modern French;The young and not so young come here to be spoiled rotten in this contemporary villa near the ring road of Brussels. Chef Verzele rustles up a varied menu in tune with the zeitgeist, adding a new spin to his classical background. Examples include perfectly poached fillets of sole, paired with fried prawns, a velvety saffron-flavoured risotto and a knockout fish sauce. Cinq is the sort of place that invites you to dig into meals steeped in gutsy, big-boned flavours whilst enjoying the casual buzzy vibe. Should you have cause for celebration, we can recommend the lobster menu.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16574;Bassud;Belgium;Torhout;Zuidstraat 42, Torhout, 8820, Belgium;51.0632357;3.1033494;38;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Bassud is the story of Michèlle and Jan, set in an attractive vintage Scandinavian décor. Chef Jan serves minimalist, no-nonsense dishes, using locally sourced produce and jazzed up by subtle twists, such as fermented ingredients or smoked charcoal oven flavours.;Terrace;[]
16575;Tablàvins;Belgium;Knokke;Zwaluwenlaan 12, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.349455;3.282443;74;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This wine-decked, book-lined eatery sports a trendy colour scheme that reeks of the Flemish flair for interior decorating. The wine-food pairing suggestions are equally inspired. The food in the zeitgeist sports a subtle blend of tradition and exoticism: you may taste a generous saddle of rabbit or a sole sprinkled in Asian flavours. A deep-rooted respect for heritage paired with a streak of daring.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
16576;René;Belgium;Anderlecht;place de la Résistance 14, Anderlecht, 1070, Belgium;50.835775;4.311223;51;true;true;Belgian, Classic Cuisine;René takes us back to a time when life was simple. This former chippy, upgraded into a natty vintage bistro, shines the spotlight on down-to-earth Belgian classics. Mussels stuffed with parsley and garlic butter, rare steak with fresh béarnaise sauce and nourishing stews are all served with heaps of French fries. Huge helpings of searingly good food! What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16577;Colonel Louise;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;rue Jean Stas 24, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8339246;4.3553472;93;true;false;Meats and Grills, Modern French;Red meat lovers fall head over heels with this swish brasserie on a street corner near Avenue Louise. As soon as you cross the threshold, you are struck by the array of cured meats on the counter. You must then decide whether you want Aubrac, Wagyu or Holstein beef, before you dig into impeccably cooked steak flanked by fresh sauces and fries cooked in beef tallow as tradition demands. The menu also features a host of other delicacies ranging from bone marrow to vitello tonnato and crispy sweetbread. Perfect for a single dish, lunch or a full-blown dinner – what’s not to like?;Terrace;[]
16578;Brasserie Fiston;Belgium;Varsenare;Gistelsteenweg 123 A, Varsenare, 8490, Belgium;51.1864997;3.1461986;34;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Fiston is a swanky brasserie depicted by a friendly, buzzy vibe. Chef Seynaeve rustles up text-book classics according to best practices. Geert Van Hecke’s pupil sources the best ingredients that he incorporates into home-made recipes. His shrimp fritters, turbot with a signature mousseline sauce and dame blanche dessert hit the spot every time. The suggestions reveal a more modern facet of the chef’s culinary score. Knock-out wine list!;Air conditioning,Car park,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16579;Brasserie Rongese;Belgium;Hasselt;Runkstersteenweg 226, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9244568;5.3161684;41;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;This characterful eatery is established in a former cafe in Runskt, a district that was once called Rongese. The owner, Peter Merken, is always on hand with excellent wine and beer tips to pair with the wonderful array of wholesome fare chalked up on the slate. Juicy rare entrecote steak with piping hot fries and al dente veggies followed by a Belle Hélène pear with vanilla ice cream and smothered in hot chocolate sauce: you can’t get more traditional than this brasserie score.;Terrace;[]
16580;Fico;Belgium;Ixelles;rue Américaine 118, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8229943;4.36016;32;false;true;Italian, Sicilian;At Fico, Nadia Bruno pays tribute to Sicily and her mamma, Grazziella. The cosy ambience and vibrant, vintage-inspired decor make for the perfect setting in which to savour her sun-drenched cooking. The chalkboard displays a tempting array of authentic dishes. Think al dente fettuccine elevated with sea urchin, an intensely flavoursome semifreddo made with grappa, honey and saffron. Here, bold flavours meet Italian finesse, with no room for pretension. Don't forget to make a reservation!;;[]
16581;Brasserie Grand Cru;Belgium;Brugge;Noorweegsekaai 5, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2221008;3.2348305;100;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, French;Red and white chequered tablecloths and a rustic interior set the delightfully vintage scene in this brasserie. The huge open kitchen is equipped with both spit-roasting and barbecue facilities. Lovers of hunger-obliterating wholesome fare will be in seventh heaven as each dish hits the spot from the Flemish stoofpotje made with Belgian beer, the vol-au-vent or sole meunière to calf’s liver in madeira sauce – an authentic lineup of no-nonsense familiar brasserie cuisine. The extensive menu has something for everyone and is a genuine ode to the cooking of yesteryear. A great vintage indeed!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16582;Seir;Belgium;Kasterlee;Geelsebaan 40, Kasterlee, 2460, Belgium;51.2384201;4.9682815;42;false;false;Creative French, Modern French;The sunny conservatory of this swish restaurant immediately catches the eye. The leather-seated lounge is ideal to sip a drink while admiring chef Thomas at work. An accomplished artist, he composes his visual masterpieces right on the counter. Intelligent combinations, precise and meticulous cooking. This youthful chef gives a free rein to his creative flair and is clearly determined to go places! A genuine treat for the senses.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16583;iOda;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;Rue de la Victoire 23, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8318431;4.3462076;88;false;true;Vegetarian, Organic;iOda defines itself as a vegetarian rotisserie. Rather than meat, expect vegetables and fruit without forgetting a few delicacies from the North Sea. Chef Hoed unveils his creative talents in dishes such as leek roasted on the rotisserie, shining the spotlight on small local producers whenever possible. Playful, delicate and gutsy – the seasons are reverently respected, allowing the ingredients to shout their name. The trendy, buzzy interior of vintage details and untreated materials is perfectly in tune with the hipster Saint Gilles district.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16584;Philema;Belgium;Ixelles;chaussée de Waterloo 437, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8214167;4.3566741;42;false;true;Greek;A gourmet festival of summertime flavours awaits you at Manos Makrygiannakis. The chef, who hails from Crete, shines the spotlight on ingredients that are steeped in Mediterranean spices and aromas. Authentic food based on top-quality produce (on sale at the shop). A friendly vibe depicts this establishment, ideal to share a delicate spanakopita, grilled cuttlefish and melt-in-the-mouth baklava with friends. A Greek feast!;Terrace;[]
16585;Leeuw;Belgium;Hasselt;Kapelstraat 51, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9299067;5.3346077;96;false;false;Modern French;Marble and black tables set the striking scene inside this splendid townhouse but lift your eyes – the ceiling is covered in mirrors! Chef Snykers, who whisks up dishes ranging from modern (set menu) to classical (à la carte), has a knack for sourcing top produce and a gift for creating punchy sauces. Now, it is up to you to taste the full range and nuances of his culinary flair and talent…;Terrace;[]
16586;Viticolo;Belgium;Oisquercq;Rue du Bon Voisin 117, Oisquercq, 1480, Belgium;50.66304;4.23681;96;false;false;Italian, Mediterranean Cuisine;A stopover in this red brick edifice on the outskirts of Oisquercq will whisk you off to Italy. The interior and the peaceful patio are both stylish and comfortably cosy. The produce is local, illustrated by the garden-fresh herbs coating the pluma iberico. Juicy octopus is enhanced and underscored by a sauce featuring the subtle acidity of cime di rapa. The pasta is naturally fresh and home-made in this restaurant, determined to uphold Italian traditions.;Terrace;[]
16587;Taverne du Passage;Belgium;Brussels;Galerie de la Reine 30, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8476738;4.3548801;48;false;true;Belgian, Classic Cuisine;This emblematic Art deco brasserie, which is housed in the exclusive Galerie du roi, just a stone’s throw from the iconic Grand Place, takes you back in time to the Roaring Twenties. Its vintage charm is enhanced by a host of elegant details like the golden origami birds. The equally nostalgic menu offers a splendid lineup of Belgian family favourites: crunchy shrimp fritters, sole meunière with fresh French fries, warm chocolate mousse with butterscotch ice cream. Living proof that tradition and generosity are timeless values!;Terrace;[]
16588;Ivresse;Belgium;Uccle;Rue du Postillon 6, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.8028726;4.339744;34;true;true;Organic, Modern Cuisine;The entrance to this trendy eatery is through a small grocery store, which boasts an impressive wine wall. Organic and natural wine fans cannot fail but find something to set their tastebuds tingling! The vibe is unsurprisingly laid-back, and you can eat at the counter. Recipes that hit the spot every time with a focus on sustainable, local and fresh produce. The stars of the show are undoubtedly vegetables and gutsy, full-bodied sauces.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16589;Black Smoke;Belgium;Antwerpen;Boomgaardstraat 1, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.1995366;4.4157102;75;false;true;Barbecue;Black Smoke packs a distinctly American punch. The dimly lit, unpolished, rough and rugged interior is steeped in the smoky aroma of BBQ. The pitmasters have perfected the art of grilled meat in true Texan fashion. Traditional techniques, Latino influences and local produce for meals rich in big-boned, heart-warming flavours. Examples include lamb tacos jazzed up with a spicy za’atar, jalapeno pepper and fresh lemon. Or how about a cut of premium beef from the De Laet & Van Haver butcher’s shop? The drinks menu is practically as long as the food menu, while the ‘Bonanza Experience’ is billed as the ultimate sharing experience! So, let’s crank up the heat!;;[]
16590;La Rigue;Belgium;Knokke;Elizabetlaan 160, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3465226;3.2795885;66;false;true;Belgian, Classic French;The stunning La Réserve hotel boasts a brasserie that is quite the equal to its elegant host. The Zegemeer landscape, visible from the handsome terrace, provides the perfect foil to this urbane restaurant. Local foodies adore the place for its extensive range of national and Gallic favourites, jazzed up with a delicate new spin. For example, the rich vol-au-vent is paired with an exquisite millefeuille and a subtly contrasting acidic sabayon while the bouillabaisse of North Sea fish explodes with big-boned gutsiness… A tailored culinary experience overflowing in generosity and a capacity of some 120 diners. Be it for a snack or a special occasion, La Rigue is just the ticket.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16591;Le Roi de Trèfle;Belgium;Namur;Avenue Baron Louis Huart 12, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.4601094;4.8674547;25;false;true;Classic French;On the banks of the Meuse, Brigitte Dekoninck and Patrick Kleeblatt welcome diners to their characterful abode, which sports a lounge vibe oozing in charm. The veteran chef is a champion of classical fare and is all for allowing the diner to choose their own main ingredient and side dishes. His craftsmanship is showcased in melt-in-the-mouth foie gras or in the subtle vin jaune sauce that flanks crunchy sweetbread and cèpe mushrooms. Lovers of nostalgic nosh will fall in love with this King of Clubs.;;[]
16592;Atelier Dolce Amaro;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;Rue Defacqz 86, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8270941;4.3580158;74;false;false;Italian;The younger sibling of Dolce Amaro is a friendly eatery overflowing in authentic Italian hospitality. The opposite of fussy and pretentious, the food is fresh, hits the spot every time and is served generously. Vitello tonnato de paccheri al ragu to start, followed by a lovingly and patiently simmered ossobuco, finishing with a semifreddo… The pinnacle of Italian simplicity!;Terrace;[]
16593;Bistro Berto;Belgium;Waregem;Zuiderlaan 17, Waregem, 8790, Belgium;50.8832425;3.4264765;33;true;false;Farm to table;Zulte-Waregem football club has hired a new striker! In the southern stand, David Bertolozzi hits the bullseye every time with his generous dishes. Start with a range of snacks to share, like generous nuggets of plaice dipped in tartare sauce, before digging into a modern version of classical recipes, such as pheasant with winter side dishes or a heart-warming vol-au-vent. Attractive lunchtime menu.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16594;Gioia;Belgium;Brussels;Rue Belliard 36, Brussels, 1040, Belgium;50.8420694;4.3713469;20;false;false;Italian;Although the sound of traffic may be somewhat deafening outside, venture into this swish restaurant done up in tasteful light colours, taking a seat on the exquisite rear terrace when the weather is fine. The homemade pasta is out of this world! Rich flavours, fresh ingredients and Italy’s renowned “simplicity” are the hallmarks of this establishment. A new spin on familiar family favourites.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16595;Fortuin;Belgium;Kontich;Gemeenteplein 4, Kontich, 2550, Belgium;51.1353799;4.4448213;40;false;true;Creative French, Belgian;The huge vats of beer and the remarkable tree immediately catch the eye on entering the Staminée. Continue on into the elegant brasserie, where a trendy playlist and hip décor set the cosmopolitan scene. Veteran chef Stijn Rotthier puts his own spin on classical recipes. Examples include tender, juicy veal loaf with a melt-in-the-mouth millefeuille of potatoes and a madeira sauce subtly perfumed with truffle or a rich vol-au-vent in a hollandaise sauce steeped in spicy, fresh and acidic notes. Fortuin’s culinary signature can be summed up as punchy and authentic. Parents may be interested to know that children are welcome (special menu) and that there is a playground almost next-door to the restaurant.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16596;Modest;Belgium;Opglabbeek;Weg naar Opoeteren 117, Opglabbeek, 3660, Belgium;51.0494814;5.599175;54;true;true;Creative French, Modern French;"Modest" was the nickname Sander Spreeuwers was given at school. His elegant restaurant is intimate and the decor is contemporary in style. To the rear, you can see the vineyard in bloom. He is distinguished as a chef by his subtlety and finesse. A deep respect for classical French culinary tradition, an appreciation for vibrancy and a penchant for incorporating Asian seasonings underpin your dining experience here. For example, he delicately enhances turbot à la meunière and lobster with a light, whipped Béarnaise sauce and potato mousseline infused with green herb oil. This bold, spontaneous cuisine is a reflection of the chef's personality.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16597;Osteria Romana;Belgium;Brussels;Avenue Legrand 11, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8155945;4.3712714;27;false;false;Roman;Don’t even try to resist the appeal of this Osteria Romana - you will be bowled over by the romantic allure of the mansion, the cocktail bar and the immaculate tailored service. Roman specialties and tableside preparations set the scene. Delicacies include Roman-Jewish deep-fried artichoke, carbonara pasta, pasta with tuna tartare, pepperoncino, combava and ginger in a lineup whose subtlety, generosity and flavour are to die for! What more proof do you need that Italians do it better!;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16598;Ukiyo;Belgium;Stekene;Polenlaan 5, Stekene, 9190, Belgium;51.2073162;4.0422066;28;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The former presbytery of Stekene is in a class of its own, boasting a sleek, trendy cocktail bar, four luxurious guestrooms and a classy contemporary restaurant leading into a manicured garden. Brothers Timothy and Bodi de Munck bend over backwards to pamper their guests. Their passion for Asia is reflected in the extensive à la carte and Omakase menus and in the beverage list. Gallic flavours with subtle Japanese nuances set the scene, exemplified by a delicious ponzu-flavoured sauce that delicately underscores fish or Anjou pigeon, cooked rare, flanked by morel mushrooms and a gravy so rich it will knock your socks off!;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16599;Bink;Belgium;Turnhout;Bloemekensgang 12, Turnhout, 2300, Belgium;51.3231886;4.9506117;26;true;false;Modern French, Creative French;If you’re looking for good food in a romantic-cum-industrial bistro vibe, make a beeline for the former Brepols printing works, where an open kitchen sets the tone of the establishment. You can choose between a primarily classical menu or a more modern repertory, strewn with Asian influences. The seabass in a salt crust is emblematic of the knowhow of the chef, who enjoys surprising diners with winter side dishes and a tangy sauce jazzed up by Sichuan pepper over a fillet of venison.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16600;Grünewald Chef’s Table;;Luxembourg;2 Rue des Hauts-Fourneaux, 1719, Luxembourg;49.6334303;6.1383319;94;false;false;Modern Cuisine;You cannot fail but remark the green marble counter that occupies the heart of this street corner building, appointed elegantly and tastefully. The chairs are positioned around the counter to better admire the chefs at work. Clovis Degrave and his team pour their creative talents into a set menu, rife with international accents, amusing textures and rugged sauces. An example: fillet of zander underscored by a caviar-flavoured beurre blanc and a velvety sauce of samphire and girolle mushrooms. A truly fascinating global experience.;Air conditioning;[]
16601;Jaco;Belgium;Uccle;chaussée de Waterloo 1372, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7885807;4.3752312;98;true;false;Italian Contemporary;Jaco blends the well-heeled ambiance of Fort Jaco with a vintage interior dripping in contemporary elegance and luxury depicts the tiniest details. From Puglia, Francesco de Vita and Dario Trimigno recreate authentic Italian flavours using outstanding premium ingredients which they craft into unusual, attractive dishes. Don’t miss their version of vitello tonnato or a pistachio soufflé that is daringly paired with a bitter ice cream. Come early and sip a cocktail at the bar, before or after stocking up in the delicatessen store. Jaco is a culinary universe in a class of its own!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
16602;Gusto Naturale;Luxembourg;Schifflange;Z.A.C op Herbett, Schifflange, 3885, Luxembourg;49.517573;6.011141;19;false;false;Italian;Walk through the sleek grocery store (we recommend stopping off to make a few purchases as you leave) to take a seat in Marc Bernardi’s urban eatery. The chef, who hails from Bolzano, Italy, adds his own spin to authentic Italian dishes. For example, he might pair homemade tortellini stuffed with shredded beef and veal with a spot-on veal gravy. He has a knack for mixing powerful, rich flavours and his flair for vegetables and fresh textures is entirely in the zeitgeist.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16603;Bistro J.E.T.T.;Belgium;Westkapelle;Dorpsstraat 113, Westkapelle, 8300, Belgium;51.3129839;3.3014944;64;true;false;Modern Cuisine;“Just enjoying time together” is the philosophy of this small, elegant eatery. Sarah supervises the dining room, while Dries can be seen in the open kitchen rustling up food to be shared with friends and family. Recipes that combine the classicism of Gallic tradition with exotic influences and a scattering of original ideas – convincing!;Air conditioning;[]
16604;Colonel Fort Jaco;Belgium;Uccle;Chaussée de Waterloo 1405, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7859485;4.3770529;56;false;false;Meats and Grills;An offshoot of Colonel, a temple of red meat, this stylish brasserie sports a tasteful colour scheme that is the epitome of suave urbanity. Diners are invited to choose one of the juicy cuts of meat from the butcher’s counter near the open-plan kitchen. The knife-edge precision offered by the Josper charcoal oven, the exquisite flavour of the cured meats, the made-to-order sauces and the crispy fries are indeed admirable, but that is not all. Side by side this traditional Belgian lineup, you will also find dishes like carpaccio or filet américain, and more nostalgic dishes like their excellent vol-au-vent. We recommend a seat at the counter to make the most of the show in the kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16605;Stable;Belgium;Edegem;Drie Eikenstraat 1, Edegem, 2650, Belgium;51.1595413;4.4403349;55;true;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;Enter the stables of Hof Ter Linden and discover a mysterious world of cosy authenticity. The historic character of the edifice provides a perfect foil to the classy designer interior. The food also combines tradition and modernity in dishes that fascinate, strewn with international floral inspirations and creative touches.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16606;Blanco;Belgium;Knokke;Keith Haringplein 7, Knokke, 8300, Belgium;51.3386107;3.2849011;50;false;false;Mexican;David and Celine describe Blanco as “highly Instagrammable” and the trendy interior definitely ticks all the boxes: fashionable, spacious and buzzy! After a refreshing cocktail, you will sample dishes of Mexican inspiration: flavoursome tacos, subtly spicy chipotle, home-made ajo blanco (white gazpacho) and fish from the North Sea. A genuine culinary adventure…;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16607;le Vugo;Belgium;Mouscron;Rue du Phénix 29, Mouscron, 7700, Belgium;50.738014;3.2234394;83;true;false;Modern French, Modern Cuisine;An excellent choice for a gourmet dining experience at outstanding value for money. A contemporary, relatively intimist interior provides the setting for up-to-the-minute cuisine. The chef plays with textures, whilst allowing the generous ingredient to shout its name loud and clear.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16608;Nonam;Belgium;Gent;Sluizekenkaai 1, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0597196;3.7238863;25;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;Nestled in the heart of Ghent's Patershol neighbourhood, Nonam has an authentic and cosy ambience with a touch of vintage charm. After stretching out in one of the luxurious guestrooms, pop into the gastrobar, which, in the evening, serves an enticing range of dishes for sharing. In the restaurant, the set menu presents a playful take on fusion cuisine. The chef transforms his grandmother's rice pudding recipe, for instance, with exciting textures of apricot and a koji-based ice cream. Or he boldly combines beetroot, blue cheese and umeboshi. The selection of fine wines, by the bottle and by the glass, has plenty of gems in store.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16609;Markt XI;Belgium;De Haan;Driftweg 11, De Haan, 8420, Belgium;51.2720632;3.0325558;45;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Benny and Katrijn are full of ambition, which you will appreciate as soon as you step foot in their restaurant. The cheerful lady of the house greets and seats her guests, suggesting food and wine pairings. The chef crafts modern cuisine, which is best described as fresh, subtle and beautifully plated. Examples include pigeon breast, cooked rare and then finished on a barbecue to give it a subtle smoky edge, paired with the meat of the legs stuffed in cabbage leaves, salsifies and a knockout sauce made out of the cooking gravy. Markt XI is truly a blue-ribbon establishment!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16610;Brabohoeve;Belgium;Schilde;Noorderlaan 27, Schilde, 2970, Belgium;51.2616344;4.6000933;52;false;true;Modern French;Brabohoeve is a villa-restaurant whose smart, modern interior is adorned in arty photos. The terrace overlooking the surrounding meadows is a must when the weather is fine. Franco-Belgian classics take the leading role in the culinary repertory with family favourites like shrimp fritters and vol-au-vent of free-range chicken in star positions, crafted with flawless technique and flanked by a succulent selection of seasonal specials. Examples include fresh, juicy brill garnished with mushrooms and gnocchi, or saddle of hare in season. Expect to find it difficult to make up your mind, such is the range tempting and enticing…;Car park,Terrace;[]
16611;Maison D;Belgium;Ronse;Charles Vandendoorenstraat 10, Ronse, 9600, Belgium;50.7461748;3.6021843;51;false;true;Modern French;The customer comes first in the elegant establishment of Delphine and Didier. Delphine’s vivacious personality depicts the front-of-house vibe, while Didier’s enthusiasm is contagious. The chef has a knack for adding a personal spin to fine produce and familiar flavours. He might add a playful edge to consummately crafted turbot, with different textures of parsley, all of which is enhanced by a spicy concoction of clams. The extensive menu embodies the establishment’s desire to pamper. First rate lunchtime menu.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16612;Commotie;Belgium;Sint-Amandsberg;Victor Braeckmanlaan 367, Sint-Amandsberg, 9040, Belgium;51.0617882;3.7613952;18;true;true;Creative;Commotie radiates a sense of Zen tranquillity. The verdant surroundings and minimalist Japanese decor create a harmonious whole. The terrace is an oasis of calm. But the arrival of the food interrupts your quiet contemplation. Chef Thomas expresses his originality through fermentation, vegetables, tart flavours, barbecue notes, intense sauces etc. His inventiveness is captivating, and his nose-to-tail vision is an inspiration. He imbues scallops, for instance, with a subtle smoky flavour, injects extra pep with an emulsion of whey and vin jaune, and adds salty nuances. Each plate tells a story, complemented by the wonderful picks of sommelier Lara, who has a penchant for natural wines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16613;Alexandre;Belgium;Herzele;Kloosterberg 31, Herzele, 9550, Belgium;50.8389165;3.8890903;56;false;false;French, Modern Cuisine;This 18C doctor’s home, set in the picturesque village of Herzele and a well-kept secret among discerning foodies, is depicted by a snug interior, a superb terrace and Tamara’s attentive service. Tim Ritserveldt deploys his virtuoso culinary skills, rustling up set menus overflowing in creativity. Hearty, gutsy flavours are his hallmark, such as feta, watermelon sorbet and guacamole cream which enhance the character and depth of thinly sliced Duroc ham. Full-bodied, spot-on food that enjoys straying from conventional culinary paths.;Terrace;[]
16614;Huize Alberic;Belgium;Kalmthout;Kapellensteenweg 69, Kalmthout, 2920, Belgium;51.3894751;4.4752492;37;false;false;French Contemporary;From the ironwork and the restored fireplace to the wooden floors, the former home (1920s) of Alberic Plettinck, ironworker and artist, has been tastefully and respectfully refurbished in a stylish vein. After being welcomed by your gracious hostess, you will sample an updated version of classical recipes in which chef Bram demonstrates his flair for plating. His consummate craftsmanship shines through in the intense creamy gravy that flanks pheasant or in his modern spin on eels in sorrel.;Terrace;[]
16615;La Strada;Belgium;Opgrimbie;Rijksweg 634, Opgrimbie, 3630, Belgium;50.9386687;5.6916189;60;true;true;Italian;Contemporary restaurant faithful to Italy’s culinary heritage. Chef Pierro hails from Umbria and Tuscan cuisine has no secrets from him. His truffle recipes are standout. His son, Valentino, adds his youthful enthusiasm in the kitchen, while Myriame’s gracious welcome completes this family affair.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16616;L'Amandier;Belgium;Genval;avenue Albert 1er, 288, Genval, 1332, Belgium;50.7250422;4.5124358;35;false;false;Creative;Martin Volkaerts and his enthusiastic team have moved to this handsome bourgeois mansion, which sports a modern interior. Virtuoso chef Martin cooks to order and creativity dictates his culinary approach, depicted by exquisite sauces. Inspired by his garden, he crafts dishes that are exquisitely balanced between spicy and acidic notes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16617;Rizoom;Belgium;Gent;Nieuwewandeling 62, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.055114;3.7062688;79;false;false;Asian Influences, Creative;Jars of fermented veggies and the crackle of a charcoal fire – just a quick glance at this sharp-edged designer restaurant gives an idea of what you can expect. Chef Yves Kerckhoffs demonstrates his passion for produce and his weakness for Japanese flavours. For example, he may dry-mature duck or use koji to age it, and his quest for umami flavours is truly fascinating. Sauces and jus take centre stage, illustrated by a torrefied yeast-based sauce and a reduction of langoustine, which flank and embellish grilled gurnard (fish). The fine lineup of natural wines and sakes ensures that you will have no difficulty finding the perfect tipple to pair with your meal.;Terrace;[]
16618;Les Gribaumonts;Belgium;Mons;rue d'Havré 95, Mons, 7000, Belgium;50.4539318;3.9564274;78;true;true;Creative French, Traditional Cuisine;The façade of this restaurant is adorned in colourful frescoes, which also set the scene in the contemporary interior. The harmony between Nicolas’ inspired wine pairings and Lisa’s elegant culinary prowess is irresistible. The chef has a fondness for local ingredients, whose rich flavours are further enhanced by delicate touches and a consummate wine list.;Interesting wine list;[]
16619;Cantine Copine;Belgium;Brugge;Steenkaai 34/s, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2187589;3.2028146;26;false;true;Farm to table, Creative;The bare brick walls of Karen Keygnaert’s friendly restaurant bear witness to their industrial heritage. Diners are welcomed like old friends, invited to share dishes creatively rustled up with fine produce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16620;Au Vieux Saint Martin;Belgium;Brussels;place du Grand Sablon 38, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8409123;4.3544938;31;true;true;Belgian;The spirit of the arty, well-heeled Sablons neighbourhood is visible in the colourful artwork and even more so on the terrace of this buzzy brasserie. The menu offers a patriotic line-up of heartwarming Belgian specialties such as filet américain (steak tartare), vol-au-vent or brains with a gribiche sauce (boiled egg, mustard, herbs). If you take a peek at the larder, you will see just how fresh everything is in this culinary landmark of Brussels, as popular with the locals as with the tourists.;Terrace;[]
16621;Du Moulin;Belgium;Ligneuville;Grand'Rue 28, Ligneuville, 4960, Belgium;50.3755861;6.0542447;95;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;The wood-burning fire in the cosy sitting room is the epitome of an Ardennes inn. This nostalgic charm is enhanced by the classical cooking of Jean Goire, who brooks no concessions. He pays tribute to his region, working closely with carefully selected suppliers. His culinary expertise unveils a deep-rooted respect and steadfast commitment to flavours that are gutsy, rustic and traditional to the core.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
16622;De Cuylhoeve;Belgium;Geel;Hollandsebaan 7, Geel, 2440, Belgium;51.1343504;4.9998671;97;true;true;Modern French;De Cuylhoeve enjoys a truly magical setting in the heart of the Campine Forest, providing the perfect stage for this romantic restaurant. Start with a glass of bubbly from the impressive list of champagnes, before sampling chef Bart Janssens’ masterful know-how. He finds his inspiration in pedigree French recipes, to which he adds his own more modern spin, sharing his passion for first-class produce along the way.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16623;Les Brigittines Aux marches de la Chapelle;Belgium;Brussels;place de la Chapelle 5, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.841358;4.3503741;92;false;true;Traditional Cuisine, Belgian;This Art nouveau brasserie is the epitome of “La Belle Époque” and it is impossible to resist either the décor or the mouth-watering recipes rustled up by chef Myny, a true-blue Brussels lad, whose exuberant personality pervades his knockout traditional nosh. From a vol-au-vent made with melt-in-the-mouth flaky pastry to a tender juicy chicken breast served with piping hot fries or veal cheeks with Cantillon beer, everything is delicious.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Valet parking;[]
16624;Patyntje;Belgium;Gent;Gordunakaai 91, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0415916;3.694252;78;false;false;Flemish;A meal in this elegant colonial-style villa is a must for any self-respecting food aficionado. A superb riverside terrace by the Lys, a bustling vibe and old-fashioned table service set the scene at Patyntje, without forgetting the extensive menu of Belgian brasserie favourites. Timeless classics such as eels in sorrel, vol-au-vent and carbonade flamande (stew) prepared with textbook skill and care. Don’t miss the sweetbread fritters – one of the Michelin inspectors’ favourites since time immemorial…;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16625;Caffè Al Dente;Belgium;Uccle;rue du Doyenné 87, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.8028805;4.3407215;46;true;true;Italian;The smart, marble - decked interior of the Caffè Al Dente oozes with the warmth and authenticity of Italy. The chef knows his classics and works with top - rate produce. Equally fine wines. Pop next - door to the boutique when you finish your meal.;Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16626;In de Zon;Belgium;Kemmel;Dikkebusstraat 80, Kemmel, 8950, Belgium;50.7961399;2.7819977;95;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;In de Zon is a haven for foodies and cycling enthusiasts (it is located in the heart of the Heuvelland region). The decor is filled with nostalgic finds from flea markets, which add a touch of charm. On a clear day, you can see all the way to France from the gorgeous terrace. This is a restaurant that is full of character and that showcases Flemish cuisine at its best. Crispy shrimp croquettes, herby paling in 't groen (eel in a green sauce) with fresh fries, succulent pork cheeks cooked in Saint Bernard beer: this heartwarming food leaves a lasting impression.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16627;Spaans Dak;Belgium;Oud-Heverlee;Maurits Noëstraat 2, Oud-Heverlee, 3050, Belgium;50.8223581;4.6551693;49;true;true;Creative;The view from this 16C manor house over Zoet Water is quite simply stunning and the modern wing, done up in designer-inspired vibe, also commands a splendid view. The food is modern and meticulously crafted in a bid to create succulent contrasts with the core ingredient. The three-course menu is one of the highlights of this splendid establishment.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16628;Rooselaer;Belgium;Heusden;Berenbosdreef 18, Heusden, 9070, Belgium;51.0232135;3.8155433;59;true;false;Grills, Classic Cuisine;Lovers of traditional fare have been frequenting this elegant manor with its conservatory and alfresco terrace and garden since 1977. The chef’s generous, traditional fare has attracted a faithful crowd of regulars who appreciate both the set and à la carte menus, in which lobster and grilled meat take pride of place. The second generation is pursuing this classical heritage, albeit with the odd more modern touch, but ever true to its hallmark hearty flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16629;Bistro Cuisine Kwizien;Belgium;Zwevezele;Bruggestraat 45, Zwevezele, 8750, Belgium;51.0382267;3.2127243;61;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;This former village café has lost none of its yesteryear appeal, even though the draught beer taps and bar stools have given way to a warm modern interior, whose open-plan kitchen cannot fail but catch the eye. Steven crafts tasty dishes oozing with flavour, including a patriotic line-up of Belgian classics such as his own take on pear Belle Hélène. His partner Lies elegantly welcomes guests to the establishment.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16630;Numerus Clausus;Belgium;Lier;Keldermansstraat 2, Lier, 2500, Belgium;51.1315261;4.5760961;46;false;true;Farm to table;You don’t get to be a culinary benchmark by accident! Chef Steven and his sommelière Annelies have devoted themselves body and soul to make this restaurant a beacon of French cuisine in Lier. That said, they aren’t afraid of dusting the cobwebs off culinary traditions or adding a personal spin, such as mustard-flavoured ice cream served with steak tartare. The intelligently curated wine list is perfectly paired to the food.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16631;Bonheur Simple;Belgium;Embourg;voie de l'Ardenne 108, Embourg, 4053, Belgium;50.5904138;5.606902;82;false;true;Thai, Asian;It is the little things that make us happy. Such as an attractive table setting in a contemporary restaurant, a peaceful atmosphere, and authentic Thai flavours in the creative cooking. Simplicity really is good.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16632;La Villa des Bégards;Belgium;Embourg;voie de l'Ardenne 112, Embourg, 4053, Belgium;50.5891382;5.6081098;54;true;false;Creative, Italian;François Piscitello has decorated his handsome villa tastefully and sparingly. The villa also boasts three guestrooms for overnight stays. A seasoned chef, Piscitello works with a set menu in which he crafts a finetuned balance between textbook French technique and Italian flair, together with the odd dash of creativity. For example, he flanks his breast of pigeon with a big-boned gravy, but he can also play with textures in a bid to jazz up a traditional risotto. The 100% Italian wine list further enhances this delicious culinary festival.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16633;Atelier de Bossimé;Belgium;Loyers;rue Bossimé 2B, Loyers, 5101, Belgium;50.4550108;4.9326939;92;false;false;Organic, Modern French;Ludovic Vanackere’s converted this old farm in line with his sustainable vision. If the produce doesn’t come from his own impressive kitchen garden, which can be admired from the floor-to-ceiling windows, it is sourced locally. The surprise menu showcases the best of Namur and the region. Veggies take the limelight, prompting extra creativity in the winter season, illustrated by the chef’s work with different cabbage textures enhanced by a sauce packed in fermented veg, peanuts and sate-flavoured spices. Regional cooking founded on throbbing recipes and powerful sauces.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16634;La Belle Maraîchère;Belgium;Brussels;place Sainte-Catherine 11a, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8509244;4.347886;99;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;Depuis 1973, les gourmets apprécient ce restaurant traditionnel où la famille Devreker choie ses hôtes. On y redécouvre le temps où Sainte Catherine était le quartier le plus prisé de Bruxelles pour les restaurants. Croquettes de crevettes, homard, gibier, sauces intenses et bien d’autres plats y sont préparés dans les règles de l’art. Pas de chichis, mais une cuisine chaleureuse et savoureuse.;Air conditioning;[]
16635;Le Bouchon et l'Assiette;Belgium;Soignies;chemin du Saussois 5a, Soignies, 7060, Belgium;50.5553103;4.0586763;41;true;true;Farm to table;From the outside it is a small brick farmstead nestling in the green countryside, inside, however, diners are greeted by a surprisingly airy and contemporary décor. A family - run establishment that specialises in generous dishes with a dash of originality prepared on the spot. Fantastic wine list.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16636;Minerva;Belgium;Antwerpen;Karel Oomsstraat 36, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.1961543;4.4093223;85;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Minerva was a legendary Belgian luxury automobile firm, whose repair workshops were located here. The site is now that of a well-oiled restaurant, whose outer industrial casing hides a warm, even stylish interior. The menu abounds in pedigree gourmet classics, prepared with textbook skill and flair, even the meat is still carved at the table. The turbot is cooked on the bone and served with a light frothy mustardy sauce, unless you wouldn’t prefer Barbary duck, carved in front of you, and garnished with a sauce that is made from blood and bone marrow that is extracted by way of a press – heroically wondrous! At Minerva, quality is much more than a word – it is a way of life!;Air conditioning;[]
16637;Hispania;Belgium;Brussels;rue Bodenbroek 2, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8408155;4.3557049;19;false;true;Spanish;Hispania is smart and contemporary, but down to earth, like the Spanish cooking it honours. Marcos Morán of the Michelin star restaurant, Casa Gerardo, in Prendes, Spain, continues to roll out a varied menu that will enable you to sample tapas, traditional rice dishes, together with more modern creations. The accent is on big-boned, punchy flavours. The memory of the Galician veal, cooked rare, served with foie gras and an espuma of potatoes and truffles lingers still with our inspectors. A lineup of authentic Hispanic flavours, designed to transport you straight to southern Europe.;Air conditioning;[]
16638;La Buvette;Belgium;Saint-Gilles;chaussée d'Alsemberg 108, Saint-Gilles, 1060, Belgium;50.8233605;4.3430762;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Organic;We wager that this restaurant will quickly become your favourite watering hole. The vintage interior of this former butcher’s shop oozes character and appeal, further enhanced by reasonably priced bistronomic fare. The single set menu overflows with elegant sauces and creative flair.;Terrace;[]
16639;'t Truffeltje;Belgium;Dendermonde;Bogaerdstraat 20, Dendermonde, 9200, Belgium;51.0310014;4.1026273;72;true;false;Modern French, Modern Cuisine;’t Truffeltje has enjoyed a stellar reputation ever since Pol and Greta first opened the restaurant back in 1988. Chef Marien demonstrates his mastery of French culinary technique, deploying his consummate know-how and choosing only the best produce. Subtle exotic influences add an occasional stylish twist.;Terrace;[]
16640;d'Artagnan;Belgium;Leuven;Naamsestraat 72, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8754822;4.7001674;28;false;false;Modern French;Epicureans will be delighted by the elegant, refined interior and charming rear terrace. Diners can choose between a classical or a more creative menu, both equally precise and flavoursome. Private parking by reservation.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16641;d'Oude Schuur;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Latem;Baarle Frankrijkstraat 1, Sint-Martens-Latem, 9830, Belgium;51.0241093;3.6239813;90;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Wine takes front stage in this pretty farmstead with a courtyard patio and warm lights twinkling indoors. In addition to adorning the walls, it is above all the passion with which the wine is served that sets the scene. Burgundy takes pride of place on the wine list, a genuine bible. The chef adds subtle, modern twists to traditional recipes, underscoring tuna tartare with Asian accents, for example, while the sole meunière is quite simply the summum of textbook perfection.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16642;Siphon;Belgium;Oostkerke;Damse Vaart-Oost 1, Oostkerke, 8340, Belgium;51.2664364;3.297937;88;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Be it with sorrel, meunière or à la crème, people flock to this characterful restaurant from near and far to enjoy the house speciality, eel. They also offer grilled lobster and steak, as a quick look at their menu, an ode to tradition, will confirm. Siphon has become something of a culinary landmark in the region, further backed up by an intelligent wine list.;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16643;De Stadt van Luijck;Belgium;Sint-Truiden;Schepen Dejonghstraat 12, Sint-Truiden, 3800, Belgium;50.814457;5.1891475;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A meal in this former solicitor’s home oozing in character will be one to remember. The stylish interior, which sports a refined Renaissance slant, and the garden are a treat for the eye. Your tastebuds will be pampered by chef Warren Vandevelde who demonstrates just how much his carefully crafted cuisine is in line with the zeitgeist. The chef works tirelessly to create surprising associations, constantly adding new twists to familiar flavours. For example, he may pair a tartare of warm langoustine with a tomato coulis, a langoustine bisque and sea lavender oil. The lunchtime menu is not be missed!;Terrace;[]
16644;Laurel & Hardy;Belgium;Oostkamp;Majoor Woodstraat 3, Oostkamp, 8020, Belgium;51.1543708;3.2346846;48;false;false;Farm to table;In tribute to the legendary comic duo, the chef of this modern restaurant will no doubt bring a smile to your face, thanks to his delicious, well-planned, unfussy cuisine, focused on fresh produce. Fine, reasonably priced wine list.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16645;Pot au Feu;Belgium;Olen;Dorp 34, Olen, 2250, Belgium;51.1445471;4.8601762;64;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Christine Van Deun has settled down in this lovely Art deco villa. Trendy interior with vintage details, inviting bar and conservatory overlooking the terrace - garden. The chef pampers our taste buds with comforting traditional recipes. The extensive menu makes choosing a conundrum!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16646;Messeyne;Belgium;Kortrijk;Groeningestraat 17, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.8299871;3.2700795;26;true;false;Creative, Modern Cuisine;The locals adore this cosy restaurant and its terrace in the adjacent gardens. The French cuisine is up - to - the - minute, full of flavour and unfussy.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16647;Njord;Belgium;Zeebrugge;Rederskaai 60, Zeebrugge, 8380, Belgium;51.33522;3.20828;79;false;true;Belgian, Classic French;Make a beeline for the top floor of the amazing ABC edifice and admire the jaw-dropping view over the port and marina below. Luxurious and trendy, the restaurant specialises in ultra-fresh delicacies straight from the local fish auction. Traditional, authentic flavours that respect the character and freshness of the ingredients. Slick service. The seafood platter is also available in individual portions.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16648;Wine in the City;Belgium;Jette;place Reine Astrid 34, Jette, 1090, Belgium;50.8723108;4.3240522;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine, International;Make your way past the shelves of bottles and into the dining room-cum-wine cellar of Eddy and Arnaud Münster. Father and son work side by side in their small open-plan kitchen, while mum Isabelle curates the knockout wine list with the chefs. The food features a range of tapas to share depicted by an international, creative and fun-loving edge. Examples include slow-baked cod in sea lavender and a sesame sauce that definitely packs a punch, or homemade lamb tortellini in a scrumptious sakura-flavoured stock. What’s not to like?;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16649;Bar(t)-à-vin;Belgium;Antwerpen;Lange Slachterijstraat 3, Antwerpen, 2060, Belgium;51.2289291;4.432903;93;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Authentic, polished and vintage – such is the vibe of this delightful bistro, quirkily established in a former butchery, as the colourful wall tiles and meat hooks bear witness. The concise menu is a guarantee of quality. Pedigree Gallic standards like steak tartare or less common dishes like a stew of girolle mushrooms, sea lavender and poached egg are crafted with text-book precision, blessedly free of fripperies and packed in punchy flavour. Ask Bart, a walking wine encyclopaedia, for his insightful tips to help you choose just the right tipple to pair with your meal. At the weekends, Bart Gils and Sally Lauwers run the joint, in line with its founding DNA.;;[]
16650;Brasserie Boulevard;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Latem;Kortrijksesteenweg 175, Sint-Martens-Latem, 9830, Belgium;51.0088711;3.6331523;21;true;true;Belgian, Classic Cuisine;This swanky, spacious brasserie flooded in light is invariably packed to the seams. Thomas endeavours to ensure that your dining experience is as pleasant as it is flavoursome. Classic brasserie fare enhanced with a few spontaneous personal touches. The inspiring choice ranges from snacks to share, luxury vol-au-vent or trendier recipes….;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16651;Les Terrasses de l'Our;Belgium;Our;rue de la Lesse 1, Our, 6852, Belgium;49.96228;5.123651;16;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The opportunity to dine on the riverside terrace of this restaurant is not to be missed. Natural materials adorn the interior of this endearing brasserie, which is emblematic of the Ardennes, as is the food: game, trout, local ham prepared to textbook perfection… A daring new spin jazzes up familiar favourites, always with lashings of fresh flavour.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16652;Nonbe Daigaku;Belgium;Ixelles;avenue Adolphe Buyl 31, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8173993;4.3807128;77;false;false;Japanese, Sushi;If you like eating Japanese, you shouldn’t miss this modest venue. The very experienced chef has mastered the subtlety and nuances that are typical of the cuisine of his home country. You can see him at work behind the sushi bar, driven and precise, creating a delicious variety of flavours and textures.;;[]
16653;Maru;Belgium;Ixelles;chaussée de Waterloo 510, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8200542;4.3598302;24;false;false;Korean, Asian;This urban Korean eatery on the doorstep of the Châtelain district never fails to deliver. The locals flock here at lunchtime to polish off a main course or take their time over a more leisurely meal with a glass of wine. Pajeon is one of its star dishes: a crisp pancake filled with meat or fish flanked by a sweet vinaigrette and a spicy chili sauce. This dish symbolises the delicate balance between sweet, sour and spicy notes achieved by the chef, further underscored by a playful melody of varied textures. The epitome of authentic Korean nosh!;;[]
16654;Hostellerie De Biek;Belgium;Moorsel;Moorsel-Dorp 3, Moorsel, 9310, Belgium;50.9478387;4.0981535;39;true;true;Country cooking;We wager that before you even set foot in this family-run eatery, you will have fallen in love with the authentic Flemish village. The immense windows of the former brewery overlook the village and a sheltered terrace, while the striking interior sports timber rafters and brick walls. Before relaxing in one of the comfortable guestrooms, treat yourself to something from the extensive menu. Brabançon-style pheasant or bouchot mussels served in a spicy nduja and red curry sauce: the chef adds a kick to Belgian classics thanks to playful, creative inventions. A knockout lineup of regional produce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16655;De Blauwe Artisjok;Belgium;Merelbeke;Gaversesteenweg 182, Merelbeke, 9820, Belgium;50.9973272;3.7402038;88;false;false;Modern French;Satisfied customers are the raison d’être of this stylish villa, where you are graciously greeted by Nathalie before taking a seat in the elegant dining room. Veteran chef Kurt Verhaege aims to work with fresh, seasonal produce. He boasts a classical training and his textbook perfect champagne sauce is a model of French culinary technique, as are his main courses and side dishes, which also feature a subtle international slant. Delicious eater-friendly prices.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16656;Jacob's;Belgium;Nandrin;route du Condroz 211, Nandrin, 4550, Belgium;50.5136485;5.4038263;97;false;false;Meats and Grills;Juicy red meat straight out of the wood-burning Josper oven is the signature of this hip joint done up in dark colours. The staff is both jovial and professional and it is a pleasure to watch the chefs in their open kitchen deploying their talent to craft spot-on food packed in flavour. Whether it is impeccably cooked hanger steak garnished with a bearnaise sauce and fresh fries or their take on French toast (to die for!), generosity defines the ethos of this establishment. It is of course heaven for meat lovers, but the menu also offers fish and lobster.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16657;La Fleur de Thym;Belgium;Houffalize;route de Liège 34, Houffalize, 6660, Belgium;50.1356609;5.7863167;100;false;false;Creative French, Modern Cuisine;David et Olivia vous emportent dans une aventure ardennaise moderne. Les bois de cerf sont bien sûr au rendez-vous, mais dans un décor intime et élégant, aux accents colorés. La cuisine est résolument au goût du jour, surtout dans son exécution. Le chef David respecte les saveurs familières de ses produits, qu’il glorifie avec un grand savoir-faire.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16658;La Croustade;Belgium;Heusy;rue Hodiamont 13, Heusy, 4802, Belgium;50.5765845;5.8690969;66;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Lovingly tended flowerbeds, a delightful cottage garden and goldfish in the pond - dining on the terrace of this exquisite country house is heavenly in fine weather. Every month, chef Thierry composes a new menu that demonstrates his classical training and know-how. He freely delves into the cottage garden to enhance dishes such as mint-crusted rack of lamb and pan-fried foie gras.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16659;Tanuki;Belgium;Brugge;Oude Gentweg 1, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2028677;3.2257552;32;false;false;Teppanyaki, Asian Influences;Since 1989 Ivan Verhelle has been treating his diners to a genuine taste of Japan. The table service and interior are larger than life and the open - plan kitchen provides a bird’s eye view of the preparation of fine ingredients, such as fresh wasabi. The chef is a fan of teppanyaki cuisine and can even organise (bookings) a tea ceremony.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16660;Apriori;Belgium;Haaltert;Sint-Goriksplein 19, Haaltert, 9450, Belgium;50.902204;4.0051572;56;true;true;Creative;Kristof Coppens lets his imagination run riot as he endeavours to source and exalt produce from all over the world, combining, enhancing and respecting each ingredient’s intrinsic qualities. For example, classical flavours find their way onto the menu, providing they can be paired with his creative recipes. The wine list is a treasure trove of tipples from Italy, Spain and France. A bijou eatery if ever there was!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16661;Bistro Rombaux;Belgium;Sint-Kruis;Moerkerkse Steenweg 139, Sint-Kruis, 8310, Belgium;51.2135199;3.2478287;100;false;true;Modern French;Pieter-Jan Rombaux and his wife, Tineke, do everything themselves and the focus is clearly home-made. She nurtures the cheerful, unstuffy vibe, while he rustles up dishes that seek to enhance the ingredient’s pure flavours with perfect seasonings. Take a seat on the secluded terrace to admire the chef at work in the kitchen. Rather than gimmicky surprises, you can look forward to heart-warming dishes such as foie gras with brioche or hanger steak with a red-wine sauce to die for.;Terrace;[]
16662;Goesepitte 43;Belgium;Brugge;Goezeputstraat 43, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.204415;3.2200066;99;true;true;Farm to table, Modern French;Step into the picturesque Goezeputstraat 43 and be transported to a jungle paradise, complete with a living moss wall and monkeys! Chef Jan Supply likes to come to the table in person to serve his dishes. These are characterised by a deft use of the Mibrasa charcoal oven, rich sauces and intriguing vegetable creations. This is bistronomy with that little bit extra, as evidenced by the hand-whipped lobster béarnaise that elevates smoky filet pur to new heights. Be sure to try the crêpe normande, a house classic.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16663;Maison du Luxembourg;Belgium;Ixelles;rue du Luxembourg 37, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8394192;4.3710638;45;true;false;Regional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;A stone's throw from the EU Parliament, this contemporary establishment champions the bounty of Luxembourg's terroir. The restaurant draws an international crowd, who come to savour an array of culinary treats, frequently sourced from the province of Wallonia, including seasonal specialties such as asparagus and wild game. To suit the palate of the modern urban diner, traditional recipes are reworked with a light touch and a sprinkle of international flair, without sacrificing their core flavours. Smoked eel, for example, forms a winning combination with foie gras, a poached egg and subtly spicy rocket coulis.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16664;Pacht 26;Belgium;Gijzegem;Pachthofstraat 26, Gijzegem, 9308, Belgium;50.985355;4.04911;76;true;false;Farm to table;Stefaan, chef and sommelier, is an enthusiastic foodie and wine connoisseur. He regularly scours eastern Europe to enrich his wine list. The many regulars to his friendly, welcoming establishment applaud the wine formula which reveals the full scope of his creativity. Each dish is a consummate blend of character and delicacy with legible ingredients such as duck’s liver and beetroot, depicted in fresh, subtle nuances.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16665;L'Esprit Bouddha;Belgium;Gosselies;Place des Martyrs 30, Gosselies, 6041, Belgium;50.4660026;4.4289001;65;false;false;Chinese, Organic;Light years from the clichés traditionally associated with Chinese restaurants, l’Esprit Bouddha is a modern establishment on a permanent quest for subtlety, but that hasn’t forgotten its roots for all that. Start your meal with beef gyoza, before digging into finger-licking tasty little house pancakes stuffed with crisp Peking duck, vegetables and a punchy hoisin sauce. The epitome of Asian generosity with an absolutely knockout wine list.;Terrace;[]
16666;Brasserie Bijgaarden;Belgium;Groot-Bijgaarden;Isidoor Van Beverenstraat 20, Groot-Bijgaarden, 1702, Belgium;50.8729734;4.2655203;68;false;false;Classic Cuisine;This highly popular brasserie with a chic and discreet decor is a real institution. There is a wide variety of specialities on the à la carte menu at reasonable prices (attractive specials). Large terrace surrounded by greenery.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16667;Karel De Stoute;Belgium;Gent;Vrouwebroerstraat 2, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0581503;3.7225504;82;false;false;Modern French, Farm to table;Karel De Stoute is steeped in character, as you will see from the elegant décor of this edifice in the heart of the Patershol district, but also in the plate. Your charming hostess, Lien, is proud to present the menu of creative chef Thomas, who is as attentive to the flavour of his food as to its presentation. Fascinating, cheerful and delicious.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16668;De Mangerie;Belgium;Brugge;Oude Burg 20, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.20666;3.2243221;93;false;true;World Cuisine;Kristof Deprez is keen to share his love of Asia. As soon as you venture over the threshold of the Mangerie, it feels like you are on holiday. The chef rustles up local Belgian dishes with oriental influences, creating a finely balanced, tempting menu.;;[]
16669;Racines;Belgium;Ixelles;chaussée d'Ixelles 353, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8280544;4.3711477;60;false;false;Italian;Leave the noisy Chaussée d'Ixelles and walk past the grocery counter into this delightfully vintage restaurant, which is awash in Mediterranean details and boasts an delightful terrace. Welcome to this authentic Italian establishment, where the chef will take you on a culinary journey from the north to the south of the Boot. Try the house-made tagliolini with parmesan and earthy cavolo nero, or the intensely flavoursome San Marzano tomato flan, drizzled with olive oil. The chef's creative and meticulous take on traditional recipes shines through. Featuring an impressive range of Italian labels, the wine list is well worth exploring.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16670;Lammekeshoeve;Belgium;Grimbergen;Veldkantstraat 100, Grimbergen, 1850, Belgium;50.9356049;4.3827285;63;false;false;Modern French;The epitome of a swish, luxurious brasserie, this establishment also boasts an exquisite leafy patio for alfresco dining and a conservatory for summer vibes the rest of the year. The chef seamlessly skips from a traditional to a modern repertory, with one guideline: generosity. Whether you sample a fresh Mediterranean medley of haddock or dig into textbook perfect profiteroles, you can depend on each dish being as flavoursome as the next. Quality takes pride of place every time, also in the wine list.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16671;Ricciocapriccio;Belgium;Ixelles;rue Américaine 90, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.823308;4.3591748;72;false;false;Italian;This bistro is a popular spot for Belgian Italians, as evidenced by the amount of Italian that is spoken here. The chef, a fan of fine produce (sea urchins and squid are his specialties), deftly whisks up enticing dishes featuring carefully considered and, occasionally, unusual combinations. For instance, he prepares risotto with a sea bream tartare and parmesan foam, or puts a new spin on the classic tiramisu, but he always respects the essence of the dishes he prepares. The ample à la carte menu promises a Mediterranean feast!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16672;Silo's;Belgium;Boortmeerbeek;Leuvensesteenweg 350, Boortmeerbeek, 3190, Belgium;50.9664788;4.5719978;97;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Silo’s is breathing life into the annex of the former malt house of Boortmeerbeek. The slick, well-oiled operations of this trendy luxury brasserie work like clockwork, seamlessly catering to large numbers of diners. The food is equally spot on, featuring updated versions of brasserie classics such as bouillabaisse and Clamart pigeon steeped in knockout flavours. Generous, voluntarily unfussy recipes that hit the nail on the head every time. The extensive menu and wine list, (including wines by the glass), ensures that there is something to tickle everyone’s fancy!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16673;Assiette Blanche;Belgium;Brugge;Philipstockstraat 23, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2096022;3.2263567;98;true;true;Modern French;The locals flock to this bistro, which appeals equally to socialites and a more casual crowd. The jovial mistress of the house and the subtle cooking of chef Timmerman further add to the establishment’s friendly vibe. Gutsy Gallic flavours are combined with vivacious Asian highlights, without forgetting local produce, in particular North Sea fish. Classical fare with a twist in the heart of picturesque Bruges.;Air conditioning;[]
16674;La Truffe Noire;Belgium;Brussels;boulevard de la Cambre 12, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8162438;4.3767059;81;true;false;Classic Cuisine, Italian;Black or white (truffle) is a frequent dilemma for diners at La Truffe Noire, a model of classical elegance since 1988. Truffles unsurprisingly take the limelight in the culinary score of its seasoned chef, who also happily adds a dash of Mediterranean flavours. Beef carpaccio prepared at your table is one of the house signature dishes. Our inspectors also fell in love with the mouthwatering sole, served with an aromatic black truffle sauce, baby artichoke and a crunchy parmesan crumble. Deftly crafted, purebred bourgeois recipes for a polished fine dining experience.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16675;Les Plats Canailles de la Bleue Maison;Belgium;Habay-la-Neuve;rue du Pont d'Oye 7, Habay-la-Neuve, 6720, Belgium;49.7351746;5.6720762;22;true;true;French, Farm to table;The picture postcard scene features a blue-shuttered gingerbread house poised between two rivers. The exquisite neo-rustic interior exudes a romantic vibe. Brice and Martin Thiry have added gusto and verve to this family business. They favour local produce and juggle with modern flavours such as acidity whilst respecting the ethos of traditional recipes. So, fancy sharing a rib of beef, carved in front of you, washed down with a glass of full-bodied wine? Good food and good vibes are the backbone of this endearing eatery.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16676;Boîte;Belgium;Sint-Idesbald;Oostendelaan 1, Sint-Idesbald, 8670, Belgium;51.11095;2.612012;89;true;false;World Cuisine;What a pity we don’t live down the road from this amusing "box"! “Taste the world, Share the food” is their baseline! The seasoned chef curates her own version of world cuisine, steeped in variety, harmony and exoticism… For example, deftly crafted spicy Lebanese toast, generous tajine, sweet and sour noodles, etc. Even better, diners can choose their own vegetable side dishes and are invited to share the main course with the rest of the table. Perfect for a casual dining experience!;Terrace;[]
16677;Cousteau;Belgium;Eernegem;Oostendsesteenweg 230, Eernegem, 8480, Belgium;51.1301771;2.9854172;32;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Guy and Julie’s elegant establishment, flanked by a garden and a leafy alfresco area, is irresistible. Together, they run the show with brio, leaving no detail to chance from the service to the food. Chef Guy’s straightforward approach seeks to craft subtle, flavourful dishes with just a few painstakingly selected ingredients, illustrated by summertime tomatoes and burrata or a generous fillet of fresh fish served with a superlative beurre blanc.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16678;Stirwen;Belgium;Etterbeek;chaussée Saint-Pierre 15, Etterbeek, 1040, Belgium;50.8361461;4.3827388;44;false;false;Modern French;Elegance and comfort depict this restaurant, a long-standing institution in the European district. François-Xavier Lambory takes a new look at textbook Gallic cuisine. He painstakingly sources his ingredients, assembling them into highly inspired, unusual recipes.;;[]
16679;Le Flore;Belgium;Wulveringem;Zwaantje 13, Wulveringem, 8630, Belgium;51.0268674;2.6400118;15;true;true;French Contemporary;Le Flore is magnificently set in a restored farm-castle. The view over the meadows from the terrace is stunning. Chef Verlande rustles up enticing lunchtime fare and a varied menu, where the focus is on fine produce such as turbot, lobster and pigeon. Rich and generous are the hallmarks of his cuisine.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16681;De Oogappel;Belgium;Veurne;Appelmarkt 3, Veurne, 8630, Belgium;51.071854;2.663;51;true;true;Sharing;This 1760’s edifice, graced in period floors and wardrobes, is now the venue of a friendly bistro serving traditional fare to the joy of discerning gourmets. The appetising menu of starters to share displays a more modern twist with Asian influences. We recommend the crispy sweetbread 'fine champagne' – the house signature dish. Go there your eyes closed.;Terrace;[]
16682;Wasserette;Belgium;Nieuwpoort;Marktstraat 38, Nieuwpoort, 8620, Belgium;51.1305837;2.7521925;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;The washing hanging from the ceiling is a reminder of the former laundromat that has morphed into a hip eatery firmly part of Nieuwpoort’s culinary scene. The menu features mouth-watering dishes served in small and large portions, flanked by a fine wine list. Unfussy recipes, often prepared à la minute, such as grilled brill with Belgian endive, velvety mash potatoes and a flavoursome shrimp sauce.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16683;Butcher's Dining;Belgium;Hove;Kapelstraat 102, Hove, 2540, Belgium;51.1550462;4.4653535;83;true;true;Meats and Grills;The cosy restaurant of butcher shop De Laet & Van Haver is a veritable paradise for carnivores. Faced with such an array of delectable options, from Secreto 07 and entrecôtes of aged meat to traditional stews and offal, you'll be spoilt for choice. The carefully considered trimmings are a testament to the butcher's commitment to quality and craftsmanship. Think beautifully marbled cut of Simmental beef, simply seasoned with coarse salt and rosemary, and served with a tomato salad and a lightly whipped béarnaise sauce. What a feast!;Terrace;[]
16684;Julia;Belgium;Sint-Idesbald;A. Vanhouttelaan 2, Sint-Idesbald, 8670, Belgium;51.1098877;2.6106461;68;true;true;Seafood;A fishmonger (Mare Nostrum) at the head of a fish bistro, complete with a maritime interior, right down to the fish scales? It sounds so authentic that it just has to be true… Fish and oysters from the “sea to the fork” and the best shrimp fritters of the Belgian coast into the bargain. Julia’s simple, generous cooking is heaven for foodies.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16685;'t Kantientje;Belgium;Ramskapelle;Ramskapellestraat 61, Ramskapelle, 8301, Belgium;51.3148404;3.2505705;34;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Pille Senior and Junior work side by side in the kitchen of this elegant canteen in the picturesque village of Ramskapelle. In summertime, the terrace is very popular. The food is stripped back, handcrafted and traditional with a weakness for fish. Shrimp fritters, lobster belle vue and freshly prepared sabayon: delicate flavours that appeal time and time again. The fine wine list is fully in tune with this high-class establishment.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16686;Storm;Belgium;Oostende;Hendrik Baelskaai 21, Oostende, 8400, Belgium;51.2337218;2.9342062;65;false;false;Modern French, Seafood;Storms do not prevent fishing boats from mooring in front of the door. The experienced chef pays them tribute with a host of delicacies, using modern techniques (including a passing nod to Asia and Scandinavia). However, relax, the cosy interior and cheerful staff will ensure you weather this storm in style.;Air conditioning;[]
16687;Mondieu;Belgium;Koksijde;Ten Bogaerdelaan 10, Koksijde, 8670, Belgium;51.0905801;2.6343461;47;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;OMG! Not only is the view over the polders from the terrace jaw-dropping, the bright interior of this former 17C cloister is equally appealing. Seasoned chef Ian Wittevrongel smoothly and seamlessly crafts first-class ingredients such as Steenvoorde pigeon and eel (he avows a weakness for local delicacies). All the no-nonsense dishes are à la carte and unveil his flair for gutsy, full-bodied flavours. The sommelier shares his knowledge and insights, guiding you through the stonking 400-reference wine bin!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16688;La Coupole;Belgium;De Panne;Nieuwpoortlaan 9, De Panne, 8660, Belgium;51.1030557;2.5910216;87;false;false;Seafood;La Coupole has been a blue - chip value since 1989. Diners enjoy the low - key, trendy atmosphere. The lobster and fish specialties are served by chef Bonnez’ brother, further proof of the establishment’s quality. Excellent wines.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16689;Saint-Christophe;Belgium;Kortrijk;Minister Tacklaan 5, Kortrijk, 8500, Belgium;50.8238866;3.2677844;92;false;false;Creative French;This handsome town house boasts a classical interior with high ceilings, a pastel brown colour scheme and a delightful terrace. The chef places great importance on the quality of his ingredients, which he incorporates into modern flavoursome recipes that are rich in character. We wholeheartedly recommend the formula and the all-inclusive menus.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16690;Bristol;Belgium;Heist;Zeedijk 291, Heist, 8301, Belgium;51.3416539;3.2454254;59;false;false;Farm to table;This bright, spacious brasserie on the seafront has been a landmark of Knokke-Heist for aeons. Expertly prepared Belgian classics are the specialities of the house. Think crispy shrimp croquettes (said to be the best around!) and pan-seared sole with a tartar sauce prepared à la minute. The chef loves working with North Sea fish, but also has a passion for meat dishes and seasonal specialties, such as hop shoots with mousseline sauce. These timeless brasserie classics are simply irresistible!;Air conditioning,Great view;[]
16691;Flavie's tafel;Belgium;Nieuwpoort;Langestraat 115, Nieuwpoort, 8620, Belgium;51.1322648;2.7505426;86;false;true;Seafood;Valérie's (Flavie) open kitchen takes centre stage in this pleasant restaurant adorned with colourful frescoes. The chef has a preference for fresh, carefully selected fish, as the tempting menu bears witness. A fine feast in store for your taste buds.;;[]
16692;GLASS;Belgium;Antwerpen;Vlaamsekaai 40, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2097546;4.3908926;69;true;true;French Contemporary, Classic French;Wine bistro GLASS is elegant and cosy – make a beeline for the terrace on Vlaamse Kaai if you really want to soak up the hip atmosphere of the Zuid neighbourhood. Sally, who presides front-of-house, consistently proves that she is a hostess at heart, while chef Alain showcases his versatility. His cuisine is intricate and draws inspiration from both Eastern and Western culinary traditions. Think house-made pasta stuffed with potato and truffle, paired with ginger and five-spice chicken, Chinese cabbage, a creamy truffle sauce and foie gras. He balances rich flavours with a sure touch, creating ingredient-led cuisine that is truly captivating.;Air conditioning;[]
16693;Basile;Belgium;Bovesse;Rue du Moulin 52, Bovesse, 5081, Belgium;50.5225986;4.779847;25;false;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Basile De Wulf’s endearing restaurant is part of La Petite Campagne farm, which boasts both a butcher’s and a dairy. Established in a modern-day wooden chalet, the chef will introduce you to local produce (some from the farm) rich in gutsy, rustic flavours. After stints in a number of top establishments, Basile seeks to showcase fresh ingredients with an international twang. The chef’s surprise menu is tailored to today’s tastebuds and his passion for wine adds the final flourish to a fine meal.;Car park;[]
16694;Bistro Le Nord;Belgium;Roeselare;Noordstraat 217, Roeselare, 8800, Belgium;50.9510234;3.1198041;62;false;true;French Contemporary;Pop into this elegant bistro and sip an aperitif with a nibble at Bar 18, before sitting down to a more substantial dish. Dimitris Karagiannis rolls out Franco-Belgian family favourites enriched with subtle international influences such as dashi stock or a buttermilk sauce. Well-crafted, modern, even amusing food that lives up to its promises. Why not stay longer and book a night in the cosy B&B?;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16695;Hertebos;Belgium;s-Gravenwezel;Wijnegemsteenweg 132, 's-Gravenwezel, 2970, Belgium;51.2537427;4.5463628;25;true;false;Farm to table;In Yasmine and Yoshi's living room-style restaurant, photographs on the walls give a glimpse into their past, and an open fireplace lends the place a cosy feel. In both the set menu and the repertoire of à la carte classics, the freshness of the ingredients stands out. The two chefs are as creative with textures as they are with their intensely flavoursome sauces. For instance, they bring out all the facets of raspberry and yoghurt, combined with a cake soaked in Amaretto, to create a dazzling dessert.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16696;Bistrot L'îlot;Belgium;Antwerpen;Kribbestraat 15, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2301524;4.4101331;66;false;false;Farm to table, French Contemporary;A Parisian vibe mixed with industrial and minimalist details sets the welcoming scene. “What you see is what you get” is their motto! The chef intertwines international inspirations and punchy flavours as he orchestrates a mouth-watering score. He gives flawlessly steamed halibut a playful edge by flanking it with a range of mushroom textures and an expressive buttermilk crème. Rather than fussy frills, you can expect dishes in the zeitgeist and a splendid selection of (mainly French) wines.;Terrace;[]
16697;La Botte;Belgium;Genk;Europalaan 99, Genk, 3600, Belgium;50.9662866;5.5011215;47;false;true;Italian;A meal at the establishment of charismatic Peppe and sommelier Gaspare Giacomazza, the second generation of the house, is a genuine feast. This unstuffy eatery, which serves authentic and original Sicilian fare, is depicted by a buzzy, easy-going vibe. The food is fresh, generous and supremely delicate. A fine tribute to Italy’s many delicacies, underscored by a handsome wine cellar, in which the quintessential Piedmontese Nebbiolo grape variety enjoys a star role.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16698;Essenz;Belgium;Antwerpen;Kronenburgstraat 35, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2122989;4.3959361;82;false;false;Modern French;Stylish modernity paints the picture in this cosy eatery, both in the setting and the plate. Joris Hoefkens adds fresh, subtle touches to the patriotic Franco-Belgian line-up, with dishes such as marinated hamachi (yellowtail fish) served with an avocado ice cream or scorpion fish with a chlorophyl jus made with mussels. These and other delicacies embody Essenz’ culinary elegance.;Terrace;[]
16699;Aux Armes de Bruxelles;Belgium;Brussels;rue des Bouchers 13, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8481096;4.3539882;85;true;false;Belgian, Classic Cuisine;This institution in the heart of historic Brussels immerses you in the Ilot Sacré district. Its traditional brasserie décor dripping in Art nouveau character and the table service in period costume are a hit every time. The varied menu is a compendium of Belgian favourites: eels in sorrel sauce or veal kidneys in mustard, served with piping hot crunchy fries, and finishing with decadent crêpes Comédie française (Grand Marnier liqueur plus vanilla ice cream) – scrumptious!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16700;Moma;Belgium;Annevoie-Rouillon;Chaussée de Namur 72, Annevoie-Rouillon, 5537, Belgium;50.34531;4.8542;26;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The view of the River Meuse and its lush green banks immediately catches the eye as you enter Moma. Olivier Bruckner reveals his flair for enhancing each dish with subtle details, like a sweet-sour tomato and rich creamy burrata which provide the perfect foil to lacquered calf sweetbread. The menu features classical and gastronomic recipes, all of which are enticingly displayed thanks to inspired plating and at gloriously eater-friendly prices.;Great view,Terrace;[]
16701;Nils;Belgium;Koksijde;Koninklijke Baan 62, Koksijde, 8670, Belgium;51.121655;2.6400151;97;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Nils is the epitome of a modern restaurant. Tasteful, low - key interior, delightful staff and a talented chef, whose cooking is both creative and refined. The interplay of textures highlights the subtle varying flavours. A night at Carnac Hotel will round off the experience perfectly.;Terrace;[]
16702;Meteor;Belgium;Heffen;Sint-Amandusstraat 5, Heffen, 2801, Belgium;51.0474555;4.422599;59;false;true;Organic;Words such as “organic” and “local” are far more than trendy or faddish for Maarten Van Essche, starting with the lovely natural interior of this former presbytery. His à la carte menu keeps pace with the seasons: when the tomatoes are ripe, he mixes them into a gutsy sauce with nduja and spelt pasta. When it’s mushroom season, he whips up his own version of the nation’s comfort food: mushrooms on toast. In summer, don’t miss the bouchot mussel appetisers. Free of fussy frills, Meteor seeks to showcase pure flavours.;Terrace;[]
16703;Brasserie Daefnis;Belgium;Lauwe;Rekkemstraat 2, Lauwe, 8930, Belgium;50.7946993;3.1804995;45;true;false;Modern French;It isn’t easy to nab a table in this luxury brasserie, which is always a sign of top-notch quality. Daefnis specialises in first-rate produce: North Sea sole, fillet of venison and premium Holstein beef are just a few of the delicacies that are showcased on the up-to-date brasserie menu. Familiar flavours are nonetheless respected, albeit with judicious nuances.;Terrace;[]
16704;Atelier Gist;Belgium;Goeferdinge;Goeferdingeplein 21, Goeferdinge, 9500, Belgium;50.7661791;3.8426655;71;true;false;Creative;Fire and fermentation are key at Atelier Gist, a converted barn with floor-to-ceiling windows that afford views of the surrounding fields. Seated at a counter overlooking the open kitchen, diners can watch chef Jason work his magic at the barbecue and charcoal-fired oven. He elevates the robust barbecue flavours with bursts of citrus and Japanese seasonings. For instance, he grills venison fillet over the binchotan and then seasons it with koji. A rich beef jus made from the carcass, red cabbage and a delicate beetroot and fig cream bring out the inherent quality of these premium ingredients. The recommended natural wines and house-made kombucha takes this symphony of flavours to new heights.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace;[]
16705;Plëss;;Luxembourg;18 place d'Armes, 1136, Luxembourg;49.611491;6.1288934;26;false;false;Classic Cuisine;The opulent Plëss brasserie is just as elegant as the swish Place d’Armes Hotel in which it is housed. A quick glance at the menu will reveal that rotisserie and carvery dishes feature prominently in the classic lineup. The veal cutlet is grilled to perfection and flanked by a punchy gravy. You have the choice of side dishes, from Robuchon mashed potato to seasonal veggies, while other delicacies include foie gras in red wine and balsamic vinegar. The meat is carved at the table in traditional brasserie style. A mouth-watering "plëss-ure"!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16706;Domaine la Forêt;Luxembourg;Remich;36 route de l'Europe, Remich, 5531, Luxembourg;49.5478168;6.3584429;52;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This elegant, classical restaurant commands a stunning view over the Luxemburg Moselle valley. Chef, Claude Wallerich, concocts tasty dishes of traditional inspiration that will introduce you to delicious regional produce. The well - stocked wine cellar is an added bonus!;Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16707;La Rameaudière;Luxembourg;Ellange;10 rue de la Gare, Ellange, 5690, Luxembourg;49.5162784;6.3044571;45;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Daniel Rameau is a connoisseur of luxury produce, among which foie gras, lobster and pigeon, which he prepares refreshingly simply in dishes that blend generosity and tradition. The equally enticing wine list features a savvy selection of Luxemburg vintages. This former village train station and its flower-decked terrace are steeped in vintage charm.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16708;Bosque FeVi;Luxembourg;Esch-sur-Alzette;50 rue Gaalgebierg, Esch-sur-Alzette, 4142, Luxembourg;49.4838769;5.9862055;40;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;If your tastebuds start to tingle at the idea of biting into a “croquetas de jamón” and a “crema catalana” with a hint of citrus fruit, then book a table straight away in this exquisite restaurant, depicted by a striking “undulating” wooden wall-cum-artwork. Fernando Andreu conjures up a Mediterranean score with a dash of modernity by delving into his Spanish roots and the odd international influence like kimchi or tikka masala. If you’re in the mood for tapas, make a beeline for FeVi Gaudium, under the same roof of the Seven Hotel.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16709;Brasserie des Jardins;;Luxembourg;27b boulevard Marcel Cahen, 1311, Luxembourg;49.6026881;6.1022744;15;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;If only we lived next-door to this modern brasserie… Slick, seamless service, a peaceful patio and a traditional lineup crafted by expert hands. The calf’s liver, cooked to perfection, is paired with a shallot sauce, the salmon, raw, cooked or smoked, glistens in an unusual starter, flanked by, among others, kiwi, mango and a coulis of red beetroot: the chef clearly knows his business. The knockout wine list further confirms the establishment’s commitment to fine produce.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16710;Octo;Belgium;Aalbeke;Aalbekeplaats 8, Aalbeke, 8511, Belgium;50.77877;3.2302;27;false;true;Classic Cuisine;This updated, new age brasserie is the work of a youthful chef and the trendy vibe and slick service are paired with traditional old-school cooking, albeit tailored to modern tastes. Rossini tournedos with a port-flavoured gravy, eel in sorrel and poached brill in a shrimp sauce. An establishment that never disappoints, all the more so as you can also pop in for just a drink or a snack.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
16711;Cécile;Belgium;Roosdaal;Brusselstraat 6, Roosdaal, 1760, Belgium;50.8432088;4.0758546;36;false;false;Modern French;A pretty brick edifice in the heart of Pajottenland, wedged in between a church and a beauty parlour. This picture postcard image of Flanders sports a trendy, predominantly black and white interior and natural light. Sisters Judith and Astrid expertly manage the front of house, while chef Tom crafts fine cuisine, such as pheasant cooked whole with a fine champagne sauce. He enjoys jazzing up steak tartare with Asian notes, but is equally at home championing comforting family favourites.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16712;Ciao;Belgium;Brussels;Place Poelaert 6, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8378168;4.3537558;32;false;false;Italian;The 17C stately house on Poelaert Square belongs to TheMerode, a private club. Have no fear, though, everyone is welcome at Ciao. Our favourite in this edifice, oozing in character and elegance, was the dining room with a pretty bar. Authentic Italian flavours are treated to a sensitive modern makeover, illustrated by homemade tortellini with beef marinated in Chianti and a parmesan sauce subtly underscored by Campari. The chef avows a weakness for Tuscan recipes and delicately crafts succulent comfort food. Making your choice from the menu can be something of a challenge!;Terrace;[]
16713;Um Plateau;;Luxembourg;6 Plateau Altmünster, 1123, Luxembourg;49.612576;6.140049;55;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Um Plateau is casual, smart and hip. Start with a glass of wine in the lively bar, before perusing the menu which offers a fine choice of dishes to share. Tataki, ceviche, gnocchi cacio e pepe, crunchy sweetbread… A traditional repertory that whisks you off on a culinary festival spanning the Mediterranean and Asia.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16714;La Maison Lefèvre;Luxembourg;Esch-sur-Alzette;138 boulevard J.F. Kennedy, Esch-sur-Alzette, 4171, Luxembourg;49.49065;5.98052;76;true;false;Modern French;L’élégance de la façade de cette maison de maître se confirme à l’intérieur, avec la splendeur de ses grands lustres. Un vaste établissement où l’on trouve pourtant aussi une belle intimité. Les cuissons traditionnelles se parent de touches de modernité riches en contrastes. Le chef aime travailler les légumes avec créativité, ce qui donne à chaque assiette une touche bien personnelle.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16715;Restaurant Mathes;Luxembourg;Ahn;39 route du Vin, Ahn, 5401, Luxembourg;49.62822;6.4240394;27;false;true;Modern French, Modern Cuisine;Today, the third generation of the family captains this lively restaurant, where the artwork adorning the walls cultivates a refined atmosphere. Try your best to snag a table with a view of the Moselle River, or one on the terrace. Foodies have flocked to Mathes for its classic cuisine since 1949, although it has moved with the times beautifully. The undisputed star of the menu is still the pike perch – oven-baked and finished with a delicate Riesling sauce. With an impressive array of Luxembourg wines on offer, this family restaurant cements its place as a highly-regarded establishment.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16716;Bick Stuff;;Luxembourg;95 rue de Clausen, 1342, Luxembourg;49.6149089;6.1458731;36;true;true;Home Cooking;A family-run establishment where you will instantly feel at home. Bick is a local word which literally means ‘beak’ in English but loosely translates as ‘food’. Owners Virginie and Denis Laissy have the same goal: to serve good food in a relaxed atmosphere. Chef Denis rustles up reassuringly classical recipes, adding his own distinctive touch. We recommend the set menu.;Air conditioning;[]
16717;De Kwizien;Belgium;Hasselt;Jeneverplein, Hasselt, 3500, Belgium;50.9331503;5.340749;37;true;true;Creative French;Food loving Hasselt is delighted to have this newcomer. Luc Bellings’ former right hand man creates cuisine with well - balanced flavours and well - prepared ingredients. The dishes are modern but inspired by tradition.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16718;OiO;;Luxembourg;48 Montée de Clausen, 1343, Luxembourg;49.6131754;6.1434861;48;false;true;Italian, Seasonal Cuisine;The pasta is prepared last minute, stuffed with a powerful ossobuco and then coated in a velvety parmesan and gremolata sauce. All the ingredients on the menu are as fresh as the homemade pasta. This fantastic Mediterranean osteria which boasts an exquisite riverside terrace on the banks of the Alzette, invites you to an Italian feast of great delicacy. Don’t miss the Negroni or the dessert trolley!;Terrace;[]
16719;Un Altro Mondo;Belgium;Wavre;Courte Rue du Rivage 1, Wavre, 1300, Belgium;50.7231189;4.6261744;94;false;true;Italian Contemporary;Quirkily tucked away behind shops, this Altro Mondo acquaints you with the highly personal vision of Luca and Caroline. Italian influences dominate the menu, such as Tagliani in truffles in a powerful gutsy sauce. You can also expect a line-up of more modern dishes that reflect the character of the enthusiastic, charismatic sommelier.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16720;Villared;Belgium;Izegem;Leenstraat 51, Izegem, 8870, Belgium;50.910587;3.1956431;75;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Pink flamingos adorn the wallpaper, green marble abounds and gold and ochre depict the colour scheme. Elegant and fashionable, Villared provides the perfect foil to chef Debal’s eclectic score. Melanzane alla parmigiana, sole meunière, Asian-inspired salmon… The enticing menu by a seasoned craftsman has something for everyone.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16721;Didier Galet;Belgium;Sprimont;rue du Grand Bru 27, Sprimont, 4140, Belgium;50.5232444;5.6577993;82;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Country cooking;Before you even sit down in this friendly joint done up in an inviting vein, you feel perfectly at home. Christine greets diners with a smile and chef Didier Galet waves a hi from the kitchen. Galet is a champion of his region and committed to working with local ingredients. From wood pigeon to fresh veggies, the chef sources everything locally, crafting each ingredient with infinite respect. His cooking draws on his classical training, jazzed up with expressive sauces. He is equally capable of rolling out a rich mushroom and truffle stock, a light frothy espuma of potatoes or a liberal grating of royal truffle. The alfresco terrace is perfect to sample this ode to Belgian produce and producers.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16722;Delys;Belgium;Bodegnée;rue d'Yernawe 3, Bodegnée, 4537, Belgium;50.5888004;5.3144707;79;true;false;Country cooking, Modern Cuisine;Delys is a haven of design depicted by a chic black colour scheme. Intimacy and mystery set the stage, while floor-to-ceiling windows seem to invite the countryside indoors. Be it for a quick lunch or a more leisurely dinner, chef Doucet’s modern approach always hits the spot. He avows a weakness for crisp, legible, contrasting flavours. For example, he may add an exuberant edge to lightly poached Atlantic cod courtesy of lemon zest and a subtly smoky mushroom stock. Doucet leaves his heroic, distinctive stamp on each dish thanks to sensitive nuances.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16723;Bacon;Belgium;Ieper;Zonnebeekseweg 32, Ieper, 8900, Belgium;50.8550061;2.8981302;16;true;false;Farm to table, Seasonal Cuisine;Your host, an enthusiastic disciple of natural and organic wines, used to be a butcher in a former life. In the company of his wife, they have embarked on a new adventure in the shape of a cosy, trendy restaurant. She woos diners with market-fresh cuisine, jazzed up with international seasonings and brimming with flavour in dishes – with or without meat!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16724;Le P'tit Gaby;Belgium;Thisnes;rue de la Croix Blanche 8a, Thisnes, 4280, Belgium;50.6697605;5.0516189;27;true;true;French Contemporary;The bright modern interior of the P’tit Gaby is now located in the heart of the Liege countryside, following a happy change of venue. The hostess’s greeting is as warm as ever, while chef Leruth’s cooking has acquired added creativity. Each dish is faultlessly thought out, meticulously prepared and sometimes inspired by exotic influences.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16725;Un temps pour Soi;Belgium;Villers-le-Bouillet;Thier du Moulin 46, Villers-le-Bouillet, 4530, Belgium;50.5624768;5.2852485;15;false;false;Farm to table;The countryside around Villers-le-Bouillet is ideal for a weekend getaway and what could be better than this elegant stone building and its romantic patio? The seasoned chef rustles up appetising food, sprinkled with crunchy, spicy, incisive and acidic notes. In a word: the epitome of market-fresh, wholesome cooking.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16726;Fleur de Sel;Belgium;Comines;Rue du Fort 36, Comines, 7780, Belgium;50.7666869;3.0031496;97;false;true;Seasonal Cuisine, Country cooking;You will instantly feel at home in this minimalist venture, two steps from the French border and founded by self-taught chefs, Slava and Antoine. The irresistible duo bowls us over - his passion and food-wine pairings and her delicate culinary flair and generous helpings. Slava’s meticulous attention to detail results in balanced dishes that combine fresh, acidic, spicy and many other subtle flavours. The ingredient takes pride of place in each carefully thought-out dish, whether it be asparagus that is enhanced in a ceviche, or lamb fillets underscored by an emulsion of beer and meat juices.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16727;Vonk;Belgium;Kachtem;Kachtemsplein 13, Kachtem, 8870, Belgium;50.9317493;3.1922759;42;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Farm to table;Stijn and chef Bart are the fifth generation of the Hoonaert family, whose DNA is rooted in culinary excellence! The conservatory of the former café, planted with trees, is now a cosy gastrobar. A charcoal Mibrasa oven adds a distinctive flavour to market-fresh recipes, made with meticulously chosen ingredients (simple lunchtime menu, more varied in the evening).;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16728;Cuichine;Belgium;Antwerpen;Draakplaats 3, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.2062069;4.4321857;64;true;true;Chinese;House-made Peking duck with crispy skin, fresh veggies and pancakes ready to be stuffed, all of which flanked by a gutsy sweet and sour hoisin sauce. This signature dish embodies the philosophy of Cuichine: a modern version of old-school Chinese nosh, starring all our favourite Cantonese recipes. The interior of this eye-catching establishment is ideally suited to the trendy vibe and the restaurant also boasts a pleasant terrace.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16729;VAS;Belgium;Beveren;Gentseweg 536, Beveren, 9120, Belgium;51.190788;4.2055149;89;true;false;Creative French, Farm to table;Jolien and Robby have moved shop, but retained their win-win formula. Near the Gentseweg highway, VAS occupies an attractive street corner edifice whose interior sports a range of elegant materials and a tasteful colour scheme. The bubbly front-of-house team sets the scene as you peruse the interesting Franco-Belgian repertory dotted with trendy, spot-on twists. Fillet of duck cooked rare might be flanked by a champagne sauce and a creamy gravy jazzed up with hints of sea buckthorn for added vibrancy together with a velvety purée and a range of textured kohlrabi. VAS is the quintessence of warm and welcoming, enhanced by a festival of familiar family favourites underscored by feelgood flavours.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16730;L'Atelier Cuisine;Belgium;Beaufays;voie de l'Air Pur 207, Beaufays, 4052, Belgium;50.5650497;5.6344128;74;false;false;Contemporary, Mediterranean Cuisine;As you set foot in this striking Art deco edifice reminiscent of the 1930s and make your way over a carpet of flowers, you will immediately feel at home. The new venue of L’Atelier Cuisine is a gem! Homemade fare and fresh produce are the name of the game. The patriotic line-up of French and Italian classics has no secrets for the chef who crafts knockout nosh, sprinkled with Mediterranean influences. A bite of the veal escalope alla Milanese will transport you straight to a sunny Northern Italy.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16731;Resto Wald;Belgium;Rotselaar;Hellichtstraat 1, Rotselaar, 3110, Belgium;50.9572621;4.7035795;43;false;true;Farm to table;Lisa and Walter Wald are keen to maintain the “Small is beautiful” ethic of their hip eatery, which adds to the home-from-home feel. Whenever possible, the enthusiastic chef prepares everything himself using locally sourced ingredients. He draws his inspiration from his many overseas trips and enjoys mixing surprising flavours. He is equally at home with juicy pheasant in a cognac sauce as with a tartare of seabass paired with shellfish oil, vanilla, cucumber extract and goat’s yoghurt and tarragon ice cream. You can expect a flavourful meal with a modern spin in a cosy setting.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16732;Brasserie Juste;Belgium;Dikkelvenne;Nijverheidsstraat 4, Dikkelvenne, 9890, Belgium;50.9180372;3.6900733;26;true;false;Traditional Cuisine, Farm to table;Back-to-basics brasserie cuisine, fresh ingredients and a chef who adds his own personal touch. “Juste” what it takes to satisfy good food lovers. Even better, the chef is a fan of wood fired Josper ovens. Hand chopped beef tartare with crunchy fries, hearty helpings of vol-au-vent and a made-to-order dame blanche with vanilla ice cream and smothered in chocolate sauce: every dish is a model of culinary generosity. A suitably tasteful trendy interior and an alfresco area overlooking the fields and the vegetable garden.;Terrace;[]
16733;Gus;Belgium;Brussels;rue des Cultes 36, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8505633;4.3681182;40;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Belgian;Pierre Baeyens and Jonathan Delhière acquaint you with the “brassonomy” concept (beer meets gastronomy) in their cosy brasserie. They skilfully incorporate the many flavours of artisan beer and hops into a Franco-Belgian line-up, in the glass and also in the subtle food. A foamy beer mousseline nestles up to a soft-poached egg and mushrooms or steak is smoked in hops: the chefs add an individual touch to creative recipes. A bubbling Brussels brasserie-cum-brewery!;;[]
16734;Fou du Goût;Belgium;Lovendegem;Kasteeldreef 63, Lovendegem, 9920, Belgium;51.0949045;3.6094232;15;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Fou du Goût manages to be both chic and cosy, with the beautiful glass conservatory being the best spot in the house. Thomas Cocquyt has a penchant for giving familiar flavours an exotic twist – chicken cooked in a spicy masala sauce, or pan-fried plaice with smoked eel and a beurre blanc infused with a yuzu gel for a burst of citrus brightness. This chef is a master of balancing bold flavours with a touch of intrigue. A perennial favourite in the Meetjesland region!;Terrace;[]
16735;De Mayeur - Patrick Vandecasserie;Belgium;Ruisbroek;Fabriekstraat 339, Ruisbroek, 1601, Belgium;50.7784075;4.2849907;61;false;false;Classic Cuisine;Fancy a good, traditional meal? Patrick Vandecasserie’s villa is right up your street. The chef has no equal when it comes to finding premium produce that he prepares classically. His game recipes are exquisite! Fine establishment.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16736;San Sablon;Belgium;Brussels;rue Joseph Stevens 12, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.841578;4.3523669;29;false;true;Creative;San Sablon features a welcoming natural decor in the smart Sablon district, albeit with a trendy, suave twist. Rather than plates, forks and knives, you will eat out of bowls with spoons – all the better to do justice to original recipes that keep pace with the seasons. The main ingredient is enhanced by gutsy vegetable side dishes that illuminate each meal.;;[]
16737;Cuisinez-Nous;Belgium;Bertrix;rue de la Gare 138, Bertrix, 6880, Belgium;49.8541;5.2659473;95;false;false;Classic French;In this tasteful townhouse, Alain and Céline further confirm their excellent reputation acquired at the Rosa restaurant. Céline caters to diners’ every whim in the dining room, while Alain deploys his talents in a traditional French repertory.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16738;Tafel 10;Belgium;Ruiselede;A. Rodenbachstraat 10, Ruiselede, 8755, Belgium;51.0419283;3.3995216;24;false;true;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;A black and white tiled floor and an open fire set the scene in this plush bourgeois 19C home, but the comfort is entirely 21C, as is the splendid terrace to the rear. The à la carte menu offers a choice of beautifully crafted classics made with first-class ingredients and flanked by powerful sauces, while the set menu is more playful and international in spirit.;Terrace;[]
16739;Roots;Belgium;Gent;Vrouwebroersstraat 5, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0582438;3.7222918;26;false;true;Creative, Modern Cuisine;A hip bistronomic offering in the heart of the buzzy Patershol district. The establishment’s popularity has nothing to do with luck and everything to do with Kim Devisschere’s uninhibited, no-holds barred cooking, doubled with a commitment to organic, locally sourced ingredients. Be it local meat, North Sea fish or fresh vegetables, each dish fascinates and intrigues. Splendid wine list (excellent natural wines) and pleasant alfresco area in fine weather.;Terrace;[]
16740;Rascasse;Belgium;Kapellen;Kalmthoutsesteenweg 121, Kapellen, 2950, Belgium;51.3550767;4.4591006;16;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;Erwin Denijs is a genuine ambassador of his region, the North Sea and Oosterschelde River. This “North Sea Chef” crafts the best seasonal produce into dishes that combine a tangy freshness with a playful element. For example, beurre blanc flanks a skate wing cooked in butter and paired with mussels and a medley of leeks. Caroline, your cheerful hostess, will ply you with wine, as well as beer tips, all of which in a pared-back setting that provides the perfect foil for striking works of art, starring fish!;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16741;Cocotte;Belgium;Lommel;Koning Leopoldlaan 94, Lommel, 3920, Belgium;51.2299897;5.324892;20;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Modern French;Authentic details, such as stained - glass windows, happily rub shoulders with modern furnishings in this hip, lounge - inspired restaurant. The ambience is warm and welcoming and the chef cooks modern, often creative dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16742;Bachtekerke;Belgium;Bachte-Maria-Leerne;Bachtekerkestraat 9, Bachte-Maria-Leerne, 9800, Belgium;50.99902;3.550455;56;false;false;Modern French, Farm to table;Bachtekerke is undeniably smart, but its pride and joy is its fantastic summer terrace on the banks of the Leie, protected by large parasols and enclosed by drift wood fencing – you will almost feel like you are on an island! The chef has no equal for generous cuisine, rich in flavour and variety. A hit with foodies of all sorts.;Terrace;[]
16744;Ploegmans;Belgium;Brussels;rue Haute 148, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8388292;4.3504785;66;false;true;Belgian, Traditional Cuisine;As you enter this former café, you will find yourself immersed in the working class ambience of the Marolles district. Everything from the decor to the menu is steeped in local traditions. Cheese croquettes, steak and chips or vol-au-vent – scrumptious!;;[]
16745;KAN10;Belgium;Kasterlee;Geelsebaan 85a, Kasterlee, 2460, Belgium;51.232654;4.9719867;83;false;true;World Cuisine, Farm to table;“Original”, “captivating”, “adventurous” and “regional” sum up the ethos of this cosy urban eatery. As a result, you can expect to sample a mind-blowing range of flavours and savours. Asian flair depicts the semi-cooked salmon, underscored by excellent homemade sambal and flanked by a traditional beurre noisette… A culinary banquet! Ask the lady of the house to show you the popular menu of shared dishes and get ready to embark on an exciting voyage of international flavours in a casual vibe.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16746;La Bottega;Belgium;Eupen;Gospertstraße 29, Eupen, 4700, Belgium;50.632052;6.03561;25;true;false;Italian;The best Italian restaurant of Eupen is on Gospertstraße. Traditional pizza, succulent lasagne and yummy Gamberoni prawn and pasta. The kitchen team combines generosity and wholehearted authenticity, without forgetting the odd, unorthodox twist. The delicatessen counter is a great success.;Terrace;[]
16747;Céma Passion;Belgium;La Louvière;avenue Gambetta 63, La Louvière, 7100, Belgium;50.4730827;4.1916562;34;false;false;Modern French;The menu features modern French cuisine, which is rich in enthusiasm and sophistication. Seasonal produce takes pride of place on the inventive menu. A genuine culinary experience.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16748;BÚN;Belgium;Antwerpen;Volkstraat 43, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.210647;4.3956871;79;false;true;Vietnamese;Leave the madding crowd far behind and relax in the hip casual vibe of this trendy Vietnamese eatery. You can expect to sample a fine dining version of characteristic Vietnamese sweet and sour, fermented and spicy flavours. The chef favours local organic produce, an ethos that is reflected in the attractive wine list, rich in natural vintages. The Little Bún noodle shop rustles up gutsy, full-bodied Vietnamese street food.;Counter dining;[]
16749;Convento Wijnbistro;Belgium;Leuven;Mechelsestraat 87, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8822611;4.6987531;41;false;true;Farm to table;Pick out a bottle from the wine shop, take a seat in the pleasant bistro-lounge and get ready to soak up the communicative enthusiasm of Convento. The sommeliers get a real kick out of explaining the wines, hence the low corkage fee. The straightforward, market-fresh menu is perfectly matched to the establishment’s stripped-back concept and stars a fine selection of veggies and authentic flavours.;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16750;Het Moment;Belgium;Temse;Parklaan 46, Temse, 9140, Belgium;51.1280301;4.2226541;51;true;false;Modern French;One invariably succumbs to the appeal of the elegant family home of chef Nicolas. Diners can choose between modern and classical dishes, safe in the knowledge that fine produce takes centre stage.;Terrace;[]
16751;L'air des Sens;Belgium;Zoutleeuw;Vincent Betsstraat 12, Zoutleeuw, 3440, Belgium;50.8328662;5.1051736;83;true;false;Farm to table, Creative;Snug, pared-back and arty – the interior of this historic 1900 edifice is equally as fascinating as David Schulz’ fine cuisine. Veggies, herbs and seasonings form the backbone of his cooking. Almost everything is prepared from scratch and many of the recipes star local meat or North Sea seafood. He works hand in hand with the seasons, adding a creative spin, unexpected twists and exciting new techniques. A keen interest in Dutch wines adds the final flourish to this enticing portrait.;;[]
16752;La Gloriette;Belgium;Marche-en-Famenne;rue de Bastogne 18, Marche-en-Famenne, 6900, Belgium;50.219168;5.3485599;39;true;false;Modern French, Seasonal Cuisine;This masterfully revamped townhouse enjoys an authentic, contemporary setting. The chef proposes dishes that suit contemporary taste buds, particularly with creative appetisers. His culinary score is personal, varied, often amusing, but always seeks to enhance the intensity of the flavours.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16753;'t Sleutelgat;Belgium;Lieferinge;Kasseide 78, Lieferinge, 9400, Belgium;50.7886597;4.0525625;97;true;true;Creative French;The daughter Laetitia warmly welcomes guests to this family business, whose terrace overlooks the lush green countryside of the village of Lieferinge. Dad, mijnheer Van Holder, demonstrates his technical precision and eye for detail in dishes served in several plates. From a new spin on traditional flammkuchen to veal jazzed up with a punchy medley of international accents, the food is surprisingly complex and fascinating. Don’t forget to book!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16754;Henri;Belgium;Brussels;rue de Flandre 113, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.852955;4.3450659;65;false;false;Modern French;This laid-back bistro perfectly embodies the hip, urban vibe of Brussels’ Rue de Flandres and we warrant you will fall in love with its casual ambience, cobbled terrace and splendid choice of wines and Brussels’ beers. The dishes are free of frills, all the better to allow the ingredients to take front stage. Mussels in a pastis-flavoured sauce, beef tartare with a Thai slant or text-book perfect sole meunière: the chef enthusiastically navigates between influences with a fondness for fresh Mediterranean fare. Fine dining with a Brussels’ signature!;Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16755;Les Caprices d'Harmony;Belgium;Schaerbeek;rue du Noyer 236, Schaerbeek, 1030, Belgium;50.8475347;4.3924348;97;true;true;Classic Cuisine;If only there were more little neighbourhood hangouts like this one! The owner chef has voluntarily eschewed modes and trends and his traditional menu is music to our ears (and tastebuds): hanger steak with shallots or dame blanche dessert (vanilla ice cream and hot chocolate). Simple, home cooking, prepared to order – at prices that make sense.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16756;Le Passage;Belgium;Uccle;avenue Jean et Pierre Carsoel 17, Uccle, 1180, Belgium;50.7945211;4.3639823;29;true;true;Classic Cuisine;This establishment and its lunchtime set menu are a favourite with the locals, such is chef Rocky Renaud’s reputation for creativity and flair, mingling tradition with modernity. Distinctive food with bold international accents!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16757;Lola;Belgium;Brussels;place du Grand Sablon 33, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8406137;4.354837;57;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, French;The fact that this inviting red and white brasserie has been a firm fixture of the swanky Sablon district since 1994 owes nothing to chance. Whether it’s a quick lunch at the bar or more elaborate fare in the dining room, the service is first class. Classic brasserie fare such as lobster ravioli, an unusual sweetbread vol-au-vent or melt-in-the-mouth Holstein steak and fries, all of which prepared with textbook skill. The chef adds a modern twist, focusing on generosity rather than fussy frills.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16758;L'Écailler du Palais Royal;Belgium;Brussels;rue Bodenbroek 18, Brussels, 1000, Belgium;50.8407674;4.3566461;18;true;false;Seafood;L'Écailler is a Brussels institution. The turquoise tiles behind the long bar, the wonderful woodwork, the gorgeous carpets and the nostalgic charm of this building make for an irresistibly inviting setting. A champion of classic cuisine, the chef excels in preparing fish and seafood dishes, but during the hunting season, his game specialities are also not to be missed. Briny oysters, the aromatic bouillabaisse, his inimitable sole meunière… Fans of traditional fare will feel right at home.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16759;Ferrier 30;Belgium;Antwerpen;Leopold de Waelplaats 30, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2086924;4.392777;43;false;false;Italian;The stylish Ferrier 30 will immerse you in the buzzy, hipster vibe of the Zuid. The terrace opposite the Fine Arts Museum attracts diners like bees to honey in fine weather. The venue is ideally suited to the text-book perfect classical Italian recipes. Truffle-flavoured home-made pasta, slowly braised ossobuco… An explosion of Italian aromas and flavours!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16760;Baarle 90;Belgium;Sint-Martens-Latem;Baarle Frankrijkstraat 90, Sint-Martens-Latem, 9830, Belgium;51.0351263;3.6193824;19;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A meal at Baarle 90, which boasts an idyllic view of the River Leie, is the opportunity for a fine dining experience. The terrace is out of this world and the interior pleasantly trendy. European recipes tinged with Belgian influences, such as shrimp fritters, steak tartare and sole prepared with textbook expertise.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16761;De Fakkels;Belgium;Sint-Truiden;Hasseltsesteenweg 61, Sint-Truiden, 3800, Belgium;50.8278933;5.2008685;89;false;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;Seppe Bleus and Liese Bams have taken over the business and welcome you to De Fakkels 2.0. They have kept its soul intact, so the imposing building still exudes warmth and a sense of romance. Goose feather lampshades, designer lighting and wooden ornaments make for a unique setting. In a bid to keep up with the times, the menu features exciting new combinations, such as the bright and zesty interplay of calamansi and orange with ultra-fresh scallops. The depth of his sauces, like the rich game sauce that graces the venison fillet, is testament to the chef's culinary mastery. This long-established haven for foodies is in good hands.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16762;Den Silveren Harynck;Belgium;Sint-Niklaas;Grote Baan 51, Sint-Niklaas, 9100, Belgium;51.1835251;4.1984189;57;false;true;Classic Cuisine;A mother and son team (Els and Sam) welcome guests into the stylishly elegant Van Landeghem family establishment. Floor to ceiling windows lead into the garden which is flanked by a patio. Dad, Luc, can be found rustling up tasty, flavourful delicacies in the kitchen, combining classical training and creative touches, ranging from Rossini tournedos steak to a bouillabaisse jazzed up with subtle, Asian notes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16763;Royal H.-Bonhomme;Belgium;Remouchamps;rue de la Reffe 26, Remouchamps, 4920, Belgium;50.4798462;5.71121;57;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This comforting inn is emblematic of the Ardennes countryside and of its history. Eight generations of Daussaint innkeepers have been at its helm since 1768! A wrought-iron pergola provides the romantic setting for a dinner for two featuring classical French fare: fried trout, lobster from the lobster tank, tournedos of venison… Delicious!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16764;Bistro Tribunal;Belgium;Leuven;Vaartstraat 9, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8807997;4.7021501;70;false;true;Meats and Grills, Classic Cuisine;Have you ever heard of a meat sommelier? Well, in this traditional bistro, one such will help you make your choice among the fine cuts of meat supplied by the prestigious Rondou butchers. A refrigerated meat display counter and a lobster tank catch the eye. Rather than prissy, complex preparations, you can expect spot-on cooking, freshly prepared sauces and regular refills of hot, crunchy French fries. The wine list (splendid selection of Bordeaux wines) is at bargain prices.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16765;Zarza;Belgium;Leuven;Bondgenotenlaan 92, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8803957;4.7103541;20;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Zarza, an authentic cosy bolthole with a pretty town garden, is the type of place that inspires loyalty. Chef Cordemans pampers his diners with flawlessly sourced ingredients. The patriotic line-up of Belgian fare is jazzed up by the occasional dash of creativity, illustrated by masterfully cooked langoustine, paired with a gutsy shellfish jus and crunchy courgettes. Sophisticated yet full-bodied flavours. The lunchtime menus are always a safe bet!;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16766;La Bru'sserie;Belgium;Durbuy;rue du Comte Théodule d'Ursel 14, Durbuy, 6940, Belgium;50.3519047;5.4551002;52;true;false;World Cuisine;In this trendy joint, Wout Bru takes your taste buds on a whirlwind trip around the world. The extensive menu features dishes from Provence, Asia and Latin America without forgetting Belgium. The mouth - watering choice fully lives up to its promise of intense and subtle savours!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16767;Kokovin;Belgium;Sint-Niklaas;Heidebaan 46, Sint-Niklaas, 9100, Belgium;51.1687259;4.1772966;78;false;false;Farm to table, Classic Cuisine;Warm and stylish, Kokovin boasts a superb garden patio, but above all, it is the scene of a successful family adventure. The cheerful lady of the house, Peggy, greets guests warmly, plying them with insightful wine tips along the way, while her hubbie, Dominique, and son, Francis, conjure up recipes that range from modern to classical. In addition to textbook prepared sole, you may sample generous shrimp fritters that melt in the mouth and duckling served with piping hot fries, together with a host of more unusual textures. Consider us smitten!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16768;Bistronoom;Belgium;Wortegem;Waregemseweg 155, Wortegem, 9790, Belgium;50.8697278;3.464727;37;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;Bistronoom is an elegant Normandy-inspired villa in the heart of the Flemish Ardennes. The appetising repertory draws on the best of French and Flemish traditions. The menu is deliciously familiar, the flavours are wholehearted and recognisable and the produce is seasonal. Examples include crispy sweetbread in a creamy cognac sauce with chives and fresh fries, unless you wouldn’t prefer a sole meunière or a gutsy osso bucco that explodes with flavour. The extensive menu is just one of the reasons that Bistronoom has earned itself such a loyal crowd of regulars.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16769;Lesco;Belgium;Wetteren;Stationsstraat 50, Wetteren, 9230, Belgium;51.0026797;3.8835057;51;false;true;Creative;The authentic décor of this handsome town house is perfectly paired with modern comforts. Wooden floors, elegant mirrors and a trendy vibe. The lovely terrace in the garden is equally enchanting. The surprise menu reflects the creative talents and playful streak of the chefs.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16770;Wilford T;Belgium;Temse;Wilfordkaai 10, Temse, 9140, Belgium;51.1233984;4.2150352;44;false;true;Modern French;The industrial sobriety of Wilford T contrasts with the works of art in the Wilford X exhibition gallery next-door. Meals are served in this arty establishment steeped in serenity, which provides the perfect foil to the exceptionally pure flavours. Chef Vermeiren, who doesn’t hesitate to add the finishing touch right in front of diners, is committed to highlighting the ingredient with unusual combinations. Sometimes complex, always flavoursome.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16771;Auberge de la Roseraie;Belgium;Ohain;route de la Marache 4, Ohain, 1380, Belgium;50.6942012;4.4689713;67;true;false;French, Traditional Cuisine;The inhabitants of well-heeled Ohain have adopted this 19C farmstead that is a bastion of French cooking served in a relaxed atmosphere. Rather than surprises, you can expect to sample deftly executed recipes by a chef who combines his deep-seated understanding of ingredients with subtle sauces. An example: juicy quail with a crispy skin, lightly seared veal sweetbread and a honey-flavoured jus. Nostalgic flavours of yesteryear!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16772;Dôme Sur Mer;Belgium;Antwerpen;Arendstraat 1, Antwerpen, 2018, Belgium;51.2063736;4.4266236;59;false;false;Seafood;You are well and truly in the Art nouveau district of Zurenborg, even if this fish bistro would be quite at home in a seaside resort. The produce is outstandingly fresh, embodied by seafood platters overflowing in briny odours, delicately flavoured langoustines, cooked to perfection on a teppanyaki or sautéed fillets of seabass garnished with a gutsy olive oil sauce… In their open-plan kitchen, the chefs demonstrate that such delicacies have no need of prissy details, courtesy of spot-on cooking and ultra fresh side dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16773;Bouffard;Belgium;Mol;Adolf Reydamslaan 24, Mol, 2400, Belgium;51.1888542;5.1146991;91;true;true;Modern French;Bouffard has two different dining spaces to suit different moods: a snug lounge area at the front and a more vibrant room adorned with colourful artworks. Thomas Dockx is very selective when it comes to his ingredients, and he takes a less-is-more approach to preparing them. Eschewing any unnecessary frills, he allows the natural flavours to shine through with the help of robust sauces. In one of his exuberant dishes, he combines golden-brown pan-fried scallops, tender pork cheek and a creamed cheek broth. This chef understands how to create a well-rounded set menu that keeps you engaged from beginning to end!;Terrace;[]
16774;Chez Duche;Belgium;Charleroi;avenue de Waterloo 5, Charleroi, 6000, Belgium;50.4144803;4.4475288;37;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;You can expect unadorned dishes that throb with flavour in what is the epitome of a neighbourhood eatery: rib of horse meat with house-made fries, lavishly served cassoulet, piled high with duck confit and Toulouse sausage or a waterzooi of seasonal veggies. A patriotic pageant of French and Belgian classics prepared and served with textbook precision and generosity. Chez Duche has been feeding us well since 1993!;;[]
16775;Het Nieuwe Palinghuis;Belgium;Antwerpen;Sint-Jansvliet 14, Antwerpen, 2000, Belgium;51.2183398;4.3965319;77;false;false;Seafood;There is an authentic feel to the dining area of this charming seafood restaurant. Adorned with various nostalgic photos of maritime scenes, it harks back to its opening year: 1983! Over the years, Het Nieuwe Palinghuis has earned a reputation for its classic fish dishes. The menu features langoustine with an intense nantua sauce, sole Véronique in a full-bodied white wine sauce, as well as a distinctively herby eel in green sauce. The dishes here have always been big on flavour, steering clear of any unnecessary frills. A firm favourite!;Air conditioning;[]
16776;Le Mystique;Belgium;Brugge;Niklaas Desparsstraat 11, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2099713;3.2238267;45;false;true;Modern French;If you’re looking for a romantic getaway venue in the picture postcard perfect city of Bruges, book a table in the restaurant of the Relais & Chateaux Heritage Hotel, whose opulent interior oozes authentic historic details. It is truly the epitome of stylish elegance! The chef avows a preference for French and Mediterranean ingredients, which he delicately crafts into spot-on dishes. Examples include a marinated fillet of mullet paired with sweet-sour fennel, labneh and radish pickles. Each dish is a master class of subtlety and originality. A date night kinda place with which you will immediately fall head over heels.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16777;Sophie et Nicolas;Belgium;Comblain-la-Tour;route de Fairon 79, Comblain-la-Tour, 4180, Belgium;50.4554414;5.5655362;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Farm to table;Sophie Gigot and Nicolas Septon have entirely refurbished their characterful establishment. The infectious friendly vibe is intact, thanks in particular to the lovely patio in the greenhouse. Chef Nicolas crafts dishes in tune with nature that respect both the seasons and his region, through subtle, creative recipes.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16778;Bistro R;Belgium;Nossegem;Leuvensesteenweg 614, Nossegem, 1930, Belgium;50.8776326;4.5051868;32;true;true;Modern French, Farm to table;Roland Debuyst is inspired by top-quality Belgian produce, but also by his globetrotting background. He focuses on bistro fare with a hint of modernity. Gyosa and ceviche are naturally combined with a dish of game, such as wild boar. This seasoned chef cannot be faulted when it comes to intelligently marrying flavours. The contemporary interior adorned with handsome works of art adds the final flourish to this enticing portrait.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16779;Bütgenbacher Hof;Belgium;Bütgenbach;Marktplatz 8, Bütgenbach, 4750, Belgium;50.42632;6.20544;64;false;false;Modern French;The second generation has further enhanced the already well-established reputation of this family-run establishment. Take your pick from a range of gourmet menus that shine the spotlight on producers from eastern Belgium. The accent is on flavoursome bistro cuisine in tune with the times, washed down with a tipple from the well-stocked wine bin. The guestrooms are equipped with all the mod cons.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16780;Le 1460;Belgium;Virginal-Samme;rue du Moulin à Vent 10, Virginal-Samme, 1460, Belgium;50.6423348;4.2101844;52;true;true;Farm to table;Just sit back and enjoy the good life in this relaxed eatery! The varied menu overflows in comforting dishes, albeit in the zeitgeist, although the chef is definitely not one for gimmicks. A fine fillet of fish with buttery mashed potatoes or game in a powerful sauce, followed by a light, airy chocolate mousse – feelgood food before all else. This former bank (the wine cellar is in the old vaults) will awaken your tastebuds!;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16781;'t Vijfde Seizoen;Belgium;Aalter;Stationsstraat 9, Aalter, 9880, Belgium;51.0846456;3.4484142;85;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Broes Tavernier hails his suppliers as “heroes”, which speaks volumes for his commitment to locally sourced produce. From asparagus and fish from the North Sea to partridges, he unfailingly selects the best. His creative, high-flying approach to cooking aims to let the ingredients shout their name. We recommend the insightful wine-food pairing suggestions. After a fine meal in this friendly establishment (great patio), pop into Eetalage and take a few goodies home.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16782;Les Eleveurs;Belgium;Halle;Suikerkaai 1a, Halle, 1500, Belgium;50.732199;4.237608;72;true;true;Classic Cuisine, Regional Cuisine;Les Eleveurs hotel restaurant, a landmark of Halle since 1897, has been run by the De Brouwer family since its foundation. Today, Annelies and Julian are breathing new life into their family heritage. Chef Borsy is in charge of the highly popular culinary score, adding his own personal touch while remaining true to Pajottenland specialties. The extensive menu ranges from family favourites such as chicory au gratin and lamb wellington to more modern fare like a vegetarian risotto of asparagus and celeriac. Go there your eyes closed – you won’t be disappointed.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16783;Calla's;Belgium;Aalter;Stationsstraat 250, Aalter, 9880, Belgium;51.0914656;3.4467045;24;true;true;Seasonal Cuisine;Calla’s immerses you in an enchanting Art deco ambience. In the heart of Aalter, this former solicitor’s home (1930) flanked by a delightful garden, is the epitome of cosy. The dishes to share bear witness to Niels Landtsheer’s creative streak, illustrated by sucrine salad leaf stuffed with subtly spiced North Sea crab and briny seaweed. Niels’ classical background comes to the forefront in recipes such as his rich vol-au-vent. Gutsy, big-boned flavours are the hallmark of this talented craftsman.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16784;Atelier Maple;Belgium;Borgerhout;Karel De Preterlei 210, Borgerhout, 2140, Belgium;51.2005996;4.4500592;64;false;true;Creative, Farm to table;Authentic details, such as a stunning glazed dome, and a plush, yet cosy ambience depict this stylish Art nouveau edifice. Chef Tynes crafts cosmopolitan fare, adding his own spin to pedigree French dishes, thanks in particular to Asian and Indonesian influences. Splendid terrace.;Terrace;[]
16785;Amen;Belgium;Ixelles;rue Franz Merjay 165, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8169839;4.3519148;40;true;true;Farm to table;Two-star chef Pascal Devalkeneer (Le Chalet de la Forêt) has a knack for picking the best produce. From the contemporary dishes and intense flavours to the range of textures, his dishes are masterpieces of culinary art. Amen!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16786;De Vijf Seizoenen;Belgium;Nederbrakel;Kasteelstraat 5, Nederbrakel, 9660, Belgium;50.8023891;3.7633966;56;true;false;Modern French;Vegetables fresh from the fields, herbs picked in the Flemish Ardennes and environmentally sustainable seafood… Authenticity, sustainability and quality are the backbone of this classy, family-run restaurant, depicted by elegant Art deco light fixtures. The creative associations of ingredients and care lavished on the vegetables are truly fascinating. An unconventional new take on asparagus pleasantly surprises, underscored by an incredible concoction of eggs and exciting fermented flavours. A fine tribute to the seasons!;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16787;Savoury;Belgium;Turnhout;Steenweg op Antwerpen 106, Turnhout, 2300, Belgium;51.3183711;4.9128104;58;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This spruce detached house does sport a faintly English hallmark, the menu, however, unveils a patriotic line-up of classical French cuisine. Kick off your meal with an aperitif in the wine cellar before taking a seat in the modern dining room or on the leafy patio. Subtle classicism depicts the textbook precision cooking, albeit with an occasional Mediterranean twang and a refreshing sprinkling of modernity. Pop into the delicatessen before you leave and take a few delicacies home.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16788;Odette en Ville;Belgium;Ixelles;rue du Châtelain 25, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8259223;4.362749;15;false;false;Modern French;Odette is a well-known eatery of the trendy Châtelain neighbourhood. The stylish 1920’s townhouse aims to combine British style, Parisian sensuality and New York glamour. The highly varied menu is equally fascinating: both classical and international, with an accent on the ingredient. Crunchy nems in a spicy sauce, al dente taglioni in lemon with pink shrimps, scallops and foie gras in a duck stock: a festival for fine food lovers. And why not treat yourself to one of the swish designer-inspired guestrooms to finish your evening in the lap of luxury?;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16789;Le Mucha;Belgium;Woluwe-Saint-Pierre;avenue Jules Du Jardin 23, Woluwe-Saint-Pierre, 1150, Belgium;50.8310782;4.4541659;85;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Belgian;The interior and character of Le Mucha are reminiscent of Parisian brasseries in the 1900s, providing the perfect foil to sample traditional French fare. A host of subtle details such as last-minute fresh fries or an unusual béarnaise sauce with steak bears witness to the ethos of this restaurant whose DNA is firmly characterised by lashings of generosity. A must should you get a hankering for nostalgic nosh, such as veal’s brains or an île flottante (meringue floating on velvety egg custard) – even better if you go on one of the jazz nights…;Terrace;[]
16790;Floris;Belgium;Sint-Andries;Gistelsesteenweg 520, Sint-Andries, 8200, Belgium;51.1973467;3.1815878;46;false;true;Modern French;As pleasing to the eye as to the palate! Wood and iron prevail in the decor, while the regional cuisine displays a blend of talent and creative flair.;Terrace;[]
16791;Jacqueline;Belgium;Boechout;Van Colenstraat 8, Boechout, 2530, Belgium;51.1595162;4.4914261;94;false;true;Farm to table;This former butchery is named after the grandmother of Evelien Swiers, who is in charge of the kitchen you can see behind the original counter. Good humoured Raf supervises the dining room, which sports a gentrified workshop vibe. Evelien’s delicious, no-frills cuisine revolves around a menu of four or five dishes. Guinea fowl from Maison Garat is cooked in a frying pan and underscored by a knockout jus enriched in miso, while chicory adds a fresh note with a mandarin sabayon. At Jacqueline, the food is rustic, gutsy and wholesome.;Terrace;[]
16792;Lijsterbes;Belgium;Donk;Donklaan 155, Donk, 9290, Belgium;51.0433029;3.9836151;17;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Chef Van Der Bruggen combines creativity with classical training, as his spit-roast veal sweetbread or his seabass in a salt crust demonstrate. High precision cooking that allows the top-notch ingredients to shout their name. The set and lunch menus remain a hit with his faithful regulars, who make a beeline for the lovely terrace. A solid bet every time!;Car park,Terrace;[]
16793;Les Caves d'Alex;Belgium;Ixelles;Rue Eugène Cattoir 14, Ixelles, 1050, Belgium;50.8208236;4.3870478;75;false;false;French;Alex and Hugues share a passion for first-class produce. The former has a weakness for cured meats, while the enthusiastic sommelier delights in unearthing great wines to pair with your meal. Chef Alex, a fan of textbook French cuisine, pays tribute to tradition through rich recipes and knockout sauces, such as Ostend-style sole or a subtle Nantua sauce that enhances his pike quenelles. Wine vats and paraphernalia set the scene indoors, while the romantic garden provides the perfect foil for a fine dining experience in summertime.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
16794;The Thrill;Belgium;Genk;Jaarbeurslaan 4, Genk, 3600, Belgium;50.9644092;5.485052;100;true;true;Grills, Meats and Grills;Hunting trophies on the walls, sheepskins on the chairs and a huge fireplace-grill in the centre: the rustic stage is set for the friendly, buzzy Thrill in Genk. The extensive menu will make your tastebuds drool, all the more so as you can be safe in the knowledge that Rik Vandersanden is a high-flying craftsman. His ravioli of woodpigeon or his chuck Black Angus, masterfully grilled to rare on the BBQ, demonstrate his talent and generosity. Heaven for lovers of authentic, down to earth flavours.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16795;Zappaz;Belgium;Leuven;Schipvaartstraat 22, Leuven, 3000, Belgium;50.8863755;4.7058159;34;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Zappaz, noted for its friendly vibe, is living proof that fine dining doesn’t have to be starched and stuffy. The several-course menu is an ode to punchy sauces, featuring a playful approach to vegetables, jazzed up with subtle globetrotting influences. Fascinating flavours add whoomph to each dish – a gourmet pageant of ingredients!;;[]
16796;Brugmann;Belgium;Forest;avenue Brugmann 52, Forest, 1190, Belgium;50.8200241;4.3521426;57;true;true;Modern Cuisine;If you fancy a slap-up meal in southwest Brussels, make a beeline for this fancy brasserie adorned with modern art and boasting a lovely alfresco space at the rear. Brugmann offers an extensive choice of pedigree Gallic dishes at lunchtime and in the evening. Traditional recipes are treated to modern, particularly Asian, interpretations, such as langoustine in a tempura of crunchy walnuts with a sweet and sour bisque sauce.;Terrace,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16797;Caillou;Belgium;Heist;Knokkestraat 282, Heist, 8301, Belgium;51.3391741;3.2545038;41;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Creative;Caillou is a hip, modern bistro, strewn with passing nods to ‘pebbles’ (its namesake). The kitchen team prepares the food on a central table that sets the scene for their culinary show. The performance continues in the plate, with an appetising blend of flavours and textures and enticing veggie dishes. The chef doesn’t hesitate to spice up traditional recipes, flanking lobster and turbot, for example, with deftly crafted side dishes such as asparagus flan, a gutsy lobster béarnaise and a poivrade of fried artichokes. The sommelier may suggest an elegant mineral wine, echoing the establishment’s name, to pair with your food.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16798;Le Monde est Petit;Belgium;Etterbeek;rue des Bataves 65, Etterbeek, 1040, Belgium;50.8377025;4.4041562;73;false;false;Creative French;This stylish and intimate restaurant enjoys a pleasant location between Montgomery and Cinquantenaire Park. The market determines what's on the menu here. Chef Loïc Villers incorporates delicious produce into well-thought-out dishes that are as international as his diners. Think quail ballotines stuffed with a delicate farce containing pistachio, a parsnip cream, grapes and juices from the meat. This cuisine is all about pleasure and celebrates the genuine flavours of the ingredients.;Terrace;[]
16799;Plassendale;Belgium;Oostende;Oudenburgsesteenweg 123, Oostende, 8400, Belgium;51.2102905;3.0032998;82;false;true;Classic Cuisine;Royal shrimp fritters with fried parsley and lemon or skate that slips off the bone with a fresh silky butter and caper sauce and creamy mashed potato: such are a few of the patriotic line-up of recipes that have ensured the success of the Plassendale for aeons. Exquisitely located by a lock, it is heaven for fans of traditional nosh in a casual vibe. Unbeatable value for money.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16800;La Brouette;Belgium;Anderlecht;boulevard Prince de Liège 61, Anderlecht, 1070, Belgium;50.8418723;4.3028248;28;false;false;French;Herman Dedapper welcomes you with open arms to his neighbourhood restaurant, decorated in warm colours and adorned with his own photo work. He is an excellent sommelier and loves to share his passion for wine. The chef’s generous, French - inspired dishes are sourced from high - quality produce.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16801;Notarishuys;Belgium;Diksmuide;Koning Albertstraat 39, Diksmuide, 8600, Belgium;51.0305559;2.8640112;68;true;false;Farm to table, Modern Cuisine;This former solicitor’s house is ideally located to explore the Westhoek region. You will stay in comfortable rooms, eat in a romantic restaurant and admire the venerable copper beech tree from the pretty patio in the garden. Chef Boussemaere blends tradition and modernity, turning out dishes whose rich familiar flavours are also a masterclass in culinary subtlety.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16802;Kwizien;Belgium;Maldegem;Brugse Steenweg 200, Maldegem, 9990, Belgium;51.2071243;3.4127447;62;true;false;Country cooking, Seasonal Cuisine;The ingredient plays the star role in this welcoming farmstead. Thomas Coppejans scours the region for produce such as Malines chicken and asparagus, which are often on the menu. He also crafts a ceviche of seabass that will doubtless find favour with younger foodies. Ellen and her team will ply you with insightful tips to help you make your choice between the à la carte, dishes to share and the set menus. Sit back and soak up the infectiously bubbly vibe.;Car park,Terrace;[]
16803;Vlass;Belgium;Middelkerke;Leopoldlaan 246, Middelkerke, 8430, Belgium;51.1839087;2.8062955;73;false;true;Creative;The Lauwereins family bends over backwards to pamper you in its swish, yet cosy restaurant. Creative chefs Stefaan and Elien deploy state-of-the-art techniques to devise dishes in which every detail is endlessly pondered and puzzled over. The result is unabashedly bold and modern. Take, for example, the crunchy vermicelli of pleurote mushrooms in an earthy truffle cream which is paired with a refreshingly punchy black garlic and spinach puree. Wine waiter Kenzo’s inspired suggestions may surprise but his expertise and insight invariably guide him to suggest the perfect wine-food pairing for each dish and each diner.;Air conditioning;[]
16804;De Normandie;Belgium;Koksijde;Koninklijke Baan 1, Koksijde, 8670, Belgium;51.1241909;2.6579112;40;false;true;Farm to table;It may look like a ship washed up on the dunes, but don’t be mistaken: this 1936 boat-shaped edifice is home to a well-oiled, contemporary brasserie. Super fresh seafood takes pride of place with lobster dishes playing the leading role! Generous, legible fare with a strong French bias, although the chef has no qualms about adding a new spin to classical recipes.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16805;Hostellerie du Grünewald;;Luxembourg;10 route d'Echternach, 1453, Luxembourg;49.6333382;6.1384305;74;false;true;Modern French;Fresh, healthy food, but also deliciously generous. This very pleasant bistro with a fine terrace provides an opportunity to sample simple ingredients devoid of unnecessary frills. Save room for the scrumptious desserts. Elegant guestrooms ensure sweet dreams.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16806;L'Horizon;Belgium;Chaumont-Gistoux;rue du Moulin 50, Chaumont-Gistoux, 1325, Belgium;50.6907755;4.672611;80;true;false;Creative;L'Horizon is definitely in tune with the zeitgeist. A fashionable interior and meticulously laid tables set the scene. The chef’s Italian roots, Asian influences and regional produce, such as poultry and herbs, are combined in dishes that cater to modern tastes. Delicate, well-prepared cuisine, fully worthy of a visit.;Car park;[]
16807;Lizanna;Belgium;Beerzel;Hoogstraat 72a, Beerzel, 2580, Belgium;51.0587388;4.6646052;49;true;true;Modern French;Their respective grandmothers, Liza and Anna, bequeathed their love of cooking to chef Levy and to the lady of the house, Stéphanie. The couple shares their passion with guests in this elegant restaurant flanked by a delightful terrace. The chef rolls out his consummate craftsmanship in classical dishes: turbot à la meunière, melt-in-the-mouth endives, intelligently seasoned beurre blanc and a subtle Robuchon puree. The pinnacle of fine French dining.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16808;Elders;Belgium;Gent;Edmond Van Beverenplein 16, Gent, 9000, Belgium;51.0728171;3.7093617;37;false;false;Organic;Urban and exciting, Elders is just the ticket if you fancy sampling modern cuisine in which veggies play the star roles. Tom Pauwelyn reverently respects the seasons, inventing inspired recipes. For example, he exalts cauliflower by preparing it in several ways, including one with an exquisitely subtle Nantua (creamy crayfish) sauce or he celebrates pears with a sabayon of stout beer. Each meal is a treasure trove of discoveries.;Terrace;[]
16809;L'aperovino;Belgium;Brugge;Academiestraat 2F, Brugge, 8000, Belgium;51.2111868;3.2243966;31;true;true;French;“Wine, dine and unwind” is the motto of this stylish upmarket bistro. Upstairs is the wine bar where sommelière Julie unveils a knockout selection of prestigious tipples and a fine choice of cocktails. Downstairs, you will sample dishes poised between tradition and exotic innovation, ranging from a winter venison stew to Sebastes fish served with a refreshing tom kha kai. “Where wining meets dining” is their other baseline…;;[]
16810;Brasserie Nieuwpoort;Belgium;Nieuwpoort;Marktplein 19, Nieuwpoort, 8620, Belgium;51.1297528;2.7520468;35;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This is light years from your run-of-the-mill seaside brasserie! The opulent décor will bowl you over, as will the mixologist who rustles up intriguing cocktails behind the bar. Each dish overflows with generosity and is crafted by gifted, veteran chefs who work with the best ingredients. A range of dishes to share and wholesome brasserie fare. Why not start with a fresh, spicy, acidic ceviche of seabass, before pursuing with a royal vol-au-vent served with piping hot crunchy French fries? THE landmark brasserie of Nieuwpoort!;Terrace;[]
16811;L'adresse;Belgium;Bastogne;Marvie 86, Bastogne, 6600, Belgium;49.9887036;5.7446552;35;true;false;Modern Cuisine;A colourful, designer establishment that serves a single set menu in a bid to guarantee optimum freshness. The focus on quality can be tasted with each bite. Don’t expect fussy frills or superfluous extras – the chef is determined to allow the ingredient to shout its name in each recipe. Immaculately cooked rockfish in a herby chorizo crust and a delicate cream of sea buckthorn berries, paired with a savoury piperade and a velvety fish stock and saffron sauce. A minimalist, stripped-back approach to cooking, particularly in the deftly crafted 100% vegetarian menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16813;Bachten De Leie;Belgium;Zulte;Staatsbaan 280, Zulte, 9870, Belgium;50.9098418;3.4236504;33;false;true;Meats and Grills, Classic Cuisine;Burnished copper saucepans and a striking colour scheme set the stylish scene in this welcoming restaurant. The youthful chef, Louis Wauters, is a butcher’s son and proud of it. You will sample perfectly cooked rib of beef with a silky béarnaise sauce and French fries, but the chef is also keen to pamper fish and seafood amateurs. Flavour and generosity are the watchwords here.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
16814;Bruun;Belgium;Destelbergen;Dendermondesteenweg 532, Destelbergen, 9070, Belgium;51.0579153;3.8386052;67;true;true;Farm to table, French Contemporary;The food of brothers Ruben and Pieter is as elegant as their restaurant and the entirely open-plan kitchen cannot fail but catch the eye. One is inevitably spellbound by the brothers’ seamlessly smooth craftsmanship, as they conjure up dishes free of fussy frills, in keeping with their vision of polished French fare. The focus is on intense gutsy sauces and subtly balanced minimalist flavours.;;[]
16815;L'Episode;Belgium;Saint-Médard;Rue de Waillimont 2, Saint-Médard, 6887, Belgium;49.8169669;5.3443913;26;false;true;Modern French;The Waillimont Estate pays a fitting tribute to the Ardennes countryside and its riverside lodges set an idyllic scene for a getaway destination. The main building is home to a luxurious inn whose snug bar, wood-burning fire, marble floors and timber ceilings would be perfectly at home in an upmarket ski resort. The region takes pride of place in chef Jordan Boreux’ subtle blend of creative and traditional cuisine (knockout sauces!). Some of the textures and personal interpretations may surprise, but familiar Ardennes flavours remain a firm fixture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16816;Loxalis;Luxembourg;Dudelange;150 Rue de la Libération, Dudelange, 3511, Luxembourg;49.4720858;6.082858;91;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Immense floor-to-ceiling windows command a splendid view of the surrounding countryside, with the bonus of a peaceful terrace (weather permitting): the scene of Loxalis is set. Diners are greeted by a genuine maitre d’, who carefully takes the time to explain the appetising menu. Chef Boccolini subtly adds a modern spin to characteristic Mediterranean recipes, such as his new take on vitello tonnato flanked by a characterful sauce. Familiar flavours abound but with intriguing new dimensions. The lunchtime menu is a best-seller!;Terrace;[]
16817;Caudalie;Belgium;Liège;Rue Saint-Jean-en-Isle 6, Liège, 4000, Belgium;50.6421904;5.5686656;55;false;false;French Contemporary;Caudalie, a pared-back fine dining establishment, is perfectly at home in the hip Le Carré neighbourhood of Liège. Chef Simon and Manon, in charge of the front-of-house, share a passion for outstanding ingredients and wine. His technical virtuosity and attention to detail shine through as much in the craftsmanship as in the plating. For example, he might add a characterful Thai stock, sesame oil and a combination of onion and mushroom textures to flawlessly fresh rainbow trout. We recommend the monthly changing menu that hits the spot every time, to the delight of its many regulars.;Air conditioning;[]
16818;Parfums de cuisine;Belgium;Namur;rue du Bailly 10, Namur, 5000, Belgium;50.4625467;4.8663084;34;true;true;French;The aromas wafting tantalisingly out of Vincenzo Romeo’s open kitchen are quite the opposite of fortuitous. This cosy eatery tucked away in the heart of Namur serves a Gallic line-up of heirloom dishes crafted with virtuoso know-how. Crunchy filo pastry stuffed with frog’s legs is paired with a subtle green vegetable soup, depicted by a distinctive acidic note. The concise but exceedingly well-curated wine list ensures that you will be able to find just the right tipple to pair with this traditional pageant of French classical nosh.;;[]
16820;La Scarpetta;Belgium;Waterloo;Chaussée de Bruxelles 178, Waterloo, 1410, Belgium;50.7206218;4.3976593;68;false;false;Italian;We warrant that you will fall head over heels when you set foot in this pleasant restaurant. Comfort, a warm welcome and generous portions – what’s not to like? Authentic Italian recipes, mainly from Marche, come to life in familiar dishes oozing with flavour. The chef might enhance fresh al dente calamarata pasta with salsiccia and a parmesan and truffle sauce. A banquet of Italian fare! The restaurant has rapidly become a favourite with the locals – booking highly recommended.;Terrace;[]
16821;Outro by Vito;South Korea;Busan;18 Millakbondong-ro 19 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48087, South Korea;35.15835;129.12786;60;true;true;European;With the new name Outro by Vito, the restaurant relocated from a location in the Haeridan-gil area to this spot near Gwangalli Beach. Not only did this fine purveyor of natural wine and cuisine change its name, but it also revamped its exterior and décor with a touch of contemporary elegance. Regardless, its pasta dishes, the quintessential offerings, have remained the same – only with enhanced flavors. The diner’s housemade pasta now features higher flour content and undergoes fermentation. The glutinous texture and impeccable pairing with the sauce make the pasta even more appetizing. In addition to a diverse array of pasta dishes, the menu features salads, meat, and various other scrumptious dishes. Come on down and savor your meal with a chef-recommended natural wine replete with a cultured vibe.;Air conditioning;[]
16822;Osteria Aboo;South Korea;Busan;58 Dongcheon-ro, Busanjin-gu, Busan, 47297, South Korea;35.15394;129.06253;45;false;true;Italian;As its sign suggests, Osteria Aboo in Jeonpo-dong oddly labels itself a Western gastropub. Since 2017, this establishment has strived to offer authentic Southern Italian cuisine, a cuisine characterized by ample use of seafood-based ingredients. Among all the exquisite items on the menu, we are partial to the bisque pasta, featuring al dente noodles and a sumptuous amount of fresh and savory red-banded lobster, as well as the newly added Mare (“sea”) course. When paired with a chef-recommended wine, the cuisine will astonish you with the rich flavors of Italy.;Air conditioning;[]
16823;Eutteum Iroribata;South Korea;Busan;20 Suyeong-ro 408 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48308, South Korea;35.1373479;129.0292733;90;true;false;Japanese;Located near Namcheon station, this Japanese diner specializes in omakase dining prepared using irori (traditional Japanese hearth). Though not as authentic as the ones in old Japanese houses, the irori here is faithful to its role as kitchen equipment. The visual and aromatic appeal of grilling seasonal fish skewers, arranged in a row in front of the irori, adds to the diner’s culinary delight. An embodiment of Chef Jung Eu-tteum’s experience with Japanese cuisine and his personal gastronomic affinities, the eatery is a perfect haven to relish a diverse array of grilled fish. Clay pot rice and other dishes served during the omakase course boast a range of refined flavors that often characterize Japanese cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
16824;Torafuguga;South Korea;Busan;480 Jwadongsunhwan-ro, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48103, South Korea;35.16417;129.1699;100;true;false;Fugu / Pufferfish;Located on a boulevard near Jungdong Intersection in the Haeundae District, Torafuguga stands out with its quaint wooden exterior and a small aquarium with live torafuku (tiger puffer) at the front. The eatery has no sign except for a small calligraphy of its name penned by the owner-chef Jung Seung-hun himself. Yet, these visual elements are enough to let you know that it’s a specialist puffer fish restaurant. Here, the chef’s precise hand movements bring out the variegated flavors of tiger puffer and deliver them, nonstop, to customers at the tables. Torafuguga’s Japanese-style puffer fish course features a wide array of faithful dishes that are parboiled, served raw in slices, fried, made into a soup, or crafted into a porridge. There are many restaurants that handle puffer fish, but few show commitment to presenting it in authentic Japanese style. In light of this, the chef’s earnestness in preparing and serving puffer fish testifies to his passion for culinary art.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16825;Essence;South Korea;Seoul;12 Banpo-daero 4-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06719, South Korea;37.48179;127.01336;77;false;true;French;After a series of twists and turns, Chef Kim Yeong-seon wrapped up his famed career as a classic French chef at Restaurant Soleil and opened Essence to offer his very own version of French cuisine. Here, the chef provides bistro-style French fare that is cozier and lighter, and therefore more accessible, than the fare at his previous restaurant. Although the winds of change are sweeping through the dining industry, he is steadfastly committed to the classic style, delivering deep flavors through precisely baked and cooked ingredients and carefully crafted sauces. In this era of contemporary cuisine that appeals to diners with a wide range of novel culinary styles, Essence’s unpretentious meals highlighting genuine authenticity remind us, once again, of the core of French cuisine.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16826;Iwa;South Korea;Busan;2F, 13 Haeundaehaebyeon-ro 209 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48093, South Korea;35.15959;129.15384;67;false;true;Japanese;The chef, who holds a patent for the aging of fish, prepares aged ingredients with clear intent. Such meticulous preparation, combined with diverse selections, produces stable flavors and gastronomic delights. Depending on the ingredients available and the chef’s tactics, the proportion of sushi, sashimi, and other Japanese dishes in the omakase can vary. All fish here are aged at least four days, and the chef carefully selects an optimal aging period for each fish based on its type, characteristics, and conditions. At Iwa, customers can enjoy at one sitting a wide variety of Japanese dishes, each prepared with aged ingredients with full-bodied flavors. And reasonable prices make this culinary feast all the more special.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16827;L'OIGNON;South Korea;Seoul;13-4, Apgujoeng-ro 4-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06028, South Korea;37.52177;127.02053;99;false;false;French;Nestled in a quiet alley within the ultra-trendy Garosu-gil district, L'Oignon, which means “the onion” in French, is a French-based pescatarian restaurant that offers dishes made only with vegetables, fish, eggs and dairy products. With a steadfast dedication to the principles of ecological harmony and compassionate treatment of animals, the chef opened this eatery with the intention of imparting to patrons the wholesome sustenance he himself reveres. The kitchen uses vegetable broth with mushrooms as a substitute for rich meat broth and creates the texture of its cakes using cauliflower and pecorino cheese instead of flour. Yet, the umami flavors and textures produced through these novel means are as deep and as luscious as those concocted by conventional recipes. If the allure of a plant-based diet beckons, why not indulge in the captivating flavors of L'Oignon's pescatarian fare?;Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16828;Le dorer;South Korea;Busan;2F, 37 Marine city 3-ro, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48118, South Korea;35.15543;129.14665;94;true;false;Contemporary;Le Dorer’s Marine City location offers a gorgeous seascape. Dorer is a French word that means “to coat with gold.” The restaurant’s name therefore symbolizes its resolve to provide a swanky and beautiful dining experience. Le Dorer started off as a Korean restaurant, but now serves contemporary fare with a touch of French and Japanese cuisine. It also features a wine cellar that boasts a wide range of vintages and varietals. For those who prefer to focus on the union of food and wine, Le Dorer also offers an a la carte menu and a bar menu with a wine and cocktail list.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16829;Chef Gon;South Korea;Busan;12 Junggu-ro 23 beon-gil, Jung-gu, Busan, 48978, South Korea;35.10168;129.03004;79;false;false;Contemporary;Situated in an alley near Jagalchi Market, this joint is run by a former hotel chef with years of experience. Every morning, the chef visits the market to buy fresh ingredients, with which he prepares the day’s seasonal menu. For this reason, the restaurant’s course meal is called “Jagalchi Chef’s Course Special.” Diners sitting near the kitchen can watch the chef in action while listening to his explanations about the ingredients. In addition to seafood offerings, the menu features a wide range of meat and a la carte dishes, as well as a well-balanced wine list, all of which await your indulgence.;Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16832;Restaurant OY;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 48-12 Seolleung-ro 148-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06064, South Korea;37.5222697;127.0432627;23;true;true;French, Contemporary;Nestled in a quiet residential alley, Restaurant OY has a homey façade that befits the ambience of the neighborhood. Run by a chef couple who have spent much of their time in Korea and France dedicated to pursuing their passion for French cuisine, this establishment serves up classy and comforting dishes rather than elaborate arrangements. Blurring the boundaries between the traditional and the modern, the cuisine still remains true to authentic tastes. Their sophisticated understanding of ingredients and precise cooking skills result in dishes with well-defined tastes and depth of flavor. In short, diners can expect culinary gems that consistently satisfy.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16833;Hakusi;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 6 Dokseodang-ro 29-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04419, South Korea;37.53667;127.01157;54;true;true;Japanese;Charcoal, fire and paper – these are the three themes Chef Choi Seong-hun seeks to convey in Hakusi’s captivating culinary narrative. The triumphant result is a testament to his masterful storytelling. Beginning at the entrance and extending all the way to the dining area, an arresting visual tableau of black and red imbues the space with personality, punctuated by white elements that exude a sense of harmony and stability. This vivid vitality is also manifest in the establishment’s distinctive cuisine that reflects the chef’s vast culinary experience. In every dish, the allure of seasonal ingredients is brought to life in vivid detail, with distinct flavors and aromas, which transcend the boundaries between modern and classic cuisine, figuring prominently.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16834;Zero Base;South Korea;Busan;2F, 17 Millak-ro 33 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48285, South Korea;35.15741;129.12097;77;false;false;Japanese;Zero Base is a new Japanese restaurant by Chef Yu Byeong-chan, who previously ran the izakaya Yoo No Woo with a stellar reputation. The chef’s unrelenting thirst for classy Japanese cuisine, which had never been fully quenched at his former spot, drove him to present his newly evolved cuisine at this up-and-coming eatery. His solid culinary skills turn ingredients into sumptuous variations on a classic theme, in a way that accentuates his sensibilities. The eatery pays special attention to selecting the freshest of seasonal ingredients. And it simply makes sense. The delicate juxtaposition between Zero Base’s contemporary décor and classic cuisine conjures up an exclusive vibe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16836;Borgo Hannam;South Korea;Seoul;3F, 31 Itaewon-ro 54-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04400, South Korea;37.53687;127.00187;99;true;true;Italian;“Borgo” in Italian means “village,” helmed by Chef Stefano Di Salvo. Once up the tiny set of stairs, you are greeted with homemade dishes and liqueurs befitting the cozy space. From the bread freshly baked in the morning to pastas and desserts, everything is handmade by the chef himself. The kitchen's signature Caldaro soup was inspired by the fisherman’s soup in Tuscany, which has good rich spicy flavor in it with chef’s own twist. Recreating the ambience of a friendly diner, this is a great spot for heartwarming Italian food from various regions. Don’t miss the diverse range of desserts served on a tiered stand.;Air conditioning;[]
16837;Il Vecchio;South Korea;Seoul;332-12 World Cup buk-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03930, South Korea;37.5763;126.89462;89;false;false;Italian;Il Vecchio is a down-to-earth, homey ristorante run by the chef couple Kim Min-gyun and Kim Bin-na. The eatery’s Italian fare brims with well-defined and focused flavors, and its signature dishes made with fresh local produce and seafood capture perfectly the tastes of the season. With meticulous execution, the chef duo cooks each and every ingredient to a precise degree with optimal juiciness, bringing out a range of nuanced flavors, aromas, and textures. Indeed, its semi-dried fresh pasta sets the standard for such extraordinary attention to culinary detail. At Il Vecchio, unrelenting gastronomic innovation that aims to delight diners with diverse yet consistent epicurean experiences is the norm. Just one caveat: The establishment is nestled in an alley, so parking may prove a challenge.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16838;Kumsu Bokguk;South Korea;Busan;23 Jungdong 1-ro 43 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48095, South Korea;35.16242;129.1645;43;false;true;Fugu / Pufferfish;Kumsu Bokguk in Haeundae District is the head restaurant of a chain that has many outposts in Seoul and Busan. For more than 50 years since 1970, and across multiple generations, this eatery has delighted seafood lovers as a specialized puffer fish restaurant. It offers four types of puffer fish. Brown-backed puffer is chewy and has a nutty flavor. Globe puffer is large and often made into a spicy stew. Yellowfin puffer is sweet, so it is usually steamed or boiled. Ocellate puffer is the largest variety of the fish. Its firm texture makes the fish more suitable to be served raw. Safety is the first priority at this head restaurant as demonstrated by the hiring of dozens of chefs, all licensed to prepare puffer fish. So why not rest assured and visit this time-tested establishment for a gastronomic adventure?;Car park,Valet parking;[]
16839;Ryunique;South Korea;Seoul;8-1 Dosan-daero 45-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06021, South Korea;37.52291;127.03599;24;false;false;Innovative;Since its opening in 2011, Ryunique has been constantly reinventing the art of cuisine, driven by Chef Ryu Tae-hwan’s independent research and creative interpretation of ingredients. The chef continually updates the menu to reflect the solar term and season, with an emphasis on fresh ingredients that vary by season and source. His talent for turning his unbounded gastronomic imagination into reality is the secret to Ryunique’s unique fare. Remarkably, this tidy and modern space is home to both the chef’s research center (first floor) and a dining area (second floor). All in all, there is something special about Ryunique’s cuisine that sparks our culinary imagination while never losing its freshness or charm.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16840;ELPIC;South Korea;Seoul;25 Dosan-daero 78-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06063, South Korea;37.52237;127.04659;37;false;true;Steakhouse;El Pic, once a famed grill house on Jeju Island, has found its new home in Seoul. Although dry-aged, wet-aged and beeswax-aged beef steaks are signature dishes at this steakhouse, its grilled fresh seasonal squid, caught in the waters off Jeju Island, and ceviche are pleasant surprises as well. The way the steaks are grilled is extraordinary: They are cooked over charcoal at low temperature and cooled, with the process repeating for more than 30 minutes to maximize tenderness and juiciness. The sliced meat looks red, but is indeed cooked to perfection. Pair the meat with wine for additional gastronomic indulgence.;Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16841;Al'aise;South Korea;Seoul;89 Dokseodang-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04419, South Korea;37.53479;127.01029;74;true;false;French;Al’aise is a French restaurant headed by Chef Lee Byeong-gon, who has dedicated extensive efforts to experience and immerse himself in authentic French cuisine. The power of such conscientious dedication is instilled in his dishes that remain faithful to the basics and are brimming with honest passion to convey the innate flavors of the ingredients. The course meals feature an exceptional balance of ingredients and sauces, bringing out the long-standing and dependable flavors expected from fine French cuisine. Another distinct culinary delight is to be found in the kitchen’s classic French sauces adorned with the chef’s singular twists. Treat yourself in this homey and cozy bistro that offers delicately flavored French fare crafted with imaginative seasonal Korean ingredients.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16842;y'east;South Korea;Seoul;3F, 26-6 Eonju-ro 170-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06017, South Korea;37.5263;127.03556;85;true;false;Contemporary;In a nod to the property’s name, an appellation that invites varied interpretations, Y’east is home to expressions of unlimited culinary possibilities. Chef Cho Young-dong, its chef de cuisine, delights diners with familiar dishes reimagined via his singular aesthetics. The chef channels his passion into creating novel flavors by artfully blending ingredients that are hard to come by in Korea. From the signature amuse bouche inspired by kaya toast to Galbi Stone, braised short ribs that come in several variations, each dish embodies the novel within the familiar, presenting out-of-the-box gastronomic ecstasy that evokes fresh new tastes while still retaining the very essence of the original flavor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16843;Yulling;South Korea;Busan;2F, 28 Dalmaji-gil 62 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48098, South Korea;35.15837;129.17324;19;false;true;Barbecue;Yulling sits on the second floor of the Mipo Oceanside Hotel at the beginning of Dalmaji-gil Road. The lengthy counter in this vast space commands a panoramic ocean view marked by the spectacular Dongbaekseom Island and Gwangandaegyo Bridge. The restaurant uses a wide array of only the choicest Korean beef cuts graded 1++ No. 9, the highest standard. On top of this, its fresh seafood dishes with an intriguing blend of Japanese and European elements create a menu brimming with impeccably balanced flavors – as suggested by the name Yulling, which denotes “harmony” and “balance.” And one more thing: Don’t miss the well-thought-out wine pairings.;Car park,Counter dining;[]
16844;Zhonghuafuchun Salon;South Korea;Seoul;10 Yeonnam-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03989, South Korea;37.56068;126.92335;86;true;false;Chinese;To convey its authenticity to diners, a cuisine that transforms and responds to changing times must be founded on a clear and accurate understanding of culinary tradition. At Zhonghuafuchun Salon, Chef Nam Bok-chun’s concern for and dedication to bringing positive change to Chinese cuisine is unmistakable in its culinary creations. The chef pays particular attention to selecting quality ingredients, the basic building blocks of good food, while engaging in active exchanges with chefs in mainland China, to promote a gradual evolution in his native cuisine, one dish at a time. Zhonghuafuchun Salon is a fascinating Chinese establishment, where traditional Chinese recipes combined with local twists translate into a feast of richly flavorful dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16845;Chez Simon;South Korea;Seoul;48 World Cup-ro 10-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04003, South Korea;37.55517;126.91419;71;false;false;French;Chez Simon, This French bistro has been growing at a steady pace. The couple who runs this eatery closes its doors every year for a certain period, so that they can travel around the world to discover new ingredients. It is this unrelenting dedication to cuisine and humility that has marked the success, even though the chefs have had no professional culinary training. This French kitchen offers only course meals, featuring plain, simple dishes that are the culmination of authentic recipes and fresh, carefully curated ingredients.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
16846;Myomi;South Korea;Seoul;5F Arario Space, 83 Yulgok-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03058, South Korea;37.57781;126.98829;77;false;true;Contemporary;Myomi is set in a gorgeous space with a spectacular view of Changdeokgung Palace, is an experience that diners eagerly await. Chef Kim Hyo-jung's use of Korean ingredients and cooking techniques remain unchanged, but the chef has added subtle new inflections to his dishes as the venue’s name Myomi (“subtle charm”) fittingly suggests.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
16847;Mr. Ahn's Craft Makgeolli;South Korea;Seoul;3 Hoenamu-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04343, South Korea;37.53858;126.9874;76;true;false;Korean;Mr. Ahn's Craft Makgeolli is a most befitting venue for the Korean term banju, or alcohol accompanying a meal. What distinguishes this gastropub is its avoidance of the stereotypical Korean pubs and expression of the direction they should take—in this age of new Korean cuisine that is traditional yet imbued with a modern touch. At this charming spot, patrons can enjoy seasonally changing menus of savory Korean anju (snacks paired with alcohol), main dishes, as well as a wide selection of traditional liquors that simply get better with time. It’s a perfect place for both light meals and friendly social drinking—a versatile venue that appeals to distinct audiences.;Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16848;Moulin;South Korea;Seoul;8 Jahamun-ro 16-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03043, South Korea;37.5814682;126.9718836;33;false;true;French, Modern French;Located on a quiet alley in Seochon, Moulin is a French establishment whose dark-colored frontage draws attention by forming a stark contrast against its surroundings. Once inside, expect to be visually enticed by an antique-style décor and walls adorned with a collection of moulins, or pepper mills, that the chef has amassed over the years. Chef Yoon Ye-rang’s desire to impart flavors of the season to her French cuisine is expressed in dishes that celebrate the balance of subtle and bold gastronomic elements. The signature pithivier series that continues to be recreated using seasonal ingredients epitomizes the culinary philosophy.;Air conditioning;[]
16849;SIIO;South Korea;Seoul;33 Dosan-daero 54-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06056, South Korea;37.5205428;127.0391949;51;true;true;Contemporary, Japanese Contemporary;At SIIO, the head chef’s experience is seen in imaginative dishes featuring seasonal Korean ingredients, ready to delight diners with sumptuous flavors. SIIO’s fare breaks free from the mold and embraces freedom of expression. At this fine diner, novel dishes represent a melting pot of culinary cultures and techniques. Yet, under the veneer of this freewheeling, fresh take on food lies the careful selection of ingredients that reflect Korea’s four distinct seasons. Meticulous rules dictate the perfect balance of subtle flavors.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16850;Olh Eum;South Korea;Seoul;3F, 37 Seolleung-ro 152-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06016, South Korea;37.52451;127.04266;41;false;false;Contemporary;Cooking honest food that respects the integrity of ingredients is the motto of Chef Seo Ho-young, who cooks with the freshest produce sent to him by his farmer parents. Transporting familiar flavors to new territories is his game. Take, for example, his shrimp and sea urchin capellini in a silky smooth bisque-like sauce made with freshwater shrimp heads, fermented fish sauce and doenjang, or his smoked striploin carpaccio served with a mushroom and soy sauce consommé.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16851;Minami;South Korea;Seoul;31-2 Seocho-daero 58-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06632, South Korea;37.4933;127.0181;91;true;true;Soba;The star of the show at Minami is Japanese-style soba noodles. Trained at the prestigious Tsuji Culinary Institute in Osaka, Japan, Chef Nam Chang-soo is no stranger to the world of Japanese cuisine, but he professes that soba is his one true love. While respecting the time-honored traditions of Japanese-style buckwheat noodles, Nam adds his own spin to the soba dishes he serves. Customer favorites include soba noodle soup topped with soy sauce-braised and grilled conger eel as well as another variety with soy sauce-braised herring imported from Kyoto.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
16852;Wooga;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 22 Dosan-daero 49-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06019, South Korea;37.52432;127.03734;50;true;true;Barbecue;Wooga was originally born in Hoengseong, the beef capital of Korea. The restaurant is known for preparing the choicest quality local beef in its unique style: dry aged and well done. Chef Heo Se-byeong has been experimenting tirelessly with beef under the slogan meat science to maximize the characteristics of this meat such as tenderness, juiciness and flavor. Don’t miss out on another perennial favorite: a stew made with soybean paste fermented over long stages by the chef’s own mom.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16853;Imun Seolnongtang;South Korea;Seoul;38-13 Ujeongguk-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03149, South Korea;37.57272;126.98388;63;false;false;Seolleongtang;Still going strong after more than 100 years of being in business, Imun Seolnongtang was the first eatery in Korea to officially register for a restaurant license when it opened in 1904. To this day, it honors the tradition of boiling ox bones for 17 hours until the broth turns rich and opaque. Other cuts of beef are later added to the intensely flavorful broth, served with a generous portion of sliced beef and soft wheat noodles.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16854;Table for Four;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 11 Sapyung-daero 14-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06575, South Korea;37.49775;126.99436;60;false;false;Contemporary;[Temporarily closed due to restaurant moving issue.]This 'Table' uses a wide range of seasonal ingredients infused with optimal flavors from Taean, South Chungcheong Province—the chef’s hometown. His affection for the region and genuine passion to serve the freshest and healthiest food to patrons are the reasons behind his use of such choice. The chef, sometimes aided by the seasoned master, is able to skillfully transform his hometown ingredients into exciting dishes, and at other times there is minimal culinary intervention. Diners who visit are bound to relish the allure of this European cuisine, imbued with the flair of Taean.;Valet parking;[]
16855;Aelgerizm;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 8 Dosan-daero 49-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06019, South Korea;37.5233164;127.0374241;80;false;false;Contemporary, Japanese Contemporary;Aelgerizm’s Japan-meets-West modern cuisine will delight your palate with delicate seasonable variations on a theme. The food is inspired by Chef Yang Min-woo’s rich culinary and life experience in Japan. He blurs the boundaries of his brand of Japanese cuisine through the inventive use of Western ingredients, always seeking to maintain the right balance to achieve culinary perfection. The menu changes four times a year, reflecting Korea’s four distinct seasons, with each seasonal menu organically related to the preceding one. Each dish brings out the genuine flavors of the ingredients, then delicately balanced with the sauces.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16856;Palais de Chine;South Korea;Seoul;6F L'Escape Hotel, 67 Toegye-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04529, South Korea;37.55983;126.97949;18;false;false;Chinese;Located inside the Parisian Belle Époque-inspired L'Escape Hotel, Palais de Chine is the only space within the hotel that offers Eastern tastes and sensibilities. Inspired by designs from Shanghai's own belle époque, the modern space offers both authentic and modern interpretations of Chinese cuisine. There is a good range of dishes on the menu that stay true to their regional eccentricities, including the dim sum selection. Palais de Chine prides itself on its Peking duck, another celebrated Chinese dish with regional distinctiveness.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16857;Continental;South Korea;Seoul;23F The Shilla Hotel, 249 Dongho-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04605, South Korea;37.5558213;127.00517;26;false;false;French;If you are looking for a refined French restaurant with all the elements of classic French luxury, Continental is a solid bet. Perched on the 23rd floor of The Shilla Seoul, the restaurant is decorated in rich colors, with large tables and French empire chairs. What’s more, the bright dining room offers diners a fantastic view of the city. The meticulously prepared food is beautifully plated and served on two different set menus of your choice.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16858;L'Espoir du Hibou;South Korea;Seoul;16 Dosan-daero 59-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06016, South Korea;37.5245;127.04227;66;true;true;French;All of the elements at this bistro — from the food to the décor to the outdoor patio — fall into place to create an ambience that is immediately charming and oh so French! Consistency has been key to L’Espoir du Hibou’s longevity, not least when it comes to food. Chef Lim Ki-hak makes traditional French charcuterie like terrines and pâtés from scratch. The onion soup is outstanding, as is the classic duck confit. Terrace dining is a must during the warmer months.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
16859;Pyeongyang Myeonok;South Korea;Seoul;207 Jangchungdan-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04615, South Korea;37.56325;127.00664;72;false;true;Naengmyeon;This establishment has been open for three generations, serving some of the finest bowls of Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodles in the city. The long queue outside the entrance constitutes a part of the street’s daily scenery during the sweltering summer months. The clear meat broth is delicately seasoned and the buckwheat noodles have a pleasant texture, firm and not too chewy. Steamed dumplings and boiled pork slices, served warm, are also standout dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16860;Restaurant Jueun;South Korea;Seoul;8F Gyeonghuidang, 36 Gyeonghuigung-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03175, South Korea;37.57276;126.96991;29;false;false;Korean, Classic Cuisine;Situated behind Gyeonghuigung Palace, Jueun is a Korean restaurant opened by Chef Park Ju-eun, former head chef at Hansikgonggan, and his team. From design elements imbued with Korean aesthetics to elegant artifacts crafted in partnership with artisans to a media art wall occupying the length of the dining hall’s wall, every nook and cranny of the establishment highlights sincere preparation. The menu consists of traditional Korean dishes, ranging from imjasutang, a soup featuring roasted sesame seeds, chicken leg flesh, and Korean mint leaves, to a porridge made with abundant scallops, shellfish, shrimps, and fragrant beach silvertop. The eatery’s solid selection of wine and traditional Korean alcohol adds to its culinary delights.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16861;Vigneto;South Korea;Busan;55 Suyeong-ro 522 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48299, South Korea;35.15182;129.11473;37;true;true;Italian;Vigneto is the very first restaurant by an owner-chef couple who settled in Busan after studying Italian cuisine at ALMA, the renowned culinary school in Italy. The building is both their home and restaurant, with the wooden ceiling and furniture in the interior creating a cozy and warm vibe. An Italian wine bar, Vigneto combines authentic Italian cuisine with a rare Italian natural wine pairing. In particular, its pastas and hams, all housemade, boast exceptional textures and flavors. For foodies who seek to revel in food and wine amidst Vigneto’s snug ambiance, we recommend reservations (which are set at 30-minute intervals).;Air conditioning;[]
16862;Légume;South Korea;Seoul;2F, Sinsa Square, 652 Gangnam-daero, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06027, South Korea;37.51938;127.01932;93;true;true;Vegan, Vegetarian;It’s no easy feat to invent dignified and alluring cuisine that is based only on plant ingredients. Yet, Chef Sung Si-woo at Légume pulls it off with panache. The chef’s fondness for veggies since childhood has led to a deeper understanding of vegetarian diets, which, coupled with his unique perspective, has given birth to his one-of-a-kind delicacies. In pursuit of 100 percent vegan cuisine, this eatery has perfected a refined vegetarian dining style that transcends the provision of mere plant-based meals, thereby highlighting the diversity and direction of Korean vegetarian cuisine. At Légume, sensorial contemporary cuisine meets the chef’s seasoned skills and is transformed into a vegan menu with a distinct identity and imaginative flavors. The evident truth is that the kitchen’s vegan fare not only appeals to vegetarians but also to people with a wide range of palates.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16863;Mater;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 16 Eonju-ro 154-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06021, South Korea;37.52337;127.03464;91;true;true;Contemporary, Scandinavian;With the focus on fermentation, Chef Kim Yeong-bin brings together the Korean and Asian cuisines he grew up with and the Western and Nordic cuisines he has been exploring as a chef, creating dishes bursting with unbridled imagination. Through the process of fermentation, the chef adds a unique twist to the flavor and texture of his ingredients, which are then exploited, sometimes subtly and at other times vigorously, for resonant and diverse expressions of fermented flavors. Such attempts reveal the kitchen’s intent and efforts to balance sour and umami taste profiles. Since Korea is where fermented foods are regular staples, it is all the more intriguing to witness Mater’s series of gastronomic experiments aimed at balancing the tastes and expressing the varied flavors of fermented dishes.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16864;Haenam Cheonilgwan;South Korea;Seoul;36-1 Banpo-daero 39-gil, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06578, South Korea;37.49862;127.00195;52;true;false;Korean;Namdo cuisine, the cuisine of South Jeolla Province, occupies an eminent position in the diverse Korean culinary landscape. Haenam Cheonilgwan is a singular undertaking as it has steadfastly safeguarded Namdo cuisine through the generations. It branched out from Cheonil Sikdang, a Haenam-based diner with a proud history, and is headed by CEO Lee Hwa-young, a relative of the original founder. The asset that distinguishes Lee’s establishment from typical diners run by chefs is its tried-and-true flavors and recipes evolved and accumulated through the everyday vignettes she shares with her family. Korean cuisine has modernized to meet changing times, yet this food haven still strives to preserve the menus, recipes, and ingredients used when traditional ingredients were aplenty. Among the mélange of dishes that sumptuously fill your table, standouts bursting with Namdo flavors include banji kimchi (Namdo-style white kimchi), chili pepper kimchi with salted freshwater shrimp, and grilled short rib patties. The dining space consists entirely of private rooms suitable for a diverse range of occasions.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16865;Mustrue;South Korea;Busan;29 Jwadongsunhwan-ro 433 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48114, South Korea;35.16149;129.17634;83;false;false;European;Mustrue is one of the representative fine dining spots in Busan. Helmed by Chef Jung Jae-yong, a Busan native, it is covertly tucked away in a back alley of Dalmaji-gil Road. Open the golden door, and you’ll be greeted with a bar counter, where the chef masterfully handles everything from cooking to serving. By using unique local ingredients, such as Korean angelica seeds and short-fruit pimpinella, he creates European cuisine with a Korean twist. Chef Jung is passionate about maintaining the harmony between his culinary creations and Korean ingredients. And his passion is uncompromising – just as Mustrue, the eatery’s name, suggests.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16866;Sogonggan;South Korea;Busan;4F, 47 Haeundaehaebyon-ro 298 beon-gil, Haeundae-gu, Busan, 48099, South Korea;35.16168;129.16738;59;false;true;Korean;Sogonggan is a double entendre that can be read as “a small space” or “a space dealing with beef.” Its thoughtfully crafted menu is rooted in Korean cuisine. The chef spent many years perfecting his Western cuisine before making the switch to its Korean counterpart. He says the switching has made cooking more enjoyable and comforting as if he were finally wearing a tailored suit. Indeed, his sense of happiness is genuinely reflected in the fare. With Sogonggan’s elegant plating, original dishes, and refined Korean menu lineup, such as beef bone soup simmered in-house for 48 hours and pot rice, the “small space” moniker is unquestionably a misnomer.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining;[]
16868;OPNNG;South Korea;Seoul;B1, 22 Dosan-daero 34-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06049, South Korea;37.51844;127.03105;74;true;false;Contemporary;At OPNNG, delight your taste buds with hard-to-find rare wines while relishing the overall vibe. The name symbolizes “the opening up of new taste vistas through gastronomy and wine.” Resembling more of a gallery than a wine bar or restaurant, this fine dining venue impresses patrons with an arch-shaped entrance, paintings by renowned artists, and a vast wine cellar that plays host to more than 500 different types of wine. It offers handmade pasta dishes and refined à la carte items.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Valet parking;[]
16869;ON;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 42 Dosan-daero 92-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06070, South Korea;37.52192;127.04938;78;true;false;French;The name may have changed from the previous Siot to the current On, but the food at this refined French restaurant retains its integrity. The elegant space is simple and intimate with just two or three tables, with the layout designed to guarantee the privacy of diners. Because there is limited seating, prior reservations are mandatory. On focuses on seasonal produce to prepare its signature offerings, including a vegetable dish that consists of ruby red grapefruit and two types of oven-dried tomatoes that highlight their exquisite sweetness and acidity.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16870;Yakitori Mook;South Korea;Seoul;165-1 Seongmisan-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03980, South Korea;37.56461;126.92449;42;false;false;Yakitori;This yakitori specialist is nestled in a quiet corner in Yeonnam-dong. Make your way inside to discover an elongated counter, open kitchen and, at its center, Chef Kim Byoung-mook busy concentrating on grilling yakitori skewers over a charcoal as well as a straw fire. This visually arresting image of the chef, standing under the intense lights that also illuminate the grill, is reminiscent of an actor delivering a monologue on stage. The restaurant's motto is plain and simple, “We prepare fresh purebred Korean chicken every day and grill our skewers over the highest-grade Japanese Binchotan charcoal and serve them immediately to our patrons.”;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16871;Oegojip Seolleongtang;South Korea;Seoul;555 Samseong-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06155, South Korea;37.51097;127.05388;84;false;false;Seolleongtang;What this restaurant lacks in variety, it makes up for it in quality. Since 2005, the establishment has been serving up hearty bowls of ox bone soup, the ultimate Korean comfort food. The recipe, handed down to the current proprietor by his mother-in-law, has been tweaked over the years, but one thing remains constant — the love and care put into each and every bowl of soup. It is highly-recommended for those seeking a truly local experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16872;JUE;South Korea;Seoul;124-7 Dokseodang-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04420, South Korea;37.53744;127.01277;34;false;true;Chinese;Resembling the Chinese pronunciation of a word which refers to a title of nobility, Jue is a restaurant that specializes in Cantonese cuisine. The set menu is also named after the different noble titles in China. One of Jue's signature dishes is its barbecued pork which, after being marinated, is roasted in a high-temperature oven to ensure a supremely crispy skin and juicy, flavorful meat. Of the 13 different varieties of dim sum on offer, the cheung fan (rice noodle roll), shumai topped with abalone, and the spring rolls are not to be missed.;Credit cards not accepted,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16873;Tenjimon;South Korea;Seoul;4F, 41 Hakdong-ro 97-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06072, South Korea;37.52237;127.05429;88;true;false;Japanese;A collaboration between Chef Kim Dae-chun—owner of TOC TOC—and Chef Zaiyu Hasegawa—owner of Den in Tokyo—"Tenjimon' is the Japanese pronunciation of a Chinese/Korean word that means “To open the door to the gastronomic world via ingredients from heaven and earth.” Although this partnership requires that the menu be confirmed from Japan, Tenjimon’s omakase features fresh Korean ingredients. Of particular note, the signature hot pot rice is a uniquely flavored delicacy made with seasonal and local ingredients, such as amur wallflower and aster leaf. Since seating is limited for this unique culinary discovery, reservations are a must.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16874;Teppan;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, Grand Hyatt Hotel, 322 Sowol-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04347, South Korea;37.53929;126.9971;79;true;true;Teppanyaki;Located along Grand Hyatt Seoul’s gourmet alley 322 Sowol-ro, Teppan is a restaurant where everything on the menu is cooked on an iron griddle — even appetizers and desserts. Food is prepared by chefs in front of the guests on flat-surface grills behind the bar counter. Diners can also gaze out at the scenic view of Namsan Mountain through the restaurant’s wide windows while enjoying their meal. The menu offers plenty of fresh seafood and meats as well as spectacular fire shows.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16875;Sooksoodoga;South Korea;Seoul;28 Dongsomun-ro 17-gil, Seongbuk-gu, Seoul, 02830, South Korea;37.5935;127.01539;40;false;false;Barbecue;Chef's years-long study and mission to “create the best aged beef using the finest Korean meat” according to its own manual, the restaurant dry-ages the meat for 720 hours under varying conditions of temperature, humidity and oxygen for optimal fermentation in order to maximize its umami taste. This aged meat is then grilled on the table using the chef’s trademark method, which is known to best bring out the beef’s distinct flavor. Depending on the cuts, there are three different course meals available. The restaurant's prices, set affordably to help popularize the appeal of aged beef, add greatly to its attraction.;Air conditioning;[]
16877;STAY;South Korea;Seoul;81F Lotteworld Tower, 300 Olympic-ro, Songpa-gu, Seoul, 05551, South Korea;37.51271;127.10258;24;false;false;French;Perched on the 81st floor of Signiel Seoul Hotel, STAY takes ‘dining with a view’ to a whole new level with its sweeping vistas of the metropolis. STAY is celebrated Chef Yannick Alléno’s modern casual French restaurant, a youthful and vibrant space accented with yellow and gold. The live Pastry Library is its signature feature that offers a tantalizing assortment of sweets and confections that guests can help themselves to.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16878;Gom Ba Wie;South Korea;Seoul;10 Yeongdong-daero 115-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06087, South Korea;37.51485;127.05885;35;false;true;Barbecue;Grilled tripe and large intestines reign supreme at Gom Ba Wie, which has seen three decades of customers hooked on their buttery, pleasantly chewy goodness. The original location and the new location stand back to back, offering a glimpse of the restaurant’s past and present. If beef intestines aren't your cup of tea, the restaurant also offers other cuts like ribeye, short ribs and brisket. All meats are grilled over wood charcoal.;Valet parking;[]
16879;Born and Bred;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 1 Majang-ro 42-gil, Seongdong-gu, Seoul, 04757, South Korea;37.56697;127.04468;24;true;true;Barbecue;Born and Bred is the brainchild of Jeong Sang-won, whose obsession with top-quality Korean beef started young, thanks to his beef purveyor father. Jeong created a one-of-a-kind space that offers three different dining concepts. The casual eatery on the second floor has been inspired by the butcher restaurants that populate the vicinity of the Majang Meat Market, but it is decidedly more modern and refined. The butcher lounge occupies the first floor while the third floor offers a multi-course beef experience. However, for a taste of what the restaurant is truly all about, head down to the basement for the chef's specialty beef course.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16880;The Green Table;South Korea;Seoul;4F Arario Space, 83 Yulgok-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03058, South Korea;37.57781;126.98829;79;true;false;French;The Green Table is a French restaurant run by Chef Kim Eun-hee. It also offers seasonal menus featuring seasonal Korean ingredients, delivering ingredients grown by nature to the table directly. On veranda, herbs such as oxalis and thyme are grown to add color to the dishes. By fusing diverse ingredients, such as grains and root vegetables, with French recipes, Chef Kim presents precise flavors. Visit The Green Table for heartwarming yet refined French cuisine imbued with the chef’s creativity.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
16881;Crystal Jade;South Korea;Seoul;B1F, 16 Namdaemun-ro 7-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.564311;126.981212;18;false;false;Chinese;Crystal Jade first opened its doors in Singapore in 1991 as a Cantonese restaurant. More than two decades later, the restaurant chain operates in many countries across Asia, including Korea with more than 10 locations. Their mission is to serve high-quality regional cuisine from China. Classics like Hong Kong-style dim sum, sautéed prawns and scallops in XO sauce, and sautéed chicken in black bean sauce are perennial highlights.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16882;July;South Korea;Seoul;164 Donggwang-ro, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06589, South Korea;37.49475;127.00008;67;false;true;Contemporary;This restaurant's creativity is apparent in the food it creates — inherently French, but with an unexpected spin on flavors from using distinctly local ingredients. For example, the chef incorporates traditional fermented condiments such as gochujang and doenjang into his sauces and uses indigenous grains like godaemi — organic ancient colored rice. It's located in Seoraemaeul, also known as 'Little France', and the restaurant's vibe is cozy and intimate.;Valet parking;[]
16883;Comme Moa;South Korea;Seoul;56 Sinheung-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04339, South Korea;37.54344;126.9877;75;true;false;French;This cozy charmer, located towards the tail end of Haebangchon’s main street, is Chef Kim Moa’s cheery French bistro that serves up authentic fare. The menu is composed of classic dishes that clearly demonstrate her philosophy that good ingredients and care for the guests should be the foundation of a tasty dish. Some of the restaurant’s best sellers include foie gras crème brûlée, pâté en croute and beef Wellington, which diners have to call ahead and order a day in advance. For dessert, the chef's special soufflé is a must.;Air conditioning;[]
16884;Bongmilga;South Korea;Seoul;664 Seolleung-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06088, South Korea;37.51598;127.0424;25;true;false;Naengmyeon;This restaurant is a relative newcomer to Seoul’s Pyeongyang cold buckwheat noodle scene but Chef Kwon Hee-seung’s passion for serving authentic bowls of cold buckwheat noodles more than makes up for its short history. Kwon begins each day by preparing the broth for the cold noodles, using cuts from local beef such as brisket, flank and round. He also throws in some medicinal herbs for good measure. Kwon’s noodles are made of 80% buckwheat flour, 20% sweet potato starch and are thicker than the versions served at most of its competitors.;Air conditioning;[]
16885;Mapo Yangji Seolleongtang;South Korea;Seoul;6 Saechang-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04168, South Korea;37.54193;126.9505;68;true;true;Seolleongtang;Mapo Yangji Seolleongtang ushers in a new era with its newly renovated two-story space. The restaurant, which first opened its doors in 1974, has been a long-time favorite among the local crowd for its hearty bowls of ox bone soup, a time-honored quickly-prepared local food, as well as the ultimate comfort food. The soup is a rich and savory blend of broth made from beef shank and brisket. Submerge a bowl of warm rice in the piping hot soup and enjoy it with a side of sweet and fragrant green onion kimchi.;Car park,Valet parking;[]
16886;Boreumsae;South Korea;Seoul;36 Teheran-ro 81-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06167, South Korea;37.509328;127.056611;25;false;true;Barbecue;Beef restaurants are ubiquitous all over Korea, but this spot which opened in late 2015, offers something prized and uncommon: Jeju black cattle. Choose from a wide range of cuts including sirloin, tenderloin, chuck tail flap, outside skirt steak, brisket and two types of raw beef dishes: tartare and sashimi. The prime meat is flown in directly from the family-operated farm. Private rooms are available on the second floor.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16887;Tongue & Groove Joint;South Korea;Seoul;7 Bogwang-ro 60-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04406, South Korea;37.53404;126.99451;22;true;false;Barbecue;Don’t expect to walk into a typical Korean barbecue restaurant when you visit Tongue and Groove Joint, a casually cool and modern space that feels more like a café or a beer hall. The restaurant specializes in quality Korean beef aged for at least three weeks as well as tender lamb chops and beef ribeye. These cuts are grilled at the table by the staff and come with a side of house-made chili oil and cilantro pesto which help cut the richness. The restaurant also has a good variety of lunch offerings and a wide selection of craft beers.;;[]
16888;Chez Nous Private Kitchen;South Korea;Seoul;3F, 210-6 Noksapyeong-Daero, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04345, South Korea;37.53634;126.98734;40;false;true;French;Meaning “our home” in French, the name Chez Nous represents the chef-owner couple’s ardent desire for guests to enjoy warm, hearty food in a home-like setting. Although the French chef and his Korean wife offer mainly homestyle meals, they are anything but ordinary, reflecting Chef Mathieu Moles’s culinary experience as an executive chef at major restaurants and hotels in France. At Chez Nous, you can enjoy authentic French dishes, including carpaccio made with fresh scallops, steak tartare featuring truffle emulsion.Chez Nous opens only for dinner, and reservations are a must. Come and discover your very own French joie de vivre in this cozy dining space that recreates the warmth of a home.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16889;Yu Yuan;South Korea;Seoul;11F Four Seasons Hotel, 97 Saemunan-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03183, South Korea;37.57049;126.97545;95;true;true;Chinese;Inspired by the glitz and glamour of 1920s Shanghai, interior designer André Fu’s dining room is drop-dead gorgeous with its alluring jade-colored walls, marbled floors, lavish furniture and refined tableware. The menu features mostly Cantonese dishes, but also offers recipes from other Chinese regions. Highlights include Peking Duck, crispy pork belly and Cantonese-style steamed sea bream. Their weekend dim sum brunch is extremely popular.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16890;L'Impasse 81;South Korea;Seoul;17-1 Donggyo-ro 30-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 03985, South Korea;37.56018;126.92521;60;true;true;French;Nestled in a quiet alley of Yeonnam-dong, L'Impasse 81 is a dining bar dedicated to the art of charcuterie, embracing the 'nose-to-tail' philosophy to utilize every part of the animal. Charcuterie, a staple of French cuisine, encompasses a variety of cured meats and sausages. Some products, such as those requiring salting and drying, undergo a meticulous aging process of six months to a year, resulting in an intense, umami-rich flavor. Adding to its charm, the restaurant is adorned with vintage furniture sourced directly from Jeju Island, enhancing its unique and sophisticated ambiance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16891;Pierre Gagnaire;South Korea;Seoul;35F Lotte Hotel, 30 Eulji-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.56529;126.98103;94;true;false;French;Internationally celebrated French Chef Pierre Gagnaire opened his eponymous contemporary fine dining restaurant on top of Lotte Hotel’s New Wing in 2008. The elegant dining space, adorned with Murano chandeliers and gold trim walls, exudes classic French luxury. The artfully presented food, made with 80% local ingredients, is respectful of the Paris-based chef’s creative style. With more than 250 labels, the wine cellar display also impresses.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16892;Sushi Cho;South Korea;Seoul;20F The Westin Chosun Hotel, 106 Sogong-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.56441;126.9797;33;false;true;Japanese;It is no secret that this restaurant has long been the stomping ground for some of the most ardent sushi aficionados. For nearly three decades, this critically acclaimed restaurant has been serving consistently sophisticated and refined Japanese cuisine in its elegant dining space, located on the 20th floor of The Westin Chosun Seoul. The top-notch food comes with charming service. Private rooms are also available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16893;Jinmi Sikdang;South Korea;Seoul;186-6 Mapo-daero, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04207, South Korea;37.55055;126.95577;58;false;false;Gejang;This humble yet busy restaurant has been serving raw soy-marinated crabs and nothing else for the past decade. Only the freshest local blue swimmer crabs, sourced from the west coast, are prepared daily with the kitchen’s special recipe soy sauce marinade. Keep in mind that just enough crab for consumption is prepared each day, so if you drop by at a late hour, they may be completely sold out. A prior reservation is highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Shoes must be removed;[]
16894;Toh Lim;South Korea;Seoul;37F Lotte Hotel, 30 Eulji-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;26;false;false;Chinese;Located on the 37th floor of the Lotte Hotel, Toh Lim offers a state-of-the-art Chinese fine dining experience. The restaurant is acclaimed for its expert handling of ingredients, whose natural flavors shine through in the individual dishes.  Led by a highly respected veteran of Korea’s culinary industry, the team serves up a wide array of Chinese, with a special focus on Cantonese-style cuisine. Private rooms are available.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16895;Mugunghwa;South Korea;Seoul;38F Lotte Hotel, 30 Eulji-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.56533;126.981;52;false;false;Korean;Located on the 38th floor with sweeping views of Seoul’s dynamic urban jungle below, Mugunghwa is a modern Korean restaurant. The cooking is based on the basic principle that dictated Eastern medicine — that food and medicine are essentially the same. Creating modern cuisine firmly rooted in traditional Korean fare, the chef is constantly studying to bring the tastiest yet also the healthiest dishes to the table.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16896;The Ninth Gate;South Korea;Seoul;1F The Westin Chosun Hotel, 106 Sogong-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.5644;126.97969;79;true;false;French;It would be challenging to discuss the evolution of French dining in Seoul without mentioning The Ninth Gate. Keeping up with Seoul’s ever-transforming restaurant scene, a newer and better The Ninth Gate reopened its doors to the delight of fans both old and new. While the food is still reflective of the classic French style from the days before its facelift, there is also greater sophistication that makes the restaurant more relevant than ever before. Wine-tasting programs are offered at the bar counter after 10 pm.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16897;Budnamujip;South Korea;Seoul;434 Hyoryeong-ro, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06729, South Korea;37.48907;127.03118;84;true;false;Barbecue;Since 1977, this family-style restaurant has garnered an appreciative following of barbecue lovers, often seeing three generations of loyal patrons from one family frequenting the shop. A popular locality for residents south of the river, it specializes in various cuts of meat exclusively from the cow including ribs, sirloin and tripe. The rich flavors of the exceptionally tender meat is enhanced simply with quality bay salt.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16898;Doughroom;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 99 Donggwang-ro, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06584, South Korea;37.566;126.9784;62;false;true;Italian;Dedicated to making artisanal pasta from scratch, Doughroom is a keeper for all Italian food lovers. The dough room itself, where all the pastas are made fresh daily, is undoubtedly the heart of the restaurant. While offering authentic flavors of Italy, it also serves fusion dishes using ingredients familiar to the local palate — for example, their buckwheat cannelloni. Asking for the action-packed dough room table when making a reservation is highly recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16899;Eonyang Bulgogi Busanjip;South Korea;Busan;32 Namcheonbada-ro, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48304, South Korea;35.14783;129.11337;55;false;true;Bulgogi;More commonly known as just Busanjip, this eatery at Gwangalli Beach has long been a popular spot, always bustling with customers waiting to get in. After decades of business in its previous location, the restaurant moved to this location in 2018. Unlike Seoul-style bulgogi, where meat is cooked in broth, the Eonyang style features marinated meat grilled on a gridiron or over a fire. As for flavor, Seoul bulgogi tends to be sweet, whereas Eonyang bulgogi is less so, with more emphasis on the nutty taste of Korean beef sirloin enhanced by the acidic flavor of the sauce. In addition to its namesake dish, Busanjip serves up a diverse range of special beef cuts. Come and relish the beauty of the coastal waters off Gwangalli today – with each scrumptious bite of beef topped on rice!;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16900;Bistrot de Yountville;South Korea;Seoul;13-7 Seolleung-ro 158-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06014, South Korea;37.52602;127.04126;70;false;true;French;With its classic French bistro charm, Bistro de Yountville feels like a slice of France transported into the heart of the city. The cozy and inviting atmosphere evokes the essence of the French countryside, while the cuisine by Chefs Tommy Lee and Jae-hyung Park reflects their dedication to the fundamentals of French cooking, infused with meticulous care and unwavering effort. The restaurant’s name pays homage to Yountville, the home of the famed French Laundry in California’s Napa Valley, where the chefs were inspired to recreate their unforgettable experiences for diners. Savoring the thoughtfully prepared dishes and warm ambiance here offers a delightful escape from the hustle and bustle of city life.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16901;Yongkangzzie;South Korea;Busan;10 Gwanganhaebyeon-ro 277 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48287, South Korea;35.15749;129.12447;62;false;true;Noodles, Taiwanese;Situated near Gwangalli Beach at the beginning of an alley leading to Millak Golmok Market, Yongkangzzie is a Taiwanese spot best known for its beef noodle soup. The consistent design concepts that permeate both exterior and interior spaces, as well as the detailed décor, have done a remarkable job of reproducing a vibe that evokes Taiwan. The warmth of the signature soup goes well with the eatery’s casual and exotic ambiance. The broth, which offers up subtle sour flavors and umami, and the thick, pleasantly textured noodles make this iconic soup a comforting choice in any season. In addition to this signature dish, Yongkangzzie serves other noodle and side dishes that are guaranteed to please the palate. Please note that the restaurant has no parking lot.;Air conditioning;[]
16903;Osteria Orzo;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 47 Hannam-daero 20-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04419, South Korea;37.53486;127.00946;45;true;false;Italian;Osteria Orzo continues to offer an authentic taste of a casual and cozy Italian osteria at its Hannam-dong location. Signature offerings on the menu include the white ragù pasta which features home-made fresh pasta drenched in rich meat sauce with mascarpone cheese and truffles. The spicy tagliatelle and the seafood tartare are also among the restaurant's all-time favorites. Reserve a table across from the open kitchen and watch the chefs in action.;Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16904;Momoyama;South Korea;Seoul;38F Lotte Hotel, 30 Eulji-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.5653;126.98097;98;false;false;Japanese;Momoyama is a sophisticated Japanese restaurant located on the 38th floor of Lotte Hotel Seoul. The kitchen team offers a wide selection of Japanese cuisine from the traditional yest refined haute cuisine kaiseki-ryōri, to sushi to the one-pot nabemono and even chazuke (cooked rice steeped in hot tea, dashi or hot water). The chef is especially meticulous with ingredients, which he personally procures directly from producers. Momoyama also has an impressive sake selection, selected by a sake sommelier.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Great view,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16905;Gigas;South Korea;Seoul;3F, 30 Toegye-ro 6ga-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04635, South Korea;37.55696;126.97809;19;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;This authentic Mediterranean restaurant is a rarity in the Korean culinary landscape. Recreating bona fide Mediterranean cuisine in Korea is not an easy feat to achieve because of the scarcity of particular ingredients. Nevertheless, using purely organic ingredients grown on his family’s farm, Chef Jung Ha-wan has managed to present fascinating Mediterranean fare with authenticity and direction that reflect the region's culinary tradition. What drives Gigas forward and ensures gastronomic pleasure is the chef’s dedication to sustainability. How this restaurant will take on this challenge and grow amidst Seoul’s culinary landscape is something that sparks our curiosity as much as the pleasant dining experience it offers.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16906;Seoul Dining;South Korea;Seoul;2F Designhouse, 272 Dongho-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04617, South Korea;37.55919;127.00359;18;true;false;Contemporary;A culinary journey that captures the essence of Seoul? The fare at this destination sprang from the chef’s own question of 'Is there a way to bring the unique gastronomic experience that Seoul embodies to restaurant patrons?" Based on this philosophy, the establishment combines seasonal ingredients with a great deal of creativity to bring brilliant, one-of-a-kind dishes to the table. Adding to its appeal is the use of ingredients and sauces that deliver a wide variety of flavors, a gesture that reflects the co-existence of diverse food cultures in Seoul. The contemporary and vibrant dining space also creates a sense of harmony worthy of its buoyant dishes.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
16907;Ile de Cheongdam;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 13 Dosan-daero 59-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06016, South Korea;37.52466;127.04189;64;true;false;Contemporary;Meaning “an island within the heart of the city,” Ile de Cheongdam brings together the best of Japanese omakase with Korean beef omakase. Formerly a membership-only venue, it has opened its doors to the public to share its gastronomic delights with a wider audience. From the chef’s pre-dining explanation of ingredients that change daily to the final tea ceremony, where the tea is steeped three times, every course of the omakase showcases the nuanced service of this establishment. Dining at Ile de Cheongdam is by reservation only.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16909;Vault Steakhouse;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 22 Apgujeong-ro 72-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06015, South Korea;37.52496;127.04496;73;true;true;Steakhouse;The dimly lit masculine décor and a comprehensive whiskey collection with nearly 400 bottles to choose from make Vault+82 one of the most sought-after whiskey bars in Seoul. Right above it is the American-style Vault Steakhouse where premium USDA-approved American beef free of antibiotics and hormones is dry-aged for 14 and 28 days. Available cuts include T-bone, L-bone, bone-in ribeye, filet mignon, New York strip and boneless ribeye.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16910;Sushi Gyeol;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 758 Seolleung-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06062, South Korea;37.52242;127.0396;28;false;true;Sushi;[This is a new address following the restaurant relocation.]A sense of elegance, from the juxtaposition of a curved seating arrangement to the empty spaces, will dominate your first impression. From start to finish, the chef’s sushi and other omakase specialties offer a restrained yet refined balance of flavors. At Sushi Gyeol, a sense of unity between the space and the cuisine augments the joy of relishing the purity of fresh, natural ingredients. That joy experienced in a cozy dining environment is what makes this eatery so very special.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16911;Au Bouillon;South Korea;Seoul;29-1 Dokseodang-ro 51-gil, Seongdong-gu, Seoul, 04718, South Korea;37.5311165;127.0073647;96;false;true;French, Classic French;Hidden in a quaint, tiny alley that's surrounded by apartment complexes in Geumho-dong, this French restaurant greets patrons with classic objets d'art and other fixings. However, the vibe here is different from the surrounding neighborhood, and thanks to an equally striking carte of familiar French fare, diners can expect nothing less than exceptional culinary enjoyment. The menu closely reflects the chef’s desire to offer well-crafted French cuisine at reasonable prices.;Air conditioning;[]
16912;Caden;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 173 Yeonhui-ro, Seodaemun-gu, Seoul, 03699, South Korea;37.57257;126.9351;85;true;false;Japanese;Chef Jeong Ho-yeong's Izakaya Robataya Caden is always striving to evolve. The chef presents his famous udon dishes served on the first floor. The spacious second-floor dining hall continues to serve up the restaurant's signature dishes for lunch as well, including the crispy grilled sea bream, mixed sashimi platter, grilled avocados dressed with soy sauce and spicy brisket champon. In addition to the wide selection of à la carte dishes, Caden also offers a good variety of Japanese liquor.;Car park,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Valet parking;[]
16913;Lee Buk Bang;South Korea;Seoul;2F, 16 Mapo-daero 1-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04165, South Korea;37.5396777;126.9431187;29;true;true;Korean;As the name suggests, Lee Buk Bang is where one can enjoy meals from the leebuk, or North Korean, region. In this setting, blood sausage and other diverse North Korean dishes with a modern flair offer a valuable dining experience to patrons. However, this spot's signature is blood sausage dishes made from the chef’s family recipes. His creativity shines in an array of dishes, from traditional to those featuring ingenious new ingredients. Also noteworthy is his effort to create familiar yet refined cuisine that combines family culinary traditions with his culinary experience. The countertops, made from old crossbeams and doors once used in century-old traditional Korean houses, add to the venue’s traditional vibe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16914;Delibong;South Korea;Busan;#110 Noblesse square, 25 Singeum-ro, Yeonje-gu, Busan, 47560, South Korea;35.19148;129.09437;44;true;false;French;A charcuterie course consisting of housemade meat products – doesn’t that pique your interest? After many years of running a French dining spot, the owner-chef Park Jeong-bong finally opened this little gem with a bar counter and tables that can seat only about ten people. With dim lighting and no sign, Delibong may be difficult for first-timers to find. Processed meats that require lengthy, meticulous curing and drying processes, as well as the polished dishes crafted with them, such as coppa, jambon, rillettes, and prosciutto, await. Aren’t you just a little bit curious? Reservations strongly advised.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16915;Hong Yuan;South Korea;Seoul;1F The Westin Chosun Hotel, 106 Sogong-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul, 04533, South Korea;37.56441;126.9797;33;true;true;Chinese;Instantly memorable with its crimson décor, this high-end restaurant at The Westin Chosun Seoul, specializes in Cantonese cuisine. The elegant space offers a taste of the best in Chinese-style formal dining, with its classic yet innovative dishes. Hong Yuan’s commitment to using the freshest ingredients to make healthy and tasty food is unparalleled, as seen in its heavy use of seafood, tofu and vegetables. Live music during dinner service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Notable sake list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
16916;Byeokje Galbi;South Korea;Seoul;1-4 Yangjae-daero 71-gil, Songpa-gu, Seoul, 05639, South Korea;37.51007;127.12619;27;false;false;Barbecue;Byeokje Galbi is a local institution that has been serving legendary barbecued beef short ribs since 1986. The restaurant’s attention to quality begins from the breeding of the cows at a local farm in Pocheon. Only the top 1% (BMS No9) are purchased, whole, at a daily auction, after which they are handled by an artisan butcher. The signature dishes are the beautifully marbled short ribs and ribeye grilled over charcoal. From a simple meal of cold buckwheat noodles and soup to an elaborate barbecue feast, Byeokje Galbi caters to all occasions.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking;[]
16917;Baek Nyun Ok;South Korea;Seoul;2407 Nambusunhwan-ro, Seocho-gu, Seoul, 06719, South Korea;37.48115;127.01374;85;false;false;Dubu;Located across the main road from Seoul Arts Center, Baek Nyun Ok has been attracting loyal patrons, including local performers and musicians in droves, since 1992. This humble institution specializes in fresh homemade bean curd, which is the central ingredient in a variety of dishes offered. These include plain soft bean curd and soft bean curd stew with nutty perilla seeds. The interior is simply decorated and offers both table and floor seating.;Air conditioning,Valet parking;[]
16918;Toc Toc;South Korea;Seoul;3F, 41 Hakdong-ro 97-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06072, South Korea;37.52237;127.05429;90;false;false;Contemporary;For Chef Kim Dae-cheon, the ingredients and precise techniques that summarize his cooking philosophy are summed up in one word: toconomy (Toc Toc + gastronomy). Signature dishes at Toc Toc and pasta with Chef Kim's original flair. In addition to the course meals, the restaurant also offers a wide range of well-executed à la carte dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Valet parking;[]
16919;Kushi Kawa;South Korea;Seoul;37 Nonhyeon-ro 24-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06300, South Korea;37.48268;127.04566;60;false;false;Kushiage;Owner Yoon Seok-hyeon's inspiration to open Kushikawa stems from his sojourn in Japan where he became a connoisseur of popular Japanese dishes including kushikatsu (deep-fried skewered meat and vegetables). The omakase course at Kushikawa consists of 12 to 14 different types of deep-fried skewers prepared with seafood, meat and vegetables. Running a restaurant on his home turf where he grew up, Yoon tries to appeal to the local palate, and nothing brings him greater joy than the joyful expressions on his customers' beaming faces.;Counter dining;[]
16920;Ichiryu;South Korea;Seoul;44 Jandari-ro 3 an-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul, 04043, South Korea;37.55061;126.91913;65;false;false;Barbecue;Meaning “first class” in Japanese, Ichiryu offers an authentic taste of a Sapporo-style grilled lamb dish prepared on a convex metal skillet. The restaurant, the first of its kind in Korea, only handles young Australian lamb under a year old, and uses skillets imported from Sapporo. The efficient chefs behind the counter make sure the meat is grilled to perfection. Counter seating makes for a casual and interactive dining experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16921;L'Essence;South Korea;Busan;3F, 17 Gwangnam-ro 22 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48307, South Korea;35.14399;129.11074;40;false;true;French;L'Essence is a French restaurant set in a quiet alley near Namcheon Station. Here, Chef Jeon Ji-seong combines seasonal local ingredients with vibrant sauces to present French cuisine offering an outstanding balance of taste and aroma. Sometimes, the chef uses fermented ingredients, such as pickled vegetables and salted seafood, to add verve to his dishes, providing diners with the fun of spotting Korean flavors hidden amidst his delicate French cuisine. Though L'Essence usually offers only an a la carte menu, customers can enjoy its multi-course meal with a reservation at least a day in advance.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16922;L'étang;South Korea;Busan;22 Seongji-ro, Busanjin-gu, Busan, 47123, South Korea;35.17255;129.05523;100;false;true;French;L'étang is a French bistro located on one of the main roads in Yeonji-dong. Here, the owner-chef Jung Dong-won does everything single-handedly, from preparing the ingredients to cooking and serving. By revamping its menu every season to reflect seasonal ingredients, L'étang incorporates the flavors of the season into its French cuisine characterized by adherence to culinary basics and traditions as well as fresh and mild flavors. Since the bar counter facing the kitchen features limited seating, reservations are recommended.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16923;Ramsey;South Korea;Busan;3F, 38 Gwanganhaebyeon-ro 284 beon-gil, Suyeong-gu, Busan, 48285, South Korea;35.15333;129.12528;62;true;false;French;Helmed by Chef Lee Gyu-jin, Ramsey pushes the boundaries of its classic French cuisine through inventive use of ingredients. Located in Millak-dong, the highly competitive dining battleground where eateries of diverse varieties keep popping up, this bistro is set apart from the pack with its alluring French fare. From the amuse-bouche, which combines diverse flavors to create culinary variations on a theme, to fantastic fish and meat dishes that highlight the chef’s seasoned cooking skills, Ramsey is well-versed in every element of a French course meal and focuses on fare that makes good use of sauce flavors. Come and enjoy a cozy meal at Ramsey accompanied by attentive and discreet service while relishing its inviting vibe to the fullest.;Air conditioning;[]
16924;Yakitori Haegong;South Korea;Busan;30-5 Millakbondong-ro 19 beon-gil, Suyoeng-gu, Busan, 48290, South Korea;35.15823;129.12712;90;false;false;Yakitori;In an alley of a quiet residential neighborhood is a pink building with an unexpected tiny little sign that reads “Haegong.” This Japanese eatery specializes in yakitori (grilled chicken skewers) made with native Korean chicken. As part of the relocation to its present location in October 2022, some upgrades were made to its space to ensure a more sophisticated dining experience. Grilled hagfish, another gem of this establishment, is not a dish to miss, with each mouthful piece brimming with juice, oceanic minerality, and delightfully firm texture. Yakitori Haegong is a rare gem in Busan to savor yakitori in a serene vibe accentuated by its refined interior décor.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
16927;La Popote;United Kingdom;Marton;Church Farm, Manchester Road, Marton, SK11 9HF, United Kingdom;53.2093291;-2.2257399;88;true;false;Classic French;A characterful converted barn with brick floors, exposed beams and linen cloths, which add a brasserie deluxe feel. The chef-owner spent several years working in Paris, and this is evident in the cooking, which incorporates classic French techniques while displaying a subtle modernity in its presentation. Service is friendly and assured.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16928;Lamb Inn;United Kingdom;Crawley;Steep Hill, Leafield Road, Crawley, OX29 9TW, United Kingdom;51.8061104;-1.5069854;42;false;false;Modern British;The hub of a pretty stone-built village, the Lamb Inn is a charming place with an open-fired bar and a quirky dining room complete with a suit of armour. Sebastian’s cooking reflects his personality and his classically based dishes have no boundaries apart from seasonality and natural flavours.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16929;Montagu's Mews;United Kingdom;Bath;16 Royal Crescent, Bath, BA1 2LS, United Kingdom;51.3872957;-2.3681617;62;true;false;Modern Cuisine;18C writer and women’s education advocate Elizabeth Montagu lends her name to this restaurant set inside the old carriage houses of her former home. The estate is now the Royal Crescent Hotel & Spa and an extensive garden separates the main hotel from the restaurant, making for a lovely early evening stroll in good weather. The menu showcases seasonal produce from the south west, such as Whaddon Grove Farm lamb, with the quality of the ingredients shining through in well-honed dishes.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16930;The Golden Ball;United Kingdom;Henley-on-Thames;Lower Assendon, Henley-on-Thames, RG9 6AH, United Kingdom;51.55753;-0.9289;91;true;false;Modern British;An endearing couple bring plenty of charm to this pretty, cream-washed former pub in the rural village of Lower Assendon. Priya provides a natural warmth in the friendly service, while Ben incorporates Priya's Indian heritage into his modern British dishes – such as cod accompanied by 'potato chaat', spiced cauliflower and tamarind sauce. A local, seasonal approach adds to the appeal too, with chicken and beef from the surrounding area featuring in cooking that is confidently executed and suitably satisfying.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16931;Bell;United Kingdom;Ramsbury;The Square, Ramsbury, SN8 2PE, United Kingdom;51.4427153;-1.6045754;69;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The charming 300 year old Bell is the hub of this lovely village. It’s split into four parts: a café, bar, restaurant and bedrooms. The short bar menu offers appealing pub favourites while the restaurant serves ambitious modern dishes. The surrounding estate provides much of the produce.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
16932;Inver;United Kingdom;Strachur;Strathlachlan, Strachur, PA27 8BU, United Kingdom;56.1056447;-5.2066967;18;true;false;Modern British;A former crofter’s cottage and boat store in a beautifully isolated spot on the shores of Loch Fyne. Sit on sheepskin-covered armchairs for a cocktail in the lounge-bar, then take in the view from the contemporary restaurant, where concise modern menus are led by the finest local and foraged ingredients. Luxurious bothy-style bedrooms in the grounds complete the picture.;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16933;The Abbey Inn;United Kingdom;Byland;Byland, YO61 4BD, United Kingdom;54.2034945;-1.1603484;78;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There is a simple, homely feel to this pub overlooking the ruins of Byland Abbey, courtesy of its flagstone floor, colourful throws and blazing fires in the winter. The comforting British cooking matches the seasons well, while providing crowd-pleasing menu mainstays like their signature 'Byland Burger'. The owners, who also run The Black Swan in nearby Oldstead, provide much of the superb produce from their own farm. Traditional bedrooms sit upstairs and, in the summer, the garden terrace makes a great spot for a pint.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16935;Lido Restaurant;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;Oakfield Place, City of Bristol, BS8 2BJ, United Kingdom;51.4597704;-2.6111844;51;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Snack on flatbreads and small plates in the poolside bar or head up to the first floor former viewing gallery of this restored Victorian lido, with its retractable floor-to-ceiling doors and daily changing menu. Spanish, Mediterranean and Moorish dishes make good use of the wood-fired oven.;Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
16936;Wilsons;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;24 Chandos Road, City of Bristol, BS6 6PF, United Kingdom;51.4679292;-2.6052331;59;true;false;Modern British;There is so much to enjoy, and so much to admire, when dining at Wilsons. It’s one of those appealing neighbourhood operations that works in pure harmony, with everyone from the chefs to the service team sharing the same ethos. Sustainability and careful sourcing of superb ingredients are at the forefront, with the restaurant’s own smallholding providing much of the produce on the tasting menu of expertly crafted dishes. Each one is exquisitely balanced and full of understated originality, like dry-aged trout with pickled mushrooms and sweet onion broth.;Credit cards not accepted;[]
16937;Shibden Mill Inn;United Kingdom;Halifax;Shibden Mill Fold, Halifax, HX3 7UL, United Kingdom;53.7414253;-1.8476016;87;false;false;Modern British;Tucked away on the floor of a steep, wooded valley, this former corn mill is full of rustic character, with cluttered, low-beamed rooms, open fires and cosy snugs. Monthly changing menus offer hearty, flavoursome dishes made with Yorkshire produce. The young team are organised and welcoming – and boutique bedrooms add to the appeal.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16938;Henry Robertson;United Kingdom;Llandderfel;Palé Estate, Llandderfel, LL23 7PS, United Kingdom;52.9129032;-3.5144635;47;false;true;Modern British;Set within an impressive Victorian hotel, this elegant restaurant is named after the industrialist-cum-MP the property was built for. Take in lovely views over the garden as you dine on one of two tasting menus, where attractively presented dishes reflect the seasons and keep the local larder to the fore.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list;[]
16939;Chalk;United Kingdom;Pulborough;North Farm, Washington, Pulborough, RH20 4BB, United Kingdom;50.8866409;-0.4097277;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Oak beams and brick walls abound in this former barn on the Wiston Estate winery, that now houses a smart restaurant. It’s named after the type of soil found in the area, which creates ideal growing conditions for the grapes and, as you would expect, you can accompany your meal with one of their own sparkling wines. The short, appealing menu changes with the seasons and offers fresh, straightforward flavours in harmonious combinations. Their generously sized house focaccia is a great way to start.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16940;Smoke & Salt;United Kingdom;London;115 Tooting High Street, Tooting, London, SW17 0SY, United Kingdom;51.4260557;-0.1698057;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This popular neighbourhood restaurant may have started life as a pop-up but it’s now a well-established member of the Tooting dining scene. Located on a High Street corner, it’s a fairly simple place in décor, but benefits from the energy emanating out of its open kitchen, friendly team and contented diners. Choose between two lengths of tasting menu based around seasonal British produce, which are also available in pescatarian, vegetarian or vegan forms. Sunday lunch consists of their more internationally influenced take on a roast dinner.;;[]
16942;Arbequina;United Kingdom;Oxford;72-74 Cowley Road, Oxford, OX4 1JB, United Kingdom;51.7488274;-1.2406398;57;false;false;Spanish;Simply furnished and with a bohemian feel to it, this tapas bar sits inside a former chemist’s and features a vintage stainless steel counter. A concise menu offers tasty, authentic and generously portioned small plates, plus a couple of larger ones if you really want filling up. Cocktails and natural wines are available from the bar and there’s a busy, relaxed atmosphere about the place.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16945;Augustus;United Kingdom;Taunton;3 The Courtyard, St. James Street, Taunton, TA1 1JR, United Kingdom;51.017158;-3.1024135;83;true;false;Modern British;An experienced chef and a bright, breezy team run this welcoming little bistro. Sit in the cosy, intimate dining room or the bright conservatory with sliding glass doors and a retractable roof. Hearty, unfussy cooking mixes French-influenced dishes with updated British classics.;Terrace;[]
16946;Porthminster Beach Café;United Kingdom;St Ives;Porthminster Beach, St Ives, TR26 2EB, United Kingdom;50.2081531;-5.4755479;28;true;false;Seafood;A charming 1930s beach house in a superb location overlooking Porthminster Sands, there are few seaside settings finer than this one. There's a bright, New England style to the restaurant, which unsurprisingly specialises in seafood. Fresh produce, from mussels and crab to squid and scallops, populates dishes that are enlivened by a range of global influences. A mixture of Asian elements, like Indonesian curry or satay sauce, are particularly prevalent – but there's still room for classic European dishes like moules marinière and seafood linguine.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16947;Coombeshead Farm;United Kingdom;Lewannick;Lewannick, PL15 7QQ, United Kingdom;50.5945366;-4.4297684;84;true;true;Country cooking;Set on a working farm, in 66 acres of meadows and woodland, this former farmhouse and dairy offers the ultimate field to fork experience. Techniques include curing, pickling and cooking over wooden embers, and the home-bred Middle White pork and home-baked sourdough are hits. They serve a set three course menu at all times, which changes seasonally depending on which quality ingredients are available. Bedrooms have a cosy farmhouse style.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
16950;The Fox;United Kingdom;Willian;Letchworth Garden City, Willian, SG6 2AE, United Kingdom;51.9611066;-0.2199293;27;true;true;Modern British;The Fox sits in the heart of the village and is a pleasingly unpretentious place. Concise monthly menus deliver a range of neatly presented, adventurous dishes with bold flavours and interesting texture contrasts. Service is sweet and friendly, and contemporary country bedrooms await.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16952;Hatched;United Kingdom;London;189 St John's Hill, Wandsworth, London, SW11 1TH, United Kingdom;51.459903;-0.178151;37;true;false;Modern British;The large open kitchen is the focus of this relaxed, simply styled neighbourhood restaurant. Behind the counter is Chef-Owner Shane Marshall, who runs the place with generosity and genuine warmth. His cooking is founded on quality ingredients and features an eclectic mix of influences from around the world, in dishes of both a classic and modern bent. If you're one for puddings, then the pain perdu is an absolute treat.;;[]
16953;Hartnett Holder & Co;United Kingdom;Lyndhurst;Beaulieu Road, Lyndhurst, SO43 7FZ, United Kingdom;50.8624137;-1.5547923;15;false;false;Italian;Lime Wood Hotel, an impressive light stone mansion in the heart of the New Forest, is the home for this lovely restaurant which looks out onto the property's extensive gardens. Take a seat in the glass-roofed bar and kick things off with a cocktail from their extensive list. The rustic cooking leans heavily into the ingredient-led ethos of Italian cuisine, with both Angela Harnett and Luke Holder (who is more often the one in the kitchen) bringing their considerable experience to proceedings.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16954;Bombay Bustle;United Kingdom;London;29 Maddox Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 2PA, United Kingdom;51.5129211;-0.142129;67;true;false;Indian;A charming train theme runs through this Indian restaurant, where the ground floor is the livelier area and downstairs is more ‘first class’. Mumbai is known for its chaat so – before a prawn curry, chicken biryani or succulent lamb chops from the tandoor – order some to share, like their wonderfully crisp and colourful Raj Kachori. And they make a fine rice pudding for dessert.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16955;Kentish Hare;United Kingdom;Bidborough;95 Bidborough Ridge, Royal Tunbridge Wells, Bidborough, TN3 0XB, United Kingdom;51.1694825;0.236476;40;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Behind the clapboard façade sits a spacious bar with bookshelf wallpaper and a modern extension where you can watch the chefs cooking steaks on two Big Green Eggs. Care is taken both in sourcing and cooking, and dishes are boldly flavoured and well-presented. Simpler dishes are available on the bar menu.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16956;Greene Oak;United Kingdom;Windsor;Oakley Green, Windsor, SL4 5UW, United Kingdom;51.4798929;-0.6633358;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Greene Oak’s modern bar has a pleasingly laid-back feel and the quirky horsebox tables on the terrace add something a little different. Menus use the best of the British larder and offer an appealing mix of dishes. The 45-day aged rare breed steaks are a speciality and the weekday lunch menu is a steal.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
16957;Sumas;United Kingdom;Gorey;Gorey Hill, Gorey, JE3 6ET, United Kingdom;49.1998338;-2.0218966;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A well-known restaurant in a whitewashed house, with a smart heated terrace affording lovely harbour views. Modern European dishes feature island produce. The monthly changing lunch and midweek dinner menus represent good value.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
16959;Brasserie Zédel;United Kingdom;London;20 Sherwood Street, Soho, London, W1F 7ED, United Kingdom;51.5106156;-0.1356086;91;true;false;French;With all its art deco flourishes and distinctively French glamour, Zédel is a restaurant that still delivers a certain expectant excitement as you descend the stairs towards the grand basement brasserie. Expect a roll-call of classic French dishes on the extensive menu, from snails to coq au vin, duck confit to profiteroles. It’s a permanently bustling place with live music and plenty of atmosphere, plus both a cocktail bar and cabaret venue attached.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
16960;Chesil Rectory;United Kingdom;Winchester;1 Chesil Street, Winchester, SO23 0HU, United Kingdom;51.0608063;-1.3071135;90;true;true;British Contemporary;This double-gabled wattle and daub house dates from the 15C and its hugely characterful interior takes in heavy beams and a large inglenook fireplace. Classically based dishes are informed by local, seasonal produce and given a modern twist by the experienced team. Service is friendly.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16961;Punch Bowl Inn;United Kingdom;Crosthwaite;Crosthwaite, LA8 8HR, United Kingdom;54.3133193;-2.8529613;85;false;true;Modern British;The picturesque Lyth Valley plays host to this charming 17C inn, which stands beside a pretty church. Sit over a pint of local beer and some homemade pork scratchings in the cosy beamed bar or dine on carefully cooked modern dishes of regional produce. Bedrooms are luxurious – one even has twin baths!;Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
16962;Seahorse;United Kingdom;Dartmouth;5 South Embankment, Dartmouth, TQ6 9BH, United Kingdom;50.350816;-3.5776442;90;false;true;Seafood;You instantly feel at ease at this elegant bistro in a prime position overlooking the Dart Estuary. Food-themed art and framed former menus exude a sense of the passion poured into this long-standing, family-run spot, where the original owner's son is now cooking. The daily changing menu is a celebration of both local seafood and Italian cooking, with the day's catch used to power classic dishes like 'spaghetti alla vongole', plus whole fish cooked in the charcoal oven. Start with a cocktail in the lovely Joe’s Bar.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16963;Durham Ox;United Kingdom;Crayke;Westway, Crayke, YO61 4TE, United Kingdom;54.1273962;-1.1420157;72;false;false;Traditional British;For over 300 years this charming pub has stood in a sleepy Yorkshire hamlet. It's a loveable, eclectically decorated place with a thoroughly welcoming feel that extends to the cosy bedrooms. As at any good inn, the fire is roaring in the winter and a lovely courtyard is available for warmer days. The cooking echoes the surroundings in its comforting heartiness, with full-flavoured and uncomplicated dishes spread across an extensive menu and plenty of seasonal specials. Steak and seafood platters are ideal for celebrations.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
16964;Adam Reid at The French;United Kingdom;Manchester;Midland Hotel, 16 Peter Street, Manchester, M60 2DS, United Kingdom;53.4774829;-2.2449364;27;true;true;Modern British;This famous hotel was first built to herald the arrival of the Midland Railway in Manchester, and its current restaurant has been created in the Belle Époque style to evoke the luxury of the day. Whilst its name remains in reference to its historical past, today, Chef Adam Reid's multi-course menu is very much a homage to his northern roots, with the menu split into sections such as ‘A Warm Northern Welcome’, 'Yesterday's Dinner' and ‘Today's Tea'. Personable chefs explain and finish each course off tableside, and dishes are richly flavoured with the occasional playful touch.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16965;Bell Inn;United Kingdom;Langford;Langford, GL7 3LF, United Kingdom;51.7223258;-1.6408646;49;true;false;Traditional British;Looking every inch the quintessential Cotswolds pub, The Bell Inn’s rustic charm is hard to resist with its cosy bar, impressive inglenook fireplace, stone walls and 16th-century origins. The appealing menu offers a mix of pub favourites – from a half pint of prawns to a choice of steaks – as well as restaurant-style dishes and homemade pizzas, which are all brought to the table by a friendly team. Nicely furnished bedrooms complete the picture.;Terrace;[]
16966;Whitstable Oyster Company;United Kingdom;Whitstable;Royal Native Oyster Stores, Horsebridge, Whitstable, CT5 1BU, United Kingdom;51.3608685;1.0232621;49;true;false;Seafood;This lovely old oyster warehouse has a wonderfully rustic style and comes with a large terrace and a tremendous view towards the estuary. The menu changes daily depending on the latest catch. Take your pick from the fresh fish counter – the oysters from the restaurant’s beds just outside are a must-try.;Great view,Terrace;[]
16969;Chubby Castor;United Kingdom;Castor;Fitzwilliam Arms, 34 Peterborough Road, Castor, PE5 7AX, United Kingdom;52.5725542;-0.3440395;32;false;false;Modern British;Having spent most of his life in London, Adebola Adeshina found a new home in this 400 year old thatched pub. Inside it’s surprisingly modern, with a smart lounge and an intimate linen-laid dining room. Time-honoured recipes are reworked, with flavourful dishes presented in a restrained modern vein.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16970;Cat Inn;United Kingdom;West Hoathly;North Lane, West Hoathly, RH19 4PP, United Kingdom;51.0766642;-0.055458;68;false;false;Traditional British;Popular with the locals and very much a village pub, with beamed ceilings, pewter tankards, open fires and plenty of cosy corners. Good value cooking focuses on tasty pub classics like locally smoked ham, egg and chips or steak, mushroom and ale pie. Service is friendly and efficient – and four tastefully decorated bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16971;Mortimers;United Kingdom;Ludlow;17 Corve Street, Ludlow, SY8 1DA, United Kingdom;52.370774;-2.719248;90;true;false;Modern British;A local forest gives this 16C townhouse restaurant its name. It has plenty of character, courtesy of exposed stone, sloping floors and lovely wood panelling. Concise set menus offer classically rooted dishes with a personal touch. Make sure you have a dessert – the cherry Bakewell tart is delicious!;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16972;Pilchards;United Kingdom;Port Gaverne;Port Gaverne, PL29 3SQ, United Kingdom;50.592651;-4.8227316;33;true;false;Seafood, Asian Influences;Park in Port Isaac and walk over to this modern timber and glass building with a large, wood-decked terrace, which overlooks the stunning cove where the famous Cornish pilchards were once landed. The menu offers sharing plates crafted from wonderfully fresh local seafood, with whole fish grilled over charcoal a speciality. The chefs show impressive judgement in incorporating a range of bold Asian flavours – mussels with Thai green curry, cured trout with wasabi buttermilk – without overwhelming the purity of the produce.This restaurant is temporarily closed for the winter.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16973;Where The Light Gets In;United Kingdom;Stockport;7 Rostron Brow, Stockport, SK1 7JY, United Kingdom;53.4109402;-2.1559164;83;true;false;Modern British;This large, loft-style restaurant is located on the top floor of a Victorian coffee warehouse and its open kitchen forms part of the room. The surprise menu is based on seasonal British produce and often incorporates foraged ingredients from the kitchen team. Adding to the sustainable approach, the whole ingredient is utilised by the kitchen, meaning nothing goes to waste and a range of pickles and ferments are incorporated into the dishes. The matching wine flights focus on natural options.This restaurant is currently operating from central Manchester, while its Stockport premises undergoes refurbishment.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16974;The Elderflower;United Kingdom;Lymington;4-5 Quay Street, Lymington, SO41 3AS, United Kingdom;50.7591258;-1.5372652;79;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Down a cobbled street in a beautiful Georgian town, you'll find a Grade II listed building housing this amiably run restaurant. The chef's experience shines through in the attractively presented dishes on the multi-course tasting menu, which shine thanks to the sourcing of excellent ingredients. As it's by the quayside, you can expect the catch of the day to be among the highlights. As an alternative to the tasting option, a 'sharing menu' offers dishes for two such as beef Chateaubriand and trout en croûte.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16975;The Set;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;50 Preston Road, Brighton and Hove, BN1 4QF, United Kingdom;50.8348606;-0.140615;46;false;false;Modern Cuisine;An intimate and rustic spot, this bistro-style restaurant has only seven tables and offers a pleasingly personable dining experience. Everyone is served together at 7pm so be sure to arrive on time for the multi-course tasting menu that features small plates with an Asian influence. The cooking has a creative element and dishes deliver well-defined flavours.;;[]
16976;Bunch of Grapes;United Kingdom;Bradford-on-Avon;14 Silver Street, Bradford-on-Avon, BA15 1JY, United Kingdom;51.3481363;-2.2492006;93;false;true;Modern British;The Bunch of Grapes might be the oldest pub in this historic town but it now comes with an appealing modern edge and a deli selling tempting treats. Downstairs has a pubby feel, while upstairs has more of a restaurant vibe, and you can have anything from a burger to an ambitious tasting menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
16977;Wilder;United Kingdom;Nailsworth;Market Street, Nailsworth, GL6 0BX, United Kingdom;51.6940714;-2.218966;60;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Everyone is asked to arrive at this well-run restaurant at 7pm – and that usually includes a loyal band of locals. The 3-hour menu takes on a surprise tasting format and there’s the option of matching wines or non-alcoholic options. Humble ingredients are used in ambitious, sometimes rather unusual combinations, which are precisely prepared. Service is structured and passionate, with dishes delivered by the chefs themselves.;;[]
16978;The Bower House;United Kingdom;Shipston-on-Stour;2-4 Market Place, Shipston-on-Stour, CV36 4AG, United Kingdom;52.0632441;-1.6248154;64;true;false;Modern British;An appealing mixture of the vintage and the contemporary lend a certain stylishness to the décor at this smart brasserie occupying two former shops in the heart of a small market town. The attractive dishes are packed with flavour and make the most of quality British produce, as with delicious, sweet Cornish crab turned into a simple, fresh-tasting tartlet. Sit in the larger room with its comfy banquettes and copper-topped tables, then treat yourself to a stay in one of the characterful bedrooms.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
16979;Anchor & Hope;United Kingdom;London;36 The Cut, Southwark, London, SE1 8LP, United Kingdom;51.5034152;-0.1066414;85;false;true;British Contemporary;There's a rustic, shabby-chic feel to this long-standing and ever-busy pub located conveniently close to The Young Vic Theatre. It's an appropriate setting for the hearty cooking informed by quality British produce, be it a generous portion of roasted beetroot with feta or suitably flavoursome ox tongue with lentils. Combine this with a lively atmosphere and relaxed yet well-drilled service, and you have all you need in a pub. If you're dining as a pair, look out for the cassoulet to share.;Terrace;[]
16980;The Seaside Boarding House;United Kingdom;Burton Bradstock;Cliff Road, Burton Bradstock, DT6 4RB, United Kingdom;50.6972786;-2.7240251;22;true;false;Traditional British;With its stunning clifftop location and menu packed full of delicious seafood, this bright and airy restaurant really makes the most of its seaside setting. It's housed within a long-standing yet fresh-looking hotel, while the restaurant itself sports a subtle maritime theme and the lovely terrace offers fabulous sea views. The cooking has a seafood bias, with dishes like whole roasted brill wisely spotlighting the top-notch produce.;Car park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16983;Chequers;United Kingdom;Churchill;Church Road, Churchill, OX7 6NJ, United Kingdom;51.9149356;-1.5906628;51;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;This welcoming Cotswold stone pub sits in the heart of the village and plays a vital role in the local community. The bar is stocked with local ales, the cooking is traditional, and flagstone floors and wooden beams give it plenty of character.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16984;Cassons;United Kingdom;Tangmere;Arundel Road, Tangmere, PO18 0DU, United Kingdom;50.8548174;-0.7180152;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Passionately run restaurant with exposed brick, wooden beams and a rustic feel. Boldly flavoured dishes are generously proportioned. Cooking is classically based but employs modern techniques. The regular gourmet evenings are a hit.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
16986;Leaping Hare;United Kingdom;Stanton;Wyken Vineyards, Stanton, IP31 2DW, United Kingdom;52.3078742;0.8810125;35;true;true;Modern British;When the weather’s right, make a beeline for the lovely terrace of this beautiful 17th-century barn, which sits in a charming spot at the centre of a seven-acre vineyard, where there’s nothing but nature as far as the eye can see. Classically based cooking relies on well-sourced seasonal ingredients – many of which come from their own farm – and dishes are brought to the table by a charming team. The wine list includes a strong selection of classics and, of course, their own vintages too – plus the shop houses a plethora of goodies to take home.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16987;Fox & Hounds;United Kingdom;Hunsdon;2 High Street, Hunsdon, SG12 8NH, United Kingdom;51.8071513;0.0535055;84;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;There's a pleasantly rustic feel to this welcoming high street pub sporting low beams and wooden furnishings. Classical dishes form the basis of the extensive menu, with tried-and-tested combinations like asparagus with hollandaise sauce proving a success. There's also a Mediterranean influence to the hearty cooking, plus the option of rare breed beef cooked over the Josper grill.;Brunch,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
16988;Tolcarne Inn;United Kingdom;Newlyn;Tolcarne Terrace, Newlyn, TR18 5PR, United Kingdom;50.1070236;-5.5484824;56;false;false;Seafood;18th century beams and a wood-burning stove contribute towards the cosy atmosphere at this unassuming pub set beside the sea wall in the heart of Newlyn. As its location would suggest, the menu is centred around fresh fish and shellfish, much of which is landed at the adjacent harbour. The appealing menu uses lots of tried-and-tested combinations and includes dishes like hake with tartare crushed ‘Cornish earlies’ potatoes.;Terrace;[]
16989;The Petersham;United Kingdom;London;2 Floral Court, Covent Garden, London, WC2E 9FB, United Kingdom;51.5117622;-0.1250904;92;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Nestled in the 'Floral Court' section of Covent Garden is this elegant restaurant adorned with fresh flowers and Murano glass. It comes from the same stable as Petersham Nurseries Café and uses produce from their Richmond nursery as well as their Devon farm. The Italian-based dishes, like vegetables pinzimonio, show off the ingredients beautifully. The lovely terrace is shared with La Goccia, their more informal spot for sharing plates, and they also have a neighbouring wine bar and deli. From Thursday to Sunday, their afternoon teas become something of an event.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
16991;Fischer's;United Kingdom;London;50 Marylebone High Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 5HN, United Kingdom;51.5216158;-0.1516614;71;false;false;Austrian;The spirit of old Vienna is alive and well at this Austrian café and konditorei that comes from the same stable as The Wolseley and Brasserie Zédel, meaning it’s a slick and well-run sort of place. It’s perennially packed too, whether people are coming in for eggs and viennoiserie at brunch or cake in the afternoon. At lunch and dinner, the menu is a roll-call of Central European favourites, including a selection of sausages and some cracking schnitzels that are well worth getting with the Holstein garnish.;Air conditioning;[]
16992;Clipstone;United Kingdom;London;5 Clipstone Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1W 6BB, United Kingdom;51.5208608;-0.1422029;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Sister to fellow neighbourhood spots Portland and 64 Goodge Street, this well-run restaurant provides a great all-round package. The young team are full of smiles, the wine list is cleverly conceived and there’s a pleasing buzz to the atmosphere. The cooking, for its part, showcases quality ingredients and an original touch in somewhat delicate dishes.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16994;The Old Bank;United Kingdom;Snettisham;10 Lynn Road, Snettisham, PE31 7LP, United Kingdom;52.8790397;0.5028772;27;false;false;Modern British;A welcoming couple run this intimate, laid-back restaurant: Aga works out front, assisted by a friendly serving team, while Lewis works alone in the kitchen. His well-balanced tasting menu comes in two forms – ‘Shorter’ and ‘Longer’ – and sees produce from their allotment and the surrounding area kept to the fore in the sophisticated, modern dishes. The passionately described wine pairings are the way to go.;Terrace;[]
16995;Arras;United Kingdom;York;The Old Coach House, Peasholme Green, York, YO1 7PW, United Kingdom;53.9605767;-1.0754505;48;false;false;Modern Cuisine;On the edge of York’s buzzing centre, you’ll find this brick-built former coaching house. Inside, the compact dining room is bright and airy thanks to a large skylight, while the white-and-blue décor lends a Mediterranean feel. In the summer, head for the lovely enclosed terrace overlooking the well-kept gardens. The cooking is guided by the seasons and comes with inventive touches and combinations. Cheese-lovers should save room for the excellent British selection presented on a handmade oak trolley.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
16998;The Vineyard;United Kingdom;Newbury;Stockcross, Newbury, RG20 8JU, United Kingdom;51.4131333;-1.3659917;92;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Stunning original artwork from the owner’s private collection hangs on the walls of this smart hotel restaurant. Elegantly presented dishes are elevated by the skilful preparation of good quality ingredients, and they offer over 50 wines by the glass – some from their own Californian vineyard. The main restaurant serves an à la carte of classically based dishes, while The Tasting Room offers a seasonal tasting menu with wine pairings.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
17000;The Longs Arms;United Kingdom;South Wraxall;South Wraxall, BA15 2SB, United Kingdom;51.3819561;-2.2428463;58;true;false;Traditional British;It’s hard not to like this handsome Bath stone pub, set opposite a medieval church in a sleepy village. It’s a family run affair with the chef-owner proudly preparing a mix of pub classics and few more modern creations. Be sure to try the home-smoked meats and fish and the delicious homemade ice creams.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17002;Stanley's;United Kingdom;London;151 Sydney Street, Chelsea, London, SW3 6NT, United Kingdom;51.4876316;-0.1692674;76;true;true;Modern British;In the very heart of Chelsea, the hidden-away Stanley's feels like a perfect fit for the neighbourhood. Plenty of regulars are among the diners seated in either a sheltered, flower-festooned courtyard or inside a lean-to glasshouse. Vibrantly colourful dishes are overtly seasonal and deliver bags of pure, unadulterated flavour thanks to great ingredients – from leeks to pork chops – which are allowed to shine by the chef's understated compositions. When the sun comes out, there's few places better for lunch on a summer's day.;Terrace;[]
17003;Nathan Marshall Clarke House;United Kingdom;Liss;Clarke House, Farnham Road, Liss, GU33 6JQ, United Kingdom;51.05025;-0.9010549;80;true;false;Modern British;From the façade, you wouldn’t guess this was once a courthouse, but inside you’ll find a door leading to what was the judge’s bench. It’s a tiny place with exposed beams and a rustic style and is keenly run by a young couple. Cooking sees a little intricacy added to well-presented, country house style dishes.;Car park;[]
17004;1863;United Kingdom;Pooley Bridge;Elm House, High Street, Pooley Bridge, CA10 2NH, United Kingdom;54.612515;-2.8177455;64;true;true;Modern British;This immaculately kept bistro is set in the heart of a pretty Lake District village and its name is a reference to the year the property was first built as the local blacksmith’s. Menus showcase seasonal local ingredients in well-executed, modern British dishes. Convivial service and seven comfortable bedrooms further add to the appeal.;Air conditioning;[]
17005;Lima;United Kingdom;London;31 Rathbone Place, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 1JH, United Kingdom;51.517793;-0.1344242;53;true;false;Peruvian;Lima is one of those restaurants that just makes you feel good about life – and that’s even without the pisco sours. The Peruvian food at this informal, fun place is the ideal antidote to times of austerity: it’s full of punchy, invigorating flavours and fantastically vivid colours.;Air conditioning;[]
17006;Purslane;United Kingdom;Cheltenham;16 Rodney Road, Cheltenham, GL50 1JJ, United Kingdom;51.8991341;-2.0738811;79;true;true;Modern British;Located just off the main high street, this modern restaurant has a comforting neighbourhood feel – and the service is equally relaxed. Fresh seafood from Cornwall and Scotland is combined with good quality locally sourced ingredients to produce interesting, original dishes with effective contrasts of flavour and texture. The lunch menu represents great value.;;[]
17008;Harborne Kitchen;United Kingdom;Birmingham;175-179 High Street, Birmingham, B17 9QE, United Kingdom;52.4586015;-1.9497716;95;true;false;Modern British;Deservedly loved by local diners, this contemporary neighbourhood restaurant is a pleasure to dine in. The attentive team run the place with such passion and the cooking shows the kitchen's ambition across a choice of menus. A tiled bull on the wall is a nod to the building's past as a butcher's shop, with an open kitchen now providing the room's focal point. Desserts are a real highlight, such as a clever, rich creation centred around 20-year-old Pedro Ximénez sherry.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17009;Chiltern Firehouse;United Kingdom;London;1 Chiltern Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 7PA, United Kingdom;51.5187592;-0.1548913;42;false;true;World Cuisine;It’s easy to be cynical about celebrity-driven restaurants but this one has substance. The atmosphere remains glamorous and contagiously fun and it’s all run with understated efficiency. The menu focuses on North and South American dishes that are strong on flavour, with the grill used to good effect.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17010;Prévost @ Haycock Manor;United Kingdom;Wansford;Haycock Manor, London Road, Wansford, PE8 6JA, United Kingdom;52.5787333;-0.4139616;73;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Set in the orangery of the Haycock Manor Hotel, a lovingly restored former coaching inn, this bright, colourful restaurant sports bird cage chandeliers, pergolas and a faux olive tree. Choose from three set menus of up to 8 courses, which demonstrate the precision of the chefs and a keen understanding of their quality ingredients. Natural flavours are allowed to shine and the sauces and consommés are a real highlight, like a rich, appetisingly glossy duck jus.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17012;The Brewers;United Kingdom;Rattlesden;Lower Road, Rattlesden, IP30 0RJ, United Kingdom;52.1931449;0.8926686;66;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A sympathetic refurbishment has left this village pub with a contemporary look but still plenty of rustic character. It was rescued by the locals and you’ll always find a group of regulars and their dogs by the fire. Pub favourites sit alongside more modern dishes and are cooked with confidence and ambition.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17015;MJP@ The Shepherds;United Kingdom;Fen Ditton;5 High Street, Fen Ditton, CB5 8ST, United Kingdom;52.2203781;0.1722092;82;false;true;Modern British;MJP refers to Chef Mark Poynton, while The Shepherds is a historic village pub that now provides a platform for the former's cooking. Housed inside a 16th-century building, it's a cosy, intimate space with a rustic touch to the décor. Mark and his brigade offer dishes that shine at their simplest, like quality sirloin served with a glossy jus and creamed potatoes. Choose between a tasting menu and an à la carte, where the dishes are available in small or large portions. Modern bedrooms are simply furnished.;Car park;[]
17016;COOK HOUSE;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;Foundry Lane Studios, Foundry Lane, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE6 1LH, United Kingdom;54.9747309;-1.590495;34;true;false;Modern British;After opening a shipping container café, local food blogger Anna Hedworth crowdfunded this stripped-back, industrial-style restaurant with a pleasant terrace and a relaxed feel. Dinner is the main event, with many of the vibrant, fiercely seasonal dishes cooked on the hibachi barbeque.;Brunch,Terrace;[]
17018;Alford Arms;United Kingdom;Frithsden;Frithsden, HP1 3DD, United Kingdom;51.7778158;-0.5276102;52;true;true;Traditional British;An attractive Victorian pub beside the village green. The menu follows the seasons and offers a broad array of dishes, so alongside British classics you’ll find dishes with more global leanings such as imam bayildi.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17019;Beach House;Ireland;Tramore;Turkey Road, Tramore, X91 Y521, Ireland;52.1603624;-7.1501375;88;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Close to the beach in a small seaside town is this double-fronted Victorian residence looking out over a lovely garden – and in the basement, its owners lovingly run this sweet bistro. The concise menu of classic, flavour-packed dishes favours seafood and the cellar wine list has some interesting vintages.;Garden or park;[]
17020;Bistro at The Boathouse;United Kingdom;Henley-on-Thames;Station Road, Henley-on-Thames, RG9 1AZ, United Kingdom;51.5354548;-0.900022;26;true;false;Modern British;Take in delightful Thames views through the floor-to-ceiling windows or from the lovely decked terrace complete with heated pods. Unfussy dishes are skilfully prepared and see the likes of soft shell crab rubbing shoulders with steak and chips.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17021;Adelina Yard;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;3 Queen Quay, Welsh Back, City of Bristol, BS1 4SL, United Kingdom;51.4505116;-2.592579;15;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The experienced chef-owners named their first restaurant after their old home. Sit at the chef's table to watch all the action or at the far end of the L-shaped room overlooking the quay. Attractively presented, well-balanced modern dishes are sometimes brought to the tables by the chefs themselves.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17022;Wildebeest;United Kingdom;Stoke Holy Cross;82 - 86 Norwich Road, Stoke Holy Cross, NR14 8QJ, United Kingdom;52.5689339;1.2966302;31;false;true;Modern British;Set in the heart of a pretty village and fronted by an attractive terrace, this former pub is now a laid-back restaurant offering satisfying modern cooking at a wallet-friendly price. The menus range from a particularly great value daily selection to an ambitious à la carte and an inventive tasting menu, all exhibiting the kitchen's skilled control of flavour and balance. Dishes like chicken liver parfait and dulche de leche cheesecake might sound straightforward, but they're executed with such aplomb. The friendly service team are eager to please.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17023;The Mariners;United Kingdom;Rock;Slipway, Rock, PL27 6LD, United Kingdom;50.5439047;-4.9192097;23;true;true;Traditional British;Part of the Paul Ainsworth stable, this large and popular pub is the ideal spot for some hearty British food while on your seaside holiday. You can arrive in the picturesque village of Rock via the ferry from Padstow, before grabbing a seat on the terrace which boasts stunning views over the Camel Estuary. The extensive menu is chock full of Cornish produce – be it cheddar, monkfish or mussels – with a seasonal menu sitting alongside 'Mariners Classics' such as shepherd's pie and fish & chips. For dessert, you can't go wrong with a crumble.;Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17024;Rising Sun Inn;United Kingdom;Altarnun;Altarnun, PL15 7SN, United Kingdom;50.6146777;-4.5228879;94;true;false;Modern British;This stone-built, 18C moorland pub boasts a cosy, characterful bar and a charming restaurant with exposed stone walls, a semi-open kitchen and local artwork on the walls. The original, highly seasonal British dishes make use of fine local ingredients, and the set lunch is a steal. It’s rurally set, so book a pitch on their campsite opposite and make a night of it.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17025;Y Polyn;United Kingdom;Capel Dewi;Capel Dewi, SA32 7LH, United Kingdom;51.8555537;-4.1871909;62;false;true;Traditional British;This well-regarded country pub sits on an old drovers’ road and is run by an experienced team. Sit downstairs and admire the tin tiles on the ceiling while supping a locally brewed ale, before tucking into unpretentious dishes like fish soup and crispy belly pork. Confidently prepared local ingredients feature heavily, and the cooking is both hearty and wholly satisfying.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17026;Hammer & Pincers;United Kingdom;Wymeswold;5 East Road, Wymeswold, LE12 6ST, United Kingdom;52.8061081;-1.10463;94;true;true;Modern British;The old water pump out the back hints at its days as the village forge but this is now a brightly decorated, intimate restaurant run with natural warmth by its experienced owners. Fixed price menus offer creative modern dishes overflowing with different textures and tastes. Boutique bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17027;Counter 71;United Kingdom;London;71 Nile Street, Shoreditch, London, N1 7RD, United Kingdom;51.5294563;-0.0879065;88;true;true;Modern Cuisine;What was once a well-known local boozer is now a swish dining experience complete with a tasting menu and a Spanish marble counter. Dinner is served to all guests at 7.15pm, so be sure to arrive on time or you’ll miss out on the boldly flavoured, modern British cooking. Cornish seafood and Lancashire Goosnargh duck are among the top quality ingredients on offer, and are brought to life using mostly classic combinations. The bar stays open late, so a post-dinner cocktail is always on the cards.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17028;The Silver Cup;United Kingdom;Harpenden;5 St Albans Road, Harpenden, AL5 2JF, United Kingdom;51.8116961;-0.3541026;52;false;false;Modern British;Dating all the way back to 1838, this Victorian pub is these days under the stewardship of siblings and Harpenden locals Matthew and Olivia. British racing green banquettes, leaded windows and a copper-topped bar give the place a comforting, traditional feel, while experienced chef Matthew is in the kitchen producing assured modern British dishes based around bold flavours. Choose the tasting menu to sample the full range of the cooking, or bring some friends and go for the sharing menu. Sunday lunch is something of an event.;Terrace;[]
17030;Fernery;United Kingdom;Narberth;Molleston, Narberth, SA67 8BX, United Kingdom;51.7827532;-4.7654287;39;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set inside The Grove, one of the finest country house hotels in Wales, the Fernery is a nature-inspired restaurant that brings the outside in. It’s a proudly Welsh place, with a tasting menu (available in 5 or 8 courses) that showcases the best produce the locale has to offer, including ingredients from their own gardens. Dishes come with incredible levels of detail that belie the understated, somewhat cryptic menu descriptions like “The King’s Estate”. Finesse and originality run throughout, while the superb service ensures your experience unfolds flawlessly.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17032;Bell at Skenfrith;United Kingdom;Skenfrith;Skenfrith, NP7 8UH, United Kingdom;51.8776984;-2.7888129;100;true;true;Classic Cuisine;The verdant valleys of the Welsh-English border are the setting for this well-run 17th-century coaching inn. The menu sticks to hearty, accessible and classically based dishes such as Welsh beef with dauphinoise potatoes and brandy peppercorn sauce. Ingredients from the organic kitchen garden are also likely to make an appearance. Warm, unobtrusive service and an impressive choice of vintage Cognacs add to the appeal, while the super-comfortable bedrooms have an understated elegance.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17033;Halfway at Kineton;United Kingdom;Kineton;Kineton, GL54 5UG, United Kingdom;51.93932;-1.85919;26;true;true;Traditional British;In a tranquil Gloucestershire village sits this 17th-century mellow stone inn, which offers a warm welcome and plenty of rustic charm, from its fireplace to its exposed timber. The appealing menu of hearty, well-cooked dishes is likely to include pies, fish & chips and a choice of locally reared steaks from the grill – plus a roast on Sundays. For desserts, expect modernised versions of classic recipes like steamed puddings and crumbles. Cosy bedrooms are also available if you want to explore the area.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17034;Scorrybreac;United Kingdom;Isle of Skye;7 Bosville Terrace, Portree, Isle of Skye, IV51 9DG, United Kingdom;57.4130271;-6.1912013;81;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The rugged, rural beauty of the Isle of Skye is a wonderful accompaniment to any meal – and so it is at this sharing plates operation named after the chef's parents' house, where he ran is first pop-up. 'Scorrybreac' also means 'speckled rock', something you can glimpse on the mountains in the distance. The restaurant itself is a small and simply furnished place, with chatty and charming service adding to its appeal. The creative modern cooking makes use of the Skye larder, including meats from the hills and seafood from the harbour below.;;[]
17035;Parva Farmhouse;United Kingdom;Tintern;Riverside, Tintern, NP16 6SQ, United Kingdom;51.7038907;-2.67982;85;true;false;Modern British;This 17C stone farmhouse sits on a bank of the River Wye and is run by a friendly couple. Its simple, rustic interior comprises a spacious lounge and a cosy, welcoming restaurant with an inglenook fireplace. The gutsy, modern British cooking has a classic French backbone and the odd Italian or Asian touch. Booking is essential and the menu is sent a day in advance for pre-ordering. Bedrooms are comfortable and some have river views.;;[]
17037;The Cotley Inn;United Kingdom;Wambrook;Wambrook, TA20 3EN, United Kingdom;50.8643;-3.00145;83;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Despite being just a 10 minute drive from the centre of Chard, there’s a wonderfully rural feeling that accompanies a visit to this former 17C farmhouse. The inn is nestled in a lush green valley overlooking the Blackdown Hills, with its converted outbuildings turned into bedrooms. The cooking offers dashes of creativity while still delivering satisfying pub dishes like slow-roasted pork belly. They take a local, seasonal and nose-to-tail approach to their ingredients, with animals reared on site and produce grown in the kitchen garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17039;Unruly Pig;United Kingdom;Bromeswell;Orford Road, Bromeswell, IP12 2PU, United Kingdom;52.1021516;1.3561737;37;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This modern dining pub is far from unruly, with a formality to the service brought by its owner – a former lawyer – and suited managers. The team's geniality adds a welcome warmth, as do stylish touches like wood panelling and interesting modern art, which are nicely integrated within the classic pub décor. The cooking shows off contemporary techniques and there's a Mediterranean influence to some of the flavoursome dishes, like Ibérico pork or bucatini vongole. The best value is to be found on the set menus.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17040;The Hare;United Kingdom;Scawton;Scawton, YO7 2HG, United Kingdom;54.2438165;-1.1590872;92;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Dating back to the 12th century, this Yorkshire stone inn makes for a lovely setting in which to dine. The building has been lovingly restored by owners Paul & Liz Jackson, who run the place with great pride. Paul is in the kitchen crafting a multi-course tasting menu that exhibits Japanese influences across creative and technically accomplished dishes. The intimate, cosy atmosphere – the dining room houses just five tables – and the addition of four splendid bedrooms all help to make The Hare an appealing destination for a weekend getaway.;Car park;[]
17041;Crockers Chef's Table;United Kingdom;Tring;74 High Street, Tring, HP23 4AF, United Kingdom;51.7934789;-0.663442;51;true;true;Modern British;On the first floor of a Tring townhouse, behind a U-shaped counter, you'll find Chef Scott Barnard in his element. He visibly enjoys interacting with his guests and proudly explaining his dishes at this chef's table operation inside a striking, copper-walled room. Scott and his enthusiastic team craft creative, eye-catching creations, such as a Japanese-influenced dessert of chocolate, miso, sesame and yuzu. Arrive early to start your visit with a cocktail in the Cellar Bar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17042;Swan Wine Kitchen;United Kingdom;Tenterden;Chapel Down Winery, Small Hythe Road, Tenterden, TN30 7NG, United Kingdom;51.041008;0.6984379;98;true;true;Modern British;This rustic, modern restaurant sits above the shop in the Chapel Down vineyard and boasts a cosy lounge and a lovely rooftop terrace with views over the vines. It’s run by a friendly team and, naturally, wines from the vineyard feature – go for the suggested pairings. Ambitious modern dishes have a British heart and have a bias towards local ingredients.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
17044;Sandpiper Inn;United Kingdom;Leyburn;Railway Street, Market Place, Leyburn, DL8 5AT, United Kingdom;54.30943;-1.828665;87;true;true;Traditional British;You’ll receive a cheery Yorkshire welcome from the friendly owners of this characterful stone pub, which has been impressing locals and visitors alike for over 25 years in this pretty market town. They refer to their three dining rooms as 'snugs' and rightly so, as there's a delightfully cosy vibe throughout. The menus are overtly seasonal and reflect the location, with the chef's experience shining through in carefully prepared, tried-and-tested dishes, where puddings are a highlight. Two ‘country-chic’ bedrooms offer excellent comforts.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17045;Jöro;United Kingdom;Sheffield;Main Road, Wharncliffe Side, Oughtibridge, Sheffield, S35 0LB, United Kingdom;53.43991;-1.50517;86;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Run by a keen husband and wife team, Jöro is named after the Old Norse word for 'Earth', reflecting its commitment to quality British ingredients – which are the bedrock of the ambitious cooking. While the produce may be local, the tasting menus have a strong East Asian base, integrating plenty of Japanese flavours like wasabi and ponzu in particular. The restaurant recently relocated outside the city to Oughtibridge Mill, but if you want your fix within the centre, head to House of Jöro where they have bedrooms and a chef's table.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17046;Salutation Inn;United Kingdom;Topsham;68 Fore Street, Topsham, EX3 0HL, United Kingdom;50.6833986;-3.4655636;67;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This characterful 1720s coaching inn has a surprisingly contemporary interior matched by understated bedrooms. Dinner takes place in the intimate dining room, while lunch and afternoon tea are served in the airy glass-covered historic courtyard – the perfect spot for a sunny afternoon. In the evening, choose between a tasting menu and a seasonally-themed à la carte, where modern dishes are well-judged and nicely balanced. Be sure to pick up some goodies from their deli and wet fish shop on your way out.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17048;Alice Hawthorn Inn;United Kingdom;Nun Monkton;The Green, Nun Monkton, YO26 8EW, United Kingdom;54.013753;-1.2253786;69;false;false;Regional Cuisine, Traditional British;This smartly modernised dining pub sits on a large village green where, as well as a duck pond, you’ll find the country’s tallest maypole. Hearty, well-presented dishes have classical roots and showcase local and garden produce. Welcoming service and smart bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17049;Ox Club;United Kingdom;Leeds;Bramleys Yard, The Headrow, Leeds, LS1 6PU, United Kingdom;53.7988884;-1.5406234;34;true;true;Meats and Grills, Barbecue;Housed in a former mill, along with a beer hall and cocktail bar, this unpretentious restaurant attracts a young and lively crowd keen to sample its wood-fired cooking using a grill imported from the US. Utilising fire and smoke to enhance quality produce is the name of the game – with the 1kg côte de boeuf on hand if you're feeling flush – but the kitchen isn't afraid of adding in bold flavours too, as evidenced by the nduja with the oysters and the gochujang glaze on the crispy pig tails. Pleasingly, there's plenty of choice for vegetarians too.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17052;Zuma;United Kingdom;London;5 Raphael Street, Knightsbridge, London, SW7 1DL, United Kingdom;51.5009622;-0.1631901;73;false;false;Japanese Contemporary;Zuma may now be a global brand, but this long-standing Knightsbridge restaurant was the originator of its informal, izakaya-inspired Japanese cuisine. Managing to still feel fresh over 20 years after opening, its home to a glamorous clientele who fit right in with the striking surroundings and bustling atmosphere. Sharing is a great way to experience as much of the extensive menu as possible – but if you have to prioritise, make sure you try the array of produce cooked on the robata grill, from tofu to chicken wings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
17053;Rubino Kitchen;United Kingdom;Inworth;Kelvedon Road, Inworth, CO5 9SP, United Kingdom;51.8290418;0.7270327;88;true;false;Modern British;A red-brick former pub provides the new home for this restaurant, which has long been a feature of the local dining scene. A large array of menus is available and the fixed price lunch is a steal. The experienced chef knows how to get the best out of his ingredients and dishes burst with flavour from the effective combinations. They even run regular cookery classes for kids.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17054;Crown;United Kingdom;Bray;High Street, Bray, SL6 2AH, United Kingdom;51.5067186;-0.7012446;60;false;true;Traditional British;Formerly two cottages and a bike shop, this restored, timbered 16th Century building is now home to this dining pub in the gastronomic haven of Bray. Inside, the place has a traditional and cosy feel, accompanied by cooking with a similarly classical outlook. Expect the menu to include robust and flavoursome dishes like grilled pork chop or fish soup with the obligatory rouille, gruyère and croutons.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17055;Bluebells;United Kingdom;Ascot;London Road, Ascot, SL5  0PU, United Kingdom;51.4090574;-0.6249969;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s a degree of opulence to this popular restaurant housed inside a whitewashed building. The striking dark green interior features glitzy rose gold panelling and distinctive tiling, ensuring the dining room feels a little bit special. Modern European dishes make use of effective, well-judged flavour combinations and there’s an assured level of technique in the cooking. Sit in the main room overlooking the fire pit or in the airy conservatory, while the smooth service team look after you with aplomb.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17056;Bass and Lobster;United Kingdom;Gorey;Gorey Coast Road, Gorey, JE3 6EU, United Kingdom;49.197466;-2.0291749;87;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;A former pub close to the beach houses this substantial bistro, where you’ll find plenty of regulars drawn in by the great value daily set menu. There’s always plenty to choose from here, including numerous daily specials and a good selection of fresh fish – and the faggots are a must-try. You can watch the island meats, vegetables and seafood being prepared through the kitchen window.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17057;Brassica;United Kingdom;Beaminster;4 The Square, Beaminster, DT8 3AS, United Kingdom;50.8091395;-2.7391617;40;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A pretty 16th-century house plays host to this sweetly run restaurant, situated in a prime spot overlooking the small square of this characterful Dorset town. Inside, the bright, colourful décor adds to the endearing feel, with its countryside shabby-chic style. The concise, Mediterranean-inflected menu moves with the seasons to show off excellent produce, delivered with a palpable simplicity and textbook technique by the confident kitchen team. If you want to go all-in on the Brassica brand, visit their homewares store, Brassica Mercantile, across the road.;;[]
17059;Daylesford Organic Farm;United Kingdom;Daylesford;Daylesford, GL56 0YG, United Kingdom;51.9293365;-1.6431474;30;false;false;Modern British;There may be Daylesford cafés spread all around London now, but this is the mothership. Found in the heart of the Cotswolds, you enter this stylishly rustic eatery through the farm shop, before dining in a choice of areas: head to the Legbar for charcuterie and nibbles, the Old Spot for pizzas and wood-roasted specials, or the main Trough Café for something a bit more substantial. Everything is organic, with much of the produce coming from the on-site farm and providing a fabulous base for the flavoursome, well-executed dishes.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17060;Paco Tapas;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;The General, 3a Lower Guinea Street, City of Bristol, BS1 6FU, United Kingdom;51.4471154;-2.5940282;24;false;false;Spanish;Start with either a fine Spanish wine or a chilled sherry straight from the cask while sitting on the terrace of this buzzy tapas bar. Dishes are skilfully prepared, packed with flavour and include all the favourites, from jamón croquetas to tortillas where the rich, golden egg just oozes out. Those unfamiliar with the Spanish way need not fret, as the knowledgeable team will guide you through the menu from start to finish.;Air conditioning;[]
17061;Nobu London Old Park Lane;United Kingdom;London;19 Old Park Lane, Mayfair, London, W1Y 4LB, United Kingdom;51.5051406;-0.1500996;86;true;false;Japanese;There are now Nobu restaurants stretching from Dallas to Dubai and Mexico to Melbourne, but this one was Europe’s first when it opened back in 1997. Like seeing a favourite popstar on stage, you can expect all the greatest hits, from seafood toban yaki to rock shrimp tempura and, of course, the dish that’s been copied a thousand times: black cod miso. There’s a decently priced weekday lunch menu and the service is smooth and confident.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17064;The Peacock at Rowsley;United Kingdom;Rowsley;Bakewell Road, Rowsley, DE4 2EB, United Kingdom;53.1889731;-1.6183257;70;false;true;Modern British;An elegant hotel restaurant where old mullioned stone windows, oak ‘Mousey Thompson’ furnishings and antique oil paintings are juxtaposed with modern lighting and contemporary art. Lunch offers traditional dishes, while dinner is more adventurous. Bedrooms are furnished with antiques.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17065;Soif;United Kingdom;London;27 Battersea Rise, Battersea, London, SW11 1HG, United Kingdom;51.4608708;-0.1637115;53;true;true;French;A classic French bistro and wine shop are rolled into one appealing package at this rustic neighbourhood operation run by a friendly team. The satisfying dishes have a largely French accent, with some Mediterranean influences also coming into play, be it burrata or kalamata olives. The rotisserie chicken to share is something of a speciality, while the thoughtfully compiled wine list includes plenty of natural wines from artisan winemakers.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17066;The Gannet;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;1155 Argyle Street, Glasgow City, G3 8TB, United Kingdom;55.8649237;-4.285212;50;false;true;Modern British;One of the stalwarts of the Finnieston dining scene, The Gannet is a proper neighbourhood restaurant run by a close-knit team. There are playful elements to the ambitious cooking and dishes are visually impressive throughout, available from either an à la carte – supplemented by specials – or a fixed-price 3 course lunch. The passion from both the kitchen and front of house teams is palpable, the latter proving to be both friendly and efficient.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17068;Stoke Mill;United Kingdom;Stoke Holy Cross;Mill Road, Stoke Holy Cross, NR14 8PA, United Kingdom;52.5688013;1.2925653;86;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A 700-year-old mill makes a terrific setting for this characterful restaurant spanning the River Tas. You can feel a palpable sense of history not only in the mill itself, but in the knowledge that the adjoining building is where the Colman family started making their famous mustard back in 1814. The cooking, for its part, consists of technically adept versions of straightforward, classically based dishes where the ingredients are strong and the flavours are distinct.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
17070;Queens Arms;United Kingdom;Corton Denham;Putt's Lane, Corton Denham, DT9 4LR, United Kingdom;50.99571;-2.52095;87;true;false;Modern British;There’s always something going on at this hub-of-the-village pub, which comes with a modern look and immaculately furnished bedrooms. Country cooking evolves with the seasons and focuses on sustainable ingredients: veg is supplied by a villager, pork is reared locally and seafood is from the Jurassic Coast.;Terrace;[]
17071;Sexy Fish;United Kingdom;London;4-6 Berkeley Square, Mayfair, London, W1J 6BR, United Kingdom;51.509327;-0.1444621;35;false;false;Asian;Everyone will have an opinion about the name but what’s indisputable is that this is a very good looking restaurant, with works by Frank Gehry and Damien Hirst, and a stunning ceiling by Michael Roberts. The fish comes with various Asian influences but don’t ignore the meat dishes like the beef rib skewers.;Air conditioning;[]
17072;Benedicts;United Kingdom;Norwich;9 St Benedicts Street, Norwich, NR2 4PE, United Kingdom;52.630834;1.2911701;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Situated in a bohemian part of the city, the modern bistro vibe perfectly suits this simply decorated restaurant that carries its unfussy ethos through into the cooking. Chef-Owner Richard Bainbridge is proud of his Norfolk roots and an ambassador for the region’s larder, and his understated dishes rely on top quality ingredients to lead the way. They serve a range of menus, varying in length and with vegetarian and, on request, vegan options available. For those looking for a lighter bite, sit outside and order small plates from the Alfresco menu.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17074;The Wild Rabbit;United Kingdom;Kingham;Church Street, Kingham, OX7 6YA, United Kingdom;51.9124916;-1.624684;64;false;true;Modern British;Just down the road from the Daylesford Farm Shop is the Bamford family’s stylishly modernised country pub. It's constantly packed with contented diners and it's no wonder why as this is an utterly charming place, looking every inch the quintessential Cotswolds inn. The accomplished cooking offers plenty of appeal, with the natural flavours of the farm’s superb organic ingredients underpinning the menu. The luxurious bedrooms are delightfully understated, if you want to continue your Cotswolds adventure.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17076;Wellington Arms;United Kingdom;Baughurst;Baughurst Road, Baughurst, RG26 5LP, United Kingdom;51.3401602;-1.1628328;77;false;false;British Contemporary;At this smart cream pub they have their own herb and vegetable beds, keep sheep, pigs, chickens and bees, and source the rest of their meats from within 20 miles. Menus feature 6 dishes per course – supplemented by a selection of specials – and cooking is generous and satisfying. Smart, rustic bedrooms come with slate floors, sheepskin rugs and big, comfy beds.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17077;The Antidote;United Kingdom;Ilfracombe;20 St James Place, Ilfracombe, EX34 9BJ, United Kingdom;51.2103855;-4.1163725;35;false;false;Modern British;Arrive early for a stroll around the harbour before dinner at this sweet, glass-fronted shop conversion where brown paper covered tables contribute to a cool, modish feel. It’s run by a friendly couple with a passion for local produce, so the thoughtfully prepared set menu changes regularly. Well-judged dishes are modern in their make-up and packed with flavour. Bedrooms are contemporary and one even has a small terrace.;;[]
17078;Corrigan's Mayfair;United Kingdom;London;28 Upper Grosvenor Street, Mayfair, London, W1K 7EH, United Kingdom;51.5100245;-0.1555445;48;false;false;Modern British;This smart spot, with its central Mayfair address and leather banquettes, makes a fitting flagship for the eponymous Chef-Owner. There's a clubby feel to the place, with dimmed lighting adding to the intimacy and Dickies Bar on hand if you're partial to a pre-dinner cocktail. Although there are subtle modern touches, the menu is largely guided by classical French techniques (pommes Anna, vin jaune sauce) and a pleasingly retro approach in dishes like the royal seafood cocktail, filled with sweet and meaty prawns.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17079;Pythouse Kitchen Garden;United Kingdom;Tisbury;West Hatch, Tisbury, SP3 6PA, United Kingdom;51.055077;-2.1323674;23;true;true;Traditional British;You'll struggle to find a lovelier all-round experience than having lunch at Pythouse Kitchen Garden. Set inside a red-brick former potting shed within a Victorian walled garden, it's a gorgeous setting with elegance and country charm to spare. The cooking is a joy too, with great value to be had in the generous fixed-price offering built around cooking over fire. The ingredients, many from the garden itself, are of real quality and used to brilliant effect – like the pickled gooseberry ketchup offsetting rich game sausage.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17080;Hakkasan Mayfair;United Kingdom;London;17 Bruton Street, Mayfair, London, W1J 6QB, United Kingdom;51.5101824;-0.1451152;34;false;true;Chinese;This seductive subterranean spot beckons you in through its discreet entrance on Bruton Street, immediately transporting you to somewhere altogether more thrilling. The ground floor is great for lunchtime dim sum, but if you’re here for dinner ask for a table on the lower floor, which has a more energising atmosphere. The extensive menus feature a roll-call of luxury ingredients, from whole native lobster to black truffle roasted duck.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17083;Sketch, The Gallery;United Kingdom;London;9 Conduit Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 2XG, United Kingdom;51.5127186;-0.1415128;58;false;true;Modern Cuisine;In 2022 artist Yinka Shonibare and designer India Mahdavi joined forces to unveil a striking new look and colour palette for this enduringly fashionable and efficiently run restaurant. The menu is equally original, mixing the classic with the esoteric. Afternoon tea is also a big hit with the bright, young things, who flock here with their cameras at the ready.;Air conditioning;[]
17084;Menu Gordon Jones;United Kingdom;Bath;2 Wellsway, Bath, BA2 3AQ, United Kingdom;51.374165;-2.3665808;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This tiny, highly likeable restaurant has a relaxed, cheerful feel, which is a reflection of its easy-going Chef-Owner. The room is dominated by an open kitchen, where you can watch Gordon preparing creative, complex dishes. The daily changing surprise menu delivers punchy flavour combinations and several playful elements. He serves many of the dishes himself and chats with guests, adding to the feel that this is a very personal operation.;;[]
17085;The Fox;United Kingdom;Lower Oddington;High Street, Lower Oddington, GL56 0UR, United Kingdom;51.93226;-1.66276;45;false;false;Modern British;Sister to The Wild Rabbit in Kingham and the Daylesford Organic Farm, this immaculately refurbished 19C Cotswold inn is bursting with style and character, boasting flagged floors, exposed stone walls and an impressive wood-fired oven. The menu covers all bases – from pizza to Hereford sirloin on the bone – and uses top quality ingredients from their estate in unfussy, generously sized, tasty combinations. Make a night of it with a stay in one of their stylish bedrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17087;The Howard Arms;United Kingdom;Ilmington;Lower Green, Ilmington, CV36 4LT, United Kingdom;52.0911897;-1.6904343;72;true;true;Modern British;Built from golden stone quarried in the village itself, The Howard Arms is very much a part of the local community. They open at 8am for coffee and breakfast, and hearty flavours are the order of the day on the appealing menu, where pub favourites are listed alongside dishes of a more global bent. Bedrooms come in a variety of styles.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17089;Greyhound on the Test;United Kingdom;Stockbridge;31 High Street, Stockbridge, SO20 6EY, United Kingdom;51.114568;-1.4962856;67;true;false;British Contemporary;The picturesque town of Stockbridge plays host to this striking mustard-coloured pub with low beams, elegant décor and a wood-burning stove. The chatty team deliver appealing modern British dishes crafted from local produce. Homely bedrooms and a mile of River Test fishing rights complete the picture.;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17090;BiBi;United Kingdom;London;42 North Audley Street, Mayfair, London, W1K 6ZP, United Kingdom;51.512403;-0.1532581;38;false;false;Indian;The two evening tasting menus at Chet Sharma's buzzy Mayfair restaurant are named after his grandmothers (bibis), Kamal and Ranjana, and a family influence can be felt right across his interesting Indian cooking. Dishes like "Sharmaji's Lahori Chicken" – using a recipe passed down from Chet's grandfather – are well-spiced and deliver on flavour, with punchy accompaniments like red pepper pickle used to pep things up. Sitting at the counter will add something to the experience, while the charming service and smooth pacing make everything more enjoyable.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17091;Maison Bleue;United Kingdom;Bury St Edmunds;30-31 Churchgate Street, Bury St Edmunds, IP33 1RG, United Kingdom;52.24352;0.7153498;64;true;true;French;A converted 17th-century house plays host to this town centre restaurant that – as the name would suggest – is firmly French at heart. The cooking is classic Gallic in base, with occasional modern and international touches on show. Seafood is a strength, with fine produce like fresh tail of turbot cooked with obvious skill by the kitchen team. Your final course will be a treat too, with desserts like brûlée of pear as well as excellent French cheeses from the trolley – accompanied by some fine wines by the glass.;Interesting wine list;[]
17092;Plough at Bolnhurst;United Kingdom;Bolnhurst;Kimbolton Road, Bolnhurst, MK44 2EX, United Kingdom;52.2157122;-0.4093551;54;false;false;Modern British;Sit in the rustic bar, modern restaurant or lovely garden of this charming whitewashed pub with Tudor origins. Menus are named after ploughing terms: ‘The Seam’ makes use of offcuts from main menu ‘The Furrow’. British and Mediterranean influences combine and there’s a great cheese selection.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17093;Park Chinois;United Kingdom;London;17 Berkeley Street, Mayfair, London, W1J 8EA, United Kingdom;51.5087303;-0.1437158;41;true;true;Chinese;Old fashioned glamour, strikingly rich surroundings and live music combine to great effect at this sumptuously decorated restaurant. The menu traverses the length of China, with dim sum at lunchtimes and afternoon tea at weekends. The delicious 'Duck de Chine' is roasted to order.;Air conditioning;[]
17097;Heritage Dulwich;United Kingdom;London;101 Rosendale Road, Dulwich, London, SE21 8EZ, United Kingdom;51.4370689;-0.094685;91;true;true;Indian;‘Heritage’ is key to the cooking at this Indian restaurant in a smart suburban shopping parade, where skilfully prepared dishes are knowledgably balanced, well-spiced and packed with authentic flavours. Dayashankar Sharma – who has led many of London’s best Indian kitchens – cooks alongside his son Anmol.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17098;Hoddington Arms;United Kingdom;Upton Grey;Bidden Road, Upton Grey, RG25 2RL, United Kingdom;51.229313;-0.9989498;46;true;true;Traditional British;‘The Hodd’ is a characterful pub at the heart of the village, and offers a friendly welcome and charm aplenty with its rustic brickwork, exposed timbers and open fires. Understated menu descriptions belie the skill in the experienced chef’s well-crafted dishes. Be sure to save room for pudding!;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17099;The Shore;United Kingdom;Penzance;13-14 Alverton Street, Penzance, TR18 2QP, United Kingdom;50.1183515;-5.5395619;79;true;true;Seafood;The gregarious and welcoming Bruce Rennie is something of a one-man band here at this intimate restaurant with room for just 10 diners. He works alone in the kitchen and presents dishes to all his guests at the same time, in a warm, engaging manner. The tasting menu incorporates international influences ranging from Japanese to French, but each course is united by the quality of its produce, much of it the finest seafood from Cornish waters.;;[]
17102;Buckland Manor;United Kingdom;Buckland;Buckland, WR12 7LY, United Kingdom;52.0221059;-1.882694;31;false;true;Modern British;Open fires and sumptuous furnishings await as you arrive at the supremely elegant Buckland Manor, a prime example of the classic English country house hotel, set in 10 acres of verdant grounds. Its restaurant is equally characterful, with wood panelling, oil paintings and garden views contributing to the luxury feel. The cooking utilises quality British ingredients that we all know and love, such as delicious Peterhead cod served with consummately seasoned cannellini beans and sea herbs.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
17103;Barshu;United Kingdom;London;28 Frith Street, Soho, London, W1D 5LF, United Kingdom;51.5128324;-0.130863;18;false;false;Chinese;The fiery flavours of China's Sichuan province are the draw here, although numerous other regions of China are well catered for too. The menu highlights both new and signature dishes, enlivened by authentic spicing – the legendary chillies and peppers are imported directly from China – and plenty of these generously proportioned dishes are great for sharing. Carved wood and lanterns decorate the room.;Air conditioning;[]
17104;Lurra;United Kingdom;London;9 Seymour Place, Marylebone, London, W1H 5BA, United Kingdom;51.51474;-0.16131;81;true;false;Basque;Its name means ‘land’ in Basque and reflects their use of the freshest produce, cooked over a charcoal grill. Choose tasty nibbles or sharing plates like 14 year old Galician beef, whole grilled turbot or slow-cooked shoulder of lamb.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17105;Rondo;United Kingdom;London;199-206 High Holborn, Holborn, London, WC1V 7BD, United Kingdom;51.5171344;-0.1225794;64;false;false;Modern British;Rondo with its open kitchen all down one side occupies a fair chunk of ground floor acreage within the Hoxton hotel and offers a fun night out. The chef is an alumnus of St John so expect cooking that is robust and satisfying, although the menu here is a little more international in its influences.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17106;Food Leigh-On-Sea;United Kingdom;Leigh-on-Sea;92 Leigh Road, Leigh-on-Sea, SS9 1BU, United Kingdom;51.5434309;0.6670931;67;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away among the shops is this narrow restaurant with a rustic look, given a cosy vibe by the friendly, engaging manner in which it's run. The creative, eye-catching dishes are full of flavour and focus on sustainability and wellbeing. The menu format changes depending on when you visit, with surprise tasting menus for Friday and Saturday evenings, small plates from a specials board at lunch and all-day Thursday, and a roast lunch on Sundays. Vegans are well catered-for too, with plant-based options always available.;Air conditioning;[]
17107;Bow Room at Grays Court;United Kingdom;York;Chapter House Street, York, YO1 7JH, United Kingdom;53.963016;-1.0803576;89;false;false;Modern British;Tucked away by the Minster and bordered by the historic city walls, this beautiful Jacobean house with luxurious bedrooms and a peaceful garden is something of a hidden gem. Enjoy an aperitif in the characterful wood-panelled gallery, then head through to the more modern restaurant with its large bow window. Seasonality, purity and freshness underpin the skilful, confidently restrained dishes that often use ingredients from their own garden. The service team have a natural charm and help to make your visit a memorable one.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17109;Packhorse Inn;United Kingdom;Moulton;Bridge Street, Moulton, CB8 8SP, United Kingdom;52.2526865;0.4846408;22;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Set near the green in a pretty village, is this smart modern pub named after the 15C flint bridge which spans the river. Understated modern dishes have subtle yet effective flavour combinations and use the best local ingredients. Ultra-stylish bedrooms have plush furnishings and roll-top baths.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17111;Folium;United Kingdom;Birmingham;8 Caroline Street, Birmingham, B3 1TW, United Kingdom;52.4860491;-1.9072294;42;false;false;Modern British;This smart, minimal-chic restaurant in the city’s Jewellery Quarter is run by a two-person team. Ben is in the kitchen and the warm, genial Lucy is out front. The cooking, like the décor, is modern in approach and allows Ben’s personality to shine through in the flavours and presentation. The menu is largely seafood-based, which results in highlight dishes like Cornish turbot with a delicious Arbroath smokie liquor.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17112;Eckington Manor;United Kingdom;Eckington;Manor Farm, Hammock Road, Eckington, WR10 3BJ, United Kingdom;52.0710289;-2.1205314;47;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You’ll find this proudly run 13C manor house and its collection of characterfully converted barns located on a 300 acre farm. Attractive modern dishes showcase local ingredients in ambitious combinations – and for those who want to get hands-on there’s a cookery school. Bedrooms are stylish.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17113;Roketsu;United Kingdom;London;12 New Quebec Street, Marylebone, London, W1H 7RW, United Kingdom;51.5155499;-0.1582895;88;true;true;Japanese;Chef-Owner Daisuke Hayashi has created a little slice of Kyoto life here in New Quebec Street. His culinary training and background may have been traditional but he’s not averse to introducing the occasional contemporary touch to some elements of his 10 course kaiseki menu. If you want to make your own choices, there's also an à la carte available, along with a set lunch menu on certain days. The charming welcome, attentive service and the counter fashioned from 100-year old hinoki wood will transport you away from the hurly burly of city life.;Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
17114;Thomas;United Kingdom;Cardiff;3-5 Pontcanna Street, Cardiff, CF11 9HQ, United Kingdom;51.4864486;-3.2000233;65;false;true;Modern British;Hidden away in the leafy suburbs of Cardiff, this is a true neighbourhood restaurant which continues to develop and evolve. Begin with a cocktail in the spacious, formal bar, before taking a seat in the cosy downstairs or moody first-floor dining room. Proud Welshman Tom Simmons is at the helm, bringing his love of local produce to bear in technically impressive, full-flavoured dishes built on the likes of Pembrokeshire oysters and saddle of Welsh lamb. Whatever you order, be sure to start with some superb sourdough from their own bakery, Ground.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17115;The Pierhouse;United Kingdom;Port Appin;Port Appin, PA38 4DE, United Kingdom;56.5531193;-5.4137751;95;true;true;Seafood, Traditional Cuisine;As locations go, it’s hard to beat: find a spot on the terrace to watch the ferry chugging across the loch and stay the night to wake up to the fabulous view. Traditional Scottish delicacies and fresh local seafood lead the way – opt for a platter and don’t miss the delicious mussels.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
17117;The Clarence Tavern;United Kingdom;London;102 Stoke Newington Church Street, London, N16 0LA, United Kingdom;51.5622648;-0.0788731;20;true;true;Traditional Cuisine;A classic Victorian-era London pub, The Clarence Tavern comes with a real characterful charm, courtesy of its 19th-century architecture fused with more contemporary details. Head past the bar to the part-panelled, part-brick dining area, where the doors open out onto a courtyard terrace. Many of the boldly flavoured dishes come from the pub classics school – like chicken, leek and bacon pie to share – and arrive in pleasingly gutsy portions. Try one of the natural wines and be sure to visit the deli before you leave.;Terrace;[]
17118;Land;United Kingdom;Birmingham;30 Great Western Arcade, Colmore Row, Birmingham, B2 5HU, United Kingdom;52.4818616;-1.8973049;70;false;true;Vegetarian, Asian Influences;The Great Western Arcade in the heart of the city is home to this intimate restaurant, where the chefs harness the power of plants for their creative vegetarian dishes. There's an original streak running through the seasonally evolving set menu – which is largely vegan – alongside a scattering of pan-Asian influences ranging from carrot char sui to sake lees, all executed with care and skill by the chefs. Wine flights are available to enhance the experience and the friendly service team will see to your every need.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17119;Wild Shropshire;United Kingdom;Whitchurch;25-27 Green End, Whitchurch, SY13 1AD, United Kingdom;52.9692073;-2.6819688;63;true;true;Modern British;Self-taught chef James Sherwin’s dream came true when he opened this endearing restaurant that’s the epitome of field-to-fork dining. Micro-seasonal produce is grown on their Wild Shropshire farm before being fashioned into a daily changing surprise menu for a maximum of 14 guests. There’s a Japanese influence throughout the harmoniously flavoured dishes, including ingredients like furikake, koji and yuzu, as well as a sake pairing. The passionate, welcoming team offer lovely, personable service.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17121;The Greyhound;United Kingdom;Beaconsfield;33 Windsor End, Beaconsfield, HP9 2JN, United Kingdom;51.6003824;-0.6357453;38;true;false;Modern British;Your visit here will be an instantly enjoyable one thanks to the genuine warmth and friendliness of owners Daniel and Margriet. They are natural hosts, providing attentive service while making all their diners feel at ease. The setting for their endearing hospitality is a charming 17th-century former coaching inn that retains many of its original features. The cooking itself consists of eye-catching dishes that are refined yet hearty, showcasing carefully crafted, classic combinations which burst with natural flavours – like the terrific prune soufflé with Armagnac Anglaise.;Terrace;[]
17122;Sam's Riverside;United Kingdom;London;1 Crisp Walk, Hammersmith, London, W6 9DN, United Kingdom;51.4879346;-0.2279421;39;false;false;Modern British;Experienced restaurateur Sam Harrison is behind this modern riverside brasserie beside Hammersmith Bridge. It's an enduringly popular place and you can see why from the appealing, pleasingly varied menu that might incorporate a range of influences but doesn't lose sight of the flavour gained by using quality produce. British ingredients from land and sea are cooked with precision and there's a whole section of the menu for oysters and other shellfish. Stock up on provisions at Sam’s Larder before you leave.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17123;Erst;United Kingdom;Manchester;9 Murray Street, Ancoats, Manchester, M4 6HS, United Kingdom;53.4843541;-2.2274321;72;false;true;British Contemporary;A modern, industrial-style wine bar run by a group of friends, laid-back Erst offers something refreshingly different in the city. It specialises in natural, low-intervention wines – many of which you can buy to take home – accompanied by a selection of flavoursome small plates.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17124;Lazy Lobster;United Kingdom;Chew Magna;5 South Parade, Chew Magna, BS40 8SH, United Kingdom;51.3657909;-2.6099932;70;true;false;Seafood;A charming local couple transformed the old high street hairdressers into this lovely little seafood restaurant complete with a wet fish counter. Choose from shellfish platters or small plates ranging from the classic to the adventurous. The great drinks list includes gin from their son’s onsite distillery.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17125;Larder;United Kingdom;Lichfield;17 Bore Street, Lichfield, WS13 6LZ, United Kingdom;52.6826125;-1.8282656;80;true;false;Modern Cuisine;‘All flavour, no pomp’ is the tagline at this relaxed, warmly run restaurant – and that’s exactly what you’ll get. Sit in the boldly decorated first floor restaurant or book a seat at the chefs table to be close to the action. Attractively presented modern dishes are sure to satisfy.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17126;Next Door;United Kingdom;Frodsham;68 Main Street, Frodsham, WA6 7AU, United Kingdom;53.2948715;-2.7281389;89;true;true;British Contemporary;A family business has been run on this 17th Century premises for three generations. For many years it was a butcher's shop, the current incarnation of which now sits two doors down, and today Sommelier Vicki has taken on the mantle to run it as this sweet restaurant with her husband Richard. His dishes are founded on excellent quality ingredients, with the meat from the family butcher's unsurprisingly being a stand-out – like the supremely flavoursome Welsh Black beef. Low-ceilinged rooms and exposed beams add to the charm.;Terrace;[]
17128;Restaurant Meudon;United Kingdom;Mawnan Smith;Maenporth Road, Mawnan Smith, TR11 5HT, United Kingdom;50.1163974;-5.0985013;18;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Imposing granite pillars and neatly laid tables help to bring an air of classical elegance to this restaurant inside the Hotel Meudon. The dining room overlooks impressive mature sub-tropical gardens, which also contribute to the all-round lovely setting. The concise, daily changing menu is Cornish at heart, especially when it comes to seafood. Dishes like Mylor crab filo tart are understated yet well-executed and wholly enjoyable.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17129;Zafferano;United Kingdom;London;16-18 Lowndes Street, Belgravia, London, SW1X 9EY, United Kingdom;51.49919;-0.1577;49;false;true;Italian;This long-standing Italian restaurant with a pavement terrace has become something of a Belgravia institution. The reassuringly familiar – if rather steeply priced – dishes take their inspiration from all over Italy, bringing together just a handful of top quality ingredients and allowing them to shine.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Terrace;[]
17130;Catch at The Old Fishmarket;United Kingdom;Weymouth;1 Custom House Quay, Weymouth, DT4 8BE, United Kingdom;50.6072663;-2.4539895;41;false;true;Seafood;Originally due to open on the first day of the 2020 lockdown, this fish shop and restaurant is a living, breathing testament to the power of determination. Now flourishing in its Portland stone, Grade II listed building, the kitchen's skill is most evident in allowing top-end produce like glistening monkfish tail to thrive unadorned, while employing impressive creativity to elevate less glamorous cuts – as evidenced by the crispy cod's cheek in a tomato and crab sauce. The set menu varies in length depending on the day and time of your visit, but the main course is always the catch of the day.;Wheelchair access;[]
17131;The Windmill;United Kingdom;Little Waltham;Chatham Green, Little Waltham, CM3 3LE, United Kingdom;51.8090025;0.4871843;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Chef-Owner Tom Clarke built up an impressive resume before returning to his Essex roots to open this lovely village inn with his partner. After a charming welcome from Nancy into the characterful interior, where a small bar still serves some local drinkers, it’s time to enjoy the hearty yet refined cooking. Classical flavour and texture combinations run throughout a menu served well by quality produce, with desserts like dark chocolate crémeux proving a real highlight.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17132;Benoli;United Kingdom;Norwich;5 Orford Street, Norwich, NR1 3LE, United Kingdom;52.6271737;1.2954137;87;true;false;Italian;‘Benoli’ might have an Italian ring to it but this three-floored restaurant is actually named after chef-owner Oliver and his brother Ben. The atmosphere is relaxed and welcoming and the appealing menu offers something for everyone – highlights include the homemade pastas and delicious desserts.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17133;The Three Horseshoes;United Kingdom;Batcombe;Batcombe, BA4 6HE, United Kingdom;51.15;-2.44428;45;true;true;Traditional British;Large fireplaces, stone floors and whitewashed walls feature inside this renovated 17C pub. The pared-back décor is joined by similarly straightforward and equally appealing cooking that includes hearty dishes like rabbit pie and mince on toast. This approach allows the ingredients to speak for themselves, with local Somerset produce a feature. Five bedrooms add to the inn’s appeal, as do an attractive terrace and small walled garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17137;Tyddyn Llan;United Kingdom;Llandrillo;Llandrillo, LL21 0ST, United Kingdom;52.92405;-3.44329;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The arrival of new owners means a refreshed feel to this long-standing country house hotel and restaurant on the edge of Snowdonia. Housed inside an elegant, slate-built former shooting lodge, the dining room now has a cleaner, more contemporary feel with light wooden floors and furnishings. The tasting menu, available in long or short form, makes a point of spotlighting the Welsh larder – in dishes that enjoyably combine classic recipes with some global influences, like vadouvan and miso with scallops or XO velouté with butter-poached cod.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17140;The Angel Inn;United Kingdom;Stoke-by-Nayland;Polstead Street, Stoke-by-Nayland, CO6 4SA, United Kingdom;51.9896559;0.8944118;56;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This red-brick pub has stood here for over 500 years and nowadays looks as good as ever thanks to its beautiful, no-expense-spared restoration. The stylish restaurant is divided into several rooms – and fans of wooden beams and open fireplaces won’t be disappointed. The kitchen team excel in making their simple yet skilled dishes uncomplicatedly delicious, like the pea and mint soup or the terrific boulangère potatoes, whose perfect crisping and flavour exemplify the virtues of the place. Stay overnight in one of the bedrooms and explore the area.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17141;Three Chimneys & The House Over-By;United Kingdom;Isle of Skye;Colbost, Dunvegan, Isle of Skye, IV55 8ZT, United Kingdom;57.44366;-6.64218;73;false;false;Modern British;The windswept beauty of the Isle of Skye provides a stunning backdrop to this immaculately kept crofter’s cottage at the edge of Loch Dunvegan. Contemporary art hangs on exposed stone walls in the characterful, low-beamed dining rooms. Unsurprisingly in an area with such bountiful produce, the menu keeps its focus local, with seafood from nearby waters among the highlights. Spacious, split-level bedrooms are stylishly understated and the residents’ lounge has a great outlook.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17142;Sapori;United Kingdom;Anstey;40 Stadon Road, Anstey, LE7 7AY, United Kingdom;52.6731463;-1.1882235;84;true;true;Italian;This sleek, modern, former Victorian Working Men’s Club is proudly run by a passionate Italian family. Sapori means ‘flavour’ and there’s certainly plenty of it in the refined, authentic dishes which centre around their home city of Naples. Service – from the chef’s brother-in-law – is charming.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17143;Samuel's;United Kingdom;Swinton;Swinton Park Hotel, Masham, Swinton, HG4 4JH, United Kingdom;54.2130983;-1.6766135;60;true;true;Modern British;The magnificent Swinton Estate looks like the platonic ideal of a British country retreat. The commanding country house and surrounding grounds play host to a hotel, a spa, a cookery school and 20,000 acres of farmland – crucially, it also has a restaurant befitting of its grandeur. A gold detailed ceiling and carved wooden fireplace make the dining room an opulent setting for boldly flavoured, generously portioned dishes that still retain a lightness of touch. Sustainability plays a large role, with lots of produce coming from the estate.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17144;Fontana;United Kingdom;Holywood;61a High Street, Holywood, BT18 9AQ, United Kingdom;54.641799;-5.8346439;72;true;false;Modern British;A cheery welcome from the chefs in the open kitchen greets all-comers at this long-standing but reenergised first-floor restaurant. The extensive selection of menus range from a 'prix fixe' to an à la carte and daily specials to a Sunday roast – and it’s almost impossible not to find a dessert that will take your fancy. Each dish showcases cooking that is crisp, modern and effective, perfectly encapsulated by fresh fish of the day with punchy romesco sauce. The room is smartly dressed and lightened by contemporary art.;;[]
17145;Slice;United Kingdom;Swansea;73-75 Eversley Road, Sketty, Swansea, SA2 9DE, United Kingdom;51.6183994;-3.9844749;78;false;false;Modern British;A personal welcome from chef-owners Chris and Adam is just one of the charms of this sweet little restaurant hidden away in the Swansea suburbs. The passion and pride of the team comes across not just in the friendly service, but in the carefully prepared dishes centred around seasonally changing ingredients – whether that be fresh crab with watermelon or pan-fried sea bass with butter-poached lobster. Choose from the concise à la carte or opt for the tasting menu for the full experience, accompanied by a well-priced wine pairing.;;[]
17146;LeftField;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;12 Barclay Terrace, Edinburgh, EH10 4HP, United Kingdom;55.9395442;-3.2039042;47;true;false;Seafood, Scottish;Honest, intimate and sweet, this is a proper neighbourhood restaurant which focuses on the country's delicious seafood. Straightforward options from Scottish waters kick things off, with fresh mussels and oysters sitting alongside the likes of a zingy crispy squid with gochujang mayo. Comforting and flavoursome main dishes pair well with the homely surroundings, where you can relax with some super views of Bruntsfield Links and The Meadows.;Counter dining;[]
17147;Purple Poppadom;United Kingdom;Cardiff;185a Cowbridge Road East, Upper Floor, Cardiff, CF11 9AJ, United Kingdom;51.4814538;-3.1976737;80;false;false;Indian;Enter via the glass door between the shop fronts and head up to this bright, sleek Indian restaurant where flashes of purple ensure it lives up to its name. Abstract murals, exposed brick walls and blonde wood chairs add to the décor’s contemporary feel. The extensive menu showcases classic, recognisable dishes like lamb rogan josh, but it’s worth keeping an eye out for the tiffin sea bass, which is considered the chef’s signature. The spicing tends to be subtle, allowing the flavours to come through in layers and fully complement the main ingredients.;Air conditioning;[]
17148;Felin Fach Griffin;United Kingdom;Brecon;Felin Fach, Brecon, LD3 0UB, United Kingdom;51.9899965;-3.3241395;97;false;false;Modern British;Warmth and character abound at this traditional pub. Relax on a sofa beside the fire with a pint of local beer, then head for the Library or Snug to dine. The organic kitchen garden provides herbs, veg and fruit for the simple, unfussy dishes. Cosy bedrooms come with good extras and are dog friendly.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17149;Sun Inn;United Kingdom;Dedham;High Street, Dedham, CO7 6DF, United Kingdom;51.958871;0.9921654;81;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A characterful yellow inn with an appealing shabby-chic style, located in a picturesque spot in the heart of Constable Country. The highly seasonal menu offers generous Mediterranean-inspired dishes and the well-chosen wine list offers plenty by the glass. Bedrooms are cosy – two have a modern New England style.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17150;Idle Rocks;United Kingdom;St Mawes;Harbourside, St Mawes, TR2 5AN, United Kingdom;50.1590913;-5.0130541;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This stylish, relaxed restaurant – running the entire length of the Idle Rocks hotel – offers superb bay views, and the water laps at its fabulous terrace. Refined, eye-catching dishes feature some fine Cornish ingredients and exhibit a wealth of flavours and textures. For the full experience go for the Signature menu.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17151;Stones Restaurant;United Kingdom;Matlock;1c Dale Road, Matlock, DE4 3LT, United Kingdom;53.137651;-1.5565447;29;false;true;Modern British;Negotiate the steep steps down to this small riverside restaurant and head for the front room with its floor to ceiling windows or the delightful rear terrace which offers wonderful views. Unfussy, modern British dishes are attractively presented and display the odd Mediterranean touch.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17153;Rafters;United Kingdom;Sheffield;220 Oakbrook Road, Nether Green, Sheffield, S11 7ED, United Kingdom;53.3683908;-1.5248721;26;true;true;Modern British;There's a characterful, rustic chic to this first-floor restaurant, courtesy of its exposed beams and brickwork. Real pride and enthusiasm is poured into both the cooking and the service, with modern, richly flavoured dishes available in a tasting menu format. A shorter set menu is served at certain times, while the 'Kitchen Bench' gives you a ringside seat in front of the pass. The wine list is usefully listed by style and characteristics, enabling you to craft the perfect pairing.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17155;Freemasons;United Kingdom;Wiswell;8 Vicarage Fold, Wiswell, BB7 9DF, United Kingdom;53.8320501;-2.3887525;100;true;true;Modern British;Tucked away down a narrow lane in the heart of the Ribble Valley, this delightful pub is as characterful inside as it is from the exterior. Cosy and welcoming, the whole place exudes a rustic charm thanks to an open fire and antique furnishings. The modern British dishes use the best of the local larder and deliver bold, well-judged flavours in adventurous, original creations like the 'Malteser' dessert. For the ultimate experience, book the "Chef's Bench", which consists of just four seats in the heart of the kitchen. Make a night of it and stay over in one of the bedrooms too.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17156;St Kew Inn;United Kingdom;St Kew;Bodmin, Cornwall, St Kew, PL30 3HB, United Kingdom;50.5586545;-4.7937332;85;true;true;Traditional British;There are few more characterful pubs in Britain than this 15th-century inn in a tranquil, quintessentially English location. Once inside you'll find flagged floors, wooden beams and an open fire, all adding to the bucolic charm. The menu offers a wide range of appealing dishes, with an emphasis on local ingredients including prime Cornish seafood like scallops and crab. Be sure to order a beer from the wooden casks behind the bar.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17157;The Conservatory;United Kingdom;Titchwell;Titchwell, PE31 8BB, United Kingdom;52.9616837;0.6187874;82;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Titchwell Manor’s formal dining room is a bright, airy space looking out over the walled gardens. Cooking champions local ingredients with seafood from Brancaster Staithe and meat and game from local estates. Unfussy modern classics focus on natural flavours, using a less-is-more approach.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17159;Gilpin Spice;United Kingdom;Bowness-on-Windermere;Crook Road, Bowness-on-Windermere, LA23 3NE, United Kingdom;54.3549349;-2.8805472;44;false;true;Asian, Fusion;Cumbria was a key player in the spice trade and this slate restaurant in the grounds of Gilpin Hotel is inspired by that history. Enter the colourful rooms via wooden walkways built over stone-filled pools, then follow the Silk Road from Cumbria to Asia on the extensive menu – where many of the vibrant dishes are designed for sharing. A seat on one of the comfortable kitchen counter couches is the best place to feel part of the action.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17160;Samphire;United Kingdom;Saint Helier;7-11 Don Street, Saint Helier, JE2 4TQ, United Kingdom;49.1845275;-2.1057946;87;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This buzzy all-day brasserie deluxe has a striking colour scheme which takes in blue velour banquettes and yellow leather chairs. Cooking adopts a modern approach and there’s a distinct Mediterranean influence. Island ingredients are to the fore and the oysters are something of a feature.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17161;Lorne;United Kingdom;London;76 Wilton Road, Victoria, London, SW1V 1DE, United Kingdom;51.4927361;-0.1403378;57;false;false;Modern Cuisine;They keep things honest at this narrow little restaurant and you can see the pay-off: a dining room full of happy customers, who are a mix of locals, tourists and business types. Staff are on the ball and well-versed on the menu, while the classically trained kitchen sends forth reliable and consistently good dishes, like Cornish cod with smoked eel, and chocolate delice with cookie crumble. The lunch and early evening menus are very good value.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17162;Grey's;United Kingdom;Malmesbury;Easton Grey, Malmesbury, SN16 0RB, United Kingdom;51.58376;-2.14954;100;false;true;Modern British;Sitting within the luxurious Whatley Manor Hotel & Spa, but with a feel all of its own, is this elegant grey-hued restaurant. It presents a slightly less formal alternative to The Dining Room, but is run with the smooth efficiency one would expect of this hotel. Salad and vegetables from the kitchen garden feature on modern menus with a British bias. Ask for a booth or dine in the garden in the summer months.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17164;Kilpeck Inn;United Kingdom;Kilpeck;Kilpeck, HR2 9DN, United Kingdom;51.9692056;-2.8072718;83;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;A popular pub which narrowly escaped being turned into private housing thanks to the villagers’ valiantly fought ‘Save Our Pub’ campaign. Its spacious interior and bedrooms are smart, modern and characterful, with impressive green credentials. Menus offer locally sourced meats and old fashioned puddings.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17165;White Hart;United Kingdom;Fyfield;Main Road, Fyfield, OX13 5LW, United Kingdom;51.6858174;-1.3891072;55;true;true;Modern British;There’s a lot to love about this imposing 15th-century chantry house. There’s the three-storey, vaulted dining room for starters, joined by a cosy open-fired bar and a minstrels’ gallery, while outside you’ll find a terrace, a vegetable garden and an outdoor kitchen with wood-fired oven. The cooking is guided by their own seasonal produce, with both British and Mediterranean influences on the flavoursome, carefully prepared dishes. The friendly service team run the restaurant well.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17166;Westwood;United Kingdom;Beverley;New Walk, Beverley, HU17 7AE, United Kingdom;53.84771;-0.4404485;82;false;true;Modern British;This smart, modern restaurant occupies one wing of an impressive Grade II listed former courthouse and has a sheltered courtyard terrace for warmer days. It’s run with passion by twins Michele and Matthew, whose menus mix traditional dishes with some more modern, creative choices.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17168;Oyster Box;United Kingdom;Saint Brelade;La Route de la Baie, Saint Brelade, JE3 8EF, United Kingdom;49.1852357;-2.2001959;80;true;false;Seafood;The smart tableware gives a clue as to this restaurant’s owners: the famous Jersey Pottery. It’s light and airy and it sits on the promenade, with a terrace affording superb views over St Brelade’s Bay. Fish and shellfish lead the way, with oysters a speciality. The décor is stylish and the service, friendly.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17169;Chadwicks Inn;United Kingdom;Maltby;High Lane, Maltby, TS8 0BG, United Kingdom;54.5138643;-1.2791416;53;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Well-prepared dishes, a wide-ranging wine list and smartly attired staff add a touch of formality to this village pub – although the locals aren't forgotten and can still come just for a drink in the bar. The modern pub cooking comes in the form of colourful and eye-catching dishes that show a clear understanding of flavours, with steaks a feature. The ‘market menu’ available during certain hours offers great value for money, and their monthly wine tasting evenings sell out in no time.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17170;63 Degrees;United Kingdom;Manchester;104 High Street, Manchester, M4 1HQ, United Kingdom;53.4846455;-2.2367466;92;false;true;French;One glance at the menu and you could be convinced you're in Paris, not Manchester's bustling Northern Quarter. Courtesy of a French Chef-Owner, the menu is filled with the likes of escargots, chou farçi and crème brûlée, all of which are delivered with strong classical technique. Interestingly, there's also a burger section to the menu, where the likes of lobster and pigeon join the usual beef option. This is a family affair, with the Chef-Owner's son serving out front, and has the feel of a true neighbourhood restaurant.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17172;Stravaigin;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;28 Gibson Street, Glasgow City, G12 8NX, United Kingdom;55.8725799;-4.2825806;95;false;true;International;Their motto here is ‘think global, eat local’ and this clear to see from the menu, where their homemade haggis sits alongside an array of ingredients from multiple Asian cuisines – be it furikake from Japan, tom yum from Thailand or lentil dahl from India. A pleasingly unfussy quality runs throughout these dishes, which are tasty and carefully prepared. The ground floor has a shabby-chic café-bar style, while The Cellar is a more intimate affair.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17173;Roger Hickman's;United Kingdom;Norwich;79 Upper Saint Giles Street, Norwich, NR2 1AB, United Kingdom;52.6293694;1.2865265;73;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Personally run restaurant in a historic part of the city, with soft hues, modern art and romantic corners. Service is attentive yet unobtrusive. Cooking is modern, intricate and displays respect for ingredients’ natural flavours.;Air conditioning;[]
17174;Olive Branch & Beech House;United Kingdom;Clipsham;Main Street, Clipsham, LE15 7SH, United Kingdom;52.7342621;-0.5645082;18;true;false;Traditional British, Regional Cuisine;Characterful village pub made up of a series of small rooms which feature open fires and exposed beams. The selection of refined British dishes changes daily, reflecting the seasons and keeping things fiercely local. These are accompanied by real ales, homemade lemonade and vodka made from hedgerow berries. Bedrooms are cosy and thoughtfully finished.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17175;Brawn;United Kingdom;London;49 Columbia Road, Hoxton, London, E2 7RG, United Kingdom;51.5289184;-0.0702678;92;false;false;Traditional British;Offering a warm welcome and robust, flavour-packed cooking, this is the kind of place everyone needs in their neighbourhood. The passionate team run it with a relaxed, upbeat vibe – sit in the back room to enjoy the buzz from the kitchen – and serve reliably tasty food that evolves with the seasons. The interesting wine list includes a number of organic options, as well as smaller producers and a good choice of orange wines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17176;Melton's;United Kingdom;York;7 Scarcroft Road, York, YO23 1ND, United Kingdom;53.9508755;-1.0858284;57;true;false;Modern British;Just outside York's bustling city centre, you'll find this cosy neighbourhood restaurant where the walls are covered with murals of ingredients and happy diners. It's apt décor for a place with a passion for local produce and a warm, inviting atmosphere thanks to the long-serving team. The ambitious cooking is underpinned by the natural flavours of the high quality ingredients, and the strong classical technique of the experienced chef is evident – if a soufflé is available for dessert, make sure you order it.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17177;The Star Inn The City;United Kingdom;York;Lendal Engine House, Museum Street, York, YO1 7DR, United Kingdom;53.9605702;-1.0872808;80;true;true;Modern British;As locations go, this buzzy all-day brasserie is in a real gem – even in a city with as many pretty spots as York. Part of the same group as The Star Inn at Harome, this city centre spin-off occupies an old brick-built engine house next to the Museum Gardens, with large windows and a lovely terrace overlooking the river. The menu of carefully cooked dishes has a pubby base and blends modern execution with a pleasing gutsiness – underscoring it all is the top Yorkshire produce, with seasonal influences leading the way.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17178;Henry's;United Kingdom;Bath;4 Saville Row, Bath, BA1 2QP, United Kingdom;51.3863363;-2.362079;34;true;false;Modern British;The simplicity of its name is reflective of this laid-back bistro as a whole. It sits on a pretty pedestrianised lane and has a straightforward yet appealing interior, plus a lovely enclosed terrace to the rear. Chef-Owner Henry runs his restaurant with passion and pride, serving bright, modern dishes that change with the seasons. The lunch menu offers good value for money, while the tasting menus – including a vegetarian version – showcase the full range of Henry's talents.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17179;Socius;United Kingdom;Burnham Market;11 Foundry Place, Burnham Market, PE31 8LG, United Kingdom;52.9468604;0.7269786;70;true;false;Modern British;One meaning of the Latin word 'socius' is ‘sharing’, making it an apt name for this friendly restaurant that's best enjoyed with a group of friends and family so you can give the menu a thorough going over. The barn-like space is bright and airy, with seating on either a steel-framed mezzanine level or the smart ground floor where you can watch the chefs at work. The flexible, constantly evolving menu draws on a range of influences for the unfussy, flavoursome small plates – among which are a good selection of vegetarian choices.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17180;Potters;United Kingdom;Bude;2 Lansdown Road, Bude, EX23 8BH, United Kingdom;50.8293158;-4.5444353;78;true;true;Seafood;Nikki and her team extend a warm welcome to both locals and tourists visiting this striking North Cornish spot. Behind the scenes, Oly is hard at work in the kitchen, crafting attractive, well-balanced modern dishes which showcase the finest Cornish ingredients. Seafood is a particular focus, with the likes of tandoori monkfish and whole Cornish sole sitting alongside a choice of fish to be battered then fried. Be sure to try the cocktails too.;;[]
17181;Rules;United Kingdom;London;35 Maiden Lane, Covent Garden, London, WC2E 7LB, United Kingdom;51.5108177;-0.1230649;60;true;true;Traditional British;Rules delivers all the charm and character you’d expect of London’s oldest restaurant. Start with a drink upstairs in the glorious cocktail bar, before winding your way down to the ground floor with its assortment of rooms decorated with antique cartoons, drawings and paintings. The menu is unashamedly traditional – game from their own estate is a highlight, along with classics like braised rabbit, steak and kidney pudding, and classic desserts from the nursery end.;Air conditioning;[]
17182;Spring;United Kingdom;London;New Wing, Somerset House, Strand, London, WC2R 1LA, United Kingdom;51.5110502;-0.1185458;41;true;false;Italian;Sporting fresh, bright décor that's befitting of its name, Spring occupies an undeniably gorgeous room in the 'New Wing' of Somerset House, that for many years was inhabited by the Inland Revenue. Under the aegis of Chef Skye Gyngell, it serves unfussy, Italian-influenced and ingredient-led food that you feel is doing you good as you eat it. For great value, go for the midweek set lunch or the 'Scratch' menu composed of ingredients that would ordinarily be thrown away and featuring dishes like a bread and butter pudding made using 'yesterday's sourdough'.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17183;Donostia;United Kingdom;London;10 Seymour Place, Marylebone, London, W1H 7ND, United Kingdom;51.5146913;-0.1610148;90;true;false;Basque, Spanish;Perch at the counter or sit at one of the tables in this fun, warmly run little spot and enjoy a selection of pintxos and tapas inspired by the food of San Sebastián. House specialities such as gilda, bacalao and txuleta are always worth ordering. Just one dessert is offered, but when it’s Basque cheesecake as wonderfully creamy as this, who would want anything else?;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17184;Cartford Inn;United Kingdom;Little Eccleston;Cartford Lane, Little Eccleston, PR3 0YP, United Kingdom;53.860601;-2.8806338;60;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;Set on the banks of the River Wyre, this fine-looking inn is a continually developing business with many strings to its bow. The operation includes a deli, art gallery, farm shop, greenhouses and boutique bedrooms enlivened by the owner's eye for interior design. The cooking, meanwhile, is hearty, gutsily flavoured fare with a comfort food quality – meaning you could start off with French onion soup and finish with rice pudding. If you're feeling indulgent, check out the 'Premeditated Gluttony' section of the menu populated by the likes of fruits de mer and lobster thermidor.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17185;Salty Monk;United Kingdom;Sidford;Church Street, Sidford, EX10 9QP, United Kingdom;50.7029291;-3.2236177;68;false;false;Regional Cuisine;Set in an old 16th-century salt house, this long-standing, proudly run restaurant is a pleasant blend of the old and the new – and is the type of place that’s always evolving. Dine in either the Abbots Den or the Garden Room, and start with a small plates selection, followed by a flavour-packed, classically based main course. Alternatively, come down for a spot of afternoon tea. Extend your visit by booking one of the bedrooms, and be sure to make the most of the gym and hot tub in the garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17186;The Oystermen;United Kingdom;London;31-32 Henrietta Street, Strand and Covent Garden, London, WC2E 8NA, United Kingdom;51.511306;-0.1235163;68;true;false;Seafood;Covent Garden isn’t an area usually associated with independent restaurants but this bustling and modestly decorated little spot is thriving. From its tiny open kitchen come oysters, crabs and expertly cooked fish.;;[]
17187;Cambio de Tercio;United Kingdom;London;163 Old Brompton Road, South Kensington, London, SW5 0LJ, United Kingdom;51.4907285;-0.1837421;88;false;true;Spanish;With three restaurants within a stone’s throw of each other, Spanish-born owner Abel Lusa is well-known for promoting his native cuisine in this smart Kensington neighbourhood, and this is his flagship. The short, well-structured menu features all the favourites, from their house specialty – croquettes – and anchovies in pickled sherry to dishes to share such as Pluma Iberica. The wine list is a voyage around the wine-making regions of Spain, and service is friendly and engaging.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17189;Cinnamon Bazaar;United Kingdom;London;28 Maiden Lane, Strand and Covent Garden, London, WC2E 7JS, United Kingdom;51.5105785;-0.123701;24;false;true;Indian;Vivek Singh’s Covent Garden restaurant provides relaxed, all-day Indian dining in a bright, colourful space with a marketplace atmosphere. The extensive menus are influenced by the trade routes of the subcontinent, with twists that encompass Afghanistan, Punjab and the Middle East. Start off with a selection of snacks and chaat, before moving on to larger plates like lamb rogan josh ‘shepherd’s pie’, which has become something of a signature.;Air conditioning;[]
17190;Oak;United Kingdom;Bath;2 North Parade Passage, Bath, BA1 1NX, United Kingdom;51.3807226;-2.3583723;88;false;true;Vegetarian, Vegan;What started out as ‘Acorn’ has matured into ‘Oak’, where a sustainable ethos feeds into the tasty, original vegetarian and vegan dishes served in unpretentious bistro surroundings. When dining in the front part of the restaurant, you'll find shelves adorned with produce from their allotment just outside the city – which provides around 40% of their produce. The well-priced small plates are designed for sharing and a 5 course ‘feasting menu’ is available at dinner.;Brunch,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17191;Dartmoor Inn;United Kingdom;Lydford;Moorside, Lydford, EX20 4AY, United Kingdom;50.6480443;-4.0907429;59;true;false;Modern Cuisine;You couldn’t meet a friendlier family than the parents, daughter and son-in-law who run this rustic roadside pub. With its cosy, shabby-chic style, it's an undeniably charming and characterful place where everyone feels welcome. The bar area is filled with locals and their dogs enjoying a drink, while diners are spread across several dining rooms in which they enjoy the straightforward, satisfying cooking that derives plenty of flavour from the quality local produce.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17192;Box Tree;United Kingdom;Ilkley;35-37 Church Street, Ilkley, LS29 9DR, United Kingdom;53.9262052;-1.8258606;32;false;false;Modern British;This iconic Yorkshire restaurant was established back in 1962 and continues to draw in diners today. It’s set within two charming, 18th-century sandstone cottages, and has a plush, antique-furnished lounge and two luxurious dining rooms. The cooking these days comes in the form of a modern, creative tasting menu featuring dishes like their take on an 'arroz negro'. Service is formal and professional, while there's a choice between the 'Sommelier's' and 'Premium' wine flights to accompany the food.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17193;Forelles;United Kingdom;Ludlow;Fishmore Road, Ludlow, SY8 3DP, United Kingdom;52.3832203;-2.7143971;25;false;false;Modern Cuisine;An appealing conservatory restaurant offering lovely views over the hotel gardens and named after the pear tree just outside. Attractively presented dishes use local produce and modern techniques, and feature some unusual flavour and texture combinations.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17194;Bistrot Vérité;United Kingdom;Southport;7 Liverpool Road, Birkdale, Southport, PR8 4AR, United Kingdom;53.6342034;-3.0135881;65;true;false;Classic French;A friendly, bustling neighbourhood bistro, serving gutsy French dishes with a classic base, punchy flavours and the occasional international touch. It’s a family affair with Mum Michaela, Dad Marc and their sons all involved, either in the kitchen or front of house. Pop into their next-door bar, Petite Vérité, for pre or post-dinner drinks.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17195;Old Butchers;United Kingdom;Stow-on-the-Wold;7 Park Street, Stow-on-the-Wold, GL54 1AQ, United Kingdom;51.9290307;-1.7199744;95;true;false;Classic Cuisine;An old butcher’s shop with quirky décor, colourful chairs and ice bucket and colander lampshades. The menu offers plenty of choice, from old favourites to dishes with a Mediterranean slant, and the well-judged cooking comes with bold flavours and appealing textural contrasts. Save room for dessert!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17197;The Cadogan Arms;United Kingdom;London;298 King's Road, Chelsea, London, SW3 5UG, United Kingdom;51.4859343;-0.1729608;100;false;true;Modern British;There’s been a pub of this name here since 1838 and it has now been restored to its Victorian glory. Drinkers mingle with diners creating a real neighbourhood feel. The menu focuses on pubby favourites with a few retro classics thrown in and cooking is unfussy and eminently satisfying.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17198;Delaunay;United Kingdom;London;55 Aldwych, Covent Garden, London, WC2B 4BB, United Kingdom;51.5131075;-0.1180972;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Delaunay was inspired by the grand cafés of Europe but, despite sharing the same buzz and celebrity clientele as its sibling The Wolseley, is not just a mere replica. The all-day menu is more mittel-European, with great schnitzels and wieners.;Air conditioning;[]
17199;The Parsons Table;United Kingdom;Arundel;2 & 8 Castle Mews, Tarrant Street, Arundel, BN18 9DG, United Kingdom;50.854353;-0.555291;85;true;false;Modern British;This cosy little restaurant is named after its owners – an experienced husband and wife team who run it with passion and pride – and it’s clearly a hit with the locals. Confidently prepared, flavoursome dishes are founded on the classics and have a subtle modern style and an honest feel.;Terrace;[]
17200;Zoilo;United Kingdom;London;9 Duke Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 3EG, United Kingdom;51.5160566;-0.1521606;50;false;false;Argentinian;The menus at this lively grill restaurant explore seasonal ingredients and regional specialities from across Argentina. The wood-panelled room is dominated by a U-shaped bar counter and bright red studded banquettes, which provide a striking contrast to the checkerboard floor. Typical dishes include sea bream ceviche, steaks from the grill and slow-cooked shoulder of lamb. The all-Argentinian wine list offers a great range, with many wines available by the glass and carafe.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
17201;J.Sheekey;United Kingdom;London;28-32 St. Martin's Court, Covent Garden, London, WC2N 4AL, United Kingdom;51.5109299;-0.1277739;52;true;false;Seafood;Festooned with photographs of actors and linked to the theatrical world since opening in the heart of theatreland in 1896, J.Sheekey comes with a sense of exclusive intimacy thanks to soft lighting, wood-panelled walls and banquette seating. This Grand Dame of the West End is a seafood restaurant at heart, with everything from extravagant shellfish platters to their signature fish pie showing off high quality produce and accomplished technique. Despite the fishy bent, there's a strong offering for vegetarians.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17203;Yorebridge House;United Kingdom;Askrigg;Bainbridge, Askrigg, DL8 3EE, United Kingdom;54.3116282;-2.1033582;77;false;true;Modern British;This romantic restaurant sits within a stylish former schoolmaster’s house in the heart of the Yorkshire Dales, and offers lovely countryside views. Top quality British ingredients feature in attractively presented dishes with a personal twist. Book a bedroom with a riverside terrace and a hot tub.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17204;Scott's;United Kingdom;London;20 Mount Street, Mayfair, London, W1K 2HE, United Kingdom;51.5098559;-0.1507326;88;false;false;Seafood;Scott's is proof that a restaurant can have a long, proud history and still be fashionable, glamorous and relevant. It has a terrific clubby atmosphere and if you’re in a two then the counter is a great spot. The choice of prime quality fish and shellfish is impressive.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17205;The Butchers Arms;United Kingdom;Eldersfield;Lime Street, Eldersfield, GL19 4NX, United Kingdom;51.9720324;-2.2722511;16;true;false;Modern British;A thick wooden door salvaged from an old ship leads you into this sweet rural inn where hop bines vie for space with the locals’ tankards on low exposed beams. The menu is short but packed full of top quality seasonal ingredients and honest flavours lead the way. The friendly team create a warm, friendly atmosphere, and they serve the ales straight from the keg.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17206;Rocpool;United Kingdom;Inverness;1 Ness Walk, Inverness, IV3 5NE, United Kingdom;57.4767633;-4.2283313;31;false;true;Modern British;Occupying a prime spot on the banks of the River Ness, this enduringly popular restaurant is to be praised for its longevity. It's a bright and colourful, brasserie-style place where the experienced team deal well with their high turnover. The extensive menu offers something for everyone and a love for Scotland and its produce is never far away, despite regular Mediterranean influences – the North Sea halibut with Arbroath smokie risotto is all the evidence you need. This is also a perfect pit-stop if you're on the North Coast 500 road trip.;Air conditioning;[]
17207;Upstairs at the Mill;United Kingdom;Tuddenham;Tuddenham Mill, High Street, Tuddenham, IP28 6SQ, United Kingdom;52.3160944;0.5406956;99;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Plenty of original features have been left intact at this delightful 18th-century watermill. Downstairs is a stylish bar where the old workings are still in situ, while above this sits the beamed restaurant with black furnishings and its own share of characterful touches. Good quality seasonal produce is showcased in modern dishes available from both a tasting menu and an à la carte, with the chocolate marquise a great way to end if you get the chance. The attractive outbuildings play host to some of the bedrooms.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17208;Café Spice Namasté;United Kingdom;London;1-2 Lower Dock Walk, Royal Albert Dock, London, E16 2GT, United Kingdom;51.5055435;0.0748988;100;false;true;Indian;Owners Cyrus and Pervin Todiwala are charming, welcoming hosts who have formed part of London's Indian dining scene for decades. The current incarnation of their restaurant is located in the east of the city, occupying the ground floor of a modern apartment building in the Docklands development overlooking the Royal Albert Wharf. Cyrus and his kitchen team produce an extensive menu of colourful small plates to share, including a few dishes from Cyrus's native Goa.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17210;The Wilderness;United Kingdom;Birmingham;Unit B, 27 Warstone Lane, Birmingham, B18 6JQ, United Kingdom;52.4872516;-1.9104396;91;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Self-proclaimed as ‘rock and roll fine dining’, this dark and moody restaurant brings something a little different to the Birmingham food scene. The all-black colour scheme extends from the décor to the staff uniforms, while punk, metal and everything in between blares out of the speakers. The cooking, for its part, throws together an array of flavours in an imaginative, playful style. Accompany your tasting menu with either an interesting wine flight or creative non-alcoholic pairing.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
17211;Lovage;United Kingdom;Bakewell;Bath Street, Bakewell, DE45 1DS, United Kingdom;53.2142581;-1.674019;21;false;false;Modern British;The chatty, informative team are sure to put a smile on your face when they enthusiastically explain the modern menu of top quality, seasonal ingredients. The building was once a stable block and the lovely wood-panelled walls of this cosy, laid-back room are now a listed feature.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17212;The Pack Horse;United Kingdom;Hayfield;3-5 Market Street, Hayfield, SK22 2EP, United Kingdom;53.3805665;-1.9462118;83;false;true;Modern British;Real ales and weekly quiz nights help this traditional stone pub to remain a true village local. Hearty pub dishes come with a refined edge and the Manchester (Scotch) Egg has become something of a signature. Characterful open fires mix with warm, contemporary décor, and it’s run by a friendly team.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
17213;The Boat;United Kingdom;Lichfield;Walsall Road, Lichfield, WS14 0BU, United Kingdom;52.651783;-1.8892139;83;true;true;Modern British;This smart roadside hostelry continues to evolve with passionate chef-owner Liam Dillon at the helm. He has developed an on-site 'micro farm' where he keeps chickens and pigs, and grows fruit, vegetables and herbs. Outside the restaurant's own land, other local producers are used to power dishes like Staffordshire lamb with BBQ lettuce. Plenty of work goes into the cooking, with desserts such as cherry mousse with white chocolate and smoked hay ice cream standing out.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17214;Bhoomi Kitchen;United Kingdom;Cheltenham;52 Suffolk Road, Cheltenham, GL50 2AQ, United Kingdom;51.8916247;-2.0804437;80;false;false;Indian;You’ll receive a warm welcome at this sumptuous restaurant, run by the third generation of a family who settled here from India 50 years ago. The menu is mostly southern Indian with some BBQ dishes from the tandoor representing the north. Save room for the indulgent chocolate samosa.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17216;Fletcher's;United Kingdom;Plymouth;27 Princess Street, Plymouth, PL1 2EX, United Kingdom;50.368726;-4.1438327;29;true;true;Modern British;It may be just around the corner from the Theatre Royal, but this warmly run restaurant is so much more than a convenient spot to eat in before curtain-up. From the good value lunch menu to the à la carte, the eponymous chef-owner, who is a local himself, knows how to cater for all tastes – and it’s clear that plenty of care and attention go into every dish.;Air conditioning;[]
17217;Café Bohème;United Kingdom;Aberdeen City;21-23 Windmill Brae, Aberdeen City, AB11 6HU, United Kingdom;57.1447789;-2.1034327;71;true;true;Modern French;Tucked away in a city centre side street is this restaurant run by a friendly team with a genuine desire to please. Given the name, it's unsurprising to find a French bistro style to the décor, including simple wooden tables and wood panelling on the walls. The menu has a similarly Gallic influence, with time-honoured classics like pommes anna and crème brûlée to be found on the à la carte – yet there is a modernity and creativity in the cooking too, alongside technical skill from the kitchen team.;;[]
17218;Savoy Grill;United Kingdom;London;Strand, London, WC2R 0EU, United Kingdom;51.5103135;-0.1207042;89;true;true;French;There's something undeniably decadent about dining at this iconic restaurant. From the moment you enter via the hotel's beautiful lobby, the décor is elegant and opulent in equal measure with the chandeliers setting the tone for a dining room that's unsurprisingly popular with celebratory couples. The menu follows in these luxury footsteps, offering a mix of French and British classics that put premium produce front and centre, whether that be caviar, Dover sole or excellent quality beef for the signature Wellington.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17220;Asha's;United Kingdom;Birmingham;Edmund House, 12-22 Newhall Street, Birmingham, B3 3LX, United Kingdom;52.4814142;-1.9020201;49;false;false;Indian;Renowned Indian singer, actress and gourmet Asha Bhosle is the eponymous driving force behind a string of international restaurants, including this stylish, passionately run and deservedly packed spot in the heart of Birmingham. The extensive menus cover most parts of the Indian Subcontinent, with tandoori kebabs a speciality and no shortage of vegetarian options. Each dish is cooked with skill and provides serious flavour – such as the superior Muscat gosht, which is a recipe from Asha herself.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17221;Fish House Fistral;United Kingdom;Newquay;Unit 5, International Surf Centre, Fistral Beach, Headland Road, Newquay, TR7 1HY, United Kingdom;50.4190818;-5.0970634;25;false;true;Seafood, International;In amongst the beach shops of the International Surf Centre you’ll find this small bistro looking out over Fistral Beach’s golden sands towards a sea dotted with surfers. Blackboards announce the daily catch, with much coming from Newquay Harbour. Dishes are appealing and full of flavour.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17222;The Pem;United Kingdom;London;22-28 Broadway, Whitehall, London, SW1H 0BH, United Kingdom;51.4995386;-0.1328053;68;true;false;Modern British;Set in the elegant surroundings of the Conrad London St. James Hotel, The Pem is named after suffragette Emily Wilding Davison's nickname. Chef-Director Sally Abé’s experience shines through in cooking that's British in inspiration, using produce like Porthilly oysters and Cotswold venison. Dishes are contemporary in style and accomplished in technique, such as crisp red mullet with a powerful tomato, red pepper and pine nut sauce. Ask the personable sommelier for recommendations.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17224;Barrafina;United Kingdom;London;26-27 Dean Street, Soho, London, W1D 3LL, United Kingdom;51.5140705;-0.1326712;53;false;false;Spanish;This is the only Barrafina that doesn’t take bookings – but the one that invariably boasts the best atmosphere – and you can order drinks and snacks while you wait for a seat at the handsome L-shaped counter. The tapas menu is supplemented by an appealing little blackboard of the day’s best produce, which may include mackerel, carabinero or sardines. Sharing a tortilla is always a good start and then, if you look at what your neighbours are having, you’ll find yourself ordering more and more of the colourful dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17225;Claude Bosi's Oyster Bar;United Kingdom;London;Michelin House, 81 Fulham Road, Chelsea, London, SW3 6RD, United Kingdom;51.4933119;-0.1689085;90;false;false;Seafood, Classic Cuisine;What was once the garage forecourt of the stunning Michelin House is home to this reinvigorated neighbourhood restaurant with a bistro-like vibe. The signature oysters and fruits de mer platters are the eye-catching highlights, but the menu offers something for everyone, from salad Niçoise to the 'Bibendum burger'. Kick off your evening in style with an expertly made cocktail from the bar.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17226;The Pony Chew Valley;United Kingdom;Chew Magna;Knowle Hill, Newtown, Chew Magna, BS40 8TQ, United Kingdom;51.3499796;-2.5939492;34;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Featuring stunning views over the eponymous valley, this aptly named former pub now operates more as a restaurant. The short menu uses the seasons as a guide and showcases produce from the kitchen garden in vibrant, colourful dishes which mix creative and a few traditional elements. Themed menus and evenings are often centred around a particular ingredient or producer, be it a celebration of seafood or a cider pairing dinner. The midweek lunch menu offers great value for money.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17227;Wild Tavern;United Kingdom;London;2 Elystan Street, Chelsea, London, SW3 3NS, United Kingdom;51.4906591;-0.165942;24;true;true;Italian;Set overlooking the tiny Chelsea Green, this homely neighbourhood restaurant has the enticing feel of a warm Tuscan trattoria, with its waxed wooden floors and terracotta hues. True to the ethos of Italian cuisine, the dishes are ingredient-led and rely on the natural flavours of the produce – an approach extended to the raw bar of oysters, tartares and carpaccios. Alongside the prime cuts of meat and fish cooked over the grill, there are some terrific homemade pastas you'd be a fool to miss, especially the 'Tavern Tortelli' with Wagyu oxtail.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17228;Amazonico;United Kingdom;London;10 Berkeley Square, Mayfair, London, W1J 6BR, United Kingdom;51.5097693;-0.144974;15;true;true;South American;There is a tremendous sense of flair to this sexy, stylish restaurant with a party atmosphere. The glowing, flaming grills are an immediate eye-catcher, as is the jungle-inspired décor that combines with live music to make this the perfect place not just for a meal, but for a proper night out. Quality ingredients power the roster of South American dishes from tiraditos to tequeños. There's a small sushi selection available too, from the playfully named 'Japazonico' menu.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17229;MO;United Kingdom;Broadway;Willersey Hill, Broadway, WR12 7LF, United Kingdom;52.0408221;-1.8273467;41;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Situated inside the stylish Dormy House Hotel and tucked away behind its main restaurant is this intimate dining room that features just 12 seats around a U-shaped kitchen counter. The "chef's table" style experience is well-paced and anchored by the chefs, who serve and explain their dishes with an affable air. Top quality ingredients are at the heart of the colourful, creative dishes, with some well-chosen wine pairings to accompany. Confit egg yolk with parmesan custard is something of a speciality and ever-present on the menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17230;Louie;United Kingdom;London;13-15 West Street, Strand and Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9NE, United Kingdom;51.5129473;-0.1281792;42;true;false;French Contemporary;There’s a decidedly French feel to this smart brasserie spread over two floors. Sit downstairs during the week, where the elegant surroundings include a shellfish counter, banquettes and a lovely old jukebox. The more formal, intimate upstairs dining room opens at the weekend. The menu comprises skilfully cooked French-influenced dishes, including sharing options like sole meunière and côte de boeuf. Desserts are a straightforward, classic affair, with choices like chocolate fondant, tarte Tatin and a cracking pecan pie. Head up to The Alligator Bar for a cocktail after dining.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17231;Townsend;United Kingdom;London;Whitechapel Gallery, 77-82 Whitechapel High Street, London, E1 7QX, United Kingdom;51.5160655;-0.0701828;26;false;false;Modern British;Set within the Whitechapel Gallery, this small, light-filled room has a classic feel and is named in honour of its architect, Charles Harrison Townsend. The menu screams seasonality and flavours burst through – and while it’s evident there’s a confident chef at the helm, no dish is over-engineered.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17232;Cord by Le Cordon Bleu;United Kingdom;London;85 Fleet Street, City of London, London, EC4Y 1AE, United Kingdom;51.5139356;-0.1058925;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Famous for their cookery schools, Le Cordon Bleu also operate restaurants, including this one in a Grade II listed building originally designed by Sir Edwin Lutyens for the Press Association. The room is stylishly decorated in soothing blues and whites, and the impeccably attired chefs are on show in the glass-fronted kitchen. The cooking shows a strong classical bent, with dishes such as venison en croûte and a reimagined Black Forest gateau presented in an eye-catching, modern style.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17234;No. Fifty Cheyne;United Kingdom;London;50 Cheyne Walk, Chelsea, London, SW3 5LR, United Kingdom;51.4833362;-0.1694066;73;false;true;Modern British, Modern Cuisine;This brightly painted, flower-festooned former pub looks very much at home in its smart Chelsea location, and the indulgent theme carries on inside with plush dining spaces set over two floors. The menu offers hearty, modern British dishes, with fish and meats cooked over the grill a speciality. In true neighbourhood style, they also offer relaxed Saturday brunches and traditional Sunday lunches.;Air conditioning;[]
17235;The Bull's Head;United Kingdom;Craswall;Craswall, HR2 0PN, United Kingdom;52.0178815;-3.0537159;38;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;Nestled in a lush valley bordered by the Black Mountains, this former drovers' inn is separated from Hay-on-Wye by a six-mile single-track road. It retains a homely charm, boasting flagstone floors, slate walls and open fires. Unfussy, ingredient-led cooking is natural, wholesome and full of flavour, with meats from the owners’ farm, homemade charcuterie and a traditional roast on Sundays. Low intervention wines feature alongside a fine selection of beers. Book one of the cabins to allow more time for countryside exploring.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17236;Artis by Phelim O'Hagan;United Kingdom;Londonderry;29-31 Craft Village, Shipquay Street, Londonderry, BT48 6AR, United Kingdom;54.99682;-7.3204;25;true;false;Modern British;Latin for ‘craft’, Artis sits in the Craft Village area of the city and is, at its core, a celebration of local produce and trusted local suppliers. The two-roomed restaurant is serene in both atmosphere and decoration thanks to the warm service and neutral hues. Dishes are clean, contemporary and technically accomplished, and the desserts are always a highlight.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17237;Petersham Nurseries Café;United Kingdom;London;Church Lane, Richmond, London, TW10 7AG, United Kingdom;51.43615;-0.30933;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;As you sit in the greenhouse with sand at your feet, surrounded by fresh flowers which even in the winter months perfume the air, it feels as though all is right with the world. A unique spot within the capital's dining scene, this restaurant forms part of the wider Petersham Nurseries complex, where you can buy plants and homeware to spruce up your abode. The cooking is informed by their own fresh produce – try a seasonal vegetable medley to make the most of it – and has a clear Italian accent, from crudo to tortellini.;Terrace;[]
17238;Six Portland Road;United Kingdom;London;6 Portland Road, Holland Park, London, W11 4LA, United Kingdom;51.5071537;-0.2079135;29;true;false;European;Tucked away off Holland Park Avenue, this intimate neighbourhood bistro is sure to become one of your favourite haunts. The concise European menu changes according to the ingredients available and dishes are robust, skilfully constructed and easy-to-eat.;Air conditioning;[]
17239;Kanishka;United Kingdom;London;17-19 Maddox Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 2QH, United Kingdom;51.513141;-0.1418111;62;true;false;Indian;Owner Atul Kochhar’s signature style is writ large across the choice of menus at this smart Mayfair restaurant. Anglo-infused Indian dishes – epitomised by the signature chicken tikka pie – provide plenty of interesting options, with the north-east of India receiving particular attention. There’s a feeling of glamour to the surroundings that would suit a special occasion, and the ground floor is the most fun place to sit.;Air conditioning;[]
17242;Black Bear Inn;United Kingdom;Bettws Newydd;Clytha Road, Bettws Newydd, NP15 1JN, United Kingdom;51.7504756;-2.9277166;27;true;true;Regional Cuisine;There's a charmingly rustic feel to this smartly run rural inn close to the Victorian market town of Usk. A white-washed exterior, log-burning stove and wooden beams all add to the appeal, while the chefs do their part with a concise menu of well-executed, classically based cuisine. The fish cookery is a particular highlight, as evidenced by dishes like hake with a terrific butter sauce and capers. Everything is made in-house, including the ice creams and sorbets for dessert.;Car park;[]
17244;Edinbane Lodge;United Kingdom;Isle of Skye;Old Dunvegan Road, Edinbane, Isle of Skye, IV51 9PW, United Kingdom;57.4693765;-6.4318507;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The characterful Edinbane Lodge dates back to 1543 and is reputedly the oldest inn on Skye. The chef, a native, loves to use the best island and Highland produce – as well as local crockery – and the imaginative multi-course dinner menu showcases bold, natural flavours. Bedrooms have a subtle Scottish theme.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17245;The Hambrough;United Kingdom;Ventnor;Hambrough Road, Ventnor, PO38 1SQ, United Kingdom;50.5938225;-1.2054676;88;false;true;Modern British;Set within an intimate hotel, in the heart of historic Ventnor, The Hambrough is a modern, understated restaurant with a formal feel, offering commanding coastal views. Carefully prepared dishes use island grown and reared produce where possible, and natural flavours take the lead. Comfy bedrooms complete the picture.;Air conditioning;[]
17247;Chakana;United Kingdom;Birmingham;140 Alcester Road, Moseley, Birmingham, B13 8HT, United Kingdom;52.4482501;-1.887945;33;true;true;Peruvian;What was once a high street bank is now the ideal destination for a fun night out with friends. Chakana has all the ingredients you need for a great time: a lively laid-back vibe, punchy Peruvian food and one of the largest ranges of pisco in the UK. The cooking itself is colourful and packed with bold flavours, across a range of recognisable Peruvian dishes including ceviches and tiraditos. There's a streak of originality running through the menu too, as evidenced by the hot crab causa.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17248;Rothay Manor;United Kingdom;Ambleside;Borrans Road, Ambleside, LA22 0EH, United Kingdom;54.4264158;-2.9685916;87;false;true;Modern British;As the 'Manor' part of its name suggests, this is not just a restaurant but a country house hotel – a Regency-era one to be specific, located on the edge of pretty Ambleside in the Lake District. The elegant dining room sports original shutters and cornicing alongside bold William Morris wallpaper and striking chandeliers. The cooking is precise, technically ambitious and visually impressive, while being underpinned by classical elements like the Bordelaise sauce with fillet of Cumbrian beef.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17249;Angelina;United Kingdom;London;56 Dalston Lane, Dalston, London, E8 3AH, United Kingdom;51.5461568;-0.0712777;72;false;false;Italian, Japanese Contemporary;Few people would think of combining Italian and Japanese cuisine, but the unusual fusion works a treat at this fun neighbourhood spot owned by two friends. Sit at the marble counter to watch the chefs at work in the open kitchen, as they craft a kaiseki-style tasting menu which could include such creations as rosemary and nori focaccia or chawanmushi flavoured with datterini tomatoes. Keep an eye out for the pasta dishes, as they're a highlight.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17251;Fletchers;United Kingdom;Ripon;Ripon, HG4 3ET, United Kingdom;54.1188327;-1.6315481;56;false;true;Modern British;Tartan upholstery and woodpanelled walls lend a historic feel to this intimate restaurant inside the luxurious Grantley Hall hotel. The dining room boasts garden views and there’s a lovely terrace on which to enjoy an aperitif in the summer. The large menu is influenced by the local area and ticks all the boxes for unfussy, flavoursome food with dishes like cheese soufflé, beef Wellington for two and a choice of cuts from the Josper grill.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17252;The Ingham Swan;United Kingdom;Ingham;Sea Palling Road, Ingham, NR12 9AB, United Kingdom;52.7793812;1.543253;38;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This 14C thatched pub now houses a contemporary restaurant, although its low beams and stone walls remain. Service is friendly, and cooking uses the best of the county’s ingredients in a range of dishes, from the classics to those showing more imagination and flair. Smart bedrooms are available in the converted coach house and a nearby cottage.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17254;Number 20;United Kingdom;Port Mulgrave;20 Rosedale Lane, Port Mulgrave, TS13 5JZ, United Kingdom;54.5434538;-0.7761193;42;true;true;Seafood;Having previously run the nearby Fox & Hounds, Jason and Sue opened this homely little restaurant in the small coastal village of Port Mulgrave. Their concise, daily changing menus have a seasonal bent and a seafood bias, with Italian cuisine the guiding inspiration for many of the dishes. The result is a fresh, unfussy cooking style, which often incorporates produce prepared on the Josper grill.;;[]
17255;Sorella;United Kingdom;London;148 Clapham Manor Street, Clapham, London, SW4 6BX, United Kingdom;51.4638266;-0.13504;33;false;false;Italian;His years spent working on Italy’s Amalfi Coast inspired this operation from experienced London restaurateur Robin Gill. The menu is divided into the classic format of cicchetti, antipasti, primi and secondi, and the selection of dishes includes traditional heavy hitters like aubergine parmigiana, ossobuco and tiramisu. Make sure you kick off with some of the arancini though, as they're certainly a highlight. There's a great buzz to the place and the service is friendly.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17257;The Terrace;United Kingdom;Yarmouth;Quay Street, Yarmouth, PO41 0PB, United Kingdom;50.7062426;-1.5005889;43;true;false;Classic Cuisine;Head to the Wightlink ticket office, go up the external staircase and you will find yourself at this lovely harbourside restaurant. It's a large space with, as the name suggests, a wonderful terrace that's perfect for alfresco dining in the summer. Fish is to the fore on the classically based menu that makes the most of the island's ingredients and incorporates some dashes of creativity – such as the tongue-in-cheek 'crab and chips' consisting of crispy polenta fingers topped with fresh picked crab meat.;Great view,Terrace;[]
17258;Le Pont de la Tour;United Kingdom;London;36d Shad Thames, Butlers Wharf, London, SE1 2YE, United Kingdom;51.5037692;-0.0737293;95;false;false;French;Few restaurants in London can claim to have a better location than this. For over 30 years, Le Pont de la Tour has been wowing diners with its jaw-dropping views of Tower Bridge, best appreciated from the terrace on a warm summer's day. The restaurant itself, as the name suggests, is thoroughly French at heart: expect confidently executed classics from ratatouille Niçoise to gratin Normande. The carefully chosen wine list offers a broad and interesting selection, of both the classic and the esoteric varieties.;Great view,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17259;Whites;United Kingdom;Beverley;12a North Bar Without, Beverley, HU17 7AB, United Kingdom;53.8452844;-0.4363999;43;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Be sure to arrive early for drinks in the first floor lounge of this small, enthusiastically run restaurant beside the old city walls. Two surprise menus showcase Yorkshire produce in carefully crafted dishes with a modern heart. Eye-catching art punctuates the neutral walls.;;[]
17260;Bala Baya;United Kingdom;London;Arch 25, Old Union Yard Arches, 229 Union Street, Southwark, London, SE1 0LR, United Kingdom;51.5033081;-0.1017264;36;false;true;Israeli;The atmosphere is loud and lively at this infectiously fun restaurant celebrating the Middle Eastern heritage of its passionate chef-owner. The bright, modern interior is inspired by the Bauhaus architecture of Tel Aviv, while the counter is the best place to sit if you want to feel an even greater buzz and watch the chefs as they cook. Dishes are fresh, vibrant and designed for sharing, with the signature Cauliflower Steak Crumble proving an absolute treat that works wonders with an often overlooked vegetable.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17261;Tehran Berlin;United Kingdom;London;20 Rosebery Avenue, Finsbury, London, EC1R 4SX, United Kingdom;51.5236286;-0.1111689;82;true;true;Persian;This is an immeasurably likeable restaurant, where enthusiastic yet softly spoken Chef-Owner Yuma Hashemi – who was born in Tehran and grew up in Berlin – has gradually moved the influences from being French with a hint of Iranian to unashamedly and wholeheartedly celebrating Iranian cuisine. The multi-course surprise menu provides a great opportunity to sample a variety of dishes and this, many of which are inspired by Yuma's family recipes. The cooking, together with the warm service and quirky, characterful interior, ensures everyone has a good night.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17262;Moro;United Kingdom;London;34-36 Exmouth Market, Finsbury, London, EC1R 4QE, United Kingdom;51.525909;-0.108941;32;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Full of customers and full of life, with service that is engaging and on-the-ball, Moro remains as popular as ever and is the perfect fit for the increasingly busy Exmouth Market. The Moorish menu is full of interesting, flavour-packed dishes, but the wood-roasted options are the ones to go for. The open kitchen adds to the atmosphere of the animated room, and their next-door tapas bar, Morito, is also worth visiting.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17263;Roux at Skindles;United Kingdom;Taplow;Mill Lane, Taplow, SL6 0AG, United Kingdom;51.5241356;-0.7010845;96;false;true;French;You can't keep Alain Roux away from the banks of the Thames. Up the road from his famous Waterside Inn, he owns this contemporary brasserie and cocktail bar in a similarly pleasant riverside setting. The skill and confidence of the chefs is evident across the menu of traditional French and other European dishes, particularly in classical elements like the rich, meaty sauces. Arrive early for drinks on the terrace or in the cocktail bar, where they also serve a 'brioche and bubbles' menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17264;Orwells;United Kingdom;Binfield Heath;Shiplake Row, Binfield Heath, RG9 4DP, United Kingdom;51.5007231;-0.9114523;28;false;true;Modern British;Named after George Orwell, who spent his childhood in the area, this 18th-century building has the appearance of a rural inn from the outside, but once indoors you'll see it for the modern place it really is. Choose between the tasting menu and the à la carte to enjoy dishes mining quality British produce and vegetables from the team's own smallholding. They make their own honey, too, which is used in the signature 'Mill Lane Honey Sponge' dessert – a real treat to end your visit on.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17265;Sorting Room;United Kingdom;Cardiff;Parkgate Hotel, Westgate Street, Cardiff, CF10 1DA, United Kingdom;51.4792029;-3.1804359;94;true;true;Modern British;Set within an impressive, modish hotel, this elegant, brasserie-style spot boasts leather banquettes, attentive staff and a wide-ranging menu of British dishes. Smoked octopus would be a great way to start, while for main course Welsh beef is a real feature of the menu, whether it's steak and ale pie or Chateaubriand to share – and if you're celebrating a special occasion, consider the signature beef Wellington experience. If you've got a sweet tooth, finish with the tarte Tatin which is big enough to share... not that you'll want to.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17266;33 The Homend;United Kingdom;Ledbury;33 The Homend, Ledbury, HR8 1BP, United Kingdom;52.0382656;-2.4237209;96;false;true;Modern British;You'll find an abundance of homespun charm at this sweet, cosy restaurant run by a husband-and-wife team. Elizabeth warmly welcomes you into the 18th-century, Grade II listed building, while her husband James works alone in the kitchen. His concise menu is a masterclass in naturally delicious cooking that is free of frippery. Ingredients are sourced from trusted suppliers and delivered with excellent complementary flavours, be it Salcombe crab with punchy romesco or in-season deer with a deep, intensely flavoured faggot.;;[]
17267;Rebel;United Kingdom;Newcastle Upon Tyne;150 Heaton Park Road, Newcastle Upon Tyne, NE6 5NR, United Kingdom;54.9801604;-1.5864146;56;false;false;Modern British;Named after chef-owner Lindsay’s boyhood dog, this intimate, personally run restaurant has a quirky narrow shape, art by a member of the family on the walls and rustic wooden tables. The seasonal set menu offers small plates with a light, modern touch. The wine list includes some interesting organic and biodynamic choices, and it’s worth going for the pairings.;;[]
17268;Winslade Manor;United Kingdom;Clyst St Mary;Winslade Park Avenue, Manor Drive, Clyst St Mary, EX15 1FY, United Kingdom;50.7084643;-3.4494493;45;true;true;Modern British;A beautifully restored, early 19C manor house with 86 acres of grounds provides the lovely setting, while the food is ably taken care of by an experienced and very capable kitchen team. Local ingredients are used extensively in various menus that offer something for everyone and allow for plenty of flexibility. Desserts are a particular highlight. The terrace overlooks the gardens and cricket field.;Brunch,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17269;Barley Sheaf;United Kingdom;Gorran Churchtown;Gorran Churchtown, PL26 6HN, United Kingdom;50.2466209;-4.8082774;64;true;true;Modern British;This attractive 18C pub has a deceptively large interior, with a rustic, pine-furnished dining area, a capacious bar and space to dine upstairs too. The well-priced menu lists pub classics alongside more ambitious dishes and much of the produce comes from in and around the Roseland Peninsula.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17272;Zahter;United Kingdom;London;30-32 Foubert’s Place, Soho, London, W1F 7PS, United Kingdom;51.5138099;-0.1388359;42;false;false;Turkish;If you’ve just returned from Istanbul and want to keep that holiday spirit alive, then get along to this colourful Turkish restaurant just off Carnaby Street and sit at the counter for extra atmosphere. The chargrill and wood-burning oven are used to good effect, whether it's the potatoes with red onions or the prawns with chilli and garlic. Hummus comes with crispy fried chickpeas and is a great way to kick off, while the chicken thighs with peppers and tomato are succulent and flavoursome.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17273;Note;Ireland;Dublin City;26 Fenian Street, Dublin City, D02 FX09, Ireland;53.3416207;-6.2488931;59;false;false;Modern Cuisine;There’s a subtle retro touch to this enjoyable wine bar turned bistro. The cooking is modern yet unfussy and unpretentious, so don’t be surprised to find the likes of pork chops or date and toffee pudding on the menu. Bold, distinct flavours abound in dishes where the kitchen’s Irish influences often shine through. A charming team run the restaurant with a relaxed efficiency, and are always happy to recommend wines from their largely natural and organic selection.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17274;Sunday in Brooklyn;United Kingdom;London;98 Westbourne Grove, North Kensington, London, W2 5RU, United Kingdom;51.5152654;-0.1941137;37;false;true;American;If you’re hankering after a taste of New York City, then this London branch of a Brooklyn-based restaurant can provide it. In this relaxed all-day eatery, it doesn’t have to be Sunday for you to kick off your day with an American brunch favourite. Settle in later on for dinner and be treated to food prepared with care by a kitchen with an excellent understanding of flavour, all served by a lively, caring team. There’s also the option of delighting in one of the many cocktails being whipped up from behind the big, busy bar.;Air conditioning;[]
17276;The Grill;United Kingdom;London;53 Park Lane, Mayfair, London, W1K 1QA, United Kingdom;51.5070936;-0.152219;35;false;false;British Contemporary;The Grill at The Dorchester Hotel might be carrying a name loaded with history, but that’s no indication of the look or the food. Bright, modern décor and a formal team make you feel cossetted, while the ornate ceiling is something of a talking point. The cooking mixes classical flavours with modern techniques, on a menu that features luxury dishes to share like skate wing, rib-eye steak and 'all the chicken'. The set lunch menu offers value for money and they list some unusual wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17277;Lisboeta;United Kingdom;London;30 Charlotte Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 2NG, United Kingdom;51.518967;-0.1352423;60;true;true;Portuguese;This Fitzrovian funhouse is Chef Nuno Mendes’ ‘love letter’ to Lisbon and he’s on a mission to showcase its vibrant and varied food and wine cultures, and bring them to the attention of a wider audience. Come with a group of friends to best sample the array of petiscos, plates, pots and platters, all bursting with colour, freshness and flavour. The atmosphere is celebratory, lively and unabashedly noisy.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17278;Le Vacherin;United Kingdom;London;76-77 South Parade, Ealing, London, W4 5LF, United Kingdom;51.4962663;-0.2643282;74;true;false;French;With its part-mirrored walls, belle époque pictures and vintage brasserie styling, Le Vacherin brings a little bit of France to its West London neighbourhood. The menu has the classical French slant you would expect, allowing you to get your fix of 'escargots' or 'longe de lapin' without leaving the country. It's all fresh, flavoursome and prepared with obvious care, while the 'prix fixe' menu offers great value for money. The chateaubriand to share is a popular choice.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17279;Little Fish Market;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;10 Upper Market Street, Brighton and Hove, BN3 1AS, United Kingdom;50.8248829;-0.1573636;37;true;false;Seafood;As the name implies, fish is the focus at this unassuming restaurant, which is fittingly located in a converted fishmonger’s opposite the old Victorian fish market. For many years, passionate chef-owner Duncan Ray has been quietly cooking, refining and pushing his restaurant forward – and he is ever-present in the dining room, ensuring his guests are having a good time. The 6 course set menu is packed with skilful seafood cookery which demonstrates great balance and understanding of the ingredients.;;[]
17280;Robun;United Kingdom;Bath;4 Princes Buildings, George Street, Bath, BA1 2ED, United Kingdom;51.38528;-2.36123;52;false;true;Japanese;This skilfully run Japanese restaurant takes its inspiration from 19C author Kanagaki Robun, who is credited with introducing barbecued food to Japan. The cooking reflects his influence, with dishes from the robata grill forming the central part of a menu that is distinguished by fresh produce and an authentic approach. Excellent sushi and a strikingly presented afternoon tea also stand out on the vast menu.;Air conditioning,Notable sake list;[]
17281;Sheeps and Leeks;United Kingdom;Caernarfon;12 East gate Street, Caernarfon, LL55 1AG, United Kingdom;53.1408069;-4.2748736;15;true;false;Modern British;Named after two of the products for which Wales is best known, this unassuming former shop, tucked away in the town centre, features a ground floor kitchen and a basement restaurant with just six tables. Homegrown and local produce form the base of the set menu, where imaginative dishes show classic techniques and subtle global flavours.;;[]
17282;Black Salt;United Kingdom;London;505-507 Upper Richmond Road West, North Sheen, London, SW14 7DE, United Kingdom;51.4642176;-0.2742426;52;false;false;Indian;Little sister to Dastaan in Ewell is this modestly decorated neighbourhood restaurant with exposed brick walls, stripped wooden floors and blonde wood tables. Vibrant Indian cooking includes plenty of street food inspired dishes. Curries are highlight and the naan bread and kulfi are must-haves.;Terrace;[]
17283;Amuse by Kevin Dalgleish;United Kingdom;Aberdeen City;1 Queen's Terrace, Aberdeen City, AB10 1XL, United Kingdom;57.1434564;-2.1195243;27;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Kevin Dalgleish is a well-known chef in Aberdeen and his restaurant occupies the spacious basement of a granite townhouse, in a quiet residential neighbourhood yet just minutes from the city centre. Kick off with a drink in the bar or by the wood burning stove. The kitchen use prime Scottish ingredients blended with French techniques to create good-looking dishes that deliver on flavour.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17284;The Mount;United Kingdom;Henley-in-Arden;97 High Street, Henley-in-Arden, B95 5AT, United Kingdom;52.293915;-1.779259;20;true;true;Modern British;Renowned Midlands chef Glynn Purnell is behind this modern take on a characterful beamed pub, situated on one of the UK’s prettiest high streets. The contemporary renovation has been beautifully done and, while the elegant bar offers a great atmosphere and some bar snacks, diners should head to the bistro to enjoy everything from steaks and burgers to their signature black pudding scotch egg and a selection of pies. Prices are keen and service is on the ball.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17285;The Suffolk;United Kingdom;Aldeburgh;152 High Street, Aldeburgh, IP15 5AQ, United Kingdom;52.1516277;1.6013791;76;false;false;Seafood;With a terrific beachside location, this smart modern brasserie provides just what you want to see on a menu when you're beside the sea – fish and shellfish galore! Time-honoured techniques are used in reliably enjoyable classics like dressed crab and moules marinière, alongside daily fish specials such as pan-friend halibut with beurre blanc. To start, venture onto land with a dozen 'escargots' to share and, if the weather's good enough, make sure you grab a seat on the rooftop terrace that overlooks the beach.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17287;Ekstedt at The Yard;United Kingdom;London;3-5 Great Scotland Yard, Whitehall, London, SW1A 2HN, United Kingdom;51.5062794;-0.1262861;55;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Niklas Ekstedt’s first restaurant outside Sweden is this cosy, designer-rustic spot in the Great Scotland Yard Hotel. The chef has become synonymous with his wood-fired cooking techniques, so expect dishes cooked over or immersed into the embers – whether its seaweed-baked langoustine or pine-smoked wild duck breast. Plenty of pickled, fermented and cured ingredients also do their bit to transport Nordic flavours to central London. Choose between a 5 or 7 course tasting menu, or treat yourself at the Chef's Table for a special occasion.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17288;Oar;Ireland;Doolin;Toomullin, Roadford, Doolin, V95 KV02, Ireland;53.0206994;-9.3729124;49;true;false;Modern Cuisine;In the rural heart of The Burren, with views out towards the Cliffs of Moher, you’ll find this well-frequented restaurant with a clean, modern interior. The menu offers an appealing choice of dishes crafted using top-notch produce, which is treated with care and skill by the kitchen team. A few ambitious, adventurous flavour combinations might appear too, like mango with salmon. The friendly service and simply furnished bedrooms complete a rather charming picture.;Car park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
17289;Cavita;United Kingdom;London;56-60 Wigmore Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 2RZ, United Kingdom;51.5163517;-0.1493431;80;false;true;Mexican;Head to the basement bar for a cocktail before taking a seat in this bright, friendly ground floor restaurant with a view of the chefs at work in the open kitchen. The menu brims with punchy, vibrant Mexican choices, including raw dishes such as hamachi tostadas and street food options like a concise range of tacos. Make sure you bring some friends to make the most of the main course platters to share. There's an enticing brunch offering too, where the mezcal and margaritas are bound to be flowing.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Counter dining;[]
17290;Story Cellar;United Kingdom;London;17 Neal's Yard, Seven Dials, Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9DP, United Kingdom;51.5143012;-0.1260856;74;true;false;Modern British;A lively younger sibling to Story, this bistro de luxe in the heart of Covent Garden offers a relaxed experience with an emphasis on counter dining. There are tables available, but overlooking the open kitchen is the place to be for a view of the grill-centric cooking. The whole menu is so utterly enticing you'll have trouble choosing, but highlights include the sweet, luscious snail bolognese on toast and the signature rotisserie chicken brined in bacon stock. The combination of bold flavours, generous portions and consummate technical skill means you're sure to leave satisfied.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17291;The Twenty Two;United Kingdom;London;22 Grosvenor Square, Mayfair, London, W1K 6LF, United Kingdom;51.5119524;-0.1530629;61;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;There’s an appealingly secretive feel to the restaurant at this converted Edwardian house. Sitting in a prime Mayfair location, it’s also home to a private members’ club. The menu offers something for everyone, with its extensive selection of largely Mediterranean dishes, some of which are designed for sharing. Service is eager and on the ball.;Air conditioning;[]
17292;The George;United Kingdom;London;55 Great Portland Street, Regent’s Park and Marylebone, London, W1W 7LQ, United Kingdom;51.5176311;-0.141859;99;false;true;Modern British;This handsome, Grade II listed Victorian pub boasts original 18th century features including marble fireplaces and ornate plasterwork, bringing a fair amount of period charm to proceedings. The concise British menu offers dishes like beef & Guinness pie and rice pudding with rum soaked prunes, which are generously sized and eminently satisfying. The English-dominated wine list is another big draw.;;[]
17293;Sessions Arts Club;United Kingdom;London;24 Clerkenwell Green, Clerkenwell, London, EC1R 0NA, United Kingdom;51.5226283;-0.1061083;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Set on the 4th floor of an old courthouse, the old judges’ dining room is now a characterful restaurant which comprises a rather infectious mix of historical, elegant and shabby-chic. Cooking is vibrant, unfussy and flavour-led, with the mix of small and large plates arriving as they’re ready.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17294;“8” By Andrew Sheridan;United Kingdom;Liverpool;16 Cook Street, Liverpool, L2 9RF, United Kingdom;53.4063407;-2.9889165;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Chef-owner Andrew Sheridan relocated his immersive restaurant from Birmingham to this city centre Victorian property in his home town of Liverpool. Guests gather in the dimly lit lounge for drinks and precisely made snacks, before heading downstairs to one of the two 8-seater counters, each with its own chef. They cook in front of the guests and talk about the dishes, making for an engaging experience. The cooking takes influences from around the globe and showcases bold, distinct flavours, with quality produce underpinning it all.;Counter dining;[]
17295;Station Road;United Kingdom;Fort Augustus;The Lovat Hotel, Fort Augustus, PH32 4DU, United Kingdom;57.1436491;-4.6824823;70;true;false;Modern British;Their tagline, ‘taste nature’s larder’, says it all at this restaurant housed inside The Lovat Hotel, a lovingly restored country house at the gateway to Loch Ness. From locally foraged ingredients to the best Highland produce, dishes showcase Scottish ingredients in detailed, modern dishes that taste as good as they look. Charming and efficient service adds to the appeal.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17296;Mayha;United Kingdom;London;43 Chiltern Street, Marylebone, London, W1U 6LS, United Kingdom;51.5198677;-0.1554527;26;true;true;Japanese;There’s a real sense of style to this small Japanese restaurant that relocated from Beirut to London. The chic interior is dominated by a curved wooden counter where the chefs take centre stage, producing a highly seasonal omakase menu. Tree-inspired lights above the counter cast an intimate glow, while a sense of theatre runs throughout the dishes. Luxury ingredients are to the fore and the menu is dominated by a succession of sushi.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17297;The Crown at Burchetts Green;United Kingdom;Maidenhead;Burchetts Green Lane, Burchetts Green, Maidenhead, SL6 6QZ, United Kingdom;51.5246782;-0.7913463;35;true;true;Modern British;Experienced and capable Chef-Owner Dominic Chapman is at the helm of this charming pub serving food that is befitting of the setting. The rewarding, flavoursome dishes – like the delicious chicken liver and duck parfait with fig chutney – are a perfect match for the warm and comforting surroundings, while the kitchen adopts a seasonal approach to the produce used. For a great value option, go for the fixed-price 'village menu'.;Car park;[]
17298;Seacliff;United Kingdom;Berrynarbor;Sandy Cove Hotel, Old Coast Road, Combe Martin, Berrynarbor, EX34 9SR, United Kingdom;51.20742;-4.05367;48;true;false;Modern British;The family-run Sandy Cove Hotel is the home for this long-standing, intimate restaurant which comes with a jewel of a terrace and commanding views of the bay. The colourful, modern dishes make use of quality seasonal ingredients, with a focus on local seafood – the mussel-stuffed sea bream shows the kitchen at its displaying technical precision and a good balance of flavours and textures. The cooking comes in the form of a 6 course tasting menu – with wine pairings available – and the service is warm and friendly.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view,Terrace;[]
17300;Silver Birch;United Kingdom;London;142 Chiswick High Road, Chiswick, London, W4 1PU, United Kingdom;51.4928159;-0.253708;30;true;true;Modern British;Among the numerous eateries on bustling Chiswick High Street, Silver Birch stands out – thanks to its appealing dishes that celebrate the wonderful ingredients we produce in the British Isles, whether that be meaty smoked eel from Devon, sweet scallops from the Isle of Mull, creamy Shetland cod or superb Lancashire fruit. There’s also a good choice of sensibly priced wines by the glass or carafe to accompany these seasonal dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17302;Tillingham;United Kingdom;Peasmarsh;Dew Farm, Dew Lane, Peasmarsh, TN31 6XD, United Kingdom;50.9601961;0.6760094;17;false;false;Modern British;Nestled deep in the countryside is this 70 acre farm and wine estate with a shop, a tasting room, a restaurant and stylish bedrooms. Flavour-driven cooking focuses on pure, fresh tastes, with some produce coming from the estate. Interesting global wines, including their naturally produced selection, accompany.;Car park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17303;eleanore;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;30-31 Albert Place, Edinburgh, EH7 5HN, United Kingdom;55.9618082;-3.1797757;24;false;true;Modern British;With its friendly service and bright monochrome décor, there is a pleasantly relaxed feel to this neighbourhood restaurant and wine bar. The kitchen team take plenty of care in preparing a set menu of fresh-tasting dishes, with desserts proving a highlight – if you're lucky, you'll get to try the wonderfully indulgent tirami-choux. Dietary requirements are well catered for, with well thought out vegetarian and vegan menus available on request.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17304;MacNean House;Ireland;Blacklion;Main Street, Blacklion, F91 YK0F, Ireland;54.2911921;-7.881198;66;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It may be found in quite a remote area near the Irish border, but MacNean House is a destination in its own right. Run by celebrity chef Neven Maguire, it houses a cookery school, bedrooms and this perennially busy restaurant. There’s a plushness to the dining room and a degree of formality in the service that make it a popular choice for celebrating a special occasion, while the generous tasting menu offers attractive, detailed cooking. The finest Irish ingredients are used and there’s no shortage of flavour across the dishes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17305;Gregans Castle;Ireland;Ballyvaughan;Ballyvaughan, H91 CF60, Ireland;53.0768168;-9.1841644;64;false;true;Modern Cuisine;An attractive country house nestled in The Burren, Gregan’s Castle is an enviable location for a restaurant. It’s a luxuriously appointed place, with open fires, cosy sitting rooms and a charming bar. The equally impressive dining room is the stage for a menu based on produce from their own gardens and the surrounding area, such as some of the finest lamb in Ireland. The quality ingredients are expertly cooked and showed off in well-balanced dishes. Ask for a seat by the window to make the most of the fabulous views.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
17306;LIGИUM;Ireland;Bullaun;Slatefort House, Bullaun, H62 H798, Ireland;53.2368192;-8.5521841;78;true;true;Creative, Innovative;Lignum is Latin for 'wood' and, as such, it’s the ancient method of cooking over an open flame which takes centre stage at this immensely likeable restaurant. It's housed in a modern barn conversion which has a distinctly Scandic vibe, from the large windows and minimalist furnishings to the roaring fire and throws on the chairs. The wood-fired cooking lends a delicious smoky dimension to the creative dishes, which – informed by the chef's heritage – blend ingredients from Ireland (such as sweet lobster tail) and Italy (Amalfi lemon). It all comes in the form of a surprise tasting menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17307;The Little Chartroom;United Kingdom;Leith;14 Bonnington Road, Leith, EH6 5JD, United Kingdom;55.9725949;-3.1758674;15;true;false;Modern British;There’s an addictive buzz to this pared-back, Nordic-style restaurant on the outer fringes of Leith. The focus of the chic dining room is on a large open kitchen running across one side, where counter seats are available for those who like to be in on the action. Go for the full tasting menu to experience the breadth of the cooking, which ranges from subtle to bold flavours while always retaining a keen sense of balance. The ingredients are of great quality and frequently Scottish, like the plump, buttery scallops. The service comes with an endearing warmth.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17309;Lyon's;United Kingdom;London;1 Park Road, Crouch End, London, N8 8TE, United Kingdom;51.58373;-0.13063;23;true;true;Seafood;In many ways the ideal neighbourhood restaurant, this seafood-centric spot comes with sensible pricing, on-the-ball service and a warm welcome from its passionate owner. The cooking takes a sustainable, 'fin-to-scale' approach that's typified by their use of fish collars – an underappreciated ingredient finally allowed its moment in the sun here. While there are a few meat and vegetable options on offer, the focus is largely on eco-friendly fish and shellfish fashioned into understated dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17310;Ananda;Ireland;Dublin City;Cinema Building, Sandyford Road, Dundrum Town Centre, Dublin City, D16 VK54, Ireland;53.2878376;-6.241412;55;false;true;Indian;Its name means ‘bliss’ and this smart Indian restaurant certainly feels like a haven from the bustling shopping centre in which it sits. Accessed via a narrow entrance, it's a sizeable place inside with a swish cocktail bar – and is stylishly decorated with attractive fretwork and vibrant art. The combination of accomplished, original cooking and assured, attentive service makes for a great all-round package. The ‘Railway Journey’ tasting menu is encouraged and is certainly the way to go if you want to sample as much of the cooking as possible.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17311;The Peregrine;Ireland;Killarney;East Avenue, Killarney, V93 CF30, Ireland;52.0580641;-9.5052779;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the ground floor of the privately-owned Killarney Park Hotel is this elegantly dressed restaurant which comes with ornate cornicing and warm lighting. An oval-shaped cocktail bar sits at one end of the room – perfect for a pre dinner drink – while the horseshoe-shaped booths are the best seats in the house. The kitchen focuses its attention on quality produce from the county, with dishes that give the main ingredients the space to shine. If there's a pasta dish on the menu, be sure to order it.This restaurant is temporarily closed for refurbishment until April 2025.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17312;Purslane;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;33a St. Stephen Street, Edinburgh, EH3 5AH, United Kingdom;55.9578926;-3.206793;60;true;true;Modern Cuisine;An affluent area of the city plays host to this cosy, atmospheric basement restaurant which comprises just 9 tables. The experienced chef-owner creates ambitious modern dishes which mix tried-and-tested flavours with contemporary techniques. Service is friendly and the set lunch menu is steal.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17314;Alumni Kitchen Table;Ireland;Rathangan;Glenaree, Feighcullen, Rathangan, R51 RH90, Ireland;53.2346697;-6.9300156;62;false;true;Modern Cuisine;There’s something charming about this personally run rural restaurant with a contemporary feel. Stay the night in one of their four rooms to make a proper occasion of your visit and dine either around the eight-seater communal table or at the small open kitchen island. The balanced tasting menu is quite an immersive experience, featuring a range of inventive, adventurous dishes using some prime Irish ingredients. Well-crafted artisan crockery, locally made leather items, fine cutlery and a well-chosen wine pairing all enhance the experience.;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park;[]
17315;mae;Ireland;Dublin City;53 Shelbourne Road, Ballsbridge, Dublin City, D04 XC66, Ireland;53.3302119;-6.232041;52;true;false;Modern Cuisine;This cosy first-floor restaurant is hidden above the French Paradox wine shop, which not only gives it an appealingly secretive feel but also makes opting for one of the interesting wine pairings a wise move. The tasting menu begins with delicate snacks and fine daily-made sourdough, before offering a choice of main course and dessert. In game season, you'd be foolish to miss the exquisitely cooked sika deer and the tarte Tatin is Chef-Owner Gráinne's crowd-pleasing signature. The chefs show not just skill but generosity, so you'll leave feeling full and satisfied.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17317;Sucre;United Kingdom;London;47B Great Marlborough Street, Soho, London, W1F 7JP, United Kingdom;51.5144998;-0.138407;39;false;true;Latin American, European Contemporary;20 years after opening in Buenos Aires, Argentinian chef-restaurateur Fernando Trocca opened this buzzy restaurant in an attractive former concert hall in London. Contemporary Latin American inspired dishes are cooked over the open fire of the parrilla. Start with a drink in the moody basement bar.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17320;Vaughan's Anchor Inn;Ireland;Liscannor;Main Street, Liscannor, V95 FN5R, Ireland;52.9387993;-9.3909995;54;true;true;Seafood;A characterful family-run pub in a small fishing village. Nautical memorabilia lines the walls and along with the impressive fish tank, gives a clue as to the focus of the menu, where locally sourced seafood underpins the cooking. Bright, stylish bedrooms are hung with photos of local sights.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17321;CUT at 45 Park Lane;United Kingdom;London;45 Park Lane, Mayfair, London, W1K 1PN, United Kingdom;51.50647;-0.1517544;100;true;true;Meats and Grills;This sumptuous restaurant on the ground floor of the 45 Park Lane Hotel comes with moody décor, rich red leather backed seating and Damien Hirst artwork. Some of the best steaks in London – including British, imported USDA prime beef and Japanese Wagyu – are on offer alongside a premium wine list.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17322;Lemon Tree;Ireland;Letterkenny;Unit 32-34, The Courtyard Shopping Centre, Lower Main Street, Letterkenny, F92 EK13, Ireland;54.9485816;-7.7370088;79;true;true;Regional Cuisine;It might not be the most glamorous of settings, but you’ll certainly leave this established, family-run restaurant with a smile on your face. A brother, sisters and cousins all work together to deliver surprisingly modern dishes which draw from Donegal’s natural larder. The salted caramel tart is a must.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17323;Noci;United Kingdom;London;4-6 Islington Green, Islington, London, N1 2XA, United Kingdom;51.5358489;-0.1030015;84;true;true;Italian;Start with the delicious homemade focaccia and share some starters before ordering the USP: generous pasta dishes which invariably hit the spot, such as veal & pork Genovese ragu or brown butter cacio e pepe. The menus are fairly priced, as are the cocktails, making this a useful pitstop in this busy part of Islington. You’ll leave feeling sated and satisfied.;Air conditioning;[]
17324;Maria G's;United Kingdom;London;Coe House, 2-4 Warwick Lane, Kensington, London, W14 8FN, United Kingdom;51.4947238;-0.203767;30;true;true;Italian;Memories of living and working on the Amalfi Coast provided the inspiration behind this restaurant from chef Robin Gill. The short seasonal menu certainly follows the Italian culinary philosophy of using prime ingredients paired simply and intelligently to create complementary flavours. The room is stylish and there's also an intimate cocktail bar and a delightful garden terrace.;Air conditioning,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17325;The Oyster Club by Adam Stokes;United Kingdom;Birmingham;43 Temple Street, Birmingham, B2 5DP, United Kingdom;52.4804994;-1.8989336;22;false;false;Seafood, Oyster Specialities;The name says it all: this is a place that’s passionate about oysters. They arrive here from several sources, provide fresh, pure flavours, and are presented either natural or dressed. There’s a whole host of other top-notch seafood on offer too, in understated, classically based dishes like Dover sole with capers and brown butter. A choice of caviars and a fine selection of champagnes complete the checklist of luxury items, which is matched by both the plush downstairs dining room with marble-topped tables and the counter seating in Aphrodite's Bar above.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17326;Nopi;United Kingdom;London;21-22 Warwick Street, Soho, London, W1B 5NE, United Kingdom;51.5117674;-0.1385556;93;false;true;World Cuisine;It's not just fans of Yotam Ottolenghi and his cookbooks who have made his Soho restaurant so successful. The menu has something for everyone, featuring an array of flavoursome and colourful dishes, with influences from the Middle East, Mediterranean and across Asia. You can go for your own main course, like sea bass with coconut sauce Véronique, or share a few dishes, such as crispy mushrooms with basil aioli or succulent soy-glazed pork belly with pear mostarda. The room is bright and animated – and if you opt for one of the shared tables downstairs you can watch the kitchen team in action.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17328;The Dipping Lugger;United Kingdom;Ullapool;4 West Shore Street, Ullapool, IV26 2UR, United Kingdom;57.8952186;-5.1609228;85;false;false;Modern British;Named after a sailing vessel, this late 18C former manse sits right on the harbourfront and comes with luxurious bedrooms and a small restaurant with a charming vintage style. The friendly team serve a tasting menu to all tables at the same time and while dishes might appear simple, flavours burst through.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17329;Clarke's;United Kingdom;London;124 Kensington Church Street, Kensington, London, W8 4BH, United Kingdom;51.5070474;-0.1944819;79;false;false;Modern Cuisine;It's been over 40 years since Sally Clarke opened her eponymous restaurant, and the loyalty of her many regular diners is testament to the warmth of the place and her kind-hearted hospitality. The seasonal menu is a combination of British and Mediterranean influences, and the kitchen displays a light touch and a healthy respect for the quality ingredients, be it lemon sole or loin of fallow deer. If you want to take something home, check out her shop across the road.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17330;Number One;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;1 Princes Street, Edinburgh, EH2 2EQ, United Kingdom;55.9530474;-3.1898992;83;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Start your evening with an aperitif in the cosy cocktail bar of this plush restaurant inside the Balmoral Hotel, one of Scotland's most iconic buildings. Red lacquered walls and richly upholstered banquettes lend an air of luxury to the place, as do premium ingredients like N25 caviar and hand-dived Orkney scallops. There is a natural flow to the well-balanced dishes on the 7 course tasting menu, while the professional, well-paced service instantly puts you at ease.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17333;Collinsons;United Kingdom;Broughty Ferry;122-124 Brown Street, Broughty Ferry, DD5 1EN, United Kingdom;56.4668604;-2.877248;56;true;true;Classic Cuisine;You know what you're getting at Collinsons: an experienced chef showing his skill in delivering generous, consistently enjoyable dishes that are classic to the core. You're likely to find some of Chef-Owner Stephen Collinson's signatures recurring on the menu, like smoked haddock rarebit with leek or roasted venison with a port and cassis sauce. Whilst it may be tucked away down a quiet street, the restaurant itself is hard to miss thanks to its name etched across the floor-to-ceiling windows.;Wheelchair access;[]
17334;Yauatcha Soho;United Kingdom;London;15 Broadwick Street, Soho, London, W1F 0DL, United Kingdom;51.5137213;-0.1351392;39;false;false;Chinese;The ground floor of this lively, contemporary Chinese restaurant features cabinets full of pastries and chocolates – but ask to sit in the more atmospheric basement, with its celestial ceiling lights, tropical fish tanks and glimpses into the busy kitchen. The extensive menu offers something for everyone, and over-ordering is easy to do.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17335;The Sea, The Sea;United Kingdom;London;174 Pavilion Road, Chelsea, London, SW1X 0AW, United Kingdom;51.4936105;-0.1589574;72;true;false;Seafood;Part-fishmongers, part-seafood bar, The Sea, The Sea is located down a charming semi-pedestrianised mews off Sloane Square. The constantly evolving menu includes stripped-back fish and shellfish dishes that rely on the superb quality of the ingredients, with just a few well-judged accompaniments to help them sing. Some of the seafood is of prime freshness, some is dry-aged for extra depth of flavour – but it's all beautifully presented and naturally delicious. Sit on the terrace at lunchtime or in the understated interior in the evening.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17336;The French House;United Kingdom;London;49 Dean Street, Soho, London, W1D 5BG, United Kingdom;51.5127846;-0.1317553;19;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This historic Soho watering hole, once a favourite haunt of writers and artists such as Dylan Thomas, Brendan Behan and Francis Bacon, has only seven tables in its oxblood and wood-panelled upstairs restaurant. It’s run in a bohemian style and offers traditional, honest cooking with integrity and flavour.;;[]
17337;Dim Sum Duck;United Kingdom;London;124 King's Cross Road, King’s Cross, London, WC1X 9DS, United Kingdom;51.530205;-0.1164485;25;false;true;Cantonese;If you're thinking of eating at this small, family owned 'simple shop', do ensure you get here early as it doesn't take bookings and is deservedly popular. A one-hour wait is not unusual but the team manage the queue well and once you're sat either in the lively interior or under the pavement gazebo, you can dive into the wide-ranging Cantonese menu. The authentic dishes are carefully cooked using good quality ingredients, with bold and well-defined flavours present in options like the xiaolong bao and the cheung fun.;;[]
17338;Angela's;United Kingdom;Margate;21 The Parade, Margate, CT9 1EX, United Kingdom;51.3894195;1.3805686;37;false;false;Seafood;Set just off the esplanade is this understated little bistro with a fiercely local, eco-friendly ethos – even the tables are made of compressed recycled plastic. With no meat on the menu, dishes are centred around sustainably caught seafood, be it Dover sole with green sauce or turbot with tomatoes and capers. Simplicity is the key to the cooking, with the quality central ingredients allowed to shine thanks to just a few, well-judged accompaniments. The friendly service creates a pleasantly relaxed atmosphere.;Terrace;[]
17339;Little Hollows Pasta;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;26 Chandos Road, City of Bristol, BS6 6PF, United Kingdom;51.4681052;-2.6048548;28;true;true;Italian;Bristol's pasta-lovers are really being spoilt with this rustic bistro run by a charming and knowledgeable team. The pasta itself is freshly made in house each morning and then hung out in the window to dry, before being fashioned into bright, flavour-packed dishes. The options are often vegetable-centric, but do look out for the utterly delicious shellfish spaghetti. For dessert, it's all about the Italian classics, including a generously portioned pistachio tiramisu that will end your visit on a high. The set lunch menu is quite the bargain.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17340;1610 at The Globe Inn;United Kingdom;Dumfries;56 High Street, Dumfries, DG1 2JA, United Kingdom;55.0673111;-3.6096531;74;false;false;Modern Cuisine, Scottish;This historic pub – whose name references its origins – is well known as a favourite haunt of legendary Scottish poet, Robert Burns, and with over 300 whiskies available in the snug in which he held court, a drink here is a must. The vintage-style restaurant, with its Tam o’Shanter mural, is an atmospheric place to dine. The menu puts Scottish produce to the fore, and dishes are creative, modern, and full of colour and flavour.;;[]
17341;Mercado Central;United Kingdom;Cambridge;24 Green Street, Cambridge, CB2 3JX, United Kingdom;52.2064508;0.1186746;57;true;false;Spanish;Located a stone's throw from Trinity College, this brightly decorated townhouse is home to a Spanish restaurant exuding a warm, buzzy vibe – whether you admire the open-flame cooking on the ground floor or sit in the quieter upstairs dining room. Northern Spain has the largest influence on the menu, with Galicia and the Basque Country featuring prominently among dishes built around proudly sourced produce of great quality, such as wonderfully marbled presa Ibérica. Save room to finish with the 'tarta de Santiago'.;;[]
17342;Heathcock;United Kingdom;Cardiff;58 Bridge Street, Cardiff, CF5 2EN, United Kingdom;51.4964368;-3.2225833;22;false;true;British Contemporary;Run by the same team as The Hare & Hounds in Aberthin, this large neighbourhood pub is the kind of place that quickly becomes your favourite haunt. Simple and rustic in décor, the focus is on the eminently satisfying cooking, which has a strong nose-to-tail ethos resulting in dishes like confit pork belly with homemade black pudding and crispy ham hock. The menu of great value small plates changes daily, while pre-ordering the tasting option will ensure you sample the full range of the kitchen’s talents.;Terrace;[]
17344;Cantinetta Antinori;United Kingdom;London;4 Harriet Street, Belgravia, London, SW1X 9JR, United Kingdom;51.5001883;-0.1594754;28;false;false;Italian;The Antinori family have owned vineyards in Tuscany since the 12C, producing their own world-renowned red wine, as well as having a hand in numerous other estates. It should come as no surprise, then, that the wine list here is something to behold. It’s joined by classic Italian cooking, pairing a notable simplicity with plenty of Tuscan ingredients and rich, hearty flavours. The delicious torta caprese is a wonderful way to round out your visit.;Air conditioning,Credit cards not accepted,Interesting wine list;[]
17345;Plates by Purnell's;United Kingdom;Birmingham;121 Edmund Street, Birmingham, B3 2HJ, United Kingdom;52.4820898;-1.9008312;36;true;true;Spanish;Located just around the corner from Purnell’s, this tapas bar offshoot is a narrow, snaking spot with authentic Spanish cooking. Choose your selection of small plates from a seasonally informed menu filled with tapas favourites like gambas, croquetas and patatas bravas, where adept flavour combinations and seasonings run throughout. The added bonuses of welcoming service and competitive pricing could help to make this your new neighbourhood go-to.;Air conditioning;[]
17347;The Butcher's Tap and Grill;United Kingdom;Marlow;15 Spittal Street, Marlow, SL7 3HJ, United Kingdom;51.5724919;-0.776774;100;false;false;Meats and Grills;A part of the ever-evolving Tom Kerridge stable, this is one of his busiest spots and it's easy to see why. Friendly and laid-back, it's a 'does what it says on the tin' kind of place where meats of undeniable quality are given pride of place on the menu and on the butcher's shop counter. There are some well-made snacks to whet the appetite, but really this is all about the main event: pop in for a quick burger or stay a while and enjoy the premium cuts cooked to your liking, which might include Aberdeen Angus beef, Blythburgh pork or Suffolk Texel lamb.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17349;Gauthier - Soho;United Kingdom;London;21 Romilly Street, Soho, London, W1D 5AF, United Kingdom;51.5127211;-0.1315225;37;false;true;Vegan;Right in the heart of Soho is this charming Regency townhouse, offering intimate, formal dining spread that is rarely found in a fully vegan restaurant – yet it's just what Chef-Owner Alexis Gauthier has set out to achieve. His tasting menu combines original dishes – like kohlrabi with aubergine, kamalata olive, spring greens and confit lemon – with classical French touches such as Landes asparagus with morels and a rich, glossy sauce. The ‘Petit Dîner’ menu, served early evening and Saturday lunchtime, offers a shorter experience and good value.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17352;OXA;United Kingdom;Birkenhead;11 Rose Mount, Oxton, Birkenhead, CH43 5SG, United Kingdom;53.3819931;-3.0429614;95;true;true;Modern British;The pretty suburb of Oxton is home to this attractive neighbourhood bistro which offers an appealing selection of small plates and sharing dishes, as well as an excellent value lunch menu. Cooking has a British base and the occasional Asian touch, with dishes such as tuna with dashi and onions providing great depth of flavour. There’s a lovely atmosphere about the place and the interesting wine list features almost exclusively British choices.;;[]
17353;Akira;United Kingdom;London;Japan House, 101-111 Kensington High Street, Kensington, London, W8 5SA, United Kingdom;51.5015932;-0.19171;65;true;true;Japanese;Japan House promotes all things Japanese, so it’s appropriate that upstairs there’s a stylish, buzzing restaurant celebrating the country’s cuisine. The open kitchen is the focal point of the room, which offers both counter and table seating from which to enjoy the extensive selection of Japanese food. There’s a wide range of sushi, but it’s the skewers from the robata charcoal grill that are the highlight – such as asparagus wrapped with bacon or chicken and shiso meatballs.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted,Notable sake list;[]
17354;45 Jermyn St;United Kingdom;London;45 Jermyn Street, St James’s, London, SW1 6DN, United Kingdom;51.5079936;-0.1382966;39;false;true;Traditional British;Style and comfort go hand in hand at this bright, contemporary brasserie that delivers the classics with aplomb. The menu is a mix of European and British dishes, with the beef Wellington and lobster spaghetti both finished off at your table, while coupes and floats for dessert bring an old-school touch and pay tribute to its past as Fortnum’s Fountain restaurant. Slick service and the undeniably luxurious surroundings make a visit even more appealing, as does the extensive cocktail menu, which is well worth exploring.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17356;Cowley Manor;United Kingdom;Cowley;Cowley, GL53 9NL, United Kingdom;51.83054;-2.05273;54;true;true;Modern British;This restaurant inside a glorious Cotswolds country house hotel offers bold, vibrant cooking that’s worthy of the rather lovely setting. Start with a drink in the sleek bar, before settling in the panelled dining room that cleverly fuses its original features with more modern elements. The cooking has Mediterranean influences and uses British ingredients well, in dishes like the house-made taglioni with Cornish lobster and pickled chilli. For dessert, their fresh-out-the-oven madeleines are hard to resist.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17358;Embers;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;42 Meeting House Lane, Brighton and Hove, BN1 1HB, United Kingdom;50.8216934;-0.1405557;97;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Tucked away in the heart of Brighton’s famous Lanes, you’ll find this contemporary bistro with a big, wood-fired heart. Their ethos is all about sharing food with friends around a fire, with a menu that combines small plates like charred broccoli with centrepiece dishes for sharing, such as venison rump or whole sea bass. As you would expect, plenty of smoky flavour comes through in the well-executed, accessible dishes.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17359;Locanda on the Weir;United Kingdom;Porlock;Porlock Weir, Exmoor National Park, Porlock, TA24 8PB, United Kingdom;51.2087758;-3.5861149;39;true;true;Italian Contemporary;Set overlooking the 15C harbour at Porlock Weir, this relaxed, slightly quirky restaurant with rooms has just five tables. You'll be warmly greeted by manager Cindy, as well as chef Pio, who hails from Naples and brings influences from his upbringing to the daily 5 course tasting menu. Modern Italian dishes champion the produce of Exmoor, with some ingredients either foraged or grown in the garden. Pio’s cooking is creative and full of flavour, but at times takes an unfussy approach to allow the natural ingredients to shine.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17360;Faru;United Kingdom;Durham;29 Silver Street, Durham, DH1 3RD, United Kingdom;54.7762618;-1.5769045;20;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Its name comes from an old English word for ‘journey’, but there is something decidedly contemporary about this city centre restaurant – from the airy, pared-back interior to the on-trend open kitchen and terse menu descriptions. An antique stained-glass window adds character and makes a fine backdrop for the chefs as they show their immense talent across colourful, precisely executed dishes that utilise punchy flavours like pickled walnut, mushroom ketchup and sweet carrot purée.;Wheelchair access;[]
17361;MINE;United Kingdom;Falmouth;4 The Old Brewery Yard, Falmouth, TR11 2BY, United Kingdom;50.15719;-5.07231;86;true;true;Farm to table;Hidden away in an attractive courtyard, this rustic little bistro is well worth the climb up the steep High Street. It’s a cosy, welcoming place, where the informality contributes to a light buzz among the contented diners. An open kitchen allows for a good view of the classic, well-crafted cooking, which takes the form of a concise, regularly changing à la carte which relies on local produce. You'd do well to start with the fabulous crab fritter and end with the honey cake.;Terrace;[]
17363;Pignut;United Kingdom;Helmsley;12 Bridge Street, Helmsley, YO62 5DX, United Kingdom;54.2453695;-1.0603944;50;false;true;Modern Cuisine;With just seven tables, there is a cosy feel to this little restaurant with clean, unfussy décor. Dishes are fed by produce from the surrounding area, including Helmsley Walled Garden and the Castle Howard estate, while the tasting menu – available in 4 or 8 courses – begins with a ‘wastage’ dish which uses up offcuts from the other courses. The cooking showcases a range of textures and flavours, sometimes with an imaginative touch. Foraged cocktails, a short but appealing choice of wines and personable service round out the experience.;;[]
17364;Bramley;Ireland;Abbeyleix;10 Main Street, Knockamoe, Abbeyleix, R32 D8C0, Ireland;52.9128884;-7.3492737;37;true;false;Modern Cuisine;There’s an endearing quality to this characterful restaurant run by a young, friendly team and set inside a former garage and shop. The cooking champions the County Laois larder and other Irish produce, in satisfying dishes with tried-and-tested flavour combinations. At dinner, choose from the concise à la carte or sample the kitchen’s full range of talents with the 7 course tasting menu. Lunchtime is a slightly simpler affair and features daily specials.;;[]
17365;Skua;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;49 St Stephen Street,  Stockbridge, Edinburgh, EH3 5AH, United Kingdom;55.9580028;-3.2065969;47;false;true;Modern British;This tiny basement operation in the suburb of Stockbridge comes with dark, moody décor and impressive cooking from the get-go. The menu of rustic sharing plates pushes flavour-packed British ingredients to the fore and the dishes are pleasingly free of superfluous elements, with the signature fried chicken being a particular highlight. A carefully curated list includes a selection of natural wines, with those available by the glass listed on the blackboard. Cheery, well-organised service adds to the experience.;;[]
17367;The Lime Tree Inn;United Kingdom;Great Ouseburn;Branton Lane, Great Ouseburn, YO26 9RS, United Kingdom;54.0540231;-1.3257618;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This North Yorkshire village inn is a 'proper' pub run by a friendly team, so you’ll always find plenty of locals in the bar. The kitchen team work away behind a large glass window on vibrant, flavoursome dishes that marry together complementary local ingredients. Portions are generous and a tasting menu is available too if you want to experience a broader range of dishes. The site also houses seven bedrooms, making it a good base from which to explore York, Harrogate and Castle Howard.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17368;Boys Hall;United Kingdom;Ashford;Boys Hall Road, Willesborough, Ashford, TN24 OLA, United Kingdom;51.134629;0.8967702;69;true;true;Traditional British;Built in 1616 for the Boys family, this charming old house has been sympathetically converted into a hotel with eye-catching features at every turn, plus 3 acres of gardens and land. The restaurant sits in an extension to the main house and serves local Kent produce, with Romney Marsh lamb a firm favourite. Great wines, also from Kent, are available to pair with your food and, should you wish to grab a drink before dining, the grounds also house a pub with a terrace.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Terrace;[]
17370;Archway;United Kingdom;London;Arch 65, Queen's Circus, Wandsworth, London, SW8 4NE, United Kingdom;51.4773041;-0.1479417;96;true;false;Italian;As the name suggests, this restaurant is nestled underneath the railway arches close to Battersea Park and the chic Battersea Power Station development. You may hear the rumble of trains overhead, but it’s often replaced by the buzz of diners flocking here to try the rustic Italian cooking with an appealing simplicity. Their focaccia is a stand out, while dishes like charred octopus with paprika romesco sauce put quality ingredients front and centre. The personable, engaging service team will make your visit even more enjoyable.;Air conditioning;[]
17371;Forge;United Kingdom;Middleton Tyas;Middleton Lodge Estate, Kneeton Lane, Middleton Tyas, DL10 6NJ, United Kingdom;54.458091;-1.660081;86;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The sprawling Middleton Lodge Estate stretches out over 200 acres and today includes this creative restaurant which sits inside the forge that once served the estate. The tasting menu – which also comes in both vegetarian and vegan forms – features seasonal produce, including some grown on the Estate, where they even harvest their own honey and birch sap. The cooking demonstrates a strong grasp of balance and flavour, with dishes that allow these local ingredients to shine like the picture-perfect Reuben blackberry and pineapple weed tart.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17373;Charlie's;United Kingdom;London;33 Albemarle Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 4BP, United Kingdom;51.5091134;-0.1421625;77;false;true;Modern British;Located inside Brown's, a quintessential English hotel, this intimate restaurant is one of the most beautiful traditional dining rooms in London, thanks to the keen eye of hotelier and designer Olga Polizzi. Wood panelling and deep armchairs combine with bright splashes of colour, including animal-adorned wallpaper that pays homage to The Jungle Book, which was apparently written by Rudyard Kipling when he stayed at the hotel. The menu, overseen by Adam Byatt, is British with a Mediterranean slant, meaning you'd do well to order the homemade pasta.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17374;The Hoebridge;United Kingdom;Gattonside;Hoebridge Road East, Gattonside, TD6 9LZ, United Kingdom;55.6053541;-2.7251881;53;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This welcoming former inn represents a return home for its self-taught Chef-Owner, who grew up in this Scottish Borders village and even worked in this place as a youngster. After a stint in New York City, he and his partner are back to run The Hoebridge as a simple, stylish restaurant serving flavour-packed, internationally influenced dishes. Quality local ingredients form the basis of the dishes, which are carefully prepared with an ambitious touch. Ebullient service adds to the welcoming feel of it all.;;[]
17375;North Port;United Kingdom;Perth;8 North Port, Perth, PH1 5LU, United Kingdom;56.3983432;-3.4294376;22;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in an end of terrace cottage dating back to the 18C, this appealing restaurant blends its characterful, dark oak panelled walls and ceiling with a bright, contemporary look. Unfussy, modern cooking proudly name-checks Scottish ingredients and comes with plenty of flavour. Be sure to try their delicious homemade haggis.;Air conditioning;[]
17376;The Gaff;United Kingdom;Abergavenny;4 The Courtyard, Lion Street, Abergavenny, NP7 5PE, United Kingdom;51.8230372;-3.0176276;74;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Three converted sheds hidden away in the heart of town play host to The Gaff: a bright, airy restaurant with a high ceiling and contemporary art hung on white walls. Menus list an appealing selection of well-priced small plates, which range from deep-fried mackerel to local game.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17377;Maiden Arch by Robert Bryant;United Kingdom;Barnstaple;14 Maiden Street, Barnstaple, EX31 1HA, United Kingdom;51.0787097;-4.0591449;87;true;false;Modern Cuisine;What was once a pop-up is now this well-settled restaurant tucked down an alleyway. You enter into the bar – where champagne and oysters are available if you're feeling celebratory – before being led up the spiral staircase to a dining room where exposed brick walls and a vaulted ceiling lend a formality that's mirrored in the service. The eponymous chef-owner's confident, intricate cooking comes in the form of a tasting menu, featuring thought-out dishes that deliver on flavour thanks to their quality ingredients. Order the wine pairing to complete the experience.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17379;Henrock;United Kingdom;Bowness-on-Windermere;Linthwaite House, Crook Road, Bowness-on-Windermere, LA23 3JA, United Kingdom;54.3518525;-2.9131132;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Named after a rocky outcrop on Lake Windermere, this elegant restaurant sits inside the charming Linthwaite House hotel and is part of Simon Rogan's ever-evolving empire. The décor is minimal yet cosy, with plain wooden tables and lovely artwork on the walls. Simon's sustainable ethos is evident on the menu, with many ingredients in the colourful dishes coming from his 'Our Farm' estate and other produce – like Cartmel Valley venison – sourced in the local area. Warm, friendly staff enhance the experience.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17380;Osteria Lucio;Ireland;Dublin City;The Malting Tower, Grand Canal Dock, Clanwilliam Terrace, Dublin City, D02 DW90, Ireland;53.340176;-6.23943;44;false;true;Italian;Located under the railway arches, this elegant restaurant comes with a lively ambience and a roll-call of recognisable Italian dishes. You could start proceedings with bruschetta or arancini before moving onto a choice of pastas, while suckling pig cooked 'al forno' has become something of a signature. Each dish is prepared with care using quality produce and in turn delivers plenty of flavour. The food is accompanied by an all-Italian wine list and a good selection of cocktails.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17381;Pompette;United Kingdom;Oxford;7 South Parade, Summertown, Oxford, OX2 7JL, United Kingdom;51.778551;-1.2665748;57;true;true;French;Located in a lovely suburb is this neat, attractive modern brasserie run by an experienced chef and his welcoming wife. There are a few Mediterranean and North African influences on the menu, but the French basis is clear – as evidenced by classic dishes like fish soup with rouille, Gruyère and croutons. The cooking is honest, unfussy and full of flavour, and there's a good value ‘prix fixe’ on offer too.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
17383;Llewelyn's;United Kingdom;London;293-295 Railton Road, Hernhill, London, SE24 0JP, United Kingdom;51.45322;-0.10282;85;true;false;Traditional British;Sitting just outside Herne Hill station, with its large windows letting diners look out and passers-by to look in, Llewellyn’s feels like a proper neighbourhood restaurant at the heart of the local community. The menu offers an appealing mix of dishes with a Mediterranean accent which focus on the freshness of the ingredients, and service is young and endearing.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17384;Colbert;United Kingdom;London;50-52 Sloane Square, Chelsea, London, SW1W 8AX, United Kingdom;51.4927981;-0.1566213;34;true;false;French;With its posters, chessboard tiles and red leather seats, Colbert bears more than a passing resemblance to a Parisian pavement café. It’s an all-day, every day operation and the menu lists all the French classics, so you can pop in for breakfast or a croque monsieur or linger over a steak Diane.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17385;Roast;United Kingdom;London;The Floral Hall, Borough Market, Southwark, London, SE1 1TL, United Kingdom;51.505614;-0.0909216;33;true;false;Modern British;Of all the restaurants dotted in and around Borough Market, few are as heavily embedded in the famed food emporium as Roast. It sits inside the historic Floral Hall, with the large windows allowing for some fabulous people-watching among the market stalls below. The menu is British to its core, a fact easily identified by their signature dishes being a scotch egg and beef Wellington. And it will come as a surprise to nobody that the kitchen offers a good range of Sunday roasts, with six different variations to choose from.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17386;Trullo;United Kingdom;London;300-302 St Paul's Road, Canonbury, London, N1 2LH, United Kingdom;51.5462408;-0.1017896;31;false;true;Italian;A stalwart of the local dining scene, this split-level restaurant is a hit with the locals and has a true neighbourhood feel. An open kitchen contributes to the light, buzzy atmosphere and the casually dressed service team are a perfect fit for the style of the place. The daily changing menu of rustic Italian dishes makes great use of the charcoal grill and the delicious pasta is hand-rolled before each service.;Air conditioning;[]
17387;Spry;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;1 Haddington Place, Edinburgh, EH7 4AE, United Kingdom;55.9592261;-3.1838791;33;false;true;Modern British;Set on the ground floor of a classic Georgian house by the famous Leith Walk, this wine shop sells a wide selection of naturally produced, organic wines. You can enjoy them in-house alongside some delicious seasonal dishes, where you have the option to choose from the à la carte or go for the 5 course set menu. Owners Matt and Marzena are always on hand to offer advice, and also run a basement coffee shop and in-house bakery selling some delightful sourdough.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17388;Artusi;United Kingdom;London;161 Bellenden Road, Southwark, London, SE15 4DH, United Kingdom;51.4666764;-0.0727785;32;false;false;Italian;Peckham may not be the first place you expect to find the spirit of Italian cooking alive and well, but there's no denying the straightforward joys to be found at this enthusiastically run neighbourhood bistro – which is named after Pellegrino Artusi, who wrote ‘The Science of Cooking and the Art of Fine Dining’ back in 1891. It's a small, sweet restaurant where the cooking is simple, honest and downright delicious, with the homemade pasta a definite highlight. The prices are fair, the portions are generous and the flavours are abundant – what more could you ask for?;;[]
17389;Cabotte;United Kingdom;London;48 Gresham Street, City of London, London, EC2V 7AY, United Kingdom;51.5149597;-0.0917405;70;false;false;French;Classic French cooking yields plenty of flavour at this appealing bistro de luxe with distressed décor and plenty of rustic charm. Despite some seasonal Mediterranean touches, the Gallic influence is clear to see on the menu, so look out for dishes like pâté-en-croûte. Quality produce is key to the ingredient-led cooking, to which the chefs bring an assured, accomplished hand. It’s owned by two master sommeliers who share a passion for the wines of Burgundy, so the stunning wine list understandably offers a top-notch selection.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17390;Shikumen;United Kingdom;London;58 Shepherd's Bush Green, Hammersmith & Fulham, London, W12 8QE, United Kingdom;51.5043099;-0.2245985;86;false;true;Chinese;Set within the Dorset Hotel, Shikumen might not appear to be anything out of the ordinary – that is, until it comes to the food. Care and skill go into preparing a mix of regional Chinese and slightly westernised dishes. The balance of textures and flavours is excellent, and the dim sum are superb.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17391;Scully;United Kingdom;London;4 St. James's Market, St James’s, London, SW1Y 4AH, United Kingdom;51.508689;-0.1330677;87;false;false;World Cuisine;With a diverse heritage and having lived and worked all over the world, it's no surprise that Ramael Scully brings an array of international influences to his self-titled restaurant. From Malaysia to Moscow via India and China, you'll go on a culinary journey throughout the chef's complex and distinctive dishes. Unlike little else you'll find in the UK, the cooking has an appealing vitality thanks to its punchy flavours and the shelves laden with spices, pickles, preserves and oils. The tasting menu leads the way, but there’s also a shorter option available Tuesday to Saturday.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17392;Pig and Butcher;United Kingdom;London;80 Liverpool Road, Islington, London, N1 OQD, United Kingdom;51.5374182;-0.10684;45;false;false;Modern British;In-house butchered meats reign supreme at this rustic, mid-19th Century pub, which is filled with diners and drinkers alike, all contributing to the lively atmosphere. 'Seasonal' and 'British' are the guiding principles behind produce ranging from Aberdeen Angus to Sutton Hoo chicken. The deeply addictive beef dripping served with the bread is one of the highlights of the experience, but it faces stiff competition from the likes of melt-in-the-mouth braised short rib.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17393;Bull & Last;United Kingdom;London;168 Highgate Road, Dartmouth Park, London, NW5 1QS, United Kingdom;51.5588606;-0.1486784;40;true;false;Traditional British;Hearty British dishes which are big on flavour are the order of the day at this sympathetically refurbished Victorian pub. The ground floor bar has a lively buzz and the more sedate first floor dining room opens later in the week. The terrific mushroom tempura is a prime example of what this kitchen does well: straightforward, moreish dishes that come in generous portions. Lovely bedrooms and a friendly, attentive team complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17395;Cheal's;United Kingdom;Knowle;1630 High Street, Knowle, B93 0JU, United Kingdom;52.38897;-1.73504;50;true;false;Modern British;Behind the half-timbered walls of this stylish building lies a spacious restaurant that pays tribute to British culture, be it the Union Jacks on the curtains or the model Spitfire hanging from the ceiling. In the cooking, Chef Matt Cheal uses prime British produce from Cornish lamb to Orkney scallops for dishes that showcase his adept modern technique. Start your evening in style in the smart Warren’s Bar or, for a lighter meal, stay there all night to enjoy individual dishes from the tasting menu served as small plates.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17397;Bowleys at The Plough;United Kingdom;Trottiscliffe;The  Plough Inn, Taylor's Lane, Trottiscliffe, ME19 5DR, United Kingdom;51.3167674;0.3522124;67;true;true;Modern British;Tucked away down a narrow street, The Plough proudly declares that it is 'community owned, family run'. The community in question is the people of Trottiscliffe, who rallied round to buy and refurbish their local pub when property developers were circling. Among their number was the Yates family, who now look after this small restaurant offering a concise menu of carefully crafted, ambitious and classically based dishes. Local produce, some of it their own, informs the menus – even the butter is homemade.;Car park;[]
17398;The Blind Bull;United Kingdom;Little Hucklow;Little Hucklow, SK17 8RT, United Kingdom;53.3037152;-1.7543184;36;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Lucky Little Hucklow having a pub like this. The residents of this tiny village high up in the Peak District are fortunate to live near such a beautifully restored 12th-century inn. It's spread over two floors with an open kitchen upstairs and a rustic, cosy feel throughout. The concise menu moves with the seasons and incorporates international influences for some extra punch. If you want time to explore the nearby walking routes, book one of the lovely bedrooms in The Old Piggery, with the ground-floor rooms being dog-friendly.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17399;Minster Mill;United Kingdom;Minster Lovell;Minster Ridings, Minster Lovell, OX29 0RN, United Kingdom;51.7989946;-1.5400135;16;true;true;Modern British;This characterful, oak-beamed restaurant is set in a charming Cotswold stone building surrounded by beautiful gardens with a river running through them. The modern British dishes come with a creative touch and are prepared with care, letting the natural flavours and textures of the ingredients shine through. Smooth, attentive service adds to the experience.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17400;Chef's Table;United Kingdom;City of Bristol;1a Avon Crescent, City of Bristol, BS1 6XQ, United Kingdom;51.4471933;-2.6188089;70;true;false;Modern British;In the old part of the city close to the famous docks you’ll find this intimate, personally run, 2-room restaurant, with a small front terrace, a warm service team and a buzzing atmosphere. The two menus – most diners plump for the tasting menu – offer original, modern and sometimes intricate dishes, which are aesthetically striking and full of flavour.;Terrace;[]
17401;The Lanesborough Grill;United Kingdom;London;Hyde Park Corner, London, SW1X 7TA, United Kingdom;51.5026778;-0.1528138;56;true;true;Modern British;This ornately decorated restaurant sits at the heart of the Lanesborough Hotel. Its menu moves with the seasons, offering modern British dishes brimming with prime ingredients, and includes lighter options as well as plenty for carnivores. Old school desserts are delivered with a degree of refinement, as befits the surroundings. Weekend dinners come with musical accompaniment.;Air conditioning;[]
17402;Bay Horse;United Kingdom;Hurworth on Tees;45 The Green, Hurworth on Tees, DL2 2AA, United Kingdom;54.4859985;-1.5280997;82;true;false;Modern Cuisine;The jewel in the crown of this 15th-century coaching inn is its lovely garden and terrace, closely followed by its crackling fire for a warm winter's welcome. It's a smart, efficiently run but still relaxed and friendly pub, with serious modern cooking made up of many elements. The kitchen team show an ambitious edge, as well as strong classical technique underpinning the dishes – such as a finely made red wine sauce with grouse. If you want to extend your trip, settle in for the night at their cottage next door.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17403;Quaglino's;United Kingdom;London;16 Bury Street, St James’s, London, SW1Y 6AJ, United Kingdom;51.5075238;-0.1390203;54;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This colourful, glamorous restaurant manages to be cavernous and cosy at the same time, with live music and a late night bar adding a certain sultriness to proceedings. The kitchen specialises in contemporary brasserie-style food.;Air conditioning;[]
17404;Hakkasan Hanway Place;United Kingdom;London;8 Hanway Place, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 1HD, United Kingdom;51.5172066;-0.1316651;59;true;false;Chinese;The very first Hakkasan continues to offer a great night out, thanks to its moody, sensual looks and glamorous, energetic atmosphere. It's well-suited to both a romantic date or a group celebration, and it's certainly worth arriving early for a cocktail or two in the bar. Luxury Cantonese specialities are plentiful across the choice of menus, with the set 'Signature' options representing the best value for money.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17406;Café Deco;United Kingdom;London;43 Store Street, Fitzrovia, London, WC1E 7DB, United Kingdom;51.5201781;-0.1305118;47;true;true;British Contemporary;The chefs also get involved in the service here at this simply furnished, intimate restaurant. Their dishes are fresh, seasonal, appealingly straightforward and packed with flavour, whether that’s cured ham hock, a lovely smoked eel pie or their delicious chicken. It's one of those relaxed restaurants where you know you’re in the hands of a clued-up and experienced team.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17408;Chapter One;United Kingdom;London;Farnborough Common, Locksbottom, Bromley, London, BR6 8NF, United Kingdom;51.3659781;0.0531159;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;They’ve got a loyal following at this long-standing restaurant that offers an extensive and appealing menu of modern European dishes. The cooking has some light, delicate touches and prime British produce cooked on the Mibrasa grill is a feature, like Cornish monkfish or Angus rib-eye. It’s all delivered inside a property that dates back to the 1930s and there are subtle references to this period in the elegant décor. The service team bring an enthusiastic smile and real care to their work.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17410;Planque;United Kingdom;London;322-324 Acton Mews, Dalston, London, E8 4EA, United Kingdom;51.5383824;-0.0757892;94;false;false;Modern British;Set under two railway arches, this boldly styled restaurant is centred around a huge communal table. Listed in size order, the modern British dishes are far more complex than they first appear and show tremendous skill from the kitchen. They are often comprised of three main ingredients, all working in perfect harmony to achieve a great balance of flavours: succulent guinea fowl, for example, might be complemented by earthy Jerusalem artichoke and a hint of bitterness from radicchio. The interesting wine list has an emphasis on small-scale and low-intervention producers.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17411;Salt Yard;United Kingdom;London;54 Goodge Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 4NA, United Kingdom;51.5191707;-0.1364677;66;false;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Having opened it 2005, this buzzy basement restaurant was one of the first in the city to offer small plates and promote the sharing philosophy. Spanish and Italian flavours lead the way, with top-notch ingredients showcased in a mix of traditional and more imaginative dishes. Plenty of Spanish wines and sherries are there to accompany, and the serving team are enthusiastic and sincere. The booths at the back are a great spot.;Air conditioning;[]
17412;Chatora;United Kingdom;London;100 Kew Road, Richmond, London, TW9 2PQ, United Kingdom;51.4663122;-0.2978517;75;true;false;Indian;With dining on 3 levels and bifold doors leading onto a small terrace, you can sit somewhere different every time you come. The experienced owner and 3 chefs represent the North, East, South and West of India. Generously proportioned, original dishes are authentically spiced and burst with flavour.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17413;Jolene;United Kingdom;London;21  Newington Green, Islington, London, N16 9PU, United Kingdom;51.5511292;-0.0845716;75;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Traditional British;Jolene is the sort of place that we'd all love to have at the end of our street. It's a bakery first and foremost, selling wonderful pastries, biscuits and cakes – as well as delicious bread from flour they mill themselves. There's also a daily written blackboard menu of confidently executed sharing plates, with their house-made pasta something of a feature. The vibe is relaxed and the friendly service team will ensure you're well looked after. You can find more of the same at their Hornsey Road branch.;Air conditioning;[]
17416;Etto;Ireland;Dublin City;18 Merrion Row, Dublin City, D02 A316, Ireland;53.3381533;-6.2538545;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Etto means ‘little’ and this cosy, rustic restaurant close to the National Gallery certainly fits the bill. Start with a snack and a sherry before enjoying eye-catching, modern dishes which are generously sized and full of flavour. The comprehensive wine list has a focus on the Med.;Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17417;Pickle;Ireland;Dublin City;43 Lower Camden Street, Dublin City, D02 N998, Ireland;53.3340349;-6.2652091;47;true;false;Indian;The modest exterior of this restaurant belies the buzzing atmosphere within. It’s a busy spot and deservedly so, with fresh, vibrant dishes and a service team that do a great job of handling their huge popularity. With spices lined up on the kitchen counter, the chefs aim to marry Irish produce with Northern Indian techniques and flavours in what they sweetly call ‘pickle country’. There’s a good value midweek lunch menu on offer and a tasting menu at dinner alongside the à la carte.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17418;Apricity;United Kingdom;London;68 Duke Street, Mayfair, London, W1K 6JU, United Kingdom;51.5135637;-0.1511802;37;true;true;British Contemporary;Just yards from the bustle of Oxford Street is a veritable sanctuary of calm. Chef-owner Chantelle Nicholson’s bright and welcoming restaurant comes with delightful service and a menu that showcases seasonal British ingredients from small producers with whom she’s built strong relationships. Her green credentials are omnipresent and inform her every decision.;Air conditioning;[]
17419;Goldsborough Hall;United Kingdom;Goldsborough;Church Street, Goldsborough, HG5 8NR, United Kingdom;53.9992428;-1.4159153;91;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A pretty village plays host to this grand, 16C country house which is surrounded by delightful grounds. There might be a classically formal feel to the place but not when it comes to the food. Modern, French-based dishes are eye-catching, well-balanced and full of bold flavours, with a good mix of classic and contemporary techniques showcasing the skill of the team. Go for the tasting menu with accompanying wine pairings.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
17422;The Morrison Room;Ireland;Maynooth;Carton House, Carton Demesne, Maynooth, W23 TD98, Ireland;53.3905215;-6.5675043;44;true;false;Modern Cuisine;We all need a little luxury in our lives and this beautiful restaurant in the heart of the impressive Carton House mansion ticks all the boxes. The breathtaking room features a high curved ceiling, Greek Corinthian columns, ornate plaster cornicing and sweeping banquettes, while the menu matches it for opulence with an abundance of first-rate produce, be it Union Hall crab or Achill lamb. The cooking is rooted in the chefs’ strong classical technique, but some wildcard flavour combinations work wonders thanks to their fine judgement.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17423;Library Street;Ireland;Dublin City;101 Setanta Place, Dublin City, DO2 W3Y7, Ireland;53.3418922;-6.2564739;39;true;false;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;As you open the door to this trendy restaurant, you’re greeted by a lively buzz and smiling faces. Sit at the counter or one of the lovingly restored 100-year-old ash tables, while surrounded by laughter and contented chatter. The cooking comes in the form of a regularly changing menu of sharing plates, including options like roast lamb with kalamata olives and Jerusalem artichoke. Local ingredients are key to the bold, original dishes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17424;Birchwood;United Kingdom;Flimwell;13 Flimwell Park, Hawkhurst Road, Flimwell, TN5 7FJ, United Kingdom;51.052442;0.4545624;59;true;false;Modern British;Set in a sustainable business park in 46 acres of woodland, this bistro features communal tables and a lovely terrace overlooking the trees. The daily changing breakfast and lunch menu is informed by the owners’ sustainable ethos, the seasons and the surroundings, and dishes are fresh and full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17425;Homestead Kitchen;United Kingdom;Goathland;Prudom House, Goathland, YO22 5AN, United Kingdom;54.3954185;-0.7267045;43;false;true;British Contemporary;The North York Moors and their produce are the inspiration behind this charming little restaurant housed inside a rural, stone-built former farmhouse. Chef-Owner Peter Neville and his partner Cecily Fearnley show great pride as they enthuse about their sustainable philosophy. Local produce – be it Moorland roe deer, Whitby crab or any number of ingredients from the kitchen garden – is used in hearty dishes that pack a punch when it comes to flavour. Sauces and accompaniments are a particular strength of the kitchen.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
17427;Cyprus Avenue;United Kingdom;Belfast;228-230 Upper Newtownards Road, Belfast, BT4 3ET, United Kingdom;54.5959643;-5.8753155;27;false;false;Contemporary;You’ll find something for everyone at this appealing, all-day bistro. It’s an expansive place, with the booths and the lovely covered terrace among the most prized seats. There’s an extensive choice at breakfast, while at lunch and dinner, freshly baked breads come with delicious hop butter and are followed by a wide selection of hearty, robustly flavoured dishes – sweet-toothed diners shouldn't miss the opportunity to try the sticky toffee madeleines. There's a substantial plant-based offering too.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17429;'Seasgair' by Michel Roux Jr;United Kingdom;Fort William;Inverlochy Castle, Torlundy, Fort William, PH33 6SN, United Kingdom;56.8440758;-5.0539785;32;true;true;Modern French;‘Seasgair’ means ‘warm and cosy’ in Gaelic, and diners will certainly feel cosseted in the impressive Inverlochy Castle. The whole experience is like stepping back in time to the country houses of old. Begin with an aperitif in the Grand Hall, accompanied by live music, before taking your seat in one of the elegant dining rooms. A 5 course set menu is served to everyone at the same time with canapés on arrival. Michel Roux Jr’s influence on the menu sees classic French dishes combined with the Scottish ingredients.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
17430;Killiecrankie House;United Kingdom;Killiecrankie;Killiecrankie, PH16 5LG, United Kingdom;56.7449428;-3.7787146;83;true;true;Modern Cuisine, Scottish;A young couple swapped their city lifestyle for this period country house in the Cairngorms National Park, which they lovingly restored to fuse original and modern features. Arrive at 7pm for drinks before dining on a tasting menu of Scottish classics brought playfully up to date. Bedrooms are sumptuous.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17431;Cafe Cecilia;United Kingdom;London;Canal Place, 32 Andrews Road, Dalston, London, E8 4FX, United Kingdom;51.5343681;-0.0597475;35;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Don’t be fooled by the name, for this popular local spot is less a café, more a pared-back, industrial-style restaurant with a modern bistro feel. The chef previously worked at St John and the River Café, and now mixes these influences with his Irish heritage. The Guinness Bread ice cream is sublime.;Air conditioning;[]
17433;Lunar;United Kingdom;Stoke-on-Trent;World of Wedgwood, Barlaston, Stoke-on-Trent, ST12 9ER, United Kingdom;52.9531581;-2.1709803;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Housed in the former staff canteen of the ‘World of Wedgwood’, this vast restaurant is named after The Lunar Society of which Josiah Wedgwood himself was a founding member. Naturally, fine Wedgwood china and tableware is a feature – as are prime British ingredients. The hidden bar is a great place for a drink and the chef’s table looks through a large window into the kitchen so you can get a good view of the team in action. Do take the time to immerse yourself in the amazing visitor experience as a whole.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17434;Smoke;United Kingdom;Hampton in Arden;Shadowbrook Lane, Hampton in Arden, B92 0EN, United Kingdom;52.4263097;-1.7032342;48;true;false;British Contemporary;There’s an air of relaxed conviviality at this charmingly rustic restaurant, which sits in the former smokehouse – beside the kitchen garden – in the grounds of Hampton Manor. A seat at the counter means you can join in the buzz of the kitchen, but in summer it's hard to look past the charms of the greenhouse. The food celebrates seasonal produce and, while dishes may appear simple, they have a hidden creativity and harbour some punchy flavours. The small wine list offers interesting natural, biodynamic and orange wines.;Car park,Counter dining,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17435;Mulcahys;Ireland;Kenmare;Main Street, Kenmare, V93 W35F, Ireland;51.8797008;-9.5824583;51;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Having been a presence in Kenmare since 1995, this smart, warm restaurant has become a part of the town’s fabric, with plenty of the locals contributing to its lively atmosphere. Come for cocktails and snacks in the bar or settle in for the evening to enjoy a menu underpinned by local beef and seafood. There is a classic edge to the cooking, with options like beef Wellington and fish pie featuring among the flavoursome, carefully cooked dishes.;Air conditioning;[]
17436;Mr Fox;Ireland;Dublin City;38 Parnell Square West, Dublin City, DO1 X9TO, Ireland;53.3530044;-6.2647538;30;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A welcoming restaurant with a charming team and a lovely tiled floor, set in the basement of a striking red-brick Georgian house. The well-priced set menu showcases wonderful Irish produce and the tasty, modern dishes are skilfully enhanced by global flavours.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17437;Volpe Nera;Ireland;Blackrock;22 Newtown Park, Blackrock, A94 D780, Ireland;53.2876023;-6.1778717;58;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Nestled away in a small parade, the ‘Black Fox’ takes its name from its position midway between the suburbs of Blackrock and Foxrock. Split over two floors, the upstairs has a slightly plusher feel, while the atmosphere is livelier downstairs, in part thanks to the open kitchen. The menu evolves with the seasons, mixing Mediterranean influences like rabbit cavatelli with Asian elements like cep dumplings, across modern, flavoursome dishes. Service comes from a friendly and knowledgeable team, while a carefully curated wine list completes the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17438;Mamó;Ireland;Howth;Harbour House, Harbour Road, Howth, D13 E9H9, Ireland;53.387763;-6.0681404;35;true;true;Contemporary;An experienced couple run this friendly bistro located in a pleasant spot on Howth seafront. Irish ingredients are the bedrock of the menu, including Winetavern Farm pork loin from Wicklow and plenty of seafood from the harbour just over the road. This produce is fashioned into fresh, flavoursome dishes that are carefully cooked and neatly presented. Stick around for dessert, as it’s likely to be a highlight.;Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17440;104;United Kingdom;London;104 Chepstow Road, Bayswater, London, W2 5QS, United Kingdom;51.5187999;-0.1961301;51;true;false;Modern Cuisine;It might only have six tables but the cosy 104 certainly proves that great things can come in small packages. The Chef-Owner works alone preparing a surprise tasting menu of sophisticated dishes with smart flavour combinations and stand-out sauces. Underlining the modernity in the cooking, there is a pleasing simplicity to each dish, allowing superb luxury ingredients like Cornish turbot or Scottish XL langoustine to shine. For dessert, look out for the deliciously rich signature '104 chocolate bar'.;Air conditioning;[]
17441;Stove Bistro;United Kingdom;Belfast;455 Ormeau Road, Belfast, BT7 3GQ, United Kingdom;54.5754184;-5.9170734;20;false;false;Modern Cuisine;As you approach the top of the staircase leading to this first floor restaurant, you are hit by the buzz of happy locals, so book well in advance to secure yourself a table. The concise à la carte menu offers flavoursome, modish bistro dishes created using locally sourced produce.;;[]
17442;Stage;United Kingdom;Exeter;31 Magdalen Road, Exeter, EX2 4TA, United Kingdom;50.7210155;-3.5213384;23;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A fun, trendy spot set up on a budget by an enthusiastic group of young men known as the ‘Taco Boys’. Foraged ingredients and produce from the kitchen garden inform the daily changing, surprise tasting menus, and the original, modern dishes have bold flavours and contrasting textures.;;[]
17443;Tallow;United Kingdom;Southborough;15a Church Road, Southborough, TN4 0RX, United Kingdom;51.1624331;0.2548375;18;true;true;Modern Cuisine;You'll get a warm and friendly welcome at this cosy neighbourhood restaurant run by experienced couple Rob and Donna. Situated overlooking the green at Southborough, it's a rustic, homely place with an intimate chef's table counter upstairs if you're looking for a special occasion. Time and care is poured into every well-constructed dish, with each one showcasing the kitchen's strong knowledge of culinary techniques while delivering bold, hearty flavours.;;[]
17445;da Mirco;Ireland;Cork;4 Bridge Street, Cork, T23 H10E, Ireland;51.9014037;-8.4700136;76;true;false;Italian, Classic Cuisine;Transport yourself to Italy at this authentic osteria in the heart of the city, where light pours over the tightly packed tables and plants line the walls. Both Irish and imported ingredients feature in the rustic, no-frills dishes, with homemade pastas like spinach and ricotta cannelloni a particular highlight. The service is led by eponymous owner Mirco, who brings a chatty approach to this lively little spot.;;[]
17447;Peploe's;Ireland;Dublin City;16 St Stephen's Green, Dublin City, D02 KF34, Ireland;53.3394746;-6.2580684;51;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;An atmospheric cellar restaurant – formerly a bank vault – named after the artist. The comfy room has a warm, clubby feel and a large mural depicts the owner. The well-drilled team present classic Mediterranean dishes and an Old World wine list.;Air conditioning;[]
17448;Awabi;United Kingdom;Saint Helier;63 Halkett Place, Saint Helier, JE2 4WG, United Kingdom;49.1857448;-2.1044725;49;true;true;Asian;Owner and self-taught chef, Stephen, takes inspiration from his travels and discoveries across Asia when compiling the immensely appealing menu at this cute neighbourhood spot, which resembles something between a little bistro and an izakaya. There are lots of local ingredients, the bao buns are delicious, and be sure to end with the Japanese French toast.;Counter dining;[]
17450;Gwen;United Kingdom;Machynlleth;21 Heol Maengwyn, Machynlleth, SY20 8EB, United Kingdom;52.5906155;-3.8519926;53;true;false;Creative;This warm and welcoming restaurant from the team behind Ynyshir is more of a cousin than a little sister – thanks to the personality Chef Corrin Harrison brings to both his cooking and the service. After a drink in the wine bar, all eight guests are served together in the intimate dining room. The surprise tasting menu offers bold flavours, a good dose of creativity and no small amount of skill. The chefs chat away with diners as the thoroughly enjoyable evening just flies by.;;[]
17451;Olivomare;United Kingdom;London;10 Lower Belgrave Street, Belgravia, London, SW1W 0LJ, United Kingdom;51.4963229;-0.1473545;73;false;true;Seafood;Sardinian cuisine is the order of the day at this bright, well-run Belgravia restaurant. It’s been around for some time, which is a testament to the quality of the seafood-centric cooking. Whether it’s steamed mussels with garlic and parsley or monkfish with courgettes and lemon, the fruits of the sea are celebrated heartily – and the simplest dishes are often the best. Much of the high quality produce in the kitchen is also available to buy at their deli, Olivino, next door.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17452;Oarsman;Ireland;Carrick-on-Shannon;Bridge Street, Carrick-on-Shannon, N41 AK19, Ireland;53.9439762;-8.094859;54;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;This traditional family-run pub sits close to the river and is filled with pottery, bygone artefacts, fishing tackle and, of course, plenty of locals. Service is chatty, there’s a lovely deli, and they even have a lager brewed specifically for them. Flavoursome cooking uses local produce, with the fish dishes being a sure-fire hit, and all of the bread is home baked. The upstairs restaurant opens later in the week.;Terrace;[]
17453;Delahunt;Ireland;Dublin City;39 Camden Street Lower, Dublin City, D02 K277, Ireland;53.3344031;-6.2650559;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Delahunt must surely be one of the most charming and characterful restaurants in Dublin. Exuding a sense of history throughout its quirky interiors, this old Victorian grocer's shop is mentioned in James Joyce’s ‘Ulysses’, and what was once the clerk’s snug is now a glass-enclosed private dining room. The cooking itself is a showcase for Irish produce, such as fine lamb from The Comeragh Mountains served with a punchy black olive ketchup. As the evening draws to a close, retire to the 'Sitting Room' for a digestif.;Wheelchair access;[]
17454;Tannery;Ireland;Dungarvan;10 Quay Street, Dungarvan, X35 XN99, Ireland;52.088686;-7.6168504;50;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Close to the harbour sits this characterful 19C stone tannery that also houses a cookery school. Sit downstairs for small plates at the counter or head upstairs to the bright restaurant. The classically based dishes are generously sized and use good seasonal ingredients – don't overlook the specials either. Stylish bedrooms are spread across two nearby townhouses.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17455;Bay Tree;Ireland;Carlingford;Newry Street, Carlingford, A91 V054, Ireland;54.0405525;-6.1866525;29;false;true;Modern Cuisine;This honest little neighbourhood restaurant sits on the bustling high street of a small town, just a stone’s throw from Carlingford Lough. The carefully prepared dishes are hearty and well-balanced, often featuring vegetables from the garden and seafood from the lough – including its renowned oysters. A range of Asian influences are also on display, be it rogan josh curry or char siu pork belly. Simple, cosy bedrooms are on hand for those staying the night.;;[]
17456;Imperial Treasure;United Kingdom;London;9 Waterloo Place, St James’s, London, SW1Y 4BE, United Kingdom;51.5079066;-0.1329154;94;true;false;Chinese;The first London outpost of this globally renowned group is housed in an imposing former bank, which provides a luxurious backdrop for the traditional, mostly Cantonese cooking. White leather, onyx walls and wood partitions provide some intimacy amongst the opulence, and the extensive selection of dishes offer ample flavour. If you’re after money-is-no-object luxury, look no further than their signature Peking duck with caviar, but you'll still have a great time with the crispy pork belly and honey-glazed char siu pork.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17457;Land to Sea;Ireland;Dingle;John Street, Dingle, V92 ET22, Ireland;52.1404179;-10.266645;78;false;true;Irish;Proving to be one of the most aptly named restaurants in Ireland, the menu here showcases fine produce from the surrounding fields and nearby waters. The kitchen team take advantage of Kerry meats and wonderfully fresh fish and shellfish with dishes that have a strong classical base and demonstrate a good understanding of flavour. Charming service enhances the overall experience.;;[]
17458;Wild Flor;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;42 Church Road, Brighton and Hove, BN3 2FN, United Kingdom;50.8272917;-0.1680673;100;true;true;Modern British;A group of lifelong friends own this relaxed neighbourhood restaurant, and they lead the service with obvious pride. The room takes on a modern bistro style and there’s a pleasingly unpretentious feel to the place. Well-prepared, seasonally changing dishes – try the goose rillettes with redcurrants in the winter – have a similarly unfussy style and good depth of flavour.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17459;Kildrummy Inn;United Kingdom;Kildrummy;Kildrummy, AB33 8QS, United Kingdom;57.2411621;-2.89312;98;true;true;Modern British;There is a luxurious feel to this smartly renovated pub, where the cooking mixes the modern with the traditional. Among the well-executed dishes on the menu are some contemporary choices alongside recognisable classics like rib-eye steak, fish & chips and chicken liver parfait. Come at lunchtime to enjoy their classically served haggis, neaps and tatties, which is a real treat. Four bedrooms, cosy sitting rooms and an immaculate terrace complete the very pretty picture.;Car park;[]
17463;The Old Bank;United Kingdom;Westerham;8 Market Square, Westerham, TN16 1AW, United Kingdom;51.2671088;0.0713048;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The contemporary interior of this former high street bank is a perfect match for the beautifully presented modern dishes. Cooking is technically accomplished and flavour combinations display depth and sophistication. You can visit the old vaults to sample wines suggested by the sommelier.;Wheelchair access;[]
17466;Rhosyn;United Kingdom;Penally;Penally Abbey, Penally, SA70 7PY, United Kingdom;51.6608644;-4.7236532;99;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Rhosyn means ‘rose’ in Welsh and there are plenty on display in the gardens of this lovingly restored country house. The gorgeous setting provides a calming atmosphere in which to dine, with a tasting menu or an à la carte to choose from. The seasonally guided cooking is modern in execution but rooted in tried-and-tested flavours we all know and love. Pembrokeshire is well-represented on the menu, so look out for delicious local lamb and some superb new potatoes.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view;[]
17468;Pizarro;United Kingdom;London;194 Bermondsey Street, Southwark, London, SE1 3TQ, United Kingdom;51.4985152;-0.0812194;71;true;false;Spanish, Mediterranean Cuisine;José Pizarro has a refreshingly simple way of naming his establishments: after José, his tapas bar, came Pizarro, a larger restaurant a few doors down. A selection of small plates – like croquetas, boquerones and padrón peppers – are joined by larger main courses including presa Ibérica, with dishes proving to be satisfying and cleanly executed. The surroundings are stylish and an all-Spanish wine list boasts some big names.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17469;La Potinière;United Kingdom;Gullane;Main Street, Gullane, EH31 2AA, United Kingdom;56.0349349;-2.8310224;91;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Classic Cuisine;An icon in the Scottish hospitality industry, this sweet little restaurant is run in a very personal way by owners Mary and Keith, who share the cooking and have showed great professionalism and dedication over the years. They offer a choice of two dishes per course, each prepared with care and pride. The cooking is traditional at heart with the odd ambitious edge, but with technique this accurate and ingredients this delicious, there's really no need for unnecessary frippery.;Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17470;Arros QD;United Kingdom;London;64 Eastcastle Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1W 8NQ, United Kingdom;51.5167086;-0.1371011;88;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine, Rice Dishes;Rice, and lots of it, is what you can expect to find at this huge, strikingly decorated restaurant from the mind of Spanish Chef Quique Dacosta. Specifically, the menu offers an array of takes on the classic Valencian paella, from pork knuckle to tofu & sea lettuce, but plenty of other dishes are available too, including several cuts of meat and fish cooked over fire. There’s a real theatrical element to the place, so ask for a table on the ground floor where you can watch the action in the open kitchen and see the flames from the wood-fired stoves.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17471;Naïfs;United Kingdom;London;56 Goldsmith Road, Peckham, London, SE15 5TN, United Kingdom;51.4756;-0.06501;93;true;true;Vegan;Owned and run by an alumnus of Vanilla Black, this friendly neighbourhood spot serves solely vegan dishes. The restaurant is simply decorated, with an on-view kitchen, and from here come hearty, original plates full of bold flavours. The set menu makes good use of what's in season and is served all at once, served 'family style' to be shared by the whole table. A few small plates and snacks are available too if you want to enhance the experience.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17472;Little Social;United Kingdom;London;5 Pollen Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 1NE, United Kingdom;51.5136076;-0.1422522;49;false;false;Modern British;Little Social has a clubby, comforting feel and a smart, stylish look, with on-trend copper, dark wood, and duck egg blue upholstery ensuring it fits in perfectly with its Mayfair surroundings. The seasonal British menu offers something for everyone, and its creative modern dishes are full of flavour.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17473;Water House Project;United Kingdom;London;1 Corbridge Crescent, Cambridge Heath, Hackney, London, E2 9DT, United Kingdom;51.5337216;-0.0587245;28;false;true;Modern British;As soon as you walk into this calm, Nordic-style restaurant with an open kitchen and smiling team, you just know you’re going to have a good time. Sit back and enjoy the house aperitif and some fabulous snacks before beginning a tasting menu founded on the finest British ingredients. The produce is treated with a deft touch in elegant dishes that offer refined, balanced flavours – such as West Country mussels with native seaweed and koji. The cooking can be accompanied by either a bespoke wine pairing or a homemade non-alcoholic option.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17476;Exmoor Forest Inn;United Kingdom;Simonsbath;Simonsbath, TA24 7SH, United Kingdom;51.1395676;-3.75473;20;false;false;Traditional British;There’s a rustic charm to this beautifully restored Victorian inn, where they make excellent use of the surrounding estate. The dishes are powered by organic produce from their own farms, which is then turned into a mixture of traditional and modern pub food. Generous and flavourful dishes do these local ingredients proud. A fire-lit lounge and 11 pleasant, relaxing bedrooms complete the package.;Car park;[]
17479;Furna;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;6 New Road, Brighton and Hove, BN1 1UF, United Kingdom;50.8229597;-0.1398026;67;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This stylish city centre restaurant is the first solo venture for Chef-Owner Dave Mothersill, who has been a fixture of the Brighton food scene for some time and brings an array of techniques to his precisely crafted dishes. The food is largely served by the proud chefs and focuses on seasonal British produce, with a few international influences and a creative edge. A chic mix of vintage and contemporary décor helps to enhance the experience, with counter seating available to make the most of the fully open kitchen.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17481;Norma;United Kingdom;London;8 Charlotte Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 2LS, United Kingdom;51.5183326;-0.1344273;74;false;true;Italian, Sicilian;This Fitzrovian townhouse has been transformed into a handsome, intimate restaurant spread over three floors, with Moroccan tiles and cosy booths. The food of Sicily and its Moorish influences inform the menu, with the 'primi' options including the dish that gave the restaurant its name: pasta alla norma. Generous portions add to the appeal, particularly the immensely satisfying fritto misto and the super-sized cannoli for dessert.;Air conditioning;[]
17482;The Small Holding;United Kingdom;Kilndown;Ranters Lane, Kilndown, TN17 2SG, United Kingdom;51.0918478;0.4269228;57;true;false;Modern British;There's a rustic, farmhouse-like feel to this former village pub run by two brothers. The team's focus is firmly on self-sufficiency, growing an array of fruit and vegetables on their own land, using no-dig and low-intervention methods. This seasonal produce heavily informs the monthly changing tasting menu, which blends British and Nordic culinary influences in dishes that have bold, well-balanced flavours and lots of personality. In summer, grab a seat on the terrace for an aperitif overlooking the garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17483;Aven;United Kingdom;Preston;10 Camden Place, Preston, PR1 3JL, United Kingdom;53.7546399;-2.7009533;92;false;false;Modern British;On the ground floor of the Winckley Stays Hotel, you’ll find this sweet restaurant where an open fire greets you on arrival in the colder months. There’s a cosy feel to the room, which is minimally decorated but enlivened by some bright artwork on the walls. The cooking takes the form of a seasonal tasting menu, with dishes like duck leg suet pudding delivering intense flavours. Friendly, efficient service enhances the experience, as does the choice between two wine flights and even a beer pairing.;;[]
17484;Orwell Road;Ireland;Dublin City;8 Orwell Road, Dublin City, D06 H2Y5, Ireland;53.3117205;-6.2745193;85;true;true;Irish, Modern Cuisine;Located in the city's smart suburbs, this buzzy little restaurant is a proper neighbourhood spot. Enjoy snacks and cocktails to start, before moving onto the menu of dishes founded on quality Irish ingredients. Each one is skilfully cooked and provides ample flavour, with the blackberry vacherin dessert a must-order if it's on the menu. It's a small place with a quick turnover of tables, but the chatty and efficient service team handle it with aplomb, making their fast-paced jobs look rather easy. The wine list includes some unusual but intriguing choices.;Counter dining;[]
17486;Aquitania;United Kingdom;Seaview;High Street, Seaview, PO34 5EX, United Kingdom;50.7204689;-1.1097587;60;false;true;Modern British;Named after an ocean liner known as 'The Ship Beautiful', The Aquitania is a delightfully intimate restaurant which upholds The Seaview Hotel’s proud culinary tradition. The team are warm and welcoming, and the wide-ranging menu bursts with the island’s artisan ingredients. As can be expected from a coastal restaurant, seafood plays an integral role, whether it's crispy crab beignets or a Friday fish & chips special.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17487;The Red Lion;United Kingdom;Freshwater;Church Place, Freshwater, PO40 9BP, United Kingdom;50.6843718;-1.5113036;51;false;true;Traditional British;It’s not just the open fires and friendly service that make this such a warm and welcoming pub – the delicious beef fat crumpet and the sticky toffee pudding also help! The traditional building has origins dating back to the 11th century, so it's a place full of character, with the garden also supplying super-fresh produce for the clean, well-executed dishes. While there are more informal 'light' and 'large bites' on offer at lunch, the à la carte is available at all times to show off the kitchen's skills.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17489;The Farmers Arms;United Kingdom;Woolfardisworthy;Woolfardisworthy, EX39 5QS, United Kingdom;50.9643463;-4.3769678;49;true;false;Modern British;Open fires and exposed timbers set against touches of contemporary design help make this restored Grade II listed pub, set in a delightful hamlet, a charming place for replenishment and recuperation. The frequently changing menu has an eye on sustainability and utilises quality ingredients from their farm, be it their own hogget or lemon verbena cleverly used to mimic the taste of lemon in a 'zero-mile' lemon geranium cake. Wonderful homemade syrups help create some refreshing aperitifs.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace;[]
17490;Levan;United Kingdom;London;12-16 Blenheim Grove, Peckham, London, SE15 4QL, United Kingdom;51.4696612;-0.0692098;17;true;true;European Contemporary;You can expect a good soundtrack playing over the speakers at this lively, friendly local restaurant named after DJ Larry Levan. The menu is a sharing plates affair – with dishes of mostly European influence – but there's also a tasting menu option, which allows you to sample more of the carefully prepared, original dishes. Be sure to start with the comté fries, and look out for the range of natural wines from smaller producers – more of which are available in Bar Levan next door. The friendly, attentive service team ensure there's a laid-back vibe to proceedings.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17491;Tytherleigh Arms;United Kingdom;Tytherleigh;Chard Road, Tytherleigh, EX13 7BE, United Kingdom;50.8257663;-2.9689222;88;true;false;Modern British;This sympathetically refurbished 16C coaching inn is an endearing place, with a characterful timbered interior that features a large inglenook fireplace. The cooking is best described as wholesome and boldly flavoured, with a menu that blends more modern dishes with pubby favourites like sirloin steak or haddock & chips. Stylish bedrooms await in the old stables if you fancy staying the night.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17492;Kutir;United Kingdom;London;10 Lincoln Street, Chelsea, London, SW3 2TS, United Kingdom;51.4916073;-0.1614972;45;false;true;Indian;A pretty end-of-terrace townhouse in an elegant Chelsea street is the setting for this relaxed, stylish Indian restaurant. There’s a lively buzz throughout the various smart yet cosy rooms, with the more intimate upstairs the best choice if you’re on a date. The interesting style of cooking draws from multiple regions of India and offers a wide choice of dishes, from tandoori broccoli to duck madras. The extensive choice of menus cater for a range of diners, with proper vegan and gluten-free options among them.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17493;Canton Blue;United Kingdom;London;1 Grosvenor Place, Belgravia, London, SW1X 7HJ, United Kingdom;51.5017552;-0.1524109;98;false;false;Cantonese;Housed inside the spectacular Peninsula Hotel, this Cantonese restaurant is part of a brand housed inside their hotels around the world. The London version boasts its own entrance at the side of the hotel and a sumptuous cocktail bar, Little Blue, which is the perfect way to kick off a rather glamorous evening. The restaurant itself is equally stylish, and the extensive menu offers a wide selection of authentic, flavoursome dishes, from finely executed dim sum to Peking duck for two. The interesting wine list includes a selection of Chinese rice wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
17494;1215;United Kingdom;Egham;Fairmont Windsor Park, Bishopsgate Road, Englefield Green, Egham, TW20 0YL, United Kingdom;51.4352157;-0.590014;80;false;false;Modern British;Named after the date of the signing of the Magna Carta 'down the road' in Runnymede, this elegant restaurant can be found in the slightly labyrinthine Fairmont Windsor Park Hotel. Choose from two lengths of tasting menu or the à la carte, all of which feature prime British ingredients like Suffolk lamb, Torbay crab and vegetables from their own estate. The chefs treat this produce with an unfussy approach, resulting in enjoyably pared-back dishes. Service is smooth and, if you’re dining as a couple, ask for one of the semi-circular booths.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17496;Giulia;United Kingdom;London;77 Askew Road, Shepherd's Bush, London, W12 9AH, United Kingdom;51.5042987;-0.243587;26;false;true;Italian;There’s an authentic, honest feel to this small Italian neighbourhood restaurant. The eponymous owner Giulia can be seen chatting away to guests in her native language and offering great hospitality alongside the cooking. Her partner Endris is in the kitchen following the ethos of pure, ingredient-led cooking with a seasonal focus. Pasta is offered as a separate course, including classic dishes like spaghetti alle vongole. The wine list is sensibly priced and, unsurprisingly, all Italian.;;[]
17497;Seasonality;United Kingdom;Maidenhead;26 Queen Street, Maidenhead, SL6 1HZ, United Kingdom;51.5219037;-0.7201551;62;false;false;Modern Cuisine;What started out as a produce shop has morphed into a bright and airy restaurant, which is run with a lovely personal touch by Chef-Owner Wesley as he cooks at an on-view island kitchen. As its name and history suggests, seasonal ingredients are the foundation of the cooking, put front and centre in assured, colourful dishes that carry an appealing clarity of flavour. Regular supper evenings offer tasting menus inspired by the produce of the moment, while they still offer the 'dine at home' boxes they've done since day one.;Counter dining;[]
17499;The Dory Bistro & Gallery;United Kingdom;Pittenweem;15 East Shore, Pittenweem, KY10 2NH, United Kingdom;56.2128697;-2.7275115;87;false;true;Seafood;Opposite the harbour in this little fishing village, you'll find a thoroughly charming restaurant where East Neuk produce is cooked with the care it deserves. Seafood dominates both the menu and the décor, with the restaurant walls doubling up as gallery space for plenty of aqua-based art. The blackboard is the place to look for fresh daily specials, like plump and juicy langoustines or hake with seaweed butter sauce. If you’re local to the area, this could quickly become a favourite haunt – you may even go home with some new artwork.;;[]
17500;The Wolseley;United Kingdom;London;160 Piccadilly, St James’s, London, W1J 9EB, United Kingdom;51.5074596;-0.1410245;52;false;true;European;Like the other restaurants in this group, The Wolseley serves classic European dishes in an elegant setting with a buzzing atmosphere – well-organised service ensures that everything runs like clockwork even in a packed dining room. The extensive menu features top quality seafood dishes, from clams and oysters to crevettes and caviar. The sweet-toothed among you will not be disappointed by a large dessert menu that includes apple strudel and a choice of coupes.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17501;Fallowfields;United Kingdom;Lizard;Housel Bay Road, Lizard, TR12 7PG, United Kingdom;49.9651083;-5.1969816;50;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Perched on a cliffside and boasting gorgeous bay views, this restaurant really does provide a setting to die for. It’s backed up by generous dishes that emerge from an open kitchen, served as either a short or long tasting menu. The cooking is detailed and creative, as evidenced by dishes like vodka-cured brill with ginger beer granita. Wine pairings are fairly priced and if there’s a chocolate dessert on the menu, you’re in for a treat.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
17502;Fish Shop;United Kingdom;Ballater;3 Netherley Place, Ballater, AB35 5QE, United Kingdom;57.0496443;-3.0396833;69;false;false;Seafood;From the genuine, professional service to the array of quality seafood, there is a lot to love about this smart restaurant decorated with a wicker shoal hanging from the ceiling and photos of fishermen on the walls. Fabulous produce, much of it Scottish, powers dishes that accentuate the flavours of their core ingredient with a few well-judged, finely made accompaniments – such as Shetland halibut accompanied by slow roasted tomatoes and salsa verde. As always with the best seafood restaurants, keep an eye on the specials board for more fresh delights.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Credit cards not accepted;[]
17503;enotèca;United Kingdom;St Aubin;Charing Cross, St Aubin, JE3 8AA, United Kingdom;49.187593;-2.1708384;60;false;true;Italian;Jersey meets Italy at this wine bar serving hearty, full-flavoured dishes in what was once a delicatessen. The owners run a business called Wild Wine, which imports natural wines from small producers – and a fabulous choice of these bottles is available to enjoy while dining. The pasta and gelato are both made in-house, and all the cooking is executed with such care. Keep an eye out for the blackboard specials.;Interesting wine list;[]
17504;Kicky's;Ireland;Dublin City;9 Castle House, South Great George's Street, Dublin City, D02 WK13, Ireland;53.3434817;-6.264568;60;false;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;A striking, pop art-style mural frames the kitchen pass at this casual, trendy and thoroughly lively restaurant. The airy interior features whitewashed brick walls, some counter seating and loud hip-hop. Start with ‘bites’ and small plates to share, before moving onto the concise selection of main courses cooked over charcoal. Fabulous produce like Wicklow venison and wild brill on the bone yields bold, satisfying flavours. Make sure you finish with the ‘Irish coffee’, their take on a tiramisu.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17505;Hearth;United Kingdom;City of Kingston-upon-Hull;10.5 King Street, City of Kingston-upon-Hull, HU1 2JJ, United Kingdom;53.7417859;-0.3360001;97;true;true;Modern British;Run by a trio of friends and located among some fine buildings in the old part of town, this buzzy spot operates over two levels. The ground floor houses a bar and bakery, while the upstairs is home to the rustic two-room restaurant. The menu fuses small plates with larger dishes, often coming from the grill – or ‘hearth’ – that takes centre stage in the open kitchen. Start with sourdough from the bakery, then make sure you check the boards for daily specials, as you might get to enjoy delicious seasonal produce like Yorkshire grouse.;;[]
17507;ÖRME;United Kingdom;Urmston;218 Church Road, Urmston, M41 9DX, United Kingdom;53.4438309;-2.3657578;86;true;false;Modern British;You will find a pleasantly welcoming quality at this small restaurant run by three young owners. There’s a distinct Nordic touch to proceedings, yet British produce is at the heart of the appealing tasting menus, available in 5 or 7 courses. Attractively presented dishes offer bold, vibrant flavours with a mix of the classic and the modern in their influences. Wine flights are also available, including a particularly interesting British themed option.;;[]
17508;Argile;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;21 Argyle Place, Edinburgh, EH9 1JJ, United Kingdom;55.9383455;-3.1915906;68;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Inspired by the sticky clay used for making pottery, the naming of this hidden-away neighbourhood restaurant feels rather apt given the wonderful array of china, pottery and earthenware they use. It’s an intimate operation with modern, sometimes technically complex dishes that draw on global influences. Chef-owner Jack Montgomery serves many dishes himself, pouring passion and a personal touch into the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17509;New Coast Kitchen;United Kingdom;Croyde;1 St Mary's Road, Croyde, EX33 1LF, United Kingdom;51.1308062;-4.2240974;58;true;false;Modern British;With its relaxed vibe and cheerful service, this is just the kind of restaurant you want to know about when on holiday around the North Devon coast. Head for the terrace out front in good weather – a perfect spot for people watching – or sit inside surrounded by the sleek, modern décor. The adventurous cooking is executed with flair and delivers well-judged combinations of bold flavours, as with the contrast between rich butter sauce and citrus marinated fennel in a wild bass dish. Save room for dessert too, as the confit apple terrine is a highlight.;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17510;Tamil Prince;United Kingdom;London;115 Hemingford Road, Barnsbury, London, N1 1BZ, United Kingdom;51.5409146;-0.1136925;76;true;false;Indian;It’s such an obvious pairing – a revived old neighbourhood pub with sharing plates of Indian food – that you wonder why there aren’t many more. The appealing menu is nominally inspired by Tamil Nadu but is not bound by its borders and does occasionally venture north. Highlights include Chettinad lamb curry and channa bhatura, while nothing goes with a pint quite like onion bhajis.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17511;Dilsk;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;44 Marine Parade, Brighton and Hove, BN2 1PE, United Kingdom;50.8194163;-0.1313419;85;false;true;Modern British;Visit this intimate and slightly moody spot inside the Drakes Hotel and you will likely be treated to some of the delicious, red-brown seaweed – more commonly known as dulse – after which the restaurant is named. Both the Short and Full tasting menus on offer include colourful dishes that are the epitome of modern British cuisine, like hogget with wild garlic and purple sprouting broccoli. The roster of well-chosen wines offers less-common choices that complement the food well.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17513;Atrium;United Kingdom;Upper Slaughter;Upper Slaughter, GL54 2JD, United Kingdom;51.9065774;-1.7745738;22;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Lords of the Manor is an appropriate name for a 17th-century Cotswolds hotel, and Atrium is an equally apt name for this restaurant located within the hotel's inner sanctum. A large skylight allows natural light to flood into the compact dining room, where diners are served a tasting menu all at the same time. The dishes come with attractive modern presentation and their greatest strength is in the natural flavours of the central ingredients, which are ably cooked by kitchen team. A wine pairing and overnight stay will make an event of your visit.;Car park,Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17515;Temple;United Kingdom;Bude;10 Granville Terrace, Bude, EX23 8JZ, United Kingdom;50.8291857;-4.5450401;99;true;true;Modern British;This chic, casually run eatery offers ethically sourced, modern rustic cooking in a lively setting. It’s a place of two halves, with the Temple Up Top bar and roof terrace the ideal spot to get the cocktails flowing. Downstairs is the restaurant, which operates more as a café in the day with a few small plates and cakes from the counter. At dinner, a fixed-price menu is served with a selection of snacks to start, followed by a choice of main and dessert. The provenance of the ingredients is paramount, and dishes are fresh, vibrant and full of flavour.;Terrace;[]
17516;Margot;United Kingdom;London;45 Great Queen Street, Holborn, London, WC2B 5AA, United Kingdom;51.5146995;-0.1217238;52;true;true;Italian;The service and the surroundings are equally slick at this plush Italian restaurant on the edge of Covent Garden. The menu offers an appealing choice of dishes, from simply prepared fish of the day to veal-based classics like ossobuco and vitello alla Milanese – and top quality ingredients and bold flavours run throughout. Take time to study the well-chosen wine list, which has a strong focus on the regional wines of Italy.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17517;Vanderlyle;United Kingdom;Cambridge;38 - 40 Mill Road, Cambridge, CB1 2AD, United Kingdom;52.2009825;0.134599;77;true;false;Vegetarian;A large, open-plan kitchen takes centre stage at Vanderlyle, which blends shabby chic styling with designer comfort. The well-balanced vegetarian tasting menu shows imagination and creativity, along with a passion for seasonal produce – all evident in dishes like roasted wild mushrooms with Roscoff onion and Bordelaise sauce. The friendly service team run the restaurant well and the wine or juice pairings enhance the experience. It’s a popular spot, so book in plenty of time.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17518;Twenty Seven;United Kingdom;Kingsbridge;9 Mill Street, Kingsbridge, TQ7 1ED, United Kingdom;50.2834524;-3.7778802;63;true;false;Modern British;Hidden away in a side street is this small and intimate restaurant which is run with infectious enthusiasm by its chef-owner – making it obvious why it’s such a hit with the locals. The split-level space includes characterful exposed beams in the upstairs dining room, while the cooking itself has an ambitious edge with roots in the county's seasonal larder. There are several menus available, from a tasting option to an à la carte, as well as fixed-price options offering good value for money.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17519;Hannah;United Kingdom;London;County Hall Building, Southbank Riverside, Belvedere Road, Lambeth, London, SE1 7PB, United Kingdom;51.5010272;-0.1186308;26;true;false;Japanese;Never judge a book by its cover – or a restaurant by its entrance! It may be quite quirky in its looks, but this sweetly run Japanese eatery provides an enjoyable and well-rounded omakase experience. It's led by Chef-Owner Daisuke Shimoyama, who shows off his impressive knife skills when preparing a procession of high quality ingredients, be it Wagyu beef, sea bream or lobster. The sake list provides the ideal accompaniment to the cooking.;Counter dining,Notable sake list;[]
17520;Decimo;United Kingdom;London;10 Argyle Street, King’s Cross, London, WC1H 8EG, United Kingdom;51.5296068;-0.1244107;62;true;true;Spanish;Cacti and succulents fill the room and a DJ adds to the buzz at this deliciously different 10th floor restaurant with commanding city views. Peter Sanchez-Iglesias blends the flavours of Spain and Mexico in appealing small plates, by drawing from his father’s Spanish heritage as well as time spent in Mexico.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17521;Bubala;United Kingdom;London;65 Commercial Street, Spitalfields, London, E1 6BD, United Kingdom;51.5179355;-0.0742101;98;false;true;Middle Eastern, Vegetarian;Start with a freshly cooked laffa flatbread and one of their delicious dips before feasting on Middle Eastern-inspired vegan and vegetarian sharing plates, which are elevated by their delicate spicing. Wines are mostly unfiltered, natural and orange – and service is charming and attentive.;Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17522;Number 16;United Kingdom;Glasgow City;16 Byres Road, Glasgow City, G11 5JY, United Kingdom;55.8707649;-4.2990336;18;false;true;Modern Cuisine;The passionately run Number 16 occupies a narrow former shop and its tables are split between the ground floor and a mezzanine level. Dishes showcase prime Scottish ingredients and many exhibit subtle modern touches. The wine list provides interest and, like the cooking, represents good value.;;[]
17523;Adrift;Ireland;Dunmore;Dunmore House, Dunmore, P85 HC03, Ireland;51.5902262;-8.8671797;39;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Run by the fourth generation of the owners’ family, this restaurant is set in an enviable position on the ground floor of the Dunmore House Hotel with views out over Clonakilty Bay. Tasty, modern dishes showcase locally sourced produce, including some from their own organic kitchen garden.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
17525;OSMA;United Kingdom;Manchester;132 Bury New Road, Prestwich, Manchester, M25 0AA, United Kingdom;53.5243229;-2.276795;23;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Located in the city’s northern suburbs, this restaurant’s name is a nod to the owners’ birthplaces – OSlo and MAnchester. They offer chatty, genuine service and are keen to recommend dishes from their mightily appealing seasonal menu. Sauces are a highlight, be it their take on ponzu with sashimi, or a simply delicious creamy romesco. The set lunch menu offers terrific value, while at dinner small plates take over. The stylish room comes with an open kitchen, a communal island table and smart curved banquettes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17526;Clockspire;United Kingdom;Milborne Port;Gainsborough, Milborne Port, DT9 5BA, United Kingdom;50.9657495;-2.4663281;55;true;true;Modern British;There's a lot of beautiful restaurants around, but Clockspire might be one of the most strikingly attractive spots you'll find. Housed within a converted 19th-century school, its high ceiling and exposed rafters provide plenty of ecclesiastical 'wow factor', while the lavishness of the refurbishment is mightily impressive. As you may expect, the dishes are impeccably presented and the polished cooking makes good use of its British ingredients. The slick service comes with a personal touch that feels as though the team really care about your experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
17527;il trillo;United Kingdom;London;4 Hollywood Road, Chelsea, London, SW10 9HY, United Kingdom;51.4859452;-0.1843674;58;true;true;Italian;The Bertuccelli family have been making wine and running a restaurant in the Tuscan Hills for over 30 years. Two of the brothers run this smart local which showcases the produce and wine from their region. Cooking is gutsy, with pasta the speciality. Relax in the delightful courtyard.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17528;THOMPSON St Albans;United Kingdom;St Albans;2 Hatfield Road, St Albans, AL1 3RP, United Kingdom;51.7545724;-0.3359709;100;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Eponymous Chef-Owner Phil Thompson’s restaurant is split over three contemporary dining rooms, each featuring bold artwork from the local gallery. The dishes are equally good-looking and can be enjoyed from either an à la carte, or a 7 or 9 course tasting menu. The kitchen’s skills are evident across the accomplished cooking, while the friendly and efficient service team run the place well.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17530;The Art School;United Kingdom;Liverpool;1 Sugnall Street, Liverpool, L7 7EB, United Kingdom;53.4010693;-2.9688401;51;false;true;Modern British;Having celebrated 10 years in business, Paul Askew's restaurant continues to nourish the good diners of Liverpool. The spacious, elegant dining room has a stylish streak with its bright red chairs and crisp white tablecloths, while the formality of the décor is matched by the service team. The cooking is ambitious and full of colour, while a serious wine list adds to the appeal, with a particularly strong selection of reds. Do check out the array of special events they run, including guest chef dinners and live music nights.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17531;Michael Nadra Primrose Hill;United Kingdom;London;42 Gloucester Avenue, Primrose Hill, London, NW1 8JD, United Kingdom;51.5400661;-0.1502479;42;true;true;International;You'll be spoilt for choice at this neighbourhood restaurant with its extensive, brasserie-style menu. Influences over the cooking come from around the world, so you'll find dishes inspired by everywhere from the Mediterranean (such as a Greek and niçoise salad cross) to Japan (miso black cod). A set lunch menu offers bang for your buck and a roast dinner is available on Sundays – not to mention a wide array of cocktails. The unusual vaulted room adds intimacy, while service is warm and friendly.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17533;Santo Remedio;United Kingdom;London;152 Tooley Street, Southwark, London, SE1 2TU, United Kingdom;51.5036696;-0.0809346;79;true;true;Mexican;The cooking inspiration comes from the owner’s time spent in Mexico City, the Yucatan and Oaxaca. Ingredients are a mix of imported – like grasshoppers to liven up the guacamole – and home-grown like Hertfordshire pork. Spread over two floors, the rooms are as colourful as the food.;Air conditioning,Brunch;[]
17534;Noble Rot;United Kingdom;London;51 Lamb’s Conduit Street, Bloomsbury, London, WC1N 3NB, United Kingdom;51.5218924;-0.1185903;90;false;false;Traditional Cuisine, Classic French;With its dark, rough-lacquered wood and tiny candles, there is something pleasingly intimate about this wine bar and restaurant, where the walls are adorned with covers of the owners' Noble Rot magazine. This really is an oenophile's paradise, with the enthusiastic, clued-up team happy to suggest a smart, sometimes surprising, pairing to go with your meal. The cooking itself is decidedly classical, unfussy and more than a little French. The braised turbot with vin jaune sauce epitomises this spirit, which comes in tandem with gutsy, satisfying flavours.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17535;36 on the Quay;United Kingdom;Emsworth;47 South Street, The Quay, Emsworth, PO10 7EG, United Kingdom;50.844638;-0.9376781;61;false;true;Modern British;A quayside cottage plays host to this intimate restaurant, which affords lovely harbour views – and the sheltered terrace is a hit come summer. Modern dishes display a wealth of different flavours and textures, with the desserts being particularly playful. Bedrooms are cosy and stylish.;Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17537;Mount St.;United Kingdom;London;First Floor, 41-43 Mount Street, Mayfair, London, W1K 2RX, United Kingdom;51.50974;-0.15151;29;false;false;Modern British;There’s nothing anodyne about the art in this particular restaurant, which is hardly a surprise when you discover that art gallery group Hauser & Wirth are behind it. It’s a striking room with a stunning collection of pieces, from Matisse to Man Ray. The menu offers satisfying, classic British dishes like omelette Arnold Bennett and others inspired by the capital, such as ‘Pigeons in Pimlico’. If you’re early, you can always nip into The Audley pub downstairs.;Air conditioning;[]
17538;Elis;United Kingdom;London;Patriot Square, Bethnal Green, London, E2 9NF, United Kingdom;51.5304444;-0.0553826;40;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Rafael Cagali, chef-owner of Da Terra, named his second restaurant, located in the Town Hall Hotel, after Brazilian jazz singer Elis Regina. The bright and lively 12-tabled room on the first floor reflects Rafael’s Italian and Brazilian heritage, so expect to see sharing dishes like 'bolinhos de bacalhau' vie with panzanella salad, and picanha skewer with crab linguini.;;[]
17540;The Spence;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;39 St Andrew Square, Edinburgh, EH2 2AD, United Kingdom;55.9541972;-3.1917515;63;false;true;Modern British;Until 2017 this was the Royal Bank of Scotland, and the restaurant now occupies what was formerly the banking hall. All the grandeur is here, from the granite columns and the exquisite plasterwork to the magnificent cupola which allows natural light to flood in. The Scottish larder is the focus of the accessible menu, with the kitchen showing a keen eye for presentation.;;[]
17541;CULTURE;United Kingdom;Falmouth;Custom House Quay, 38b Arwenack Street, Falmouth, TR11 3JF, United Kingdom;50.1524759;-5.0660623;43;true;true;Modern British;The open kitchen takes centre stage at this old quayside warehouse. Each dish on the set menu is named after the inspiration behind it, be it a local farmer or place, and foraged ingredients also play their part. Don’t be surprised to see the occasional South African influence too though, as the chef-owner is from Cape Town. The pared-back room has a natural feel, and it’s worth checking out the glass-walled wine cellar.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17542;Fish & Forest;United Kingdom;York;13 Grape Lane, York, YO1 7HU, United Kingdom;53.96088;-1.08207;58;false;false;Modern British;The name is a clue as to this intimate restaurant’s focus, as well as to its sustainable ethos. Tucked down a narrow cobbled-street in York's pretty city centre, not far from the famous Shambles, its menu focuses on fish from small boats, meats reared putting husbandry first and game from local shoots. All parts of the ingredients are used too, so that the constantly evolving blackboard menu produces little waste. The self-taught chef's cooking has an ambitious edge, with dishes proving to be fresh and vibrant. The friendly team add to the appeal.;;[]
17544;The Stile Bridge;United Kingdom;Marden;Staplehurst Road, Marden, TN12 9BH, United Kingdom;51.2016967;0.5167818;46;false;true;South American, Mediterranean Cuisine;Vintage charm blends with contemporary cool at this roadside pub. The chef’s South American roots are clear to see on the menu, but there are plenty of Mediterranean and Asian flavours too, with much use made of the open fire. If you’ve come in a pair, choose the rib of beef to share.;Car park;[]
17546;Brigadiers;United Kingdom;London;1-5 Bloomberg Arcade, City of London, London, EC4N 8AR, United Kingdom;51.5126859;-0.0919562;59;false;false;Indian;The army mess clubs of India provide the theme for this large restaurant spread across several rooms on the ground floor of the Bloomberg building. The cooking has a strong live fire element, blending street food dishes and those cooked on the barbecue, like the delicious goat tikki bun kebab. 'Feast' menus are available if you're in a big group and there's a decent selection of beers and whiskies too. It's a perennially busy place and they have several screens for showing sport, so the atmosphere is predictably loud and lively.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17547;Les 110 de Taillevent;United Kingdom;London;16 Cavendish Square, Marylebone, London, W1G 9DD, United Kingdom;51.5169853;-0.145719;34;false;true;French;Ornate high ceilings and deep green banquettes create an elegant look for this formal French restaurant, which is more food orientated than the Paris original. Attractively presented, modern French dishes are accompanied by an exceptional wine list, which includes Château Lafite Rothschild back to 1897 and Château d'Yquem back to 1924. There are also 110 wines available by the glass, with 4 different pairings (covering 4 price brackets and 2 sizes), suggested for each dish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17548;Noizé;United Kingdom;London;39 Whitfield Street, Fitzrovia, London, W1T 2SF, United Kingdom;51.5201809;-0.135102;21;true;false;Modern French;A delightfully relaxed French restaurant, personally run by a warm and welcoming owner. The menu features a mix of classic and more modern French food, prepared with love and care. The wine list – with plenty of depth and fair mark-ups – is a highlight, as are the cheeses and desserts.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17549;Medlar;United Kingdom;London;438 King's Road, Chelsea, London, SW10 0LJ, United Kingdom;51.4830988;-0.1777222;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;After more than a decade of service, this neighbourhood spot is becoming something of a Cheslea institution. The locals keep it well-patronised and it's easy to see why, thanks to the relaxed air and spring-like decoration with apple green banquettes and faux blossoming trees. The kitchen doesn't compromise on ingredient quality, with fine produce used in classic dishes like crab raviolo or roast quail with a textbook potato terrine. The wine list is knowledgably curated and pairings are suggested for every dish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17551;Legacy;United Kingdom;York;Station Rise, York, Y01 6GD, United Kingdom;53.9585543;-1.0887997;58;true;false;Modern British;The Grand Hotel – built in 1906 as the HQ of the North-Eastern Railway Company – is a building that certainly lives up to its name. Among its historic interiors lies Legacy, a formal restaurant with an elegant feel thanks to its parquet flooring and marble-topped tables. The kitchen is strong on technique and fuses Yorkshire ingredients with Japanese influences, from the use of ponzu to a chawanmushi-like dish of shiitake custard. The knowledgeable service team keep things running smoothly.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17552;Gingerman;United Kingdom;Brighton and Hove;21a Norfolk Square, Brighton and Hove, BN1 2PD, United Kingdom;50.8240694;-0.1551756;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The flagship of the Gingerman Group is a long-standing neighbourhood restaurant a short way from the sea. It has a slight Scandic look and an intimate feel. Understated modern dishes provide plenty of appeal and have an unforced natural style and good clarity of flavour.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17553;The Rectory;United Kingdom;Crudwell;Crudwell, SW16 9EP, United Kingdom;51.6350836;-2.0651686;90;true;false;Modern British;All the charm, elegance and character you’d expect from a restored Georgian former rectory are present and correct here, and that includes a lovely garden, dining room and spacious glasshouse. The confident kitchen focuses on seasonality and top British ingredients, and there is never anything extraneous on the plate – just satisfying and complementary flavours.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17554;The Checkers;United Kingdom;Montgomery;Broad Street, Montgomery, SY15 6PN, United Kingdom;52.5603544;-3.1482336;65;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A husband-and-wife team run this low-beamed former village pub with an unfussy, modern style. Across the tasting menu, the classically trained chef shows off his skill for getting the best from local, seasonal ingredients. His eye-catching dishes often shine brightest at their simplest, as with line-caught turbot accompanied by a delicious laverbread and chervil butter sauce. Go for the wine pairing and book one of the four cosy bedrooms to complete the experience.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17556;Memsahib's Lounge;United Kingdom;Cheltenham;47-49 Promenade, Cheltenham, GL50 1PJ, United Kingdom;51.8995659;-2.0767336;80;true;true;Indian;There’s a certain style to this two-roomed basement in a smart Georgian terrace: the colonial-themed bar offers a good range of cocktails, as well as gin and vodka infusions, while the adjoining dining room has a clubby feel, with its charcoal portraits and sepia prints. The Indian dishes are for sharing, although the 'Experience' tasting menu is perhaps the best way to go, and there are also vegetarian and pescatarian versions. They even serve an Indian-themed afternoon tea.;Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17557;Little Seeds;United Kingdom;Stone;16-18 Radford Street, Stone, ST15 8DA, United Kingdom;52.9041596;-2.148413;56;false;false;Modern British;Little Seeds has a bright, fresh, natural look with green walls, foliage and rustic, upcycled furniture. A smattering of cookery books adds to the homely feel – and there’s a walled garden and drinks terrace out the back too. Great quality regional ingredients are used to create eye-catching British dishes with the occasional playful touch. The popular Sunday lunch menu features roast Staffordshire beef.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17558;Another Hand;United Kingdom;Manchester;Unit F, 253 Deansgate, Manchester, M3 4EN, United Kingdom;53.4770583;-2.250041;94;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This 24-seater bistro offers an appealing array of sharing plates which champion produce from local, ethical growers. The eye-catching, vegetarian-led dishes are served one at a time and their flavours are punchy and pronounced. Craft beers and low intervention wines accompany. Service is bubbly and the atmosphere, buzzing.;;[]
17559;The Bear Inn;United Kingdom;Hodnet;Drayton Road, Hodnet, TF9 3NH, United Kingdom;52.8538232;-2.5757121;96;true;true;Modern British;In the spot where there was once a 16C coaching inn, now sits this smart, modern gastropub hidden away in the Shropshire countryside. A welcoming and homely atmosphere accompanies stylishly presented food that’s full of hearty flavours. The menu is rooted in English classics with occasional international influences, and some of the produce could scarcely be more local, coming from the gardens of nearby Hodnet Hall.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17560;Blas;United Kingdom;St Davids;Twr y Felin Hotel, St Davids, SA62 6QT, United Kingdom;51.8790045;-5.2592944;60;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Originally built in 1806 as a working windmill, the Twr y Felin Hotel features contemporary artwork and is decorated in an understated, modern style. Its restaurant, named after the Welsh word for 'taste’, offers appealing menus which showcase seasonal Pembrokeshire produce from John Dory to lamb in pared-back, modern dishes. The friendly team run the place with pride, enhancing the overall experience.;Air conditioning,Car park,Wheelchair access;[]
17561;Arkle;United Kingdom;Chester;Eastgate, Chester, CH1 1LT, United Kingdom;53.1907773;-2.8890883;70;false;false;Modern Cuisine;The Grade II listed Chester Grosvenor Hotel has stood in the heart of the city since the 19C, and its newly renovated restaurant blends stylish, modern décor with the luxury and elegance for which the hotel is known. The tasting menu highlights the best of British produce, and the modern dishes are tasty and well-presented. Extend your evening in the chic cocktail lounge.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17563;Kingdom 1795;Ireland;Killorglin;Main Street, Killorglin, V93 XED7, Ireland;52.1062789;-9.7860096;89;false;false;Modern Cuisine;A former town centre pub is the setting for this stylish, relaxed restaurant, whose modern, brasserie-style interior comes as a contrast to its classic whitewashed façade. Experienced chef Damien uses fine local ingredients to create his concise menu of unfussy, well-judged dishes. Service from his partner Suzi is warm and endearing.;Wheelchair access;[]
17564;Harbour House;United Kingdom;Flushing;Trefusis Rd, Flushing, TR11 5TY, United Kingdom;50.1642977;-5.070313;50;true;false;Modern British;Local suppliers are at the heart of this attractively refurbished pub on the Cornish coast. Owing to their seasonal and sustainable approach, the daily changing menus are shaped by local producers. The cooking is wholly understated, but impressive all the same, with pared-back dishes like homemade crisps with whipped cod's roe, roast brill from Cadgwith and a marvellous panela Basque cheesecake. The set lunch menu offers super value and drinkers are treated to a selection of local beers, best enjoyed outside overlooking the water with a bar snack in hand.;;[]
17566;Owenmore;Ireland;Ballynahinch;Ballynahinch Castle, Recess, Connemara, Ballynahinch, H91 F4A7, Ireland;53.4601314;-9.8630973;60;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Located inside the grand 18C Ballynahinch Castle Hotel and surrounded by a particularly picturesque part of the Wild Atlantic Way, there are few more impressive locations to dine than here. Spectacular views of the grounds and river accompany well-versed service and modern, precisely executed dishes. The West Coast larder is used to great effect and features the likes of delicious mussels and clams from Killary Fjord. Be sure to fit in a walk around the grounds or spend time on the peaceful terrace before you leave.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17568;Seafood Ristorante;United Kingdom;St Andrews;Bruce Embankment, The Scores, St Andrews, KY16 9AB, United Kingdom;56.3438203;-2.800284;27;true;false;Seafood;The simple combination of great quality seafood and commanding bay views is a sure-fire winner at this smart restaurant housed in a striking glass cube. Perched over St Andrews Bay, locally landed seafood is very much at the heart of the menu, which has a subtle Italian slant. The kitchen team know not to mess around with super ingredients like day boat halibut, allowing the natural flavours to come to the fore. The friendly service is of a similarly high standard.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17570;Engine Social Dining;United Kingdom;Sowerby Bridge;72 Wharf Street, Sowerby Bridge, HX6 2AF, United Kingdom;53.7098412;-1.9058171;49;true;false;Modern Cuisine;While this friendly neighbourhood restaurant is housed in a traditional stone building, its interior is contrastingly modern, with closely-set, dark wood tables looking onto an open-plan kitchen with a wood-burning oven. The menu of well-priced sharing plates may have a Spanish heart – from the boquerones to the croquetas – but also offers the opportunity to go on a global culinary journey. Start in Mexico with the generously topped tacos, fly over to Vietnam for the bánh mì prawn toast, then end up back in Blighty for sticky toffee pudding. Whatever you choose, it will burst with colour and flavour.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17571;The Gunroom;United Kingdom;Bontnewydd;Plas Dinas Country House, Bontnewydd, LL54 7YF, United Kingdom;53.1087029;-4.2746917;17;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Formerly home to Lord Snowdon, the cosy Plas Dinas Country House dates from the 17C, and was built around the stone fireplace that still stands in The Gunroom today. Come for afternoon tea or for dinner at either 6 or 8pm. Welsh produce takes the lead on the concise, classically based monthly menu.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17572;The Oarsman;United Kingdom;Marlow;46 Spittal Street, Marlow, SL7 1DB, United Kingdom;51.5730282;-0.7760436;95;false;true;British Contemporary;Head down the side of this part red brick, part timbered pub and you’ll find first the ‘front’ door, as well as an enclosed terrace hidden to the rear. Sit at chunky wood tables or in a leather-clad booth and enjoy British dishes with big flavours and the occasional Mediterranean or Scottish influence.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17574;Quince;United Kingdom;Westgate-on-Sea;39 Station Road, Westgate-on-Sea, CT8 8QY, United Kingdom;51.3815507;1.3386563;54;false;false;British Contemporary;Two alumni of The Goods Shed in Canterbury are behind this unfussy modern bistro, which is a hit with locals and tourists alike. The simple dish descriptions on the concise seasonal menu belie the depth of the dishes, which are made with high quality ingredients and come with distinct flavours and textures. Smooth service adds to the experience.;;[]
17575;Bath Priory;United Kingdom;Bath;Weston Road, Bath, BA1 2XT, United Kingdom;51.3900021;-2.3822839;32;true;false;Modern British;This elegant restaurant is housed inside a charming country house hotel of the same name, which boasts an immaculately kept rear garden and a delightful terrace that makes the perfect spot for an aperitif. The seasonal à la carte showcases the kitchen’s skills, offering quality British produce – like Wiltshire lamb loin – in carefully executed dishes. Ingredient combinations are well thought-out and dishes are always full of flavour.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17576;argoe;United Kingdom;Newlyn;The Strand, Newlyn, TR18 5HW, United Kingdom;50.103804;-5.5486918;73;false;false;Seafood;Part-owned by a local fishmonger and named after an old fishing boat, this modern, wood-clad 'shack' overlooks Newlyn Harbour, where much of its produce lands. The concise menu offers great value seafood dishes designed for sharing, varying daily depending on the catch. Whether it's sardines or black bream, the grill-centric cooking remains pleasingly simple and wholly enjoyable, allowing the quality fresh produce to do the work. On-tap natural wines are served by the glass and carafe. Be sure to book a table on the covered waterside terrace when the sun's out.;Counter dining,Great view,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17577;Manifest;United Kingdom;Liverpool;4a Watkinson Street, Liverpool, L1 0AG, United Kingdom;53.3962704;-2.9817059;94;false;false;Modern British;In Liverpool's regenerated Baltic Triangle district, you'll find this restaurant situated on the ground floor of a converted former warehouse. An open-plan kitchen dominates the room and there are counter seats for those who wish to be close to the action. Carefully cooked, flavourful modern British dishes are available either as an à la carte or a seasonally influenced tasting menu. Whatever you choose, accompany it with some wine from the well-presented list, with each bottle available by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17580;Fancett's;United Kingdom;Cambridge;96a Mill Road, Cambridge, CB1 2BD, United Kingdom;52.1993982;0.1385864;65;false;true;Classic French;The vibrant Mill Road is a focal point for Cantabrigians looking for everything from independent eateries to small antique shops, and this friendly restaurant brings a generous dose of enthusiasm to the area. The eponymous Dan Fancett and his team demonstrate both great care and skilled craft in their preparation of generously portioned dishes that are French to their core, such as the terrific twice-baked cheddar soufflé and the pear tarte Tatin for dessert.;;[]
17581;Bar des Prés - Mayfair;United Kingdom;London;16 Albemarle Street, Mayfair, London, W1S 4HW, United Kingdom;51.5095881;-0.1422697;78;true;true;Asian;From the Mayfair postcode to the impressive marble counter, there is a luxury feel to this first international venture from French celebrity chef Cyril Lignac. Sharing a name with its pre-cursor in Saint-Germain, it also mirrors that restaurant's Japanese-influenced approach – expect maki, sashimi and miso black cod. For the terrific desserts, you travel back to France for classics like mille-feuille, tarte fine and profiteroles.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17583;The Barrington Boar;United Kingdom;Barrington;Main Street, Barrington, TA19 0JB, United Kingdom;50.9595632;-2.8710073;30;false;true;Modern British;Dating back to the 18C, this lovely stone-built inn sits in a picture postcard village and its back garden and terrace is a real jewel. The chef-owner’s personality, his experience in previous kitchens, and his knowledge of the locale, all inform his appealing menu of modern, balanced dishes that are big on flavour and guaranteed to hit the spot. Four bedrooms occupy what was once the skittle alley.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17584;The Victoria;United Kingdom;Oxshott;High Street, Oxshott, KT22 0JR, United Kingdom;51.3319058;-0.3565107;77;false;true;Modern British;This red brick, 19C former beer house blends original features like exposed brickwork and fireplaces with tan banquettes, wood panelling and vintage photos. Cooking delivers bold flavours, with dishes to share and salt chamber aged steaks from the charcoal grill. Service comes from a cheery young team.;Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17585;Holm;United Kingdom;South Petherton;28 St James Street, South Petherton, TA13 5BW, United Kingdom;50.9492535;-2.8093154;57;true;false;Modern British;There’s something special about this former bank, with its impressive architecture and delightful village setting. Seasonal ingredients feature on a range of menus and appealing local drinks accompany. Sit in the spacious dining room with its distressed designer style or bag a spot at the kitchen counter.;Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17587;Browns Bonds Hill;United Kingdom;Londonderry;1 Bonds Hill, Waterside, Londonderry, BT47 6DW, United Kingdom;54.9932502;-7.3118408;80;false;false;Modern British;The flagship of the Browns group sits on the east bank of the River Foyle and comes with a plush lounge and an intimate, art deco style dining room. The artful modern cooking is elaborate in its techniques and combinations and represents good value for money.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17588;The Broughton;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;46-48A Broughton Street, Edinburgh, EH1 3SA, United Kingdom;55.9583843;-3.1900335;48;false;false;Modern British;A warm, genial atmosphere prevails as soon as you enter this smart dining pub, which is located within walking distance of Calton Hill and bustling Princes Street. You can just pop in for a pint if you wish, but you’d be a fool to miss the appealing, good value cooking. Flavoursome dishes like duck confit terrine and vanilla panna cotta hit the mark for elevated pub food, with a strong wine list on hand to accompany.;Wheelchair access;[]
17589;Max's;Ireland;Kinsale;48 Main Street, Kinsale, P17 XY07, Ireland;51.7046581;-8.5222517;17;false;true;Seafood;This well-loved restaurant is an efficiently run spot located on Kinsale's quaint main street. Inside, it has a simple yet smart rustic style, with guests spread across two dining rooms. The menu sticks to unfussy, classically based dishes that deliver well-executed, wholly satisfying versions of tried-and-tested combinations. As you're not far from the coast here, seafood plays a large role, including prime fish and shellfish from local suppliers.;Air conditioning;[]
17590;Chakra by Jaipur;Ireland;Greystones;Meridian Point Centre, Church Road, Greystones, A63 HD43, Ireland;53.1442407;-6.0628053;43;true;false;Indian;An elegant, intimate restaurant with bold décor, unusually set within a shopping centre. Interesting dishes represent the country from north to south. Spicing is delicate, flavours are refined and desserts are a highlight.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17591;The Duck;Ireland;Gorey;Marlfield House Hotel, Courtown Road, Gorey, Y25 DK23, Ireland;52.6688292;-6.2745367;39;true;true;International;Sisters Margaret and Laura Bowe had a clear vision when they decided to turn the carriage house and gardener's store rooms of Marlfield House – a well-known country house hotel – into this accessible bistro-style restaurant. A sunny terrace is the ideal spot in summer, while the cocktail bar inside is a popular haunt before dinner. The menu takes on influences from around the globe, so don't be surprised to find an Irish version of a pulled pork bao bun or spiced lamb kofta. The seafood landed at Kilmore Quay nearby is worth looking out for.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace;[]
17592;Bon Appetit;Ireland;Malahide;9 St. James's Terrace, Malahide, K36 KR66, Ireland;53.451846;-6.151691;54;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This smart Georgian terraced house near the harbour is home to a contemporary brasserie with a lively atmosphere. Modern dishes have a classical French base and plenty of Asian influences. The intimate cellar bar offers afternoon tea, with brunch available at weekends.;Air conditioning;[]
17593;Black & Green;United Kingdom;Barnt Green;49 Hewell Road, Barnt Green, B45 8LT, United Kingdom;52.361897;-1.9900403;28;true;true;Modern Cuisine;A bijou neighbourhood restaurant with stools set at tall tables and a black and green colour scheme. The short, sensibly priced tasting menu moves with the seasons, using prime ingredients to deliver layers of texture and flavour in imaginative dishes. All guests are served at the same time and most go for the wine pairings. Add in the cheese course for a satisfying meal.;;[]
17595;George V;Ireland;Cong;Ashford Castle, Cong, F31 CA48, Ireland;53.5345265;-9.2852897;38;true;true;Classic Cuisine;Wood-panelling and Waterford Crystal chandeliers set the tone at this sophisticated dining room within the Ashford Castle hotel. It was built in 1905 to honour the visit of the Prince of Wales, who later became King George V, and retains an impressively grand feel. Classic French flavours are to the fore, but are delivered with a modern flourishes, and warm Irish hospitality completes the picture.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Interesting wine list;[]
17596;Clunie Dining Room;United Kingdom;Braemar;Mar Road, Braemar, AB35 5YN, United Kingdom;57.0059263;-3.4002315;63;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Queen Victoria made this area fashionable when she started visiting Balmoral Castle in the 1840s, and this restaurant inside The Fife Arms hotel certainly has its own brand of eclectic chic. Murano chandeliers hang from the ceiling and a huge stag oversees proceedings, while the staff are dressed in tartan that matches the cubist painted walls. Come in winter and you'll be welcomed by the glowing embers of the fire. Prime Scottish ingredients from lobster to venison are presented in classical dishes that often incorporate the smoky aromas of a wood fire.;Car park,Garden or park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Wheelchair access;[]
17597;Grano;Ireland;Dublin City;5 Norseman Court, Manor Street, Stoneybatter, Dublin City, D07 XD89, Ireland;53.3510989;-6.2827705;56;false;false;Italian;To the northwest of the city, you’ll find this lovely little Italian restaurant specialising in homemade pasta. Unfussy dishes like spinach balanzoni or cavatelli with venison ragu are expertly cooked and deliver great flavours thanks to their quality ingredients. It’s a friendly and passionately run place, with an owner and chef who hail from Calabria and regularly import produce from their home town for an authentic touch. The all-Italian wine list features some organic and biodynamic options.;;[]
17598;Brown Bear;Ireland;Kildare;Two Mile House, Kildare, W91 PWH5, Ireland;53.1693693;-6.7025686;96;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The village may seem appealingly sleepy, but this is an area renowned for the breeding and training of some top racehorses. The building sits on what was once part of the owner’s family dairy farm, with a lively locals’ bar on one side and a smart bistro on the other. The menu offers a mix of classical dishes and those displaying subtle international flavours, and there is a reassuring confidence to the service.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17599;aizle;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;38 Charlotte Square, Edinburgh, EH2 4HQ, United Kingdom;55.9515087;-3.2060383;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Aizle sits within the appropriately named Garden Room of the Kimpton Charlotte Square Hotel – a bright, cool setting in the heart of the city. The constantly evolving menu takes on a tasting format, featuring fresh, colourful dishes made up of the latest seasonal harvest and given the occasional creative or Japanese twist. Be sure to try their house-made kombucha.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17600;Fhior;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;36 Broughton Street, Edinburgh, EH1 3SB, United Kingdom;55.958305;-3.1898117;36;false;true;Creative;A husband and wife team run this appealing Scandic-style restaurant whose name means ‘True’. Creative modern cooking showcases local and foraged produce, with their one acre garden the real driving force behind the menus. They preserve their home-grown ingredients so they can use them all year round.;;[]
17601;Mister S;Ireland;Dublin City;32 Camden Street Lower, Dublin City, D02 P029, Ireland;53.3345949;-6.2650164;65;true;false;Modern Cuisine;No one knows who Mister S is  – or if he even exists – but no one really minds either, since they’re all here for the flavour-packed cooking over fire. Both charcoal and wood are used to help impart smoky aromas to the produce, but it's the natural flavours of the quality ingredients that really shine through, with the generous sirloin on the bone being a good example of what they're all about. Go with a group of friends, sit in one of the booths and order several dishes to share – perhaps including the signature burnt end rendang spring rolls.;Air conditioning;[]
17605;Dax;Ireland;Dublin City;23 Upper Pembroke Street, Dublin City, D02 AK20, Ireland;53.3348301;-6.2543774;64;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Dublin’s historic Georgian quarter is home to this well-established restaurant, located in the cellar of an old townhouse near Fitzwilliam Square. The décor has a classical quality to it, with white tablecloths and leather upholstery. There’s a French influence to the menu, which offers simple yet flavourful dishes that make the most of prime Irish produce like Wicklow Gap sika deer and Celtic Sea scallops.;Air conditioning;[]
17606;East Room;Ireland;Limerick;University of Limerick, Castletroy, Limerick, V94 PX58, Ireland;52.6746214;-8.570661;41;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Start with an aperitif in the drawing room of this whitewashed Palladian-style house, which sits within grounds of The University of Limerick. There's an old-fashioned feel to the place, with the grand dining room boasting ornate plasterwork, Corinthian pillars and an impressive art collection. Beautifully presented dishes have a sophisticated feel, courtesy of quality produce and a deft touch.;Car park,Garden or park,Wheelchair access;[]
17608;An Port Mór;Ireland;Westport;Brewery Place, Bridge Street, Westport, F28 KP70, Ireland;53.7990288;-9.5218548;75;false;true;Classic Cuisine, Irish;Friendly Chef-Owner Frankie named this permanently popular restaurant after his home village, and there is certainly a welcoming homeliness to the place. It’s tucked away down a narrow town centre alleyway and its cosy interior has a simple, shabby-chic style. Choose between two fixed-price menus named after nearby mountain ranges: the good value Néifinn Bheag and the more adventurous Cruach Phádraig. Both include dishes informed by local produce – such as excellent sea trout – that have a classical base and plenty of flavour.;;[]
17609;Restaurant Roots;United Kingdom;Southbourne;141 Belle Vue Road, Southbourne, BH6 3EN, United Kingdom;50.7216635;-1.797413;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;Just around the corner from the beach, behind frosted glass, is this jovial, laid-back restaurant. The décor is bright and fresh, with pictures of crashing waves on the walls and a large mobile of tiny fish hanging from the ceiling. Chef Jan imbues his ambitious tasting menu with influences from his German heritage, including family recipes like "mamma's red cabbage". Enthusiastic service from Geza illustrates the team's overall passion.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17610;Chutney Mary;United Kingdom;London;73 St James's Street, St James’s, London, SW1A 1PH, United Kingdom;51.5056937;-0.1386661;79;false;false;Indian;This long-standing, popular Indian restaurant comes from the same stable as Veeraswamy and Amaya, and its stylish dining room may be the jewel in the group’s crown. A certain luxury is to be expected when Buckingham Palace is just a short walk away, but there’s a relaxed, fashionable feel to the surroundings here too. The appealing menu offers lots of choice and the well-judged, flavourful dishes (mostly from northern India) have been subtly updated, while still respecting the foundations of the cuisine.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17612;Paradise;United Kingdom;London;61 Rupert Street, Soho, London, W1D 7PW, United Kingdom;51.5122031;-0.1337855;90;true;true;Sri Lankan, Contemporary;It was out with the old and in with the new in mid-2024 for this Sri Lankan restaurant, as it underwent a refit and changed its menu offering. There’s now a choice of three tasting menus: one with fish and meat, one with fish and veg, and one exclusively vegetarian. Traditional Sri Lankan spices and flavours are added to largely British ingredients like Cornish pollock and Brixham crab to create attractive, colourful dishes that are thoughtfully constructed, and then proudly explained by the service team. The cooling greys of the intimate room provide a stylishly understated backdrop to the creative cuisine.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17613;Silo;United Kingdom;London;Unit 7, Queens Yard, Hackney Wick, London, E9 5EN, United Kingdom;51.5428444;-0.0219865;76;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Billed as the world's first zero-waste restaurant, Silo has been a pioneer in the field of sustainable gastronomy for years. It was born out of Chef-Owner Douglas McMaster's challenge to himself to cook 'without a bin', and even the kitchen counter is made from recycled plastic bottles. The tasting menu features many plant-based elements, while the 'siloaf' bread – made using flour milled in-house – typifies the eco-friendly approach, and makes a return for dessert in the form of a 'siloaf ice cream sandwich'.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17614;ANNWN;United Kingdom;Narberth;1 Market Square, Narberth, SA67 7AU, United Kingdom;51.7981302;-4.7430385;97;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Folklore, foraging and flavour guide your visit to this sustainable, proudly Welsh restaurant. Sat inside a lovingly converted former bank, there is a real sense of warmth to the place, with the passionate chef recounting stories while serving and bringing round ‘top ups’ of sauces and ingredients as you dine. From the expertly foraged produce to the Preseli Hills lamb, local ingredients bring with them a great burst of flavour. Extend your experience by joining one of their occasional foraging days.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17615;The Moorings;United Kingdom;Gorey;Gorey Pier, Gorey, JE3 6EW, United Kingdom;49.1995716;-2.0204666;76;false;true;Traditional Cuisine;The picture postcard location beneath Mont Orgueil Castle is not the only attraction at this good-looking hotel restaurant. Along with a well-stocked bar, is a menu offering the chance to sample the best from Jersey’s waters, including local oysters, scallops and crab. There’s plenty of choice for non-fish eaters too though, with the likes of mature steak or pheasant schnitzel. Save room for dessert, which is a real highlight.;Great view;[]
17617;Square;Ireland;Dundalk;6 Market Square, Dundalk, A91 X9WY, Ireland;54.0041049;-6.4032226;71;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Sister restaurant to The Courthouse in Carrickmacross, this cosy, modern bistro offers a concise, balanced menu of seasonal ingredients. The generous dishes are executed with care, full of flavour and won’t break the bank. It’s a keenly run place and the friendly service further adds to the experience.;Terrace;[]
17618;henne;United Kingdom;Moreton-in-Marsh;High Street, Moreton-in-Marsh, GL56 0AT, United Kingdom;51.9920356;-1.7024599;93;true;true;Modern British;‘henne’ refers to Marsh Henne, the original name of this Cotswold town, and this likeable restaurant – run by two friends – sits proudly at its heart. Local produce is showcased via a surprise tasting menu of modern British dishes which have punchy flavours and an appealing simplicity about them.;;[]
17619;Shell Bay;United Kingdom;Studland;Ferry Road, Studland, BH19 3BA, United Kingdom;50.6784605;-1.9514966;39;true;true;Seafood;Brownsea Island and Poole Harbour can be seen from many of the tables at this superbly located bistro on the water's edge. Unsurprisingly in a place like this, fish and shellfish dominate the menu. Sometimes the produce is treated with international influences, as with the Kerala seafood curry, but the majority of mains involve whole fish cooked over fire, imparting a gentle smokiness while keeping the flesh succulent and adding a crispy skin.;Great view,Terrace;[]
17620;Gordon's;United Kingdom;Inverkeilor;Main Road, Inverkeilor, DD11 5RN, United Kingdom;56.6350875;-2.5480789;43;false;false;Modern Cuisine;This long-standing, passionately run restaurant never stands still, always investing and evolving over time. It’s still very much a family concern, with Garry Watson alone in the kitchen and his mother Maria handling the service with aplomb. There’s a modern feel to both the décor and the cooking, with the latter proving colourful and technically accomplished. Dishes really shine in their use of the Scottish larder, like local lamb with seasonal girolles. An interesting wine list and five bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park;[]
17622;Nest;United Kingdom;London;374-378 Old Street, Shoreditch, London, EC1V 9LT, United Kingdom;51.5271332;-0.0796771;71;false;false;Modern British;Three friends founded this restaurant and they run the place with obvious pride. A move form Hackney to Shoreditch brought with it a larger premises, lovely vintage décor and the Nest Cellar bar, which also serves a selection of snacks. The set menu is based around British produce and changes regularly, focusing on a season or a particular theme – such as game, beef or seafood – and everything is handled with aplomb by the chefs. Service from the friendly team is smooth and efficient.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17623;Garrison;United Kingdom;London;99-101 Bermondsey Street, Southwark, London, SE1 3XB, United Kingdom;51.5007361;-0.0816959;41;false;false;Modern British;Something of a Bermondsey institution, this charming pub is known for its vintage look and relaxed, buzzy atmosphere. Get comfy in one of the cosy booths to enjoy contemporary British dishes made from good quality seasonal produce. Roasts are a big hit on Sundays and the daily changing menu makes a feature of the fresh fish specials, such as a fabulous John Dory to share. The friendly, organised service team have an eye for detail that further enhances the experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17624;The Chandlers Arms;United Kingdom;Epwell;Sibford Road, Epwell, OX15 6LH, United Kingdom;52.0594224;-1.4862687;72;true;true;Modern Cuisine;It may sit within a 17C former pub, but there’s now more of a restaurant feel to this intimate family-run operation – where you’re guaranteed a warm welcome. The regularly updated menus showcase cooking that is well-balanced, thoughtfully composed and makes great use of the local larder. Flavour and texture combinations are both original and effective, in dishes largely served by chef Harry Flockhart himself. When the weather allows, head for the terrace.;Car park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17625;Pophams;United Kingdom;London;197 Richmond Road, London Fields, London, E8 3NJ, United Kingdom;51.5435327;-0.057621;92;true;true;Italian;Pophams is an artisan bakery during the day but, on four evenings a week, it morphs into an appealingly simple Italian restaurant. Dishes are bright and carefully prepared, with the pasta dishes the stars of the show. A stool at the stone counter looking into the open kitchen is the place to sit, although the pavement terrace is perfect on summer days.;Air conditioning;[]
17626;Kintsu;United Kingdom;Colchester;11a North Hill, Colchester, CO1 1DZ, United Kingdom;51.8908961;0.8970308;20;true;true;Modern British;Well-crafted and eye-catching modern dishes populate the multi-course surprise tasting menus here, which have a seasonal British element running throughout. The restaurant is tucked away in a courtyard inside a Grade II listed former barn, with stylish contemporary décor inside and an open kitchen allowing guests to get a good view of the chefs as they work. A friendly service team add to the experience.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17628;Ye Horns Inn;United Kingdom;Goosnargh;Horns Lane, Goosnargh, PR3 2FJ, United Kingdom;53.8470828;-2.6470671;82;false;false;Modern British;There’s a snug bar, a comfy lounge and a stylish vaulted dining space with an inglenook fireplace at this lovingly restored pub, parts of which date back to the 17C. They keep the menu short and seasonal, offering eye-catching, modern, ingredient-led dishes alongside local ales and an extensive list of sensibly priced wines. Personable service completes the picture.;Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17630;Docket Restaurant;United Kingdom;Whitchurch;33 High Street, Whitchurch, SY13 1AZ, United Kingdom;52.9700295;-2.6844908;23;true;false;Modern British;Stuart and Frances Collins spent many years working overseas before moving to this old Shropshire market town to open their popular neighbourhood restaurant, sandwiched between two shops on the high street. Their travels are reflected in Stuart's cooking, which comes in the form of a tasting menu and takes an imaginative approach while being underpinned by his strong classical technique. Frances runs the efficient service with a smile and her enthusiastic team follow suit.;;[]
17631;The Bell;United Kingdom;Charlbury;1 Church Street, Charlbury, OX7 3PP, United Kingdom;51.872386;-1.4829216;81;true;true;Modern British;The quaint village of Charlbury is the setting for this 17C pub, which looks gorgeous thanks to a lavish makeover. The bar and dining areas ooze charm and character, with exposed Cotswold stone walls and crackling log fires among the many appealing features. In summer, the garden and orchard come into their own with a covered terrace and even a small stream. Many ingredients come from their sister operation, Daylesford Organic Farm, and are used in comforting, full-flavoured dishes like Cornish fish pie. Tastefully decorated bedrooms complete the picture.;Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17632;Tom, Dick & Harry's;United Kingdom;Loughton;153 High Road, Loughton, IG10 4LF, United Kingdom;51.6443587;0.0522692;48;true;true;World Cuisine;If you’re after a fun, lively atmosphere, you’re in the right place at this laid-back brasserie with a quirky contemporary style. The experienced chef sources good quality ingredients and the charcoal oven is used to good effect. Global menus include brunch on Saturdays – and it has a playful cocktail list too.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17635;Woodsman;United Kingdom;Stratford-on-Avon;4 Chapel Street, Stratford-on-Avon, CV37 6HA, United Kingdom;52.1906723;-1.7079909;45;false;false;Meats and Grills;Even in the dead of winter, you’ll likely find a big crowd and a lively buzz at this well-run restaurant. It’s easy to see why it’s such a busy place, as the attentive service is joined by hearty, satisfying cooking. Dishes often revolve around wood-fired produce, be it skate wing or partridge, and there’s a proper roast dinner served on Sundays. Shakespeare fans have an extra reason to visit, as the famed playwright’s childhood classroom is located just up the road and is open to visitors.;Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17636;Ginza St James's;United Kingdom;London;15 Bury Street, St James’s, London, SW1Y 6AL, United Kingdom;51.5072349;-0.1386792;98;false;false;Japanese;In one of London's swishest districts, this is an appropriately elegant spot to celebrate the joys of Japanese cuisine. A large cocktail bar will greet you as you enter, before you head down to the equally stylish restaurant where the seating options include teppanyaki and sushi counters. The vast à la carte is so appealing, with everything from sashimi to tempura, but if you can't decide then go for one of the well-priced set options – and don't miss the chance to have the delicious 'nasu dengaku'. The sake list is one of the best in London.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Notable sake list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17637;The Hut;United Kingdom;Freshwater;Colwell Chine Road, Colwell Bay, Freshwater, PO40 9NP, United Kingdom;50.6897236;-1.5391706;79;false;true;Modern Cuisine, Seafood;This elegant restaurant is superbly set amongst colourful beach huts and looks out over the sea to Hurst Castle. Sit on one of the terraces or under retractable roofs and enjoy anything from fish tacos to a fruits de mer platter. Most diners arrive by boat (they’ll even collect you from your mooring).;Counter dining,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17640;Tropea;United Kingdom;Birmingham;27 - 33 Lordswood Road, Harborne, Birmingham, B17 9RP, United Kingdom;52.4585824;-1.9587848;62;false;true;Italian;The Italian ethos of uncluttered, straightforwardly delicious cooking is alive and well at this bright neighbourhood restaurant. Let the staff guide you when it comes to ordering the sharing plates, but you're sure to be satisfied by any of the terrific homemade pastas plus the beautifully balanced cannoli to finish. The Italian wine list is as fabulously well-priced as the food, and the buzzing atmosphere and friendly service add to the appeal. It's easy to see why the place is so popular.;Air conditioning,Wheelchair access;[]
17641;wilks;United Kingdom;Bath;13 Chelsea Road, Bath, BA1 3DU, United Kingdom;51.3852341;-2.3889046;58;true;false;Seafood;Fitting in nicely among a parade of independent shops in the west of the city, this intimate operation holds just three tables. The set menu features plenty of prime seafood like sweet langoustines and meaty wild monkfish, alongside meats such as tender, flavoursome pigeon. This seasonal produce is often accompanied by subtle international flavours, reflecting the chef’s global travels. There’s a French slant to the wine list, with small batch winemakers pushed to the fore.;Interesting wine list;[]
17642;Barnaby's;United Kingdom;Saint Issey;Trevibban Mill Vineyard, Dark Lane, Saint Issey, PL27 7SE, United Kingdom;50.49233;-4.93967;70;true;false;Modern Cuisine, Middle Eastern;A few miles inland from Padstow and its older sibling Prawn on the Lawn, this lively pop-up-turned-permanent sits within a working vineyard and orchard. Start your visit on the charming terrace with a glass of their own wine or cider, accompanied by oysters either deep-fried or raw. A fixed menu of small plates is joined by larger daily specials from the blackboard, with quality local produce given a kick by hints of Middle Eastern or North African spicing – such as crab toast with muhammara or beetroot with whipped feta and chermoula.;Car park,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17643;Franco's;United Kingdom;London;61 Jermyn Street, St James’s, London, SW1Y 6LX, United Kingdom;51.5075157;-0.1397462;16;false;true;Italian;One of London’s oldest Italian restaurants, this reliably enjoyable spot has benefitted from the years of practice. The kitchen focuses on an extensive menu of classically based dishes like veal and beef lasagne or linguine with lobster, with each one proving to be uncomplicated and well-executed. The many regulars come back time and again for their favourite dishes and the intimate, cosy atmosphere. The wine list is joyfully Italian, with some wonderful barolos among the choices.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17644;Mark Poynton at Caistor Hall;United Kingdom;Caistor St Edmund;Stoke Road, Caistor St Edmund, NR14 8QN, United Kingdom;52.5860232;1.2983797;19;true;true;Modern Cuisine;The Caistor Hall Hotel is a Georgian country house with a contemporary flourish inside, and a manicured lawn and terrace for those seeking fresh air. Experienced restaurateur Mark Poynton runs the hotel’s flagship restaurant, offering a balanced seasonal set menu in a choice of lengths. The terse menu descriptions belie the complexity of the cooking, evidenced by technically adept elements such as a perfectly seasoned red wine jus with rare aged beef. If there’s a chocolate dessert on the menu, then you’re in for a treat.;Car park,Garden or park;[]
17645;LYLA;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;3 Royal Terrace, Edinburgh, EH7 5AB, United Kingdom;55.9568362;-3.1807017;81;false;true;Modern British, Creative;Edinburgh’s finest row of Georgian townhouses is the setting for this elegant seafood restaurant, where only the very best produce will do. Start in the stunning first-floor bar for an aperitif and finely crafted snacks prepared at the island counter, before moving to the understated dining room for a tasting menu based on delicious, sustainably caught fish and shellfish, be it wild halibut or Scottish langoustines. This produce drives the eye-catching dishes, which deliver subtle yet complex blends of flavours and textures. If you’re staying the night, luxurious bedrooms are available.;Air conditioning;[]
17646;Chef's Table;United Kingdom;West Malling;46 King Street, West Malling, ME19 6QT, United Kingdom;51.2942311;0.4082177;80;true;false;Modern British;The chef in question is the passionate Brad Redding, and his ‘table’ is a tiny restaurant in the centre of this pretty market town. It’s a highly personal operation, as Brad cooks his overtly seasonal tasting menu for around a dozen diners. There is technical skill on show across interesting, generous dishes that reflect the locale well – and the friendly service is nicely paced. Both bread and flavoured butters are made in house.;;[]
17647;The Pearly Queen;United Kingdom;London;44 Commercial Street, Spitalfields, London, E1 6LT, United Kingdom;51.5170863;-0.0731653;43;false;false;Seafood;There’s a terrific buzz about this trendy 21st century take on an oyster bar that feels right at home in the streets of Shoreditch. Contemporary artwork – much of it oyster-based – lines the walls of this well-run restaurant, which is split across two levels. The menu makes great reading for seafood-lovers, mixing small plates with a few larger options like grilled cuttlefish with gooseberry hoisin – alongside a selection of both dressed and natural oysters, of course. Be sure not to leave without trying the sticky toffee madeleines.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17649;Darjeeling Express;United Kingdom;London;2.1-2.4 Kingly Court, Carnaby Street, Soho, London, W1B 5PW, United Kingdom;51.5131068;-0.1389917;43;true;true;Indian;The cooking of Kolkata and chef-owner Asma Khan’s Mughal ancestry inform the menu at this bright and breezy restaurant on the top floor of the perennially busy Kingly Court. Asma can be found chatting away with diners while the all-female kitchen team create authentic, vibrant dishes where careful spicing enhances the central ingredient. The menu is presented as an à la carte at lunch and served all together as a thali at dinner.;Air conditioning;[]
17650;eòrna;United Kingdom;Edinburgh;68 Hamilton Place, Edinburgh, EH3 5AZ, United Kingdom;55.9591976;-3.20711;69;true;true;Modern British;There's a plush quality to this smart counter restaurant in the suburb of Stockbridge. Small "chef’s table" operations like this allow for a much greater intimacy to your dining experience and, indeed, there are just two people working here: Brian in the kitchen and Glen looking after service and wines. Following a warm welcome, you can enjoy a highly seasonal tasting menu that has a strong Scottish heart, from the Orkney beef to the fantastic Perthshire strawberries.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17651;The Devonshire;United Kingdom;London;17-19  Denman Street, Soho, London, W1D 7HW, United Kingdom;51.5106645;-0.1353791;90;true;true;Traditional British;One of the hottest tickets in town, The Devonshire is a 'proper' London pub that's been restored to its former glory. On the ground floor, and spilling out onto the pavement, you find the drinkers seeing off pints of Guinness, with food served upstairs. Most of the cooking takes place on the first floor, in the aptly named Grill Room, with the top-floor Claret Room providing a little more calm. Dishes are traditional in style and robust in flavour, with the quality of the produce shining through. Highly personable service rounds out the experience.;Air conditioning;[]
17652;The Flintlock;United Kingdom;Cheddleton;11 Cheadle Road, Cheddleton, ST13 7HN, United Kingdom;53.0704422;-2.0413983;58;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Set inside a fine stone building overlooking a peaceful canal, this spacious, elegant restaurant is packed with charm. There are period features aplenty across the sitting area and the two dining rooms, where the self-taught chef serves dishes with a modern approach. Hake with fermented lettuce is something of a favourite, as are the fabulous Parker House roles, and puddings are a highlight too. Sweet, engaging service makes a visit all the more enjoyable, as does a stroll along the canal before dining.;Car park,Garden or park,Great view,Wheelchair access;[]
17653;Akara;United Kingdom;London;Arch 208, 18 Stoney Street, Borough Market, London, SE1 9AD, United Kingdom;51.5066914;-0.0914987;25;false;false;African;The team from Akoko are behind this appealing restaurant tucked underneath the arches in Borough Yards. An akara is a black-eyed pea fritter commonly found in West African and Brazilian cuisine, which gives a clue as to the influences found on the concise menu. Sharp execution and careful balancing of flavours runs throughout, with the signature akara a must to begin with, coming with various accompaniments such as barbecue prawn or celeriac. Some of the friendliest service around adds to the wonderfully warm experience.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17654;Updown Farmhouse;United Kingdom;Deal;Updown Road, Betteshanger, Deal, CT14 0EF, United Kingdom;51.2359848;1.3214244;32;true;false;Regional Cuisine;Hidden in the heart of the glorious Kent countryside, this delightful 17C farmhouse has been lovingly restored by its owners, and in the garden you'll find a charming, vine-laden conservatory restaurant with rustic décor. There are Italian influences aplenty on the menu, with dishes like ossobuco and crab tagliolini, alongside many cooked over an open fire and steak night on Wednesday. The gardens stretch over 7 acres in total, with individually styled bedrooms spread about the place.;Car park,Terrace;[]
17655;Mauro Colagreco at Raffles London at The OWO;United Kingdom;London;Whitehall, London, SW1A 2BX, United Kingdom;51.5052663;-0.1262861;59;true;true;Modern Cuisine;On the ground floor of the mightily impressive Raffles hotel – which opened in 2023 and occupies The Old War Office – sits this elegant, comfortable and discreet dining room. The sophisticated, technically elaborate cooking offers intriguing flavour and texture combinations, while displaying an emphasis on over 70 varieties of British fruit and vegetables –  the plant produce is always listed first on the menu. The wine list is comprehensive, the pairings are well-considered and the service is pitched just right, being both structured and relaxed.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17656;Rambutan;United Kingdom;London;10 Stoney Street, Borough Market, London, SE1 9AD, United Kingdom;51.5055515;-0.0914511;58;true;true;Sri Lankan;When negotiating the plethora of eateries around Borough Market, be sure not to miss this popular spot offering a taste of authentic Sri Lankan cooking. The Tamil region of northern Sri Lanka is the largest inspiration for the menu, with dishes providing satisfying flavours and well-balanced spicing. It’s a busy place, so there’s a suitable buzz in the air – and the knowledgeable service team are on hand with suggestions to suit your palate and appetite.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17657;The Kirkstyle Inn and Sportsman’s Rest.;United Kingdom;Brampton;Slaggyford, Brampton, CA8 7PB, United Kingdom;54.8812966;-2.5023813;75;false;false;British Contemporary;There’s plenty of rustic character to this appealing pub in a beautiful North Pennine hamlet. A warm welcome gets things off to a great start, before you tuck into dishes founded on produce that all comes from within 50 miles of the kitchen. This is shooting country, so that includes plenty of game – such as roasted grouse or partridge ballotine. Keep an eye out for the raspberry soufflé too, which is a cut above your typical pub pudding. Four bedrooms make this a great base for exploring the gorgeous surrounding countryside.;;[]
17659;Tern;United Kingdom;Worthing;Worthing Pier, Marine Parade, Worthing, BN11 3PX, United Kingdom;50.8089753;-0.3695428;38;true;true;Modern Cuisine;Tern sits on the first floor of an art deco building, in a unique location at the end of Worthing Pier – and when the tide draws in, you'll feel like you're on an ocean liner. It has a clean, contemporary feel, with an open kitchen dominating the room. Ingredient-led cooking is the order of the day, using a mixture of modern and classical techniques, while desserts like apple, caramel and buttermilk are a highlight. The short selection of English wines, nearly all available by the glass, cements their credentials in supporting producers along the south coast.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Great view;[]
17660;Sucre;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Mariscal Antonio José De Sucre 676, Buenos Aires, C1428DUB, Argentina;-34.5531162;-58.4368309;23;true;true;Contemporary;Any mention of Sucre, situated in the section of the Belgrano district closest to the sea and the extensive Regatas lake, cannot be made without referring to Fernado Trocca, a man with an entrepreneurial vision who successfully expanded his business model to other countries (Sucre has Michelin-recommended subsidiaries in London and Dubai). This spacious setting with an urban-industrial vibe, in which the open kitchen, long bar and glass-fronted wine cellar stand out, is aimed at a cosmopolitan clientele in search of new experiences. Its cuisine is always centred around seasonal ingredients, many of which are organic, and includes a good selection of contemporary dishes with an international flair (“fish of the day” tiraditos, wild prawns sautéed in thyme butter, certified grass-fed beef cooked on the quebracho wood grill, Cavatelli pasta, organic quince etc. A key principle here is ensuring that they do not source meat from animals reared via intensive feedlots. An impressive brunch and extensive choice of cocktails complete the picture.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
17661;Casa Cavia;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Cavia 2985, Buenos Aires, C1425DDA, Argentina;-34.577532;-58.4072881;52;false;false;Modern Cuisine;If we were to look for an expression that defines the culinary philosophy of this restaurant occupying an attractive mansion in the Palermo Chico district, it would be “loyalty to local ingredients”. Casa Cavia boasts an elegantly classic interior which combines with the contemporary decor, but what is particularly striking here is the delightful terrace to the rear (embellished with a water feature in the middle) that has become a trendy setting where people come to eat but also to be seen. The chef at the helm, Julieta Caruso, showcases her cuisine on a concise contemporary-style à la carte where vegetables play a predominant role in dishes that are seemingly simply prepared but based around the very best ingredients. Her vegetarian recipes, which take pride of place here, are accompanied by others featuring fish and meat, such as grilled fish of the day, roasted prawns, marinated beef ribs etc.;Air conditioning,Brunch,Terrace;[]
17662;La Vida;Argentina;Mendoza;Viamonte 5022, Mendoza, M5505, Argentina;-32.9891733;-68.8862201;93;true;true;Contemporary;La Vida is part of the Susana Balbo Winemaker's House & Spa Suites, a small luxury hotel in Chacras de Coria, a small town 13km from Mendoza, where everything revolves around wine. After the approach along a tree-lined track, the first thing to strike you here is the highly attentive service – you are met at the door and accompanied to the bar, and from there, with a welcome cocktail in hand, there’s an option of exploring this family hacienda before heading to your table to learn about the property’s history and admire its works of art. In the restaurant’s contemporary-style dining room, with its glass-fronted kitchen and exposed beams which add a certain character, choose between two up-to-date menus (seven and fourteen courses designed by chef Flavia Amad Di Leo, who is also in charge of the Osadía de Crear restaurant). Presentation is paramount, with dishes paired with Susana Balbo Wines’s most exclusive labels.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17663;Basa;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Basavilbaso 1328, Buenos Aires, C1006AAD, Argentina;-34.5924602;-58.377135;63;true;false;Mediterranean Cuisine;Although it is always busy with a business clientele at lunchtime, the ambience and style of this basement restaurant adds a nocturnal feel to proceedings. Basa features a large bar counter that extends along one side of a dining room that is contemporary in feel and dominated by the presence of concrete and metal. You’ll also find plenty of tables and bar stools, but if you’re looking for a more relaxed experience, ask for a seat on one of the leather sofas with low dining tables. The menu offers options for all tastes, with a mix of well-known local dishes and others inspired by the Mediterranean. The kitchen team is on top of every dish here, so why not start with delicious stuffed lamb empanadas, before moving on to salmon-filled “culurgiones” pasta or something from the grill, such as prawn kebabs or veal loin milanesa?;;[]
17664;Osadía de Crear;Argentina;Mendoza;Cochabamba 7801, Mendoza, M5509, Argentina;-33.03747;-68.88775;75;true;false;Contemporary;In the province of Mendoza there’s no excuse for not visiting a winery to enjoy an authentic wine-tourism experience. And with this in mind, Susana Balbo, famous as the first female wine expert in Argentina and a leading wine reference on the South American continent, founded the family-run Susana Balbo Wines bodega, 30km or so south of Mendoza. The Osadía de Crear restaurant, which has existed on the estate since 2013 and is now under the baton of chef Flavia Amad Di Leo, aims to enhance this wine appreciation experience with modern cuisine that is highly delicate and always focuses on local and seasonal ingredients (pumpkin, string beans, beetroot, pomegranate etc). This is presented on two tasting menus (four or six courses), each with different and equally superb estate wine pairing options. Informal brunches, picnics and afternoon tea can also be arranged in the winery’s galleries and gardens.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17665;Sál;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Thames 2450, Buenos Aires, C1425FIJ, Argentina;-34.5815574;-58.4223548;27;false;true;Scandinavian, Contemporary;The influence of Nordic nouvelle cuisine extends everywhere and, here, in this attractive period-style house, its impact is clear to see. The basic principles on display at Sál (which means “soul” in Icelandic) are centred around local ingredients, natural flavours and the use of techniques such as pickling, fermentation, smoking and salting. The cooking is also based on these fundamentals, with an added Asian influence. Start with something from the Smørrebrød on the à la carte – there are few things more Scandinavian than Skagen avocado toast (with the addition of shrimp). The squid tartare is also delicious and is memorable for the XO mayonnaise that accompanies it, while main course options include the delicious duck with smoked cabbage and the loin of lamb (served pink) with fennel. The ambience is as sophisticated as it is relaxed, with attentive and charming service from the young team.;;[]
17666;Raggio Osteria;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Gurruchaga 2121, Buenos Aires, C1425FEE, Argentina;-34.586102;-58.4241995;54;true;false;Italian;Gigli pasta with clams and mussels from the Mar del Plata, spaghetti alla Chitarra with a traditional carbonara sauce, conchiglioni alla Puttanesca, and the family’s own recipe for panna cotta are just some of the delights on offer in this contemporary-style restaurant on the ground floor of the Pleno Palermo Soho hotel, not far from the luxuriant Carlos Thays botanical garden, where Italian cuisine is the undoubted star of the show. Chef Sebastián Raggiante, who hails from Bologna (the capital of the northern Italian region of Emilia Romagna), reinterprets recipes from his homeland with an honest approach, with a primary focus on flavour and the use of the best zero-mile Argentinian ingredients. A dish that particularly impressed us was the “brasato di guancia” (cheek stew with tomatoes, red wine and capers), requiring a minimum of six hours of low-temperature cooking.;Air conditioning;[]
17667;Sottovoce;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida del Libertador 1098, Buenos Aires, C1112ABN, Argentina;-34.586003;-58.387497;87;false;false;Italian;Aubergine parmigiana, rotolo alla bolognese, black spaghetti with prawns, delicious home-made malfatti pasta filled with ricotta and spinach are just some of the dishes to savour at this corner restaurant opposite the Thays de Recoleta park, which takes its name from the French landscape architect Carlos Thays. Considered to be one of the city’s classic dining venues and one of its best Italian eateries, it is split between two floors, with a small terrace beneath the arches by the entrance. As well as its delicious home-made pasta (made with Candeal durum wheat and eggs), it also offers specialities that are hard to find anywhere else, such as brains alla siciliana. Sottovoce’s menus are decorated with drawings by the late Miguel Brascó, a famous Argentinian writer, humourist, illustrator and food critic, who always booked the same table when eating here!;Air conditioning,Terrace,Valet parking;[]
17668;Restó SCA;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Montevideo 938, Buenos Aires, C1019ABT, Argentina;-34.5977615;-58.3898645;82;false;true;International;Restó SCA occupies a listed building in Recoleta, widely considered the most elegant district in Buenos Aires, where it shares occupancy with the headquarters of the Sociedad Central de Arquitectos (SCA), founded in 1886 and one of the country’s oldest professional associations. Located at the end of the building’s former carriage entrance, the restaurant has a subdued bistro-style feel with just a few tables and a bar that is home to an enticing display of cheeses. Previous incumbents here have included renowned chefs such as María Barrutia and Guido Tassi, although it is now the turn of María Magdalena Piaggio, a chef who has an in-depth knowledge of French cuisine and whose fresh Mediterranean and international recipes are based around Argentinian ingredients. Standout dishes include the stuffed quail (the stuffing changes with the seasons), the ricotta gnocchi, and several of her fish dishes, such as the cured Bariloche trout which we particularly enjoyed.;Air conditioning;[]
17670;4ta Pared;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Habana 3499, Buenos Aires, C1419GQA, Argentina;-34.5940909;-58.5074421;91;false;false;Contemporary;If you’re strolling through the essentially residential district of Villa Devoto, we recommend a visit to 4ta Pared, a restaurant that is somewhat off the main gastronomic trail but which is well worth tracking down, and whose name (literally, the “4th Wall) refers to the theatrical situations in which actors break down barriers by interacting directly with their audience. It occupies a corner property with large windows (use the phone at the door to make a (compulsory) booking before gaining access). Once inside, you’ll find a contemporary-style decor with two different ambiences: a room with low tables, and a space dominated by a large island laid out for dining, where owner-chef Pablo Cerne completes his dishes in full view of guests. The aim of the single contemporary tasting menu is to extract maximum flavour from each ingredient, with a focus on micro-seasonality, organic vegetables, and the importance of sustainability, textures and presentation.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus;[]
17671;Fogón Asado;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Uriarte 1423, Buenos Aires, C1414DAM, Argentina;-34.5886122;-58.4337672;73;false;false;Meats and Grills;If the idea of a dining experience based around a traditional grill concept sounds appealing, this unusual restaurant in the Palermo district will definitely fit the bill but you’ll need to book ahead! Attention to detail is to the fore here, and the subdued lighting and open brickwork ensure that all the focus is on the large grill at the centre of the dining room. The dining experience, based around an 8-course menu (fire-roasted aubergines, chorizo, morcilla, Provoleta cheese, a succulent glazed pork belly, pine cone-smoked “ceja” and ribeye), is both informative and interactive with constant communication between the grill chefs and guests, the majority of whom are tourists or groups of friends. Everything the chefs do is explained in detail, from the provenance of the wood used, the feed used for the cattle, the best accompanying salsas etc. A splendid and fun journey lasting over two hours across Argentina’s most popular culinary art form!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17672;Chuí;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Loyola 1250, Buenos Aires, C1414AVB, Argentina;-34.5900676;-58.441071;83;true;false;Vegetarian, Vegan;The four young owners of this vegetarian/vegan restaurant have taken full advantage of the potential of this empty piece of land next to the railway tracks. It occupies a huge semi-open industrial-style warehouse alongside a rustic garden that transforms the setting into an oasis in the heart of the city. If you look closely you’ll notice four main features: a cabinet for growing mushrooms, another to store preserves and pickles, plus a clay oven and a pizza oven in the huge open kitchen. Wild mushrooms pay a starring role on the menu in delicious dishes such as the oyster mushroom milanesa and the mushroom pâté. Chuí also usually offers four types of pizza – the female chef here is an expert at adding an extra fermented element or escabeche to give them an extra-special touch. The colourful desserts include a delicious cheesecake brûlée.;Garden or park,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17673;Ajo Negro - Mar de Tapas;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Córdoba 6237, Buenos Aires, C1427BZC, Argentina;-34.5830389;-58.4479413;29;false;false;Modern Cuisine;We particularly enjoy variety and a sense of personality, hence our attraction to this relaxed industrial-style restaurant where everything revolves around informally, yet meticulously prepared fish, including tapas. Located in the heart of the Colegiales district, the overall feel here is original and fun. The decor features a large steel scaffolding-style bar counter (the tables are similar in design), colourful maritime-inspired murals and, in the centre of the room, a maturing cabinet that aims to add more flavour and new textures to some of the ingredients used here (bass, mullet, bream, bluefish, pollack, palometa etc). One of the most popular and successful starters here is the Pan Bao with panko prawns, wasabi mayo and grape or cucumber pickle, although the fresh fish of the day is another worthwhile option. This successful restaurant is particularly popular, so it is essential to book well ahead in order to secure a table.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17674;Roux;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Peña 2300, Buenos Aires, C1126ABF, Argentina;-34.590734;-58.3974536;69;false;true;Contemporary;When we think of a French bistro we all have a general idea of what to expect. This corner restaurant, complemented by small pavement terraces on each side for alfresco dining, boasts an intimate and attractively classical interior with tables set close together, a kitchen that is partially visible from the bar, whitewashed woodwork and large windows that provide plenty of natural light. Chef Martín Rebaudino who, as part of his career path, travelled to Europe and had the good fortune to share a kitchen with legendary Spanish chefs such as Martín Berasategui, Juan Mari Arzak and Pedro Subijana, offers an extensive contemporary-style à la carte with French, Spanish and Argentinian influences that includes an appetising array of hot and cold starters, delicious risottos, and top-quality red meats. If you sit out on the terrace, you’ll almost feel as though you’re dining on a Parisian boulevard!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17676;Elena;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Posadas 1086/88, Buenos Aires, C1011ABB, Argentina;-34.5905196;-58.3825924;84;false;true;Steakhouse;If we were to rank the best Argentinian hotel restaurants, Elena, occupying the luxury Four Seasons Hotel Buenos Aires, would definitely figure high up on the list! Aesthetically inspired by the interior of old houses in the San Telmo district famous for its tango venues, it features a private dining room in the wine cellar and a main dining space brightened by a large glass dome, with an open kitchen to one side (note the ageing cabinets full of different cuts of meat). The culinary concept here, in what we would describe as a contemporary steakhouse, is traditional with meat (Angus sirloin, 45-day-aged Angus T-Bone, Argentinian wagyu ribeye etc) cooked on the Josper grill, but you can also order delicious ham and cheeseboards, catches of the day with different garnishes, as well as the occasional pasta dish.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Wheelchair access;[]
17677;Kōnā;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Castañeda 1899, Buenos Aires, C1428BBA, Argentina;-34.5532829;-58.4370682;88;true;false;Japanese;This collaboration between Narda Lepes and Inés de los Santos, one of the standout new restaurants of 2023, has been a roaring success. This semicircular wood structure on the corner (hence its name) of Castañeda street is definitely striking and comes with enough discreet Japanese design features to make you feel as though you’re sitting in the Shibuya district of Tokyo. Make sure you start (or finish) with a drink at the bar upstairs, perhaps sipping an “Ash”, its own version of a martini. The open kitchen is fully respectful of the traditions and flavours of Japanese cuisine, so don’t expect any extravagant combinations. The gyozas are a good way to kickstart proceedings, and then we recommended moving on to the Temaki and Nabe sections of the menu: the former come with delicious flavours and marvellously contrasting textures, while the latter will definitely warm your soul!;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17678;Anchoíta;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Juan Ramírez De Velasco 1520, Buenos Aires, C1414ARF, Argentina;-34.5894403;-58.4453965;15;true;true;Contemporary;A tiny gastronomic jewel which is usually fully booked, although you can turn up early and join the queue in the hope of a table becoming available. In this contemporary eatery with an industrial vibe (it was originally a siphon factory) in the Chacarita district, everything is directed towards the centre of the dining room, with its open kitchen and a grill surrounded by a highly original counter where you can eat while watching the chefs at work. The cuisine here, complemented by delicious Argentinian charcuterie and cheeses, is designed for sharing, with some dishes inspired by Guaraní recipes (“chipa guazú” with smoked surubí), alongside pastas, rice dishes, organic vegetables from the restaurant’s own farm, and fish from Argentina’s rivers (patí, surubí etc) and coastline, as well as superb cuts of meat (three cooking options are available (55°C - medium rare, 49°C – rare, and 42°C - bleu). It also runs two neighbouring businesses - Anchoíta Cava (perfect for a glass of wine with tapas) and the Panadería de Anchoíta bakery.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17679;Cabaña Las Lilas;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Alicia Moreau de Justo 516, Buenos Aires, C1107AAL, Argentina;-34.6036631;-58.3667068;100;false;false;Meats and Grills, Barbecue;When you ask for advice on the best steakhouse for grilled Argentinian meat in Buenos Aires, this large-scale restaurant in Puerto Madero, featuring lots of private spaces and an open-view grill, is always mentioned. In this pleasant eatery with an elegant air overlooking the river, the undisputed star of the menu is its grilled meat (veal chitterlings, mixed offal, ribeye, Summus Rubaiyat picanha etc) from different breeds of cattle, although it also offers a good choice of cold plates, salads, fish of the day, and an impressive array of side dishes. The restaurant is located just a few metres from the century-old Corbeta ARA Uruguay museum ship and its renown is such that it is not unusual to see famous personalities dining here – past customers have included the likes of tennis player Roger Federer and French President Emmanuel Macron. The extensive wine cellar and the option of ordering half plates for most dishes complete the picture here.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17680;Piedra Infinita Cocina;Argentina;Mendoza;Costa Canal Uco Paraje Altamira, Mendoza, M5569, Argentina;-33.781445;-69.1702416;21;false;true;Contemporary;For those who enjoy visiting wineries as part of a vacation, this restaurant, part of the highly modern Zuccardi bodega in the Valle de Uco, 120km or so from Mendoza, won’t disappoint. With a name (Infinite Stone) that is inspired by its unique setting between the vineyards, with the majestic Andes as a backdrop, the complex has been recognised by the Best of Wine Tourism awards as the world’s best winery in the “Architecture, Parks and Gardens” category (its cupola is particularly striking). The spacious entrance leads to a dining room which is contemporary in style and with large picture windows looking out on to its impressive natural surroundings. The thoroughly modern menu features four courses that champion locally sourced ingredients and recipes (beetroot, creamy Pepato cheese, trout and apples from Tunuyán, “tortita mendocina” baked in a clay oven, grilled T-bone etc) that are paired with some of the winery’s most distinct and exclusive labels. Lunch here also includes a visit to the bodega.;Air conditioning;[]
17682;Niño Gordo;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Thames 1810, Buenos Aires, C1414DDL, Argentina;-34.5864068;-58.4289204;47;true;false;Asian;The popularity of this Asian-style steakhouse, which was opened in 2017 by the owners of La Carnicería, demonstrates the perfect fit between this restaurant and the district of Palermo Soho. An ideal venue for a night out with friends, or a restorative weekend lunch, it is bold, lively and exuberantly decorated – the red hanging lanterns must have featured on thousands of Instagram accounts! It has the feel of traditional Japanese izakaya, especially if you sit at the bar directly in front of the chefs. The ingredients may be Argentinian, but the flavours and techniques are either Japanese, Korean, Vietnamese or Thai. If you were to choose a dish that sums up Niño Gordo it would be the ever-popular Katsusando, made with brioche-style bread instead of shokupan and with beef steak replacing the usual pork. Sweetbreads with miso and choclo (corn) are another original creation, while the spicy fried rice is both vibrant and highly satisfying.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17683;Angélica Cocina Maestra;Argentina;Mendoza;Cobos s/n, Mendoza, M5509, Argentina;-33.1616247;-68.9176047;38;false;true;Creative;This restaurant, the name of which pays homage to the mother of Nicolás Catena Zapata (the man credited with putting Argentinian wines on the world map), showcases the authentic flavours of Mendoza from a modern perspective. The dining room, which is as imposingly impressive as the rest of the building (it is reminiscent of medieval Italian architecture with its sturdy stone walls, open brickwork, vaulted arches and valuable works of art), is part of the Catena Zapata winery in Agrelo (in the department of Luján de Cuyo), famous both for the quality of its wines and its design in the shape of a Mayan pyramid. The cuisine is centred around an exclusive and creatively inspired tasting menu which evolves in various stages or courses, starting with small and sophisticated appetisers (such as spherical olives) and moving on to dishes with the full DNA of Mendoza (such as the smooth-textured and charcoal-cooked pork pancetta with green apple chutney). It’s also well worth visiting the underground distillery where the winery’s red Vicenzo vermouth is produced.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park;[]
17684;Fogón Cocina de Viñedo;Argentina;Mendoza;San Martín 1745, Mendoza, M5507, Argentina;-33.0246477;-68.8725424;33;false;false;Meats and Grills;Here, at the Lagarde winery in Luján de Cuyo, half an hour from Mendoza, there’s a total commitment on local cuisine to complement the wine experience. Between this restaurant and Zonda, which could be described as its elder sibling, there is a strong emphasis on history, the connection with the local area, and the setting in this stunning natural paradise. Access to Fogón is via the winery’s boutique, where guests can also enjoy a tasting of food as well as wine. In the dining room, with its high ceilings and a kitchen visible at one end, you can choose between two tasting menus, both with wine pairings from the estate, plus an à la carte with a clear penchant for superb grilled Argentinian meats (ribeye, tri-tip, T-bone etc), Italian recipes (we particularly enjoyed the al dente Cavatelli pasta with lamb) and creative cuisine. It’s also possible to arrange a scenic open-air lunch here with views of the vineyards.;Air conditioning,Car park,Garden or park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17685;Centauro;Argentina;Mendoza;Avenida Perú 1156, Mendoza, M5500, Argentina;-32.8883595;-68.8483254;86;true;false;Contemporary;The core principle behind this restaurant is a love for its region and its products and ingredients. Occupying an attractively fronted old mansion that was once a small hotel, this converted property now features a cocktail bar, a space transformed into a wine cellar, and several contemporary-style dining rooms occupying the former guestrooms (part of the kitchen is visible from one of these). The modern cooking here is showcased in well-constructed dishes that are featured on two menus (4 or 6 courses, including wine pairings) which champion sustainable and organic ingredients and products (including many native varieties) from the Mendoza region, with a strong commitment to provenance and to small-scale producers. The somewhat surprising names of the dishes here (the Queen of Fantasy, Autumn Foam, Bloom, Enchantment etc) are an invitation to head off on a gastronomic flight of fancy!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17686;5 Suelos - Cocina de Finca;Argentina;Mendoza;Pasaje de la Reta, Mendoza, M5549, Argentina;-33.0247973;-68.951299;48;false;false;Farm to table;When they talk about “cocina de finca” (literally “estate cuisine”) here, it is a serious business! It is perhaps, a little surprising to find two brothers and wine-experts Héctor and Pablo Durigutti at the helm, both of whom had the clear idea of focusing their efforts on fine dining as the perfect complement to their unique microcosmos at Finca Victoria, a family-run winery with two charming guest houses. The restaurant itself, located just a few metres from the winery’s HQ and totally surrounded by vineyards, occupies an elegant glass cube with a thatched roof and takes its name from the five types of soil found on the property. The cuisine is centred around two tasting menus: one entitled “5 Suelos” (5 courses), the other a more exclusive 14-course option called Historia. The latter also features an astute wine pairing that explores the evolution of wine from Antiquity to its arrival in Argentina, and then to its expansion as a result of the country’s immigrant community.;Air conditioning,Car park,Great view;[]
17687;Uni Omakase;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Guatemala 5820, Buenos Aires, C1425BVN, Argentina;-34.5785706;-58.4341818;51;true;true;Japanese;“Omakase” is a Japanese term that effectively means leaving the menu to the complete discretion of the chef, who will normally source the best ingredients from the market that day. This philosophy is the key tenet in this restaurant located in the residential district of Palermo, now in the hands of chef Damián Shiizu, whose cuisine came as a very pleasant surprise to us. Once you’ve rung the bell at the entrance to confirm your booking, you need to wait until every guest has arrived before entering together and taking seats at the bar counter. The surprise menu here might include dishes such as marinated edemame cooked with soy, superb nigiri (sole, matured pejerrey fish, amberjack, torched squid etc), sashimi, temaki, and a delicious dashi soup. Small cups of sake are served throughout the meal to provide the perfect pairing.;;[]
17690;1884 Francis Mallmann;Argentina;Mendoza;Belgrano 1188, Mendoza, M5500, Argentina;-32.9122939;-68.8430762;99;true;true;Traditional Cuisine, Argentinian;The idea of creating a restaurant inside a wine cellar is not a new one, but there’s always a pioneering first in every destination. In this case, the honour goes to Francis Mallmann, an Argentinian chef who was keen to develop the concept after an eye-opening trip to the Napa Valley in California. This restaurant, located at the Escorihuela Gascón bodega in the department of Godoy Cruz, was founded in 1884, hence the reference in its name, and features a contemporary dining room, a bar space and a pleasant terrace, where you’ll find the grill, the wood store and the roasting oven. The cuisine is based around a single menu which pays full homage to local and traditional cooking, and features a choice of seven courses (we loved the baked Mendoza-style empanada and the rotola pasta with spinach and fresh mushrooms) plus an Argentinian cheese option. We strongly recommend that you save space for the selection of “River Plate” desserts!;Air conditioning;[]
17691;El Preferido de Palermo;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Jorge Luis Borges 2108, Buenos Aires, C1425FFD, Argentina;-34.5855314;-58.4253891;83;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;If you’re on the lookout for a restaurant with plenty of history, make sure you pay a visit to El Preferido de Palermo, which opened its doors in 1952 as a modest tavern. This busy eatery, occupying an iconic pink building dating back to 1885, is now run by the owner of the Don Julio parrilla, just one block away, and has retained its bygone character (period floors, mirrors, colourful jars of pickles etc) following heavy restoration, while at the same time updating its cuisine with an à la carte that respects the Buenos Aires DNA of this former warehouse. You can’t leave without trying the famous sirloin milanesa, which is striking for the quality of the meat, which is tender and fried almost without any oil, and the sweetness of the accompanying tomato salsa. The menu also features a large selection of artisanal charcuterie: Chacarero salami, spianata, bondiola, pancetta etc. The organic vegetables used are grown by the restaurant itself, and include unique varieties such as heirloom tomatoes.;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17692;Riccitelli Bistró;Argentina;Mendoza;Callejón de La Reta 750, Mendoza, M5509, Argentina;-33.0339742;-68.959131;67;true;false;Seasonal Cuisine, Innovative;At the Riccitelli Bistró, they have gone one step further to bring together fine cuisine, an appreciation of wine, and sustainability. The Matias Riccitelli Wines bodega in Luján de Cuyo has created this restaurant, built out of remodelled containers and “planted” amid old wines, to enhance its wine experience. Chef Juan Ventureyra’s cuisine, which can be sampled in the informal dining room or on the lower terrace, explores Mendoza’s culinary roots on two menus (one with 6 courses, the other with 7) with a strong focus on native, locally sourced produce and ingredients mainly from its own gardens. Vegetables play a starring role here, hence the vegetarian influence in its “farm to table” concept (in summer, it grows over 80 varieties of tomato from seed), enhanced by adding protein to its dishes. A unique experience and a place that is well worth a visit.;Car park,Great view;[]
17693;Corte Comedor;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Olazábal 1391, Buenos Aires, C1428DGE, Argentina;-34.5668739;-58.4697613;75;false;false;Meats and Grills;Here, in the heart of the Belgrano district, everything revolves around a varied array of top-quality cuts of meat, traceability and the maturing process… which is hardly surprising given the restaurant’s location next door to its own butcher’s shop! The first thing you notice when you walk into the bright and open dining room are the flames and embers from the grill behind the counter. The “asado” croquettes are a good way to start proceedings, along with the Provoleta cheese, although you’ll need someone from your table to help share the huge portion. The sausages here, ranging from merguez to morcilla, are also popular, but the majority of customers come here for one thing: the succulent, tender and delicious cuts of meat. The high ceilings give a sense of space, while the tables and school-like chairs add to the relaxed atmosphere. The restaurant is used to being full, so the team here is fully under control of everything from the word go.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17694;Espacio Trapiche;Argentina;Mendoza;Nueva Mayorga, Mendoza, M5513, Argentina;-32.9722096;-68.7462561;95;false;false;Contemporary;For those on a quest for a gastronomic experience rather than just a simple meal, this restaurant offering a combination of fine wine and fine dining is the perfect option. Occupying a glass-fronted annexe with views of the vineyards at the entrance to the prestigious Trapiche winery, Espacio Trapiche features an open-view kitchen visible from the entrance hall (part of the floor is covered with glass to enable guests to view the underground wine cellar below) as well as an attractive contemporary-style dining room. Chef Lucas Bustos, whose popularity has skyrocketed since his appearance in a Netflix documentary on Mendoza’s cuisine (Magical Andes), surprises guests with his modern cooking that celebrates ingredients from the surrounding mountains (potatoes, lamb, trout, vegetables from his own garden etc) that are exclusively showcased on his meticulously prepared menus: Premium, Ultra Premium (both with identical dishes, some chosen by guests, but with different wine pairings) and Degustación (Tasting), the latter requiring prior booking.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
17695;Renacer;Argentina;Mendoza;Brandsen 1863, Mendoza, M5507, Argentina;-33.0663477;-68.9055117;64;true;true;Argentinian;Patricio Reich, founder of the Renacer winery, has revealed the secret to his wines: “A combination of three key factors – our staff, the unique Mendoza terroir, and our passion for excellence”. Alongside these attributes, it was important not to neglect gastronomy when it came to understanding the bodega’s surroundings, hence the idea of offering a complete experience that allows guests to discover more about the region from every angle. The restaurant itself is located in a separate annexe to the winery and features a pleasant lakeside terrace with romantic views of both the Tuscan-inspired stone tower and the imposing Andes cordillera. A visit here usually starts with a short visit to the bodega, with its steel fermentation tanks and barrel storeroom, and a stroll through the vineyards, before continuing to the dining room, where you can choose between three menus (2, 3 or 5 courses). Picnics and more informal dining options are also possible, the latter including a tasting of hams, cheeses and empanadillas.;Air conditioning,Great view,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17696;Crizia;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Fitz Roy 1819, Buenos Aires, C1414CIA, Argentina;-34.583215;-58.435084;18;false;true;Contemporary;The veteran Crizia restaurant has been one of the most respected in the city since it opened its doors in 2004. The contemporary loft-style vibe in the dining room contributes to the sophisticated ambience and makes it the perfect option for a date or to impress friends. This includes intimate lighting and professional service, with the team attentive to every detail and keen for customers to leave completely satisfied. Owner-chef Gabriel Oggero works with small-scale independent producers, fishermen and farmers in order to source the very best seasonal ingredients (the restaurant also has its own rooftop city garden). Oysters are a particular speciality and fish-lovers will delight in a menu which is completely focused on seafood and shellfish. The à la carte includes charcoal- and wood-grilled dishes such as the succulent roasted Peking Duck. An expertly curated wine list, featuring a good choice of wines by the glass, provides the perfect accompaniment.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Interesting wine list;[]
17697;La Carniceria;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Thames 2317, Buenos Aires, C1425FIG, Argentina;-34.5827037;-58.423512;20;true;false;Meats and Grills;If you’re on the lookout for a different type of restaurant in which to enjoy Argentinian meat, this restaurant will definitely fit the bill, with a backdrop that re-creates the interior of a butcher’s shop (carnicería) with large photos of cuts of beef hanging from the ceiling to simulate a meat cold store, and a wood-fired grill behind the bar counter with its smoky aromas and glowing embers. In addition to the delicate and impressively updated traditional cuisine (interesting starters, chitterlings, smoked cuts etc), the quality of the meat stands out. This is enhanced by the traceability process from the rearing of 500kg Angus cattle on natural pasture at the “Los Abuelos” de Rivera family farm in the heart of the Humid Pampas region all the way through to the grill. These meat cuts are matured for different periods of time to enhance tenderness and maximise flavour. La Carniceria is full every day and is particularly popular with tourists.;Air conditioning;[]
17698;Piedra Pasillo Al Fondo;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Campos Salles 2145, Buenos Aires, C1429CFC, Argentina;-34.5506645;-58.4631704;94;false;false;Contemporary;This restaurant occupies a restored house in the Nuñez district of the city. Boasting tons of charm, it is one of those places with a character that comes as a pleasant surprise due to the charming team at the helm and its somewhat “broken” design, characterised by the kitchen visible through a large hole in the brickwork. It is run by its two owners (Lucas Canga and Tomás Couriel) who focus on modern, creative and complex cooking based around colourful dishes that aim to showcase seasonal ingredients and successful combinations of flavours. Standout dishes here include the venison tartare with marinera biscuit and vitello tonnato, and the langoustines with XO sherry and fresh cream, a cold dish featuring delicious prawn carpaccio wrapped in cabbage leaves and served with an XO sauce that combines perfectly with crème fraîche to transform the dish into a culinary delight. The restaurant also features a spacious patio-terrace and a bar (Al Fondo) where you can enjoy signature cocktails prepared by its head bartender.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17699;Duhau Restaurant & Vinoteca;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Alvear 1661, Buenos Aires, C1014AAD, Argentina;-34.5893201;-58.3861778;21;true;false;Grills;The fully laden wine shelves and cheese room with its display cabinets exert a Pavlovian effect as you enter this restaurant in the Park Hyatt hotel. The best Argentinian products – the majority of which are cooked on the parrilla grill – are the main attraction here, accompanied by an impressive wine list featuring the country’s most acclaimed wines. There are lots of dishes for sharing, from the grilled rib chops and Atlantic fish to the slow-grilled shoulder of lamb. Everything is abundant here, both in terms of flavour and portions, but make sure you order a side of the delicious and buttery smoked potato purée! The restaurant is popular with a business clientele, no doubt attracted by the good-value-for-money menu, as well as by the more relaxed ambience in the evening. The dining room is elegantly appointed and the staff highly attentive, while the arched doors lead to a charming terrace with views of the garden. The perfect place if you’re looking for a gastronomic bolthole to escape the hustle and bustle of the city.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17700;Mercado de Liniers;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Gorriti 6012, Buenos Aires, C1414BKN, Argentina;-34.5816198;-58.4416321;90;false;true;Contemporary;A fine-dining restaurant, the name of which pays homage to the culture of the countryside, the omnipresence of meat and, above all, to the former Liniers livestock market where workers and breeders worked together like a family for generations. It is located in the extensive and lively Palermo Hollywood district and occupies a modern setting that was once a workshop (hence the light industrial vibe) with a kitchen that opens on to the dining room. Chef Dante Liporace, who spent time in Spain working under the legendary Ferran Adrià (at the erstwhile El Bulli) and several years behind the stove at Casa Rosada (under the baton of Mauricio Macri), showcases his cuisine exclusively on menus (Almuerzo (Lunch), Hangar, Highway Star and, lastly, the more gastronomically focused Too Tough To Die), with the leitmotif throughout his dishes the true soul of city of Buenos Aires and its surrounding area.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Wheelchair access;[]
17701;Buri Omakase;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Guatemala 5781, Buenos Aires, C1425BVK, Argentina;-34.5788465;-58.4337269;85;true;true;Japanese, Sushi;Anyone familiar with Japan and with the challenges faced when setting up a restaurant, will appreciate the complexities posed by Buri Omakase, where you have to ring the bell to property 002 in a small office block, and are then escorted by lift up to the authentically decorated dining room with seating for just 10 guests. There’s just one sitting (which starts at 8.30pm), so make sure you arrive on time to avoid unwelcome glances from other diners! Here, the owner-chef is inspired more by the traditions of Kyoto rather than Edomae, hence the prevalence of dishes prior to the nigiri courses, including an excellent miso soup and a creamy “chawanmushi”. For the nigiri, this chef uses high-quality local fish caught by trusted fishermen, while the rice is the Koshihikari variety from Niigata, famous for its excellent quality. As tradition dictates, the chef starts with fish with a gentle flavour, which then gradually intensifies through the course of the meal. An authentic experience in every sense!;Air conditioning,Counter dining;[]
17702;Águila Pabellón;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Sarmiento 2725, Buenos Aires, C1425FGC, Argentina;-34.5792565;-58.4188001;36;false;true;Contemporary;This white Art Nouveau-style property, which dates from 1905 and has been carefully restored, reopened its doors in 2023 with great fanfare, adding its honourable name to the city’s food scene. The à la carte will appeal to everyone, featuring recognisable dishes and classic flavours which have been brought up to date through the use of contemporary techniques. The ingredients used are high on quality and the chef is conscious of the benefits of allowing space on the plate for natural flavours to fully express themselves, as witnessed by dishes such as chargrilled squid with a sweet red pepper salsa, confit of chicken with a mushroom cream, and pork loin milanesa. Choose from an array of dining spaces in which the traditional decor respects the building’s heritage and style. The large arch-shaped windows provide lots of natural light as well as views of the Ecoparque, the perfect place to spend a family weekend.;Terrace,Valet parking;[]
17703;CAUCE de los Fuegos;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Alicia Moreau De Justo 440, Buenos Aires, C1107AAJ, Argentina;-34.6031969;-58.3673318;48;true;true;Meats and Grills, Argentinian;It’s not easy to be successful in Puerto Madero, so to succeed with a premium steakhouse in a district home to myriad other restaurants specialising in meat is no mean feat! In this modern eatery with a hint of industrial decor that reminds guests of its location in a restored port area (note the iron columns in the dining room and the huge old terrace visible from the terrace), the traditionally inspired à la carte includes an impressive choice of starters, salads, fish such as Patagonian trout, and pasta dishes including Mediterranean-style linguine with prawns, although it also features a particularly varied list of grilled and roast meats. Make sure you choose some of the empanadas (pork loin, pacú fish and lamb), the roasted “Emperador Cauce” short ribs (cooked for 14 hours) and the delicious Shorthorn ribeye from pasture-fed cattle reared at liberty on the restaurant’s Ayacucho estate.;Air conditioning;[]
17704;Franca - Fuego y Vino;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Darwin 1111, Buenos Aires, C1414CUW, Argentina;-34.5903769;-58.4403206;72;true;true;Grills, Argentinian;If you’ve heard of or are already familiar with the highly successful Julia restaurant, located just a couple of blocks away, the easiest way to describe this eatery is “Julia’s younger sibling”, with the same independent outlook and principles when it comes to working with organic ingredients but with a strong determination when it comes to the cooking concepts of fire and the parrilla grill, which are its cornerstones. In this modern restaurant with glass-panelled walls that look out on to a colourful street corner, the large work counter, which also doubles as a dining space, is a strong presence, enabling guests to watch dishes being prepared and the constant hustle around the grill, where the colourful embers of white quebracho hardwood burn brightly in the background. Chef Julio Martín Baez’s cuisine includes numerous small plates (raw mullet, tartare, cured prawns with garlic, mushrooms etc) so that guests can try a little of everything, as well as vegetarian starters and aged meats for mains. Impressive choice of wines by the glass.;Air conditioning,Counter dining,Terrace;[]
17705;Sacro;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Costa Rica 6038, Buenos Aires, C1414BTN, Argentina;-34.5791581;-58.4392217;44;false;false;Vegetarian;If you’re on the lookout for a restaurant focusing on “plant -based” cuisine, this eatery on the ground floor of the CasaSur boutique hotel in the Palermo Hollywood is definitely worth considering, a sensation enhanced by its bright façade in different tones of white, featuring striking circular perforations that create contrast and add light. Its elongated layout boasts a modern design, and includes a pleasant, verdant terrace to the rear. Here, the contemporary à la carte showcases vegetarian dishes made to share and to create an element of surprise, mouthwatering snacks (the unmissable kimchi-based dumplings with ginger foam and coriander), gently flavoured dishes (artichokes with Sicilian caponata, putanesca, corn remolacha and herbs) alongside more hearty options (roasted salsify, kale, edamame cream and hazelnuts), all of which showcase vegetables but from a Far Eastern and Latin American perspective. It’s not a bad idea to pair the dining experience with some of Sacro’s cocktails!;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17706;Ruca Malen;Argentina;Mendoza;Ruta Nacional 7 km. 1059, Bodega Ruca Malen, Mendoza, M5507, Argentina;-33.0944306;-68.9295179;84;true;true;Contemporary;At the Ruca Malen winery, situated in Agrelo (in the department of Luján de Cuyo) just over half an hour to the south of Mendoza, guests can enjoy a dining experience that will live long in the memory. Its eponymous restaurant (the name comes from a Mapuche legend) takes a fresh, immersive look at the world of wine, with both the chef and the young sommelier wandering around the tables to chat with diners. Here, wine takes on major importance and has always been the key to everything, hence the choice of dishes on the 7-course tasting menu which have been deliberately created with the choice of wine pairings in mind (somewhat unusually, on the menu the wine is listed first in capital letters with the accompanying dish written in lowercase). The dishes themselves are highly contemporary, delicate and influenced by the local terroir, hence the showcasing of seasonal ingredients and produce and the purity of each individual flavour (we particularly enjoyed the spinach, eggs and alubia bean dish).;Air conditioning,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17707;Abrasado;Argentina;Mendoza;Lateral Norte Acceso Este 1360, Mendoza, M5519, Argentina;-32.8964661;-68.8172543;40;false;false;Meats and Grills;If you rely on a restaurant’s list of awards when it comes to booking a table and if the delicious flavour of aged meats brings tears to your eyes, then the Abrasado restaurant (part of the Los Toneles winery not far from the centre of Mendoza - the recipient of various Best of Wine Tourism awards over the years) is the place for you! The dining room, located next to the spaces reserved for tastings and events, boasts a contemporary design and high ceilings, along with a maturing cabinet at the entrance and a bar to the rear with a resident bartender. Although Abrasado offers an extensive à la carte with an impressive array of fresh and aged meats (dry-aged ribeye, T-bone aged in black garlic, fillet steak aged in kombu) designed for sharing, the vast majority of guests opt for its set menus (Andes, 100 Aniversario and Abrasado) as they all include a wine pairing option.;Air conditioning;[]
17708;Narda Comedor;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Mariscal Antonio José De Sucre 664, Buenos Aires, C1428DUB, Argentina;-34.5530315;-58.4364087;34;false;false;Country cooking;The love that locals in Buenos Aires have for meat has been long documented, however Narda Lepes, a woman who is well known thanks to her cookery books and TV appearances, is slowly changing this attitude. She is a champion of healthy ingredients and a vegetarian diet, hence the predominance she gives to vegetables here. Her stuffed onion dish will satisfy even the most die-hard of carnivores, while her silky tofu is a culinary legacy that originates from her travels overseas. Although there’s a plethora of vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free options, that doesn’t mean that her restaurant is fully vegetarian as evidenced by her ossobuco, a legendary dish in every respect. The bright and roomy white dining space gives the impression of being in a particularly elegant cafeteria, enhanced by the equally spacious open kitchen. Service here begins with breakfast, hence the different dining incarnations through the day, from morning coffee to lunchtime snacks and dinner with friends.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17709;Mishiguene;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Lafinur 3368, Buenos Aires, C1425FAJ, Argentina;-34.5768986;-58.4122209;16;true;false;Israeli;Situated just a few metres from the stunning Jardín Japonés, a verdant garden that highlights the friendship that exists between Argentina and Japan, you’ll come across Mishiguene (“crazy” in Yiddish), a restaurant that is full every day and that everyone is talking about. In its busy dining room, with its classic English style and a bar counter for customers, discover cuisine that revives the flavours of Jewish cuisine from a contemporary perspective. These revive Jerusalem-trained chef Tomás Kalika’s childhood recollections and his quest for “emotional memories” that demonstrate the imprint of an immigrant population marked by history. On his à la carte, which is complemented by a tasting menu, you’ll find delicious and copious dishes full of personality which usually feature lots of ingredients. One of Mishiguene’s signature dishes is Pastrón, a beef prime rib cured for ten days with salt, herbs and spices, which is then smoked over wood embers for four hours, and steam-cooked for a further fourteen.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17710;Quimera Bistro;Argentina;Mendoza;Cochabamba S/N, Agrelo (Bodega Quimera), Mendoza, M5509, Argentina;-33.1056095;-68.9023865;60;false;true;Argentinian;Here, in Achaval Ferrer, 28km from Mendoza, the team at Quimera Bistró consider themselves as the “guardians of a legacy”, a sentiment that goes far beyond the production of wine and is further demonstrated in a restaurant that adds to the wine experience. Once you’ve reached the estate via a dirt track between the vineyards, you come to a landscaped area with a small duck pond, and then the winery with the restaurant on the first floor. The latter features a bright, rustic-cum-contemporary dining room that is particularly striking as a result of the glass floor, through which the wooden wine barrels can be seen on the floor below. The bistro is run by a young, dynamic team who showcase their talents on a single, traditionally inspired 3-course menu featuring highly original seasonal options that champion small-scale producers from the Mendoza region – the kitchen team particularly enjoys working with fruit and vegetables that are home grown and sourced daily, cheeses from La Linqueñita, vinegars from Alquería, Andean oyster mushrooms etc.;Air conditioning,Great view,Terrace;[]
17711;Picarón;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Avenida Dorrego 866, Buenos Aires, C1414CKQ, Argentina;-34.5910944;-58.4469591;67;false;false;Contemporary;If you enjoy dishes that come in small portions enabling you to try lots of different options, make a beeline for Picarón, in the Chacarita district, a restaurant with a sign depicting a large bear riding a velocipede, behind which you’ll find a culinary world that is both playful and fun. The colourful façade, complemented by a pavement terrace, leads to a simple bistro-style dining room with an open kitchen behind the bar counter and a glass-fronted wine cellar to one side. The à carte showcased by Maximiliano Rossi, enhanced by an affordable set menu at lunchtime (no bookings so first-come, first served), is centred around contemporary and Argentinian-based small plates which are transformed with touches of fusion, predominantly using recipes from Latin America but also more exotic dishes from Asia. We definitely recommend the popular “picarones” (sweet potato fritters with spiced Mascabo honey), the tatemado avocado, the surprising “tonnato maiale”, and the exquisite smoked prawns – all prepared with the best-possible ingredients.;Air conditioning,Terrace;[]
17712;Ácido;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Charlone 999, Buenos Aires, C1427BXU, Argentina;-34.5806989;-58.4578382;31;true;false;Contemporary;“We don’t take ourselves too seriously” is the claim of the young owner-chef at this modern and lively restaurant in the city’s Chacarita district. The à la carte here features just eight dishes, two of which are desserts, so you only need to order a few to enjoy this family-style dining experience (these dishes are sized the same way as clothes: S, M, L, XL and XXL!). There’s a contagious exuberance in the kitchen where the bold and honest flavours emanate from every corner of the globe. As an example, it was a surprise to find the Korean “tteok” prepared with typical “cacio e pepe” from Central Italy. Another favourite dish, fried chicken, is served with an array of sides, while the “Torrija” brioche provides a delicious finale to proceedings. The large open kitchen stands next to the rustic-style dining room which seems to have been decorated and furnished by a grandmother with help from her grandchildren! The atmosphere here is fun and relaxed and you can’t book ahead, so you’ll need to arrive well before 8pm to guarantee a table.;;[]
17713;A Fuego Fuerte;Argentina;Buenos Aires;Estado De Palestina 1167, Buenos Aires, C1182ADM, Argentina;-34.5966552;-58.4243567;93;true;true;Contemporary;If you’re keen to enjoy an experience that makes you feel as though you’re eating in someone’s private house, this is the place for you. Ring the bell and you’ll be led into a large room with space for just 16 guests, each of whom is seated at impressively laid out tables adorned with ornamental crystal glassware. Supper starts at 9pm for everyone and lasts for 3 hours, during which the owner-chef, who makes regular forays into the dining room to chat with guests, conjures up a 17-course tasting menu. His culinary influences are mainly from France and Italy, although theatrical presentation and elaborately constructed dishes are also to the fore. Somewhat disguised beneath this culinary spectacle are high-quality ingredients and dishes such as veal with asparagus, smoked trout with almonds, and scallops with a delicious lemon cream. Despite its formality, the service is not lacking in personality, and if you prefer not to have make any decisions whatsoever, the best option is to go for the wine pairing option.;;[]
17714;Fricska 2.0;Hungary;Budapest;Dob utca 56-58, Budapest, 1073, Hungary;47.5014847;19.0663189;34;false;false;Traditional Cuisine;When Fricska was reborn as Fricska 2.0, it took on something of a speakeasy vibe. Its unassuming exterior gives nothing away, but downstairs you’ll find a bright and trendy bar-cum-restaurant with a contemporary bistro feel. The food is a perfect match, with traditional dishes lightened and modernised to take on an appealingly fresh style. The lunch menu is a steal and the chocolate soufflé is a sure-fire hit. Service is smooth and attentive, and the friendly team will happily guide you through the fully Hungarian wine list.;Air conditioning;[]
17717;Bobajka;Hungary;Tarcal;Andrássy Kúria &  Spa, Fő út 94., Tarcal, 3915, Hungary;48.1278925;21.346742;58;true;true;Contemporary, Modern Cuisine;The Andrássy Kúria & Spa hotel sits within a 200-year-old manor house once used as a hunting lodge by the Andrássy family. Bobajka occupies its impressive vaulted cellar and extends out onto a terrace. Named after a traditional poppy seed bread pudding from the nearby Zemplén Mountains (available for dessert), the restaurant takes traditional regional dishes like lángos and brassói and gives them a refreshingly modern, colourful touch. Local Tokaj wines are also a draw, with many available by the glass.;Car park,Interesting wine list,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17718;Samwon Garden;South Korea;Seoul;835 Eonju-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, 06023, South Korea;37.52499;127.03297;87;true;true;Barbecue;In the cultural landscape of Korean barbeque, Samwon Garden has long enjoyed fame based on its intricate balance between comfort and haute cuisine. It is where diverse cuts of prime Korean beef meet the seasoned grilling skills of its staff, a synergy that creates a delightful and comfortable gastronomic experience. What’s more, a gorgeously landscaped outdoor garden, coupled with high ceilings and glass walls infused with the Korean aesthetics of empty space, adds a sense of openness to this gracious dining. Its various private dining rooms cater to a variety of communal dining needs. For several decades, Samwon Garden has transformed Korean barbeque culture while carrying on the country’s culinary tradition. Visit this culinary landmark and enjoy a meal loaded with great traditional flavors.;Air conditioning,Car park,Valet parking,Wheelchair access;[]
17719;De Tempore;South Korea;Seoul;37 Hannam-daero, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 04410, South Korea;37.532213;127.0081086;28;true;false;French;‘De tempore,’ true to its name, is a modern French restaurant that embraces the essence of seasonal ingredients in its dishes. Within the broad framework of French cuisine, the chef's refined touch brings a sense of seasonality and harmony to each plate. Signature creations like duck breast with duck jus sauce or seasonal fish paired with bisque sauce showcase the restaurant's culinary artistry, with its diverse and distinctive sauces adding an extra layer of enjoyment to the dining experience.;Air conditioning,Car park;[]
17720;Casa De Carli;Czechia;Prague;Vězeňská 5, Prague, 11 000, Czechia;50.0905468;14.4218581;45;false;false;Italian;A modern, family-run restaurant with a beautiful straightforward interior, open show kitchen and a walk-in wine fridge worth seeing as well as a wine fridge wall. Flavoursome cooking has a subtle North Italian bias, and the breads, pastas and ice creams are homemade. Make sure to consider the daily specials - the turbot in puff pastry crust, for exapmle, is a delight! In front of the house there are tables on the cobbled street. Tip: private chef's table in the kitchen for up to 12 persons.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17721;Portfolio;Czechia;Prague;Lannův Palác, Havlíčkova 1030/1, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.0873709;14.4323733;46;false;true;Modern Cuisine;A keenly run restaurant with an appealingly relaxed atmosphere, set over two floors and decorated in a contemporary style. The cooking has its roots in French and Italian cuisine and the ambitious dishes are elaborate in their construction.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17722;Výčep;Czechia;Prague;Korunní 1304/92, Prague, 101 00, Czechia;50.0753145;14.4534435;72;true;true;Czech, Contemporary;Jars of preserved fruit and veg fill the walls, delicious pork matures in small fridges, and you can watch the chefs in the kitchen via the TVs at this rustic, modern pub. Czech recipes from yesteryear are brought up-to-date in generous, flavoursome dishes – and there are some great beers to accompany.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17723;Café Imperial;Czechia;Prague;Na Poříčí 15, Prague, 110 00, Czech Republic;50.0897946;14.4327661;38;true;false;Traditional Cuisine;The Imperial hotel’s restaurant is an impressive room, with a high ceiling and colourful mosaic-tiled walls and pillars. Menus list robust Czech dishes. It was the place to be seen in the 1920s and, as they say, Kafka's spirit lives on...;Air conditioning,Booking essential;[]
17725;QQ Asian Kitchen;Czechia;Prague;Odborů 278/4, Prague, 12000, Czech Republic;50.0776554;14.4181496;85;true;true;Asian;The Mosaic Hotel plays host to this pleasant restaurant with a sunny terrace and photos of Asia decorating the room. The cheery team serve well-priced dishes which are superbly spiced. The beef rendang curry will soon become a favourite and don't miss the delicious changing desserts.;Air conditioning,Restaurant offering vegetarian menus,Terrace;[]
17727;Grand Cru;Czechia;Prague;Lodecká 4, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.0918429;14.4330317;19;true;false;Modern Cuisine;Across a cobbled courtyard is this sophisticated orangery-style restaurant where an experienced chef takes classic Czech and French recipes and delivers them in a balanced modern style. The charming wine bar offers simpler fare.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17728;Monarch;Czechia;Prague;Na Perštýně 15, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.0838301;14.4182738;70;false;true;Meats and Grills;With its comprehensive range of aged Czech and American USDA steaks and a blackboard filled with numerous special cuts, Monarch is a carnivore’s delight. The shelves are packed with wines and they offer some superb choices by the glass. The semolina mousse with cinnamon and gingerbread ice cream is a must.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list,Terrace;[]
17729;CottoCrudo;Czechia;Prague;Veleslavínova 1098/2A, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.0878182;14.4144453;33;true;true;Italian;Refined Italian cuisine based on seasonal ingredients awaits you in this restaurant of the elegant "Four Seasons Hotel". You can dine à la carte or in menu form. You will be looked after attentively in a lively atmosphere, and in summer you can enjoy the terrace with a view of the Vltava. Don't miss the cosy, modern bar with its Czech-inspired cocktail menu.;Air conditioning,Car park,Terrace,Wheelchair access;[]
17730;V Zátiši;Czechia;Prague;Liliová 1, Betlémské Nám., Prague, 110 00, Czech Republic;50.0843162;14.4164476;34;true;true;Modern Cuisine;This modern city centre restaurant is a popular spot. Its name means ‘timeless’ and with its clever blend of modern Czech and international dishes, it looks set to stand up to its name. In the open kitchen selected products are used. You can dine à la carte or in the form of a set menu, accompanied by the matching wine.;Air conditioning,Booking essential - dinner;[]
17731;Pot au Feu;Czechia;Prague;Rybná 13, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.0891287;14.4259349;59;false;false;French;The chef-owner’s cooking is inspired by the French classics but also by his travels. The intimate interior comes with striking artwork and shelves packed with directly sourced French wines. Service is relaxed yet clued-up.;Air conditioning,Interesting wine list;[]
17732;Yamato;Czechia;Prague;U Kanálky 14, Prague, 120 00, Czech Republic;50.0784842;14.4460905;82;false;true;Japanese;The chef is a local but he trained in Japan, so alongside an array of authentic dishes you’ll find some original creations. A selection of Japanese beers and whiskies complement the cooking, and the place is run with real passion.;Air conditioning,Booking essential - dinner,Notable sake list;[]
17733;La Finestra in Cucina;Czechia;Prague;Platnérská 13, Prague, 110 00, Czech Republic;50.0873376;14.4163668;91;true;false;Italian;You’d never guess but from 1918-1945, this lovely restaurant with its red-brick vaulted ceiling was an Alfa Romeo showroom! Expect rustic Italian dishes, an extensive selection of daily specials and fine Italian wines – and be sure to stop off for some treats from their neighbouring shop.;Air conditioning,Booking essential - dinner,Interesting wine list;[]
17734;Kampa Park;Czechia;Prague;Na Kampe 8b, Malá Strana, Prague, 118 00, Czechia;50.0870377;14.4089916;89;false;true;Modern Cuisine;Kampa Park is stunningly located by the water’s edge, next to Charles Bridge. Choose from several dining areas: the best spots are the Winter Garden and the riverside terrace. The décor is contemporary, as is the interesting menu.;Air conditioning,Booking essential - dinner,Great view,Terrace;[]
17735;La Veranda;Czechia;Prague;Elišky Krásnohorské 2, Prague, 110 00, Czechia;50.090262;14.419907;63;true;true;Mediterranean Cuisine;Sit surrounded by books in the colourfully decorated main room or head down to the intimate basement. Cooking takes its inspiration from the Med, with Italy playing a big part. Staff are friendly and welcoming.;Air conditioning;[]
